// 繁體中文權威辭典 (含完整釋義、及物/不及物詞性與權威例句)
window.YAHOO_DICT_DB = {"able":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"能夠，有能力的；聰明能幹的，精通（某事）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are able to</b> do something, you have skills or qualities which make it possible for you to do it. (因具有某技能或素質而) 能夠","examples":["The older child should be able to prepare a simple meal. 這個大點兒的孩子應該能做頓簡單的飯菜。","The company says they're able to keep pricing competitive. 這個公司說他們能夠保持價格競爭力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are able to</b> do something, you have enough freedom, power, time, or money to do it. (因有足夠的自由、權力、時間或財力而) 可以","examples":["You'll be able to read in peace. 你將可以安靜地看書。","Have you been able to have any kind of contact? 你取得任何聯絡了嗎?"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>able</b> is very intelligent or very good at doing something. 有才能的","examples":["...one of the brightest and ablest members of the government. …最聰明、最有才能的政府成員之一。"]}]}]},"another":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"（同類的）另一，又一；（不同類的）另外一個，其他一個；類似的（人或事物）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"又一個，再一個；另一個，另一種；不確切的事物，某些事物（用於與 one 或 some 構成的短語）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"再加一個的；另一的，不同的；另一類似的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Another</b> thing or person means an additional thing or person of the same type as one that already exists. 又一的","examples":["Divers this morning found the body of another American sailor drowned during yesterday's ferry disaster. 潛水員們今天早晨發現了在昨天渡輪失事中淹死的又一名美國水手的屍體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>another</b> when you want to emphasize that an additional thing or person is different from one that already exists. 另一的","examples":["I think he's just going to deal with this problem another day. 我想他只是打算改天再處理這個問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>another</b> at the beginning of a statement to link it to a previous statement. 另一的 (用於一陳述句的開頭以使之與前一陳述句銜接)","examples":["Another time of great excitement for us boys was when war broke out. 另一個對於我們小夥子來講極為興奮的時刻是在戰爭爆發的時候。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>another</b> before a word referring to a distance, length of time, or other amount, to indicate an additional amount. 再加的 (用於表示距離、時長、數量等的詞前)","examples":["Continue down the same road for another 2 miles until you reach the church of Santa Maria. 沿著同一條路繼續走2英里直到你到達聖瑪麗亞教堂。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Another</b> is also a pronoun. 又一個","examples":["The demand generated by one factory required the construction of another. 一家工廠提出的需要再建一家工廠的要求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Another</b> is also a pronoun. 另一個","examples":["He didn't really believe that any human being could read another's mind. 他並不真地相信一個人能夠看出另一個人的心思。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>one another</b> to indicate that each member of a group does something to or for the other members. 相互","examples":["...women learning to help themselves and one another. …學習自助和互助的女人們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about <b>one</b> thing <b>after another</b>, you are referring to a series of repeated or continuous events. 一個接一個的","examples":["They had faced one difficulty after another with bravery and dedication. 他們曾以勇敢與執著面對了一個又一個困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>or another</b> in expressions such as <b>one kind or another</b> when you do not want to be precise about which of several alternatives or possibilities you are referring to. 或那種的","examples":["...family members and visiting artists of one kind or another crowding the huge kitchen. …擠滿了這間巨大的廚房的家庭成員以及這類或那類的訪問藝術家們。"]}]}]},"basic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最重要的，基本的；最簡單的，初級的；（產品和服務）必需的；（化）鹼性的；含鹼的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"基本要素，基本原則"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>basic</b> to describe things, activities, and principles that are very important or necessary, and on which others depend. 基本的","examples":["...the basic skills of reading, writing and communicating. …閱讀、寫作和交際等基本技巧。","Access to justice is a basic right. 享有公正是一種基本權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Basic</b> goods and services are very simple ones which every human being needs. You can also refer to people's <b>basic</b> needs for such goods and services. 基本必需的","examples":["...shortages of even the most basic foodstuffs. …甚至最基本食品的短缺。","Hospitals lack even basic drugs for surgical operations. 醫院甚至缺乏外科手術的基本必需的藥品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is <b>basic</b> <b>to</b> another, it is absolutely necessary to it, and the second thing cannot exist, succeed, or be imagined without it. 必不可少的","examples":["...an oily liquid, basic to the manufacture of a host of other chemical substances. …生產許多其它化學材料所必不可少的一種油狀液體。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>basic</b> to emphasize that you are referring to what you consider to be the most important aspect of a situation, and that you are not concerned with less important details. 主要的","examples":["There are three basic types of tea. 有3種主要的茶。","The basic design changed little from that patented by Edison more than 100 years ago. 這個主要設計與100多年前愛迪生取得專利的設計相比沒什麼變化。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>basic</b> to describe something that is very simple in style and has only the most necessary features, without any luxuries. 簡單的","examples":["We provide 2-person tents and basic cooking and camping equipment. 我們提供雙人帳篷以及簡單的烹飪和露營裝置。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>basic</b> rate of income tax is the lowest or most common rate, which applies to people who earn average incomes. (所得稅) 最低標準額的","examples":["All this is to be done without big increases in the basic level of taxation. 所有這一切將在沒有大幅度提高最低所得稅標準的情況下進行。"]}]}]},"brave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勇敢的，無畏的；非常好的；華麗的，盛裝的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"勇敢面對"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇敢的人；<舊>印第安武士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>brave</b> is willing to do things that are dangerous, and does not show fear in difficult or dangerous situations. 勇敢的","examples":["He was not brave enough to report the loss of the documents. 他當時不夠勇敢去報失檔案的丟失。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"勇敢地","examples":["Our men wiped them out, but the enemy fought bravely and well. 我們的人殲滅了敵人,不過敵人也打得很勇猛頑強。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>brave</b> unpleasant or dangerous conditions, you deliberately expose yourself to them, usually in order to achieve something. 勇於置身 (惡劣或危險的環境)","examples":["Thousands have braved icy rain to demonstrate their support. 數千人曾頂著冰冷的雨表示他們的支援。"]}]}]},"beautiful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"美麗的，漂亮的；令人愉悅的，美妙的；（完成得）出色的，極好的；<美>仁慈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beautiful</b> person is very attractive to look at. 美麗的","examples":["She was a very beautiful woman. 她是個非常美麗的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>beautiful</b>, you mean that it is very attractive or pleasing. 迷人的","examples":["New England is beautiful. 新英格蘭很迷人。","It was a beautiful morning. 那是個迷人的早晨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe something that someone does as <b>beautiful</b> when they do it very skilfully. 出色的","examples":["That's a beautiful shot! 那一射真漂亮！"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"迷人地","examples":["The children behaved beautifully. 孩子們表現甚佳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"出色地","examples":["The Sixers played beautifully. 費城76人隊打得很出色。"]}]}]},"angry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"憤怒的，生氣的；狂風暴雨的，波濤洶湧的；紅腫的，感染的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>angry</b>, you feel strong dislike or impatience about something. 生氣的","examples":["Are you angry with me for some reason? 你是因為某個原因生我的氣了嗎？","I was angry about the rumours. 我對這些謠言感到生氣。","An angry mob gathered outside the courthouse. 一群憤怒的民眾聚集到了法院外面。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"生氣地","examples":["Officials reacted angrily to those charges. 官員們憤怒地回應了那些指控。"]}]}]},"born":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天生的，生來就有的；出生的；產生的，（機構、想法等）問世的"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"以……的順序（或方式、地點等）出生的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"忍受；承擔；具有（bear 的過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"被動及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a baby <b>is born</b>, it comes out of its mother's body at the beginning of its life. In formal English, if you say that someone <b>is born</b> <b>of</b> someone or <b>to</b> someone, you mean that person is their parent. 出生","examples":["She was born in Milan on April 29, 1923. 她1923年4月29日生於米蘭。","He was born of German parents and lived most of his life abroad. 他的父母是德國人，他一生大部分時間生活在國外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is born</b> <b>with</b> a particular disease, problem, or characteristic, they have it from the time they are born. 先天的","examples":["He was born with only one lung. 他生下來就只有一個肺。","Some people are born brainy. 有些人生來就聰明。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>be born</b> in front of a particular name to show that a person was given this name at birth, although they may be better known by another name. 出生取名","examples":["She was born Jenny Harvey on June 11, 1946. 1946年6月11日她出生時取名珍妮·哈維。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When an idea or organization <b>is born</b>, it comes into existence. If something <b>is born</b> <b>of</b> a particular emotion or activity, it exists as a result of that emotion or activity. (思想或組織) 產生; 誕生","examples":["The idea for the show was born in his hospital room. 這個演出的想法是在他醫院病房裡產生的。","Congress passed the National Security Act, and the CIA was born. 國會透過了《國家安全法案》，中央情報局由此誕生。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>born</b> to describe someone who has a natural ability to do a particular activity or job. For example, if you are a <b>born</b> cook, you have a natural ability to cook well. 天生的","examples":["Jack was a born teacher. 傑克是個天生的教師。"]}]}]},"certain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"必然的，必定的；確定的，無疑的；某個，特定的；某位，一位叫……的；一定程度上的，有點兒"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"某些，某幾個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Certain）（美、法）塞爾坦（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>certain</b> about something, you firmly believe it is true and have no doubt about it. If you are not <b>certain</b> about something, you do not have definite knowledge about it. 確信的","examples":["She's absolutely certain she's going to make it in the world. 她確信自己將享譽全球。","We are not certain whether the appendix had already burst or not. 我們不能確定闌尾破了沒有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>certain</b> <b>to</b> happen, you mean that it will definitely happen. 肯定的; 有把握的","examples":["However, the scheme is certain to meet opposition from fishermen's leaders. 不過這個計劃肯定會遭到漁夫頭領們的反對。","It's not certain they'll accept that candidate if he wins. 如果那位候選人勝出，無法肯定他們是否會接受他。","The prime minister is heading for certain defeat if he forces a vote. 如果首相強令大家投票表決，那他一定會遭遇失敗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>certain</b>, you firmly believe that it is true, or have definite knowledge about it. 確鑿的","examples":["One thing is certain, both have the utmost respect for each other. 有一點是確定無疑的，即兩人對彼此都非常敬重。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>certain</b> to indicate that you are referring to one particular thing, person, or group, although you are not saying exactly which it is. 某","examples":["There will be certain people who'll say \"I told you so!\" 會有某些人說，“我告訴過你了！”","You owe a certain person a sum of money. 你欠著某人一筆錢。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>a certain</b> to indicate that something such as a quality or condition exists, and often to suggest that it is not great in amount or degree. 稍微的","examples":["That was the very reason why he felt a certain bitterness. 那正是他感到有點痛苦的原因。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you know something <b>for certain</b>, you have no doubt at all about it. 肯定地","examples":["She couldn't know what time he'd go, or even for certain that he'd go at all. 她不知道他何時要走，甚至於還不能確定他究竟要不要走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make certain</b> <b>that</b> something is the way you want or expect it to be, you take action to ensure that it is. 確保","examples":["Parents should make certain that the children spend enough time doing homework. 父母應該確保孩子花足夠多的時間做作業。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you refer to <b>certain</b> <b>of</b> a group of people or things, you are referring to some particular members of that group. 某些","examples":["They'll have to give up completely on certain of their studies. 他們將不得不完全放棄某些課程。"]}]}]},"cute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"漂亮的，可愛的；<美>性感迷人的；<美>精明的，機靈的；<美，非正式>矯揉造作的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>cute</b> is very pretty or attractive, or is intended to appear pretty or attractive. 可愛的","examples":["Oh, look at that dog! He's so cute. 哦，看那條狗！它真可愛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>cute</b>, you think they are sexually attractive. 性感的","examples":["There was this girl, and I thought she was really cute. 就是這個女孩，我覺得她真的很性感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>cute</b>, you mean that they deal with things cleverly. 聰明的","examples":["That's a cute trick. 那是個聰明的把戲。"]}]}]},"different":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不同的；分別的，各別的；與眾不同的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people or things are <b>different</b>, they are not like each other in one or more ways. 不同的","examples":["London was different from most European capitals. 倫敦與大多數的歐洲首都城市不同。","If he'd attended music school, how might things have been different? 如果他上的是音樂學校，一切會怎樣地不同呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People sometimes say that one thing is <b>different than</b> another. This use is acceptable in American English, but is often considered incorrect in British English. 與…不同的 (美式英語中可用，英式英語常認為是錯的)","examples":["We're not really any different than they are. 我們與他們其實沒有什麼不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>different</b> to indicate that you are talking about two or more separate and distinct things of the same kind. 各不相同的","examples":["Different countries specialized in different products. 不同的國家專門生產各不相同的產品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe something as <b>different</b> when it is unusual and not like others of the same kind. 不尋常的; 與眾不同的","examples":["The result is interesting and different, but do not attempt the recipe if time is short. 結果有趣且非同尋常，但如果時間緊張就不要嘗試這個食譜。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不同地","examples":["Every individual learns differently. 每個人的學習方式都不一樣。"]}]}]},"careful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"仔細的，小心的；謹慎的，周密的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>careful</b>, you give serious attention to what you are doing, in order to avoid harm, damage, or mistakes. If you are <b>careful</b> <b>to</b> do something, you make sure that you do it. 謹慎的; 注意的","examples":["Be very careful with this stuff, it can be dangerous if it isn't handled properly. 對這東西要小心，處理得不好可能會發生危險。","Careful on those stairs! 小心那些樓梯！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Careful</b> work, thought, or examination is thorough and shows a concern for details. 仔細的","examples":["He has decided to prosecute her after careful consideration of all the relevant facts. 他仔細考慮了所有相關事實後，決定起訴她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you tell someone to be <b>careful about</b> doing something, you think that what they intend to do is probably wrong, and that they should think seriously before they do it. 當心的","examples":["I think you should be careful about talking of the rebels as heroes. 我認為你還是當心點好，別把叛亂分子說成是英雄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>careful</b> <b>with</b> something such as money or resources, you use or spend only what is necessary. 精打細算的","examples":["Industries should be more careful with natural resources. 各行業對自然資源應該更加精打細算。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"小心地","examples":["Have a nice time, dear, and drive carefully. 好好玩，親愛的，要小心駕駛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"仔細地","examples":["...a vast series of deliberate and carefully planned thefts. …多起精心策劃、周密安排的盜竊案件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"當心地","examples":["He should think carefully about actions like this which play into the hands of his opponents. 他應該留神這類對對手有利的行為。"]}]}]},"difficult":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"困難的，費力的；不友好的，難對付的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>difficult</b> is not easy to do, understand, or deal with. 困難的","examples":["The lack of childcare provisions made it difficult for single mothers to get jobs. 兒童保育服務的缺乏使得單身媽媽們很難找到工作。","It was a very difficult decision to make. 這是個非常難作的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>difficult</b> behaves in an unreasonable and unhelpful way. 難相處的","examples":["I had a feeling you were going to be difficult about this. 我有種感覺，在這件事情上你將很難對付。"]}]}]},"bad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"壞的，不好的，令人不悅的；難以接受的，令人遺憾的；粗魯的，下流的；抱歉的，難過的；質量差的，不合格的；邪惡的，不道德的；頑皮的，不乖的；有病的，疼痛的；腐爛的，變質的；嚴重的，劇烈的；不明智的，不合適的；不利的，不幸的；拙於，不擅；無價值的，偽造的；<美，非正式> 非常好的（比較級badder，最高階baddest）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"壞人，壞事"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美，非正式>很，非常；<美，非正式>厲害地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>bad</b> is unpleasant, harmful, or undesirable. 壞的","examples":["The bad weather conditions prevented the plane from landing. 惡劣的天氣使飛機無法著陸。","Divorce is bad for children. 離婚對孩子不好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>bad</b> to indicate that something unpleasant or undesirable is severe or great in degree. 嚴重的","examples":["Glick had a bad accident two years ago and had to give up farming. 格利克兩年前遭遇一次嚴重事故，不得不放棄務農。","The floods are described as the worst in nearly fifty years. 這場洪水被描述為近五十年來最嚴重的一次。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bad</b> idea, decision, or method is not sensible or not correct. 糟糕的; 不明智的","examples":["Giving your address to a man you don't know is a bad idea. 把你的地址告訴一個你不認識的男人不太明智。","The worst thing you can do is underestimate an opponent. 最糟的做法就是低估對手。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a piece of news, an action, or a sign as <b>bad</b>, you mean that it is unlikely to result in benefit or success. 不利的","examples":["The closure of the project is bad news for her staff. 該專案的結束對她的員工來說是個壞訊息。","It was a bad start in my relationship with Warr. 對我和沃爾的關係來說，這是個不好的開端。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>bad</b> is of an unacceptably low standard, quality, or amount. 低劣的","examples":["Many old people in the United States are living in bad housing. 美國的許多老年人住房條件惡劣。","The schools' main problem is that teachers' pay is so bad. 這些學校的主要問題是教師的工資太低。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bad</b> <b>at</b> doing something is not skilful or successful at it. 不擅長的","examples":["Howard was so bad at basketball. 霍華德的籃球打得真臭。","He was a bad driver. 他車技不佳。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>bad</b> that something happens, you mean it is unacceptable, unfortunate, or wrong. 不能接受的; 不幸的; 錯的","examples":["Not being able to hear doesn't seem as bad to the rest of us as not being able to see. 對我們其他人來說，聽不見似乎不像看不見那麼糟。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>not bad</b> to mean that it is quite good or acceptable, especially when you are rather surprised about this. (與not同用，表示)不錯","examples":["\"How much is he paying you?\"—\"Oh, five thousand.\"—\"Not bad.\" “他付你多少工資？”—“哦，五千。”—“還不錯。”","That's not a bad idea. 那個主意不錯。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>bad</b>, you mean that they are very good. 非常好的","examples":["...the baddest bass music from Miami, featuring Dr. Boom & The Dominator. …來自邁阿密最棒的低音音樂，由布姆博士和霸主伴唱。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>bad</b> person has morally unacceptable attitudes and behaviour. (指人) 惡的","examples":["I was selling drugs, but I didn't think I was a bad person. 我賣毒品，但我不認為自己是壞人。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"A <b>bad</b> child disobeys rules and instructions or does not behave in a polite and correct way. 不聽話的; 沒規矩的","examples":["You are a bad boy for repeating what I told you. 你是個沒規矩的男孩，重複我對你講的話。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you are in a <b>bad</b> mood, you are angry and behave unpleasantly to people. (情緒) 糟的","examples":["She is in a bit of a bad mood because she's just given up smoking. 因為剛戒菸，她心情有點糟。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> <b>bad</b> <b>about</b> something, you feel sorry or guilty about it. 內疚的","examples":["You don't have to feel bad about relaxing. 你不必因為放鬆而感到內疚。","I feel bad that he's doing most of the work. 讓我感到愧疚的是，他在做大部分的工作。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you have a <b>bad</b> back, heart, leg, or eye, it is injured, diseased, or weak. (身體某部位) 不適的","examples":["Joe has a bad back so we have a hard bed. 喬的背不好，所以我們睡硬板床。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"Food that has <b>gone</b> <b>bad</b> is not suitable to eat because it has started to decay. 變質的","examples":["They bought so much beef that some went bad. 他們買了這麼多牛肉，有些都變質了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"<b>Bad</b> language is language that contains offensive words such as swear words. (語言) 帶髒字的","examples":["I don't like to hear bad language in the street. 我不喜歡在大街上聽到髒話。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"badly 極度地","examples":[]}]}]},"afraid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"害怕的；擔心的；（害怕後果而）不願意的，勉強的；遺憾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>afraid</b> <b>of</b> someone or <b>afraid</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are frightened because you think that something very unpleasant is going to happen to you. 害怕的","examples":["She did not seem at all afraid. 她一點兒也沒顯得害怕。","I was afraid of the other boys. 我害怕其他的男孩子們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>afraid</b> <b>for</b> someone else, you are worried that something horrible is going to happen to them. (為某人) 擔心的","examples":["She's afraid for her family in Somalia. 她為她在索馬利亞的家人擔心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>afraid</b> that something unpleasant will happen, you are worried that it may happen and you want to avoid it. (對令人不快的事情會發生) 擔心的","examples":["I was afraid that nobody would believe me. 我擔心沒有人會相信我的話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you want to apologize to someone or to disagree with them in a polite way, you can say <b>I'm afraid</b>. 恐怕","examples":["We don't have anything like that, I'm afraid. 我們恐怕沒有任何像那樣的東西。"]}]}]},"easy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"容易的，不費力的；舒適的，自如的；隨和的；輕浮的；平緩的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"小心；容易地，悠閒地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a job or action is <b>easy</b>, you can do it without difficulty or effort, because it is not complicated and causes no problems. 容易的","examples":["The shower is easy to install. 淋浴器易於安裝。","This is not an easy task. 這不是項容易的任務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an action or activity as <b>easy</b>, you mean that it is done in a confident, relaxed way. If someone is <b>easy</b> <b>about</b> something, they feel relaxed and confident about it. 輕鬆自如的","examples":["He was an easy person to talk to. 他是個可以與之輕鬆交談的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has an <b>easy</b> life, you mean that they live comfortably without any problems or worries. 舒適的","examples":["She has not had an easy life. 她不曾有過舒適的生活。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>easy</b> or too <b>easy</b>, you are criticizing someone because they have done the most obvious or least difficult thing, and have not considered the situation carefully enough. 容易的","examples":["That's easy for you to say. 你說得容易。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"容易地","examples":["Dress your child in layers of clothes you can remove easily. 給你的孩子穿幾層你能容易地脫掉的衣服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"輕鬆自如地","examples":["They talked amiably and easily about a range of topics. 他們親切而又輕鬆地談著一系列的話題。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>go easy on</b> something, you are telling them to use only a small amount of it. 省著點","examples":["Go easy on the alcohol. 少喝點兒酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>go easy on</b>, or <b>be easy on</b>, a particular person, you are telling them not to punish or treat that person very severely. 對某人溫和點兒","examples":["\"Go easy on him,\" Sam repeated, opening the door. “對他溫和點兒，”薩姆開門時又重複了一遍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone tells you to <b>take it easy</b> or <b>take things easy</b>, they mean that you should relax and not do very much at all. 悠著點","examples":["It is best to take things easy for a week or two. 最好放鬆一兩個星期。"]}]}]},"dead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"死的，去世的；不再使用的，用盡的；（因無電力）不工作的；無生氣的，死氣沉沉的；過時的，不再有關的；（身體部位）無知覺的，麻木的；筋疲力盡的；神情冷漠的，漠不關心的；完全的，精確的；無生命的，無生物的；界外的；（時間段）空檔的，無事可做的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"恰好，精確地；完全地，全然地；<英，非正式>非常，十分；突然，頓時"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"死人，死者；死；深夜，隆冬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person, animal, or plant that is <b>dead</b> is no longer living. 死的","examples":["\"You're a widow?\"—\"Yes. My husband's been dead a year now.\" “你是個寡婦？”——“是的，我丈夫去世1年了。”","The group had shot dead another hostage. 這夥人又打死了一名人質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place or a period of time as <b>dead</b>, you do not like it because there is very little activity taking place in it. 無生氣的","examples":["...some dead little town where the liveliest thing is the flies. …最有活力的東西是蒼蠅的死氣沉沉的某個小鎮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>dead</b> is no longer being used or is finished. 用盡的; 結束的","examples":["The dead cigarette was still between his fingers. 燃盡的香菸還夾在他指縫間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that an idea, plan, or subject is <b>dead</b>, you mean that people are no longer interested in it or willing to develop it any further. 過時的; 不再重要的","examples":["It's a dead issue, Baxter. 這件事已經不重要了，巴克斯特。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A telephone or piece of electrical equipment that is <b>dead</b> is no longer functioning, for example, because it no longer has any electrical power. 不運轉的","examples":["On another occasion I answered the phone and the line went dead. 還有一次我接了電話，但緊接著就斷線了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Dead</b> is used to mean \"complete\" or \"absolute,\" especially before the words \"centre,\" \"silence,\" and \"stop.\" 全然的; 絕對的","examples":["They hurried about in dead silence, with anxious faces. 他們四下忙亂，人人一言不發，面有憂色。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The dead</b> are people who are dead. 死者","examples":["Two American soldiers were among the dead. 死者中有兩名美軍士兵。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dead</b> means \"precisely\" or \"exactly.\" 精確地","examples":["Mars was visible, dead in the centre of the telescope. 火星清晰可辨，正好就在望遠鏡的中心。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you reply \"<b>Over my dead body</b>\" when a plan or action has been suggested, you are emphasizing that you dislike it, and will do everything you can to prevent it. 除非我死了 (表示強烈反對)","examples":["\"Let's invite her to dinner.\"—\"Over my dead body!\" “我們請她共進晚餐吧。”——“除非我死了!”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or animal <b>dropped dead</b> or <b>dropped down dead</b>, you mean that they died very suddenly and unexpectedly. 猝死","examples":["He dropped dead of a heart attack. 他心臟病突發而猝死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>feel dead</b> or <b>are half dead</b>, you mean that you feel very tired or ill and very weak. 累得半死的","examples":["I thought you looked half dead at dinner, and who could blame you after that trip. 我覺得你晚飯的時候看上去累得要命，但在那次旅行之後誰會怪你呢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>in the dead of night</b>, <b>at dead of night</b>, or <b>in the dead of winter</b>, it happens in the middle part of the night or the winter, when it is darkest or coldest. 在深夜; 在嚴冬","examples":["All three incidents occurred in the dead of night. 3起事件都發生在深夜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you wouldn't <b>be seen dead</b> or <b>be caught dead</b> in particular clothes, places, or situations, you are expressing strong dislike or disapproval of them. 決不","examples":["I wouldn't be seen dead in a straw hat. 我決不戴草帽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>stop dead</b> means to suddenly stop happening or moving. To <b>stop</b> someone or something <b>dead</b> means to cause them to suddenly stop happening or moving. 突然停止","examples":["We all stopped dead and looked at it. 我們都突然停下來看著它。"]}]}]},"false":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"錯誤的，不真實的；偽造的；人造的；站不住腳的，全無根據的；不真誠的；不忠誠的；外表上與……相似的；非法的；妄動的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"欺詐地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>false</b>, it is incorrect, untrue, or mistaken. 錯誤的","examples":["It was quite clear the president was being given false information by those around him. 很明顯，總統身邊的那些人正給總統提供著錯誤資訊。","You do not know whether what you're told is true or false. 你不知道別人告訴你的是真的還是假的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>false</b> to describe objects which are artificial but which are intended to look like the real thing or to be used instead of the real thing. 假的","examples":["...a set of false teeth. …一副假牙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>false</b>, you are criticizing them for being insincere or for hiding their real feelings. 不真誠的","examples":["\"Thank you,\" she said with false enthusiasm. “謝謝你，” 她故作熱情地說。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"錯誤地","examples":["...a man who is falsely accused of a crime. …一名被錯誤地指控犯有一個罪行的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不真誠地","examples":["They smiled at one another, somewhat falsely. 他們相互微笑，有點假惺惺地。"]}]}]},"every":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"每個，每一；每……之中的；每隔，每逢（表頻率）；所有可能的，完全可能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>every</b> to indicate that you are referring to all the members of a group or all the parts of something and not only some of them. 每個","examples":["Every room has a window facing the ocean. 每個房間都有一扇面對大海的窗。","Record every expenditure you make. 記下你的每筆花銷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>every</b> in order to say how often something happens or to indicate that something happens at regular intervals. (時間段) 每隔…的","examples":["We were made to attend meetings every day. 我們每天都被迫參加會議。","A burglary occurs every three minutes in London. 入室盜竊案在倫敦每3分鐘就發生一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>every</b> in front of a number when you are saying what proportion of people or things something happens to or applies to. (一定數目中) 每…之中的","examples":["Two out of every three people have a cell phone. 每3人中有2人有一部手機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>every</b> before some nouns, for example \"sign,\" \"effort,\" \"reason,\" and \"intention\" in order to emphasize what you are saying. 全部的 (用於某些名詞前，表示強調)","examples":["The Congressional Budget Office says the federal deficit shows every sign of getting larger. 國會預算辦公室稱聯邦赤字顯示出種種增加的跡象。","I think that there is every chance that you will succeed. 我認為你完全有機會成功。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Every</b> is also an adjective. 每個的","examples":["His every utterance will be scrutinized. 他說的每句話都會被細查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone's <b>every</b> whim, wish, or desire will be satisfied, you are emphasizing that everything they want will happen or be provided. (幻想、願望) 所有可能的","examples":["Dozens of servants had catered to his every whim. 幾十個僕人曾迎合他所有離奇的想法。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>every</b> in the expressions <b>every now and then</b>, <b>every now and again</b>, <b>every once in a while</b>, and <b>every so often</b> in order to indicate that something happens occasionally. 不時; 間或","examples":["Stir the batter every now and then to keep it from separating. 不時地攪拌麵糊以防止其成分相分離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>every other day</b> or <b>every second day</b>, for example, it happens one day, then does not happen the next day, then happens the day after that, and so on. You can also say that something happens <b>every third week</b>, <b>every fourth year</b>, and so on. 每隔 (一天、一週等)","examples":["I went home every other week. 我每隔一週回一次家。"]}]}]},"foreign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外國的，來自國外的；外交的，涉外的；陌生的，不熟悉的；外來的，異質的；外地的，不屬於本地區的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>foreign</b> comes from or relates to a country that is not your own. 外國的","examples":["She was on her first foreign holiday without her parents. 她首次不在父母的陪同下到國外度假。","...a foreign language. …一門外語。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In politics and journalism, <b>foreign</b> is used to describe people, jobs, and activities relating to countries that are not the country of the person or government concerned. 涉外的","examples":["...the German foreign minister. …德國外交部長。","I am the foreign correspondent in Washington of La Tribuna newspaper of Honduras. 我是宏都拉斯《論壇報》駐華盛頓的記者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>foreign</b> object is something that has got into something else, usually by accident, and should not be there. 異質的","examples":["The patient's immune system would reject the transplanted organ as a foreign object. 該病人的免疫系統會將移植器官作為異物加以排斥。"]}]}]},"few":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"一些，幾個；很少，不多，幾乎沒有"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"一些人（或物）；很少的人（或物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"少數的；很少（的），幾乎沒有（的）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指享有某種機遇等的）少數派，少數（the few） ；參加過不列顛之戰的少數幾個英國皇家空軍飛行員（the Few）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>a few</b> to indicate that you are talking about a small number of people or things. You can also say <b>a very few</b>. 幾個","examples":["I gave a dinner party for a few close friends. 我為幾個密友舉辦了一個晚餐聚會。","Here are a few more ideas to consider. 這兒還有幾點建議可以考慮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>few</b> to indicate that you are talking about a small number of people or things. You can use \"so,\" \"too,\" and \"very\" in front of <b>few</b>. 很少","examples":["She had few friends, and was generally not functioning up to her potential. 她很少有什麼朋友，總體來看沒有發揮她的潛能。","Few members planned to vote for him. 很少有成員計劃投他的票。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Few</b> is also a pronoun. 幾個","examples":["Doctors work an average of 90 hours a week, while a few are on call for up to 120 hours. 醫生們平均每週工作90個小時，而有些出診長達120個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Few</b> is also a pronoun. 很少","examples":["Few can survive more than a week without water. 很少有人沒有水能活過一週。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Few</b> is also a quantifier. 幾個","examples":["There are many ways eggs can be prepared; here are a few of them. 烹調雞蛋的方法有很多；這裡是其中的幾個。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Few</b> is also a quantifier. 很少","examples":["Few of the beach houses still had lights on. 岸邊的房屋很少還亮著燈。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Few</b> is also an adjective. 很少的","examples":["...spending her few waking hours in front of the TV. …把她清醒的個把鐘頭花在電視機前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>few</b> after adjectives and determiners to indicate that you are talking about a small number of things or people. 少數的","examples":["The past few weeks of her life had been the most pleasant she could remember. 過去的寥寥幾星期是她生命中所能記起的最快樂的時光。","...in the last few chapters. …在最後幾章裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The few</b> means a small set of people considered as separate from the majority, especially because they share a particular opportunity or quality that the others do not have. 少數人","examples":["This should not be an experience for the few. 這應該不只是少數人的經歷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as few as</b> before a number to suggest that it is surprisingly small. 少到只有","examples":["One study showed that even as few as ten cigarettes a day can damage fertility. 一項研究表明，每天哪怕只抽10支菸也會損害生育能力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Things that are <b>few and far between</b> are very rare or do not happen very often. 稀少的; 罕見的","examples":["Successful women politicians are few and far between. 成功的女政治家少之又少。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>no fewer than</b> to emphasize that a number is surprisingly large. 不少於","examples":["No fewer than thirteen foreign ministers attended the session. 不少於13個國家的外長參加了會議。"]}]}]},"fresh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"新鮮的；新近的，剛經歷的；新的，不同的；新穎的，獨創的；清新的，清爽的；（水）淡的，無鹽的；（風）涼爽的，強勁的；潔淨的，亮麗的；精力充沛的；剛來的；（對異性）放肆的，無禮的；年輕可愛但缺乏經驗的；<西印度>氣味難聞的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"剛剛，新近地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fresh</b> thing or amount replaces or is added to a previous thing or amount. 新加的","examples":["He asked the police, who carried out the original investigation, to make fresh inquiries. 他要求原先進行調查的警方做一輪新的調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>fresh</b> has been done, made, or experienced recently. 新近的","examples":["There were no fresh car tracks or footprints in the snow. 雪地裡沒有新的車轍或腳印。","A puppy stepped in the fresh cement. 一隻小狗走到新鋪的水泥路面上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fresh</b> food has been picked or produced recently, and has not been preserved, for example, by being frozen or put in a can. 新鮮的","examples":["...locally caught fresh fish. …當地捕獲的鮮魚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>fresh</b>, you like it because it is new and exciting. 新穎的","examples":["These designers are full of fresh ideas. 這些設計師滿是新穎的想法。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>fresh</b>, you mean that it is pleasant, bright, and clean in appearance. 鮮豔的","examples":["Gingham fabrics always look fresh and pretty. 方格花布看起來總是鮮豔而美麗。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something smells, tastes, or feels <b>fresh</b>, it is clean or cool. 清新的","examples":["The air was fresh and for a moment she felt revived. 空氣清新，一會兒她就感到精力恢復了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you feel <b>fresh</b>, you feel full of energy and enthusiasm. 精力充沛的","examples":["It's vital we are as fresh as possible for those games. 至關重要的是，我們要儘可能精力充沛地去打那些比賽。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Fresh</b> paint is not yet dry. (油漆) 未乾的","examples":["There was fresh paint on the walls. 牆上有未乾的油漆。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you are <b>fresh from</b> a particular place or experience, you have just come from that place or you have just had that experience. You can also say that someone is <b>fresh out of</b> a place. 剛從…來的; 剛經歷過…的","examples":["I returned to the office, fresh from the airport. 我剛從機場回到辦公室。"]}]}]},"funny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滑稽的，有趣的；古怪的，難以解釋的；微恙的，稍有不適的；生氣的，不友好的；瘋瘋癲癲的；出故障的；可疑的，不誠實的；放肆的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（報紙上的）滑稽連環漫畫；<非正式>笑話"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"古怪地，奇怪地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>funny</b> is amusing and likely to make you smile or laugh. 好笑的","examples":["I'll tell you a funny story. 我將給你講個好笑的故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>funny</b>, you think it is strange, surprising, or puzzling. 奇怪的","examples":["Children get some very funny ideas sometimes!. 孩子們有時候有一些非常奇怪的想法。","There's something funny about him. 他有點兒怪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you feel <b>funny</b>, you feel slightly ill. 稍有不適的","examples":["My head had begun to ache and my stomach felt funny. 我的頭開始疼了，我的胃也感到不對勁。"]}]}]},"grand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"壯麗的，堂皇的；宏偉的，宏大的；傲慢的，高高在上的；令人愉快的；<非正式>出色的，極好的；總括的；（常用於大型建築物的名稱前）大的；（對上層社會的人的稱呼）大；（罪行）嚴重的；壯麗的，富麗堂皇的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>一千美元，一千英鎊；大鋼琴，三角鋼琴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a building or a piece of scenery as <b>grand</b>, you mean that its size or appearance is very impressive. 宏偉的","examples":["This grand building in the centre of town used to be the hub of the capital's social life. 這座位於城鎮中央的宏偉建築曾經是首都社交生活的中心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Grand</b> plans or actions are intended to achieve important results. (計劃等) 宏大的","examples":["Hamilton revealed his grand design for the economic future of the United States. 漢密爾頓透露了他對美國未來經濟的宏偉計劃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People who are <b>grand</b> think they are important or socially superior. 自視高貴的","examples":["He is grander and even richer than the Prince of Wales. 他自視比威爾士王子還要高貴、還要富有。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>grand</b> total is one that is the final amount or the final result of a calculation. 總計的","examples":["It came to a grand total of $220,329. 總計是$220329。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Grand</b> is often used in the names of buildings such as hotels, especially when they are very large. 大的 (常用於大建築物的名稱前)","examples":["They stayed at The Grand Hotel, Budapest. 他們下榻在布達佩斯大飯店。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grand</b> is a thousand dollars or a thousand pounds. 一千美元; 一千英鎊","examples":["They're paying you ten grand now for those adaptations of old plays. 他們現在要付你1萬美元作為那些老劇目的改編費用。"]}]}]},"glad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高興的；感激的；樂意的，非常願意的；令人愉快的，充滿歡樂的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>取悅，使高興"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>唐菖蒲屬植物，唐菖蒲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>glad</b> about something, you are happy and pleased about it. 高興的","examples":["The people seem genuinely glad to see you. 人們看到你似乎真得很高興。","I'd be glad if the boys slept a little longer so I could do some ironing. 如果男孩子們多睡一會兒我就高興了，可以熨熨衣服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you will be <b>glad</b> <b>to</b> do something, usually for someone else, you mean that you are willing and eager to do it. 樂意的","examples":["I'll be glad to show you everything. 我將樂意向你展示每樣東西。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"高興地","examples":["Malcolm gladly accepted the invitation. 馬爾科姆欣然接受了邀請。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"樂意地","examples":["The counsellors will gladly baby-sit during their free time. 諮詢員在空閒時也會樂意照看一下孩子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"gladiolus的縮寫 (Also called (Austral) gladdie)","examples":[]}]}]},"huge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"龐大的，極大的；<非正式>很受歡迎的，著名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>huge</b> is extremely large in size. (尺寸) 巨大的","examples":["...a tiny little woman with huge black glasses. …一位個子很小的戴著碩大黑色眼鏡的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>huge</b> is extremely large in amount or degree. (數量或程度) 極大的","examples":["I have a huge number of ties because I never throw them away. 我有非常多的領帶，因為我從不扔掉它們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>huge</b> exists or happens on a very large scale, and involves a lot of different people or things. (規模上) 極大的","examples":["Another team is looking at the huge problem of debts between companies. 另一組人正在研究公司間債務這個大問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(數量或程度) 極大地","examples":["In summer this hotel is a hugely popular venue for wedding receptions. 夏天，這家飯店是非常受歡迎的婚宴場所。"]}]}]},"happy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"快樂的；幸福的，使人高興的；滿意的；樂意的；幸運的；合適的"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"<非正式>濫用……的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>happy</b> has feelings of pleasure, usually because something nice has happened or because they feel satisfied with their life. 快樂的","examples":["Marina was a confident, happy child. 瑪麗娜是個自信、快樂的孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>happy</b> time, place, or relationship is full of happy feelings and pleasant experiences, or has an atmosphere in which people feel happy. 令人愉快的","examples":["Except for her illnesses, she had a particularly happy childhood. 除了幾場病痛之外，她有個特別快樂的童年。","It had always been a happy place. 這裡從前一直是個令人愉快的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>happy</b> <b>about</b> a situation or arrangement, you are satisfied with it, for example, because you think that something is being done in the right way. 對...滿意的","examples":["If you are not happy about a repair, go back and complain. 如果你對修理不滿意，就回去投訴。","He's happy that I deal with it myself. 他對我自己處理這件事感到很滿意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say you are <b>happy</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you are very willing to do it. 樂意的","examples":["I'll be happy to answer questions if there are any. 如果有什麼問題的話，我將很樂意回答。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Happy</b> is used in greetings and other conventional expressions to say that you hope someone will enjoy a special occasion. (表示祝賀) 快樂","examples":["Happy Birthday! 生日快樂！"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"快樂地","examples":["Albert leaned back happily and lit a cigarette. 艾伯特開心地向後斜靠著並點燃一支香菸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"樂意地","examples":["If I've caused any offence over something I have written, I will happily apologize. 如果我所寫的東西冒犯了他人，我將很樂意道歉。"]}]}]},"hungry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感到餓的，飢餓的；渴望的，熱望的；使人飢餓的，引起食慾的；不毛的，貧瘠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>hungry</b>, you want some food because you have not eaten for some time and have an uncomfortable or painful feeling in your stomach. 飢餓的","examples":["My friend was hungry, so we drove to a shopping mall to get some food. 我朋友餓了，於是我們就驅車來到一家購物商場買些吃的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>hungry</b> for something, you are emphasizing that they want it very much. 渴望的","examples":["I was hungry to be heard by my contemporaries. 我渴望被同齡人所傾聽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hungry</b> is also a combining form. 渴望…的 (用作構詞成分)","examples":["...power-hungry politicians. …渴求權力的政客們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"飢餓地","examples":["James ate hungrily. 詹姆斯狼吞虎嚥地吃了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熱望地","examples":["He looked at her hungrily. What eyes! What skin! 他如飢似渴地望著她。多美的眼睛啊！多好的皮膚啊！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>go hungry</b>, they do not have enough food to eat. 捱餓","examples":["They brought her meat so that she never went hungry. 他們給她帶來了肉，這樣她就再也不用捱餓了。"]}]}]},"heavy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重的，沉的；大量的，嚴重的；大而結實的，不精緻的；厚實的；充滿（某物）（heavy with）；重型的，大型的；繁忙的；辛苦的，費力的；用力的，重重的；難消化的；難懂的，艱澀的；危險的，洶湧的；悶熱的，沉悶的；濃郁的；（土壤）黏重的；苛刻的，嚴厲的；認真的，嚴肅的；（聲音）粗重的；（身體部位）沉重的；（心情）憂傷的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"保鏢，打手；（電影或戲劇中的）反派；<非正式>重要人物；<英，非正式> 嚴肅報紙（heavies）；<蘇格蘭>烈性啤酒"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"濃濃地，沉重地；使不安，使擔憂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>heavy</b> weighs a lot. 重的","examples":["These scissors are awfully heavy. 這些剪刀非常重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>heavy</b> to ask or talk about how much someone or something weighs. 重的","examples":["How heavy are you? 你有多重？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Heavy</b> means great in amount, degree, or intensity. 大量的; 過度的; 強烈的","examples":["Heavy fighting has been going on. 激戰一直在進行。","He worried about her heavy drinking. 他為她的酗酒感到擔憂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>heavy</b> meal is large in amount and often difficult to digest. 量大而難以消化的","examples":["He had been feeling drowsy, the effect of an unusually heavy meal. 他一直感到昏昏欲睡，因為吃了一頓異常量大而難以消化的飯、菜。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>heavy with</b> things is full of them or loaded with them. 充滿了…的","examples":["The air is heavy with moisture. 空氣中充滿了溼氣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a person's breathing is <b>heavy</b>, it is very loud and deep. 粗重的 (呼吸)","examples":["Her breathing became slow and heavy. 她的呼吸變得緩慢而粗重。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>heavy</b> movement or action is done with a lot of force or pressure. 粗重的","examples":["...a heavy blow on the back of the skull. …後腦勺上的一記重擊。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>heavy</b> machine or piece of military equipment is very large and very powerful. 重型的","examples":["...government militia backed by tanks and heavy artillery. …有坦克和重炮支援的政府民兵組織。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you describe a period of time or a schedule as <b>heavy</b>, you mean it involves a lot of work. 繁忙的","examples":["It's been a heavy day and I'm tired. 這是繁忙的一天，我累壞了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Heavy</b> work requires a lot of strength or energy. 繁重的","examples":["The business is thriving and Philippa employs two full-timers for the heavy work. 生意很興隆，於是菲莉帕僱了兩名全職員工來乾重活兒。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>heavy on</b> another thing, you mean that it uses a lot of that thing or too much of that thing. 耗費…的","examples":["Tanks are heavy on fuel, destructive to roads and difficult to park. 坦克耗油量大，對道路有破壞性，並且難以停放。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"Air or weather that is <b>heavy</b> is unpleasantly still, hot, and damp. (空氣或天氣) 陰沉的; 悶熱的; 潮溼的","examples":["The outside air was heavy and moist and sultry. 戶外的空氣陰沉、潮溼而悶熱。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A situation that is <b>heavy</b> is serious and difficult to cope with. 棘手的","examples":["I don't want any more of that heavy stuff. 我可再也不想碰那種麻煩事兒了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沉重","examples":["...a sensation of warmth and heaviness in the muscles. …一種肌肉的溫暖和沉重感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>heavy</b> is a large strong man who is employed to protect a person or place, often by using violence. You can also use <b>heavy</b> to refer to a male character who represents such a man in a film or play. 保鏢; 打手","examples":["They had employed heavies to evict squatters from neighbouring sites. 他們僱了一些打手，以趕走來自鄰近地區的私自佔地者。","In 1943, he received his first role as a heavy in \"Double Indemnity.\" 1943年，他接了第一個角色，在影片《雙重保險》中扮演保鏢。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"大量地; 過度地; 強烈地","examples":["It has been raining heavily all day. 一整天雨都下得很大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"粗重地","examples":["She sank back on the pillow and closed her eyes, breathing heavily as if asleep. 她躺回到枕頭上，閉上雙眼，呼吸粗重，就像睡熟了似的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"粗重地","examples":["I sat down heavily on the ground beside the road. 我重重地坐在路邊的地上。"]}]}]},"big":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尺寸、數量、規模或年齡）大的；重大的，嚴重的；有影響力的；糟糕的；有雄心的；受歡迎的；熱衷於……的；程度深的，效果好的；大方的，大度的；生僻的，晦澀的；大寫的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大大，給人印象深地；誇口地；大量地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"招搖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>big</b> person or thing is large in physical size. (體積、體態) 大的","examples":["Australia's a big country. 澳大利亞是一個幅員遼闊的國家。","Her husband was a big man. 她丈夫是個身材高大的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>big</b> consists of many people or things. (數量) 多的","examples":["The crowd included a big contingent from Cleveland. 人群中包括一個來自克利夫蘭的大型代表團。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as a problem, increase, or change as a <b>big</b> one, you mean it is great in degree, extent, or importance. 重大的; 嚴重的","examples":["Her problem was just too big for her to tackle on her own. 她的問題太嚴重了，她無法獨力應付。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>big</b> organization employs many people and has many customers. (規模) 大的","examples":["...one of the biggest companies in Italy. …義大利規模最大的公司之一。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>big</b> <b>in</b> a particular organization, activity, or place, you mean that they have a lot of influence or authority in it. 有影響力的","examples":["Their father was very big in the army. 他們的父親在軍界很有威望。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>big</b> bully or a <b>big</b> coward, you are emphasizing your disapproval of them. (用以強調厭惡等語氣) 大的","examples":["His personality changed. He turned into a big bully. 他性格變了，成了一個大壞蛋。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Children often refer to their older brother or sister as their <b>big</b> brother or sister. 年齡較大的","examples":["She always introduces me as her big sister. 她總對別人介紹我是她的姐姐。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Big</b> words are long or rare words which have meanings that are difficult to understand. 艱深難懂的 (詞)","examples":["They use a lot of big words. 他們用許多難懂的大詞。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make it big</b>, you become successful or famous. 獲得巨大成功","examples":["Capone was an underdog hero, a poor boy who made it big. 卡彭是個草莽英雄，一個飛黃騰達了的窮小子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>think big</b>, you make plans on a large scale, often using a lot of time, effort, or money. 著眼大局","examples":["Maybe we're not thinking big enough. 也許我們不夠著眼大局。"]}]}]},"full":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滿的，滿是……的；飽的；最大量的；完整的，詳盡的；足足的；圓潤的，濃郁的；充實的；正式的；寬鬆的；豐滿的；（書面裝訂材料）用於全書面裝訂的；（頭髮）過肩的，披肩的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"充分地，完全地；恰好，直接地；非常，極其"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>盛期，頂點；月亮的滿月（期）；<古>全部，整個"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝滿，使充滿；把（織物）打多褶（或大褶）以使（衣服）寬鬆；<美>（月）變圓,（潮）漲；使（布料）縮呢（或縮絨、氈化）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>full</b>, it contains as much of a substance or as many objects as it can. 裝滿的","examples":["Once the container is full, it stays shut until you turn it clockwise. 該容器一旦滿了就會保持關閉，直到你將其按順時針方向旋轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place or thing <b>is full of</b> things or people, it contains a large number of them. 滿是…的","examples":["The case was full of clothes. 該箱子滿是衣服。","The streets are still full of debris from two nights of rioting. 那些街上依然滿是兩夜暴亂後的狼藉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that a place or vehicle is <b>full</b> when there is no space left in it for any more people or things. (某處、車輛) 滿的","examples":["The parking lot was full when I left about 10:45. 停車場在我10:45左右離開時已滿了。","They stay here a few hours before being sent to refugee camps, which are now almost full. 他們在這裡呆了幾個小時後被送到了難民營，難民營現在幾乎滿了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your hands or arms are <b>full</b>, you are carrying or holding as much as you can carry. (雙手) 拿滿的; (雙臂) 抱滿的","examples":["Sylvia entered, her arms full of packages. 西爾維婭進來了，懷裡抱滿了包裹。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you feel <b>full</b>, you have eaten or drunk so much that you do not want anything else. (感到) 飽的","examples":["It's healthy to eat when I'm hungry and to stop when I'm full. 我餓了就吃、飽了就停是有益健康的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is full of</b> a particular feeling or quality, they have a lot of it. 充滿 (某種感情或品質) 的","examples":["I feel full of confidence and so open to possibilities. 我感到充滿信心且對各種可能都願意接受。","Mom's face was full of pain. 媽媽的臉上充滿了痛苦。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>full</b> before a noun to indicate that you are referring to all the details, things, or people that it can possibly include. 全部的","examples":["Full details will be sent to you once your application has been accepted. 一旦您的申請被接受，全部的細節資料將寄給您。","May I have your full name? 我能知道您的全名嗎？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Full</b> is used to describe a sound, light, or physical force which is being produced with the greatest possible power or intensity. 最大的 (音量、力); 最強的 (光)","examples":["From his study came the sound of Mahler, playing at full volume. 從他的書房裡傳來了馬勒的音樂，以最大的音量在播放。","Officials say the operation will be carried out in full daylight. 官員們說此項活動將在大白天進行。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>full</b> to emphasize the completeness, intensity, or extent of something. 充分的","examples":["We should conserve oil and gas by making full use of other energy sources. 我們應該透過充分利用其他能源節約石油和天然氣。","The lane leading to the farm was in full view of the house windows. 通往農場的那條車道從那房子的窗戶可一覽無餘。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>full</b> statement or report contains a lot of information and detail. 詳盡的 (陳述、報告)","examples":["Mr. Primakov gave a full account of his meeting with the president. 普里馬科夫先生對他與總統的會面給予了詳盡的敘述。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that someone has or leads a <b>full</b> life, you approve of the fact that they are always busy and do a lot of different things. 充實的 (生活)","examples":["You will be successful in whatever you do and you will have a very full and interesting life. 你在你做的任何事情中都會很成功，你會擁有非常充實而有趣的生活。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>full</b> to refer to something which gives you all the rights, status, or importance for a particular position or activity, rather than just some of them. (權力、地位、重要性等) 完全的","examples":["How did the meeting go, did you get your full membership? 會議進行得如何？你得到了完全會員資格嗎？"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A <b>full</b> flavour is strong and rich. (味道) 濃郁的","examples":["Italian plum tomatoes have a full flavour, and are best for cooking. 義大利李子形番茄有著濃郁的味道，最適合烹飪。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you describe a part of someone's body as <b>full</b>, you mean that it is rounded and quite large. (身體) 豐滿的","examples":["The Juno Collection specializes in large sizes for ladies with a fuller figure. 朱諾時裝店專賣適合體型比較豐滿的女士的大號女裝。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"A <b>full</b> skirt or sleeve is wide and has been made from a lot of fabric. 寬大多褶的 (裙子、袖子)","examples":["My wedding dress has a very full skirt so I need to wear a good quality slip. 我的結婚禮服有一個非常寬大多褶的下襬，所以我需要穿一條質地好的襯裙。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"When there is a <b>full</b> moon, the moon appears as a bright, complete circle. 圓的 (月亮)","examples":["...those nights when the moon is full. …那些月圓之夜。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"飽","examples":["High fibre diets give the feeling of fullness. 高纖維飲食給人飽腹感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"寬大","examples":["The coat has raglan sleeves, and is cut to give fullness at the back. 這件外套有一對插肩袖，剪裁得使背部寬大。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>full</b> to emphasize the force or directness with which someone or something is hit or looked at. 徑直地","examples":["She kissed him full on the mouth. 她嘴正對嘴地吻了他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that something has been done or described <b>in full</b> when everything that was necessary has been done or described. 全部地; 全面地","examples":["The medical experts have yet to report in full. 醫學專家們還得全面彙報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a person <b>knows full well</b> that something is true, especially something unpleasant, you are emphasizing that they are definitely aware of it, although they may behave as if they are not. 十分清楚","examples":["He knew full well he'd be ashamed of himself later. 他十分清楚他以後會為自己感到羞愧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is done or experienced <b>to the full</b> is done to as great an extent as is possible. 充分地","examples":["She probably has a good mind, which should be used to the full. 她可能有個好腦子，應該充分加以利用。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of cloth, yarn, etc) to become or to make (cloth, yarn, etc) heavier and more compact during manufacture through shrinking and beating or pressing 使(布、紗等)透過皺縮、擊打或壓迫的製造過程變得更重及更緊密","examples":[]}]}]},"important":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重要的，重大的；（人）影響很大的，權威的；大量的，許多的；自負的，自命不凡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>important</b> is very significant, is highly valued, or is necessary. 重要的","examples":["The most important thing in my life was my career. 我生活中最重要的部分是我的事業。","It's important to answer her questions as honestly as you can. 重要的是你要儘可能如實地回答她的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>important</b> has influence or power within a society or a particular group. 有勢力的","examples":["...an important figure in the media world. …一位傳媒界有勢力的人物。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"重要地","examples":["I was hungry, and, more importantly, my children were hungry. 我餓了，更重要的是，我的孩子們餓了。"]}]}]},"lazy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"懶惰的，不願工作的；悠閒的，懶洋洋的；粗心的，馬虎的；行進緩慢的，慢吞吞的；<美>（牲口身上的烙印）打在一側的"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"懶散地移動或躺下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>lazy</b>, they do not want to work or make any effort to do anything. 懶惰的","examples":["Lazy and incompetent police officers are letting the public down. 懶惰無能的警官們讓公眾失望。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>lazy</b> to describe an activity or event in which you are very relaxed and which you do or take part in without making much effort. 悠懶的","examples":["Her latest novel is perfect for a lazy summer's afternoon's reading. 她的最新小說是悠懶的夏日午後的完美讀物。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"懶惰","examples":["Current employment laws will be changed to reward effort and punish laziness. 現行的僱傭法將被修改以便獎勤罰懶。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悠懶地","examples":["Liz went back into the kitchen, stretching lazily. 莉茲回到廚房，悠懶地伸了伸腰。"]}]}]},"hot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱的，高溫的；（使人）感到熱的；辣的；活躍的，激烈的；棘手的，危險的；<非正式>熱門的；有望成功的；性感的；暴躁的；過激的，過火的；<非正式>（某方面）極好的；重視；（音樂）節奏強的；偷來的，難以銷贓的；快找到了，快猜中了；緊跟著的；帶電的；明亮的，鮮豔的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<西印度>使熱，變熱（hot up）；變得激烈（hot up）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"熱；熱切地，緊迫地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>hot</b> has a high temperature. 熱的","examples":["When the oil is hot, add the sliced onion. 油熱之後，加入切好的洋蔥。","What he needed was a hot bath and a good sleep. 他所需要的是泡個熱水澡和睡個好覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hot</b> is used to describe the weather or the air in a room or building when the temperature is high. (天氣) 炎熱的","examples":["It was too hot even for a gentle stroll. 這樣的天氣連慢慢散步都太熱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>hot</b>, you feel as if your body is at an unpleasantly high temperature. (人) 感到熱的","examples":["I was too hot and tired to eat more than a few mouthfuls. 我又熱又累，只能吃下幾口。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say that food is <b>hot</b> when it has a strong, burning taste caused by chillies, pepper, or other spices. (食物) 辛辣的","examples":["...hot curries. …辛辣的咖哩食品。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>hot</b> issue or topic is one that is very important at the present time and is receiving a lot of publicity. (問題或話題等) 熱門的","examples":["The role of women in war has been a hot topic of debate since the Gulf conflict. 自海灣衝突以來，女性在戰爭中的作用一直是一個熱門的爭論話題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Hot</b> news is new, recent, and fresh. (訊息) 最新的","examples":["...eight pages of the latest movies, video releases, and the hot news from Tinseltown. …有關最新電影、錄影新片以及好萊塢最新訊息的8頁內容。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>hot</b> to describe something that is very exciting and that many people want to see, use, obtain, or become involved with. 火爆的; 風行的","examples":["When I was in Chicago in 1990 a friend got me a ticket for the hottest show in town: the Monet Exhibition at the Art Institute. 1990年我在芝加哥的時候，一個朋友給我弄到了一張城裡最搶手的展覽門票：藝術學院的莫奈畫展。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>hot</b> contest is one that is intense and involves a great deal of activity and determination. (比賽等) 激烈的","examples":["It took hot competition from abroad, however, to show us just how good our product really is. 然而，正是來自國外的激烈競爭讓我們看到自己的產品有多好。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a person or team is the <b>hot</b> favourite, people think that they are the one most likely to win a race or competition. (比賽或競爭中) 最有可能得勝的","examples":["Atlantic City is the hot favourite to stage the fight. 大西洋城最有可能贏得這次拳擊賽的主辦權。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>hot</b> temper gets angry very quickly and easily. 暴躁的","examples":["His hot temper was making it increasingly difficult for others to work with him. 他暴躁的脾氣使得別人越來越難與他一起工作。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>hot</b>, you mean that they are sexually attractive or sexually desirable. 性感的","examples":["\"He's great,\" Caroline said, \"hot.\" “他太棒了，”卡羅琳說道，“性感極了。”","If a hot chick comes on to you, smile and walk away. 如果一個性感妞兒向你挑逗，你應該一笑走開。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>blows hot and cold</b>, they keep changing their attitude toward something, sometimes being very enthusiastic and at other times expressing no interest at all. 反覆無常","examples":["The media, meanwhile, has blown hot and cold over the affair. 同時，媒體對這件事的態度一直搖擺不定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>hot and bothered</b>, you are so worried and anxious that you cannot think clearly or behave sensibly. 焦慮不安的; 六神無主的","examples":["Ray was getting very hot and bothered about the idea. 雷為這個想法感到焦慮不安。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that one person <b>has the hots for</b> another, you mean that they feel a strong sexual attraction to that person. 對…有強烈的性吸引力","examples":["I've had the hots for him ever since he arrived. 自從他來到後，我就迷戀上他了。"]}]}]},"large":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尺寸、範圍、容量）大的；廣泛的，重要的；身材高大的；（公司或組織）大規模的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大號，同類中最大者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>（尤指跳舞和飲酒）作樂，狂歡"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"誇大地；大大地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>large</b> thing or person is greater in size than usual or average. 大的","examples":["The pike lives mainly in large rivers and lakes. 梭魚主要生活在大的江河湖泊裡。","In the largest room about a dozen children and seven adults are sitting on the carpet. 在最大的那個房間裡，十幾個孩子和七個大人正坐在地毯上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>large</b> amount or number of people or things is more than the average amount or number. 大量的","examples":["The gang finally fled with a large amount of cash and jewellery. 那幫歹徒最終帶著大量的現金和珠寶逃走了。","There are a large number of centres where you can take full-time courses. 這裡有很多你可以上全日制課程的培訓中心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Large</b> is used to indicate that a problem or issue which is being discussed is very important or serious. 重要的; 嚴重的","examples":["...the already large problem of under-age drinking. …已頗為嚴重的未成年人酗酒問題。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at large</b> to indicate that you are talking in a general way about most of the people mentioned. 大多數","examples":["I think the chances of getting reforms accepted by the community at large remain extremely remote. 我認為，讓該團體的大部分人都接受改革的希望仍然極其渺茫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a dangerous person, thing, or animal is <b>at large</b>, you mean that they have not been captured or made safe. 逍遙法外","examples":["The man who tried to have her killed is still at large. 企圖謀殺她的那個男人仍然逍遙法外。"]}]}]},"lucky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幸運的，走運的；吉祥的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that someone is <b>lucky</b> when they have something that is very desirable or when they are in a very desirable situation. 幸運的","examples":["I am luckier than most. I have a job. 我比大多數人幸運，有份工作。","He is incredibly lucky to be alive. 他竟然幸運地活了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>lucky</b> seems to always have good luck. 常走運的","examples":["Some people are born lucky, aren't they? 一些人天生好運不斷，不是嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe an action or experience as <b>lucky</b>, you mean that it was good or successful, and that it happened by chance and not as a result of planning or preparation. 僥倖的","examples":["They admit they are now desperate for a lucky break. 他們承認現在非常渴望交上好運。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>lucky</b> object is something that people believe helps them to be successful. 吉祥的","examples":["He did not have on his other lucky charm, a pair of green socks. 他沒穿另一件吉祥物：一雙綠襪子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>will be lucky</b> <b>to</b> do or get something, you mean that they are very unlikely to do or get it, and will definitely not do or get any more than that. 某人可就走運了 (指不太可能做成)","examples":["You'll be lucky if you get any breakfast. 如果你能弄到早餐那可就幸運了。","Those remaining in work will be lucky to get the smallest of pay increases. 那些仍在工作的人若能漲一點點薪水就算是幸運的了。"]}]}]},"noisy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嗓門大的，聒噪的；嘈雜的，充滿噪音的；吵吵嚷嚷的，譁眾取寵的；（尤指電子裝置的）干擾，干擾資訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>noisy</b> person or thing makes a lot of loud or unpleasant noise. 喧鬧的; 有噪音的","examples":["...my noisy old typewriter. …我的噪音大的舊打字機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>noisy</b> place is full of a lot of loud or unpleasant noise. 嘈雜的","examples":["It's a noisy place with film clips showing constantly on one of the cafe's giant screens. 這是一個嘈雜的地方，電影片斷不停地在咖啡廳其中一個大螢幕上放映。","The baggage hall was crowded and noisy. 行李大廳擁擠而嘈雜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>noisy</b>, you are critical of them for trying to attract attention to their views by frequently and forcefully discussing them. 過分渲染的; 譁眾取寵的","examples":["It might, at last, silence the small but noisy intellectual clique. 它或許最終能讓那個人數不多卻譁眾取寵的知識分子群體安靜下來。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"喧鬧地; 有噪音地","examples":["The students on the grass bank cheered noisily. 學生們在草堤上喧鬧地歡呼。"]}]}]},"mad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生氣的，氣憤的；極愚蠢的，很不明智的；混亂的，失控的；瘋癲的，患精神病的；狂熱的，著迷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>mad</b>, you mean that they are very angry. 狂怒的","examples":["You're just mad at me because I don't want to go. 因為我不想去，你就衝我發火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>mad</b> to describe people or things that you think are very foolish. 蠢瘋的","examples":["You'd be mad to work with him again. 你要是再和他一起工作就是蠢瘋了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>mad</b> has a mind that does not work in a normal way, with the result that their behaviour is very strange. (人) 瘋的","examples":["She was afraid of going mad. 她擔心變瘋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>mad about</b> something or someone, you like them very much. 瘋迷的","examples":["She's not as mad about sports as I am. 她不像我那樣對體育瘋迷。","He's mad about you. 他對你瘋迷。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Mad</b> is also a combining form. 瘋迷…的 (用於構成合成詞)","examples":["...his football-mad son. …他的瘋迷足球的兒子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Mad</b> behaviour is wild and uncontrolled. (行為) 瘋狂的","examples":["You only have an hour to complete the game so it's a mad dash against the clock. 你們只有一個小時完成比賽，因此這是和時間的一次瘋狂角逐。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"蠢瘋","examples":["It is political madness. 這是政治蠢瘋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"瘋","examples":["He was driven to the brink of madness. 他被逼到了瘋狂的邊緣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"瘋狂地","examples":["Down in the streets people were waving madly. 下面大街上，人們在瘋狂地揮手。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>drives</b> you <b>mad</b>, you mean that you find them extremely annoying. 使某人發瘋","examples":["There are certain things he does that drive me mad. 他乾的某些事使我發瘋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>like mad</b>, you do it very energetically or enthusiastically. 瘋了似地","examples":["He was weight training like mad. 他在瘋了似地進行舉重訓練。"]}]}]},"many":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"許多；（與單數名詞及動詞連用）許多，大量"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"許多；許多人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"許多的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大多數人（the many）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> to indicate that you are talking about a large number of people or things. 許多的","examples":["I don't think many people would argue with that. 我認為許多人對那都不會有爭議。","Not many films are made in Finland. 芬蘭出品的電影並不多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> after \"how\" to ask questions about numbers or quantities. You use <b>many</b> after \"how\" in reported clauses to talk about numbers or quantities. 用於(how)之後，詢問數量多少","examples":["How many years have you been here? 你在這兒多少年了？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> with \"as\" when you are comparing numbers of things or people. 和(as)連用，用於比較物或人的數量","examples":["I've always entered as many photo competitions as I can. 我總是儘可能多地參加攝影比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Many</b> is also a pronoun. 許多","examples":["We stood up, thinking through the possibilities. There weren't many. 我們站起來，考慮著各種可能的情況，並無多少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Many</b> is also a pronoun. 用於(how)之後，作代詞","examples":["How many do you smoke a day? 你一天吸多少支菸？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Many</b> is also a pronoun. 和(as)連用，作代詞","examples":["Let the child try on as many as she likes. 讓這個孩子愛試穿多少就試多少吧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> to mean \"many people.\" 許多人","examples":["Iris Murdoch was regarded by many as a supremely good and serious writer. 艾里斯·默多克被許多人認為是一位極其出色而又嚴肅的作家。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Many</b> is also a quantifier. 許多","examples":["So, once we have cohabited, why do many of us feel the need to get married? 那麼，一旦我們同居了，為何我們中的許多人就覺得有必要結婚呢？","It seems there are not very many of them left in the sea. 似乎在海洋中它們所剩不多了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Many</b> is also an adjective. 許多的","examples":["Among his many hobbies was the breeding of fine horses. 在他的眾多愛好中有飼養名馬。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> in expressions such as \"not many,\" \"not very many,\" and \"too many\" when replying to questions about numbers of things or people. 多","examples":["\"How many of the songs that dealt with this theme became hit songs?\"—\"Not very many.\" “有多少關於這個主題的歌曲成為了暢銷歌曲？”—“不太多。”"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>many</b> followed by \"a\" and a noun to emphasize that there are a lot of people or things involved in something. 許多 (用於)(a)(+單數名詞之前)","examples":["Many a mother tries to act out her unrealized dreams through her daughter. 許多母親都試圖透過女兒實現她們未能實現的夢想。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The many</b> means a large group of people, especially the ordinary people in society, considered as separate from a particular small group. 多數人","examples":["The printing press gave power to a few to change the world for the many. 印刷機賦予了少數人為多數人改變世界的力量。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as many as</b> before a number to suggest that it is surprisingly large. 多達","examples":["As many as 4 million people watched today's parade. 多達400萬的人觀看了今天的遊行。"]}]}]},"nice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"美好的，令人愉快的；好心的，友好的；（天氣）溫暖的，宜人的；（觀點、區別等）細緻的，微妙的；（用於打招呼）很高興見到你；幹得好的，出色的；壞的，令人不愉快的；正派的，有教養的；<古>挑剔的，謹慎的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"尼斯（法國城市，Nice）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>nice</b>, you mean that you find it attractive, pleasant, or enjoyable. 好看的; 令人愉快的","examples":["I think silk ties can be quite nice. 我覺得真絲領帶會非常好看。","It's nice to be here together again. 又在這兒相聚太好了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>nice of</b> someone to say or do something, you are saying that they are being kind and thoughtful. This is often used as a way of thanking someone. 體貼人的 (常表謝意)","examples":["It's awfully nice of you to come all this way to see me. 你大老遠趕來看我，真是太體貼了。","\"How are your boys?\"—\"How nice of you to ask.\" “你的兒子們好嗎？”—“勞您惦記”。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>nice</b>, you mean that you like them because they are friendly and pleasant. 友好的; 可愛的","examples":["I've met your father and he's rather nice. 我見過你父親了，他非常和藹可親。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>nice</b> <b>to</b> people, you are friendly, pleasant, or polite toward them. 對…友好的; 對…親切的","examples":["She met Mr. and Mrs. Ricciardi, who were very nice to her. 她見到了裡恰爾迪先生和太太，他們對她非常友好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When the weather is <b>nice</b>, it is warm and pleasant. (天氣) 宜人的","examples":["He nodded to us and said, \"Nice weather we're having.\" 他對我們點點頭說：“我們遇上好天氣了。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>nice</b> to emphasize a particular quality that you like. 令人喜愛的 (用於加強語氣)","examples":["With a nice dark colour, the wine is medium to full bodied. 這種葡萄酒具有令人喜愛的深色調，從中度到高度都有。","I'll explain it nice and simply so you can understand. 我會把它解釋得清楚簡單，以便你能明白。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>nice</b> when you are greeting people. For example, you can say \"<b>Nice to meet you</b>,\" \"<b>Nice to have met you</b>,\" or \"<b>Nice to see you</b>.\" 很高興的 (用於打招呼)","examples":["Good morning. Nice to meet you and thanks for being with us this weekend. 早上好！很高興認識大家，謝謝和我們共度這個週末。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"好看地; 令人愉快地","examples":["He's just written a book, nicely illustrated and not too technical. 他剛寫完一本書，插圖精美，專業性也不是太強。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"對…友好地; 對…親切地","examples":["He treated you very nicely and acted like a decent guy. 他待你很好，行為舉止非常得體。"]}]}]},"new":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"新出現的，新興的；新買的；未用過的，嶄新的；有別於從前的，新穎的；新發現的，新近知道的；生疏的，未體驗過的；現代的，最新型的；新時期的，新開始的；富有朝氣的，生氣勃勃的；時鮮的（蔬菜）；更新的，變樣的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於構成複合詞）新的，新近的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"新東西，新事物（the new）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>new</b> has been recently created, built, or invented or is in the process of being created, built, or invented. 新的","examples":["They've just opened a new hotel in the area. 他們剛在該地區新開了一家旅館。","These ideas are nothing new. 這些想法並不新鮮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>new</b> has not been used or owned by anyone. 嶄新的","examples":["That afternoon she went out and bought a new dress. 那天下午她出去買了一條新裙子。","There are many boats, new and used, for sale. 有許多新船和舊船出售。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>new</b> to describe something which has replaced another thing, for example because you no longer have the old one, or it no longer exists, or it is no longer useful. 更新的","examples":["Under the new rules, some factories will cut emissions by as much as 90 percent. 根據新規定，一些工廠將要削減多達90%的排放量。","I had to find somewhere new to live. 我不得不找個新住處。","Rachel has a new boyfriend. 雷切爾交了一個新的男朋友。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>New</b> is used to describe something that has only recently been discovered or noticed. 新發現的","examples":["The new planet is about ten times the size of the earth. 這個新發現的行星大約是地球大小的10倍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>new</b> day or year is the beginning of the next day or year. 新開始的 (一天、一年等)","examples":["The start of a new year is a good time to reflect on the many achievements of the past. 新年伊始正是回顧過去許多成績的好時候。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>New</b> is used to describe someone or something that has recently acquired a particular status or position. 新具有某一身份的","examples":["...the usual exhaustion of a new mother. …初為人母常有的疲憊不堪。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you are <b>new</b> <b>to</b> a situation or place, or if the situation or place is <b>new</b> <b>to</b> you, you have not previously seen it or had any experience with it. 新接觸的","examples":["She wasn't new to the company. 她對於公司來說並非是新人。","His name was new to me then and it stayed in my mind. 那時他的名字對我來說是陌生的，後來我記住了它。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>New</b> potatoes, carrots, or peas are produced early in the season for such vegetables and are usually small with a sweet flavour. 時鮮的 (蔬菜)","examples":["Serve with a salad and new potatoes. 配著色拉和時鮮土豆一起吃。"]}]}]},"old":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）……歲的，（事物）存在……久的；年老的，年紀大的；衰老的；古老的，歷史悠久的；陳舊的；過去的，從前的；原來（屬於自己的）的；結識久的；<非正式>（表示親暱）老……；（語言形式）古的，早期的；老派的，守舊的；老一套的，經歷多次的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"老年人；某個年齡段的人；古時"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>old</b> has lived for many years and is no longer young. 年老的","examples":["...a white-haired old man. …一位白髮老人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>old</b> to talk about how many days, weeks, months, or years someone or something has lived or existed. …歲的; …久的","examples":["He was abandoned by his father when he was three months old. 他3個月大的時候被父親遺棄了。","How old are you now? 你現在多大了？","Bill was six years older than David. 比爾比戴維大6歲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>old</b> has existed for a long time. 古老的","examples":["She loved the big old house. 她喜愛那座古老的大房子。","These books must be very old. 這些書一定年頭很久了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>old</b> is no longer in good condition because of its age or because it has been used a lot. 破舊的","examples":["He took a bunch of keys from the pocket of his old corduroy trousers. 他從他那條破舊的燈心絨褲子口袋裡掏出了一串鑰匙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>old</b> to refer to something that is no longer used, that no longer exists, or that has been replaced by something else. 廢棄的; 過時的","examples":["The old road had disappeared under grass and heather. 這條廢棄的道路已消失在草叢和石南花中。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>old</b> to refer to something that used to belong to you, or to a person or thing that used to have a particular role in your life. 從前 (擁有或珍惜) 的","examples":["I'll make up the bed in your old room. 我會把你以前房間的床鋪收拾好。","I still have affection for my old school. 我對母校依然很有感情。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"An <b>old</b> friend, enemy, or rival is someone who has been your friend, enemy, or rival for a long time. 多年的","examples":["I called my old friend John Horner. 我給老朋友約翰·霍納打了個電話。","Mr. Brownson, I assure you, King's an old enemy of mine. 布朗森先生，我向你保證，金是我的夙敵。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>old</b> to express affection when talking to or about someone you know. (表示親暱) 老…","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The old</b> are people who are old. 老年人","examples":["...providing a caring response for the needs of the old and the handicapped. …對老年人和殘疾人的需要做出一個充滿關懷的回應。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>any old</b> to emphasize that the quality or type of something is not important. If you say that a particular thing is <b>not</b> <b>any old</b> thing, you are emphasizing how special or famous it is. 隨便的/非同一般的","examples":["Any old paper will do. 隨便一張紙就行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>In the old days</b> means in the past, before things changed. 以前","examples":["In the old days, doctors made housecalls. 以前，醫生們都上門看病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people refer to <b>the good old days</b>, they are referring to a time in the past when they think that life was better than it is now. 過去的好時光","examples":["He remembers the good old days when everyone in his village knew him and you could leave your door open at night. 他常想起過去的好時光。那時，村裡人都認識他，而且大家夜不閉戶。"]}]}]},"possible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可能的，可能做到的；可能發生的，可能存在的；合乎事實的，合理的；儘可能……的；（用於形容詞後表示強調）最好的（或最差的等）；可能的（但可能性很小）；（數字或分數）最高的；如果可能的話"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能適合的人（事物）；可能性，能完成的事（the possible）；（尤指射擊比賽的）最高分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>possible</b> to do something, it can be done. (做某事) 可能的","examples":["If it is possible to find out where your brother is, we will. 如果有可能找到你哥哥的下落，我們會找的。","Everything is possible if we want it enough. 如果我們非常想要的話，任何事都是有可能的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>possible</b> event is one that might happen. 可能 (發生) 的","examples":["He referred the matter to the attorney general for possible action against several newspapers. 他將此事交給首席檢察官處理，以求可能訴訟幾家報社。","One possible solution, if all else fails, is to take legal action. 如果其他方案都不行，一個可能的解決辦法就是提起訴訟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>possible</b> <b>that</b> something is true or correct, you mean that although you do not know whether it is true or correct, you accept that it might be. 可能 (真實) 的","examples":["It is possible that there's an explanation for all this. 這一切可能真有個解釋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>as</b> soon <b>as possible</b>, you do it as soon as you can. If you get <b>as</b> much <b>as possible</b> of something, you get as much of it as you can. 儘可能的 (早、多等)","examples":["Please make your decision as soon as possible. 請儘可能快地出你們的決定。","Mrs. Pollard decided to learn as much as possible about the country before going there. 波拉德夫人決定儘可能多地瞭解那個國家後再去那兒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>possible</b> with superlative adjectives to emphasize that something has more or less of a quality than anything else of its kind. 和形容詞最高階連用，表示“最…不過”","examples":["They have joined the job market at the worst possible time. 他們在一個最遭糕不過的時候進入了職場。","We expressed in the clearest possible way our disappointment, hurt, and anger. 我們以最清晰不過的方式表達了我們的失望、傷痛和憤怒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you describe someone as, for example, a <b>possible</b> governor, you mean that they could be elected as governor. 可能 (當選) 的","examples":["Government sources are now openly speculating about a possible successor for Dr. Lawrence. 各官方訊息源現在正公開地推測繼勞倫斯博士之任的可能人選。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Possible</b> is also a noun. 可能的人","examples":["Kennedy, who divorced wife Joan in 1982, was tipped as a presidential possible. 1982年和妻子瓊離婚的肯尼迪被認為最可能成為總統人選。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The possible</b> is everything that can be done in a situation. 可能的事","examples":["He is a Democrat with the skill, nerve, and ingenuity to push the limits of the possible. 作為民主黨人，他有著技巧、膽量和智謀來利用一切可能性。"]}]}]},"other":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（表示與已知的人或事物不同）別的，另外的；（表示在與已知的人或事物同一類中）別的，另外的；（兩個中）另一的；（一組人或事物中）其餘的；（用於列舉之後）其他的；對面的，相反方向的；（泛指）別（人）的，他（人）的；最近的，前不久的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（表示與已知的人或事物不同）另外；（表示在與已知的人或事物同一類中）另外；（兩個中）另一個（the other）；其餘的人（或事物）（the others）；（用於列舉之後）其他；對面，相反方向（the other）；<非正式>性交（the other）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……看作異類，以異類對待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>other</b> to refer to an additional thing or person of the same type as one that has been mentioned or is known about. 其他的 (指屬於同一類別的)","examples":["They were just like any other young couple. 他們那時就和其他任何年輕夫婦一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>other</b> to indicate that a thing or person is not the one already mentioned, but a different one. 別的 (指屬於不同型別的)","examples":["The authorities insist that the discussions must not be linked to any other issue. 官方堅持這些討論絕不能和任何別的問題聯絡起來。","He would have to accept it; there was no other way. 他不得不接受它，沒有別的辦法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> <b>other</b> to refer to the second of two things or people when the identity of the first is already known or understood, or has already been mentioned. (兩個中) 另一個的","examples":["The captain was at the other end of the room. 隊長在房間的另一頭。","You deliberately went in the other direction. 你故意朝另一個方向走了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>other</b> at the end of a list or a group of examples, to refer generally to people or things like the ones just mentioned. (泛指) 其他的","examples":["The new Station Centre will have shops, restaurants and other amenities. 新的中央車站將會有商店、飯店及其他設施。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> <b>other</b> to refer to the rest of the people or things in a group, when you are talking about one particular person or thing. 其餘的","examples":["When the other kids were taken to the zoo, he was left behind. 其餘的孩子被帶去動物園時，他被留了下來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Other</b> people are people in general, as opposed to yourself or a person you have already mentioned. (總稱) 他人的","examples":["The suffering of other people appals me. 他人的苦難使我大為震驚。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>other</b> in informal expressions of time such as <b>the other day</b>, <b>the other evening</b>, or <b>the other week</b> to refer to a day, evening, or week in the recent past. (不久) 以前的","examples":["I called her the other day and she said she'd like to come over. 我前幾天給她打電話，她說她想過來。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Other</b> is also a pronoun. 其他","examples":["Four crewmen were killed, one other was injured. 四名船員被殺，另外一個受了傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Other</b> is also a pronoun. 別的","examples":["This issue, more than any other, has divided her cabinet. 正是這個問題，而不是任何別的問題，使她的內閣產生了分裂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Other</b> is also a pronoun. 其他","examples":["Descartes received his stimulus from the new physics and astronomy of Copernicus, Galileo, and others. 笛卡兒從哥白尼、伽利略和其他科學家的新物理學和天文學中獲得了靈感。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>others</b> is also a pronoun. 其餘","examples":["Aubrey's on his way here, with the others. 奧布里和其餘的人正在來這兒的路上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>other</b> is also a pronoun. 另一個","examples":["Almost everybody had a cigarette in one hand and a martini in the other. 幾乎每個人都是一手一支香菸，一手一杯馬提尼酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Others</b> means the same as <b>other people</b>. 他人","examples":["His humour depended on contempt for others. 他的幽默基於對他人的蔑視。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions like <b>among other</b> things or <b>among others</b> to indicate that there are several more facts, things, or people like the one or ones mentioned, but that you do not intend to mention them all. 除了別的以外 (表省略不多言)","examples":["He moved to Ohio in 2005 where, among other things, he worked as a journalist. 他2005年搬到了俄亥俄州。在那兒除了做其他事情外，他還當了記者。","His travels took him to Peru, among other places. 他除了去其他地方之外，還旅行到了秘魯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens, for example, <b>every other day</b> or <b>every other month</b>, there is a day or month when it does not happen between each day or month when it happens. 每隔一天 (或一週、一月等)","examples":["Their food is adequate. It includes meat at least every other day, vegetables and fruit. 他們的食物足夠了，有蔬菜和水果，至少每隔一天還有肉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>every other</b> to emphasize that you are referring to all the rest of the people or things in a group. 所有其他的","examples":["The same will apply in every other country. 這同樣將適用於所有其他的國家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>nothing other than</b> and <b>no other than</b> when you are going to mention a course of action, decision, or description and emphasize that it is the only one possible in the situation. 只有","examples":["Nothing other than an immediate custodial sentence could be justified. 只有立即判處監禁才合理。","The rebels would not be happy with anything other than the complete removal of the current regime. 叛亂者們只有徹底推翻現政權才會高興。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>or other</b> in expressions like <b>somehow or other</b> and <b>someone or other</b> to indicate that you cannot or do not want to be more precise about the information that you are giving. 什麼什麼的 (指模糊說法)","examples":["I was going to have him called away from the house on some pretext or other. 我當時正打算用什麼藉口，讓人把他從房子裡叫出去。","The foundation is holding a dinner in honour of something or other. 基金會正設宴慶祝著什麼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>other than</b> after a negative statement to say that the person, item, or thing that follows is the only exception to the statement. 除了…之外","examples":["She makes no reference to any feminist work other than her own. 除了自己的作品之外，她根本不提任何其他女權主義作品。"]}]}]},"poor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"貧窮的；可憐的，不幸的；（身體）虛弱的，衰弱的；不擅長的，不熟練的；劣質的，差的，次的；貧乏的；（數量、比率等）不理想的，不合理的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>poor</b> has very little money and few possessions. (人) 貧窮的","examples":["The reason our schools cannot afford better teachers is because people here are poor. 我們學校請不起更好的老師是因為這裡的人窮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The people in a <b>poor</b> country or area have very little money and few possessions. 貧困的 (國家、地區等)","examples":["Many countries in the Third World are as poor as they have ever been. 許多第三世界國家一如既往地貧困。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>poor</b> to express your sympathy for someone. 可憐的","examples":["I feel sorry for that poor child. 我為那個可憐的孩子感到難過。","It was way too much for the poor guy to overcome. 它對那個可憐的傢伙來講太難客服。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>poor</b>, you mean that it is of a low quality or standard or that it is in bad condition. (質量、水準、條件等) 差的","examples":["...the poor state of the economy. …經濟的不良狀況。","The gap between the best and poorest childcare provision has widened. 兒童保育供給的最佳和最低水準之間加大了差距。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe an amount, rate, or number as <b>poor</b>, you mean that it is less than expected or less than is considered reasonable. 低的 (數量或比率)","examples":["...poor wages and working conditions. …低的工資和差的工作條件。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>poor</b> to describe someone who is not very skilful in a particular activity. (技術) 差勁的","examples":["He was a poor actor. 他是個差勁的演員。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something is <b>poor in</b> a particular quality or substance, it contains very little of the quality or substance. (某特質或物質) 貧乏的","examples":["Fats and sugar are very rich in energy but poor in vitamins and minerals. 脂肪和糖富含熱量，但缺乏維生素和礦物質。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The poor</b> are people who are poor. 窮人 (與)(the)(連用)","examples":["Even the poor have their pride. 即使窮人也有他們的自尊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"差地","examples":["Some are living in poorly built dormitories, even in tents. 一些人住在建得很差的宿舍裡，甚至住在帳篷裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"低地","examples":["During the first week, the evening meetings were poorly attended. 第一個星期晚間會議出勤率低。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"差勁地","examples":["Cheetahs breed very poorly in captivity. 獵豹在圈養的情況下繁殖力很差。"]}]}]},"selfish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自私的，利己的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>selfish</b>, you mean that he or she cares only about himself or herself, and not about other people. 自私的","examples":["I think I've been very selfish. I've been mainly concerned with myself. 我覺得我一直很自私。我總是隻關心自己。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自私地","examples":["Someone has selfishly emptied the biscuit jar. 有人自私地吃光了餅乾罐裡的餅乾。"]}]}]},"sad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傷心的，難過的；令人傷心的，讓人難過的；糟糕的，不能令人接受的；不幸的，可憐的；（歌曲或音樂）顯露悲傷的，傷感的；狀況不佳的；<非正式>（人）可悲的，不受人尊敬的；<非正式> 老土的，過時的；（麵糰）發得不好的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"季節性情感障礙（SAD）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sad</b>, you feel unhappy, usually because something has happened that you do not like. 悲傷的; 難過的","examples":["The relationship had been important to me and its loss left me feeling sad and empty. 這種關係對我一直都很重要，失去它讓我感到難過而空虛。","I'm sad that Julie's marriage is on the verge of splitting up. 我為朱莉的婚姻處於破裂的邊緣感到難過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sad</b> stories and <b>sad</b> news make you feel sad. 令人難過的","examples":["...a desperately humorous, impossibly sad novel. …一部極其幽默又催人淚下的小說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sad</b> event or situation is unfortunate or undesirable. 不幸的; 令人遺憾的","examples":["It's a sad truth that children are the biggest victims of passive smoking. 可悲的事實是，孩子們是被動吸菸的最大受害者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>sad</b>, you do not have any respect for them and think their behaviour or ideas are ridiculous. 荒唐的","examples":["...sad old bikers and youngsters who think that Jim Morrison is God. …視吉姆·莫里森為上帝的那些荒唐的老車手和年輕人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悲傷地; 難過地","examples":["...a gallant man who will be sadly missed by all his comrades. …一位將被他所有的同志沉痛懷念的勇士。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不幸地; 令人遺憾地","examples":["Sadly, bamboo plants die after flowering. 令人遺憾的是，竹子開花後就會死亡。"]}]}]},"real":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"實際存在的，非想象的；名副其實的；真正的，真實的；真的，非人工的；真誠的；強烈的；確實重大的；十足的，絕對的（用來加強語氣）；（數量、數字）真實的，實際的；（光學）（影象）實的；（書或電影中的場景）逼真的，似真的；（哲學）實在的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很，非常地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雷阿爾（巴西1994年以來的基本貨幣單位，等於100分）；雷阿爾（多個西班牙語國家以前的硬幣和貨幣單位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>real</b> actually exists and is not imagined, invented, or theoretical. 真實的","examples":["No, it wasn't a dream. It was real. 不，那不是夢。它是真實的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>real</b> <b>to</b> someone, they experience it as though it really exists or happens, even though it does not. 逼真的","examples":["Whitechild's life becomes increasingly real to the reader. 懷特菜爾德的生活在讀者看來越來越像是真的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A material or object that is <b>real</b> is natural or functioning, and not artificial or an imitation. 天然的; 非仿製的","examples":["...the smell of real leather. …真皮的氣味。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> to describe someone or something that has all the characteristics or qualities that such a person or thing typically has. 名副其實的; 真正的","examples":["...his first real girlfriend. …他的第一個名副其實的女朋友。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> to describe something that is the true or original thing of its kind, in contrast to one that someone wants you to believe is true. 真實的; 最初的","examples":["This was the real reason for her call. 這是她打電話的真實原因。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> to describe something that is the most important or typical part of a thing. 最重要的; 最典型的","examples":["When he talks, he only gives glimpses of his real self. 他講話時只是偶爾流露出真實的自我。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> when you are talking about a situation or feeling to emphasize that it exists and is important or serious. 確實存在的; 真切而嚴重的","examples":["Global warming is a real problem. 全球變暖是個確實存在的問題。","The prospect of civil war is very real. 內戰爆發的可能性確實存在。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> to emphasize a quality that is genuine and sincere. 真實的; 真誠的","examples":["You've been drifting from job to job without any real commitment. 你從一個工作換到另一個工作，從沒有真正地投入過。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> before nouns to emphasize your description of something or someone. (用在名詞前) 十足的","examples":["\"You must think I'm a real idiot.\" “你一定認為我是個十足的傻瓜。”"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"The <b>real</b> cost or value of something is its cost or value after other amounts have been added or subtracted and when factors such as the level of inflation have been considered. (成本或價值) 實際的; 淨的","examples":["...the real cost of borrowing. …借款的實際成本。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also talk about the cost or value of something <b>in real terms</b>. 實 (價)","examples":["In real terms the cost of driving is cheaper than a decade ago. 駕車的實際花費比10年前要少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>for real</b>, you mean that they actually do it and do not just pretend to do it. 確實地; 真正地","examples":["I have gone to premieres in my dreams but I never thought I'd do it for real. 我在夢中多次參加過首演，但我從沒想到我會真的參加。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>real</b> to emphasize an adjective or adverb. 非常 (用以強調形容詞或副詞)","examples":["He is finding prison life \"real tough.\" 他現在發現監獄生活“非常艱苦。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the standard monetary unit of Brazil, divided into 100 centavos 雷亞爾; 巴西貨幣標準單位","examples":[]}]}]},"several":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不同的，各自的；<法律>單獨，各個"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"幾個，數個"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"幾個，數個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Several</b> is used to refer to a number of people or things that is not large but is greater than two. 幾; 一些","examples":["I had lived two doors away from this family for several years. 我與相隔兩戶的這家人做了幾年的鄰居。","Several blue plastic boxes under the window were filled with CDs. 窗子下面的幾個藍色塑膠盒子裡裝滿了鐳射唱片。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Several</b> is also a quantifier. 幾個; 若干","examples":["The building was picketed by demonstrators, several of whom were well-known actors. 這座建築被示威者們包圍了起來，其中幾位是著名的演員。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Several</b> is also a pronoun. 幾個; 幾種","examples":["No one drug will suit or work for everyone and sometimes several may have to be tried. 沒有任何一種藥會對每個人都適用或有效，有時得試好幾種。"]}]}]},"rich":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有錢的，富有的；富含……的，豐富的；非常有趣的，豐富多彩的；（食物）油膩的；（色彩、氣味）濃郁的，（聲音）渾厚的；肥沃的，豐產的；華麗昂貴的；<非正式>（指某人的評論或批評）荒唐的，可笑的；值錢的，生財的；（內燃機內的混合燃料）可燃性成分高的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rich</b> person has a lot of money or valuable possessions. 富的","examples":["You're going to be a very rich man. 你將成為一個非常富的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rich</b> country has a strong economy and produces a lot of wealth, so many people who live there have a high standard of living. 富強的","examples":["There is hunger in many parts of the world, even in rich countries. 飢餓在世界許多地方都存在，甚至在一些富國。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>rich in</b> a useful or valuable substance or is a <b>rich source</b> <b>of</b> it, it contains a lot of it. 富含的","examples":["Liver and kidneys are particularly rich in vitamin A. 肝臟和腎臟尤其富含維生素A。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Rich</b> food contains a lot of fat or oil. (食物) 油膩的","examples":["Additional cream would make it too rich. 額外的奶油會使它過於油膩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Rich</b> soil contains large amounts of substances that make it good for growing crops or flowers. (土壤) 肥沃的","examples":["Farmers grow rice in the rich soil. 農民們在肥沃的土地上種水稻。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>rich</b> deposit of a mineral or other substance is a large amount of it. 富饒的 (礦藏等)","examples":["...the country's rich deposits of the metal lithium. …該國富饒的鋰金屬礦藏。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>rich</b> vein or source of something such as humour, ideas, or information, you mean that it can provide a lot of that thing. 豐富的 (來源)","examples":["The director discovered a rich vein of sentimentality. 導演發現了多愁善感的豐富源泉。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Rich</b> smells are strong and very pleasant. <b>Rich</b> colours and sounds are deep and very pleasant. 濃郁的 (氣味); 濃厚的 (色彩)","examples":["...a rich and luxuriously perfumed bath essence. …一種濃郁的、富含香氣的沐浴精華乳。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>rich</b> life or history is one that is interesting because it is full of different events and activities. 豐富多彩的 (生活、歷史)","examples":["A rich and varied cultural life is essential for this couple. 豐富多彩的、多樣化的文化生活對於這對夫婦而言是必不可少的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>rich</b> collection or mixture contains a wide and interesting variety of different things. 各種各樣的; 豐富的 (種類)","examples":["Visitors can view a rich and colourful array of aquatic plants and animals. 參觀者可以觀賞到一系列各種各樣、色彩斑斕的水生動植物。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The rich</b> are rich people. 富人","examples":["This is a system in which the rich are taken care of and the poor are left to suffer. 這是個富人受關照，而窮人遭罪的制度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Riches</b> are valuable possessions or large amounts of money. 財富","examples":["An Olympic gold medal can lead to untold riches for an athlete. 一枚奧運金牌能為一名運動員帶來數不盡的財富。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about the Earth's <b>riches</b>, you are referring to things that exist naturally in large quantities and that are useful and valuable, for example minerals, wood, and oil. (自然) 資源","examples":["...Russia's vast natural riches. …俄羅斯巨大的自然資源。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"油膩","examples":["A squeeze of fresh lime juice cuts the richness of the avocado. 擠一點鮮青檸汁能減少鱷梨的油膩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"富饒","examples":["...the richness of Tibet's mineral deposits. …西藏礦藏之富饒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"(氣味的) 濃郁; (色彩的) 濃厚","examples":["His musicals were infused with richness of colour and visual detail. 他的音樂劇充滿了濃厚色彩與視覺細節。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"豐富多彩性","examples":["It all adds to the richness of human life. 這都增添了人類生活的豐富多彩性。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"豐富性; 多樣性","examples":["...a huge country, containing a richness of culture and diversity of landscape. …一個具有文化豐富性和地貌多樣性的大國。"]}]}]},"shy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"害羞的，靦腆的；顯得靦腆的，看著羞怯的；（動物）易受驚的，膽小的；猶豫的，有所顧忌的；躲避（或不喜歡）……的；不足的，缺乏的；在……之前（shy of）；（植物）開花不多的，結果很少的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指馬）驚退，驚逸；（由於緊張或缺乏信心而）迴避，避開（shy from）； 投擲，扔；突然投出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指馬的）驚退，驚逸；投擲，扔；<英> 以球打落椰子的遊戲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shy</b> person is nervous and uncomfortable in the company of other people. 害羞的; 靦腆的","examples":["She was a shy, quiet girl. 她是個靦腆安靜的女孩。","She was a shy and retiring person off-stage. 臺下她是個害羞、沉默寡言的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>shy</b> <b>about</b> or <b>shy</b> <b>of</b> doing something, you are unwilling to do it because you are afraid of what might happen. (因擔心後果) 不情願的","examples":["They feel shy about showing their feelings. 他們不願表達自己的感情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"害羞地; 靦腆地","examples":["The children smiled shyly. 孩子們靦腆地笑了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to move suddenly, as from fear (因害怕而)突然移動","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to throw (something) with a sideways motion 斜擲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a sudden movement, as from fear (因害怕而)突然的移動","examples":[]}]}]},"silly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愚蠢的，傻的；嬉笑滑稽的；失去理智的；微不足道的，不實用的；（板球）（防守位置）靠近擊球手的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>傻瓜，笨蛋（尤指兒童）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極度地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>silly</b>, you mean that they are foolish, childish, or ridiculous. 愚蠢的; 幼稚的; 荒唐的","examples":["My best friend tells me that I am silly to be upset about this. 我最好的朋友說我為此事心煩太傻了。","I thought it would be silly to be too rude at that stage. 我覺得處在那個階段上太過粗魯是很幼稚的。"]}]}]},"simple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"簡單的，簡明的；簡樸的，樸素的；純粹的，完全的；結構單一的，簡易的；普通的，平凡的；愚笨的，遲鈍的；（動詞時態）簡單的；（數）簡單的；（葉、莖）沒有分杈的；（鏡頭、顯微鏡等）單鏡頭的；（利息）單利的；（句子）無從句的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<史> 草藥，藥草；出身低微者；笨蛋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>simple</b>, you mean that it is not complicated, and is therefore easy to understand. 簡單的; 簡明的","examples":["...simple pictures and diagrams. …簡明的圖片和圖表。","...pages of simple advice on filling in your tax form. …幾頁有關填寫納稅表格的簡單建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe people or things as <b>simple</b>, you mean that they have all the basic or necessary things they require, but nothing extra. 簡樸的; 樸素的","examples":["He ate a simple dinner of rice and beans. 他吃了一頓米飯加豆子的簡單晚餐。","...the simple pleasures of childhood. …童年純樸的快樂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a problem is <b>simple</b> or if its solution is <b>simple</b>, the problem can be solved easily. 好辦的; 易解決的","examples":["Some puzzles look difficult but are actually quite simple. 有些謎看似很難，但實際上相當容易解開。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>simple</b> task is easy to do. 容易的; 簡易的","examples":["The job itself had been simple enough. 這工作本身一直就相當容易。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>simple</b> to emphasize that the thing you are referring to is the only important or relevant reason for something. 純粹的; 完全的","examples":["His refusal to talk was simple stubbornness. 他拒絕交談只是出於固執。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In grammar, <b>simple</b> tenses are ones which are formed without an auxiliary verb \"be,\" for example,\"I dressed and went for a walk\" and \"This tastes nice.\" <b>Simple</b> verb groups are used especially to refer to completed actions, regular actions, and situations. Compare . 簡單的 (時態或動詞片語)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"簡單地","examples":["When applying for a visa extension state simply and clearly the reasons why you need an extension. 申請簽證續簽時，簡單明瞭地陳述你需要延期的理由。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"簡樸地; 樸素地","examples":["The living room is furnished simply with white wicker furniture and blue-and-white fabrics. 起居室樸素地擺放著白柳條傢俱和藍白相間的織物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"簡易地; 容易地","examples":["We can do things that were not possible before, and they can be done simply. 我們現在可以做以前不可能的事情，而且可以輕而易舉地做成。"]}]}]},"smart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聰明的，明智的；（人）衣著得體的；整潔而漂亮的，光鮮的；耍小聰明的，不恭的；時髦的，高檔的；迅速有力的，迅猛的；智慧的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（身體部位）感到刺痛；（因批評、失敗等）難過，煩惱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇痛，刺痛；痛苦，苦惱；<美，非正式>聰明，敏銳（smarts）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"機敏地，整潔地，瀟灑地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe someone who is clever or intelligent as <b>smart</b>. 聰明的; 機智的","examples":["He thinks he's smarter than Sarah is. 他認為他比薩拉更聰明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Smart</b> people and things are pleasantly neat and clean in appearance. 整潔的","examples":["He was smart and well groomed but not good looking. 他時髦而且打扮整齊，但是長得不帥。","I was dressed in a smart navy blue suit. 我穿一身整潔的海軍藍制服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>smart</b> place or event is connected with wealthy and fashionable people. 時髦的","examples":["...smart dinner parties. …時髦的宴會。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"整潔地","examples":["He dressed very smartly, which was important in those days. 他穿得非常整潔，這在當時很重要。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body or a wound <b>smarts</b>, you feel a sharp stinging pain in it. (身體某部位或傷口) 刺痛","examples":["My eyes smarted from the smoke. 我的雙眼被煙燻得刺痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are smarting</b> <b>from</b> something such as criticism or failure, you feel upset about it. (因批評或失敗) 感到難受","examples":["The Americans were still smarting from their defeat in the Vietnam War. 美國人仍在為越戰中失利而難受。"]}]}]},"sick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生病的，患病的；病人的；噁心的，想吐的；不快的，惱怒的；厭倦的，厭煩的；（情感）強烈得令人不適的；（人）變態的，病態的；（故事、笑話等）令人毛骨悚然的，病態的；不祥的；（喻）（組織，體系，社團）面臨嚴重問題的，不景氣的；<非正式> 極好的；渴望的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"病人（the sick）；<英，非正式> 嘔吐物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式> 嘔吐；放狗咬；<非正式> 派某人去追擊（或監視、陪伴）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sick</b>, you are ill. <b>Sick</b> usually means physically ill, but it can sometimes be used to mean mentally ill. (生理上) 有病的; 精神不健全的","examples":["He's very sick. He needs medication. 他病得很重，需要藥物治療。","She found herself with two small children, a sick husband, and no money. 她發現自己帶著2個年幼的孩子和1個有病的丈夫，而且身無分文。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>sick</b>, the food that you have eaten comes up from your stomach and out of your mouth. If you <b>feel</b> <b>sick</b>, you feel as if you are going to be sick. 噁心的; 嘔吐的","examples":["She got up and was sick in the sink. 她起身往水池裡嘔吐起來。","The very thought of food made him feel sick. 一想到食物他就想吐。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>sick of</b> something or <b>sick and tired of</b> it, you are emphasizing that you are very annoyed by it and want it to stop. 厭倦的","examples":["I am sick and tired of hearing all these people moaning. 我厭倦了聽所有這些人抱怨個沒完。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something such as a joke or story as <b>sick</b>, you mean that it deals with death or suffering in an unpleasantly humorous way. 令人毛骨悚然的","examples":["...a sick joke about a cat. …有關貓的一個令人毛骨悚然的笑話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The sick</b> are people who are sick. 病人","examples":["There were no doctors to treat the sick. 那時沒有醫生醫治病人們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something or someone <b>makes</b> you <b>sick</b>, you mean that they make you feel angry or disgusted. 使某人生氣; 使某人厭惡","examples":["It makes me sick that this wasn't disclosed. 這事被隱瞞了讓我很生氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>out sick</b>, you are not at work because you are sick. 因病沒上班","examples":["That afternoon she was fired from her job as a nurse, because she'd been out sick so much. 那天下午她因經常生病沒去上班被開除，丟掉了護士工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>worried sick</b>, you are emphasizing that you are extremely worried. 擔心得要命","examples":["He was worried sick about what our mothers would say. 他對我們的媽媽們可能要說的話擔心得要命。"]}]}]},"special":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"特殊的，特別的；格外看重的，特別要好的；專門的，特設的；特有的，獨具特色的；格外的，分外的；（主題）研究深入的；（數）特殊（矩陣）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"特色菜；特別節目；特價商品，折扣商品；特派員，臨時警察，特約記者；專車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>special</b> is better or more important than other people or things. 特別的","examples":["You're very special to me, darling. 你對我來說很特別，親愛的。","My special guest will be Jerry Seinfeld. 我的特邀嘉賓將是傑瑞•塞菲爾德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Special</b> means different from normal. 特殊的","examples":["In special cases, a husband can deduct the travel expenses of his wife who accompanies him on a business trip. 在特殊情況下，丈夫可以扣除差旅中隨行妻子的旅費。","So you didn't notice anything special about him? 這麼說你沒有注意到他的特別之處？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>special</b> to describe someone who is officially appointed or who has a particular position specially created for them. 特派的","examples":["Due to his wife's illness, he returned to the State Department as special adviser to the president. 由於妻子的病，他返回國務院做了總統的特派顧問。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>special</b> to describe something that relates to one particular person, group, or place. 特有的","examples":["Every anxious person will have his or her own special problems or fears. 每個焦慮的人都將有他/她自己特有的問題或擔心。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>special</b> is a product, programme, or meal which is not normally available, or which is made for a particular purpose. 特產; 特別節目; 特色菜","examples":["...complaints about the Halloween special, \"Ghostwatch.\" …對萬聖節特別節目《幽靈觀察》的抱怨。","Grocery stores have to offer enough specials to bring people into the shop 雜貨店得提供足夠多的特色產品以招攬顧客。"]}]}]},"short":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"短暫的，短期的；（長度或距離）短的；個子矮的；簡短的，短篇的；短缺的，稀少的；不夠（長、高或遠）的；縮寫的；呼吸困難的；唐突的，無禮的；短音的；短球的；（板球）靠近擊球手位置的；機率大的；（糕點）鬆脆的；（黏土）黏性差的；簡直，無異於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>少量烈酒；電影短片；短褲（shorts）；<美>男用短內褲（shorts）；短音；細麩粉（shorts）；短路；賣空的人；短期證券（shorts）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"達不到標準（或預期）地；突然，短暫；使變短地；短距離地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）短路；（股票）賣空"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>short</b> or lasts for a <b>short</b> time, it does not last very long. 短暫的","examples":["The announcement was made a short time ago. 這個通告是在不久前剛釋出的。","Kemp gave a short laugh. 肯普笑了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>short</b> speech, letter, or book does not have many words or pages in it. 簡短的","examples":["They were performing a short extract from Shakespeare's Two Gentlemen of Verona. 他們正在表演莎士比亞戲劇《兩位維羅納紳士》中一個簡短的片段。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>short</b> is not as tall as most people are. 矮的","examples":["I'm tall and thin and he's short and fat. 我又高又瘦，他又矮又胖。","...a short, elderly woman with grey hair. …一個頭發灰白的矮小老婦人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>short</b> measures only a small amount from one end to the other. 短的","examples":["The restaurant is only a short distance away. 那個飯店就在不遠處。","A short flight of steps led to a grand doorway. 一段短短的樓梯通向一個寬敞的門道。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>short of</b> something or if it is <b>short</b>, you do not have enough of it. If you are running <b>short of</b> something or if it is running <b>short</b>, you do not have much of it left. 短缺的","examples":["Her father's illness left the family short of money. 他父親的病使得全家缺錢。","Government forces are running short of ammunition and fuel. 政府軍正缺少彈藥和燃料。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something is or stops <b>short of</b> a place, they have not quite reached it. If they are or fall <b>short of</b> an amount, they have not quite achieved it. 未達到的","examples":["He stopped a hundred yards short of the building. 他停在離那座建築還有100碼遠的地方。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a name or abbreviation is <b>short for</b> another name, it is the short version of that name. 簡稱的","examples":["Her friend Kes (short for Kesewa) was in tears. 她的朋友凱斯（凱斯瓦的簡稱）在流淚。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you have a <b>short</b> temper, you get angry very easily. 易怒的","examples":["...an awkward, self-conscious woman with a short temper. …一個笨拙忸怩而且脾氣暴躁的女人，。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you are <b>short with</b> someone, you speak briefly and rather rudely to them, because you are impatient or angry. 簡慢無禮的","examples":["She seemed nervous or tense, and she was definitely short with me. 她似乎是緊張或焦急，顯然對我簡慢無禮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Short of</b> a particular thing means except for that thing or without actually doing that thing. 除…外","examples":["Short of gagging the children, there was not much she could do about the noise. 除了不讓孩子們說話之外，她對那噪音無能為力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing is called something <b>for short</b>, that is the short version of their name. 作為簡稱","examples":["Opposite me was a woman called Jasminder (Jazzy for short). 我對面是個叫傑絲明德（簡稱傑絲）的女人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>in short</b> when you have been giving a lot of details and you want to give a conclusion or summary. 簡而言之","examples":["Try tennis, badminton or windsurfing. In short, anything challenging. 試試網球、羽毛球或帆板運動。簡而言之，任何有挑戰性的東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is short on</b> a particular good quality, they do not have as much of it as you think they should have. 缺少某物","examples":["The proposals were short on detail. 這些提議缺少細節。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>stops short of</b> doing something, they come close to doing it but do not actually do it. 險些","examples":["He stopped short of explicitly criticizing the government. 他險些就直言不諱地批評政府了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>cut</b> <b>short</b> or <b>stops</b> <b>short</b>, it is stopped before people expect it to or before it has finished. 提早結束地","examples":["His glittering career was cut short by a heart attack. 他輝煌的事業被一次心臟病發作給提早完結了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shorts</b> are trousers with very short legs that people wear in hot weather or for taking part in sports. 短褲","examples":["...two women in bright cotton shorts and tee shirts. …兩個穿著鮮麗棉短褲和T恤的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shorts</b> are men's underpants with short legs. (男子的) 內褲","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>short</b> is a short film, especially one that is shown before the main film at the cinema. (電影院正片前放映的) 短片","examples":[]}]}]},"sorry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"抱歉的，慚愧的，歉疚的；表示同情的，難過的；後悔的，懊悔的；可憐的，糟糕的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於表示歉意）對不起，抱歉；沒聽清，請再講一遍；（糾正自己說錯的話）不對，應該是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Sorry</b>\" or \"<b>I'm sorry</b>\" as a way of apologizing to someone for something that you have done which has upset them or caused them difficulties, or when you bump into them accidentally. 對不起","examples":["\"We're all talking at the same time.\"—\"Yeah. Sorry.\" “我們都在同時說話。”—“呃，對不起。”","Sorry I took so long. 對不起，我用了這麼長時間。","I'm really sorry if I said anything wrong. 真抱歉，如果我有說錯的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>I'm sorry</b> or <b>sorry</b> as an introduction when you are telling a person something that you do not think they will want to hear, for example when you are disagreeing with them or giving them bad news. 抱歉 (用於表示不同意或不好的訊息)","examples":["No, I'm sorry, I can't agree with you. 不，抱歉，我不同意你。","\"I'm sorry,\" he told the real estate agent, \"but we really must go now.\" “對不起，”他告訴房地產經紀人，“但我們的確要走了。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>I'm sorry</b>\" to express your regret and sadness when you hear sad or unpleasant news. 很難過","examples":["\"I'm afraid he's ill.\"—\"I'm sorry to hear that.\" “恐怕他病了。”—“聽到這個訊息我很難過。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say \"<b>Sorry?</b>\" when you have not heard something that someone has said and you want them to repeat it. 抱歉 (請求再講一遍)","examples":["Once or twice I heard her muttering, but when I said, \"Sorry? What did you say?\" she didn't respond. 有一兩次我聽見她在嘀嘀咕咕，但當我說“抱歉? 你說什麼？”時，她沒有回答。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>sorry</b> when you correct yourself and use different words to say what you have just said, especially when what you say the second time does not use the words you would normally choose to use. 抱歉 (用於說話時自我糾正)","examples":["Barcelona will be hoping to bring the trophy back to Spain (sorry, Catalonia) for the first time. 巴塞羅那將會希望第一次把獎盃帶回西班牙（抱歉，是卡塔洛尼亞）。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sorry</b> about a situation, you feel regret, sadness, or disappointment about it. 遺憾的; 悲傷的","examples":["She was very sorry about all the trouble she'd caused. 她對自己造成的麻煩感到很內疚。","I'm sorry he's gone. 他走了我感到遺憾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel <b>sorry for</b> someone who is unhappy or in an unpleasant situation, you feel sympathy and sadness for them. 同情的","examples":["I felt sorry for him and his colleagues – it must have been so frustrating for them. 我很同情他和他的同事們–這對他們來說肯定是非常令人沮喪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that someone is feeling <b>sorry for</b> <b>themselves</b> when you disapprove of the fact that they keep thinking unhappily about their problems, rather than trying to be cheerful and positive. (自我) 憐憫的","examples":["What he must not do is to sit around at home feeling sorry for himself. 他絕不該做的事情就是坐在家裡自我憐憫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something is in a <b>sorry</b> state, they are in a bad state, mentally or physically. 糟糕的","examples":["The fire left Kuwait's oil industry in a sorry state. 大火使科威特的石油工業陷入糟糕的境地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the expression <b>I'm sorry to say</b> to express regret together with disappointment or disapproval. 很遺憾","examples":["I've only done half of it, I'm sorry to say. 我只做了一半，很遺憾。"]}]}]},"soft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易彎曲的，柔軟的；柔滑的，細嫩的；無稜角的，輪廓不鮮明的；柔和的，悅目的；（聲音）安靜的，輕柔的；（雨、風等）溫和的，不猛烈的；有同情心的，心腸軟的；力度不夠的，不嚴厲的；輕鬆的，安逸的；（水）軟性的；膽小的，懦弱的；虛弱的，健康欠佳的；發軟音的；（毒品）毒性不強的；（飲料）不含酒精的；（市場或經濟）疲軟的；<非正式>愚蠢的；（目標）易被攻擊的；非嚴肅性的，不重要的；<方>（天氣）多雨的，潮溼的，解凍的；（輻射）穿透力弱的；（洗滌劑）生物降解性的；（色情描寫）非赤裸裸的，隱晦的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"溫柔地；<美>輕輕地；<非正式>無力地，愚蠢地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"柔性；柔軟的東西；柔軟部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>soft</b> is pleasant to touch, and not rough or hard. 柔軟的","examples":["Regular use of a body lotion will keep the skin soft and supple. 定期使用潤膚乳液可以使皮膚保持柔軟光滑。","When it's dry, brush the hair using a soft, nylon baby brush. 天氣乾燥時，用嬰兒用的軟尼龍刷子梳頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>soft</b> changes shape or bends easily when you press it. 軟的","examples":["She lay down on the soft, comfortable bed. 她躺到柔軟舒適的床上。","Add enough milk to form a soft dough. 加足牛奶，以便揉成一個軟麵糰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that has a <b>soft</b> appearance has smooth curves rather than sharp or distinct edges. (外觀) 柔和的","examples":["This is a smart, yet soft and feminine look. 這是一張透著精明的面孔，但是線條柔和、女性味十足。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>soft</b> is very gentle and has no force. For example, a <b>soft</b> sound or voice is quiet and not harsh. A <b>soft</b> light or colour is pleasant to look at because it is not bright. (聲音、光線或色彩) 柔和的","examples":["There was a soft tapping on my door. 有人在輕輕地敲我的房門。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>soft</b> <b>on</b> someone, you do not treat them as strictly or severely as you should. 心慈手軟的","examples":["The president says the measure is soft and weak on criminals. 總統說這項措施對罪犯來說太寬容、軟弱了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone has a <b>soft</b> <b>heart</b>, you mean that they are sensitive and sympathetic toward other people. 心腸軟的; 有同情心的","examples":["Her rather tough and worldly exterior hides a very soft and sensitive heart. 她那相當堅強而世故的外表下掩藏著一顆非常柔軟敏感的心。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>soft</b> to describe a way of life that is easy and involves very little work. 輕鬆的","examples":["...a soft life and easy living. …輕鬆安逸的生活。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Soft</b> water does not contain much of the mineral calcium and so makes bubbles easily when you use soap. (水) 軟性的","examples":["...an area where the water is very soft. …一個水質很軟的地區。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Soft</b> drugs are drugs, such as cannabis, which are illegal but which many people do not consider to be strong or harmful. (毒品) 毒性不強的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"柔軟","examples":["The sea air robbed her hair of its softness. 海邊的空氣有損她頭髮的柔滑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"柔和地","examples":["She wore a softly tailored suit. 她穿了件剪裁柔和得體的套裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"柔和地","examples":["She crossed the softly lit room. 她穿過燈光柔和的房間。"]}]}]},"some":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"若干，一些；某個，某種；相當多，大量；少量的，不多的；了不起的，很不錯的；不怎麼樣的，算不上……的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"有些，一部分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美>有些，稍微；大約"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>some</b> to refer to a quantity of something or to a number of people or things, when you are not stating the quantity or number precisely. 一些","examples":["Robin opened some champagne. 羅賓開啟了一些香檳酒。","He went to fetch some books. 他去取來了一些書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>some</b> to emphasize that a quantity or number is fairly large. For example, if an activity takes <b>some</b> time, it takes quite a lot of time. 相當多","examples":["I have discussed this topic in some detail. 我已相當詳細地討論過這個話題。","He remained silent for some time. 他好長時間都保持沉默。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>some</b> to emphasize that a quantity or number is fairly small. For example, if something happens to <b>some</b> extent, it happens a little. 一點","examples":["\"Isn't there some chance that William might lead a normal life?\" asked Jill. “威廉難道就沒有一點機會可以過一種正常的生活？”吉爾問道。","All mothers share to some extent in the tension of a wedding. 所有的母親都有些許程度上的婚禮緊張。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to <b>some</b> person or thing, you are referring to that person or thing but in a vague way, without stating precisely which person or thing you mean. 某些","examples":["If you are worried about some aspect of your child's health, call us. 如果你擔心孩子的某些健康問題，就給我們打電話。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>some</b> in front of a noun in order to express your approval or disapproval of the person or thing you are mentioning. 在名詞前表對該人或事物的褒貶","examples":["\"Some party!\"—\"Yep. One hell of a party.\" “那還算晚會！”—“是啊，晚會簡直是一塌糊塗。”"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Some</b> is also a pronoun. 一些","examples":["This year all the apples are all red. My niece and nephew are going out this morning with step-ladders to pick some. 今年所有的蘋果都紅了。我的侄女和侄子今天上午就要帶著摺梯出去摘一些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Some</b> is also a pronoun. 一部份","examples":["When the chicken is cooked I'll freeze some. 雞肉做熟後我會冷凍一部份。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>some of</b> the people or things in a group, you mean a few of them but not all of them. If you refer to <b>some of</b> a particular thing, you mean a part of it but not all of it. 一部份","examples":["Some of the people already in work will lose their jobs. 一部份已經工作的人將會失去他們的工作。","Remove the cover and spoon some of the sauce into a bowl. 開啟蓋子，用勺子舀一部份調味汁放到碗裡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>some</b> in front of a number to indicate that it is approximate. 大約","examples":["I have kept birds for some 30 years. 我養鳥大約有三十年了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Some</b> is used to mean to a small extent or degree. 稍微","examples":["If Susanne is off somewhere, I'll kill time by looking around some. 如果蘇珊娜去了別的什麼地方，我就稍微逛逛來消磨時間。"]}]}]},"strange":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇怪的，不尋常的；陌生的，不熟悉的；令人侷促不安的，令人不自在的，令人難受的；（亞原子粒子）有奇異性非零值的，奇異性的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"奇怪地，不尋常地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>strange</b> is unusual or unexpected, and makes you feel slightly nervous or afraid. 奇怪的","examples":["Then a strange thing happened. 接著一件怪事發生了。","There was something strange about the flickering blue light. 那閃爍的藍光有點兒奇怪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>strange</b> place is one that you have never been to before. A <b>strange</b> person is someone that you have never met before. 陌生的","examples":["I ended up alone in a strange city. 我最終是獨自呆在了一個陌生的城市。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"奇怪地","examples":["She noticed he was acting strangely. 她注意到他行為怪異。"]}]}]},"stupid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"笨的，傻的，腦子不好使的；欠考慮的，糊塗的；（用以加強語氣）討厭的，惱人的，無聊的；（因醉、累等）不省人事的，神思恍惚的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"傻瓜，笨蛋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>stupid</b>, you mean that they show a lack of good judgment or intelligence and they are not at all sensible. 愚蠢的","examples":["I'll never do anything so stupid again. 我再也不會做這麼愚蠢的事了。","I made a stupid mistake. 我犯了個愚蠢的錯誤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that something is <b>stupid</b> to indicate that you do not like it or that it annoys you. 討厭的","examples":["I wouldn't call it art. It's just stupid and tasteless. 我不會稱它為藝術。它令人討厭且毫無品味。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"愚蠢地","examples":["We had stupidly been looking at the wrong column of figures. 我們愚蠢地一直在看那個錯的數字欄。"]}]}]},"tall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高的，高大的；（用於指高度）有……高的，身高……的；過分的，誇大的；（飲料）含少量酒精的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>tall</b> has a greater height than is normal or average. 高的","examples":["Being tall can make you feel incredibly self-confident. 個子高能使你感覺極其自信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>tall</b> to ask or talk about the height of someone or something. (有多) 高","examples":["How tall are you? 你有多高？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>a tall order</b>, it is very difficult. 難辦的事","examples":["Financing your studies may seem like a tall order, but there is plenty of help available. 資助你的學業似乎是一件難辦的事，但有很多可利用的幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>walks tall</b>, you mean that they behave in a way that shows that they have pride in themselves and in what they are doing. 昂首闊步","examples":["They shouldn't be disappointed or let their heads fall, but walk tall. 他們不應該失望或垂頭喪氣，而應該昂首闊步。"]}]}]},"tiny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極小的，微小的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>幼童"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>tiny</b> is extremely small. 極小的","examples":["The living room is tiny. 這間起居室極小。","Though she was tiny, she had a very loud voice. 雖然她個頭很小，嗓門卻很大。"]}]}]},"these":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"這些（this 的複數）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"這些（this 的複數）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"這些的（this 的複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> at the beginning of noun groups to refer to someone or something that you have already mentioned or identified. 這些 (用於名詞前，指前文曾提到的人或物)","examples":["A committee has been formed. These people can make decisions in ten minutes which would take us months. 委員會已經成立。這些人能在10分鐘內做出決定，換作我們則要花幾個月。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> to introduce people or things that you are going to talk about. 這些 (用於引出將要談及的人或物)","examples":["Your camcorder should have these basic features: autofocus, playback facility, zoom lens. 你的行動式攝像機應該具有這些基本特徵：自動調焦、回放及變焦鏡頭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In spoken English, people use <b>these</b> to introduce people or things into a story. 這些 (口語中用於引出故事中的人或物)","examples":["I was by myself and these guys suddenly came towards me. 我獨自一人時，這些人忽然向我走來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> to refer to people or things that are near you, especially when you touch them or point to them. 這些 (尤指所碰觸或指向的附近的人或物)","examples":["These scissors are awfully heavy. 這幾把剪刀非常重。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> when you refer to something which you expect the person you are talking to to know about, or when you are checking that you are both thinking of the same person or thing. 這些 (指雙方均瞭解的事物)","examples":["You know these last few months when we've been expecting it to warm up a little bit? 你知道最近這幾個月我們一直盼望天氣能暖和一些嗎？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> in the expression <b>these days</b> to mean \"at the present time.\" 目前","examples":["These days, people appreciate a chance to relax. 目前人們很珍惜能放鬆的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>These</b> is also a pronoun. 這些","examples":["\"I have faith in these guys,\" the coach said. \"These are good players.\" “我相信這些人，”教練說道。“這些都是好球員。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>These</b> is also a pronoun. 這些","examples":["Take care of yourself while you are pregnant. These are some of the things you can do for yourself. 懷孕期間要照顧好自己。這些是你自己可以做的事情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>these</b> when you are identifying a group or asking about their identity. 這些 (用於識別或詢問身份)","examples":["These are my children. 這些是我的孩子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>These</b> is also a pronoun. 這些","examples":["These are the people who are helping us. 這些是正在幫助我們的人。"]}]}]},"such":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"如此的，這等的；如此（……以致）；這種的，那樣的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"這種人（或事物），這類的；（上文提到的）那樣的情況，那件事"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"這麼，如此（用於加強敘述語氣）；如此程度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>such</b> to refer back to the thing or person that you have just mentioned, or a thing or person like the one that you have just mentioned. You use <b>such as</b> and <b>such...as</b> to introduce a reference to the person or thing that has just been mentioned. 這樣的; 如此的","examples":["There have been previous attempts at coups. We regard such methods as entirely unacceptable. 先前有過政變企圖。我們認為這樣的方法完全不可接受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>such...as</b> or <b>such as</b> to link something or someone with a clause in which you give a description of the kind of thing or person that you mean. (像…) 那樣的","examples":["...incentive payments for such activities as planting hardwood trees. …給予像種植硬木樹那樣的活動的獎金。","Children do not use inflections such as are used in mature adult speech. 兒童不使用像成年人言語中使用的那些詞形變化。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>such...as</b> or <b>such as</b> to introduce one or more examples of the kind of thing or person that you have just mentioned. (諸如…) 之類的","examples":["...such careers as teaching, nursing, hairdressing and catering. …諸如教學、護理、美髮和餐飲等事業。","...serious offences, such as assault on a police officer. …諸如襲擊警官等嚴重違法行為。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>such</b> before noun groups to emphasize the extent of something or to emphasize that something is remarkable. 如此的","examples":["I think most of us don't want to read what's in the newspaper anyway in such detail. 我想我們中的多數人無論如何都不願如此詳細地去讀報紙上的東西。","One will never be able to understand why these political issues can acquire such force. 人們將永遠不會明白為什麼這些政治問題能獲得如此的影響力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Such</b> is also a determiner. 如此的 (作限定詞)","examples":["She looked at him in such distress that he had to look away. 她如此憂傷地看著他，以至他不得不把目光轉向別處。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>such...that</b> or <b>such that</b> in order to say what the result or consequence of something that you have just mentioned is. 如此這般的","examples":["The operation has uncovered such backstreet dealing in stolen property that police might now press for changes in the law. 這次行動發現瞭如此這般的地下贓物交易以致警方現在可能迫切要求修改法律。","Their cost structure is such that they just can't compete with the low-cost carriers. 他們的成本結構是這樣的以致於他們就是沒法與那些低成本的運輸公司競爭。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Such</b> is also a predeterminer. 這樣的 (作前位限定詞)","examples":["If your request is for information about a child, please contact the registrar to find out how to make such a request. 如果你尋求的是有關孩子的資訊，請與登記員聯絡以獲知如何作這樣的請求。","She has told us that when she goes back to stay with her family, they make her pay rent. We could not believe such a thing. 她告訴過我們，當她回去和家人一起住時，他們讓她付租金。我們不能相信這樣的事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Such</b> is also a predeterminer. 如此的 (作前位限定詞)","examples":["It was such a pleasant surprise. 它是如此一個驚喜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>such...that</b> or <b>such that</b> in order to emphasize the degree of something by mentioning the result or consequence of it. 如此 (…以至)","examples":["This is something where you can earn such a lot of money that there is not any risk that you will lose it. 這是能賺到很多錢而沒有任何虧錢風險的事。","Though Vivaldi had earned a great deal in his lifetime, his extravagance was such that he died in poverty. 儘管維瓦爾蒂一生中掙了許多錢，但其揮霍如此之巨，以至在貧困中死去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Such</b> is also a predeterminer. 如此的 (作前位限定詞)","examples":["He could put an idea in such a way that Alan would believe it was his own. 他能夠以這樣的方式表達觀點，以致於艾倫會相信那是他自己的觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Such</b> is also a pronoun used before <b>be</b>. 這 (用於)(be)(前)","examples":["We are scared because we are being watched – such is the atmosphere in Pristina and other cities in Kosovo. 我們因被監視而害怕–這就是普裡什蒂納和科索沃其他城市的氣氛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>such and such</b> to refer to a thing or person when you do not want to be exact or precise. 某某","examples":["I said, \"Well, what time'll I get to Baltimore?\" and he said such and such a time but I missed my connection. 我說，“那麼，我幾點會到巴爾的摩呢？”他說了某某時間，可我錯過了聯運列車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>as such</b> with a negative to indicate that a word or expression is not a very accurate description of the actual situation. 準確意義上的 (與否定詞連用)","examples":["I am not a learner as such – I used to ride a bike years ago. 我不是個準確意義上的初學者–我多年前常常騎腳踏車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>as such</b> after a noun to indicate that you are considering that thing on its own, separately from other things or factors. 作為…本身 (用於名詞後)","examples":["Mr. Simon said he was not against taxes as such, \"but I do object when taxation is justified on spurious or dishonest grounds,\" he says. 西蒙先生說過他並不反對稅收本身，“但我確實反對以無根據或不誠實的理由徵稅，”他說道。"]}]}]},"useful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有用的，有益的；<英，非正式>好的，熟練的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>useful</b>, you can use it to do something or to help you in some way. 有用的","examples":["The pressure cooker is very useful for people who go out all day. 壓力鍋對整天外出的人非常有用。","Hypnotherapy can be useful in helping you give up smoking. 催眠療法在幫助你戒菸方面可能有用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有用地","examples":["...the problems to which computers could be usefully applied. …可以應用計算機來解決的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object or skill <b>comes in useful</b>, it can help you achieve something in a particular situation. 有用","examples":["Extra blank paper will probably come in useful. 額外的空白紙可能用得著。"]}]}]},"yucky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>令人作嘔的，噁心的；討人厭的，不愉快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a food or other substance as <b>yucky</b>, you mean that it disgusts you. 令人作嘔的","examples":["She says it tastes yucky, so nurses add sweetener to make it go down easier. 她說這吃起來很噁心，所以護士加了增甜劑，讓她能吃下去。","...yucky cigar smoke. ...令人噁心的香菸味道。"]}]}]},"strong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"強壯的，健壯的；堅固的，結實的；堅強的，有主見的；堅定的，強烈的；有影響的，深刻的；（關係）穩固的，持久的；強有力的，有說服力的；實力強的，厲害的；有望成功的，可能性大的；精通的，擅長的；健康的；味重的；濃的；強效的；明顯的，顯著的；（貨幣）堅挺的，（行業）景氣的；強勁的，高速移動的；大量的，眾多的；多達……的，計有……的；強硬的，冒犯的；（語法）（動詞）強變化的，強變格的；（語音學）強讀式的，重讀的；（物理）強，強相互作用的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"強勁地，猛烈地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"強勢群體（the strong）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>strong</b> is healthy with good muscles and can move or carry heavy things, or do hard physical work. 強壯的","examples":["I'm not strong enough to carry him. 我不夠強壯，抱不動他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>strong</b> is confident and determined, and is not easily influenced or worried by other people. 堅定的","examples":["He is sharp and manipulative with a strong personality. 他機靈且善於擺佈別人，有著很強的個性。","It's up to managers to be strong and do what they believe is right. 立場堅定並做他們認為正確的事情是經理們的責任。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Strong</b> objects or materials are not easily broken and can support a lot of weight or resist a lot of strain. 堅固的","examples":["The vacuum flask has a strong casing, which won't crack or chip. 這個真空瓶有一個堅固的外殼，不會破裂。","Glue the mirror in with a strong adhesive. 用牢固的粘合劑把這面鏡子粘上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> wind, current, or other force has a lot of power or speed, and can cause heavy things to move. (風、水流等) 強勁的","examples":["Strong winds and torrential rain combined to make conditions terrible for golfers in the Scottish Open. 強風和暴雨交加使得蘇格蘭公開賽的環境對高爾夫球員很糟糕。","A fairly strong current seemed to be moving the whole boat. 一股非常強勁的水流似乎要把整隻小船沖走。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> impression or influence has a great effect on someone. (印象或影響) 深刻的; 強烈的","examples":["We're glad if our music makes a strong impression, even if it's a negative one. 如果我們的音樂能產生一個深刻的印象，即使它是負面的，我們也很高興。","There will be a strong incentive to enter into a process of negotiation. 將會有一個強烈的刺激來進入談判的過程。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have <b>strong</b> opinions on something or express them using <b>strong</b> words, you have extreme or very definite opinions which you are willing to express or defend. (觀點、言辭) 堅定的","examples":["She is known to hold strong views on Cuba. 她因對古巴持有堅定的觀點而聞名。","I am a strong supporter of the president. 我是總統的一位堅定的支持者。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone in authority takes <b>strong</b> action, they act firmly and severely. 堅決的","examples":["The American public deserves strong action from Congress. 美國公眾應受到來自國會的堅決的行動。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If there is a <b>strong</b> case or argument for something, it is supported by a lot of evidence. 有說服力的","examples":["The testimony presented offered a strong case for acquitting her on grounds of self-defence. 所出示的證據為以正當防衛之由宣判她無罪提供了一個有說服力的理由。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If there is a <b>strong</b> possibility or chance that something is true or will happen, it is very likely to be true or to happen. (可能性、機率) 極大的","examples":["There is a strong possibility that the cat contracted the condition by eating contaminated pet food. 有一種極大的可能性就是那隻貓吃了受汙染的寵物食品而染上了病。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Your <b>strong</b> points are your best qualities or talents, or the things you are good at. 優秀的; 擅長的","examples":["Discretion is not Jeremy's strong point. 謹慎不是傑里米的長處。","Exports may be the only strong point in the economy over the next six to 12 months. 出口也許是隨後的6至12個月經濟中的惟一強項。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> competitor, candidate, or team is good or likely to succeed. (競爭對手等) 強大的","examples":["She was a strong contender for the Olympic team. 她曾是奧林匹克隊的一個強大的競爭者。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If a relationship or link is <b>strong</b>, it is close and likely to last for a long time. (關係) 牢固的","examples":["He felt he had a relationship strong enough to talk frankly to Sarah. 他覺得他有著一種足夠牢固的關係以使他與莎拉坦誠地交談。","This has tested our marriage, and we have come through it stronger than ever. 這已經考驗了我們的婚姻，我們經歷它之後比以往更加牢固。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> currency, economy, or industry has a high value or is very successful. (貨幣) 堅挺的; (經濟、行業) 有實力的","examples":["The U.S. dollar continued its strong performance in Tokyo today. 美元今天在東京繼續了其堅挺的表現。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If something is a <b>strong</b> element or part of something else, it is an important or large part of it. (成分) 重要的; 強大的","examples":["We are especially encouraged by the strong representation, this year, of women in information technology disciplines. 我們尤其被今年女性在資訊科技學科中的重要表現所鼓舞。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You can use <b>strong</b> when you are saying how many people there are in a group. For example, if a group is twenty strong, there are twenty people in it. 多達…的","examples":["Ukraine indicated that it would establish its own army, 400,000 strong. 烏克蘭表示它將建立自己的軍隊，多達40萬人。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> drink, chemical, or drug contains a lot of the particular substance which makes it effective. (飲品) 濃的; (化學品、藥物) 含量高的","examples":["Strong coffee or tea late at night may cause sleeplessness. 晚上喝濃咖啡或濃茶可能引起失眠。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"A <b>strong</b> colour, flavour, smell, sound, or light is intense and easily noticed. (顏色、味道) 濃烈的; 響亮的; (光線) 強烈的","examples":["As she went past there was a gust of strong perfume. 當她經過時有一股濃烈的香水味。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If someone has a <b>strong</b> accent, they speak in a distinctive way that shows very clearly what country or region they come from. (口音) 濃重的","examples":["\"Good, Mr. Ryle,\" he said in English with a strong French accent. “好，賴爾先生，”他用帶著濃重的法國口音的英語說道。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堅固地","examples":["The fence was very strongly built, with very large posts. 這個柵欄用粗大的木樁建得非常堅固。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"強勁地","examples":["The metal is strongly attracted to the surface. 這塊金屬牢牢地附在表面上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"深刻地; 強烈地","examples":["He is strongly influenced by Spanish painters such as Goya and El Greco. 他被戈雅、艾爾·格列柯等西班牙畫家們強烈地影響了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"堅定地","examples":["Obviously you feel very strongly about this. 顯然你對此感覺很堅定。","Republicans in the House were strongly opposed to lifting the ban. 眾議院的共和黨人們曾堅定地反對解除該禁令。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"有說服力地","examples":["He argues strongly for retention of NATO as a guarantee of peace. 他據理力爭北大西洋公約組織作為一個和平保障的保留。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"濃烈地; 響亮地; 強烈地","examples":["He leaned over her, smelling strongly of sweat. 他朝她俯下身來，散發著濃烈的汗味。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is still <b>going strong</b>, they are still alive, in good condition, or popular after a long time. 狀況良好; 興盛不衰","examples":["The old machinery was still going strong. 這臺舊機器依然狀況良好。"]}]}]},"yummy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>美味的，可口的；性感的，迷人的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"美味的食物（yummies）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yummy</b> food tastes very good. 好吃的","examples":["I'll bet they have yummy ice cream. 我打賭他們有好吃的冰激淋。","It smells yummy. 聞著好香。"]}]}]},"weak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"虛弱的，無力的；不牢固的；懦弱的，無判斷力的；無影響力的，無權力的；疲軟的，蕭條的；不擅長的；無說服力的；力量微弱的，無強度的；（光、熱或聲音）微弱的；無活力的，無生氣的；（飲品）稀的；（臉的部分）瘦小的，（容貌）不突出的；（受強烈情感影響而）腿發軟的；無效力的，沒有吸引力的；（動詞）弱的，規則的；非重讀的；弱電解的，弱電解質的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窮人，弱者，病人（the weak）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>weak</b>, they are not healthy or do not have good muscles, so that they cannot move quickly or carry heavy things. 虛弱的","examples":["I was too weak to move or think or speak. 我太虛弱了，不能動、不能思維、不能說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has an organ or sense that is <b>weak</b>, it is not very effective or powerful, or is likely to fail. (人的器官、感官) 衰弱的","examples":["She tired easily and had a weak heart. 她容易疲勞，心臟也比較弱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>weak</b>, you mean that they are not very confident or determined, so that they are often frightened or worried, or easily influenced by other people. 懦弱的","examples":["He was a nice doctor, but a weak man who wasn't going to stick his neck out. 他是個好醫生，但為人懦弱，遇事不敢出頭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone's voice or smile as <b>weak</b>, you mean that it not very loud or big, suggesting that the person lacks confidence, enthusiasm, or physical strength. (聲音、微笑等) 微弱的","examples":["His weak voice was almost inaudible. 他聲音微弱得幾乎聽不到。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an object or surface is <b>weak</b>, it breaks easily and cannot support a lot of weight or resist a lot of strain. 易碎的; 薄弱的","examples":["The owner said the bird may have escaped through a weak spot in the aviary. 主人說那隻鳥可能是從鳥舍的一個薄弱處逃出去的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If individuals or groups are <b>weak</b>, they do not have any power or influence. (個人或團體) 弱小的; 缺少力量和影響力的","examples":["The council was too weak to do anything about it. 理事會軟弱無能，對此無能為力。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>weak</b> government or leader does not have much control, and is not prepared or able to act firmly or severely. (政府或領導人) 軟弱無力的","examples":["The changes come after mounting criticism that the government is weak and indecisive. 隨著對政府軟弱無能、優柔寡斷的批評不斷高漲，情況終於有了變化。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you describe something such a country's currency, economy, industry, or government as <b>weak</b>, you mean that it is not successful, and may be likely to fail or collapse. (貨幣、經濟、工業、政府等) 疲軟的","examples":["The weak dollar means American goods are relative bargains for foreigners. 美元疲軟意味著美國產品對外國顧客來說是相對便宜的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something such as an argument or case is <b>weak</b>, it is not convincing or there is little evidence to support it. (論點) 沒有說服力的; (案例) 缺少證據的","examples":["Do you think the prosecution made any particular errors, or did they just have a weak case? 你認為控方是真的出了紕漏，還是隻是證據不足？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>weak</b> drink, chemical, or drug contains very little of a particular substance, for example, because a lot of water has been added to it. 稀薄的","examples":["Grace poured a cup of weak tea. 格萊斯倒了一杯淡茶。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Your <b>weak</b> points are the qualities or talents you do not possess, or the things you are not very good at. 弱的","examples":["Geography was my weak subject. 地理課是我的弱項。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"虛弱地","examples":["\"I'm all right,\" Max said weakly, but his breathing came in jagged gasps. “我沒事，”馬克斯虛弱地說，但是他呼吸艱難，長短不均。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"微弱地","examples":["He smiled weakly at reporters. 他朝記者們淡淡一笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>weak</b> physical force does not have much power or intensity. (力量) 微弱的","examples":["The molecules in regular liquids are held together by relatively weak bonds. 常規液體中的分子被相對較弱的結合物聚合在一起。","Strong winds can turn boats when the tide is weak. 潮汐微弱時，強風可以掀翻船隻。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"微弱地","examples":["The mineral is weakly magnetic. 這種礦石有輕微的磁性。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"軟弱無力地","examples":["...the weakly-led movement for reform. …領導乏力的改革運動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"沒有說服力地","examples":["Bush listened to that statement and responded rather weakly. 布什聽了那個宣告，做的回應卻相當沒有說服力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"懦弱","examples":["Many people felt that admitting to stress was a sign of weakness. 很多人認為，承認壓力是懦弱的表現。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The weak</b> are people who are weak. 弱勢群體","examples":["He voiced his solidarity with the weak and defenseless. 他表示自己站在弱勢無助群體一邊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"軟弱無能","examples":["It made me feel patronized, in a position of weakness. 這讓我感到受惠於人，處於弱勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"疲軟","examples":["The weakness of his regime is showing more and more. 他政權的疲弱性日益顯露。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"弱點","examples":["His only weakness is his temperament. 他惟一的弱點是他的脾氣。"]}]}]},"which":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"哪一個，哪一些；（指明事物）……的那個，……的那些；（進一步提供有關某事物的資訊）那個，那些；哪個是哪個（用於 cannot tell/know which is which）"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"哪一個，哪一些；（指明事物）……的那個，……的那些；（進一步提供有關某事物的資訊）那個，那些"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"哪一個，哪一些；無論哪個；（進一步提供有關某事物的資訊）那個，那些"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算）Unix/Linux 命令，用於在 PATH 中查詢可執行檔案的位置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>which</b> in questions when there are two or more possible answers or alternatives. 哪一個 (用於疑問句，表示選擇)","examples":["\"You go down that passageway over there.\"—\"Which one?\" “你順著那邊的過道走。”—“哪個過道？”","Which vitamin supplements are good for you? 哪種維生素補品對你有好處？"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>which</b> to refer to a choice between two or more possible answers or alternatives. 哪個 (指所做出的那個選擇)","examples":["I wanted to know which school it was you went to. 我想知道你就讀的是哪所學校。","I can't remember which teachers I had. 我不記得哪些老師教過我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Which</b> is also a determiner. 這個","examples":["The chances are you haven't fully decided what you want from your career at the moment, in which case you're definitely not cut out to be a boss yet! 很可能你目前沒有完全確定要從職業中得到什麼，在這種情況下，你肯定還沒有具備做老闆的素質。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Which</b> is also a conjunction. 哪個","examples":["In her panic she couldn't remember which was Mr. Grainger's cabin. 慌亂中，她不記得哪間是格蘭傑先生的船艙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>which</b> at the beginning of a relative clause when specifying the thing that you are talking about. In such clauses, which has the same meaning as <b>that</b>. 引導關係從句，具體說明所談論的事，此時與(that)意思相同","examples":["Soldiers opened fire on a car which failed to stop at an army checkpoint. 士兵們向一輛沒在軍事檢查站停下來的汽車開了火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>which</b> to refer back to an idea or situation expressed in a previous sentence or sentences, especially when you want to give your opinion about it. 這個 (指前面所說過的內容，尤其要發表個人意見時)","examples":["They ran out of drink. Which actually didn't bother me because I wasn't drinking. 他們沒有酒了，這個其實對我倒無所謂，因為我當時沒在喝酒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cannot tell the difference between two things, you can say that you do not know <b>which is which</b>. 哪個是哪個 (指無法區分兩者的不同)","examples":["They all look so alike to me that I'm never sure which is which. 它們在我看來簡直一模一樣，我永遠分不清哪個是哪個。"]}]}]},"those":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"那些（that 的複數；用於複數可數名詞前，指已提及、雙方共知或較遠的人或事物）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"那些（that 的複數；單獨指代已提及或語境中明確的人或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> to refer to people or things which have already been mentioned. 那些 (指已提及的人或物)","examples":["Witnesses said that two people were killed, but those accounts could not be confirmed. 目擊者說兩人遇害，但那些說法都沒法得到證實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> when you are referring to people or things that are a distance away from you in position or time, especially when you indicate or point to them. 那些 (指在空間或時間上離說話者稍遠的人或物)","examples":["What are those buildings? 那些建築物是什麼？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> to refer to someone or something when you are going to give details or information about them. 那些 (指將要詳細談到的人或物)","examples":["Those people who took up weapons to defend themselves are political prisoners. 那些拿起武器自衛的人是些政治犯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> when you refer to things that you expect the person you are talking to to know about or when you are checking that you are both thinking of the same people or things. 那些 (指雙方均瞭解的人或事物)","examples":["He did buy me those daffodils a week or so ago. 他確實在大約一週前給我買了那些水仙花。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Those</b> is also a pronoun. 那些","examples":["I understand that there are a number of projects going on. Could you tell us a little bit about those? 我知道有一些專案正在進行之中。你能給我們簡單談談那些專案嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Those</b> is also a pronoun. 那些","examples":["I like these but not those. 我喜歡這些，而不是那些。","Those are nice shoes. Where'd you get them? 那些鞋子很不錯。你在哪兒買的？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> to introduce more information about something already mentioned, instead of repeating the noun which refers to it. 那些 (對已提及事物作補充說明以免重複)","examples":["The interests he is most likely to enjoy will be those which enable him to show off himself or his talents. 他最有可能感興趣的，是那些能讓他自我炫耀或賣弄才華的事情。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>those</b> to mean \"people.\" 人們","examples":["A little selfish behaviour is unlikely to cause real damage to those around us. 有點兒自私的行為不太可能對我們周圍的人們造成真正的傷害。"]}]}]},"what":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"什麼，什麼樣的；（指數量的全部）所……的；全部的，所有的；多麼（好或壞）的，何等的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"什麼；（感嘆）多麼；無論什麼；……的事物"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（用於動詞和形容詞後引導名詞性關係從句）什麼，所……的事物；（用於強調句型句首）所……的（是……）；……那樣的（事物）；（指全部的量）所有的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（表示驚訝、氣憤、懷疑、喜歡、厭惡等）什麼，真的嗎；（口語，用於應答或請對方重複）什麼？"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"到什麼程度，在哪一方面；（口語）哦，呃（用於暫停思考）；<非正式，舊>（用於句末徵求同意）是吧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> in questions when you ask for specific information about something that you do not know. 什麼 (用於疑問句，就所不知道的事詢問具體資訊)","examples":["What do you want? 你要什麼？","What did she tell you, anyway? 她到底對你說了什麼？","\"Has something happened?\"—\"It certainly has.\"—\"What?\" “發生了什麼事嗎？”—“是的。”—“是什麼事？”"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>What</b> is also a determiner. 什麼","examples":["What time is it? 現在幾點鐘？","What crimes are the defendants being charged with? 被告被控何罪？","\"The heater works.\"—\"What heater?\" “加熱器可以用。” —“什麼加熱器？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>What</b> is also a determiner. 什麼","examples":["I didn't know what college I wanted to go to. 我不知道我想上什麼樣的大學。","I didn't know what else to say. 我不知道還能再說點什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>What</b> is also a determiner. 所有的","examples":["They had used what money they had. 他們用盡了所有的錢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>What</b> is also a determiner. 多麼","examples":["What pretty hair she has, nice and thick. 她的頭髮多漂亮啊，好看又濃密。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, when you are referring to a situation that is unknown or has not been specified. 什麼 (用在某些詞後，尤其是動詞和形容詞後，指未知或不確定的情形)","examples":["You can imagine what it would be like driving a car into a brick wall at 30 miles an hour. 你可以想像以每小時30英里的速度，開車向一面磚牆撞去會是什麼樣子。","I want to know what happened to Norman. 我想知道諾曼出什麼事了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> at the beginning of a clause in structures where you are changing the order of the information to give special emphasis to something. 用於某些從句之首，表示強調","examples":["What precisely triggered off yesterday's riot is still unclear. 具體是什麼引發了昨天的暴亂仍然不清楚。","What I wanted, more than anything, was a few days' rest. 我最想要的是休息幾天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> in expressions such as <b>what is called</b> and <b>what amounts to</b> when you are giving a description of something. …那樣的","examples":["She had been in what doctors described as an irreversible vegetative state for five years. 她陷入醫生們所說的一種不可逆轉的植物人狀態已達5年之久。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> to indicate that you are talking about the whole of an amount that is available to you. 所有的 (指所能獲得的全部)","examples":["He drinks what is left in his glass as if it were water. 他把杯子裡所剩下的全部喝光，好像那是水一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>What?</b>\" to tell someone who has indicated that they want to speak to you that you have heard them and are inviting them to continue. 什麼？ (表示聽到對方的話，請對方繼續說下去)","examples":["\"Dad?\"—\"What?\"—\"Can I have the car tonight?\" “爸爸？”—“什麼？”—“我今晚可以用車嗎？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>What?</b>\" when you ask someone to repeat the thing that they have just said because you did not hear or understand it properly. \"What?\" is more informal and less polite than expressions such as \"Pardon?\" and \"Excuse me?\" 什麼 (表示沒聽清楚或沒聽明白而請別人重複剛說過的話，沒有)(pardon)(和)(excuse me##excuse)(正式和禮貌)","examples":["\"They could paint this place,\" she said. \"What?\" he asked. “他們可以把這個地方油漆一下，”她說。“什麼？”他問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>What</b>\" to express surprise. 表示吃驚","examples":["\"Adolphus Kelling, I arrest you on a charge of trafficking in narcotics.\"—\"What?\" 阿道弗斯·克林，我現在以販毒的罪名逮捕你。”—“什麼？”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>guess what</b> or <b>do you know what</b> to introduce a piece of information that is surprising, that is not generally known, or that you want to emphasize. 你知道嗎 (用於講述讓人吃驚的、不為人知的訊息，或表示強調)","examples":["Guess what? I'm going to dinner at Mrs. Chang's tonight. 你知道嗎？我今晚要去常太太家吃晚飯啦。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>so what?</b> or <b>what of it?</b> to indicate that the previous remark seems unimportant, uninteresting, or irrelevant to you. 那又怎麼樣呢 (表示別人剛說的話對自己不重要、沒意思或不相干)","examples":["\"What if there is no kerosene this winter?\" said Al.—\"So what?\" she said. \"We still have electricity.\" “今年冬天如果沒有煤油可怎麼辦呢？”阿爾說。—“那又怎麼樣？”她說。“我們還有電呢。”","\"You're talking to yourself.\"—\"Well, what of it?\" “你在自言自語。”—“呵，那又怎麼樣？”"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> in exclamations to emphasize an opinion or reaction. 多麼 (用於感嘆句，強調某種看法或反應)","examples":["What a horrible thing to do. 做這樣的事多可怕！"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>what</b> to indicate that you are making a guess about something such as an amount or value. 嗯 (表示對數量或價值等的猜測)","examples":["It's, what, eleven years or more since he's seen her. 自從他上次見到她，已經有，嗯，11年甚至更久了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In conversation, you say <b>or what?</b> after a question as a way of stating an opinion forcefully and showing that you expect other people to agree. 不然又是什麼 (用於問句末尾，更有力地陳述觀點，並期待別人同意自己的看法)","examples":["Look at that moon. Is that beautiful or what? 看那月亮。很美，不是嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>Tell you what</b>\" to introduce a suggestion or offer. 你聽我說 (表示提出建議)","examples":["Tell you what, let's stay here another day. 你聽我說，咱們在這兒再住一天吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>what about</b> at the beginning of a question when you make a suggestion, offer, or request. …怎麼樣 (用於問句句首，表示提建議或要求)","examples":["What about going out with me tomorrow? 明天和我一塊出去怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>what about</b> or <b>what of</b> when you introduce a new topic or a point that seems relevant to a previous remark. …又怎麼樣 (用於引入與剛說過的話相關的新話題或觀點)","examples":["Now you've talked about work on daffodils, what about other commercially important flowers, like roses? 既然你談到了種植水仙，那麼其他有重要商業價值的花卉，如玫瑰，又怎麼樣呢？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>what about</b> a particular person or thing when you ask someone to explain why they have asked you about that person or thing. …怎麼了 (用於請別人解釋提問的原因)","examples":["\"This thing with the Corbett woman.\"—\"Oh, yeah. What about her?\" “與那個姓科位元的女人有關的那件事。”—“噢，是啊，她怎麼了？”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say <b>what if</b> at the beginning of a question when you ask about the consequences of something happening, especially something undesirable. 如果…怎樣 (用於疑問句之首，詢問某事尤其是不希望發生的事的後果)","examples":["What if this doesn't work out? 如果這行不通怎麼辦呢？"]}]}]},"am":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是（be 的第一人稱單數現在時）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"上午（同 a.m.）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（AM）調幅（Amplitude Modulation）；威爾士國民議會（assembly member）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（Am.）<書面>美國人（American）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（AM）（中、英）安（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Am</b> is the first person singular of the present tense of . <b>Am</b> is often shortened to <b>'m</b> in spoken English. The negative forms are \"I am not\" and \"I'm not.\" In questions and tags in spoken English, these are usually changed to \"aren't I.\" (be)的現在時第一人稱單數形式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Armenia 亞美尼亞","examples":[]}]}]},"add":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"新增，摻入；（使）相加，加；增加；增添（某種特性）；把……計算在內，包括；補充說，繼續說"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"注意力缺陷障礙，多動症（ADD）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>add</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you put it in or on the other thing, to increase, complete, or improve it. 新增","examples":["Add the grated cheese to the sauce. 把磨碎的乳酪加進那種醬中。","Since 1908, chlorine has been added to drinking water. 自從1908年起，氯就被新增到飲用水當中了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>add</b> numbers or amounts <b>together</b>, you calculate their total. 加","examples":["Banks add all the interest and other charges together. 銀行把所有利息和其他費用加在一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>add</b> a particular quality <b>to</b> something means to cause it to have that quality. 增添 (某種特性)","examples":["The generous amount of garlic adds flavour. 大量的蒜會增添滋味。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>add</b> something when you are speaking, you say something more. (講話) 補充","examples":["\"You can tell that he is extremely embarrassed,\" Mr. Montoya added. “你可以看出他是非常尷尬的，”蒙託亞先生補充道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>adds</b> <b>to</b> another, it makes the other thing greater in degree or amount. 增加","examples":["This latest incident will add to the pressure on the White House. 最近的這起事件會給白宮增加更多的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>add</b>, you are able to calculate the total of numbers or amounts. 做加法","examples":["More than a quarter of seven-year-olds cannot add properly. 超過1/4的7歲兒童不會正確地做加法。"]}]}]},"are":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是；be 的現在時複數形式及第二人稱單數形式（there are 表示“有、存在”；口語中常縮略為 -'re）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"公畝（面積單位，等於 100 平方米，符號為 a）；Are（阿雷）人名或姓氏，多見於義大利語、西班牙語、芬蘭語語境"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Are</b> is the plural and the second person singular of the present tense of the verb . <b>Are</b> is often shortened to <b>-'re</b> after pronouns in spoken English. 是 (be)(的現在時複數以及第二人稱單數形式)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a unit of area equal to 100 sq metres or 119.599 sq yards; one hundredth of a hectare (面積單位)100平方米; 119.599平方碼 ; 一公頃的百分之一 ( symbol: a)","examples":[]}]}]},"agree":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"同意，贊成；答應，接受；達成一致意見；商定，約定；相符，吻合；贊同；（語法）呼應；批准，認可（計劃、要求等）；適合（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>agree</b> <b>with</b> each other about something, they have the same opinion about it or say that they have the same opinion. 同意","examples":["Both have agreed on the need for the money. 雙方都同意需要那筆錢。","So we both agree there's a problem? 那麼我們兩個人都同意是有一個問題啦？","I agree with you that the open system is by far the best. 我同意你的觀點，開放的系統是目前最好的。","\"It's appalling.\"—\"It is. I agree.\" “這糟透了。”—“對。我同意。”","I agree with every word you've just said. 我同意你剛剛說的每個字。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>agree</b> <b>on</b> something, they all decide to accept or do something. 達成一致意見","examples":["The warring sides have agreed on an unconditional ceasefire. 交戰各方已經對無條件停火達成了一致意見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In grammar, if a word <b>agrees</b> <b>with</b> a noun or pronoun, it has a form that is appropriate to the number or gender of the noun or pronoun. For example, in \"He hates it,\" the singular verb agrees with the singular pronoun \"he.\" 一致","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one account of an event or one set of figures <b>agrees</b> <b>with</b> another, the two accounts or sets of figures are the same or are consistent with each other. 一致","examples":["His second statement agrees with facts as stated by the other witnesses. 他的第二項陳述和其他證人所陳述的事實一致。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>agree</b> <b>to</b> do something, you say that you will do it. If you <b>agree</b> <b>to</b> a proposal, you accept it. 答應; 接受","examples":["He agreed to pay me for the drawings. 她答應為這些畫付給我錢。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>agree</b> <b>with</b> an action or suggestion, you approve of it. 贊同","examples":["You didn't want to ask anybody whether they agreed with what you were doing. 你不想問任何人他們是否贊同你在做的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people who are arguing about something <b>agree to disagree</b> or <b>agree to differ</b>, they decide to stop arguing because neither of them is going to change their opinion. 同意各自保留意見 (以停止爭論)","examples":["You and I are going to have to agree to disagree then. 那麼你和我將同意各自保留意見。"]}]}]},"allow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"允許，准許；使有可能；任憑；<正式>接受，認可；促使；（特地）酌留；承認，同意；讓對方得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is allowed</b> <b>to</b> do something, it is all right for them to do it and they will not get into trouble. 允許","examples":["The children are allowed to watch TV after school. 孩子們被允許在放學後看電視。","Smoking will not be allowed. 吸菸將被禁止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are allowed</b> something, you are given permission to have it or are given it. 准許","examples":["Gifts like chocolates or flowers are allowed. 像巧克力或者花這樣的禮物是准許的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>allow</b> something <b>to</b> happen, you do not prevent it. 容許","examples":["He won't allow himself to fail. 他不容許自己失敗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>allows</b> another thing <b>to</b> happen, the first thing creates the opportunity for the second thing to happen. 使能夠 (發生)","examples":["The compromise will allow him to continue his free market reforms. 這個妥協將使他得以繼續他的自由市場改革。","...an attempt to allow the Muslim majority a greater share of power. …使穆斯林多數派分享更多權力的一種嘗試。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>allow</b> a particular length of time or a particular amount of something <b>for</b> a particular purpose, you include it in your planning. (在計劃中) 酌留","examples":["Please allow 28 days for delivery. 請留出28天的送貨時間。"]}]}]},"bathe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"洗澡，給（某人）洗澡；游泳，嬉水；用水清洗（尤指身體部位）；（光線）灑滿，覆蓋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"游泳，洗浴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bathe</b>, you have a bath. 洗盆浴","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bathe</b> in a sea, river, or lake, you swim, play, or wash yourself in it. Birds and animals can also <b>bathe</b>. (在海、河、湖裡) 游泳、戲水; 洗澡","examples":["The police have warned the city's inhabitants not to bathe in the polluted river. 警方已經警告該市市民不要在受汙染的河裡游泳。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bathe</b> someone, especially a child, you wash them in a bathtub. 給…洗澡","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bathe</b> a part of your body or a wound, you wash it gently or soak it in a liquid. 浸洗; 浸泡","examples":["Bathe the infected area in a salt solution. 把感染的部位浸泡在鹽水溶液裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place <b>is bathed</b> <b>in</b> light, it is covered with light, especially a gentle, pleasant light. 以 (尤為柔和、令人愉悅的光線) 覆蓋","examples":["The arena was bathed in warm sunshine. 該運動場沐浴在溫暖的陽光中。","I was led to a small room bathed in soft red light. 我被領進了一個被柔和的紅光籠罩著的小房間。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bathe</b> is also a noun. 游泳","examples":["They took an early morning bathe in the lake. 他們在湖裡進行了晨泳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"游泳; 戲水; 洗澡","examples":["Bathing is not allowed. 禁止游泳。"]}]}]},"become":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"變得，變成，成為；適合，使顯得漂亮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>becomes</b> a particular thing, they start to change and develop into that thing, or start to develop the characteristics mentioned. 變成","examples":["I first became interested in Islam while I was doing my nursing training. 我在進行護理訓練的時候，我初次對伊斯蘭教產生了興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>becomes</b> someone, it makes them look attractive or it seems right for them. 適合; 與…相稱","examples":["Does khaki become you? 卡其布適合你嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you wonder <b>what</b> has <b>become of</b> someone or something, you wonder where they are and what has happened to them. (某人、某事物) 怎麼樣了","examples":["She thought constantly about her family; she might never know what had become of them. 她經常想著她的家人；她也許永遠都不知道他們怎麼樣了。"]}]}]},"ask":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"詢問，打聽；要求，請求；邀請，約請 ；指望，期待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ask</b> someone something, you say something to them in the form of a question because you want to know the answer. 問","examples":["\"How is Frank?\" he asked. “弗蘭克怎麼樣？”他問道。","I asked him his name. 我問了他的名字。","She asked me if I'd enjoyed my dinner. 她問我是否喜歡我的晚餐。","Maybe we should adopt the policy of \"don't ask, don't tell.\" 或許我們應該採用“不問不提”的政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>ask</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you tell them that you want them to do it. 讓 (某人做某事)","examples":["We had to ask him to leave. 我們不得不讓他離開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>ask</b> <b>to</b> do something, you tell someone that you want to do it. 要求","examples":["I asked to see the Director. 我要求見總經理。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>ask</b> someone's permission, opinion, or forgiveness, you try to obtain it by making a request. 徵求 (意見); 請求 (許可、原諒)","examples":["Please ask permission from whoever pays the phone bill before making your call. 打電話前請先徵得話費支付人的許可。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>ask</b> someone <b>to</b> an event or place, you invite them to go there. 邀請","examples":["Couldn't you ask Juan to the party? 你不能邀請胡安參加這個聚會嗎？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>is asking</b> a particular price <b>for</b> something, they are selling it for that price. 要 (價)","examples":["Mr. Pantelaras was asking $6,000 for his collection. 潘特萊拉斯先生在為他的藏品要價$6000。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ask for</b> something, you say that you would like it. 索要","examples":["I decided to go to the next house and ask for food. 我決定到隔壁房子去要吃的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>ask for</b> someone, you say that you would like to speak to them. 求見","examples":["There's a man at the gate asking for you. 大門口有個男人要見你。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You reply \"<b>don't ask me</b>\" when you do not know the answer to a question, usually when you are annoyed or surprised that you have been asked. 別問我","examples":["\"She's got other things on her mind, wouldn't you think?\" \"Don't ask me,\" murmured Chris. \"I've never met her.\" “她腦子裡想著別的事，你不認為嗎？”“別問我，”克里斯咕噥道，“我從未見過她。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>if you ask me</b>\" to emphasize that you are stating your personal opinion. 依我看","examples":["He was nuts, if you ask me. 依我看，他當時是瘋了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is asking for trouble</b> or <b>is asking for it</b>, you mean that they are behaving in a way that makes it very likely that they will get into trouble. 自找麻煩","examples":["To go ahead with the match after such clear advice had been asking for trouble. 在得到如此明確的忠告之後還要繼續比賽是在自找麻煩。"]}]}]},"belong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"應在……地方，應處於……狀況；適應，合得來；歸……所有；是……的成員，屬於（某團體或組織）；居住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>belongs to</b> you, you own it. 屬於","examples":["The house had belonged to her family for three or four generations. 這座房子屬於她家已有三四代了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that something <b>belongs to</b> a particular person when you are guessing, discovering, or explaining that it was produced by or is part of that person. (某人) 所做; 所有","examples":["The handwriting belongs to a male. 這筆跡出自一名男子之手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>belongs to</b> a particular group, they are a member of that group. 是…的成員","examples":["I used to belong to a youth club. 我曾是一個青年俱樂部的成員。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something or someone <b>belongs in</b> or <b>to</b> a particular category, type, or group, they are of that category, type, or group. 屬 (某一類別、型別、群)","examples":["The judges could not decide which category it belonged in. 法官們無法決定它屬於哪一類別。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>belongs to</b> a particular time, it comes from that time. 源自於; 屬於 (某一時期)","examples":["The pictures belong to an era when there was a preoccupation with high society. 這些圖片源於上層社會佔據主流的時代。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something <b>belongs to</b> someone, you mean that person has the right to it. 有權擁有","examples":["...but the last word belonged to Rosanne. …但最後的決定權歸羅桑所有。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that a time <b>belongs to</b> a particular system or way of doing something, you mean that that time is or will be characterized by it. (時代) 具有…的特徵","examples":["The future belongs to democracy. 未來將是民主的時代。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a baby or child <b>belongs to</b> a particular adult, that adult is his or her parent or the person who is looking after him or her. (小孩) 為…所監護","examples":["He deduced that the two children belonged to the couple. 他推斷這兩個孩子是那對夫婦的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>belongs</b> in a particular place or situation, that is where they should be. 屬於 (某地或環境情形)","examples":["You don't belong here. 你不屬於這裡。","They need to feel they belong. 他們需要有歸屬感。"]}]}]},"believe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"相信；認為，猜想；信教"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>believe</b> that something is true, you think it is true, but you are not sure. 認為","examples":["Experts believe that the coming drought will be extensive. 專家們認為即將到來的乾旱將會是大面積的。","We believe them to be hidden here in this apartment. 我們認為他們藏匿在這所公寓裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>believe</b> someone or if you <b>believe</b> what they say or write, you accept that they are telling the truth. 相信","examples":["He did not sound as if he believed her. 聽起來他似乎不相信她的話。","Never believe anything a married man says about his wife. 永遠別相信一個已婚男人說的關於自己妻子的話。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>believe</b> <b>in</b> fairies, ghosts, or miracles, you are sure that they exist or happen. If you <b>believe</b> <b>in</b> a god, you are sure of the existence of that god. 相信…的存在","examples":["I don't believe in ghosts. 我不相信有鬼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>believe in</b> a way of life or an idea, you are in favour of it because you think it is good or right. 贊成","examples":["He believed in marital fidelity. 他贊成對婚姻忠實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>believe in</b> someone or what they are doing, you have confidence in them and think that they will be successful. 對…有信心","examples":["If you believe in yourself you can succeed. 對自己有信心，你就能成功。"]}]}]},"begin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始，著手；開始說；開始發生，開始進行；以……為起點，起始於；首字母為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>begin</b> <b>to</b> do something means to start doing it. 開始 (做某事)","examples":["He stood up and began to move around the room. 他站了起來，開始在屋子裡走來走去。","The weight loss began to look more serious. 體重的減輕開始顯得更嚴重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>begins</b> or when you <b>begin</b> it, it takes place from a particular time onward. 使開始發生; 開始發生","examples":["The problems began last November. 問題於去年11月開始出現。","He has just begun his fourth year in hiding. 他剛剛開始他東躲西藏的生活的第4個年頭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>begin</b> <b>with</b> something, or <b>begin</b> <b>by</b> doing something, this is the first thing you do. 以 (某事、做某事) 開始","examples":["Could I begin with a few formalities? 我可以從一些例行程式開始嗎？","...a businessman who began by selling golf shirts from the boot of his car. …一個從銷售汽車行李箱裡的高爾夫襯衫起家的商人。","He began his career flipping hamburgers. 他以翻轉漢堡包開始他的職業生涯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>begin</b> to mention the first thing that someone says. 開始說; 以…做開場白","examples":["\"Professor Theron,\" he began, \"I'm very pleased to see you.\" “西倫教授，”他開始說道，“我非常高興見到你。”","He didn't know how to begin. 他不知道如何開場。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>began as</b> another thing, it first existed as the other thing before it changed into its present form. 起初是","examples":["What began as a local festival has blossomed into an international event. 起初的一個地方性的節日已經發展成了一項國際盛事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a thing or place <b>begins</b> somewhere, you are talking about one of its limits or edges. 起始於","examples":["The fate line begins close to the wrist. 命運線始於接近手腕處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a word <b>begins with</b> a particular letter, that is the first letter of that word. (某詞) 以 (某字母) 開頭","examples":["The first word begins with an F. 第一個詞以F開頭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>to begin with</b> when you are talking about the first stage of a situation, event, or process. 起初; 剛開始","examples":["It was great to begin with but now it's difficult. 這起初很順利，但現在難了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>to begin with</b> to introduce the first of several things that you want to say. 首先","examples":["\"What do scientists you've spoken with think about that?\"—\"Well, to begin with, they doubt it's going to work.\" “和你交談過的科學家們對此怎麼看？”——“噢，首先，他們懷疑這是否會奏效。”"]}]}]},"appear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"出現，呈現；首次使用，起源；出庭；演出，出場；出版，發表；記載，提及；看來，似乎；表現得……；<非正式>到達"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>appears</b> <b>to</b> be the way you describe it, you are reporting what you believe or what you have been told, though you cannot be sure it is true. 似乎","examples":["There appears to be increasing support for the leadership to take a more aggressive stance. 似乎有不斷增長的對領導層採取更強立場的支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>appears</b> <b>to</b> have a particular quality or characteristic, they give the impression of having that quality or characteristic. 表現得","examples":["She did her best to appear more self-assured than she felt. 她竭力表現得比她感覺的更為自信。","He is anxious to appear a gentleman. 他急於表現得像一位紳士。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>appears</b>, they move into a position where you can see them. 出現","examples":["A woman appeared at the far end of the street. 一個女人在街那端出現了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something new <b>appears</b>, it begins to exist or reaches a stage of development where its existence can be noticed. 顯現","examples":["...small white flowers which appear in early summer. …在初夏出現的小白花。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as a book <b>appears</b>, it is published or becomes available for people to buy. 出版","examples":["I could hardly wait for \"Boys' Life\" to appear each month. 我每個月幾乎都等不及《男孩生活》出版。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone <b>appears</b> <b>in</b> something such as a play, a show, or a television programme, they take part in it. (在戲劇、訪談、電視節目等中) 露面","examples":["Jill Bennett became John Osborne's fourth wife, and appeared in several of his plays. 吉爾·貝納特成為了約翰·奧斯本的第4任妻子，並在他的幾部戲劇中出演角色。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When someone <b>appears</b> <b>before</b> a court of law or <b>before</b> an official committee, they go there in order to answer charges or to give information as a witness. (在法庭上、正式委員會中) 出席","examples":["The defendants are expected to appear in federal court today. 被告們今天預期會在聯邦法院出庭。"]}]}]},"busy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"繁忙的，忙碌的；熱鬧的；全神貫注的；佔線的；繁瑣的，雜亂的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使自己忙於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"警官，警察"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>busy</b>, you are working hard or concentrating on a task, so that you are not free to do anything else. 忙碌的","examples":["What is it? I'm busy. 你說什麼？我正忙著呢。","They are busy preparing for a hectic day's activity on Saturday. 他們正忙著為星期六這一天熱鬧的活動做準備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>busy</b> time is a period of time during which you have a lot of things to do. 繁忙的","examples":["It'll have to wait. This is our busiest time. 不得不等一等。這是我們最繁忙的時候。","Even with her busy schedule she finds time to watch TV. 即使有著繁忙的日程安排，她還是抽時間看看電視。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>busy</b> thinking or worrying about something, you mean that it is taking all their attention, often to such an extent that they are unable to think about anything else. 全神貫注的","examples":["Companies are so busy analysing the financial implications that they overlook the effect on workers. 公司太專注於分析其財務影響，而忽略了對工人的影響。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>busy</b> place is full of people who are doing things or moving around. 熱鬧的","examples":["...a busy commercial street. …熱鬧的商業街。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a telephone line is <b>busy</b>, you cannot make your call because the line is already being used by someone else. 佔線的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>busy</b> <b>yourself</b> with something, you occupy yourself by dealing with it. 使忙於","examples":["He busied himself with the camera. 他忙於擺弄這部相機。","She busied herself getting towels ready. 她忙著準備好毛巾。"]}]}]},"be":{"summaries":[{"pos":"aux.","zh":"被（用於被動語態）；正，正在（用於進行時）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"是；有，存在；做，成為；發生"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Be）（緬）拜；（日）部（姓）；（朝）培；（中非）貝（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"aux.","pos_name":"助動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> with a present participle to form the continuous tenses of verbs. 後接動詞的現在分詞，構成動詞進行體","examples":["This is happening in every school throughout the country. 這在全國各校都正在發生。","She didn't always think carefully about what she was doing. 她不總是仔細思考自己正在做什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> with a past participle to form the passive voice. 後接動詞的過去分詞，構成被動語態","examples":["Her husband was killed in a car crash. 她丈夫在一場車禍中被奪去了性命。","Similar action is being taken by the U.S. government. 類似的行動正被美國政府所採取。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> with an infinitive to indicate that something is planned to happen, that it will definitely happen, or that it must happen. 後接動詞不定式，表“安排、註定、必然”等意","examples":["The talks are to begin tomorrow. 會談將於明天開始。","It was to be Johnson's first meeting with the board in nearly a month. 那將是近一個月來約翰遜與董事會的首次會面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> with an infinitive to say or ask what should happen or be done in a particular situation, how it should happen, or who should do it. 後接動詞不定式，用於說明或詢問特定情況下應該會怎樣、怎樣做、誰來做等","examples":["What am I to do without him? 沒有他我該怎麼辦？","Who is to say which of them had more power? 誰知道他們當中誰有更大權利？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>was</b> and <b>were</b> with an infinitive to talk about something that happened later than the time you are discussing, and was not planned or certain at that time. (was)和(were)接不定式表示說話時間之後發生的事","examples":["He started something that was to change the face of China. 他發起了某項後來改變了中國面貌的行動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>to be</b> seen, heard, or found in a particular place to mean that people can see it, hear it, or find it in that place. 後接(seen)、(heard)、(found)，表“可見到、可聽到、可發現”之意","examples":["Little traffic was to be seen on the streets. 路上幾乎沒有車輛可見。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> to introduce more information about the subject, such as its identity, nature, qualities, or position. 用於補充說明主語，表示其身份、性質、品質、位置等","examples":["She's my mother. 她是我母親。","He is a very attractive man. 他是個非常有吸引力的人。","He is fifty and has been through two marriages. 他50歲，已經經歷了兩次婚姻。","The sky was black. 天是黑的。","His house is next door. 他的房間在隔壁。","He's still alive, isn't he? 他還活著，是嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>be</b>, with \"it\" as the subject, in clauses where you are describing something or giving your judgment of a situation. 與主語(it)連用，用以描述事物或給出判斷","examples":["It was too chilly for swimming. 游泳太冷了。","Sometimes it is necessary to say no. 有時候說“不”是必要的。","It is likely that investors will face losses. 那時投資者將面臨虧損是很可能的。","It's nice having friends to chat to. 有朋友一起聊真好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> with the impersonal pronoun \"there\" in expressions like <b>there is</b> and <b>there are</b> to say that something exists or happens. 與非人稱代名詞(there)連用，表示存在或發生","examples":["Clearly there is a problem here. 顯然這裡有問題。","There are very few cars on this street. 這條馬路上很少有車輛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> as a link between a subject and a clause and in certain other clause structures, as shown below. 用於連線主語和分句或其他分句結構","examples":["Our greatest problem is convincing them. 我們最重要的問題是說服他們。","All she knew was that I'd had a broken marriage. 她所知道的就是我曾有過一次破裂的婚姻。","Local residents said it was as if there had been a nuclear explosion. 當地居民說好像發生過核爆炸。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>be</b> in expressions like <b>the thing is</b> and <b>the point is</b> to introduce a clause in which you make a statement or give your opinion. 用於(the thing is##thing)和(the point is)等表達中，引導一個分句，以陳述事實或表達觀點","examples":["The fact is, the players gave everything they had. 事實是，運動員們傾盡了所有。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The form \"<b>be</b>\" is used occasionally instead of the normal forms of the present tense, especially after \"whether.\" (be)有時用來替代通常的現在時形式，尤其在(whether)之後","examples":["They should then be able to refer you to the appropriate type of practitioner, whether it be your GP, dentist, or optician. 然後他們應當能夠介紹你去見合適科別的執業醫生，不管是你的全科醫師、牙醫還是配鏡師。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about what would happen <b>if it wasn't for</b> someone or something, you mean that they are the only thing that is preventing it from happening. 若不是因為","examples":["I could happily move back into an apartment if it wasn't for the fact that I'd miss my garden. 若不是因為我會惦記著花園，我本可以高興地搬回公寓。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Belgium 比利時","examples":[]}]}]},"darken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變暗，變黑；（使）變得陰鬱；（臉色）變陰沉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>darkens</b> or if a person or thing <b>darkens</b> it, it becomes darker. 變暗; 使變暗","examples":["The sky darkened abruptly. 天突然變暗了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's mood <b>darkens</b> or if something <b>darkens</b> their mood, they suddenly become unhappy. 黯淡; 使黯淡","examples":["My sunny mood suddenly darkened. 我快樂的情緒突然黯淡下來。"]}]}]},"decide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"影響（或決定）……的結果；斷定，判定；使下決心；決定，選定；裁決，判決"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>decide</b> to do something, you choose to do it, usually after you have thought carefully about the other possibilities. 決定","examples":["She decided to take a course in philosophy. 她決定修一門哲學課。","Think about it very carefully before you decide. 在你決定之前慎重地考慮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or group of people <b>decides</b> something, they choose what something should be like or how a particular problem should be solved. 裁定","examples":["She was still young, he said, and that would be taken into account when deciding her sentence. 她還年輕，他說，這一點對裁定關於她的判決時要考慮進去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event or fact <b>decides</b> something, it makes it certain that a particular choice will be made or that there will be a particular result. 決定","examples":["What happens next could decide their destiny. 接下來發生的事可能會決定他們的命運。","The election will decide if either party controls both houses of Congress. 這次選舉將決定是否由任一黨控制國會兩院。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>decide</b> that something is true, you form that opinion about it after considering the facts. 斷定","examples":["He decided Franklin must be suffering from a bad cold. 他斷定富蘭克林肯定是得了重感冒。"]}]}]},"bring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拿來，帶來； 使……轉入（新的話題）；移動；使處於某種狀況；導致，引起；起訴；提供；強迫（自己）做；標價，售價為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> someone or something <b>with</b> you when you come to a place, they come with you or you have them with you. 帶來","examples":["Remember to bring an apron or an old shirt to protect your clothes. 記著帶一條圍裙或一件舊襯衫來保護你的衣服。","Someone went upstairs and brought down a huge kettle. 有人上樓拿下來一個巨大的水壺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> something somewhere, you move it there. 把…移動到","examples":["Reaching into her pocket, she brought out a cigarette. 她把手伸進口袋，拿出一根香菸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> something that someone wants or needs, you get it for them or carry it to them. 拿給","examples":["He went and poured a brandy for Dena and brought it to her. 他去給德娜倒了杯白蘭地並拿給了她。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>bring</b> something or someone to a place or position means to cause them to come to the place or move into that position. 把…引到","examples":["I told you about what brought me here. 我告訴過你是什麼把我引到這裡來的。","The shock of her husband's arrival brought her to her feet. 丈夫的到來驚得她不由自主地站了起來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> something new <b>to</b> a place or group of people, you introduce it to that place or cause those people to hear or know about it. 把…引入 (某地); 把…介紹給 (某些人)","examples":["...the drive to bring art to the public. …把藝術介紹給大眾的動力。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>bring</b> someone or something into a particular state or condition means to cause them to be in that state or condition. 使處於 (某種狀態、情勢等)","examples":["He brought the car to a stop in front of the square. 他在廣場前把車停了下來。","They have brought down income taxes. 他們已經降低了所得稅。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>brings</b> a particular feeling, situation, or quality, it makes people experience it or have it. 帶來","examples":["He called on the United States to play a more effective role in bringing peace to the region. 他呼籲美國在給該地區帶來和平的問題上發揮更加有效的作用。","Her three children brought her joy. 她的3個孩子給她得帶來了快樂。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a period of time <b>brings</b> a particular thing, it happens during that time. 帶來","examples":["For Sandro, the new year brought disaster. 對桑德羅來說，新年給他帶來了災難。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When you are talking, you can say that something <b>brings</b> you <b>to</b> a particular point in order to indicate that you have now reached that point and are going to talk about a new subject. 帶入 (某話題)","examples":["And that brings us to the end of this special report from Germany. 那我們就此結束這篇來自德國的特別報道。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you cannot <b>bring</b> <b>yourself to</b> do something, you cannot do it because you find it too upsetting, embarrassing, or disgusting. 使自己 (做某事)","examples":["It is all very tragic and I am afraid I just cannot bring myself to talk about it at the moment. 太悲慘了，恐怕我現在還無法讓自己去談論它。"]}]}]},"build":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"建造，修建；發展，建立；逐漸增強"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"體形，體格；（尤指車輛的）造型，構造；構件"}],"sections":[]},"carry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提，扛，背；攜帶，佩戴；運送，載運；傳輸（水、電等）；傳播（疾病）；能記住，能回想起；支撐，承載；承擔（責任）；推動，發展；具有（某種特質）；帶有，導致；被判處（某種刑罰）；傳得遠；扔（或踢）到……距離；以多數同意批准（提議）；贏得……的支援；<美>贏得（州或地區的）選舉；標有，貼有；刊登，廣播；出售；懷（胎）；保持姿態；（加法）進位；準確地唱；超重，超載"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搬運；<美>帶球跑；擲（擊）球距離，（槍的）射程；<美>隨身攜帶（尤指槍）；（財政）轉記，結轉；<美，史>水上運輸的地方或路線；進位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>carry</b> something, you take it with you, holding it so that it does not touch the ground. 提; 抱","examples":["He was carrying a briefcase. 他提著公文包。","She carried her son to the car. 她抱著兒子向車走去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>carry</b> something, you have it with you wherever you go. 攜帶","examples":["You have to carry a pager so that they can call you in at any time. 你得帶個傳呼機，以便他們隨時可以聯絡到你。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>carries</b> a person or thing somewhere, it takes them there. 傳送","examples":["Flowers are designed to attract insects which then carry the pollen from plant to plant. 花兒天生就能吸引昆蟲，昆蟲則在植物之間傳遞花粉。","The delegation was carrying a message of thanks to President Mubarak. 代表團向穆巴拉克總統傳達謝意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>is carrying</b> a disease, they are infected with it and can pass it on to other people or animals. 攜帶 (病毒)","examples":["The test could be used to screen healthy people to see if they are carrying the virus. 這項測試可以用來檢查健康人群，看他們是否攜帶該病毒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an action or situation has a particular quality or consequence, you can say that it <b>carries</b> it. 具有; 帶有","examples":["Check that any medication you're taking carries no risk for your developing baby. 要確保服用的藥物不會對你正在發育的胎兒造成危險。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a quality or advantage <b>carries</b> someone into a particular position or through a difficult situation, it helps them to achieve that position or deal with that situation. 使位居; 使透過","examples":["He had the ruthless streak necessary to carry him into the cabinet. 他有著躋身內閣所必需的冷酷品性。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>carry</b> an idea or a method to a particular extent, you use or develop it to that extent. 運用; 發揮","examples":["It's not such a new idea, but I carried it to extremes. 這不是什麼新想法，但我卻把它發揮到了極致。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a newspaper or poster <b>carries</b> a picture or a piece of writing, it contains it or displays it. 刊登","examples":["Several papers carry the photograph of Mr. Anderson. 好幾家報紙都刊登了安德森先生的照片。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"In a debate, if a proposal or motion <b>is carried</b>, a majority of people vote in favour of it. 以多數票透過","examples":["A motion backing its economic policy was carried by 322 votes to 296. 一項支援其經濟政策的動議以322票對296票獲得透過。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a crime <b>carries</b> a particular punishment, a person who is found guilty of that crime will receive that punishment. 受 (某種處罰)","examples":["It was a crime of espionage and carried the death penalty. 那是間諜罪，處了死刑。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>carry</b> <b>yourself</b> in a particular way, you walk and move in that way. 帶…姿態","examples":["They carried themselves with great pride and dignity. 他們帶著非常驕傲和高貴的姿態。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a sound <b>carries</b>, it can be heard a long way away. (聲音) 傳得遠","examples":["Even in this stillness Leaphorn doubted if the sound would carry far. 即使置身如此的寧靜之中，利普霍恩仍然懷疑聲音是否可以傳得很遠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get carried away</b> or <b>are carried away</b>, you are so eager or excited about something that you do something hasty or foolish. 忘乎所以","examples":["I got completely carried away and almost cried. 我差點忘乎所以地叫出聲來。"]}]}]},"continue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）繼續，（使）延續；繼續說，接著說；移動，延伸；留任，維持原狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>continues</b> <b>to</b> do something, they keep doing it and do not stop. 繼續","examples":["I hope they continue to fight for equal justice after I'm gone. 我希望我走後他們繼續為司法公正而奮鬥。","Diana and Roy Jarvis are determined to continue working when they reach retirement age. 戴安娜·賈維斯和羅伊·賈維斯決心到退休年齡後還繼續工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>continues</b> or if you <b>continue</b> it, it does not stop. 使繼續; 繼續","examples":["He insisted that the conflict would continue until conditions were met for a ceasefire. 他堅持認為衝突會持續下去，直至停火條件得到滿足為止。","Outside the building people continue their vigil, huddling around bonfires. 在樓外，人們圍聚在篝火旁繼續守夜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> something or <b>continue</b> with something, you start doing it again after a break or interruption. (某人在歇息或被打斷後) 繼續 (做某事或某事)","examples":["I went up to my room to continue with my packing. 我上我房間去繼續收拾行李。","She looked up for a minute and then continued drawing. 她抬頭看了一會兒，然後繼續畫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>continues</b> or if you <b>continue</b> it, it starts again after a break or interruption. (某事在停頓或被打斷後) 繼續","examples":["He denies 18 charges. The trial continues today. 他否認18項指控。審判今天繼續。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b>, you begin speaking again after a pause or interruption. (在停頓或被打斷後) 繼續說","examples":["\"You have no right to intimidate this man,\" Alison continued. “你無權威脅這個男人，”愛麗森繼續說。","Tony drank some coffee before he continued. 託尼喝了些咖啡繼續講。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> <b>as</b> something or <b>continue</b> in a particular state, you remain in a particular job or state. 繼續 (原有工作或狀態)","examples":["He had hoped to continue as a full-time career officer. 他原本希望繼續當全職警官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> in a particular direction, you keep walking or travelling in that direction. 繼續走","examples":["He continued rapidly up the path, not pausing until he neared the Chapter House. 他繼續快速地沿著那小徑走，直到走近牧師會禮堂才停下腳步。"]}]}]},"discover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發現，找到；瞭解到，發覺，查明；發掘（人才）；初次接觸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>discover</b> something that you did not know about before, you become aware of it or learn of it. 發覺","examples":["She discovered that they'd escaped. 她發覺他們已經逃走了。","It was difficult for the inspectors to discover which documents were important and which were not. 檢查員們難以發現哪些檔案重要，哪些不重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is discovered</b>, someone finds them, either by accident or because they have been looking for them. 發現; 找到","examples":["A few days later his badly beaten body was discovered on a roadside outside the city. 幾天之後，他曾被毒打的屍體在城外一個路邊被發現了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>discovers</b> a new place, substance, scientific fact, or scientific technique, they are the first person to find it or become aware of it. (首次) 發現","examples":["...the first European to discover America. …第1個發現美洲的歐洲人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When an actor, musician, or other performer who is not well known <b>is discovered</b>, someone recognizes that they have talent and helps them in their career. 發現 (人才)","examples":["The Beatles were discovered in the early 1960s. 披頭士樂隊是在20世紀60年代初期被發現的。"]}]}]},"dirty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"骯髒的；下流的；卑鄙的，不誠實的；暗淡的；<美，非正式>吸毒的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弄髒，使變髒；變髒"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很，非常；卑鄙地，不誠實地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>dirty</b>, it is marked or covered with stains, spots, or mud, and needs to be cleaned. 骯髒的","examples":["She still did not like the woman who had dirty fingernails. 她仍然不喜歡那個手指甲很髒的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an action as <b>dirty</b>, you disapprove of it and consider it unfair, immoral, or dishonest. 卑鄙的","examples":["The gunman had been hired by a rival Mafia family to do the dirty deed. 該殺手被敵對的黑手黨家族僱來幹這件卑鄙的勾當。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as a joke, a book, or someone's language as <b>dirty</b>, you mean that it refers to sex in a way that some people find offensive. 下流的","examples":["He laughed at their dirty jokes and sang their raucous ballads. 他聽了他們的黃色笑話而發笑，又唱著他們吵鬧的民謠。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dirty</b> is also an adverb. 卑鄙地","examples":["Jim Browne is the kind of fellow who can fight dirty, but make you like it. 吉姆·布朗是那種可以卑鄙地和人爭鬥，卻又能讓你喜歡他的那種人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dirty</b> is also an adverb. 下流地","examples":["I'm often asked whether the men talk dirty to me. The answer is no. 經常有人問我那些男人是否跟我說過下流話，我的回答是沒有。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>dirty</b> something means to cause it to become dirty. 把…弄髒","examples":["He was afraid the dog's hairs might dirty the seats. 他擔心狗毛會把座椅弄髒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone gives you a <b>dirty look</b>, they look at you in a way which shows that they are angry with you. 怒視","examples":["Jack was being a real pain. Michael gave him a dirty look and walked out. 傑克真是個討厭的人。邁克爾厭惡地看了他一眼，然後走了出去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>do</b> someone's <b>dirty work</b> means to do a task for them that is dishonest or unpleasant and which they do not want to do themselves. 替…幹卑鄙的勾當; 為…幹難對付的活","examples":["As a member of an elite army hit squad, the army would send us out to do their dirty work for them. 身為精銳突擊隊的成員，部隊會派我們去執行艱難的任務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that an expression is <b>a dirty word</b> in a particular group of people, you mean it refers to an idea that they strongly dislike or disagree with. 非常難聽的詞; 禁忌字眼","examples":["Marketing became a dirty word at the company. “營銷”成了該公司的禁忌字眼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>airs</b> their <b>dirty laundry in public</b>, you disapprove of their discussing or arguing about unpleasant or private things in front of other people. There are several other forms of this expression, for example <b>wash</b> your <b>dirty linen in public</b>, or <b>wash</b> your <b>dirty laundry in public</b>. 家醜外揚","examples":["The captain refuses to air the team's dirty laundry in public. 隊長拒絕把球隊的醜事暴露在公眾面前。"]}]}]},"enter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"進入；開始從事，開始做；參加，報名；登記，輸入；正式提出；登場"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"回車鍵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>enter</b> a place such as a room or building, you go into it or come into it. 進入","examples":["He entered the room briskly and stood near the door. 他輕快地進入房間，靠近門站著。","When Spinks entered they all turned to look at him. 當斯平克斯進來的時候，他們都轉過來看著他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>enter</b> an organization or institution, you start to work there or become a member of it. 加入","examples":["He entered the firm as a junior associate. 他作為一名初級職員進入了該公司。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something new <b>enters</b> your mind, you suddenly think about it. 突然出現於","examples":["Dreadful doubts began to enter my mind. 可怕的疑慮開始突然出現在我的腦子裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If it does not <b>enter</b> your head <b>to</b> do, think, or say something, you do not think of doing that thing although you should have. 想過","examples":["It never enters his mind that anyone is better than him. 他從來沒有想過有人比他更出色。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>enters</b> a particular situation or period of time, they start to be in it or part of it. 開始進入","examples":["The war has entered its second month. 戰爭已進入了第二個月。","A million young people enter the labour market each year. 100萬年輕人每年進入勞動力市場。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>enter</b> a competition, race, or examination, you officially state that you will compete or take part in it. 參加","examples":["I run so well I'm planning to enter some races. 我跑得如此快，正計劃參加一些比賽。","As a boy soprano he entered many competitions, winning several gold medals. 作為一位童聲高音歌手，他參加過很多比賽，獲得過好幾枚金牌。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>enter</b> someone <b>for</b> a race or competition, you officially state that they will compete or take part in it. 使報名參加競賽","examples":["His wife Marie secretly entered him for the championship. 他的妻子瑪麗偷偷給他報名參加錦標賽。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>enter</b> something in a notebook, register, or financial account, you write it down. 記下","examples":["Each week she meticulously entered in her notebooks all sums received. 每週她在筆記本上一絲不苟地記下所收到的一切款項。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"To <b>enter</b> information <b>into</b> a computer or database means to record it there by typing it on a keyboard. 輸入","examples":["When a baby is born, they enter that baby's name into the computer. 當一個嬰兒出生時，他們將那個嬰兒的名字輸入電腦。"]}]}]},"correct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正確的，無誤的；恰當的，合適的；（行為）合乎禮節的，得體的；（行為）被人認可的，讚許的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"改正，糾正；批改；指出錯誤；（醫療）矯正"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>correct</b>, it is right and true. 正確的","examples":["The correct answers can be found at the bottom of page 8. 正確答案可以在第8頁的底部找到。","The following information was correct at time of going to press. 以下資訊在付印時是準確無誤的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>correct</b>, what they have said or thought is true. 正確的","examples":["You are absolutely correct. The leaves are from a bay tree. 你的看法完全正確。這些是月桂樹的葉子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>correct</b> thing or method is the thing or method that is required or is most suitable in a particular situation. 合適的; 恰當的","examples":["The use of the correct materials was crucial. 使用合適材料是重要的。","White was in no doubt the referee made the correct decision. 懷特毫不懷疑裁判做出了恰當的判罰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>correct</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you approve of their action. 正確的","examples":["You are perfectly correct in trying to steer your mother toward increased independence. 你在試圖引導你媽媽變得越來越獨立這點上是完全正確的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person or their behaviour is <b>correct</b>, their behaviour is in accordance with social or other rules. 符合公認準則的; 得體的","examples":["He was very polite and very correct. 他很有禮貌且舉止得體。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"正確地","examples":["Did I pronounce your name correctly? 我把你的名字讀對了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"合適地","examples":["If correctly executed, this shot will give them a better chance of getting the ball close to the hole. 如果處理得當，這一擊將使他們更有機會使球接近球洞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"正確地","examples":["I think the police commission acted correctly. 我認為警方行動正確。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"得體地","examples":["She began speaking politely, even correctly. 她開始禮貌地講了起來，甚至還很得體。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>correct</b> a problem, mistake, or fault, you do something which puts it right. 矯正","examples":["He may need surgery to correct the problem. 他可能需要手術來矯正這一問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>correct</b> someone, you say something which you think is more accurate or appropriate than what they have just said. 糾正","examples":["\"Actually, that isn't what happened,\" George corrects me. “事實上，不是那樣發生的，”喬治糾正我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>corrects</b> a piece of writing, they look at it and mark the mistakes in it. 批改","examples":["It took an extraordinary effort to focus on preparing his classes or correcting his students' work. 集中精力去備課或批改學生的作業費了他相當大的勁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"改正","examples":["...legislation to require the correction of factual errors. …要求對事實上的錯誤做出改正的法規。"]}]}]},"examine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"檢查，調查；考核，測驗；（醫生）診察；（尤指在法庭上）審問，查問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>examine</b> something, you look at it carefully. 仔細檢查","examples":["He examined her passport and stamped it. 他仔細檢查了她的護照，然後在上面蓋了章。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a doctor <b>examines</b> you, he or she looks at your body, feels it, or does simple tests in order to check how healthy you are. 診察","examples":["Another doctor examined her and could still find nothing wrong. 另一個醫生對她進行了檢查，仍然找不出任何毛病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an idea, proposal, or plan <b>is examined</b>, it is considered very carefully. 審查","examples":["The plans will be examined by officials. 這些計劃將由官員們審查。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are examined</b>, you are given a formal test in order to show your knowledge of a subject. 考試","examples":["...learning to cope with the pressures of being judged and examined by our teachers. …學會應付被老師們評價和考試所帶來的壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"仔細檢查","examples":["The navy is to carry out an examination of the wreck tomorrow. 海軍明天將會對失事船隻作仔細檢查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"診察","examples":["He was later discharged after an examination at the hospital. 後來他在醫院做過檢查後就出院了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"審查","examples":["The government said it was studying the implications, which \"required very careful examination and consideration.\" 政府稱正在對可能的影響進行研究，而這“需要仔細的審查和考慮”。"]}]}]},"eat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吃，吃飯；侵蝕，損耗；煩擾（be eating）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"少量食物，點心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>eat</b> something, you put it into your mouth, chew it, and swallow it. 吃","examples":["She was eating a sandwich. 她正在吃一個三明治。","I ate slowly and without speaking. 我慢慢地吃著，沒講話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>eat</b>, you have a meal. 吃飯","examples":["Let's go out to eat. 我們出去吃飯吧。","We ate lunch together every day. 我們每天一起吃午餐。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is eating</b> you, it is annoying or worrying you. 煩擾","examples":["\"What the hell's eating you?\" he demanded. “到底是什麼在煩你？”他問道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>eat</b> sensibly or healthily, you eat food that is good for you. 飲食","examples":["...a campaign to persuade people to eat more healthily. …一場勸說人們健康飲食的運動。"]}]}]},"dry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"乾的；乾旱的，少雨的；（頭髮或皮膚）乾燥的，乾性的；冷麵幽默的；枯燥乏味的；口乾的，口渴的；脫水的，沒有汁的；（酒）無甜味的，不含糖的；（國家）禁酒的；冷漠的，沒有感情的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變幹；變乾硬；（因忘記說什麼而）張口結舌，說不出話來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"乾燥過程（或事例）；<美>支援禁酒者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>dry</b>, there is no water or moisture on it or in it. 乾的; 乾燥的","examples":["Clean the metal with a soft dry cloth. 用柔軟的乾布把這金屬擦乾淨。","Pat it dry with a soft towel. 用柔軟的毛巾將它輕輕拍幹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that your skin or hair is <b>dry</b>, you mean that it is less oily than, or not as soft as, normal. (皮膚、頭髮) 乾枯的","examples":["Nothing looks worse than dry, cracked lips. 沒有什麼比干裂的嘴唇看上去更糟糕了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the weather or a period of time is <b>dry</b>, there is no rain or there is much less rain than average. 乾旱的","examples":["Exceptionally dry weather over the past year had cut agricultural production. 過去一年裡異常乾旱的氣候降低了農業產量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>dry</b> place or climate is one that gets very little rainfall. 乾旱的; 乾燥的","examples":["It was one of the driest and dustiest places in Africa. 這裡是非洲最乾旱、灰塵最多的地方之一。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a river, lake, or well is <b>dry</b>, it is empty of water, usually because of hot weather and lack of rain. 乾涸的","examples":["The aquifer which had once fed the wells was pronounced dry. 曾經給這些井提供水源的蓄水層已被宣告枯竭。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an oil well is <b>dry</b>, it is no longer producing any oil. (油井) 不再產油的","examples":["To harvest oil and gas profitably from the North Sea, we must focus on the exploitation of small reserves as the big wells run dry. 由於大油井的枯竭，要想從北海有利地獲取石油和天然氣，我們必須集中精力於小儲量油井的開採。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If your mouth or throat is <b>dry</b>, it has little or no saliva in it, and so feels very unpleasant, perhaps because you are tense or ill. (口、咽) 乾的","examples":["His mouth was still dry, he would certainly be glad of a drink. 他的口還是幹，他當然會樂於喝點什麼。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone has <b>dry</b> eyes, there are no tears in their eyes; often used with negatives or in contexts where you are expressing surprise that they are not crying. 無淚的","examples":["There were few dry eyes in the house when I finished. 當我結束時，屋裡幾乎沒有人不掉眼淚的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Dry</b> humour is very amusing, but in a subtle and clever way. 冷麵的 (幽默)","examples":["Though the pressure Fulton is under must be considerable, he has retained his dry humour. 雖然富尓頓承受的壓力一定是相當大的，但他還保持著冷麵幽默。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you describe something such as a book, play, or activity as <b>dry</b>, you mean that it is dull and uninteresting. 枯燥乏味的","examples":["My eyelids were drooping over the dry, academic phrases. 這些枯燥乏味的學術用語讓我的眼皮直向下耷拉。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>Dry</b> sherry or wine does not have a sweet taste. 無甜味的 (酒)","examples":["...a glass of chilled, dry white wine. …一杯冰凍乾白葡萄酒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"乾燥","examples":["...the parched dryness of the air. …空氣的炎熱乾燥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"乾枯","examples":["Dryness of the skin can also be caused by living in centrally heated homes and offices. 皮膚乾燥還會因呆在有中央供暖的居室或辦公室而引起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"乾燥; 乾旱","examples":["He was advised to spend time in the warmth and dryness of Italy. 他被建議在義大利的溫暖和乾燥中過些日子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(口、咽) 幹","examples":["Symptoms included frequent dryness in the mouth. 症狀包括經常口乾。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"冷嘲","examples":["It has a wry dryness you won't recognize. 有一種你聽不出來的諷刺。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>dries</b> or when you <b>dry</b> it, it becomes dry. 使…變幹; 變幹","examples":["Let your hair dry naturally whenever possible. 無論何時儘可能讓你的頭髮自然幹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>dry</b> the dishes after a meal, you wipe the water off the plates, cups, knives, pans, and other things when they have been washed, using a cloth. 擦乾","examples":["Mrs. Madrigal picked up a towel and began drying dishes next to her daughter. 馬德里格夫人拿起一條毛巾，開始擦乾她女兒旁邊的盤子。"]}]}]},"forget":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"忘記，遺忘；忘做；忽略，不再關注；不再打算做，放棄；忘乎所以，舉止不得體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>forget</b> something or <b>forget</b> how to do something, you cannot think of it or think how to do it, although you knew it or knew how to do it in the past. 忘了 (某事物、如何做某事)","examples":["She forgot where she left the car and it took us two days to find it. 她忘了把車停在了哪裡，我們花了兩天時間才找到它。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>forget</b> something or <b>forget</b> to do it, you fail to think about it or fail to remember to do it, for example, because you are thinking about other things. 忘記 (某事物、做某事)","examples":["She never forgets her daddy's birthday. 她從不忘記她爸爸的生日。","She forgot to lock her door one day and two men got in. 她有一天忘了鎖門，結果兩名男子進去了。","When I close my eyes, I forget about everything. 我閉上眼睛就忘記一切。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>forget</b> something that you had intended to bring with you, you do not bring it because you did not think about it at the right time. 忘記帶 (某物)","examples":["Once when we were going to Paris, I forgot my passport. 有一次我們去巴黎時，我忘了帶護照。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>forget</b> something or someone, you deliberately put them out of your mind and do not think about them any more. 忘掉 (某事物、某人)","examples":["I hope you will forget the bad experience you had today. 我希望你會忘掉你今天的這次不愉快經歷。","I found it very easy to forget about Sumner. 我發現要忘掉薩姆納很容易。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Forget it</b>\" in reply to someone as a way of telling them not to worry or bother about something, or as an emphatic way of saying no to a suggestion. 沒關係; 休想","examples":["\"Sorry, Liz. I think I was a bit rude to you.\"—\"Forget it, but don't do it again!\" “對不起，莉茲。我想我剛才對你有點粗魯。” —“沒關係，不過以後別再這樣做了！”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>not forgetting</b> a particular thing or person when you want to include them in something that you have already talked about. 別忘了 (某物或人)","examples":["Leave a message, not forgetting your name and address. 留張條，別忘了留下你的姓名和地址。"]}]}]},"follow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跟著，跟隨；跟蹤；（時間或順序）在……後；循著，沿著（道路等）；沿著……伸延；遵循，聽從；仿效，追隨；理解，明白；可以推斷；注視，密切關注；信奉，信仰；（電影、書等）呈現，描述；從事（行業、職業）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跟隨，追隨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> someone who is going somewhere, you move along behind them because you want to go to the same place. 跟隨","examples":["We followed him up the steps into a large hall. 我們跟他上了臺階，進入一個大廳。","Please follow me, madam. 夫人，請跟我來。","They took him into a small room and I followed. 他們把他帶進一間小屋，我跟了過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> someone who is going somewhere, you move along behind them without their knowledge, in order to catch them or find out where they are going. 跟蹤","examples":["She realized that the Mercedes was following her. 她意識到那輛賓士在跟蹤她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> someone to a place where they have recently gone and where they are now, you go to join them there. 跟隨","examples":["He followed Janice to New York, where she was preparing an exhibition. 他跟隨賈妮絲去了紐約，她正在那兒準備一個展覽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An event, activity, or period of time that <b>follows</b> a particular thing happens or comes after that thing, at a later time. 在…後到來; 接著…發生","examples":["...the rioting and looting that followed the verdict. …判決之後發生的暴亂和搶劫。","Other problems may follow. 其它問題也許會隨之而來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> one thing <b>with</b> another, you do or say the second thing after you have done or said the first thing. 隨後做","examples":["Her first major role was in Martin Scorsese's \"Goodfellas\" and she followed this with a part in Spike Lee's \"Jungle Fever.\" 她首先在馬丁·斯柯席斯的《好傢伙》中演了重要角色，隨後又演了斯派克·李的《叢林熱》。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If it <b>follows</b> that a particular thing is the case, that thing is a logical result of something else being true or being the case. 理所當然","examples":["Just because a bird does not breed one year, it does not follow that it will fail the next. 不能僅僅因為鳥一年沒有繁殖就推斷它下一年也不會繁殖。","If the explanation is right, two things follow. 如果該解釋正確，那麼就有兩種情形。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you refer to the words that <b>follow</b> or <b>followed</b>, you are referring to the words that come next or came next in a piece of writing or speech. 接下來","examples":["What follows is an eye-witness account. 接下來是目擊者的陳述。","There followed a list of places where Hans intended to visit. 接下來是一張漢斯打算參觀的地點列表。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> a path, route, or set of signs, you go somewhere using the path, route, or signs to direct you. 沿著…走","examples":["If they followed the road, they would be certain to reach a village. 如果他們沿著這條路走，一定會抵達一個村莊。","All we had to do was follow the map. 所有我們要做的是按照地圖走。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something such as a path or river <b>follows</b> a particular route or line, it goes along that route or line. 沿著","examples":["Our route follows the Pacific coast through densely populated neighbourhoods. 我們一路沿著太平洋海岸，穿過人口稠密的街區。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> something with your eyes, or if your eyes <b>follow</b> it, you watch it as it moves or you look along its route or course. (視線) 隨…而移動","examples":["Ann's eyes followed a police car as it drove slowly past. 安的眼睛注視著一輛緩緩開過的警車。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Something that <b>follows</b> a particular course of development happens or develops in that way. 按照…方式發展","examples":["His release turned out to follow the pattern set by that of the other six hostages. 他的獲釋方式結果和其他6位人質相同。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> someone in what you do, you do the same thing or job as they did previously. 沿襲","examples":["He followed his father and became a surgeon. 他沿襲了他父親，成了一名外科醫生。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> advice, an instruction, or a recipe, you act or do something in the way that it indicates. 聽從 (建議、指示或藥法)","examples":["Take care to follow the instructions carefully. 注意嚴格遵循說明。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> what someone else has done, you do it too because you think it is a good thing or because you want to copy them. 仿效","examples":["His admiration for the athlete did not extend to the point where he would follow his example in taking drugs. 他對這名運動員的崇拜還不至於到效仿他吸毒的程度。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> something, you take an interest in it and keep informed about what happens. 隨時關注","examples":["...the millions of people who follow football because they genuinely love it. …數百萬人隨時關注足球是因為真正熱愛足球。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> a particular religion or political belief, you have that religion or belief. 信奉 (宗教或政治主張)","examples":["\"Do you follow any particular religion?\"—\"Yes, we're all Hindus.\" “你們信什麼教嗎？” —“信，我們都是印度教教徒。”"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you are able to <b>follow</b> something such as an explanation or the story of a film, you understand it as it continues and develops. 理解","examples":["Can you follow the plot so far? 你到目前能理解這個情節嗎？","I'm sorry, I don't follow. 對不起，我不理解。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Follow up</b> means the same as <b>follow</b>. 隨後做","examples":["The book proved such a success that the authors followed it up with \"The Messianic Legacy.\" 該書獲得瞭如此大的成功，以至作者隨後又出了一本《天主的遺產》。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as follows</b> in writing or speech to introduce something such as a list, description, or an explanation. 如下","examples":["The winners are as follows: E. Walker; R. Foster; R. Gates; A. Mackintosh. 獲勝者如下：E.沃克、R.福斯特、R.蓋茨和A.麥金託什。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>followed by</b> to say what comes after something else in a list or ordered set of things. 由…緊接著","examples":["Potatoes are still the most popular food, followed by white bread. 土豆仍然是最受歡迎的食品，其次為白麵包。"]}]}]},"is":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是（be 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Is</b> is the third person singular of the present tense of . <b>Is</b> is often added to other words and shortened to <b>-'s</b>. (be)的第三人稱單數現在時","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Iceland 冰島","examples":[]}]}]},"happen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發生；使遭遇；碰巧"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<北英格蘭>或許，大概"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>happens</b> occurs or is done without being planned. (偶然地) 發生","examples":["We cannot say for sure what will happen. 我們說不準將會發生些什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>happens</b>, it occurs as a result of a situation or course of action. (作為結果) 發生","examples":["She wondered what would happen if her parents found her. 她不知道如果父母發現了她會怎麼樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something, especially something unpleasant, <b>happens to</b> you, it takes place and affects you. (尤指不愉快的事) 發生 (在某人身上)","examples":["If we had been spotted at that point, I don't know what would have happened to us. 如果那時我們被發現了，我不知道我們會有什麼後果。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>happen</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it by chance. If <b>it</b> <b>happens</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, it occurs by chance. 碰巧","examples":["We happened to discover we had a friend in common. 我們碰巧發現我們有個共同的朋友。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as it happens</b> in order to introduce a statement, especially one that is rather surprising. 碰巧 (尤用以引出令人意外的內容)","examples":["He called Amy to see if she knew where his son was. As it happened, Amy did know. 他打電話給埃米，看她是否知道他兒子在哪兒。碰巧的是，埃米還真知道。"]}]}]},"hear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聽到，聽見；聆聽，傾聽；聽說，得知；審理，聽審；腦際響起；聽明白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>hear</b> a sound, you become aware of it through your ears. 聽見","examples":["She heard no further sounds. 她再也沒有聽見任何響聲。","They heard the protesters shout: \"No more fascism!\" 他們聽見抗議者在高呼：“打倒法西斯主義！”","He doesn't hear very well. 他聽覺不是很好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hear</b> something such as a lecture or a piece of music, you listen to it. 聽","examples":["You can hear commentary on the game at halftime. 你可在中場休息時聽到對比賽的評論。","I don't think you've ever heard Doris talking about her emotional life before. 我想你以前從未聽過多麗絲談論自己的感情生活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a judge or a court of law <b>hears</b> a case, or evidence in a case, they listen to it officially in order to make a decision about it. 聽審","examples":["The jury has heard evidence from defence witnesses. 陪審團聽取了被告方證人的證詞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>hear</b> some news or information about something, you find out about it by someone telling you, or from the radio or television. 聽說","examples":["My mother heard of this school through Leslie. 我母親從萊斯利那裡聽說了這所學校。","He had heard that the trophy had been sold. 他聽說那個獎盃已經被賣掉了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hear</b> <b>from</b> someone, you receive a letter or telephone call from them. 接到 (信或電話)","examples":["Drop us a line, it's always great to hear from you. 給我們寫封信，能收到你的信總是讓人很高興。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>have heard</b> <b>of</b> something or someone, you know about them, but not in great detail. 大致知道","examples":["Many people haven't heard of reflexology. 很多人沒有聽說過反射療法。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have heard</b> something <b>before</b>, you mean that you are not interested in it, or do not believe it, or are not surprised about it, because you already know about it or have experienced it. 已經知道","examples":["Frank shrugs wearily. He has heard it all before. 弗蘭克倦怠地聳聳肩，他早已知道了這一切。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>can't hear</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>think</b>, you are complaining and emphasizing that there is a lot of noise, and that it is disturbing you or preventing you from doing something. 吵得要死","examples":["...those noisy late-night clubs where you can't even hear yourself think. …那些開至深夜能把人吵死的夜總會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>won't hear of</b> someone doing something, you mean that you refuse to let them do it. 不同意","examples":["I've always wanted to be an actor but Dad wouldn't hear of it. 我一直想當演員，但爸爸總是不同意。"]}]}]},"grow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"長大，成長；成活，生長；發展，增加；逐漸變得；產生，形成；栽種，種植；留長，蓄；變長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people, animals, and plants <b>grow</b>, they increase in size and change physically over a period of time. 成長","examples":["We stop growing at maturity. 我們在成熟後就停止成長了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a plant or tree <b>grows</b> in a particular place, it is alive there. 生長","examples":["The station had roses growing at each end of the platform. 車站月臺兩端生長著玫瑰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone's hair <b>grows</b>, it gradually becomes longer. Your nails also <b>grow</b>. (毛髮、指甲等) 逐漸變長","examples":["Then the hair began to grow again and I felt terrific. 接著頭髮又長起來了，我感覺棒極了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>grows</b> mentally, they change and develop in character or attitude. (心理方面的) 成長","examples":["They began to grow as individuals. 他們開始發展獨自的個性。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an amount, feeling, or problem <b>grows</b>, it becomes greater or more intense. (數量) 增加; (情感) 增強; (問題) 變嚴重","examples":["From 2000 to 2002, the number of uninsured grew by almost 4 million. 從2000年到2002年，未參加保險的人數增加了差不多四百萬。","Opposition grew and the government agreed to negotiate. 反對勢力日益強烈，政府同意進行談判。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If one thing <b>grows into</b> another, it develops or changes until it becomes that thing. 發展為","examples":["The boys grew into men. 這些男孩長大成為男人了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something such as an idea or a plan <b>grows out of</b> something else, it develops from it. (觀點或計劃等) 產生於","examples":["The idea for this book grew out of conversations with Philippa Brewster. 這本書的想法產生於與菲莉帕·布魯斯特的談話。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If the economy or a business <b>grows</b>, it increases in wealth, size, or importance. (經濟或企業的) 增長","examples":["The economy continues to grow. 經濟持續增長。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grow</b> a particular type of plant, you put seeds or young plants in the ground and take care of them as they develop. 種植","examples":["Lettuce was grown by the ancient Romans. 萵苣是由古羅馬人種植的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>grows</b> their hair, or <b>grows</b> a beard or moustache, they stop cutting their hair or shaving so that their hair becomes longer. You can also <b>grow</b> your nails. 留 (頭髮、鬍鬚、指甲等)","examples":["I'd better start growing my hair. 我最好開始留頭髮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>grows</b> a business, they take actions that will cause it to increase in wealth, size, or importance. 使增長","examples":["To grow the business, he needs to develop management expertise and innovation across his team. 為了拓展業務,他需要提高其團隊的專業管理技能和創新能力。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>grow</b> to say that someone or something gradually changes until they have a new quality, feeling, or attitude. 變得","examples":["I grew a little afraid of the guy next door. 我變得有點害怕隔壁那傢伙。","He's growing old. 他正在變老。"]}]}]},"learn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"學習，學會；得知，獲悉；背熟，熟記；認識到，（從……）吸取教訓；<舊>教導（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>learn</b> something, you obtain knowledge or a skill through studying or training. 學習","examples":["Their children were going to learn English. 他們的孩子們打算學英語。","He is learning to play the piano. 他正在學彈鋼琴。","It's going to be tough, but these guys learn quickly. 這會很難，但是這些傢伙們學得很快。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>learn</b> of something, you find out about it. 得知","examples":["It was only after his death that she learned of his affair with Betty. 是在他去世之後她才得知他和貝蒂的風流事。","It didn't come as a shock to learn that the fuel and cooling systems are the most common causes of breakdown. 不足為怪的是，燃料和冷卻系統是故障的最常見原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>learn</b> <b>to</b> behave or react in a particular way, they gradually start to behave in that way as a result of a change in attitudes. 學會","examples":["You have to learn to face your problem. 你得學會面對自己的問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>learn</b> <b>from</b> an unpleasant experience, you change the way you behave so that it does not happen again or so that, if it happens again, you can deal with it better. 從…吸取教訓","examples":["I am convinced that he has learned from his mistakes. 我確信他已經從錯誤中吸取了教訓。","I just hope we all learn some lessons from this. 我只是希望我們都能以此為戒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>learn</b> something such as a poem or a role in a play, you study or repeat the words so that you can remember them. 學會","examples":["He learned this song as an inmate at a Texas prison. 他在德克薩斯監獄服刑時學會了這首歌。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"學習","examples":["...a bilingual approach to the learning of English. …英語學習的雙語法。"]}]}]},"know":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"知道；認識到，懂得；熟悉，瞭解；確信，確定；把……看作是；將……稱為；認出，辨認出；能區分；精通，掌握；經歷，體驗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> a fact, a piece of information, or an answer, you have it correctly in your mind. 知道","examples":["I don't know the name of the place. 我不知道那個地方的名稱。","\"People like doing things for nothing.\"—\"I know they do.\" “人們喜歡白忙活。”—“我知道他們是那樣。”","I don't know what happened to her husband. 我不知道她的丈夫出了什麼事。","\"How did he meet your mother?\" —\"I don't know.\" “他是怎麼遇到你母親的？” —“我不知道。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> someone, you are familiar with them because you have met them and talked to them before. 認識","examples":["Gifford was a friend. I'd known him for nine years. 吉福德曾是個朋友。我那時認識他已有9年。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> a language, you have learned it and can understand it. 懂 (某種語言)","examples":["It helps to know French and Creole if you want to understand some of the lyrics. 如果你想明白其中一些歌詞，需要懂法語和克里奧爾語。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> something such as a place, a work of art, or an idea, you have visited it, seen it, read it, or heard about it, and so you are familiar with it. 熟悉","examples":["No matter how well you know this city, it is easy to get lost. 不論你多麼熟悉這座城市，都容易迷路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> <b>how to</b> do something, you have the necessary skills and knowledge to do it. 知道","examples":["The health authorities now know how to deal with the disease. 衛生部門現在知道如何對付這種疾病。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>knows</b> <b>that</b> something is happening when they become aware of it. 意識到","examples":["Then I saw a gun under the hall table so I knew that something was wrong. 當時我看到大廳的桌子下面有一支槍，就意識到出問題了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> something or someone, you recognize them when you see them or hear them. 辨認出","examples":["Would she know you if she saw you on the street? 如果在街上見到你，她會認出你嗎？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is known</b> <b>as</b> a particular name, they are called by that name. 把…稱作","examples":["The disease is more commonly known as Mad Cow Disease. 這種病一般更多地被稱作“瘋牛病”。","...Peter and his wife Antonella (also known as Tony). 彼得和妻子安託妮拉（亦稱託妮）。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a person or thing that has particular qualities, you consider that they have those qualities. 認為","examples":["Lots of people know her as a very kind woman. 很多人都認為她是一個很善良的女人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>know of</b> something, you mean that you have heard about it but you do not necessarily have a lot of information about it. 聽說過","examples":["We know of the incident but have no further details. 我們聽說過那個事件，但不瞭解更多的細節。","The president admitted that he did not know of any rebels having surrendered so far. 總統承認迄今為止他未曾聽說有任何反叛分子投降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> <b>about</b> a subject, you have studied it or taken an interest in it, and understand part or all of it. 瞭解","examples":["Hire someone with experience, someone who knows about real estate. 用一位有經驗並瞭解房地產的人。","She didn't know anything about music. 她對音樂一點都不瞭解。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a thing or system <b>as we know it</b>, you are referring to the form in which it exists now and which is familiar to most people. 如我們所知","examples":["He planned to end the welfare system as we know it. 正如我們所知，他曾計劃廢除這種福利制度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get to know</b> someone, you find out what they are like by spending time with them. (逐漸) 瞭解","examples":["The new neighbours were getting to know each other. 新鄰居們正在逐漸彼此瞭解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People use expressions such as <b>goodness knows</b>, <b>Heaven knows</b>, and <b>God knows</b> when they do not know something and want to suggest that nobody could possibly know it. 天曉得","examples":["\"Who's he?\"—\"God knows.\" “他是誰？”—“天曉得。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>I don't know</b> to indicate that you do not completely agree with something or do not really think that it is true. 我說不準 (表不完全同意)","examples":["\"He should quite simply resign.\"—\"I don't know about that.\" “他只要辭職就行了。”—“我說不準。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I don't know about you</b>\" to indicate that you are going to give your own opinion about something and you want to find out if someone else feels the same. 我不知道你怎麼想","examples":["I don't know about the rest of you, but I'm hungry. 不知道你們怎麼樣，我可是餓了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>I don't know</b> in expressions which indicate criticism of someone's behaviour. For example, if you say that you <b>do not know how</b> someone can do something, you mean that you cannot understand or accept them doing it. 我真想像不出","examples":["I don't know how he could do this to his own daughter. 我真想像不出他怎麼能這樣對待自己的女兒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you are <b>in the know</b> about something, especially something that is not known about or understood by many people, you have information about it. 瞭解內幕","examples":["It was gratifying to be in the know about important people. 瞭解重要人物的內幕令人滿足。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can say \"<b>You don't know</b>\" in order to emphasize how strongly you feel about the remark you are going to make. 你想像不出","examples":["You don't know how good it is to speak to somebody from home. 你不知道跟家裡來的人說說話有多好！"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>I know</b>\" to show that you agree with what has just been said. 我知道 (表示贊同)","examples":["\"This country is so awful.\"—\"I know, I know.\" “這個國家真糟糕。”—“我知道，我知道。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>you know what I mean</b> and <b>if you know what I mean</b> to suggest that the person listening to you understands what you are trying to say, and so you do not have to explain any more. 你懂我的意思","examples":["None of us stayed long. I mean, the atmosphere wasn't – well, you know what I mean. 我們都沒久留。我是說，氣氛不是–嗯，你懂我的意思。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>You never know</b>\" or \"<b>One never knows</b>\" to indicate that it is not definite or certain what will happen in the future, and to suggest that there is some hope that things will turn out well. (指有希望向好的方向發展) 很難說; 難以預料","examples":["You never know, I might get lucky. 很難說，我也許會走運。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say \"<b>Not that I know of</b>\" when someone has asked you whether or not something is true and you think the answer is \"no\" but you cannot be sure because you do not know all the facts. 據我所知並非如此","examples":["\"Is he married?\"—\"Not that I know of.\" “他結婚了嗎？”—“據我所知沒有。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>you know</b> to emphasize or to draw attention to what you are saying. 你知道","examples":["The conditions in there are awful, you know. 你知道，那裡的條件非常糟糕。"]}]}]},"come":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"來；來到，到達；來做，來取；同行，同去；行進（一定距離）來；趕走（某人）；變成，成為；達到，進入（某種狀態或境地）；（事件）發生，（時間）到來；<非正式>（提及的時間）到來；（如何）發生，出現；備有，可提供；達到（某一點或水準）；（經過時間的流逝）開始認為；想起，想到；談論，談到；位於，處於；（信件或訊息）被收到；由……繼承，歸……所有；（案件）提交……審理；總共，共計；出身於；由……引起；（性質）體現出來"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用以鼓勵或安慰）好了，得啦"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<俚>精液，精子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or thing <b>comes</b> to a particular place, especially to a place where you are, they move there. 來 (某地)","examples":["Two police officers came into the hall. 兩位警官來到大廳裡。","Come here, Tom. 來這兒，湯姆。","We heard the train coming. 我們聽見火車來了。","The impact blew out some of the windows and the sea came rushing in. 衝擊力擊碎了一些窗戶，海水衝了進來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>come to</b> a place, you reach it. 到達","examples":["He came to a door that led into a passageway. 他來到一扇通往走廊的門前。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>comes up</b> <b>to</b> a particular point or <b>down</b> <b>to</b> it, it is tall enough, deep enough, or long enough to reach that point. 達到","examples":["The water came up to my chest. 水漫到了我的胸部。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>comes apart</b> or <b>comes to pieces</b>, it breaks into pieces. If something <b>comes off</b> or <b>comes away</b>, it becomes detached from something else. 破碎; 脫離","examples":["The lid won't come off. 蓋子不會脫掉。","The pistol came to pieces, easily and quickly. 手槍輕易地就破碎了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a particular event or time <b>comes</b>, it arrives or happens. 來臨; 發生","examples":["The announcement came after a meeting at the White House. 通告是在白宮的一次會議後釋出的。","There will come a time when they will have to negotiate. 他們終將會進行談判的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a thought, idea, or memory <b>comes to</b> you, you suddenly think of it or remember it. (想法、主意或記憶等) 突然出現","examples":["He was about to shut the door when an idea came to him. 他正準備關門時，突然想起了一個主意。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If money or property is going to <b>come to</b> you, you are going to inherit or receive it. (錢財) 降臨 (在某人身上)","examples":["He did have retirement money coming to him when the factory shut down. 工廠倒閉時，他的確領到了退休金。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a case <b>comes before</b> a court or tribunal or <b>comes to</b> court, it is presented there so that the court or tribunal can examine it. (案子) 被提交到 (法庭)","examples":["The membership application came before the committee in September. 會員資格申請9月呈交給了委員會。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something <b>comes to</b> a particular number or amount, it adds up to it. 合計達","examples":["Lunch came to $80. 午餐合計達80美元。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone or something <b>comes from</b> a particular place or thing, that place or thing is their origin, source, or starting point. 來自","examples":["Nearly half the students come from overseas. 幾乎一半學生來自海外。","Chocolate comes from the cacao tree. 巧克力來自可可樹。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Something that <b>comes from</b> something else or <b>comes of</b> it is the result of it. 源自","examples":["There is a feeling of power that comes from driving fast. 開快車可以產生力量感。","Some good might come of all this gloomy business. 某種好的結果也許會從這種慘淡的經營中產生。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If a type of thing <b>comes</b> <b>in</b> a particular range of colours, forms, styles, or sizes, it can have any of those colours, forms, styles, or sizes. (以某些顏色、形式、樣式、尺碼) 出現","examples":["Bikes come in all shapes and sizes. 腳踏車有各種不同的形狀和大小。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"The next subject in a discussion that you <b>come to</b> is the one that you talk about next. 談到","examples":["Finally, I come to the subject of genetic engineering. 最後，我來談基因工程。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>comes</b> <b>to</b> do something, they move to the place where someone else is in order to do it, and they do it. Someone can also <b>come</b> do something and <b>come and</b> do something. However, you always say that someone <b>came and</b> did something. 來 (做某事)","examples":["Eleanor had come to see her. 埃莉諾是來看她的。","I want you to come visit me. 我希望你來看我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>comes</b> <b>to</b> do something, they do it at the end of a long process or period of time. 達到 (做某事的境界)","examples":["She said it so many times that she came to believe it. 她說了如此多遍以致於最後她都相信了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can ask how something <b>came</b> <b>to</b> happen when you want to know what caused it to happen or made it possible. 達到 (做某事的地步)","examples":["How did you come to meet him? 你怎麼會遇見他的？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>comes</b> first, next, or last, they are first, next, or last in a series, list, or competition. 排在 (第一、下一個或最後)","examples":["The two countries have been unable to agree which step should come next. 這兩個國家無法就下一步該怎麼走達成一致。","The alphabet might be more rational if all the vowels came first. 要是所有的母音都排在前面，字母表也許會更合理些。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"來臨; 發生","examples":["Most of my patients welcome the coming of summer. 我的大多數病人都喜歡夏天的來臨。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>come</b> in expressions such as <b>come to an end</b> or <b>come into operation</b> to indicate that someone or something enters or reaches a particular state or situation. 達到 (某種狀態或情形)","examples":["The summer came to an end. 夏天結束了。","Their worst fears may be coming true. 他們最恐懼的事也許會變成現實。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>come</b> before a date, time, or event to mean when it arrives. For example, you can say <b>come spring</b> to mean \"when the spring arrives.\" 到來","examples":["Come the election on the 20th of May, we will have to decide. 5月20日選舉到來時，我們就不得不做出決定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use the expression <b>when it comes down to it</b> or <b>when you come down to it</b> for emphasis, when you are giving a general statement or conclusion. 歸結起來","examples":["When you come down to it, however, the basic problems of life have not changed. 然而，歸結起來，生活的基本問題並未改變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use the expression <b>come to think of it</b> to indicate that you have suddenly realized something, often something obvious. 突然意識到","examples":["He was his distant relative, as was everyone else on the island, come to think of it. 我突然意識到, 他像島上的其他人一樣是他的遠親."]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you refer to a time or an event <b>to come</b> or one that is still <b>to come</b>, you are referring to a future time or event. 未來的","examples":["I hope in years to come he will reflect on his decision. 我希望在未來的幾年裡他會反思他的決定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use expressions like <b>I know where you're coming from</b> or <b>you can see where she's coming from</b> to say that you understand someone's attitude or point of view. 態度; 觀點","examples":["To understand why they are doing it, it is necessary to know where they are coming from. 要理解他們為什麼這樣做，有必要知道他們的想法。"]}]}]},"listen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聽，傾聽；聽從，聽信；努力聽，留神地聽（listen for/listen out for）；<非正式>聽著"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聽，傾聽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>listen</b> <b>to</b> someone who is talking or <b>to</b> a sound, you give your attention to them or it. 聽","examples":["He spent his time listening to the radio. 他把時間花在了聽收音機上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>listen</b> <b>for</b> a sound, you keep alert and are ready to hear it if it occurs. 留心聽","examples":["We listen for footsteps approaching. 我們側耳傾聽腳步聲靠近。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>listen</b> <b>to</b> someone, you do what they advise you to do, or you believe them. 聽從","examples":["Anne, you need to listen to me this time. 安妮，這次你要聽我的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聽者","examples":["One or two listeners had fallen asleep while the president was speaking. 總統講話時，有一兩個聽眾睡著了。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>listen</b> when you want someone to pay attention to you because you are going to say something important. 聽我說","examples":["Listen, I finish at one. 聽著，我一點鐘結束。"]}]}]},"lay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"安放，放置；鋪放，鋪設；下（蛋），產（卵）；<英>擺放（餐具）；提出，提交；使處於特定狀態；制定計劃或設圈套；下賭注；安排，決定（戲劇、小說情節）的場景；阻止（某物）從地面揚起；安葬（某人）；使倒伏，擊倒；（擺好木、柴或煤）生火；沿（特定航線）航行；修整，編整（樹籬）；與（某人）性交"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩，民歌；（某物的）位置，方向；地勢，地貌；（捻繩索時每股的）捻向；產卵，產卵期；<非正式>性夥伴"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外行的，非專業的；平信徒的，在俗的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"躺；平放；存在，在於（lie 的過去式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lay</b> something somewhere, you put it there in a careful, gentle, or neat way. 放置","examples":["Lay a sheet of newspaper on the floor. 把一張報紙放在地板上。","Mothers routinely lay babies on their backs to sleep. 母親們通常會把嬰兒平躺著放下睡覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lay</b> something such as carpets, cables, or foundations, you put them into their permanent position. 鋪設","examples":["A man came to lay the carpet. 一名男子來鋪地毯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a female bird <b>lays</b>, or <b>lays</b> an egg, it produces an egg by pushing it out of its body. 下 (蛋)","examples":["My canary has laid an egg. 我的金絲雀下了一個蛋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Lay</b> is used with some nouns to talk about making official preparations for something. For example, if you <b>lay the basis</b> for something or <b>lay plans</b> for it, you prepare it carefully. 奠定 (基礎); 制定 (規劃)","examples":["Diplomats meeting in Chile have laid the groundwork for far-reaching environmental regulations. 在智利會晤的外交官們已經為長遠的環境保護規則奠定了基礎。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Lay</b> is used with some nouns in expressions about accusing or blaming someone. For example, if you <b>lay the blame</b> for a mistake on someone, you say it is their fault, or if the police <b>lay charges</b> against someone, they officially accuse that person of a crime. 歸罪於","examples":["She refused to lay the blame on any one party. 她拒絕歸罪於任何一方。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>lay</b> the table or <b>lay</b> the places at a table, you arrange the knives, forks, and other things that people need on the table before a meal. 擺放 (餐具)","examples":["The butler always laid the table. 餐具總是由管家來擺放。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>lay</b> to describe people who are involved with a Christian church but are not members of the clergy or are not monks or nuns. 世俗的","examples":["Edwards is a Methodist lay preacher and social worker. 愛德華茲是一位衛理公會的世俗佈道者和社工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>lay</b> to describe people who are not experts or professionals in a particular subject or activity. 非專業的","examples":["It is difficult for a lay person to gain access to medical libraries. 非專業人員很難進入醫學圖書館。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a ballad or short narrative poem, esp one intended to be sung (能唱的)短敘事詩","examples":[]}]}]},"give":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給，交給；贈送，贈與，送給；提供，供給；捐贈；支付，付款；將（時間、精力等）用於；舉辦，舉行；表演，公開進行；允許；使產生（某種感覺）；使擁有（某一特性）；生產，引起；給（某人）打（電話）；告訴，說出，說明；給……評定（等級）；（把藥等）注入，服入；看待，承認；做（動作）；傳染；使受懲罰，讓（某人）做；作出（決定或判決）；預計將持續（時間）；伸長，彎曲，斷裂；讓步，妥協；表示一種可能的情況或狀態"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"伸展性，彈性；適應（或順應）能力，靈活性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>give</b> with nouns that refer to physical actions. The whole expression refers to the performing of the action. For example, <b>She gave a smile</b> means almost the same as \"She smiled.\" 與表示身體動作的名詞連用，表示做這一動作","examples":["She stretched her arms out and gave a great yawn. 她伸開手臂，打了個大呵欠。","He gave her a fond smile. 他充滿柔情地朝她微微一笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>give</b> to say that a person does something for another person. For example, if you <b>give</b> someone a lift, you take them somewhere in your car. 為…做…","examples":["I gave her a lift back to her house. 我讓她搭我的車回家。","He was given mouth-to-mouth resuscitation. 對他進行了口對口的人工呼吸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>give</b> with nouns that refer to information, opinions, or greetings to indicate that something is communicated. For example, if you <b>give</b> someone some news, you tell it to them. 告知","examples":["He gave no details. 他沒有提供任何細節。","Would you like to give me your name? 能告訴我你的名字嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>give</b> to say how long you think something will last or how much you think something will be. 預計","examples":["A recent poll gave Campbell a 68 percent support rating. 最近的一次民意調查預計坎貝爾的支援率為68%。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"People use <b>give</b> in expressions such as <b>I don't give a damn</b> to show that they do not care about something. 用於(I don't give a damn)等表達中表示“毫不在乎”","examples":["They don't give a damn about the country. 他們一點都不在乎這個國家。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something <b>gives</b> you a particular idea or impression, it causes you to have that idea or impression. 使產生 (某種想法或印象)","examples":["They gave me the impression that they were doing exactly what they wanted in life. 他們給我的印象是，他們正在做他們一生中想做的事情。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone or something <b>gives</b> you a particular physical or emotional feeling, it makes you experience it. 使產生 (某種情緒或感受)","examples":["He gave me a shock. 他讓我大吃一驚。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> a performance or speech, you perform or speak in public. 作 (演出或演講)","examples":["Kotto gives a stupendous performance. 科託作了一場令人驚歎的演出。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> something thought or attention, you think about it, concentrate on it, or deal with it. 予以 (考慮或關注)","examples":["I've been giving it some thought. 我一直在考慮這個問題。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> a party or other social event, you organize it. 舉行 (聚會或社交活動等)","examples":["That evening, I gave a dinner party for a few close friends. 那天晚上，我設宴招待了幾位密友。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone something that you own or have bought, you provide them with it, so that they have it or can use it. 提供","examples":["They gave us T-shirts and stickers. 他們給我們提供了T恤衫和貼上標籤。","He gave money to the World Health Organization to help defeat smallpox. 他給世界衛生組織提供了資金以幫助消滅天花。","Americans are still giving to charity despite hard times. 儘管時世艱難，美國人依然在捐助慈善事業。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone something that you are holding or that is near you, you pass it to them, so that they are then holding it. 遞給","examples":["Give me that pencil. 請把那支鉛筆遞給我。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"To <b>give</b> someone or something a particular power or right means to allow them to have it. 賦予 (權力或權利)","examples":["The new law would give the president the power to appoint the central bank's chairman. 新法律將賦予總統任命中央銀行行長的權力。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You say that you <b>are given</b> <b>to</b> understand or believe that something is the case when you do not want to say how you found out about it, or who told you. 獲悉","examples":["We were given to understand that he was ill. 我們獲悉他生病了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>gives</b>, it collapses or breaks under pressure. 坍塌; 斷裂","examples":["My knees gave under me. 我的膝蓋發軟了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>give me</b> to say that you would rather have one thing than another, especially when you have just mentioned the thing that you do not want. 我寧願要","examples":["\"I hate Sundays,\" he said. \"They're endless. Give me a Saturday night any day.\" “我討厭星期日，”他說。“星期日沒完沒了的。我寧願要星期六晚上，哪天都行。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something requires <b>give-and-take</b>, you mean that people must compromise or cooperate for it to be successful. 互諒互讓","examples":["...a happy relationship where there's a lot of give-and-take. …在很多事情上互諒互讓的美滿情愛關係。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Give or take</b> is used to indicate that an amount is approximate. For example, if you say that something is fifty years old, <b>give or take</b> a few years, you mean that it is approximately fifty years old. 相差不到…","examples":["They grow to a height of 12 in. – give or take a couple of inches. 它們能長到12英寸高–誤差不超過2英寸。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an audience is asked to <b>give it up for</b> a performer, they are being asked to applaud. 為…鼓掌","examples":["Ladies and gentlemen, give it up for Fred Durst. 女士們先生們，為弗雷德·德斯特鼓掌吧。"]}]}]},"get":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"收到，接到；獲得，得到；掙得，賺得；去取，去帶來；買；得（病），患（病）；遭受……之苦；變成，變得；形成（想法、感覺）；促使，使得；使開始，使進展；得以做，有機會做；到達；達到（某一點或某一階段）；移動，去；理解，明白；有，經歷；做（飯）；搭乘，乘坐；接（電話），應（門鈴）；與……通電話；捕獲，抓獲；襲擊，打傷，殺死；<非正式>使惱火，使難過；使困惑，難住；接收（電視廣播訊號）；受到（懲罰）；<非正式>注意到"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>（說話人）討厭（或鄙夷）的人；<舊>（動物的）後代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>get</b> with adjectives to mean \"become.\" For example, if someone <b>gets cold</b>, they become cold, and if they <b>get angry</b>, they become angry. (與形容詞連用) 變得","examples":["The boys were getting bored. 男孩子們漸漸變得厭煩起來。","From here on, it can only get better. 從現在開始，情況只會變得更好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Get</b> is used with expressions referring to states or situations. For example, to <b>get into trouble</b> means to start being in trouble. 處於","examples":["Half the pleasure of an evening out is getting ready. 晚上外出的樂趣一半在於出門前的準備。","Perhaps I shouldn't say that – I might get into trouble. 也許我不該說那些–我可能會遇到麻煩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When <b>it</b> <b>gets</b> <b>to be</b> a particular time, it is that time. If <b>it</b> <b>is getting</b> <b>toward</b> a particular time, it is approaching that time. 到/接近 (…時間)","examples":["It got to be after 1 a.m. and I was exhausted. 已到了凌晨一點多，我已筋疲力盡了。","It was getting toward evening when we got back. 我們回來時已將近傍晚。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>get</b> someone or something into a particular state or situation means to cause them to be in it. 使…處於","examples":["I don't know if I can get it clean. 我不知道我能否把它清理乾淨。","Brian will get them out of trouble. 布賴恩會使他們擺脫困境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you cause them to do it by asking, persuading, or telling them to do it. 使 (某人做某事)","examples":["...a long campaign to get U.S. politicians to take the AIDS epidemic more seriously. …一項長期運動，旨在使美國政界人士更嚴肅地對待艾滋病流行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> something done, you cause it to be done. 使…做好","examples":["I might benefit from getting my teeth fixed. 把牙齒補好可能對我有好處。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>get</b> something or someone into a place or position means to cause them to move there. 使移動到","examples":["Mack got his wallet out. 麥克掏出了錢包。","Go and get your coat on. 去把你的外套穿上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> <b>to</b> do something, you eventually or gradually reach a stage at which you do it. 最終或逐步達到 (某個階段)","examples":["No one could figure out how he got to be so wealthy. 沒人能弄清楚他是怎樣變得如此富有的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> <b>to</b> do something, you manage to do it or have the opportunity to do it. 設法做; 有機會做","examples":["How do these people get to be the bosses of major companies? 這些人是怎麼得以成為大公司的老總的？","Do you get to see him often? 你能經常見到他嗎？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>get</b> in expressions like <b>get moving</b>, <b>get going</b>, and <b>get working</b> when you want to tell people to begin moving, going, or working quickly. 迅速開始做","examples":["I aim to be at the lake before dawn, so let's get moving. 我打算天亮之前到湖邊，所以我們馬上就動身吧。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>get</b> to talk about the progress that you are making. For example, if you say that you <b>are</b> <b>getting somewhere</b>, you mean that you are making progress, and if you say that something <b>won't get</b> you <b>anywhere</b>, you mean it will not help you to progress at all. 取得進展","examples":["Radical factions say the talks are getting nowhere and they want to withdraw. 激進派們說會談沒有什麼進展，他們要退出。","This bout of self-pity was getting me nowhere. 這一陣自哀自憐對我不會有什麼好處。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> something that you want or need, you obtain it. 得到","examples":["I got a job at the sawmill. 我在鋸木廠找到了一份工作。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> something, you receive it or are given it. 收到","examples":["I'm getting a bike for my birthday. 我過生日時會得到一輛腳踏車。","He gets a lot of letters from women. 他收到很多女人的來信。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> someone or something, you go and bring them to a particular place. 去拿來","examples":["I came down this morning to get the newspaper. 我今天上午下來拿了報紙。","Go and get me a large brandy. 去給我拿一大杯白蘭地來。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a particular result, you obtain it from some action that you take, or from a calculation or experiment. 得出","examples":["What do you get if you multiply six by nine? 6乘9得幾？"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a particular price <b>for</b> something that you sell, you obtain that amount of money by selling it. 賣得","examples":["He can't get a good price for his crops. 他不能把莊稼賣個好價錢。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> the time or opportunity to do something, you have the time or opportunity to do it. 有 (做…的時間或機會)","examples":["You get time to think in prison. 你在獄中有時間思考。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> an idea, impression, or feeling, you begin to have that idea, impression, or feeling as you learn or understand more about something. 開始有 (想法、印象或感受)","examples":["I get the feeling that you're an honest man. 我開始覺得你是個誠實的男人了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a feeling or benefit from an activity or experience, the activity or experience gives you that feeling or benefit. 獲得 (感受或好處)","examples":["Charles got a shock when he saw him. 查爾斯看到他時大吃一驚。","She gets enormous pleasure out of working freelance. 她從事自由職業感受到極大的樂趣。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a look, view, or glimpse of something, you manage to see it. 看到","examples":["Young men climbed on buses and fences to get a better view. 年輕人紛紛爬上公共汽車頂和圍牆想看得更清楚些。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a joke or <b>get</b> the point of something that is said, you understand it. 理解","examples":["Did you get that joke, Ann? I'll explain later. 安，你聽懂了那個笑話嗎？我以後會解釋的。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> an illness or disease, you become ill with it. 患 (病)","examples":["When I was five I got measles. 我5歲時患過麻疹。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"When you <b>get</b> a train, bus, plane, or boat, you leave a place on a particular train, bus, plane, or boat. 乘坐","examples":["It'll be a dollar to get the bus. 乘坐公共汽車要一美元。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>get</b> somewhere means to move there. 移動","examples":["I got off the bed and opened the door. 我下床並開了門。","How can I get past her without her seeing me? 我怎樣才能從她旁邊經過而不讓她看見我呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>get</b> to a place, you arrive there. 到達","examples":["Generally I get to work at 9:30 a.m. 我通常上午9:30上班。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> <b>to</b> a particular stage in your life or in something you are doing, you reach that stage. 到達 (人生等的某一階段)","examples":["We haven't got to the stage of a full-scale military conflict. 我們還沒有到達全面軍事衝突的階段。","It got to the point where I was so ill I was waiting to die. 我已病入膏肓，到了等死的階段。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something that has continued for some time <b>gets to</b> you, it starts causing you to suffer. 使痛苦","examples":["That's the first time I lost my cool in 20 years in this job. This whole thing's getting to me. 那是我幹這份工作20年來頭一次失去冷靜。這整件事讓我痛苦不堪。"]}]},{"pos":"aux.","pos_name":"助動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Get</b> is often used in place of \"be\" as an auxiliary verb to form passives. 常用作助動詞，替代(be)構成被動語態","examples":["A pane of glass got broken. 一塊玻璃被打碎了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say that something is, for example, <b>as good as you can get</b> to mean that it is as good as it is possible for that thing to be. …極了","examples":["Consort has a population of 714 and is about as rural and isolated as you can get. 康索特有居民714人，地處農村，極其偏遠。","...the diet that is as near to perfect as you can get it. …近乎完美的飲食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say <b>you can't get away from</b> something or <b>there is no getting away from</b> something, you are emphasizing that it is true, even though people might prefer it not to be true. 無法否認","examples":["There is no getting away from the fact that he is on the left of the party. 無法否認他是該黨左派的事實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get away from it all</b>, you have a holiday in a place that is very different from where you normally live and work. 外出度假以換換環境","examples":["...the ravishing island of Ischia, where rich Italians get away from it all. …令人陶醉的伊斯基亞島，有錢義大利人的消遣度假之地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>you get</b> instead of \"there is\" or \"there are\" to say that something exists, happens, or can be experienced. 有","examples":["That's where you get some differences of opinion. 那是你們的觀點分歧所在。"]}]}]},"marry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"結婚，嫁，娶；為……主持婚禮；把……嫁給，為……娶親；使結合在一起；拼接纜繩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two people <b>get married</b> or <b>marry</b>, they legally become husband and wife in a special ceremony. <b>Get married</b> is less formal and more commonly used than <b>marry</b>. 結婚","examples":["I thought he would change after we got married. 我原以為他會在我們結婚後改變的。","They married a month after they met. 他們在認識一個月後就結婚了。","He wants to marry her. 他想娶她。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a priest or official <b>marries</b> two people, he or she conducts the ceremony in which the two people legally become husband and wife. 為…主持婚禮","examples":["The minister has agreed to marry us in the college chapel. 這位牧師已經同意在學校的小教堂為我們主持婚禮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to unite closely or intimately 緊密聯合","examples":[]}]}]},"let":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"允許，准許，同意；使透過；任由，隨；（用於提出建議或表示贊同）讓我們；（提出幫助時說）讓，由；（用於引出命令）要；但願；（用於引出要說的話）讓我（們）來；（計算時說）假設，設；（表示猶豫或思考）讓我想想；（表示認為某人應該做某事）讓；出租（房屋或土地）；（將工程）承包給某一競標者； <古> 妨礙，阻礙"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擦網球，觸網重發；<英>出租，租借；待租房，可出租房產；障礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> something happen, you allow it to happen without doing anything to stop or prevent it. 任由","examples":["People said we were interfering with nature, and that we should just let the animals die. 人們說我們在干涉大自然，還說我們應該任由那些動物去死。","I can't let myself be distracted by those things. 我不能任由自己被那些東西分散注意力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> someone do something, you give them your permission to do it. 允許","examples":["I love sweets but Mum doesn't let me have them very often. 我愛吃糖果，但是媽媽不允許我常吃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> someone into, out of, or through a place, you allow them to enter, leave, or go through it, for example, by opening a door or making room for them. 允許 (進入、離開、透過等)","examples":["I had to let them into the building because they had lost their keys. 我不得不允許他們進樓，因為他們丟了鑰匙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>let me</b> when you are introducing something you want to say. 讓我 (引出要說的內容)","examples":["Let me tell you what I saw last night. 讓我告訴你昨晚我見到的事。","Let me explain why. 讓我來解釋為什麼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>let me</b> when you are offering politely to do something. 讓我 (表示禮貌地提出幫忙)","examples":["Let me take your coat. 讓我幫您拿外套吧。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say <b>let's</b> or, in more formal English, <b>let us</b>, to direct the attention of the people you are talking to toward the subject that you want to consider next. 讓我們 (引起人們對將談論的事物的注意)","examples":["Let us look at these views in more detail. 讓我們更詳細地看待這些觀點。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You say <b>let's</b> or, in formal English, <b>let us</b>, when you are making a suggestion that involves both you and the person you are talking to, or when you are agreeing to a suggestion of this kind. 讓我們 (表示提議或同意)","examples":["I'm bored. Let's go home. 我無聊著呢。讓我們回家吧。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Someone in authority, such as a teacher, can use <b>let's</b> or, in more formal English, <b>let us</b>, in order to give a polite instruction to another person or group of people. 我們…吧 (表示禮貌地下達指令)","examples":["Let's have some quiet, please. 我們安靜點吧。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>let</b> when you are saying what you think someone should do, usually when they are behaving in a way that you think is unreasonable or wrong. 讓 (表示批評和要求)","examples":["Let him get his own cup of tea. 讓他自己去倒茶。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> your house or land <b>to</b> someone, you allow them to use it in exchange for money that they pay you regularly. 出租","examples":["She let rooms to university students. 她曾把房間租給大學生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act of letting property or accommodation 出租","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Let out</b> means the same as . 同let","examples":["I couldn't sell the apartment, so I let it out. 我不能把公寓賣掉，因此把它出租了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Let alone</b> is used after a statement, usually a negative one, to indicate that the statement is even more true of the person, thing, or situation that you are going to mention next. 更不用說","examples":["It is incredible that the 12-year-old managed to even reach the pedals, let alone drive the car. 這個12歲的小孩能夠得著踏板都令人難以置信，更不用說開汽車了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>let go</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you stop holding them. 放開某人/某物","examples":["She let go of Mona's hand and took a sip of her drink. 她放開莫娜的手，輕輕呷了一口她的飲料。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> someone or something <b>go</b>, you allow them to leave or escape. 放走某人","examples":["They held him for three hours and they let him go. 他們扣押了他3個小時才放走他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone leaves a job, either because they are told to or because they want to, the employer sometimes says that they are <b>letting</b> that person <b>go</b>. 解僱某人","examples":["I've assured him I have no plans to let him go. 我已經向他保證我不打算解僱他。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you did not know what you were <b>letting</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>in for</b> when you decided to do something, you mean you did not realize how difficult, unpleasant, or expensive it was going to be. 給自己惹上 (麻煩)","examples":["He got the impression that Miss Hawes had no idea of what she was letting herself in for. 他感覺霍伊斯小姐並不知道她給自己惹了多大的麻煩。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> someone <b>know</b> something, you tell them about it or make sure that they know about it. 讓某人知道","examples":["They want to let them know that they are safe. 他們想讓他們知道，他們很安全。"]}]}]},"live":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"生存，活著；生活在；居住；生長，棲息；（以某種方式）生活，過日子；為……而生活；以……為生；繼續存在，銘記；過精彩的生活，享受生活；<非正式>（物）擱置在（某處）；恪守（規則、信念、理想等）；<古>（船）逃過劫難，未沉沒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"活的，有生命的；含乳酸菌的；現場直播的，實況轉播的；現場演出的；（電線或裝置等）通電的，帶電的；仍可爆炸的，隨時可用的；（火、煤炭或火柴）燃燒的，可燃的；（火柴）未用過的；當前所關心的，時下重大的；（球類運動中的球）處於比賽狀態的；（電子連結）有效的；（機器中輪或軸）轉動的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"現場直播地，實況轉播地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>lives</b> in a particular place or with a particular person, their home is in that place or with that person. 居住","examples":["She has lived here for 10 years. 她在這裡住了10年了。","Where do you live? 你住在哪裡？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>lives for</b> a particular thing, you mean that it is the most important thing in their life. (為…而) 活","examples":["He lived for his work. 他為了工作而活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>live by</b> doing a particular activity, they get the money, food, or clothing they need by doing that activity. 以…為生","examples":["...the last indigenous people to live by hunting. …最後一個以打獵為生的土著民族。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>lives</b> in particular circumstances or that they <b>live</b> a particular kind of life, you mean that they are in those circumstances or that they have that kind of life. 生活","examples":["We lived quite grandly. 我們生活得相當快樂。","Compared to people living only a few generations ago, we have greater opportunities to have a good time. 與生活在僅僅幾代之前的人相比，我們有更大的過得快樂的機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>live</b> means to be alive. If someone <b>lives</b> <b>to</b> a particular age, they stay alive until they are that age. 活著","examples":["He's got a terrible disease and will not live long. 他得了一種重病，活不長了。","He lived to be 103. 他活到了103歲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>live it up</b>, you have a very enjoyable and exciting time, for example by going to lots of parties or going out drinking with friends. 盡情玩樂","examples":["There is no reason why you couldn't live it up once in a while. 沒有理由不讓你偶爾盡情玩樂一下的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Live</b> animals or plants are alive, rather than being dead or artificial. 活的","examples":["...a protest against the company's tests on live animals. …反對該公司對活的動物進行實驗的抗議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>live</b> television or radio programme is one in which an event or performance is broadcast at exactly the same time as it happens, rather than being recorded first. 現場直播的","examples":["Murray was a guest on a live radio show. 默裡曾是一個無線電直播節目的嘉賓。","They watch all the live matches. 他們觀看所有現場直播的比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>live</b> performance is given in front of an audience, rather than being recorded and then broadcast or shown in a film. 現場表演的","examples":["The Rainbow has not hosted live music since the end of 1981. 彩虹樂隊自1981年底以來還沒有舉辦過現場音樂會。","A live audience will pose the questions. 一位現場觀眾將會提些問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>live</b> wire or piece of electrical equipment is directly connected to a source of electricity. 帶電的","examples":["The plug broke, exposing live wires. 插頭壞了，露出帶電的電線。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Live</b> bullets are made of metal, rather than rubber or plastic, and are intended to kill people rather than injure them. 實 (彈) 的","examples":["They trained in the jungle using live ammunition. 他們在叢林裡使用真槍實彈進行訓練。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Live</b> is also an adverb. 現場直播地","examples":["It was broadcast live in 50 countries. 它在50個國家進行了現場直播。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Live</b> is also an adverb. 現場表演地","examples":["Kat Bjelland has been playing live with her new band. 凱特·本傑拉德與她的新樂團一直在進行現場表演。"]}]}]},"die":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"死亡；消失，滅亡；停止運轉；渴望；<古>達到性高潮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"骰子；金屬模具，壓模"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people, animals, and plants <b>die</b>, they stop living. 死亡","examples":["A year later my dog died. 1年後，我的狗死了。","Sadly, both he and my mother died of cancer. 令人悲傷的是，他和我母親都死於癌症。","I would die a very happy person if I could stay in music my whole life. 如果我這一生都能生活在音樂之中，就是死，我也會死得快樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>are dying for</b> something or <b>are dying</b> <b>to</b> do something to emphasize that you very much want to have it or do it. 渴望","examples":["I'm dying for a breath of fresh air. 我真想呼吸點新鮮空氣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>die</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I almost died</b>\" or \"<b>I'd die if anything happened</b>\" where you are emphasizing your feelings about a situation, for example, to say that it is very shocking, upsetting, embarrassing, or amusing. (差點) 死去","examples":["I nearly died when I read what she'd written about me. 看到她對我的描述，我差點沒死。","I nearly died of shame. 我羞愧得要命。","I thought I'd die laughing. 我以為我要笑死了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a machine or device <b>dies</b>, it stops completely, especially after a period of working more and more slowly or inefficiently. 停止運轉","examples":["Then suddenly, the engine coughed, spluttered, and died. 突然，發動機發出喀喀聲、噼啪聲，然後就熄火了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>are dying of</b> thirst, hunger, boredom, or curiosity to emphasize that you are very thirsty, hungry, bored, or curious. (飢渴、厭倦、好奇得) 要命","examples":["Order me a soda, I'm dying of thirst. 給我要杯汽水，我快渴死了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>to die for</b>, you mean that you want it or like it very much. 令人非常想要; 令人非常喜歡","examples":["It may be that your property has a stunning view, or perhaps it has a kitchen or bathroom to die for. 也許是你的房子有極漂亮的景色，也許它的廚房和衛生間太令人嚮往。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that habits or attitudes <b>die hard</b>, you mean that they take a very long time to disappear or change, so that it may not be possible to get rid of them completely. (習慣、觀念等) 難以消除; 難以改變","examples":["Old habits die hard. 舊習難改。"]}]}]},"prepare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使做好準備，把……預備好；（為……）做好準備；預備（飯菜），做（飯）；配製（藥品或化學制品）；樂意做（be prepared to do sth.）；（在和絃中）預備（不和諧音）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prepare</b> something, you make it ready for something that is going to happen. 準備","examples":["Two technicians were preparing a videotape recording of last week's programme. 兩名技師正在準備上週節目的錄影。","On average each report requires 1,000 hours to prepare. 平均每份報告需要1000個小時來準備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>prepare</b> <b>for</b> an event or action that will happen soon, you get yourself ready for it or make the necessary arrangements. (為…) 作準備; 準備 (做某事)","examples":["The party leadership is using management consultants to help prepare for the next election. 該政黨的領導層正聘用管理顧問來幫助準備下一次選舉。","He had to go back to his hotel and prepare to catch a train for New York. 他不得不回賓館準備趕火車去紐約。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>prepare</b> food, you get it ready to be eaten, for example, by cooking it. 準備 (食物)","examples":["She made her way to the kitchen, hoping to find someone preparing dinner. 她朝廚房走去，希望看到有人在準備晚餐。"]}]}]},"own":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"有，擁有；<舊> 承認；為（某事）承擔全責，承認為（某事）負全責；<美，非正式> 徹底擊敗，徹底羞辱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自己的，屬於自己的；自己做的，為自己的；具有自己特點的，特有的"},{"pos":"pronoun.","zh":"自己的，屬於自己的；自己做的，自己生產的；具有自己特點的，特有的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>own</b> to indicate that something belongs to a particular person or thing. 自己的","examples":["My wife decided I should have my own shop. 我妻子決定我應該有自己的店鋪。","He could no longer trust his own judgement. 他再也不相信自己的判斷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>own</b> to indicate that something is used by, or is characteristic of, only one person, thing, or group. 自己獨有的","examples":["Jennifer insisted on her own room. 詹尼弗堅持要自己專用的房間。","Each nation has its own peculiarities when it comes to doing business. 說到做生意，每個民族都有它自己獨有的一些特性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>own</b> to indicate that someone does something without any help from other people. 自己的","examples":["They enjoy making their own decisions. 他們喜歡做他們自己的決定。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Own</b> is also a pronoun. 自己的","examples":["He saw the major's face a few inches from his own. 他看到少校的臉離他自己的臉只有幾英寸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Own</b> is also a pronoun. 自己獨有的","examples":["This young lady has a sense of style that is very much her own. 這位年輕女士具有一種她自己獨有的時尚觀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Own</b> is also a pronoun. 自己的","examples":["There's no career structure; you have to create your own. 沒有什麼職業架構，你必須創造你自己的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>own</b> something, it is your property. 擁有","examples":["His father owns a local video shop 他父親擁有一家當地的音像店。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something you can <b>call</b> your <b>own</b>, it belongs only to you, rather than being controlled by or shared with someone else. 專屬於自己的","examples":["I would like a place I could call my own. 我想要一個只屬於我自己的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>comes into</b> their <b>own</b>, they become very successful or start to perform very well because the circumstances are right. 得心應手","examples":["Many women have come into their own as teachers, healers, and leaders. 許多女性成為很成功的教師、醫師和領導者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> your <b>own back</b> on someone, you have your revenge on them because of something bad that they have done to you. 報復","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has a particular thing <b>of</b> their <b>own</b>, you mean that that thing belongs or relates to them, rather than to other people. 屬於自己的","examples":["He set out in search of ideas for starting a company of his own. 他開始著手想辦法創辦屬於自己的一家公司。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something has a particular quality or characteristic <b>of</b> their <b>own</b>, that quality or characteristic is especially theirs, rather than being shared by other things or people of that type. 特有的","examples":["The cries of the seagulls gave this part of the harbour a fascinating character of its own. 海鷗的鳴叫聲賦予海港的這邊一種特有的迷人特質。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you are <b>on</b> your <b>own</b>, you are alone. 獨自地","examples":["He lives on his own. 他獨自居住。","I felt pretty lonely last year being on my own. 我去年獨自生活時感到特別孤獨。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you do something <b>on</b> your <b>own</b>, you do it without any help from other people. 獨立地","examples":["I work best on my own. 我獨立工作最出色。"]}]}]},"please":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"好嗎，請（用於客氣地請求）；請千萬，請務必（用於加強請求的語氣）；行，謝謝（用於接受別人的好意）；請別，請不要；得了吧；讓我說"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）開心，（使）滿意；想，選擇，喜歡；請便，隨你的便"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>please</b> when you are politely asking or inviting someone to do something. 請 (用於禮貌地請求或邀請某人做某事)","examples":["Can you help us please? 能請你幫助我們嗎？","Please come in. 請進。","Can we have the bill please? 請給我們賬單好嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>please</b> when you are accepting something politely. 有請 (用於禮貌地接受某物)","examples":["\"Tea?\"—\"Yes, please.\" “要茶嗎？—“好的，有請。”"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>please</b> to indicate that you want someone to stop doing something or stop speaking. You would say this if, for example, what they are doing or saying makes you angry or upset. 求你了 (請求別人停止做某事或停止講話)","examples":["Please, Mary, this is all so unnecessary. 求你了，瑪麗，這一切根本沒有必要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say <b>please</b> in order to attract someone's attention politely. 對不起 (用以引起某人注意)","examples":["Please, Miss Smith, a moment. 對不起，史密斯小姐，稍等。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>pleases</b> you, they make you feel happy and satisfied. 使高興; 討好","examples":["More than anything, I want to please you. 最重要的是，我想讓你高興。","It pleased him to talk to her. 和她談話讓他高興。","He appeared anxious to please. 他似乎急於討好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>please</b> in expressions such as <b>as she pleases</b>, <b>whatever you please</b>, and <b>anything he pleases</b> to indicate that someone can do or have whatever they want. 隨 (某人) 喜歡","examples":["Women should be free to dress and act as they please. 女人應該有自由隨自己的意願著裝和行事。","He does whatever he pleases. 他想做什麼就做什麼。"]}]}]},"mean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"意味著；表示……的意思，作……的解釋；打算，意欲；使專門用於；導致，結果是；十分熟識；當真，說到做到；對某人重要"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"吝嗇的，小氣的；不善良的，刻薄的；要發怒的；熟練的，出色的；平均的；簡陋的，破舊的；微薄的；<舊>出身卑賤的，社會地位低下的；中庸的，中等的；<美>兇狠的，好鬥的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"中庸，折衷；平均數，中數；中間點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you want to know what a word, code, signal, or gesture <b>means</b>, you want to know what it refers to or what its message is. 意思是…","examples":["\"Credible\" means \"believable.\" 的意思是。","What does \"evidence\" mean? 是什麼意思？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you ask someone what they <b>mean</b>, you are asking them to explain exactly what or who they are referring to or what they are intending to say. 意指","examples":["Do you mean me? 你指我嗎？","Let me illustrate what I mean with an old story. 讓我用一個老故事來說明我指的是什麼吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>means</b> something <b>to</b> you, it is important to you in some way. (對某人) 很重要","examples":["The idea that she witnessed this shameful incident meant nothing to him. 他知道她目擊了這可恥的一幕，但這對他來說並不重要。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>means</b> another, it shows that the second thing exists or is true. 表明…的存在; 表明…屬實","examples":["An enlarged prostate does not necessarily mean cancer. 腫大的前列腺並不一定表明癌症的存在。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If one thing <b>means</b> another, the first thing leads to the second thing happening. 導致","examples":["It would almost certainly mean the end of NATO. 這的確幾乎導致北大西洋公約組織的終結。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If doing one thing <b>means</b> doing another, it involves doing the second thing. 意味著","examples":["Children universally prefer to live in peace and security, even if that means living with only one parent. 孩子們普遍願意過平靜安寧的生活，即使那意味著只能和單親生活在一起。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that you <b>mean</b> what you are saying, you are telling someone that you are serious about it and are not joking, exaggerating, or just being polite. 對…當真","examples":["He says you're fired if you're not back at work on Friday. And I think he meant it. 他說如果你週五不回來上班的話，就會被解僱。我想他是當真的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>meant</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are saying that they did it deliberately. 有意","examples":["I didn't mean to hurt you. 我不是有意要傷害你。","If that sounds harsh, it is meant to. 如果那聲音聽起來是刺耳的，它就是如此。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>did not</b> <b>mean</b> <b>any</b> harm, offence, or disrespect, you are saying that they did not intend to upset or offend people or to cause problems, even though they may in fact have done so. 本意為","examples":["I'm sure he didn't mean any harm. 我敢肯定他本無惡意。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>mean</b> <b>to</b> do something, you intend or plan to do it. 打算","examples":["Summer is the perfect time to catch up on the new books you meant to read. 夏天是補看想讀的新書的最佳時間。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that something <b>was meant</b> <b>to</b> happen, you believe that it was made to happen by God or fate, and did not just happen by chance. 註定","examples":["John was constantly reassuring me that we were meant to be together. 約翰不停地安慰我說，我們註定在一起。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>I mean</b>\" when making clearer something that you have just said. 也就是說","examples":["It was his idea. Gordon's, I mean. 那是他的主意。也就是說，戈登的主意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use \"<b>I mean</b>\" to introduce a statement, especially one that justifies something that you have just said. 我的意思是 (證明前述)","examples":["I'm sure he wouldn't mind. I mean, I was the one who asked him. 我肯定他不會介意。我的意思是，我就是問他的那個人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>I mean</b> when correcting something that you have just said. 我剛才是說","examples":["It was law or classics – I mean English or classics. 那是法律或者古典文學–我是說，英語或者古典文學。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>know what it means</b> to do something, you know everything that is involved in a particular activity or experience, especially the effect that it has on you. (親身) 體會了解","examples":["I know what it means to lose a child under such tragic circumstances. 我能切身體會在那樣悲慘的情況下失去孩子的感覺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a name, word, or phrase <b>means something to</b> you, you have heard it before and you know what it refers to. 對某人來說意味著什麼","examples":["\"Oh, Gairdner,\" he said, as if that meant something to him. “啊，蓋爾德納，”他說道，好像這個名字對他來說意味著什麼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use \"<b>you mean</b>\" in a question to check that you have understood what someone has said. 你是說 (疑問句中用於核實是否理解別人所說的話)","examples":["What accident? You mean Christina's? 什麼事故？你是說克里斯蒂娜的那次嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is being <b>mean</b>, they are being unkind to another person, for example by not allowing them to do something. 不友好的","examples":["The little girls had locked themselves in the room because Mack had been mean to them. 這些小女孩們把自己鎖在房間裡，因為麥克對她們不友好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or animal as <b>mean</b>, you are saying that they are very bad-tempered and cruel. 脾氣極壞的; 殘忍的","examples":["The state's former commissioner of prisons once called Leonard the meanest man he'd ever seen. 這個州的前任監獄長曾經把倫納德稱為他所見過的最殘忍的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>mean</b>, you are being critical of them because they are unwilling to spend much money or to use very much of a particular thing. 吝嗇的","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"intermediate or medium in size, quantity, etc (尺寸、數量等)中間的; 中等的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The mean</b> is a number that is the average of a set of numbers. 平均數","examples":["Take a hundred and twenty values and calculate the mean. 取120個值計算平均數。"]}]}]},"prove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"證實，證明；證明是，結果是；顯示（自己的）才幹（或勇氣）（prove oneself）；<法律> 檢驗，認證（遺囑）；（用數學或科學原理）證明，驗算；試（槍），查驗；（麵糰）發酵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>proves</b> <b>to</b> be true or <b>to</b> have a particular quality, it becomes clear after a period of time that it is true or has that quality. 證明是","examples":["We have been accused of exaggerating before, but unfortunately all our reports proved to be true. 我們曾被指責誇大其詞，但遺憾的是，我們所有的報告都證明是真實的。","In the past this process of transition has often proven difficult. 在過去，這種轉變過程常證明是艱難的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prove</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you show by means of argument or evidence that it is definitely true. 證明","examples":["You brought this charge. You prove it! 你提出了這一指控。你來證明它！","The results prove that regulation of the salmon farming industry is inadequate. 結果證明，大馬哈魚養殖業的管理是失當的。","That made me hopping mad and determined to prove him wrong. 這使我暴跳如雷並且使我下決心要證明他錯了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>prove</b> <b>yourself</b> to have a certain good quality, you show by your actions that you have it. 顯示 (優點)","examples":["Margie proved herself to be a good mother. 瑪吉顯示了自己是個好母親。","As a composer he proved himself adept at large dramatic forms. 作為一名作曲家，他顯示出自己擅長創作大型的戲劇體裁。"]}]}]},"move":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）改變位置，（使）移動；搬家，搬遷；（使）變換，調動；（使）改變觀點（或做法）；前進，進展；採取行動；使感動，打動；促使，驅使；更改（時間或日期）；改變話題；走棋，移動棋子；（在會議或法庭上）提議；<非正式>快速行進；（商品）被銷售，銷售（商品）；進行社交活動，交往；<非正式>離去；使（腸）排空"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"措施，行動；移動，活動；轉變，改變；一步棋，走棋；搬家，遷移"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>move</b> something or when it <b>moves</b>, its position changes and it does not remain still. 移動","examples":["She moved the sheaf of papers into position. 她把那捆紙移到了位置上。","A traffic policeman asked him to move his car. 一位交警讓他挪動一下他的車。","The train began to move. 火車開動了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people in authority <b>move</b> someone, they make that person go from one place or job to another one. 調動","examples":["His superiors moved him to another parish. 他的上級把他調到了另一個教區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>move</b> an event or the date of an event, you change the time at which it happens. 更改 (時間)","examples":["The club has moved its meeting to Saturday, January 22nd. 該俱樂部把會議日期改到了星期六，1月22日。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you will not <b>be moved</b>, you mean that you have come to a decision and nothing will change your mind. 使動搖","examples":["Everyone thought I was crazy to go back, but I wouldn't be moved. 人人都認為我回去是瘋了，可我是不會動搖的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>moves</b> you <b>to</b> do something, it influences you and causes you to do it. 促使","examples":["It was punk that first moved him to join a band seriously. 最初是朋克搖滾樂促使他認真地加入了一個樂隊。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>moves</b> you, it has an effect on your emotions and causes you to feel sadness or sympathy for another person. 感動","examples":["These stories surprised and moved me. 這些故事令我吃驚，並且感動了我。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"At a meeting, if you <b>move</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>move</b> <b>that</b> something should happen, you formally suggest it so that everyone present can vote on it. 提議","examples":["Somebody needs to move for an adjournment. 需要有人提議休會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>move</b>, you change your position or go to a different place. 移動 (位置)","examples":["She waited for him to get up, but he didn't move. 她等著他起來，可他沒有動。","He moved around the room, putting his possessions together. 他在屋裡走來走去，把他的東西都放在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>move</b>, you act or you begin to do something. 採取行動","examples":["Industrialists must move fast to take advantage of new opportunities in Eastern Europe. 實業家們必須快速採取行動，抓住東歐的新機遇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person or company <b>moves</b>, they leave the building where they have been living or working, and they go to live or work in a different place, taking their possessions with them. 搬遷","examples":["Two people in love are at home wherever they are, no matter how often they move. 無論在哪裡，不管搬多少次家，兩個相愛的人都會過得舒舒服服。","She had often considered moving to Seattle. 她那時常常考慮搬到西雅圖去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>move</b> <b>from</b> one job or interest <b>to</b> another, you change to it. 變換 (職業); 改變 (興趣)","examples":["He moved from being a part-time tutor to being a lecturer in social history. 他從一名兼職助教轉變成了一名社會史講師。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>move</b> <b>to</b> a new topic in a conversation, you start talking about something different. 改變 (話題)","examples":["Let's move to another subject, Dan. 丹，我們換個話題吧。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>move</b> toward a particular state, activity, or opinion, you start to be in that state, do that activity, or have that opinion. 轉變","examples":["The Labour Party has moved to the right and become like your Democratic Party. 工黨已經轉向右翼，變得像你們民主黨了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a situation or process <b>is moving</b>, it is developing or progressing, rather than staying still. 進展","examples":["Events are moving fast. 事件進展很快。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>moves in</b> a particular society, circle, or world, you mean that they know people in a particular social class or group and spend most of their time with them. 躋身於 (某個社會、圈子或領域)","examples":["She moves in high-society circles in Palm Beach. 她躋身於棕櫚海灘的上流社會。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Move</b> is also a noun. 位移","examples":["The doctor made a move toward the door. 醫生朝門口挪了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>move</b> is an action that you take in order to achieve something. 行動","examples":["The one-point cut in interest rates was a wise move. 利率下調1個點是明智之舉。","It may also be a good move to suggest she talks things over. 建議她仔細討論一下這些事情可能也是一個好的做法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Move</b> is also a noun. 搬遷","examples":["Modigliani announced his move to Montparnasse in 1909. 莫迪里亞尼1909年宣佈他要搬到蒙帕爾納斯去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Move</b> is also a noun. (職業的) 變換; (興趣的) 改變","examples":["His move to the chairmanship means he will take a less active role in day-to-day management. 他主席職務的調任意味著他將更少地參與日常管理工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Move</b> is also a noun. 轉變","examples":["His move to the left was not a sudden leap but a natural working out of ideas. 他左傾的轉變並非突然，而是思想發展的自然結果。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>move</b> is an act of putting a chess piece or other counter in a different position on a board when it is your turn to do so in a game. 一步棋","examples":["With no idea of what to do for my next move, my hand hovered over the board. 不知道我下一步棋該怎麼走，我的手在棋盤上方舉棋不定。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被感動的","examples":["Those who listened to him were deeply moved. 聽他講話的人都被深深地感動了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one <b>false move</b> will cause a disaster, you mean that you or someone else must not make any mistakes because the situation is so difficult or dangerous. 錯誤之舉","examples":["He knew one false move would end in death. 他知道稍有差池就會送命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make a move</b>, you prepare or begin to leave one place and go somewhere else. 準備出發; 出發","examples":["He glanced at his wristwatch. \"I suppose we'd better make a move.\" 他看了一眼手錶說：“我想我們最好動身吧。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make a move</b>, you take a course of action. 採取行動","examples":["The week before the deal was supposed to close, fifteen Japanese banks made a move to pull out. 該交易本應結束的前一週，15家日本銀行採取行動撤出了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>on the move</b>, you are going from one place to another. 奔波","examples":["Jack never wanted to stay in one place for very long, so they were always on the move. 傑克從不想在一個地方久留，所以他們總在輾轉奔波。"]}]}]},"make":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"製造；制定，擬定；使變得，使處於；造成，引起；整理（床鋪）；做，作出；強迫；挑選，任命；成為，適合；合計，等於；計算，估算；安排，組織；表現，描繪；掙錢，賺錢；（體育比賽）得分；（盡力）趕往，到達；排成 （某圖案）；使形成，留下（印記、洞等）；使成功，使圓滿；在……佔一席之地；似乎要做；朝（特定方向）走去；<美，非正式>求歡；（橋牌等）贏一墩牌；（潮）漲，（潮）退"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（機器、裝置等的）品牌，型號；結構，構造；通電，接電"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>make</b> with a wide range of nouns to indicate that someone performs an action or says something. For example, if you <b>make</b> a suggestion, you suggest something. 與名詞連用，表示做動作或說某事","examples":["I'd just like to make a comment. 我只想做一下評論。","I made a few phone calls. 我打了幾個電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>make</b> with certain nouns to indicate that someone does something well or badly. For example, if you <b>make</b> a success of something, you do it successfully, and if you <b>make</b> a mess of something, you do it very badly. 與某些名詞連用，表示做得好或做得糟","examples":["Apparently he made a mess of his audition. 顯然他把試演搞得一團糟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> <b>as if to</b> do something or <b>make</b> <b>to</b> do something, you behave in a way that makes it seem that you are just about to do it. 擺出 (要做某事的姿態)","examples":["Mary made as if to protest, then hesitated. 瑪麗似乎要抗議，又猶豫了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>makes</b> you do something, it causes you to do it. 致使 (某人做某事)","examples":["Dirt from the motorway made him cough. 公路上的灰塵使他咳嗽起來。","The white tips of his shirt collar made him look like a choirboy. 他襯衣的白色領尖使他看起來像個唱詩班男童。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> someone do something, you force them to do it. 迫使 (某人做某事)","examples":["You can't make me do anything. 你不能強迫我做任何事。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>make</b> to talk about causing someone or something to be a particular thing or to have a particular quality. For example, to <b>make</b> someone a star means to cause them to become a star, and to <b>make</b> someone angry means to cause them to become angry. 使 (某人、某事物) 變成…; 使變得…","examples":["...James Bond, the role that made him a star. …詹姆斯·邦德，那個使他成為明星的角色。","She made life very difficult for me. 她使我的生活變得很艱難。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that one thing or person <b>makes</b> another seem, for example, small, stupid, or good, you mean that they cause them to seem small, stupid, or good in comparison, even though they are not. 使 (某物、某人) 顯得…","examples":["They live in fantasy worlds which make Disneyland seem uninventive. 他們生活在幻想世界裡，那些幻想使迪斯尼樂園也顯得毫無創意。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> <b>yourself</b> understood, heard, or known, you succeed in getting people to understand you, hear you, or know that you are there. 使 (自己被人理解﹑聽到﹑知曉等)","examples":["He learned enough Spanish to make himself understood. 他學的西班牙語足以讓別人明白他。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> someone something, you appoint them to a particular job, role, or position. 任命 (某人擔任某職或角色)","examples":["He made her a director in his numerous companies. 他任命她為他數家公司的主管。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> something <b>into</b> something else, you change it in some way so that it becomes that other thing. 把 (某物) 變成 (另一物)","examples":["We made it into a beautiful home. 我們把它變成了一個漂亮的家。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"To <b>make</b> a total or score a particular amount means to increase it to that amount. 使 (總數、分數) 升為 (某數)","examples":["This makes the total cost of the bulb and energy $27. 這使得燈泡和電量的總耗費升為$27。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When someone <b>makes</b> a friend or an enemy, someone becomes their friend or their enemy, often because of a particular thing they have done. 結成 (朋友或敵人)","examples":["Lorenzo was a natural leader who made friends easily. 洛倫佐是個天生的領導者，結交朋友容易。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"To <b>make</b> something means to produce, construct, or create it. 製作; 創作","examples":["She made her own bread. 她自己做了麵包。","Having curtains made professionally can be costly. 找專業人員製作窗簾會很貴。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> a note or list, you write something down in that form. 寫 (筆記、清單等)","examples":["Mr. Perry made a note in his book. 佩裡先生在他的書裡做了批註。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> rules or laws, you decide what these should be. 制定 (規則、法律等)","examples":["The police don't make the laws, they merely enforce them. 警察不制定法律，只是執行法律。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> money, you get it by working for it, by selling something, or by winning it. 掙; 賺; 贏 (錢)","examples":["I think every business's goal is to make money. 我想每筆生意的目的都是賺錢。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> a case <b>for</b> something, you try to establish or prove that it is the best thing to do. (為某事) 做解釋","examples":["You could certainly make a case for this point of view. 你當然可以為這種觀點做解釋。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If someone <b>makes</b> a particular team or <b>makes</b> a particular high position, they do so well that they are put in that team or get that position. 成為 (某隊成員); 得到 (某職位)","examples":["The athletes are just happy to make the team. 那些運動員很高興加入該隊。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> a place in or by a particular time, you get there in or by that time, often with some difficulty. (常指艱難地) 到達 (某地)","examples":["The engine is gulping two tons of fuel an hour in order to make New Orleans by nightfall. 引擎每小時消耗兩噸燃料以便在天黑之前趕到新奧爾良。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"You use <b>make</b> <b>it</b> when saying what you calculate or guess an amount to be. 計算; 估計","examples":["\"How many shots has she got left?\"—\"I make it two.\" “她還剩幾顆子彈？”–“我估計是兩顆。”"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"You use <b>make</b> <b>it</b> when saying what time your watch says it is. 看錶上是 (某時間)","examples":["I make it nearly nine o'clock. 我的表上快9:00了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make do</b> <b>with</b> something, you use or have it instead of something else that you do not have, although it is not as good. (拿…) 湊合","examples":["Why make do with a copy if you can afford the genuine article? 如果你買得起正品，為什麼還拿複製品湊合呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make it</b> somewhere, you succeed in getting there, especially in time to do something. 成功到達 (某地)","examples":["So you did make it to America, after all. 這樣你終究成功到達了美國。","...the hostages who never made it home. …始終沒能回家的人質們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make it</b>, you are successful in achieving something difficult, or in surviving through a very difficult period. (歷經艱難) 獲得成功","examples":["I believe I have the talent to make it. 我相信我有獲得成功的才幹。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you cannot <b>make it</b>, you are unable to attend an event that you have been invited to. 如約而至","examples":["He hadn't been able to make it to our dinner. 他沒能如約參加我們的晚宴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>make</b> of something such as a car or radio is the name of the company that made it. (產品的) 牌子","examples":["The only car parked outside is a black Saab – a different make. 停在外面的惟一一輛車是黑色的薩博–一個不同的牌子。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>make</b> to say that someone or something has the right qualities for a particular task or role. For example, if you say that someone will <b>make</b> a good politician, you mean that they have the right qualities to be a good politician. 成為","examples":["She'll make a good actress, if she gets the right training. 如果她得到恰當訓練，她會成為一名好演員。","You've a very good idea there. It will make a good book. 你的那個絕妙觀點會使之成為一本好書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>make</b> a particular pattern such as a line or a circle, they arrange themselves in this way. 排成 (某圖案)","examples":["A group of people made a circle around the Pentagon. 一群人繞五角大樓圍成了一個圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>make</b> to say what two numbers add up to. 是 (用於加法)","examples":["Four twos make eight. 4個2是8。"]}]}]},"ready":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（某人）準備好（做某事）的；預先備好的，可供使用的；樂意的；方便使用的，現成的；迅速的，敏捷的；即將……的；需要的，想要的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>現款（the ready/readies）；預備好的狀態"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"已做完，已完成"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>做好……的準備"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>ready</b>, they are properly prepared for something. If something is <b>ready</b>, it has been properly prepared and is now able to be used. 準備好的","examples":["It took her a long time to get ready for church. 她花了很長時間才準備好去教堂。","Are you ready to board, Mr. Daly? 準備好上飛機了嗎，戴利先生？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>ready</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>ready</b> <b>to</b> do something, you have enough experience to do it or you are old enough and sensible enough to do it. 勝任的; 準備好的","examples":["She says she's not ready for marriage. 她說她還沒有準備好結婚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>ready</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are willing to do it. 樂意的","examples":["They were ready to die for their beliefs. 他們願意為信仰而獻身。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>ready for</b> something, you need it or want it. 需要的","examples":["I don't know about you, but I'm ready for bed. 我不知道你怎樣，但我想去睡了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To be <b>ready</b> <b>to</b> do something means to be about to do it or likely to do it. 即將…的; 可能…的","examples":["She looked ready to cry. 她看起來將要哭了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>ready</b> to describe things that are able to be used very quickly and easily. 現成的","examples":["I didn't have a ready answer for this dilemma. 我沒有現成的答案來解決這個進退兩難的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ready</b> something, you prepare it for a particular purpose. 使準備好","examples":["John's soldiers were readying themselves for the final assault. 約翰計程車兵們正在為最後的進攻做好準備。"]}]}]},"receive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"得到，收到；遭受，經受（特定待遇）；對……作出反應；接待，招待；接收（某人為成員）；接收，收聽（訊號）；（透過無線電）聽到；購買，窩藏（贓物）；接（球）；領受（聖餐麵包或葡萄酒）；接受（治療）；形成（看法，印象）；容納，承接"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>receive</b> something, you get it after someone gives it to you or sends it to you. 接到; 收到","examples":["They will receive their awards at a ceremony in Stockholm. 他們將在斯德哥爾摩的典禮上接受給他們的獎勵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>receive</b> to say that certain kinds of things happen to someone. For example if they are injured, you can say that they <b>received</b> an injury. 受到; 遭受","examples":["He received more of the blame than anyone when the plan failed to work. 當計劃失敗之後他受到的指責比任何人都多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>receive</b> a visitor or a guest, you greet them. 接待; 迎接","examples":["The following evening the hotel was again receiving guests. 第二天晚上飯店又接待起客人來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is received</b> in a particular way, you mean that people react to it in that way. (用某種特定方式) 回應","examples":["The resolution had been received with great disappointment within the PLO. 巴勒斯坦解放組織內部對此決議感到極其失望。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a radio or television <b>receives</b> signals that are being transmitted, it picks them up and converts them into sound or pictures. 接收 (訊號)","examples":["The reception was a little faint but clear enough for him to receive the signal. 接收有些弱，但足夠清晰到使他能夠接收訊號。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are on the receiving end</b> or <b>at the receiving end</b> of something unpleasant, you are the person that it happens to. 成為 (不愉快事件的) 承受方","examples":["You saw hate in their eyes and you were on the receiving end of that hate. 你在他們的眼中看到仇恨，而你就是那仇恨的物件。"]}]}]},"read":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閱讀，讀懂；朗讀；（在書籍、報紙等中）讀到，看到；解讀，（按某種方式）理解；看透（想法或心思）；讀起來（給人以某種印象）；有……的字樣，寫著；換用，改作（用於訂正訛誤）；讀取（磁碟中的資訊）；（透過無線電）收聽到，聽明白；（測量儀器）指示，顯示；看（度量儀器顯示的數字）；攻讀；將（議案或其他法令）提交立法機構"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>閱讀，閱讀時間；<英，非正式>讀物；<美>解釋，闡明"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"博學的，有學問的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>read</b> something such as a book or article, you look at and understand the words that are written there. 閱讀","examples":["Have you read this book? 你讀過這本書嗎？","I read about it in the paper. 我在報上讀到有關它的訊息。","She spends her days reading and watching television. 她每天就是看書和看電視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>read</b> a piece of writing to someone, you say the words aloud. 朗讀","examples":["Jay reads poetry so beautifully. 傑伊朗讀詩歌非常動聽。","I like it when she reads to us. 我很喜歡她讀書給我們聽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People who can <b>read</b> have the ability to look at and understand written words. 識字","examples":["He couldn't read or write. 他不識字，也不會寫字。","The kid can read words, but did miserably on the test. 這孩子能認字，但考試時卻一塌糊塗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you can <b>read</b> music, you have the ability to look at and understand the symbols that are used in written music to represent musical sounds. 識 (樂譜)","examples":["Later on I learned how to read music. 後來我學會了如何識樂譜。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a computer <b>reads</b> a file or a document, it takes information from a disk or tape. (電腦) 讀取 (檔案或文件)","examples":["How can I read an Excel file on a computer that only has Word installed? 我怎麼在只裝了文書處理軟體的電腦上讀取表格檔案呢？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>read</b> when saying what is written on something or in something. For example, if a notice <b>reads</b> \"Entrance,\" the word \"Entrance\" is written on it. 寫著","examples":["The sign on the bus read \"Private: Not In Service.\" 公共汽車上的標誌寫著“私人所有：不運營。”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>is read</b> in a particular way, it is understood or interpreted in that way. 理解; 詮釋","examples":["The play is being widely read as an allegory of imperialist conquest. 這出戏正被廣泛地詮釋為帝國主義征服的寓言。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>read</b> someone's mind or thoughts, you know exactly what they are thinking without them telling you. 看透 (心思或想法)","examples":["From behind her, as if he could read her thoughts, Benny said, \"You're free to go any time you like, Madame.\" 從她身後，好像他可以看透她的想法，本尼說道，“你什麼時候想走都可以，夫人。”"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you can <b>read</b> someone or you can <b>read</b> their gestures, you can understand what they are thinking or feeling by the way they behave or the things they say. 領會 (某人或其言談舉止的意圖)","examples":["If you have to work as part of a team, you must learn to read people. 如果你不得不在一個團隊中工作，你必須學會領會別人的意圖。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When you <b>read</b> a measuring device, you look at it to see what the figure or measurement on it is. 檢視; 讀出 (測量儀器的數字)","examples":["It is essential that you are able to read a thermometer. 能讀出溫度計上的溫度是基本要求。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If a measuring device <b>reads</b> a particular amount, it shows that amount. (測量儀表) 顯示為; 標明","examples":["The thermometer read 105 degrees Fahrenheit. 溫度計顯示為華氏105度。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Read</b> is also a noun. 閱讀","examples":["I settled down to have a good read. 我舒舒服服地坐下來，想好好讀書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a book or magazine is a good <b>read</b>, you mean that it is very enjoyable to read. 讀物","examples":["Ben Okri's latest novel is a good read. 本·奧克里的最新小說是本好讀物。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to how a piece of writing <b>reads</b>, you are referring to its style. (作品) 讀起來 (有…風格)","examples":["The book reads like a ballad. 這本書讀起來像民謠的風格。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"read的過去式及過去分詞","examples":[]}]}]},"remember":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"回想起，記得；記起，憶起（某事物）；記牢，不忘記；紀念，緬懷；（祈禱時）為......祝福；送錢，送禮（給某人）；代（某人）問候（某人）；（失態後）檢點，補救"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>remember</b> people or events from the past, you still have an idea of them in your mind and you are able to think about them. 記得","examples":["You wouldn't remember me. I was in another group. 你不會記得我的，我當時在另一個組。","I remembered that we had made the last of the coffee the day before. 我記得我們前一天剛煮完了最後一點咖啡。","What a day that was, do you remember? 那是怎樣的一天，你還記得嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>remember</b> that something is the case, you become aware of it again after a time when you did not think about it. 憶起; 回想起","examples":["She remembered that she was going to the club that evening. 她回想起那天晚上她要去俱樂部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you cannot <b>remember</b> something, you are not able to bring it back into your mind when you make an effort to do so. 記住","examples":["If you can't remember your number, write it in code in an appointment book. 如果你記不住你的號碼，就用密碼把它寫在預約本里。","I can't remember what I said. 我記不起我說過什麼了。","Don't tell me you can't remember. 別告訴我你不記得了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>remember</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it when you intend to. 記住 (做某事)","examples":["Please remember to enclose a stamped self-addressed envelope when writing. 請記住寫信的時候附上一個貼好郵票、寫好自己姓名地址的信封。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You tell someone to <b>remember</b> <b>that</b> something is the case when you want to emphasize its importance. It may be something that they already know about or a new piece of information. 要記住 (表示強調重要性)","examples":["It is important to remember that each person reacts differently. 重要的是要記住每個人的反應不同。"]}]}]},"seem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（涉及推斷）似乎，看來；（用於表示謹慎、禮貌或委婉）好像，可能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>seem</b> to say that someone or something gives the impression of having a particular quality, or of happening in the way you describe. 似乎; 看起來","examples":["The explosions seemed quite close by. 爆炸似乎就在近旁。","To everyone who knew them, they seemed an ideal couple. 在每個認識他們的人看來，他們似乎是一對佳偶。","The calming effect seemed to last for about ten minutes. 鎮靜效果好像持續了大約10分鐘。","It seems that the attack was carefully planned. 看起來，這次襲擊是精心策劃的。","It seemed as if she'd been gone forever. 好像她已經永遠地離開了一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>seem</b> when you are describing your own feelings or thoughts, or describing something that has happened to you, in order to make your statement less forceful. 感覺好像","examples":["I seem to have lost all my self-confidence. 我好像已經喪失了所有的自信。","I seem to remember giving you very precise instructions. 我好像記得曾給過你非常明確的指示。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>cannot seem</b> or <b>could not seem</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you have tried to do it and were unable to. 好像總是不能","examples":["No matter how hard I try I cannot seem to catch up on all the bills. 不管我怎麼努力，我好像總也無法付清所有的賬單。"]}]}]},"save":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"救助，搭救；避免，減少；積攢，儲蓄；節省（錢、時間或其他資源）；儲存，保留；收集；（為某人）保留；（計算機）儲存（資料）；使健康長壽，護佑；（足球等）救球，防止對方進球；（棒球）（替補投手） 保持（其他投手取得的領先地位）；（基督教）拯救（某人），使擺脫罪孽"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（足球等守門員的）救球；（棒球）（替補投手） 保持（其他投手取得的領先地位）；（計算機）儲存資料"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"<正式> 除……之外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>save</b> someone or something, you help them to avoid harm or to escape from a dangerous or unpleasant situation. 救助; 拯救","examples":["...an austerity programme designed to save the country's failing economy. …一個旨在拯救該國衰退的經濟的緊縮計劃。","The meeting is an attempt to mobilize nations to save children from death by disease and malnutrition. 該會議試圖動員各國救助兒童，以免死於疾病和營養不良。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>save</b>, you gradually collect money by spending less than you get, usually in order to buy something that you want. 儲蓄","examples":["The majority of people intend to save, but find that by the end of the month there is nothing left. 大多數人都想要儲蓄，但到月底的時候卻發現已經一分不剩了。","Tim and Barbara are now saving for a house in the suburbs. 蒂姆和芭芭拉眼下正為郊區的一所房子攢錢。","I was trying to save money to go to college. 我當時正努力攢錢去上大學。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>save</b> something such as time or money, you prevent the loss or waste of it. 節約","examples":["It saves time in the kitchen to have things you use a lot within reach. 在廚房裡把常用的東西放在手邊可以節省時間。","I'll try to save him the expense of a flight from Perth. 我會想辦法給他省下從珀斯過來的機票費用。","A new filter can save on energy bills. 一個新的過濾器能節省能源開支。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>save</b> something, you keep it because it will be needed later. 保留 (備用)","examples":["Drain the beans thoroughly and save the stock for soup. 把豆子徹底濾幹，留下豆汁做湯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>saves</b> you <b>from</b> an unpleasant action or experience, they change the situation so that you do not have to do it or experience it. 免去","examples":["The scanner will reduce the need for exploratory operations which will save risk and pain for patients. 掃描器將減少所需的探查手術，從而為病患者免除風險和疼痛。","She was hoping that something might save her from having to make a decision. 她真希望有什麼可以使自己免於作決定。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>save</b> data in a computer, you give the computer an instruction to store the data on a tape or disk. 儲存; 存檔","examples":["Try to get into the habit of saving your work regularly. 要努力養成經常儲存工作內容的習慣。","Save frequently when you are creating graphics. 當你在製圖的時候要經常存檔。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a goalkeeper <b>saves</b>, or <b>saves</b> a shot, they succeed in preventing the ball from going into the goal. 救球; 撲救","examples":["He saved one shot when the ball hit him on the head. 他撲住了一次射門，球打在了他的頭上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Save up</b> means the same as . 同(save)","examples":["Julie wanted to put some of her money aside for holidays or save up for something special. 朱莉想留出一些錢去度假或是存些錢以備專門之需。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Save</b> is also a noun. 救球; 撲救","examples":["The goalie made some great saves. 這名守門員撲住了幾個好球。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"with the exception of 除了 (Also saving)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"but; except 但是","examples":[]}]}]},"sell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"出讓，轉讓；出售，售賣；以……價錢出售；促銷，推銷；有銷路；說服，使接受；<古> 出賣，做交易；<古> 欺騙；用以銷售（一定數量）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式> 銷售，出售；推銷品，銷售品；<非正式> 讓人失望的東西；推銷術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sell</b> something that you own, you let someone have it in return for money. 賣","examples":["Catlin sold the paintings to Philadelphia industrialist Joseph Harrison. 卡特林把這些畫賣給了費城實業家約瑟夫·哈里森。","The directors sold the business for $14.8 million. 董事們把這個公司以1480萬美元賣掉了。","When is the best time to sell? 什麼時候才是出售的最佳時機呢?"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a shop <b>sells</b> a particular thing, it is available for people to buy there. 出售; 經銷","examples":["It sells everything from hair ribbons to oriental rugs. 這裡出售各種商品，從扎頭髮的髮帶到東方小地毯都有。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that <b>sells</b> a product makes people want to buy the product. 促進…的銷路","examples":["It is only the sensational that sells news magazines. 只有轟動性的訊息才能促進新聞雜誌的銷售。","...the maxim that safety doesn't sell. …安全並不意味著暢銷的格言。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>sell</b> someone an idea or proposal, or <b>sell</b> someone <b>on</b> an idea, you convince them that it is a good one. 推薦; 使接受","examples":["She tried to sell me the idea of buying my own paper shredder. 她努力向我灌輸買一臺自己的碎紙機的想法。","She is hoping she can sell the idea to clients. 她希望她能使客戶接受這一想法。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>sells</b> <b>for</b> a particular price, that price is paid for it. 售價為…","examples":["Unmodernized property can sell for up to 40 percent of its modernized market value. 未經現代化改造的房地產售價至多是其現代化改造後市價的40%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>sells</b>, it is bought by the public, usually in fairly large quantities. 有銷路; 行銷","examples":["Even if this album doesn't sell and the critics don't like it, we wouldn't ever change. 即使這張專輯沒有銷路，並且也不討評論家們喜歡，我們也決不會改變。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>sells</b> their <b>body</b>, they have sex for money. 出賣肉體","examples":["85 percent said they would rather not sell their bodies for a living. 85%的人說她們不會出賣肉體以謀生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about someone <b>selling</b> their <b>soul</b> in order to get something, you are criticizing them for abandoning their principles. 出賣靈魂","examples":["...a man who would sell his soul for political viability. …一個為了政治前途甘願出賣靈魂的人。"]}]}]},"send":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"郵寄，傳送；傳達，告知；派遣，打發，安排去；使快速（或猛然）移動；使作出（某種反應），使表現出（某種行為）；排放，排出（煙或化學反應的產生物等）；<非正式> 使著迷，使入迷"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古> 波浪的推力，波浪引起的水位上升（=scend）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>send</b> someone something, you arrange for it to be taken and delivered to them, for example, by mail. 郵寄; 傳送","examples":["Myra Cunningham sent me a note thanking me for dinner. 邁拉·坎寧安寄給了我一封簡訊，感謝我請她吃飯。","I sent a copy to the school principal. 我寄了一份影印件給校長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>send</b> someone somewhere, you tell them to go there. 派遣; 打發","examples":["Inspector Banbury came up to see her, but she sent him away. 班伯裡警官過來看她，但她卻把他打發走了。","...the government's decision to send troops to the region. …政府向該地區派遣軍隊的決定。","I suggested that he rest, and sent him for an X-ray. 我建議他休息，並叫他去作一次X光檢查。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>send</b> someone <b>to</b> an institution such as a school or a prison, you arrange for them to stay there for a period of time. 把…送進 (學校、監獄等)","examples":["It's his parents' choice to send him to a boarding school, rather than a convenient day school. 把他送到寄宿學校而不是去附近的走讀學校，是他父母的決定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>send</b> a signal means to cause it to go to a place by means of radio waves or electricity. (透過電波或電) 傳送 (訊號)","examples":["The transmitters will send a signal automatically to a local base station. 發射臺會自動將訊號傳送到地方基站。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>sends</b> things or people in a particular direction, it causes them to move in that direction. 使 (向某方向) 移動","examples":["The explosion sent shrapnel flying through the sides of cars on the crowded motorway. 這場爆炸使得炸彈碎片從擁擠公路上的車輛兩側飛過。","A left hook sent him reeling. 一記左鉤拳打得他踉踉蹌蹌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>send</b> someone or something <b>into</b> a particular state means to cause them to go into or be in that state. 使進入 (某種狀態)","examples":["My attempt to fix it sent Lawrence into fits of laughter. 我嘗試著修理它，逗得勞倫斯笑得前仰後合。","...before civil war and famine sent the country plunging into anarchy. …在內戰和饑荒讓這個國家陷入一片混亂之前。"]}]}]},"sing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"唱（歌），演唱；鳴，啼；嗚嗚作響，發出嗖嗖聲；<非正式>（向警方）告密；（尤指用詩歌等文學作品）歌頌，讚頌"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式> 唱歌，演唱；<美，非正式> 業餘演唱會；鳴聲，呼嘯聲"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"單數（singular 的縮寫形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sing</b>, you make musical sounds with your voice, usually producing words that fit a tune. 唱","examples":["I can't sing. 我不會唱歌。","I sing about love most of the time. 我大部分時間都在歌唱愛情。","They were all singing the same song. 他們在唱同一首歌。"]}]}]},"say":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"說，講；宣稱，說明；認為，據說；發音，讀；確信，確定（事實）；（對某人）意味著；表達，傳達；指明，表明；假設，比如說；讓某人做（某事）；複述，誦唸；念，背誦；替（某人或某事）說好話（壞話）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"發言權，決定權"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<美，非正式> （吃驚或吸引注意力）哎呀，喂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>say</b> something, you speak words. 說","examples":["\"I'm sorry,\" he said. “我很抱歉，”他說。","She said they were very impressed. 她說他們被深深打動了。","Forty-one people are said to have been seriously hurt. 據說有41人嚴重受傷。","I packed and said goodbye to Charlie. 我收拾好行裝，跟查理說了再見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>say</b> in expressions such as <b>I would just like to say</b> to introduce what you are actually saying, or to indicate that you are expressing an opinion or admitting a fact. If you state that you <b>can't say</b> something or you <b>wouldn't say</b> something, you are indicating in a polite or indirect way that it is not the case. (表達觀點或陳述事實，否定用法表示婉轉陳述某事並非事實) 說","examples":["I would just like to say that this is the most hypocritical thing I have ever heard in my life. 我只想說這是我一生中聽到過的最虛偽的事。","I must say that rather shocked me, too. 我得說那件事也讓我頗為震驚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can mention the contents of a piece of writing by mentioning what it <b>says</b> or what someone <b>says</b> in it. 宣稱","examples":["The report says there is widespread and routine torture of political prisoners in the country. 報告稱在那個國家存在著普遍的、慣常的虐待政治犯的現象。","You can't have one without the other, as the song says. 正如那首歌所唱的，二者你不能只取其一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>say</b> something <b>to yourself</b>, you think it. 心中暗想","examples":["Perhaps I'm still dreaming, I said to myself. 我心中暗想，可能我仍在做夢吧。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You indicate the information given by something such as a clock, dial, or map by mentioning what it <b>says</b>. (鍾，地圖等) 表明","examples":["The clock said four minutes past eleven when we set off. 我們出發時，時鐘顯示11點4分。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>says</b> something <b>about</b> a person, situation, or thing, it gives important information about them. 說明","examples":["I think that says a lot about how well Safin is playing. 我認為那足以說明薩芬表現得有多出色。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>says</b> a lot <b>for</b> a person or thing, it shows that this person or thing is very good or has a lot of good qualities. 說明 (某人或某物有很多優點)","examples":["That the Escort is still the nation's bestselling car in 1992 says a lot for the power of Ford's marketing people. 雅仕車仍是1992年全國銷售得最好的汽車，這足以說明福特公司營銷人員的非凡的能力。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>say</b> in expressions such as <b>I'll say that for them</b> and <b>you can say this for them</b> after or before you mention a good quality that someone has, usually when you think they do not have many good qualities. 有一點該肯定 (用於表揚沒有多少優點的人)","examples":["He's usually well-dressed, I'll say that for him. 有一點該肯定的是，他通常穿著很考究。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>say</b> when you want to discuss something that might possibly happen or be true. 假定","examples":["Say you were buying a new car, would your discussion begin and end with the monthly payment? 假定你要買輛新車，你開始和結束討論時的問題會是按月付款的數額嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>a</b> <b>say</b> <b>in</b> something, you have the right to give your opinion and influence decisions relating to it. 發言權","examples":["You can get married at sixteen, and yet you haven't got a say in the running of the country. 你可以在16歲結婚，然而對國家的管理你還沒有發言權。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>say</b> or <b>let's say</b> when you mention something as an example. 比如說","examples":["To see the problem here more clearly, let's look at a different biological system, say, an acorn. 為了把這裡的問題看得更清楚，讓我們看一種不同的生物系統，比如說，橡實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>says it all</b>, you mean that it shows you very clearly the truth about a situation or someone's feelings. 清楚說明事實","examples":["This is my third visit in a week, which says it all. 這是我一週內的第三次來訪，這本身就說明了一切。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say there is a lot <b>to be said for</b> something, you mean you think it has a lot of good qualities or aspects. 有很多優點","examples":["There's a lot to be said for being based in the country. 以農村為依託有很多優勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone asks <b>what</b> you <b>have to say for</b> <b>yourself</b>, they are asking what excuse you have for what you have done. 某人有何要為自己辯解的","examples":["\"Well,\" she said eventually, \"what have you to say for yourself?\" “好了，”她最後說，“你有什麼要為自己說的？”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>goes without saying</b>, it is obvious. 不言而喻","examples":["It goes without saying that if someone has lung problems they should not smoke. 肺部有了問題就不該抽菸，這是不言而喻的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When one of the people or groups involved in a discussion <b>has</b> their <b>say</b>, they give their opinion. 發表意見","examples":["Voters were finally having their say today. 選民們今天終於發表他們的意見了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>that is to say</b> or <b>that's to say</b> to indicate that you are about to express the same idea more clearly or precisely. 也就是說","examples":["That would mean voting no, that is to say, using the veto. 那就意味著投反對票，也就是說，行使否決權。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use \"<b>You don't say</b>\" to express surprise at what someone has told you. People often use this expression to indicate that in fact they are not surprised. 真的嗎 (用於並不太驚訝時)","examples":["\"I'm a writer.\"—\"You don't say. What kind of book are you writing?\" “我是個作家。”—“真的嗎，你在寫什麼樣的書呢？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use \"<b>I wouldn't say no</b>\" to indicate that you would like something, especially something that has just been offered to you. 我不反對","examples":["I wouldn't say no to a drink. 我不反對喝一杯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use \"<b>You can say that again</b>\" to express strong agreement with what someone has just said. 說得太對了","examples":["\"You are in enough trouble already.\"—\"You can say that again,\" sighed Richard. “你現在麻煩已經夠多的。”—“說得太對了，”理查德嘆息著說。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an exclamation to attract attention or express surprise, etc 引起注意或表達吃驚的叫聲","examples":[]}]}]},"put":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放，放置；猛推，用力插入；將……送往，安置；使與……連線，安裝；寫下；使處於（某狀態或情況）；使受到……的影響，把……施加給；給予（重視、信任、價值等）；把……視為（或列為）；表述，提出；使工作，使用；投擲（鐵餅），推（鉛球）；（船）（沿某個方向）行駛；譜曲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鉛球或鐵餅的）投擲，推；（股票）put option 的簡稱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"固定不動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>put</b> something in a particular place or position, you move it into that place or position. 放置","examples":["Leaphorn put the photograph on the desk. 利普霍恩把那張照片放在桌子上。","She hesitated, then put her hand on Grace's arm. 她猶豫了一下，然後把手搭在格雷斯的臂膀上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone somewhere, you cause them to go there and to stay there for a period of time. 安置","examples":["Rather than put him in the hospital, she had been caring for him at home. 她沒有把他送進醫院，而是一直在家裡照料他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>put</b> someone or something in a particular state or situation means to cause them to be in that state or situation. 致使 (…處於某種狀態)","examples":["This is going to put them out of business. 這將使他們歇業。","He was putting himself at risk. 他在把自己置於危險境地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>put</b> something <b>on</b> people or things means to cause them to have it, or to cause them to be affected by it. 把…施加給; 使受…的影響","examples":["He didn't put any pressure on her. 他並沒有給她施加任何壓力。","Be aware of the terrible strain it can put on a child when you expect the best grades. 當你期盼最佳成績時，要意識到這可能給孩子帶來的可怕壓力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> your trust, faith, or confidence <b>in</b> someone or something, you trust them or have faith or confidence in them. 把 (信任、信仰、信心等) 寄託在","examples":["He had decided long ago that he would put his trust in socialism when the time came. 他很久以前就已決定，他到時候將信仰社會主義。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> time, strength, or energy <b>into</b> an activity, you use it in doing that activity. 把 (時間、體力或精力) 用於","examples":["We're not saying that activists should put all their effort and time into party politics. 我們並不是說，積極分子們應把他們所有的精力和時間都投入到黨政工作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> money <b>into</b> a business or project, you invest money in it. 投入 (資金)","examples":["Investors should consider putting some money into an annuity. 投資者們應考慮在年金上投入一些資金。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When you <b>put</b> an idea or remark in a particular way, you express it in that way. You can use expressions like <b>to put it simply</b> and <b>to put it bluntly</b> before saying something when you want to explain how you are going to express it. 表達","examples":["I had already met Pete a couple of times through – how should I put it – friends in low places. 我已經見過皮特好幾次了，透過–怎麼說呢–底層社會的朋友們。","He admitted the security forces might have made some mistakes, as he put it. 如他所說的，他承認治安部隊可能犯了一些錯誤。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When you <b>put a question</b> <b>to</b> someone, you ask them the question. 提出 (問題)","examples":["Is this fair? Well, I put that question today to the mayor. 這公平嗎? 好吧，我今天就向市長提出那個問題。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> a case, opinion, or proposal, you explain it and list the reasons why you support or believe it. 解釋","examples":["He always put his point of view with clarity and with courage. 他一貫勇於清晰地闡釋自己的觀點。","He put the case to the Saudi foreign minister. 他向沙特外交部長解釋了此事。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> something <b>at</b> a particular value or <b>in</b> a particular category, you consider that it has that value or that it belongs in that category. 給…估 (值); 把…歸 (類)","examples":["I would put her age at about 50 or so. 我估計她的年紀大約是五十歲左右。","All the more technically advanced countries put a high value on science. 所有技術更發達的國家都高度重視科學。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> written information somewhere, you write, type, or print it there. 寫下; 用打字機打下; 印下","examples":["Mary's family was so pleased that they put an announcement in the local paper to thank them. 瑪麗的家人如此高興，以至於在當地報紙上登了一則啟事感謝他們。","I think what I put in that book is now pretty much the agenda for this country. 我認為我在那本書裡寫的正是該國目前亟待解決的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>put it to</b> someone <b>that</b> something is true, you suggest that it is true, especially when you think that they will be unwilling to admit this. 向…指出","examples":["But I put it to you that they're useless. 但我要告訴你，他們沒用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is bigger or better than several other things <b>put together</b>, you mean that it is bigger or has more good qualities than all of those other things if they are added together. 加在一起","examples":["Mary ate more than the rest of us put together. 瑪麗吃得比我們其他人加在一起還要多。"]}]}]},"shut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"關閉，合上；把……關在；<英>（使）停止運作，（使）停止營業；禁止通行，封閉"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"關閉的，關上的；<英>打烊的，停止營業的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"關閉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shut</b> something such as a door or if it <b>shuts</b>, it moves so that it fills a hole or a space. 關上; 關閉","examples":["Just make sure you shut the gate. 你務必關上那幢大門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shut</b> your eyes, you lower your eyelids so that you cannot see anything. 閉上 (眼睛)","examples":["Lucy shut her eyes so she wouldn't see it happen. 露西閉上了眼睛，以便不會看到它發生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your mouth <b>shuts</b> or if you <b>shut</b> your mouth, you place your lips firmly together. 閉上 (嘴); (嘴) 閉上","examples":["Daniel's mouth opened, and then shut again. 丹尼爾的嘴張開後又閉上了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a shop, bar, or other public building <b>shuts</b> or when someone <b>shuts</b> it, it is closed and you cannot use it until it is open again. 使停止營業; 使關門; 停止營業; 關門","examples":["There is a tendency to shut museums or shops at a moment's notice. 有一接到通知就關閉博物館或商店的趨勢。","Stores usually shut from noon-3pm, and stay open late. 商店通常都中午到下午3點關門，然後開到很晚。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shut</b> is also an adjective. 關閉的","examples":["They have warned residents to stay inside and keep their doors and windows shut. 他們已警告居民待在屋內並關好門窗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shut</b> is also an adjective. 閉合的","examples":["His eyes were shut and he seemed to have fallen asleep. 他的雙眼閉著，看上去像是已經睡著了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Shut</b> is also an adjective. 合上的","examples":["She was silent for a moment, lips tight shut, eyes distant. 她沉默了片刻，雙唇緊閉，兩眼茫然。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Shut</b> is also an adjective. 關門的","examples":["Make sure you have food to tide you over when the local shop may be shut. 在那家當地商店可能關門時，你一定要確保自己有度過難關的食物。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone tells you to <b>keep</b> your <b>mouth shut</b> about something, they are telling you not to let anyone else know about it. 保密","examples":["I don't have to tell you how important it is for you to keep your mouth shut about all this. 我不必告訴你對這件事保密有多麼重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>mouth shut</b>, you do not express your opinions about something, even though you would like to. 保持沉默","examples":["If she had kept her mouth shut she would still have her job now. 如果她當時能保持沉默，她現在還能有工作。"]}]}]},"serve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……工作，服役；端上，給……提供（餐飲）；夠……吃； 接待，服務；對……有用，滿足；（向某地或某群體）供應，提供；服刑，服勞役；<法律> 送達（傳票、令狀等）；（網球、排球等）發球；<古>開（某人）（玩笑）；產生……的效果；（軍）操作（槍炮）；（航海）捲纏（繩索）；（雄性種畜）與（雌性）交配；（基督教）在彌撒中擔任助祭"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（網球、排球等的）發球；<澳，非正式> 申斥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>serve</b> your country, an organization, or a person, you do useful work for them. 為…服務; 為…效力","examples":["It is unfair to soldiers who have served their country well for many years. 對忠心效力國家多年計程車兵們來說，這是不公平的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>serves</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing or <b>serves</b> a particular purpose, it performs a particular function, which is often not its intended function. 對…有用; 能起…作用","examples":["She ushered me into the front room, which served as her office. 她領我進入前廳，那兒用做她的辦公室了。","I really do not think that an inquiry would serve any useful purpose. 我真的認為一場諮詢不會起什麼作用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>serves</b> people or an area, it provides them with something that they need. 供應; 提供","examples":["This could mean the closure of thousands of small businesses which serve the community. 這意味著數以千計的為社群提供服務的小企業可能會關閉。","...improvements in the public water-supply system serving the Nairobi area. …內羅畢地區公共供水系統的改善。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that <b>serves</b> someone's interests benefits them. 滿足; 對…有益","examples":["The economy should be organized to serve the interests of all the people. 經濟規劃應該符合全體民眾的利益。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>serve</b> food and drinks, you give people food and drinks. 上 (菜、飲料)","examples":["Serve it with French bread. 這個與法式麵包一起上。","Serve the cakes warm. 烤餅要趁熱端上來。","Refrigerate until ready to serve. 一直冷藏到準備上桌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Serve</b> is used to indicate how much food a recipe produces. For example, a recipe that <b>serves</b> six provides enough food for six people. 足以供…人食用","examples":["Garnish with fresh herbs. Serves 4. 綴上新鮮的香草，供4人食用。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone who <b>serves</b> customers in a shop or a bar helps them and provides them with what they want to buy. 接待 (顧客)","examples":["They wouldn't serve me in any bars because I looked too young. 任何酒吧都不肯接待我，因為我看上去太年輕了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When the police or other officials <b>serve</b> someone <b>with</b> a legal order or <b>serve</b> an order <b>on</b> them, they give or send the legal order to them. 送交 (令狀/傳票)","examples":["Immigration officers tried to serve her with a deportation order. 移民局官員試圖向她交送驅逐出境令。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>serve</b> something such as a prison sentence or an apprenticeship, you spend a period of time doing it. 服 (刑); 做 (學徒)","examples":["...Leo, who is currently serving a life sentence for murder. …目前正因謀殺罪在服無期徒刑的利奧。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When you <b>serve</b> in games such as tennis and badminton, you throw up the ball or shuttlecock and hit it to start play. (網球、羽毛球等) 發球","examples":["He served 17 double faults. 他有17次雙發失誤。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>serve</b> in a particular place or as a particular official, you perform official duties, especially in the armed forces, as a civil servant, or as a politician. 服役; 任職","examples":["During the second world war he served with 92nd Airborne. 第二次世界大戰期間，他在第92空降師服役。","They have both served on the school board. 他們倆都曾在學校董事會任職。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Serve up</b> means the same as . 上 (菜、飲料)","examples":["After all, it is no use serving up TV dinners if the kids won't eat them. 歸根到底，如果孩子們不肯吃，就是端上即食快餐也沒有什麼用。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Serve</b> is also a noun. 發球","examples":["His second serve clipped the net. 他的第2次發球擦到了球網。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you describe someone's <b>serve</b>, you are indicating how well or how fast they serve a ball or shuttlecock. 發球","examples":["His powerful serve was too much for the defending champion. 他有力的發球使衛冕冠軍難以招架。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>it serves</b> someone <b>right</b> when something unpleasant happens to them, you mean that it is their own fault and you have no sympathy for them. 某人活該受懲罰","examples":["Serves her right for being so stubborn. 她這麼頑固，受到懲罰是活該。"]}]}]},"see":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"看見，看到；有視力，看得見；看（電影或電視節目）；注意到，看出；瞭解，發現；設想，預測；考慮，定奪；理解，認識到；參閱，參見；閱讀；認為，看待；看望，探訪；遇見，碰見；會見，會晤；交往；確保，查明；經歷，遭受； （地點或時間）目睹，見證；幫助（或支援）……度過；送，護送；與（對方）下同樣賭注；看（用於口語，引導注意力）；看上（see sth. in）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"主教教區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>see</b> something, you notice it using your eyes. 看見","examples":["You can't see colours at night. 你在夜間看不見顏色。","She can see, hear, touch, smell, and taste. 她看得見、聽得到、有觸覺、嗅覺和味覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> someone, you visit them or meet them. 看望; 會見","examples":["I saw him yesterday. 我昨天見了他了。","Mick wants to see you in his office right away. 米克要你馬上去他的辦公室見他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> an entertainment such as a play, movie, concert, or sports game, you watch it. 觀看","examples":["I haven't been to see a movie in 10 years. 我已有10年沒去看電影了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> that something is true or exists, you realize by observing it that it is true or exists. 看出","examples":["I could see she was lonely. 我能看出她很寂寞。","...a lot of people saw what was happening but did nothing about it. …很多人都看到發生了什麼事，但卻都袖手旁觀。","My taste has changed a bit over the years as you can see. 就像你看到的，這些年來我的品味有些改變。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> what someone means or <b>see</b> why something happened, you understand what they mean or understand why it happened. 明白","examples":["Oh, I see what you're saying. 哦，我明白你說的了。","I really don't see any reason for changing it. 我實在想不出有任何理由要改變它。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a certain thing, you have the opinion that they are that thing. 認為; 視為","examples":["She saw him as a visionary, but her father saw him as a man who couldn't make a living. 她認為他是個夢想家，但她的父親卻認為他沒有謀生的能力。","Others saw it as a betrayal. 其他人都視它為一種背叛。","As I see it, Steve has three choices open to him. 我認為，史蒂夫有3種選擇。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> a particular quality <b>in</b> someone, you believe they have that quality. If you ask what someone <b>sees</b> <b>in</b> a particular person or thing, you want to know what they find attractive about that person or thing. 看中; 欣賞","examples":["Frankly, I don't know what Paul sees in her. 坦白地說，我不知道保羅看中她什麼了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> something happening in the future, you imagine it, or predict that it will happen. 想像; 預測","examples":["A good idea, but can you see Taylor trying it? 主意很好，但是你能想像泰勒試著做嗎?"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a period of time or a person <b>sees</b> a particular change or event, it takes place during that period of time or while that person is alive. 歷經; 目睹","examples":["Yesterday saw the resignation of the chief financial officer. 昨天，首席財政長官辭職了。","He had worked with the general for three years and was sorry to see him go. 他與將軍一起共事3年，看他離去很難過。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> <b>that</b> something is done or if you <b>see</b> <b>to it that</b> it is done, you make sure that it is done. 確保","examples":["See that you take care of him. 你一定要好好照顧他。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> someone to a particular place, you accompany them to make sure that they get there safely, or to show politeness. 陪同; 護送","examples":["He didn't offer to see her to her car. 他沒有表示要送她上她的汽車。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> a lot <b>of</b> someone, you often meet each other or visit each other. 遇到; 拜訪","examples":["We used to see quite a lot of his wife, Carolyn. 我們過去經常見到他的妻子卡羅琳。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>are seeing</b> someone, you spend time with them socially, and are having a romantic or sexual relationship. 與…交往; 與…有戀情","examples":["My husband was still seeing her and he was having an affair with her. 當時我丈夫仍與她交往，並跟她有曖昧關係。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"<b>See</b> is used in books to indicate to readers that they should look at another part of the book, or at another book, because more information is given there. 參見","examples":["Surveys consistently find that men report feeling safe on the street after dark. See, for example, Hindelang and Garofalo (1978, p.127). 調查一致顯示，男性天黑後在街上感到安全。可參見如欣德朗和加羅法洛的著作(1978年，127頁)。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You can use <b>see</b> in expressions to do with finding out information. For example, if you say \"<b>I'll see what's happening</b>,\" you mean that you intend to find out what is happening. 察看","examples":["Let me just see what the next song is. 讓我看看下一首歌是什麼。","Every time we asked our mother, she said, \"Well, see what your father says.\" 每次我們問母親，她總是說: \"喔，看看你父親怎麼說。\""]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You can use <b>see</b> in expressions in which you promise to try and help someone. For example, if you say \"<b>I'll see if I can do it</b>,\" you mean that you will try to do the thing concerned. 試試看","examples":["I'll see if I can call her for you. 我試試看能不能幫你叫她來。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"Some writers use <b>see</b> in expressions such as <b>we saw</b> and <b>as we have seen</b> to refer to something that has already been explained or described. (如上所) 述","examples":["We saw in Chapter 16 how annual cash budgets are produced. 在第16章我們已經瞭解了年度現金預算是如何制定的。","Laws are often not clear, as we saw in Chapter 1. 正如第1章中所述，法律往往是含糊不清的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>seeing that</b> or <b>seeing as</b> to introduce a reason for what you are saying. 既然","examples":["Seeing as Mr. Moreton is a doctor, I assume he is reasonably intelligent. 既然莫爾頓先生是個醫生，我猜想他應該相當聰明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you try to make someone <b>see sense</b> or <b>see reason</b>, you try to make them realize that they are wrong or are being stupid. 認識到錯誤; 明白事理","examples":["He was hopeful that by sitting together they could both see sense and live as good neighbours. 他希望透過坐在一起溝通，他們雙方都能認識到自己的錯誤，成為和睦相處的好鄰居。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I see</b>\" to indicate that you understand what someone is telling you. 我明白","examples":["\"He came home in my car.\"—\"I see.\" “他坐我的車回的家。”—“哦，是這樣。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People say \"<b>I'll see</b>\" or \"<b>We'll see</b>\" to indicate that they do not intend to make a decision immediately, and will decide later. 看看再說","examples":["We'll see. It's a possibility. 看看再說吧，這有可能。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People say \"<b>let me see</b>\" or \"<b>let's see</b>\" when they are trying to remember something, or are trying to find something. 讓我想一想; 讓我看看","examples":["Let's see, they're six – no, make that five hours ahead of us. 讓我想想，他們比我們早了6個小時–不，就算是6個小時吧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say \"<b>you see</b>\" when you are explaining something to someone, to encourage them to listen and understand. (用於解釋時) 你瞧","examples":["Well, you see, you shouldn't really feel that way about it. 好了，你瞧，你真的不該有那種感覺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"\"<b>See you</b>,\" \"<b>be seeing you</b>,\" and \"<b>see you later</b>\" are ways of saying goodbye to someone when you expect to meet them again soon. 再見; 回頭見","examples":["\"Talk to you later.\"—\"All right. See you love.\" “以後再聊”。—“好的。回頭見，親愛的。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say \"<b>You'll see</b>\" to someone if they do not agree with you about what you think will happen in the future, and you believe that you will be proved right. 你等著瞧吧","examples":["The thrill wears off after a few years of marriage. You'll see. 那股興奮勁兒結婚幾年後就會慢慢消失，你等著瞧吧。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the diocese of a bishop, or the place within it where his cathedral or procathedral is situated 主教教區; 主教駐地","examples":[]}]}]},"spend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"度過，花（時間）；花（錢），花費；消耗，用盡（精力等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"花費，開銷"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"預算"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>spend</b> money, you pay money for things that you want or need. 花 (錢)","examples":["By the end of the holiday I had spent all my money. 到那個假期結束時我已經花光了我所有的錢。","Businessmen spend enormous amounts advertising their products. 商人們花鉅額資金為他們的產品做廣告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>spend</b> time or energy doing something, you use your time or effort doing it. 花 (時間、精力)","examples":["Engineers spend much time and energy developing brilliant solutions. 工程師們花大量時間和精力開發出色的解決方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>spend</b> a period of time in a place, you stay there for a period of time. 度過 (一段時間)","examples":["We spent the night in a hotel. 我們在一家賓館過了夜。"]}]}]},"spell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一段時間；（疾病突然的）一次發作；咒語，符咒，著魔；魅力，魔力；輪班；<澳>休息期；（板球）（一個投手的）一輪投球時間；木片"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拼寫，拼綴出（單詞）；拼作，拼成；招致，意味著（通常指壞事）；具有……的顯著特徵；替換，頂替；<澳>稍事休息"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>spell</b> a word, you write or speak each letter in the word in the correct order. 拼寫; 拼讀","examples":["He gave his name and then helpfully spelled it. 他說出了他的名字，然後又熱心地把它拼讀了出來。","How do you spell \"potato?\" “”怎麼拼寫？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who can <b>spell</b> knows the correct order of letters in words. 寫; 寫字","examples":["It's shocking how students can't spell these days. 如今學生居然不會寫字真讓人震驚。","He can't even spell his own name. 他甚至不會寫自己的名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>spells</b> a particular outcome, often an unpleasant one, it suggests that this will be the result. 預示 (通常不好的結果)","examples":["If the irrigation plan goes ahead, it could spell disaster for the birds. 如果該灌溉計劃繼續的話，這對鳥類可能預示著災難。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spell out</b> means the same as . 拼寫; 拼讀","examples":["If I don't know a word, I ask them to spell it out for me. 假如我不知道某個詞，我請他們替我拼寫出來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spell</b> <b>of</b> a particular type of weather or a particular activity is a short period of time during which this type of weather or activity occurs. (某種天氣或活動的) 短暫發生期","examples":["There has been a long spell of dry weather. 乾旱天氣已持續很長一段時間了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spell</b> is a situation in which events are controlled by a magical power. 魔","examples":["They say she died after a witch cast a spell on her. 人們說一個女巫對她施了魔後她就死了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a period or tour of duty after which one person or group relieves another 輪班的時間","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to take over from (a person) for an interval of time; relieve temporarily 在間歇期接替(某人); 暫時換崗","examples":[]}]}]},"teach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"教授，講授；教會，訓練；教育，使懂得（情理）；<非正式>勸誡，教訓"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>教師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>teach</b> someone something, you give them instructions so that they know about it or how to do it. 教","examples":["She taught me fractions and counting. 他教我分數和計算。","George had taught him how to ride a horse. 喬治曾教過他騎馬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>teach</b> someone something means to make them think, feel, or act in a new or different way. 教導","examples":["Their daughter's death had taught him humility. 他們女兒的死使他懂得了做人要謙遜。","He taught his followers that they could all be members of the kingdom of God. 他教導他的信徒說他們都會成為天國的成員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>teach</b> or <b>teach</b> a subject, you help students to learn about it by explaining it or showing them how to do it, usually as a job at a school or college. 教 (某一科目); 教書","examples":["Ingrid is currently teaching mathematics at the high school. 英格麗德目前在那所中學教數學。","She taught English to Japanese business people. 她教日本商人英語。","She has taught for 34 years. 她教書已有34年。"]}]}]},"speak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"談話，交談；說，講述；（會）講（某種語言）；發言，演講；（不用言語）表明，顯示；代表……講話，充當……的代言人；（發言或寫作中）提到，談及；以……方式說；表達（思想、觀點）；（樂器或其他物體）發出特有的響聲；（獵狗）吠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>speak</b>, you use your voice in order to say something. 說話","examples":["He tried to speak, but for once, his voice had left him. 他試圖說話，但這一次，他已說不出聲。","I rang the hotel and spoke to Louie. 我打電話給賓館，跟路易通了話。","She cried when she spoke of Oliver. 她提起奧利弗時哭了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>speaks</b> <b>to</b> a group of people, they make a speech. 演講; 發言","examples":["When speaking to the seminar Mr. Franklin spoke of his experience, gained on a recent visit to Trinidad. 在研討會上發言時，富蘭克林先生談到了他最近一次在特立尼達訪問時所獲得的經驗。","He's determined to speak at the Democratic Convention. 他決心在民主黨大會上發言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>speak for</b> a group of people, you make their views and demands known, or represent them. 為…說話; 代表…發言","examples":["He said it was the job of the Church to speak for the underprivileged. 他說為弱勢群體說話是教會的職責。","I speak for all 7,000 members of our organization. 我代表我們組織的全體7000名成員發言。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"People sometimes mention something that has been written by saying what the author <b>speaks of</b>. 談及","examples":["Throughout the book Liu speaks of the abuse of Party power. 劉在全書中都談到黨權的濫用。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something <b>speaks for</b> <b>itself</b>, you mean that its meaning or quality is so obvious that it does not need explaining or pointing out. (自己) 會說話; (本身) 能說明問題","examples":["...the figures speak for themselves – bleak prospects at home and a worsening outlook for exports. …這些數字本身就能說明問題–國內暗淡的前景和日益糟糕的出口展望。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"口頭的","examples":["...a marked decline in the standards of written and spoken English. …書面和口頭英語標準的明顯下降。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>speak</b> a foreign language, you know the language and are able to have a conversation in it. 說 (某種語言)","examples":["He doesn't speak English. 他不說英語。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>are</b> <b>not</b> <b>speaking</b>, they no longer talk to each other because they have argued. (吵架之後) 相互說話","examples":["He is not speaking to his mother because of her friendship with his ex-wife. 他因母親跟其前妻的友誼而不跟母親說話了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is spoken for</b> or <b>has been spoken for</b>, someone has claimed them or asked for them, so no one else can have them. 已有人認領的; 已有人請求過的","examples":["She'd probably drop some comment about her \"fiancé\" into the conversation so that he'd think she was already spoken for. 她很可能會在交談中故意提到她的“未婚夫”，這樣他就會知道她已名花有主了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>speak well of</b> someone or <b>speak highly of</b> someone, you say good things about them. If you <b>speak ill of</b> someone, you criticize them. 說某人好話/壞話","examples":["Both spoke highly of the Russian president. 雙方都高度評價了那位俄羅斯總統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>so to speak</b> to draw attention to the fact that you are describing or referring to something in a way that may be amusing or unusual rather than completely accurate. 可以說","examples":["I ought not to tell you but I will, since you're in the family, so to speak. 我不該告訴你，但我會告訴你，因為說來你也是這個家庭的一員。"]}]}]},"understand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"理解，懂得；瞭解，明白（某事物）；諒解，體諒；得知，聽說；預設，默許；領會，推斷出；解釋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>understand</b> someone or <b>understand</b> what they are saying, you know what they mean. 明白 (某人的話的意思)","examples":["I think you heard and also understand me. 我想你聽到了我的話，而且也明白我的意思。","I don't understand what you are talking about. 我不明白你在說什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>understand</b> a language, you know what someone is saying when they are speaking that language. 懂 (某種語言)","examples":["I couldn't read or understand a word of Yiddish, so I asked him to translate. 我完全不懂意第緒語，所以請他翻譯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>understand</b> someone means to know how they feel and why they behave in the way that they do. 理解 (某人)","examples":["It would be nice to have someone who really understood me, a friend. 有個真正理解我的人，一個朋友，就太好啦。","Trish had not exactly understood his feelings. 特里希並沒有確切地理解他的感受。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that you <b>understand</b> something when you know why or how it happens. 明白 (某事)","examples":["They are too young to understand what is going on. 他們太小，不明白在發生什麼事。","She didn't understand why the TV was kept out of reach of the patients. 她那時不明白為什麼不讓病人看電視。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>understand</b> that something is the case, you think it is true because you have heard or read that it is. You can say that something <b>is understood</b> to be the case to mean that people generally think it is true. 知道; 聽說; 獲悉","examples":["We understand that she's in the studio recording her second album. 我們得知她正在錄音室裡錄製她的第2張專輯。","As I understand it, she has a house in the city. 據我所知，她在市裡有座房子。","The management is understood to be very unwilling to agree to this request. 據說管理層很不願意答應這項要求。"]}]}]},"run":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跑，奔跑；參加（賽跑），舉行（比賽）；跑壘，持球跑動進攻；奔忙，趕快去；管理，經營，使用（車輛）；（使）運轉，操作；刊登，播放；（使）行駛；（使）移動，揉擦；闖紅燈；（使）流動，流淌；掉色，滲色；變成，變得；達到（一定數量或比率）；（對……）進行（測試或檢驗）；參加競選；（連褲襪、長統襪）抽絲，脫線；（使）延伸；（感覺或想法）掠過，迅速傳遍；包含（某種詞語、內容等）；持續，延續；偷運，走私；印刷；（特徵）共有，世代相傳（run in）；<美>（物品，行動）花費（某人）（特定數額的錢）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跑步，賽跑；旅程，航程；一系列（成功或失敗）；連續上演（或放映）；嘗試，努力；額定產量；拋售（美元、英鎊等）；爭購，擠兌；滑道，路徑；（板球或棒球中的）得分；使用自由，出入自由（the run of）；競選；普通人，普通事物；飼養場；急奏，走句；順子；<非正式>腹瀉（the runs）；<美>（長統襪或連褲襪的）抽絲；（油漆或類似物刷得過厚引起的）掛流，小溪；（航海）船尾端部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>run</b>, you move more quickly than when you walk, for example because you are in a hurry to get somewhere, or for exercise. 跑","examples":["I excused myself and ran back to the telephone. 我道了歉，跑回去接電話。","He ran the last block to the White House with two cases of gear. 他帶著兩箱工具跑過最後一個街區到了白宮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>runs</b> in a race, they run in competition with other people. 參加…賽跑; 賽跑","examples":["...when I was running in the New York Marathon. …當我正參加紐約馬拉松賽跑時。","He ran a tremendous race. 他參加了一場大規模賽跑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a horse <b>runs</b> in a race or when its owner <b>runs</b> it, it competes in a race. 使 (馬) 參加比賽; (馬) 參加比賽","examples":["He was overruled by the owner, Peter Bolton, who insisted on Cool Ground running in the Gold Cup. 他的意見被堅持讓酷地參加金盃賽的主人彼得•博爾頓否決了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> a wire or tube somewhere, you attach it or pull it from, to, or across a particular place. 鋪設 (電線、管道等)","examples":["Our host ran a long extension cord out from the house and set up a screen and a projector. 我們的主人從那所房子裡牽出了一條長的延長導線，安置了一塊螢幕和一個投影儀。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> your hand or an object <b>through</b> something, you move your hand or the object through it. 移動","examples":["He laughed and ran his fingers through his hair. 他大笑了並用手指梳理他的頭髮。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> something through a machine, process, or series of tests, you make it go through the machine, process, or tests. 執行","examples":["They have gathered the best statistics they can find and run them through their own computers. 他們已經蒐集了他們所能找到的最佳資料並將其在他們自己的電腦裡執行。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> something such as a business or an activity, you are in charge of it or you organize it. 經營; 管理","examples":["His stepfather ran a prosperous paint business. 他的繼父曾經營一家生意興旺的塗料公司。","...a well-run, profitable organization. …一家經營很好的贏利機構。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> an experiment, computer program, or other process, or start it <b>running</b>, you start it and let it continue. 進行; 執行","examples":["He ran a lot of tests and it turned out I had an infection called mycoplasma. 他進行了許多化驗，結果證明我感染了支原體病毒。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When a machine <b>is running</b> or when you <b>are running</b> it, it is switched on and is working. 使 (機器) 運轉; (機器) 運轉","examples":["We told him to wait out front with the engine running. 我們告訴他在入口外等候，不要熄火。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> someone somewhere in a car, you drive them there. (開車) 送","examples":["Could you run me up to Baltimore? 你能開車送我去巴爾的摩嗎？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> water, or if you <b>run</b> a faucet or a bath, you cause water to flow from a faucet. 從水管放 (水)","examples":["She went to the sink and ran water into her empty glass. 她走到了洗滌槽邊，往空玻璃杯裡灌水。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When you <b>run</b> a cassette or videotape or when it <b>runs</b>, it moves through the machine as the machine operates. 播放","examples":["Leaphorn pushed the play button again, ran the tape, pushed stop, pushed rewind. 利福恩又按下播放按鈕，播放了磁帶，接著按了停止鍵，然後又按下倒帶鍵。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"When newspapers or magazines <b>run</b> a particular item or story or if it <b>runs</b>, it is published or printed. 刊登; 發表","examples":["The New Orleans Times-Picayune ran a series of four scathing editorials entitled \"The Choice of Our Lives.\" 《新奧爾良時代花絮報》連續刊登了題為“我們生活的選擇”的4篇尖刻的社論。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>are running</b> a temperature or a fever, you have a high temperature because you are ill. 患","examples":["The little girl is running a fever and she needs help. 這個小女孩正在發燒，她需要幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something long, such as a road, <b>runs</b> in a particular direction, you are describing its course or position. You can also say that something <b>runs</b> the length or width of something else. (道路等) 延伸","examples":["...the sun-dappled trail which ran through the beech woods. …一條穿過山毛櫸樹林的陽光斑駁的小路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>runs</b> <b>for</b> office in an election, they take part as a candidate. 競選","examples":["It was only last February that he announced he would run for president. 直到去年2月他才宣佈自己將競選總統。","It is no easy job to run against John Glenn, Ohio's Democratic senator. 與俄亥俄州民主黨參議員約翰•格倫競選絕非易事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about how a system, an organization, or someone's life <b>is running</b>, you are saying how well it is operating or progressing. 運作; 運轉","examples":["Officials in charge of the camps say the system is now running extremely smoothly. 負責營房的官員說這一體制目前運作得相當順利。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A machine or equipment that <b>runs</b> <b>on</b> or <b>off</b> a particular source of energy functions using that source of energy. 運轉","examples":["The buses run on diesel. 這些公共汽車使用的是柴油。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you say that vehicles such as trains and buses <b>run</b> from one place to another, you mean they regularly travel along that route. 行駛","examples":["A shuttle bus runs frequently between the inn and the country club. 一輛區間往返公共汽車頻繁地往來於小客棧與鄉村俱樂部之間。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> over or down to a place that is quite near, you drive there. 駕車去","examples":["I'll run over to Short Mountain and check on Mrs. Adams. 我將開車去肖特山看看亞當斯夫人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a liquid <b>runs</b> in a particular direction, it flows in that direction. (液體) 流","examples":["Tears were running down her cheeks. 淚水當時正沿著她的臉頰流下。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a faucet or a bath <b>is running</b>, water is coming out of a faucet. 流水","examples":["The kitchen sink had been stopped up and the faucet left running, so water spilled over onto the floor. 那廚房的洗滌槽堵塞了，而水龍頭在那裡流水，所以水溢滿流到了地板上。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If your nose <b>is running</b>, liquid is flowing out of it, usually because you have a cold. 流鼻涕","examples":["Timothy was crying, mostly from exhaustion, and his nose was running. 蒂莫西在哭，主要是因為太累了，而且在流鼻涕。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a surface <b>is running</b> <b>with</b> a liquid, that liquid is flowing down it. 流下","examples":["After an hour he realized he was completely running with sweat. 一個小時後，他發現自己已是大汗淋漓。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If the dye in some cloth or the ink on some paper <b>runs</b>, it comes off or spreads when the cloth or paper gets wet. 滲開","examples":["The ink had run on the wet paper. 墨跡在那張溼紙上滲開了。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If a feeling <b>runs</b> <b>through</b> your body or a thought <b>runs</b> <b>through</b> your mind, you experience it or think it quickly. (感覺) 傳遍; (念頭) 掠過","examples":["She felt a surge of excitement run through her. 她感到一陣激動傳遍全身。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a feeling or noise <b>runs</b> <b>through</b> a group of people, it spreads among them. (感受、噪音等) 傳開","examples":["A buzz of excitement ran through the crowd. 一陣興奮的嗡嗡聲在人群中蔓延開來。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If a theme or feature <b>runs</b> <b>through</b> something such as someone's actions or writing, it is present in all of it. 貫穿","examples":["Another thread running through this series is the role of doctors in the treatment of the mentally ill. 貫穿這部連續劇的另一主線是醫生們在心理疾病患者的治療過程中的作用。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If an amount <b>is running</b> at a particular level, it is at that level. 處於 (某一水平)","examples":["Today's figures show inflation running at 10.9 percent. 今天的資料顯示通貨膨脹率為10.9%。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If a play, event, or legal contract <b>runs</b> for a particular period of time, it lasts for that period of time. (戲劇、事件、法律合同等) 延續","examples":["It pleased critics but ran for only three months on Broadway. 它得到了評論家的好評，但在百老匯只上演了3個月。","The contract was to run from 1992 to 2020. 該合同從1992年至2020年有效。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is running</b> late, they have taken more time than had been planned. If they <b>are running</b> on time or ahead of time, they have taken the time planned or less than the time planned. 進展","examples":["Tell her I'll call her back later, I'm running late again. 告訴她我待會兒再給她回電話，我又要晚了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>run</b> is a time when you move somewhere on foot more quickly than when you walk, usually for exercise. 跑步","examples":["After a six-mile run, Jackie returns home for a substantial breakfast. 6英里跑之後，傑基回家吃一頓豐盛的早餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>run for</b> office is an attempt to be elected to office. 競選","examples":["He was already preparing his run for the presidency. 他已經在為總統競選做準備。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>run</b> is a trip somewhere. 出行","examples":["...doing the morning school run. …早上去學校。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>run</b> of a play or television programme is the period of time during which performances are given or programmes are shown. (戲劇或電視節目的) 演出期; 播放期","examples":["The show will transfer to Broadway on October 9, after a month's run in Philadelphia. 這出戏在費城為期一個月的演出之後，將於10月9日轉到百老匯上演。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>run</b> <b>of</b> successes or failures is a series of successes or failures. 一連串 (成功或失敗)","examples":["The team is haunted by a run of low scores. 這個隊被一連串的低分所折磨。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>run</b> of a product is the amount that a company or factory decides to produce at one time. (產品的) 批次","examples":["Wayne plans to increase the print run to 1,000. 韋恩計劃將印量增加到1千冊。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In baseball or cricket, a <b>run</b> is a score of one, which is made by players running between marked places on the field after hitting the ball. (棒球或板球比賽中跑動得到的) 一分","examples":["The Padres scored four runs off Terry Adams in the last 2 innings. 在最後2個回合中，教士隊力挫特里•亞當斯，跑壘得4分。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone gives you <b>the run of</b> a place, they give you permission to go where you like in it and use it as you wish. (對某地的) 使用權","examples":["He had the run of the house and the pool. 他曾有這座房子和游泳池的使用權。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If there is a <b>run on</b> something, a lot of people want to buy it or get it at the same time. 搶購; 爭先獲取","examples":["A run on the dollar has killed off hopes of a rate cut. 對美元的擠兌使降息徹底無望了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>run</b> is a hole or torn part in a woman's stocking or tights, where some the vertical threads have broken, leaving only the horizontal threads. (長筒襪或連褲襪的) 抽絲","examples":[]},{"num":"11.","zh":"A ski <b>run</b> or bobsled <b>run</b> is a course or route that has been designed for skiing or for riding in a bobsled. (滑雪或乘雪橇的) 滑道","examples":["...an avalanche on Colorado's highest ski run. …一次在科羅拉多州最高的滑雪道上發生的雪崩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> someone <b>a close second</b>, or <b>run a close second</b>, you almost beat them in a race or competition. (比賽中) 以極小劣勢位居第二","examples":["While \"Nightly\" has led in the ratings all season, \"World News Tonight\" is running a close second. 《晚間新聞》全年收視率名列前茅，而《今夜世界新聞》緊隨其後。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a river or well <b>runs dry</b>, it no longer has any water in it. If an oil well <b>runs dry</b>, it no longer produces any oil. (河流、井) 乾涸; (油井) 枯竭","examples":["Streams had run dry for the first time in memory. 溪流在記憶中第一次乾涸了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a source of information or money <b>runs dry</b>, no more information or money can be obtained from it. (資訊或資金) 枯竭","examples":["Three days into production, the kitty had run dry. 投產3天，資金已經用完了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a characteristic <b>runs in</b> someone's <b>family</b>, it often occurs in members of that family, in different generations. 在某人的家族中遺傳","examples":["The insanity which ran in his family haunted him. 家族世代相襲的精神病令他惴惴不安。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>make a run for it</b> or if you <b>run for it</b>, you run away in order to escape from someone or something. 逃離","examples":["A helicopter hovered overhead as one of the gang made a run for it. 那夥人中的一個逃跑的時候，一架直升飛機在頭頂上空盤旋。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If people's feelings <b>are running high</b>, they are very angry, concerned, or excited. (情緒) 高漲","examples":["Feelings there have been running high in the wake of last week's killing. 緊隨上週殺人事件之後，那裡已是群情激憤。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you talk about what will happen <b>in the long run</b>, you are saying what you think will happen over a long period of time in the future. If you talk about what will happen <b>in the short run</b>, you are saying what you think will happen in the near future. 從長期/短期來看","examples":["Sometimes expensive drugs or other treatments can be economical in the long run. 有時昂貴的藥物或其他療法從長遠來看是省錢的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone could <b>give</b> someone else <b>a run for</b> their <b>money</b>, you mean you think they are almost as good as the other person. 幾乎比得上某人","examples":["...a youngster who even now could give Meryl Streep a run for her money. …一位現在就幾乎能與梅里爾•斯特里普相媲美的年輕人。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone is <b>on the run</b>, they are trying to escape or hide from someone such as the police or an enemy. 在逃","examples":["Fifteen-year-old Danny is on the run from a juvenile detention centre. 15歲的丹尼從少年犯拘留所逃了出來。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone is <b>on the run</b>, they are being severely defeated in a contest or competition. 慘敗","examples":["I knew I had him on the run. 我知道我已打得他落花流水。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>are running short</b> <b>of</b> something or <b>running low</b> <b>on</b> something, you do not have much of it left. If a supply of something <b>is running short</b> or <b>running low</b>, there is not much of it left. 所剩無幾","examples":["Government forces are running short of ammunition and fuel. 政府軍所剩彈藥和燃料已不多。"]}]}]},"weigh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"稱，稱……的重量；重，有……重；認真考慮，權衡；具有重要性，影響；起（錨），啟航；使煩惱，使憂慮；斟酌（字句）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（航海）（船）在航行中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>weighs</b> a particular amount, this amount is how heavy they are. 重量為","examples":["It weighs nearly 27 kilos (about 65 pounds). 它重量接近27公斤（約65磅）。","This little ball of gold weighs a quarter of an ounce. 這個小金球重0.25盎司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>weigh</b> something or someone, you measure how heavy they are. 稱 (重量)","examples":["The scales can be used to weigh other items such as parcels. 這檯秤可以用來稱量包裹等其他物品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>weigh</b> the facts about a situation, you consider them very carefully before you make a decision, especially by comparing the various facts involved. 權衡","examples":["She weighed her options. 她在各種選擇間權衡斟酌。","He is weighing the possibility of filing criminal charges against the doctor. 他在權衡向這位醫生提起刑事訴訟的可能性。"]}]}]},"sit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"坐下，就座；能容納，可坐（……人）；為……做模特；<美>（比賽）不用（某選手）；（狗等動物）蹲坐；處在，坐落在； 擔任職務，當委員；開會，開庭；<英>參加（考試）；照看小孩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"坐的一段時間；<古>（衣服的）合身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are sitting</b> somewhere, for example, in a chair, your bottom is resting on the chair and the upper part of your body is upright. 坐","examples":["Mother was sitting in her chair in the kitchen. 媽媽正坐在廚房的椅子上。","They had been sitting watching television. 他們一直坐著看電視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>sit</b> somewhere, you lower your body until you are sitting on something. (在某處) 坐下","examples":["He set the cases against a wall and sat on them. 他把箱子靠在牆上，然後坐在上面。","Eva pulled over a chair and sat beside her husband. 伊娃拽過一張椅子，在她丈夫身邊坐下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>sit</b> <b>on</b> a committee or other official group, you are a member of it. 擔任…的成員","examples":["He was asked to sit on numerous committees. 他應邀擔任許多委員會的委員。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a legislature, court, or other official body <b>sits</b>, it officially carries out its work. (立法院) 開會; (法院) 開庭","examples":["The court sits under tight security in a former museum. 法院在一所舊時的博物館開庭，保安措施很嚴密。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sit down</b> means the same as . 坐下 (同 )(sit)","examples":["I sat down, stunned. 我坐了下來，大吃一驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>sit</b> someone <b>down</b> somewhere means to  them there. 使坐下","examples":["She helped him out of the water and sat him down on the rock. 她把他從水裡拉出來，讓他坐在岩石上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sit</b> someone somewhere, you tell them to sit there or put them in a sitting position. 使坐下; 使就位","examples":["He used to sit me on his lap. 他過去常常讓我坐在他的腿上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sit tight</b>, you remain in the same place or situation and do not take any action, usually because you are waiting for something to happen. 留在原地不動; 不採取任何行動","examples":["Sit tight. I'll be right back. 別慌張，我馬上回來。"]}]}]},"think":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"認為，以為；明白（用於問句表氣憤、吃驚）；覺得；考慮，思考；想出，想象；料想，預料；想要，打算；想起，記得；琢磨，尋思；對……評價（很高）；為……著想；想來，想想看；所指的是；具有某種思維方式；只想，對……著迷；邊想邊說出聲來，自言自語"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"想，思索，思考"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"思想的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> that something is the case, you believe that it is the case. 認為","examples":["I certainly think there should be a ban on tobacco advertising. 我確實認為應該禁止香菸廣告。","A generation ago, it was thought that babies born this small could not survive. 在上一代以前，人們認為這麼小的新生兒是沒法存活的。","Tell me, what do you think of my theory? 告訴我，你認為我的理論怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>think</b> that something is true or will happen, you mean that you have the impression that it is true or will happen, although you are not certain of the facts. 覺得","examples":["Nora thought he was seventeen years old. 諾拉覺得他有17歲。","The storm is thought to be responsible for as many as four deaths. 這場暴風雨據信造成多達4人死亡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> in a particular way, you have those general opinions or attitudes. 考慮","examples":["You were probably brought up to think like that. 你可能從小就被教成那樣來考慮問題的。","If you think as I do, vote as I do. 如果你考慮問題和我一樣，就和我投一樣的票。","I don't blame you for thinking that way. 我不怪你那樣想。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> in a particular way, you consider things, solve problems, or make decisions in this way, for example, because of your job or your background. (以某種方式) 考慮","examples":["To make the computer work at full capacity, the programmer has to think like the machine. 為了使計算機能充分發揮作用，程式設計師必須像機器那樣思考。","Why do they think the way they do? 為什麼他們這麼想？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> <b>of</b> something, it comes into your mind or you remember it. 想到","examples":["Nobody could think of anything to say. 誰也想不出什麼話說。","I was trying to think what else we had to do. 我在努力想我們還得做些什麼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>are thinking</b> something at a particular moment, you have words or ideas in your mind without saying them out loud. 心想","examples":["She must be sick, Tatiana thought. 她一定是病了，塔蒂亞娜心想。","I remember thinking how lovely he looked. 我記得曾在心裡想過他看起來有多麼可愛。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>think of</b> someone or something <b>as</b> having a particular quality or purpose, you regard them as having this quality or purpose. 認為 (某人或某物具有某種特性或功能)","examples":["We all thought of him as a father. 我們都當他是一位父親。","He thinks of it as his home. 他把這兒當作自己的家。","I wouldn't have thought him capable of it. 我不會想到他能幹這事。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> a lot <b>of</b> someone or something, you admire them very much or think they are very good. 對…評價 (高)","examples":["To tell the truth, I don't think much of psychiatrists. 說實話，我認為精神病醫生不怎麼樣。","Everyone in my family thought very highly of him. 我們家的所有人都非常欽佩他。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>think</b> when you are commenting on something which you did or experienced in the past and which now seems surprising, foolish, or shocking to you. 想想看 (用於評論過去做過或經歷的事，現在看來令人驚訝、愚蠢或荒唐)","examples":["To think I left you alone in a strange place. 想想我居然把你留在一個陌生的地方。","When I think of how you've behaved and the trouble you've caused! 想想你的行為，還有你惹的麻煩！"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>think</b> about ideas or problems, you make a mental effort to consider them. 思考","examples":["She closed her eyes for a moment, trying to think. 她閉了一會兒眼，想好好思考一下。","I have often thought about this problem. 我經常思考這個問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>think of</b> an idea, you make a mental effort and use your imagination and intelligence to create it or develop it. 想出","examples":["He thought of another way of making electricity. 他想出另一種發電的方法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>think</b> <b>of</b> someone or <b>about</b> someone, you show consideration for them and pay attention to their needs. 為…著想","examples":["I'm only thinking of you. 我只是在為你著想。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are thinking of</b> or <b>are thinking about</b> taking a particular course of action, you are considering it as a possible course of action. 考慮 (採取某行動)","examples":["Martin was thinking of taking legal action against Zuckerman. 馬丁正考慮起訴朱克曼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that you <b>are thinking of</b> a particular aspect or subject, in order to introduce an example or explain more exactly what you are talking about. 所指的是 (用於引出例子或進一步解釋)","examples":["The parts of the enterprise which are scientifically the most exciting are unlikely to be militarily useful. I am thinking here of the development of new kinds of lasers. 這份計劃中，從科學角度看最讓人興奮的部分在軍事上卻可能無用。我指的是新型鐳射開發。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>think</b> in questions where you are expressing your anger or shock at someone's behaviour. 想 (用於問句，表示生氣或震驚)","examples":["What were you thinking of? You shouldn't steal. 你當時在想什麼？你不該偷東西。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Think</b> is also a noun. 思考","examples":["I'll have a think about that. 我會就那件事有所考慮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>come to think of it</b>, <b>when you think about it</b>, or <b>thinking about it</b>, when you mention something that you have suddenly remembered or realized. 想起來了","examples":["He was her distant relative, as was everyone else on the island, come to think of it. 想起來了，他和島上的其他人一樣都是她的遠親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use \"<b>I think</b>\" as a way of being polite when you are explaining or suggesting to someone what you want to do, or when you are accepting or refusing an offer. 我想 (用於委婉地表達想法或表示接受或拒絕)","examples":["I think I'll go home and have a shower. 我想我要回家沖澡了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use \"<b>I think</b>\" in conversations or speeches to make your statements and opinions sound less forceful, rude, or direct. 我認為 (用於對話或演說中，使陳述聽起來委婉些)","examples":["Thanks, but I think I can handle it. 謝謝，不過我認為我能處理這件事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>just think</b> when you feel excited, fascinated, or shocked by something, and you want the listener to feel the same. 想像一下 (用於表示興奮、著迷或震驚，並想將這種感覺傳給聽者)","examples":["Just think; tomorrow we shall walk out of this place and leave it all behind us forever. 想像一下，明天我們就要走出這地方，並且永遠地離開。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>think again</b> <b>about</b> an action or decision, you consider it very carefully, often with the result that you change your mind and decide to do things differently. 重新考慮","examples":["It has forced politicians to think again about the wisdom of trying to evacuate refugees. 這已迫使政客們重新考慮試圖疏散難民是否明智。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>think nothing of</b> doing something that other people might consider difficult, strange, or wrong, you consider it to be easy or normal. 覺得…沒什麼了不起","examples":["I thought nothing of betting $1,000 on a horse. 我覺得在一匹馬上花$1000的賭注沒什麼了不起的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something happens and you <b>think nothing of it</b>, you do not pay much attention to it or think of it as strange or important, although later you realise that it is. 對…不在意; 不覺得…奇怪","examples":["When she went off to see her parents for the weekend I thought nothing of it. 她週末去看她的父母時，我沒覺得有什麼奇怪的。"]}]}]},"cannot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"情態動詞 can 的否定式：不能，無法，不可能；不可以，不允許；用於 cannot help doing、cannot help but、cannot but 等結構，表示“不得不，禁不住，忍不住”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cannot</b> is the negative form of . (can)的否定式","examples":[]}]}]},"shall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"aux.","zh":"將要，將會（同I和we連用，表示將來）； ……好嗎？要不要……？（用於主動提供幫助、建議或詢問意見）；必須，一定（表示決心、命令或指示）；可以（與“you”連用，用以告知某人能做某事或擁有想要的東西）；應，必須（用於法律、規則）；應該，就會（表示可能的結果或後果）；（用於 look forward to 和 hope 之類的動詞前表示語氣的委婉）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>shall</b> with \"I\" and \"we\" in questions in order to make offers or suggestions, or to ask for advice. 可以 (用於疑問句中“)(I)(”和“)(we)(”前，用以提供建議或徵求意見)","examples":["Shall I get the keys? 我拿鑰匙可以嗎？","Well, shall we go? 那，我們走好嗎？","Let's have a nice little stroll, shall we? 咱們去好好散散步，好嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>shall</b>, usually with \"I\" and \"we,\" when you are referring to something that you intend to do, or when you are referring to something that you are sure will happen to you in the future. 將 (與“)(I)(”和“)(we)(”連用，表示意欲做某事或將要發生的事)","examples":["We shall be landing in Paris in sixteen minutes, exactly on time. 我們將在16分鐘後準時在巴黎降落。","I shall know more next month, I hope. 我希望下個月我將知道更多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>shall</b> with \"I\" or \"we\" during a speech or piece of writing to say what you are going to discuss or explain later. 將 (與“)(I)(”和“)(we)(”連用，表示將要論及或解釋的內容)","examples":["In Chapter 3, I shall describe some of the documentation that I gathered. 在第3章，我將講述我所蒐集到的一些文獻資料。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>shall</b> to indicate that something must happen, usually because of a rule or law. You use <b>shall not</b> to indicate that something must not happen. 將 (指按規定或規律一定會發生)","examples":["The president shall hold office for five years. 總統將任職5年。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>shall</b>, usually with \"you,\" when you are telling someone that they will be able to do or have something they want. 可以 (與“)(you)(”連用，用以告知某人能做某事或擁有想要的東西)","examples":["Very well, if you want to go, go you shall. 很好，如果你想走的話，你可以走了。"]}]}]},"write":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"寫作，編寫；寫道；寫信；書寫，寫字；譜寫（音樂作品）；編寫（計算機程式）；將（計算機中的）資料寫入（磁碟或其他儲存媒體）；填寫（表格、支票等），擬定；（筆）能寫字；拼寫；<加，南非>參加（筆試）；書寫，手寫（與鉛印相對）；以寫作為生；承保（保險單）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>write</b>, you use something such as a pen or pencil to produce words, letters, or numbers. 寫","examples":["Simply write your name and address on a postcard and send it to us. 只要在明信片上寫下你的名字和地址，然後寄給我們。","They were still trying to teach her to read and write. 他們當時仍在試圖教她讀書寫字。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>write</b> something such as a book, a poem, or a piece of music, you create it and record it on paper or perhaps on a computer. 創作","examples":["I had written quite a lot of orchestral music in my student days. 我在學生時代創作了許多管絃樂曲。","Thereafter she wrote articles for papers and magazines in Paris. 從那以後，她為巴黎的報紙和雜誌撰稿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>write</b> someone or <b>to</b> someone or <b>write</b> them a letter, you give them information, ask them something, or express your feelings in a letter. 寫 (信)","examples":["Apparently she had written to her aunt in Holland asking for advice. 顯然，她已給她荷蘭的姑媽寫信徵求意見了。","She had written him a note a couple of weeks earlier. 兩週前她曾給他寫過一張便條。","I wrote a letter to the car rental agency, explaining what had happened. 我給汽車出租代理機構寫了一封信，解釋所發生的事情。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone <b>writes</b> something such as a cheque, receipt, or prescription, they put the necessary information on it and usually sign it. 填寫 (支票、收據或處方)","examples":["Snape wrote a receipt with a gold fountain pen. 斯內普用自來水金筆填寫了一張收據。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>writes</b> creates books, stories, or articles, usually for publication. 創作","examples":["Jay wanted to write. 傑伊那時想搞創作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>write</b> to a computer or a disk, you record data on it. (在電腦或磁碟上) 寫入 (資料)","examples":["You should write-protect all disks that you do not usually need to write to. 你應該對你通常不需要寫入內容的磁碟進行防寫。"]}]}]},"ago":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以前，從前"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"以前的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>ago</b> when you are referring to past time. For example, if something happened one year <b>ago</b>, it is one year since it happened. If it happened a long time <b>ago</b>, it is a long time since it happened. 以前","examples":["He was killed a few days ago in a skiing accident. 他幾天以前在一次滑雪事故中喪生。","The meeting is the first ever between the two sides since the war there began 14 years ago. 這是自從14年前雙方爆發戰爭以來的第一次會晤。"]}]}]},"ahead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在前面，朝前面；領先，佔優勢；提前，預先；在將來，今後；（數量或價值上）更多，更高；取得進步，獲得成功；超出預期地，超前地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在前的，提前的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>ahead</b> is in front of you. If you look <b>ahead</b>, you look directly in front of you. 在前面地; 筆直向前地","examples":["Brett looked straight ahead. 布瑞特向前直視。","The road ahead was now blocked solid. 前方道路現在被堵死了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>ahead</b> with verbs such as \"push,\" \"move,\" and \"forge\" to indicate that a plan, programme, or organization is making fast progress. 向前地","examples":["Western countries were moving ahead with plans to send financial aid to all of the former Soviet republics. 西方國家正推行對所有前蘇聯國家提供經濟援助的計劃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>ahead</b> in your work or achievements, you have made more progress than you expected to and are performing well. 提前地","examples":["First half profits have charged ahead from $127.6m to $134.2m. 上半年利潤已經提前從1.276億美元提升到了1.342億美元。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or a team is <b>ahead</b> in a competition, they are winning. 領先地","examples":["Australia was ahead throughout the game. 澳大利亞隊在整場比賽中一直領先。","The Communists are comfortably ahead in the opinion polls. 共產黨在民意調查中遙遙領先。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Ahead</b> also means in the future. 在將來","examples":["A much bigger battle is ahead for the president. 總統還將面臨一場更大的戰鬥。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you prepare or plan something <b>ahead</b>, you do it some time before a future event so that everything is ready for that event to take place. 提前地","examples":["The government wants figures that help it to administer its policies and plan ahead. 政府想要可以助其提前實施其政策和計劃的資料。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you go <b>ahead</b>, or if you go on <b>ahead</b>, you go in front of someone who is going to the same place so that you arrive there some time before they do. 提前地","examples":["I went ahead and waited with Sean. 我提前去了，和肖恩一起等。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>ahead of</b> you, they are directly in front of you. If someone is moving <b>ahead of</b> you, they are in front of you and moving in the same direction. 在前面","examples":["I saw a man in a blue jacket thirty yards ahead of me. 我看見在我前面30碼處有一個穿藍色夾克的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or period of time lies <b>ahead of</b> you, it is going to happen or take place soon or in the future. 在將來","examples":["I tried to think about all the problems that were ahead of me tomorrow. 我試著想考慮一下明天要面對的所有問題。","Heather had been awake all night thinking about the future that lay ahead of her. 海瑟整夜未眠，考慮著她所要面臨的未來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a competition, if a person or team does something <b>ahead of</b> someone else, they do it before the second person or team. (競賽中) 領先於","examples":["Robert Millar finished 1 minute and 35 seconds ahead of the Frenchman. 羅伯特·米拉爾領先法國選手1分35秒完成比賽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>ahead of</b> schedule or <b>ahead of</b> time, it happens earlier than was planned. 提前","examples":["The election was held six months ahead of schedule. 選舉比計劃日程提前了6個月舉行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone is <b>ahead of</b> someone else, they have made more progress and are more advanced in what they are doing. 領先於","examples":["Henry generally stayed ahead of the others in the academic subjects. 亨利的文化課成績上通常都領先於其他人。"]}]}]},"also":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"此外，而且；也，同樣"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"另外，又"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>also</b> to give more information about a person or thing, or to add another relevant fact. 還","examples":["The book also includes an appendix with a listing of all U.S. presidents. 這本書還包含一個列有所有美國總統的附錄。","He is an asthmatic who is also anaemic. 他是一個哮喘病人，並且還貧血。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>also</b> to indicate that something you have just said about one person or thing is true of another person or thing. 也","examples":["General Geichenko was a survivor. His father, also a top-ranking officer, had perished during the war. 格晨科將軍是一位倖存者。他的父親也是一位高階軍官，在戰爭中喪生了。","This rule has also been applied in the case of a purchase of used tyres and tubes. 這個規定也已經用於購買使用過的輪胎和內胎。"]}]}]},"already":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"已經，早已；<美，非正式>馬上，夠了（用於表達不耐煩或氣惱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>already</b> to show that something has happened, or that something had happened before the moment you are referring to. Some speakers use <b>already</b> with the simple past tense of the verb instead of a perfect tense. 已經","examples":["They had already voted for him at the first ballot. 他們已經在第一輪投票中投了他的票。","She says she already told the neighbours not to come over for a couple of days. 她說她已經告訴了鄰居們這兩天不要過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>already</b> to show that a situation exists at this present moment or that it exists at an earlier time than expected. You use <b>already</b> after the verb \"be\" or an auxiliary verb, or before a verb if there is no auxiliary. When you want to add emphasis, you can put <b>already</b> at the beginning of a sentence. 早已","examples":["The authorities believe those security measures are already paying off. 當局相信那些安全措施已經在起作用了。","He was already rich. 他早就富了。","Already, she is thinking ahead. 她早就在考慮未來了。"]}]}]},"alone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨自的；單獨的；孤獨的，無依無靠的；唯一的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"獨自，單獨；獨力，單幹（地）；單，只；僅僅……就"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>alone</b>, you are not with any other people. 獨自的","examples":["There is nothing so fearful as to be alone in a combat situation. 沒有比獨自一人處於戰鬥環境中更可怕的事了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person is <b>alone</b> <b>with</b> another person, or if two or more people are <b>alone</b>, they are together, without anyone else present. 獨處的","examples":["I couldn't imagine why he would want to be alone with me. 我想像不出他為什麼想要和我獨處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>alone</b> or feel <b>alone</b>, you mean that nobody who is with you, or nobody at all, cares about you. 孤獨的","examples":["Never in her life had she felt so alone, so abandoned. 她一輩子從沒有感到過如此孤獨、如此被拋棄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>alone</b> <b>in</b> doing something, they are the only person doing it, and so are different from other people. 惟一的","examples":["Am I alone in recognizing that these two statistics have quite different implications? 惟獨我看出這兩個統計有完全不同含意嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alone</b> is also an adverb. 獨自地","examples":["She has lived alone in this house for almost five years now. 她現在已經獨自在這所房子裡住了差不多五年了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Alone</b> is also an adverb. 惟一地","examples":["I alone was sane, I thought, in a world of crazy people. 我以為在這個狂人的世界中我是惟一清醒的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that one person or thing <b>alone</b> does something when you are emphasizing that only one person or thing is involved. 只有","examples":["You alone should determine what is right for you. 只有你應該決定什麼對你是合適的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that one person or thing <b>alone</b> is responsible for part of an amount, you are emphasizing the size of that part and the size of the total amount. 單單","examples":["CNN alone is sending 300 technicians, directors and commentators. 僅有線電視新聞網就派了300名技師、導演和實況播音員。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When someone does something <b>alone</b>, they do it without help from other people. 獨力地","examples":["Bringing up a child alone should give you a sense of achievement. 獨力一人養大一個孩子會給你一種成就感。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>go it alone</b>, you do something without any help from other people. 單幹","examples":["I missed the stimulation of working with others when I tried to go it alone. 當我試著自己單幹時，我想念和別人一起工作的那種刺激。"]}]}]},"almost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"幾乎，差不多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>almost</b> to indicate that something is not completely the case but is nearly the case. 差不多; 幾乎","examples":["The couple had been dating for almost three years. 這對情侶談戀愛差不多三年了。","The effect is almost impossible to describe. 這影響幾乎無法言表。","He contracted Spanish flu, which almost killed him. 他傳染上了西班牙型流感，那幾乎要了他的命。"]}]}]},"have":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擁有；有（想法、主意、觀點等）；顯示出，帶有（性質、特徵）；做，進行（活動）；吃，喝，抽（煙）；患病，得病；得到，收到；經歷，經受；擔負（責任）；導致，產生（影響）；生，生育；包括；使保持，使處於；明白，懂得；抓住，緊握；<非正式>欺騙；讓，叫，命令；照看；（在家中）招待，款待；允許，容忍；<非正式>辯過，勝過；已經，曾經（與過去分詞連用構成完成時）；與（某人）性交"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>有錢人（the haves）；<英，非正式>詐騙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"aux.","pos_name":"助動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the forms <b>have</b> and <b>has</b> with a past participle to form the present perfect tense of verbs. 後接過去分詞，構成現在完成時態","examples":["Alex has already gone. 亞歷克斯已經走了。","What have you found so far? 迄今為止，你發現了什麼？","Frankie hasn't been feeling well for a long time. 弗朗姬感覺不舒服已經很長一段時間了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use the form <b>had</b> with a past participle to form the past perfect tense of verbs. (had)後接過去分詞，構成過去完成時態","examples":["When I met her, she had just returned from a job interview. 我遇到她時，她剛剛從一次求職面試回來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Have</b> is used in question tags. 用於反意疑問句","examples":["You haven't sent her away, have you? 你還沒有把她送走，是嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>have</b> when you are confirming or contradicting a statement containing \"have,\" \"has,\" or \"had,\" or answering a question. 代替前一句中的(have)、(has)或(had)加上動詞構成的片語，表示肯定或否定含義","examples":["\"You'd never seen the Marilyn Monroe film?\"—\"No I hadn't.\" “你從來沒看過瑪麗蓮•夢露的電影嗎？”—“是的，從來沒有。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The form <b>having</b> with a past participle can be used to introduce a clause in which you mention an action which had already happened before another action began. (having)後接過去分詞，所引導的從句其動作先於另一有關的動作","examples":["He arrived in San Francisco, having left New Jersey on January 19th. 他1月19號離開新澤西后，到達了聖弗朗西斯科。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>have</b> followed by a noun to talk about an action or event, when it would be possible to use the same word as a verb. For example, you can say \"<b>I had a look at the photos</b>\" instead of \"I looked at the photos.\" 後接描述某一動作或事件的名詞，如(to have a look)同(to look)意義幾乎一樣","examples":["I went out and had a walk around. 我出了門在附近散了散步。","We had a laugh over that one. 我們對此大笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In normal spoken or written English, people use <b>have</b> with a wide range of nouns to talk about actions and events, often instead of a more specific verb. For example people are more likely to say \"<b>we had ice cream</b>\" or \"<b>he's had a shock</b>\" than \"we ate ice cream,\" or \"he's suffered a shock.\" 後接名詞來描述某一動作或事件，以取代某一特定的動詞","examples":["Come and have a meal with us tonight. 今晚過來和我們一起吃晚飯吧。","We will be having a meeting to decide what to do. 我們將開會決定該做什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>have</b> to say that someone or something owns a particular thing, or when you are mentioning one of their qualities or characteristics. 擁有","examples":["Oscar had a new bicycle. 奧斯卡擁有一輛新的腳踏車。","I want to have my own business. 我想擁有自己的事業。","She had no job and no money. 她既沒工作也沒錢。","You have beautiful eyes. 你有美麗的眼睛。","Do you have any brothers and sisters? 你有什麼兄弟姐妹嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something <b>to</b> do, you are responsible for doing it or must do it. 必須 (做)","examples":["He had plenty of work to do. 他有一大堆工作必須做。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>have</b> instead of \"there is\" to say that something exists or happens. For example, you can say \"<b>you have no alternative</b>\" instead of \"there is no alternative,\" or \"<b>he had a good view from his window</b>\" instead of \"there was a good view from his window.\" 有","examples":["He had two tenants living with him. 他有兩個房客與他同住。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something such as a part of your body in a particular position or state, it is in that position or state. 使處於","examples":["Mary had her eyes closed. 瑪麗讓自己的眼睛閉著。","They had the curtains open. 他們把窗簾開著。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something done, someone does it for you or you arrange for it to be done. 讓…做…","examples":["I had your rooms cleaned and aired. 我叫人把你的房間打掃了並通了風。","They had him killed. 他們找人殺了他。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone <b>has</b> something unpleasant happen to them, it happens to them. 遭遇","examples":["We had our money stolen. 我們的錢被偷掉了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> someone do something, you persuade, cause, or order them to do it. 勸說; 命令","examples":["The bridge is not as impressive as some guides would have you believe. 這座橋並不像有些導遊試圖讓你相信的那樣令人印象深刻。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>has</b> you <b>by</b> a part of your body, they are holding you there and they are trying to hurt you or force you to go somewhere. 抓住 (某人身體的某部位)","examples":["He had her by the arm and he was screaming at her. 他抓住她的胳膊，衝著她大喊。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something from someone, they give it to you. 得到","examples":["You can have my ticket. 你可以得到我的票。","Can I have your name please? 我能知道你的名字嗎？"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> an illness or disability, you suffer from it. 患","examples":["I had a headache. 我頭疼。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a woman <b>has</b> a baby, she gives birth to it. If she <b>is having</b> a baby, she is pregnant. 生","examples":["My wife has just had a baby boy. 我妻子剛生了個男孩。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You can use <b>have</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I won't have it</b>\" or \"<b>I'm not having that,</b>\" to mean that you will not allow or put up with something. 容忍","examples":["I'm not having any of that nonsense. 我不要聽那些廢話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>has it</b> in expressions such as \"<b>rumour has it that</b>\" or \"<b>as legend has it</b>\" when you are quoting something that you have heard, but you do not necessarily think it is true. 據謠傳","examples":["Rumour has it that tickets were being sold for $300. 據謠傳，票價賣到了$300。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>has it in for</b> you, they do not like you and they want to make life difficult for you. 跟某人過不去","examples":["He's always had it in for the Dawkins family. 他總是同道金斯一家過不去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>have it in</b> you, you have abilities and skills which you do not usually use and which only show themselves in a difficult situation. 有本領","examples":["\"You were brilliant!\" he said. \"I didn't know you had it in you.\" “你真棒！”他說道。“我真不知道你還有這兩下子。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>have it out</b> or <b>have things out</b> <b>with</b> someone, you discuss a problem or disagreement very openly with them, even if it means having an argument, because you think this is the best way to solve the problem. 同…講個明白","examples":["Why not have it out with your critic, discuss the whole thing face to face? 為什麼不同批評你的人講個明白，面對面說說整件事情呢？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>have to</b> when you are saying that something is necessary or required, or must happen. If you do not <b>have to</b> do something, it is not necessary or required. 不得不","examples":["He had to go to Germany. 他不得不去德國。","You have to be careful what you say on TV. 在電視上說話時你不得不謹慎。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>have to</b> in order to say that you feel certain that something is true or will happen. 肯定","examples":["There has to be some kind of way out. 肯定有辦法解決。"]}]}]},"tell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"告訴，告知；說，講述；吐露，顯示；看出，確切地判斷；辨別，區別；命令，吩咐；告訴自己，暗自叮囑；表明，說明；（不快的或令人疲倦的經歷）產生效果，產生影響；洩密；數，計算；（通常指小孩）告狀；警告，告誡；（某種因素）影響，起作用"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤作紙牌用語）（洩露試圖作弊的）不經意動作；（中東）臺形（土墩）遺址（由遠古人村落遺蹟堆積而成的）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tell</b> someone something, you give them information. 告訴 (某人某事)","examples":["In the evening I returned to tell Phyllis I got the job. 晚上我回來告訴菲莉絲我得到了那份工作。","I called Andie to tell her how spectacular the stuff looked. 我打電話給安迪告訴她那東西看上去多麼壯觀。","Claire had made me promise to tell her the truth. 克萊爾已經逼我答應了告訴她真相。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tell</b> something such as a joke, a story, or your personal experiences, you communicate it to other people using speech. 講述 (笑話、故事、個人經歷等)","examples":["His friends say he was always quick to tell a joke. 他的朋友們說他以前總是張口就能講笑話。","He told his story to The L.A. Times and produced photographs. 他向《洛杉機時報》敘述了自己的故事，並提供了一些照片。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>tell</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you order or advise them to do it. 命令; 建議 (某人做某事)","examples":["He said officers told him to get out of his car and lean against it. 他說警官們命令他從他的車裡出來並靠在車上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>tell</b> <b>yourself</b> something, you put it into words in your own mind because you need to encourage or persuade yourself about something. 叮囑 (自己)","examples":["\"Come on,\" she told herself. “加油，”她叮囑自己。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you can <b>tell</b> what is happening or what is true, you are able to judge correctly what is happening or what is true. 判斷","examples":["It was already impossible to tell where the bullet had entered. 已經不可能判斷子彈是從哪裡射進來的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you can <b>tell</b> one thing <b>from</b> another, you are able to recognize the difference between it and other similar things. 辨別","examples":["I can't really tell the difference between their policies and ours. 我真地看不出他們的政策和我們的政策有什麼區別。","How do you tell one from another? 你怎麼把它們區分開來？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If facts or events <b>tell</b> you something, they reveal certain information to you through ways other than speech. (事實、事件) 告訴 (某人某事)","examples":["The facts tell us that this is not true. 事實告訴我們這不是真的。","I don't think the unemployment rate ever tells us much about the future. 我認為失業率不會告訴我們很多關於未來的東西。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tell</b>, you reveal or give away a secret. 洩密","examples":["Many of the children know who they are but are not telling. 許多孩子知道他們是誰，但不願洩露秘密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an unpleasant or tiring experience begins to <b>tell</b>, it begins to have a serious effect. (讓人不愉快或疲倦的經歷) 產生嚴重影響","examples":["It wasn't long before the strain began to tell on our relationship. 很快，這種極度的緊張就開始對我們的關係產生嚴重影響。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as far as</b> I <b>can tell</b> or <b>so far as</b> I <b>could tell</b> to indicate that what you are saying is based on the information you have, but that there may be things you do not know. 就某人判斷","examples":["As far as I can tell, Jason is basically a nice guy. 就我判斷，傑森基本上是個好人。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I tell you</b>,\" \"<b>I can tell you</b>,\" or \"<b>I can't tell you</b>\" to add emphasis to what you are saying. 我告訴你/我可以告訴你/我沒法告訴你 (用以強調)","examples":["I tell you this, I will not rest until that day has come. 我告訴你，不到那天我不會休息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone disagrees with you or refuses to do what you suggest and you are eventually proved to be right, you can say \"<b>I told you so</b>.\" 我早跟你說過","examples":["Her parents did not approve of her decision and, if she failed, her mother would say, \"I told you so.\" 她的父母沒有同意她的決定，如果她失敗了，她的母親就會說，“我早跟你說過。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>I'll tell you what</b> or <b>I tell you what</b> to introduce a suggestion or a new topic of conversation. 你聽我說 (用以引入建議或新話題)","examples":["I tell you what, I'll bring the beer over to your house. 你聽我的，由我帶啤酒到你家來。"]}]}]},"do":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"做，幹，辦（某事）；行動，表現；順利進行，進展；從事（工作）；執行（任務）；學習，研究；解答，解決，算出；製作，做出；演出，編排（戲劇等）；仿效，模仿；完成，做好；處理；供給，提供；適合，足夠；參觀，遊覽，旅行；走過，行過；以……速度行進；達到（一定銷售額）；度過（一段時間）；服（刑）；導致，引起；煮制；整理，梳（發）；護理；欺騙；懲罰；（從某地方）盜竊；（非正式）吸（毒）；（非正式）性交；（非正式）痛打，殺死；生長"},{"pos":"aux.","zh":"與動詞連用構成否定句和疑問句；用於構成疑問尾句；用於避免重複某一動詞；用於強調主要動詞；用於祈使句中表示禮貌；用於肯定或否定回答；用在倒裝句中"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聚會，社交活動；（主英國、紐西蘭口語）宴會；（口語）事件；（主英國口語）詐騙；要求，規定，必須做到的事情（口語，常用複數 dos）；（音樂）唱名，音階的第一音（如 C 大調音階中的 do）；（非正式）（女子）髮型；（Do）多（人名 Dorothea 和 Dorothy 的暱稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"aux.","pos_name":"助動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Do</b> is used to form the negative of main verbs, by putting \"not\" after \"do\" and before the main verb in its infinitive form, that is the form without \"to.\" 用於構成動詞的否定式，後面加\"not\"，放在主要動詞前面，是一種不帶\"to\"的動詞不定式","examples":["They don't want to work. 他們不想工作。","I did not know Jamie had a knife. 我不知道傑米有把刀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Do</b> is used to form questions, by putting the subject after \"do\" and before the main verb in its infinitive form, that is the form without \"to.\" 用於構成疑問句，主語放在\"do\"和主要動詞中間，是不帶\"to\"的動詞不定式","examples":["Do you like music? 你喜歡音樂嗎？","What did he say? 他說了什麼？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Do</b> is used in question tags. 用於附加疑問句中","examples":["You know about Andy, don't you? 你瞭解安迪，不是嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>do</b> when you are confirming or contradicting a statement containing \"do,\" or giving a negative or positive answer to a question. 用於肯定或否定回答","examples":["\"Did he think there was anything suspicious going on?\"—\"Yes, he did.\" “他認為有什麼可疑的事情發生嗎？”— “是的，他是這樣認為的。”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Do</b> can be used to refer back to another verb group when you are comparing or contrasting two things, or saying that they are the same. 比較兩件事物時用於代替前面出現的動詞，表示同一概念","examples":["I make more money than he does. 我掙的錢比他多。","I had fantasies, as do all mothers, about how life would be when my girls were grown. 和所有母親一樣，我也有幻想，想像我的女兒們長大成人後生活會是怎樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>do</b> after \"so\" and \"nor\" to say that the same statement is true for two people or groups. 用在\"so\"和\"nor\"後面，表示同一陳述適用於兩個或兩組人","examples":["You know that's true, and so do I. 你知道那是真的，我也知道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>do</b> something, you take some action or perform an activity or task. <b>Do</b> is often used instead of a more specific verb, to talk about a common action involving a particular thing. For example you can say \"do your hair\" instead of \"brush your hair.\" 表示從事某種活動或工作，常用來替代有具體含義的動詞","examples":["I was trying to do some work. 我正試圖做些工作。","After lunch Elizabeth and I did the dishes. 午餐後，我和伊麗莎白洗了碗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Do</b> can be used to stand for any verb group, or to refer back to another verb group, including one that was in a previous sentence. 用於代表任何動詞或代替前面出現過的動詞","examples":["What are you doing? 你在幹什麼？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>do</b> in a clause at the beginning of a sentence after words like \"what\" and \"all,\" to give special emphasis to the information that comes at the end of the sentence. 用於以\"what\"或\"all\"等開頭的句中，強調句子後面所說的事情","examples":["All she does is complain. 她只顧抱怨。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> a particular thing <b>with</b> something, you use it in that particular way. 做; 幹","examples":["I was allowed to do whatever I wanted with my life. 我被允許自由安排我的生活。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> something <b>about</b> a problem, you take action to try to solve it.  採取行動","examples":["They refuse to do anything about the real cause of crime: poverty. 他們拒絕採取任何行動解決引發犯罪的真正原因：貧困。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If an action or event <b>does</b> a particular thing, such as harm or good, it has that result or effect. 造成","examples":["A few bombs can do a lot of damage. 幾顆炸彈足以造成嚴重破壞。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you ask someone what they <b>do</b>, you want to know what their job or profession is. 從事 (某種職業)","examples":["\"What does your father do?\"—\"Well, he's a civil servant.\" “你父親是做什麼工作的？”— “哦，他是個公務員。”"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>are doing</b> something, you are busy or active in some way, or have planned an activity for some time in the future. 忙於; 準備做","examples":["Are you doing anything tomorrow night? 明晚你有事嗎？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You can use <b>do</b> when referring to the speed or rate that something or someone achieves or is able to achieve. 達到 (某種速度)","examples":["They were doing 70 miles an hour. 他們每小時達到70英里。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone <b>does</b> drugs, they take illegal drugs. 吸食 (毒品)","examples":["I don't do drugs. 我不吸毒。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that something <b>will</b> <b>do</b> or <b>will</b> <b>do</b> you, you mean that there is enough of it or that it is of good enough quality to meet your requirements or to satisfy you. 夠用; 滿足需要","examples":["Anything to create a scene and attract attention will do. 只要能當眾大鬧，吸引人們的注意，做什麼都行。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> a subject, author, or book, you study them at school or college. 攻讀; 研究","examples":["She planned to do maths at night school. 她打算上夜校學數學。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>does</b> well or badly, you are talking about how successful or unsuccessful they are. 表現; 進展","examples":["Connie did well at school and graduated with honours. 康妮在學校表現很好，以優等成績畢業。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>could do with</b> something, you mean that you need it or would benefit from it. 需要; 從…中獲益","examples":["I could do with a cup of tea. 我需要一杯茶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can ask someone <b>what</b> they <b>did with</b> something as another way of asking them where they put it. 把…放在何處","examples":["What did you do with that notebook? 你把那本筆記本放哪兒去了？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you ask <b>what</b> someone or something <b>is doing</b> in a particular place, you are asking why they are there. 為何出現在此處","examples":["\"Dr. Campbell,\" he said, clearly surprised. \"What are you doing here?\" “坎貝爾醫生，”他一臉驚訝地說道，“你怎麼會在這兒？”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>has</b> something <b>to do with</b> or <b>is</b> something <b>to do with</b> another thing, you mean that the two things are connected or that the first thing is about the second thing. 與…有關","examples":["Mr. Butterfield denies having anything to do with the episode. 巴特菲爾德先生否認他和這一事件有關。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone tells you the <b>dos and don'ts</b> of a particular situation, they advise you what you should and should not do in that situation. 該做的和不該做的; 行為準則; 注意事項","examples":["Please advise me on the most suitable colour print film and some dos and don'ts. 請就最適用的彩照膠捲及其使用須知給我建議。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a formal or festive gathering; party (正式的)集會; (節日中的)集會; 聚會","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Dominican Republic 多明尼加共和國","examples":[]}]}]},"both":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"雙方，兩者"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"兩者"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"…和…都；……和……都"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兩…，雙…"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>both</b> when you are referring to two people or things and saying that something is true about each of them. 兩個 (都)","examples":["She cried out in fear and flung both arms up to protect her face. 她害怕得哭起來，急忙伸出雙臂以保護自己的臉。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Both</b> is also a quantifier. 兩個","examples":["Both of these women have strong memories of the Vietnam War. 兩個女人對越南戰爭有著深刻的記憶。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Both</b> is also a pronoun. 兩者","examples":["Miss Brown and her friend, both from Brooklyn, were arrested on the 8th of June. 布朗小姐和她的朋友，兩人來自布魯克林，於6月8日被捕了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"強調代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Both</b> is also an emphasizing pronoun. 兩者都","examples":["He visited the Institute of Neurology in Havana where they both worked. 他在哈瓦那參觀了他們倆都曾工作過的神經病學研究所。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Both</b> is also a predeterminer. 兩者","examples":["Both the horses were out, tacked up and ready to ride. 兩匹馬都在門外被套上了馬鞍，隨時可以騎。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the structure <b>both...and</b> when you are giving two facts or alternatives and emphasizing that each of them is true or possible. …和…都","examples":["Now women work both before and after having their children. 如今，女性在生孩子前和生孩子後都工作。"]}]}]},"again":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"再一次；復原；<非正式>請再說一遍；不過，然而（then again）；增加，多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>again</b> to indicate that something happens a second time, or after it has already happened before. 再一次 (發生); 又","examples":["He kissed her again. 他再一次親了她。","Again there was a short silence. 又有一陣短暫的沉默。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>again</b> to indicate that something is now in a particular state or place that it used to be in. 又 (回到過去的狀態或地方)","examples":["He opened his attaché case, removed a folder, then closed it again. 他開啟了他的公文包，拿出了一個資料夾，然後又把它合上了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>again</b> when you want to point out that there is a similarity between the subject that you are talking about now and a previous subject. 又 (和以前類似)","examples":["Again the pregnancy was very similar to my previous two. 這次懷孕又和我前兩次懷孕非常類似。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>again</b> in expressions such as <b>but again</b>, <b>then again</b>, and <b>there again</b> when you want to introduce a remark that contrasts with or weakens something that you have just said. (但是、然後) 又 (用以對比前後所說的話)","examples":["You may be happy to buy imitation leather, and then again, you may wonder what you're getting for your money. 你可能樂於買仿製皮革，然後你也許又想知道你花的錢買到的是什麼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can add <b>again</b> to the end of your question when you are asking someone to tell you something that you have forgotten or that they have already told you. 再 (問一次)","examples":["Sorry, what's your name again?. 對不起，你叫什麼名字來著？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>again</b> in expressions such as <b>half as much again</b> when you are indicating how much greater one amount is than another amount that you have just mentioned or are about to mention. 又一個 (同樣的量)","examples":["A similar wine from France would cost you half as much again. 類似的法國葡萄酒會花你多一半的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>again and again</b> or <b>time and again</b> to emphasize that something happens many times. 一再","examples":["He would go over his work again and again until he felt he had it right. 他會反覆檢查他的工作直到他覺得準確無誤為止。"]}]}]},"away":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"距離……有多遠，距離……有多久；朝另一個方向；不在，離開；（放）在安全的地方；逐漸消失；一直，繼續不斷地；移走；（比賽）在客場"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（球隊比賽）客場的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"客場比賽，客場獲勝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something moves or is moved <b>away</b> <b>from</b> a place, they move or are moved so that they are no longer there. If you are <b>away</b> <b>from</b> a place, you are not in the place where people expect you to be. 離開","examples":["An injured policeman was led away by colleagues. 一位受傷的警察被同事們帶走了。","He walked away from his car. 他從他的車邊走開了。","Jason was away on a business trip. 賈森出差在外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you look or turn <b>away</b> <b>from</b> something, you move your head so that you are no longer looking at it. (目光) 移開地","examples":["She quickly looked away and stared down at her hands. 她迅速轉移目光，低頭盯著自己的雙手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you put something <b>away</b>, you put it where it should be. If you hide someone or something <b>away</b>, you put them in a place where nobody can see them or find them. (收藏) 好","examples":["I put my journal away and prepared for bed. 我把日記收好，準備睡覺。","All her letters were carefully filed away in folders. 她所有的信件都被仔細地歸檔在資料夾裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>away</b> to talk about future events. For example, if an event is a week <b>away</b>, it will happen after a week. 距離 (某事件的時間)","examples":["...the Washington summit, now only just over two weeks away. …現在離華盛頓峰會的召開只有兩個多星期。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a sports team plays <b>away</b>, it plays on its opponents' playing court or field. (比賽) 在客場地","examples":["...a sensational 4-3 victory for the team playing away. …該隊在客場4-3轟動性的勝利。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>away</b> to say that something slowly disappears, becomes less significant, or changes so that it is no longer the same. 漸逝地","examples":["So much snow has already melted away. 那麼多雪已經逐漸融化掉了。","His voice died away in a whisper. 他的聲音漸漸放低成了耳語。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>away</b> to show that there has been a change or development from one state or situation to another. 變化發展地","examples":["British courts are increasingly moving away from sending young offenders to prison. 英國法庭逐漸地不再將犯法的年輕人送進監獄。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>away</b> to emphasize a continuous or repeated action. 持續不斷地","examples":["He would often be working away on his word processor late into the night. 他經常會在他的文書處理機上持續工作到深夜。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>away</b> to show that something is removed. 拿走","examples":["If you take my work away I can't be happy anymore. 如果你帶走了我的工作，那我就再也高興不起來了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Away</b> is also an adjective. 客場的","examples":["Pittsburgh is about to play an important away game. 匹茲堡隊將要打一場重要的客場比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>away from</b> a person or place, it is at a distance from that person or place. 離 (某人或某地) 一段距離","examples":["The two women were sitting as far away from each other as possible. 那兩個女人坐得離對方儘可能地遠。"]}]}]},"any":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"任何的，任一的；一點，些許；不尋常的；儘可能多的，所有的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何一個；任何數量，任一數額"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一點，絲毫；<美，非正式>壓根兒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"任何的，任一的；一點，一些"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>any</b> in statements with negative meaning to indicate that no thing or person of a particular type exists, is present, or is involved in a situation. 任何的 (用於含否定意義的陳述句中)","examples":["I'm not making any promises. 我不是在作任何承諾。","We are doing this all without any support from the hospital. 我們在沒有來自醫院的任何支援的情況下做著這一切。","It is too early to say what effect, if any, there will be on the workforce. 說對職工會有什麼影響，如果有的話，也還為時過早。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>any</b> in questions and conditional clauses to ask whether there is some of a particular thing or some of a particular group of people, or to suggest that there might be. 某個的 (用於疑問句和條件分句中)","examples":["Do you speak any foreign languages? 你說某種外語嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>any</b> in positive statements when you are referring to someone or something of a particular kind that might exist, occur, or be involved in a situation, when their exact identity or nature is not important. 任何一個的 (用於肯定陳述句中)","examples":["Any actor will tell you that it is easier to perform than to be themselves. 任何演員都會告訴你表演比做自己更容易。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a quantifier. 任何一個","examples":["You don't know any of my friends. 你不認識任何一個我的朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a quantifier. 某個","examples":["Introduce foods one at a time and notice if you feel uncomfortable with any of them. 一次嘗一種食物，看你是否對其中某種食物感到不適。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a quantifier. 任何一個","examples":["Nealy disappeared two days ago, several miles away from any of the fighting. 尼利兩天前失蹤了，離任何一個戰場都有幾英里。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a pronoun. 任何一個","examples":["The children needed new school clothes and Kim couldn't afford any. 孩子們需要新校服，金買不起任何一件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a pronoun. 某個","examples":["If any bright thoughts occur to you pass them straight to me. Have you got any? 如果你想到某個好主意就直接告訴我。你有什麼好主意嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Any</b> is also a pronoun. 任何一個","examples":["Clean the mussels and discard any that do not close. 清洗這些蚌，並且丟掉任何合不上的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also use <b>any</b> to emphasize a comparative adjective or adverb in a negative statement. 任何地 (用於否定陳述句中以強調某比較級形容詞或副詞)","examples":["I can't see things getting any easier for graduates. 我看不到對於畢業生們事情有任何變容易的趨勢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>not just any</b> person or thing, you mean that they are special in some way. 並非任何的","examples":["Finzer is not just any East Coast businessman. 芬澤並非一般的東海岸商人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something does not happen or is not true <b>any longer</b>, it has stopped happening or is no longer true. (不) 再","examples":["I couldn't keep the tears hidden any longer. 我再也藏不住淚水了。"]}]}]},"always":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"總是，每次都是；一直，長久以來；永遠；老是，一再；總還有（表示有另一種可能）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>always</b> do something, you do it whenever a particular situation occurs. If you <b>always</b> did something, you did it whenever a particular situation occurred. 總是; 每次","examples":["She's always late for everything. 她總是每件事都遲到。","Always lock your garage. 每次都要鎖好你的車庫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>always</b> the case, was <b>always</b> the case, or will <b>always</b> be the case, it is, was, or will be the case all the time, continuously. 永遠地","examples":["We will always remember his generous hospitality. 我們將永遠記住他的慷慨好客。","He has always been the family solicitor. 他一直是這個家的律師。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>always</b> happening, especially something that annoys you, you mean that it happens repeatedly. 老是","examples":["She was always moving things around. 她老是把東西挪來挪去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>always</b> in expressions such as <b>can always</b> or <b>could always</b> when you are making suggestions or suggesting an alternative approach or method. (用於提出建議或替換方案) 總還","examples":["If you can't find any decent apples, you can always try growing them yourself. 如果你找不到任何像樣的蘋果，你總還可以試著自己種。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>always</b> was, for example, awkward or lucky to indicate that you are not surprised about what they are doing or have just done. 一向以來地","examples":["She's going to be fine. She always was pretty strong. 她一切都會好的。她一向以來都挺堅強。"]}]}]},"bright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明亮的；鮮豔的；聰明的；歡快的，有活力的；光明的，有希望的；清晰嘹亮的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>前大燈，頭燈；明亮醒目的顏色"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<文>光亮地，明亮地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bright</b> colour is strong and noticeable, and not dark. 鮮豔的 (顏色)","examples":["...a bright red dress. …一條鮮豔的紅色連衣裙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bright</b> light, object, or place is shining strongly or is full of light. 明亮的","examples":["...a bright October day. …一個明媚的10月天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>bright</b>, you mean that they are quick at learning things. 聰明的","examples":["I was convinced that he was brighter than average. 我確信他比一般人聰明。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bright</b> idea is clever and original. 巧妙新穎的 (主意)","examples":["There are lots of books crammed with bright ideas. 有很多書都充滿了巧妙新穎的點子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone looks or sounds <b>bright</b>, they look or sound cheerful and lively. 歡快活潑的","examples":["The boy was so bright and animated. 這個男孩非常歡快活潑、有生氣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If the future is <b>bright</b>, it is likely to be pleasant or successful. (未來) 光明的","examples":["Both had successful careers and the future looked bright. 兩人都有過成功的事業,前途看上去很光明。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鮮豔地","examples":["...a display of brightly coloured flowers. …色彩鮮豔的花卉的一次展示。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"明亮地","examples":["...a warm, brightly lit room. …一間溫暖的、燈光明亮的房間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"歡快活潑地","examples":["He smiled brightly as Ben approached. 當本走近時,他歡快地笑了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>brights</b> on a vehicle are its headlights when they are set to shine their brightest. (開到最亮的) 車頭燈","examples":["...a Bronco with its brights on, parked in the middle of the street. …一輛烈馬牌的汽車打著開到最亮的頭燈，停在街中央。"]}]}]},"each":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"每，各，每一"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"每個，各個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每個的，各自的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"給每個，對各個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>each</b> thing or <b>each</b> person in a group, you are referring to every member of the group and considering them as individuals. 每","examples":["Each book is beautifully illustrated. 每本書都配有精美的插圖。","Each year, hundreds of animals are killed in this way. 每年，數百隻動物就是這樣被殺死的。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Each</b> is also a pronoun. 每","examples":["...two bedrooms, each with three beds. …兩間臥室，每間有3張床。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"強調代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Each</b> is also an emphasizing pronoun. 每個","examples":["We each have different needs and interests. 我們每人有不同的需要和興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>each other</b> when you are saying that each member of a group does something to the others or has a particular connection with the others. 相互","examples":["We looked at each other in silence, each equally shocked. 我們無言地相互對視，每個人都同樣地震驚。","Both sides are willing to make allowances for each other's political sensitivities. 雙方都願意顧及相互的政治敏感性。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Each</b> is also an adverb. 每個地","examples":["The children were given one each, handed to them or placed on their plates. 孩子們每人給一個，遞給他們或者放在他們的盤子裡。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Each</b> is also a quantifier. 每個","examples":["He handed each of them a page of photos. 他遞給他們每人一張照片。","Each of these exercises takes one or two minutes to do. 這些練習題每一道要花一兩分鐘做完。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to <b>each one</b> <b>of</b> the members of a group, you are emphasizing that something applies to every one of them. 每個","examples":["He picked up forty of these publications and read each one of them. 他從這些出版物中挑了40本，每本都讀了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to <b>each and every</b> member <b>of</b> a group to emphasize that you mean all the members of that group. 每一個","examples":["My goal was that each and every person responsible for Yankel's murder be brought to justice. 我的目標是，讓每一個對揚克爾被謀殺負有責任的人都受到懲處。"]}]}]},"else":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"此外，其他；否則，要不然"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"其他的，另外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>else</b> after words such as \"anywhere,\" \"someone,\" and \"what\" to refer in a vague way to another person, place, or thing. (不確指人、處、事) 別的","examples":["If I can't make a living at painting, at least I can teach someone else to paint. 如果我不能以畫畫謀生的話，至少我能教別人畫畫。","We had nothing else to do on those long trips. 在那些漫長的旅途中我們別無他事可做。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>else</b> after words such as \"everyone,\" \"everything,\" and \"everywhere\" to refer in a vague way to all the other people, things, or places except the one you are talking about. 其他的","examples":["As I try to be truthful, I expect everyone else to be truthful. 因為我努力做到誠實，所以我期望每個其他也都誠實。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Else</b> is also an adverb. 其他地","examples":["I never wanted to live anywhere else. 我從未想要到其他任何地方去住。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Else</b> is also an adverb. 其他地","examples":["Cleveland seems so much dirtier than everywhere else. 克利夫蘭似乎比其他任何地方都髒得多。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>or else</b> after stating a logical conclusion, to indicate that what you are about to say is evidence for that conclusion. 否則 (用於給出推斷的理由)","examples":["Evidently no lessons have been learned or else the government would not have handled the problem so badly. 顯然沒有吸取教訓，否則政府不會把這個問題處理得如此糟糕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>or else</b> to introduce a statement that indicates the unpleasant results that will occur if someone does or does not do something. 否則","examples":["This time we really need to succeed or else people will start giving us funny looks. 這次我們真地得要成功，否則人們會開始用奇怪的眼光看我們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>or else</b> to introduce the second of two possibilities when you do not know which one is true. 要不然","examples":["You are either a total genius or else you must be totally crazy. 你要麼是個純粹的天才，要不然你準是完全瘋了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Above all else</b> is used to emphasize that a particular thing is more important than other things. 最重要地","examples":["Above all else I hate the cold. 我最討厭寒冷。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say \"<b>if nothing else</b>\" to indicate that what you are mentioning is, in your opinion, the only good thing in a particular situation. 至少","examples":["If nothing else, you'll really enjoy meeting them. 至少，你會真地喜歡見到他們。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say \"<b>or else</b>\" after a command to warn someone that if they do not obey, you will be angry and may harm or punish them. 否則不客氣了","examples":["Behave, or else! 守規矩，否則不客氣了！"]}]}]},"deep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"深的，厚的；縱深的，寬的；有……深的；成……排的；深呼吸的；（聲音）低沉的；深色的；酣睡的；嚴重的；（感情）深厚的；透徹的，深刻的；深奧的；全神貫注，深陷；（人）深沉的；（目光）銳利的，深邃的；靠近場地邊界的；神秘的；<美>大幅下降的；<美>有很多優秀選手的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"深深地，至深處；有……深；成……排地；靠近場地邊界地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>海洋（the deep）；海洋深處（deeps）；<文>中間部分（the deep）；（板球）外圍場地（the deep）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>deep</b>, it extends a long way down from the ground or from the top surface of something. 深的","examples":["The water is very deep and mysterious looking. 水很深，而且看起來很神秘。","Den had dug a deep hole in the centre of the garden. 登在花園中間挖了一個深洞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>deep</b> container, such as wardrobe, extends or measures a long distance from front to back. 縱深的","examples":["The wardrobe was very deep. 櫥櫃很深。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>deep</b> to emphasize the seriousness, strength, importance, or degree of something. 深切的","examples":["I had a deep admiration for Sartre. 我對薩特懷有深深的敬意。","He wants to express his deep sympathy to the family. 他想對那家人表示自己深切的同情。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are in a <b>deep</b> sleep, you are sleeping peacefully and it is difficult to wake you. (睡) 熟的","examples":["Una soon fell into a deep sleep. 尤納很快就睡熟了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>deep in</b> thought or <b>deep in</b> conversation, you are concentrating very hard on what you are thinking or saying and are not aware of the things that are happening around you. 深入的","examples":["Before long, we were deep in conversation. 我們很快就進入深談。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>deep</b> breath or sigh uses or fills the whole of your lungs. (指呼吸、嘆息) 深長的","examples":["Cal took a long, deep breath, struggling to control his own emotions. 卡爾深吸了一口氣，努力控制住自己的情緒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>deep</b> sound is low in pitch. 低沉的","examples":["His voice was deep and mellow. 他的聲音低沉而柔和。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you describe something such as a problem or a piece of writing as <b>deep</b>, you mean that it is important, serious, or complicated. 重要的; 嚴肅的; 複雜的","examples":["They're written as adventure stories. They're not intended to be deep. 這些內容被寫成了歷險故事，不想太嚴肅。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Deep</b> is also an adjective. 深的 (顏色)","examples":["These Amish cushions in traditional deep colours are available in two sizes. 這些傳統的深色阿米希墊子有兩種尺寸現貨供應。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deep</b> is also an adverb. 深地","examples":["Gingerly, she put her hand in deeper, to the bottom. 她小心翼翼地把手伸得更深，直到底部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"深地","examples":["There isn't time to dig deeply and put in manure or compost. 沒有時間挖得再深些，並放入糞肥或堆肥。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"深深地","examples":["He loved his brother deeply. 他深愛自己的哥哥。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(睡) 熟地","examples":["She slept deeply but woke early. 她睡得很熟，但醒得也早。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"(指呼吸、嘆息) 深長地","examples":["She sighed deeply and covered her face with her hands. 她長長地嘆了口氣，用手捂住了臉。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Deep</b> in an area means a long way inside it. 深入地","examples":["Picking up his bag the giant strode off deep into the forest. 巨人拿起袋子，大步走入森林深處。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you experience or feel something <b>deep</b> <b>inside</b> you or <b>deep</b> <b>down</b>, you feel it very strongly even though you do not necessarily show it. 在內心深處","examples":["Deep down, she supported her husband's involvement in the organization. 她從內心深處支援丈夫介入這個組織。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are <b>deep</b> <b>in</b> debt, you have a lot of debts. 深陷地","examples":["He is so deep in debt and desperate for money that he's apparently willing to say anything. 他債臺高築，急需錢，因此他顯然什麼都願意說。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"深陷地","examples":["Because of her medical and her legal bills, she is now penniless and deeply in debt. 由於醫療費和律師費，她現在身無分文，深陷負債。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>deep</b> to describe colours that are strong and fairly dark. 深色的","examples":["The sky was peach coloured in the east, deep blue and starry in the west. 東方的天空色澤桃紅，西方的天空深藍並星光燦爛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>goes deep</b> or <b>runs deep</b>, you mean that it is very serious or strong and is hard to change. 非常嚴重","examples":["His anger and anguish clearly went deep. 很明顯，他的憤怒和痛苦已根深蒂固。"]}]}]},"early":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"早期的，初期的；提早的，提前的；早開花的，早熟的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在早期，在初期；提早，提前"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Early</b> means before the usual time that a particular event or activity happens. 早","examples":["I knew I had to get up early. 我知道我得早起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Early</b> is also an adverb. 在早期","examples":["We'll hope to see you some time early next week. 我們希望在下週初的某個時候見你。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Early</b> means before the time that was arranged or expected. 提前","examples":["She arrived early to get a place at the front. 她提前到達，好在前排找個位置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Early</b> is also an adverb. 在開始階段","examples":["...an incident that occurred much earlier in the game. …一個在比賽剛開始時發生的事件。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Early</b> is also an adverb. 早開花地","examples":["This early flowering gladiolus is not very hardy. 這株開花早的劍蘭不是很耐寒。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Early</b> is also an adjective. 早的","examples":["I decided that I was going to take early retirement. 我決定了我將提早退休。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Early</b> means near the beginning of a day, week, year, or other period of time. 早期的","examples":["...in the 1970s and the early 1980s. …在20世紀70年代和20世紀80年代初期。","She was in her early teens. 她有十三四歲了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Early</b> is also an adjective. 提前的","examples":["I'm always early. 我總是提早。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Early</b> means near the beginning of a period in history, or in the history of something such as the world, a society, or an activity. 早期的; 初期的","examples":["...the early stages of pregnancy. …懷孕初期。","...Fassbinder's early films. …法斯賓德的早期電影。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Early</b> means near the beginning of something such as a piece of work or a process. 開始的","examples":["...the book's early chapters. …該書開頭幾章。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Early</b> refers to plants that flower or crop before or at the beginning of the main season. 早開花的; 早熟的","examples":["...these early cabbages and cauliflowers. …這些早熟的捲心菜和花椰菜。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Early</b> reports or indications of something are the first reports or indications about it. 初期的","examples":["The early indications look encouraging. 初期的跡象看起來鼓舞人心。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>as early as</b> to emphasize that a particular time or period is surprisingly early. 早在","examples":["Inflation could fall back into single figures as early as this month. 通貨膨脹最早在本月就能回落到一位數。"]}]}]},"direct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"徑直的，筆直的；坦率的；直射的；直接的，親身的；正好的；直系的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……對準；管理，指導；給……指路；指引，引導；導演；指示，命令；交予，寄至"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"徑直地，直達地；親自，直接"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Direct</b> means moving toward a place or object, without changing direction and without stopping, for example, in a trip. 直達的","examples":["They'd come on a direct flight from Athens. 他們是從雅典乘坐直達航班來的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is in <b>direct</b> heat or light, it is strongly affected by the heat or light, because there is nothing between it and the source of heat or light to protect it. 直接 (受熱) 的; (光) 直射的","examples":["All medicines should be stored away from moisture, direct sunlight, and heat. 所有藥物應避免儲存在潮溼、陽光直射或者高溫的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>direct</b> to describe an experience, activity, or system which only involves the people, actions, or things that are necessary to make it happen. (經歷、行動、體制等) 直接的","examples":["He has direct experience of the process of privatization. 他有參與私有化過程的直接經驗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>direct</b> to emphasize the closeness of a connection between two things. 直接相關的","examples":["They were unable to prove that the unfortunate lady had died as a direct result of his injection. 他們不能證明那名不幸女士的死亡是由於他的注射直接造成的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>direct</b>, you mean that they are honest and open, and say exactly what they mean. 直率的","examples":["He avoided giving a direct answer. 他迴避作出直截了當的回答。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Direct</b> is also an adverb. 直達地","examples":["You can fly direct from Seattle to Europe. 你可以從西雅圖直飛歐洲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"直達地","examples":["On arriving in New York, Dylan went directly to Greenwich Village. 迪倫一到紐約就直接去了格林威治村。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Direct</b> is also an adverb. 直接地","examples":["More farms are selling direct to consumers. 更多的農場在直接向消費者銷售產品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"直接地","examples":["We cannot measure pain directly. It can only be estimated. 我們無法直接測量疼痛的程度，只能估計。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"直率地","examples":["At your first meeting, explain simply and directly what you hope to achieve. 第一次會面時，簡明扼要、直截了當地說明你希望達到什麼目標。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>direct</b> something <b>at</b> a particular thing, you aim or point it at that thing. 瞄準","examples":["I reached the cockpit and directed the extinguisher at the fire without effect. 我進入駕駛艙，把滅火器對準火焰噴射，但沒有效果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your attention, emotions, or actions <b>are directed</b> <b>at</b> a particular person or thing, you are focusing them on that person or thing. (把注意力、感情或者行動) 集中於…","examples":["The learner's attention needs to be directed to the significant features. 學習者的注意力需要集中在重要特徵上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a remark or look <b>is directed</b> <b>at</b> you, someone says something to you or looks at you. 針對; (目光) 投向","examples":["She could hardly believe the question was directed toward her. 她幾乎不相信這個問題是針對她的。","The abuse was directed at the TV crews. 辱罵是針對電視臺工作人員的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>direct</b> someone somewhere, you tell them how to get there. 指路","examples":["Could you direct them to Dr. Lamont's office, please? 你能告訴他們去拉蒙特醫生的辦公室怎麼走嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When someone <b>directs</b> a project or a group of people, they are responsible for organizing the people and activities that are involved. 指揮","examples":["Christopher will direct day-to-day operations. 克里斯托弗將指揮日常工作。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When someone <b>directs</b> a film, play, or television programme, they are responsible for the way in which it is performed and for telling the actors and assistants what to do. 導演","examples":["He directed various TV shows. 他導演過各種電視節目。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"指揮","examples":["Organizations need clear direction, set priorities and performance standards, and clear controls. 組織需要明確的指揮、即定的主次順序、績效標準，以及正確的管理。"]}]}]},"take":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攜帶，拿走；帶去，引領；使達到，提升；拿，取；移走，拿開；偷走，誤拿；取材於，收集；攻佔，控制；選中，買下；訂閱（報紙等）；吃，服用；減去；記錄，摘錄；照相，攝影；量取，測定；就（座）；以…...為例；接受，收取；接納，接待（顧客、患者等）；遭受，經受；忍受，容忍；（以某種方式）對待，處理；理解，考慮；誤以為；贏得（比賽、競賽等）；產生（感情），持有（看法）；採取（措施），採用（方法）；做，擁有；採用（形式），就任（職位）；花費，佔用（時間）； 需要，要求；使用；穿（特定尺碼的鞋或衣物）；容納；授課；學習，選修（課程）；參加（考試或測驗）；走（路線），乘坐（交通工具）；跨過，跳過；踢，擲；舉行投票，進行民意調查；成功，奏效；（語法）需帶有（某種結構）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（一次拍攝的）鏡頭，場景；收入量；看法，態度；（印刷）一次排版量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>take</b> followed by a noun to talk about an action or event, when it would also be possible to use the verb that is related to that noun. For example, you can say \"<b>she took a shower</b>\" instead of \"she showered.\" 後接名詞描述動作或事件","examples":["She was too tired to take a shower. 她累得不想淋浴了。","Betty took a photograph of us. 貝蒂給我們拍了一張照片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In ordinary spoken or written English, people use <b>take</b> with a range of nouns instead of using a more specific verb. For example, people often say \"<b>he took control</b>\" or \"<b>she took a positive attitude</b>\" instead of \"he assumed control\" or \"she adopted a positive attitude.\" 與許多名詞連用，代替更具體的動詞","examples":["The Patriotic Front took power after a three-month civil war. 愛國陣線經過3個月的內戰後奪取了政權。","I felt it was important for women to join and take a leading role. 我感覺婦女參與並擔任領導角色很重要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something, you reach out for it and hold it. 拿","examples":["Here, let me take your coat. 來，我幫你拿大衣。","Colette took her by the shoulders and shook her. 科利特抓住她的雙肩，搖晃著她。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something with you when you go somewhere, you carry it or have it with you. 隨身帶著","examples":["Mark often took his books to Bess's house to study. 馬克經常帶著書去貝絲家學習。","You should take your passport with you when changing money. 你換匯時應該帶著你的護照。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person, vehicle, or path <b>takes</b> someone somewhere, they transport or lead them there. 運送; 帶領","examples":["She took me to a Mexican restaurant. 她帶我去了一家墨西哥餐館。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something such as a job or interest <b>takes</b> you to a place, it is the reason for you going there. (工作或興趣等) 使某人去","examples":["He was a poor student from Madras whose genius took him to Stanford. 他是個來自馬德拉斯的窮學生，他的才華使他考上了斯坦福。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something such as your problems or your business to someone, you go to that person when you have problems you want to discuss or things you want to buy. 請教 (問題); 洽談 (生意)","examples":["You need to take your problems to a trained counsellor. 你需要向一位訓練有素的顧問請教你的問題。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If one thing <b>takes</b> another <b>to</b> a particular level, condition, or state, it causes it to reach that level or condition. 使達到 (某種水平或狀態)","examples":["A combination of talent, hard work and good looks have taken her to the top. 天賦、勤奮和美貌的組合使她成了佼佼者。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something from a place, you remove it from there. 拿走","examples":["He took a handkerchief from his pocket and lightly wiped his mouth. 他從口袋裡拿出一塊手帕，輕輕地擦了擦嘴。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something from someone who owns it, you steal it or go away with it without their permission. 偷走; 擅自拿走","examples":["He has taken my money, and I have no chance of getting it back. 他偷了我的錢，我不可能把它要回來了。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If an army or political party <b>takes</b> something or someone, they win them from their enemy or opponent. 奪取","examples":["A Serb army unit took the town. 一支塞爾維亞部隊奪取了這個鎮。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> one number or amount from another, you subtract it or deduct it. 減去","examples":["Take off the price of the house, that's another hundred thousand. 減去房價，又是10萬。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you cannot <b>take</b> something difficult, painful, or annoying, you cannot tolerate it without becoming upset, ill, or angry. 忍受","examples":["Don't ever ask me to look after those kids again. I just can't take it! 不要再叫我照看那些孩子們了。我簡直無法忍受！"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something such as damage or loss, you suffer it, especially in war or in a battle. (尤指在戰爭中) 遭受","examples":["They have taken heavy casualties. 他們遭受了慘重的傷亡。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something <b>takes</b> a certain amount of time, that amount of time is needed in order to do it. 花費 (時間)","examples":["Since the roads are very bad, the trip took us a long time. 由於道路很差，這次旅程花費了我們很長時間。","I had heard an appeal could take years. 我已聽說一項訴訟可能要花費好幾年時間。","The sauce takes 25 minutes to prepare and cook. 從準備到烹製成這種調味汁需要25分鐘。","It takes 15 minutes to convert the plane into a car by removing the wings and the tail. 拆除機翼和機尾，把那架飛機改成汽車需要15分鐘的時間。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If something <b>takes</b> a particular quality or thing, that quality or thing is needed in order to do it. 需要 (某種品質或事物)","examples":["At one time, walking across the room took all her strength. 曾經有段時間，穿過這個房間得用盡她全部的力氣。","It takes courage to say what you think. 說出你的想法需要勇氣。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something that is given or offered to you, you agree to accept it. 接受","examples":["When I took the job I thought I could change the system, but it's hard. 當我接受這份工作時我以為我能改變這種體制，但太難了。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a feeling such as pleasure, pride, or delight in a particular thing or activity, it gives you that feeling. 感到","examples":["They take great pride in their heritage. 他們為自己的傳統感到十分自豪。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a prize or medal, you win it. 贏得","examples":["\"Poison\" took first prize at the 1991 Sundance Film Festival. 《毒藥》在1991年的聖丹斯電影節上贏得一等獎。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> the blame, responsibility, or credit for something, you agree to accept it. 承擔","examples":["His brother Raoul did it, but Leonel took the blame and kept his mouth shut. 萊昂內爾的兄弟拉烏爾做了這件事，但萊昂內爾承擔了責任而且對此絕口不提。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> patients or clients, you accept them as your patients or clients. 接納","examples":["Some universities would be forced to take more students than they wanted. 有些大學將被迫接納比他們想要的更多的學生。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a telephone call, you speak to someone who is telephoning you. 接聽 (電話)","examples":["Douglas telephoned Catherine at her office. She refused to take his calls. 道格拉斯把電話打到凱瑟琳的辦公室。她拒絕接聽他的電話。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something in a particular way, you react in the way mentioned to a situation or to someone's beliefs or behaviour. (以某種方式) 看待","examples":["Unfortunately, no one took my opinion seriously. 不幸的是，沒有人嚴肅地看待我的意見。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"You use <b>take</b> when you are discussing or explaining a particular question, in order to introduce an example or to say how the question is being considered. 舉出… (為例)","examples":["There's confusion and resentment, and it's almost never expressed out in the open. Take this office, for example. 混亂和怨恨是存在的，而幾乎從沒人公開表露出來過。就以這個辦公室為例。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone's meaning or point, you understand and accept what they are saying. 理解","examples":["I had made it as plain as I could so that he could not fail to take my meaning. 我已經盡我所能地說明白，所以他不會不理解我的意思。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone <b>for</b> something, you believe wrongly that they are that thing. 把…錯當成","examples":["She had taken him for a journalist. 她把他錯當成記者了。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a road or route, you choose to travel along it. 選擇走 (某條路)","examples":["From the community college take Old Mill Road to the outskirts of town. 從社群學院出發，走老磨坊路到達市郊。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a car, train, bus, or plane, you use it to go from one place to another. 搭乘","examples":["It's the other end of town so we should take the car. 它在城鎮的那頭，因此我們應該乘車去。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a subject or course at school or college, you choose to study it. 選修","examples":["Students are allowed to take European history and American history. 學生被允許選修歐洲史和美國史。"]},{"num":"30.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a test or examination, you do it in order to show your knowledge or ability. 參加 (考試)","examples":["She took her driving test yesterday. 她昨天參加了駕照考試。"]},{"num":"31.","zh":"If someone <b>takes</b> drugs, pills, or other medicines, they take them into their body, for example, by swallowing them. 服用","examples":["She's been taking sleeping pills. 她一直在服用安眠藥。"]},{"num":"32.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a note or a letter, you write down something you want to remember or the words that someone says. 寫下","examples":["She sat expressionless, carefully taking notes. 她面無表情地坐著，仔細地記著筆記。"]},{"num":"33.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a measurement, you find out what it is by measuring. 測量","examples":["By drilling, geologists can take measurements at various depths. 透過鑽孔，地質學家可以在不同深度測量。"]},{"num":"34.","zh":"If a place or container <b>takes</b> a particular amount or number, there is enough space for that amount or number. 容納","examples":["The place could just about take 2,000 people. 這個地方只能容納大約兩千人。"]},{"num":"35.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a particular size in shoes or clothes, that size fits you. 穿 (某個尺寸的鞋子或衣服)","examples":["\"What size do you take?\"—\"I take a size 7.\" “你穿多少號？”—“我穿7號。”"]},{"num":"36.","zh":"If a shop, restaurant, theatre, or other business <b>takes</b> a certain amount of money, they get that amount from people buying goods or services. 賺得","examples":["They plan to take £1.6 billion. 他們計劃要收入16億美元。"]},{"num":"37.","zh":"If you <b>are taken</b> <b>by</b> someone, you are cheated or deceived by them. 欺騙","examples":["They got taken by a scam artist. 他們被一個假冒的藝術家騙了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>take</b> to refer to the amount of money that a business such as a shop or theatre gets from selling its goods or tickets during a particular period. 營業收入","examples":["It added another $11.8 million to the take, for a grand total of $43 million. 它又增加了1180萬美元的營業收入，總計為4300萬美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>take</b> is a short piece of action which is filmed in one continuous process for a movie. (電影中一次連續拍攝的) 鏡頭","examples":["She couldn't get it right – she never knew the lines and we had to do several takes. 她就是做不好–她一直不熟悉臺詞，我們只好一個鏡頭拍好幾次。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>take</b> <b>on</b> a particular situation or fact is their attitude to it or their interpretation of it. 態度; 解釋","examples":["What's your take on the new government? Do you think it can work? 你對新政府持什麼態度？你認為它能行嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say to someone \"<b>take it or leave it</b>,\" you are telling them that they can accept something or not accept it, but that you are not prepared to discuss any other alternatives. 要麼接受，要麼走開","examples":["A 72-hour week, 12 hours a day, six days a week, take it or leave it. 1周72小時，每天12小時，每週6天，要麼接受，要麼走開。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>takes</b> an insult or attack <b>lying down</b>, they accept it without protesting. 心甘情願地忍受","examples":["The government is not taking such criticism lying down. 政府不會心甘情願地忍受這種批評。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>takes a lot out of</b> you or <b>takes it out of</b> you, it requires a lot of energy or effort and makes you feel very tired and weak afterward. 使某人筋疲力盡","examples":["He looked tired, as if the argument had taken a lot out of him. 他看上去累了，似乎這場辯論已使他筋疲力盡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone tells you to <b>take five</b> or to <b>take ten</b>, they are telling you to have a five or ten minute break from what you are doing. 休息5分鐘; 休息10分鐘","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>on the take</b> is receiving illegal income such as bribes. 受賄","examples":["I can also name cops who are on the take. 我也能說出受賄警察的名字。"]}]}]},"even":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平坦的，水平的；平靜的，平和的；平齊的，挨著的；無變化的，平穩的；勢均力敵的，不相上下的；雙數的，偶數的；平等的，公平的；不變的，恆定的；（某事發生的機率）對半的，各半的；扯平的，互不相欠的；勻稱的，同樣大小的；正好的，不多不少的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"甚至，即使；更加，愈加；其實，實際上"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使相等，使平均；變平坦；使變平，使平整"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>傍晚，晚上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>even</b> to suggest that what comes just after or just before it in the sentence is rather surprising. 甚至; 連","examples":["He kept calling me for years, even after he got married. 他多年來不斷給我打電話，甚至到他結婚以後。","Even dark-skinned women should use sunscreens. 就連膚色黑的女性也應該用防曬油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>even</b> with comparative adjectives and adverbs to emphasize a quality that someone or something has. (與比較級連用) 更加","examples":["On television he made an even stronger impact as an interviewer. 他作為採訪者在電視上造成了更大的影響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"保持不變地","examples":["He looked at Ellen, breathing evenly in her sleep. 他看著在睡夢中呼吸均勻的埃倫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"均等地","examples":["The meat is divided evenly and boiled in a stew. 肉被均等地切開並在鍋裡燉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"實力相當地","examples":["They must choose between two evenly matched candidates for governor. 他們必須從兩個不相上下的候選人中選出州長。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>even if</b> or <b>even though</b> to indicate that a particular fact does not make the rest of your statement untrue. 即使","examples":["Cynthia is not ashamed of what she does, even if she ends up doing something wrong. 辛西婭並不為她所做的事感到慚愧，即使她最終把事情做錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>even so</b> to introduce a surprising fact that relates to what you have just said. 即便如此; 儘管這樣","examples":["The bus was only half full. Even so, a young man asked Nina if the seat next to her was taken. 公共汽車上只坐滿了一半，即便如此，一個小夥子還問尼娜她旁邊的座位有沒有人坐。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>even then</b> to say that something is the case in spite of what has just been stated or whatever the circumstances may be. 即便那樣","examples":["Peace could come only gradually, in carefully measured steps. Even then, it sounds almost impossible to achieve. 和平只能以謹慎的步伐逐步到來。即便那樣，它聽起來還是幾乎不可能實現。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a company or a person running a business <b>breaks even</b>, they make neither a profit nor a loss. 盈虧平衡","examples":["The airline hopes to break even next year and return to profit the following year. 該航空公司希望來年盈虧平衡，並在隨後一年重新開始盈利。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>even</b> measurement or rate stays at about the same level. 保持不變的","examples":["How important is it to have an even temperature when you're working? 工作時保持恆溫有多重要？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>even</b> surface is smooth and flat. 平滑的","examples":["The tables are fitted with a glass top to provide an even surface. 那些桌子都裝有玻璃檯面以提供平滑的表面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is an <b>even</b> distribution or division of something, each person, group, or area involved has an equal amount. 均等的","examples":["Divide the dough into 12 even pieces and shape each piece into a ball. 把麵糰分為12等份並把每一塊麵團揉成球形。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>even</b> contest or competition is equally balanced between the two sides who are taking part. 實力相當的","examples":["It was an even game. 這是一場勢均力敵的比賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>even</b> number can be divided exactly by the number two. 偶數的","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If there is an <b>even</b> chance that something will happen, the chances that it will or will not happen are equal. (機會) 各半的","examples":["They have a more than even chance of winning the next election. 他們在下次競選中有過半的勝機。"]}]}]},"ever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"曾經，從來，在任何時候；一直，始終；越來越，愈發；究竟，到底；非常，確實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ever</b> means at any time. It is used in questions and negative statements. 在任何時候 (用於否定句和疑問句)","examples":["I'm not sure I'll ever trust people again. 我不確定我會不會再相信人。","Neither of us had ever skied. 我們倆誰也沒有滑過雪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>ever</b> in expressions such as \"<b>did you ever</b>\" and \"<b>have you ever</b>\" to express surprise or shock at something you have just seen, heard, or experienced, especially when you expect people to agree with you. 曾經 (表示驚訝)","examples":["Have you ever seen anything like it? 你可曾見過像這樣的東西？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>ever</b> after comparatives and superlatives to emphasize the degree to which something is true or when you are comparing a present situation with the past or the future. 以往任何時候 (用於形容詞或副詞的比較級和最高階之後)","examples":["She's got a great voice and is singing better than ever. 她有一副好嗓音，比以往任何時候都唱得好。","Japan is wealthier and more powerful than ever before. 日本現在比以往任何時候都富有和強大。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>ever</b> to say that something happens more all the time. 愈發","examples":["They grew ever further apart. 他們愈發疏遠了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>ever</b> for emphasis after \"never.\" 絕不 (用於“)(never)(”後，表示強調)","examples":["I can never, ever, forgive myself. 我絕不能原諒自己。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>ever</b> in questions beginning with words such as \"why,\" \"when,\" and \"who\" when you want to emphasize your surprise or shock. 究竟 (用於特殊疑問句以強調語氣)","examples":["Why ever didn't you tell me? 你究竟為何不告訴我？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Ever</b> is also an adverb. 從此","examples":["I simply gave in to him, and I've regretted it ever since. 我當時完全向他屈服了，從此我為此事後悔不迭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something has been the case <b>ever since</b> a particular time, it has been the case all the time from then until now. 自從","examples":["He's been there ever since you left! 自從你離開，他一直都在那兒！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use the expression <b>all</b> someone <b>ever does</b> when you want to emphasize that they do the same thing all the time, and this annoys you. (某人) 只會…","examples":["All she ever does is complain. 她就會抱怨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>as ever</b> in order to indicate that something or someone's behaviour is not unusual because it is like that all the time or very often. 一如既往","examples":["As ever, the meals are primarily fish-based. 像往常那樣，餐餐以魚類為主。"]}]}]},"how":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"怎樣，如何；（指狀況、情況）好否，怎麼樣；（用於詢問數量、程度）多少，怎麼；（強調程度）多麼，何等；（用於引出想要談及的事實）"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"怎樣，如何；以任何方式，無論用什麼方法"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"方式，方法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> to ask about the way in which something happens or is done. 怎樣; 如何","examples":["How do I make payments into my account? 我怎樣付款到我的賬戶呢？","How do you manage to keep the place so neat? 你是怎麼把這個地方保持得如此整潔的呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> to ask questions about the quantity or degree of something.  多少","examples":["How much money are we talking about? 我們所說的這筆錢有多大數目？","How many full-time staff have we got? 我們有多少全職員工？","How long will you be staying? 你要呆多長時間？","How old is your son now? 現在你兒子有多大？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> when you are asking someone whether something was successful or enjoyable. (用以詢問某人某事是否順利或愉快) 怎麼樣","examples":["How was your trip down to Orlando? 你南下奧蘭多之旅怎麼樣？","How did your date go? 你的約會怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> to ask about someone's health or to find out someone's news. (用以詢問某人健康或有關某人的訊息) 怎樣","examples":["Hi! How are you doing? 你好！最近怎麼樣？","How's Rosie? 羅茜身體好嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> in expressions such as \"<b>How can you...</b>\" and \"<b>How could you...</b>\" to indicate that you disapprove of what someone has done or that you find it hard to believe. 你怎麼能… (表示不贊成或很難相信)","examples":["How can you drink so much beer, Luke? 盧克，你怎麼可以喝這麼多啤酒？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> in expressions such as \"<b>How about...</b>\" or \"<b>How would you like...</b>\" when you are making an offer or a suggestion. …怎麼樣 (表示提出建議)","examples":["How about a cup of coffee? 來杯咖啡怎麼樣？"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>How</b> is also a conjunction. 用作連詞","examples":["I don't want to know how he died. 我不想知道他是如何死的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> after certain adjectives and verbs to introduce a statement or fact, often something that you remember or expect other people to know about. 用於某些形容詞或動詞後，以引出一個陳述或事實","examples":["It's amazing how people collect so much stuff over the years. 人們這些年下來竟能收集到這麼多東西，真令人驚奇。","It's funny how I never seem to get a thing done on my day off. 好笑的是，在休息日裡我好像從沒做成一件事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> to emphasize the degree to which something is true. (用以強調某事的真實程度) 多麼","examples":["I didn't realize how heavy that bag was going to be. 我沒有想到那個包會有多重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>how</b> in exclamations to emphasize an adjective, adverb, or statement. (用於感嘆句中以強調形容詞、副詞或句子) 多麼","examples":["How strange that something so simple as a walk on the beach could suddenly mean so much. 在海灘上散步這麼簡單的事突然間變得意義如此重大，真是奇怪。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you ask someone \"<b>How about you?</b>\" you are asking them what they think or want. 你呢 (用以詢問對方的想法或要求)","examples":["Well, I enjoyed that. How about you two? 嗯，我很喜歡那個。你倆覺得呢？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the way a thing is done 方式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"sentence substitute.","pos_name":"sentence substitute.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a greeting supposed to be or have been used by American Indians and often used humorously 問候語; 美國印第安人的幽默招呼用語","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>how about</b> to introduce a new subject which you think is relevant to the conversation you have been having. …怎麼樣 (用以引導一個與正在談論的話題有關的新題目)","examples":["Are your products and services competitive? How about marketing? 你們的產品和服務具有競爭力嗎？營銷怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You ask \"<b>How come?</b>\" or \"<b>How so?</b>\" when you are surprised by something and are asking why it happened or was said. 怎麼會這樣 (由於吃驚而詢問)","examples":["\"They don't say a single word to each other.\"—\"How come?\" “他們相互不說一句話。”—“怎麼會這樣？”"]}]}]},"clear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易懂的，明白的；明顯的，明確的；完全瞭解的，清楚的；透明的，清澈的；易看清的，聽得清的；（顏色）明亮的，鮮明的；（皮膚）光潔的；沒有問題的，健康的；晴朗的；暢通的，無阻礙的；（時間）空閒的；完整的；問心無愧的，清白的；頭腦清醒的，思維敏銳的；（比分）領先的；未碰觸的，懸離的；擺脫掉（不愉快事物）的；（錢款）淨得的，純收入的；發音清晰的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"清除，清理；恢復暢通，不再受阻；證明……無罪；批准，許可；准許……入境（出境）；（使）不再困惑，（使）變清醒；獲利，淨賺；清償（債務）；兌現（支票）；（天氣）變晴朗；（液體）變清澈；（視力）變清晰；（煙霧等）開始消失；（皮膚）變光滑，變健康；（表情）放鬆，舒展；使離開，清場；穿過，越過；解決，成功地處理；做完（所有工作）；踢出解圍球"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美>一直；離開，不靠近；清除了地，理清了地；全地，整地，滿地，足地；清楚地，清晰地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"清白的，無罪的（in the clear）；不再困難的，已脫險的（in the clear）；清除；空隙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>clear</b> is easy to understand, see, or hear. 清楚的; 明白易懂的","examples":["The book is clear, readable, and adequately illustrated. 這本書易懂易讀，而且圖解充足。","The space telescope has taken the clearest pictures ever of Pluto. 太空望遠鏡拍下了有史以來最清晰的冥王星的照片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>clear</b> is obvious and impossible to be mistaken about. 明顯的","examples":["It was a clear case of homicide. 這是一起確信無疑的謀殺案。","It became clear that I hadn't been able to convince Mike. 顯然我沒能說服邁克。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>clear</b> <b>about</b> something, you understand it completely. 徹底明白的","examples":["It is important to be clear about what Chomsky is doing here. 明確喬姆斯基在這幹什麼很重要。","He is not entirely clear on how he will go about it. 他不完全清楚要如何著手做這件事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your mind or your way of thinking is <b>clear</b>, you are able to think sensibly and reasonably, and you are not affected by confusion or by a drug such as alcohol. (頭腦) 清醒的","examples":["She needed a clear head to carry out her instructions. 她需要一個清醒的頭腦來執行命令。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>clear</b> substance is one which you can see through and which has no colour, like clean water. 透明的","examples":["...a clear glass panel. …一塊透明的玻璃鑲板。","...a clear gel. …一種透明的凝膠。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a surface, place, or view is <b>clear</b>, it is free of unwanted objects or obstacles. 無障礙物的; 開闊的","examples":["The runway is clear – go ahead and land. 跑道暢通無阻–繼續前行並著陸。","Caroline prefers her countertops to be clear of clutter. 卡羅琳喜歡廚房檯面上沒有雜亂的東西。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If it is a <b>clear</b> day or if the sky is <b>clear</b>, there is no mist, rain, or cloud. 晴朗的","examples":["On a clear day you can see the coast. 天晴時你能看見海岸。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Clear</b> eyes look healthy, attractive, and shining. (眼睛) 明亮的","examples":["...clear blue eyes. …明亮的藍眼睛。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If your skin is <b>clear</b>, it is healthy and free from blemishes. (皮膚) 光潔的","examples":["No amount of cleansing or mineral water consumption can guarantee a clear skin. 再多的潔膚和礦泉水的消耗都不能確保光潔的皮膚。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>clear</b> <b>of</b> something else, it is not touching it or is a safe distance away from it. 不與…接觸的; 不與…靠近的","examples":["As soon as he was clear of the terminal building, he looked around. 他一走出航站樓就四處張望。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that your conscience is <b>clear</b>, you mean you do not think you have done anything wrong. 問心無愧的","examples":["Mr. Garcia said his conscience was clear over the jail incidents. 加西亞先生說對監獄發生的事他問心無愧。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"清楚地; 明白易懂地","examples":["Whales journey up the coast of California, clearly visible from the beach. 鯨魚們朝著加利福尼亞海岸游過來，從海灘就能清楚地看見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"顯然無疑地","examples":["Clearly, the police cannot break the law in order to enforce it. 顯然地，警察不能為了執法而違法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"清醒地","examples":["The only time I can think clearly is when I'm alone. 我能清醒思考的惟一時間就是當我獨處時。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clear</b> your mind or your head means to free it from confused thoughts or from the effects of a drug such as alcohol. 使清醒","examples":["He walked up Fifth Avenue to clear his head. 他在第五大街上走，讓頭腦清醒清醒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>clear</b> an area or place or <b>clear</b> something <b>from</b> it, you remove things from it that you do not want to be there. 清空; 清理出","examples":["To clear the land and harvest the bananas, they decided they needed a male workforce. 為了清理土地和收割香蕉，他們決定需要男勞力。","Workers could not clear the tunnels of smoke. 工人們無法把煙從隧道里全部排出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a bank <b>clears</b> a cheque or when a cheque <b>clears</b>, the bank agrees to pay the sum of money mentioned on it. 兌現","examples":["Banks can still take two or three weeks to clear a cheque. 銀行還要兩三週的時間才能兌現支票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something or someone <b>clears</b> the way or the path <b>for</b> something to happen, they make it possible. 使…成為可能","examples":["The prime minister resigned today, clearing the way for the formation of a new government. 首相今天辭職了，為新政府的組建鋪平了道路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a course of action <b>is cleared</b>, people in authority give permission for it to happen. 允許","examples":["Linda Gradstein has this report from Jerusalem, which was cleared by an Israeli censor. 琳達•格雷德斯坦從耶路撒冷報道，該報道已經被以色列審查員批准了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>is cleared</b>, they are proved to be not guilty of a crime or mistake. 宣判無罪","examples":["She was cleared of murder and jailed for just five years for manslaughter. 她謀殺罪不成立，只為過失殺人罪坐了5年牢。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Is that clear?</b>\" or \"<b>Do I make myself clear?</b>\" after you have told someone your wishes or instructions, to make sure that they have understood you, and to emphasize your authority. 清楚了嗎？/我說明白了嗎？","examples":["We're only going for half an hour, and you're not going to buy anything. Is that clear? 我們只去半個小時，你不許買任何東西。明白了嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> something <b>clear</b>, you say something in a way that makes it impossible for there to be any doubt about your meaning, wishes, or intentions. 把事情說明白","examples":["Mr. O'Friel made it clear that further insults of this kind would not be tolerated. 奧弗瑞爾先生把意思說得清清楚楚，以後這種侮辱是不會被容忍的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>in the clear</b>, they are not in danger, or are not blamed or suspected of anything. 沒有危險的; 無辜的","examples":["It would be stupid to do anything until we know we're in the clear. 在得知我們沒有危險之前採取任何行動，那會是愚蠢的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When fog or mist <b>clears</b>, it gradually disappears. (煙霧等) 消散","examples":["The early morning mist had cleared. 清晨的霧氣已經消散了。"]}]}]},"fast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"快的，迅速的；繫牢的，緊縛的；尋歡作樂的；不褪色的；忠實的，可靠的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"快速地；堅定地，牢固地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"齋戒，禁食"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"齋戒，齋戒期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fast</b> means happening, moving, or doing something at great speed. You also use <b>fast</b> in questions or statements about speed. 迅速的","examples":["...fast cars with flashing lights and sirens. …閃燈、鳴笛、快速行駛的汽車。","The only question is how fast the process will be. 惟一的問題是這個過程會有多快。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a watch or clock is <b>fast</b>, it is showing a time that is later than the real time. (鐘錶) 快於準確時間的","examples":["That clock's an hour fast. 那個鐘快了一個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If colours or dyes are <b>fast</b>, they do not come out of the fabrics they are used on when they get wet. 不褪色的","examples":["The fabric was ironed to make the colours fast. 這布被熨燙過以使其不褪色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Fast</b> is also an adjective. 毫不耽擱的","examples":["That would be an astonishingly fast action on the part of the Congress. 那將是國會方面一次快得驚人的行動。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fast</b> is also an adverb. 迅速地","examples":["They work terrifically fast. 他們工作極快。","It would be nice to go faster and break the world record. 再快一些，打破世界紀錄就好了。","How fast would the disease develop? 這種疾病發展有多快？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>fast</b> to say that something happens without any delay. 毫不耽擱地","examples":["When you've got a crisis like this you need professional help – fast!. 在遇到這樣的危機時，你需要專業的救助–絲毫不能耽擱！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you hold something <b>fast</b>, you hold it tightly and firmly. If something is stuck <b>fast</b>, it is stuck very firmly and cannot move. 緊緊地","examples":["She climbed the staircase cautiously, holding fast to the rail. 她緊握扶手，小心翼翼地爬上樓梯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you hold <b>fast</b> to a principle or idea, or if you stand <b>fast</b>, you do not change your mind about it, even though people are trying to persuade you to. 堅定地","examples":["We can only try to hold fast to the age-old values of honesty, decency and concern for others. 我們只能努力堅守那些古老的價值觀：誠實、正派、關心他人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fast</b>, you eat no food for a period of time, usually for either religious or medical reasons, or as a protest. (因宗教、醫療或抗議等原因) 禁食","examples":["I fasted for a day and a half and asked God to help me. 我禁食了一天半，請求上帝幫助我。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fast</b> is also a noun. 禁食","examples":["The fast is broken at sunset, traditionally with dates and water. 日落時開齋，按傳統會吃海棗、喝水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"禁食","examples":["...the Muslim holy month of fasting and prayer. …穆斯林齋戒和祈禱的聖月。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>fast asleep</b> is completely asleep. 熟睡","examples":["When he went upstairs five minutes later, she was fast asleep. 他5分鐘後上樓時，她已熟睡。"]}]}]},"far":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"遠，遙遠地；久遠地；非常，很大程度上；發展，進展（到）；過分地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遙遠的，久遠的；另一邊的，較遠的；偏遠的，極端的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one place, thing, or person is <b>far</b> away from another, there is a great distance between them. 很遠地","examples":["I know a nice little Italian restaurant not far from here. 我知道一家很好的義大利小餐館離這兒不遠。","Both of my sisters moved even farther away from home. 我的兩個姐妹都搬得離家更遠了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you ask <b>how</b> <b>far</b> a place is, you are asking what distance it is from you or from another place. If you ask <b>how</b> <b>far</b> someone went, you are asking what distance they travelled, or what place they reached. (距離) 遠至","examples":["How far is Pawtucket from Providence? 波塔基特離普羅維登斯有多遠？","How far is it to Malcy? 這裡到馬爾錫有多遠？","She followed the tracks as far as the road. 她沿著小徑一直走到公路邊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A time or event that is <b>far</b> away in the future or the past is a long time from the present or from a particular point in time. 久遠地","examples":["...hidden conflicts whose roots lie far back in time. …根源久遠的各種隱藏的衝突。","I can't see any farther than the next six months. 我無法預見比6個月更往後的事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>far</b> to talk about the extent or degree to which something happens or is true. 到…程度","examples":["How far did the film tell the truth about Barnes Wallis? 這部電影對巴恩斯·沃利斯的講述有多大程度的真實性？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can talk about how <b>far</b> someone or something gets to describe the progress that they make. (進展) 到…程度","examples":["Discussions never progressed very far. 討論從未有太大進展。","Think of how far we have come in a little time. 想一想我們在短時間內已經有了多麼大的進展。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can talk about how <b>far</b> a person or action goes to describe the degree to which someone's behaviour or actions are extreme. (人或行為) 極端到…程度","examples":["It's still not clear how far the Russian parliament will go to implement its own plans. 現在還不清楚俄羅斯議會在實施其計劃方面會極端到何種程度。","Competition can be healthy, but if it is pushed too far it can result in bullying. 競爭可以是良性的，但如果被推向極端，就會導致恃強凌弱。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>far</b> in expressions like \"<b>as far as I know</b>\" and \"<b>so far as I remember</b>\" to indicate that you are not absolutely sure of the statement you are about to make or have just made, and you may be wrong. 用於(as far as I know##far)和(so far as I remember)中，意為“據我所知”和“就我記憶所及”","examples":["It only lasted a couple of years, as far as I know. 據我所知，它僅維持了幾年。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>far</b> to mean \"very much\" when you are comparing two things and emphasizing the difference between them. For example, you can say that something is <b>far better</b> or <b>far worse</b> than something else to indicate that it is very much better or worse. You can also say that something is, for example, <b>far too big</b> to indicate that it is very much too big. (作比較時用於強調) …得多","examples":["Women who eat plenty of fresh vegetables are far less likely to suffer anxiety or depression. 吃大量新鮮蔬菜的女人患焦慮症或抑鬱症的機率要少得多。","The police say the response has been far better than expected. 警方說反應比預料的好得多。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there are two things of the same kind in a place, <b>the</b> <b>far</b> one is the one that is a greater distance from you. 較遠一端的","examples":["He had wandered to the far end of the room. 他已漫步走到房間的那一頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>far</b> to refer to the part of an area or object that is the greatest distance from the centre in a particular direction. For example, <b>the</b> <b>far</b> north <b>of</b> a country is the part of it that is the greatest distance to the north. (離中心) 最大距離的","examples":["A storm was brewing off Port Angeles in the far north of Washington State. 一場暴風雨正在華盛頓州最北端的安吉利斯港外醞釀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe people with extreme left-wing or right-wing political views as the <b>far</b> left or the <b>far</b> right. (政治觀點) 極端的","examples":["The far right is now a greater threat than the extreme left. 極右派現在是一個比極左派更大的威脅。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>will go far</b>, you mean that they will be very successful in their career. 大有前途","examples":["I was very impressed with the talent of Michael Ball. He will go far. 我對邁克爾·鮑爾的天賦印象極為深刻。他將前途無量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>far gone</b> is in such a bad state or condition that not much can be done to help or improve them. 無藥可救的; 迴天無力的","examples":["In his last few days the pain seemed to have stopped, but by then he was so far gone that it was no longer any comfort. 在他最後的幾天裡疼痛似乎已經停止，但那時他已病入膏肓，這已不再是什麼安慰了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use the expression \"<b>as far as I can see</b>\" when you are about to state your opinion of a situation, or have just stated it, to indicate that it is your personal opinion. 在我看來","examples":["That's the problem as far as I can see. 在我看來，那就是問題所在。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something only goes <b>so far</b> or can only go <b>so far</b>, you mean that its extent, effect, or influence is limited. (程度、作用、影響) 僅能如此","examples":["Their loyalty only went so far. 他們的忠誠只能到這個程度。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you tell or ask someone what has happened <b>so far</b>, you are telling or asking them what has happened up until the present point in a situation or story, and often implying that something different might happen later. 到目前為止","examples":["It's been quiet so far. 到目前為止還是安靜的。","So far, they have met with no success. 到目前為止，他們還沒有成功過。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say <b>so far so good</b> to express satisfaction with the way that a situation or activity is progressing, developing, or happening. 到目前為止還算良好","examples":["Of course, it's a case of so far, so good, but it's only one step. 當然，到目前為止一切都還順利，但它只是一步而已。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use the expression <b>by far</b> when you are comparing something or someone with others of the same kind, in order to emphasize how great the difference is between them. For example, you can say that something is <b>by far the best</b> or <b>the best by far</b> to indicate that it is definitely the best. (比較時強調差異巨大) 顯然","examples":["By far the most important issue for them is unemployment. 顯然對他們來說最重要的問題是失業。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>far from</b> a particular thing or <b>far from</b> being the case, you are emphasizing that it is not that particular thing or not at all the case, especially when people expect or assume that it is. 絕非","examples":["It was obvious that much of what they recorded was far from the truth. 很顯然，他們所記錄的很多內容絕非事實。","Far from being relaxed, we both felt so uncomfortable we hardly spoke. 我們倆非但沒有放鬆，反而覺得很不舒服，我們幾乎沒說話。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use the expression \"<b>far from it</b>\" to emphasize a negative statement that you have just made. (用於強調否定陳述) 絕非如此","examples":["Being dyslexic does not mean that one is unintelligent. Far from it. 誦讀困難並不意味著人不聰明。絕非如此。"]}]}]},"free":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"免費的；自由的；隨心所欲的；不含……的；免於，不遭受；空閒的；未使用的，空著的；無阻礙的；不拘泥於原文的；遊離的；不吝惜的；乾淨整潔的；（風）順的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"自由地；免費地；帆腳索被鬆開地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"釋放；使解脫出來；使免於；使可用於；使能騰出時間"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>自由轉會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>free</b>, you can have it or use it without paying for it. 免費的","examples":["The seminars are free, with lunch provided. 研討會是免費的，還提供午餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>free</b> is not restricted, controlled, or limited, for example, by rules, customs, or other people. 自由的; 不受限制的","examples":["The government will be free to pursue its economic policies. 政府將自由實行其經濟政策。","The elections were free and fair. 選舉是自由公正的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>free</b> is no longer a prisoner or a slave. 自由的","examples":["He walked from the court house a free man. 他走出法庭，重獲自由。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>free of</b> or <b>free from</b> an unpleasant thing, they do not have it or they are not affected by it. 沒有…的","examples":["...a future far more free of fear. …遠無恐懼的未來。","She retains her slim figure and is free of wrinkles. 她保持著苗條的身材，而且沒有皺紋。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A sum of money or type of goods that is <b>free of</b> tax or duty is one that you do not have to pay tax on. 免去…的","examples":["This benefit is free of tax under current legislation. 按照現行法律此項收益是免稅的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have a <b>free</b> period of time or are <b>free</b> at a particular time, you are not working or occupied then. 空閒的","examples":["She spent her free time shopping. 她將空閒時間花在購物上。","I used to write during my free periods at school. 我過去上學時常在空閒時間寫作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something such as a table or seat is <b>free</b>, it is not being used or occupied by anyone, or is not reserved for anyone to use. (桌子或座位) 空著的","examples":["There was only one seat free on the train. 火車上只有一個空座。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you get something <b>free</b> or if it gets <b>free</b>, it is no longer trapped by anything or attached to anything. 不受束縛的","examples":["He pulled his arm free, and strode for the door. 他抽出他的胳膊擺脫束縛，大步朝門走去。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When someone is using one hand or arm to hold or move something, their other hand or arm is referred to as their <b>free</b> one. 空閒的 (手或胳膊)","examples":["He snatched up the receiver and his free hand groped for the switch on the bedside lamp. 他一把抓起聽筒，空著的手則摸索著找床頭燈的開關。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自由地","examples":["They cast their votes freely and without coercion on election day. 他們在選舉日自由地投票，不受強迫。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>free</b> someone of something that is unpleasant or restricting, you remove it from them. 使免除","examples":["It will free us of a whole lot of debt. 這將免除我們一大筆債務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>free</b> a prisoner or a slave means to let them go or release them from prison. 釋放","examples":["Israel is set to free more Lebanese prisoners. 以色列準備釋放更多黎巴嫩犯人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>free</b> someone or something means to make them available for a task or function that they were previously not available for. 解放","examples":["Toolbelts free both hands and lessen the risk of dropping hammers. 工具帶解放了雙手，並減少了錘子掉落的危險。","His deal with Disney will run out shortly, freeing him to pursue his own project. 他同迪斯尼的協議不久就將結束，這可以使他騰出手來從事自己的專案。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>free</b> someone or something, you remove them from the place in which they have been trapped or become fixed. 解救","examples":["Rescue workers tried to free him by cutting away part of the car. 救援人員設法透過切除部分車體將他解救出來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Free up</b> means the same as . 使解放","examples":["It can handle even the most complex graphic jobs, freeing up your computer for other tasks. 它甚至能處理最複雜的繪圖事宜，使你的計算機騰出來完成其他任務。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>feel free</b>\" when you want to give someone permission to do something, in a very willing way. 隨意","examples":["If you have any questions at all, please feel free to ask me. 如果你有什麼問題，請隨意問我好了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something or get something <b>for free</b>, you do it without being paid or get it without having to pay for it. 無償地; 免費地","examples":["I wasn't expecting you to do it for free. 我並沒指望你無償地做這個。"]}]}]},"just":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"正好，恰好；正當……時；不少於，同樣；差一點就不，勉強；剛才，剛剛；正在，正要；只是，僅僅是；確實，完全；請，就；可能，也許；表示贊同"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正義的，公平的；應得的，合理的；正確的，精確的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to say that something happened a very short time ago, or is starting to happen at the present time. For example, if you say that someone <b>just arrived</b> or <b>has just arrived</b>, you mean that they arrived a very short time ago. 剛剛","examples":["I've just bought a new house. 我剛買了一個新房子。","I just had the most awful dream. 我剛做了一個最可怕的夢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>just</b> doing something, you mean that you are doing it now and will finish it very soon. If you say that you are <b>just about to</b> do something, or <b>just going to</b> do it, you mean that you will do it very soon. 正在; 正要","examples":["I'm just making the sauce for the cauliflower. 我正在給花椰菜做調味汁。","I'm just going to go mail a letter. 我正要去寄一封信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>just</b> to emphasize that something is happening at exactly the moment of speaking or at exactly the moment that you are talking about. 正 (表強調)","examples":["Randall would just now be getting the Sunday paper. 蘭德爾這個時候正應該要去取星期日的報紙。","Just then the phone rang. 正在那時，電話鈴響了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to indicate that something is no more important, interesting, or difficult, for example, than you say it is, especially when you want to correct a wrong idea that someone may get or has already got. 只不過","examples":["It's just a suggestion. 這只是一個建議。","It's not just a financial matter. 這不只是個財務問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to emphasize that you are talking about a small part, not the whole of an amount. 只是","examples":["That's just one example of the kind of experiments you can do. 這只是你所能做的實驗中的一個例子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to emphasize how small an amount is or how short a length of time is. 僅僅 (強調數量少或時間短)","examples":["Stephanie and David redecorated a room in just three days. 斯蒂芬妮和戴維僅在3天之內就重新裝修了一個房間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>just</b> in front of a verb to indicate that the result of something is unfortunate or undesirable and is likely to make the situation worse rather than better. 只會 (造成不良後果)","examples":["By doing what they did, they just hurt the people in their community. 透過做他們的那些事，他們只會傷害自己社群的人們。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to indicate that what you are saying is the case, but only by a very small degree or amount. 勉強地","examples":["Her hand was just visible in the dimly lit room. 她的手在這個昏暗的房間裡勉強可見。","I arrived just in time for my flight to London. 我勉強趕上了飛往倫敦的航班。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> with \"might,\" \"may,\" and \"could,\" when you mean that there is a small chance of something happening, even though it is not very likely. 也許 (may)(和)(could)(連用)","examples":["It's an old trick but it just might work. 它是個老把戲，不過也許能管用。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> to emphasize the following word or phrase, in order to express feelings such as annoyance, admiration, or certainty. 就是 (加強表示感情的語氣)","examples":["She just won't relax. 她就是不放鬆。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> in expressions such as <b>just a minute</b> and <b>just a moment</b> to ask someone to wait for a short time. 用於(just a minute)和(just a moment)等短語中，表示稍等","examples":["\"Let me in, Di.\"—\"Okay. Just a minute.\" “讓我進去，迪。”—“好的，稍等。”"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You can use <b>just</b> in expressions such as <b>just a second</b> and <b>just a moment</b> to interrupt someone, for example, in order to disagree with them, explain something, or calm them down. 用於(just a minute)和(just a moment)等短語中，插話時用","examples":["Well, now just a second, I don't altogether agree. 哎，等一下，我不完全同意。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that you can <b>just</b> see or hear something, you mean that it is easy for you to imagine seeing or hearing it. 簡直 (表示能想像出)","examples":["I can just hear her telling her friends, \"Well, I blame his mother!\" 我簡直都能聽到她對朋友們說：“哎，是他母親的錯！”"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>just</b> in expressions such as <b>just like</b>, <b>just as...as</b>, and <b>just the same</b> when you are emphasizing the similarity between two things or two people. 用於(just like)，(just as...as)和(just the same)等短語中，強調相似性","examples":["Behind the facade they are just like the rest of us. 在這種外表背後，他們同我們其他的人一樣。","He worked just as hard as anyone. 他同每個人一樣勤奮工作。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"正義地","examples":["They were not treated justly in the past. 他們過去沒有被公正地對待過。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>just about</b> to indicate that what you are talking about is so close to being the case that it can be regarded as being the case. 幾乎可算是","examples":["There are those who believe that Nick Price is just about the best golfer in the world. 有些人認為尼克·普賴斯算是世界上最優秀的高爾夫球手了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>just about</b> to indicate that what you are talking about is in fact the case, but only by a very small degree or amount. 勉強","examples":["I can just about tolerate it at the moment. 我眼下勉強可以忍受它。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation, action, or idea as <b>just</b>, you mean that it is right or acceptable according to particular moral principles, such as respect for all human beings. 正義的","examples":["They believe that they are fighting a just war. 他們相信他們在打一場正義的戰爭。"]}]}]},"hard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"硬的，堅固的；困難的；困苦的，艱苦的；費力的，努力的；堅強的，勇敢的；猛烈的，用力的；冷酷的，嚴厲的；寒冷的，凜冽的；可證實的，確鑿的；刺眼的，（感覺上）難受的；（水）硬的；烈性的，強烈的；（酒）苦澀的；仔細的，認真的；嚴肅的；強壯的；（政治上）極端的；發硬音的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"努力地，費力地；用力地，猛烈地；仔細地，認真地；沉重地，大量地；變硬；在最大程度上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>海灘路"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>hard</b> is very firm and stiff to touch and is not easily bent, cut, or broken. 堅硬的","examples":["He shuffled his feet on the hard wooden floor. 他拖著腳走在堅硬的木地板上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>hard</b> is very difficult to do or deal with. 困難的","examples":["It's hard to tell what effect this latest move will have. 很難說最近的這次行動將會有什麼樣的影響。","That's a very hard question. 那是個很難的問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> is also an adjective. 努力的","examples":["I admired him as a true scientist and hard worker. 我欽佩他是一名真正的科學家和勤奮的工作者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> work involves a lot of activity and effort. 費勁的","examples":["Coping with three babies is very hard work. 照顧3個小寶寶是件很累人的活兒。","...a hard day's work. …一天累人的工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> is also an adjective. 仔細的","examples":["It might be worth taking a long hard look at your frustrations and resentments. 也許值得對你的挫折感與憤懣做仔細的分析。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> is also an adjective. 用力的","examples":["He gave her a hard push which toppled her backwards into an armchair. 他給了她用力的一推，將她向後推倒在一把扶手椅上。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a person or their expression is <b>hard</b>, they show no kindness or sympathy. 冷酷無情的","examples":["His father was a hard man. 他父親是個冷酷無情的人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are <b>hard on</b> someone, you treat them severely or unkindly. 嚴厲的","examples":["Don't be so hard on him. 別對他太嚴厲。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>hard on</b> a person or thing, you mean it affects them in a way that is likely to cause them damage or suffering. 難以忍受的","examples":["The grey light was hard on the eyes. 昏暗的光線使眼睛很難受。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you have a <b>hard</b> life or a <b>hard</b> period of time, your life or that period is difficult and unpleasant for you. 艱難的","examples":["It had been a hard life for her. 對她而言，那曾是一段艱難的日子。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> evidence or facts are definitely true and do not need to be questioned. 確鑿的","examples":["He wanted more hard evidence. 他想要更多確鑿的證據。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> drugs are very strong illegal drugs such as heroin or cocaine. 烈性的 (毒品)","examples":["He then graduated from soft drugs to hard ones. 他隨後從服用軟性毒品逐步發展到服用烈性毒品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堅硬","examples":["He felt the hardness of the iron railing press against his spine. 他感覺到硬梆梆的鐵欄杆抵住了他的脊樑骨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"艱難","examples":["In America, people don't normally admit to the hardness of life. 在美國，人們通常不承認生活的艱辛。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you work <b>hard</b> doing something, you are very active or work intensely, with a lot of effort. 努力地","examples":["I'll work hard. I don't want to let him down. 我會努力工作。我不想讓他失望。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you look, listen, or think <b>hard</b>, you do it carefully and with a great deal of attention. 仔細地","examples":["He looked at me hard. 他仔細地看著我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you strike or take hold of something <b>hard</b>, you strike or take hold of it with a lot of force. 用力地","examples":["I kicked a rubbish bin very hard and broke my toe. 我狠狠踢一個垃圾桶，踢破了腳趾頭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>hard</b> to indicate that something happens intensely and for a long time. 厲害地","examples":["I've never seen Terry laugh so hard. 我從沒見過特里笑得如此厲害。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Hard</b> is also an adverb. 嚴厲地","examples":["He said the security forces would continue to crack down hard on the protestors. 他說安全部隊將繼續嚴厲鎮壓抗議者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>hard going</b>, you mean it is difficult and requires a lot of effort. 艱難的","examples":["The talks had been hard going at the start. 會談在開始時是艱難的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To be <b>hard hit</b> <b>by</b> something means to be affected very severely by it. 被...嚴重影響","examples":["California's been particularly hard hit by the recession. 加利福尼亞受到經濟衰退的影響尤為嚴重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>plays hard to get</b>, they pretend not to be interested in another person or in what someone is trying to persuade them to do. 故意擺譜","examples":["I wanted her and she was playing hard to get. 我渴望她，她卻擺架子。"]}]}]},"likely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可能發生的；似乎合適的，彷彿恰當的；似乎真實的，可信的；看上去精力充沛（或有能力）的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大概，很可能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>likely</b> to indicate that something is probably the case or will probably happen in a particular situation. 可能的","examples":["Experts say a \"yes\" vote is still the likely outcome. 專家們表示投贊成票仍是可能的結果。","If this is your first baby, it's far more likely that you'll get to the hospital too early. 如果這是你的第一胎，你就非常有可能會太早到醫院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>likely</b> <b>to</b> do a particular thing, they will very probably do it. 很可能地","examples":["In the meantime the war of nerves seems likely to continue. 同時心理戰似乎很有可能要繼續下去。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Likely</b> is also an adverb. 可能地","examples":["Profit will most likely have risen by about $25 million. 利潤將極有可能增長約2500萬美元。"]}]}]},"least":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一點兒；最少的（little 的最高階）；最微不足道的（little 的最高階形式）；用於極小動植物的名稱，如least shrew（little 的最高階形式）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最低程度地；最少，至少"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最不重要的事物，最微小的事物；至少，起碼"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"最少量；起碼"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"最少的，最小的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at least</b> to say that a number or amount is the smallest that is possible or likely and that the actual number or amount may be greater. The forms <b>at the least</b> and <b>at the very least</b> are also used. (在數量上) 至少","examples":["Aim to have at least half a pint of milk each day. 目標是每天至少喝半品脫牛奶。","About two-thirds of adults consult their doctor at least once a year. 大約三分之二的成年人一年至少看一次醫生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>at least</b> to say that something is the minimum that is true or possible. The forms <b>at the least</b> and <b>at the very least</b> are also used. 至少 (最小的可能性)","examples":["She could go on a nice holiday at least. 她至少能過一個美好的假期。","His possession of classified documents in his home was, at the very least, a violation of navy security regulations. 他把機密檔案放在家裡，這最起碼是違反了海軍安全條例。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>at least</b> to indicate an advantage that exists in spite of the disadvantage or bad situation that has just been mentioned. 儘管如此","examples":["We've no idea what his state of health is but at least we know he is still alive. 我們不清楚他健康狀況怎樣，儘管如此我們知道他還活著。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>at least</b> to indicate that you are correcting or changing something that you have just said. 至少 (修正剛說過的話)","examples":["It's not difficult to get money for research or at least it's not always difficult. 獲得研究的資金不難，至少說，不總是很難。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>the least</b> to mean a smaller amount than anyone or anything else, or the smallest amount possible. 最少的","examples":["I try to offend the least amount of people possible. 我儘可能少得罪人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>the least</b> to emphasize the smallness of something, especially when it hardly exists at all. 一點兒","examples":["I don't have the least idea of what you're talking about. 我一點兒也不明白你在說什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>least</b> in structures where you are emphasizing that a particular situation or event is much less important or serious than other possible or actual ones. 最微不足道的","examples":["Having to get up at three o'clock every morning was the least of her worries. 必須每天早晨3點起床是她煩惱中最微不足道的。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Least</b> is also a pronoun. 最少量","examples":["On education funding, Japan performs best but spends the least per student. 在教育資金方面，日本做得最好，但是對每個學生的投入卻最少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>the least</b> in structures where you are stating the minimum that should be done in a situation, and suggesting that more should really be done. 起碼","examples":["Well, the least you can do, if you won't help me yourself, is to tell me where to go instead. 哦，如果你不願意親自幫助我，起碼應該告訴我往哪兒走吧。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Least</b> is also an adverb. 最少地","examples":["Damming the river may end up benefiting those who need it the least. 在河上建大壩最終可能有利於那些最不需要大壩的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>least</b> to indicate that someone or something has less of a particular quality than most other things of its kind. 最少地","examples":["He was one of the least warm human beings I had ever met. 他是我所見過的最不熱情的人之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>least</b> to indicate that something is true or happens to a smaller degree or extent than anything else or at any other time. 最低程度地","examples":["He had a way of throwing Helen off guard with his charm when she least expected it. 他有辦法用他的魅力讓海倫在最意想不到的時候失去戒備。"]}]}]},"late":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"晚期的，末期的；晚的，遲的；近日暮的，近深夜的；已故的；不久前的，最近的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"晚，遲；（時間上）接近終了，在晚年；臨近日暮，接近午夜；（時間上）接近終了，臨近末了，在晚年"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Late</b> means near the end of a day, week, year, or other period of time. (時間) 接近終了","examples":["It was late in the afternoon. 那是在接近傍晚的時候。","His autobiography was written late in life. 他的自傳是在晚年寫的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Late</b> means after the time that was arranged or expected. (比安排或預計時間) 遲","examples":["Steve arrived late. 史蒂夫遲到了。","The talks began some fifteen minutes late. 商談遲了約十五分鐘才開始。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Late</b> means after the usual time that a particular event or activity happens. (比通常時間) 晚","examples":["We went to bed very late. 我們很晚才睡覺。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Late</b> is also an adjective. 接近終了的","examples":["The talks eventually broke down in late spring. 會談最終在暮春時破裂。","He was in his late 20s. 他年近三十。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is <b>late</b>, it is near the end of the day or it is past the time that you feel something should have been done. 晚的; 遲的","examples":["It was very late and the streets were deserted. 天很晚了，街道上空無一人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Late</b> is also an adjective. 遲的","examples":["His campaign got off to a late start. 他的競選活動開始較遲。","The train was 40 minutes late. 火車晚點了40分鐘。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Late</b> is also an adjective. 晚的","examples":["They had a late lunch in a café. 他們很晚才在一家餐館吃了午飯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>late</b> when you are talking about someone who is dead, especially someone who has died recently. 已故的","examples":["...my late husband. …我已故的丈夫。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"晚","examples":["A large crowd had gathered despite the lateness of the hour. 儘管時間很晚了，還有一大群人聚集在了一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"遲到","examples":["He apologized for his lateness. 他為自己的遲到道歉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an action or event is <b>too late</b>, it is useless or ineffective because it occurs after the best time for it. 太遲的","examples":["It was too late to turn back. 要回頭，為時已晚。"]}]}]},"maybe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（不確定）大概，或許；（提出建議）或許，也許；（贊同並補充資訊）或許，也許；（不置可否）也許，或許"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能性，不確定性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>maybe</b> to express uncertainty, for example when you do not know that something is definitely true, or when you are mentioning something that may possibly happen in the future in the way you describe. 也許","examples":["Maybe she is in love. 也許她是戀愛了。","I do think about having children, maybe when I'm 40. 我確實考慮要孩子，也許在我40歲時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>maybe</b> when you are making suggestions or giving advice. <b>Maybe</b> is also used to introduce polite requests. 也許該 (用於提出建議、作出禮貌的請求)","examples":["Maybe we can go to the movies or something. 也許我們可以去看電影什麼的。","Maybe you'd better tell me what this is all about. 也許你該告訴我，這到底是怎麼一回事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>maybe</b> to indicate that, although a comment is partly true, there is also another point of view that should be considered. 可能 (用於表示某個評論部分屬實，但另一觀點也應該加以考慮)","examples":["Maybe there is jealousy, but I think the envy is more powerful. 可能是有嫉妒，但我想更強烈的是羨慕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say <b>maybe</b> as a response to a question or remark, when you do not want to agree or disagree. 可能吧 (用於表示未置可否)","examples":["\"Is she coming back?\"—\"Maybe. No one hears from her.\" “她快回來了嗎？” — “可能吧，沒有人知道她的訊息。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>maybe</b> when you are making a rough guess at a number, quantity, or value, rather than stating it exactly. 大約","examples":["The men were maybe a hundred feet away and coming closer. 那些人大約有一百英尺遠，正在向這裡靠近。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"People use <b>maybe</b> to mean \"sometimes,\" particularly in a series of general statements about what someone does, or about something that regularly happens. 有時","examples":["They'll come to the bar for a year, or maybe even two, then they'll find another favourite spot. 他們將會來這個酒吧待上一年，或者有時甚至兩年，然後他們會再找另外一個喜歡的地方。"]}]}]},"loud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大聲的，響亮的；（人或舉止）吵鬧的，聒噪的；大聲疾呼的，堅定的；（衣服）花哨的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大聲地，響亮地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a noise is <b>loud</b>, the level of sound is very high and it can be easily heard. Someone or something that is <b>loud</b> produces a lot of noise. 大聲的; 吵鬧的","examples":["Suddenly there was a loud bang. 突然砰地一聲響。","His voice became harsh and loud. 他的聲音變得又尖又響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something, especially a piece of clothing, as <b>loud</b>, you dislike it because it has very bright colours or very large, bold patterns which look unpleasant. (尤指衣服) 花哨的","examples":["He liked to shock with his gold chains and loud clothes. 他喜歡戴金鍊子，穿花哨衣服，以此製造轟動。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Loud</b> is also an adverb. 大聲地; 吵鬧地","examples":["She wonders whether Paul's hearing is OK because he turns the television up very loud. 她懷疑保羅的聽力有問題，因為他把電視機的音量調得很大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"大聲地; 吵鬧地","examples":["His footsteps echoed loudly in the tiled hall. 他的腳步聲響亮地迴盪在鋪著瓷磚的大廳裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say or read something <b>out loud</b>, you say it or read it so that it can be heard, rather than just thinking it. 出聲地","examples":["Even Ford, who seldom smiled, laughed out loud a few times. 即使是平時不苟言笑的福特也好幾次笑出了聲。"]}]}]},"nope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>不，不是，沒有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nope</b> is sometimes used instead of \"no\" as a negative response. (有時用於替代)(no)(作否定回答) 不","examples":["\"Is she supposed to work today?\"—\"Nope, tomorrow.\" “她今天應該上班嗎？”—“不，明天。”"]}]}]},"most":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"（數量上）最多，最大（ much, a lot of, many 的最高階）；大多數"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（數量上）最多，最大（ much, a lot of, many 的最高階）；大多數"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最；（程度上）最大；極其，非常；<北美，非正式>幾乎；（在談話中用於引起注意）最……；通常；（可能的）最大量"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大多數的；最大程度的，最大數量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>most</b> to refer to the majority of a group of things or people or the largest part of something. 大多數; 大部分","examples":["Most of the houses in the capital don't have indoor plumbing. 首都大多數房屋沒有室內管道裝置。","By stopping smoking you are undoing most of the damage smoking has caused. 透過戒菸，你就是在消除吸菸所致的大多數危害。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Most</b> is also a determiner. 大多數的","examples":["Most people think the queen has done a good job over the last 50 years. 大多數人認為女王在過去的50年中盡職盡責。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Most</b> is also a pronoun. 大多數","examples":["Seventeen civilians were hurt. Most are students who had been attending a twenty-first birthday party. 17名平民受了傷，其中大多數是參加一個21歲生日聚會的學生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Most</b> is also a pronoun. 最多","examples":["The most they earn in a day is fifty rubles. 他們一天最多掙50盧布。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>the most</b> to mean a larger amount than anyone or anything else, or the largest amount possible. 最多的","examples":["The president himself won the most votes. 總統本人贏得了最多的選票。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>most</b> to indicate that something is true or happens to a greater degree or extent than anything else. 最","examples":["What she feared most was becoming like her mother. 她最害怕的是變得像她母親一樣。","...Professor Morris, the person he most hated. …莫里斯教授，他最恨的那個人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>most</b> to indicate that someone or something has a greater amount of a particular quality than most other things of its kind. 最","examples":["Her children had the best, most elaborate birthday parties in the neighbourhood. 她孩子們的生日聚會是左鄰右舍中最好、最精心策劃的。","He was one of the most influential performers of modern jazz. 他是最有影響力的現代爵士樂表演者之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>the most</b>, you do it to the greatest extent possible or with the greatest frequency. 最大程度地; 最頻繁地","examples":["What question are you asked the most? 什麼問題是你最常被問到的？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>most</b> in conversations when you want to draw someone's attention to something very interesting or important that you are about to say. (談話中用於吸引注意力) 最","examples":["Most surprisingly, quite a few said they don't intend to vote at all. 最令人吃驚的是，相當一部分人說他們根本不打算投票。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>most of all</b> to indicate that something happens or is true to a greater extent than anything else. 最","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>at most</b> or <b>at the most</b> to say that a number or amount is the maximum that is possible and that the actual number or amount may be smaller. 至多","examples":["Poach the pears in apple juice or water and sugar for ten minutes at most. 把梨放入蘋果汁或水和糖中，煮最多十分鐘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make the most of</b> something, you get the maximum use or advantage from it. 充分利用","examples":["Happiness is the ability to make the most of what you have. 幸福就是充分享用你所擁有的一切的能力。"]}]}]},"never":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"決不，永不；不會，不可能（表示驚訝或震驚）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Never</b> means at no time in the past or at no time in the future. 從不; 永不","examples":["I have never lost the weight I put on in my teens. 我在十幾歲時增加的體重從沒減下去過。","Never had he been so free of worry. 他從沒這樣無憂無慮過。","That was a mistake. We'll never do it again. 那是個錯誤，我們永遠不會再犯了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Never</b> means \"not in any circumstances at all.\" 決不","examples":["I would never do anything to hurt him. 我決不會做任何事去傷害他。","Divorce is never easy for children. 離婚對於孩子們來說決不輕鬆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Never</b> is used to refer to the past and means \"not.\" 沒有; 不","examples":["He never achieved anything. 他一事無成。","I never knew him. 我不認識他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Never ever</b> is an emphatic way of saying \"never.\" (Never ever)是(never)的強調說法","examples":["I never, ever sit around thinking, \"What shall I do next?\" 我從來就不會閒坐著想：“我下一步該做什麼？”"]}]}]},"more":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"（數、量等）更多的，更大的（much、a lot of 和 many 的比較級）；另外的，附加的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（數、量等）更多的，更大的（much、a lot of 和 many 的比較級）；多了的部分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"更；（程度上）更強，更多；繼續，再；又一次；還有，再者；額外地；更像（前者）地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"更多的，更大的；額外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>more</b> to indicate that there is a greater amount of something than before or than average, or than something else. You can use \"a little,\" \"a lot,\" \"a bit,\" \"far,\" and \"much\" in front of <b>more</b>. 更多的","examples":["More and more people are surviving heart attacks. 越來越多的人在心臟病發作後存活下來。","He spent more time perfecting his dance moves instead of gym work. 他用更多的時間來完善他的舞蹈動作而不是健身。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>more</b> to refer to an additional thing or amount. You can use \"a little,\" \"a lot,\" \"a bit,\" \"far,\" and \"much\" in front of <b>more</b>. 額外的","examples":["They needed more time to consider whether to hold an inquiry. 他們需要更多的時間來考慮是否進行一次調查。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>More</b> is also a pronoun. 更多","examples":["As the level of work increased from light to heavy, workers ate more. 隨著工作強度由輕轉重，工人們吃得更多了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>More</b> is also a pronoun. 更多","examples":["Oxfam has appealed to western nations to do more to help the refugees. 牛津饑荒救濟委員會已經呼籲西方國家採取更多的措施來幫助這些難民。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>More</b> is also a quantifier. 更多","examples":["Employees may face increasing pressure to take on more of their own medical costs in retirement. 僱員們可能面臨越來越大的在退休後自己負擔更多醫療費用的壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>more than</b> before a number or amount to say that the actual number or amount is even greater. 超過","examples":["The Afghan authorities say the airport had been closed for more than a year. 阿富汗當局稱該機場已關閉1年以上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>some more</b> to indicate that something continues to happen for a further period of time. 繼續","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>more and more</b> to indicate that something is becoming greater in amount, extent, or degree all the time. 越來越","examples":["Her life was heading more and more where she wanted it to go. 她的生活正越來越朝著她想要的方向發展。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>more or less</b> true, it is true in a general way, but is not completely true. 或多或少地; 大致","examples":["The conference is more or less over. 會議大致結束了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>more than</b> a particular thing, it has greater value or importance than this thing. 不只是","examples":["He's more than a coach, he's a friend. 他不只是個教練，還是個朋友。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>more than</b> to say that something is true to a greater degree than is necessary or than average. 超出 (需要或平均水平)","examples":["The company has more than enough cash available to refinance the loan. 公司有綽綽有餘的現金再為貸款提供資金。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>what is more</b> or <b>what's more</b> to introduce an extra piece of information which supports or emphasizes the point you are making. 此外","examples":["Many more institutions, especially banks, were allowed to lend money for mortgages, and what was more, banks could lend out more money than they actually held. 更多機構，特別是銀行，被允許做抵押貸款；此外，銀行還可以借出比實際持有量更多的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>more</b> to indicate that something or someone has a greater amount of a quality than they used to or than is average or usual. 更加","examples":["Prison conditions have become more brutal. 監獄的條件已經變得更加嚴酷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>more</b> one thing <b>than</b> another, you mean that it is like the first thing rather than the second. 與其說…，倒不如說…","examples":["He's more like a film star than a lifeguard, really. 與其說他像個救生員，倒不如說他像個影星，真的。","Sue screamed, not loudly, more in surprise than terror. 蘇尖叫起來，聲音不大，與其說是害怕不如說是吃驚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>more</b> than before or <b>more</b> than someone else, you do it to a greater extent or more often. 更大程度地; 更經常地","examples":["When we are tired, tense, depressed, or unwell, we feel pain much more. 當我們疲勞、緊張、沮喪或者身體不適時，就更覺得疼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>more</b> to indicate that something continues to happen for a further period of time. 繼續","examples":["Things might have been different if I'd talked a bit more. 如果我再多說一點，結果或許會不同。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>more</b> to indicate that something is repeated. For example, if you do something \"once more,\" you do it again once. 再次","examples":["This train would stop twice more in the suburbs before rolling southeast toward Baltimore. 這輛火車在朝東南開往巴爾的摩前將在郊區多停兩站。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>more</b> in conversations when you want to draw someone's attention to something interesting or important that you are about to say. 更 (用來吸引聽話人的注意力)","examples":["More seriously for him, there are members who say he is wrong on this issue. 對他而言更嚴重的是，有些成員說他在這個問題上是錯的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>More</b> is also an adjective. 額外的","examples":["We stayed in Danville two more days. 我們在丹維爾多呆了兩天。"]}]}]},"often":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"常常，時常；在許多情況下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>often</b> happens, it happens many times or much of the time. 經常","examples":["They often spent Christmas together. 他們經常一起過聖誕節。","That doesn't happen very often. 那不常發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>how often</b> to ask questions about frequency. You also use <b>often</b> in reported clauses and other statements to give information about the frequency of something. 時常的","examples":["How often do you brush your teeth? 你多久刷一次牙？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>every so often</b>, it happens regularly, but with fairly long intervals between each occasion. 偶爾","examples":["She's going to come back every so often. 她會偶爾回來一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>as often as not,</b> or <b>more often than not</b>, you mean that it happens fairly frequently, and that this can be considered as typical. 往往","examples":["Yet, as often as not, they find themselves the target of persecution rather than praise. 然而，他們往往發現自己是迫害物件，而不是表揚物件。"]}]}]},"perhaps":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"可能；（用以緩和語氣或表示禮貌）也許，可能；（委婉地表示不贊同或不接受）也許，大概；（用於提出建議或請求）也許"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"假定，猜想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>perhaps</b> to express uncertainty, for example, when you do not know that something is definitely true, or when you are mentioning something that may possibly happen in the future in the way you describe. 可能","examples":["In the end they lose millions, perhaps billions. 最終他們損失了數百萬，也許數億。","Perhaps, in time, the message will get through. 可能，過一段時間，這訊息將會送到。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>perhaps</b> in opinions and remarks to make them appear less definite or more polite. (用於表示不確定性或禮貌) 或許","examples":["Perhaps the most important lesson to be learned is that you simply cannot please everyone. 或許應吸取的最重要的教訓是你不可能取悅每一個人。","His very last paintings are perhaps the most puzzling. 他最後的那些繪畫作品也許是最令人費解的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>perhaps</b> when you are making suggestions or giving advice. <b>Perhaps</b> is also used in formal English to introduce requests. (用於提出建議或請求) 也許","examples":["Perhaps I may be permitted a few suggestions. 也許能容許我提幾條建議。","Well, perhaps you'll come and see us at our place? 呃，也許你會來我們住的地方看看我們？"]}]}]},"next":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"下一個的，接下來的；（時間）緊接著來到的，下次的；緊鄰的；其他的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"緊接著，隨後；僅次於；下次，再次；（用於詢問，表示吃驚或困惑）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"下一個人或事件"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"下一（年、月、星期等）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"下一個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"ord.","pos_name":"序數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>next</b> period of time, event, person, or thing is the one that comes immediately after the present one or after the previous one. 下一個的","examples":["I got up early the next morning. 第二天早晨我起得很早。","...the next available flight. …下一趟可以乘坐的航班。","Who will be the next mayor? 誰將是下一任市長呢？"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>next</b> in expressions such as <b>next Friday</b>, <b>next day</b> and <b>next year</b> to refer, for example, to the first Friday, day, or year that comes after the present or previous one. 下一 (年、月、星期等)","examples":["Let's plan a big night next week. 我們下週組織一次盛大的晚會吧。","He retires next January. 他明年1月份退休。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Next</b> is also an adjective. 下一 (年、月、星期等) 的","examples":["I'll be 26 years old next Friday. 我下週五就26歲了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>next</b> place or person is the one that is nearest to you or that is the first one that you come to. 緊鄰的","examples":["Grace sighed so heavily that Trish could hear it in the next room. 格雷絲沉重地嘆氣，特蕾什在隔壁房間都聽到了。","The man in the next chair was asleep. 鄰座的男子睡著了。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Next</b> is also a pronoun. 下一個","examples":["He predicted that the region's economy would grow by about six percent both this year and next. 他預測該地區的經濟在今年和明年都會以約6%的速度增長。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The thing that happens <b>next</b> is the thing that happens immediately after something else. 緊接著","examples":["Next, close your eyes then screw them up tight. 接著，合上雙眼，再閉緊。","I don't know what to do next. 我不知道接著該做什麼了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>next</b> do something, you do it for the first time since you last did it. 再次","examples":["I next saw him at his house in Vermont. 我在他佛蒙特州的家裡再次見到了他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>next</b> to say that something has more of a particular quality than all other things except one. For example, the thing that is <b>next</b> best is the one that is the best except for one other thing. 僅次於","examples":["The one thing he didn't have was a son. I think he's felt that a grandson is the next best thing. 有一樣東西他沒有，就是兒子。我覺得他有個外孫感覺也不錯。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>after next</b> in expressions such as <b>the week after next</b> to refer to a period of time after the next one. For example, when it is May, the month after next is July. 下下 (星期、月等)","examples":["...the party's annual conference, to be held the week after next. …在下下週舉行的該黨的年會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you do something or experience something as much <b>as the next</b> person, you mean that you are no different from anyone else in the respect mentioned. 跟別人一樣","examples":["I enjoy pleasure as much as the next person. 我享受的樂趣和別人一樣多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is <b>next to</b> another thing, it is at the other side of it. 靠近","examples":["She sat down next to him on the sofa. 她在沙發上靠著他坐下來。","...at the southern end of the Gaza Strip next to the Egyptian border. …在鄰近埃及邊境的加沙地帶的南端。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>next to</b> in order to give the most important aspect of something when comparing it with another aspect. 僅次於","examples":["Her children were the number two priority in her life next to her career. 她的孩子們在她的生活裡佔第2位，僅次於她的事業。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>next to</b> before a negative, or a word that suggests something negative, to mean almost, but not completely. 幾乎 (用於否定性詞語之前)","examples":["Johnson still knew next to nothing about tobacco. 約翰遜仍然對菸草幾乎一無所知。"]}]}]},"not":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"表示否定，不（常與動詞或助動詞連用構成否定句，也可表示部分否定或代替前面已出現的否定內容）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"“非”（計算機、邏輯學中邏輯運算的一種，即邏輯非）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"neg.","pos_name":"否定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>not</b> with verbs to form negative statements. (與動詞連用構成否定句) 不","examples":["The sanctions are not working the way they were intended. 制裁沒有像他們原本打算的那樣奏效。","I don't trust my father anymore. 我再也不相信我父親了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>not</b> to form questions to which you expect the answer \"yes.\" (用於構成期待肯定回答的疑問句) 難道不","examples":["Haven't they got enough problems there already? 難道他們那裡的問題還不夠多嗎？","Didn't I see you at the party last week? 難道我在上週的聚會上沒見到你嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>not</b>, usually in the form <b>n't</b>, in questions which imply that someone should have done something, or to express surprise that something is not the case.  不","examples":["Why didn't you do it months ago? 為什麼你幾個月前不做呢？","Why couldn't he listen to her? 為什麼他不能聽她的話？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>not</b>, usually in the form <b>n't</b>, in question tags after a positive statement.  不是嗎","examples":["It's crazy, isn't it? 這真是瘋了，不是嗎？","I've been a great husband, haven't I? 我一直是個很不錯的丈夫，不是嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>not</b>, usually in the form <b>n't</b>, in polite suggestions.  不","examples":["Actually we do have a position in mind. Why don't you fill out our application? 實際上我們確實在考慮設一個職位。你為什麼不填一下我們的申請表呢？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>not</b> to represent the negative of a word, group, or clause that has just been used. (用於表示對前面出現過的單詞、片語或從句的否定) 不","examples":["\"Have you found Paula?\"—\"I'm afraid not, Kate.\" “你找到葆拉了嗎？”—“恐怕還沒有，凱特。”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>not</b> in front of \"all\" or \"every\" when you want to say something that applies only to some members of the group that you are talking about. (every)(之前，表示部分否定) 並非 (所有)","examples":["Not all the money, to put it mildly, has been used wisely. 客氣地講，並非所有的錢都花得很明智。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something is <b>not</b> always the case, you mean that sometimes it is the case and sometimes it is not. 並非 (總是)","examples":["He didn't always win the arguments, but he often was right. 他並非總是在辯論中獲勝，但他常常是正確的。","She couldn't always afford a babysitter. 她並非總能僱得起一名臨時保姆。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>not</b> or <b>not even</b> in front of \"a\" or \"one\" to emphasize that there is none at all of what is being mentioned. (連一個) 也不","examples":["...no office, no phone, not even a shelf on which to put my meagre belongings. 沒有辦公室，沒有電話，甚至連個擺放我寥寥無幾的物品的架子也沒有。","I sent report after report. But not one word was published. 我寄了一篇又一篇報告，但一個字也沒有發表。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can use <b>not</b> in front of a word referring to a distance, length of time, or other amount to say that the actual distance, time, or amount is less than the one mentioned. (用於表示距離、時間或其他數量的詞之前) 不到","examples":["The tug crossed our stern not fifty yards away. 那艘拖船在不到50碼的地方與我們的船尾錯過。","...a large crowd not ten yards away waiting for a bus. …不到10碼遠的一大群等公共汽車的人。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>not</b> when you are contrasting something that is true with something that is untrue. You use this especially to indicate that people might think that the untrue statement is true. (用以對比真實和不真實的情況，尤用於可能會被誤認為真實的陳述) 不是","examples":["He has his place in the Asian team not because he is white but because he is good. 他在亞洲隊有一席之地，不是因為他是白人而是因為他很出色。","Training is an investment not a cost. 培訓是一種投資而不是一種花費。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>not</b> in expressions such as \"not only,\" \"not just,\" and \"not simply\" to emphasize that something is true, but it is not the whole truth. (用於)(not only##not)(，)(not just##not)(和)(not simply##not)(片語中) 不僅","examples":["These movies were not only making money; they were also perceived to be original. 這些電影不僅賺錢，它們還被認為是有創意的。","What's it going to cost us, not just in terms of money, but in terms of lives? 它將讓我們付出什麼代價，不僅在錢的方面，而且還在生命方面？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>not that</b> to introduce a negative clause that contradicts something that the previous statement implies. (用於引出否定從句以與前句形成矛盾) 並非","examples":["His death took me a year to get over; not that you're ever really over it. 我用了一年的時間才從他的去世中恢復過來；不過永遠也不可能真正恢復過來。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Not at all</b> is an emphatic way of saying \"No\" or of agreeing that the answer to a question is \"No.\" 一點不","examples":["\"Sorry. I sound like Abby, don't I?\"—\"No. Not at all.\" “抱歉。我聽上去像阿比，是嗎？”—“不，一點不像。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Not at all</b> is a polite way of acknowledging a person's thanks. 不用謝; 不客氣","examples":["\"Thank you very much for speaking with us.\"—\"Not at all.\" “非常感謝您與我們交談。”—“不客氣。”"]}]}]},"much":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"許多"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"許多；優秀的事物"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常；<非正式>用在否定句末表示相反的意思；優秀的事物；經常；很大程度上；長時間地；多達（強調數量大得驚人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> to indicate the great intensity, extent, or degree of something such as an action, feeling, or change. <b>Much</b> is usually used with \"so,\" \"too,\" and \"very,\" and in negative clauses with this meaning. (做得、感到得、變得等) 多地","examples":["She laughs too much. 她笑得太多了。","Thank you very much. 非常感謝您。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something does not happen <b>much</b>, it does not happen very often. (發生得) 多地 (常用於否定句)","examples":["He said that his father never talked much about the war. 他說他父親從不多談這場戰爭。","Gwen had not seen her dad all that much, because mostly he worked on the ships. 格溫見她爸爸不是很多，因為他多數時間都在船上工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> in front of \"too\" or comparative adjectives and adverbs in order to emphasize that there is a large amount of a particular quality. 很大程度上 (用於比較級或)(too)(前)","examples":["The skin is much too delicate. 皮膚太過嬌嫩了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing is <b>much</b> the same as another thing, it is very similar to it. 很 (像…那樣)","examples":["The day ended much as it began. 這一天結束時還像開始時一樣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> in expressions such as <b>not much</b>, <b>not very much</b>, and <b>too much</b> when replying to questions about amounts. 多地 (too much##much)(等表達中)","examples":["\"Can you hear it where you live?\" He shook his head. \"Not much.\" “在你住的地方能聽到嗎？”他搖搖頭：“不怎麼聽得到。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Much</b> is also an adverb. 多少","examples":["She knows how much this upsets me but she persists in doing it. 她知道這讓我有多煩，但她還是堅持這麼做。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> to indicate that you are referring to a large amount of a substance or thing. 多的","examples":["They are grown on the hillsides in full sun, without much water. 它們被種在陽光充足、沒有多少水分的山坡上。","Japan has been reluctant to offer much aid to Russia. 日本向來不願為俄羅斯提供多少援助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> in the expression <b>how much</b> to ask questions about amounts or degrees, and also in reported clauses and statements to give information about the amount or degree of something. 多少的","examples":["How much money can I afford? 我能出得起多少錢？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>much</b> in the expression <b>as much</b> when you are comparing amounts. (和…一樣) 多的","examples":["I shall try, with as much patience as is possible, to explain yet again. 我會盡量耐心地再解釋一遍。","Their aim will be to produce as much milk as possible. 他們的目標是儘可能多地產奶。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Much</b> is also a pronoun. 多","examples":["...eating too much and drinking too much. …暴飲暴食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Much</b> is also a pronoun. 多少","examples":["How much do you earn? 你掙多少？"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Much</b> is also a quantifier. 多","examples":["Much of the time we do not notice that we are solving problems. 很多時候我們沒有注意到我們正在解決問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do not see <b>much of</b> someone, you do not see them very often. 多 (見面)","examples":["I don't see much of Tony nowadays. 我現在見託尼不多。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>much as</b> to introduce a fact which makes something else you have just said or will say rather surprising. 儘管","examples":["Much as they hope to go home tomorrow, they're resigned to staying on until the end of the year. 儘管他們很希望明天就回家，但不得不待到年底。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>as much</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I thought as much</b>\" and \"<b>I guessed as much</b>\" after you have just been told something and you want to say that you already believed or expected it to be true. 如此","examples":["You're waiting for a woman – I thought as much. 你在等一個女人–這我早料到了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>as much as</b> before an amount to suggest that it is surprisingly large. 多達","examples":["The organizers hope to raise as much as $6M for charity. 組織者們希望籌集到多達6百萬美元的慈善款。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>much less</b> after a statement, often a negative one, to indicate that the statement is more true of the person, thing, or situation that you are going to mention next. 更不用說","examples":["They are always short of water to drink, much less to bathe in. 他們總是缺飲用水，更不用說洗澡水了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something is not <b>so much</b> one thing <b>as</b> another, you mean that it is more like the second thing than the first. (不如…) 那麼多","examples":["I don't really think of her as a daughter so much as a very good friend. 我其實更多地把她當做好朋友，而不是女兒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>so much so</b> to indicate that your previous statement is true to a very great extent, and therefore it has the result mentioned. 到如此程度以至於","examples":["He himself believed in freedom, so much so that he would rather die than live without it. 他本人如此信奉自由，以至於寧死也不願沒有自由地活著。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a situation or action is <b>too much</b> <b>for</b> you, it is so difficult, tiring, or upsetting that you cannot cope with it. 非…所能忍受; 非…力所能及","examples":["His inability to stay at one job for long had finally proved too much for her. 他幹什麼工作都不能長久，終於讓她無法忍受。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>very much</b> to emphasize that someone or something has a lot of a particular quality, or that the description you are about to give is particularly accurate. 非常","examples":["...a man very much in charge of himself. …一個很能自制的人。"]}]}]},"long":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"長的；長久的，長期的；漫長的；長篇的；長音的；出界的；（面部表情）不高興的，愁苦的；記得牢的，記得久的；（可能性，機會）小的，渺茫的；遠期（獲利）的；（酒與涼飲料）混合的，大量的；（運動中的球）長傳的，遠距離的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"長久地，長期地；很久（以前或以後）；整個（時間段）；（球扔得）遠；整個 (時間段)"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"渴望"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長時間，長時期；長音；遠期證券；長期資本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Long</b> means a great amount of time or for a great amount of time. 長時間地","examples":["Repairs to the cable did not take too long. 維修電纜沒花太長時間。","Have you known her parents long? 你認識她的父母很久了嗎？","I learned long ago to avoid these invitations. 我很早以前就學會了迴避這些邀請。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>long</b> to ask or talk about amounts of time. 長久地","examples":["How long have you lived around here? 你在這附近住多久了？","He has been on a diet for as long as any of his friends can remember. 從他的朋友能記得時開始，他就一直在節食。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Long</b> is used in expressions such as <b>all year long</b>, <b>the whole day long</b>, and <b>your whole life long</b> to say and emphasize that something happens for the whole of a particular period of time. 整個 (時間段)","examples":["We played that CD all night long. 我們整晚都在播放那張CD。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The expression <b>for long</b> is used to mean \"for a great amount of time.\" 長久","examples":["\"Did you live there?\"—\"Not for long.\" “你以前住在那裡嗎？”—“沒住多久。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is the case <b>as long as</b> or <b>so long as</b> something else is the case, you mean that it is only the case if the second thing is the case. 只要","examples":["He said he would still support them, as long as they didn't break the rules. 他說只要他們不違反規則，他仍然會支援他們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>won't be long</b>, you mean that you think they will arrive or be back soon. If you say that it <b>won't be long</b> before something happens, you mean that you think it will happen soon. (某人) 很快就來; (某事) 即將發生","examples":["\"What's happened to her?\"—\"I'm sure she won't be long.\" “她出什麼事了？”— “我肯定她馬上就到了。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something will happen or happened <b>before long</b>, you mean that it will happen or it happened soon. 不久","examples":["German interest rates will come down before long. 德國的利率不久就會降下來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>no longer</b> the case used to be the case but is not the case now. You can also say that something is not the case <b>any longer</b>. 不再","examples":["Food shortages are no longer a problem. 食物短缺不再是個問題。","She could no longer afford to keep him at school. 她再也供不起他上學了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say <b>so long</b> as an informal way of saying goodbye. 再見","examples":["Well, so long, pal, see you around. 好了，再見，夥計，回頭見。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>long</b> event or period of time lasts for a great amount of time or takes a great amount of time. 長時間的","examples":["We had a long meeting with the attorney general. 我們和首席檢察官開了一個長會。","She is planning a long holiday in Europe. 她正打算去歐洲度一次長假。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Long</b> is also an adjective. 長久的","examples":["So how long is your commute? 那麼你上下班路程要花多長時間？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>long</b> speech, book, film, or list contains a lot of information or a lot of items and takes a lot of time to listen to, read, watch, or deal with. (篇幅) 長的","examples":["He was making quite a long speech. 他當時正在發表一個相當長的演講。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a period of time or work as <b>long</b>, you mean it lasts for more hours or days than is usual, or seems to last for more time than it actually does. 長的 (時間)","examples":["Go to sleep. I've got a long day tomorrow. 去睡吧。我明天要工作很長時間。","She was a TV reporter and worked long hours. 她曾是個電視記者，長時間工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a <b>long</b> memory, they are able to remember things that happened far back in the past. (記性) 好的","examples":["Mr. Assad, who has a long memory, will not have forgotten that meeting. 好記性的阿薩德先生不會忘記那次會面的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that is <b>long</b> measures a great distance from one end to the other. (長度) 長的","examples":["...a long table. …一張長桌子。","Lucy was 27, with long dark hair. 露西27歲，留著長長的黑髮。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>long</b> distance is a great distance. A <b>long</b> journey or route covers a great distance. (路程) 長的","examples":["These people were a long way from home. 這些人離家遙遠。","The long journey tired him. 漫長的旅程使他疲倦。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>long</b> piece of clothing covers the whole of someone's legs or more of their legs than usual. Clothes with <b>long</b> sleeves cover the whole of someone's arms. (衣服) 長的","examples":["She is wearing a long black dress. 她穿著一件黑色長裙。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>long</b> to talk or ask about the distance something measures from one end to the other. (某長度) 長的","examples":["An eight-week-old embryo is only an inch long. 一個8周大的胎兒僅1英寸長。","How long is the tunnel? 這隧道有多長？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Long</b> is also a combining form. (某長度) 長的","examples":["...a three-foot-long gash in the tanker's side. …油輪側面一條3英尺長的裂縫。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>long</b> <b>for</b> something, you want it very much. 渴望; 極想念","examples":["Steve longed for the good old days. 史蒂夫懷念過去的好時光。","I'm longing to meet her. 我正渴望著見她。"]}]}]},"sometimes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有時，間或"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>sometimes</b> to say that something happens on some occasions rather than all the time. 有時","examples":["During the summer, my skin sometimes gets greasy. 在夏季我的皮膚有時會變得多油。","Sometimes I think he dislikes me. 有時我覺得他不喜歡我。"]}]}]},"quite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相當，很；非常，十分；完全地，徹底地；（用於否定詞後面表示某事不完全正確或清楚）不大確切地，差不多；<英>（表示贊同或理解）對，正是；（用於名詞片語前，表示強調）出眾的，了不起的；<西印度>自始至終，一路上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>quite</b> to indicate that something is the case to a fairly great extent. <b>Quite</b> is less emphatic than \"very\" and \"extremely.\" 相當; 頗","examples":["I felt quite bitter about it at the time. 當時我對此感到相當痛苦。","Well, actually it requires quite a bit of work and research. 呃，實際上這需要相當多的工作和研究。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>quite</b> to emphasize what you are saying. 用於強調","examples":["It is quite clear that we were firing in self defence. 非常清楚，我們當時是自衛還擊。","My position is quite different. 我的立場完全不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>quite</b> after a negative to make what you are saying weaker or less definite. 用於否定詞之後表示語氣較弱或不確定","examples":["Something here is not quite right. 這兒有什麼不太對勁兒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say <b>quite</b> to express your agreement with someone. 正是這樣; 可不是嘛","examples":["\"It's your choice isn't it.\"—\"Quite.\" “這是你的選擇，不是嗎？”—“可不是嘛。”"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>quite</b> in front of a noun group to emphasize that a person or thing is very impressive or unusual. 出眾的; 不同尋常的","examples":["\"Oh, he's quite a character,\" Sean replied. “哦，他真是一個不同尋常的人。”肖恩答道。"]}]}]},"quick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"迅速的，快的；持續時間很短的，短暫的；敏捷的，腦子反應快的；馬上的，即刻的；性情急躁的，容易發怒的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式> 以很快的速度；<非正式>迅速發生地，很快發生地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（指甲下的）活肉（the quick）；<文>要害，核心（the quick）；<古>活著的人們（the quick）；<非正式>（板球）快投手"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"快，快點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>quick</b> moves or does things with great speed. 快的; 迅速的","examples":["You'll have to be quick. The flight leaves in about three hours. 你得快點了，那個航班大約3小時後就起飛了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>quick</b> takes or lasts only a short time. 短暫的","examples":["He took one last quick look around the room. 他朝房間匆匆掃了最後一眼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Quick</b> means happening without delay or with very little delay. 立刻發生的; 很快發生的","examples":["Officials played down any hope for a quick end to the bloodshed. 官員們對快速了結這場流血衝突不抱太大希望。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>quick</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do not hesitate to do it. 毫不遲疑的","examples":["Mark says the ideas are Katie's own, and is quick to praise her talent. 馬克說這些主意都是凱蒂自己的，接著便毫不遲疑地稱讚她的才幹。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a <b>quick</b> temper, they are easily made angry. (性情) 暴躁的; 易怒的","examples":["He readily admitted to the interviewer that he had a quick temper, with a tendency toward violence. 他欣然向採訪者承認他性情暴躁，有暴力傾向。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"快地; 迅速地","examples":["Cussane worked quickly and methodically. 丘薩恩幹得快而且有條不紊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Quicker</b> is sometimes used to mean \"at a greater speed,\" and <b>quickest</b> to mean \"at the greatest speed.\" <b>Quick</b> is sometimes used to mean \"with great speed.\" Some people consider this to be non-standard. 有時分別用(quick)、(quicker)和(quickest)表示“以很快的速度”、“以更快的速度”和“以最快的速度”，但有人認為此用法並不規範","examples":["Warm the sugar slightly first to make it dissolve quicker. 首先把糖微微加熱讓它更快地溶化。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"短暫地","examples":["You can get in shape quite quickly and easily. 你能又快又容易地恢復好身段。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"立刻","examples":["We need to get it back as quickly as possible. 我們需要儘快把它拿回來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Quick</b> is sometimes used to mean \"with very little delay.\" 馬上","examples":["I got away as quick as I could. 我儘快地離開了。"]}]}]},"super":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>極好的，極優秀的；超級的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極其，非常"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>（英國的）警官，（美國的）警長；<美>（大樓的）管理人；<非正式>主管，上司；過磷酸鹽，過磷酸鈣；特級品，特優產品；<美，俚>跑龍套的角色，臨時演員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Super</b> is used before adjectives to indicate that something has a lot of a quality. 超級地","examples":["I'm going to Greece in the summer so I've got to be super slim. 我這個夏天要去希臘，所以我得變得超級苗條才行。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Super</b> is used before nouns to indicate that something is larger, better, or more advanced than similar things. 超級的","examples":["Winners of each regional will advance to the super regionals. 每個地區分支機構的獲勝者們將會晉級為超級地區性人物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some people use <b>super</b> to mean very nice or very good. 超好的","examples":["We had a super time. 我們度過了一段超好的時光。","That's a super idea. 那是個超好的想法。"]}]}]},"same":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同一的；一模一樣的；沒有變化的；獨一無二的人（或物）；上述的（this/that same）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"同樣的人，同樣的事物；（數目、顏色、大小、質量等）相同；（與前述之事）同樣的事（the same）；未改變的人（或事物），和從前一樣的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"同樣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more things, actions, or qualities are <b>the same</b>, or if one is <b>the same</b> <b>as</b> another, they are very like each other in some way. 一樣的; 極相似的","examples":["The houses were all the same – square, close to the street, needing paint. 這些房子都是一樣的–四方形、鄰街、需要粉刷。","People with the same experience in the job should be paid the same. 同等工作經驗的人應該報酬相等。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>same</b> to indicate that you are referring to only one place, time, or thing, and not to different ones. 同一的","examples":["Bernard works at the same institution as Arlette. 伯納德與阿萊特在同一個機構工作。","It's impossible to get everybody together at the same time. 不可能把每個人同時召集在一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is still <b>the same</b> has not changed in any way. 毫無變化的","examples":["Taking ingredients from the same source means the beers stay the same. 從同一來源選取原料意味著啤酒保持不變。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Same</b> is also an adjective. 同前的; 前面提到的","examples":["He's so effective. I admire Ginny for pretty much the same reason. 他真有效。我佩服金尼也出於此因。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is happening <b>the same as</b> something else, the two things are happening in a way that is similar or exactly the same. 和…相似; 跟…一樣","examples":["I mean, it's a relationship, the same as a marriage is a relationship. 我是說，這是一種關係，跟婚姻是一種關係一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>same again</b>\" when you want to order another drink of the same kind as the one you have just had. 再來一份 (同樣的酒水)","examples":["Give Roger another pint, Imogen, and I'll have the same again. 給羅傑再來一品脫，伊摩根，我也再來一個。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say <b>all the same</b> or <b>just the same</b> to introduce a statement which indicates that a situation or your opinion has not changed, in spite of what has happened or what has just been said. (儘管如此…) 同樣; 依然","examples":["I arranged to pay him the dollars when he got there, a purely private arrangement. All the same, it was illegal. 我安排好了，他到那兒就付給他錢，純粹的個人安排。同樣，這是違法的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say \"<b>It's all the same to me</b>,\" you mean that you do not care which of several things happens or is chosen. 我無所謂; 對我來說都一樣","examples":["Whether I've got a moustache or not it's all the same to me. 我留不留鬍子對自己來說都一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>the same</b> to refer to something that has previously been mentioned or suggested. 一樣","examples":["We made the decision which was right for us. Other parents must do the same. 我們做了適合我們的決定。其他家長一定也會如此。","In the United States small bookstores survive quite well. The same applies to small publishers. 在美國小書店生存得很好。小出版商也是一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>same here</b>\" in order to suggest that you feel the same way about something as the person who has just spoken to you, or that you have done the same thing. 我也一樣","examples":["\"Nice to meet you,\" said Michael. \"Same here,\" said Mary Ann. “很高興見到你，” 邁克爾說。“我也一樣，” 瑪麗·安說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>same to you</b>\" in response to someone who wishes you well with something. (用於致以對方同樣的祝願) 你也一樣","examples":["\"Have a nice Easter.\"—\"And the same to you Bridie.\" “復活節快樂。”—“你也一樣，布賴迪。”"]}]}]},"pretty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尤指女孩）漂亮的，標緻的；（事物）悅目的，悅耳的；（男子）女子氣的，俊俏的；巨大的，令人印象深刻的；好看的，令人愉快的； <非正式>非常糟糕的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相當，頗；非常，很"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>漂亮東西（尤指悅人但不必要的小飾品）；<非正式>（以高人一等的口吻）漂亮的人，漂亮的孩子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝飾，使漂亮"}],"sections":[]},"soon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很快，馬上，不久；早，快；寧可，寧願"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is going to happen <b>soon</b>, it will happen after a short time. If something happened <b>soon</b> after a particular time or event, it happened a short time after it. 不久","examples":["You'll be hearing from us very soon. 你很快就會收到我們來信的。","This chance has come sooner than I expected. 這個機會比我預想的來得快。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>as soon as</b> something else happens, you mean that it happens immediately after the other thing. 一…就","examples":["As soon as relations improve they will be allowed to go. 關係一改善他們就會獲准離開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>would just as soon</b> do something or you<b>'d just as soon</b> do it, you mean that you would prefer to do it. 寧願","examples":["These people could afford to retire to Florida but they'd just as soon stay put. 這些人能負擔得起退隱到佛羅里達，但他們寧願留在原地。","I'd just as soon not have to make this public. 我寧願不公開此事。"]}]}]},"sharp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鋒利的，尖的；急轉彎的；（變化）急劇的；清晰的，鮮明的；劇烈的，強烈的；（語言）尖銳的；刺耳的；聰明的，敏銳的；（味道）濃烈的，辛辣的；時髦的；（風或霜）刺骨的；狡詐的；（音）偏高（的），升半音（的）；瘦削的，不豐滿的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"正點，準時；突然地，急劇地；音調偏高地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"升半音，升半音號；銳利的東西；<非正式>騙子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>升音演奏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sharp</b> point or edge is very thin and can cut through things very easily. A <b>sharp</b> knife, tool, or other object has a point or edge of this kind. 鋒利的","examples":["With a sharp knife, make diagonal slashes in the chicken breast. 用鋒利的刀子斜著切開雞胸脯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a shape or an object as <b>sharp</b> if part of it or one end of it comes to a point or forms an angle. 尖的","examples":["His nose was thin and sharp. 他的鼻子又細又尖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sharp</b> bend or turn is one that changes direction suddenly. 急劇的 (轉彎)","examples":["I was approaching a fairly sharp bend that swept downhill to the left. 我那時正接近一個朝山下向左急轉的彎道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>sharp</b>, you are praising them because they are quick to notice, hear, understand, or react to things. 機敏的","examples":["He is very sharp, a quick thinker and swift with repartee. 他很機敏、思維敏捷並且能機智應答。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone says something in a <b>sharp</b> way, they say it suddenly and rather firmly or angrily, for example, because they are warning or criticizing you. (說話、措辭等) 嚴厲的","examples":["\"Don't contradict your mother,\" was Charles's sharp reprimand. “不要頂撞你的母親，”查爾斯嚴厲的斥責。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>sharp</b> change, movement, or feeling occurs suddenly, and is great in amount, force, or degree. (變化、動作等) 急劇的; (情感等) 劇烈的","examples":["There's been a sharp rise in the rate of inflation. 通貨膨脹率急劇上升了。","Tennis requires a lot of short sharp movements. 網球運動需要大量快速而劇烈的動作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>sharp</b> difference, image, or sound is very easy to see, hear, or distinguish. (差異、影象、聲音等) 清晰可辨的","examples":["Many people make a sharp distinction between humans and other animals. 許多人將人類和其他動物截然分開。","All the footmarks are quite sharp and clear. 所有的足跡都很清楚明晰。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>sharp</b> taste or smell is rather strong or bitter, but is often also clear and fresh. (味道、氣味等) 濃烈的","examples":["The apple tasted just as I remembered – sharp, sour, yet sweet. 這蘋果嚐起來跟我記憶中的完全一樣–味道十足，酸中帶甜。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sharp</b> is also an adverb. 急劇地","examples":["Do not cross the bridge but turn sharp left to go down on to the towpath. 不要過橋，而是向左急轉下到纖道上去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"急劇地","examples":["Room number nine was at the far end of the corridor where it turned sharply to the right. 9號房間在過道盡頭右急轉彎處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"嚴厲地","examples":["\"You've known,\" she said sharply, \"and you didn't tell me?\" “你已經知道了，”她嚴厲地說道，“而你卻沒有告訴我？”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"急劇地","examples":["Unemployment has risen sharply in recent years. 近年來失業率已急劇上升。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"清晰可辨地","examples":["Opinions on this are sharply divided. 對這事的看法迥然各異。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Sharp</b> is used after stating a particular time to show that something happens at exactly the time stated. (…點) 整","examples":["She planned to unlock the shop at 8:00 sharp this morning. 她計劃今早8點整開啟店門。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sharp</b> is used after a letter representing a musical note to show that the note should be played or sung half a tone higher. <b>Sharp</b> is often represented by the symbol ♯. 升半音","examples":["A solitary viola plucks a lonely, soft F sharp. 一把中提琴獨奏出孤寂婉約的升F調。"]}]}]},"still":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"還，依舊；仍然，還是（會或可能）；儘管那樣，儘管如此；更加，還要（用於表示強調）；還有（更多）；靜止地，不動地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"靜止的，不動的；寧靜的，寂靜的；無風的；不含碳酸氣的，不起泡的；（照片）靜態的，（畫面）定格的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電影或錄影的）定格畫面，劇照；（制酒的）蒸餾器；靜止，安靜，平靜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）靜止，平靜，安靜；使（感情）減輕，使（感情）平息；蒸餾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation that used to exist <b>still</b> exists, it has continued and exists now. 仍然","examples":["I still dream of home. 我仍然夢見家。","Brian's toe is still badly swollen and he cannot put on his shoe. 布賴恩的腳趾頭仍腫得厲害，不能穿鞋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something that has not yet happened could <b>still</b> happen, it is possible that it will happen. If something that has not yet happened is <b>still</b> <b>to</b> happen, it will happen at a later time. 仍然","examples":["Big money could still be made if the crisis keeps oil prices high. 如果這場危機使得油價居高不下，仍然還是可以掙大錢的。","We could still make it, but we won't get there till three. 我們仍然能去，但3點以前無法到達。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there <b>is still</b> an amount of something left, you are emphasizing that there is that amount left. 還","examples":["There are still some outstanding problems. 還有一些突出的問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>still</b> to emphasize that something remains the case or is true in spite of what you have just said. 然而","examples":["I'm average for my height. But I still feel I'm fatter than I should be. 我身材中等，但還是覺得胖了些。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>still</b> to indicate that a problem or difficulty is not really worth worrying about. 不過","examples":["Their luck had simply run out. Still, never fear. 他們的好運已經結束。不過，別害怕。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>still</b> in expressions such as <b>still further</b>, <b>still another</b>, and <b>still more</b> to show that you find the number or quantity of things you are referring to surprising or excessive. 更加","examples":["We look forward to strengthening still further our already close co-operation with the police. 我們期待進一步加強和警方現有的密切合作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>still</b> with comparatives to indicate that something has even more of a quality than something else. 更加 (與比較級連用)","examples":["Formula One motor car racing is supposed to be dangerous. \"Indycar\" racing is supposed to be more dangerous still. 一級方程式賽車被認為是危險的。印第賽車則被認為更加危險。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you stay <b>still</b>, you stay in the same position and do not move. 靜止不動的","examples":["David had been dancing about like a child, but suddenly he stood still and looked at Brad. 戴維一直像孩子那樣蹦蹦跳跳，但突然打住，瞧著布拉德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If air or water is <b>still</b>, it is not moving. 靜止的","examples":["The night air was very still. 夜晚的空氣靜止不動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place is <b>still</b>, it is quiet and shows no sign of activity. 安靜的","examples":["In the room it was very still. 這房間裡很安靜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Drinks that are <b>still</b> do not contain any bubbles of carbon dioxide. 無碳酸氣的","examples":["...a glass of still water. …一杯無汽的水。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"安靜","examples":["Four deafening explosions shattered the stillness of the night air. 4聲震耳欲聾的爆炸打破了夜空的寧靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>still</b> is a photograph taken from a movie which is used for publicity purposes. 電影劇照","examples":["...stills from the James Bond movie series. …詹姆斯·邦德電影系列片的劇照。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>still</b> is a piece of equipment used to make strong alcoholic drinks by a process called distilling. (制酒的) 蒸餾器","examples":[]}]}]},"thus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<正式>因此；<正式>這樣，以此種方式；<正式>到如此程度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>thus</b> to show that what you are about to mention is the result of something else that you have just mentioned. 因此","examples":["Neither of them thought of turning on the news. Thus Caroline didn't hear of John's death until Peter telephoned. 他們倆都沒想到要收看新聞。因此，直到彼得打來電話卡羅琳才獲悉約翰的死訊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>thus</b> or happens <b>thus</b> you mean that it is, or happens, as you have just described or as you are just about to describe. 如此; 那樣","examples":["Joanna was pouring the wine. While she was thus engaged, Charles sat on one of the bar-stools. 喬安娜在倒葡萄酒。就在她忙著時，查爾斯坐在了其中一張酒吧椅上。"]}]}]},"yeah":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"（非正式口語）是，對"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（非正式口語）是，對；表示驚訝、懷疑、不信或反對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yeah</b> means yes. 是","examples":["\"Bring us something to drink.\"—\"Yeah, yeah.\" “給我們拿點兒喝的來。”—“好，好。”"]}]}]},"twice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"兩次；兩倍，強（或好、難）的多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>twice</b>, it happens two times, or there are two actions or events of the same kind. 兩次","examples":["He visited me twice that autumn and called me on the telephone often. 他那年秋天兩次來看我，並經常給我打電話。","The government has twice declined to back the scheme. 政府已經兩次拒絕支援該計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>twice</b> in expressions such as <b>twice a day</b> and <b>twice a week</b> to indicate that something happens two times in each day or week. 兩次","examples":["I phoned twice a day, leaving messages with his wife. 我一天打了兩次電話，留言給他妻子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is, for example, <b>twice as</b> big or old <b>as</b> another, the first thing is double the size or age of the second. People sometimes say that one thing is <b>twice as</b> good or hard <b>as</b> another when they want to emphasize that the first thing is much better or harder than the second. 兩倍","examples":["The figure of seventy-million dollars was twice as big as expected. 7千萬美元這個數字是預計的兩倍。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twice</b> is also a predeterminer. 兩倍","examples":["Unemployment here is twice the national average. 這兒的失業率是全國平均數的兩倍。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>think twice</b> about doing something, you consider it again and decide not to do it, or decide to do it differently. 三思","examples":["From now on, think twice before saying stupid things. 從現在起，說蠢話前要三思。"]}]}]},"this":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"這，這個；這樣；今，本；……的這個；有個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"這，這個（離說話人較近的）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"這樣地，這麼"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"這（指前面曾提及或暗指的人或物）； 這（指當前所處的地方或時間）；這（指即將要發生某事的時間）；這個（指說話或寫字時使用的媒介）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"(This) （法、美、印、巴）蒂斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to refer back to a particular person or thing that has been mentioned or implied. 這 (指前面曾提及或暗指的人或物)","examples":["The entire portfolio is worth $160,312. Of this amount, my investment is worth only $7,748. 整個投資組合價值為$160312。在這當中，我的投資額僅為$7748。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>This</b> is also a determiner. 這","examples":["This report is from our Science Unit. 這份報告出自我們的科學部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>This</b> is also a determiner. 這","examples":["There have been continual demands to put an end to this situation. 人們不斷要求要結束這種局面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In spoken English, people use <b>this</b> to introduce a person or thing into a story. 口語中用以引出故事裡的人或物","examples":["I came here by chance and was just watching what was going on, when this girl came up to me. 我碰巧來到這裡，正在看熱鬧，這時一個女孩向我走來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>This</b> is also a determiner. 這個","examples":["This church was built by the Emperor Constantine Monomarchus in the eleventh century. 這座教堂是11世紀時君主康斯坦丁·莫諾馬庫斯建造的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> when you refer to the place you are in now or to the present time. 這 (指當前所處的地方或時間)","examples":["This country is weird. 這個國家很怪。","This place is run like a hotel ought to be run. 這個地方經營得像一個酒店一樣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to refer to the next occurrence in the future of a particular day, month, season, or festival. 這 (指即將要發生某事的時間)","examples":["...this Sunday's 7:45 performance. …這個星期天7:45的演出。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to refer to the medium of communication that you are using at the time of speaking or writing. 這個 (指說話或寫字時使用的媒介)","examples":["What I'm going to do in this lecture is focus on something very specific. 我在這次講座中將集中講解非常具體的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>This</b> is also a pronoun. 這","examples":["I don't know how bad the injury is, because I have never had one like this before. 我不知道傷勢有多重，因為我以前從未受過這樣的傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to introduce someone or something that you are going to talk about. 這 (用於引出將要談論的人或物)","examples":["This is what I will do. I will telephone Anna and explain. 這就是我要做的。我會打電話向安娜解釋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to refer back to an idea or situation expressed in a previous sentence or sentences. 這一點 (指前文曾提到的觀點或情況)","examples":["You feel that it's uneconomical. Why is this? 你覺得這很不划算。這是為什麼呢？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> to refer to a person or thing that is near you, especially when you touch them or point to them. When there are two or more people or things near you, <b>this</b> refers to the nearest one. 這個 (用於指附近或最近的人或物)","examples":["I like this coat better than that one. 我更喜歡這件大衣，而不是那件。","\"If you'd prefer something else I'll gladly have it changed for you.\"—\"No, this is great.\" “如果您喜歡別的東西，我很樂意幫您調換一下。”—“不用，這個很好。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> when you refer to a general situation, activity, or event which is happening or has just happened and which you feel involved in. 這 (指正在發生或剛發生的與自己有關的事)","examples":["I thought, this is why I've travelled thousands of miles. 我想，這就是我走了幾千英里路的原因。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>This</b> is also a pronoun. 這","examples":["This is the worst place I've come across. 這是我到過的最糟糕的地方。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>this is</b> in order to say who you are or what organization you are representing, when you are speaking on the telephone, radio, or television. 我是 (用在電話、廣播或電視中作自我介紹)","examples":["Hello, this is John Thompson. 你好，我是約翰·湯普森。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> when you are indicating the size or shape of something with your hands. 這麼 (用手錶示物體的大小或形狀時可說)","examples":["\"They'd said the wound was only about this big,\" and he showed me with his fingers. “他們說傷口只有這麼大。”他用手指比劃給我看。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>this</b> when you are going to specify how much you know or how much you can tell someone. 這麼 (用於說明自己所知道或所能告知內容的多少)","examples":["I don't know if it's the best team I've ever had, but I can tell you this much, they're incredible people to be around. 我不知道這是否是我擁有過的最好的團隊，但我可以這麼告訴你，他們是非常棒的合作伙伴。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>this is it</b>, you are agreeing with what someone else has just said. 是這樣","examples":["\"You know, people conveniently forget the things they say.\"—\"Well this is it.\" “你知道，人們會輕易地忘記自己說的話。”—“嗯，是這樣。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are doing or talking about <b>this and that</b>, or <b>this, that, and the other</b> you mean that you are doing or talking about a variety of things that you do not want to specify. 各種事情","examples":["\"And what are you doing now?\"—\"Oh this and that.\" “那麼你目前在做什麼？”—“哦，各種事情。”"]}]}]},"too":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"太，過於，過度；也，亦，還；而且，再者（用於補充進一步的觀點）；很，十分，非常（用於否定句）；確實地，無可否認地；（表示感謝，較為正式）極其，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>too</b> after mentioning another person, thing, or aspect that a previous statement applies to or includes. 也","examples":["\"Nice to talk to you.\"—\"Nice to talk to you too.\" “和你交談很高興。”—“和你交談我也很高興。”","\"I've got a great feeling about it.\"—\"Me too.\" “我對此感覺棒極了。”—“我也一樣。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>too</b> after adding a piece of information or a comment to a statement, in order to emphasize that it is surprising or important. (用於補充資訊或評論) 還","examples":["We did learn to read, and quickly too. 我們確實識了字，而且還很快。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>too</b> in order to indicate that there is a greater amount or degree of something than is desirable, necessary, or acceptable. 太","examples":["Leather jeans that are too big will make you look larger. 皮仔褲太大會讓你顯得更胖。","I'm turning up the heat, it's too cold. 我在調高暖氣，天太冷了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>too</b> with a negative to make what you are saying sound less forceful or more polite or cautious. (與否定詞連用以使語氣更緩和、更禮貌或更謹慎) 非常","examples":["I wasn't too happy with what I'd written so far. 我對自己到目前為止所寫的東西還不是非常滿意。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>all too</b> or <b>only too</b> to emphasize that something happens to a greater extent or degree than is good or desirable. (用於強調程度之好) 極其","examples":["She remembered it all too well. 她對這事記得極其清楚。"]}]}]},"slow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（移動，執行）低速的，緩慢的；慢速的，低速的；耗時的，太慢的；遲緩的，慢吞吞的；（鐘錶）慢的；遲鈍的，愚笨的；（膠片）曝光慢的；（鏡頭）小孔徑的；（生意）清淡的，不景氣的；不曲折的，乏味的，無趣的；（火，烤箱）小火的，弱火的；（球場或地面）軟的，阻球的，奔跑困難的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）放慢速度，（使）減速；（使）降低，（使）減少；（生活，工作）放鬆"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"低速地，緩慢地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>slow</b> moves, happens, or is done without much speed. 緩慢的","examples":["The traffic is heavy and slow. 車很多，走得慢。","Electric whisks should be used on a slow speed. 電子打蛋器應該慢速運轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>slow</b> takes a long time. 漫長的","examples":["The distribution of passports has been a slow process. 頒發護照一直是個漫長的過程。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>slow</b> to do something, they do it after a delay. 遲緩的","examples":["The world community has been slow to respond to the crisis. 國際社會對該危機的反應向來遲緩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>slow</b> is not very clever and takes a long time to understand things. 遲鈍的","examples":["He got hit on the head and he's been a bit slow since. 他的頭被打了一下，從那以後，就有點遲鈍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe a situation, place, or activity as <b>slow</b>, you mean that it is not very exciting. 乏味的","examples":["Don't be faint-hearted when things seem a bit slow or boring. 當事情似乎有點乏味或無聊時，不要膽怯。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a clock or watch is <b>slow</b>, it shows a time that is earlier than the correct time. (鐘錶) 慢的","examples":["The clock is about two and a half minutes slow. 那鐘慢兩分半左右。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"緩慢地","examples":["He spoke slowly and deliberately. 他說得緩慢而慎重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In informal English, <b>slower</b> is used to mean \"at a slower speed\" and <b>slowest</b> is used to mean \"at the slowest speed.\" In nonstandard English, <b>slow</b> is used to mean \"with little speed.\" 緩慢地","examples":["I began to walk slower and slower. 我開始走得越來越慢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"漫長地","examples":["My resentment of her slowly began to fade. 我對她的怨恨慢慢地開始消退了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>slows</b> or if you <b>slow</b> it, it starts to move or happen more slowly. 使慢下來; 慢下來","examples":["The rate of bombing has slowed considerably. 轟炸頻率已經放慢了許多。","She slowed the car and began driving up a narrow road. 她放慢了車速，開始駛上一條狹窄的道路。"]}]}]},"sure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"確信的，有把握的；肯定的，一定的；可靠的，準確的；一定會（發生或出現某種結果）的；緊緊的，堅定的；沉著自信的，胸有成竹的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（表示同意）當然；確實，的確，誠然（用於肯定前半部分）；（回答他人的感謝）不用客氣，應該的；真的，肯定，無疑（用於強調）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sure</b> that something is true, you are certain that it is true. If you are not <b>sure</b> about something, you do not know for certain what the true situation is. 確定的","examples":["He'd never been in a class before and he was not even sure that he should have been teaching. 他以前從未講過課，他甚至不能確定自己是否應當從事教學。","The president has never been sure which direction he wanted to go in on this issue. 這位總統從未確定在這個問題上自己想要朝哪個方向走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>sure of</b> getting something, they will definitely get it or they think they will definitely get it. 肯定的","examples":["A lot of people think that it's better to pay for their education so that they can be sure of getting quality. 很多人認為最好是自己掏錢受教育，為的是能肯定得到高品質的教育。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sure</b> is used to emphasize that something such as a sign or ability is reliable or accurate. 可靠的; 準確的","examples":["Sharpe's leg and shoulder began to ache, a sure sign of rain. 夏普的腿和肩開始痛了，這是要下雨的準確跡象。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>be sure</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they must not forget to do it. 務必的","examples":["Be sure to read about how mozzarella is made, on page 65. 務必要閱讀第65頁上如何製作莫澤雷勒乾酪的內容。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is sure to</b> happen, you are emphasizing your belief that it will happen. 一定","examples":["With over 80 beaches to choose from, you are sure to find a place to lay your towel. 有八十多個海灘可供挑選，你一定能找到一個曬日光浴的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>sure enough</b>, especially when telling a story, to confirm that something was really true or was actually happening. (尤用於講故事時) 果然","examples":["We found the apple pie pudding too good to resist. Sure enough, it was delicious. 我們覺得這塊蘋果餡餅布丁令人無法抗拒。果然，它很美味。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>for sure</b> or that you know it <b>for sure</b>, you mean that it is definitely true. 千真萬確","examples":["One thing's for sure, Manilow's vocal style hasn't changed much over the years. 有一點是千真萬確的，馬尼洛的演唱風格這些年來沒有太大的變化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>make sure</b> <b>that</b> something is done, you take action so that it is done. 確保","examples":["Make sure that you follow the instructions carefully. 一定保證你認真遵循這些用法說明。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>make sure</b> <b>that</b> something is the way that you want or expect it to be, you check that it is that way. 核實","examples":["He looked in the bathroom to make sure that he was alone. 他往那間浴室裡看了看，以核實那就他一個人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>sure of yourself</b>, you are very confident about your own abilities or opinions. 自信","examples":["I'd never seen him like this, so sure of himself, so in command. 我從未見過他像這樣，如此自信，如此得心應手。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sure</b> is an informal way of saying \"yes\" or \"all right.\" 當然","examples":["\"Do you know where she lives?\"—\"Sure.\" “你知道她住在哪兒嗎？”—“當然啦！”"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>sure</b> in order to emphasize what you are saying. 確實","examples":["\"Has the whole world just gone crazy?\"—\"Sure looks that way, doesn't it.\" “整個世界都瘋了嗎？”—“看起來確實如此，不是嗎？”"]}]}]},"together":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在一起，共同；以使接觸（或相結合），到一起；（位置）在一起，緊挨地；關係密切，有婚姻關係；同時，一齊；（團結）在一起，合作地；合計地，總和地；不間斷地，接連地；靠著，貼著"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>自信而有條理的，沉穩的；（兩人）結婚的，有性關係（或戀愛關係）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people do something <b>together</b>, they do it with each other. 在一起","examples":["We went on long bicycle rides together. 我們一起騎著腳踏車進行長途旅行。","He and I worked together on a book. 他和我合寫了一本書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If things are joined <b>together</b>, they are joined with each other so that they touch or form one whole. (物體結合) 到一起","examples":["Mix the ingredients together thoroughly. 把這些配料充分地混合到一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If things or people are situated <b>together</b>, they are in the same place and very near to each other. 緊挨著","examples":["The trees grew close together. 這些樹緊挨著一起成長。","Ginette and I gathered our things together. 吉內特和我把我們的東西集中到一起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a group of people are held or kept <b>together</b>, they are united with each other in some way. 一致地","examples":["He has done a lot to keep the family together. 他做了很多努力來保持家庭和睦。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If two things happen or are done <b>together</b>, they happen or are done at the same time. 同時","examples":["Three horses crossed the finish line together. 3匹馬同時衝過終點線。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>together</b> when you are adding two or more amounts or things to each other in order to consider a total amount or effect. 總共","examples":["Together we earn $60,000 per year. 我們每年總共賺$60000。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Together</b> is also an adjective. 一致的","examples":["We are together in the way we're looking at this situation. 我們對這種情況的看法一致。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people are <b>together</b>, they are married or having a sexual relationship with each other. (因婚姻、性關係) 在一起的","examples":["We were together for five years. 我們在一起5年了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that two things <b>go together</b>, or that one thing <b>goes together</b> <b>with</b> another, you mean that they go well with each other or cannot be separated from each other. 相配; 不可分割","examples":["I can see that some colours go together and some don't. 我能看出一些顏色相配，一些則不相配。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>together with</b> to mention someone or something else that is also involved in an action or situation. 加之","examples":["Every month we'll deliver the very best articles, together with the latest fashion and beauty news. 每個月我們都會刊登最好的文章，加之最新的時尚美容資訊。"]}]}]},"true":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真實的；正確的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"真實地；準確地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"真實；準確"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"裝準"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（True）(英)特魯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>true</b>, it is based on facts rather than being invented or imagined, and is accurate and reliable. 真實的","examples":["Everything I had heard about him was true. 我所聽到的關於他的一切都是真的。","He said it was true that a collision had happened. 他說碰撞真的發生了一次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>true</b> to emphasize that a person or thing is sincere or genuine, often in contrast to something that is pretended or hidden. (人或物品) 真實的","examples":["I allowed myself to acknowledge my true feelings. 我願意承認自己的真實感情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you use <b>true</b> to describe something or someone, you approve of them because they have all the characteristics or qualities that such a person or thing typically has. 真正的","examples":["This country professes to be a true democracy. 該國宣稱自己是一個真正的民主國家。","Maybe one day you'll find true love. 也許有一天你會找到真愛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a fact is <b>true</b> <b>of</b> a particular person or situation, you mean that it is valid or relevant for them. 確實的; 符合的","examples":["I accept that the romance may have gone out of the marriage, but surely this is true of many couples. 我承認浪漫可能已從婚姻中消失，但許多夫妻的確都是如此。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>true to</b> someone, you remain committed and loyal to them. If you are <b>true to</b> an idea or promise, you remain committed to it and continue to act according to it. 忠誠的","examples":["David was true to his wife. 大衛忠於他的妻子。","India has remained true to democracy. 印度一直恪守民主。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a dream, wish, or prediction <b>comes true</b>, it actually happens. (夢想、願望或預測) 成為現實","examples":["Many of his predictions are coming true. 他的許多預言都在成為現實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a general statement <b>holds true</b> in particular circumstances, or if your previous statement <b>holds true</b> in different circumstances, it is true or valid in those circumstances. 同樣適用","examples":["This law is known to hold true for galaxies at a distance of at least several billion light years. 這個定律被普遍認為同樣適用於至少數十億光年之遠的星系。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something seems <b>too good to be true</b>, you are suspicious of it because it seems better than you had expected, and you think there may be something wrong with it that you have not noticed. 好得令人難以置信","examples":["On the whole the celebrations were remarkably good-humored and peaceful. It seemed almost too good to be true. 大體上說，慶祝活動非常快樂祥和，似乎好得令人難以置信。"]}]}]},"according to":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"根據：表示根據某人或某事的陳述、說法或信念。"},{"pos":"","zh":"按照：表示按照某個標準、規則或方法。"},{"pos":"","zh":"據……所述：表示根據某人的陳述或說法。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone says that something is true <b>according to</b> a particular person, book, or other source of information, they are indicating where they got their information. 根據","examples":["The van raced away, according to police reports, and police gave chase. 根據警方的報告，這輛貨車飛馳而去，警方進行了追趕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is done <b>according to</b> a particular set of principles, these principles are used as a basis for the way it is done. 按照","examples":["They both played the game according to the rules. 他們兩個都按照那些規則進行了這場遊戲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something varies <b>according to</b> a changing factor, it varies in a way that is determined by this factor. 根據… (變化)","examples":["Prices vary according to the quantity ordered. 價格根據所訂數量而變化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>according to plan</b>, it happens in exactly the way that it was intended to happen. 按照計劃","examples":["If all goes according to plan, the first concert will be Tuesday evening. 如果一切按照計劃進行，首場音樂會將是在週二晚上。"]}]}]},"about":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大約；幾乎；到處，各處；無所事事；周圍，在……附近；無序地，凌亂地；朝相反方向"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"關於，對於；目的是；針對（問題）；忙於，從事於；對……表示（情緒或心態）；各處，四下；在……附近；（某人或某事物）具有（某種特性）；圍繞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"現成的，能得到的；即將（做……）的，快要（發生……）的 （be about to do sth.）；四處走動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>about</b> to introduce who or what something relates to or concerns. 關於; 對於","examples":["She knew a lot about food. 她對食品懂得很多。","He never complains about his wife. 他對他妻子從不抱怨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you mention the things that an activity or institution is <b>about</b>, you are saying what it involves or what its aims are. 涉及; 旨在","examples":["Leadership is about the ability to implement change. 領導才能是一種實行變革的能力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>about</b> after some adjectives to indicate the person or thing that a feeling or state of mind relates to. 為…感到 (用在某些形容詞後，表示與某種感覺或心態有關的人或事)","examples":["\"I'm sorry about Patrick,\" she said. “我為帕特里克感到難過，”她說道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>about</b> a problem, you take action in order to solve it. 針對","examples":["Rachel was going to do something about Jacob. 雷切爾要對雅各布採取行動。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you say that there is a particular quality <b>about</b> someone or something, you mean that they have this quality. 在… (具有某種品質)","examples":["There was a warmth and passion about him I never knew existed. 他身上有一種我從來沒有認識到的熱情和激情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you put something <b>about</b> a person or thing, you put it around them. 圍繞","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>About</b> is also a preposition. 各處","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>About</b> is used in front of a number to show that the number is not exact. 大約","examples":["The rate of inflation is running at about 2.7 percent. 通貨膨脹率大約在2.7%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something moves <b>about</b>, they keep moving in different directions. 到處","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>about</b>, they are present or available. 在場的; 可得到的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>about</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are going to do it very soon. If something is <b>about</b> <b>to</b> happen, it will happen very soon. 就要…的","examples":["I think he's about to leave. 我想他就要離開。","Argentina has lifted all restrictions on trade and visas are about to be abolished. 阿根廷已經取消了所有的貿易限制，簽證就要被廢除了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>out and about</b>, they are going out and doing things, especially after they have been unable to for a while. 到外面活動","examples":["Despite considerable pain she has been getting out and about almost as normal. 儘管很疼，她已經在幾乎像正常人一樣到外面活動了。"]}]}]},"across":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"從一邊到另一邊；在……對面；朝，向；寬；橫向字謎答案"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"從一邊到另一邊；橫過，穿過；在……對面；遍及；在……上；跨越（政治、宗教、社會隔閡等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something goes <b>across</b> a place or a boundary, they go from one side of it to the other. 過","examples":["She walked across the floor and lay down on the bed. 她走過地板躺在了床上。","He watched Karl run across the street to Tommy. 他看著卡爾橫穿那條街道向湯米跑去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is situated or stretched <b>across</b> something else, it is situated or stretched from one side of it to the other. 跨越","examples":["...the floating bridge across Lake Washington in Seattle. …橫跨西雅圖華盛頓湖的浮橋。","He scrawled his name across the bill. 他在賬單上草草地寫了他的名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is lying <b>across</b> an object or place, it is resting on it and partly covering it. 在…上","examples":["She found her clothes lying across the chair. 她發現她的衣服平放在椅子上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>across</b> something such as a street, river, or area is on the other side of it. 在…另一邊","examples":["Anyone from the houses across the road could see him. 在路另一邊的那些房子裡的任何一個人都能看到他。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>across</b> to say that a particular expression is shown on someone's face. (表情) 在 (某人臉) 上","examples":["An enormous grin spread across his face. 一個燦爛的笑容綻開在他的臉上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone hits you <b>across</b> the face or head, they hit you on that part. (擊打) 在…上","examples":["Graham hit him across the face with the gun, then pushed him against the wall. 格林厄姆用槍打在他的臉上，然後把他推到牆上。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When something happens <b>across</b> a place or organization, it happens equally everywhere within it. 在…各處","examples":["The film opens across the country on December 11. 這部電影於12月11日在全國各地上映。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When something happens <b>across</b> a political, religious, or social barrier, it involves people in different groups. 在…裡","examples":["...parties competing across the political spectrum. …在政治領域裡競爭的黨派。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Across</b> is also an adverb. 從一邊到另一邊","examples":["Richard stood up and walked across to the window. 理查德站起來，走到了窗戶那邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Across</b> is also an adverb. 跨越","examples":["Trim toenails straight across using nail clippers. 用指甲刀整塊地剪腳指甲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Across</b> is also an adverb. 在對面","examples":["They parked across from the Castro Theatre. 他們在卡斯特羅劇院對面停了車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you look <b>across</b> at a place, person, or thing, you look toward them. 向","examples":["He glanced across at his sleeping wife. 他瞥向睡著的妻子。","She rose from the chair and gazed across at him. 她從椅子上站起凝目朝他望去。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Across</b> is used in measurements to show the width of something. …寬","examples":["This hand-decorated plate measures 14 inches across. 這個手繪盤子有14英寸寬。"]}]}]},"along":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"沿著，順著；靠著……邊；在某處"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向前；一起，一道；進行，進展；（前）來，到某處；到相當的程度；傳播"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move or look <b>along</b> something such as a road, you move or look toward one end of it. 沿著","examples":["Pedro walked along the street alone. 佩德羅獨自一人沿著這條街走。","The young man led Mark Ryle along a corridor. 那個青年男子帶著馬克·賴爾沿著一條走廊走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is situated <b>along</b> a road, river, or corridor, it is situated in it or beside it. 在…裡; 在…邊上","examples":["...enormous traffic jams all along the roads. …各條道路上嚴重的交通堵塞。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something moves <b>along</b>, they keep moving in a particular direction. 向前地","examples":["She skipped and danced along. 她向前蹦跳著、舞蹈著。","He raised his voice a little, talking into the wind as they walked along. 當他們向前走時, 他提高了一點兒嗓門, 迎風講著話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is going <b>along</b> in a particular way, you mean that it is progressing in that way. 一直","examples":["...the negotiations which have been dragging along interminably. …這場一直以來無限地拖沓著的談判。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you take someone or something <b>along</b> when you go somewhere, you take them with you. 一起地","examples":["This is open to women of all ages, so bring along your friends and colleagues. 這對所有年齡的婦女開放，所以帶你的朋友和同事一起來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something is coming <b>along</b> or is sent <b>along</b>, they are coming or being sent to a particular place. 與“來”或“去”搭配，表示來或去某一地方","examples":["She invited everyone she knew to come along. 她邀請了所有認識的人過來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>along with</b> to mention someone or something else that is also involved in an action or situation. 同…一起","examples":["The baby's mother escaped from the fire along with two other children. 這個嬰兒的母親和其他兩個孩子一起從火裡逃了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something has been true or been present <b>all along</b>, it has been true or been present throughout a period of time. 一直","examples":["I've been fooling myself all along. 我一直在騙我自己。"]}]}]},"above":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（數量或度量）在……以上，超過；在（或向）……上面；（級別或地位上）高於； （重要性、質量）超過，勝過；（因善良或誠實正直而）不至於，不屑於（做某事）；（聲音）比……更響亮，蓋過；不受……影響，免於；（重要性、質量）超過，勝過"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（級別或地位上）高於；在（或向）上面，在（或向）較高處；高於，超出（特定數量、比率或標準）；上文，前文"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"前文述及的，上述的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上文提及之事，前文所提之事（the above）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>above</b> another one, it is directly over it or higher than it. 在…上方","examples":["He lifted his hands above his head. 他雙手舉過頭頂。","Apartment 46 was a quiet apartment, unlike the one above it. 46號公寓是一套安靜的公寓，不像它上面的那一套。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or measurement is <b>above</b> a particular level, it is greater than that level. (數量或度量) 高於","examples":["The temperature crept up to just above 40 degrees. 氣溫慢慢升至剛過40度。","Victoria Falls has had above average levels of rainfall this year. 維多利亞瀑布今年的降雨量高於平均水平。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you hear one sound <b>above</b> another, it is louder or clearer than the second one. (聲音) 高過","examples":["Then there was a woman's voice, rising shrilly above the barking. 然後是一個女人的聲音，尖利刺耳，高過了狗吠聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>above</b> you, they are in a higher social position than you or in a position of authority over you. (職位或社會地位) 高於","examples":["I married above myself. 我和比我地位高的人結了婚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone thinks they are <b>above</b> something, you mean that they act as if they are too good or important for it. 不屑於; 不至於","examples":["This was clearly a failure by someone who thought he was above failure. 這顯然是一個自以為不會失敗的人所經歷的一次失敗。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone is <b>above</b> criticism or suspicion, they cannot be criticized or suspected because of their good qualities or their position. 不受 (批評或懷疑)","examples":["He was a respected academic and above suspicion. 他是一位受敬重的學者，不能受懷疑。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you value one person or thing <b>above</b> any other, you value them more or consider that they are more important. 勝過","examples":["...his tendency to put the team above everything. …他的一切以團隊為重的傾向。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Above</b> is also an adverb. 在上面","examples":["A long scream sounded from somewhere above. 從上面什麼地方傳來一聲長長的尖叫。","...a picture of the new plane as seen from above. …一張該新型飛機的俯瞰圖片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Above</b> is also an adverb. 高於","examples":["Banks have been charging 25 percent and above for unsecured loans. 銀行一直以來對無擔保貸款收取25%或更高的費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Above</b> is also an adverb. (職位或社會地位) 在上","examples":["The policemen admitted beating the student, but said they were acting on orders from above. 警察承認打了這個學生，但是說他們是根據上級命令列事的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In writing, you use <b>above</b> to refer to something that has already been mentioned or discussed. 以上","examples":["Several conclusions could be drawn from the results described above. 幾個結論可從上述的那些結果中得出。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Above</b> is also a noun. 上述內容","examples":["For additional information, contact any of the above. 欲知詳情，請與上述任一人聯絡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Above</b> is also an adjective. 上述的","examples":["For a copy of their brochure, write to the above address. 欲取得一份他們的宣傳手冊, 寫信到上述地址。"]}]}]},"among":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……當中，周圍是；與……在一起；……之一；在……群體中；為……所共有；彼此間；以及"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is situated or moving <b>among</b> a group of things or people is surrounded by them. 在…當中","examples":["...youths in their late teens sitting among adults. …坐在成年人當中的十八九歲的青年們。","They walked among the crowds in Red Square. 他們走在紅場上的人群之中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>among</b> people of a particular kind, you are with them and having contact with them. 與…在一起","examples":["Things weren't so bad, after all. I was among friends again. 情況畢竟沒有那麼糟。我又和朋友們在一起了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>among</b> a group, they are a member of that group and share its characteristics. …之一","examples":["A fifteen year old girl was among the injured. 一個15歲的女孩是受傷人員之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you want to focus on something that is happening within a particular group of people, you can say that it is happening <b>among</b> that group. 在…中間","examples":["Homicide is the leading cause of death among black men. 兇殺在黑人男子中是主要死因。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something happens <b>among</b> a group of people, it happens within the whole of that group or between the members of that group. 在…之中","examples":["The calls for reform come as intense debate continues among the leadership over the next five-year economic plan. 當圍繞下一個五年經濟計劃的激烈爭論在領導層中繼續時，改革的呼聲到來了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something such as a feeling, opinion, or situation exists <b>among</b> a group of people, most of them have it or experience it. 為…所共有","examples":["There was some concern among book and magazine retailers after last Wednesday's news. 上週三的新聞之後，圖書與雜誌零售商都有了些擔憂。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something applies to a particular person or thing <b>among</b> <b>others</b>, it also applies to other people or things. 以及","examples":["...a news conference attended among others by our foreign affairs correspondent. …有我們的駐外記者和其他人參加的一個新聞釋出會。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something is shared <b>among</b> a number of people, some of it is given to all of them. 在…中","examples":["Most of the furniture was left to the neighbours or distributed among friends. 大多數傢俱留給了鄰居們或者分給了朋友們。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If people talk, fight, or agree <b>among</b> <b>themselves</b>, they do it together, without involving anyone else. 在 (他們自己) 之間","examples":["The girls stood aside, talking among themselves, looking over their shoulders at the boys. 這些女孩子站在一邊，互相交談著並且扭過頭去看著那些男孩子。"]}]}]},"beside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……旁邊，在……附近；與……相比；除……以外（還），除……以外（不再）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在附近；況且，此外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>beside</b> something else is at the side of it or next to it. 在…旁邊","examples":["On the table beside an empty plate was a pile of books. 桌上的空碟子旁擺著一摞書。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>beside yourself</b> <b>with</b> anger or excitement, you are extremely angry or excited. 發狂","examples":["He had shouted down the phone at her, beside himself with anxiety. 他在電話裡衝她大吼大叫，急得要發狂了。"]}]}]},"at":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（表示存在或出現的地點、場所、位置、空間）；在……歲時；在……遠；以（某種價格、速度等）；向，朝；處於……狀態；處於最佳（或最差等）狀態；達；因為；在……方面；響應；忙於；（武器）瞄準；用，以；（抓）住；從事於；衝（某人……）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"阿特（寮國貨幣基本單位att）；砈（極不穩定放射性元素）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"密封的（airtight）；大氣（atmosphere）；原子的（atomic）；氣溫（air temperature）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to indicate the place or event where something happens or is situated. 在 (某地)","examples":["He will be at the airport to meet her. 他將在機場見她。","I didn't like being alone at home. 我不喜歡獨自在家。","They agreed to meet at a restaurant in Soho. 他們約定了在索霍區的一家餐館裡見面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>at</b> something such as a table, a door, or someone's side, you are next to it or them. 在…旁邊","examples":["An assistant sat typing away at a table beside him. 一名助手坐在他身邊的一張桌子旁打字。","At his side was a beautiful young woman. 他的身邊是一位漂亮的年輕女子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you are describing where someone or something is, you can say that they are <b>at</b> a certain distance. You can also say that one thing is <b>at</b> an angle in relation to another thing. 以 (某距離、某角度)","examples":["The two journalists followed at a discreet distance. 那兩名記者保持一段適當的距離跟在後面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>at</b> a particular time, that is the time when it happens or begins to happen. 在 (某時刻)","examples":["The funeral will be carried out this afternoon at 3:00. 葬禮將在今天下午3點舉行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>at</b> a particular age, you do it when you are that age. 在 (某歲時)","examples":["Zachary started playing violin at age 4. 扎卡里4歲開始拉小提琴。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone is <b>at</b> a particular school or college, they go there regularly to study. 在 (某學校)","examples":["Their daughter is a sophomore at Yale. 他們的女兒在耶魯大學讀大二。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to express a rate, frequency, level, or price. 以 (某速度、頻率、水平或價格)","examples":["I drove back down the motorway at normal speed. 我以正常速度沿高速公路往回開。","Check the oil at regular intervals, and have the car serviced regularly. 定期檢查機油，經常保養汽車。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> before a number or amount to indicate a measurement. 在 (某數量)","examples":["...as unemployment stays pegged at three million. …由於失業人數維持在300萬。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you look <b>at</b> someone or something, you look toward them. If you direct an object or a comment <b>at</b> someone, you direct it toward them. 朝 (方向)","examples":["He looked at Michael and laughed. 他朝邁克爾看去，笑了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can use <b>at</b> after verbs such as \"smile\" or \"wave\" and before nouns referring to people to indicate that you have put on an expression or made a gesture that someone is meant to see or understand. 衝 (某人…)","examples":["She opened the door and stood there, frowning at me. 她開啟門站在那裡，衝我皺著眉頭。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you point or gesture <b>at</b> something, you move your arm or head in its direction so that it will be noticed by someone you are with. 對著(某物)","examples":["He pointed at the empty bottle and the waitress quickly replaced it. 他向那個空瓶指了指，女服務員迅速換了它。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you are working <b>at</b> something, you are dealing with it. If you are aiming <b>at</b> something, you are trying to achieve it. 在 (某目標上)","examples":["She has worked hard at her marriage. 她在婚姻上已經很努力了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something is done <b>at</b> someone's invitation or request, it is done as a result of it. 應 (某人之邀)","examples":["She left the light on in the bathroom at his request. 她應他的要求讓浴室裡的燈開著。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to say that someone or something is in a particular state or condition. 在 (某狀態或情況下)","examples":["I am afraid we are not at liberty to disclose that information. 恐怕我們無權透露那資訊。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> before a possessive pronoun and a superlative adjective to say that someone or something has more of a particular quality than at any other time. 在 (某人或某事物最…的時候)","examples":["When I'm on the soccer field, I'm at my happiest. 當我在足球場上時，我最開心了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to say how something is being done. 以 (某方式)","examples":["Three people were killed by shots fired at random from a minibus. 三個人被一輛小巴里亂射的子彈打死了。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to show that someone is doing something repeatedly. 在 (某物上反覆做某事)","examples":["She lowered the handkerchief which she had kept dabbing at her eyes. 她放下了那塊她一直在反覆擦眼睛的手絹。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to indicate an activity or task when saying how well someone does it. 在 (某方面)","examples":["I'm good at my work. 我擅長我的工作。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You use <b>at</b> to indicate what someone is reacting to. 因 (某事物)","examples":["Elena was annoyed at having had to wait so long for him. 埃琳娜因不得不等他那麼長的時間而惱火。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a Laotian monetary unit worth one hundredth of a kip 老特; 寮國貨幣單位，100老特等於1基普","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Austria 奧地利","examples":[]}]}]},"behind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（或向）……的後面；落後於；是……背後的原因；支援；（……的外表）之下；成為（某人的）過去；低於；在……死後"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在後面；留在原地；落後（於）；拖欠，不按時"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>屁股；（澳橄）射門得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>behind</b> a thing or person, it is on the other side of them from you, or nearer their back rather than their front. 在…後面","examples":["I put one of the cushions behind his head. 我把其中一個墊子放在了他腦後。","They were parked behind the truck. 它們被停在了卡車後面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are walking or travelling <b>behind</b> someone or something, you are following them. (跟隨) 在…後面","examples":["Keith wandered along behind him. 基思跟在他後面閒逛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>behind</b> a desk, counter, or bar, they are on the other side of it from where you are. 在…後面 (指另一側)","examples":["The colonel was sitting behind a cheap wooden desk. 上校坐在一張廉價的木質書桌後面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you shut a door or gate <b>behind</b> you, you shut it after you have gone through it. 在…身後","examples":["I walked out and closed the door behind me. 我走了出來並關上了身後的門。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The people, reason, or events <b>behind</b> a situation are the causes of it or are responsible for it. 在背後; 在幕後","examples":["It is still not clear who was behind the killing. 至今尚不清楚誰是這起謀殺案的幕後策劃者。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>behind</b> you, they support you and help you. 在背後 (支援)","examples":["He had the state's judicial power behind him. 他有國家司法力量在其背後支援他。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you refer to what is <b>behind</b> someone's outside appearance, you are referring to a characteristic which you cannot immediately see or is not obvious, but which you think is there. 在 (某人的外表) 背後","examples":["What lay behind his anger was really the hurt he felt at Grace's refusal. 在他的憤怒背後其實是遭格雷斯拒絕而感到的心痛。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are <b>behind</b> someone, you are less successful than them, or have done less or advanced less. (成就、業績、進展等) 在 (某人) 之後","examples":["She finished second behind the American, Ann Cody, in the 800 metres. 她在800米賽跑中在美國的安•科迪之後跑到終點，位居第2。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If an experience is <b>behind</b> you, it happened in your past and will not happen again, or no longer affects you. (將經歷拋) 到…腦後","examples":["Maureen put the nightmare behind her. 莫琳將噩夢拋諸腦後。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you have a particular achievement <b>behind</b> you, you have managed to reach this achievement, and other people consider it to be important or valuable. (成就) 在…背後","examples":["He has 20 years of loyal service to Barclays Bank behind him. 他背後有20年忠心為巴克利銀行工作的經歷。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something is <b>behind</b> schedule, it is not as far advanced as people had planned. If someone is <b>behind</b> schedule, they are not progressing as quickly at something as they had planned. (落) 在 (時間進度) 之後","examples":["The work is 22 weeks behind schedule. 這項工作比預計時間推遲了22周。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Behind</b> is also an adverb. 在後面","examples":["Rising into the hills behind are 800 acres of parkland. 往上延伸至後面小山的是800英畝的草木區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Behind</b> is also an adverb. (跟隨) 在後面","examples":["The troopers followed behind, every muscle tensed for the sudden gunfire. 騎兵們跟在後面，每一塊肌肉都因突如其來的炮火而繃得緊緊的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Behind</b> is also an adverb. 在後面","examples":["The rapid development of technology means that she is now far behind, and will need retraining. 科技的快速發展意味著她現在已經遠遠落後了，將需要再訓練。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you stay <b>behind</b>, you remain in a place after other people have gone. (留) 在後面","examples":["About 1,200 personnel will remain behind to take care of the air base. 約有1200名人員將留下來照管空軍基地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you leave something or someone <b>behind</b>, you do not take them with you when you go. (把…留) 在後面","examples":["The rebels fled into the mountains, leaving behind their weapons and supplies. 叛亂者逃進了山裡，丟下了武器和給養物資。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>behind</b> is the part of your body that you sit on. 臀部","examples":[]}]}]},"during":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……期間；在……期間的某個時候"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>during</b> a period of time or an event, it happens continuously, or happens several times between the beginning and end of that period or event. 在…期間內 (不斷髮生)","examples":["Sandstorms are common during the Saudi Arabian winter. 在沙烏地阿拉伯的冬季期間內沙暴很常見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something develops <b>during</b> a period of time, it develops gradually from the beginning to the end of that period. 在…期間 (逐步發展)","examples":["Wages have fallen by more than twenty percent during the past two months. 在過去的兩個月期間工資已下降了二十多個百分點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An event that happens <b>during</b> a period of time happens at some point or moment in that period. 在…期間的某一刻 (發生)","examples":["During his visit, the Pope will also bless the new hospital. 在他訪問期間，教皇也將為新醫院祈福。"]}]}]},"against":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"反對；（行為）違背……；（法律或法規）禁止；與……競爭；對……造成傷害（威脅，不利）；碰；倚著；逆向；以……為背景；與……相比；防備，抵禦；討厭某人，不贊同某人；作為（某物的）應付款項；（賭博用語）預計……的失敗"}],"sections":[]},"around":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"圍繞，環繞；大約；周圍，四周；以圓周計算；到處，向各處；轉彎，掉頭；閒散地，無目的地；迴圈往復地；出現，可用；活躍"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"圍繞，環繞；到處，向各處；在那邊，到那邊；在……周圍，在附近；大約，大概；以……為中心；避開，繞過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be positioned <b>around</b> a place or object means to surround it or be on all sides of it. To move <b>around</b> a place means to go along its edge, back to your starting point. 在…四周","examples":["She looked at the papers around her. 她看了看她四周的報紙。","Today she wore her hair down around her shoulders. 今天她把頭髮披在了肩上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you move <b>around</b> a corner or obstacle, you move to the other side of it. If you look <b>around</b> a corner or obstacle, you look to see what is on the other side. 繞過","examples":["The photographer stopped clicking and hurried around the corner. 該攝影師停止按動快門，匆匆繞過那個拐角。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you move <b>around</b> a place, you travel through it, going to most of its parts. If you look <b>around</b> a place, you look at every part of it. 四處 (走動、看)","examples":["I've been walking around Moscow and the town is terribly quiet. 我一直在莫斯科四處走動，城裡極其安靜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone moves <b>around</b> a place, they move through various parts of that place without having any particular destination. 在…四處 (閒轉)","examples":["These days much of my time is spent weaving my way around cocktail parties. 這些日子我的很多時間花在閒轉於各雞尾酒會上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>around</b> to say that something happens in different parts of a place or area. 在各處","examples":["Police in South Africa say ten people have died in scattered violence around the country. 南非警方稱，該國各地的暴力事件中已有10人死亡。","Elephants were often to be found in swamp in eastern Kenya around the Tana River. 大象經常會在肯亞東部沼澤塔納河各處被發現。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The people <b>around</b> you are the people whom you come into contact with, especially your friends and relatives, and the people you work with. 在…周圍的","examples":["We change our behaviour by observing the behaviour of those around us. 我們透過觀察周圍人的行為舉止來改變自己的行為舉止。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something such as a film, a discussion, or a plan is based <b>around</b> something, that thing is its main theme. 圍繞 (某主題)","examples":["The novel is a political thriller loosely based around current political issues. 這部小說是一本在一定程度上圍繞當前政治問題撰寫的政治驚悚小說。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When you are giving measurements, you can use <b>around</b> to talk about the distance along the edge of something round. 繞…一週 (的長度)","examples":["She was 5 foot 4 inches, 38 around the chest, 28 around the waist and 40 around the hips. 她身高5英尺4英寸，胸圍38英寸，腰圍28英寸，臀圍40英寸。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also a preposition. 在… (無所事事)","examples":["He used to skip lessons and hang around the harbour with some other boys. 他過去經常逃課，和其他一些男孩子在碼頭上閒蕩。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also a preposition. 在…左右","examples":["He expects the elections to be held around November. 他期待選舉在11月左右舉行。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also an adverb. 在…四周地","examples":["...a village with a rocky river, a ruined castle and hills all around. …一個有一條多石的河流和一座被毀的城堡、四面環山的村莊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also an adverb. 四處地","examples":["He backed away from the edge, looking all around at the flat horizon. 他從那邊上退了回來，環視著平坦的地平線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also an adverb. 四處地","examples":["My mornings are spent rushing around after him. 我的那些上午都花在跟著他四處奔波上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Around</b> is also an adverb. 在各處地","examples":["What the hell do you think you're doing following me around? 你到處跟著我究竟是在幹什麼？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you turn <b>around</b>, you turn so that you are facing in the opposite direction. 朝相反方向地","examples":["I turned around and wrote the title on the blackboard. 我轉過身將標題寫在了黑板上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you go <b>around</b> to someone's house, you visit them. (去) 拜訪地","examples":["She helped me unpack my things and then we went around to see the other girls. 她幫助我開啟行李，然後我們去看望別的女孩。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>around</b> in expressions such as <b>sit around</b> and <b>hang around</b> when you are saying that someone is spending time in a place and not doing anything very important. 無所事事地","examples":["I'm just going to be hanging around twiddling my thumbs. 我正要無所事事地旋弄拇指。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you move things <b>around</b>, you move them so that they are in different places. 別處地","examples":["Furniture in the classroom should not be changed around without warning the blind child. 該教室裡的設施未經告知該盲童不得挪動。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a wheel or object turns <b>around</b>, it turns. 繞圈地","examples":["The boat started to spin around in the water. 那條船開始在水裡打轉。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>around</b>, they exist or are present in a place. 在某處","examples":["You haven't seen my publisher anywhere around, have you? 你還沒有在哪兒看見我的出版商，是吧？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>around</b> in expressions such as <b>this time around</b> or <b>to come around</b> when you are describing something that has happened before or things that happen regularly. 又一次地","examples":["Senator Bentsen has declined to get involved this time around. 參議員本特森這次又拒絕了介入。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>Around</b> means approximately. 大約地","examples":["My salary was around $45,000 plus a car and expenses. 我的工資大約是$45000，外加一輛車和各種報銷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Around about</b> means approximately. 大約","examples":["There is an outright separatist party but it only scored around about 10 percent in the vote. 有一個極端分離主義黨派，但是該黨在選舉中只取得了大約10%的選票。"]}]}]},"excepting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"<正式>除……之外"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"只是，要不是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>excepting</b> to introduce the only thing that prevents a statement from being completely true. 除…外","examples":["The source of meat for much of this region (excepting Japan) has traditionally been the pig. 該區域大部分地區（除日本外）的食肉傳統上都是豬肉。"]}]}]},"except":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除……外，不包括"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"除了，只是；要不是"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不包括，把……排除在外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>except</b> to introduce the only thing or person that a statement does not apply to, or a fact that prevents a statement from being completely true. 除…之外","examples":["I wouldn't have accepted anything except a job in New York. 我當時是不會接受一份除紐約以外任何其他地方的工作的。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Except</b> is also a conjunction. 除了…","examples":["Freddie would tell me nothing about what he was writing, except that it was to be a Christmas play. 弗雷迪不願告訴我他在寫什麼，只說會是個聖誕劇本。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>except</b> or <b>except for</b> to introduce the only thing or person that prevents a statement from being completely true. 除了…","examples":["He hadn't eaten a thing except for one forkful of salad. 除了一口沙拉，他什麼都沒吃。"]}]}]},"between":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（空間上）在……中間；（時間上）在……之間；（數量、重量、距離等）介於……之間；分隔著；（表示兩方或多方關係）在……之間；合用，共享；透過共同努力，一起；（兩人）私下間；往返於"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（空間或時間上）介於……之間（in between）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>between</b> two things or is <b>in between</b> them, it has one of the things on one side of it and the other thing on the other side. 在…中間","examples":["She left the table to stand between the two men. 她離開桌子，站在兩個男人中間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people or things travel <b>between</b> two places, they travel regularly from one place to the other and back again. (往返) 於…之間","examples":["I spent a lot of time in the early Eighties travelling between Waco and El Paso. 在八十年代早期，我花了很多時間往返於韋科和埃爾帕索之間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A relationship, discussion, or difference <b>between</b> two people, groups, or things is one that involves them both or relates to them both. (表示相互關係) 在…之間","examples":["I think the relationship between patients and doctors has got a lot less personal. 我認為醫生和患者之間的關係已經少了許多人情味。","There have been intensive discussions between the two governments in recent days. 最近兩國政府之間進行了集中的會談。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something stands <b>between</b> you and what you want, it prevents you from having it. 在…之間 (阻礙)","examples":["His sense of duty often stood between him and the enjoyment of life. 他的責任感常使他不能安心地享受生活。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>between</b> two amounts or ages, it is greater or older than the first one and smaller or younger than the second one. (數量、年齡) 介乎…之間","examples":["Increase the amount of time you spend exercising by walking between 15 and 20 minutes. 步行15到20分鐘來增加你用於運動的時間。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something happens <b>between</b> or <b>in between</b> two times or events, it happens after the first time or event and before the second one. (指時間) 在…之間","examples":["The canal was built between 1793 and 1797. 該運河建於1793至1797年之間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you must choose <b>between</b> two or more things, you must choose just one of them. 在…之中 (選擇一個)","examples":["Students will be able to choose between English, French and Russian as their first foreign language. 學生們將可以在英語、法語和俄語中任選一門作為他們的第一外語。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If people or places have a particular amount of something <b>between</b> them, this is the total amount that they have. 共有","examples":["The three sites employ 12,500 people between them. 3個工地共僱傭12500個人。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When something is divided or shared <b>between</b> people, they each have a share of it. 共同享有","examples":["There is only one bathroom shared between eight bedrooms. 只有一個供8個臥室共同使用的衛生間。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Between</b> or <b>in</b> <b>between</b> is also an adverb. (指時間) 在…之間","examples":["My life had been a journey from crisis to crisis with only a brief time in between. 我的生活總是從一個危機到另一個危機，其間間隔的時間都很短。"]}]}]},"by":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"由，被；透過，憑藉……；相差；在……旁邊；到……之前；抓著（身體或東西某個部位）；按照，依據；以……計；在……期間；在（某處）短暫停留；乘以，除以；以……名義（發誓）；就（本性、職業或出身）而言"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"經過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>by</b> a person or thing, that person or thing does it. 被","examples":["The feast was served by his mother and sisters. 宴席由他的母親和姐妹們招待。","I was amazed by their discourtesy and lack of professionalism. 我為他們的無禮和職業精神的缺乏所震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a book, a piece of music, or a painting is <b>by</b> a particular person, you mean that this person wrote it or created it. 由…創作","examples":["A painting by Van Gogh has been sold in New York for more than eighty-two million dollars. 一幅由梵高創作的畫在紐約賣到超過八千二百萬美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>by</b> a particular means, you do it using that thing. 以…方式","examples":["If you're travelling by car, ask whether there are parking facilities nearby. 如果你開汽車旅行，問問附近是否有停車設施。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you achieve one thing <b>by</b> doing another thing, your action enables you to achieve the first thing. 透過","examples":["Make the sauce by boiling the cream and stock together in a pan. 透過將乳酪和高湯一起放在平底鍋裡煮來製作調味料。","The all-female yacht crew made history by becoming the first to sail round the world. 全部由女性組成的遊艇船員透過首次環球航行而創造了歷史。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>by</b> in phrases such as \"by chance\" or \"by accident\" to indicate whether or not an event was planned. 由於","examples":["I met him by chance out walking yesterday. 昨天出去散步時我無意中遇到了他。","He opened Ingrid's letter by mistake. 他誤拆了英格麗德的信。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone is a particular type of person <b>by</b> nature, <b>by</b> profession, or <b>by</b> birth, they are that type of person because of their nature, their profession, or the family they were born into. 就…而言","examples":["I am certainly lucky to have a kind wife who is loving by nature. 我的確幸運有一位仁慈的妻子，她天生富有愛心。","She's a nurse by profession and now runs a counselling service for women. 她是護士出身，現在經營著一家針對女性的諮詢服務公司。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something must be done <b>by</b> law, it happens according to the law. If something is the case <b>by</b> particular standards, it is the case according to the standards. 根據","examples":["Pharmacists are required by law to give the medicine prescribed by the doctor. 根據法律，藥劑師被要求只配醫生開列的藥。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say what someone means <b>by</b> a particular word or expression, you are saying what they intend the word or expression to refer to. 透過 (說某詞或某話)","examples":["Stella knew what he meant by \"start again.\" 斯特拉知道他說“再次開始”是什麼意思。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you hold someone or something <b>by</b> a particular part of them, you hold that part. 透過","examples":["He caught her by the shoulder and turned her around. 他抓住她的肩膀，使她轉過身。","She was led by the arm to a small room at the far end of the corridor. 她被抓著胳膊帶到走廊另一頭的一個小屋裡。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>by</b> something else is beside it and close to it. 在…旁邊","examples":["Judith was sitting in a rocking chair by the window. 朱迪絲坐在窗邊的搖椅上。","Felicity Maxwell stood by the bar and ordered a glass of wine. 費利西蒂·馬克斯韋爾站在吧檯旁，叫了一杯葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If a person or vehicle goes <b>by</b> you, they move past you without stopping. 經過","examples":["A few cars passed close by me. 幾輛車從我近旁駛過。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you stop <b>by</b> a place, you visit it for a short time. 暫時 (拜訪)","examples":["We had made arrangements to stop by her house in Pacific Grove. 我們已安排好順道去她在太平洋路的家拜訪。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something happens <b>by</b> a particular time, it happens at or before that time. 到…時; 在…之前","examples":["By eight o'clock he had arrived at my hotel. 他八點前已到了我住的旅館。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you do something <b>by</b> day, you do it during the day. If you do it <b>by</b> night, you do it during the night. 在…期間","examples":["By day a woman could safely walk the streets. 白天，婦女可以安全地在街上走。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"In arithmetic, you use <b>by</b> before the second number in a multiplication or division sum. 用於乘除法中","examples":["...an annual rate of 22.8 percent (1.9 multiplied by 12). …每年22.8％的比率（1.9乘以12）。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>by</b> to talk about measurements of area. For example, if a room is twenty feet <b>by</b> fourteen feet, it measures twenty feet in one direction and fourteen feet in the other direction. 表示面積尺寸","examples":["Three prisoners were sharing one small cell 3 metres by 2½ metres. 3名囚犯共住一間3米長2.5米寬的小牢房。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If something increases or decreases <b>by</b> a particular amount, that amount is gained or lost. (表示數量、程度等) 以…之差","examples":["Violent crime has increased by 10 percent since last year. 暴力犯罪自去年以來已上升了10％。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"Things that are made or sold <b>by</b> the million or <b>by</b> the dozen are made or sold in those quantities. 按…計算","examples":["Packages arrived by the dozen from America. 成打的包裹從美國寄來。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You use <b>by</b> in expressions such as \"minute by minute\" and \"drop by drop\" to talk about things that happen gradually, not all at once. 表示循序漸進的速度","examples":["His father began to lose his memory bit by bit, becoming increasingly forgetful. 他父親的記憶力開始一點點衰退，變得越來越健忘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>by yourself</b>, you are alone. 獨自地","examples":["...a dark-haired man sitting by himself in a corner. …一個獨自坐在角落裡的、深色頭髮的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>by yourself</b>, you succeed in doing it without anyone helping you. 獨立地","examples":["I didn't know if I could raise a child by myself. 我不知道是否能獨立撫養一個孩子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>By</b> is also an adverb. 在旁邊","examples":["Large numbers of security police stood by. 許多秘密警察站在旁邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>By</b> is also an adverb. 經過","examples":["The bomb went off as a police patrol went by. 炸彈在巡警隊經過時爆炸了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>By</b> is also an adverb. 暫時地","examples":["I'll stop by after dinner and we'll have that talk. 晚餐後我會過來待會兒，我們可以談談那件事。"]}]}]},"below":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（位置）在……下面； （數、量、水平等）在……以下；（職位、官銜等）低於"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在下面；（數字或級別）在……以下；在下文中；在下層甲板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>below</b> something else, it is in a lower position. 在…下面","examples":["He appeared from the apartment directly below Leonard's. 他從倫納德家正下方的公寓裡走了出來。","The sun had already sunk below the horizon. 太陽已沉下地平線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>below</b> a particular amount, rate, or level, it is less than that amount, rate, or level. (數量、比率、水平等) 在…下面","examples":["Night temperatures can drop below 15 degrees Celsius. 夜間溫度可能會降到15攝氏度以下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>below</b> you in an organization, they are lower in rank. (地位) 低於","examples":["Such people often experience less stress than those in the ranks immediately below them. 這些人經受的壓力通常比那些職位剛好低於他們的人要小。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Below</b> is also an adverb. 在下面","examples":["We climbed rather perilously down a rope-ladder to the boat below. 我們冒著危險沿著繩梯爬到了下邊的小船上。","...a view to the street below. …樓下街景。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>below</b> in a piece of writing to refer to something that is mentioned later. 在下文中","examples":["Please write to me at the address below. 請按以下地址給我寫信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Below</b> is also an adverb. 在下面","examples":["...temperatures at zero or below. …零度或零度以下。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>below ground</b> or <b>below the ground</b>, it is in the ground. 在地表下","examples":["They have designed a system which pumps up water from nearly 1,000 feet below ground. 他們設計了一個能從地表以下1000英尺處抽水的系統。"]}]}]},"into":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"到……裡面；觸及，碰撞；朝，向；轉向；關於；轉變成；造成（某種結果）；除；<非正式>對……很有興趣；從事（某職業等）；被迫做，被說服做；成為……的一部分；持續到，直到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you put one thing <b>into</b> another, you put the first thing inside the second. 放到…裡面","examples":["Combine the remaining ingredients and put them into a dish. 把剩餘的配料混起來放到一個盤子裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go <b>into</b> a place or vehicle, you move from being outside it to being inside it. 進; 上 (車)","examples":["I have no idea how he got into Iraq. 我不知道他是怎麼進入伊拉克的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing goes <b>into</b> another, the first thing moves from the outside to the inside of the second thing, by breaking or damaging the surface of it. (透過破壞表面) 進","examples":["The blade missed his kidney, but went into his bowel. 刀片沒刺中他的腎臟，但卻扎進了他的腸子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing gets <b>into</b> another, the first thing enters the second and becomes part of it. 融入; 滲入","examples":["Poisonous chemicals got into the water supply. 有毒的化學藥品進入了供水系統。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are walking or driving a vehicle and you bump <b>into</b> something or crash <b>into</b> something, you hit it accidentally. (意外) 撞上","examples":["A train from New Jersey ploughed into the barrier at the end of the track. 從新澤西駛來的一輛火車撞上了軌道盡頭的柵欄。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you get <b>into</b> a piece of clothing, you put it on. (穿) 上","examples":["She could change into a different outfit in two minutes. 她能在兩分鐘內換上一套不同的衣服。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone or something gets <b>into</b> a particular state, they start being in that state. 進入 (某種狀態)","examples":["I slid into a depression. 我漸漸陷入了抑鬱之中。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you talk someone <b>into</b> doing something, you persuade them to do it. 從事","examples":["They sweet-talked him into selling the farm. 他們甜言蜜語地哄騙他賣掉了那個農場。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something changes <b>into</b> something else, it then has a new form, shape, or nature. 成為","examples":["...to turn a nasty episode into a joke. …把一件不愉快的事轉化成一個小玩笑。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something is cut or split <b>into</b> a number of pieces or sections, it is divided so that it becomes several smaller pieces or sections. 分成","examples":["Sixteen teams are taking part, divided into four groups. 16支隊伍參加，它們被分成4組。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"An investigation <b>into</b> a subject or event is concerned with that subject or event. 關於","examples":["It would provide hundreds of millions of dollars for research into alternative energy sources. 它可以提供數億美元用於可替代能源的研究。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you move or go <b>into</b> a particular career or business, you start working in it. 進入 (某種職業或行業)","examples":["In the early 1980s, it was easy to get into the rental business. 在20世紀80年代早期，進入租賃業是很容易的。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something continues <b>into</b> a period of time, it continues until after that period of time has begun. 進入 (時期)","examples":["He had three children, and lived on into his sixties. 他有3個孩子，並活到了六十多歲。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you are very interested in something and like it very much, you can say that you are <b>into</b> it. 對…很感興趣","examples":["I'm into electronics myself. 我自己對電子學很感興趣。"]}]}]},"less":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"更少地，程度較低地"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"（與不可數名詞連用）較少的，更少的"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"減去，扣除"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"更少，較小；更小（或更無關緊要）的事物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古>等級較低的，次要的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>less</b> to indicate that there is a smaller amount of something than before or than average. You can use \"a little,\" \"a lot,\" \"a bit,\" \"far,\" and \"much\" in front of <b>less</b>. 較少的; 更少的","examples":["People should eat less fat to reduce the risk of heart disease. 人們應該少吃脂肪以減少患心臟病的風險。","...a dishwasher that uses less water and electricity than older machines. …一臺比老式機器用水用電更少的洗碗機。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Less</b> is also a pronoun. 較少","examples":["Borrowers are striving to ease their financial position by spending less and saving more. 借款者都在努力透過少花多存來緩解經濟緊張狀況。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Less</b> is also a quantifier. 較少","examples":["Last year less of the money went into high-technology companies. 去年，投入到高科技公司的錢較少。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>less than</b> before a number or amount to say that the actual number or amount is smaller than this. 少於","examples":["...a country whose entire population is less than 12 million. …一個總人口少於1200萬的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>less than</b> to say that something does not have a particular quality. For example, if you describe something as <b>less than</b> perfect, you mean that it is not perfect at all. 根本不","examples":["Her greeting was less than enthusiastic. 她打招呼根本不熱情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>less</b> to indicate that something or someone has a smaller amount of a quality than they used to or than is average or usual. 比…少地","examples":["I often think about those less fortunate than me. 我經常想到那些不如我幸運的人。","Other amenities, less commonly available, include a library and exercise room. 其他不常有的便利設施包括一個圖書館和健身房。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>less</b> one thing <b>than</b> another, you mean that it is like the second thing rather than the first. 不像…更像…","examples":["At first sight it looked less like a capital city than a mining camp. 第一眼看上去它不像一座首都城市倒更像一個採礦工地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>less</b> than before or <b>less</b> than someone else, you do it to a smaller extent or not as often. 更少地","examples":["We are eating more and exercising less. 我們吃得更多，鍛鍊得卻更少。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are referring to amounts, you use <b>less</b> in front of a number or quantity to indicate that it is to be subtracted from another number or quantity already mentioned. 減去","examples":["You will pay between ten and twenty five percent, less tax. 你要付稅後的10%到25%。"]}]}]},"from":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"從，從……起，從……開始；從……（到……）；來自，出自，寄自，得自；由……（製成）；（兩地的距離）離；從……（離開、取出、扣除）；由於，因為，出於；根據，從……來看；與……（不同）；防，使免受，免遭，防止，阻止，妨礙；不在（通常所在之處）；從……（某位置）看或聽"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（From）（美）弗羅姆（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something comes <b>from</b> a particular person or thing, or if you get something <b>from</b> them, they give it to you or they are the source of it. 來自","examples":["He appealed for information from anyone who saw the attackers. 他呼籲來自目睹襲擊者的資訊。","...an anniversary present from his wife. …他妻子送的一件結婚紀念禮物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who comes <b>from</b> a particular place lives in that place or originally lived there. Something that comes <b>from</b> a particular place was made in that place. 來自","examples":["...an art dealer from Zurich. …一名來自蘇黎世的藝術品商人。","Katy Jones is nineteen and comes from Biloxi. 凱蒂·瓊斯19歲，來自比洛克西。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A person <b>from</b> a particular organization works for that organization. 為…工作","examples":["...a representative from the Israeli embassy. …以色列大使館的一位代表。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something moves or is moved <b>from</b> a place, they leave it or are removed, so that they are no longer there. 從 (某處離開)","examples":["The guests watched as she fled from the room. 客人們看著她逃離房間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you take one thing or person <b>from</b> another, you move that thing or person so that they are no longer with the other or attached to the other. (取) 自","examples":["In many bone transplants, bone can be taken from other parts of the patient's body. 在許多骨移植手術中，骨頭可以取自病人身體的其它部分。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you take something <b>from</b> an amount, you reduce the amount by that much. 從… (扣除)","examples":["The $103 is deducted from Mrs. Adams' salary. 這$103是從亞當斯太太的薪水中扣除的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>From</b> is used in expressions such as <b>away from</b> or <b>absent from</b> to say that someone or something is not present in a place where they are usually found. 從… (離開)","examples":["Her husband worked away from home a lot. 她丈夫經常離家在外工作。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you return <b>from</b> a place or an activity, you return after being in that place or doing that activity. 從… (回來)","examples":["My son has just returned from Amsterdam. 我兒子剛剛從阿姆斯特丹回來。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you are back <b>from</b> a place or activity, you have left it and have returned to your former place. 從… (回來)","examples":["Elaine was just back from work when he called. 他打電話的時候，伊萊恩剛下班回來。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you see or hear something <b>from</b> a particular place, you are in that place when you see it or hear it. 從… (看到或聽到)","examples":["Visitors see the painting from behind a plate glass window. 參觀者可以從平板玻璃窗後面看到這幅畫。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something hangs or sticks out <b>from</b> an object, it is attached to it or held by it. 從… (垂下或伸出)","examples":["Hanging from his right wrist is a heavy gold bracelet. 從他的右腕上垂下的是一隻沉甸甸的金手鐲。","...large fans hanging from ceilings. …在天花板上吊著的大風扇。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You can use <b>from</b> when giving distances. For example, if a place is fifty miles <b>from</b> another place, the distance between the two places is fifty miles. 離…","examples":["...a small park only a few hundred yards from Zurich's main shopping centre. …一個小公園，距離蘇黎世主要購物中心只有幾百碼。","How far is it from here? 離這兒有多遠？"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a road or railway line goes <b>from</b> one place to another, you can travel along it between the two places. 從… (到…)","examples":["...the road from St. Petersburg to Tallinn. …從聖彼得堡到塔林的路。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"<b>From</b> is used, especially in the expression <b>made from</b>, to say what substance has been used to make something. 由… (製成)","examples":["...bread made from white flour. …白麵粉做的麵包。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something changes <b>from</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, it stops being the first thing and becomes the second thing. 由… (變成)","examples":["The expression on his face changed from sympathy to surprise. 他臉上的表情由同情變成驚訝。","Unemployment has fallen from 7.5 to 7.2%. 失業率已從7.5%降至7.2%。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>from</b> after some verbs and nouns when mentioning the cause of something. 因為…","examples":["The problem simply resulted from a difference of opinion. 問題僅因意見不同而引起。","They really do get pleasure from spending money on other people. 他們確實因把錢花在別人身上而從中得到快樂。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>from</b> when you are giving the reason for an opinion. 根據…","examples":["She knew from experience that Dave was about to tell her the truth. 她根據經驗得知戴夫將要告訴她實情。","He sensed from the expression on her face that she had something to say. 他根據她臉上的表情意識到她有話要說。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You can use <b>from</b> when you are talking about the beginning of a period of time. 從 (某時) 起","examples":["She studied painting from 1926 and also worked as a commercial artist. 她從1926年開始研究繪畫，同時也是一名商業美術家。","Breakfast is available to fishermen from 6 a.m. 漁民們從早上6點起就能吃到早飯。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You say <b>from</b> one thing <b>to</b> another when you are stating the range of things that are possible, or when saying that the range of things includes everything in a certain category. 從… (到…)","examples":["There are 94 countries represented in Barcelona, from Algeria to Zimbabwe. 巴塞羅那有從阿爾及利亞到辛巴威94個國家的代表處。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"<b>From</b> is used after verbs with meanings such as \"protect,\" \"free,\" \"keep,\" and \"prevent\" to introduce the action that does not happen, or that someone does not want to happen. (免) 於…","examples":["Such laws could protect the consumer from harmful or dangerous remedies. 這類法律能保護消費者免受有害或危險的治療。"]}]}]},"of":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"……的，屬於；……的一部分；（用於數量詞或容器名詞後）表示計量；住在（某地）；關於，有關；由……製成或組成的；因為，由於；用於動作名詞後表示動作的執行者或承受者；（用於同位結構）即，也就是；（表示人或事物的時空位置）在，當"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> to combine two nouns when the first noun identifies the feature of the second noun that you want to talk about. 用以連線2個名詞，其中第1個名詞指明第2個名詞的特徵","examples":["The average age of the women interviewed was only 21.5. 受訪女性的平均年齡只有21.5歲。","...the population of this town. …這個城鎮的人口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> to combine two nouns, or a noun and a present participle, when the second noun or present participle defines or gives more information about the first noun. 用以連線2個名詞或1個名詞和1個現在分詞，其中第2個名詞或現在分詞限定第1個名詞或給出有關第1個名詞的更多資訊","examples":["She let out a little cry of pain. 她疼得輕輕叫了一聲。","...the problem of having a national shortage of teachers. …一個全國性教師短缺問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after nouns referring to actions to specify the person or thing that is affected by the action or that performs the action. For example, \"the kidnapping of the child\" refers to an action affecting a child; \"the arrival of the next train\" refers to an action performed by a train. 用於動作名詞後以說明此動作的受影響者或執行者","examples":["It sets targets for reduction of greenhouse-gas emissions. 它為減少溫室氣體排放設立了目標。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after words and phrases referring to quantities or groups of things to indicate the substance or thing that is being measured. 用於指數量或物群的詞或短語後以表示受量的物質或事物","examples":["...dozens of people. …幾十人。","...a collection of short stories. …一部短篇小說集。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after the name of someone or something to introduce the institution or place they belong to or are connected with. 用於人或事物名稱後以引入其所屬或所關聯的機構或地點","examples":["...the governor of Missouri. …密蘇里州州長。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after a noun referring to a container to form an expression referring to the container and its contents. 用於指容器的名詞後以構成指該容器及其所容之物的表達","examples":["...a box of tissues. …一盒紙巾。","...a roomful of people. …一屋子人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after a countable noun and before an uncountable noun when you want to talk about an individual piece or item. 用於可數名詞後或不可數名詞前以談論一單片或一項","examples":["...a blade of grass. …一片草葉","Marina ate only one slice of bread. 瑪麗娜只吃了一片面包。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> to indicate the materials or things that form something. 用以表示構成某物的材料或物體","examples":["...local decorations of wood and straw. …用木頭和草做的本地飾品。","...loose-fitting garments of linen. …寬鬆的亞麻衣服。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after a noun which specifies a particular part of something, to introduce the thing that it is a part of. 用於名詞後以指明某物的某部分","examples":["...the other side of the square. …廣場的另一邊。","...the beginning of the year. …那年年初。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after some verbs to indicate someone or something else involved in the action. 用於某些動詞後以表示動作所涉及的人或事物","examples":["He'd been dreaming of her. 他一直在夢想著她。","Listen, I shall be thinking of you always. 聽著，我會一直想著你。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after some adjectives to indicate the thing that a feeling or quality relates to. 用於某些形容詞後以表示與某情感或特質所繫之物","examples":["I have grown very fond of Alec. 我已變得很喜歡亞力克。","His father was quite naturally very proud of him. 他父親很自然地為他感到自豪。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> before a word referring to the person who performed an action when saying what you think about the action. 用於指執行了某動作的人的詞前以表達對該動作的評價","examples":["This has been so nice, so terribly kind of you. 你這樣實在是太好了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something is <b>more of</b> or <b>less of</b> a particular thing, it is that thing to a greater or smaller degree. 用以表示具有某事物的特徵","examples":["Your extra fat may be more of a health risk than you realize. 多餘的脂肪可能是一種比你認識到的更嚴重的健康威脅。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> to indicate a characteristic or quality that someone or something has. 用以表示某人或某事物具有的某種特性和性質","examples":["...the worth of their music. …他們音樂的價值。","She is a woman of enviable beauty. 她這個女人美麗得讓人羨慕。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> to specify an amount, value, or age. 用以說明某數量、價值或年齡","examples":["Last Thursday, Nick announced record revenues of $3.4 billion. 上週四，尼克宣佈了34億美元的創記錄收入。","...young people under the age of 16 years. …16歲以下的年輕人。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>of</b> after a noun such as \"month\" or \"year\" to indicate the length of time that some state or activity continues. 用於(month)、(year)等名詞後以表示某狀態或活動持續的時長","examples":["...eight bruising years of war. …堅苦卓絕的8年戰爭。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You can use <b>of</b> to say what time it is by indicating how many minutes there are before the hour mentioned. 用於透過表示所提鐘點之前有多少分鐘來表達時間","examples":["At about a quarter of eight in the evening Joe Urber calls. 在晚上大約八點差一刻時喬·烏爾貝打了電話。"]}]}]},"near":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"距離不遠，在附近；不久，很快；差不多，幾乎"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在......附近，靠近；接近（某時間、某事件）；（用於數字前）接近；與......相似；近乎（一種狀態），就要"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"近，在附近；差不多的；與……相似；不久以後；隨後，接近；近親的；（車輛）近路緣一側的；<古>（人）吝嗇的，小氣的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（時間或空間上）接近，靠近"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>near</b> a place, thing, or person, it is a short distance from them. 離…近","examples":["Don't come near me. 別靠近我。","He drew his chair nearer the fire. 他把他的椅子向爐火拉近了些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Near</b> means the same as <b>near to</b>. 接近","examples":["He was near tears. 他幾乎要流淚了。","For almost a month he lay near death. 他半死不活地躺了將近一個月。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Near</b> means the same as <b>near to</b>. 與…相似","examples":["Often her feelings were nearer hatred than love. 她的感情往往更像是恨，而不是愛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>near</b> a particular time, it happens just before or just after that time. 離 (某一時間) 近","examples":["Performance is lowest between 3 a.m. and 5 a.m., and reaches a peak near midday. 工作狀態凌晨3點到5點最差，近中午時分達到最高點。","\"Since I retired to this place,\" he wrote near the end of his life, \"I have never been out of these mountains.\" “自從退休到這裡，”他在快到生命盡頭時寫到，“我從沒出過這些山。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>near</b> to say that something is a little more or less than an amount or number stated. 接近於 (某數量或數字)","examples":["...to increase manufacturing from about 2.5 million cars a year to nearer 4.75 million. …把轎車年產量從250萬輛左右提高到接近475萬輛。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say that someone will <b>not go</b> <b>near</b> a person or thing when you are emphasizing that they refuse to see them or go there. 拒絕與 (某人或某物) 接觸","examples":["He will absolutely not go near a hospital. 他絕不去醫院。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Near</b> is also an adverb. 靠近","examples":["He crouched as near to the door as he could. 他蜷縮在儘可能靠近門的地方。","She took a step nearer to the barrier. 她向路障走近了一步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a time or event draws <b>near</b>, it will happen soon. 臨近","examples":["The time for my departure from Japan was drawing nearer every day. 我離開日本的時間一天天臨近了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Near</b> is also an adverb. 差不多地","examples":["...his near fatal accident two years ago. …兩年前那場險些讓他喪命的事故。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Near</b> is also an adjective. 靠近的","examples":["He collapsed into the nearest chair. 他癱在最近的椅子上。","The nearer of the two barges was perhaps a mile away. 兩條駁船中較近的一條約有一英里遠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You describe the thing most similar to something as <b>the</b> <b>nearest</b> thing <b>to</b> it when there is no example of the thing itself. 與 (某物) 最相似的","examples":["It would appear that the legal profession is the nearest thing to a recession-proof industry. 看起來司法行業最接近於一種不怕經濟衰退的行業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>near</b> one of two things is the one that is closer. (二者中) 離得近些的","examples":["...a mighty beech tree on the near side of the little clearing. …小片林間空地近側一棵碩大的山毛櫸樹。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>near</b> to indicate that something is almost the thing mentioned. 差不多的","examples":["She was believed to have died in near poverty. 人們相信，她死時幾乎一貧如洗。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a contest, your <b>nearest</b> rival or challenger is the person or team that is most likely to defeat you. 最接近的 (對手或挑戰者)","examples":["He completed the lengthy course some three seconds faster than his nearest rival, Jonathon Ford. 他比勁敵喬納松·福特快約三秒鐘完成了漫長的賽程。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>near to</b> a particular state, they have almost reached it. 接近 (某一狀態)","examples":["After the war, the firm came near to bankruptcy. 戰後這家公司瀕臨破產。","The repairs to the Hafner machine were near to completion. 哈芙納牌機器的維修工作已接近尾聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is similar to something else, you can say that it is <b>near to</b> it. 與…相似","examples":["It combined with the resinous cedar smell of the logs to produce a sickening sensation that was near to nausea. 它與那些圓木的雪松樹脂氣味混雜在一起，以產生一種快要嘔吐的噁心感覺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>near and far</b> to indicate that you are referring to a very large area or distance. 四處","examples":["People would gather from near and far. 人們會從四面八方聚起來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>in the near future</b>, you mean that it will happen quite soon. 在不久的將來","examples":["The controversy regarding vitamin C is unlikely to be resolved in the near future. 關於維生素C的爭論近期不大可能被解決。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>nowhere near</b> and <b>not anywhere near</b> to emphasize that something is not the case. 遠不","examples":["They are nowhere near good enough. 他們遠不夠好。","It was nowhere near as painful as David had expected. 這遠遠不像大衛預料的那麼痛苦。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>near</b> a place, you get quite near to it. 接近 (地點)","examples":["As he neared the stable, he slowed the horse and patted it on the neck. 接近馬廄時，他讓馬慢下來並拍拍它的脖子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone or something <b>nears</b> a particular stage or point, they will soon reach that stage or point. 快到 (某個階段或時間)","examples":["His age was hard to guess – he must have been nearing fifty. 他的年齡很難猜出來–他肯定快50歲了。","You are nearing the end of your training and you haven't attempted any assessments yet. 你們的培訓快結束了，而你們還未嘗試做過任何評估。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that an important time or event <b>nears</b> when it is going to occur quite soon. (重要時刻或事件等) 臨近","examples":["As half time neared, Hardyman almost scored twice. 中場休息臨近時，哈迪曼幾乎兩度得分。"]}]}]},"toward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"向，朝，往；趨向，趨於；對於；接近（時間）；靠近；用於，為了（同 towards）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"即將來到的；進行中的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move, look, or point <b>toward</b> something or someone, you move, look, or point in their direction. 向","examples":["They were all moving toward him down the stairs. 他們都正朝著他走下樓梯。","When he looked toward me, I smiled and waved. 他朝我看時，我微笑著揮了揮手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If things develop <b>toward</b> a particular situation, that situation becomes nearer in time or more likely to happen. 趨向","examples":["The agreement is a major step toward peace. 這項協議是走向和平的一大步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a particular attitude <b>toward</b> something or someone, you have that attitude when you think about them or deal with them. 對","examples":["My attitude toward religion has been shaped by this man. 我對宗教的態度受到了這個男人的影響。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>toward</b> a particular time, it happens just before that time. 接近 (時間)","examples":["There was a forecast of cooler weather toward the end of the week. 天氣預報說接近週末時天氣會更涼爽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>toward</b> part of a place or thing, it is near that part. 靠近","examples":["Gulls are nesting on a small island toward the eastern shore. 海鷗正在靠近東海岸的一個小島上築巢。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you give money <b>toward</b> something, you give it to help pay for that thing. (錢) 用於","examples":["Taxes only get part of the way toward a $50 billion deficit. 稅收只會部分解決500億美元的赤字。"]}]}]},"off":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"離開（某處），（在時間或空間上）距，離；從……移開，從……脫離；不再會發生，被取消；關掉，切斷；沒有，不再供應；不上課，不工作，休息；削價，減價；入睡；做完，光；獲得，擁有；<英>（接在數詞後）一次的產量；在劇院舞臺的後面（或旁邊）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"從……離開，向下；靠近，離……不遠；從……去掉，從……移開；低於……水平；遠離；不上課，不工作，休息；依靠……（過活）；（表示來源或原因）來自，由於"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（食物）不新鮮的；<非正式>令人不快的，不公平的；<英，非正式>不友好的，敵對的；狀態不如平常好的；<美>不正確的，不對的；微小的；不連線的，不蓋在上面的；蕭條的，淡季的；離開家的，不工作的；不運轉的，不運作的；<英>（一對之中）右邊的，右側的；（某些體育比賽）越位的；在車輛離人行道邊緣最遠的一側的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"起跑，開始，出發（the off）；（板球）擊球手對面的半場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>殺死（某人）；<非正式>離開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is taken <b>off</b> something else or moves <b>off</b> it, it is no longer touching that thing. (從某物) 下來","examples":["He took his feet off the desk. 他把雙腳從書桌上移開。","I took the key for the room off a rack above her head. 我從她頭頂上方的一個架子上拿下了該房間的鑰匙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you get <b>off</b> a bus, train, or plane, you come out of it or leave it after you have been travelling on it. 下 (公車、火車、飛機等)","examples":["Don't try to get on or off a moving train! 火車執行中勿要上下！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you keep <b>off</b> a street or piece of land, you do not step on it or go there. 不在 (某街道、某地等) 上","examples":["Locking up men does nothing more than keep them off the streets. 把男人鎖起來只是不讓他們上街而已。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is situated <b>off</b> a place such as a coast, room, or road, it is near to it or next to it, but not exactly in it. 在離 (某地) 不遠處","examples":["The boat was anchored off the northern coast of the peninsula. 那隻船停泊在了離半島北海岸不遠處。","Lily lives in a penthouse just off Park Avenue. 莉莉住在離公園大街不遠的一處頂層公寓裡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Off</b> is also a preposition. 不在工作中; 不在學習中","examples":["He could not get time off work to go on holiday. 他難以從工作中抽出時間去休假。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you keep <b>off</b> a subject, you deliberately avoid talking about it. 避開 (某話題)","examples":["Keep off the subject of politics. 避開政治話題。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If there is money <b>off</b> something, its price is reduced by the amount specified. 減 (價)","examples":["20 per cent off all jackets this Saturday. 這個星期六所有上衣減價20%。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you get something <b>off</b> someone, you obtain it from them. 從 (某人那裡得到)","examples":["I don't really get a lot of information, and if I do I get it off Mark. 我真沒得到很多資訊，即便有也是從馬克那裡得到的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone is <b>off</b> something harmful such as a drug, they have stopped taking or using it. 停服 (藥物)","examples":["She felt better and the psychiatrist took her off antidepressants. 她感覺好些了，於是精神科醫師給她停用了抗抑鬱藥。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you are <b>off</b> something, you have stopped liking it. 不再喜歡 (某物)","examples":["I'm off coffee at the moment. 我暫時不再喜歡咖啡。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you live <b>off</b> a particular kind of food, you eat it in order to live. If you live <b>off</b> a particular source of money, you use it to live. 靠 (某種食物、某種資金等生存)","examples":["Her husband's memories are of living off roast chicken and drinking whisky. 她丈夫所記得的是靠吃烤雞喝威士忌過日子。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If a machine runs <b>off</b> a particular kind of fuel or power, it uses that power in order to function. (機器) 靠 (某種燃料或動力執行)","examples":["The electric armour runs off the tank's power supply. 該電動裝甲車靠這坦克的動力供應運轉。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Off</b> is also an adverb. 下","examples":["Lee broke off a small piece of orange and held it out to him. 李掰下一小瓣橘子遞給他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Off</b> is also an adverb. 下 (公車、火車、飛機等)","examples":["At the next stop the man got off too and introduced himself. 在下一站那個男人也下了，並介紹了他自己。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Off</b> is also an adverb. 不在 (某街道、某地等) 上地","examples":["...a sign saying \"Keep Off.\" …一個寫著“勿靠近”的牌子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you go <b>off</b>, you leave a place. 離開","examples":["He was just about to drive off when the secretary came running out. 他正要開車離去，這時秘書跑了出來。","She was off again, to Kenya. 她又走了，去肯亞。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you take <b>off</b> clothing or jewellery that you are wearing, you remove it from your body. (從身體上脫、摘) 下","examples":["He took off his spectacles and rubbed frantically at the lens. 他摘下眼鏡慌亂地擦鏡片。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have time <b>off</b> or a particular day <b>off,</b> you do not go to work or school, for example, because you are sick or it is a day when you do not usually work. 不在工作中地; 不在學習中地","examples":["The rest of the men had the day off. 其餘的人放假一天。","I'm off tomorrow. 我明天休息。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Off</b> is also an adverb. 減 (價)","examples":["Take $5 off the regular price of any membership. 從會員正價中減$5。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something is a long way <b>off</b>, it is a long distance away from you. 離 (某處) 遠","examples":["Florida was a long way off. 佛羅里達離得很遠。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something is a long time <b>off</b>, it will not happen for a long time. 離 (某時) 遠","examples":["An end to the crisis seems a long way off. 危機的結束似乎還要一長段時間。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something such as an agreement or a sports event is <b>off</b>, it is cancelled. (協議、運動事件等) 取消","examples":["Until Pointon is completely happy, however, the deal's off. 等到波因頓完全高興起來，那筆交易卻取消了。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When something such as a machine or electric light is <b>off</b>, it is not functioning or in use. When you switch it <b>off</b>, you stop it from functioning. (機器、電燈等) 關閉著","examples":["As he pulled into the driveway, he saw her bedroom light was off. 當他駛入車道時,他看見她臥室的燈關著。","We used sail power and turned the engine off to save our fuel. 我們關掉了發動機，用帆航行以節省燃料。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If food has gone <b>off</b>, it tastes and smells bad because it is no longer fresh enough to be eaten. (食物) 變質了的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>on and off</b>, or <b>off and on</b>, it happens occasionally, or only for part of a period of time, not in a regular or continuous way. 有時","examples":["I was still working on and off as a waitress to support myself. 我仍然有時做女招待來維持生活。"]}]}]},"in":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……內，在……裡（面），在（某地）；進……裡；在……期間；在……以後；在……之內（表示將來時間）；在……歲時；當……時；穿著，戴著，覆蓋著……；帶……顏色的；在……狀態中；在……方面，關於；用……（語言、媒介、方式），以……方式，按照（表示方式）；以……調；從事……，參加；在（活動）過程中；在（書、電影、圖片等）中；包含在……中；佔……，每……中有……，在……之中（用於較大和較小數字之間）；以……的數量；具有……特性；（引出具某種品質的人的名字）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"進入，朝裡，向中間；在裡頭，在屋裡，在家（或在工作處）；到達，到站，在車站；當選；漲潮；收到；遞交，送到；填寫；著色；擊球；（球）落在界內"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在裡面的，內部的；時髦的，流行的；（用球）界內的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"執政者；門路，關係，接近……的機會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>in</b> something else is enclosed by it or surrounded by it. If you put something <b>in</b> a container, you move it so that it is enclosed by the container. 在…裡面","examples":["He was in his car. 他在他的汽車裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>in</b> a place, it happens there. 在…地方","examples":["...spending a few days in a hotel. …在賓館住了幾天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>in</b> a window, especially a shop window, is just behind the window so that you can see it from outside. 在 (櫥窗) 裡面","examples":["There was a camera for sale in the window. 櫥窗裡有一架待售的相機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you see something <b>in</b> a mirror, the mirror shows an image of it. 在 (鏡子) 裡","examples":["I couldn't bear to see my reflection in the mirror. 我受不了看鏡子裡我的模樣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are dressed <b>in</b> a piece of clothing, you are wearing it. 穿著","examples":["He was a big man, dressed in a suit and tie. 他是個高大的男人，穿著西服、打著領帶。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that is covered or wrapped <b>in</b> something else has that thing over or around its surface. 在…表面","examples":["His legs were covered in mud. 他的雙腿沾滿了泥。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If there is something such as a crack or hole <b>in</b> something, there is a crack or hole on its surface. (裂縫、洞) 在…表面","examples":["There was a deep crack in the ceiling above him. 他頭頂上的天花板上有一個很深的裂縫。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something is <b>in</b> a book, film, play, or picture, you can read it or see it there. 在...之中","examples":["Don't stick too precisely to what it says in the book. 不要過分拘泥於書本上的內容。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you are <b>in</b> something such as a play or a race, you are one of the people taking part. 在...其中","examples":["Alfredo offered her a part in the play he was directing. 阿爾弗雷德讓她在他導演的一齣戲裡擔任一個角色。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Something that is <b>in</b> a group or collection is a member of it or part of it. 在...之中","examples":["The New England team is the worst in the league. 該新英格蘭隊是聯盟中最差勁的球隊。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to specify a general subject or field of activity. 在...方面","examples":["...those working in the defence industry. …在國防工業工作的那些人。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something happens <b>in</b> a particular year, month, or other period of time, it happens during that time. 在…時候","examples":["...that early spring day in April 1949. …1949年4月早春的那一天。","Export orders improved in the last month. 出口訂單在上個月增加了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something happens <b>in</b> a particular situation, it happens while that situation is going on. 在...情況中","examples":["His father had been badly wounded in the last war. 他父親在上次戰爭中受了重傷。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you do something <b>in</b> a particular period of time, that is how long it takes you to do it. 在...時間內","examples":["He walked two hundred and sixty miles in eight days. 他在八天裡走了二百六十英里。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something will happen <b>in</b> a particular length of time, it will happen after that length of time. 在 之後","examples":["I'll have some breakfast ready in a few minutes. 我將在幾分鐘後把早餐準備好。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to indicate roughly how old someone is. For example, if someone is <b>in</b> their fifties, they are between 50 and 59 years old. 在…歲數","examples":["...young people in their twenties. …二十幾歲的年輕人。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to indicate roughly how many people or things do something. 以…的數量","examples":["...men who came there in droves. …成群結隊到那兒的男人們。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to express a ratio, proportion, or probability. 從…之中","examples":["One in three fourth-graders couldn't find their state on a map of the U.S. 四年級學生中有三分之一在美國地圖上找不到自己所在的州。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>in</b> a particular state or situation, that is their present state or situation. 處於...中","examples":["The economy was in trouble. 經濟陷於困境。","Dave was in a hurry to get back to work. 戴夫急於回去工作。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to indicate the feeling or desire that someone has when they do something, or which causes them to do it. 處於...之中","examples":["Simpson looked at them in surprise. 辛普森驚異地看著他們。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If a particular quality or ability is <b>in</b> you, you naturally have it. 在(本性)中","examples":["Violence is not in his nature. 粗暴不在他的本性中。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> when saying that someone or something has a particular quality. 具有...的特性","examples":["He had all the qualities I was looking for in a partner. 他有我所要找的合夥人具有的所有品質。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to indicate how someone is expressing something. 以…方式","examples":["Information is given to the patient verbally and in writing. 病人以口頭和書面方式被告知資訊。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> in expressions such as <b>in a row</b> or <b>in a ball</b> to describe the arrangement or shape of something. 以...樣式","examples":["The cards need to be laid out in two rows. 這些卡片需擺放成兩排。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If something is <b>in</b> a particular colour, it has that colour. 帶有...顏色的","examples":["...white flowers edged in pink. …帶粉邊的白花。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> to specify which feature or aspect of something you are talking about. 在…方面","examples":["The film is nearly two hours in length. 這部電影長達近兩個小時。","There is a big difference in the amounts that banks charge. 各個銀行在收費數額上有很大差異。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"You use <b>in</b> with a present participle to indicate that when you do something, something else happens as a result. (與現在分詞連用)在…過程中","examples":["He shifted uncomfortably on his feet. In doing so he knocked over Steven's briefcase. 他不自在地變換著站姿。在這過程中，他碰倒了史蒂文的公文包。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are in</b>, you are present at your home or place of work. 在家; 在工作地方","examples":["My roommate was in at the time. 我的室友當時在房間裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone comes <b>in</b>, they enter a room or building. 進入","examples":["She looked up anxiously as he came in. 他進來時，她焦慮地抬頭看了一眼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a train, boat, or plane has come <b>in</b> or is <b>in</b>, it has arrived at a station, port, or airport. 到站了","examples":["...every plane coming in from Melbourne. …從墨爾本飛來的每一架飛機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When the sea or tide comes <b>in</b>, the sea moves toward the shore rather than away from it. (潮水) 在上漲","examples":["She thought of the tide rushing in, covering the wet sand. 她想到潮水漲上來，淹沒了潮溼的沙灘。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in</b>, or is the <b>in</b> thing, you mean it is fashionable or popular. 時髦的; 流行的","examples":["A few years ago jogging was the in thing. 幾年前慢跑是流行的事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is in for</b> a shock or a surprise, you mean that they are going to experience it. 就要經歷...","examples":["You might be in for a shock at the sheer hard work involved. 對所涉及的這些絕對艱難的工作，你也許會大吃一驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>has it in for</b> you, they dislike you and try to cause problems for you. 對某人懷恨在心","examples":["The other kids had it in for me. 別的孩子對我懷有仇恨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>in on</b> something, you are involved in it or know about it. 參與; 瞭解","examples":["I don't know. I wasn't in on that particular argument. 我不知道。我沒有參與那場爭論。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are in with</b> a person or group, they like you and accept you, and are likely to help you. 與…處得很好","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>in that</b> to introduce an explanation of a statement you have just made. 因為","examples":["I'm lucky in that I've got four sisters. 我很幸運，因為我有四個姐妹。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>ins and outs</b> of a situation are all the detailed points and facts about it. 詳情","examples":["...the ins and outs of high finance. …鉅額融資的來龍去脈。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"India 印度","examples":[]}]}]},"towards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"向，朝著；接近達到（目的）；接近，將近（某一時間）；接近，靠近（某地）；對，關於；（錢）用於"}],"sections":[]},"on":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……上（表示接觸、附著、由……支撐或移動到……上）；向，朝，對著；關於；在（某一天、日期或特定時間）；根據，依據，憑；帶在……身上；一……就；以……為食（或燃料、收入來源等）；吃，喝；服用（藥物）；以……支付；在……上賺（錢）；藉助（儀器、器械或方式）；在（廣播、電視）上播放；參加或處於（活動、狀態）中；忙於；作為……成員；靠近，接近，在……旁邊；在……基礎上（又）增加；與……相比"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在上面；穿上，穿著；向前；繼續，不停；進行中；開著，接通；當班；上演，播出；以後"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"開著的；發生著的，正在進行中；計劃舉行的；覆蓋；附著（尤指在正確的位置上）；寫著的；正在播出的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（On）（中、菲）溫（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on</b> a surface or object, the surface or object is immediately below them and is supporting their weight. (表示接觸、支撐) 在…上","examples":["He is sitting beside her on the sofa. 他正挨著她坐在沙發上。","On top of the cupboards are straw baskets. 櫥櫃頂上是幾個草籃子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>on</b> a surface or object, it is stuck to it or attached to it. (表示貼上、附著) 在…上","examples":["I stared at the peeling paint on the ceiling. 我盯著天花板上剝落的油漆。","The clock on the wall showed one minute to twelve. 牆上的鐘顯示11：59。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you put, throw, or drop something <b>on</b> a surface, you move it or drop it so that it is then supported by the surface. (表示方向) 到…上","examples":["He got his winter jacket from the wardrobe and dropped it on the sofa. 他從衣櫃裡拿出冬天的夾克，把它扔到沙發上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> to say what part of your body is supporting your weight. 倚在 (身體某部位) 之上","examples":["He continued to lie on his back and look at clouds. 他繼續仰面朝天躺著，看著雲彩。","He raised himself on his elbows, squinting into the sun. 他用雙肘撐起身體，眯起眼睛看著太陽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> to say that someone or something touches a part of a person's body. 與 (身體某部位) 接觸","examples":["He leaned down and kissed her lightly on the mouth. 他斜下身子，輕輕地吻了她的嘴。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone has a particular expression <b>on</b> their face, their face has that expression. (表情) 在 (臉) 上","examples":["The maid looked at him, a nervous smile on her face. 侍女看著他，臉上帶著緊張的微笑。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can say that you have something <b>on</b> you if you are carrying it in your pocket or in a purse. 帶在…身上","examples":["I didn't have any money on me. 我身上一點兒錢也沒帶。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone's eyes are <b>on</b> you, they are looking or staring at you. (視線) 在…上","examples":["Everyone's eyes were fixed on him. 大家的目光都鎖定在他身上。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you hurt yourself <b>on</b> something, you accidentally hit a part of your body against it and that thing causes damage to you. (身體某部位碰撞) 到某物上","examples":["Mr. Pendle hit his head on a wall as he fell. 彭德爾先生摔倒時，頭撞到了牆上。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> an area of land, you are there. 在 (區域) 上","examples":["He was able to spend only a few days on the island. 他只能在這個島上待幾天。","You lived on the farm until you came back to America? 回美國之前你一直住在農場？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something is situated <b>on</b> a place such as a road or coast, it forms part of it or is by the side of it. (坐落) 在…上; 在…旁","examples":["Bergdorf Goodman has opened a men's shop on Fifth Avenue. 伯格多夫·古德曼在第五大道上開了一家男裝店。","The hotel is on the coast. 那家賓館在海邊。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you get <b>on</b> a bus, train, or plane, you go into it in order to travel somewhere. If you are <b>on</b> it, you are travelling in it. 在 (交通工具) 上","examples":["We waited till twelve and we finally got on the plane. 我們一直等到12點，終於登上了飛機。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If there is something <b>on</b> a piece of paper, it has been written or printed there. (寫或印) 在…上","examples":["The writing on the back of the card was cramped but scrupulously neat. 卡片背面的字跡密密麻麻，但卻工整乾淨。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If something is <b>on</b> a list, it is included in it. 在 (名單) 上","examples":["I've seen your name on the list of deportees. 我已經在被驅逐出境人員名單上見到你的名字了。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> to introduce the method, principle, or system which is used to do something. 以…方式","examples":["...a television that we bought on credit two months ago. …我們兩個月前以賒購的方式買的一臺電視機。","They want all groups to be treated on an equal basis. 他們希望所有的族群都能以一種平等的原則受到對待。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If something is done <b>on</b> an instrument or a machine, it is done using that instrument or machine. 藉助 (儀器或機械)","examples":["...songs that I could just sit down and play on the piano. …我一坐下來就可以用鋼琴彈奏的歌曲。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If information is, for example, <b>on</b> tape or <b>on</b> computer, that is the way that it is stored. (儲存) 在…上","examples":["We've got her statement on tape. 我們已經把她的陳述錄在磁帶上了。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If something is being broadcast, you can say that it is <b>on</b> the radio or television. 透過 (廣播、電視) 播出","examples":["Every sporting event on television and satellite over the next seven days is listed. 未來7天透過電視和衛星轉播的每個體育賽事均已列出。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> to introduce an activity that someone is doing, particularly travelling. 在從事 (旅行等活動) 中","examples":["I've always wanted to go on a cruise. 我一直想去乘船旅遊。","We're going on a trip next month. 我們下個月要去旅行。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"You can indicate when something happens by saying that it happens <b>on</b> a particular day, date, or part of the week. 在 (某日)","examples":["This year's event will take place on June 19th, a week earlier than usual. 今年的比賽將在6月19日進行，比往常提前一個星期。","I was born on Christmas Day. 我出生在聖誕節。","The motorway is often lined with cars on the weekend. 這條公路在週末常排滿了汽車。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> when mentioning an event that was followed by another one. 在…之後","examples":["She waited in her hotel to welcome her children on their arrival from Vancouver. 她在旅館等著迎接將從溫哥華回來的孩子們。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"Books, discussions, or ideas <b>on</b> a particular subject are concerned with that subject. 關於","examples":["They offer free counselling on legal matters. 他們提供有關法律事務的免費諮詢。","He declined to give any information on the presidential election. 他拒絕透露有關總統選舉的任何資訊。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> a committee or council, you are a member of it. 是…的成員","examples":["Claire and Alita were on the organizing committee. 克萊爾和阿利塔都曾是組委會成員。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"Someone who is <b>on</b> a drug takes it regularly. 定期服用","examples":["She was on antibiotics for an eye infection that wouldn't go away. 她為持續不愈的眼部感染定期服用抗生素。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If you live <b>on</b> a particular kind of food, you eat it. If a machine runs <b>on</b> a particular kind of power or fuel, it uses it in order to function. 靠 (某食物為生); 用 (某動力運轉)","examples":["The caterpillars feed on a wide range of trees, shrubs and plants. 毛蟲以各種樹木、灌木叢和植物為食。","He lived on a diet of water and canned fish. 他靠水和罐頭魚為生。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> a particular income, that is the income that you have. 擁有 (某程度收入)","examples":["...young people who are unemployed or on low wages. …失業或低收入的年輕人。","He's on three hundred a week. 他每週有300元的收入。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"Taxes or profits that are obtained from something are referred to as taxes or profits <b>on</b> it. 從某事物中獲得 (稅收或利潤)","examples":["...a general strike to protest a tax on food and medicine. …一次抗議對食物和藥品徵稅的大罷工。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"When you buy something or pay for something, you spend money <b>on</b> it. 為某事物 (花錢)","examples":["I resolved not to waste money on a hotel. 我決定不因住旅館浪費錢。","He spent more on feeding the dog than he spent on feeding himself. 他養狗花的錢比養自己花的錢還多。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"When you spend time or energy <b>on</b> a particular activity, you spend time or energy doing it. 在…方面 (花時間或精力)","examples":["People complain about how children spend so much time on computer games. 人們抱怨孩子怎麼花那麼多時間玩電腦遊戲。","You all know why I am here, so I won't waste time on preliminaries. 你們都知道我為什麼來這兒，因此我就不浪費時間作介紹了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>On</b> is also an adverb. 在…上","examples":["I know how to sew a button on. 我知道怎麼縫上釦子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you put a piece of clothing <b>on</b>, you place it over part of your body in order to wear it. If you have it <b>on</b>, you are wearing it. (穿) 上; (戴) 上","examples":["He put his coat on while she opened the front door. 她開啟前門時，他穿上了他的外套。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>On</b> is also an adverb. (登) 上","examples":["He showed his ticket to the conductor and got on. 他向乘務員出示了車票，就上了車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> in expressions such as \"<b>have a lot going on</b>\" and \"<b>not have very much on</b>\" to indicate how busy someone is. 用在(have a lot going on)和(not have very much on)中，表示忙碌","examples":["I have a lot on in the next week. 下星期我會非常地忙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> to say that someone is continuing to do something. (繼續) 下去","examples":["They walked on in silence for a while. 他們默默地繼續走了一會兒。","We worked on into the night. 我們一直工作到夜裡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>on</b> in expressions such as <b>from now on</b> and <b>from then on</b> to indicate that something starts to happen at the time mentioned and continues to happen afterward. (從某時) 起","examples":["Perhaps it would be best not to see much of you from now on. 或許從現在開始最好少和你見面。","We can expect trouble from this moment on. 從此時開始，我們可能會有麻煩。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You often use <b>on</b> after the adverbs \"early,\" \"late,\" \"far,\" and their comparative forms, especially at the beginning or end of a sentence, or before a preposition. 常用在副詞(early)，(late)，(far)及其比較級後，尤置於句子開頭、結尾或介詞後","examples":["The market square is a riot of colour and animation from early on in the morning. 這個集市廣場從一大早就色彩繽紛，生機勃勃。","Later on I learned how to read music. 後來我學會了識譜。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When something such as a machine or an electric light is <b>on</b>, it is functioning or in use. When you switch it <b>on</b>, it starts functioning. (機器、電器等) 工作著","examples":["The light was on and the door was open. 燈亮著，門開著。","The heating's been turned off. I've turned it on again. 暖氣已經被關掉了，我已經又把它開啟了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>On</b> is also an adjective. 播出的","examples":["...teenagers complaining there's nothing good on. …抱怨沒什麼好節目播出的青少年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an activity is taking place, you can say that it is <b>on</b>. 正在發生的","examples":["There's an exciting match on at Wimbledon right now. 有一場精彩的比賽此刻正在溫布林頓正進行著。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>on and on</b>, you mean that it continues to happen for a very long time. 不停地","examples":["...designers, builders, fitters – the list goes on and on. …設計師，建築工，裝配工–名單長得沒完沒了。","Lobell drove on and on through the dense and blowing snow. 洛貝爾迎著濃密、紛飛的雪花不停地開車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>not on</b> or is <b>just not on</b>, you mean that it is unacceptable or impossible. 不被接受的; 不可能的","examples":[]}]}]},"to":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"朝；位於……；到某處；到某狀態；差；給；對於；比；連著；對著；等於；向……表示敬意；伴隨；為了給……；適合；按……的看法；（結算賬目時）記入"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（門等）關上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（To）（湯霍特、丹）多（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when indicating the place that someone or something visits, moves toward, or points at. (表示方向、目的地) 向","examples":["Two friends and I drove to Florida during spring break. 我和兩位朋友在春假期間開車去了佛羅里達州。","She went to the window and looked out. 她走到窗前向外望去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go <b>to</b> an event, you go where it is taking place. 去 (參加)","examples":["We went to a party at the Kurt's house. 我們去庫爾特家參加了一個聚會。","He came to dinner. 他來吃晚飯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is attached <b>to</b> something larger or fixed <b>to</b> it, the two things are joined together. 附著","examples":["There was a piece of cloth tied to the dog's collar. 有一條布系在狗項圈上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when indicating the position of something. For example, if something is <b>to</b> your left, it is nearer your left side than your right side. (表示方位) 在","examples":["Hemingway's studio is to the right. 海明威的工作室在右邊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you give something <b>to</b> someone, they receive it. 給","examples":["He picked up the knife and gave it to me. 他撿起刀並拿給我。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> to indicate who or what an action or a feeling is directed toward. (表示行為或情感針對的目標) 對於","examples":["Marcus has been really mean to me today. 馬庫斯今天確實一直對我不友好。","...troops loyal to the government. …忠於政府的軍隊。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>To</b> can show who is affected by something. 對 (表示受某事影響)","examples":["He is a witty man, and an inspiration to all of us. 他是一個風趣的男人，對我們所有的人是一種鼓舞。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say something <b>to</b> someone, you want that person to listen and understand what you are saying. 對… (說)","examples":["I will explain to them that I can't pay them. 我會向他們解釋說我無法付錢給他們。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when showing someone's reaction to something or their feelings about a situation or event. For example, if you say that something happens <b>to</b> someone's surprise you mean that they are surprised when it happens. (表示反應或情感) 致使","examples":["To his surprise, the bedroom door was locked. 使他吃驚的是，臥室的門是鎖著的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>To</b> can show whose opinion is being stated. 在…看來","examples":["It was clear to me that he respected his boss. 在我看來，顯然他尊重他的老闆。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when indicating what something or someone is becoming, or the state or situation that they are progressing toward. (表示狀態或形勢等的變化) 成為","examples":["The shouts changed to laughter. 叫喊聲變成了笑聲。","...an old ranch house that has been converted to a nature centre. …一幢破舊的牧場主住宅，已被改裝成一個大自然中心。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>To</b> can be used as a way of introducing the person or organization you are employed by. (表示僱傭關係) 為…工作","examples":["Rickman worked as a dresser to Nigel Hawthorne. 裡克曼曾做過奈傑爾•霍索恩的服裝師。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"<b>To</b> can show a span of time. (表示時間跨度) 直到","examples":["From 1977 to 1985 the United States gross national product grew 21 percent. 從1977年至1985年，美國的國民生產總值增長了21%。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> to show two extreme examples of something. (從…) 到… (用於舉例)","examples":["I read everything from fiction to history. 我從小說到歷史書什麼書都讀。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If someone goes from place <b>to</b> place or from job <b>to</b> job, they go to several places, or work in several jobs, and spend only a short time in each one. (從…) 到… (表示處所和工作的變換)","examples":["Larry and Andy had drifted from place to place, working at this and that. 拉里和安迪四處漂泊，幹了各種各樣的活。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when you are stating a time less than thirty minutes before an hour. For example, if it is \"five <b>to</b> eight,\" it is five minutes before eight o'clock. (表示時間) 差…不到","examples":["At twenty to six I was waiting by the entrance to the station. 6點差20分時，我在車站入口處等著。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when giving ratios and rates. (表示比例) 每","examples":["...engines that can run at 60 miles to the gallon. …發動機，每加侖油可行駛60英里。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> when indicating that two things happen at the same time. For example, if something is done <b>to</b> music, it is done at the same time as music is being played. 伴隨著","examples":["Romeo left the stage, to enthusiastic applause. 羅密歐在熱烈的掌聲中離開了舞臺。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> before the base form of a verb to form the to-infinitive. You use the to-infinitive after certain verbs, nouns, and adjectives, and after words such as \"how,\" \"which,\" and \"where.\" 置於動詞原形前構成不定式，該不定式結構可置於某些動詞、名詞和形容詞以及如(how)，(which)和(where)等詞之後","examples":["The management wanted to know what I was doing there. 管理層想知道我在那兒做什麼。","She told the family of her decision to resign. 她告訴她家裡人她要辭職的決定。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> before the base form of a verb to indicate the purpose or intention of an action. 用於動詞原形前表示行為的目的或意圖","examples":["...using the experience of big companies to help small businesses. …用大公司的經驗來幫助小企業。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> before the base form of a verb when you are commenting on a statement that you are making, for example, when saying that you are being honest or brief, or that you are summing up or giving an example. 用於動詞原形前表示對自己的話的評論","examples":["I'm disappointed, to be honest. 我很失望，說實在的。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> before the base form of a verb when indicating what situation follows a particular action. 用於動詞原形前，表明某個動作之後的情況","examples":["From the garden you walk down to discover a large and beautiful lake. 從花園往前走你會發現一個美麗的大湖。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone moves <b>to and fro</b>, they move repeatedly from one place to another and back again, or from side to side. 來回地","examples":["She stood up and began to pace to and fro. 她站起來開始來回地踱步。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>There's nothing to it,</b>\" \"<b>There's not much to it</b>,\" or \"<b>That's all there is to it,</b>\" you are emphasizing how simple you think something is. (表示強調) 容易得很","examples":["\"There is nothing to it,\" those I asked about it told me. “那容易得很，”我問過的那些人告訴我說。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>to</b> with \"too\" and \"enough\" in expressions like <b>too much to</b> and <b>old enough to</b>; see  and . 用於短語(too much to)和(old enough to)中；見(too) 和 (enough)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Tonga 湯加","examples":[]}]}]},"over":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向下，倒下；翻過，翻轉；越過；超過，以上；完全覆蓋；在上方；剩下，餘下；再，又；改變，掉換；結束，完；去，到（某處）；很，太；仔細地；度過一段時間"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"蓋在……上面；懸在……上面；從一邊到另一邊；翻越；在……的對面；從……落下；遍及；超過，多於；控制，支配；在……期間；渡過（難關等）；由於，關於；利用，透過；聲音大於；勝過，優於；儘管；漏掉，略過；除以"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（板球）一輪投球"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"結束的；剩下的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"越過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>over</b> another thing or is moving <b>over</b> it, the first thing is directly above the second, either resting on it, or with a space between them. 在…之上","examples":["He looked at himself in the mirror over the table. 他看著桌子上方鏡子中的自己。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing is <b>over</b> another thing, it is supported by it and its ends are hanging down on each side of it. (搭或掛) 在…上","examples":["A grey raincoat was folded over her arm. 一件灰色的雨衣被摺疊著搭在她的手臂上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is <b>over</b> another thing, it covers part or all of it. (部分或全部地覆蓋) 在…之上","examples":["Mix the ingredients and pour over the mushrooms. 把這些調料混合然後倒在蘑菇上。","He was wearing a light-grey suit over a shirt. 他在襯衣外面套了件淺灰色的西裝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you lean <b>over</b> an object, you bend your body so that the top part of it is above the object. (身體探) 在…之上","examples":["They stopped to lean over a gate. 他們停下來，將身子從一個柵欄門上面探出去。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you look <b>over</b> or talk <b>over</b> an object, you look or talk across the top of it. 越過…上方","examples":["I went and stood beside him, looking over his shoulder. 我走過去站在他身旁，從他的肩頭上方望了過去。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a window has a view <b>over</b> an area of land or water, you can see the land or water through the window. 從一邊到另一邊","examples":["...a light and airy bar with a wonderful view over the river. …一個明亮通風而且看得見優美河景的酒吧。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone or something goes <b>over</b> a barrier, obstacle, or boundary, they get to the other side of it by going across it, or across the top of it. 越過","examples":["I stepped over a broken piece of wood. 我邁過一根斷裂的木頭。","Nearly one million people crossed over the river into Moldavia. 近一百萬人渡過了這條河，進入摩爾達維亞。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone or something moves <b>over</b> an area or surface, they move across it, from one side to the other. 穿過","examples":["She ran swiftly over the lawn to the gate. 她輕快地跑過草坪，來到大門口。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something is on the opposite side of a road or river, you can say that it is <b>over</b> the road or river. 在…的另一邊","examples":["...a fashionable neighbourhood, just over the river from Manhattan. …一個時尚街區，正好與曼哈頓隔河相望。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something is <b>over</b> a particular amount, measurement, or age, it is more than that amount, measurement, or age. 超過","examples":["They say that tobacco will kill over 4 million people worldwide this year. 他們說菸草今年將在全球範圍內奪去超過400萬人的生命。","His family have accumulated property worth well over $1 million. 他家已經積累了價值遠遠超過一百萬美元的財產。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you are <b>over</b> an illness or an experience, it has finished and you have recovered from its effects. 從…中恢復","examples":["I'm glad that you're over the flu. 我很高興你的流感好了。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you have control or influence <b>over</b> someone or something, you are able to control them or influence them. 對…","examples":["He's never had any influence over her. 他對她從沒有過任何影響。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>over</b> to indicate what a disagreement or feeling relates to or is caused by. 對於","examples":["...concern over recent events in the Dominican Republic. …對於多明尼加共和國最近若干事件的關注。","Staff at some air and sea ports are beginning to protest over pay. 一些機場和海港的工作人員開始就工資進行抗議。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If something happens <b>over</b> a particular period of time or <b>over</b> something such as a meal, it happens during that time or during the meal. 在…期間","examples":["The number of attacks on the capital had gone down over the past week. 在過去一週裡對首都的襲擊次數下降了。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>over</b> to indicate that you give or receive information using a telephone, radio, or other piece of electrical equipment. 透過…","examples":["I'm not prepared to discuss this over the telephone. 我不準備透過電話來討論這件事。","The head of state addressed the nation over the radio. 國家元首透過廣播向全國人民發表了講話。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Over</b> is also an adverb. 越過","examples":["...planes flying over every 10 or 15 minutes. …每隔10或15分鐘飛越上空的飛機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Over</b> is also an adverb. (部分或全部地覆蓋) 在…之上","examples":["Heat this syrup and pour it over. 把糖漿加熱然後倒上去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Over</b> is also an adverb. (身體探) 在…之上","examples":["Sam leaned over to open the door of the car. 薩姆探出身子去開啟車門。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Over</b> is also an adverb. 越過","examples":["I climbed over into the back seat. 我爬過去坐在了後座上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you go <b>over</b> to a place, you go to that place. 到…","examples":["I got out the car and drove over to Greg's place. 我把車開出來，驅車到格雷格那兒去。","I thought you might have invited her over. 我想你大概已經邀請過她到這裡來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>over</b> to indicate a particular position or place a short distance away from someone or something. 在那邊","examples":["He noticed Rolfe standing silently over by the window. 他注意到羅尓夫默默地站在窗旁。","John reached over and took Joanna's hand. 約翰伸過手去牽起了喬安娜的手。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>over</b> to say that someone or something falls toward or onto the ground, often suddenly or violently. (突然或猛然) 倒下","examples":["If he drinks more than two glasses of wine he falls over. 他喝兩杯以上的酒就會醉倒。","She pushed past me, almost knocking me over. 她從我身邊擠過去，差點把我撞倒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something rolls <b>over</b> or is turned <b>over</b>, its position changes so that the part that was facing upward is now facing downward. 翻轉倒置","examples":["His car rolled over after a tyre was punctured. 在一個車胎被扎破之後，他的車翻了個底朝天。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Over</b> is also an adverb. 以上","examples":["...people aged 65 and over. …65歲及以上的人。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that you have some food or money <b>over</b> or left <b>over</b>, you mean that it remains after you have used all that you need. 剩餘地","examples":["The Larsons pay me well enough, but there's not much left over for luxuries. 拉森家給我的報酬不錯，但是剩不下多少錢來買奢侈品。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you do something <b>over</b>, you do it again or start doing it again from the beginning. 再一次","examples":["She said if she had the chance to do it over, she would have hired a press secretary. 她說如果她有機會再做一遍此事，她會僱一個新聞秘書。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All over</b> a place means in every part of it. 遍及各處","examples":["...doctors who work all over the country. …工作在全國各地的醫生們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Over here</b> means near you, or in the country you are in. 這裡; 在國內","examples":["Why don't you come over here tomorrow evening. 你明晚到這裡來吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Over there</b> means in a place a short distance away from you, or in another country. 那邊; 在別國","examples":["The cafe is just across the road over there. 咖啡館就在馬路對面那邊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Over and above</b> an amount, especially a normal amount, means more than that amount or in addition to it. 多於; 除…之外","examples":["Expenditure on education has gone up by seven point eight per cent over and above inflation. 教育支出增長率比通貨膨脹率高出7.8%。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something happened <b>twice over</b>, <b>three times over</b> and so on, you are stating the number of times that it happened and emphasizing that it happened more than once. 兩遍","examples":["James had to have everything spelled out twice over for him. 詹姆斯不得不讓人把每個單詞都為他拼寫兩遍。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you do something <b>over again</b>, you do it again or start doing it again from the beginning. 重新","examples":["If I could live my life over again, I would do things exactly the same way. 如果我可以重新活一次，我還會以完全一樣的方式來處事。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something is happening <b>all over again</b>, you are emphasizing that it is happening again, and you are suggesting that it is tiring, boring, or unpleasant. 又一次","examples":["The whole process started all over again. 整個過程又重新開始了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something happened <b>over and over</b> or <b>over and over again</b>, you are emphasizing that it happened many times. 反覆地","examples":["He plays the same songs over and over. 他反覆演奏同樣的幾首歌曲。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"The presenter of a radio or television programme says \"<b>over to</b> someone\" to indicate the person who will speak next. 交由 (某人) 播報","examples":["With the rest of the sports news, over to Mike Martinez. 其餘的體育新聞，由邁克·馬丁內斯播報。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an activity is <b>over</b> or <b>all</b> <b>over</b>, it is completely finished. 結束的","examples":["Warplanes that have landed there will be kept until the war is over. 已經著陸在那裡的軍用飛機將被留到戰爭結束。","I am glad it's all over. 我真高興，一切都結束了。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people such as the police or the army are using a radio to communicate, they say \"<b>Over</b>\" to indicate that they have finished speaking and are waiting for a reply. 完畢 (無線電聯絡的交接用語)","examples":[]}]}]},"under":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（或到、透過）……下面；在……表面下，由……覆蓋著；少於，小於，低於；由……控制（或管理、經營）； 按照，依據（法律、協議或制度）；在……過程中；在……的影響下；用，以（尤指假名）；屬於，列入，在……項之下；在……情況下，在……條件下；在（治療）中；（計算機）在（某個系統）下；栽有；（尤指看法不正確時）以為……"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在下面；在下面穿過；在水下；少於，小於，較年輕；在昏迷中，陷入昏迷狀態"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較低的，下面的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>under</b> something, they are at a lower level than that thing, and may be covered or hidden by it. 在…下面","examples":["They found a labyrinth of tunnels under the ground. 他們發現了地下一處迷宮似的地道。","...swimming in the pool or lying under an umbrella. …在池裡游泳或躺在遮陽傘下。","A path runs under the trees. 一條小路在樹下延伸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a place such as an ocean, river, or swimming pool, if someone or something is <b>under</b> the water, they are fully in the water and covered by it. 在 (水) 下","examples":["She held her breath for three minutes under the water. 她在水下屏息了3分鐘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you go <b>under</b> something, you move from one side to the other of something that is at a higher level than you. 從 (較高物) 下面","examples":["He went under a brick arch. 他從一座磚拱門下面走過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>under</b> a layer of something, especially clothing, is covered by that layer. 在 (一層衣服等) 裡面","examples":["I was wearing two sweaters under the green army jacket. 我那時在綠色的軍上衣裡面穿著兩件毛衣。","...a faded striped shirt under a knitted sweater. …穿在一件針織毛衣裡邊的一件褪了色的條紋襯衫。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>under</b> before a noun to indicate that a person or thing is being affected by something or is going through a particular process. 在 (…的影響或過程) 中","examples":["...fishermen whose livelihoods are under threat. …生計受到威脅的漁民們。","Firemen said they had the blaze under control. 消防員們說他們已控制住了火勢。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something happens <b>under</b> particular circumstances or conditions, it happens when those circumstances or conditions exist. 在 (…情況或條件) 下","examples":["His best friend died under questionable circumstances. 他最好的朋友在不明的情況下死了。","Under normal conditions, only about 20 to 40 percent of vitamin E is absorbed. 在正常情況下，只有約百分之二十到百分之四十的維生素E被吸收。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something happens <b>under</b> a law, agreement, or system, it happens because that law, agreement, or system says that it should happen. 在 (法律、協議、制度等的規定) 下","examples":["Under law, your employer has the right to hire a temporary worker to replace you. 按法律規定，你的僱主有權聘用臨時工來代替你。","Under the new regulations, one in five cars may need repairs costing as much as $120. 在新的規定下，1/5的車可能需要費用高達$120的維修。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something happens <b>under</b> a particular person or government, it happens when that person or government is in power. 在 (…的領導或統治) 下","examples":["There would be no new taxes under his leadership. 在他的領導下不會有新的稅項。","...the realities of life under a brutal dictatorship. …在殘酷的獨裁統治下的生活現實。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you study or work <b>under</b> a particular person, that person teaches you or tells you what to do. 在 (…的指導或帶領) 下","examples":["Kiefer was just one of the artists who had studied under Beuys in the early Sixties. 基弗只是60年代初期在博伊斯指導下學藝的藝術家之一。","General Lewis Hyde had served under General Mitchell. 劉易斯·海德將軍曾在米切爾將軍麾下服役。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you do something <b>under</b> a particular name, you use that name instead of your real name. 以 (…名)","examples":["Were any of your books published under the name Amanda Fairchild? 你的書有以阿曼達·費爾柴爾德的名字出版的嗎？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>under</b> to say which section of a list, book, or system something is in. 在 (…部分) 下","examples":["The \"General Diseases of the Eye\" study is filed under E. “普通眼病”研究歸在E下。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>under</b> a particular age or amount, they are less than that age or amount. 在 (某年齡或數量) 以下","examples":["...jobs for those under 65. …適合65歲以下人士的工作。","Nearly half of mothers with children under five have a job. 孩子不足5歲的母親中近一半有工作。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Under</b> is also an adverb. 在水下","examples":["He took a deep breath before he went under. 他在鑽下水前深深地吸了口氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Under</b> is also an adverb. 在 (某年齡或數量) 以下","examples":["...free or subsidized health insurance for children 13 and under. …13歲及13歲以下兒童的免費的或給予補助的健康保險。"]}]}]},"with":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"和……在一起，與……一同；用，以；具有；帶著，攜帶；穿著；患（病）；關於，對於，在……方面；反對（與……爭鬥、爭論或競爭時）；支援，擁護；由於，因為；受……影響；隨著，隨；順著，沿著；包括，包含；雖然，儘管；受僱於，在……工作；由……負責；交給……處理；（與 part、dispense 等連用）表示與某物分離、去除或放棄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person is <b>with</b> another, they are together in one place. 和…一起 (指在同一個地點)","examples":["With her were her son and daughter-in-law. 和她在一起的是她兒子和兒媳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is put <b>with</b> or is <b>with</b> something else, they are used at the same time. 和…同時用","examples":["Serve hot, with pasta or rice and French beans. 趁熱端上，與義大利麵或米飯和四季豆一起享用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> someone else, you both do it together or are both involved in it. 與…一起 (做或參與某事)","examples":["Parents will be given reports on their child's progress and the right to discuss it with a teacher. 家長將收到關於他們孩子進步的報告，並有權就此與老師一起進行探討。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you fight, argue, or compete <b>with</b> someone, you oppose them. 和 (某人爭鬥、爭論或競爭)","examples":["About a thousand students fought with riot police in the capital. 約一千名學生在首都和防暴警察發生衝突。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> a particular tool, object, or substance, you do it using that tool, object, or substance. 用 (某種工具、物品或材料)","examples":["Remove the meat with a fork and divide it among four plates. 用叉把肉移開，分到4個盤裡。","Pack the fruits and nuts into the jars and cover with brandy. 把水果和堅果裝進罐子，用白蘭地浸沒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone stands or goes somewhere <b>with</b> something, they are carrying it. 帶著","examples":["A young woman came in with a cup of coffee. 一個年輕女子端著一杯咖啡走了進來。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone or something <b>with</b> a particular feature or possession has that feature or possession. 具有 (某種特徵)","examples":["He was in his early forties, tall and blond with bright blue eyes. 他四十出頭，高個，長著一頭金髮和一雙明亮的藍眼睛。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Someone <b>with</b> an illness has that illness. 患 (病)","examples":["I spent a week in bed with flu. 我患了流感臥床一個星期。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something is filled or covered <b>with</b> a substance or <b>with</b> things, it has that substance or those things in it or on it. 用… (充滿或覆蓋)","examples":["His legs were caked with dried mud. 他的雙腿結著幹泥巴。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you are, for example, pleased or annoyed <b>with</b> someone or something, you have that feeling toward them. 對 (某人或某事有某種感情)","examples":["He was still a little angry with her. 他還是對她有點生氣。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> to indicate what a state, quality, or action relates to, involves, or affects. 在…方面","examples":["Our aim is to allow student teachers to become familiar with the classroom. 我們的目的是讓實習老師熟悉課堂。","He still has a serious problem with money. 他在金錢方面還存在著嚴重問題。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> when indicating the way that something is done or the feeling that a person has when they do something. 用 (某種方式); 帶 (某種感情)","examples":["...teaching her to read music with skill and sensitivity. …教她熟練而敏銳地識樂譜。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> when indicating a sound or gesture that is made when something is done, or an expression that a person has on their face when they do something. 伴著 (聲音或手勢); 帶著 (表情)","examples":["With a sigh, she leant back and closed her eyes. 伴著一聲嘆息，她往後一靠，閉上了眼睛。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> to indicate the feeling that makes someone have a particular appearance or type of behaviour. 由於 (某種感情而使某人有某種表現或行為)","examples":["Gil was white and trembling with anger. 吉爾由於生氣，臉色煞白，渾身發抖。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> when mentioning the position or appearance of a person or thing at the time that they do something, or what someone else is doing at that time. 在…同時","examples":["Joanne stood with her hands on the sink, staring out the window. 喬安妮站著，同時雙手放在水槽上，眼睛盯著窗外。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> to introduce a current situation that is a factor affecting another situation. 在…情況下","examples":["With all the night school courses available, there is no excuse for not getting some sort of training. 在夜校有那麼多課程可供選擇的條件下，就沒有理由不去接受一些培訓。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>with</b> when making a comparison or contrast between the situations of different people or things. 與 (表示比較或對比)","examples":["We're not like them. It's different with us. 我們不像他們。這對我們來說是不同的。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If something increases or decreases <b>with</b> a particular factor, it changes as that factor changes. 隨著","examples":["The risk of developing heart disease increases with the number of cigarettes smoked. 患心臟病的風險隨著吸菸數量的增多而加大。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If something moves <b>with</b> a wind or current, it moves in the same direction as the wind or current. 與 (風或水流) 同向","examples":["...a piece of driftwood carried down with the current. …順流而下的一塊浮木。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If someone says that they are <b>with</b> you, they mean that they understand what you are saying. 理解","examples":["Yes, I know who you mean. Yes, now I'm with you. 是的，我知道你指的是誰。是的，我現在理解你的意思了。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If someone says that they are <b>with</b> you, they mean that they support or approve of what you are doing. 支援","examples":["\"I'm with you all the way.\"—\"Thank you.\" “我一直都支援你。” —“謝謝你。”"]}]}]},"because":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（說明原因）因為，由於；（作出解釋）因為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>because</b> when stating the reason for something. 因為 (用以陳述理由)","examples":["He is called Mitch, because his name is Mitchell. 他被叫做米奇，因為他的名字是米切爾。","Because it is an area of outstanding natural beauty, the number of boats available for hire on the river is limited. 這是一個自然風景極美的地方，所以河上可供租用的船隻數量有限。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>because</b> when stating the explanation for a statement you have just made. 因為 (用以陳述解釋)","examples":["Maybe they just didn't want to ask too many questions, because they rented us a room without even asking to see our papers. 也許他們只是不想問太多的問題，因為他們甚至沒要求檢視我們的證件就把房間租給了我們。","The president has played a shrewd diplomatic game because from the outset he called for direct talks. 總統玩了一場精明的外交遊戲，因為從一開始他就要求進行直接對話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event or situation occurs <b>because of</b> something, that thing is the reason or cause. 由於","examples":["Many families break up because of a lack of money. 許多家庭因缺錢而破裂。"]}]}]},"after":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……之後；緊接著；一次接著一次，持續不斷地；跟隨，在……身後；（按順序、重要性）在……後面，僅次於；與……對照，對比；鑑於，由於；儘管；尋找，追捕；關於；模仿，依照；以……命名；（表示時間）（…點）過（…分）"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"在……以後"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"後來，以後"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<舊>後來的，以後的；靠近船尾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>after</b> a particular date or event, it happens during the period of time that follows that date or event. 在 (某日、某事件) 以後","examples":["After May 19, strikes were occurring on a daily basis. 在5月19日以後，罷工每天都在發生。","After breakfast Amy took a taxi to the station. 早飯以後，埃米乘計程車去了車站。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>after</b> doing another, you do it during the period of time that follows the other thing. 在 (做某事) 以後","examples":["After completing and signing it, please return the form to us in the envelope provided. 填完並且簽名以後，請將表格裝入所提供的信封中返還給我們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>after</b> when you are talking about time. For example, if something is going to happen during <b>the day after</b> or <b>the weekend after</b> a particular time, it is going to happen during the following day or during the following weekend. 在 (某日、某周) 以後","examples":["She's leaving the day after tomorrow. 她定於後天離開。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you go <b>after</b> someone, you follow or chase them. (追隨) 在 (某人) 之後","examples":["Alice said to Gina, \"Why don't you go after him, he's your son.\" 艾麗斯對吉娜說：“你為什麼不追他，他是你兒子。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>after</b> something, you are trying to get it. 以…為目標","examples":["They were after the money. 他們想得到這筆錢。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you call, shout, or stare <b>after</b> someone, you call, shout, or stare at them as they move away from you. 在 (某人) 身後 (喊、叫、瞪眼等)","examples":["\"Come back!\" he called after me. “回來！”他在我身後衝我喊。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you tell someone that one place is a particular distance <b>after</b> another, you mean that it is situated beyond the other place and further away from you. 在 (某地) 以外 (某距離處)","examples":["...a station 134 miles after the train starts its journey. …在火車出發後的134英里以外的一個車站。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If one thing is written <b>after</b> another thing on a page, it is written following it or underneath it. (寫) 在 (某物) 之後","examples":["I wrote my name after Penny's at the bottom of the page. 我把我的名字寫在了這頁最下面彭尼的名字之後。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>after</b> in order to give the most important aspect of something when comparing it with another aspect. (重要性) 在…之後","examples":["After Germany, America is Britain's second-biggest customer. 僅次於德國，美國是英國的第二大客戶。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"To be named <b>after</b> someone means to be given the same name as them. 以 (同樣的名字命名)","examples":["He persuaded Virginia to name the baby after him. 他勸弗吉妮亞給孩子命以他的名字。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>After</b> is used when telling the time. If it is, for example, <b>ten after six</b>, the time is ten minutes past six. (…點) 過 (…分)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>After</b> is also a conjunction. (某事) 以後","examples":["After Don told me this, he spoke of his mother. 唐告訴我這件事以後，他談到了他的母親。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>After</b> is also an adverb. (某日、某周) 以後地","examples":["Tomorrow. Or the day after. 明天。或者後天。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>after you</b>\" to someone, you are being polite and allowing them to go in front of you or through a doorway before you do. 您先走","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something to several things <b>one after the other</b> or <b>one after another</b>, you do it to one, then the next, and so on, with no break between your actions. 一個接一個地","examples":["...a lawyer who wins three cases, one after another. …一位連贏３個案子的律師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>day after day</b> or <b>year after year</b>, it happens every day or every year, for a long time. 日復一日地/年復一年地","examples":["...people who'd been coming here year after year. …年復一年地來這裡的人們。"]}]}]},"and":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（用於並列連線）和，與，及；（表示結果）於是，就；（表示先後）然後，接著；（表示轉折）但是，然而；（用於句首引出補充）而且，此外；（連線同一詞）表示程度加深或持續，如 more and more（越來越）；（用於數字）加，又（英式英語亦連線百位與後接數字）；（非正式，用於 go/come/try 後接另一動詞）去，來，試著"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"邏輯與（AND）；（And）人名（土耳其、瑞典，常譯作安德）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to link two or more words, groups, or clauses. 和; 並且","examples":["When he returned, she and Simon had already gone. 當他回來時，她和西蒙已經走了。","I'm going to write good jokes and become a good comedian. 我要創作出好的笑話並且成為一個優秀的喜劇演員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to link two words or phrases that are the same in order to emphasize the degree of something, or to suggest that something continues or increases over a period of time. 用於強調程度，或者表示某事持續或增長了一段時間","examples":["Learning becomes more and more difficult as we get older. 當我們年紀越大，學習就變得越來越困難。","We talked for hours and hours. 我們談了好多個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to link two statements about events when one of the events follows the other. 然後","examples":["I waved goodbye and went down the stone harbour steps. 我揮手告別，然後走下了港口的石頭臺階。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to link two statements when the second statement continues the point that has been made in the first statement. (表示延續上個陳述的意思) 而","examples":["You could only really tell the effects of the disease in the long term, and five years wasn't long enough. 這種疾病的影響只有在長期內才能真正看清楚，而5年是不夠長的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to link two clauses when the second clause is a result of the first clause. 結果","examples":["All through yesterday crowds have been arriving and by midnight thousands of people packed the square. 昨天一整天人們一直不斷地到達，結果到午夜的時候成千上萬的人擠滿了這個廣場。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to interrupt yourself in order to make a comment on what you are saying. (表示對自己的話加以評價) 而且","examples":["Danielle was among the last to find out, and as often happens, too, she learned of it only by chance. 丹妮爾是最後一個才知道的人之一，而且同往常一樣，她也只是偶然聽到的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> at the beginning of a sentence to introduce something else that you want to add to what you have just said. Some people think that starting a sentence with <b>and</b> is ungrammatical, but it is now quite common in both spoken and written English. 此外","examples":["Commuter airlines fly to out-of-the-way places. And business travellers are the ones who go to those locations. 通勤航空公司飛往偏僻的地方。此外，商務旅客就是去那些地方的人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to introduce a question that follows logically from what someone has just said. 那麼","examples":["\"He used to be so handsome.\"—\"And now?\" “他過去曾經那麼英俊。”—“那麼現在呢？”"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>And</b> is used by broadcasters and people making announcements to change a topic or to start talking about a topic they have just mentioned. 接下來","examples":["And now the drought in Sudan. 現在接下來是關於蘇丹的乾旱。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> to indicate that two numbers are to be added together. 加","examples":["What does two and two make? 2加2是多少？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>And</b> is used before a fraction that comes after a whole number. 用於連線整數後的分數","examples":["McCain spent five and a half years in a prisoner-of-war camp in Vietnam. 麥凱恩在越南的一所戰俘營裡度過了五年半。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>and</b> in numbers larger than one hundred, after the words \"hundred\" or \"thousand\" and before other numbers. 用於大於100的數字，在百位或千位數和緊跟的數之間","examples":["We printed two hundred and fifty invitations. 我們印了250份請柬。"]}]}]},"either":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"或者，要麼；兩者都（不），既（不）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（兩者之中）任意一個；兩者都（不）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"也（不），亦（不）；而且，還"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"（兩者中的）每個，各方"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（兩者中的）每個的，各方的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>either</b> in front of the first of two or more alternatives, when you are stating the only possibilities or choices that there are. The other alternatives are introduced by \"or.\" 與(or)連用，表示幾個可選項中只能選其一","examples":["Sightseeing is best done either by tour bus or by bicycles. 觀光最好要麼乘遊覽巴士，要麼騎腳踏車。","The former president was demanding that he should be either put on trial or set free. 前總統一直要求要麼對他進行審判，要麼就無罪釋放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>either</b> in a negative statement in front of the first of two alternatives to indicate that the negative statement refers to both the alternatives. 用於否定句中，表示“兩者都不”","examples":["There had been no indication of either breathlessness or any loss of mental faculties right until his death. 直到去世，他既沒有出現呼吸困難也沒有腦功能喪失的跡象。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>either</b> to refer to one of two things, people, or situations, when you want to say that they are both possible and it does not matter which one is chosen or considered. 用於表示“兩者中的任一個”","examples":["There were glasses of iced champagne and cigars. Unfortunately not many of either were consumed. 有很多杯冰鎮香檳和雪茄。可惜兩樣東西中哪一樣都沒被受用多少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>either</b> in a negative statement to refer to each of two things, people, or situations to indicate that the negative statement includes both of them. 用於否定句中，表示“兩者中任何一個都不”","examples":["She warned me that I'd never marry or have children.—\"I don't want either.\" 她警告我說我永遠不會結婚、生孩子。—“我哪一樣都不想要。”"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Either</b> is also a quantifier. 用於表示“兩者中任一…”","examples":["Do either of you smoke or drink heavily? 你們倆當中有誰抽菸、喝酒兇嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Either</b> is also a quantifier. 用於否定句，表示“兩者中任何一個…都不”","examples":["There are no simple answers to either of those questions. 對那兩個問題哪一個都沒有簡單的答案。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Either</b> is also a determiner. 用於表示“兩者中任一…”","examples":["...a special Indian drug police that would have the authority to pursue suspects into either country. …有權到這兩國中任意一國追捕嫌犯的一位印度緝毒特警。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Either</b> is also a determiner. 用於否定句，表示“兩者中任一…都不”","examples":["He sometimes couldn't remember either man's name. 他有時候這兩個男人誰的名字都記不起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>either</b> to introduce a noun that refers to each of two things when you are talking about both of them. 用於引出名詞，表示“兩者中每一個”","examples":["The basketball nets hung down from the ceiling at either end of the gymnasium. 籃球網垂懸於體育館天花板的兩頭。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>either</b> by itself in negative statements to indicate that there is a similarity or connection with a person or thing that you have just mentioned. 用於否定句，表示“也不”，與剛提過的人或事物類似或有關聯","examples":["He did not even say anything to her, and she did not speak to him either. 他甚至什麼都沒跟她說，而她也沒跟他說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When one negative statement follows another, you can use <b>either</b> at the end of the second one to indicate that you are adding an extra piece of information, and to emphasize that both are equally important. 用於否定句中提供附加資訊，表示“也不”","examples":["Don't agree, but don't argue either. 不要贊同，但是也不要爭辯。"]}]}]},"before":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（時間上）在……之前，早於；在（某個鐘點）之前；（次序）在……之前；當面，在……面前；由……考慮中；面對（法院，法庭或其他官方機構）並受審；比……更重要；（位置）在……前面；（未來將發生的事）等待著，面臨著；（寧可……而）不願……；在……影響下，在……威懾下"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"在……以前；到……為止；以免，不然；（先）……才……；（寧可……而）不願"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以前，過去；在（某時間或某事）以前；在前面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>before</b> a particular date, time, or event, it happens earlier than that date, time, or event. 在 (某日、某時、某事件) 以前","examples":["Annie was born a few weeks before Christmas. 安妮在聖誕節前幾個禮拜出生。","Before World War II, women were not recruited as intelligence officers. 二戰前，女性不被徵募為情報官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>before</b> doing something else, you do it earlier than the other thing. 在 (做某事) 之前","examples":["He spent his early life in Sri Lanka before moving to Canada. 移居加拿大前，他早年生活在斯里蘭卡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Before</b> is also a preposition. (某時、某事) 以前","examples":["It's interesting that he sent me the book twenty days before the deadline for my book. 有趣的是，在距離我書的截止日期20天前他把那本書寄給了我。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>before</b> something, they are in front of it. 在 (某物) 前面","examples":["They drove through a tall iron gate and stopped before a large white villa. 他們開車穿過一扇高高的鐵門，然後停在了一幢白色大別墅前。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you tell someone that one place is a certain distance <b>before</b> another, you mean that they will come to the first place first. 在 (某地) 前方 (某距離處)","examples":["The station is on the right, one mile before downtown Romney. 車站在右側，羅姆尼市中心前方一英里處。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you appear or come <b>before</b> an official person or group, you go there and answer questions. 在 (人或組織) 面前 (回答提問)","examples":["The governor will appear before the committee next Tuesday. 這名行政官員將於下週二面對該委員會回答提問。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something happens <b>before</b> a particular person or group, it is seen by or happens while this person or this group is present. (發生) 在 (某人、某組織) 面前","examples":["The game followed a colourful opening ceremony before a crowd of seventy-four thousand. 緊隨一場精彩的開幕式，該比賽在7.4萬名觀眾面前拉開了帷幕。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you have something such as a trip, a task, or a stage of your life <b>before</b> you, you must do it or live through it in the future. (必須經歷的事情) 在 (某人) 面前","examples":["Everyone in the room knew it was the single hardest task before them. 屋子裡每個人都知道這是擺在他們面前的一項最艱鉅的任務。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When you want to say that one person or thing is more important than another, you can say that they come <b>before</b> the other person or thing. (重要性) 以…為先","examples":["Her husband and her children came before her needs. 她的丈夫和孩子們比她的需要更重要。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Before</b> is also a conjunction. 在 (某日、某時、某事件) 以前","examples":["Stock prices have climbed close to the peak they'd registered before the stock market crashed in 1987. 股票價格已經快爬升到了1987年股市崩潰前的最高紀錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Before</b> is also a conjunction. 在 (做某事) 之前","examples":["He took a cold shower and then towelled off before he put on fresh clothes. 他穿上乾淨衣服之前，衝了個冷水澡，再擦乾身子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Before</b> is also a conjunction. (某時、某事) 以前","examples":["Kelman had a book published in the U.S. more than a decade before a British publisher would touch him. 科爾曼在美國已經出版了一本書，十多年後英國的出版商才願意出版他的作品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>before</b> someone else can do something, you do it when they have not yet done it. 在 (某人能做某事) 之前","examples":["Before Gallacher could catch up with the ball, Nadlovu had beaten him to it. 在加拉赫能接住球之前，納德洛夫就已經比他先接到了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If there is a period of time or if several things are done <b>before</b> something happens, it takes that amount of time or effort for this thing to happen. 經過 (一段時間或努力) 才","examples":["It was some time before the door opened in response to his ring. 他按過門鈴後好一會兒門才開啟。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a particular situation has to happen <b>before</b> something else happens, this situation must happen or exist in order for the other thing to happen. 在 (某事發生) 之前 (另一情況必須發生)","examples":["There was additional work to be done before all the troops would be ready. 在全軍準備就緒之前還有些事情要做。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>before</b> when you are talking about time. For example, if something happened the day <b>before</b> a particular date or event, it happened during the previous day. (某時、某事) 以前","examples":["The war had ended only a month or so before. 戰爭大約在一個月前才結束。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has done something <b>before</b>, they have done it on a previous occasion. If someone has not done something <b>before</b>, they have never done it. 以前 (做過某事)","examples":["I've been here before. 我以前來過這兒。","I had met Professor Lown before. 我以前見過勞恩教授。"]}]}]},"but":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"而，相反；（用於表示歉意）但是；可是（用來提出異議）；除了；（與重複詞連用，表示強調）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除了，除……外"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"僅僅，只是"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"藉口，託詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>but</b> to introduce something that contrasts with what you have just said, or to introduce something that adds to what you have just said. 但是","examples":["\"You said you'd stay till tomorrow.\"—\"I know, Bel, but I think I would rather go back.\" “你說過要待到明天。” — “我知道，貝爾，但我想我還是要回去。”","Place the saucepan over moderate heat until the cider is very hot but not boiling. 將燉鍋置於中火上，直到把蘋果酒煮熱，但不要煮沸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>but</b> when you are about to add something further in a discussion or to change the subject. 但是","examples":["After three weeks, they gradually reduced their sleep to about eight hours. But another interesting thing happened. 3周後，他們把睡眠時間逐漸縮短到8小時。但是另一件有趣的事發生了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>but</b> after you have made an excuse or apologized for what you are just about to say. (表示歉意) 不過","examples":["Please excuse me, but there is something I must say. 請原諒，不過有件事我必須說一下。","I'm sorry, but it's nothing to do with you. 對不起，不過這和你無關。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>but</b> to introduce a reply to someone when you want to indicate surprise, disbelief, refusal, or protest. 可是","examples":["\"I don't think I should stay in this house.\"—\"But why?\" “我想我不應該再呆在這棟房子裡了” — “可這是為什麼？”"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>But</b> is used to mean \"except.\" 除了","examples":["Europe will be represented in all but two of the seven races. 7場比賽中除了2場之外, 都將有歐洲的代表參加。","He didn't speak anything but Greek. 他除了希臘語之外不會說其他任何語言。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>But</b> is used to mean \"only.\" 僅僅","examples":["Zach insists that he is but one among many who are fighting for equality. 扎克堅持認為他僅僅是許多為平等而戰的人們中的一個。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>but for</b> to introduce the only factor that causes a particular thing not to happen or not to be completely true. 要不是","examples":["...the small square below, empty but for a dirty white van and a clump of palm trees. …下面那個小小的、要不是有一輛骯髒的白色貨車和一叢棕櫚樹將空無一物的廣場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>but then</b> or <b>but then again</b> before a remark which slightly contradicts what you have just said. 不過話說回來","examples":["My husband spends hours in the bathroom, but then again so do I. 我丈夫總在浴室泡數小時，不過話說回來，我也一樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>but then</b> before a remark which suggests that what you have just said should not be regarded as surprising. 不過","examples":["He was a fine young man, but then so had his father been. 他是個不錯的年輕人，不過他父親也曾是這樣。"]}]}]},"nor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"也不（通常與 neither 連用）； （用於肯定動詞前，表示同意剛提及的否定命題）也不"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"也不（通常與 neither 連用）；（用於肯定動詞前，表示同意剛提及的否定命題）也不"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電子）“或非”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>nor</b> after \"neither\" in order to introduce the second alternative or the last of a number of alternatives in a negative statement. (用於)(neither)(後，以引出被否定的第二項或幾項中的最後一項) 也不","examples":["Neither Mr. Rose nor Mr. Woodhead was available for comment yesterday. 羅斯先生和伍德黑德先生昨天都沒有時間做出評論。","I can give you neither an opinion nor any advice. 我既不能給你一個意見，也不能給你任何建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>nor</b> after a negative statement in order to introduce another negative statement which adds information to the previous one. (用於否定句後，引出另一否定句以補充前句) 也不","examples":["Cooking up a quick dish doesn't mean you have to sacrifice flavour. Nor does fast food have to be junk food. 做一道快餐並不意味著你就得犧牲味道。快餐也不見得非得是垃圾食品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>nor</b> after a negative statement in order to indicate that the negative statement also applies to you or to someone or something else. (用於否定句後，以表示此否定也適用於自己、他人或別的事情) 也不","examples":["\"None of us has any idea how long we're going to be here.\"—\"Nor do I.\" “我們當中沒人知道我們將要在這兒呆多久。”—“我也不知道。”","\"If my husband has no future,\" she said, \"then nor do my children.\" “要是我丈夫沒有前途，”她說道，“那麼我的孩子們也沒有。”"]}]}]},"as":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"作為；以……身份；當作；像，如同；當……時"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（程度或數量上）同樣，一樣；例如，諸如"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"像……一樣；（說明某事應完成的時間或發生的頻率）；照……方式，和……一樣；正如，如同；當……時候，在……時候；雖然，儘管；因為，由於；（關係）就像，相當於；以至於（與so或such連用表結果）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>as</b> something else happens, it happens at the same time. 在 (某事發生的) 同時","examples":["Another policeman has been injured as fighting continued this morning. 又一名警察在今天上午打鬥繼續過程中受了傷。","All the jury's eyes were on him as he continued. 所有陪審員的目光在他繼續下去時都集中在了他身上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>as</b> to say how something happens or is done, or to indicate that something happens or is done in the same way as something else. 像 (做某事、某事發生) 一樣","examples":["I'll behave toward them as I would like to be treated. 我希望別人怎樣對待我，我就會怎樣對待他們。","Today, as usual, he was wearing a three-piece suit. 今天他像往常一樣穿著一套三件套西裝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>as</b> to introduce short clauses that comment on the truth of what you are saying. 如… (用於引導評註性短從句)","examples":["As you can see, we're still working. 如你看到的，我們仍在工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>as</b> to mean \"because\" when you are explaining the reason for something. 由於","examples":["Enjoy the first hour of the day. This is important as it sets the mood for the rest of the day. 享受一天中的第一個小時。這很重要，因為這第一個小時決定當天其餘時間的情緒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the structure <b>as...as</b> when you are comparing things. 像…一樣","examples":["I never went through a final exam that was as difficult as that one. 我從未經歷過像那次一樣難的期末考試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>As</b> is also a conjunction. 像 …一樣","examples":["Being a mother isn't as bad as I thought at first! 做一位母親並不像我當初想的那樣糟！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>as...as</b> to emphasize amounts of something. (數量)多達","examples":["She gets as many as eight thousand letters a month. 她每月收到多達8千封信。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>as it were</b> in order to make what you are saying sound less definite. 好像是","examples":["I'd understood the words, but I didn't, as it were, understand the question. 我已經理解了這些詞，但我似乎還不理解這個問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>as it is</b>, <b>as it turns out</b>, and <b>as things stand</b> when you are making a contrast between a possible situation and what actually happened or is the case. 事實是; 結果是; 情況是","examples":["I want to work at home on a Tuesday but as it turns out sometimes it's a Wednesday or a Thursday. 我想在星期二在家裡工作，但結果是有時是在星期三或星期四。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>as for</b> and <b>as to</b> at the beginning of a sentence in order to introduce a slightly different subject that is still connected to the previous one. 至於","examples":["I don't know why the guy yelled at me. And as for going back there, certainly I would never go back, for fear of receiving further abuse. 我不知道為什麼這個傢伙衝我吼叫。至於回到那兒去，我肯定永遠也不會回去了，生怕遭到更多的虐待。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>as to</b> to indicate what something refers to. 就…","examples":["They should make decisions as to whether the student needs more help. 他們應該就該學生是否需要更多幫助作決定。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>as of</b> a particular date or time, you mean that it will happen from that time on. 從 (某日、某時) 起","examples":["The border, effectively closed since 1981, will be opened as of January the 1st. 自1981年以來實際上關閉了的邊境將從1月1日起開放。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>as if</b> and <b>as though</b> when you are giving a possible explanation for something or saying that something appears to be the case when it is not. 好像","examples":["Anne shrugged, as if she didn't know. 安妮聳了聳肩，好像她不知道。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as</b> when you are indicating what someone or something is or is thought to be, or what function they have. 作為","examples":["He has worked as a diplomat in the U.S., Sudan and Saudi Arabia. 他曾做過駐美國、蘇丹和沙烏地阿拉伯的外交官。","The news apparently came as a complete surprise. 這訊息顯然是個徹頭徹尾的意外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>as</b> a child or <b>as</b> a teenager, for example, you do it when you are a child or a teenager. 還是 (小孩) 時","examples":["She loved singing as a child and started vocal training at 12. 她還是個小孩的時候就愛唱歌，12歲就開始了聲樂訓練。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>as</b> in expressions like <b>as a result</b> and <b>as a consequence</b> to indicate how two situations or events are related to each other. 作為 (結果等)","examples":["As a result of the growing fears about home security, more people are arranging for someone to stay in their home when they're away. 由於日益增長的對家庭安全的擔心，更多人在外出時會安排個人呆在他們家裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an ancient Roman unit of weight approximately equal to 1 pound troy (373 grams) 阿斯; 古羅馬重量單位，等於373克","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"American Samoa 美屬薩摩亞","examples":[]}]}]},"if":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"如果，假如，要是；每當，無論何時；即使，雖然，儘管；（用於間接問句或禮貌問詢）是否；〔if only〕要是…多好；〔as if〕好像，彷彿；〔if not〕如果不；即便不；或許不；（常與 can、could、may、might 等情態動詞連用）表示婉轉請求；（if it isn't…）這不是……嗎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"條件，設想；不確定的情況（常用複數 ifs）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>if</b> in conditional sentences to introduce the circumstances in which an event or situation might happen, might be happening, or might have happened. (引導條件從句) 如果","examples":["She gets very upset if I exclude her from anything. 如果有什麼事我將她排除在外，她就會非常難過。","You can go if you want. 如果你想走就走吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>if</b> in indirect questions where the answer is either \"yes\" or \"no.\" (用於間接是非問句中) 是否","examples":["He asked if I had left with you, and I said no. 他問我是不是和你一起離開的，我說不是。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>if</b> to suggest that something might be slightly different from what you are stating in the main part of the sentence, for example, that there might be slightly more or less of a particular quality. (表示與主句所述事實可能有少許不同) 即使","examples":["Sometimes that standard is quite difficult, if not impossible, to achieve. 有時那個標準，即使並非不可能，也是很難達到的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>if</b>, usually with \"can,\" \"could,\" \"may,\" or \"might,\" in a conversation when you are politely trying to make a point, change the subject, or interrupt another speaker. 常與(can)、(could)、(may)、(might)等情態動詞連用，表示婉轉客氣","examples":["If I could just make another small point about the weightlifters in the Olympics. 請允許我就奧運會的舉重運動員們再稍說一句。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>if</b> at or near the beginning of a clause when politely asking someone to do something. (用於從句句首或靠近句首的位置，表示禮貌的請求) 是否","examples":["I wonder if you'd be kind enough to give us some information, please? 不知能否請您向我們提供些資訊？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>if</b> to introduce a subordinate clause in which you admit a fact that you regard as less important than the statement in the main clause. (引導從句，提出次要的事實) 即使","examples":["If there was any disappointment it was probably temporary. 即使有任何遺憾，可能也是暫時的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>if not</b> in front of a word or phrase to indicate that your statement does not apply to that word or phrase, but to something closely related to it that you also mention. 即便不","examples":["She understood his meaning, if not his words, and took his advice. 她即便不懂他的語言，也明白了他的意思，並且接受了他的建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>if ever</b> with past tenses when you are introducing a description of a person or thing, to emphasize how appropriate it is. (與過去式連用，強調對人或事物的描述極為恰當) 如果有…的話","examples":["I became a distraught, worried mother, a useless role if ever there was one. 如果有個心煩意亂、憂心忡忡的母親，一個完全無用的角色，那就是我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>if only</b> with past tenses to introduce what you think is a fairly good reason for doing something, although you realize it may not be a very good one. 即使僅僅 (與過去式連用，引出能勉強說明做某事的原因)","examples":["She always writes me once a month, if only to scold me because I haven't answered her last letter yet. 她總是一個月寫一封信給我，即使僅僅是為了責備我還沒有回她的上一封信。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>if only</b> to express a wish or desire, especially one that cannot be fulfilled. (尤指不能實現的願望) 要是…多好","examples":["If only you had told me that some time ago. 要是你之前告訴我那件事該多好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>as if</b> when you are making a judgment about something that you see or notice. Your belief or impression might be correct, or it might be wrong. (表示判斷) 好像","examples":["It looked as if she had forgotten how to breathe. 她看上去好像是忘了如何呼吸似的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>as if</b> to describe something or someone by comparing them with another thing or person. (表示類比) 彷彿","examples":["He points two fingers at his head, as if he were holding a gun. 他用兩個手指對著自己的腦袋，彷彿正拿著一把槍。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>as if</b> to emphasize that something is not true. (強調某事不是真的) 好像…一樣","examples":["Getting my work done! My God! As if it mattered. 把我的活兒幹完！我的天哪！好像這很要緊似的。"]}]}]},"since":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"自……以後，自……以來；（表示氣憤）何曾，什麼時候"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"在……以後，自……以來；因為，由於，既然"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"自……以後，自……以來；此後，後來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Since）（法、美）新斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>since</b> when you are mentioning a time or event in the past and indicating that a situation has continued from then until now. 自…以來; 從…以後","examples":["He's been in exile in India since 1959. 他自1959年以來一直流亡印度。","She had a sort of breakdown some years ago, and since then she has been very shy. 她幾年前曾遭遇精神崩潰，從那以後她一直怯生生的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>since</b> to mention a time or event in the past when you are describing an event or situation that has happened after that time. 自…以來","examples":["The percentage increase in reported crime this year is the highest since the war. 今年報道的犯罪增長率是該戰爭以來最高的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Since</b> is also an adverb. 自那時起","examples":["They worked together in the 1960s, and have kept in contact ever since. 他們在20世紀60年代曾一起工作，自那時起就一直保持著聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you are talking about an event or situation in the past, you use <b>since</b> to indicate that another event happened at some point later in time. 此後; 後來","examples":["About six thousand people were arrested, several hundred of whom have since been released. 約六千人被逮捕，不過他們中有幾百人後來被釋放了。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Since</b> is also a conjunction. 自…以來","examples":["I've earned my own living since I was seven, doing all kinds of jobs. 我自從7歲就自己謀生，做各種各樣的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Since</b> is also a conjunction. 自…以來","examples":["So much has changed in the sport since I was a teenager. 自我十幾歲以來，該項運動發生了很大變化。","Since I have become a mother, the sound of children's voices has lost its charm. 我當了母親之後，孩子的聲音就失去了魅力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>since</b> to introduce reasons or explanations. 由於; 既然","examples":["I'm forever on a diet, since I put on weight easily. 我一直在節食，因為我的體重很容易增加。"]}]}]},"for":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（表示物件、用途等）給，對；為了，以幫助；為了（表示目的、用途）；（表示感情的物件）對於；代表；受僱於；意思是，表示；支援，擁護；因為，由於；為得到，為獲取；換取；就……而言；對（某人）來說；……後（更好、更快樂等）；（表示去向）往，向；（用來表示時間或距離）達，計；（安排或預定）在……時；為 （某場合或時間）；由……負責；要不是；想要；取（某人的）名；表名單或系列中的某些部分；表數字或數量間的聯絡；表一頓飯中的食物"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"因為，由於"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"外國（foreign）；林業（forestry）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"支援地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>for</b> someone, they are intended to have it or benefit from it. 為","examples":["Isn't that enough for you? 那對你來說不夠嗎？","...a table for two. …一張雙人桌。","He wanted all the running of the business for himself. 他想要自己管理整個企業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you work or do a job <b>for</b> someone, you are employed by them. 為… (工作)","examples":["I knew he worked for a security firm. 我知道他為一家保安公司工作。","Have you had any experience writing for radio? 你有為電臺撰稿的經驗嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you speak or act <b>for</b> a particular group or organization, you represent them. 代表 (某團體或機構)","examples":["She appears nightly on the television news, speaking for the State Department. 她每晚出現在電視新聞上，代表國務院發言。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone does something <b>for</b> you, they do it so that you do not have to do it. 替… (做事)","examples":["If your pharmacy doesn't stock the product you want, have them order it for you. 如果藥房沒有你所要的產品，讓他們替你訂貨。","I hold a door open for an old person. 我替一位老人把門開開。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you feel a particular emotion <b>for</b> someone, you feel it on their behalf. 替… (感到)","examples":["This is the best thing you've ever done – I am so happy for you! 這是你做過的最好的事–我真為你高興！"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you feel a particular emotion <b>for</b> someone or something, they are the object of that emotion, and you feel it when you think about them. 對… (常懷有某種感情)","examples":["John, I'm sorry for Steve, but I think you've made the right decisions. 約翰，我為史蒂夫感到難過，但我想你作出了正確的決定。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> after words such as \"time,\" \"space,\" \"money,\" or \"energy\" when you say how much there is or whether there is enough of it in order to be able to do or use a particular thing. 供…使用","examples":["Many new trains have space for wheelchair users. 許多新火車都為坐輪椅者留有空間。","...a huge room with plenty of room for books. …可存放大量書籍的一間大屋子。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> when you make a statement about something in order to say how it affects or relates to someone, or what their attitude to it is. 對…來說","examples":["What matters for most scientists is money and facilities. 對大多數科學家來說，重要的是經費和裝置。","For her, books were as necessary to life as bread. 對她來說，書就像麵包一樣是生活的必需。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"After some adjective, noun, and verb phrases, you use <b>for</b> to introduce the subject of the action indicated by the following infinitive verb. 用於某些形容詞、名詞或動詞片語之後，引出動詞不定式的執行主語","examples":["It might be possible for a single woman to be accepted as a foster parent. 有可能接受單身女子做養母。","I had made arrangements for my affairs to be dealt with by one of my children. 我安排了自己的一個孩子處理我的事務。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>not</b> <b>for</b> you, you mean that you do not enjoy it or that it is not suitable for you. 不被…喜歡; 不適合","examples":["Wendy decided the sport was not for her. 溫迪認定這項運動不適合她。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If it is <b>for</b> you <b>to</b> do something, it is your responsibility or right to do it. 由… (負責)","examples":["I wish you would come back to Washington with us, but that's for you to decide. 我希望你和我們一起回華盛頓，但由你自己決定。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>For</b> is the preposition that is used after some nouns, adjectives, or verbs in order to introduce more information or to indicate what a quality, thing, or action relates to. 用於某些名詞、形容詞或動詞之後，引出更多資訊或指出相關的性質、事物、行為等","examples":["Reduced-calorie cheese is a great substitute for cream cheese. 低卡路里乾酪是奶油乾酪的極好替代品。","Parking lot owners should be legally responsible for protecting vehicles. 停車場場主應該依法負責保護車輛。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a word or expression has the same meaning as another word or expression, you can say that the first one is another word or expression <b>for</b> the second one. (意思) 相當於","examples":["The technical term for sunburn is erythema. 曬斑的專業術語是紅斑病。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"To be named <b>for</b> someone means to be given the same name as them. 以… (命名)","examples":["The Brady Bill is named for former White House Press Secretary James Brady. 布雷迪法案是以前白宮新聞秘書詹姆斯·布雷迪命名的。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> in a piece of writing when you mention information which will be found somewhere else. 至於… (用於指可以在文中其它地方找到的資訊)","examples":["For further information on the life of William James Sidis, see Amy Wallace, \"The Prodigy.\" 要了解更多關於威廉·詹姆斯·西迪斯的生平，參閱艾米·華萊士的《神童》。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"<b>For</b> is used in conditional sentences, in expressions such as \"<b>if not for</b>\" and \"<b>were it not for</b>,\" to introduce the only thing which prevents the main part of the sentence from being true.  要不是","examples":["If not for John, Brian wouldn't have learned the truth. 要不是約翰，布萊恩不會了解真相。","The earth would be a frozen ball if it were not for the radiant heat of the sun. 要是沒有太陽的輻射熱，地球將會是一個冰凍的球體。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> when you state or explain the purpose of an object, action, or activity. 為了 (表示目的、用途)","examples":["...drug users who use unsterile equipment for injections of drugs. …用未消過毒的器具注射毒品的吸毒者們。","The knife for cutting sausage was sitting in the sink. 用於切香腸的刀在水槽裡。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> after nouns expressing reason or cause. 因為 (作介詞，用於表示原因的名詞後)","examples":["He's soon to make a speech explaining his reasons for going. 他很快將會發表講話說明去的原因。","The county hospital could find no physical cause for Sumner's problems. 縣醫院查不出薩姆納的問題的生理原因。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If something is <b>for</b> sale, hire, or use, it is available to be sold, hired, or used. 供 (銷售、租用、使用)","examples":["Freshwater fish for sale. 供出售的淡水魚。","...a room for rent. …一間供租用的房間。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you do something <b>for</b> a particular occasion, you do it on that occasion or to celebrate that occasion. 為 (某場合)","examples":["He asked his daughter what she would like for her birthday. 他問他女兒想要如何過她的生日。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you leave <b>for</b> a particular place or if you take a bus, train, plane, or boat <b>for</b> a place, you are going there. 前往 (某地)","examples":["They would be leaving for Rio early the next morning. 他們次日一早將前往裡約。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> to say how long something lasts or continues. 用於表示持續的時間","examples":["The toaster was on for more than an hour. 烤箱開了一個多小時。","They talked for a bit. 他們談了會兒。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> to say how far something extends. 用於表示延伸的距離","examples":["We drove on for a few miles. 我們繼續開了幾英里。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If something is bought, sold, or done <b>for</b> a particular amount of money, that amount of money is its price. 以 (某數量的錢)","examples":["We got the bus back to Tange for 30 cents. 我們以30美分乘公共汽車回到了坦格。","The Martins sold their house for about 1.4 million dollars. 馬丁一家以約一百四十萬美元把他們的房子賣了。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If something is planned <b>for</b> a particular time, it is planned to happen then. 於 (某時間)","examples":["...the Baltimore Boat Show, planned for January 21 – 29. …計劃於1月21至29日舉行的巴爾的摩船展。","The designer will be unveiling her latest fashions for autumn and winter. 該設計師將公佈她的最新款秋冬時裝。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> when you say that an aspect of something or someone is surprising in relation to other aspects of them. 對…來說","examples":["He was tall for an eight-year-old. 對一個8歲的孩子來說他長得很高。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> with \"every\" when you are stating a ratio, to introduce one of the things in the ratio. 對於 (與every連用，用於引出比率中之一)","examples":["For every farm job that is lost, two or three other jobs in the area are put at risk. 對於失去的每份農場工作，該地區的其它兩三個工作就會被置於危險中。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"You can use <b>for</b> in expressions such as <b>dollar for dollar</b> or <b>mile for mile</b> when you are making comparisons between the values or qualities of different things. 對應 (用於比較不同事物間的價值或品質)","examples":["...the Antarctic, mile for mile one of the planet's most lifeless areas. …每英里都是地球上最無生命的地區之一的南極洲。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>for</b> a particular activity, you mean that this is what you want or intend to do. 想要","examples":["Right, who's for a toasted sandwich then? 好了，那誰想要一個吐司三明治呢？"]},{"num":"30.","zh":"If you are <b>for</b> something, you agree with it or support it. 贊成; 支援","examples":["Are you for or against public transportation? 你是支援還是反對公共交通？"]},{"num":"31.","zh":"You use <b>for</b> after words such as \"argue,\" \"case,\" \"evidence,\" or \"vote\" in order to introduce the thing that is being supported or proved. 支援","examples":["Another union has voted for industrial action in support of a pay claim. 又一個工會已投票贊成支援加薪要求的勞工行動。","The case for nuclear power is impressive. 支援核能的論據令人印象深刻。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>for the first time</b> and <b>for the last time</b> when you are talking about how often something has happened before. 首次/最後一次","examples":["He was married for the second time. 他第二次結婚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>all for</b> doing something, you agree or strongly believe that it should be done, but you are also often suggesting that other people disagree with you or that there are practical difficulties. 完全贊成; 極力支援","examples":["He is all for players earning what they can while they are in the game. 他完全贊成運動員在役期間能賺多少錢就賺多少。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>For</b> is also an adverb. 支援地","examples":["833 delegates voted for, and only 432 against. 833名代表投票支援，只有432人反對。"]}]}]},"than":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（用以引出比較的第二部分）比；（比較數量、距離等）多於；（表示一事緊跟另一事發生）就；除……（外）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（用以引出比較的第二部分）比；（比較數量、距離等）多於；（表示一事緊跟另一事發生）就；除……（外）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Than）（越）丹（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>than</b> after a comparative adjective or adverb in order to link two parts of a comparison. (用於形容詞或副詞的比較級後，連線相比較的兩個部分) 比","examples":["Children learn faster than adults. 孩子比大人學得快。","The radio only weighs a few ounces and is smaller than a pack of cigarettes. 這個收音機只有幾盎司重，比一包香菸還小。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>than</b> when you are stating a number, quantity, or value approximately by saying that it is above or below another number, quantity, or value. (數、量或價值) 高於; 低於","examples":["They talked on the phone for more than an hour. 他們在電話裡聊了一個多小時。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Than</b> is also a conjunction. 比","examples":["He wished he could have helped her more than he did. 他希望自己當時能更多地幫幫她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>than</b> in order to link two parts of a contrast, for example, in order to state a preference. (連線相比較的兩個部分，表優先選擇) 與其說","examples":["The arrangement was more a formality than a genuine partnership of two nations. 這種安排與其說是兩國間真正的夥伴關係的表現，還不如說是裝樣子。"]}]}]},"or":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（用以引出另一種可能性）或，或者，還是；（用於否定動詞後）也不；（用於警告或忠告）否則，不然；（用於兩個數字之間表示約略數目）大約；（用於引出解釋性詞語）或者說；（用於說明原因）不然，否則；（用於引出對比的概念）；<文>還是"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電子）（邏輯電路的）或（OR）；（紋章）金色，黃色"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"俄勒岡州（Oregon）；手術室（operating room）；運籌學（operational research）；普通士兵（other ranks）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>or</b> to link two or more alternatives. 或者","examples":["\"Tea or coffee?\" John asked. “喝茶還是喝咖啡？” 約翰問。","He said he would try to write or call as soon as he reached the Canary Islands. 他說他一到加那利群島就會盡快寫信或打電話過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>or</b> to give another alternative, when the first alternative is introduced by \"either\" or \"whether.\" 還是 (與either或whether連用)","examples":["Items like bread, milk and meat were either unavailable or could be obtained only on the black market. 像麵包、牛奶和肉這樣的食品要麼沒有，要麼只有從黑市才能買到。","Either you can talk to him, or I will. 要麼你和他談，要麼我來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>or</b> between two numbers to indicate that you are giving an approximate amount. 或 (表示大概的數量)","examples":["Everyone benefited from limiting their intake of coffee to just one or two cups a day. 每個人都從每天限量喝一杯或兩杯咖啡的做法中受益了。","When I was nine or ten someone explained to me that when you are grown up you have to work. 在我9歲或10歲的時候，有人跟我解釋說，人長大之後必須工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>or</b> to introduce a comment which corrects or modifies what you have just said. 抑或 (用於更正剛說過的話)","examples":["The man was a fool, he thought, or at least incompetent. 他想，那人是個傻子，或者至少是無能。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone should do something <b>or</b> something bad will happen, you are warning them that if they do not do it, the bad thing will happen. 否則 (引導一個表示警告的從句)","examples":["She had to have the operation, or she would die. 她必須進行手術，否則會死的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>or</b> to introduce something which is evidence for the truth of a statement you have just made. 否則 (引導用作解釋、辯護的一件事)","examples":["He must have thought Jane was worth it or he wouldn't have wasted time on her, I suppose. 我想，他當時肯定認為簡值得他費心思，否則他就不會在她身上浪費時間了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"before; when 在...之前; 當..之時","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"before 在...之前","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"of the metal gold 金牌的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>or not</b> to emphasize that a particular thing makes no difference to what is going to happen. …也好 (表示某事對要發生的事無關緊要)","examples":["Like it or not, you're in charge. 喜歡也好，不喜歡也罷，反正是你負責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>or no</b> between two occurrences of the same noun in order to say that whether something is true or not makes no difference to a situation. 不管有沒有… (表示某事對形勢無關緊要)","examples":["The next day, rain or no rain, it was business as usual. 不管第二天下不下雨，一切事情照舊。"]}]}]},"only":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"只，只有；僅在……情況下（或地方等）；只是，不過（表示不重要、不嚴重等）；（強調數量少或時間段）僅僅，才；不早於，直到……才；（除此之外別無可為）只能；（用於說明事情的惡果）只會；不料，竟然；只能（希望或願望等）；（強調行動恰當）完全，真正；剛剛（強調某事剛發生）；險些沒，差點沒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"僅有的，唯一的；最好的，最適合的；獨生的"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"<非正式>不過，但是；<非正式>要不是，若非"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>only</b> to indicate the one thing that is true, appropriate, or necessary in a particular situation, in contrast to all the other things that are not true, appropriate, or necessary. 只有","examples":["Only the president could authorize the use of the atomic bomb. 只有總統能授權原子彈的使用。","A business can only be built and expanded on a sound financial base. 一家企業只有在穩定的財政基礎上才能開辦並擴大規模。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>only</b> to introduce the thing which must happen before the thing mentioned in the main part of the sentence can happen. 只有…才","examples":["The lawyer is paid only if he wins. 律師只有打贏官司才會被付費。","The Bank of England insists that it will cut interest rates only when it is ready. 英格蘭銀行堅持只有在它做好準備時才會降低利率。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>only</b> to indicate that something is no more important, interesting, or difficult, for example, than you say it is, especially when you want to correct a wrong idea that someone has or may get. 僅僅…而已","examples":["At the moment it is only a theory. 眼下，它還只是個理論而已。","\"I'm only a sergeant,\" said Clements. “我不過是個中士，”克萊門茨說。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>only</b> to emphasize how small an amount is or how short a length of time is. (強調數量小或時間短) 僅僅","examples":["Child car seats only cost about $10 a week to rent. 兒童汽車座椅租用一週僅花費約$10。","...spacecraft guidance systems weighing only a few grams. …重量只有幾克的宇宙飛船導航系統。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>only</b> to emphasize that you are talking about a small part of an amount or group, not the whole of it. (強調只是一小部分而非全部) 僅僅","examples":["These are only a few of the possibilities. 這些只是其中的幾個可能性。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Only</b> is used after \"can\" or \"could\" to emphasize that it is impossible to do anything except the rather inadequate or limited action that is mentioned. (用於)(can)(或)(could)(之後，強調除此之外別無他法) 只","examples":["For a moment I could say nothing. I could only stand and look. 一時間我什麼也說不出來，只能站在那兒看著。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>only</b> in the expressions <b>I only wish</b> or <b>I only hope</b> in order to emphasize what you are hoping or wishing. (強調願望或希望) 確實","examples":["I only wish he were here now that things are getting better for me. 既然我的情況正在好轉，我真希望他在這兒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>only</b> before an infinitive to introduce an event which happens immediately after one you have just mentioned, and which is surprising or unfortunate. (用於不定式前) 不料","examples":["Ron tried the embassy, only to be told that Hugh was in a meeting. 羅恩到使館試了試，不料被告知休正在開會。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>only</b> to emphasize how appropriate a certain course of action or type of behaviour is. (用來強調適宜性) 很","examples":["It's only fair to let her know that you intend to apply. 讓她知道你有意申請是很公平的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can use <b>only</b> in front of a verb to indicate that the result of something is unfortunate or undesirable and is likely to make the situation worse rather than better. (用於動詞前) 反而","examples":["The embargo would only hurt innocent civilians. 禁運反而會傷及無辜的平民。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about <b>the</b> <b>only</b> person or thing involved in a particular situation, you mean there are no others involved in it. 惟一的","examples":["She was the only woman in Shell's legal department. 她曾是殼牌公司法律部惟一的女性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>only</b> child is a child who has no brothers or sisters. 獨生的","examples":["The actor, an only child, grew up in the Bronx. 那位演員是位獨生子，在布朗克斯區長大。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Only</b> can be used to add a comment which slightly changes or limits what you have just said. (用來補充) 只是","examples":["It's just as dramatic as a film, only it's real. 這真和電影一樣富有戲劇性，只不過它是現實。","It's a bit like my house, only nicer. 這有點兒像我的房子，不過更漂亮些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Only</b> can be used after a clause with \"would\" to indicate why something is not done. 要不是","examples":["I'd invite you to come with me, only it's such a long way. 要不是路途太遠，我就請你和我一起去了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say you <b>only have to</b> do one thing in order to achieve or prove a second thing, you are emphasizing how easily the second thing can be achieved or proved. 只要…即可","examples":["Any time you want a babysitter, dear, you only have to ask. 親愛的，任何時候你想要一個臨時照看孩子的人，只要開口說就是了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that something has <b>only just</b> happened when you want to emphasize that it happened a very short time ago. 剛剛","examples":["I've only just arrived. 我剛剛才到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>only just</b> to emphasize that something is true, but by such a small degree that it is almost not true at all. 勉強","examples":["For centuries farmers there have only just managed to survive. 幾個世紀以來，那兒的農民勉強能維持生存。","I am old enough to remember the War, but only just. 我這個年齡足以記住那場戰爭，不過只是勉強記得。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>only too</b> to emphasize that something is true or exists to a much greater extent than you would expect or like. 極其","examples":["I know only too well that plans can easily go wrong. 我非常清楚，計劃會很容易出問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that you are <b>only too</b> happy to do something to emphasize how willing you are to do it. (強調樂意做某事) 太","examples":["I'll be only too pleased to help them out with any questions. 我將十分樂意為他們解決任何問題。"]}]}]},"though":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"雖然，儘管；可是，不過"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不過，可是，然而"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>though</b> to introduce a statement in a subordinate clause which contrasts with the statement in the main clause. You often use <b>though</b> to introduce a fact which you regard as less important than the fact in the main clause. 儘管","examples":["Everything I told them was correct, though I forgot a few things. 我告訴他們的全部正確，儘管我忘了幾件事。","I like him. Though he makes me angry sometimes. 我喜歡他，儘管他有時惹我生氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>though</b> to introduce a subordinate clause which gives some information that is relevant to the main clause and weakens the force of what it is saying. 不過","examples":["He did reply, though not immediately. 他確實回覆了，不過不是立馬回覆。"]}]}]},"till":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"直到，到……為止；<蘇格蘭>向，朝"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"直到，到……為止"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（商店等處的）現金出納機，收銀機；<英，非正式>（大商店中的）交款處，收銀臺；（商店或銀行）放錢的抽屜，收銀盒；（地質）冰磧（物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"耕作，犁地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In spoken English and informal written English, <b>till</b> is often used instead of . 直到…為止","examples":["They had to wait till Monday to phone the bank. 他們不得不等到星期一才打電話給銀行。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Till</b> is also a conjunction. 直到…為止","examples":["I hadn't left home till I was nineteen. 我直到19歲才離開家門。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>till</b> is the drawer of a cash register, where the money is kept. (收銀機中的) 錢櫃","examples":["He checked the register. There was money in the till. 他檢查了收銀機。錢櫃裡有錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a shop or other place of business, a <b>till</b> is a counter or cash register where money is kept, and where customers pay for what they have bought. (商店等的) 收銀臺; 收銀機","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an unstratified glacial deposit consisting of rock fragments of various sizes. The most common is boulder clay 冰磧物; 冰磧","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cultivate and work (land) for the raising of crops 耕種; 耕耘; 耕作","examples":[]}]}]},"until":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"到……時，直到……為止"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"到……時，直到……為止；直到（某處）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>until</b> a particular time, it happens during the period before that time and stops at that time. 直到…為止","examples":["Until 2004, she lived in Canada. 到2004年為止，她一直住在加拿大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>until</b> with a negative to emphasize the moment in time after which the rest of your statement becomes true, or the condition which would make it true. 直到…才","examples":["The traffic laws don't take effect until the end of the year. 交通法要到年底才生效。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Until</b> is also a conjunction. 直到…為止","examples":["I waited until it got dark. 我一直等到天黑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Until</b> is also a conjunction. 直到…才","examples":["The government said that it has suspended all aid to Haiti until that country's legitimate government is restored. 政府說它已經暫停對海地的所有援助，直到海地恢復合法政府為止。"]}]}]},"whether":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"是否（表選擇或可能性）；不管，無論"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"<古>兩個中的哪一個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whether</b> when you are talking about a choice or doubt between two or more alternatives. 是否","examples":["To this day, it's unclear whether he shot himself or was murdered. 直到今天，他是自殺還是被謀殺仍然不清楚。","Whether it turns out to be a good idea or a bad idea, we'll find out. 最終這個點子是好還是壞，我們會搞清楚的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>whether</b> to say that something is true in any of the circumstances that you mention. 無論","examples":["This happens whether the children are in two-parent or one-parent families. 這種情況無論在雙親家庭還是單親家庭的孩子身上都會發生。","Whether they say it aloud or not, most men expect their wives to be faithful. 無論他們是否說出來，大部分男人都希望他們的妻子忠貞不渝。"]}]}]},"that":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"那，那個；那，那種"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"那，那個；那，那種；（非正式，用於 that's that 等）就這樣，就那樣；（正式，用於 that of、that which 等結構）……的；（關係代詞，引導定語從句）……的"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（引導名詞性從句，本身無實義，常略去不譯）；（用於 it may be that 等結構）可能是；由於；以至於；（表示目的）為了；（詩、文）真希望"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"那樣，那麼；（非正式）很，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> to refer back to an idea or situation expressed in a previous sentence or sentences. 那 (指前面句子提過的想法或情形)","examples":["They said you particularly wanted to talk to me. Why was that? 他們說你特別想和我談談。那是為什麼？","\"There's a party tonight.\"—\"Is that why you're phoning?\" “今晚有聚會。”—“那就是你打電話的原因嗎？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> in expressions such as <b>that of</b> and <b>that which</b> to introduce more information about something already mentioned, instead of repeating the noun which refers to it. 那 (用於引入有關已提及的事物的更多資訊，避免重複提及相關名詞)","examples":["A recession like that of 1973-74 could put one in ten American companies into bankruptcy. 一場像1973到1974年那樣的經濟衰退會使1/10的美國公司破產。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> in front of words or expressions which express agreement, responses, or reactions to what has just been said. 那 (用於對已說過的話表示同意或應答的詞前)","examples":["\"She said she'd met you in England.\"—\"That's true.\" “她說她在英格蘭見過你。”—“沒錯。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>That</b> is also a pronoun. 那個","examples":["Leo, what's that you're writing? 利奧，你寫的那是什麼呀？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> when you are identifying someone or asking about their identity. 那個 (用於識別或詢問他人的身份)","examples":["That's my wife you were talking to. 剛才和你說話的是我妻子。","\"Who's that with you?\"—\"A friend of mine.\" “和你在一起的那個人是誰？”—“我的一位朋友。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>That</b> is also a pronoun. 那","examples":["That was a terrible case of blackmail in the paper today. 那是今天報紙裡刊登的一宗可怕的勒索案。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>That</b> is also a determiner. 那","examples":["She's away; for that reason I'm cooking tonight. 她不在家，所以今晚我煮飯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> to refer to someone or something already mentioned. 那 (指已提及的人或物)","examples":["The salespeople get between $50,000 and $60,000 a year but that amount can double with commission. 推銷員每年的收入在5萬到6萬美元之間，但是加上佣金，那數額能翻倍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you have been talking about a particular period of time, you use <b>that</b> to indicate that you are still referring to the same period. You use expressions such as <b>that morning</b> or <b>that afternoon</b> to indicate that you are referring to an earlier period of the same day. 那 (指前文提到的同一時期)","examples":["The story was published in a Sunday newspaper later that week. 這個故事在那周晚些時候被刊登在一家星期日報紙上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> when you are referring to someone or something which is a distance away from you in position or time, especially when you indicate or point to them. When there are two or more things near you, <b>that</b> refers to the more distant one. 那個 (指距離或時間上較遠的人或事物)","examples":["Look at that guy. He's got red socks. 看那傢伙，他穿著紅襪子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>that</b> when you expect the person you are talking to to know what or who you are referring to, without needing to identify the particular person or thing fully. 那個 (不需明確指出，指代對方應該知道的人或物)","examples":["I really thought I was something when I wore that hat and my patent leather shoes. 當我戴上那頂帽子，穿著我的漆皮鞋的時候，我還真以為自己是個人物。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>not</b> <b>that</b> bad, funny, or expensive for example, it is not as bad, funny, or expensive as it might be or as has been suggested. 那麼","examples":["Not even Gary, he said, was that stupid. 他說，就是加里也沒那麼笨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>that</b> to emphasize the degree of a feeling or quality. 那樣 (用於強調感情或品質的程度)","examples":["I would have walked out, I was that angry. 我本要走出去的，我是那樣的生氣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>and all that</b> or <b>and that</b> to refer generally to everything else which is associated with what you have just mentioned. 諸如此類","examples":["I'm not a cook myself but I am interested in nutrition and all that. 我本人不是廚師，但我對營養之類的事感興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>at that</b> after a statement which modifies or emphasizes what you have just said. 而且","examples":["Success never seems to come but through hard work, often physically demanding work at that. 成功不透過努力工作似乎是無法取得的，而且往往是很耗費體力的工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>that is</b> or <b>that is to say</b> to indicate that you are about to express the same idea more clearly or precisely. 也就是說","examples":["I am a disappointing, though generally dutiful, student. That is, I do as I'm told. 我是個令人失望的學生，儘管一般來說我很聽話，也就是說，我按別人說的做。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>that's it</b> to indicate that nothing more needs to be done or that the end has been reached. 就這樣","examples":["When he left the office, that was it, the workday was over. 他一離開辦公室，工作日就這樣結束了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>just like that</b> to emphasize that something happens or is done immediately or in a very simple way, often without much thought or discussion. 就那樣","examples":["Just like that, I was in love. 就那樣，我戀愛了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>that's that</b> to say there is nothing more you can do or say about a particular matter. 就那樣好了","examples":["\"Well, if that's the way you want it,\" he replied, tears in his eyes, \"I guess that's that.\" “哦，如果你要那樣的話，”他淚汪汪地回答道，“我想就那樣好了。”"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>that's it</b> to express agreement with or approval of what has just been said or done. 沒錯","examples":["\"You got married, right?\"—\"Yeah, that's it.\" “你結婚了，對吧？”—“是的，沒錯。”"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>that</b> after many verbs, adjectives, nouns, and expressions to introduce a clause in which you report what someone has said, or what they think or feel. 用於某些動詞、形容詞、名詞和短語後,引導從句來引述某人的話語、思想或感覺","examples":["He called her up one day and said that he and his wife were coming to New York. 他有一天給她打電話,說他和他妻子要來紐約。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> after \"it\" and a linking verb and an adjective to comment on a situation or fact. 用於(it)、系動詞或形容詞後來評論某種情況或事實","examples":["It's interesting that you like him. 很有意思，你喜歡他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> after expressions with \"so\" and \"such\" in order to introduce the result or effect of something. 用於帶(so)和(such)的短語後，引入某事的結果或影響","examples":["She became so nervous that she shook violently. 她緊張得全身猛烈顫抖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>that</b> to introduce a clause which gives more information to help identify the person or thing you are talking about. 用於引導定語從句來幫助說明所談及的人或物","examples":["...pills that will make the problem disappear. …會消除該症狀的藥丸。"]}]}]},"actress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女演員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>actress</b> is a woman whose job is acting in plays or films. 女演員","examples":["She's not only a great dramatic actress but she's also very funny. 她不僅是一位偉大的女戲劇演員，而且也很幽默。"]}]}]},"actor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"演員；像在演戲的人；（行動或過程）參與者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>actor</b> is someone whose job is acting in plays or films. \"Actor\" in the singular usually refers to a man, but some women who act prefer to be called \"actors\" rather than \"actresses.\" 演員","examples":["His father was an actor in the Cantonese Opera Company. 他父親曾是粵劇團的一名演員。"]}]}]},"when":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"什麼時候；什麼情況下；什麼場合下；（用於時間的表達方式之後）在那時，其時；當時，當場"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"什麼時候；何時（多用於 since、till、until 等之後）"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"當……時，在……時候；在……之後；一……就；隨時，在任何……時候；既然，考慮到；雖然，然而，可是；這時，突然"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"時間，時候；日期；場合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> to ask questions about the time at which things happen. 什麼時候 (用於疑問句，詢問某事發生的時間)","examples":["When are you going home? 你什麼時候回家？","When did you get married? 你是什麼時候結婚的？"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>when</b> something else is happening, the two things are happening at the same time. (表示兩件事同時發生) 當…的時候","examples":["When eating a whole cooked fish, you should never turn it over to get at the flesh on the other side. 吃一整條做熟的魚時，你永遠都不要把魚翻過來吃另一邊的肉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> to introduce a clause in which you mention something that happens at some point during an activity, event, or situation. 當…時 (引導從句，表示從句中提到的事發生在另一活動、事件或情況期間)","examples":["When I met the Gills, I had been gardening for nearly ten years. 我結識吉爾一家時，我已經幾乎做了十年的園藝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> to introduce a clause where you mention the circumstances under which the event in the main clause happened or will happen. 在…情況下 (引導從句，表示從句中提到的情況是主句中已經發生或即將發生的事的前提)","examples":["When he brought Imelda her drink she gave him a genuine, sweet smile of thanks. 當他給艾梅爾達拿來一杯飲料時，她給了他一個真誠、甜美、表示謝意的微笑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause where you mention the time at which something happens. 什麼時候 (用在某些詞尤其是動詞和形容詞後，引導從句說明某事發生的時間)","examples":["I asked him when he'd be back to pick me up. 我問他什麼時候回來接我。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> to introduce the reason for an opinion, comment, or question. 既然 (用於引入觀點、評論、或問題的原因)","examples":["How can I love myself when I look like this? 既然我這麼一副樣子，我怎麼能愛我自己？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> in order to introduce a fact or comment which makes the other part of the sentence rather surprising or unlikely. 而 (引出令人吃驚的事實或評論)","examples":["Our mothers sat us down to read and paint, when all we really wanted to do was to make a mess. 我們的媽媽們讓我們坐下讀書、畫畫，而我們真正想要做的卻是胡鬧一陣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>when</b> to introduce a clause that specifies or refers to the time at which something happens. 當…的時候 (引導表示某事發生的具體時間的從句)","examples":["He could remember a time when he had worked like that himself. 他還記得當他自己也像那樣工作的那段時間。"]}]}]},"so":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（表程度）如此，這麼；也一樣（用於倒裝）；（口語）那麼（引出新話題）；確是如此"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"所以，因此；以便，為了（表目的）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"這樣，如此（指代前述內容、情況或方式）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（So）人名；（柬）索"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>so</b> to refer back to something that has just been mentioned. 如此 (用以指代剛剛提及的事)","examples":["\"Do you think that made much of a difference to the family?\"—\"I think so.\" “你認為那樣給全家帶來了很大變化嗎？”—“我覺得是。”","If you can't play straight, then say so. 如果你不能做到誠實坦率，那就直說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>so</b> when you are saying that something which has just been said about one person or thing is also true of another one. 也一樣 (用以表示說過的事也適用於另一人或物)","examples":["I enjoy Ann's company and so does Martin. 我喜歡有安相伴，馬丁也一樣。","They had a wonderful time and so did I. 他們玩得很開心，我也是。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a state of affairs <b>is so</b>, you mean that it is the way it has been described. (某一情況) 就是這樣","examples":["In those days English dances as well as songs were taught at school, but that seems no longer to be so. 那時，英語歌曲還有舞蹈都要在學校教授，但現在情況似乎不再是這樣了。","It is strange to think that he held strong views on many things, but it must have been so. 想到當時他對許多事情的觀點都很強硬，真是很奇怪，但那時應該就是這樣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>so</b> with actions and gestures to show a person how to do something, or to indicate the size, height, or length of something. 這樣 (用以演示如何做某事或展示某物)","examples":["Clasp the chain like so. 就像這樣抓住鏈子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>so</b> in conversations to introduce a new topic, or to introduce a question or comment about something that has been said. 那麼 (用以提出新話題、疑問、評論等)","examples":["So how was your day? 那麼，你今天怎麼樣？","So you're a runner, huh? 這麼說，你是個跑步愛好者嘍？","So as for your question, Miles, the answer still has to be no. 那麼至於你的問題，邁爾斯，回答依然是否定的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>so</b> in conversations to show that you are accepting what someone has just said. 確實 (用以表示接受某人的說法)","examples":["\"It makes me feel, well, important.\"—\"And so you are.\" “這使我覺得，嗯，自己很重要。”—“你確實重要。”","\"You can't possibly use this word.\"—\"So I won't.\" “你不可能會用這個詞。”—“我確實不會用。”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>so</b> in front of adjectives and adverbs to emphasize the quality that they are describing. 如此 (用於形容詞或副詞前，表示強調)","examples":["He was surprised they had married – they had seemed so different. 他很吃驚他們居然已經結婚了–他們看上去他們如此不同。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>so...that</b> and <b>so...as</b> to emphasize the degree of something by mentioning the result or consequence of it. 如此…以致…","examples":["The tears were streaming so fast she could not see. 淚水湧出如此迅速，讓她都看不見了。","He's not so stupid as to listen to rumours. 他還沒有笨到聽信謠言份兒上。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the structures <b>as...so</b> and <b>just as...so</b> when you want to indicate that two events or situations are similar in some way. 也亦然 (用以表示兩個事件或情況在某方面相似)","examples":["As computer systems become even more sophisticated, so too do the methods of those who exploit the technology. 正如計算機系統變得越來越複雜，開發計算機技術的人所採用的方法也日趨複雜。","Just as John has changed, so has his wife. 正如約翰已經變了，他妻子也變了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>so</b> and <b>so that</b> to introduce the result of the situation you have just mentioned. 因此","examples":["I am not an emotional type and so cannot bring myself to tell him I love him. 我不是情感外露的人，因此難以開口對他說我愛他。","People are living longer than ever before, so even people who are 65 or 70 have a surprising amount of time left. 人們的壽命比以前都要長，所以即便是65或70歲的人，餘下光陰也還長得驚人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>so</b>, <b>so that</b>, and <b>so as</b> to introduce the reason for doing the thing that you have just mentioned. 為了 (用以說明理由)","examples":["Come to my suite so I can tell you all about this wonderful play I saw in Boston. 到我的套房來吧，這樣我就可以把我在波士頓看的這部好戲好好跟你說說。","He took her arm and hurried her upstairs so that they wouldn't be overheard. 他抓著她的手臂，急忙將她拉上樓，這樣他們就不會被偷聽了。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>So?</b>\" and \"<b>So what?</b>\" to indicate that you think that something that someone has said is unimportant. 那又怎樣呢？","examples":["\"My name's Bruno.\"—\"So?\" “我的名字是布魯諾。”—“那又怎樣？”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>and so on</b> or <b>and so forth</b> at the end of a list to indicate that there are other items that you could also mention. 如此等等","examples":["...the government's policies on such important issues as health, education, tax, and so on. …政府有關醫療、教育、稅收等重大問題的政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>so much</b> and <b>so many</b> when you are saying that there is a definite limit to something but you are not saying what this limit is. 這麼多 (用以強調某事的限度)","examples":["There is only so much time in the day for answering letters. 白天只有這麼多時間用來回信。","There is only so much fuel in the tank and if you burn it up too quickly you are in trouble. 油罐裡只有這麼多燃料了，如果你用得太快，就有麻煩了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use the structures <b>not...so much</b> and <b>not so much...as</b> to say that something is one kind of thing rather than another kind. 與其說…不如說是…","examples":["I did not really object to Will's behaviour so much as his personality. 我與其說是反感威爾的行為，還不如說是討厭他的個性。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>or so</b> when you are giving an approximate amount. 大約","examples":["Though rates are heading down, they still offer real returns of 8% or so. 儘管利率在下降，但他們仍然給出了8%左右的實際收益率。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Somalia 索馬利亞","examples":[]}]}]},"yet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"仍然，還；現在，此刻；迄今為止，到目前為止；還需，還差；終歸，遲早；又，甚至（強調增加或重複）；然而，儘管"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"然而，但是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>yet</b> in negative statements to indicate that something has not happened up to the present time, although it probably will happen. You can also use <b>yet</b> in questions to ask if something has happened up to the present time. 尚 (用於否定句); 已經 (用於疑問句)","examples":["They haven't finished yet. 他們還沒有結束。","No decision has yet been made. 尚未作出決定。","She hasn't yet set a date for her marriage. 她尚未定下她結婚的日子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>yet</b> with a negative statement when you are talking about the past, to report something that was not the case then, although it became the case later. (當時) 還 (用於否定句)","examples":["There was so much that Sam didn't know yet. 有那麼多薩姆當時還不知道的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something should not or cannot be done <b>yet</b>, you mean that it should not or cannot be done now, although it will have to be done at a later time. (此時) 還 (用於否定句)","examples":["Don't get up yet. 還別起床。","The hostages cannot go home just yet. 人質們這時還不能回家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>yet</b> after a superlative to indicate, for example, that something is the worst or the best of its kind up to the present time. 迄今 (最…)","examples":["This is the network's worst idea yet. 這是到目前為止該網路最糟糕的點子。","Her latest novel is her best yet. 她的最新小說是到目前為止她的最好的小說。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>yet</b> to say that there is still a possibility that something will happen. 仍 (用以表示某事仍有發生的可能性)","examples":["Like the best stories, this one may yet have a happy ending. 像那些最好的故事一樣，這個故事可能仍有個幸福的結局。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>yet</b> after expressions that refer to a period of time, when you want to say how much longer a situation will continue for. 還 (會繼續某段時間)","examples":["Unemployment will go on rising for some time yet. 失業人數還會繼續增長一段時間。","Nothing will happen for a few years yet. 幾年內還不會發生什麼事。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that you have <b>yet</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you have never done it, especially when this is surprising or bad. 還 (不曾做某事)","examples":["She has yet to spend a Christmas with her husband. 她還不曾跟丈夫一起度過一個聖誕節。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>yet</b> to emphasize a word, especially when you are saying that something is surprising because it is more extreme than previous things of its kind, or a further case of them. 還 (尤用以強調令人吃驚的事物)","examples":["I saw yet another doctor. 我還看了另一位醫生。","They would criticize me, or worse yet, pay me no attention. 他們會批評我，甚或更糟，會不理我。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>yet</b> to introduce a fact that is rather surprising after the previous fact you have just mentioned. 然而","examples":["I don't eat much, yet I am a size 16. 我吃得不多，然而我是個穿16號的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as yet</b> with negative statements to describe a situation that has existed up until the present time. 迄今還 (用於否定陳述句中)","examples":["As yet it is not known whether the crash was the result of an accident. 迄今尚不知該撞擊是否是由於一起事故。"]}]}]},"address":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地址，住址；網址；電子郵箱地址；演講，演說；（電子表格中某個單元格的）位置；<古>（對他人的）談吐；<古>謙恭（或脈脈含情）的方式；<舊>機敏，迅速；位置儲存編碼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"演說，演講；處理，設法解決；在（信封、包裹等）上寫姓名和地址，致函；<正式> 向……講話；稱呼；<正式>（向某人）提出（陳述、投訴等）；（高爾夫）就位擊（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>address</b> is the number of the house or apartment and the name of the street and the town where you live or work. 地址","examples":["The address is 2025 M Street, NW, Washington, DC, 20036. 地址是華盛頓哥倫比亞特區，華盛頓西北，M街2025號，郵編20036。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>address</b> of a website is its location on the Internet, for example, http://www.thomson.com. 網址","examples":["Full details, including the website address to log on to, are at the bottom of this page. 包括要登陸的網址的完整資訊在本頁下端。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Address</b> is also a noun. 演講","examples":["He had scheduled an address to the American people for the evening of May 27. 他已經安排在5月27日晚向美國人民作一個演講。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a letter, envelope, or parcel <b>is addressed to</b> you, your name and address have been written on it. 寫 (收信人的) 姓名地址","examples":["Applications should be addressed to: The business affairs editor. 申請信應該寄給商務編輯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>address</b> a group of people, you give a speech to them. 作演講","examples":["He is due to address a conference on human rights next week. 他下週要在一個人權會議上發言。"]}]}]},"action":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行動；行為；戰鬥；訴訟；<非正式>令人激動的事；動作；情節；驚險刺激的活動（或事件）；作用；開始（電影導演開拍的指令）；賺錢的機會；性交；運轉方式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"處理"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"動作（片）的，動作片中的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Action</b> is doing something for a particular purpose. 行動","examples":["The government is taking emergency action to deal with a housing crisis. 該政府正在採取緊急行動來處理一次住房危機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The fighting which takes place in a war can be referred to as <b>action</b>. (軍事) 行動","examples":["Our leaders have generally supported military action if it proves necessary. 我們的領導者們一般都支援必要軍事行動的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>action</b> is something that you do on a particular occasion. 行為","examples":["As always, Peter had a reason for his action. 如往常一樣，彼得對他的行為總有理由。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To take legal <b>action</b> or to bring a legal <b>action</b> against someone means to bring a case against them in a court of law. 訴訟","examples":["Two leading law firms are to prepare legal actions against tobacco companies. 兩大律師事務所準備對菸草公司提起法律訴訟。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>action</b> movie is a film in which a lot of dangerous and exciting things happen. An <b>action</b> hero is the main character in one of these films. 動作 (影片、演員)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>action</b> something that needs to be done, you deal with it. 處理","examples":["Documents can be actioned, or filed immediately. 這些檔案可以立即得到處理或被存檔。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>out of action</b>, they are injured or damaged and cannot work or be used. (人) 無法工作; (物體) 無法使用","examples":["He's been out of action for 16 months with a serious knee injury. 他因嚴重的膝傷已經16個月不能活動了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone wants to have <b>a piece of the action</b> or <b>a slice of the action</b>, they want to take part in an exciting activity or situation, usually in order to make money or become more important. 插手","examples":["In the late 1990s, investors big and small wanted a piece of the dot.com action. 在20世紀90年代末，投資者們無論大小都想在網路概念股中插一手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> an idea or policy <b>into action</b>, you begin to use it or cause it to operate. 將…付諸行動","examples":["They have excelled in learning the lessons of business management theory, and putting them into action. 他們在學習商業管理理論並將其付諸實踐方面表現優異。"]}]}]},"airmail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"航空郵件，航空信；航空郵遞，航空郵政，空郵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用航空郵寄，空郵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Airmail</b> is the system of sending letters, parcels, and goods by air. 航空郵遞","examples":["...an airmail letter. …一封航空信。"]}]}]},"act":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"行動；舉動，表現；假裝；表演，演出；擔任；起作用；代理；（心理分析）行為表現"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為，行動；法案；裝模作樣；（戲劇、歌劇等的）一幕；一段表演；節目；表演者，演出團體；發現某人正在（做某事）；判決書；<舊>會議記錄，公報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>act</b>, you do something for a particular purpose. 行動","examples":["The deaths occurred when police acted to stop widespread looting and vandalism. 當警方行動起來去制止大範圍的洗劫和蓄意破壞時，死亡事件發生了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>act on</b> advice or information, you do what has been advised or suggested. (按照建議或資訊) 行動","examples":["A patient will usually listen to the doctor's advice and act on it. 病人通常會聽從醫生的建議並且按照它行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>acts</b> in a particular way, they behave in that way. 表現","examples":["...a gang of youths who were acting suspiciously. …一幫表現可疑的年輕人。","He acted as if he hadn't heard any of it. 他表現得好像一點都沒有聽過這件事一樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>acts as</b> a particular thing, they have that role or function. 擔任","examples":["Among his other duties, he acted both as the ship's surgeon and as chaplain for the men. 另外，他兼任船上的外科醫生以及船員們的牧師。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>acts</b> in a particular way, they pretend to be something that they are not. 假裝","examples":["Chris acted astonished as he examined the note. 在克里斯檢查這張便條時，他假裝很吃驚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When professionals such as lawyers <b>act for</b> you, or <b>act on</b> your <b>behalf</b>, they are employed by you to deal with a particular matter. 代理","examples":["Daniel Webster acted for Boston traders while still practising in New Hampshire. 丹尼爾·韋伯斯特還在新罕布什爾州實習時，就為波斯頓的商人們代理過。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a force or substance <b>acts on</b> someone or something, it has a certain effect on them. 作用 (於)","examples":["He's taking a dangerous drug: it acts very fast on the central nervous system. 他在使用一種危險的藥物——這種藥物很快作用於中樞神經系統。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>act</b> in a play or film, you have a part in it. 表演","examples":["She confessed to her parents her desire to act. 她向父母承認了她想表演的慾望。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>act</b> is a single thing that someone does. 行為","examples":["Language interpretation is the whole point of the act of reading. 語言詮釋是閱讀行為的全部意義。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>Act</b> is a law passed by the government. 法案","examples":["...an Act of Congress. …一項議會法案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>act</b> in a play, opera, or ballet is one of the main parts into which it is divided. 幕","examples":["Act II contained one of the funniest scenes I have ever witnessed. 第二幕包含了我所看過的最為可笑的場景之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>act</b> in a show is a short performance which is one of several in the show. 節目","examples":["This year numerous bands are playing, as well as comedy acts. 今年有許多樂隊在表演，也有喜劇節目。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone's behaviour is an <b>act</b>, you mean that it does not express their real feelings. 裝樣子","examples":["His anger was real. It wasn't an act. 他的生氣是真的，不是裝樣子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> someone <b>in the act</b>, you discover them doing something wrong or committing a crime. 逮個正著","examples":["The men were caught in the act of digging up buried explosives. 這些人在挖掩埋起來的炸藥時被逮了個正著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone who has been behaving badly <b>cleans up</b> their <b>act</b>, they start to behave in a more acceptable or responsible way. 檢點 (某人的) 行為","examples":["The nation's advertisers need to clean up their act. 該國的廣告商們需要檢點他們的行為。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get in on the act</b>, you take part in or take advantage of something that was started by someone else. 插手其中","examples":["In the 1970s Kodak, anxious to get in on the act, launched its own instant camera. 在20世紀70年代，急於插手其中的柯達公司推出了自己的即時成像照相機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that someone was <b>in the act of</b> doing something to indicate what they were doing when they were seen or interrupted. 在 (做某事的) 行動中","examples":["Ken was in the act of paying his bill when Neil came up behind him. 當尼爾走到他身後時，肯正在付賬單。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> your <b>act together</b>, you organize your life or your affairs so that you are able to achieve what you want or to deal with something effectively. 有條理地安排 (生活或事務)","examples":["The government should get its act together. 政府應該有條理地安排其事務。"]}]}]},"adult":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成年人或動物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"成年的，發育成熟的；成人的，理智的；（電影、雜誌等）僅限於成人的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>像成年人一樣表現；<非正式>變成熟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adult</b> is a mature, fully developed person. An adult has reached the age when they are legally responsible for their actions. 成年人","examples":["Becoming a father signified that he was now an adult. 成為一名父親意味著他現在是一個成年人了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>adult</b> is a fully developed animal. 成年動物","examples":["...a pair of adult birds. …一對成鳥。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Adult</b> means relating to the time when you are an adult, or typical of adult people. 成年人的","examples":["I've lived most of my adult life in Arizona. 我已在亞利桑那州度過了我大部分的成年生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe things such as films or books as <b>adult</b> when they deal with sex in a very clear and open way. (電影、書籍等) 只適合成人的","examples":["...an adult film. …一部成人電影。"]}]}]},"afternoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"午後，下午"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式>下午好（問候用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>afternoon</b> is the part of each day that begins at lunchtime and ends at about six o'clock. 下午","examples":["He's arriving in the afternoon. 他將於下午到達。","He had stayed in his room all afternoon. 他整個下午都呆在他的房間裡。"]}]}]},"agreement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"協議，協定，契約；共識；應允，同意；（在數、性或人稱方面的）一致"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>agreement</b> is a formal decision about future action that is made by two or more countries, groups, or people. 協議","examples":["It looks as though a compromise agreement has now been reached. 看起來好像現在已經達成了一個妥協協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Agreement</b> <b>on</b> something is a joint decision that a particular course of action should be taken. 共識","examples":["A spokesman said, however, that the two men had not reached agreement on the issues discussed. 但是，一位發言人說這兩個人對討論的問題還未達成共識。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Agreement</b> with someone means having the same opinion as they have. 同意","examples":["The judge kept nodding in agreement. 法官不斷點頭表示同意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Agreement</b> to a course of action means allowing it to happen or giving it your approval. 許可","examples":["The clinic doctor will then write to your doctor to get his agreement. 臨床醫生會給你的大夫寫信取得他的許可。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in agreement</b> <b>with</b> someone, you have the same opinion as they have. 意見相同","examples":[]}]}]},"airplane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>飛機"}],"sections":[]},"airport":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機場，航空站 （港）；空旅通俗讀物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>airport</b> is a place where aircraft land and take off, and that has buildings and facilities for passengers. 飛機場","examples":["...Heathrow Airport, the busiest international airport in the world. …希斯羅飛機場——世界上最繁忙的國際機場。"]}]}]},"air":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大氣，空氣；空中，天空；乘坐飛機，航空；神態，氛圍；曲調，旋律；裝腔作勢，做作；空氣媒質；氣，風"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使公開，宣揚；（使）通風；（使）晾乾，（使）烘乾；播送，播放；<古>出去透氣；<古>炫耀，誇示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Air</b> is the mixture of gases that forms the Earth's atmosphere and that we breathe. 空氣","examples":["Draughts help to circulate air. 通風有助於迴圈空氣。","Keith opened the window and leaned out into the cold air. 基斯開啟窗戶，探出身到冷風中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Air</b> is used to refer to travel in aircraft. 空運","examples":["Air travel will continue to grow at about 6% per year. 乘飛機旅行的人數將以每年大約6%的速度持續增加。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>air</b> is the space around things or above the ground. 空中","examples":["Government troops broke up the protest by firing their guns in the air. 政府軍透過朝天鳴槍驅散了這場抗議示威。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"播放","examples":["...the airing of a new television commercial that attacked the president's war record. …一個對總統的戰爭記錄進行攻擊的新電視廣告片的播放。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a broadcasting company <b>airs</b> a television or radio programme, they show it on television or broadcast it on the radio. 播放","examples":["Tonight PBS will air a documentary called \"Democracy In Action\". 今晚PBS電臺將播放一部名為《民主進行時》的紀錄片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>air</b> a room or building, you let fresh air into it. 使通風","examples":["One day a week her mother cleaned and aired each room. 每週一天，她的母親給每一個房間進行清掃並通風。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something to <b>clear the air</b>, you do it in order to resolve any problems or disagreements that there might be. 澄清視聽","examples":["...an inquiry just to clear the air and settle the facts of the case. …一個只是澄清視聽並確認事實的調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>in the air</b> it is felt to be present, but it is not talked about. 可感覺到 (但不說出來)","examples":["There was great excitement in the air. 人人都感到了無比的激動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>on the air</b>, they are broadcasting on radio or television. If a programme is <b>on the air</b>, it is being broadcast on radio or television. If it is <b>off the air</b>, it is not being broadcast. (人) 播報; (節目) 播放","examples":["We go on the air, live, at 11:30 a.m. 我們上午11:30進行現場直播。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something disappears <b>into thin air</b>, they disappear completely. If someone or something appears <b>out of thin air</b>, they appear suddenly and mysteriously. 完全消失/突然神秘出現","examples":["He had materialized out of thin air; I had not seen or heard him coming. 他突然神秘地出現了；我既沒看到也沒聽到他進來。"]}]}]},"ant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螞蟻；Ant（人名，土耳其、芬蘭人名譯作“安特”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ants</b> are small crawling insects that live in large groups. 螞蟻","examples":["Ants swarmed up out of the ground and covered her shoes and legs. 螞蟻從地裡成群地爬出來，爬滿了她的鞋和腿。"]}]}]},"anger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憤怒，怒火"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使生氣，激怒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anger</b> is the strong emotion that you feel when you think that someone has behaved in an unfair, cruel, or unacceptable way. 憤怒","examples":["He cried with anger and frustration. 他憤怒而沮喪地哭了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>angers</b> you, it makes you feel angry. 使氣憤","examples":["The decision to allow more offshore oil drilling angered some Californians. 這個允許更多海底石油鑽探的決定激怒了一些加利福尼亞人。"]}]}]},"age":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"年齡，年紀；壽命，（物的）年代；法定年齡；時代，時期；年齡段；<非正式>很長時間；成長，年老，陳年；（地質）代"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"變老，老化；（使）顯老，（使）蒼老；（使）變陳，（使）成熟；<英>推算年齡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>age</b> is the number of years that you have lived. (人的) 年齡","examples":["She has a nephew who is just ten years of age. 她有個才滿10歲的侄子。","At the age of sixteen he qualified for a place at the University of North Carolina. 16歲時他取得了北卡羅來納大學的入學資格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>age</b> of a thing is the number of years since it was made. (物的) 年代","examples":["Everything in the room looks in keeping with the age of the building. 該房間裡的一切看起來都和該樓的年代相符。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Age</b> is the state of being old or the process of becoming older. 年長; 成長","examples":["Perhaps he has grown wiser with age. 或許他已經隨著年齡的增長變得更睿智了。","This cologne, like wine, improves with age. 這種科隆香水像葡萄酒一樣越陳越香。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>age</b> is a period in history. 時代","examples":["...the age of steam and steel. …蒸汽與鋼鐵時代。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say <b>an age</b> or <b>ages</b> to mean a very long time. 很長時間","examples":["He waited what seemed an age. 他等了似乎很長時間。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>ages</b>, or when something <b>ages</b> them, they seem much older and less strong or less alert. 使顯老; 顯老","examples":["He had always looked so young, but he seemed to have aged in the last few months. 他曾一直顯得很年輕，但是在過去的幾個月裡他似乎顯得老了。"]}]}]},"ape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"猿，類人猿；粗野的人，蠢人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"模仿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Apes</b> are chimpanzees, gorillas, and other animals in the same family. 猿","examples":["...chimpanzees and other apes. …黑猩猩和其他猿。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ape</b> someone's speech or behaviour, you imitate it. 模仿","examples":["Modelling yourself on someone you admire is not the same as aping all they say or do. 以你仰慕的某個人為榜樣並不等於模仿他們的全部言行。"]}]}]},"apple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蘋果；蘋果樹；蘋果公司（Apple Inc.）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apple</b> is a round fruit with smooth red, yellow, or green skin and firm white flesh. 蘋果","examples":["I want an apple. 我要一個蘋果。","...his ongoing search for the finest varieties of apple. …他對最佳品種蘋果的不斷尋找。"]}]}]},"animal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動物；獸類；<非正式>衣冠禽獸，畜牲；某一類人或物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"動物的；肉體的，肉慾的；取自動物的；（胚胎）動物極的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>animal</b> is a living creature such as a dog, lion, or rabbit, rather than a bird, fish, insect, or human being. 動物 (不包括鳥類、魚類、昆蟲和人類)","examples":["He was attacked by wild animals. 他被野獸襲擊了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Any living creature other than a human being can be referred to as an <b>animal</b>. 獸類; 動物 (不包括人類)","examples":["Language is something that fundamentally distinguishes humans from animals. 語言是從根本上把人類與動物區分開的事物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Any living creature, including a human being, can be referred to as an <b>animal</b>. (包括人類在內的) 動物","examples":["Watch any young human being, or any other young animal. 觀察任意一個年少的人，或者任意其他幼小的動物。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Animal</b> products come from animals rather than from plants. 動物的","examples":["...food high in animal fats such as red meat and dairy products. …富含動物脂肪的食物，如紅色肉類和奶製品。"]}]}]},"april":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"四月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>April</b> is the fourth month of the year in the Western calendar. 4月","examples":["The changes will be introduced in April. 這些變更將於4月實施。"]}]}]},"august":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"威嚴的，令人敬畏的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"八月（August）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>august</b> is dignified and impressive. 莊嚴的","examples":["...that august body, the United States Senate. …那莊嚴的團體，美國參議院。"]}]}]},"aunty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>姑媽，伯母，舅媽（同 auntie）；阿姨，大嬸（對年長女性的稱呼，常與人名連用）"}],"sections":[]},"army":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陸軍，軍隊；大批，大群"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>army</b> is a large organized group of people who are armed and trained to fight on land in a war. Most armies are organized and controlled by governments. 陸軍","examples":["Perkins joined the Army in 1990. 珀金斯於1990年加入了陸軍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>army</b> <b>of</b> people, animals, or things is a large number of them, especially when they are regarded as a force of some kind. 大群","examples":["...data collected by an army of volunteers. …由一大群志願者蒐集的資料。"]}]}]},"answer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"回答，答覆；回覆；接電話；應門；答（題）；回應，反擊；滿足，適合；與……相符，相配；解決（問題）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"回答，答覆；答案；解決辦法；回信，回函；接聽，應門；相當的人，對應物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>answer</b> someone who has asked you something, you say something back to them. (口頭) 回答","examples":["Just answer the question. 只回答這個問題。","He paused before answering. 他在回答前停了下來。","Williams answered that he had no specific proposals yet. 威廉斯回答說他還沒有具體的提議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>answer</b> a letter or advertisement, you write to the person who wrote it. 回覆","examples":["Did he answer your letter? 他回覆你的信了嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>answer</b> the telephone, you pick it up when it rings. When you <b>answer</b> the door, you open it when you hear a knock or the bell. 應答","examples":["She answered her phone on the first ring. 她在響第一聲鈴時就接了電話。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>answer</b> a question in a test or quiz, you write or say something in an attempt to give the facts that are asked for. (書面) 回答","examples":["Always read an exam all the way through at least once before you start to answer any questions. 在開始回答任何問題之前總是把試卷從頭到尾讀至少一遍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>answers</b> a particular description or <b>answers to</b> it, they have the characteristics described. 符合","examples":["Two men answering the description of the suspects tried to enter Switzerland. 符合嫌疑犯特徵的兩個男人試圖進入瑞士。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Answer</b> is also a noun. 應答","examples":["I knocked at the front door and there was no answer. 我敲了前門，沒有應答。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>answer</b> is something that you say when you answer someone. 回答","examples":["Without waiting for an answer, he turned and went in through the door. 他沒有等候應答，轉身進了門。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>answer</b> is a letter that you write to someone who has written to you. 回信","examples":["I wrote to him but I never had an answer back. 我給他寫了信，但是我從未收到回信。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>answer</b> <b>to</b> a problem is a solution to it. 解決方法","examples":["There are no easy answers to the problems facing the economy. 經濟所面臨的問題沒有簡單的解決方法。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone's <b>answer</b> <b>to</b> a question in a test or quiz is what they write or say in an attempt to give the facts that are asked for. The <b>answer</b> <b>to</b> a question is the fact that was asked for. 解答","examples":["Simply marking an answer wrong will not help the student to get future examples correct. 只將某個解答判為錯誤不會幫助學生答對以後的例題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Your <b>answer</b> <b>to</b> something that someone has said or done is what you say or do in response to it or in defence of yourself. 回應","examples":["In answer to speculation that she wouldn't finish the race, she boldly declared her intention of winning it. 作為對她不會完成賽程的推測的回應，她大膽地宣佈了她獲勝的意圖。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone will not <b>take no for an answer</b>, you mean that they go on trying to make you agree to something even after you have refused. 不答應不罷休","examples":["She is tough, unwilling to take no for an answer. 她很難對付，不答應不肯罷休。"]}]}]},"auntie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>伯母，阿姨，姑媽，姨媽，舅媽（同 aunt；亦作 aunty；亦用作親暱稱呼）；（Auntie）<英，非正式>“大嬸”（對英國廣播公司的謔稱）；（Auntie）<澳，非正式>“大嬸”（對澳大利亞廣播公司的謔稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>auntie</b> is their aunt. 姨媽; 舅媽; 姑姑; 伯母; 嬸孃","examples":["His uncle is dead, but his auntie still lives here. 他舅舅死了，但他舅媽還住在這兒。"]}]}]},"aunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"姑媽，伯母，舅媽等（指父親或母親的姐妹，或伯父、叔父、舅父等的妻子；也可放在名字前作稱呼）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>aunt</b> is the sister of their mother or father, or the wife of their uncle. 姨母; 舅母; 姑母; 伯母; 嬸母","examples":["She wrote to her aunt in Alabama. 她給在阿拉巴馬州的姑母寫了信。"]}]}]},"area":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地區，區域；場地，地方；領域；面積；部位；罰球區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>area</b> is a particular part of a town, a country, a region, or the world. 地區","examples":["...the large number of community groups in the area. …該地區大量的社團。","The survey was carried out in both urban and rural areas. 該調查在城市和鄉村地區都開展了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>area</b> is the part of a town, country, or region where you live. An organization's <b>area</b> is the part of a town, country, or region that it is responsible for. 居住區域; 管轄區域","examples":["Local authorities have been responsible for the running of schools in their areas. 地方政府一直負責其轄區內各校的運作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular <b>area</b> is a piece of land or part of a building that is used for a particular activity. (作某用途的) 區域","examples":["...a picnic area. …一個野餐區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>area</b> is a particular place on a surface or object, for example, on your body. 部位","examples":["You will notice that your baby has two soft areas on the top of his head. 你會注意到你孩子的頭頂有兩個柔軟的部位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>area</b> to refer to a particular subject or topic, or to a particular part of a larger, more general situation or activity. 話題; 方面","examples":["...the politically sensitive area of social security. …社保這個政治敏感話題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>area</b> of a surface such as a piece of land is the amount of flat space or ground that it covers, measured in square units. 面積","examples":["The islands cover a total area of 400 square miles. 這些島嶼的總面積為400平方英里。"]}]}]},"art":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美術，藝術；藝術品；技術，技巧；人文學科；藝術活動（the arts）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"藝術性的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>be 的第二人稱單數現在式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Art</b> consists of paintings, sculpture, and other pictures or objects that are created for people to look at and admire or think deeply about. 藝術品","examples":["...the first exhibition of such art in the West. …這種藝術品在西方的初次展出。","...contemporary and modern American art. …美國當代與現代的藝術品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Art</b> is the activity or educational subject that consists of creating paintings, sculptures, and other pictures or objects for people to look at and admire or think deeply about. 藝術","examples":["...a painter, content to be left alone with her all-absorbing art. …一個樂於獨自沉浸在她的迷人藝術中的畫家。","...Savannah College of Art and Design. …薩瓦納藝術設計學院。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>arts</b> are activities such as music, painting, literature, film, and dance, which people can take part in for enjoyment, or to create works that express certain meanings or ideas of beauty. 藝術活動","examples":["Catherine the Great was a patron of the arts and sciences. 葉卡捷琳娜大帝是藝術和科學活動的贊助人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"At a university or college, <b>arts</b> are subjects such as history, literature, or languages in contrast to scientific subjects. 人文學科","examples":["...arts and social science graduates. …人文與社會科學的畢業生們。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe an activity as an <b>art</b>, you mean that it requires skill and that people learn to do it by instinct or experience, rather than by learning facts or rules. 技藝","examples":["...pioneers who transformed clinical medicine from an art to a science. …把臨床醫學從技藝轉化成科學的先驅們。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Arts</b> or <b>art</b> is used to describe theatres that show plays or films that are intended to make the audience think deeply about the content, and not simply to entertain them. 藝術性的","examples":["...a lower Manhattan art theatre. …下曼哈頓區的一座藝術劇院。"]}]}]},"autumn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"秋天，秋季；晚年，漸衰期；秋（從秋分到冬至）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"秋天的，秋季的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Autumn</b> is the season between summer and winter when the weather becomes cooler and the leaves fall off the trees. 秋天","examples":["He was elected judge in the autumn of 1991. 他於1991年秋被選為法官。"]}]}]},"all":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"全部；每一個；極度，儘量；無論什麼，任何；唯一，僅僅"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全部的；每一個的；任何的；儘可能多的；全然是……的，完全表現出……的；（某一體徵）顯著突出的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地；各方，各選手；非常，太"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"所有，全部；唯一"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"全部，所有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> to indicate that you are referring to the whole of a particular group or thing or to everyone or everything of a particular kind. 所有的","examples":["...the restaurant that Hugh and all his friends go to. …休和他所有的朋友們去的那家飯館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also a predeterminer. 整個","examples":["She's worked all her life. 她已經工作了一輩子。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also a determiner. 所有的","examples":["There is built-in storage space in all bedrooms. 所有臥室裡都有內建儲藏空間。","He was passionate about all literature. 他對所有文學作品都有熱情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> to refer to the whole of a particular period of time. 整個","examples":["George had to cut grass all afternoon. 喬治不得不整個下午都割草。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> in expressions such as <b>in all sincerity</b> and <b>in all probability</b> to emphasize that you are being sincere or that something is very likely. 完全 (用來強調)","examples":["In all fairness he had to admit that she was neither dishonest nor lazy. 公正地說，他不得不承認她既非不誠實也非懶惰。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also a quantifier. 全部的","examples":["He was told to pack up all of his letters and personal belongings. 他被告知整理好他的全部信件和個人物品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also a quantifier. 整個","examples":["He spent all of that afternoon polishing the silver. 他花了那整個一下午擦銀器。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also a pronoun. 全部","examples":["The only salon produces its own shampoos and hair-care products, all based on herbal recipes. 這惟一的髮廊全部使用草本配方生產自己的洗髮水和護髮用品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> to refer to a situation or to life in general. 一切","examples":["All is silent on the island now. 現在這個島上一片寂靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> at the beginning of a clause when you are emphasizing that something is the only thing that is important. 只是 (用在從句句首，表示強調)","examples":["He said all that remained was to agree to a time and venue. 他說剩下的只是同意一個時間和地點。","All you ever want to do is going shopping! 你想做的事情就是購物！"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"強調代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All</b> is also an emphasizing pronoun. 全都","examples":["Milk, oily fish and eggs all contain vitamin D. 牛奶、油性魚類和雞蛋全都含維他命D。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> in expressions such as <b>seen it all</b> and <b>done it all</b> to emphasize that someone has had a lot of experience of something. 全都","examples":["They've seen it all, so it takes a lot to rattle them. 他們已經全都見識過了，所以要費很大的勁兒才能讓他們感到緊張。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All but</b> a particular person or thing means everyone or everything except that person or thing. 除了…都","examples":["The general was an unattractive man to all but his most ardent admirers. 除了他的那些最熱切的仰慕者以外，這位將軍對於其他人並無吸引力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>all but</b> to say that something is almost the case. 差不多","examples":["The concrete wall that used to divide this city has now all but gone. 這堵曾經被用來分隔這座城市的水泥牆現在差不多不存在了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>In all</b> means in total. 總共","examples":["There was evidence that thirteen people in all had taken part in planning the murder. 有證據表明總共有13個人參與策劃了這起謀殺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>all in all</b> to introduce a summary or general statement. 總之","examples":["We both thought that all in all it might not be a bad idea. 我們倆都認為總的來說這可能不是個壞主意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>above all</b> to indicate that the thing you are mentioning is the most important point. 首先","examples":["Above all, chairs should be comfortable. 首先椅子應該舒適。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>and all</b> when you want to emphasize that what you are talking about includes the thing mentioned, especially when this is surprising or unusual. 等等","examples":["He dropped his hot dog on the pavement and someone's dog ate it, mustard and all. 他把熱狗掉在了街上，然後不知誰的狗給吃了，連帶芥末全都吃了個精光。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>at all</b> at the end of a clause to give emphasis in negative statements, conditional clauses, and questions. 根本","examples":["Robin never really liked him at all. 羅賓根本從來沒有真正喜歡過他。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>for all</b> in phrases such as <b>for all I know</b>, and <b>for all he cares</b>, to emphasize that you do not know something or that someone does not care about something. 強調對某事不瞭解、不在乎、無所謂","examples":["For all we know, he may not even be in this country. 說不準，他或許都已不在這個國家了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>of all</b> to emphasize the words \"first\" or \"last,\" or a superlative adjective or adverb. 用來強調(first)、(last)，或者最高階形容詞或副詞","examples":["First of all, answer these questions. 首先，回答這些問題。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>of all</b> in expressions such as <b>of all people</b> or <b>of all things</b> when you want to emphasize someone or something surprising. 偏偏","examples":["One group of women, sitting on the ground, was singing, of all things, \"Greensleeves.\" 一群席地而坐的婦女偏偏在唱《綠袖子》。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>of all</b> in expressions like <b>of all the nerve</b> or <b>of all the luck</b> to emphasize how angry or surprised you are at what someone else has done or said. 竟然如此","examples":["Of all the lazy, indifferent, unbusinesslike attitudes to have! 竟然有如此懶惰、冷漠、不認真的態度！"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>all of</b> before a number to emphasize how small or large an amount is. 足足有","examples":["It took him all of 41 minutes to score his first goal. 用了足足有41分鐘他才進了第一個球。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>after all</b> when introducing a statement that supports or helps explain something you have just said. 畢竟","examples":["I thought you might know somebody. After all, you're the man with connections. 我想你可能認識什麼重要人物。畢竟，你交遊甚廣。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>after all</b> when you are saying that something that you thought might not be the case is in fact the case. 竟然","examples":["I came out here on the chance of finding you at home after all. 我到這兒來心想也許會在家找到你，沒想到竟然還真是。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>for all</b> to indicate that the thing mentioned does not affect or contradict the truth of what you are saying. 儘管","examples":["For all its beauty, Prague could soon lose some of the individuality that the communist years helped to preserve. 儘管布拉格美不勝收，但是它可能會很快失去在共產主義時期存留下來的一些特色。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>all that</b> in statements with negative meaning when you want to weaken the force of what you are saying. (沒) 那麼","examples":["He wasn't all that much older than we were. 他當時並不比我們大多少。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You can say <b>that's all</b> at the end of a sentence when you are explaining something and want to emphasize that nothing more happens or is the case. 就是這樣","examples":["\"Why do you want to know that?\" he demanded.—\"Just curious, that's all.\" “你為什麼想了解它？”他索問道。—“只是好奇，僅此而已。”"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>all very well</b> to suggest that you do not really approve of something or you think that it is unreasonable. 好倒是好","examples":["It is all very well to urge people to give more to charity when they have less, but is it really fair? 這樣好倒是好，敦促人們給慈善機構更多東西，當他們自己卻沒那麼多東西的時候，但是這真的公平嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> to emphasize that something is completely true, or happens everywhere or always, or on every occasion. 完全地","examples":["He loves animals and he knows all about them. 他熱愛動物，並且對動物無所不知。","He was doing it all by himself. 全都是他獨自一個人乾的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>All</b> is used in structures such as <b>all the more</b> or <b>all the better</b> to mean even more or even better than before. 更加","examples":["The living room is decorated in pale colours that make it all the more airy. 這個客廳用淺色裝飾，顯得更加清爽通風。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>all</b> when you are talking about an equal score in a game. For example, if the score is three <b>all</b>, both players or teams have three points. 打平地","examples":[]}]}]},"baby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嬰兒，嬰孩；動物幼崽；（家庭或團體中）最小的成員；幼稚的人，軟弱的人；差事，責任；寶貝，親愛的；喜歡的東西，寶貝東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……當嬰兒般對待，對……嬌生慣養；小心翼翼地操作，小心對待"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（蔬菜）幼嫩的；（幼）小的，小型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>baby</b> is a very young child, especially one that cannot yet walk or talk. 嬰兒","examples":["She used to take care of me when I was a baby. 她曾在我還是嬰兒的時候照看過我。","My wife has just had a baby. 我妻子剛生小孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>baby</b> animal is a very young animal. 幼崽","examples":["...a baby elephant. …一頭幼象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>baby</b>, you mean that they are behaving in a cowardly way or they are being too sensitive about something. 孩子氣的人","examples":["I know he's an ex-champion boxer, but he can be a big baby sometimes! He hates spiders. 我知道他是前拳擊冠軍，但有時他像個大孩子！他恨蜘蛛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people use <b>baby</b> as an affectionate way of addressing someone, especially a young woman, or referring to them. 寶貝兒 (尤用於稱呼年輕姑娘)","examples":["You have to wake up now, baby. 你現在得醒了，寶貝兒。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Baby</b> vegetables are vegetables picked when they are very small. (蔬菜) 小的","examples":["Cook the baby potatoes in their skins. 把這些小土豆連皮煮。"]}]}]},"banana":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香蕉；香蕉樹；（Banana）巴納納（姓氏）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（非正式，通常作 bananas）愚蠢的，發狂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bananas</b> are long curved fruit with yellow skins. 香蕉","examples":["...a bunch of bananas. …一串香蕉。"]}]}]},"balloon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣球；熱氣球；氣球狀對話方塊；球形大酒杯；<非正式>蠢人；分期付款中最後一筆數目特大的還款"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"激增；突然長胖；膨脹，鼓起來；乘熱氣球旅行；（球）被踢（或打）得騰空飛起；（把球）踢飛，打飛"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"像氣球般鼓起的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>balloon</b> is a small, thin, rubber bag that you blow air into so that it becomes larger and rounder or longer. Balloons are used as toys or decorations. 氣球","examples":["She popped a balloon with her fork. 她用叉子把氣球砰的一聲戳爆了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>balloon</b> is a large, strong bag filled with gas or hot air, which can carry passengers in a container that hangs underneath it. 熱氣球","examples":["They are to attempt to be the first to circle the Earth non-stop by balloon. 他們將試圖成為首批乘熱氣球不間斷環球飛行的人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>balloons</b>, it increases rapidly in amount. (數量上) 猛增","examples":["The jail's female and minority populations have both ballooned in recent years. 該監獄的女性及少數民族犯人在近幾年都猛增了。"]}]}]},"barber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"理髮師；（男子）理髮店 （the barber's）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（男子）理髮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barber</b> is a man whose job is cutting men's hair. 理髮師","examples":["My father marched me over to Otto, the local barber, to have my hair cut short. 爸爸把我拽到當地理髮師奧托跟前，讓他把我的頭髮剪短。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>barber's</b> is a shop where a barber works. 理髮店","examples":[]}]}]},"bag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"袋，包；一袋的量；大量，很多；醜婦；<舊>寬鬆的褲子；眼袋；一批，一套；愛好，品味；壘，壘包；全部獵物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……裝進袋子；搶佔，佔有；捕獲，獵殺；批評，嘲笑；進球，得分；放棄，離開；給（病人）戴上氧氣面罩；松垂，變形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bag</b> is a container made of thin paper or plastic, for example, one that is used in stores to put things in that a customer has bought. (薄紙或塑膠做的) 袋子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>bag</b> to refer to a bag and its contents, or to the contents only. (紙、塑膠) 袋; 一袋之物","examples":["...a bag of sweets. …一袋糖果。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bag</b> is a strong container with one or two handles, used to carry things in. (有手柄的結實的) 袋子","examples":["She left the hotel carrying a shopping bag. 她拎著一個購物袋離開了賓館。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>bag</b> to refer to a bag and its contents, or to the contents only. 一袋; 一袋之物","examples":["Mama came in the back door carrying two bags of groceries. 媽媽提著兩袋食品走進了後門。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>bag</b> is the same as a . 手提包","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have <b>bags</b> under your eyes, you have folds of skin there, usually because you have not had enough sleep. 眼袋","examples":["The bags under his eyes have grown darker. 他眼袋的顏色變得更深了。"]}]}]},"ball":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"球，球狀物；球類運動；踢出（或擊出、投出）的一球；舞會；腳趾球，拇指球；勇氣；彈丸；睪丸"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成球狀（或團塊）；和（女人）發生性關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ball</b> is a round or oval object that is used in games such as tennis, baseball, American football, basketball, and soccer. 球","examples":["...a golf ball. …一個高爾夫球。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a ball propelled in a particular way in a sport 運動中以特殊的式往前滾動的球","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various rudimentary games with a ball 基礎的球類運動","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>ball</b> is something or an amount of something that has a round shape. 球狀物","examples":["Thomas screwed the letter up into a ball. 托馬斯把信揉成一團。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>ball</b> <b>of</b> your foot or <b>the</b> <b>ball</b> <b>of</b> your thumb is the rounded part where your toes join your foot or where your thumb joins your hand. (腳趾與腳掌之間或大拇指與手掌之間的) 球狀部位","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>ball</b> is a large formal social event at which people dance. (正式的) 舞會","examples":["My Mama and Daddy used to have a grand Christmas ball every year. 我媽媽和爸爸以前每年都要辦一場盛大的聖誕節舞會。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ball</b> something or when it <b>balls</b>, it becomes round. 使...成球狀; 成球狀","examples":["He picked up the sheets of paper, and balled them tightly in his fists. 他撿起那幾張紙，在手裡緊緊地攥成團。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are having a ball</b>, you are having a very enjoyable time. 玩得高興","examples":["Outside the boys were sitting on the ground and, judging by the gales of laughter, they were having a ball. 男孩子們在外面席地而坐，從他們發出的陣陣笑聲來看，他們玩得很開心。"]}]}]},"band":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樂隊；一夥，一群；範圍，段；帶，箍；帶狀物，條紋；波段，頻帶；戒指"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……分級，把……分段；用帶綁紮；加彩條"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a small group of musicians who play popular music such as jazz, rock, or pop. (演奏流行音樂的) 樂隊","examples":["He was a drummer in a rock band. 他曾是一支搖滾樂隊裡的鼓手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a group of musicians who play brass and percussion instruments. (演奏管樂和打擊樂的) 樂隊","examples":["Bands played German marches. 管樂隊演奏了德國的進行曲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>band</b> <b>of</b> people is a group of people who have joined together because they share an interest or belief. (趣味相投的) 群體","examples":["Bands of government soldiers, rebels and just plain criminals have been roaming some neighbourhoods. 一群群政府士兵、叛亂分子和純屬一般的罪犯一直在一些街區裡遊蕩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a flat, narrow strip of cloth which you wear around your head or wrists, or which forms part of a piece of clothing. (指服飾) 帶子","examples":["Almost all hospitals use a wrist-band of some kind with your name and details on it. 幾乎所有醫院都使用某種腕帶，上面有你的名字和詳細資訊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a strip of something such as colour, light, land, or cloth that contrasts with the areas on either side of it. 帶狀物","examples":["...bands of natural vegetation between strips of crops. …在帶狀的莊稼之間的一行行天然植被帶。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a strip or loop of metal or other strong material which strengthens something, or which holds several things together. (用以加固或捆綁的) 箍; 帶","examples":["Surgeon Geoffrey Horne placed a metal band around the knee cap to help it knit back together. 外科醫生傑弗裡·霍恩在膝蓋骨上放了一個金屬箍以幫助其癒合。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a ring for the finger (esp in phrases such as <b>wedding band</b>, <b> band of gold</b>, etc) 戒指(如結婚戒指或金戒指等)","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>band</b> is a range of numbers or values within a system of measurement. (測量的) 範圍","examples":["For an initial service, a 10 megahertz-wide band of frequencies will be needed. 初期制動將需要10兆赫茲寬的頻帶。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to unite; assemble 聯合(起來)","examples":[]}]}]},"baseball":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棒球運動；棒球（比賽用的小硬球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Baseball</b> is a game played by two teams of nine players. Each player from one team hits a ball with a bat and then tries to run around three bases and get to home plate before the other team can get the ball back. Compare . 棒球運動","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>baseball</b> is a small hard ball which is used in the game of baseball. 棒球","examples":[]}]}]},"basketball":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"籃球；籃球運動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Basketball</b> is a game in which two teams of five players each try to score goals by throwing a large ball through a circular net fixed to a metal ring at each end of the court. 籃球運動","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>basketball</b> is a large ball which is used in the game of basketball. 籃球","examples":[]}]}]},"bank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行；儲蓄罐；庫存，庫；河岸；斜坡；雲團，霧團；一排，一組；莊家的賭本；（泥）灘，沙洲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（錢）存入銀行，把……儲存入庫；與銀行有業務往來；（飛機）傾斜飛行；使反彈；（把某物）堆積起來，聚集起來；（用煤等）封爐火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bank</b> is an institution where people or businesses can keep their money. 銀行","examples":["Students should look to see which bank offers them the service that best suits their financial needs. 學生們應該去了解哪家銀行的服務最適合他們的財務需求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bank</b> is a building where a bank offers its services. 銀行 (大樓)","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a small container used at home for keeping money 儲錢罐","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the funds held by a gaming house or a banker or dealer in some gambling games 莊家賭本","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>bank</b> to refer to a store of something. For example, a blood <b>bank</b> is a store of blood that is kept ready for use. 庫","examples":["...a national data bank of information on hospital employees. …一個有關醫院職工資訊的國家資料庫。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>banks</b> <b>of</b> a river, canal, or lake are the raised areas of ground along its edge. 岸","examples":["We pedalled north along the east bank of the river. 我們沿著這條河的東岸騎車北上。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>bank</b> of ground is a raised area of it with a flat top and one or two sloping sides. 堤","examples":["...lounging on the grassy bank. …懶洋洋地躺在長滿草的堤岸上。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>bank</b> <b>of</b> something is a long high mass of it. (指事情多成)堆","examples":["A bank of clouds had built up along the western horizon. 一堆堆的雲沿著西邊的地平線積聚起來了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>bank</b> <b>of</b> things, especially machines, switches, or dials, is a row of them, or a series of rows. (一)排 (機器、開關或儀表盤)","examples":["The typical labourer now sits in front of a bank of dials. 這個典型的勞工正在一排儀表盤面前坐著。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bank</b> <b>with</b> a particular bank, you have an account with that bank. (在某銀行)開戶","examples":["I have banked with Coutts & Co. for years. 我已經使用僱資銀行很多年了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an aircraft <b>banks</b>, one of its wings rises higher than the other, usually when it is changing direction. (飛機轉向時) 傾斜著飛行","examples":["A single-engine plane took off and banked above the motorway in front of him. 一架單引擎飛機起飛了，傾斜地飛行在他前面的高速公路上空。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cover (a fire) with ashes, fresh fuel, etc, so that it will burn slowly (用灰等)封火; 使緩慢地燃燒","examples":[]}]}]},"basket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"籃子；一籃的量；（籃球運動的）籃；投籃得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>basket</b> is a stiff container that is used for carrying or storing objects. Baskets are made from thin strips of materials such as straw, plastic, or wire woven together. 籃; 筐; 簍","examples":["...big wicker picnic baskets filled with sandwiches. …裝滿三明治的大的藤條野餐籃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>basket</b> to refer to a basket and its contents, or to the contents only. 一籃 (簍、筐); 一籃 (簍、筐) 之量","examples":["...a small basket of fruit and snacks. …一小籃水果和點心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In economics, a <b>basket</b> <b>of</b> currencies or goods is the average or total value of a number of different currencies or goods. 一籃子 (貨幣或商品)","examples":["The dollar has fallen 6.5 percent this year against a basket of currencies from its largest trading partners. 美元對其最大貿易伙伴們的一籃子貨幣今年貶值了6.5%。"]}]}]},"bar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酒吧；吧檯；小吃店；塊，棒；（金屬）條，欄杆；球門橫樑；障礙；小節；條紋，帶；功能條；律師職業；（法庭中的）圍欄，被告席；電熱棒；沙洲，暗礁；軍階槓；巴（氣壓單位）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"封，堵；阻擋，攔住；阻止，禁止；做條紋標記"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除……外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bar</b> is a place where you can buy and drink alcoholic drinks. 酒吧","examples":["...Devil's Herd, the city's most popular country and western bar. …“魔鬼群”，全城最受歡迎的西部鄉村酒吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bar</b> is a room in a hotel or other establishment where alcoholic drinks are served. (旅館等的) 酒吧間","examples":["Last night in the hotel there was some talk in the bar about drugs. 昨天晚上，在旅館的酒吧間裡有人說起毒品了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bar</b> is a counter on which alcoholic drinks are served. 吧檯","examples":["Michael was standing alone by the bar when Brian rejoined him. 布賴恩回來的時候，邁克爾正獨自站在吧檯旁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bar</b> is a long, straight, stiff piece of metal. (金屬)棒","examples":["...a brick building with bars across the ground floor windows. …底樓窗戶有鐵柵穿過的一座磚樓。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>bar</b> <b>of</b> something is a piece of it which is roughly rectangular. (長方形的) 條","examples":["What is your favourite chocolate bar? 你最喜愛的巧克力棒是什麼？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something is a <b>bar</b> <b>to</b> doing a particular thing, it prevents someone from doing it. 障礙","examples":["One of the fundamental bars to communication is the lack of a universally spoken, common language. 溝通的根本障礙之一就是缺乏一種通用的共同語言。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>bar</b> is used to refer to the profession of any kind of lawyer in the United States, or of a barrister in England. 律師職業","examples":["Less than a quarter of graduates from the law school pass the bar exam on the first try. 不到1/4的法學院畢業生能一次就透過律師考試。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"In music, a <b>bar</b> is one of the several short parts of the same length into which a piece of music is divided. (音樂的) 小節","examples":["She sat down at the piano and played a few bars of a Chopin Polonaise. 她坐在鋼琴邊彈奏了肖邦的波洛奈茲舞曲的幾個小節。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"a cgs unit of pressure equal to 10<b>6</b> dynes per square centimetre. 1 bar is equivalent to 10<b>5</b> newtons per square metre 巴(壓強單位)","examples":[]},{"num":"10.","zh":"immunity from being caught or otherwise penalized in a game (法律上或比賽中的)豁免權","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>behind bars</b>, you mean that they are in prison. 在獄中的","examples":["Fisher was behind bars last night, charged with attempted murder. 由於被指控犯有謀殺未遂罪，費希爾昨晚進了監獄。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bar</b> a door, you place something in front of it or a piece of wood or metal across it in order to prevent it from being opened. 閂 (門)","examples":["For added safety, bar the door to the kitchen. 為了更加安全，把廚房的門閂上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bar</b> someone's way, you prevent them from going somewhere or entering a place, by blocking their path. 擋 (路)","examples":["Harry moved to bar his way. 哈里挪過去擋住了他的路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is barred</b> <b>from</b> a place or <b>from</b> doing something, they are officially forbidden to go there or to do it. 禁止","examples":["Amnesty workers have been barred from the country since 1982. 自1982年以來特赦的工人被禁止進入該國。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>bar</b> when you mean \"except.\" For example, all the work <b>bar</b> the laundry means all the work except the laundry. 除…外","examples":["Bar a plateau in 1989, there has been a rise in inflation ever since the mid-1980s. 自20世紀80年代中期以來，除了1989年穩定之外，通貨膨脹一直在增長。"]}]}]},"base":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"根基，底部；基礎；基地；基礎成分；（數字進位制中的）基數；（棒球）壘；鹼，鹽基；（電晶體的）基極；詞根"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以……為基礎；把基地設在……"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"卑鄙的，下流的；低劣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>base</b> of something is its lowest edge or part. 底邊; 底部","examples":["There was a bike path running along this side of the wall, right at its base. 沿著牆的這一邊，就在牆腳下，有一條腳踏車道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>base</b> of something is the lowest part of it, where it is attached to something else. 基部","examples":["The surgeon placed catheters through the veins and arteries near the base of the head. 外科醫生把導管插入靠近大腦底部附近的血管和動脈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>base</b> of an object such as a box or vase is the lower surface of it that touches the surface it rests on. (箱或瓶等器皿的) 底部","examples":["Remove from the heat and plunge the base of the pan into a bowl of very cold water. 把烤盤從高溫中取出，把盤的底部浸泡在一盆極冷的水中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>base</b> of an object that has several sections and that rests on a surface is the lower section of it. 底座","examples":["The mattress is best on a solid bed base. 床墊最好放在結實的床座上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>base</b> is a layer of something which will have another layer added to it. 底層","examples":["Mix together the cream cheese, yoghurt and honey, and spread over the meringue base. 把乾酪、酸奶和蜂蜜拌在一起，然後塗在蛋白甜餅底層上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A position or thing that is a <b>base</b> for something is one from which that thing can be developed or achieved. 基礎","examples":["The post will give him a powerful political base from which to challenge the Kremlin. 這個職位將為他挑戰克里姆林宮提供一個有力的政治基礎。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A company's client <b>base</b> or customer <b>base</b> is the group of regular clients or customers that the company gets most of its income from. (客戶) 群","examples":["The company has been expanding its customer base using trade magazine advertising. 這家公司一直透過商業雜誌廣告來擴大客戶群。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A military <b>base</b> is a place that part of the armed forces works from. (軍事) 基地","examples":["Gunfire was heard at an army base close to the airport. 在臨近機場的一個軍事基地聽到了槍聲。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"Your <b>base</b> is the main place where you work, stay, or live. 主要 (工作、逗留或生活) 地點","examples":["For most of the spring and early summer her base was her home in Connecticut. 春天和初夏的大部分時間她的主要活動地點是她在康涅狄格州的家。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a place is a <b>base</b> for a certain activity, the activity can be carried out at that place or from that place. (活動) 大本營","examples":["The two hotels are attractive bases from which to explore southeast Tuscany. 這兩個旅館是去托斯卡納東南探險最有吸引力的大本營。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"The <b>base</b> of a substance such as paint or food is the main ingredient of it, to which other substances can be added. 主要配料","examples":["Just before cooking, drain off any excess marinade and use it as a base for a sauce. 臨烹飪前，瀝乾多餘的醃汁，用它做調味汁的主要配料。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"A <b>base</b> is a system of counting and expressing numbers. The decimal system uses base 10, and the binary system uses base 2. 基數","examples":[]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A <b>base</b> in baseball or softball is one of the places at each corner of the diamond on the field. A player who is at <b>first base</b>, <b>second base</b>, or <b>third base</b>, is standing at the first, second, or third base in a clockwise direction from home plate. (棒球或壘球中的) 壘","examples":["The first runner to reach second base in the game was John Flaherty. 比賽中首先到達二壘的跑壘員是約翰•弗萊厄蒂。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>base</b> one thing <b>on</b> another thing, the first thing develops from the second thing. 以…為基礎","examples":["He based his conclusions on the evidence given by the captured prisoners. 他根據俘虜提供的證據得出了自己的結論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to station, post, or place (a person or oneself) 安置(某人)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"以…為基礎的","examples":["Three of the new products are based on traditional herbal medicines. 新產品中有三種是根據傳統草藥研製的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Base</b> is used to describe a price or someone's income when this does not include any additional amounts. 基本的 (價格或收入)","examples":["...an increase of more than twenty percent on the base pay of a typical worker. …一個普通工人的基本工資超過20%的增長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"devoid of honour or morality; ignoble; contemptible 不道德的; 卑劣的; 可鄙的","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"of inferior quality or value 劣質的","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"debased; alloyed; counterfeit 貶值的; 混合的; 偽造的","examples":[]}]}]},"bathroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"浴室，盥洗室；<美>衛生間，廁所；（尤指成套出售的）浴室用具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bathroom</b> is a room in a house that contains a bath or shower, a sink, and sometimes a toilet. 浴室","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bathroom</b> is a room in a house or public building that contains a sink and toilet. 洗手間","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People say that they <b>are going to the bathroom</b> when they want to say that they are going to use the toilet. 去洗手間","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>goes to the bathroom</b> to mean that they get rid of waste substances from their body, especially when you want to avoid using words that you think may offend people. 去洗手間","examples":[]}]}]},"beach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海灘，海濱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（船）拖上岸；擱淺；（垂釣者）釣（魚）上岸；讓（某人）受損"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beach</b> is an area of sand or stones beside the ocean. 海灘","examples":["...a beautiful sandy beach. …一片美麗的沙灘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a boat <b>beaches</b>, or if it <b>is beached</b>, it is pulled or forced out of the water and onto land. 使上岸; 上岸","examples":["We beached the canoe, running it right up the bank. 我們把獨木舟拖上了海灘，直朝堤岸拖去。","The boat beached on a mud flat. 船在泥沼上擱淺了。"]}]}]},"bat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"球棒，球拍；蝙蝠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用球板（棒）擊球；揮打，擊走"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bat</b> is a specially shaped piece of wood that is used for hitting the ball in baseball, softball, or cricket. (棒球、壘球或板球的) 球棒","examples":["...a baseball bat. …一隻棒球棒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"batsman的縮寫","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bat</b> is a small flying animal that looks like a mouse with wings made of skin. Bats are active at night. 蝙蝠","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an irritating or eccentric woman (esp in the phrase <b>old bat</b>) 令人生厭的婦女; 古怪的婦女","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bat</b>, you have a turn at hitting the ball with a bat in baseball, softball, or cricket. (在棒球、壘球或板球運動中) 擊球","examples":["Pettitte hurt an elbow tendon while batting. 佩蒂特在擊球時傷了肘腱。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to wink or flutter (one's eyelids) 眨眼","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>right off the bat</b>, it happens immediately. 馬上","examples":["He learned right off the bat that you can't count on anything in this business. 他馬上就認識到在這件事上你不能指望任何事物。"]}]}]},"bath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"浴缸，浴盆；洗澡，沐浴；浴室；池，盆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……洗澡；洗澡，沐浴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bath</b> is the process of washing your body in a bath. 泡澡","examples":["The midwife gave him a warm bath. 助產士給他洗了個溫水澡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you have a <b>bath</b>, you sit or lie in a bath filled with water in order to wash your body. 盆浴","examples":["Have a shower instead of a bath. 別泡澡了，洗淋浴吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bath</b> is a container, usually a long rectangular one, which you fill with water and sit in while you wash your body. 浴缸","examples":["...a gigantic pink marble bath. …一個巨大的粉紅色大理石浴缸。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bath</b> or a <b>baths</b> is a public building containing a swimming pool, and sometimes other facilities that people can use to wash or have a bath. 澡堂","examples":["...a thriving town with houses, government buildings and public baths. …一個有住宅、政府辦公樓以及公共澡堂的繁榮城鎮。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>bath</b> is a container filled with a particular liquid, such as a dye or an acid, in which particular objects are placed, usually as part of a manufacturing or chemical process. (裝有液體的) 容器","examples":["...a developing photograph placed in a bath of fixer. …一張正放在一盆定影液裡顯影的照片。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bath</b> someone, especially a child, you wash them in a bath. 給…洗澡","examples":["Back home, Shirley plays with, feeds and baths the baby. 回到家裡，雪莉逗嬰兒玩，給嬰兒餵飯並洗澡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bath</b>, you have a bath. 洗盆浴","examples":["At least 60% of us now bath or shower once a day. 如今我們中至少有60%的人每天洗盆浴或沖淋浴一次。"]}]}]},"back":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"後面，後部；背部；（檔案等的）背面；（書等的）末尾；椅背，靠背；後衛；（the Backs）（背向劍河的）劍橋大學後園"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"後面的，位於後部的；偏遠的，偏僻的；到期未付的，拖欠的；早期出版的，過期的；向後的，相反的；（18穴高爾夫球場的）後9穴的；（音）後位的，舌後的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"回原處，恢復原狀；回報，回覆；向後；束起 ，收攏；與（某物）有距離，在遠處；（將鐘錶）撥回；在曾去過（或提到過）的地方；回到過去，追溯至；控制住，忍住；歸還，取回；再次，又一次"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）後退，倒退；支援，資助；下賭注於；伴奏，伴唱；給……加背襯；在……後面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move <b>back</b>, you move in the opposite direction to the one in which you are facing or in which you were moving before. 向後","examples":["She stepped back from the door expectantly. 她充滿期待地從門口往後退。","He pushed her away and she fell back on the wooden bench. 他把她推開，然後她向後跌坐在長木椅上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go <b>back</b> somewhere, you return to where you were before. 回到原處","examples":["I went back to bed. 我回到床上。","I'll be back as soon as I can. 我會盡快回來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>back</b> in a particular state, they were in that state before and are now in it again. 恢復原狀","examples":["The rail company said it expected services to get slowly back to normal. 鐵路公司稱，預計服務會慢慢恢復正常。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you give or put something <b>back</b>, you return it to the person who had it or to the place where it was before you took it. If you get or take something <b>back</b>, you then have it again after not having it for a while. (放、取) 回","examples":["She handed the knife back. 她把小刀遞了回去。","Put it back in the freezer. 把它放回到冰櫃裡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"in reply, repayment, or retaliation 回覆、償還或報復地","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you put a clock or watch <b>back</b>, you change the time shown on it so that it shows an earlier time, for example, when the time changes to standard time. (將鍾、表等撥) 回","examples":["The clocks go back at 2 o'clock tomorrow morning. 鍾明天早上往回撥到2點。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you write or call <b>back</b>, you write to or telephone someone after they have written to or telephoned you. If you look <b>back</b> at someone, you look at them after they have started looking at you. 作為回覆; 往回 (望)","examples":["They wrote back to me and told me I didn't have to do it. 他們給我回信告訴我不必做它。","If the phone rings, say you'll call back after dinner. 如果有電話，就說你晚飯後打回去。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can say that you go or come <b>back</b> <b>to</b> a particular point in a conversation to show that you are mentioning or discussing it again. 回到 (先前談論的地方)","examples":["Can I come back to the question of policing once again? 我能回過頭來再說說治安問題嗎？"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something is or comes <b>back</b>, it is fashionable again after it has been unfashionable for some time. 再度 (流行)","examples":["Short skirts are back. 短裙又流行起來了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone or something is kept or situated <b>back</b> <b>from</b> a place, they are at a distance away from it. 在一段距離之外","examples":["Keep back from the edge of the platform. 請勿靠近站臺邊緣。","I'm a few miles back from the border. 我離邊境有幾英里遠。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something is held or tied <b>back</b>, it is held or tied so that it does not hang loosely over something. 收攏地","examples":["The curtains were held back by tassels. 窗簾用流蘇紮了起來。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you lie or sit <b>back</b>, you move your body backward into a relaxed sloping or flat position, with your head and body resting on something. 後仰地; 後靠地","examples":["She lay back and stared at the ceiling. 她躺下來，盯著天花板。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you look or shout <b>back</b> at someone or something, you turn to look or shout at them when they are behind you. 回頭向後 (看或喊)","examples":["Nick looked back over his shoulder and then stopped, frowning. 尼克扭過頭朝後看，然後皺著眉頭停了下來。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>back</b> in expressions like <b>back in Chicago</b> or <b>back at the house</b> when you are giving an account, to show that you are going to start talking about what happened or was happening in the place you mention. 在 (某地)","examples":["Meanwhile, back in Everett, Marc Fulmer is busy raising money to help get the project off the ground. 此時在埃弗裡特，馬克·富爾默正忙著籌資來幫助該專案啟動。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you talk about something that happened <b>back</b> in the past or several years <b>back</b>, you are emphasizing that it happened quite a long time ago. 早在","examples":["The story starts back in 1950, when I was five. 這件事始於1950年，當時我5歲。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you think <b>back</b> <b>to</b> something that happened in the past, you remember it or try to remember it. 回 (想)","examples":["I thought back to the time in 1975 when my son was desperately ill. 我回想起1975年的時候，當時我兒子病得很重。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone moves <b>back and forth</b>, they repeatedly move in one direction and then in the opposite direction. 來回地","examples":["He paced back and forth. 他來回踱步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something was done <b>behind</b> someone's <b>back</b>, you disapprove of it because it was done without them knowing about it, in an unfair or dishonest way. 背地裡","examples":["You eat her food, enjoy her hospitality and then criticize her behind her back. 你吃她的飯菜，享受她的熱情款待，然後在背地裡卻批評她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two or more things are done <b>back to back</b>, one follows immediately after the other without any interruption. 接連相繼地","examples":["...two half-hour shows, which will be screened back to back. …將被相繼播放的兩場半小時的表演。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are wearing something <b>back to front</b>, you are wearing it with the back of it at the front of your body. If you do something <b>back to front</b>, you do it the wrong way around, starting with the part that should come last. (穿) 反; (做事) 首尾顛倒","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's or animal's <b>back</b> is the part of their body between their head and their legs that is on the opposite side to their chest and stomach. 背部","examples":["Her son was lying peacefully on his back. 她兒子正靜靜地仰面躺著。","She turned her back to the audience. 她轉過身背對著觀眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>back</b> <b>of</b> something is the side or part of it that is toward the rear or farthest from the front. The back of something is normally not used or seen as much as the front. 後面; 後部","examples":["...a room at the back of the shop. …商店後部的一個房間。","She raised her hands to the back of her neck. 她把雙手伸到後脖子上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>back</b> of a chair or sofa is the part that you lean against when you sit on it. 靠背","examples":["There was a pink sweater on the back of the chair. 在椅背上有一件粉色毛線衫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>back</b> of something such as a piece of paper or an envelope is the side that is less important. (紙、信封等的) 背面","examples":["Send your answers on the back of a postcard or sealed, empty envelope. 把你的答案寫在明信片或封好的空信封背面寄來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>back</b> of a book is the part nearest the end, where you can find the index or the notes, for example. (書的) 末尾","examples":["The index at the back of the book lists both brand and generic names. 書末尾的索引把商標名和通用名都列了出來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a mainly defensive player behind a forward 後衛","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"the position of such a player","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>out back</b> to refer to the area behind a house or other building. You also use <b>in back</b> to refer to the rear part of something, especially a car or building. (房屋等建築物的) 後面; (車、建築物等的) 後部","examples":["Dan informed her that he would be out back on the patio cleaning his shoes. 丹告訴她說，他要到後面露臺上弄乾淨他的鞋子。","...the trees in back of the building. …大樓後面的樹。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Back</b> is used to refer to the side or part of something that is toward the rear or farthest from the front. 後面的; 後部的","examples":["He opened the back door. 他開啟了後門。","Ann could remember sitting in the back seat of their car. 安能記得曾坐在他們車子的後座上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(of a road) not direct (街道)偏遠的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a building <b>backs</b> <b>onto</b> something, the back of it faces in the direction of that thing or touches the edge of that thing. (指建築物) 背朝; 背靠","examples":["He lives in a loft that backs onto Friedman's Bar. 他住在一間背朝弗裡德曼酒吧的閣樓裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>back</b> a car or other vehicle somewhere or when it <b>backs</b> somewhere, it moves backward. 倒 (車); (車) 倒退","examples":["He backed his car out of the drive. 他把車倒出車道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>back</b> a person or a course of action, you support them, for example, by voting for them or giving them money. 支援","examples":["His defence says it has found a new witness to back his claim that he is a victim of mistaken identity. 他的辯詞稱已經找到一位新的證人來證實他是弄錯了的身份的受害者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>back</b> a particular person, team, or horse in a competition, you predict that they will win, and usually you bet money that they will win. 下賭注於","examples":["She backed the Detroit Lions to beat the Chicago Bears by at least 20-10. 她下注賭底特律獅隊至少會以20-10擊敗芝加哥熊隊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a singer <b>is backed</b> <b>by</b> a band or by other singers, they provide the musical background for the singer. 為…伴奏; 為…伴唱","examples":["She chose to be backed by a classy trio of acoustic guitar, bass and congas. 她選擇了用原聲吉他、低音吉他和康茄鼓組成的經典三重奏組合為自己伴奏。"]}]}]},"beauty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美麗，漂亮；美好的事物，上品；美人，美女；魅力，吸引人之處；優點，妙處；美容品，化妝品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（產品、工作或活動）美容的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beauty</b> is the state or quality of being beautiful. 美麗","examples":["...an area of outstanding natural beauty. …一處具有非凡自然之美的地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>beauty</b> is a beautiful woman. 美人","examples":["She is known as a great beauty. 她是個眾所皆知的大美人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that something is a <b>beauty</b> when you think it is very good. 美的東西","examples":["It was the one opportunity in the game – the pass was a real beauty, but the shot was poor. 那是比賽中的一個機會–傳球的確很漂亮，但射門卻很糟。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>beauties</b> of something are its attractive qualities or features. 麗質","examples":["He was beginning to enjoy the beauties of nature. 他漸漸喜歡上了大自然的迷人之處。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a particular feature is <b>the</b> <b>beauty</b> <b>of</b> something, you mean that this feature is what makes the thing so good. 優點; 妙處","examples":["There would be no effect on animals – that's the beauty of such water-based materials. 它將不會對動物產生影響–這就是該種基於水的材料的優點所在。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beauty</b> is used to describe people, products, and activities that are concerned with making women look beautiful. 美容的","examples":["Additional beauty treatments can be booked in advance. 額外的美容專案可以提前預訂。"]}]}]},"bee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜜蜂；<美>聚會，聯誼賽；工作忙碌的人（busy bee）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bee</b> is an insect with a yellow-and-black striped body that makes a buzzing noise as it flies. Bees make honey, and can sting. 蜜蜂","examples":["A bee buzzed in the flowers. 一隻蜜蜂在花叢中嗡嗡作響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a social gathering for a specific purpose, as to carry out a communal task or hold competitions 聚會; 聯誼賽","examples":[]}]}]},"bed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"床，床鋪，床位；底部，基座；花壇，苗圃；海底，河床；岩層；（車輛的）拖斗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……固定，嵌入；與（某人）上床"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bed</b> is a piece of furniture that you lie on when you sleep. 床","examples":["We finally went to bed at about 4am. 我們最後在凌晨四點左右上了床。","By the time we got back from dinner, Nona was already in bed. 等我們吃完飯回來，諾娜已經上床了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place such as a hospital or a hotel has a particular number of <b>beds</b>, it is able to hold that number of patients or guests. (醫院、旅館等的) 床位","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bed</b> in a garden or park is an area of ground that has been specially prepared so that plants can be grown in it. 苗床","examples":["...beds of strawberries and rhubarb. …草莓與大黃的苗床。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bed</b> of shellfish or plants is an area in the sea or in a lake where a particular type of shellfish or plant is found in large quantities. (某種貝類生物或植物密集的) 地帶","examples":["The whole lake was rimmed with thick beds of reeds. 整個湖邊長滿了厚厚的蘆葦叢。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The sea <b>bed</b> or a river <b>bed</b> is the ground at the bottom of the sea or of a river. 海床; 河床","examples":["For three weeks a big operation went on to recover the wreckage from the sea bed. 一項大規模行動持續3周以從海床尋找殘骸。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>bed</b> of rock is a layer of rock that is found within a larger area of rock. (巖) 層","examples":["Between the white limestone and the greyish pink limestone is a thin bed of clay. 在白色石灰石與略帶淺灰色的粉紅色石灰石之間的是薄薄的黏土層。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a recipe or a menu says that something is served on a <b>bed</b> <b>of</b> a food such as rice or vegetables, it means it is served on a layer of that food. (米飯、菜) 底","examples":["Heat the curry thoroughly and serve it on a bed of rice. 將咖哩加熱透再澆到一層米飯上。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"On a vehicle such a truck or a pickup, the <b>bed</b> is the long, flat part at the back where goods are carried. (車輛的) 拖斗","examples":["They loaded about a ton of canned goods into the covered bed of a pickup truck. 他們將約一噸重的罐裝食品裝到了小卡車的有篷拖斗裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>go to bed</b> <b>with</b> someone means to have sex with them. 發生性關係","examples":["I went to bed with him once, just once. 我有一次、僅有一次和他上過床。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>make</b> the <b>bed</b>, you neatly arrange the sheets and covers of a bed so that it is ready to sleep in. 鋪床","examples":["He had made the bed after breakfast. 早飯後他就把床鋪好了。"]}]}]},"bicycle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"單車，腳踏車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎腳踏車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bicycle</b> is a vehicle with two wheels which you ride by sitting on it and pushing two pedals with your feet. You steer it by turning a bar that is connected to the front wheel. 腳踏車","examples":[]}]}]},"bell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鍾，鈴；鐘聲，鈴聲（the bell）；鍾狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"系鈴，裝鍾；發出響鈴（或敲鐘）般的聲音；<英，非正式> 給……打電話；呈鍾狀，成鍾狀鼓起（或張開）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bell</b> is a device that makes a ringing sound and is used to give a signal or to attract people's attention. 鈴","examples":["I had just enough time to finish eating before the bell rang and I was off to my first class. 我在鈴響前剛好有時間吃完，然後就去上第一節課了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bell</b> is a hollow metal object shaped like a cup which has a piece hanging inside it that hits the sides and makes a sound. 鍾","examples":["My brother, Nick, was born on a Sunday, when all the church bells were ringing. 我的弟弟尼克，出生在一個星期天，當時所有教堂的鐘都在鳴響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a bellowing or baying cry, esp that of a hound or a male deer in rut 吼叫聲; 吠叫聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to utter (such a cry) 發出(叫喊聲)","examples":[]}]}]},"bike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳踏車，腳踏車，單車；摩托車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>騎腳踏車（單車）；<英> 用腳踏車（或摩托車）投遞（信件，包裹）；<英>用腳踏車（或摩托車）投遞（信件，包裹）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Bike)（土、土庫、塞）比克"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bike</b> is a bicycle. 腳踏車","examples":["When you ride a bike, you exercise all of the leg muscles. 騎腳踏車時，你可以鍛鍊腿部的全部肌肉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bike</b> is a motorcycle. 摩托車","examples":["She parked her bike in the alley. 她把摩托車停在巷子裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a promiscuous woman 蕩婦","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bike</b> somewhere means to go there on a bicycle. 騎腳踏車","examples":["I biked home from the beach. 我從海灘騎腳踏車回家。"]}]}]},"birth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出生，誕生；出身，血統；開始，起源"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<北美，非正式>生，產"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a baby is born, you refer to this event as his or her <b>birth</b>. 出生","examples":["It was the birth of his grandchildren that gave him greatest pleasure. 是孫兒孫女們的降生給了他最大的歡樂。","She weighed 5lb 7oz at birth. 她出生時重5磅7盎司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the beginning or origin of something as its <b>birth</b>. 開始; 起源","examples":["...the birth of popular democracy. …人民民主的開始"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Some people talk about a person's <b>birth</b> when they are referring to the social position of the person's family. 出身","examples":["...men of low birth. …出身低微的男人們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If, for example, you are French <b>by birth</b>, you are French because your parents are French, or because you were born in France. 在血統上","examples":["Sadrudin was an Iranian by birth. 薩德魯丁在血統上是伊朗人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a woman <b>gives birth</b>, she produces a baby from her body. 分娩","examples":["She's just given birth to a baby girl. 她剛剛生下一個女嬰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>give birth to</b> something such as an idea means to cause it to start to exist. 使產生","examples":["In 1980, strikes at the Lenin shipyards gave birth to the Solidarity trade union. 1980年，列寧造船廠的罷工導致團結工會的建立。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The country, town, or village <b>of</b> your <b>birth</b> is the place where you were born. 出生地","examples":["He left the town of his birth five years later for Australia. 他5年後離開故鄉去了澳大利亞。"]}]}]},"bird":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鳥；年輕女子，姑娘；人，傢伙；飛機，飛船，衛星；供捕獵（或食用）的鳥；羽毛球；<英，非正式>監獄，服刑期（doing bird）；喝倒彩，起鬨（give sb. the bird）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bird</b> is a creature with feathers and wings. Female birds lay eggs. Most birds can fly. 鳥","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to two people as <b>birds of a feather</b>, you mean that they have the same interests or are very similar. 志趣相同的人","examples":["We're birds of a feather, you and me, Mr. Plimpton. 我們志趣相投，我和你，普林頓先生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>A bird in the hand</b> is something that you already have and do not want to risk losing by trying to get something else. 已到手的東西","examples":["Another temporary discount may not be what you want, but at least it is a bird in the hand. 再一次臨時打折可能達不到你所希望的，但至少這是已經到手的東西。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a <b>little bird</b> told you about something, you mean that someone has told you about it, but you do not want to say who it was. 訊息靈通的人","examples":["Incidentally, a little bird tells me that your birthday's coming up. 順便提一句，有個訊息靈通的人告訴我你的生日快到了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that doing something will <b>kill two birds with one stone</b>, you mean that it will enable you to achieve two things that you want to achieve, rather than just one. 一箭雙鵰","examples":["We can talk about Union Hill while I get this business over with. Kill two birds with one stone, so to speak. 我們可以談談尤寧山，同時我把這件事幹完。可以說是一舉兩得吧。"]}]}]},"beat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（反覆地）敲，擊，打；狠打，猛抽；攪拌，混合；拍動，扇動（翅膀）；（心臟）跳動，搏動；擊敗，戰勝；搶……之先，趕在……之前；避開，避免"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"敲，擊；（音樂或詩歌的）強音拍；（經常去或經過的）路線，地點；以之字形航線搶風航行"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>筋疲力盡，疲憊不堪；垮掉的一代的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>beat</b> someone or something, you hit them very hard. 用力打","examples":["My wife tried to stop them and they beat her. 我妻子試圖阻止他們，他們就猛打她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>beat</b> a drum or similar instrument, you hit it in order to make a sound. You can also say that a drum <b>beats</b>. 敲 (樂鼓等); (樂鼓等) 敲打","examples":["When you beat the drum, you feel good. 當你擊鼓時，你感覺良好。","... drums beating and pipes playing. …樂鼓在敲打，風笛在演奏。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>beat</b> eggs, cream, or butter, you mix them thoroughly using a fork or beater. 攪打 (蛋、奶油等)","examples":["Beat the eggs and sugar until they start to thicken. 將蛋和奶油攪打到開始變黏稠為止。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a bird or insect <b>beats</b> its wings or when its wings <b>beat</b>, its wings move up and down. 拍打 (翅膀); (翅膀) 連續拍動","examples":["Beating their wings they flew off. 它們拍打著翅膀飛走了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>beat</b> someone in a competition or election, you defeat them. 打敗","examples":["In yesterday's game, Switzerland beat the United States two to one. 在昨天的比賽中，瑞士以2比1擊敗了美國。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>beats</b> a record or achievement, they do better than it. 打破 (紀錄等)","examples":["He was as eager as his Captain to beat the record. 他和他的隊長一樣渴望打破紀錄。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>beat</b> something that you are fighting against, for example, an organization, a problem, or a disease, you defeat it. 戰勝","examples":["It became clear that the Union was not going to beat the government. 情形變得很清楚，工會敵不過政府。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If an attack or an attempt <b>is beaten</b> <b>off</b> or <b>is beaten</b> <b>back</b>, it is stopped, often temporarily. (常指暫時) 擊退","examples":["The rescuers were beaten back by strong winds and currents. 救助者被強風和水流擊退了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>beats</b> another, you mean that it is better than it. 好過; 勝過","examples":["Being boss of a software firm beats selling insurance. 當一家軟體公司的老闆好過賣保險。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"To <b>beat</b> a time limit or an event means to achieve something before that time or event. (在某時限前) 完成","examples":["They were trying to beat the midnight deadline. 他們正在試圖趕在午夜的最後期限前完成。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>beat</b> <b>on</b>, <b>at</b>, or <b>against</b> something means to hit it hard, usually several times or continuously for a period of time. (常指多次或連續地) 重擊","examples":["There was dead silence but for a fly beating against the glass. 若沒有一隻蒼蠅在撲打著玻璃，便是一片死寂。","Nina managed to free herself and began beating at the flames with a pillow. 尼娜設法自救，開始用一個枕頭連續地拍打著火焰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When your heart or pulse <b>beats</b>, it continually makes regular rhythmic movements. (心臟、脈搏) 跳動","examples":["I felt my heart beating faster. 我感覺心臟跳得更快了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beat</b> is also a noun. 擊打","examples":["...the rhythmic beat of the surf. …海浪有韻律的拍擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"敲打","examples":["The silence was broken only by the beating of the rain. 唯有雨的敲擊打破了寧靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Beat</b> is also a noun. 跳動","examples":["He could hear the beat of his heart. 他能聽到自己的心跳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"跳動","examples":["I could hear the beating of my heart. 我能聽到自己心臟的跳動。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Beat</b> is also a noun. 敲打","examples":["...the rhythmical beat of the drum. …樂鼓的有節奏的敲打。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>beat</b> of a piece of music is the main rhythm that it has. (音樂的) 節奏","examples":["...the thumping beat of rock music. …搖滾樂的強烈節奏。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In music, a <b>beat</b> is a unit of measurement. The number of beats in a measure of a piece of music is indicated by two numbers at the beginning of the piece. (音樂的) 節拍","examples":["It's got four beats to a measure. 1小節有4拍。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A police officer's or journalist's <b>beat</b> is the area for which he or she is responsible. (警察、記者等的) 負責區","examples":["A policeman was patrolling his regular beat, when he saw a group of boys milling about the street. 一名警察在其轄區內巡邏時發現一群男孩子在街上瞎轉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you intend to do something but someone <b>beats</b> you <b>to it</b>, they do it before you do. 搶先做","examples":["Don't be too long about it or you'll find someone has beaten you to it. 別耽擱太久，否則你會發現已經有人搶在你前面了。"]}]}]},"best":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最好的，最出色的；最愉快的，最幸福的；最合適的，最恰當的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最，最高程度地；最出色地，最高標準地；最適合地，最恰當地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最好的事物（或人）；（人或事物所能達到的）最高標準；最合乎要求的事物；（個人的）最高水平，最高紀錄；最好的衣服，盛裝；<美>（書信結尾的）良好祝願"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打敗，勝過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Best</b> is the superlative of <b>good</b>. 最好的","examples":["If you want further information the best thing to do is have a word with the driver as you get on the bus. 如果你想了解得更清楚，最好的辦法就是上公共汽車後向司機詢問。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Best</b> is the superlative of <b>well</b>. 最好地","examples":["James Fox is best known as the author of \"White Mischief,\" and he is currently working on a new book. 詹姆斯·福克斯以其作品《慾望城》最為知名，目前他正在寫一本新書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Best</b> is used to form the superlative of compound adjectives beginning with \"good\" and \"well.\" For example, the superlative of \"well-known\" is \"best-known.\" 用於構成由(good)或(well)開頭的複合詞的最高階形式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The best</b> is used to refer to things of the highest quality or standard. 最好的東西","examples":["We offer only the best to our clients. 我們只提供最好的東西給顧客。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>best</b> is the greatest effort or highest achievement or standard that they are capable of. 最佳狀態; 最大努力","examples":["Miss Blockey was at her best when she played the piano. 布洛基小姐彈鋼琴那會兒正處於最佳狀態。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>the best</b> that can be done or hoped for, you think it is the most pleasant, successful, or useful thing that can be done or hoped for. 最好的事物","examples":["A draw seems the best they can hope for. 看來平局已經是他們所能期盼的最好結局了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you like something <b>best</b> or like it <b>the best</b>, you prefer it. 最大程度地","examples":["The thing I liked best about the show was the music. 這場演出中我最喜歡的是音樂。","Mother liked it best when Daniel got money. 丹尼爾掙到錢是母親最喜歡的事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>best of all</b> to indicate that what you are about to mention is the thing that you prefer or that has most advantages out of all the things you have mentioned. 最好的是","examples":["It was comfortable and cheap: best of all, most of the rent was being paid by two American friends. 這裡又舒適又便宜，最好的是，大部分租金由兩個美國朋友付了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something <b>as best</b> they <b>can</b>, they do it as well as they can, although it is very difficult. 盡最大努力","examples":["Let's leave people to get on with their jobs and do them as best they can. 放手讓人們去開展工作並盡最大努力做好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>at best</b> to indicate that even if you describe something as favourably as possible or if it performs as well as it possibly can, it is still not very good. 充其量","examples":["This policy, they say, is at best confused and at worst non-existent. 他們說這項政策說好聽點是混亂不清，說不好聽點就是根本不存在。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> your <b>best</b> or <b>try</b> your <b>best</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try as hard as you can to do it, or do it as well as you can. 儘自己最大努力","examples":["I'll do my best to find out. 我將盡最大努力查清楚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>for the best</b>, you mean it is the most desirable or helpful thing that could have happened or could be done, considering all the circumstances. (所有因素考慮在內) 能產生的最好結果","examples":["Whatever the circumstances, parents are supposed to know what to do for the best. 不論情況如何，父母應該知道做什麼才能達到最佳效果。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that a particular person <b>knows best</b>, you mean that they have a lot of experience and should therefore be trusted to make decisions for other people. 最具權威性","examples":["He was convinced that doctors and dentists knew best. 他對醫生的權威性深信不疑。"]}]}]},"better":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較好的，更好的；能力更強的，更熟練的；（健康狀況）好轉的，康復的；更合適的，更得體的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"較好地，更好地；更，更大程度上；更妥，更恰當"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"更好的事物，較好者；更好的表現，更好的待遇；<舊>上司，比自己能力強的人；打賭者（=bettor）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"超過，勝過；改善，改進"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"更大成就，更好待遇，更好行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Better</b> is the comparative of <b>good</b>. 更好的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Better</b> is the comparative of <b>well</b>. 更好地","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Better</b> is used to form the comparative of compound adjectives beginning with \"good\" and \"well.\" For example, the comparative of \"well-off\" is \"better-off.\" 用於構成由(good)或(well)開頭的複合詞的比較級形式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you like one thing <b>better</b> <b>than</b> another, you like it more. 更大程度地","examples":["I like your interpretation better than the one I was taught. 與我所學的相比，我更喜歡你這種解釋。","They liked it better when it rained. 他們更喜歡下雨天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In spoken English, people sometimes use <b>better</b> without 'had' or `be' before it. It has the same meaning. 口語中，(had)或(be)經常省略，意思不變","examples":["Better not say too much aloud. 說話聲最好不要太大。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>better</b> after an illness or injury, you have recovered from it. If you feel <b>better</b>, you no longer feel so ill. 痊癒的","examples":["He is much better now, he's fine. 他現在病好多了，他沒什麼事了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a person who is superior, esp in social standing or ability (身份或能力)較高者","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person who bets 打賭者","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you expect or deserve <b>better</b>, you mean that you expect or deserve a higher standard of achievement, behaviour, or treatment from people than they have shown you. 更高標準 (的成就、表現、待遇等)","examples":["We expect better of you in the future. 我們期待你將來有更好的表現。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something changes <b>for the better</b>, it improves. 變好","examples":["He dreams of changing the world for the better. 他夢想將世界變得更美好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a feeling such as jealousy, curiosity, or anger <b>gets the better of</b> you, it becomes too strong for you to hide or control. 某人讓 (妒忌、好奇心、憤怒等情緒) 打敗","examples":["She didn't allow her emotions to get the better of her. 她沒有讓情緒打敗自己。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get the better of</b> someone, you defeat them in a contest, fight, or argument. 擊敗","examples":["He is used to tough defenders, and he usually gets the better of them. 他習慣了強悍的防守隊員，而且通常都能擊敗他們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>knows better</b> <b>than to</b> do something, they are old enough or experienced enough to know it is the wrong thing to do. 明事理而不至於","examples":["She knew better than to argue with Adeline. 她不會糊塗到和阿德琳爭論。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>know better</b> <b>than</b> someone, you have more information, knowledge, or experience than them. 懂得更多; 更有頭腦","examples":["He thought he knew better than I did, though he was much less experienced. 他認為他比我懂得更多，雖然他經驗遠不如我。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say \"<b>so much the better</b>\" or \"<b>all the better</b>\" to indicate that it is desirable that a particular thing is used, done, or available. 要是…就好了","examples":["The fog had come in; so much the better when it came to sneaking away. 起霧了；如果霧慢慢散去就好了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you intend to do something and then <b>think better of it</b>, you decide not to do it because you realize it would not be sensible. 重新考慮後決定不做","examples":["Alberg opened his mouth, as if to protest. But he thought better of it. 阿爾伯格張口像是要抗議，但轉念一想就放棄了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>had better</b> or <b>'d better</b> when you are advising, warning, or threatening someone, or expressing an opinion about what should happen. 最好","examples":["It's half past two. I think we had better go home. 現在兩點半了，我想我們該回家了。","You'd better run if you're going to get your ticket. 如果你要去拿你的票，最好抓緊。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>is better</b> doing one thing than another, or <b>it is better</b> doing one thing than another, to advise someone about what they should do. (做某事) 更好","examples":["Wouldn't it be better putting a time-limit on the task? 給任務定個截止期限不是更好嗎？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that someone would <b>be better off</b> doing something, you are advising them to do it or expressing the opinion that it would benefit them to do it. 最好是","examples":["If you've got bags you're better off taking a taxi. 如果你有行李，最好是坐計程車。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>That's better</b>\" in order to express your approval of what someone has said or done, or to praise or encourage them. 這樣好多了","examples":["\"I came to ask your advice – no, to ask for your help.\"—\"That's better. And how can I help you?\" “我來向你請教——不，請你幫個忙。” —“這就對了，我能為你做什麼？”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>betters</b> a high achievement or standard, they achieve something higher. 超過","examples":["His throw bettered the American junior record set in 2003. 他的這一投超越了2003年美國少年組的記錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>better</b> your situation, you improve your social status or the quality of your life. If you <b>better</b> <b>yourself</b>, you improve your social status. 改善","examples":["He had dedicated his life to bettering the lot of the oppressed people of South Africa. 他一生致力於改善南非被壓迫人民的命運。"]}]}]},"blood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"血，血液；出身，血統；成員，人員；殺戮，流血；氣質，脾氣；<舊>紈絝子弟，花花公子；血樣，血檢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使取得初次經驗；用獵物的血塗（新手的）臉；讓（獵狗）第一次嘗血"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Blood</b> is the red liquid that flows inside your body, which you can see if you cut yourself. 血液","examples":["His shirt was covered in blood. 他的襯衫沾滿了血。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>blood</b> to refer to the race or social class of someone's parents or ancestors. 血統","examples":["There was Greek blood in his veins: his ancestors originally bore the name Karajannis. 他有希臘血統——他的祖先原來姓卡拉揚尼斯。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>bad blood</b> <b>between</b> people, you mean that they have argued about something and dislike each other. 積怨","examples":["There is, it seems, some bad blood between Mills and the Baldwins. 米爾和鮑德溫兩家看上去好像有積怨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something violent and cruel is done <b>in cold blood</b>, it is done deliberately and in an unemotional way. 殘忍蓄意地","examples":["The crime had been committed in cold blood. 這起案件是蓄意犯罪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has a person's <b>blood on</b> their <b>hands</b>, you mean that they are responsible for that person's death. 應對某人的死亡負責","examples":["He has my son's blood on his hands. I hope it haunts him for the rest of his days. 他應該對我兒子的死負責，但願他終生不得安寧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a quality or talent is <b>in</b> your <b>blood</b>, it is part of your nature, and other members of your family have it too. 天生遺傳的","examples":["Diplomacy was in his blood: his ancestors had been feudal lords. 他的外交能力是天生的：他的祖上曾是封建王侯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use the expressions <b>new blood</b>, <b>fresh blood</b>, or <b>young blood</b> to refer to people who are brought into an organization to improve it by thinking of new ideas or new ways of doing things. 新生力量","examples":["There's been a major reshuffle of the cabinet to bring in new blood. 內閣進行了重大改組以吸納新生力量。"]}]}]},"bit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小片，小塊；小部分，片段；（一組東西中的）一個；<美>喜劇小品，小笑話；位元；輔幣，12.5美分；馬嚼子；鑽頭；<非正式>（與某活動、過程有關的）所有事情；<非正式>女孩，姑娘；<英，非正式>（人的）生殖器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很小的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"制約，限制；給（馬）上嚼子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"咬，咬傷；叮，蜇（bite 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A bit</b> <b>of</b> something is a small amount of it. 一點兒","examples":["All it required was a bit of work. 它所需要的只是少量工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A bit</b> means to a small extent or degree. It is sometimes used to make a statement less extreme. 有點兒","examples":["This girl was a bit strange. 這個女孩有點兒古怪。","I think people feel a bit more confident. 我認為人們感覺更自信一點兒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>a bit of</b> to make a statement less forceful. For example, the statement \"It's a bit of a nuisance\" is less forceful than \"It's a nuisance.\" 有點兒 (用於使陳述不那麼強烈)","examples":["It's all a bit of a mess. 它整個有點兒亂。","Students have always been portrayed as a bit of a joke. 學生們總是被描述得有些荒唐可笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Quite a bit</b> means quite a lot. 相當多","examples":["They're worth quite a bit of money. 它們值很多錢。","Things have changed quite a bit. 情況大有改觀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>a bit</b> before \"more\" or \"less\" to mean a small amount more or a small amount less. (多或少) 一點兒","examples":["I still think I have a bit more to offer. 我仍然認為我可以多提供一點兒。","Maybe we'll hear a little bit less noise. 也許我們聽見的噪音會少一點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>a bit</b> or do something <b>for a bit</b>, you do it for a short time. 一會兒","examples":["Let's wait a bit. 我們稍等片刻。","I hope there will be time to talk a bit—or at least ask you about one or two things this evening. 我希望今晚能有時間和你談一會兒，—或者至少能問你一兩件事兒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something happens <b>bit by bit</b>, it happens in stages. 逐漸地","examples":["Bit by bit I began to understand what they were trying to do. 漸漸地，我開始明白了他們正在努力做什麼。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> your <b>bit</b>, you do something that, to a small or limited extent, helps to achieve something. 盡本分","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You say that one thing is <b>every bit as</b> good, interesting, or important <b>as</b> another to emphasize that the first thing is just as good, interesting, or important as the second. 同樣","examples":["My dinner jacket is every bit as good as his. 我的小禮服和他的一樣好。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a bit much</b>, you are annoyed because you think someone has behaved in an unreasonable way. 太過分","examples":["Her stage outfit of hot trousers, over-the-knee boots and a tube top was a bit much. 她在舞臺上的裝扮是熱褲、過膝長靴加緊身抹胸，太過分了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>not a bit</b> when you want to make a strong negative statement. 一點也不","examples":["I'm really not a bit surprised. 我確實毫不吃驚。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You can use <b>bits and pieces</b> to refer to a collection of different things. 零碎的東西","examples":["The drawers are full of bits and pieces of armour. 抽屜裡滿是零零碎碎的盔甲片。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bit</b> <b>of</b> something is a small part or section of it. 小部分","examples":["Only a bit of the barley remained. 只有一小部分大麥保留了下來。","Now comes the really important bit. 現在到了非常重要的一小部分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bit</b> of something is a small piece of it. 小塊兒","examples":["Only a bit of string looped round a nail in the doorpost held it shut. 僅憑一小段繞在門框釘子上的繩子將門關住。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>bit</b> to refer to a particular item or to one of a group or set of things. For example, a <b>bit</b> <b>of</b> information is an item of information. (一組東西中的) 一個","examples":["There was one bit of vital evidence which helped win the case. 有一項至關重要的證據幫助贏了這場官司。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In computing, a <b>bit</b> is the smallest unit of information that is held in a computer's memory. It is either 1 or 0. Several bits form a byte. 位元 (計算機儲存的最小資訊單位)","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>bit</b> is 12 1/2 cents; mainly used in expressions such as two <b>bits</b>, which means 25 cents, or <b>four bits</b>, which means 50 cents. 12.5美分","examples":["They weren't worth four bits. 它們不值50美分了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a metal mouthpiece, for controlling a horse on a bridle (金屬製的)馬嚼子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to put a bit in the mouth of (a horse) 給(一匹馬)上嚼子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bit</b> is the past tense of . (bite)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"black":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"黑的，黑色的；黑色人種的；不加牛奶的；髒的，佈滿汙垢的；悲傷的，無望的；憤怒的，仇恨的；罪惡的，邪惡的；（幽默）黑色的；（滑雪道）難度最大的；（軍事活動）秘密的；黑桃和梅花組牌的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"黑，黑色；<冒犯>黑人；黑色衣服；黑色的東西（尤指斯諾克中的黑球）；執黑子的一方"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變黑，弄黑；<英>抵制，拒絕（貨品或公司）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>black</b> is of the darkest colour that there is, the colour of the sky at night when there is no light at all. 黑色的","examples":["She was wearing a black coat with a white collar. 她穿著一件白領黑上衣。","He had thick black hair. 他有著濃密烏黑的頭髮。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>black</b> person belongs to a race of people with dark skins, especially a race originally from Africa. 黑色人種的","examples":["He worked for the rights of black people. 他為黑人的權利而工作。","Sherry is black, tall, slender and soft-spoken. 謝里是黑人，個頭高挑，身材苗條，說話柔聲細氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Black</b> coffee or tea has no milk or cream added to it. (咖啡、茶) 不加牛奶或奶油的","examples":["A cup of black tea or black coffee contains no calories. 一杯紅茶或黑咖啡不含任何卡路里。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>black</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very bad indeed. 糟糕的","examples":["It was, he said later, one of the blackest days of his political career. 後來他說，那一天是他政治生涯中最糟糕的日子之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is in a <b>black</b> mood, they feel very miserable and depressed. 鬱悶的","examples":["In late 1975, she fell into a black depression. 1975年末，她陷入極度消沉中。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Black people are sometimes referred to as <b>blacks</b>. This use could cause offence. 黑人","examples":["There are about thirty-one million blacks in the U.S. 美國大約有三千一百萬黑人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or an organization is <b>in the black</b>, they do not owe anyone any money. 不欠債","examples":["Remington's operations in Japan are now in the black. 雷明頓在日本的經營現在沒有赤字。"]}]}]},"bite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"咬，咬傷；叮，蜇；卡緊，咬住；產生不良影響；接受，相信；咬餌，上鉤；（酸）腐蝕；<非正式>使生氣，使煩惱；（物體）刺痛，勒痛；使傷心，使痛苦"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"咬；一口的量；咬傷，叮傷；少量吃的東西，小吃；寒冷，刺骨；濃烈的味道；影響力，感染力；吞餌，上鉤；咬合；簡短的資訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bite</b> something, you use your teeth to cut into it, for example, in order to eat it or break it. If an animal or person <b>bites</b> you, they use their teeth to hurt or injure you. 咬; 咬傷","examples":["Both sisters bit their nails as children. 這兩姐妹在孩童時都啃指甲。","He bit into his sandwich. 他咬了一口三明治。","Every year in this country more than 50,000 children are bitten by dogs. 每年這個國家有五萬多個孩子被狗咬傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a snake or a small insect <b>bites</b> you, or if it <b>bites</b>, it makes a mark or hole in your skin, and often causes the surrounding area of your skin to become painful or itchy. (蛇、蟲等) 叮咬","examples":["When an infected mosquito bites a human, spores are injected into the blood. 受感染的蚊子叮人時，孢子就被注入人體血液。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bite</b> of something, especially food, is the action of biting it. 咬","examples":["He took another bite of apple. 他又咬了一口蘋果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bite</b> of food is the amount of food you take into your mouth when you bite it. 一口的量","examples":["Look forward to eating the food and enjoy every bite. 盼望吃到那個食品並享受吃它的每一口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>a bite</b> to eat, you have a small meal or a snack. 少量吃的東西","examples":["It was time to go home for a little rest and a bite to eat. 是該回家休息一會兒，吃點東西了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bite</b> is an injury or a mark on your body where an animal, snake, or small insect has bitten you. (叮、咬的) 傷痕","examples":["Any dog bite, no matter how small, needs immediate medical attention. 任何狗咬的傷口，無論多小，都需要立即就醫。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a food or drink has <b>bite</b>, you like it because it has a strong or sharp taste. (食物、飲料等) 夠刺激的味道","examples":["The olive salad has to have bite and tang. 橄欖色拉的味道一定要夠足夠衝。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Bite</b> is also a noun. 上鉤","examples":["If I don't get a bite in a few minutes I lift the rod and twitch the bait. 如果好幾分鐘也不見魚上鉤，我就提起魚竿猛拉釣餌。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an action or policy begins to <b>bite</b>, it begins to have a serious or harmful effect. 產生嚴重影響","examples":["As the sanctions begin to bite there will be more political difficulties ahead. 隨著制裁真正開始起作用，今後將會有更多的政治困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>bites</b> into a surface, it presses hard against it or cuts into it. 咬住; 切入","examples":["There may even be some wire or nylon biting into the flesh. 甚至可能有金屬絲或尼龍勒進肉裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a fish <b>bites</b> when you are fishing, it takes the hook or bait at the end of your fishing line in its mouth. 上鉤","examples":["After half an hour, the fish stopped biting and we moved on. 過了半小時，魚不再上鉤，我們就走開了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>bites the hand that feeds</b> them, they behave badly or in an ungrateful way toward someone who they depend on. 恩將仇報","examples":["She may be cynical about the film industry, but ultimately she has no intention of biting the hand that feeds her. 她也許會對電影業冷嘲熱諷，但終究不打算恩將仇報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bite</b> your <b>lip</b> or your <b>tongue</b>, you stop yourself from saying something that you want to say, because it would be the wrong thing to say in the circumstances. 忍住不說","examples":["I must learn to bite my lip. 我必須學會不隨便說話。"]}]}]},"boat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小船；輪船"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"划船"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>boat</b> is something in which people can travel across water. 船","examples":["One of the best ways to see the area is in a small boat. 參觀這一地區的最好方式之一是乘小船。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a passenger ship as a <b>boat</b>. 客船","examples":["When the boat reached Cape Town, we said goodbye. 客船抵達開普敦後，我們就分手了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>missed the boat</b>, you mean that they have missed an opportunity and may not get another. 坐失良機","examples":["If you don't want to miss the boat, the auction is scheduled for 2:30 p.m. on June 26. 如果你不想坐失良機，拍賣會定在6月26日下午2:30。"]}]}]},"block":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大塊，一塊（木料、石頭等）；（四面臨街的）街段，街區；大樓，大廈；棟，座，幢；障礙物，阻礙；（短時間的）思維停滯，思維中斷；一組，一批，一疊；（連續的）一段時間；阻擋，攔截；積木；（古代斬首用的）墊頭木；<美>一大片土地；（物體的）平面，純色色塊；滑輪，滑輪組；區塊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻塞，堵塞（道路、管道等）；遮住（視線）；封鎖，擋住（去路）；阻撓，阻止；阻截，攔截（對方的球）；對……進行塊操作；用模具使（帽等）成形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>block</b> <b>of</b> a substance is a large rectangular piece of it. 大塊","examples":["...a block of ice. …一大塊冰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>block</b> of apartments or offices is a large building containing them. 大樓","examples":["...a white-painted apartment block. …一幢漆成白色的公寓樓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>block</b> in a town or city is an area of land with streets on all its sides, or the area or distance between such streets. 街區","examples":["He walked around the block three times. 他繞著這個街區走了3圈。","She walked four blocks down High Street. 她沿著高街走了4個街區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Blocks</b> are wooden or plastic cubes, such as those used as toys by children. 積木","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>block</b> <b>of</b> something such as tickets or shares is a large quantity of them, especially when they are all sold at the same time and are in a particular sequence or order. 一大疊 (一次大量購買的入場券、股票等)","examples":["Those booking a block of seats get them at reduced rates. 那些一次預訂大量座位的人可以享受折扣價。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have a <b>mental block</b> or a <b>block</b>, you are temporarily unable to do something that you can normally do which involves using, thinking about, or remembering something. (思維、記憶等的) 阻滯","examples":["I cannot do maths. I've got a mental block about it. 我做不了數學。我一做就大腦一片空白。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>block</b> a road, channel, or pipe means to put an object across it or in it so that nothing can pass through it or along it. 堵塞; 封鎖","examples":["Some students today blocked a main road that cuts through the centre of the city. 一些學生今天封鎖了穿過市中心的公路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>blocks</b> your view, it prevents you from seeing something because it is between you and that thing. 擋住","examples":["...a row of spruce trees that blocked his view of the long north slope of the mountain. …擋住了他看向山北長坡視線的一排雲杉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>block</b> someone's way, you prevent them from going somewhere or entering a place by standing in front of them. 阻擋","examples":["I started to move around him, but he blocked my way. 我開始繞開他走，但他擋著我的路。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>block</b> something that is being arranged, you prevent it from being done. 阻止","examples":["For years the country has tried to block imports of various cheap foreign products. 多年以來，這個國家曾試圖阻止多種外國廉價產品的進口。"]}]}]},"blue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"藍色的；憂鬱的，沮喪的；<英，非正式> 保守的，守舊的；（笑話、故事等）黃色的，色情的；（由於冷或呼吸困難）發青的，青紫的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"天藍色，藍色；天空，大海；<英>（劍橋或牛津大學的）校隊運動員，藍色榮譽者；<澳新>紅頭髮者；<澳新>錯誤，紕漏；<澳新>爭論，毆打；近生的牛排"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變成藍色；<史>用藍色漂白劑洗（白色衣服）；<英，非正式>揮霍，亂花（錢財）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>blue</b> is the colour of the sky on a sunny day. 藍色的; 天藍色的","examples":["There were swallows in the cloudless blue sky. 燕子在無雲的藍天上飛翔。","She fixed her pale blue eyes on her father's. 她用那蔚藍色的雙眼盯著父親的眼睛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The blues</b> is a type of music which was developed by African American musicians in the southern United States. It is characterized by a slow tempo and a strong rhythm. 藍調音樂","examples":["Can white girls sing the blues? 白人女孩會唱藍調嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are feeling <b>blue</b>, you are feeling sad or depressed, often when there is no particular reason. 心情低落的","examples":["There's no earthly reason for me to feel so blue. 我完全沒有理由感到如此低落。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a U.S. state is described as <b>blue</b>, it means that the majority of its residents vote for the Democratic Party in elections, especially in the presidential elections. 藍色陣營的 (美國總統大選時民主黨的主要選區)","examples":["This issue could drive an even bigger wedge between the red and blue states. 這個問題可能會進一步造成紅色選區和藍色選區之間的不和。"]}]}]},"bone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"骨，骨頭；骨質；基本結構，基本（bones）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挑刺，剔骨頭；施骨肥於；（與某人）性交；（為應付考試）臨時突擊"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，完全地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>bones</b> are the hard parts inside your body that together form your skeleton. 骨頭","examples":["Many passengers suffered broken bones. 許多乘客骨折了。","The body is made up primarily of bone, muscle, and fat. 人體主要由骨、肌肉和脂肪組成。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bone</b> a piece of meat or fish, you remove the bones from it before cooking it. 去 (肉、魚) 骨或刺","examples":["Make sure that you do not pierce the skin when boning the chicken thighs. 給雞腿去骨時，確保不要刺破皮。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bone</b> tool or ornament is made of bone. 骨制的","examples":["...a small, expensive pocketknife with a bone handle. …一把昂貴的、帶骨制刀把的小刀。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>bare bones</b> <b>of</b> something are its most basic parts or details. 基本要素","examples":["There are not even the bare bones of a garden here – I've got nothing. 這兒連花園的最基本的東西都沒有–我一無所獲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as costs are cut <b>to the bone</b>, they are reduced to the minimum possible. 減到最低","examples":["It has survived by cutting its costs to the bone. 把成本降到最低，它才撐了過來。"]}]}]},"body":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"身體，軀體；軀幹；屍體；（與靈魂或精神相對的）肉體；<舊>（尤指某種型別或性格的）人；（建築物、檔案等的）主體，主要部分；車身，機身；衣身；器身，（球拍的）拍身；團體，機構，群體；大量；物體，天體；水域；（酒的）醇度，醇厚；（頭髮的）稠密度，濃密；（婦女或嬰兒的）緊身衣褲；（製陶用語）坯體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"賦予（抽象事物）以形體，使具體化；製造（汽車）的車身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>body</b> is all your physical parts, including your head, arms, and legs. 身體","examples":["The largest organ in the body is the liver. 體內最大的器官是肝臟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can also refer to the main part of your body, except for your arms, head, and legs, as your <b>body</b>. 軀幹","examples":["Lying flat on the floor, twist your body on to one hip and cross your upper leg over your body. 平躺在地板上，軀幹扭向胯一側，將上邊的腿跨過軀幹。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a person's dead body as a <b>body</b>. 屍體","examples":["Officials said they had found no traces of violence on the body of the politician. 官方說他們在這位政治家的屍體上沒有發現任何暴力痕跡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>body</b> is an organized group of people who deal with something officially. 團體; 組織","examples":["She was elected student body president at the University of North Carolina. 她當選為北卡羅萊納大學學生社團主席。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>body of</b> people is a group of people who are together or who are connected in some way. 一群 (人)","examples":["...that large body of people which teaches other people how to teach. …教別人如何教學的那一大群人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The body</b> <b>of</b> something such as a building or a document is the main part of it or the largest part of it. 主體; 正文","examples":["The main body of the church had been turned into a massive television studio. 教堂的主體已經被改建成了巨型電視演播室。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>body</b> of a car or aeroplane is the main part of it, not including its engine, wheels, or wings. 車身; 機身","examples":["The only shade was under the body of the plane. 惟一的陰涼處是機身下面。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>body of</b> water is a large area of water, such as a lake or an ocean. (水域) 一大片","examples":["It is probably the most polluted body of water in the world. 這也許是世界上最為汙染的一片水域。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>body of</b> information is a large amount of it. 大量","examples":["An increasing body of evidence suggests that all of us have cancer cells in our bodies at times during our lives. 越來越多的證據表明在一生中我們所有人有時在體內都會出現癌細胞。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that an alcoholic drink has <b>body</b>, you mean that it has a full and strong flavour. (酒的) 醇味","examples":["...a dry wine with good body. …醇味佳的幹葡萄酒。"]}]}]},"bread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵包；（透過工作等掙得的）錢財"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……上撒麵包屑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bread</b> is a very common food made from flour, water, and usually yeast. 麵包","examples":["...a loaf of bread. …一條麵包","...bread and butter. …麵包和黃油。"]}]}]},"bowl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碗，盆；一碗之量；碗狀物；<英>草地滾球；（草地滾球中的）木球，圓球 ；<美>橢圓形運動場，環形劇場 ；美式足球季後賽；盆地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滾（球，箍或其他圓形物）；（板球等）投球；擊中三柱門使（擊球手）出局；迅速移動；打保齡球；（打保齡球）得（分）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bowl</b> is a round container with a wide uncovered top. Some kinds of bowl are used, for example, for serving or eating food from, or in cooking, while other larger kinds are used for washing or cleaning. 碗","examples":["Put all the ingredients into a large bowl. 把所有的配料放進一個大碗裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The contents of a bowl can be referred to as a <b>bowl</b> <b>of</b> something. 一碗的量","examples":["...a bowl of soup. …一碗湯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the hollow rounded part of an object as its <b>bowl</b>. 碗狀物","examples":["He smacked the bowl of his pipe into his hand. 他在手裡磕了磕菸斗。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a sport such as bowling or lawn bowling, when a bowler <b>bowls</b> a ball, he or she rolls it down a narrow track or field of grass. (保齡球或草地滾球運動中) 滾球","examples":["Neither finalist bowled a particularly strong game. 兩位決賽選手滾球得分都不是特別高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a sport such as cricket, when a bowler <b>bowls</b> a ball, he or she throws it down the field toward a batsman. (板球等) 投球","examples":["I can't see the point of bowling a ball like that. 我不能理解那樣的投球。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bowl</b> <b>along</b> in a car or on a boat, you move along very quickly, especially when you are enjoying yourself. (乘車、船) 飛馳","examples":["Veronica looked at him, smiling, as they bowled along. 在他們一路飛馳的當兒，韋羅妮卡微笑著看他。"]}]}]},"book":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"書，書籍；本子，簿冊；（長篇作品的）篇，卷，部；裝訂成冊之物；賭局，打賭；賬冊，賬簿"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"預訂，預約；（警方）將……記錄在案；（裁判）記名警告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>book</b> is a number of pieces of paper, usually with words printed on them, which are fastened together and fixed inside a cover of stronger paper or cardboard. Books contain information, stories, or poetry, for example. 書","examples":["His eighth book came out earlier this year and was an instant best-seller. 他的第8本書今年早些時候出版了，並很快成為了一本暢銷書。","...the author of a book on politics. …一本政治書的作者。","...a new book by Rosella Brown. …羅賽拉·布朗寫的一本新書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>book</b> <b>of</b> something such as stamps, matches, or tickets is a small number of them fastened together between thin cardboard covers. (郵票) 冊; (火柴) 紙板; (票) 版","examples":["Can I have a book of first class stamps please? 請給我一版一等郵票，好嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A company's or organization's <b>books</b> are its records of money that has been spent and earned or of the names of people who belong to it. (公司或機構的) 帳簿; 名冊","examples":["For the most part he left the books to his managers and accountants. 他大多把賬簿留給他的經理和會計們處理。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In a very long written work such as the Bible, a <b>book</b> is one of the sections into which it is divided. 卷","examples":["...the last book of the Bible. …《聖經》的最後一卷。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>book</b> something such as a hotel room or a ticket, you arrange to have it or use it at a particular time. 預訂","examples":["American officials have booked hotel rooms for the women and children. 美國官員已經為這些婦女和兒童預訂了賓館房間。","Laurie booked herself a flight home. 勞裡為自己預訂了回家的機票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a police officer <b>books</b> someone, he or she officially records their name and the offence that they may be charged with. 把…記錄在案","examples":["They took him to the station and booked him for assault with a deadly weapon. 他們把他帶回警察局，以使用致命武器進行攻擊的罪名將他記錄在案。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is a <b>closed book</b>, you mean that you do not know anything about them. 不被知曉的人或事","examples":["Frank Spriggs was a very able man but something of a closed book. 弗蘭克· 斯普里格斯是個非常能幹的人，卻不被人所知曉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If transportation or a hotel, restaurant, or theatre is <b>booked up</b>, <b>fully booked</b>, or <b>booked solid</b>, it has no tickets, rooms, or tables left for a particular time or date. 預訂一空的","examples":["The car ferries from the mainland are often fully booked by February. 從大陸出發的汽車渡輪常常到2月底前就被預訂一空。"]}]}]},"boy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"男孩；兒子；男青年，小夥子；男性朋友們，一群男夥伴（the boys）；一群從事同一職業的男子（boys）；（從事某一職業的）男子；小傢伙（用於稱呼雄性的狗或馬）；夥計（尤用於親切談論某人時）；（尤指在戰場上作戰的）士兵，戰友；指稱某地等的人；運動隊隊員（the boys）；小子（對黑人男性的冒犯語）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（尤用於表示羨慕或興奮）好傢伙，好樣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>boy</b> is a child who will grow up to be a man. 男孩","examples":["He was still just a boy. 他還只是個男孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a young man as a <b>boy</b>, especially when talking about relationships between boys and girls. 小夥子","examples":["...the age when girls get interested in boys. …女孩兒開始對小夥子感興趣的年紀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>boy</b> is their son. 兒子","examples":["Eric was my cousin Edward's boy. 埃裡克是我堂兄愛德華的兒子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a man as a <b>boy</b>, especially when you are talking about him in an affectionate way. 小夥兒","examples":["...the local boy who made president. …那個當上總統的本地小夥兒。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>boy</b>\" or \"<b>oh boy</b>\" in order to express feelings of excitement or admiration. 好傢伙 (表示興奮或羨慕)","examples":["Oh boy! what resourceful children I have. 好傢伙！我的孩子們多機智啊。"]}]}]},"breakfast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"早餐；早餐的，早餐時用的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吃早餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Breakfast</b> is the first meal of the day. It is usually eaten in the early part of the morning. 早餐","examples":["What's for breakfast? 早餐吃什麼？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>breakfast</b>, you have breakfast. 用早餐","examples":["All the ladies breakfasted in their rooms. 所有女士在她們房間裡用了早餐。"]}]}]},"blow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（風）刮，吹；（用嘴）吹氣；吹響，吹奏；毀掉，炸燬；（輪胎）爆開，爆裂；（保險絲）燒斷，熔化；擤（鼻子）；浪費，揮霍（金錢）；<非正式>出錯，錯失機會；洩露，暴露；<美，非正式>迅速離開（某地）；<美，非正式>用力投（球）；<英，非正式>討厭，糟糕；開花；（鯨魚）噴水；吹制（玻璃）；（蒼蠅）產卵於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大風，強風；吹氣，擤鼻子；猛擊，一擊；奮鬥，努力；打擊，挫折；開花，開花期；<非正式>爵士樂演奏；<非正式>大麻；（鍊鋼用語）吹煉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a wind or breeze <b>blows</b>, the air moves. 颳風","examples":["A chill wind blew at the top of the hill. 山頂上颳了一陣涼颼颼的風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b>, you send out a stream of air from your mouth. 呵氣","examples":["Danny rubbed his arms and blew on his fingers to warm them. 丹尼搓著胳膊，向他的手指上呵氣來暖手。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the wind <b>blows</b> something somewhere or if it <b>blows</b> there, the wind moves it there. 把…吹到; 吹","examples":["The wind blew her hair back from her forehead. 風把她額頭上的頭髮向後吹。","Sand blew in our eyes. 沙子吹進了我們眼裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b> something somewhere, you move it by sending out a stream of air from your mouth. (人) 把…吹到","examples":["He picked up his mug and blew off the steam. 他端起杯子吹掉蒸汽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b> bubbles or smoke rings, you make them by blowing air out of your mouth through liquid or smoke. 吹出 (肥皂泡、菸圈等)","examples":["He blew a ring of blue smoke. 他吐出了一圈藍煙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a whistle or horn <b>blows</b> or someone <b>blows</b> it, they make a sound by blowing into it. 吹 (口哨、喇叭); 吹響","examples":["The whistle blew and the train slid forward. 汽笛吹響，火車向前滑動。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>blow</b> your nose, you force air out of it through your nostrils in order to clear it. 擤 (鼻子)","examples":["He took out a handkerchief and blew his nose. 他掏出手帕擤鼻子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>blow</b> something <b>out</b>, <b>off</b>, or <b>away</b> means to remove or destroy it violently with an explosion. 炸燬","examples":["The can exploded, wrecking the kitchen and bathroom and blowing out windows. 罐子爆炸了，毀了廚房和浴室，也炸掉了窗戶。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b> a chance or attempt to do something, you make a mistake which wastes the chance or causes the attempt to fail. 使 (機會) 告吹","examples":["One careless word could blow the whole deal. 一句不經意的話可能使整筆交易告吹。","Oh you fool! You've blown it! 傻瓜！你把它搞砸了！"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something <b>blows</b> an event, situation, or argument into a particular extreme state, especially an uncertain or unpleasant state, you mean that it causes it to be in that state. 搞成 (極端局面)","examples":["Someone took an inappropriate use of words on my part and tried to blow it into a major controversy. 有人不當借用了我說的話，想要挑起一場大爭端。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b> a large amount of money, you spend it quickly on luxuries. 揮霍","examples":["My brother lent me some money and I went and blew it all. 我哥哥借給我一些錢，我全都揮霍掉了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a plant or flower) to blossom or open out (植物或花)開花; 開放","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone receives a <b>blow</b>, they are hit with a fist or weapon. (用拳或武器的) 擊打","examples":["He went to the hospital after a blow to the face. 他臉上捱了一拳後就去了醫院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something that happens is a <b>blow</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, it is very upsetting, disappointing, or damaging to them. 打擊","examples":["That ruling comes as a blow to environmentalists. 那項規定對環境保護主義者是一個打擊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a mass of blossoms 許多花","examples":[]}]}]},"box":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盒，箱，匣；（戲院的）包廂，（法庭的）專席；小亭，崗亭；方框，方格；郵箱；（運動場上的）區，特定區域；<英，非正式>電視（the box）；耳光；黃楊；<英>（運動員的）下體護身"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……裝箱；（與……）鬥拳，參加拳擊比賽；<澳新>（非同群牲畜）混雜，混群（box sheep up）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>box</b> is a square or rectangular container with hard or stiff sides. Boxes often have lids. 盒子; 箱子","examples":["He reached into the cardboard box beside him. 他把手伸進他旁邊的紙板箱。","They sat on wooden boxes. 他們坐在木箱上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>box</b> to refer to a box and its contents, or to the contents only. 一盒的量","examples":["She ate two boxes of chocolates. 她吃了兩盒巧克力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>box</b> is a square or rectangle that is printed or drawn on a piece of paper, a road, or on some other surface. 方格","examples":["For more information, just check the box and send us the form. 若需更多資訊，在方框內打勾，然後把表格寄給我們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>box</b> is a small separate area in a theatre or at a sports arena or stadium, where a small number of people can sit to watch the performance or game. 包廂","examples":["Jim watched the game from a private box. 吉姆在私人包廂裡觀看比賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"penalty box的縮寫","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Box</b> is used before a number as a mailing address by people or organizations that rent a post office box. 郵箱","examples":["...Country Crafts, Box 111, Landisville. …蘭迪斯維爾克拉福特斯地區111號郵箱。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Box</b> is a small evergreen tree with dark leaves that is often used to form hedges. 黃楊","examples":["...box hedges. …黃楊樹籬。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"a punch with the fist, esp on the ear 用拳打出的一擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to put into a box 放入盒中或箱中","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>box</b> means to fight someone according to the rules of boxing. 拳擊","examples":["At school I boxed and played rugby. 在學校，我打拳擊並玩英式橄欖球。"]}]}]},"bottom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"底，底部；盡頭，遠端；最低水平，底層位置；（套裝的）下裝；臀部；水底；河邊窪地；（一局棒球比賽的）後半局；（汽車變速箱的）最低擋；龍骨，船體；底夸克；<古>（尤指馬的）持久力，耐力；<古>船（尤指貨船）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"底部的，最後的；最不重要的，最差的；離得最遠的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（船）到達海底，觸到海底；<澳新>鑽探……直到礦物層；<古>發現……範圍（或本質）；（成績，局勢）到達最低點後趨於平衡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>bottom</b> <b>of</b> something is the lowest or deepest part of it. 底部","examples":["He sat at the bottom of the stairs. 他坐在樓梯底部。","Answers can be found at the bottom of page 8. 答案可以在第8頁下端找到。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>bottom</b> <b>of</b> an object is the flat surface at its lowest point. You can also refer to the inside or outside of this surface as the <b>bottom</b>. 底","examples":["Spread the onion slices on the bottom of the dish. 把洋蔥絲鋪在盤底。","...the bottom of their shoes. …他們的鞋底。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that <b>the bottom</b> has dropped or fallen out of a market or industry, you mean that people have stopped buying the products it sells. (市場、行業) 底部","examples":["The bottom had fallen out of the city's property market. 該市的房地產市場暴跌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The bottom</b> <b>of</b> an organization or career structure is the lowest level in it, where new employees often start. 最底層","examples":["He had worked in the theatre for many years, starting at the bottom. 他從最底層做起，在這個劇院工作了很多年。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone is <b>bottom</b> or at <b>the bottom</b> in a survey, test, or league, their performance is worse than that of all the other people involved. 最後一名","examples":["He was always bottom of the class. 他總是班上的最後一名。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The lower part of a swimsuit, tracksuit, or pair of pyjamas can be referred to as the <b>bottoms</b> or the <b>bottom</b>. 服裝的下半部","examples":["She wore blue tracksuit bottoms. 她下穿藍色田徑褲。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>The bottom</b> <b>of</b> a street or garden is the end farthest away from you or from your house. (街道或庭院的) 盡頭","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>The bottom</b> <b>of</b> a table is the end farthest away from where you are sitting. <b>The bottom</b> <b>of</b> a bed is the end where you usually rest your feet. (桌子或床的) 末端","examples":[]},{"num":"9.","zh":"Your <b>bottom</b> is the part of your body that you sit on. 臀部","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>bottom</b> thing or layer in a series of things or layers is the lowest one. 最下面的","examples":["There's an extra duvet in the bottom drawer of the cupboard. 在櫃子最下層的抽屜裡還有一床羽絨被。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at bottom</b> to emphasize that you are stating what you think is the real nature of something or the real truth about a situation. 實際上","examples":["The two systems are, at bottom, conceptual models. 這兩個系統實際上是概念模型。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>at the bottom of</b> a problem or an unpleasant situation, it is the real cause of it. 某事的實際原因","examples":["Often I find that anger and resentment are at the bottom of the problem. 我經常發現憤怒與不滿是問題的實際原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you want to <b>get to the bottom of</b> a problem, you want to solve it by finding out its real cause. 徹底查明某事","examples":["I have to get to the bottom of this. 我必須把此事一查到底。"]}]}]},"bridge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橋；橋樑，紐帶；船橋，艦橋；鼻樑，鼻樑架；琴馬；（固定的）假牙，齒橋；（連線兩地的）狹窄地帶；過渡樂節，間奏；球杆的凹口支架；橋牌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"彌合（分歧），消除（隔閡）；兼具……的特點；在……上架橋，橫跨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bridge</b> is a structure that is built over a railway, river, or road so that people or vehicles can cross from one side to the other. 橋","examples":["He walked back over the railway bridge. 他從鐵路橋上走了回去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bridge</b> between two places is a piece of land that joins or connects them. (連線兩地的) 陸橋","examples":["...a land bridge linking Serbian territories. …連線塞爾維亞領土的陸橋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something or someone acts as a <b>bridge</b> between two people, groups, or things, they connect them. 紐帶","examples":["We hope this book will act as a bridge between doctor and patient. 我們希望這本書將成為溝通醫生與病人的紐帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>bridge</b> is the place on a ship from which it is steered. 艦橋","examples":["Captain Ronald Warwick was on the bridge when the wave hit. 浪打來時,羅納德·沃裡克船長正在艦橋上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>bridge</b> of your nose is the thin top part of it, between your eyes. (鼻) 梁","examples":["On the bridge of his hooked nose was a pair of gold rimless spectacles. 在他的鷹勾鼻樑上是一副鍍金無邊眼鏡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>bridge</b> of a pair of glasses is the part that rests on your nose. (眼鏡的) 鼻樑架","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a dental plate containing one or more artificial teeth that is secured to the surrounding natural teeth (Also called bridgework)","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>bridge</b> of a violin, guitar, or other stringed instrument is the small piece of wood under the strings that holds them up. (小提琴、吉他等絃樂器的) 琴馬","examples":[]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Bridge</b> is a card game for four players in which the players begin by declaring how many tricks they expect to win. 橋牌","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bridge</b> the gap between two people or things means to reduce it or get rid of it. 克服 (障礙)","examples":["It is unlikely that the two sides will be able to bridge their differences. 雙方不太可能會克服彼此間的分歧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>bridges</b> the gap between two very different things has some of the qualities of each of these things. 結合 (極為不同的兩者)","examples":["...the singer who bridged the gap between pop music and opera. …結合了流行音樂和歌劇的歌手。"]}]}]},"brown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"褐色的，棕色的；膚色深的，曬黑的；未去殼的，糙的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"褐色，棕色；褐色的東西；眼蝶，褐蝶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變成棕色，成褐色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>brown</b> is the colour of earth or of wood. 褐色的","examples":["...her deep brown eyes. …她深邃的褐色眼睛。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe a white-skinned person as <b>brown</b> when they have been sitting in the sun until their skin has become darker than usual. 曬黑了的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Brown</b> is used to describe grains that have not had their outer layers removed, and foods made from these grains. (穀物) 未去殼的; 全糧製作的","examples":["...brown bread. …全麥麵包。","...spicy tomato sauce served over a bed of brown rice. …放在一層糙米飯上的辣番茄醬。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When food <b>browns</b> or when you <b>brown</b> food, you cook it, usually for a short time on a high flame. 使呈褐色; 呈褐色","examples":["Cook for ten minutes until the sugar browns. 烹調10分鐘直到糖變成褐色。"]}]}]},"brother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兄弟，哥哥，弟弟；同類人（指同一種族、宗教、國家、職業或志同道合的人，如同事、戰友、教友）；修士（宗教團體中男性成員的稱呼，常置於名字前）；兄弟（用於公司或商店名稱，常作 Brothers）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"老兄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>brother</b> is a boy or a man who has the same parents as you. 兄弟","examples":["Oh, so you're Peter's younger brother. 噢，這麼說你是彼得的弟弟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a man as your <b>brother</b> if he belongs to the same race, religion, country, or profession as you, or if he has similar ideas to you. 弟兄 (用於指同一種族、宗教、國家、職業或有相同思想的人)","examples":["He told reporters he'd come to be with his Latvian brothers. 他告訴記者他將和他的拉脫維亞弟兄們在一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Brother</b> is a title given to a man who belongs to a religious community such as a monastery. 修士","examples":["...Brother Otto. …奧托修士。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Brothers</b> is used in the names of some companies and stores. 用於公司、商店名","examples":["...the film company Warner Brothers. 華納兄弟影業公司"]}]}]},"bus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公共汽車；（計算機／電子技術）匯流排；母線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘公共汽車；用公共汽車運送；<美>收拾（餐桌）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bus</b> is a large motor vehicle that carries passengers from one place to another. Buses drive along particular routes, and you usually have to pay to travel in them. 公共汽車","examples":["He missed his last bus home. 他沒趕上回家的末班公共汽車。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone is <b>bused</b> to a particular place or when they <b>bus</b> there, they travel there on a bus. 用公共汽車運送; 乘公共汽車","examples":["On May Day hundreds of thousands used to be bused in to parade through East Berlin. 昔日每逢五一勞動節，成千上萬的人們通常會被公共汽車載著遊行穿過東柏林。","To get our Colombian visas we bused back to Medellin. 為了獲得哥倫比亞簽證，我們又乘公共汽車回到麥德林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>bus</b> tables means to clear away dirty dishes and reset the tables. 收拾 (餐桌)","examples":["As a fund-raiser, police officers will don aprons, take orders and bus tables today. 作為募捐方，警官們今天將穿上圍裙，接受點菜，收拾餐桌。"]}]}]},"butter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃油，牛油；水果醬，乾果醬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"塗黃油於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Butter</b> is a soft yellow substance made from cream. You spread it on bread or use it in cooking. 黃油","examples":["...bread and butter. ...麵包和黃油。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>butter</b> something such as bread or toast, you spread butter on it. 塗黃油","examples":["She spread pieces of bread on the counter and began buttering them. 她放了幾片面包在櫃檯上，開始給它們塗黃油。"]}]}]},"building":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建築物，房屋，樓房；建築，建築業"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"建造；發展，建立；逐漸增強（build 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>building</b> is a structure that has a roof and walls, for example, a house or a factory. 建築物","examples":["They were on the upper floor of the building. 他們在該建築物的上層。"]}]}]},"buck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>（美）元；雄性動物；<非正式>小夥子；<古>紈絝子弟，花花公子；責任，過失"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"反對，抵制；鼓舞，使振作；弓背躍起；猛烈顛簸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"齙牙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>buck</b> is a U.S. or Australian dollar. 美元; 澳元","examples":["That would probably cost you about fifty bucks. 那可能會花費你大約五十美元。","Why can't you spend a few bucks on a coat? 為什麼你不能花幾美元買件外套呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>buck</b> is the male of various animals, including the deer, antelope, rabbit, and kangaroo. (雄鹿、公羊、雄兔、雄袋鼠等) 雄性動物","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a young man 年輕男人","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a type of vaulting horse 鞍馬","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a marker in the jackpot to remind the winner of some obligation when his turn comes to deal (提醒贏家履行義務的)標識","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>buck</b> teeth, their upper front teeth stick forward out of their mouth. 外齙的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a horse <b>bucks</b>, it kicks both of its back legs wildly into the air, or jumps into the air wildly with all four feet off the ground. (馬) 狂蹬後腿躍起; 四蹄離地狂跳","examples":["The stallion bucked as he fought against the reins holding him tightly in. 那匹種馬四蹄離地狂跳，試圖掙脫緊緊拴住它的韁繩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>buck</b> the trend, you obtain different results from others in the same area. If you <b>buck</b> the system, you get what you want by breaking or ignoring the rules. 違逆 (潮流); 抗拒 (體制)","examples":["While other newspapers are losing circulation, we are bucking the trend. 其他報紙發行量在下降，而我們卻逆勢而進。","He wants to be the tough rebel who bucks the system. 他想成為抗拒體制的強硬叛逆者。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut (a felled or fallen tree) into lengths 把(伐倒的樹木)截成段","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pass the buck</b>, you refuse to accept responsibility for something, and say that someone else is responsible. 推諉責任","examples":["David says the responsibility is Mr. Smith's and it's no good trying to pass the buck. 大衛說責任應該由史密斯先生承擔，試圖推諉責任毫無益處。"]}]}]},"bug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>昆蟲，蟲子；<非正式>小病，輕微的傳染病；（計算機程式中的）漏洞，故障；竊聽器；<非正式>熱衷，著迷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>煩擾，使惱怒；裝竊聽器；（由於吃驚或害怕）張大眼睛，瞪大雙眼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bug</b> is an insect or similar small creature. 小蟲","examples":["We noticed tiny bugs that were all over the walls. 我們發現牆上爬滿了小蟲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bug</b> is an illness which is caused by small organisms such as bacteria. (由細菌引起的) 疾病","examples":["I think I've got a bit of a stomach bug. 我覺得我有點腸胃感染。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>bug</b> in a computer program, there is a mistake in it. (計算機程式的) 故障","examples":["There is a bug in the software. 軟體出了故障。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bug</b> is a tiny hidden microphone that transmits what people are saying. 微型竊聽器","examples":["There was a bug on the phone. 那部電話裡裝有一個微型竊聽器。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>bugs</b> a place, they hide tiny microphones in it that transmit what people are saying. (在某處) 裝竊聽器","examples":["He heard that they were planning to bug his office. 他聽說他們正計劃在他的辦公室安裝竊聽器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>bugs</b> you, they worry or annoy you. 使煩惱","examples":["I only did it to bug my parents. 我那樣做只不過是為了煩擾我父母。"]}]}]},"butterfly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蝴蝶；見異思遷的人，輕浮易變的人；蝶泳，蝶泳比賽；<非正式>緊張，心慌；耳環託"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（將食物）切成蝴蝶展翅狀，使成蝶形"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"蝴蝶狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>butterfly</b> is an insect with large colourful wings and a thin body. 蝴蝶","examples":["Butterflies and moths are attracted to the wild flowers. 蝴蝶和飛蛾為野花所吸引。"]}]}]},"bye":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"（非正式）再見，拜拜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輪空（淘汰制比賽中參賽者無對手而直接晉級下一輪）；無接觸得分（板球：投球未觸及球棒或擊球者身體時攻方跑動所得的附加分）；餘穴（高爾夫比洞賽中因勝負已定而未繼續打的球洞）；（非正式）次要的、附帶的事物（多用於 by the bye 等搭配）；（Bye）拜伊（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bye</b> and <b>bye-bye</b> are informal ways of saying goodbye. 再見","examples":["Bye, Daddy. 再見，爸爸。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the situation in which a player or team in an eliminatory contest wins a preliminary round by virtue of having no opponent (體育比賽)輪空晉級","examples":[]}]}]},"cab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"駕駛室；計程車，計程車；（舊時的）出租馬車；<非正式>（吉他的）揚聲器箱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘計程車旅行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cab</b> is a taxi. 計程車","examples":["Could I use your phone to call a cab? 我能用你的電話叫一輛計程車嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>cab</b> of a truck or train is the front part in which the driver sits. (卡車或列車的) 駕駛室","examples":["The van has additional load space over the driver's cab. 該貨車在駕駛室上方有額外的載貨空間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an ancient Hebrew measure equal to about 2.3 litres (4 pints) 古希伯來計量單位，相當於2.3升","examples":[]}]}]},"buy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"購買，能買；<非正式>相信，接受；（付出代價）獲得，贏得；收買，賄賂；買，購買"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"合算的東西，便宜貨；購買"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>buy</b> something, you obtain it by paying money for it. 購買","examples":["He could not afford to buy a house. 他買不起房子。","Lizzie bought herself a mountain bike. 莉齊給自己買了一輛山地腳踏車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the quantity or standard of goods an amount of money <b>buys</b>, you are referring to the price of the goods or the value of the money. 買得到","examples":["About $70,000 buys a habitable house. 大約七萬美元才買得到一棟適合居住的房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>buy</b> something like time, freedom, or victory, you obtain it but only by offering or giving up something in return. 換取","examples":["It was a risky operation, but might buy more time. 這是一項冒險的舉動，但也許能換得更多的時間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a person can <b>be bought</b>, you are criticizing the fact that they will give their help or loyalty to someone in return for money. 收買","examples":["Any number of our military and government officials can be bought. 我們的軍官和政府官員中有許多可以被收買。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>buy</b> an idea or a theory, you believe and accept it. 相信","examples":["I'm not buying any of that nonsense. 我一點也不相信那些廢話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Buy into</b> means the same as . 相信","examples":["I bought into the popular myth that when I got the new car or the next house, I'd finally be happy. 我相信了這種大眾神話，以為只要買上新車或再買棟房子就會最終幸福起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is a good <b>buy</b>, it is of good quality and not very expensive. 買得合算的東西","examples":["This was still a good buy even at the higher price. 即便價格再高些，這仍買得合算。"]}]}]},"camel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"駱駝；駝絨織品；駝色，淺黃褐色；打撈浮筒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"駝色的，暗棕色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>camel</b> is a large animal that lives in deserts and is used for carrying goods and people. Camels have long necks and one or two lumps on their backs called humps. 駱駝","examples":[]}]}]},"cage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"籠子；監獄；電梯梯廂；（擊球練習的）擋球網；足球（或曲棍球）球門"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……關進籠中，把……囚禁起來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cage</b> is a structure of wire or metal bars in which birds or animals are kept. 籠子","examples":["I hate to see birds in cages. 我不喜歡看到鳥在籠子裡。"]}]}]},"camera":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"照相機；攝影機；（Camera）人名；（英、意、西）卡梅拉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>camera</b> is a piece of equipment that is used for taking photographs, making films, or producing television pictures. 照相機; 攝影機","examples":["Her grandmother lent her a camera for a school trip to Venice and Egypt. 她的祖母借給她一部相機，讓她在學校組織的到威尼斯和埃及的旅行中使用。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on camera</b>, they are being filmed. 在拍攝中; 上鏡頭","examples":["Fay was so impressive on camera that a special part was written in for her. 鏡頭中的費伊太令人印象深刻了，因此有一個專門寫給她的角色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something or if something happens <b>off camera</b>, you do it or it happens when not being filmed. 不在拍攝中","examples":["They were anything but friendly off camera, refusing even to take the same lift. 不拍攝時他們根本稱不上友好，甚至拒絕乘同一部電梯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a trial is held <b>in camera</b>, the public and the press are not allowed to attend. 不對外公開的","examples":["This morning's appeal was held in camera. 今天上午的上訴是不對外公開的。"]}]}]},"cake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餅狀食物，餅；塊，小塊；<非正式>輕而易舉的事；錢或資產總額；蛋糕"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用會變乾的東西厚厚地）覆蓋；（幹後）結成硬塊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cake</b> is a sweet food made by baking a mixture of flour, eggs, sugar, and fat in an oven. Cakes may be large and cut into slices or small and intended for one person only. 蛋糕","examples":["...a piece of cake. …一塊蛋糕。","Would you like some chocolate cake? 你想來點兒巧克力蛋糕嗎？","...a birthday cake. …一個生日蛋糕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Food that is formed into flat round shapes before it is cooked can be referred to as <b>cakes</b>. (未煮的) 餅狀食物","examples":["...fish cakes. …魚糜餅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cake</b> <b>of soap</b> is a small block of it. 一塊 (肥皂)","examples":["...a small cake of lime-scented soap. …一小塊酸橙味香皂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Take the cake</b> means the same as <b>take the biscuit</b>. 差勁到極點","examples":[]}]}]},"candy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"糖果，巧克力；冰糖；中看不中用的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（水果）製成蜜餞；用糖煮；使結晶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Candy</b> is sweet foods such as chocolate or toffees. 糖果","examples":["...a piece of candy. …一塊糖果。"]}]}]},"camp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"營地；兵營，軍營；度假營；陣營，集團；（藝術和娛樂表現形式的）誇張；放牧區；年度短期兵役；<英>史前古營壘遺址"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"野營，露營；據守，堅守；<澳新>（牲畜）集中休息；扎圍欄"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尤指男子為引人注意而行為）忸怩作態的；（藝術或娛樂）滑稽可笑的，做作的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>camp</b> is a collection of huts and other buildings that is provided for a particular group of people, such as refugees, prisoners, or soldiers, as a place to live or stay. (難民、囚犯、士兵等的) 集中生活營","examples":["...a refugee camp. …一個難民營。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people who all support a particular person, policy, or idea as a particular <b>camp</b>. 陣營","examples":["The press release provoked furious protests from the Gore camp and other top Democrats. 這篇新聞稿引發了戈爾陣營和民主黨其他高層的激烈抗議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>camp</b> is an outdoor area with cabins, tents, or trailers where people stay on holiday. 度假營","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>camp</b> is a collection of tents or trailers where people are living or staying, usually temporarily while they are travelling. 營地","examples":["...gypsy camps. …吉普賽人的營地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"宿營; 露營","examples":["They went camping in the wild. 他們在野外露營。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a camp quality, style, etc 營地特性; 營地型別","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>camp</b> somewhere, you stay or live there for a short time in a tent or trailer, or in the open air. 宿營; 露營","examples":["We camped near the beach. 我們在海灘附近宿營。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Camp out</b> means the same as . 宿營; 露營","examples":["For six months they camped out in a meadow at the back of the house. 他們在房子後面的草地上露宿了6個月。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour, performance, or style of dress as <b>camp</b>, you mean that it is exaggerated and amusing, often in a way that is thought to be typical of some male homosexuals. 裝模作樣的; 忸怩作態的","examples":["James Barron turns in a delightfully camp performance. 詹姆斯·巴倫忸怩作態的表演令人忍俊不禁。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to perform or invest with a camp quality 以營地特徵執行; 以營地特徵授予","examples":[]}]}]},"break":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打破，折斷；（使）破裂，撕開；弄破，使流血；（使）骨折；破紀錄；打斷，中斷；終止；斷絕（聯絡）；損壞；違反，違背；使……放棄習慣；休息；稍停，暫留；突破，掙脫；（被）摧毀，削弱；使心碎；透露，傳開；告訴（壞訊息）；馴化，馴服；得分（低於或高於規定總分）；超過；（雲）散開；開始，（風暴）發作；拍岸，迸濺；（男孩嗓音）變粗；（因激動）變調；破解，破譯；兌開（紙幣）；減緩；（網球中）破發球；（球）轉向，曲線飛行；（股價）暴跌；猛衝，開始快跑；發生，發展；（熱度）降低，退燒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"間歇，小憩；課間休息；停頓，暫停；（電臺或電視節目）插播廣告的間隙；短假；機會，機遇；結束，斷絕；逃跑（尤指越獄）；裂縫，缺口；骨折；（因情感作用）嗓音突變；<文>黎明，破曉；天氣突變；接發球得分；接連擊中；（球的）弧線飛行；（尤指球員或球隊）進攻；有幫助的事物；芽，蓓蕾；雙輪驅馬大車（breaking cart 的原稱）；<史>敞篷四輪馬車（同 brake）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an object <b>breaks</b> or when you <b>break</b> it, it suddenly separates into two or more pieces, often because it has been hit or dropped. 打碎; 破碎","examples":["He fell through the window, breaking the glass. 他打破玻璃，從視窗摔了出去。","The plate broke. 盤子碎了。","The plane broke into three pieces. 那架飛機碎成了3塊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> a part of your body such as your leg, your arm, or your nose, or if a bone <b>breaks</b>, you are injured because a bone cracks or splits. 弄折 (骨頭); 骨折","examples":["She broke a leg in a skiing accident. 她在一次滑雪事故中摔斷了一條腿。","Old bones break easily. 老骨頭容易骨折。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a surface, cover, or seal <b>breaks</b> or if something <b>breaks</b> it, a hole or tear is made in it, so that a substance can pass through. 拆裂; 開裂","examples":["Once you've broken the seal of a bottle there's no way you can put it back together again. 一旦你撕開瓶子的封口,就沒法將它重新合上。","The bandage must be put on when the blister breaks. 水皰破口後必須包紮上繃帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a tool or piece of machinery <b>breaks</b> or when you <b>break</b> it, it is damaged and no longer works. 損壞","examples":["When the clutch broke, the car was locked into second gear. 離合器損壞了後,那輛轎車被鎖在了二檔。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>breaks</b> something, especially a difficult or unpleasant situation that has existed for some time, they end it or change it. 結束; 打破 (困難或不快的情形)","examples":["We need to break the vicious cycle of violence and counterviolence. 我們需要結束暴力和反暴力的惡性迴圈。","New proposals have been put forward to break the deadlock among rival factions. 新的提議已被提出來以打破對立派之間的僵局。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something <b>breaks</b> a silence, they say something or make a noise after a long period of silence. 打破 (沉默)","examples":["Hugh broke the silence. \"Is she always late?\" he asked. 休打破了沉默。問道：“她總是遲到嗎？”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> <b>with</b> a group of people or a traditional way of doing things, or you <b>break</b> your connection with them, you stop being involved with that group or stop doing things in that way. 斷絕 (關係); 打破 (傳統)","examples":["In 1959, Akihito broke with imperial tradition by marrying a commoner. 1959年,明仁天皇打破皇室傳統,與一個平民結了婚。","They were determined to break from precedent. 他們決心打破先例。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> a habit or if someone <b>breaks</b> you <b>of</b> it, you no longer have that habit. 戒除 (習慣)","examples":["If you continue to smoke, keep trying to break the habit. 如果你繼續吸菸,繼續試著戒掉這一習慣吧。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> your journey somewhere, you stop there for a short time so that you can have a rest. (旅行中) 使歇腳","examples":["We broke our journey at a small country hotel. 我們在一家小鄉村旅店歇了歇腳。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> a rule, promise, or agreement, you do something that you should not do according to that rule, promise, or agreement. 違反","examples":["We didn't know we were breaking the law. 我們那時不知道我們在違法。","The company has consistently denied it had knowingly broken arms embargoes. 該公司始終否認故意違反了武器禁運規定。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"To <b>break</b> the force of something such as a blow or fall means to weaken its effect, for example, by getting in the way of it. 減弱 (打擊、墜落等的力度)","examples":["He sustained serious neck injuries after he broke someone's fall. 他被墜落的人砸中之後受了嚴重頸傷。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When you <b>break</b> a piece of bad news to someone, you tell it to them, usually in a kind way. (常指善意地) 說出 (不好的訊息)","examples":["Then Louise broke the news that she was leaving me. 之後路易絲說出了她要離開我的訊息。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> a record, you beat the previous record for a particular achievement. 打破 (記錄)","examples":["Carl Lewis has broken the world record in the 100 metres. 卡爾·劉易斯打破了百米賽跑的世界紀錄。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> a secret code, you work out how to understand it. 破解 (密碼)","examples":["It was feared they could break the Allies' codes. 只怕他們能破解盟軍的密碼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Break</b> is also a noun. 骨折","examples":["It has caused a bad break to Gabriella's leg. 這導致了加布裡埃拉的一條腿嚴重骨折。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Break</b> is also a noun. 結束; (對困難或不快的情形的) 打破","examples":["Nothing that might lead to a break in the deadlock has been discussed yet. 任何可能促成僵局破除的舉措尚未被討論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Break</b> is also a noun. (對關係的) 斷絕; (對傳統的) 打破","examples":["Making a completely clean break with the past, the couple got rid of all their old furniture. 為了與過去斷得一乾二淨,這對夫妻丟棄了他們所有的舊傢俱。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>break</b> is a short period of time when you have a rest or a change from what you are doing, especially if you are working or if you are in a boring or unpleasant situation. 短暫休息","examples":["They may be able to help with childcare so that you can have a break. 他們或許能幫忙看孩子,這樣你可以歇歇。","I thought a 15 minute break from his work would do him good. 我認為15分鐘的工作休息對他會有好處。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>break</b> is a short holiday. 短假","examples":["They are currently taking a short break in Spain. 他們目前在西班牙休短假。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>break</b> is a lucky opportunity that someone gets to achieve something. 時來運轉","examples":["Her first break came when she was chosen out of 100 guitarists auditioning for a spot on Michael Jackson's tour. 她的第一次時來運轉是被從100名吉他手的試奏中選出來參加邁克爾·傑克遜的巡演。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>breaks</b> <b>for</b> a short period of time, they rest or change from what they are doing for a short period. (短暫) 休息","examples":["They broke for lunch. 他們停下來吃午飯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>break</b> free or loose, you free yourself from something or escape from it. 掙脫","examples":["She broke free by thrusting her elbow into his chest. 她用胳膊肘猛杵他的胸部掙脫了開來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a piece of news <b>breaks</b>, people hear about it from the newspapers, television, or radio. (訊息) 傳開","examples":["The news broke that Montgomery was under investigation. 訊息傳出說蒙哥馬利在受到調查。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When day or dawn <b>breaks</b>, it starts to grow light after the night has ended. 破曉","examples":["They continued the search as dawn broke. 他們在天亮之後繼續搜尋。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a wave <b>breaks</b>, it passes its highest point and turns downward, for example, when it reaches the shore. (波浪) 落下","examples":["Danny listened to the waves breaking against the shore. 丹尼聽著波浪拍岸的聲音。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone's voice <b>breaks</b> when they are speaking, it changes its sound, for example, because they are sad or afraid. (嗓音因悲傷、害怕等而) 變調","examples":["Godfrey's voice broke, and halted. 戈弗雷的嗓音變了調,然後停了下來。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When a boy's voice <b>breaks</b>, it becomes deeper and sounds more like a man's voice. (男孩) 變聲","examples":["He sings with the strained discomfort of someone whose voice hasn't quite broken. 他緊張不適地唱著, 嗓音像個還未完全變聲的人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If the weather <b>breaks</b> or a storm <b>breaks</b>, it suddenly becomes rainy or stormy after a period of sunshine. (天氣) 突變; (暴風雨) 驟起","examples":["I've been waiting for the weather to break. 我一直在等待下雨。"]}]}]},"car":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汽車，轎車；<美>（火車的）車廂；（火車上作特殊用途的）車廂（如餐車、臥鋪車廂）；（電梯的）梯廂，（索道或氣球的）吊艙；<文>戰車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>car</b> is a motor vehicle with room for a small number of passengers. 小汽車","examples":["He had left his tickets in his car. 他把票落在自己的小汽車裡了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>car</b> is the same as a . 火車車廂","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The separate sections of a train are called <b>cars</b> when they are used for a particular purpose. (有特殊用途的) 火車車廂","examples":["He made his way into the dining car for breakfast. 他擠進餐車吃早點。"]}]}]},"cap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帽子；（對物件起保護作用的）罩，蓋，套；最高限額；國家隊隊員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"覆蓋；限額收取（或支出）；選入國家隊；給（牙齒）上牙套；勝過，超過；脫帽致意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cap</b> is a soft, flat hat with a curved part at the front which is called a visor. 軟扁帽; 便帽","examples":["...a dark blue baseball cap. …一頂深藍色的棒球帽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cap</b> is a special hat which is worn as part of a uniform. 制服帽","examples":["...a border guard in olive grey uniform and a cap. …一個穿橄欖綠軍服、戴軍帽的邊防衛士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>cap</b> of a bottle is its lid. 瓶蓋","examples":["She unscrewed the cap of her water bottle and gave him a drink. 她擰開水瓶蓋，給他喝了一口水。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone says that a good or bad event <b>caps</b> a series of events, they mean it is the final event in the series, and the other events were also good or bad. 成為…的結尾","examples":["The unrest capped a weekend of right-wing attacks on foreigners. 整個週末右翼分子對外國人的襲擊最終發展成為騷亂。"]}]}]},"card":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行卡，身份證；明信片，賀卡；名片；紙牌；紙牌遊戲（cards）；<舊>活寶，怪人；硬紙板；優勢，王牌；儲存卡，外掛；賽事安排；梳理工具"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"要求出示身份證；亮牌；（高爾夫比賽中）得分；在卡片上記錄；梳理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is a piece of stiff paper or thin cardboard on which something is written or printed. 卡片","examples":["Check the numbers below against the numbers on your card. 核對下面的數字是否和您卡片上的相符。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is a piece of cardboard or plastic, or a small document, which shows information about you and which you carry with you, for example to prove your identity. 身份證明卡","examples":["...they check my bag and press card. …他們檢查了我的包和記者證。","...her membership card. …她的會員卡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is a rectangular piece of plastic, issued by a bank, company, or shop, which you can use to buy things or obtain money. 消費卡","examples":["He paid the whole bill with an American Express card. 他用美國運通卡支付了全款。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is a folded piece of stiff paper with a picture and sometimes a message printed on it, which you send to someone on a special occasion. 賀卡","examples":["She sends me a card on my birthday. 她在我生日那天送了一張賀卡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is the same as a . 明信片","examples":["Send your details on a card to the following address. 將你的詳細資訊寫在明信片上，寄到下面的地址。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>card</b> is a piece of thin cardboard carried by someone such as a businessperson in order to give it to other people. A card shows the name, address, telephone number, and other details of the person who carries it. 名片","examples":["Here's my card. You may need me. 這是我的名片。你可能會需要我。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Cards</b> are thin pieces of cardboard with numbers or pictures printed on them which are used to play various games. 紙牌","examples":["...a deck of cards. …一副紙牌。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are playing <b>cards</b>, you are playing a game using cards. 紙牌遊戲","examples":["They enjoy themselves drinking wine, smoking, and playing cards. 他們喝酒、抽菸、打牌，玩得不亦樂乎。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Card</b> is strong, stiff paper or thin cardboard. 硬紙片","examples":["She put the pieces of card in her pocket. 她把那些硬紙片塞進口袋裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in the cards</b>, you mean that it is very likely to happen. 很可能發生","examples":["Last summer she began telling friends that a New Year marriage was in the cards. 去年夏天她開始通知朋友們她很可能在新年結婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> your <b>cards read</b>, you have your fortune told by someone who uses playing cards or tarot cards to tell you about yourself and predict your future. 找人算命","examples":["The shop had a sign in the window: \"Have your cards read here, $25.\" 那家商店的窗戶上有個招牌，寫著：“算命，$25”。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to comb out and clean fibres of wool or cotton before spinning (紡紗前對毛線或棉線進行的)梳通清理","examples":[]}]}]},"cent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分（美元、歐元等的貨幣單位）；<非正式>小錢；<非正式>分毫（用來強調沒錢）；（樂）音分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cent</b> is a small unit of money worth one hundredth of some currencies, for example the dollar and the euro. 分 (如美元、歐元等基本貨幣單位的1%)","examples":["A cup of rice which cost thirty cents a few weeks ago is now being sold for up to one dollar. 幾周前價值30美分的1杯米如今賣到了1美元。"]}]}]},"can":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（表示有能力做或能夠發生）能，會；（表示可能性）可以，能；（用於請求）能，可以；（表示允許）可以；應該（表示某事該做或不該做）；（用於禮貌地提出幫忙）可以，能；把食品裝罐儲存；<美，非正式>解僱，開除；<美，非正式>停止，結束（某事）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"罐，聽；（裝液體、垃圾等帶蓋的）金屬容器，塑膠容器；<美，非正式>監獄；<美，非正式>廁所；臀部；驅逐艦；破壞者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> when you are mentioning a quality or fact about something which people may make use of if they want to. 可以","examples":["Tickets can be purchased at the Madstone Theatre box office. 票可在麥德斯通劇院售票處買到。","A central reservation number can direct you to accommodations that best suit your needs. 預訂總機可以幫你找到最適合你需求的住處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> to indicate that someone has the ability or opportunity to do something. 能夠; 會","examples":["Don't worry yourself about me, I can take care of myself. 別為我擔心，我會照顧好自己的。","I can't give you details because I don't actually have any details. 我無法告訴你詳情，因為我確實不瞭解具體情況。","The United States will do whatever it can to help Greece. 美國將盡一切所能幫助希臘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>cannot</b> to indicate that someone is not able to do something because circumstances make it impossible for them to do it. 無法","examples":["We cannot buy food and clothes and pay for rent and utilities on $20 a week. 我們無法靠每星期$20來購買食品、衣物，付房租和水電費。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> to indicate that something is true sometimes or is true in some circumstances. 可能","examples":["...long-term therapy that can last five years or more. …可能要持續5年或者更長時間的長期治療。","Exercising alone can be boring. 獨自一個人鍛鍊可能會很無聊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>cannot</b> and <b>can't</b> to state that you are certain that something is not the case or will not happen. 不可能; 不會","examples":["From her knowledge of Douglas's habits, she feels sure that that person can't have been Douglas. 根據她對道格拉斯的習慣的瞭解，她肯定那人不會是道格拉斯。","Things can't be that bad. 情況不會那麼糟。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> to indicate that someone is allowed to do something. You use <b>cannot</b> or <b>can't</b> to indicate that someone is not allowed to do something. 可以","examples":["Can I really have your jeans when you go? 你走後，我真的可以穿你的牛仔褲嗎？","We can't answer any questions, I'm afraid. 我們恐怕不能再回答任何問題了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>cannot</b> or <b>can't</b> when you think it is very important that something should not happen or that someone should not do something. 不應該","examples":["It is an intolerable situation and it can't be allowed to go on. 這種情形令人無法容忍，不應該被允許繼續下去。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>can</b>, usually in questions, in order to make suggestions or to offer to do something. 可以; 能 (用於表示建議或給予)","examples":["What can I do around here? 在這裡我能做什麼？","This elderly woman was struggling out of the train and I said, \"Oh, can I help you?\" 這位老婦人力圖擠出列車時，我問道，“哦，我能幫忙嗎？”"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> in questions in order to make polite requests. You use <b>can't</b> in questions in order to request strongly that someone does something. 可以; 能 (用於表示請求)","examples":["Can I have a look at that? 我能看看那個東西嗎？","Why can't you leave me alone? 你為什麼不能別管我的事情？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> as a polite way of interrupting someone or of introducing what you are going to say next. 可不可以 (打斷談話或插嘴時)","examples":["Can I interrupt you just for a minute? 我可不可以打斷你一會兒？","But if I can interrupt, Joe, I don't think anybody here is personally blaming you. 恕我打斷你，喬，我認為這裡並沒有人在怪你。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> with verbs such as \"imagine,\" \"think,\" and \"believe\" in order to emphasize how you feel about a particular situation. 能夠 (與imagine， think， believe連用，表示強調)","examples":["You can imagine he was terribly upset. 你能想像他有多苦惱。","You can't think how glad I was to see them all go. 你想不到看到他們都走掉我有多開心。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>can</b> in questions with \"how\" to indicate that you feel strongly about something. 與(how)連用，表示強烈的感受","examples":["How can millions of dollars go astray? 數百萬美元怎麼會丟失了呢？","How can you say such a thing? 你怎麼能說這樣的話？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>can</b> is a metal container in which something such as food, drink, or paint is put. The container is usually sealed to keep the contents fresh. 罐; 罐頭","examples":["Several young men were kicking a tin can along the middle of the road. 幾個小夥子正在馬路中間踢著一個錫罐。","...empty beer cans. …空啤酒罐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>can</b> to refer to a can and its contents, or to the contents only. 一罐","examples":["She grabbed a can of soda out of the refrigerator. 她從冰箱裡取出一罐汽水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The can</b> is the toilet. 廁所","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When food or drink <b>is canned</b>, it is put into a metal container and sealed so that it will remain fresh. 把…裝罐","examples":["...fruits and vegetables that will be canned, skinned, diced, or otherwise processed. …將要經過裝罐、去皮、切塊或其他加工程式的水果和蔬菜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are canned</b>, you are dismissed from your job. 解僱","examples":["The extremists prevailed, and the security chief was canned. 極端分子佔了上風，那名安全主管被解僱。"]}]}]},"cat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貓，貓科動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cat</b> is a furry animal that has a long tail and sharp claws. Cats are often kept as pets. 貓","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cats</b> are lions, tigers, and other wild animals in the same family. 貓科動物","examples":["The lion is perhaps the most famous member of the cat family. 獅子可能是貓科家族裡最有名的成員了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"catamaran的縮寫","examples":[]}]}]},"case":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"具體情況，例項；病例，病案；訴訟，官司；案件，案子；容器，箱子；事實，論據；（特定處境或品性的）人；（語法的）格"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"圍繞，包蓋；（盜搶前）探察，踩點兒；裝入保護容器內"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>case</b> is a particular situation or incident, especially one that you are using as an individual example or instance of something. 情況","examples":["Surgical training takes at least nine years, or 11 in the case of obstetrics. 外科培訓至少需要9年，產科則要11年。","In extreme cases, insurance companies can prosecute for fraud. 在極個別情況下，保險公司會起訴騙保行為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>case</b> is a person or their particular problem that a doctor, social worker, or other professional is dealing with. 案例","examples":["Dr. Thomas Bracken describes the case of a 45-year-old Catholic priest much given to prayer whose left knee became painful. 托馬斯·布拉肯醫生描述了那個病例：一名45歲天主教牧師由於經常祈禱導致左膝疼痛。","Some cases of arthritis respond to a gluten-free diet. 不含谷蛋白的飲食對一些關節炎病例有療效。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is a sad <b>case</b> or a hopeless <b>case</b>, you mean that they are in a sad situation or a hopeless situation. (處於某種狀況的) 人","examples":["I knew I was going to make it – that I wasn't a hopeless case. 我知道自己能行–我不是無藥可救的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>case</b> is a crime or mystery that the police are investigating. 案件","examples":["The police have several suspects in the case of five murders committed in Gainesville, Florida. 警方就佛羅里達州蓋恩斯維爾市的5起謀殺案已經鎖定了幾名嫌疑人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>case</b> <b>for</b> or <b>against</b> a plan or idea consists of the facts and reasons used to support it or oppose it. 事實","examples":["He sat there while I made the case for his dismissal. 他坐在那兒，聽我講著他被解僱的原因。","Both these facts strengthen the case against hanging. 這兩大事實都是反對絞刑的充實理由。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In law, a <b>case</b> is a trial or other legal inquiry. 訴訟","examples":["It can be difficult for public figures to win a libel case. 公眾人物要贏得誹謗訴訟是有難度的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>case</b> is a container that is specially designed to hold or protect something. 容器; 箱子; 盒","examples":["...a black case for his glasses. ...他的黑色的眼鏡盒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"In the grammar of many languages, the <b>case</b> of a group such as a noun group or adjective group is the form it has which shows its relationship to other groups in the sentence. (語法) 格","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>in any case</b> when you are adding something which is more important than what you have just said, but which supports or corrects it. 再者","examples":["The concert was sold out, and in any case, most of the people gathered in the square could not afford the price of a ticket. 音樂會的票已售完，再說，聚在廣場上的人也大都買不起票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>in case</b> or <b>just in case</b> a particular thing happens, you do it because that thing might happen. 以防","examples":["In case anyone was following me, I made an elaborate detour. 我特意繞了一圈，以防有人跟蹤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something or have something <b>in case of</b> a particular thing, you do it or have it because that thing might happen or be true. 以免","examples":["Many stores along the route have been boarded up in case of trouble. 沿途很多商店都用板封上了，以免招來麻煩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>in case</b> in expressions like \"in case you didn't know\" or \"in case you've forgotten\" when you are telling someone in a rather irritated way something that you think is either obvious or none of their business. 難道","examples":["She's nervous about something, in case you didn't notice. 她對某些事情神經兮兮的，難道你沒注意到？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>in that case</b> or <b>in which case</b> to indicate that what you are going to say is true if the possible situation that has just been mentioned actually exists. 那樣的話","examples":["Perhaps you've some doubts about the attack. In that case it may interest you to know that Miss Woods witnessed it. 或許你對本次襲擊有些懷疑。要是那樣的話，你可能會有興趣瞭解伍茲小姐目睹了一切。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say that you are doing something <b>just in case</b> to refer vaguely to the possibility that a thing might happen or be true, without saying exactly what it is. 以防萬一","examples":["I guess we've already talked about this but I'll ask you again just in case. 我想我們已經討論過了這個問題，但為保險起見，我再問你一次。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that a task or situation is <b>a case of</b> a particular thing, you mean that it consists of that thing or can be described as that thing. …的事","examples":["It's not a case of whether anyone would notice or not. 這不是人們會不會注意到的問題。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is the case</b>, you mean that it is true or correct. 情況是那樣","examples":["You'll probably notice her having difficulty swallowing. If this is the case, give her plenty of liquids. 你可能會發現她吞嚥有困難。要真是那樣，多給她一些流質食物。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to put into or cover with a case 包圍","examples":[]}]}]},"center":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（地理位置）中間，中心點；（機構，組織）活動中心；關注點，焦點；中間派，中間立場；中鋒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……放在中央；（使）以……為中心，（使）注意力集中於；（使）主要發生在，（使）集中於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Center）森特（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"care":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"照料，護理；小心，謹慎；憂慮，煩惱；收養，監護"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"照顧，照料；在意，擔憂；喜歡，想要"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>care</b> about something, you feel that it is important and are concerned about it. 關注","examples":["...a company that cares about the environment. …一家關心環境的公司。","...young men who did not care whether they lived or died. …一群不在乎自己死活的年輕人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can ask someone if they would <b>care</b> <b>for</b> something or if they would <b>care</b> <b>to</b> do something as a polite way of asking if they would like to have or do something. 想要","examples":["Would you care for some orange juice? 你想要些橙汁嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>care</b> <b>for</b> someone, you feel a lot of affection for them. 喜愛","examples":["He wanted me to know that he still cared for me. 他想讓我知道他仍然愛著我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>care</b> <b>for</b> someone or something, you look after them and keep them in a good state or condition. 照顧","examples":["They hired a nurse to care for her. 他們僱了個護士來照顧她。","...these distinctive cars, lovingly cared for by private owners. …這些被私家車主精心呵護著的各具特色的汽車。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"體貼","examples":["...the \"feminine\" traits of caring and compassion. …體貼和同情這些“女性”的特質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Care</b> is also a noun. 照顧","examples":["Most of the staff specialize in the care of children. 大部分員工都擅長照顧孩子。","...sensitive teeth which need special care. …需要特殊護理的敏感型牙齒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> <b>care</b>, you give careful attention to it because you do not want to make any mistakes or cause any damage. 謹慎","examples":["Condoms are an effective method of birth control if used with care. 避孕套如果謹慎使用，是一種有效的節育方法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>cares</b> are your worries, anxieties, or fears. 煩惱","examples":["Lean back in a hot bath and forget all the cares of the day. 躺下享受個熱水浴，忘掉一天中所有的煩惱。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>for all</b> I <b>care</b> to emphasize that it does not matter at all to you what someone does. 不關某人的事","examples":["You can go right now for all I care. 你現在就可以走，我才不管呢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>couldn't care less</b> <b>about</b> someone or something, you are emphasizing that you are not interested in them or worried about them. You can also say that you <b>could care less</b>, with the same meaning. 不在乎","examples":["I couldn't care less about the woman. 我才不在乎那個女人呢。","I don't care if they respect me. I could care less. 我不在乎他們是否尊重我。我一點都不在乎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone sends you a letter or package <b>care of</b> or <b>in care of</b> a particular person or place, they send it to that person or place, and it is then passed on to you. 經某人轉交","examples":["Please write to me care of the publishers. 寫給我的信請透過出版商轉交。","He wrote to me in care of my publisher. 他寫信給我，經由我的出版商轉交。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>take care of</b> someone or something, you look after them and prevent them from being harmed or damaged. 照顧某人/某事","examples":["There was no one else to take care of their children. 沒有其他人照看他們的孩子了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>take care</b> <b>to</b> do something, you make sure that you do it. 留意做某事","examples":["Foley followed Albert through the gate, taking care to close the latch. 福利隨著艾伯特進了大門，留心地把門閂上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>take care of</b> a problem, task, or situation means to deal with it. 處理某事","examples":["They leave it to the system to try and take care of the problem. 他們把問題留給體制去設法解決。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Who cares?</b>\" to emphasize that something does not matter to you at all. 管它呢","examples":["\"But we might ruin the stove.\"—\"Who cares?\" “我們可能會毀了爐子。” —“管它呢！”"]}]}]},"call":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……命名，稱呼；認為……是，把……看作；喊，叫；召開，召集；召喚，呼喚；傳喚（證人）；打電話；打電話叫……來；點（名），從（清單上）讀出；（動物）啼叫，鳴叫；（模仿動物的叫聲）把……引過來；短暫拜訪；（火車、船、公共汽車等）短暫停留；預測，推測；猜擲幣結果；（比賽中裁判等）判定；取消（比賽等）；決定（進攻戰術）；叫（對方）攤牌，叫牌；執行子程式命令"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"打電話，通話；喊叫，呼叫；（動物的）叫聲；短暫拜訪；號召，呼籲；需求，需要；需要關注或努力的事；吸引力，魅力；登機廣播；器樂聲；決定，抉擇；裁定，判決；叫牌，吊牌；擲錢幣猜正反面；舞步指示；催交；買入期權，購買選擇權；執行子程式的命令"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> someone or something <b>by</b> a particular name or title, you give them that name or title. 稱呼","examples":["I always wanted to call the dog Mufty for some reason. 出於某種原因，我總想叫那條狗穆夫蒂。","\"Doctor...\"—\"Will you please call me Sarah?\" “…醫生” — “請叫我薩拉好嗎？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> someone or something a particular thing, you suggest they are that thing or describe them as that thing. 把…描述為; 把…說成","examples":["The speech was interrupted by members of the Republican Party, who called him a traitor. 演講被稱他為叛徒的共和黨成員們打斷了。","She calls me lazy and selfish. 她說我又懶又自私。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> something, you say it in a loud voice, because you are trying to attract someone's attention. 喊","examples":["He could hear the others downstairs calling his name. 他能聽到其他人在樓下喊他的名字。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> someone, you ask them to come to you by shouting to them. 喊某人過來","examples":["She called her young son: \"Here, Stephen, come and look at this!\" 她喊她的小兒子過來，“這兒，斯蒂芬，來看這個！”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> someone such as a doctor or the police, you ask them to come to you, usually by telephoning them. (打電話) 叫…來","examples":["He screamed for his wife to call an ambulance. 他尖叫著，要妻子叫輛救護車來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>calls</b> something such as a meeting, rehearsal, or election, they arrange for it to take place at a particular time. 安排召開; 安排舉行","examples":["We're going to call a meeting and discuss how we can work with other groups. 我們打算開個會，討論如何與其他團隊協作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>is called</b> before a court or committee, they are ordered to appear there, usually to give evidence. 傳訊; 傳喚","examples":["The child waited two hours before she was called to give evidence. 那個小孩等了2個小時才被傳喚去做證。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>call</b> a game or sporting event means to cancel it, for example because of rain or bad light. 取消","examples":["We called the next game. 我們取消了下一場比賽。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> someone, you telephone them. 給…打電話","examples":["Would you call me as soon as you find out? My number's in the phone book. 你一查清就給我打電話好嗎？我的號碼在電話簿裡。","A friend of mine gave me this number to call. 我的一個朋友讓我打這個號碼。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Call out</b> means the same as <b>call</b>. 喊","examples":["The butcher's son called out a greeting. 那屠夫的兒子聲音洪亮地招呼了一聲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>call</b> <b>for</b> something, someone demands that it should happen. 要求","examples":["There have been calls for a new kind of security arrangement. 有人要求採用新型的安保措施。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>call</b> of a particular bird or animal is the characteristic sound that it makes. (鳥、獸的) 叫聲","examples":["...a wide range of animal noises and bird calls. …動物和鳥的各種各樣叫聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is little or no <b>call for</b> something, very few people want it to be done or provided. 要求; 需求","examples":["\"Have you got just plain chocolate?\"—\"No, I'm afraid there's not much call for that.\" “有純巧克力嗎？” — “沒有，恐怕對這種巧克力的需求不多。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>call</b> <b>of</b> something such as a place is the way it attracts or interests you strongly. 吸引力; 魅力","examples":["But the call of the wild was simply too strong and so he set off once more. 但大自然的吸引力實在太大了，所以他又一次出發了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Call</b> is also a noun. 短暫訪問","examples":["He decided to pay a call on Tommy Cummings. 他決定去拜訪湯米·卡明斯。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you make a telephone <b>call</b>, you telephone someone. 打電話","examples":["I made a phone call to the United States to talk to a friend. 我打電話到美國同一個朋友交談。","I've had hundreds of calls from other victims. 我已經接到幾百個其他受害者打來的電話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>on call</b>, they are ready to go to work at any time if they are needed, especially if there is an emergency. 隨叫隨到","examples":["In theory I'm on call day and night. 理論上，我不分晝夜隨叫隨到。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>call</b> somewhere, you make a short visit there. 短暫訪問","examples":["A market researcher called at the house where my uncle was living. 一位市場調查員到過我叔叔的住處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a train, bus, or ship <b>calls</b> somewhere, it stops there for a short time to allow people to get on or off. (火車、公共汽車或船隻) 停靠","examples":["The steamer calls at several palm-fringed ports along the way. 汽船一路上停靠過好幾個棕櫚樹掩映的港口。"]}]}]},"cause":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"原因；事業；理由"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"引起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>cause</b> <b>of</b> an event, usually a bad event, is the thing that makes it happen. 起因; 原因","examples":["Smoking is the biggest preventable cause of death and disease. 吸菸是造成不必要疾病和死亡的最大原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cause</b> is an aim or principle which a group of people supports or is fighting for. 奮鬥目標; 事業","examples":["Refusing to have one leader has not helped the cause. 拒絕接受領導無益於該事業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>cause</b> <b>for</b> a particular feeling or action, you have good reasons for feeling it or doing it. 理由","examples":["Only a few people can find any cause for celebration. 只有少數人能找到慶祝的理由。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>cause</b> something, usually something bad, means to make it happen. 引起","examples":["The insecticide used on some weeds can cause health problems. 噴灑在野草上的殺蟲劑會引發各種健康問題。","This was a genuine mistake, but it did cause me some worry. 這純屬失誤，但它確實令我有些不安。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>for a good cause</b>, you mean that it is worth doing or giving to because it will help other people, for example by raising money for charity. 為了高尚的事業 (如慈善捐贈)","examples":["The Raleigh International Bike Ride is open to anyone who wants to raise money for a good cause. 羅利國際腳踏車騎行會歡迎有志為慈善事業籌錢者參加。"]}]}]},"chart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖表，曲線圖；海圖，星點陣圖；排行榜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"繪製；記錄，跟蹤；制定（行動計劃）；進榜，上榜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chart</b> is a diagram, picture, or graph which is intended to make information easier to understand. 圖表","examples":["Male unemployment was 14.2%, compared with 5.8% for women (see chart on next page). 男性失業率是14.2%，相比女性為5.8% (參見下頁圖表)。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chart</b> is a map of the sea or stars. 海圖; 星圖","examples":["...charts of Greek waters. …希臘水域圖。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chart</b> an area of land, sea, or sky, or a feature in that area, you make a map of the area or show the feature in it. 繪製","examples":["Ptolemy charted more than 1,000 stars in 48 constellations. 托勒密繪製了48個星座中1000多顆星的星圖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>chart</b> the development or progress of something, you observe it and record or show it. You can also say that a report or graph <b>charts</b> the development or progress of something. 用圖表記錄","examples":["One doctor has charted a dramatic rise in local childhood asthma since the road was built. 一位醫生用圖表記錄的方式，說明道路建成後當地兒童哮喘發病率急劇上升。"]}]}]},"chick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雛鳥，小雞；少女，小妞兒（男性用語，有冒犯意味）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chick</b> is a baby bird. 雛鳥","examples":["...newly-hatched chicks. …剛孵出的雛鳥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some men refer to women as <b>chicks</b>. This use could cause offence. 妞 (這一稱謂可能引起冒犯)","examples":["I'm madly in love with this hot biker chick. 我瘋狂地愛上了這個迷人的騎摩托車的妞。"]}]}]},"chase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"追逐，追趕；匆忙趕往，急奔；追求，努力爭取；求愛；驅逐，趕走；撤職；催促；鏤刻，雕刻"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"追趕，追逐；爭取，努力獲得；狩獵，獵捕；越野賽馬，障礙賽馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chase</b> someone, or <b>chase</b> <b>after</b> them, you run after them or follow them quickly in order to catch or reach them. 追趕","examples":["She chased the thief for 100 yards. 她追了小偷100碼遠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are chasing</b> something you want, such as work or money, or are <b>chasing after</b> it, you are trying hard to get it. 追求 (事業、金錢等)","examples":["In some areas, 14 people are chasing every job. 在某些地區，14個人角逐每一個崗位。","There are too many schools chasing after too few students. 有太多的學校爭搶太少的學生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>chases</b> someone that they are attracted to, or <b>chases</b> <b>after</b> them, they try hard to persuade them to have a sexual relationship with them. 追求 (異性)","examples":["Women also have another reason for not chasing men too hard, of course. 當然，婦女還有另一個不緊追男人的理由。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>chases</b> you from a place, they force you to leave by using threats or violence. 驅逐","examples":["Many farmers will then chase you off their land quite aggressively. 到那時，許多農民便會毫不留情地將你逐出他們的土地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>chase</b> someone <b>from</b> a job or a position or <b>from</b> power means to force them to leave it. 逼迫卸職","examples":["In the '70s he had been chased out of his job. 在70年代他被迫離開了他的職位。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chase</b> is also a noun. 追趕","examples":["He was reluctant to give up the chase. 他不願意放棄追逐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chase</b> is also a noun. (對事業、金錢等的) 追求","examples":["They took an invincible lead in the chase for the championship. 他們在冠軍角逐中遙遙領先。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Chase</b> is also a noun. (對異性的) 追求","examples":["The chase is always much more exciting than the conquest anyway. 無論如何，追求總比征服更令人興奮。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chase</b> somewhere, you run or rush there. 衝","examples":["They chased down the stairs into the narrow, dirty street. 他們衝下樓梯，跑到狹窄骯髒的街道上。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut a groove, furrow, or flute in (a surface, column, etc) 雕刻(表面、柱子等) (Also chamfer)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>cuts to the chase</b>, they start talking about or dealing with what is important, instead of less important things. 切入主題","examples":["Hi everyone, we all know why we are here today, so let's cut to the chase. 大家好，我們都知道今天為何來此，讓我們切入主題吧。"]}]}]},"chicken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雞；雞肉；<非正式>膽小鬼，懦夫；（兒童玩的）比試膽量的遊戲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"沒勇氣的，膽小的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>因害怕而放棄，膽怯（chicken out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chickens</b> are birds which are kept on a farm for their eggs and for their meat. 雞","examples":["Lionel built a coop so that they could raise chickens and have a supply of fresh eggs. 萊昂內爾搭建了一個雞籠，這樣他們就可以養雞，得到新鮮雞蛋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chicken</b> is the flesh of this bird eaten as food. 雞肉","examples":["...roast chicken with wild mushrooms. …烤雞肉和野蘑菇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone calls you a <b>chicken</b>, they mean that you are afraid to do something. 膽小鬼","examples":["I'm scared of the dark. I'm a big chicken. 我很怕黑。我是個十足的膽小鬼。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chicken</b> is also an adjective. 膽小的","examples":["Why are you so chicken, Gregory? 你為什麼這麼膽小，格雷戈裡？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is counting</b> their <b>chickens</b>, you mean that they are assuming that they will be successful or get something, when this is not certain. 蛋尚未孵出就數小雞; 指望得過早","examples":["I don't want to count my chickens before they are hatched. 我不想指望得過早。"]}]}]},"chief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"首要的，主要的；為首的，首席的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"領袖，首領；酋長；（紋章）上段（盾徽頂部的寬橫帶）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"主要地；首要地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>chief</b> of an organization is the person who is in charge of it. 長官","examples":["...a commission appointed by the police chief. …由警察局長任命的委員會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>chief</b> of a tribe is its leader. (部落) 首領","examples":["...Sitting Bull, chief of the Sioux tribes of the Great Plains. …大平原蘇人部落的首領西延·布林。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chief</b> is used in the job titles of the most senior worker or workers of a particular kind in an organization. 首席的","examples":["...the chief test pilot. …首席試飛員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>chief</b> cause, part, or member of something is the most important one. 首要的","examples":["Financial stress is well established as a chief reason for divorce. 經濟壓力被充分證實為導致離婚的一個首要因素。"]}]}]},"christmas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聖誕節；聖誕節期間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Christmas</b> is a Christian festival when the birth of Jesus Christ is celebrated. Christmas is celebrated on the 25th of December. 聖誕節","examples":["The day after Christmas is generally a busy one for retailers. 聖誕節次日對零售商們來說通常都是繁忙的一天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Christmas</b> is the period of several days around and including Christmas Day. 聖誕節期間","examples":["During the Christmas holidays there's a tremendous amount of traffic between the Northeast and Florida. 在聖誕節期間，東北部和弗羅裡達州之間的交通異常繁忙。"]}]}]},"chance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機會，時機；可能性；危險，冒險；運氣，偶然"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"偶然，碰巧；冒險做"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偶然的，碰巧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>chance</b> <b>of</b> something happening, it is possible that it will happen. 可能性","examples":["Do you think they have a chance of beating Australia? 你認為他們有可能擊敗澳大利亞隊嗎?","There was really very little chance that Ben would ever have led a normal life. 那時本幾乎不可能過上正常的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>chance</b> <b>to</b> do something, you have the opportunity to do it. 機會","examples":["The electoral council announced that all eligible people would get a chance to vote. 選舉委員會曾宣佈所有符合條件者都將獲得投票機會。","Most refugee doctors never get the chance to practise medicine in our hospitals. 絕大部分難民醫生在我們的醫院裡從未得到行醫的機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Chance</b> is also a noun. 偶然; 意外","examples":["...a victim of chance and circumstance. …一個時運不濟的倒黴者。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chance</b> meeting or event is one that is not planned or expected. 偶然的","examples":["...a chance meeting. …一次邂逅。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chance</b> something, you do it even though there is a risk that you may not succeed or that something bad may happen. 冒…險","examples":["Andy knew the risks. I cannot believe he would have chanced it. 安迪知道那些風險，我不能相信他會冒那個險。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that happens <b>by chance</b> was not planned by anyone. 偶然地; 意外地","examples":["He had met Mr. Maude by chance. 他曾與莫德先生邂逅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>by any chance</b> when you are asking questions in order to find out whether something that you think might be true is actually true. 可能","examples":["Are they by any chance related? 他們可能有關聯嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>stands a chance</b> <b>of</b> achieving something, you mean that they are likely to achieve it. If you say that someone doesn't <b>stand a chance</b> <b>of</b> achieving something, you mean that they cannot possibly achieve it. 有可能","examples":["Being very good at science subjects, I stood a good chance of gaining high grades. 我很擅長理科科目，所以很有可能得高分。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>take a chance</b>, you try to do something although there is a large risk of danger or failure. 碰運氣; 冒險","examples":["You take a chance on the weather if you holiday in Maine. 你若在緬因州度假，對天氣得碰運氣。","Retailers are taking no chances on unknown brands. 零售商們不在無名品牌上冒險。"]}]}]},"child":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兒童，小孩；子女；深受（某時期思想）影響的人；孩子氣的人，幼稚的人；缺乏經驗的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>child</b> is a human being who is not yet an adult. 小孩","examples":["When I was a child I lived in a country village. 小時候我住在鄉村裡。","...a child of six. …一個6歲的小孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>children</b> are their sons and daughters of any age. 子女","examples":["How are the children? 孩子們好嗎？","His children have left home. 他的兒女們已經離開家了。"]}]}]},"catch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"接住；抓住，握住；逮住，捕獲；發現，撞見；鉤住，絆住；擊中，碰到；得病，染病；引起，吸引（注意或興趣）；（對某事）感到興奮；搭乘，趕上；及時做（或談等）；出席，觀看；表現，再現；使措手不及；察覺，瞥見；聽清，理解；突然意識到；盛住（液體）；（板球）使被接殺出局；（棒球中）當接球手；受（光）照射；（風或水）裹挾，推動；著火，燃燒；遭遇，陷入（困境）；固定，繫牢；被（懸浮物）覆蓋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"接（球等）；（魚的）捕獲量，捕獲物；<舊>理想的物件；門閂，吊扣；（聲息）哽塞；隱患，隱藏的困難；（樂）輪唱片段；傳接球遊戲；捉人遊戲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> a person or animal, you capture them after chasing them, or by using a trap, net, or other device. 捉住; 捕獲","examples":["Police say they are confident of catching the gunman. 警方說他們有信心抓獲槍手。","Where did you catch the fish? 你在哪兒捕到了這條魚？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> an object that is moving through the air, you seize it with your hands. 接住","examples":["I jumped up to catch a ball and fell over. 我跳起來接球，結果摔倒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> a part of someone's body, you take or seize it with your hand, often in order to stop them from going somewhere. 抓住; 握住","examples":["Liz caught his arm. 利茲抓住了他的胳膊。","He knelt beside her and caught her hand in both of his. 他跪在她旁邊，雙手握住她的手。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>catches</b> another, it hits it accidentally or manages to hit it. 打擊; 擊中","examples":["The stinging slap almost caught his face. 這狠狠的一巴掌差點打在他的臉上。","I may have caught him with my elbow but it was just an accident. 我的胳膊肘可能碰了他，不過那只是個意外。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>catch</b> a bus, train, or plane, you get on it in order to travel somewhere. 搭上; 趕上 (車、飛機等)","examples":["We were in plenty of time for Anthony to catch the ferry. 我們有足夠的時間等安東尼搭上渡船。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> someone doing something wrong, you see or find them doing it. 撞見; 發現","examples":["He caught a youth breaking into a car. 他撞見一青年正在撬一輛車。","I don't want to catch you pushing yourself into the picture to get some personal publicity. 我不想看到你為出點風頭而搶鏡頭。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> <b>yourself</b> doing something, especially something surprising, you suddenly become aware that you are doing it. (突然) 發覺","examples":["I caught myself feeling almost sorry for poor Mr. Laurence. 我突然發覺自己幾乎是在為可憐的勞倫斯先生感到難過了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> something or <b>catch</b> a glimpse of it, you notice it or manage to see it briefly. 瞥見; 突然看到","examples":["As she turned back she caught the puzzled look on her mother's face. 她轉身時瞥到母親一臉茫然的神情。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> something that someone has said, you manage to hear it. 聽到","examples":["His ears caught a faint cry. 他的耳朵聽到微弱的哭聲。","I do not believe I caught your name. 我想我沒聽清你的名字。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> a TV or radio programme or an event, you manage to see or listen to it. 收看; 收聽","examples":["Bill turns on the radio to catch the local news. 比爾開啟收音機收聽地方新聞。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> someone, you manage to contact or meet them to talk to them, especially when they are just about to go somewhere else. 聯絡上","examples":["I dialled Elizabeth's number thinking I might catch her before she left for work. 我撥了伊麗莎白的電話號碼，心想我或許能趕在她動身上班前和她取得聯絡。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something or someone <b>catches</b> you by surprise or at a bad time, you were not expecting them or do not feel able to deal with them. 驚擾","examples":["She looked as if the photographer had caught her by surprise. 她看起來好像是被攝影師嚇了一跳。","I'm sorry but I just cannot say anything. You've caught me at a bad time. 很抱歉我真的無可奉告。你找我找得很不是時候。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something <b>catches</b> your attention or your eye, you notice it or become interested in it. 引起 (注意、興趣); 吸引住","examples":["My shoes caught his attention. 我的鞋子引起了他的注意。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> a cold or a disease, you become ill with it. 患上; 染上 (疾病)","examples":["The more stress you are under, the more likely you are to catch a cold. 你所受的壓力越大，越有可能患感冒。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something <b>catches</b> the light or if the light <b>catches</b> it, it reflects the light and looks bright or shiny. 受 (光) 照射; (光) 照射於","examples":["They saw the ship's guns, catching the light of the moon. 他們看到船上的槍支映著月光閃閃發亮。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>are caught</b> in a storm or other unpleasant situation, it happens when you cannot avoid its effects. 遭遇 (暴風雨、不幸)","examples":["When he was fishing off the island he was caught in a storm and almost drowned. 他離島出海釣魚時遭遇暴風雨襲擊，差點被淹死。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>are caught between</b> two alternatives or two people, you do not know which one to choose or follow. 左右為難","examples":["The Jordanian leader is caught between both sides in the dispute. 這位約旦元首夾在爭執雙方之間左右為難。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Catch</b> is also a noun. 接住","examples":["He missed the catch and the game was lost. 他沒接住球，輸了這場比賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>catch</b> on a window, door, or container is a device that fastens it. 窗鉤; 門閂; 釦子","examples":["She fiddled with the catch of her bag. 她撥弄著提包的鎖釦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>catch</b> is a hidden problem or difficulty in a plan or an offer that seems surprisingly good. 隱藏的困難; 意料不到的情況","examples":["The catch is that you work for your supper, and the food and accommodations can be very basic. 問題在於你工作是為了頓飯，而且吃住條件非常一般。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>catches</b> <b>on</b> or <b>in</b> an object, it accidentally becomes attached to the object or stuck in it. 絆住; 卡住","examples":["Her ankle caught on a root, and she almost lost her balance. 她的腳踝絆到一個樹根上，身體差點失去平衡。"]}]}]},"church":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教堂；禮拜儀式；教派，教會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>把（產婦等）帶到教堂做感恩禮拜；<美>對……進行教會裁決"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"教會的；禮拜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>church</b> is a building in which Christians worship. You usually refer to this place as <b>church</b> when you are talking about the time that people spend there. 教堂","examples":["...one of the country's most historic churches. …該國家歷史上最著名的教堂之一。","...St Helen's Church. …聖海倫教堂。","The family had gone to church. 這家人都去教堂了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>Church</b> is one of the groups of people within the Christian religion, for example Catholics or Methodists, that have their own beliefs, clergy, and forms of worship. (基督教的) 教派","examples":["...cooperation with the Catholic Church. …與天主教派的合作。","Church leaders said he was welcome to return. 該教派領袖說歡迎他回皈。"]}]}]},"city":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"城市，都市；市民，全市居民；市政府；<非正式>充滿……的地方；<英>倫敦金融、商業區；<英>（國王或女王授權的）特許市；<美>（由州政府劃定市界並授予特權的）特權市"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>city</b> is a large town. 城市","examples":["...the city of Bologna. …波洛尼亞市。"]}]}]},"check":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"檢查，核對；檢視，查詢；剋制，抑制；存放，寄放；託運；在……上打鉤；將（對方的）軍"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"檢查，核對；制止（手段），抑制（手段）；結賬單；支票（=cheque）；方格圖案；衣帽寄存處；寄存憑證；鉤號；（國際象棋）將軍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>check</b> something such as a piece of information or a document, you make sure that it is correct or satisfactory. 檢查; 核實","examples":["Check the accuracy of everything in your résumé. 核查你簡歷中每一項的準確性。","I think there is an age limit, but I'd have to check. 我覺得是有年齡限制的，但我得去核實一下。","She hadn't checked whether she had a clean, ironed shirt. 她沒有檢視自己是否有件乾淨並熨好的襯衣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>check</b> something that is written on a piece of paper, you put a mark, like a V with the right side extended, next to it to show that something is correct or has been selected or dealt with. 打勾","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>check</b> something, usually something bad, means to stop it from spreading or continuing. 抑制","examples":["Sex education is also expected to help check the spread of AIDS. 性教育也有望抑制艾滋病的蔓延。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>check</b> your luggage at an airport, you give it to an official so that it can be taken on to your plane. 託運","examples":["We arrived at the airport, checked our baggage and wandered around the gift shops. 我們到達了機場，託運了行李，然後逛了逛禮品店。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Check</b> is also a noun. 檢查; 核實","examples":["He is being constantly monitored with regular checks on his blood pressure. 他一直受到持續地監測，接受定期的血壓檢測。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>check</b> in a restaurant is a piece of paper on which the price of your meal is written and which you are given before you pay. (餐館的) 賬單","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A pattern of squares, usually of two colours, can be referred to as <b>checks</b> or a <b>check</b>. 格子圖案 (通常雙色)","examples":["Styles include stripes and checks. 樣式有條紋的和格子的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>check on</b> someone or something, you make sure they are in a safe or satisfactory condition. 察看","examples":["Stephen checked on her several times during the night. 斯蒂芬夜間察看了她幾次。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>check in</b> your luggage means the same as to  it. 託運","examples":["They checked in their luggage and found seats in the departure lounge. 他們託運了行李，然後在候機室找到了座位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is held in check</b> or <b>is kept in check</b>, they are controlled and prevented from becoming too great or powerful. 抑制住某物","examples":["Life on Earth will become unsustainable unless population growth is held in check. 地球上的生命將無法延續，除非人口增長得到控制。"]}]}]},"climb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攀登，攀爬；爬升，升高；上升，升值；提高社會地位，晉升；吃力地爬（移動）；（植物）攀緣而上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"攀登，爬升；攀登的地方，攀登物；增值，上升；提高地位，晉升"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>climb</b> something such as a tree, mountain, or ladder, or <b>climb</b> <b>up</b> it, you move toward the top of it. If you <b>climb</b> <b>down</b> it, you move toward the bottom of it. 爬","examples":["Climbing the first hill took half an hour. 爬第一座山花了半個小時。","I told her about him climbing up the drainpipe. 我把他爬排水管的事告訴了她。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Climb</b> is also a noun. 爬","examples":["...an hour's leisurely climb through olive groves and vineyards. …橄欖叢和葡萄園中的一個小時的悠閒攀爬。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>climb</b> somewhere, you move there carefully, for example because you are moving into a small space or trying to avoid falling. 小心翼翼地爬","examples":["The girls hurried outside, climbed into the car, and drove off. 女孩子們趕緊跑了出去，爬進車裡，開走了。","He must have climbed out of his bed. 他肯定已經爬下了床。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something such as an aeroplane <b>climbs</b>, it moves upward to a higher position. When the sun <b>climbs</b>, it moves higher in the sky. (飛機、太陽) 爬升","examples":["The plane took off for L.A., lost an engine as it climbed, and crashed just off the runway. 那架飛機起飛前往洛杉磯，在升空時掉了一個引擎，就在跑道邊上墜機了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>climbs</b>, it increases in value or amount. (價值、數量) 上漲","examples":["The nation's unemployment rate has been climbing steadily since last June. 去年6月以來這個國家的失業率在穩步持續上升。","Prices have climbed by 21% since the beginning of the year. 今年年初以來價格已經上漲了21%。"]}]}]},"cocoa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可可粉；可可豆；可可飲料；深褐色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cocoa</b> is a brown powder made from the seeds of a tropical tree. It is used in making chocolate. 可可粉","examples":["The Ivory Coast became the world's leading cocoa producer. 象牙海岸成了世界上領先的可可粉生產地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cocoa</b> is a hot drink made from cocoa powder and milk or water. 熱巧克力","examples":["...a cup of cocoa. …一杯熱巧克力。"]}]}]},"class":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"班級；（一節）課，上課時間；（某一科目的）課程；階級，階層；等級劃分，等級制度；（貨物、服務或人的）等級，類別；（飛機、火車等的）艙位等級，車廂等級；品味；同屆畢業生；<英>（英國大學的）學位等級；（生物）（植物或動物分類的）綱；（比賽的）組別"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……歸類，把……看作；把……編入某一班級；屬於……類（或等級），被列為某類（或某級）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>優秀的，出色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>class</b> is a group of students who are taught together. 班","examples":["He had to spend about six months in a class with younger students. 他不得不在一個比他小的學生的班上呆了大約六個月。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>class</b> is a course of teaching in a particular subject. 課程","examples":["He acquired a law degree by taking classes at night. 他透過上晚上的課獲得了法律學位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>class</b> <b>of</b> things is a group of them with similar characteristics. 種類","examples":["Harbour staff noticed that measurements given for the same class of boats often varied. 港口員工們注意到對同一類小船所給出的尺寸經常不同。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>in class</b>, you do it during a lesson in school. 課","examples":["There is lots of reading in class. 課上有大量閱讀。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>class</b>, you mean that they are elegant and sophisticated. 品位","examples":["The most elegant woman I've ever met – she had class in every sense of the word. 我曾見過的最高雅的女人–從各種意義上講她都有品位。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The students in a school or college who finish their course in a particular year are often referred to as the <b>class of</b> that year. 同屆學生","examples":["These two members of Yale's Class of '57 never miss a reunion. 這兩位耶魯57屆的同學從未錯過一次重聚聯歡會。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Class</b> refers to the division of people in a society into groups according to their social status. 階級","examples":["...the relationship between social classes. …社會階級間的關係。","What it will do is create a whole new ruling class. 它要做的就是創造一個全新的統治階級。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is classed as</b> a particular thing, they are regarded as belonging to that group of things. 把…歸類為","examples":["Since they can and do successfully inter-breed, they cannot be classed as different species. 既然它們能夠而且確實可以成功雜交繁殖，它們就不能被歸為不同的物種。","I class myself as an ordinary working person. 我把自己歸類為一名普通的勞動者。"]}]}]},"coat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外套，大衣；<美>（指套裝的）短上衣；（動物）皮毛，（植物）表皮；塗料層，覆蓋層"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……塗上，用……覆蓋；給……穿外套"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coat</b> is a piece of clothing with long sleeves which you wear over your other clothes when you go outside. 外套","examples":["He turned off the television, put on his coat, and walked out. 他關掉電視，穿上外套，走了出去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An animal's <b>coat</b> is the fur or hair on its body. (動物的) 皮毛","examples":["Vitamin B6 is great for improving the condition of dogs' and horses' coats. 維生素B6對改善狗和馬的皮毛非常有效。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>coat</b> <b>of</b> paint or varnish is a thin layer of it on a surface. (油漆、清漆等的) 層","examples":["The front door needs a new coat of paint. 前門要新刷一層油漆。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>coat</b> something <b>with</b> a substance or <b>in</b> a substance, you cover it with a thin layer of the substance. 塗上","examples":["Coat the fish with seasoned flour. 往魚身上塗調好味道的麵粉。"]}]}]},"clock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時鐘，時鐘的；考勤鍾（the clock）；里程錶（the clock）；（比賽）計時器，時間段（the clock）；速度計（the clock）；<英>（尤指蒲公英的）絨毛頭；<英，非正式>人臉；（電腦）啟動與同步內部操作的電子裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"達到，記錄下（一定時間，距離，速度）；記錄（時間，速度）；打卡；<英，非正式>注意；<非正式>痛打，狠揍；回撥里程錶作弊；獲（勝）；需時"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clock</b> is an instrument that shows what time of day it is. 鍾","examples":["He was conscious of a clock ticking. 他意識到了時間正在消逝。","...a digital clock. …一個數字時鐘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A time <b>clock</b> in a factory or office is a device that is used to record the hours that people work. Each worker puts a special card into the device when they arrive and leave, and the times are recorded on the card. 考勤刷卡機","examples":["Government workers were made to punch time clocks morning, noon and night. 政府工作人員被要求早晨、中午和晚上要在考勤機上打卡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an ornamental design either woven in or embroidered on the side of a stocking (長襪的)花邊設計","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clock</b> a particular time or speed in a race means to reach that time or speed. 以…的速度競賽","examples":["Elliott clocked the fastest time this year for the 800 metres. 埃利奧特跑出了今年800米的最快速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is clocked</b> <b>at</b> a particular time or speed, their time or speed is measured at that level. 測…的速度","examples":["He has been clocked at 11 seconds for 100 metres. 他100米跑的速度已被測出是11秒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to strike, esp on the face or head 打(在臉上或頭上)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are doing something <b>against the clock</b>, you are doing it in a great hurry, because there is very little time. 爭分奪秒","examples":["The emergency services were working against the clock as the tide began to rise. 潮水開始上漲，應急部門正在爭分奪秒地工作著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is done <b>around the clock</b> or <b>round the clock</b>, it is done all day and all night without stopping. 夜以繼日","examples":["Rescue services have been working round the clock to free stranded motorists. 救援工作一直在晝夜不停地進行著，來解救被困的開車的人們。"]}]}]},"coast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海岸，海濱；（車輛的）滑行"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人，車輛）滑行；毫不費力地做，（尤指）輕鬆獲勝；不夠努力，應付；沿海航行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>coast</b> is an area of land that is next to the sea. 海岸","examples":["Campsites are usually situated along the coast, close to beaches. 宿營地通常都在海岸邊，靠近沙灘的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>coasts</b> somewhere, it continues to move there with the motor switched off, or without being pushed or pedalled. (車輛的) 慣性滑行","examples":["He pushed in the clutch and coasted to a halt. 他踩下離合器，滑行了一會兒便停下來了。"]}]}]},"cloud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雲，雲朵；雲狀物，一團；陰影，令人憂慮的事；皺眉，沮喪的表情"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……搞糊塗，使難以理解；破壞，給……蒙上陰影；（使）顯得陰沉；模糊不清，（使）起霧；佈滿雲；使（房間、天空等）煙霧繚繞，使塵土飛揚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cloud</b> is a mass of water vapour that floats in the sky. Clouds are usually white or grey in colour. 雲","examples":["...the varied shapes of the clouds. …雲朵的各種形狀。","...a black mass of cloud. …一團烏雲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cloud</b> <b>of</b> something such as smoke or dust is a mass of it floating in the air. (煙塵) 團","examples":["The hens darted away on all sides, raising a cloud of dust. 母雞四處飛奔，揚起一團塵土。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>clouds</b> your view of a situation, you mean that it makes you unable to understand the situation or judge it properly. 矇蔽","examples":["Perhaps anger had clouded his vision, perhaps his judgment had been faulty. 也許怒火矇蔽了他的眼睛，也許他的判斷有誤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>clouds</b> a situation, you mean that it makes it unpleasant. 使不快","examples":["The atmosphere has already been clouded by the party's anger at the media. 該黨對媒體的憤怒已經使得氣氛很不愉快。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If glass <b>clouds</b> or if moisture <b>clouds</b> it, tiny drops of water cover the glass, making it difficult to see through. 起霧","examples":["The mirror clouded beside her cheek. 緊貼她臉頰的鏡子起了霧。"]}]}]},"coffee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"咖啡（飲品）；一杯咖啡；咖啡豆或咖啡粉；咖啡色；咖啡樹；（Coffee）人名，（英）科菲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Coffee</b> is a hot drink made with water and ground or powdered coffee beans. 咖啡","examples":["Would you like some coffee? 你想喝點咖啡嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>coffee</b> is a cup of coffee. 一杯咖啡","examples":["I made a coffee. 我衝了一杯咖啡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Coffee</b> is the roasted beans or powder from which the drink is made. 咖啡豆; 咖啡粉","examples":["Brazil harvested 28 million bags of coffee in 1991, the biggest crop for four years. 1991年巴西收穫了2800萬袋咖啡豆，這是4年來的最大收成。"]}]}]},"cola":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可樂飲料，一杯可樂；可樂果樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cola</b> is a sweet, brown, nonalcoholic carbonated drink. 可樂","examples":["...a can of cola. …一罐可樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"either of two tropical sterculiaceous trees, <b>Cola nitida</b> or <b>C. acuminata,</b> widely cultivated in tropical regions for their seeds 可樂樹; 喜樹","examples":[]}]}]},"coke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可口可樂， 一瓶（罐，杯）可口可樂（Coke）；焦炭，焦煤；（汽油或其他燃料不完全燃燒後所剩的）廢氣渣；<非正式>可卡因，古柯鹼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（煤）煉成焦炭；（尤指用可卡因）使……麻醉；吸食可卡因"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Coke</b> is a solid, black substance that is produced from coal and is burned as a fuel. 焦炭","examples":["...a coke-burning stove. …一個燒焦炭的爐子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Coke</b> is the same as . 可卡因","examples":[]}]}]},"clean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"潔淨的，乾淨的；講衛生的，愛乾淨的；無有害物的，無汙染的；清醇的，清新的；無汙點的，清白的；公正的，遵守規則的；不私藏違禁品的；沒吸毒的，沒喝酒的；純潔的，正派的；文明的，無色情的；平滑的，平整的；迅速徹底的；（行動）乾淨利落的；空白的，未寫過的；（檔案）無錯誤的；（木材）無樹節的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）清潔，清理；變乾淨；清掃，做清潔工；乾洗；（烹飪前）清除（動物）內臟"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"清潔，清掃，打掃"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"徹底地，完全地；乾淨地，純潔地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>clean</b> is free from dirt or unwanted marks. 清潔的","examples":["The subway is efficient and spotlessly clean. 地鐵快，而且一塵不染。","Tiled kitchen floors are easy to keep clean. 鋪了地磚的廚房地面容易保持清潔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that people or animals are <b>clean</b> when they keep themselves or their surroundings clean. 愛乾淨的","examples":["We like pigs, they're very clean. 我們喜歡豬，它們很愛乾淨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>clean</b> fuel or chemical process does not create many harmful or polluting substances. 無汙染的","examples":["Fans of electric cars say they are clean, quiet, and economical. 電動車愛好者說電動車無汙染，無噪音，而且經濟。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something such as a book, joke, or lifestyle as <b>clean</b>, you think that they are not sexually immoral or offensive. 純潔的; 不淫穢的","examples":["They're trying to show clean, wholesome, decent movies. 他們在努力放純潔、健康、正派的電影。","Flirting is good clean fun. 調情是謔而不虐。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a <b>clean</b> reputation or record, they have never done anything illegal or wrong. 清白的","examples":["Accusations of tax evasion have tarnished his clean image. 逃稅的指控玷汙了他清廉的形象。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>clean</b> game or fight is carried out fairly, according to the rules. 公正的","examples":["He called for a clean fight in the election and an end to \"negative campaigning.\" 他呼籲在競選中公正交鋒，停止“消極競選”。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>clean</b> sheet of paper has no writing or drawing on it. (紙張) 空白的","examples":["Take a clean sheet of paper and down the left-hand side make a list. 拿一張白紙，在左下邊列個清單。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"公正地","examples":["The game had been cleanly fought. 這場比賽打得公平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Clean</b> is used to emphasize that something was done completely. 徹底地","examples":["It burned clean through the seat of my overalls. 把我的連身工作服的臀部全給燒穿了。","The thief got clean away with the money. 賊偷了錢逃之夭夭了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>clean</b> something or <b>clean</b> dirt off it, you make it free from dirt and unwanted marks, for example by washing or wiping it. If something <b>cleans</b> easily, it is easy to clean. 把…弄乾淨; 清潔","examples":["Her father cleaned his glasses with a paper napkin. 她父親用一張餐巾紙擦他的眼鏡。","It took half an hour to clean the orange powder off the bathtub. 用了半個小時才把浴缸裡的橙色粉末擦掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>clean</b> a room or house, you make the inside of it and the furniture in it free from dirt and dust. 打掃 (房間、房子); 打掃衛生","examples":["Mary cooked and cleaned for them. 瑪麗為他們做飯、打掃衛生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"清潔","examples":["The windows will have to be given a thorough cleaning. 窗戶必須得做徹底的清潔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"打掃衛生的工作","examples":["I do the cleaning myself. 我自己做打掃衛生的工作。"]}]}]},"cooky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餅乾，小甜餅（等於 cookie）"}],"sections":[]},"cookie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"曲奇餅，小甜餅；……樣的人；（瀏覽網頁後儲存在計算機的）快取檔案；<蘇格蘭>淡麵包；漂亮的年輕女子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cookie</b> is a small sweet cake. 小甜餅乾","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cookie</b> is a piece of computer software which enables a website you have visited to recognize you if you visit it again. 再次訪問某一網站時，能令網站識別訪問人的計算機軟體","examples":[]}]}]},"color":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顏色，色彩；膚色；有色人種（常用於 people of color 等短語）；顏料；臉色，氣色；生動，趣味，地方色彩"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"給……著色，塗顏色；影響，左右；歪曲，粉飾"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"變色，呈現顏色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"彩色的，能產生彩色的（用於名詞前）"}],"sections":[]},"cook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廚師，炊事員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"煮，燒；烹飪，烹調；<非正式>發生，計劃中；<美，非正式>幹得起勁，幹得好；<非正式>篡改，偽造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>cook</b> a meal, you prepare food for eating by heating it. 烹調","examples":["I have to go and cook dinner. 我要去做飯了。","Chefs at the restaurant once cooked for President Kennedy. 這家飯店的廚師曾經給肯尼迪總統做過飯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>cook</b> food, or when food <b>cooks</b>, it is heated until it is ready to be eaten. 烹製","examples":["...some basic instructions on how to cook a turkey. ...火雞的一些基本做法。","Let the vegetables cook gently for about 10 minutes. 把蔬菜小火煮約十分鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"烹飪","examples":["Her hobbies include music, dancing, sport, and cooking. 她的愛好包括音樂、跳舞、運動和烹飪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cook</b> is a person whose job is to prepare and cook food, especially in someone's home or in an institution. (職業) 廚師","examples":["They had a butler, a cook, and a maid. 他們有一位管家、一位廚師和一位女僕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is a good <b>cook</b>, you mean they are good at preparing and cooking food. 廚師 (指擅長烹調的人)","examples":["I'm a lousy cook. 我是個蹩腳的廚師。"]}]}]},"cop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"警察；管紗，緯管；<愛爾蘭>精明，明智"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"抓獲，逮捕；遭受，蒙受；收到，得到；表明，擺出；偷，盜竊；<非正式>失敗，送命（cop out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cop</b> is a policeman or policewoman. 警察","examples":["Frank didn't like having the cops know where to find him. 弗蘭克不願意讓警察知道他的去向。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"worth or value 價值","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to seize or catch 抓住","examples":[]}]}]},"corn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"穀物，穀粒；玉米；雞眼；老一套，煽情的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"醃（肉類等）；使成粒狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Corn</b> is a tall plant which produces long vegetables covered with yellow seeds. It can also be used to refer to the yellow seeds. 玉米; 玉米粒","examples":["...rows of corn in an Iowa field. …愛荷華州農田裡成排的玉米。","We're having corn-on-the-cob for lunch. 我們吃玉米棒子當午飯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Corn</b> is used to refer to crops such as wheat and barley. It can also be used to refer to the seeds from these plants. 穀物 (指小麥、燕麥等); (小麥、燕麥等的) 穀粒","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a hardening or thickening of the skin around a central point in the foot, caused by pressure or friction 雞眼","examples":[]}]}]},"common":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"共同的，共享的；常見的，普遍的，一般的；普通的，平凡的；出於禮貌的，起碼的；粗俗的，庸俗的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"公共用地，公地；校園公共食堂；<英，非正式>常識；（基督教教會適用於各種場合的）普通禮拜；平民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>common</b>, it is found in large numbers or it happens often. 常見的","examples":["His name was Hansen, a common name in Norway. 他叫漢森，一個在挪威很常見的名字。","Oil pollution is the most common cause of death for seabirds. 石油汙染是海鳥死亡的最常見的原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>common</b> <b>to</b> two or more people or groups, it is done, possessed, or used by them all. 共同的; 共有的; 共用的","examples":["Moldavians and Romanians share a common language. 摩爾達維亞人和羅馬尼亞人使用一種共同的語言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When there are more animals or plants of a particular species than there are of related species, then the first species is called <b>common</b>. (物種) 常見的","examples":["...the common house fly. …常見的家蠅。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Common</b> is used to indicate that someone or something is of the ordinary kind and not special in any way. 普通的","examples":["Democracy might elevate the common man to a position of political superiority. 民主可能會讓普通人升至政治上優越的位置。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Common</b> decency or <b>common</b> courtesy is the decency or courtesy which most people have. You usually talk about this when someone has not shown these characteristics in their behaviour to show your disapproval of them. 起碼的 (修養、禮貌等)","examples":["It is common decency to give your seat to anyone in greater need. 把座位讓給更需要的人是起碼的修養。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>common</b> to describe knowledge, an opinion, or a feeling that is shared by people in general. 普遍的 (知識、觀點、情感等)","examples":["It is common knowledge that swimming is one of the best forms of exercise. 游泳是最好的運動之一是普遍常識。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe someone or their behaviour as <b>common</b>, you mean that they show a lack of taste, education, and good manners. 粗俗的","examples":["She might be a little common at times, but she was certainly not boring. 她也許有時會有點兒粗俗，但她絕不令人厭煩。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"常見地","examples":["Parsley is one of the most commonly used herbs. 歐芹是最常用的草藥之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"普遍地","examples":["A little adolescent rebellion is commonly believed to be healthy. 少許青春期叛逆被普遍認為是一個健康的現象。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>common</b> is an area of grassy land, usually in or near a village or small town, where the public is allowed to go. 公共草地","examples":["We are warning women not to go out on to the common alone. 我們在告誡女性不要單獨去公共草地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more things have something <b>in common</b>, they have the same characteristic or feature. 共同的 (特點等)","examples":["The oboe and the clarinet have certain features in common. 雙簧管和單簧管有某些共同特點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two or more people have something <b>in common</b>, they share the same interests or experiences. 共同的 (興趣或經歷)","examples":["He had very little in common with his sister. 他和他姐姐幾乎沒有相同之處。"]}]}]},"cold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冷的，涼的；冷淡的，冷漠的；冷色調的；已變淡的；失去知覺的；真實的，客觀的；掃興的，灰濛濛的；遠未猜中的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"感冒，傷風；寒冷，低溫"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"突然地，徹底地；毫無準備地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>cold</b> has a very low temperature or a lower temperature than is normal or acceptable. 冷的","examples":["Rinse the vegetables under cold running water. 用冷自來水沖洗蔬菜。","He likes his tea neither too hot nor too cold. 他喜歡茶不太燙也不太涼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is <b>cold</b>, or if a place is <b>cold</b>, the temperature of the air is very low. 寒冷的","examples":["It was bitterly cold. 天氣冷得刺骨。","The house is cold because I can't afford to turn the heat on. 屋子冷冰冰的，因為我開不起暖氣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>cold</b>, your body is at an unpleasantly low temperature. 感覺冷的","examples":["I was freezing cold. 我快凍僵了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Cold</b> colours or <b>cold</b> light give an impression of coldness. (顏色或燈光) 冷的","examples":["Generally, warm colours advance in painting and cold colours recede. 一般來說，先上暖色調油漆，再上冷色調油漆。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>cold</b> person does not show much emotion, especially affection, and therefore seems unfriendly and unsympathetic. If someone's voice is <b>cold</b>, they speak in an unfriendly, unsympathetic way. 冷漠的; 不友好的","examples":["What a cold, unfeeling woman she was. 她是一個多麼冷漠無情的女人啊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"冷","examples":["She complained about the coldness of his hands. 她抱怨他的那雙手冷冰冰的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"寒冷","examples":["Within a quarter of an hour, the coldness of the night had gone. 一刻鐘之內，夜晚的寒冷就消退了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Cold weather or low temperatures can be referred to as <b>the</b> <b>cold</b>. (天氣或氣溫的) 寒冷","examples":["He must have come inside to get out of the cold. 他肯定進來避過寒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>cold</b>, you have a mild, very common illness which makes you sneeze a lot and gives you a sore throat or a cough. 感冒","examples":["I had a pretty bad cold. 我得了很重的感冒。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"冷漠地; 不友好地","examples":["\"I'll see you in the morning,\" Hugh said coldly. “我會在早上見你，”休冷冷地說。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>catch cold</b>, or <b>catch a cold</b>, you become ill with a cold. 患感冒","examples":["Let's dry our hair so we don't catch cold. 我們把頭髮弄乾吧，省得患感冒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>out cold</b>, they are unconscious or sleeping very heavily. 失去知覺的; 沉睡的","examples":["She was out cold but still breathing. 她失去了知覺，但還在呼吸。"]}]}]},"close":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）關閉；合上，合攏；（使）暫時性關閉；（永久）停業，停止活動；（使）結束，（使）停止；關閉（計算機程式）；（股票等）收盤；拉近（距離），縮小（差距）；抱住，抓住，握住；（使）（傷口）癒合；封鎖（公路、公園等）；完成，做成（交易等）；接通（電路）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"接近的；酷似的，幾乎相等的；快要……的；（壞事）險些發生的；近親的；親近的，親密的；（關聯）密切的；仔細的，全面的；勢均力敵的；悶熱的，不通風的；密集的，空間很小的；（頭髮或鬍子）齊根的；守口如瓶的，掩飾感情的；吝嗇的，小氣的；嚴加保護（守衛）的；閉塞音的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（空間或時間上）接近地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"結束，結尾；（大教堂的）圍地；死衚衕；<英>英國某些傳統公學的操場；<蘇格蘭>通路，入口；（股市一日的）收盤（the close）；（板球一日比賽的）終賽（the close）；（樂）短句結尾，收束；關閉（尤指關門）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>close</b> something such as a door or lid or when it <b>closes</b>, it moves so that a hole, gap, or opening is covered. 關閉; 閉合","examples":["If you are cold, close the window. 如果你冷就關上窗戶。","Zacharias heard the door close. 札哈里亞斯聽到門關上了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>close</b> something such as an open book or umbrella, you move the different parts of it together. 把 (書、傘等) 合上","examples":["Slowly he closed the book. 慢慢地他把書合上了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>close</b> something such as a computer file or window, you give the computer an instruction to remove it from the screen. 關閉 (計算機檔案、視窗)","examples":["To close your document, press CTRL+W on your keyboard. 要關閉你的檔案同時按下鍵盤上的CTRL和W鍵。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>close</b> your eyes or your eyes <b>close</b>, your eyelids move downward, so that you can no longer see. 閉上眼睛","examples":["Bess closed her eyes and fell asleep. 貝絲閉上眼睛，睡著了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a place <b>closes</b> or <b>is closed</b>, work or activity stops there for a short period. (地方) 暫時關閉","examples":["Shops close only on Christmas Day and New Year's Day. 商店只在聖誕日和元旦停業。","Government troops closed the airport. 政府軍隊臨時關閉了機場。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a place such as a factory, shop, or school <b>closes</b>, or if it <b>is closed</b>, all work or activity stops there permanently. 使永久關閉; 永久關閉","examples":["Many enterprises will be forced to close. 許多企業將被迫關閉。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"To <b>close</b> a road or border means to block it in order to prevent people from using it. 封鎖 (道路、邊境)","examples":["They were cut off from the West in 1948 when their government closed that border crossing. 當他們的政府於1948年封鎖了那個那個邊境通道以後，他們與西方國家的聯絡就被切斷了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>close</b> a conversation, event, or matter means to bring it to an end or to complete it. 結束","examples":["Judge Isabel Oliva said last night: \"I have closed the case. There was no foul play.\" 伊莎貝爾•奧莉芙法官昨晚說：“我已經結案了，其中沒有違規做法。”","The governor is said to now consider the matter closed. 據說州長認為此事已經了結了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>close</b> a bank account, you take all your money out of it and inform the bank that you will no longer be using the account. 結清 (銀行賬戶)","examples":["He had closed his account with the bank five years earlier. 他早在5年前就已經跟銀行結清了戶頭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Close down</b> means the same as <b>close</b>. 永久關閉","examples":["Minford closed down the business and went into politics. 明福特關了買賣，進入了政界。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"關閉","examples":["...since the closing of the steel mill in 1984. …自從1984年鋼鐵廠的關閉以來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"親密關係","examples":["I asked whether her closeness to her mother ever posed any problems. 我問她與她母親的親密關係是否曾帶來過問題。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"On the stock market or the currency markets, if a share price or a currency <b>closes</b> at a particular value, that is its value at the end of the day's business. (股票) 收盤","examples":["The U.S. dollar closed higher in Tokyo today. 美元今天在東京的收盤價更高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are closing</b> <b>on</b> someone or something that you are following, you are getting nearer and nearer to them. 接近","examples":["I was within 15 seconds of the guy in second place and closing on him. 我當時和第2名相距15秒，而且逐步向他接近。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person is <b>close</b> <b>to</b> another, there is only a very small distance between them. 靠近的","examples":["Her lips were close to his head and her breath tickled his ear. 她的嘴唇靠近他的頭，她的氣息輕撓他的耳朵。","The man moved closer, lowering his voice. 那個男人湊得更近了，壓低了聲音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that people are <b>close</b> <b>to</b> each other when they like each other very much and know each other very well. 親密的","examples":["She and Linda became very close. 她和琳達變得很親密。","I shared a house with a close friend from school. 我和學校的一位密友共住一座房子"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>close</b> relatives are the members of your family who are most directly related to you, for example your parents and your brothers or sisters. 直系的","examples":["...large changes such as the birth of a child or death of a close relative. …如孩子的誕生或直系親屬的死亡之類的巨大變化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>close</b> ally or partner of someone knows them well and is very involved in their work. (工作上) 關係密切的","examples":["He was once regarded as one of Mr. Brown's closest political advisers. 他曾一度被認為是與布朗先生關係最密切的政治顧問之一。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Close</b> contact or cooperation involves seeing or communicating with someone often. (接觸、合作) 緊密的","examples":["Both nations are seeking closer links with the West. 這兩個國家都正在尋求與西方國家更緊密的聯絡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If there is a <b>close</b> connection or resemblance between two things, they are strongly connected or are very similar. 緊密的 (關聯); 相似的","examples":["There is a close connection between pain and tension. 疼痛和緊張之間有緊密的關聯。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Close</b> inspection or observation of something is careful and thorough. 全面細緻的","examples":["He discovered, on closer inspection, that the rocks contained gold. 透過更周密的探查，他發現那些岩石中含有黃金。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>close</b> competition or election is won or seems likely to be won by only a small amount. 勢均力敵的","examples":["It is still a close contest between two leading opposition parties. 兩大主要反對黨之間的較量仍然旗鼓相當。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you are <b>close</b> <b>to</b> something or if it is <b>close</b>, it is likely to happen or come soon. If you are <b>close</b> <b>to</b> doing something, you are likely to do it soon. 即將發生的; 在即的","examples":["She sounded close to tears. 她聽起來就要哭了。","A senior White House official said the agreement is close. 一位白宮高階官員說協議就要達成了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something is <b>close</b> or comes <b>close</b> <b>to</b> something else, it almost is, does, or experiences that thing. 幾近的","examples":["An airliner came close to disaster while approaching Kennedy Airport. 一架客機在飛近肯尼迪機場時險些出事。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If the atmosphere somewhere is <b>close</b>, it is unpleasantly warm with not enough air. 悶熱的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"靠近地","examples":["They crowded more closely around the stretcher. 他們更近地圍到擔架旁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"緊密地","examples":["Our agencies work closely with local groups in developing countries. 我們的機構與發展中國家的地方團體密切協作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"緊密地; 相似地","examples":["...a pattern closely resembling a cross. …一個酷似十字架的圖案。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"全面細緻地","examples":["If you look closely at many of the problems in society, you'll see evidence of racial discrimination. 如果你仔細思考社會中的很多問題，你就會發現種族歧視的證據。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"closely; tightly 緊密地; 牢固地","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"勢均力敵地","examples":["This will be a closely fought race. 這將是一場出手勢均力敵的比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>close by</b> or <b>close at hand</b> is near to you. 在附近; 在身邊","examples":["Did a new hair salon open close by? 附近開了家新發廊嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Close to</b> a particular amount or distance means slightly less than that amount or distance. (數量、距離) 接近於","examples":["Sisulu spent close to 30 years in prison. 西蘇魯在監獄裡呆了近三十年。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you look at something <b>close up</b>, you look at it when you are very near to it. 近距離地","examples":["They always look smaller close up. 它們從近處看總是更小。"]}]}]},"country":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國，國家；全國人民，全體國民（the country）；鄉下，鄉村；地區，區域；鄉村音樂；故鄉"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鄉下的，農村的；鄉村音樂的；祖國的，故鄉的；粗魯的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>country</b> is one of the political units which the world is divided into, covering a particular area of land. 國家","examples":["Indonesia is the fifth most populous country in the world. 印度尼西亞是世界上人口第五大國。","...the boundary between the two countries. …這兩個國家的分界線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The people who live in a particular country can be referred to as <b>the</b> <b>country</b>. 國民","examples":["Finally the country got some much-needed good news. 最後該國人民得到了一些他們最需要的好訊息。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The country</b> consists of places such as farms, open fields, and villages which are away from towns and cities. 鄉村","examples":["...a healthy life in the country. …在鄉村的健康生活。","She was cycling along a country road near Compiègne. 她正沿著貢比涅附近的一條鄉間小路騎車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>country</b> is an area of land which has particular characteristics or is connected with a particular well-known person. 地區","examples":["Varese Ligure is a small town in mountainous country east of Genoa. 瓦雷澤·利古里亞是一座位於熱那亞東部山區的小鎮。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Country</b> music is popular music from the southern United States. 鄉村 (音樂)","examples":["For a long time I just wanted to play country music. 在過去的很長一段時間，我只想演奏鄉村音樂。"]}]}]},"cowboy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牧牛工，牛仔；（美國西部影片中）牛仔；<英>奸商，不負責任的人；牛仔競技表演者；有牛仔特質的人，（尤指）冒險莽撞的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當牛仔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cowboy</b> is a male character in a western. (美國西部的) 牛仔","examples":["Boys used to play at cowboys and Indians. 男孩子們過去常玩牛仔和印第安人的遊戲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cowboy</b> is a man employed to look after cattle in North America, especially in former times. (尤指舊時北美地區的) 牧牛工","examples":["In his twenties Roosevelt had sought work as a cowboy on a ranch in the Dakota Territory. 二十多歲時，羅斯福曾經到達科他地區的一個大牧場去找牧牛工的活兒。"]}]}]},"cool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"涼的，涼爽的；（衣服布料）使人涼爽的；冷靜的，沉著的；時髦的，酷的；沒問題，不介意；冷漠的，冷淡的；冷色調的；<非正式>（錢）大筆的，不折不扣的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）冷卻，（使）變涼；（感情）冷靜下來，冷淡下來"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>冷靜地，鎮定地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"涼快，涼爽；平靜，鎮靜；時髦，酷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>cool</b> has a temperature which is low but not very low. 涼的","examples":["I felt a current of cool air. 我感覺到了一陣涼風。","The water was slightly cooler than a child's bath. 這水比小孩子的洗澡水稍微涼一點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is <b>cool</b>, or if a place is <b>cool</b>, the temperature of the air is low but not very low. 涼爽的","examples":["Thank goodness it's cool in here. 謝天謝地，這裡很涼爽。","Store grains and cereals in a cool, dry place. 把穀物和雜糧儲存在涼爽、乾燥的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Clothing that is <b>cool</b> is made of thin material so that you do not become too hot in hot weather. (衣服) 涼快的","examples":["In warm weather, you should wear clothing that is cool and comfortable. 天氣熱時，你應該穿涼快舒適的衣服。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Cool</b> colours are light colours which give an impression of coolness. 冷色的","examples":["Choose a cool colour such as cream. 選擇一個冷色，比如乳白色。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a person or their behaviour is <b>cool</b>, you mean that they are calm and unemotional, especially in a difficult situation. 冷靜的","examples":["He was marvellously cool again, smiling as if nothing had happened. 他又變得出奇的冷靜，微笑著，似乎什麼都沒有發生過一樣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that a person or their behaviour is <b>cool</b>, you mean that they are unfriendly or not enthusiastic. 冷漠的","examples":["I didn't like him at all. I thought he was cool, aloof, and arrogant. 我一點都不喜歡他。我認為他冷漠、不合群又狂妄。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing is <b>cool</b>, you mean that they are fashionable and attractive. 酷的","examples":["He was trying to be really cool and trendy. 他總想變得又酷又時髦。","That's a cool hat. 那是一頂很酷的帽子。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>cool</b> <b>about</b> something, you mean that they accept it and are not angry or upset about it. 冷靜的","examples":["Bev was really cool about it all. 貝文對這整件事真的很冷靜。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>cool</b>, you think they are excellent in some way. 很棒的","examples":["Kathleen gave me a really cool dress. 凱瑟琳給了我一件很漂亮的衣服。","He's such a cool guy. 他是一個很優秀的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cool</b> is also a noun. 涼爽","examples":["She walked into the cool of the hallway. 她走入了涼爽的過道。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"冷靜地","examples":["Everyone must think this situation through calmly and coolly. 每個人必須冷靜沉著地考慮當前形勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"冷漠地","examples":["\"It's your choice, Nina,\" David said coolly. 大衛冷漠地說：“這是你的選擇，尼娜”。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>cools</b> or when you <b>cool</b> it, it becomes lower in temperature. 使變涼; 變涼","examples":["Drain the meat and allow it to cool. 把肉晾乾，讓它冷卻。","Huge fans will have to cool the concrete floor to keep it below 150 degrees. 為了讓水泥地溫度一直低於150度，必須用巨大的風扇來降溫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a feeling or emotion <b>cools</b>, or when you <b>cool</b> it, it becomes less powerful. (情緒等) 冷靜下來","examples":["Within a few minutes tempers had cooled. 幾分鐘之內，就冷靜了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>cool down</b> means the same as to . 降溫","examples":["Avoid putting your car away until the engine has cooled down. 等發動機冷卻之後再把汽車放回原處。"]}]}]},"cow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"母牛，奶牛；雌性動物；<澳新>討厭的人（或事物、情況）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"恐嚇，威脅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cow</b> is a large female animal that is kept on farms for its milk. People sometimes refer to male and female animals of this species as <b>cows</b>. 母牛; 奶牛","examples":["He kept a few dairy cows. 他養了幾頭奶牛。","Dad went out to milk the cows. 爸爸出去給牛擠奶去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some female animals, including elephants and whales, are called <b>cows</b>. 大型雌獸","examples":["...a cow elephant. …一頭母象。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is cowed</b>, they are made afraid, or made to behave in a particular way because they have been frightened or badly treated. 脅迫; 恐嚇","examples":["The government, far from being cowed by these threats, has vowed to continue its policy. 政府根本沒有被這些威脅嚇倒，發誓要繼續執行自己的政策。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受到脅迫的; 受到恐嚇的","examples":["By this time she was so cowed by the beatings that she meekly obeyed. 到了這時候她被這些毆打嚇得不行，以至溫順地服從。"]}]}]},"cost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"價錢，費用；成本，開支；代價，損失；訴訟費用"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"價錢為，需花費；估算成本，估價；使喪失，使損失；使付出努力，使做不愉快的事；<非正式>使花許多錢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>cost</b> <b>of</b> something is the amount of money that is needed in order to buy, do, or make it. 費用","examples":["The cost of a loaf of bread has increased five-fold. 一塊麵包的價格已經漲了5倍。","In 1989 the price of coffee fell so low that in many countries it did not even cover the cost of production. 1989年咖啡的價格跌得那麼低，以致在許多國家還抵不上其生產成本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>costs</b> are the total amount of money that you must spend on running your home or business. (家庭或公司) 開銷","examples":["Costs have been cut by 30 to 50 percent. 開銷已經減少了30%到50%。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is ordered by a court of law to pay <b>costs</b>, they have to pay a sum of money toward the expenses of a court case they are involved in. 訴訟費用","examples":["He was jailed for 18 months and ordered to pay $550 costs. 他被判入獄18個月，並支付$550的訴訟費。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is sold <b>at</b> <b>cost</b>, it is sold for the same price as it cost the seller to buy it. 成本價格","examples":["...a shop that provided cigarettes and sweets at cost. …一家以成本價出售香菸和糖果的商店。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>cost</b> <b>of</b> something is the loss, damage, or injury that is involved in trying to achieve it. 代價","examples":["In March Mr. Salinas shut down the city's oil refinery at a cost of $500 million and 5,000 jobs. 3月時薩利納斯先生關閉了該市的煉油廠，損失了5億美元和5000個工作崗位。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>costs</b> a particular amount of money, you can buy, do, or make it for that amount. 要價","examples":["This course is limited to 12 people and costs $150. 這門課程限招12人，費用為$150。","Painted walls look much more interesting and don't cost much. 粉刷過的牆壁看上去更有趣，要價也不高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something that you plan to do or make <b>is costed</b>, the amount of money you need is calculated in advance. 估算…的費用","examples":["The building work has not been fully costed but runs into millions of dollars. 建築工作的費用還未完全估算出來，但要高達幾百萬美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event or mistake <b>costs</b> you something, you lose that thing as the result of it. 使…付出","examples":["...a six-year-old boy whose life was saved by an operation that cost him his sight. …一個透過手術保住生命但雙目失明的6歲男孩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something must be avoided <b>at all costs</b>, you are emphasizing that it must not be allowed to happen under any circumstances. 不惜任何代價地","examples":["They told Jacques Delors a disastrous world trade war must be avoided at all costs. 他們告訴雅克·得洛斯，必須不惜一切代價避免災難性的世界貿易大戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something must be done <b>at any cost</b>, you are emphasizing that it must be done, even if this requires a lot of effort or money. 無論如何","examples":["This book is of such importance that it must be published at any cost. 這本書如此重要，無論如何也要出版。"]}]}]},"cub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幼獸；<舊>（尤指笨拙或舉止粗魯的）毛頭小夥子；幼年童子軍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"產仔，生幼獸；獵幼狐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cub</b> is a young wild animal such as a lion, wolf, or bear. (獅子、狼、熊等的) 幼仔","examples":["...three five-week-old lion cubs. …3只5周大的幼獅。"]}]}]},"count":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（按順序）數數；計數，點數目；把……算入，包括；重要；被允許，被接受；看作，認為"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"計算，總數；數數；量的計數；（被指控的）罪狀，事項；論點，觀點；伯爵；（紗線的）支數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>count</b>, you say all the numbers one after another up to a particular number. 數數","examples":["He was counting slowly under his breath. 他在低聲慢慢地數數。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>counts</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>counts</b>, they are important or valuable. 有價值; 有重要意義","examples":["Surely it doesn't matter where charities get their money from: what counts is what they do with it. 當然，慈善組織從哪裡得到錢並不重要，重要的是他們用這些錢做什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>count</b> all the things in a group, you add them up in order to find how many there are. 數…的數目","examples":["I counted the money. It was more than five hundred dollars. 我數了數錢，有五百多美元。","I counted 34 wild goats grazing. 我數了有34只野山羊在吃草。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>counts</b> or <b>is counted</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing, it is regarded as being that thing, especially in particular circumstances or under particular rules. 看作","examples":["No one agrees on what counts as a desert. 沒有人對於什麼可以看作是荒漠有共識。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>count</b> something when you are making a calculation, you include it in that calculation. 把…計算在內","examples":["It's under 7 percent only because statistics don't count the people who aren't qualified to be in the work force. 數字不到7%，這只是因為統計沒有把未達勞動力標準的人算在內。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Count up</b> means the same as . 數…的數目","examples":["Couldn't we just count up our ballots and bring them to the courthouse? 我們不能就數好我們的選票然後把它們送到法院嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>count</b> is the action of counting a particular set of things, or the number that you get when you have counted them. 點數; 點出的數目","examples":["The final count in last month's referendum showed 56.7 per cent in favour. 上個月全民投票的最後計票顯示支援率為56.7%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>count</b> when referring to the level or amount of something that someone or something has. 數目; 數量","examples":["A glass or two of wine will not significantly add to the calorie count. 一兩杯酒不會顯著增加卡路里的數量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In law, a <b>count</b> is one of a number of charges brought against someone in court. 罪狀","examples":["He was indicted by a grand jury on two counts of murder. 他被大陪審團以兩項謀殺罪名正式起訴。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>count</b> is a European nobleman. 伯爵","examples":["Her father was a Polish count. 她父親是波蘭的一位伯爵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep count</b> <b>of</b> a number of things, you note or keep a record of how many have occurred. If you <b>lose count</b> <b>of</b> a number of things, you cannot remember how many have occurred. 計其數/無法計其數","examples":["The authorities say they are not able to keep count of the bodies still being found as bulldozers clear the rubble. 當局稱他們不能記下推土機清理瓦礫時不斷被找到的屍體數目。"]}]}]},"dad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（非正式）爸爸，爹爹；（Dad）人名：（孟、巴基、阿富）達德；（泰）達"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>dad</b> is your father. 爸爸","examples":["How do you feel, Dad? 你感覺怎麼樣，爸爸？"]}]}]},"daddy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爸爸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Children often call their father <b>daddy</b>. 爸爸","examples":["Look at me, Daddy! 看著我，爸爸！"]}]}]},"course":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"課程；過程；道路，航線；程序，進展；方針，總方向；行動方式，處理方法；療程；一道菜；比賽場地；（磚、石等牆的）層；（常sing.）追蹤狩獵（尤指野兔）；橫帆；一組同音弦；追蹤狩獵（尤指野兔）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"奔流，快速流動；（感情、思想）湧動；（用獵犬）追蹤（兔子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Course</b> is often used in the expression \"of course,\" or instead of \"of course\" in informal spoken English. See . 當然 (在口語中代替)(of course)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>course</b> of a vehicle, especially a ship or aircraft, is the route along which it is travelling. 路線","examples":["Aircraft can avoid each other by altering course to left or right. 飛行器可以透過向左或向右改變航線來避免相撞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>course</b> <b>of</b> action is an action or a series of actions that you can do in a particular situation. 做法","examples":["My best course of action was to help Gill by being sympathetic. 我最好的做法是透過表達同情去幫助吉爾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>course</b> is a series of lessons or lectures on a particular subject. 課程","examples":["...a course in business administration. …一門工商管理課程。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>course of</b> medical treatment is a series of treatments that a doctor gives someone. 療程","examples":["He had a course of antibiotics to kill the bacterium. 他服了一療程的抗生素來殺死細菌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>course</b> is one part of a meal. 一道菜","examples":["The lunch was excellent, especially the first course. 午飯非常好吃，尤其是第一道菜。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In sports, a <b>course</b> is an area of land where races are held or golf is played, or the land over which a race takes place. 跑馬場; 跑道; 高爾夫球場","examples":["Only 12 seconds separated the first three riders on the course. 跑道上的前3名選手12秒就拉開距離了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>course</b> of a river is the channel along which it flows. 河道","examples":["Romantic castles overlook the river's twisting course. 一座座傳奇式的城堡俯瞰著小河蜿蜒曲折的河道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>in the course of</b> a particular period of time, it happens during that period of time. 在…期間","examples":["In the course of the 1930s steel production approximately doubled. 20世紀30年代間，鋼產量幾乎翻了一番。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>as a matter of course</b>, you do it as part of your normal work or way of life. 作為理所當然的事","examples":["If police are carrying arms as a matter of course, then doesn't it encourage criminals to carry them? 如果警察理所當然地攜帶武器，這難道不是鼓勵罪犯也攜帶武器嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a ship or aircraft is <b>on course</b>, it is travelling along the correct route. If it is <b>off course</b>, it is no longer travelling along the correct route. 在正確路線上/偏離正確路線","examples":["The ship was sent off course into shallow waters. 輪船被駛出軌，進入了淺水區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>on course for</b> something, you are likely to achieve it. 極有可能得到…","examples":["The company is on course for profits of $20m. 這家公司的利潤有望達到2000萬美元。"]}]}]},"dancer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"舞者，舞蹈演員，舞蹈家；跳舞者，舞跳得……的人；（舊）舞女，伴舞女郎；（Dancer）人名，（英）丹瑟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dancer</b> is a person who earns money by dancing, or a person who is dancing. 舞蹈演員; 舞者","examples":["His girlfriend was a dancer with the New York City Ballet. 他的女朋友曾是紐約市芭蕾舞團的舞蹈演員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is a good <b>dancer</b> or a bad <b>dancer</b>, you are saying how well or badly they can dance. 舞跳得…的人","examples":["He was the best dancer in LA. 他曾是洛杉磯舞跳得最好的人。"]}]}]},"cry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"哭，哭泣；喊叫，呼喊；（獸或鳥）大叫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（表達強烈感情的）叫喊，叫聲，哭聲；大喊，大叫；抗議，請求；吠，嗥叫；哭，哭泣；急需；口號，公眾輿論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>cry</b>, tears come from your eyes, usually because you are unhappy or hurt. 哭","examples":["I hung up the phone and started to cry. 我掛掉電話，開始哭了起來。","He cried with anger and frustration. 他憤怒而失望地哭了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cry</b> is also a noun. 哭","examples":["A nurse patted me on the shoulder and said, \"You have a good cry, dear.\" 一個護士拍著我的肩膀，說道：“親愛的，你就痛痛快快地哭吧。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"啼哭","examples":["She had been unable to sleep for three days because of her 13-week-old son's crying. 由於她13周大的兒子的啼哭，她3天沒睡著覺了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cry</b> is a loud, high sound that you make when you feel a strong emotion such as fear, pain, or pleasure. 尖叫","examples":["A cry of horror broke from me. 我發出的一聲驚恐的尖叫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>cry</b> is a shouted word or phrase, usually one that is intended to attract someone's attention. 喊叫聲","examples":["Thousands of Ukrainians burst into cries of \"bravo.\" 數千名烏克蘭人放聲高呼“好！”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to a public protest about something or an appeal for something as a <b>cry</b> of some kind. (抗議某事、為某事請願的) 公眾呼聲","examples":["There have been cries of outrage about this expenditure. 公眾對這項開支發出了憤怒的呼聲。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A bird's or an animal's <b>cry</b> is the loud, high sound that it makes. (鳥的) 啼叫聲; (動物的) 嚎叫聲","examples":["...the cry of a seagull. …一隻海鷗的鳴叫聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cry</b> something, you shout it or say it loudly. 大聲叫喊","examples":["\"Nancy Drew,\" she cried, \"you're under arrest!\" “南茜·德魯，”她喊道：“你被捕了！”"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cry out</b> means the same as . 大叫","examples":["\"You're wrong, quite wrong!\" Henry cried out, suddenly excited. “你錯了，大錯特錯！”亨利突然激動起來，大聲叫道。"]}]}]},"cup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"杯子；一杯（的量）；杯（烹飪的計量單位），量杯（金屬或塑膠量器）；優勝杯，獎盃；杯狀物；（胸罩的）罩杯；（含酒精的）混合飲料；<美>（高爾夫球的）球洞；<美>（男子運動時穿的）護襠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用手）做成杯狀；窩起手掌托住；<舊>為……拔火罐（或做吸杯治療）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cup</b> is a small round container that you drink from. Cups usually have handles and are made from china or plastic. (有把手的陶瓷或塑膠) 杯子","examples":["...cups and saucers. …茶杯和茶碟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>cup</b> to refer to the cup and its contents, or to the contents only. 一杯···","examples":["...a cup of coffee. …一杯咖啡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cup</b> is a unit of measurement used in cooking. It is equal to 16 tablespoons or 8 fluid ounces. 量杯 (等於16大湯匙或8液盎司)","examples":["Gradually add 1 cup of milk, stirring until the liquid is absorbed. 逐漸加入一量杯牛奶，一邊攪動直到液體被吸收。","...half a cup of sugar. …半量杯糖。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Things, or parts of things, that are small, round, and hollow in shape can be referred to as <b>cups</b>. 杯狀物","examples":["...the brass cups of the small chandelier. …小枝形吊燈上的黃銅杯狀燈罩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>cup</b> is a large metal cup with two handles that is given to the winner of a game or competition. 獎盃","examples":["The Stars won the Stanley Cup in 1999. 明星隊贏得了1999年的斯坦利杯。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Cup</b> is used in the names of some sports competitions in which the prize is a cup. …盃賽","examples":["Sri Lanka's cricket team will play India in the final of the Asia Cup. 斯里蘭卡板球隊將在亞洲盃決賽中與印度隊交鋒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cup</b> your <b>hands</b>, you make them into a curved shape like a cup. 把 (手等) 窩成杯狀","examples":["He cupped his hands around his mouth and called out for Diane. 他兩手窩成杯狀圍在嘴邊，大聲地呼喚黛安。","David knelt, cupped his hands and splashed river water on to his face. 大衛跪下去，雙手成杯狀，捧起河水潑到他的臉上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cup</b> something in your hands, you make your hands into a curved dish-like shape and support it or hold it gently. 窩起手掌托住","examples":["He cupped her chin in the palm of his hand. 他窩起手掌托住她的下巴。"]}]}]},"cover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"覆蓋，遮蓋；包括，涉及；報道；佔（一片面積）；行走（一段路程）；足夠支付；給……保險；頂替，代替；找藉口，包庇；採取行動（保護自己）；掩護；守住，封鎖；翻唱；（橋牌）蓋打"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"覆蓋物，遮蓋物；封面，封底；被子，床單；遮蓋，覆蓋；保險；掩護；掩飾，幌子；掩蔽處；代替；轉錄，翻唱；（板球）外場防守；（生態）蓋度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cover</b> something, you place something else over it in order to protect it, hide it, or close it. 蓋","examples":["Cover the casserole with a tight-fitting lid. 用緊實的蓋子把砂鍋蓋住。","He whimpered and covered his face. 他嗚咽著捂住了臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>covers</b> another, it has been placed over it in order to protect it, hide it, or close it. 蓋住","examples":["His finger went up to touch the black patch which covered his left eye. 他的手指抬起來去摸蓋在他左眼上的黑眼罩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>covers</b> another, it forms a layer over its surface. 覆蓋","examples":["The clouds had spread and covered the entire sky. 烏雲鋪開，遮蔽了整個天空。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>cover</b> something <b>with</b> or <b>in</b> something else means to put a layer of the second thing over its surface. 鋪蓋","examples":["The desk was covered with papers. 書桌上鋪了些報紙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>cover</b> a particular distance, you travel that distance. 走過 (一段距離)","examples":["It would not be easy to cover ten miles on that amount of petrol. 要靠那些數量的汽油跑10英里可不容易。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An insurance policy that <b>covers</b> a person or thing guarantees that money will be paid by the insurance company in relation to that person or thing. 保險","examples":["Their insurer paid the $900 bill, even though the policy did not strictly cover it. 他們的保險公司賠付了他們$900，儘管保單並沒有嚴格保到此項。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a law <b>covers</b> a particular set of people, things, or situations, it applies to them. 適用於","examples":["The law covers four categories of experiments. 這一原理適用於4類試驗。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>cover</b> a particular topic, you discuss it in a lecture, course, or book. 論及","examples":["Introduction to Chemistry aims to cover important topics in organic chemistry. 《化學入門》意在論及有機化學的重要問題。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a sum of money <b>covers</b> something, it is enough to pay for it. 足夠支付","examples":["Send it to the address given with $2.50 to cover postage and administration. 把這封信寄到所給地址，$2.50足以支付郵資和手續費。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cover for</b> someone who is doing something secret or illegal, you give false information or do not give all the information you have, in order to protect them. 包庇","examples":["Why would she cover for someone who was trying to kill her? 她為何要包庇那個試圖要殺死她的人呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cover for</b> someone who is ill or away, you do their work for them while they are not there. 代替","examples":["She did not have enough nurses to cover for those who were sick. 她沒有足夠的護士來代替她們生病的同事的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cover</b> your <b>arse</b>, you do something in order to protect yourself, for example against criticism or against accusations of doing something wrong. 為自己開脫","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take cover</b>, you shelter from gunfire, bombs, or the weather. 躲避","examples":["Shoppers took cover behind cars as the gunman fired. 持槍歹徒開槍時，購物者們都躲到了汽車後面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>under cover of</b> a particular situation, you are able to do it without being noticed because of that situation. 在…的掩護下","examples":["They move under cover of darkness. 他們在黑夜的掩護下行進。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cover</b> is something which is put over an object, usually in order to protect it. 套子","examples":["...a sofa with washable covers. …一張沙發套可拆洗的沙發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>cover</b> of a book or a magazine is the outside part of it. 封面","examples":["...a small book with a green cover. …一本綠色封面的小冊子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Cover</b> is protection from enemy attack that is provided for troops or ships carrying out a particular operation, for example, by aircraft. 掩護","examples":["They could not provide adequate air cover for ground operations. 他們無法為地面作戰行動提供足夠的空中掩護。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Cover</b> is trees, rocks, or other places where you shelter from the weather or from an attack, or hide from someone. 掩蔽處","examples":["Charles lit the fuses and they ran for cover. 查爾斯點燃了導火索，大家跑向掩蔽處。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Insurance <b>cover</b> is a guarantee from an insurance company that money will be paid by them if it is needed. (保險) 保障","examples":["Make sure that the firm's insurance cover is adequate. 要確保該公司的保險保障是足夠的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that is a <b>cover</b> for secret or illegal activities seems respectable or normal, and is intended to hide the activities. 掩護","examples":["He ran a construction company as a cover for drug dealing. 他經營了一家建築公司，作為毒品交易的掩護。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>covers</b> on your bed are the things such as sheets and blankets that you have on top of you. 床上蓋具","examples":["She set her glass down and slid under the covers. 她放下杯子，鑽進了被子。"]}]}]},"dance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳舞；跳（某種舞）；跳躍，雀躍；和……共舞；（某物）擺動，搖晃；（某人眼睛）因快樂（或激動）而閃爍"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"舞蹈，舞步；舞蹈（藝術）；跳舞；舞會；舞曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dance</b>, you move your body and feet in a way which follows a rhythm, usually in time to music. 跳舞","examples":["Polly had never learned to dance. 波莉從未學過跳舞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dance</b> somewhere, you move there lightly and quickly, usually because you are happy or excited. 跳躍; 雀躍","examples":["He danced off down the road. 他沿著馬路蹦蹦跳跳地走了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>dances</b>, you mean that it moves around, or seems to move around, lightly and quickly. (輕快地) 跳動","examples":["Patterns of light, reflected by the river, dance along the base of the cliffs. 被河水倒映出的光影沿著懸崖底部輕快地跳動。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dance</b> a particular kind of dance, you do it or perform it. 跳…舞","examples":["Then we put the music on, and we all danced the Charleston. 然後我們放起音樂，一塊跳起了查爾斯頓舞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dance</b> is a particular series of graceful movements of your body and feet, which you usually do in time to music. 舞蹈","examples":["Sometimes the people doing this dance hold brightly coloured scarves. 有時候跳這種舞的人拿著色彩鮮豔的圍巾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dance</b> is a social event where people dance with each other. 舞會","examples":["At the school dance he sat and talked to her all evening. 在學校的舞會上，他整晚坐著和她聊天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dance</b> is also a noun. 一支舞","examples":["Come and have a dance with me. 來和我跳支舞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Dance</b> is the activity of performing dances, as a public entertainment or an art form. 舞蹈藝術","examples":["Their contribution to international dance, drama and music is inestimable. 他們對國際舞蹈、戲劇和音樂的貢獻是不可估量的。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dance</b> <b>with</b> someone, the two of you take part in a dance together, as partners. You can also say that two people <b>dance</b>. 和…共舞","examples":["It's a terrible thing when nobody wants to dance with you. 沒有人想和你跳舞是件糟糕的事。","Shall we dance? 我們跳舞吧？"]}]}]},"danger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"危險，風險；威脅，危險因素；（不愉快之事發生的）可能性，風險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Danger</b> is the possibility that someone may be harmed or killed. 危險","examples":["My friends endured tremendous danger in order to help me. 為了幫助我，我的朋友們經歷了巨大的危險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>danger</b> is something or someone that can hurt or harm you. 威脅; 危害","examples":["...the dangers of smoking. …吸菸的危害。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>danger</b> <b>that</b> something unpleasant will happen, it is possible that it will happen. 危險; 風險","examples":["There is a real danger that some people will no longer be able to afford insurance. 一個真正的風險是有些人將再也負擔不起保險費。","There was no danger that any of these groups would be elected to power. 絲毫不存在這些團體勝選掌權的危險。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who has been seriously ill is <b>out of danger</b>, they are still ill, but they are not expected to die. 脫離危險期","examples":["There is some risk of the lung collapsing again, but he is out of danger. 肺部的確存在再次衰竭的危險，但他脫離危險期了。"]}]}]},"daughter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女兒；（遺傳學、農學）子代"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"女兒的；子代的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>daughter</b> is their female child. 女兒","examples":["...Flora and her daughter Catherine. …弗洛拉和她的女兒凱瑟琳。","...the daughter of a university professor. …一位大學教授的女兒。"]}]}]},"dark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"黑暗的，昏暗的；深色的，暗色的；恐怖的，悲慘的；神秘的，隱秘的；憂鬱的，悲觀的；邪惡的，陰險的；（頭髮、眼睛或皮膚）褐色的，黑色的；（劇院）關閉的，停業的；（嗓音）低沉圓潤的；（語音）暗的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"黑暗，暗處；暗色，陰影；黃昏，夜幕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When it is <b>dark</b>, there is not enough light to see properly, for example, because it is night. 黑暗的","examples":["It was too dark inside to see much. 裡面太黑，看不見什麼東西。","People usually draw the curtains once it gets dark. 天一黑，人們通常就會拉上窗簾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>dark</b>, you mean that it is black in colour, or a shade that is close to black. 黑色的; 暗色的","examples":["He wore a dark suit and carried a black attaché case. 他穿著深色套裝，手提黑色公文包。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone has <b>dark</b> hair, eyes, or skin, they have brown or black hair, eyes, or skin. (頭髮、皮膚等) 棕色或黑色的","examples":["He had dark, curly hair. 他有一頭黑色捲髮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>dark</b> period of time is unpleasant or frightening. 黯淡的","examples":["Once again there's talk of very dark days ahead. 人們又一次提到了極其黯淡的前途。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>dark</b> place or area is mysterious and not fully known about. 神秘的","examples":["The spacecraft will enable scientists to study some dark corners of the solar system. 太空船使得科學家可以研究太陽系中一些不為人知的角落。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Dark</b> thoughts are sad, and show that you are expecting something unpleasant to happen. 悲觀的","examples":["Troy's endless happy chatter kept me from thinking dark thoughts. 特洛伊興高采烈地說個不停，使我忘記了悲觀的想法。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>dark</b>, you mean that it is related to things that are serious or unpleasant, rather than lighthearted. 沉重的","examples":["There's plenty of dark humour in the film. 這部電影充滿了黑色幽默。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"黑暗","examples":["The light went out, and the room was plunged into darkness. 燈滅了，房間陷入了黑暗之中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The dark</b> is the lack of light in a place. 黑暗","examples":["I've always been afraid of the dark. 我一直懼怕黑暗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"呈黑色地","examples":["The freckles on Joanne's face suddenly stood out darkly against her pale skin. 在蒼白的膚色映襯下，喬安臉上的雀斑一下子更明顯了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"悲觀地","examples":["She hinted darkly that she might have to resign. 她悲觀地暗示她可能得辭職。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"沉重地","examples":["The atmosphere after Wednesday's debut was as darkly comic as the film itself. 週三首映式之後的氣氛和電影本身一樣像是沉重的喜劇。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you use <b>dark</b> to describe a colour, you are referring to a shade of that colour which is close to black, or seems to have some black in it. 深色的","examples":["She was wearing a dark blue dress. 她穿著深藍色的連衣裙。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>after dark</b>, you do it when the sun has set and night has begun. 黃昏以後","examples":["They avoid going out alone after dark. 他們避免黃昏後獨自出門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>before dark</b>, you do it before the sun sets and night begins. 黃昏以前","examples":["They'll be back well before dark. 他們會在天黑以前回來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>in the dark</b> <b>about</b> something, you do not know anything about it. 一無所知","examples":["The investigators admit that they are completely in the dark about the killing. 調查人員承認他們對這起兇殺案一無所知。"]}]}]},"date":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"日期，日子；約會，幽會；約會物件；椰棗，海棗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"註明日期；確定年代；<美>談戀愛，約會；過時，不流行；使顯老"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>date</b> is a specific time that can be named, for example, a particular day or a particular year. 日期","examples":["What's the date today? 今天是幾號？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>date</b> is an appointment to meet someone or go out with them, especially someone with whom you are having, or may soon have, a romantic relationship. 約會","examples":["I have a date with Bob. 我和鮑勃有個約會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a date with someone with whom you are having, or may soon have, a romantic relationship, you can refer to that person as your <b>date</b>. (戀愛中的) 約會物件","examples":["He lied to Essie, saying his date was one of the girls in the show. 他對埃西撒謊說他約會的物件是參加演出的女孩兒其中的一個。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>date</b> is a small, dark-brown, sticky fruit with a stone inside. Dates grow on palm trees in hot countries. 椰棗","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are dating</b> someone, you go out with them regularly because you are having, or may soon have, a romantic relationship with them. You can also say that two people <b>are dating</b>. (戀愛中) 約會","examples":["For a year I dated a woman who was a research assistant. 有一年的時間，我一直和一個女助理研究員約會。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>date</b> something, you give or discover the date when it was made or when it began. 推斷…的年代","examples":["I think we can date the decline of Western Civilization quite precisely. 我認為我們可以非常準確的推斷出西方文明衰落的年代。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>date</b> something such as a letter or a cheque, you write that day's date on it. 給…標註日期","examples":["Once the decision is reached, he can date and sign the sheet. 一旦做出決定，他就可以在那張表上籤上日期和名字。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to have originated (at a specified time) 始於(某一特定時間)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>dates</b>, it goes out of fashion and becomes unacceptable to modern tastes. 過時","examples":["Blue and white is the classic colour combination for bathrooms. It always looks smart and will never date. 藍色和白色是浴室的經典色彩搭配，看起來總是很時髦，永遠不會過時。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>To date</b> means up until the present time. 至今為止","examples":["\"Dottie\" is by far his best novel to date. 《小多特》是他至今最為出色的小說。"]}]}]},"december":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"十二月，公曆（西方曆法）中的第十二個月，也是一年的最後一個月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>December</b> is the twelfth and last month of the year in the Western calendar. 12月","examples":["...a bright morning in mid-December. …12月中旬一個晴朗的早晨。"]}]}]},"dear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"珍視的；(用於信函抬頭名字或頭銜前)親愛的；昂貴的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（稱呼所愛的人）親愛的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"啊，天吶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>dear</b> to describe someone or something that you feel affection for. 親愛的","examples":["Mrs. Cavendish is a dear friend of mine. 凱文迪許太太是我親愛的朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>dear to</b> you or <b>dear to</b> your <b>heart</b>, you care deeply about it. 寶貴的; 珍視的","examples":["This is a subject very dear to the hearts of academics up and down the country. 這是全國學者都極為重視的話題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dear</b> is written at the beginning of a letter, followed by the name or title of the person you are writing to. 親愛的 (寫在信首，位於收信人的姓名或稱呼前)","examples":["Dear Peter, I have been thinking about you so much during the past few days. 親愛的彼得，在過去的幾天中我一直深深思念著你。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You begin formal letters with \"<b>Dear Sir</b>\" or \"<b>Dear Madam</b>.\" You can also begin them with \"Sir\" or \"Madam.\" 尊敬的","examples":["\"Dear Sir,\" she began. “尊敬的先生”，她開始寫到。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can call someone <b>dear</b> as a sign of affection. 親愛的","examples":["You're a lot like me, dear. 你和我太像了，親愛的。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>dear</b> in expressions such as \"<b>oh dear</b>,\" \"<b>dear me</b>,\" and \"<b>dear, dear</b>\" when you are sad, disappointed, or surprised about something. 啊呀","examples":["\"Oh dear, oh dear.\" McKinnon sighed. \"You, too.\" “啊，天哪，”麥金農嘆息道，“你也一樣。”"]}]}]},"deer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鹿；（Deer）人名；<英>迪爾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deer</b> is a large wild animal that eats grass and leaves. A male deer usually has large, branching horns. 鹿","examples":[]}]}]},"death":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"死，死亡；破滅，終止；死神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Death</b> is the permanent end of the life of a person or animal. 死亡","examples":["1.5 million people are in immediate danger of death from starvation. 150萬人正因飢餓而即將面臨死亡的危險。","...the thirtieth anniversary of Judy Garland's death. …朱迪·嘉蘭逝世30週年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>death</b> <b>of</b> something is the permanent end of it. 終止","examples":["It meant the death of everything he had ever been or ever hoped to be. 這意味著他曾擁有或希望擁有的一切的結束。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>at death's door</b>, you mean they are very ill and likely to die. 病危","examples":["He told his boss a tale about his mother being at death's door. 他給老闆講述了自己母親病危的情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you will <b>fight to the death</b> for something, you are emphasizing that you will do anything to achieve or protect it, even if you suffer as a consequence. 拼死搏鬥","examples":["She'd have fought to the death for that child. 她原想為那個孩子拼盡全力的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is a matter <b>of</b> <b>life and death</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely important, often because someone may die or suffer great harm if people do not act immediately. 生死攸關","examples":["Well, never mind, John, it's not a matter of life and death. 好了，別介意，約翰，這不是多麼了不起的事情。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is put to death</b>, they are executed. 處死某人","examples":["Those put to death by firing squad included three generals. 被行刑隊處死的人裡有3位將軍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>to death</b> after an adjective or a verb to emphasize the action, state, or feeling mentioned. For example, if you are <b>frightened to death</b> or <b>bored to death</b>, you are extremely frightened or bored. 極度","examples":["He scares teams to death with his pace and power. 他的速度和力量把其他隊嚇破了膽。"]}]}]},"desk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"書桌，辦公桌，寫字檯；服務檯，問詢臺；（辦理某項業務的）部門；樂譜架，演奏者席；<美>（報社）編輯部"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"書桌的，桌上適合用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>desk</b> is a table, often with drawers, which you sit at to write or work. 書桌; 辦公桌","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The place in a hotel, hospital, airport, or other building where you check in or obtain information is referred to as a particular <b>desk</b>. (接待、諮詢) 臺","examples":["I told the girl at the reception desk that I was terribly sorry, but I was half an hour late. 我對接待服務檯的女孩說我很抱歉，遲到了半小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular department of a broadcasting company, or of a newspaper or magazine company, can be referred to as a particular <b>desk</b>. …部","examples":["Let our news desk know as quickly as possible. 儘快通知我們的新聞部。"]}]}]},"deal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大量；交易；壞運氣，不公平的對待；發牌；冷衫木；優惠的價格，划算的價格；牌戲的一局；一手牌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"應對（難纏的人，困難局面）（deal with）；（以某種方式）對付，對待（deal with）；論及，討論（deal with）；買賣，交易；給予；販賣（毒品、藝術品等）；與……有關；發牌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you need or have <b>a great deal of</b> or <b>a good deal of</b> a particular thing, you are emphasizing that you need or have a lot of it. 數量","examples":["...a great deal of money. …許多錢。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal</b> is also an adverb. 非常","examples":["As a relationship becomes more established, it also becomes a good deal more complex. 當一段關係固定下來以後，它也會變得複雜得多。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal</b> is also a pronoun. 量","examples":["Although he had never met Geoffrey Hardcastle, he knew a good deal about him. 儘管他從未見過傑弗裡·哈德卡斯爾，他還是十分了解他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> a <b>deal</b>, <b>do</b> a <b>deal</b>, or <b>cut</b> a <b>deal</b>, you complete an agreement or an arrangement with someone, especially in business. 達成協議; 達成交易","examples":["He made a deal to testify against the others and wasn't charged. 他達成了協議出庭指證別人，因而未獲指控。","Japan will have to do a deal with the U.S. on rice imports. 日本將不得不就水稻進口問題和美國達成協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has had a <b>bad deal</b>, they have been unfortunate or have been treated unfairly. 不公的待遇","examples":["The people of Hartford have had a bad deal for many, many years. 許多年來，哈特福德地區的人們遭受著不幸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a plank of softwood timber, such as fir or pine, or such planks collectively 軟木板","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, company, or shop <b>deals in</b> a particular type of goods, their business involves buying or selling those goods. 經營","examples":["They deal in antiques. 他們經營古董生意。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>deals</b> illegal drugs, they sell them. 販賣 (毒品)","examples":["I certainly don't deal drugs. 我當然不做毒品生意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>deal</b> playing cards, you give them out to the players in a game of cards. (紙牌遊戲中) 發 (牌)","examples":["The croupier dealt each player a card, face down. 賭局主持人給每個玩牌者發了一張牌，牌面向下。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to give (a blow) to (someone); inflict 給(某人)以打擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal out</b> means the same as . (紙牌遊戲中) 發 (牌)","examples":["Dalton dealt out five cards to each player. 多爾頓給每個玩牌的人發了5張牌。"]}]}]},"day":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一天；白晝，白天；工作日，一天的活動時間；時期，時代；如今，現在；（過去或將來的）一天；重大日子；太陽日；恆星日；（天體）白晝；<古>日光"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"白晝的，日間的；（人）日間工作的，上白班的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>day</b> is one of the seven twenty-four hour periods of time in a week. (一週中的) 一天","examples":["And it has snowed almost every day for the past week. 而且過去的一週幾乎每天都在下雪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a particular period in history as a particular <b>day</b> or as particular <b>days</b>. 時期","examples":["He began to talk about the Ukraine of his uncle's day. 他開始談論他叔叔那個年代的烏克蘭。","...his early days of struggle and deep poverty. …他早年的奮鬥和極度窮困時期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Day</b> is the time when it is light, or the time when you are up and doing things. 白天","examples":["Twenty-seven million working days are lost each year due to work accidents and sickness. 由於工傷事故和疾病，每年損失掉2700萬個工作日。","She gives herself one day a week off, on Thursdays. 她每週放自己一天假，在星期四。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the period of time, the solar day, during which the earth makes one complete revolution on its axis relative to the sun. The mean solar day is the average length of the apparent solar day and is some four minutes (3 minutes 56.5 seconds of sidereal time) longer than the sidereal day 太陽日","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the period of time, the sidereal day, during which the earth makes one complete revolution on its axis relative to a particular star. The <b>mean sidereal day</b> lasts 23 hours 56 minutes 4.1 seconds of the mean solar day 恆星日","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>day after day</b>, it happens every day without stopping. 日復一日","examples":["The newspaper job had me doing the same thing day after day. 這份報業的工作讓我日復一日地做同一件事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>day in, day out</b> or <b>day in and day out</b>, you mean that it happens regularly over a long period of time. 天天","examples":["I used to drink coffee day in, day out. 過去我每天喝咖啡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>In this day and age</b> means in modern times. 在現代","examples":["Even in this day and age the old attitudes persist. 即使在今天，一些陳舊的觀念仍然存在。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something <b>has seen better days</b>, you mean that it is old and in poor condition. 破舊","examples":["The tweed jacket she wore had seen better days. 她穿的那件斜紋軟呢夾克衫已經十分破舊了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>call it a day</b>, you decide to stop what you are doing because you are tired of it or because it is not successful. 結束工作; 收工","examples":["Faced with mounting debts, the decision to call it a day was inevitable. 面對不斷增加的債務，停工的決定是不可避免的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>makes</b> your <b>day</b>, it makes you feel very happy. 使某人非常高興","examples":["Come on, Bill. Send Tom a card and make his day. 來，比爾，給湯姆寄張卡片讓他高興一下。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>One day</b> or <b>some day</b> or <b>one of these days</b> means at some time in the future. 有朝一日","examples":["I too dreamed of living in Dallas one day. 我也曾夢想有朝一日能住在達拉斯。","I hope some day you will find the woman who will make you happy. 我希望有一天你會找到能讓你幸福的女人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something happened <b>the other day</b>, you mean that it happened a few days ago. 幾天前","examples":["I phoned your office the other day. 幾天前，我往你的辦公室打過電話。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone or something <b>saves the day</b> in a situation which seems likely to fail, they manage to make it successful. 扭轉敗局","examples":["...this story about how he saved the day at his daughter's birthday party. …關於他如何在女兒的生日聚會上扭轉局面的故事。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something happens <b>from day to day</b> or <b>day by day</b>, it happens each day. 每天","examples":["Your needs can differ from day to day. 你的需要可能每天都在變化。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If it is a month or a year <b>to the day</b> since a particular thing happened, it is exactly a month or a year since it happened. (日期) 正好","examples":["It was January 19, a year to the day since he had arrived in Singapore. 那是1月19日，他到新加坡正好滿1年。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>To this day</b> means up until and including the present time. 至今","examples":["The controversy continues to this day. 這場爭論直到今天仍在繼續。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that a task is <b>all in a day's work</b> for someone, you mean that they do not mind doing it although it may be difficult, because it is part of their job or because they often do it. 家常便飯","examples":["For war reporters, dodging snipers' bullets is all in a day's work. 對於戰地記者來說，躲避狙擊手的子彈是家常便飯。"]}]}]},"dinner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正餐，晚餐；晚宴，宴會；速食飯，方便飯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dinner</b> is the main meal of the day, usually served in the early part of the evening. 正餐 (常指晚餐)","examples":["She invited us to her house for dinner. 她請我們到她家吃晚飯。","Would you like to stay and have dinner? 你願意留下來吃晚餐嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Any meal you eat in the middle of the day can be referred to as <b>dinner</b>. 午餐","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dinner</b> is a formal social event at which a meal is served. It is held in the evening. 晚宴","examples":["...a series of official lunches and dinners. …一系列正式的午餐和晚宴。"]}]}]},"doll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洋娃娃，玩偶；<舊，非正式>美人兒(現多認為含冒犯意)；<美，非正式>大方的人，體貼的人；賽馬場（或馬賓士道路中）的臨時障礙；<非正式>樂於助人的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>把……打扮得花枝招展；在（需跳躍的地方或跑道上其他不需跑的部分）前放置障礙物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doll</b> is a child's toy which looks like a small person or baby. 玩具娃娃","examples":[]}]}]},"dish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碟，盤；一盤食物；全部餐具（the dishes）；菜餚；碟狀物，盤狀物；性感的人；輪盤；拋物面天線；凹形容器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"說……的閒話；把（食物）裝盤；<英，非正式>使（希望等）破滅；<美，非正式>閒談；成盤形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dish</b> is a shallow container with a wide uncovered top. You eat and serve food from dishes and cook food in them. 盤子","examples":["...plastic bowls and dishes. …塑膠碗和盤子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Food that is prepared in a particular style or combination can be referred to as a <b>dish</b>. (一道) 菜","examples":["There are plenty of vegetarian dishes to choose from. 有許多道素菜可供選擇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>dish</b> to refer to anything that is round and hollow in shape with a wide uncovered top. 盤形物","examples":["...a dish used to receive satellite broadcasts. …一個用於接收衛星廣播的圓盤天線。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"All the objects that have been used to cook, serve, and eat a meal can be referred to as <b>the</b> <b>dishes</b>. 餐具","examples":["He'd cooked dinner and washed the dishes. 他做了晚餐，洗了餐具。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>do the dishes</b>, you wash the dishes. 洗碗","examples":["I hate doing the dishes. 我討厭洗碗。"]}]}]},"cut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"切，割，剪；削減，縮減；刪節，刪減；停止，切斷；抄近路，穿過；切（牌），倒（牌）；灌製（唱片），錄製（講話）；劃傷，割傷；剪裁；開始長（新牙）；<美>逃學，逃課；停止做不好的事情；切下；切開，把……切碎；鑿，挖，刻；剪短，修剪；（割斷束縛物）使脫身，使鬆開；可用於切割；能被切割；剪下（計算機文件）； 剪輯，剪接；停止拍片（或錄音、錄影）；切換畫面；（從感情上）傷害；（與另一條線）相交；沖淡，稀釋；劃分（區域）；砍（植物）；開除，除名；快速行進；突然轉向；插隊；（直截了當地）處理；去除（汙垢、油汙等）；削（球）；<美，非正式>符合要求（cut it）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"切下的肉塊；份額，一份利潤；（開出的）通道；傷口，劃口；開口，破口；（數量或尺寸上的）削減；理髮，髮型；款式，式樣；刪剪，刪節；剪輯；（錄製的）樂曲；精簡，淘汰（如參賽人員）；切，割，削；不理睬，傷人的話（或舉動）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"縮減的；割下的；雕過的；閹割過的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> something, you use a knife or a similar tool to divide it into pieces, or to mark it or damage it. If you <b>cut</b> a shape or a hole in something, you make the shape or hole by using a knife or similar tool. 切; 剪","examples":["Mrs. Haines stood nearby, holding scissors to cut a ribbon. 海恩斯太太站在旁邊，拿著剪刀剪緞帶。","Cut the tomatoes in half vertically. 把西紅柿豎著切成兩半。","The thieves cut a hole in the fence. 小偷在把籬笆割出了個洞。","This little knife cuts really well. 這把小刀切東西很好用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> <b>yourself</b> or <b>cut</b> a part of your body, you accidentally injure yourself on a sharp object so that you bleed. 割破","examples":["Johnson cut himself shaving. 約翰遜刮鬍子時割傷了自己。","I started to cry because I cut my finger. 因為割破了自己的手指，我哭了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> something such as grass, your hair, or your fingernails, you shorten them using scissors or another tool. 修剪","examples":["The most recent tenants hadn't even cut the grass. 最新來的房客竟然草坪都還沒修剪。","You've had your hair cut, it looks great. 你理髮了，很好看。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The way that clothes <b>are cut</b> is the way they are designed and made. 裁剪","examples":["...badly cut blue suits. …裁剪得很糟的藍色套裝。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> something, you reduce it. 削減","examples":["The first priority is to cut costs. 首要任務是削減費用。","The U.N. force is to be cut by 90%. 聯合國部隊將被裁減90%。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> a text, broadcast, or performance, you shorten it. If you <b>cut</b> a part of a text, broadcast, or performance, you do not publish, broadcast, or perform that part. 刪減","examples":["Branagh has cut the play judiciously. 布拉納格已經審慎地刪減了那個劇作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"To <b>cut</b> a supply of something means to stop providing it or stop it from being provided. 中斷","examples":["Winds have knocked down power lines, cutting electricity to thousands of people. 風颳斷了電線，中斷了數千人的電力供應。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> a deck of playing cards, you divide it into two. 切 (牌)","examples":["Place the cards face down on the table and cut them. 把撲克牌正面朝下放在桌上，然後切牌。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>cut</b> something, you are telling them in an irritated way to stop it.  停止","examples":["\"Cut the euphemisms, Daniel,\" Brenda snapped. “別繞彎子了，丹尼爾，”布倫達厲聲說到。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun. 切口","examples":["Carefully make a cut in the shell with a small serrated knife. 用有鋸齒的小刀小心地在殼上切個口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun. 傷口","examples":["He had sustained a cut on his left eyebrow. 他的左眉留下了一處傷口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun. 修剪","examples":["Prices vary from salon to salon, starting at $30 for a cut and blow-dry. 各家美髮店價格不一，剪吹起價$30。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun. 削減","examples":["The economy needs an immediate 2 percent cut in interest rates. 經濟即刻需要一個2%的利率下調。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun. 刪減","examples":["It has been found necessary to make some cuts in the text. 已發現有必要對文章作些刪節。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Cut</b> is also a noun.  中斷","examples":["The strike had already led to cuts in electricity and water supplies in many areas. 這次罷工已經導致很多地區供電和供水中斷。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>cut</b> of meat is a piece or type of meat which is cut in a particular way from the animal, or from a particular part of it. 塊","examples":["Use a cheap cut such as spare rib chops. 用一塊便宜的肉，比如排骨。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Someone's <b>cut</b> of the profits or winnings from something, especially ones that have been obtained dishonestly, is their share. 抽取份額","examples":["The agency is expected to take a cut of the money awarded to its client. 這家代理商理應從獎給其客戶的錢中抽取它的一份。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>cut</b> is a narrow valley which has been cut through a hill so that a road or railway line can pass through.  峽窄通道","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cut across</b> or <b>through</b> a place, you go through it because it is the shortest route to another place. 抄近路","examples":["Jesse cut across the parking lot and strolled through the main entrance. 傑西抄近道穿過停車場，漫步透過大門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cut</b> in front of someone, you move in front of them and take their place. 插隊","examples":["Somebody tried to cut in line and a fight broke out. 有人想插隊，引發了一場打鬥。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the director of a film says \"<b>cut</b>,\" they want the actors and the camera crew to stop filming. 停","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a situation is<b>cut and dried</b>, you mean that it is clear and definite. 已成定局的","examples":["Unfortunately, things cannot be as cut and dried as many people would like. 不幸的是，事情並不像很多人希望的那樣板上釘釘。"]}]}]},"dollar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美元；元（美國、加拿大、澳大利亞等許多國家的貨幣單位，1 dollar = 100 cents）；一美元紙幣或硬幣；（比喻）金錢、商業主義或貪婪的象徵；（Dollar）人名（英：多拉爾）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>dollar</b> is the unit of money used in the U.S., Canada, Australia, and some other countries. It is represented by the symbol $, the dollar sign. A dollar is divided into one hundred smaller units called cents. 元 (美國、加拿大、澳大利亞以及其他一些國家的貨幣單位)","examples":["She gets paid seven dollars an hour. 她的報酬是每小時7元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The dollar</b> is also used to refer to the American currency system. 美元","examples":["In early trading in Tokyo, the dollar fell sharply against the yen. 在東京的早盤交易中，美元對日元的匯率急劇下跌。"]}]}]},"dove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鴿子；鴿派人士，主和派人士"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Dove）（基督教藝術作品和詩歌中的）聖靈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳水；潛水；突然大幅貶值，暴跌（dive 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dove</b> is a bird that looks like a pigeon but is smaller and lighter in colour. Doves are often used as a symbol of peace. 和平鴿","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In politics, you can refer to people who support the use of peaceful methods to solve difficult situations as <b>doves</b>. Compare . 鴿派人物","examples":["A clear split over tactics appears to be emerging between doves and hawks in the party. 一個明顯的戰術上的分歧似乎正出現在黨內主和派和主戰派之間。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dove</b> is sometimes used as the past tense of . (dive)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"dog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狗，犬；公狗，公狐，公狼；質量極差的東西；卑鄙小人，無賴；<美，非正式>朋友"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"困擾，糾纏；跟蹤，尾隨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dog</b> is a very common four-legged animal that is often kept by people as a pet or to guard or hunt. There are many different breeds of dog. 狗","examples":["The British are renowned as a nation of dog lovers. 英國人以愛狗著稱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People use <b>dog</b> to refer to something that they consider unsatisfactory or of poor quality. 蹩腳貨","examples":["It's a real dog. 這是個不折不扣的蹩腳貨。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If problems or injuries <b>dog</b> you, they are with you all the time. (問題、傷病等) 長期困擾","examples":["His career has been dogged by bad luck. 他的職業生涯厄運不斷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>dog eat dog</b> to express your disapproval of a situation where everyone wants to succeed and is willing to harm other people in order to do so. 相互傾軋","examples":["It is very much dog eat dog out there. 那簡直就是自相傾軋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is going to the dogs</b>, you mean that it is becoming weaker and worse in quality. 衰落","examples":["They sit doing nothing while the country goes to the dogs. 他們坐視整個國家衰落下去。"]}]}]},"dig":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搜尋，尋找；<非正式，舊>喜歡；挖，掘"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"挖苦，嘲諷；（用手指或肘部）輕碰，輕戳；考古發掘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or animals <b>dig</b>, they make a hole in the ground or in a pile of earth, stones, or rubbish. 挖掘","examples":["I grabbed the spade and started digging. 我抓起鐵鍬開始挖了起來。","Dig a large hole and drive the stake in first. 先挖個大洞，把樁子打進去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dig</b> one thing <b>into</b> another or if one thing <b>digs</b> <b>into</b> another, the first thing is pushed hard into the second, or presses hard into it. 刺入; 戳進","examples":["She digs the serving spoon into the moussaka. 她把分菜匙插進茄合裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>dig</b> <b>yourself out of</b> a difficult or unpleasant situation, especially one which you caused yourself, you manage to get out of it. 擺脫 (困境)","examples":["He's taken these measures to try and dig himself out of a hole. 他採取了這些措施，力圖擺脫困境。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dig</b> <b>into</b> something such as a deep container, you put your hand in it to search for something. 將手伸入… (以探尋某物)","examples":["He dug into his coat pocket for his keys. 他把手伸進大衣口袋裡找鑰匙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dig into</b> a subject or a store of information, you study it very carefully in order to discover or check facts. 鑽研","examples":["...as a special congressional enquiry digs deeper into the alleged financial misdeeds of his government. …隨著一項國會特別調查行動對其政府所謂的不當財政行為的深入調查。","He has been digging into the local archives. 他一直在仔細研究當地的檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>dig</b> <b>at</b> someone, you say something which is intended to make fun of them or upset them. 挖苦; 嘲弄","examples":["She couldn't resist a dig at Dave after his unfortunate performance. 戴夫演出失敗之後，她忍不住給了他一頓嘲弄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>dig</b> in a part of their body, you push them with your finger or your elbow, usually as a warning or as a joke. (出於警告或開玩笑而用手指或肘進行的) 戳","examples":["Cassandra silenced him with a sharp dig in the small of the back. 卡桑德拉在他腰背上狠狠地戳了一下讓他閉上了嘴。"]}]}]},"downstairs":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"順樓梯而下，往樓下；在樓下"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在樓下的，在底樓的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"樓下（尤指地面的一層），下面的幾層樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>downstairs</b> in a building, you go down a staircase toward the ground floor. 往樓下","examples":["Denise went downstairs and made some tea. 丹尼絲下樓沏茶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>downstairs</b> in a building, they are on the ground floor or on a lower floor than you. 在樓下","examples":["The telephone was downstairs in the entrance hall. 電話在樓下的門廳裡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Downstairs</b> means situated on the ground floor of a building or on a lower floor than you are. 在樓下的","examples":["She repainted the downstairs rooms and closed off the second floor. 她重新粉刷了樓下的房間，並把二樓封上了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The downstairs</b> of a building is its lower floor or floors. 下面的樓層","examples":["The downstairs of the two little houses had been entirely refashioned. 兩座小房子的底層已徹底翻新過了。"]}]}]},"door":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"門；門口，門道；建築，門戶 ；（尤與 open 或 unlock 連用）機會，可能性"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"車門撞擊（騎腳踏車經過的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>door</b> is a piece of wood, glass, or metal, which is moved to open and close the entrance to a building, room, wardrobe, or vehicle. 門","examples":["I was knocking at the front door but there was no answer. 我敲了敲前門，但無人應答。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>door</b> is the space in a wall when a door is open. 門口","examples":["She looked through the door of the kitchen. Her daughter was at the stove. 透過廚房開著的門，她看到女兒正在爐子旁邊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Doors</b> is used in expressions such as <b>a few doors down</b> or <b>three doors up</b> to refer to a place that is a particular number of buildings away from where you are. 建築物 (表示兩個地點之間的距離)","examples":["Mrs. Cade's house was only a few doors down from her daughter's apartment. 從凱德夫人的房子到她女兒的公寓只隔了幾座房屋。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>answer the door</b>, you go and open the door because a visitor has knocked on it or rung the bell. 應門","examples":["Carol answered the door as soon as I knocked. 我剛敲過門，卡羅爾就把門開啟了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone gets or does something <b>by the back door</b> or <b>through the back door</b>, you are criticizing them for doing it secretly and unofficially. 走後門地","examples":["The government would not allow anyone to sneak in by the back door and seize power by force. 政府不允許任何人用不正當的手段混進來，然後透過武力奪權。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people have talks and discussions <b>behind closed doors</b>, they have them in private because they want them to be kept secret. 秘密地","examples":["...decisions taken in secret behind closed doors. …秘密做出的決定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone goes <b>from door to door</b> or goes <b>door to door</b>, they go along a street calling at each house in turn, for example, selling something. 挨家挨戶地","examples":["They are going from door to door collecting money from civilians. 他們挨家挨戶地從老百姓那裡收錢。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you talk about a distance or trip <b>from door to door</b> or <b>door to door</b>, you are talking about the distance from the place where the trip starts to the place where it finishes. 全程的","examples":["...tickets covering the whole trip from door to door. …全程票。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something helps someone to get their <b>foot in the door</b>, you mean that it gives them an opportunity to start doing something new, usually in an area that is difficult to succeed in. 獲得 (從事某項艱鉅事業的) 機會","examples":["If we can get our foot in the door, that can help us build our market. 如果能獲得這個機會，對我們開拓市場就會有所幫助。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>shuts the door in</b> your <b>face</b> or <b>slams the door in</b> your <b>face</b>, they refuse to talk to you or give you any information. 拒之門外","examples":["Did you say anything to him or just shut the door in his face? 你對他說了什麼還是直接將他拒於門外？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>lay</b> something <b>at</b> someone's <b>door</b>, you blame them for an unpleasant event or situation. 把…歸咎於","examples":["Much of the blame for the long delay could be laid at the door of the manufacturer. 拖延了這麼久，大部分的責任在於生產商。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When you are <b>out of doors</b>, you are not inside a building, but in the open air. 在戶外","examples":["The weather was fine enough for working out of doors. 天氣這麼好，很適合戶外工作。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>see</b> someone <b>to the door</b>, you go to the door with a visitor when they leave. 送至門口","examples":["Politely he saw her to the door and opened it for her. 他禮貌地將她送至門口，併為她開啟了門。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If someone <b>shows</b> you <b>the door</b>, they ask you to leave because they are angry with you. 逐出","examples":["Would they forgive and forget – or show him the door? 他們會原諒並忘記他的過失–還是會將他趕出門去？"]}]}]},"dozen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一打，十二個；大量，許多；十多個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>a</b> <b>dozen</b> things, you have twelve of them. 十二","examples":["You will be able to take ten dozen bottles free of duty through customs. 你可以攜帶120瓶免稅透過海關。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of approximately twelve things or people as <b>a</b> <b>dozen</b>. You can refer to a group of approximately six things or people as <b>half a dozen</b>. 大約一打","examples":["In half a dozen words, he had explained the bond that linked them. 他用五六個字解釋了將他們聯絡在一起的那種關係。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>dozens of</b> things or people, you are emphasizing that there are very many of them. 許多","examples":["...a storm which destroyed dozens of homes and buildings. …一場毀壞了許多房屋和建築物的暴風雨。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also use <b>dozens</b> as a pronoun. 許多東西","examples":["Just as revealing are Mr. Johnson's portraits, of which there are dozens. 透過約翰遜先生的許多肖像畫，同樣也可以瞭解其人。"]}]}]},"drinking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喝，飲；喝酒，飲酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"drink 的現在分詞和動名詞：喝，飲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（多作定語）供飲用的；飲酒的，一起喝酒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>drinking</b> friends or companions are people they regularly drink alcohol with. 定期飲酒的","examples":[]}]}]},"duckling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小鴨子，幼鴨，雛鴨；（用於固定搭配 ugly duckling）醜小鴨，指小時難看長大後變得才貌出眾的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>duckling</b> is a young duck. 小鴨子","examples":[]}]}]},"driver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"司機，駕駛員；驅動程式；推動力；驅趕某種動物的人；傳動裝置，主動輪；（電子）激勵器；高爾夫球棒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>driver</b> of a vehicle is the person who is driving it. 駕駛員","examples":["The driver got out of his van. 司機從貨車裡下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>driver</b> is a computer program that controls a device such as a printer. 驅動程式","examples":["Printer driver software includes standard features such as print layout and fit-to-page printing. 印表機驅動程式軟體包含標準功能，比如列印版面設定和符合紙張大小的列印。"]}]}]},"drink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"喝，飲；喝酒；飽覽，欣賞；<非正式>吸收（水分）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"飲料；一杯，一口，一份（飲料）；酒，酒精飲料；酒會，酒宴；<非正式>一片水（the drink）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>drink</b> a liquid, you take it into your mouth and swallow it. 喝","examples":["He drank his cup of tea. 他喝了他那杯茶。","He drank thirstily. 他迫不及待地喝了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>drink</b> means to drink alcohol. 喝酒","examples":["By his own admission, he was smoking and drinking too much. 他自己承認抽菸飲酒過度。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"喝酒","examples":["She had left him because of his drinking. 她離開了他，因為他酗酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drink</b> is an amount of a liquid which you drink. 一杯 (飲料)","examples":["I'll get you a drink of water. 我去給你弄杯水來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>drink</b> is an alcoholic drink. (一杯) 酒","examples":["She felt like a drink after a hard day. 勞累一天後，她想喝杯酒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Drink</b> is alcohol, such as beer, wine, or whisky. 酒 (如啤酒、葡萄酒、威士忌等)","examples":["Too much drink is bad for your health. 飲酒過度對你的身體有害。"]}]}]},"eagle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鷹，雕；鷹擊（比標準桿少打兩杆）；（尤指作為美國標誌的，或曾作羅馬和法國軍旗的）鷹狀圖形；<美>（曾在美國通行的價值10美元的）鷹徽金幣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（高爾夫）在（某洞）上打出老鷹球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>eagle</b> is a large bird that lives by eating small animals. 鷹","examples":[]}]}]},"dream":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夢；夢想；恍惚，出神；夢一般美妙的人或事物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做夢，夢見；夢想，想象；做白日夢，開小差；考慮，料想；白白浪費時間，虛度光陰"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"理想的，完美的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dream</b> is a series of events that you experience only in your mind while you are asleep. 夢","examples":["He had a dream about Claire. 他做了一個關於克萊爾的夢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a situation or event as a <b>dream</b> if you often think about it because you would like it to happen. 夢想; 願望","examples":["He had finally accomplished his dream of becoming a pilot. 他最終實現了成為了一名飛行員的夢想。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a situation or event that does not seem real as a <b>dream</b>, especially if it is very strange or unpleasant. 夢境般的事","examples":["When the right woman comes along, this bad dream will be over. 當合適的女人出現時，這場噩夢就會結束了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>a</b> particular person's <b>dream</b>, you think that it would be ideal for that person and that he or she would like it very much. 夢想; 夢寐以求的事物","examples":["Greece is said to be a botanist's dream. 希臘被稱作植物學家的理想聖地。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dream</b>, you experience events in your mind while you are asleep. 夢見; 做夢","examples":["Ivor dreamed that he was on a bus. 艾弗夢見了他在公共汽車上。","She dreamed about her baby. 她夢見了她的小寶貝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you often think about something that you would very much like to happen or have, you can say that you <b>dream</b> <b>of</b> it. 夢想; 渴望","examples":["As a schoolgirl, she had dreamed of becoming an actress. 當她是一名女學生的時候，她曾夢想過成為一名女演員。","For most of us, a brand new designer kitchen is something we can only dream about. 對我們大部分人來說，一個嶄新的名師設計的廚房是我們只能夢想的東西。","I dream that my son will attend college. 我夢想著我的兒子將來能上大學。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>never</b> <b>dreamed</b> <b>that</b> something would happen, you are emphasizing that you did not think that it would happen because it seemed very unlikely. 沒有想到","examples":["I never dreamed that I would be able to afford a home here. 我從未想到我能買得起這裡的房子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>would not</b> <b>dream of</b> doing something, you are emphasizing that you would never do it because you think it is wrong or is not possible or suitable for you. 決不; 不願","examples":["I wouldn't dream of making fun of you. 我決不會拿你取樂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>dream</b> to describe something that you think is ideal or perfect, especially if it is something that you thought you would never be able to have or experience. 理想的; 完美的","examples":["...a dream holiday to Jamaica. …一個去牙買加的理想假期。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>like a dream</b>, you think that they do it very well. If you say that something happens <b>like a dream</b>, you mean that it happens successfully without any problems. 完美地; 美妙地","examples":["She cooked like a dream. 她的烹飪技術棒極了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as the person or thing <b>of</b> your <b>dreams</b>, you mean that you consider them to be ideal or perfect. (某人) 理想中的","examples":["This could be the man of my dreams. 這可能是我理想的男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you could not imagine a particular thing <b>in</b> your <b>wildest dreams</b>, you are emphasizing that you think it is extremely strange or unlikely. 異想天開地","examples":["\"Never in my wildest dreams did I think I'd ever accomplish this,\" said Toni. “即便在我異想天開的時候，也從來沒有想到過我能實現它，”託尼說。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as being <b>beyond</b> your <b>wildest dreams</b>, you are emphasizing that it is better than you could have imagined or hoped for. 做夢也想不到的; 出乎意料的","examples":["She had already achieved success beyond her wildest dreams. 她已經獲得了做夢也沒想到的成功。"]}]}]},"duck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鴨子；鴨肉；母鴨；（板球）零分；<非正式>幸運兒，不尋常的人；<英，非正式>寶貝兒，親愛的；突然的低頭；帆布，粗布"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"逃避，迴避；躲避；（開玩笑地）把（人）按入水中；迅速移動；（橋牌）放掉；（迅速）低頭，彎身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>duck</b> is a common water bird with short legs, a short neck, and a large flat beak. 鴨","examples":["Chickens and ducks scratch around the outbuildings. 雞鴨在外屋四周挖扒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Duck</b> is the flesh of this bird when it is eaten as food. 鴨肉","examples":["...honey roasted duck. …蜜汁烤鴨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a score of nothing by a batsman 零分","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a heavy cotton fabric of plain weave, used for clothing, tents, etc 粗布","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"an amphibious vehicle used in World War II (第二次世界大戰中用的)水陸兩用車","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>duck</b>, you move your head or the top half of your body quickly downward to avoid something that might hit you, to avoid being seen, or to hide the expression on your face. 迅速低頭; 猛然俯身","examples":["He ducked in time to save his head from a blow from the poker. 他猛地低下頭，及時地躲過飛來一棒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>duck</b> something such as a blow, you avoid it by moving your head or body quickly downward. 閃避","examples":["Hans deftly ducked their blows. 漢斯靈活地躲過了他們的猛擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>duck</b> your head, you move it quickly downward to hide the expression on your face. 迅速低下 (頭)","examples":["He ducked his head to hide his admiration. 他低下頭以掩飾他的羨慕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that someone <b>ducks</b> a duty or responsibility when you disapprove of the fact that they avoid it. 逃避 (責任)","examples":["The defence secretary ducked the question of whether the United States was winning the war. 該國防部長迴避了美國是否在打贏這場戰爭的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to submerge or plunge suddenly and often briefly under water 忽潛忽露","examples":[]}]}]},"down":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"朝下，向下；（坐）下，（躺）下；倒，垮，塌；（寫）下，（記）下；在下方，在低處；在南部，向南方；傳下去（的）；在較低水平，下降；減到更小，變得更弱；失利，落後；不能動彈地，不能移動地；到，去，在；完全地，徹底地；初付，首付；在肚子裡；已完成，已處理；（縱橫填字遊戲）由上至下；<英>離開學校（或大學）；<英>離開首都（或重要城市）；（美橄）（球或持球隊員）成死球；（航海）順水（或順風）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在低處的，在下方的；向下的；便宜的，低廉的；降低的，低於正常水平的；不活躍的，蕭條的；比分落後於對手的；不運轉的，出故障的；悲傷的，低落的；已完成的，完結了的；完全掌握的；正式簽署（或記錄）的；瞭解的，贊成的 ；（某人數）出局的；（美橄）成死球的；趕時髦的；（火車）從大的始發站出發的；（物理）（夸克）下的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"羽絨；絨毛，軟毛，汗毛；（美橄）十碼進攻；失敗，挫折；<非正式>不快樂，沮喪；丘陵；唐斯錨地（the Downs）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"向下，朝下；沿著，順；在……的那一端； 貫穿……時間，遍及……時期；<非正式>在（或往）（某地）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使掉落；喝下，吃下；擊敗，戰勝；（美橄）使成死球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To go <b>down</b> something such as a slope or a pipe means to go toward the ground or to a lower level. 沿…而下","examples":["We're going down a mountain. 我們向山下走去。","A man came down the stairs to meet them. 一個男人走下臺階迎接他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are a particular distance <b>down</b> something, you are that distance below the top or surface of it. 在…下方","examples":["He managed to cling on to a ledge 40 feet down the rock face. 他設法抓住了巖面下方40英尺處的巖脊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you go or look <b>down</b> something such as a road or river, you go or look along it. If you are <b>down</b> a road or river, you are somewhere along it. 沿著","examples":["They set off at a jog up one street and down another. 他們跑步出發，沿著一條街跑過來又沿另外一條街跑過去。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Down</b> is also an adverb. 向下地","examples":["She went down to the kitchen again. 她又下到廚房去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Down</b> is also an adverb. 在下方地","examples":["At the bottom of the pit, some 1,300 feet down, are huge heaps of ore. 在距地面大約一千三百英尺的坑底，有大堆的礦石。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>down</b> to say that you are looking or facing in a direction that is toward the ground or toward a lower level. 向下","examples":["She was still looking down at her papers. 她還在低頭看著那些紙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you put something <b>down</b>, you put it onto a surface. (放) 到平面上","examples":["Danny put down his glass. 丹尼放下他的玻璃杯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an amount of something goes <b>down</b>, it decreases. If an amount of something is <b>down</b>, it has decreased and is at a lower level than it was. 下降","examples":["Interest rates came down today. 利率今天下降了。","Inflation will be down to three percent. 通貨膨脹將下降到3%。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Down to</b> a particular detail means including everything, even that detail. <b>Down to</b> a particular person means including everyone, even that person. 甚至包括","examples":["The bedroom was an exact replica of the original, perfect right down to the patterns on the wallpaper and the hairbrushes on the dressing table. 這間臥室精確地複製了原來的房間，模仿之細甚至連牆紙的圖案和梳妝檯上的發刷都一模一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>down to</b> a certain amount of something, you have only that amount left. 只剩下","examples":["The poor man's down to his last $5. 那個可憐的男人只剩下最後的5美元了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>down for</b> a particular thing, it has been arranged that they will do that thing, or that thing will happen. 被安排做","examples":["Mark had told me that he was down for an interview. 馬克已經告訴我他有個採訪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you pay money <b>down</b> on something, you pay part of the money you owe for it. 部分支付","examples":["He had a simple, conventional deal and paid 20 percent down at settlement. 他做了一筆簡單而常規的交易，在結算時預付了20%的定金。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If people shout \"<b>down with</b>\" something or someone, they are saying that they dislike them and want to get rid of them. 打倒","examples":["Demonstrators chanted \"down with the rebels.\" 遊行的人群高呼“打倒叛亂分子！”"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are feeling <b>down</b>, you are feeling unhappy or depressed. 情緒不高的","examples":["The old man sounded really down. 那位老人聽起來情緒真的不高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>down</b> <b>on</b> paper, it has been written on the paper. 記在紙上的","examples":["That date wasn't down on our news sheet. 該日期沒有寫在我們的報導裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a piece of equipment, especially a computer system, is <b>down</b>, it is temporarily not working. Compare <b>up</b>. 出故障的; 宕機的","examples":["The computer's down again. 那臺電腦又宕機了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>downs</b> food or a drink, you mean that they eat or drink it. 吃下; 喝下","examples":["We downed bottles of local wine. 我們喝了好幾瓶本地酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is downed</b>, they fall to the ground because they have been hurt or damaged in some way. 擊落","examples":["A couple of jet fighters were downed during the five-week rebellion. 在為期5周的叛亂期間，有兩三架噴氣式戰鬥機被擊落。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Down</b> consists of the small, soft feathers on young birds. <b>Down</b> is used to make bed-covers and pillows. 羽絨","examples":["... goose down. …鵝絨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Down</b> is very fine hair. 絨毛","examples":["The whole plant is covered with fine down. 整株植物上長滿了絨毛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"one of a maximum of four consecutive attempts by one team to advance the ball a total of at least ten yards (橄欖球)檔","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a hill, esp a sand dune 小山(尤指沙丘)","examples":[]}]}]},"ear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耳朵；靈敏的聽力；傾聽；穗；耳狀物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ears</b> are the two parts of your body, one on each side of your head, with which you hear sounds. 耳朵","examples":["He whispered something in her ear. 他在她耳邊低聲說了些什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>an</b> <b>ear</b> <b>for</b> music or language, you are able to hear its sounds accurately and to interpret them or reproduce them well. 聽覺分辨力","examples":["Moby certainly has a fine ear for a tune. 莫比對音調的分辨能力一定很強。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ear</b> is often used to refer to people's willingness to listen to what someone is saying. 聽的意願","examples":["What would cause the masses to give him a far more sympathetic ear? 什麼能使大眾更富同情心地聽他訴說呢？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>ears</b> of a cereal plant such as corn or barley are the parts at the top of the stem that contain the seeds or grains. 穗","examples":["American farmers use machines to pick the ears of corn from the plants. 美國農民使用機器收割穀穗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a request <b>falls on deaf ears</b> or if the person to whom the request is made <b>turns a deaf ear</b> <b>to</b> it, they take no notice of it. 不理會","examples":["I hope that our appeals will not fall on deaf ears. 我希望我們的請求不會被當作耳邊風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>play by ear</b> or <b>play</b> a piece of music <b>by ear</b>, you play music by relying on your memory rather than by reading printed music. 憑記憶演奏","examples":["Neil sat at the piano and began playing, by ear, the music he'd heard his older sister practising. 尼爾坐在鋼琴邊，憑著記憶開始演奏曾聽他姐姐練習過的曲子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has a tin ear </b> for something, you mean that they do not have any natural ability for it and cannot appreciate or understand it fully. 無鑑賞力","examples":["Worst of all, for a playwright specializing in characters who use the vernacular, he has a tin ear for dialogue. 最糟的是，作為一個專門刻畫使用方言人物的劇作家，他在對話方面沒有鑑賞力。"]}]}]},"eighteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"十八，十八個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十八個的，十八的"},{"pos":"num.","zh":"十八"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eighteen</b> is the number 18. 18","examples":["He was employed by them for eighteen years. 他被他們僱傭了18年。"]}]}]},"earth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地球，世界；陸地，地面；泥土，土壤；地線，電線；<英，非正式>一大筆錢；塵世；獸穴"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（電線）接地；用土掩蓋；追趕入洞穴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Earth</b> or <b>the Earth</b> is the planet on which we live. People usually say <b>Earth</b> when they are referring to the planet as part of the universe, and <b>the Earth</b> when they are talking about the planet as the place where we live. 地球","examples":["The space shuttle Atlantis returned safely to Earth today. 亞特蘭蒂斯號太空梭今天安全返回地球。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The earth</b> is the land surface on which we live and move around. 陸地; 地面","examples":["The earth shook and swayed and the walls of neighbouring houses fell around them. 地面晃動起來，附近房子的牆壁在他們周圍坍塌了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Earth</b> is the substance on the land surface of the earth, for example clay or sand, in which plants grow. 土壤; 土地","examples":["The road winds for miles through parched earth, scrub and cactus. 那條路蜿蜒數英里，穿過乾熱的土地、灌木叢和仙人掌，。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>earth</b> in an electric plug or piece of electrical equipment is the wire through which electricity passes into the ground and which makes the equipment safe. 地線","examples":["...an insulated earth. …一根絕緣地線。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>On earth</b> is used for emphasis in questions that begin with words such as \"how,\" \"why,\" \"what,\" or \"where.\" It is often used to suggest that there is no obvious or easy answer to the question being asked. 到底; 究竟","examples":["How on earth did that happen? 那到底是怎麼發生的？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>On earth</b> is used for emphasis after some negative noun groups, for example \"no reason.\" 根本 (常用在否定句中)","examples":["There was no reason on earth why she couldn't have moved in with us. 她不能跟我們一起搬進來根本沒有道理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you come <b>down to earth</b> or <b>back to earth</b>, you have to face the reality of everyday life after a period of great excitement. 回到現實","examples":["When he came down to earth after his win he admitted: \"It was an amazing feeling.\" 當在勝利之後回來面對現實時他承認：“當時感覺太棒了。”"]}]}]},"eight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"八；八個；第八；八歲；八點"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"八的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"八人划船隊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eight</b> is the number 8. 8","examples":["So far eight workers have been killed. 到目前為止已有8名員工遇難。"]}]}]},"drive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"駕車送（人）；迫使，驅使；驅趕；敲，擊；猛踢，猛擊（球）；驅動；吹，刮；鑿，挖掘；開車，駕駛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"驅車出行；強烈慾望，本能需求；私人車道；有組織的努力，運動；幹勁，驅動力；驅動器；猛踢，猛擊；驅趕，圍殲；（用於路名）路，大道；<英>（有組織的）惠斯特牌戲等的比賽；（有自動傳動裝置的汽車的）自動擋；（從球座上）發球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>drive</b> somewhere, you operate a car or other vehicle and control its movement and direction. 駕駛","examples":["I drove into town and went to a restaurant for dinner. 我開車進城到一家餐館用餐。","She never learned to drive. 她從未學過開車。","We drove the car down to Richmond for the weekend. 我們開車南下到里士滿度週末。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>drive</b> someone somewhere, you take them there in a car or other vehicle. 開車送 (某人去某處)","examples":["His daughter Carly drove him to the train station. 她的女兒卡莉開車送他去火車站。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>drives</b> a machine, it supplies the power that makes it work. 驅動","examples":["The current flows into electric motors that drive the wheels. 電流流入驅動輪子的電動機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>drive</b> something such as a nail <b>into</b> something else, you push it in or hammer it in using a lot of effort. (把釘子等) 釘進","examples":["I had to use our sledgehammer to drive the pegs into the side of the path. 我不得不用我們的大錘把樁子砸進路邊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>drive</b> people or animals somewhere, you make them go to or from that place. 驅趕","examples":["The last offensive drove thousands of people into Thailand. 最近的一次進攻把成千上萬的人驅趕到了泰國。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>drive</b> someone <b>into</b> a particular state or situation means to force them into that state or situation. 強迫; 迫使","examples":["The recession and hospital bills drove them into bankruptcy. 經濟蕭條和醫院的賬單逼得他們破產了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The desire or feeling that <b>drives</b> a person <b>to</b> do something, especially something extreme, is the desire or feeling that causes them to do it. 驅使","examples":["More than once, depression drove him to attempt suicide. 不止一次，抑鬱驅使他試圖自殺。","Jealousy drives people to murder. 忌妒心驅使人謀殺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"駕駛","examples":["...a qualified driving instructor. …一名合格的駕駛教練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drive</b> is a trip in a car or other vehicle. 駕車旅行; 乘車兜風","examples":["I thought we might go for a drive on Sunday. 我想週日我們可以去開車兜風。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>drive</b> is a wide piece of hard ground, or sometimes a private road, that leads from the road to a person's house. (將私人住宅和大路連線起來的) 車道","examples":["The boys followed Eleanor up the drive to the house. 男孩們跟著埃莉諾上了通向房子的車道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>drive</b> to refer to the mechanical part of a computer which reads the data on disks and tapes, or writes data onto them. 驅動裝置","examples":["The firm specialized in supplying pieces of equipment, such as terminals, tape drives, or printers. 這家公司專營各種裝置配件，比如終端機、磁帶機、印表機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>drive</b> is a very strong need or desire in human beings that makes them act in particular ways. 慾望","examples":["...compelling, dynamic sex drives. …不可扼制的強烈性慾。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>drive</b>, you mean they have energy and determination. 幹勁兒","examples":["John will be best remembered for his drive and enthusiasm. 約翰將因其幹勁和熱情被人們牢記。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>drive</b> is a special effort made by a group of people for a particular purpose. 運動","examples":["The ANC is about to launch a nationwide recruitment drive. 南非非洲人國民大會打算發動一次全國徵兵運動。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Drive</b> is used in the names of some streets. …道; …街","examples":["...3091 North Beverly Hills Drive, Beverly Hills, CA. …加利福尼亞州貝弗利山，北貝弗利山莊街3091號。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the wind, rain, or snow <b>drives</b> in a particular direction, it moves with great force in that direction. (向某個方向猛烈地) 吹打","examples":["Rain drove against the window. 雨打著窗戶。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(向某個方向猛烈) 吹打的","examples":["He crashed into a tree in driving rain. 在暴雨中他撞上了樹。"]}]}]},"east":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"東，東方（the east）；（世界或某個國家、地區或城市的）東部；東方（指亞洲南部和東部，包括印度、中國和日本）（the East）；（舊時）東歐共產主義國家（the East）；（橋牌）坐在東首位置的人（East）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"近東的，面朝東的；（特定的地區、城市、國家或其居民）東部的；東風的；在教堂設有聖壇的一端的（實際上的東端）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向東，在東方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>east</b> is the direction where the sun rises. 東方","examples":["...the vast swamps that lie to the east of the River Nile. …位於尼羅河以東的大片沼澤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>east</b> <b>of</b> a place, country, or region is the part which is in the east. 東部","examples":["...a village in the east of the country. …該國東部的一個村莊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The East</b> is used to refer to the southern and eastern part of Asia, including India, China, and Japan. 東南亞地區","examples":["Every so often, a new martial art arrives from the East. 時不時地，一種新武術從東南亞到達至此。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>east</b>, you travel toward the east. 向東地","examples":["To drive, go east on Route 9. 開車的話，向東上9號路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>east</b> <b>of</b> a place is positioned to the east of it. 以東地","examples":["...just east of the centre of town. …就在城中心以東。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>east</b> edge, corner, or part of a place or country is the part toward the east. 在東邊的","examples":["...a low line of hills running along the east coast. …沿著東海岸延伸的一排小山丘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>East</b> is used in the names of some countries, states, and regions in the east of a larger area. 東部的","examples":["He had been on safari in East Africa with his son. 他和他的兒子曾在東非狩獵旅行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>east</b> wind is a wind that blows from the east. 從東而來的","examples":["...a bitter east wind. …一陣刺骨的東風。"]}]}]},"ease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"容易；舒適，自在"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"減輕，緩和，放鬆；緩緩移動；使容易；降低；使離職；熟悉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>with ease</b>, you do it easily, without difficulty or effort. 輕易地","examples":["Anne was intelligent and capable of passing her exams with ease. 安妮很聰明，能夠輕易地透過考試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>at ease</b>, you are feeling confident and relaxed, and are able to talk to people without feeling nervous or anxious. If you put someone <b>at ease</b>, you make them feel at ease. 放鬆的; 自在的","examples":["It is essential to feel at ease with your therapist. 與治療師在一起時，關鍵是放鬆心情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>ill at ease</b>, you feel somewhat uncomfortable, anxious, or worried. 不舒適; 不自在","examples":["He appeared embarrassed and ill at ease with the sustained applause that greeted him. 他對持久的掌聲顯得尷尬、不自在。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>ease of</b> a particular activity, you are referring to the way that it has been made easier to do, or to the fact that it is already easy to do. 簡便","examples":["For ease of reference, only the relevant extracts of the regulations are included. 為便於參閱，只收錄了相關條例的摘錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ease</b> is the state of being very comfortable and able to live as you want, without any worries or problems. 舒適; 悠閒","examples":["She lived a life of ease. 她過著悠閒自在的生活。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something unpleasant <b>eases</b> or if you <b>ease</b> it, it is reduced in degree, speed, or intensity. 減輕; 減緩","examples":["Tensions had eased. 緊張緩解了。","I gave him some brandy to ease the pain. 我給了他一些白蘭地以減輕疼痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>ease</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere or <b>ease</b> somewhere, you move there slowly, carefully, and gently. If you <b>ease</b> something somewhere, you move it there slowly, carefully, and gently. 小心緩慢地移動","examples":["I eased my way toward the door. 我緩慢地向門口走去。","He eased his foot off the accelerator. 他慢慢地把腳從油門上挪開。"]}]}]},"edge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊，邊緣；鋒，刃；優勢；影響力，奇特的品質；（聲音裡的）尖銳，怒氣；（壞事的）邊緣，臨界點；稜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩慢地移動；給……加邊；險勝；用球拍邊擊球；傾斜滑雪；修剪（草地邊緣）；使銳利，使尖銳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>edge</b> of something is the place or line where it stops, or the part of it that is farthest from the middle. 邊緣; 邊際","examples":["We were on a hill, right on the edge of town. 我們在一座小山上，正好位於城鎮邊緣。","She was standing at the water's edge. 她正站在水邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>edge</b> of something sharp such as a knife or an axe is its sharp or narrow side. 刃","examples":["...the sharp edge of the sword. …鋒利的劍刃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>edge</b> <b>of</b> something, especially something bad, is the point at which it may start to happen. 邊緣","examples":["They have driven the rhino to the edge of extinction. 他們已經把犀牛逼到了滅絕的邊緣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something has an <b>edge</b>, they have an advantage that makes them stronger or more likely to be successful than another thing or person. 優勢","examples":["The three days Uruguay have to prepare could give them the edge over Brazil. 3天的準備時間也許能使烏拉圭比巴西略勝一籌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>an edge</b>, you mean that they have a powerful quality. 銳氣","examples":["Featuring new bands gives the show an edge. 突出新樂隊的特色給該演出一種銳氣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone's voice has an <b>edge</b> <b>to</b> it, it has a sharp, bitter, or emotional quality. 尖銳; 尖刻","examples":["But underneath the humour is an edge of bitterness. 在幽默的背後卻是一種怨恨的尖刻。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>edges</b> somewhere, they move very slowly in that direction. 慢慢移動","examples":["He edged closer to the telephone, ready to grab it. 他慢慢地移近電話，準備抓起它。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you or your nerves are <b>on edge</b>, you are tense, nervous, and unable to relax. 緊張不安的","examples":["My nerves were constantly on edge. 我的神經處於不斷緊張中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>takes the edge off</b> an unpleasant situation, it weakens its effect or intensity. 減弱","examples":["Poor health took the edge off her performance. 健康不佳使她的表演減色。"]}]}]},"eighty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"八十；八十歲；八十年代"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"八十的，八十個的；八十歲的"},{"pos":"num.","zh":"八十"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eighty</b> is the number 80. 80","examples":["Eighty horses trotted up. 80匹馬小跑上來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>eighties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 80 and 89. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>eighties</b>, you are aged between 80 and 89. If the temperature is <b>in the eighties</b>, the temperature is between 80 and 89 degrees. 八十幾","examples":["He was in his late eighties and had become the country's most respected elder statesman. 那時他年近九十，並且已經成為該國最受尊敬的政界元老。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The eighties</b> is the decade between 1980 and 1989. 80年代","examples":["He ran a property development business in the eighties. 他在80年代經營一家房地產開發公司。"]}]}]},"egg":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鳥類的）卵，蛋；（尤指用作食品的）蛋，雞蛋；卵子，卵細胞；<非正式>人，傢伙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"煽動，慫恿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>egg</b> is an oval object that is produced by a female bird and contains a baby bird. Other animals such as reptiles and fish also lay eggs. 蛋; 卵","examples":["...a baby bird hatching from its egg. …一隻從蛋殼裡孵出來的雛鳥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In many countries, <b>eggs</b> often means hen's eggs, eaten as food. 雞蛋","examples":["Break the eggs into a shallow bowl and beat them lightly. 把雞蛋打在一個淺碗裡並且稍微攪打。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Egg</b> is used to refer to an object in the shape of a hen's egg. 卵狀物","examples":["...a chocolate egg. …一個巧克力蛋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>egg</b> is a cell that is produced in the bodies of female animals and humans. If it is fertilized by a sperm, a baby develops from it. 卵子","examples":["It only takes one sperm to fertilize an egg. 只需一個精子就可以使卵受精。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone puts <b>all</b> their <b>eggs in one basket</b>, they put all their effort or resources into doing one thing so that, if it fails, they have no alternatives left. 孤注一擲","examples":["The key word here is diversify; don't put all your eggs in one basket. 這裡的關鍵詞是多樣化投資，不要孤注一擲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has <b>egg on</b> their <b>face</b> or has <b>egg all over</b> their <b>face</b>, they have been made to look foolish. 出洋相","examples":["If they take this game lightly they could end up with egg on their faces. 如果他們輕率地對待這場比賽，他們可能會以出洋相收場。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to throw eggs at 向...扔雞蛋","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to urge or incite, esp to daring or foolish acts 煽動; 慫恿","examples":[]}]}]},"draw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"畫，繪畫；草擬，制定；吸引，使注意；引起（反應）；獲得，得到；推斷出；抽出，吸出；（從銀行賬戶）取出；拉，拖；利用，動用；抽（煙），吸（氣）；放（血），抽（血）；拔出，掏出；以平局結束；抽籤，抓鬮；（向特定方向）移動；使說出，使吐露；作（比較或對比）；（船）吃（水）；（帆）吃飽風；（滾木球）使（球）朝預定的目標作弧線運動；（茶）被泡開"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"平局；抽彩，抽籤；有吸引力的人（或事物）；吸菸；拔槍；（高爾夫）偏球；<非正式>大麻製品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>draw</b>, or when you <b>draw</b> something, you use a pencil or pen to produce a picture, pattern, or diagram. 畫","examples":["She would sit there drawing with the pencil stub. 她會坐在那兒用鉛筆頭畫畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> something or someone in a particular direction, you move them in that direction, usually by pulling them gently. 輕拖; 輕拉","examples":["He drew his chair nearer the fire. 他把椅子輕輕拉近火邊。","He put his arm around Caroline's shoulders and drew her close to him. 他把手臂摟在卡羅琳的肩膀上並且把她輕輕拉近自己。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>draw</b> a curtain or blind, you pull it across a window, either to cover or to uncover it. 拉 (窗簾等)","examples":["After drawing the curtains, she lit a candle. 拉上窗簾後，她點了一根蠟燭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>draws</b> a gun, knife, or other weapon, they pull it out of its container and threaten you with it. 拔出 (武器)","examples":["He drew his dagger and turned to face his pursuers. 他拔出匕首並且轉過身去面對追他的人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> a deep breath, you breathe in deeply once. 吸入","examples":["He paused, drawing a deep breath. 他停下，深吸了一口氣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>draw</b> something such as water or energy <b>from</b> a particular source means to take it from that source. 汲取 (水、能源等); 提取 (水、能源等)","examples":["Villagers still have to draw their water from wells. 村民仍然要從井裡打水。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something that hits you or presses part of your body <b>draws</b> blood, it cuts your skin so that it bleeds. 抽 (血)","examples":["Any practice that draws blood could increase the risk of getting the virus. 任何形式抽血都能增加感染病毒的危險。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> money out of a bank account, you get it from the account so that you can use it. 提取 (錢款)","examples":["She was drawing out cash from an ATM. 她那時正在從自動取款機上取錢。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"To <b>draw</b> something means to choose it or to be given it, as part of a competition, game, or lottery. 抽 (獎); 抽 (籤)","examples":["He put the pile of chips in the centre of the table and drew a card. 他把一堆籌碼放在桌子中央，抽了一張牌。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"To <b>draw</b> something <b>from</b> a particular thing or place means to take or get it from that thing or place. 取得","examples":["I draw strength from the millions of women who have faced this challenge successfully. 我從許許多多成功面對這種挑戰的婦女身上獲得了力量。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something such as a film or an event <b>draws</b> a lot of people, it is so interesting or entertaining that a lot of people go to it. 吸引","examples":["The game is currently drawing huge crowds. 這項比賽目前正吸引著大批群眾。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone or something <b>draws</b> you, it attracts you very strongly. 強烈吸引","examples":["In no sense did he draw and enthral her as Alex had done. 他遠不如亞歷克斯那麼強烈地吸引她，讓她著迷。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> a particular conclusion, you decide that that conclusion is true. 得出 (結論)","examples":["He draws two conclusions from this. 他由此得出兩個結論。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> a comparison, parallel, or distinction, you compare or contrast two different ideas, systems, or other things. 作出 (比較); 加以 (區別)","examples":["...literary critics drawing comparisons between George Sand and George Eliot. …把喬治·桑和喬治·艾略特進行比較的文學評論家。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> someone's attention to something, you make them aware of it or make them think about it. 使注意","examples":["He was waving his arms to draw their attention. 他正揮動手臂吸引他們的注意力。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If someone or something <b>draws</b> a particular reaction, people react to it in that way. 引起 (某種反應)","examples":["Such a policy would inevitably draw fierce resistance from farmers. 這樣的政策將不可避免地引起農民的激烈抵制。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"畫畫","examples":["I like dancing, singing, and drawing. 我喜歡跳舞、唱歌和畫畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Draw</b> is also a noun. 抽獎; 抽籤","examples":["...the final draw for all prize winners takes place on March 17. …最後一輪所有獲獎者的抽籤在3月17日舉行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Draw</b> is also a noun. 平局","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> somewhere, you move there slowly. 緩慢移動","examples":["She drew away and did not smile. 她慢步走開，面無笑容。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a vehicle <b>draws</b> somewhere, it moves there smoothly and steadily. 平穩地前進","examples":["Claire had seen the taxi drawing away. 克萊爾看著計程車緩緩駛走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> <b>on</b> a cigarette, you breathe the smoke from it into your mouth or lungs. 吸菸","examples":["He drew on an American cigarette. 他吸了一口美國香菸。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a game or competition, if one person or team <b>draws</b> <b>with</b> another one, or if two people or teams <b>draw</b>, they have the same number of points or goals at the end of the game. (在遊戲或競賽中) 打平","examples":["Holland and the Republic of Ireland drew one-one. 荷蘭隊與愛爾蘭隊一比一平。","We drew with Ireland in the first game. 我們同愛爾蘭隊在第一局打成平局。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an event or period of time <b>draws to a close</b> or <b>draws to an end</b>, it finishes. 結束","examples":["Another celebration had drawn to its close. 另一個慶典已經結束了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or period of time <b>is drawing closer</b> or <b>is drawing nearer</b>, it is approaching. 來臨; 臨近","examples":["Next spring's elections are drawing closer. 下一個春季選舉即將來臨。"]}]}]},"eleven":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十一；十一個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十一；十一個；（體育）由十一人組成的運動隊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十一的；十一個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eleven</b> is the number 11. 11","examples":["...the Princess and her eleven friends. …該公主和她的11個朋友。"]}]}]},"elephant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"象，大象；大號圖畫紙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>elephant</b> is a very large animal with a long, flexible nose called a trunk, which it uses to pick up things. Elephants live in India and Africa. 大象","examples":[]}]}]},"english":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"英國的；英國人的；英語的，英文的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"英語，英文；英語（學科）；（總稱）英國人，英格蘭人；（檯球等的）側旋"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把……譯成英語，把……譯成英文"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>English</b> is the language spoken by people who live in Great Britain and Ireland, the United States, Canada, Australia, and many other countries. 英語","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The English</b> are English people. 英格蘭人","examples":["It is often said that the English are reserved. 人們常說英格蘭人保守。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>English</b> means belonging or relating to England, or to its people or language. It is also often used to mean belonging or relating to Great Britain, although many people object to this. 英格蘭 (人) 的; 英國 (人) 的; 英語的","examples":["...the English way of life. …英格蘭人的生活方式。"]}]}]},"examination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"考試；審查，調查；醫學檢查；<法律>訊問，查問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>examination</b> is a formal test that you take to show your knowledge or ability in a particular subject, or to obtain a qualification. 考試","examples":["...college examination results. …大學考試成績。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a medical <b>examination</b>, a doctor looks at your body, feels it, or does simple tests in order to check how healthy you are. (健康狀況) 檢查","examples":["You must see your doctor for a thorough examination. 你必須去看醫生，做個全面體檢。"]}]}]},"evening":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"晚上，傍晚；晚會，晚間活動；暮年，晚年"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"晚上好（good evening 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在晚上的，為晚上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>evening</b> is the part of each day between the end of the afternoon and the time when you go to bed. 傍晚; 晚上","examples":["All he did that evening was sit around the house. 那天晚上他所做的就是閒坐在家裡。","Supper is from 5:00 to 6:00 in the evening. 晚餐是在傍晚5至6點間。"]}]}]},"exam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"考試；試卷；<美>醫學檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>exam</b> is a formal test that you take to show your knowledge or ability in a particular subject, or to obtain a qualification. 考試","examples":["I don't want to take any more exams. 我不想再參加任何考試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a medical <b>exam</b>, a doctor looks at your body, feels it, or does simple tests in order to check how healthy you are. (健康狀況) 檢查","examples":["These medical exams have shown I am in perfect physical condition. 這些體檢已表明我健康狀況非常好。"]}]}]},"enough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"充足的，足夠的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"足夠，充分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"充分地，足夠地；相當，很；說來奇怪，說起來有趣（strangely/interestingly enough）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"足夠的（數目或數量），充分"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"夠了，別再說了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> means as much as you need or as much as is necessary. 足夠的","examples":["They had enough cash for a one-way ticket. 他們有足夠的現金買一張單程票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also a determiner. 足夠量的","examples":["Would you shut up, please! I'm having enough trouble with these children! 請住口！我和這幫孩子之間的麻煩已經夠多了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also an adverb. 足夠地","examples":["I was old enough to work and earn money. 我到了可以工作、掙錢的年齡了。","Do you believe that sentences for criminals are tough enough at present? 你認為對犯罪分子目前的刑罰足夠嚴厲嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also an adverb. 足夠量地","examples":["I'm serious, things are difficult enough as they are. 我是認真的，事情照現在這樣已經夠困難的了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>enough</b> to say that something is the case to a moderate or fairly large degree. 相當地","examples":["Winters is a common enough surname. 溫特斯是一個相當普通的姓。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>enough</b> in expressions such as <b>strangely enough</b> and <b>interestingly enough</b> to indicate that you think a fact is strange or interesting. 真…","examples":["Strangely enough, the last thing he thought of was his beloved Tanya. 真奇怪，他最後想到的是他心愛的坦尼婭。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also a pronoun. 足夠的人或事","examples":["Although the police say efforts are being made, they are not doing enough. 儘管警方說他們正在努力，但是他們做得還不夠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>enough</b>, you mean that you do not want it to continue any longer or get any worse. 夠了","examples":["I met him only the once, and that was enough. 我只見過他一次，那就夠了。","I think I have said enough. 我想我已經說得夠多了。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also a quantifier. 足夠的量","examples":["All parents worry about whether their child is getting enough of the right foods. 所有父母都擔心他們的孩子是否得到足夠量的恰當的食物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also a quantifier. 足夠的量","examples":["Ann had heard enough of this. 安這種話已經聽夠了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enough</b> is also an adjective. 足夠量的","examples":["Her disappearance and death would give proof enough of Charles' guilt. 她的失蹤和死亡將提供足夠的證據證明查爾斯有罪。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have had enough</b>, you mean that you are unhappy with a situation and you want it to stop. 受夠了","examples":["I had had enough of other people for one night. 一個晚上我就受夠其他人了。"]}]}]},"equal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（在數量、大小、程度、價值方面）相等的，相同的；平等的，同等的；勝任的，合適的；勢均力敵的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在大小、數字、數量上）等於；比得上，達到；導致，結果為"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同等的人，相等物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two things are <b>equal</b> or if one thing is <b>equal</b> <b>to</b> another, they are the same in size, number, standard, or value. 相等的","examples":["Investors can borrow an amount equal to the property's purchase price. 投資者可以借與房地產購買價相等數額的款項。","...in a population having equal numbers of men and women. …男女人數相等的人口中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If different groups of people have <b>equal</b> rights or are given <b>equal</b> treatment, they have the same rights or are treated the same as each other, however different they are. 平等的 (權利、待遇等)","examples":["We will be demanding equal rights at work. 我們將要求工作中的平等權利。","...the commitment to equal opportunities. …平等機會的承諾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that people are <b>equal</b>, you mean that they have or should have the same rights and opportunities as each other. (權利、機會等) 平等的","examples":["We are equal in every way. 我們在各方面都是平等的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>equal to</b> a particular job or situation, they have the necessary ability, strength, or courage to deal successfully with it. 能成功應付 (某工作、某情形等) 的","examples":["She was determined that she would be equal to any test the corporation put to them. 她決意要成功應對該公司對他們的任何考驗。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is your <b>equal</b> has the same ability, status, or rights as you have. (能力、地位或權利等) 同等的人","examples":["She was one of the boys, their equal. 她是男孩們中的一員，和他們平起平坐。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>equals</b> a particular number or amount, it is the same as that amount or the equivalent of that amount. (數量上) 等於","examples":["9 percent interest less 7 percent inflation equals 2 percent. 9％的利息減去7％的通貨膨脹等於2％。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>equal</b> something or someone means to be as good or as great as them. 比得上","examples":["The victory equalled the team's best in history. 這次勝利平了該隊歷史上的最佳。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>other things being equal</b>\" or \"<b>all things being equal</b>\" when talking about a possible situation, you mean if nothing unexpected happens or if there are no other factors that affect the situation. 同等條件下; 如無意外情況發生","examples":["It appears reasonable to assume that, other things being equal, most hostel tenants would prefer single to shared rooms. 似乎有理由這樣想：同等條件下，大多數旅店房客更喜歡住單人間而不願意與人合住。"]}]}]},"example":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"例子，例證；榜樣，楷模；典型，範例；例句，例題；警戒，受罰（以示警告）者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"得到說明，可加以舉例說明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>example</b> <b>of</b> something is a particular situation, object, or person that shows that what is being claimed is true. 例子","examples":["The doctors gave numerous examples of patients being expelled from the hospital. 醫生給出了大量病人被逐出醫院的例項。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>example</b> <b>of</b> a particular class of objects or styles is something that has many of the typical features of such a class or style, and that you consider clearly represents it. 範例","examples":["Symphonies 103 and 104 stand as perfect examples of early symphonic construction. 第103和104號交響曲是早期交響樂譜曲的完美範本。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a person or their behaviour as an <b>example</b> <b>to</b> other people, you mean that he or she behaves in a good or correct way that other people should copy. 榜樣","examples":["He is a model professional and an example to the younger boys. 他是個模範的專業人員，是年輕人的榜樣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>for example</b> to introduce and emphasize something that shows that something is true. 例如","examples":["Take, for example, the simple sentence: \"The man climbed up the hill.\" 以這個簡單句為例：“那個人爬上了山坡。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> someone's <b>example</b>, you behave in the same way as they did in the past, or in a similar way, especially because you admire them. 以 (某人) 為榜樣","examples":["Following the example set by her father, she has fulfilled her role and done her duty. 她以父親為榜樣，履行了她的職責，完成了她的使命"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>make an example of</b> someone who has done something wrong means to punish them severely as a warning to other people not to do the same thing. 嚴懲 (某人) 以警告他人","examples":["Let us at least see our courts make an example of these despicable criminals. 讓我們至少看到我們的法庭嚴懲卑鄙的罪犯們以示儆戒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>set an example</b>, you encourage or inspire people by your behaviour to behave or act in a similar way. 樹立榜樣","examples":["An officer's job was to set an example. 一個官員的任務就是樹立榜樣。"]}]}]},"factory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工廠，製造廠；（在外國的）代理店"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>factory</b> is a large building where machines are used to make large quantities of goods. 工廠","examples":["He owned furniture factories in New York State. 他在紐約州擁有一些傢俱廠。"]}]}]},"fact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事實，真相；現實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Facts</b> are pieces of information that can be discovered. 例項","examples":["There is so much information you can almost effortlessly find the facts for yourself. 有這麼多資訊，你幾乎能毫不費力地為自己找到例項。","His opponent swamped him with facts and figures. 他的對手用例項和數字讓他難以招架。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you refer to something as a <b>fact</b> or as <b>fact</b>, you mean that you think it is true or correct. 事實","examples":["...a statement of verifiable historical fact. …一個對可考證的歷史事實的說明。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>the fact that</b> after some verbs or prepositions, especially in expressions such as <b>in view of the fact that</b>, <b>apart from the fact that</b>, and <b>despite the fact that</b>, to link the verb or preposition with a clause. …這一事實","examples":["His chances do not seem good in view of the fact that the Chief Prosecutor has already voiced his public disapproval. 鑑於首席檢察官已公開表示反對這一事實，他的機會看起來不好。","Despite the fact that the disease is so prevalent, treatment is still far from satisfactory. 儘管事實上這種疾病非常普遍，治療卻遠不盡如人意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>the fact that</b> instead of a simple that-clause either for emphasis or because the clause is the subject of your sentence. …這一事實","examples":["My family now accepts the fact that I don't eat sugar or bread. 我的家人現在接受了我不吃糖或麵包這一事實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>in fact</b>, <b>in actual fact</b>, or <b>in point of fact</b> to indicate that you are giving more detailed information about what you have just said. 確切地說","examples":["We've had a pretty bad time while you were away. In fact, we very nearly split up this time. 我們在你走的那段時間過得非常糟糕。確切地說，我們這次幾乎分道揚鑣了。","He apologized as soon as he realized what he had done. In actual fact he wrote a nice little note to me. 他一意識到他所做的一切就道歉了。確切地說，他給我寫了一張友善的小便條。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>in fact</b>, <b>in actual fact</b>, or <b>in point of fact</b> to introduce or draw attention to a comment that modifies, contradicts, or contrasts with a previous statement. 實際上","examples":["That sounds rather simple, but in fact it's very difficult. 那聽起來很簡單，但實際上非常難。","They complained that they had been trapped inside the police station, but in fact most were seen escaping over the adjacent roofs to safety in nearby buildings. 他們抱怨說他們被困在警察局，但實際上大部分人被看見透過毗鄰的屋頂逃往附近建築物內的安全地帶。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>as a matter of fact</b> to introduce a statement that gives more details about what has just been said, or an explanation of it, or something that contrasts with it. 確切地講; 事實上","examples":["The local people saw the suffering to which these deportees were subjected. And, as a matter of fact, the local people helped the victims. 當地人目睹了這些被放逐的人遭受的苦難。而且，確切地講，當地人幫助了這些受害者。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that you know something <b>for a fact</b>, you are emphasizing that you are completely certain that it is true. 確實","examples":["I know for a fact that baby corn is very expensive in Europe. 我確實知道玉米筍在歐洲是非常昂貴的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>the fact is</b> or <b>the fact of the matter is</b> to introduce and draw attention to a summary or statement of the most important point about what you have been saying. 總而言之","examples":["The fact is blindness hadn't stopped the children from doing many of the things that sighted children enjoy. 總而言之，失明並沒有阻止這些孩子做有視力兒童喜愛做的許多事情。"]}]}]},"farmer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"農夫，農民，農場主；（Farmer，人名）法默（英），法爾梅（法），法梅爾（西）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>farmer</b> is a person who owns or manages a farm. 農場主","examples":[]}]}]},"farm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"農場，養殖場；農舍；生產企業"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"耕種，養殖；（收取一定費用）將（稅收）包出；承包，外包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>farm</b> is an area of land, together with the buildings on it, that is used for growing crops or raising animals, usually in order to sell them. 農場","examples":["Farms in France are much smaller than those in the United States or even Britain. 法國的農場比美國甚至英國的都小得多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A mink <b>farm</b> or a fish <b>farm</b>, for example, is a place where a particular kind of animal or fish is bred and kept in large quantities in order to be sold. 養殖場","examples":["...trout fresh from a local trout farm. …來自當地一家鮭魚養殖場的新鮮鮭魚。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>farm</b> an area of land, you grow crops or keep animals on it. 耕種; 養殖","examples":["They farmed some of the best land in the country. 他們耕種著該國最好的一些土地。","Bease has been farming for 30 years. 比斯經營農場已有30年。"]}]}]},"end":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"最後部分，末尾；結束，結局；端點；目的；剩餘物，殘餘；過世；部分，方面；半邊球場；城區；邊鋒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結束，終止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The end</b> <b>of</b> something such as a period of time, an event, a book, or a film is the last part of it or the final point in it. 結尾","examples":["The report is expected by the end of the year. 這份報告預期年底前出臺。","...families who settled in the region at the end of the 17th century. …於17世紀末定居該地區的家庭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>end</b> <b>to</b> something or the <b>end</b> <b>of</b> it is the act or result of stopping it so that it does not continue any longer. 結束","examples":["The government today called for an end to the violence. 政府今天呼籲結束暴力。","I was worried she would walk out or bring the interview to an end. 我擔心她會突然退席或者終止採訪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The two <b>ends</b> of something long and narrow are the two points or parts of it that are farthest away from each other. 末端","examples":["The company is planning to place surveillance equipment at both ends of the tunnel. 該公司計劃在隧道的兩端安裝監視裝置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>end</b> <b>of</b> a long, narrow object such as a finger or a pencil is the tip or smallest edge of it, usually the part that is furthest away from you. 末梢","examples":["He tapped the ends of his fingers together. 他用手指尖相互輕叩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>End</b> is used to refer to either of the two extreme points of a scale, or of something that you are considering as a scale. (天平等的) 任一端","examples":["At the other end of the social scale was the grocer. 處於社會階層另一端的是雜貨商。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>other</b> <b>end</b> is one of two places that are connected because people are communicating with each other by telephone or writing, or are travelling from one place to the other. 兩地之一","examples":["When he answered the phone, Fred was at the other end. 當他接起電話，電話那頭是弗雷德。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you refer to a particular <b>end</b> of a project or piece of work, you mean a part or aspect of it, such as a part of it that is done by a particular person or in a particular place. (專案、工作的) 部分","examples":["You take care of your end, kid, I'll take care of mine. 你管好你那塊兒，年輕人，我會管好我這塊兒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"An <b>end</b> is the purpose for which something is done or toward which you are working. 目的","examples":["The police force is being manipulated for political ends. 警察機關正被操控用以達到政治目的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"終止","examples":["The ending of a marriage by death is different in many ways from an ending caused by divorce. 死亡造成的婚姻終止同離婚造成的婚姻終止在很多方面是不同的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>at an end</b>, it has finished and will not continue. 結束了","examples":["The recession is definitely at an end. 蕭條期肯定是要結束了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>comes to an end</b>, it stops. 終止","examples":["The cold war came to an end. 冷戰終止。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>at the end of the day</b> when you are talking about what happens after a long series of events or what appears to be the case after you have considered the relevant facts. 最終; 到頭來","examples":["At the end of the day it's up to them to decide. 到頭來，還得由他們決定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>in the end</b> when you are saying what is the final result of a series of events, or what is your final conclusion after considering all the relevant facts. 最終","examples":["I toyed with the idea of calling the police, but in the end I didn't. 我不經意地想過要報警，但最終沒有。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you find it difficult to <b>make ends meet</b>, you cannot manage very well financially because you hardly have enough money for the things you need. 餬口","examples":["With Betty's salary they barely made ends meet. 靠貝蒂的工資，他們簡直無法餬口。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>No end</b> means a lot. 許多","examples":["Teachers inform me that Todd's behaviour has improved no end. 老師們告訴我託德的行為改善了許多。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When something happens for hours, days, weeks, or years <b>on end</b>, it happens continuously and without stopping for the amount of time that is mentioned. 連續地","examples":["He is a wonderful companion and we can talk for hours on end. 他是個極好的夥伴，我們可以連續談上幾個小時。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Something that is <b>on end</b> is upright, instead of in its normal or natural position, for example, lying down, flat, or on its longest side. 豎著","examples":["Wet books should be placed on end with their pages kept apart. 弄溼的書應該豎著放置，書頁分開。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"To <b>put an end to</b> something means to cause it to stop. 使某事終止","examples":["Only a political solution could put an end to the violence. 只有一個政治的解決方式才能終止暴力。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a process or person has reached <b>the end of the road</b>, they are unable to progress any further. 窮途末路","examples":["Given the results of the vote, is this the end of the road for the hardliners in Congress? 就投票的結果來看，國會里的強硬派是不是已經走到盡頭了？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that something bad is <b>not the end of the world</b>, you are trying to stop yourself or someone else being so upset by it, by suggesting that it is not the worst thing that could happen. 天塌不下來","examples":["Obviously I'd be disappointed if we don't make it, but it wouldn't be the end of the world. 顯然，如果我們不能成功我會失望的，但天不會塌下來。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone <b>ends it all</b>, they kill themselves. 自殺","examples":["He grew suicidal, thinking up ways to end it all. 他變得想自殺，想出了多種自殺方式。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a situation, process, or activity <b>ends</b>, or when something or someone <b>ends</b> it, it reaches its final point and stops. 結束","examples":["The meeting quickly ended and Steve and I left the room. 會議很快結束了，之後史蒂夫和我離開了房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>ends</b> a period of time in a particular way, you are indicating what the final situation was like. You can also say that a period of time <b>ends</b> in a particular way. 以…終止","examples":["The markets ended the week on a quiet note. 市場本週在平靜氣氛中收市。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a book, speech, or performance <b>ends</b> <b>with</b> a particular thing or the writer or performer <b>ends</b> it <b>with</b> that thing, its final part consists of the thing mentioned. 以…收尾","examples":["His statement ended with the words: \"Pray for me.\" 他的宣告以一句“為我祈禱”收尾。","The book ends on a lengthy description of Hawaii. 這本書以一段對夏威夷的冗長描述作結。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a period of time <b>ends</b>, it reaches its final point. (時間) 結束","examples":["Reports usually come out about three weeks after each month ends. 報告通常在每月結束後大約三週釋出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation or event <b>ends</b> in a particular way, it has that particular result. 以…告終","examples":["The incident could have ended in tragedy. 這個事件原本可能以悲劇告終。","Our conversations ended with him saying he would try to be more understanding. 我們的談話結束的時候，他說他會試著更為通情達理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an object <b>ends with</b> or <b>in</b> a particular thing, it has that thing on its tip or point, or as its last part. 以…為末端","examples":["It has three pairs of legs, each ending in a large claw. 它有3對腿，每條腿的末端都有一個大爪子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A journey, road, or river that <b>ends</b> at a particular place stops there and goes no further. (旅程、道路、河流等) 終止","examples":["The motorway ended at an intersection. 這條公路止於一個十字路口。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something <b>ends</b> at a particular point, you mean that it is applied or exists up to that point, and no further. 侷限於","examples":["Heather is also 25 and from Boston, but the similarity ends there. 希瑟也是25歲，也是波士頓人，但是他們的相似之處僅限於此。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>end</b> <b>by</b> doing something or <b>end</b> in a particular state, you do that thing or get into that state even though you did not originally intend to. 到頭來","examples":["They ended by making themselves miserable. 他們到頭來把自己弄慘了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to surpass; outdo 超越; 勝過","examples":[]}]}]},"eye":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"眼睛；目光，所看之處；眼力，鑑賞力；眼光，視角；觀點，態度；（鉤）環，釦眼；（馬鈴薯上的）芽眼，芽；（颶風等風暴的）風眼；拍攝物件，取景器；（電）眼，（紅外）眼，眼狀探測裝置；針眼，針鼻兒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"注視，仔細打量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>eyes</b> are the parts of your body with which you see. 眼睛","examples":["I opened my eyes and looked. 我睜開眼睛看了看。","...a tall, thin white-haired lady with piercing dark brown eyes. …有一雙深邃的深棕色眼睛的一位瘦高個白髮女士。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>eye</b> when you are talking about a person's ability to judge things or about the way in which they are considering or dealing with things. 眼光","examples":["William was a man of discernment, with an eye for quality. 威廉是個有鑑賞力的人，對於品質的優劣很有眼力。","He first learned to fish under the watchful eye of his grandmother. 他最初在祖母留心的眼光下學習釣魚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>eye</b> is a small metal loop that a hook fits into, as a fastening on a piece of clothing. (衣服搭扣之) 環扣","examples":["There were lots of hooks and eyes in Victorian costumes! 維多利亞時代的服裝上有很多鉤子和環扣！"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>eye</b> of a needle is the small hole at one end that the thread passes through. (針) 眼","examples":["The only difficult part was threading the cotton through the eye of the needle! 唯一困難的部分是將棉線穿過針眼！"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The eye of</b> a storm, tornado, or hurricane is the centre of it. (暴風雨、龍捲風或颶風的) 中心; (龍捲風、颶風的) 眼","examples":["The eye of the hurricane hit Florida just south of Miami. 颶風中心襲擊了邁阿密正南面的佛羅里達州。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>eye</b> someone or something in a particular way, you look at them carefully in that way. 注視","examples":["Sally eyed Claire with interest. 薩莉饒有興味地注視著克萊爾。","We eyed each other thoughtfully. 我們若有所思地看了看彼此。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to look at in a manner indicating sexual interest; ogle 色迷迷地看; 送秋波 (Also eye up)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>before</b> your <b>eyes</b>, <b>in front of</b> your <b>eyes</b>, or <b>under</b> your <b>eyes</b>, you are emphasizing that it happens where you can see it clearly and often implying that it is surprising or unpleasant. 在…眼前/下","examples":["A lot of them died in front of our eyes. 他們中有很多死在我們眼前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cast</b> your <b>eye</b> or <b>run</b> your <b>eye</b> over something, you look at it or read it quickly. 投以一瞥","examples":["I would be grateful if he could cast an expert eye over it and tell me what he thought of it. 如果他能以專家的眼光看一下它並告訴我他的想法，我將不勝感激。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>catches</b> your <b>eye</b>, you suddenly notice it. 突然注意到","examples":["As she turned back, a movement across the lawn caught her eye. 當她轉身時，草地那頭的一個動靜引起了她的注意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>catch</b> someone's <b>eye</b>, you do something to attract their attention, so that you can speak to them. 吸引注意","examples":["He tried to catch Annie's eye as he walked by her seat. 從安妮座位旁走過時，他設法吸引她的注意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>close</b> your <b>eyes to</b> something bad or if you <b>shut</b> your <b>eyes to</b> it, you ignore it. 不理會某事物","examples":["Most governments must simply be shutting their eyes to the problem. 大多數政府定會乾脆不理會這個問題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>cry</b> your <b>eyes out</b>, you cry very hard. 痛哭","examples":["He didn't mean to be cruel but I cried my eyes out. 他並非有意苛刻，但我還是大哭了一場。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If there is something <b>as far as the eye can see</b>, there is a lot of it and you cannot see anything else beyond it. 視線所能及","examples":["There are pine trees as far as the eye can see. 極目望去只見松林。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has an eye for</b> something, you mean that they are good at noticing it or making judgments about it. 對…有眼力; 對…有判別力","examples":["Susan has a keen eye for detail, so each dress is beautifully finished. 蘇珊對細節有敏銳的眼力，所以每件衣服都完成得相當漂亮。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>in</b> his <b>eyes</b> or <b>to</b> her <b>eyes</b> to indicate that you are reporting someone's opinion and that other people might think differently. 在某人看來","examples":["The other serious problem in the eyes of the new government is communalism. 在新政府看來，另外一個嚴峻的問題是地方自治主義。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>eyes open</b> or <b>keep an eye out</b> <b>for</b> someone or something, you watch for them carefully. 密切注意","examples":["I ask the mounted patrol to keep their eyes open. 我要求巡邏騎警密切注意。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>keep an eye on</b> something or someone, you watch them carefully, for example to make sure that they are satisfactory or safe, or not causing trouble. 照看; 留意","examples":["I went for a run there, keeping an eye on the children the whole time. 我去那裡跑步，其間始終留意著孩子們。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you say that <b>all eyes are on</b> something or that the <b>eyes of the world are on</b> something, you mean that everyone is paying careful attention to it and what will happen. 眾目關注","examples":["All eyes will be on tomorrow's vote. 明天的投票將是眾目所注。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If someone <b>has</b> their <b>eye on</b> you, they are watching you carefully to see what you do. 密切注意某人","examples":["A spokesman for the shop said: \"He comes here quite a lot. We've had our eye on him before.\" 該商店一位發言人說：“他常常光顧這裡。我們以前就注意他了。”"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> your <b>eye on</b> something, you want to have it. 看中","examples":["If you're saving up for a new outfit you've had your eye on, cheap dinners for a month might let you buy it. 如果你想省錢買一套你看中的新套裝，吃一個月的廉價晚餐也許會讓你買得起。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you say that you did something <b>with</b> your <b>eyes open</b> or <b>with</b> your <b>eyes wide open</b>, you mean that you knew about the problems and difficulties that you were likely to have. 負責任地","examples":["We want all our members to undertake this trip responsibly, with their eyes open. 我們希望我們所有的成員都明白其中的困難、負責任地進行這次旅行。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If something <b>opens</b> your <b>eyes</b>, it makes you aware that something is different from the way that you thought it was. (開)眼界","examples":["Watching your child explore the world about her can open your eyes to delights long forgotten. 看著你的孩子探索她周圍的世界能使你看到遺忘很久的快樂。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>see eye to eye</b> <b>with</b> someone, you agree with them and have the same opinions and views. (與某人) 看法一致","examples":["Yuriko saw eye to eye with Yul on almost every aspect of the production. 百合子和尤爾幾乎在產品的每一個方面都意見一致。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"When you <b>take</b> your <b>eyes off</b> the thing you have been watching or looking at, you stop looking at it. 把目光移開","examples":["She took her eyes off the road to glance at me. 她把目光移開馬路，瞥了我一眼。"]}]}]},"family":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家，家庭；家屬，親屬；家族；子女，孩子；（動植物的）科；語族；祖先； 一窩（動物）； 有組織的犯罪團伙；（具有明顯共同特徵的）一類東西；（在某些方面）像家人一樣的一群人；（數）族；派別；氏族"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"家庭的；一家所有的；老少咸宜的；全家用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>family</b> is a group of people who are related to each other, especially parents and their children. 家人","examples":["There's room in there for a family of five. 那兒能住得下一家5口。","Does he have any family? 他有什麼家人嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people talk about a <b>family</b>, they sometimes mean children. 孩子","examples":["They decided to start a family. 他們決定了要孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people talk about their <b>family</b>, they sometimes mean their ancestors. 祖先","examples":["Her family came to Los Angeles at the turn of the century. 她的祖先在世紀之交時來到了洛杉磯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>family</b> of animals or plants is a group of related species. (動植物的) 科","examples":["...foods in the cabbage family, such as Brussels sprouts. …十字花科食物，如抱子甘藍。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>family</b> to describe things that belong to a particular family. 家庭的","examples":["He returned to the family home. 他回到了自己家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>family</b> to describe things that are designed to be used or enjoyed by both parents and children. 全家用的","examples":["It had been designed as a family house. 它已被設計成一幢適合全家人居住的房子。"]}]}]},"face":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臉，面部；面部表情，臉色；人；初看，初聽；尊嚴，威信；面貌；（物體的）正面，表面；斜坡，山坡；鐘面，錶盤；採掘面，工作面；（球拍的）拍面；（尤指足球的）球門"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"面臨，遭遇；正視，面對；與……交往，與……交談；面向，面朝；迎戰，對陣；抹蓋，覆蓋；接受，容忍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>face</b> is the front part of your head from your chin to the top of your forehead, where your mouth, eyes, nose, and other features are. 臉","examples":["He rolled down his window and stuck his face out. 他搖下窗戶，探出臉來。","He was going red in the face and breathing with difficulty. 他臉面發紅，費力地喘著氣。","She had a beautiful face. 她有張漂亮的臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your <b>face</b> is happy, sad, or serious, for example, the expression on your face shows that you are happy, sad, or serious. 面部表情","examples":["He was walking around with a sad face. 他四處走著，面帶哀傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>face</b> of a cliff, mountain, or building is a vertical surface or side of it. (懸崖、山、建築物的) 側面","examples":["Harrer was one of the first to climb the north face of the Eiger. 哈勒是第一批登上艾格爾山北坡的人之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>face</b> of a clock or watch is the surface with the numbers or hands on it, which shows the time. 鐘面; 錶盤","examples":["It was too dark to see the face of my watch. 天太黑了，以致看不見我錶盤上的時間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that <b>the face of</b> an area, institution, or field of activity is changing, you mean its appearance or nature is changing. (地方、機構或活動區域的) 外觀特徵","examples":["...the changing face of the countryside. …該鄉村變化著的面貌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you refer to something as <b>the</b> particular <b>face of</b> an activity, belief, or system, you mean that it is one particular aspect of it, in contrast to other aspects. (活動、信仰或制度的) 方面","examples":["Brothels, she insists, are the acceptable face of prostitution. 妓院，她堅持說，是賣淫可接受的方面。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you lose <b>face</b>, you do something which makes you appear weak and makes people respect or admire you less. If you do something in order to save <b>face</b>, you do it in order to avoid appearing weak and losing people's respect or admiration. 臉面","examples":["They don't want a war, but they don't want to lose face. 他們不想要戰爭，但他們也不想丟臉面。","To cancel the airport would mean a loss of face for the present governor. 取消這個機場對現任州長會意味著丟面子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>face down</b>, their face or front points downward. If they are <b>face up</b>, their face or front points upward. 面朝下/朝上","examples":["All the time Stephen was lying face down and unconscious in the bathtub. 斯蒂芬始終面朝下趴在浴缸裡，不省人事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you come <b>face to face</b> with someone, you meet them and can talk to them or look at them directly. 面對面","examples":["We were strolling into the town when we came face to face with Jacques Dubois. 我們溜達進城時，迎面碰上了雅克·杜波依斯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you come <b>face to face with</b> a difficulty or reality, you cannot avoid it and have to deal with it. 正視 (困難或現實)","examples":["Eventually, he came face to face with discrimination again. 最後，他再次直面歧視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an action or belief <b>flies in the face of</b> accepted ideas or rules, it seems to completely oppose or contradict them. 完全違背","examples":["...scientific principles that seem to fly in the face of common sense. …一些看似完全有悖常識的科學原理。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you take a particular action or attitude <b>in the face of</b> a problem or difficulty, you respond to that problem or difficulty in that way. 面對","examples":["The president has called for national unity in the face of the violent anti-government protests. 總統面對激烈的反政府抗議呼籲全國團結一致。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>make a face</b>, you show a feeling such as dislike or disgust by putting an exaggerated expression on your face, for example, by sticking out your tongue. 做鬼臉","examples":["Opening the door, she made a face at the musty smell. 開啟門，她對黴味做了個鬼臉。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You say <b>on the face of it</b> when you are describing how something seems when it is first considered, in order to suggest that people's opinion may change when they know or think more about the subject. 乍看起來","examples":["On the face of it that seems to make sense. But the figures don't add up. 乍一看，那好像講得通。但是數字對不上。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> your <b>face</b> somewhere, you go there and see people, although you are not welcome, are somewhat unwilling to go, or have not been there for some time. 露面","examples":["If she shows her face again back in Massachusetts she'll find a warrant for her arrest waiting. 如果她回馬薩諸塞州再次露面的話，她會發現一張拘捕令正等著她。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you manage to keep <b>a straight face</b>, you manage to look serious, although you want to laugh. 繃著的臉","examples":["What went through Tom's mind I can't imagine, but he did manage to keep a straight face. 湯姆心裡在想什麼我想像不出來，但是他確實裝著一臉嚴肅。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say something <b>to</b> someone's <b>face</b>, you say it openly in their presence. 當著某人的面","examples":["Her opponent called her a liar to her face. 她的對手當著她的面叫她騙子。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use the expression \"<b>let's face it</b>\" when you are stating a fact or making a comment about something which you think the person you are talking to may find unpleasant or be unwilling to admit. 面對事實吧","examples":["She was always attracted to younger men. But, let's face it, who is not? 她過去總是被比她年輕的男性吸引。不過，面對現實吧，誰不是呢？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>faces</b> a particular thing, person, or direction, they are positioned opposite them or are looking in that direction. 面向","examples":["They stood facing each other. 他們面對面站著。","Our house faces south. 我們的房子面朝南。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>face</b> someone or something, you turn so that you are looking at them. 面向","examples":["She stood up from the table and faced him. 她從桌前站起來，面向著他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have to <b>face</b> a person or group, you have to stand or sit in front of them and talk to them, although it may be difficult and unpleasant. (不得不) 面對","examples":["Christie looked relaxed and calm as he faced the press. 克里斯蒂面對媒體時顯得輕鬆而鎮靜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>face</b> or <b>are faced</b> with something difficult or unpleasant, or if it <b>faces</b> you, it is going to affect you and you have to deal with it. 面臨","examples":["Williams faces life in prison if convicted of attempted murder. 威廉斯如被判謀殺未遂罪，將面臨終身監禁。","The immense difficulties facing European businessmen in Russia were only too evident. 擺在俄羅斯的歐洲商人面前的巨大困難是極其明顯的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>face</b> the truth or <b>face</b> the facts, you accept that something is true. If you <b>face</b> someone with the truth or with the facts, you try to make them accept that something is true. 正視","examples":["Although your heart is breaking, you must face the truth that a relationship has ended. 儘管你的心碎了，但是你必須正視事實，那就是一段戀愛關係已經結束了。","He accused the Government of refusing to face facts about the economy. 他指責政府拒絕正視有關經濟的現實情況。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>cannot</b> <b>face</b> something, you do not feel able to do it because it seems so difficult or unpleasant. 對付","examples":["I couldn't face the prospect of spending a Saturday night there, so I decided to press on. 我感到無法在那裡過週六晚上，所以我決定繼續趕路。","My children want me with them for Christmas Day, but I can't face it. 我的孩子們想讓我和他們一起過聖誕節，但是我感到無法做到。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Face up to</b> means the same as <b>face</b>. 正視","examples":["I have grown up now and I have to face up to my responsibilities. 我現在已經長大了，所以必須要正視自己的責任。"]}]}]},"fat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"肥的，肥胖的；厚的，寬的；鉅額的；<非正式>極少的，沒有的；好打的，易中的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"脂肪，肥肉；食用油，烹呼叫油；多餘的部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>（使）長肥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or animal is <b>fat</b>, you mean that they have a lot of flesh on their body and that they weigh too much. You usually use the word <b>fat</b> when you think that this is a bad thing. 肥胖的","examples":["I could eat what I liked without getting fat. 我可以吃我喜歡的東西而不發胖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fat</b> object, especially a book, is very thick or wide. (尤指書) 厚的; 寬的","examples":["...\"Europe in Figures,\" a fat book published on September 22nd. …《數說歐洲》，9月22日出版的一本厚書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fat</b> profit or fee is a large one. (利潤、費用) 豐厚的","examples":["They are set to make a big fat profit. 他們決心努力大賺一筆。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fat</b> is a substance contained in foods such as meat, cheese, and butter which forms an energy store in your body. (食物中的) 脂肪","examples":["An easy way to cut the amount of fat in your diet is to avoid eating red meats. 減少你飲食中脂肪含量的一個簡易方法就是避免吃紅色肉類。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fat</b> is a solid or liquid substance obtained from animals or vegetables, which is used in cooking. 食用油","examples":["When you use oil or fat for cooking, use as little as possible. 當你用油烹飪時，要儘可能少放。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fat</b> is the extra flesh that animals and humans have under their skin, which is used to store energy and to help keep them warm. (動物或人的) 脂肪","examples":["Because you're not burning calories, everything you eat turns to fat. 因為你沒有消耗卡路里，所以你吃的每樣東西都會變成脂肪。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>fat chance</b> <b>of</b> something happening, you mean that you do not believe that it will happen. 沒門兒","examples":["\"Would your car be easy to steal?\"—\"Fat chance. I've got a device that shuts down the petrol and ignition.\" “你的車容易被偷嗎？”—“不可能。我有一個可以關閉油門和點火開關的裝置。”"]}]}]},"father":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"父親，爸爸；祖先；發明者，創始人；（Father）天父，上帝；（Father）（尤指天主教和東正教的）神父；父親般的人；（城邦、市鎮等的）元老；（動物的）父代；保護人，庇護人；（Father）（用於擬人化的專有名稱）……老人；早期基督教神學家"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"是……的父親；創立（新思想），創造，發明（新方法）；如父親般對待（或撫養、照料）；確定（某人）的生父為……，確定（某事物）的責任應由……來承擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>father</b> is your male parent. You can also call someone your <b>father</b> if he brings you up as if he were this man. 父親","examples":["His father was a painter. 他父親是一位畫家。","He would be a good father to my children. 他會成為我孩子們的好父親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The man who invented or started something is sometimes referred to as the <b>father of</b> that thing. 發明者; 創始人","examples":["...Max Dupain, regarded as the father of modern photography. …被認為是現代攝影之父的馬科斯∙杜龐。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a man <b>fathers</b> a child, he makes a woman pregnant and their child is born. 是…的父親","examples":["She claims Mark fathered her child. 她聲稱馬克是她孩子的父親。"]}]}]},"feelings":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感情，情緒；感覺，觸覺，知覺；意見，觀點，態度（常與 about 連用）；易受傷害的感情（常作 one's feelings，如 hurt one's feelings）；對某人的愛慕、好感或同情（have/develop feelings for someone）；百感交集，喜憂參半（mixed feelings）；……感（feeling 的複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>feeling</b> is an emotion, such as anger or happiness. 情緒","examples":["It gave me a feeling of satisfaction. 它給了我一種滿足感。","He was unable to contain his own destructive feelings. 他無法剋制自己的消極情緒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>feeling</b> of hunger, tiredness, or other physical sensation, you experience it. 感覺","examples":["I also had a strange feeling in my neck. 我的脖子也有一種奇怪的感覺。","Focus on the feeling of relaxation. 專注於放鬆的感覺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>a</b> <b>feeling</b> <b>that</b> something is the case or <b>that</b> something is going to happen, you think that is probably the case or that it is probably going to happen. 預感","examples":["I have a feeling that everything will be all right. 我有種預感一切都會好起來的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>feelings</b> about something are the things that you think and feel about it, or your attitude toward it. 看法; 態度","examples":["She has strong feelings about the alleged growth in violence against female officers. 她對據稱的女性軍官遭遇暴力事件的增多有強烈的看法。","I think that sums up the feelings of most discerning and intelligent Indians. 我認為那綜合了最有眼力和智慧的印第安人的觀點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you refer to someone's <b>feelings</b>, you are talking about the things that might embarrass, offend, or upset them. For example, if you hurt someone's <b>feelings</b>, you upset them by something that you say or do. 感情","examples":["He was afraid of hurting my feelings. 他害怕傷我的感情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> is a way of thinking and reacting to things which is emotional and not planned rather than logical and practical. 感情用事","examples":["He was prompted to a rare outburst of feeling. 他被激發而感情用事，這很少見。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> for someone is love, affection, sympathy, or concern for them. (愛、關切、同情等) 感情","examples":["Thomas never lost his feeling for Harriet. 托馬斯從未失去對哈麗雅特的感情。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> in part of your body is the ability to experience the sense of touch in this part of the body. 知覺","examples":["After the accident he had no feeling in his legs. 事故之後他的雙腿失去了知覺。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> is used to refer to a general opinion that a group of people has about something. (一群人的) 觀點","examples":["There is still some feeling in the art world that the market for such works may be declining. 藝術界仍存在一種看法，認為這種作品的市場前景暗淡。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you have a <b>feeling of</b> being in a particular situation, you feel that you are in that situation. (處於某種處境的) 感覺","examples":["I had the terrible feeling of being left behind to bring up the baby while he had fun. 我有種可怕的感覺，覺得自己被扔下撫養孩子，而他卻在享樂。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something such as a place or book creates a particular kind of <b>feeling</b>, it creates a particular kind of atmosphere. 氣氛","examples":["That's what we tried to portray in the book, this feeling of opulence and grandeur. 那正是我們想要在這本書裡所要營造的，那種繁榮且偉大的氣氛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bad feeling</b> or <b>ill feeling</b> is bitterness or anger which exists between people, for example, after they have had an argument. 敵意","examples":["There's been some bad feeling between the two families. 這兩個家族之間互有敵意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hard feelings</b> are feelings of anger or bitterness toward someone who you have had an argument with or who has upset you. If you say \"<b>no hard feelings</b>,\" you are making an agreement with someone not to be angry or bitter about something. 芥蒂","examples":["I don't want any hard feelings between our companies. 我不希望我們兩家公司之間有任何芥蒂。"]}]}]},"february":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"二月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>February</b> is the second month of the year in the Western calendar. ２月","examples":["He joined the Army in February 1943. 他1943年2月參軍。","His exhibition opens on February 5. 他的展覽2月5日開幕。"]}]}]},"fifteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十五"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十五；十五個（人或物）；（英式橄欖球）十五人組成的橄欖球隊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十五的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fifteen</b> is the number 15. 15","examples":["In India, there are fifteen official languages. 在印度有15種官方語言。"]}]}]},"fear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"害怕，畏懼；擔心，憂慮；敬畏"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"恐懼；擔心；（壞事發生的）可能性；敬畏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fear</b> is the unpleasant feeling you have when you think that you are in danger. 害怕","examples":["I was sitting on the floor shivering with fear because a bullet had been fired through a window. 我坐在地板上嚇得渾身發抖，因為有一顆子彈射穿窗戶打了進來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fear</b> is a thought that something unpleasant might happen or might have happened. 擔憂","examples":["These youngsters are motivated by fear of failure. 這些年輕人因擔心失敗而被激發。","Then one day his worst fears were confirmed. 後來有一天，他最大的擔心被證實了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is a <b>fear</b> <b>that</b> something unpleasant or undesirable will happen, you mean that you think it is possible or likely. (發生壞事的) 可能性","examples":["There is a fear that the freeze on bank accounts could prove a lasting deterrent to investors. 凍結銀行帳戶很可能對投資者是一個長期的威懾因素。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>fears for</b> someone or something, you are very worried because you think that they might be in danger. 擔憂","examples":["He also spoke of his fears for the future of his country's culture. 他也談及了他對祖國文化前景的擔憂。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fear</b> someone or something, you are frightened because you think that they will harm you. 害怕","examples":["It seems to me that if people fear you they respect you. 在我看來，如果人們怕你，那他們就尊重你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fear</b> something unpleasant or undesirable, you are worried that it might happen or might have happened. 擔心","examples":["She had feared she was coming down with pneumonia or bronchitis. 她擔心自己會得肺炎或支氣管炎。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fear for</b> someone or something, you are very worried because you think that they might be in danger. 擔心","examples":["Carla fears for her son. 卡拉為她的兒子擔心。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in fear of</b> doing or experiencing something unpleasant or undesirable, you are very worried that you might have to do it or experience it. 在對…的擔心中; 在對…的恐懼中","examples":["The elderly live in fear of assault and murder. 老年人生活在對襲擊和謀殺的恐懼中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you take a particular course of action <b>for fear of</b> something, you take the action in order to prevent that thing happening. 惟恐; 以免","examples":["She was afraid to say anything to them for fear of hurting their feelings. 她不敢對他們說什麼，惟恐傷害他們的感情。"]}]}]},"fifty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"五十；五十個（人或物）；（複數 fifties）五十多歲（年齡）或五十多度（溫度）；（the fifties）二十世紀五十年代；（美國口語，a fifty）五十美元紙幣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"數量為五十的；（非正式）眾多的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fifty</b> is the number 50. 50","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>fifties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 50 and 59. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>fifties</b>, you are aged between 50 and 59. If the temperature is <b>in the fifties</b>, the temperature is between 50 and 59 degrees. 五十多","examples":["I probably look as if I'm in my fifties rather than my seventies. 我可能看起來像五十多歲，而不像七十多歲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The fifties</b> is the decade between 1950 and 1959. 19世紀50年代","examples":["He began performing in the early fifties, singing and playing guitar. 他於50年代早期開始表演唱歌和吉他彈奏。"]}]}]},"fall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"降落，落下；跌倒，倒塌；（水平、數量、價格等）下跌，減少；屬於；下垂，低垂；照射（到），（陰影）落在；降臨，發生；倒臺，失勢；被打敗，淪陷；陣亡，被擊斃；打中，擊中；（嗓音或聲音）變輕，變小；進入（某狀態），開始變成（某事物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"落下，跌倒；（數量、水平、價格等的）下降，降低；秋天，秋季；失敗，垮臺 ；瀑布；（摔跤或柔道專案中的）摔倒，壓倒；（雨、雪等的）降落；墮落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>falls</b>, they move quickly downward onto or toward the ground, by accident or because of a natural force. 落下","examples":["He has again fallen from his horse. 他又一次從馬上落下來。","Bombs fell in the town. 炸彈落在了城裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or structure that is standing somewhere <b>falls</b>, they move from their upright position, so that they are then lying on the ground. 跌倒","examples":["The woman gripped the shoulders of her man to stop herself from falling. 這個女人緊緊抓住了她男人的肩膀以防自己跌倒。","He lost his balance and fell backwards. 他失去了平衡，往後跌倒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When rain or snow <b>falls</b>, it comes down from the sky. (雨或雪) 降落","examples":["Winds reached up to 100 mph in some places with an inch of rain falling within 15 minutes. 風在有些地方達到每小時100英里，伴有15分鐘內1英寸的降雨量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>fall</b> somewhere, you allow yourself to drop there in a hurried or disorganized way, often because you are very tired. 一頭倒下","examples":["Totally exhausted, he tore his clothes off and fell into bed. 他疲憊極了，胡亂地脫下衣服便一頭倒在了床上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>falls</b>, it decreases in amount, value, or strength. (總數、價值、強度或實力等) 下降","examples":["Output will fall by 6%. 產量將下降6%。","The rate of convictions has fallen. 有罪判決率已經下降。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a powerful or successful person <b>falls</b>, they suddenly lose their power or position. 垮臺","examples":["Regimes fall, revolutions come and go, but places never really change. 政權垮臺了，革命起起伏伏，但各個地方從未真正改變。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a place <b>falls</b> in a war or election, an enemy army or a different political party takes control of it. 失守","examples":["Croatian army troops retreated from northern Bosnia and the area fell to the Serbs. 克羅埃西亞軍隊從波斯尼亞北部撤退，隨後該地區失守了，落入塞爾維亞人之手。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something or someone <b>falls into</b> a particular group or category, you mean that they belong in that group or category. 屬於","examples":["The problems generally fall into two categories. 這些問題一般屬於兩種類別。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a celebration or other special event <b>falls on</b> a particular day or date, it happens to be on that day or date. 適逢 (某日)","examples":["...the oddly named Quasimodo Sunday which falls on the first Sunday after Easter. …被古怪地命名為“卸白衣主日”是復活節後的第一個星期天。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When light or shadow <b>falls</b> on something, it covers it. (光線或影子) 落在","examples":["Nancy, out of the corner of her eye, saw the shadow that suddenly fell across the doorway. 南希從眼角餘光看到那突然落在門道上的影子。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that someone's eyes <b>fell</b> <b>on</b> something, you mean they suddenly noticed it. 突然注意到","examples":["As he laid the flowers on the table, his eye fell upon a note in Grace's handwriting. 他把花放在桌上時，突然注意到一張有格雷斯筆跡的便條。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When night or darkness <b>falls</b>, night begins and it becomes dark. (夜色或黑暗) 降臨","examples":["As darkness fell outside, they sat down to eat at long tables. 當外面黑暗降臨時，他們坐在長條桌子旁吃飯。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 落下","examples":["The helmets are designed to withstand impacts equivalent to a fall from a bicycle. 頭盔設計成能承受相當於從腳踏車上摔下來的力度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 跌倒","examples":["She broke her right leg in a bad fall. 她在一次嚴重的跌倒中右腿骨折了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 降落","examples":["One night there was a heavy fall of snow. 一天晚上天降大雪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 下降","examples":["There was a sharp fall in the value of the dollar. 美元的價值有大幅下降。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 垮臺","examples":["Following the fall of the military dictator in March, the country has had a civilian government. 軍事獨裁者3月垮臺之後，該國已有了一個平民政府。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is also a noun. 失守","examples":["...the fall of Rome. …羅馬的失守。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can refer to a  as <b>the</b> <b>falls</b>. 瀑布","examples":["The falls have always been an insurmountable obstacle for salmon and sea trout. 這些瀑布始終是鮭魚和海鱒魚不可逾越的障礙。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Fall</b> is the season between summer and winter when the weather becomes cooler. 秋季","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fall down</b> means the same as . 跌倒","examples":["I hit him so hard he fell down. 我使勁地打他，他摔倒了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"倒下的","examples":["A number of roads have been blocked by fallen trees. 一些道路被倒下的樹堵住了。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>fall</b> to show that someone or something passes into another state. For example, if someone <b>falls ill</b>, they become ill, and if something <b>falls into disrepair</b>, it is then in a state of disrepair. 進入 (某種狀態)","examples":["It is almost impossible to visit Florida without falling in love with the state. 參觀佛羅里達州卻不愛上這個州，這幾乎是不可能的。","Almost without exception these women fall victim to exploitation. 幾乎毫無例外這些女人都成為了剝削的犧牲品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>fall to pieces</b> means the same as to . 同(fall apart)","examples":["At that point the radio handset fell to pieces. 就在那一刻收音機的遙控器摔碎了。"]}]}]},"feed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"飼養，餵養，為……提供食物；以……為食物，吃食；提供（意見或資訊等），灌輸；施肥；新增燃料；把……放進機器，將……塞進機器；加深，強化；使（緩慢平穩地）移動，使穿過（有限的空間）；<非正式>維持，滿足（習慣）；傳球；流入，進入"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"哺乳，餵養；動物的飼料，植物的肥料；（機器的）進料裝置；（機器、裝置的）原料供給；（衛星或網路）轉播，（訊號）傳輸；（計算機）訂閱源；（給舞臺演員的）提詞，提白；<非正式>豐盛的一餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feed</b> a person or animal, you give them food to eat and sometimes actually put it in their mouths. 餵養","examples":["We brought along pieces of old bread and fed the birds. 我們帶了幾片陳麵包來喂鳥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>feed</b> a family or a community means to supply food for them. 為…提供食物","examples":["Feeding a hungry family can be expensive. 為一家子飢餓的人張羅食物要花不少錢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a baby <b>feeds</b>, or when you <b>feed</b> it, it drinks breast milk or milk from a bottle. 給 (嬰兒) 餵奶; (嬰兒) 吃奶","examples":["When a baby is thirsty, it feeds more often. 嬰兒口渴時，吃奶更頻繁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>feed</b> something to a place, means to supply it to that place in a steady flow. 供給","examples":["...blood vessels that feed blood to the brain. …給大腦供血的血管。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>feed</b> something <b>into</b> a container or piece of equipment, you put it into it. 把…放入 (容器或裝置中)","examples":["He took the compact disc from her, then fed it into the player. 他從她那兒拿過光碟，然後把它放進播放機裡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>feed</b> a plant, you add substances to it to make it grow well. 給 (植物) 施肥","examples":["Feed plants to encourage steady growth. 給植物施肥以促進其不斷生長。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"To <b>feed</b> information <b>into</b> a computer means to gradually put it into it. 將 (訊息) 輸入","examples":["An automatic weather station feeds information on wind direction to the computer. 一個自動化氣象站把風向資訊輸入電腦。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"餵食","examples":["The feeding of dairy cows has undergone a revolution. 奶牛的餵食已經歷了一場革命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Animal <b>feed</b> is food given to animals, especially farm animals. 飼料","examples":["The grain just rotted and all they could use it for was animal feed. 這些穀物都腐爛了，他們只能將它用作動物飼料。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an animal <b>feeds</b>, it eats or drinks something. (動物) 進食","examples":["After a few days the caterpillars stopped feeding. 幾天後毛蟲停止了進食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>feeds</b> <b>on</b> another, it becomes stronger as a result of the other thing's existence. 因...而強壯","examples":["The drinking and the guilt fed on each other. 喝酒和犯罪互相滋長。"]}]}]},"feel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"感受到，體會到；覺得，相信；使人感覺……；察覺到，意識到；觸控；受到；摸索；有知覺，能感知……"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"感覺，氣氛；觸覺，手感；觸控；感知，理解；熟練使用；特性，特質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> a particular emotion or physical sensation, you experience it. 感覺","examples":["I am feeling very depressed. 我感到很沮喪。","Suddenly I felt a sharp pain in my shoulder. 我突然感到肩部一陣劇痛。","I felt as if all my strength had gone. 我覺得好象自己的力氣已經全沒了。","I felt like I was being kicked in the teeth every day. 我感覺我好像每天都在經受挫折。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about how an experience or event <b>feels</b>, you talk about the emotions and sensations connected with it. 使人感覺","examples":["It feels good to have finished a piece of work. 完成一項工作讓人感覺很好。","The speed at which everything moved felt strange. 一切進展的速度讓人感覺怪異。","Within five minutes of arriving back from holiday, it feels as if I've never been away. 度假回來還沒過5分鐘，就感覺好像我從未離開過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about how an object <b>feels</b>, you talk about the physical quality that you notice when you touch or hold it. For example, if something <b>feels</b> soft, you notice that it is soft when you touch it. 摸上去…; 拿起來…","examples":["The metal felt smooth and cold. 這種金屬摸上去光滑而冰冷。","The ten-foot oars felt heavy and awkward. 這些10英尺長的船槳拿起來又重又不方便。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you talk about how the weather <b>feels</b>, you describe the weather, especially the temperature or whether or not you think it is going to rain or snow. (天氣，尤指氣溫) 感覺起來","examples":["It felt wintry cold that day. 那天感覺像冬天一樣寒冷。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Feel</b> is also a noun. 手感","examples":["He remembered the feel of her skin. 他記得她的皮膚摸上去的那種感覺。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> an object, you touch it deliberately with your hand, so that you learn what it is like, for example, what shape it is or whether it is rough or smooth. 觸控","examples":["The doctor felt his head. 醫生摸了摸他的頭。","Feel how soft the skin is in the small of the back. 摸一摸腰背部的皮膚有多麼柔軟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>feel</b> something, you are aware of it because it is touching you. (由於碰觸) 感覺到","examples":["Through several layers of clothes I could feel his muscles. 透過好幾層衣服，我可以感覺到他的肌肉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> something happening, you become aware of it because of the effect it has on your body. (身體) 感覺到","examples":["She felt something being pressed into her hands. 她感覺到有什麼東西正塞進她的雙手。","He felt something move beside him. 他感覺到身邊有東西在移動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> <b>yourself</b> doing something or being in a particular state, you are aware that something is happening to you which you are unable to control. 感覺到 (不禁做某事)","examples":["I felt myself blush. 我感到自己臉紅了。","If at any point you feel yourself becoming tense, make a conscious effort to relax. 如果什麼時候你感到自己變得緊張了，就有意識地努力去放鬆。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> the presence of someone or something, you become aware of them, even though you cannot see or hear them. 感覺到 (某人或某物的存在)","examples":["He felt her eyes on him. 他感覺到她的眼睛正盯著他。","I could feel that a man was watching me very intensely. 我能感覺到一個男人正緊盯著我看。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> that something is the case, you have a strong idea in your mind that it is the case. 覺得","examples":["I feel that not enough is being done to protect the local animal life. 我覺得在保護當地動物方面做得還不夠。","I feel certain that it will all turn out well. 我覺得最後肯定一切都會很好"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> that you should do something, you think that you should do it. 認為","examples":["I feel I should resign. 我認為我應該辭職。","You need not feel obliged to contribute. 你不必認為你非得捐款。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you talk about how you <b>feel</b> <b>about</b> something, you talk about your opinion, attitude, or reaction to it. 對…表示看法","examples":["We'd like to know what you feel about abortion. 我們想知道你對墮胎有什麼看法。","She feels guilty about spending less time lately with her two kids. 她為最近和自己的兩個孩子在一起的時間少了而感到內疚。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feel like</b> doing something or having something, you want to do it or have it because you are in the right mood for it and think you would enjoy it. 想要","examples":["Neither of them felt like going back to sleep. 他們倆都不想回去睡覺。"]}]}]},"final":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最終的，結束的；(出現次序)最後的，末尾的；決定性的，不可變更的；無比的，極度的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"決賽；期末考試，課程終結考試；主調音；當日報紙的末版；（飛機進入著陸跑道的）最終邊，第五邊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a series of events, things, or people, the <b>final</b> one is the last one. 最後的","examples":["Astronauts will make a final attempt today to rescue a communications satellite from its useless orbit. 宇航員們今天將做最後一次嘗試，把一顆通訊衛星從它無用的軌道上拯救出來。","This is the fifth and probably final day of testimony before the Senate Judiciary Committee. 這是第5天，也可能是最後一天在參議院司法委員會面前作證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Final</b> means happening at the end of an event or series of events. 最終的","examples":["You must have been on stage until the final curtain. 你肯定是在臺上一直呆到終場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a decision or someone's authority is <b>final</b>, it cannot be changed or questioned. 不可更改的","examples":["The judges' decision is final. 該法官的判決是不可更改的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>final</b> is the last game or contest in a series and decides who is the winner. 決賽","examples":["...the Gold Cup final. …金盃決賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>finals</b> of a sports tournament consist of a smaller tournament that includes only players or teams that have won earlier games. The finals decide the winner of the whole tournament. (錦標賽的) 決賽階段的比賽","examples":["Poland knows it has a chance of qualifying for the World Cup Finals. 波蘭隊知道自己有機會獲得參加世界盃決賽階段比賽的資格。"]}]}]},"feeling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感覺，感觸；預感；看法，態度；情感，情緒；理解力，領悟力；好感，同情；知覺；氛圍；品質，特點"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多愁善感的，多情的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"感受到，體會到；覺得，相信；使人感覺……(feel 的現在分詞形式)"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>feeling</b> is an emotion, such as anger or happiness. 情緒","examples":["It gave me a feeling of satisfaction. 它給了我一種滿足感。","He was unable to contain his own destructive feelings. 他無法剋制自己的消極情緒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>feeling</b> of hunger, tiredness, or other physical sensation, you experience it. 感覺","examples":["I also had a strange feeling in my neck. 我的脖子也有一種奇怪的感覺。","Focus on the feeling of relaxation. 專注於放鬆的感覺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>a</b> <b>feeling</b> <b>that</b> something is the case or <b>that</b> something is going to happen, you think that is probably the case or that it is probably going to happen. 預感","examples":["I have a feeling that everything will be all right. 我有種預感一切都會好起來的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>feelings</b> about something are the things that you think and feel about it, or your attitude toward it. 看法; 態度","examples":["She has strong feelings about the alleged growth in violence against female officers. 她對據稱的女性軍官遭遇暴力事件的增多有強烈的看法。","I think that sums up the feelings of most discerning and intelligent Indians. 我認為那綜合了最有眼力和智慧的印第安人的觀點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you refer to someone's <b>feelings</b>, you are talking about the things that might embarrass, offend, or upset them. For example, if you hurt someone's <b>feelings</b>, you upset them by something that you say or do. 感情","examples":["He was afraid of hurting my feelings. 他害怕傷我的感情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> is a way of thinking and reacting to things which is emotional and not planned rather than logical and practical. 感情用事","examples":["He was prompted to a rare outburst of feeling. 他被激發而感情用事，這很少見。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> for someone is love, affection, sympathy, or concern for them. (愛、關切、同情等) 感情","examples":["Thomas never lost his feeling for Harriet. 托馬斯從未失去對哈麗雅特的感情。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> in part of your body is the ability to experience the sense of touch in this part of the body. 知覺","examples":["After the accident he had no feeling in his legs. 事故之後他的雙腿失去了知覺。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Feeling</b> is used to refer to a general opinion that a group of people has about something. (一群人的) 觀點","examples":["There is still some feeling in the art world that the market for such works may be declining. 藝術界仍存在一種看法，認為這種作品的市場前景暗淡。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you have a <b>feeling of</b> being in a particular situation, you feel that you are in that situation. (處於某種處境的) 感覺","examples":["I had the terrible feeling of being left behind to bring up the baby while he had fun. 我有種可怕的感覺，覺得自己被扔下撫養孩子，而他卻在享樂。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something such as a place or book creates a particular kind of <b>feeling</b>, it creates a particular kind of atmosphere. 氣氛","examples":["That's what we tried to portray in the book, this feeling of opulence and grandeur. 那正是我們想要在這本書裡所要營造的，那種繁榮且偉大的氣氛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bad feeling</b> or <b>ill feeling</b> is bitterness or anger which exists between people, for example, after they have had an argument. 敵意","examples":["There's been some bad feeling between the two families. 這兩個家族之間互有敵意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hard feelings</b> are feelings of anger or bitterness toward someone who you have had an argument with or who has upset you. If you say \"<b>no hard feelings</b>,\" you are making an agreement with someone not to be angry or bitter about something. 芥蒂","examples":["I don't want any hard feelings between our companies. 我不希望我們兩家公司之間有任何芥蒂。"]}]}]},"finger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手指；（手套的）手指部分；（酒在杯中的深度）一指寬；指狀物；豎中指；指標"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用手指觸控；<美>告發，告密；撥弄（樂器）；用某種指法演奏（樂曲）；給（樂譜）標明指法符號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>fingers</b> are the long thin parts at the end of each hand, sometimes also including the thumb. 手指","examples":["She suddenly held up a small, bony finger and pointed across the room. 她突然舉起一根瘦小的手指指向房間的另一頭。","She ran her fingers through her hair. 她用手指捋了捋頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>fingers</b> of a glove are the parts that a person's fingers fit into. (手套的) 指套","examples":["He bit the fingers of his right glove and pulled it off. 他咬住右手手套的指套，把它扯了下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>finger of</b> something such as smoke or land is an amount of it that is shaped rather like a finger. 指狀物","examples":["...a thin finger of land that separates Pakistan from the former Soviet Union. …一片分隔巴基斯坦和前蘇聯的狹長地帶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>finger</b> something, you touch or feel it with your fingers. 用手指觸控","examples":["He fingered the few coins in his pocket. 他用手指摸了摸他兜裡的幾枚硬幣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cross</b> your <b>fingers</b>, you put one finger on top of another and hope for good luck. If you say that someone <b>is keeping their fingers crossed</b>, you mean they are hoping for good luck. (交叉手指以) 祈求好運","examples":["He crossed his fingers, asking for luck for the first time in his life. 他把手指交叉起來，平生第一次祈求好運。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone did not <b>lay a finger on</b> a particular person or thing, you are emphasizing that they did not touch or harm them at all. 動…一個指頭","examples":["I must make it clear I never laid a finger on her. 我必須說清楚，我從未動過她一個指頭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a person does not <b>lift a finger</b> or <b>raise a finger</b> to do something, especially to help someone, you are critical of them because they do nothing. 盡舉手之勞","examples":["She never lifted a finger around the house. 她在家裡從來沒有幫過忙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>point the finger at</b> someone or <b>point an accusing finger at</b> someone, you blame them or accuse them of doing wrong. 指責","examples":["He said he wasn't pointing an accusing finger at anyone in the government or the army. 他說他並不是在指責政府或軍隊裡的任何人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> your <b>finger on</b> something, for example, a reason or problem, you see and identify exactly what it is. 確切地指出","examples":["Midge couldn't quite put her finger on the reason. 米吉不能非常確切地指出原因所在。"]}]}]},"fill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）充滿，佔滿；堵塞，填補；滿足；（聲音、氣味或光）遍及，瀰漫；擔任，充任；（感情）充盈於；打發，佔據（時間）；（帆）迎風（或受風）鼓起（或張開）；使吃飽，填飽……的肚子；(按訂單)供貨，(按藥方)配藥；（用吊牌的方法）湊成，做成（一手好牌）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"總量，（某人的）需求總量；填充物，填方，填土；（容器的）最大容量；（某種樂器上的）插入短句，插入樂句"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fill</b> a container or area, or if it <b>fills</b>, an amount of something enters it that is enough to make it full. 裝滿","examples":["She went to the bathroom, filled a glass with water, returned to the bed. 她去了盥洗室，灌滿了一杯水，回到床前。","The boy's eyes filled with tears. 那男孩的眼裡充滿了淚水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>fills</b> a space, it is so big, or there are such large quantities of it, that there is very little room left. 佔滿","examples":["He cast his eyes at the rows of cabinets that filled the enormous work area. 他把目光投向了一排排佔滿了龐大工作區的櫃子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fill</b> a crack or hole, you put a substance into it in order to make the surface smooth again. 填平","examples":["Fill small holes with wood filler in a matching colour. 用顏色相配的木質填充料填平小洞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a sound, smell, or light <b>fills</b> a space, or the air, it is very strong or noticeable. 充滿","examples":["In the parking lot of the school, the siren filled the air. 學校的停車場上，警報響徹天空。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>fills</b> you <b>with</b> an emotion, or if an emotion <b>fills</b> you, you experience this emotion strongly. 使充滿 (感情)","examples":["I admired my father, and his work filled me with awe and curiosity. 我崇拜我的父親，他的工作使我充滿了敬畏和好奇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>fill</b> a period of time with a particular activity, you spend the time in this way. 打發","examples":["If she wants a routine to fill her day, let her do community work. 如果她想用例行事物來打發日子，就讓她做社群工作吧。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>fills</b> a need or a gap, it puts an end to this need or gap by existing or being active. 滿足; 填補","examples":["She brought him a sense of fun, of gaiety that filled a gap in his life. 她帶給他一種快樂、歡愉的感覺，填補了他生命中的空白。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>fills</b> a role, position, or function, they have that role or position, or perform that function, often successfully. 擔任","examples":["Dena was filling the role of diplomat's wife with the skill she had learned over the years. 德娜憑藉多年來學到的技巧擔任著外交家妻子的角色。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a company or organization <b>fills</b> a job vacancy, they choose someone to do the job. If someone <b>fills</b> a job vacancy, they accept a job that they have been offered. 選人接任; 接任","examples":["A vacancy has arisen which I intend to fill. 我想接任的職位已經空出來了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When a dentist <b>fills</b> someone's tooth, he or she puts a filling in it. 補","examples":["Dentists fill teeth and repair broken ones. 牙醫補牙並修理壞牙。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>fill</b> an order or a prescription, you provide the things that are asked for. 供應 (訂貨或處方上的藥)","examples":["A pharmacist can fill any prescription if, in his or her judgment, the prescription is valid. 一名藥劑師可以供應任何處方上的藥，如果他或她認為藥方有效的話。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fill up</b> means the same as . 裝滿","examples":["Warehouses at the frontier between the two countries fill up with sacks of rice and flour. 兩國交界處的倉庫裡裝滿了一袋袋大米和麵粉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fill up</b> means the same as . 佔滿 (同)(fill)","examples":["...the complicated machines that fill up today's laboratories. …佔滿了現今實驗室的複雜機器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fill in</b> means the same as . 填平 (同)(fill)","examples":["Start by filling in any cracks and gaps between window and door frames and the wall. 先把門窗框架和牆壁之間的所有裂縫和空隙填平。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Fill up</b> means the same as . 打發 (同)(fill)","examples":["On Thursday night she went to her yoga class, glad to have something to fill up the evening. 星期四晚上她去上了瑜珈課，很高興有事可做來打發晚上的時間。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"佔滿的","examples":["...four museum buildings filled with historical objects. …滿是歷史文物的4幢博物館大樓。"]}]}]},"fight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"與……作鬥爭，堅決反對；努力爭取，為……而鬥爭；打仗，作戰；打架；爭吵，爭論；參加拳擊賽；打官司，進行（訴訟，辯護等）；努力抑制（情感）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬥爭；打鬥，打架；爭吵，爭論；拳擊比賽；戰鬥；鬥志"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> something unpleasant, you try in a determined way to prevent it or stop it from happening. 與…作鬥爭","examples":["More units to fight forest fires are planned. 已經計劃增派部隊來撲滅森林大火。","I've spent a lifetime fighting against racism and prejudice. 我花了畢生的時間與種族歧視和偏見作鬥爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or army <b>fights</b> in a battle or a war, they take part in it. 參戰","examples":["He fought in the war and was taken prisoner by the Americans. 他參加了戰爭，後來被美軍俘虜。","If I were a young man I would sooner go to prison than fight for this country. 如果我還是個年輕人，我寧可坐牢也不願為這個國家去打仗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> your way to a place, you move toward it with great difficulty, for example, because there are a lot of people or obstacles in your way. 擠","examples":["I fought my way into a carriage just before the doors closed. 我正好在車門關閉之前擠進了一節車廂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>fight</b> means to take part in a boxing match. 參加拳擊賽","examples":["In a few hours' time one of the world's most famous boxers will be fighting here for the first time. 再過幾個小時，世界最著名的拳擊手之一將首次在這裡參加比賽。","I'd like to fight him because he's undefeated and I want to be the first man to beat him. 我想跟他比賽拳擊，因為他從未被打敗過，而我想成為第一個戰勝他的人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> an election, you are a candidate in the election and try to win it. 參加 (競選)","examples":["He helped raise almost $40 million to fight the election campaign. 他幫忙募集了將近四千萬美元來參加競選活動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> a case or a court action, you make a legal case against someone in a very determined way, or you put forward a defence when a legal case is made against you. 打 (官司)","examples":["Watkins sued the Army and fought his case in various courts for 10 years. 沃特金斯起訴了軍隊並用10年在不同的法庭打他的官司。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> an emotion or desire, you try very hard not to feel it, show it, or act on it, but do not always succeed. 剋制","examples":["I desperately fought the urge to giggle. 我拼命地忍著不笑。","He fought with the urge to smoke one of the cigars he'd given up a while ago. 他剋制自己的煙癮，不去想剛才沒吸的那支雪茄。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fight</b> is also a noun. 鬥爭","examples":["...the fight against drug addiction. …與毒品上癮的鬥爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fight</b> is also a noun. 奮鬥","examples":["I too am committing myself to continue the fight for justice. 我也正致力於繼續正義之戰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"戰鬥","examples":["More than nine hundred people have died in the fighting. 九百多人在這場戰鬥中死去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Fight</b> is also a noun. 打架","examples":["He had a fight with Smith and bloodied his nose. 他跟史密斯打了一架，把他的鼻子打出了血。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Fight</b> is also a noun. 吵架","examples":["We think maybe he took off because he had a big fight with his dad the night before. 我們認為或許他離開是因為他和他父親在前天晚上大吵了一架。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>fight</b> is a boxing match. 拳擊賽","examples":["The referee stopped the fight. 裁判叫停了那場拳擊賽。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>fight</b> to refer to a contest such as an election or a sports competition. 角逐","examples":["...the fight for power between the two parties. …兩黨之間權力的角逐。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Fight</b> is the desire or ability to keep fighting. 鬥志","examples":["I thought that we had a lot of fight in us. 我認為我們鬥志昂揚。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fight</b> for something, you try in a determined way to get it or achieve it. 奮鬥","examples":["Lee had to fight hard for his place on the expedition. 李必須為他在考察隊的一席之地而努力奮鬥。","I told him how we had fought to hold on to the company. 我告訴他我們是如何為保住公司而奮鬥的。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an army or group <b>fights</b> a battle with another army or group, they oppose each other with weapons. You can also say that two armies or groups <b>fight</b> a battle. 打 (仗)","examples":["Police fought a gun battle with a gang which used hand grenades against them. 警察與使用手榴彈的一個團伙進行了槍戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person <b>fights</b> with another, or <b>fights</b> them, the two people hit or kick each other because they want to hurt each other. You can also say that two people <b>fight</b>. 打架","examples":["As a child she fought with her younger sister. 小時候她跟她的妹妹打過架。","I did fight him, I punched him but it was like hitting a wall. 我確實打了他，我用拳頭打他，卻像打在一面牆上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one person <b>fights</b> with another, or <b>fights</b> them, they have an angry disagreement or quarrel. You can also say that two people <b>fight</b>. 吵架","examples":["She was always arguing with him and fighting with him. 她總是跟他爭論和吵架。","Gwendolen started fighting her teachers. 格溫德琳開始和她的老師們爭吵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>is fighting for</b> their <b>life</b> is making a great effort to stay alive, either when they are being physically attacked or when they are very ill. 與死神作鬥爭","examples":["He is still fighting for his life in the hospital. 他還在醫院裡與死神作鬥爭。"]}]}]},"fine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人滿意的，可以接受的；值得崇敬的；健康的，身體好的；優質的，出色的，美好的；晴朗的；纖細的，細小的；精美的，精巧的；細微的，細密的；<非正式>糟糕的；矯飾的，華而不實的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很，很好；精緻地，精美地；細小地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"罰款，處以罰金；使變純，使澄清；使變細，使變瘦；<非正式>放晴"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"罰金，罰款；微小顆粒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>fine</b> to describe something that you admire and think is very good. 美好的","examples":["There is a fine view of the countryside. 有一幅美麗的鄉村景色。","This is a fine book. 這是一本好書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>fine</b>, you mean that you are in good health or reasonably happy. 健康的; 開心的","examples":["Lina is fine and sends you her love and best wishes. 莉娜很好，她向你問候並祝福你。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>fine</b>, you mean that it is satisfactory or acceptable. 令人滿意的","examples":["The skiing is fine. 滑雪挺好的。","Everything was going to be just fine. 一切都會好起來的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>fine</b> is very delicate, narrow, or small. 精緻的; 纖細的","examples":["The heat scorched the fine hairs on her arms. 炙熱烤焦了她胳膊上的細毛。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Fine</b> objects or clothing are of good quality, delicate, and expensive. 精緻的; 華貴的","examples":["We waited in our fine clothes. 我們身著華麗的服裝等待。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>fine</b> detail or distinction is very delicate, small, or exact. 精確的; 細微的","examples":["Johnson likes the broad outline but is reserving judgment on the fine detail. 約翰遜喜歡這個大框架，但對小細節則保留看法。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>fine</b> person is someone you consider good, moral, and worth admiring. 品德高尚的; 值得欽佩的","examples":["He was an excellent journalist and a very fine man. 他是名優秀的記者，也是個品德很高尚的人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When the weather is <b>fine</b>, the sun is shining and it is not raining. 晴朗的","examples":["He might be doing some gardening if the weather is fine. 如果天氣晴朗，他也許會幹點兒園藝活。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"美好地","examples":["They are finely engineered boats. 它們是設計精美的船隻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fine</b> is also an adverb. 令人滿意地","examples":["All the instruments are working fine. 所有的儀器都運轉良好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"精緻地; 纖細地","examples":["Chop the ingredients finely and mix them together. 把這些原料剁得很細然後和在一起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"精確地; 細微地","examples":["They had to take the finely balanced decision to let the visit proceed. 他們不得不做出仔細權衡後的決定，讓訪問繼續下去。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>fine</b>\" or \"<b>that's fine</b>\" to show that you do not object to an arrangement, action, or situation that has been suggested. 好的 (表示同意)","examples":["If competition is the best way to achieve it, then, fine. 如果競爭是實現它的最佳方式，那麼，好吧。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make or become finer; refine 使更好; 提煉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fine</b> is a punishment in which a person is ordered to pay a sum of money because they have done something illegal or broken a rule. 罰款","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the point at which a piece is to end, usually after a <b>da capo</b> or <b>dal segno</b> 結束; 通常發生於從頭再奏或從有記號的地方開始重複之後","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"brandy of ordinary quality 品質一般的白蘭地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is fined</b>, they are punished by being ordered to pay a sum of money because they have done something illegal or broken a rule. 罰款","examples":["She was fined $300 and banned from driving for one month. 她被罰款$300，並被禁止駕車1個月。"]}]}]},"find":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"找到，找回；發現，發覺；（經過研究）找出，查明；感到，認為；生長在某處，存在於某地；設法獲得；開始有……；裁決，判決；自然到達，達到；鼓起（勇氣），振作（精神）；（獵人，獵犬）發現獵物（尤指發現狐狸）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"被發現的人，發現物（尤指有價值的人或物）；發現狐狸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> someone or something, you see them or learn where they are. 發現; 找到","examples":["The police also found a pistol. 警察還發現了一把手槍。","They have spent ages looking at the map and can't find a trace of anywhere called Darrowby. 他們已花了很長時間察看地圖，卻怎麼也找不到一個叫“達羅比”的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> something that you need or want, you succeed in achieving or obtaining it. 得到","examples":["Many people here cannot find work. 這裡很多人找不到工作。","He has to apply for a permit and we have to find him a job. 他得申請一個許可證，而我們得給他找一份工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> someone or something in a particular situation, they are in that situation when you see them or come into contact with them. 發現 (某人或某物處於某種狀態)","examples":["They found her walking alone and depressed on the beach. 他們發現她獨自一人、神情沮喪地走在海灘上。","She returned to her home to find her back door forced open. 她回到家中，發現後門被強行開啟了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> <b>yourself</b> doing something, you are doing it without deciding or intending to do it. 意識到 (自己無意中的動作)","examples":["It's not the first time that you've found yourself in this situation. 這已經不是你第一次意識到自己處於這種情形了。","I found myself having more fun than I had had in years. 我發現自己多年來從未玩得這樣開心過。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> that something is the case, you become aware of it or realize that it is the case. 發覺","examples":["The two biologists found, to their surprise, that both groups of birds survived equally well. 這兩位生物學家驚奇地發覺，兩組鳥都同樣很好地活了下來。","At my age I would find it hard to get another job. 在我這個年紀，我覺得很難再找到另一份工作。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When a court or jury decides that a person on trial is guilty or innocent, you say that the person <b>has been found</b> guilty or not guilty. 判決","examples":["She was found guilty of manslaughter and put on probation for two years. 她被判過失殺人罪，緩刑兩年。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>find</b> to express your reaction to someone or something. 覺得","examples":["I find most of the young men of my own age so boring. 我覺得大多數和我同齡的年輕人都很無趣。","I find it ludicrous that nothing has been done to protect passengers from fire. 我認為沒有采取任何措施來保護乘客免受火患是荒唐的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> a feeling such as pleasure or comfort <b>in</b> a particular thing or activity, you experience the feeling mentioned as a result of this thing or activity. 體會到","examples":["How could anyone find pleasure in hunting and killing this beautiful creature? 怎麼會有人在獵殺這種美麗的動物中體會到快樂呢？"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> the time or money <b>to</b> do something, you succeed in making or obtaining enough time or money to do it. 找得出 (時間、金錢)","examples":["I was just finding more time to write music. 我剛好抽得出更多的時間來作曲。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something <b>is found</b> in a particular place or thing, it exists in that place. 發現 (某物的存在)","examples":["Two thousand of France's 4,200 species of flowering plants are found in the park. 法國的4200種開花植物中有2000種可以在這個公園裡找到。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something that has been discovered as a <b>find</b>, you mean that they are valuable, interesting, good, or useful. (有價值的) 發現","examples":["Another of his lucky finds was a pair of candleholders. 他另一個幸運的發現是一對燭臺。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>find</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you successfully get there by choosing the right way to go. 找到 (去某地的路)","examples":["He was an expert at finding his way, even in strange surroundings. 他是個找路的高手，即使在陌生的環境中也一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>finds</b> its <b>way</b> somewhere, it comes to that place, especially by chance. (尤指偶然地) 來到","examples":["It is one of the very few Michelangelos that have found their way out of Italy. 它是流傳到義大利境外的少數幾幅米開朗基羅的作品之一。"]}]}]},"finish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"完成，做好；（使）結束；消耗盡（所剩之物）；（比賽中）獲得（名次）；（英式足球用語）進球；對（物件）做最後加工；殺死，殲滅；使精疲力竭；<舊>為（少女）進入上流社會做好準備；<非正式>使精疲力竭"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"結尾，結局；（賽跑、比賽的）終點；最後精細加工；飾面，飾面材料；（葡萄酒或啤酒的）餘味"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>finish</b> doing or dealing with something, you do or deal with the last part of it, so that there is no more for you to do or deal with. 結束","examples":["As soon as he'd finished eating, he excused himself. 他一吃完就藉口離開了。","Mr. Gould was given a standing ovation and loud cheers when he finished his speech. 古爾德先生結束他的演講時觀眾起立為他鼓掌並大聲歡呼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>finish</b> something that you are making or producing, you reach the end of making or producing it, so that it is complete. 完成","examples":["The consultants had been working to finish a report this week. 顧問們一直在爭取於本週完成一份報告。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as a course, show, or sale <b>finishes</b>, especially at a planned time, it ends. (尤指按計劃) 結束","examples":["The teaching day finishes at around 4 p.m. 教學日在下午4點左右結束。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that someone or something <b>finishes</b> a period of time or an event in a particular way to indicate what the final situation was like. You can also say that a period of time or an event <b>finishes</b> in a particular way. (以某種方式) 結束","examples":["The two of them finished by kissing each other goodbye. 他們兩人以互相吻別結束。","The evening finished with the welcoming of three new members. 這個晚會以歡迎3位新成員結束。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Finish up</b> means the same as . 結束","examples":["We waited a few minutes outside his office while he finished up his meeting. 我們在他辦公室外面等了幾分鐘，這時他結束了他的會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Finish off</b> and <b>finish up</b> mean the same as . 完成","examples":["Now she is busy finishing off a biography of Queen Caroline. 現在她正忙於完成卡羅琳女王的傳記。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>finishes</b> second, for example, in a race or competition, they are in second place at the end of the race or competition. 最後得到 (比賽名次)","examples":["He finished second in the championship four years in a row. 他連續4年獲得錦標賽亞軍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>finish</b> means to reach the end of saying something. 說完","examples":["Her eyes flashed, but he held up a hand. \"Let me finish.\" 她的眼睛一閃，但是他舉起一隻手說：“讓我說完。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The finish</b> of something is the end of it or the last part of it. 結尾; 最後部分","examples":["I intend to continue it and see the job through to the finish. 我打算繼續做下去，幫助把這項工作做到最後。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>finish</b> of a race is the end of it. (比賽的) 最後階段","examples":["Win a trip to see the finish of the Tour de France! 贏取一次去看環法腳踏車賽最後階段比賽的旅行吧！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the surface of something that has been made has a particular kind of <b>finish</b>, it has the appearance or texture mentioned. (物體表面的) 拋光; 修飾","examples":["The finish and workmanship of the woodwork were excellent. 這件木製品的拋光和做工都是極好的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you add <b>the finishing touches</b> to something, you add or do the last things that are necessary to complete it. (完成某事前所必需的) 最後修飾","examples":["Right up until the last minute, workers were still putting the finishing touches on the pavilions. 直到最後一刻，工人們還在給那些亭子作最後的修飾。"]}]}]},"five":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"五，五個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"五，五個；（口語）五點鐘；五美元鈔票；（籃球）五人球隊；（人名）Five（挪威姓氏菲弗）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"五的，五個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Five</b> is the number 5. 5","examples":["I spent five years there and had a really good time. 我在那裡呆了5年，過得很愉快。"]}]}]},"fish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魚；魚肉；雙魚座；接合板；<非正式>魚雷；<非正式>（在某方面怪異的）怪人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"釣魚，捕魚；搜尋；在……中捕魚；打聽訊息；用接合板修補"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fish</b> is a creature that lives in water and has a tail and fins. There are many different kinds of fish. 魚","examples":["An expert angler was casting his line and catching a fish every time. 一名垂釣高手每次丟擲魚線都能釣到一條魚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fish</b> is the flesh of a fish eaten as food. 魚肉","examples":["Does dry white wine go best with fish? 乾白葡萄酒和魚肉是最佳搭配嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fish</b>, you try to catch fish, either for food or as a form of sport or recreation. 釣魚","examples":["Brian remembers learning to fish in the Colorado River. 布萊恩記得在科羅拉多河學過釣魚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>fishing</b> <b>for</b> information or praise, you disapprove of the fact that they are trying to get it from someone in an indirect way. 拐彎抹角地獲取","examples":["He didn't want to create the impression that he was fishing for information. 他不想給人留下拐彎抹角打探訊息的印象。"]}]}]},"fire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"失火，火災；火焰；爐火，灶火；<英>取暖器；射擊，火力；怒火，激情；嚴厲批評，猛烈批判"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"射擊，開火；射（箭）；扔，拋；點火，啟動；連珠炮似的提出（問題）；解僱，開除；激發；燒製（陶器）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fire</b> is the hot, bright flames produced by things that are burning. 火","examples":["They saw a big flash and a huge ball of fire reaching hundreds of feet into the sky. 他們看到一道強光和一個巨大的火球直衝天空達幾百英尺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fire</b> or a <b>fire</b> is an occurrence of uncontrolled burning which destroys buildings, forests, or other things. 火災","examples":["87 people died in a fire at the Happy Land Social Club. 87人死於樂土社交俱樂部的火災中。","A forest fire is sweeping across portions of north Maine this evening. 今天傍晚一場森林大火正席捲著緬因州北部的部分地區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fire</b> is a burning pile of wood, coal, or other fuel that you make, for example, to use for heat, light, or cooking. 爐火","examples":["There was a fire in the grate. 壁爐裡燒著火。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>fire</b> is a device that uses electricity or gas to give out heat and warm a room. 電爐; 煤氣爐","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"射擊","examples":["The firing continued even while the protestors were fleeing. 即使在抗議者逃離時，槍擊仍在繼續。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>fire</b> to refer to the shots fired from a gun or guns. 槍擊; 炮火","examples":["His car was raked with fire from automatic weapons. 他的汽車遭到了自動武器炮火的掃射。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"解僱","examples":["There was yet another round of firings. 還有另一輪的解僱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a pot or clay object <b>is fired</b>, it is heated at a high temperature in a special oven, as part of the process of making it. 燒製","examples":["After the pot is dipped in this mixture, it is fired. 這個壺在混合料裡浸過之後，就進行燒製。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fire</b> someone <b>with</b> enthusiasm, you make them feel very enthusiastic. If you <b>fire</b> someone's imagination, you make them feel interested and excited. 激發","examples":["...the potential to fire the imagination of an entire generation. …激發整整一代人的想像力的潛能。","It was Allen who fired this rivalry with real passion. 是艾倫滿懷激情地激發了這次對抗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>fires</b> a gun or a bullet, or if they <b>fire</b>, a bullet is sent from a gun that they are using. 開 (槍); (槍) 開火","examples":["Seven people were wounded when soldiers fired rubber bullets to disperse crowds. 有7人在士兵們發射橡皮子彈驅散人群時受了傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>fire</b> an arrow, you send it from a bow. 射 (箭)","examples":["He fired an arrow into a clearing in the forest. 他把箭射進森林中的一片空地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>fire</b> questions at someone, you ask them a lot of questions very quickly, one after another. 連珠炮似地提出 (問題)","examples":["They were bombarded by more than 100 representatives firing questions on pollution. 他們遭到了一百多位代表就汙染問題連珠炮似的發問。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an employer <b>fires</b> you, they dismiss you from your job. 解僱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the engine of a motor vehicle <b>fires</b>, an electrical spark is produced which causes the fuel to burn and the engine to work. (引擎等) 點火","examples":["The engine fired and we moved off. 引擎點火後我們就開走了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object or substance <b>catches fire</b>, it starts burning. 起火","examples":["The blast caused several buildings to catch fire. 爆炸導致了幾個建築物起火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>on fire</b>, it is burning and being damaged or destroyed by an uncontrolled fire. 著火; 在燃燒","examples":["The captain radioed that the ship was on fire. 船長髮無線電報說船著火了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>set fire to</b> something or if you <b>set</b> it <b>on fire</b>, you start it burning in order to damage or destroy it. 放火燒","examples":["They set fire to vehicles outside that building. 他們放火燒了那幢樓外的車輛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>holds</b> their <b>fire</b> or <b>holds fire</b>, they stop shooting or they wait before they start shooting. 停止射擊; 等待射擊","examples":["Devereux ordered his men to hold their fire until the ships got closer. 德弗羅命令他計程車兵等船駛近了再開火。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are in the <b>line of fire</b>, you are in a position where someone is aiming their gun at you. If you move into their <b>line of fire</b>, you move into a position between them and the thing they were aiming at. (槍炮的) 發射線","examples":["He cheerfully blows away any bad guy stupid enough to get in his line of fire. 他興高采烈地將那些蠢得跑進他發射線內的任何壞蛋炸死。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>open fire</b> <b>on</b> someone, you start shooting at them. 開火","examples":["Then without warning, the troops opened fire on the crowd. 接著，在沒有警告的情況下，軍隊向人群開了火。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>return fire</b> or you <b>return</b> someone's <b>fire</b>, you shoot back at someone who has shot at you. 還擊","examples":["The soldiers returned fire after being attacked. 士兵們在受到攻擊之後進行了還擊。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you come <b>under fire</b> or are <b>under fire</b>, someone starts shooting at you. 遭到炮火襲擊","examples":["The Belgians fell back as the infantry came under fire. 比利時人在步兵部隊遭到炮火襲擊時撤退了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you come <b>under fire</b> <b>from</b> someone or are <b>under fire</b>, they criticize you strongly. 受到嚴厲批評","examples":["The president's plan first came under fire from critics who said he hadn't included enough spending cuts. 總統的計劃首先受到了反對者們的猛烈抨擊，他們說他沒有把足夠的費用削減包含在內。"]}]}]},"flower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花，開花植物；精華，最好的部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開花；繁榮，興旺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flower</b> is the part of a plant which is often brightly coloured, grows at the end of a stem, and only survives for a short time. 花 (朵)","examples":["Each individual flower is tiny. 每一朵花都很小。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>flower</b> is a stem of a plant that has one or more flowers on it and has been picked, usually with others, for example, to give as a present or to put in a vase. 花 (株)","examples":["...a bunch of flowers sent by a new admirer. …一位新崇拜者送來的一束花。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Flowers</b> are small plants that are grown for their flowers as opposed to trees, shrubs, and vegetables. 花卉","examples":["...a lawned area surrounded by screening plants and flowers. …四周環繞著屏障植物和花卉的一塊草地。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a plant or tree <b>flowers</b>, its flowers appear and open. 開花","examples":["Several of these rhododendrons will flower this year for the first time. 這些杜鵑花中有好幾株今年將第一次開花。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>flowers</b>, for example, a political movement or a relationship, it gets stronger and more successful. (政治運動等) 壯大; (關係等) 變得更好","examples":["Their relationship flowered. 他們的關係變得更好了。"]}]}]},"first":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"第一位的，最先的；首（次）的；（某一時間或某事後的）緊接著來到的；（一列中）最前面的；最重要的；（用於工作或職位的頭銜中）最高的；最迫切的，最合適的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"第一，最初；起初；第一次；（列舉時用）首先；（強調不願意）寧可；以身體的某一部位（或某人）在先（或為首）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"第一個人（或事物)；前所未有的事情；（汽車、腳踏車等的）最低檔；（英國大學學位）最高成績；（棒球）第一壘；一等品"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"第一次"}],"sections":[{"pos":"ord.","pos_name":"序數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>first</b> thing, person, event, or period of time is the one that happens or comes before all the others of the same kind. 第一 (個) 的","examples":["She lost 16 pounds in the first month of her diet. 她節食的第一個月減掉了16磅。","...the first few flakes of snow. …最初的幾片雪花。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something happens or is done for the <b>first</b> time, it has never happened or been done before. 第一次的","examples":["This is the first time she has experienced disappointment. 這是她第一次感受到失望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>first</b> thing, person, or place in a line is the one that is nearest to you or nearest to the front. (列隊中) 最前面的; (距離自己) 最近的","examples":["Before him, in the first row, sat the president. 在他前面第一排坐著總統。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>first</b> to refer to the best or most important thing or person of a particular kind. 最好的; 首要的","examples":["The first duty of any government must be to protect the interests of the taxpayers. 任何政府的首要職責都必須是保護納稅人的利益。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>First</b> is also an ordinal. 第一","examples":["She told him that her first reaction was disgust. 她告訴他她的第一反應是厭惡。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>First</b> is also a pronoun. 第一 (個)","examples":["The second paragraph startled me even more than the first. 第二段甚至比第一段更讓我吃驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The first</b> you hear of something or <b>the</b> <b>first</b> you know about it is the time when you first become aware of it. 第一次","examples":["We heard it on the TV last night – that was the first we heard of it. 我們是昨晚從電視上聽到的–那是我們第一次聽到這件事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>First</b> is also an adverb. 第一次","examples":["Anne and Steve got engaged two years after they had first started going out. 安妮和史蒂夫在他們第一次約會的兩年後訂婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>first</b>, you do it before anyone else does, or before you do anything else. 首先","examples":["I do not remember who spoke first, but we all expressed the same opinion. 我不記得誰先發了言，但是我們都表達了同樣的觀點。","First, tell me what you think of my products. 首先，告訴我你對我的產品有什麼看法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>first</b> when you are talking about what happens in the early part of an event or experience, in contrast to what happens later. 最初","examples":["When he first came home he wouldn't say anything about what he'd been doing. 剛回到家時，他對自己一直在做的事隻字也不願提。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In order to emphasize your determination not to do a particular thing, you can say that rather than do it, you would do something else <b>first</b>. 寧願","examples":["I'll die first, before I let you have all my money! 我寧願死，也不會讓你得到我所有的錢！"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An event that is described as <b>a first</b> has never happened before and is important or exciting. 首次發生的事","examples":["It is a first for New York. An outdoor exhibition of Fernando Botero's sculpture on Park Avenue. 在公園大道上舉辦費爾南多·博特羅的雕塑戶外展覽，這在紐約可是第一次！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>first of all</b> to introduce the first of a number of things that you want to say. 首先; 第一","examples":["The cut in the interest rates has not had very much impact in California for two reasons. First of all, banks are still afraid to loan. 降低利率在加利福尼亞州沒造成很大影響的原因有二。第一，銀行仍然害怕放貸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>at first</b> when you are talking about what happens in the early stages of an event or experience, or just after something else has happened, in contrast to what happens later. 起初","examples":["At first, he seemed surprised by my questions. 起初，他似乎對我的問題感到意外。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>comes first</b> for a particular person, you mean they treat or consider that person or thing as more important than anything else. 居於首要地位","examples":["There's no time for boyfriends, my career comes first. 我沒有時間交男朋友，我的事業是第一位的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you learn or experience something <b>at first hand</b>, you experience it yourself or learn it directly rather than being told about it by other people. 親自地; 直接地","examples":["He arrived in Natal to see at first hand the effects of the recent heavy fighting. 他到納塔爾親自察看最近的激戰所造成的影響。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>do not know the first thing about</b> something, you are emphasizing that you know absolutely nothing about it. 對某事一無所知","examples":["You don't know the first thing about farming. 你對耕種一無所知。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone or something <b>first</b>, you treat or consider them as more important than anything else. 把某人或某事放在首要地位","examples":["Somebody has to think for the child and put him first. 得有人替這個孩子著想，把他放在第一位。"]}]}]},"food":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（植物生長的）養料；食物，食品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Food</b> is what people and animals eat. 食物","examples":["Enjoy your food. 用餐愉快。","...frozen foods. …冷凍食品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone <b>food for thought</b>, you make them think carefully about something. 發人深思的事","examples":["Her speech offers much food for thought. 她的演講有許多發人深思的內容。"]}]}]},"fog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"霧；煙霧，塵霧；困惑，迷惘；（底片等的）灰霧，霧翳"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使令人困惑，使費解；底片產生灰霧；起霧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is <b>fog</b>, there are tiny drops of water in the air which form a thick cloud and make it difficult to see things. 霧","examples":["The crash happened in thick fog. 這次撞車發生在濃霧中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fog</b> is an unpleasant cloud of something such as smoke inside a building or room. 一團 (煙霧)","examples":["...a fog of stale cigarette smoke. …一團難聞的香菸煙霧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a second growth of grass after the first mowing (第一次割草後長的)新草","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"grass left to grow long in winter 過冬長草","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to confuse or become confused 使困惑; 變得困惑","examples":[]}]}]},"floor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（房間的）地板，地面；樓層，同樓層所有房間（或地方）；（海、森林、洞穴等的）底部；（工資或物價的）最低額，底價；（建築物內的）場地，（活動的）場所；（議會的）議員席，全體與會者（the floor）；（辯論中）發言權，發言機會；<非正式>地面；（車廂內的）底板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指體育運動中）擊倒，打倒；使驚訝得不知所措；給…鋪設地板（或地面）；<美，非正式>踩足（汽車的）油門，使全速行駛；（被困難）難倒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>floor</b> of a room is the part of it that you walk on. 地板","examples":["Jack's sitting on the floor watching TV. 傑克正坐在地板上看電視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>floor</b> of a building is all the rooms that are on a particular level. 樓層","examples":["The café was on the top floor of the hospital. 咖啡館在醫院的頂層。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> ocean <b>floor</b> is the ground at the bottom of an ocean. <b>The</b> valley <b>floor</b> is the ground at the bottom of a valley. (海洋、山谷等的) 底","examples":["They spend hours feeding on the ocean floor. 它們花幾個小時在海底進食。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The place where official debates and discussions are held, especially between members of a legislature, is referred to as <b>the</b> <b>floor</b>. 議政廳","examples":["The issues were debated on the floor of the House. 這些問題在眾議院議政廳進行了辯論。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a debate or discussion, <b>the floor</b> is the people who are listening to the arguments being put forward but who are not among the main speakers. 與會者","examples":["The president is taking questions from the floor. 會議主席正在回答與會者提出的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are floored</b> <b>by</b> something, you are unable to respond to it because you are so surprised by it. (因驚訝而) 不知所措","examples":["He was floored by the announcement. 他被這個通告震驚得不知所措。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>has the floor</b>, they are the person who is speaking in a debate or discussion. 發言","examples":["Since I have the floor for the moment, I want to go back to a previous point. 藉此發言的機會，我想回到前面的一個問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take to the floor</b>, you start dancing at a dance or disco. 開始跳舞","examples":["The happy couple and their respective parents took to the floor. 那幸福的一對和他們各自的父母開始跳起舞來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>wipe the floor with</b> someone, you defeat them completely in a competition or discussion. 徹底擊敗","examples":["He could wipe the floor with the opposition. 他能徹底擊敗反對派。"]}]}]},"forest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"森林，林區；（森林似的）一叢，一片；御獵場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"被森林覆蓋，植林於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>forest</b> is a large area where trees grow close together. 森林","examples":["Parts of the forest are still dense and inaccessible. 森林的一些地方仍然茂密不可進入。"]}]}]},"forty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"四十；複數形式 forties 指四十至四十九之間的數字（如年齡或溫度）；the forties 指某個世紀的四十年代（如二十世紀四十年代）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"四十的，四十個的（用於名詞前表示數量）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Forty</b> is the number 40. 四十; 40","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>forties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 40 and 49. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>forties</b>, you are aged between 40 and 49. If the temperature is <b>in the forties</b>, the temperature is between 40 and 49 degrees. 四十幾 (指40至49之間的數字)","examples":["He was a big man in his forties, smartly dressed in a suit and tie. 他是一個四十幾歲的高大男子，穿著西服打著領帶，很精神。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The forties</b> is the decade between 1940 and 1949. 四十年代 (指某世紀40到49年)","examples":["Steel cans were introduced sometime during the forties. 鋼罐是在四十年代的某個時候開始使用的。"]}]}]},"fourteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十四；十四個；十四歲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"數字十四，十四的記號；十四歲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十四的；十四個的；十四歲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fourteen</b> is the number 14. 14","examples":["I'm fourteen years old. 我14歲。"]}]}]},"fork":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餐叉，叉子；耙，叉；岔路，支流；叉狀部件，叉狀物；（棋）一捉兩，一捉多"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（道路、河流等）分岔，岔開；（用餐叉）叉起；耙地，叉掘；（不情願地）大把花錢，付出；走岔路中的一條；用一個棋子同時進攻（兩個棋子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fork</b> is a tool used for eating food which has a row of three or four long metal points at the end. 餐叉","examples":["...knives and forks. ...刀和叉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fork</b> in a road, path, or river is a point at which it divides into two parts and forms a \"Y\" shape. (道路、河流等的) 岔口","examples":["We arrived at a fork in the road. 我們來到了該路的一個岔口。","The road divides; you should take the right fork. 路分岔了；你應該走右岔路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A garden <b>fork</b> is a tool used for breaking up soil which has a row of three or four long metal points at the end. 耙","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fork</b> food <b>into</b> your mouth or <b>onto</b> a plate, you put it there using a fork. 叉起","examples":["He forked an egg onto a piece of bread and folded it into a sandwich. 他叉起一個雞蛋放到一片面包上並將其折成了一個三明治。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a road, path, or river <b>forks</b>, it forms a fork. (公路、路徑、河流等) 分岔","examples":["Beyond the village the road forked. 過了那個村子公路就分岔了。"]}]}]},"four":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"四，四個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"四個人（或事）的一組；（板球）四分的一擊；（衣服等）四號；四點的紙牌；四槳賽艇，四人划船隊；（Four）（法、美）福爾（人名）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"四的，四個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Four</b> is the number 4. 4","examples":["Judith is married with four children. 朱迪斯已經結婚，有4個孩子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on all fours</b>, your knees, feet, and hands are on the ground. 趴","examples":["She crawled on all fours over to the window. 她匍匐著爬到窗邊。"]}]}]},"fly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"飛，飛行；乘飛機，搭乘（某公司航班）；駕駛（飛機）；空運；飛越；疾馳，快速移動；放飛（風箏）；飛舞，飄蕩；懸掛，飄揚；（使）逃離，匆忙離開；成功；飛逝；擊騰空球；流傳，四處傳播；（指責，謾罵）往來激烈；被認可，被接受"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蒼蠅，假蠅；褲門襟；騰空球，高飛球；<澳，非正式>努力，嘗試；（帳篷的）篷頂；（劇院）吊景區，懸吊佈景的空間；<英，史>單馬出租馬車"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>時髦漂亮的；<英>機靈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fly</b> is a small insect with two wings. There are many kinds of flies, and the most common are black in colour. 蒼蠅","examples":["Flies buzzed at the animals' swishing tails. 蒼蠅在動物甩動的尾巴邊嗡嗡叫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a lure made from a fish-hook dressed with feathers, tinsel, etc, to resemble any of various flies or nymphs: used in fly-fishing (“飛蠅釣法”中使用的)假蠅魚餌","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The front opening on a pair of trousers is referred to as the <b>fly</b>. It usually consists of a zipper or row of buttons behind a band of cloth. 褲子的前開口","examples":["I'm the kind of person who checks to see if my fly is undone. 我是那種會檢查褲前拉鍊是否拉上的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a flap forming the entrance to a tent 帳篷門簾","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a piece of canvas drawn over the ridgepole of a tent to form an outer roof 帳篷的外層帆布帳頂","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"the space above the stage out of view of the audience, used for storing scenery, etc (不在觀眾視野內、用於存放舞臺佈景等的)舞臺上部空間","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"飛行","examples":["...a flying instructor. …一名飛行教練。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"a flap forming the entrance to a tent","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as a bird, insect, or aircraft <b>flies</b>, it moves through the air. 飛","examples":["The planes flew through the clouds. 飛機穿越雲層。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fly</b> somewhere, you travel there in an aircraft. 乘飛機","examples":["He flew to Los Angeles. 他乘飛機去洛杉磯。","He flew back to London. 他乘飛機回到倫敦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as your hair <b>is flying</b> about, it is moving about freely and loosely in the air. 飛舞","examples":["His long, uncovered hair flew back in the wind. 他那無遮蓋的長髮隨風向後飛舞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>flies</b> in a particular direction, you are emphasizing that they move there with a lot of speed or force. 飛奔","examples":["She flew to their bedsides when they were ill. 她在他們生病時飛奔到他們的床邊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>flies</b> an aircraft, they control its movement in the air. 駕駛 (飛機); 駕駛飛機","examples":["Parker had successfully flown both aircraft. 帕克成功地駕駛過這兩架飛機。","He flew a small plane to Cuba. 他駕駛一架小飛機去古巴。","I learned to fly in Vietnam. 我在越南學會了駕駛飛機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>fly</b> someone or something somewhere means to take or send them there in an aircraft. 空運","examples":["It may be possible to fly the women and children out on Thursday. 週四有可能將這些婦女和兒童空運出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fly</b> a flag or if it <b>is flying</b>, you display it at the top of a pole. 升 (旗); 飄揚","examples":["They flew the flag of the African National Congress. 他們揮動著非洲國民大會的旗幟。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"knowing and sharp; smart 博學而敏銳的; 聰明的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"furtive or sneaky 鬼祟的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone wouldn't <b>hurt a fly</b> or wouldn't <b>harm a fly</b>, you are emphasizing that they are very kind and gentle. “連一隻蒼蠅都不願傷害”指“溫柔、善良”","examples":["Ray wouldn't hurt a fly. 雷很溫柔善良。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>let fly</b>, you attack someone, either physically by hitting them, or with words by insulting them. 攻擊","examples":["A simmering dispute ended with her letting fly with a stream of obscenities. 一次激烈的爭吵以她那一連串汙言穢語的攻擊告終。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>send</b> someone or something <b>flying</b> or if they <b>go flying</b>, they move through the air and fall down with a lot of force. 把 (某人/某物) 打翻在地","examples":["The blow sent the young man flying. 那一擊將那年輕人打翻在地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>on the fly</b>, you do it quickly or automatically, without planning it in advance. 立刻; 飛快","examples":["You've got to be able to make decisions on the fly as deadlines loom. 你必須能夠立刻作出決定，因為最後期限迫在眉睫。"]}]}]},"friday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期五；忠僕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Friday</b> is the day after Thursday and before Saturday. 星期五","examples":["Mr. Cook is intending to go to the Middle East on Friday. 庫克先生正打算星期五去中東。","...Friday November 6. …11月6日星期五。"]}]}]},"foot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳，足；英尺；基礎，底部；襪底；音步；<文>步態，步伐；（縫紉機的）壓腳板"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"有……只腳（的），用……腳（或足的）(-footed)；……英尺高的人(或東西)，……英尺長的東西(-footer)"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（剎車或泵）用腳操作的，腳踏的；（巡邏隊）步行的，步（兵）的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>支付（尤指大額或不合理賬單）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>feet</b> are the parts of your body that are at the ends of your legs, and that you stand on. 腳","examples":["She stamped her foot again. 她又跺了跺腳。","...a foot injury. …腳傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>foot</b> is a unit for measuring length, height, or depth, and is equal to 12 inches or 30.48 centimetres. When you are giving measurements, the form \"foot\" is often used as the plural instead of the plural form \"feet.\" 英尺 (常用單數形式表示複數)","examples":["This beautiful and curiously shaped lake lies at around fifteen thousand feet. 這座形狀奇特的美麗湖泊周長約一萬五千英尺。","He occupies a cell 10 foot long, 6 foot wide and 10 foot high. 他住在一個10英尺長、6英尺寬、10英尺高的小房間裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>foot</b> <b>of</b> something is the part that is farthest from its top. 底部","examples":["David called to the children from the foot of the stairs. 大衛在樓梯下喊孩子們。","...the foot of the hill. …山腳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>foot</b> <b>of</b> a bed is the end nearest to the feet of the person lying in it. (床) 尾","examples":["Friends stood at the foot of the bed, looking at her with serious faces. 朋友們站在床尾，表情嚴肅地看著她。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>foot</b> brake or <b>foot</b> pump is operated by your foot rather than by your hand. 腳踏的","examples":["I tried to reach the foot brakes but I couldn't. 我試著去踩腳剎，但夠不著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>foot</b> patrol or <b>foot</b> soldiers walk rather than travelling in vehicles or on horseback. 步行的","examples":["Paratroopers and foot-soldiers entered the building on the government's behalf. 傘兵和步兵代表政府進入了大樓。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get <b>cold feet</b> <b>about</b> something, you become nervous or frightened about it because you think it will fail. 緊張; 害怕","examples":["The Government is getting cold feet about the reforms. 政府在改革上變得緊張膽小。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is finding</b> their <b>feet</b> in a new situation, you mean that they are starting to feel confident and to deal with things successfully. (在新環境) 站住腳","examples":["I don't know anyone here but I am sure I will manage when I find my feet. 我在這兒什麼人都不認識，但我確信一旦站住腳就會應付過來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has their <b>feet on the ground</b>, you approve of the fact that they have a sensible and practical attitude toward life, and do not have unrealistic ideas. 腳踏實地","examples":["In that respect he needs to keep his feet on the ground and not get carried away. 就那方面看來，他需要腳踏實地而不能飄飄然。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you go somewhere <b>on foot</b>, you walk, rather than using any form of transport. 步行","examples":["We rowed ashore, then explored the island on foot for the rest of the day. 我們將船靠岸，然後在這天餘下的時間裡徒步上島探險。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> your <b>feet</b>, you are standing up. 站著","examples":["Everyone was on their feet applauding wildly. 每個人都站起來熱烈鼓掌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>on</b> their <b>feet</b> again after an illness or difficult period, you mean that they have recovered and are back to normal. 恢復","examples":["You need someone to take the pressure off and help you get back on your feet. 你需要有人為你減減壓，幫你恢復。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that someone always <b>lands on</b> their <b>feet</b>, you mean that they are always successful or lucky, although they do not seem to achieve this by their own efforts. 走運","examples":["He has good looks and charm, and always lands on his feet. 他長相好、有魅力，總走好運。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone <b>puts</b> their <b>foot down</b>, they use their authority in order to stop something from happening. 堅決反對","examples":["He had planned to go skiing on his own in March but his wife had decided to put her foot down. 他原計劃在3月獨自去滑雪，但他的妻子堅決反對。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone <b>puts</b> their <b>foot down</b> when they are driving, they drive as fast as they can. 開快車","examples":[]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>puts</b> their <b>foot in it</b> or <b>puts</b> their <b>foot in</b> their <b>mouth</b>, they accidentally do or say something which embarrasses or offends people. (不經意間) 犯錯誤","examples":["Our chairman has really put his foot in it, poor man, though he doesn't know it. 我們的主席確實錯了，可憐的人，儘管他還不知道。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> your <b>feet up</b>, you relax or have a rest, especially by sitting or lying with your feet supported off the ground. 放鬆休息 (尤指坐著或躺著把腳抬高)","examples":["After supper he'd put his feet up and read. 晚餐後他會放鬆休息一下，讀點什麼。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you never <b>put a foot wrong</b>, you never make any mistakes. 不出錯","examples":["When he's around, we never put a foot wrong. 他在的時候，我們從不出錯。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>sets foot</b> in a place, you mean that they enter it or reach it, and you are emphasizing the significance of their action. If you say that someone <b>never</b> <b>sets foot</b> in a place, you are emphasizing that they never go there. 涉足; 介入","examples":["...the day the first man set foot on the moon. …人類首次踏上月球的那一天。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If someone has to <b>stand on</b> their <b>own two feet</b>, they have to be independent and manage their life without help from other people. 自立","examples":["My father didn't mind whom I married, so long as I could stand on my own two feet and wasn't dependent on my husband. 我父親並不介意我跟誰結婚，只要我能夠自立、不靠丈夫就行。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you get or rise <b>to</b> your <b>feet</b>, you stand up. 站起來","examples":["Malone got to his feet and followed his superior out of the suite. 馬隆站起來跟著他的上司走出套房。","The delegates cheered and rose to their feet. 代表們歡呼著站起來。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If someone <b>gets off on the wrong foot</b> in a new situation, they make a bad start by doing something in completely the wrong way. 出師不利","examples":["Even though they called the election and had been preparing for it for some time, they got off on the wrong foot. 雖然他們召集了這次選舉，也為此準備了一段時間，他們還是出師不利。"]}]}]},"frog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛙，青蛙；法國佬（對法國人的蔑稱）（Frog）；（外套的紡錘狀）裝飾盤花紐扣（或裝飾緶）；蹄楔；（鐵路線上的）開槽鐵盤或鋼盤；尤指支撐（或繫緊）某物的東西；（腰帶上掛劍、刺刀或類似武器的）搭環；花插（插花用的底座）；（絃樂器的）弓根，馬尾箱；（平面上的）隆起部分，腫塊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捕蛙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>frog</b> is a small creature with smooth skin, big eyes, and long back legs which it uses for jumping. Frogs usually live near water. 蛙","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a decorative fastening of looped braid or cord, as on the front of a 19th-century military uniform (19世紀軍裝上的)裝飾性盤扣","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a tough elastic horny material in the centre of the sole of a horse's foot (馬蹄鐵底部的)彈力硬角狀物","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a grooved plate of iron or steel placed to guide train wheels over an intersection of railway lines (鐵路線上的)開槽鐵盤或鋼盤","examples":[]}]}]},"force":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴力，武力；力，力量；自然力；（有某目的）一群人；有影響力的人（或事）；影響力；武裝部隊；警察部門；風力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強迫；用力推；使發生；勉強做出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>forces</b> you <b>to</b> do something, they make you do it even though you do not want to, for example, by threatening you. 強迫","examples":["He took two women hostage and forced them to drive away from the area. 他劫持了兩名女人質並強迫她們開車離開這個地區。","They were grabbed by three men who appeared to force them into a car. 他們被三名男子抓住，這些人看上去強使他們進入了一輛汽車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation or event <b>forces</b> you to do something, it makes it necessary for you to do something that you would not otherwise have done. 迫使","examples":["A back injury forced her to withdraw from Wimbledon. 一處背傷迫使她退出了溫布林登網球賽。","He turned right, down a dirt road that forced him into four-wheel drive. 他向右轉彎，開上了一條土路，這迫使他開始四輪驅動行駛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>forces</b> something <b>on</b> or <b>upon</b> you, they make you accept or use it when you would prefer not to. 強加","examples":["To force this agreement on the nation is wrong. 把這項協議強加於這個國家是錯誤的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>force</b> something into a particular position, you use a lot of strength to make it move there. 用力壓住","examples":["They were forcing her head under the icy waters, drowning her. 他們在用力把她的頭按到冰冷的水中，淹她。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>forces</b> a lock, a door, or a window, they break the lock or fastening in order to get into a building without using a key. 強行 (開啟)","examples":["That evening police forced the door of the apartment and arrested Mr. Roberts. 那晚警察強行開啟那公寓的門逮捕了羅伯茨先生。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cause (plants or farm animals) to grow or fatten artificially at an increased rate 人工提速育肥(植物和家禽)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>force</b> your <b>way</b> <b>through</b> or <b>into</b> somewhere, you have to push or break things that are in your way in order to get there. 強行進入","examples":["The miners forced their way through a police cordon. 那些礦工們衝破了警察的封鎖線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>from</b> <b>force of habit</b>, you do it because you have always done it in the past, rather than because you have thought carefully about it. 習慣做法","examples":["He looked around from force of habit, but nobody paid any attention to him. 他出於習慣環顧四周，但沒人注意他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A law, rule, or system that is <b>in force</b> exists or is being used. 在實施中","examples":["Although the new tax is already in force, you have until November to lodge an appeal. 儘管新稅制已經實行，但你在11月之前仍可以提起上訴。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When people do something <b>in force</b>, they do it in large numbers. 大批地","examples":["Voters turned out in force for their first taste of multiparty elections. 選民大批到場初次體驗多黨選舉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>join forces</b> <b>with</b> someone, you work together in order to achieve a common aim or purpose. (與…) 聯手","examples":["Both groups joined forces to persuade voters to approve a tax break for the industry. 兩集團合力遊說選民們同意給予這個行業減稅。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone uses <b>force</b> to do something, or if it is done by <b>force</b>, strong and violent physical action is taken in order to achieve it. 武力","examples":["The government decided against using force to break up the demonstrations. 政府決定不使用武力來驅散示威遊行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Force</b> is the power or strength which something has. 力量","examples":["The force of the explosion shattered the windows of several buildings. 那次爆炸的力量震碎了幾棟建築的窗子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>force</b> <b>of</b> something is the powerful effect or quality that it has. 強大的效力; 高品質","examples":["He changed our world through the force of his ideas. 他以其思想的強大影響力改變了我們的世界。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Force</b> is used before a number to indicate a wind of a particular speed or strength, especially a very strong wind. 風力","examples":["The airlift was conducted in force ten winds. 空運是在10級大風中進行的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to someone or something as a <b>force</b> in a particular type of activity, you mean that they have a strong influence on it. 勢力; 強大影響力","examples":["For years the army was the most powerful political force in the country. 多年來軍隊都是該國最強大的政治勢力。","The band is still an innovative force in music. 該樂隊仍是音樂界的一支創新力量。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>forces</b> to refer to processes and events that do not appear to be caused by human beings, and are therefore difficult to understand or control. (非人為的、非人類所能理解或控制的) 力量","examples":["...the protection of mankind against the forces of nature: epidemics, predators, floods, hurricanes. …使人類免受流行病、食肉動物、洪水和颶風等自然力傷害的保護。","The principle of market forces was applied to some of the country's most revered institutions. 市場力量的原理被應用在了該國一些最受尊崇的機構。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In physics, a <b>force</b> is the pulling or pushing effect that something has on something else. (物理學中的) 力","examples":["...the Earth's gravitational force. …地球的引力。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"(in northern England) a waterfall (英格蘭北部的)瀑布","examples":[]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Forces</b> are groups of soldiers or military vehicles that are organized for a particular purpose. 軍事力量","examples":["...the deployment of American forces in the region. …美國軍事力量在該地區的部署。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>forces</b> means the army, the navy, or the air force, or all three. 軍隊; 海陸空軍","examples":["The more senior you become in the forces, the more likely you are to end up in a desk job. 你在軍隊中的級別升得越高，你就越有可能落得個坐辦公室的職位。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>force</b> is sometimes used to mean the police force. 警察部門","examples":["It was hard for a police officer to make friends outside the force. 一名警官在警察部門之外交朋友很難。"]}]}]},"friend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"朋友，友人；（社交網站上的）好友；（與……是） 朋友，朋友關係（friends）；（組織或政治運動等的）支持者，（尤指）贊助者；自己人，同盟者；熟悉（或有幫助）的事物；相識的人，（偶然遇見的）陌生人（常作禮貌稱呼語或諷刺用語）；友好國家；<英>（議員間或律師間的一種稱呼）朋友，閣下，同人；（基督教）公誼會教友，貴格會成員，教友派信徒（Friend）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在社交網站上） 把（某人）加為好友；<古>與……為友，幫助"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>friend</b> is someone who you know well and like, but who is not related to you. 朋友","examples":["I had a long talk about this with my best friend. 我和我最好的朋友就此進行了長談。","She never was a close friend of mine. 她從來就不是我的密友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one country refers to another as a <b>friend</b>, they mean that the other country is not an enemy of theirs. 盟國","examples":["The president said that Japan is now a friend and international partner. 總統說日本現在是盟國和國際夥伴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>friends</b> <b>with</b> someone, you are their friend and they are yours. (與…是) 朋友","examples":["I still wanted to be friends with Alison. 我仍然希望同艾莉森做朋友。","We remained good friends. 我們一直是好朋友。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>friends</b> <b>of</b> a country, cause, organization, or a famous politician are the people and organizations who help and support them. 支持者","examples":["...the friends of Israel. …以色列的支持者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make friends</b> <b>with</b> someone, you begin a friendship with them. You can also say that two people <b>make friends</b>. 同…交朋友","examples":["He has made friends with the kids on the street. 他同街上的孩子們交上了朋友。","Dennis made friends easily. 丹尼斯容易交上朋友。"]}]}]},"fruit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水果；（植物的）果實；成果，結果，後果；（自然的）產物，物產；<古>子孫，後代；<美，非正式>男同性戀者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）結果實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fruit</b> or a <b>fruit</b> is something which grows on a tree or bush and which contains seeds or a pit covered by a substance that you can eat. 水果","examples":["Fresh fruit and vegetables provide fibre and vitamins. 新鮮的水果和蔬菜提供纖維素和多種維生素。","...bananas and other tropical fruits. …香蕉和其他熱帶水果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>fruits</b> or <b>the</b> <b>fruit</b> <b>of</b> someone's work or activity are the good things that result from it. 成果","examples":["The team has really worked hard and Mansell is enjoying the fruits of that labour. 那個團隊真地已很努力，而曼塞爾正在享受這一勞動的成果。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a plant <b>fruits</b>, it produces fruit. 結果實","examples":["The scientists will study the variety of trees and observe which are fruiting. 科學家們將研究樹木的多樣性並觀察哪些樹木結果實。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the effort that you put into something or a particular way of doing something <b>bears fruit</b>, it is successful and produces good results. (付出的努力) 有成效","examples":["Eleanor's work among the women will, I trust, bear fruit. 埃莉諾在這些婦女中所做的工作我相信會有成效。"]}]}]},"ghost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬼，幽靈；（尤指對可怕事物的）記憶，回憶；一絲，一點；（電視或計算機螢幕上的）重像，重影"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"代人寫作，為人代筆；（平穩不費力地）滑行；作祟於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ghost</b> is the spirit of a dead person that someone believes they can see or feel. 幽靈","examples":["...the ghost of Marie Antoinette. …瑪麗·安託瓦內特的幽靈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>ghost of</b> something, especially of something bad that has happened, is the memory of it. 陰魂 (指對壞事的記憶)","examples":["...the ghost of anti-Americanism. …反美主義的陰魂。"]}]}]},"garden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花園，菜園，果園；庭園；公園；（用於街名）街，廣場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做園藝工作，種植花木"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>garden</b> is a piece of land next to someone's house, with grass and plants growing in it.","examples":["...the most beautiful garden on Earth. …地球上最美的花園。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>garden</b> is the part of a yard which is used for growing flowers and vegetables. 花園; 菜園","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"園藝活","examples":["I have taken up gardening again. 我又開始幹起了園藝活。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Gardens</b> are places like a park that have areas of plants, trees, and grass, and that people can visit and walk around. 公園","examples":["The Gardens are open from 10:30 a.m. until 5:00 p.m. 這些公園從上午10:30開放到下午5:00。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Gardens</b> is sometimes used as part of the name of a street. (用作街名) …街","examples":["He lives at 9 Acacia Gardens. 他住在金合歡街9號。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>garden</b>, you do work in your garden such as weeding or planting. 幹園藝活","examples":["Jim gardened at the homes of friends on weekends. 吉姆每逢週末在朋友們的家裡幹園藝活。"]}]}]},"glasses":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"眼鏡；玻璃杯（glass 的複數）；雙筒望遠鏡（尤見於 field glasses）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……裝上玻璃；把……裝入玻璃容器內（glass 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glasses</b> are two lenses in a frame that some people wear in front of their eyes in order to help them see better. 眼鏡","examples":["...the 140 million Americans who wear glasses or contact lenses. …1.4億戴眼鏡或者隱性眼鏡的美國人。"]}]}]},"fun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樂趣，享受；嬉戲，玩笑"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有趣的，令人愉快的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式> 開玩笑，取笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to an activity or situation as <b>fun</b> if you think it is pleasant and enjoyable and it causes you to feel happy. 樂趣","examples":["It's been a learning adventure and it's also been great fun. 那是一次很受教育的冒險活動，也是極大的樂趣。","It could be fun to watch them. 看他們會是樂趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>fun</b>, you mean that you enjoy being with them because they say and do interesting or amusing things. 有趣的人","examples":["Liz was fun to be with. 莉茲是與之相處有趣的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as a <b>fun</b> thing, you mean that you think it is enjoyable. If you describe someone as a <b>fun</b> person, you mean that you enjoy being with them. 令人愉快的","examples":["It was a fun evening. 那是個令人愉快的夜晚。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>for fun</b> or <b>for the fun of it</b>, you do it in order to enjoy yourself rather than because it is important or necessary. 為了好玩","examples":["We used to drive too fast, just for fun. 我們過去常常開得太快，就為了好玩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>in fun</b>, you do it as a joke or for amusement, without intending to cause any harm. 鬧著玩兒地","examples":["Don't say such things, even in fun. 別說這樣的話，即使是鬧著玩兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make fun of</b> someone or something or <b>poke fun at</b> them, you laugh at them, tease them, or make jokes about them in a way that causes them to seem ridiculous. 拿…開玩笑","examples":["Don't make fun of me. 別拿我開玩笑。"]}]}]},"gift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禮物，贈品；恩賜，授予；輕而易舉的事，絕對不會錯失的機會；才能，天賦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贈送；（無意中）讓（對手）獲得"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gift</b> is something that you give someone as a present. 禮物","examples":["...a gift of $50.00. …一件$50.00的禮物。","They believed the unborn child was a gift from God. 他們相信那個尚未出生的孩子就是上帝賜予的一份禮物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has a <b>gift</b> <b>for</b> doing something, they have a natural ability for doing it. 天賦","examples":["As a youth he discovered a gift for teaching. 年輕的時候他就發現了自己教書的天賦。"]}]}]},"front":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"前面，正面；前線，前方；方面，領域；掩護；鋒；海濱，湖畔；封面，頭版；建築物的面；（裝出的）樣子；（政治組織名稱）陣線；膽大，自信；胸部；<古>（人的）臉，前額"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"前面的，正面的；（足球等）踢前鋒的；（母音）舌前位的；起掩護作用的；（18穴高爾夫球場的）前9穴的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"領導（機構、樂隊）；主持（電視節目）；面向；用……覆蓋正面；提供資金；<古，澳新>面臨，對抗；<澳新>露面，到達；以舌前位發（母音）；（語言學）將（句子成分）前置；為……作掩護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>front</b> <b>of</b> something is the part of it that faces you, or that faces forward, or that you normally see or use. 前面","examples":["One man sat in an armchair, and the other sat on the front of the desk. 一個男人坐在扶手椅上，另一個坐在桌前。","Stand at the front of the line. 站在隊伍的前面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>front</b> <b>of</b> a building is the side or part of it that faces the street. 臨街面","examples":["Attached to the front of the house, there was a large veranda. 連著房子的臨街面有一個大陽臺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a war, the <b>front</b> is a line where two opposing armies are facing each other. 前線","examples":["Sonja's husband is fighting at the front. 索妮亞的丈夫正在前線打仗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something is happening on a particular <b>front</b>, you mean that it is happening with regard to a particular situation or field of activity. 領域","examples":["...research across a wide academic front. …跨多個學術領域的研究。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone puts on a particular kind of <b>front</b>, they pretend to have a particular quality. (裝出的) 樣子","examples":["Michael kept up a brave front both to the world and in his home. 邁克爾在家外家內都保持著一副勇敢的樣子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An organization or activity that is <b>a</b> <b>front</b> <b>for</b> one that is illegal or secret is used to hide it. (非法或秘密組織或活動的) 掩護者","examples":["...a firm later identified by the police as a front for crime syndicates. …後來被警方證實是為犯罪團伙做掩護的一家公司。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In relation to the weather, a <b>front</b> is a line where a mass of cold air meets a mass of warm air. (冷暖空氣交匯的) 鋒面","examples":["The snow signalled the arrival of a front, and a high-pressure area seemed to be settling in. 降雪標誌了一個鋒面的到來，一個高壓區似乎正在進入本地。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A person's or animal's <b>front</b> is the part of their body between their head and their legs that is on the opposite side to their back. 身體的前部","examples":["When baby is lying on his front, hold something so that he has to raise his head to see it. 當寶寶趴著時，抓一樣東西逗他，這樣他就得抬起頭來才能看到。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Front</b> is used to refer to the side or part of something that is toward the front or nearest to the front. 前面的","examples":["I went out there on the front porch. 我走了出來，到了前門廊。","She was only six and still missing her front teeth. 她只有6歲，還沒有長出門牙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>front</b> page of a newspaper is the outside of the first page, where the main news stories are printed. 頭 (版)","examples":["The front page carries a photograph of the two foreign ministers. 報紙頭版刊登了兩位外交部長的一張合影。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>in front</b>, they are ahead of others in a moving group, or further forward than someone or something else. 在前面","examples":["Officers will crack down on lunatic motorists who speed or drive too close to the car in front. 警官們將嚴懲那些超速行駛或與前面車輛追尾的瘋狂駕車者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>in front</b> in a competition or contest at a particular point is winning at that point. (在比賽中) 領先","examples":["Richard Dunwoody is in front in the jockeys' title race. 理查德·鄧伍迪在職業賽馬冠軍賽中處於領先位置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in front of</b> a particular thing, they are facing it, ahead of it, or close to the front part of it. 在…的前面","examples":["She sat down in front of her dressing-table mirror to look at herself. 她在梳妝檯的鏡子前面坐下來端詳自己。","Something darted out in front of my car, and my car hit it. 有東西突然從我車前衝出來，隨即我的車就撞了它。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do or say something <b>in front of</b> someone else, you do or say it when they are present. 當著…的面","examples":["They never argued in front of their children. 他們從來不當著孩子們的面爭吵。"]}]}]},"glass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玻璃；玻璃杯；一杯之量；玻璃器皿，玻璃製品；玻璃保護面；眼鏡，透鏡；<英>鏡子；（計時）沙漏；氣壓表，晴雨表"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用玻璃覆蓋，給……裝玻璃；（尤指在打獵時）用望遠鏡觀察（周圍環境）；<英，非正式>用啤酒杯打（某人的臉）；反映；成玻璃狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glass</b> is a hard, transparent substance that is used to make things such as windows and bottles. 玻璃","examples":["...a pane of glass. …一塊玻璃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>glass</b> is a container made from glass, which you can drink from and which does not have a handle. 玻璃杯","examples":["Grossman raised the glass to his lips. 格羅斯曼把玻璃杯舉到唇邊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The contents of a glass can be referred to as a <b>glass</b> <b>of</b> something. 一玻璃杯的量","examples":["...a glass of milk. …一玻璃杯牛奶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Glass</b> is used to mean objects made of glass, for example drinking containers and bowls. 玻璃製品","examples":["There's a glittering array of glass to choose from at markets. 市場上有大量光彩奪目的玻璃製品可供選擇。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Glasses</b> are two lenses in a frame that some people wear in front of their eyes in order to help them see better. 眼鏡","examples":["He took off his glasses. 他摘掉了眼鏡。"]}]}]},"girl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女孩；姑娘，年輕女子，未婚女子；（常與物主限定詞連用）女兒；（非正式）（男人的）女朋友；（舊或用於複合詞）女職員，女演員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>girl</b> is a female child. 女孩","examples":["...an eleven-year-old girl. …一個11歲的女孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's daughter as a <b>girl</b>. 女兒","examples":["We had a little girl. 我們有個小女兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Young women are often referred to as <b>girls</b>. This use could cause offence. 妞兒 (常指年輕女人，可能有冒犯之意)","examples":["...a pretty twenty-year-old girl. …一個20歲的漂亮妞兒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people refer to a man's girlfriend as his <b>girl</b>. 女朋友","examples":["I've been with my girl for nine years. 我和我女友在一起已有9年了。"]}]}]},"game":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遊戲，比賽；一局，一場；運動會；體育課，體育活動；兒戲；詭計，花招；獵物，野味；行當，行業；玩耍，消遣；比賽技巧"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"願意嘗試的，有冒險精神的；<舊>（腿）殘疾的，瘸的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"操縱；玩影片（或電視、電腦）遊戲；賭博"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>game</b> is an activity or sport usually involving skill, knowledge, or chance, in which you follow fixed rules and try to win against an opponent or to solve a puzzle. 遊戲; 運動","examples":["...the wonderful game of football. …精彩的足球運動。","...a playful game of hide-and-seek. …一個有趣的捉迷藏遊戲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>game</b> is one particular occasion on which a game is played. 比賽","examples":["It was the first game of the season. 那是本賽季的第一場比賽。","He regularly watched our games from the stands. 他經常從看臺上觀看我們的比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>game</b> is a part of a match, for example in tennis or bridge, consisting of a fixed number of points. (比賽中的) 一局","examples":["She won six games to love in the second set. 第2盤她以6-0取勝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Games</b> are an organized event in which competitions in several sports take place. 運動會","examples":["...the 1996 Olympic Games at Atlanta. …1996年亞特蘭大奧林匹克運動會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>game</b> to describe a way of behaving in which a person uses a particular plan, usually in order to gain an advantage for himself or herself. 計謀","examples":["Until now, the Americans have been playing a very delicate political game. 至今美國人們還在玩弄非常微妙的政治計謀。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Wild animals or birds that are hunted for sport and sometimes cooked and eaten are referred to as <b>game</b>. 獵物","examples":["As men who shot game for food, they were natural marksmen. 作為捕捉獵物當食物的人，他們是天生的射手。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>game</b> <b>for</b> something, you are willing to do something new, unusual, or risky. 敢嘗試的","examples":["He said he's game for a similar challenge next year. 他說明年他敢嘗試一次類似的挑戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"full of fighting spirit; plucky; brave 勇敢的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to play games of chance for money, stakes, etc; gamble 賭博","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>gives the game away</b>, they reveal a secret or reveal their feelings, and this puts them at a disadvantage. 洩露秘密; 露出馬腳","examples":["The faces of the two conspirators gave the game away! 兩個同謀者的表情露出了馬腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>new to</b> a particular <b>game</b>, you have not done a particular activity or been in a particular situation before. 對…不熟悉","examples":["Don't forget that she's new to this game and will take a while to complete the task. 別忘了她對此沒有經驗，將需要一些時間來完成那項任務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you beat someone <b>at</b> their <b>own game</b>, you use the same methods that they have used, but more successfully, so that you gain an advantage over them. 將計就計戰勝某人","examples":["He must anticipate the manoeuvres of the other lawyers and beat them at their own game. 他必須對其他律師的策略有所準備，從而將計就計戰勝他們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>playing games</b> or <b>playing silly games</b>, you mean that they are not treating a situation seriously and you are annoyed with them. 敷衍","examples":["This seemed to annoy Professor Steiner. \"Don't play games with me,\" he thundered. 這似乎觸怒了斯坦納教授。“別敷衍我了，”他吼道。"]}]}]},"good-by":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"告別"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"再見"}],"sections":[]},"god":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"神；上帝，天主， 真主（God）；受崇敬的人，偶像；（某一領域的）要人，權威；至為重要的事物；<英>（劇場中的）頂層樓座（the gods）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"膜拜，崇拜"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用以表示吃驚、憤怒或悲痛等）天哪（God）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The name <b>God</b> is given to the spirit or being who is worshipped as the creator and ruler of the world, especially by Jews, Christians, and Muslims. 上帝","examples":["He believes in God. 他信奉上帝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In many religions, a <b>god</b> is one of the spirits or beings that are believed to have power over a particular part of the world or nature. 神","examples":["...Zeus, king of the gods. …宙斯，眾神之王。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is admired very much by a person or group of people, and who influences them a lot, can be referred to as a <b>god</b>. 神一般的人物","examples":["To his followers he was a god. 對他的追隨者們來說，他是個神一般的人物。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>God</b> in exclamations to emphasize something that they are saying, or to express surprise, fear, or excitement. This use could cause offence. 天哪","examples":["Oh my God, he's shot somebody. 噢，我的天哪，他向人開了槍。","Good God, it's Mr. Harper! 天哪，是哈珀先生！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>God knows</b>, <b>God only knows</b>, or <b>God alone knows</b> to emphasize that you do not know something. 天曉得 (用以強調不知情)","examples":["God alone knows what she thinks. 天曉得她想什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone says <b>God knows</b> in reply to a question, they mean that they do not know the answer. 天曉得 (用以強調不知道答案)","examples":["\"Where is he now?\"—\"God knows.\" “他現在在哪裡？”—“天曉得。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone uses expressions such as <b>what in God's name</b>, <b>why in God's name</b>, or <b>how in God's name</b>, they are emphasizing how angry, annoyed, or surprised they are. 到底 (用以強調憤怒、煩惱、吃驚的程度)","examples":["What in God's name do you expect me to do? 你到底要我做什麼？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person thinks they are <b>God's gift</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, they think they are perfect or extremely good. 上帝的恩賜","examples":["Are men God's gift to women? Some of them think they are. 男人是上帝對女人的恩賜嗎？有些男人認為他們是。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>plays God</b>, they act as if they have unlimited power and can do anything they want. 扮上帝","examples":["You have no right to play God in my life! 你無權在我的生活中扮演上帝！"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>God</b> in expressions such as <b>I hope to God</b>, or <b>I wish to God</b>, or <b>I swear to God</b>, in order to emphasize what you are saying. 對天 (希望、發誓)","examples":["I hope to God they are paying you well. 我真心希望他們給你好的報酬。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say <b>God willing</b>, you are saying that something will happen if all goes well. 天公作美","examples":["God willing, there will be a breakthrough. 天公作美的話，會有所突破。"]}]}]},"good-bye":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"告辭"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"再見"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Goodbye</b>\" to someone when you or they are leaving, or at the end of a telephone conversation. 再見","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you say your <b>goodbyes</b>, you say something such as \"Goodbye\" when you leave. 告別","examples":["He said his goodbyes knowing that a long time would pass before he would see his child again. 他道了別，清楚要過很久才能再見到他的孩子。","Perry and I exchanged goodbyes. 我和佩裡互相道了別。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>say goodbye</b> or <b>wave goodbye</b> <b>to</b> something that you want or usually have, you accept that you are not going to have it. 放棄","examples":["He has probably said goodbye to his last chance of Olympic gold. 他或許已經放棄了奪取奧運金牌的最後機會。"]}]}]},"gold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金；金幣，黃金製品；金色，金黃色；金牌；寶貴的東西，難能可貴的人；（箭術中的）靶心"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"金色的；金制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gold</b> is a valuable, yellow-coloured metal that is used for making jewellery and ornaments, and as an international currency. 黃金","examples":["...a sapphire set in gold. …一顆鑲嵌在金子裡的藍寶石。","The price of gold was going up. 黃金的價格上漲了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gold</b> is jewellery and other things that are made of gold. 金飾物; 金製品","examples":["We handed over all our gold and money. 我們把所有的金飾物和錢都交了出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>gold</b> is the same as a . 金牌","examples":["His ambition was to win gold at the Atlanta Games in 1996. 他的目標是在1996年的亞特蘭大奧運會上奪得金牌。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>gold</b> is a bright yellow colour, and is often shiny. 金色的","examples":["I'd been wearing Michel's black and gold shirt. 我一直穿著米歇爾那件黑色和金色相間的襯衫。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a child is being <b>as good as gold</b>, you are emphasizing that they are behaving very well and are not causing you any problems. (小孩) 很乖的","examples":["The boys were as good as gold on our walk. 這些小男孩兒在我們散步時很乖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>a heart of gold</b>, you are emphasizing that they are very good and kind to other people. 一顆金子般的心","examples":["They are all good boys with hearts of gold. They would never steal. 他們都是有著金子般心靈的好孩子。他們決不會偷竊。"]}]}]},"goddess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女神；極受崇敬（或敬慕）的女人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In many religions, a <b>goddess</b> is a female spirit or being that is believed to have power over a particular part of the world or nature. 女神","examples":["...Diana, the goddess of war. …戰爭女神黛安娜。"]}]}]},"grandchild":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孫輩（孫子、孫女、外孫、外孫女）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>grandchild</b> is the child of their son or daughter. 孫子; 孫女; 外孫子; 外孫女","examples":["Mary loves her grandchildren. 瑪麗很疼愛她的孫子孫女們。"]}]}]},"granddaughter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孫女，外孫女"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>granddaughter</b> is the daughter of their son or daughter. 孫女; 外孫女","examples":["...a drawing of my granddaughter Amelia. …一幅我孫女阿梅莉亞的畫像。"]}]}]},"goose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鵝；鵝肉；雌鵝；<非正式> 傻瓜；（裁縫用的）熨斗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式> 觸控（或捏）某人的臀部；<美，非正式> 推動，激勵；<非正式>開大（汽車等）的油門；<非正式>作噓噓聲反對（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>goose</b> is a large bird that has a long neck and webbed feet. Geese are often farmed for their meat. 鵝","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Goose</b> is the meat from a goose that has been cooked. (熟) 鵝肉","examples":["...roast goose. …烤鵝。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to prod (a person) playfully in the behind (開玩笑的)戳人屁股","examples":[]}]}]},"grandmother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（外）祖母，奶奶，外婆；女祖先"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>grandmother</b> is the mother of your father or mother. 祖母; 外祖母","examples":["My grandmothers are both widows. 我的祖母和外祖母都是寡婦。"]}]}]},"grandpa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>爺爺；外公"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>grandpa</b> is your grandfather. 爺爺; 外公","examples":["Grandpa was not yet back from the war. 爺爺那時還沒從戰場歸來。"]}]}]},"grandson":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孫子；外孫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>grandson</b> is the son of their son or daughter. 孫子; 外孫","examples":["My grandson's birthday was on Tuesday. 我孫子的生日是星期二。"]}]}]},"grandfather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"祖父，外祖父；始祖，鼻祖"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（法律、政策）使（現有人員、企業、安排等）不受新規定限制，對…予以豁免"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>grandfather</b> is the father of your father or mother. 祖父; 外祖父","examples":["His grandfather was a professor. 他爺爺曾是位教授。"]}]}]},"grandma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>奶奶；外婆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>grandma</b> is your grandmother. 奶奶; 外婆","examples":["Grandma was from Scotland. 奶奶來自蘇格蘭。"]}]}]},"gray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"灰色的；蒼白的；灰白頭髮的；陰鬱的；昏暗的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"灰色；暗淡的光線；戈瑞（吸收電離輻射劑量單位，符號 Gy）；（Gray）人名；（意）格拉伊；（英、法、葡、瑞典）格雷"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"成為灰色或灰白"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使成灰色或灰白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the derived SI unit of absorbed ionizing radiation dose or kerma equivalent to an absorption per unit mass of one joule per kilogram of irradiated material. 1 gray is equivalent to 100 rads 格雷; 國際單位制中吸收離子輻射量的一個單位 ( symbol: Gy)","examples":[]}]}]},"grass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"草；草地，草坪；<非正式>大麻；<英，非正式> 告密者；草地網球場；牧場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……上種草；<英，非正式>（向警方）告發；捕（魚）並帶上河岸；將（某人）撞倒；<美>給（牲畜）喂草"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grass</b> is a very common plant consisting of large numbers of thin, spiky, green leaves that cover the surface of the ground. 青草","examples":["Small things stirred in the grass around the tent. 帳篷周圍的草叢裡有小東西在動。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>the grass is greener</b> somewhere else, you mean that other people's situations always seem better or more attractive than your own, but may not really be so. 這山望著那山高","examples":["He was very happy with us but wanted to see if the grass was greener elsewhere. 他當時對我們感到很滿意，但想看看有沒有更好的。"]}]}]},"grey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"灰色的；（頭髮）灰白的，花白的；（面色）蒼白的；（天氣）昏暗的，陰沉的；單調乏味的，毫無吸引力的；陰鬱的，暗淡的；老年人的；不明確的，難以處理的；（金融或貿易活動）不在官方統計數字之內的，灰色的；<南非>（與）民族雜居區（相關）的，黑人白人雜居區的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"灰色，灰色顏料；灰色衣服；灰白頭髮；灰馬，白馬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（頭髮）變灰白，變花白；（人，群體）變老，老化；成為灰色，變得昏暗；使變成灰色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grey</b> is the colour of ashes or of clouds on a rainy day. 灰色的","examples":["...a grey suit. …一套灰色西裝。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the weather is <b>grey</b>, there are many clouds in the sky and the light is dull. (天氣) 陰沉的","examples":["It was a grey, wet, April Sunday. 那是一個陰沉、潮溼、4月裡的星期天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>grey</b>, you mean that it is dull, unpleasant, or difficult. 陰鬱的","examples":["Brazilians look gloomily forward to a New Year that even the president admits will be grey and cheerless. 巴西民眾沮喪地期待著一個連總統都承認將會是陰鬱而沉悶的新年。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>grey</b>, you think that they are boring and unattractive, and very similar to other things or other people. 無特色的","examples":["Miles is one of those little grey men you find in every company. 邁爾斯是那種你在每家公司都找得到的毫無特色的小個子男人。"]}]}]},"green":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"綠色的；青春的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"綠色；青春"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使……變綠色"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"變綠色"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Green）人名；（英、意）格林；（瑞典、芬）格倫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Green</b> is the colour of grass or leaves. 綠色的","examples":["Yellow and green together make a pale green. 黃色和綠色在一起就成了嫩綠色。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A place that is <b>green</b> is covered with grass, plants, and trees and not with houses or factories. 綠色植物覆蓋的","examples":["Every street ends at a park or bit of green space. 每條街的盡頭都是一個公園或一塊綠地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Green</b> issues and political movements relate to or are concerned with the protection of the environment. 與環保有關的","examples":["The power of the Green movement in Germany has made that country a leader in the drive to recycle more waste materials. 德國環保運動的力量已經使該國成了迴圈利用更多廢料運動中的領先者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>green</b>, you mean they harm the environment as little as possible. 環保的","examples":["...trying to persuade governments to adopt greener policies. …試圖說服政府透過更環保的政策。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>green</b>, you mean that they have had very little experience of life or a particular job. 缺乏經驗的","examples":["He was a young fellow, very green, very immature. 他是個年輕的傢伙，沒什麼經驗，很不成熟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"翠綠","examples":["...the lush greenness of the river valleys. …河谷的鬱鬱蔥蔥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"環保","examples":["If you'd like to recognize the greenness of an individual or organization, why not nominate them for an Environmental Achievement Award. 如果你想讚揚某個人或團體的綠色環保行為，何不將他們提名為環境成就獎的候選人？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Greens</b> are members of green political movements. 環保運動的成員","examples":["The Greens see themselves as a radical alternative to the two major political parties. 綠黨成員們將自己視為與兩大政黨截然不同的選擇。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>green</b> is a smooth, flat area of grass around a hole on a golf course. 果嶺 (高爾夫球場中靠近球洞的平整區域)","examples":["...the 18th green. …第18洞果嶺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>green</b> is an area of land covered with grass, especially in a town or in the middle of a village. (尤指城鎮或村莊中心的) 綠地","examples":["...the village green. …村子中心的綠地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>green fingers</b>, they are very good at gardening and their plants grow well. 高超的園藝技能","examples":["She has unbelievably green fingers, she can grow anything. 她的園藝技能相當高超，什麼都會種。"]}]}]},"good":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"優良的；能幹的，擅長的；令人愉快的，滿意的；合適的，方便的；有益的；乖的；虔誠的；健康的；善良的；正直的；相當大的，相當多的；至少；徹底的；明智的，合理的；划算的，收益可觀的；贏得讚許的，令人尊敬的；（用於表示回應）好的；表示驚訝、生氣或者加強語氣；（用於打招呼）好；有趣的；有效的；能提供……的；（踢、射、投）命中；親密的；<非正式>夠了"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"善，正義；好事；商品，所有物；<英>（運載的）貨物（goods）；優勢，利益；<非正式>真貨，正品（the goods）；好人，有道德的人（the good）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>好地；<美>徹底地，完全地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Good</b> means pleasant or enjoyable. 令人愉快的","examples":["We had a really good time together. 我們一起度過了非常愉快的時光。","I know they would have a better life here. 我知道他們在這兒會過上更好的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Good</b> means of a high quality, standard, or level. 質量高的; 水準高的","examples":["Exercise is just as important to health as good food. 鍛鍊和好的飲食對身體健康一樣重要。","His parents wanted Raymond to have the best possible education. 他的父母想讓雷蒙德儘可能得到最好的教育。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>good at</b> something, you are skilful and successful at doing it. 擅長的","examples":["He was very good at his work. 他十分擅長他的工作。","I'm not very good at singing. 我不很擅長唱歌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a piece of news, an action, or an effect as <b>good</b>, you mean that it is likely to result in benefit or success. 很可能帶來好結果的","examples":["On balance, biotechnology should be good news for developing countries. 總的來說，生物技術對發展中國家來說應該是好訊息。","I think the response was good. 我認為這樣的反應很有利。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>good</b> idea, reason, method, or decision is a sensible or valid one. 合理的; 有效的","examples":["They thought it was a good idea to make some offenders do community service. 他們認為讓一些違法者為社群服務是個合理的意見。","There is good reason to doubt this. 有正當理由懷疑這件事。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that <b>it is good</b> <b>that</b> something should happen or <b>good</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean it is desirable, acceptable, or right. 令人嚮往的; 可接受的; 對的","examples":["I think it's good that some people are going. 我認為有些人要走是件好事。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>good</b> estimate or indication of something is an accurate one. 準確的","examples":["We have a fairly good idea of what's going on. 我們對正在發生的事情有相當準確的瞭解。","This is a much better indication of what a school is really like. 這更準確地體現了學校究竟該是什麼樣子。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you get a <b>good</b> deal or a <b>good</b> price when you buy or sell something, you receive a lot in exchange for what you give. (買賣) 合算的","examples":["Whether such properties are a good deal will depend on individual situations. 這樣的房產是否買得值要視具體情況而定。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"Someone who is in a <b>good</b> mood is cheerful and pleasant to be with. 愉快的","examples":["People were in a pretty good mood. 那時人們心情很好。","He exudes natural charm and good humour. 他表現出一種與生俱來的魅力和幽默感。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If people are <b>good</b> friends, they get along well together and are very close. 親密的","examples":["She and Gavin are good friends. 她和加文是好朋友。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>good</b> to emphasize the great extent or degree of something. 十足的","examples":["We waited a good fifteen minutes. 我們足足等了15分鐘。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something is <b>good for</b> a person or organization, it benefits them. 有益的","examples":["Rain water was once considered to be good for the complexion. 雨水曾一度被認為對膚色有益。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"Someone who is <b>good</b> is morally correct in their attitudes and behaviour. 有道德的","examples":["The president is a good man. 總統是個品德高尚的人。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"Someone, especially a child, who is <b>good</b> obeys rules and instructions and behaves in a socially correct way. (尤指小孩) 聽話的","examples":["The children were very good. 孩子們很聽話。","I'm going to be a good boy now. 我現在要做一個聽話的男孩。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"Someone who is <b>good</b> is kind and thoughtful. 好心的","examples":["You are good to me. 你對我很好。","Her good intentions were thwarted almost immediately. 她的好意幾乎立即被拒絕。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>no good</b> or is <b>not any good</b>, they are not satisfactory or are of a low standard. 令人不滿意","examples":["If the weather's no good then I won't take any pictures. 如果天氣不好，我就不拍照。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is done for <b>the</b> <b>good</b> of a person or organization, it is done in order to benefit them. 利益","examples":["The president urged him to resign for the good of the country. 總統敦促他為了國家利益辭職。","Victims want to see justice done not just for themselves, but for the greater good of society. 受害者們希望看到正義得到伸張，這不僅是為了他們自己, 也是為了社會更大的利益。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that doing something is <b>no good</b> or does <b>not</b> do <b>any good</b>, you mean that doing it is not of any use or will not bring any success. 沒用處","examples":["It's no good worrying about it now. 現在擔心已沒什麼用處。","We gave them water and kept them warm, but it didn't do any good. 我們給他們水喝並讓他們保持溫暖，但都不管用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Good</b> is what is considered to be right according to moral standards or religious beliefs. 善","examples":["Good and evil may co-exist within one family. 善與惡可能共存於同一個家庭。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Good</b>\" or \"<b>Very good</b>\" to express pleasure, satisfaction, or agreement with something that has been said or done, especially when you are in a position of authority. 很好 (用於表示高興、滿意、同意)","examples":["\"Are you all right?\"—\"I'm fine.\"—\"Good. So am I.\" “你還好嗎？”—“我很好。”—“那就好。我也很好。”","Oh good, Tom's just come in. 嗯好，湯姆正好進來了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>it's a good thing</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you mean that it is fortunate. 慶幸的是","examples":["It's a good thing you aren't married. 幸好你沒有結婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>as good as new</b>, you mean that they are in a very good condition or state, especially after they have been damaged or ill. 完好如新","examples":["I only use that on special occasions, so it's as good as new. 我只在特殊場合用，所以它完好如新。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>good old</b> before the name of a person, place, or thing when you are referring to them in an affectionate way. 我親愛的 (用以稱呼某人、某地或某事物)","examples":["Good old Harry. Reliable to the end. 我親愛的哈里，一直那麼可靠。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something will <b>do</b> someone <b>good</b>, you mean that it will benefit them or improve them. 對某人有益","examples":["The outing will do me good. 這次旅行將對我有益。","It's probably done you good to get away for a few hours. 離開了幾小時也許已使你受益。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>As good as</b> can be used to mean \"almost.\" 差不多","examples":["His career is as good as over. 他的事業差不多要完了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something changes or disappears <b>for good</b>, it never changes back or comes back as it was before. 永久地","examples":["Some of the nation's manufacturing jobs may be gone for good. 該國製造產業中有些職業也許會永遠消失。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>makes good</b> a threat or promise or <b>makes good on</b> it, they do what they have threatened or promised to do. 履行 (諾言、威脅等)","examples":["He was confident the allies would make good on their pledges. 他有信心盟國將履行他們的誓言。"]}]}]},"group":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"集體，團體；組，群；集團；樂團，樂隊；空軍大隊（通常由兩個或兩個以上的基地組成）；（元素週期表中的）族；（系統語法中的）片語；原子團"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成組，聚集；將……分類"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>group</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a number of people or things that are together in one place at one time. 群","examples":["The trouble involved a small group of football fans. 那次騷亂涉及到一小撮足球迷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>group</b> is a set of people who have the same interests or aims, and who organize themselves to work or act together. 集體; 團體","examples":["Members of an environmental group are staging a protest inside a chemical plant. 一個環保團體的成員們正在一家化工廠內進行抗議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>group</b> is a set of people, organizations, or things which are considered together because they have something in common. (有共同之處的) 組","examples":["She is among the most promising players in her age group. 在她那個年齡組中她是最有前途的選手之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>group</b> is a number of separate commercial or industrial firms that all have the same owner. (企業) 集團","examples":["The group made a pretax profit of $1.05 million. 該集團賺取了105萬美元的稅前利潤。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>group</b> is a number of musicians who perform together, especially ones who play popular music. (尤指演奏流行音樂的) 樂隊","examples":["At school he played bass in a pop group called The Urge. 上學的時候他在一個叫“衝動”的流行樂隊中擔任低音電吉他手。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a number of things or people <b>are grouped together</b> or <b>group together</b>, they are together in one place or within one organization or system. 把…歸在一起; 形成一組","examples":["Plants are grouped into botanical \"families\" that have certain characteristics in common. 具有某些共同特點的植物被歸為植物學的科。","The Species Survival Network groups together 80 international environmental organizations. 物種生存網路把80個國際環境組織結合在一起。"]}]}]},"guess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猜測，估計；猜中，猜到；認為，以為"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"猜測，推測"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>guess</b> something, you give an answer or provide an opinion which may not be true because you do not have definite knowledge about the matter concerned. 猜測","examples":["Yvonne guessed that he was a very successful publisher or a banker. 伊馮娜猜測他是一位非常成功的出版商或銀行家。","You can only guess at what mental suffering they endure. 你只能猜測他們忍受著什麼樣的精神痛苦。","Guess what I did for the whole of the first week. 猜猜整個第一週我都做了些什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>guess</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you correctly form the opinion that it is the case, although you do not have definite knowledge about it. 猜中","examples":["By now you will have guessed that I'm back in Ohio. 此刻，你將已經猜出我回到了俄亥俄。","He should have guessed what would happen. 他本應該猜出將會發生什麼的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guess</b> is an attempt to give an answer or provide an opinion which may not be true because you do not have definite knowledge about the matter concerned. 猜想","examples":["My guess is that the chance that these vaccines will work is zero. 我的猜想是這些疫苗將起作用的可能性為零。","He'd taken her pulse and made a guess at her blood pressure. 他為她把了脈，對她的血壓做了估量。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>anyone's guess</b> or <b>anybody's guess</b>, you mean that no one can be certain about what is really true. 誰也拿不準的事","examples":["Just when this will happen is anyone's guess. 誰也拿不準這件事什麼時候會發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>at a guess</b> to indicate that what you are saying is only an estimate or what you believe to be true, rather than being a definite fact. 憑猜測","examples":["At a guess he's been dead for two days. 據猜測，他已經死了兩天了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>I guess</b> to show that you are slightly uncertain or reluctant about what you are saying. 我想","examples":["I guess he's right. 我想他是對的。","\"I think you're being paranoid.\"—\"Yeah. I guess so.\" “我認為你是多疑了。” — “是的，我想是的。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>keeps</b> you <b>guessing</b>, they do not tell you what you want to know. 使某人猜不透","examples":["The author's intention is to keep everyone guessing until the bitter end. 這位作者的意圖是在最終結尾前讓所有人都猜不透。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>guess what</b> to draw attention to something exciting, surprising, or interesting that you are about to say. 想不到吧","examples":["Guess what, I just got my first part in a film. 想不到吧，我剛得到我的第一個電影角色。"]}]}]},"guest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"客人；特邀嘉賓，客串演員；顧客，房客；寄居昆蟲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做特邀嘉賓，客串"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guest</b> is someone who is visiting you or is at an event because you have invited them. 客人","examples":["She was a guest at the wedding. 她是參加婚禮的客人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>guest</b> is someone who visits a place or organization or appears on a radio or television show because they have been invited to do so. 特邀嘉賓","examples":["...a frequent talk show guest. …一位經常參加訪談節目的特邀嘉賓。","Dr. Gerald Jeffers is the guest speaker. 傑拉爾德·傑弗斯博士是特邀演講人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>guest</b> is someone who is staying in a hotel. (旅館的) 客人","examples":["I was the only hotel guest. 我是旅館的惟一客人。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>be my guest</b> to someone, you are giving them permission to do something. 請便","examples":["If anybody wants to work on this, be my guest. 如果有人想做這件事的話，請便吧。"]}]}]},"great":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偉大的，著名的；大型的，巨大的；（數量或程度）極大的，很大的；美妙的；身心健康的，精力充沛的；重要的，重大的；熱心的，熱衷的；和藹的，隨和的；（外）曾祖（或曾孫）的；<愛爾蘭>（二人）親近的，親密的；擅長……的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很好地，很棒地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"偉人，偉大的事物；金曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>great</b> to describe something that is very large. <b>Great</b> is more formal than <b>big</b>. 大型的","examples":["The room had a great bay window. 這個房間有個巨大的凸窗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Great</b> means large in amount or degree. (數量或程度) 大的","examples":["Benjamin Britten did not live to a great age. 本傑明•布里滕沒有活到很大的歲數。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>great</b> to describe something that is important, famous, or exciting. 重大的","examples":["...the great cultural achievements of the past. …過去重大的文化成就。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe someone who is successful and famous for their actions, knowledge, or skill as <b>great</b>. 偉大的","examples":["He has the potential to be a great player. 他有潛力成為一位傑出的演員。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>great</b>, you approve of them or admire them. 極好的","examples":["Arturo has this great place in Cozumel. 阿圖羅在科蘇梅爾有這樣一個很不錯的住所。","They're a great bunch of guys. 他們是一群很棒的小夥子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>feel great</b>, you feel very healthy, energetic, and enthusiastic. 精力充沛的","examples":["I feel just great. 我感覺好極了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>great</b> in order to emphasize the size or degree of a characteristic or quality. 十足的","examples":["...a great big Italian wedding. …一場盛大的義大利式婚禮。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"重大","examples":["A nation must take certain risks to achieve greatness. 一個國家必須冒一定風險來成就偉大的事業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"偉大","examples":["Abraham Lincoln achieved greatness. 亞伯拉罕•林肯取得了偉大功績。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>greats</b> in a particular subject or field of activity are the people who have been most successful or famous in it. 大人物","examples":["...all the greats of Hollywood. …所有的好萊塢名人。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>great</b> in order to emphasize that you are pleased or enthusiastic about something. 美妙的; 很棒的","examples":["Oh great! That'll be good for Fred. 噢，太棒了！那對弗雷德將會很有利。"]}]}]},"haircut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"理髮；髮型；（金融）估值折扣，扣減額"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get a <b>haircut</b>, someone cuts your hair for you. 理髮","examples":["Your hair is all right; it's just that you need a haircut. 你的頭髮沒問題，只是你需要理個髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>haircut</b> is the style in which your hair has been cut. 髮型","examples":["Who's that guy with the funny haircut? 那個髮型古怪的傢伙是誰？"]}]}]},"guide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"帶領，引導（某人至某地）；任嚮導；指導，影響；解釋，闡明"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"指南，手冊；導遊，嚮導；準則，指標；女童子軍，女童子軍成員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guide</b> is a book that gives you information or instructions to help you do or understand something. 指南","examples":["Our 10-page guide will help you to change your life for the better. 我們這本10頁的指南將會幫助改善你們的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>guide</b> is a book that gives tourists information about a town, area, or country. 旅行指南","examples":["The Rough Guide to Paris lists accommodations for as little as $35 a night. 《巴黎旅遊簡明指南》列出了價格低至每晚$35的住宿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>guide</b> is someone who shows tourists around places such as museums or cities. 導遊","examples":["We've arranged a walking tour of the city with your guide. 我們已經和你的導遊安排了一個城市步行遊覽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>guide</b> is someone who shows people the way to a place in a difficult or dangerous region. 嚮導","examples":["The mountain people say that, with guides, the journey can be done in fourteen days. 山裡人說，有嚮導的話，這趟旅行可以在14天內完成。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>guide</b> is something that can be used to help you plan your actions or to form an opinion about something. 指導原則","examples":["As a rough guide, a horse needs 2.5 percent of its body weight in food every day. 作為一個大致的標準，一匹馬每天需要相當於它體重2.5%的食物。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>guide</b> someone around a city, museum, or building, you show it to them and explain points of interest. 給…導遊","examples":["...a young Egyptologist who guided us through tombs and temples with enthusiasm. …一位熱心地領著我們參觀陵墓和寺廟的年輕的埃及學家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>guide</b> someone somewhere, you go there with them in order to show them the way. 給…領路","examples":["He took the bewildered Elliott by the arm and guided him out. 他挽著暈頭轉向的埃利奧特的手臂，領著他出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>guide</b> a vehicle somewhere, you control it carefully to make sure that it goes in the right direction. 駕駛 (車輛等)","examples":["Captain Shelton guided his plane down the runway and took off. 謝爾頓機長駕駛飛機沿著跑道滑行起飛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>guides</b> you somewhere, it gives you the information you need in order to go in the right direction. 給…指明方向","examples":["They sailed across the Caribbean with only a compass to guide them. 他們僅靠一隻指南針來指引他們駛過了加勒比海。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something or someone <b>guides</b> you, they influence your actions or decisions. 指導…的行動; 影響…的決定","examples":["He should have let his instinct guide him. 他本該讓直覺指導他的行動。","Development has been guided by a concern for the ecology of the area. 關注本地區的生態狀況一直是發展的指導原則。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>guide</b> someone through something that is difficult to understand or to achieve, you help them to understand it or to achieve success in it. 指導","examples":["Gym owner David Barton will guide them through a workout. 健身房主人戴維•巴頓將指導他們完成鍛鍊。"]}]}]},"ground":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地，地面；土地，土壤；（某種用途的）場地；充分的理由，根據；話題，知識領域；觀點，立場；優勢，有利條件；地線；庭院，花園；渣滓；（繪畫或印刷的）背景，底子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以……為根據；（在某學科上）給……以紮實的基礎教育；使停飛；禁足；（使）擱淺；落地，著陸；把……放在地上，以……觸地；把（電器）接地；（擊球員）擊出內場地滾球被殺出局"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"切碎的，磨碎的；（航空用語）地面的，地勤的；打磨成的，磨光的；生活於地面、地下或水底的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"研磨（grind 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The ground</b> is the surface of the earth. 地面","examples":["Forty or fifty women were sitting cross-legged on the ground. 四五十個婦女正盤腿坐在地上。","We slid down the roof and dropped to the ground. 我們從屋頂滑下來，掉到地上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something takes place <b>on the</b> <b>ground</b>, you mean it takes place on the surface of the earth and not in the air.  在地面上","examples":["Coordinating airline traffic on the ground is as complicated as managing the traffic in the air. 協調飛機在地面上的交通和掌控空中交通一樣複雜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>ground</b> is the soil and rock on the earth's surface. 地面土壤和石頭","examples":["The ground had eroded. 地表已遭腐蝕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to land as <b>ground</b>, especially when it has very few buildings or when it is considered to be special in some way.  土地","examples":["...a stretch of waste ground. …一大片荒地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>ground</b> to refer to an area of land, sea, or air which is used for a particular activity.  場地","examples":["The best fishing grounds are around the islands. 最好的漁場是在島嶼周圍。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>grounds</b> of a large or important building are the garden or area of land which surrounds it.  庭院","examples":["...the palace grounds. …皇家庭院。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>ground</b> to refer to a place or situation in which particular methods or ideas can develop and be successful.  地方; 環境","examples":["The company has maintained its reputation as the developing ground for new techniques. 該公司仍保持著新技術研發地的聲譽。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>ground</b> in expressions such as <b>on shaky ground</b> and <b>the same ground</b> to refer to a particular subject, area of experience, or basis for an argument. 依據","examples":["Sensing she was on shaky ground, Marie changed the subject. 感覺自己的根據站不住腳，瑪麗於是轉變了話題。","This is the most solid ground for optimism. 這是樂觀主義最有力的根據。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Ground</b> is used in expressions such as <b>gain ground</b>, <b>lose ground</b>, and <b>give ground</b> in order to indicate that someone gets or loses an advantage. 優勢","examples":["There are signs that the party is gaining ground in the latest polls. 有跡象表明該黨在最近的民意測驗中正逐漸領先。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something is <b>grounds for</b> a feeling or action, it is a reason for it. If you do something <b>on the grounds</b> of a particular thing, that thing is the reason for your action. 理由","examples":["In the interview he gave some grounds for optimism. 採訪中他給出了一些樂觀的理由。","The court overturned that decision on the grounds that the prosecution had withheld crucial evidence. 法庭以起訴方拒絕出示關鍵證據為由推翻了那個判決。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"The <b>ground</b> in an electric plug or piece of electrical equipment is the same as the . 地線","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>below ground</b> is under the Earth's surface or under a building. Something that is <b>above ground</b> is on top of the earth's surface. 在地面上/在地面下","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>break new ground</b>, you do something completely different or you do something in a completely different way. 開闢新天地","examples":["Gellhorn may have broken new ground when she filed her first report on the Spanish Civil War. 當蓋爾霍恩把她關於西班牙內戰的第一份報道傳送出去時，她也許已經開闢了新天地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a town or building <b>is burned to the ground</b> or <b>is razed to the ground</b>, you are emphasizing that it has been completely destroyed by fire. 燒為平地","examples":["The town was razed to the ground after the French Revolution. 該鎮在法國大革命後被大火夷為平地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If two people or groups find <b>common ground</b>, they agree about something, especially when they do not agree about other things. 共同立場","examples":["The participants seem unable to find common ground on the issue of agriculture. 這些參與者似乎無法就農業議題達成共識。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>middle ground</b> between two groups, ideas, or plans involves things which do not belong to either of these groups, ideas, or plans but have elements of each, often in a less extreme form. 中間立場","examples":["The sooner we find a middle ground between freedom of speech and protection of the young, the better for everyone. 我們越早在言論自由和保護青年之間找到一箇中間點，對大家就越好。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something such as a project gets <b>off the ground</b>, it begins or starts functioning. 開始","examples":["We help small companies to get off the ground. 我們幫助小公司運作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>prepare the ground</b> <b>for</b> a future event, course of action, or development, you make it easier for it to happen. 打下基礎","examples":["...a political initiative which would prepare the ground for war. …一個為戰爭埋下伏筆的政治倡議。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>shift</b> your <b>ground</b> or <b>change</b> your <b>ground</b>, you change the basis on which you are arguing. 改變立場","examples":["Robert considered this, then shifted his ground slightly in line with a new thought. 羅伯特對此進行了考慮，然後為跟新想法保持一致，稍微改變了立場。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>stand</b> your <b>ground</b> or <b>hold</b> your <b>ground</b>, you do not run away from a situation, but face it bravely. 不退卻","examples":["She had to force herself to stand her ground when she heard someone approaching. 聽到有人走近時，她得強迫自己不要退卻。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an argument, belief, or opinion <b>is grounded</b> in something, that thing is used to justify it. 以…為根據","examples":["Her argument was grounded in fact. 她的論述以事實為根據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an aircraft or its passengers <b>are grounded</b>, they are made to stay on the ground and are not allowed to take off. 使停飛","examples":["The civil aviation minister ordered all the planes to be grounded. 該民航部長命令所有飛機不得起飛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When parents <b>ground</b> a child, they forbid them to go out and enjoy themselves for a period of time, as a punishment. 限制外出","examples":["They grounded him for a month, and banned television. 他們罰他一個月不能外出，並且不能看電視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a ship or boat <b>is grounded</b> or if it <b>grounds</b>, it touches the bottom of the sea, lake, or river it is on, and is unable to move off. 使擱淺; 擱淺","examples":["Residents have been told to stay away from the region where the ship was grounded. 居民們被告知要遠離輪船擱淺的區域。","The boat finally grounded on a soft, underwater bank. 那條船最終在一個鬆軟的水下淺灘擱淺了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>grounds</b> you, it causes you to have a sensible and practical attitude toward life and not to have unrealistic ideas. 使變得現實","examples":["These things have grounded me and made me who I am. 這些事使我變得很實際，造就了現在的我。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"現實的","examples":["She seems very grounded and down-to-earth. 她看上去非常現實，注重實際。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ground</b> meat has been cut into very small pieces in a machine. 切碎的","examples":["...The sausages are made of coarsely ground pork. …這些香腸是用切得很粗的豬肉做的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"having the surface finished, thickness reduced, or an edge sharpened by grinding 磨光的; 磨薄的; 開刃的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ground</b> is the past tense and past participle of . (grind)過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]}]},"gun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"槍，炮；起跑訊號，發令槍聲；<美，非正式>僱用殺手，持槍歹徒；噴射器；<英>獵人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加大……的油門，使加速；<美> 猛投，猛擲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gun</b> is a weapon from which bullets or other things are fired. 槍","examples":["He fled, pointing the gun at officers as they chased him. 他一邊逃跑，一邊用槍對準追他的警察。","He just seemed like a normal military guy who liked guns. 他看上去就好像一個喜歡槍的普通軍人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gun</b> or a <b>starting gun</b> is an object like a gun that is used to make a noise to signal the start of a race. 發令槍","examples":["The starting gun blasted and they were off. 發令槍一響，他們跑了出去。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>gun</b> an engine or a vehicle means to make it start or go faster by pressing on the accelerator pedal. 把…發動起來; 給…加大油門","examples":["He gunned his engine and drove off. 他把引擎發動起來，開車走了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you come out <b>with guns blazing</b> or <b>with all guns blazing</b>, you put all your effort and energy into trying to achieve something. 奮力","examples":["The company came out with guns blazing. 這家公司盡了全力，大幹了一場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>jump the gun</b>, you do something before everyone else or before the proper or right time. 過早行動","examples":["It wasn't due to be released until September 10, but some booksellers have jumped the gun and decided to sell it early. 應該到9月10日才發行的，但一些書商已搶先行動，決定提早銷售。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stick to</b> your <b>guns</b>, you continue to have your own opinion about something even though other people are trying to tell you that you are wrong. 固執己見","examples":["He should have stuck to his guns and refused to meet her. 他本該堅持立場，拒絕見她。"]}]}]},"hair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毛髮，（尤指）頭髮；些微；（植物葉莖上的）茸毛"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"有……毛髮（或頭髮）的 (-haired)"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>hair</b> is the fine threads that grow in a mass on your head. 頭髮","examples":["I wash my hair every night. 我每晚洗頭髮。","I get some grey hairs but I pull them out. 我長了幾根白頭髮，但我把它們拔掉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hair</b> is the short, fine threads that grow on different parts of your body. 汗毛","examples":["The majority of men have hair on their chest. 大多數男人長有胸毛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hair</b> is the threads that cover the body of an animal such as a dog, or make up a horse's mane and tail. (動物的) 毛","examples":["I am allergic to cat hair. 我對貓毛過敏。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>let</b> your <b>hair down</b>, you relax completely and enjoy yourself. 徹底放鬆","examples":["...the world-famous Oktoberfest, a time when everyone in Munich really lets their hair down. …世界著名的啤酒節，一個讓身在慕尼黑的每個人徹底放鬆的節日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>makes</b> your <b>hair stand on end</b> shocks or frightens you very much. 使毛骨悚然","examples":["This was the kind of smile that made your hair stand on end. 這是那種使你毛骨悚然的微笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>not a hair out of place</b>, you are emphasizing that they are extremely neat and well dressed. 衣冠楚楚","examples":["She had a lot of makeup on and not a hair out of place. 她濃妝豔抹，衣冠楚楚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is splitting hairs</b>, you mean that they are making unnecessary distinctions between things when the differences between them are so small they are not important. 做不必要的過細區分","examples":["Don't split hairs. You know what I'm getting at. 不要鑽牛角尖。你知道我是什麼意思。"]}]}]},"ham":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火腿；蹩腳演員；無線通訊愛好者；（人的）大腿後部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"過火地表演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ham</b> is meat from the top of the back leg of a pig, specially treated so that it can be kept for a long period of time. 火腿","examples":["...ham sandwiches. …火腿三明治。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the part of the hindquarters of a pig or similar animal between the hock and the hip (豬及其他動物的)後腿肉","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an actor who overacts or relies on stock gestures or mannerisms 表演過火的演員","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"overacting or clumsy acting 過火的表演; 拙劣的表演","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(<b>as modifier</b>) 表演過火的; 表演拙劣的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to overact 過火地表演","examples":[]}]}]},"hat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（常指帶簷的）帽子；（雙重的）職位，角色"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……戴上帽子；供應帽子，製造帽子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hat</b> is a head covering, often with a brim around it, which is usually worn outdoors to give protection from the weather. (常指有簷的) 帽子","examples":["...a plump woman in a red hat. …一個戴紅帽子的豐滿女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is wearing a particular <b>hat</b>, you mean that they are performing a particular role at that time. If you say that they wear several <b>hats</b>, you mean that they have several roles or jobs. 角色; 職位","examples":["Now I'll take off my \"friend hat\" and put on my \"therapist hat.\" 現在我將從朋友的角色轉為治療專家的角色。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are ready to do something <b>at the drop of a hat</b>, you mean that you are willing to do it immediately, without hesitating. 立刻","examples":["India is one part of the world I would go to at the drop of a hat. 印度是世界上我即刻就想去的一個地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>keep</b> a piece of information <b>under</b> their <b>hat</b>, you are asking them not to tell anyone else about it. 保守秘密","examples":["Look, if I tell you something, will you promise to keep it under your hat? 喂，如果我告訴你什麼事情，你能答應保守秘密嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>take</b> your <b>hat off to</b> someone, you mean that you admire them for something that they have done. 讚賞","examples":["I take my hat off to Mr. Clarke for taking this action. 我很讚賞克拉克先生採取了這樣的行動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>pull</b> something <b>out of</b> <b>the</b> <b>hat</b> means to do something unexpected which helps you to succeed, often when you are failing. 出乎意料地獲取","examples":["There are expectations that he'll pull a cease-fire out of a hat. 人們期望他會意外地消弭戰火。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In competitions, if you say that the winners will be drawn or picked <b>out of the hat</b>, you mean that they will be chosen randomly, so everyone has an equal chance of winning. 任意抽取","examples":["The first 10 correct entries drawn out of the hat will win a pair of tickets, worth $30 each. 任意抽取的前10名符合要求的入圍者將贏得兩張入場券，每張價值$30。"]}]}]},"half":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一半，二分之一；半場，半局；（足球、橄欖球等的）中場隊員；<英，非正式>半品脫；<英，非正式>兒童半票；<英>半學年，一學期；（高爾夫）一穴擊球得分與對手相等"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"一半；（時間）……點半（=half past）；大量，許多"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"一半"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一半的；不完整的，部分的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一半地，接近一半地；部分地，不完全地；極其，非常（強調情況很糟）；一半……血統地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"fraction.","pos_name":"分數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Half</b> <b>of</b> a number, an amount, or an object is one of two equal parts that together make up the whole number, amount, or object. 一半","examples":["She wore a diamond ring worth half a million dollars. 她戴了一枚價值50萬美元的鑽戒。","More than half of all U.S. households are heated with natural gas. 超過半數的美國家庭用天然氣供暖。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Half</b> is also a predeterminer. 半","examples":["We just sat and talked for half an hour or so. 我們只是坐著談了半小時左右。","They had only received half the money promised. 他們只收到了一半當初承諾的錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Half</b> can also be used in this way with a noun referring to a long period of time or a large quantity. 半…的","examples":["I thought about you half the night. 我想了你半夜。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Half</b> is also an adjective. 一半的","examples":["...a half measure of fresh lemon juice. …半量杯的新鮮檸檬汁。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>half</b> to say that something is only partly the case or happens to only a limited extent. 部分地; 有點兒","examples":["His eyes were half closed. 他的雙眼半閉著。","His refrigerator frequently looked half empty. 他的冰箱經常看上去有點兒空。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>half</b> to say that someone has parents of different nationalities. For example, if you are <b>half</b> German, one of your parents is German but the other is not. 一半…血統地","examples":["She was half Italian and half English. 她是一半義大利一半英國血統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>half</b> before an adjective describing an extreme quality, as a way of emphasizing and exaggerating something. 半…的","examples":["He felt half dead with tiredness. 他感覺累得半死。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>not half</b> to emphasize a negative quality that someone has. 一點兒也不","examples":["You're not half the man you think you are. 你一點兒也不是你自認為的那種男人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In games such as football, American football, rugby, and basketball, games are divided into two equal periods of time which are called <b>halves</b>. (球賽的) 半場","examples":["The only goal was scored by Jakobsen early in the second half. 這惟一的進球是雅各布森在下半場開始不久打進的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>half past</b> to refer to a time that is thirty minutes after a particular hour. …點半","examples":["\"What time were you planning lunch?\"—\"Half past twelve, if that's convenient.\" “你打算什麼時間吃午飯？”—“12:30，如果方便的話。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people <b>go halves</b>, they divide the cost of something equally between them. 分攤費用","examples":["She went halves on gas. 她分攤了煤氣費用。"]}]}]},"health":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"身體狀況；健康；醫療，衛生；（組織或系統的）執行狀況，運作狀況；發達，興旺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>health</b> is the condition of their body and the extent to which it is free from illness or is able to resist illness. 健康狀況","examples":["Tea contains caffeine. It's bad for your health. 茶含有咖啡因，對你的健康不利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Health</b> is a state in which a person is not suffering from any illness and is feeling well. 健康","examples":["In the hospital they nursed me back to health. 在醫院裡他們精心照料我，使我恢復了健康。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>health</b> of something such as an organization or a system is its success and the fact that it is working well. 興旺","examples":["There's no way to predict the future health of the banking industry. 根本無法預測銀行業將來的興旺。"]}]}]},"go":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"去，走；（尤指與某人）去（某處或出席某項活動）；可能要，打算做；移動，行走；在移動中做；做某個動作；離開；（為某目的）去（某處）；去做（某事）；被髮送，被傳遞；參加（電視或電臺節目）；通向，延伸到；上升；放在（通常的位置上）；放得進，適合；相配，協調；除盡，除；進行，進展；被接受，被允許；開始做（某事），進入（某種狀態）；變為，變得（尤指朝壞的方面）；處於（尤指令人不快的狀況）；（故事、歌詞等）內容是；發出（某種聲音）；發出訊號（或警告）；<非正式>說；開始（活動）；<非正式>走開，滾開；參與（表示對所提到行為不贊成）；運轉，工作；停止正常運轉；消失，不見；得辭掉，被扔掉；（官能）衰退，下降；死亡；用掉，花掉；賣掉，歸於；出價購買；促成，顯示；流逝，消逝；繼續，持續；<非正式>上廁所；（某人的話）算數；（決定、判決等）對…...不利；取得（某成績、比分等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（遊戲或活動中）輪到的機會；嘗試；<英>精力，活力；<美>某事順利進行；圍棋"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>執行正常的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>go</b> somewhere, you move or travel there. 去; 行進","examples":["We went to Rome. 我們去了羅馬。","I went home for the weekend. 我回家過週末了。","It took us an hour to go three miles. 行進3英里花了我們1小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>go</b> to say that someone leaves the place where they are and does an activity, often a leisure activity. 去 (從事某活動)","examples":["We went swimming very early. 我們很早就去游泳了。","Maybe they've just gone shopping. 或許他們剛剛去買東西了。","He went for a walk. 他去散步了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>go</b> do something, you move to a place in order to do it and you do it. You can also <b>go and</b> do something, but you always say that someone <b>went and</b> did something. 去 (做某事)","examples":["I have to go see the doctor. 我得去看醫生。","I finished my beer, then went and got another. 我喝完了自己的啤酒，然後又去拿了一瓶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>go</b> to introduce something you are quoting. For example, you say <b>the story goes</b> or <b>the argument goes</b> just before you quote all or part of it. (故事、理由) 是","examples":["The story goes that she went home with him that night. 據說那天晚上她和他一起回的家。","The story goes like this. 故事是這樣的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>go</b> when indicating that something makes or produces a sound. For example, if you say that something <b>goes</b> \"<b>bang</b>,\" you mean it produces the sound \"bang.\" 發出 (某種聲音)","examples":["She stopped in front of a painting of a dog and she started going \"woof woof.\" 她在一幅狗的畫像跟前停下，開始“汪汪”叫起來了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>go</b> instead of \"say\" when you are quoting what someone has said or what you think they will say. 說 (用於引出某人所說的話)","examples":["He goes to me: \"Oh, what do you want?\" 他對我說：“噢，你要什麼？”"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>go</b>, you leave the place where you are. 離開","examples":["Let's go. 我們走吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>go to</b> school, work, or church, you attend it regularly as part of your normal life. (經常性地) 去 (上學、上班或去教堂等)","examples":["She will have to go to school. 她將不得不去上學。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you say where a road or path <b>goes</b>, you are saying where it begins or ends, or what places it is in. (道路) 通向","examples":["There's a mountain road that goes from Blairstown to Millbrook Village. 有一條從布萊爾斯敦通向米爾布魯克村的山路。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>go</b> with words like \"further\" and \"beyond\" to show the degree or extent of something. 與\"further\"和\"beyond\"等詞連用，表示程度","examples":["The governor went further by agreeing that all policy announcements should be made first in the House. 該州長進一步同意所有政策的宣佈都應首先在議院進行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a period of time <b>goes</b> quickly or slowly, you mean that it seems to pass quickly or slowly. (時間) 流逝","examples":["The weeks go so quickly! 一週周過得真快！"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say where money <b>goes</b>, you are saying what it is spent on. (錢) 花費在","examples":["Most of my money goes toward bills. 我的錢大多花在支付各種賬單上。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something <b>goes to</b> someone, you mean that it is given to them. 被給予","examples":["A lot of credit must go to the chairman and his father. 很多讚譽必須給予主席和他的父親。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone <b>goes on</b> television or radio, they take part in a television or radio programme. 出現 (在電視或電臺上)","examples":["The president has gone on television to defend stringent new security measures. 該總統在電視上為嚴格的新安全措施進行了辯護。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something <b>goes</b>, someone gets rid of it. 失去","examples":["Exactly how many jobs will go remains unclear. 具體要失去多少個職位尚不清楚。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>goes</b>, they leave their job, usually because they are forced to. (常指被迫) 離職","examples":["He had made a humiliating tactical error and he had to go. 他犯下了一個令他恥辱的戰術錯誤，被迫離職。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something <b>goes into</b> something else, it is put in it as one of the parts or elements that form it. 加入","examples":["...the really interesting ingredients that go into the dishes that we all love to eat. …我們都喜歡吃的菜餚中所加入的真正有意思的配料。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something <b>goes</b> in a particular place, it belongs there or should be put there, because that is where you normally keep it. (正常) 應置放於","examples":["The shoes go on the shoe shelf. 鞋子應該放在鞋架上。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that one number <b>goes into</b> another number a particular number of times, you are dividing the second number by the first. 除","examples":["Six goes into thirty five times. 6除30得5。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If one of a person's senses, such as their sight or hearing, <b>is going</b>, it is getting weak and they may soon lose it completely. (官能) 衰退","examples":["His eyes are going; he says he has glaucoma. 他的視力在衰退；他說他得了青光眼。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something such as a light bulb or a part of an engine <b>is going</b>, it is no longer working properly and will soon need to be replaced. (燈泡、引擎等) 不再正常工作","examples":["I thought it looked as though the battery was going. 我看像是電池不行了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>go</b> to talk about the way something happens. For example, if an event or situation <b>goes well</b>, it is successful. 進展","examples":["She says everything is going smoothly. 她說一切進展順利。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If a machine or device <b>is going</b>, it is working. 運轉","examples":["What about my copier? Can you get it going again? 我的影印機呢？你能讓它重新運轉起來嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>go</b> to say that a person or thing changes to another state or condition. For example, if someone <b>goes crazy</b>, they become crazy, and if something <b>goes bad</b>, it deteriorates. 變得","examples":["I'm going bald. 我在脫髮。","Sometimes food goes bad, but people don't know it, so they eat it anyway and then they get sick. 有時食物變質了人們卻不知道，所以還是食用了它，結果就病了。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>goes with</b> something else, or if two things <b>go together</b>, they look or taste good together. (與…) 相配","examples":["I was searching for a pair of grey gloves to go with my new gown. 我在找一副灰色手套來配我的新禮服。","I can see that some colours go together and some don't. 我能看出有些顏色相配而有些則不配。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>go</b> is an attempt at doing something. 嘗試","examples":["I always wanted to have a go at football. 我一直都想嘗試踢足球。","She won on her first go. 她第一次嘗試就贏了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is your <b>go</b> in a game, it is your turn to do something, for example to play a card or move a piece. (出牌或下棋的) 輪次","examples":["Now whose go is it? 現在該誰了？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a game for two players in which stones are placed on a board marked with a grid, the object being to capture territory on the board 圍棋","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>as</b> you <b>go along</b>, you do it while you are doing another thing, without preparing it beforehand. (隨做其它事而) 做某事","examples":["Learning how to become a parent takes time. It's a skill you learn as you go along. 學會為人父母需要時間，這是一種在實踐中學習的技能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is</b> <b>making a go of</b> something such as a business or relationship, you mean that they are having some success with it. 在…方面獲得成功","examples":["I knew we could make a go of it and be happy. 我知道我們能做成這件事而且會很開心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is always <b>on the go</b>, you mean that they are always busy and active. 忙碌","examples":["I got a new job this year where I am on the go all the time. 我今年有了份新工作，一直在忙碌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that there are a particular number of things <b>to go</b>, you mean that they still remain to be dealt with. 要做的 (事情)","examples":["I still had another five operations to go. 我還有另外五個手術要做。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that there is a certain amount of time <b>to go</b>, you mean that there is that amount of time left before something happens or ends. 剩餘的 (時間)","examples":["There is a week to go until the elections. 還有1周才到選舉時間。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are in a café or restaurant and ask for an item of food <b>to go</b>, you mean that you want to take it with you and not eat it there. 外賣的 (食物)","examples":["... large fries to go. …大份外賣炸薯條。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone says \"<b>Where do we go from here?</b>\" they are asking what should be done next, usually because a problem has not been solved in a satisfactory way. 我們下一步該怎麼辦？","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"functioning properly and ready for action: esp used in astronautics 尤指航天器械執行正常可隨時啟動的","examples":[]}]}]},"hello":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"喂，你好（用於問候或打招呼）；喂，你好（打電話時的招呼語）；喂，你好（引起別人注意的招呼語）；<非正式>喂，嘿 (認為別人說了蠢話或分心)；<英，舊>嘿（表示驚訝）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"招呼，問候；（Hello）（法、印、美、俄）埃洛（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"說（或大聲說）“喂”；打招呼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Hello</b>\" to someone when you meet them. 你好 (打招呼用語)","examples":["Hello, Trish. I won't shake hands, because I'm filthy. 你好，特里斯。我就不握手了，我的手好髒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>Hello</b>\" to someone at the beginning of a telephone conversation, either when you answer the phone or before you give your name or say why you are phoning. 喂 (打電話時的招呼語)","examples":["A moment later, Cohen picked up the phone. \"Hello?\" 一會兒之後，科恩拿起電話。“喂？”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can call \"<b>hello</b>\" to attract someone's attention. 喂 (用於喚起別人注意)","examples":["Very softly, she called out: \"Hello? Who's there?\" 她很輕柔地喊道：“喂？誰在那兒？”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hello</b> is also a noun. 招呼","examples":["The salesperson greeted me with a warm hello. 那位推銷員向我打了個熱情的招呼。"]}]}]},"hate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"厭惡，不喜歡；仇恨，憎恨；（表示不願說某事，或客氣地請求）不願，不想"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"憎惡，憎恨；<非正式>所憎惡的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hate</b> someone or something, you have an extremely strong feeling of dislike for them. 仇恨","examples":["Most people hate him, but they don't dare to say so, because he still rules the country. 大部分人都恨他只是不敢說出來，因為他仍統治著國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>hate</b> something such as a particular activity, you mean that you find it very unpleasant. 討厭","examples":["Ted hated parties, even gatherings of people he liked individually. 特德討厭聚會，即便是聚會上的每一個人他都喜歡。","He hates to be interrupted during training. 他討厭訓練中被打斷。","He hated coming home to the empty house. 他討厭回到空無一人的家裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>hate</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I hate to trouble you</b>\" or \"<b>I hate to bother you</b>\" when you are apologizing to someone for interrupting them or asking them to do something. 不想","examples":["I hate to rush you but I have another appointment later on. 我真不想催你，但我稍後還有一個約會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>hate</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I hate to say it</b>\" or \"<b>I hate to tell you</b>\" when you want to express regret about what you are about to say, because you think it is unpleasant or should not be the case. 遺憾","examples":["I hate to tell you this, but tomorrow's your last day. 我對告訴你這個很遺憾，但明天是你最後一天了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>hate</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I hate to see</b>\" or \"<b>I hate to think</b>\" when you are emphasizing that you find a situation or an idea unpleasant. 不願","examples":["I just hate to see you doing this to yourself. 我只是不願看到你這樣對待自己。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>hate</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I'd hate to think</b>\" when you hope that something is not true or that something will not happen. 不希望","examples":["I'd hate to think my job would not be secure if I left it temporarily. 我不希望一旦我暫時離開，這份工作就不保。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hate</b> is also a noun. 仇恨","examples":["I was 17 and filled with a lot of hate. 我那時17歲，滿腔仇恨。"]}]}]},"heat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熱能，熱量；炎熱，高溫；（做飯的）熱源，熱度；辣味；憤怒，激動；壓力，逼迫；暖氣；預賽；（尤指在熔爐中熔鍊金屬時的）單次熔鍊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>激起，使激動；加熱，使變暖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>heat</b> something, you raise its temperature, for example, by using a flame or a special piece of equipment. 加熱","examples":["Meanwhile, heat the tomatoes and oil in a pan. 與此同時，將西紅柿和油放在平底鍋里加熱。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heat</b> is warmth or the quality of being hot. 熱","examples":["The seas store heat and release it gradually during cold periods. 海洋儲存熱量，並在寒冷季節裡逐漸將其釋放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>heat</b> is very hot weather. 高溫天氣","examples":["As an asthmatic, he cannot cope with the heat and humidity. 身為氣喘病患者，他受不了炎熱與潮溼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>heat</b> of something is the temperature of something that is warm or that is being heated. 熱度","examples":["Adjust the heat of the barbecue by opening and closing the air vents. 透過開關氣閥來調節燒烤架的熱度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>heat</b> to refer to a source of heat, for example a burner on a stove or the heating system of a house. 熱源","examples":["Immediately remove the pan from the heat. 立即將平底鍋從熱源上移開。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>heat</b> to refer to a state of strong emotion, especially of anger or excitement. 激動狀態","examples":["It was all done in the heat of the moment and I have certainly learned by my mistake. 所有這一切都是在一時衝動下乾的，我當然已經從我的過失中吸取了教訓。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The heat of</b> a particular activity is the point when there is the greatest activity or excitement. 最激烈的時刻","examples":["People say all kinds of things in the heat of an argument. 人們在爭論進行到最激烈的時候口無遮攔。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>heat</b> is one of a series of races or competitions. The winners of a heat take part in another race or competition, against the winners of other heats. 預賽","examples":["...the heats of the men's 100 metre breaststroke. …男子100米蛙泳預賽。"]}]}]},"hill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"山丘，小山；（道路的）斜坡；土堆，小堆；<美，非正式>國會山"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成堆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hill</b> is an area of land that is higher than the land that surrounds it. 小山","examples":["...the shady street that led up the hill to the office building. …通往山上的辦公樓的林蔭道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>over the hill</b>, you are saying rudely that they are old and no longer fit, attractive, or capable of doing useful work. 在走下坡路","examples":["He doesn't take kindly to suggestions that he is over the hill. 他不愛聽別人說他在走下坡路。"]}]}]},"heart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心，心臟；內心，感情；胸前；重點，核心；中心，中央；信心，勇氣；（表示愛的）心形物；紅桃牌，紅心牌；菜心；同情，憐憫；愛情，情愛；（土地的）肥力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>喜愛，深愛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>heart</b> is the organ in your chest that pumps the blood around your body. People also use <b>heart</b> to refer to the area of their chest that is closest to their heart. 心臟; 心口處","examples":["The bullet had passed less than an inch from Andrea's heart. 子彈從距安德烈亞心臟不到一英寸處穿過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's <b>heart</b> when you are talking about their deep feelings and beliefs. 內心","examples":["Alik's words filled her heart with pride. 亞歷克的話讓她的內心充滿驕傲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>heart</b> when you are talking about someone's character and attitude toward other people, especially when they are kind and generous. 心腸","examples":["She loved his brilliance and his generous heart. 她愛他的才華橫溢和心地寬厚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>heart of</b> something is the most central and important part of it. 核心","examples":["The heart of the problem is supply and demand. 問題的核心是供給和需求。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>heart</b> <b>of</b> a place is its centre. (地方的) 中心","examples":["...a busy dentists' practice in the heart of the city. …位於市中心的一家忙碌的牙醫診所。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>heart</b> is a shape that is used as a symbol of love: ♥. 心形","examples":["...heart-shaped chocolates. …心形巧克力。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Hearts</b> is one of the four suits in a deck of playing cards. Each card in the suit is marked with one or more symbols in the shape of a heart. 紅桃牌","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>heart</b> is a playing card of this suit. (一張) 紅桃牌","examples":["West had to decide whether to play a heart. 韋斯特不得不決定是否要出一張紅桃牌。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel or believe something <b>with all</b> your <b>heart</b>, you feel or believe it very strongly. 真心實意地","examples":["My own family I loved with all my heart. 我真心實意地愛我的家人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is a particular kind of person <b>at heart</b>, you mean that that is what they are really like, even though they may seem very different. 實際上","examples":["He was a very gentle boy at heart. 他實際上是一個非常溫和的男孩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has your interests or your welfare <b>at heart</b>, you mean that they are concerned about you and that is why they are doing something. 放在心上","examples":["She told him she only had his interests at heart. 她告訴他，她心裡頭只有他的利益。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>breaks</b> your <b>heart</b>, they make you very sad and unhappy, usually because they end a love affair or close relationship with you. 使某人心碎","examples":["I fell in love on holiday but the girl broke my heart. 我在度假時墜入情網，但那個女孩卻使我心碎。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>breaks</b> your <b>heart</b>, it makes you feel very sad and depressed, especially because people are suffering but you can do nothing to help them. 使某人心碎","examples":["It really breaks my heart to see them this way. 看到他們這樣確實讓我心裡難過。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you know something such as a poem <b>by heart</b>, you have learned it so well that you can remember it without having to read it. 靠記憶","examples":["Mack knew this passage by heart. 麥克會背這一段。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone has a <b>change of heart</b>, their attitude toward something changes. 態度的改變","examples":["Several brokers have had a change of heart about prospects for the company. 幾位代理商對於該公司前景的態度已有所改變。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something such as a subject or project is <b>close to</b> your <b>heart</b> or <b>near to</b> your <b>heart</b>, it is very important to you and you are very interested in it and concerned about it. 為某人所重視","examples":["This is a subject very close to my heart. 這是我十分關心的一個話題。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you can do something <b>to</b> your <b>heart's content</b>, you can do it as much as you want. 盡情地","examples":["I was delighted to be able to eat my favourite dishes to my heart's content. 我很高興能夠盡情地享用我最喜歡的菜餚。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say something <b>from the heart</b> or <b>from the bottom of</b> your <b>heart</b>, you sincerely mean what you say. 發自內心地","examples":["He spoke with confidence, from the heart. 他講話充滿自信，發自內心。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you want to do something but do <b>not have the heart</b> <b>to</b> do it, you do not do it because you know it will make someone unhappy or disappointed. 不忍做","examples":["We knew all along but didn't have the heart to tell her. 我們一直都知道，但是不忍心告訴她。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you believe or know something <b>in</b> your <b>heart of hearts</b>, that is what you really believe or think, even though it may sometimes seem that you do not. 在內心深處","examples":["I know in my heart of hearts that I am the right man for that mission. 我在內心深處知道，我正是完成那項使命的最合適人選。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If your <b>heart isn't in</b> the thing you are doing, you have very little enthusiasm for it, usually because you are depressed or are thinking about something else. 不熱衷於","examples":["I tried to learn some lines but my heart wasn't really in it. 我試圖記住幾行詩句，但我確實對此不感興趣。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>lose heart</b>, you become sad and depressed and are no longer interested in something, especially because it is not progressing as you would like. 灰心喪氣","examples":["He appealed to his countrymen not to lose heart. 他呼籲同胞們不要灰心喪氣。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If your <b>heart is in</b> your <b>mouth</b>, you feel very excited, worried, or frightened. 心提到嗓子眼裡","examples":["My heart was in my mouth when I walked into her office. 我走進她的辦公室時，心提到了嗓子眼。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> your <b>heart</b> or <b>pour out</b> your <b>heart</b> to someone, you tell them your most private thoughts and feelings. 對某人敞開心扉","examples":["She opened her heart to millions yesterday and told how she came close to suicide. 她昨天向大眾敞開心扉，講述了自己幾乎要自殺的原委。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you say that someone's <b>heart is in the right place</b>, you mean that they are kind, considerate, and generous, although you may disapprove of other aspects of their character. 心地善良","examples":["He's rich, handsome, funny, and his heart is in the right place. 他富有、英俊、風趣，而且心地善良。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you have <b>set</b> your <b>heart on</b> something, you want it very much or want to do it very much. 一心渴望","examples":["He had always set his heart on a career in the fine arts. 他一心想從事一項美術方面的職業。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>take heart</b> <b>from</b> something, you are encouraged and made to feel optimistic by it. 得到鼓舞","examples":["Investors and dealers also took heart from the better than expected industrial production figures. 投資者和經銷商們也從高於預期的工業產值中受到鼓舞。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something <b>to heart</b>, for example someone's behaviour, you are deeply affected and upset by it. 對某事物十分介意","examples":["If someone says something critical I take it to heart. 如果誰說一些批評的話，我就往心裡去。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>cross my heart</b>\" when you want someone to believe that you are telling the truth. You can also ask \"<b>cross your heart?</b>\" when you are asking someone if they are really telling the truth. 在胸口劃十字發誓","examples":["And I won't tell any of the other girls anything you tell me about it. I promise, cross my heart. 我不會把你告訴我的與其有關的任何事情告訴任何其他女孩。我保證，我發誓。"]}]}]},"here":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在這裡，此處；到這裡，朝這裡（常與 come、go 等連用）；此時，此刻；在這一點上，在這方面；給，這就是（用於句首或給予時引出）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"嘿，喂！（用於引起注意或應答）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"這裡，此處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> when you are referring to the place where you are. 在這裡","examples":["I'm here all by myself and I know I'm going to get lost. 我獨自一人在這兒，我知道我會迷路的。","Well, I can't stand here chatting all day. 唉，我不能一整天都站在這裡閒聊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> when you are pointing toward a place that is near you, in order to draw someone else's attention to it. 在 (所指向的) 這裡","examples":["...if you will just sign here. …如果你願意就在這裡簽字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> in order to indicate that the person or thing that you are talking about is near you or is being held by you. 在身邊","examples":["My friend here writes for radio. 我身邊這位朋友為電臺撰稿。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>here</b> <b>to</b> do something, that is your role or function. 來此…","examples":["I'm here to help you. 我是來此幫助你的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> in order to draw attention to something or someone who has just arrived in the place where you are, or to draw attention to the place you have just arrived at. (通報用語) …來了","examples":["\"Here's the taxi,\" she said politely. “計程車來了，”她禮貌地說。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> to refer to a particular point or stage of a situation or subject that you have come to or that you are dealing with. 在這一點上","examples":["It's here that we come up against the difference of approach. 正是在這一點上我們遇到方法上的分歧。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> to refer to a period of time, a situation, or an event that is present or happening now. 出現了","examples":["Economic recovery is here. 經濟復甦現在開始了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> at the beginning of a sentence in order to draw attention to something or to introduce something. (用於句首以引起注意或介紹) 這就是","examples":["Now here's what I want you to do. 聽著，這就是我想讓你做的事。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>here</b> when you are offering or giving something to someone. 給","examples":["Here's your coffee, just the way you like it. 給，這是你的咖啡，按你口味調的。","Here are some letters I want you to sign. 給，我這有些信需要你簽字。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>here we are</b>\" when you have just found something that you have been looking for. 找到了","examples":["I rummaged through the drawers and came up with Amanda's folder. \"Here we are.\" 我翻遍了抽屜，終於發現了阿曼達的活頁夾。“找到了。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>here goes</b>\" when you are about to do or say something difficult or unpleasant. 這就開始了 (表示準備做或說困難或不愉快的事)","examples":["Dr. Culver nervously muttered \"Here goes,\" and gave the little girl an injection. 卡爾弗醫生緊張地嘀咕了一句“要打了啊”，接著就給那小女孩打了一針。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use expressions such as \"<b>here's to us</b>\" and \"<b>here's to your new job</b>\" before drinking a toast in order to wish someone success or happiness. (祝酒用語) 為…乾杯","examples":["He raised his glass. \"Here's to neighbours.\" 他舉起酒杯。“為鄰居們乾杯！”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as \"<b>here we go</b>\" and \"<b>here we go again</b>\" in order to indicate that something is happening again in the way that you expected, especially something unpleasant. 又來了","examples":["\"Police! Open up!\"—\"Oh well,\" I thought, \"here we go.\" “警察!開門！”—“噢，天哪，”我想，“又來了。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>here and now</b> to emphasize that something is happening at the present time, rather than in the future or past, or that you would like it to happen at the present time. 眼下","examples":["I'm a practising physician trying to help people here and now. 我眼下是一名盡力幫助別人的專業醫師。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>here and there</b>, it happens in several different places. 在各處","examples":["I do a bit of teaching here and there. 我在各處教些書。"]}]}]},"hand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手；（鐘錶的）指標；一局牌，一手牌；幫助，援手；工人；船員，水手；支配，掌管；作用，影響；鼓掌，拍手喝彩；<文>字跡；一手之寬（用來測量馬匹的高度）；<舊>（女方的）允婚；表演藝人，製作工匠"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"用……手的；手工"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"交，遞；支援，攙扶；卷（帆）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>hands</b> are the parts of your body at the end of your arms. Each hand has four fingers and a thumb. 手","examples":["I put my hand into my pocket and pulled out the letter. 我把手伸進衣袋，掏出那封信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>hand</b> of someone or something is their influence in an event or situation. 影響","examples":["The hand of the military authorities can be seen in the entire electoral process. 軍方的影響在整個選舉過程中都可以看到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in</b> a particular person's <b>hands</b>, you mean that they are taking care of it, own it, or are responsible for it. 照顧; 掌控","examples":["I feel that possibly the majority of these dogs are in the wrong hands. 我覺得這些狗中大多數可能沒有得到適當的照顧。","We're in safe hands. 我們得到妥善的照顧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you ask someone for <b>a hand</b> with something, you are asking them to help you in what you are doing. 幫助","examples":["Come and give me a hand in the garden. 到花園裡來給我搭把手。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone asks an audience to give someone <b>a hand</b>, they are asking the audience to clap loudly, usually before or after that person performs. 鼓掌","examples":["Let's give 'em a big hand. 讓我們為他們熱烈鼓掌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In a game of cards, your <b>hand</b> is the set of cards that you are holding in your hand at a particular time or the cards that are dealt to you at the beginning of the game. (紙牌遊戲) 手中的牌","examples":["He carefully inspected his hand. 他仔細檢查手中的牌。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>hands</b> of a clock or watch are the thin pieces of metal or plastic that indicate what time it is. (鐘錶的) 指標","examples":["The hands of the clock on the wall moved with a slight click. Half past ten. 牆上時鐘的指標伴著輕輕的嘀嗒聲走著。10:30了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>at hand</b>, <b>near at hand</b>, or <b>close at hand</b>, it is very near in place or time. 在手邊; 在眼前","examples":["Having the right equipment at hand will be enormously helpful. 有合適的工具在手邊將會極為有用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone experiences a particular kind of treatment, especially unpleasant treatment, <b>at the hands of</b> a person or organization, they receive it from them. 在…的手中 (尤指受到不好的待遇)","examples":["The civilian population was suffering greatly at the hands of the security forces. 這些平民在保安部隊的手中吃盡了苦頭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>by hand</b>, you do it using your hands rather than a machine. 手工","examples":["Each pleat was stitched in place by hand. 每個褶子都是手工縫製的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When something <b>changes hands</b>, its ownership changes, usually because it is sold to someone else. (常指某物因賣給他人) 易主","examples":["The firm has changed hands many times over the years. 這家公司幾年來已多次易主。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> your <b>hands full</b> <b>with</b> something, you are very busy because of it. 為...忙得不可開交","examples":["She had her hands full with new arrivals. 她為這些新來的忙得不可開交。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone gives you <b>a free hand</b>, they give you the freedom to use your own judgment and to do exactly as you wish. 便宜行事","examples":["He gave Stephanie a free hand in the decoration. 他讓斯蒂芬妮在裝潢時便宜行事。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> your <b>hands on</b> something or <b>lay</b> your <b>hands on</b> something, you manage to find it or obtain it, usually after some difficulty. 搞到","examples":["Patty began reading everything she could get her hands on. 帕蒂開始閱讀她能搞到的所有東西。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If two people are <b>hand in hand</b>, they are holding each other's nearest hand, usually while they are walking or sitting together. People often do this to show their affection for each other. 手拉手","examples":["I saw them making their way, hand in hand, down the path. 我看到他們手拉手沿著小路朝前走。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If two things <b>go</b> <b>hand in hand</b>, they are closely connected and cannot be considered separately from each other. 密切相關","examples":["For us, research and teaching go hand in hand. 對於我們來說，研究與教學密切相關。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>have a hand in</b> something such as an event or activity, you are involved in it. 參與某事","examples":["He thanked all who had a hand in his release. 他感謝了所有參與解救他的人。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If two people <b>are holding hands</b>, they are holding each other's nearest hand, usually while they are walking or sitting together. People often do this to show their affection for each other. 手拉手","examples":["She approached a young couple holding hands on a bench. 她走近一對手拉手坐在長凳上的年輕情侶。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"The job or problem <b>in hand</b> is the job or problem that you are dealing with at the moment. 處理中的","examples":["The business in hand was approaching some kind of climax. 這件正在處理中的事情正接近某種關鍵時刻。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a situation is <b>in hand</b>, it is under control. 在控制之下","examples":["The Olympic organizers say that matters are well in hand. 奧運會組織者說各項事務完全在掌控之中。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>lend</b> someone <b>a hand</b>, you help them. 幫助某人","examples":["I'd be glad to lend a hand. 我樂意幫忙。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If someone <b>lives hand to mouth</b> or <b>lives from hand to mouth</b>, they have hardly enough food or money to live on. 勉強餬口","examples":["I have a wife and two children and we live from hand to mouth on what I earn. 我有妻子和兩個孩子，我們靠我掙的錢勉強餬口。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>keep</b> their <b>hands off</b> something or to <b>take</b> their <b>hands off</b> it, you are telling them in a slightly aggressive way not to touch it or interfere with it. 不許碰; 不許干涉","examples":["Keep your hands off my milk. 不許碰我的牛奶。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you do not know something <b>off hand</b>, you do not know it without having to ask someone else or look it up in a book. 馬上; 無需查詢地","examples":["I can't think of any off hand. 我一下子什麼也想不起來。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you have a problem or responsibility <b>on</b> your <b>hands</b>, you have to deal with it. If it is <b>off</b> your <b>hands</b>, you no longer have to deal with it. 由某人處理/不再由某人處理","examples":["They now have yet another drug problem on their hands. 他們現在又在處理另一個與毒品有關的問題。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on hand</b>, they are near and able to be used if they are needed. 現成的","examples":["There are experts on hand to give you all the help and advice you need. 有現成的專家隨時為你提供所需的一切幫助和建議。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"You use <b>on the one hand</b> to introduce the first of two contrasting points, facts, or ways of looking at something. It is always followed later by \"on the other hand\" or \"on the other.\" 一方面","examples":["On the one hand, if the body doesn't have enough cholesterol, we would not be able to survive. On the other hand, if the body has too much cholesterol, the excess begins to line the arteries. 一方面，如果身體沒有足夠的膽固醇，我們將無法生存；另一方面，如果體內膽固醇過多，多餘的膽固醇就開始讓動脈變厚。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"You use <b>on the other hand</b> to introduce the second of two contrasting points, facts, or ways of looking at something. 另一方面","examples":["The film lost money; reviews, on the other hand, were by and large favourable. 這部電影賠了錢；但從另一方面來看，評論大體上是積極的。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If a person or a situation gets <b>out of hand</b>, you are no longer able to control them. 失去控制","examples":["His drinking got out of hand. 他飲酒已失去控制。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you dismiss or reject something <b>out of hand</b>, you do so immediately and do not consider believing or accepting it. 不假思索地","examples":["I initially dismissed the idea out of hand. 我起初不假思索地一口否決了這個主意。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something or someone <b>in hand</b>, you take control or responsibility over them, especially in order to improve them. 對某人/某事負責","examples":["She took the twins in hand, encouraging them to turn their thoughts to the future. 她對這對雙胞胎負起責任，鼓勵他們要多想想未來。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If you say that your <b>hands are tied</b>, you mean that something is preventing you from acting in the way that you want to. 受到阻礙","examples":["Politicians are always saying that they want to help us but their hands are tied. 政客們總說他們想幫助我們，但是卻受到阻礙。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"If you <b>try</b> your <b>hand</b> <b>at</b> an activity, you attempt to do it, usually for the first time. (通常指初次) 嘗試","examples":["He tried his hand at fishing, but he wasn't really very good at it. 他嘗試過釣魚，但他真的不在行。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"If you <b>turn</b> your <b>hand to</b> something such as a practical activity, you learn about it and do it for the first time. 學做某事","examples":["...a person who can turn his hand to anything. …一個什麼事都可以學著去做的人。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"If you <b>wash</b> your <b>hands of</b> someone or something, you refuse to be involved with them any more or to take responsibility for them. 洗手不幹; 不再負責","examples":["He seems to have washed his hands of the job. 這種工作他似乎已洗手不幹了。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you <b>win hands down</b>, you win very easily. 輕易取勝","examples":["We have been beaten in some games which we should have won hands down. 我們曾經在一些本應輕易取勝的比賽中落選。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hand</b> something <b>to</b> someone, you pass it to them. 遞...給...","examples":["He handed me a little rectangle of white paper. 他遞給我一小條白紙。"]}]}]},"help":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"幫助，援助；改善狀況，對……有益；給（自己或某人）食物或飲料；擅自拿走，竊取；攙扶，帶領"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"幫助，協助；有助益的東西（如忠告、錢等）；有用；救助；有幫助的人（或事物）；傭人；（計算機程式提供使用說明的）求助程式"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"救命（呼救用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>help</b> someone, you make it easier for them to do something, for example by doing part of the work for them or by giving them advice or money. 幫助","examples":["He has helped to raise a lot of money. 他幫著籌到了很多錢。","You can of course help by giving them a donation directly. 你當然可以透過直接給他們一筆捐贈來幫助他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>helps</b>, you mean that it makes something easier to do or get, or that it improves a situation to some extent. 有助於","examples":["The right style of swimsuit can help to hide, minimize, or emphasize what you want it to. 款式得當的泳衣有助於按你的意願掩飾、縮小或突出某些部位。","Building more bypasses will help the environment by reducing pollution and traffic jams in towns and cities. 修建更多的支路將減少城鎮中的汙染和交通堵塞，從而改善環境。","If it would help, I'd be happy to take photographs. 如果用得著，我很樂意拍照。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>help</b> someone go somewhere or move in some way, you give them support so that they can move more easily. 扶持","examples":["Martin helped Tanya over the rail. 馬丁扶著塔尼婭翻過欄杆。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>help</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>to</b> something, you serve yourself or you take it for yourself. If someone tells you to <b>help</b> <b>yourself</b>, they are telling you politely to serve yourself anything you want or to take anything you want. 自取","examples":["There's bread on the table. Help yourself. 桌上有面包。你自己拿吧。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>helps</b> <b>themselves</b> <b>to</b> something, they steal it. 偷","examples":["Two men forced the clerks to flee before helping themselves to the cash register. 兩名男子強迫店員跑開，然後偷走了現金出納機裡的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Help</b> is also a noun. 幫助","examples":["Thanks very much for your help. 非常感謝你的幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has been <b>a help</b> or has been some <b>help</b>, you mean that they have helped you to solve a problem. 幫助解決困難的人 (或物)","examples":["Thank you. You've been a great help already. 謝謝你。你已經幫了很大的忙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Help</b> is action taken to rescue a person who is in danger. You shout \"<b>help!</b>\" when you are in danger in order to attract someone's attention so that they can come and rescue you. 救命","examples":["He was screaming for help. 他正尖聲叫喊救命。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In computing, <b>help</b>, or the <b>help</b> menu, is a file that gives you information and advice, for example about how to use a particular program. 幫助","examples":["If you get stuck, click on Help. 如果你碰到困難，請點選“幫助”。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>can't help</b> the way you feel or behave, you cannot control it or stop it from happening. You can also say that you <b>can't help</b> <b>yourself</b>. 不禁","examples":["I can't help feeling sorry for the poor man. 我不禁為這個可憐的男子感到難過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say you <b>can't help</b> thinking something, you are expressing your opinion in an indirect way, often because you think it seems rude. (用以使唐突語氣變得婉轉) 不免","examples":["I can't help feeling that this may just be another of her schemes. 我不免覺得這也許正是她的又一個詭計。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is of help</b>, they make a situation easier or better. 有幫助","examples":["Can I be of help to you? 我能幫你什麼忙嗎？"]}]}]},"history":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歷史；沿革，發展過程；歷史課，歷史學；史書，歷史記載；個人經歷，履歷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the events of the past as <b>history</b>. You can also refer to the past events which concern a particular topic or place as its <b>history</b>. 歷史","examples":["The Catholic Church has played a prominent role throughout Polish history. 天主教在整個波蘭歷史中扮演了重要的角色。","...the most evil mass killer in history. …歷史上最邪惡的殺人狂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>History</b> is a subject studied in schools, colleges, and universities that deals with events that have happened in the past. 歷史學","examples":["...a lecturer in history at Birmingham University. …伯明翰大學的一位歷史講師。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>history</b> is an account of events that have happened in the past. 歷史事件紀錄","examples":["...his magnificent history of broadcasting in Canada. …他對加拿大播音史的出色紀錄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or a place has <b>a</b> <b>history</b> <b>of</b> something, it has been very common or has happened frequently in their past. 記錄","examples":["He had a history of drinking problems. 他有酗酒的記錄。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone's <b>history</b> is the set of facts that are known about their past. 履歷","examples":["He couldn't get a new job because of his medical history. 由於他的病史，他無法找到新工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>goes down in history</b>, people in the future remember them because of particular actions that they have done or because of particular events that have happened. 載入史冊","examples":["Bradley will go down in history as Los Angeles' longest serving mayor. 布拉德利將作為洛杉磯任職時間最長的市長載入史冊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>makes history</b> does something that is considered to be important and significant in the development of the world or of a particular society. 創造歷史","examples":["Willy Brandt made history by visiting East Germany in 1970. 威利·勃蘭特1970年對東德的訪問創造了歷史。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are telling someone about an event and say <b>the rest is history</b>, you mean that you do not need to tell them what happened next because everyone knows about it already. 後來發生的事情眾人皆知","examples":["We met in college, the rest is history. 我們在大學相識，接下來的事大家都知道了。"]}]}]},"head":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頭；頭腦，智力；頂部；排頭；領導人，負責人；<英>校長，院長；人數，（動物的）頭數；（植物的）葉球，頭狀花序；一頭長，一頭高；釘頭，錘頭；啤酒沫；（河流）源頭；膿頭；硬幣正面（有人頭像）；磁頭；（短語的）中心詞，主導詞；水壓，蒸汽壓力；緊要關頭；桌子的上首座位，床頭；<非正式>頭痛；蓄水高度，水頭"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"朝（某方向）行進；領導，主管；居……之首；加標題；用頭頂（球）；形成……的頭或頂部；砍（植物或樹木的）枝；（萵苣，捲心菜）結球，長成球狀；發源"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"領頭的，負責的；頭的；在頂端的；從前方來的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（硬幣）有頭像的一面朝上（heads）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>head</b> is the top part of your body, which has your eyes, mouth, and brain in it. 頭部","examples":["She turned her head away from him. 她扭過頭，不看他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>head</b> to refer to your mind and your mental abilities. 頭腦","examples":["...an exceptional analyst who could do complex maths in his head. …一位能做複雜心算的傑出分析家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>head</b> <b>of</b> a line of people or vehicles is the front of it, or the first person or vehicle in the line. (人群或車輛的) 前端","examples":["He made his way to the head of the line. 他來到隊伍的最前端。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>head</b> of a company or organization is the person in charge of it and in charge of the people in it. (公司、團體的) 負責人","examples":["Heads of government from more than 100 countries gather in Geneva tomorrow. 來自一百多個國家的政府首腦明天將聚集在日內瓦。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>head</b> of something long and thin is the end which is wider than or a different shape from the rest, and which is often considered to be the most important part. (長而細的物體的) 頂部","examples":["There should be no exposed screw heads. 螺釘頭不應暴露在外。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you flip a coin and it comes down <b>heads</b>, you can see the side of the coin which has a picture of a head on it. (硬幣) 有頭像的一面","examples":["\"We might flip a coin for it,\" suggested Ted. \"If it's heads, then we'll talk.\" “我們來擲硬幣決定這件事”，特德建議說，“如果是人頭，我們就說。”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>heads</b> a line or procession, they are at the front of it. 行進在…的前頭","examples":["The parson, heading the procession, had just turned right toward the churchyard. 走在行列最前頭的那位牧師，剛朝右轉走向了教堂墓地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>heads</b> a list or group, it is at the top of it. 居…之首","examples":["Running a business heads the list of ambitions among the 1,000 people interviewed by Good Housekeeping magazine. 在《好管家》雜誌對1000人關於事業志向的採訪中，開公司位列名單之首。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>head</b> a department, company, or organization, you are the person in charge of it. 掌管","examples":["...Michael Williams, who heads the department's Office of Civil Rights. …邁克爾•威廉姆斯，他掌管著部門的民事權利辦公室。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are heading</b> or <b>are headed</b> for a particular place, you are going toward that place. 朝著…行進","examples":["He was headed for the bus stop. 他朝公交車站走去。","It is not clear how many of them will be heading back to Saudi Arabia tomorrow. 尚不清楚他們當中有多少人明天將折回沙烏地阿拉伯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is heading for</b> or <b>is headed for</b> a particular result, the situation they are in is developing in a way that makes that result very likely. 朝…發展","examples":["The latest talks aimed at ending the civil war appear to be heading for deadlock. 旨在結束內戰的最新談判看來要走入僵局。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a piece of writing <b>is headed</b> a particular title, it has that title written at the beginning of it. 加標題於…","examples":["One chapter is headed, \"Beating the Test.\" 有一章的標題是“戰勝考驗。”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>head</b> a ball in football, you hit it with your head in order to make it go in a particular direction. 用頭頂 (球)","examples":["He headed the ball across the face of the goal. 他用頭頂球，球越過了門框。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>a head</b> or <b>per head</b> after stating a cost or amount in order to indicate that that cost or amount is for each person in a particular group. 每人","examples":["This simple chicken dish costs less than $3 a head. 吃這道簡單的雞肉菜餚，每人的花費還不到$3。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you a have <b>a</b> <b>head for</b> something, you can deal with it easily. For example, if you have <b>a</b> <b>head for figures</b>, you can do arithmetic easily, and if you have <b>a</b> <b>head for heights</b>, you can climb to a great height without feeling afraid. 有…的才能","examples":["I don't have a head for business. 我沒有做生意的才能。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> a fact or idea <b>into</b> your <b>head</b>, you suddenly realize or think that it is true and you usually do not change your opinion about it. 充分理解並接受","examples":["Once they get an idea into their heads, they never give up. 他們一旦接受了某個想法，就永遠不會放棄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>got</b> something <b>into</b> their <b>head</b>, you mean that they have finally understood or accepted it, and you are usually criticizing them because it has taken them a long time to do this. 終於明白","examples":["Managers have at last got it into their heads that they can no longer rest content with inefficient operations. 經理們最後終於明白不能再滿足於低效率的運作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If alcoholic drink <b>goes to</b> your <b>head</b>, it makes you feel drunk. (酒) 使人感到醉","examples":["That wine was strong, it went to your head. 那種酒很烈，喝了會上頭。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something such as praise or success <b>goes to</b> someone's <b>head</b>, you are criticizing them because you think that it makes them too proud or confident. (成功等) 衝昏…的頭腦","examples":["Ford is definitely not a man to let a little success go to his head. 福特絕不是那種會被一點點成功衝昏頭腦的人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you are <b>head over heels</b> or <b>head over heels in love</b>, you are very much in love. 深陷情網","examples":["I was very attracted to men and fell head over heels many times. 我那時很容易被男性吸引，多次深陷情網。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>head</b>, you remain calm in a difficult situation. If you <b>lose</b> your <b>head</b>, you panic or do not remain calm in a difficult situation. 鎮定自若; 張皇失措","examples":["She was able to keep her head and not panic. 她當時能夠鎮定自若、不慌張。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"Phrases such as <b>laugh</b> your <b>head off</b> and <b>scream</b> your <b>head off</b> can be used to emphasize that someone is laughing or screaming a lot or very loudly. 大笑","examples":["He carried on telling a joke, laughing his head off. 他不停地說笑話，大笑著。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something such as an idea, joke, or comment goes <b>over</b> someone's <b>head</b>, it is too difficult for them to understand. 超過…的理解力","examples":["I admit that a lot of the ideas went way over my head. 我承認有許多想法我都不能理解。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If someone does something <b>over</b> another person's <b>head</b>, they do it without asking them or discussing it with them, especially when they should do so because the other person is in a position of authority. 越級","examples":["He was reprimanded for trying to go over the heads of senior officers. 他因試圖越過上級官員而遭嚴斥。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you say that something unpleasant or embarrassing <b>rears its ugly head</b> or <b>raises its ugly head</b>, you mean that it occurs, often after not occurring for some time. (不好的事情) 再次出現","examples":["There was a problem which reared its ugly head about a week after she moved back in. 在她搬回去約一週後，有個問題又冒出來了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>stand on</b> your <b>head</b>, you balance upside down with the top of your head and your hands on the ground. 倒立","examples":["He was photographed standing on his head doing yoga. 他倒立著做瑜伽時被拍了下來。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you say that you cannot <b>make head nor tail of</b> something or you cannot <b>make heads or tails of</b> it, you are emphasizing that you cannot understand it at all. 理解","examples":["I couldn't make head nor tail of the damn film. 我壓根兒看不懂這部該死的電影。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If somebody <b>takes it into</b> their <b>head</b> <b>to</b> do something, especially something strange or foolish, they suddenly decide to do it. 突然決定 (做某事，尤指做古怪或愚蠢的事)","examples":["He suddenly took it into his head to go out to Australia to stay with his son. 他突然心血來潮決定去澳大利亞同他兒子一起住。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If a problem or disagreement <b>comes to a head</b> or <b>is brought to a head</b>, it becomes so bad that something must be done about it. 到了緊要關頭","examples":["These problems came to a head in September when five of the station's journalists were fired. 這些問題在9月份變得十分尖銳，當時臺裡有5名記者被解僱。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If two or more people <b>put</b> their <b>heads together</b>, they talk about a problem they have and try to solve it. 集思廣益","examples":["So everyone put their heads together and eventually an amicable arrangement was reached. 因此大家集思廣益並最終作出了妥善的安排。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>head above water</b>, you just avoid getting into difficulties; used especially to talk about business. (尤指生意上) 避免陷入困境","examples":["We are keeping our head above water, but our cash flow position is not too good. 我們雖然還未陷入困境，但資金流轉狀況不太好。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you say that <b>heads will roll</b> as a result of something bad that has happened, you mean that people will be punished for it, especially by losing their jobs. 要有許多人掉腦袋 (尤指失去工作)","examples":["The group's problems have led to speculation that heads will roll. 該集團的問題已經引發有些人將會失業的猜測。"]}]}]},"homework":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（學生的）家庭作業；準備工作；（尤指低酬勞計件活）在家裡做的活計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Homework</b> is schoolwork that teachers give to students to do at home in the evening or on the weekend. 家庭作業","examples":["Have you done your homework, Gemma? 你做完家庭作業了嗎，傑瑪？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> your <b>homework</b>, you find out what you need to know in preparation for something. 做必要的準備工作","examples":["Before you go near a stockbroker, do your homework. 在你去見股票經紀人之前，先要做好必要的準備工作。"]}]}]},"holiday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"假日；度假期；法定節假日，節日；（分期付款、稅費等的）暫緩繳付期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"度假"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>holiday</b> is a day when people do not go to work or school because of a religious or national celebration. 公眾假日","examples":["New Year's Day is a public holiday. 元旦是公休日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>holiday</b> is a period of time during which you relax and enjoy yourself away from home. People sometimes refer to their holiday as their <b>holidays</b>. (外出度過的) 假期","examples":["During his summer holiday he visited Russia. 暑假期間他遊覽了俄羅斯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>holidays</b> are the time when children do not have to go to school. (學校的) 假期","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a particular number of days' or weeks' <b>holiday</b>, you do not have to go to work for that number of days or weeks. (工作) 假期","examples":["The French get five to six weeks' holiday a year. 法國人一年有5到6周的假期。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are holidaying</b> in a place away from home, you are on holiday there. (外出) 度假","examples":["Myles holidayed in Jamaica. 邁爾斯在牙買加度了假。"]}]}]},"high":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高的；富含……的；重要的；先進的，高階的；崇高的；高音的，聲音尖銳的；興高采烈的；喝醉了的，（吸毒後）極度興奮的；十分贊同的，非常尊敬的；中間的，全盛的；開始變質的，開始發餿的；（宗教或政治觀點）極端的，偏激的；（母音）舌位高的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最高水平，最大數量；興奮，高興；高氣壓區；（毒品引致的）快感；高中，中學；強檔；高音，高音符"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（成本、價值、音量）高，（數量）大；在高處，向高處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>high</b> extends a long way from the bottom to the top when it is upright. You do not use <b>high</b> to describe people, animals, or plants. 高的 (不用於形容人、動物或植物)","examples":["...a house with a high wall all around it. …四周圍著高牆的房子。","Mount Marcy is the highest mountain in the Adirondacks. 馬西山是阿迪朗達克山脈中最高的山。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>high</b> to talk or ask about how much something upright measures from the bottom to the top. 高度為…的","examples":["...an elegant bronze horse only nine inches high. …一尊高度僅為9英寸的精緻的青銅馬。","The grass in the garden was a foot high. 院子裡的草有1英尺高。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>high</b>, it is a long way above the ground, above sea level, or above a person or thing. (與地面、海平面、其他人或物相比而言) 高的","examples":["I looked down from the high window. 我從高高的窗戶往下看。","The sun was high in the sky, blazing down on us. 太陽高掛在空中，朝我們發出耀眼的光芒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>high</b> to indicate that something is great in amount, degree, or intensity. (數量、程度或強度) 高的","examples":["The European country with the highest birth rate is Ireland. 出生率最高的歐洲國家是愛爾蘭。","Official reports said casualties were high. 官方報道稱人員傷亡很大。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a food or other substance is <b>high in</b> a particular ingredient, it contains a large amount of that ingredient. (含量) 高的","examples":["Don't indulge in rich sauces, fried food, and thick pastry as these are high in fat. 不要吃太多油膩的調味汁、油炸食品和厚油酥點心，因為這些食品脂肪含量很高。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>high</b> priority or is <b>high</b> <b>on</b> your list, you mean that you consider it to be one of the most important things you have to do or deal with. 首要的","examples":["The party has not made the issue a high priority. 該黨還沒有把這個問題列為首要考慮的事項。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone who is <b>high</b> <b>in</b> a particular profession or society, or has a <b>high</b> position, has a very important position and has great authority and influence. (地位) 高的","examples":["Was there anyone particularly high in the administration who was an advocate of a different policy? 管理部門裡有沒有職位特別高的人支援採納不同政策？","...corruption in high places. …高層的腐敗。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone has a <b>high</b> reputation, or people have a <b>high</b> opinion of them, people think they are very good in some way, for example at their work. (聲望或評價) 高的","examples":["People have such high expectations of you. 人們對你抱有如此之高的期望。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If the quality or standard of something is <b>high</b>, it is extremely good. (品質或標準) 高的","examples":["This is high quality stuff. 這是高品質的東西。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>high</b> sound or voice is close to the top of a particular range of notes. (音調) 尖聲的","examples":["Her high voice really irritated Maria. 她的尖嗓門真的惹怒了瑪麗亞。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If your spirits are <b>high</b>, you feel happy and excited. 興奮的","examples":["Her spirits were high with the hope of seeing Nick in minutes rather than hours. 她很興奮，因為只消等上幾分鐘而不是幾個小時就有希望見到尼克了。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone is <b>high</b> <b>on</b> alcohol or drugs, they are affected by the alcoholic drink or drugs they have taken. 喝醉了的; (吸毒後) 極度興奮的","examples":["He was too high on drugs and alcohol to remember them. 他吸毒和酗酒後興奮過度，已經記不起他們了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>High</b> is also an adverb. 高高地","examples":["...wagons packed high with bureaus, bedding, and cooking pots. …高高地推放著衣櫃、寢具和炊具的四輪運貨馬車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>High</b> is also an adverb. 高高地","examples":["...being able to run faster or jump higher than other people. …能比其他人跑得更快或跳得更高。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>High</b> is also an adverb. 高地","examples":["He expects the unemployment figures to rise even higher in coming months. 他預計失業人數在未來的幾個月中會繼續上升。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you aim <b>high</b>, you try to obtain or to achieve the best that you can. 向高的目標","examples":["You should not be afraid to aim high in the quest for an improvement in your income. 在尋求收入提高方面，你應該敢於給自己設定高的目標。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>high up</b>, it is a long way above the ground, above sea level, or above a person or thing. (與地面、海平面、其他人或物相比而言) 高的","examples":["His farm was high up in the hills. 他的農場在山的高處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use phrases such as \"<b>in the high 80s</b>\" to indicate that a number or level is, for example, more than 85 but not as much as 90. 中間偏上","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>high up</b> <b>in</b> a profession or society has a very important position. (地位或職位) 高的","examples":["His cousin is somebody quite high up in the navy. 他的堂兄在海軍裡地位相當高。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something came from <b>on high</b>, you mean that it came from a person or place of great authority. 高層人物","examples":["Orders had come from on high that extra care was to be taken during this week. 上頭傳來話說這個星期要格外小心。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you were left <b>high and dry</b>, you are emphasizing that you were left in a difficult situation and were unable to do anything about it. 陷入困境","examples":["Schools with better reputations will be flooded with applications while poorer schools will be left high and dry. 聲譽好些的學校將會收到大量申請，而差些的學校則將陷入困境。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>highs and lows</b> <b>of</b> someone's life or career, you are referring to both the successful or happy times, and the unsuccessful or bad times. 快樂和痛苦; 成功和失敗","examples":["Here, she talks about the highs and lows of her life. 此刻，她正談論著自己生活中的酸甜苦辣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that you looked <b>high and low</b> for something, you are emphasizing that you looked for it in every place that you could think of. 四處尋找","examples":["...and I rambled around the apartment looking high and low for an aspirin or painkiller. …我在公寓裡四處尋找阿司匹林或者止痛片。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something reaches a <b>high</b> <b>of</b> a particular amount or degree, that is the greatest it has ever been. 最高點","examples":["Traffic from Jordan to Iraq is down to a dozen loaded trucks a day, compared with a high of 200 a day. 從約旦到伊拉克的車輛少的時候1天有一打滿載的卡車，高峰時一天則有200輛之多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>high</b> is a feeling or mood of great excitement or happiness. 興奮","examples":["\"I'm still on a high,\" she said after the show. “我還興奮著呢，” 她在演出結束後說。"]}]}]},"horse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"馬；<非正式>賽馬；跳馬，鞍馬；鋸木架；<非正式>馬力；<美，非正式>主力隊員；<非正式>海洛因；夾塊，夾石；騎兵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（人或車輛）提供馬；使騎馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>horse</b> is a large animal which people can ride. Some horses are used for pulling ploughs and carts. 馬","examples":["A small man on a grey horse had appeared. 一個騎著灰馬的小個子男人出現了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you hear something <b>from the horse's mouth</b>, you hear it from someone who knows that it is definitely true. (訊息等) 來自可靠人士","examples":["He has got to hear it from the horse's mouth. Then he can make a judgment as to whether his policy is correct or not. 他必須獲得可靠訊息。然後他就能判斷出他的政策是否正確。"]}]}]},"hit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打，擊；撞擊，碰撞；擊中，命中；擊（球）；產生不良影響，危害；攻擊，襲擊；達到（一個特定的水平，階段，數字）；碰到，遇到（困難、問題等）；使（某人）突然意識到；使（突然）聞到，使看到；按，摁；<非正式>給（人）一劑毒品（或烈酒）；<非正式>（產品）面市併產生影響；<非正式>給（21點紙牌遊戲玩家）發另一張紙牌"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"打擊；命中，擊中；很受歡迎的人（或事物），成功；（對網站的）訪問，點選；<非正式>毒品的一劑；<美，非正式>暴力犯罪，兇殺；很受歡迎的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hit</b> someone or something, you deliberately touch them with a lot of force, with your hand or an object held in your hand. 打","examples":["Find the exact grip that allows you to hit the ball hard. 找到能讓你大力擊球的準確握拍方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When one thing <b>hits</b> another, it touches it with a lot of force. 猛撞","examples":["The car had apparently hit a traffic sign before skidding out of control. 汽車顯然在失控滑出前猛地撞到了一個交通指示牌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a bomb or missile <b>hits</b> its target, it reaches it. (炸彈或導彈) 擊中","examples":["...multiple-warhead missiles that could hit many targets at a time. …可以一次擊中多個目標的多彈頭導彈。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>hits</b> a person, place, or thing, it affects them very badly. 對…造成嚴重影響","examples":["The plan to charge motorists to use the motorway is going to hit me hard. 向汽車駕駛員收取高速公路使用費這一方案會嚴重影響到我。","About two hundred people died in the earthquake which hit northern Peru. 大約兩百人在那場襲擊秘魯北部的地震中喪生。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a feeling or an idea <b>hits</b> you, it suddenly affects you or comes into your mind. 使突然意識到","examples":["It hit me that I had a choice. 我突然意識到我可以有所選擇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>hit</b> a particular high or low point on a scale of something such as success or health, you reach it. 達到","examples":["He admits to having hit the lowest point in his life. 他承認自己跌到了一生中的最低谷。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hit</b> is also a noun. 擊中","examples":["First a house took a direct hit and then the rocket exploded. 首先一幢房子被直接擊中，接著火箭彈爆炸了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a CD, film, or play is a <b>hit</b>, it is very popular and successful. (唱片、電影或戲劇的) 成功","examples":["The song became a massive hit in 1945. 這首歌在1945年取得了巨大成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hit</b> is a single visit to a website. (網站的) 點選","examples":["Our small company has had 78,000 hits on its Internet pages. 我們的小公司的網頁已被點選了7.8萬次。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone who is searching for information on the Internet gets a <b>hit</b>, they find a website where there is that information. (在網際網路上搜到) 所要找的網頁","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>hit it off</b>, they like each other and become friendly as soon as they meet. 一見如故","examples":["Dad and Walter hit it off straight away. 爸爸和沃爾特一見如故。"]}]}]},"hope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"希望"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"希望；期盼的東西，盼望的事；（發生好事的）可能性；被寄予希望的人（或物）；<古>信賴感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hope</b> that something is true, or if you <b>hope</b> for something, you want it to be true or to happen, and you usually believe that it is possible or likely. 希望","examples":["She had decided she must go on as usual, follow her normal routine, and hope and pray. 她已決定自己必須一如既往地過下去，遵循自己的日常生活規律，同時心存希望並祈禱。","He hesitates before leaving, almost as though he had been hoping for conversation. 他離開前有些猶豫，好像希望跟人說些什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you cannot <b>hope</b> <b>for</b> something, or if you talk about the only thing that you can <b>hope</b> <b>to</b> get, you mean that you are in a bad situation, and there is very little chance of improving it. 指望","examples":["Things aren't ideal, but that's the best you can hope for. 事情並不理想，但你只能指望這些了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hope</b> is also a noun. 指望","examples":["The only hope for underdeveloped countries is to become, as far as possible, self-reliant. 欠發達國家的惟一指望就是儘可能地做到自力更生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hope</b> is a feeling of desire and expectation that things will go well in the future. 期望","examples":["Now that he has become president, many people once again have hope for genuine changes in the system. 既然他已成為總統，許多人又一次寄期望於體制的真正改革。","But Kevin hasn't given up hope of getting in shape. 但是凱文仍沒有放棄康復的希望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone wants something to happen, and considers it likely or possible, you can refer to their <b>hopes</b> <b>of</b> that thing, or to their <b>hope</b> <b>that</b> it will happen. 希望","examples":["They have hopes of increasing trade between the two regions. 他們抱有增加兩個地區之間貿易的希望。","My hope is that, in the future, I will go over there and marry her. 我的希望就是有朝一日我能去那裡跟她結婚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you think that the help or success of a particular person or thing will cause you to be successful or to get what you want, you can refer to them as your <b>hope</b>. 被寄予希望的人 (或物)","examples":["Roemer represented the best hope for a businesslike climate in Louisiana. 羅默最有可能給路易斯安那州帶來務實高效的風氣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are in a difficult situation and do something and <b>hope for the best</b>, you hope that everything will happen in the way you want, although you know that it may not. 寄予最大希望 (尤指在困境中)","examples":["Some companies are cutting costs and hoping for the best. 一些公司在削減成本，希望能有轉機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone not to <b>get</b> their <b>hopes up</b>, or not to <b>build</b> their <b>hopes up</b>, you are warning them that they should not become too confident of progress or success. 抱太大希望","examples":["There is no reason for people to get their hopes up over this mission. 人們沒有理由對這次任務抱有太大的希望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>not</b> got <b>a hope in hell</b> <b>of</b> doing something, you are emphasizing that they will not be able to do it. 毫無希望 (做成某事)","examples":["Everybody knows they haven't got a hope in hell of forming a government anyway. 人人皆知他們毫無希望建成一個政府。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>high hopes</b> or <b>great hopes</b> <b>that</b> something will happen, you are confident that it will happen. 很大的希望","examples":["I had high hopes that Derek Randall might play an important part. 我對德里克·蘭德爾發揮重要作用抱有很大希望。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>hope against hope</b> <b>that</b> something will happen, you hope that it will happen, although it seems impossible. 抱一線希望","examples":["She glanced about the hall, hoping against hope that Richard would be waiting for her. 她掃視了一下大廳，抱一線希望理查德在等著她。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use \"<b>I hope</b>\" in expressions such as \"<b>I hope you don't mind</b>\" and \"<b>I hope I'm not disturbing you</b>,\" when you are being polite and want to make sure that you have not offended someone or disturbed them. 我希望 (後接否定句，表示客氣)","examples":["I hope you don't mind me coming to see you. 我希望你不會介意我來看你。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You say \"<b>I hope</b>\" when you want to warn someone not to do something foolish or dangerous. 但願 (警告某人不要做愚蠢或危險的事)","examples":["You're not trying to see him, I hope? 但願你不是在想方設法去見他吧？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>in the hope</b> <b>of</b> another thing happening, you do it because you think it might cause or help the other thing to happen, which is what you want. 懷著…的希望","examples":["He was studying in the hope of being admitted to an engineering college. 他在學習，希望能被某個工學院錄取。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>live in hope</b> that something will happen, you continue to hope that it will happen, although it seems unlikely, and you realize that you are being foolish. (在不大可能的情況下) 對…繼續抱有希望","examples":["I just live in hope that one day she'll talk to me. 我只是希望有一天她會和我說話。"]}]}]},"hole":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洞，坑；裂口，開口；（高爾夫球運動中的）球洞；（小動物的）洞穴；令人不舒適的地方；缺點，破綻；<非正式>困境，窘境；禁閉室，單人牢房；空缺的地方（或位置）；（兩個守場員間的）空地，空隙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指給船）鑽洞，打洞；擊球入洞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hole</b> is a hollow space in something solid, with an opening on one side. 洞","examples":["He took a shovel, dug a hole, and buried his once-prized possessions. 他拿了一把鏟子，挖了個坑，埋下了他曾經珍愛的物品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hole</b> is an opening in something that goes right through it. (貫穿的) 孔洞","examples":["...kids with holes in the knees of their jeans. …牛仔褲的膝蓋上有破洞的孩子們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hole</b> is the home or hiding place of a mouse, rabbit, or other small animal. (鼠、兔等小動物的) 洞穴","examples":["...a rabbit hole. …一個兔子窩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>hole</b> <b>in</b> a law, theory, or argument is a fault or weakness that it has. (法律、理論、論點等的) 漏洞","examples":["There were some holes in that theory, some unanswered questions. 那個理論中有些漏洞，一些沒有得到解答的問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>hole</b> is also one of the nine or eighteen sections of a golf course. (高爾夫球場上的) 球洞","examples":["I played nine holes with Gary Carter today. 我今天同加里·卡特打了9洞高爾夫球。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>in a hole</b>, you mean that you are in a difficult or embarrassing situation. 身陷困境或窘境","examples":["We were in a hole, but I was proud with the way we came back. 我們雖然身陷困境，但我很為我們能像這樣東山再起感到自豪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or organization is <b>in the hole</b>, they owe money to someone else. 虧空","examples":["Some estimates show next year's budget could be $2.5 billion in the hole. 一些估計顯示，明年的預算將會虧空25億美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you get <b>a hole in one</b> in golf, you get the golf ball into the hole with a single stroke. (高爾夫球運動中) 一桿進洞","examples":["All they ever dream about is getting a hole in one. 他們一直夢想著能一桿進洞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pick holes in</b> an argument or theory, you find weak points in it so that it is no longer valid. 在 (論據或理論中) 挑毛病","examples":["He then goes on to pick holes in the article before reaching his conclusion. 然後，他繼續挑這篇文章的毛病，最後得出了自己的結論。"]}]}]},"hour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小時；一小時的路程；（工作，辦公等的）固定時間；某個時間；長時間；整點，正點；（西派教會中）固定時分短禮拜；（天文）黃經（或赤經）15°"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>hour</b> is a period of sixty minutes. 小時","examples":["They waited for about two hours. 他們等了大約兩個鐘頭。","I only slept about half an hour that night. 那天晚上我只睡了大約半個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People say that something takes or lasts <b>hours</b> to emphasize that it takes or lasts a very long time, or what seems like a very long time. 很長的一段時間","examples":["Getting there would take hours. 到那兒要花很長時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A clock that strikes <b>the hour</b> strikes when it is exactly one o'clock, two o'clock, and so on. 整點","examples":["She'd heard a clock somewhere strike the hour as she'd slipped from her room. 她悄悄地從自己房間裡溜出來時，聽到某個地方的一隻時鐘正在整點報時。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a particular time or moment as a particular <b>hour</b>. 時間; 時刻","examples":["...the hour of his execution. …他的死刑執行時間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer, for example, to someone's <b>hour</b> <b>of</b> need or <b>hour</b> <b>of</b> happiness, you are referring to the time in their life when they are or were experiencing that condition or feeling. (人生中需要幫助、感到幸福等的) 時刻","examples":["He recalled her devotion to her husband during his hour of need. 他回想起她在丈夫需要幫助時所做出的無私奉獻。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to the period of time during which something happens or operates each day as the <b>hours</b> during which it happens or operates. (一天中的某個) 時間段","examples":["...the hours of darkness. …夜間。","Phone us on this number during office hours. 上班時間給我們打這個電話。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>hours</b> involved in a job, you are talking about how long you spend each week doing it and when you do it. 工作時間","examples":["I worked quite irregular hours. 我的工作時間很不固定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>after hours</b>, you do it outside normal business hours or the time when you are usually at work. 辦公 (或營業) 時間之外","examples":["...a local restaurant where steel workers unwind after hours. …鋼鐵工人下班後去休息放鬆的一家當地餐館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>at all hours</b> <b>of</b> the day or night, you disapprove of it happening at the time that it does or as often as it does. 不分時候","examples":["She didn't want her fourteen-year-old daughter coming home at all hours of the morning. 她不希望自己14歲的女兒在半夜凌晨才回家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>in the early hours</b>, <b>in the small hours</b>, or <b>in the wee hours</b>, it happens in the early morning after midnight. 在凌晨","examples":["Gibbs was arrested in the early hours of yesterday morning. 吉布斯在昨天凌晨被捕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens <b>on the hour</b>, it happens every hour at, for example, nine o'clock, ten o'clock, and so on, and not at any number of minutes past an hour. 在整點","examples":["During this war in the Persian Gulf, NPR will have newscasts every hour on the hour. 在這場海灣戰爭期間，美國國家公共廣播電臺會進行整點新聞報道。"]}]}]},"human":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人的，人類的；（尤指缺點或弱點）顯示人的本性的；有人情味的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"人，人類"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Human</b> means relating to or concerning people. 人 (類) 的","examples":["...the human body. …人體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Human</b> feelings, weaknesses, or errors are ones that are typical of humans rather than machines. 人的 (感情、弱點); 人為的 (錯誤)","examples":["...an ever-growing risk of human error. …一種日益增長的人為誤差的風險。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to people as <b>humans</b>, especially when you are comparing them with animals or machines. 人 (類)","examples":["Like humans, cats and dogs are omnivores. 和人類一樣，貓和狗是雜食性動物。"]}]}]},"home":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家，住宅；（可買賣的）房子，寓所；家庭；養育院，收容所；適於存放……的地方；發源地，發祥地；棲息地，生息地；家鄉，祖國；（組織、公司等的）本部，基地；（比賽的）主場"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"家庭的，家用的；在家裡做（或進行）的；本國的，國內的；在主場進行的；<美>總部的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"回家，在家；到正確的位置；朝著球門，進入到球門裡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"歸巢；對準（目標）；把（思想、注意力）集中於；把（動物）養作寵物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>home</b> is the house or apartment where they live. 家","examples":["Last night they stayed at home and watched TV. 昨天晚上他們待在家裡看電視。","The general divided his time between his shabby offices and his home in Hampstead. 將軍的時間一部分在他那破舊的辦公室裡度過，另一部分在他漢普斯特德的家度過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>home</b> to refer in a general way to the house, town, or country where someone lives now or where they were born, often to emphasize that they feel they belong in that place. 家鄉; 祖國","examples":["She gives frequent performances of her work, both at home and abroad. 她經常在國內外演出自己的作品。","His father worked away from home for much of Jim's first five years. 在吉姆5歲前的大部分時間裡，他的爸爸離家在外地工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>home</b> is a large house or institution where a number of people live and are cared for, instead of living in their own houses or apartments. They usually live there because they are too old or ill to take care of themselves or for their families to care for them. 養育院; 養老院","examples":["It's going to be a home for handicapped children. 它將成為一家殘疾兒童福利院。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a family unit as a <b>home</b>. 家庭","examples":["She had, at any rate, provided a peaceful and loving home for Harriet. 她至少給哈麗雅特提供了一個寧靜的、充滿愛的家。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>home</b> <b>of</b> something, you mean the place where it began or where it is most typically found. 發源地","examples":["This southwest region of France is the home of claret. 法國西南部的這個地區是波爾多幹紅葡萄酒的產地。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you find a <b>home</b> <b>for</b> something, you find a place where it can be kept. 適於存放…的地方","examples":["The equipment itself is getting smaller, neater and easier to find a home for. 該裝置本身變得越來越小、越來越精巧，因而也就越來越便於存放。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When a sports team plays <b>at</b> <b>home</b>, they play a game on their own field, rather than on the opposing team's field. (體育比賽的) 主場","examples":["I scored in both games; we tied at home and beat them away. 我在兩場比賽中都進了球；我們在主場打成平局，在客場擊敗了他們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Home</b> means to or at the place where you live. 回家; 在家","examples":["His wife wasn't feeling too well and she wanted to go home. 他妻子感覺有些不舒服，想要回家。","I'll call you as soon as I get home. 我一到家就給你打電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you press, drive, or hammer something <b>home</b>, you explain it to people as forcefully as possible. 徹底地","examples":["It is now up to all of us to debate this issue and press home the argument. 現在要靠我們大家對這個問題進行辯論，並儘可能將論點闡釋清楚。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Home</b> means made or done in the place where you live. 在家裡做的或進行的","examples":["...cheap but healthy home cooking. …便宜卻健康的家常便飯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Home</b> means relating to your own country as opposed to foreign countries. 本國的","examples":["Europe's software companies still have a growing home market. 歐洲的軟體公司仍擁有一個不斷增長的本土市場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Home</b> is also an adjective. 主場的","examples":["All three are fans, and attend all home games together. 3個人都是球迷，並且都一起觀看了所有主場的比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>at home</b>, you feel comfortable in the place or situation that you are in. 舒適自在","examples":["He spoke very good English and appeared pleased to see us, and we soon felt quite at home. 他英語說得非常好，見到我們時顯得很高興，我們很快就感到毫無拘束。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>bring</b> something <b>home</b> <b>to</b> someone means to make them understand how important or serious it is. 使…清楚地領會 (重要性或嚴重性)","examples":["Their sobering conversation brought home to everyone present the serious and worthwhile work the Red Cross does. 他們的談話發人深省，使得在場的每個人都清楚地認識到紅十字會所做的嚴肅而有價值的工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>home free</b> you mean that they have been successful or that they are certain to be successful. 大功告成; 穩操勝券","examples":["Just when she thought she was home free, her father spoke from behind her. 就在她認為已經大功告成的時候，身後傳來她爸爸說話的聲音。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a situation or what someone says <b>hits home</b> or <b>strikes home</b>, people accept that it is real or true, even though it may be painful for them to realize. 被深刻領會","examples":["Did the reality of war finally hit home? 人們最終深刻認識到戰爭的現實了嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say <b>a home away from home</b> to refer to a place in which you are as comfortable as in your own home. 像家一樣舒適的地方","examples":["The café seems to be her home away from home these days. 這些天來，咖啡館似乎成了她的第二個家。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>nothing to write home about</b>, you mean that it is not very interesting or exciting. 平平常常","examples":["I see growth slightly up, but nothing to write home about. 我看到稍有增長，但也沒什麼令人激動的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something that is thrown or fired <b>strikes home</b>, it reaches its target. 打中目標","examples":["Only two torpedoes struck home. 只有兩枚魚雷擊中目標。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say to a guest \"<b>Make yourself at home</b>,\" you are making them feel welcome and inviting them to behave in an informal, relaxed way. 請別拘束","examples":["Take off your jacket and make yourself at home. 請脫下外套，隨便些。"]}]}]},"hundred":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一百；許多，數量大；一百美元（英鎊）的紙幣；百位數；（表示24小時制的整點）一點、兩點、三點等整；（板球）擊球手獲得的一百（或以上）的得分"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一百的；許多的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>hundred</b> or <b>one</b> <b>hundred</b> is the number 100. 100; 百","examples":["According to one official more than a hundred people have been arrested. 據一名官員說，已有一百多人被捕。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>hundreds of</b> things or people, you are emphasizing that there are very many of them. 許許多多; 數百","examples":["Hundreds of tree species face extinction. 很多樹種瀕臨滅絕。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also use <b>hundreds</b> as a pronoun. 成百上千","examples":["Hundreds have been killed in the fighting and thousands made homeless. 成百上千的人在戰鬥中喪生，並有成千上萬的人變得無家可歸。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>a hundred percent</b> or <b>one hundred percent</b> to emphasize that you agree completely with something or that it is completely right or wrong. 百分之百","examples":["Are you a hundred percent sure it's your neighbour? 你百分百肯定這是你的鄰居？"]}]}]},"house":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房子，住宅；一家人，同住一幢房子的人們；（有特定用途的）大樓，大廈；公司，商業機構；觀眾席，觀眾；演出場次；餐館，餐廳；豪斯音樂；王室，皇族（House）；（某些英國學校學生為進行比賽而分的）組；動物的籠舍；議院，議會；（占星）黃道十二宮之一，黃道宮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"讓……居住，給……提供住房；給……提供場地，收藏存放；包裹，覆蓋；住"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"家養的，常在室內的；公司的，機構的；（樂隊，組合）（在俱樂部或別的場所）常駐的，定期表演的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>house</b> is a building in which people live, usually the people belonging to one family. 房屋","examples":["She has moved to a small house and is living off her meagre savings. 她搬進了一幢小房子，靠自己微薄的積蓄過日子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to all the people who live together in a house as <b>the</b> <b>house</b>. 一家人; 同住一幢房子的人","examples":["If he set his alarm clock for midnight, it would wake the whole house. 如果他把鬧鐘設定在午夜，鈴聲會把全家人都吵醒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>House</b> is used in the names of types of places where people go to eat and drink. …館 (用於某些型別的餐館名稱中)","examples":["...a steak house. …一家牛排館。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>House</b> is used in the names of types of companies, especially ones which publish books, lend money, or design clothes. …公司 (用於某些型別的公司名稱中，尤其是出版、貸款或服裝設計等公司)","examples":["Many of the clothes come from the world's top fashion houses. 這些服裝中有很多來自世界頂級時裝設計公司。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to one of the two bodies of the U.S. Congress as a <b>House</b>. The House of Representatives is sometimes referred to as <b>the</b> <b>House</b>. (美國) 眾議院","examples":["Some members of the House and Senate worked all day yesterday. 昨天眾議院和參議院的一些議員工作了一整天。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A restaurant's <b>house</b> wine is the cheapest wine it sells, which is not listed by name on the wine list. 店酒 (某餐館沒有列在酒水單上的最便宜的葡萄酒)","examples":["Tweed ordered a carafe of the house wine. 特威德點了一瓶店酒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>house</b> someone means to provide a house or apartment for them to live in. 為…提供住房","examples":["...homes that house up to nine people. …最多可容納9人的住處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A building or container that <b>houses</b> something is the place where it is located or from where it operates. 給…提供場地","examples":["The building is open to the public and houses a museum of motorcycles and cars. 這座大樓對公眾開放，並設有一個摩托車和汽車博物館。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a building <b>houses</b> a number of people, you mean that is the place where they live or where they are staying. 供…居住","examples":["The building will house twelve boys and eight girls. 這棟房子要住12個男孩和8個女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or their performance or speech <b>brings the house down</b>, the audience claps, laughs, or shouts loudly because the performance or speech is very impressive or amusing. 博得全場喝彩","examples":["It's really an amazing dance. It just always brings the house down. 這個舞蹈簡直太精彩了。它總是博得全場喝彩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people <b>get on like a house on fire</b>, they quickly become close friends, for example because they have many interests in common. 一見如故","examples":["I went over and struck up a conversation, and we got on like a house on fire. 我走過去搭訕聊天，我們一見如故。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are given something in a restaurant or bar <b>on the house</b>, you do not have to pay for it. 由店家免費提供的","examples":["The owner knew about the engagement and brought them glasses of champagne on the house. 店主知道了他們訂婚的事，便免費請他們喝了幾杯香檳酒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>gets</b> their <b>house in order</b>, <b>puts</b> their <b>house in order</b>, or <b>sets</b> their <b>house in order</b>, they arrange their affairs and solve their problems. 把自己的事情處理妥當","examples":["He's got his house in order and made some tremendous decisions. 他已把自己的事情處理好，並做出了一些重大決定。"]}]}]},"husband":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"丈夫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"節約使用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A woman's <b>husband</b> is the man she is married to. 丈夫","examples":["Eva married her husband Jack in 1957. 1957年伊娃與其丈夫傑克結婚。"]}]}]},"hurt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使受傷，使疼痛；感到受傷，感到疼痛；損害；處於困境，手頭拮据；傷心"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（身體上）受傷的；（感情上）痛苦的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"心靈創傷，委屈；（身體上的）傷，痛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hurt</b> <b>yourself</b> or <b>hurt</b> a part of your body, you feel pain because you have injured yourself. 使受傷","examples":["Yasin had seriously hurt himself while trying to escape from the police. 亞辛在企圖從警方手中逃脫時把自己傷得很厲害。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hurt</b> someone, you cause them to feel pain. 弄痛","examples":["I didn't mean to hurt her, only to keep her still. 我沒想把她弄痛，只是想讓她別動。","That hurts! 好痛呀！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>hurts</b> you, they say or do something that makes you unhappy. 使傷心; 傷心","examples":["He is afraid of hurting Bessy's feelings. 他是怕傷了貝西的感情。","What hurts most is the betrayal. 最讓人傷心的是背叛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>hurt</b> someone or something means to have a bad effect on them or prevent them from succeeding. 對…產生不良影響","examples":["The combination of hot weather and decreased water supplies is hurting many industries. 天氣炎熱和供水減少這兩個因素結合在一起對很多行業造成了損害。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>hurts</b>, you feel pain there. 感到疼痛","examples":["His collar bone only hurt when he lifted his arm. 他的鎖骨只是在舉起手臂時才感覺疼痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>are hurting</b>, you mean that you are experiencing emotional pain. 感到痛苦的","examples":["I am lonely and I am hurting. 我很孤獨，也很痛苦。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>hurt</b>, you have been injured. 受了傷的","examples":["His comrades asked him if he was hurt. 他的夥伴們問他是否受傷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>hurt</b>, you are upset because of something that someone has said or done. (感情上) 受到傷害的","examples":["She was deeply hurt and shocked by what Smith had said. 史密斯的話深深地傷害了她，並使她感到吃驚。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A feeling of <b>hurt</b> is a feeling that you have when you think that you have been treated badly or judged unfairly. (感情上的) 傷心或痛苦","examples":["I was full of jealousy and hurt. 我內心充滿了嫉妒和痛苦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(Also whort)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>It won't hurt</b> <b>to</b> do something\" or \"<b>It never hurts</b> <b>to</b> do something,\" you are recommending an action which you think is helpful or useful. (做…) 不會有壞處","examples":["It never hurts to ask. 提問總沒壞處。"]}]}]},"ice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰；冰塊；冰凍甜食，刨冰；溜冰場；<美，非正式>鑽石，珠寶；（態度，表情）冰冷；<英>一份冰淇淋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（糕餅上）加糖霜；冷卻，冰鎮；<非正式>確保（勝利等）；<美，非正式>殺死；結冰；長射（冰球）過全場越過對方球門線"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冰的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ice</b> is frozen water. 冰","examples":["Glaciers are moving rivers of ice. 冰川是流動成河的冰。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ice</b> a cake, you cover it with icing. 在 (糕餅) 上裹糖霜","examples":["I've made the cake. I've iced and decorated it. 我做了蛋糕，給它裹上了糖霜並進行了裝飾。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>break the ice</b> at a party or meeting, or in a new situation, you say or do something to make people feel relaxed and comfortable. 打破僵局","examples":["That sort of approach should go a long way toward breaking the ice. 那種方法應該對打破僵局大有幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>cuts no ice</b> <b>with</b> you, you mean that you are not impressed or influenced by it. 不起作用","examples":["That sort of romantic attitude cuts no ice with moneymen. 那種羅曼蒂克的態度對金融家們不起作用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone puts a plan or project <b>on ice</b>, they delay doing it. 暫時擱置","examples":["There would be a three-month delay while the deal would be put on ice. 會有3個月的延誤，與此同時這筆交易也將暫時擱置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>on thin ice</b> or <b>is skating on thin ice</b>, you mean that they are doing something risky that may have serious or unpleasant consequences. 如履薄冰","examples":["I had skated on thin ice on many assignments and somehow had got away with it. 我曾在多項任務中都處於危險的境地，但不知怎麼地都化險為夷了。"]}]}]},"idea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"想法，主意；觀點，看法；原則，信念；理解，瞭解；猜想；目標，意圖；（柏拉圖哲學）理念"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>idea</b> is a plan, suggestion, or possible course of action. 主意; 打算","examples":["It's a good idea to have your blood pressure checked regularly. 定期檢查你的血壓是個好主意。","I really like the idea of helping people. 我非常喜歡幫助他人這個主意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>idea</b> is an opinion or belief about what something is like or should be like. 看法; 信念","examples":["Some of his ideas about democracy are entirely his own. 他對民主的一些看法完全是個人的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone gives you an <b>idea of</b> something, they give you information about it without being very exact or giving a lot of detail. 大致的資訊","examples":["This table will give you some idea of how levels of ability in a foreign language can be measured. 這個表格將告訴你一些如何衡量外語能力級別的大致資訊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have an <b>idea</b> of something, you know about it to some extent. (對某事有) 一定的瞭解","examples":["No one has any real idea how much the company will make next year. 沒有人真正知道公司明年將賺多少錢。","We had no idea what was happening. 我們不知道正在發生什麼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have an <b>idea</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you think that it may be the case, although you are not certain. 猜想","examples":["I had an idea that he joined the army later, after college, but I may be wrong. 我猜想他大學畢業後參了軍，不過我也許錯了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The idea</b> of an action or activity is its aim or purpose. 目的","examples":["The idea is to get industry to be more efficient in the way it uses energy. 目的是使工業在使用能源的方式上效率更高。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you have the <b>idea of</b> doing something, you intend to do it. 意圖","examples":["He sent for a number of books he admired with the idea of rereading them. 他訂購了許多他讚賞的書，打算再讀一遍。"]}]}]},"january":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>January</b> is the first month of the year in the Western calendar. 1月","examples":["We always have snow in January. 我們這裡1月份總會下雪。"]}]}]},"inch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英寸；（距離或數量）少許；<非正式>身高，腰圍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（數量）逐漸增加（或減少）；（使）緩慢移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inch</b> is an imperial unit of length, approximately equal to 2.54 centimetres. There are twelve inches in a foot. 英寸","examples":["...18 inches below the surface. …表層以下18英寸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a small island 小島","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>inch</b> somewhere means to move there very slowly and carefully, or to make something do this. 緩慢地移動; 使緩慢地移動","examples":["...a climber inching up a vertical wall of rock. …一個沿著陡峭的巖壁緩慢往上攀登的人。","He inched the van forward. 他駕著廂式貨車緩緩前行。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone looks <b>every inch</b> a certain type of person, you are emphasizing that they look exactly like that kind of person. 在各方面","examples":["He looks every inch the businessman, with his grey suit, dark blue shirt and blue tie. 他身穿灰色西服、深藍色襯衫、打著藍色領帶，在各方面儼然一副生意人的模樣。"]}]}]},"inside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部，內側；<非正式>內臟，（尤指）胃；裡道，內圈；（靠近路邊的）慢車道"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在（或向）裡面；在監牢裡"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（或向）……內，在（或向）……裡；在……時間之內；（足球、英式橄欖球等體育運動）（比另一隊員）更靠近球場中心"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"裡面的；從內部瞭解到的，內線乾的；（馬路車道）靠近路邊的，慢（道）的；（曲棍球、足球等體育運動）場地中心附近的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>inside</b> a place, container, or object is in it or is surrounded by it. 在…裡面; 在…內側","examples":["Inside the passport was a folded slip of paper. 護照裡面是一張摺疊的紙條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>inside</b> an organization, you belong to it. 在 (組織) 的內部","examples":["75 percent of chief executives come from inside the company. 75%的高層主管來自公司內部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also a preposition. 在…的心裡","examples":["He felt a great weight of sorrow inside him. 他感到沉重的悲痛壓在心口。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>inside</b> a particular time, you do it before the end of that time. 在 (某段時間) 之內","examples":["They should have everything working inside an hour. 他們應該在一小時之內讓一切都運轉起來。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also an adverb. 在裡面; 往裡面","examples":["The couple chatted briefly on the doorstep before going inside. 夫婦倆進屋前在門階上簡單地聊了幾句。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also an adverb. 在內部","examples":["The potato cakes can be shallow or deep-fried until crisp outside and meltingly soft inside. 薯餅可以微煎或熟炸，直到變得外脆內軟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that someone is <b>inside</b> when they are in prison. 在監牢裡","examples":["They've both done prison time – he's been inside three times. 他們倆都蹲過監獄–他蹲過3次。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has a feeling <b>inside</b>, you mean that they have it but have not expressed it. 在心裡","examples":["There is nothing left inside – no words, no anger, no tears. 心裡頭空落落的啥也沒留下–沒有話語，沒有憤怒，沒有眼淚。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also an adjective. 裡面的","examples":["...an inside wall. …一面內牆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also an adjective. 內部的","examples":["The popular papers all have photo features on their inside pages. 通俗報紙的內頁都有照片特寫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> information is obtained from someone who is involved in a situation and therefore knows a lot about it. (訊息) 內幕的","examples":["Sloane used inside diplomatic information to make himself rich. 斯隆利用外交內幕訊息發了財。","I cannot claim any inside knowledge of government policies. 我不能說自己瞭解政府政策的內幕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also an adjective. 內部的","examples":["...a recent book about the inside world of pro football. …最近的一本關於職業足球運動內幕的書。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>inside</b> of something is the part or area that its sides surround or contain. 裡面; 內部","examples":["The doors were locked from the inside. 門從裡面鎖住了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also a noun. 內部","examples":["McAvoy was convinced he could control things from the inside but he lost control. 麥卡沃伊深信他能夠從內部控制形勢，可他卻失去了控制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>insides</b> are your internal organs, especially your stomach. 內臟 (尤指胃)","examples":["Every pill made my insides turn upside down. 每片藥都使我的胃翻江倒海。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Inside</b> is also a noun. 內心","examples":["What is needed is a change from the inside, a real change in outlook and attitude. 所需要的是來自內心深處的改變，在觀點和態度上的真正改變。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a piece of clothing is <b>inside out</b>, the part that is normally inside now faces outward. 裡面朝外地","examples":["Her umbrella blew inside out. 她的傘被吹得往外翻了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you know something or someone <b>inside out</b>, you are emphasizing that you know them extremely well. 徹底地","examples":["He knew the game inside out. 他對這個遊戲瞭如指掌。"]}]}]},"iron":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鐵；熨斗；鐵器，鐵製工具；鐐銬；（矯正畸形腿的）夾腿；<非正式>馬蹬；隕鐵，鐵隕石；（高爾夫球）鐵頭球杆；剛強，毅力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"熨，燙"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鐵的，鐵製的；剛強的，堅強的；強硬的，嚴酷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Iron</b> is an element that usually takes the form of a hard, dark grey metal. It is used to make steel, and also forms part of many tools, buildings, and vehicles. Very small amounts of iron occur in your blood and in food. 鐵","examples":["The huge, iron gate was locked. 那扇巨大的鐵門被鎖上了。","...the highest grade iron ore deposits in the world. …世界上最優質的鐵礦床。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>iron</b> is an electrical device with a flat metal base. You heat it until the base is hot, then rub it over clothes to remove creases. 熨斗","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"熨燙","examples":["I managed to get all the ironing done this morning. 今天上午我設法把所有的衣物都熨了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>iron</b> clothes, you remove the creases from them using an iron. 熨","examples":["She used to iron his shirts. 她過去常給他熨襯衫。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>iron</b> to describe the character or behaviour of someone who is very firm in their decisions and actions, or who can control their feelings well. 堅強的","examples":["...a man of icy nerve and iron will. …一個頭腦冷靜、意志堅強的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Iron</b> is used in expressions such as <b>an iron hand</b> and <b>iron discipline</b> to describe strong, harsh, or unfair methods of control that do not allow people much freedom. 強硬的","examples":["He died in 1985 after ruling Albania with an iron fist for 40 years. 他用鐵腕統治了阿爾巴尼亞40年後，於1985年去世。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has a lot of <b>irons in the fire</b>, they are involved in several different activities or have several different plans. 同時要做的事情","examples":["Too many irons in the fire can sap your energy and prevent you from seeing which path to take. 同時做太多的事情可能會消耗你的精力，使你看不清該走哪條路。"]}]}]},"interest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"興趣，關注；吸引力，趣味；愛好；利息；利益，好處；權益，股權；利害關係，重要影響；利益集團，利益相關者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使感興趣，引起……的關注；勸說（某人）做（或參與）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>interest</b> <b>in</b> something, you want to learn or hear more about it. 興趣","examples":["There has been a lively interest in the elections in the last two weeks. 過去兩週人們對選舉一直有強烈的興趣。","She'd liked him at first, but soon lost interest. 最初她喜歡過他，但很快就失去了興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>interests</b> are the things that you enjoy doing. 愛好","examples":["Encourage your child in her interests and hobbies. 鼓勵你的孩子發展她的興趣和愛好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is in the <b>interests</b> of a particular person or group, it will benefit them in some way. 利益","examples":["Did those directors act in the best interests of their club? 那些董事們是從他們俱樂部的最大利益出發而行動的嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>interests</b> to refer to groups of people who you think use their power or money to benefit themselves. 利益集團","examples":["The government accused unnamed \"foreign interests\" of inciting the trouble. 政府不點名地指責一些“外國利益集團”煽動騷亂。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A person or organization that has an <b>interest</b> in an area, a company, a property or in a particular type of business owns stock in it. 股權","examples":["My father had many business interests in Vietnam. 我父親在越南有許多公司股權。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a person, country, or organization has an <b>interest</b> <b>in</b> a possible event or situation, they want that event or situation to happen because they are likely to benefit from it. 利害關係","examples":["The West has an interest in promoting democratic forces in Eastern Europe. 西方國家在促使東歐民主力量壯大中有利害關係。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Interest</b> is extra money that you receive if you have invested a sum of money. <b>Interest</b> is also the extra money that you pay if you have borrowed money or are buying something on credit. 利息","examples":["Does your current account pay interest? 你的活期存款賬戶計息嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>interests</b> you, it attracts your attention so that you want to learn or hear more about it or continue doing it. 使感興趣","examples":["Your financial problems do not interest me. 我對你的財務問題不感興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are trying to persuade someone to buy or do something, you can say that you are trying to <b>interest</b> them <b>in</b> it. 引起 (購買或做某事) 的意願","examples":["Can I interest you in a new car? 我給你介紹一下新車，你感興趣嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in the interests of</b> a particular result or situation, you do it in order to achieve that result or maintain that situation. 為了…的利益","examples":["...a call for all businessmen to work together in the interests of national stability. …為了國家穩定而向所有商人發出的共同合作的號召。"]}]}]},"july":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"七月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>July</b> is the seventh month of the year in the Western calendar. 7月","examples":["In July 1969, Neil Armstrong walked on the moon. 1969年7月，尼爾·阿姆斯特朗踏上了月球。"]}]}]},"joy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歡欣，高興；使人高興的人（或物），樂趣；成功，滿足"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"感到高興，感到欣喜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Joy</b> is a feeling of great happiness. 高興","examples":["Salter shouted with joy. 索爾特高興地叫起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>joy</b> is something or someone that makes you feel happy or gives you great pleasure. 使人高興的事; 使人高興的人","examples":["Spending evenings outside is one of the joys of summer. 在戶外消磨晚間時光是夏天的樂事之一。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is jumping for joy</b>, you mean that they are very pleased or happy about something. 興高采烈","examples":["He jumped for joy on being told the news. 聽到這個訊息他興高采烈。"]}]}]},"hold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抓住，托住；按住，捂住；擁抱；使保持（在某位置）；支撐……的重量；容納，包含；監禁，拘留；守衛，控制；（好形勢）保持不變；吸引某人的注意/興趣；（使）保持（價值或水平）；儲存，存貯；擁有；擔任，任職；獲得，贏得；持有，懷有（觀點、信念等）；認為，相信；舉行，進行；（車輛）抓（地）；（船或飛機）保持航線；持續（一種音符）；別結束通話；停下，推遲；有效，適用；（使）具有；大量喝（酒）而不醉；<美>不包括，排除在外；（使）堅持；<美，非正式>攜有違禁毒品"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"握，抓；擒拿法；影響，控制；支撐點；底艙，貨艙；預定；堅持，繼續擁有；理解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>hold</b> something, you carry or support it, using your hands or your arms. 拿著; 托住","examples":["Hold the knife at an angle. 斜握著刀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>hold</b> someone, you put your arms around them, usually because you want to show them how much you like them or because you want to comfort them. (常因想表示喜愛和安慰而) 抱住","examples":["If only he would hold her close to him. 他要是緊緊抱住她就好了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> someone in a particular position, you use force to keep them in that position and stop them from moving. 按住; 使不動","examples":["He then held the man in an armlock until police arrived. 然後他反扭手臂將那人按住，直到警察趕來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>hold</b> a part of your body, you put your hand on or against it, often because it hurts. (常指因疼痛而) 捂住","examples":["Soon she was crying bitterly about the pain and was holding her throat. 不一會兒她就疼得捂著喉嚨哭了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>hold</b> a part of your body in a particular position, you put it into that position and keep it there. 使 (自己身體某部位) 保持某種姿勢","examples":["Hold your hands in front of your face. 把雙手放在面前。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If one thing <b>holds</b> another in a particular position, it keeps it in that position. 使…保持 (在某位置) 不動","examples":["...the wooden wedge which held the heavy door open. …卡住沉重的門使之洞開著的木楔。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If one thing is used to <b>hold</b> another, it is used to store it. 存放","examples":["Two knife racks hold her favourite knives. 兩個刀架上放著她最喜愛的刀。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a place <b>holds</b> something, it keeps it available for reference or for future use. 儲備; 儲存","examples":["The Better Business Bureau holds an enormous amount of information on any business problem. 商業信用局儲存著有關任何商務問題的大量資訊。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something <b>holds</b> a particular amount of something, it can contain that amount. 容納得下","examples":["One CD-ROM disk can hold over 100,000 pages of text. 一張CD光碟能容納10萬多頁的文字資料。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with words and expressions indicating an opinion or belief, to show that someone has a particular opinion or believes that something is true. 持有 (觀點或信念等)","examples":["He held firm opinions which usually conflicted with my own. 他持有堅定的觀點，通常都與我的觀點相左。","Current thinking holds that obesity is more a medical than a psychological problem. 現代觀點認為肥胖更多是生理問題而不是心理問題。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with words such as \"fear\" or \"mystery\" to indicate someone's feelings toward something, as if those feelings were a characteristic of the thing itself. 有 (可怕、神秘的) 特質","examples":["Death doesn't hold any fear for me. 死亡對我來說沒什麼可怕的。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"office,\" \"power,\" and \"responsibility\" to indicate that someone has a particular position of power or authority. 擔任 (職務); 掌握 (權力); 承擔 (責任)","examples":["She has never held an elected office. 她從未擔任過由選舉產生的職務。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"permit,\" \"degree,\" or \"ticket\" to indicate that someone has a particular document that allows them to do something. 持有 (許可證、學位證、票據等)","examples":["Applicants should normally hold a good degree. 申請人通常應擁有優秀學位。","He did not hold a firearms licence. 他沒有持槍許可證。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"party,\" \"meeting,\" \"talks,\" \"election,\" and \"trial\" to indicate that people are organizing a particular activity. 舉行 (聚會、會議、會談、選舉和審判等)","examples":["The country will hold democratic elections within a year. 該國將在一年之內舉行民主選舉。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"shares\" and \"stock\" to indicate that someone owns a particular proportion of a business. 擁有 (股份、股票等)","examples":["The group said it continues to hold 1,774,687 shares in the company. 該集團說他們繼續持有這家公司1774687股的股份。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"attention\" or \"interest\" to indicate that what you do or say keeps someone interested or listening to you. 吸引住 (注意力); 保持 (興趣)","examples":["If you want to hold someone's attention, look them directly in the eye but don't stare. 如果你想吸引別人的注意力，就看著他們的眼睛，但不要死盯著看。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> someone responsible, liable, or accountable for something, you will blame them if anything goes wrong. 讓 (某人承擔責任)","examples":["It's impossible to hold any individual responsible. 不可能讓任何個人承擔責任。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If someone <b>holds</b> you in a place, they keep you there as a prisoner and do not allow you to leave. 扣留","examples":["The inside of a van was as good a place as any to hold a kidnap victim. 廂式小型貨車裡面像其他地方一樣是扣押被綁架者的好地方。","Somebody is holding your wife hostage. 有人在扣留你的妻子當人質。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If people such as an army or a violent crowd <b>hold</b> a place, they control it by using force. 佔據","examples":["Demonstrators have been holding the square since Sunday. 自星期天以來，示威者們一直佔據著廣場。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you ask someone to <b>hold</b>, or to <b>hold</b> <b>the line</b>, when you are answering a telephone call, you are asking them to wait for a short time, for example so that you can find the person they want to speak to. (打電話時) 不結束通話","examples":["Could you hold the line and I'll just get my pen. 請別結束通話，我去拿支筆，好嗎？"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> telephone calls for someone, you do not allow people who phone to speak to that person, but take messages instead. 代接 (電話) 並留言","examples":["He tells his secretary to hold his calls. 他讓他的秘書代接電話。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If something <b>holds</b> at a particular value or level, or <b>is held</b> there, it is kept at that value or level. 保持在 (在一定數值或水平)","examples":["OPEC production is holding at around 21.5 million barrels a day. 石油輸出國組織的石油產量目前保持在每天兩千一百五十萬桶左右。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> a sound or musical note, you continue making it. 持續發出 (聲音或音符)","examples":["...a voice which hit and held every note with perfect ease and clarity. …非常輕鬆而清晰地唱出每個音符的歌喉。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> something such as a train or a lift, you delay it. 延遲; 推遲","examples":["A spokesman defended the decision to hold the train until police arrived. 一位發言人為延遲火車發車直到警察到來的決定作了辯解。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If someone or something <b>holds</b> you <b>to</b> a promise or <b>to</b> high standards of behaviour, they make you keep that promise or those standards. 使…恪守 (諾言或高尚的行為準則)","examples":["\"I won't make you marry him.\" — \"I'll hold you to that.\" “我不會讓你嫁給他的。” — “我要你保證說話算話。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is also a noun. 拿; 托住","examples":["He released his hold on the camera. 他鬆開了握著照相機的手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used in expressions such as <b>grab hold of</b>, <b>catch hold of</b>, and <b>get hold of</b>, to indicate that you close your hand tightly around something, for example to stop something moving or falling. 抓住","examples":["I was woken up by someone grabbing hold of my sleeping bag. 有人抓住我的睡袋把我弄醒了。","A doctor and a nurse caught hold of his arms. 一名醫生和一名護士抓住了他的雙臂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hold</b> is a particular way of keeping someone in a position using your own hands, arms, or legs. 按住 (使某人不得動彈)","examples":["The man wrestled the Indian to the ground, locked in a hold he couldn't escape. 那人把印第安人摔倒在地，並將他死死按住，使他無法逃脫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In a ship or aeroplane, a <b>hold</b> is a place where cargo or luggage is stored. (船、飛機等的) 貨艙","examples":["A fire had been reported in the cargo hold. 據報告貨艙失火了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"舉行","examples":["They also called for the holding of multi-party general elections. 他們還呼籲舉行多黨大選。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have a <b>hold</b> <b>over</b> someone, you have power or control over them, for example because you know something about them you can use to threaten them or because you are in a position of authority. 對…有控制的力量","examples":["He had ordered his officers to keep an exceptionally firm hold over their men. 他已經命令軍官們要對他們的下屬保持極為嚴格的控制。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hold</b> is used with nouns such as \"conversation,\" \"interview,\" and \"talks\" to indicate that two or more people meet and discuss something. 進行 (談話、訪談等)","examples":["The prime minister is holding consultations with his colleagues to finalize the deal. 首相正和他的同僚進行磋商，以最終敲定這項協議。","The engineer and his son held frequent meetings concerning technical problems. 工程師和他的兒子經常就技術問題進行討論。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an offer or invitation still <b>holds</b>, it is still available for you to accept. (報價或邀請等) 有效","examples":["Does your offer still hold? 你的報價仍然有效嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a good situation <b>holds</b>, it continues and does not get worse or fail. (好的狀態) 保持不變","examples":["Our luck couldn't hold forever. 我們的好運不可能永遠保持不變。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an argument or theory <b>holds</b>, it is true or valid, even after close examination. (論點、理論等) 站得住腳","examples":["Today, most people think that argument no longer holds. 今天，大多數人認為這個論點不再站得住腳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If part of a structure <b>holds</b>, it does not fall or break although there is a lot of force or pressure on it. (在重壓下) 支撐住","examples":["How long would the roof hold? 這屋頂還能支撐多久？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If laws or rules <b>hold</b>, they exist and remain in force. (法規等) 有效","examples":["These laws also hold for universities. 這些法律同樣適用於大學。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>hold to</b> a promise or to high standards of behaviour, you keep that promise or continue to behave according to those standards. 遵守 (諾言或高尚的行為準則)","examples":["Will the president be able to hold to this commitment? 總統能恪守這一承諾嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hold up</b> means the same as <b>hold</b>. 站得住腳","examples":["Democrats say arguments against the bill won't hold up. 民主黨人說，反對這項議案的論點站不住腳。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hold forth</b> <b>on</b> a subject, you speak confidently and for a long time about it, especially to a group of people. (尤指當眾) 滔滔不絕地說","examples":["Barry was holding forth on something. 巴里正滔滔不絕地說著什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get hold of</b> an object or information, you obtain it, usually after some difficulty. (通常指克服困難後) 獲得","examples":["It is hard to get hold of guns in this country. 在這個國家很難弄到槍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>get hold of</b> someone, you manage to contact them. 設法與…聯絡","examples":["The only electrician we could get hold of was miles away. 我們惟一能夠聯絡上的電工在幾英里之外。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you put something <b>on hold</b>, you decide not to do it, deal with it, or change it now, but to leave it until later. 推遲","examples":["He put his retirement on hold to work 16 hours a day, seven days a week to find a solution. 為了找到一個解決方案，他推遲了退休，每週工作7天，每天工作16小時。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>hold</b> your <b>own</b>, you are able to resist someone who is attacking or opposing you. (面對攻擊或反對等) 頂住","examples":["The Frenchman held his own against the challenger. 那個法國人頂住了挑戰者的攻擊。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you can do something well enough to <b>hold</b> your <b>own</b>, you do not appear foolish when you are compared with someone who is generally thought to be very good at it. 與…相匹敵","examples":["She can hold her own against almost any player. 她幾乎能與所有選手相匹敵。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>hold still</b>, you do not move. 不動","examples":["Can't you hold still for a second? 你一秒鐘不動都不行？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>takes hold</b>, it gains complete control or influence over a person or thing. 完全控制 (某人或某物)","examples":["She felt a strange excitement taking hold of her. 她感到一種奇怪的興奮感控制住了自己。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>hold tight</b>, you put your hand around or against something in order to prevent yourself from falling over. A bus driver might say \"<b>Hold tight!</b>\" to you if you are standing on a bus when it is about to move. 抓牢","examples":["He held tight to the rope. 他緊緊抓住繩子。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>hold tight</b>, you do not immediately start a course of action that you have been planning or thinking about. 不輕易行動","examples":["The advice for individual investors is to hold tight. 給個人投資者的建議是不要輕舉妄動。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>Hold it</b>,\" you are telling someone to stop what they are doing and to wait. 停下","examples":["Hold it! Don't move! 停下！別動！"]}]}]},"juice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（水果和蔬菜的）汁，水果（蔬菜）汁飲料；肉汁；<美，非正式>電，電能；胃液；精力，活力；<美，非正式>權勢，影響力；<非正式>汽油；<美，非正式>酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"榨（果汁或蔬菜汁）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Juice</b> is the liquid that can be obtained from a fruit or vegetable. (果、蔬菜) 汁","examples":["...fresh orange juice. …新鮮橙汁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>juices</b> of a piece of meat are the liquid that comes out of it when you cook it. (肉) 汁","examples":["When cooked, drain off the juices and put the meat in a processor. 肉煮熟後，把汁控幹，然後放入加工機。"]}]}]},"joke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"笑話，玩笑；荒唐可笑的人（或事物），笑料；惡作劇，捉弄人的玩笑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"說笑話，開玩笑；取笑，開……的玩笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>joke</b> is something that is said or done to make you laugh, such as a funny story. 笑話; 玩笑","examples":["No one told worse jokes than Claus. 沒人比克勞斯講笑話講得更糟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>joke</b> is something untrue that you tell another person in order to amuse yourself. 說著玩的把戲","examples":["It was probably just a joke to them, but it wasn't funny to me. 這對他們來說可能只是說著玩，但對我來說一點也不好笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>a joke</b>, you think they are ridiculous and do not deserve respect. 可笑的人或事","examples":["It's ridiculous, it's pathetic, it's a joke. 這真是荒唐、可悲、可笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>joke</b>, you tell funny stories or say amusing things. 說笑話; 開玩笑","examples":["She would joke about her appearance. 她會拿她的長相開玩笑。","Luanne was laughing and joking with Tritt. 露安妮邊笑邊和特里特開著玩笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>joke</b>, you tell someone something that is not true in order to amuse yourself. 說著玩","examples":["Don't get defensive, Charlie. I was only joking. 不要有戒心，查理。我只是說著玩呢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make a joke of</b> something, you laugh at it even though it is in fact serious or sad. 拿…當玩笑","examples":["I wish I had your courage, Michael, to make a joke of it like that. 我真希望能有你那般勇氣，邁克爾，那樣拿它當玩笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>no joke</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very difficult or unpleasant. 不是鬧著玩的","examples":["Eight hours on a bus is no joke, is it. 坐８個小時的公交車可不是鬧著玩兒的，對吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that <b>the joke is on</b> a particular person, you mean that they have been made to look very foolish by something. 玩笑開在某人身上","examples":["\"For once,\" he said, \"the joke's on me. And it's not very funny.\" “只一次，”他說，“玩笑開在了我身上。而且那並不是很有趣。”"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>you're joking</b> or <b>you must be joking</b> to someone when they have just told you something that is so surprising or unreasonable that you find it difficult to believe. 你是在／你一定是在／你肯定是在開玩笑","examples":["You're joking. Are you serious? 你在開玩笑吧。你是認真的嗎？"]}]}]},"join":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"成為……的一員，參加；連線，接合；聯合，匯合；上（火車、飛機等）；和……作伴，隨同"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"連線處，接合點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person <b>joins</b> another, they move or go to the same place, for example, so that both of them can do something together. 和…一道","examples":["His wife and children moved to join him in their new home. 他的妻子和孩子們搬來和他一起住在新家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>join</b> an organization, you become a member of it or start work as an employee of it. 參加 (組織)","examples":["He joined the Army five years ago. 他５年前參了軍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>join</b> an activity that other people are doing, you take part in it or become involved with it. 參加 (活動)","examples":["The United States joined the war in April 1917. 美國於1917年4月參戰。","The pastor requested the women present to join him in prayer. 該牧師請在場的婦女和他一起祈禱。","Nine Republicans joined in supporting the measure. ９名共和黨人加入支援這項舉措。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>join</b> a line, you stand at the end of it so that you are part of it. 加入 (佇列)","examples":["It is advised that fans seeking autographs join the line before practice starts. 建議尋求親筆簽名的影迷們在活動開始前排好隊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>join</b> two things means to attach or fasten them together. 連線; 接合","examples":["The opened link is used to join the two ends of the chain. 這個開口環是用來連線鏈條兩頭的。","...the conjunctiva, the skin which joins the eye to the lid. …結膜，連線眼球和眼瞼的外膜。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something such as a line or path <b>joins</b> two things, it connects them. (線、路等) 連線 (兩物)","examples":["...a global highway of cables joining all the continents together. …一條連線各大洲的全球電纜主幹線路。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two roads or rivers <b>join</b>, they meet or come together at a particular point. 匯合","examples":["Do you know the motorway to Tulsa? The airport road joins it. 你知道通往塔爾薩的公路嗎？機場公路和它相連。"]}]}]},"job":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工作，職業；零工，任務；職責，責任；<非正式>罪行，（尤指）盜竊；<非正式> 東西，物件；費力的事；幸運的事；刺，捅；<非正式>東西，物件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"刺，捅；（尤指經紀人小規模操作）買賣股票；<非正式>欺騙，出賣；假公濟私，營私舞弊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>job</b> is the work that someone does to earn money. 工作","examples":["Once I'm in Miami I can get a job. 一旦我到了邁阿密就能找到工作。","Thousands have lost their jobs. 數千人都丟了工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>job</b> is a particular task. 任務","examples":["He said he hoped that the job of putting together a coalition wouldn't take too much time. 他說他希望結成聯盟這項任務不會花太長時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>job</b> of a particular person or thing is their duty or function. 職責","examples":["Their main job is to preserve health rather than treat illness. 他們的主要職責是保健而不是治病。","His first job will be to try and get talks going between the two sides. 他的首要職責將是設法讓雙方的談話進行下去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is doing a good <b>job</b>, you mean that they are doing something well. 活兒","examples":["We could do a far better job of managing it than they have. 我們會比他們管理得好得多。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you have <b>a</b> <b>job</b> doing something, you are emphasizing how difficult it is. 難做的事情","examples":["He may have a hard job selling that argument to investors. 他要讓投資者們接受那一觀點可能是件難事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>on the job</b>, they are actually doing a particular job or task. 在職; 在崗","examples":["The top pay scale after five years on the job would reach $5.00 an hour. 從事這一工作５年後最高薪金等級可達每小時$5。"]}]}]},"june":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"六月；瓊（女名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>June</b> is the sixth month of the year in the Western calendar. 6月","examples":["He spent two and a half weeks with us in June 1986. 1986年6月，他和我們呆了兩個半星期。","I am moving out on June 5th. 我將於6月5日搬出去。"]}]}]},"keeper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監護人，守護者；飼養員，牧人；看守人，門衛，管理員；店主，經營者；（體育）守門員；<非正式>值得保留的人或事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In American football, a <b>keeper</b> is a play in which the quarterback keeps the ball. (足球運動中) 守球","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>keeper</b> at a zoo is a person who takes care of the animals. (動物園) 飼養員","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>keeper</b> is something or someone that you value and that you feel is worth keeping. 值得保留的東西; 值得保留的人","examples":["The show's a keeper–daring, imaginative and provocative. 這部電影值得收藏–大膽、富於想像力和煽動性。","His sweet nature and kindness made him a keeper, she said. 她說他的可愛和善良使他成為值得珍視的人。"]}]}]},"kid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小孩，年輕人；小山羊；小山羊皮革"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"戲弄，開玩笑；欺騙，哄騙；（山羊）分娩"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較年幼的；小山羊皮製的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a child as a <b>kid</b>. 孩子","examples":["They've got three kids. 他們有三個孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>kid</b> is a young goat. 小山羊","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"soft smooth leather made from the hide of a kid 小山羊皮製品","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a small wooden tub 小木桶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are kidding</b>, you are saying something that is not really true, as a joke. 開玩笑","examples":["I'm not kidding, Frank. There's a cow out there, just standing around. 我不是在開玩笑，弗蘭克。那邊有一頭奶牛，就在那裡站著呢。","I'm just kidding. 我只是在開玩笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>kid</b> someone, you tease them. 戲弄","examples":["He liked to kid Ingrid a lot. 他很喜歡戲弄英格里德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>kid</b> <b>themselves</b>, they allow themselves to believe something that is not true because they wish that it was true. 欺騙 (自己)","examples":["We're kidding ourselves, Bill. We're not winning, we're not even doing well. 我們是在欺騙自己，比爾。我們不會贏的。我們做得甚至都不好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>you've got to be kidding</b>\" or \"<b>you must be kidding</b>\" to someone if they have said something that you think is ridiculous or completely untrue. 你一定是在開玩笑","examples":["You've got to be kidding! I can't live here! 你一定是在開玩笑！我不能住這兒！"]}]}]},"king":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"君主，國王；某物之王，首屈一指者；（國際象棋中的）王；極具影響；（紙牌中的）老K；（英國）男性國王在位時使用的國歌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>立……為王"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>king</b> is a man who is the most important member of the royal family of his country, and who is considered to be the head of state of that country. 君主; 國王","examples":["...the king and queen of Spain. …西班牙國王和王后。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a man as <b>the king of</b> something, you mean that he is the most important person doing that thing or he is the best at doing it. 首屈一指的男性; 佼佼者","examples":["He was the king of the cowboys. 他是牛仔之王。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>king</b> is a playing card with a picture of a king on it. (撲克牌的) 老(K)","examples":["...the king of diamonds. …方片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In chess, the <b>king</b> is the most important piece. When you are in a position to capture your opponent's king, you win the game. (國際象棋的) 王","examples":[]}]}]},"kill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"殺死；扼殺，終止；使痛苦，折磨；使減輕（疼痛）；消磨（時間），打發（時光）；使笑得前仰後合；（用開關）關閉；從檔案（或計算機）中刪除（行，段，檔案）；（英式足球或其他球類比賽）停（球）；扣（球）；中和，抵消（效果，性質）；喝光（一瓶酒）；使傾倒，使折服"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"殺死，捕殺；被捕殺的動物，獵物；（敵機、敵潛水艇等的）擊落，擊沉，撞毀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, animal, or other living thing <b>is killed</b>, something or someone causes them to die. 殺死","examples":["More than 1,000 people have been killed by the armed forces. 已經有一千多人被武裝部隊殺死。","He had attempted to kill himself on several occasions. 他好幾次都企圖自殺。","Drugs can kill. 毒品可以致死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>kills</b> a project, activity, or idea, they completely destroy or end it. 使停止; 扼殺","examples":["His objective was to kill the space station project altogether. 他的目的是使太空站計劃完全停止。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>kills</b> pain, it weakens it so that it is no longer as strong as it was. 緩解 (疼痛等)","examples":["He was forced to take opium to kill the pain. 他被迫服用鴉片止痛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is killing</b> you, you mean that it is causing you physical or emotional pain. 使痛得要命","examples":["My feet are killing me. 我的腳痛死了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>kill</b> <b>yourself to</b> do something, you are emphasizing that you make a great effort to do it, even though it causes you a lot of trouble or suffering. 拼命去做","examples":["I'm killing myself to get my work done. 我正在拼命完成我的工作。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that you will <b>kill</b> someone for something they have done, you are emphasizing that you are extremely angry with them. (因為極度憤怒而想要) 殺死","examples":["Tell Richard I'm going to kill him when I get hold of him. 告訴理查德，我要抓住他就殺了他。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something will not <b>kill</b> you, you mean that it is not really as difficult or unpleasant as it might seem. 難倒; 傷害","examples":["Three or four more weeks won't kill me! 再多上三四個星期也難不倒我。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>are killing</b> time, you are doing something because you have some time available, not because you really want to do it. 消磨 (時間)","examples":["I'm just killing time until I can talk to the other witnesses. 我正在消磨時間，直到能跟其他的證人交談。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"殺害","examples":["There is tension in the region following the killing of seven civilians. 7名平民被殺害後，該地區的局勢緊張。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The act of killing an animal after hunting it is referred to as <b>the</b> <b>kill</b>. 獵殺","examples":["After the kill the men and old women collect in an open space and eat a meal of whale meat. 獵殺結束後，男人們和年長的婦女們聚在一個空地吃了一頓鯨肉宴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kill off</b> means the same as . 使停止; 扼殺","examples":["He would soon launch a second offensive, killing off the peace process. 他將很快發起第二次攻擊，扼殺和平程序。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you will do something <b>if it kills</b> you, you are emphasizing that you are determined to do it even though it is extremely difficult or painful. 即使把命豁出去","examples":["I'll make this marriage work if it kills me. 即使把命豁出去，我也要使這婚姻成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>killed</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>laughing</b>, you are emphasizing that you laughed a lot because you thought something was extremely funny. 笑得要死","examples":["I eventually got to the top about an hour after everyone else, and they were all killing themselves laughing. 我終於在所有其他人之後又用了大概1小時到了頂部，他們都笑得要死。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>move in for the kill</b> or if you <b>close in for the kill</b>, you take advantage of a changed situation in order to do something that you have been preparing to do. 伺機而動","examples":["Seeing his chance, Dennis moved in for the kill. 看到機會來了，丹尼斯伺機而動。"]}]}]},"kitchen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廚房；一套廚具；<非正式>管絃樂隊中的打擊樂器組；（語言）不標準的，俚俗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kitchen</b> is a room that is used for cooking and for household jobs such as washing dishes. 廚房","examples":[]}]}]},"jump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳，躍；跨越；快速（突然）移動；猛地一動；激增，暴漲；突然轉換；略過；突然襲擊（某人）；歡躍，雀躍；逃離，逃避；插（隊）；<非正式>馬上照辦；跳吃（對方的棋子）；<非正式>與……性交；<美> 侵佔（他人開採權或土地）；（橋牌）跳叫；<美>跨接起動（汽車）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跳，躍；驚跳；障礙物；激增；鉅變；<非正式>心神不安；（橋牌）跳叫；<美，粗>性交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jump</b>, you bend your knees, push against the ground with your feet, and move quickly upward into the air. 跳","examples":["I jumped over the fence. 我從籬笆上跳了過去。","I'd jumped seventeen feet six in the long jump, which was a school record. 我跳遠曾跳了17.6英尺，這是個校紀錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>jump</b> from something above the ground, you deliberately push yourself into the air so that you drop toward the ground. 跳下","examples":["I jumped the last six feet down to the deck. 我跳下最後6英尺，到了甲板上。","He jumped out of a third-floor window. 他從3樓的一個視窗跳了出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>jump</b> something such as a fence, you move quickly up and through the air over or across it. 跳過","examples":["He jumped the first fence beautifully. 他漂亮地躍過了第一道籬笆。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an amount or level <b>jumps</b>, it suddenly increases or rises by a large amount in a short time. 猛增","examples":["Sales jumped from $94 million to over $101 million. 銷售額從9400萬美元猛增到超過1.01億美元。","The number of crimes jumped by ten percent last year. 犯罪數量去年猛增了10%。","Squibb shares jumped $2.50. 施貴寶的股票猛漲了$2.50。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>jumps</b> you, they attack you suddenly or unexpectedly. 突然襲擊","examples":["Half a dozen sailors jumped him. 6名水手突襲了他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jump</b> is also a noun. 跳","examples":["The longest jumps by a man and a woman were witnessed in Sestriere, Italy, yesterday. 男女跳遠專案最遠的一跳都於昨天在義大利的塞斯特雷得以見證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Jump</b> is also a noun. 猛增","examples":["A big jump in energy conservation could be achieved without much disruption of anyone's standard of living. 能源節約的一個大飛躍可以在不太影響任何人生活水平的前提下得以實現。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jump</b> somewhere, you move there quickly and suddenly. 跳起","examples":["Adam jumped from his seat at the girl's cry. 聽到女孩的哭聲，亞當從座位上跳起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>makes</b> you <b>jump</b>, it makes you make a sudden movement because you are frightened or surprised. 驚跳","examples":["The phone shrilled, making her jump. 電話突然響起，把她嚇了一跳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>jump at</b> an offer or opportunity, you accept it quickly and eagerly. 迫不及待地接受","examples":["Members of the public would jump at the chance to become part owners of the corporation. 公眾成員會迫不及待地抓住機會成為該公司的部分所有人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>jumps on</b> you, they quickly criticize you for doing something that they do not approve of. 立刻斥責","examples":["A lot of people jumped on me about that, you know. 很多人馬上就為那個指責我，你知道的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get a jump on</b> something or someone or <b>get the jump on</b> them, you gain an advantage over them. 勝過","examples":["Helicopters helped fire crews get a jump on the blaze. 直升機幫助救火人員控制住了火勢。"]}]}]},"key":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鑰匙；（電腦、打字機或樂器的）鍵；關鍵，要訣；答案；音調，聲調；圖例，符號說明；低島，礁；扳手；銷子，楔；（文章、形勢等）主調，基調；（梣樹、楓樹或無花果樹的）翼果；板條間首層灰泥；（有助於石膏等黏附的）粗糙表面；罰球區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鍵入；成為（獲勝）的關鍵；<非正式>用鑰匙劃壞（汽車）；用別針（或楔子、栓）固定；將……的表面處理好；給（廣告）加識別編碼"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"關鍵的，主要的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>key</b> is a specially shaped piece of metal that you place in a lock and turn in order to open or lock a door, or to start or stop the engine of a vehicle. 鑰匙","examples":["They put the key in the door and entered. 他們用鑰匙開了門然後走了進去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>keys</b> on a computer keyboard or typewriter are the buttons that you press in order to operate it. 鍵","examples":["Finally, press the Delete key. 最後，按刪除鍵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>keys</b> of a piano or organ are the long narrow pieces of wood or plastic that you press in order to play it. 琴鍵","examples":["...the black and white keys on a piano keyboard. …一架鋼琴鍵盤上的黑白琴鍵。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In music, a <b>key</b> is a scale of musical notes that starts on one specific note. 調","examples":["...the key of A minor. …A小調。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>key</b> on a map or diagram or in a technical book is a list of the symbols or abbreviations used and their meanings. 略語記號","examples":["You will find a key at the front of the book. 你在書的前面會看到一個略語記號。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>key</b> <b>to</b> a desirable situation or result is the way in which it can be achieved. 關鍵","examples":["The key to success is to be ready from the start. 成功的關鍵是從一開始就做好準備。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>key</b> is a small low island or reef, especially one in the Gulf of Mexico. (尤指墨西哥灣內的) 低島; 礁","examples":["...the Florida Keys. …佛羅里達群島。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>key</b> person or thing in a group is the most important one. 關鍵的","examples":["He is expected to be the key witness at the trial. 預計他將成為審判時的關鍵證人。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to scratch the paintwork of (a car) with a key 用鑰匙刮(汽車的)漆面","examples":[]}]}]},"kiss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"親吻，接吻；輕拂，輕觸；用唇輕觸（以示敬意）；（球）輕輕擦過（另一球）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吻，接吻；（一球與另一球的）輕擦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>kiss</b> someone, you touch them with your lips to show affection or sexual desire, or to greet them or say goodbye. 吻","examples":["She leaned up and kissed him on the cheek. 她靠過來吻了他的臉頰。","Her parents kissed her goodbye as she set off from their home. 當她動身離開家時，她的父母跟她吻別。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kiss</b> is also a noun. 吻","examples":["I put my arms around her and gave her a kiss. 我抱住她然後給了她一個吻。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>kisses</b> another thing, you mean that it touches that thing very gently. 輕觸","examples":["The wheels of the aircraft kissed the runway. 飛機的輪子擦過跑道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blow</b> someone <b>a kiss</b> or <b>blow a kiss</b>, you touch the palm of your hand lightly with your lips, and then blow across your hand toward the person, in order to show them your affection. 給…飛吻","examples":["Maria blew him a kiss. 瑪麗亞給了他一個飛吻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>kiss</b> something <b>goodbye</b> or <b>kiss goodbye to</b> something, you accept the fact that you are going to lose it, although you do not want to. 不捨地告別","examples":["I felt sure I'd have to kiss my dancing career goodbye. 我確實感到我將不得不告別自己的舞蹈生涯。"]}]}]},"kick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"踢，踢腿；對（自己）生氣；戒除（惡習）；踢球得分；（槍）射擊時後坐，朝……反衝；活躍，精力充沛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"踢，踢腿；極度興奮，極大的樂趣；（毒品或酒精的）效力，刺激性；突然的猛烈震動；（槍射擊時的）反衝，後坐力；（沙塵造成的）球的不規則運動；（賽跑接近終點時的）衝刺；有特定踢球能力的運動員；（一次）踢球（動作）；（玻璃瓶等的）凹底"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>kick</b> someone or something, you hit them forcefully with your foot. 踢","examples":["He kicked the door hard. 他用力踢門。","He threw me to the ground and started to kick. 他把我摔在地上開始踢我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>kick</b> a ball or other object, you hit it with your foot so that it moves through the air. 踢","examples":["I went to kick the ball and I completely missed it. 我去踢球卻踢空了。","He kicked the ball away. 他把球踢開了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>kick</b> or if you <b>kick</b> your legs, you move your legs with very quick, small, and forceful movements, once or repeatedly. 踢動","examples":["They were dragged away struggling and kicking. 他們又掙又踢地被拖走了。","First he kicked the left leg, then he kicked the right. 他先踢左腿，然後踢右腿。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>kick</b> your legs, you lift your legs up very high one after the other, for example when you are dancing. 高高踢起","examples":["...kicking his legs like a cancan dancer. …像康康舞演員一樣把他的腿高高踢起。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>kick</b> a habit, you stop doing something that is bad for you and that you find difficult to stop doing. 戒絕 (惡習)","examples":["She's kicked her drug habit and learned that her life has value. 她已經戒掉吸毒的惡習，懂得了她的生命有價值。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kick</b> is also a noun. 踢","examples":["He suffered a kick to the knee. 他的膝蓋被踢了一腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Kick</b> is also a noun. 踢","examples":["He missed an easy kick. 他錯失很容易的一腳球。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something gives you <b>a kick</b>, it makes you feel very excited or very happy for a short period of time. 極大的快感; 極度的興奮","examples":["I got a kick out of seeing my name in print. 看到我的名字被印成鉛字，我感到非常興奮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kick out</b> means the same as . 踢動","examples":["As its rider tried to free it, the horse kicked out and rolled over, crushing her. 當騎手設法把它放開的時候，那匹馬一陣踢，又一打滾，把她壓傷了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>kicks</b> you <b>when</b> you <b>are down</b>, you think they are behaving unfairly because they are attacking you when you are in a weak position. 落井下石","examples":["In the end I just couldn't kick Jimmy when he was down. 最後我就是不忍對吉米落井下石。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>for kicks</b>, you mean that they do it because they think it will be exciting. 為了追求刺激","examples":["They made a few small bets for kicks. 為了追求刺激，他們下了幾個小賭注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is dragged <b>kicking and screaming</b> <b>into</b> a particular course of action, you are emphasizing that they are very unwilling to do what they are being made to do. 極不情願","examples":["He had to be dragged kicking and screaming into action. 他非要被強迫著極不情願地去做事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe an event as <b>a kick in the teeth</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very disappointing and upsetting. 重大打擊","examples":["We've been struggling for years and it's a real kick in the teeth to see a new band make it ahead of us. 我們一直奮鬥了很多年，看到一個新樂隊在我們之前成功，這對我們是個重大打擊。"]}]}]},"kind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"種類；同類的人；特徵，性質；聖餐的聖體（指麵包或葡萄酒）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寬容的，體貼的，親切友好的；溫和的，無害的；關愛的，好心的（尤用於答謝語中）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a particular <b>kind</b> <b>of</b> thing, you are talking about one of the types or sorts of that thing. 種類","examples":["The party needs a different kind of leadership. 該黨需要一種不同的領導。","Had Jamie ever been in any kind of trouble? 傑米曾經遇到過什麼樣的麻煩嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>kind</b>, you are referring to all the other people that are like them or that belong to the same class or set. 同一類的人","examples":["I can take care of your kind. 我能對付你這類人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>all kinds of</b> to emphasize that there are a great number and variety of particular things or people. 各種各樣的","examples":["Adoption can fail for all kinds of reasons. 收養可能因為各種各樣的原因失敗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>kind of</b> when you want to say that something or someone can be roughly described in a particular way. 有點","examples":["It was kind of sad, really. 這真的有點傷感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone or something as <b>one of a kind</b>, you mean that there is nobody or nothing else like them. 獨一無二的","examples":["She's a very unusual woman, one of a kind. 她是個很不平常的女人，獨一無二。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer, for example, to <b>two, three,</b> or <b>four of a kind</b>, you mean two, three, or four similar people or things that seem to go well or belong together. 兩/三/四個同一類的人","examples":["They were two of a kind, from the same sort of background. 他們兩個是一類人，來自相同的背景。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you respond <b>in kind</b>, you react to something that someone has done to you by doing the same thing to them. 以同樣的方式","examples":["They hurled defiant taunts at the riot police, who responded in kind. 他們對著防暴警察憤然大罵，對方也以牙還牙。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you pay a debt <b>in kind</b>, you pay it in the form of goods or services and not money. 以貨代款; 以服務代款","examples":["...benefits in kind. …實物形式的收益。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>of a kind</b> to indicate that something is not as good as it might be expected to be, but that it seems to be the best that is possible or available. 差強人意的一種","examples":["She finds solace of a kind in alcohol. 她在酒精裡勉強找到一點安慰。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>kind</b> behaves in a gentle, caring, and helpful way toward other people. 和藹的; 仁慈的; 樂於助人的","examples":["I must thank you for being so kind to me. 真要感謝您對我這麼好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>kind</b> in expressions such as <b>please be so kind as to</b> and <b>would you be kind enough to</b> in order to ask someone to do something in a firm but polite way. 用於(please be so kind as to)和(would you be kind enough to)中，表堅定而禮貌的命令","examples":["Please be so kind as to see to it that all the alterations are made at once! 請注意所有變更必須馬上完成！"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"和藹地; 仁慈地; 樂於助人地","examples":["\"You seem tired this morning, Jenny,\" she said kindly. “今天早上你看起來有些疲倦，詹妮，”她和藹地說道。"]}]}]},"kitten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小貓；（某些其他動物）幼崽（如兔和海狸）；一種灰白色舟蛾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（貓、某些其他動物）產仔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kitten</b> is a very young cat. 小貓","examples":[]}]}]},"kite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風箏；鳶（猛禽）；<非正式>空頭支票，非法支票；<非正式>大三角帆；非法（或秘密）的信件（便條）；風箏形四邊形；<古>剝削者，掠奪者；<英，非正式>飛機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"增加（費用）；飛，飛奔；<美，非正式>使用（非法支票）騙錢，塗改（支票）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kite</b> is an object, usually used as a toy, which is flown in the air. It consists of a light frame covered with paper or cloth and has a long string attached which you hold while the kite is flying. 風箏","examples":["Willy asks if I've ever flown a kite before. 威利問我以前是否放過風箏。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any diurnal bird of prey of the genera <b>Milvus, Elanus,</b> etc, typically having a long forked tail and long broad wings and usually preying on small mammals and insects: family <b>Accipitridae</b> (hawks, etc) 鷹科晝行的鳥","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>as high as a kite</b>, you mean that they are very excited or that they are greatly affected by alcohol or drugs. 如痴如狂的; 因飲酒或吸毒而飄飄然的","examples":["The steroids made me feel so strange. I was as high as a kite some of the time. 類固醇令我感覺很奇特。有時我感到飄飄然。"]}]}]},"kitty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>小貓，貓咪（也用作對貓的暱稱或呼喚語）；公共儲金，共同資金；（賭博等）賭注總額，獎金池"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kitty</b> is an amount of money gathered from several people, which is meant to be spent on things that these people will share or use together. 公共儲金","examples":["You haven't put any money in the kitty for three weeks. 你已經3個星期不交公共儲金了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>kitty</b> is the total amount of money which is bet in a gambling game, and which is taken by the winner or winners. (賭博中贏家獲得的) 全部賭注","examples":["Each month the total prize kitty is $13.5 million. 每月全部的賭注獎金是1350萬美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>kitty</b> is a cat, especially a young cat. 小貓","examples":["...a cute little kitty. …一隻可愛的小貓。","...kitty litter made of wood shavings. …刨花做的貓砂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Kitty</b> is sometimes used as an affectionate way of referring to a cat or a kitten. 貓咪","examples":["\"Gertie!\" the kids were calling into the garden. \"Here kitty, kitty, kitty!\" “格蒂！”孩子們衝著院子裡喊，“貓咪，貓咪，貓咪過來！”"]}]}]},"knee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膝蓋，膝關節；（褲子的）膝部；（坐下時）大腿朝上的面；膝蓋的猛擊；（木船上的）肘板，肘材；曲線圖的彎曲處，拐點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用膝蓋頂（撞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>knee</b> is the place where your leg bends. 膝","examples":["He will receive physical therapy on his damaged left knee. 他受損的左膝將接受理療。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>on</b> your <b>knee</b> or <b>on</b> your <b>knees</b>, they are resting or sitting on the upper part of your legs when you are sitting down. (坐著時) 大腿上部","examples":["He sat with the package on his knees. 他坐著，包放在大腿上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> your <b>knees</b>, your legs are bent and your knees are on the ground. 膝部","examples":["She fell to the ground on her knees and prayed. 她跪在地上祈禱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knee</b> someone, you hit them using your knee. 用膝蓋撞擊","examples":["Ian kneed him in the groin. 伊恩用膝蓋撞擊他的腹股溝。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country or organization <b>is brought to its knees</b>, it is almost completely destroyed by someone or something. 徹底擊敗; 使屈服","examples":["The country was being brought to its knees by the loss of 2.4 million manufacturing jobs. 該國由於失去240萬製造業工作機會，瀕臨崩潰。"]}]}]},"lack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺乏，不足"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"缺乏，不足；需要"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>lack</b> <b>of</b> something, there is not enough of it or it does not exist at all. 缺乏; 不存在","examples":["Despite his lack of experience, he got the job. 儘管缺乏經驗，他還是得到了那份工作。","The charges were dropped for lack of evidence. 由於缺少證據，起訴被撤銷了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>lacks</b> a particular quality or that a particular quality <b>is lacking</b> in them, you mean that they do not have any or enough of it. 缺乏; 沒有","examples":["It lacked the power of the Italian cars. 它沒有義大利汽車那樣的動力。","He lacked the judgment and political acumen for the post of chairman. 他缺少作為主席的判斷力和政治敏銳性。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say there is <b>no lack of</b> something, you are emphasizing that there is a great deal of it. 不缺某物","examples":["He said there was no lack of things for them to talk about. 他說他們不缺話題談。"]}]}]},"knife":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餐刀；刀子，刀具，匕首；手術刀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用刀傷害（或殺害）；如刀般劃過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>knife</b> is a tool for cutting or a weapon and consists of a flat piece of metal with a sharp edge on the end of a handle. 刀","examples":["...a knife and fork. …一副刀叉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>knife</b> someone means to attack and injure them with a knife. 用刀砍","examples":["Dawson takes revenge on the man by knifing him to death. 道森向那人報仇，用刀砍死了他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>twist the knife in someone's wound</b>, you do or say something to make an unpleasant situation they are in even more unpleasant. 在某人傷口上撒鹽","examples":["Hearing his own plans was like having a knife twisted in his wound. 聽到他自己的計劃就像是有人在自己傷口上撒鹽。"]}]}]},"keep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）保持，（使）留在；繼續，重複；耽擱，延誤；保有，留下；存放，儲存；經營，管理；保鮮；保守（秘密）；遵守；記錄，記載；飼養；供養；保護；（按規定）紀念，慶祝；守門；尊重（法律或習俗）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"生活必需品，生活費用；城堡主樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>keeps</b> or <b>is kept</b> in a particular state, they remain in it. 保持 (特定狀態)","examples":["The noise kept him awake. 噪音使他一直醒著。","People had to burn these trees to keep warm during harsh winters. 在寒冷的冬天，人們得靠燒這些樹保暖。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> or you <b>are kept</b> in a particular position or place, you remain in it. 留在","examples":["Keep away from the doors while the train is moving. 列車執行時請遠離車門。","He kept his head down, hiding his features. 他一直低著頭藏住臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> doing something, you do it repeatedly or continue to do it. 繼續","examples":["I keep forgetting it's December. 我總是忘了現在是12月份。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Keep</b> is used with some nouns to indicate that someone does something for a period of time or continues to do it. For example, if you <b>keep a grip</b> <b>on</b> something, you continue to hold or control it. 繼續 (持有或控制)","examples":["Until last year, the regime kept a tight grip on the country. 直到去年，該政權一直牢牢地控制著這個國家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> something, you continue to have it in your possession and do not throw it away, give it away, or sell it. 保留","examples":["We must decide what to keep and what to give away. 我們必須決定哪些該留、哪些該扔。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> something in a particular place, you always have it or store it in that place so that you can use it whenever you need it. 儲存","examples":["She kept her money under the mattress. 她把錢存放在床墊下面。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>keep</b> something such as a promise or an appointment, you do what you said you would do. 信守","examples":["I'm hoping you'll keep your promise to come for a long visit. 我希望你會信守諾言，來這裡多呆一段時間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> a record of a series of events, you write down details of it so that they can be referred to later. 記錄","examples":["Eleanor began to keep a diary. 埃莉諾開始記日記了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone or something <b>keeps</b> you <b>from</b> a particular action, they prevent you from doing it. 阻止","examples":["Embarrassment has kept me from doing all sorts of things. 難為情使得我什麼也做不了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone or something <b>keeps</b> you, they delay you and make you late. 耽擱","examples":["Sorry to keep you, Jack. 抱歉耽擱你了，傑克。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> something <b>from</b> someone, you do not tell them about it. 隱瞞","examples":["She knew that Gabriel was keeping something from her. 她知道加布裡埃爾正有事瞞著她。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> animals, you own them and take care of them. 飼養","examples":["I've brought you some eggs. We keep chickens. 我給你帶來了些雞蛋。我們養著一些雞。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> yourself or <b>keep</b> someone else, you support yourself or the other person by earning enough money to provide food, clothing, money, and other necessary things. 撫養","examples":["She could just about afford to keep her five kids. 她勉強能撫養她的5個孩子。","I just cannot afford to keep myself. 我連自己也養活不了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> <b>off</b> something or <b>keep</b> <b>away from</b> it, you avoid it. If you <b>keep</b> <b>out of</b> something, you avoid getting involved in it. 避開","examples":["I managed to stick to the diet and keep off sweet foods. 我設法堅持節食，不吃甜食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If food <b>keeps</b> for a certain length of time, it stays fresh and suitable to eat for that time. 保鮮","examples":["Whatever is left over may be put into the refrigerator, where it will keep for 2-3 weeks. 所有吃剩下的東西都可以放進冰箱，可保鮮2至3周。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say or ask how someone <b>is keeping</b> as a way of saying or asking whether they are well. 保持健康","examples":["She hasn't been keeping too well lately. 她最近身體一直不太好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Keep on</b> means the same as <b>keep</b>. 繼續","examples":["Did he give up or keep on trying? 他是放棄了，還是在繼續努力？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep at it</b>, you continue doing something that you have started, even if you are tired and would prefer to stop. 堅持","examples":["It may take a number of attempts, but it is worth keeping at it. 可能需要多次嘗試，但這件事值得堅持做下去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep going</b>, you continue moving along or doing something that you have started, even if you are tired and would prefer to stop. 堅持下去","examples":["She forced herself to keep going. 她強迫自己堅持下去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is <b>in keeping</b> <b>with</b> another, it is suitable in relation to that thing. If one thing is <b>out of keeping</b> <b>with</b> another, you mean that it is not suitable in relation to that thing. 與… (不) 一致","examples":["This is not in keeping with our objective of representing the community. 這與我們代表該社群的目標不一致。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>keep it up</b>, you continue working or trying as hard as you have been in the past. 堅持不懈","examples":["There are fears that he will not be able to keep it up when he gets to the particularly demanding third year. 有人擔心到了極其艱難的第3年他會堅持不下去的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> something <b>to</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do not tell anyone else about it. 對某事守口如瓶","examples":["I have to tell someone. I can't keep it to myself. 我得告訴別人。我不能對此守口如瓶。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>keep to</b> <b>yourself</b>, you stay on your own most of the time and do not mix socially with other people. 不與人交往","examples":["He was a quiet man who always kept to himself. 他不愛說話，總是獨來獨往。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>keep</b> is the cost of food and other things that they need in their daily life. 生活費","examples":["Ray will earn his keep on local farms while studying. 學習期間，雷將在當地農場掙取生活費。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>keep</b> is the main tower of a medieval castle, in which people lived. 中世紀城堡主樓","examples":["...the first stone-built castle keep in Britain. …英國第一座石建中世紀城堡主樓。"]}]}]},"lamb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羔羊，小羊；羊羔肉；<非正式>寶貝，乖乖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"產羊羔；照看（產羔母羊）；<非正式> 慫恿（某人）大筆花錢（尤指花錢縱酒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lamb</b> is a young sheep. 羔羊","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lamb</b> is the flesh of a lamb eaten as food. 羔羊肉","examples":["Laura was basting the leg of lamb. 勞拉正在往烤羔羊腿上塗油。"]}]}]},"lamp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燈，光源；（用於醫療和科研的）發熱燈，照射器；靈感的源泉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"照明，照亮；<文>發光；燈下捕獵（尤指捕兔）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lamp</b> is a light that works by using electricity or by burning oil or gas. 燈","examples":["She switched on the bedside lamp. 她開啟了床頭燈。"]}]}]},"lady":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤為表示禮貌或尊敬的指稱）女士；淑女； （尤用於稱呼或談及不認識的女子）女士；<美> （不尊重的非正式稱呼）女人；（尤指舊時上層階級的）貴婦；（在英國用作對女貴族或爵士妻子的稱謂）夫人（Lady）；女廁所（the ladies）；（羅馬天主教常用）聖母（Our Lady）；對同屬議會下院女議員的敬稱；女主人；<舊>妻子（one's lady）；女友，女情人（=lady friend）；<史>騎士或男子願為之效勞的女人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lady</b> when you are referring to a woman, especially when you are showing politeness or respect. 女士","examples":["She's a very sweet old lady. 她是一位非常親切的老太太。","...a cream-coloured lady's shoe. …一隻奶黃色的女鞋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"\"<b>Lady</b>\" is sometimes used by men as a form of address when they are talking to a woman that they do not know, especially in stores and on the street. 女士 (對陌生女子的稱呼)","examples":["What seems to be the trouble, lady? 有什麼麻煩嗎，女士？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In Britain, <b>Lady</b> is a title used in front of the names of some female members of the nobility, or the wives of knights. (在英國用在女貴族成員或爵士妻子名前) 夫人; 小姐","examples":[]}]}]},"leader":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"領導者，首領；領先者，佼佼者；首席小提琴手；指揮；社論；<美>（報紙的）要聞，頭條；（膠捲，磁帶的）空白段；（漁線）接鉤繩；（植物的）頂枝；（尤指表格中的）指向符"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>leader</b> of a group of people or an organization is the person who is in control of it or in charge of it. 領導人","examples":["We now need a new leader of the party and a new style of leadership. 我們現在需要一個新的政黨領導人和一種新的領導風格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>leader</b> at a particular point in a race or competition is the person who is winning at that point. 領先者","examples":["The leaders came in two minutes clear of the field. 領先的選手們早兩分鐘到達終點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>leader</b> of an orchestra is the most senior violin player, who acts as a deputy to the conductor. (交響樂團的)首席小提琴手","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A leader in a newspaper is a piece of writing which gives the editor's opinion on an important news item. (報紙上的)社評","examples":[]}]}]},"leaf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葉，葉子；紙頁，書頁；薄金屬片，（尤指金或銀）箔；活動桌板；（窗，門等）扇；空心牆（或雙層窗）的內面（或外面）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"長新葉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>leaves</b> of a tree or plant are the parts that are flat, thin, and usually green. Many trees and plants lose their leaves in the winter and grow new leaves in the spring. 葉子","examples":["In the garden, the leaves of the horse chestnut had already fallen. 園子裡的七葉樹已經落葉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>leaf</b> is one of the pieces of paper of which a book is made. 一頁","examples":["He flattened the wrappers and put them between the leaves of his book. 他撫平了包裝紙，把它們夾在了書頁中間。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are going to <b>turn over a new leaf</b>, you mean that you are going to start to behave in a better or more acceptable way. 開始新的一頁","examples":["He realized he was in the wrong and promised to turn over a new leaf. 他認識到自己錯了，承諾要重新開始。"]}]}]},"land":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陸地，地面；土地（尤指耕地或建築用地）；地產，地皮；農耕，農村生活；國度，國土；想象（或虛構）的地方；（槍炮）陽膛線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"著陸，降落；使（飛機）平穩著陸；登陸，上岸；（從船或飛機上）卸下（貨物）；落下，跌落；<非正式>使陷入（困境）；<非正式>（令人不快的事）突然出現；<非正式>（尤指輕而易舉或意外地）獲得；打中（一拳）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Land</b> is an area of ground, especially one that is used for a particular purpose such as farming or building. 土地","examples":["Good agricultural land is in short supply. 肥沃的農業用地短缺。","...160 acres of land. …160英畝土地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an area of land which someone owns as their <b>land</b> or their <b>lands</b>. 地產","examples":["Their home is on his father's land. 他們的家坐落在他父親的土地上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about <b>the land</b>, you mean farming and the way of life in farming areas, in contrast to life in the cities. 農村生活","examples":["Living off the land was hard enough at the best of times. 即使是在最好的時期靠種地生活也是很艱難的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Land</b> is the part of the world that consists of ground, rather than sea or air. 陸地","examples":["It isn't clear whether the plane went down over land or sea. 不清楚飛機是落在陸地上還是海里。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>land</b> to refer to a country in a poetic or emotional way. 國家","examples":["...America, land of opportunity. …美國，充滿機會的國度。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>lands</b>, they come down to the ground after moving through the air or falling. 降落","examples":["He was sent flying into the air and landed 20 feet away. 他被拋入空中，在20英尺以外落地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>lands</b> somewhere, it arrives there unexpectedly, often causing problems. 意外出現","examples":["Two days later the book had already landed on his desk. 兩天後，這本書意外地出現在了他的桌子上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>lands</b> a plane, ship, or spacecraft, or when it <b>lands</b>, it arrives somewhere after a journey. 抵達","examples":["The jet landed after a flight of just under three hours. 這架噴氣式飛機在僅僅不到三個小時的飛行後就抵達了。","He landed his troops on the western shore. 他的部隊抵達了西海岸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>land</b> <b>in</b> an unpleasant situation or place or if something <b>lands</b> you <b>in</b> it, something causes you to be in it. 陷入 (不愉快境地)","examples":["He landed in a psychiatric ward. 他住進了精神病病房。"]}]}]},"left":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"左邊的；剩餘的；左派的，左翼的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在左面，向左"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"左側，左方（the left）；左邊的道路，左側的通道；（認為應將財產、金錢和權力更平等地分配的）左翼人士，左派組織（the Left）；（尤指拳擊中的）左手拳；（在足球或類似運動中面向對手球門的）左半場；（軍隊的）左翼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"離開（某人或某處）；拋棄，丟棄；不立刻做（leave 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Left</b> is the past tense and past participle of <b>leave</b>. (leave)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a certain amount of something <b>left</b>, or if you have a certain amount of it <b>left</b>, it remains when the rest has gone or been used. 剩下的","examples":["Is there any gin left? 還有杜松子酒嗎？","They still have six games left to play. 他們還剩下6場比賽要打。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>left</b> arm, leg, or ear, for example, is the one which is on the left side of your body. Your <b>left</b> shoe or glove is the one which is intended to be worn on your left foot or hand. 左邊的","examples":["Ferdinand landed awkwardly on top of Delgado's right boot and twisted his left leg. 費迪南笨拙地落地，踩在德爾加多的右靴上，扭傷了左腿。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a certain amount of something <b>left over</b>, or if you have it <b>left over</b>, it remains when the rest has gone or been used. 剩餘","examples":["So much income is devoted to monthly mortgage payments that nothing is left over. 這麼多的收入都用來償還每月的抵押貸款了，因此沒什麼剩餘。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>left</b> is one of two opposite directions, sides, or positions. If you are facing north and you turn to the left, you will be facing west. In the word \"to,\" the \"t\" is to the left of the \"o.\" 左邊","examples":["Go back to the last fork in the road and take a left. 回到路的上一個岔口，然後左轉。","...the brick wall to the left of the conservatory. …溫室左邊的磚牆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the U.S., <b>the left</b> refers to people who want to use legislation and the tax system to improve social conditions. In most other countries, <b>the left</b> refers to people who support the ideas of socialism. 左派","examples":["...the traditional parties of the Left. …傳統的左派政黨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a person or political party has moved <b>to the</b> <b>left</b>, you mean that their political beliefs have become more left-wing. 左傾","examples":["After 1979, the party moved sharply to the left. 1979年以後，該黨迅速左傾。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Left</b> is also an adverb. 向左地","examples":["Turn left at the crossroads into Clay Lane. 在十字路口向左轉到克萊路上。"]}]}]},"laugh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"笑，發笑；嘲笑，不以為然；愉悅地說；用嘲笑使（某人）離開；（特別表示因成功而）處於有利地位"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"笑，笑聲；令人開心的時刻；引人發笑的人或事，笑料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>laugh</b>, you make a sound with your throat while smiling and show that you are happy or amused. People also sometimes laugh when they feel nervous or are being unfriendly. 笑","examples":["He was about to offer an explanation, but she was beginning to laugh. 他剛要加以解釋，她就開始笑起來了。","I just couldn't laugh at his jokes the way I used to. 我就是不能像以前那樣笑他講的笑話。","\"We could do with some help from our friends,\" he laughed. “如果我們朋友來幫助就好了，”他笑著說道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Laugh</b> is also a noun. 笑","examples":["Lysenko gave a deep rumbling laugh at his own joke. 李森科對自己講的笑話報以朗聲大笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>laugh at</b> someone or something, they mock them or make jokes about them. 嘲笑","examples":["I thought they were laughing at me because I was ugly. 我想他們在嘲笑我長得醜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>for a laugh</b> or <b>for laughs</b>, you do it as a joke or for fun. 為了開玩笑","examples":["They were persuaded onstage for a laugh. 為了開開玩笑，他們被說服登上了臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>a laugh</b> or <b>a good laugh</b>, you think that it is fun and do not take it too seriously. 有趣的事","examples":["Working there's great. It's a good laugh. 在那裡工作很棒，是一件有趣的事情。"]}]}]},"law":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"法律（體系）；法令，法規；規律，法則，定律；法學，法律學；司法界，律師業；（道德或宗教上的）準則，守則；警方，警察"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"起訴，控告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The law</b> is a system of rules that a society or government develops in order to deal with crime, business agreements, and social relationships. You can also use <b>the law</b> to refer to the people who work in this system. 法律; 執法者","examples":["Obscene and threatening phone calls are against the law. 猥褻電話和恐嚇電話是違法的。","They are beginning criminal proceedings against him for breaking the law on financing political parties. 他們正開始對他進行刑事訴訟，因為他違反了政黨資助法。","The book analyses why women kill and how the law treats them. 這本書分析了婦女為什麼殺人以及法律如何處置她們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Law</b> is used to refer to a particular branch of the law, such as <b>criminal law</b> or <b>business law</b>. (某一類) 法律","examples":["He was a professor of criminal law at Harvard University law school. 他曾是哈佛大學法學院的刑法教授。","Under international law, diplomats living in foreign countries are exempt from criminal prosecution. 按照國際法，駐外外交官免受刑事訴訟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>law</b> is one of the rules in a system of law which deals with a particular type of agreement, relationship, or crime. (特定的) 法規","examples":["...the country's liberal political asylum law. …該國的自由政治避難法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>laws</b> <b>of</b> an organization or activity are its rules, which are used to organize and control it. 戒律; 守則","examples":["...the laws of the Catholic Church. …天主教會的戒律。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>law</b> is a rule or set of rules for good behaviour which is considered right and important by the majority of people for moral, religious, or emotional reasons. 準則","examples":["...inflexible moral laws. …不容更改的道德準則。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>law</b> is a natural process in which a particular event or thing always leads to a particular result. 規律","examples":["The laws of nature are absolute. 自然規律是絕對確鑿的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>law</b> is a scientific rule that someone has invented to explain a particular natural process. 定律","examples":["...the law of gravity. …萬有引力定律。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Law</b> or <b>the law</b> is all the professions which deal with advising people about the law, representing people in court, or giving decisions and punishments. 法律行業","examples":["A career in law is becoming increasingly attractive to young people. 從事法律行業對於年輕人越來越有吸引力。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Law</b> is the study of systems of law and how laws work. 法學","examples":["He studied law. 他學習法學。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of thinking they are <b>above the law</b>, you criticize them for thinking that they are so clever or important that they do not need to obey the law. 凌駕於法律之上","examples":["He accuses the government of wanting to be above the law. 他譴責政府想凌駕於法律之上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have to do something <b>by law</b> or if you are not allowed to do something <b>by law</b>, the law states that you have to do it or that you are not allowed to do it. 根據法律","examples":["By law all restaurants must display their prices outside. 根據法律所有飯店必須在外面亮出他們的價目。"]}]}]},"leg":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腿；動物腿，腿肉；褲腿；傢俱的腿，支撐柱條；（旅程或賽程的）一段，一程；<非正式>（球，尤指高爾夫球）力度不夠；<非正式>（產品或想法的）持久流行或成功；（板球）腿側區；叉狀物的一分支；<古>屈膝禮"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"有……腿的(-legged)"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（撐船者）用腿蹬洞頂或洞壁使（船）透過運河隧洞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or animal's <b>legs</b> are the long parts of their body that they use to stand on. 腿","examples":["He was tapping his walking stick against his leg. 他用柺杖輕輕敲打著他的腿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>legs</b> of a pair of trousers are the parts that cover your legs. 褲腿","examples":["He moved on through wet grass that soaked the legs of his trousers. 他繼續走在溼漉漉的草地上，弄溼了他的褲腿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>leg</b> of lamb, pork, chicken, or other meat is a piece of meat that consists of the animal's or bird's leg, especially the thigh. (羊、豬、雞等的) 腿肉","examples":["...a chicken leg. …一隻雞腿。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>legs</b> of a table, chair, or other piece of furniture are the parts that rest on the floor and support the furniture's weight. (桌子、椅子等傢俱的) 腿","examples":["His ankles were tied to the legs of the chair. 他的腳踝被綁在了椅腿上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>leg</b> of a long journey is one part of it, usually between two points where you stop. 一段旅程","examples":["The first leg of the journey was by boat to Lake Naivasha in Kenya. 第一段旅程是坐船到肯亞的奈瓦夏湖。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>leg</b> of a sports competition is one of a series of games that are played to find an overall winner. 一段賽程","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are pulling</b> someone's <b>leg</b>, you are teasing them by telling them something shocking or worrying as a joke. 開某人的玩笑","examples":["Of course I won't tell them; I was only pulling your leg. 我當然不會告訴他們；我只是和你開玩笑的。"]}]}]},"lake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"湖，湖泊；大量的液體；（液體）一灘；沉澱色料；胭脂紅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）血球溶解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lake</b> is a large area of fresh water, surrounded by land. 湖","examples":["They can go fishing in the lake. 他們可以去湖裡釣魚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a bright pigment used in textile dyeing and printing inks, produced by the combination of an organic colouring matter with an inorganic compound, usually a metallic salt, oxide, or hydroxide 色澱; 沉澱染料","examples":[]}]}]},"last":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最後的；最近的，上一個的；最後剩下的；最不可能的；最末的；僅存的；最不重要的，最無關緊要的；最後遇見的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"持續；持久；維持，夠用；堅持，支撐下去"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞋楦；僅剩下的部分（或事項）；最後來的人（或發生的事）（the last）；殘餘，剩餘（the last of）；末尾；結束，最後時刻（尤指死亡）（the last）；最後一次提及，最後一次看見（the last）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"最近發生的事情；最後的人或事物；最後的人；最後一次；最後的動作，最後的話；用於指最新獲得的訊息"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最近，上次；最後；（用於引出最後的話或資訊）最後，最後一點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>last</b> in expressions such as <b>last Friday,</b> <b>last night</b>, and <b>last year</b> to refer, for example, to the most recent Friday, night, or year. 上一個的","examples":["I got married last July. 我去年７月結的婚。","He never made it home at all last night. 他昨天晚上根本沒有回家。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>last</b> event, person, thing, or period of time is the most recent one. 最近的","examples":["Much has changed since my last visit. 自我上次來訪後，變化很大。","I split up with my last boyfriend three years ago. 我和前任男友在3年前分手了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Last</b> is used to refer to the only thing, person, or part of something that remains. 僅剩的","examples":["Jed nodded, finishing off the last piece of pizza. 傑德點了點頭，吃完了僅剩的一塊比薩餅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>last</b> to indicate that something is extremely undesirable or unlikely. 最不想要的; 最不可能的","examples":["The last thing I wanted to do was teach. 我最不想做的事就是教書了。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Last</b> is also a pronoun. 最近發生的事情","examples":["The next tide, it was announced, would be even higher than the last. 通告說下次漲潮會比上次更高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Last</b> is also a pronoun. 最後的人或事物","examples":["It wasn't the first time that this particular difference had divided them and it wouldn't be the last. 這個特殊差異使他們產生分歧不是第一次，也不會是最後一次。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>the</b> <b>last</b> <b>to</b> do or know something, everyone else does or knows it before you. 最後的人","examples":["She was the last to go to bed. 她是最後一個睡覺的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Last</b> is also a pronoun. 最不想要的事; 最不可能的事","examples":["I would be the last to say that science has explained everything. 我絕不可能說科學已經解釋了一切。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The last</b> you see of someone or <b>the last</b> you hear of them is the final time that you see them or talk to them. 最後一次","examples":["She disappeared shouting, \"To the river, to the river!\" And that was the last we saw of her. 她喊著“去河邊，去河邊”，然後就不見了。那是我們最後一次看到她。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>last</b> happened on a particular occasion, that is the most recent occasion on which it happened. 最近一次","examples":["When were you there last? 你最近一次在那裡是什麼時候？","The house is a little more dilapidated than when I last saw it. 這幢房子比我上次看到時更破一些了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>last</b>, you do it after everyone else does, or after you do everything else. 最後地","examples":["I testified last. 我最後作了證。","I was always picked last for the football team at school. 我在上學時總是最後一個被選入足球隊。"]}]},{"pos":"ord.","pos_name":"序數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>last</b> thing, person, event, or period of time is the one that happens or comes after all the others of the same kind. 最後的","examples":["...the last three pages of the chapter. …這章的最後3頁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Last</b> is also a noun. 剩下的東西 (或人)","examples":["He finished off the last of the wine. 他喝完了剩下的酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the wooden or metal form on which a shoe or boot is fashioned or repaired 鞋楦","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event, situation, or problem <b>lasts</b> for a particular length of time, it continues to exist or happen for that length of time. 持續","examples":["The marriage had lasted for less than two years. 這樁婚姻持續了不到兩年。","The games lasted only half the normal time. 這場比賽只持續了正常比賽時間的一半。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>lasts</b> for a particular length of time, it continues to be able to be used for that time, for example, because there is some of it left or because it is in good enough condition. 夠用 (一段時間)","examples":["You only need a very small blob of glue, so one tube lasts for ages. 你僅需要很小一滴膠水，所以一管膠水能用很久。","The repaired sail lasted less than 24 hours. 修好的帆只維持了不到二十四小時。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something has happened <b>at last</b> or <b>at long last</b> you mean it has happened after you have been hoping for it for a long time. 終於","examples":["I'm so glad that we've found you at last! 我太高興了，我們終於找到你了！","Here, at long last, was the moment he had waited for. 終於，他期待的時刻來臨了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>the night before last</b>, <b>the election before last</b> and <b>the leader before last</b> to refer to the period of time, event, or person that came immediately before the most recent one in a series. 再上一次; 再上一個人或物","examples":["It was the dog he'd heard the night before last. 這是他前天夜裡聽見吼叫的那隻狗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>the last I heard</b> and <b>the last she heard</b> to introduce a piece of information that is the most recent that you have on a particular subject. 某人最近獲悉","examples":["The last I heard, Joe and Irene were still happily married. 我最近得知，喬和艾琳的婚姻依然幸福。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something or someone <b>until last</b>, you delay using, choosing, or dealing with them until you have used, chosen, or dealt with all the others. 把…留到最後","examples":["I have left my best wine until last. 我把最好的酒留到最後喝。"]}]}]},"lesson":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一節課，一課時；教學單元，（課本中的）課；經驗，教訓；（教堂禮拜中的）《聖經》選讀"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"<古>給……上課；教訓，訓誡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lesson</b> is a fixed period of time when people are taught about a particular subject or taught how to do something. 課","examples":["It would be his last French lesson for months. 這將是他以後幾個月裡的最後一次法語課。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>lesson</b> to refer to an experience which acts as a warning to you or an example from which you should learn. 教訓","examples":["There's still one lesson to be learned from the crisis – we all need to better understand the thinking of the other side. 從危機中還要吸取一個教訓–我們都需要更好地理解對方的想法。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are going to <b>teach</b> someone <b>a lesson</b>, you mean that you are going to punish them for something that they have done so that they do not do it again. 給某人一個教訓","examples":[]}]}]},"leave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"離開（某人或某處）；離開居住地點（或群體、工作單位等）；與……脫離關係， 離開（某人）；不立刻做，不馬上處理；使保留，讓……處於（某種狀態、某地等）；給……留下（不愉快的東西）；留下（資訊或答覆）；遺留，遺忘；剩下（食物或飲料）；遺下（家人）；（去世時）遺贈，遺留；把……留交，交託；遞送，遞交；留（空隙或空白）；留給（指有限的機會）；不再談論；（數學）剩餘，餘下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"假期，休假；准許，許可；（斯努克、槌球等）收盤球勢，（球被擊後）停留的位置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> a place or person, you go away from that place or person. 離開","examples":["He would not be allowed to leave the country. 他不準離開這個國家。","My flight leaves in less than an hour. 我的航班一小時內起飛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> an institution, group, or job, you permanently stop attending that institution, being a member of that group, or doing that job. 離開 (機構、團體或工作)","examples":["He left school with no qualifications. 他離開學校時沒有拿到證書。","I am leaving to concentrate on writing fiction. 我要離開去專心寫小說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> your husband, wife, or some other person with whom you have had a close relationship, you stop living with them or you end the relationship. 與…脫離關係; 離開 (某人)","examples":["He'll never leave you. You needn't worry. 他永遠都不會離開你的，你不必擔心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something or someone in a particular place, you let them remain there when you go away. If you <b>leave</b> something or someone with a person, you let them remain with that person so they are safe while you are away. 留下","examples":["I left my bags in the car. 我把包留在車裡。","From the moment that Philippe had left her in the bedroom at the hotel, she had heard nothing of him. 自從菲利普把她遺棄在旅店房間的那一刻起，她就再沒有他的任何訊息。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> a message or an answer, you write it, record it, or give it to someone so that it can be found or passed on. 留下 (資訊或答覆)","examples":["You can leave a message on our answering machine. 你可以在我們的電話留言機上留言。","I left my phone number with several people. 我把我的電話號碼留給了幾個人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> someone doing something, they are doing that thing when you go away from them. 留下…繼續作某事","examples":["Salter drove off, leaving Callendar surveying the scene. 索特爾開車走了，留下加林達繼續調查現場。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you go away from them so that they do it on their own. If you <b>leave</b> someone <b>to</b> himself or herself, you go away from them and allow them to be alone. 留給…自己做; 把…留下","examples":["I'll leave you to get to know each other. 我讓你們自己互相認識一下。","Diana took the hint and left them to it. 戴安娜心領神會，讓他們自己完成這件事。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>leave</b> an amount of something means to keep it available after the rest has been used or taken away. 留出","examples":["He always left a little food for the next day. 他總是留出一點食物第二天吃。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"To <b>leave</b> someone <b>with</b> something, especially when that thing is unpleasant or difficult to deal with, means to make them have it or make them deal with it. 給…留下 (不愉快的東西)","examples":["...a crash which left him with a broken collar-bone. …一次給他留下鎖骨骨折的車禍。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If an event <b>leaves</b> people or things in a particular state, they are in that state when the event has finished. 致使","examples":["...violent disturbances which have left at least ten people dead. …致使至少十人死亡的暴力騷亂。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> food or drink, you do not eat or drink it, often because you do not like it. 剩下 (食物或飲料)","examples":["If you don't like the cocktail you ordered, just leave it and try a different one. 如果你不喜歡你點的雞尾酒，剩著吧，嚐嚐別的。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something <b>leaves</b> a mark, effect, or sign, it causes that mark, effect, or sign to remain as a result. 留下 (痕跡、影響等)","examples":["A muscle tear will leave a scar after healing. 肌肉撕裂在治癒後會留下傷疤。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something in a particular state, position, or condition, you let it remain in that state, position, or condition. 使處於 (某種狀態、位置或情形)","examples":["He left the album open on the table. 他把相簿敞開著放在桌子上了。","I've left the car lights on. 我把車燈開著。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> a space or gap in something, you deliberately make that space or gap. 留 (空隙或空白)","examples":["Leave a gap at the top and bottom so air can circulate. 在頂部和底部各留一點空隙，這樣空氣就可以流通了。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> a job, decision, or choice <b>to</b> someone, you give them the responsibility for dealing with it or making it. 留給…辦理","examples":["Affix the blue airmail label and leave the rest to us. 貼上藍色航空郵件標籤，剩下的就留給我們辦吧。","The judge should not have left it to the jury to decide. 法官本不應該讓陪審團作決定。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"To <b>leave</b> someone <b>with</b> a particular course of action or the opportunity to do something means to let it be available to them, while restricting them in other ways. 留給 (指有限的機會)","examples":["He was left with no option but to resign. 留給他的除了辭職別無選擇。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something <b>until</b> a particular time, you delay doing it or dealing with it until then. 留到…時才","examples":["Don't leave it all until the last minute. 不要把什麼事都留到最後一分鐘。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something <b>too late</b>, you delay doing it so that when you eventually do it, it is useless or ineffective. 耽誤","examples":[]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> a particular subject, you stop talking about it and start discussing something else. 不再談論","examples":["I think we'd better leave the subject of nationalism. 我想我們最好不要再談論民族主義這個話題了。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> property or money <b>to</b> someone, you arrange for it to be given to them after you have died. 把 (遺產) 留給","examples":["He died two and a half years later, leaving everything to his wife. 他兩年半後去世，把所有的財產都留給了他的妻子。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> something somewhere, you forget to bring it with you. 忘拿","examples":["I left my purse back there on the gas pump. 我把錢包忘在那兒的油泵上了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leave</b> is a period of time when you are not working at your job, because you are on holiday, or for some other reason. If you are <b>on leave</b>, you are not working at your job. 休假","examples":["Why don't you take a few days' leave? 你為什麼不休幾天假？","...maternity leave. …產假。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"permission to do something 准許; 許可","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>leave</b> someone or something <b>alone</b>, or if you <b>leave</b> them <b>be</b>, you do not pay them any attention or bother them. 不管; 不打擾","examples":["Some people need to confront a traumatic past; others find it better to leave it alone. 一些人需要面對傷痕累累的過去；另一些人認為最好不管它。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something continues <b>from</b> <b>where</b> it <b>left off</b>, it starts happening again at the point where it had previously stopped. 死灰復燃","examples":["As soon as the police disappear the violence will take up from where it left off. 只要警察不在，暴力就會死灰復燃。"]}]}]},"letter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信，信函；字母；<美>（縫製在運動服上的）校運動隊首字母標誌；<英，非正式>（代表學位或職位等資格的）首字母縮略詞（letters）；文學；法律文書，正式文書（letters）；字面確切含義；（印刷）一種鉛字字型；<古> 學識，淵博的學問"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用字母標註；把字母印刷（或縫製等）於；<美>贏得學校運動隊的字母標誌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you write a <b>letter</b> to someone, you write a message on paper and send it to them, usually through the mail. 信","examples":["I had received a letter from a very close friend. 我收到了一位非常親近的朋友的來信。","...a letter of resignation. …一封辭職信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Letters</b> are written symbols which represent one of the sounds in a language. 字母","examples":["...the letters of the alphabet. …字母表中的字母。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a student <b>letters</b> in sports or athletics by being part of the university or college team, they are entitled to wear on their jacket the initial letter of the name of their university or college. (因體育運動出色) 贏得校名首字母徽章","examples":["Burkoth lettered in American football. 伯考斯在足球賽中贏得了校名首字母徽章。"]}]}]},"lily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"百合；睡蓮（water lily）；鳶尾花形的紋章"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"純潔的，潔白的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lily</b> is a plant with large flowers that are often white. 百合","examples":[]}]}]},"lift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提起，舉起；抬起（身體某一部位）；空運；解除，撤銷；高興起來，使更愉快；消散，消失；偷盜，盜竊；剽竊，抄襲；挖出，拔起（蔬菜或植物）；提高（嗓音）；提高，增加；使更有趣；（個人、運動隊的）晉級；贏得（獎品或比賽）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電梯，升降機；免費搭車，搭便車；鼓舞，振奮；抬，提；（空氣的）升力，提升力；（飛機的）最大提升重量；高飛（投出的球觸地反彈時急速上升）；後跟墊，插跟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lift</b> something, you move it to another position, especially upward. 舉起; 拿起","examples":["The colonel lifted the phone and dialled his superior. 上校拿起電話撥了他上司的號碼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lift</b> your eyes or your head, you look up, for example, when you have been reading and someone comes into the room. 抬起 (眼睛或頭)","examples":["When he finished he lifted his eyes and looked out the window. 他完成以後抬眼向窗外看去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people in authority <b>lift</b> a law or rule that prevents people from doing something, they end it. 解除 (法令等)","examples":["The European Commission has urged France to lift its ban on imports of British beef. 歐盟委員會已敦促法國解除對英國牛肉進口的禁令。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>lifts</b> your spirits or your mood, or if they <b>lift</b>, you start feeling more cheerful. 鼓舞","examples":["He used his incredible sense of humour to lift my spirits. 他以不可思議的幽默感鼓舞了我計程車氣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a government or organization <b>lifts</b> people or goods in or out of an area, it transports them there by aircraft, especially when there is a war. 空運","examples":["The army lifted people off rooftops where they had climbed to escape the flooding. 軍隊把爬到房頂躲避洪水的人們空運走。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>lift</b> something means to increase its amount or to increase the level or the rate at which it happens. 提高","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lift up</b> means the same as . 舉起","examples":["She put her arms around him and lifted him up. 她雙臂擁住他，把他舉起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>lift</b> somewhere, you take them there in your car as a favour to them. 搭便車","examples":["He had a car and often gave me a lift home. 他有一輛汽車，經常讓我搭便車回家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lift </b> is the force that makes an aircraft leave the ground and stay in the air. 提升力","examples":["An aeroplane has to reach a certain speed before there is enough lift to get it off the ground. 飛機得在達到一定的速度以後，才能有足夠的提升力從地面起飛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lift</b> is a device that carries people or goods up and down inside tall buildings. 電梯","examples":["We took the lift to the fourteenth floor. 我們乘電梯到了第14層。"]}]}]},"lie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"平躺，平臥；位於，坐落在；存在，在於；處於，保持（某種狀態）；（尤用於墓碑上的文字中）長眠；（比賽時）名列，排名；撒謊，編造謊言；（物體）平放在……上，平放著；朝……方向；造成假象，不可靠；（尤指不快或困難之事）將發生，在等待；（光、雲、霧等）存在，展現；（訴訟，控告，索賠）可受理，可立案"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"方向，位置；謊言，謊話；（動物的）穴，（鳥的）巢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are lying</b> somewhere, you are in a horizontal position and are not standing or sitting. 躺","examples":["There was a child lying on the ground. 地上躺著一個小孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>lies</b> in a particular place, it is in a flat position in that place. 平放在","examples":["...a newspaper lying on a nearby couch. …平放在旁邊沙發上的一張報紙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>lies</b> in a particular position or direction, you mean that it is situated there. 位於","examples":["The islands lie at the southern end of the Kurile chain. 這些島嶼位於千島群島的南端。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can talk about where something such as a problem, solution, or fault <b>lies</b> to say what you think it consists of, involves, or is caused by. (問題、辦法或錯誤) 在於","examples":["The problem lay with the family and the school system rather than with television. 問題在於家庭和學校體制而非電視。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>lie</b> in expressions such as <b>lie ahead</b>, <b>lie in store</b>, and <b>lie in wait</b> when you are talking about what someone is going to experience in the future, especially when it is something unpleasant or difficult. (尤指不愉快或困難的事情) 即將發生","examples":["She'd need all her strength and bravery to cope with what lay in store. 她需要拿出全部的力量和勇氣來應對即將發生的事情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>is lying</b>, they are saying something which they know is not true. 撒謊","examples":["I know he's lying. 我知道他在撒謊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the manner, place, or style in which something is situated 狀態; 方位; 方式","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lie</b> is something that someone says or writes which they know is untrue. 謊言","examples":["\"Who else do you work for?\"—\"No one.\"—\"That's a lie.\" “你還為其他什麼人工作嗎？” —“沒其他人。” —“撒謊。”","I've had enough of your lies. 我已經聽夠了你的謊言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"撒謊","examples":["Lying is something that I will not tolerate. 撒謊是我所不能容忍的。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lie</b> to say that something is or remains in a particular state or condition. For example, if something <b>lies forgotten</b>, it has been and remains forgotten. 處於 (某種狀態)","examples":["The picture lay hidden in the archives for over 40 years. 這張畫在檔案室藏了40多年。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lie</b> to say what position a competitor or team is in during a competition. (比賽中) 名列","examples":["I was going well and was lying fourth. 我幹得不錯，名列第4。"]}]}]},"level":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"數量，程度；標準，水平；層次，級別；看待（或應對、理解）事物的方式；水平高度，相對高度；樓層；平地；水平儀"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平坦的，水平的；相同價值的，相同地位的；比分相同的；平靜的，冷靜的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使平整；推倒，夷平；（使）比分相同；（尤指用槍）瞄準；針對……（進行批評等）；穩定下來，達到平衡（level off）；坦誠相見；作水準測量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>level</b> is a point on a scale, for example, a scale of amount, quality, or difficulty. 水平","examples":["If you don't know your cholesterol level, it's a good idea to have it checked. 如果你不知道自己的膽固醇水平，最好去查一下。","We do have the lowest level of inflation for some years. 我們幾年來的確保持最低水平的通貨膨脹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>level</b> of a river, lake, or ocean or the <b>level</b> of liquid in a container is the height of its surface. 水位","examples":["The water level of the Mississippi River is already 6.5 feet below normal. 密西西比河的水位已經比正常水位低6.5英尺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is at a particular <b>level</b>, it is at that height. 水平高度","examples":["Liz sank down until the water came up to her chin and the bubbles were at eye level. 莉茲下沉直到水漫到她的下巴，泡沫到了她眼睛的高度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>level</b> of a building is one of its different storeys, which is situated above or below other storeys. 層","examples":["Thurlow and Brown's rooms were on the second level, to the rear of the building. 瑟洛和布朗的房間都在大樓背面的第二層。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>level</b> <b>with</b> another thing, it is at the same height as it. 與…等高的","examples":["He leaned over the counter so his face was almost level with the boy's. 他俯在櫃檯上，這樣他的臉幾乎和那男孩的臉一樣高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something is <b>level</b>, it is completely flat with no part higher than any other. 平坦的","examples":["The floor was level, but the ceiling sloped toward his head. 地面平平坦坦，但是天花板向他的頭部傾斜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Level</b> is also an adjective. 接近的","examples":["He waited until they were level with the door before he pivoted around sharply and punched Graham hard. 他等他們接近門口時才一個急轉身用拳頭猛揍格雷厄姆。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you draw <b>level</b> with someone or something, you get closer to them until you are by their side. 接近","examples":["Just before we drew level with the gates, he slipped out of the jeep and disappeared. 就在我們快接近大門口時，他溜出吉普車不見了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something such as a violent storm <b>levels</b> a building or area of land, they destroy it completely or make it completely flat. 夷平","examples":["The storm was the most powerful to hit Hawaii this century. It levelled sugar plantations and destroyed homes. 這是本世紀襲擊夏威夷最猛烈的暴風雨。它夷平了甘蔗種植園，也摧毀了家園。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an accusation or criticism <b>is</b> <b>levelled</b> <b>at</b> someone, they are accused of doing wrong or they are criticized for something they have done. (指責或批評) 針對","examples":["Allegations of corruption were levelled at him and his family. 對腐敗的指控是針對他和他的家人的。"]}]}]},"lip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘴唇；（傷口或洞口）邊緣；容器邊緣，開口；<非正式> 粗魯無禮的話"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（水）拍打；（高爾夫）擊球至（洞穴）的邊緣（而未落入）；用嘴唇觸及，吻；（在吹奏管樂器時）運唇"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"口頭上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>lips</b> are the two outer parts of the edge of your mouth. 嘴唇","examples":["Wade stuck the cigarette between his lips. 韋德嘴裡叼著煙。"]}]}]},"lion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獅子；名人，社交場合的名流；勇猛的人；獅子座（也指出生於獅子座的人）；the lion's share（最大的一份，絕大部分）；（大寫 Lion）人名或姓氏（西、葡語：利昂；德、法、意、捷、瑞典語：利翁；英語：萊昂）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lion</b> is a large wild member of the cat family that is found in Africa. Lions have yellowish fur, and male lions have long hair on their head and neck. 獅子","examples":[]}]}]},"list":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"列表，清單；（船）傾側；圍欄；（織物的）鑲邊；<舊>渴望，喜好；（尤指按重要程度排列的）事物清單；賽場，戰場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"列清單，擬訂清單；把……列入名單；（使）（公司）上市；標價；（船）傾斜；<舊>徵召（士兵）；<舊>想要，喜好"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>list</b> of things such as names or addresses is a set of them which all belong to a particular category, written down one below the other. 清單","examples":["We are making a list of the top ten men we would not want to be married to. 我們正在列一個我們最不想嫁的10種男人的名單。","There were six names on the list. 單子上有6個名字。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>list</b> of things is a set of them that you think of as being in a particular order. (按一定順序排列的) 系列事項","examples":["High on the list of public demands is to end military control of broadcasting. 高居公眾要求事項前列的是結束對廣播的軍事控制。","The criminal judicial system always comes up at the top of the list of voters' concerns in focus groups. 刑事司法制度總是出現在焦點小組中投票者關注事項之首。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the act or an instance of leaning to one side 傾向一邊的行為","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>list</b> several things such as reasons or names means to write or say them one after another, usually in a particular order. 列出","examples":["The pupils were asked to list the sports they loved most and hated most. 學生們被要求列出他們最喜歡的和最討厭的運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>list</b> something in a particular way means to include it in that way in a list or report. 把…列入 (表、報告)","examples":["A medical examiner has listed the deaths as homicides. 驗屍官已將這些死亡列為他殺案件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a company <b>is listed</b>, or if it <b>lists</b>, on a stock exchange, it obtains an official quotation for its shares so that people can buy and sell them. 使 (公司) 上市; (公司) 上市","examples":["...a basket of blue chip stocks listed on the American Exchange. …在美國證券交易所上市的一組績優股。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(esp of ships) to lean over or cause to lean over to one side (尤指船)傾側","examples":[]}]}]},"life":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生命；人命，性命；生物，活物；壽命，一生；（某事物的）存在期；生活，人生；生活方式；（某種）生活；生氣，活力；（繪畫的）模特兒，實物；（遊戲中的）一次機會，命；傳記；無期徒刑，終身監禁；今生，來世"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生命的；一生的，終身的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Life</b> is the quality which people, animals, and plants have when they are not dead, and which objects and substances do not have. 生命","examples":["...a baby's first minutes of life. …嬰兒生命的頭幾分鐘。","Amnesty International opposes the death penalty as a violation of the right to life. 大赦國際組織反對死刑，因其侵犯生存權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>life</b> to refer to things or groups of things which are alive. 生物; 生命","examples":["Is there life on Mars? 火星上有生命嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>life</b>, you mean their state of being alive, especially when there is a risk or danger of them dying. 生存; 性命","examples":["Your life is in danger. 你有生命危險。","A nurse began to try to save his life. 一名護士開始設法搶救他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>life</b> is the period of time during which they are alive. 一生","examples":["He spent the last fourteen years of his life in retirement. 他生命的最後14年退休在家。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>life</b> to refer to a period of someone's life when they are in a particular situation or job. 人生階段; 生涯","examples":["Interior designers spend their working lives keeping up to date with the latest trends. 室內設計者們把他們的職業生涯都花在追趕最新潮流上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>life</b> to refer to particular activities which people regularly do during their lives. 生活","examples":["My personal life has had to take second place to my career. 我的個人生活不得不放在我的事業之後。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>life</b> to refer to the things that people do and experience that are characteristic of a particular place, group, or activity. (特定的) 生活","examples":["How did you adjust to college life? 你是怎麼適應大學生活的？","He abhors the wheeling-and-dealing associated with conventional political life. 他憎惡傳統政治生活中的爾虞我詐。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A person, place, book, or film that is full of <b>life</b> gives an impression of excitement, energy, or cheerfulness. 活力","examples":["The town itself was full of life and character. 這座城鎮本身就充滿了活力和個性。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone is sentenced to <b>life</b>, they are sentenced to stay in prison for the rest of their life or for a very long time. 終身監禁","examples":["He could get life in prison, if convicted. 他會遭終身監禁，如果罪名成立的話。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"The <b>life</b> of something such as a machine, organization, or project is the period of time that it lasts for. (機器、組織或專案的) 壽命","examples":["The repairs did not increase the value or the life of the equipment. 這些修理沒有提高裝置的價值，也沒有延長它的壽命。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> something <b>to life</b> or if it <b>comes to life</b>, it becomes interesting or exciting. 帶來生機; 使變得生動","examples":["The cold, hard cruelty of two young men is vividly brought to life in this true story. 兩個年輕人的冷漠和殘忍在這個真實的故事裡被生動地表現了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is fighting for</b> their <b>life</b>, you mean that they are in a very serious condition and may die as a result of an accident or illness. 掙扎在死亡線上","examples":["...a horrifying robbery that left a man fighting for his life. …一場恐怖的搶劫，導致一人生命垂危。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>For life</b> means for the rest of a person's life. 終身","examples":["He was jailed for life in 1966 for the murder of three policemen. 1966年，由於殺害了3名警察他被終身監禁。","She may have been scarred for life. 她可能已受到終身難以癒合的創傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>takes</b> another person's <b>life</b>, they kill them. If someone <b>takes</b> their own <b>life</b>, they kill themselves. 殺死某人","examples":["Before execution, he admitted to taking the lives of at least 35 more women. 在赴死刑前，他承認了還殺死過另外至少35名婦女。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>to come to life</b>, <b>to spring to life</b>, and <b>to roar into life</b> to indicate that a machine or vehicle suddenly starts working or moving. (機器或車輛) 突然開動","examples":["To his great relief the engine came to life. 讓他鬆一口氣的是，引擎發動起來了。"]}]}]},"like":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"像，如同；符合……的方式；（指某人常做的事）符合……的特點，像……才會；（用於詢問）……怎麼樣；例如，好比；（用於否定式短語中）比得上；大約，左右"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"喜歡，喜愛；希望，想要；（用於請求）想要，希望得到；喜歡（做某事、習慣某事）；（用於詢問）你覺得……怎麼樣；對……反感，討厭；喜好（某種環境）"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"像……一樣，如同；好像，似乎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜好，愛好（常複數）；類似或同類的人或物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"類似的，相似的；（畫像，影象）逼真的，像的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（非正式口語，思考說下句話、解釋或舉例時用）大概，可能；（非正式口語）我說，他說，她說；（非正式口語，代替as）和…一樣，像；（非正式口語，代替as）和……一樣，像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one person or thing is <b>like</b> another, you mean that they share some of the same qualities or features. 像","examples":["He looks like Father Christmas. 他長得像聖誕老人。","It's a bit like going to the dentist; it's never as bad as you fear. 這有點像去看牙醫，它決不像你所擔心的那樣糟糕。","It's nothing like what happened in the mid-Seventies. 那根本不像發生在七十年代中期的事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about what something or someone is <b>like</b>, you are talking about their qualities or features. (指人或事物的品質、特點) 像…樣","examples":["What was Bulgaria like? 保加利亞情況怎麼樣？","What did she look like? 她長什麼樣？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>like</b> to introduce an example of the set of things or people that you have just mentioned. 例如","examples":["The neglect that large cities like New York have received over the past 12 years is tremendous. 諸如紐約這樣的大城市在過去12年裡所受到的忽視是巨大的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>like</b> to say that someone or something is in the same situation as another person or thing. 像…一樣","examples":["It also moved those who, like me, are too young to have lived through the war. 它也感動了那些跟我一樣、太年輕而沒有經歷過戰爭的人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone is behaving <b>like</b> something or someone else, you mean that they are behaving in a way that is typical of that kind of thing or person. <b>Like</b> is used in this way in many fixed expressions, for example, <b>to cry like a baby</b> and <b>to watch someone like a hawk</b>. 像…一樣","examples":["I was shaking all over, trembling like a leaf. 我渾身顫抖、像一片葉子似的抖動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>like</b> in negative expressions such as <b>nothing like it</b> and <b>no place like it</b> to emphasize that there is nothing as good as the situation, thing, or person mentioned. (用於否定式短語中) 比得上","examples":["There's nothing like candlelight for creating a romantic mood. 沒有什麼比燭光更能營造浪漫氛圍了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>like</b> in expressions such as <b>nothing like</b> to make an emphatic negative statement. 用於固定短語中表否定強調","examples":["Three hundred million dollars will be nothing like enough. 3億美元根本不夠。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Like</b> is sometimes used as a conjunction in order to say that something appears to be the case when it is not. Some people consider this use to be incorrect. 彷彿","examples":["His arms look like they might snap under the weight of his gloves. 他的雙臂看起來好像要在他手套的重壓下突然折斷似的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Like</b> is sometimes used as a conjunction in order to indicate that something happens or is done in the same way as something else. Some people consider this use to be incorrect. 像…那樣","examples":["People are strolling, buying ice cream for their children, just like they do every Sunday. 人們散著步，給孩子們買著冰淇淋，就像他們每個週日做的一樣。","He spoke exactly like I did. 他說得跟我一模一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"similar; resembling 相似的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>like</b> something or someone, you think they are interesting, enjoyable, or attractive. 喜歡","examples":["He likes baseball. 他喜歡棒球運動。","I just didn't like being in crowds. 我只是不喜歡呆在人群中。","Do you like to go swimming? 你喜歡去游泳嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you ask someone how they <b>like</b> something, you are asking them for their opinion of it and whether they enjoy it or find it pleasant. 覺得","examples":["How do you like America? 你覺得美國怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>like</b> <b>to</b> do something or that you <b>like</b> something to be done, you mean that you prefer to do it or prefer it to be done as part of your normal life or routine. 喜歡 (做某事、習慣某事)","examples":["I like to get to airports in good time. 我喜歡提前到機場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you <b>would</b> <b>like</b> something or <b>would</b> <b>like</b> to do something, you are indicating a wish or desire that you have. 想","examples":["I'd like a bath. 我想洗個澡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you ask someone if they <b>would like</b> something or <b>would like</b> to do something, you are making a polite offer or invitation. 想要 (向某人提供幫助、提出邀請)","examples":["Here's your change. Would you like a bag? 這是找給您的零錢。您要個袋子嗎？","Perhaps while you wait you would like a drink at the bar. 也許你等的時候會想要去酒吧喝一杯。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say to someone that you <b>would like</b> something or you <b>would like</b> them to do something, or ask them if they <b>would like</b> to do it, you are politely telling them what you want or what you want them to do. 想要 (請別人做某事)","examples":["I'd like an explanation. 我想要一個解釋。","We'd like you to look around and tell us if anything is missing. 我們想請你四處看看，並且告訴我們是否缺少什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>like</b> in expressions such as <b>like attracts like</b>, when you are referring to two or more people or things that have the same or similar characteristics. 同樣 (或相似) 的人或事物","examples":["You have to make sure you're comparing like with like. 你得確定你是在把同類事物相比較。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>likes</b> are the things that they enjoy or find pleasant. 喜好","examples":["I thought that I knew everything about Jemma: her likes and dislikes, her political viewpoints. 我曾以為我瞭解傑瑪的一切：她的喜惡以及她的政治觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>if you like</b> when you are making or agreeing to an offer or suggestion in a casual way. 如果你願意的話","examples":["You can stay here if you like. 如果你願意的話，你可以呆在這裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>like this</b>, <b>like that</b>, or <b>like so</b> when you are showing someone how something is done. 像那樣; 像這樣","examples":["It opens and closes, like this. 它就像這樣開啟和關上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>like this</b> or <b>like that</b> when you are drawing attention to something that you are doing or that someone else is doing. 像這樣","examples":["I'm sorry to intrude on you like this. 很抱歉這樣打擾你。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use the expression <b>something like</b> with an amount, number, or description to indicate that it is approximately accurate. 大約","examples":["They can get something like $3,000 a year. 他們一年能得到大約$3000。"]}]}]},"light":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"光，光線；光源（如電燈）；某種光亮；交通訊號燈；車燈；打火機，點火器； 角度，（事物呈現的）狀態；眼光，處世標準（lights）；（對問題的）瞭解，啟迪；眼神；亮色，淺色；窗，天窗，採光口；直欞窗窗玻璃上的豎框；傑出的人，有聲望的人；<英>（字謎遊戲中的）待填空格"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淺色的，淡色的；採光好的，光線足的；天亮的，白天的；輕的，不重的；分量不足的；輕型的，輕便的；少量的，程度低的；不嚴厲的；（風）輕柔的；輕聲的；（碰觸）輕輕的；不累的，輕鬆的；不嚴肅的，愉快的；單薄的，不保暖的；（睡眠）不深的，易醒的；（飯食）簡單的；酒精含量低的，低度酒的；（食物）清淡的，易消化的；（食物）鬆軟的；（土地）輕質的；（字型）細體的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）照亮；（使）燃燒，點燃；用光指引；點菸"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（旅行）輕裝地；輕地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Light</b> is the brightness that lets you see things. Light comes from sources such as the sun, moon, lamps, and fire. 光; 光線","examples":["Cracks of light filtered through the shutters. 一束束陽光透過百葉窗照射進來。","...ultraviolet light. …紫外線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>light</b> is something such as an electric lamp which produces light. 燈","examples":["The janitor comes around to turn the lights out. 看門人回來把燈關掉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>lights</b> to refer to a set of traffic lights. 交通訊號燈","examples":["...the heavy city traffic with its endless delays at lights and crosswalks. …擁擠的城市交通，以及在交通訊號燈和人行橫道前沒完沒了的耽擱。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"明亮","examples":["The dark green spare bedroom is in total contrast to the lightness of the large main bedroom. 深綠色的客臥與明亮寬敞的主臥形成了鮮明的對比。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is presented in a particular <b>light</b>, it is presented so that you think about it in a particular way or so that it appears to be of a particular nature. 角度; 狀態","examples":["He has worked hard in recent months to portray New York in a better light. 最近幾個月他一直努力工作要從一個更好的角度描繪紐約。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"輕巧","examples":["The toughness, lightness, strength, and elasticity of whalebone gave it a wide variety of uses. 鯨鬚的堅韌、輕巧、結實而又有彈性賦予它廣泛的用途。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or object <b>is lit</b> by something, it has light shining on it. 照亮","examples":["It was dark and a giant moon lit the road so brightly you could see the landscape clearly. 天黑了，一輪明月照亮了道路，你都可以清楚地看到風景。","The room was lit by only the one light. 這個房間只有這一盞燈照明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>light</b> something such as a cigarette or fire, or if it <b>lights</b>, it starts burning. 點燃","examples":["Stephen hunched down to light a cigarette. 斯蒂芬弓起身子點了一支菸。","If the charcoal does fail to light, use a special liquid spray and light it with a long taper. 如果木炭確實點不著，噴一種專用液體噴霧劑，再用一根長蠟燭把它點燃。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>light</b>, the sun is providing light at the beginning or end of the day. 天亮的","examples":["It was still light when we arrived at Lalong Creek. 我們到達拉隆港時，天還亮著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a room or building is <b>light</b>, it has a lot of natural light in it, for example, because it has large windows. 明亮的","examples":["It is a light room with tall windows. 這是一間明亮的房間，窗戶高大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>light</b> does not weigh very much, or weighs less than you would expect it to. (重量) 輕的","examples":["Modern tennis rackets are now apparently 20 per cent lighter. 據我所知現代的網球拍輕了20%。","...weight training with light weights. …使用輕量負荷的舉重訓練。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>light</b> is not very great in amount, degree, or intensity. (數量) 少的; (程度、強度等) 低的","examples":["It's a Sunday like any other with the usual light traffic in the city. 和以往的星期天一樣，今天城裡車輛稀少。","Trading was very light ahead of yesterday's auction. 昨天的拍賣之前交易很少。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>light</b> is very pale in colour. 淺色的","examples":["He is light haired with grey eyes. 他長著淺色的頭髮和灰色的眼睛。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>light</b> sleep is one that is easily disturbed and in which you are often aware of the things around you. If you are a <b>light</b> sleeper, you are easily woken when you are asleep. (睡眠) 淺的; 易醒的","examples":["She had drifted into a light sleep. 她已經慢慢進入了淺睡眠。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>light</b> meal consists of food that is easy to digest. 易消化的","examples":["...a light, healthy lunch. …易消化的健康午餐。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Light</b> work does not involve much physical effort. (工作) 輕鬆的","examples":["He was on the training field for some light work yesterday. 他昨天在訓練場進行一些輕鬆的訓練。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you describe the result of an action or a punishment as <b>light</b>, you mean that it is less serious or severe than you expected. (事情) 不嚴重的; (懲罰) 輕的","examples":["She confessed her astonishment at her light sentence when her father visited her at the jail. 她父親去牢裡探望她的時候，她承認自己對於受到從輕判決感到吃驚。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Movements and actions that are <b>light</b> are graceful or gentle and are done with very little force or effort. (動作、活動等) 輕盈的","examples":["Use a light touch when applying cream or makeup. 用面霜或化妝品時動作要輕柔。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>Light</b> is used to describe foods or drinks that contain few calories or low amounts of sugar, fat, or alcohol. (食品) 清淡的; (酒) 低度的; (飲料) 低熱量的","examples":["There's been a flood of low-fat and light ice creams on the market. 市場上一直有大量低脂低熱量冰淇淋。","They refreshed themselves with cans of light beer. 他們喝了幾聽低度啤酒提神。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you describe things such as books, music, and movies as <b>light</b>, you mean that they entertain you without making you think very deeply. 輕鬆的","examples":["He doesn't like me reading light novels. 他不喜歡我讀輕鬆的小說。","...light classical music. …古典輕音樂。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say something in a <b>light</b> way, you sound as if you think that something is not important or serious. 輕鬆的","examples":["Talk to him in a friendly, light way about the relationship. 以一種友好輕鬆的方式跟他談談這一關係。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>comes to light</b> or <b>is brought to light</b>, it becomes obvious or is made known to a lot of people. 暴露; 被揭露","examples":["Nothing about this sum has come to light. 這個數目一點也被沒揭露。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone in authority gives you <b>a green light</b>, they give you permission to do something. 准許","examples":["The food industry was given a green light to extend the use of these chemicals. 食品業獲准擴大這些化學品的應用範圍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is possible <b>in the light of</b> particular information, it is only possible because you have this information. 根據","examples":["In the light of this information it is now possible to identify a number of key issues. 根據這一資訊，現在有可能發現很多關鍵問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>shed light on</b>, <b>throw light on</b>, or <b>cast light on</b> something means to make it easier to understand, because more information is known about it. 闡明某事","examples":["A new approach offers an answer, and may shed light on an even bigger question. 一種新方法提供一個答案，而且可能闡明更大的問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>set light to</b> something, you make it start burning. 點燃","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>make light of</b> something, you treat it as though it is not serious or important, when in fact it is. 輕視","examples":["Roberts attempted to make light of his discomfort. 羅伯茨試圖不去在乎自己的不適。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕地","examples":["Put the onions in the pan and cook until lightly browned. 把洋蔥放入鍋中，炒到稍微發褐色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"易醒地","examples":["He was dozing lightly in his chair. 他在椅子上淺淺地打著瞌睡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"易消化地","examples":["She found it impossible to eat lightly. 她當時發現不可能吃到易消化的東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"輕地","examples":["One of the accused got off lightly in exchange for pleading guilty to withholding information from Congress. 其中一名被告獲得了從輕發落，因其承認了未向國會提供情報的罪行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"輕輕地","examples":["He kissed her lightly on the mouth. 他輕輕地吻了一下她的嘴。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"輕鬆地","examples":["\"Once a detective, always a detective,\" he said lightly. 他輕鬆地說：“一朝是偵探，終身是偵探。”"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Light</b> is also a combining form. (Light)也是一個構詞成分","examples":["We know he has a light green van. 我們知道他有一輛淺綠色的貨車。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(esp of birds) to settle or land after flight (尤指鳥)飛落","examples":[]}]}]},"lunch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"午餐，午飯"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>（尤指在餐館）用午餐；請（人）吃午餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lunch</b> is the meal that you have in the middle of the day. 午餐","examples":["Shall we meet somewhere for lunch? 我們約個地方一起吃午飯好嗎？","He did not enjoy business lunches. 他不喜歡工作午餐。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>lunch</b>, you have lunch, especially at a restaurant. (尤指在餐館) 進午餐","examples":["Only the extremely rich could afford to lunch at the Mirabelle. 只有大富豪才吃得起米拉貝爾飯店的午餐。"]}]}]},"lot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"(常sing.) 一群，一批；小塊土地；電影攝製場；（汽車經銷處的）停車場；拍賣品；<英>全體成員；（尤指不太好的）命運, 處境；籤，鬮；一群，一批"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（拍賣前）將（商品）分成批組"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"大量，許多；所有，全部"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很多地，非常（a lot）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A lot of</b> something or <b>lots of</b> it is a large amount of it. <b>A lot of</b> people or things, or <b>lots of</b> them, is a large number of them. 大量","examples":["A lot of our land is used to grow crops for export. 我們的土地大多用來種植出口農作物。","He drank lots of milk. 他喝了許多奶。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lot</b> is also a pronoun. 大量","examples":["I personally prefer to be in a town where there's lots going on. 我個人更喜歡呆在充滿生機的小鎮上。","I learned a lot from him about how to run a band. 我從他那裡學了很多管理樂隊的知識。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A lot</b> means to a great extent or degree. 非常","examples":["Matthew's out quite a lot doing his research. 馬修經常出去做研究。","I like you, a lot. 我非常喜歡你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>a lot</b>, you do it often or for a long time. 頻繁地; 長期地","examples":["They went out a lot, to restaurants and bars. 他們經常去飯店和酒吧。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lot</b> to refer to a set or group of things or people. 一組","examples":["He bought two lots of 1,000 shares in the company during August and September. 他在8月和9月期間兩次購進了這家公司的股票，每次1千股。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a specific group of people as a particular <b>lot</b>. 一群人","examples":["Future generations are going to think that we were a pretty boring lot. 後輩們會認為我們是一群無聊的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>the lot</b> to refer to the whole of an amount that you have just mentioned. 全部; 全體","examples":["This may turn out to be the best football game of the lot. 這可能會是全部足球比賽中最棒的一場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>lot</b> is the kind of life you have or the things that you have or experience. 命運","examples":["She tried to accept her marriage as her lot in life but could not. 她試圖認命接受這樁婚姻，但做不到。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>lot</b> is a small area of land that belongs to a person or company. (個人或公司的) 一小塊地","examples":["If oil or gold are discovered under your lot, you can sell the mineral rights. 如果在你的地裡發現石油或金子，你可以出售開採權。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>lot</b> in an auction is one of the objects or groups of objects that are being sold. 拍賣物","examples":["The receivers are keen to sell the stores as one lot. 接受方非常願意把這些商店一起拍賣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>draw lots</b> to decide who will do something, they each take a piece of paper from a container. One or more pieces of paper is marked, and the people who take marked pieces are chosen. 抽籤","examples":["For the first time in the World Cup finals, lots had to be drawn to decide who would finish second and third. 世界盃決賽中首次由抽籤決定誰將獲得第二名和第三名。"]}]}]},"luncheon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正式的午餐，午宴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>luncheon</b> is a formal lunch, for example, to celebrate an important event or to raise money for charity. 午宴","examples":["Earlier this month, a luncheon for former U.N. staff was held in Vienna. 本月早些時候在維也納為前聯合國工作人員舉行了午宴。"]}]}]},"line":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"線，線條；（運動場地的）場界，場地線；皺紋，褶子；分界線，邊界線；（思想或行為等的）界限；輪廓，外形；排，行，列；佇列，隊伍；一系列（類似事物），家族；各級人員；字行，詩行；（戲劇或電影的）臺詞，對白；<英>罰抄寫（對學童的處罰）（lines）；妙語，謊話；線，繩，索；電話線（路）；熱線（電話），電話服務；（鐵道或公交）線路；鐵軌，軌道；管線；（行進的）方向，路線；路徑，渠道；（尤指公開表明的）態度，看法；方法，方式；行業，行當；種類，型別；運輸公司，航運公司；防線，前線，戰線；生產線，流水線；一串音符；（準備吸用的）散放成細線的毒品；赤道（the Line）；（印刷，計算機）線條的；字母底部水平線（the line）；（正規）戰鬥部隊（the line）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"沿……形成行（或列、排）；給……安襯裡，鋪，墊；（在某物的內部）形成一層；擊出（平直球）；用線條標出，佈滿線條（lined）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>line</b> is a long thin mark which is drawn or painted on a surface. 線","examples":["Draw a line down that page's centre. 沿著那一頁的中心向下畫一條線。","...a dotted line. …一條虛線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>lines</b> on someone's skin, especially on their face, are long thin marks that appear there as they grow older. 皺紋","examples":["He has a large, generous face with deep lines. 他寬大的面龐上帶著很深的皺紋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>line</b> of people or things is a number of them arranged one behind the other or side by side. (一) 排","examples":["The sparse line of spectators noticed nothing unusual. 稀稀疏疏的一排觀眾並沒注意到什麼特別之處。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>line</b> of people or vehicles is a number of them that are waiting one behind another, for example, in order to buy something or to go in a particular direction. 佇列","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>line</b> of a piece of writing is one of the rows of words, numbers, or other symbols in it. (一) 行 (文字、數字、符號)","examples":["The next line should read: Five days, 23.5 hours. 下一行文字應是：5天，23.5小時。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>line</b> of a poem, song, or play is a group of words that are spoken or sung together. If an actor <b>learns</b> his or her <b>lines</b> for a play or film, they learn what they have to say. 臺詞; 詩行","examples":["...a line from Shakespeare's Othello: \"one that loved not wisely but too well.\" …莎士比亞戲劇《奧賽羅》裡的一句臺詞：“一個在戀愛上不聰明卻過於深情的人。”","Every time I sing that line, I have to compete with that darn trombone! 每當我唱那行歌詞時，我都得和那該死的長號比賽。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can refer to a long piece of wire, string, or cable as a <b>line</b> when it is used for a particular purpose. 線; 繩","examples":["She put her washing on the line. 她把洗好的衣服晾在繩子上。","...a piece of fishing-line. …一根釣魚線。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>line</b> is a connection which makes it possible for two people to speak to each other on the telephone. 電話線路","examples":["The telephone lines went dead. 電話線路不通了。","It's not a very good line. Shall we call you back Susan? 線路不太好。蘇珊，我們給你打回去好嗎？"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>line</b> to refer to a telephone number which you can call in order to get information or advice. 諮詢電話號碼","examples":["...the 24-hour information line. …24小時資訊諮詢電話號碼。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A <b>line</b> is a route, especially a dangerous or secret one, along which people move or send messages or supplies. (傳送資訊、輸送人員或物資的危險、秘密) 通道","examples":["The North American continent's geography severely limited the lines of attack. 北美大陸的地形嚴格限制了進攻通道。","Negotiators say they're keeping communication lines open. 談判代表聲稱他們保持著溝通管道的通暢。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"The <b>line</b> in which something or someone moves is the particular route that they take, especially when they keep moving straight ahead. 運動路線","examples":["Walk in a straight line. 走直線。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"A <b>line</b> is a particular route, involving the same stations, roads, or stops along which a train or bus service regularly operates. (火車、公共汽車執行的) 路線","examples":["They've got to ride all the way to the end of the line. 他們得乘車直到路線的終點。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A railway <b>line</b> consists of the pieces of metal and wood which form the track that the trains travel along. 鐵軌","examples":["Floods washed out much of the railway line. 洪水沖毀了很多鐵軌。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"A shipping, air, or bus <b>line</b> is a company which provides services for transporting people or goods by sea, air, or bus. 運輸公司","examples":["The Cunard shipping line came up with a clever slogan: \"Getting there is half the fun...\" 冠達海運公司想出了一個聰明的口號：“一半的樂趣來自於到達目的地…”"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"A state or county <b>line</b> is a boundary between two states or counties. 界限","examples":["...the California state line. …加利福尼亞州的州界。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You can use <b>lines</b> to refer to the set of physical defences or the soldiers that have been established along the boundary of an area occupied by an army. 防線","examples":["Their unit was shelling the German lines only seven miles away. 他們的部隊正炮轟僅7英里外的德國防線。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"The particular <b>line</b> that a person has toward a problem is the attitude that they have toward it. For example, if someone takes a <b>hard line</b> on something, they have a firm strict policy which they refuse to change. 方針","examples":["Forty members of the governing Conservative party rebelled, voting against the government line. 執政的保守黨中的40名成員倒戈，投票反對政府方針。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You can use <b>line</b> to refer to the way in which someone's thoughts or activities develop, particularly if it is logical. 思路","examples":["Our discussion in the previous chapter continues this line of thinking. 我們在前一章的討論延續了這種思維方式。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>along</b> particular <b>lines</b>, or <b>on</b> particular <b>lines</b>, you are giving a general summary or approximate account of what happens, which may not be correct in every detail. 概況","examples":["There followed an assortment of praise for the coffee along the lines of \"Hey, this coffee is fantastic!\" 接著是各種各樣大概就像“嘿，這咖啡真棒”一樣的對咖啡的稱讚。","He'd said something on those lines already. 他已說過內容大致類似的話。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If something is organized <b>on</b> particular <b>lines</b>, or <b>along</b> particular <b>lines</b>, it is organized according to that method or principle. 原則; 方法","examples":["...so-called autonomous republics based on ethnic lines. …建立在種族原則基礎上的所謂自治共和國。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"Your <b>line</b> <b>of</b> business or work is the kind of work that you do. 行業","examples":["So what was your father's line of business? 那麼你父親是幹哪一行的？"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"In a factory, a <b>line</b> is an arrangement of workers or machines where a product passes from one worker to another until it is finished. 流水線","examples":["...a production line capable of producing three different products. …一條能生產3種不同產品的流水線。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"You can use <b>line</b> when you are referring to a number of people who are ranked according to status. 次序","examples":["Nicholas Paul Patrick was seventh in the line of succession to the throne. 尼古拉斯·保羅·帕特里克在王位繼承順序上排第7。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"A particular <b>line</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a series of them that has existed over a period of time, when they have all been similar in some way, or done similar things. (某個時期有某種共同之處的人、事物的) 系列","examples":["We were part of a long line of artists. 我們是由古至今代代藝術家中的一代。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>crossed the line</b> or has <b>stepped over the line</b>, you mean that they have behaved in a way that is considered unacceptable. 舉止不當","examples":["Sometimes, I think the administration steps over the line when they make these kinds of accusations. 有時候，我認為行政部門在發出這類指責時，他們已經出格了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>draw the line</b> <b>at</b> a particular activity, you refuse to do it, because you disapprove of it or because it is more extreme than what you normally do. 拒絕","examples":["Letters have come from prisoners, declaring that they would draw the line at hitting an old lady. 來自囚犯們的信件宣告他們不會襲擊一個老婦人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something or if it happens to you <b>in the line of duty</b>, you do it or it happens as part of your regular work or as a result of it. 在執行公務中","examples":["More than 3,000 police officers were wounded in the line of duty last year. 去年三千多名警官在執行任務時受傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to a method as <b>the first line of</b>, for example, defence or treatment, you mean that it is the first or most important method to be used in dealing with a problem. 首要手段","examples":["Residents have the responsibility of being the first line of defence against wildfires. 居民有責任成為野火的首要防衛人員。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If one object is <b>in line</b> <b>with</b> others, or moves <b>into line</b> <b>with</b> others, they are arranged in a line. You can also say that a number of objects are <b>in line</b> or move <b>into line</b>. 成一直線","examples":["The device itself was right under the vehicle, almost in line with the gear lever. 這個裝置本身就在車子下面，幾乎與換擋桿成一直線。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If one thing is <b>in line</b> <b>with</b> another, or is brought <b>into line</b> <b>with</b> it, the first thing is, or becomes, similar to the second, especially in a way that has been planned or expected. 與…一致","examples":["The structure of our schools is now broadly in line with the major countries of the world. 目前我國學校的結構與世界主要國家的是基本一致的。","This brings the law into line with most medical opinion. 這使得該法律與醫療界的大多數意見一致。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> someone <b>in line</b> or <b>bring</b> them <b>into line</b>, you make them obey you, or you make them behave in the way you want them to. 守規矩","examples":["All this was just designed to frighten me and keep me in line. 所有這一切只是設計來嚇唬我、讓我守規矩。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a machine or piece of equipment comes <b>on line</b>, it starts operating. If it is <b>off line</b>, it is not operating. 在執行中","examples":["The new machine will go on line in June 2006. 這臺新機器將在2006年6月投入使用。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you do something <b>on line</b>, you do it using a computer or a computer network. 在網上","examples":["They can order their requirements on line. 他們可以在網上定購所需物品。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things <b>line</b> a road, room, or other place, they are present in large numbers along its edges or sides. 沿…排列成行","examples":["Thousands of local people lined the streets and clapped as the procession went by. 遊行隊伍經過時，數以千計的當地人在街上列隊並鼓掌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>line</b> a wall, container, or other object, you put a layer of something such as leaves or paper on the inside surface of it in order to make it stronger, warmer, or cleaner. 給…加襯","examples":["Line the basket with a bright chequered napkin just before adding the cookies. 放入餅乾前，先往籃子裡墊上一張鮮亮的方格餐巾。"]}]}]},"ma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"媽"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Ma）（老、柬、剛（金））馬（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people refer to or address their mother as <b>ma</b>. 媽媽","examples":["Ma was still at work when I got back. 我回來的時候媽媽還在工作。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Morocco 摩洛哥","examples":[]}]}]},"little":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小的，比較小的；用於強調對某人或某物的意見；年幼的；短暫的，近的；微不足道的；可愛的，可憐的"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"一點兒，少得幾乎沒有；少量的，一些"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極少，輕微；幾乎不；短時間地，一會兒地"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"少許"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>little</b> to indicate that there is only a very small amount of something. You can use \"so,\" \"too,\" and \"very\" in front of <b>little</b>. 微少的","examples":["I had little money and little free time. 我沒什麼錢，也很少有空閒時間。","I find that I need very little sleep these days. 我覺得我現在需要的睡眠很少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>A little</b> of something is a small amount of it, but not very much. You can also say <b>a very little</b>. 一點兒","examples":["Mrs. Caan needs a little help getting her groceries home. 凱恩夫人需要一點兒幫助才能把雜貨弄回家。","A little food would do us all some good. 吃一點兒東西會對我們大家都有些好處。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Little</b> is also a quantifier. 一點","examples":["Little of the existing housing is of good enough quality. 現有的住房中少有質量夠好的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Little</b> is also a quantifier. 一點","examples":["Pour a little of the sauce over the chicken. 往雞肉上倒一點調料。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Little</b> is also a pronoun. 少量","examples":["He ate little, and drank less. 他吃得不多，喝得更少。","In general, employers do little to help the single working mother. 總的來說，僱主很少幫助那些工作的單身媽媽們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Little</b> is also a pronoun. 一點兒","examples":["They get paid for it. Not much. Just a little. 他們拿到工資了。不太多，就一點點。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Little</b> means not very often or to only a small extent. 不多","examples":["On their way back to Marseille they spoke very little. 在他們回馬賽的路上，他們說話不多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>a little</b>, you do it for a short time. 一小會兒","examples":["He walked a little by himself in the garden. 他在花園裡獨自散了會兒步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>A little</b> or <b>a little bit</b> means to a small extent or degree. (程度上) 有點","examples":["He complained a little of a nagging pain between his shoulder blades. 他抱怨說他的肩胛之間有點持續的疼痛。","He was a little bit afraid of his father's reaction. 他有點害怕他父親的反應。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Little</b> things are small in size. <b>Little</b> is slightly more informal than . (尺寸) 小的","examples":["We sat around a little table, eating and drinking wine. 我們圍坐在一張小桌子旁吃飯、喝酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>little</b> to indicate that someone or something is small, in a pleasant and attractive way. 小巧的","examples":["She's got the nicest little house not far from the library. 她在離圖書館不遠處有座最漂亮的小房子。","...a little old lady. …一位嬌小的老太太。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>little</b> sister or brother is younger than you are. 年紀小的","examples":["Whenever Daniel's little sister was asked to do something she always had a naughty reply. 每次讓丹尼爾的小妹妹做點事情，她總是有調皮的回應。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>little</b> distance, period of time, or event is short in length. (時間、距離、比賽) 短的","examples":["Just go down the road a little way, turn left, and cross the bridge. 只沿著公路走一小段距離，向左轉，然後跨過那座橋。","Why don't we just wait a little while and see what happens. 我們何不就等一小會兒，看看發生什麼事。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>little</b> sound or gesture is quick. (聲音或動作) 迅速的","examples":["I had a little laugh to myself. 我暗自笑了笑。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>little</b> to indicate that something is not serious or important. 微小的","examples":["...irritating little habits. …惱人的小習慣。"]}]}]},"love":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對家庭成員或摯友的）喜愛，關愛；愛情，戀愛；喜好，喜愛；<英，非正式>（暱稱）親愛的；（用於信尾署名前）愛你的；心愛之人，心愛之物；（網球、軟式牆網球和其他運動）零分；<非正式>（用於表示對某人的親切好感）寶貝（a love）；仁慈的人，樂於助人的人；愛神（Love）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"愛戀（某人）；關愛（尤指家庭成員或密友）；喜歡（某物或某事）；熱愛（國家、組織等）；很願意；<非正式>感到好笑；適於（某些特定的條件）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>love</b> someone, you feel romantically or sexually attracted to them, and they are very important to you. 愛","examples":["Oh, Amy, I love you. 啊，埃米，我愛你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that you <b>love</b> someone when their happiness is very important to you, so that you behave in a kind and caring way toward them. 疼愛","examples":["You'll never love anyone the way you love your baby. 你永遠不會像疼愛你的孩子那樣愛任何人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>love</b> something, you like it very much. 非常喜歡","examples":["We loved the food so much, especially the fish dishes. 我們非常喜歡這些食物，尤其是那幾盤魚。","...one of these people that loves to be in the outdoors. …那些喜歡戶外生活的人們中的一員。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say that you <b>love</b> something when you consider that it is important and want to protect or support it. 熱愛","examples":["I love my country as you love yours. 我熱愛我的國家，就像你熱愛你的國家一樣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>would love</b> <b>to</b> have or do something, you very much want to have it or do it. 很願意","examples":["I would love to play for England again. 我很願意再次為英格蘭參賽。","I would love a hot bath and clean clothes. 我很想洗個熱水澡，換身乾淨衣服。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Love</b> is a very strong feeling of affection toward someone who you are romantically or sexually attracted to. 愛情","examples":["Our love for each other has been increased by what we've been through together. 我們對彼此的愛因我們共同經歷的一切而增強。","...an old fashioned love story. …一個老套的愛情故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Love</b> is the feeling that a person's happiness is very important to you, and the way you show this feeling in your behaviour toward them. 疼愛","examples":["My love for all my children is unconditional. 我對我所有孩子的疼愛是無條件的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Love</b> is a strong liking for something, or a belief that it is important. 熱愛","examples":["This is no way to encourage a love of literature. 這不可能激發對文學的熱愛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>love</b> is someone or something that you love. 心愛之人; 心愛之物","examples":["\"She is the love of my life,\" he said. “她是我今生至愛，”他說道。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you send someone your <b>love</b>, you ask another person, who will soon be speaking or writing to them, to tell them that you are thinking about them with affection. 問候","examples":["Please give her my love. 請代我問候她。"]}]},{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In tennis, <b>love</b> is a score of zero. (網球比賽中的) 零分","examples":["He beat Thomas Muster of Austria three sets to love. 他以3比0戰勝了奧地利的托馬斯·穆斯特。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>love</b>, <b>love from</b>, and <b>all my love</b>, followed by your name, as an informal way of ending a letter to a friend or relative. (給親友的書信結尾，置於寫信人名前) 愛你的","examples":["...with love from Grandma and Grandpa. …愛你的祖父母。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fall in love</b> <b>with</b> someone, you start to be in love with them. 愛上 (某人)","examples":["I fell in love with him because of his kind nature. 我愛上了他，因為他天性善良。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fall in love</b> <b>with</b> something, you start to like it very much. 非常喜歡 (某物)","examples":["I fell in love with the movies. 我非常喜歡這些電影。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are in love</b> <b>with</b> someone, you feel romantically or sexually attracted to them, and they are very important to you. (與某人) 戀愛","examples":["Laura had never before been in love. 勞拉以前從未談過戀愛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>in love</b> <b>with</b> something, you like it very much. 迷戀 (某物)","examples":["He had always been in love with the enchanted landscape of the West. 他一直都非常迷戀西部令人陶醉的風光。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When two people <b>make love</b>, they have sex. 做愛","examples":["Have you ever made love to a girl before? 你以前和女孩子做過愛嗎？"]}]}]},"mamma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"媽媽；乳房"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Mamma）人名；（意）馬馬"}],"sections":[]},"mama":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"〈舊〉媽媽，母親（亦作 mamma）；〈非正式〉女人；（Mama）馬馬（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mama</b> means the same as . 同mother","examples":[]}]}]},"low":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"低的，矮的；在底部的；領口開得低的；（緯度）低的，近赤道的；低於通常（或平均）數量（或水平、價值）的；（聲、熱或光）低的，暗的；（地位、階層上）低微的，低等的；消沉的，精神不振的；（質量或標準）低的；（藝術，文化）低俗的；不誠實的，下流的；（觀點）貶低的，輕蔑的； （供應品）將耗盡的，短缺的；（母音）舌位低的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在（或向）低位置；低於通常（或期望）的水平；低聲地，小聲地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"低點；（人生的）低谷；低氣壓區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（牛）哞哞叫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>low</b> measures only a short distance from the bottom to the top, or from the ground to the top. 低矮的","examples":["...the low garden wall that separated the front garden from next door. …低矮的花園圍牆隔開了前花園與鄰院。","The country, with its low, rolling hills was beautiful. 這一地區山勢低緩，連綿起伏，非常美麗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>low</b>, it is close to the ground, to sea level, or to the bottom of something. 接近地面的; 接近海平面的; 接近底部的","examples":["He bumped his head on the low beams. 他的頭撞到了低矮的橫樑上。","It was late afternoon and the sun was low in the sky. 當時是傍晚時分，太陽低低地掛在天上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a river is <b>low</b>, it contains less water than usual. 水位淺的","examples":["...pumps that guarantee a constant depth of water even when the supplying river is low. …那些即使在供應水源的河流水位很低時仍能保持水位的水泵。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>low</b> to indicate that something is small in amount or that it is at the bottom of a particular scale. You can use phrases such as <b>in the low 80s</b> to indicate that a number or level is less than 85 but not as little as 80. 數量少的; 數值偏低的","examples":["Casualties remained remarkably low. 傷亡人數依然很少。","They are still having to live on very low incomes. 他們仍然不得不靠微薄的收入為生。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Low</b> is used to describe people who are not considered to be very important because they are near the bottom of a particular scale or system. (級別等) 低微的","examples":["She refused to promote Colin above the low rank of \"legal adviser.\" 她拒絕提升科林，只讓他做低階別的“法律顧問”。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If the quality or standard of something is <b>low</b>, it is very poor. (品質) 差的; (水平) 低的","examples":["A school would not accept low-quality work from any student. 學校不會接受任何學生的低水平作品。","The inquiry team criticizes staff at the psychiatric hospital for the low standard of care. 該調查組批評精神病醫院工作人員的低護理水平。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a food or other substance is <b>low in</b> a particular ingredient, it contains only a small amount of that ingredient. 含量低的","examples":["They look for foods that are low in calories. 他們尋找低熱量食物。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Low</b> is also a combining form. 用於構成合成詞","examples":["...low-sodium tomato sauce. …鈉含量低的番茄醬。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you have a <b>low</b> opinion of someone or something, you disapprove of them or dislike them. (評價) 很差的","examples":["The majority of sex offenders have a low opinion of themselves. 大多數性犯罪者自我評價都很低。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can use <b>low</b> to describe negative feelings and attitudes. 消沉的","examples":["We are all very tired and morale is low. 我們都疲憊不堪，士氣低落。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If a sound or noise is <b>low</b>, it is deep. 低沉的","examples":["Then suddenly she gave a low, choking moan and began to tremble violently. 然後她突然發出一聲低沉的、令人窒息的呻吟，身體開始劇烈地抖動。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone's voice is <b>low</b>, it is quiet or soft. 輕聲的","examples":["Her voice was so low he had to strain to catch it. 她的聲音太小，他不得不費力地聽著。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"A light that is <b>low</b> is not bright or strong. 暗淡的","examples":["Their eyesight is poor in low light. 他們在昏暗的光線下看不清東西。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If a radio, oven, or light is on <b>low</b>, it has been adjusted so that only a small amount of sound, heat, or light is produced. (收音機音量、烤箱溫度或燈光亮度調成)低的","examples":["She turned her little kitchen radio on low. 她把廚房的小收音機聲音調得很低。","Buy a dimmer switch and keep the light on low, or switch it off altogether. 買一個調光器，把亮度調低，或者完全關掉。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you are <b>low</b> <b>on</b> something or if a supply of it is <b>low</b>, there is not much of it left. 不足的","examples":["We're a bit low on bed linen. 我們的床上用品不足了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you are <b>low</b>, you are depressed. 情緒低落的","examples":["\"I didn't ask for this job, you know,\" he tells friends when he is low. “我沒有要求做這份工作，你知道的。”他在情緒低落的時候告訴朋友們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something reaches a <b>low</b> of a particular amount or degree, that is the smallest it has ever been. 最低點","examples":["Prices dropped to a low of about $1.12 in December. 價格在12月份跌到大約$1.12的最低點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the sound uttered by cattle; moo 牛叫聲","examples":[]}]}]},"mail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵政，郵遞系統；郵件，信件；電子郵件；鎧甲，鎖子甲；（某些動物的）甲殼，鱗；<舊>郵車，郵政運輸工具；<古>郵件包，郵袋；郵報（用於報紙名稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"郵寄；用電子郵件傳送；給……披上鎧甲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The mail</b> is the public service or system by which letters and packages are collected and delivered. 郵政","examples":["Your cheque is in the mail. 你的支票在郵寄中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to letters and packages that are delivered to you as <b>mail</b>. 郵件","examples":["There was no mail except the usual junk addressed to the occupant. 除了寄給住戶的常見的垃圾郵件之外，沒有其他郵件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a type of flexible armour consisting of riveted metal rings or links 鎖子甲","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the hard protective shell of such animals as the turtle and lobster (龜、龍蝦等的)保護殼","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Mail</b> is also a noun. 電子郵件","examples":["If you have any problems then send me a mail. 如有任何問題就給我發郵件。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mail</b> a letter or package to someone, you send it to them by putting it in a postbox or taking it to a post office. 郵寄","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>mail</b> a message to someone means to send it to them by means of e-mail or a computer network. 傳送 (電子郵件)","examples":[]}]}]},"machine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機器，機械（裝置）；計算機，電腦；（組織的）核心機構，領導核心；車輛（常指摩托車）；效率高的人（或動物）；機械般工作的人；（投幣式）自動售貨機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用機器製造（加工）；機器縫製，用縫紉機縫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>machine</b> is a piece of equipment that uses electricity or an engine in order to do a particular kind of work. 機器","examples":["I put the coin in the machine and pulled the lever. 我把硬幣投進機器，然後拉了控制桿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>machine</b> to refer to a large and well-controlled system or organization. 機構","examples":["...Nazi Germany's military machine. …納粹德國的軍事機構。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>machine</b> something, you make it or work on it using a machine. 用機器製造; 用機器加工","examples":["The material is machined in a factory. 該材料在一家工廠用機器加工而成。","...machined brass zinc alloy gears. …機器加工的黃銅鋅合金齒輪。"]}]}]},"map":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地圖；分佈圖；（基因）圖譜，染色體圖；天體圖；對映；<非正式>臉，面孔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"繪製……的地圖；瞭解資訊；詳細安排；對映；與……有關，與……有聯絡；使（基因）在染色體上定位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>map</b> is a drawing of a particular area such as a city, a country, or a continent, showing its main features as they would appear if you looked at them from above. 地圖","examples":["He unfolded the map and set it on the floor. 他展開地圖，把它放在了地板上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>map</b> an area means to make a map of it. 繪製…的地圖","examples":["...a spacecraft which is using radar to map the surface of Venus. …一艘利用雷達繪製金星表面地圖的航天器。"]}]}]},"meat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肉類，（某種）食用肉；重要的部分，有趣的部分；<美>棒球球棒等物體最粗的部分；<古>食物；果肉，堅果仁，（蛋的）可食用部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Meat</b> is flesh taken from a dead animal that people cook and eat. (供食用的) 肉","examples":["Meat and fish are relatively expensive. 肉和魚相對較貴。","...imported meat products. …進口的肉製品。"]}]}]},"market":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"集市，市場；交易，交易量；行銷地區，購買人群；市場機制；股市；市面，市況"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"推銷，促銷；出售；做買賣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"市場的，由市場決定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>market</b> is a place where goods are bought and sold, usually outdoors. 市場","examples":["He sold boots at a market stall. 他在市場的一個攤位上賣靴子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>market</b> for a particular type of thing is the number of people who want to buy it, or the area of the world in which it is sold. 需求量; 商品行銷地區","examples":["The foreign market was increasingly crucial. 國外的市場越來越關鍵了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>market</b> refers to the total amount of a product that is sold each year, especially when you are talking about the competition between the companies who sell that product. 年總銷售量","examples":["The two big companies control 72% of the market. 這兩家大公司控制了72%的市場份額。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The job market</b> or <b>the labour market</b> refers to the people who are looking for work and the jobs available for them to do. 就業市場","examples":["Every year, 250,000 people enter the job market. 每年有250000人進入就業市場。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The stock market is sometimes referred to as <b>the market</b>. 股票市場","examples":["The market collapsed last October. 股票市場去年10月崩盤了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a <b>market</b> economy, or the <b>market</b> price of something, you are referring to an economic system in which the prices of things depend on how many are available and how many people want to buy them, rather than prices being fixed by governments. 市場的","examples":["Their ultimate aim was a market economy for Hungary. 他們的最終目標是為匈牙利建立市場經濟。","He must sell the house for the current market value. 他必須按照目前的市場價格出售這套房子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>market</b> a product means to organize its sale, by deciding on its price, where it should be sold, and how it should be advertised. 營銷","examples":["...if you marketed our music the way you market pop music. …如果你按照營銷流行音樂的方式營銷我們的音樂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>a buyer's market</b>, you mean that it is a good time to buy a particular thing, because there is a lot of it available, so its price is low. If you say that it is <b>a seller's market</b>, you mean that very little of it is available, so its price is high. 買方市場; 賣方市場","examples":["Don't be afraid to haggle: for the moment, it's a buyer's market. 別怕討價還價：目前是買方市場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in the market for</b> something, you are interested in buying it. 很想購買","examples":["If you're in the market for a new radio, you'll see that the latest models are very different. 如果你想買臺新收音機，你會發現最新的款型很不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>on the market</b>, it is available for people to buy. If it comes <b>onto the market</b>, it becomes available for people to buy. 在市場上出售","examples":["...putting more empty offices on the market. …把更多的閒置辦公間投入市場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>price</b> yourself <b>out of the market</b>, you try to sell goods or services at a higher price than other people, with the result that no one buys them from you. 要價過高而未能成交","examples":["At $250,000 for a season, he really is pricing himself out of the market. 一個賽季要25萬美元，他確實要價太高，讓別人不敢問津了。"]}]}]},"may":{"summaries":[{"pos":"aux.","zh":"可能，也許（表示某情況是可能的）；可以（徵求同意或表示允許）；可能（表示某情況屬實，另一情況也屬實）；祝，願（用於表達願望）；可以，能夠（表明目的）；可以，也許（用於提出禮貌的建議）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"山楂花；五月（May）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> to indicate that something will possibly happen or be true in the future, but you cannot be certain. (將來) 可能","examples":["We may have some rain today. 今天可能會下點雨。","I may be back next year. 我可能明年回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> to indicate that there is a possibility that something is true, but you cannot be certain. 可能 (是真的)","examples":["Civil rights officials say there may be hundreds of other cases of racial violence. 負責公民權利的官員說可能有幾百起其他的種族暴力案件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> to indicate that something is sometimes true or is true in some circumstances. 可能 (有時或在某些情況下屬實)","examples":["A vegetarian diet may not provide enough calories for a child's normal growth. 素食可能無法提供一名孩子正常成長所需要的足夠熱量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>may have</b> with a past participle when suggesting that it is possible that something happened or was true, or when giving a possible explanation for something. 與過去分詞連用，表示某事可能已經發生、屬實或提供解釋","examples":["He may have been to some of those places. 那些地方他可能去過一些。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> in statements where you are accepting the truth of a situation, but contrasting it with something that is more important. 用於承認情況屬實，但同時將之與更重要的東西作比較","examples":["I may be almost 50, but there's not much I've forgotten. 我是快五十歲了，但我沒忘記多少事情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> when you are mentioning a quality or fact about something that people can make use of if they want to. 可以 (加以利用)","examples":["The bag has narrow straps, so it may be worn over the shoulder or carried in the hand. 這個書包有細長帶子，所有它可以被肩挎，也可以用手拎。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> to indicate that someone is allowed to do something, usually because of a rule or law. You use <b>may not</b> to indicate that someone is not allowed to do something. (法規) 允許/不允許","examples":["In the US, any two persons may marry provided that both persons are at least 16 years of age on the day of their marriage. 在美國，任何兩個人都可以結婚，只要在結婚日雙方都至少十六歲。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> when you are giving permission to someone to do something, or when asking for permission. 可以 (表示許可)","examples":["Mr. Hobbs? May we come in? 霍布斯先生？我們可以進去嗎？"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> when you are making polite requests. 可以 (用於禮貌的請求)","examples":["I'd like the use of your living room, if I may. 如果可以，我想用用你的起居室。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>may</b> when you are mentioning the reaction or attitude that you think someone is likely to have to something you are about to say. 可能會 (用於別人對自己所說的話可能會有的反應或態度)","examples":["You know, Brian, whatever you may think, I work hard for a living. 你知道，布雷恩，不管你會怎麼想，我是為了生計而努力工作。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you do something so that a particular thing <b>may</b> happen, you do it so that there is an opportunity for that thing to happen. 以便能","examples":["...the need for an increase in the numbers of surgeons so that patients may be treated as soon as possible. …增加外科醫生人數以便讓病人能儘快被救治的需要。"]}]}]},"middle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中間的，中等的；折中的，中庸之道的；（語言）中古的，介於現代與古代之間的；語法中動態的，中間反身態的；（英語及物動詞）無被動態的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"中間，中部，中等；腰部；語法中動態，中間反身態"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（板球、網球等中）用球棒（或拍）中部擊（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>middle</b> <b>of</b> something is the part of it that is farthest from its edges, ends, or outside surface. 中間","examples":["Howard stood in the middle of the room sipping a cup of coffee. 霍華德站在房子中間，啜飲著一杯咖啡。","They had a volleyball court in the middle of the courtyard. 他們在院子中央有一個排球場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>middle</b> <b>of</b> an event or period of time is the part that comes after the first part and before the last part. 中期","examples":["I woke up in the middle of the night and could hear a tapping on the window. 我半夜醒來，聽到輕敲窗戶的聲音。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>middle</b> object in a row of objects is the one that has an equal number of objects on each side. 當中的","examples":["The middle button of his uniform jacket was strained over his belly. 他制服上衣中間的那個釦子在他的肚子上繃得緊緊的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Middle</b> is also an adjective. 中期的","examples":["Many classical violinists and pianists become conductors in their middle years. 許多古典小提琴手和鋼琴演奏者在中年時變成指揮家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in the middle of</b> doing something, you are busy doing it. 正忙於","examples":["It's a bit hectic. I'm in the middle of cooking for nine people. 有點兒忙不過來了。我正忙著給9個人做飯呢。"]}]}]},"man":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成年男子，男人；人類；（不論性別的）人；（來自某地、從事某種工作的）人；（喜歡某事的）人 ； （支援某組織或為其工作的）人；士兵，（男性）工人 ；上門服務的人；夥計，哥兒們；（表示不耐煩或生氣）你這傢伙；丈夫，男友；男子漢，大丈夫；棋子；<非正式>頭頭，老闆，警察（the Man）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"負責，操控（某物）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<美，非正式>（表示驚奇、氣憤等）嘿，天哪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>man</b> is an adult male human being. 男子; 男人","examples":["He had not expected the young man to reappear before evening. 他沒想到那個年輕男子傍晚前會再次出現。","I have always regarded him as a man of integrity. 我一直把他看作個正直的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Man</b> and <b>men</b> are sometimes used to refer to all human beings, including both males and females. Some people dislike this use. 人 (用以泛指)","examples":["The chick initially has no fear of man. 小雞最初不怕人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a man is, for example, <b>a gambling man</b> or <b>an outdoors man</b>, you mean that he likes gambling or outdoor activities. (有某嗜好的) 人","examples":["Are you a gambling man, Mr. Graham? 你是個賭徒嗎，格雷勒姆先生?"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a man is, for example, <b>a Harvard man</b> or <b>a Yale man</b>, you mean that he went to that university. (屬某院校的) 人","examples":["Stewart, a Yale man, was invited to stay on and write the script. 斯圖爾特，一個耶魯人，應邀留下來寫該劇本。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to a particular company's or organization's <b>man</b>, you mean a man who works for or represents that company or organization. (屬某公司或組織的) 人","examples":["...the Chicago Tribune's man in Abu Dhabi. …駐阿布扎比的《芝加哥論壇》人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Some people refer to a woman's husband, lover, or boyfriend as her <b>man</b>. 男人 (指丈夫、情人或男友)","examples":["...if they see your man cuddle you in the kitchen or living room. …要是他們看見你的男人在廚房或客廳擁抱你。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In very informal social situations, <b>man</b> is sometimes used as a greeting or form of address to a man. 老兄","examples":["Hey wow, man! Where d'you get those boots? 哇，老兄！你從哪兒弄來的那雙靴子？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>man</b> something such as a place or machine, you operate it or are in charge of it. 操控 (機器等); 控制 (某地)","examples":["French soldiers manned roadblocks in the capital city. 法國士兵控制了首都的路障。","...the person manning the phone at the complaint department. …在投訴部負責接聽電話的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a man is <b>man enough</b> to do something, you mean that he has the necessary courage or ability to do it. 有足夠的勇氣或能力 (做某事)","examples":["I told him that he should be man enough to admit he had done wrong. 我告訴過他應該有足夠的勇氣承認自己做錯了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a man as <b>a man's man</b>, you mean that he has qualities which make him popular with other men rather than with women. 受男人喜愛的男人","examples":["Very much a man's man, he enjoyed drinking and jesting with his cronies. 作為一個很受男人喜愛的男人，他喜歡和朋友喝酒開玩笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a man <b>is</b> his <b>own man</b>, you approve of the fact that he makes his decisions and his plans himself, and does not depend on other people. 自己的主人","examples":["Be your own man. Make up your own mind. 做自己的主人，自己做決定吧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a group of men are, do, or think something <b>to a man</b>, you are emphasizing that every one of them is, does, or thinks that thing. 一致地","examples":["To a man, the survivors blamed the government. 倖存者們一致譴責該政府。"]}]}]},"master":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僱主，主子；主宰者，控制者；大師，能手；碩士；原版，母帶；男教師；（動物的）主人；少爺；（英國）校長，院長；船長；著名畫家；主控機件；國業公會主管，共濟會地方分會會長；最高法院官員；<蘇格蘭>（子爵或男爵的）長子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"精通，掌握；控制，掌控；製作……母版"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熟練的，精通的；最重要的，主要的；原版的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A servant's <b>master</b> is the man that he or she works for. 主人","examples":["My master ordered me not to deliver the message except in private. 主人命令我不能傳送資訊，除非在私下裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>master</b> of a particular activity, you mean that they are extremely skilled at it. 專家","examples":["She was a master of the English language. 她曾是一名英語語言專家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>master</b> of a situation, you have complete control over it. 控制者","examples":["Jackson remained calm and always master of his passions. 傑克遜保持著平靜，始終是自己情感的掌控者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A famous male painter of the past is often called a <b>master</b>. (舊時) 著名男畫家","examples":["...a portrait by the Dutch master, Vincent Van Gogh. …一幅荷蘭著名男畫家文森特·凡·高所作的畫像。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>master's degree</b> can be referred to as a <b>master's</b>. 碩士學位","examples":["I've got a master's in economics. 我已經獲得了經濟學碩士學位。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Master</b> is also an adjective. 精通的","examples":["...a master craftsman. …一名手藝高超的工匠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>master</b> copy of something, such as a film or a tape recording, is an original copy that can be used to produce other copies. 母帶的","examples":["Keep one as a master copy for your own reference and circulate the others. 留下一盤作為母帶供你自己參考,然後分發其他的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>master</b> something, you learn how to do it properly or you succeed in understanding it completely. 掌握","examples":["Duff soon mastered the skills of radio production. 達夫很快掌握了廣播節目製作的技能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>master</b> a difficult situation, you succeed in controlling it. 掌控","examples":["When you have mastered one situation you have to go on to the next. 當你掌控了一種局面，你不得不繼續下一個。"]}]}]},"mile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英里；一英里賽跑；很長的距離；很多，遠遠地；英里"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mile</b> is a unit of distance equal to 1760 yards or approximately 1.6 kilometres. 英里","examples":["They drove 600 miles across the desert. 他們驅車600英里橫穿沙漠。","She lives just half a mile away. 她就住在半英里之外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Miles</b> is used, especially in the expression <b>miles away</b>, to refer to a long distance. 很遠的距離","examples":["If you enrol at a gym that's miles away, you won't be visiting it as often as you should. 如果你加入的健身房離這兒很遠的話，你就不會像應該地那樣經常去了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Miles</b> or <b>a mile</b> is used with the meaning \"very much\" in order to emphasize the difference between two things or qualities, or the difference between what you aimed to do and what you actually achieved. (相差) 遠","examples":["You're miles better than most of the performers we see nowadays. 你比我們現今看到的大多數表演者們要好得多。","With a Democratic candidate in place they won by a mile. 隨著一位民主黨候選人的到位，他們輕鬆勝出。"]}]}]},"milk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（牛或羊等的）奶；奶汁，母乳；乳液（用於清潔或保護皮膚）；（椰子等植物的）白色汁液"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擠奶；榨取，勒索；充分利用；迎合（觀眾）；（動物，尤指母牛）產奶，出奶；從……抽取液汁（或毒液等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Milk</b> is the white liquid produced by cows, goats, and some other animals, which people drink and use to make butter, cheese, and yoghurt. 奶","examples":["He stepped out to buy a quart of milk. 他出去買了一夸脫奶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Milk</b> is the white liquid produced by women to feed their babies. 母乳","examples":["Milk from the mother's breast is a perfect food for the human baby. 母乳是嬰兒的最佳食物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Liquid products for cleaning your skin or making it softer are sometimes referred to as <b>milks</b>. 乳劑","examples":["Sales of cleansing milks, creams, and gels have doubled over the past decade. 在過去10年中，潔面乳、面霜以及髮膠的銷售已經增長了一倍。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>milks</b> a cow or goat, they get milk from it, using either their hands or a machine. 給…擠奶","examples":["Farm workers milked cows by hand. 農場工人們手工給奶牛擠奶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>milks</b> something, you mean that they get as much benefit or profit as they can from it, without caring about the effects this has on other people. 榨取","examples":["A few people tried to milk the insurance companies. 有些人試圖榨取保險公司的錢。"]}]}]},"meet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"結識，被引見；（與某人）會面；偶遇，遇見；開會，會晤；迎接；交手，交戰；交匯，相交；接觸，連線；滿足；經歷，遭遇；支付；對付，應付；對視；被感知到；等同於，與……相符； 實現（計劃），履行（諾言）；實現（計劃），履行（諾言）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動會，賽事；<非正式>（尤指為不正當的目的）約會，碰頭；獵狐活動"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古>合適的，恰當的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> someone, you happen to be in the same place as them and start talking to them. You may know the other person, but be surprised to see them, or you may not know them at all. 遇見","examples":["I have just met the man I want to spend the rest of my life with. 我剛剛遇到了我想與之共度餘生的男人。","He's the kindest and sincerest person I've ever met. 他是我見過的最和善、最真誠的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two or more people <b>meet</b>, they go to the same place, which they have earlier arranged to do, so that they can talk or do something together. 會見","examples":["We could meet for a drink after work. 我們可以在下班後見面喝一杯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a moving object <b>meets</b> another object, it hits or touches it. 擊中; 碰到","examples":["He held the lighter so it met the tip of his cigarette. 他舉起了打火機，這樣它就碰到了香菸頭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your eyes <b>meet</b> someone else's, you both look at each other at the same time. (目光) 接觸","examples":["Nina's eyes met her sisters' across the table. 尼娜的目光碰上了桌對面她的姐妹們的目光。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If two areas <b>meet</b>, especially two areas of land or sea, they are next to one another. (尤指兩片地域或海域) 相接","examples":["It is one of the rare places in the world where the desert meets the sea. 那是世界上沙漠和海洋相接的少有的地方之一。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The place where two lines <b>meet</b> is the place where they join together. 相交","examples":["Parallel lines will never meet no matter how far extended. 相平行的線不管延伸多長，永遠都不會相交。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Meet up</b> means the same as . 同(meet)","examples":["Last night, when he was parking my car, he met up with a buddy he had at Stanford. 昨晚他為我泊車時，遇見了他在斯坦福時的一位朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Meet up</b> means the same as . 同(meet)","examples":["We tend to meet up for lunch once a week. 我們往往會每週共進一次午餐。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> someone, you are introduced to them and begin talking to them and getting to know them. 被引見給…","examples":["Hey, Terry, come and meet my Dad. 嗨，特里，過來見見我爸爸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>meet</b> in expressions such as \"<b>Pleased to meet you</b>\" and \"<b>Nice to have met you</b>\" when you want to politely say hello or goodbye to someone you have just met for the first time. 認識","examples":["\"Jennifer,\" Miss Mallory said, \"this is Leigh Taylor.\"—\"Pleased to meet you,\" Jennifer said. “珍妮弗，”馬洛裡小姐說，“這位是利·泰勒。” —“很高興認識你，” 珍妮弗說道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> someone at or off their train, plane, or bus, you go to the station, airport, or bus stop in order to be there when they arrive. 迎接","examples":["Mama met me at the station. 媽媽在車站接了我。","Lili and my father met me off the boat. 莉莉和我爸爸接我下了船。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as a suggestion, proposal, or new book <b>meets with</b> or <b>is met with</b> a particular reaction, it gets that reaction from people. 遇到","examples":["The idea met with a cool response from various quarters. 這個想法遭到了各方人士的冷遇。","We hope today's offer will meet with your approval too. 我們希望今天的提議也將會得到您的批准。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>meets</b> a need, requirement, or condition, it is good enough to do what is required. 滿足","examples":["He suggested that the current arrangements for the care of severely mentally ill people are inadequate to meet their needs. 他認為目前對患有嚴重精神病的人的護理安排不足以滿足他們的需要。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> something such as a problem or challenge, you deal with it satisfactorily or do what is required. 成功應付","examples":["Manufacturing failed to meet the crisis of the 1970s. 製造業沒能成功地應對20世紀70年代危機的考驗。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> the cost of something, you provide the money that is needed for it. 支付","examples":["The government said it will help meet some of the cost of the damage. 政府說它會幫助支付一些損害造成的費用。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> a situation, attitude, or problem, you experience it or become aware of it. 遇到 (情況、態度、問題等)","examples":["I honestly don't know how I will react the next time I meet a potentially dangerous situation. 老實說，下次再遇到有潛在危險的情況時，我不知道自己會如何反應。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a group of people such as a committee <b>meet</b>, they gather together for a particular purpose. 會晤","examples":["Officials from the two countries will meet again soon to resume negotiations. 兩國的官員們不久將再次會晤以重新開始談判。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>meet with</b> someone, you have a meeting with them. (與…) 會晤","examples":["Most of the lawmakers who met with the president yesterday said they backed the mission. 大多數昨天與總統會面的立法委員們說他們支援這項使命。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>meets with</b> success or failure when they are successful or unsuccessful. 獲得 (成功); 遇到 (失敗)","examples":["Attempts to find civilian volunteers have met with embarrassing failure. 尋找平民志願者的種種嘗試均遭遇到了令人尷尬的失敗。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a meeting, esp a sports meeting 會議(尤指體育會議)","examples":[]}]}]},"matter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事情，問題；事態，情況；困境，麻煩（the matter）；物質；材料，物品，東西；書面材料，印刷品；（身體感染部位排出的）膿，黃水；命題內容；（表示數量或時間之少）大約，左右；（法庭審問或證明的）事項，案件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"要緊，有關係；（傷口）化膿，流膿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>matter</b> is a task, situation, or event which you have to deal with or think about, especially one that involves problems. 事情","examples":["It was clear that she wanted to discuss some private matter. 很明顯她想討論一些私事。","Business matters drew him to Louisville. 生意上的事情吸引他去路易斯維爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>matters</b> to refer to the situation you are talking about, especially when something is affecting the situation in some way. 事態","examples":["We have no objection to this change, but doubt that it will significantly improve matters. 我們不反對這種變化，但懷疑這是否將明顯地改善事態。","If it would facilitate matters, I would be happy to come to New York. 如果這有利於事態，我將樂意來紐約。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a situation is <b>a</b> <b>matter</b> <b>of</b> a particular thing, you mean that that is the most important thing to be done or considered when you are involved in the situation or explaining it. 問題","examples":["History is always a matter of interpretation. 歷史總是一個詮釋的問題。","Observance of the law is a matter of principle for us. 遵守法律對於我們是一個原則問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Printed <b>matter</b> consists of books, newspapers, and other texts that are printed. Reading <b>matter</b> consists of things that are suitable for reading, such as books and newspapers. (印刷或閱讀的) 物品","examples":["...the government's plans to place a tax on printed matter. …政府對印刷品徵稅的計劃。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Matter</b> is the physical part of the universe consisting of solids, liquids, and gases. 物質","examples":["A proton is an elementary particle of matter that possesses a positive charge. 質子是帶正電荷的物質的基本粒子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>matter</b> to refer to a particular type of substance. 物料","examples":["...waste matter from industries. …來自工業的廢料。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>matter</b> in expressions such as \"<b>What's the matter?</b>\" or \"<b>Is anything the matter?</b>\" when you think that someone has a problem and you want to know what it is. 麻煩事","examples":["Carole, what's the matter? You don't seem happy. 卡蘿爾，你怎麼啦？你好像不高興。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>matter</b> in expressions such as \"<b>a matter of weeks</b>\" when you are emphasizing how small an amount is or how short a period of time is. 僅僅","examples":["Within a matter of days she was back at work. 僅僅幾天之後，她又回來工作了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something does not <b>matter</b>, you mean that it is not important to you because it does not have an effect on you or on a particular situation. 要緊","examples":["A lot of the food goes on the floor but that doesn't matter. 很多食物掉在地板上，但是那不要緊。","As long as staff members are well-groomed, it does not matter how long their hair is. 只要工作人員打扮整齊，他們的頭髮多長不要緊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>another matter</b> or <b>a different matter</b>, you mean that it is very different from the situation that you have just discussed. 另一碼事","examples":["Being responsible for one's own health is one thing, but being responsible for another person's health is quite a different matter. 對自己的健康負責是一碼事，但對別人的健康負責完全是另一碼事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are going to do something <b>as a matter of</b> urgency or priority, you are going to do it as soon as possible, because it is important. 作為…的事情","examples":["Your doctors can help a great deal and you need to talk about it with them as a matter of urgency. 你的醫生能夠幫你很大的忙，你應該把此事當作緊急情況和他們談談。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>no easy matter</b>, it is difficult to do it. 並非易事","examples":["Choosing the colour for the living-room walls was no easy matter. 為起居室的牆壁選擇顏色並非易事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone says <b>that's the end of the matter</b> or <b>that's an end to the matter</b>, they mean that a decision that has been taken must not be changed or discussed any more. 此事已定","examples":["\"He's moving in here,\" Maria said. \"So that's the end of the matter.\" “他就要搬來住了，”瑪麗亞說。“所以此事已定。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>the fact of the matter is</b> or <b>the truth of the matter is</b> to introduce a fact which supports what you are saying or which is not widely known, for example because it is a secret. 事實","examples":["The fact of the matter is that most people consume far more protein than they actually need. 事實是大多數人攝入的蛋白質比他們真正需要的要多。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something <b>makes matters worse</b>, you mean that it makes a difficult situation even more difficult. 使情況變得更糟","examples":["Don't let yourself despair; this will only make matters worse. 別讓你自己絕望；這樣將只會使情況變得更糟。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>no matter</b> in expressions such as \"<b>no matter how</b>\" and \"<b>no matter what</b>\" to say that something is true or happens in all circumstances. 不管…","examples":["No matter what your age, you can lose weight by following this programme. 不管你多大年齡，你都可以透過這個方案減輕體重。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>it doesn't matter</b>\" to tell someone who is apologizing to you that you are not angry or upset, and that they should not worry. 沒關係","examples":["\"Did I wake you?\"—\"Yes, but it doesn't matter.\" “我把您吵醒了嗎？” — “是的，不過沒關係。”"]}]}]},"mister":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"先生；平民"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"稱……先生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Men are sometimes addressed as <b>mister</b>, especially by children and especially when the person talking to them does not know their name. 先生 (對男子的稱呼，尤為兒童使用或稱呼不知姓名的男子)","examples":["Look, Mister, we know our job, so don't try to tell us what to do. 哎，先生，我們瞭解自己的工作，所以你不必告訴我們該幹什麼。"]}]}]},"mom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"媽媽，母親（非正式，主要用於北美英語；作稱呼語時常大寫為 Mom）；soccer mom：足球媽媽（北美文化用語，指非常重視子女休閒活動、常親自開車接送孩子參加體育活動的母親）；（Mom）人名（柬埔寨音譯“蒙”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>mom</b> is your mother. 媽媽","examples":["We waited for Mom and Dad to get home. 我們等著爸爸媽媽回家。"]}]}]},"mommy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"媽咪（兒童或非正式用語，指媽媽）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people, especially young children, call their mother <b>mommy</b>. 媽咪 (尤為兒童使用)","examples":["Be very good and very quiet and help your mommy. 你要乖乖的，安靜些，要幫媽咪。"]}]}]},"minute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分，分鐘；片刻，一會兒，瞬間；時刻；一分鐘的路程；分（角度單位，即六十分之一度）；會議記錄；摘要，備忘錄"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極小的，微小的；詳細的，細緻入微的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將（某事）寫進會議記錄；傳送備忘錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>minute</b> is one of the sixty parts that an hour is divided into. People often say \"<b>a minute</b>\" or \"<b>minutes</b>\" when they mean a short length of time. 分鐘; 片刻","examples":["The pizza will then take about twenty minutes to cook. 接下來，比薩餅大約要用20分鐘烤好。","Bye Mom, see you in a minute. 再見，媽媽，一會兒見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>minutes</b> of a meeting are the written records of the things that are discussed or decided at it. 會議記錄","examples":["He'd been reading the minutes of the last meeting. 他一直在看上次會議的記錄。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>minutes</b> something that is discussed or decided at a meeting, they make a written record of it. 做會議記錄","examples":["You don't need to minute that. 你不必記錄那些。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People often use expressions such as <b>wait a minute</b> or <b>just a minute</b> when they want to stop you doing or saying something. 等一下","examples":["Wait a minute, folks, something is wrong here. 等一下，夥計們，這地方不對勁。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will or may happen <b>at any minute</b> or <b>any minute now</b>, you are emphasizing that it is likely to happen very soon. 隨時","examples":["It looked as though it might rain at any minute. 看起來隨時都有可能下雨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>last-minute</b> action is one that is done at the latest time possible. 最後一刻","examples":["He will probably wait until the last minute. 他可能會等到最後一刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>the minute</b> something else happens, you are emphasizing that it happens immediately after the other thing. 一…就…","examples":["The minute you do this, you'll lose control. 你一干這個，就會失去控制。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>minute</b>, you mean that it is very small. 非常小的","examples":["Only a minute amount is needed. 只需很少的一點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"precise or detailed 精確的; 詳細的","examples":[]}]}]},"monday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期一，週一"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在星期一，在週一"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Monday</b> is the day after Sunday and before Tuesday. 星期一","examples":["I went back to work on Monday. 我星期一回去上班了。","The first meeting of the group took place last Monday. 該集團的第一次會議於上週一召開。"]}]}]},"mistake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯誤，過失；（用詞或數字上的）錯誤，口誤，筆誤；（令人後悔的）錯誤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"誤解，誤會；錯誤判斷；把……誤認為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>mistake</b>, you do something which you did not intend to do, or which produces a result that you do not want. 錯誤","examples":["They made the big mistake of thinking they could seize its border with a relatively small force. 他們犯了個大錯，認為他們可以用相對少的軍隊佔領邊界。","There must be some mistake. 一定是出了什麼錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mistake</b> is something or part of something that is incorrect or not right. 錯事","examples":["Her mother sighed and rubbed out another mistake in the crossword puzzle. 她母親嘆了口氣，擦掉了拼字遊戲中的另一個填錯的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mistake</b> one person or thing <b>for</b> another, you wrongly think that they are the other person or thing. 誤認為","examples":["When hay fever first occurs it is often mistaken for a summer cold. 花粉病剛發作時，常會被誤認為是熱傷風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mistake</b> something, you fail to recognize or understand it. 誤解","examples":["The administration completely mistook the feeling of the country. 政府完全誤解了國民的感情。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>there is no mistaking</b> something when you are emphasizing that you cannot fail to recognize or understand it. 不會弄錯","examples":["There's no mistaking the eastern flavour of the food. 該食物的東方口味肯定不會錯的。"]}]}]},"miss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女士，小姐，年輕未婚女子"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"錯過，想念，缺（勤）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> something, you fail to hit it, for example when you have thrown something at it or you have shot a bullet at it. 未擊中","examples":["She hurled the ashtray across the room, narrowly missing my head. 她從屋子那頭兒把菸灰缸扔過來，差一點就打中我的腦袋。","When I'd missed a few times, he suggested I rest the rifle on a rock to steady it. 由於我幾次都沒打中，他就建議我把步槍放到石頭上來保持穩定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In sports, if you <b>miss</b> a shot, you fail to get the ball in the goal, net, or hole. (體育運動中) 未投中 (球)","examples":["He scored four of the baskets but missed a free throw. 他4次投籃得分，可是一次罰籃卻沒中。","He dived for the ball and missed. 他去撲球，卻沒撲到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> something, you fail to notice it. 未注意到","examples":["From this vantage point he watched, his searching eye never missing a detail. 從這個有利的位置進行觀察，他那銳利的目光從未漏掉一個細節。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> the meaning or importance of something, you fail to understand or appreciate it. 沒有領會","examples":["One ABC correspondent had totally missed the point of the question. 美國廣播公司的一名記者完全沒有領會這個問題的關鍵。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> a chance or opportunity, you fail to take advantage of it. 錯過 (機會)","examples":["It was too good an opportunity to miss. 這個機會太好了，不容錯過。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> someone who is no longer with you or who has died, you feel sad and wish that they were still with you. 想念","examples":["Your mama and I are going to miss you at Christmas. 我和你媽媽在聖誕節會想你的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> something, you feel sad because you no longer have it or are no longer doing or experiencing it. 留戀","examples":["I could happily move back into an apartment if it wasn't for the fact that I'd miss my garden. 我要不是留戀我的花園，會很高興地搬回到一套公寓裡。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> something such as a plane or train, you arrive too late to catch it. 沒有趕上 (飛機或火車等)","examples":["He missed the last bus home and had to stay with a friend. 他沒趕上回家的末班車，只好住在一個朋友那裡。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>miss</b> something such as a meeting or an activity, you do not go to it or take part in it. 未參加 (會議或活動)","examples":["It's a pity Martha and I had to miss our class last week. 很遺憾，我和瑪莎上週不得不缺課。","You won't be missing much on TV tonight apart from the usual repeats. 除了通常的重播節目外，今晚的電視節目你不會錯過什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Miss</b> is also a noun. 未擊中","examples":["After more misses, they finally put two arrows into the lion's chest. 又射偏了幾次後，他們終於將兩隻箭射進了獅子的胸膛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Miss</b> is also a noun. (體育運動中) 未投中 (球)","examples":["Snow made his first basket of the game after eight misses. 斯諾在8次投球不中後，投進了他本場比賽的第一個球。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an unmarried woman or girl, esp a schoolgirl 女孩子; 女學生","examples":[]}]}]},"moment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"片刻，瞬間；某一時刻；現在，目前；時機，機會；（事物發展的）關頭，轉折點；重大，重要；力矩；矩，動差"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a very short period of time, for example a few seconds, as a <b>moment</b> or <b>moments</b>. 瞬間","examples":["In a moment he was gone. 不一會兒他就不見了。","In moments, I was asleep once more. 很快，我又睡著了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>moment</b> is the point in time at which something happens. 時刻","examples":["At this moment a car stopped at the house. 就在此時，一輛汽車停在那座房子前。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will or may happen <b>at any moment</b> or <b>any moment now</b>, you are emphasizing that it is likely to happen very soon. 隨時","examples":["He'll be here to see you any moment now. 他隨時會來這裡看你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>at the moment</b>, <b>at this moment</b>, and <b>at the present moment</b> to indicate that a particular situation exists at the time when you are speaking. 此刻","examples":["At the moment, no one is talking to me. 此刻沒人和我說話。","He's touring South America at this moment in time. 他此刻正在周遊南美。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>for the moment</b> to indicate that something is true now, even if it will not be true in the future. 至少目前","examples":["For the moment, a potential crisis appears to have been averted. 至少目前，一個潛在的危機好像已被避免了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>has</b> their <b>moments</b>, you are indicating that there are times when they are successful or interesting, but that this does not happen very often. 有成功或吸引人的時刻","examples":["The film has its moments. 這部電影有它走紅的時候。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone does something at <b>the last moment</b>, they do it at the latest time possible. 最後一刻","examples":["They changed their minds at the last moment and refused to go. 他們在最後一刻改變了主意，拒絕前往。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use the expression <b>the next moment</b>, or expressions such as \"<b>one moment</b> he was there, <b>the next</b> he was gone,\" to emphasize that something happens suddenly, especially when it is very different from what was happening before. 緊接著","examples":["He is unpredictable, weeping one moment, laughing the next. 他令人難以捉摸，一會兒哭，一會兒笑。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>of the moment</b> to describe someone or something that is or was especially popular at a particular time, especially when you want to suggest that their popularity is unlikely to last long or did not last long. 當前紅極一時的 (尤指這種受歡迎的情況不會持續很久)","examples":["He's the man of the moment, isn't he? 他是當前的紅人，對吧？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>the moment</b> something else happens, you are emphasizing that it happens immediately after the other thing. 一…就","examples":["The moment I closed my eyes, I fell asleep. 我一閉上眼睛就睡著了。"]}]}]},"mind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頭腦，大腦；智慧，思維方式；聰明人，富有才智的人；注意力，心思；記憶力；意願，意向"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"苦惱，反對；（請求允許或客氣地請人做事）介意；不在意，不考慮；願意做，樂意做；關心，照看；<英>當心，注意；<美>聽從"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to someone's <b>mind</b> when talking about their thoughts. For example, if you say that something is <b>in your mind</b>, you mean that you are thinking about it, and if you say that something is <b>at the back of your mind</b>, you mean that you are aware of it, although you are not thinking about it very much. 想法","examples":["I'm trying to clear my mind of all this. 我正試圖把這一切都從我腦子裡清理出去。","There was no doubt in his mind that the man was serious. 毫不懷疑在他的腦海裡這個人是認真的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>mind</b> is your ability to think and reason. 才智","examples":["You have a good mind. 你很有才智。","Studying stretched my mind and got me thinking about things. 學習擴充套件了我的才智，使我開始思考事情了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a particular type of <b>mind</b>, you have a particular way of thinking which is part of your character, or a result of your education or professional training. 思維方式","examples":["Andrew, you have a very suspicious mind. 安德魯，你疑心太重了。","The key to his success is his logical mind. 他成功的關鍵在於他的邏輯思維。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to someone as a particular kind of <b>mind</b> as a way of saying that they are smart, intelligent, or imaginative. 有才智的人","examples":["She moved to New York, meeting some of the best minds of her time. 她搬到了紐約，遇到了她那個時代最具才智的一些人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>bear</b> something <b>in mind</b> or to <b>keep</b> something <b>in mind</b>, you are reminding or warning them about something important which they should remember. 記住","examples":["Bear in mind that gas stations are scarce in the more remote areas. 記住，加油站在那些比較偏遠的地區是很稀少的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cast</b> your <b>mind back</b> <b>to</b> a time in the past, you think about what happened then. 回想起","examples":["Cast your mind back to 1978, when Forest won the title. 回想一下1978年，那時福里斯特贏得了這個頭銜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>change</b> your <b>mind</b>, or if someone or something <b>changes</b> your <b>mind</b>, you change a decision you have made or an opinion that you had. 改變主意","examples":["I was going to vote for him, but I changed my mind and voted for Reagan. 我本打算投他的票，但後來改變了主意投了里根的票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>comes to mind</b> or <b>springs to mind</b>, you think of it without making any effort. 馬上想到","examples":["Integrity and honesty are words that spring to mind when talking of the man. 談到這個人時就會馬上想到“正直”和“誠實”這兩個詞。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that an idea or possibility never <b>crossed</b> your <b>mind</b>, you mean that you did not think of it. 想到","examples":["It had never crossed his mind that there might be a problem. 他從來沒想到過會有問題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you see something <b>in</b> your <b>mind's eye</b>, you imagine it and have a clear picture of it in your mind. 在腦海中","examples":["In his mind's eye, he can imagine the effect he's having. 在他腦海中，他可以想像到自己正在產生的影響。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have a good mind to</b> do something or <b>have half a mind to</b> do it, you are threatening or announcing that you have a strong desire to do it, although you probably will not do it. 非常想做","examples":["He raged on about how he had a good mind to resign. 他很惱火他怎麼會那麼想辭職。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you ask someone what they <b>have in mind</b>, you want to know in more detail about an idea or wish they have. 打算做某事","examples":["\"Maybe we could celebrate tonight.\"—\"What did you have in mind?\" “或許我們今晚可以慶祝一下。”—“你有什麼打算？”"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> a particular thing <b>in mind</b>, you do it with that thing as your aim or as the reason or basis for your action. 心中懷有某事","examples":["These families need support. With this in mind a group of 35 specialists met last weekend. 這些家庭需要資助。懷著這個想法，35人的專家組於上週末聚在了一起。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that something such as an illness is <b>all</b> <b>in the mind</b>, you mean that it relates to someone's feelings or attitude, rather than having any physical cause. 憑空想像","examples":["It could be a virus, or it could be all in the mind. 這可能是種病毒，或者可能全是憑空想像。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> your <b>own mind</b>, you are sure about your opinions, and are not easily influenced by other people. 有主見","examples":["She knows her own mind and won't let anyone talk her into something she doesn't want to do. 她很有主見，不會聽從任何人勸說去做自己不想做的事。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is losing</b> their <b>mind</b>, you mean that they are becoming mad. 失去理智","examples":["Sometimes I feel like I'm losing my mind. 有時我覺得自己好像要失去理智了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>make up</b> your <b>mind</b> or <b>make</b> your <b>mind up</b>, you decide which of a number of possible things you will have or do. 下定決心","examples":["Once he made up his mind to do something, there was no stopping him. 他一旦下定決心做什麼事，沒有什麼可以阻止他。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If a number of people are <b>of one mind</b>, <b>of like mind</b>, or <b>of the same mind</b>, they all agree about something. 意見一致","examples":["Contact with other disabled yachtsmen of like mind would be helpful. 聯絡一下其他具有同樣想法的殘疾帆船賽手是會有幫助的。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you say that something that happens is <b>a load off</b> your <b>mind</b> or <b>a weight off</b> your <b>mind</b>, you mean that it causes you to stop worrying, for example because it solves a problem that you had. 使不再憂慮","examples":["Knowing that she had medical insurance took a great load off her mind. 知道自己有醫療保險，她不再擔心了。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If something is <b>on</b> your <b>mind</b>, you are worried or concerned about it and think about it a lot. 惦記著","examples":["This game has been on my mind all week. 整整一週我一直惦記著這場比賽。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If your <b>mind is on</b> something or you <b>have</b> your <b>mind on</b> something, you are thinking about that thing. 專心於某事","examples":["At school I was always in trouble – my mind was never on my work. 上學時我一直麻煩不斷–總也無法專注於我的功課。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you have <b>an open mind</b>, you avoid forming an opinion or making a decision until you know all the facts. 開放的心態","examples":["It's hard to see it any other way, though I'm trying to keep an open mind. 儘管我試圖保持開放的心態，可是很難換個角度去看這件事。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If something <b>opens</b> your <b>mind</b> <b>to</b> new ideas or experiences, it makes you more willing to accept them or try them. 使願意嘗試; 使願意接受","examples":["She also stimulated his curiosity and opened his mind to other cultures. 她還激發了他的好奇心，使他願意接受其他文化。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>out of their mind</b>, you mean that they are mad or very foolish. 發瘋","examples":["What are you doing? Are you out of your mind? 你在幹什麼？你瘋了嗎？"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>out of their mind</b> <b>with</b> a feeling such as worry or fear, you are emphasizing that they are extremely worried or afraid. 極度 (焦慮、害怕等)","examples":["I was out of my mind with fear. I didn't know what to do. 我害怕極了。我不知道該怎麼辦。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If you say that someone is, for example, <b>bored out of</b> their <b>mind</b>, <b>scared out of</b> their <b>mind</b>, or <b>stoned out of</b> their <b>mind</b>, you are emphasizing that they are extremely bored, scared, or affected by drugs. 感到非常無聊、害怕或受毒品的影響","examples":["That was one of the most depressing experiences of my life. I was bored out of my mind after five minutes. 那是我一生中最沮喪的經歷之一。5分鐘後我就覺得無聊透頂了。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> your <b>mind to</b> something, you start making an effort to do it. 專心做某事","examples":["You could do fine in the world if you put your mind to it. 在這個世界上，只要你認真做事，就能做好。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If you can <b>read</b> someone's <b>mind</b>, you know what they are thinking without them saying anything. 看出某人的心思","examples":["Don't expect others to read your mind. 不要期望別人能看出你的心思。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"To <b>put</b> someone's <b>mind at rest</b> or <b>set</b> their <b>mind at rest</b> means to stop them from worrying about something. 使某人安心","examples":["It may be advisable to have a blood test to put your mind at rest. 驗一下血讓你自己安心也許是明智的。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"If you say that nobody <b>in</b> their <b>right mind</b> would do a particular thing, you are emphasizing that it is an irrational thing to do and you would be surprised if anyone did it. 神智正常 (不會做某事)","examples":["No one in her right mind would make such a major purchase without asking questions. 沒有一個神智正常的女人會不問問題就買這麼一個大件。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> your <b>mind on</b> something or <b>have</b> your <b>mind set on</b> it, you are determined to do it or obtain it. 決心做某事","examples":["When my wife sets her mind on something, she invariably finds a way to achieve it. 當我妻子下定決心做什麼事情,她總會找到辦法做到。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"If something <b>slips</b> your <b>mind</b>, you forget it. 忘記","examples":["I was going to mention it, but it slipped my mind. 我正要說到它，可是想不起來了。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you <b>speak</b> your <b>mind</b>, you say firmly and honestly what you think about a situation, even if this may offend or upset people. 說出心中所想","examples":["Martina Navratilova has never been afraid to speak her mind. 馬丁娜·納夫拉蒂洛娃從來不怕說出自己心中的想法。"]},{"num":"30.","zh":"If something <b>sticks in</b> your <b>mind</b>, it remains firmly in your memory. 被銘記於心","examples":["I've always been fond of poetry and one piece has always stuck in my mind. 我一直喜歡詩歌，有一首詩一直被我銘記於心。"]},{"num":"31.","zh":"If something <b>takes</b> your <b>mind off</b> a problem or unpleasant situation, it helps you to forget about it for a while. 轉移注意力","examples":["\"How about a game of tennis?\" suggested Alan. \"That'll take your mind off things.\" “打一場網球怎麼樣？”艾倫建議道，“那會轉移一下你的注意力。”"]},{"num":"32.","zh":"You say or write <b>to my mind</b> to indicate that the statement you are making is your own opinion. 依我看","examples":["There are scenes in this play which, to my mind, are incredibly violent. 這部戲中的一些場面依我看太過暴力了。"]},{"num":"33.","zh":"If you are <b>of two minds</b>, you are uncertain about what to do, especially when you have to choose between two courses of action. 猶豫不決","examples":["He was of two minds about this plan. 他對於這個計劃猶豫不決。"]},{"num":"34.","zh":"People use the expression <b>if you don't mind</b> when they are rejecting an offer or saying that they do not want to do something, especially when they are annoyed. 如果你不介意 (用於委婉地拒絕別人的提議和建議)","examples":["\"Sit down.\"—\"I prefer standing for a while, if you don't mind.\" “坐吧。”—“如果你不介意，我想站一會兒。”"]},{"num":"35.","zh":"You use <b>mind you</b> to emphasize a piece of information that you are adding, especially when the new information explains what you have said or contrasts with it. Some people use <b>mind</b> in a similar way. 記住; 務必","examples":["They pay full rates. Mind you, they can afford it. 他們是全額支付的。記住，他們能付得起。"]},{"num":"36.","zh":"You use <b>never mind</b> to tell someone that they need not do something or worry about something, because it is not important or because you will do it yourself. 別擔心","examples":["\"Was his name David?\"—\"No I don't think it was, but never mind, go on.\" “他的名字是大衛嗎？”——“不，我想不是，不過沒關係，繼續。”","Dorothy, come on. Never mind your shoes. They'll soon dry off. 多蘿西，快點。別擔心你的鞋。它們很快就會幹的。"]},{"num":"37.","zh":"You use <b>never mind</b> after a statement, often a negative one, to indicate that the statement is even more true of the person, thing, or situation that you are going to mention next. 更不用說","examples":["I'm not going to believe it myself, never mind convince anyone else. 我自己都不會相信它，更不用說說服其他人了。"]},{"num":"38.","zh":"If you say that you <b>wouldn't mind</b> something, you mean that you would quite like it. 很喜歡; 很願意","examples":["I wouldn't mind a coffee. 我很想喝杯咖啡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do not <b>mind</b> something, you are not annoyed or bothered by it. 介意","examples":["I don't mind the noise during the day. 白天我不介意這種噪聲。","I hope you don't mind me stopping in like this, without an appointment. 我希望你別介意我這樣冒昧拜訪，都沒有事先約定。","I lit a cigarette and nobody seemed to mind. 我點了一支菸，好像並沒有人介意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>mind</b> in the expressions \"<b>do you mind?</b>\" and \"<b>would you mind?</b>\" as a polite way of asking permission or asking someone to do something. 介意 (表示禮貌地徵詢許可或提出請求)","examples":["Do you mind if I ask you one more thing? 您介意我再提一個問題嗎？","Would you mind waiting outside for a moment? 您介意在外面等一會兒嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone does not <b>mind</b> what happens or what something is like, they do not have a strong preference for any particular thing. 介意 (用於否定句中表達“…均可”之意)","examples":["I don't mind what we play, really. 我不介意咱們玩什麼，真的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>mind</b> a child or something such as a shop or luggage, you take care of it, usually while the person who owns it or is usually responsible for it is somewhere else. 照看","examples":["Jim Coulters will mind the shop while I'm away. 我不在時，吉姆·庫爾特斯會照看商店。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>mind</b> something, you are warning them to be careful not to hurt themselves or other people, or damage something. 當心","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>mind</b> when you are reminding someone to do something or telling them to be careful not to do something. 注意","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>never mind</b> when you are emphasizing that something is not serious or important, especially when someone is upset about it or is saying they are sorry. 沒什麼","examples":["Her voice trembled. \"Oh, Sylvia, I'm so sorry.\"—\"Never mind.\" 她的聲音顫抖著。“哎呀，西爾維婭，我真抱歉。”—“沒什麼。”"]}]}]},"monkey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"猴子；頑皮兒童，淘氣鬼；受支配的人，受控制的人；<英，非正式>五百英鎊；錘式打樁機；<美，非正式>毒癮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"胡鬧，搗蛋；<舊>模仿，學……的樣子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monkey</b> is an animal with a long tail which lives in hot countries and climbs trees. 猴子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a child as a <b>monkey</b>, you are saying in an affectionate way that he or she is very lively and naughty. 淘氣鬼","examples":["She's such a little monkey. 她是這麼個小淘氣。"]}]}]},"money":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錢，鈔票，貨幣；財產，財富；款項，金額；工資，薪金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Money</b> is the coins or bank notes that you use to buy things, or the sum that you have in a bank account. 錢","examples":["A lot of the money that you pay at the movies goes back to the film distributors. 你付給電影院的錢有很多又回到了電影發行人的手裡。","Players should be allowed to earn money from advertising. 應該允許運動員拍廣告掙錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Monies</b> is used to refer to several separate sums of money that form part of a larger amount that is received or spent. 款項","examples":["We drew up a schedule of payments for the rest of the monies owed. 我們制定了一個剩餘欠款的還款計劃。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has money to burn</b>, you mean that they have more money than they need, or that they spend their money on things that you think are unnecessary. 有花不完的錢; 亂花錢","examples":["He was a high-earning broker with money to burn. 他是一個收入高得花不完的經紀人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in the money</b>, you have a lot of money to spend. 非常有錢的","examples":["If you are one of the lucky callers chosen to play, you could be in the money. 如果你是一個幸運打進電話的人，且被選中參賽，你就可能要發財了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make money</b>, you obtain money by earning it or by making a profit. 賺錢","examples":["...the only part of the firm that consistently made money. …公司裡惟一一個一直賺錢的部門。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you want someone to <b>put</b> their <b>money where their mouth is</b>, you want them to spend money to improve a bad situation, instead of just talking about improving it. 說話兌現","examples":["The government might be obliged to put its money where its mouth is to prove its commitment. 政府可能要被迫兌現它的承諾來證明其信用。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that <b>money talks</b>, you mean that if someone has a lot of money, they also have a lot of power. 金錢萬能","examples":["The formula in Hollywood is simple – money talks. 好萊塢的規則很簡單–金錢萬能。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>throwing money at</b> a problem, you are critical of them for trying to improve it by spending money on it, instead of doing more thoughtful and practical things to improve it. (不採用合理有效的辦法解決問題，而是) 對…大肆花錢","examples":["The governor's answer to the problem has been to throw money at it. 州長對這個問題的解決就是在濫花冤枉錢。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> your <b>money's worth</b>, you get something which is worth the money that it costs or the effort you have put in. 錢花得值","examples":["The fans get their money's worth. 星迷們的錢花得值。"]}]}]},"moon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"月亮，月球；月光；衛星；月份；渴望之物；月狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"懶散度日，浪蕩；出神，呆視；（向某人）亮屁股；虛度（時間）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>moon</b> is the object that you can often see in the sky at night. It goes around the earth once every four weeks, and as it does so its appearance changes from a circle to part of a circle. 月亮","examples":["...the first man on the moon. …登月第一人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>moon</b> is an object similar to a small planet that travels around a planet. 衛星","examples":["...Neptune's large moon. …海王星的大衛星。"]}]}]},"month":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"月，月份；一個月的時間；數月，很長時間（months）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>month</b> is one of the twelve periods of time that a year is divided into, for example January or February. 月份","examples":["The trial is due to begin next month. 審判定於下個月開始。","...an exhibition which opens this month at the Guggenheim Museum. …本月在古根海姆博物館開幕的展覽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>month</b> is a period of about four weeks. 1個月的時間","examples":["She was here for a month. 她在這裡呆了1個月。","Over the next several months I met most of her family. 在此後的幾個月中，我見到了她大部分家人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the period of time (<b>sidereal month</b>) taken by the moon to make one complete revolution around the earth, measured between two successive conjunctions with a distant star; 27.321 66 days (approximately 27 days, 7 hours, 43 minutes, 11 seconds) 恆星月(約27天7小時43分11秒)","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the period of time (<b>tropical month</b>) taken by the moon to return to the same longitude after one complete revolution around the earth; 27.321 58 days (approximately 27 days, 7 hours, 43 minutes, 4.5 seconds) 分至月(約27天7小時43分4.5秒)","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the period of time (<b>lunar</b> or <b>synodic month</b>) taken by the moon to make one complete revolution around the earth, measured between two successive new moons; 29.530 59 days (approximately 29 days, 12 hours, 44 minutes, 3 seconds) 朔望月(約29天12小時44分3秒) (Also called lunation)","examples":[]}]}]},"morning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"早晨，上午，早上；黎明，破曉，清早；初期，開端（多用於文學或比喻）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>morning</b> is the part of each day between the time that people usually wake up and 12 o'clock noon or lunchtime. 早晨; 上午","examples":["During the morning your guide will take you around the city. 上午導遊將帶你們逛逛這座城市。","On Sunday morning Bill was woken by the telephone. 週日早晨，比爾被電話吵醒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a particular time in <b>the</b> <b>morning</b>, you mean a time between 12 o'clock midnight and 12 o'clock noon. 從子夜12:00到中午12:00之間","examples":["I often stayed up until two or three in the morning. 我經常熬夜到凌晨兩三點鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>in the morning</b>, you mean that it will happen during the morning of the following day. 次日上午","examples":["I'll fly it to St Louis in the morning. 我會在明天上午把它空運到聖路易斯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>morning, noon and night</b>, you mean that it happens all the time. 從早到晚; 一直","examples":["You get fit by playing the game, day in, day out, morning, noon and night. 每日堅持做這項運動，你就會變得健壯。"]}]}]},"mother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"母親；大娘；女修道院院長"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"生下；養育；像母親般關懷或照管"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"母親的；出生地的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>mother</b> is the woman who gave birth to you. You can also call someone your <b>mother</b> if she brings you up as if she was this woman. 母親","examples":["She sat on the edge of her mother's bed. 她坐在她母親的床邊。","She's an English teacher and a mother of two children. 她是一位英語老師，兩個孩子的母親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a female who has given birth to offspring 母(體)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a woman <b>mothers</b> a child, she takes care of it and brings it up, usually because she is its mother. 撫養","examples":["Colleen had dreamed of mothering a large family. 科琳曾經夢想過要養育一大群孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mother</b> someone, you treat them with great care and affection, as if they were a small child. 愛護","examples":["Stop mothering me. 別再像媽媽似的照顧我了。"]}]}]},"look":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"看；尋找；與……外表相似；看似，顯得；注意；面向；檢查，檢視；打算（look to）；預料，期待；瀏覽；研究，考慮；看待（look at/on）；（用於喚起他人注意）瞧；看上去精神好（look oneself）；四處看看（look round/around）；調查（look into）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"看；尋找，搜尋；表情，神色；景象，樣子；容貌（looks）；風格，樣式；察看，考慮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>look</b> in a particular direction, you direct your eyes in that direction, especially so that you can see what is there or see what something is like. 看","examples":["I looked down the hallway to room number nine. 我沿著走廊向9號房間看過去。","If you look, you'll see what was a lake. 如果你看一下，就會看到那個曾經是湖的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>look at</b> a book, newspaper, or magazine, you read it fairly quickly or read part of it. 瀏覽","examples":["You've just got to look at the last bit of Act Three. 你只須瀏覽一下第三幕最後一小段。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>look at</b> someone in a particular way, you look at them with your expression showing what you are feeling or thinking. (帶著某種神情) 看","examples":["She looked at him earnestly. \"You don't mind?\" 她誠摯地看著他說：“你不介意吧？”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>look</b> <b>for</b> something, for example, something that you have lost, you try to find it. 尋找","examples":["I'm looking for a child. I believe your husband can help me find her. 我正在找一個孩子。我相信你丈夫能幫我找到她。","I looked everywhere for ideas. 我到處搜尋意見。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>looking for</b> something such as the solution to a problem or a new method, you want it and are trying to obtain it or think of it. 尋求","examples":["The working group will be looking for practical solutions to the problems faced by doctors. 工作組將會尋求切實可行的方案，以解決醫生們所面臨的問題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>look at</b> a subject, problem, or situation, you think about it or study it, so that you know all about it and can perhaps consider what should be done in relation to it. 考慮; 研究","examples":["Next term we'll be looking at the Second World War period. 下學期我們將研究一下二戰時期。","Anne Holker looks at the pros and cons of making changes to your property. 安妮·霍爾卡會研究對你的財產進行變更的利與弊。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>look at</b> a person, situation, or subject from a particular point of view, you judge them or consider them from that point of view. 看待","examples":["Brian had learned to look at her with new respect. 布賴恩已學會從新的角度看待她。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something such as a building or window <b>looks</b> somewhere, it has a view of a particular place. (建築物、窗戶等) 面朝","examples":["The castle looks over private parkland. 這座城堡面朝私家綠地。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Look</b> is also a noun. 看","examples":["Lucille took a last look in the mirror. 露西爾往鏡子裡看了最後一眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Look</b> is also a noun. 瀏覽","examples":["A quick look at Monday's newspapers shows that there's plenty of interest in foreign news. 快速瀏覽一下星期一的報紙，就會發現許多有趣的國外新聞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Look</b> is also a noun. 看","examples":["He gave her a blank look, as if he had no idea who she was. 他茫然地看了看她，好像不認識她似的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Look</b> is also a noun. 尋找","examples":["Go and have another look. 再去找一找。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Look</b> is also a noun. 考慮; 研究","examples":["A close look at the statistics reveals a troubling picture. 對這些統計資料的仔細研究顯示情況不妙。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something has a particular <b>look</b>, they have a particular appearance or expression. 外表; 神態","examples":["She had the look of someone deserted and betrayed. 她露出被拋棄、被背叛的人的神情。","When he came to decorate the kitchen, Kenneth opted for a friendly rustic look. 當他來裝修廚房時，肯尼思顯出一副友好質樸的樣子。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When you refer to someone's <b>looks</b>, you are referring to how beautiful or ugly they are, especially how beautiful they are. 外貌","examples":["I never chose people just because of their looks. 我從不單憑外貌取人。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>look</b> when you want someone to pay attention to you because you are going to say something important. (用於引起注意) 喂","examples":["Look, I'm sorry. I didn't mean it. 喂，對不起。我不是故意的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>look</b> to draw attention to a particular situation, person, or thing, for example because you find it very surprising, significant, or annoying. (表達驚奇、重要或討厭) 瞧","examples":["Hey, look at the time! We'll talk about it tonight. All right? 嘿，看看時間吧！我們今晚再談論這個，好嗎？","I mean, look at how many people watch television and how few read books. 我想說的是，看看有多少人看電視，又有幾個人讀書。","Look what you've done! 瞧你都幹了些什麼！"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Look out</b> means the same as <b>look</b>. 面朝","examples":["Nine windows looked out over the sculpture gardens. 九扇窗戶面朝雕塑花園。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say or shout \"<b>look out!</b>\" to someone, you are warning them that they are in danger. 小心","examples":["\"Look out!\" somebody shouted, as the truck started to roll toward the sea. 卡車開始滾向大海時，有人大喊：“小心！”"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>look</b> when describing the appearance of a person or thing or the impression that they give. 看上去","examples":["Sheila was looking miserable. 希拉當時顯得痛苦。","They look like stars to the naked eye. 用肉眼看上去它們像星星。","He looked as if he was going to smile. 他看上去好像要微笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>look</b> when indicating what you think will happen in the future or how a situation seems to you. 看起來","examples":["He had lots of time to think about the future, and it didn't look good. 他有很多時間考慮未來，而未來看上去並不樂觀。","So far it looks like Warner Brothers' gamble is paying off. 就目前情況來看，華納兄弟公司的冒險一博似乎要贏了。","The Europeans had hoped to win, and, indeed, had looked like they would win. 歐洲人原本希望能贏，而且當時看起來他們的確會贏。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>by the look of him</b> and <b>by the looks of it</b> when you want to indicate that you are giving an opinion based on the appearance of someone or something. 由表象 (來看)","examples":["He was not a well man by the look of him. 他表面看來不是個健康的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>don't like the look of</b> something or someone, you feel that they may be dangerous or cause problems. 看出…危險或麻煩","examples":["I don't like the look of those clouds. 我看這些烏雲不對頭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you ask <b>what</b> someone or something <b>looks like</b>, you are asking for a description of them. (某人、某物的) 樣子是","examples":[]}]}]},"mountain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"山，高山；許多，大量（a mountain/mountains of）；（食物的）過剩，積壓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mountain</b> is a very high area of land with steep sides. 山","examples":["Mt. McKinley, in Alaska, is the highest mountain in North America. 位於阿拉斯加的麥金利山是北美最高的山。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a <b>mountain</b> <b>of</b> something, or <b>mountains</b> <b>of</b> something, you are emphasizing that there is a large amount of it. 大堆","examples":["They are faced with a mountain of bureaucracy. 他們面臨著一大堆的官僚制度。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>a mountain to climb</b>, you mean that it will be difficult for them to achieve what they want to achieve. 困難","examples":["\"We had a mountain to climb after the second goal went in,\" said Crosby. 克羅斯比說:“第2個球進了後，我們面臨著很大的困難。”"]}]}]},"movie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>電影；<美>電影院（the movies）；<美>電影業（the movies）；<美>電影（總稱）（the movies）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>movie</b> is a series of moving pictures that have been recorded so that they can be shown in a theatre or on television. A movie tells a story, or shows a real situation. 電影","examples":["In the first movie Tony Curtis ever made he played a grocery clerk. 在託尼·柯蒂斯製作的第一部影片中，他出演一名雜貨店店員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can talk about <b>the movies</b> when you are talking about seeing a movie in a movie theatre. 看電影","examples":[]}]}]},"mouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"老鼠；滑鼠；安靜害羞的人；淺棕灰色，鼠皮色；<非正式>（尤指眼部或其附近的）青腫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（貓，貓頭鷹）捕鼠；<非正式>用滑鼠在計算機螢幕上移動游標"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mouse</b> is a small, furry animal with a long tail. 鼠","examples":["...a mouse running in a wheel in its cage. …籠子裡一隻踩著轉輪跑的老鼠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mouse</b> is a device that is connected to a computer. By moving it over a flat surface and pressing its buttons, you can move the cursor around the screen and do things without using the keyboard. 滑鼠","examples":["Her message had been written; all she had to do was click the mouse. 她的資訊已經寫好；她要做的只是點選滑鼠。"]}]}]},"mummy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>媽媽，媽咪；木乃伊，乾屍；乾癟的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mummy</b> is a dead body which was preserved long ago by being rubbed with special oils and wrapped in cloth. 木乃伊","examples":["...an Egyptian mummy. …一具埃及木乃伊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some people, especially young children, call their mother <b>mummy</b>. (尤指兒語)媽媽; 媽咪","examples":["Be very good and very quiet and help your mummy. 你要乖乖的，安安靜靜的，要幫媽媽幹活。"]}]}]},"mud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泥，淤泥，泥漿；（多指與腐化有關的）侮蔑，誹謗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mud</b> is a sticky mixture of earth and water. 泥","examples":["His uniform was crumpled, untidy, splashed with mud. 他的制服皺皺巴巴，邋里邋遢，還濺上了泥點。"]}]}]},"movement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移動，轉移；（具有共同思想或目標的）運動；軍隊有計劃的移動；行蹤；樂章；改進，發展；量的變化；（活動）機件；排便；（飛機）抵達，起飛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>movement</b> is a group of people who share the same beliefs, ideas, or aims. 運動 (指具有共同信仰、思想或目標的團體)","examples":["It's part of a broader nationalist movement that's gaining strength throughout the country. 這是一場正在全國範圍內日益壯大的更為廣泛的民族主義運動的一部分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Movement</b> involves changing position or going from one place to another. 移動","examples":["They actually monitor the movement of the fish going up river. 他們實際上在觀測魚向上遊的遷移活動。","There was movement behind the window in the back door. 後門窗戶的後面有動靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>movement</b> is a planned change in position that an army makes during a battle or military exercise. (軍隊作戰或演習時的) 調遣","examples":["There are reports of fresh troop movements across the border. 有報道稱新近有部隊越過邊境。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Movement</b> is a gradual development or change of an attitude, opinion, or policy. (態度、觀點、政策等的) 逐漸變化","examples":["...the movement toward democracy in Latin America. …拉丁美洲民主的漸進。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>movements</b> are everything that you do or plan to do during a period of time. (某人在某段時間內的) 行蹤","examples":["I want a full account of your movements the night Mr. Gower was killed. 我想要了解高爾先生被殺當晚你的所有行蹤。"]}]}]},"mug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大杯，馬克杯；一大杯的容量；<非正式>（人的）臉；<英，非正式>傻瓜，笨蛋；<美，非正式>惡棍，暴徒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（公開）行兇搶劫，打劫；<美，非正式>（尤指在舞臺上或攝影機前）扮鬼臉，扮怪相"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mug</b> is a large, deep cup with straight sides and a handle, used for hot drinks. 圓筒形有柄大杯","examples":["He spooned instant coffee into two of the mugs. 他用勺子把速溶咖啡舀進其中兩個大杯裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>mug</b> to refer to the mug and its contents, or to the contents only. 一大杯; 一大杯...","examples":["He had been drinking mugs of coffee to keep himself awake. 他一直在喝大杯大杯的咖啡讓自己保持清醒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>mug</b> is their face. 臉","examples":["He managed to get his ugly mug on TV. 他設法讓他那張醜臉上了電視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"行兇搶劫","examples":["Bank robberies, burglaries, and muggings are reported almost daily in the press. 銀行搶劫、入室盜竊以及行兇搶劫幾乎在每天的新聞中都有報道。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mugs</b> you, they attack you in order to steal your money. 襲擊並搶劫","examples":["I was walking out to my car when this guy tried to mug me. 這傢伙企圖搶劫我的時候，我正向我的汽車走去。"]}]}]},"mouth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘴，口腔；需要供養的人，食客；入口，開口；入海口，河口；講話方式，言談；<非正式>饒舌，出言不遜；（受嚼子控制的）馬口；（葡萄酒的不同於氣味的）口感"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不出聲地說，用口型默示；言不由衷地說，（自己並不明白卻）信口開河；（清晰明確地）說，發……的音；吃，用嘴觸碰；訓練（馬）使之習慣於服從嚼子"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"有……嘴的，……口的(-mouthed)；言談……的，口齒……的(-mouthed)"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>mouth</b> is the area of your face where your lips are, or the space behind your lips where your teeth and tongue are. 嘴","examples":["She clamped her hand against her mouth. 她用手緊緊捂住嘴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that someone has a particular kind of <b>mouth</b> to indicate that they speak in a particular kind of way or that they say particular kinds of things. 說話 (方式或內容)","examples":["I've always had a loud mouth, I refuse to be silenced. 我總是有話就講，我拒絕保持沉默。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>mouth</b> of a cave, hole, or bottle is its entrance or opening. (洞) 口; (瓶) 口","examples":["By the mouth of the tunnel he bent to retie his shoelace. 到隧道的入口處，他彎腰重新系了繫鞋帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>mouth</b> of a river is the place where it flows into the sea. 河口","examples":["...the town at the mouth of the River Fox. …位於福克斯河河口的那座城鎮。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(用於構成複合形容詞) 嘴…的","examples":["He straightened up and looked at me, open-mouthed. 他直起身子看著我，嘴大張著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(用於構成複合形容詞) 說話…的","examples":["...Sam, their smart-mouthed teenage son. …薩姆，他們十幾歲的伶牙俐齒的兒子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(用於構成複合形容詞) 口…的","examples":["He put the flowers in a wide-mouthed blue vase. 他把花放進一隻藍色的大口花瓶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mouth</b> something, you form words with your lips without making any sound. 用口形不出聲地說","examples":["I mouthed a goodbye and hurried in behind Momma. 我只張嘴不出聲地說了個再見就趕緊跟在媽媽身後進去了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a number of <b>mouths to feed</b>, you have the responsibility of earning enough money to feed and take care of that number of people. 需要撫養的人","examples":["He had to feed his family on the equivalent of seven hundred dollars a month and, with five mouths to feed, he found this very hard. 他每月不得不用相當於700美元的錢來養家，5張嘴等著吃飯，他覺得很困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone does not <b>open</b> their <b>mouth</b>, you are emphasizing that they never say anything at all. 開口說話","examples":["Sometimes I hardly dare open my mouth. 有時我幾乎不敢開口說話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>mouth shut</b> about something, you do not talk about it, especially because it is a secret. 守口如瓶","examples":["You wouldn't be here now if she'd kept her mouth shut. 如果她當時守口如瓶，你現在就不會在這裡了。"]}]}]},"music":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"音樂，樂曲；樂譜；悅耳的聲音；音樂（學），音樂創作（或演奏）技能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Music</b> is the pattern of sounds produced by people singing or playing instruments. 音樂","examples":["...classical music. …古典音樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Music</b> is the art of creating or performing music. 音樂創作; 音樂表演","examples":["He went on to study music, specializing in the clarinet. 他繼續學習音樂，專攻單簧管。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Music</b> is the symbols written on paper which represent musical sounds. 樂譜","examples":["He's never been able to read music. 他從來就不識樂譜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something that you hear is <b>music to</b> your <b>ears</b>, it makes you feel very happy. 佳音","examples":["Popular support – it's music to the ears of any politician. 公眾的支援–這對任何政客都是佳音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>face the music</b>, you put yourself in a position where you will be criticized or punished for something you have done. 承擔自己行為的後果","examples":["Sooner or later, I'm going to have to face the music. 遲早我得自食其果。"]}]}]},"nation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國家，民族；國民；（美洲土著居民的）部落，部族"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nation</b> is an individual country considered together with its social and political structures. 國家","examples":["Such policies would require unprecedented cooperation between nations. 這樣的一些政策會要求國與國之間前所未有的合作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>nation</b> is sometimes used to refer to all the people who live in a particular country, or all the people who belong to a particular ethnic group. 全國國民; 民族","examples":["It was a story that touched the nation's heart. 這是一個感動了全民族的故事。","...the former chief of the Cherokee nation. …前任切羅基族酋長。"]}]}]},"newspaper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"報紙，報；報社；（尤指用作他途的）舊報紙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>newspaper</b> is a publication consisting of a number of large sheets of folded paper, on which news, advertisements, and other information is printed. 報紙","examples":["He was carrying a newspaper. 他正拿著一份報紙。","They read their daughter's allegations in the newspaper. 他們從報紙上看到女兒的宣告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>newspaper</b> is an organization that produces a newspaper. 報社","examples":["It is the nation's fastest growing national daily newspaper. 這是該國發展最快的全國性日報社。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Newspaper</b> consists of pieces of old newspapers, especially when they are being used for another purpose such as wrapping things up. (尤指作其他用途的) 舊報紙","examples":["He found two pots, each wrapped in newspaper. 他找到了兩隻罐子，分別用舊報紙包著。"]}]}]},"neck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頸項，脖子；衣領，領口；（物體的）細長部分，頸部；狹長地帶，狹長水域；（動物的）頸肉；（賽馬）以微弱優勢（獲勝），險（勝）；<非正式>在這一帶，在某人的地區；<英>受到懲罰（批評）；（喻）（對責任或過失的）揹負；（剖）頸；（蕨、苔蘚或菌類的）莖部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"摟著脖子親吻，相擁互吻；<英，非正式>一口喝下（某物，尤指酒）；（因拉伸而）變狹，變細"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>neck</b> is the part of your body which joins your head to the rest of your body. 頸","examples":["She threw her arms around his neck and hugged him warmly. 她伸出雙臂摟住他的脖子，熱烈地擁抱他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>neck</b> of an article of clothing such as a shirt, dress, or sweater is the part which surrounds your neck. 領口","examples":["...the low, ruffled neck of her blouse. …她褶邊低胸的襯衫領口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>neck</b> of something such as a bottle or a guitar is the long narrow part at one end of it. (瓶子、吉他等的) 頸狀部位","examples":["Catherine gripped the broken neck of the bottle. 凱瑟琳緊握著破裂的瓶頸。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is breathing down</b> your <b>neck</b>, you mean that they are watching you very closely and checking everything you do. 密切監視","examples":["Most farmers have loan officers breathing down their necks. 大多數農場主受到信貸員的密切監視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a competition, especially an election, if two or more competitors are <b>neck and neck</b>, they are level with each other and have an equal chance of winning. 勢均力敵","examples":["The latest polls indicate that the two main parties are neck and neck. 最新的民意測驗顯示兩個主要政黨勢均力敵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stick</b> your <b>neck out</b>, you bravely say or do something that might be criticized or might turn out to be wrong. 敢說敢幹","examples":["During my political life I've earned myself a reputation as someone who'll stick his neck out, a bit of a rebel. 我在自己的政治生涯中得了一個敢說敢幹、有點叛逆的名聲。"]}]}]},"must":{"summaries":[{"pos":"aux.","zh":"（表示必要或很重要）必須；（用於表示肯定推測）一定，諒必；（提出建議）應該；（用於表示意圖）一定要，堅持要；（用於表示同情）必定；（用於問句中表示生氣）非要 ；（用於感嘆句，表示驚訝或震驚）一定是"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>必不可少的事物；（發酵前或發酵中的）葡萄汁；潮氣，黴菌；（尤指發情期的公象、雄駱駝等的）狂暴狀態（=musth）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> to indicate that you think it is very important or necessary for something to happen. You use <b>must not</b> or <b>mustn't</b> to indicate that you think it is very important or necessary for something not to happen. 必須 (表示重要或必要)","examples":["What you wear should be stylish and clean, and must definitely fit well. 你的穿著應該時尚整潔，而且必須非常合體。","You are going to have to take a certain amount of criticism, but you must cope with it. 你會受到一定程度的批評，但這是你必須面對的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> to indicate that it is necessary for something to happen, usually because of a rule or law. 必要 (表示依據法律或規則)","examples":["Candidates must satisfy the general conditions for admission. 應試者必須滿足錄取的一般條件。","Mr. Allen must pay Mr. Farnham's legal costs. 艾倫先生必須支付法納姆先生的訴訟費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> to indicate that you are fairly sure that something is the case. 肯定 (表示猜測)","examples":["At 29 Russell must be one of the youngest ever international referees. 29歲的拉塞爾想必是迄今為止最年輕的國際裁判之一。","Claire's car wasn't there, so she must have gone to her mother's. 克萊爾的汽車不在那兒，想必她是去她母親家了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>must</b>, or <b>must have</b> with a past participle, to indicate that you believe that something is the case, because of the available evidence. 必定 (表示有據推斷)","examples":["\"You must be Emma,\" said the visitor. “你一定是埃瑪,”來訪者說道。","Miss Holloway had a weak heart. She must have had a heart attack. 霍洛韋小姐心臟衰弱。她一定得過心臟病。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>must have</b> happened in order for something else to happen, you mean that it is necessary for the first thing to have happened before the second thing can happen. 肯定已經發生 (表示前者為後者的前提)","examples":["In order to take that job, you must have left another job. 為了去做那份工作，你肯定已經辭去了另一份工。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> to express your intention to do something. 一定要 (表示意願)","examples":["I must be getting back. 我該回去了。","I must telephone my parents. 我一定要給父母打個電話。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> to make suggestions or invitations very forcefully. 務必; 一定得 (提出建議或邀請)","examples":["You must see a doctor, Frederick. 弗雷德裡克，你一定得看醫生。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> in remarks and comments where you are expressing sympathy. 想必 (表示同情)","examples":["This must be a very difficult job for you. 這對你來說肯定是一項非常艱鉅的任務。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> in conversation in expressions such as \"<b>I must say</b>\" and \"<b>I must admit</b>\" in order to emphasize a point that you are making. 必須 (用於表示強調)","examples":["This came as a surprise, I must say. 我得說這發生得很突然。","I must admit I like looking feminine. 我得承認我喜歡看上去嬌柔些。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> in expressions such as \"<b>it must be noted</b>\" and \"<b>it must be remembered</b>\" in order to draw the reader's or listener's attention to what you are about to say. 一定 (用於引起注意)","examples":["It must be noted, however, that not all British and American officers carried out orders. 然而，一定要注意，並非所有英美軍官都執行命令。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> in questions to express your anger or irritation about something that someone has done, usually because you do not understand their behaviour. 偏要 (用於問句中，表示因不理解某人的行為而憤怒)","examples":["Why must she interrupt? 她為什麼偏要打斷呢？"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>must</b> in exclamations to express surprise or shock. 一定 (用於感嘆句，表示驚奇或震驚)","examples":["\"Go! Please go.\"—\"You must be joking!\" “走吧！請走吧。”—“你一定是在開玩笑！”","I really must be quite mad! 我真的一定是氣壞了！"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to something as <b>a</b> <b>must</b>, you mean that it is absolutely necessary. 必不可少的事物; 必須要做的事","examples":["Taking out travel insurance may seem an unnecessary expense, but it is a must. 旅遊保險費用看起來似乎是沒必要的，但卻是必不可少的開支。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the newly pressed juice of grapes or other fruit ready for fermentation (待發酵)葡萄汁; 果汁","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"mustiness or mould 黴臭; 黴菌","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>if you must</b>\" when you know that you cannot stop someone doing something that you think is wrong or stupid. 如果你一定要 (表示雖不贊同但無法阻止)","examples":["If you must be in the sunlight, use the strongest sunscreen you can get. 如果你一定要呆在陽光下的話，就用你能買到的最有效的防曬霜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>if you must know</b>\" when you tell someone something that you did not want them to know and you want to suggest that you think they were wrong to ask you about it. 如果你一定要知道的話","examples":["It scared the hell out of her, if you must know. And me, too. 這把她的魂都嚇飛了，如果你一定要知道的話。而且我也被嚇壞了。"]}]}]},"nature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大自然，自然界；性格，秉性；本質，特點；型別，種類；<古>具有某種特性的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nature</b> is all the animals, plants, and other things in the world that are not made by people, and all the events and processes that are not caused by people. 大自然","examples":["The most amazing thing about nature is its infinite variety. 大自然最讓人驚歎的地方在於它的無限多樣性。","...grasses that grow wild in nature. …自然界生長的野草"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>nature</b> of something is its basic quality or character. 本質","examples":["Mr. Sharp would not comment on the nature of the issues being investigated. 夏普先生不願就被調查問題的本質發表評論。","The rise of a major power is both economic and military in nature. 一個大國的崛起本質上既是經濟上的，也是軍事上的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>nature</b> is their character, which they show by the way they behave. 性格","examples":["Jeya feels that her ambitious nature made her unsuitable for an arranged marriage. 耶雅覺得她的雄心勃勃的個性使她不適合包辦婚姻。","She trusted people. That was her nature. 她信任人，那是她的天性。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something has a particular characteristic <b>by</b> its <b>nature</b> or <b>by</b> its <b>very nature</b>, you mean that things of that type always have that characteristic. 本質上","examples":["Peacekeeping, by its nature, makes pre-planning difficult. 維和行動本質上很難預先計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in the nature of things</b>, you mean that you would expect it to happen in the circumstances mentioned. 事出必然","examples":["Of course, in the nature of things, and with a lot of drinking going on, people failed to notice. 當然了，事出必然，酒酣之間人們沒有注意到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that one thing is <b>in the nature of</b> another, you mean that it is like the other thing. 和…類似的","examples":["There is movement toward, I think, something in the nature of a pluralistic system. 我認為，有向類多元化體系發展的趨勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a way of behaving is <b>second nature</b> <b>to</b> you, you do it almost without thinking because it is easy for you or obvious to you. 第二天性","examples":["Planning ahead had always come as second nature to her. 預先計劃一直是她的第二天性。"]}]}]},"news":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訊息，新情況；新聞（報道）；新聞人物，新聞事件；電視新聞節目（the news）；（用於報紙名）新聞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>News</b> is information about a recently changed situation or a recent event. 訊息","examples":["We waited and waited for news of him. 我們等啊等啊，等他的訊息。","They still haven't had any news about when they'll be able to go home. 他們仍然沒有得到任何關於他們何時才能回家的訊息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>News</b> is information that is published in newspapers and broadcast on radio and television about recent events in the country or world or in a particular area of activity. 新聞","examples":["Foreign News is on page 16. 國外新聞在第16版。","Those are some of the top stories in the news. 那是新聞中的一些頂級報道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The news</b> is a television or radio broadcast which consists of information about recent events in the country or the world. (電視、電臺等的) 新聞廣播","examples":["I heard all about the bombs on the news. 我從新聞廣播裡聽到了關於炸彈的所有訊息。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>news</b>, you mean that they are considered to be interesting and important at the moment, and that people want to hear about them on the radio and television and in newspapers. 新聞人物; 新聞事件","examples":["A murder was big news. 謀殺案是大新聞。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>bad news</b>, you mean that it will cause you trouble or problems. If you say that something is <b>good news</b>, you mean that it will be useful or helpful to you. 壞事/好事","examples":["The drop in travel is bad news for the airline industry. 旅遊業滑坡對航空業來說是件壞事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is news to</b> you, you mean that you did not previously know what you have just been told, especially when you are surprised or annoyed about it. 對…來說是新聞","examples":["I'd certainly tell you if I knew anything, but I don't. What you're saying is news to me. 我要是知道點兒什麼，我肯定告訴你，可我不知道。你現在說的對我還是新聞呢。"]}]}]},"nine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"九，九個"},{"pos":"num.","zh":"九；九個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"九的，九個的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Nine）人名；（塞）尼內"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nine</b> is the number 9. 9","examples":["We still sighted nine yachts. 我們還是看到了九艘遊艇。"]}]}]},"nineteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十九"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十九個；十九歲；十九號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nineteen</b> is the number 19. 19","examples":["They have nineteen days to make up their minds. 他們有十九天的時間來做出決定。"]}]}]},"ninety":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"九十"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"九十的；九十歲的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"九十（數字 90）；複數 nineties：九十幾（指 90 至 99 之間的年齡、溫度等範圍）；the nineties：（二十世紀）九十年代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ninety</b> is the number 90. 90","examples":["It was decided she had to stay another ninety days. 經決定，她必須再呆九十天。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>nineties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 90 and 99. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>nineties</b>, you are aged between 90 and 99. If the temperature is <b>in the nineties</b>, the temperature is between 90 and 99 degrees. 九十幾 (指從90到99之間)","examples":["By this time she was in her nineties and needed help more and more frequently. 到這時她已經九十多歲了，越來越頻繁地需要幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The nineties</b> is the decade between 1990 and 1999. (二十世紀) 九十年代","examples":["These trends only got worse as we moved into the nineties. 當我們進入了90年代，這些風氣只不過變得更糟了。"]}]}]},"need":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"需要；（表示應該或不得不做）有必要；<古>需要"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"需要，必須； 特別需要，迫切要求；需要的事物，慾望；（食物、錢或生活來源的）短缺，缺乏"},{"pos":"aux.","zh":"必要（用於勸告或建議）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>need</b> something, or <b>need</b> <b>to</b> do something, you cannot successfully achieve what you want or live properly without it. 需要","examples":["He desperately needed money. 他急需錢。","I need to make a phone call. 我需要打個電話。","I need you to do something for me. 我需要你為我做些事。","I need you here, Wally. 沃利，我這兒需要你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object or place <b>needs</b> something done to it, that action should be done to improve the object or place. If a task <b>needs</b> doing, it should be done to improve a particular situation. 需要","examples":["The building needs quite a few repairs. 這棟樓不少處需要修繕。","...a garden that needs tidying. …一個需要整理的花園。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone does not <b>need</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are telling them not to do it, or advising or suggesting that they should not do it. 必要 (用於勸告或建議)","examples":["Well, for Heaven's sake, you don't need to apologize. 好啦，看在老天爺的份上，你不必道歉了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone that they don't <b>need</b> <b>to</b> do something, or that something <b>need</b> not happen, you are telling them that that thing is not necessary, in order to make them feel better. 一定 (用於勸告或建議)","examples":["He replied, with a reassuring smile, \"Oh, you don't need to worry about them.\" 他面帶鼓勵的微笑答道：“哦，你不必為他們擔心。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use don't <b>need</b> <b>to</b> when you are giving someone permission not to do something. 否定詞後接(need to)，表示允許不做某事","examples":["You don't need to wait for me. 你不用等我。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>didn't need to</b> do something, it wasn't necessary or useful for them to do it, although they did it. 本不需要","examples":["You didn't need to give me any more money you know, but thank you. 你知道你本不需要再給我錢了，不過謝謝了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Need</b> is also a verb. (Need)亦為動詞","examples":["I hardly need to say that I have never lost contact with him. 幾乎不用說，我從未和他失去聯絡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Need</b> is also a noun. 需要","examples":["Charles has never felt the need to compete with anyone. 查爾斯從未感覺到與人競爭的需要。","...the child who never had his need for attention and importance satisfied. …那個受關注和重視的需要從未得到過滿足的孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is a <b>need</b> <b>for</b> something, that thing would improve a situation or something cannot happen without it. 需要; 必要","examples":["Mr. Forrest believes there is a need for other similar schools throughout the country. 福里斯特先生相信全國上下有對其他類似學校的需要。","\"I think we should see a specialist.\"—\"I don't think there's any need for that.\" “我想我們應該看個專家。”—“我認為沒那必要。”"]}]},{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Need</b> is also a modal. 必要 (用於勸告或建議)","examples":["\"I'll put the key in the window.\"—\"You needn't bother,\" he said gruffly. “我將把鑰匙放進窗戶裡去。”—“不必麻煩，”他粗聲粗氣地說。","Look, you needn't shout. 喂，你不必喊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Need</b> is also a modal. 一定 (用於勸告或建議)","examples":["You needn't worry. 你不必擔心。","We have learned that a market crash need not lead to economic disaster. 我們已經認識到一次市場崩潰未必導致經濟災難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Need</b> is also a modal. (Need)也作情態動詞","examples":["You needn't come again, if you don't want to. 如果你不願意，就不用再來了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>needn't</b> <b>have</b> done something, they didn't need to do it. 本不需要","examples":["She could have made the sandwich herself; her mother needn't have bothered to do anything. 她本可以自己做三明治；她母親本來不用費心做任何事。","I was a little nervous when I announced my engagement to Grace, but I needn't have worried. 當宣佈和格雷絲訂婚時我有點兒緊張，其實不用擔心。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>need</b> in expressions such as <b>I need hardly say</b> and <b>I needn't add</b> to emphasize that the person you are talking to already knows what you are going to say. 用於(I need hardly say)和(I needn't add)短語中，強調對方已然知曉將要說的話","examples":["I needn't add that if you fail to do as I ask, you will suffer the consequences. 我不必再說了，如果你不能按我說的做，你要承擔一切後果。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People <b>in need</b> do not have enough of essential things such as money, food, or good health. 需要幫助的","examples":["The portable clinic will take doctors to children in need. 移動診所將為需要幫助的孩子們帶去醫生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in need of</b> something, you need it or ought to have it. 需要","examples":["I was all right but in need of rest. 當時我挺好的，就是需要休息。","He was badly in need of a shave. 當時他特別需要刮個鬍子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you will do something, especially an extreme action, <b>if need be</b>, you mean that you will do if it is necessary. 需要的話","examples":["They will act as my legal advisers if need be. 需要的話，他們會作我的法律顧問。"]}]}]},"night":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夜間，夜晚；晚上，傍晚；<文>黃昏；（特殊活動之）夜；黑夜，夜色；挫敗時期"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"夜晚的；夜晚使用的；夜間進行的；夜晚活動的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"晚安（goodnight 的簡稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>night</b> is the part of each day when the sun has set and it is dark outside, especially the time when people are sleeping. 夜","examples":["The fighting began in the late afternoon and continued all night. 那場戰鬥傍晚開始，持續了一整夜。","Finally night fell. 夜幕終於降臨了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>night</b> is the period of time between the end of the afternoon and the time that you go to bed, especially the time when you relax before going to bed. 晚上 (尤指睡前)","examples":["So whose party was it last night? 那麼昨天晚上是誰的晚會？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular <b>night</b> is a particular evening when a special event takes place, such as a show or a play. (演出等的) 夜場","examples":["The first night crowd packed the building. 首次夜場演出，觀眾全場爆滿。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is a particular time <b>at night</b>, it is during the time when it is dark and is before midnight. 晚上","examples":["It's eleven o'clock at night in Moscow. 現在莫斯科是晚上11點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>at night</b>, it happens regularly during the evening or night. 每晚","examples":["He was going to college at night, in order to become an accountant. 他為了當會計，每晚要去學院聽課。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>day and night</b> or <b>night and day</b>, it happens all the time without stopping. 夜以繼日地","examples":["Dozens of doctors and nurses have been working day and night for weeks. 很多醫生和護士夜以繼日地工作了幾周了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>an early night</b>, you go to bed early. If you have <b>a late night</b>, you go to bed late. 早睡/晚睡","examples":["I've had a hell of a day, and all I want is an early night. 今天真是太糟糕了，我只想早早睡覺。"]}]}]},"name":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名字，名稱；名聲，名譽；<非正式>名人，有名的事物；（侮辱人的）綽號，別稱；（英國）屬勞埃德保險社辛迪加的承保人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"命名，給……取名；說出……的名稱，叫出……的名字；說定，確定；任命，委任；<英>（下議院議長）點名開除（立法委員會成員）的議員身份"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有名的，出名的；姓名的，據以取名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>name</b> of a person, place, or thing is the word or group of words that is used to identify them. 名字","examples":["\"What's his name?\"—\"Peter.\" “他叫什麼名字？”—“彼得。”","I don't even know if Sullivan's his real name. 我甚至不知道沙利文是不是他的真名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the reputation of a person or thing as their <b>name</b>. 名聲","examples":["He had a name for good judgement. 他以判斷力強著稱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to someone as, for example, a famous <b>name</b> or a great <b>name</b> when they are well known. (名) 人","examples":["...some of the most famous names in modelling and show business. …模特界和演藝界的一些大人物。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>name</b> someone or something, you give them a name, usually at the beginning of their life. 給…取名","examples":["My mother insisted on naming me Horace. 我母親執意給我取名叫霍勒斯。","...a man named John T. Benson. …一個叫約翰·T·本森的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>name</b> someone or something <b>after</b> another person or thing, you give them the same name as that person or thing. 以 (某人或某物的名字) 命名","examples":["Why haven't you named any of your sons after yourself? 為什麼你沒用你名字給你兒子中的任何一個命名？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>name</b> someone, you identify them by stating their name. 說出…的名稱","examples":["It's nearly thirty years since a journalist was jailed for refusing to name a source. 一名記者因拒絕說出訊息來源而入獄已近三十年了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>name</b> something such as a price, time, or place, you say what you want it to be. 提出 (價格、時間、地點等)","examples":["Call Marty, tell him to name his price. 給馬蒂打電話，讓他開個價。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>name</b> the person for a particular job, you say who you want to have the job. 提名","examples":["The CEO has named a new chief financial officer. 執行總裁已經提名了一位新的財務總監。","When the chairman of Campbell's retired, McGovern was named as his successor. 坎貝爾公司的董事長退休時，麥戈文被被提名為其繼任者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in</b> someone's <b>name</b>, it officially belongs to them or is reserved for them. 在…的名下","examples":["The house is in my husband's name. 這所房子在我丈夫名下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something <b>in the name of</b> a group of people, they do it as the representative of that group. 代表","examples":["In the United States the majority governs in the name of the people. 在美國，多數派代表民眾執政。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>in the name of</b> an ideal or an abstract thing, you do it in order to preserve or promote that thing. 為了 (理想或抽象的事物)","examples":["...one of those rare occasions in history when a political leader risked his own power in the name of the greater public good. …政治領袖為了更大的公共利益而將自己權力置於風險之中的那些罕有歷史時刻之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you mention someone or something <b>by name</b>, or address someone <b>by name</b>, you use their name. 用名字 (提到或稱呼)","examples":["When he walks down 131st street, he greets most people he sees by name. 當他沿第131大街走著的時候，他跟他看見的大多數人用名字打著招呼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>by name</b> or <b>by the name of</b> when you are saying what someone is called. 名叫…的","examples":["In 1911 he met up with a young Australian by the name of Harry Busteed. 1911年，他與一個叫哈里·巴斯蒂德的年輕澳大利亞人會了面。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>calls</b> you <b>names</b>, they insult you by saying unpleasant things to you or about you. 謾罵","examples":["At my last school they called me names because I was so slow. 在上一所學校，他們罵過我，因為我反應太慢。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>make a name for</b> <b>yourself</b> or <b>make</b> your <b>name</b> <b>as</b> something, you become well known for that thing. 使某人出名","examples":["She was beginning to make a name for herself as a portrait photographer. 她當時作為一名肖像攝影師開始出名。"]}]}]},"noon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正午，中午；全盛期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Noon</b> is twelve o'clock in the middle of the day. 中午","examples":["The long day of meetings started at noon. 漫長的會議日從中午開始了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Noon</b> means happening or appearing in the middle part of the day. 中午的","examples":["The noon sun was fierce. 中午的太陽火辣辣的。"]}]}]},"november":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"十一月；（北約音標字母）代表字母 N 的程式碼詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>November</b> is the eleventh month of the year in the Western calendar. 11月","examples":["He arrived in London in November 1939. 他於1939年11月到達倫敦。"]}]}]},"noise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噪音，嘈雜聲；聲音，響聲；用言語暗示；（電流）雜音，干擾（訊號）；垃圾資訊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"議論，傳開；<文>喧鬧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Noise</b> is a loud or unpleasant sound. 噪音","examples":["There was too much noise in the room and he needed peace. 房間裡有太多噪音了，他需要安靜。","The noise of bombs and guns was incessant. 爆炸聲和槍擊聲接連不斷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>noise</b> is a sound that someone or something makes. 聲音","examples":["Gerald made a small noise in his throat. 傑拉爾德從他的嗓子裡發出輕輕的一聲。","...birdsong and other animal noises. …鳥鳴聲和其他動物的叫聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>makes noises</b> of a particular kind about something, they say things that indicate their attitude to it in a rather indirect or vague way. (間接、含蓄地表達的) 觀點","examples":["The president took care to make encouraging noises about the future. 那位總統小心謹慎地表達了對未來的樂觀。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>makes the right noises</b> or <b>makes all the right noises</b>, you think that they are showing concern or enthusiasm about something because they feel they ought to rather than because they really want to. 故作熱情地附和","examples":["But at the annual party conference he always made the right noises. 但在年會上他總是故作熱情地隨聲附和。"]}]}]},"no":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不，完全不（也常用於比較級前，表示並不、一點也不）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於否定的回答或陳述）不，沒有，不行；（糾正剛說的話）不對；（感到驚訝）不會吧"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"沒有；不是"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"沒有，無；不準，禁止；沒有可能（做某事）；（表示情況的反面）不是，並不，絕非"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"否定的回答；（複數 noes）（投票表決中的）反對，否決；（No）（柬、越）諾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to give a negative response to a question. (用於否定回答) 不; 沒有","examples":["\"Any problems?\"—\"No, I'm O.K.\" “有問題嗎？”—“沒有，我挺好。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to say that something that someone has just said is not true. (用於否定別人的陳述) 不; 沒有","examples":["\"We thought you'd emigrated.\"—\"No, no.\" “我們還以為你已經移民了呢。”—“不，沒有。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to refuse an offer or a request, or to refuse permission. (用於拒絕建議、請求或許可) 不用; 不行","examples":["\"Here, have mine.\"—\"No, this is fine.\" “給，用我的。”—“不用，這個挺好的。”","\"Can you just get the message through to Pete for me?\"—\"No, no I can't.\" “你能幫我把這個信兒帶給皮特嗎？—“不行，我不能。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to acknowledge a negative statement or to show that you accept and understand it. (表示接受或理解對方的否定陳述) 對，不是","examples":["\"We're not on the main campus.\"—\"No.\" “我們不在主校園。”—“是的。”","\"It's not one of my favourite forms of music.\"—\"No.\" “它不是我最喜歡的音樂形式之一。”—“對，不是。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> before correcting what you have just said. (用於糾正剛說過的話) 噢不","examples":["I was twenty-two – no, twenty-one. 我那時22歲。—噢不，21歲。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to indicate that you do not want someone to do something. (表示禁止) 不要","examples":["No. I forbid it. You cannot. 不，我不準。你不可以。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to express shock or disappointment at something you have just been told. (表示對獲知的事情的驚訝或失望) 是嗎; 不會吧","examples":["\"We went with Sarah and the married man that she's currently seeing.\"—\"Oh no.\" “我們與薩拉和她最近約會的那個已婚男子一起去的。”—“不會吧。”"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to mean not any or not one person or thing. 沒有","examples":["He had no intention of paying the cash. 他絲毫沒有付現金的意思。","No job has more influence on the future of the world. 沒有哪種工作對世界的未來具有更大的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> to emphasize that someone or something is not the type of thing mentioned. 絕非","examples":["He is no singer. 他絕非唱歌家。","I make it no secret that our worst consultants earn nothing. 我毫不隱瞞地說我們最差的顧問掙不到一分錢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>no</b> in front of an adjective and noun to make the noun group mean its opposite. (用於名詞及其修飾形容詞前表示否定) 並非","examples":["Sometimes a bit of selfishness, if it leads to greater self-knowledge, is no bad thing. 有時候一點點的自私，如果能引發更多自知之明，也並非壞事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>No</b> is used in notices or instructions to say that a particular activity or thing is forbidden. (用於通知或指示中) 禁止","examples":["The captain turned out the \"no smoking\" signs. 機長關掉了“禁止吸菸”標誌燈。","No talking after lights out. 熄燈後禁止說話。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>no</b> to make the negative form of a comparative. (用於比較級的否定形式) 不","examples":["It is to start broadcasting no later than the end of 1994. 開始廣播不會晚於1994年底。","Yesterday no fewer than thirty climbers reached the summit. 昨天不少於三十名登山者到達了頂峰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>no</b> is a person who has answered \"no\" to a question or who has voted against something. <b>No</b> is also used to refer to their answer or vote. 作否定回答者; 投反對票者; 否定回答","examples":["According to the latest opinion polls, the noes have 50 percent, the yeses 35 percent. 根據最新的民意測驗，投反對票的人佔50%，投贊成票的人佔35%。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>there is no</b> doing a particular thing, you mean that it is very difficult or impossible to do that thing. 不可能 (做某事)","examples":["There is no going back to the life she had. 不可能回到她過去的生活。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Norway 挪威的網路域名","examples":[]}]}]},"north":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"北，北方；北部（地區）；北方發達國家（the North）；（橋牌）北家（North）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"北方的，朝北的；（風）北方吹來的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向北，朝北；大於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>north</b> is the direction which is on your left when you are looking toward the direction where the sun rises. 北方","examples":["In the north the ground becomes very cold as the winter snow and ice covers the ground. 在北方地面變得很冷，因為冬天的冰雪覆蓋著地面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>north</b> of a place, country, or region is the part which is in the north. 北部","examples":["The plan mostly benefits people in the North and Midwest. 該計劃使北部和中西部的人們最為受益。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The North</b> is used to refer to the richer, more developed countries of the world. 北方發達國家","examples":["Malaysia has emerged as the toughest critic of the North's environmental attitudes. 馬來西亞已成為對北方發達國家環境態度的最強硬的批評者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>north</b>, you travel toward the north. 向北方","examples":["Anita drove north up Pacific Highway. 安尼塔開車沿著太平洋公路向北行駛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>north</b> of a place is positioned to the north of it. 在…以北","examples":["...a little village a few miles north of Portland. …在波特蘭以北幾英里處的一個小村子。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>north</b> edge, corner, or part of a place or country is the part which is toward the north. 北部的","examples":["...the north side of the mountain. …山的北側。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"\"<b>North</b>\" is used in the names of some countries, states, and regions in the north of a larger area. (用於某區域北部的國名、州名或地名中) 北","examples":["There were demonstrations this weekend in cities throughout North America, Asia and Europe. 本週末示威遊行遍佈了北美洲、亞洲和歐洲的多個城市。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>north</b> wind is a wind that blows from the north. (風等) 來自北方的","examples":["...a bitterly cold north wind. …一陣非常寒冷的北風。"]}]}]},"nose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼻子；（飛機、火箭等的）頭部，機首；嗅覺；覺察力；（酒的）特有的氣味；<非正式>警方線人；探聽，探問"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（車輛、船隻等）緩慢地前行；（動物用鼻子）拱，嗅；勉強領先（或獲勝）；<非正式>窺探，搜尋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>nose</b> is the part of your face which sticks out above your mouth. You use it for smelling and breathing. 鼻子","examples":["She wiped her nose with a tissue. 她用一張紙巾擦了擦鼻子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>nose</b> of a vehicle such as an aeroplane or a boat is the front part of it. (飛機、船等的) 前部","examples":["They went over to the aeroplane and stood near its nose. 他們朝飛機走了過去並站在靠近機頭的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to your sense of smell as your <b>nose</b>. 嗅覺","examples":["The river that runs through Middlesbrough became ugly on the eye and hard on the nose. 那條流經米德爾斯伯勒的河變得醜不忍睹，臭不可聞。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>noses</b> in a certain direction or if you <b>nose</b> it there, you move it slowly and carefully in that direction. 使緩慢行駛; 緩慢行駛","examples":["He could not see the driver as the car nosed forward. 當那輛車緩慢向前行駛時，他看不見司機。","A motorboat nosed out of the mist and nudged into the branches of a tree. 一艘摩托艇緩緩地駛出薄霧，輕觸上一棵樹的枝條。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>nose clean</b>, you behave well and stay out of trouble. 行為規矩","examples":["If you kept your nose clean, you had a job for life. 你要是規規矩矩的，就一輩子會有工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> your <b>nose</b> to get to a place, you go straight ahead or follow the most obvious route. 直著往前走; 沿最明顯路線","examples":["Just follow your nose and in about five minutes you're at the old railway. 就直著往前走大約五分鐘你會到達舊鐵道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>follow</b> your <b>nose</b>, you do something in a particular way because you feel it should be done like that, rather than because you are following any plan or rules. 憑直覺行事","examples":["You won't have to think, just follow your nose. 你不必考慮，憑直覺行事就行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has a nose for</b> something, you mean that they have a natural ability to find it or recognize it. 有發現…的能力; 善於識別","examples":["He had a nose for trouble and a brilliant tactical mind. 他有發現問題的能力和一個精於謀略的頭腦。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>looks down</b> their <b>nose</b> at something or someone, you mean that they believe they are superior to that person or thing and treat them with disrespect. 輕視","examples":["I don't look down my nose at comedy. 我不輕視喜劇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that you <b>paid through the nose</b> for something, you are emphasizing that you had to pay what you consider too high a price for it. 花大價錢","examples":["We don't like paying through the nose for our wine when eating out. 我們在外面吃飯時不喜歡將大把的錢花在酒水上。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>pokes</b> their <b>nose into</b> something or <b>sticks</b> their <b>nose into</b> something, they try to interfere with it even though it does not concern them. 管閒事","examples":["We don't like strangers who poke their noses into our affairs. 我們不喜歡那些干預我們事務的陌生人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>rub</b> someone's <b>nose in</b> something that they do not want to think about, such as a failing or a mistake they have made, means to remind them repeatedly about it. 揭 (某人的) 傷疤; 抓住 (某人的過失等) 不放","examples":["His enemies will attempt to rub his nose in past policy statements. 他的對手們將試圖揪住他過去政策宣告中的紕漏不放。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>turn up</b> your <b>nose</b> <b>at</b> something, you reject it because you think that it is not good enough for you. 對…不屑一顧","examples":["I'm not in a financial position to turn up my nose at several hundred thousand dollars. 我沒有達到對幾十萬美元不屑一顧的經濟境況。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you do something <b>under</b> someone's <b>nose</b>, you do it right in front of them, without trying to hide it from them. 當著…的面","examples":["We've been married 25 years and this carrying on under my nose was the last straw. 我們已經結婚25年了，而我眼皮底下發生的這事兒使我最終忍無可忍。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If vehicles are <b>nose to tail</b>, the front of one vehicle is close behind the back of another. (車輛) 首尾相接","examples":[]}]}]},"o'clock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"……點鐘，整點（用於數字 1 至 12 後表示準確鐘點，等於 of the clock）；……點鐘方向（用於航空、軍事或口語，指以鐘面位置表示的方向，如 twelve o'clock 為正前方）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>o'clock</b> after numbers from one to twelve to say what time it is. For example, if you say that it is 9 o'clock, you mean that it is nine hours after midnight or nine hours after noon. …點鐘","examples":["The trouble began just after ten o'clock last night. 麻煩在昨晚剛過10點時開始了。"]}]}]},"note":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短箋，便條；筆記，記錄；註釋，批註；正式檔案，票據，證明書；音，音符；語氣，氣氛；鈔票；重要性，值得注意之處（of note）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"留意，注意；指出，提及；記錄，記下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>note</b> is a short letter. 便條","examples":["Stevens wrote him a note asking him to come to his apartment. 史蒂文斯給他寫了個便條讓他到他的公寓來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>note</b> is something that you write down to remind yourself of something. 記錄; 筆記","examples":["I knew that if I didn't make a note I would lose the thought so I asked to borrow a pen or pencil. 我知道如果我不做一個記錄我就會忘記這個想法，於是我要求借支鋼筆或鉛筆。","She wasn't taking notes on the lecture. 她沒記講座筆記。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a book or article, a <b>note</b> is a short piece of additional information. 註釋","examples":["See Note 16 on p. 223. 參見223頁的註釋16。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>note</b> is a short document that has to be signed by someone and that gives official information about something. 證明; 單據","examples":["Since Mr. Bennett was going to need some time off work, he asked for a sick note. 因為本內特先生需要請假一段時間，所以他要求開一張病假條。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In music, a <b>note</b> is the sound of a particular pitch, or a written symbol representing this sound. 音符","examples":["She has a deep voice and doesn't even try for the high notes. 她有一副低沉的嗓音，對高音她甚至試都不試。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>note</b> to refer to a particular quality in someone's voice that shows how they are feeling. 聲調; 語氣","examples":["There is an unmistakable note of nostalgia in his voice when he looks back on the early years of the family business. 在他回憶早年的家族企業時，他的聲音裡帶有一種確定無疑的懷舊語氣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>note</b> to refer to a particular feeling, impression, or atmosphere. (特別的) 感覺; 印象; 氣氛","examples":["Yesterday's testimony began on a note of passionate but civilized disagreement. 昨天的證詞是在一種激烈但文明的爭執氛圍中開始的。","Somehow he tells these stories without a note of horror. 不知為什麼，他講述這些故事時沒有一絲害怕的感覺。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can refer to a banknote as a <b>note</b>. 鈔票","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>note</b> a fact, you become aware of it. 注意到","examples":["The White House has noted his promise to support any attack that was designed to enforce the UN resolutions. 白宮已經注意到他支援任何旨在加強聯合國決議的抨擊的承諾。","Suddenly, I noted that the rain had stopped. 突然，我注意到雨已經停了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>note</b> something, you are drawing their attention to it. 注意","examples":["Note the statue to Sallustio Bandini, a prominent Sienese. 注意那座薩盧斯蒂奧·班迪尼的雕像，一個傑出的錫耶納人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>note</b> something, you mention it in order to draw people's attention to it. 提到","examples":["The report notes that export and import volumes picked up in leading economies. 該報道提到主要經濟大國的進出口額增加了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>note</b> something, you write it down as a record of what has happened. 記錄","examples":["\"He has had his tonsils out and has been ill, too,\" she noted in her diary. “他已經做了扁桃腺切除，又一直在生病。”她在自己的日記中寫道。","They never noted the building's history of problems. 他們從未記錄過那座建築的問題的歷史。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>of note</b> is important, worth mentioning, or well-known. 顯要的; 有名的","examples":["...politicians of note. …顯要的政客們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take note</b> <b>of</b> something, you pay attention to it because you think that it is important or significant. 注意","examples":["Take note of the weather conditions. 注意天氣情況。"]}]}]},"nothing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"沒有什麼，沒有一件東西；無關緊要的事，無足輕重的人；不值錢，不花錢；沒有什麼；（表示強調）沒有別的東西；（計算機數量上的）零"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"並不，毫不；<美，非正式> 用於強烈地表示相反看法根本不是（這樣）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"無關緊要的事，無足輕重的人；空地，虛空；零；無"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>沒前途的，沒價值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"否定不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nothing</b> means not a single thing, or not a single part of something. 沒有一個; 沒有一點","examples":["I've done nothing much since this morning. 自從今天上午我什麼都沒做。","There is nothing wrong with the car. 那輛車沒有一點毛病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>nothing</b> to indicate that something or someone is not important or significant. 無關緊要的事; 無足輕重的人","examples":["Because he had always had money it meant nothing to him. 因為他一直很有錢，所以錢對他來說無關緊要。","Do our years together mean nothing? 我們在一起的這些年一點都不重要嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Nothing</b> is also a noun. 無關緊要的事; 無足輕重的人","examples":["It is the picture itself that is the problem; so small, so dull. It's a nothing, really. 是這張圖片本身的問題，那麼小，那麼乏味。它沒什麼價值，真的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something cost <b>nothing</b> or is worth <b>nothing</b>, you are indicating that it cost or is worth a surprisingly small amount of money. 極低的價格; 極低的價值","examples":["The furniture was threadbare; he'd obviously picked it up for nothing. 那件傢俱破破爛爛；顯然他沒花什麼錢就撿來了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>nothing</b> before an adjective or `to'-infinitive to say that something or someone does not have the quality indicated. (用於形容詞或帶)(to)(的不定式之前，表示事物或人不具備所說的性質) 沒有什麼","examples":["Around the lake the countryside generally is nothing special. 那片湖周圍的鄉村總的來說沒什麼特別的。","There was nothing remarkable about him. 他沒有什麼非凡之處。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>nothing</b> before \"so\" and an adjective or adverb, or before a comparative, to emphasize how strong or great a particular quality is. (表示強調) 沒有別的東西","examples":["Youngsters learn nothing so fast as how to beat the system. 年輕人沒有什麼別的東西學得像如何鑽制度的空子這樣快。","I consider nothing more important in my life than songwriting. 我認為我的生活中沒有什麼比歌曲創作更重要。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>all or nothing</b> to say that either something must be done fully and completely or else it cannot be done at all. 要麼徹底做完，要麼徹底不做","examples":["Either he went through with this thing or he did not; it was all or nothing. 他要麼把這件事做完，要麼就不做，只有這兩種選擇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>better than nothing</b>, you mean that it is not what is required, but that it is better to have that thing than to have nothing at all. 比沒有強","examples":["After all, 15 minutes of exercise is better than nothing. 畢竟，15分鐘的鍛鍊比沒鍛鍊強。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>nothing but</b> in front of a noun, an infinitive without \"to,\" or an \"-ing\" form to mean \"only.\" (用於名詞、不帶)(to) 僅僅","examples":["All that money brought nothing but sadness and misery and tragedy. 所有那些錢帶來的僅僅是悲傷、痛苦和悲劇。","It did nothing but make us ridiculous. 它只是讓我們顯得可笑。","He is focused on nothing but winning. 他只關注勝利。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say about a story or report that there is <b>nothing to it</b>, you mean that it is untrue. 不真實","examples":["It's all superstition, and there's nothing to it. 這全是迷信，不是真的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say about an activity that there is <b>nothing to it</b>, you mean that it is extremely easy. 輕而易舉","examples":["If you've shied away from making pancakes in the past, don't be put off – there's really nothing to it! 如果你過去沒有信心做烙餅的話，就別再被它嚇著–真沒什麼難的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Nothing of the sort</b> is used when strongly contradicting something that has just been said. 絕無此事","examples":["\"We're going to talk this over in my office.\"—\"We're going to do nothing of the sort.\" “我們將在我的辦公室討論這件事。”–“我們將絕對不會這麼做。”"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say \"<b>It's nothing</b>\" as a polite response after someone has thanked them for something they have done. 不用謝; 沒什麼","examples":["\"Thank you for the wonderful dinner.\"—\"It's nothing,\" Sarah said. “謝謝你這頓豐盛的晚餐。”—“沒什麼，”薩拉說道。"]}]}]},"now":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"現在，此刻；馬上，立刻；（用於引起注意或用於轉換話題）好了；到現在為止，迄今；這樣一來；（用於婉轉地強調請求或命令）好了；你要知道（用於資訊承上啟下）；然而；用於敘述過去的事當時，那時；現在到了這個地步；嗯（在決定下面說什麼時的停頓用語）；（用於諷刺性反問的結尾）哦；<文>時而"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"現在的；<非正式>流行的，時髦的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"現在，此刻"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"由於，既然"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>now</b> to refer to the present time, often in contrast to a time in the past or the future. 現在","examples":["She's a widow now. 她現在是一個寡婦。","But we are now a much more fragmented society. 但是我們現在是一個更加四分五裂的社會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>now</b>, you do it immediately. 馬上","examples":["I'm sorry, but I must go now. 對不起，但是我得馬上走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>now</b> to indicate that a particular situation is the result of something that has recently happened. 這樣一來","examples":["Mrs. Chandra has received one sweater for each of her five children and says that the winter will not be so hard now. 錢德拉太太已經收到了發給她5個孩子每人一件的毛衫，並且說這樣一來冬天就不會那麼難過了。","She told me not to repeat it, but now I don't suppose it matters. 她告訴我不要重複它，但是這樣一來我認為它不重要了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In stories and accounts of past events, <b>now</b> is used to refer to the particular time that is being written or spoken about. 這會兒; 那時候","examples":["She felt a little better now. 這會兒她覺得好點兒了。","It was too late now for Blake to lock his room door. 布萊克那時鎖他的房門已經太晚了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>now</b> in statements which specify the length of time up to the present that something has lasted. 到現在","examples":["They've been married now for 30 years. 他們結婚至今已30年。","They have been missing for a long time now. 到現在他們已經失蹤很長時間了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say \"<b>Now</b>\" or \"<b>Now then</b>\" to indicate to the person or people you are with that you want their attention, or that you are about to change the subject. (用於引起注意或用於轉換話題) 好了","examples":["\"Now then,\" Max said, \"to get back to the point.\" “好了，”馬克斯說：“回到正題。”","Now then, what's the trouble? 好了，出什麼問題了？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>now</b> to give a slight emphasis to a request or command. (用於婉轉地強調請求或命令) 好了","examples":["Come on now. You know you must be hungry. 好了。你看你一定是餓了。","Come and sit down here, now. 好了，來坐在這裡吧。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Now</b>\" to introduce information which is relevant to the part of a story or account that you have reached, and which needs to be known before you can continue. 你要知道 (用於資訊承上啟下)","examples":["My son went to Aspen, in Colorado. Now he and his wife are people who love a quiet holiday. 我兒子去了科羅拉多的阿斯彭。你要知道，他和他妻子是喜歡安靜假期的人。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You say \"<b>Now</b>\" to introduce something which contrasts with what you have just said. 然而","examples":["Now, if it was me, I'd want to do more than just change the locks. 然而，如果是我，我要做的遠不只是換換鎖。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Now</b> is also a pronoun. 現在","examples":["Now is the time when we must all live as economically as possible. 現在是我們都必須儘可能節儉度日的時候了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Now</b> is also a pronoun. 馬上","examples":["Now is your chance to talk to him. 馬上就是你和他談話的機會了。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>now</b> or <b>now that</b> to indicate that an event has occurred and as a result something else may or will happen. 既然","examples":["Now you're settled, why don't you take up some serious study? 既然你安頓下來了，為什麼不做些認真的研究呢？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>now and then</b> or <b>every now and again</b>, you mean that it happens sometimes but not very often or regularly. 偶爾","examples":["My father has a collection of magazines to which I return every now and then. 我父親收藏雜誌,我偶爾會翻閱一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>any day now</b>, <b>any moment now</b>, or <b>any time now</b>, you mean that it will happen very soon. 不久","examples":["Jim expects to be sent to Europe any day now. 吉姆期待不久就被派往歐洲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Just now</b> means a very short time ago. 剛才","examples":["You looked pretty upset just now. 你剛才看上去很沮喪。","I spoke just now of being in love. 我剛才說到戀愛了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>just now</b> when you want to say that a particular situation exists at the time when you are speaking, although it may change in the future. 此刻","examples":["I'm pretty busy just now. 我此刻很忙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"People such as television hosts sometimes use <b>now for</b> when they are going to start talking about a different subject or start presenting a new activity. 現在轉到 (另一個話題或活動)","examples":["And now for something completely different. 現在談點完全不同的事情。"]}]}]},"notice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"注意，察覺；通告，佈告；公告牌，警示牌；通知；事先宣告，警告；預先通知期；劇評，書評；辭職信，搬遷通知；（報紙、雜誌上的）小型廣告，簡短通告；警告書，說明書"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"意識，注意；留意；正式通知；簡評；客氣對待；<古>提到，談到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>notice</b> something or someone, you become aware of them. 注意到; 察覺","examples":["He stressed that people should not hesitate to contact the police if they've noticed any strangers recently. 他強調人們最近如果注意到任何陌生人，要馬上與警方聯絡。","I noticed that most academics were writing papers during the summer. 我注意到大部分學者那個暑期都在撰寫論文。","Luckily, I'd noticed where you left the car. 幸好，我注意了你停車的地點。","If he thought no one would notice, he's wrong. 如果他認為無人察覺，那他就錯了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>notice</b> is a written announcement in a place where everyone can read it. 告示","examples":["Notices in the waiting room requested that you neither smoke nor spit. 等候室的告示要求人們不要吸菸也不要隨地吐痰。","A few guest houses had \"No Vacancies\" notices in their windows. 幾家旅社在他們的窗戶上貼出了“客滿”的告示。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give <b>notice</b> about something that is going to happen, you give a warning in advance that it is going to happen. 事先通知","examples":["Interest is paid monthly. Three months' notice is required for withdrawals. 利息按月給付。提款要求提前三個月通知。","The insured must be given at least 10 days' notice of cancellation. 取消保險必須給被保險人至少十天的事先通知。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>notice</b> is a formal announcement in a newspaper or magazine about something that has happened or is going to happen. 啟事","examples":["I spotted a notice in a local newspaper. 我在當地一家報紙上看到了一則啟事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>notice</b> is one of a number of letters that are similar or exactly the same which an organization sends to people in order to give them information or ask them to do something. 通告","examples":["Bonus notices were issued each year from head office to local agents. 紅利通告每年由總公司發給各地方代理商。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>notice</b> is a written article in a newspaper or magazine in which someone gives their opinion of a play, film, or concert. (報刊上的) 評論","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Notice</b> is used in expressions such as \"<b>on short notice</b>,\" \"<b>at a moment's notice</b>,\" or \"<b>at twenty-four hours' notice</b>,\" to indicate that something can or must be done within a short period of time. 提前…時間通知","examples":["There's no one available on such short notice to take her class. 僅提前這麼短時間通知，找不到人接她的課。","I live just a mile away, so I can usually be available on short notice. 我就住在一英里遠，所以我通常接到通知就能到。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation is said to exist <b>until further notice</b>, it will continue for an uncertain length of time until someone changes it. 直到另行通知","examples":["The bad news was that all flights had been cancelled until further notice. 壞訊息是所有航班都已被取消，何時恢復另行通知。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an employer <b>gives</b> an employee <b>notice</b>, the employer tells the employee that he or she must leave his or her job within a short fixed period of time. 通知某人在限期內離職","examples":["The next morning I telephoned him and gave him his notice. 第二天早晨我給他打電話通知他在限期內離職。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>give notice</b> or <b>hand in notice</b> you tell your employer that you intend to leave your job soon, within a set period of time. You can also <b>hand in</b> your <b>notice</b>. 提出辭職","examples":["He handed in his notice at the bank and ruined his promising career. 他向銀行提交了辭呈，毀掉了他的大好前程。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>take notice</b> <b>of</b> a particular fact or situation, you behave in a way that shows that you are aware of it. 提起注意","examples":["We want the government to take notice of what we think they should do for single parents. 我們希望政府對我們希望他們為單親母親應該做的事情提起注意。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>take no notice</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you do not consider them to be important enough to affect what you think or what you do. 不理會","examples":["They took no notice of him, he did not stand out, he was in no way remarkable. 他們對他不予理會，他不出眾，一點也不優秀。"]}]}]},"ok":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好的；不錯的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"行；很好"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"好；可以"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"對…表示同意"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同意"}],"sections":[]},"nurse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"護士；<舊>保姆，奶媽；保育蟲；（保護其他作物的）防護作物；沙錐齒鯊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看護，照料；細心打理；調養，調治；餵奶，哺乳；吃奶；懷有；慢慢地喝；愛惜地摟抱；<舊>（在某種特定條件下）被撫養長大；（檯球，斯諾克）聚球，使球互相靠攏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nurse</b> is a person whose job is to care for people who are ill. 護士","examples":["She had spent 29 years as a nurse. 她已當了29年護士。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nurse</b> someone, you care for them when they are ill. 護理","examples":["All the years he was sick my mother had nursed him. 在他有病的那些年裡，我母親一直照顧他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>nurse</b> an illness or injury, you allow it to get better by resting as much as possible. 調治","examples":["We're going to go home and nurse our colds. 我們打算回家調治感冒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>nurse</b> an emotion or desire, you feel it strongly for a long time. 懷有","examples":["Jane still nurses the pain of rejection. 簡依然懷著被拒絕的痛苦。"]}]}]},"ocean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>海洋，大海（the ocean）；（五大洋之一的）洋；<非正式>許多，大量（an ocean of/oceans of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The ocean</b> is the sea. 大海","examples":["There were few sights as beautiful as the calm ocean on a warm night. 很少有景色像溫暖夜晚的平靜大海那樣美麗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>ocean</b> is one of the five very large areas of sea on the Earth's surface. 洋","examples":["They spent many days cruising the northern Pacific Ocean. 他們花了很多天巡遊北太平洋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is an <b>ocean of</b> something, you are emphasizing that there is a very large amount of it. 極大量","examples":["I had cried oceans of tears. 我已哭得淚流成河。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a drop in the ocean</b>, you mean that it is a very small amount which is unimportant compared to the cost of other things or is so small that it has very little effect on something. 滄海一粟","examples":["His fee is a drop in the ocean compared with the real cost of broadcasting. 他的費用與廣播的實際成本相比是滄海一粟。"]}]}]},"october":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"[天] 十月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>October</b> is the tenth month of the year in the Western calendar. 10月","examples":["Most seasonal hiring is done in early October. 多數季節性招聘是在10月初進行。","The first plane is due to leave on October 2. 第一架飛機定於10月2日起飛。"]}]}]},"number":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"數字；編號，序數；電話號碼；總量，數量；大量（numbers）；一群人；（雜誌的）期，號；（演出中的）一首歌，一段舞蹈；<非正式>有吸引力的人（或事物）；數，單複數；歷史資料（numbers）；數字彩票（numbers）；錢數（numbers）；<俚>具有……特徵的人；常說的事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"標號，編號；總計；包括，列入（某類）；計算，數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>number</b> is a word such as \"two,\" \"nine,\" or \"twelve,\" or a symbol such as 1, 3, or 47. You use numbers to say how many things you are referring to or where something comes in a series. 數字; 號碼","examples":["No, I don't know the room number. 不，我不知道房間號。","Stan Laurel was born at number 3, Argyll Street. 斯坦·勞雷爾出生於阿蓋爾街3號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>number</b> with words such as \"large\" or \"small\" to say approximately how many things or people there are. 數量","examples":["Quite a considerable number of interviews are going on. 許許多多的面試正在進行。","I have had an enormous number of letters from single parents. 我收到了大量單親家長的來信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there are <b>a</b> <b>number</b> <b>of</b> things or people, there are several of them. If there are <b>any</b> <b>number</b> <b>of</b> things or people, there is a large quantity of them. 幾個; 許多","examples":["I seem to remember that Sam told a number of lies. 我記得好像薩姆撒過一些謊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to someone's or something's position in a list of the most successful or most popular of a particular type of thing as, for example, <b>number</b> one or <b>number</b> two. (排名) 第…號","examples":["Martin now faces the world number one, Jansher Khan of Pakistan. 馬丁現在面對的是世界頭號選手，巴基斯坦的詹舍爾漢。","Before you knew it, the single was at number 90 in the U.S. singles charts. 轉眼間這張單曲唱片在美國單曲唱片排行榜上排第90位了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>number</b> is the series of numbers that you dial when you are making a telephone call. 電話號碼","examples":["...a list of names and telephone numbers. …一張姓名和電話號碼單子。","My number is 414-3925. 我的電話號碼是414-3925。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to a short piece of music, a song, or a dance as a <b>number</b>. 一首 (歌曲、樂曲); 一段 (舞蹈)","examples":["...\"Unforgettable,\" a number that was written and performed in 1951. …《難以忘懷》，一首在1951年創作並演唱的歌曲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people or things <b>numbers</b> a particular total, that is how many there are. 總計","examples":["They told me that their village numbered 100. 他們告訴我他們村共有100人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is numbered</b> <b>among</b> a particular group, they are believed to belong in that group. 把…列入","examples":["Lech Walesa and Nelson Mandela are numbered among my personal heroes. 萊奇·維爾薩和納爾遜·曼德拉被列入了我心目中的英雄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>number</b> something, you mark it with a number, usually starting at 1. 把…編號","examples":["He cut his paper up into tiny squares, and he numbered each one. 他把紙裁成小方塊並給每個方塊編號。"]}]}]},"okay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"好，行"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可以，不錯的；對；安全的，沒事的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"可以，不錯；對；很好地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同意，批准"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"批准，同意，認可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>okay</b>, you find it satisfactory or acceptable. 不錯的; 可以的","examples":["...a shooting range where it's OK to use weapons. …一個可以使用武器的靶場。","Is it okay if I come by myself? 我獨自來行嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>okay</b>, you mean that they are safe and well. 安全的; 狀況好的","examples":["Check that the baby's okay. 看一下嬰兒是否沒事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Okay</b> is also an adverb. 不錯; 可以","examples":["We seemed to manage okay for the first year or so after David was born. 戴維出生後的第一年左右，我們好像過得還可以。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Okay</b>\" to show that you agree to something. (表示同意) 行","examples":["\"Just tell him I would like to talk to him.\"—\"OK.\" “你就告訴他我想跟他談談。” — “行。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Okay?</b>\" to check whether the person you are talking to understands what you have said and accepts it. 行嗎","examples":["We'll get together next week, OK? 我們下星期聚一聚，好嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>okay</b> to indicate that you want to start talking about something else or doing something else. 好了","examples":["OK. Now, let's talk some business. 好了。現在，咱們談點正事吧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>okay</b> to stop someone from arguing with you by showing that you accept the point they are making, though you do not necessarily regard it as very important. 好吧","examples":["Okay, there is a slight difference. 好吧，是有稍稍的不同。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>okays</b> something, they officially agree to it or allow it to happen. 批准","examples":["His doctor wouldn't OK the trip. 他的醫生不會同意這趟旅行的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Okay</b> is also a noun. 批准","examples":["He gave the okay to issue a new press release. 他做出批准發表一篇新的新聞稿。"]}]}]},"officer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軍官；（政府或大機構的）官員，高階職員；警察，警官；船長；某一榮譽等級中的一分子（如英帝國勳位中四等勳爵士以下的級別）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"配備軍官；指揮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the armed forces, an <b>officer</b> is a person in a position of authority. 軍官","examples":["...a retired army officer. …一位退役陸軍軍官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Members of the police force can be referred to as <b>officers</b>. 警察; 警官","examples":["The officer saw no obvious signs of a break-in. 那個警察沒看到任何闖入的明顯痕跡。","Officer Montoya was first on the scene. 蒙託亞警官是第一個到達現場的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>officer</b> is a person who has a responsible position in an organization, especially a government organization. (尤指政府部門的) 官員","examples":["...a local authority education officer. …一名地方政府教育官員。"]}]}]},"office":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"辦公室；辦公樓，辦事處；（提供某項服務的）室，處，局；（尤指政府的）部，局，廳；<美>診所；（辦公室、辦公樓、事務所等的）全體辦事人員，全體工作人員；重要官職，重要職務；（天主教牧師、教徒等）每日的祈禱 （=Divine Office）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>office</b> is a room or a part of a building where people work sitting at desks. 辦公室","examples":["By the time Flynn arrived at his office it was 5:30. 弗林到達辦公室時已經5:30了。","Telephone their head office for more details. 給他們總部打電話詢問更多的詳細情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>office</b> is a department of an organization, especially the government, where people deal with a particular kind of administrative work. (尤指政府的) 行政部門","examples":["Thousands have registered with unemployment offices. 數千人已在失業服務處登記了。","...the Congressional Budget Office. …國會預算辦公室。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>office</b> is a small building or room where people can go for information, tickets, or a service of some kind. 服務處","examples":["The tourist office operates a useful room-finding service. 這個旅遊辦事處開辦了實用的找房業務。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A doctor's or dentist's <b>office</b> is a place where a doctor or dentist sees their patients. 診所","examples":["The chance of getting AIDS at the doctor's or dentist's office is extremely low. 在診所或牙醫診所感染艾滋病的可能性極小。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone holds <b>office</b> in a government, they have an important job or position of authority. 公職","examples":["The events to mark the president's four years in office went ahead as planned. 紀念總統執政4年的活動按計劃舉行。","The treasurer shall hold office for five years. 財務主管將任職5年。"]}]}]},"oil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燃油，潤滑油；石油，原油；潤膚油，護髮油；食用油；油性塗料，油畫顏料（oils）；油畫；<澳新，非正式>資訊，事實"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加油於……，給……加潤滑油；給（皮膚）塗油，抹油"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oil</b> is a smooth, thick liquid that is used as a fuel and for making the parts of machines move smoothly. Oil is found underground. 石油","examples":["The company buys and sells about 600,000 barrels of oil a day. 這家公司一天買賣約六十萬桶石油。","...the rapid rise in prices for oil and petrol. …石油和汽油價格的飆漲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Oil</b> is a smooth, thick liquid made from plants and is often used for cooking. 植物油","examples":["Combine the beans, chopped mint, and oil in a large bowl. 將豆子、剁碎的薄荷和植物油混在一個大碗裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Oil</b> is a smooth, thick liquid, often with a pleasant smell, that you rub into your skin or add to your bath. 潤膚油; 沐浴液","examples":["Try a hot bath with some relaxing bath oil. 試試用點兒放鬆身心的沐浴液洗個熱水澡吧。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>oil</b> something, you put oil onto or into it, for example, to make it work smoothly or to protect it. 給某物上油","examples":["A crew of assistants oiled and adjusted the release mechanism until it worked perfectly. 助手們給排放裝置加了潤滑油並做了調節，直到其運轉良好。"]}]}]},"orange":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橙，柑橘；橙色，橘黃色；橙汁，橘汁飲料；橙樹，橘樹；橙黃色蝴蝶；（Orange）（美、法、俄、英）奧林奇（人名）；奧蘭治（地名）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"橙紅色的，橘黃色的；奧蘭治黨或社團的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>orange</b> is of a colour between red and yellow. 橙色的","examples":["...men in bright orange uniforms. …身穿鮮豔橙色制服的男人們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orange</b> is a round juicy fruit with a thick, orange-coloured skin. 柑; 橘; 橙","examples":["...orange trees. …橘樹。"]}]}]},"once":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一次， 一回；曾經，一度；任何一次，從來；乘以一"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"一.....就， 一旦"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一次"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>once</b>, it happens one time only. 一次","examples":["I met Miquela once, briefly. 我見過蜜凱拉一次，時間很短。","Since that evening I haven't once slept through the night. 自那晚之後，我再也沒睡過一次囫圇覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>once</b> with \"a\" and words like \"day,\" \"week,\" and \"month\" to indicate that something happens regularly, one time in each day, week, or month. 每隔…一次","examples":["Lung cells die and are replaced about once a week. 肺細胞約每週死亡、更新一次。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something was <b>once</b> true, it was true at some time in the past, but is no longer true. 從前","examples":["Her parents once ran a shop. 她父母從前開過一家商店。","I lived there once myself, before I got married. 我從前自己住在那兒，沒結婚前。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>once</b> did something, they did it at some time in the past. 曾經","examples":["I once went camping at Lake Michigan with a friend. 我曾和一個朋友去密執安湖野營。","We once walked across the frozen pond at two in the morning. 我們曾在凌晨2點徒步橫穿冰凍的池塘。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Once</b> is also a pronoun. 一次","examples":["\"Have they been to visit you yet?\"—\"Just the once, yeah.\" “他們已經去看過你了嗎？”— “來過，就那一次。”"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>once</b> another thing has happened, it happens immediately afterward. 一…就","examples":["The decision had taken about 10 seconds once he'd read a market research study. 他讀完一份市場調研報告後，10秒鐘就做出了決定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>all at once</b>, it happens suddenly, often when you are not expecting it to happen. 突然","examples":["All at once there was someone knocking on the door. 突然有人敲門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>at once</b>, you do it immediately. 立刻","examples":["I have to go at once. 我得馬上走。","Remove from the heat, add the parsley, toss and serve at once. 從火上端下來，加入香芹，攪拌後立刻上桌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a number of different things happen <b>at once</b> or <b>all at once</b>, they all happen at the same time. 同時","examples":["You can't be doing two things at once. 你不能同時做兩件事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>For once</b> is used to emphasize that something happens on this particular occasion, that it has never happened before, and may never happen again. 就此一次","examples":["For once, Dad is not complaining. 就這一次，爸爸沒有抱怨。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something happens <b>once again</b> or <b>once more</b>, it happens again. 再一次","examples":["Amy picked up the hairbrush and brushed her hair once more. 艾米拿起梳子，又梳了一遍頭髮。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something happens <b>once and for all</b>, it happens completely or finally. 最終地","examples":["We have to resolve this matter once and for all. 我們必須徹底解決這件事情。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something happens <b>once in a while</b>, it happens sometimes, but not very often. 偶爾","examples":["Your body, like any other machine, needs a full service once in a while. 你的身體就像其他機器一樣，偶爾也需要一次全面保養。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you have done something <b>once or twice</b>, you have done it a few times, but not very often. 一兩次; 幾次","examples":["I visited once or twice. 我參觀過一兩次。","Once or twice she had caught a flash of interest in William's eyes. 有一兩次，她捕捉到威廉眼中一閃的關注。"]}]}]},"pa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爸爸（口語）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Pa）人名；（中）巴（普通話·威妥瑪）；（柬、緬）巴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people address or refer to their father as <b>pa</b>. 爸爸","examples":["Pa used to be in the army. http://yourhc/default.aspx 爸爸過去當過兵。 http://yourhc/default.aspx"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a Māori village or settlement 毛利村莊; 毛利定居點","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Panama 巴拿馬","examples":[]}]}]},"page":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書、報紙、檔案等的）頁，面；網頁；歷史重要事件（或時期），歷史篇章；<英>伴童，（新娘的）小男儐相；（旅館或俱樂部中通常身穿制服的）男侍從，聽差；（中世紀作為接受騎士訓練服侍某個騎士的）學習騎士；（舊時高層人員的）男侍從；<美>（美國議員的）青年助理（本身為學生）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在公共場所）用擴音器呼叫（某人或釋出資訊）；用尋呼機呼叫（某人）；隨意翻閱，瀏覽（page through）；（軟體、資料的）分頁（儲存）；為……編頁碼，為……標註頁碼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>page</b> is one side of one of the pieces of paper in a book, magazine, or newspaper. Each page usually has a number printed at the top or bottom. (書、報刊等的) 頁; 版","examples":["Take out your book and turn to page 4. 拿出你的書，翻到第4頁。","...the front page of USA Today. …《今日美國》的頭版。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pages</b> of a book, magazine, or newspaper are the pieces of paper it consists of. (書、報刊等的) 紙頁","examples":["He turned the pages of his notebook. 他翻著他筆記本的紙頁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to an important event or period of time as a <b>page</b> of history. (歷史的) 一頁","examples":["...a new page in the country's political history. …這個國家政治歷史上新的一頁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>page</b> is a young person who takes messages or does small jobs for members of the United States Congress or state legislatures. (美國國會或州立法機關的) 青年助理","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>page</b> is a small boy who accompanies the bride at a wedding. 男小儐相","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a boy employed to run errands, carry messages, etc, for the guests in a hotel, club, etc 跑腿的男孩","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who is in a public place <b>is paged</b>, they receive a message, often over a speaker, telling them that someone is trying to contact them. (在公共場合透過揚聲器) 呼叫","examples":["He was paged repeatedly as the flight was boarding. 登機時，他被反覆地呼叫著。"]}]}]},"papa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爸爸，父親（兒語或親暱稱呼，亦作 poppa）；（Papa）人名，音譯“帕帕”（俄、意、葡、羅、幾）；（舊用法，羅馬天主教會）教皇，亦作 Papa；（紐西蘭，罕用）軟質藍灰色粘土"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"家庭成員名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people refer to or address their father as <b>papa</b>. 爸爸","examples":["He was so much older than me, older even than my papa. 他比我老那麼多，甚至比我爸爸還老。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>rare.</b> a soft blue-grey clay of marine siltstone or sandstone 一種軟質藍灰色粘土","examples":[]}]}]},"one":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"一；一個；一歲；一點鐘"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"一個人；任何人，人們（表泛指）；那個人；（特指的）那種人"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"一個（強調某人或某事）；一個（用於比較相似的人或物）；某個（用於不認識的人的名字前）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"唯一的；一的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一；一美元紙幣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（One）（印、馬、美）溫（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>One</b> is the number 1. 1","examples":["They had three sons and one daughter. 他們有3兒1女。","...one thousand years ago. …1000年以前。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is the <b>one</b> person or thing of a particular kind, you are emphasizing that they are the only person or thing of that kind. 惟一的","examples":["They had alienated the one man who knew the business. 他們已經疏遠了那個惟一懂這行的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>One</b> is also an adjective. 這個","examples":["The one thing that she accomplished was raising money to update our facilities. 她完成的這項工作就是募集資金來更新我們的裝置。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>One</b> can be used instead of \"a\" to emphasize the following noun. 用來代替(a)，強調後接的名詞","examples":["There is one thing I would like to know – What is it about Tim that you find so irresistible? 有一件事我想知道–蒂姆到底有什麼讓你覺得那麼不可抗拒？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> instead of \"a\" to emphasize the following adjective or expression. 用來代替(a)，強調後接的形容詞或短語","examples":["If we ever get married we'll have one terrific wedding. 如果我們結婚，我們會舉辦一場盛大的婚禮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> to refer to the first of two or more things that you are comparing. (表示與其他事物作比較) 這個","examples":["Prices vary from one shop to another. 各家商店價格不同。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> when you have been talking or writing about a group of people or things and you want to say something about a particular member of the group. (特定的一群人或事物中的) 一個","examples":["\"A college degree isn't enough,\" said one honours student. “只有一個大學的學位還不夠，”一位優等生說。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> when referring to a time in the past or in the future. For example, if you say that you did something <b>one day</b>, you mean that you did it on a day in the past. 某一個 (過去或將來的時間)","examples":["How would you like to have dinner one night, just you and me? 哪天晚上一起吃飯怎麼樣，就你和我？"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>One</b> is also a pronoun. 這一個","examples":["The twins were dressed differently and one was thinner than the other. 這對雙胞胎穿著各異，而且其中一個比另一個瘦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> or <b>ones</b> instead of a noun when it is clear what type of thing or person you are referring to and you are describing them or giving more information about them. 用來替代名詞所指的很明確的人、物","examples":["They are selling their house to move to a smaller one. 他們要賣掉他們的房子，搬到一個小點的房子去住。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>ones</b> to refer to people in general. 人們","examples":["We are the only ones who know. 我們是惟一知情的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>one</b> instead of a noun group when you have just mentioned something and you want to describe it or give more information about it. 用以替代名詞片語表示的剛提到的且要詳細描述的事物","examples":["The issue of land reform was one that dominated Hungary's parliamentary elections. 土地改革是一個左右匈牙利議會選舉的問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>One</b> is also a pronoun. 一個","examples":["Some of them couldn't eat a thing. One couldn't even drink. 他們中有些人一點東西都不能吃，有一人甚至連水都不能喝。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>one</b> to make statements about people in general which also apply to themselves. <b>One</b> can be used as the subject or object of a sentence. 人們","examples":["If one looks at the bigger picture, a lot of positive things are happening. 如果人們從更宏觀的角度看，許多積極的事情正在發生。","Where does one go from there? 人們從那兒能去哪裡？"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>one</b> in expressions such as \"<b>one of the biggest airports</b>\" or \"<b>one of the most experienced players</b>\" to indicate that something or someone is bigger or more experienced than most other things or people of the same kind. (最…) 之一","examples":["Subaru is one of the smallest Japanese car makers. 斯巴魯是最小的日本汽車製造商之一。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>for one</b> to emphasize that a particular person is definitely reacting or behaving in a particular way, even if other people are not. 就某人來說","examples":["I, for one, hope you don't get the job. 就我來說，我不希望你得到那份工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>a hundred and one</b>, <b>a thousand and one</b>, and <b>a million and one</b> to emphasize that you are talking about a large number of things or people. (表示強調) 很多","examples":["There are a hundred and one ways in which you can raise money. 有很多你可以籌錢的辦法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>in one</b> to indicate that something is a single unit, but is made up of several different parts or has several different functions. 集為一體","examples":["...a love story and an adventure all in one. …一個集愛情與冒險於一體的故事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>one after the other</b> or <b>one after another</b> to say that actions or events happen with very little time between them. 一個接一個地","examples":["My three guitars broke one after the other. 我的3把吉它一個接著一個地壞了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The one and only</b> can be used in front of the name of an actor, singer, or other famous person when they are being introduced on a show. (用在演出前的介紹中) 獨一無二的","examples":["...one of the greatest ever rock performers, the one and only Tina Turner. …有史以來最偉大的搖滾歌手之一，舉世無雙的蒂納·特納。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>one by one</b> to indicate that people do things or that things happen in sequence, not all at the same time. 依次地","examples":["We went into the room one by one. 我們依次走進了房間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>one or other</b> to refer to one or more things or people in a group, when it does not matter which particular one or ones are thought of or chosen. 或者這個或者那個","examples":["One or other of the two women was wrong. 這兩個婦女中總有一個錯了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>One or two</b> means a few. 幾個","examples":["We may make one or two changes. 我們可以作幾處改變。","I've also sold one or two to a publisher. 我也賣了幾個給一位出版商。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you try to get <b>one up on</b> someone, you try to gain an advantage over them. 略勝某人一籌","examples":["...the competitive kind who will see this as the opportunity to be one up on you. …那種會把這視為一次勝過你的機會的好勝者。"]}]}]},"pants":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美> 褲子；<英> 內褲，短褲；<英，非正式> 廢物，劣質品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英，非正式>無價值的，低劣的；褲子的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"氣喘，喘息；喘著氣說；渴望（pant 的第三人稱單數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pants</b> are a piece of clothing that covers the lower part of your body and each leg. 長褲","examples":["She described him as wearing brown corduroy pants and a white cotton shirt. 她描述說他穿著棕色的燈芯絨長褲和一件白色的棉襯衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pants</b> are a piece of underwear which have two holes to put your legs through and elastic around the top to hold them up around your waist or hips. 內褲","examples":[]}]}]},"outside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外表，外部（the outside）；（建築物、車輛等的）周圍，外圍（the outside）；（人行道的）外側；（彎曲路面或軌道的）外道，邊緣；一令紙的上下兩張（outsides）；局外（人士），外界（人士）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……的外面，在戶外；超出……的範圍（或界限）；（團體或組織）以外的；<美>除了，除……之外（outside of）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在外面；在戶外，在四周；在外側，表面上"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外邊的，表面的；（曲棍球、足球等）邊鋒的；（建築物）外圍的，四周的；不屬於本團體（或機構、國家等）的，不相關的；（可能性）極微小的，不大可能的；（車道）靠近路中間的，快車道的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>outside</b> of something is the part which surrounds or encloses the rest of it. 外部","examples":["...the outside of the building. …該建築物的外部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also a noun. 外部","examples":["Peace cannot be imposed from the outside by the United States or anyone else. 和平不能由美國或其他任何國家從外部強加。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also an adjective. 外部的","examples":["...high up on the outside wall. …在外牆上很高的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also an adjective. 外面的","examples":["...the outside temperature. …外面的溫度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>outside</b> world, you are referring to things that happen or exist in places other than your own home or community. 外界的","examples":["...a side of Morris's character she hid carefully from the outside world. …莫里斯對外界小心掩藏的其性格的一面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> people or organizations are not part of a particular organization or group. 外來的; 外聘的","examples":["The company now makes much greater use of outside consultants. 該公司現在更多地利用外聘顧問。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>outside</b>, you are not inside a building but are quite close to it. 在外面","examples":["I stepped outside and pulled up my collar against the cold mist. 我走到外面，拉起衣領以抵禦寒霧。","Outside, the light was fading rapidly. 在外面，光在快速消失。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also an adverb. 在外面","examples":["They heard voices coming from outside in the corridor. 他們聽到來自外面走廊的說話聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also an adverb. 在外界","examples":["The scheme was good for the prisoners because it brought them outside into the community. 該方案對犯人們有益，因為這能讓他們到外界去融入社會。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also a preposition. 在…外面","examples":["The victim was outside a shop when he was attacked. 受害人被襲擊時正在一家商店外面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>outside</b> a room, you are not in it but are in the passage or area next to it. 在 (房間) 外面","examples":["She'd sent him outside the classroom. 她叫他到教室外面去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People or things <b>outside</b> a country, town, or region are not in it. 在 (某國、城市、地區) 之外","examples":["...an old castle outside Budapest. …布達佩斯外的一座古堡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> is also a preposition. 從外面來; 從外面聘","examples":["He is hoping to recruit a chairman from outside the company. 他在希望從公司之外招聘一位董事長。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Outside</b> a particular institution or field of activity means in other fields of activity or in general life. 在 (某機構或領域) 以外","examples":["...the largest merger ever to take place outside the oil industry. …石油行業以外有史以來最大的合併。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that is <b>outside</b> a particular range of things is not included within it. 在 (某範圍) 以外","examples":["She is a beautiful boat, but way, way outside my price range. 她是條漂亮的船，但遠在我的價格承受範圍以外。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Something that happens <b>outside</b> a particular period of time happens at a different time from the one mentioned. 在 (某時期) 以外","examples":["They are open outside normal daily banking hours. 它們在銀行日常營業時間以外開放。"]}]}]},"paint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"油漆，塗料；繪畫顏料（paints）；（已乾的）油漆層，塗層；<非正式>化妝，塗脂抹粉；（計算機）（尤指模擬真畫效果的）繪圖功能；<美>花馬，雜色馬；（籃球）三秒區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給……）上油漆，（給……）塗顏料；用油漆（或塗料）覆蓋（paint sth. out）；（用顏料）繪畫；塗，抹（嘴唇、指甲等）；（以某種方式）描繪，描寫；（計算機）用繪圖程式作圖；（在雷達螢幕上）顯示（飛機，車輛）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Paint</b> is a coloured liquid that you put onto a surface with a brush in order to protect the surface or to make it look nice, or that you use to produce a picture. 油漆; 塗料","examples":["...a can of red paint. …一罐紅色油漆。","They saw some large letters in white paint. 他們看見了幾個用白漆寫的大大的字母。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"On a wall or object, <b>the paint</b> is the covering of dried paint on it. 油漆層; 塗層","examples":["The paint was peeling on the window frames. 窗框上的油漆正在剝落。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>paint</b> a wall or an object, you cover it with paint. 給…刷油漆; 給…刷塗料","examples":["They started to mend the woodwork and paint the walls. 他們開始修理木建部分並粉刷牆壁。","I had come here to paint. 我到這兒來是刷漆的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>paint</b> something or <b>paint</b> a picture of it, you produce a picture of it using paint. 畫","examples":["He is painting a huge volcano. 他正在畫一座巨型火山。","Why do people paint pictures? 為什麼人們要畫畫？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>paint</b> a design or message on a surface, you put it on the surface using paint. 用顏料畫; 用顏料寫","examples":["...a machine for painting white lines on roads. …一臺用來在馬路上畫白線的機器。","They went around painting rude slogans on cars. 他們到處用顏料在轎車上寫粗魯的標語。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>paint</b> a grim or vivid picture of something, you give a description of it that is grim or vivid. 把…描繪成","examples":["The report paints a grim picture of life there. 該報道把那裡的生活描繪成一副陰森的畫面。"]}]}]},"pair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（成雙的兩物品）一對，一雙；（由兩個相連的類似部分組成的）一套，一副；兩個共事（或有特殊關係）的人；（成對物的）另一隻，（搭檔的）另一人；（交配的）一對動物；兩匹並排駕車的馬；對子（指兩張同點的紙牌）；（議會中）相約放棄投票權的敵對兩黨的兩名議員（或其中一名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成對，配對；（使）結成一對（戀人）（pair off/up）；（動物）交配（=pair up）；使（敵對兩黨的兩名議員）組成不投票的一對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pair</b> <b>of</b> things are two things of the same size and shape that are used together or are both part of something, for example, shoes, earrings, or parts of the body. 雙; 對","examples":["...a pair of socks. …一雙襪子","...earrings that cost $142.50 a pair. …價值$142.50一對的耳環。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some objects that have two main parts of the same size and shape are referred to as a <b>pair</b>, for example, <b>a pair of trousers</b> or <b>a pair of scissors</b>. 副; 條 (褲子)","examples":["...a pair of faded jeans. …一條退色的牛仔褲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to two people as a <b>pair</b> when they are standing or walking together or when they have some kind of relationship with each other. (站或走在一起的) 兩人; (有某種關係的) 一對","examples":["A pair of teenage boys were smoking cigarettes. 兩個青少年正在抽菸。","The pair admitted that their three-year-old marriage was going through \"a difficult time.\" 那對夫婦承認他們3年的婚姻正在經歷一個困難時期。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>is paired with</b> another, it is put with it or considered with it. 把…配對","examples":["The trainees will then be paired with experienced managers. 這些實習生之後將被配給有經驗的經理們。"]}]}]},"out":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"出現；向外；在室外；出獄；遙遠地；出海；退潮；指離球門線或終點線的距離；在公共娛樂場所；公開；出聲地；殆盡；直至完成；完全；熄滅；除去；出局"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"從……裡面出去，離開"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熄滅的；盛開的；面市的；出局的；不能被接受的；過時的；不準確的；打算做……的；被公開的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擊倒，擊暈；揭露（某人）是同性戀；熄滅；驅逐；拒絕；解除"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"出路，脫身辦法；（棒球）使球員出局的辦法；在野黨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something is in a particular place and you take it <b>out</b>, you remove it from that place. (拿) 出","examples":["I like the pop you get when you pull out a cork. 我喜歡你拔出瓶塞時弄出的那“砰”的一聲。","He took out his notebook and flipped the pages. 他拿出了筆記本，快速地翻著頁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>out</b> to indicate that you are talking about the situation outside, rather than inside buildings. 在室外","examples":["It's hot out – very hot, very humid. 外面熱烘烘的–非常熱，非常潮溼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>out</b>, you are not at home or not at your usual place of work. 不在 (家或工作地)","examples":["I tried to get in touch with you yesterday evening, but I think you were out. 我昨晚聯絡過你，但你那時可能不在家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>out</b> in a particular place, you mean that they are in a different place, usually one far away. 遠在","examples":["The police tell me they've finished their investigations out there. 警方告訴我他們已經完成了在那邊的調查。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When the sea or tide goes <b>out</b>, the sea moves away from the shore. (潮水) 退去","examples":["The tide was out and they walked among the rock pools. 潮水退了，他們在岩石區的潮水潭間散步。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>out</b> a particular amount of money, you have that amount less than you should or than you did. 缺少 (一筆錢)","examples":["I'm out ten thousand dollars, with nothing to show for it! 我缺1萬美元，沒啥可說的！"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Out</b> is also an adverb. 盛開地","examples":["I usually put it in my diary when I see the wild flowers coming out. 我看到野花盛開時，通常會記在日記本里。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Out</b> is also an adverb. 面市地","examples":["The French edition came out in early 2006. 法文版在2006年初面市。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a light or fire is <b>out</b> or goes <b>out</b>, it is no longer shining or burning. (燈、火等) 熄滅的","examples":["All the lights were out in the house. 房裡所有的燈都熄滅了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If flowers are <b>out</b>, their petals have opened. (花) 盛開的","examples":["Well, the daffodils are out in the gardens and they're always a beautiful show. 哇，花園裡的水仙開了，它們總是一道亮麗的風景。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a book or CD is <b>out</b>, it is available for people to buy. 面市的","examples":["Their new album is out now. 他們的新專輯現已面市。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In a game or sport, if someone is <b>out</b>, they can no longer take part either because they are unable to or because they have been defeated. 不能參賽的; 出局的","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In baseball, a player is <b>out</b> if they do not reach a base safely. When three players on a team are out in an inning, then the team is <b>out</b>. (棒球比賽中) 出局的","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that a proposal or suggestion is <b>out</b>, you mean that it is unacceptable. (提議等) 不能被接受的","examples":["That idea is out, I'm afraid. 那個觀點恐怕是不能接受的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that a particular thing is <b>out</b>, you mean that it is no longer fashionable at the present time. 過時的","examples":["Romance is making a comeback. Reality is out. 浪漫正迴歸；現實已過時。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that a calculation or measurement is <b>out</b>, you mean that it is incorrect. (計算、測量) 不準確的","examples":["When the two ends of the tunnel met in the middle they were only a few inches out. 隧道兩端在中間相接時，只有幾英寸的誤差。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone is <b>out</b> to do something, they intend to do it. 打算做…的","examples":["Most companies these days are just out to make a quick profit. 大多數公司如今只圖快速獲利。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If news or information about something is <b>out</b>, information about it has been made public. 被公開的","examples":["The word is out that she has fled the country. 有訊息說，她已經逃離了那個國家。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people <b>out</b> a public figure or famous person, they reveal that person's homosexuality against their wishes. 揭露 (名人的同性戀身份)","examples":["The New York gay action group \"Queer Nation\" recently outed an American Congressman. 紐約同性戀行動團體“酷兒國度”最近揭露了一位美國國會議員的同性戀身份。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"揭露","examples":["The gay and lesbian rights group, Stonewall, sees outing as completely unhelpful. 男女同性戀權利團體“石牆”認為揭露同性戀身份是完全無用的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>out of</b> a place, you leave it. 從…離開","examples":["She let him out of the house. 她讓他離開了那座房子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you take something <b>out of</b> the container or place where it has been, you remove it so that it is no longer there. 從… (拿) 出來","examples":["I always took my key out of my bag and put it in my pocket. 我總是把鑰匙從包裡拿出來再放進口袋裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you look or shout <b>out of</b> a window, you look or shout away from the room where you are toward the outside. 向…外面 (看或喊)","examples":["He went on staring out of the window. 他依舊凝視著窗外。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>out of</b> the sun, the rain, or the wind, you are sheltered from it. 躲開 (陽光、雨、風等)","examples":["People can keep out of the sun to avoid skin cancer. 人們可以透過躲開陽光來避免患上皮膚癌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something gets <b>out of</b> a situation, especially an unpleasant one, they are then no longer in it. If they keep <b>out of</b> it, they do not start being in it. 擺脫","examples":["In the past army troops have relied heavily on air support to get them out of trouble. 過去，陸軍部隊嚴重依賴空中支援來擺脫困境。","The economy is starting to climb out of recession. 經濟正開始慢慢走出蕭條。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>out of</b> to say that someone leaves an institution. 從…離開","examples":["That is precisely what I came out of college thinking I was supposed to do. 那正是我大學畢業時認為自己應該做的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you are <b>out of</b> range of something, you are beyond the limits of that range. 在…之外","examples":["Shaun was in the bedroom, out of earshot, watching television. 肖恩在臥室裡看電視，聽不到。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>out of</b> to say what feeling or reason causes someone to do something. For example, if you do something <b>out of</b> pity, you do it because you pity someone. 出於","examples":["He took up office out of a sense of duty. 他任職是出於一種責任感。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you get something such as information or work <b>out of</b> someone, you manage to make them give it to you, usually when they are unwilling to give it. 從…那裡 (獲得資訊、工作等)","examples":["\"Where is she being held prisoner?\" I asked. \"Did you get it out of him?\" “她現在被囚禁在哪裡？”我問道。“你從他那兒打聽到了嗎？”"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you get pleasure or an advantage <b>out of</b> something, you get it as a result of being involved with that thing or making use of it. 從…中 (得到快樂、好處等)","examples":["Jenkins hasn't let the pressure take the fun out of the sport. 詹金斯沒有讓壓力奪走這項運動的樂趣。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you are <b>out of</b> something, you no longer have any of it. 沒有","examples":["I can't find the sugar – and we're out of milk. 我找不到糖，而且我們也沒有牛奶了。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something is made <b>out of</b> a particular material, it consists of that material because it has been formed or constructed from it. 用 (製成)","examples":["Would you advise people to make a building out of wood or stone? 你會建議人們用木頭還是石頭造房子？"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>out of</b> to indicate what proportion of a group of things something is true of. For example, if something is true of one <b>out of</b> five things, it is true of one fifth of all things of that kind. 從…中 (挑出一個或一組等)","examples":["Two out of five thought the business would be sold privately on their retirement or death. 2/5的人認為該企業會在他們退休或去世後被私下賣掉。"]}]}]},"order":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"順序，次序；條理；秩序，治安；命令，指示；點餐，訂購；點的餐，訂購的貨物；匯票，送貨單；（社會的）制度，結構；社會階級，階層；種類，水準；（會議的）程式，規程；宗教團體，（尤指）修道會；秘密組織（社團）；聖職，牧師職（orders）；勳位，勳爵士團；（動植物）目；（軍）專用裝備；勳章；裝飾樣式；（數）階；<美>（計算機的）等待佇列"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"命令，指示；訂購，訂貨；點（酒菜等）；排列，整理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in order to</b> achieve a particular thing or <b>in order that</b> something can happen, you do it because you want to achieve that thing. 為了","examples":["Most schools are extremely unwilling to cut down on staff in order to cut costs. 大多數學校都極不願意為了減少開支而裁員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone must be in a particular situation <b>in order to</b> achieve something they want, they cannot achieve that thing if they are not in that situation. (唯有…) 才能","examples":["We need to get rid of the idea that we must be liked all the time in order to be worthwhile. 我們需要擺脫那種必須一直受人愛戴才有價值的觀念。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something must happen <b>in order for</b> something else to happen, the second thing cannot happen if the first thing does not happen. 為了使","examples":["In order for their computers to trace a person's records, they need both the name and address of the individual. 為了使他們的計算機跟蹤某個人的記錄，他們需要這個人的名字和地址。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>on order</b> at a shop or factory has been asked for but has not yet been supplied. 訂購中","examples":["The airlines still have 2,500 new planes on order. 航空公司還有已訂購的2500架新飛機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>to order</b>, you do it whenever you are asked to do it. 按要求","examples":["She now makes wonderful dried flower arrangements to order. 她現在按訂單要求製作精美的乾花插花。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>under orders</b> <b>to</b> do something, you have been told to do it by someone in authority. 奉命","examples":["I am under orders not to discuss his mission or his location with anyone. 我奉命不得跟任何人談論他的任務或去向。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you put or keep something <b>in order</b>, you make sure that it is neat or well organized. 有條理","examples":["Now he has a chance to put his life back in order. 現在，他有機會使自己的生活重新走上正軌。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you think something is <b>in order</b>, you think it should happen or be provided. 應當發生的","examples":["Reforms are clearly in order. 改革顯然是順理成章的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>in the order of</b> or <b>on the order of</b> when mentioning an approximate figure. 大約","examples":["They borrowed something in the order of $10 million. 他們大約借了一千萬美元。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something is <b>in good order</b>, it is in good condition. 處於良好狀態","examples":["The vessel's safety equipment was not in good order. 這艘船的安全裝置出了故障。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"A machine or device that is <b>in working order</b> is functioning properly and is not broken. 處於良好的工作狀態","examples":["Only half of the spacecraft's six science instruments are still in working order. 宇宙飛船的6種科學儀器中，只有一半還能正常運轉。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"A machine or device that is <b>out of order</b> is broken and does not work. 出現故障","examples":["Their phone's out of order. 他們的電話出故障了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that someone or their behaviour is <b>out of order</b>, you mean that their behaviour is unacceptable. 不合常規","examples":["Kent, you're out of order. 肯特，你太過分了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person in authority <b>orders</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, they tell them to do it. 命令","examples":["Williams ordered him to leave. 威廉斯命令他離開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>orders</b> something, they give instructions that it should be done. 下達指示","examples":["The president has ordered a full investigation. 總統已下達指示進行徹底調查。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>order</b> something that you are going to pay for, you ask for it to be brought to you, sent to you, or obtained for you. 訂購; 點 (餐)","examples":["The couple ordered a new set of sterling silver rings from Tiffany for $200 each. 這對夫婦從蒂芙尼珠寶店訂購了一套新的純銀戒指，每隻$200。","The waitress appeared. \"Are you ready to order?\" 女服務員走了過來，“你們準備好點菜了嗎？”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The way that something <b>is ordered</b> is the way that it is organized and structured. 安排","examples":["...a society which is ordered by hierarchy. …一個等級森嚴的社會。","We know the French order things differently. 我們知道法國人處理事情的方式是不同的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority gives you an <b>order</b>, they tell you to do something. 命令","examples":["The activists were shot when they refused to obey an order to halt. 當那些激進分子拒絕聽從要他們停下來的命令時，他們遭到了射擊。","As darkness fell, Clinton gave orders for his men to rest. 夜幕降臨時，克林頓下命令讓自己的人休息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A court <b>order</b> is a legal instruction stating that something must be done. (法院) 決議","examples":["She has decided not to appeal against a court order banning her from keeping animals. 她已決定不對禁止她養動物的判決上訴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>order</b> is a request for something to be brought, made, or obtained for you in return for money. 訂購","examples":["The city is going to place an order for a hundred and eighty-eight buses. 這個城市將下單訂購188輛公交車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>order</b> is what they have asked to be brought, made, or obtained for them in return for money. 所訂的貨","examples":["The waiter returned with their order and Graham signed the bill. 服務員拿著他們點的東西回來，接著格雷厄姆簽了單。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a set of things are arranged or done <b>in</b> a particular <b>order</b>, they are arranged or done so one thing follows another, often according to a particular factor such as importance. 順序","examples":["Write down (in order of priority) the qualities you'd like to have. （按先後順序）寫下你所希望擁有的品質。","Music shops should arrange their recordings in simple alphabetical order, rather than by category. 音像店應按照簡單的字母順序擺放其唱片，而不是按類別。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Order</b> is the situation that exists when everything is in the correct or expected place, or happens at the correct or expected time. 秩序","examples":["The wish to impose order upon confusion is a kind of intellectual instinct. 對混亂進行有序管理的希望是一種高智力的本能。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Order</b> is the situation that exists when people obey the law and do not fight or riot. 治安","examples":["Troops were sent to the islands to restore order last November. 部隊去年11月份被派到島上去恢復治安。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When people talk about a particular <b>order</b>, they mean the way society is organized at a particular time. 社會秩序","examples":["The end of the Cold War has produced the prospect of a new world order based on international co-operation. 冷戰的結束使得基於國際合作的世界新秩序成為可能。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A religious <b>order</b> is a group of monks or nuns who live according to a particular set of rules. 修道會","examples":["...the Benedictine order of monks. …本篤會。"]}]}]},"parent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"父親（或母親）；（動植物的）親代，親本；母公司，總公司；母體，本體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做……的父親（或母親）；為人父母"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>parents</b> are your mother and father. 父母親","examples":["Children need their parents. 孩子們需要父母。","This is where a lot of parents go wrong. 正是在這一點上許多父母都錯了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An organization's <b>parent</b> organization is the organization that created it and usually still controls it. 創始的 (組織); 母 (公司)","examples":["Each unit including the parent company has its own, local management. 每家單位，包括母公司，都有自己的地方管理層。"]}]}]},"park":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公園；自然保護區；（鄉間大宅的）庭園，園林；<英>足球場，橄欖球場；運動場，（尤指）棒球場；專用區，園區；<英>停車場；（汽車）制動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"停車，泊車；存放，寄存； （在某處）坐，站立（park yourself）；<非正式>把……擱置，推遲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>park</b> is a public area of land with grass and trees, usually in a town, where people go in order to relax and enjoy themselves. 公園","examples":["...Central Park. ...中央公園。","...a brisk walk with the dog around the park. …帶著狗在公園裡的一次輕快的散步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a place where a particular activity is carried out as a <b>park</b>. (作為專用場地的) …區; …園","examples":["...a science and technology park. …一個科技園。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>park</b> a vehicle or <b>park</b> somewhere, you drive the vehicle into a position where it can stay for a period of time, and leave it there. 停車","examples":["Greenfield turned into the next side street and parked. 格林菲爾德拐進下一個小巷停了車。","He found a place to park the car. 他找到了一個停車的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>park yourself</b> somewhere, you sit there. 坐下","examples":["Every Friday, I would park myself in front of the TV. 每個週五，我都會坐在電視前。"]}]}]},"party":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聚會，派對；政黨，黨派；<正式>（契約或爭論的）當事人，一方；隊，組，群；<正式>參加者；<非正式>人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式> 盡情歡樂，歡宴"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（紋章）分割開的，分成不同顏色部分的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>party</b> is a political organization whose members have similar aims and beliefs. Usually the organization tries to get its members elected to the legislature of a country. 政黨","examples":["...a member of the Republican Party. …一名共和黨黨員。","...opposition parties. …反對黨們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>party</b> is a social event, often in someone's home, at which people enjoy themselves doing things such as eating, drinking, dancing, talking, or playing games. 派對","examples":["The couple met at a party. 這對夫婦相識於一個派對。","We threw a huge birthday party. 我們舉辦了一次盛大的生日派對。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>party</b> <b>of</b> people is a group of people who are doing something together, for example, travelling together. 群; 隊; 組","examples":["They became separated from their party. 他們跟他們團隊走散了。","...a party of sightseers. …一群遊客。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"One of the people involved in a legal agreement or dispute can be referred to as a particular <b>party</b>. (契約或爭論的) 一方","examples":["It has to be proved that they are the guilty party. 尚需證明他們是有過錯的一方。","...he was the injured party. …他是受害方。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>party</b>, you enjoy yourself doing things such as going out to parties, drinking, dancing, and talking to people. 盡情歡樂","examples":["They come to eat and drink, to swim, to party. 他們來吃飯、喝酒、游泳，盡情歡樂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>is a party to</b> or <b>is party to</b> an action or agreement is involved in it, and therefore partly responsible for it. 參與","examples":["You were the one that brought up the idea of blackmail. I'd never be a party to such a thing. 你是那個提出敲詐主意的人。我從來沒想過參與這種事。"]}]}]},"open":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"開放的，營業的；開著的，敞開的；（身體部位）張開的；露天的，無遮蓋的；開闊的，未圍上的；可通行的，暢通的；伸開的，展開的；坦率的；不保密的，公開的；易受影響的，易受攻擊的；人人可以參加的；（對特定群體）開放的 ；可得到的，可使用的；思想開明的；尚未決定的；（資料夾、文件等）正在使用中的；（勝利者）贏得公開賽的；（票子）未註明旅行日期的；<英>（支票）未簽註的；（數）（集合）開的；（母音）開的；（樂）開放的 ；（電路）開路的，斷路的；（紡織品）鬆散的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開，開啟；開封，開啟；睜開（眼睛），張開（嘴巴）；翻開，展開；開通，開放；開門，營業 ；開業，開幕；（股市）開盤，開市；著手，開始；啟動（計算機程式或檔案）；開立賬戶；通往，通向；展現，出現；使某人更樂意考慮某事；斷開（電路）；暢談"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"戶外，野外；公開，洩露；公開賽（Open）；斷開（電路）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> something such as a door, window, or lid, or if it <b>opens</b>, its position is changed so that it no longer covers a hole or gap. 開啟","examples":["He opened the window and looked out. 他開啟窗戶往外看。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> something such as a bottle, box, parcel, or envelope, you move, remove, or cut part of it so you can take out what is inside. 開封","examples":["I opened the letter. 我拆開了那封信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> something such as a book, an umbrella, or your hand, or if it <b>opens</b>, the different parts of it move away from each other so that the inside of it can be seen. 開啟; 張開","examples":["He opened the heavy Bible. 他翻開了那本厚厚的《聖經》。","The flower opens to reveal a bee. 花開了，露出來一隻蜜蜂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> a computer file, you give the computer an instruction to display it on the screen. 開啟 (電腦檔案)","examples":["Double click on the icon to open the file. 雙擊圖示來開啟檔案。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>open</b> your eyes or your eyes <b>open</b>, you move your eyelids upward, for example, when you wake up, so that you can see. 睜開","examples":["When I opened my eyes I saw Melissa standing at the end of my bed. 我睜開雙眼時，看見梅利莎站在我的床腳。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> your arms, you stretch them wide apart in front of you, usually in order to put them around someone. 張開 (雙臂)","examples":["She opened her arms and gave me a big hug. 她張開雙臂，緊緊地擁抱了我。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> your shirt or coat, you undo the buttons or pull down the zipper. 解開 (衣服)","examples":["I opened my coat and let him see the belt. 我解開外套，讓他看了看腰帶。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If people <b>open</b> something such as a blocked road or a border, or if it <b>opens</b>, people can then pass along it or through it. 開放 (被封鎖的道路、邊界等)","examples":["The rebels have opened the road from Monrovia to the Ivory Coast. 叛亂分子開放了從蒙羅維亞到象牙海岸的公路。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When a shop, office, or public building <b>opens</b> or <b>is opened</b>, its doors are unlocked and the public can go in. 使開門營業; 開門營業","examples":["Banks closed on Friday afternoon and did not open again until Monday morning. 銀行星期五下午關門，直到星期一早上才會再開門營業。","I'd been waiting for him to open the shop. 我一直在等他開門營業。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When a public building, factory, or company <b>opens</b> or when someone <b>opens</b> it, it starts operating for the first time. 使開張; 開張","examples":["The original station opened in 1954. 原來的車站是1954年啟用的。","The complex opens to the public tomorrow. 該建築群明天向公眾開放。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"To <b>open</b> opportunities or possibilities means the same as to <b>open</b> them <b>up</b>. 提供 (機會)","examples":["The Chief of Naval Operations wants to open opportunities for women in the navy. 海軍作戰部部長想給海軍中的女性提供機會。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something such as a meeting or series of talks <b>opens</b>, or if someone <b>opens</b> it, it begins. 召開; 開始","examples":["...an emergency session of the Russian Parliament due to open later this morning. …將於今天上午晚些時候開始的一次俄羅斯議會緊急會議。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If an event such as a meeting or discussion <b>opens</b> <b>with</b> a particular activity, that activity is the first thing that happens or is dealt with. You can also say that someone such as a speaker or singer <b>opens</b> <b>by</b> doing a particular thing. (活動或活動表演者) 以…開始; 開始","examples":["The service opened with a hymn. 禮拜式以唱讚美詩開始。","I opened by saying, \"Honey, you look sensational.\" 我以這句話作為開場白：“寶貝，你看起來真是棒極了！”"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>open</b> an account with a bank or a commercial organization, you begin to use their services. 開立 (賬戶)","examples":["He tried to open an account at the branch of his bank nearest to his workplace. 他試圖在離他工作地點最近的銀行分行開立賬戶。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 開著的","examples":["...an open window. …一扇開著的窗戶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 開啟的","examples":["...an open bottle of milk. …一瓶開啟的牛奶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 張開的","examples":["Without warning, Bardo smacked his fist into his open hand. 毫無預警地，巴多用拳頭啪地猛擊了他張開的手。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 睜著的","examples":["As soon as he saw that her eyes were open he sat up. 一看見她眼睛睜著，他馬上坐了起來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 解開的","examples":["The top can be worn buttoned up or open over a T-shirt. 這件上衣可以繫上釦子或不繫釦子套在T恤衫的外面穿。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 暢通的","examples":["We were part of an entire regiment that had nothing else to do but to keep that motorway open. 我們是整個團的一部分，這個團無其他任務,只是保證公路暢通。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"An <b>open</b> area is a large area that does not have many buildings or trees in it. 開闊的","examples":["Officers will also continue their search of nearby open ground. 警察們也會繼續搜尋附近的開闊地。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"An <b>open</b> structure or object is not covered or enclosed. 無遮蓋的","examples":["Don't leave a child alone in a room with an open fire. 別把小孩單獨放在有明火的房間裡。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Open</b> is also an adjective. 營業中的","examples":["The gallery is open Monday through Friday, 9 am to 6 pm. 美術館的開放時間為週一到週五，上午9點到下午6點。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a factory or company remains <b>open</b>, it continues to operate. 運營中的","examples":["The government says it's no longer willing to spend $170 million a month to keep the pits open. 政府宣稱將不願再每月花費1.7億美元維持這些礦井的運轉。","...any operating subsidy required to keep the airline open. …維持航空公司執行所需要的任何運營補貼。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you describe a person or their character as <b>open</b>, you mean they are honest and do not want or try to hide anything or to deceive anyone. 坦誠的","examples":["He had always been open with her and she always felt she would know if he lied. 他對她一向很坦誠。而她也一直覺得如果他撒謊了，她是會知道的。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you describe a situation, attitude, or way of behaving as <b>open</b>, you mean it is not kept hidden or secret. 公然的; 公開的","examples":["The action is an open violation of the Vienna Convention. 這次行動是對《維也納公約》的公然違犯。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you are <b>open to</b> suggestions or ideas, you are ready and willing to consider or accept them. 願意接受的","examples":["They are open to suggestions on how working conditions might be improved. 他們願意接受有關工作條件如何改善的建議。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you say that a system, person, or idea is <b>open to</b> something such as abuse or criticism, you mean they might receive abuse or criticism because of their qualities, effects, or actions. 容易受到 (辱罵、批評) 的","examples":["The system, though well-meaning, is open to abuse. 儘管這個制度立意很好，卻容易遭到濫用。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you say that a fact or question is <b>open</b> <b>to</b> debate, interpretation, or discussion, you mean that people are uncertain whether it is true, what it means, or what the answer is. 有 (討論、解釋) 的餘地","examples":["Her interpretation of the facts may be open to doubt. 她對事實的解釋可能有待質疑。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You can use <b>open</b> to describe something that anyone is allowed to take part in or accept. 對公眾開放的","examples":["It's an open meeting, everybody's invited. 這是一個開放的會議，誰來都歡迎。","...an open invitation. …一個公開的邀請。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If something such as an offer or job is <b>open</b>, it is available for someone to accept or apply for. (報價) 可用的; (職位) 空缺的","examples":["The offer will remain open until further notice. 該報價將一直有效，直到另有通知。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If an opportunity or choice <b>is open to</b> you, you are able to do a particular thing if you choose to. 可供…利用的","examples":["There are a wide range of career opportunities open to young people. 有廣泛的求職機會可供年輕人選擇。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Open up</b> means the same as <b>open</b>. 同(open)","examples":["He opened up a cage and lifted out a 6ft python. 他開啟一個籠子，提起了一條6英尺長的蟒蛇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Open out</b> means the same as <b>open</b>. 同(open)","examples":["Keith took a map from the dashboard and opened it out on his knees. 基思從儀表板上拿了張地圖，攤開放在了膝蓋上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Open up</b> means the same as <b>open</b>. 同(open)","examples":["As rescue workers opened up roads today, it became apparent that some small towns were totally devastated. 今天營救人員清除路障時發現，顯然有些小鎮已完全淪為廢墟。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Open out</b> means the same as <b>open</b>. 同(open)","examples":["...narrow streets opening out into charming squares. …通向迷人的廣場的狹窄街道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place <b>opens</b> <b>into</b> another, larger place, you can move from one directly into the other. 通向 (更大的地方)","examples":["The corridor opened into a low smoky room. 這條走廊通向一個既低矮又煙霧瀰漫的房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"On the stock exchange, the price at which currencies, shares, or commodities <b>open</b> is their value at the start of that day's trading. 開盤","examples":["Gold declined $2 in Zurich to open at $385.50. 蘇黎世證券交易所的金價跌了$2，以$385.50開盤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a film, play, or other public event <b>opens</b>, it begins to be shown, be performed, or take place for a limited period of time. 開演","examples":["A photographic exhibition opens at the Smithsonian on Wednesday. 一個攝影展週三在史密森尼博物館開幕。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"運營的開始","examples":["He was there, though, for the official opening. 然而，他到了那兒是為了參加正式開幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"坦率","examples":["...a relationship based on honesty and openness. …一種在誠實、坦率的基礎上建立起來的關係。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"公開性","examples":["...the new climate of political openness. …政治透明的新氣象。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"開始","examples":["...a statement issued at the opening of the talks. …會談開始時發表的一項宣告。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"開幕","examples":["He is due to attend the opening of the Asian Games on Saturday. 他定於星期六出席亞運會的開幕式。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in the open</b> or <b>out in the open</b>, you do it outdoors rather than in a house or other building. 在戶外","examples":["Many are sleeping in the open because they have no shelter. 許多人因為沒有棲身之所而睡在戶外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an attitude or situation is <b>in the open</b> or <b>out in the open</b>, people know about it and it is no longer kept secret. 公開的","examples":["They had advised us to keep it a secret, but we wanted it out in the open. 他們曾建議我們對其保密，但我們卻想將它公之於眾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>wide open</b>, it is open to its full extent. 大開的","examples":["The child had left the inner door wide open. 這個孩子讓裡面的門大開著。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a competition, race, or election is <b>wide open</b>, you mean that anyone could win it, because there is no competitor who seems to be much better than the others. 勝負不確定的","examples":["The competition has been thrown wide open by the absence of the world champion. 世界冠軍的缺席使這場比賽變得勝負難定。"]}]}]},"paper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紙；報紙；（工作、學習或個人的）資料，檔案（papers）；證明，證件（如護照、身份證等）（papers）；政府報告，官方政策檔案；<英>考試，答卷；（研究）論文，（學術）講話；<美>（學校課程的）學期論文；牆紙，桌布；有價證券；手紙，衛生紙；<俚>（劇院等娛樂場所的）免費入場券"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用牆紙裱糊（牆壁）；用牆紙覆蓋（洞，汙點）（paper sth. over）；掩蓋（尷尬問題）（paper sth. over）；<俚>發免費入場券使（劇院）滿座"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紙做的，紙質的；書面的，印刷的；紙上的，有名無實的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Paper</b> is a material that you write on or wrap things with. The pages of this book are made of paper. 紙","examples":["He wrote his name down on a piece of paper for me. 他把他的名字寫在一張紙上給我。","...a paper bag. …一個紙袋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>paper</b> is a newspaper. 報紙","examples":["I might get a paper in the town. 我或許能在城裡買到一份報紙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to newspapers in general as <b>the paper</b> or <b>the papers</b>. (總稱) 報紙","examples":["You can't believe everything you read in the paper. 你不能相信在報紙上讀到的所有內容。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>papers</b> are sheets of paper with information on them that you might keep in a safe place at home. 資料","examples":["After her death, her papers – including unpublished articles and correspondence – were deposited at the library. 她死後，她的資料–包括未發表的文章和信函–都被存放在圖書館裡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>papers</b> are official documents, such as your passport or identity card, that prove who you are or that give you official permission to do something. 身份證件; 證明","examples":["A young Moroccan stopped by police refused to show his papers. 一個被警察攔住的摩洛哥青年拒絕出示他的身份證件。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>paper</b> is a long, formal piece of writing about an academic subject. 論文","examples":["He just published a paper in the journal Nature analysing the fires. 他剛剛在《自然》雜誌上發表了一篇分析火災的論文。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>paper</b> is an essay written by a student. (學生) 作文","examples":["...the ten common errors that appear most frequently in student papers. …最常出現在學生作文中的10個錯誤。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>paper</b> prepared by a government or a committee is a report on a question they have been considering or a set of proposals for changes in the law. (政府) 檔案","examples":["...a new government paper on electoral reform. …一份關於選舉改革的新的政府檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Paper</b> agreements, qualifications, or profits are ones that are stated by official documents to exist, although they may not really be effective or useful. (協議、資格或利益等) 書面的","examples":["They expressed deep mistrust of the paper promises. 他們對書面的承諾表示出十分的不信任。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>paper</b> a wall, you put wallpaper on it. 給…貼牆紙","examples":["We papered all four bedrooms. 我們給4個臥室都貼了牆紙。","We have papered this bedroom in softest grey. 我們給這間臥室貼上了最柔和的灰色牆紙。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you put your thoughts down <b>on paper</b>, you write them down. 在紙上","examples":["It is important to get something down on paper. 重要的是要把一些事情寫在紙上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something seems to be the case <b>on paper</b>, it seems to be the case from what you read or hear about it, but it may not really be the case. 在理論上","examples":["On paper, their country is a multi-party democracy. 從理論上講，他們的國家是一個多黨派民主國家。"]}]}]},"pen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"筆，鋼筆；（圈養動物用的）圍欄，圈；（計算機上使用的）電子筆；<美>監獄；<英，非正式>處罰，（尤指足球的）點球；墨水；雌天鵝；（動）（槍烏賊的）羽狀殼；（西印度群島）農莊，大農場；（潛艇等戰艦的）隱蔽塢，掩藏塢；國際筆會（國際詩人，劇作家，編輯，散文家和小說家協會）（PEN）；秘魯新索爾（PEN）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"寫，撰寫；（把……）關起來，圈起來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pen</b> is a long thin object which you use to write in ink. 鋼筆","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pen</b> is a small area with a fence around it in which farm animals are kept for a short time. (臨時圈養牲畜的) 圈","examples":["...a holding pen for sheep. …一個羊群候宰圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a female swan 母天鵝","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"penitentiary的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>pens</b> a letter, article, or book, they write it. 撰寫","examples":["I really intended to pen this letter to you early this morning. 我本來真的打算今天一大早就給你撰寫這封信的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people or animals <b>are penned</b> somewhere or <b>are penned up</b>, they are forced to remain in a very small area. 關 (人或動物)","examples":["The cattle were penned for the night. 這頭牛晚上被關了起來。","The animals were penned up in cages. 這些動物被關在籠子裡了。"]}]}]},"past":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過去的，昔日的；剛過去的，剛結束的；完成的，結束的；（語法）過去時的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"過去，昔日（the past）；往事，經歷；（語法）過去時，（動詞的）過去式（the past）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"晚於，在…...之後；在…...的更遠處；經過，越過；超出，超過"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"從一側到另一側，經過；（時間）過去，逝去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The past</b> is the time before the present, and the things that have happened. 過去","examples":["In the past, about a third of the babies born to women with diabetes died. 在過去，患有糖尿病的婦女生的嬰兒中大約有三分之一都死了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>past</b> consists of all the things that you have done or that have happened to you. 經歷","examples":["...revelations about his past. …關於他的過往經歷的揭露。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of <b>living in the past</b>, you mean that they think too much about the past or believe that things are the same as they were in the past. 活在過去","examples":["What was the point in living in the past, thinking about what had or had not happened? 活在過去有什麼意義，思考已經發生的或者沒有發生的事情？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Past</b> events and things happened or existed before the present time. 以前的","examples":["I knew from past experience that alternative therapies could help. 我知道根據以前的經驗其他的治療方法可能有效。","...a return to the turbulence of past centuries. …回到過去幾個中世紀的動盪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>past</b> to talk about a period of time that has just finished. For example, if you talk about the <b>past five years</b>, you mean the period of five years that has just finished. 剛過去的","examples":["Most stores have remained closed for the past three days. 在剛過去的3天裡大多數商店一直關著門。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>past</b> when you are stating a time that is thirty minutes or less after a particular hour. For example, if it is <b>twenty past</b> six, it is twenty minutes after six o'clock. (指鐘點) 過","examples":["It's ten past eleven. 11:10了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is <b>past</b> a particular time, it is later than that time. 晚於","examples":["It was past midnight. 過了午夜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you go <b>past</b> someone or something, you go near them and keep moving, so that they are then behind you. 經過","examples":["I dashed past him and out of the door. 我飛奔著經過他，跑出門外。","A steady procession of people filed past the coffin. 穩步前行的人們排成一行，經過靈柩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you look or point <b>past</b> a person or thing, you look or point at something behind them. 越過","examples":["She stared past Christine at the bed. 她越過克里斯蒂娜盯著那張床。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>past</b> a place, it is on the other side of it. 在…另一側","examples":["Go north on I-15 to the exit just past Barstow. 順著I-15公路向北走，出口就在巴斯托的另一側。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>past</b> a particular point or stage, they are no longer at that point or stage. 超過 (某一點或階段)","examples":["He was well past retirement age. 他大大超過了退休年齡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Past</b> is also an adverb. 過了","examples":["I have my lunch at half past. 我半點的時候吃午餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Past</b> is also an adverb. 經過","examples":["An ambulance drove past. 一輛救護車駛了過去。"]}]}]},"payment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"支付款項，支付額；付款，支付；報答，報復"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>payment</b> is an amount of money that is paid to someone, or the act of paying this money. 支付的款項; 支付","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Payment</b> is the act of paying money to someone or of being paid. 支付","examples":["He had sought to obtain payment of a sum which he had claimed was owed to him. 他曾試圖獲得一筆他聲稱是欠他的錢。"]}]}]},"pencil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鉛筆；石墨芯，類似石墨芯的東西；化妝筆；筆狀物；一束光"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用鉛筆寫（或畫、塗色）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用鉛筆寫（或畫、描、記）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pencil</b> is an object that you write or draw with. It consists of a thin piece of wood with a rod of a black or coloured substance through the middle. If you write or draw something <b>in pencil</b>, you do it using a pencil. 鉛筆","examples":["I found a pencil and some blank paper in her desk. 我在她的書桌裡找到了一支鉛筆和一些白紙。"]}]}]},"part":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"部分；某物的部分（區域性）；（書、戲劇、電視劇等的）部，篇，集；（動植物的）器官，部位；部件，零件；成員，參與人員；（世界、國家或城鎮等的）區域，地區；（頭髮的）分縫；（角色的）臺詞和動作，角色；（在活動或事件中的）作用；（樂器或聲音的）聲部，音部；（等）份；<古>能力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）分開，（使）分離；分別；分手；放棄，移交；給（頭髮）分縫"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"既有……又有……（part sth., part sth.）；不完全地，部分地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"部分的，不完全的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>part of</b> something is one of the pieces, sections, or elements that it consists of. 部分","examples":["I like that part of Cape Town. 我喜歡開普敦的那個地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>part</b> for a machine or vehicle is one of the smaller pieces that is used to make it. 零件","examples":["...spare parts for military equipment. …軍事裝置的備用零件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>part</b> when you are talking about the proportions of substances in a mixture. For example, if you are told to use five <b>parts</b> water to one <b>part</b> paint, the mixture should contain five times as much water as paint. (等分中的) 一份","examples":["Use turpentine and linseed oil, three parts to two. 用松節油和亞麻籽油，三份松節油兌兩份亞麻籽油。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>part</b> in a play or film is one of the roles in it which an actor or actress can perform. 角色","examples":["Alf Sjoberg offered her a large part in the play he was directing. 阿爾夫•肖博格在他執導的戲裡給了她一個重要角色。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>part in</b> something that happens is your involvement in it. 參與","examples":["If only he could conceal his part in the accident. 如果他能掩蓋他在那次事故中有份參與就好了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>part of</b> a group or organization, they belong to it or are included in it. 成員","examples":["Annie had never been part of the in-crowd. 安妮從未成為那個小圈子的一員。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>part</b> in someone's hair is the line running from the front to the back of their head where their hair lies in different directions. 分發線","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Part of</b> something is some of it. 一部分","examples":["It was a very severe accident and he lost part of his foot. 那是一起嚴重的事故，他的一隻腳殘了。","Perry spent part of his childhood in Canada. 佩裡在加拿大度過了童年的部分時光。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>part</b> one thing, <b>part</b> another, you mean that it is to some extent the first thing and to some extent the second thing. 一半","examples":["The television producer today has to be part news person, part educator. 今天的電視製作人必須一半是新聞人，一半是教育者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>plays</b> a large or important <b>part</b> <b>in</b> an event or situation, they are very involved in it and have an important effect on what happens. 起作用","examples":["These days work plays an important part in a single woman's life. 現今，工作在一個單身婦女的生活中起著重要作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take part in</b> an activity, you do it together with other people. 參加","examples":["Thousands of students have taken part in demonstrations. 成千上萬的學生參加了遊行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> your <b>part</b>, you do something that, to a small or limited extent, helps to achieve something. 盡你的本分; 做你應該做的","examples":["Each of you is going to have to do your part in keeping the community crime-free. 你們每一個人都要儘自己的本分，讓社群內沒有犯罪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you are describing people's thoughts or actions, you can say <b>for</b> her <b>part</b> or <b>for</b> my <b>part</b>, for example, to introduce what a particular person thinks or does. 就某人而言","examples":["For my part, I feel elated and close to tears. 就我而言，我感覺興高采烈，都快哭出來了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you talk about a feeling or action <b>on</b> someone's <b>part</b>, you are referring to something that they feel or do. 某人所做的","examples":["...techniques on their part to keep us from knowing exactly what's going on. …他們那些防止我們確切瞭解事態進展的技術。","There is no need for any further instructions on my part. 我不需要做任何進一步的指示。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>in part</b> to indicate that something exists or happens to some extent but not completely. 在某種程度上","examples":["The levels of blood glucose depend in part on what you eat and when you eat. 血糖水平在一定程度上依賴於你吃什麼及什麼時候吃。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things that are next to each other <b>part</b> or if you <b>part</b> them, they move in opposite directions, so that there is a space between them. 分開","examples":["Her lips parted as if she were about to take a deep breath. 她張開了嘴，好像要做深呼吸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>part</b> your hair in the middle or at one side, you make it lie in two different directions so that there is a straight line running from the front of your head to the back. 把 (頭髮) 分開","examples":["Picking up a brush, Joanna parted her hair. 拿起一把刷子，喬安娜把頭髮分開了。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two people <b>part</b>, or if one person <b>parts from</b> another, they leave each other. 分手","examples":["He gave me the envelope and we parted. 他把信封給我，我們就分手了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are parted from</b> someone you love, you are prevented from being with them. 被分開","examples":["I don't believe Laverne and I will ever be parted. 我相信拉弗內和我永遠都不會分開。"]}]}]},"piano":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋼琴（pianoforte 的簡稱）；（Piano）人名，法、意、葡譯作皮亞諾"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（音樂記譜用語）柔和的（常縮略為 p）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（音樂記譜用語）輕柔地（常縮略為 p）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>piano</b> is a large musical instrument with a row of black and white keys. When you press these keys with your fingers, little hammers hit wire strings inside the piano which vibrate to produce musical notes. 鋼琴","examples":["I taught myself how to play the piano. 我自學彈鋼琴。","He started piano lessons at the age of 7. 他7歲開始學鋼琴。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"adj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(to be performed) softly (演奏)輕輕地 ( symbol: )","examples":[]}]}]},"person":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人；自然人，法人；（用於不知其人是誰時）某人，傢伙；（語法）人稱；（用於複合詞）從事……工作（或擔任……職務）的人；人品，為人；身體，人身；喜愛（某事物）的人；（戲劇或故事中的）人物，角色；（基督教神學）（聖父、聖子、聖靈三位一體的）位；容貌，外表"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>person</b> is a man, woman, or child. 人","examples":["At least one person died and several others were injured. 至少一人死亡，另有幾人受傷。","They were both lovely, friendly people. 他們倆都是可愛、友好的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Persons</b> is used as the plural of <b>person</b> in formal, legal, and technical writing. (person)的複數形式，用於正式、法律和技術文體中","examples":["...removal of the right of accused persons to remain silent. …對被告人沉默權的剝奪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about someone <b>as a person</b>, you are considering them from the point of view of their real nature. (從其真正本質出發而言的) 人","examples":["Robin didn't feel good about herself as a person. 羅賓對她自己的為人感覺不佳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>person</b> is your body. 身體","examples":["The suspect had refused to give any details of his identity and had carried no documents on his person. 嫌疑犯拒絕交代任何有關他身份的細節，身上也沒帶任何證件。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In grammar, we use the term <b>first person</b> when referring to \"I\" and \"we,\" <b>second person</b> when referring to \"you,\" and <b>third person</b> when referring to \"he,\" \"she,\" \"it,\" \"they,\" and all other noun groups. <b>Person</b> is also used like this when referring to the verb forms that go with these pronouns and noun groups. (語法中的) 人稱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in person</b>, you do it yourself rather than letting someone else do it for you. 親自","examples":["You must collect the mail in person and take along some form of identification. 你必須親自去取郵件，並帶上某種身份證明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you meet, hear, or see someone <b>in person</b>, you are in the same place as them, rather than, for example, speaking to them on the telephone, writing to them, or seeing them on television. 當面; 本人","examples":["It was the first time she had seen him in person. 這是她第一次見到他本人。"]}]}]},"people":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人，人類；人們，大家（the people）；平民，老百姓（the people）；民族，種族（peoples）；（具有共同品質、興趣等的）人員，團體；與某人有聯絡的人們（one's people）；<美，非正式>各位，諸位；<美>（審判中的）公訴人（the People）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"居住在，定居於；充滿，充斥著（某種型別的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>People</b> are men, women, and children. <b>People</b> is normally used as the plural of , instead of \"persons.\" 人們","examples":["Millions of people have lost their homes. 數百萬人失去了家園。","...the people of Angola. …安哥拉人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The people</b> is sometimes used to refer to ordinary men and women, in contrast to the government or the military. 人民","examples":["...the will of the people. …人民的意願。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>people</b> is all the men, women, and children of a particular country or race. 國民; 民族","examples":["...the native peoples of Central and South America. …中美洲和南美洲的各本土民族。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or country <b>is peopled by</b> a particular group of people, that group of people live there. 居住","examples":["It was peopled by a fiercely independent race of peace-loving Buddhists. 那裡由極其獨立的一群熱愛和平的佛教徒居住著。"]}]}]},"pet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寵物；寵兒，得寵的人；<英，非正式>寶貝，親愛的；生氣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撫摸；（男女間）親吻，愛撫；寵愛；生氣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很喜歡的，鍾愛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pet</b> is an animal that you keep in your home to give you company and pleasure. 寵物","examples":["It is plainly cruel to keep turtles as pets. 把海龜當寵物養顯然是殘忍的。","...a bachelor living alone in a house with his pet dog. …一個與寵物狗獨住一棟房子的單身漢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a fit of sulkiness, esp at what is felt to be a slight; pique 慍怒; 不開心","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>pet</b> theory, project, or subject is one that they particularly support or like. 鍾愛的 (理論、專案、學科等)","examples":["He would not stand by and let his pet project be killed off. 他不會袖手旁觀，任由自己鍾愛的專案被否決。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pet</b> a person or animal, you touch them in an affectionate way. 愛撫","examples":["The policeman reached down and petted the wolfhound. 警察伸出手，摸了摸那條獵狼犬。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to treat (a person, animal, etc) as a pet; pamper 寵愛","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to take offence; sulk 生氣","examples":[]}]}]},"pie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餡餅，果餡餅；肉餡餅，蔬菜餡餅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pie</b> consists of fruit, meat, or vegetables baked in pastry. 餡餅","examples":["...a slice of apple pie. …一片蘋果餡餅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a very small former Indian coin worth one third of a pice 舊時，印度的小硬幣，值三分之一印度銅幣","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a book for finding the Church service for any particular day 查詢在任何特定日子的禮拜儀式的書 (Also pye)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to be keen on 愛好","examples":[]}]}]},"pass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"經過，穿過；傳遞，傳送；傳（球）；（所有權）轉移，轉讓；（狀態）轉變；（數量上）超過，突破；（時間）流逝；度過，消磨；透過（考試、課程等）；批准（法律或議案）；發生，說過；略過（問題）；排洩；使（貨幣等）流通；結束，停止；拒絕邀請（提議）；宣佈，宣告；（紙牌等遊戲中）不叫，過"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"出入證，通行證；及格，合格；傳球；山道，山口；階段，步驟；（計算機）一次瀏覽，一次掃描；越過；變戲法；（擊劍中的）戳刺；（不好的）境遇，處境；（橋牌）不叫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>pass</b> someone or something means to go past them without stopping. 經過","examples":["As she passed the library door, the telephone began to ring. 她經過圖書館門口時，電話開始響鈴了。","Jane stood aside to let her pass. 簡站到一邊讓她過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b> something through, over, or around something else, you move or push it through, over, or around that thing. 穿; 越; 繞","examples":["She passed the needle through the rough cloth, back and forth. 她用針在那塊粗布上來來回回地穿進穿出。","\"I don't understand,\" the detective mumbled, passing a hand through his hair. “我不明白，”那個偵探嘟囔著，同時用一隻手捋頭髮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b> something <b>to</b> someone, you take it in your hand and give it to them. 傳遞","examples":["Ken passed the books to Sergeant Wong. 肯把那些書遞給了黃巡佐。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>passes</b> or <b>is passed</b> <b>from</b> one person <b>to</b> another, the second person then has it instead of the first. 轉給","examples":["His mother's small estate had passed to him after her death. 他母親死後，微薄的財產轉給了他。","These powers were eventually passed to municipalities. 這些權力最終轉給了市政當局。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b> information <b>to</b> someone, you give it to them because it concerns them. 傳達","examples":["Officials failed to pass vital information to their superiors. 官員們沒能把重要情報傳達給他們的上司。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b>, or <b>pass</b> the ball <b>to</b> someone on your team in a game such as football or basketball, you throw it to them. 傳 (球) 給","examples":["Your partner should then pass the ball back to you. 你的夥伴該把球回傳給你。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b> a period of time in a particular way, you spend it in that way. 消磨 (時間)","examples":["The children passed the time playing in the streets. 孩子們在街上玩耍消磨時間。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If an amount <b>passes</b> a particular total or level, it becomes greater than that total or level. 超過","examples":["They became the first company in their field to pass the $2 billion turn-over mark. 他們成為他們那個領域第一家市場營業額超過$20億的公司。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone or something <b>passes</b> a test, they are considered to be of an acceptable standard. 透過 (考試)","examples":["Kevin has just passed his driving test. 凱文剛剛透過駕駛考試。","...new drugs which have passed early tests to show that they are safe. …已經透過了早期試驗顯示是安全的新藥。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>passes</b> a person or thing, they declare that they are of an acceptable standard or have reached an acceptable standard. 宣佈…合格","examples":["Several popular beaches were found unfit for swimming although the government passed them last year. 好幾個人氣很旺的海灘被發現不適合游泳，儘管去年官方宣佈他們都合格。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When people in authority <b>pass</b> a new law or a proposal, they formally agree to it or approve it. 批准; 認可","examples":["The Estonian parliament has passed a resolution declaring the republic fully independent. 愛沙尼亞議會已經批准了一項決議，宣佈該共和國完全獨立。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When a judge <b>passes</b> sentence on someone, he or she says what their punishment will be. 宣佈 (判決)","examples":["Passing sentence, the judge said it all had the appearance of a con trick. 宣判時，法官說這個事情具有一個騙局所有的全部外在形式。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>pass</b> comment or <b>pass</b> a comment, you say something. 評論","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>passes</b> in a particular direction, they move in that direction. 穿過","examples":["He passed through the doorway into the kitchen. 他穿過門道去廚房。","He passed down the tunnel. 他穿過隧道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a road or pipe <b>passes</b> along a particular route, it goes along that route. (沿某路線) 穿過","examples":["A dirt road passes through the town. 一條土路穿過那座城鎮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a period of time <b>passes</b>, it happens and finishes. (時間) 消逝","examples":["He couldn't imagine why he had let so much time pass without contacting her. 他想像不出為什麼他這麼長時間沒跟她聯絡。","As the years passed he felt trapped by certain realities of marriage. 隨著歲月的流逝，他感到受困於某些婚姻的現實情況。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pass through</b> a stage of development or a period of time, you experience it. 經歷","examples":["The country was passing through a grave crisis. 那個國家正經歷著一場嚴重的危機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>passes for</b> or <b>passes as</b> something that they are not, they are accepted as that thing or mistaken for that thing. 被當作","examples":["Children's toy guns now look so realistic that they can often pass for the real thing. 孩子們的玩具槍現在看起來那麼真以至於常可被當作真槍。","It is doubtful whether Ted, even with his fluent French, passed for one of the locals. 讓人存疑的是特德——即使法語說得很流利——能否被人當作一名當地人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone makes you an offer or asks you a question and you say that you will <b>pass</b> <b>on</b> it, you mean that you do not want to accept or answer it now. 對…不接受; 對…不予理會","examples":["I think I'll pass on the swimming. 我想我不會去游泳。","\"You can join us if you like.\" Brad shook his head. \"I'll pass, thanks.\" “如果喜歡，你可以加入我們。”布拉德搖搖頭說。“我不去了，謝謝。”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In some card games and other games, if you <b>pass</b>, you choose not to play at that stage in the game. 不出牌","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pass on</b> means the same as <b>pass</b>. 傳達","examples":["I do not know what to do with the information if I cannot pass it on. 如果無法傳送出去，我不知道該拿這情報怎麼辦。","From time to time he passed on confidential information to him. 他不時地傳送機密情報給他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pass</b> in an examination, test, or course is a successful result in it. 考試透過","examples":["He's been allowed to re-take the exam, and he's going to get a pass. 他已經被允許再參加一次這個考試，他將得到考試透過的結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pass</b> is a document that allows you to do something. 通行證; 許可證","examples":["I got myself a pass into the barracks. 我搞到一張進兵營的通行證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pass</b> in a game such as football or basketball is an act of throwing the ball to someone on your team. 傳球","examples":["Hirst rolled a short pass to Merson. 赫斯特給默森傳了個短球。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pass</b> is a narrow path or route between mountains. 山坳通道","examples":["The monastery is in a remote mountain pass. 那僧院在一個偏遠的山坳通道處。"]}]}]},"pig":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豬；<非正式>令人討厭的人，豬玀；<俚>警官（侮辱性用語）；<英>難辦的事，不愉快的事；<非正式>貪吃的人；生鐵塊，生鉛錠；清管器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>狼吞虎嚥；<非正式>像豬一樣擠在一起；（母豬）生小豬；（在石油或天然氣管道中）操作清管器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pig</b> is a pink or black animal with short legs and not much hair on its skin. Pigs are often kept on farms for their meat, which is called pork, ham, or bacon. 豬","examples":["...the grunting of the pigs. …豬的哼哼聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>pig</b>, you think that they are unpleasant in some way, especially that they are greedy or unkind. 豬 (用來比喻貪婪、刻薄的人)","examples":["These guys destroyed the company. They're all a bunch of greedy pigs. 這些傢伙毀了公司。他們是一群貪婪的豬。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>when pigs fly</b>\" after someone has said that something might happen, you are emphasizing that you think it is very unlikely. 等到猴年馬月","examples":["When would they be hired again? Perhaps, as the saying goes, when pigs fly. 他們什麼時候會被重新僱用？也許正像俗話說的，等到猴年馬月吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is</b> <b>making a pig of</b> <b>themselves</b>, you are criticizing them for eating a very large amount at one meal. 狼吞虎嚥","examples":["I'm afraid I made a pig of myself at dinner. 恐怕晚飯我是狼吞虎嚥了。"]}]}]},"picture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖片，繪畫；照片；肖像；（電視或電影的）影象；情況，局面；腦海中的情景，形象；電影院（the pictures）；影片；描述；酷似的人（或物）；典範"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"想象；繪畫，拍攝；描繪；（在報紙、雜誌等上）登載……的照片（或圖片）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>picture</b> consists of lines and shapes that are drawn, painted, or printed on a surface and show a person, thing, or scene. 圖畫","examples":["...drawing a small picture with coloured chalk. …用彩色粉筆畫一幅小畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>picture</b> is a photograph. 照片","examples":["The tourists have nothing to do but take pictures of each other. 遊客們無事可做，只有相互拍照。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Television <b>pictures</b> are the scenes that you see on a television screen. (電視) 畫面","examples":["...heartrending television pictures of human suffering. …令人心碎的人類受難的電視畫面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a film as a <b>picture</b>. 電影","examples":["...a director of epic action pictures. …一位大製作動作片的導演。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have a <b>picture</b> of something in your mind, you have a clear idea or memory of it in your mind as if you were actually seeing it. (頭腦中的) 影像","examples":["We are just trying to get our picture of the whole afternoon straight. 我們正努力在腦海中理清整個下午的情景。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>picture</b> of something is a description of it or an indication of what it is like. 描述","examples":["I'll try and give you a better picture of what the boys do. 我會盡力給你一個關於這些男孩所作事情的更好描述。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When you refer to the <b>picture</b> in a particular place, you are referring to the situation there. 局面; 情況","examples":["It's a similar picture across the border in Ethiopia. 在邊界那邊的衣索比亞也是類似的局面。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>be pictured</b> somewhere, for example, in a newspaper or magazine, means to appear in a photograph or picture. (在報紙、雜誌上) 登載照片","examples":["The golfer is pictured on many of the front pages, kissing his trophy as he holds it aloft. 這位高爾夫球手高舉獎盃親吻的照片被刊登在許多報紙的頭版上。","...a woman who claimed she had been pictured dancing with a celebrity in a nightclub. …一位聲稱自己和一位名人在夜總會跳舞的照片被刊登的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>picture</b> something in your mind, you think of it and have such a clear memory or idea of it that you seem to be able to see it. 想像","examples":["He pictured her with long black braided hair. 他想像她扎著長長的黑麻花辮。","He pictured Carrie sitting out in the car, waiting for him. 他想像卡麗正坐在外面的車裡等他的情景。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>in the picture</b>, you mean that they are involved in the situation that you are talking about. If you say that they are <b>out of the picture</b>, you mean that they are not involved in the situation you are talking about. 在/不在其中","examples":["Meyerson is back in the picture after disappearing in July. 繼7月份失蹤後，邁耶森又重回其中。","His dad had been out of the picture since he was eight. 自從他8歲時起，他的爸爸就一直不在其中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone <b>in the picture</b>, you tell them about a situation which they need to know about. 使…瞭解內情","examples":["Has anyone put you in the picture? 有人把內情告訴你了嗎？"]}]}]},"plane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飛機；（幾何學中的）平面；（物體的）平面；（穿過或連線物體的）虛構平面；（存在、思想或發展）水平；木工刨，刨子；懸鈴木；翼面"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平的，平坦的；二維平面的，二維空間的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滑翔；擦著水面疾駛；刨平；刨除；<罕>乘飛機旅行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plane</b> is a vehicle with wings and one or more engines that can fly through the air. 飛機","examples":["He had plenty of time to catch his plane. 他有足夠多的時間趕飛機。","Her mother was killed in a plane crash. 她的母親死於一次飛機失事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>plane</b> is a flat, level surface that may be sloping at a particular angle. (可能有坡度的) 平面","examples":["...a building with angled planes. …一幢外觀有一定坡度的建築物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a number of points are in the same <b>plane</b>, one line or one flat surface could pass through them all. 平面","examples":["All the planets orbit the Sun in roughly the same plane, around its equator. 所有行星基本在同一個平面上圍繞太陽赤道運轉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>plane</b> is a tool that has a flat bottom with a sharp blade in it. You move the plane over a piece of wood in order to remove thin pieces of its surface. 刨子","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>plane</b> or a <b>plane tree</b> is the same as a sycamore. 懸鈴木","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fly without moving wings or using engines; glide 滑翔; 滑行","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"level or flat 平的; 平坦的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plane</b> a piece of wood, you make it smaller or smoother by using a plane. 刨","examples":["She watches him plane the surface of a walnut board. 她看著他刨一塊胡桃木板。"]}]}]},"playground":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指學校或公園中的兒童）操場，遊樂場；（某一群體的）遊憩勝地，度假場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>playground</b> is a piece of land, at school or in a public area, where children can play. 遊戲場","examples":["...a seven-year-old boy playing in a school playground. …一個在學校操場上玩耍的7歲男孩。"]}]}]},"player":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動員，選手；（樂器的）演奏者；<舊>演員，表演者；參與者，角色；（錄音或錄影的）播放器；<非正式>風流浪子；（用於劇團的名稱中）劇團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>player</b> in a sport or game is a person who takes part, either as a job or for fun. 選手","examples":["...his greatness as a player. …他作為運動員的偉大。","She was a good golfer and tennis player. 她曾是一名優秀的高爾夫球手和網球運動員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>player</b> to refer to a musician. For example, a <b>piano player</b> is someone who plays the piano. 演奏者","examples":["...a professional trumpet player. …一個職業小號手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person, country, or organization is a <b>player</b> <b>in</b> something, they are involved in it and important in it. 重要參與者","examples":["Big business has become a major player in the art market. 大公司已經成為藝術市場中的重要參與者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a person who spends a lot of time enjoying themselves, especially by having a lot of sexual relationships, as a <b>player</b>. 尋歡作樂者","examples":["He was a ladies' man. A cheater. A player. 他曾是個花花公子，一個騙子，一個四處尋歡作樂的浪子。"]}]}]},"plan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（詳細）規劃；（養老金、儲蓄、保險）方案；計劃，打算；平面圖，詳圖；分佈圖，示意圖；（衛理公會教堂）巡迴傳教士名單；（手機流量、話費等）套餐"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"計劃，籌劃；打算；設計；期望，預料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plan</b> is a method of achieving something that you have worked out in detail beforehand. 計劃; 方案","examples":["The three leaders had worked out a peace plan. 這3位領導人已制定出了一份和平計劃。","He maintains that everything is going according to plan. 他堅持說一切都在按計劃進行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>plans</b>, you are intending to do a particular thing. (具體) 安排","examples":["\"I'm sorry,\" she said. \"I have plans for tonight.\". “抱歉，”她說。“我今晚有安排。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plan</b> <b>of</b> something that is going to be built or made is a detailed diagram or drawing of it. 設計圖","examples":["...when you have drawn a plan of the garden. …在你畫完這個花園的設計圖時。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plan</b> what you are going to do, you decide in detail what you are going to do, and you intend to do it. 計劃","examples":["If you plan what you're going to eat, you reduce your chances of overeating. 如果你對要吃的東西加以計劃，飲食過度的機率就會減少。","He planned to leave Baghdad on Monday. 他計劃星期一離開巴格達。","Moderate Republicans gathered together to plan for the future. 溫和的共和黨人集會籌劃未來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>plan</b> something that you are going to make, build, or create, you decide what the main parts of it will be and do a drawing of how it should be made. 規劃","examples":["It is no use trying to plan an 18-hole golf course on a 120-acre site if you have to ruin the environment to do it. 要規劃一個佔地120公頃、擁有18洞的高爾夫球場如果必須破壞環境才能做到，那就毫無益處了。"]}]}]},"piece":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"塊，張，片，段；碎片，零件；（成套物品的）部件，部分；（藝術、音樂、戲劇、文學的）一部作品；（報道、新聞、廣播的）一篇；份額，一份股權；樁，項，條，件； 一點；（土地的）一塊；一段距離；硬幣；槍；<非正式>女人；<蘇格蘭>（三明治等）小吃"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拼合，拼裝；慢慢理解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>piece of</b> something is an amount of it that has been broken off, torn off, or cut off. (從某物上拆下、撕下或切下的) 塊; 片; 段","examples":["...a piece of cake. …一塊蛋糕。","Cut the ham into pieces. 把火腿切成片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>piece</b> of an object is one of the individual parts or sections that it is made of, especially a part that can be removed. 部件","examples":["...assembling objects out of standard pieces. …用標準部件組裝物品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>piece of</b> land is an area of land. (一) 塊 (土地)","examples":["People struggle to get the best piece of land. 人們競相爭奪最好的一塊土地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>piece of</b> with many uncount nouns to refer to an individual thing of a particular kind. For example, you can refer to some advice as a <b>piece of advice</b>. 與不可數名詞搭配，表示某種事物的個體","examples":["When I produced this piece of work, my lecturers were very critical. 當我創作這件作品的時候，我的老師們批評甚多。","...an interesting piece of information. …一條有趣的資訊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to an article in a newspaper or magazine, some music written by someone, a broadcast, or a play as a <b>piece</b>. (報紙、雜誌上的) 文章; 作品","examples":["She wrote a piece on Gwyneth Paltrow for the New Yorker. 她為《紐約客》寫了一篇關於格溫妮絲·帕爾特羅的文章。","...a vaguely familiar orchestral piece. …一首隱約熟悉的管絃樂曲。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to a work of art as a <b>piece</b>. 藝術品","examples":["Each piece is unique, an exquisite painting of a real person, done on ivory. 每件藝術品都很獨特，均為繪在象牙上的真人精緻畫像。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can refer to specific coins as <b>pieces</b>. For example, a 5 cent <b>piece</b> is a coin that is worth 5 cents. 硬幣","examples":["...lots of 10 cent, 20 cent, and 50 cent pieces. …很多10分、20分和50分的硬幣。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>pieces</b> that you use when you play a board game such as chess are the specially made objects that you move around on the board. 棋子","examples":["How many pieces does each player have in backgammon? 西洋雙陸棋裡每方各有多少枚棋子？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone <b>a piece of</b> your <b>mind</b>, you tell them very clearly that you think they have behaved badly. 鮮明地批評","examples":["How very thoughtless. I'll give him a piece of my mind. 太欠考慮了。我要狠狠地批評他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is still <b>in one piece</b> after a dangerous journey or experience, they are safe and not damaged or hurt. 完好無損","examples":["...providing that my brother gets back alive and in one piece from his mission. …假若我哥哥完成任務後，活著安然無恙地回來的話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>to pieces</b> in expressions such as \"smash to pieces,\" or \"take something to pieces,\" when you are describing how something is broken or comes apart so that it is in separate pieces. 成為片","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>go to pieces</b>, you are so upset or nervous that you lose control of yourself and cannot do what you should do. (因緊張不安而) 崩潰","examples":["She's a strong woman, but she nearly went to pieces when Arnie died. 她是個堅強的女人，但阿尼死的時候她幾乎崩潰了。"]}]}]},"plant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"植物；工廠，發電廠；<美>房屋，設施；重型機械，機械裝置；栽贓物品；密探，臥底；（斯諾克）擊接觸球犯規"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"栽種，種植；灌輸（思想）；栽贓；安放（炸彈），（秘密）放置；安插（眼線、密探等）；把……牢牢插進，穩固地放置……；（通常出於不可告人的目的）釋出，散佈；移栽，移植（室外）；<非正式>埋葬（人）；建立，建立（殖民地，城市，社群）；（在河流或湖泊中）放養（魚苗、魚卵、牡蠣等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plant</b> is a living thing that grows in the earth and has a stem, leaves, and roots. 植物","examples":["Water each plant as often as required. 按要求經常給每棵植物澆水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"栽種","examples":["Extensive flooding in the country has delayed planting and many crops are still under water. 該國大範圍的洪水已經延誤了栽種，許多莊稼現在還泡在水中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plant</b> is a factory or a place where power is produced. 工廠; 電廠","examples":["...Ford's car assembly plants. …福特公司的汽車裝配廠。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Plant</b> is large machinery that is used in industrial processes. (工業用) 大型機械裝置","examples":["Companies may start to invest in plant and equipment abroad where costs may be lower. 各公司可能要開始在國外投資大型機械裝置，那裡成本可能低一些。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>plant</b> a seed, plant, or young tree, you put it into the ground so that it will grow there. 栽種","examples":["He says he plans to plant fruit trees and vegetables. 他說他計劃栽種果樹和蔬菜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>plants</b> land <b>with</b> a particular type of plant or crop, they put plants, seeds, or young trees into the land to grow them there. 將 (土地) 種植 (植被)","examples":["They plan to plant the area with grass and trees. 他們計劃在這個地區植樹種草。","Recently much of their energy has gone into planting a large vegetable garden. 最近，他們的大部分精力已經花在種植一個大型蔬菜園上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>plant</b> something somewhere, you put it there firmly. (穩固地) 放置","examples":["She planted her feet wide and bent her knees slightly. 她雙腳大步穩穩分開，雙膝微微彎曲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>plant</b> something such as a bomb means to hide it somewhere so that it explodes or works there. 埋設 (炸彈等)","examples":["So far no one has admitted planting the bomb. 到目前為止，沒有人承認埋設了炸彈。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something such as a weapon or drugs <b>is planted</b> on someone, it is put among their possessions or in their house so that they will be wrongly accused of a crime. 放置 (武器、毒品等以栽贓)","examples":["He always protested his innocence and claimed that the drugs had been planted to incriminate him. 他一直堅稱自己是清白的，聲稱毒品是有人放置要栽贓於他。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an organization <b>plants</b> someone somewhere, they send that person there so that they can get information or watch someone secretly. 安插 (臥底)","examples":["Journalists informed police who planted an undercover detective to trap Smith. 記者們向警方提供了資訊，警方安插了一名臥底偵探誘捕史密斯。"]}]}]},"poetry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩歌；詩一般的美麗，詩的意境；（學校或大學裡的）詩歌課"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Poems, considered as a form of literature, are referred to as <b>poetry</b>. 詩歌","examples":["...Russian poetry. …俄羅斯詩歌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe something very beautiful as <b>poetry</b>. 富有詩意的東西","examples":["His music is purer poetry than a poem in words. 他的音樂比詩文更具詩意。"]}]}]},"policeman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"警察，警員；（分化）澱帚（橡皮頭玻璃攪棒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>policeman</b> is a man who is a member of the police force. 警察","examples":[]}]}]},"popcorn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爆米花，爆玉米花；（植物學）爆裂玉米（Zea mays everta）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Popcorn</b> is a snack that consists of grains of corn that have been heated until they have burst and become large and light. 爆米花","examples":[]}]}]},"pond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人工或自然的）池塘；<非正式>大西洋（the pond）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"攔截（或築壩堵塞）（流水或其他流動液體）以形成小湖；（流水或其他液體）形成小湖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pond</b> is a small area of water that is smaller than a lake. Ponds are often made artificially. 池塘","examples":["She chose a bench beside the duck pond and sat down. 她選了鴨池旁的一張長椅坐了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People sometimes refer to the Atlantic Ocean as <b>the pond</b>. 大西洋","examples":["Tourist numbers from across the pond have dropped dramatically. 來自大西洋彼岸的遊客數量已急劇減少。"]}]}]},"police":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"警察部門；警察"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"巡查，維護治安；監督，管制；執行（法律，協議，條約）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>police</b> are the official organization that is responsible for making sure that people obey the law. 警方","examples":["The police are also looking for a second car. 警方也在尋找第二輛車。","Police say they have arrested twenty people following the disturbances. 警方稱他們已經在騷亂後逮捕了20個人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Police</b> are men and women who are members of the official organization that is responsible for making sure that people obey the law. 警察","examples":["More than one hundred police have ringed the area. 一百多名警察已經包圍了這個地區。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the police or military forces <b>police</b> an area or event, they make sure that law and order is preserved in that area or at that event. 維持…的治安","examples":["...the tiny U.N. observer force whose job it is to police the border. …維持邊界治安的那一小支聯合國觀察部隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or group in authority <b>polices</b> a law or an area of public life, they make sure that what is done is fair and legal. 監督","examples":["...the self-regulatory body that polices the investment management business. …監督投資管理事務的自律機構。"]}]}]},"pocket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣袋，口袋；錢財，財力；（附在某物上的）小口袋，小容器；<南非>（用作貿易計量的）（農產品）袋；（與周圍不同的）小群體，小區域；（檯球）網袋，球袋；岩石或地層中充滿礦石或其他物質的空洞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……放入口袋；把……裝進腰包，將……據為己有；賺取，獲得（錢財）；擊（球）入袋；收斂，抑制（感情）；包，圍"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"袖珍的，袋裝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pocket</b> is a kind of small bag that forms part of a piece of clothing, and that is used for carrying small things such as money or a handkerchief. 衣兜","examples":["He took his flashlight from his jacket pocket and switched it on. 他從上衣口袋裡拿出手電筒並將其開啟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>pocket</b> in a lot of different ways to refer to money that people have, get, or spend. For example, if someone gives or pays a lot of money, you can say that they <b>dig deep into</b> their <b>pocket</b>. If you approve of something because it is very cheap to buy, you can say that it <b>suits people's pockets</b>. 財力","examples":["When you come to choosing a dining table, it really is worth digging deep into your pocket for the best you can afford. 說到選擇餐桌，的確值得盡你的財力買張最好的。","...ladies' fashions to suit all shapes, sizes, and pockets. …適合所有體形、尺寸和價格選擇的女士時裝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pocket</b> <b>of</b> something is a small area where something is happening, or a small area which has a particular quality, and which is different from the other areas around it. (與周圍區域不同或孤立的) 小塊地區","examples":["Trapped in a pocket of air, they had only 40 minutes before the tide flooded the chamber. 他們被困在有一點空氣的彈丸之地，再過40分鐘洪水就會淹沒這間屋子了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>pocket</b> to describe something that is small enough to fit into a pocket, often something that is a smaller version of a larger item. 袖珍的","examples":["...a pocket calculator. …一個袖珍計算器。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who is in possession of something valuable such as a sum of money <b>pockets</b> it, they steal it or take it for themselves, even though it does not belong to them. 將…據為己有","examples":["Banks have passed some of the savings on to customers and pocketed the rest. 銀行將部分存款轉給顧客，其餘的則據為己有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>pockets</b> something such as a prize or sum of money, you mean that they win or obtain it, often without needing to make much effort or in a way that seems unfair. (輕鬆或不公正地) 獲得 (獎賞、金錢等)","examples":["He pocketed more money from this tournament than in his entire three years as a professional. 他從這次錦標賽中撈到的錢比他作為一名職業運動員整整3年賺的還要多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>pockets</b> something, they put it in their pocket, for example, because they want to steal it or hide it. 把…放入衣袋","examples":["Anthony snatched his letters and pocketed them. 安東尼抓過他的信，放進了衣袋中。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or organization has <b>deep pockets</b>, you mean that they have a lot of money with which to pay for something. 雄厚的財力","examples":["The church will do anything to avoid scandal – and everyone knows it has deep pockets. 教會將不惜一切來避開醜聞–大家都知道它有的是錢。","...investors with deep pockets. …財力雄厚的投資者們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>out of pocket</b>, you have less money than you should have or than you intended, for example, because you have spent too much or because of a mistake. 缺錢的","examples":["Make sure you are not out of pocket for your expenses. 你要確保別把日常開銷的錢都花沒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>picks</b> your <b>pocket</b>, they steal something from your pocket, usually without you noticing. 扒竊","examples":["They were more in danger of having their pockets picked than being shot at. 他們遭遇扒竊的危險大於遭受槍擊。"]}]}]},"pool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"游泳池；池塘，水坑；一小片（液體或光）；（河的）深水處，深潭；後備人員，備用物品；共用的資源（或資金）；（有相同職業或共同從事某項活動的）人群；賭球（或其他體育比賽），賭注；<英>足球普爾（the pools)；落袋檯球；壟斷性聯營；預賽組"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"集中（資源、錢財等）以備共用；積水成窪；（血液）在靜脈中淤積"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pool</b> is the same as a . 游泳池","examples":["...a heated indoor pool. …一個室內溫水游泳池。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pool</b> is a fairly small area of still water. 水池","examples":["The pool had dried up and was full of bracken and reeds. 該水池已經乾涸，長滿了歐洲蕨和蘆葦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pool of</b> liquid or light is a small area of it on the ground or on a surface. 一灘 (液體); 一片 (光)","examples":["She was found lying in a pool of blood. 她被發現躺在一灘血泊中。","It was raining quietly and steadily and there were little pools of water on the gravel drive. 雨正靜靜地下著，砂礫車道上積了一灘灘的水。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pool</b> <b>of</b> people, money, or things is a quantity or number of them that is available for an organization or group to use. 一撥人; 一筆錢; 一筆物資","examples":["The available pool of healthy manpower was not as large as military officials had expected. 一撥可用的健康勞力人數達不到軍方官員們的期望值。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"any of various billiard games in which the object is to pot all the balls with the cue ball, esp that played with 15 coloured and numbered balls; pocket billiards 落袋檯球戲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people or organizations <b>pool</b> their money, knowledge, or equipment, they share it or put it together so that it can be used for a particular purpose. 集中(資金、知識或裝置，供大家分享)","examples":["We pooled ideas and information. 我們彙集了意見和資訊。"]}]}]},"place":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地點，場所；城鎮（或建築物等）；有某用途的建築（或土地）；表面的某處；家，住所；（書本或講話中的）點；座位，位置；地位，資格；機會，名額；適當的地方；境況；排名；<美>第二名；（數學的）位；廣場，短街；鄉間住宅；一套餐具"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"放置；使處於某種境地；以某種態度對待（或看待）；認出，想起；下指示，請求；安置；排名，歸類；（賽跑）獲前三/四名；定位球得分；證明……在場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>place</b> is any point, building, area, town, or country. (任何) 地方","examples":["...a list of museums and places of interest. …一份博物館和名勝地的列表。","We're going to a place called Platoro. 我們要去一個叫普拉託羅的地方。","The pain is always in the same place. 疼痛總是在同一個地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>the place</b> to refer to the point, building, area, town, or country that you have already mentioned. (提到過的點、建築、地區、城鎮、國家等) 地方","examples":["Except for the remarkably tidy kitchen, the place was a mess. 除了異常整潔的廚房外，這個地方一團糟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to somewhere that provides a service, such as a hotel, restaurant, or institution, as a particular kind of <b>place</b>. (旅館、飯店、機構等某種提供服務的) 地方","examples":["He found a bed-and-breakfast place. 他找到一個提供住宿帶早餐的地方。","My wife and I discovered some superb places to eat. 我妻子和我發現了一些很棒的吃飯的地方。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Place</b> can be used after \"any,\" \"no,\" \"some,\" or \"every\" to mean \"anywhere,\" \"nowhere,\" \"somewhere,\" or \"everywhere.\" 用在(any), (no), (some)或(every)之後，分別表示(anywhere), (nowhere), (somewhere)或(everywhere)","examples":["The poor guy obviously didn't have any place to go for Easter. 這個可憐的傢伙顯然復活節沒有任何地方可去。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to the position where something belongs, or where it is supposed to be, as its <b>place</b>. (常處的、應在的) 位置","examples":["He returned the album to its place on the shelf. 他將像冊放回到架上原來的地方。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>place</b> is a seat or position that is available for someone to occupy. (空閒的) 座位; 位置","examples":["He walked back to the table and sat at the nearest of two empty places. 他走回桌旁，在兩個空位中就近的一個位子上坐下。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>place</b> in a society, system, or situation is their position in relation to other people or things. 地位","examples":["They want to see more women take their place higher up the corporate or professional ladder. 他們希望看到更多女性擔任公司或職業階梯上更高的職位。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Your <b>place</b> in a race or competition is your position in relation to the other competitors. If you are in first place, you are ahead of all the other competitors. 排名","examples":["He has risen to second place in the opinion polls. 他在民意調查中排名已升至第二位。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you get a <b>place</b> on a team, on a committee, or in an institution, for example, you are accepted as a member of the team or committee or as a resident of the institution. (在團隊、委員會或機構等中的) 位置","examples":["Derek had lost his place on the team. 德里克已經丟了他在那個隊的位置。","They should be in residential care but there are no places available. 他們應該得到住院護理，但是沒有空床位。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"A good <b>place</b> <b>to</b> do something in a situation or activity is a good time or stage at which to do it. (適當的) 時機","examples":["It seemed an appropriate place to end somehow. 似乎是到了該結束的時候了。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Your <b>place</b> is the house or apartment where you live. (居住地) 地方","examples":["Let's all go back to my place! 咱們都回我的住處吧！"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"Your <b>place</b> <b>in</b> a book or speech is the point you have reached in reading the book or making the speech. (書讀到的或話說到的) 地方","examples":["...her finger marking her place in the book. …她的手指指著書上她讀到的地方。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say how many decimal <b>places</b> there are in a number, you are saying how many numbers there are to the right of the decimal point. (數) 位","examples":["A pocket calculator only works to eight decimal places. 袖珍計算器只計算到小數點後8位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>takes place</b>, it happens, especially in a controlled or organized way. (尤指在控制或組織下) 發生; 進行","examples":["The discussion took place in a famous villa on the lake's shore. 討論在湖濱一座著名別墅舉行。","She wanted Randy's wedding to take place quickly. 她想讓蘭迪的婚禮馬上舉行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is happening <b>all over the place</b>, it is happening in many different places. 到處","examples":["Businesses are closing down all over the place. 到處都有企業在倒閉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If things are <b>all over the place</b>, they are spread over a very large area, usually in a disorganized way. 遍地","examples":["Our fingerprints are probably all over the place. 我們的指紋很可能到處都有。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>change places</b> <b>with</b> another person, you start being in their situation or role, and they start being in yours. 互換角色","examples":["With his door key in his hand, knowing Millie and the kids awaited him, he wouldn't change places with anyone. 手裡拿著門鑰匙，知道米莉和孩子們正等著自己，他決不會同任何人互換位置。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have been trying to understand something puzzling and then everything <b>falls into place</b> or <b>clicks into place</b>, you suddenly understand how different pieces of information are connected and everything becomes clearer. (情況) 豁然開朗","examples":["When the reasons behind the decision were explained, of course, it all fell into place. 當這個決定背後的原因得到了解釋後，當然，一切都變得豁然開朗了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If things <b>fall into place</b>, events happen naturally to produce a situation you want. (事情) 順理成章","examples":["Once the decision was made, things fell into place rapidly. 一旦決定了，事情很快順理成章。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is going places</b>, you mean that they are showing a lot of talent or ability and are likely to become very successful. 出色","examples":["You always knew Barbara was going places, she was different. 你一直知道芭芭拉很出色，她與眾不同。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"People <b>in high places</b> are people who have powerful and influential positions in a government, society, or organization. (在政府、社會或組織中) 身居高位","examples":["He had friends in high places. 他有一些高層的朋友。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something is <b>in place</b>, it is in its correct or usual position. If it is <b>out of place</b>, it is not in its correct or usual position. 在恰當/不恰當的位置","examples":["Gary hastily pushed the drawer back into place. 加里匆忙把抽屜推回去。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something such as a law, a policy, or an administrative structure is <b>in place</b>, it is working or able to be used. (法律、政策、行政機構等) 在執行","examples":["Similar legislation is already in place in Utah. 類似的法規已在猶他州實施。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If one thing or person is used or does something <b>in place of</b> another, they replace the other thing or person. 替代","examples":["Cooked kidney beans can be used in place of French beans. 做熟的四季豆可以用來代替菜豆。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something has particular characteristics or features <b>in places</b>, it has them at several points within an area. 在幾處","examples":["Even now the snow along the roadside was five or six feet deep in places. 即使現在，路邊的雪有的地方有五六英尺深。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say what you would have done <b>in</b> someone else's <b>place</b>, you say what you would have done if you had been in their situation and had been experiencing what they were experiencing. 處於 (某人的) 位置","examples":["In her place I wouldn't have been able to resist it. 若處在她的位置上，我也會無法抵擋它的。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You say <b>in the first place</b> when you are talking about the beginning of a situation or about the situation as it was before a series of events. 最初","examples":["What brought you to Washington in the first place? 最初是什麼使你來到華盛頓？"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You say <b>in the first place</b> and <b>in the second place</b> to introduce the first and second in a series of points or reasons. <b>In the first place</b> can also be used to emphasize a very important point or reason. 首先/其次 (用於列舉，首先也可以用於強調)","examples":["In the first place you are not old, Conway. And in the second place, you are a very strong and appealing man. 首先，你不老，康韋。其次，你是個非常強壯、有魅力的男人。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you say that <b>it is not</b> your <b>place</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that it is not right or appropriate for you to do it, or that it is not your responsibility to do it. 不是 (某人) 該做的事","examples":["He says that it is not his place to comment on government commitment to further funds. 他說，他不便評論政府對進一步提供資金的承諾。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If someone or something seems <b>out of place</b> in a particular situation, they do not seem to belong there or to be suitable for that situation. 不屬於; 不適宜","examples":["I felt out of place in my suit and tie. 穿著西裝打著領帶，我感到不自在。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you <b>place</b> one thing <b>above</b>, <b>before</b>, or <b>over</b> another, you think that the first thing is more important than the second and you show this in your behaviour. 置…於…之上/前","examples":["He continued to place security above all other objectives. 他繼續將安全置於其他所有目標之上。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone <b>in</b> their <b>place</b>, you show them that they are less important or clever than they think they are. 使 (某人) 有自知之明","examples":["In a few words she had put him in his place. 幾句話她就讓他安分了下來。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you say that someone should <b>be shown</b> their <b>place</b> or <b>be kept in</b> their <b>place</b>, you are saying, often in a humorous way, that they should be made aware of their low status. (以幽默的方式) 使 (某人) 識相","examples":["...an uppity bartender who needs to be shown his place. …一個盛氣凌人的需要有點自知之明的酒吧招待。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If one thing <b>takes second place</b> <b>to</b> another, it is considered to be less important and is given less attention than the other thing. 居次要地位","examples":["My personal life has had to take second place to my career. 我的個人生活得讓位於我的事業。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If one thing or person <b>takes the place of</b> another or <b>takes</b> another's <b>place</b>, they replace the other thing or person. 替代","examples":["Optimism was gradually taking the place of pessimism. 樂觀正逐漸替代悲觀。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>places</b>, you visit pleasant or interesting places. (去) 各地地","examples":["I don't have money to go places. 我沒有錢到處玩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>place</b> something somewhere, you put it in a particular position, especially in a careful, firm, or deliberate way. (小心地、穩妥地或從容地) 放置","examples":["Brand folded it in his handkerchief and placed it in the inside pocket of his jacket. 布蘭德把它包在手絹裡，放進了他夾克衫的內兜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>place</b> a person or thing in a particular state means to cause them to be in it. 使處於 (某種狀態)","examples":["Widespread protests have placed the president under serious pressure. 大範圍的抗議已經使總統處於巨大的壓力之下。","The crisis could well place the relationship at risk. 這場危機很可能使這個關係岌岌可危。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>place</b> instead of \"put\" or \"lay\" in certain expressions where the meaning is carried by the following noun. For example, if you <b>place emphasis</b> <b>on</b> something, you emphasize it, and if you <b>place the blame</b> <b>on</b> someone, you blame them. 替代(put)或(lay)，用於(place emphasis on)、(place the blame on)等由其後的名詞決定意思的短語中","examples":["He placed great emphasis on the importance of family life and ties. 他非常重視家庭生活和家庭紐帶。","She seemed to be placing most of the blame on her mother. 她好像是在把大部分責任推到她母親身上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>place</b> someone or something in a particular class or group, you label or judge them in that way. 評定","examples":["The authorities have placed the drug in Class A, the same category as heroin and cocaine. 當局已把這種毒品定為A級，與海洛因和可卡因屬同一類。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a competitor in a race or competition <b>is placed</b> first, second, or third, they finish first, second or third. If a horse <b>is placed</b> in a race, it finishes second. 取得名次; (馬在賽跑中) 位居第二","examples":["I had been placed 2nd and 3rd a few times but had never won. 我得過幾次第二名和第三名，但是從來沒有得過第一。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>place an order</b> <b>for</b> a product or <b>for</b> a meal, you ask for it to be sent or brought to you. 訂 (產品或餐)","examples":["It is a good idea to place your order well in advance as delivery can often take months rather than weeks. 早早提前訂購是個好主意，因為交貨常常要花幾個月的時間，而不是幾星期。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>place an advertisement</b> <b>in</b> a newspaper, you arrange for the advertisement to appear in the newspaper. 登廣告","examples":["They placed an advertisement in the local paper for a secretary. 他們把一則秘書招聘廣告登在當地報紙上。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>place a bet</b>, you bet money on something. 下賭注","examples":["For this race, though, he had already placed a bet on one of the horses. 不過，這次賽馬，他已經在其中的一匹馬上下了注。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If an agency or organization <b>places</b> someone, it finds them a job or somewhere to live. 安置 (工作或住所)","examples":["They managed to place fourteen women in paid positions. 他們設法為14名婦女安排了有報酬的工作。"]}]}]},"play":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"玩，玩耍；捉弄，戲弄；擺弄，玩弄；耍弄，愚弄；不認真地幹，鬧（play at）；參加（遊戲、比賽等）；與……比賽；擊，踢（球）；出（牌），走（棋子）；派（某人）上場；（在球隊中）打（某位置）；扮演，演出；佯裝，假裝；假扮……玩；（戲劇或電影）上演，上映；演奏，彈奏；（使）播放；閃爍，浮現；（以某方式）行事，做事；（使）發射（或噴射、照射）；賭，投機；<美>被接受，被認可；（喻）合作，買某人的賬；寄於；讓（上鉤的魚）掙扎得筋疲力盡；（板球場狀況對比賽）產生影響"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇本，戲劇；遊戲，玩樂；比賽；比賽中的動作；（運動或遊戲中的）打法，走法；活動空間，間隙；影響，作用；閃爍，變幻；玩笑；（音訊或影象的）播放次數，播放時長；播放（功能）；<美>（報紙或電視的）關注；（對文字的）巧用，妙用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When children, animals, or adults <b>play</b>, they spend time doing enjoyable things, such as using toys and taking part in games. 玩耍","examples":["...invite the children over to play. …邀請孩子們過來玩。","They played in the little garden. 他們在小花園裡玩耍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>play with</b> an object or with your hair, you keep moving it or touching it with your fingers, perhaps because you are bored or nervous. 擺弄","examples":["She stared at the floor, idly playing with the strap of her handbag. 她盯著地板，隨手擺弄著手提包的提帶。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Play</b> is also a noun. 玩","examples":["...a few hours of play until the babysitter puts them to bed. …直到保姆讓他們上床睡覺之前的幾小時的玩耍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Play</b> is also a noun. (對運動、遊戲、比賽等的) 參加","examples":["They've got more exciting players and a more exciting style of play. 他們有更精彩的選手和更精彩的比賽風格。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Play</b> is also a noun. 比賽","examples":["Fischer won after 5 hours and 41 minutes of play. 費希爾在5小時41分鐘的較量後獲勝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>play</b> is a piece of writing performed in a theatre, on the radio, or on television. 戲劇","examples":["It's my favourite Shakespeare play. 這是我最喜歡的莎士比亞劇。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>play</b> a sport, game, or match, you take part in it. 參加 (體育運動、遊戲、比賽等)","examples":["While the twins played cards, Leona sat reading. 那對雙胞胎玩牌的時候，利昂娜坐著看書。","I used to play basketball. 我過去常打籃球。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When one person or team <b>plays</b> another or <b>plays against</b> them, they compete against them in a sport or game. 與…比賽","examples":["Dallas will play Green Bay. 達拉斯隊將迎戰綠灣隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>play</b> a joke or a trick on someone, you deceive them or give them a surprise in a way that you think is funny, but that often causes problems for them or annoys them. 開 (玩笑); 搞 (惡作劇)","examples":["Someone had played a trick on her, stretched a piece of string at the top of those steps. 有人對她搞惡作劇，在那些臺階的頂部拉了一根繩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an actor <b>plays</b> a role or character in a play or film, he or she performs the part of that character. (在戲劇或電影中) 扮演 (角色)","examples":["...Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde, in which he played Hyde. …他在其中扮演海德的《化身博士》。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe how someone deals with a situation by saying that they <b>play it</b> in a certain way. For example, if someone <b>plays it cool</b>, they keep calm and do not show much emotion, and if someone <b>plays it straight</b>, they behave in an honest and direct way. 對待","examples":["Investors are playing it cautious, and they're playing it smart. 投資者們在謹慎應對，同時他們也在巧妙應對。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>play</b> a musical instrument or <b>play</b> a tune on a musical instrument, or if a musical instrument <b>plays</b>, music is produced from it. 演奏 (樂器或樂曲); 奏響","examples":["Nina had been playing the piano. 尼娜一直在彈鋼琴。","He played for me. 他為我彈奏。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>play</b> a record, a CD, or a DVD, you put it into a machine and sound and sometimes pictures are produced. If a record, CD, or DVD <b>is playing</b>, sound and sometimes pictures are being produced from it. 播放","examples":["She played her records too loudly. 她放唱片的聲音太大。","There is classical music playing in the background. 背景中正在播放古典音樂。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a musician or group of musicians <b>plays</b> or <b>plays</b> a concert, they perform music for people to listen or dance to. (在音樂會上) 演奏","examples":["A band was playing. 一支樂隊正在演奏。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>play</b> to describe how someone behaves, when they are deliberately behaving in a certain way or like a certain type of person. For example, to <b>play the innocent</b>, means to pretend to be innocent, and to <b>play deaf</b> means to pretend not to hear something. 假裝","examples":["Hill tried to play the peacemaker. 希爾試圖假扮成和事佬。","She was just playing the devoted mother. 她只是在裝成一位負責的母親。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>comes into play</b> or <b>is brought into play</b>, it begins to be used or to have an effect. 開始起作用","examples":["The real existence of a military option will come into play. 現有的軍事手段將開始起作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>plays a part</b> or <b>plays a role</b> <b>in</b> a situation, they are involved in it and have an effect on it. 起作用","examples":["They played a part in the life of their community. 他們在自己的社群生活中發揮了作用。","The U.N. would play a major role in monitoring a ceasefire. 聯合國將在監督停火方面發揮主要作用。"]}]}]},"position":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"位置，方位；姿勢，安置方式；處境，狀況；觀點，立場；地位，身份；職務，職位；名次；（隊員的）職責，角色；恰當位置；陣地；持有狀態；（邏輯）命題，主張"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"安置，使處於；為（產品）定位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>position</b> of someone or something is the place where they are in relation to other things. 位置","examples":["The ship was identified, and its name and position were reported to the Coast Guard. 該輪船的身份已得到確認，其名稱和位置已報告給了海岸警衛隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone or something is in a particular <b>position</b>, they are sitting, lying, or arranged in that way. 姿勢","examples":["It is crucial that the upper back and neck are held in an erect position to give support for the head. 重要的是：上背和頸部要挺直以支撐頭部，這一點很重要。","Mr. Dambar had raised himself to a sitting position. 丹巴先生已坐了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>position</b> in society is the role and the importance that you have in it. (社會) 地位","examples":["Adjustment to their changing role and position in society can be painful for some old people. 對有些老年人適應他們在社會中不斷變化的角色和地位可能是痛苦的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>position</b> in a company or organization is a job. 職位","examples":["He left a career in teaching to take up a position with the NEH. 他放棄了教職，以便在國家人文基金會任職。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>position</b> in a race or competition is how well you did in relation to the other competitors or how well you are doing. (比賽、競賽中的) 名次","examples":["By the ninth hour the car was running in eighth position. 比賽進行到第9個小時的時候該賽車跑在第8位。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can describe your situation at a particular time by saying that you are in a particular <b>position</b>. 處境; 狀況","examples":["He's going to be in a very difficult position if things go badly for him. 他處境將非常困難，如果情況變糟的話。","Companies should be made to reveal more about their financial position. 應該要求各公司披露更多的財務狀況資料。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>position</b> <b>on</b> a particular matter is your attitude toward it or your opinion of it. 態度; 看法","examples":["He could be depended on to take a moderate position on most of the key issues. 可以相信，他會在大多數關鍵問題上持溫和態度。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are <b>in a position</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are able to do it. If you are <b>in no position</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are unable to do it. (做某事的) 適當位置","examples":["I am not in a position to comment. 我不便發表評論。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>position</b> something somewhere, you put it there carefully, so that it is in the right place or position. 小心放置","examples":["Position the cursor where you want the new margins to begin. 將游標放在你所要的新頁邊空白開端。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in position</b>, they are in their correct or usual place or arrangement. 在合適的位置上","examples":["28,000 U.S. troops are moving into position. 2.8萬名美國士兵即將到位。"]}]}]},"problem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"問題，難題，困難；疾病；（透過算數或仔細思考而解決的）題；（感覺上）不喜歡，不情願；（尤指國際象棋等）棋式，排局"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難對付的，成問題的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>problem</b> is a situation that is unsatisfactory and causes difficulties for people. 問題","examples":["...the economic problems of the inner city. …內城的經濟問題。","I do not have a simple solution to the drug problem. 我並沒有一個簡單的解決毒品問題的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>problem</b> is a puzzle that requires logical thought or mathematics to solve it. 題目","examples":["With mathematical problems, you can save time by approximating. 對於數學題，你可以用近似法省時間。"]}]}]},"practice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"實踐，實際操作；通常的做法，慣例；練習；練習課，固定的訓練時間；（醫生、律師或其他專業人士的）業務，事務所；訴訟手續，訴訟程式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"練習；經常做，養成……的習慣；信奉（宗教）；（醫生、律師等）執業，從業"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to something that people do regularly as a <b>practice</b>. 做法","examples":["Some firms have reached agreements to cut workers' pay below the level set in their contract, a practice that is illegal in Germany. 有些公司已達成一致意見將工人的工資削減到低於合同中規定的水平，這種做法在德國是違法的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Practice</b> means doing something regularly in order to be able to do it better. A <b>practice</b> is one of these periods of doing something. 練習","examples":["She was taking all three of her daughters to basketball practice every day. 她那時每天帶她的3個女兒去進行籃球訓練。","...the hard practice necessary to develop from a learner to an accomplished musician. …從初學者成長為有造詣的音樂家所必需的艱苦練習。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The work done by doctors and lawyers is referred to as the <b>practice</b> of medicine and law. People's religious activities are referred to as the <b>practice</b> of a religion. (醫療或法律的) 業務; (宗教) 活動","examples":["...maintaining or improving his skills in the practice of internal medicine. …保持或提高他在內科醫療業務方面的技能。","I eventually realized I had to change my attitude towards medical practice. 我終於認識到我得改變我對醫務工作的態度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A doctor's or lawyer's <b>practice</b> is his or her business, often shared with other doctors or lawyers. 醫生的診所; 律師的事務所","examples":["The new doctor's practice was miles away from where I lived. 那位新醫生的診所離我的住處有數英里遠。"]}]}]},"power":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"控制力，操控力；政權，統治；權力，職權；強國，大國；有影響力的人（或組織）；能力，本領；支配力，實力；（某事物或社會集團的）影響力，勢力；力量，體能；能量，電力；動力，功率；冪，乘方，指數；放大率；神靈，神力；（基督教）掌權天使（powers）；（旨在提升某群體地位的）權力運動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"驅動，推動（機器或車輛）；（使）迅猛移動，快速前進；猛力踢（或推、頂）（尤指球）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"電力的，電動的；強大的；有重要人士參與的；（服裝）禮服的，顯示權勢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>power</b>, they have a lot of control over people and activities. 權力","examples":["In a democracy, power must be divided. 在民主政體中，權力必須被分散。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>power</b> <b>to</b> do something is your ability to do it. 能力","examples":["Human societies have the power to solve the problems confronting them. 人類社會有能力解決他們面臨的問題。","Fathers have the power to dominate children and young people. 父輩們有控制孩子們和年輕人的能力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If it is <b>in</b> or <b>within</b> your <b>power</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are able to do it or you have the resources to deal with it. 能力範圍","examples":["Your debt situation is only temporary, and it is within your power to resolve it. 你的債務狀況只是暫時的，解決它在你的能力範圍裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone in authority has the <b>power</b> to do something, they have the legal right to do it. (法律賦予的) 權力","examples":["The police have the power of arrest. 警察有逮捕權。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If people take <b>power</b> or come to <b>power</b>, they take charge of a country's affairs. If a group of people are <b>in power</b>, they are in charge of a country's affairs. 政權","examples":["Idi Amin came into power several years later. 伊迪·阿明幾年後執掌了政權。","He first assumed power in 1970. 他於1970年首次執掌了政權。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>power</b> to refer to a country that is very rich or important, or has strong military forces. 強國","examples":["....the emergence of the new major economic power, Japan. …新的主要經濟強國日本的崛起。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>power</b> of something is the ability that it has to move or affect things. 動力","examples":["The vehicle had better power, better tyres, and better brakes. 這種車輛有更好的動力、更好的輪胎和更好的剎車。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Power</b> is energy, especially electricity, that is obtained in large quantities from a fuel source and used to operate lights, heating, and machinery. (尤指電) 能量","examples":["Nuclear power is cleaner than coal. 核能比煤更清潔。","Power has been restored to most parts that were hit last night by high winds. 昨天夜裡受到強風襲擊的大部分地區已經恢復了供電。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The device or fuel that <b>powers</b> a machine provides the energy that the machine needs in order to work. 為…提供動力","examples":["The \"flywheel\" battery, it is said, could power an electric car for 600 miles on a single charge. 據說，“飛輪”電池每充電一次可驅動一輛電動汽車行駛600英里。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Power</b> tools are operated by electricity. 電動的","examples":["...large power tools, such as chainsaws. …大型電動工具，如鏈鋸。"]}]}]},"price":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"價格；代價；開價，價碼；投注賠率；<古> 價值"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……定價；給（商店中的產品）標價；比較……的價格；問……的價格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>price</b> of something is the amount of money that you have to pay in order to buy it. 價格","examples":["...a sharp increase in the price of petrol. …燃氣價格的一次猛漲。","They expected house prices to rise. 他們預期房價會上漲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>price</b> that you pay for something that you want is an unpleasant thing that you have to do or suffer in order to get it. 代價","examples":["There may be a price to pay for such relentless activity, perhaps ill health or even divorce. 這樣沒完沒了的活動可能是要付出代價的，也許是不良健康狀況甚至是離婚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"定價","examples":["It's hard to maintain competitive pricing. 很難保持有競爭力的定價。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is priced at</b> a particular amount, the price is set at that amount. 將…定價","examples":["The bond is currently priced at $900. 這種債券當前定價為$900。","Analysts predict that Digital will price the new line at less than half the cost of comparable IBM mainframes. 分析家們預測迪吉多公司會將其新線產品的價格定在低於可比的IBM公司大型主機成本的一半的水平。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you want something <b>at any price</b>, you are determined to get it, even if unpleasant things happen as a result. 不惜任何代價","examples":["If they wanted a deal at any price, they would have to face the consequences. 如果他們不惜任何代價想要一筆生意，他們將得面對其後果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can buy something that you want <b>at a price</b>, it is for sale, but it is extremely expensive. 以極高的價格","examples":["Most goods are available, but at a price. 大部分商品都可以買到，但價格昂貴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you get something that you want <b>at a price</b>, you get it but something unpleasant happens as a result. 以一定代價","examples":["Fame comes at a price. 成名是要付出代價的。"]}]}]},"print":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"列印；印刷，出版；（在報紙或雜誌上）刊登，刊載；用印刷體書寫；沖印（照片）；印花樣於（尤指織物或衣服上）；印上（印痕）；（用模子）印；銘記，銘刻"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"印刷；印刷字型；印刷出的文字；印刷行業，出版界；印刷品，出版物；印跡，痕跡；印章；印花布，印花布服裝；印花，印製圖案；（沖印出的）照片； 版畫，(用照相製版法制作的）繪畫複製品；電影複製"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>prints</b> something such as a book or newspaper, they produce it in large quantities using a machine. 印刷","examples":["He started to print his own posters to distribute abroad. 他開始印刷他自己的宣傳海報以在國外散發。","Our brochure is printed on environmentally-friendly paper. 我們的宣傳手冊是用環保紙印刷的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a newspaper or magazine <b>prints</b> a piece of writing, it includes it or publishes it. 發表; 刊登","examples":["We can only print letters which are accompanied by the writer's name and address. 我們只能發表有作者姓名和地址的信件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If numbers, letters, or designs <b>are printed</b> <b>on</b> a surface, they are put on it in ink or dye using a machine. You can also say that a surface <b>is printed</b> <b>with</b> numbers, letters, or designs. 印 (數字、字母或圖案)","examples":["...the number printed on the receipt. …印在發票上的編號。","The company has for some time printed its phone number on its products. 這家公司將其電話號碼印在其產品上已有一段時間了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>print</b> a photograph, you produce it from a negative. 沖印","examples":["Printing a black-and-white negative on to colour paper produces a similar monochrome effect. 將黑白底片沖印在彩色紙上產生一種類似的單色效果。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>print</b> words, you write in letters that are not joined together. 用印刷體書寫","examples":["Print your name and address on a postcard and send it to us. 用印刷體將你的名字和地址寫在一張明信片上寄給我們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In American English, <b>print up</b> means the same as . 印刷","examples":["Community workers here are printing up pamphlets for peace demonstrations. 這裡的社群工作者們正在印製和平示威遊行用的小冊子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"印刷","examples":["His brother ran a printing and publishing company. 他兄弟開辦過一家印刷出版公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>print</b> is a piece of clothing or material with a pattern printed on it. You can also refer to the pattern itself as a <b>print</b>. 印花布料; 印花","examples":["Her mother wore one of her dark summer prints. 她母親穿了她的一件深色印花布夏裝。","In this living room we've mixed glorious floral prints. 在這客廳裡我們將各種漂亮的花卉圖案搭配在了一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>print</b> is a photograph from a film that has been developed. 沖印出的照片","examples":["...black and white prints of Margaret and Jean as children. …瑪格麗特和瓊小時侯的黑白照片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>print</b> is one of a number of copies of a particular picture. It can be either a photograph, something such as a painting, or a picture made by an artist who puts ink on a prepared surface and presses it against paper. 版畫; 印出來的畫","examples":["...12 original copper plates engraved by William Hogarth for his famous series of prints. …由威廉·霍格思為他著名的系列版畫刻制的12塊原始銅板。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Print</b> is used to refer to letters and numbers as they appear on the pages of a book, newspaper, or printed document. 印刷字","examples":["...columns of tiny print. …一欄欄極小的印刷字。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to a mark left by someone's foot as a <b>print</b>. 腳印","examples":["He crawled from print to print, sniffing at the earth, following the scent left in the tracks. 他從一個腳印爬到另一個腳印，嗅著泥土，跟著路上留下的氣味。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can refer to oily marks left by someone's fingers as their <b>prints</b>. 指印","examples":["Fresh prints of both girls were found in the house. 兩個女孩剛留下的指印都在屋子裡找到了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>print</b> media consists of newspapers and magazines, but not television or radio. 印刷的 (媒體)","examples":["I have been convinced that the print media are more accurate and more reliable than television. 我一直深信印刷媒體比電視更準確、更可靠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you appear <b>in print</b>, or get <b>into print</b>, what you say or write is published in a book, newspaper, or magazine. (出現在) 印刷媒體","examples":["Many of these poets appeared in print only long after their deaths. 這些詩人中許多只是在去世很久之後才出現在印刷媒體上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>small print</b> or the <b>fine print</b> of something such as an advertisement or a contract consists of the technical details and legal conditions, which are often printed in much smaller letters than the rest of the text. (廣告、合同裡的技術細節、法律條款等) 小體印刷的內容","examples":["I'm looking at the small print; I don't want to sign anything that I shouldn't sign. 我在讀小體印刷的細則，我不想在不該籤的檔案上簽字。"]}]}]},"purple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紫色的，紫紅色的；（作品）詞藻華麗的，華而不實的；帝王的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"紫色，紫紅色；紫色衣服（或料子）；（古羅馬，拜占庭）紫色衣服（the purple）；（從某些軟體動物提取的）深紅色染料；（古羅馬）要職，高位，擁有特權的職位（the purple）；（紅衣主教的）大紅袍（the purple）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成紫色，（使）發紫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>purple</b> is of a reddish-blue colour. 紫色的","examples":["She wore purple and green silk. 她穿著紫色和綠色的絲綢。"]}]}]},"point":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀點，論點；要點，核心問題；目的，意圖；具體細節；特點，特徵；地點；時刻，階段；得分；小數點，點；羅盤（方位）點；點（標度）；（電影的）利潤百分比；尖端，尖頭；岬角；光點，色點；<英>插座；（字號的）磅值；<英>軌尖，道岔（points）；（芭蕾）腳尖（points）；（分電器中的）接點；<非正式>稱讚，認可（points）；（板球）防守；尖兵隊；<美>排頭位置；（動物的）外部位；（獵）直竄（位置）；<史>束衣帶；束帆繩；狗指方向；（樂曲的）重要樂句或主題"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"指，指向；對準，瞄準；朝向，對著；指路；引導，指引；暗示，表明；強調（話語或行動）；（用水泥）勾縫；繃直（腳趾）；削尖；使（游標）指著；插入點號；（狗）示意有（獵物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>point</b> to refer to something that someone has said or written. 看法","examples":["We disagree with every point she makes. 我們不同意她提出的任何觀點。","The following account will clearly illustrate this point. 以下的陳述將清楚地闡明這一看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has a point</b>, or if you <b>take</b> their <b>point</b>, you mean that you accept that what they have said is important and should be considered. 重要性","examples":["\"If he'd already killed once, surely he'd have killed Sarah?\" She had a point there. “如果他已經殺過一次人，莎拉就一定是他殺的了嗎？”她這句話有道理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The point</b> of what you are saying or discussing is the most important part that provides a reason or explanation for the rest. 要點","examples":["\"Did I ask you to talk to me?\"—\"That's not the point.\" “我要你跟我說了嗎？”—“問題不在這兒。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you ask what <b>the</b> <b>point</b> <b>of</b> something is, or say that there is <b>no point</b> <b>in</b> it, you are indicating that a particular action has no purpose or would not be useful. 意義; 目的","examples":["What was the point of thinking about him? 想著他有什麼意義呢？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>point</b> is a detail, aspect, or quality of something or someone. 細節 (之處)","examples":["Many of the points in the report are correct. 報告中的很多細節是正確的。","The most interesting point about the village was its religion. 這個村莊最有趣的一點是它的宗教。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>point</b> is a particular place or position where something happens. 地點","examples":["I'm sure there's another point we could meet at, but not there. 我確信我們還有別的地點可以會面，但不是那兒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>point</b> to refer to a particular time, or to a particular stage in the development of something. 時刻; 階段","examples":["We're all going to die at some point. 我們都會在某一時刻死去的。","It got to the point where he had to leave. 到了他不得不離開的時候了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>point</b> of something such as a pin, needle, or knife is the thin, sharp end of it. (別針、針、刀等的) 尖端","examples":["Put the tomatoes into a bowl and stab each one with the point of a knife. 把那些西紅柿放在一隻碗裡，然後用刀尖把每個都劃開。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"In some sports, competitions, and games, a <b>point</b> is one of the single marks that are added together to give the total score. (體育比賽中的) 得分","examples":["Chamberlain scored 50 or more points four times in the season. 張伯倫在那個賽季中4次得分在50或50以上。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"The <b>points of the compass</b> are directions such as North, South, East, and West. (羅盤的) 方位點","examples":["Sightseers arrived from all points of the compass. 觀光客從四面八方趕了過來。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"On a railway line, the <b>points</b> are the levers and rails at a place where two tracks join or separate. The points enable a train to move from one track to another. (鐵軌的) 接點","examples":["...a set of railway tracks – including points – and a model train. …一套鐵軌–含轉轍器–和一個火車模型。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"A <b>point </b>is a unit of measurement equal to one twelfth of a pica, or approximately 0.01384 inch. There are approximately 72 points to the inch. 點(計量單位)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In spoken English, you use <b>point</b> to refer to the dot or mark in a decimal number that separates the whole numbers from the fractions. 點; 小數點","examples":["This is FM stereo one oh three point seven. 這裡是調頻立體聲廣播103.7兆赫。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>point at</b> a person or thing, you hold out your finger toward them in order to make someone notice them. (用手指) 指向","examples":["I pointed at the boy sitting nearest me. 我指了指坐得離我最近的那個男孩。","He pointed at me with the stem of his pipe. 他用他的菸斗柄指著我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>points</b> <b>to</b> a place or <b>points</b> in a particular direction, it shows where that place is or it faces in that direction. 指向","examples":["An arrow pointed to the toilets. 一個箭頭指向了廁所。","He controlled the car until it was pointing forward again. 他控制住了汽車，直到車頭再次朝向前方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>points to</b> a particular situation, it suggests that the situation exists or is likely to occur. 表明; 顯示","examples":["Earlier reports pointed to students working harder, more continuously, and with enthusiasm. 早期的報告顯示學生學習更刻苦、持續的時間更長，而且興致高昂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>point to</b> something that has happened or that is happening, you are using it as proof that a particular situation exists. 著重指出","examples":["George Fodor points to other weaknesses in the campaign. 喬治·福多爾著重指出了這場活動的其他缺點。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>point</b> something <b>at</b> someone, you aim the tip or end of it toward them. 對準","examples":["David pointed his finger at Mary. 戴維手指著瑪麗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>beside the point</b>, you mean that it is not relevant to the subject that you are discussing. 不相關的","examples":["Brian didn't like it, but that was beside the point. 布賴恩是不喜歡它，但這同討論的問題不相關。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>comes to the point</b> or <b>gets to the point</b>, they start talking about the thing that is most important to them. 談正題; 言歸正傳","examples":["He came to the point at once. \"You did a splendid job on this case.\" 他立刻切入正題。“你這件事情幹得真棒。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> your <b>point</b> or <b>prove</b> your <b>point</b>, you prove that something is true, either by arguing about it or by your actions or behaviour. 證明自己的論點","examples":["I think you've made your point, dear. 我想你已經證明了你的論點，親愛的。","Dr. David McCleland studied one-hundred people, aged eighteen to sixty, to prove the point. 戴維·麥克萊蘭博士對100個年齡在18歲到60歲之間的人進行了研究，以證明自己的論點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>make a point of</b> doing something, you do it in a very deliberate or obvious way. 有意","examples":["She made a point of spending as much time as possible away from Oklahoma. 她有意儘可能長時間地呆在俄克拉何馬以外的地方。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>on the point of</b> doing something, you are about to do it. 正要…之際","examples":["He was on the point of saying something when the phone rang. 他正要說些什麼的時候，電話響了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that is <b>to the point</b> is relevant to the subject that you are discussing, or expressed neatly without wasting words or time. 中肯的","examples":["The description which he had been given was brief and to the point. 對他所作的描述簡要、中肯。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>up to a point</b>, you mean that it is partly but not completely true. 在一定程度上","examples":["\"Was she good?\"—\"Mmm. Up to a point.\" “她優秀嗎？”—“嗯，還過得去。”"]}]}]},"public":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公眾的，大眾的；公共的，公用的；政府的，公眾事務的；<英> 大學的，為大學的；（宣告、事件等）公開的，公諸於眾的；公開場合的，大庭廣眾的；上市的；眾所周知的，廣為人知的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"公眾，大眾（the public）；志趣相投（或從事同一類活動、具有共同特徵）的群體；<非正式>（對某個藝術家、作家或表演家感興趣的）讀者，觀眾（one's public）；<英>（酒館中的）低價吧檯（=public bar），酒吧（=public house）；公共場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to people in general, or to all the people in a particular country or community, as <b>the public</b>. 公眾","examples":["The park is now open to the public. 那公園現在對公眾開放了。","Pure alcohol is not for sale to the general public. 純酒精是不對大眾銷售的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a set of people in a country who share a common interest, activity, or characteristic as a particular kind of <b>public</b>. 群體","examples":["Market research showed that 93% of the viewing public wanted a hit movie channel. 市場調查顯示，93%的收視群體希望有一個熱門電影頻道。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Public</b> means relating to all the people in a country or community. 公眾的","examples":["The president is attempting to drum up public support for his economic programme. 總統正試圖為他的經濟計劃爭取公眾的支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Public</b> means relating to the government or state, or things that are done for the people by the state. 政府的","examples":["The social services account for a substantial part of public spending. 社會服務性事業佔政府開支的相當大的一部分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Public</b> buildings and services are provided for everyone to use. (建築、服務) 公共的","examples":["...the New York Public Library. …紐約公共圖書館。","The new museum must be accessible by public transportation. 新博物館必須能通公共交通。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>public</b> place is one where people can go about freely and where you can easily be seen and heard. (地方) 公共的","examples":["...the heavily congested public areas of international airports. …國際機場裡嚴重擁擠的公共區域。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone is a <b>public figure</b> or in <b>public life</b>, many people know who they are because they are often mentioned in newspapers and on television. 公眾熟悉的","examples":["He hit out at public figures who commit adultery. 他猛烈抨擊犯通姦的公眾人物。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Public</b> is used to describe statements, actions, and events that are made or done in such a way that any member of the public can see them or be aware of them. (陳述、行為、事件) 公開的","examples":["...a public inquiry into the most grievous breakdown in security our nation has ever known. …對我們國家迄今所知最嚴重的安全體系崩潰的公開的調查。","The comments were the governor's first detailed public statement on the subject. 這些評論是州長在這個問題上的首個詳盡的、公開的宣告。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a fact is made <b>public</b> or becomes <b>public</b>, it becomes known to everyone rather than being kept secret. (事實) 公開的","examples":["The facts could cause embarrassment if they ever became public. 如果公開的話，這些事實可能會引起尷尬。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"政府地","examples":["...publicly funded legal services. …政府資助的法律服務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"公開地","examples":["He never spoke publicly about the affair. 他從未公開地談論過此事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company <b>goes public</b>, it starts selling its shares on the stock exchange. 上市","examples":["The company went public at $21 per share. 這家公司以每股$21的價格上市了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say or do something <b>in public</b>, you say or do it when a group of people are present. 當眾","examples":["I probably won't be performing in public much. 我很可能不會再經常當眾演出。"]}]}]},"queen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女王，女首領；王后；（某一活動的）出眾的女子，精髓；（節日或活動中）當選要職的女子；（紙牌中的）Q牌，王后；（國際象棋中的）王后；（蜜蜂、螞蟻等的）王，後；母貓；<非正式>（舉止像女人的）男同性戀者；<非正式> 愛妻，女朋友"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（國際象棋）使（兵）變後；（女人）對……擺架子，對……專橫跋扈；使……成為女王或王后；做女王"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>queen</b> is a woman who rules a country as its monarch. 女王","examples":["...Queen Victoria. …維多利亞女王。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>queen</b> is a woman who is married to a king. 王后","examples":["The king and queen had fled. 國王和王后已經逃跑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a woman as <b>the</b> <b>queen</b> <b>of</b> a particular activity, you mean that she is well-known for being very good at it. 出眾的女子","examples":["...the queen of crime writing. …犯罪小說之王。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>queen</b> is a male homosexual who dresses and speaks rather like a woman. 男同性戀中的女性角色","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In chess, the <b>queen</b> is the most powerful piece. It can be moved in any direction. (國際象棋中的) 後","examples":["Chris will either have to take his queen's knight and lose his own knight, or he'll lose a rook. 克里斯要麼吃掉他的後翼馬而失去自己的馬，要麼失去一個車。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>queen</b> is a playing card with a picture of a queen on it. (紙牌中的) 王后","examples":["...the queen of spades. …黑桃王后。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>queen</b> or a <b>queen bee</b> is a large female bee which can lay eggs. 蜂王","examples":["Glass hives offer a close-up view of the bees at work, with the queen bee in each hive marked by a white dot. 玻璃蜂房可以近距離觀察工作中的蜜蜂，每個蜂房的蜂王都被打上白點標記。"]}]}]},"purpose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目的，意圖；目標，計劃；（達到生活中目標的）決心，毅力；（情勢等的）需要，用意（purposes）；重要意義，有價值的意義"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"有意，打算"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>purpose</b> of something is the reason for which it is made or done. 目的; 用途","examples":["The purpose of the occasion was to raise money for medical supplies. 此次活動的目的是為醫療用品籌款。","...the use of nuclear energy for military purposes. …軍事用途的核能的使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>purpose</b> is the thing that you want to achieve. 目標","examples":["They might well be prepared to do you harm in order to achieve their purpose. 他們很可能有備而來傷害你，以實現其目標。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Purpose</b> is the feeling of having a definite aim and of being determined to achieve it. 意志","examples":["The teachers are enthusiastic and have a sense of purpose. 教師們熱情高漲，感到很有奔頭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on purpose</b>, you do it intentionally. 故意地","examples":["Was it an accident or did David do it on purpose? 這是個意外呢，還是戴維故意乾的？"]}]}]},"railroad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>鐵路，鐵軌；<美>鐵路公司，鐵路部門"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迫使……倉促行事，強迫……做；迫使……草率透過；<美>輕率判處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>railroad</b> is a route between two places along which trains travel on steel rails. 鐵路","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>railroad</b> is a company or organization that operates railway routes. 鐵路公司","examples":["The Chicago and Northwestern Railroad wouldn't go along with that arrangement and said it would shut down completely. 芝加哥西北鐵路公司不同意那項安排並說要徹底停止。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>railroad</b> someone <b>into</b> doing something, you make them do it although they do not really want to, by hurrying them and putting pressure on them. (透過催促和施壓) 迫使某人做某事","examples":["He more or less railroaded the rest of Europe into recognizing the new \"independent\" states. 他或多或少地強迫了歐洲其他國家承認這些新“獨立”的國家。"]}]}]},"radio":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收音機；無線電收發裝置；無線電通訊；無線電廣播節目；無線電廣播事業；廣播電臺（或頻道）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用無線電通訊（或傳送資訊）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Radio</b> is the broadcasting of programmes for the public to listen to, by sending out signals from a transmitter. 無線電廣播","examples":["The last 12 months have been difficult ones for local radio. 最近的12個月對地方廣播電臺來說是艱難的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the programmes broadcast by radio stations as <b>the radio</b>. 無線電廣播節目","examples":["A lot of people listen to the radio in the mornings. 很多人早上收聽廣播節目。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>radio</b> is the piece of equipment that you use in order to listen to radio programmes. 收音機","examples":["He sat down in the armchair and turned on the radio. 他在扶手椅上坐下來，開啟了收音機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Radio</b> is a system of sending sound over a distance by transmitting electrical signals. 無線電通訊系統","examples":["They are in twice daily radio contact with the rebel leader. 他們一天兩次透過無線電通訊系統與反叛者領導人保持聯絡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>radio</b> is a piece of equipment that is used for sending and receiving messages. 無線電收發裝置","examples":["Judge Bruce Laughland praised the courage of the young policeman, who managed to raise the alarm on his radio. 布魯斯·勞赫蘭法官讚揚了那名年輕警察的勇氣，該警察設法透過自己的無線電收發裝置發出了警報。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>radio</b> someone, you send a message to them by radio. 用無線電傳送","examples":["The officer radioed for advice. 那名軍官發電請求指示。"]}]}]},"quiet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕聲的，安靜的；不出聲的；沉默寡言的，文靜的；寂靜的，平靜的；不受打擾的，悠然的；（感情）不外露的，不張揚的；秘密的，私下的；（顏色、服飾）素淨的，樸素大方的；清淡的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"安靜，靜謐"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>（使）平靜，安靜；<美>消除，減輕（恐懼），平息（抱怨）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>quiet</b> makes only a small amount of noise. 輕聲的; 安靜的","examples":["Tania kept the children reasonably quiet and contented. 塔妮婭把孩子們料理得安心而滿足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place is <b>quiet</b>, there is very little noise there. 寂靜的","examples":["She was received in a small, quiet office. 她在一間寂靜的小辦公室裡受到接見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place, situation, or time is <b>quiet</b>, there is no excitement, activity, or trouble. 平靜的; 清靜的","examples":["...a quiet rural backwater. …一個清靜的鄉間隱蔽處。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>quiet</b>, you are not saying anything. 不出聲的","examples":["I told them to be quiet and go to sleep. 我叫他們不要說話，去睡覺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>quiet</b> person behaves in a calm way and is not easily made angry or upset. 冷靜的; 不易動怒的","examples":["He's a nice quiet man. 他是個冷靜的好男人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕聲地; 安靜地","examples":["\"This is goodbye, isn't it?\" she said quietly. “這就算告別了，不是嗎？”她輕聲地說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"平靜地; 清靜地","examples":["His most prized time, though, will be spent quietly on his farm. 不過，他最珍貴的時光將在自己的農場上平靜地度過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"不出聲地","examples":["Amy stood quietly in the doorway watching him. 艾米一聲不響地站在門口看著他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"寂靜","examples":["I miss the quietness of the countryside. 我懷念農村的寂靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Quiet</b> is silence. 安靜","examples":["He called for quiet and announced that the next song was in our honour. 他要求靜下來，並宣佈下一首歌是獻給我們的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep quiet about</b> something or <b>keep</b> something <b>quiet</b>, you do not say anything about it. 保守秘密","examples":["I told her to keep quiet about it. 我叫她對此保守秘密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is done <b>on the quiet</b>, it is done secretly or in such a way that people do not notice it. 秘密地","examples":["She'd promised to give him driving lessons, on the quiet, when no one could see. 她答應在無人看見時秘密地給他上駕駛課。"]}]}]},"question":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"問題，疑問；試題，題目；（待討論或處理的）事情，議題；不確定，懷疑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……提出問題，盤問；對……提出質疑（異議），懷疑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>question</b> is something that you say or write in order to ask a person about something. 問題","examples":["They asked a lot of questions about China. 他們問了許多有關中國的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"詢問","examples":["The police have detained thirty-two people for questioning. 警方拘留了32個人進行審問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is some <b>question</b> about something, you mean that there is doubt or uncertainty about it. If something is <b>in question</b> or has been <b>called</b> <b>into question</b>, doubt or uncertainty has been expressed about it. 疑問; 不確定","examples":["There's no question about their success. 他們毫無疑問會成功。","Her political future is in question. 她的政治前途還是個疑問。","My integrity has been called into question by people who have never spoken to me. 我的正直品行竟遭到素昧平生之人的質疑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>question</b> is a problem, matter, or point which needs to be considered. (需考慮的) 問題","examples":["But the whole question of aid is a tricky political one. 但是整個援助問題是個棘手的政治問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>questions</b> on an examination are the problems that test your knowledge or ability. 試題","examples":["That question did come up on the test. 那道題真的在試卷上出現了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>question</b> someone, you ask them a lot of questions about something. 詢問","examples":["This led the therapist to question Jim about his parents and their marriage. 這讓治療師詢問起吉姆關於其父母以及他們的婚姻情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>question</b> something, you have or express doubts about whether it is true, reasonable, or worthwhile. 懷疑","examples":["It never occurs to them to question the doctor's decisions. 他們從來沒有想到去懷疑那個醫生的決定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The person, thing, or time <b>in question</b> is one which you have just been talking about or which is relevant. 正被提及的; 有關的","examples":["Add up all the income you've received over the period in question. 把相關時期內你獲得的所有收入加起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>out of the question</b>, you are emphasizing that it is completely impossible or unacceptable. 完全不可能的; 不能接受的","examples":["For the homeless, private medical care is simply out of the question. 對於無家可歸的人來說，私人醫療保健簡直就是天方夜譚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pop the question</b>, you ask someone to marry you. 求婚","examples":["Stuart got serious quickly and popped the question six months later. 斯圖爾特很快認真起來，6個月後就求婚了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say <b>there is no question of</b> something happening, you are emphasizing that it is not going to happen. …是不可能的","examples":["There was no question of my blaming Janet. 我不可能責備珍妮特。"]}]}]},"rainbow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"彩虹；眾多花色品種，五顏六色的組合，五花八門的聚合；五彩繽紛的展示；多種顏色，五彩繽紛"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不同種族（或文化等）人群的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rainbow</b> is an arch of different colours that you can sometimes see in the sky when it is raining. 彩虹","examples":["...silk and satin in every shade of the rainbow. …如彩虹般五顏六色的絲綢與錦緞。"]}]}]},"rain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雨，雨水；（熱帶地區的）雨季（the rains）；（降雨般的）一陣，（大量的）降落物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"下雨；（使）大量降落，雨點般落下；（使）如雨般地猛擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rain</b> is water that falls from the clouds in small drops. 雨","examples":["I hope you didn't get soaked standing out in the rain. 我希望你站在外面雨裡沒淋得渾身透溼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In countries where rain only falls in certain seasons, this rain is referred to as <b>the rains</b>. 雨季","examples":["...the spring, when the rains came. …春天，雨季來臨時。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When rain falls, you can say that <b>it is raining</b>. 下雨","examples":["It was raining hard, and she didn't have an umbrella. 雨下得很大，而她沒有帶傘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>rains</b> blows, kicks, or bombs <b>on</b> a person or place, the person or place is attacked by many blows, kicks, or bombs. You can also say that blows, kicks, or bombs <b>rain</b> <b>on</b> a person or place. 使像雨點般落下; 像雨點般落下","examples":["The police, raining blows on rioters and spectators alike, cleared the park. 警察對暴亂者和旁觀者都一陣猛打，清空了公園。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rain down</b> means the same as . 同(rain)","examples":["Fighter aircraft rained down high explosives. 戰鬥機如雨點般投下烈性炸彈。"]}]}]},"pull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拉，拽；拖動，移走；拔出，抽出；挪動，掙脫；拉開，拉上；牽引（車輛）；吃力地運轉；（使車輛）打斜；劃（船），划動；（迅速地）穿脫衣服；拉傷，扭傷；扳動，拉（開關）；犯下（罪行），使出（詭計）；吸引，影響；吸引異性；鼓勵，為……打氣；（把車）停在某處；拆開，拆散；從酒桶中取酒；取消，撤銷；深吸菸鬥（或煙）（pull at/on）；<非正式>舉止像（某人）；逮捕，拘留；控制（馬）的速度；把（球）從前方場地打向外場；（把球）擊向左側（右側）；列印（草樣，校樣）；（計算機）拉式檢索（資料）；（美橄）側翼迂迴阻擋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拉，拽；力，引力；吸引力，影響；<非正式>（對他人的）影響力；<英>艱難攀登；拉傷，扭傷；深吸，大口喝；拉手，拉繩，拉環；<英，非正式>性引誘；向左側（右側）的一擊；草樣，校樣；null"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>pull</b> something, you hold it firmly and use force in order to move it toward you or away from its previous position. 拉; 拔","examples":["They have pulled out patients' teeth unnecessarily. 他們毫無必要地拔掉了病人的牙。","Erica was solemn, pulling at her blonde curls. 埃麗卡表情嚴肅，拉扯著她金黃色的捲髮。","I helped pull him out of the water. 我幫著把他從水裡拉了出來。","Someone pulled her hair. 有人揪她的頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>pull</b> an object from a bag, pocket, or cabinet, you put your hand in and bring the object out. 掏出","examples":["Jack pulled the slip of paper from his shirt pocket. 傑克從襯衣口袋裡掏出那張紙條。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a vehicle, animal, or person <b>pulls</b> a cart or piece of machinery, they are attached to it or hold it, so that it moves along behind them when they move forward. 拉","examples":["He pulls a rickshaw, probably the oldest form of human taxi service. 他拉一輛黃包車，這可能是最古老形式的人類計程車服務。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pull yourself</b> or <b>pull</b> a part of your body in a particular direction, you move your body or a part of your body with effort or force. (使勁) 移動","examples":["Hughes pulled himself slowly to his feet. 休斯挪動身體，慢慢地站了起來。","He pulled his arms out of the sleeves. 他把雙臂從袖子裡抽了出來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>pull</b> something <b>apart</b>, you break or divide it into small pieces, often in order to put them back together again in a different way. 拆下","examples":["If I wanted to improve the car significantly I would have to pull it apart and start again. 如果我想大大提高這輛車的效能，我就得將它拆開來重新組裝。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>pull</b> crowds, viewers, or voters means to attract them. 吸引","examples":["The organizers have to employ performers to pull a crowd. 那些組織者不得不僱表演者來吸引群眾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pull</b> is also a noun. 拉; 拔","examples":["The feather must be removed with a straight, firm pull. 羽毛必須筆直地用力一拔才能拔掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pull</b> is a strong physical force that causes things to move in a particular direction. 引力","examples":["...the pull of gravity. …地心引力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a driver or vehicle <b>pulls to</b> a stop or a halt, the vehicle stops. 停車","examples":["He pulled to a stop behind a pickup truck. 他把車停在了一輛小型貨車後面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a race or contest, if you <b>pull ahead of</b> or <b>pull away from</b> an opponent, you gradually increase the amount by which you are ahead of them. 逐漸拉開 (領先的距離)","examples":["He pulled away, extending his lead to 15 seconds. 他甩開了對手，領先優勢擴大到了15秒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pull in</b> means the same as . 吸引","examples":["They provided a far better news service and pulled in many more viewers. 他們提供了好得多的新聞節目，吸引了更多的觀眾。"]}]}]},"race":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賽跑，速度競賽；競爭，角逐；賽馬會（the races）；人種，種族；民族；（動植物）種，屬；（具有共同特徵的）一群（或一批）人（或物）；急流；溝槽，通道；<古>血統，門第"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（和……）比賽，參加比賽；使（動物或車輛）參賽參賽；（使）快速移動，快速運轉；疾走，全速行進；競相，趕（時間）；（因害怕、興奮而）急速跳動，快速轉動；（發動機）猛轉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>race</b> is a competition to see who is the fastest, for example in running, swimming, or driving. (速度的) 比賽","examples":["The women's race was won by the only American in the field, Patti Sue Plumer. 女子賽跑被田賽場上惟一的一名美國人帕蒂·休·普盧默贏得了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The races</b> are a series of horse races that are held in a particular place on a particular day. People go to watch and to bet on which horse will win. 賽馬會","examples":["The high point of this trip was a day at the races. 這次旅行的高潮是在賽馬會上度過的一天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>race</b> is a situation in which people or organizations compete with each other for power or control. 競爭","examples":["The race for the White House begins in earnest today. 為入主白宮而展開的競選今天正式開始。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>race</b> is one of the major groups which human beings can be divided into according to their physical features, such as the colour of their skin. 種族","examples":["The college welcomes students of all races, faiths, and nationalities. 該學院歡迎來自各種族、有各種宗教信仰和國籍的學生。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a ginger root 姜根","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>race</b>, you take part in a race. 參賽; 與…比賽","examples":["In the 10 years I raced in Europe, 30 drivers were killed. 我在歐洲參賽的10年間，有30名車手身亡。","We raced them to the summit. 我們和他們一路賽跑到最高點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>race</b> a vehicle or animal, you prepare it for races and make it take part in races. 使參賽 (多指車輛或動物)","examples":["He still raced sports cars as often as he could. 他仍然儘可能頻繁地開著跑車參加比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>race</b> somewhere, you go there as quickly as possible. 疾走","examples":["He raced across town to the State House building. 他急速穿過市區去州議會大廈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>races</b> toward a particular state or position, it moves very fast toward that state or position. (向某種狀態或位置) 快速發展; 快速運動","examples":["Do they realize we are racing toward complete economic collapse? 他們是否意識到我們正迅速走向徹底的經濟崩潰？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your mind <b>races</b>, or if thoughts <b>race</b> through your mind, you think very fast about something, especially when you are in a difficult or dangerous situation. (尤指在面臨困難或危險時大腦) 急速運轉","examples":["I made sure I sounded calm but my mind was racing. 我確保自己聽起來很平靜，但大腦卻在急速運轉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your heart <b>races</b>, it beats very quickly because you are excited or afraid. (心臟因激動或恐懼而) 急速跳動","examples":["Her heart raced uncontrollably. 她的心臟難以控制地急速跳動起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe a situation as a <b>race against time</b> when you have to work very fast in order to do something before a particular time, or before another thing happens. 與時間賽跑","examples":["A spokesman said the rescue operation was a race against time. 一位發言人說該營救工作是在與時間賽跑。"]}]}]},"rat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"老鼠；<非正式>卑鄙小人（尤指欺詐或變節者）；<非正式> 常客，常待在某處的人；<美>（為頭髮定型做出飽滿效果的）女用發墊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捕（捉）老鼠，滅鼠；<非正式> 告發，告密；<非正式> 背信棄義，食言；<美>用發墊給（頭髮）定型"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（rats） <非正式>胡說，去你的（用以表示輕度煩惱，惱怒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rat</b> is an animal which has a long tail and looks like a large mouse. 老鼠","examples":["This was demonstrated in a laboratory experiment with rats. 這點透過在實驗室中用老鼠做試驗得到證明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>rat</b>, you mean that you are angry with them or dislike them, often because they have cheated you or betrayed you. 卑鄙小人","examples":["What did you do with the gun you took from that little rat Turner? 你要用從卑鄙小人特納那裡弄來的那支槍幹什麼呢？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>rats on</b> you, they tell someone in authority about things that you have done, especially bad things. 告發","examples":["They were accused of encouraging children to rat on their parents. 他們被指控慫恿孩子們告發他們的父母。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>rats on</b> an agreement, they do not do what they said they would do. 違約","examples":["She claims he ratted on their divorce settlement. 她聲稱他違背了他們的離婚協議。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smell a rat</b>, you begin to suspect or realize that something is wrong in a particular situation, for example that someone is trying to deceive you or harm you. 感覺事情不妙","examples":["If I don't send a picture, he will smell a rat. 如果我不寄張照片，他會起疑心。"]}]}]},"push":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推，移動；按；擠，推搡；推動，促使；推銷，推廣；說服，強迫；鼓勵，督促；努力爭取；堅持地做；（軍隊）挺進；趕走；販賣（毒品）；<非正式>接近（某年齡或數字）；使（棧）準備接收頂層資料；對（底片）作增感處理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"推 ；按；努力；鼓勵，敦促；挺進，進攻 ；毅力，進取心；<非正式>棘手的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>push</b> something, you use force to make it move away from you or away from its previous position. 推","examples":["The woman pushed back her chair and stood up. 那女人把椅子向後一推，站了起來。","They pushed him into the car. 他們把他推進了汽車。","...a pregnant woman pushing a stroller. …一位推著嬰兒車的孕婦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>push through</b> things that are blocking your way or <b>push</b> your <b>way through</b> them, you use force in order to move past them. 擠過","examples":["I pushed through the crowds and on to the escalator. 我擠過人群，上了自動扶梯。","Dix pushed forward carrying a glass. 迪克斯拿著一個玻璃杯往前擠。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>push</b> a value or amount <b>up</b> or <b>down</b> means to cause it to increase or decrease. 推動 (價值、數量上升或下降)","examples":["Any shortage could push up grain prices. 任何短缺都會推動糧價上漲。","The government had done everything it could to push down inflation. 政府已經竭盡全力遏制通貨膨脹。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>pushes</b> an idea or project in a particular direction, they cause it to develop or progress in a particular way. 使發展; 推進","examples":["China would use its influence to help push forward the peace process. 中國將會利用其影響力幫助推進和平程序。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>push</b> someone <b>to</b> do something or <b>push</b> them <b>into</b> doing it, you encourage or force them to do it. 鼓勵; 逼迫","examples":["She thanks her parents for keeping her in school and pushing her to study. 她感謝她的父母一直讓她上學，並鼓勵她學習。","Jason did not push her into stealing the money. 賈森並沒有逼迫她去偷那錢。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>pushes</b> an idea, a point, or a product, they try in a forceful way to convince people to accept it or buy it. 力勸…接受 (思想、論點); 推銷 (產品)","examples":["The commissioners will push the case for opening the plant. 委員們將力陳開辦此廠的理由。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When someone <b>pushes</b> drugs, they sell them illegally. 販賣 (毒品)","examples":["You would be on welfare with your kids pushing drugs to pay the rent. 你將靠福利救濟過活，靠你的孩子們販毒來支付租金。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Push</b> is also a noun. 推","examples":["He gave me a sharp push. 他猛地推了我一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Push</b> is also a noun. 挺進","examples":["All that was needed was one final push, and the enemy would be vanquished once and for all. 只需要最後一次挺進，敵軍就將被徹底擊敗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Push</b> is also a noun. 鼓勵; 逼迫","examples":["We need a push to take the first step. 我們需要鼓勵來邁出第一步。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Push</b> is also a noun. 努力; 勸服","examples":["In its push for economic growth it has ignored projects that would improve living standards. 在努力追求經濟增長的同時卻忽視了改善生活水平的專案。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an army <b>pushes into</b> a country or area that it is attacking or invading, it moves further into it. 挺進","examples":["One detachment pushed into the eastern suburbs toward the airfield. 一支小分隊挺進了東郊往機場去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>push for</b> something, you try very hard to achieve it or to persuade someone to do it. 努力爭取; 力勸…做","examples":["Doctors are pushing for a ban on all cigarette advertising. 醫生們正力求禁止所有香菸廣告。"]}]}]},"red":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紅的，紅色的；（毛髮）紅褐色的；（臉）漲紅的；（眼睛）充血的，紅腫的；（葡萄酒）紅色的；（表示停止）紅（燈），紅（旗）；被禁止的，危險的；（美國政治）支援共和黨的；革命的，激進的，赤色的（尤指冷戰期間指前蘇聯）；（紙牌）紅桃的，紅方塊的；（人）紅種的；沾有鮮血的；流血的（古或詩/文）；（物理）（表示夸克三種色荷之一的）紅色的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"紅色，紅顏料；紅衣；紅葡萄酒；赤字，虧空，負債；激進分子；（Red）雷德（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"整理（同 redd）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>red</b> is the colour of blood or fire. 紅色 (的)","examples":["...a bunch of red roses. …一束紅色的玫瑰花。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone's face is <b>red</b>, you mean that it is redder than its normal colour, because they are embarrassed, angry, or out of breath. 臉紅的","examples":["With a bright red face I was forced to admit that I had no real idea. 我滿臉通紅，被迫承認我其實沒有什麼想法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You describe someone's hair as <b>red</b> when it is between red and brown in colour. (頭髮) 紅褐色的","examples":["...a girl with red hair. …一位紅褐色頭髮的女孩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a U.S. state is described as <b>red</b>, it means that the majority of its residents vote for the Republican Party in elections, especially in the presidential elections. 支援共和黨的","examples":["...policies that could guarantee her enough support in red states to win the White House in 2008. …保證她能在支援共和黨的各個州獲得足夠支援以在2008年白宮的競選中獲勝的政策。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to red wine as <b>red</b>. 紅葡萄酒","examples":["The spicy flavours in these dishes call for reds rather than whites. 這些菜餚味道辛辣，宜配紅葡萄酒而不是白葡萄酒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or company is <b>in the red</b> or if their bank account is <b>in the red</b>, they have spent more money than they have in their account and therefore they owe money to the bank. 負債的","examples":["The theatre is $500,000 in the red. 劇院負債50萬美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>see red</b>, you suddenly become very angry. 勃然大怒","examples":["I didn't mean to break his nose. I just saw red. 我不是有意打破他的鼻子的。我只是一時憤怒。"]}]}]},"raise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提起，舉起；（使）直立，站立；建造，樹立（塑像等）；增加，提高；籌募，徵集；提出，提起；引起，使出現；飼養，種植；撫養，養育；使自乘……次；比（對手）多下賭注；叫醒；使復活；終止，解除；與……取得聯絡；（海上人員）駛近能看見（陸地或其他船隻）的地方；（免疫）刺激（抗血清、抗體等的）生成"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>加薪；（撲克牌或勃萊格牌用語）賭注加碼；（舉重）（持槓鈴時的）提，舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> something, you move it so that it is in a higher position. 舉起","examples":["He raised his hand to wave. 他舉起手來揮動。","Milton raised the glass to his lips. 米爾頓舉起杯子放到嘴唇邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> a flag, you display it by moving it up a pole or into a high place where it can be seen. 升起","examples":["They had raised the white flag in surrender. 他們已經升起白旗投降。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> <b>yourself</b>, you lift your body so that you are standing up straight, or so that you are no longer lying flat. 站立; 起身","examples":["He raised himself into a sitting position. 他起身坐了起來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> the rate or level of something, you increase it. 增加","examples":["The Federal Reserve Board is expected to raise interest rates. 聯邦儲備委員會預計將增加利率。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>raise</b> the standard of something means to improve it. 提高 (水平)","examples":["...a new drive to raise standards of literacy in New York's schools. …一場提高紐約各學校文化程度的新運動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> your <b>voice</b>, you speak more loudly, usually because you are angry. (常指因生氣) 提高 (嗓門)","examples":["Don't you raise your voice to me! 別對我高聲大氣！"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> money <b>for</b> a charity or an institution, you ask people for money which you collect on its behalf. 籌募 (資金)","examples":["...events held to raise money for flood victims. …為水患災民募捐而舉行的活動。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a person or company <b>raises</b> money that they need, they manage to get it, for example by selling their property or by borrowing. 籌措 (資金)","examples":["They raised the money to buy the house and two hundred acres of land. 他們籌措了資金來購買房子和200英畝土地。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If an event <b>raises</b> a particular emotion or question, it makes people feel the emotion or consider the question. 喚起; 引發","examples":["The agreement has raised hopes that the war may end soon. 合約喚起了戰爭也許很快會結束的希望。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> a subject, an objection, or a question, you mention it or bring it to someone's attention. 提出","examples":["He had been consulted and had raised no objections. 他已經被徵詢意見，並沒有提出異議。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Someone who <b>raises</b> a child takes care of it until it is grown up. 撫養","examples":["My mother was an amazing woman. She raised four of us kids virtually singlehandedly. 我母親是個了不起的女人。她幾乎是獨自撫養大了我們4個孩子。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone <b>raises</b> a particular type of animal or crop, they breed that type of animal or grow that type of crop. 飼養; 種植","examples":["He raises 2,000 acres of wheat and hay. 他種植了2000英畝的小麥和飼料用草。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>raise</b> is an increase in your wages or salary. 加薪","examples":[]}]}]},"rice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"稻，水稻；米，大米，稻米；米飯，白飯；（Rice）人名、姓氏，常譯作賴斯（英）、萊斯，亦譯裡瑟（瑞典）、裡採（塞）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把……搗成米糊狀；把（熟馬鈴薯等）壓（或擦）成米粒狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rice</b> consists of white or brown grains taken from a cereal plant. You cook rice and usually eat it with meat or vegetables. 米","examples":["...a meal consisting of chicken, rice, and vegetables. …有雞肉、米飯和蔬菜的一餐。"]}]}]},"reach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"到達，抵達；被看見，被聽到；達到（特定的水平或數量）；達到（一個特定的時間或階段）；（經討論或思考後）達成，實現；伸，伸手；能伸到，能夠到；把……遞給；（大或長等）足夠達到；（用電話等）與……聯絡；影響，打動；（航海）橫風航駛；為……提供幫助（reach out to）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（臂的）伸出；伸手可及的距離；可到達的距離；（權力或能力）能及的範圍；邊遠地區；層級，層次；河段，直水道；（特定時期內）觀眾人數，聽眾人數；（航海）橫風行程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>reaches</b> a place, they arrive there. 到達 (某地)","examples":["He did not stop until he reached the door. 他到門口才停住。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something has <b>reached</b> a certain stage, level, or amount, they are at that stage, level, or amount. 達到 (某一階段、水平或數量)","examples":["The process of political change in South Africa has reached the stage where it is irreversible. 南非的政治變革程序已經到了不可逆轉的階段。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you can <b>reach</b> something, you are able to touch it by stretching out your arm or leg. (伸展手臂或腿) 夠到","examples":["Can you reach your toes with your fingertips? 你能用手指尖觸到腳趾頭嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you try to <b>reach</b> someone, you try to contact them, usually by telephone. (常指透過電話) 聯絡上 (某人)","examples":["Has the doctor told you how to reach him or her in emergencies? 醫生有沒有告訴你在緊急狀況下如何聯絡上他或她？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>reaches</b> a place, point, or level, it extends as far as that place, point, or level. 延伸到; 延伸","examples":["...a nightshirt that reached to his knees. …一件長及他膝蓋的男用睡衣。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When people <b>reach</b> an agreement or a decision, they succeed in achieving it. 達成","examples":["A meeting of agriculture ministers has so far failed to reach agreement over farm subsidies. 農業部長們的會議到目前為止還沒有達成有關農業補貼的協議。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reach</b> somewhere, you move your arm and hand to take or touch something. 伸手去 (拿或夠東西)","examples":["Judy reached into her handbag and handed me a small, printed leaflet. 朱迪把手伸進手提袋中，遞給我一張小小的印刷傳單。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>reach</b> is the distance or limit to which they can stretch, extend, or travel. (人或物所能及的) 距離; 限度","examples":["Isabelle placed a wine cup on the table within his reach. 伊莎貝爾把一隻酒杯放在桌上他伸手可及的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place or thing is within <b>reach</b>, it is possible to have it or get to it. If it is out of <b>reach</b>, it is not possible to have it or get to it. 可及的範圍","examples":["It is located within reach of many important Norman towns, including Bayeux. 它位於諾曼許多重要城鎮的附近，包括巴約。"]}]}]},"reason":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"原因，理由；充分理由，正當理由；道理，情理；判斷力，理智"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"推理，邏輯思考；推論出，推斷出（reason sth. out）；對（某人）以理相勸，勸告（reason with）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>reason</b> <b>for</b> something is a fact or situation which explains why it happens or what causes it to happen. 原因","examples":["There is a reason for every important thing that happens. 發生的每一件重要事情都是有原因的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you have <b>reason</b> <b>to</b> believe something or <b>to</b> have a particular emotion, you mean that you have evidence for your belief or there is a definite cause of your feeling. 道理; 理由","examples":["They had reason to believe there could be trouble. 他們有理由相信會有麻煩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The ability that people have to think and to make sensible judgments can be referred to as <b>reason</b>. 理智","examples":["...a conflict between emotion and reason. …情感與理智的衝突。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reason</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you decide that it is true after thinking carefully about all the facts. 推斷","examples":["I reasoned that changing my diet would lower my cholesterol level. 我推斷改變我的飲食會降低我的膽固醇水平。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing happens <b>by reason of</b> another, it happens because of it. 因為","examples":["The boss retains enormous influence by reason of his position. 老闆因為職位的關係保持著巨大的影響力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you try to make someone <b>listen to reason</b>, you try to persuade them to listen to sensible arguments and be influenced by them. 聽從道理","examples":["The company's top executives had refused to listen to reason. 公司的高階主管們拒絕聽從道理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something happened or was done <b>for no reason</b>, <b>for no good reason</b>, or <b>for no reason at all</b>, you mean that there was no obvious reason why it happened or was done. 無緣無故","examples":["The guards, he said, would punch them for no reason. 他說看守人員們會無緣無故地用拳頭打他們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you will do anything <b>within reason</b>, you mean that you will do anything that is fair or reasonable and not too extreme. 合情合理的; 正當的","examples":["I will take any job that comes along, within reason. 我有什麼工作就幹什麼，只要是正當的。"]}]}]},"river":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"河，江；（River）人名；（英）裡弗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>river</b> is a large amount of fresh water flowing continuously in a long line across the land. 河; 江","examples":["...a chemical plant on the banks of the river. …這條河岸上的一家化工廠。"]}]}]},"report":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"報告，彙報；新聞報道；官方檔案，調查報告；傳聞，傳說；<英>（學生）成績報告單；<法律>案情報告；下屬；<正式>爆炸聲，槍聲；<舊>謠言，流傳；<古>名譽，名聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"報道；據說，傳聞；述說，報告；公告，公佈；舉報（罪案）， 報告（事故）；報到；描述（感情、病情等）；<英>（議會委員會主席）正式宣佈委員會已討論（法案）；<美>（議會委員會）將法案交還給議會表決；對（上級或監督者）負責，由......領導；告發，檢舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>report</b> something that has happened, you tell people about it. 報告; 告知","examples":["I reported the theft to the police. 我向警察報告了這起盜竊案。","The officials also reported that two more ships were apparently heading for Malta. 官員們也報告說另有兩艘船顯然正朝馬耳他駛去。","\"He seems to be all right now,\" reported a relieved Taylor. “他現在似乎完全好了，”泰勒放心地報告說。","She reported him missing the next day. 她第二天報告說他失蹤了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>reports</b> you <b>to</b> a person in authority, they tell that person about something wrong that you have done. 告發; 控告","examples":["His ex-wife reported him to police a few days later. 他前妻幾天後向警察告發了他。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>report</b> <b>on</b> an event or subject, you tell people about it, because it is your job or duty to do so. 報道; (工作或職責上) 彙報","examples":["Many journalists based outside of Sudan have been refused visas to enter the country to report on political affairs. 很多駐在蘇丹境外的記者遭到拒籤，無法進入該國報道政治事件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>report</b> <b>to</b> a person or place, you go to that person or place and say that you are ready to start work or say that you are present. 報到","examples":["Mr. Ashwell has to surrender his passport and report to the police every five days. 阿什維爾先生不得不交出他的護照，而且每5天去警察局報到一次。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that one employee <b>reports</b> <b>to</b> another, you mean that the first employee is told what to do by the second one and is responsible to them. 隸屬; 被…領導","examples":["He reported to a section chief, who reported to a division chief, and so on up the line. 他受科長領導，科長受處長領導，如此逐級向上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>report</b> is a news article or broadcast which gives information about something that has just happened. (報刊或廣播電視上的) 報道","examples":["According to a report in the newspaper, he still has control over the remaining shares. 根據報紙上的報道，他依然控制著剩餘的股份。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>report</b> is an official document which a group of people issue after investigating a situation or event. (調查) 報告","examples":["The education committee will today publish its report on the supply of teachers for the next decade. 教育委員會今天將公佈關於今後十年師資儲備的報告。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>report</b> on something, you tell them what has been happening. 報告; 告知","examples":["She came back to give us a progress report on how the project is going. 她回來給我們做了專案進展情況的報告。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that there are <b>reports</b> that something has happened, you mean that some people say it has happened but you have no direct evidence of it. 傳聞","examples":["There are unconfirmed reports that two people have been shot in the neighbouring town of Springfield. 根據未經證實的傳聞，有兩個人在鄰近斯普林菲爾德的城鎮遭到槍擊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>report</b> is an official written account of how well or how badly a pupil has done during the term or year that has just finished. 成績單","examples":["The only time I got their attention was when I brought home straight A's on my report. 我僅有一次引起他們注意的是在我把全A的成績單拿回家的時候。"]}]}]},"rest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"休息，歇息；使（運動員）暫時離隊； （問題，事情）被擱置；（被）支撐，（使）倚靠；安息，長眠；在於，存放於；（目光）停留（rest on）；依靠，仰仗（rest on/upon）；寄（希望）於，相信；讓（土地）休耕；（原告或被告）完成向法庭提出證據（或辯論）；保持不變；<英>（演員）無戲可演"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"休息（時間）；剩餘部分，餘下的人（物）（the rest）；靜止，停止；（音樂的）休止，休止符；（演說或詩句的）停頓；撐架，支座；（剖）（器官或組織的）一小碎塊；（網球）對打，回合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The rest</b> is used to refer to all the parts of something or all the things in a group that remain or that you have not already mentioned. 其餘部分","examples":["It was an experience I will treasure for the rest of my life. 這是一次我將終生珍視的經歷。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rest</b> is also a pronoun. 其餘部分","examples":["The first payment was made yesterday, and the rest will be paid next month. 第一筆款在昨天支付了，其餘部分將在下個月支付。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to continue to be (as specified); remain 仍然是; 保持不變","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can add <b>and the rest</b> or <b>all the rest of it</b> to the end of a statement or list when you want to refer in a vague way to other things that are associated with the ones you have already mentioned. 諸如此類; 如此等等","examples":["...a man with nice clothes, an SUV, and the rest. …一個衣著考究、開一輛四輪驅動，諸如此類的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an object that has been moving <b>comes to rest</b>, it finally stops. 停止","examples":["The plane had ploughed a path through a patch of forest before coming to rest in a field. 該飛機從一小塊森林中間犁出一條小徑，而後停在一片曠野上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone refuses to <b>let</b> a subject <b>rest</b>, they refuse to stop talking about it, especially after they have been talking about it for a long time. 停止談論","examples":["I am not prepared to let this matter rest. 我不準備停止談論這件事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>put</b> someone's <b>mind at rest</b> or <b>set</b> their <b>mind at rest</b> means to tell them something that stops them from worrying. 使某人安心","examples":["A brain scan last Friday finally set his mind at rest. 上週五進行的一次腦部掃描終於讓他安心了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rest</b> or if you <b>rest</b> your body, you do not do anything active for a time. 休息","examples":["He's tired and exhausted, and has been advised to rest for two weeks. 他勞累而疲憊，被建議休息兩個星期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rest</b> something somewhere, you put it there so that its weight is supported. 使倚靠","examples":["He rested his arms on the back of the chair. 他把他的兩條胳膊倚在那把椅子的靠背上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is resting</b> somewhere, or if you <b>are resting</b> it there, it is in a position where its weight is supported. 靠放","examples":["His head was resting on her shoulder. 他的頭正靠在她的肩上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get some <b>rest</b> or have a <b>rest</b>, you do not do anything active for a time. 休息","examples":["\"You're worn out, Laura,\" he said. \"Go home and get some rest.\" “你太累了，勞拉，”他說。“回家休息一下吧。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rest</b> is an object that is used to support something, especially your head, arms, or feet. 支架","examples":["When you are sitting, keep your elbow on the arm rest. 當你坐著的時候，把胳膊肘靠在扶手上。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a theory or someone's success <b>rests</b> <b>on</b> a particular thing, it depends on that thing. 依賴","examples":["Such a view rests on a number of incorrect assumptions. 這一觀點基於一些錯誤的假定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If authority, a responsibility, or a decision <b>rests</b> <b>with</b> you, you have that authority or responsibility, or you are the one who will make that decision. 取決","examples":["The final decision rested with the president. 最終決定取決於該總統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>rest</b> on or against someone or something, you lean on them so that they support the weight of your body. 倚靠","examples":["He rested on his pickaxe for a while. 他在他的鎬上倚靠了一會兒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your eyes <b>rest</b> <b>on</b> a particular person or object, you look directly at them, rather than somewhere else. (目光) 停留","examples":["As she spoke, her eyes rested on her husband's face. 當她說話的時候，目光停留在她丈夫的臉上。"]}]}]},"ride":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎馬，騎車；乘坐；航行，漂浮；穿越，翻越；（車輛）行駛；<美>數落，嘲弄；駕馭，被……所支配；取決於（ride on）；得益於；（騎馬或車）參賽；<南非>運輸（貨物）；突伸，重疊；順勢退躲以緩衝（擊打）；<俚>與……性交"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"乘騎旅行，搭乘旅行；大型遊樂設施，乘坐裝置；免費搭車；<美>搭載別人者；行車質量，乘坐感覺；<美，非正式>機動車輛；騎馬道；<加>騎馬錶演；<俚>性交，交媾；節奏鈸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ride</b> a horse, you sit on it and control its movements. 騎 (馬); 騎馬","examples":["I saw a girl riding a horse. 我看見一個騎著馬的女孩。","Can you ride? 你會騎馬嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>ride</b> a bicycle or a motorcycle, you sit on it, control it, and travel along on it. 騎 (腳踏車或摩托車); 騎車","examples":["Riding a bike is great exercise. 騎腳踏車是很好的鍛鍊。","Two men riding on motorcycles opened fire on him. 兩個騎在摩托車上的人向他開了槍。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ride</b> <b>in</b> a vehicle such as a car, you travel in it. 乘坐","examples":["He prefers travelling on the subway to riding in a limousine. 他寧願乘坐地鐵出行而不願乘坐豪華加長轎車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>is riding on</b> another, you mean that the first thing depends on the second thing. 依賴於; 取決於","examples":["Billions of dollars are riding on the outcome of the election. 數十億美元取決於選舉的結果。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ride</b> is a trip on a horse or bicycle, or in a vehicle. (騎馬、騎車、乘車的) 旅程","examples":["She took some friends for a ride in the family car. 她用私家車載了朋友們一程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In an amusement park, a <b>ride</b> is a large machine that people ride on for fun. (遊樂園中的) 飛車","examples":["...roller coasters or other thrill rides at amusement parks. …遊樂園裡的過山車或其他的飛車娛樂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone faces <b>a rough ride</b>, you mean that things are going to be difficult for them because people will criticize them a lot or treat them badly. 難關","examples":["The president could face a rough ride unless the plan works. 除非計劃奏效，否則該總統會面臨一個難關。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>a free ride</b>, you mean that things are going to be very easy and that people will take advantage of this. 順利無阻的事","examples":["I've had an opponent every time. I've never had a free ride. I've had to fight. 每次我都有一個對手。我從未遇到一件一帆風順的事。我一直都得奮鬥。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has been taken for a ride</b>, you mean that they have been deceived or cheated. 受騙","examples":["You got taken for a ride. Why did you give him five thousand dollars? 你受騙了。你為什麼要給他5000美元？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>rides herd on</b> other people or their actions, they supervise them or watch them closely. 監督; 嚴管","examples":["...state efforts to ride herd on the oil companies. …國家嚴管石油公司的努力。","...Hank, who often stayed late riding herd on the day-to-day business of the magazine. …經常為監督雜誌社的日常事務而工作到很晚的漢克。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone who <b>rides the rails</b> travels by train, especially over a long period of time and without buying a ticket. (長期乘火車) 逃票","examples":["It is 1933, the height of the Great Depression, and the hobos are busy riding the rails. 那是1933年，經濟大蕭條的高峰期，流動工人們加緊在火車上逃票。"]}]}]},"robot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機器人，自動操作裝置；機器般的人；<南非>自動交通訊號機；（計算機）爬蟲程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>robot</b> is a machine that is programmed to move and perform certain tasks automatically. 機器人","examples":["...very lightweight robots that we could send to the moon for planetary exploration. …我們能夠送上月球用於行星探索的重量很輕的機器人。"]}]}]},"return":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"回來，回去；歸還，退還；回報，回應；（感覺或情況）重新出現，恢復；重新開始，繼續（某項活動）；帶來，產生（利潤或損失）；回擊，擊回； 宣告（裁決）；選舉，選出；（建築）（尤指成直角）轉延（牆壁）；（高爾夫）打後九穴；（美橄）截獲（對方傳、踢或漏球）反攻；（橋牌）（尤指同伴所攻出的同花色牌贏墩後）跟著打出，回出；把（空瓶或空罐頭盒）送到回收站"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"回來，返回；歸還，退回；重新開始，恢復；回報，收益；<英> 往返票，來回票；返回鍵，回車鍵；（選舉）結果；（網球等）回擊球；（納稅）申報表，申報單；（建築）轉延，轉延側面；迴路導線；被退回（或送回）的東西，退票；（可以回收的）空罐頭盒，空瓶子（returns）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（票）雙程的，往返的；（旅途）返回的，返程的；（比賽）回訪的；再度的，再次的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>return</b> <b>to</b> a place, you go back there after you have been away. 返回","examples":["There are unconfirmed reports that Aziz will return to Moscow within hours. 有未經證實的報道稱阿齊茲將在數小時內返回莫斯科。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a feeling or situation <b>returns</b>, it comes back or happens again after a period when it was not present. 再現; 恢復","examples":["Official reports in Algeria suggest that calm is returning to the country. 阿爾及利亞官方的報道暗示該國正在恢復平靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> <b>to</b> a state that you were in before, you start being in that state again. 恢復","examples":["Life has improved and returned to normal. 生活改善了且恢復了正常。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> <b>to</b> a subject that you have mentioned before, you begin talking about it again. 回到 (前面的話題)","examples":["The power of the church is one theme all these writers return to. 教會的權力是所有這些作家迴歸的一個主題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> <b>to</b> an activity that you were doing before, you start doing it again. 重新開始; 繼續 (做)","examples":["At that stage he will be 52, young enough to return to politics if he wishes to do so. 到那時候他將是52歲，足夠年輕，只要他願意還可以繼續從政。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>return</b> is your arrival back at a place where you had been before. 返回","examples":["Kenny explained the reason for his sudden return to Dallas. 肯尼解釋了他突然返回達拉斯的理由。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Return</b> is also a noun. 歸還","examples":["The main demand of the Indians is for the return of one-and-a-half-million acres of forest to their communities. 印第安人的主要要求是把150萬英畝的森林歸還給他們的族群。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Return</b> is also a noun. 再現; 恢復","examples":["It was like the return of his youth. 這好像是他青年重現。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Return</b> is also a noun. 恢復","examples":["He made an uneventful return to normal health. 他順利地恢復到了正常健康狀態。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Return</b> is also a noun. 重新開始; 繼續","examples":["He has not ruled out the shock possibility of a return to football. 他沒有排除重返足壇的這個驚人的可能性。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>return</b> <b>on</b> an investment is the profit that you get from it. 返利; 收益","examples":["Profits have picked up this year but the return on capital remains tiny. 利潤本年度上升了，但資本收益仍然很少。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> something that you have borrowed or taken, you give it back or put it back. 歸還","examples":["I enjoyed the book and said so when I returned it. 我很喜歡這本書，歸還它的時候就這麼說了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> something somewhere, you put it back where it was. 放回","examples":["He returned the notebook to his jacket. 他把筆記本放回自己的夾克裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>return</b> someone's action, you do the same thing to them as they have just done to you. If you <b>return</b> someone's feelings, you feel the same way toward them as they feel toward you. 回應; 回報","examples":["Back at the station the chief inspector returned the call. 回到警察局後，督察長回了電話。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a judge or jury <b>returns</b> a verdict, they announce whether they think the person on trial is guilty or not. 宣佈 (裁決)","examples":["They returned a verdict of not guilty. 他們宣佈了無罪判決。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>return</b> ticket is a ticket for a trip from one place to another and then back again. 往返的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>return</b> trip is the part of a trip that takes you back to where you started from. 返程的","examples":["Buy an extra ticket for the return trip. 額外再買一張返程票。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in return</b> <b>for</b> what someone else has done for you, you do it because they did that thing for you. 作為回報","examples":["You pay regular premiums and in return the insurance company will pay out a lump sum. 你定期交納保險費，作為回報，保險公司會一次性付給你一筆錢。"]}]}]},"road":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"路，公路，馬路，街； 途徑，方法，路子；（礦）地下巷道；<史>貿易路線；<美>鐵路；<英>（列車可通行的）無障礙鐵路路軌，特殊情況鐵路路軌；近岸錨地，港外錨地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>road</b> is a long piece of hard ground that is built between two places so that people can drive or ride easily from one place to the other. 公路","examples":["There was very little traffic on the roads. 那時這些公路上車輛很少。","We just go straight up the Boston Post Road. 我們就徑直沿著波士頓郵政大道走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>road</b> <b>to</b> a particular result is the means of achieving it or the process of achieving it. 途徑; 過程","examples":["We are bound to see some ups and downs along the road to recovery. 在復甦的道路上我們一定會經歷一些波折起伏。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>on the road</b> <b>to</b> something, you mean that they are likely to achieve it. 在 (取得成功的) 的道路上","examples":["The government took another step on the road to political reform. 政府又在政治改革的道路上邁進了一步。"]}]}]},"rooster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>公雞，雄雞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rooster</b> is an adult male chicken. 公雞","examples":[]}]}]},"roof":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"屋頂，車頂；（洞穴、礦井等的）頂部；口腔頂部，上顎；住處，棲身之處；（價格或工資的）最高限度，上限"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給......蓋上屋頂；覆遮，遮蔽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>roof</b> of a building is the covering on top of it that protects the people and things inside from the weather. 屋頂","examples":["...a small stone cottage with a red slate roof. …一座有一個紅石板屋頂的小石屋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>roof</b> of a car or other vehicle is the top part of it, which protects passengers or goods from the weather. (車的) 頂篷","examples":["The car rolled onto its roof, trapping him. 那輛小汽車翻了個底朝天，把他困在裡面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The roof of</b> your mouth is the highest part of the inside of your mouth. 上顎","examples":["She clicked her tongue against the roof of her mouth. 她用舌頭抵著上顎發出咔噠聲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the level of something such as the price of a product or the rate of inflation <b>goes through the roof</b>, it suddenly increases very rapidly indeed. 突然猛漲","examples":["Prices for Korean art have gone through the roof. 韓國藝術品價格突然猛漲了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hit the roof</b> or <b>go through the roof</b>, you become very angry, and usually show your anger by shouting at someone. 怒氣沖天","examples":["Sergeant Long will hit the roof when I tell him you've gone off. 如果我告訴朗警官你已經走了，他一定會怒火沖天的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a number of things or people are <b>under one roof</b> or <b>under the same roof</b>, they are in the same building. 在同一建築物裡","examples":["The firms intend to open either together under one roof or alongside each other in shopping malls. 這些公司打算要麼開在同一棟樓裡，要麼在商業街上比鄰而開。"]}]}]},"ring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戒指，指環；環狀物，圈形物；圓圈；圓形表演場（或競技場）；圍成一圈的人（或物）；團伙，幫派；鈴聲，鐘聲，按鈴，敲鐘；（說法、討論、辯論等的）特性；<英>圓形灶盤，爐頭；<俚>肛門；（化）環；（數）環"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"包圍；<英>繞……畫圓，把……圈起來；（尤指在動物身上）套環；敲鐘，按鈴；<英>（給……）打電話；嗡嗡作響；迴響；充滿；<非正式>非法將（汽車）改頭換面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a telephone <b>rings</b>, it makes a sound to let you know that someone is phoning you. (電話) 響鈴","examples":["As soon as he got home, the phone rang. 他一到家，電話就響了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>is ringing</b> <b>with</b> sound, usually pleasant sound, you mean that the place is completely filled with that sound. (優美的聲音) 迴盪","examples":["The whole place was ringing with music. 整個地方迴盪著音樂聲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ring</b> is also a noun. (電話) 響鈴聲","examples":["After at least eight rings, an ancient-sounding maid answered the phone. 電話至少八聲後，一位聽上去很老的女僕接了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(電話) 響鈴","examples":["She was jolted out of her sleep by the ringing of the telephone. 她被電話響鈴驚醒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ring</b> is also a noun. (鈴的) 響聲","examples":["There was a ring of the bell. 鈴響了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(鈴) 響","examples":["...the ringing of church bells. …教堂的鐘響。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>ring</b> to describe a quality that something such as a statement, discussion, or argument seems to have. For example, if an argument <b>has a familiar ring</b>, it seems familiar. 感覺","examples":["His proud boast of leading \"the party of low taxation\" has a hollow ring. 他有關領導“主張低稅收的政黨”的豪言有空洞的感覺。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>ring</b> is a small circle of metal or other substance that you wear on your finger as jewellery. 戒指","examples":["...a gold wedding ring. …一枚黃金婚戒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"An object or substance that is in the shape of a circle can be described as a <b>ring</b>. 環狀物; 圈","examples":["Frank took a large ring of keys from his pocket. 弗蘭克從口袋裡拿出了一個大串鑰匙。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A group of people or things arranged in a circle can be described as a <b>ring</b>. (人或物圍成的) 圈","examples":["They then formed a ring around the square. 他們隨後沿廣場圍成了一圈。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"At a boxing or wrestling match or a circus, the <b>ring</b> is the place where the contest or performance takes place. It consists of an enclosed space with seats around it. 圓形 (表演、競技) 場地","examples":["He will never again be allowed inside a boxing ring. 他將再也不會被允許進入拳擊場了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can refer to an organized group of people who are involved in an illegal activity as a <b>ring</b>. 團伙","examples":["Police are investigating the suspected drug ring at the school. 警方正在調查這所學校販毒嫌疑團夥。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ring</b> someone, you telephone them. 給…打電話","examples":["Would you ring me as soon as you find out? My number's in the phone book. 你一查清就給我打電話好嗎？我的號碼在電話簿裡。","A friend of mine gave me this number to call. 我的一個朋友讓我打這個號碼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>ring</b> a bell or when a bell <b>rings</b>, it makes a sound. 使 (鈴) 響; (鈴) 響","examples":["He heard the school bell ring. 他聽見學校的鈴響了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a building or place <b>is ringed</b> <b>with</b> or <b>by</b> something, it is surrounded by it. 圍住","examples":["The areas are sealed off and ringed by troops. 這一地區被封鎖了，被軍隊包圍了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ring up</b> means the same as <b>ring</b>. 給…打電話; 打電話","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to emit or cause to emit a sonorous or resonant sound, characteristic of certain metals when struck (撞擊金屬時)叮叮響","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone <b>a ring</b>, you phone them. 給某人電話","examples":["We'll give him a ring as soon as we get back. 我們一回來就會給他電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a statement <b>rings true</b>, it seems to be true or genuine. If it <b>rings hollow</b>, it does not seem to be true or genuine. 聽起來真實","examples":["Joanna's denial rang true. 喬安娜的否認聽上去像是真的。"]}]}]},"room":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房間，室；客房；<英，舊>（租用的）住所，寓所（rooms）；空間，地方；機會， 餘地；房間裡所有的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>租房，合住； <美>讓……同住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>room</b> is one of the separate sections or parts of the inside of a building. Rooms have their own walls, ceilings, floors, and doors, and are usually used for particular activities. You can refer to all the people who are in a room as <b>the room</b>. 房間","examples":["A minute later he excused himself and left the room. 一分鐘後他告辭了，離開了房間。","The largest conference room could seat 5,000 people. 最大的會議室可坐5千人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about your <b>room</b>, you are referring to the room that you alone use, especially your bedroom at home or your office at work. (我的) 房間","examples":["If you're running upstairs, go to my room and bring down my sweater, please. 如果你要上樓的話，請到我的房間把我的毛衣拿下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>room</b> is a bedroom in a hotel. (酒店的) 客房","examples":["Toni reserved a room in a hotel not far from Arzfeld. 託妮在離阿茨費爾德不遠的酒店預定了一個房間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If there is <b>room</b> somewhere, there is enough empty space there for people or things to be fitted in, or for people to move freely or do what they want to. 空間","examples":["There is usually room to accommodate up to 80 visitors. 通常可以多能容納80名來賓。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If there is <b>room</b> <b>for</b> a particular kind of behaviour or action, people are able to behave in that way or to take that action. 機會","examples":["The intensity of the work left little room for personal grief or anxiety. 該工作的強度很少給個人留下悲傷或憂慮的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>room</b> <b>with</b> someone, you share a rented room, apartment, or house with them, for example when you are a student. 合住","examples":["I had roomed with him in New Haven when we were both at Yale Law School. 我們倆在耶魯法學院上學的時候，我和他在紐黑文合住。"]}]}]},"rise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（數字、 數量、價值）增加；升高，上升；起身，站起；（權力或地位）提高；聳立，隆起；（聲音）變響，變大；（太陽、月亮）升起；（感情或情緒） 變得強烈；（麵包、蛋糕等）發酵；起床；復活，再生；休會，休庭；（風力）加強，增強；（河流）發源；起義，反抗；臉紅，漲紅；（毛髮）豎起；（胃）感到噁心；接近（某個年齡）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（數量或水平的）增加，改善；<英>加薪；（地位的）升高，增強；上升，升起；小山丘，斜坡；（聲音或聲調的）提高；源頭，起源；興起，高漲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>rises</b>, it moves upward. 上升; 升起","examples":["Wilson's ice-cold eyes watched the smoke rise from his cigarette. 威爾遜那雙冰冷的眼睛注視著煙霧從他的香菸中冒出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>rise</b>, you stand up. 起身","examples":["Luther rose slowly from the chair. 盧瑟慢慢從椅子上站起身來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>rise</b>, you get out of bed. 起床","examples":["Tony had risen early and gone to the cottage to work. 託尼很早就起床去那間小屋幹活了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When the sun or moon <b>rises</b>, it appears in the sky. (太陽或月亮) 升起","examples":["He wanted to be over the line of the ridge before the sun had risen. 他想趕在太陽昇起前翻過那山脊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that something <b>rises</b> when it appears as a large, tall shape. 聳立","examples":["The building rose before him, tall and stately. 那棟大樓聳立在他面前，高大而又雄偉。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If the level of something such as the water in a river <b>rises</b>, it becomes higher. (河水等) 上漲","examples":["The waters continue to rise as more than 1,000 people are evacuated. 在1000多人被疏散的同時，河水持續上漲。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If land <b>rises</b>, it slopes upward. (地面) 隆起","examples":["He looked up the slope of land that rose from the house. 他抬頭看了看從那所房子向上隆起的斜坡。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If an amount <b>rises</b>, it increases. (數量) 增加; 上漲","examples":["Interest rates rise from 4% to 5%. 利率從4%上升到5%。","Tourist trips of all kinds rose by 10.5% between 1977 and 1987. 各類旅遊在1977至1987年間增長了10.5%。","Exports rose 23%. 出口貨品增長了23%。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If the wind <b>rises</b>, it becomes stronger. (風力) 增強","examples":["The wind was still rising, approaching a force nine gale. 風力仍在增強，接近九級。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a sound <b>rises</b> or if someone's voice <b>rises</b>, it becomes louder or higher. (聲音或嗓音) 升高","examples":["\"Bernard?\" Her voice rose hysterically. “伯納德？”她的嗓門歇斯底里地升高了。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When the people in a country <b>rise</b>, they try to defeat the government or army that is controlling them. 起義","examples":["President Bush had encouraged the Panamanian military to rise against General Noriega. 布什總統曾鼓動巴拿馬軍方起來反抗諾列加將軍。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If someone <b>rises</b> <b>to</b> a higher position or status, they become more important, successful, or powerful. (職位、地位) 升高","examples":["She is a strong woman who has risen to the top of a deeply sexist organization. 她是一位堅強的女性，在一個性別歧視嚴重的組織中升到了頂層。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rise up</b> means the same as . 上升; 升起","examples":["Spray rose up from the surface of the water. 水花從水面上濺起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rise up</b> means the same as . 起身","examples":["The only thing I wanted was to rise up from the table and leave this house. 我惟一想做的是從餐桌旁站起身來，離開這所房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Rise up</b> means the same as . 聳立","examples":["The White Mountains rose up before me. 懷特山聳立在我面前。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Rise up</b> means the same as . 起義","examples":["He warned that if the government moved against him the people would rise up. 他警告說如果政府對他採取行動，人民將起來反抗。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Rise up</b> means the same as . (職位、地位) 升高","examples":["I started with Hoover 26 years ago in sales and rose up through the ranks. 我26年前加入胡佛公司作銷售，而後一步步晉升。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rise in</b> the amount of something is an increase in it. 增長; 上漲","examples":["...the prospect of another rise in interest rates. …又一次利率上升的可能性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The rise of</b> a movement or activity is an increase in its popularity or influence. (運動或行為的) 興起; 抬頭","examples":["The rise of racism in America is a serious concern. 美洲種族主義的抬頭是一個嚴重憂慮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rise</b> is an increase in your wages or your salary. (薪水、工資的) 增加","examples":["Within two months Kelly got a rise. 兩個月內凱利就獲得了加薪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>rise</b> of someone is the process by which they become more important, successful, or powerful. 崛起","examples":["Haig's rise was fuelled by an all-consuming sense of patriotic duty. 黑格的崛起被一種壓倒一切的愛國責任感推動著。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>gives rise to</b> an event or situation, it causes that event or situation to happen. 引發","examples":["Low levels of choline in the body can give rise to high blood pressure. 體內膽鹼含量低可引發高血壓。"]}]}]},"rope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"粗繩，繩索；（球狀物的）（一）串，（一）條；<美>（套捕牛、馬等的）套索；（拳擊臺、摔跤臺的）圍繩（the ropes）；絞刑（the rope）；<非正式>辦事的規矩，訣竅（the ropes）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用繩子捆（或綁、系）；<美>用繩套捕捉（動物）；用繩（或帶子）圍起（或隔開）（rope sth. off）；借繩爬下/借繩登山（rope down/up）；<非正式>說服……參加（活動） (rope someone in/into)；擰成繩狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rope</b> is a thick cord or wire that is made by twisting together several thinner cords or wires. Ropes are used for jobs such as pulling cars, tying up boats, or tying things together. 纜繩","examples":["He tied the rope around his waist. 他把那條纜繩系在他的腰上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rope</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you tie the two things together with a rope. (用繩) 系","examples":["I roped myself to the chimney. 我用繩子將自己系在了那個煙囪上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone <b>enough rope to hang</b> <b>themselves</b>, you give them the freedom to do a job in their own way because you hope that their attempts will fail and that they will look foolish. 任某人自作自受","examples":["The king has merely given the politicians enough rope to hang themselves. 那位國王不過是任那些政客自作自受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are learning the ropes</b>, you are learning how a particular task or job is done. 熟悉門道","examples":["He tried hiring more salesmen to push his radio products, but they took too much time to learn the ropes. 他試圖僱傭更多的銷售員來推銷無線電產品，但那些人用了太多時間熟悉門道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>know the ropes</b>, you know how a particular job or task should be done. 懂行","examples":["The moment she got to know the ropes, there was no stopping her. 一旦她懂了行，她就一往無前了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> someone <b>the ropes</b>, you show them how to do a particular job or task. 給某人指點門道","examples":["We had a patrol out on the border, breaking in some young soldiers, showing them the ropes. 我們在邊境上進行了一次巡邏，訓練一些年輕士兵，對他們做了指點。"]}]}]},"right":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"符合道德的，正當的；正確的，真實的；（人、物）合適的，般配的；（意見，判斷）對的；右邊的，右側的；（狀態或情況）健康的，正常的；<英，非正式> 十足的，真正的（用於強調某人或某物多麼糟糕）；正面的，外面的；時尚的，上流社會的；（人或政黨）支援保守觀點的，右翼的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"糾正，矯正；補救，扭轉；把（尤指小船）扶正，使直立"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"正當，公正；正當的要求，權利；版權，發行權（rights）；右邊，右方（the right）；右拐，右轉彎；右邊的路（或入口）；（足球等運動）右外場；部隊的右翼；右翼組織，右派政黨（the right/the Right）；右翼人士的立場，右翼立場（the right）；右手拳"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（地方、位置或時間）正好，就在；直接地，徑直地；一直地，完全地；<非正式>立即，毫不耽擱；正確地，確切地；<非正式>順利，正常；在右面，向右邊；（政治上）右傾地；<美>用右手地；徹底地，十足地"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"好的，對（用於表示明白或同意某人的話）；好（用於引起注意）；對嗎（用於確認自己說的話是否正確）；（表示不相信或不同意）是嗎，好哇；對不對，懂嗎（用於確認對方是否在聽並明白你說的話）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>right</b>, it is correct and agrees with the facts. 正確的","examples":["That's absolutely right. 那是完全正確的。","Clocks never told the right time. 時鐘從來都不報正確的時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something in the <b>right</b> way or in the <b>right</b> place, you do it as or where it should be done or was planned to be done. 適當的; 恰當的","examples":["Walking, done in the right way, is a form of aerobic exercise. 走路方法得當的話是一種有氧鍛鍊。","They have computerized systems to ensure delivery of the right pizza to the right place. 他們有計算機化的系統來確保把相應的比薩餅送到相應的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is seen in <b>all the</b> <b>right</b> places or knows <b>all the</b> <b>right</b> people, you mean that they go to places that are socially acceptable or know people who are socially acceptable. 入流的","examples":["He was always to be seen in the right places. 他總是在入流的場所露面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>right</b> <b>about</b> something, they are correct in what they say or think about it. (說法或想法) 正確的","examples":["Ron has been right about the result of every general election but one. 除了一次以外，羅恩對每次大選的結果都判斷正確。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something such as a choice, action, or decision is the <b>right</b> one, it is the best or most suitable one. 最好的; 最恰當的","examples":["She'd made the right choice in leaving New York. 她在離開紐約這件事上做出了正確的選擇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something is <b>not</b> <b>right</b>, there is something unsatisfactory about the situation or thing that you are talking about. 對勁的","examples":["Ratatouille doesn't taste right with any other oil. 普羅旺斯雜燴用其他任何油做出的味道都不正。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you think that someone was <b>right</b> <b>to</b> do something, you think that there were good moral reasons why they did it. (道德上) 對的; 正當的","examples":["You were right to do what you did, under the circumstances. 在那種情況下，你所做的是對的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Right</b> is used to refer to activities or actions that are considered to be morally good and acceptable. (道德上) 正確的","examples":["It's not right, leaving her like this. 這樣拋棄她是不對的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"The <b>right</b> side of a material is the side that is intended to be seen and that faces outward when it is made into something. 正面的","examples":["Trim off excess fabric and turn the right side out. 修剪掉多餘的料子，把正面翻出來。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"Your <b>right</b> arm, leg, or ear, for example, is the one which is on the right side of your body. Your <b>right</b> shoe or glove is the one which is intended to be worn on your right foot or hand. 右邊的","examples":["She shattered her right leg in a fall. 她摔斷了右腿。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Right</b> is also an adverb. 正確地","examples":["He guessed right about some things. 他對有些事情猜對了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Right</b> is also an adverb. 適當地; 恰當地","examples":["To make sure I did everything right, I bought a fat instruction book. 為了確保每件事情都做對，我買了一本厚厚的說明書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Right</b> is also an adverb. 向右","examples":["Turn right into the street. 向右拐進那條街。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>right</b> in order to attract someone's attention or to indicate that you have dealt with one thing so you can go on to another. 好; 好了","examples":["Right, I'll be back in a minute. 好，我馬上回來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say \"<b>right</b>\" to show that you are listening to what someone is saying and that you accept it or understand it. 對; 嗯","examples":["\"It was probably much harder for older people. Don't you think?\"—\"Right.\" “這對老年人來說可能要困難得多。你不這麼認為嗎？” — “對。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>right</b> to emphasize the precise place, position, or time of something. (地點、位置、時間) 正好","examples":["The back of a car appeared right in front of him. 一輛車的尾部正好出現在他面前。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>right</b> to emphasize how far something moves or extends or how long it continues. (強調長度) 一直; 徑直","examples":["...the motorway that runs through the neutral zone right to the army positions. …穿越中立區一直通到軍隊陣營的公路。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>right</b> to emphasize that an action or state is complete. 完全地 (強調動作或狀態已結束)","examples":["The candle had burned right down. 這支蠟燭已全燒完了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that something happened <b>right</b> <b>after</b> a particular time or event or <b>right</b> <b>before</b> it, you mean that it happened immediately after or before it. (指發生時間) 恰好; 就在","examples":["All of a sudden, right after the summer, Mother gets married. 突然之間，夏天剛過完母親就結婚了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say <b>I'll be right there</b> or <b>I'll be right back</b>, you mean that you will get to a place or get back to it in a very short time. 馬上就; 立即就","examples":["I'm going to get some water. I'll be right back. 我去拿些水，馬上就回來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Right</b> is also a noun. 正確","examples":["At least he knew right from wrong. 至少他明白是非。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"正確性","examples":["Many people have very strong opinions about the rightness or wrongness of abortion. 許多人對於墮胎的對與錯有著十分鮮明的意見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>right</b> is one of two opposite directions, sides, or positions. If you are facing north and you turn to the right, you will be facing east. In the word \"to,\" the \"o\" is to the right of the \"t.\" 右邊; 右側","examples":["Ahead of you on the right will be a lovely garden. 你的右前方將是一個可愛的花園。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to people who support the political ideals of capitalism and conservatism as <b>the right</b>. They are often contrasted with <b>the left</b>, who support the political ideals of socialism. 右翼分子","examples":["The Republican Right despise him. 共和黨右翼分子看不起他。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>rights</b> are what you are morally or legally entitled to do or to have. (道德或法律賦予的) 權利","examples":["They don't know their rights. 他們不知道自己的權利。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you have a <b>right</b> <b>to</b> do or to have something, you are morally or legally entitled to do it or to have it. (做某事、擁有某物的) 權利","examples":["...a woman's right to choose. …婦女的選擇權。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone has <b>the rights</b> <b>to</b> a story or book, they are legally allowed to publish it or reproduce it in another form, and nobody else can do so without their permission. 版權","examples":["An agent bought the rights to his life. 一個代理商購買了他生平傳記的出版權。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>right</b> something or if it <b>rights</b> <b>itself</b>, it returns to its normal or correct state, after being in an undesirable state. 糾正; 矯正","examples":["They recognize the urgency of righting the economy. 他們認識到整頓經濟的迫切性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>right</b> a wrong, you do something to make up for a mistake or something bad that you did in the past. 改正","examples":["We've made progress in righting the wrongs of the past. 我們已經在改正過去的錯誤方面取得了進展。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>right</b> something that has fallen or rolled over, or if it <b>rights</b> <b>itself</b>, it returns to its normal upright position. 扶正","examples":["He righted the yacht and continued the race. 他扶正了帆船，繼續比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that things <b>are going right</b>, you mean that your life or a situation is developing as you intended or expected and you are pleased with it. 進展順利","examples":["I can't think of anything in my life that's going right. 我想不出我的生活中有任何進展順利的事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> something <b>right</b>, you correct something that was wrong or that was causing problems. 糾正某事","examples":["We've discovered what went wrong and are going to put it right. 我們已經發現錯誤所在並會將其糾正。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is not the case but you think that it should be, you can say that <b>by rights</b> it should be the case. 按理說","examples":["She did work which by rights should be done by someone else. 她做了按理本應由其他人做的工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is a successful or respected person <b>in</b> their <b>own right</b>, they are successful or respected because of their own efforts and talents rather than those of the people they are closely connected with. 全憑自己地","examples":["Although now a celebrity in her own right, actress Lynn Redgrave knows the difficulties of living in the shadow of her famous older sister. 儘管現在女演員林恩•雷德格雷夫依靠自己的努力成了名人，但她明白生活在她那著名的姐姐的陰影之下的艱難。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>reserve the right</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you will do it if you feel that it is necessary. 保留 (做某事) 的權利","examples":["He reserved the right to change his mind. 他保留了改變主意的權利。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>within</b> their <b>rights</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they are morally or legally entitled to do it. 在某人的許可權之內; 某人有權 (做某事)","examples":["You were quite within your rights to refuse to cooperate with him. 你完全有權拒絕與他合作。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you do something <b>right away</b>, you do it immediately. 馬上; 立刻","examples":["He wants to see you right away. 他想立刻見你。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>right now</b> to emphasize that you are referring to the present moment. 此刻","examples":["Right now I'm feeling very excited. 此刻我感到非常激動。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>right</b> to check whether what you have just said is correct. 對吧; 是吧","examples":["They have a small plane, right? 他們有一架小型飛機，對吧？"]}]}]},"rose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玫瑰，薔薇；玫瑰形物，玫瑰花飾，玫瑰花形紋章（尤指英國國徽）；玫瑰色，玫瑰紅；紅潤的膚色；安樂的境地，有利的環境，輕易成功；（水管或灑水壺的）蓮蓬式噴嘴；玫瑰紅葡萄酒；羅經花，向位圈，方位刻度圖（compass rose的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>使成玫瑰色，使變紅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（數字、數量、價值）增加，（質量）提高；升起，達到較高水平（或位置）；（尤指從坐姿）起身，站起（rise的過去式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rose</b> is the past tense of . rise的過去時","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rose</b> is a flower, often with a pleasant smell, which grows on a bush with stems that have sharp points called thorns on them. 玫瑰花","examples":["She bent to pick a red rose. 她彎下腰摘了一朵紅玫瑰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rose</b> is a bush that roses grow on. 薔薇","examples":["Prune rambling roses when the flowers have faded. 花兒已經凋謝了的時候，修剪那些凌亂的薔薇。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>rose</b> is reddish pink in colour. 玫瑰色 (的)","examples":["...the rose and violet hues of a twilight sky. …這種紫紅色的微明天空。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make rose-coloured; cause to blush or redden 使···變成玫瑰色","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a situation is not <b>a</b> <b>bed of roses</b>, you mean that it is not as pleasant as it seems, and that there are some unpleasant aspects to it. 盡如人意","examples":["We all knew that life was unlikely to be a bed of roses back in Nebraska. 我們都知道回到內布拉斯加生活不太可能盡如人意。"]}]}]},"root":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"根，根莖；（牙齒、頭髮等的）根部；底部，基部；根源，起因；起源，背景；根脈，祖籍（roots）；與……的特殊關聯（roots in）；詞根；（數學）方根；（聖經）根苗，苗裔；翻找，搜尋；（神經的）根；（樂）根音（=root note）；<澳新，俚>性交；根用作物；根音樂"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）生根；紮根於，在……中根深蒂固；根源在於，由……產生（be rooted in）；翻尋；使（某人）無法移動；（與某人）性交；使精疲力竭，挫敗"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（蔬菜、作物等）塊根的，根莖可食用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>roots</b> of a plant are the parts of it that grow under the ground.  根","examples":["...the twisted roots of an apple tree. …一棵蘋果樹的那些彎曲的樹根。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>root</b> of a hair or tooth is the part of it that is underneath the skin. (毛髮或牙齒的) 根","examples":["...decay around the roots of teeth. …牙根周圍的蛀蝕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the place or culture that a person or their family comes from as their <b>roots</b>. (指某人或家族的)根","examples":["I am proud of my Brazilian roots. 我為自己的巴西血統而自豪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to the cause of a problem or of an unpleasant situation as <b>the</b> <b>root</b> <b>of</b> it or <b>the</b> <b>roots</b> <b>of</b> it.  根源","examples":["We got to the root of the problem. 我們觸及了這個問題的根源。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>root</b> a plant or cutting or if it <b>roots</b>, roots form on the bottom of its stem and it starts to grow. 使...生根; 生根","examples":["Most plants will root in about six to eight weeks. 大多數植物會在六到八週內生根。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Root</b> vegetables or <b>root</b> crops are grown for their roots, which are large and can be eaten. 根莖的","examples":["...root crops such as carrots and potatoes. …諸如胡蘿蔔和土豆等根莖作物。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a pig) to burrow in or dig up the earth in search of food, using the snout (豬)用鼻子拱","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to give support to (a contestant, team, etc), as by cheering 用歡呼支援(選手、隊伍等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>root</b> <b>through</b> or <b>in</b> something, you search for something by moving other things around. 搜; 翻","examples":["She rooted through the bag, found what she wanted, and headed toward the door. 她在這個包裡搜尋了一番，找到了她想要的東西，然後朝門口走去。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>puts down roots</b>, they make a place their home, for example by taking part in activities there or by making a lot of friends there. 紮根","examples":["When they got to Montana, they put down roots and built a life. 到達蒙大拿後，他們便在那裡紮根，過上了日子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an idea, belief, or custom <b>takes root</b>, it becomes established among a group of people. 深入人心","examples":["Time would be needed for democracy to take root. 民主的深入人心需要時間。"]}]}]},"row":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一排，一行；（劇院、體育場等的）一排座位；街（用於某些道路名稱）；（表格的）橫線，橫欄；（編織中的）針行；划船（時間）；<英> 嚴重分歧，糾紛；<英> 吵架，爭吵；<英> （持續時間長的）喧鬧聲，吵嚷聲；<英> 嚴厲斥責"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"劃（船）；划船送（某人或某物）；參加划船比賽；<英> 爭吵，吵架；<英> 痛斥，責罵；使……成排"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>row</b> <b>of</b> things or people is a number of them arranged in a line. 排","examples":["...a row of pretty little cottages. …一排漂亮的小村舍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Row</b> is sometimes used in the names of streets. …街 (用於街道名)","examples":["...the house at 236 Larch Row. …位於拉齊街236號的那棟房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Row</b> is also a noun. 划船","examples":["I took Daniel for a row. 我帶丹尼爾去划船了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a noisy quarrel or dispute 爭吵","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens several times <b>in a row</b>, it happens that number of times without a break. If something happens several days <b>in a row</b>, it happens on each of those days. 連續地","examples":["They have won five championships in a row. 他們已經贏得了五連冠。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>row</b>, you sit in a boat and make it move through the water by using oars. If you <b>row</b> someone somewhere, you take them there in a boat, using oars. 划船運送; 划船","examples":["He rowed as quickly as he could to the shore. 他儘可能快速地將船划向了岸邊。","The boatman refused to row him back. 那船伕拒絕划船送他回去。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to quarrel noisily 爭吵","examples":[]}]}]},"rubber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橡膠，合成橡膠；<英> 橡皮擦；<英> 黑板擦；<美，非正式> 避孕套；<美，非正式> 橡膠套鞋；（橋牌或板球的）一盤，決勝局；（棒球比賽中投手站的）投手板；多輪決勝負的比賽（如三局兩勝）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"橡膠製成的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扭轉脖子看，好奇地引頸而望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rubber</b> is a strong, waterproof, elastic substance made from the juice of a tropical tree or produced chemically. It is used for making tyres, boots, and other products. 橡膠","examples":["...the smell of burning rubber. …橡膠燒著的氣味"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rubber</b> is a condom. 保險套","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rubber</b> is a small piece of rubber or other material that is used to remove mistakes that you have made while writing, drawing, or typing. 橡皮","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a match of three games 決勝局","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the deal that wins such a match 勝局比賽","examples":[]}]}]},"rub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擦，磨擦；揉擦，按摩（尤指疼痛部位）；擦痛，磨損；塗，抹；摹拓，拓印（黃銅碑或墓石的）碑文；（滾木球）（球）受阻，轉向；（使）相互摩擦，搓；把（配料）揉擦進（混合物）（rub sth. in/into/through）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（用手或物體）擦，揉；按摩膏，面膜；<正式>困難，問題（the rub）；<美>（烹飪肉之前塗抹在肉表面的）混合香料；（球）受阻，轉向；磨損處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> a part of your body or if you <b>rub</b> <b>at</b> it, you move your hand or fingers backward and forward over it while pressing firmly. 揉","examples":["He rubbed his arms and stiff legs. 他揉了揉他的兩條胳膊和兩條僵硬的腿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> <b>against</b> a surface or <b>rub</b> a part of your body <b>against</b> a surface, you move it backward and forward while pressing it against the surface. 蹭","examples":["A cat was rubbing against my leg. 一隻貓當時在我腿上蹭來蹭去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> an object or a surface or you <b>rub</b> <b>at</b> it, you move a cloth backward and forward over it in order to clean or dry it. 擦","examples":["She took off her glasses and rubbed them hard. 她摘下了她的眼鏡，用力擦著。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> a substance <b>into</b> a surface or <b>rub</b> something such as dirt <b>from</b> a surface, you spread it over the surface or remove it from the surface using your hand or something such as a cloth. 抹","examples":["He rubbed oil into my back. 他在我的背上抹上了油。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> two things <b>together</b> or if they <b>rub</b> <b>together</b>, they move backward and forward, pressing against each other. 揉搓","examples":["He rubbed his hands together a few times. 他把雙手搓了好幾遍。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something you are wearing or holding <b>rubs</b>, it makes you sore because it keeps moving backward and forward against your skin. 蹭得疼","examples":["It should be comfortable against the skin without rubbing, chafing, or cutting into anything. 它貼身穿應是舒服的，不會蹭傷、磨傷或劃傷皮膚。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A massage can be referred to as a <b>rub</b>. 按摩","examples":["She sometimes asks if I want a back rub. 她有時問我是否想要一次背部按摩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rub shoulders with</b> famous people, you meet them and talk to them. You can also say that you <b>rub elbows with</b> someone. 與某人接觸","examples":["He regularly rubbed shoulders with the likes of Elizabeth Taylor and Kylie Minogue. 他常與伊麗莎白•泰勒和凱莉•米洛之類的人接觸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rub</b> someone <b>the wrong way</b>, you offend or annoy them without intending to. 無意中冒犯某人","examples":["What are you going to get out of him if you rub him the wrong way? 如果你無意中惹惱了他，你能從他那裡得到什麼呢？"]}]}]},"saturday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期六，週六"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Saturday</b> is the day after Friday and before Sunday. 星期六","examples":["He called her on Saturday morning at the studio. 他星期六早上在工作室給她打電話。","Every Saturday dad made a beautiful pea and ham soup. 每個星期六爸爸都做一道鮮美的豌豆火腿湯。"]}]}]},"salt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鹽，食鹽（=common salt）；（化學）鹽；鹽狀物（用於某種特殊目的的物質或藥品）（salts）；<文>風趣，刺激性；<非正式>有經驗的水手，老水手（old salt）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（食物）加鹽調味；用鹽醃製（食物）（=salt down）；（為融化雪或冰）撒鹽於（道路）上；給……增添刺激，使……更有趣；<非正式>使（礦區、礦山）呈虛假的富礦狀"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"含鹽的，鹹的；用鹽醃製的；（植物）海生的，生長於鹽沼的；<舊>猥褻的"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（美俄）限制戰略武器談判（Strategic Arms Limitation Talks）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Salt</b> is a strong-tasting substance, in the form of white powder or crystals, which is used to improve the flavour of food or to preserve it. Salt occurs naturally in sea water. 食鹽","examples":["Season lightly with salt and pepper. 用鹽和胡椒稍微調一下味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Salts</b> are substances that are formed when an acid reacts with an alkali. 鹽","examples":["The rock is rich in mineral salts. 這種岩石富含礦物鹽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>salt</b> food, you add salt to it. (給食物) 加鹽","examples":["Salt the stock to your taste and leave it simmering very gently. 按照你的口味在原湯里加鹽，然後用文火慢燉。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"加了鹽的","examples":["Put a pan of salted water on to boil. 把一鍋加了鹽的水放上去煮沸。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something <b>with a grain of salt</b>, you do not believe that it is completely accurate or true. 對…半信半疑","examples":["You have to take these findings with a grain of salt because respondents tend to give the answers they feel they should. 你必須對這些結果有所保留，因為調查物件們傾向於給出他們認為應該給的答案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say, for example, that any doctor <b>worth</b> his or her <b>salt</b> would do something, you mean that any doctor who was good at his or her job or who deserved respect would do it. 稱職的; 值得尊敬的","examples":["No golf teacher worth his salt would ever recommend that you grip the club tightly. 沒有哪位稱職的高爾夫教練會建議你緊緊地握住球杆。"]}]}]},"sail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人）航行；（船）航行；啟航；駕駛（船隻）；飄過，（輕快地）移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"帆；乘船航行；（用作交通工具的）帆船的使用；（潛艇的）瞭望塔；油布，篷帆布；帆狀物，功能似帆的物體；（風車的）翼板；（旗魚或一些史前爬行動物的）脊鰭；（僧帽水母等的）帆器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sails</b> are large pieces of material attached to the mast of a ship. The wind blows against the sails and pushes the ship along. 帆","examples":["The white sails billow with the breezes they catch. 片片白帆隨風揚起。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say a ship <b>sails</b> when it moves over the sea. 航行","examples":["The trawler had sailed from the port of Zeebrugge. 那隻拖網漁船已經從澤布呂赫港啟航。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sail</b> a boat or if a boat <b>sails</b>, it moves across water using its sails. 駕駛 (船); (船) 揚帆航行","examples":["His crew's job is to sail the boat. 他的船員的職責是駕船。","I'd buy a big boat and sail around the world. 我要買條大船航遊世界。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a ship <b>sets sail</b>, it leaves a port. 啟航","examples":["He loaded his vessel with another cargo and set sail. 他又往他的船上裝了一件貨就啟航了。"]}]}]},"sale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出售，銷售；銷售額（sales）；銷售活動，（尤指）拍賣；降價出售，大減價；銷售部門（sales）；銷售業務，銷售工作（sales）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>sale</b> of goods is the act of selling them for money. 銷售","examples":["Efforts were made to limit the sale of alcohol. 做出努力來限制酒的銷售。","...a proposed arms sale to Saudi Arabia. …擬議中對沙烏地阿拉伯的武器銷售。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>sales</b> of a product are the quantity of it that is sold. 銷售量","examples":["The newspaper has sales of 1.72 million. 該報有172萬份的銷售量。","...the huge Christmas sales of computer games. …電腦遊戲在聖誕節的鉅額銷售量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The part of a company that deals with <b>sales</b> deals with selling the company's products. 銷售部門","examples":["Until 1983 he worked in sales and marketing. 到1983年為止他一直供職於市場營銷部。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>sale</b> is an occasion when a shop sells things at less than their normal price. 減價出售","examples":["...a pair of jeans bought half-price in a sale. …一條減價時半價買的牛仔褲。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>sale</b> is an event when goods are sold to the person who offers the highest price. 拍賣","examples":["The Old Master was bought by dealers at the Christie's sale. 這幅早期名畫被商人們在克里斯蒂的拍賣會上買走。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>for sale</b>, it is being offered to people to buy. 供出售","examples":["The yacht is for sale at a price of 1.7 million dollars. 這艘遊艇以170萬美元的價格待售。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If products in a shop are <b>on sale</b>, they can be bought for less than their normal price. 減價出售","examples":["A good shopper doesn't just buy things because they're on sale. 善於購物的人不會僅僅因為商品減價出售就買。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Products that are <b>on sale</b> can be bought. 出售","examples":["English textbooks and dictionaries are on sale everywhere. 英語教材和詞典到處都有出售。","Tickets go on sale this week. 票本週開始出售。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a property or company is <b>up for sale</b>, its owner is trying to sell it. 待售","examples":["The mansion has been put up for sale. 該豪宅已待售。"]}]}]},"sand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙，沙子；沙堆，沙地；沙灘，沙漠（sands）；沙石層，沙層；（尤指大於0.06毫米的沙粒構成的）沉積沙土；沙土色，淺黃灰色；<美，非正式>堅定，剛毅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用砂紙或打磨機）磨光；撒沙於，鋪沙於；使撒沙似地佈滿；給……摻沙子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sand</b> is a substance that looks like powder, and consists of extremely small pieces of stone. Some deserts and many beaches are made up of sand. 沙","examples":["They all walked barefoot across the damp sand to the water's edge. 他們都光著腳走過潮溼的沙地來到了水邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sands</b> are a large area of sand, for example, a beach. 沙灘","examples":["...miles of golden sands. …數英里的金色沙灘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sand</b> a wood or metal surface, you rub sandpaper over it in order to make it smooth or clean. 用砂紙打磨","examples":["Sand the surface softly and carefully. 輕輕地、小心地用砂紙打磨表面。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sand down</b> means the same as . 同(sand)","examples":["I was going to sand down the chairs and repaint them. 我打算用砂紙打磨這些椅子然後重新刷漆。"]}]}]},"safe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"安全的，平安的；不損害（或危害）健康的；謹慎的；（地點或局勢）安全的；不會丟失，不會被拿走；<非正式> 不錯的；不致引起爭議的，有把握的；（棒球）成功上壘的；（選舉中席位）十拿九穩的；無風險的，穩妥的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"保險箱；<美，非正式> 陰莖套，安全套；紗櫥"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英，非正式> 嗨，喂（年輕人打招呼時說）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美，非正式> 安全地，平安地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>safe</b> does not cause physical harm or danger. 安全的","examples":["Officials arrived to assess whether it is safe to bring emergency food supplies into the city. 官員們過來評估調撥緊急救濟食品進入該市是否安全。","Most foods that we eat are safe for birds. 我們吃的絕大部分食物對鳥類是安全的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>safe</b> <b>from</b> something, they cannot be harmed or damaged by it. 不會受損傷的","examples":["They are safe from the violence that threatened them. 他們不會受到威脅性暴力的傷害。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>safe</b>, you have not been harmed, or you are not in danger of being harmed. 未受傷害的; 安全的","examples":["Where is Sophy? Is she safe? 索菲在哪兒？她沒受到傷害吧？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>safe</b> place is one where it is unlikely that any harm, damage, or unpleasant things will happen to the people or things that are there. (地方) 安全的","examples":["The continuing tension has prompted more than half the inhabitants of the refugee camp to flee to safer areas. 持續的緊張局勢已經促使難民營中一半以上的人逃往了更安全的地區。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If people or things have a <b>safe</b> trip, they reach their destination without harm, damage, or unpleasant things happening to them. (旅途) 平安的","examples":["I told him good night, come back any time, and have a safe trip home. 我祝他晚安、回家一路平安，並告訴他可以隨時回來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are at a <b>safe</b> distance from something or someone, you are far enough away from them to avoid any danger, harm, or unpleasant effects. (距離) 安全的","examples":["I shall conceal myself at a safe distance from the battlefield. 我將把自己藏在一個遠離戰場的安全地帶。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something you have or expect to obtain is <b>safe</b>, you cannot lose it or be prevented from having it. 保險的; 不會失去的","examples":["We as consumers need to feel confident that our jobs are safe before we will spend spare cash. 我們作為消費者需要確信我們的工作是不會丟的，這樣才會去花閒錢。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>safe</b> course of action is one in which there is very little risk of loss or failure. 穩妥的; 風險小的","examples":["Electricity shares are still a safe investment. 電力股仍然是小風險投資。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If <b>it is</b> <b>safe</b> <b>to</b> say or assume something, you can say it with very little risk of being wrong. 有把握的","examples":["I think it is safe to say that very few students expend the effort to do quality work in school. 我認為有把握這麼說，幾乎沒有學生能在學校用心讀書。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"未受傷害地; 安全地","examples":["All 140 guests were brought out of the building safely by firemen. 140位客人全部被消防人員安然無恙地救出了大樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"安全地","examples":["The banker keeps the money tucked safely under his bed. 那位銀行家把錢安置在他的床下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"平安地","examples":["The space shuttle returned safely today from a 10-day mission. 太空梭在為期10天的任務之後於今日平安返回。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"穩妥地; 風險小地","examples":["We reveal only as much information as we can safely risk at a given time. 我們只透露那些在特定時期我們可以穩妥地承擔風險的資訊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"有把握地","examples":["I think you can safely say she will not be appearing in another of my films. 我想你可以有把握地說她不會在我的另一部電影中現身了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>safe</b> is a strong metal cabinet with special locks, in which you keep money, jewellery, or other valuable things. 保險櫃","examples":["The files are now in a safe to which only he has the key. 那些檔案如今在一個保險櫃裡，只有他有鑰匙。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing is <b>in safe hands</b>, or is <b>safe in</b> someone's <b>hands</b>, you mean that they are being taken care of by a reliable person and will not be harmed. 得到 (某可靠之人的) 妥善照顧","examples":["I had a huge responsibility to ensure these packets remained in safe hands. 我有重大責任保證這些包裹在可靠的人手裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>play safe</b> or <b>play it safe</b>, you do not take any risks. 萬無一失","examples":["If you want to play safe, cut down on the amount of salt you eat. 如果你想萬無一失，就少吃鹽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say you are doing something <b>to be on the safe side</b>, you mean that you are doing it in case something undesirable happens, even though this may be unnecessary. 為保險起見","examples":["You might still want to go for an X-ray, however, just to be on the safe side. 但你也許還想去拍張X光片，為保險起見。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say \"<b>it's better to be safe than sorry</b>,\" you are advising someone to take action in order to avoid possible unpleasant consequences later, even if this seems unnecessary. 免吃後悔藥","examples":["Don't be afraid to have this checked by a doctor – better safe than sorry! 別怕把這個讓醫生檢查一下–以免吃後悔藥！"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say that someone is <b>safe and sound</b> when they are still alive or unharmed after being in danger. 安然無恙地","examples":["All I'm hoping for is that wherever Trevor is he will come home safe and sound. 我所希望的是不論特雷弗在哪兒他都能安然無恙地回家。"]}]}]},"rule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"規章，條例；（語言、科學等的）規則，法則；行事準則，指導方針；常規，慣常做法；統治，管轄；尺，直尺；鉛線印出的線，破折號；<澳> 澳大利亞式橄欖球規則（兩隊各18人參賽）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"統治，管轄；支配，控制；佔首要地位；（尤指對法律問題）判定，裁定；（用尺等）劃（線）；<非正式> 好極了，非常棒；（行星）對（黃道十二宮圖的宮，房子，生活等）有影響；（價格或貿易商品的價格）普遍處於某一水平（或堅挺趨勢）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rules</b> are instructions that tell you what you are allowed to do and what you are not allowed to do. 規則","examples":["...a thirty-two-page pamphlet explaining the rules of basketball. …一本說明籃球規則的32頁的小冊子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rule</b> is a statement telling people what they should do in order to achieve success or a benefit of some kind. 原則; 準則","examples":["An important rule is to drink plenty of water during any flight. 一條重要的原則是在任何一次飛行中都要喝大量的水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>rules</b> <b>of</b> something such as a language or a science are statements that describe the way that things usually happen in a particular situation. 規律; 法則","examples":["...according to the rules of quantum theory. …根據量子論的法則。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>the rule</b>, it is the normal state of affairs. 常規; 慣例","examples":["However, for many Americans today, weekend work has unfortunately become the rule rather than the exception. 然而，如今對許多美國人而言，週末工作已不幸成為慣例而不是特例。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Rule</b> is also a noun. 統治","examples":["...demands for an end to one-party rule. …結束一黨統治的要求。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The person or group that <b>rules</b> a country controls its affairs. 統治","examples":["For four centuries, he says, foreigners have ruled Angola. 他說4個世紀以來外國人一直統治著安哥拉。","He ruled for eight months. 他在位了8個月。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>rules</b> your life, it influences or restricts your actions in a way that is not good for you. 嚴重影響; 制約","examples":["Scientists have always been aware of how fear can rule our lives and make us ill. 科學家們從來都知道恐懼是如何嚴重影響我們的生活並使我們患病的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone in authority <b>rules</b> that something is true or should happen, they state that they have officially decided that it is true or should happen. 裁定","examples":["The court ruled that laws passed by the assembly remained valid. 該法庭裁定由議會透過的法律仍然有效。","The Israeli court has not yet ruled on the case. 以色列法院尚未對此案做出裁決。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>rule</b> a straight line, you draw it using something that has a straight edge. 畫","examples":["...a ruled grid of horizontal and vertical lines. …一個畫好的由水平線及垂直線構成的網格。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>as a rule</b>, you mean that it usually happens. 通常","examples":["As a rule, however, such attacks have been aimed at causing damage rather than taking life. 然而，通常此類攻擊意在造成破壞而非要人性命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>bends the rules</b> or <b>stretches the rules</b>, they do something even though it is against the rules. 變通規則; 通融","examples":["There happens to be a particular urgency in this case, and it would help if you could bend the rules. 這次碰巧有緊急情況，如果你能通融一下將會很有幫助。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rule of thumb</b> is a rule or principle that you follow which is not based on exact calculations, but rather on experience. 經驗法則","examples":["A good rule of thumb is that a broker must generate sales of ten times his salary if his employer is to make a profit. 一個很好的經驗法則是，僱主要獲取利潤的話，其中間人必須創造10倍於自己薪水的銷售額。"]}]}]},"round":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"圓形的，球形的；弧形的；微胖的，豐滿的；<喻>（聲音）圓潤的；整數的；<古>（錢）大量的；耿直的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"旋轉，環繞；周長；在周圍，圍繞；到處，四處；朝反方向，轉過來；繞彎，向另一側；逐一，挨個；到某地，在某地；大約；閒著；從頭至尾"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"環繞，圍繞；繞過，在另一側；解決（問題）；在……周圍，包圍；在……各處；在……整個期間；適應，以……為中心"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輪次；（比賽的）局，場；一系列常規活動；（固定的）遞送路線；巡防，巡診；一巡（飲料）；一陣（掌聲）；輪唱曲；一次射擊，一發子彈；圓形物；<英> 一片（麵包），一個（三明治）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"環繞，繞過；（使）成圓形，變圓；取整，四捨五入；圓滿結束，圓滿完成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>all year round</b>, it happens throughout the year. 全年","examples":["Many of these plants are evergreen, so you can enjoy them all year round. 這些植物中有許多都是四季常青的，所以可以全年觀賞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make the rounds</b> or <b>do the rounds</b>, you visit a series of different places. 巡訪","examples":["After school, I had picked up Nick and Ted and made the rounds of the dry cleaner and the food stores. 放學後，我接了尼克和特德,然後去了那乾洗店和食品店。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>round</b> <b>of</b> events is a series of related events, especially one which comes after or before a similar series of events. (一) 輪","examples":["It was agreed that another round of preliminary talks would be held in Beijing. 商定了又一輪預備會談將在北京舉行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In sports, a <b>round</b> is a series of games in a competition. The winners of these games go on to play in the next round, and so on, until only one player or team is left. (運動比賽的) 一輪; 一場","examples":["...in the third round of the Ryder Cup. …萊德杯高爾夫球賽的第三輪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a boxing or wrestling match, a <b>round</b> is one of the periods during which the boxers or wrestlers fight. (拳擊或摔跤比賽的) 回合","examples":["He was declared the victor in the 11th round. 他在第11個回合被宣佈為獲勝者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>round</b> <b>of</b> golf is one game, usually including 18 holes. (高爾夫球賽的) 一場","examples":["...two rounds of golf. …兩場高爾夫球賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do your <b>rounds</b> or your <b>round</b>, you make a series of visits to different places or people, for example as part of your job. 巡訪","examples":["The doctors still did their morning rounds. 醫生們依舊做晨訪。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you buy a <b>round</b> <b>of</b> drinks, you buy a drink for each member of the group of people that you are with. (一) 巡 (飲料)","examples":["They sat on thesnd clubhouse terrace, downing a round of drinks. 他們都坐在那個俱樂部會所的露臺上，豪飲著一巡飲料。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>round</b> <b>of</b> ammunition is the bullet or bullets released when a gun is fired. 射擊一次的量","examples":["...firing 1,650 rounds of ammunition during a period of ten minutes. …10分鐘發射1650堂彈藥。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If there is a <b>round</b> <b>of applause</b>, everyone claps their hands to welcome someone or to show that they have enjoyed something. (一) 陣 (掌聲)","examples":["Sue got a sympathetic round of applause. 蘇獲得了一陣同情的掌聲。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>round</b> is shaped like a circle or ball. 圓形的","examples":["She had small feet and hands and a flat, round face. 她有一對小手小腳和一張扁平的圓臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>round</b> number is a multiple of 10, 100, 1,000, and so on. Round numbers are used instead of precise ones to give the general idea of a quantity or proportion. 整十，整百，整千…的數","examples":["I asked how much silver could be bought for a million dollars, which seemed a suitably round number. 我問了100萬美元，這似乎是個合適的整數，能買多少白銀。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>round</b> a place or obstacle, you move in a curve past the edge or corner of it. 繞過","examples":["The house disappeared from sight as we rounded a corner. 那棟房屋在我們繞過街角時從視線中消失了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>round</b> an amount <b>up</b> or <b>down</b>, or if you <b>round</b> it <b>off</b>, you change it to the nearest whole number or nearest multiple of 10, 100, 1000, and so on. 四捨五入","examples":["We needed to do decimals to round up and round down numbers. 我們需要把小數四捨五入成整數。","The fraction was then multiplied by 100 and rounded to the nearest half or whole number. 該分數然後被乘以100，再四捨五入成半數或者整數。"]}]}]},"saw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋸；鋸床；格言，諺語；鋸齒狀部位（或器官）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鋸，鋸開；亂剪；拉鋸似的來回移動；<加拿大>（兩人或多人） 透過互讓解決，相互妥協"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看見；觀看（電影、電視節目等）；理解，領會（see 的過去式形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Saw</b> is the past tense of <b>see</b>. (see)的過去式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saw</b> is a tool for cutting wood, which has a blade with sharp teeth along one edge. Some saws are pushed backward and forward by hand, and others are powered by electricity. 鋸","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a wise saying, maxim, or proverb 格言","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>saw</b> something, you cut it with a saw. 鋸","examples":["He escaped by sawing through the bars of his cell. 他鋸斷牢房的鐵柵逃跑了。"]}]}]},"scare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使驚恐，嚇唬；害怕，恐懼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚恐，驚嚇；（社會上的）大恐慌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>scares</b> you, it frightens or worries you. 驚嚇","examples":["You're scaring me. 你嚇著我了。","The prospect of failure scares me rigid. 失敗的可能嚇得我都僵了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you want to emphasize that something scares you a lot, you can say that it <b>scares the hell out of</b> you or <b>scares the life out of</b> you. 嚇死了","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a sudden unpleasant experience gives you a <b>scare</b>, it frightens you. 驚嚇","examples":["Don't you realize what a scare you've given us all? 你難道沒意識到你給了我們大家一個什麼樣的驚嚇嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scare</b> is a situation in which many people are afraid or worried because they think something dangerous is happening which will affect them all. 恐慌; 恐懼","examples":["The news set off a continent-wide health scare. 這一訊息引起了整個大陸的健康恐慌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A bomb <b>scare</b> or a security <b>scare</b> is a situation in which there is believed to be a bomb in a place. (炸彈或安全) 恐慌","examples":["Despite many recent bomb scares, no one has yet been hurt. 儘管最近發生多次炸彈恐慌，但至今為止還沒有人員受傷。"]}]}]},"seesaw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蹺蹺板；拉鋸局面，不斷起伏的狀態"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"來回往復的，拉鋸式的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"搖擺不定，時起時伏；（使）上下或來回搖動；玩蹺蹺板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seesaw</b> is a long board which is balanced in the middle. To play on it, a child sits on each end, and when one end goes up, the other goes down. 蹺蹺板","examples":["There was a sandpit, a seesaw and a swing in the playground. 操場上有一個沙坑,一副蹺蹺板和一架鞦韆。"]}]}]},"sea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海洋；內海；海（指月球或火星表面的一片廣闊平原）；海面情況，海浪狀況；大量，茫茫一片；（用於海名）海（Sea）；巨浪（seas）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>sea</b> is the salty water that covers about three-quarters of the Earth's surface. 海洋","examples":["Most of the kids have never seen the sea. 這些孩子中的大多數從沒見過大海。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>seas</b> when you are describing the sea at a particular time or in a particular area. (某時、某區域的) 海","examples":["He drowned after 30 minutes in the rough seas. 他在波濤洶湧的海里掙扎了30分鐘後溺死了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sea</b> is a large area of salty water that is part of an ocean or is surrounded by land. (作為海洋的一部分的或陸地圍起來的) 海","examples":["...the North Sea. …北海。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>At sea</b> means on or under the sea, far away from land. 在海上; 在海里","examples":["The boats remain at sea for an average of ten days at a time. 這些船平均每次在海上呆10天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go or look out <b>to sea</b>, you go or look across the sea. 到海上/向海上","examples":["...fishermen who go to sea for two weeks at a time. …每次出海兩週的漁民們。"]}]}]},"scene":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事發地，現場；事件，場面；（戲劇、書、電影等的）片段，情節；（戲劇的）一場；（戲劇）佈景；活動領域，圈子；（某地方或圖畫中的）景色，景象；（當眾）發脾氣，吵鬧；<非正式>同性戀者常去的社交場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scene</b> in a play, movie, or book is part of it in which a series of events happen in the same place. 場面; 片斷","examples":["...the opening scene of \"A Christmas Carol.\" …《聖誕頌歌》的開場。","...Act I, scene 1. …第1幕，第1場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You refer to a place as a <b>scene</b> when you are describing its appearance and indicating what impression it makes on you. 景象","examples":["It's a scene of complete devastation. 那是一幅滿目瘡痍的景象。","Thick black smoke billowed over the scene. 黑色的濃煙從現場滾滾升起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe an event that you see, or that is broadcast or shown in a picture, as a <b>scene</b> of a particular kind. 場面; 事件","examples":["There were emotional scenes as the refugees enjoyed their first breath of freedom. 難民們享受第一口自由的呼吸時，有一些感人至深的場面。","Television broadcasters were warned to exercise caution over depicting scenes of violence. 電視臺受到警告，在描述暴力場面時要採取謹慎態度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>scene</b> <b>of</b> an event is the place where it happened. 現場","examples":["The area has been the scene of fierce fighting for three months. 這個地區是3個月來激烈戰鬥的現場。","...traces left at the scene of a crime. …在犯罪現場留下的痕跡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to an area of activity as a particular type of <b>scene</b>. 活動領域","examples":["Sandman's experimentation has made him something of a cult figure on the local music scene. 桑德曼的實驗已經使他成為當地音樂領域頗受人崇拜的人物。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you make a <b>scene</b>, you embarrass people by publicly showing your anger about something. 發脾氣; 當眾吵鬧","examples":["I'm sorry I made such a scene. 很抱歉我剛才發了這麼一通火。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>behind the scenes</b>, it is done secretly rather than publicly. 秘密地; 在幕後","examples":["But behind the scenes Mr. Cain will be working quietly to try to get a deal done. 但在幕後，凱恩先生將會不聲不響地工作，努力把交易做成。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to what happens <b>behind the scenes</b>, you are referring to what happens during the making of a movie, play, or radio or television programme. 在幕後; 在後臺","examples":["It's an exciting opportunity to learn what goes on behind the scenes. 這是個令人激動的機會，可以瞭解幕後發生的事情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>a change of scene</b>, you go somewhere different after being in a particular place for a long time. 換個環境","examples":["What you need is a change of scene. Why not go on a cruise? 你需要的是換個環境。為何不乘遊輪去旅行呢？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that <b>sets the scene for</b> a particular event creates the conditions in which the event is likely to happen. 為…做好準備","examples":["An improving economy helped set the scene for his re-election. 好轉的經濟為他的再選鋪平了道路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a person or thing appears <b>on the scene</b>, they come into being or become involved in something. When they disappear <b>from the scene</b>, they are no longer there or are no longer involved. 登場/離場; 到場/消失","examples":["He could react jealously when and if another child comes on the scene. 如果有別的孩子加入其中，他可能會表現得相當嫉妒。"]}]}]},"seat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"座位；（椅子等的）座部；（機器的）基座；（議會、委員會、法庭等的）席位，職位；<英> 議會議員選區；（組織或重大活動的）所在地；（大戶人家在鄉間的）別墅，宅邸；（裙子或褲子的）臀部，後襠；屁股；（騎馬的）騎姿"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使坐下，使就座；容納，坐得下；使就職；固定，安裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seat</b> is an object that you can sit on, for example, a chair. 座位","examples":["Stephen returned to his seat. 斯蒂芬回到了他的座位上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>seat</b> of a chair is the part that you sit on. (椅子的) 坐部","examples":["The stool had a torn, red plastic seat. 這條無靠背凳子有一個破了的、紅色的塑膠坐部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>seat</b> <b>of</b> a piece of clothing is the part that covers your bottom. (衣物的) 臀部","examples":["Then he got up, brushed off the seat of his jeans, and headed slowly down the slope. 接著他站了起來，拍了拍他牛仔褲的臀部，然後沿山坡緩緩而下。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone is elected to a legislature you can say that they, or their party, have won a <b>seat</b>. (立法機構的) 席位","examples":["Independent candidates won the majority of seats on the local council. 獨立派候選人贏得了地方議會的多數席位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a <b>seat</b> on the board of a company or on a committee, they are a member of it. (董事會、委員會) 席位","examples":["He has been unsuccessful in his attempt to win a seat on the board of the company. 他在該公司董事會謀得一席之地的企圖未能成功。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>seat</b> of an organization, a wealthy family, or an activity is its base. (組織、富裕家庭、活動的) 基地","examples":["Gunfire broke out early this morning around the seat of government in Lagos. 今天清晨在拉各斯政府基地周圍爆發了槍戰。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>seat</b> <b>yourself</b> somewhere, you sit down. 使 (自己) 坐下","examples":["He waved toward a chair, and seated himself at the desk. 他朝一把椅子一揮手，在桌旁坐了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A building or vehicle that <b>seats</b> a particular number of people has enough seats for that number. (建築物、車等) 提供 (一定數量的) 坐席","examples":["The theatre seats 570. 這家劇院可容納570名觀眾。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take a back seat</b>, you allow other people to have all the power and to make all the decisions. 退居次位","examples":["You need to take a back seat and think about both past and future. 你需要退居次位思考過去和將來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take a seat</b>, you sit down. 坐下","examples":["\"Take a seat,\" he said in a bored tone. “坐下，”他以一種厭倦的口氣說道。"]}]}]},"season":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"季節；（某種特殊氣候的）季；（某種活動或事件發生的）時期；體育賽季；（水果、蔬菜等的）當令期，上市期；度假旺季，法定假期；（一年中時裝、髮型等的）流行期；（一系列新的電視劇、戲劇等的）播出期，上映期；發情期；（英國上流社會的）社交活動時節（the season）；<古>適當的時機；<古>某時，一段時間"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加調料，給……調味；給……增添趣味；使（木材）風乾，曬乾（木材）；變乾燥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>seasons</b> are the main periods into which a year can be divided and which each have their own typical weather conditions. (一年中有某典型天氣狀況的) 季","examples":["Autumn is my favourite season. 秋季是我最喜歡的季節。","...the only region of Brazil where all four seasons are clearly defined. …巴西惟一四季分明的地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>season</b> to refer to the period during each year when a particular activity or event takes place. For example, the planting <b>season</b> is the period when a particular plant or crop is planted. (一年中某活動或事件發生的) 季節","examples":["...birds arriving for the breeding season. …為繁殖季節而到來的鳥類。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>season</b> to refer to the period when a particular fruit, vegetable, or other food is ready for eating and is widely available. (水果、蔬菜或其他食物的) 當季期","examples":["The plum season is about to begin. 李子的當季期就要開始了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>season</b> to refer to a fixed period during each year when a particular sport is played or when a particular activity is allowed. (一年中某體育比賽或某活動被允許的) 季節","examples":["...the baseball season. …棒球賽季。","Deer hunting season is only a couple of weeks long. 獵鹿季節只有幾個星期長。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>season</b> is a period in which a play or show, or a series of plays or shows, is performed in one place. (戲劇、演出的) 上演期","examples":["...a season of three new plays. …3出新戲劇的上演期。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>season</b> <b>of</b> movies is several of them shown as a series because they are connected in some way. (影片的) 連續上映期","examples":["...a brief season of films in which Artaud appeared. …阿爾托出演的影片的一個短暫的連續上映期。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The holiday or vacation <b>season</b> is the time when most people take their holiday. (多數人休假的) 時期","examples":["...the peak holiday season. …休假高峰期。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>season</b> food with salt, pepper, or spices, you add them to it in order to improve its flavour. 給 (食物) 調味","examples":["Season the meat with salt and pepper. 用鹽和胡椒粉給肉調味。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a female animal is <b>in season</b>, she is in a state where she is ready to have sex. (雌性動物) 在發情期","examples":["There are a few ideas around on how to treat fillies and mares in season. 關於如何對待發情期的小母馬和母馬有幾種觀點。"]}]}]},"school":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（中、小）學校；全校師生；上學時間；上學期間；專科學校；大學，大學期間；（大學的）系，學院；學派，流派；（魚、鯨、海豚等的）群；<英>（牛津大學的）期末考試大廳；（牛津大學的）期末考試；<英>一夥賭徒；（輪番到酒吧請客喝酒的）酒友"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"教育，培養（兒童）；訓練，教育；（尤指為競賽）馴馬；（魚，海獸）成群；強迫自己（做難事）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<南非>（科薩人）受過西化教育的；（名字）源自西方的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>school</b> is a place where children are educated. You usually refer to this place as <b>school</b> when you are talking about the time that children spend there and the activities that they do there. 學校","examples":["...a boy who was in my class at school. …上學時我班上的一個男孩。","Even the good students say homework is what they most dislike about school. 就連好學生也說家庭作業是他們最討厭學校的一點。","...a school built in the Sixties. …一所建於六十年代的學校。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>school</b> is the students or staff at a school. 全校師生","examples":["Deirdre, the whole school's going to hate you. 迪爾德麗，全校師生都要恨你了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A privately-run place where a particular skill or subject is taught can be referred to as a <b>school</b>. 私立專科學校","examples":["...a riding school. …一所私立騎術學校。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A university, college, or university department specializing in a particular type of subject can be referred to as a <b>school</b>. 學院; 系","examples":["...a lecturer in the school of veterinary medicine at the University of Pennsylvania. …賓夕法尼亞大學獸醫學系的一名講師。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>School</b> is used to refer to college. 大學","examples":["Jack eventually graduated from school, got married, and got his first real job. 傑克終於大學畢了業，結了婚，找到了第一份真正的工作。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A particular <b>school</b> <b>of</b> writers, artists, or thinkers is a group of them whose work, opinions, or theories are similar. 學派; 流派","examples":["...the Chicago school of economists. …芝加哥經濟學派。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a group of porpoises or similar aquatic animals that swim together 魚群; 水生動物群","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>school</b> someone <b>in</b> something, you train or educate them to have a certain skill, type of behaviour, or way of thinking. 訓練; 教育","examples":["Many mothers schooled their daughters in the myth of female inferiority. 許多母親用男尊女卑的錯誤觀念教育女兒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to form such a group (魚、水生動物)成群","examples":[]}]}]},"self":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自己，自我；（指一個人）自己，本人；私心，私利；本人（用於商業函件、支票等）；（自己的）通常的行為方式，本來面目"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（裝飾品，封面）與其他部分同質同色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（主植）使自花授粉，使自體受精；（遺傳）（動物、植物）同系繁衍，同系受精；自花受精"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"自己（用於自謔的讚美語中）；本人（用於票根、支票等，指稱持有人或簽署人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>self</b> is your basic personality or nature, especially considered in terms of what you are really like as a person. 自身; 本性","examples":["You're looking more like your usual self. 你現在看上去更像你平常的樣子了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>self</b> is the essential part of their nature which makes them different from everyone and everything else. 個性","examples":["I want to explore and get in touch with my inner self. 我想認真探索，瞭解我內在的個性。","The face is the true self visible to others. 面孔是外人能看到的真實自我。"]}]}]},"seed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"種子，籽；<美>（蘋果或橙子等的）果核，籽；<舊> 精液，精子（常為幽默用法）；<古，文>（古時用語，原用於《聖經》中）子嗣，子孫；（感情、過程的）起源，開端；（網球、羽毛球等體育專案中的）種子選手， 種子隊；晶粒，晶種；輻射管，鐳管"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（蔬菜，水果）去籽（去核），給......脫籽；選定......為種子選手（或種子隊）；在（地裡）播種；（植物）結籽，脫籽；（植物）自播；（喻）使萌芽，使發展；用晶粒物質使冷凝（結晶）（尤指促雲化雨）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用作種子的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seed</b> is the small, hard part of a plant from which a new plant grows. 種子","examples":["I sow the seed in pots of soil-based compost. 我把種子種在一盆盆施有堆肥的土裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the <b>seeds of</b> something when you want to talk about the beginning of a feeling or process that gradually develops and becomes stronger or more important. (事物的) 起源","examples":["He raised questions meant to plant seeds of doubts in the minds of jurors. 他提出了一些問題，意欲引起陪審員的疑心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports such as tennis or badminton, a <b>seed</b> is a player who has been ranked according to his or her ability. 種子選手","examples":["...Roger Federer, Wimbledon's top seed and the world No.1. …羅傑·費德勒，溫布林登網球賽的頭號種子選手，世界排名第一。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>seed</b> a piece of land, you plant seeds in it. 在 (地裡) 播種","examples":["Men mowed the wide lawns and seeded them. 男人們修剪了大片的草坪，然後在上面播了種。","The primroses should begin to seed themselves down the steep hillside. 報春花應該開始沿那個陡峭的山坡一路撒播種子了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a player or a team <b>is seeded</b> in a sports competition, they are ranked according to their ability. 將 (選手或球隊) 排列名次","examples":["The Longhorns have won a national title and are seeded first overall. 朗霍恩隊曾得過一次全國冠軍，整體排名第一。","He is seeded second, behind Brad Beven. 他排名第二，位於布拉德·貝文之後。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If vegetable plants <b>go to seed</b>, they produce flowers and seeds as well as leaves. 開花結籽","examples":["...plants that had long since flowered, gone to seed, and died. …已經開花好久、結過籽並死去的植物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>has gone to seed</b>, you mean that they have become much less attractive, healthy, or efficient. 衰退; 退化","examples":["He says the economy has gone to seed. 他說經濟已經走向衰退。","...a retired cop who has gone to seed. …一名衰老的退休警察。"]}]}]},"september":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"九月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>September</b> is the ninth month of the year in the Western calendar. 9月","examples":["Her son, Jerome, was born in September. 她的兒子傑羅姆出生於9月。","We didn't make the original September 30 release date. 我們沒有趕上原定9月30日的發行日。"]}]}]},"second":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"第二（的），第二個（的）；（重要性、規模、質量等）居第二位的；另外的，外加的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"秒（時間單位）；片刻，瞬間；秒（角度單位）；次品，二等貨；<非正式>第二次上菜，添菜（seconds）；（車輛的）第二擋；（英國大學本科的）二等成績學位；<英>（學校或大學的）二年級；（棒球的）二壘；正式支援，附議；（體育俱樂部的）預備隊（the seconds）；粗麵粉，粗粉面包；（尤指拳擊比賽或舊時決鬥中的）助手；（樂）二度音程"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"支援，附議；<英>臨時調派，短期調任"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以第二位；第二，其次"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>second</b> is one of the sixty parts that a minute is divided into. People often say \"<b>a second</b>\" or \"<b>seconds</b>\" when they simply mean a very short time. 秒; 片刻","examples":["For a few seconds nobody said anything. 有幾秒鐘沒一個人說話。","It only takes forty seconds. 這隻需40秒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>seconds</b>, you have a second helping of food. (食物) 第二份","examples":["There's seconds if you want them. 你想要的話還有。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Seconds</b> are goods that are sold cheaply in stores because they have slight faults. 次品","examples":["These are not seconds, or unbranded goods, but first-quality products. 這些既不是次品也不是無牌貨，而是質量一流的產品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an honours degree of the second class, usually further divided into an upper and lower designation 二等榮譽學位 (Full term second-class honours degree)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"ord.","pos_name":"序數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>second</b> item in a series is the one that you count as number two. 第二","examples":["...the second day of his visit to Delhi. …他訪問德里的第二天。","...their second child. …他們的第二個孩子。","...the Second World War. …第二次世界大戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Second</b> is used before superlative adjectives to indicate that there is only one thing better or larger than the thing you are referring to. 第二…的 (用於形容詞最高階前)","examples":["The party is still the second strongest in Italy. 該黨仍是義大利第二大黨。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>second</b> when you want to make a second point or give a second reason for something. 第二; 其次","examples":["First, the weapons should be intended for use only in retaliation after a nuclear attack. Second, the possession of the weapons must be a temporary expedient. 首先，這些武器應當只在遭受核襲擊後反擊時才使用。其次，這些武器的擁有必須是一種臨時的應急手段。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>second</b> a proposal in a meeting or debate, you formally express your agreement with it so that it can then be discussed or voted on. 附議","examples":["...Bryan Sutton, who seconded the motion against fox hunting. …附議反對獵狐動議的布賴恩·薩頓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>second</b> what someone has said, you say that you agree with them or say the same thing yourself. 贊同","examples":["The UN secretary-general seconded the appeal for peace. 聯合國秘書長支援這項和平呼籲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you experience something <b>at second hand</b>, you are told about it by other people rather than experiencing it yourself. 間接地","examples":["Most of them, after all, had not been at the battle and had only heard of the massacre at second hand. 他們中的大多數畢竟沒有親歷那場戰爭而只是間接聽說過那場大屠殺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>second to none</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very good indeed or the best that there is. 不亞於任何一個的","examples":["Our scientific research is second to none. 我們的科學研究不亞於任何人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>second only to</b> something else, you mean that only that thing is better or greater than it. 僅次於某物","examples":["As a major health risk hepatitis is second only to tobacco. 肝炎僅次於菸草是主要的健康隱患之一。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to transfer (an employee) temporarily to another branch, etc 借調(某僱員)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to transfer (an officer) to another post, often retiring him to a staff or nonregimental position 使(軍官)調離","examples":[]}]}]},"sentence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"句子，句；判決，判刑；命題"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"判決，宣判，判刑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sentence</b> is a group of words which, when they are written down, begin with a capital letter and end with a period, question mark, or exclamation mark. Most sentences contain a subject and a verb. 句子","examples":["Here we have several sentences incorrectly joined by commas. 這裡有幾個誤用逗號連線的句子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a law court, a <b>sentence</b> is the punishment that a person receives after they have been found guilty of a crime. 刑罰","examples":["They are already serving prison sentences for their part in the assassination. 他們已經因為參與暗殺而在監獄服刑。","He was given a four-year sentence. 他被判處了4年徒刑。","The court is expected to pass sentence later today. 預計法庭將於今天晚些時候宣佈判決。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a judge <b>sentences</b> someone, he or she states in court what their punishment will be. 宣判; 判決","examples":["A military court sentenced him to death in his absence. 一家軍事法院在他未到庭的情況下判處他死刑。","She was sentenced to nine years in prison. 她被判處9年監禁。"]}]}]},"seventeen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十七"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十七，十七個；（首字母大寫，Seventeen）美國青少女雜誌《十七歲》"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十七的，十七個的；十七歲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Seventeen</b> is the number 17. 17; 十七","examples":["Jenny is seventeen years old. 珍妮17歲。"]}]}]},"seventy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"七十"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"七十；七十個（人或物）；七十歲；（複數 seventies）70 到 79 之間的數字，如年齡七十多歲、溫度七十多度（多指華氏）；（the seventies）二十世紀七十年代（1970–1979）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"七十的；七十個的；七十歲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Seventy</b> is the number 70. 70; 七十","examples":["Seventy people were killed. 70人喪生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>seventies</b>, you are referring to numbers between 70 and 79. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>seventies</b>, you are aged between 70 and 79. If the temperature is <b>in the seventies</b>, it is between 70 and 79. 70多; 七十幾 (指70到79之間的數字)","examples":["I thought it was a long way to go for two people in their seventies, but Sylvia loved the idea. 我認為對於兩個七十多歲的人來說這是一段很長的路，但是西爾維婭卻喜歡這個主意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The seventies</b> is the decade between 1970 and 1979. 70年代; 七十年代 (指1970 到1979之間的年代)","examples":["In the late Seventies, things had to be new, modern, revolutionary. 在20世紀70年代末，一切都得新奇、現代、有創意。"]}]}]},"seven":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"七，七個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"七；七個人；七點鐘；七歲；（Seven）（土、法、俄）謝文（人名）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"七的，七個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Seven</b> is the number 7. 7; 七","examples":["Sarah and Ella have been friends for seven years. 薩拉和埃拉已經是7年的朋友了。"]}]}]},"sense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感覺官能（即視、聽、嗅、味、觸五覺）；（對某物的）感覺；道理，合理性；見識，良好的判斷；理智，理性；理解力，判斷力；意義，含義；（數，物理）指向，方向"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"感覺到，覺察到；（機器）檢測出"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（遺傳）有意義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>senses</b> are the physical abilities of sight, smell, hearing, touch, and taste. 感覺功能","examples":["She stared at him again, unable to believe the evidence of her senses. 她再次盯著他，不敢相信自己的感覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>sense</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you think that it is the case, although you may not have firm, clear evidence for this belief. 感覺","examples":["Suddenly you got this sense that people were drawing themselves away from each other. 突然你有了這樣的感覺即人們正在彼此疏遠。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>sense of</b> guilt or relief, for example, you feel guilty or relieved. 感覺","examples":["When your child is struggling for life, you feel this overwhelming sense of guilt. 當你的孩子為生活而奔波時，你就會有這種強烈的內疚感。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>sense of</b> something such as duty or justice, you are aware of it and believe it is important. 意識; 觀念","examples":["My sense of justice was offended. 我的正義感受到了冒犯。","We must keep a sense of proportion about all this. 我們必須把握好所有這些事情的輕重緩急。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>sense</b> <b>of</b> timing or style has a natural ability with regard to timing or style. You can also say that someone has a bad <b>sense</b> <b>of</b> timing or style. 理解力; 天賦","examples":["He has an impeccable sense of timing. 他時間感很強。","Her dress sense is appalling. 她的著裝品位讓人汗顏。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Sense</b> is the ability to make good judgments and to behave sensibly. 理智; 判斷力","examples":["...when he was younger and had a bit more sense. …當他較為年輕、較為理智的時候。","When that doesn't work they sometimes have the sense to seek help. 當那樣做行不通時，他們會想到時不時地去尋求幫助。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that there is no <b>sense</b> or little <b>sense</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you mean that it is not a sensible thing to do because nothing useful would be gained by doing it. 意義","examples":["There's no sense in pretending this doesn't happen. 假裝此事沒有發生是沒用的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>sense</b> of a word or expression is one of its possible meanings. 意義; 含義","examples":["...a noun which has two senses. …一個有兩種含義的名詞。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sense</b> something, you become aware of it or you realize it, although it is not very obvious. 覺察到; 意識到","examples":["She probably sensed that I wasn't telling her the whole story. 她很可能覺察到我沒有告訴她全部真相。","He looks about him, sensing danger. 他環顧四周，覺察到了危險。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sense</b> is used in several expressions to indicate how true your statement is. For example, if you say that something is true <b>in a sense</b>, you mean that it is partly true, or true in one way. If you say that something is true <b>in a</b> general <b>sense</b>, you mean that it is true in a general way. 在某種意義上; 在一般意義上","examples":["In a sense, both were right. 在某種意義上，兩者都對。","Though his background was modest, it was in no sense deprived. 他的出身背景一般般，但絕算不上貧窮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>makes sense</b>, you can understand it. 有意義; 言之有理","examples":["He was sitting there saying, \"Yes, the figures make sense.\" 他坐在那裡說：“是的，這些數字有其道理。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>make sense of</b> something, you succeed in understanding it. 理解","examples":["Provided you didn't try to make sense of it, it sounded beautiful. 只要你不試圖理解，它聽起來是美的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a course of action <b>makes sense</b>, it seems sensible. 看來明智","examples":["It makes sense to look after yourself. 照顧好你自己是明智的。","The project should be re-appraised to see whether it made sound economic sense. 該專案應重新評估，看看在經濟上是否合情合理。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has come to</b> their <b>senses</b> or <b>has been brought to</b> their <b>senses</b>, you mean that they have stopped being foolish and are being sensible again. 恢復理智","examples":["Eventually the world will come to its senses and get rid of them. 最終這個世界會恢復理智，除掉它們。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>talks sense</b>, you mean that what they say is sensible. 說得有理","examples":["When he speaks, he talks sense. 他言之必有理。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>have a sense that</b> something is true or <b>get a sense that</b> something is true, you think that it is true. 意識到","examples":["Do you have the sense that you are loved by the public? 你意識到自己受公眾喜愛了嗎?"]}]}]},"shark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鯊魚；<非正式>坑蒙拐騙的人，詐騙者；鯊尾魚；冬夜蛾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>（多指男子在社交場合中）努力追逐性伴侶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shark</b> is a very large fish. Some sharks have very sharp teeth and may attack people. 鯊魚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person who preys on or victimizes others, esp by swindling or extortion 坑蒙拐騙的人; 詐騙者","examples":[]}]}]},"sheep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羊，綿羊；膽小鬼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sheep</b> is a farm animal which is covered with thick curly hair called wool. Sheep are kept for their wool or for their meat. 羊","examples":["...grassland on which a flock of sheep were grazing. …有一群羊正在吃草的草地。"]}]}]},"service":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公共服務系統，公共事業；（服務性行業或機構所提供的）服務；（對顧客的）接待，招待；工作，效勞；服務費；政府機構，公務部門；兵役，軍隊；（機器的）使用；<舊>僕人，傭人；<英> 服務站；宗教儀式；檢修，保養；整套餐具；發球，發球方式；班車，車次；（法律檔案的）送達"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"維修，檢修；支付（債務）利息；為……提供服務；（雄性動物）與（雌性動物）交配"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"員工專用的； 部隊的；提供服務的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>service</b> is something that the public needs, such as transportation, communications facilities, hospitals, or energy supplies, which is provided in a planned and organized way by the government or an official body. 公共服務機構; 公共服務系統","examples":["The postal service has been trying to cut costs. 郵政系統一直在試圖削減成本。","We have started a campaign for better nursery and school services. 我們已開展了一場運動，以改善幼兒園和學校的服務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can sometimes refer to an organization or private company as a particular <b>service</b> when it provides something for the public or acts on behalf of the government. 官方機構; 政府的行政部門","examples":["The Agriculture Department has ultimate control over the Forest Service. 農業部對林務局有最終控制權。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an organization or company provides a particular <b>service</b>, they can do a particular job or a type of work for you. 服務; 服務專案","examples":["The kitchen maintains a twenty-four hour service and can be contacted via reception. 廚房提供24小時服務，可透過接待處聯絡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Services</b> are activities such as tourism, banking, and selling things which are part of a country's economy, but are not concerned with producing or manufacturing goods. 服務性工作; 服務性行業","examples":["Mining rose by 9.1%, manufacturing by 9.4% and services by 4.3%. 採礦業增長了9.1%，製造業增長了9.4%，服務業增長了4.3%。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The level or standard of <b>service</b> provided by an organization or company is the amount or quality of the work it can do for you. 服務質量; 服務水平","examples":["Taking risks is the only way employees can provide effective and efficient customer service. 只有承擔風險，僱員們才能提供高效的客戶服務。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A bus or train <b>service</b> is a route or regular trip that is part of a transportation system. 交通線路","examples":["The local bus service is well run and extensive. 當地的公交線路運營良好，四通八達。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>services</b> are the things that you do or the skills that you use in your job, which other people find useful and are usually willing to pay you for. 專業性服務","examples":["I have obtained the services of a top photographer to take our pictures. 我得到了一位頂級攝影師的服務。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>service</b> or <b>services</b> <b>to</b> a particular organization or activity, you mean that they have done a lot of work for it or spent a lot of their time on it. 效力; 供職","examples":["You've given a lifetime of service to athletics. 你一生致力於體育事業。","Most employees had long service with the company and were familiar with our products. 絕大部分僱員在公司供職多年，熟悉我們的產品。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>Services</b> are the army, the navy, the air force and the marines. (包括陸、海、空軍和海軍陸戰隊在內的) 軍隊","examples":["Some of the money could be spent on persuading key specialists to stay in the Services. 可以花費一部分資金挽留重要專家在軍隊工作。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Service</b> is the work done by people or equipment in the army, navy, or air force, for example, during a war. 兵役; 作戰","examples":["Units are being called up today for service in the Gulf. 今天正在徵調一些部隊去海灣服役。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When you receive <b>service</b> in a restaurant, hotel, or shop, an employee asks you what you want or gives you what you have ordered. (飯店、酒店、商店等的) 服務","examples":["Service was attentive and the meal proceeded at a leisurely pace. 服務很周到，飯吃得悠閒從容。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"A <b>service</b> is a religious ceremony that takes place in a church or synagogue. 宗教儀式; 禮拜","examples":["After the hour-long service, his body was taken to a cemetery in the south of the city. 長達1小時的宗教儀式之後，他的遺體被送往城南的一座公墓裡。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If a vehicle or machine has a <b>service</b>, it is examined, adjusted, and cleaned so that it will keep working efficiently and safely. 保養","examples":["The car needs a service. 這輛車需要一次保養。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"A <b>dinner</b> <b>service</b> or a <b>tea</b> <b>service</b> is a complete set of plates, cups, saucers, and other pieces of china. 整套餐具","examples":["...a 60-piece dinner service. …一套60件的餐具。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"In tennis, badminton, and some other sports, when it is your <b>service</b>, it is your turn to serve. (網球、羽毛球等的) 發球","examples":["She conceded just three points on her service during the first set. 她在第1局中發球只丟了3分。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Service</b> is used to describe the parts of a building or structure that are used by the staff who clean, repair, or take care of it, and are not usually used by the public. 員工專用的","examples":["I went out through the kitchen and down the service lift 我穿過廚房，乘員工專用電梯下樓。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a vehicle or machine <b>serviced</b>, you arrange for someone to examine, adjust, and clean it so that it will keep working efficiently and safely. 做保養","examples":["I had my car serviced at the local garage. 我在當地的汽車修理廠給我的車做了保修。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>services</b> an organization, a project, or a group of people, they provide it with the things that it needs in order to function properly or effectively. 為…效力","examples":["There are now 400 staff at headquarters, servicing our regional and overseas work. 目前總部有400名員工致力於我們本地以及海外的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> someone <b>a service</b>, you do something that helps or benefits them. 幫某人一個忙","examples":["You are doing me a great service, and I'm very grateful to you. 你正在幫我一個大忙，我非常感謝你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a piece of equipment or type of vehicle is <b>in service</b>, it is being used or is able to be used. If it is <b>out of service</b>, it is not being used, usually because it is not working properly. (不) 在使用中","examples":["Cuts in funding have meant that equipment has been kept in service long after it should have been replaced. 撥款減少意味著裝置達到該替換的期限後還要使用很長時間。","In 1882, the city's first electric tram cars went into service. 1882年，該市第1批電車投入使用。"]}]}]},"shirt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"襯衫，恤衫；球衣；<英>運動隊隊員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shirt</b> is a piece of clothing that you wear on the upper part of your body. Shirts have a collar, sleeves, and buttons down the front. 襯衫","examples":[]}]}]},"shake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搖動，抖動；削弱，動搖；發抖，哆嗦；握手；使震驚，使煩亂；使改變（態度、信念）；擺脫，克服；舞動（拳頭、棍子等）；抖掉，抖出；使勁甩動，急劇晃動；搖頭（以示否定）；（聲音）顫抖"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搖動，搖晃；奶昔；（搖動容器後的）撒出物；<非正式>哆嗦，顫抖（the shakes）；<美>木製牆面板；<非正式>地震；（樂）顫音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shake</b> something, you hold it and move it quickly backward and forward or up and down. You can also <b>shake</b> a person, for example, because you are angry with them or because you want them to wake up. 搖晃; 抖動; 甩動","examples":["The nurse took the thermometer, shook it, and put it under my armpit. 護士拿出體溫計，甩了甩，然後放在我的腋窩下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shake</b> <b>yourself</b> or your body, you make a lot of quick, small, repeated movements without moving from the place where you are. 搖晃 (身體)","examples":["As soon as he got inside, the dog shook himself. 他一進去，那條狗就搖頭擺尾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>shake</b> your <b>head</b>, you turn it from side to side in order to say \"no\" or to show disbelief or sadness. 搖 (頭)","examples":["\"Anything else?\" Chris asked. Kathryn shook her head wearily. “還有別的事嗎？”克里斯問道。凱瑟琳疲憊地搖了搖頭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>shake</b> your fist or an object such as a stick <b>at</b> someone, you wave it in the air in front of them because you are angry with them. 揮舞 (拳頭、棍棒等)","examples":["The colonel rushed up to Earle and shook his gun at him. 上校衝到厄爾面前，衝他揮舞著槍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a force <b>shakes</b> something, or if something <b>shakes</b>, it moves from side to side or up and down with quick, small, but sometimes violent movements. 震動; 搖動","examples":["...an explosion that shook buildings several kilometres away. …震動了數公里之外的建築的一次爆炸。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>shake</b> something into a certain place or state means to bring it into that place or state by moving it quickly up and down or from side to side. 抖撒","examples":["She shook some pepper onto her sandwich. 她在她的三明治上撒了些胡椒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If an event or a piece of news <b>shakes</b> you, or <b>shakes</b> your confidence, it makes you feel upset and unable to think calmly. 震驚; 動搖 (信心)","examples":["There was no doubt that the news of Tandy's escape had shaken them all. 毫無疑問，坦迪逃跑的訊息震驚了他們所有人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If an event <b>shakes</b> a group of people or their beliefs, it causes great uncertainty and makes them question their beliefs. 動搖 (人心、信仰)","examples":["The five years she spent as a news correspondent in Moscow were five years that shook the world. 她在莫斯科當新聞記者的5年是動搖了世界的5年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shake</b> is also a noun. 搖晃; 抖動; 甩動","examples":["She picked up the bag of salad and gave it a shake. 她拿起了那袋沙拉搖了搖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shake</b> is also a noun. 搖晃","examples":["Take some slow, deep breaths and give your body a bit of a shake. 做幾次慢慢的深呼吸，輕輕晃動身體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Shake</b> is also a noun. 搖動","examples":["\"The elm trees are all dying,\" said Palmer, with a sad shake of his head. “這些榆樹全都要死了，”帕爾默說道，難過地搖了搖頭。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are shaking</b>, or a part of your body <b>is shaking</b>, you are making quick, small movements that you cannot control, for example, because you are cold or afraid. (因寒冷、害怕等而) 顫抖","examples":["He roared with laughter, shaking in his chair. 他放聲大笑，身子在椅子裡直搖晃。","My hand shook so much that I could hardly hold the microphone. 我的手抖得厲害以至於幾乎握不住麥克風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your voice <b>is shaking</b>, you cannot control it properly and it sounds very unsteady, for example, because you are nervous or angry. (聲音) 顫抖","examples":["His voice shaking with rage, he asked how the committee could keep such a report from the public. 他氣得聲音發抖，責問該委員會怎麼能向公眾隱瞞這樣一份報告。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shake</b> someone's <b>hand</b> or <b>shake</b> someone <b>by the hand</b>, you shake hands with them. 握某人的手","examples":["I said congratulations and walked over to him and shook his hand. 我向他表示祝賀並走過去和他握手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shake hands</b> <b>with</b> someone, you take their right hand in your own for a few moments, often moving it up and down slightly, when you are saying hello or goodbye to them, congratulating them, or agreeing on something. You can also say that two people <b>shake hands</b>. (與某人) 握手","examples":["He nodded greetings to Mary Ann and Michael and shook hands with Burke. 他對瑪麗·安和邁克爾點頭致意，然後和伯克握了手。"]}]}]},"sheet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"床單，被單；布罩，蓋布；紙片，紙張；（Excel 中的）工作表；簡要記錄，紀要；一整版郵票；（尤指大地區系列地圖的一部分的）一張地圖；薄板，薄片；（冰或水的）一大片；（雨或火）一大片；拉帆繩，帆腳索；敞艙船的首尾區域"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用布）蓋上，裹上；把（帆）扣緊（或放鬆）；（雨）傾盆（或瓢潑）而下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sheet</b> is a large rectangular piece of cotton or other cloth that you sleep on or cover yourself with in a bed. 床單; 被單","examples":["Once a week, a maid changes the sheets. 女僕每個星期換一次床單。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sheet</b> <b>of</b> paper is a rectangular piece of paper. (一) 張 (紙)","examples":["...a sheet of newspaper. …一張報紙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>sheet</b> to refer to a piece of paper which gives information about something. (一份) 資料","examples":["...information sheets on each country in the world. …有關世界各國的情報資料。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>sheet</b> <b>of</b> glass, metal, or wood is a large, flat, thin piece of it. (一) 塊 (玻璃、金屬或木頭等)","examples":["...a cracked sheet of glass. …一塊裂開的玻璃。","Overhead cranes were lifting giant sheets of steel. 高架起重機正吊起一塊塊巨大的鋼材。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>sheet</b> <b>of</b> something is a thin wide layer of it over the surface of something else. (一) 大層 (覆蓋物)","examples":["...a sheet of ice. …一大層冰。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to provide with, cover, or wrap in a sheet 包裹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(of rain, snow, etc) to fall heavily (雨，雪等)下得很大","examples":[]}]}]},"ship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大）船，艦；三（或多）桅帆船；<非正式> 艇（尤指賽艇）；宇宙飛船；<美> 飛機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用船、飛機、卡車）運送，運輸；遣送（某人）；推出（計算機商品），（使）上市；（水手）在船上工作，在船上服役；舷側進水；把（槳架中的槳）放在船內；給船安裝（舵、桅杆等）；<舊> 上船，乘船；乘船旅行；提供船隻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ship</b> is a large boat which carries passengers or cargo. 輪船","examples":["Within ninety minutes the ship was ready for departure. 90分鐘內輪船就準備好了出發。","We went by ship over to America. 我們乘輪船去美國。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people, supplies, or goods <b>are shipped</b> somewhere, they are sent there on a ship or by some other means of transportation. 運送","examples":["We'll ship your order to the address we print on your cheques. 我們將把你預訂的貨物送到我們印在你單據上的地址。","Food is being shipped to drought-stricken Southern Africa. 食物正被運送到遭受旱災的南非。"]}]}]},"shape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"形狀，外形；形態，特徵；狀況，身體狀況；健壯；（朦朧的）影像；（事物平常或本來的）樣子；有序的排列，條理清楚；偽裝，假裝；特定形狀的東西，模型；身材"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"形成，影響；使成形，塑造；計劃，思考出；產生（聲音，詞）；使適合，使符合；（運動員）擺姿勢，做動作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>shape</b> <b>of</b> an object, a person, or an area is the appearance of their outside edges or surfaces, for example, whether they are round, square, curved, or fat. 外形; 形狀","examples":["Each mirror is made to order and can be designed to almost any shape or size. 每面鏡子都是定製做的，而且能設計成幾乎任何形狀或規格。","...little pens in the shape of baseball bats. …棒球球棒形狀的小鋼筆。","...sofas and chairs of contrasting shapes and colours. …形狀和顏色反差很大的沙發和椅子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to something that you can see as a <b>shape</b> if you cannot see it clearly, or if its outline is the clearest or most striking aspect of it. (模糊的) 影像","examples":["The great grey shape of a tank rolled out of the village. 一個坦克狀的巨大灰影從村子裡開了出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>shape</b> is a space enclosed by an outline, for example, a circle, a square, or a triangle. 形狀","examples":["Imagine a sort of a kidney shape. 想像一種類似腎臟的形狀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>shape</b> <b>of</b> something that is planned or organized is its structure and character. (計劃或組織的) 框架","examples":["The last two weeks have seen a lot of talk about the future shape of Europe. 在過去的兩週裡有許多關於歐洲的未來格局的討論。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that <b>shapes</b> a situation or an activity has a very great influence on the way it develops. 塑造","examples":["Like it or not, our families shape our lives and make us what we are. 不管喜歡與否，我們的家庭塑造我們的生活並鑄就我們的個性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shape</b> an object, you give it a particular shape, using your hands or a tool. 使成…形","examples":["Cut the dough in half and shape each half into a loaf. 把生麵糰切成兩半，分別捏成長條狀。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say, for example, that you will not accept something <b>in any shape or form</b>, or <b>in any way, shape or form</b>, you are emphasizing that you will not accept it in any circumstances. 以任何形式","examples":["I don't condone violence in any shape or form. 我決不容忍任何形式的暴力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in shape</b>, or <b>in good shape</b>, they are in a good state of health or in a good condition. If they are <b>in bad shape</b>, they are in a bad state of health or in a bad condition. (身體、物體) 處於（良好/不良）狀況","examples":["...the Fatburner Diet Book, a comprehensive guide to getting in shape. …《減肥飲食指南》，一本保持健康的綜合指南。","He was still in better shape than many young men. 他依然比許多年輕人都健康。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lick</b>, <b>knock,</b> or <b>whip</b> someone or something <b>into shape</b>, you use whatever methods are necessary to change or improve them so that they are in the condition that you want them to be in. 用盡辦法塑造","examples":["You'll have four months in which to lick the recruits into shape. 你將有4個月的時間練就這些新兵。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>out of shape</b>, it is no longer in its proper or original shape, for example, because it has been damaged or wrongly handled. 變形了的","examples":["Once most wires are bent out of shape, they don't return to the original position. 大多數電線一旦彎曲變形就恢復不了原狀。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>out of shape</b>, you are unhealthy and unable to do a lot of physical activity without getting tired. 不健康的","examples":["I weighed 245 pounds and was out of shape. 我那時體重245磅，健康狀況不佳。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When something <b>takes shape</b>, it develops or starts to appear in such a way that it becomes fairly clear what its final form will be. 成形","examples":["In 1912 women's events were added, and the modern Olympic programme began to take shape. 1912年增加了女子專案，現代奧林匹克運動會開始初具雛形。"]}]}]},"shine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（太陽或其他光源）發光，照耀；（用電筒等）照射；（表面）發亮；磨光，擦亮；（眼睛或臉上因快樂而）放光；表現突出，出眾"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"光亮，光澤；擦亮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the sun or a light <b>shines</b>, it gives out bright light. 發光","examples":["It is a mild morning and the sun is shining. 這是一個和煦的早晨，太陽在照耀著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>shines</b> is very bright and clear because it is reflecting light. (因反光而) 發亮","examples":["Her blue eyes shone and caught the light. 她的藍眼睛在光照下閃閃發亮。","...a pair of patent leather shoes that shone like mirrors. …一雙像鏡子那樣閃光的黑漆皮鞋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who <b>shines</b> at a skill or activity does it extremely well. 幹得出色","examples":["Did you shine at school? 你在學校出類拔萃嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shine</b> a flashlight or other light somewhere, you point it there, so that you can see something when it is dark. 用…照射","examples":["One of the men shone a torch in his face. 其中一個男子用火把照著他的臉。","The man walked slowly toward her, shining the flashlight. 那個男子照著手電筒慢慢地向她走去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that has a <b>shine</b> is bright and clear because it is reflecting light. 光澤","examples":["This gel gives a beautiful shine to the hair. 這種髮膠帶給頭髮一種美麗的光澤。"]}]}]},"shoe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞋；馬蹄鐵；剎車蹄片；（尤指照相機上的）插口；（尤指雪橇滑板的）金屬箍；柱腳，樁靴；（巴卡拉紙牌或其他紙牌戲的）發牌盒；他人的處境（shoes）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（馬）釘蹄鐵；穿鞋（或靴）（be shod）；用金屬片包覆；為（輪子）裝輪胎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shoes</b> are objects which you wear on your feet. They cover most of your foot and you wear them over socks or stockings. 鞋","examples":["...a pair of shoes. …一雙鞋。","Low-heeled comfortable shoes are best. 舒適的低跟鞋是最好的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shoe</b> is the same as a . 馬蹄鐵","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a blacksmith <b>shoes</b> a horse, they attach horseshoes onto their feet. 給…釘蹄鐵","examples":["Blacksmiths spent most of their time repairing tools and shoeing horses. 鐵匠們把他們大部分時間用來修理工具和給馬釘蹄鐵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fill</b> someone's <b>shoes</b> or <b>step into</b> their <b>shoes</b>, you take their place by doing the job they were doing. 接替某人的位置","examples":["No one has been able to fill his shoes. 沒有人能接替他的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about being <b>in</b> someone's <b>shoes</b>, you talk about what you would do or how you would feel if you were in their situation. 處在某人的境地","examples":["I wouldn't want to be in his shoes. 我不願意處於他的境地。"]}]}]},"shore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（海、湖或大河的）濱，岸；沿海國家（或地區）（shores）；<法律>漲潮線與落潮線之間的地帶；支柱，撐柱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用支撐物（或梁）支撐；支援，幫助（shore up）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>shores</b> or the <b>shore</b> of a sea, lake, or wide river is the land along the edge of it. Someone who is <b>on shore</b> is on the land rather than on a ship. 岸","examples":["They walked down to the shore. 他們往下走到了岸邊。","...elephants living on the shores of Lake Kariba. …生活在卡里巴湖濱的大象。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a prop, post, or beam used to support a wall, building, ship in dry dock, etc 支柱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to move or drag (a boat) onto a shore 把(船)拖上海岸","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to prop or make safe with or as if with a shore 用支柱撐住; 使穩住","examples":[]}]}]},"shop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商店，店鋪；作坊，工場；<美>手工課，工藝課；<美>手工課教室；<英，非正式>購物，採購；<非正式>有關工作（或公事）的談話；<非正式>工作室，辦公室"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"購物；<英，非正式>舉報，告發；<美>試圖說服（公司出版或生產）；<非正式>（用軟體 Photoshop）修（圖）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shop</b> is a small store that sells one type of merchandise. (賣一種商品的) 店","examples":["...a gift shop. …一個禮品店。","He and his wife run their own antiques shop. 他和他的妻子經營他們自己的古董店。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shop</b> is a building or part of a building where things are sold. 商店","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"購物者","examples":["...crowds of Christmas shoppers. …聖誕節的購物人潮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a place where a particular service is offered as a particular type of <b>shop</b>. (提供某種服務的) 店","examples":["...the barber shop where Rodney sometimes had his hair cut. …羅德尼有時去理髮的那間理髮店。","...betting shops. …彩票銷售店。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>shop</b>, you go to stores or shops and buy things. 購物","examples":["He always shopped at the co-op. 他總在合作社購物。","...some advice that's worth bearing in mind when shopping for a new carpet. …一些在買新地毯時值得記住的建議。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that people <b>are talking shop</b>, you mean that they are talking about their work, and this is boring for other people who do not do the same work. 談論本行工作","examples":["Although I get on well with my colleagues, if you hang around together all the time you just end up talking shop. 儘管我和同事們相處得很融洽，但如果老呆在一起最後往往就談論工作了。"]}]}]},"singer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歌手，歌唱家；Singer（英語姓氏或人名，譯名有“桑熱”，常見“辛格”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>singer</b> is a person who sings, especially as a job. 歌手; 歌唱家","examples":["My mother was a singer in a dance band. 我媽媽是一個舞蹈團的歌手。"]}]}]},"shoulder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肩，肩膀；雙肩，上背部（shoulders）；（衣服的）肩部；（動物的）前腿連肩肉，肘子；山肩，瓶肩；<美> （公路旁的）路肩，緊急停車道；（擔負責任或艱難困苦或提供力量的）肩膀；（四足動物的）肩背；（鳥、昆蟲的）肩背"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"承擔，擔負；擠，闖；（用肩膀）推開，頂開；肩扛，肩挑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>shoulders</b> are between your neck and the tops of your arms. 肩","examples":["She led him to an armchair, with her arm round his shoulder. 她把他領到扶手椅上，手臂摟住了他的肩膀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you talk about someone's problems or responsibilities, you can say that they carry them <b>on</b> their <b>shoulders</b>. 承擔","examples":["No one suspected the anguish he carried on his shoulders. 沒有人懷疑他所承受的痛苦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>shoulder</b> is a cut of meat from the upper part of the front leg of an animal. 前腿肉","examples":["...shoulder of lamb. …羊的前腿肉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"On a busy road such as a motorway, the <b>shoulder</b> is the area at the side of the road where vehicles are allowed to stop in an emergency. (道路兩旁的) 緊急停車帶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shoulder</b> the responsibility or the blame for something, you accept it. 肩負","examples":["He has had to shoulder the responsibility of his father's mistakes. 他不得不肩負起他父親所犯錯誤的責任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shoulder</b> someone <b>aside</b> or if you <b>shoulder</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you push past people roughly using your shoulder. 用肩推; 用肩擠著走","examples":["The policemen rushed past him, shouldering him aside. 警察們從他身邊匆匆走過，用肩膀把他推到了一邊。","She could do nothing to stop him as he shouldered his way into the house. 當他用肩推擠著進那房子時，她根本就阻止不了他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone offers you <b>a shoulder to cry on</b> or is <b>a shoulder to cry on</b>, they listen sympathetically as you talk about your troubles. 聆聽傾訴者","examples":["Mrs. Barrantes longs to be at her daughter's side to offer her a shoulder to cry on. 巴蘭茨夫人希望能在女兒身邊聽她的傾訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something stands <b>head and shoulders</b> <b>above</b> other people or things, you mean that they are a lot better than them. 遠遠 (勝過)","examples":["The two candidates stood head and shoulders above the rest. 這兩名候選人遠遠勝過其他人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two or more people stand <b>shoulder to shoulder</b>, they are next to each other, with their shoulders touching. 肩並肩地","examples":["They fell into step, walking shoulder to shoulder with their heads bent against the rain. 他們步伐一致，肩並肩低著頭冒雨走著。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If people work or stand <b>shoulder to shoulder</b>, they work together in order to achieve something, or support each other. 同心協力地","examples":["They could fight shoulder-to-shoulder against a common enemy. 他們能同心協力地抗擊一個共同的敵人。"]}]}]},"shout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"叫嚷，大聲說；呼叫，喊叫；呼喚，呼喊（以引起注意）；大聲吼叫使……住口（或講話被淹沒）（shout sb. down）；將嗓子喊啞；<英> 張揚（shout about）；明確無誤地指出（或表示）；<澳新，非正式>（在酒吧、餐廳等）請人喝飲料（或吃東西）；使用大寫字母（寫電子郵件，表示生氣）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（憤怒、害怕、激動等的）呼喊，喊叫聲；<英，非正式> 請客的酒，輪到買酒請客；<英，非正式> 緊急召集消防隊（或警察）的叫喊聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shout</b>, you say something very loudly, usually because you want people a long distance away to hear you or because you are angry. 大聲說出; 大喊","examples":["He had to shout to make himself heard above the wind. 他不得不大喊，好讓別人能在風中聽見。","\"She's alive!\" he shouted triumphantly. “她活著！”他狂喜地大喊。","Andrew rushed out of the house, shouting for help. 安德魯衝出房子大喊救命。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shout</b> is also a noun. 大喊","examples":["The decision was greeted with shouts of protest from the crowd. 這項決定遭到了人群抗議的呼喊。"]}]}]},"silver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀；銀器（尤指餐具）；銀幣；銀（白）色；銀牌（silver medal 的簡寫）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"銀（白）色的；銀製的，含銀的，（有關）銀的；二十五週年紀念的，銀婚紀念的；<美>口才流利的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鍍（或包）銀於；<文>使具有銀色光澤，使變成銀色；使（頭髮）變成銀灰色（或銀白色）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Silver</b> is a valuable pale grey metal that is used for making jewellery and ornaments. 銀","examples":["...a hand-crafted brooch made from silver. …一枚銀製的手工胸針。","...amber earrings set in silver. …鑲於銀中的琥珀耳環。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Silver</b> consists of coins that are made from silver or that look like silver. 銀幣","examples":["...the basement where $150,000 in silver was buried. …埋著15萬美元銀幣的地下室。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>silver</b> to refer to all the things in a house that are made of silver, especially the cutlery and dishes. 銀器","examples":["He beat the rugs and polished the silver. 他拍打了地毯，擦亮了銀器。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Silver</b> is used to describe things that are shiny and pale grey in colour. 銀色的","examples":["He had thick silver hair which needed cutting. 他有一頭需要修剪的濃密銀髮。"]}]}]},"set":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放，置；使開始；把故事情節安排在；設定；擺放餐具；鑲嵌；安排；樹立；佈置；凝固；使現出堅定的表情；固定髮型；把（斷骨）復位；排版；為……譜曲；落（下）；佈置（戲劇、電影或電視節目的佈景）；（斷骨）癒合"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一組（類似的東西）；一組（配套使用的東西）；一夥（或一幫、一群）人；電視機；佈景 ；舞臺；（網球、排球比賽等的）盤；集；一組歌曲（或樂曲）；（在某學科上能力相當的）一批學生 ；（尤指堅定的）姿勢；頭髮的定型；凝固；獸穴；（供移植的）秧苗"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"位於（或處於）……的；安排好的；固定的；套（餐）；有可能的；不自然的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>set</b> <b>of</b> things is a number of things that belong together or that are thought of as a group. 套; 系列","examples":["There must be one set of laws for the whole of the country. 必須有一套適用於全國的法律。","The mattress and base are normally bought as a set. 床墊和床基通常成套購買。","...a chess set. …一副國際象棋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In tennis, a <b>set</b> is one of the groups of six or more games that form part of a match. (網球賽的) 一盤","examples":["Graf was leading 5-1 in the first set. 格拉夫在首盤比賽中以5-1領先。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In mathematics, a <b>set</b> is a group of mathematical quantities that have some characteristic in common. 集合","examples":["...the field of set theory. …集合論領域。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>set</b> for a play, movie, or television show is the furniture and scenery that is on the stage when the play is being performed or in the studio where filming takes place. (話劇的) 佈景; (電影的) 攝影棚; 拍片現場","examples":["From the first moment he got on the set, he wanted to be a director too. 從踏進攝影棚的第一刻起，他就也想成為一名導演。","He achieved fame for his stage sets for the Folies Bergeres. 他因為為《瘋狂的藤椅》設計舞臺佈景而一舉成名。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>set</b> is an appliance that receives television or radio signals. For example, a television set is a television. 電器裝置 (如電視機、收音機)","examples":["Children spend so much time in front of the television set. 孩子們在電視機前花的時間太多了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> something somewhere, you put it there, especially in a careful or deliberate way. (小心地) 放置","examples":["He took the case out of her hand and set it on the floor. 他從她手中接過箱子並置於地板上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>set</b> to say that a person or thing causes another person or thing to be in a particular condition or situation. For example, to <b>set</b> someone free means to cause them to be free, and to <b>set</b> something going means to cause it to start working. 使…處於某種狀況; 使開始","examples":["Set the kitchen timer going. 啟動廚房定時器。","Dozens of people have been injured and many vehicles set on fire. 已經有幾十人受傷，很多車輛被放火焚燒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>set</b> a clock or control, you adjust it to a particular point or level. 撥; 調","examples":["Set the volume as high as possible. 把音量儘量調大。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> a date, price, goal, or level, you decide what it will be. 決定; 確定","examples":["The conference chairman has set a deadline of noon tomorrow. 會議主席設定明天中午為最後期限。","A date will be set for a future meeting. 將為未來的會議確定一個日期。."]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> a certain value <b>on</b> something, you think it has that value. 確定","examples":["She sets a high value on autonomy. 她高度重視自主權。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> something such as a record, an example, or a precedent, you do something that people will want to copy or try to achieve. 樹立 (樣板)","examples":["Legal experts said her case would not set a precedent because it was an out-of-court settlement. 法律專家說她的案子不會開創先例，因為是庭外和解。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>sets</b> you a task or aim or if you <b>set</b> <b>yourself</b> a task or aim, you need to succeed in doing it. 分派; 制訂","examples":["I have to plan my academic work very rigidly and set myself clear objectives. 我必須給我的學術工作制訂非常嚴格的計劃，並給自己規定明確的目標。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>set</b> a trap means to prepare it to catch someone or something. 設定","examples":["He seemed to think I was setting some sort of trap for him. 他似乎認為我正給他設定某種陷阱。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When someone <b>sets</b> the table, they prepare it for a meal by putting plates and cutlery on it. 擺放","examples":["One would shop and cook, another would set the table and another would wash up. 一人會購物和烹飪，一人擺桌子，另外一人洗餐具。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>sets</b> a poem or a piece of writing <b>to</b> music, they write music for the words to be sung to. 為…譜曲; 為…配樂","examples":["He has attracted much interest by setting ancient religious texts to music. 他為古代宗教經文譜曲，引起了很多人的興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>set</b> in a particular place or position, it is in that place or position. 處於…的; 位於…的","examples":["The castle is set in 25 acres of beautiful grounds. 城堡坐落於方圓25英畝的宜人場地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>set</b> <b>into</b> a surface, it is fixed there and does not stick out. 嵌入的","examples":["The man unlocked a gate set in a high wall and let me through. 那人開啟砌在高牆中的門，放我過去了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>set</b> to describe something which is fixed and cannot be changed. 固定不變的","examples":["A set period of fasting is supposed to bring us closer to godliness. 通常認為一段固定的齋戒期可以使我們更虔誠。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>set</b> book must be studied by students taking a particular course. 指定的","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a play, movie, or story is <b>set</b> in a particular place or period of time, the events in it take place in that place or period. 以…為背景的","examples":["The play is set in a small Midwestern town. 這出戏是以中西部的一個小城鎮為背景的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>set</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are ready to do it or are likely to do it. If something is <b>set</b> <b>to</b> happen, it is about to happen or likely to happen. 作好準備的; 有可能的","examples":["Roberto Baggio was set to become one of the greatest players of all time. 羅伯特·巴喬有可能成為有史以來最偉大的球星之一。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you are <b>set on</b> something, you are strongly determined to do or have it. If you are <b>set against</b> something, you are strongly determined not to do or have it. 執意的","examples":["She was set on going to an all-girls school. 她執意要去一所女子學校讀書。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as jelly, melted plastic, or cement <b>sets</b>, it becomes firm or hard. 凝固; 凝結","examples":["You can add ingredients to these desserts as they begin to set. 你可以在那些甜點快凝固時新增一些成分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the sun <b>sets</b>, it goes below the horizon. (太陽) 落下","examples":["They watched the sun set behind the distant dales. 他們遠觀夕陽落下山谷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>sets the scene</b> or <b>sets the stage</b> <b>for</b> an event to take place, they make preparations so that it can take place. 為…作好準備; 為…創造條件","examples":["The Democratic convention has set the scene for a ferocious election campaign this autumn. 民主黨全國代表大會已為今秋激烈的競選活動作好了準備。"]}]}]},"sir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"先生，長官（尤指對上級的尊稱）；老師（學生對男教師的稱呼）；先生，閣下（正式或商業信函開頭的稱呼）（Dear Sir）；爵士（用於爵士或準男爵名字之前）（Sir）；<美，非正式>決不，的確（no/yes sir）（同 siree）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say <b>sir</b> as a polite way of addressing a man whose name they do not know, or an older man. For example, a shop assistant might address a male customer as <b>sir</b>. 先生 (對男性的客氣稱呼)","examples":["Excuse me sir, but would you mind telling me what sort of car that is? 對不起，先生，您能告訴我那是什麼樣的汽車嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sir</b> is the title used in front of the name of a knight or baronet. (爵士或從男爵名字前的頭銜) 爵士","examples":["She introduced me to Sir Tobias and Lady Clarke. 她把我介紹給託拜厄斯爵士和克拉克夫人。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use the expression <b>Dear Sir</b> at the beginning of a formal letter or a business letter when you are writing to a man. 敬啟者 (常用於正式函件或商務函件)","examples":["Dear Sir, Enclosed is a copy of my résumé for your consideration. 敬啟者，茲附上我的簡歷一份，請予以考慮。"]}]}]},"shot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"射擊，開槍（或炮），槍聲；射手，槍手；彈丸；批評的話；嘗試，努力；擊球，射門；鉛球；發射；照片，（電影的）鏡頭；注射；一口，一小杯（烈性酒）；少量；機率，可能性 ；鉛沙彈"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雜色的，閃色的；破爛不堪，筋疲力盡；充滿（某種特質或情感）；<美，澳新>醉的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開（槍），射擊；射出（弓箭等）；狩獵（shoot 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shot</b> is the past tense and past participle of . (shoot)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shot</b> is an act of firing a gun. 開槍","examples":["He had murdered Perceval at point blank range with a single shot. 他在近距離只用一槍就射殺了珀西瓦爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is a good <b>shot</b> can shoot well. Someone who is a bad <b>shot</b> cannot shoot well. 射擊手","examples":["He was not a particularly good shot because of his eyesight. 他由於視力緣故並不是一個特別好的射手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports such as football, golf, or tennis, a <b>shot</b> is an act of kicking, hitting, or throwing the ball, especially in an attempt to score a point. 射門; 擊球; 投籃","examples":["He had only one shot at goal. 他只有一次射門在門框內。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>shot</b> is a photograph or a particular sequence of pictures in a movie. 照片; (電影的) 連續鏡頭","examples":["I decided to try for a more natural shot of a fox peering from the bushes. 我決定嘗試拍攝一隻狐狸從灌木叢中偷窺的一個更自然的鏡頭。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have a <b>shot at</b> something, you attempt to do it. 嘗試","examples":["The heavyweight champion will be given a shot at Holyfield's world title. 這個重量級拳擊冠軍將要挑戰霍利菲爾德的世界冠軍頭銜。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>shot</b> <b>of</b> a drug is an injection of it. 注射","examples":["He administered a shot of Nembutal. 他進行了一針“寧必妥”的注射。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>shot</b> <b>of</b> a strong alcoholic drink is a small glass of it. 一小杯","examples":["...a shot of vodka. …一小杯伏特加酒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"small round pellets of lead collectively, as used in cartridges 鉛彈","examples":[]},{"num":"9.","zh":"a heavy metal ball used in the shot put 鉛球","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to weight or load with shot 將子彈上膛","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of textiles) woven to give a changing colour effect 閃色的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> something your <b>best shot</b>, you do it as well as you possibly can. 盡力做某事","examples":["I don't expect to win. But I am going to give it my best shot. 我並不期望能贏。但是我要盡力而為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The person who <b>calls the shots</b> is in a position to tell others what to do. 發號施令","examples":["The directors call the shots and nothing happens without their say-so. 董事們發號施令，沒有他們的指示什麼都不能做。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>like a shot</b>, you do it without any delay or hesitation. 立刻; 毫不遲疑地","examples":["I heard the key turn in the front door and I was out of bed like a shot. 我聽見鑰匙開前門的聲音，立刻從床上起來了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>a</b> <b>long shot</b>, you mean that it is unlikely to succeed, but is worth trying. 勝算不大的嘗試","examples":["The deal was a long shot, but Bagley had little to lose. 這宗交易不太可能成功，但巴格萊沒什麼可損失的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"People sometimes use the expression <b>by a long shot</b> to emphasize the opinion they are giving. 根本 (表示強調)","examples":["The missile-reduction treaty makes sweeping cuts, but the arms race isn't over by a long shot. 削減導彈條約引起大範圍的裁減，但是軍備競賽根本沒有結束。"]}]}]},"sixteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十六，十六個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十六的，十六個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sixteen</b> is the number 16. 16; 16個","examples":["...exams taken at the age of sixteen. …16歲時參加的考試。","He worked sixteen hours a day. 他每天工作16個小時。"]}]}]},"sixty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"六十，六十個；六十歲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（僅複數 sixties）六十幾；六十多歲；the sixties 指二十世紀六十年代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sixty</b> is the number 60. 60; 60個","examples":["...the sunniest April for more than sixty years. …六十多年來晴天最多的一個4月。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>sixties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 60 and 69. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>sixties</b>, you are aged between 60 and 69. If the temperature is <b>in the sixties</b>, it is between 60 and 69 degrees. (年齡或溫度) 60到69的數字","examples":["...a lively widow in her sixties. …一位年過花甲精神抖擻的寡婦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The sixties</b> is the decade between 1960 and 1969. (20世紀的) 60年代","examples":["In the sixties there were the deaths of the two Kennedy brothers and Martin Luther King. 20世紀60年代發生了肯尼迪兩兄弟和馬丁·路德·金的死亡事件。"]}]}]},"sight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"視力，視覺；看見，見到；視野，視域；景物，景象；名勝，景點（sights）；志向，目標；（槍或炮上的）瞄準器，（光學儀器的）觀測器；<非正式> 奇怪的人，滑稽的人（或事物）；<非正式> 許多，大量；<舊> 觀點，見解"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（突然）看到，（遠遠）看見；把（槍）瞄準；（用觀測器）觀測；調整（火器）的瞄準器，調整（光學儀器）的觀測器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"見票即付的；即席的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>sight</b> is their ability to see. 視力","examples":["My sight is failing, and I can't see to read any more. 我的視力正在下降，不能再看書了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The sight of</b> something is the act of seeing it or an occasion on which you see it. 看見","examples":["I faint at the sight of blood. 我一看見血就暈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sight</b> is something that you see. 景象","examples":["The practice of hanging clothes across the street is a common sight in many parts of the city. 在大街上晾曬衣服在該市的許多地區是很常見的景象。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>sights</b> are the places that are interesting to see and that are often visited by tourists. 名勝; 風景","examples":["We'd toured the sights of Paris. 我們已遊覽了巴黎的名勝。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sight</b> someone or something, you suddenly see them, often briefly. (在一瞬間) 突然看見","examples":["The security forces sighted a group of young men that had crossed the border. 安全部隊在一瞬間突然看見了一群越過了邊境的年輕人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>catch sight of</b> someone, you suddenly see them, often briefly. 瞬間內突然看見某人","examples":["Then he caught sight of her small black velvet hat in the crowd. 隨後他突然看見她的黑色絲絨小帽在人群中閃過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something seems to have certain characteristics <b>at first sight</b>, you mean that it appears to have the features you describe when you first see it but later it is found to be different. 乍一看","examples":["The theory is not as simple as you might think at first sight. 這個理論並不像你乍看時想到的那麼簡單。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>in sight</b> or <b>within sight</b>, you can see it. If it is <b>out of sight</b>, you cannot see it. 看得見/看不見","examples":["The sandy beach was in sight. 那片沙灘映入眼簾。","The Atlantic coast is within sight of the hotel. 從那個酒店可以看見大西洋的海岸線。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a result or a decision is <b>in sight</b> or <b>within sight</b>, it is likely to happen within a short time. 即將發生","examples":["An agreement on many aspects of trade policy was in sight. 有關貿易政策諸多方面的一項協議即將簽訂了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>lose sight of</b> an important aspect of something, you no longer pay attention to it because you are worrying about less important things. 忽略","examples":["In some cases, U.S. industry has lost sight of customer needs in designing products. 在一些情況下，美國工業在設計產品時忽略了顧客的需求。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone is ordered to do something <b>on sight</b>, they have to do it without delay, as soon as a person or thing is seen. 一看見…就","examples":["Troops shot anyone suspicious on sight. 軍隊一見可疑的人就開槍。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>set</b> your <b>sights on</b> something, you decide that you want it and try hard to get it. 以某事為奮鬥目標","examples":["They have set their sights on the world record. 他們把目標瞄向了世界紀錄。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something <b>in</b> your <b>sights</b>, you are trying hard to achieve it, and you have a good chance of success. If you <b>have</b> someone <b>in</b> your <b>sights</b>, you are determined to catch, defeat, or overcome them. 志在取得某事; 決意抓獲、打敗或征服某人","examples":["The Giants' slugger also has fourth place in his sights, needing 13 homers to move past Frank Robinson's 586. 巨人隊的強擊手也對第4名志在必得，需要擊出13個本壘打才能超過弗蘭克·羅賓遜的586分。","Is this knowledge of yours the reason the murderer now has you in his sights? 就是因為你知道的這些事兇犯才在追殺你嗎？"]}]}]},"six":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"六，數字 6；六個；六個人（或物）一組；六歲；六點鐘"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Six）<美，德>西克斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Six</b> is the number 6. 六; 六個","examples":["...a glorious career spanning more than six decades. …六十多年輝煌的職業生涯。"]}]}]},"sister":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"姐姐，妹妹；（稱志同道合者）姐妹；（女權運動中的）姐妹；姊妹，大姐，妹妹（婦女對其他婦女表示友好和支援時的用語）；<非正式>姐妹，大姐，妹子（用作女性間的稱呼）；<美>大姐，小妹（美國黑人婦女之間使用的稱呼）；修女，女教友（Sister）；<英>護士（長）（Sister）；（美國大學）女生聯誼會會員；（尤指組織之間的）姐妹（關係）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同類的，同質的，如同姐妹的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>sister</b> is a girl or woman who has the same parents as you. 姐; 妹","examples":["His sister Sarah helped him. 他姐姐薩拉幫助了他。","...Vanessa Bell, the sister of Virginia Woolf. …弗吉尼亞·伍爾夫的姐姐瓦內莎·貝爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sister</b> is a title given to a woman who belongs to a religious community. 修女","examples":["Sister Francesca entered the chapel. 弗朗西絲卡修女走進小教堂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe a woman as your <b>sister</b> if you feel a connection with her, for example, because she belongs to the same race, religion, country, or profession. 姐妹 (對同種族、宗教、國家，或職業女性的親切說法); 女同胞","examples":["Modern woman has been freed from many of the duties that befell her sisters in times past. 現代女性已從舊時代姐妹們肩負的許多責任中解放出來了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>sister</b> to describe something that is of the same type or is connected in some way to another thing you have mentioned. For example, if a company has a <b>sister</b> company, they are connected. 同型別的; 姐妹般的","examples":["...the International Monetary Fund and its sister organization, the World Bank. …國際貨幣基金組織和它的姐妹機構，世界銀行。"]}]}]},"side":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一旁，側邊；（相對中間而言的）邊，側；側面；方面，情況；立場，意見；一方，一派；邊緣；體側，肋部；身旁，身邊；（平面圖形的）邊；一面；內壁，內面；（立方體的）面；斜面，坡面；一面紙的文字；<英， 非正式>自負，傲慢；運動隊，球隊；母系，父系，血統；<美>配菜；一扇（肉）；<英>電影片道；<西印度>（一對東西中的）一個，一隻；（球的）側旋"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"旁邊的，側面的；次要的，附帶的；主菜外附加的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"支援，站在……一邊；給......鋪外牆板；給......裝上側面，形成......的側面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>side</b> <b>of</b> something is a position to the left or right of it, rather than in front of it, behind it, or on it. 一側","examples":["On one side of the main entrance there's a red plaque. 大門口的一側有塊紅色匾牌。","...a photograph with Joe and Ken on each side of me. …一張喬和肯在我兩側的照片。","...the nations on either side of the Pacific. …太平洋兩岸的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>side</b> of an object, building, or vehicle is any of its flat surfaces which is not considered to be its front, its back, its top, or its bottom. 側面","examples":["We put a notice on the side of the box. 我們在這箱子的一側貼了一張通知。","A carton of milk lay on its side. 一盒牛奶側躺著放在那裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>sides</b> of a hollow or a container are its inside vertical surfaces. 內側面","examples":["The rough rock walls were like the sides of a deep canal. 粗糙的巖壁就像一條很深的運河的兩岸。","Line the base of the dish with greaseproof paper and lightly grease the sides. 在盤子的底部墊一層防油紙，並在內側塗上少許油。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>sides</b> <b>of</b> an area or surface are its edges. 邊緣","examples":["Park on the side of the road. 在那條路邊停車。","...a small beach on the north side of the peninsula. …那個半島北邊上的一個小海灘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The two <b>sides</b> <b>of</b> an area, surface, or object are its two halves. (地區、表面或物體的一分為二的) 一半","examples":["She turned over on her stomach on the other side of the bed. 她翻身趴到了床的另一半邊。","The major centre for language is in the left side of the brain. 語言的主要中心在左半腦。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The two <b>sides</b> of a road are its two halves on which traffic travels in opposite directions. (往返車道的) 一半","examples":["It had gone on to the wrong side of the road and hit a car coming in the other direction. 它駛入了逆行車道，撞上了一輛迎面開來的車。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you talk about the other <b>side</b> of a town, a country, or the world, you mean a part of the town, the country, or the world that is very far from where you are. (城鎮、國家或世界的) 一端","examples":["He lives the other side of town. 他住在城鎮的另一端。","He saw the ship that was to transport them to the other side of the world. 他看到了那艘要把他們載往世界另一端的船。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Your <b>sides</b> are the parts of your body between your front and your back, from under your arms to your hips. 肋部","examples":["His arms were limp at his sides. 他的手臂無力地垂在兩側。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone is <b>by</b> your <b>side</b> or <b>at</b> your <b>side</b>, they stay near you and give you comfort or support. 身邊","examples":["He was constantly at his wife's side. 他那時一直陪伴在他妻子身邊。","He calls me 20 times a day and needs me by his side in the evening. 他一天給我打20次電話，晚上還需要我陪在他身邊。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"The two <b>sides</b> of something flat, for example, a piece of paper, are its two flat surfaces. You can also refer to one side of a piece of paper filled with writing as one <b>side</b> of writing. (紙張等的) 一面","examples":["The new copiers only copy onto one side of the paper. 這批新影印機只能影印到單面紙上。","Fry the chops until brown on both sides. 把排骨的兩面煎成棕色。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"One <b>side</b> of a tape or record is what you can hear or record if you play the tape or record from beginning to end without turning it over. (磁帶或唱片的) 一面","examples":["We want to hear side A. 我們想聽A面。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"The different <b>sides</b> in a war, argument, or negotiation are the groups of people who are opposing each other. (戰爭、爭論或談判中的) 一方","examples":["Both sides appealed for a new ceasefire. 雙方都呼籲新一輪的停火。","Any solution must be acceptable to all sides. 任何解決方案都必須使各方能接受。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"The different <b>sides</b> <b>of</b> an argument or deal are the different points of view or positions involved in it. (爭論或交易中的) 一方的觀點","examples":["His words drew sharp reactions from people on both sides of the issue. 他的言辭激起了問題雙方的強烈反應。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"In sports, a <b>side</b> is a team. 運動隊","examples":[]},{"num":"15.","zh":"A particular <b>side</b> of something such as a situation or someone's character is one aspect of it. 方面","examples":["He is in charge of the civilian side of the UN mission. 他在聯合國使團中負責平民方面的事務。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"The <b>mother's side</b> and the <b>father's side</b> of your family are your mother's relatives and your father's relatives. 家系; 血統","examples":["So was your father's side more well off? 那麼你父親那邊的親戚以前更富裕？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Side</b> is used to describe things that are not the main or most important ones of their kind. 次要的","examples":["She slipped in and out of the theatre by a side door. 她從側門溜進去又溜出了那家劇院。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person or country <b>sides</b> <b>with</b> another, they support them in an argument or a war. If people or countries <b>side</b> <b>against</b> another person or country, they support each other against them. 支援; 站在一起反對","examples":["There has been much speculation that they might be siding with the rebels. 有很多猜測說他們可能會支援叛亂者們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people or things are <b>side by side</b>, they are next to each other. 並排","examples":["We sat side by side on two wicker seats. 我們並排坐在兩張柳條椅上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people work or live <b>side by side</b>, they work or live closely together in a friendly way. 和睦相處","examples":["...areas where different nationalities have lived side by side for centuries. …不同民族的人和睦相處了幾個世紀的地區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something moves <b>from side to side</b>, it moves repeatedly to the left and to the right. 左右來回","examples":["She was shaking her head from side to side. 她那時正左右來回搖著頭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> someone's <b>side</b>, you are supporting them in an argument or a war. (在爭論或戰爭中) 支援","examples":["He has the Democrats on his side. 他有民主黨人的支援。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>on</b> your <b>side</b> or if you have it <b>on</b> your <b>side</b>, it helps you when you are trying to achieve something. 對你有利","examples":["The weather is rather on our side. 這天氣對我們很有利。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>on the</b> small <b>side</b>, you are saying politely that you think it is slightly too small. If you say that someone is <b>on the</b> young <b>side</b>, you are saying politely that you think they are slightly too young. 稍有點大或稍有點小等","examples":["He's quiet and a bit on the shy side. 他很安靜，稍微有點害羞。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone does something <b>on the side</b>, they do it in addition to their main work. 兼職","examples":["...ways of making a little bit of money on the side. …靠兼職賺點錢的方法。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> something <b>to one side</b> or <b>put</b> it <b>on one side</b>, you temporarily ignore it in order to concentrate on something else. 將某事暫時擱置一邊","examples":["He can now concentrate on a project he'd originally put to one side. 他現在能集中做他以前暫時擱置一邊的一個專案了。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone <b>to one side</b> or <b>draw</b> them <b>to one side</b>, you speak to them privately, usually in order to give them advice or a warning. 私下勸告某人","examples":["He took Sabrina to one side and told her about the safe. 他把薩博莉娜叫到了一邊，私下告訴了她有關安全的事項。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>take sides</b> or <b>take</b> someone's <b>side</b> in an argument or war, you support one of the sides against the other. (在爭論或戰爭中) 支援一方","examples":["We cannot take sides in a civil war. 內戰中，我們不能支援任何一方。"]}]}]},"skill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"技巧， 技藝；（特定的）技術，技能"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"培訓（工人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>skill</b> is a type of work or activity which requires special training and knowledge. (專門) 技術","examples":["Most of us will know someone who is always learning new skills, or studying new fields. 我們大多數人都會認識一些總在學習新技術或研究新領域的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Skill</b> is the knowledge and ability that enables you to do something well. 技能; 技藝","examples":["The cut of a diamond depends on the skill of its craftsman. 切割鑽石的好壞取決於工匠的技藝。"]}]}]},"show":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"顯示，表明；給……看，出示；演示，教；帶領，引領；表露出，顯示出；（對某人）表現出，對待；容易顯出，容易看到；標示，標明；描繪，描述；放映，播出；展示，展出；露面，出現；證明，證實；替（動物）報名參加比賽；<非正式> （婦女）已顯出身孕；<美>獲得第三名（或前三名）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"演出，歌舞表演；（電視或廣播）節目；展覽，展覽會；表現，行為；假象，假裝；景象；事情，場面；動物比賽；（分娩或月經時的）見紅；<美，澳新，非正式>（做某事的）機會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shows</b> <b>that</b> a state of affairs exists, it gives information that proves it or makes it clear to people. 顯示; 表明","examples":["Research shows that young people still look to parents as their main source for health information. 研究表明年輕人仍然指望父母作為他們主要的健康資訊來源。","These figures show an increase of over one million in unemployment. 這些資料表明失業人數增長超過100萬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a picture, chart, movie, or piece of writing <b>shows</b> something, it represents it or gives information about it. (圖畫、圖表、文章等) 表示","examples":["Figure 4.1 shows the respiratory system. 圖4.1所示的是呼吸系統。","The cushions, shown left, measure 20 x 12 inches and cost $39.95. 左邊展示的墊子尺寸是20 x 12英寸，價格為$39.95。","Much of the film shows the painter simply going about his task. 這部電影主要演的是這位畫家只是忙著自己的工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> someone something, you give it to them, take them to it, or point to it, so that they can see it or know what you are referring to. 拿給…看; 指給…看","examples":["Cut out this article and show it to your boss. 把這篇文章剪下來拿給你的老闆看。","He showed me the apartment he shares with Esther. 他指給我看他和埃斯特合住的公寓。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> someone to a room or seat, you lead them there. 引領","examples":["It was very good of you to come. Let me show you to my study. 你能來真是太好了。讓我帶你看我的書房。","Milton was shown into the office. 米爾頓被領進了辦公室。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> someone how to do something, you do it yourself so that they can watch you and learn how to do it. 向…演示","examples":["Claire showed us how to make a chocolate cake. 克萊爾向我們演示如何做巧克力蛋糕。","There are seasoned professionals who can teach you and show you what to do. 有經驗豐富的專業人員可以教你，並向你示範做什麼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>shows</b> or if you <b>show</b> it, it is visible or noticeable. 顯露","examples":["When he smiled he showed a row of strong white teeth. 他笑的時候露出了一排結實而潔白的牙齒。","Faint glimmers of daylight were showing through the trees. 微弱的日光從樹叢中透出。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>show</b> a particular attitude, quality, or feeling, or if it <b>shows</b>, you behave in a way that makes this attitude, quality, or feeling clear to other people. 流露出; 表現","examples":["She showed no interest in her children. 她流露出對自己的孩子沒有興趣。","Ferguson was unhappy and it showed. 弗格森不高興，而且表現了出來。","You show me respect. 請你對我尊重點。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>shows</b> a quality or characteristic or if that quality or characteristic <b>shows</b> <b>itself</b>, it can be noticed or observed. 表露出; 顯示出 (品質、特徵)","examples":["The story shows a strong narrative gift and a vivid eye for detail. 這個故事顯示出很強的敘事才能和對細節的生動觀察力。","Her popularity clearly shows no sign of waning. 她的受歡迎程度顯然沒有顯示出下降的跡象。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a company <b>shows</b> a profit or a loss, its accounts indicate that it has made a profit or a loss. 出現 (贏利或虧損)","examples":["It is the only one of the three companies expected to show a profit for the quarter. 這是3家公司中惟一1家有望在本季度出現贏利的公司。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>shows</b> a film or television programme, it is broadcast or appears on television or in the movie theatre. 放映; 播放","examples":["The TV news showed the same film clip. 電視新聞播放了同一個電影短片。","The movie is now showing at theatres around the country. 該部影片目前正在全國各地的影院上映。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"To <b>show</b> things such as works of art means to put them in an exhibition where they can be seen by the public. 展出","examples":["50 dealers will show oils, watercolours, drawings and prints from 1900 to 1992. 50位經銷商將要展出1900年到1992年的油畫、水彩畫、素描畫和版畫。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person you are expecting to meet does not <b>show</b>, they do not arrive at the place where you expect to meet them. 露面","examples":["There was always a chance he wouldn't show. 他總有可能不會露面。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Show up</b> means the same as . 露面","examples":["We waited until five o'clock, but he did not show up. 我們一直等到5點，但他卻沒有露面。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something <b>to show for</b> your efforts, you have achieved something as a result of what you have done. (努力) 收到成效","examples":["I'm nearly 31 and it's about time I had something to show for my time in my job. 我快三十一歲了，該是我在工作中的付出收穫成果的時候了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say <b>it just goes to show</b> or <b>it just shows</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you mean that what you have just said or experienced demonstrates that it is the case. 這就證明了…","examples":["I forgot all about the ring. Which just goes to show that getting good grades in school doesn't mean you're clever. 我完全忘了戒指的事情。這證明在校取得好成績並不意味著你就聰明。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>show</b> <b>of</b> a feeling or quality is an attempt by someone to make it clear that they have that feeling or quality. 表示","examples":["Miners gathered in the centre of Bucharest in a show of support for the government. 礦工聚集在了布加勒斯特市中心表示對政府的支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>for</b> <b>show</b>, you mean that it has no real purpose and is done just to give a good impression. 虛飾","examples":["The change in government is more for show than for real. 政府的這個變化更多是在裝樣子而不是真的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A television or radio <b>show</b> is a programme on television or radio. (電視或廣播) 節目","examples":["I had my own TV show. 我有過自己的電視節目。","...a popular talk show on a Cuban radio station. …古巴廣播電臺的一個受歡迎的訪談節目。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>show</b> in a theatre is an entertainment or concert, especially one that includes different items such as music, dancing, and comedy. 演出","examples":["How about going shopping and seeing a show? 去購物然後看場演出如何？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>show</b> is a public exhibition of things, such as works of art, fashionable clothes, or things that have been entered in a competition. 展覽會","examples":["Currently, the show is in Boston. 目前，這場展覽會正在波士頓舉行。","It plans about 30 such fashion shows this autumn in department stores. 計劃今年秋天在百貨公司舉行大約三十場這樣的時裝展覽會。"]}]}]},"size":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大小，尺寸；龐大，巨大；數量，規模；（尤指衣服、鞋子等的）尺寸，尺碼；特定尺寸；相應尺碼的人（或衣物）；（使紙張、布料堅挺且光亮的）漿料，（貼桌布用的）塗料"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"依大小分類（或排列）；按一定大小製作；改變......的大小； 給（衣服、紙張等）上漿，給......塗膠；<非正式> 大致評價，估量；估算（或測量某物）大小；可比擬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一定大小（或尺碼）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>size</b> <b>of</b> something is how big or small it is. Something's size is determined by comparing it to other things, counting it, or measuring it. 大小; 規模","examples":["In 1970 the average size of a French farm was 19 hectares. 1970年法國農場的平均面積是19公頃。","...shelves containing books of various sizes. …擺放著大大小小書籍的書架。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>size</b> <b>of</b> something is the fact that it is very large. 巨大; 龐大","examples":["He knows the size of the task. 他知道任務很重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>size</b> is one of a series of graded measurements, especially for things such as clothes or shoes. 尺寸; 尺碼","examples":["My sister is the same height but only a size 12. 我妹妹的身高一樣，但只穿12碼的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a thin gelatinous mixture, made from glue, clay, or wax, that is used as a sealer or filler on paper, cloth, or plaster surfaces 膠料; 漿糊 (Also called sizing)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to sort according to size 按大小排列","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to treat or coat (a surface) with size 上漿; 上塗料","examples":[]}]}]},"sky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天，天空；<文>天堂，天國之力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>把（球）擊向空中；（尤指在展覽中）把（畫）高掛在牆上；踢或擊高空球；把槳葉翹得過高；飛漲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>sky</b> is the space around the earth which you can see when you stand outside and look upward. 天空","examples":["The sun is already high in the sky. 太陽早已高掛在天上了。","...warm sunshine and clear blue skies. …溫暖的陽光和清澈的藍天。"]}]}]},"smile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"微笑；微笑著說，以微笑表示；現出（笑容）；覺得好笑，覺得高興；惠及，讚許"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"微笑，笑容；一臉笑意，喜滋滋的（all smiles）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>smile</b>, the corners of your mouth curve up and you sometimes show your teeth. People smile when they are pleased or amused, or when they are being friendly. 微笑","examples":["When he saw me, he smiled and waved. 他見到我時，他笑了笑，揮了揮手。","He rubbed the back of his neck and smiled ruefully at me. 他揉搓著後脖頸，衝我懊悔地笑了一下。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>smile</b> is the expression that you have on your face when you smile. 微笑","examples":["She gave a wry smile. 她露出苦笑。","\"There are some sandwiches if you're hungry,\" she said with a smile. “如果你餓了，那兒有些三明治，”她微笑著說。"]}]}]},"snake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛇；陰險狡詐的人；管道疏通器；蛇形浮動匯率制（the snake）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"蛇行，蜿蜒前進；拉（重物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snake</b> is a long, thin reptile without legs. 蛇","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>snakes</b> in a particular direction goes in that direction in a line with a lot of bends. 蜿蜒行進","examples":["The road snaked through forested mountains. 這條路蜿蜒穿過樹林覆蓋的群山。"]}]}]},"small":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小型的；（數量）少的；小規模的；無關緊要的，不重要的；幼小的，年幼的；（字母）小寫的；（嗓音）微弱的，輕柔的；一般的，非極端的；出醜的，羞愧的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>小件衣服（尤指內衣）（smalls）；後腰（the small of the/sb.'s back）；<西印度>小費，小額禮金（smalls）；小件物品；矮小的人"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"成小塊地；小小地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>small</b> person, thing, or amount of something is not large in physical size. (體積或規模等) 小的","examples":["She is small for her age. 相對她的年齡而言，她個子小了。","Stick them on using a small amount of glue. 用少量膠水把它們粘上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>small</b> group or quantity consists of only a few people or things. (規模) 小的","examples":["A small group of students meets regularly to learn Japanese. 一個小組的學生定期聚在一起學日語。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>small</b> child is a very young child. 幼小的","examples":["I have a wife and two small children. 我有妻子和兩個年幼的孩子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>small</b> to describe something that is not significant or great in degree. (程度上) 不重要的","examples":["It's quite easy to make quite small changes to the way that you work. 對你的工作方式做些相當細微的調整是很容易的。","No detail was too small to escape her attention. 最微小的細節也逃不過她的注意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Small</b> businesses or companies employ a small number of people and do business with a small number of clients. (生意或公司) 小規模的","examples":["...shops, restaurants and other small businesses. …商店、餐館和其他小規模生意。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone makes you look or feel <b>small</b>, they make you look or feel stupid or ashamed. 卑微的; 感到慚愧的","examples":["This may just be another of her schemes to make me look small. 這也許就是她要讓我羞愧的又一個詭計。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The small of</b> your <b>back</b> is the bottom part of your back that curves in slightly. (人體的) 後腰","examples":["Place your hands on the small of your back and breathe in. 把你的雙手放在後腰，然後吸氣。"]}]}]},"skin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"皮，皮膚；獸皮，皮毛；（水果或蔬菜的）外皮；香腸衣；（液體表面凝結的）薄皮，薄層；（建築物、飛機等的）外殼；<非正式>捲菸紙；（軟體、網站等的）介面，皮膚；<英，非正式>光頭；（盛液體的）皮囊；雪橇外皮，防滑底層（用海豹皮或其他材料做成，繫於雪橇下側以防攀登時向後滑動）；<非正式>（尤作爵士樂用語）鼓，鼓面；<非正式>色情文學作品（或影片）；<美>斯金牌戲（每一位玩牌者有一張牌，各自打賭這張牌不會是第一張與發出的牌配對）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"剝皮，削皮；擦破（身體某部位）；（傷口）長出新皮；<古>皮膚癒合；<非正式>（選手）輕鬆過球；<非正式>徹底擊敗，輕易擊敗（對手）；<非正式>騙取（某人的）錢財；<英，非正式>製作大麻香菸（skin up）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>skin</b> is the natural covering of your body. 皮膚","examples":["His skin is clear and smooth. 他的皮膚光潔滑潤。","There are three major types of skin cancer. 皮膚癌有3大類。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An animal <b>skin</b> is skin which has been removed from a dead animal. Skins are used to make things such as coats and rugs. 獸皮; 毛皮","examples":["That was real crocodile skin. 那是真正的鱷魚皮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>skin</b> of a fruit or vegetable is its outer layer or covering. 果皮; (蔬菜的) 外皮","examples":["The outer skin of the orange is called the \"zest.\" 橙子外層皮叫“橙皮”。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a <b>skin</b> forms on the surface of a liquid, a thin, fairly solid layer forms on it. (液體表面凝結的) 薄層; 薄皮","examples":["Stir the custard occasionally to prevent a skin forming. 不時攪動蛋奶沙司，以免凝結奶皮。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>skin</b> a dead animal, you remove its skin. 剝去…的皮","examples":["...with the expertise of a chef skinning a rabbit. …具有大廚剝兔皮的專長。"]}]}]},"soda":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蘇打，碳酸鈉；蘇打水，碳酸水；汽水（甜味碳痠軟飲料）；一杯（或一瓶、一罐）汽水；（Soda）人名（意）索達，（日）曾田（姓）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soda</b> is a sweet carbonated drink. 汽水","examples":["...a glass of diet soda. …一杯低熱量汽水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>soda</b> is a bottle of soda. 一瓶汽水","examples":["They had liquor for the adults and sodas for the children. 他們為成年人準備了酒，為孩子們準備了汽水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Soda</b> is the same as . 蘇打水","examples":[]}]}]},"soap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肥皂；<非正式>肥皂劇"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擦肥皂；<俚>對……拍馬屁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soap</b> is a substance that you use with water for washing yourself or sometimes for washing clothes. 肥皂","examples":["...a bar of lavender soap. …一塊薰衣草肥皂。","...a large box of soap powder. …一大盒肥皂粉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>soap</b> is the same as a . 肥皂劇","examples":[]}]}]},"smell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣味；臭味；嗅覺；嗅，聞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"有……氣味，發出......的氣味；聞出，聞到；（用鼻子湊過去）聞，嗅；有嗅覺，能聞出（smell sth. out）；散發異味，有難聞的氣味；覺察出，感覺到；看起來像，有……意味"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>smell</b> of something is a quality it has which you become aware of when you breathe in through your nose. 氣味","examples":["...the smell of freshly baked bread. …新烤麵包的氣味。","...horrible smells. …令人噁心的氣味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your sense of <b>smell</b> is the ability that your nose has to detect things. 嗅覺","examples":["...people who lose their sense of smell. …失去嗅覺的人們。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>smells</b> a particular way, it has a quality which you become aware of through your nose. 有…的氣味; 聞起來","examples":["The room smelled of lemons. 房間有股檸檬的氣味。","It smells delicious. 它聞起來真香。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>smells</b>, you mean that it smells unpleasant. 有臭味","examples":["Ma threw that out. She said it smelled. 媽把那個扔出去了。她說它已經有臭味了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smell</b> something, you become aware of it when you breathe in through your nose. 聞到","examples":["As soon as we opened the front door we could smell the gas. 我們一開啟前門就能聞到那煤氣味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>smell</b> something, you put your nose near it and breathe in, so that you can discover its smell. (鼻子湊近) 嗅","examples":["I took a fresh rose out of the vase on our table, and smelled it. 我從我們桌上的花瓶裡取出一支新鮮的玫瑰，聞了聞。"]}]}]},"sleep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"睡，睡覺；供……住宿；（尤指入夜後某地或建築物）沉寂，靜寂；<文>安息，安眠；發生性關係"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"睡眠，睡覺；（一段）睡眠時間；眵，眼屎；<文>死，長眠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sleep</b> is the natural state of rest in which your eyes are closed, your body is inactive, and your mind does not think. 睡眠; 睡覺","examples":["They were exhausted from lack of sleep. 他們因睡眠不足而疲憊不堪了。","Be quiet and go to sleep. 安靜，睡覺吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sleep</b> is a period of sleeping. (一段) 睡眠時間","examples":["I think he may be ready for a sleep soon. 我想他可能準備好了馬上睡一覺。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sleep</b>, you rest with your eyes closed and your mind and body inactive. 睡著; 睡覺","examples":["During the drive, the baby slept. 在行駛中那個嬰兒睡了。","I've not been able to sleep for the last few nights. 最近幾個晚上我一直無法入睡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a building or room <b>sleeps</b> a particular number of people, it has beds for that number of people. 供…住宿","examples":["The villa sleeps 10. 這幢別墅可供10人住宿。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cannot <b>get to sleep</b>, you are unable to sleep. 入睡","examples":["I can't get to sleep with all that singing. 那樣的歌聲讓我無法入睡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you didn't <b>lose</b> any <b>sleep</b> <b>over</b> something, you mean that you did not worry about it at all. 擔心","examples":["I didn't lose too much sleep over that investigation. 我不太擔心那起調查。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are trying to make a decision and you say that you will <b>sleep on it</b>, you mean that you will delay making a decision on it until the following day, so you have time to think about it. 把…留待以後解決","examples":["I need more time to sleep on it. It's a big decision and I want to make the right one. 我需要更多的時間再考慮一下。這是個重大的決定，我想做出正確的決定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a sick or injured animal <b>is put to sleep</b>, it is killed by a vet in a way that does not cause it pain. 使 (有病或受傷的動物) 無痛苦地死去","examples":["I'm going take the dog down to the vet's and have her put to sleep. 我打算把這隻狗帶到獸醫那兒，讓她無痛苦地死去。"]}]}]},"smoke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（燃燒所產生的）煙，煙霧；吸菸，抽菸；<非正式>（抽的）香菸，（吸的）毒品； <英，非正式>（倫敦之類的）大城市（the Smoke）；無常的事物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸菸，吸毒品；（作為習慣）抽菸；冒煙，冒氣；用煙燻制；（戰鬥或競賽中）徹底擊敗；<美，非正式>開槍殺死（某人）；<美，非正式>用力快擊（球）；瀰漫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Smoke</b> consists of gas and small bits of solid material that are sent into the air when something burns. 煙","examples":["A cloud of black smoke blew over the city. 一團黑煙拂過了這座城市。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Smoke</b> is also a noun. 吸菸","examples":["Someone came out for a smoke. 有人為了吸菸而出來了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is smoking</b>, smoke is coming from it. 冒煙","examples":["The chimney was smoking fiercely. 煙囪猛烈地冒著煙。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>smokes</b> a cigarette, cigar, or pipe, they suck the smoke from it into their mouth and blow it out again. If you <b>smoke</b>, you regularly smoke cigarettes, cigars, or a pipe. 吸 (煙); 吸菸","examples":["He was sitting alone, smoking a big cigar. 他那時正獨自坐著，抽著一根大雪茄。","It's not easy to quit smoking. 戒菸不容易。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If fish or meat <b>is smoked</b>, it is hung over burning wood so that the smoke preserves it and gives it a special flavour. 熏製 (魚或肉)","examples":["...the grid where the fish were being smoked. …當時燻魚所用的烤架。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone says <b>where there's smoke there's fire</b>, they mean that there are rumours or signs that something is true so it must be at least partly true. 有火就冒煙; 無風不起浪","examples":["A lot of the stuff in the story is not true, but I have to say that where there's smoke there's fire. 故事中有許多事情都不是真的，但我不得不說，無風不起浪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>goes up in smoke</b>, it is destroyed by fire. 被燒燬","examples":["The crew were able to put out the fire after only 25 acres had gone up in smoke. 在僅僅25公頃被燒燬之後，隊員們能夠將火撲滅了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something that is very important to you <b>goes up in smoke</b>, it fails or ends without anything being achieved. 化為烏有","examples":["I was afraid you'd say no, and my dream would go up in smoke. 我擔心你會說不，那我的夢想就化為烏有了。"]}]}]},"snow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雪，積雪；降雪，一場雪；下雪天；（因訊號差出現在電視螢幕的）“雪花”干擾；似雪的菜餚；似雪的冷凍氣體；<非正式>可卡因"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"下雪，飄雪；<美，非正式>（用花言巧語）矇騙，使相信；使灑落；使變白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Snow</b> consists of a lot of soft white pieces of frozen water that fall from the sky in cold weather. 雪","examples":["Six inches of snow blocked roads. 六英寸的大雪阻塞了道路。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When <b>it snows</b>, snow falls from the sky. 下雪","examples":["It had been snowing all night. 整個晚上一直在下雪。"]}]}]},"sofa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙發；長椅；（Sofa）人名；（塞）索法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sofa</b> is a long, comfortable seat with a back and usually with arms, which two or three people can sit on. 長沙發","examples":[]}]}]},"someone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"有人，某人；重要人物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>someone</b> or <b>somebody</b> to refer to a person without saying exactly who you mean. 某人","examples":["Her father was shot by someone trying to rob his small retail shop. 她父親被某個試圖搶劫他的小零售店的人開槍打中了。","I need someone to help me. 我需要有人幫我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a person is <b>someone</b> or <b>somebody</b> <b>in</b> a particular kind of work or <b>in</b> a particular place, you mean that they are considered to be important in that kind of work or in that place. 重要人物","examples":["\"Before she came around,\" she says, \"I was somebody in this town.\" “她來這之前，”她說，“我在這個鎮上是個人物。”"]}]}]},"son":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兒子；孩子（長者對男孩或年輕男子的稱呼）；（某國或地區出生並能作其代表的）男性，子；聖子（耶穌基督）（the Son）；（動物的）雄性後代；男性後裔；（某個人、某種影響或某種環境）薰陶出的人；（司鐸對男子或男孩的稱呼）孩子（my son）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>son</b> is their male child. 兒子","examples":["He shared a pizza with his son Laurence. 他與他的兒子勞倫斯共吃一個比薩餅。","Sam is the seven-year-old son of Eric Davies. 薩姆是埃裡克•戴維斯的7歲兒子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A man, especially a famous man, can be described as a <b>son</b> of the place he comes from. 來自某地的人 (尤指名人)","examples":["...New Orleans's most famous son, Louis Armstrong. …新奧爾良最有名氣的人，路易斯•阿姆斯特朗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Some people use <b>son</b> as a form of address when they are showing kindness or affection to a boy or a man who is younger than them. 孩子 (用於稱呼年齡小於自己的男子)","examples":["Don't be frightened by failure, son. 不要被失敗嚇倒了，孩子。"]}]}]},"soup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"湯，羹；<非正式>發動機等的馬力，動力；<非正式>困境，麻煩（主要用於 in the soup）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（常作 soup up）給（發動機、車輛等）加速，增加馬力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soup</b> is liquid food made by boiling meat, fish, or vegetables in water. 湯","examples":["...home-made chicken soup. …自家做的雞湯。"]}]}]},"something":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"某事，某物；……或諸如此類的東西，……什麼的；大致，大約，左右；什麼什麼（用於表示不記得人名、數字的餘下部分或歌詞等）；還算幸運的事；重要的人（或事）；（想法或建議）有道理，值得考慮；有點兒，有幾分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"稍微，有點；很，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>something</b> to refer to a thing, situation, event, or idea, without saying exactly what it is. 某物; 某事","examples":["He realized right away that there was something wrong. 他馬上意識到有地方不對了。","There was something vaguely familiar about him. 他身上有某些東西似曾相識。","\"You said there was something you wanted to ask me,\" he said politely. “你說過有什麼事情要問我，”他彬彬有禮地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>something</b> to say that the description or amount that you are giving is not exact. 有點像; 差不多","examples":["Clive made a noise, something like a grunt. 克萊夫發出了一陣噪聲，有點像呼嚕聲。","Their membership seems to have risen to something over 10,000. 他們的會員似乎已經增加到差不多超過一萬人了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing is <b>something</b> or is really <b>something</b>, you mean that you are very impressed by them. 真不錯","examples":["You're really something. 你的確真不錯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>something</b> in expressions like \"<b>that's something</b>\" when you think that a situation is not very good but is better than it might have been. 差強人意","examples":["Well, at least he was in town. That was something. 哦，至少他還在城裡。那也算不錯啦。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a thing is <b>something of</b> a disappointment, you mean that it is quite disappointing. If you say that a person is <b>something of</b> an artist, you mean that they are quite good at art. 有點兒","examples":["The city proved to be something of a disappointment. 結果這座城市證明有點兒令人失望。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>something in</b> an idea or suggestion, you mean that it is quite good and should be considered seriously. (想法或建議) 有道理","examples":["Could there be something in what he said? 他說的話是否有道理？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>something</b> in expressions such as \"<b>or something</b>\" and \"<b>or something like that</b>\" to indicate that you are referring to something similar to what you have just mentioned but you are not being exact. 諸如此類的東西","examples":["This guy, his name was Briarly or Beardly or something. 這個傢伙，他的名字叫布賴爾利，或比亞特利，或跟這差不多的。"]}]}]},"soil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泥土，土壤；（可供某物發展的）土壤，溫床；國土，領土；<文>耕作，務農（the soil）；糞便"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弄髒，玷汙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soil</b> is the substance on the surface of the earth in which plants grow. 土壤","examples":["We have the most fertile soil in the Midwest. 我們在中西部有最肥沃的土壤。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make or become dirty or stained 弄髒; 沾上汙垢","examples":[]}]}]},"song":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歌，歌曲；歌唱，聲樂；（鳥的）鳴囀，啼囀；押韻的詩歌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>song</b> is words and music sung together. 歌曲","examples":["...a voice singing a Spanish song. …一個唱著西班牙歌曲的嗓音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Song</b> is the art of singing. 歌唱","examples":["...dance, music, mime, and song. …舞蹈、音樂、啞劇和歌唱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A bird's <b>song</b> is the pleasant, musical sounds that it makes. 鳥鳴聲","examples":["It's been a long time since I heard a blackbird's song in the evening. 我已經好長時間沒在晚上聽到黑鸝的鳴叫聲了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>bursts into song</b> or <b>breaks into song</b>, they start singing. 開始唱歌","examples":["I feel as if I should break into song. 我感覺我似乎應該開始歌唱。"]}]}]},"soul":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靈魂；心靈；某種人；（用於否定句中）一個人（也沒有）；靈樂；感受強烈感情的能力；（藝術、音樂作品或文章中的）熱情，氣魄；精神，精髓；（某地的）人們，人口（souls）；（人類整體的）精神狀況，道德品質；（某種品質的）典範，化身；美國黑人文化（或種族尊嚴）；鬼魂"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"激情黑人的，黑人文化的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>soul</b> is the part of you that consists of your mind, character, thoughts, and feelings. Many people believe that your soul continues existing after your body is dead. 靈魂","examples":["She went to pray for the soul of her late husband. 她去為已故丈夫的靈魂祈禱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone as a particular kind of <b>soul</b> when you are describing their character or condition. 個性","examples":["He's a jolly soul. 他是個快活的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>soul</b> in negative statements like <b>not a soul</b> to mean nobody at all. 人 (用於否定句中)","examples":["I've never harmed a soul in my life. 我一生中從未傷害過任何人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Soul</b> is the same as . 靈魂音樂","examples":["...American soul singer Anita Baker. …美國靈樂歌手安妮塔•貝克。"]}]}]},"sour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"酸的，酸味的；（牛奶等）餿（味）的，酸臭的；不友善的，脾氣壞的；（關係、計劃等變得）壞的，令人不快的；（土壤）缺少石灰質的，酸性過重的；（石油，天然氣）含硫量較高的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）（關係、情況）變糟，變壞；（使）變酸，（使）酸腐；使喜悅減少"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有酸味的酒精飲料；酸味；苦事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>sour</b> has a sharp, unpleasant taste like the taste of a lemon. 酸的","examples":["The stewed apple was sour even with honey. 燉過的蘋果即使加了蜂蜜也還是酸的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sour</b> milk is milk that has an unpleasant taste because it is no longer fresh. 餿的","examples":["The milk had gone sour. 牛奶已經餿了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>sour</b> is bad-tempered and unfriendly. 脾氣壞的; 不友好的","examples":["She made a sour face in his direction. 她給了他一副不友善的臉色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a situation or relationship <b>turns</b> <b>sour</b> or <b>goes</b> <b>sour</b>, it stops being enjoyable or satisfactory. 令人失望的","examples":["Everything turned sour for me there. 對我來說那兒的一切都變得令人失望了。","The American dream is beginning to turn sour. 美國夢正開始破滅。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"脾氣壞地; 不友好地","examples":["\"Leave my mother out of it,\" he said sourly. “不要把我母親扯進去。”他生氣地說。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a friendship, situation, or attitude <b>sours</b> or if something <b>sours</b> it, it becomes less friendly, enjoyable, or hopeful. 使變糟; 變糟","examples":["If anything sours the relationship, it is likely to be real differences in their world-views. 假如有什麼事情使關係惡化的話，那可能就是他們在世界觀方面所存在的實質性差異。"]}]}]},"south":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"南，（羅盤的）南方；（某個地方、國家、區域的）南部；美國南部各州，英格蘭南部（the South）；（南半球的）發展中國家（the South）；（橋牌）坐在南首位置的人（South）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"位於南方的，朝南的；（風）來自南方的；（用於國家、州或地區等的名稱中）南部的，南部居民的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向南，朝南；去南方，在南方；低於（south of）；<美，非正式>下滑，惡化"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向南方，朝南；（天體）穿過子午線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>south</b> is the direction which is on your right when you are looking toward the direction where the sun rises. 南方","examples":["The town lies ten miles to the south of here. 該鎮位於這裡以南10英里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>south</b> <b>of</b> a place, country, or region is the part which is in the south. 南部","examples":["...vacations in the south of Mexico. …在墨西哥南部的假期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The South</b> is used to refer to the poorer, less developed countries of the world. 南方國家 (指較貧窮的不發達國家)","examples":["The debate will pit the industrial North against developing countries in the South. 這場辯論會使北方的工業國家和南方的發展中國家針鋒相對。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>south</b>, you travel toward the south. 向南","examples":["I drove south on Motorway 9. 我在9號高速公路上向南行駛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>south of</b> a place is positioned to the south of it. 在…的南方","examples":["They now own and operate a farm 50 miles south of Rochester. 他們現在在羅徹斯特南部50英里處擁有並經營一個農場。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>south</b> edge, corner, or part of a place or country is the part which is toward the south. 朝南的","examples":["...the south coast of Long Island. …長島的南海岸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"\"<b>South</b>\" is used in the names of some countries, states, and regions in the south of a larger area. 南部的","examples":["Next week the president will visit five South American countries in six days. 下週總統將在6天內訪問5個南美國家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>south</b> wind is a wind that blows from the south. (風) 來自南方的","examples":["...a mild south wind. …一股溫暖的南風。"]}]}]},"spoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"匙，勺子；（作打擊樂器用的）調羹對；一匙的量；調羹狀物品"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用匙舀，使成匙狀；高挑球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spoon</b> is an object used for eating, stirring, and serving food. One end of it is shaped like a shallow bowl and it has a long handle. 勺; 匙","examples":["He stirred his coffee with a spoon. 他用匙攪了攪咖啡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spoon</b> food into something, you put it there with a spoon. 用勺舀; 用匙舀","examples":["He spooned instant coffee into two of the mugs. 他用勺把速溶咖啡舀進了兩個杯子裡。"]}]}]},"stair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樓梯，階梯（stairs）；梯級；<文>（建築物內的）樓梯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stairs</b> are a set of steps inside a building which go from one floor to another. (建築物內樓層之間的) 樓梯","examples":["Nancy began to climb the stairs. 南希開始爬樓梯。","We walked up a flight of stairs. 我們往上走了一段樓梯。"]}]}]},"speech":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"演說，發言，談話；說話的能力；說話方式；口語，言語；（戲劇中的）臺詞；（該詞常用於使某人感到自己所說的話很愚蠢）長篇大論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Speech</b> is the ability to speak or the act of speaking. 言語能力; 說話","examples":["...the development of speech in children. …孩子言語能力的發展。","Intoxication interferes with speech and coordination. 醉酒影響言語能力和協調性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>speech</b> is the way in which you speak. 說話方式","examples":["His speech became increasingly thick and nasal. 他說話變得越來越帶口音且鼻音越來越重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Speech</b> is spoken language. 口語","examples":["He could imitate in speech or writing most of those he admired. 他能在口語或書寫中模仿大多數他崇拜的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>speech</b> is a formal talk which someone gives to an audience. 演說","examples":["She is due to make a speech on the economy next week. 她將在下週作有關經濟的演說。","He delivered his speech in French. 他用法語作的演講。"]}]}]},"sound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聲音，聲響；聽力範圍，聽距；樂音；（音樂演出、電影等的）音響錄製和播出，音響製作；無線電廣播；聲音，音響；（個人或樂隊的）音樂特色，音樂風格；<非正式>流行音樂（sounds）；海峽，海灣；厄勒海峽（the Sound）；印象，感覺；（檢查體腔的）醫用探子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）發聲，（使）作響；發出（警告等），（以……語調）發表；測量（水體）的深度；試探，探詢；聽起來像；（從嗓音中）聽起來；（用於談論印象或觀點）聽起來，似乎；發音；聽診（肺或其他體腔）；（醫）用探子檢查（人的膀胱或其他內腔）；（尤指鯨魚）向深海潛入"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無損傷的，健康的，堅實的；合理的，明智的，可靠的；全面的，透徹的；酣睡的，沉睡的；（懲罰）嚴厲的；不錯的，實實在在的；資金充實的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"酣暢地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sound</b> is something that you hear. 聲音","examples":["Peter heard the sound of gunfire. 彼得聽見了槍炮聲。","Liza was so frightened she couldn't make a sound. 莉莎驚嚇得發不出任何聲音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a relatively narrow channel between two larger areas of sea or between an island and the mainland 海峽","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sound</b> is energy that travels in waves through air, water, or other substances, and can be heard. 聲能","examples":["The aeroplane will travel at twice the speed of sound. 飛機將以兩倍於音速的速度飛行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>sound</b> on a television, radio, or CD player is what you hear coming from the machine. Its loudness can be controlled. (可調大小聲的) 播音","examples":["She went and turned the sound down. 她過去把聲音調小。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A singer's or band's <b>sound</b> is the distinctive quality of their music. 音樂風格","examples":["They have started showing a strong soul element in their sound. 他們已經開始在音樂風格中展示出一種強烈的靈歌因素。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can describe your impression of something you have heard about or read about by talking about <b>the sound of</b> it. (聽到或看到的) 感覺","examples":["Here's a new idea we liked the sound of. 這是個新想法，聽起來我們就喜歡。","I don't like the sound of Toby Osborne. 我不喜歡託比•奧斯伯恩的感覺。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a horn or a bell <b>sounds</b> or if you <b>sound</b> it, it makes a noise. 使發出聲音; 發出聲音","examples":["The buzzer sounded in Daniel's office. 丹尼爾辦公室的蜂鳴器響了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sound</b> a warning, you publicly give it. If you <b>sound</b> a note of caution or optimism, you say publicly that you are cautious or optimistic. 宣告","examples":["The archbishop has sounded a warning to world leaders on third world debt. 大主教已經發出警告提醒世界領導人注意第三世界的債務。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to seek to discover (someone's views, etc), as by questioning 透過詢問了解(某人的觀點)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to measure the depth of (a well, the sea, etc) by lowering a plumb line, by sonar, etc 測量(井、海等的)深度","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are describing a noise, you can talk about the way it <b>sounds</b>. 聽起來","examples":["They heard what sounded like a huge explosion. 他們聽見了一種像是巨大爆炸的聲音。","The creaking of the hinges sounded very loud in that silence. 鉸鏈的嘎吱聲在那寂靜中聽起來很響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you talk about the way someone <b>sounds</b>, you are describing the impression you have of them when they speak. 聽起來","examples":["She sounded a bit worried. 她聽起來有點焦慮不安。","Murphy sounds like a child. 墨菲聽起來像個孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you are describing your impression or opinion of something you have heard about or read about, you can talk about the way it <b>sounds</b>. 令人覺得","examples":["It sounds like a wonderful idea to me, does it really work? 在我聽來那像個好主意，但真管用嗎？","It sounds as if they might have made a dreadful mistake. 感覺似乎他們已經犯下了一個大錯。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a structure, part of someone's body, or someone's mind is <b>sound</b>, it is in good condition or healthy. 健康的; 狀況良好的","examples":["When we bought the house, it was structurally sound. 當我們買下這房子時，其結構完好無損。","Although the car is basically sound, I was worried about certain areas. 雖然這輛汽車基本狀況完好，但我擔心某幾個部分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sound</b> advice, reasoning, or evidence is reliable and sensible. 可靠的","examples":["They are trained nutritionists who can give sound advice on diets. 他們是訓練有素的營養師，能提供有關飲食的可靠建議。","Buy a policy only from an insurance company that is financially sound. 只買財政狀況良好的保險公司的保險。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's ideas as <b>sound</b>, you mean that you approve of them and think they are correct. 正確的","examples":["I am not sure that this is sound democratic practice. 我不能肯定這就是正確的民主做法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is in a <b>sound</b> sleep, they are sleeping very deeply. 酣 (睡) 的","examples":["She had woken me out of a sound sleep. 她把我從酣睡中叫醒了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sound</b> is also an adverb. 酣 (睡) 地","examples":["He was lying in bed, sound asleep. 他正躺在床上，睡得很香。"]}]}]},"sport":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某項）體育運動；體育運動；運動會（sports）；野外運動（尤指打獵或釣魚）；（狩獵、釣魚等活動帶來的）成就感；樂趣；<非正式>開朗大度的人；<澳>（用作友好稱呼，尤指對男子）朋友，老兄，哥們兒；（生）突變，芽變"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（引人注目地）穿戴，展示；嬉戲，玩耍"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"運動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sports</b> are games such as football and basketball and other competitive leisure activities which need physical effort and skill. 體育運動","examples":["I chose boxing because it is my favourite sport. 我選擇了拳擊，因為那是我最喜愛的運動。","She excels at sports. 她在體育運動方面很優秀。"]}]}]},"space":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"空間，空地；（尤指有特定用途的）空位，處所；（公共汽車等的）空座；開闊地，空曠處；開闊，空曠；太空，外層空間；宇宙空間；一段時間；屬於自己的空間；空格，空行；版面，篇幅；廣告專頁，廣告插播時間；（樂）（譜表的）線間空白；（電信）空號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（某物）隔開；在（詞語等）之間加空格；變得昏昏沉沉，瞪著眼發呆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>space</b> to refer to an area that is empty or available. The area can be any size. For example, you can refer to a large area outside as a large open <b>space</b> or to a small area between two objects as a small <b>space</b>. 空間; 間隔","examples":["...cutting down yet more trees to make space for houses. …砍掉更多的樹以騰出空間來蓋房屋。","I had plenty of space to write and sew. 我有足夠的空間來寫作和縫紉。","The space underneath could be used as a storage area. 下面的空間可被用作一個儲藏區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>space</b> is the area that is available for a particular activity or for putting a particular kind of thing in. 場所","examples":["...the high cost of office space. …辦公場所的高額費用。","You don't want your living space to look like a bedroom. 你不會希望你的起居室看上去像一間臥室。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place gives a feeling of <b>space</b>, it gives an impression of being large and open. 寬敞的空間","examples":["Large paintings can enhance the feeling of space in small rooms. 大幅畫作能增加小房間的寬敞感。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you give someone <b>space</b> to think about something or to develop as a person, you allow them the time and freedom to do this. 餘地","examples":["You need space to think everything over. 你需要留有餘地來仔細考慮一切。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The amount of <b>space</b> for a topic to be discussed in a document is the number of pages available to discuss the topic. 篇幅","examples":["We can't promise to publish a reply as space is limited. 因為篇幅有限，我們無法允諾刊登答覆。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>space of</b> time is a period of time. 一段 (時間)","examples":["They've come a long way in a short space of time. 他們在很短時間內從很遠的地方過來了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Space</b> is the area beyond the Earth's atmosphere, where the stars and planets are. 太空","examples":["The six astronauts on board will spend ten days in space. 宇宙飛船上的六位宇航員將在太空度過10天的時間。","...launching satellites into space. …發射人造衛星到外層空間。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Space</b> is the whole area within which everything exists. 宇宙空間","examples":["She felt herself transcending time and space. 她感覺自己正在超越時空。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"間隔","examples":["Generous spacing gives healthier trees and better crops. 足夠大的間距使樹長得更健康，莊稼長得更好。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>space</b> a series of things, you arrange them so that they are not all together but have gaps or intervals of time between them. 使分隔開","examples":["Women once again are having fewer children and spacing them further apart. 婦女們又一次開始生育較少的孩子，而且生孩子的時間間隔越來越大。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Space out</b> means the same as . 使分隔開","examples":["He talks quite slowly and spaces his words out. 他說得很慢，詞與詞之間都有停頓。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are staring <b>into space</b>, you are looking straight in front of you, without actually looking at anything in particular, for example because you are thinking or because you are feeling shocked. 茫然直視","examples":["He just sat in the dressing room staring into space. 他就坐在化妝室裡，茫然地望著前方。"]}]}]},"star":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星，恆星；演藝界明星，體壇名將；（電影、戲劇中的）主角，主演；重要人物，優秀人士；星狀，星形物；星號；（飯店、賓館等的）星級標誌；（占星術的）星相，星座（stars）；一定會發生；<非正式>好心的人，樂於助人者；星章；Y形三相電繞組；星狀網；用於海星或類似的棘皮動物的名字中"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"主演，使主演；給……加上星號；表現傑出；用星形物裝飾（或覆蓋）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最好的，最出色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>star</b> is a large ball of burning gas in space. Stars appear to us as small points of light in the sky on clear nights. 星","examples":["The nights were pure with cold air and lit with stars. 那些夜晚十分清靜，空氣清涼、繁星點點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a shape or an object as a <b>star</b> when it has four, five, or more points sticking out of it in a regular pattern. 星形; 星形物","examples":["Children at school receive coloured stars for work well done. 上學的孩子們表現好會得到彩星。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say how many <b>stars</b> something such as a hotel or restaurant has as a way of talking about its quality, which is often indicated by a number of star-shaped symbols. The more stars something has, the better it is. (賓館或飯店等的) 星級","examples":["...five star hotels. …五星級酒店。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Famous actors, musicians, and sports players are often referred to as <b>stars</b>. 明星","examples":["...star of the TV series Scrubs. …電視連續劇《實習醫生風雲》裡的明星。","By now Murphy is Hollywood's top male comedy star. 現在墨菲已是好萊塢頂級男喜劇明星。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Predictions about people's lives which are based on astrology and appear regularly in a newspaper or magazine are sometimes referred to as <b>the</b> <b>stars</b>. 星相","examples":["There was nothing in my stars to say I'd have travel problems! 我的星相上沒說我會有旅行問題！"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an actor or actress <b>stars in</b> a play or movie, he or she has one of the most important parts in it. (在某戲劇、電影中) 扮演主要角色","examples":["The previous year Adolphson had starred in a play in which Ingrid had been an extra. 上個年度阿道夫森曾主演了一部戲，在該戲中英格麗德是臨時演員。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a play or movie <b>stars</b> a famous actor or actress, he or she has one of the most important parts in it. 由…主演","examples":["...a Hollywood movie, \"The Secret of Santa Vittoria,\" directed by Stanley Kramer and starring Anthony Quinn. …一部由斯坦利·克萊默執導、安東尼·奎因主演的名為《聖維多利亞的秘密》的好萊塢影片。"]}]}]},"statement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宣告，報告；說明，說法，表態；結算單，報表；（某觀點的） 表達；（嫌犯或證人向警方提供的） 陳述，證詞；（文字）陳述，表述；評估報告（英國地方教育主管部門針對兒童的特殊需要而提出意見）；（樂）（作品主題或旋律的）呈現；（計算機程式中的）語句"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"對兒童進行特殊教育評估認定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>statement</b> is something that you say or write which gives information in a formal or definite way. (正式或明確的口頭或書面) 陳述; 宣告","examples":["Andrew now disowns that statement, saying he was depressed when he made it. 安德魯現在否認了那個宣告，說那是自己心情沮喪時作的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>statement</b> is an official or formal announcement that is issued on a particular occasion. (在特定場合的官方或正式的) 宣告","examples":["The statement by the military denied any involvement in last night's attack. 軍方的宣告否認其與昨晚的襲擊有任何關係。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the official account of events which a suspect or a witness gives to the police as a <b>statement</b>. (嫌犯或證人向警方提供的) 陳述; 證詞","examples":["The 350-page report was based on statements from witnesses to the events. 這份350頁的報告基於該事件目擊者的證詞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe an action or thing as a <b>statement</b>, you mean that it clearly expresses a particular opinion or idea that you have. (某觀點的) 表達","examples":["The following recipe is a statement of another kind – food is fun! 下面的食譜是另一種表述–食物就是樂趣！"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A printed document showing how much money has been paid into and taken out of a bank or investment account is called a <b>statement</b>. 結算清單","examples":["...the address at the top of your monthly statement. …你的月結算清單頂端的地址。"]}]}]},"station":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公共汽車、火車等的）車站；電視臺，廣播電臺；站，所，局；<舊>社會地位，身份；須堅守的位置，崗位；駐地，基地；（電臺或電視的）頻率，頻道；（澳大利亞或紐西蘭的）大牧場"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"駐紮，派駐；派往，安置在"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>station</b> or a train <b>station</b> is a building by a railway track where trains stop so that people can get on or off. 火車站","examples":["Ingrid went with him to the train station to see him off. 英格麗德和他一起去火車站送他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A bus <b>station</b> is a building, usually in a town or city, where buses stop, usually for a while, so that people can get on or off. (汽車) 站","examples":["I walked the two miles back to the bus station and bought a ticket home. 我走了兩英里回到汽車站買了一張回家的票。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about a particular radio or television <b>station</b>, you are referring to the company that broadcasts programmes. (電、電視) 臺","examples":["...an independent local radio station. …一家獨立的地方廣播電臺。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"被動及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If soldiers or officials <b>are stationed</b> in a place, they are sent there to do a job or to work for a period of time. 派駐","examples":["Reports from the capital, Lome, say troops are stationed on the streets. 來自首都洛美的報道說部隊駐紮在街道上。"]}]}]},"state":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狀態，狀況；緊張，焦慮；政府；國家；州，邦；<非正式>美國（the States）；國事禮儀，隆重儀式；（物質的）形態，態；（物理學）量子態；澤西、根西和奧爾德尼三島的立法機關（the States）；壓印，印圖；受公眾瞻仰和弔唁"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"州的；國事的，國事禮儀的；國家提供（或控制）的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"陳述，說明；規定，公佈；表現（主題，旋律）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to countries as <b>states</b>, particularly when you are discussing politics. (政治上所指的) 國家","examples":["Mexico is a secular state and does not have diplomatic relations with the Vatican. 墨西哥是個非宗教國家，和梵蒂岡沒有外交關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some large countries such as the U.S. are divided into smaller areas called <b>states</b>. (美國等大國的) 州","examples":["Leaders of the Southern states are meeting in Louisville. 南部各州的領導人們正在路易斯維爾會晤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The U.S. is sometimes referred to as <b>the States</b>. 美國","examples":["She bought it last year in the States. 她去年在美國買了它。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to the government of a country as <b>the state</b>. 政府","examples":["The state does not collect enough revenue to cover its expenditure. 政府沒有徵到足夠的稅來支付它的費用。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>state</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you are referring to the condition they are in or what they are like at a particular time. 狀況; 狀態","examples":["For the first few months after Daniel died, I was in a state of clinical depression. 丹尼爾去世後的頭幾個月，我一直處在臨床抑鬱狀態。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>State</b> industries or organizations are financed and organized by the government rather than private companies. 政府的; 國家的","examples":["...reform of the state social-security system. …國家社會保障體制的改革。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>state</b> occasion is a formal one involving the head of a country. 國事的","examples":["The president of the Czech Republic is in Washington on a state visit. 捷克共和國總統正在華盛頓進行國事訪問。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>state</b> something, you say or write it in a formal or definite way. 說明; 寫明","examples":["Clearly state your address and telephone number. 清楚地寫明你的地址和電話號碼。","The police report stated that he was arrested for allegedly assaulting his wife. 警方報告稱，他因涉嫌毆打妻子而被捕。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is not in a fit state</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they are too upset or ill to do it. 不在 (做某事的) 適宜狀態","examples":["When you left our place, you weren't in a fit state to drive. 你離開我們家時，你的狀態不適合開車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in a state</b> or if you get <b>into a state</b>, you are very upset or nervous about something. 處於苦惱狀態; 處於焦慮狀態","examples":["I was in a terrible state because nobody could understand why I had this illness. 我極度不安，因為沒人能明白我為什麼得了這種病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the dead body of an important person <b>lies in state</b>, it is publicly displayed for a few days before it is buried. (要人的遺體) 供瞻仰","examples":["...the 30,000 people who filed past the cardinal's body while it lay in state last week. …上週紅衣主教的遺體供瞻仰時排隊瞻仰了的3萬民眾。"]}]}]},"stone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"石頭，石料；石塊；寶石；果核；結石；<英> 英石（英國重量單位,相當於6.35千克或14磅）；紀念碑，石碑；（指重量或缺少感情、表情或動作）像石頭一樣；（天文）隕石；CURLING STONE的簡稱；（桌遊中的）棋子，籌碼；排版用石臺，石印臺；（表示觀念或規則固定而不可改變）板上釘釘；石頭色，石青色"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……扔石頭；去核；用石頭建（或鋪）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"石的，石制的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地，全部地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stone</b> is a hard solid substance found in the ground and often used for building houses. 石頭","examples":["He could not tell whether the floor was wood or stone. 他分不清這地板是木頭的還是石頭的。","People often don't appreciate that marble is a natural stone. 人們往往不瞭解大理石是一種天然石頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stone</b> is a small piece of rock that is found on the ground. 石子","examples":["He removed a stone from his shoe. 他清除了鞋中的一粒石子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stone</b> is a large piece of stone put somewhere in memory of a person or event, or as a religious symbol. 石碑","examples":["The monument consists of a circle of gigantic stones. 該紀念碑由一圈巨大的石碑組成。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Stone</b> is used in expressions such as <b>set in stone</b> and <b>tablets of stone</b> to suggest that an idea or rule is firm and fixed, and cannot be changed. (思想或規則) 固定不變","examples":["He is merely throwing the idea forward for discussion, it is not cast in stone. 他只是丟擲個想法供討論，不是固定不變的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to a jewel as a <b>stone</b>. 寶石","examples":["...a diamond ring with three stones. …一枚有3顆寶石的鑽戒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>stone</b> is a small hard ball of minerals and other substances which sometimes forms in a person's kidneys or gallbladder. 結石","examples":["He had kidney stones. 他有腎結石。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>stone</b> in a plum, cherry, or other fruit is the large hard seed in the middle of it. 果核","examples":["...cherry stones. …櫻桃核。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>stone</b> someone or something, they throw stones at them. 向…扔石頭","examples":["Youths burned cars and stoned police. 年輕人燒車輛並向警察扔石頭。"]}]}]},"stay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"停留，逗留；保持原狀，維持；堅持；（到訪或作客時）留宿，暫住；不去，遠離某地；避開，不參與（麻煩或不利局面）；停止，延期，延緩；<文>控制，中止，抑制；<蘇格蘭>定居；暫時解除（飢餓）；用支索支撐（桅杆），用牽索固定；<文>支援，支撐"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"暫住，逗留；<法律>（審判的）推遲，延緩；（船桅的）支索，（杆子等的）牽索，撐條；（襯衫衣領的）撐條；<文>控制，中止，抑制；<史>胸衣，緊身褡，緊身背心；支撐物，穩固物；（飛機的）拉桿，拉索"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stay</b> where you are, you continue to be there and do not leave. 停留","examples":["\"Stay here,\" Trish said. \"I'll bring the car down the drive to take you back.\" “呆在這兒，”特里希說道，“我會把車開下來送你回去。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stay</b> in a town, or hotel, or at someone's house, you live there for a short time. (在某城市、酒店、某人家裡) 暫住; 逗留","examples":["Gordon stayed at The Park Hotel, Milan. 戈登住在了米蘭的帕克酒店。","Can't you stay a few more days? 你不能多住幾天嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stay</b> <b>away from</b> a place, you do not go there. 不去 (某地)","examples":["Management also stayed away from work during the strike. 管理人員在那次罷工期間也不去上班了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>stay out of</b> something, you do not get involved in it. 不參與","examples":["In the past, the UN has stayed out of the internal affairs of countries unless invited in. 在過去，除非受邀請介入，否則聯合國不參與各國的內部事務。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stay</b> is also a noun. 暫住; 逗留","examples":["An experienced Indian guide is provided during your stay. 在你逗留期間給你配備一位經驗豐富的印第安嚮導。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"anything that supports or steadies, such as a prop or buttress 支撐物; 穩固物","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>stays</b> in a particular state or situation, they continue to be in it. 保持 (某種狀態)","examples":["The Republican candidate said he would \"work like crazy to stay ahead.\" 該共和黨候選人說他將“拼命工作以保持領先地位。”","...community care networks that offer classes on how to stay healthy. …提供如何保持健康的課程的社群護理網路。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stay put</b>, you remain somewhere. 留在原地","examples":["He was forced by his condition to stay put and remain out of politics. 他受自身狀況所迫呆在原處，置身政治之外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stay the night</b> in a place, you sleep there for one night. 住一宿","examples":["They had invited me to come to supper and stay the night. 他們已經邀請我共進晚餐並住一宿。"]}]}]},"start":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始，著手；（使）發生；發動，啟動；創辦，開辦；出發，啟程；以……起步（或起家）；（由……）起，起始；突然一驚，嚇一跳；<非正式>開始抱怨，開始爭論；（比賽中）首發上場；（眼睛）突起，鼓出；使鬆動，使脫落；使（獵物）離巢"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"開始，開端；啟程，啟動；（事業的）最初機遇，起步機會；起點（the start）；比賽，上場；突然一驚；領先的時間（距離）；新工作，新企業，新手；先發上場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>start</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do something that you were not doing before and you continue doing it. 開始 (做某事)","examples":["John then unlocked the front door and I started to follow him up the stairs. 接著約翰開啟前門，我開始隨他上樓。","It was 1956 when Susanna started the work on the garden. 蘇珊娜是在1956年開始修建那個花園的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>starts</b>, or if someone <b>starts</b> it, it takes place from a particular time. 使開始發生; 開始發生","examples":["The fire is thought to have started in an upstairs room. 這火被認為是從樓上的一間房開始的。","All of the passengers started the day with a swim. 所有乘客都以游泳開始了這一天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>starts</b> something such as a new business, they create it or cause it to begin. 開辦","examples":["George Granger has started a health centre and I know he's looking for qualified staff. 喬治·格蘭傑開了個保健中心，我知道他正在物色合格的員工。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>start</b> an engine, car, or machine, or if it <b>starts</b>, it begins to work. 發動 (引擎、汽車、機器等); (引擎、汽車或機器等) 發動","examples":["He started the car, which hummed smoothly. 他發動了汽車，汽車平穩地發出嗡嗡聲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Start</b> is also a noun. 開始","examples":["After several starts, she read the report properly. 幾次起頭之後，她正確地讀了那份報告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Start</b> is also a noun. 開始","examples":["...1918, four years after the start of the Great War. …第一次世界大戰開始4年後的1918年。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Start</b> is also a noun. 驚動","examples":["Sylvia woke with a start. 希爾維婭驚醒了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>start by</b> doing something, or if you <b>start with</b> something, you do that thing first in a series of actions. (以做某事) 開始","examples":["I started by asking how many day-care centres were located in the United States. 我以詢問在美國有多少日託中心開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>start</b> to say what someone's first job was. For example, if their first job was that of a factory worker, you can say that they <b>started as</b> a factory worker. (以做…) 開始 (職業生涯)","examples":["Betty started as a shipping clerk at the clothes factory. 貝蒂以做這家服裝廠的運務員開始職業生涯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>start</b>, your body suddenly moves slightly as a result of surprise or fear. 驚動","examples":["She put the bottle on the coffee table beside him, banging it down hard. He started at the sound, his concentration broken. 她把那個瓶子砰地一聲放在他身邊的咖啡桌上，他被這聲音嚇了一跳，注意力被打斷了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Start off</b> means the same as . 開始","examples":["Mr. Dambar had started off as an assistant to Mrs. Spear's husband. 丹巴先生以做斯皮爾夫人的先生的助手開始職業生涯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Start up</b> means the same as . 開辦","examples":["The cost of starting up a day-care centre for children ranges from $150,000 to $300,000. 開辦一家兒童日託中心的費用在15到30萬美元之間不等。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Start up</b> means the same as . 發動","examples":["He waited until they went inside the building before starting up the car and driving off. 他等他們走進那座樓之後才發動汽車開走了。","Put the key in the ignition and turn it to start the car up. 把鑰匙插入點火裝置，然後轉動鑰匙發動汽車。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>for a start</b> or <b>to start with</b> to introduce the first of a number of things or reasons that you want to mention or could mention. 首先; 第一","examples":["You must get her name and address, and that can be a problem for a start. 你得弄到她的姓名和住址,而這可能就是第一個難題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>To start with</b> means at the very first stage of an event or process. (事情、過程) 剛開始時","examples":["To start with, the pressure on her was very heavy, but it's eased off a bit now. 剛開始時她的壓力非常大，但現在輕鬆些了。"]}]}]},"stand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"站，站立；起立，站起來；使直立，豎放；位於（某處或某位置）；高度為，高達；處於（某種狀態）；停，停靠；擱，不流動；很可能會；持有（某種態度或看法）；達特定水平（或數量、高度等）；保持有效，維持不變；忍受，容忍；經得起，經受；請（某人吃飯、喝酒）；競選，當候選人；屹立，矗立；走，邁（一小步）；具有……地位，排在第……位；（不小心）踩到；承擔……職責；擔任（板球賽）裁判員"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"架，座，臺；立場，見解；貨攤，售貨亭；反抗，抵抗；看臺；攤位，展臺；證人席；堅守時間，總計得分；停車處，站；林分；<南非>地塊；舞臺，講臺，演奏臺；通常站立（或坐）的位置；停止，停住；<罕>一群獵鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>are standing</b>, your body is upright, your legs are straight, and your weight is supported by your feet. 站立","examples":["She was standing beside my bed staring down at me. 她當時站在我床邊低頭凝視著我。","They told me to stand still and not to turn round. 他們叫我站著不動並且不要轉身。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone who is sitting <b>stands</b>, they change their position so that they are upright and on their feet. 站起來","examples":["Becker stood and shook hands with Ben. 貝克爾站起來和本握了手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stand</b> <b>aside</b> or <b>stand</b> <b>back</b>, you move a short distance sideways or backward, so that you are standing in a different place. 往旁邊站; 往後站","examples":["I stood aside to let her pass me. 我往邊上站以讓她從我身邊過去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as a building or a piece of furniture <b>stands</b> somewhere, it is in that position, and is upright. (建築物、傢俱等) 豎立著","examples":["The house stands alone on top of a small hill. 那所房子孤零零地立在一座小山頂上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that a building <b>is standing</b> when it remains after other buildings around it have fallen down or been destroyed. (在周圍建築物都已倒下或被摧毀的情況下依然) 矗立著","examples":["The palace, which was damaged by bombs in World War II, still stood. 這座在二戰中被炮火破壞的宮殿依然矗立著。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you leave food or a mixture of something <b>to</b> <b>stand</b>, you leave it without disturbing it for some time. 擱置一段時間","examples":["The salad improves if made in advance and left to stand. 該色拉如果提前做好並擱上些時候味道會更好。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you ask someone <b>where</b> or <b>how</b> they <b>stand</b> <b>on</b> a particular issue, you are asking them what their attitude or view is. 持 (何種) 態度; 採取 (何種) 立場","examples":["The amendment will force senators to show where they stand on the issue of sexual harassment. 該修正案將迫使參議員們表明他們在性騷擾問題上採取什麼立場。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you do not know <b>where</b> you <b>stand</b> <b>with</b> someone, you do not know exactly what their attitude to you is. (在某人心中) 處於 (何種) 位置; 被 (如何) 看待","examples":["No one knows where they stand with him; he is utterly unpredictable. 誰也不知道他們在他心中被如何看待，他這個人絕對難以琢磨。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If a decision, law, or offer <b>stands</b>, it still exists and has not been changed or cancelled. (決定、法律或提議) 繼續有效","examples":["Although exceptions could be made, the rule still stands. 儘管有可能有特例，但這條規則繼續有效。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something that can be measured <b>stands at</b> a particular level, it is at that level. 處於 (某水平)","examples":["The inflation rate now stands at 3.6 percent. 通貨膨脹率現在是3.6％。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>stand</b> <b>in</b> an election, you are a candidate in it. 參加 (競選)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stand up</b> means the same as . 站立","examples":["We waited, standing up, for an hour. 我們站著等了一個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Stand up</b> means the same as . 站起來","examples":["When I walked in, they all stood up and started clapping. 我走進去的時候，他們全體起立開始鼓掌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stand</b> something somewhere, you put it there in an upright position. 使豎立","examples":["Stand the plant in the open in a sunny, sheltered place. 把這株植物立在戶外陽光充足、有遮護的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something can <b>stand</b> a situation or a test, it is good enough or strong enough to experience it without being damaged, harmed, or shown to be inadequate. 經受住","examples":["These are the first machines that can stand the wear and tear of continuously crushing glass. 這些是第一批能經得住連續碾碎玻璃造成的磨損的機器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you cannot <b>stand</b> something, you cannot bear it or tolerate it. 忍受; 容忍 (某事物)","examples":["I can't stand any more. I'm going to run away. 我再也忍受不了了，我打算逃跑。","Stoddart can stand any amount of personal criticism. 斯托達特能容忍針對其個人的無論多少的批評。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you cannot <b>stand</b> someone or something, you dislike them very strongly. 忍受 (某人或某事物)","examples":["I can't stand that man and his arrogance. 我受不了那人和他的傲慢態度。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>stand to gain</b> something, you are likely to gain it. If you <b>stand to lose</b> something, you are likely to lose it. 有可能 (獲得、失去)","examples":["The management group would stand to gain millions of dollars if the company were sold. 如果公司被出售的話，管理層有可能獲得數百萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>stand</b> instead of \"be\" when you are describing the present state or condition of something or someone. 處於 (某種狀態或狀況)","examples":["The alliance stands ready to do what is necessary. 該聯盟已準備好採取必要行動。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>it</b> <b>stands to reason</b> <b>that</b> something is true or likely to happen, you mean that it is obvious. 顯然","examples":["It stands to reason that if you are considerate and friendly to people you will get a lot more back. 顯然，如果你通情達理、對人友善，你會得到比你付出的多得多的回報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stand in the way of</b> something or <b>stand in</b> a person's <b>way</b>, you prevent that thing from happening or prevent that person from doing something. 阻止某事物/某人","examples":["The administration would not stand in the way of such a proposal. 該行政部門不會阻止這樣一個提議。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you take or make a <b>stand</b>, you do something or say something in order to make it clear what your attitude to a particular thing is. 立場","examples":["He felt the need to make a stand against racism in South Africa. 他覺得有必要表明反對南非種族主義的立場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stand</b> is a small shop or stall, outdoors or in a large public building. 攤位","examples":["He ran a newspaper stand outside the American Express office. 他曾在美國運通辦公樓外經營一個報攤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>stands</b> at a sports stadium or arena are a large structure where people sit or stand to watch what is happening. (運動場或競技場的) 看臺","examples":["The people in the stands at Candlestick Park are standing and cheering with all their might. 燭臺公園看臺上的人們正站著盡情歡呼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In British English, <b>stand</b> is used with the same meaning. 看臺","examples":["I was sitting in the stand for the first game. 我當時正坐在看臺上觀看首場比賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>stand</b> is an object or piece of furniture that is designed for supporting or holding a particular kind of thing. 托架","examples":["The teapot came with a stand to catch the drips. 那把茶壺配有一個接滴水的壺託。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>stand</b> is an area where taxis or buses can wait to pick up passengers. (計程車或公共汽車) 候客處","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In a law court, <b>the stand</b> is the place where a witness sits to answer questions. (法庭上的) 證人席","examples":["When the father took the stand today, he contradicted his son's testimony. 今天那位父親出席作證時，他駁斥了他兒子的證詞。"]}]}]},"store":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商店；倉庫，儲存處；（事物的）儲存，儲備；大量，豐富；儲存的物品（stores）；軍需品，補給品（stores）；<英>（計算機的）儲存器；重視，注重；待育肥的小羊（或小公牛、小母牛、小豬）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"貯存，儲藏；（在頭腦或計算機中）儲存（事實或資訊）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>store</b> is a building or part of a building where things are sold. 商店","examples":["They are selling them for $10 apiece at a few stores in Texas and Oklahoma. 得克薩斯和俄克拉何馬的一些商店正以每個$10的價錢出售它們。","...grocery stores. …雜貨店。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>store</b> <b>of</b> things is a supply of them that you keep somewhere until you need them. 儲存","examples":["I handed over my secret store of chocolate. 我交出了我偷偷藏起來的巧克力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>store</b> is a place where things are kept while they are not being used. 儲存處","examples":["...a store for spent fuel from submarines. …一個潛艇廢燃料的儲存處。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>store</b> things, you put them in a container or other place and leave them there until they are needed. 存放","examples":["Store the cookies in an airtight tin. 把曲奇餅乾存放在一個密封罐中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>store</b> information, you keep it in your memory, in a file, or in a computer. 儲存 (資訊)","examples":["Where in the brain do we store information about colours? 我們在大腦的哪個地方儲存有關顏色的資訊？"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Store away</b> means the same as . 存放","examples":["He simply stored the tapes away. 他只是把那些磁帶存放起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in store</b> <b>for</b> you, it is going to happen at some time in the future. 即將發生","examples":["Surprises were also in store for me. 令人吃驚的事也將發生在我身上。"]}]}]},"street":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"街道，街；馬路，車行道；街頭，戶外（公共場合）；（用於街道名稱或地址）…街，…大街"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>street</b> is a road in a city, town, or village, usually with houses along it. 街道","examples":["He lived at 66 Bingfield Street. 他住在賓菲爾德街66號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>street</b> or <b>streets</b> when talking about activities that happen out of doors in a city or town rather than inside a building. 街頭","examples":["Changing money on the street is illegal – always use a bank. 在街頭兌換貨幣是非法的–始終要去銀行。","Their aim is to raise a million dollars to get the homeless off the streets. 他們的目的是募集100萬美元以使無家可歸者不再流浪街頭。"]}]}]},"step":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邁步，腳步；臺階，梯級；措施，手段；階段，程序；一步（的距離）；舞步；步態，步姿；<英>摺梯，梯子；踏板操；健身踏板；<美>音級，度；腳步聲；等級，級別；桅座；（量值，尤指電壓的）突然改變落差；（在傾斜的冰上鑿出的）踏腳處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跨步，邁步；踏，踩；做，採取行動；（短距離）移動；豎立（桅杆）於桅座上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you take a <b>step</b>, you lift your foot and put it down in a different place, for example when you are walking. 腳步","examples":["I took a step toward him. 我朝他邁出了一步。","She walked on a few steps. 她繼續走了幾步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Steps</b> are a series of surfaces at increasing or decreasing heights, on which you put your feet in order to walk up or down to a different level. 臺階","examples":["This little room was along a passage and down some steps. 這小房間在沿著一個過道再走下幾級臺階的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>step</b> is a raised flat surface in front of a door. 門檻","examples":["A little girl was sitting on the step of the end house. 有個小女孩坐在最後面那棟房子的門檻上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>step</b> is one of a series of actions that you take in order to achieve something. 步驟","examples":["He greeted the agreement as the first step toward peace. 他贊稱這項協議是邁向和平的第一步。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>step</b> in a process is one of a series of stages. 階段","examples":["The next step is to put the theory into practice. 下一階段要把理論付諸實踐。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>steps</b> of a dance are the sequences of foot movements which make it up. 舞步","examples":["She was a better dancer than Gordon. At least she knew the steps. 她舞跳得比戈登好，至少她會那些舞步。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone's <b>step</b> is the way they walk. 步伐","examples":["He quickened his step. 他加快了步伐。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>step</b> <b>on</b> something or <b>step</b> in a particular direction, you put your foot on the thing or move your foot in that direction. 踩","examples":["This was the moment when Neil Armstrong became the first man to step on the Moon. 正是在這一刻，內爾·阿姆斯特朗成為了登月第一人。","She accidentally stepped on his foot on a crowded commuter train. 她在一輛擁擠的通勤火車上不小心踩到他的腳。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you stay <b>one step ahead of</b> someone or something, you manage to achieve more than they do or avoid competition or danger from them. 領先一步; 避開","examples":["Successful travel is partly a matter of keeping one step ahead of the crowd. 成功的旅遊在某種程度上就是避開眾人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people who are walking or dancing are <b>in step</b>, they are moving their feet forward at exactly the same time as each other. If they are <b>out of step</b>, their feet are moving forward at different times. 步伐 (不) 一致","examples":["They were almost the same height and they moved perfectly in step. 他們身高相仿，而且走路的步伐也完全一致。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people are <b>in step</b> <b>with</b> each other, their ideas or opinions are the same. If they are <b>out of step</b> <b>with</b> each other, their ideas or opinions are different. 意見 (不) 一致","examples":["Moscow is anxious to stay in step with Washington. 莫斯科迫切希望與華盛頓保持一致。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>step by step</b>, you do it by progressing gradually from one stage to the next. 一步一步地","examples":["I am not rushing things and I'm taking it step by step. 我沒急於求成，我正在一步一步地來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone tells you to <b>watch</b> your <b>step</b>, they are warning you to be careful about how you behave or what you say so that you do not get into trouble. 謹慎行事","examples":["He said I'd come to a bad end, if I didn't watch my step. 他說如果我不謹慎行事，我的結局會很慘的。"]}]}]},"story":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（真實或虛構的）故事，敘述；新聞報道；（尤指口頭的）敘述，描述；謊言，虛假的藉口；（書籍、電影、戲劇等的）情節；紀事，史話；樓層；情況；（公司的）商業前景，商業現狀；謠言，傳聞；一種測量單位（1 story 等於 3.3 米）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用歷史故事畫裝飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>story</b> is a description of imaginary people and events, which is written or told in order to entertain. (虛構的) 故事","examples":["The second story in the book is titled \"The Scholar.\" 這本書中的第2個故事標題為《學者》。","I shall tell you a story about four little rabbits. 我將給你講個關於4只小兔子的故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>story</b> is a description of an event or something that happened to someone, especially a spoken description of it. (尤指口頭的) 敘述","examples":["The parents all shared interesting stories about their children. 那些家長們都會互相講起有關自己孩子的趣事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>story</b> <b>of</b> something is a description of all the important things that have happened to it since it began. 史話","examples":["...the story of the women's movement. …婦女運動的史話。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone invents a <b>story</b>, they give a false explanation or account of something. 謊話","examples":["He invented some story about a cousin. 他們編造了一些關於一位表親的謊話。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A news <b>story</b> is a piece of news in a newspaper or in a news broadcast. 新聞報道","examples":["Those are some of the top stories in the news. 那些都是一些頭條新聞報道。","They'll do anything for a story. 他們會為了新聞報道不擇手段。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>a different story</b> to refer to a situation, usually a bad one, which exists in one set of circumstances when you have mentioned that it does not exist in another set of circumstances. 情況不同","examples":["Where Marcella lives, the rents are fairly cheap, but a little further north it's a different story. 在馬斯拉住的地方房租相當便宜，但再往北一點兒情況就不同了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say <b>it's the same old story</b> or <b>it's the old story</b>, you mean that something unpleasant or undesirable seems to happen again and again. 老一套","examples":["It's the same old story. They want one person to do three people's jobs. 又是老一套。他們想讓一個人幹3個人的活兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>only part of the story</b> or is <b>not the whole story</b>, you mean that the explanation or information given is not enough for a situation to be fully understood. 只是部分情況; 並非全部情況","examples":["This may be true but it is only part of the story. 這也許是真的，但它只是部分情況。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone tells you their <b>side of the story</b>, they tell you why they behaved in a particular way and why they think they were right, when other people think that person behaved wrongly. 某人一方的說法","examples":["He had already made up his mind before even hearing her side of the story. 他甚至在聽到她那一方的說法之前就已下定決心了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to decorate (a pot, wall, etc) with scenes from history or legends 用歷史故事畫裝飾(罐、牆等)","examples":[]}]}]},"stop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）停止，結束；（使）中斷；（機器等）停止運轉；（汽車或火車）停靠；暫時中斷（以便做某事）；防止，阻攔；堵塞；短暫停留；停付，扣除；處於，表現"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"停止，終止；車站；<美>停車路口；（旅行中的）逗留，停留；塞音；（風琴的）音栓；（管風琴的）音管；（讓銀行）止付；救球；句號；光圈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have been doing something and then you <b>stop</b> doing it, you no longer do it. 停止","examples":["Stop throwing those stones! 別再扔那些石頭了！","Does either of the parties want to stop the fighting? 雙方中有誰想停止戰鬥呢？","She stopped in mid-sentence. 她說了半句就停下了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stop</b> something from happening, or you <b>stop</b> something happening, you prevent it from happening or prevent it from continuing. 阻止","examples":["He proposed a new diplomatic initiative to try to stop the war. 他提出了一個新的試圖阻止戰爭的外交倡議。","He would do what he must to stop her from destroying him. 他將做該做的事來阻止她把他毀了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as machine <b>stops</b> or <b>is stopped</b>, it is no longer moving or working. 停止 (轉動或工作)","examples":["The clock stopped at 11:59 Saturday night. 鍾在星期六晚11點59分停了。","Arnold stopped the engine and got out of the car. 阿諾德關閉發動機然後下了車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a moving person or vehicle <b>stops</b> or <b>is stopped</b>, they no longer move and they remain in the same place. 停下","examples":["The car failed to stop at an army checkpoint. 那輛車未能在一個軍隊檢查站停下。","He stopped and let her catch up with him. 他停下了，讓她趕上自己。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone does not <b>stop</b> <b>to</b> think or <b>to</b> explain, they continue with what they are doing without taking any time to think about or explain it. 停下來 (思考或解釋)","examples":["She doesn't stop to think about what she's saying. 她沒有停下來想想自己在說些什麼。","There is something rather strange about all this if one stops to consider it. 如果停下來考慮一下，就會發覺這一切相當蹊蹺。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an activity or process <b>stops</b>, it is no longer happening. 停下","examples":["The rain had stopped and a star or two was visible over the mountains. 雨停了，山上的天空可見一兩顆星星。","The system overheated and filming had to stop. 系統過熱，拍攝工作不得不停下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a quality or state <b>stops</b> somewhere, you mean that it exists or is true up to that point, but no further. 結束","examples":["The cafe owner has put up the required \"no smoking\" signs, but thinks his responsibility stops there. 咖啡店老闆已貼上所要求的“禁止吸菸”的標誌，但他認為自己的責任到此為止。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stop</b> somewhere on a journey, you stay there for a short while. 停留一下","examples":["He insisted we stop at a small restaurant just outside of Atlanta. 他堅持要我們在亞特蘭大外的一家小餐館停留一下。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something that is moving comes <b>to a stop</b> or is brought <b>to a stop</b>, it slows down and no longer moves. 停下","examples":["People often wrongly open doors before the train has come to a stop. 人們常常在火車停下之前錯誤地開啟車門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stop</b> is a place where buses or trains regularly stop so that people can get on and off. 車站","examples":["The closest subway stop is Houston Street. 最近的地鐵站是休斯敦街。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stop</b> is a time or place at which you stop during a journey. 停留時間; 停留地","examples":["The last stop in Mr. Robinson's lengthy tour was Paris. 魯濱遜先生漫長旅程的最後一站是巴黎。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone will <b>stop at nothing</b> <b>to</b> get something, you are emphasizing that they are willing to do things that are extreme, wrong, or dangerous in order to get it. 不顧一切","examples":["Their motive is money, and they will stop at nothing to get it. 他們的動機是錢，因此他們將不顧一切地撈錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put a stop to</b> something that you do not like or approve of, you prevent it from happening or continuing. 制止某事","examples":["His daughter should have stood up and put a stop to all these rumours. 他的女兒本應站出來制止所有這些謠言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone does not <b>know when to stop</b>, you mean that they do not control their own behaviour very well and so they often annoy or upset other people. 知道如何把握分寸","examples":["Like many politicians before him, Mr. Bentley did not know when to stop. 如他之前的許多政客一樣，本特利先生不知道如何把握分寸。"]}]}]},"sugar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"食糖；一匙糖，一塊方糖；（植物、水果等所含的）糖；親愛的；<非正式>麻醉藥，毒品（尤指海洛因或二乙基麥角醯胺）；甜言蜜語"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加糖；美化（討厭的事物）；（透過熬楓樹汁）提取楓蜜（或楓糖）；（昆）在樹幹上塗撒糖、糖漿、啤酒等的混合物作蛾餌"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（代替 shit，用於表示懊惱）糟糕，哎呀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sugar</b> is a sweet substance that is used to make food and drinks sweet. It is usually in the form of small white or brown crystals. 食用糖","examples":["...bags of sugar. …袋袋食用糖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has one <b>sugar</b> in their tea or coffee, they have one small spoon of sugar or one sugar lump in it. 一匙糖; 一塊糖","examples":["How many sugars do you take? 你用多少塊糖？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sugars</b> are substances that occur naturally in food. When you eat them, the body converts them into energy. 糖","examples":["Plants produce sugars and starch to provide themselves with energy. 植物製造糖和澱粉來為自身提供能量。"]}]}]},"student":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學生；學者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>student</b> is a person who is studying at an elementary school, secondary school, college, or university. 學生","examples":["Warren's eldest son is an art student. 沃倫的長子是一名學藝術的學生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>student of</b> a particular subject is interested in the subject and spends time learning about it. 學者","examples":["...a passionate student of history and an expert on nineteenth century prime ministers. …一位熱衷歷史的學者和一個研究19世紀首相們的專家。"]}]}]},"sunday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期日；禮拜日"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sunday</b> is the day after Saturday and before Monday. 星期日","examples":["I thought we might go for a drive on Sunday. 我原以為我們可能星期日去開車兜風。"]}]}]},"supper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"晚餐（尤指在家吃的非正式晚餐）；夜宵，宵夜；<美>（尤指為慈善事業籌款舉辦的）晚餐會；<蘇格蘭>一種薯片伴特定事物的餐食"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……供餐；吃晚飯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people refer to the main meal eaten in the early part of the evening as <b>supper</b>. 晚餐","examples":["Some guests like to dress for supper. 有些客人喜歡穿禮服出席晚餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Supper</b> is a simple meal eaten just before you go to bed at night. 夜宵","examples":["She gives the children their supper, then puts them to bed. 她給孩子們吃了夜宵，然後讓他們上床睡覺。"]}]}]},"summer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夏天，夏季；<文>年，歲；（建築）大梁；（天文）從夏至到秋分這段時期；全盛期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在某地）避暑，過夏；夏天放牧（牛）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Summer</b> is the season between spring and fall. In the summer the weather is usually warm or hot. 夏季","examples":["I escaped the heatwave in Washington earlier this summer and flew to Maine. 我今年初夏躲避了華盛頓的熱浪，飛到了緬因州。","It was a perfect summer's day. 那是個完美的夏日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a large horizontal beam or girder, esp one that supports floor joists (建築)大梁 (Also called summer tree)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to spend the summer (at a place) (在某地)避暑","examples":[]}]}]},"study":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（專題）研究，調查；（尤指透過書本的）學習，攻讀；用於某些學科名稱（studies）；功課，課業，學業（studies）；學術專著，專題論文；<美>學習者；學習物件，研究物件；（繪畫的）試畫， 習作；書房，書齋；細緻考慮，仔細檢查，審視； 特別的事物（或人）；以特定速度背臺詞的演員（舞臺俚語）；描寫，描繪；練習曲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"學習，攻讀；認真閱讀，仔細看；研究，調查；<西印度>仔細考慮，慎重思考；（演員）記住（或背下）（臺詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>study</b>, you spend time learning about a particular subject or subjects. 學習","examples":["...a relaxed and happy atmosphere that will allow you to study to your full potential. …一個將使你學習到充分發揮潛能的輕鬆又愉快的氛圍。","He studied History and Economics. 他學過歷史和經濟學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>study</b> something, you look at it or watch it very carefully, in order to find something out. 端詳","examples":["Debbie studied her friend's face for a moment. 黛比端詳了一會兒她朋友的臉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>study</b> something, you consider it or observe it carefully in order to be able to understand it fully. 研究; 仔細觀察","examples":["I know that you've been studying chimpanzees for thirty years now. 我知道你研究黑猩猩至今已有30年了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Study</b> is the activity of studying. 學習","examples":["...the use of maps and visual evidence in the study of local history. …在當地歷史的學習中地圖和影象證據的使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>study</b> of a subject is a piece of research on it. 研究","examples":["Recent studies suggest that as many as 5 in 1,000 new mothers are likely to have this problem. 最近的研究表明，1000個新媽媽中有多達5個可能有這個問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to educational subjects or courses that contain several elements as <b>studies</b> of a particular kind. 學科","examples":["...a centre for Islamic studies. …一個伊斯蘭教學科中心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>study</b> is a room in a house which is used for reading, writing, and studying. 書房","examples":["That evening we sat together in his study. 那天晚上我們一起坐在他的書房裡。"]}]}]},"swim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"游泳；橫渡；遊（某一泳姿）；（魚、禽等）遊過，遊動；浸，泡；漂浮；使漂浮，使渡過；（物體）彷彿旋轉；眩暈"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"游泳；（河流中）適合釣魚的靜止深水處，深潭；漂浮；眩暈"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"游泳時穿戴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>swim</b>, you move through water by making movements with your arms and legs. 游泳","examples":["She learned to swim when she was really tiny. 她很小就學會了游泳。","He was rescued only when an exhausted friend swam ashore. 當一個精疲力盡的朋友游上岸時，他才得救。","I swim a mile a day. 我每天遊一英里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>swim</b> a race, you take part in a swimming race. 參加游泳比賽","examples":["She swam the 400 metres medley. 她參加了400米混合泳比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>swim</b> a stretch of water, you keep swimming until you have crossed it. 遊過 (一段水域)","examples":["By the time we reached the other side, Maram vowed that he would never swim a river again. 我們到河對岸時，馬拉姆發誓說他再也不游泳渡河了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Swim</b> is also a noun. 游泳","examples":["When can we go for a swim? 我們什麼時候可以去游泳？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a fish <b>swims</b>, it moves through water by moving its body. (魚) 游水","examples":["The barriers are lethal to fish trying to swim upstream. 這些障礙物對於逆流而上的魚來說是致命的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your head <b>is swimming</b>, you feel unsteady and slightly ill. 頭暈","examples":["The musty aroma of incense made her head swim. 薰香的黴味令她頭暈。"]}]}]},"tale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"故事，傳說；（對真人真事精彩的或誇張的）描述，講述；謊言；流言蜚語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tale</b> is a story, often involving magic or exciting events. 故事 (常包含神奇的或令人激動的事件)","examples":["...a collection of stories, poems and folk tales. …一部由故事、詩歌和民間傳說構成的作品集。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an interesting, exciting, or dramatic account of a real event as a <b>tale</b>. (對真實事件的有趣的、令人激動的、戲劇性的) 描述","examples":["The media have been filled with tales of horror and loss resulting from Monday's earthquake. 媒體上已充斥著對星期一地震造成的恐怖和損失的種種描述。"]}]}]},"sweet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"含糖的，甜的；<美> 未加鹽的，淡的；芳香的，芬芳的；清新的，純淨的，新鮮的；（聲音）甜美的，悅耳的，動聽的；<美>（音樂，尤指爵士樂）甜派風格的；惹人喜愛的，可愛的；親愛的；溫和的，和藹的，善良的；愉快的，愜意的，令人滿意的；<非正式> （用於表示同意，贊成）好的；容易操縱的，運轉平穩的；絲毫的，一丁點兒的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>糖果；甜食；<英>餐後甜點；<舊>（親暱的稱呼）寶貝兒，親愛的；快樂，樂趣（sweets）；芳香"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sweet</b> food and drink contains a lot of sugar. 甜的","examples":["...a mug of sweet tea. …一杯甜茶。","If the sauce seems too sweet, add a dash of red wine vinegar. 如果醬太甜，就加少許紅酒醋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sweet</b> smell is a pleasant one, for example the smell of a flower. 芳香的","examples":["...the sweet smell of her shampoo. …她的洗髮水芳香的味道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sweet</b> sound is pleasant, smooth, and gentle. 悅耳的","examples":["Her voice was as soft and sweet as a young girl's. 她的聲音和小女孩的一樣溫柔悅耳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>sweet</b>, you mean that it gives you great pleasure and satisfaction. 令人痛快的","examples":["There are few things quite as sweet as revenge. 幾乎沒有什麼事情像復仇一樣讓人痛快。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>sweet</b>, you mean that they are pleasant, kind, and gentle toward other people. 溫柔的","examples":["He was a sweet man but when he drank he tended to quarrel. 他是個溫柔的男人，但一喝酒他就愛吵架。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you describe a small person or thing as <b>sweet</b>, you mean that they are attractive in a simple or unsophisticated way. (小孩或小東西) 可愛的","examples":["...a sweet little baby girl. …一個可愛的小女嬰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"甜味","examples":["Florida oranges have a natural sweetness. 佛羅里達柑桔有一種天然的甜味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sweets</b> are foods that have a lot of sugar. 甜食","examples":["To maintain her weight, she simply chooses fruits and vegetables over fats and sweets. 為了保持自己的體重，她選擇只吃水果和蔬菜而不吃肥肉和甜食。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sweets</b> are small sweet things such as chocolates and mints. 糖果","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>sweet</b> is the same as a . 餐後甜點","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悅耳地","examples":["He sang much more sweetly than he has before. 他唱歌比以前悅耳多了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"溫柔地","examples":["I just smiled sweetly and said no. 我只是溫和地笑了笑，說了聲“不”。"]}]}]},"surprise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不尋常的事件，意外之事；驚奇，驚訝；令某人意外驚喜的事物（如禮物、旅行等）；出其不意（出人意料）的方法；讓人大吃一驚的人；（鳴鐘術）一種複雜的敲奏編鐘的方法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（某人）吃驚；意外發現，當場抓獲，突然襲擊；給……驚喜，使喜出望外"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"感到驚奇吧！"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人驚奇的，意外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>surprise</b> is an unexpected event, fact, or piece of news. 意外 (資訊或事件等)","examples":["I have a surprise for you: We are moving to Switzerland! 我要告訴你一件意想不到的事：我們要搬到瑞士去！","It may come as a surprise to some that a normal, healthy child is born with many skills. 一個正常健康的孩子天生具有很多技藝，這對某些人來說可能是個意外資訊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Surprise</b> is the feeling that you have when something unexpected happens. 驚訝","examples":["The Pentagon has expressed surprise at these allegations. 五角大樓對這些指控表示了驚訝。","\"You mean he's going to vote against her?\" Scobie asked in surprise. “你的意思是他將投票反對她？”斯考比驚訝地問道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as a <b>surprise</b>, you mean that they are very good or pleasant although you were not expecting this. 驚喜","examples":["...Senga MacFie, one of the surprises of the World Championships three months ago. …森加·麥克菲，3個月前世界錦標賽中的驚喜之一。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Surprise</b> is also an adjective. 意外的","examples":["Baxter arrived here this afternoon, on a surprise visit. 巴克斯特今天下午突然到了這裡，做意外造訪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>surprises</b> you, it gives you a feeling of surprise. 使吃驚","examples":["We'll solve the case ourselves and surprise everyone. 我們將自己解決這件事，並讓所有人吃驚。","It surprised me that a driver of Alain's experience should make those mistakes. 令我吃驚的是，像阿萊恩這樣有經驗的一位司機竟然會犯那些錯誤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>surprise</b> someone, you give them, tell them, or do something pleasant that they are not expecting. 使驚喜","examples":["Surprise a new neighbour with one of your favourite home-made dishes. 做一道你自己拿手的家常菜，給你的新鄰居一個驚喜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>surprise</b> someone, you attack, capture, or find them when they are not expecting it. 出其不意地抓獲 (襲擊、找到)","examples":["U.S. troops surprised eight enemy fighters in a cave complex. 美國軍隊在一個洞穴群裡出其不意地抓獲了8名敵軍士兵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>takes</b> you <b>by surprise</b>, it happens when you are not expecting it or when you are not prepared for it. 使某人吃驚","examples":["His question took his two companions by surprise. 他的提問讓他的兩位同伴吃了一驚。"]}]}]},"sun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"太陽（the sun）；日光，陽光；恆星；<文>成功，榮耀；<文>一天，一年；<文>被視為榮譽（或靈感、理解）源泉的人（或物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"曬太陽，（尤指）日光浴"}],"sections":[]},"taxi":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計程車，計程車，計程車；（南非的）小型不定時公交車；出租汽船（或其他交通工具）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（飛機）緩慢滑行；（飛行員）駕駛（飛機）緩慢滑行；乘計程車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>taxi</b> is a car driven by a person whose job is to take people where they want to go in return for money. 計程車","examples":["The taxi drew up in front of the Riviera Club. 該計程車在裡維埃拉俱樂部前停了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an aircraft <b>taxis</b> along the ground or when a pilot <b>taxis</b> a plane somewhere, it moves slowly along the ground. 使 (飛機) 緩慢滑行; (飛機) 緩慢滑行","examples":["She gave permission to the plane to taxi into position and hold for takeoff. 她允許飛機滑行入位並準備起飛。"]}]}]},"table":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桌子，臺子；一桌人；一桌酒席，飯菜；整理餐桌；表，一覽表；排名榜，積分表；乘法表；（橋牌）明手，明家；（建築）簷板；木匾，石碑；（寶石的）切平面；有雙切平面的寶石；棋盤；水平模製（尤指簷口）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英> 正式提交討論；<美> 擱置，暫緩審議；用寬貼邊加固（帆）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>table</b> is a piece of furniture with a flat top that you put things on or sit at. 桌子","examples":["She was sitting at the kitchen table eating a peach. 她正坐在餐桌旁吃著桃子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>table</b> is a written set of facts and figures arranged in columns and rows. 表格","examples":["Consult the table on page 104. 查閱104頁的表格。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>tables</b> a proposal or plan which has been put forward, they decide to discuss it or deal with it at a later date, rather than right away. 擱置 (提議或計劃)","examples":["We will table that for later. 我們將把那件事留到以後再討論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>tables</b> a proposal, they say formally that they want it to be discussed at a meeting. 正式提交 (議案)","examples":["They've tabled a motion criticizing the government for doing nothing about the problem. 他們已經正式提交了批評政府對該問題不作為的動議。"]}]}]},"taxicab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計程車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>taxicab</b> is the same as a . 同taxi","examples":[]}]}]},"tail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動物的）尾巴；（一些蝴蝶的）狹翅須；（物體的）尾狀物，尾部；（離去事物的）末尾部分；<非正式>盯梢人，跟蹤者；（男子）燕尾服（tails）；硬幣的反面（tails）；（水池的）淺水端，（河流的）下游；（屋瓦的）疊餘外露部分；（板球）最弱的擊球手；（數）截尾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跟蹤，盯梢；（飛行物體）曲線移動； 拉緊（絞索）；除去（水果或蔬菜的）梗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tail</b> of an animal, bird, or fish is the part extending beyond the end of its body. 尾巴","examples":["...a black dog with a long tail. …一隻長尾巴的黑狗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>tail</b> to refer to the end or back of something, especially something long and thin. (尤指細長物體的) 尾部","examples":["...the horizontal stabilizer bar on the plane's tail. …飛機尾部的水平穩定杆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a man is wearing <b>tails</b>, he is wearing a formal jacket which has two long pieces hanging down at the back. 燕尾服","examples":["...men in tails and women in party dresses. …穿燕尾服的男士和穿宴會禮服的女士。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>tail</b> someone means to follow close behind them and watch where they go and what they do. 跟蹤","examples":["Officers had tailed the gang during a major undercover operation. 警方在一次重大的秘密行動中跟蹤過這個團伙。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you toss a coin and it comes down <b>tails</b>, you can see the side of it that does not have a picture of a head on it. (硬幣) 反面朝上地","examples":["\"Heads or tails?\" “正面還是反面？”","The captain called heads as usual — and the coin came down tails. 隊長像以往一樣叫了正面—可硬幣反面朝上地落了下來。"]}]}]},"taste":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"味道，滋味；味覺；愛好，興趣；（個人）喜歡的事物（tastes）；鑑賞力，品味；體驗，嘗試；（某段經歷造成的）感覺，感受；（用來品嚐的）一點兒，少量，一口；（用於短語，表示某人的言行舉止等）得當，不得當"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"嚐起來；嚐出……的味道；嘗，品嚐；（短暫地）體驗，領略，經歷；意識到，感覺到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Taste</b> is one of the five senses that people have. When you have food or drink in your mouth, your sense of taste makes it possible for you to recognize what it is. 味覺","examples":["...a keen sense of taste. …靈敏的味覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>taste</b> of something is the individual quality that it has when you put it in your mouth and that distinguishes it from other things. For example, something may have a sweet, bitter, sour, or salty taste. 味道","examples":["I like the taste of wine and enjoy trying different kinds. 我喜歡葡萄酒的味道，喜歡品嚐不同種類的葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>taste</b> of some food or drink, you try a small amount of it in order to see what the flavour is like. 嘗","examples":["Yves sometimes gives customers a taste of a wine before they order. 伊維斯有時候會在顧客們點酒前讓他們先嚐一下。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>taste of</b> a particular way of life or activity, you have a brief experience of it. (短暫的) 體驗","examples":["This voyage was his first taste of freedom. 這次航行使他第一次體驗到自由的滋味。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have a <b>taste for</b> something, you have a liking or preference for it. 喜好","examples":["That gave me a taste for reading. 那使我有了讀書的喜好。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A person's <b>taste</b> is their choice <b>in</b> the things that they like or buy, for example, their clothes, possessions, or music. If you say that someone has good <b>taste</b>, you mean that you approve of their choices. If you say that they have bad <b>taste</b>, you disapprove of their choices. 品味","examples":["His taste in clothes is extremely good. 他在服裝上品味極好。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If food or drink <b>tastes</b> <b>of</b> something, it has that particular flavour, which you notice when you eat or drink it. 有…味道","examples":["I drank a cup of tea that tasted of diesel. 我喝了一杯有柴油味的茶。","It tastes like chocolate. 它吃起來像巧克力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>taste</b> some food or drink, you eat or drink a small amount of it in order to try its flavour, for example, to see if you like it or not. 品嚐","examples":["I tasted the wine the waiter had produced. 我嚐了嚐服務員端上來的葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>taste</b> something that you are eating or drinking, you are aware of its flavour. 嚐出…味道","examples":["You can taste the green chilli in the dish but it is a little sweet. 你能吃出菜裡有青辣椒的味道，但它有點甜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>taste</b> something such as a way of life or a pleasure, you experience it for a short period of time. (短暫地) 體驗","examples":["Once you have tasted the outdoor life in southern California, it's hard to return to Montana in winter. 一旦你體驗過南加州的戶外生活，再要回到蒙大拿過冬就會感到很難。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something that is said or done is <b>in bad taste</b> or <b>in poor taste</b>, you mean that it is offensive, often because it concerns death or sex and is inappropriate for the situation. If you say that something is <b>in good taste</b>, you mean that it is not offensive and that it is appropriate for the situation. 品味低/高","examples":["He rejects the idea that his film is in bad taste. 他拒絕接受那種認為他的電影品味低的觀點。"]}]}]},"teacher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教師，老師，教員；<喻>給人教益的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>teacher</b> is a person who teaches, usually as a job at a school or similar institution. 教師","examples":["I'm a teacher with 21 years' experience. 我是一個有21年經驗的教師。"]}]}]},"ten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十個，十"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十的"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"十個；十個（東西）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Ten）（美、俄、加、德、荷、西、英）登（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ten</b> is the number 10. 10; 十","examples":["Over the past ten years things have changed. 在過去的10年中，情況已經發生了變化。"]}]}]},"tea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"茶，茶水；（用其他植物葉子沏的）飲料；茶葉；<英>茶點，下午茶；<英>便餐，晚點；<西印度>（咖啡、可可等）熱飲；<西印度>（尤指帶有熱飲、麵包的）早點"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<古>喝茶，吃下午茶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tea</b> is a drink made by adding boiling water to tea leaves or tea bags. Tea usually refers to black tea from India or China. Herbal tea is made from various plants. 茶","examples":["...a cup of tea. …一杯茶。","Would you like some tea? 你想喝茶嗎？","...chamomile tea. …甘菊花茶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The chopped dried leaves of the plant that tea is made from is referred to as <b>tea</b>. 茶葉","examples":["...a box of tea. …一盒茶葉。"]}]}]},"thank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"感謝，向……表示謝意；（諷）要……負責，責怪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"感謝"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"謝謝（thanks）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>thank you</b> or, in more informal English, <b>thanks</b> to express your gratitude when someone does something for you or gives you what you want. 謝謝 (用於表示感謝別人所做之事或贈與所需之物)","examples":["Thank you very much for your call. 非常感謝您打電話來。","Thanks for the information. 謝謝您告訴我這訊息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>thank you</b> or, in more informal English, <b>thanks</b> to politely accept something that has just been offered to you. 謝謝 (用於禮貌接受別人給與之物)","examples":["\"Would you like a cup of coffee?\"—\"Thank you, I'd love one.\" “你要喝杯咖啡嗎？”—“謝謝，來一杯吧。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>no thank you</b> or, in more informal English, <b>no thanks</b> to politely refuse something that has just been offered to you. 謝謝 (用於禮貌拒絕別人給與之物)","examples":["\"Would you like a cigarette?\"—\"No thank you.\" “你要來支香菸嗎？”—“不了，謝謝。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>thank you</b> or, in more informal English, <b>thanks</b> to politely acknowledge what someone has said to you, especially when they have answered your question or said something nice to you. 謝謝 (用於禮貌地感謝別人的回答或讚美)","examples":["\"You look very nice indeed.\"—\"Thank you.\" “你看起來真漂亮。”—“謝謝。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>thank you</b> or <b>thank you very much</b> in order to say firmly that you do not want someone's help or to tell them that you do not like the way that they are behaving toward you. 謝謝 (用於拒絕別人的幫助或告訴對方自己不喜歡這種對待方式)","examples":["I can find my own way home, thank you. 我自己能找到路回家，謝謝。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>thank</b> someone <b>for</b> something, you express your gratitude to them for it. 感謝","examples":["I thanked them for their long and loyal service. 我感謝他們長期忠誠的效力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you express your <b>thanks</b> to someone, you express your gratitude to them for something. 謝意","examples":["They accepted their certificates with words of thanks. 他們接過證書，同時表示了謝意。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Thank God</b>,\" \"<b>Thank Goodness</b>,\" or \"<b>Thank heavens</b>\" when you are very relieved about something. 謝天謝地","examples":["I was wrong, thank God. 原來我錯了，謝天謝地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have</b> someone <b>to thank</b> <b>for</b> something, you mean that they caused it to happen. 歸因於某人","examples":["I have her to thank for my life. 我多虧她才保住性命。","You have only yourself to thank for this mess. 你只能怪你自己把事情弄得這麼糟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>thanks to</b> a particular person or thing, you mean that they are responsible for it happening or caused it to happen. 歸功於","examples":["It is thanks to this committee that many new sponsors have come forward. 多虧這個委員會，才來了這麼多新的贊助商。"]}]}]},"third":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"第三"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"三分之一；（機動車變速器的）第三檔；（音樂）三度音；三等學位（英國大學中低於平均水平的學位）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"第三的；三分之一的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"第三（點）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"ord.","pos_name":"序數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>third</b> item in a series is the one that you count as number three. 第3","examples":["I sleep on the third floor. 我睡在3樓。"]}]},{"pos":"fraction.","pos_name":"分數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>third</b> is one of three equal parts of something. 1/3","examples":["A third of the cost went into technology and services. 1/3的成本用於技術和服務。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>third</b> when you want to make a third point or give a third reason for something. 第三 (點)","examples":["First, interest rates may take longer to fall than is hoped. Second, lending may fall. Third, bad loans could wipe out much of any improvement. 首先，利率下調可能比預期的時間要久。第二，貸款可能下降。第三，壞帳可能抵消大部分的成效。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>third</b> is the lowest honours degree that can be obtained from a British university. 三等學位 (英國大學的最低榮譽學位)","examples":["...Ms. Hodge, who graduated in 2002 with a third in economics. …霍奇小姐，2002年畢業並獲得經濟學三等學位。"]}]}]},"thirteen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十三"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十三；十三歲；十三個（人或物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十三的；十三個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thirteen</b> is the number 13. 13","examples":[]}]}]},"then":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（指過去）當時，（指將來）到那時；接下來，然後；因此，既然如此；另外，還有；總之；（表示交談、陳述等的開始或結束）那麼；這麼說（用於表示對已知情況的判斷或詢問）；畢竟，話說回來"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"當時（任職等）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Then</b> means at a particular time in the past or in the future. 那時","examples":["He wanted to have a source of income after his retirement; until then, he wouldn't require additional money. 他想在退休後有個收入來源，而這之前則不需要額外的錢。","Executives pledged to get the company back on track. Since then, though, shares have fallen 30 per cent. 主管們發誓要讓公司重上軌道，不過從那以後股票價格還是下降了30％。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Then</b> is also an adverb. 當時","examples":["Richard Strauss, then 76 years old, suffered through the war years in silence. 理查德·斯特勞斯當時已76歲，默默地熬過了戰爭歲月。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> to say that one thing happens after another, or is after another on a list. 然後","examples":["Add the oil and then the scallops to the pan, leaving a little space for the garlic. 往鍋裡倒入油，然後加入扇貝，再放一點大蒜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> in conversation to indicate that what you are about to say follows logically in some way from what has just been said or implied. 那麼","examples":["\"I wasn't a very good scholar in school.\"—\"Then why did you become a teacher?\" “我在學校時成績不是很好。”— “那你為什麼當老師呢？”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> to signal the end of a topic or the end of a conversation. 用於表示話題或談話結束","examples":["\"I'll talk to you on Friday anyway.\"—\"Yep. Okay then.\" “我星期五總歸要和你談談的。” —“行，就這麼定了。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> with words like \"now,\" \"well,\" and \"okay,\" to introduce a new topic or a new point of view. 用於引入新話題或新觀點","examples":["Now then, I'm going to explain everything to you before we do it. 嗯，我要在我們動手之前向你們把一切解釋清楚。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> to introduce the second part of a sentence which begins with \"if.\" The first part of the sentence describes a possible situation, and <b>then</b> introduces the result of the situation. (引導以“if”開頭的句子，敘述可能的情況) 那麼","examples":["If the answer is \"yes,\" then we need to leave now. 如果答案為“是”，那麼我們現在就該離開了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>then</b> at the beginning of a sentence or after \"and\" or \"but\" to introduce a comment or an extra piece of information to what you have already said. (用於句首或“)(and)(”、“)(but)(”之後) 話說回來","examples":["He sounded sincere, but then, he always did. 他聽起來很誠懇，不過，話說回來，他一貫如此。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Then</b> is used when you refer to something which was true at a particular time in the past but is not true now. 當時的","examples":["...a tour of the then new airport. …在當時新機場的一次參觀。"]}]}]},"thirty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"二十世紀三十年代（the thirties）；三十（數字 30）；三十幾（複數 thirties，指 30 至 39）"},{"pos":"num.","zh":"三十"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"三十個的；（作表語）三十歲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thirty</b> is the number 30. 30","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>thirties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 30 and 39. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>thirties</b>, you are aged between 30 and 39. If the temperature is <b>in the thirties</b>, the temperature is between 30 and 39 degrees. 三十幾","examples":["Mozart clearly enjoyed good health throughout his twenties and early thirties. 莫扎特顯然在二十幾歲和三十剛出頭時身體很好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The thirties</b> is the decade between 1930 and 1939. 20世紀30年代","examples":["She became quite a notable director in the thirties and forties. 她在20世紀的三四十年代成為一位名導演。"]}]}]},"talk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"說話，交談，談話；談判，商討；（就某一主題）演講，作報告；講（某種語言）；說服；<非正式>有說服力；招認，洩露秘密；議論，說閒話；<非正式>正在討論；批評（某人）；（用訊號、數字等）交流，傳遞資訊；一直說到……為止；（書面）論述"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"交談，討論；（政府、機構等之間的）正式會談，談判；（專題）報告，演講；空談；謠言；話題，說話方式；閒談"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>talk</b>, you use spoken language to express your thoughts, ideas, or feelings. 說話","examples":["He was too distressed to talk. 他傷心得說不出話來。","The boys all began to talk at once. 男孩們都馬上開始說話了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>talk</b> <b>on</b> or <b>about</b> something, you make an informal speech telling people what you know or think about it. 發表 (非正式的) 講話","examples":["She will talk on the issues she cares passionately about including education and nursery care. 她將就她熱切關注的問題發表講話，包括教育和幼兒護理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>are talking</b> <b>about</b> another person or <b>are talking</b>, they are discussing that person. 議論","examples":["Everyone is talking about him. 大家都在議論他。","We'd better not be seen together. People will talk. 我們最好不要被人看見在一起。人們會議論。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>talks</b> when they are being held by police or soldiers, they reveal important or secret information, usually unwillingly. 供出訊息","examples":["They'll talk, they'll implicate me. 他們將招供，他們將把我牽連進去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Talk</b> is also a noun. 說話","examples":["That's not the kind of talk one usually hears from accountants. 那不是人們通常從會計人員那裡聽到的那種話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Talk</b> is also a noun. 交談","examples":["We had a long talk about her father, Tony, who was a friend of mine. 關於她父親託尼我們進行了一次長時間的交談，託尼是我的一個朋友。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Talk</b> is also a noun. 談話","examples":["I think it's time we had a talk. 我認為是我們進行一次談話的時候了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Talk</b> is also a noun. 非正式的講話","examples":["A guide gives a brief talk on the history of the site. 一位導遊就這個遺址的歷史作了一次簡要的講述。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Talks</b> are formal discussions intended to produce an agreement, usually between different countries or between employers and employees. (通常指國家間或僱主和僱員間的) 談判","examples":["...the next round of Middle East peace talks. …下一輪中東和平談判。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Talk</b> is also a noun. 議論","examples":["There has been a lot of talk about me getting married. 有很多關於我要結婚了的議論。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something such as an idea or threat is just <b>talk</b>, or <b>all talk</b>, you mean that it does not mean or matter much, because people are exaggerating about it or do not really intend to do anything about it. 空談","examples":["Has much of this actually been tried here? Or is it just talk? 這其中有多少在這裡真正被試過？或者這只是空談？"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>talk</b> <b>to</b> someone, you have a conversation with them. You can also say that two people <b>talk</b>. 交談","examples":["We talked and laughed a lot. 我們暢懷說笑。","I talked to him yesterday. 我昨天和他談過。","When she came back, they were talking about American food. 當她回來時，他們正在談論美國食品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>talk</b> <b>to</b> someone, you tell them about the things that are worrying you. You can also say that two people <b>talk</b>. 訴說","examples":["Your first step should be to talk to a teacher or school counsellor. 你第一步應該是去找個老師或學校輔導員談談。","Do call if you want to talk about it. 一定要打電話來，如果你想談這件事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one group of people <b>talks</b> <b>to</b> another, or if two groups <b>talk</b>, they have formal discussions in order to do a deal or produce an agreement. 磋商","examples":["We're talking to some people about opening an office in Boston. 我們正與一些人磋商在波士頓設立辦事處的事。","It triggered speculation that GM and Jaguar might be talking. 這引發了通用公司和捷豹公司可能正在進行磋商的猜測。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When different countries or different sides in a dispute <b>talk</b>, or <b>talk</b> <b>to</b> each other, they discuss their differences in order to try and settle the dispute. 和談","examples":["They are collecting information in preparation for the day when the two sides sit down and talk. 他們正在收集資訊，為雙方坐下來和談的那一天做準備。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>talk</b> a particular language or <b>talk</b> with a particular accent, you use that language or have that accent when you speak. 說 (某種語言); 帶 (某種口音)","examples":["You don't sound like a foreigner talking English. 你聽起來不像外國人在說英語。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>talk</b> something such as politics or sports, you discuss it. 談論 (政治、體育等)","examples":["The guests were mostly middle-aged men talking business. 客人們大多是談生意的中年男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>talk</b> to say what you think of the ideas that someone is expressing. For example, if you say that someone <b>is</b> <b>talking sense</b>, you mean that you think the opinions they are expressing are sensible. 說話 (有道理或沒道理)","examples":["You must admit George, you're talking absolute nonsense. 你必須承認，喬治，你正在說廢話。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say that you <b>are talking</b> a particular thing to draw attention to your topic or to point out a characteristic of what you are discussing. 正在討論 (的是)","examples":["We're talking megabucks this time. 我們這次正在討論的可是一筆鉅款。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>talk about</b> before mentioning a particular expression or situation, when you mean that something is a very striking or clear example of that expression or situation. 這就叫…","examples":["Took us quite a while to get here, didn't it? Talk about fate moving in a mysterious way! 用了我們好長一段時間才到這裡，不是嗎？這叫作命運難料啊！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use the expression <b>talking of</b> to introduce a new topic that you want to discuss, and to link it to something that has already been mentioned. (用於引出新話題) 說起","examples":["I'll give a prize to the best idea. Talking of good ideas, here's one to break the ice at a wedding reception. 我將獎勵最佳主意。說起好主意，這裡就有一個，能活躍婚禮氣氛。"]}]}]},"three":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"三（基數詞）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"三，三個；由三個組成的一組（複數 threes）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"三的，三個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Three</b> is the number 3. 3","examples":["We waited three months before going back to see the specialist. 我們等了3個月後才回去見那位專家。"]}]}]},"thousand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"（數字）一千；許許多多，數以千計；千位數"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"成千上萬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>thousand</b> or <b>one</b> <b>thousand</b> is the number 1,000. 1000","examples":["...five thousand acres. …5000英畝。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>thousands of</b> things or people, you are emphasizing that there are very many of them. 成千上萬","examples":["Thousands of refugees are packed into overcrowded towns and villages. 成千上萬的難民擠入擁擠不堪的城鎮與村莊。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also use <b>thousands</b> as a pronoun. 成千上萬","examples":["Hundreds have been killed in the fighting and thousands made homeless. 數百人在戰鬥中喪生，成千上萬的人無家可歸。"]}]}]},"thursday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期四（星期三之後、星期五之前的一天；正式拼寫首字母通常大寫，常與介詞 on 連用；非正式也作“週四”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thursday</b> is the day after Wednesday and before Friday. 星期四","examples":["On Thursday Barrett invited me for a drink. 星期四巴雷特請我喝了一杯。","We go and do the weekly shopping every Thursday morning. 我們每週四早上都去進行每週一次的採購。"]}]}]},"there":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在那裡；在那邊；在那點上"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"你瞧"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"那個地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>There</b> is used as the subject of the verb \"be\" to say that something exists or does not exist, or to draw attention to it. 用作動詞(be)的主語，表示某物是否存在，或使人注意該物","examples":["There are temporary traffic lights now at the school. 那所學校現在設有臨時交通訊號燈。","Are there any cookies left? 有剩下的曲奇餅嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> in front of certain verbs when you are saying that something exists, develops, or can be seen. Whether the verb is singular or plural depends on the noun which follows the verb. 用於某些動詞前表示某物存在、發展或可見；動詞的單複數形式取決於其後的名詞","examples":["There remains considerable doubt over when the road will be completed. 對於道路何時能竣工，人們還有相當多的疑慮。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>There</b> is used after \"hello\" or \"hi\" when you are greeting someone. 表問候，用於(hello)或(hi)後","examples":["\"Hello there,\" said the woman, smiling at them.—\"Hi!\" they chorused. “嗨，你們好！”那婦人朝他們笑著招呼道。—“你好！”他們齊聲回答。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>there there</b>\" to someone who is very upset, especially a small child, in order to comfort them. (用來安慰別人，尤其是孩子) 好了，好了","examples":["\"There, there,\" said Mommy. \"You've been having a bad dream.\" “好了，好了，”媽媽說道。“你是在作惡夢。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>there you are</b>\" or \"<b>there you go</b>\" when you are offering something to someone. 給你","examples":["\"There you go, Mr. Walters,\" she said, giving him his documents. “給你，沃爾特斯先生，”她邊說邊把檔案給了他。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>there</b>, it exists or is available. 存在","examples":["The group of old buildings is still there today. 那個舊樓群如今還在。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> to refer to a place which has already been mentioned. 在那兒 (指前面提到的地方)","examples":["The next day we drove 33 miles to Siena (the Villa Arceno is a great place to stay while you are there). 第二天我們驅車33英里到了錫耶納（在那兒，阿爾切諾別墅是個很不錯的落腳之處）。","\"Come on over, if you want.\"—\"How do I get there?\" “過來看看吧，如果你願意。”—“我怎麼到那兒？”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> to indicate a place that you are pointing to or looking at, in order to draw someone's attention to it. (用來引起注意) 那兒","examples":["There it is, on the corner over there. 在那兒，在那邊轉角處。","There she is on the left up there. 她在那兒，在左邊那兒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> in expressions such as \"<b>there he was</b>\" or \"<b>there we were</b>\" to sum up part of a story or to slow a story down for dramatic effect. (用於概括故事或放慢講故事的速度) 就這樣","examples":["So there he was all covered in mud, and still in a good mood. 就這樣他全身是泥，但仍然情緒高昂。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> when speaking on the telephone to ask if someone is available to speak to you. (電話用語) ...在嗎","examples":["Hello, is Gordon there please? 您好，請問戈登在嗎？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> to refer to a point that someone has made in a conversation. 在那點上","examples":["I think you're right there John. 我認為你在那一點上說對了，約翰。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> to refer to a stage that has been reached in an activity or process. (指活動或過程已達到的階段) 那裡","examples":["We are making further investigations and will take the matter from there. 我們正在進一步調查，並將從那裡入手。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>there</b> to indicate that something has reached a point or level which is completely successful. 做成地; 達成地","examples":["We had hoped to fill the back page with extra news; we're not quite there yet. 我們原本希望在最後一版面載滿附加新聞；但我們現在還沒真正做到。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>there</b> in expressions such as <b>there you go</b> or <b>there we are</b> when accepting that an unsatisfactory situation cannot be changed. 別無他法","examples":["This is a little cruel, but there you go. 這是有點兒殘忍，但也沒辦法。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can use <b>there</b> in expressions such as <b>there you go</b> and <b>there we are</b> when emphasizing that something proves that you were right. 我沒說錯吧","examples":["You see? There you go. That's why I didn't mention it earlier. I knew you'd take it the wrong way. 瞧見了沒？我沒說錯吧。這就是我沒早說的原因，就知道你們會弄錯的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Phrases such as <b>there</b> you <b>go again</b> are used to show anger at someone who is repeating something that has annoyed you in the past. 又來了","examples":["\"There you go again, upsetting the child!\" said Shirley. “你又來折騰孩子了！”雪莉說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can add \"<b>so there</b>\" to what you are saying to show that you have won an argument, or that you will not change your mind about a decision you have made, even though the person you are talking to disagrees with you. This is usually said by children or to be funny. 沒錯吧; 就這麼定了","examples":["I think that's sweet, so there. 我覺得那很好，就這麼定了。","You see? Mom said I could - so there! 瞧見了沒？媽媽說我能行—沒錯吧！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>there and then</b> or <b>then and there</b>, it happens immediately. 立即","examples":["Many felt that he should have resigned there and then. 很多人覺得他原本就應該立即辭職。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is there for</b> you, they help and support you, especially when you have problems. (尤指在別人困難時) 幫助支援某人","examples":["Despite what happened in the past I want her to know I am there for her. 儘管過去發生了一些事，我仍希望她知道我支援她。"]}]}]},"thought":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"想法，看法，主意；考慮，深思；關心，顧慮；意圖，希望，念頭；思想，思潮；思考，思維；心思，思想（thoughts）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"認為，覺得；思考，考慮；想做，打算做（think 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thought</b> is the past tense and past participle of <b>think</b>. (think)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>thought</b> is an idea that you have in your mind. 想法","examples":["The thought of Nick made her throat tighten. 一想到尼克就會讓她的喉嚨發緊。","I've just had a thought. 我剛剛有了個想法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>thoughts</b> are their mind, or all the ideas in their mind when they are concentrating on one particular thing. 心思","examples":["I jumped to my feet so my thoughts wouldn't start to wander. 我猛地站了起來，這樣我就不會走神了。","Usually at this time our thoughts are on Christmas. 通常在這種時候我們的心思都放在聖誕節上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A person's <b>thoughts</b> are their opinions on a particular subject. 看法","examples":["Many of you have written to us to express your thoughts on the conflict. 你們中的很多人已經寫信給我們表達對這次衝突的看法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Thought</b> is the activity of thinking, especially deeply, carefully, or logically. 思考","examples":["Alice had been so deep in thought that she had walked past her car without even seeing it. 愛麗斯陷入深深的思考之中，連經過自己的車都沒看到。","He had given some thought to what she had told him. 他已對她告訴自己的話做了些思考。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>thought</b> is an intention, hope, or reason for doing something. 意圖; 希望; 理由","examples":["Sarah's first thought was to run back and get Max. 薩拉首先想到的是跑回去叫馬克斯。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Thought</b> is the group of ideas and beliefs which belongs, for example, to a particular religion, philosophy, science, or political party. 思想體系","examples":["Aristotle's scientific theories dominated Western thought for fifteen hundred years. 亞里士多德的科學理論統治西方思想長達1500年之久。"]}]}]},"tiger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"老虎；兇暴的人（也指勇猛的人）；Tiger 用作人名或綽號，可譯作泰格（英）、蒂熱（法）、蒂格（瑞典）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tiger</b> is a large fierce animal belonging to the cat family. Tigers are orange with black stripes. 老虎","examples":[]}]}]},"ticket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"票，入場券；（交通違章）通知單，罰款單；（政黨在選舉中支援的）候選人名單；（競選時所支援的）綱領，政見；（商店中標明貨物價格、尺碼等的）標籤；彩票，獎券；途徑；（貨物）收條；（船員、飛行員等的）執照；工單；<英>退役證書；<蘇格蘭，美，非正式>……人，……傢伙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"售票；給（違章停車、超速行駛的人）開罰單；（為顯示價格、尺寸等）貼標籤於；給定目標；<美>註定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ticket</b> is a small, official piece of paper or card which shows that you have paid to enter a place such as a theatre or a sports stadium, or shows that you have paid for a trip. 入場券; 票","examples":["He had a ticket for a flight on Friday. 他有一張星期五的機票。","...two tickets for the game. …兩張比賽入場券。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ticket</b> is an official piece of paper which orders you to pay a fine or to appear in court because you have committed a driving or parking offence. (交通) 罰款通知單; 違章傳票","examples":["Slow down or you'll get a ticket. 開慢點兒，否則你會接到一張罰款通知單。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>ticket</b> for a game of chance such as a raffle or a lottery is a piece of paper with a number on it. If the number on your ticket matches the number chosen, you win a prize. 彩票","examples":["She bought a lottery ticket and won more than $33 million. 她買了一張彩票，中了三千三百多萬美元。"]}]}]},"tire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）感到累，（使）感到疲勞；厭倦，厭煩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>輪胎（同 tyre）；頭飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>tires</b> you or you <b>tire</b>, you feel that you have used a lot of energy and you want to rest or sleep. 使感到疲倦; 感到疲倦","examples":["If driving tires you, take the train. 如果開車使你感到疲勞，那就坐火車吧。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tire of</b> something, you no longer wish to do it, because you have become bored of it or unhappy with it. 厭倦","examples":["He felt he would never tire of listening to her stories. 他覺得自己永遠也不會厭倦聽她的故事。"]}]}]},"today":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"今天，今日；現今，在當代"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"今天，今日；現在，當代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>today</b> to refer to this day on which you are speaking or writing. 今天","examples":["How are you feeling today? 你今天感覺怎麼樣？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the present period of history as <b>today</b>. 當今","examples":["The United States is in a serious recession today. 美國當今處於嚴重的經濟蕭條期。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Today</b> is also a noun. 今天","examples":["Today is Friday, September 14th. 今天是9月14日，星期五。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Today</b> is also a noun. 當今","examples":["In today's America, health care is one of the very biggest businesses. 在當今的美國，醫療保健是幾個最大的行業之一。"]}]}]},"tomorrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在明天，在明日；（尤指不久的）將來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"明天，明日；未來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>tomorrow</b> to refer to the day after today. 明天","examples":["Bye, see you tomorrow. 再見，明天見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the future, especially the near future, as <b>tomorrow</b>. 在 (尤指不久的) 將來","examples":["What is education going to look like tomorrow? 教育將來會是什麼樣子呢？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tomorrow</b> is also a noun. 明天","examples":["What's on your agenda for tomorrow? 你明天日程有什麼安排？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tomorrow</b> is also a noun. 未來","examples":["...tomorrow's computer industry. …未來的計算機業。"]}]}]},"thing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"東西，物；（無生命的）物體，物件；個人物品，衣物（things）；器具，用品（things）；情形，事件；行為，活動；想法，觀點；情況，形勢（things）；……之類的東西，特定的事物；需要的東西，適當的東西；事實本身；（生活的）方面；目標，目的；生物，有生命的東西；傢伙，東西（指人或動物，常帶感情色彩）；（用於強調）任何東西；（某人喜歡或擅長的）事情；<非正式>（對某事物或某人的）喜歡，憎惡；爛東西，破爛玩意兒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>thing</b> to refer to any object, feature, or event when you cannot, need not, or do not want to refer to it more precisely. (不具體指稱的) 東西; 事情","examples":["\"What's that thing in the middle of the fountain?\"—\"Some kind of statue, I guess.\" “噴泉中間那個東西是什麼？”—“我想是雕像之類的吧。”","She was in the middle of clearing the breakfast things. 她正忙著清理早餐後的那些東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Thing</b> is used in lists and descriptions to give examples or to increase the range of what you are referring to. (用於舉例或擴大所指範圍) 等事物","examples":["They spend their money on things like rent and groceries. 他們把錢花在房租和雜貨之類的事情上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Thing</b> is often used after an adjective, where it would also be possible just to use the adjective. For example, you can say <b>it's a different thing</b> instead of <b>it's different</b>. 東西 (用於形容詞後，單用該形容詞也可表示相同的意思)","examples":["Of course, literacy isn't the same thing as intelligence. 當然，識字與智力不是一回事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Thing</b> is often used instead of the pronouns \"anything,\" or \"everything\" in order to emphasize what you are saying. 任何事情 (用於強調)","examples":["I haven't done a thing all day. 我一整天還沒做任何事情。","It isn't going to solve a single thing. 這解決不了任何問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Thing</b> is used in expressions such as <b>such a thing</b> or <b>a thing like that</b>, especially in negative statements, in order to emphasize the bad or difficult situation you are referring back to. 這種事情 (尤用於否定句，強調前面提到的糟糕或困難情況)","examples":["I don't believe he would tell Leo such a thing. 我不信他會告訴利奧這種事。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>thing</b> to refer in a vague way to a situation, activity, or idea, especially when you want to suggest that it is not very important. (尤指不重要的) 情形; 活動; 想法","examples":["I'm a bit unsettled tonight. This war thing's upsetting me. 我今晚有點兒不安，這種爭鬥很讓我心煩。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You often use <b>thing</b> to indicate to the person you are addressing that you are about to mention something important, or something that you particularly want them to know. 表示將要提及重要的事情或特別希望對方知道的事情","examples":["One thing I am sure of was that she was scared. 有一點我可以肯定的是她被嚇壞了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>thing</b> is often used to refer back to something that has just been mentioned, either to emphasize it or to give more information about it. 常指前面曾提到的內容，表示強調或提供更多資訊","examples":["Getting drunk is a thing all young men do. 喝醉酒是所有小夥子都會幹的事。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>thing</b> is a physical object that is considered as having no life of its own. (無生命的) 物體; 東西","examples":["It's not a thing. It's a human being! 這不是一件東西，這是一個人！"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Thing</b> is used to refer to something, especially a physical object, when you want to express contempt or anger toward it. (用於表示蔑視或憤怒) 東西","examples":["Turn that thing off! 把那個東西關掉！"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You can call a person or an animal a particular <b>thing</b> when you want to mention a particular quality that they have and express your feelings toward them, usually affectionate feelings. 東西 (常指惹人憐愛的人或動物)","examples":["She is such a cute little thing. 她是個非常可愛的小東西。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"Your <b>things</b> are your clothes or possessions. 衣物; 財物","examples":["Sara told him to take all his things and not to return. 薩拉叫他帶上他的所有東西離開，別再回來。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"<b>Things</b> can refer to the situation or life in general and the way it is changing or affecting you. 情況","examples":["Everyone agrees things are getting better. 大家都認為情況正在好轉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If, for example, you <b>do the</b> right <b>thing</b> or <b>do the</b> decent <b>thing</b> in a situation, you do something which is considered correct or socially acceptable in that situation. 做 (正確、合宜) 的事","examples":["People want to do the right thing and buy \"green.\" 人們想做正確的事，購買“綠色”商品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>first thing</b>, you do it at the beginning of the day, before you do anything else. If you do it <b>last thing</b>, you do it at the end of the day, before you go to bed or go to sleep. 第一/最後一件事; 一大早/臨睡前","examples":["I'll go see her, first thing. 我一大早就去看她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>it is a</b> good <b>thing to</b> do something to introduce a piece of advice or a comment on a situation or activity. …是件好/壞事","examples":["Can you tell me whether it is a good thing to prune an apple tree? 你能否告訴我，修剪蘋果樹是不是件好事？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say that the first of two ideas, actions, or situations <b>is one thing</b> when you want to contrast it with a second idea, action, or situation and emphasize that the second one is much more difficult, important, or extreme. …是一回事 (用於兩種想法、行動或局勢的對比，以強調第二種情況更困難、重要或極端)","examples":["It was one thing to talk about leaving; it was another to physically walk out the door. 說要離開是一回事；真正走出門又是另一回事。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say <b>for one thing</b> when you are explaining a statement or answering a question, to suggest that you are not giving the whole explanation or answer, and that there are other points that you could add to it. 其一 (用於引出更多的理由)","examples":["She was a monster. For one thing, she really enjoyed cruelty. 她是個惡魔。其中之一就是，她真的以殘忍為樂。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use the expression \"<b>one thing and another</b>\" to suggest that there are several reasons for something or several items on a list, but you are not going to explain or mention them all. 種種原因","examples":["What with one thing and another, it was fairly late in the day when we got home. 由於種種原因，我們回到家時已經相當晚了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say <b>it is just one of those things</b> you mean that you cannot explain something because it seems to happen by chance. 這是無法解釋的事情","examples":["\"I wonder why.\" Mr. Dambar shrugged. \"It must be just one of those things, I guess.\" “我想知道原因。”丹巴先生聳了聳肩說道。“我想這肯定是無法解釋的事情。”"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is seeing</b> or <b>hearing things</b>, you mean that they believe they are seeing or hearing something, but it is not really there. 幻視; 幻聽","examples":["Dr. Payne led Lana back into the examination room and told her she was seeing things. 佩恩醫生把拉娜帶回檢查室並告訴她這是她的視覺幻象。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can say there is <b>no such thing</b> <b>as</b> something to emphasize that it does not exist or is not possible. 沒有這回事","examples":["There really is no such thing as a totally risk-free industry. 完全沒風險的行業實際上是不存在的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You say <b>the thing is</b> to introduce an explanation, comment, or opinion, that relates to something that has just been said. <b>The thing is</b> is often used to identify a problem relating to what has just been said. 問題是","examples":["\"What does your market research consist of?\"—\"Well, the thing is, it depends on our target age group.\" “你的市場研究包含什麼內容？”—“哦，問題是，這取決於我們的目標年齡群體。”"]}]}]},"tonight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在今晚，今夜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"今晚，今夜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tonight</b> is used to refer to the evening of today or the night that follows today. 在今晚","examples":["I'm at home tonight. 我今晚在家。","Tonight he proved what a great player he was. 今晚他證明了自己是一個多麼了不起的選手。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tonight</b> is also a noun. 今晚","examples":["Tonight is the opening night of the opera. 今晚是這部歌劇的首演之夜。"]}]}]},"tone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"語氣，腔調，口吻；氣氛，基調，風格；（尤指樂器或電子音響裝置的）音質，音色；色調，明暗；強健狀況，（尤指肌肉的）緊實度；（電話或應答機等發出的）聲音訊號；（音樂）全音，音程；（說話的）聲調，音調；（生理）神經纖維的正常活動狀態"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使強健，使結實；與……協調，與……相配；（用化學溶液使黑白照片在潤色時）變色；用某種調子說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tone</b> of a sound is its particular quality. 音質","examples":["Cross could hear him speaking in low tones to Sarah. 克羅斯可以聽到他在低聲對薩拉說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>tone</b> is a quality in their voice which shows what they are feeling or thinking. 語氣","examples":["I still didn't like his tone of voice; he sounded angry and accusing. 我仍然不喜歡他說話的語氣；他的聲音聽起來好像是怒氣衝衝地在指責人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>tone</b> of a speech or piece of writing is its style and the opinions or ideas expressed in it. > 風格; (講話或文章的) 口氣","examples":["The tone of the letter was very friendly. 這封信的語氣相當友好。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>tone</b> of a place or an event is its general atmosphere. 氛圍","examples":["There were no stores that would lower the tone of the area. 沒有一家商店會降低該地區的氛圍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>tone</b> of someone's body, especially their muscles, is its degree of firmness and strength. (尤指肌肉的) 結實度","examples":["...stretch exercises that improve muscle tone. …提高肌肉結實度的伸展鍛鍊。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>tone</b> is one of the lighter, darker, or brighter shades of the same colour. 色調","examples":["Each brick also varies slightly in tone, texture and size. 每塊磚在色調、質地和尺寸上也略有不同。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>tone</b> is one of the sounds that you hear when you are using a telephone, for example, the sound that tells you that a number is busy, or no longer exists. (電話的) 提示音","examples":["I can't get a dial tone on this phone. 我在這部電話上聽不到撥號音。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>tones</b> your body makes it firm and strong. 使強健","examples":["This movement lengthens your spine and tones the spinal nerves. 該運動能伸展你的脊柱，強健脊髓神經。","Try these toning exercises before you start the day. 試著在開始新的一天前練練這些健身操。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tone up</b> means the same as . 同(tone)","examples":["Exercise tones up your body. 運動強健身體。"]}]}]},"throw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投，擲，拋，扔；擲（色子），擲出（色子的點數）；隨手扔下（某物）；猛推，使勁撞；急伸，猛動（身體部位）；使迅猛地摔倒在地；使突然陷入；使困惑，使驚奇；把……拉成坯；投射（光或影子）；使嗓音聽起來像來自他人（或別處）；故意輸掉（比賽）；扳動（開關、操作杆等）；將……關進（監獄等）；大發脾氣；（揮拳）猛擊；舉辦（聚會）；投入，投身（於）；將……投向（某人）；（車輛）突然換擋；<美，非正式>成功完成；迅速放置（或立起）；（馬）脫落（蹄鐵）；（動物）下仔；（在車床上）車（木料等）；捻（絲等）成線"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"投，擲；投射距離；套，罩；摔倒對手；<非正式>每一份（花費）；（地質）落差，位移；速轉裝置，旋轉工具；擺動；（指標的）行程；冒險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>throw</b> an object that you are holding, you move your hand or arm quickly and let go of the object, so that it moves through the air. 投; 扔","examples":["He spent hours throwing a tennis ball against a wall. 他花了數小時對著一堵牆扔網球。","The crowd began throwing stones. 那群人開始扔石頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> your body or part of your body into a particular position or place, you move it there suddenly and with a lot of force. 猛然移動 (身體或身體部位)","examples":["She threw her arms around his shoulders. 她猛地伸出雙臂抱住他的肩膀。","She threatened to throw herself in front of a train. 她威脅說要臥軌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> something into a particular place or position, you put it there in a quick and careless way. (漫不經心地) 扔下","examples":["He struggled out of his bulky jacket and threw it on to the back seat. 他用力脫下笨重的夾克，順手把它扔到後座上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>throw</b> someone into a particular place or position means to force them roughly into that place or position. 使摔倒","examples":["He threw me to the ground. 他把我摔倒在地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is thrown</b> <b>into</b> prison, you mean that they are put there by the authorities. 把…關進 (監獄)","examples":["Those two should have been thrown in jail. 那兩個人當時就該被關進監獄。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a horse <b>throws</b> its rider, it makes him or her fall off, by suddenly jumping or moving violently. (馬) 摔落 (騎手)","examples":["The horse reared, throwing its rider and knocking down a youth standing beside it. 這匹馬向後一仰，摔下騎手並撞倒站在它旁邊的一個年輕人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is thrown</b> <b>into</b> a bad situation or state, something causes them to be in that situation or state. 使陷入 (困境等)","examples":["Abidjan was thrown into turmoil because of a protest by taxi drivers. 阿比讓因計程車司機們的抗議而陷入了混亂。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>throws</b> light or a shadow <b>on</b> a surface, it causes that surface to have light or a shadow on it. 投下 (光線或影子)","examples":["The sunlight is white and blinding, throwing hard-edged shadows on the ground. 陽光亮白刺眼，在地上投下輪廓分明的影子。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something <b>throws</b> doubt <b>on</b> a person or thing, it causes people to doubt or suspect them. 使…產生懷疑","examples":["This new information does throw doubt on their choice. 這個新訊息確實讓人對他們的選擇產生懷疑。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> a look or smile at someone or something, you look or smile at them quickly and suddenly. 猛然投以 (一瞥或一笑)","examples":["Emily turned and threw her a suggestive grin. 埃米莉轉過身，猛然地向她投了個暗示性的微笑。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> yourself, your energy, or your money <b>into</b> a particular job or activity, you become involved in it very actively or enthusiastically. 投身於; 投入","examples":["She threw herself into a modelling career. 她投身於模特職業。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> a fit or a tantrum, you suddenly start to behave in an uncontrolled way. 爆發 (脾氣); 耍 (性子)","examples":["I used to get very upset and scream and swear, throwing tantrums all over the place. 我以前經常很不開心，喊叫罵人，到處亂發脾氣。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If something such as a remark or an experience <b>throws</b> you, it surprises you or confuses you because it is unexpected. 使吃驚; 使困惑","examples":["Her sudden change in attitude threw me. 她態度上的突然變化令我吃驚。","This new confession threw me for a loop. 這份新口供使我很震驚。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>throw</b> a punch, you punch someone. 打 (一拳)","examples":["Everything was fine until someone threw a punch. 一切都還好，直到有人動了拳頭。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"When someone <b>throws</b> a party, they organize one, usually in their own home. (常指在家) 舉行 (聚會)","examples":["Why not throw a party for your friends? 為何不給你的朋友們搞一個聚會呢？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Throw</b> is also a noun. 投; 扔","examples":["That was a good throw. 那是一次很棒的投擲。","A throw of the dice allows a player to move himself forward. 投擲一次骰子，玩家即可向前移動。"]}]}]},"tie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用線、繩索等）系，扎，捆；將……系在……上，繫牢；打結；使相聯絡；束縛；（比賽中）打成平局；用系材（或橫杆）連線；用連結線連線（音符）；連音演奏（兩個音符）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"領帶，領結；（綁紮東西用的）帶子，繩子；紐帶，聯絡；束縛；平局；<英>淘汰賽；<美>枕木，軌枕；延音連線線；繫帶鞋；系梁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tie</b> two things <b>together</b> or <b>tie</b> them, you fasten them together with a knot. 系; 把…打成結","examples":["He tied the ends of the plastic bag together. 他把塑膠袋的兩頭系在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tie</b> something or someone in a particular place or position, you put them there and fasten them using rope or string. (用繩索) 捆綁; 固定","examples":["He had tied the dog to one of the trees near the canal. 他已經把狗拴在運河邊的一棵樹上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>tie</b> a piece of string or cloth around something or <b>tie</b> something <b>with</b> a piece of string or cloth, you put the piece of string or cloth around it and fasten the ends together. (用繩子或布條) 捆","examples":["She tied her scarf over her head. 她把圍巾圍在頭上。","Roll the meat and tie it with string. 把肉捲起來用線捆好。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>tie</b> a knot or bow <b>in</b> something or <b>tie</b> something <b>in</b> a knot or bow, you fasten the ends together. 打 (結); 把…打成 (結)","examples":["He took a short length of rope and swiftly tied a slip knot. 他拿了一小段繩子迅速打了個活結。","She tied a knot in a cherry stem. 她在櫻桃梗上打了個結。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>tie</b> something or when something <b>ties</b>, you close or fasten it using a bow or knot. 打結繫牢","examples":["He pulled on his heavy suede shoes and tied the laces. 他穿上那雙厚重的絨面革皮鞋並繫好鞋帶。","...a long white thing around his neck that tied in front in a floppy bow. …一條圍著他脖子、前面打了個蓬鬆蝴蝶結的白色長東西。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If one thing <b>is tied</b> <b>to</b> another or two things <b>are tied</b>, the two things have a close connection or link. 使…緊密聯絡","examples":["Their cancers are not so clearly tied to radiation exposure. 他們的癌症與接觸輻射並沒有太明顯的聯絡。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>are tied</b> <b>to</b> a particular place or situation, you are forced to accept it and cannot change it. 束縛","examples":["They had children and were consequently tied to the school vacations. 他們有幾個孩子，因此被學校假期束縛住了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tie</b> is a long narrow piece of cloth that is worn around the neck under a shirt collar and tied in a knot at the front. Ties are worn mainly by men. 領帶","examples":["Jason had taken off his jacket and loosened his tie. 賈森已經脫下夾克，鬆開了領帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ties</b> are the connections you have with people or a place. 聯絡","examples":["Quebec has always had particularly close ties to France. 魁北克一直都與法國有著特別密切的聯絡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Tie</b> is also a noun. 平局","examples":["The first game ended in a tie. 第一場比賽以平局結束。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In sports, a <b>tie</b> is a match that is part of a competition. The losers leave the competition and the winners go on to the next round. 淘汰賽","examples":["They'll meet the winners of the first round tie. 他們將迎戰第一輪淘汰賽的勝出者。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>tie</b> in a competition or game or if they <b>tie</b> <b>with</b> each other, they have the same number of points or the same degree of success. (在競賽或比賽中) 打成平局","examples":["Ronan Rafferty had tied with Frank Nobilo. 羅南·拉弗蒂與諾比羅打成了平局。"]}]}]},"tool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指手用）工具；（完成工作或達到目標的）工具，手段；受人利用的人，工具；<忌，俚>陰莖；容易被利用（或欺騙）的人，蠢人；（計算機）工具；（書籍裝訂時的）壓印圖案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"驅車兜風，駕車到處跑；（用工具）製作，在（皮革，尤指書籍的皮革封面）上壓印圖案；（為生產而）配置裝置；鑿刻（石頭）；<英，非正式>（尤指為犯罪活動而）武裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tool</b> is any instrument or simple piece of equipment that you hold in your hands and use to do a particular kind of work. For example, spades, hammers, and knives are all tools. 工具","examples":["I find the best tool for the purpose is a pair of shears. 我發現達到這一目的的最好工具是一把大剪刀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to anything that you use for a particular purpose as a particular type of <b>tool</b>. 方法","examples":["Writing is a good tool for expressing feelings. 寫作是表達情感的一種好方法。"]}]}]},"toy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玩具；玩意兒，小擺設；受人控制（或利用）的人，玩物；小型的東西"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"玩具的，和玩具有關的；個頭很小的，小體型品種的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"漫不經心地考慮；調情，調戲；心不在焉地（或緊張地）擺弄；不熱情地（或有節制地）吃（或喝）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toy</b> is an object that children play with, for example, a doll or a model car. 玩具","examples":["He was really too old for children's toys. 他確實過了玩孩子的玩具的年紀了。"]}]}]},"town":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"城鎮，市鎮； （生活、工作或剛提到的）城鎮；（城鎮的）商業區，中心區；全體鎮民，全鎮人；城市生活（與鄉村生活相對）；鎮政府"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>town</b> is a place with streets and buildings, where people live and work. Towns are larger than neighbourhoods and smaller than cities. In informal English, cities are sometimes called towns. 城鎮","examples":["...the northern California town of Albany. …加利福尼亞北部的奧爾巴尼鎮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>the town</b> to refer to the people of a town. (某一城鎮的) 居民","examples":["The town takes immense pride in recent achievements. 鎮上的居民為最近的成就感到無比自豪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>town</b> in order to refer to the town where you live. (自己居住的) 城鎮","examples":["He admits he doesn't even know when his brother is in town. 他承認甚至不知道他的兄弟什麼時候在鎮上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>town</b> in order to refer to the central area of a town where most of the stores and offices are. 市中心","examples":["I walked into town. 我走進了市中心。"]}]}]},"tree":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹（喬木）；樹狀物；樹狀圖，樹形結構；（舊用或複合詞中）木料、木製構件；（Tree，英國人名）特里"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把（動物）趕上樹；使陷入困境"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"爬上樹；逃上樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tree</b> is a tall plant that has a hard trunk, branches, and leaves. 樹","examples":["I planted those apple trees. 我種了那些蘋果樹。"]}]}]},"total":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總的，全部的；完全的，絕對的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"總數達，總計；把……加起來；<美，非正式>徹底毀壞（汽車）；殺死，嚴重傷害（某人）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"總數，合計"}],"sections":[]},"t-shirt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"T恤；短袖汗衫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>T-shirt</b> is a cotton shirt with no collar or buttons. T-shirts usually have short sleeves. T恤衫","examples":[]}]}]},"train":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火車，列車；（行進中的）行列，佇列；隨從，扈從；一系列，一連串（事件或想法）；裙裾，拖裾；（轉動的）輪系，齒輪組；（引爆炸藥用的）導火線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"培訓，訓練；（為準備體育賽事而）操練；鍛鍊，培養（某一素質或能力）；訓（獸）；（尤指用槍、照相機）對準，瞄準；使（植物）朝某方向生長，修整"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>train</b> is a number of containers on wheels which are all connected together and which are pulled by an engine along a railway. Trains carry people and goods from one place to another. 火車","examples":["The train pulled into a station. 那列火車駛入了一個車站。","We can catch the early morning train. 我們能趕上清晨的那班火車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>train</b> <b>of</b> vehicles, people, or animals is a long line of them travelling slowly in the same direction. (行進中的) 佇列","examples":["In the old days this used to be done with a baggage train of camels. 在古時候，這常常由一隊拉行李的駱駝來完成。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>train</b> <b>of</b> thought or a <b>train</b> <b>of</b> events is a connected sequence, in which each thought or event seems to occur naturally or logically as a result of the previous one. (一) 連串 (想法或事件)","examples":["He lost his train of thought for a moment, then recovered it. 他一時斷了思路，接著又重新想起來了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"教練員","examples":["She went to the gym with her personal trainer. 她和她的私人教練一起去了健身房。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"馴獸師","examples":["The horse made a winning start for his new trainer. 這匹馬讓它的新馴馬師旗開得勝。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>trains</b> you <b>to</b> do something, they teach you the skills that you need in order to do it. If you <b>train</b> <b>to</b> do something, you learn the skills that you need in order to do it. 培訓; 接受培訓","examples":["He was training us to be soldiers. 他正把我們訓練成士兵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>train</b> a natural quality or talent that someone has, for example, their voice or musical ability, means to help them to develop it. 開發 (天生的素質或才能)","examples":["I see my degree as something which will train my mind and improve my chances of getting a job. 我把我的學歷視為開發心智、增加就業機會的東西。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>train</b> <b>for</b> a physical activity such as a race or if someone <b>trains</b> you <b>for</b> it, you prepare for it by doing particular physical exercises. (為體育比賽等) 訓練","examples":["Strachan is training for the new season. 斯特羅恩正在為新賽季進行訓練。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an animal or bird <b>is trained</b> <b>to</b> do particular things, it is taught to do them, for example, in order to be able to work for someone or to be a good pet. 訓練 (動物或鳥類)","examples":["Sniffer dogs could be trained to track them down. 可以訓練嗅探犬來追捕他們。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受過培訓的","examples":["Michael is a professionally-trained chef. 邁克爾是受過職業培訓的廚師。"]}]}]},"tuesday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期二"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tuesday</b> is the day after Monday and before Wednesday. 星期二","examples":["He phoned on Tuesday, just before you came. 他星期二打了電話，剛好在你來之前。","Talks are likely to start next Tuesday. 會談可能在下星期二開始。"]}]}]},"trip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指短程往返的）旅行，旅遊；出門，出行；絆倒；<非正式>（吸毒所致的）幻覺，迷幻感受；<美，非正式>讓人開心的奇人，奇妙有趣的經歷；強烈的情感體驗；（賽跑等比賽的）賽程；自我放縱的態度（或行動）；（機器、電路的）開關；<古>輕捷的腳步；<古>錯誤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"絆，絆倒；腳步輕快地走（或跑、跳舞）；（尤指意外地）觸動（開關）；（部分電路）自動斷開；<非正式>（服用毒品後）產生幻覺；（字句）輕鬆自如地吐出；作短程旅行；豎起（帆桁等）；（航海）起（錨）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trip</b> is a journey that you make to a particular place. 旅行","examples":["We're taking a trip to Montana. 我們要去一趟蒙大拿州。","On Thursday we went out on a day trip. 週四我們出去旅行了一天。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trip</b> when you are walking, you knock your foot against something and fall or nearly fall. 絆倒; 絆","examples":["She tripped and fell last night and broke her hip. 她昨晚絆倒了，摔斷了髖關節。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trip up</b> means the same as . 絆倒; 絆","examples":["I tripped up and hurt my foot. 我絆倒了，弄傷了腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Trip up</b> means the same as . 絆倒; 絆 (某人)","examples":["He made a sudden dive for Uncle Jim's legs to try to trip him up. 他突然撲向吉姆大叔的雙腿，試圖把他絆倒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trip</b> someone who is walking or running, you put your foot or something else in front of them, so that they knock their own foot against it and fall or nearly fall. 絆倒; 絆 (某人)","examples":["One guy stuck his foot out and tried to trip me. 有個傢伙伸出他的腳試圖絆倒我。"]}]}]},"time":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（以分鐘、小時、天等計量的）時間；（鐘錶上的）時刻；（世界各地不同的）計時體系；（某事發生或應該發生的）時候；一段時間，某段日子；規定時間，可用時間；時代，時期；時光，歲月；生命（期），期限；次，回；倍（times）；完成（競賽等）的時間；（棒球，美橄）暫停；拍子，節奏；（用於報刊名）時報（the Times）；<英>（酒吧）打烊時間；刑期；服役期；計時工資率；分娩時間；學徒期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……安排時間；把握（擊球、射門等）的時機；為……計時，測定……所需的時間"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"乘以（times）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"定時的，定期的，分期的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Time</b> is what we measure in minutes, hours, days, and years. 時間","examples":["...a two-week period of time. …一段為期兩週的時間。","Time passed, and still Ma did not appear. 時間一點點過去，可是瑪還沒有出現。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> to ask or talk about a specific point in the day, which can be stated in hours and minutes and is shown on clocks. 鐘點","examples":["\"What time is it?\"—\"Eight o'clock.\" “幾點了？”—“8點。”","He asked me the time. 他問了我時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>time</b> when something happens is the point in the day when it happens or is supposed to happen. (某事發生的) 時間","examples":["Departure times are 08:15 from Baltimore, and 10:15 from Newark. 從巴爾的摩的出發時間是08:15，從紐瓦克的出發時間是10:15。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> to refer to the system of expressing time and counting hours that is used in a particular part of the world. (世界某時區的) 時間","examples":["The incident happened just after ten o'clock local time. 該事件發生在當地時間剛過10點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> to refer to the period that you spend doing something or when something has been happening. 時間 (段)","examples":["Adam spent a lot of time in his grandfather's office. 亞當在他祖父的辦公室裡度過了很多時間。","He wouldn't have the time or money to take care of me. 他不會有時間，也沒有錢來照看我。","Listen to me, I haven't got much time. 聽我說，我沒有多少時間。","It's obvious that you need more time to think. 顯然你需要更多的時間來思考。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something has been happening for <b>a time</b>, you mean that it has been happening for a fairly long period of time. (相當長的) 一段時間","examples":["He was also for a time an art critic. 他曾有相當長的一段時間是一位藝術評論家。","He stayed for quite a time. 他呆了很長一段時間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> to refer to a period of time or a point in time, when you are describing what is happening then. For example, if something happened <b>at</b> a particular <b>time</b>, that is when it happened. If it happens <b>at all times</b>, it always happens. (某事發生的) 時期; 時刻","examples":["We were in the same college, which was male-only at that time. 我們當時在同一所學院，那時還是男子學院。","By this time he was thirty. 到這時他30歲了。","It was a time of terrible uncertainty. 那是一段非常不確定的時期。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> or <b>times</b> to talk about a particular period in history or in your life. (歷史上或一生中的特殊) 時期","examples":["They were hard times and his parents had been struggling to raise their family. 那是困難時期，他的父母一直掙扎著養家餬口。","We'll be alone together, just like old times. 我們會單獨在一起，就像過去一樣。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>the times</b> to refer to the present time and to modern fashions, tastes, and developments. For example, if you say that someone <b>keeps up with the times</b>, you mean they are fashionable or aware of modern developments. If you say they are <b>behind the times</b>, you mean they are unfashionable or not aware of them. 時代潮流","examples":["This approach is now seriously out of step with the times. 這種方法如今與時代潮流嚴重脫節。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When you describe the <b>time</b> that you had on a particular occasion or during a particular part of your life, you are describing the sort of experience that you had then. (經歷的) 一段時光","examples":["Sarah and I had a great time while the kids were away. 薩拉和我在孩子們不在時度過了一段美好的時光。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Your <b>time</b> is the amount of time that you have to live, or to do a particular thing. 生命期; 期限","examples":["Now that Martin has begun to suffer the effects of AIDS, he says his time is running out. 馬丁已開始遭受艾滋病的折磨，他說自己時日不多了。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you say it is <b>time</b> <b>for</b> something, <b>time</b> <b>to</b> do something, or <b>time</b> you did something, you mean that this thing ought to happen or be done now. (該做某事的) 合適時候","examples":["Opinion polls indicated a feeling among the public that it was time for a change. 民意測驗表明，公眾覺得該是改變的時候了。","It was time for him to go to work. 該是他去上班的時間了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"When you talk about a <b>time</b> when something happens, you are referring to a specific occasion when it happens. 次","examples":["Every time she travels on the bus it's delayed by at least three hours. 每次她坐公共汽車出行時，至少要耽擱3個小時。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>time</b> after numbers to say how often something happens. (表示頻率) 次","examples":["It was her job to make tea three times a day. 她的任務是每天泡3次茶。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>times</b> after numbers when comparing one thing to another and saying, for example, how much bigger, smaller, better, or worse it is. 倍","examples":["Its profits are rising four times faster than the average company. 其利潤正以快於一般公司4倍的速度增長。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"Someone's <b>time</b> in a race is the amount of time it takes them to finish the race. 時間 (完成賽跑所用的)","examples":["He was over a second faster than his previous best time. 他比自己以前的最好成績快了一秒多。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>times</b> to show multiplication. Three times five is 3x5. 乘","examples":["Four times six is 24. 4乘以6等於24。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>time</b> something <b>for</b> a particular hour, day, or period, you plan or decide to do it or cause it to happen at this time. 為…安排時間","examples":["He timed the election to coincide with new measures to boost the economy. 他把選舉的時間安排在振興經濟的新措施出臺的時候。","I timed our visit for March 7. 我把我們訪問時間定在3月7日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>time</b> an action or activity, you measure how long someone takes to do it or how long it lasts. 測量…所花的時間","examples":["A radar gun timed the speed of the baseball. 一支雷達槍測出了棒球的速度。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say it is <b>about time</b> that something was done, you are saying in an emphatic way that it should happen or be done now, and really should have happened or been done sooner. 該是…的時候了","examples":["It's about time a few movie makers with original ideas were given a chance. 該是給一些有創意的電影製作者一個機會的時候了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>ahead of time</b>, you do it before a particular event or before you need to, in order to be well prepared. 提前","examples":["Find out ahead of time what regulations apply to your situation. 提前弄清楚什麼規定適合你的情況。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>ahead of</b> their <b>time</b> or <b>before</b> their <b>time</b>, they have new ideas a long time before other people start to think in the same way. 思想先進","examples":["He was indeed ahead of his time in employing women, ex-convicts, and the handicapped. 他的確思想先進，僱用了女性、刑滿釋放犯和殘疾人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something happens or is done <b>all the time</b>, it happens or is done continually. 一直","examples":["We can't be together all the time. 我們不能一直在一起。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>at a time</b> after an amount to say how many things or how much of something is involved in one action, place, or group. 一次","examples":["Beat in the eggs, one at a time. 把這些雞蛋打破，一次一個。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something could happen <b>at any time</b>, it is possible that it will happen very soon, though nobody can predict exactly when. 在任何時候","examples":["Conditions are still very tense and the fighting could escalate at any time. 形勢依然很緊張，戰鬥隨時可能升級。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something was the case <b>at one time</b>, you mean that it was the case during a particular period in the past. 曾經","examples":["At one time 400 men, women and children lived in the village. 曾一度有400個男人、女人和兒童住在這個村子。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If two or more things exist, happen, or are true <b>at the same time</b>, they exist, happen, or are true together although they seem to contradict each other. 同時","examples":["I was afraid of her, but at the same time I really liked her. 我害怕她，但同時我又實在喜歡她。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>At the same time</b> is used to introduce a statement that slightly changes or contradicts the previous statement. 然而","examples":["I don't think I set out to come up with a different sound for each CD. At the same time, I do have a sense of what is right for the moment. 我想我一開始就沒打算為每張CD設計不同的聲音。然而，我確實能感覺到目前什麼是對的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>at times</b> to say that something happens or is true on some occasions or at some moments. 有時","examples":["The debate was highly emotional at times. 辯論有時非常情緒化。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that something will be the case <b>for all time</b>, you mean that it will always be the case. 永遠","examples":["He promised to love her for all time. 他許諾要永遠愛她。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something is the case or will happen <b>for the time being</b>, it is the case or will happen now, but only until something else becomes possible or happens. 目前","examples":["For the time being, however, immunotherapy is still in its experimental stages. 然而，目前免疫療法還處於試驗階段。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you do something <b>from time to time</b>, you do it occasionally but not regularly. 不時地","examples":["Her daughters visited him from time to time when he was bedridden. 他臥床不起時她的女兒們不時地來探望他。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you say that something is the case <b>half the time</b> you mean that it often is the case. 經常","examples":["Half the time, I don't have the slightest idea what he's talking about. 我常常對他所談論的沒有一丁點兒概念。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you are <b>in time</b> <b>for</b> a particular event, you are not too late for it. 及時","examples":["I arrived just in time for my flight to Hawaii. 我正好及時趕上飛往夏威夷的航班。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>in time</b> or <b>given time</b>, you mean that it will happen eventually, when a lot of time has passed. 遲早","examples":["He would sort out his own problems, in time. 他遲早會解決自己的問題。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you are playing, singing, or dancing <b>in time</b> with a piece of music, you are following the rhythm and speed of the music correctly. If you are <b>out of time</b> with it, you are not following the rhythm and speed of the music correctly. (演奏、唱歌或跳舞) 合拍/不合拍","examples":["Her body swayed in time with the music. 她的身體隨著音樂節拍搖擺。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you say that something will happen, for example, <b>in</b> a week<b>'s time</b> or <b>in</b> two years<b>' time</b>, you mean that it will happen a week from now or two years from now. 在 (幾分鐘、幾天、幾周等) 之後","examples":["Presidential elections are due to be held in ten days' time. 總統競選將在10天后如期舉行。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you arrive somewhere <b>in good time</b>, you arrive early so that there is time to spare before a particular event. 提早","examples":["We got there in good time for the opening ceremony. 我們提早到了那兒參加開幕式。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If something happens <b>in no time</b> or <b>in next to no time</b>, it happens almost immediately or very quickly. 立刻; 很快","examples":["He's going to be just fine. At his age he'll heal in no time. 他會好起來的。以他的年紀，會很快痊癒。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you <b>keep time</b> when playing or singing music, you follow or play the beat, without going too fast or too slowly. 按節拍","examples":["As he sang he kept time on a small drum. 他唱歌時和著一面小鼓的節拍。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"When you talk about how well a watch or clock <b>keeps time</b>, you are talking about how accurately it measures time. (鐘錶) 走得準","examples":["Some pulsars keep time better than the Earth's most accurate clocks. 有些脈衝星表比地球上最精確的時鐘還準。"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"If you <b>make time</b> <b>for</b> a particular activity or person, you arrange to have some free time so that you can do the activity or spend time with the person. 騰出時間","examples":["Before leaving the city, be sure to make time for a shopping trip. 在離開這個城市前，一定要騰出時間購一次物。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If you say that you <b>made good time</b> on a trip, you mean it did not take you very long compared to the length of time you expected it to take. (旅途耗時) 比預計時間少","examples":["They had left early in the morning, on quiet roads, and made good time. 他們一大早就出發了，路上行人稀少，所以旅途花的時間比預期要少。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If someone <b>is</b> <b>making up for lost time</b>, they are doing something actively and with enthusiasm because they have not had the opportunity to do it before or when they were younger. 彌補失去的時光","examples":["Five years older than the majority of officers of his same rank, he was determined to make up for lost time. 他比同級別的大多數官員大5歲，他決心彌補自己失去的時光。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"If you say that something happens or is the case <b>nine times out of ten</b> or <b>ninety-nine times out of a hundred</b>, you mean that it happens on nearly every occasion or is almost always the case. 十之八九","examples":["When they want something, nine times out of ten they get it. 當他們想要什麼時，十之八九都能得到。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is, for example, the best writer <b>of all time</b>, or the most successful movie <b>of all time</b>, you mean that they are the best or most successful that there has ever been. 有史以來的","examples":["\"Monopoly\" is one of the best-selling games of all time. “大富翁”是有史以來最暢銷的遊戲之一。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"If you are <b>on time</b>, you are not late. 準時","examples":["Don't worry, she'll be on time. 別擔心，她會準時的。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>only a matter of time</b> or <b>only a question of time</b> before something happens, you mean that it cannot be avoided and will definitely happen at some future date. 只是時間問題","examples":["It now seems only a matter of time before they resign. 如今看來，他們辭職只是個時間問題。"]},{"num":"30.","zh":"If you do something to <b>pass the time</b> you do it because you have some time available and not because you really want to do it. 消磨時間","examples":["Without particular interest and just to pass the time, I read a story. 沒有特別的興趣，只是為了消磨時間，我才讀了一篇故事。"]},{"num":"31.","zh":"If you say that something will <b>take time</b>, you mean that it will take a long time. 需要很長時間","examples":["Change will come, but it will take time. 變化會有的，但需要很長時間。"]},{"num":"32.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> your <b>time</b> doing something, you do it slowly and do not hurry. 慢慢地; 不著急","examples":["\"Take your time,\" Ted told him. \"I'm in no hurry.\" “慢慢來，”泰德告訴他說，“我不著急。”"]},{"num":"33.","zh":"If a child can <b>tell the time</b>, they are able to find out what the time is by looking at a clock or watch. 認時間","examples":["My four-year-old daughter cannot quite tell the time. 我4歲的女兒不太會看時間。"]},{"num":"34.","zh":"If something happens <b>time after time</b>, it happens in a similar way on many occasions. 屢次","examples":["Burns had escaped from jail time after time. 伯恩斯屢次越獄逃跑。"]},{"num":"35.","zh":"If you say that <b>time flies</b>, you mean that it seems to pass very quickly. 時光飛逝","examples":["Time flies when you're having fun. 當你開心的時候，時光飛逝。"]},{"num":"36.","zh":"If you say there is <b>no time to lose</b> or <b>no time to be lost</b>, you mean you must hurry as fast as you can to do something. 必須儘快","examples":["He rushed home, realizing there was no time to lose. 他意識到時間緊迫，急忙趕回家去。"]},{"num":"37.","zh":"If you say that <b>time will tell</b> whether something is true or correct, you mean that it will not be known until some time in the future whether it is true or correct. 時間會證明","examples":["Only time will tell whether Broughton's optimism is justified. 只有時間能證明布勞頓的樂觀有沒有道理。"]},{"num":"38.","zh":"If you <b>waste no time</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you take the opportunity to do it immediately or quickly. 立即","examples":["Tom wasted no time in telling me why he had come. 湯姆立即告訴我他來的原因。"]}]}]},"top":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頂部，頂端，上端；上層表面；最高的級別，最重要的職位；盡頭，遠端；帽，蓋，塞；上衣，上裝；（根菜作物的）莖葉；陀螺；<非正式>特別好的人（或事）（tops）；<英>（用於款額後）最高額（tops）；開始，開端；（棒球比賽的）前半局；（球的）上旋（topspin 的簡稱）；（待紡的）毛條；（物理）夸克六味之一；用於馬蹄螺的名字"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"頂端的，頂部的，最上面的；（地位、程度或重要性）最高的；<英，非正式>很好的，頂呱呱的；<英>（距說話者、參照點）最遠的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"高於，超過，高過；優於，勝過；居……之首，為……之冠；覆蓋，放在……的上面；到達山頂，達到頂端；<英，非正式>殺；切除頂部；（作為主要表演者，受關注者而）出場，露面；（高爾夫）誤擊（球上部）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>最多，至多（tops）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>top</b> of something is its highest point or part. 頂端","examples":["I waited at the top of the stairs. 我在樓梯頂端上等著。","...the picture at the top of the page. …頁端的圖片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>top</b> of something such as a bottle, jar, or tube is a cap, lid, or other device that fits or screws onto one end of it. (瓶、罐或軟管等的) 蓋子","examples":["...the plastic tops from soda bottles. …汽水瓶的塑膠蓋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>top</b> of a street, garden, bed, or table is the end of it that is farthest away from where you usually enter it or from where you are. 盡頭","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>top</b> is a piece of clothing that you wear on the upper half of your body, for example, a blouse or shirt. 上衣","examples":["Look at my new top. 看看我的新上衣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a toy that is spun on its pointed base by a flick of the fingers, by pushing a handle at the top up and down, etc 陀螺","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>top</b> of an organization or career structure is the highest level in it. 最高層","examples":["We started from the bottom and we had to work our way up to the top. 我們從最底層做起，必須奮鬥到最高層。","...his dramatic rise to the top of the military hierarchy. …他戲劇性地晉升到軍隊的最高層。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone is <b>at the top</b> <b>of</b>, for example, a table or league or is <b>the top</b> <b>of</b> the table or league, their performance is better than that of all the other people involved. 首位","examples":["...the golfer at the top of the leaderboard. …居積分榜首位的高爾夫球選手。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Top</b> is also an adjective. 頂端的","examples":["...the top corner of the newspaper. …報紙頂端的一角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>top</b> thing or layer in a series of things or layers is the highest one. 最上面的","examples":["I can't reach the top shelf. 我夠不著最上面的架子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>top</b> to indicate that something or someone is at the highest level of a scale or measurement. 最高的; 最快的","examples":["The vehicles have a top speed of 80 miles per hour. 這些車的最高時速達80英里。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Top</b> is also an adjective. 最高層的","examples":["I need to have the top people in this company pull together. 我需要把這家公司最高層的人員團結在一起。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>top</b> to describe the most important or famous people or things in a particular area of work or activity. 最重要的; 最著名的","examples":["So you want to be a top model. 如此說來，你想成為一名頂級名模。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Top</b> is also an adjective. 居首位的","examples":["He was the top student in physics. 他是物理學尖子生。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>top</b> to indicate that something is the first thing you are going to do, because you consider it to be the most important. 最重要的","examples":["Cleaning up the water supply is their top priority. 清洗供水系統是他們的首要任務。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You can use <b>top</b> to indicate that someone does a particular thing more times than anyone else or that something is chosen more times than anything else. 居首位的","examples":["Jamillah Lang was Colorado's top scorer. 賈米拉·蘭是科羅拉多州得分最多的球員。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>top</b> a list means to be mentioned or chosen more times than anyone or anything else. 位居…榜首","examples":["It was the first time in years that a Japanese manufacturer had not topped the list for imported vehicles. 這是多年來日本廠商第一次未能位居進口汽車名單榜首。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to remove the top of or from 去掉...頂部; 從...頂部去掉","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to exceed or surpass 超過","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"to kill 殺死","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"to form a top on (something) 在(某物)上面形成頂部","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you clean or examine something <b>from top to bottom</b>, you are emphasizing that you do it completely and thoroughly. 徹底地","examples":["She would clean the house from top to bottom. 她會徹底地打掃房子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>from top to toe</b> to emphasize that the whole of someone's body is covered or dressed in a particular thing or type of clothing. 從頭到腳","examples":["They were sensibly dressed from top to toe in rain gear. 他們非常明智，從頭到腳裹著雨具。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>gets on top of</b> you, it makes you feel unhappy or depressed because it is very difficult or worrying, or because it involves more work than you can manage. 使沮喪","examples":["Things have been getting on top of me lately. 事情最近太多，令我很沮喪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are on top of</b> or <b>get on top of</b> something that you are doing, you are dealing with it successfully. 成功處理","examples":["...the government's inability to get on top of the situation. …政府無力處理這種局面。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say something <b>off the top of</b> your <b>head</b>, you say it without thinking about it much before you speak, especially because you do not have enough time. 不假思索地","examples":["It was the best I could think of off the top of my head. 這是我能馬上想出的最好辦法。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If one thing is <b>on top</b> of another, it is placed over it or on its highest part. 在上面","examples":["He was sound asleep on top of the covers. 他在床單上睡得很香。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>on top</b> or <b>on top of</b> to indicate that a particular problem exists in addition to a number of other problems. 另外","examples":["A stepfamily faces all the problems that a normal family has, with a set of additional problems on top. 再婚家庭會面臨正常家庭的所有問題，另外還有一系列其他問題。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You say that someone is <b>on top</b> when they have reached the most important position in an organization or business. 處於顯要職位","examples":["In such a fast-changing business, it's hard to stay on top. 在一個變化如此迅速的行業裡，要保持顯要地位很難。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that you feel <b>on top of the world</b>, you are emphasizing that you feel extremely happy and healthy. 極其幸福","examples":["Two months before she gave birth to Jason she left work feeling on top of the world. 在生下賈森的兩個月前，她辭去了工作，感到極其幸福。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone pays <b>top dollar</b> for something, they pay the highest possible price for it. 最高價格","examples":["People will always pay top dollar for something exclusive. 人們總願意為奢侈品付最高價。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If one thing is <b>over the top</b> of another, it is placed over it so that it is completely covering it. 蓋上","examples":["I placed a sheet of plastic over the top of the container. 我在容器的上面蓋了一層塑膠紙。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You describe something as <b>over the top</b> when you think that it is exaggerated, and therefore unacceptable. 誇張的","examples":["The special effects are a bit over the top but I enjoyed it. 特技效果有點誇張，不過我很欣賞。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say something <b>at the top of</b> your <b>voice</b>, you say it very loudly. 聲嘶力竭地","examples":["\"Stephen, come back!\" shouted Marcia at the top of her voice. “斯蒂芬，回來！”馬西婭聲嘶力竭地喊道。"]}]}]},"twelve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十二，十二個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十二，十二個；十二點（可指正午或午夜）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十二的，十二個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twelve</b> is the number 12. 12","examples":[]}]}]},"touch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"觸控，碰；接觸，觸及；損壞，傷害；吃，喝，使用；感動，觸動；影響，與……有關；與……媲美，比得上；達到（某一水平等）；參與，涉及；處理，做（某事）；（在臉上）閃現，掠過；輕輕擊（球）；具有……特性；<非正式>向（某人）討要（物品）；跑壘得分；（幾何）與（曲線，表面）切觸；（用畫筆、鉛筆）輕輕勾勒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"觸覺，觸感；觸控，碰；觸控時的感覺；潤色，裝點；作風，風格，手法；一點兒，少許；略微，稍微；邊線以外的區域；觸球，控球；（音樂家的）觸鍵法，彈奏法；（樂器鍵、弦的）彈性，彈力；（鋼筆、鉛筆等的）輕觸；轉調較少的鐘樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>touch</b> something, you put your hand onto it in order to feel it or to make contact with it. 觸控; 碰","examples":["Her tiny hands gently touched my face. 她的小手輕輕地觸控我的臉。","Don't touch! 請勿觸控！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>touch</b> something means to strike it, usually quite gently. 輕擊","examples":["He scored the first time he touched the ball. 他第一次擊球就得了分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>has</b> not <b>been touched</b>, nobody has dealt with it or taken care of it. 處理; 照管","examples":["When John began to restore the house in the 1960s, nothing had been touched for 40 years. 約翰在20世紀60年代開始重修這座房子時，它已經40年沒有任何照管了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you did not <b>touch</b> someone or something, you are emphasizing that you did not attack, harm or destroy them, especially when you have been accused of doing so. 碰 (指攻擊、傷害、破壞等)","examples":["Pearce remained adamant, saying \"I didn't touch him.\" 皮爾斯還是毫不動搖，說：“我沒碰他。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say that you never <b>touch</b> something or that you have not <b>touched</b> something for a long time to emphasize that you never use it, or you have not used it for a long time. 碰 (指使用)","examples":["He doesn't drink much and doesn't touch drugs. 他酒喝得不多，而且不碰毒品。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>touches</b> you, it affects you in some way for a short time. 影響到","examples":["...a guilt that in some sense touches everyone. …在某種意義上影響到每個人的內疚感。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something that someone says or does <b>touches</b> you, it affects you emotionally, often because you see that they are suffering a lot or that they are being very kind. 感動","examples":["It has touched me deeply to see how these people live. 我看到這些人如何生活而深受感動。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Touch</b> is also a noun. 觸控; 接觸","examples":["Sometimes even a light touch on the face is enough to trigger off this pain. 有時甚至在臉上輕摸一下也足以引發這種痛苦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your sense of <b>touch</b> is your ability to tell what something is like when you feel it with your hands. 觸覺","examples":["The evidence suggests that our sense of touch is programmed to diminish with age. 該證據表明我們的觸覺會隨著年齡的增長而逐漸變弱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>touch</b> is a detail which is added to something to improve it. 點睛之筆","examples":["They called the event \"a tribute to heroes,\" which was a nice touch. 他們把這次活動稱為“向英雄致敬”，這是個點睛妙筆。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone has a particular kind of <b>touch</b>, they have a particular way of doing something. 風格","examples":["The dishes he produces all have a personal touch. 他做的菜都具有一種個人的風格。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two things <b>are touching</b>, or if one thing <b>touches</b> another, or if you <b>touch</b> two things, their surfaces come into contact with each other. 相碰","examples":["Their knees were touching. 他們的膝蓋相碰。","A cyclist crashed when he touched wheels with another rider. 一名騎車人同另一名騎車人車輪相碰而摔倒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>touch on</b> a particular subject or problem, you mention it or write briefly about it. 觸及","examples":["The film touches on these issues, but only superficially. 這部電影觸及了這些問題，但很膚淺。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受感動的","examples":["I was touched to find that he regards me as engaging. 讓我感動的是，他認為我很有魅力。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A touch of</b> something is a very small amount of it. 一點","examples":["She thought she just had a touch of the flu. 她覺得她只是有一點感冒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at the touch of</b> in expressions such as <b>at the touch of a button</b> and <b>at the touch of a key</b> to indicate that something is possible by simply touching a switch or one of the keys of a keyboard. 一按","examples":["Staff will be able to trace calls at the touch of a button. 員工只要一按按鈕就可以追蹤電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you get <b>in touch</b> <b>with</b> someone, you contact them by writing to them or telephoning them. If you are, keep, or stay <b>in touch</b> <b>with</b> them, you write, phone, or visit each other regularly. 聯絡","examples":["I will get in touch with my lawyer about this. 我會就此與我的律師聯絡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>in touch</b> <b>with</b> a subject or situation, or if someone keeps you <b>in touch</b> <b>with</b> it, you know the latest news or information about it. If you are <b>out of touch</b> <b>with</b> it, you do not know the latest news or information about it. 瞭解/不瞭解","examples":["...keeping the unemployed in touch with the job market. …讓那些沒有工作的人瞭解就業市場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>lose touch</b> <b>with</b> someone, you gradually stop writing, telephoning, or visiting them. 失去聯絡","examples":["In my job one tends to lose touch with friends. 從事我這種工作的人往往會與朋友們失去聯絡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>lose touch</b> <b>with</b> something, you no longer have the latest news or information about it. 不再瞭解","examples":["Their leaders have lost touch with what is happening in the country. 他們的領導人已不再瞭解國內正發生的事情。"]}]}]},"trouble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"困難，難題，苦惱；險境，困境；費事，不便；問題，麻煩，缺陷；（機器、車輛或系統的）故障，毛病；動盪，騷亂；疾病，疼痛；需勞神費力的人（或動物）；內戰，動亂時期（the Troubles）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使憂慮，苦惱；費神，費力；勞駕，麻煩；給……造成麻煩（困難）；折磨，使疼痛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to problems or difficulties as <b>trouble</b>. 麻煩; 困難","examples":["I had trouble parking. 我停車有困難。","You've caused us a lot of trouble. 你已經給我們造成了很多麻煩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one aspect of a situation is <b>the</b> <b>trouble</b>, you mean that it is the aspect which is causing problems or making the situation unsatisfactory. 問題 (指引起麻煩的事情)","examples":["The trouble is that these restrictions have remained while other things have changed. 問題是，雖然其他事情已經改變，這些限制卻依舊存在。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>troubles</b> are the things that you are worried about. 煩惱","examples":["She tells me her troubles. I tell her mine. 她告訴了我她的煩惱，我也把我的告訴了她。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have kidney <b>trouble</b> or back <b>trouble</b>, for example, there is something wrong with your kidneys or your back. 疾病","examples":["An old bed is the most likely cause of back trouble. 舊床最有可能導致背部疾病。","Her husband had never before had any heart trouble. 她丈夫以前從未得過任何心臟疾病。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If there is <b>trouble</b> somewhere, especially in a public place, there is fighting or rioting there. 騷亂","examples":["Riot police are being deployed throughout the city to prevent any trouble. 防暴警察正部署至全城以防止騷亂。","Fans who make trouble during the World Cup will be arrested. 在世界盃期間搗亂的球迷將被逮捕。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you tell someone that it is <b>no</b> <b>trouble</b> to do something for them, you are saying politely that you can or will do it, because it is easy or convenient for you. 麻煩","examples":["It's no trouble at all; on the contrary, it will be a great pleasure to help you. 這根本不麻煩。相反，我很樂意幫助你。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that a person or animal is <b>no</b> <b>trouble</b>, you mean that they are very easy to look after. 令人操心的人 (或動物)","examples":["My little grandson is no trouble at all, but his 6-year-old sister is a handful. 我的小孫子一點不用人操心，但他6歲的姐姐卻很難管教。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>troubles</b> you, it makes you feel worried. 使煩惱","examples":["Is anything troubling you? 有什麼事使你煩惱嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>troubles</b> you, it causes you physical pain or discomfort. 使疼痛; 使不適","examples":["The ulcer had been troubling her for several years. 潰瘍已經摺磨她好幾年了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone does <b>not</b> <b>trouble</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are critical of them because they do not do something that they should, and you think that this would require very little effort. 費力","examples":["He burps, not troubling to cover his mouth. 他打嗝連嘴巴都懶得捂住。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>trouble</b> in expressions such as <b>I'm sorry to trouble you</b> when you are apologizing to someone for disturbing them in order to ask them something. 打擾","examples":["I'm sorry to trouble you, but I wondered if by any chance you know where he is. 對不起打擾您了，我想問問您是否碰巧知道他在哪裡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人煩惱的","examples":["But most troubling of all was the simple fact that nobody knew what was going on. 但是最令人煩惱的就是沒人知道正發生什麼事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>in trouble</b>, they are in a situation in which a person in authority is angry with them or is likely to punish them because they have done something wrong. 受訓斥; 惹上麻煩","examples":["He was in trouble with his teachers. 他受到了他的老師們的訓斥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take the trouble</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do something which requires a small amount of additional effort. 費神; 費力","examples":["He did not take the trouble to see the movie before he attacked it. 他在抨擊那部電影前並沒有費心去看看電影。"]}]}]},"uncle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"叔叔，伯父，伯伯，舅父，姑父，姨丈；（對年長男性親屬的稱呼，用於姓名前常大寫）叔叔，伯父，舅舅；（非正式，小孩或年輕人對非親屬年長男性的友好稱呼）叔叔，大叔，伯伯；（Uncle Sam，非正式，多用於美國）山姆大叔（美國或美國政府的綽號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>uncle</b> is the brother of their mother or father, or the husband of their aunt. 舅父; 伯父; 叔父; 姨父; 姑父","examples":["My uncle was the mayor of Memphis. 我叔叔是孟菲斯市市長。","An e-mail from Uncle Fred arrived. 來自弗雷德叔叔的電子郵件到了。"]}]}]},"twenty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"二十"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"二十；二十幾（用複數形式 twenties，指年齡、溫度等二十至二十九之間的數字）；二十年代（the twenties，指二十世紀二十年代）；二十美元紙幣（常作 a twenty）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"二十的，二十個的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twenty</b> is the number 20. 20","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>twenties</b>, you are referring to numbers between 20 and 29. For example, if you are <b>in</b> your <b>twenties</b>, you are aged between 20 and 29. If the temperature is <b>in the twenties</b>, the temperature is between 20 and 29 degrees. 二十幾","examples":["They're both in their twenties and both married with children of their own. 他們倆都二十幾歲了，都已結婚有了自己的孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The twenties</b> is the decade between 1920 and 1929. 20世紀20年代","examples":["It was written in the Twenties, but it still really stands out. 它寫於20世紀20年代，但現在仍很引人注目。"]}]}]},"try":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"試圖，努力；試用，試做，試驗；品嚐；考驗，磨鍊；到（某處）試試，找一找；試著開啟（門、窗等）；審理，審判；用刨子刨平（木頭粗糙面）；加熱以提取（油，脂肪），熬（油）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"試圖，努力；試用，試驗；（橄欖球）持球觸地得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>try</b> to do something, you want to do it, and you take action which you hope will help you to do it. 試圖","examples":["He secretly tried to help her at work. 他試圖悄悄地在工作上幫助她。","Does it annoy you if others don't seem to try hard enough? 如果其他人做得似乎不夠努力，這會使你煩惱嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>try</b> <b>and</b> do something means to try to do it. 設法","examples":["I must try and see him. 我必須設法見到他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>try</b> something new or different, you use it, do it, or experience it in order to discover its qualities or effects. 試用","examples":["It's best not to try a new recipe for the first time on such an important occasion. 在這樣的重要場合，最好不要首次試用新的食譜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>try</b> a particular place or person, you go to that place or person because you think that they may be able to provide you with what you want. 試試 (去某處或找某人)","examples":["Have you tried the local music shops? 你試過當地的音樂商店嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>try</b> a door or window, you try to open it. 試著 (開門、窗)","examples":["Bob tried the door. To his surprise it opened. 鮑勃試著推推門。令他吃驚的是門開了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When a person <b>is tried</b>, he or she has to appear in a law court and is found innocent or guilty after the judge and jury have heard the evidence. When a legal case <b>is tried</b>, it is considered in a court of law. 審訊; 審理","examples":["He suggested that those responsible should be tried for crimes against humanity. 他建議那些責任人應該以反人類罪受審。","Whether he is innocent or guilty is a decision that will be made when the case is tried in court. 他有罪還是無罪要等案子經由法庭審理後才能做出判決。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Try</b> is also a noun. 嘗試","examples":["It wasn't that she'd really expected to get any money out of him; it had just seemed worth a try. 並非是她真的期望從他那裡弄到一些錢；只是似乎值得一試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Try</b> is also a noun. 試用","examples":["If you're still skeptical about exercising, we can only ask you to trust us and give it a try. 如果你仍對鍛鍊持懷疑態度，我們只能請你相信我們，試一試。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the game of rugby, a <b>try</b> is the action of scoring by putting the ball down behind the goal line of the opposing team. (橄欖球運動中在對方球門線後) 帶球觸地得分","examples":["The French, who led 21-3 at half time, scored eight tries. 法國隊在上半場結束時以21比3領先，他們有8次帶球觸地得分。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>try for</b> something, you make an effort to get it or achieve it. 試圖 (獲得)","examples":["My partner and I have been trying for a baby for two years. 我和我的配偶兩年來一直試著生個孩子。"]}]}]},"two":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"二；兩個"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兩個的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"兩個；數字二；兩個一組"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Two</b> is the number 2. 2","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>it takes two</b> or <b>it takes two to tango</b>, you mean that a situation or argument involves two people and they are both therefore responsible for it. 一個巴掌拍不響","examples":["Divorce is never the fault of one partner; it takes two. 離婚從來就不是哪一方的錯；雙方都有責任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put two and two together</b>, you work out the truth about something for yourself, by using the information that is available to you. 根據已知資訊分析","examples":["Putting two and two together, I assume that this was the car he used. 根據所掌握的資訊判斷，我認為這就是他用的那輛車。"]}]}]},"upstairs":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"往樓上，在樓上；腦力上，精神上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"樓上（the upstairs）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"樓上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>upstairs</b> in a building, you go up a staircase toward a higher floor. 往樓上","examples":["He went upstairs and changed into clean clothes. 他上樓換了乾淨的衣裳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>upstairs</b> in a building, they are on a floor that is higher than the ground floor. 在樓上","examples":["The restaurant is upstairs and consists of a large, open room. 餐館在樓上，是一個寬敞的大開間。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>upstairs</b> room or object is situated on a floor of a building that is higher than the ground floor. 樓上的","examples":["Marsani moved into the upstairs apartment. 瑪薩妮搬進了樓上的公寓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The upstairs</b> of a building is the floor or floors that are higher than the ground floor. 一樓以上的樓層","examples":["Together we went through the upstairs. 我們一起走過上面各樓層。"]}]}]},"unit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"單位；一件（商品）；（公寓樓的）單元；部件，元件；（傢俱的）組合件，配件；科，室，部門；班組，小隊；（課本）單元；（計量）單位；個位數；<美>警車；學習量；<英>股份單位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you consider something as a <b>unit</b>, you consider it as a single, complete thing. 單元","examples":["Agriculture was based in the past on the family as a unit. 農業過去以一個家庭單元為基礎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>unit</b> is a group of people who work together at a specific job, often in a particular place. (工作) 單位","examples":["...the environmental research unit. …環境研究單位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>unit</b> is a group within an armed force or police force, whose members fight or work together or carry out a particular task. 分隊","examples":["...a firefighting unit. …一個消防分隊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>unit</b> is a small machine which has a particular function, often part of a larger machine. 部件","examples":["The unit plugs into any TV set. 該部件可接入任何電視機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>unit</b> of measurement is a fixed standard quantity, length, or weight that is used for measuring things. The quart, the inch, and the ounce are all units. (計量用的) 單位","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>unit</b> is one of the parts that a textbook is divided into. (教科書的) 單元","examples":["Unit V of this book explains those errors in detail and shows you ways to correct them. 這本書的第5單元詳細解釋那些錯誤並且教你改正的方法。"]}]}]},"vegetable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蔬菜；植物人；呆板懶散的人；植物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"植物的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vegetables</b> are plants such as cabbages, potatoes, and onions that you can cook and eat. 蔬菜","examples":["A good general diet should include plenty of fresh vegetables. 一份良好的日常飲食應當包括大量的新鮮蔬菜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone refers to a brain-damaged person as a <b>vegetable</b>, they mean that the person cannot move, think, or speak. 植物人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vegetable</b> matter comes from plants. 植物的","examples":["...compounds of animal, vegetable or mineral origin. …來自動物、植物或礦物的化合物。"]}]}]},"visit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"參觀，遊覽；拜訪，作客；瀏覽（網頁）；視察，巡視；找（醫生或律師）諮詢；<美>閒談；（多作聖經用語）（上帝）救助（某人），降臨（某地）；使某人遭受（有害或不快之事）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"參觀，遊覽；拜訪，作客；（政治領導人或公務員的）訪問，視察；（到網站的）訪問；（在賓館或汽車旅館等的）住宿，逗留；就診，諮詢（律師等）；<美，非正式>會面，閒聊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>visit</b> someone, you go to see them and spend time with them. 拜訪","examples":["He wanted to visit his brother in Worcester. 他想去拜訪住在伍斯特的兄弟。","In the evenings, friends would visit. 晚上朋友們會來拜訪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>visit</b> a place, you go there for a short time. 訪問","examples":["He'll be visiting four cities including Cagliari in Sardinia. 他將訪問4座城市，包括撒丁島的卡利亞里。","...a visiting family from Texas. …一個從得克薩斯來訪的家庭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>visit</b> a website, you look at it. 瀏覽","examples":["For details visit our website at www.harpercollins.com. 欲知詳情請瀏覽我們的網站www.harpercollins.com。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>visit</b> a professional person such as a doctor or lawyer, you go and see them in order to get professional advice. If they <b>visit</b> you, they come to see you in order to give you professional advice. 上門諮詢; (專業人士) 上門服務","examples":["If necessary the patient can then visit his doctor for further advice. 如果必要的話，病人可向自己的醫生諮詢以得到更多的建議。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Visit</b> is also a noun. 拜訪","examples":["Helen had recently paid him a visit. 海倫最近拜訪了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Visit</b> is also a noun. 訪問","examples":["...the pope's visit to Canada. …教皇對加拿大的訪問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Visit</b> is also a noun. 諮詢; 上門服務","examples":["You may have regular home visits from a neonatal nurse. 你可以讓育嬰護士定期上門服務。"]}]}]},"use":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"用，使用；使用（詞語）；耗費，消費；利用（他人或某種情形）；服（藥，尤指毒品）；需要；用（名字），自稱；對待；用（洗手間或衛生間）（禮貌說法）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"使用；用途，用法；詞義，說法；使用機會，使用權；（尤指思想，體力）運用能力；耗費，耗用；（經常）服用（毒品）；<法律，史>（尤指受委託代管人的）受益；（教堂，教區）特色禮拜儀式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>use</b> something, you do something with it in order to do a job or to achieve a particular result or effect. 使用","examples":["Trim off the excess pastry using a sharp knife. 用一把鋒利刀削掉過多的油酥麵糰。","The U.S. has used ships to bring most of its heavy material, like tanks, to the region. 美國已用船把坦克等大多數重型物資運到了該地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>use</b> a supply of something, you finish it so that none of it is left. 用光","examples":["You used all the ice cubes and didn't put the ice trays back. 你用光了所有的冰塊，也沒有把冰格盤放回去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>uses</b> drugs, they take drugs regularly, especially illegal ones. 服; 吸食 (藥、毒品)","examples":["He denied he had used drugs. 他否認吸食過毒品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>uses</b> the toilet or bathroom as a polite way of saying that they go to the toilet. 用 (廁所、衛生間)","examples":["Wash your hands after using the bathroom. 如廁後請洗手。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>use</b> a particular word or expression, you say or write it, because it has the meaning that you want to express. 用 (某詞語或表達方式)","examples":["The judge liked using the word \"wicked\" of people he had sent to jail. 那位法官喜歡用“邪惡的”這個詞來形容他判決入獄的人。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>use</b> a particular name, you call yourself by that name, especially when it is not the name that you usually call yourself. 用 (某個名字)","examples":["Now I use a false name if I'm meeting people for the first time. 現在我和素未謀面的人見面都用假名。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>uses</b> people, you disapprove of them because they make others do things for them in order to benefit or gain some advantage from it, and not because they care about the other people. 利用 (人)","examples":["Why do I have the feeling I'm being used again? 為什麼我覺得自己又在被人利用呢？"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Use up</b> means the same as <b>use</b>. 用光","examples":["It isn't animals who use up the world's resources. 不是動物耗盡了世界資源。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>use</b> of something is the action or fact of your using it. 使用","examples":["The treatment does not involve the use of any artificial drugs. 這種療法不涉及任何人造藥物的使用。","...research related to microcomputers and their use in classrooms. …有關微型計算機及其在課堂中的使用的研究。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>a use for</b> something, you need it or can find something to do with it. 用處","examples":["You will no longer have a use for the magazines. 你將不再用得著這些雜誌了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something has a particular <b>use</b>, it is intended for a particular purpose. 用途","examples":["Infrared detectors have many uses. 紅外探測器有多種用途。","It's an interesting scientific phenomenon, but of no practical use whatever. 這是一種有趣的科學現象，但沒有什麼實際用途。","The report outlined possible uses for the new weapon. 該報告勾畫了這種新武器的可能用途。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have the <b>use</b> <b>of</b> something, you have the permission or ability to use it. (對某物的) 使用權; 使用能力","examples":["She will have the use of the car one night a week. 她每週可以有一個晚上使用這輛車。","...young people who at some point in the past have lost the use of their limbs. …在過去某個時刻喪失了肢體使用能力的年輕人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>use</b> of a word is a particular meaning that it has or a particular way in which it can be used. (詞的) 意義; 用法","examples":["There are new uses of words coming in and old uses dying out. 詞語的新用法在湧現，舊用法在消亡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Your <b>use of</b> a particular name is the fact of your calling yourself by it. (某名字的) 使用","examples":["Police have been hampered by Mr. Urquhart's use of bogus names. 厄克特先生使用假名，警察的調查受阻。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>for the use of</b> a particular person or group of people, it is for that person or group to use. 以供 (某人、某些人) 使用","examples":["The facilities are there for the use of guests. 那些設施擺在那兒以供客人們使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that being something or knowing someone <b>has</b> its <b>uses</b>, you mean that it makes it possible for you to do what you otherwise would not be able to do. 有其用途","examples":["It wasn't a life she particularly enjoyed, but it had its uses. 這不是她特別喜歡的一種生活，但有它的用處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a technique, building, or machine is <b>in use</b>, it is used regularly by people. If it has gone <b>out of use</b>, it is no longer used regularly by people. 在用/不再用","examples":["...the methods of making champagne which are still in use today. …今天仍在使用的釀造香檳的方法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>make use of</b> something, you do something with it in order to do a job or achieve a particular result or effect. 利用; 發揮","examples":["Few found jobs in which they could make use of their new skills. 幾乎無人找得到能發揮自己新技能的工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say <b>it's no use</b>, you mean that you have failed to do something and realize that it is useless to continue trying because it is impossible. 沒有用; 不奏效","examples":["It's no use. Let's hang up and try for a better line. 沒用。我們結束通話電話試打更好的線路吧。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>of use</b>, they are useful. If they are <b>no use</b>, they are not at all useful. 有用/無用","examples":["The contents of this booklet should be of use to all students. 這本小冊子的內容應該對所有的學生都有用。"]}]}]},"voice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嗓音，說話聲，歌唱聲；發言權，表達意願的權利；願望，意見，呼聲；（突然閃現的）想法，感覺；代言人，喉舌；（語法）語態；（語音）濁音；（文學作品或作者的）獨特風格；（樂曲）聲部；單音，單聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"表達，吐露（感情或意見）；（語音）發濁音；（樂）給（管風琴）調音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone speaks or sings, you hear their <b>voice</b>. 嗓音","examples":["Miriam's voice was strangely calm. 米里亞姆的聲音出奇地平靜。","\"The police are here,\" she said in a low voice. “警察在這兒，”她低聲說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>voice</b> is their opinion on a particular topic and what they say about it. 意見","examples":["What does one do when a government simply refuses to listen to the voice of the opposition? 當政府完全拒絕傾聽反對意見時，那該怎麼辦？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>voice</b> something such as an opinion or an emotion, you say what you think or feel. 表達","examples":["Some scientists have voiced concern that the disease could be passed on to humans. 一些科學家已經表示，擔心這種疾病可能會傳染給人類。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give voice to</b> an opinion, a need, or a desire, you express it aloud. 大聲表達","examples":["...a community radio run by the Catholic Church that gave voice to the protests of the slum-dwellers. …一家由天主教教會開辦的、表達貧民窟居民抗議之聲的社群電臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone tells you to <b>keep</b> your <b>voice down</b>, they are asking you to speak more quietly. 放低嗓門","examples":["Keep your voice down, for goodness sake. 看在上帝的份上，把你的嗓門放低點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> your <b>voice</b>, you cannot speak for a while because of an illness. 失聲","examples":["I had to be careful not to get a sore throat and lose my voice. 我必須小心，不要患上咽喉炎而啞了嗓子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>raise</b> your <b>voice</b>, you speak more loudly. If you <b>lower</b> your <b>voice</b>, you speak more quietly. 提高嗓門; 壓低嗓門","examples":["He raised his voice for the benefit of the other two women. 他提高了嗓門，以便讓另兩個女人聽得到。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say something <b>at the top of</b> your <b>voice</b>, you say it as loudly as possible. 用最大的音量","examples":["\"Damn!\" he yelled at the top of his voice. “該死！”他聲嘶力竭地喊道。"]}]}]},"view":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀點，看法；（理解或思維的）方法，方式；景象，視野；風景，景色；風景畫，風景照；影象，檢視；（一次）觀看，一睹，一覽；（文字或圖表在計算機螢幕上的）顯示方式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看待，考慮；觀看；檢視，觀察；（在計算機螢幕上）閱讀，看；看見（狐狸）離開隱藏處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>views</b> on something are the beliefs or opinions that you have about it, for example,whether you think it is good, bad, right, or wrong. 觀點","examples":["Washington and Moscow are believed to have similar views on Kashmir. 華盛頓和莫斯科被認為在克什米爾問題上持有相似的觀點。","You should also make your views known to your congressperson. 你們的觀點也應該讓國會議員們知道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>view</b> <b>of</b> a particular subject is the way that you understand and think about it. 看法","examples":["The whole point was to get away from a Christian-centered view of religion. 整個核心問題是要擺脫以基督教為中心的宗教觀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>view</b> from a window or high place is everything that can be seen from that place, especially when it is considered to be beautiful. 景色","examples":["The view from our window was one of beautiful green countryside. 從我們視窗可以看到一片綠色鄉村的美景。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>view</b> <b>of</b> something, you can see it. 看到","examples":["He stood up to get a better view of the blackboard. 他站了起來，以便能更清楚地看黑板。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>view</b> in expressions to do with being able to see something. For example, if something is <b>in view</b>, you can see it. If something is <b>in full view of everyone</b>, everyone can see it. 在視線內","examples":["She was lying there in full view of anyone who walked by. 她躺在那兒，任何路過的人都能看到她。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>View</b> refers to the way in which a piece of text or graphics is displayed on a computer screen. (文字或圖表在計算機螢幕上的) 顯示方式","examples":["To see the current document in full-page view, click the Page Zoom Full button. 要全頁顯示來察看當前檔案，請點選全屏顯示按鈕。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>view</b> something in a particular way, you think of it in that way. 看待","examples":["First-generation Americans view the United States as a land of golden opportunity. 第一代美國人把美國看成一個充滿良機的大陸。","Abigail's mother Linda views her daughter's talent with a mixture of pride and worry. 阿比蓋爾的母親琳達看待女兒的天賦時既驕傲又擔憂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>view</b> something, you look at it for a particular purpose. 察看","examples":["They came back to view the house again. 他們又回來察看了一下房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>view</b> a television programme, video, or movie, you watch it. 觀看","examples":["We have viewed the video recording of the incident. 我們已觀看了該事件的錄影。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in my view</b> when you want to indicate that you are stating a personal opinion, that other people might not agree with. 在我看來","examples":["In my view things won't change. 在我看來形勢不會改變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>in view of</b> when you are taking into consideration facts that have just been mentioned or are just about to be mentioned. 鑑於; 考慮到","examples":["In view of the fact that Hobson was not a trained economist his achievements were remarkable. 鑑於霍布森非科班出身的經濟學家這一事實，他的成就是很了不起的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a work of art is <b>on view</b>, it is shown in public for people to look at. 在展出","examples":["A significant exhibition of contemporary sculpture will be on view at the Portland Gallery. 一場意義重大的當代雕塑展將在波特蘭美術館展出。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>with a view to</b> doing something else, you do it because you hope it will result in that other thing being done. 目的在於","examples":["He has called a meeting of all parties tomorrow, with a view to forming a national reconciliation government. 他已召集各派於明天會談，目的在於組建一個民族和解政府。"]}]}]},"wall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"城牆，圍牆；牆，壁，牆壁；屏障，壁壘；（感情或行為的）障礙，隔閡；人牆，隔離牆；（身體器官或動植物細胞等的）外壁；（盒子或管道等空心物的）內壁；堆得像牆一樣的大量東西；柏林牆（the Wall）；防波堤，防洪堤；（尤指宏大的）峭立面；圍住礦脈（或礦層）的岩石；梅戈拉毛眼蝶（同 wall brown）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用牆圍住（一區域）；砌牆封閉，砌牆堵住（wall sth. up）；把……關起來，禁閉（wall sb./sth. in/up）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"牆壁的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wall</b> is one of the vertical sides of a building or room. 牆; 牆壁","examples":["Kathryn leaned against the wall of the church. 凱瑟琳倚靠在教堂的牆壁上。","The bedroom walls would be papered with chintz. 臥室的牆上將會貼上印花棉布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wall</b> is a long narrow vertical structure made of stone or brick that surrounds or divides an area of land. 圍牆","examples":["He sat on the wall in the sun. 他坐在圍牆上曬太陽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>wall</b> of something that is hollow is its side. (中空物體的) 壁","examples":["He ran his fingers along the inside walls of the box. 他用手摸了摸箱子的內壁。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something or someone <b>is driving</b> you <b>up the wall</b>, you are emphasizing that they annoy and irritate you. 惹惱","examples":["The heat is driving me up the wall. 我熱得快瘋了。"]}]}]},"wait":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"等候；盼望，期待；推遲，延緩；（已備好）可處理，可取用；（用於鼓勵或威脅）等著；（用於打斷講話）等一下，慢著；服侍，招待"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"等待，等候的時間；<史>（城鎮）官方樂隊（waits）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wait</b> for something or someone, you spend some time doing very little, because you cannot act until that thing happens or that person arrives. 等候","examples":["I walk to a street corner and wait for the school bus. 我走到一個街道拐角處等校車。","I waited to see how she responded. 我等著看她如何反應。","We had to wait a week before we got the results. 我們不得不等候一個星期才拿到了結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is waiting</b> <b>for</b> you, it is ready for you to use, have, or do. 等 (你) 使用; 等 (你) 去做","examples":["There'll be a car waiting for you. 將會有輛車等著你。","When we came home we had a meal waiting for us. 我們回到家時，有一頓飯正等著我們去享用。","He had a car waiting to take him back to the office. 有一輛車等著送他回辦公室。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Wait</b> is used in expressions such as <b>wait a minute</b>, <b>wait a second</b>, and <b>wait a moment</b> to interrupt someone when they are speaking, for example, because you object to what they are saying or because you want them to repeat something. 等一下 (用以打斷對方的談話，或要求對方重複); 且慢","examples":["\"Wait a minute!\" he broke in. \"This is not giving her a fair hearing!\" “且慢！”他插話道。“這沒有給她一個公平的辯解機會。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"等候","examples":["The waiting became almost unbearable. 等待變得幾乎令人難以忍受了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wait</b> is a period of time in which you do very little, before something happens or before you can do something. 等待的時間","examples":["...the four-hour wait for the organizers to declare the result. …組織者們宣佈結果前4個小時的等待。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something can <b>wait</b>, you mean that it is not important or urgent and so you will deal with it or do it later. 延緩","examples":["I want to talk to you, but it can wait. 我想和你談談，但可以等會兒再說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>wait</b> when you are trying to make someone feel excited, or to encourage or threaten them. 等著吧 (期望引起對方興奮之情，或鼓勵對方); 等著瞧 (表示威脅)","examples":["If you think this all sounds very exciting, just wait until you read the book. 如果你覺得所有這些聽起來令人興奮，那就等你看了書之後再說吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an employee <b>waits</b> <b>on</b> you, for example, in a restaurant or hotel, they take orders from you and bring you what you want. 服侍; 招待","examples":["There were plenty of servants to wait on her. 有許多傭人服侍她。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>can't wait</b> to do something or <b>can hardly wait</b> to do it, you are emphasizing that you are very excited about it and eager to do it. 急於要 (做某事)","examples":["We can't wait to get started. 我們迫不及待地想要開始了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>wait and see</b>, you tell them that they must be patient or that they must not worry about what is going to happen in the future because they have no control over it. 等著瞧","examples":["We'll have to wait and see what happens. 我們只有等著看將會發生什麼事情。"]}]}]},"up":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向上，由低向高；到樓上；（太陽）升起；在高處；面朝上，面朝天；從地下到表面，向水面；向北方，朝北方；往（較高或較遠的）某處；去，在（更重要的地方，如大城市或大學）；到……的近處，靠近；到前面，朝前面；處於（或進入）直立狀態；起床；用勁地，以較大氣力；（吐）出來；（強度，音量，活動）由弱到強，由低到高，由輕到響；（列表中）處於更高位置，（議程中）處於更重要的位置；（水平、數量或比率）由低到高；高出，多；向較高地位，向更好的狀態；出現，出席；（在品質、知識或成就方面）相等，比得上；一起，聚攏地；緊緊地，牢固地；計劃要，被建議，正被考慮；<非正式>願意做（或參與）；出庭受審的；處於工作（或可用）狀態，進入（可用）狀態；（在討論或思考時）引起某人的注意；靠近（某人）；靠近頂端；做完地，完成地；封閉，關閉；成碎片，分成部分；處於活躍期，進入興奮狀態；公開展示地；停下來；每名隊員，每個隊；（航行）逆風地，逆水地；（舵柄）迎風轉舵；（棒球）在場上擊球；（長髮）向頭上（或腦後）梳理的；徹底地，完全地；（時間）到；（道路）正在整修的；<非正式>（尤指異常或不愉快的事情）發生，出現"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"往較高處，向較高處；沿著……，順著……；近頂端；往（河，溪）上游"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在高處；（向上）開；升於地平線之上；冒出地面，冒出水面；在前方，在前面；起床；上漲； (時間) 到點的；（正在）發生，進行，出現；得分領先於（對手），超前於（對手）；正常執行，正常工作，起作用；（在活動中）輪到某人；高興，興奮；對……瞭如指掌的，熟悉的；（道路）正在修整的；（騎師）騎著馬的；（物理）（夸克的味）帶有+2/3電荷的，上夸克的（質子和中子被認為是由上夸克和下夸克組成）；向上移動的，上行的； （時間）到點的；（時間）終止，結束"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使…更高，提高；舉起，抬起；突然行動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某一階段的）成功，繁榮；<非正式>走運；在增長，在改善中；（人或企業）誠實守法；蒸蒸日上，越來越成功"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於命令士兵或動物）起來！起立！"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing goes <b>up</b> something such as a slope, ladder, or chimney, they move away from the ground or to a higher position. 向上","examples":["They were climbing up a narrow mountain road. 他們正爬上一條狹窄的山路。","I ran up the stairs and saw Alison lying at the top. 我跑上樓梯，看見艾莉森躺在頂上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>up</b> something such as a ladder or a mountain, they are near the top of it. 靠近…頂端","examples":["He was up a ladder sawing off the tops of his apple trees. 他在梯子上鋸蘋果樹的樹冠。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you go or look <b>up</b> something such as a road or river, you go or look along it. If you are <b>up</b> a road or river, you are somewhere along it. 沿著","examples":["A line of tanks came up the road from the city. 一排坦克由市裡沿路開過來了。","We leaned on the wooden rail of the bridge and looked up the river. 我們靠在橋的木欄杆上，沿河望去。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Up</b> is also an adverb. 向上地","examples":["Finally, after an hour, I went up to Jeremy's room. 一個小時後，我終於上樓去了傑里米的房間。","Intense balls of flame rose up into the sky. 炙熱的火球衝上天空。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Up</b> is also an adverb. 靠近頂端","examples":["...a research station perched 4,000 metres up on the lip of the crater. …位於海拔4000米，靠近火山口的一個研究站。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>up</b> to indicate that you are looking or facing in a direction that is away from the ground or toward a higher level. 朝上","examples":["Keep your head up, and look around you from time to time. 抬起頭來,不時地環顧四周。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone stands <b>up</b>, they move so that they are standing. 起來","examples":["He stood up and went to the window. 他站了起來，走向窗戶。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are travelling to a particular place, you can say that you are going <b>up</b> to that place, especially if you are going toward the north or to a higher level of land. If you are already in such a place, you can say that you are <b>up</b> there. 向上 (尤指向北方或向高處); 在 (北方或高處)","examples":["I'll be up to see you tomorrow. 我明天上來看你。","He was living up North. 他當時正住在北方。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you go <b>up</b> to something or someone, you move to the place where they are and stop there. 往","examples":["The girl ran the rest of the way across the street and up to the car. 那個女孩穿過街道，跑完剩下的一段路，來到那輛車旁。","On the way out a boy of about ten came up on roller skates. 在出去的路上，一個大約十歲的男孩穿著旱冰鞋滑了過來。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If an amount of something goes <b>up</b>, it increases. If an amount of something is <b>up</b>, it has increased and is at a higher level than it was. 增多; 上漲","examples":["The total budget went up almost $300 million. 總預算幾乎增加了3億美元。","Tourism is up, jobs are up, individual income is up. 旅遊火了，職位多了，個人收入漲了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>up</b>, you are not in bed. 起床的","examples":["Are you sure you should be up? 你肯定你該起床了嗎?","These days they were up at the crack of dawn. 這些天他們在破曉時就起床。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a period of time is <b>up</b>, it has come to an end. (時間) 到點的","examples":["The moment the half-hour was up, Brooks rose. 半小時一到,布魯克斯就起來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a computer or computer system is <b>up</b>, it is working. Compare <b>down</b>. (計算機或計算機系統) 工作的","examples":["The new system is up and ready to run. 新系統工作了，可以開始執行了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who has been in bed for some time, for example because they have been sick, is <b>up and about</b>, they are now out of bed and living their normal life. 已下床從事正常活動的","examples":["How are you Lennox? Good to see you up and about. 倫諾克斯你好嗎? 真高興看到你恢復正常活動了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that <b>something is up</b>, you mean that something is wrong or that something worrying is happening. 出問題","examples":["What is it then? Something's up, isn't it? 那麼這是怎麼回事？出問題了，是不是？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say to someone \"<b>What's up?</b>\" or if you tell them <b>what's up</b>, you are asking them or telling them what is wrong or what is worrying them. 出了什麼事？","examples":["\"What's up?\" I said to him.—\"Just tired,\" he answered. “出了什麼事？”我對他說。— “只是累了，”他答道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you move <b>up and down</b> somewhere, you move there repeatedly in one direction and then in the opposite direction. 上下地; 來來回回","examples":["I used to jump up and down to keep warm. 我過去常常上下跳動來保暖。","I strolled up and down thoughtfully before calling a taxi. 叫計程車前,我若有所思地來回踱步。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you feel <b>up to</b> doing something, you are well enough to do it. 能勝任","examples":["Those patients who were up to it could move to the adjacent pool. 身體狀況允許的病人可以到旁邊的那個游泳池去。","His fellow directors were not up to running the business without him. 沒有他，其他主管管理不了這家企業。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To be <b>up to</b> something means to be secretly doing something that you should not be doing. 搗鬼","examples":["Why did you need a room unless you were up to something? 除非你要搗什麼鬼，不然為什麼需要一個房間呢？","They must have known what their father was up to. 他們一定已經知道他們的父親在暗地裡做什麼。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>up to</b> someone to do something, you mean that it is their responsibility to do it. 是…的責任","examples":["It was up to him to make it right, no matter how long it took. 不管需要花多長時間，把事情擺平是他的責任。","I'm sure I'd have spotted him if it had been up to me. 要是換了我，我肯定已經認出他了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Up until</b> or <b>up to</b> are used to indicate the latest time at which something can happen, or the end of the period of time that you are referring to. 直至","examples":["Please feel free to call me any time up until 9:30 at night. 晚上9:30之前隨時都可以給我打電話。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>up to</b> to say how large something can be or what level it has reached. 多達; 高達","examples":["Up to twenty thousand students paid between five and six thousand dollars. 多達2萬名學生支付了5000到6000美元。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>up for</b> election, review, or discussion, they are about to be considered. 將被考慮","examples":["A third of the Senate and the entire House are up for re-election. 1/3的參議員和全體眾議員將重新選舉。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you are <b>up for</b> something, you are willing or eager to do it. 願意做; 急於做","examples":["I'm starved. Who's up for pizza? 我快餓死了。誰想吃比薩餅？"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you are <b>up against</b> something, you have a very difficult situation or problem to deal with. 面臨 (困境或困難)","examples":["The chairwoman is up against the greatest challenge to her position. 女主席面臨她職位的最大挑戰。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>up</b> something such as the amount of money you are offering for something, you increase it. 增加; 提高","examples":["He upped his offer for the company. 他提高了對該公司的出價。","Drug stores upped sales by 63 percent. 藥店的銷售額增加了63%。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>up</b> and leave a place, you go away from it, often suddenly or unexpectedly. 突然行動","examples":["One day he just upped and left. 有一天他突然離開了。"]}]}]},"want":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"想要，希望；需要；（用於提出建議）應該；缺少；搜捕，追捕；想見（某人），想與（某人）談話；（用於疑問句中表示提議或邀請）想要，需要；照料，愛護（小孩）；想要進去，想要出去；應受"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺乏，缺少；貧窮，貧困；渴望的東西，需要的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>want</b> something, you feel a desire or a need for it. 想要","examples":["I want a drink. 我想要點喝的。","People wanted to know who this talented designer was. 人們想知道這位天才的設計者是誰。","They began to want their father to be the same as other daddies. 他們開始想要自己的爸爸和別人的爸爸一樣。","They didn't want people staring at them as they sat on the lawn, so they put up high walls. 他們不想自己坐在草坪時被人盯著看，所以修築了高牆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>want</b> <b>to</b> say something to indicate that you are about to say it. 想要 (說)","examples":["I want to say how delighted I am that you're having a baby. 我想要說，你懷孕了我是多麼高興啊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say to someone that you <b>want</b> something, or ask them if they <b>want</b> <b>to</b> do it, you are firmly telling them what you want or what you want them to do. 想要得到; 想做","examples":["I want an explanation from you, Jeremy. 我要你給我一個解釋，傑里米。","Do you want to tell me what all this is about? 你是否想告訴我這究竟是怎麼回事？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone that they <b>want</b> <b>to</b> do a particular thing, you are advising them to do it. 必須","examples":["You want to be very careful not to have a man like Crevecoeur for an enemy. 你必須非常小心，不要與像克雷弗克那樣的人為敵。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>is wanted</b> by the police, the police are searching for them because they are thought to have committed a crime. 通緝","examples":["He was wanted for the murder of a judge. 他因謀殺一位法官而被通緝。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被通緝的","examples":["He is one of the most wanted criminals in Europe. 他是歐洲的頭號通緝犯之一。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>wants</b> are the things that you want. 想要的東西","examples":["She couldn't lift a spoon without a servant anticipating her wants and getting it for her. 若沒有傭人揣摩她想要什麼而且遞給她，她連個湯勺都舉不起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>for want of</b> something else, you do it because the other thing is not available or not possible. 由於缺少","examples":["The factories shut down for want of fuel and materials. 這家工廠由於缺少燃料和原料而停產。"]}]}]},"walk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"走，步行；徒步旅行，散步；陪（某人）走，護送（某人）；帶（寵物）散步，遛；把（某物）移走，使（某物）移動；<非正式>消失，被偷；輕易做成（某事）；<非正式>放棄，突然退出；出現，顯靈；（使）上一壘；被無罪釋放，未獲刑罰；（擊球手不等裁判指示）離開球場；<古>生活"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"步行，散步；徒步旅行；散步的小路，步行的路徑；步態；步行的距離（或時間）；步行速度；（棒球）自由上壘；<英>（護林人的）管轄林區；鬥雞場；<英>小獵犬馴養場；<英>（郵遞員的）投遞路線；<罕>一群沙錐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>walk</b>, you move forward by putting one foot in front of the other in a regular way. 行走; 步行","examples":["Rosanna and Forbes walked in silence. 羅莎娜與福布斯默默地走著。","We walked into the foyer. 我們走進前廳。","I walked a few steps toward the fence. 我向柵欄走了幾步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>walk</b> someone somewhere, you walk there with them in order to show politeness or to make sure that they get there safely. 陪伴護送","examples":["She walked me to my car. 她陪我走到我的汽車旁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>walk</b> is a trip that you make by walking, usually for pleasure. 散步","examples":["I went for a walk. 我去散步了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>walk</b> of a particular distance is the distance that a person has to walk to get somewhere. 步行的距離","examples":["It was only a three-mile walk to Kabul from there. 從那裡到喀布林只有3英里的步行路程。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>walk</b> is a route suitable for walking along for pleasure. (適宜散步的) 人行道","examples":["...a 2-mile coastal walk. …一條2英里長的海邊人行道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>A walk</b> is a paved pathway. 小徑; 走道","examples":["She started up the walk toward the front door. 她踏上了通向前門的小路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>A walk</b> is the action of walking rather than running. 行走","examples":["She slowed to a steady walk. 她慢下來，穩步行走。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Someone's <b>walk</b> is the way that they walk. 步態","examples":["George, despite his great height and gangling walk, was a great dancer. 儘管喬治身材高大，步態笨拙，舞卻跳得好極了。"]}]}]},"warming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加溫，變暖，氣溫升高（常構成 global warming，即全球變暖）；（關係）升溫，緩和；（Warming）（丹、瑞、美）瓦明（人名）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"讓人感到溫暖的，給人溫暖感的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變暖，加溫（常與 up 連用：warming up，預熱、加熱）；（使關係）升溫，變友好；（對某人）產生好感，（對某事）開始感興趣（warm 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>warm</b> has some heat but not enough to be hot. 溫暖的","examples":["Wheat is grown in places which have cold winters and warm, dry summers. 小麥生長在冬季寒冷、夏季溫暖乾燥的地方。","Because it was warm, David wore only a white cotton shirt. 因為天氣暖和，戴維只穿了一件白色棉衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Warm</b> clothes and blankets are made of a material such as wool that protects you from the cold. 保暖的","examples":["They have been forced to sleep in the open without food or warm clothing. 他們被迫睡在露天裡，沒有食物也沒有保暖的衣服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Warm</b> colours have red or yellow in them rather than blue or green, and make you feel comfortable and relaxed. 暖色調的; 有暖感的","examples":["The basement hallway is painted a warm yellow. 地下室的走廊被塗成暖色調的黃色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>warm</b> person is friendly and shows a lot of affection or enthusiasm in their behaviour. 熱心的","examples":["She was a warm and loving mother. 她是位既熱心又慈愛的母親。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"保暖地","examples":["Remember to wrap up warmly on cold days. 記得天冷時穿暖和些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熱情地; 熱烈地","examples":["New members are warmly welcomed. 新成員受到熱烈歡迎。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>warm</b> a part of your body or if something hot <b>warms</b> it, it stops feeling cold and starts to feel hotter. 使…暖和","examples":["The sun had come out to warm his back. 太陽出來了，把他的背曬得暖暖的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>warm to</b> a person or an idea, you become fonder of the person or more interested in the idea. (對某人) 產生好感; (對某事) 開始感興趣","examples":["Those who got to know him better warmed to his openness and honesty. 那些逐漸瞭解了他的人對他的率真與坦誠產生了好感。"]}]}]},"war":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰爭，戰爭狀態；競爭，鬥爭，對抗；（為消滅有害事物的）長期鬥爭，頑強抵禦；舌戰，論戰；軍事，戰術"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進行戰爭，鬥爭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>war</b> is a period of fighting or conflict between countries or states. 戰爭","examples":["He spent part of the war in the National Guard. 他戰時在國民警衛隊服役了一段時間。","...matters of war and peace. …戰爭與和平的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>War</b> is intense economic competition between countries or organizations. 激烈競爭","examples":["The most important thing is to reach an agreement and to avoid a trade war. 最重要的就是達成協議，避免貿易戰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you make <b>war</b> <b>on</b> someone or something that you are opposed to, you do things to stop them from succeeding. 鬥爭","examples":["She has been involved in the war against organized crime. 她參與了打擊有組織犯罪的鬥爭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country <b>goes to war</b>, it starts fighting a war. 開戰","examples":["Do you think this crisis can be settled without going to war? 你認為不發動戰爭就能解決這場危機嗎？"]}]}]},"turn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"旋轉，轉動；轉身，扭轉（身體部位）；翻轉；旋動，擰動；翻動（書頁）；轉向，拐（彎）；（路或河流）轉彎；對準；（潮）漲落；（使）鬆開，釋放；表演，做；（使）扭轉局勢；（使）變成，成為；轉移（思考、處理、觀察等的物件）；求助於，求教於；達到（一定年齡或時間）；（使）反胃，（使）噁心；車削；獲得（利益）；扭傷（腳踝）；造（句），組（詞）；（印刷）倒排，倒空；包抄（敵軍）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"轉動，旋轉；轉向；（道路的）轉彎處；輪到的機會；（情況的）變化，轉變；交替時刻；短小節目；短小節目表演者；散步，轉一圈；（疾病的）一陣發作，不適；（影響他人的）舉止，行為；<非正式>嚇唬，驚嚇；（股票等的）買賣差價；（板球）（球）彈地轉向；（一卷繩子等的）一圈；漲潮或落潮；（樂）迴音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>turn</b> or when you <b>turn</b> part of your body, you move your body or part of your body so that it is facing in a different or opposite direction. 轉動 (身體); 轉身","examples":["He turned abruptly and walked away. 他突然轉身走開了。","He sighed, turning away and surveying the sea. 他嘆了口氣，轉過身去，眺望著大海。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>turn</b> something, you move it so that it is facing in a different or opposite direction, or is in a very different position. 使轉向","examples":["They turned their telescopes toward other nearby galaxies. 他們把望遠鏡轉向附近的其他星系。","She had turned the bedside chair to face the door. 她已經把那張床邊的椅子轉過來對著門。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as a wheel <b>turns</b>, or when you <b>turn</b> it, it continually moves around in a particular direction. 轉動","examples":["As the wheel turned, the potter shaped the clay. 隨著輪子的轉動，製陶工人給黏土塑形。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>turn</b> something such as a key, knob, or switch, or when it <b>turns</b>, you hold it and twist your hand, in order to open something or make it start working. 轉動 (開啟)","examples":["Turn the key three times to the right. 把那鑰匙向右轉3次。","Turn the heat to very low and cook for 20 minutes. 把爐火轉到很低，煮上20分鐘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>turn</b> in a particular direction or <b>turn</b> a corner, you change the direction in which you are moving or travelling. 轉向; 拐彎","examples":["He turned into the narrow street where he lived. 他拐進了他住的那條狹窄的街道。","Now turn right to follow West Ferry Road. 現在向右轉沿著西渡口路走。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>turn</b> a page of a book or magazine, you move it so that it is flat against the previous page, and you can read the next page. 翻動 (書頁)","examples":["He turned the pages of a file in front of him. 他翻著面前的一份檔案。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>turn</b> a weapon or an aggressive feeling <b>on</b> someone, you point it at them or direct it at them. 把 (武器或挑釁的情緒) 指向","examples":["He tried to turn the gun on me. 他試圖把槍對著我。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>turn</b> your attention or thoughts <b>to</b> a particular subject or if you <b>turn to</b> it, you start thinking about it or discussing it. (注意力) 轉向","examples":["We turned our attention to the practical matters relating to forming a company. 我們把注意力轉向了與組建公司有關的實際問題上。","We turn now to our primary question. 我們現在轉到我們的主要問題上。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"To <b>turn</b> or <b>be turned</b> <b>into</b> something means to become that thing. 變成 (某物)","examples":["A prince turns into a frog in this cartoon fairytale. 在這部卡通童話片裡，一位王子變成了一隻青蛙。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a business <b>turns</b> a profit, it earns more money than it spends. 賺取","examples":["The firm will be able to pay off its debts and still turn a modest profit. 該公司將能夠還清其債務，而且還會稍有贏利。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When someone <b>turns</b> a particular age, they pass that age. When it <b>turns</b> a particular time, it passes that time. 達到 (一定的年齡或時間)","examples":["It was his ambition to accumulate a million dollars before he turned thirty. 他的雄心是在30歲以前積攢100萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Turn around</b> means the same as <b>turn</b>. 轉身","examples":["I felt a tapping on my shoulder and I turned around. 我感到有人拍了一下我的肩膀，於是轉過身去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Turn</b> is also a noun. 轉向; 拐彎","examples":["You can't do a right-hand turn here. 你不能在這裡右轉彎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Turn</b> is also a noun. 轉彎","examples":["...a sharp turn in the road. …公路上的一個急轉彎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a situation or trend takes a particular kind of <b>turn</b>, it changes so that it starts developing in a different or opposite way. (情況的) 變化","examples":["The scandal took a new turn over the weekend. 這一醜聞在週末時發生了新的變化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Turn</b> is used in expressions such as <b>the turn of the century</b> and <b>the turn of the year</b> to refer to a period of time when one century or year is ending and the next one is beginning. (世紀或年代的) 交替時期","examples":["They fled to South America around the turn of the century. 他們在世紀之交時逃往南美。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If it is your <b>turn</b> <b>to</b> do something, you now have the duty, chance, or right to do it, when other people have done it before you or will do it after you. (多人依次) 輪到的機會","examples":["Tonight it's my turn to cook. 今晚輪到我做飯。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The point where a road, path, or river <b>turns</b> is the point where it has a bend or curve in it. (路或河流) 轉彎","examples":["...the corner where Tenterfield Road turned into the main road. …坦特菲爾德路轉向主幹道的那個拐角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the tide <b>turns</b>, it starts coming in or going out. (潮水) 漲; 落","examples":["There was not much time before the tide turned. 沒過多少時間就退潮了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>turn to</b> a particular page in a book or magazine, you open it at that page. 翻到 (某頁)","examples":["To order, turn to page 236. 要訂貨，請翻到第236頁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>turn to</b> someone, you ask for their help or advice. 求助於","examples":["For assistance, they turned to one of the city's most innovative museums. 為了尋求幫助，他們求助於該市最具創新精神的博物館中的一座。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>turn</b> <b>to</b> a particular activity, job, or way of doing something, you start doing or using it. 開始做; 開始用","examples":["These communities are now turning to recycling as a cheaper alternative to landfills. 這些社群現正開始用回收這種較為廉價的方法替代廢物填埋法。"]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>turn</b> before an adjective to indicate that something or someone changes by acquiring the quality described by the adjective. 變得 (接形容詞)","examples":["If the bailiff thinks that things could turn nasty he will enlist the help of the police. 如果司法官認為情況可能會變糟，他會尋求警方幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>turns</b> a particular colour or if something <b>turns</b> it a particular color, it becomes that color. 變成 (某種顏色)","examples":["The sea would turn pale pink and the sky blood red. 大海將變成淺粉色，而天空將變成血紅色。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>turn</b> to indicate that there is a change to a particular kind of weather. For example, if it <b>turns</b> cold, the weather starts being cold. (天氣) 變得","examples":["If it turns cold, cover the plants. 如果天氣變冷，就把植物蓋起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a particular <b>turn of events</b>, a particular series of things happen. 形勢的變化","examples":["They were horrified at this unexpected turn of events. 他們對出乎意料的形勢變化感到震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>at every turn</b>, you are emphasizing that it happens frequently or all the time, usually so that it prevents you from achieving what you want. 常常; 總是","examples":["Its operations were hampered at every turn by inadequate numbers of trained staff. 它的運轉常常因受過培訓的員工人數不夠而受到限制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do someone <b>a good turn</b>, you do something that helps or benefits them. 有利的事","examples":["He did you a good turn by resigning. 他辭職對你有利。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>in turn</b> to refer to actions or events that are in a sequence one after the other, for example, because one causes the other. 轉而","examples":["One of the members of the surgical team leaked the story to a fellow physician who, in turn, confided in a reporter. 該外科小組的一名成員把此事洩露給一個同行醫生，而後者轉而又將此透露給了一位記者。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If each person in a group does something <b>in turn</b>, they do it one after the other in a fixed or agreed order. 依次地","examples":["There were cheers for each of the women as they spoke in turn. 女士們依次發言時，每一位都得到了喝彩。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If two or more people <b>take turns</b> <b>to</b> do something, they do it one after the other several times, rather than doing it together. 輪流","examples":["We took turns driving. 我們輪流駕駛。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a situation <b>takes a turn for the worse</b>, it suddenly becomes worse. If a situation <b>takes a turn for the better</b>, it suddenly becomes better. 突然變壞; 突然變好","examples":["Her condition took a sharp turn for the worse. 她的病情突然急劇惡化。"]}]}]},"warm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"暖和的，溫暖的；（衣服或建築物）保暖的，防寒的；友好的，熱情的；暖色調的；（尤指兒童遊戲中）快要發現的，即將猜中的；（土壤）吸熱快的，保溫的；（獵）（氣味，蹤跡）新鮮的，強烈的；（聲音）充滿情感的，渾厚飽滿的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）溫暖，（使）變暖和；（對某人） 產生好感，（對想法） 開始感興趣；同情；激動；使……興奮；  （使）變得更友好，變得更可愛；<非正式>打（某人屁股）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"暖和的地方（或地區）（the warm）；取暖；厚呢短大衣（British warm的簡稱）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"溫暖地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>warm</b> has some heat but not enough to be hot. 溫暖的","examples":["Wheat is grown in places which have cold winters and warm, dry summers. 小麥生長在冬季寒冷、夏季溫暖乾燥的地方。","Because it was warm, David wore only a white cotton shirt. 因為天氣暖和，戴維只穿了一件白色棉衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Warm</b> clothes and blankets are made of a material such as wool that protects you from the cold. 保暖的","examples":["They have been forced to sleep in the open without food or warm clothing. 他們被迫睡在露天裡，沒有食物也沒有保暖的衣服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Warm</b> colours have red or yellow in them rather than blue or green, and make you feel comfortable and relaxed. 暖色調的; 有暖感的","examples":["The basement hallway is painted a warm yellow. 地下室的走廊被塗成暖色調的黃色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>warm</b> person is friendly and shows a lot of affection or enthusiasm in their behaviour. 熱心的","examples":["She was a warm and loving mother. 她是位既熱心又慈愛的母親。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"保暖地","examples":["Remember to wrap up warmly on cold days. 記得天冷時穿暖和些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熱情地; 熱烈地","examples":["New members are warmly welcomed. 新成員受到熱烈歡迎。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>warm</b> a part of your body or if something hot <b>warms</b> it, it stops feeling cold and starts to feel hotter. 使…暖和","examples":["The sun had come out to warm his back. 太陽出來了，把他的背曬得暖暖的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>warm to</b> a person or an idea, you become fonder of the person or more interested in the idea. (對某人) 產生好感; (對某事) 開始感興趣","examples":["Those who got to know him better warmed to his openness and honesty. 那些逐漸瞭解了他的人對他的率真與坦誠產生了好感。"]}]}]},"waste":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"浪費，濫用；廢物，廢棄物（同 wastes）；荒地，荒原（wastes）；<法律>（尤指因租借人的行為或疏忽而導致的）不動產的損壞，產業損傷；糞便，尿液"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"浪費，濫用；未能充分利用，沒有物盡其用；<美，非正式>殺害，謀殺（某人）；（使）（人，身體部位）逐漸變虛弱，變消瘦；<文>破壞，毀壞（地方）；<文>（時間）流逝，被花掉"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（通常指城市中的某地）荒蕪的，荒廢的；（材料、物質等）廢棄的，無用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>waste</b> something such as time, money, or energy, you use too much of it doing something that is not important or necessary, or is unlikely to succeed. 浪費","examples":["There could be many reasons and he was not going to waste time speculating on them. 原因可能很多，而他不打算浪費時間猜測這些原因。","I resolved not to waste money on a hotel. 我決定不把錢白白浪費在旅館住宿上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>waste</b> an opportunity for something, you do not take advantage of it when it is available. 錯過 (機會)","examples":["Let's not waste an opportunity to see the children. 我們別錯過看看孩子們的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Waste</b> is also a noun. (時間、金錢等的) 浪費","examples":["It is a waste of time going to the doctor with most mild complaints. 為了種種小毛病去看醫生是浪費時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Waste</b> is the use of money or other resources on things that do not need it. 浪費","examples":["The packets are measured to reduce waste. 測量包裹尺寸以減少浪費。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Waste</b> is material that has been used and is no longer wanted, for example, because the valuable or useful part of it has been taken out. 廢物; 廢水","examples":["Congress passed a law that regulates the disposal of waste. 國會透過了一條管理廢物處理的法律。","...the dangers posed by toxic waste. …有毒廢棄物造成的危險。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Waste</b> land is land, especially in or near a city, that is not used or taken care of by anyone, and so is covered by wild plants and rubbish. 荒蕪的; 廢棄的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>goes to waste</b>, it remains unused or has to be thrown away. 被浪費掉","examples":["So much of his enormous effort and talent will go to waste if we are forced to drop one hour of the film. 如果我們被迫刪減一小時的電影，就會浪費掉他的非凡努力和才華。"]}]}]},"wednesday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期三"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wednesday</b> is the day after Tuesday and before Thursday. 星期三","examples":["Come and have supper with us on Wednesday, if you're free. 星期三過來和我們一起吃晚飯，如果有空的話。","Did you happen to see her leave last Wednesday? 上星期三你正好碰巧看見她離開？"]}]}]},"wedding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"婚禮，結婚慶典；婚禮的；<英>結婚紀念，結婚紀念日；結合"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結婚，娶，嫁；（使）結合；堅持，專心於（活動、信仰或制度）（wed 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wedding</b> is a marriage ceremony and the party or special meal that often takes place after the ceremony. 婚禮","examples":["Most couples want a traditional wedding. 多數情侶希望舉辦一個傳統的婚禮。","...the couple's 22nd wedding anniversary. …這對夫婦的第22個結婚紀念日。"]}]}]},"wash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"清洗，洗滌；洗澡，（用水和肥皂）洗（身體的某部分）；（水）漫過，流過，沖刷；<非正式>站得住腳，令人相信或接受；（織物，服裝，染料）耐洗；（情感）強烈衝擊；粉刷；鍍（金，銀）於；<文>使溼透，浸泡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"洗滌；正在洗的衣物，將要洗的衣物；（塗料的）薄塗層，塗料；<美>（對對立雙方均無益處的）形勢（或結果）；（船駛過劃出的）波浪，波浪拍打聲；（尤指用於清洗皮膚的）洗藥，清潔劑；（水流的）沖積物；淺水沙灘；泔水，泔腳；已發酵的麥芽汁；(the Wash) 沃什灣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wash</b> something, you clean it using water and usually a substance such as soap or detergent. 洗滌","examples":["We did odd jobs like farm work and washing dishes. 我們做了一些諸如幹農活兒和洗盤子之類的零活兒。","It took a long time to wash the mud out of his hair. 花了很長時間才把泥從他頭髮上洗掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wash</b> or if you <b>wash</b> part of your body, especially your hands and face, you clean part of your body using soap and water. 洗; 盥洗","examples":["They looked as if they hadn't washed in days. 他們看起來好像有好幾天沒洗澡了。","She washed her face with cold water. 她用冷水洗臉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a sea or river <b>washes</b> somewhere, it flows there gently. You can also say that something carried by a sea or river <b>washes</b> or <b>is washed</b> somewhere. 緩緩流向; (被) 沖走","examples":["The sea washed against the shore. 海水沖刷著海岸。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a feeling <b>washes</b> <b>over</b> you, you suddenly feel it very strongly and cannot control it. (情緒) 衝擊","examples":["A wave of self-consciousness can wash over her when someone new enters the room. 當有陌生人進入房間時，她會感到不自在。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something such as an item of clothing <b>is in the wash</b>, you mean that it is being washed, is waiting to be washed, or has just been washed and should therefore not be worn or used. 待洗; 正洗; 剛洗","examples":["Your jeans are in the wash. 你的牛仔褲正在洗呢。"]}]}]},"watch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"看，注視；觀看（電視節目、比賽等）；關注；照看，守護；當心，留意；監視"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"表，手錶；觀察，監視； 警衛隊，治安隊；警戒時間，（警衛或治安隊等的）值班時間；<史>巡夜人，巡夜隊（the watch）；<罕>一群夜鶯；（某人的）管理期；<美>（官方）天氣預警，天氣警報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>watch</b> someone or something, you look at them, usually for a period of time, and pay attention to what is happening. 觀看","examples":["The man was standing in his doorway watching him. 那個男人正站在自家門道里看著他。","He seems to enjoy watching me work. 他似乎喜歡看我幹活。","Here, now watch how I cut this, OK? 嘿，現在看我怎樣切，好嗎？","He watched as the Yankees rallied for a second comeback victory. 他看著北方佬為了又一次東山再起而集結。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>watch</b> something on television or an event such as a sports contest, you spend time looking at it, especially when you see it from the beginning to the end. 觀看 (電視節目、比賽等)","examples":["I'd stayed up late to watch the movie. 我熬夜看了那部電影。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>watch</b> a situation or event, you pay attention to it or you are aware of it, but you do not influence it. 關注","examples":["Human rights groups have been closely watching the case. 人權組織一直在密切關注著這件案子。","He watched as nine people were swept into the crevasse. 他眼看著9個人被捲入冰縫中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>watch</b> people, especially children or animals, you are responsible for them, and make sure that they are not in danger. 照看","examples":["Parents can't be expected to watch their children 24 hours a day. 不能指望父母全天24小時都照看自己的孩子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>watch</b> a particular person or thing, you are warning them to be careful that the person or thing does not get out of control or do something unpleasant. 當心; 留神","examples":["You really ought to watch these quiet types. 你真該當心這類不聲不響的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>keeps watch</b>, they look and listen all the time, while other people are asleep or doing something else, so that they can warn them of danger or an attack. 守望; 放哨","examples":["Jose, as usual, had climbed a tree to keep watch. 喬斯一如往常地爬到樹上放哨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep watch</b> on events or a situation, you pay attention to what is happening, so that you can take action at the right moment. 注意; 關注 (事態發展，以便適時採取行動)","examples":["U.S. officials have been keeping close watch on the situation. 美國官員們一直密切關注著事態的發展。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>watch it</b>\" in order to warn someone to be careful, especially when you want to threaten them about what will happen if they are not careful. 當心; 留神","examples":["\"Now watch it, Patsy,\" the sergeant told her. “當心，帕齊，”警官提醒她說。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is being kept <b>under watch</b>, they are being guarded or observed all the time. 受到保衛; 受到監視","examples":["Doctors confirmed how serious Josephine's condition was, and she is still being kept under watch. 醫生證實了約瑟芬的情況很糟糕，她仍被留床觀察。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say to someone \"<b>you watch</b>\" or \"<b>just watch</b>\" when you are predicting that something will happen, and you are very confident that it will happen as you say. 你瞧著吧","examples":["You watch. Things will get worse before they get better. 你瞧著吧。事情會先變糟，然後再好轉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>watch</b> is a small clock that you wear on a strap on your wrist, or on a chain. 表; 手錶","examples":[]}]}]},"weather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天氣，氣象；惡劣天氣（指寒冷、潮溼等），自然力；氣象預報；處境；氣候"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（受風吹雨打而）（使）褪色，（使）風化；平安度過（困境）；（船）航行到（海角）的上風，安全繞過（海角）；使（板，瓦片）交搭向下傾斜以擋雨；讓（鷹）在露天棲息一段時間"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"露天的；迎風的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>weather</b> is the condition of the atmosphere in one area at a particular time, for example, if it is raining, hot, or windy. 天氣","examples":["The weather was bad. 天氣惡劣。","I like cold weather. 我喜歡寒冷的天氣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as wood or rock <b>weathers</b> or <b>is weathered</b>, it changes colour or shape as a result of the wind, sun, rain, or cold. 風化; 褪色","examples":["Unpainted wooden furniture weathers to a grey colour. 沒有上漆的木質傢俱會褪成灰色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>weather</b> a difficult time or a difficult situation, you survive it and are able to continue normally after it has passed or ended. 經受住","examples":["The company has weathered the recession. 公司度過了蕭條期。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>under the weather</b>, you mean that you feel slightly ill. 身體不適","examples":["I was still feeling a bit under the weather. 我依然感覺有些不適。"]}]}]},"water":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水，雨水；水域，（江、河、湖、海等）大片的水；（某個國家的）領海，海域（waters）；不明朗（或未知的、困難、危險等）局面（waters）；羊水（waters）；（湖、海的）水面；水位；乘船，走水路"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……澆水，灌溉；給…...水喝，飲（動物）；（風等使眼睛）流淚；流口水；（江河）流經並給（某地區）供水；加水沖淡，稀釋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Water</b> is a clear thin liquid that has no colour or taste when it is pure. It falls from clouds as rain and enters rivers and seas. All animals and people need water in order to live. 水","examples":["Get me a glass of water. 給我一杯水。","...the sound of water hammering on the metal roof. …雨水敲打著金屬屋頂的聲音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>waters</b> to refer to a large area of sea, especially the area of sea that is near to a country and that is regarded as belonging to it. 海域; (尤指) 領海","examples":["The ship will remain outside Chinese territorial waters. 這艘船將繼續停留在中國領海之外。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>water</b> plants, you pour water over them in order to help them to grow. 澆水","examples":["He went out to water the plants. 他出去給植物澆水。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your eyes <b>water</b>, tears build up in them because they are hurting or because you are upset. 流淚","examples":["His eyes watered from cigarette smoke. 他的眼睛被香菸煙霧嗆出了淚水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that your mouth <b>is watering</b>, you mean that you can smell or see some nice food that makes you want to eat it. 流口水","examples":["...cookies to make your mouth water. …令你流口水的曲奇餅。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that an event or incident is <b>water under the bridge</b>, you mean that it has happened and cannot now be changed, so there is no point in worrying about it anymore. 橋下水 (比喻無需再掛懷的往事)","examples":["He was relieved his time in jail was over and regarded it as water under the bridge. 他對自己的刑期已滿而感到如釋重負，把那視為橋下之水過往之事而不再掛懷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in deep water</b>, you are in a difficult or awkward situation. 陷入困境","examples":["You certainly seem to be in deep water. 你的確看起來像是陷入了困境中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an argument or theory does not <b>hold water</b>, it does not seem to be reasonable or be in accordance with the facts. (理論或論點) 符合邏輯; 與事實相符","examples":["This argument simply cannot hold water in Europe. 這種論點在歐洲根本就說不通。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>in hot water</b>, you are in trouble. 陷入困境","examples":["The company has already been in hot water over high prices this year. 該公司今年已陷入了高價的困境中。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>pour cold water on</b> an idea or suggestion, you show that you have a low opinion of it. (對想法或建議) 潑冷水","examples":["University economists pour cold water on the idea that the economic recovery has begun. 大學的經濟學家們對經濟已經開始復甦的觀點潑冷水。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>test the water</b> or <b>test the waters</b>, you try to find out what reaction an action or idea will get before you do it or tell it to people. 試探","examples":["You should be cautious when getting involved and test the water before committing yourself. 當你涉足其中時你應該小心謹慎，在表態之前要先行試探。"]}]}]},"wear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿（衣服），戴（首飾等）；蓄（須），留（發）；銷蝕，磨損，踩出（路），磨出（洞）；流露，面帶（某種表情）；使疲乏，使虛弱，使厭倦；經久耐用；不顯老；<英，非正式>允許，接受；（船）升，掛（旗）；<文>消磨（時間）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（特定人群、場合或用途穿的）服裝；穿，戴；（因長期使用而造成的）磨損，損壞；耐用性，經久性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wear</b> something such as clothes, shoes, or jewelry, you have them on your body or on part of your body. 穿; 戴","examples":["He was wearing a brown uniform. 他穿著一件棕色制服。","I sometimes wear contact lenses. 我有時候戴隱形眼鏡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wear</b> your hair or beard in a particular way, you have it cut or styled in that way. 留著 (某種樣式的頭髮或鬍鬚)","examples":["She wore her hair in a long braid. 她留著長辮子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>wear</b> to refer to clothes that are suitable for a certain time or place. For example, <b>evening wear</b> is clothes suitable for the evening. (在特定時間或場合穿戴的) 服裝","examples":["The shop stocks an extensive range of beach wear. 這家商店備有品種繁多的沙灘服裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wear</b> is the amount or type of use that something has over a period of time. 耐用性; 經久性","examples":["You'll get more wear out of a hat if you choose one in a neutral colour. 如果選擇中性顏色的帽子，戴的時間會更久一些。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Wear</b> is the damage or change that is caused by something being used a lot or for a long time. 磨損","examples":["...a large, well-upholstered armchair which showed signs of wear. …一張寬大、裝飾精美的有些磨損的扶手椅。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>wears</b>, it becomes thinner or weaker because it is constantly being used over a long period of time. 磨損","examples":["The stone steps, dating back to 1855, are beginning to wear. 這些可以追溯到1855年的石階開始出現磨損。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>wear</b> to talk about how well something lasts over a period of time. For example, if something <b>wears well</b>, it still seems quite new or useful after a long time or a lot of use. 耐用","examples":["Ten years on, the original concept was wearing well. 十年過去，最初的觀念依然適用。"]}]}]},"week":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星期，周；一個星期的時間，一週；一週工作時間，工作周；（除去星期六和星期日的）星期，周；活動周（舉行某項活動的一週）；（從某天算起的）一週；（某天之前的）一週；一週又一週，接連好幾個星期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>week</b> is a period of seven days. Some people consider that a week starts on Monday and ends on Sunday. 星期","examples":["I had a letter from my mother last week. 我上星期收到了母親的一封信。","This has been on my mind all week. 我整個星期都在想這件事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>week</b> is a period of about seven days. 一週時間","examples":["Her mother stayed for another two weeks. 她母親又呆了兩週時間。","Only 12 weeks ago he underwent major heart transplant surgery. 僅僅12周之前，他接受了一次心臟移植的大手術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your working <b>week</b> is the hours that you spend at work during a week. 工作周 (指一週的工作時數)","examples":["It is not unusual for women to work a 40-hour week. 女性1周工作40小時並不少見。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The week</b> is the part of the week that does not include Saturday and Sunday. (除星期六和星期日以外的) 周工作日","examples":["...the hard work of looking after the children during the week. …除週末外每天都照看孩子的辛苦活。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>week</b> in expressions such as \"a week last Monday,\" \"a week ago this Tuesday,\" and \"a week ago yesterday\" to mean exactly one week before the day that you mention. 用於(a week last Monday), (a week ago this Tuesday), 以及(a week ago yesterday)等片語中，表示前一星期的該日","examples":["\"That's the time you weren't well, wasn't it?\"—\"Yes, that's right, that was a week ago last Monday.\" “就是那個時候你不舒服，是嗎？”——“是的，就是一週前的星期一。”"]}]}]},"weekend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"週末；週末旅行，週末度假"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"週末的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"度週末"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weekend</b> is Saturday and Sunday. 週末","examples":["She had agreed to have dinner with him in town the following weekend. 她同意下週末和他一起到城裡吃晚飯。"]}]}]},"where":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在哪裡，去哪兒，從哪裡；……的地方，在那裡；到什麼地步，在哪方面"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"哪裡"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"在……的地方，哪裡，什麼地方"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"地點，位置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>where</b> to ask questions about the place something is in, or is coming from or going to. 哪裡 (用於就地點提問)","examples":["Where did you meet him? 你在哪裡見到他的？","Where's Anna? 安娜在哪裡？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>where</b> to ask questions about a situation, a stage in something, or an aspect of something. 哪裡 (在疑問句中，就某一情況、某事所處的階段或方面等提問)","examples":["If they get their way, where will it stop? 如果他們說了算，那麼哪裡才是盡頭？"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>where</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause in which you mention the place in which something is situated or happens. 哪裡 (用於某些詞特別是動詞和形容詞後，引導從句表示某物所處或發生的地點)","examples":["People began looking across to see where the noise was coming from. 人們開始望過去，看響聲是從哪裡發出的。","He knew where Henry Carter had gone. 他知道亨利·卡特去了哪裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>where</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause in which you mention a situation, a stage in something, or an aspect of something. 哪裡 (用於某些詞特別是動詞和形容詞後，引導從句表示某一情況、某事所處的階段或方面等)","examples":["It's not hard to see where she got her feelings about herself. 不難看出她從何處獲得了對自己的那種感覺。","She had a feeling she already knew where this conversation was going to lead. 她感覺到她已經知道這次談話將導向何處。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Where</b> is also a relative pronoun. …的地方 (用作關係代詞)","examples":["The area where the explosion occurred was closed off by police. 爆炸發生的地方被警察封鎖起來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Where</b> is also a relative pronoun. 用作關係代詞","examples":["The government is at a stage where it is willing to talk to almost anyone. 政府已經到了幾乎願意與任何人對話的地步。"]}]}]},"west":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"西，西方；（某個國家、地區或地方的）西部；西方國家 (指美國、加拿大以及西歐、北歐和南歐諸國)（the West)；（美國）西部（尤指密西西比河以西諸州）(the West, the west)；<史>西方（國家）（與東歐前共產主義國家相對的歐洲和北美洲的非共產主義國家）（the West)；（橋牌）坐在西首位置的人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"西方的,向西的；（風）來自西方的；（用於國家、州和地區的名稱中）西部的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向西方，朝西方；……以西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>west</b> is the direction you look toward in the evening in order to see the sun set. 西方","examples":["I pushed on toward Flagstaff, a hundred miles to the west. 我繼續向西邊100英里處的弗拉格斯塔夫市前進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>west</b> <b>of</b> a place, country, or region is the part of it which is in the west. 西部","examples":["Many of the buildings in the west of the city are on fire. 該城西部的許多建築都著火了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The West</b> is used to refer to the United States, Canada, and the countries of Western, Northern, and Southern Europe. 西方國家 (指美國、加拿大以及西歐、北歐和南歐諸國)","examples":["...relations between Iran and the West. …伊朗和西方國家之間的關係。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>west</b>, you travel toward the west. 往西邊","examples":["We are going west to California. 我們將往西去加利福尼亞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>west</b> <b>of</b> a place is positioned to the west of it. …以西","examples":["Penryn is about 60 miles west of Philadelphia. 彭林位於費城以西60英里的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>west</b> part of a place, country, or region is the part which is toward the west. 西部的","examples":["...a small island off the west coast of South Korea. …韓國西海岸外的一個小島。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>West</b> is used in the names of some countries, states, and regions in the west of a larger area. (用於國家、州和地區的名稱中) 西部的","examples":["Mark has been working in West Africa for about six months. 馬克已在西非工作了大約六個月。","...his West Hollywood home. …他在西好萊塢的家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>west</b> wind blows from the west. 從西邊吹來的 (風)","examples":["...the warm west wind. …和煦的西風。"]}]}]},"while":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"當……的時候；與……同時；而，然而（表示對比）；儘管，雖然；直到……為止"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一段時間；同時；<文>在此期間"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"消磨時間"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（北英格蘭）直到"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在……的時候"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>while</b> something else is happening, the two things are happening at the same time. 當…的時候 (表示兩事同時發生)","examples":["They were grinning and watching while one man laughed and poured beer over the head of another. 當一個男人大笑著將啤酒倒在另一個男人頭上時，他們正邊看邊咧著嘴笑。","I sat on the chair to unwrap the package while he stood behind me. 我坐在椅子上開啟包裹，當時他就站在我身後。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>while</b> something else happens, the first thing happens at some point during the time that the second thing is happening. 正值…之時 (表示一件事是在另一件事發生過程中的某個時間發生的)","examples":["The two ministers have yet to meet, but may do so while in New York. 兩位部長還未會面，但他們在紐約期間可能會見面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>while</b> at the beginning of a clause to introduce information that contrasts with information in the main clause. 而 (用於從句之首，引出與主句內容相對比的資訊)","examples":["Most digital camera owners are male, while women prefer film. 大部分數碼相機的主人都是男性，而女性偏愛用膠捲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>while</b>, before making a statement, in order to introduce information that partly conflicts with your statement. 雖然 (用於發表陳述之前，引入和陳述內容部分矛盾的資訊)","examples":["While the news, so far, has been good, there may be days ahead when it is bad. 雖然到目前為止都是好訊息，但是可能過幾天就有壞訊息了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>while</b> is a period of time. 一段時間","examples":["They walked on in silence for a while. 他們默默地走了一會兒。","He was married a little while ago. 他前不久剛結了婚。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>all the while</b> in order to say that something happens continually or that it happens throughout the time when something else is happening. 一直","examples":["All the while the people at the next table watched me eat. 鄰桌的人一直在看著我吃東西。"]}]}]},"weight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重量，分量，體重；重；槓鈴，啞鈴；砝碼，秤砣；重體，重物；重量單位，衡制；重擔，負擔；影響力，重要性；大量的某物；投擲器械（包括鐵餅、鉛球、鏈球等）；（布料）表面密度；重心；（引力場作用於物體上的）重力；（統計）權重，權數"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加重量於，使變重；（經改動）使傾向於……；重視，加權重於；加重壓於（馬）上；對（織物）作加重處理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>weight</b> of a person or thing is how heavy they are, measured in units such as kilograms, pounds, or tons. 重量","examples":["What is your height and weight? 你的身高和體重是多少？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's or thing's <b>weight</b> is the fact that they are very heavy. 分量重","examples":["His weight was harming his health. 他沉重的體重正危害著他的健康。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you move your <b>weight</b>, you change position so that most of the pressure of your body is on a particular part of your body. (身體的) 重心","examples":["He shifted his weight from one foot to the other. 他將身體的重心從一隻腳挪到另一隻腳上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Weights</b> are objects that weigh a known amount and that people lift as a form of exercise. 啞鈴","examples":["I was in the gym lifting weights. 我正在健身房舉啞鈴。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Weights</b> are metal objects that weigh a known amount and that are used on a set of scales to weigh other things. 砝碼","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to a heavy object as a <b>weight</b>, especially when you have to lift it. (尤其指必須舉起的) 重物","examples":["Straining to lift heavy weights can lead to a rise in blood pressure. 用盡全身力氣舉起重物會導致血壓升高。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something is given a particular <b>weight</b>, it is given a particular value according to how important or significant it is. 權重","examples":["The scientists involved put different weight on the conclusions of different models. 相關科學家們對不同模型的結論賦予的權重各不相同。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone or something gives <b>weight</b> to what a person says, thinks, or does, they emphasize its significance. 分量","examples":["The fact that he is gone has given more weight to fears that he may try to launch a civil war. 他已離開這一事實讓人更加擔心他可能要發動一場內戰。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you give something or someone <b>weight</b>, you consider them to be very important or influential in a particular situation. 重視","examples":["Consumers generally place more weight on negative information than on the positive when deciding what to buy. 消費者在決定購買的時候，一般更看重負面資訊而不是正面資訊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>loses weight</b>, they become lighter. If they <b>gain weight</b> or <b>put on weight</b>, they become heavier. 體重減輕; 體重增加","examples":["I'm lucky really as I never put on weight. 我真的很幸運，體重從未增加過。","The boy appeared anxious, had lost weight and was not sleeping well. 那個男孩顯得很焦慮，體重減輕了，覺也睡不好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or their opinion <b>carries weight</b>, they are respected and are able to influence people. 有影響力","examples":["Senator Kerry carries considerable weight in Washington. 參議員克里在華盛頓舉足輕重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>worth</b> their <b>weight in gold</b>, you are emphasizing that they are so useful, helpful, or valuable that you feel you could not manage without them. 極有價值","examples":["Any successful manager is worth his weight in gold. 任何成功的經理都非常有價值。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pull</b> your <b>weight</b>, you work as hard as everyone else who is involved in the same task or activity. 盡本分","examples":["He accused the team of not pulling their weight. 他指責隊員們沒有盡到自己的本分。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>weight</b> something, you make it heavier by adding something to it, for example, in order to stop it from moving easily. 加重量於","examples":["It can be sewn into curtain hems to weight the curtain and so allow it to hang better. 可以把它縫在窗簾的摺邊裡以增加窗簾的重量，使之更有下垂感。"]}]}]},"welcome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"歡迎，迎接；迎新；樂意接納，欣然接受；樂於接受（已發生的事）；慶祝"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（某人）受歡迎的；令人愉快的；（表示樂於讓某人做某事）可隨意；儘管……好了（指非常樂意讓別人擁有自己不想要的東西）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"歡迎，迎接；（對觀念的）接受"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"歡迎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>welcome</b> someone, you greet them in a friendly way when they arrive somewhere. 歡迎","examples":["Several people came by to welcome me. 幾個人走過來歡迎我。","She was there to welcome him home from war. 她在那裡歡迎他從戰場回家。","...a welcoming speech. …歡迎辭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>welcome</b> an action, decision, or situation, you approve of it and are pleased that it has occurred. 欣然接受","examples":["She welcomed this move but said that overall the changes didn't go far enough. 她欣然接受了這一舉措，但又說總體上改變還不徹底。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>welcome</b> certain people or actions, you are inviting and encouraging people to do something, for example, to come to a particular place. 歡迎","examples":["We would welcome your views about the survey. 我們歡迎你們對這項調查提出意見。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Welcome</b> is also a noun. 歡迎","examples":["There would be a fantastic welcome awaiting him back here. 會有一場熱烈的歡迎儀式迎接他回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Welcome</b> is also a noun. 歡迎","examples":["Environmental groups have given a guarded welcome to the prime minister's proposal. 環保組織對首相的提議表示了謹慎的歡迎。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>welcome</b> in expressions such as <b>welcome home</b>, <b>welcome to Boston</b>, and <b>welcome back</b> when you are greeting someone who has just arrived somewhere. 歡迎來到…","examples":["Welcome to Washington. 歡迎來到華盛頓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>You're welcome</b>\" to someone who has thanked you for something in order to acknowledge their thanks in a polite way. 不用客氣 (對別人為某事表示感謝時所作的禮貌回答)","examples":["\"Thank you for the information.\"—\"You're welcome.\" “謝謝你提供的資訊。”—“不客氣。”"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>welcome</b>, you mean that people wanted it and are happy that it has occurred. 受歡迎的","examples":["Any progress in reducing chemical weapons is welcome. 削減化學武器的任何進展都是受歡迎的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>welcome</b> in a particular place, you are encouraging them to go there by telling them that they will be liked and accepted. 受歡迎的","examples":["New members are always welcome. 新成員歡迎加入。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you tell someone that they are <b>welcome</b> to do something, you are encouraging them to do it by telling them that they are allowed to do it. 可任意的","examples":["You are welcome to visit the hospital at any time. 你可隨時來醫院參觀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>welcome to</b> something, you mean that you do not want it yourself because you do not like it and you are very willing for them to have it. 儘管…好了","examples":["If women want to take on the business world they are welcome to it as far as I'm concerned. 就我而言，如果婦女想承擔起商業領域的重任，她們儘管這樣做好了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> someone <b>welcome</b> or <b>make</b> them <b>feel welcome</b>, you make them feel happy and accepted in a new place. 使受歡迎","examples":["Here are six Mexican hotels where children are made to feel welcome. 這裡有6家墨西哥旅館，孩子們覺得在那兒頗受歡迎。"]}]}]},"why":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於問句）為什麼，為何；（反問，表示不必）何必；……的原因；為什麼（不）；為什麼（表生氣或惱火）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"理由，原因"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"哎呀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>why</b> in questions when you ask about the reasons for something. 為什麼 (用於提問原因)","examples":["Why hasn't he brought the whiskey? 為什麼他還沒把威士忌酒帶來？","Why didn't he stop me? 為什麼他沒有阻止我？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>why</b> with \"not\" in questions in order to introduce a suggestion. (問句中與)(not)(連用，引入建議) 為什麼","examples":["Why not give Charmaine a call? 為什麼不給莎梅因打個電話呢？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>why</b> with \"not\" in questions in order to express your annoyance or anger. (在問句中與)(not)(連用，表達懊惱或憤怒) 為什麼","examples":["Why don't you look where you're going? 為什麼你不看看自己在往哪兒走？"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>why</b> at the beginning of a clause in which you talk about the reasons for something. …的原因 (用在從句開頭)","examples":["He still could not throw any further light on why the lift could have become jammed. 他對電梯為什麼會卡住仍給不出更多解釋。","Experts wonder why the U.S. government is not taking similarly strong actions against AIDS in this country. 專家們想弄明白為什麼美國政府沒有對該國的艾滋病採取類似的強硬舉措。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Why</b> is also an adverb. 為什麼","examples":["I don't know why. 我不知道為什麼。","It's obvious why. 很明顯是為什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Why</b> is also an adverb. 為什麼","examples":["He confirmed that the city had been closed to foreigners, but gave no reason why. 他證實這座城市已經禁止外國人進入，但沒有給出原因。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>why</b> to introduce a relative clause after the word \"reason.\" 用在(reason)後面，引導關係從句","examples":["There's a reason why women don't read this stuff; it's not funny. 婦女們不讀這種東西是有原因的：它並不逗趣。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>why not</b> in order to agree with what someone has suggested. (表示贊同某人的建議) 為什麼不呢","examples":["\"Want to spend the afternoon with me?\"—\"Why not?\" “想和我一起度過這個下午嗎？”—“為什麼不呢？”"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People say \"<b>Why!</b>\" at the beginning of a sentence when they are surprised, shocked, or angry. (用於句首表達驚訝、震驚或憤怒) 哎呀 ！","examples":["Why hello, Tom. 哎呀，你好，湯姆。"]}]}]},"whole":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全部的，整個的；完整的，完好無損的；(強調大小或重要性）整個的，全部的；要點，主旨；健全的，健康的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"整體，全部"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地；整個"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>the whole of</b> something, you mean all of it. 整個","examples":["He has said he will make an apology to the whole of Asia for his country's past behaviour. 他說過他將為他的國家在過去的所作所為向全體亞洲人民道歉。","I was cold throughout the whole of my body. 我渾身冰冷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whole</b> is also an adjective. 整個的","examples":["We spent the whole summer in Italy that year. 我們那一年在義大利度過了整個夏天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>whole</b>, it is in one piece and is not broken or damaged. 完整的","examples":["I struck the glass with my fist with all my might; yet it remained whole. 我使盡全力用拳頭砸那塊玻璃，但它卻完好無損。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Whole</b> is also an adjective. 完全的","examples":["That saved me a whole bunch of money. 那給我節省下一大筆錢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>whole</b> is a single thing that contains several different parts. (包含幾個不同部分的) 整體","examples":["An atom itself is a complete whole, with its electrons, protons and neutrons and other elements. 原子本身是個整體，含電子、質子、中子以及其他組成部分。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whole</b> to emphasize what you are saying. (表強調) 完全地","examples":["It was like seeing a whole different side of somebody. 這就像見到了某個人完全不同的一面。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to something <b>as a whole</b>, you are referring to it generally and as a single unit. 總體上","examples":["He described the move as a victory for the people of South Africa as a whole. 他把這一行動描述成全體南非人民的一次勝利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>on the whole</b> to indicate that what you are saying is true in general but may not be true in every case, or that you are giving a general opinion or summary of something. 大體上說","examples":["On the whole, people miss the opportunity to enjoy leisure. 大體上說，人們都渴望享受休閒時光的機會。"]}]}]},"white":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"白色的；白種人的，白膚色的；蒼白的；加牛奶（或奶油）的；（葡萄酒）白的，淡黃色的；（麵粉）精白的；<美>空白的；樹皮淡色的；（玻璃）透明的，無色的；<非正式>完全公正的，非常誠實的；（魔法）善意的；（血細胞）白的；<史>（政治）反動的；純潔的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"白色，白顏料；白種人，白人；白葡萄酒；眼白；蛋清，蛋白；白色運動服（whites）；要洗滌的白色織物（whites）；白衣服；執白棋者，白方；白色的東西，白球；白粉蝶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>把……漆成白色，使變白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>white</b> is the colour of snow or milk. 白色","examples":["He had nice square white teeth. 他有整齊潔白的漂亮牙齒。","Issa's white beach hat gleamed in the harsh lights. 伊薩的白色沙灘帽在刺目的燈光下閃閃發光。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>white</b> person has a pale skin and belongs to a race of European origin. 白色人種的","examples":["Working with white people hasn't been a problem for me or for them. 和白種人在一起工作對我或對他們來說一直都不是個問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>White</b> wine is pale yellow in colour. 白葡萄酒","examples":["Gregory poured another glass of white wine and went back to his bedroom. 格雷戈裡又倒了一杯白葡萄酒，回臥室去了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>White</b> blood cells are the cells in your blood your body uses to fight infection. 白 (細胞)","examples":["...an AIDS drug that helps restore a patient's white blood cells. …幫助修復病人白細胞的一種治療艾滋病的藥。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whites</b> are white people. 白種人","examples":["It's a school that's brought blacks and whites and Hispanics together. 這是一所讓黑人、白種人和西班牙裔人走到了一起的學校。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>white</b> of an egg is the transparent liquid that surrounds the yellow part called the yolk. 蛋清","examples":["As soon as the whites of the eggs have set, remove the cover. 蛋清一凝固，就把蓋子揭開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>white</b> of someone's eye is the white part that surrounds the coloured part called the iris. 眼白 (指眼球中的白色部分)","examples":["Susanne stared at me, the whites of her eyes gleaming in the streetlight. 蘇珊娜盯著我看，她的眼白在街燈下發亮。"]}]}]},"wife":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"妻子，已婚婦女，夫人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A man's <b>wife</b> is the woman he is married to. 妻子","examples":["He married his wife Jane 37 years ago. 他和妻子簡37年前結婚。"]}]}]},"way":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方法，手段；習俗，習慣，行為方式；（行事）作風，（某事發生的）方式；道路，路線；行進路線，通路；方向；……路（用於道路的名稱）；出入通道，門口；距離，時段；方面；（兩種之一的）選擇；情況，狀態；（某人居住的）地區，地方；（分成的）部分；<蘇格蘭，正式>職業，行當；（船）航行，動力；船臺，滑道（ways）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大大地，遠遠地；<美>非常，很"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"途中的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to a <b>way</b> of doing something, you are referring to how you can do it, for example, the action you can take or the method you can use to achieve it. 方式; 方法","examples":["Freezing isn't a bad way of preserving food. 冷凍不失為儲存食品的一種好方法。","I worked myself into a frenzy plotting ways to make him jealous. 我絞盡腦汁，處心積慮，就是為了讓他嫉妒。","There just might be a way. 可能會有個辦法的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>way</b> someone does something, you are talking about the qualities their action has. 態度; 樣子","examples":["She smiled in a friendly way. 她友好地笑了笑。","He had a strange way of talking. 他說話的樣子很奇怪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a general statement or description is true <b>in</b> a particular <b>way</b>, this is the form of it that is true in a particular case. 形式; 方面","examples":["Computerized reservation systems help airline profits in several ways. 電子訂票系統讓航空公司在好幾個方面獲利。","She was afraid in a way that was quite new to her. 她感到害怕，而這種害怕是以前不曾有過的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> in expressions such as <b>in some ways</b>, <b>in many ways</b>, and <b>in every way</b> to indicate the degree or extent to which a statement is true. 某方面; 某點","examples":["In some ways, the official opening is a formality. 從某些方面來說，官方開幕儀式是個形式而已。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>ways</b> of a particular person or group of people are their customs or their usual behaviour. 習俗; 習慣","examples":["He denounces people who urge him to alter his ways. 他指責那些敦促他改變習慣的人們。","She began to study the ways of the Native Americans. 她開始研究土著印第安人的習俗。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>way</b>, you are referring to their usual or preferred type of behaviour. 習慣; 作風","examples":["She is now divorced and, in her usual resourceful way, has started her own business. 她現在離婚了，並以她一貫機敏能幹的作風開始自己創業。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> to refer to one particular opinion or interpretation of something, when others are possible. 看法","examples":["I suppose that's one way of looking at it. 我想那是其中的一種看法。","With most of Dylan's lyrics, however, there are other ways of interpreting the words. 然而，迪倫的大多數歌詞都有其他的解讀方法。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> when mentioning one of a number of possible, alternative results or decisions. 結果; 決定","examples":["There is no indication which way the vote could go. 沒有跡象表明投票的結果會怎麼樣。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"The <b>way</b> you feel about something is your attitude to it or your opinion about it. 態度; 觀點","examples":["I'm so sorry – I had no idea you felt that way. 我很抱歉–我不知道你是那樣想的。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you mention <b>the</b> <b>way</b> that something happens, you are mentioning the fact that it happens. 情形","examples":["I hate the way he manipulates people. 我討厭他擺佈人。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> in expressions such as <b>push your way</b>, <b>work your way</b>, or <b>eat your way</b>, followed by a prepositional phrase or adverb, in order to indicate movement, progress, or force as well as the action described by the verb. 用於(push your way), (work your way)或者(eat your way)等片語中，表示運動、程序、力量以及所用動詞所表示的動作","examples":["She thrust her way into the crowd. 她擠進了人群。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>way</b> somewhere consists of the different places that you go through or the route that you take in order to get there. 路徑","examples":["Does anybody know the way to the bathroom? 有沒有人知道到衛生間的路怎麼走？","I'm afraid I can't remember the way. 恐怕我不記得路了。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you go or look a particular <b>way</b>, you go or look in that direction. 方向","examples":["As he strode into the kitchen, he passed Pop coming the other way. 他大步走進廚房，同迎面過來的爸爸擦肩而過。","They paused at the top of the stairs, doubtful as to which way to go next. 他們在樓梯的頂頭停了下來，不知道下一步朝哪個方向走。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You can refer to the direction you are travelling in as your <b>way</b>. 行進方向","examples":["She would say she was going my way and offer me a lift. 她會說和我同路，可以載我一程。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If you lose your <b>way</b>, you take a wrong or unfamiliar route, so that you do not know how to get to the place that you want to go to. If you find your <b>way</b>, you manage to get to the place that you want to go to. 路途","examples":["The men lost their way in a sandstorm and crossed the border by mistake. 這些男人在沙塵暴中迷了路，誤越了邊境。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You talk about people going their different <b>ways</b> in order to say that their lives develop differently and they have less contact with each other. 生活道路","examples":["It wasn't until we each went our separate ways that I began to learn how to do things for myself. 直到我們各奔東西后，我才開始學會如何自己做事情。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If something comes your <b>way</b>, you get it or receive it. 獲得","examples":["Take advantage of the opportunities coming your way in a couple of months. 把握住這幾個月之內你可能獲得的機會。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> in expressions such as <b>the right way up</b> and <b>the other way around</b> to refer to one of two or more possible positions or arrangements that something can have. 可能的位置","examples":["Books have a right and a wrong way up. 書可以正著放，也可以反著放。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you split something a number of <b>ways</b>, you divide it into a number of different parts or quantities, usually fairly equal in size. (分成的通常大小相同的) 部分","examples":["The region was split three ways, between Greece, Serbia and Bulgaria. 該地區被希臘、塞爾維亞和保加利亞一分為三。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"<b>Way</b> is used in expressions such as <b>a long way</b>, <b>a little way</b>, and <b>quite a way</b>, to say how far away something is or how far you have traveled. 距離","examples":["Some of them live in places quite a long way from here. 他們當中一些人住在離這兒相當遠的地方。","A little way further down the lane we passed the driveway to a house. 我們沿著小巷又走了一小段距離，穿過車道來到一幢房子前。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"<b>Way</b> is used in expressions such as <b>a long way</b>, <b>a little way</b>, and <b>quite a way</b>, to say how far away in time something is. (時間的) 距離","examples":["Success is still a long way off. 離成功還遠著呢。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"You use <b>way</b> in expressions such as <b>all the way</b>, <b>most of the way</b> and <b>half the way</b> to refer to the extent to which an action has been completed. (行為完成的) 程度","examples":["He had unscrewed the caps most of the way. 他已經快要把瓶蓋擰開了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>way</b> to emphasize, for example, that something is a great distance away or is very much below or above a particular level or amount. 大大地; 遠遠地","examples":["Way down in the valley to the west is the town of Freiburg. 遠遠的西邊山谷中坐落著弗賴堡鎮。","You've waited way too long. 你們已經等了太久了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Way</b> is also a combining form. 部分 (用於構成合成詞)","examples":["...a simple three-way division. …一種簡單的3分法。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>all the way</b> to emphasize how long a distance is. 一路","examples":["He had to walk all the way home. 他不得不一路步行回家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>all the way</b> to emphasize that your remark applies to every part of a situation, activity, or period of time. 一直","examples":["Having started a revolution we must go all the way. 既然我們已經開始革命了，就必須一直堅持下去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone says that you <b>can't have it both ways</b>, they are telling you that you have to choose between two things and cannot do or have them both. 二者不能兼得","examples":["Countries cannot have it both ways: the cost of a cleaner environment may sometimes be fewer jobs in dirty industries. 各國不能二者兼得：環境更為潔淨的代價有可能是汙染工業的減少。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>by the way</b> when you add something to what you are saying, especially something that you have just thought of. 順便提一下","examples":["The name Latifah, by the way, means \"delicate.\" 順便提一下，Latifah這個名字有“精緻”之意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>clear the way</b>, <b>open the way</b>, or <b>prepare the way</b> for something, you create an opportunity for it to happen. (為某事) 創造機會; 掃清道路","examples":["The talks are meant to clear the way for formal negotiations on a new constitution. 會談旨在為新憲法的正式協商掃清道路。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone takes <b>the easy way out</b>, you disapprove of them because they do what is easiest for them in a difficult situation, rather than dealing with it properly. 走捷徑","examples":["As soon as things got difficult he took the easy way out. 事情剛變得有些棘手他就走捷徑脫身。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>either way</b> in order to introduce a statement that is true in each of the two possible or alternative cases that you have just mentioned. (兩種情況中) 不論發生哪種情況","examples":["The sea may rise or the land may fall; either way the sand dunes will be gone in a short time. 海平面可能會升高，或者陸地可能會下降；不論發生哪種情況，沙丘都將很快消失。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that a particular type of action or development is <b>the way forward</b>, you approve of it because it is likely to lead to success. 進步","examples":["...people who genuinely believe that anarchy is the way forward. …真正相信無政府狀態是一種進步的人。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone <b>gets</b> their <b>way</b> or <b>has</b> their <b>way</b>, nobody stops them from doing what they want to do. You can also say that someone <b>gets</b> their <b>own</b> way or <b>has</b> their <b>own way</b>. 隨心所欲","examples":["She is very good at using her charm to get her way. 她非常擅長利用自己的魅力來為所欲為。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If one thing <b>gives way to</b> another, the first thing is replaced by the second. 被…取代","examples":["First he had been numb. Then the numbness gave way to anger. 一開始他只是麻木。後來麻木被憤怒代替。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If an object that is supporting something <b>gives way</b>, it breaks or collapses, so that it can no longer support that thing. 斷裂; 倒塌","examples":["The hook in the ceiling had given way and the lamp had fallen blazing on to the table. 天花板上的鉤子脫落，結果掛燈大亮著掉到了桌子上。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>in no way</b> or <b>not in any way</b> to emphasize that a statement is not at all true. 決不","examples":["In no way am I going to adopt any of his methods. 我決不會採用他的任何一個方法。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>in a way</b>, you mean that although it is not completely true, it is true to a limited extent or in certain respects. You use <b>in a way</b> to reduce the force of a statement. 在某種程度上","examples":["In a way, I suppose I'm frightened of failing. 我想，從某種程度上來說我害怕失敗。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>gets in the way</b> or <b>is in the way</b>, you are annoyed because their presence or their actions stop you from doing something properly. 妨礙","examples":["\"We wouldn't get in the way,\" Suzanne promised. \"We'd just stand quietly in a corner.\" “我們不會妨礙你的，”蘇珊保證說，“我們就在角落裡安安靜靜地站著。”"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"To <b>get in the way</b> <b>of</b> something means to make it difficult for it to happen, continue, or be appreciated properly. 阻礙","examples":["She had a job which never got in the way of her leisure interests. 她有一份工作，但絲毫不妨礙她的個人愛好。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>know</b> your <b>way around</b> a particular subject, system, or job, you know all the procedures and facts about it. 通曉","examples":["He knows his way around the intricate maze of patent law. 他通曉錯綜複雜的專利法。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you <b>lead the way</b> along a particular route, you go along it in front of someone in order to show them where to go. 領路","examples":["She grabbed his suitcase and led the way. 她抓過他的手提箱，在前面帶路。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If a person or group <b>leads the way</b> <b>in</b> a particular activity, they are the first person or group to do it or they make the most new developments in it. 領先","examples":["Sony has also led the way in shrinking the size of compact-disc players. 索尼公司在縮小CD播放機尺寸方面也處於領先地位。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>has come a long way</b>, you mean that they have developed, progressed, or become very successful. 取得了長足進步","examples":["He has come a long way since the days he could only afford one meal a day. 和以前那種一天只吃得起一頓飯的日子相比他取得了很大的成就。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a long way from</b> being true, you are emphasizing that it is definitely not true. 還差很遠","examples":["She is a long way from being the richest person in Florida. 她遠遠算不上是佛羅里達最富有的人。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you say that something <b>goes a long way</b> <b>toward</b> doing a particular thing, you mean that it is an important factor in achieving that thing. 是…的重要因素","examples":["Being respectful and courteous goes a long way toward building a relationship. 對人恭謹、彬彬有禮是建立關係的重要因素。"]},{"num":"22.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>lost</b> their <b>way</b>, you are criticizing them because they do not have any good ideas anymore, or seem to have become unsure about what to do. 不知所措","examples":["Why has the White House lost its way on tax and budget policy? 為什麼白宮在稅收和預算政策方面會不知所措呢？"]},{"num":"23.","zh":"When you <b>make</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you walk or travel there. 前往","examples":["He made his way to the marketplace. 他去了市場。"]},{"num":"24.","zh":"If one person or thing <b>makes way</b> <b>for</b> another, the first is replaced by the second. 讓位","examples":["He said he was prepared to make way for younger people in the party. 他說他準備讓位於黨內的年輕人。"]},{"num":"25.","zh":"If you say <b>there's no way</b> that something will happen, you are emphasizing that you think it will definitely not happen. 沒有可能","examples":["There was absolutely no way that we were going to be able to retrieve it. 我們絕對不可能把它找回來。"]},{"num":"26.","zh":"You can say <b>no way</b> as an emphatic way of saying no. 絕不","examples":["Mike, no way am I playing cards with you for money. 邁克，我是決不會和你玩牌賭錢的。"]},{"num":"27.","zh":"If you <b>are on</b> your <b>way</b>, you have started your trip somewhere. 在路途中","examples":["He has been allowed to leave the country and is on his way to Hawaii. 他已獲准離開該國，現正在前往夏威夷的途中。"]},{"num":"28.","zh":"If something happens <b>on the way</b> or <b>along the way</b>, it happens during the course of a particular event or process. 在過程中","examples":["You may have to learn a few new skills along the way. 你也許還得在這個過程中學習一些新的技能。"]},{"num":"29.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> your <b>way</b> or <b>well on</b> your <b>way</b> to something, you have made so much progress that you are almost certain to achieve that thing. 大有進展","examples":["I am now out of the hospital and well on the way to recovery. 我現已出院，很快就會康復。"]},{"num":"30.","zh":"If something is <b>on the way</b>, it will arrive soon. 即將到來","examples":["The forecasters say more snow is on the way. 天氣預報員說不久還將有更多降雪。"]},{"num":"31.","zh":"You can use <b>one way or another</b> or <b>one way or the other</b> when you want to say that something definitely happens, but without giving any details about how it happens. 無論怎樣","examples":["You know pretty well everyone here, one way or the other. 你不管怎麼說肯定非常瞭解這裡的每個人。"]},{"num":"32.","zh":"You use <b>one way or the other</b> or <b>one way or another</b> to refer to two possible decisions or conclusions that have previously been mentioned, without stating which one is reached or preferred. (兩種可能的決定或結論中) 無論哪個","examples":["We've got to make our decision one way or the other. 我們無論如何都得作出決定。"]},{"num":"33.","zh":"You use <b>the other way around</b> to refer to the opposite of what you have just said. 相反地","examples":["You'd think you were the one who did me the favour, and not the other way around. 你會認為是你幫助了我，而不是我幫助了你。"]},{"num":"34.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>on the way out</b> or <b>on</b> their <b>way out</b>, they are likely to disappear or to be replaced very soon. 行將消失; 即將被取代","examples":["There are encouraging signs that cold war attitudes are on the way out. 令人欣慰的是有跡象表明冷戰思維行將消失。"]},{"num":"35.","zh":"If you <b>go out of</b> your <b>way</b> <b>to</b> do something, for example, to help someone, you make a special effort to do it. 特地","examples":["He was very kind to me and seemed to go out of his way to help me. 他對我非常友善，好像是在特意幫我的忙。"]},{"num":"36.","zh":"If you <b>keep out of</b> someone's <b>way</b> or <b>stay out of</b> their <b>way</b>, you avoid them or do not get involved with them. 躲避某人","examples":["I'd kept out of his way as much as I could. 我一直儘量躲避著他。"]},{"num":"37.","zh":"When something is <b>out of the way</b>, it has finished or you have dealt with it, so that it is no longer a problem or needs no more time spent on it. 結束; 得到解決","examples":["The plan has to remain confidential at least until the local elections are out of the way. 此項計劃至少得保密到地方選舉結束為止。"]},{"num":"38.","zh":"If you <b>go</b> your <b>own way</b>, you do what you want rather than what everyone else does or expects. 自行其是","examples":["In school I was a loner. I went my own way. 在學校裡我是個不合群的人，自行其是。"]},{"num":"39.","zh":"You use <b>in the same way</b> to introduce a situation that you are comparing with one that you have just mentioned, because there is a strong similarity between them. 同樣地","examples":["There is no reason why an aircraft designer should also be a good pilot. In the same way, a good pilot can be a bad driver. 沒有理由期待一個飛機設計師同時也是一個優秀的飛行員。同樣的道理，優秀的飛行員可能是個糟糕的汽車駕駛員。"]},{"num":"40.","zh":"You can use <b>that way</b> and <b>this way</b> to refer to a statement or comment that you have just made. 那樣; 這樣","examples":["We have a beautiful city and we pray it stays that way. 我們擁有一個漂亮的城市，並祈禱永遠如此。"]},{"num":"41.","zh":"You can use <b>that way</b> or <b>this way</b> to refer to an action or situation that you have just mentioned, when you go on to mention the likely consequence or effect of it. 那樣; 這樣(用於引出結果)","examples":["Keep the soil moist. That way, the seedling will flourish. 保持土壤溼潤,那樣小苗就會茁壯成長。"]}]}]},"wide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寬的，寬闊的，廣闊的；…寬的（用於數詞或度量短語後）；張大的，完全張開的（指眼睛、嘴等）；廣泛的，範圍廣的；差距大的，程度大的；偏離的，未中的，遠離目標的；寬鬆的，肥大的（指衣物）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"廣泛地，廣闊地，遠及各處；充分地，完全地；偏離目標地，未中地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大千世界，廣闊的世界；（板球）投偏的球，偏球；（Wide）維德（瑞典、芬蘭人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>wide</b> measures a large distance from one side or edge to the other. 寬的","examples":["All worktops should be wide enough to allow plenty of space for food preparation. 所有的廚房操作檯都必須足夠寬，以便有充足的空間準備食物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you open or spread something <b>wide</b>, you open or spread it as far as possible or to the fullest extent. 完全張開的","examples":["\"It was huge,\" he announced, spreading his arms wide. “它大極了，”他大張開雙臂比劃著說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>wide</b> to talk or ask about how much something measures from one side or edge to the other. …寬的","examples":["...a corridor of land four miles wide. …一條4英里寬的陸地走廊。","The road is only one lane wide. 這條路只有一個車道那麼寬。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>wide</b> to describe something that includes a large number of different things or people. 範圍廣的","examples":["The brochure offers a wide choice of hotels, apartments and holiday homes. 這本手冊提供了選擇範圍很廣的旅館、公寓及度假屋。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>wide</b> to say that something is found, believed, known, or supported by many people or throughout a large area. 廣泛的","examples":["The case has attracted wide publicity. 這個案件得到廣泛的關注。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>wide</b> difference or gap between two things, ideas, or qualities is a large difference or gap. (不同或差距) 很大的","examples":["Research shows a wide difference in tastes around the country. 研究表明全國各地的口味大不相同。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Wider</b> is used to describe something that relates to the most important or general parts of a situation, rather than to the smaller parts or to details. 更大的","examples":["He emphasized the wider issue of superpower cooperation. 他強調超級大國合作這個更大的話題。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"範圍廣地","examples":["He published widely in scientific journals. 他在科學期刊上廣泛地發表各類文章。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"廣泛地","examples":["At present, no widely approved vaccine exists for malaria. 目前沒有被廣泛認可的瘧疾疫苗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"很大地","examples":["The treatment regime may vary widely depending on the type of injury. 治療方法可能會因受傷型別的不同而有很大差別。"]}]}]},"well":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"順利地，令人滿意地；熟練地，技術好地；妥善地，恰當地；讚揚地，讚許地；有益地，有利地；容易地；友善地；有充分理由，合理地；很，非常；富裕地，舒適地；完全地，充分地；大大地，遠遠地；（程度或標準）多少，怎樣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"健康的；令人滿意的；明智的，可取的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水井，油井，氣井；樓梯井，電梯井道；<英>（法庭中的）律師席；韋爾斯（有礦泉的地方）（Wells）；（儲液體的）凹槽；（大量）來源，源泉；吧檯酒架；廉價酒；（物理）勢阱，電位阱"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於表示想要開口說話）嗯，好；唔，嗯，哦（表示對要說的話不確定）；好吧，算了（對不愉快的事表示接受）；好啦，哎呀（用於勸說或讓人不要生氣、焦慮等）；噯（表示生氣或不贊成）；怎麼樣呢，哎（表示等待回答或行動）；好啦（用於結束活動或對話）；（停頓後繼續交談）唔，這個；（表示驚奇、憤怒或寬慰）哎呀，喲，啊；噢（用於糾正剛才說過的話）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（液體）流出，湧出；（感情）湧上，湧起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> to indicate that you are about to say something. 哦 (用於將要說的話之前)","examples":["Well, it's a pleasure to meet you. 哦,很高興見到你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> just before or after you pause, especially to give yourself time to think about what you are going to say. (用於說話停頓的前後，尤用於給自己考慮的時間) 嗯","examples":["Look, I'm really sorry I woke you, and, well, I just wanted to tell you I was all right. 你看，我真抱歉吵醒了你，嗯，我只是想告訴你我一切都很好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> when you are correcting something that you have just said. (用於更正剛說過的話) 哦","examples":["The comet is going to come back in 2061 and we are all going to be able to see it. Well, our offspring are, anyway. 這顆彗星將於2061年返回，到時我們都可以看到它。哦，無論如何，我們子孫是可以看到的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> to express your doubt about something that someone has said. (用於表示對別人說過的話的懷疑) 啊","examples":["\"But finance is far more serious.\"—\"Well I don't know really.\" “但是財政形勢更加嚴峻了。”—“啊，我真的不知道。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>well</b>, you do it to a high standard or to a great extent. (標準或程度) 出色地","examples":["It's important that we play well at home. 重要的是我們應該打好國內的比賽。","He speaks English better than I do. 他英語比我講得好。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you do something <b>well</b>, you do it thoroughly and completely. 完全地","examples":["Mix all the ingredients well. 把所有配料攪拌均勻。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you speak or think <b>well</b> <b>of</b> someone, you say or think favorable things about them. (評價) 令人滿意地","examples":["\"He speaks well of you.\"—\"I'm glad to hear that.\" “他對你評價很高。”—“很高興聽見這話。”"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> to ask or talk about the extent or standard of something. (程度或標準) 怎樣","examples":["How well do you remember your mother, Franzi? 關於你的母親你還記得多少，弗蘭齊？","He wasn't dressed any better than me. 他穿得並不比我好多少。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> in front of a prepositional phrase to emphasize it. For example, if you say that one thing happened <b>well before</b> another, you mean that it happened a long time before it. (用於介詞短語之前，表示強調) 遠遠地; 很久地","examples":["Franklin did not turn up until well after midnight. 富蘭克林直到午夜過後很久才露面。","...a war in which well over a million people died. …一場死亡人數遠遠超過一百萬人的戰爭。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> before certain adjectives to emphasize them. (用於某些形容詞之前，表示強調) 很","examples":["She has a close group of friends who are very well aware of what she has suffered. 她有一群密友，十分了解她的遭遇。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> after adverbs such as \"perfectly,\" \"jolly,\" or \"damn\" in order to emphasize an opinion or the truth of what you are saying. 用於(perfectly), (jolly), (damn)副詞之後，強調觀點或真相","examples":["You know perfectly well I can't be blamed for the failure of that mission. 你非常清楚這次任務的失敗不該怪我。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> after verbs such as \"may\" and \"could\" when you are saying what you think is likely to happen. (用於may, could等詞的後面) 很可能","examples":["Ours could well be the last generation for which moviegoing has a sense of magic. 我們很可能是感到去電影院看電影很神奇的最後一代人。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> to express your surprise or anger at something that someone has just said or done. (用於表達驚訝或氣憤) 哎呀","examples":["She beamed at Patty. \"Well! That was a bit of unexpected excitement.\" 她對帕蒂燦爛地一笑。“哎呀，那真是有些出人意料，叫人興奮哦。”"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>well</b> to indicate that you are waiting for someone to say something and often to express your irritation with them. (用於等待別人回應，常表示不耐煩) 嗯","examples":["\"Well?\" asked Barry, \"What does it tell us?\" “嗯？”巴里問道，“這到底告訴我們什麼呢？”","\"Well, why don't you ask me?\" he said finally. “嗯，那你為什麼不問我呢？”他最後說了一句。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>well</b> to indicate that you are amused by something you have heard or seen, and often to introduce a comment on it. (表示高興並常引出評價) 好啊","examples":["Well, well, well. How quickly things change. 好啊，好啊，好啊。變化真快啊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>oh well</b> to indicate that you accept a situation or that someone else should accept it, even though you or they are not very happy about it, because it is not too bad and cannot be changed. (表示勉強接受) 算了","examples":["Oh well, it could be worse. 哎，算了，情況本可能會更糟的。","\"I called her and she said no.\"—\"Oh well.\" “我給她打過電話，但她拒絕了。”—“唉，那就算了吧。”"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Well</b> is used in front of past participles to indicate that something is done to a high standard or to a great extent. 用於過去分詞之前，表示高水準或高程度","examples":["Helen is a very well-known novelist in Australia. 海倫是澳大利亞著名的小說家。","People live longer nowadays, and they are better educated. 如今，人們越來越長壽，受教育程度也提高了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>well</b>, you are healthy and not ill. 健康的","examples":["I'm not very well today, I can't come in. 我今天身體不太舒服，不能參加了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as well</b> when mentioning something that happens in the same way as something else already mentioned, or that should be considered at the same time as that thing. 也","examples":["It is most often diagnosed in women in their thirties and forties, although I've seen it in many younger women, as well. 這種病多發於三四十歲女性的身上，不過我見過很多更年輕的女性也患了此症。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>as well as</b> when you want to mention another item connected with the subject you are discussing. 除了…外 (還); 和","examples":["The movie will appeal to adults as well as children. 這部電影除了將吸引兒童外，還會吸引成年人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something that has happened <b>is just as well</b>, you mean that it is fortunate that it happened in the way it did. 幸好","examples":["Blue asbestos is far less common in buildings, which is just as well because it's more dangerous than white asbestos. 藍色的石棉在建築中要少見得多，幸好是這樣，因為它比白色石棉更危險。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something, usually something bad, <b>might as well</b> be true or <b>may as well</b> be true, you mean that the situation is the same or almost the same as if it were true. 簡直就像…一樣 (常指不好的事情)","examples":["The couple might as well have been strangers. 這對夫婦簡直就像是陌路人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>might as well</b> do something, or that you <b>may as well</b> do it, you mean that you will do it although you do not have a strong desire to do it and may even feel slightly unwilling to do it. (做…) 也無妨","examples":["If I've got to go somewhere I may as well go to Tulsa. 如果我必須去一個地方的話，我就去塔爾薩吧。","Anyway, you're here; you might as well stay. 無論如何你已在這裡，你就留下來吧。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>well and truly</b> finished, gone, or done, you are emphasizing that it is completely finished or gone, or thoroughly done. 徹底地","examples":["The war is well and truly over. 戰爭徹底結束了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>well</b> is a hole in the ground from which a supply of water is extracted. 水井","examples":["I had to fetch water from the well. 我得去從水井裡打水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>well</b> is an oil well. 油井","examples":["About 650 wells are on fire. 約六百五十口油井在燃燒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If liquids <b>well</b>, they come to the surface and form a pool. (液體) 湧出","examples":["Tears welled in her eyes. 淚水從她的眼中湧出。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Well up</b> means the same as <b>well</b>. 湧出","examples":["Tears welled up in Anni's eyes. 淚水從安妮的眼中湧出。"]}]}]},"winter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冬季，（天文）從冬至點到春分點的期間；<文>年，歲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冬天的，冬天出現的；用於冬天的；（水果）冬季才成熟的；（麥等）秋季播種來年收穫的，越冬的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在某處）過冬，越冬；使度過冬季"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Winter</b> is the season between fall and spring. In the winter the weather is usually cold. 冬季","examples":["In winter the nights are long and cold. 冬季的夜晚又長又冷。","...the late winter of 1941. …1941年的晚冬。"]}]}]},"window":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"窗，窗玻璃；（計算機螢幕的）視窗；（信封上的）透明紙窗；（商店的）陳列窗，櫥窗；一絲的機會，短暫的時機；觀察（或學習）的渠道；（辦理業務的）視窗；（物理）大氣窗；（干擾雷達用的）金屬箔片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>window</b> is a space in the wall of a building or in the side of a vehicle, which has glass in it so that light can come in and you can see out. 窗戶","examples":["He stood at the window, moodily staring out. 他站在窗旁，憂鬱地盯著外面。","The room felt very hot and she wondered why someone did not open a window. 房間裡感覺非常熱，她納悶為什麼沒人開啟一扇窗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>window</b> is a glass-covered opening above a counter, for example, in a bank, post office, train station, or museum, which the person serving you sits behind. (銀行、郵局、火車站、博物館等提供服務的) 視窗","examples":["The woman at the ticket window told me that the admission fee was $17.50. 售票視窗的那位女士告訴我入場費為$17.50。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On a computer screen, a <b>window</b> is one of the work areas that the screen can be divided into. (電腦螢幕上的) 視窗","examples":["Yahoo! Pager puts a small window on your screen containing a list of your \"friends.\" 雅虎通在您的螢幕上彈出一個包含您的“朋友”名單的小視窗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something such as a plan or a particular way of thinking or behaving <b>has gone out of the window</b> or <b>is out the window</b>, you mean that it has disappeared completely. (計劃或某種思維或行為方式) 完全消失","examples":["By now all logic had gone out of the window. 到此時，已沒有什麼道理可講。"]}]}]},"woman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成年女子，婦女；（泛指）女性；帶修飾語指來自……（或做……、喜歡……等）的女子；女工，女僕；<非正式>妻子，女友，情人；（盛氣凌人的稱呼）女人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>使女性化；<罕>配備女性員工；<罕>使（某人）與女性交往"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>woman</b> is an adult female human being. 成年女子","examples":["...a young Lithuanian woman named Dayva. …一個名叫戴瓦的年輕立陶宛女子。","...men and women over 75 years old. …75歲以上的男女。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to women in general as <b>woman</b>. 女性","examples":["...the oppression of woman. …對女性的壓迫。"]}]}]},"win":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在戰鬥、比賽、遊戲等中）贏，獲勝；贏得（獎品等）；透過努力得到（某物）；為……贏得，使……獲得；採（礦）；晾（乾草）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（在比賽、競賽等中的）勝利"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>win</b> something such as a competition, battle, or argument, you defeat those people you are competing or fighting against, or you do better than everyone else involved. 贏得 (比賽、戰爭或辯論等); 贏","examples":["He does not have any realistic chance of winning the election. 他沒有任何贏得這次選舉的實際機會。","The top four teams all won. 排名最靠前的4支隊伍都贏了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>wins</b> you something such as an election, competition, battle, or argument, it causes you to defeat the people competing with you or fighting you, or to do better than everyone else involved. 使…贏得 (選舉、比賽、戰爭或辯論等)","examples":["The Democrats had found a message that could win them the White House. 民主黨人已找到了一條可以使他們贏得總統選舉的口號。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>win</b> something such as a prize or medal, you get it because you have defeated everyone else in something such as an election, competition, battle, or argument, or have done very well in it. 贏得 (獎或獎牌)","examples":["Trent Dimas won gold in the final men's gymnastic event. 特倫特·迪馬斯在男子體操決賽中贏得了金牌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>win</b> something that you want or need, you succeed in getting it. 贏得 (想要或需要的事物)","examples":["...moves to win the support of the poor. …贏得窮人支援的舉措。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Win</b> is also a noun. 贏","examples":["The voters gave a narrow win to Vargas Llosa. 選民們使瓦爾加斯·略薩取得險勝。"]}]}]},"will":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"將，將要；請（請求某人做某事）；總是，慣於；（表示對習慣性發生行為不滿）老是，一直；可能，大概；願意，樂意；必須，一定；表示能力、容量能；（表示承諾或威脅）會，要；希望，想要；立定志向，決意；立遺囑遺贈"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"意志，決心，毅力；意願，心願；遺囑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to indicate that you hope, think, or have evidence that something is going to happen or be the case in the future. 將會","examples":["I'm sure we will find a wide variety of choices available in school cafeterias. 我相信我們將會發現學校的自助餐廳裡有多種多樣的選擇。","Will you ever feel at home here? 你在這兒會感到自在嗎？","The ship will not be ready for a month. 這艘船一個月內將不會準備就緒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> in order to make statements about official arrangements in the future. 表示將來的正式安排","examples":["The show will be open to the public at 2 pm; admission will be $5. 展覽將於下午2點對公眾開放；入場費為$5。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> in order to make promises and threats about what is going to happen or be the case in the future. (表示承諾或威脅) 將","examples":["I'll call you tonight. 我今晚將會打電話給你。","Price quotes on selected product categories will be sent on request. 所選產品型別的報價將索要即寄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to indicate someone's intention to do something. 想要","examples":["I will say no more on these matters, important though they are. 我不想對這些事再說些什麼，儘管它們很重要。","In this section we will describe common myths about cigarettes, alcohol, and marijuana. 在這一節我們想講述有關香菸、酒和大麻的一些常見的錯誤認識。","\"Dinner's ready.\"—\"Thanks, Carrie, but we'll have a drink first.\" “晚飯做好了。” — “謝謝，卡麗，但是我們想先喝一杯。”","Will you be remaining in the city? 你想留在這座城市裡嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> in questions in order to make polite invitations or offers. …好嗎 (用在問句中，表示禮貌的邀請或提議)","examples":["Will you stay for supper? 你留下來吃晚飯好嗎？","Will you join me for a drink? 和我喝一杯好嗎？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> in questions in order to ask or tell someone to do something. 好嗎 (用在問句中，表示請人或告訴某人做某事)","examples":["Will you drive me home? 你開車送我回家好嗎？","Will you listen again, Andrew? 再聽一遍好嗎，安德魯？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to say that someone is willing to do something. You use <b>will not</b> or <b>won't</b> to indicate that someone refuses to do something. 願意","examples":["All right, I'll forgive you. 好吧，我願意原諒你。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to say that a person or thing is able to do something in the future. 表示將來能做某事","examples":["How the country will defend itself in the future has become increasingly important. 這個國家將來如何防禦已經變得越來越重要。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to indicate that an action usually happens in the particular way mentioned. 通常會 (用於表明某動作通常以特定方式發生)","examples":["The thicker the material, the less susceptible the garment will be to wet conditions. 布料越厚，衣服通常就越不容易浸溼。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> in the main clause of some \"if\" and \"unless\" sentences to indicate something that you consider to be fairly likely to happen. 會 (用在)(if)(和)(unless)(引導的從句的主句中，表示某事很可能發生)","examples":["If you overcook the meat it will be dry. 你如果煮過頭，肉會很乾。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>will</b> to say that someone insists on behaving or doing something in a particular way and you cannot change them. You emphasize <b>will</b> when you use it in this way. 總是要","examples":["He will leave his socks lying all over the place and it drives me crazy. 他總是把襪子丟得到處都是，這簡直讓我發瘋。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>will have</b> with a past participle when you are saying that you are fairly certain that something will be true by a particular time in the future. (與過去分詞連用，表示某事將來肯定如此) 將已經","examples":["As many as ten-million children will have been infected with the virus by the end of the decade. 多達1千萬的兒童到這個時代末將已染上這種病毒。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>will have</b> with a past participle to indicate that you are fairly sure that something is the case. (與過去分詞連用，表示相當肯定) 將","examples":["Jack will have been very upset by all this. 這一切肯定會讓傑克非常難過。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Will</b> is the determination to do something. 意志","examples":["He was said to have lost his will to live. 據說他已經喪失了活下去的意志。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>the</b> <b>will</b> <b>of</b> a person or group of people with authority, they want it to happen. 意願","examples":["He has submitted himself to the will of God. 他已經讓自己聽從上帝的意旨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>will</b> is a document in which you declare what you want to happen to your money and property when you die. 遺囑","examples":["Attached to his will was a letter he had written to his wife just days before his death. 他遺囑中附帶的是他去世前幾天寫給妻子的一封信。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>will</b> something <b>to</b> happen, you try to make it happen by using mental effort rather than physical effort. 希望 (某事發生)","examples":["I looked at the telephone, willing it to ring. 我看著電話，希望它響起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>against</b> your <b>will</b>, it is done even though you do not want it to be done. 違背某人的意願","examples":["No doubt he was forced to leave his family against his will. 毫無疑問，他是被迫違心地離開家人的。"]}]}]},"wood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木材，木料，木頭；樹林，林地；（高爾夫）木頭球棒，木棒；木製酒桶；木棒揮擊；（滾木球戲中所用重心略偏的）圓球；（保齡球戲的）木瓶；上天保佑（表示希望繼續走好運）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"木製的；用來切割或加工木材的；用木材做燃料的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"收集木材；植林於；給……新增木柴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wood</b> is the material that forms the trunks and branches of trees. 木頭","examples":["Their dishes were made of wood. 他們的盤子是用木頭製成的。","There was a smell of damp wood and machine oil. 有一股溼木頭和機油的氣味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wood</b> or <b>woods</b> is a fairly large area of trees growing near each other. 樹林","examples":["After dinner Alice slipped away for a walk in the woods with Artie. 晚飯後，艾麗斯悄悄溜到樹林裡與阿迪散步。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to plant a wood upon 在…上植樹","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>not out of the woods</b> yet, they are still having difficulties or problems. 尚未擺脫困境","examples":["The nation's economy is not out of the woods yet. 該國的經濟尚未擺脫困境。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>knock on wood</b>\" to indicate that you hope to have good luck in something you are doing, usually after saying that you have been lucky with it so far. 但願好運仍在","examples":["I got it all taken care of, knock on wood. 我把它各個方面都照顧到了，但願好運仍在。"]}]}]},"wish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"希望（做某事），想要（某事發生）；祝，祝願（某人好運、幸福等）；願望，心願；希望（不可能或可能性很小的事變成事實）；真希望（用於表示對做過某事或未做某事感到後悔或失望）；（用來表示對某人行為的厭煩）我希望……；（用於要說的話可能使人不快或擔心等時）不想，無意；這是再好不過的，沒有比這更好的了；希望……發生在……身上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"希望，願望；（靠魔術實現的）願望，心願；（書信或賀卡等中的）祝願，祝福（wishes）；想要的東西，希望的事；請求，要求"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wish</b> is a desire or strong feeling that you want to have something or do something. 願望","examples":["She was sincere and genuine in her wish to make amends for the past. 她誠懇而真心地希望彌補過去的錯誤。","The decision was made against the wishes of the party leader. 這項決定是在違背該黨領袖願望的情況下作出的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wish</b> is also a noun. 祈願","examples":["The custom is for people to try and eat 12 grapes as the clock strikes midnight. Those who are successful can make a wish. 這個習俗是讓人們在午夜鐘聲敲響時試著吃12顆葡萄。那些成功做到這一點的人就可以許個願。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you express your good <b>wishes</b> toward someone, you are politely expressing your friendly feelings toward them and your hope that they will be successful or happy. 祝福","examples":["I found George's story very sad. Please give him my best wishes. 我覺得喬治的經歷很可憐。請向他表達我最好的祝福。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wish</b> to do something or to have it done for you, you want to do it or have it done. 想要","examples":["If you wish to go away for the weekend, our office will be delighted to make hotel reservations. 如果您想在週末外出，我們的辦事處將很高興為您預定旅館。","We can dress as we wish now. 我們如今想穿什麼就可以穿什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wish</b> something were true, you would like it to be true, even though you know that it is impossible or unlikely. 但願 (表某事不可能成為現實)","examples":["I wish I could do that. 我但願我能做那件事。","Pa, I wish you wouldn't shout. 爸，我但願你不要嚷嚷了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you would not <b>wish</b> a particular thing <b>on</b> someone, you mean that the thing is so unpleasant that you would not want them to be forced to experience it. (不) 希望 (不愉快的事會發生在某人身上)","examples":["It's a horrid experience and I wouldn't wish it on my worst enemy. 這是一次可怕的經歷，我甚至不希望它發生在我仇敵的身上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>wish</b> someone something such as luck or happiness, you express the hope that they will be lucky or happy. 祝願","examples":["I wish you both a good trip. 我祝你們倆旅途愉快。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wish for</b> something, you express the desire for that thing silently to yourself. In fairy tales, when a person wishes for something, the thing they wish for often happens by magic. 默默期盼","examples":["Be careful what you wish for. You might get it! 留意你所期盼的。你可能會得到它！"]}]}]},"wind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風，氣流；風向，逼近的形勢；呼吸，呼吸能力；腸胃氣脹；管樂器，吹奏樂器；大話，空談；放屁；彎，彎曲處；一圈，一轉；（給鐘錶）上發條；（由風帶來，表明附近有動物、人存在的）氣味"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"彎曲前進，蜿蜒而行；捲纏，纏繞，繞成團；卷繞（磁帶等）；給（鍾、表）上發條；轉動（把手）；（用轆轤、絞車等）吊起（某物）；使喘不過氣來，使喘大氣；給（嬰兒）拍嗝兒； 嗅出（人，動物）的氣味；<文>吹（號角，哨子）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"管樂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wind</b> is a current of air that is moving across the earth's surface. 風","examples":["There was a strong wind blowing. 正颳著一陣大風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Journalists often refer to a trend or factor that influences events as a <b>wind</b> <b>of</b> a particular kind. (影響事態發展的) 趨勢; 因素","examples":["The winds of change are blowing across the country. 轉變之風正吹遍全國。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a single turn, bend, etc 拐彎","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are winded</b> by something such as a blow, the air is suddenly knocked out of your lungs so that you have difficulty breathing for a short time. 呼吸困難","examples":["He was winded and shaken. 他呼吸困難，身體發抖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a road, river, or line of people <b>winds</b> in a particular direction, it goes in that direction with a lot of bends or twists in it. (路、河流或一行人) 蜿蜒而行","examples":["Quiet mountain roads wind through groves of bamboo and cedar. 幽靜的山路蜿蜒穿過竹林和雪松林。","...a narrow winding road. …一條狹窄蜿蜒的道路。","We wound our way southeast. 我們向東南方向蜿蜒前行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>wind</b> something flexible around something else, you wrap it around it several times. 纏繞","examples":["The horse jumped forward and around her, winding the rope around her waist. 那匹馬向前一跳，然後圍著她把繩子纏在她的腰際。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>wind</b> a mechanical device, for example, a watch or a clock, you turn a knob, key, or handle on it several times in order to make it operate. 給 (鐘錶等) 上發條","examples":["I still hadn't wound my watch so I didn't know the time. 我還沒給手錶上發條，所以我不知道時間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>wind</b> a tape or film <b>back</b> or <b>forward</b> means to make it move toward its starting or ending position. 倒/快進 (磁帶或膠捲)","examples":["The camcorder winds the tape back or forward at high speed. 行動式攝像機可以高速度倒帶或快進。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>breaks wind</b>, they release gas from their intestines through their anus. 放屁","examples":["If I break wind at dinner, should I say \"Pardon,\" or pretend nothing has happened? 如果我在用餐的時候放屁，我是應該說“對不起”，還是假裝什麼事情都沒發生？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get wind of</b> something, you hear about it, especially when someone else did not want you to know about it. 聽到…的訊息 (尤指在別人不想讓知道的情況下)","examples":["I don't want the public, and especially not the press, to get wind of it at this stage. 我不想讓公眾，尤其是新聞界，在這個階段聽到什麼訊息。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wind up</b> means the same as <b>wind</b>. 給 (鐘錶等) 上發條","examples":["I wound up the watch and listened to it tick. 我給手錶上好發條，聽著它滴答作響。"]}]}]},"worker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工作者，工作人員；勞工，工人；工作做得……的人；工人階級（the workers）；工蜂，工蟻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>worker</b> does the kind of work mentioned. 人員","examples":["She ate her sandwich alongside several other office workers taking their break. 她在其他幾位正在休息的辦公室人員旁邊吃自己的三明治。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Workers</b> are people who are employed in industry or business and who are not managers. 工人; 員工","examples":["Wages have been frozen and workers laid off. 工資已被凍結，員工們下崗了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>worker</b> to say how well or badly someone works. 工作 (好或壞) 的人","examples":["He is a hard worker and a skilled gardener. 他是一個工作努力的人，一個技藝嫻熟的園藝工。"]}]}]},"worm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蠕蟲；（某些昆蟲的）幼蟲；寄生蟲，寄生蟲病；小人物，懦夫；蠕蟲病毒；蛆蟲；螺紋狀物，蝸桿，旋管"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給動物）驅腸蟲；蠕動，曲折行進；（通常為欺騙別人或得到好處）逐漸取得（成功或好感）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"一次寫入型光碟，單寫多讀型光碟（write-once read-many）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>worm</b> is a small animal with a long thin body, no bones, and no legs. 蠕蟲","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>worm</b> is a computer program that contains a virus which duplicates itself many times in a network. 蠕蟲病毒","examples":["...a new computer worm that disables security software. …一種使安全軟體失靈的新型計算機蠕蟲病毒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is worming</b> their <b>way</b> to success, or <b>is worming</b> their <b>way</b> into someone else's affection, you disapprove of the way that they are gradually making someone trust them or like them, often in order to deceive them or gain some advantage. 贏得 (歡心等)","examples":["She never misses a chance to worm her way into the public's hearts. 她從不錯過任何討公眾喜愛的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is opening <b>a can of worms</b>, you are warning them that they are planning to do or talk about something that is much more complicated, unpleasant, or difficult than they realize and that might be better left alone. 馬蜂窩","examples":["Introducing this legislation would be like opening a can of worms. 提出這項法規會像捅了馬蜂窩一樣。"]}]}]},"wine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葡萄酒，果蔬酒；深紫紅色"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"喝酒；設酒宴款待（某人）；<西印度>跳擺臀舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wine</b> is an alcoholic drink made from grapes. You can also refer to alcoholic drinks made from other fruits or vegetables as <b>wine</b>. 葡萄酒; 果酒","examples":["...a bottle of white wine. …一瓶白葡萄酒。"]}]}]},"worse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"更糟的，更壞的，更差的；（病得）更厲害的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"更壞，更差，更糟；更糟的是，更倒黴的是"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"更糟的事，更惡劣的情況"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worse</b> is the comparative of . (bad)的比較級","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Worse</b> is the comparative of . (badly)的比較級","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation changes <b>for the worse</b>, it becomes more unpleasant or more difficult. 更糟糕的情況","examples":["The grandparents sigh and say how things have changed for the worse. 祖父母嘆著氣然後說事情是如何變得更糟糕的。"]}]}]},"writer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（職業的）作家，作者；執筆者，撰寫人；寫字……的人；（計算機）記錄器；〈英，史〉文書，抄寫員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>writer</b> is a person who writes books, stories, or articles as a job. 作家","examples":["Turner is a writer and critic. 特納是一位作家和評論家。","...detective stories by American writers. …美國作家們的那些偵探故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>writer</b> of a particular article, report, letter, or story is the person who wrote it. 撰寫者","examples":["No one is to see the document without the permission of the writer of the report. 任何人沒有報告撰寫者的允許不得看這份檔案。"]}]}]},"xmas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聖誕節（Christmas 的非正式書面縮寫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Xmas</b> is used in informal written English to represent the word Christmas. 聖誕節 (非正式書面形式)","examples":["It would be nice to have my Dad home for Xmas. 聖誕節有爸爸在家就好了。"]}]}]},"worry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擔心，發愁；使擔憂，使發愁，使焦慮；煩擾，使不安寧；（狗）追趕，撕咬（其他動物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"令人擔憂的事，令人發愁的問題；擔心，憂慮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>worry</b>, you keep thinking about problems that you have or about unpleasant things that might happen. 擔心","examples":["Don't worry, your luggage will come on afterwards by taxi. 不要擔心，你的行李隨後將由計程車送到。","I worry about her constantly. 我一直在為她擔心。","They worry that high interest rates are keeping the dollar too high. 他們擔心高利率會使美元比值過高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>worries</b> you, they make you anxious because you keep thinking about problems or unpleasant things that might be connected with them. 使擔心","examples":["I'm still in the early days of my recovery and that worries me. 我仍處於恢復期的初始階段，這使我擔心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something does not <b>worry</b> you, you do not dislike them or you are not annoyed by them. 使煩惱 (用於否定句中)","examples":["The cold doesn't worry me. 寒冷不會使我煩惱。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worry</b> is the state or feeling of anxiety and unhappiness caused by the problems that you have or by thinking about unpleasant things that might happen. 憂慮","examples":["Modern American life is full of worry: the job, the kids, money, the stock market. 現代美國生活充滿了憂慮：工作、孩子、金錢、股市。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>worry</b> is a problem that you keep thinking about and that makes you unhappy. 令人煩惱的事","examples":["My main worry was that Madeleine Johnson would still be there. 我的主要煩惱是瑪得琳•約翰遜還會在那裡。"]}]}]},"yam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薯蕷，山藥；〈北美〉番薯，山芋"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<愛爾蘭，蘇格蘭>貓叫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yam</b> is a root vegetable like a potato with orange flesh that grows in tropical regions. 薯蕷; 山藥","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Yams</b> are the same as <b>sweet potatoes</b>. 同sweet potato","examples":[]}]}]},"worst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最差的，最糟的，最嚴重的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最差地，最糟地，最嚴重地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最壞的人（或事），最糟的情況"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打敗，擊敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worst</b> is the superlative of . (bad)的最高階","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Worst</b> is the superlative of . (badly)的最高階","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Worst</b> is used to form the superlative of compound adjectives beginning with \"bad\" and \"badly.\" For example, the superlative of \"badly-affected\" is \"worst-affected.\" 最糟糕地 (以)(bad)(或)(badly)(開頭的複合形容詞的最高階)","examples":["The worst-affected areas were in Jefferson Parish. 影響最嚴重的地區是在傑斐遜教區。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The worst</b> is the most unpleasant or unfavorable thing that could happen or does happen. 最糟糕的情況","examples":["Though mine safety has much improved, miners' families still fear the worst. 雖然礦井安全已極大改善，礦工的家屬們仍然擔心發生最糟糕的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>worst of all</b> to indicate that what you are about to mention is the most unpleasant or has the most disadvantages out of all the things you are mentioning. 最糟糕的是","examples":["The people most closely affected are the passengers who were injured and, worst of all, those who lost relatives. 受影響最嚴重的是那些受傷的乘客，最糟糕的是其中那些失去親人的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>at worst</b> or <b>at the worst</b> to indicate that you are mentioning the worst thing that might happen in a situation. 最糟糕的情況是","examples":["At best Nella would be an invalid; at worst she would die. 最好的情況是內納會成為一個殘疾人，最糟糕的情況是她會死亡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone is <b>at their worst</b>, they are as unpleasant, bad, or unsuccessful as it is possible for them to be. 最糟糕的","examples":["This was their mother at her worst. Her voice was strident, she was ready to be angry at anyone. 這是他們的母親最糟糕的情形。她聲音刺耳，隨時會對人發脾氣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>if worst comes to worst</b> or <b>if the worst comes to the worst</b> to say what you might do if a situation develops in the most unfavorable way possible. 如果最糟的情形產生","examples":["If worst comes to worst, Europe could withstand a trade war. 如果最糟的情形產生，歐洲可以頂住一場貿易戰。"]}]}]},"world":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"世界，地球，天下；星球，天體；地區，國家，時代；社會，生活；領域，界，圈子；生物界，自然界；人生，生活圈子，閱歷；人世，今生，來世；世俗；（有某種特色的）地方，情景；大量，無數；一切，重要性（the world）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"世界上最重要的，世界聞名的；世界（性）的；環球的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The world</b> is the planet that we live on. 地球","examples":["The satellite enables us to calculate their precise location anywhere in the world. 這顆衛星使得我們可以計算他們在地球上的任何準確位置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>world</b> refers to all the people who live on this planet, and our societies, institutions, and ways of life. 世人","examples":["The world was, and remains, shocked. 世人震驚了，並且仍然震驚。","He wants to show the world that anyone can learn to be an ambassador. 他想向世人展示，任何人都能夠學做一名大使。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>world</b> in expressions such as <b>the Arab world</b>, <b>the Western world</b>, and <b>the ancient world</b> to refer to a particular group of countries or a particular period in history. 世界 (指某些國家或時期)","examples":["Athens had strong ties to the Arab world. 雅典與阿拉伯世界有著緊密的聯絡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>world</b> is the life they lead, the people they have contact with, and the things they experience. 生活世界; 生活圈子","examples":["His world seemed so different from mine. 他的生活圈子與我的似乎是那麼的不同。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>world</b> to refer to a particular field of activity, and the people involved in it. 界","examples":["The publishing world had certainly never seen an event quite like this. 出版界當然從未見過類似這樣的事情。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>world</b> to refer to a particular group of living things, for example, <b>the animal world</b>, <b>the plant world</b>, and <b>the insect world</b>. (某生物) 界","examples":["When it comes to dodging disaster, the champions of the insect world have to be cockroaches. 談到躲避災難，昆蟲界的冠軍非蟑螂莫屬。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>world</b> to describe someone or something that is one of the most important or significant of its kind on earth. 世界性的","examples":["China has once again emerged as a world power. 中國再次成為一個世界性的強國。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>the best of both worlds</b>, you mean that they have only the benefits of two things and none of the disadvantages. 兩全其美","examples":["Her living room provides the best of both worlds, with an office at one end and comfortable sofas at the other. 她的起居室兩全其美，一端是個辦公室，另一端有舒服的沙發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>has done</b> someone <b>a world of good</b>, you mean that it has made them feel better or improved their life. 對…大有好處","examples":["Just sit for a while and relax. It will do you a world of good. 就坐一會兒，放鬆放鬆。這將對你大有好處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>in the world</b> in expressions such as <b>what in the world</b> and <b>who in the world</b> to emphasize a question, especially when expressing surprise or anger. 到底 (表示強調)","examples":["What in the world is he doing? 他到底在幹什麼呢？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>in an ideal world</b> or <b>in a perfect world</b> when you are talking about things that you would like to happen, although you realize that they are not likely to happen. 在理想狀態下","examples":["In an ideal world Karen Stevens says she would love to stay at home with her two-and-half-year-old son. 卡林·斯蒂芬斯說，她願意和兩歲半的兒子待在家裡，但那只是理想狀態。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>the outside world</b> to refer to all the people who do not live in a particular place or who are not involved in a particular situation. 外界","examples":["For many, the post office is the only link with the outside world. 對許多人來說，郵局是與外界聯絡的惟一紐帶。"]}]}]},"yellow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"黃的，黃色的；黃色人種的，黃皮膚的；<非正式>膽怯的；（新聞報道）誇張失實的，聳人聽聞的；黃色危險警報的；嫉妒的，猜疑的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃色，黃顏料；黃色衣服，黃色衣料；（運動或比賽中的）黃色球，黃色物（尤指斯諾克的黃球）；黃蛾（或黃蝴蝶）；（植物的）黃化病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變黃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>yellow</b> is the colour of lemons, butter, or the middle part of an egg. 黃色 (的)","examples":["The walls have been painted bright yellow. 這些牆壁已被漆成亮黃色。"]}]}]},"yesterday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在昨天；日前，不久前"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"昨天；最近，往昔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>yesterday</b> to refer to the day before today. 昨天","examples":["She left yesterday. 她昨天離開了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yesterday</b> is also a noun. 昨天","examples":["In yesterday's games, Switzerland beat the United States two to one. 在昨天的比賽中，瑞士隊2比1打敗了美國隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the past, especially the recent past, as <b>yesterday</b>. (尤指不久前的) 過去","examples":["The worker of today is different from the worker of yesterday. 如今的工人跟過去的工人不一樣了。"]}]}]},"yes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"是，是的，對；是嗎？（升調，表示疑問或請對方繼續說）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"是（表示肯定），肯定答覆；贊成票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to give a positive response to a question. 是的 (用以對問題作肯定回答)","examples":["\"Are you a friend of Nick's?\"—\"Yes.\" “你是尼克的朋友嗎？”—“是的。”","\"You actually wrote it down, didn't you?\"—\"Yes.\" “你實際上把它寫下來了，不是嗎？”—“是的。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to accept an offer or request, or to give permission. 好的 (用以接受提議、要求或給予許可)","examples":["\"More wine?\"—\"Yes please.\" “再要點兒葡萄酒？”—“好的，請來點。”","\"Will you take me there?\"—\"Yes, I will.\" “你帶我去那兒嗎？”—“好的，我會的。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to tell someone that what they have said is correct. 對 (用以告訴某人他所說的是正確的)","examples":["\"Well I suppose it is based on the old lunar months, isn't it?\"—\"Yes, that's right.\" “嗯，我想它是基於舊的陰曆月份的，不是嗎？”—“對，是那樣的。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to show that you are ready or willing to speak to the person who wants to speak to you, for example when you are answering a telephone or a knock at your door. 請講; 請進 (用於表示準備好或願意跟想跟自己說話的人說話)","examples":["He pushed a button on the intercom. \"Yes?\" came a voice. 他按了對講機的一個按鈕。“什麼事？”傳來一個聲音。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to indicate that you agree with, accept, or understand what the previous speaker has said. (用以表示同意、接受或理解前一說話者的話) 是的","examples":["\"A lot of people find it very difficult indeed to give up smoking.\"—\"Oh yes. I used to smoke three packs a day.\" “許多人發現戒菸確實很難。”— “噢，是的。我過去1天抽3包。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to encourage someone to continue speaking. (用以鼓勵某人繼續說) 嗯哼","examples":["\"I remembered something funny today.\"—\"Yes?\" “我今天想起件有趣的事。”—“是嗎？”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b>, usually followed by \"but,\" as a polite way of introducing what you want to say when you disagree with something the previous speaker has just said. 不錯 (後接)(but)(，禮貌地引出反對意見)","examples":["\"She is entitled to her personal allowance which is three thousand dollars of income.\"—\"Yes, but she doesn't earn any money.\" “她享有她3000美元收入的個人免稅額。”—“不錯，不過她根本不掙錢。”"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to say that a negative statement or question that the previous speaker has made is wrong or untrue. 不 (用以說明前一說話人的否定陳述或問題是不正確或不真實的)","examples":["\"That is not possible,\" she said.—\"Oh, yes, it is!\" Mrs. Gruen insisted. “那是不可能的，”她說。—“哦，不，那是可能的！”格倫太太堅持道。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>yes</b> to suggest that you do not believe or agree with what the previous speaker has said, especially when you want to express your annoyance about it. 是嗎 (用以暗示不相信或不同意前一說話人的話，尤用於想表達厭煩時)","examples":["\"There was no way to stop it.\"—\"Oh yeah? Well, here's something else you won't be able to stop.\" “沒法阻止它。”—“哦，是嗎？那麼，這兒還有別的你無法阻止的事。”"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to indicate that you had forgotten something and have just remembered it. (表示忘了某事又剛想起來) 對了","examples":["What was I going to say. Oh yeah, we've finally got our second computer. 我想說什麼來著？噢，對了，我們終於有了我們的第二臺電腦。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>yes</b> to emphasize and confirm a statement that you are making. 沒錯 (用以強調並確認所作的陳述)","examples":["He collected the $10,000 first prize. Yes, $10,000. 他獲得了1萬美元的一等獎。沒錯，1萬美元。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You say <b>yes and no</b> in reply to a question when you cannot give a definite answer, because in some ways the answer is yes and in other ways the answer is no. 說不好 (用以作不可斷言是或不是的回答)","examples":["\"Was it strange for you, going back after such a long absence?\"—\"Yes and no.\" “這對你來講奇怪嗎，這麼長時間不在之後又回去？”—“不好說。”"]}]}]},"word":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"字，詞，單詞；（某人說的）話，言語（words）；簡短的交談，談話；命令，指示；訊息，資訊；諾言，承諾；口角，吵架（words）；（警告、建議、讚揚的）話，話語；歌詞（words）；一個字（所說或所寫的最小量）（a word）；（不同於行動的）言，言語；字（尤指16或32個位元組的計算機資料基本單位）；《聖經》，福音（the Word）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"措辭，用詞"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<美> （表示接受或同意別人剛說的話）就是，說得對"}],"sections":[]},"zoo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動物園；<非正式>混亂喧鬧的場所（或場面）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>zoo</b> is a park where live animals are kept so that people can look at them. 動物園","examples":["He took his son Christopher to the zoo. 他帶兒子克里斯托弗去了動物園。"]}]}]},"zero":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"零"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"零點，零度"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Zero）（意）澤羅（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Zero</b> is the number 0. 零","examples":["Visibility at the city's airport came down to zero, bringing air traffic to a standstill. 這個城市機場的能見度下降到了零，使航空運輸陷入停頓狀態。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Zero</b> is a temperature of 0°. It is freezing point on the centigrade and Celsius scales, and 32° below freezing point on the Fahrenheit scale. (攝氏) 零度","examples":["It's a sunny late winter day, just a few degrees above zero. 這是晚冬晴朗的一天，只有零上幾度。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>zero</b> to say that there is none at all of the thing mentioned. 為零的","examples":["This new ministry was being created with zero assets and zero liabilities. 這個新部門當時是以零資產零負債進行建立。"]}]}]},"wrong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"錯誤的，不合乎事實的；（狀況）有問題的，（身體）有毛病的；（決定、選擇、行動等）錯誤的；（言論或想法）錯的；不道德的，不能被社會所接受的；不合適的，不適宜的；（機器裝置）出毛病的；上下（或前後、裡外）顛倒的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"錯誤地，不符合事實地；（方式或方向）不適當地，不適宜地；出問題；不正當地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"壞事，不道德行為， 錯誤的行為（或情況）；冤枉，不公平的行為"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不公正地對待，冤枉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say there is something <b>wrong</b>, you mean there is something unsatisfactory about the situation, person, or thing you are talking about. 有毛病的","examples":["Pain is the body's way of telling us that something is wrong. 疼痛是身體在告訴我們有地方出毛病了。","Nobody seemed to notice anything wrong. 似乎沒人注意到有什麼問題。","What's wrong with him? 他怎麼啦？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you choose the <b>wrong</b> thing, person, or method, you make a mistake and do not choose the one that you really want. 錯誤的","examples":["He went to the wrong house. 他走錯了房子。","The wrong man had been punished. 罰錯了人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a decision, choice, or action is <b>the</b> <b>wrong</b> one, it is not the best or most suitable one. 不恰當的","examples":["I really made the wrong decision there. 在那一點上我的決定確實不恰當。","The wrong choice of job might limit your chances of success. 工作選擇不當可能會限制你成功的機會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>wrong</b>, it is incorrect and not in accordance with the facts. 錯的","examples":["How do you know that this explanation is wrong? 你怎麼知道這個解釋錯了？","...a clock which showed the wrong time. …一座時間不準的鐘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>wrong</b> or goes <b>wrong</b> <b>with</b> a machine or piece of equipment, it stops working properly. (機器或裝置) 有問題的","examples":["We think there's something wrong with the computer. 我們認為計算機出了問題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>wrong</b> about something, what you say or think about it is not correct. 錯的","examples":["I was wrong about it being a casual meeting. 我錯認為那是一次非正式的會面。","I'm sure you've got it wrong. Kate isn't like that. 我確信你錯了，凱特不像那樣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you think that someone was <b>wrong</b> <b>to</b> do something, you think that they should not have done it because it was bad or immoral. 不應該的","examples":["She was wrong to leave her child alone. 她丟下孩子是不應該的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Wrong</b> is used to refer to activities or actions that are considered to be morally bad and unacceptable. 不道德的","examples":["Is it wrong to try to save the life of someone you love? 盡力挽救你愛的人的生命錯了嗎？","They thought slavery was morally wrong. 他們當時認為奴隸制是不道義的。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>wrong</b> to describe something that is not thought to be socially acceptable or desirable. 不被認可的","examples":["If you went to the wrong school, you won't get the job. 如果你上了一個不被認可的學校，你就會找不到工作。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wrong</b> is also an adverb. 錯誤地","examples":["You've done it wrong. 你做錯了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wrong</b> is also an adverb. 錯地","examples":["I must have added it up wrong, then. 那我一定是加錯了。","It looks like it's spelled wrong. 看起來像是拼錯了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"錯地","examples":["A child was wrongly diagnosed as having a bone tumor. 一個孩子被誤診為有骨瘤。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wrong</b> is also a noun. 錯事","examples":["...a man who believes that he has done no wrong. …一個相信自己沒做錯什麼的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wrong</b> is also a noun. 不道德","examples":["Johnson didn't seem to be able to tell the difference between right and wrong. 約翰遜似乎不能明辨是非。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>wrong</b> is an unfair or immoral action. 不公正的行為; 不道德的行為","examples":["No matter how difficult it might be, she had to right the terrible wrong she'd done to him. 不管有多難，她都得糾正她對他犯下的可怕錯誤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation <b>goes wrong</b>, it stops progressing in the way that you expected or intended, and becomes much worse. 出問題","examples":["We should investigate what happened, what went wrong. 我們應該調查發生了什麼事情，什麼地方出了問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone who is involved in an argument or dispute has behaved in a way which is morally or legally wrong, you can say that they are <b>in the wrong</b>. (道義或法律上) 錯的","examples":["He didn't press charges because he was in the wrong. 他沒有提起訴訟，因為是他不對。"]}]}]},"year":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"年，日曆年；年，一年時間；與某事相關的一年，年度；學年；年級，某年級的學生；年齡，年紀，歲；很久，好長時間；年代，時代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>year</b> is a period of twelve months or 365 or 366 days, beginning on the first of January and ending on the thirty-first of December. 年","examples":["The year was 1840. 那是1840年。","We had an election last year. 我們去年進行了一次選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>year</b> is any period of twelve months. 1年時間","examples":["The museums attract more than two and a half million visitors a year. 這些博物館一年吸引二百五十多萬參觀者。","She's done quite a bit of work this past year. 她在這過去的一年裡做了很多工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Year</b> is used to refer to the age of a person. For example, if someone or something is twenty <b>years</b> old or twenty <b>years</b> of age, they have lived or existed for twenty years. 年齡","examples":["He's 58 years old. 他58歲。","I've been in trouble since I was eleven years of age. 我從11歲以後一直處於麻煩中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A school <b>year</b> or academic <b>year</b> is the period of time in each twelve months when schools or colleges are open and students are studying there. The school year starts in August or September. 學年","examples":["...the 1990/91 academic year. …1990/91學年。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A financial or business <b>year</b> is an exact period of twelve months which businesses or institutions use as a basis for organizing their finances. (財政) 年度","examples":["He announced big tax increases for the next two financial years. 他宣佈了下兩個財政年度的大幅稅收增加。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>years</b> to emphasize that you are referring to a long time. 很久","examples":["I haven't laughed so much in years. 我很久沒有笑這麼多了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"the period of time, the <b>solar year</b>, during which the earth makes one revolution around the sun, measured between two successive vernal equinoxes: equal to 365.242 19 days 分點年 (Also called astronomical year, tropical year)","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"the period of time, the <b>sidereal year</b>, during which the earth makes one revolution around the sun, measured between two successive conjunctions of a particular distant star: equal to 365.256 36 days 恆星年","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>year after year</b>, it happens regularly every year. 年復一年","examples":["Regulars return year after year. 常客年年都回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something changes <b>year by year</b>, it changes gradually each year. 一年一年地","examples":["This problem has increased year by year. 這個問題一年年地加重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say something happens <b>all year round</b> or <b>all the year round</b>, it happens continually throughout the year. 全年地","examples":["Town gardens are ideal because they produce flowers nearly all year round. 城市花園是理想的，因為它們幾乎全年都開花。"]}]}]},"young":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幼小的，年輕的；存在不久的，新成立的；（顯得）年輕的，（顯得）歲數不大的；適合年輕人的；由年輕人（或兒童）構成的，青少年的，平均年齡小的；夭折的，早逝的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"年輕人（the young）；幼崽，雛鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>young</b> person, animal, or plant has not lived or existed for very long and is not yet mature. 年輕的; 幼小的 (人、動物、植物等)","examples":["...sex information written for young people. …為年輕人寫的性知識。","I crossed the hill, and found myself in a field of young barley. 我翻過那座山，發現自己來到了一塊大麥苗地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>young</b> to describe a time when a person or thing was young. 幼小的; 年輕的 (時期)","examples":["In her younger days my mother had been a successful saleswoman. 在年輕的時侯，我母親曾是位成功的推銷員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>young</b> in appearance or behaviour looks or behaves as if they are young. (外表、行為) 顯得年輕的","examples":["I was twenty-three, I suppose, and young for my age. 我想我那時是23歲，看起來比我實際年齡小。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The young</b> are people who are young. 年輕人","examples":["The association is advising pregnant women, the very young and the elderly to avoid such foods. 該協會在建議孕婦、幼兒和老人避免這類食品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>young</b> of an animal are its babies. 幼崽; 幼禽","examples":["The hen may not be able to feed its young. 這隻母雞也許不能餵它的幼雛。"]}]}]},"work":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工作，職業；勞動，活計；職責，工作內容；作品，著作；工作成果，作為；工作地點，工作時間；工作所需的材料（或檔案等）；（機器的）活動部件（the works）；<非正式>所有東西，全套物品（the works）；土木工程，建築（works）；工廠（works）；善行，德行（works）；防禦工事；（物理學）功；<非正式>整形手術"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"工作，幹活兒；從事體力（或腦力）勞動；從事……工作，在……工作；努力取得，力爭；運轉，執行；開動，操作（機器、裝置等）；奏效，成功；產生……作用；（使）變成，逐步移動；（使）（身體某部位）抽動；（用某種材料）畫畫，創作；使成形，加工；博得，贏得（眾人的支援或歡心）；<美>計算，算出；思考，動腦筋；以（某種假定或思想）為基礎（或前提）；<非正式>安排；耕種；開採（礦）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"工作的，與工作有關的；適合工作時穿戴的；用於工作的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who <b>work</b> have a job, usually one which they are paid to do. 工作","examples":["I started working in a recording studio. 我開始在一個錄音棚裡工作。","He worked as a teacher for 50 years. 他從事教師工作50年了。","I want to work, I don't want to be on welfare. 我想工作，我不想依靠救濟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>work</b>, you spend time and effort doing a task that needs to be done or trying to achieve something. 努力從事","examples":["Linda spends all her time working on the garden. 琳達用所有的時間在那座花園裡勞作。","The government expressed hope that all the sides will work toward a political solution. 該政府希望所有各方致力於一個政治解決方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is working on</b> a particular subject or question, they are studying or researching it. 研究","examples":["Professor Bonnet has been working for many years on molecules of this type. 博內特教授多年來一直在研究這類分子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>work</b> <b>with</b> a person or a group of people, you spend time and effort trying to help them in some way. 幫助","examples":["She spent a period of time working with people dying of cancer. 她用一段時間幫助即將死於癌症的人們。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a machine or piece of equipment <b>works</b>, it operates and performs a particular function. (機器或裝置) 運轉","examples":["The pump doesn't work and we have no running water. 這個水泵不運轉了，我們沒有自來水。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an idea, system, or way of doing something <b>works</b>, it is successful, effective, or satisfactory. (想法、系統或方法) 奏效","examples":["95 percent of these diets do not work. 這些節食方法中的95%都不奏效。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a drug or medicine <b>works</b>, it produces a particular physical effect. (藥物) 起作用","examples":["I wake up at 6 a.m. as the sleeping pill doesn't work for more than nine hours. 我早上6點醒來，因為這種安眠藥作用不會超過9個小時。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If your mind or brain <b>is working</b>, you are thinking about something or trying to solve a problem. (腦子或思想) 運轉","examples":["My mind was working frantically, running over the events of the evening. 我的腦子瘋狂地運轉著, 將那天晚上發生的事情過了一遍。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>work on</b> an assumption or idea, you act as if it were true or base other ideas on it, until you have more information. 基於 (一個假設) 而行動","examples":["We are working on the assumption that it was a gas explosion. 我們正依據它是一起燃氣爆炸的假設而行動。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you work on someone, you persuade or attempt to persuade or influence them. 影響; 勸說(某人)","examples":[]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something <b>works</b> into a particular state or condition, it gradually moves so that it is in that state or condition. 逐漸變成","examples":["It's important to put a lock washer on that last nut, or it can work loose. 重要的是要在最後一個螺母上安裝一個防松墊圈，否則它會逐漸變鬆。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>work</b>, you do the things that you are paid or required to do in your job. 工作","examples":["I can't talk to you right now – I'm working. 我這會兒不能和你說話–我正在工作。","He was working at his desk. 他正在伏案工作。","They work forty hours a week. 他們一週工作40個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>work</b> someone, you make them spend time and effort doing a particular activity or job. 使幹活","examples":["They're working me too hard. I'm too old for this. 他們讓我幹得太苦。我幹這個年紀太大了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people <b>work</b> the land, they do all the tasks involved in growing crops. 開墾","examples":["Farmers worked the fertile valleys. 農民們開墾了這個肥沃的山谷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>work</b> a machine or piece of equipment, you use or control it. 操作 (機器或裝置)","examples":["Many adults still depend on their children to work the video. 許多成年人仍依靠他們的孩子來操作錄影機。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>work</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you move or progress there slowly, and with a lot of effort or work. 逐漸移動到某處","examples":["Rescuers were still working their way toward the trapped men. 救援人員仍在慢慢地挪近那些被困人員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>at work</b> they are doing their job or are busy doing a particular activity. 在工作; 在從事某種活動","examples":["The salvage teams are already hard at work trying to deal with the spilled oil. 那些救援隊已在拼命工作，設法處理洩漏的油。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a force or process is <b>at work</b>, it is having a particular influence or effect. 正起作用","examples":["It is important to understand the powerful economic and social forces at work behind our own actions. 重要的是要理解在我們自己的行動背後起作用的那些強大的經濟和社會力量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone <b>to work</b> or <b>set</b> them <b>to work</b>, you give them a job or task to do. 給某人工作","examples":["By stimulating the economy, we're going to put people to work. 透過刺激經濟，我們將給人們工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>get to work</b>, <b>go to work</b>, or <b>set to work</b> on a job, task, or problem, you start doing it or dealing with it. 開始工作; 著手處理","examples":["He promised to get to work on the state's massive deficit. 他承諾著手處理該國嚴重的赤字問題。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who have <b>work</b> or who are <b>in work</b> have a job, usually one which they are paid to do. 工作","examples":["Fewer and fewer people are in work. 越來越少的人有工作。","I was out of work at the time. 那時我失業了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>work</b> consists of the things you are paid or required to do in your job. 工作","examples":["We're supposed to be running a business here. I've got work to do. 我們本應該在這做生意。我有工作要做。","I used to take work home, but I don't do it any more. 我過去常把工作帶回家，但現在再也不那樣做了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Work</b> is tasks that need to be done or things that need to be achieved. 活計","examples":["There was a lot of work to do on their house. 他們的房子有很多活要幹。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Work</b> is the place where you do your job. 工作單位","examples":["Many people travel to work by car. 許多人乘車去工作單位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Work</b> is something that you produce as a result of an activity or as a result of doing your job. 工作成果","examples":["It can help to have an impartial third party look over your work. 讓中立的第3方來檢查你的工作會有所幫助。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>work</b> is something such as a painting, book, or piece of music produced by an artist, writer, or composer. 作品; 著作","examples":["In my opinion, this is Rembrandt's greatest work. 在我看來，這是倫勃朗最偉大的作品。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Someone's <b>work</b> is the study or research that they have done on a particular subject or question. 研究","examples":["Their work shows that one-year-olds are much more likely to have allergies if either parent smokes. 他們的研究顯示，如果父母任何一方吸菸，1歲的嬰兒更有可能患過敏。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Work</b> with a particular person or a group of people is time and effort spent trying to help them in some way. (幫助他人的) 工作","examples":["She became involved in social and relief work among the refugees. 她參加了針對難民的社會救濟工作。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>works</b> is a place where something is manufactured or where an industrial process is carried out. <b>Works</b> is used to refer to one or to more than one of these places. 工廠","examples":["...the steelworks in Gary, Indiana. …在印第安納州蓋瑞市的那家鋼廠。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"<b>Works</b> are activities such as digging the ground or building on a large scale. 施工","examples":["...six years of disruptive building works, road construction and urban development. …6年混亂的建築施工、路政和城市開發。"]}]}]},"believable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可信的，可相信的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>believable</b> makes you think that it could be true or real. 可信的","examples":["...believable evidence. …可信的證據。"]}]}]},"bony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"骨瘦如柴的；似骨的，骨制的；多骨的，多刺的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>bony</b> face or <b>bony</b> hands, for example, has a very thin face or very thin hands, with very little flesh covering their bones. 瘦削的","examples":["...an old man with a bony face and white hair. …一個面部瘦削、白髮蒼蒼的老人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>bony</b> parts of a person's or animal's body are the parts made of bone. 骨的","examples":["...the bony ridge of the eye socket. …眼窩的骨架。"]}]}]},"alive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"活著的；仍然存在的；活躍的，充滿活力的；熱鬧的；尚未失敗，仍有成功機會；注意到的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or animals are <b>alive</b>, they are not dead. 活著的","examples":["She does not know if he is alive or dead. 她不知道他是活還是死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone seems <b>alive</b>, you mean that they seem to be very lively and to enjoy everything that they do. 有活力的","examples":["She seemed more alive and looked forward to getting up in the morning. 她似乎更有活力，並且期待著一早就起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an activity, organization, or situation is <b>alive</b>, it continues to exist or function. 繼續存在的","examples":["The big factories are trying to stay alive by cutting costs. 大工廠試圖透過減少開支以維持生存。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a place is <b>alive</b> <b>with</b> something, there are a lot of people or things there and it seems busy or exciting. 滿是 (人或物，顯得繁忙或興奮的) 的","examples":["The river was alive with birds. 這條河流周圍滿是各種鳥類。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people, places, or events <b>come alive</b>, they start to be lively again after a quiet period. If someone or something <b>brings</b> them <b>alive</b>, they cause them to come alive. 恢復生機; 使變活躍","examples":["The doctor's voice had come alive and his small eyes shone. 醫生的聲音變得響亮起來，兩隻小眼睛也有了神采。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a story or description <b>comes alive</b>, it becomes interesting, lively, or realistic. If someone or something <b>brings</b> it <b>alive</b>, they make it seem more interesting, lively, or realistic. 使變得有趣; 使顯得生動","examples":["She made history come alive with tales from her own memories. 她用自己記憶中的往事使歷史變得生動有趣起來。"]}]}]},"ancient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"古代的，遠古的；古老的，年代久遠的；老的，老掉牙的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指埃及、希臘和羅馬的）古代人；<古>老頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ancient</b> means belonging to the distant past, especially to the period in history before the end of the Roman Empire. 古代的","examples":["They believed ancient Greece and Rome were vital sources of learning. 他們認為古希臘和古羅馬是至關重要的知識來源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ancient</b> means very old, or having existed for a long time. 古老的","examples":["...ancient Jewish tradition. …古老的猶太傳統。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a member of a civilized nation in the ancient world, esp a Greek, Roman, or Hebrew 古(希臘、羅馬或希伯來)人","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a flag or other banner; standard 旗幟; 標準","examples":[]}]}]},"asleep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"睡著的；麻木的，發麻的；<美，非正式>不專心的，不活躍的；長眠的，已死的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"處於睡眠狀態地，進入睡眠狀態地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>asleep</b> is sleeping. 睡著的","examples":["My four-year-old daughter was asleep on the sofa. 我4歲的女兒在沙發上睡著了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that your arm or leg is <b>asleep</b>, you mean that it is numb, for example because you have been sitting in an awkward position. (胳膊、腿等) 麻木的","examples":["Her left leg was asleep from sitting on the floor. 她的左腿在地板上坐得麻木了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>fall asleep</b>, you start sleeping. 入睡","examples":["Sam snuggled down in his pillow and fell asleep. 薩姆舒適地枕著枕頭睡著了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>fast asleep</b> or <b>sound asleep</b> is sleeping deeply. 熟睡的","examples":["They were both fast asleep in their beds. 他們倆在各自的床上都熟睡了。"]}]}]},"active":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好動的；積極主動的；定期進行的，起作用的；（思想等）活躍的；切實的；（火山）活的；主動語態的；活性的；（疾病）惡化的；服役的；參戰的；（動詞）表動作的；（電路系統）在運轉中的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"主動語態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>active</b> moves around a lot or does a lot of things. 好動的","examples":["With three active little kids running around, there was plenty to keep me busy. 有3個好動的小孩到處跑，就夠讓我忙的了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have an <b>active</b> mind or imagination, you are always thinking of new things. (思維或想像力) 活躍的","examples":["...the tragedy of an active mind trapped by failing physical health. …活躍的頭腦被衰弱的生理健康所困擾的悲劇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>active</b> in an organization, cause, or campaign, they do things for it rather than just giving it their support. 積極主動的","examples":["We should play an active role in politics, both at the national and local level. 我們應該在國家和地方層面的政治生活中扮演積極主動的角色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Active</b> is used to emphasize that someone is taking action in order to achieve something, rather than just hoping for it or achieving it in an indirect way. 積極的","examples":["Companies need to take active steps to increase exports. 那些公司需要採取積極的措施來增加出口。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a person or animal is <b>active</b> in a particular place or at a particular time, you mean that they are performing their usual activities or performing a particular activity. 活動的","examples":["Guerrilla groups are active in the province. 游擊隊組織在該省活動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An <b>active</b> volcano has erupted recently or is expected to erupt soon. (火山) 活的","examples":["...molten lava from an active volcano. …一座活火山的熔岩。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"An <b>active</b> substance has a chemical or biological effect on things. 活性的","examples":["The active ingredient in some of the mouthwashes was simply detergent. 某些漱口劑中的活性成分只是清潔劑而已。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"積極主動地","examples":["They actively campaigned for the vote. 他們積極主動地為爭取選票而活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"積極地","examples":["They have never been actively encouraged to take such risks. 他們從未被積極地鼓勵去冒這樣的風險。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In grammar, <b>the active</b> or <b>the active voice</b> means the forms of a verb which are used when the subject refers to a person or thing that does something. For example, in \"I saw her yesterday,\" the verb is in the active. Compare . 主動語態","examples":[]}]}]},"bloody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"流血的，沾滿血的；血腥的，殘酷的；<英>該死的，討厭的；非常的；含血的，似血的；血紅的，血色的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，很（用於強調）；該死地，討厭地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使受傷，使流血；血染，使沾上鮮血；傷害，損害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation or event as <b>bloody</b>, you mean that it is very violent and a lot of people are killed. 血腥的","examples":["Forty-three demonstrators were killed in bloody clashes. 43名示威者在血腥衝突中喪命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone or something as <b>bloody</b> if they are covered in a lot of blood. 沾滿血跡的","examples":["He was arrested last October still carrying a bloody knife. 他去年10月被捕時還拿著一把血跡斑斑的刀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Bloody</b>\nis used by some people to emphasize what they are saying, especially when they are angry. 該死的; 氣惱時用來加重語氣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>bloodied</b> part of your body, there is blood on it, usually because you have had an accident or you have been attacked. 使流血","examples":["One of our children fell and bloodied his knee. 我們的一個孩子摔得膝蓋流血了。"]}]}]},"childish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"孩子的，孩子般的；幼稚的，孩子氣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Childish</b> means relating to or typical of a child. 孩子的; 孩子特有的","examples":["...childish enthusiasm. …孩子特有的熱情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone, especially an adult, as <b>childish</b>, you disapprove of them because they behave in an immature way. 幼稚的","examples":["...Penny's selfish and childish behaviour. …佩尼自私而幼稚的行為。"]}]}]},"childlike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天真爛漫的，孩子似的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe someone as <b>childlike</b> when they seem like a child in their character, appearance, or behaviour. 像孩子的","examples":["His most enduring quality is his childlike innocence. 他最持久不變的特質是孩子般的天真無邪。"]}]}]},"bitter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"味苦的；痛苦的，辛酸的；激烈的，充滿敵意的；憤憤不平的；嚴寒的，刺骨的；（巧克力）黑色不加糖的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"苦啤酒"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"嚴寒刺骨地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變苦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a <b>bitter</b> argument or conflict, people argue very angrily or fight very fiercely. 激烈的","examples":["...the scene of bitter fighting during the Second World War. …第二次世界大戰期間激烈的戰鬥場面。","...a bitter attack on the government's failure to support manufacturing. …對政府未能支援製造業的猛烈抨擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>bitter</b> after a disappointing experience or after being treated unfairly, they continue to feel angry about it. 依然憤怒的","examples":["She is said to be very bitter about the way she was fired. 據說她對自己被解僱的方式仍很氣憤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bitter</b> taste is sharp, not sweet, and often slightly unpleasant. 苦的","examples":["The leaves taste rather bitter. 這些葉子嚐起來相當苦。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bitter</b> experience makes you feel very disappointed. You can also use <b>bitter</b> to emphasize feelings of disappointment. 慘痛的","examples":["The decision was a bitter blow from which he never quite recovered. 這個決定是個沉重的打擊，他一直沒有完全恢復過來。","A great deal of bitter experience had taught him how to lose gracefully. 大量痛苦的經歷已經教會了他如何體面地認輸。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Bitter</b> weather, or a <b>bitter</b> wind, is extremely cold. 嚴寒的; 刺骨的","examples":["Outside, a bitter east wind was accompanied by flurries of snow. 外面，凜冽的東風挾著陣陣小雪。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"激烈地","examples":["Any such thing would be bitterly opposed by most of the world's democracies. 任何此類事件都將受到世界上絕大多數民主國家的強烈反對。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"依然憤怒地","examples":["\"And he sure didn't help us,\" Grant said bitterly. “他確實沒有幫助過我們，”格蘭特仍很氣憤地說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"慘痛地","examples":["I was bitterly disappointed to have lost yet another race so near the finish. 我感到痛心沮喪，在那麼接近終點的情形下又輸掉了一場比賽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"嚴寒地; 刺骨地","examples":["It's been bitterly cold here in Moscow. 在莫斯科這裡，天氣一直極其寒冷。"]}]}]},"colorful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"富有色彩的，色彩鮮豔的，華美的；有趣的，豐富多彩的，生動有趣的"}],"sections":[]},"broad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寬廣的，寬闊的；……寬；咧開嘴的；廣泛的，普遍的；大致的，概括的；明確的，明顯的；粗俗滑稽的；口音重的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>對女人的粗俗稱呼；寬闊部分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"寬闊地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>broad</b> is wide. 寬的","examples":["His shoulders were broad and his waist narrow. 他肩寬腰細。","The hills rise green and sheer above the broad river. 群山青翠，陡然屹立於寬闊的大河之上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>broad</b> smile is one in which your mouth is stretched very wide because you are very pleased or amused. 咧開大嘴的 (笑)","examples":["He greeted them with a wave and a broad smile. 他咧嘴笑著揮手和他們打招呼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>broad</b> to describe something that includes a large number of different things or people. 廣泛的","examples":["A broad range of issues was discussed. 廣泛的問題得到了討論。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>broad</b> to describe a word or meaning which covers or refers to a wide range of different things. 寬泛的","examples":["...restructuring in the broad sense of the word. …以該詞的廣義而言的調整。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>broad</b> to describe a feeling or opinion that is shared by many people, or by people of many different kinds. 普遍的","examples":["The agreement won broad support in the U.S. Congress. 這項協議在美國議會贏得了普遍的支援。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"咧開大嘴地","examples":["Charles grinned broadly. 查爾斯咧大嘴笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"廣泛地","examples":["Such policies will do little to resolve long-standing problems more broadly affecting America's global competitiveness. 這些政策對於解決長久以來更廣泛地影響美國全球競爭力的問題將沒什麼作用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"寬泛地","examples":["We define education very broadly and students can study any aspect of its consequences for society. 我們對教育的定義很寬泛，學生們可以研究它對社會任何一面的影響。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"普遍地","examples":["The new law has been broadly welcomed by road safety organizations. 新法律得到了道路安全組織的普遍歡迎。"]}]}]},"central":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中央的，中心的；起支配作用的，有控制力的；最重要的，主要的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美，非正式>活動中心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>central</b> is in the middle of a place or area. 中心的; 中部的","examples":["...Central America's Caribbean coast. …美國中部的加勒比海岸。","The disruption has now spread and is affecting a large part of central Liberia. 分裂活動範圍如今已擴大，正影響著賴比瑞亞中部的大部分地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A place that is <b>central</b> is easy to reach because it is in the centre of a city, town, or particular area. (地點) 近市中心的; 在中心地帶的","examples":["...a central location in the capital. …首都的一箇中心地帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>central</b> group or organization makes all the important decisions that are followed throughout a larger organization or a country. 中央的; 首要的","examples":["There is a lack of trust toward the central government in Rome. 對羅馬中央政府缺乏信任。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>central</b> person or thing in a particular situation is the most important one. 最重要的","examples":["Black dance music has been central to mainstream pop since the early '60s. 黑人舞蹈音樂自20世紀60年代初以來對主流流行音樂一直都是最重要的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在中心; 在中央","examples":["The main cabin has its full-sized double bed centrally placed with plenty of room around it. 主艙正中擺了一張標準的雙人床，床周圍空間很大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"在中心地帶","examples":["...this centrally located hotel, situated on the banks of the river. …地處中心位置的這家旅館，座落在河岸邊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"中央地; 首要地","examples":["This is a centrally planned economy. 這是一種中央計劃經濟。"]}]}]},"cloudy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多雲的，陰天的；渾濁的，不清澈的；含糊的，困惑的；（眼睛）淚眼矇矓的；愁容滿面的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>cloudy</b>, there are a lot of clouds in the sky. 多雲的","examples":["...a windy, cloudy day. …有風多雲的一天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cloudy</b> liquid is less clear than it should be. (液體) 渾濁的","examples":["If the water's cloudy like that, it'll be hard to see anyone underwater. 如果水渾濁成那樣，就很難看得到水下的人。"]}]}]},"clever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聰明的，機靈的；機敏的，巧妙的；詼諧的；熟練的，靈巧的；耍小聰明的，滑頭的；真聰明（用於諷刺某人做的蠢事）；<英，非正式>健壯的，健康的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>clever</b> is intelligent and able to understand things easily or plan things well. 聰明的","examples":["He's a very clever man. 他是個很聰明的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clever</b> idea, book, or invention is extremely effective and shows the skill of the people involved. 巧妙的","examples":["It is a clever and gripping novel, yet something is missing from its heart. 這是一部構思巧妙、引人入勝的小說，不過在精神上還缺少點什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聰明地","examples":["She would cleverly pick up on what I said. 她會很聰明地留心我說的話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"巧妙地","examples":["...a cleverly designed swimsuit. …一件設計巧妙的游泳衣。"]}]}]},"costly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"昂貴的，值錢的；造成嚴重損失的，代價大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>costly</b>, you mean that it costs a lot of money, often more than you would want to pay. 昂貴的","examples":["Having professionally made curtains can be costly, so why not make your own? 買專業製造的窗簾可能很貴，你為什麼不自己做呢？"]}]}]},"convenient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"方便的，便利的；附近的，方便到達的；<舊>適當的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a way of doing something is <b>convenient</b>, it is easy, or very useful or suitable for a particular purpose. 方便的","examples":["...a flexible and convenient way of paying for business expenses. …一種靈活方便的支付商務費用的方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place as <b>convenient</b>, you are pleased because it is near to where you are, or because you can reach another place from there quickly and easily. 近便的","examples":["The town is well placed for easy access to Washington D.C. and convenient for Dulles Airport. 這個小鎮離華盛頓和杜勒斯機場都很近。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>convenient</b> time to do something, for example to meet someone, is a time when you are free to do it or would like to do it. 方便的","examples":["She will try to arrange a mutually convenient time and place for an interview. 她會盡量把面談安排在一個雙方都方便的時間和地點。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"方便","examples":["They may use a credit card for convenience. 他們可以為了方便而使用信用卡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"近便地","examples":["It was very conveniently situated just across the road from the City Reference Library. 它所處位置非常便利，就在市參考圖書館的馬路對面。"]}]}]},"comfortable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人舒適的；感到舒服的，安逸的；自信的，自在的；富裕的，寬裕的；滿意的；易取勝的，輕鬆領先的；（病、傷後）疼痛減緩的，狀況良好的；足夠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>溫暖的蓋被"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a piece of furniture or an item of clothing is <b>comfortable</b>, it makes you feel physically relaxed when you use it, for example because it is soft. 令人舒服的","examples":["...a comfortable fireside chair. …一把令人舒服的爐邊椅子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a building or room is <b>comfortable</b>, it makes you feel physically relaxed when you spend time in it, for example because it is warm and has nice furniture. 令人舒適的","examples":["A home should be comfortable and friendly. 家應使人感到舒適與和睦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>comfortable</b>, you are physically relaxed because of the place or position you are sitting or lying in. 感到舒服的","examples":["Lie down on your bed and make yourself comfortable. 躺在床上讓你自己舒服些。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>comfortable</b>, you mean that they have enough money to be able to live without financial problems. 寬裕的","examples":["\"Is he rich?\"—\"He's comfortable.\" “他富有嗎？”—“他生活寬裕。”"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a race, competition, or election, if you have a <b>comfortable</b> lead, you are likely to win it easily. If you gain a <b>comfortable</b> victory or majority, you win easily. 輕易的","examples":["By half distance we held a comfortable two-lap lead. 賽程未過半我們就輕易領先了兩圈。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you feel <b>comfortable</b> <b>with</b> a particular situation or person, you feel confident and relaxed with them. 輕鬆的; 自在的","examples":["Nervous politicians might well feel more comfortable with a step-by-step approach. 緊張不安的政治家們也許會對逐步解決問題的方式感到更輕鬆些。","He liked me and I felt comfortable with him. 他喜歡我，而我和他在一起也感覺輕鬆自在。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When a sick or injured person is said to be <b>comfortable</b>, they are without pain. 無痛苦的","examples":["He was described as comfortable in the hospital last night. 據說昨晚他在醫院裡沒有感到痛苦。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人舒適地","examples":["...the comfortably furnished living room. …佈置舒適的起居室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"感到舒服地","examples":["Are you sitting comfortably? 你坐得舒服嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"寬裕地","examples":["Cayton describes himself as comfortably well-off. 凱頓把自己描述為生活很富裕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"輕易地","examples":["...the Los Angeles Raiders, who comfortably beat the Bears earlier in the season. …曾在本賽季的早些時候輕易地擊敗了熊隊的洛杉磯襲擊者隊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"輕鬆地; 自在地","examples":["They talked comfortably of their plans. 他們輕鬆地討論了他們的計劃。"]}]}]},"deaf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聾的；置若罔聞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>deaf</b> is unable to hear anything or is unable to hear very well. 聾的; 聽不清的","examples":["She is now profoundly deaf. 她現在幾乎一點聲音都聽不到了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The deaf</b> are people who are deaf. 失聰者","examples":["Many regular TV programmes are captioned for the deaf. 許多固定的電視節目都為失聰者提供字幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"失聰","examples":["Because of her deafness she was hard to make conversation with. 由於她失聰，和她交流很困難。"]}]}]},"cruel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"殘酷的，殘忍的；引起痛苦的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>弄糟，使沒有成功可能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cruel</b> deliberately causes pain or distress to people or animals. 殘忍的","examples":["Children can be so cruel. 孩子也會這麼殘忍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A situation or event that is <b>cruel</b> is very harsh and causes people distress. 嚴酷的","examples":["...struggling to survive in a cruel world with which they cannot cope. …在一個他們不能承受的嚴酷世界中掙扎著求生。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"殘忍地","examples":["Douglas was often cruelly tormented by jealous siblings. 道格拉斯過去常遭到嫉妒他的兄弟姐妹們的殘忍折磨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嚴酷地","examples":["His life has been cruelly shattered by an event not of his own making. 他的生活由於一個非他自身因素造成的事件被無情地破壞了。"]}]}]},"delicious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"美味的，芬芳的；令人愉快的，宜人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Food that is <b>delicious</b> has a very pleasant taste. 美味的","examples":["There's always a wide selection of delicious meals to choose from. 總有很多種美味佳餚可供選擇。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"美味地","examples":["This yoghurt has a deliciously creamy flavour. 這種酸奶有可口的奶油味道。"]}]}]},"curious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好奇的，求知慾強的；稀奇的，不尋常的；愛挑剔的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>curious</b> <b>about</b> something, you are interested in it and want to know more about it. 好奇的","examples":["Steve was intensely curious about the world I came from. 史蒂夫對我是從哪裡來的有強烈的好奇心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>curious</b>, you mean that it is unusual or difficult to understand. 不尋常的; 難以理解的","examples":["The pageant promises to be a curious mixture of the ancient and modern. 這次旅行可望是一次古典與現代風格的不尋常的組合。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"好奇地","examples":["The woman in the shop had looked at them curiously. 商店裡的那個女人好奇地看著他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"令人不解的地","examples":["Harry was curiously silent through all this. 哈利自始至終都令人不解地保持著沉默。"]}]}]},"crazy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愚蠢的，古怪的，不理智的；極度煩惱的，瘋狂的；精神失常的；狂熱的，迷戀的；（角度）極其歪斜的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘋子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>crazy</b>, you think they are very foolish or strange. 傻的; 怪的","examples":["People thought they were all crazy to try to make money from manufacturing. 人們認為他們都試著從製造業中賺錢太傻了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>crazy</b> is insane. 發瘋的","examples":["If I sat home and worried about all this stuff, I'd go crazy. 要是我坐在家裡為所有這些事發愁，我會發瘋的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>crazy about</b> something, you are very enthusiastic about it. If you are <b>not</b> <b>crazy</b> <b>about</b> something, you do not like it. 著迷的","examples":["He's still crazy about both his work and his hobbies. 他依舊迷戀於自己的工作和業餘愛好。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Crazy</b> is also a combining form. …狂熱的 (用於詞構成合成詞)","examples":["Sports-crazy Coloradans will buy tickets to anything. 運動狂熱的科羅拉多人什麼票都會買。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>crazy about</b> someone, you are deeply in love with them. 狂愛的","examples":["We're crazy about each other. 我們為彼此瘋狂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傻地; 怪地","examples":["The teenagers shook their long, black hair and gesticulated crazily. 那群十幾歲的青少年甩動著長長的黑髮，怪怪地比著手勢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crazy</b> is also a noun. 瘋子","examples":["Outside, mumbling, was one of New York's ever-present crazies. 在外面喃喃自語的人是紐約常有的瘋子之一。"]}]}]},"dangerous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"危險的，有威脅的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>dangerous</b>, it is able or likely to hurt or harm you. 危險的","examples":["It's a dangerous stretch of road. 這是一截危險路段。","...dangerous drugs. …危險的藥品。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"危險地","examples":["He is dangerously ill. 他病得很重。"]}]}]},"dizzy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"頭暈目眩的；使人眩暈的，使人感到變化太快的；傻乎乎的，蠢的；粗心大意的，心不在焉的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使眩暈，使暈頭轉向；使困惑，使思想混亂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>dizzy</b>, you feel that you are losing your balance and are about to fall. 眩暈的","examples":["Her head still hurt, and she felt slightly dizzy and disoriented. 她的頭還在痛，感覺有些眩暈，分不清方向。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>dizzy</b> to describe a woman who is careless and forgets things, but is easy to like. (女人) 沒頭腦但招人喜愛的","examples":["She is famed for playing dizzy blondes. 她以扮演沒頭腦但招人喜愛的金髮美女而聞名。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"眩暈","examples":["His head injury causes dizziness and nausea. 他頭部受傷引起眩暈和嘔吐。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has reached <b>the</b> <b>dizzy heights</b> <b>of</b> something, you are emphasizing that they have reached a very high level by achieving it. 顯赫的地位","examples":["I escalated to the dizzy heights of director's secretary. 我逐漸升到了主任秘書這樣的職位。"]}]}]},"distant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遙遠的，久遠的；冷淡的；心不在焉的；遠親的；不相似的，不同的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Distant</b> means very far away. 遙遠的","examples":["The mountains rolled away to a distant horizon. 群山綿延至遙遠的天邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>distant</b> to describe a time or event that is very far away in the future or in the past. 久遠的","examples":["There is little doubt, however, that things will improve in the not too distant future. 然而毋庸置疑的是，事情在不遠的將來會有改觀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>distant</b> relative is one who you are not closely related to. 遠房的","examples":["He's a distant relative of the mayor. 他是市長的遠房親戚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>distant</b>, you mean that you find them cold and unfriendly. 冷淡的; 不友好的","examples":["He found her cold, icelike, and distant. 他發現她冷若冰霜，不易接近。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>distant</b>, you mean that they are not concentrating on what they are doing because they are thinking about other things. 恍惚的; 茫然的","examples":["There was a distant look in her eyes from time to time, her thoughts elsewhere. 她的眼中時而出現恍惚的神情，她的思緒飄到別處。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遠親地","examples":["The O'Shea girls are distantly related to our family. 奧謝家的姑娘們和我們家沾點兒親。"]}]}]},"dishonest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不誠實的，不正直的；欺詐的，欺騙性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or their behaviour is <b>dishonest</b>, you mean that they are not truthful or honest and that you cannot trust them. 不誠實的","examples":["It would be dishonest to mislead people and not to present the data as fairly as possible. 誤導人們、不儘可能公正地提供資料是不誠實的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不誠實地","examples":["The key issue was whether the four defendants acted dishonestly. 關鍵問題在於這4名被告是不是做事不誠實。"]}]}]},"dumb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"啞的，不能說話的；一時說不出話的，不肯開口的；<非正式>愚蠢的；（計算機終端）簡易的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使通俗化；<文>使變啞，使沉默"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>dumb</b> is completely unable to speak. 啞的","examples":["...a young deaf and dumb man. …一名年輕的聾啞人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>dumb</b> on a particular occasion, they cannot speak because they are angry, shocked, or surprised. 說不出話的","examples":["We were all struck dumb for a minute. 我們一時個個都啞口無言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you call a person <b>dumb</b>, you mean that they are stupid or foolish. 蠢的","examples":["The questions were set up to make her look dumb. 這些問題是安排好讓她顯得蠢的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>dumb</b>, you think that it is silly and annoying. 愚蠢而惱人的","examples":["I came up with this dumb idea. 我想出了這個愚蠢而惱人的主意。"]}]}]},"entire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全部的，整個的；完全的，絕對的；（公馬）未經閹割的；（葉子）全緣的，邊緣光滑的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"未經閹割的公馬，種馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>entire</b> when you want to emphasize that you are referring to the whole of something, for example, the whole of a place, time, or population. 全部的; 整個的","examples":["He had spent his entire life in China as a doctor. 他整個一生都在中國做醫生。","There are only 60 swimming pools in the entire country. 整個國家僅有60個游泳池。"]}]}]},"effective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"產生預期結果的，有效的；實際的，事實上的；（法律、規則等）生效的，起作用的；給人深刻印象的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"實際可作戰計程車兵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>effective</b> works well and produces the results that were intended. 有效的","examples":["The project looks at how we could be more effective in encouraging students to enter teacher training. 該專案研究如何更有效地鼓勵學生參加教師培訓。","Simple antibiotics are effective against this organism. 普通的抗生素就能夠有效地抑制這種微生物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Effective</b> means having a particular role or result in practice, though not officially or in theory. 實際的","examples":["They have had effective control of the area since the security forces left. 自從安全部隊離開後，他們實際控制了這一地區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as a law or an agreement becomes <b>effective</b>, it begins officially to apply or be valid. (法律、協議等) 生效的","examples":["The new rules will become effective in the next few days. 這些新條例將在接下來的幾天內生效。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有效地","examples":["Services need to be organized more effectively than they are at present. 服務需要比現在更有效地被組織起來。"]}]}]},"excellent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，卓越的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"太好了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>excellent</b> is extremely good. 極好的; 優秀的","examples":["The recording quality is excellent. 錄製質量極好。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極好地; 優秀地","examples":["They're both playing excellently. 他們演奏得都很棒。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>Excellent!</b>\" to show that they approve of something. 太棒了; 太好了","examples":["\"Excellent!\" he shouted, yelping happily at the rain. \"Now we'll see how this boat really performs!\" “太好了！”他衝著雨高興地喊著，“這下我們可以看看這艘船真正如何表現了！”"]}]}]},"foggy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有霧的，霧氣茫茫的；迷糊的，朦朧的；模糊的，糊塗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When it is <b>foggy</b>, there is fog. 有霧的","examples":["It's quite foggy now. 現在霧很大。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>haven't the foggiest</b> or you <b>haven't the foggiest idea</b>, you are emphasizing that you do not know something. 壓根兒不知道","examples":["I did not have the foggiest idea what he meant. 我壓根兒不知道他是什麼意思。"]}]}]},"expensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"花錢多的，昂貴的；（錯誤或決定）代價高的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>expensive</b>, it costs a lot of money. 昂貴的","examples":["Broadband is still more expensive than dial-up services. 寬頻還是要比撥號服務費錢得多。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"昂貴地","examples":["She was expensively dressed, with fine furs and jewels. 她衣飾奢華，穿戴著上好的毛皮和珠寶。"]}]}]},"fearful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"害怕的，擔心的；可怕的；極壞的，極端的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>fearful</b> <b>of</b> something, you are afraid of it. 害怕的","examples":["Bankers were fearful of a world banking crisis. 銀行家們害怕會有一場世界性的銀行業危機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>fearful</b> to emphasize how serious or bad a situation is. 極嚴重的; 極糟糕的","examples":["The region is in a fearful recession. 該地區處於極嚴重的經濟衰退中。"]}]}]},"exact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"確切的，精確的；嚴謹的，一絲不苟的；精密的，嚴密的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強取，勒索；實施（報復）；造成重大苦難（或損失等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exact</b> means correct in every detail. For example, an <b>exact</b> copy is the same in every detail as the thing it is copied from. 精確的; 確切的","examples":["I don't remember the exact words. 我不記得確切的話了。","The exact number of protest calls has not been revealed. 抗議電話的確切次數尚未披露。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>exact</b> before a noun to emphasize that you are referring to that particular thing and no other, especially something that has a particular significance. 正好的 (用於名詞前表示強調)","examples":["I hadn't really thought about it until this exact moment. 一直到此時此刻我才真正考慮它。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精確地; 確切地","examples":["Try to locate exactly where the smells are entering the room. 設法確定氣味是從哪裡進入房間的。","Both drugs will be exactly the same. 兩種藥將會完全一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"正好","examples":["These are exactly the people who do not vote. 這些正好是那些不投票的人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>exacts</b> something, they demand and obtain it from another person, especially because they are in a superior or more powerful position. (尤指因處於上級地位而) 強行要求並獲得","examples":["Already he has exacted a written apology from the chairman of the commission. 他已經透過強行要求得到了委員會主席的書面道歉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>exacts</b> revenge <b>on</b> a person, they have their revenge on them. 實施","examples":["She uses the media to help her exact a terrible revenge. 她利用媒體幫助她實施一次可怕的報復。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>exacts</b> a high price, it has a bad effect on a person or situation. 使…付出 (代價)","examples":["The sheer physical effort had exacted a heavy price. 純粹的體力支出已付出了沉重的代價。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>to be exact</b> to indicate that you are slightly correcting or giving more detailed information about what you have been saying. 確切地說","examples":["A small number – five, to be exact – have been bad. 一個小數目–確切地說是5–已經很糟了。"]}]}]},"famous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"著名的，出名的；<非正式>極好的，了不起的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>famous</b> is very well known. 有名的","examples":["...one of Kentucky's most famous landmarks. …肯塔基州最有名的標誌之一。"]}]}]},"eastern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"東方的；向東的，朝東的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eastern</b> means in or from the east of a region, state, or country. 東部的","examples":["...Eastern Europe. …東歐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Eastern</b> means coming from or associated with the people or countries of the East, such as India, China, or Japan. 東方國家的","examples":["In many Eastern countries massage was and is a part of everyday life. 在許多東方國家，按摩過去和現在都是日常生活的一部分。"]}]}]},"foolish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愚蠢的，傻的；（因做傻事而）困窘的，難堪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone's behaviour or action is <b>foolish</b>, it is not sensible and shows a lack of good judgment. 愚蠢的","examples":["It would be foolish to raise hopes unnecessarily. 無緣無故地寄託希望是愚蠢的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you look or feel <b>foolish</b>, you look or feel so silly or ridiculous that people are likely to laugh at you. 傻乎乎的","examples":["I just stood there feeling foolish and watching him. 我就傻乎乎地站在那兒看著他。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"愚蠢地","examples":["He admitted that he had acted foolishly. 他承認自己做得很愚蠢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"傻乎乎地","examples":["He saw me standing there, grinning foolishly at him. 他看到我站在那兒咧著嘴朝他傻乎乎地笑。"]}]}]},"grassy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"長滿草的，被草覆蓋的；具有草的特點的，似草的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grassy</b> area of land is covered in grass. 長滿草的","examples":["The buildings are hidden behind grassy banks. 那些建築掩蔽在長滿草的河岸後面。"]}]}]},"formal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"莊重的，合乎禮儀的；（語言）正式的，規範的；合法的；整齊的，佈置井然的；正統的，拘謹的；（教育或培訓）正規的；形式上的，表面的；官方的，公開的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"正式的社交聚會；（女子的）正式禮服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Formal</b> speech or behaviour is very correct and serious rather than relaxed and friendly, and is used especially in official situations. 正式的 (演講、行為)","examples":["He wrote a very formal letter of apology to Douglas. 他寫了一封非常正式的道歉信給道格拉斯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>formal</b> action, statement, or request is an official one. 官方的; 正式的 (行為、陳述、要求等)","examples":["UN officials said a formal request was passed to American authorities. 聯合國官員們稱一份正式的要求已轉給了美國當局。","No formal announcement had been made. 尚無官方宣告。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Formal</b> occasions are special occasions at which people wear elegant clothes and behave according to a set of accepted rules. 正式的 (場合)","examples":["One evening the company arranged a formal dinner after the play. 一天晚上該公司在演出後安排了一場正式的晚宴。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Formal</b> clothes are very elegant clothes that are suitable for formal occasions. 適合正式場合的 (服裝)","examples":["They wore ordinary ties instead of the more formal high collar and cravat. 他們打著普通的領帶而不是更為正式的高領領結。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Formal</b> education or training is given officially, usually in a school, college, or university. 正規的 (教育、培訓等)","examples":["Wendy didn't have any formal dance training. 溫迪沒受過任何正規的舞蹈訓練。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"正式地","examples":["He took her back to Vincent Square in a taxi, saying goodnight formally on the doorstep. 他打計程車將她送回文森特廣場，在門階上客氣地道了晚安。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"官方地; 正式地","examples":["Diplomats haven't formally agreed to Anderson's plan. 外交官們還沒有正式同意安德森的計劃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"正式地","examples":["It was really too warm for her to dress so formally. 她穿得這麼正式真的太熱了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"正規地","examples":["Usually only formally-trained artists from established schools are chosen. 通常只有在知名學校受過正規訓練的藝術家才能被選中。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Formal</b> is also a noun. 正式的社交活動","examples":["...a wide array of events, including school formals and speech nights, weddings, and balls. …一系列豐富多樣的活動，包括學校舞會、演講之夜、婚禮和大型舞會等。"]}]}]},"generous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"慷慨的，大方的；大量的，豐富的；寬宏大量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>generous</b> person gives more of something, especially money, than is usual or expected. 慷慨的","examples":["Dietler is generous with his time and money. 迪特勒在他的時間和金錢方面慷慨大方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>generous</b> person is friendly, helpful, and willing to see the good qualities in someone or something. 寬厚的","examples":["He was always generous in sharing his enormous knowledge. 他一直不吝分享自己豐富的知識。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>generous</b> amount of something is much larger than is usual or necessary. 大量的","examples":["He should be able to keep his room tidy with the generous amount of storage space. 有大量的儲物空間，他應該可以保持他房間的整潔。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"慷慨地","examples":["We would like to thank all the judges who gave so generously of their time. 我們想感謝所有慷慨地付出時間的裁判們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"寬厚地","examples":["The students generously gave them instruction in social responsibility. 學生們欣然為他們講解了社會責任。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"大量地","examples":["Season the steaks generously with salt and pepper. 大量地使用鹽和胡椒給牛排調味。"]}]}]},"former":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"舊時的；以前的，前……；（兩者中）前者的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"模子，模型；形成某事的人（或事）；線圈架，繞線模；（機翼、機身的）翼肋"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（兩者中的）前者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Former</b> is used to describe someone who used to have a particular job, position, or role, but no longer has it. 前任的","examples":["The unemployed executives include former sales managers, directors and accountants. 失業的高管包括前銷售經理、主管和會計。","...former president Richard Nixon. …前總統理查德·尼克松。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Former</b> is used to refer to countries which no longer exist or whose boundaries have changed. (國家) 已不存在的; 疆界已變的","examples":["...the former Soviet Union. …前蘇聯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Former</b> is used to describe something which used to belong to someone or which used to be a particular thing. 昔日的","examples":["...the former home of Robert E. Lee. …羅伯特·E·李的故居。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two people, things, or groups have just been mentioned, you can refer to the first of them as <b>the former</b>. 前者","examples":["They grappled with the problem of connecting the electricity and water supplies. The former proved simple compared with the latter. 他們設法解決供電和供水的連線問題。前者與後者相比證明很簡單。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a person or thing that forms or shapes 形成者; 樣板","examples":[]}]}]},"golden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"金制的；金色的；極好的，成功的；美好的，幸福的；很有才幹的，很受歡迎的；聲音圓潤的；處於有利地位的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>golden</b> is bright yellow in colour. 金黃色的","examples":["She combed and arranged her golden hair. 她梳理好自己的金髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Golden</b> things are made of gold. 金制的","examples":["...a golden chain with a golden locket. …一條帶金制盒式項鍊墜的金項鍊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>golden</b>, you mean it is wonderful because it is likely to be successful and rewarding, or because it is the best of its kind. 黃金般的","examples":["He says there's a golden opportunity for peace which must be seized. 他說必須抓住這個謀求和平的黃金時機。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to a man as a <b>golden boy</b> or a woman as a <b>golden girl</b>, you mean that they are especially popular and successful. 黃金男孩/女郎","examples":["When the film came out the critics went wild, hailing Tarantino as the golden boy of the 1990s. 該影片一上映評論家們就大肆追捧，把塔蘭蒂諾譽為20世紀90年代的黃金男孩。"]}]}]},"friendly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"親切的，友善的；朋友（般）的，要好的；為友誼的，非對抗性的；（國家或政府）友好的，無敵意的；（部隊，裝備）我軍的，友軍的；好用的，無害的；支援的，提供幫助的；令人愉快的；（公司的兼併）自願的"},{"pos":"cn.","zh":"友誼賽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>friendly</b>, they behave in a pleasant, kind way, and like to be with other people. 友好的","examples":["Godfrey had been friendly to me. 戈弗雷過去曾經對我是友好的。","...a man with a pleasant, friendly face. …一個和顏悅色的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>friendly</b> <b>with</b> someone, you like each other and enjoy spending time together. 與…要好的","examples":["I'm friendly with his mother. 我和他的母親很要好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe another country or their government as <b>friendly</b> when they have good relations with your own country rather than being an enemy. (國家或政府) 友好的","examples":["...a worsening in relations between the two previously friendly countries. …兩個先前友好的國家之間關係的惡化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Friendly</b> is also an adjective. 友誼賽的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"友善","examples":["She also loves the friendliness of the people. 她也喜愛人們的友善。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In sports, a <b>friendly</b> is a game which is not part of a competition, and is played for entertainment or practice, often without any serious effort to win. 友誼賽","examples":[]}]}]},"frank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"坦率的，直言不諱的；明白無誤的，症狀明顯的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在信件上）蓋郵資已付印記，蓋免付郵資印記；免費郵寄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美> 法蘭克福燻腸；免費郵寄權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>frank</b>, they state or express things in an open and honest way. 坦率的","examples":["\"It is clear that my client has been less than frank with me,\" said his lawyer. “顯然我的委託人對我不夠坦率，” 他的律師說。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"坦率地","examples":["You can talk frankly to me. 你可以坦率地對我談。"]}]}]},"greedy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"貪婪的，貪心的；貪吃的，嘴饞的；渴望的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>greedy</b>, you mean that they want to have more of something such as food or money than is necessary or fair. 貪婪的","examples":["He attacked greedy bosses for awarding themselves big raises. 他攻擊那些給自己大幅漲工資的貪婪的老闆們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"貪婪地","examples":["Laurie ate the pastries greedily and with huge enjoyment. 勞裡十分快樂而貪婪地吃著那些糕點。"]}]}]},"gentle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"文靜的，溫柔的；（動作）輕柔的，徐緩的；（坡度）平緩的，不陡的；微熱的；<古>出身高貴的，品格高尚的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（或變）溫柔，（使）平靜；使馴服"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛆，餌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>gentle</b> is kind, mild, and calm. 溫和的","examples":["My son was a quiet and gentle man who liked sports and enjoyed life. 我兒子是個安靜溫和的男人，他喜歡運動和享受生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gentle</b> actions or movements are performed in a calm and controlled manner, with little force. (動作) 輕柔的","examples":["...a gentle game of tennis. …一場不很激烈的網球比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>gentle</b> slope or curve is not steep or severe. 平緩的 (斜坡或彎道)","examples":["...gentle, rolling meadows. …平緩、起伏的草地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>gentle</b> heat is a fairly low heat. 微熱的","examples":["Cook for 30 minutes over a gentle heat. 用文火烹飪30分鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"溫和地","examples":["She smiled gently at him. 她溫柔地對他微笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"輕柔地","examples":["Patrick took her gently by the arm and led her to a chair. 帕特里克輕輕地扶著她的手臂，引她落座。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"平緩地","examples":["With its gently rolling hills it looks like Tuscany. 它擁有平緩起伏的山丘，看起來像托斯卡納。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"微熱地","examples":["Add the onion and cook gently for about 5 minutes. 加入洋蔥，文火烹飪5分鐘左右。"]}]}]},"hateful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可惡的，令人討厭的；心懷仇恨的，充滿憎恨的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>hateful</b> is extremely bad or unpleasant. 極壞的; 可惡的","examples":["I'm sorry. That was a hateful thing to say. 對不起，我不該說那麼難聽的話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>hateful</b> hates someone else. 心懷怨恨的","examples":["These are not necessarily hateful, malicious people. 這些不一定是心懷怨恨、有惡意的人。"]}]}]},"humid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"潮溼的，溼熱的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>humid</b> to describe an atmosphere or climate that is very damp, and usually very hot. 溼熱的","examples":["Visitors can expect hot and humid conditions. 遊客們會遇到炎熱潮溼的天氣狀況。"]}]}]},"homesick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"想家的，思鄉病的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>homesick</b>, you feel unhappy because you are away from home and are missing your family, friends, and home very much. 想家的","examples":["She's feeling a little homesick. 她感到有些想家了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"想家","examples":["There were inevitable bouts of homesickness. 難免會生出一陣陣思鄉之情。"]}]}]},"handsome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（男子）英俊的，帥氣的；（女子）端莊健美的；寬敞而美觀的，宏偉的；慷慨的，氣量大的；（金額）可觀的，優厚的；（禮品、獎品）貴重的，值錢的；（勝利）重大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handsome</b> man has an attractive face with regular features. 英俊的","examples":["...a tall, dark, handsome sheep farmer. …一位高個、皮膚黝黑、相貌英俊的牧羊人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>handsome</b> sum of money is a large or generous amount. (款項) 相當大的; 可觀的","examples":["They will make a handsome profit on the property. 他們將從地產中賺取一筆可觀的利潤。"]}]}]},"helpful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有幫助的，有用的；願意幫忙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>helpful</b>, you mean that they help you in some way, such as doing part of your job for you or by giving you advice or information. 有幫助的","examples":["The staff in the branch office are helpful but only have limited information. 該分支機構的員工是幫忙的，但他們僅有有限的資訊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe information or advice as <b>helpful</b>, you mean that it is useful for you. 有用的 (資訊或建議)","examples":["The catalogue includes helpful information on the different bike models available. 該目錄包含所銷售的各種型號腳踏車的有用資訊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>helpful</b> makes a situation more pleasant or more easy to tolerate. 有助益的","examples":["It is often helpful to have your spouse in the room when major news is expected. 在等待重大訊息時，讓你的配偶在場往往是很有好處的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"熱心地","examples":["They had helpfully provided us with instructions on how to find the house. 他們已經熱心地給我們提供瞭如何找到那所房子的說明。"]}]}]},"juicy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多汁的，汁液豐富的；生動有趣的，妙趣橫生的；值很多錢的，報酬豐厚的；<非正式>充滿誘惑的，吸引人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If food is <b>juicy</b>, it has a lot of juice in it and is very enjoyable to eat. 多汁的","examples":["...a thick, juicy steak. …一塊厚而多汁的牛排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Juicy</b> gossip or stories contain details about people's lives, especially details that are normally kept private. 繪聲繪色的","examples":["It provided some juicy gossip for a few days. 這提供了些繪聲繪色的、夠聊幾天的談資。"]}]}]},"latest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最近的，最新的；<古>最遲的，最後的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最新事物，最新訊息（the latest）；最遲，最晚（at the latest）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Latest</b> is the superlative of . (Latest)是(late)的最高階形式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>latest</b> to describe something that is the most recent thing of its kind. 最近的","examples":["...her latest book. …她最近出版的書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>latest</b> to describe something that is very new and modern and is better than older things of a similar kind. 最新式的","examples":["Crooks are using the latest laser photocopiers to produce millions of fake banknotes. 騙子們用最新型的鐳射影印機製作出了上百萬的假鈔。","I got to drive the latest model. 我得以駕駛最新式的車。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>at the latest</b> in order to indicate that something must happen at or before a particular time and not after that time. 最晚","examples":["She should be back by ten o'clock at the latest. 她最晚應該在10點鐘回來。"]}]}]},"independent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自治的，獨立的；自立的，自力更生的；公正的，不受他人影響的；分離的，單獨的；私營的；無黨派的；有主見的，有獨立見解的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨立自主者，獨立團體；無黨派政治家；公理會教友"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person is <b>independent</b> <b>of</b> another, they are separate and not connected, so the first one is not affected or influenced by the second. 無關聯的; 相互獨立的","examples":["Your questions should be independent of each other. 你們的問題應該是相互間毫無關聯的。","We're going independent from the university and setting up our own group. 我們將從大學獨立出去，成立我們自己的集團。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>independent</b>, they do not need help or money from anyone else. 不依賴的","examples":["Phil was now much more independent of his parents. 菲爾現在不大依賴他的父母了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Independent</b> countries and states are not ruled by other countries but have their own government. (國家) 獨立的","examples":["Papua New Guinea became independent from Australia in 1975. 巴布亞紐幾內亞1975年脫離澳大利亞而獨立。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>independent</b> organization or other body is one that controls its own finances and operations, rather than being controlled by someone else. 獨立的; 不受他人左右的","examples":["...an independent television station. …一家獨立的電視臺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>independent</b> inquiry or opinion is one that involves people who are not connected with a particular situation, and should therefore be fair. 客觀公正的; 不偏不倚的","examples":["There were calls in Congress for an independent inquiry. 國會中有對一次獨立調查的呼籲。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An <b>independent</b> politician is one who does not represent any political party. 無黨派的","examples":["There's been a late surge of support for an independent candidate. 對一位獨立候選人的支援最近有驟然的增多。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"獨立地","examples":["...several people working independently in different areas of the world. …在世界不同地區獨立工作的幾個人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不依賴地","examples":["...helping disabled students to live and study as independently as possible. …幫助殘疾學生儘可能不依賴地生活和學習。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>independent</b> is an independent politician. 無黨派人士","examples":["Mr. Vassiliou, standing as an independent, succeeded in convincing a significant number of voters of his argument. 瓦西里歐先生以無黨派人士身份成功地說服了大量選民支援他的觀點。"]}]}]},"lone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨自的，孤單的，寂寞的；唯一的，僅有的；單身的；（地方）人跡稀少的，偏僻的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Lone）人名；（西、肯）洛內；（丹）隆娜；（緬）倫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a <b>lone</b> person or thing, you mean that they are alone. 孤單的","examples":["A lone woman motorist waited for six hours for help yesterday because of a name mix-up. 一位女性獨自駕車者昨日因名字弄混等待了6個小時才得到救援。"]}]}]},"international":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"國際的，國際上的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>國際比賽；<英>國際比賽選手；<美>外國人；共產國際（International）；國際組織，跨國公司"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>International</b> means between or involving different countries. 國際的","examples":["...an international agreement against exporting arms to that country. …一項禁止向那個國家出口武器的國際協議。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"國際上","examples":["...internationally agreed-upon rules. …國際上公認的章程。"]}]}]},"honest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"誠實的，正直的；坦誠的，直率的；真誠的，顯示誠意的；正當獲得的；純正的，不花哨的；無意（傷害別人）的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"真的，確實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>honest</b>, you mean that they always tell the truth, and do not try to deceive people or break the law. 誠實的; 正直的","examples":["I know she's honest and reliable. 我知道她是誠實可靠的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>honest</b> in a particular situation, you tell the complete truth or give your sincere opinion, even if this is not very pleasant. 坦誠的","examples":["I was honest about what I was doing. 我對我所做的一切毫不隱瞞。","He had been honest with her and she had tricked him! 他對她是真誠的，而她卻欺騙了他。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"誠實地; 正直地","examples":["She fought honestly for a just cause and for freedom. 她正直地為正義事業和自由而戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"坦誠地","examples":["It came as a shock to hear an old friend speak so honestly about Ted. 聽到一位老朋友如此坦誠地談論特德真是令人震驚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>honest</b>\" before or after a statement to emphasize that you are telling the truth and that you want people to believe you. 真的; 不騙你","examples":["I'm not sure, honest. 我不能肯定，不騙你。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>honest to God</b>\" to emphasize their feelings or to emphasize that something is really true. (表示強調) 千真萬確","examples":["I wish we weren't doing this, Lillian, honest to God, I really do. 我希望我們沒在做這件事，莉蓮，真的，我確實這麼想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>to be honest</b>\" before or after a statement to indicate that you are telling the truth about your own opinions or feelings, especially if you think these will disappoint the person you are talking to. 老實說","examples":["To be honest the house is not quite our style. 說實話，我們不大喜歡這房子。"]}]}]},"legal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"法律允許的，合法的；與法律有關的，法律的；（與衡平法相對）普通法或成文法確認的；神學律法的，與神學律法有關的；<美>（紙張）標準大小的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Legal</b> is used to describe things that relate to the law. 法律的","examples":["He vowed to take legal action. 他發誓要訴諸法律行動。","...the legal system. …法律制度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An action or situation that is <b>legal</b> is allowed or required by law. 合法的","examples":["What I did was perfectly legal. 我做的事情完全合法。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在法律上","examples":["It could be a bit problematic, legally speaking. 從法律上說，可能是有點問題。"]}]}]},"measurable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"顯著的，有明顯影響的；可測量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>measurable</b>, you mean that it is large enough to be noticed or to be significant. 顯著的","examples":["Both leaders seemed to expect measurable progress. 兩位領導人好像都期待著顯著的進展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>measurable</b> can be measured. 可測量的","examples":["Economists emphasize measurable quantities – the number of jobs, the per capita income. 經濟學家們強調可以測算的量–職位數量，人均收入。"]}]}]},"healthy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"健康的，健壯的；有益身心的；明智的，合理的；運作良好的，興旺發達的；大量的，可觀的"}],"sections":[]},"lovely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可愛的，迷人的；令人愉快的，美好的；親切和善的；<英，非正式>（用於表示對某事物感到惱火）天哪；<英，非正式>（用於表示對某事滿意）好極了"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>美女，佳人；可愛的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>lovely</b>, you mean that they are very beautiful and therefore pleasing to look at or listen to. 美麗的; 美妙的","examples":["You look lovely, Marcia. 你看起來很美，馬西婭。","He had a lovely voice. 他嗓音甜美。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>lovely</b>, you mean that it gives you pleasure. 令人愉快的","examples":["Mary! How lovely to see you! 瑪麗，見到你多麼愉快！","It's a lovely day. 天氣很好。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"漂亮","examples":["You are a vision of loveliness. 你貌美如畫。"]}]}]},"movable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可移動的，活動的；動產的；（節日、日期等）不固定的，逐年變動的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"動產；可移動的東西（常作複數 movables）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>movable</b> can be moved from one place or position to another. 可移動的","examples":["It's a vinyl doll with movable arms and legs. 這是個胳膊和腿都能活動的乙烯基塑膠娃娃。"]}]}]},"modern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"近代的，現代的；當代風格的，現代派的；現代化的，新式的；摩登的，時髦的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"現代人；現代派藝術家；主張現代風格的人，宣揚現代價值觀的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Modern</b> means relating to the present time, for example the present decade or present century. 現代的","examples":["We had a long talk about the problem of materialism in modern society. 我們就現代社會中的實利主義問題進行了一次長談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>modern</b> is new and involves the latest ideas or equipment. 現代化的","examples":["In many ways, it was a very modern school for its time. 從多方面看，這是當時很現代化的一所學校。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People are sometimes described as <b>modern</b> when they have opinions or ways of behaving that have not yet been accepted by most people in a society. 時髦的","examples":["She is very modern in outlook. 她的看法很時髦。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Modern</b> is used to describe styles of art, dance, music, and architecture that have developed in recent times, in contrast to classical styles. (藝術、舞蹈、音樂和建築) 現代派的","examples":["She'd been a dancer with a modern dance company in New York. 她過去一直是紐約一家現代舞公司的舞蹈演員。"]}]}]},"national":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"國家的，全國的；國家所有的，國立的；國內的，本國的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"國民，僑民；全國性比賽；全國性報紙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>National</b> means relating to the whole of a country or nation rather than to part of it or to other nations. 全國的","examples":["...major national and international issues. …重大的國內和國際問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>National</b> means typical of the people or customs of a particular country or nation. 國民的; 民族的","examples":["...the national characteristics and history of the country. …該國的民族特點和歷史。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"全國地","examples":["...a nationally televised speech. …一個全國電視講話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to someone who is legally a citizen of a country as a <b>national</b> of that country. 國民","examples":["...a Sri-Lankan national. …一位斯里蘭卡國民。"]}]}]},"lonely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"孤單的，寂寞的；在孤單中度過的；偏僻的，人跡罕至的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>lonely</b> is unhappy because they are alone or do not have anyone they can talk to. (人) 孤獨的","examples":["...lonely people who just want to talk. …只想聊聊天的孤獨的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lonely</b> situation or period of time is one in which you feel unhappy because you are alone or do not have anyone to talk to. 孤獨的 (情形、時期)","examples":["I desperately needed something to occupy me during those long, lonely nights. 在那些漫長而又孤獨的夜晚我拼命想找點事做。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lonely</b> place is one where very few people come. 偏僻的","examples":["It felt like the loneliest place in the world. 這就像是世界上最偏僻的地方。"]}]}]},"naughty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"頑皮的，淘氣的；不妥當的，（成人）沒規矩的；下流的，淫穢的；<古>邪惡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a child is <b>naughty</b>, you mean that they behave badly or do not do what they are told. 淘氣","examples":["Girls, you're being very naughty. 姑娘們，你們太調皮了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe books, pictures, or words as <b>naughty</b> when they are slightly vulgar or related to sex. 下流的","examples":["You know what little boys are like with naughty words. 你知道小男孩們說下流話是什麼樣子。"]}]}]},"northern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"北方的，向北的，北部的；生活在北方的，源自北方的；（風）北方吹來的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國）北部方言（Northern）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Northern</b> means in or from the north of a region, state, or country. 在北部的; 來自北部的","examples":["Their two children were immigrants to Northern Ireland from Pennsylvania. 他們的兩個孩子是從賓夕法尼亞到北愛爾蘭的移民。"]}]}]},"neat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"整齊的；愛整潔的；巧妙的，簡潔的；靈巧的，利落的；精緻的，小巧的；<美，非正式>很棒的，令人愉快的；（酒）純的，不加冰的；光潔的，光滑的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>neat</b> place, thing, or person is organized and clean, and has everything in the correct place. 整潔的","examples":["So they left her in the neat little house, alone with her memories. 因此他們把她留在那個整潔的小房子裡，獨自一人回憶往事。","Everything was neat and tidy and gleamingly clean. 所有的東西都井然有序，潔淨得閃閃發光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>neat</b> keeps their home or possessions organized and clean, with everything in the correct place. 整潔的 (人)","examples":["\"That's not like Alf,\" he said, \"leaving papers muddled like that. He's always so neat.\" “那可不像阿爾夫，”他說，“讓檔案亂成那樣。他總是很整潔的。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>neat</b> object, part of the body, or shape is quite small and has a smooth outline. 小巧秀氣","examples":["...neat handwriting. …娟秀的字型。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>neat</b> movement or action is done accurately and skilfully, with no unnecessary movements. 乾淨利索的 (行動)","examples":["\"Did you have any trouble?\" Byron asked, driving into a small parking lot and changing the subject in the same neat manoeuvre. “有什麼麻煩嗎？”拜倫問道，同時把車開進了一個小停車場並用同樣乾淨利落的手法轉換了話題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>neat</b> way of organizing, achieving, explaining, or expressing something is clever and convenient. 高明而簡便易行的 (辦法)","examples":["It had been such a neat, clever plan. 這曾是一個如此簡便易行的高明計劃。","Neat solutions are not easily found to these issues. 對這些問題，簡便巧妙的解決辦法不容易被找到。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>neat</b>, you mean that it is very good. 很棒的","examples":["He thought Mick was a really neat guy. 他認為邁克是個很棒很棒的傢伙。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When someone drinks strong alcohol <b>neat</b>, they do not add a weaker liquid such as water to it. 未經稀釋的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"整齊地","examples":["He folded his paper neatly and sipped his coffee. 他把報紙疊整齊，抿著他的咖啡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"整潔地","examples":["I followed her into that room which her mother had maintained so neatly. 我跟著她進了那個她母親保持得特別整潔的房間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"乾淨利索地","examples":["He watched her peel and dissect a pear neatly, no mess, no sticky fingers. 他看著她利索地削了個梨並切成幾塊，整整齊齊，手指乾乾淨淨。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"高明而簡便易行地","examples":["Real people do not fit neatly into these categories. 真實的人們不會簡便地融入這些類別。"]}]}]},"necessary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"必要的，必需的；必然的，不可避免的；迫不得已的，非自願的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（生活）必需品；<英，非正式>必要的事（the necessary）；<英，非正式>足夠的錢（the necessary）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>necessary</b> is needed in order for something else to happen. 必要的","examples":["I kept the engine running because it might be necessary to leave fast. 我讓發動機一直開著，因為可能需要快速離開。","Make the necessary arrangements. 做必要的一些安排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>necessary</b> consequence or connection must happen or exist, because of the nature of the things or events involved. 必然的","examples":["Scientific work is differentiated from art by its necessary connection with the idea of progress. 科學工作不同於藝術在於它與進步的概念有必然聯絡。"]}]}]},"natural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天然的，非人為的；合理的，意料之中的；天生的，本能的；不做作的，真實的；親生的；<舊>私生的；符合是非判斷的；自然科學的；本位音的；（織物）原色的，本白色的；（銅管樂器）無鍵（或孔）的；（與）泛音列音符和間隔（有關）的；（橋牌）（叫牌）實叫的；（基督教神學）物質世界的，非精神的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有天賦的人；適合人選；本位音；白鍵；（紙牌、擲骰子中）最好的組合；天然魚餌；白痴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>natural</b> for someone to act in a particular way or for something to happen in that way, you mean that it is reasonable in the circumstances. 自然的","examples":["It is only natural for youngsters to crave the excitement of driving a fast car. 年輕人渴望開快車的刺激相當自然。","It is only natural that he should resent you. 他會怨恨你是很自然的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Natural</b> behaviour is shared by all people or all animals of a particular type and has not been learned. 天生的 (行為)","examples":["...the insect's natural instinct to feed. …昆蟲進食的天生本能。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone with a <b>natural</b> ability or skill was born with that ability and did not have to learn it. 天賦的 (才能等)","examples":["She has a natural ability to understand the motives of others. 她具備洞察別人動機的天賦。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone's behaviour is <b>natural</b>, they appear to be relaxed and are not trying to hide anything. 自然的","examples":["Bethan's sister was as friendly and natural as the rest of the family. 伯森的姊妹和其他家庭成員一樣親切自然。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Natural</b> things exist or occur in nature and are not made or caused by people. 天然的","examples":["The gigantic natural harbour is a haven for boats. 這個巨大的天然港是船舶的避風港。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>a</b> <b>natural</b>, you mean that they do something very well and very easily. 天才","examples":["He's a natural with any kind of engine. 他是發動機方面的天才。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自然地","examples":["For pictures of people behaving naturally, not posing for the camera, it is essential to shoot unnoticed. 要拍攝人物表現自然、不對鏡頭擺姿式的照片，抓拍很關鍵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"天然地","examples":["Nitrates are chemicals that occur naturally in water and the soil. 硝酸鹽是水和土壤裡天然存在的化學物質。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone dies <b>of</b> or <b>from</b> <b>natural causes</b>, they die because they are ill or old rather than because of an accident or violence. 自然原因","examples":["Your brother died of natural causes. 你哥哥是自然死亡。"]}]}]},"ordinary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普通的，平常的；平淡無奇的，平庸的；（尤指法官、主教）常任的，本身有權的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常見的人（或事物）（the ordinary）；<英>常任法官；管區長，教區長（the Ordinary）；（羅馬天主教）常規彌撒（Ordinary）；禮拜式規程書典（Ordinary）；（紋章）普通圖記；普通股（ordinary share 的簡稱）；<美>（前輪大後輪小的）老式腳踏車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ordinary</b> people or things are normal and not special or different in any way. 普通的","examples":["I strongly suspect that most ordinary people would agree with me. 我強烈地感到大多數普通老百姓會贊同我。","It has 25 calories less than ordinary ice cream. 它的熱量比普通的冰淇淋少25卡路里。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>out of the ordinary</b> is unusual or different. 不尋常的","examples":["The boy's knowledge was out of the ordinary. 這個男孩的知識面非同尋常。"]}]}]},"naked":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"裸露的，無遮蓋的；肉眼的；裸體的，不穿衣服的；露骨的，明顯的；缺乏保護的，無力自衛的；（動物）沒有皮毛的，沒有羽毛的；公然的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>naked</b> is not wearing any clothes. 裸體的","examples":["Her naked body was found wrapped in a sheet in a field. 她赤裸的屍體在野外被找到了，裹在一張床單裡。","They stripped me naked. 他們扒了我的衣服使我全身赤裸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an animal or part of an animal is <b>naked</b>, it has no fur or feathers on it. 沒有毛的","examples":["The nest contained eight little mice that were naked and blind. 這窩裡有8只小老鼠，沒毛也看不見東西。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe an object as <b>naked</b> when it does not have its normal covering. 無 (正常) 遮蓋的","examples":["...a naked bulb dangling in a bare room. …一隻沒有燈罩、在一個空房間裡搖盪的燈泡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>naked</b> to describe unpleasant or violent actions and behaviour which are not disguised or hidden in any way. 公然的; 赤裸裸的 (行為等)","examples":["Naked aggression and an attempt to change frontiers by force could not go unchallenged. 對公然侵略和企圖用武力改變疆域，人們不會坐視不管。","...violence and the naked pursuit of power. …暴力和對權力赤裸裸的追求。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"裸體","examples":["He had pulled the blanket over his body to hide his nakedness. 他拽過了毯子蓋在他的身體上以遮住他的裸體。"]}]}]},"playful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛嬉戲的，頑皮的，活潑的；開玩笑的，幽默的，鬧著玩的；（用於作品、設計等）輕鬆有趣的，俏皮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>playful</b> gesture or person is friendly or humorous. 鬧著玩的","examples":["...a playful kiss on the tip of his nose. …在他鼻尖上的戲吻。","...a playful fight. …一場鬧著玩的打鬧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>playful</b> animal is lively and cheerful. 頑皮的","examples":["...a playful puppy. …一隻頑皮的小狗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鬧著玩地","examples":["She pushed him away playfully. 她開玩笑地將他推開。"]}]}]},"painful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"疼痛的；引起疼痛的；令人痛苦（難受）的，困難的；<非正式>令人難堪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body is <b>painful</b>, it hurts because it is injured or because there is something wrong with it. 疼痛的","examples":["Her glands were swollen and painful. 她的腺體腫脹且疼痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as an illness, injury, or operation is <b>painful</b>, it causes you a lot of physical pain. 令人疼痛的","examples":["...a painful back injury. …令人疼痛的背傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Situations, memories, or experiences that are <b>painful</b> are difficult and unpleasant to deal with, and often make you feel sad and upset. (情形、記憶或經歷) 痛苦的","examples":["Remarks like that brought back painful memories. 像那樣的評論勾起了痛苦的記憶。","...the painful transition to democracy. …邁向民主的艱難過渡期。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"疼痛地","examples":["His tooth had started to throb painfully again. 他的牙又開始抽痛了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"令人疼痛地","examples":["...cracking his head painfully against the cupboard. …他的頭撞到碗櫃上，很痛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"痛苦地; 令人難過地","examples":["...their old relationship, which he had painfully broken off. …他們之間已經被他痛苦地斬斷了的老關係。"]}]}]},"particular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"特定的，某一的；格外的，特別的；講究的，挑剔的；特殊的，獨特的；詳細的，詳盡的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一點，一個細節； 詳細資料，詳情（particulars）；（哲學）（與普遍性相對的）特殊性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>particular</b> to emphasize that you are talking about one thing or one kind of thing rather than other similar ones. 專指的","examples":["I remembered a particular story about a mailman who was a murderer. 我記得一個故事，關於一個郵遞員是殺人犯。","I have to know exactly why it is I'm doing a particular job. 我必須確切地知道我為什麼做某項工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing has a <b>particular</b> quality or possession, it is distinct and belongs only to them. 獨特的","examples":["I have a particular responsibility to ensure I make the right decision. 我有特別責任要確保做出正確的決定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>particular</b> to emphasize that something is greater or more intense than usual. 非同尋常的","examples":["Particular emphasis will be placed on oral language training. 口語訓練將給予非同尋常的重視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>particular</b>, you mean that they choose things and do things very carefully, and are not easily satisfied. 挑剔的","examples":["Ted was very particular about the colours he used. 特德對於他使用的顏色是非常挑剔的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in particular</b> to indicate that what you are saying applies especially to one thing or person. 特別","examples":["The situation in Ethiopia in particular is worrisome. 衣索比亞的局勢特別令人擔憂。","Why should he notice her car in particular? 他為什麼要特別注意她的轎車呢？"]}]}]},"peaceful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寧靜的，安靜的；和平的，非暴力的；愛好和平的；安詳的，平和的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Peaceful</b> activities and situations do not involve war. 和平的 (活動、局面)","examples":["He has attempted to find a peaceful solution to the Ossetian conflict. 他曾試圖找到一個解決奧塞梯衝突的和平的辦法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Peaceful</b> occasions happen without violence or serious disorder. 和平的 (場景)","examples":["The farmers staged a noisy but peaceful protest outside the headquarters of the organization. 農民們在該組織總部外舉行了一次喧鬧但和平的抗議活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Peaceful</b> people are not violent and try to avoid arguing or fighting with other people. 和平的 (人們)","examples":["...warriors who killed or enslaved the peaceful farmers. …殺死或奴役和平的農民們的那些武士。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>peaceful</b> place or time is quiet, calm, and free from disturbance. 安寧的 (地方、時期)","examples":["...a peaceful house in the heart of the Ozarks. …在歐扎克山脈中心地帶的一幢安寧的房子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"和平地","examples":["The U.S. military expects the matter to be resolved peacefully. 美國軍方期望這一事件能和平解決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"和平地","examples":["The governor asked the crowd of protestors to leave peacefully. 州長要求抗議人群和平離開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"和平地","examples":["They've been living and working peacefully with members of various ethnic groups. 他們一直與各種族群的成員們和平地生活和工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"安寧地","examples":["Except for traffic noise the night passed peacefully. 除了交通噪音，那夜安寧地過去了。"]}]}]},"polite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有禮貌的，客氣的；禮節性的，客套的；上流的，有教養的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>polite</b> has good manners and behaves in a way that is socially correct and not rude to other people. 有禮貌的","examples":["Everyone around him was trying to be polite, but you could tell they were all bored. 他身邊的每一個人都盡力表現得彬彬有禮，但你可以看出他們都厭倦了。","Gonzales, a quiet and very polite young man, made a favourable impression. 岡薩雷斯是個文靜而又很有禮貌的年輕人，給人留下了很好的印象。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"禮貌地","examples":["\"Your home is beautiful,\" I said politely. “你的家很漂亮，”我客氣地說。"]}]}]},"pleasant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人愉快的，愜意的；禮貌而友善的，和藹可親的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>pleasant</b> is nice, enjoyable, or attractive. 令人愉快的","examples":["I've got a pleasant little apartment. 我有一套舒適的小公寓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>pleasant</b> is friendly and likeable. 友善的","examples":["The woman had a pleasant face. 那個女人長著一張和善的臉。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人愉快地","examples":["We talked pleasantly of old times. 我們愉快地談論著過去的時光。"]}]}]},"popular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"受大眾喜愛的，受歡迎的；（想法、情緒或態度）普遍的；通俗的，大眾化的；民眾的，百姓的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>popular</b> is enjoyed or liked by a lot of people. (物) 廣受喜愛的","examples":["Chocolate sauce is always popular with youngsters. 巧克力醬總是受年輕人喜愛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>popular</b> is liked by most people, or by most people in a particular group. (人) 廣受喜愛的","examples":["He remained the most popular politician in Arkansas. 他仍是阿肯色州最廣受喜愛的政治家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Popular</b> newspapers, television programmes, or forms of art are aimed at ordinary people and not at experts or intellectuals. 面向大眾的; 通俗的","examples":["Once again the popular press in Britain has been rife with stories about their marriage. 英國大眾媒體中又充斥著他們的婚事報導。","...one of the classics of modern popular music. …現代通俗音樂的經典之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Popular</b> ideas, feelings, or attitudes are approved of or held by most people. 廣受贊同的","examples":["Contrary to popular belief, the oil companies can't control the price of crude. 和大眾的想法相反，各石油公司控制不了原油的價格。","The military government has been unable to win popular support. 軍政府沒能贏得公眾的支援。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Popular</b> is used to describe political activities that involve the ordinary people of a country, and not just members of political parties. 民眾的 (政治活動)","examples":["The late president Ferdinand Marcos was overthrown by a popular uprising in 1986. 已故總統費迪南德·馬科斯於1986年被民眾起義所推翻。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(物的) 受喜愛度","examples":["...the growing popularity of Australian wines among consumers. …澳大利亞葡萄酒越來越受消費者青睞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(人的) 受喜愛度","examples":["It is his popularity with ordinary people that sets him apart. 他深受普通群眾的喜愛，正是這一點使他與眾不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"受贊同度","examples":["Over time, though, Watson's views gained in popularity. 然而，隨著時間的推移，沃森的觀點越來越受到贊同。"]}]}]},"powerful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人，組織，國家）強大的，有影響力的；大功率的，高效能的；（文章、演講或藝術品）極具感染力的，有震撼力的；（感情）強烈的，（效果）巨大的；強壯的，強健的；猛烈的，有力的；（毒品或化學品）強效的；刺耳的，刺眼的，刺鼻的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，很"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>powerful</b> person or organization is able to control or influence people and events. 有影響力的","examples":["You're a powerful man – people will listen to you. 你是個有影響力的人–人們會聽你的。","...Russia and India, two large, powerful countries. …俄羅斯和印度——兩個有影響力的大國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that someone's body is <b>powerful</b> when it is physically strong. 強壯的","examples":["Hans flexed his powerful muscles. 漢斯放鬆了他強壯的肌肉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>powerful</b> machine or substance is effective because it is very strong. 效力強大的","examples":["The more powerful the car the more difficult it is to handle. 汽車的功效越大，操縱起來越難。","...powerful computer systems. …強大的計算機系統。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>powerful</b> smell is very strong. 濃烈的","examples":["There was a powerful smell of stale beer. 有一股濃烈的餿啤酒的氣味。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>powerful</b> voice is loud and can be heard from a long way away. 洪亮的","examples":["At that moment Mrs. Jones's powerful voice interrupted them, announcing a visitor. 這時，瓊斯太太洪亮的嗓音打斷了他們，說有位客人來了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You describe a piece of writing, speech, or work of art as <b>powerful</b> when it has a strong effect on people's feelings or beliefs. 有感染力的","examples":["...a powerful 11-part drama about a corrupt city leader. …一部有關一位腐敗的市領導、有感染力的、由11部分組成的戲劇作品。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"強壯地","examples":["He is described as a strong, powerfully-built man of 60. 他被描述成一個身強力壯的60歲的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"效力大地","examples":["Crack is a much cheaper, smokable form of cocaine which is powerfully addictive. 強效可卡因是一種便宜得多的可吸食性可卡因，非常容易上癮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"強烈地","examples":["The air smelled powerfully of dry dust. 空氣中瀰漫著濃烈的塵土味。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"有感染力地","examples":["It's a play – painful, funny, and powerfully acted. 這是一齣戲–令人痛苦而又逗人發笑，演得很有感染力。"]}]}]},"personal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"個人的，私人的；私密的，隱私的；針對個人的，人身攻擊的；人身的，身體的；人際的，私交的；供個人使用的；親自的；有人性的；（語法）人稱的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（報紙私人廣告欄內的）私人資訊釋出，私人廣告；（報紙或雜誌上的）個人啟事欄，私人廣告欄（the personals）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>personal</b> opinion, quality, or thing belongs or relates to one particular person rather than to other people. 個人的; 私人的","examples":["He learned this lesson the hard way – from his own personal experience. 他慘痛地得到了這一教訓–從他自己的親身經歷中得來的。","That's my personal opinion. 這是我的個人意見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give something your <b>personal</b> care or attention, you deal with it yourself rather than letting someone else deal with it. 親自的","examples":["...a business that requires a lot of personal contact. …一樁需要很多親自聯絡的生意。","...a personal letter from the president's secretary. …一封來自總統秘書的親筆信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Personal</b> matters relate to your feelings, relationships, and health. 有關個人的","examples":["...teaching young people about marriage and personal relationships. …教導年輕人婚姻和人際關係。","You never allow personal problems to affect your performance. 絕不容許個人問題影響你的表現。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Personal</b> comments refer to someone's appearance or character in an offensive way. 人身的","examples":["Newspapers resorted to personal abuse. 報紙搞起了人身攻擊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Personal</b> care involves taking care of your body and appearance. 個人體貌的","examples":["...the new breed of men who take as much time and trouble over personal hygiene as the women in their lives. …生活中，和女人花一樣多時間和精力在個人衛生上的新型男士。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>personal</b> relationship is one that is not connected with your job or public life. 與公務無關的; 私人的","examples":["He was a great and valued personal friend whom I've known for many years. 他是個非常好的、很寶貴的私人朋友，我們已相識多年。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone has a <b>personal</b> shopper or a <b>personal</b> trainer, they employ another person to shop for them or to help them keep fit. 屬於個人的","examples":["Another way of escaping the crowds and the changing rooms is to employ a personal shopper. 另一個逃避人群和更衣室的辦法是僱一個私人採購專員。","The best clubs also offer personal trainers to help motivate and ensure that exercises are properly performed. 最好的俱樂部還提供私人教練，來幫助激發動力，並確保訓練適當地進行。"]}]}]},"rainy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多雨的；下雨的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"During a <b>rainy</b> day, season, or period it rains a lot. 多雨的","examples":["The rainy season in the Andes normally starts in December. 安第斯山脈的雨季一般從12月開始。"]}]}]},"proud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自豪的，得意的；令人自豪的；傲慢的，自負的；自尊的，自重的；秀麗的，壯觀的；凸出的，隆起的；（肌肉）癒合傷口四周贅生的；（動物）有力量的，精力充沛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>proud</b>, you feel pleased about something good that you possess or have done, or about something good that a person close to you has done. 自豪的","examples":["I felt proud of his efforts. 我為他的努力感到自豪。","They are proud that she is doing well at school. 他們為她在學校功課好而自豪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>proudest</b> moments or achievements are the ones that you are most proud of. 最自豪的","examples":["This must have been one of the proudest moments of his busy and hard-working life. 在他忙碌、勤奮的一生中，這可能是他最自豪的時刻之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>proud</b> has respect for themselves and does not want to lose the respect that other people have for them. 有自尊心的","examples":["He was too proud to ask his family for help and support. 他自尊心太高，不肯請求家裡人的幫助和支援。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>proud</b> feels that they are better or more important than other people. 驕傲的","examples":["She was said to be proud and arrogant. 據說，她驕傲且自大。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自豪地","examples":["\"That's the first part finished,\" he said proudly. “那是完成的第一部分，”他自豪地說。"]}]}]},"rare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"少見的，不常發生的；稀罕的，珍貴的；半熟的，半生的；（品質）極好的，傑出的；（空氣）稀薄的，缺氧的；<英，非正式>非常的，極度的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>rare</b> is not common and is therefore interesting or valuable. 稀有的","examples":["...the black-necked crane, one of the rarest species in the world. …黑頸鶴，世界上最珍稀的物種之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An event or situation that is <b>rare</b> does not occur very often. 罕見的","examples":["...on those rare occasions when he did eat alone. …在他獨自吃飯的那些不常有的時候。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>rare</b> to emphasize an extremely good or remarkable quality. 極好的 (素質)","examples":["Ferris has a rare ability to record her observations on paper. 費里斯有將自己的觀察結果以書面形式記錄下來的傑出能力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Meat that is <b>rare</b> is cooked very lightly so that the inside is still red. (肉類) 半熟的","examples":["Thick tuna steaks are eaten rare, like beef. 厚厚的金槍魚片要半熟吃，就像牛肉一樣。"]}]}]},"rapid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"快的，迅速的；（移動，活動）快速的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"急流，湍灘；高速交通工具，高速交通網"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rapid</b> change is one that happens very quickly. (變化) 快速的","examples":["...the country's rapid economic growth in the 1980s. …這個國家在20世紀80年代快速的經濟增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rapid</b> movement is one that is very fast. (動作) 迅速的","examples":["He walked at a rapid pace along Charles Street. 他沿著查爾斯大街快步行走。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"快速地","examples":["...countries with rapidly growing populations. …人口快速增長的國家。","Try to rip it apart as rapidly as possible. 試著儘快把它撕開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"迅速地","examples":["He was moving rapidly around the room. 他正在房間裡快速地來回走著。"]}]}]},"private":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"私有的，自用的；（服務，行業）私營的，民營的；沒有股票上市的；私下的，秘密的；（交易未涉及商業機構的）私下裡的；（想法、感覺）私密的；未擔任公職的，無官職的；與官職（或工作）無關的；安靜的，不受打擾的；（人）內斂的，不喜歡談論私事的；（尤指兩人）單獨的；私下輔導的；（教育，醫療）私立的；只有自己人明白的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美、英陸軍或美國海軍陸戰隊）二等兵；<非正式> 私處，陰部（privates）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Private</b> companies, industries, and services are owned or controlled by individuals or stockholders, rather than by the government or an official organization. 私有的","examples":["...a joint venture with private industry. …一個與私有企業合資的企業。","They sent their children to private schools. 他們送孩子們上私立學校。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Private</b> individuals are acting only for themselves, and are not representing any group, company, or organization. 代表個人行事的","examples":["Private individuals with money to lend are more difficult to find than traditional lenders. 有錢借的個人比傳統的放貸者更難找。","The king was on a private visit to enable him to pray at the tombs of his ancestors. 國王在做一次私訪以便能祭拜其祖墳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>private</b> things belong only to you, or may only be used by you. 私人的 (財物)","examples":["They want more state control over private property. 他們想要對私人財產更多國家控制。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Private</b> places or gatherings may be attended only by a particular group of people, rather than by the general public. 不對外開放的","examples":["673 private golf clubs took part in a recent study. 673家不對外開放的高爾夫俱樂部參加了最近的一次調查。","The door is marked \"Private.\" 門上寫著“閒人免進”。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Private</b> meetings, discussions, and other activities involve only a small number of people, and very little information about them is given to other people. 私下的 (會晤、討論等)","examples":["Don't bug private conversations, and don't buy papers that reprint them. 不要竊聽私下談話，也不要買翻印這種談話的報紙。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Your <b>private</b> <b>life</b> is that part of your life that is concerned with your personal relationships and activities, rather than with your work or business. 私人的 (生活)","examples":["I've always kept my private and professional life separate. 我一向將我的私生活和職業生涯分開。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>private</b> thoughts or feelings are ones that you do not talk about to other people. 私下的 (想法、情感)","examples":["We all felt as if we were intruding on his private grief. 我們都覺得好像我們在觸犯他的個人悲痛。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you describe a place as <b>private</b>, or as somewhere where you can be <b>private</b>, you mean that it is a quiet place and you can be alone there without being disturbed. 無他人打擾的 (地方)","examples":["It was the only reasonably private place they could find. 這是他們能找到的惟一頗不受他人打擾的地方。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>private</b> person, you mean that they are very quiet by nature and do not reveal their thoughts and feelings to other people. 孤僻的","examples":["Gould was an intensely private individual. 古爾德曾是個相當孤僻的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"私有地","examples":["No other European country had so much state ownership and so few privately owned businesses. 沒有任何別的歐洲國家有這麼多的國有企業和這麼少的私有企業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"私下地","examples":["Few senior figures have issued any public statements but privately the resignation's been welcomed. 幾乎沒有高階人物發表過任何公開宣告，但私底下辭職是受歡迎的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"私下地","examples":["Privately, she worries about whether she's really good enough. 私下裡，她擔心她是不是真的夠好。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>private</b> is a soldier of the lowest rank in an army or the marines. 列兵","examples":["He was a private in the U.S. Army. 他是美國陸軍中的一名列兵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in private</b>, you do it without other people being present, often because it is something that you want to keep secret. 私下地","examples":["Some of what we're talking about might better be discussed in private. 我們正在談論的有些事也許私下討論更好。"]}]}]},"recent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最近的，最新的；（地質）全新世的 （Recent）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>recent</b> event or period of time happened only a short while ago. 最近的","examples":["In the most recent attack, one man was shot dead and two others were wounded. 在最近的這次襲擊中有1人被打死，另2人受傷。"]}]}]},"rocky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"岩石構成的，多岩石的；堅如岩石的；晃動的，不穩的；身體搖搖晃晃的，頭暈目眩的；（局勢、關係）不穩固的，困難重重的；與搖滾樂有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rocky</b> place is covered with rocks or consists of large areas of rock and has nothing growing on it. 多岩石的","examples":["The paths are often very rocky so strong boots are advisable. 這些道路通常有很多岩石，所以建議穿結實的靴子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"weak, shaky, or unstable 軟弱的; 搖晃的; 不穩定的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rocky</b> situation or relationship is unstable and full of difficulties. 不穩定的; 艱難的","examples":["They had gone through some rocky times together when Ann was first married. 當安剛結婚的時候，他們已經一起度過了一些不尋常的日子。"]}]}]},"salty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鹹的，含鹽的；<舊>有趣而略顯粗俗的；<非正式>粗魯的，愛鬧事的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>salty</b> contains salt or tastes of salt. 含鹽的; 鹹的","examples":["...salty foods such as ham and bacon. …例如火腿和燻肉這樣的鹹味食品。"]}]}]},"royal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"國王的，女王的，王室的；（用於機構或組織名稱）皇家的 ；盛大的，隆重的；<非正式>（用於強調某人或某物極度糟糕）極其的，極度的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>王室成員；（鳴鐘術）敲奉十口鐘的變換響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Royal</b> is used to indicate that something is connected with a king, queen, or emperor, or their family. A <b>royal</b> person is a king, queen, or emperor, or a member of their family. 王室的","examples":["...an invitation to a royal garden party. …一張參加皇家花園聚會的請帖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Royal</b> is used in the names of institutions or organizations that are officially appointed or supported by a member of a royal family. 皇家的","examples":["...the Royal Academy of Music. …皇家音樂學院。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Members of the royal family are sometimes referred to as <b>royals</b>. 王室成員","examples":["The royals have always been patrons of charities pulling in large donations. 王室成員一直都是慈善機構的資助人，注入大量捐贈。"]}]}]},"responsible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（對某人、某事）負責的；（對事故、錯誤、罪行等）負有責任的，應承擔責任的；（工作或職位）重要的，責任重大的；可靠的，負責任的；作為緣由的，應受歸咎的；向......負責的，向......彙報的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>responsible</b> <b>for</b> a particular event or situation, they are the cause of it or they can be blamed for it. 負有責任的","examples":["He still felt responsible for her death. 他依然覺得對她的死負有責任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>responsible</b> <b>for</b> something, it is your job or duty to deal with it and make decisions relating to it. 負責的","examples":["...the cabinet member responsible for the environment. …負責環境的內閣成員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>responsible to</b> a person or group, they have authority over you and you have to report to them about what you do. 向…彙報的","examples":["I'm responsible to my board of directors. 我向我的董事會彙報。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Responsible</b> people behave properly and sensibly, without needing to be supervised. 有責任心的","examples":["He feels that the media should be more responsible in what they report. 他覺得媒體應該對他們的報道更負責些。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Responsible</b> jobs involve making important decisions or carrying out important tasks. 責任重大的","examples":["You are too young for such a responsible position. 對於這樣一個責任重大的職位，你太年輕了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有責任心地","examples":["He urged everyone to act responsibly. 他力勸每一個人做事要負責。"]}]}]},"rude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗魯的，無禮的；粗俗的，下流的；突如其來的，猛烈的；<文> 簡陋的，粗製的；<英> 有活力的，粗壯的；<古> 未開化的，原始的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people are <b>rude</b>, they act in an impolite way toward other people or say impolite things about them. 無禮的; 粗魯的","examples":["He's rude to her friends and obsessively jealous. 他對她的朋友粗魯無禮而且過分嫉妒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rude</b> is used to describe words and behaviour that are likely to embarrass or offend people, because they relate to sex or to body functions. 下流的","examples":["Fred keeps cracking rude jokes with the guests. 弗雷德不停地和那些客人開下流的玩笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone receives a <b>rude</b> shock, something unpleasant happens unexpectedly. 令人不快的","examples":["It will come as a rude shock when their salary or income-tax refund cannot be cashed. 如果他們的薪水或所得稅返還不能兌現，那對他們將是一個晴天霹靂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無禮地; 粗魯地","examples":["I could not understand why she felt compelled to behave so rudely to a friend. 我不能理解為什麼她非要如此粗魯地對待一位朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"令人不快地","examples":["People were rudely awakened by a siren just outside their window. 人們被窗外的一聲警報驚醒了。"]}]}]},"shocked":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"吃驚的，震驚的；憤慨的，十分厭惡的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使震驚，使驚愕；（使）生氣，（使）不快；使生理休克，使受電擊（shock 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>shock</b>, something suddenly happens which is unpleasant, upsetting, or very surprising. 震驚","examples":["The extent of the violence came as a shock. 暴力的程度令人震驚。","He has never recovered from the shock of your brother's death. 他從來沒有從你兄弟的死所帶來的震驚中恢復過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shock</b> is a person's emotional and physical condition when something very frightening or upsetting has happened to them. (身心受到的) 驚嚇","examples":["The little boy was speechless with shock. 這個小男孩被嚇得說不出話來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>in</b> <b>shock</b>, they are suffering from a serious physical condition in which their blood is not flowing around their body properly, for example, because they have had a bad injury. 休克","examples":["He was found beaten and in shock. 他被發現遭到毆打，處於休克中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>shock</b> is the force of something suddenly hitting or pulling something else. 衝擊力","examples":["Steel barriers can bend and absorb the shock. 鐵柵欄會彎曲並吸收衝擊力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>shock</b> is the same as an . 電擊","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a thick bushy mass, esp of hair (尤指頭髮)濃密厚重的一把","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shocks</b> you, it makes you feel very upset, because it involves death or suffering and because you had not expected it. 使震驚","examples":["After forty years in the police force nothing much shocks me. 在警察部門幹了40年後，沒有什麼能令我非常震驚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>shocks</b> you, it upsets or offends you because you think it is vulgar or morally wrong. 使不快; 不快","examples":["You can't shock me. 你不會讓我生氣。","They were easily shocked in those days. 他們那時候容易被激怒。","...the desire to shock …發怒的慾望。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"震驚的","examples":["This was a nasty attack and the woman is still very shocked. 這是一次嚴重的襲擊，這個女人仍然感到非常震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"生氣的","examples":["Don't look so shocked. 別這麼生氣。"]}]}]},"skillful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（指人）熟練的，有技巧的，靈巧的；（指動作、作品等）巧妙的，精巧的"}],"sections":[]},"skilled":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熟練的，有技能的；技術性的，需要熟練技術的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>skilled</b> has the knowledge and ability to do something well. 有技術的; 熟練的","examples":["Few doctors are actually trained, and not all are skilled, in helping their patients make choices. 在幫助病人做選擇方面，沒有幾個醫生實際受過訓練，也並非所有的醫生都很熟練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Skilled</b> work can only be done by people who have had some training. 需要熟練能力的; 需要專門技術的","examples":["New industries demanded skilled labour not available locally. 新興產業需要熟練技術工人，而當地沒有。"]}]}]},"skinny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極瘦的，皮包骨的；（衣服）緊身的；<非正式>低脂肪的，加脫脂奶的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"骨瘦如柴的人，瘦骨嶙峋的人；<美，非正式>內部訊息，機密情報（the skinny）；緊身牛仔褲或長褲（skinnies）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>skinny</b> person is extremely thin, often in a way that you find unattractive. 瘦得皮包骨的","examples":["He was quite a skinny little boy. 他是個骨瘦如柴的小男孩。"]}]}]},"similar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相像的，類似的；（幾何圖形）相似的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>相似之人（或物）；順勢藥物（指療效與某些疾病症狀相似的藥物，為順勢療法的基礎）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>similar to</b> another, or if two things are <b>similar</b>, they have features that are the same. 相似的","examples":["...a savoury cake with a texture similar to that of carrot cake. …一塊口感跟胡蘿蔔餅差不多的鹹味餅。","The accident was similar to one that happened in 1973. 這起事故跟1973年發生的那起相似。"]}]}]},"silent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）安靜的，沉默的；沉默寡言的，不愛說話的；（事物）無聲的，寂靜的；（情感、行為等）不用言語表達的，默默的；隻字不提的，不願講的；（電影）無聲的；（字母）不發音的；（疾病或問題等）悄然的，無症狀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>silent</b> is not speaking. 沉默的","examples":["Trish was silent because she was reluctant to put her thoughts into words. 特里希一言不發，因為她不願意把她的想法說出來。","He spoke no English and was completely silent during the visit. 他不會說英語，在整個參觀中一言不發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A place that is <b>silent</b> is completely quiet, with no sound at all. Something that is <b>silent</b> makes no sound at all. 寂靜的","examples":["The room was silent except for the TV. 除了電視的聲音，那房間裡寂靜無聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>silent</b> movie has pictures usually accompanied by music but does not have the actors' voices or any other sounds. (電影) 無聲的","examples":["...one of the famous silent films of Charlie Chaplin. …查理·卓別林著名的無聲電影之一。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沉默地","examples":["She and Ned sat silently for a moment, absorbing the peace of the lake. 她和內德默默地坐了片刻，享受著那湖泊的寧靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"寂靜地","examples":["Strange shadows moved silently in the almost permanent darkness. 奇怪的影子在幾乎永遠的黑暗中靜靜地移動。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give</b> someone <b>the silent treatment</b>, you do not speak to them for a period of time because you are annoyed at something they have done. 長期不跟某人說話","examples":["He fully expected his mother to give him the silent treatment. 他完全預料得到他母親會長時間不跟他講話。"]}]}]},"sleepy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"睏倦的，想睡的；（城鎮或地區）寂靜的，冷清的；（生意，組織，工業）沒有活力的，呆滯的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sleepy</b>, you are very tired and are almost asleep. 睏倦的; 昏昏欲睡的","examples":["I was beginning to feel amazingly sleepy. 我開始感覺到特別困。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sleepy</b> place is quiet and does not have much activity or excitement. 寂靜的; 不活躍的","examples":["Valence is a sleepy little town just south of Lyon. 瓦朗斯是里昂正南方一個寂靜的小鎮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"睏倦地; 昏昏欲睡地","examples":["Joanna sat up, blinking sleepily. 喬安娜坐了起來，睡意未消地眨著眼睛。"]}]}]},"serious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嚴重的，危急的；認真的，嚴肅的；重要的，須重視的；（音樂、文學等藝術）嚴肅的；（人）莊重的，嚴肅的；<非正式>大量的，極多的；（戀愛中）態度認真的；極感興趣的，熱衷的；<非正式>很好的，質優價高的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Serious</b> problems or situations are very bad and cause people to be worried or afraid. 嚴重的; 危急的","examples":["Crime is an increasingly serious problem in Russian society. 犯罪是俄羅斯社會一個日益嚴重的問題。","The government still face very serious difficulties. 政府仍面臨著非常嚴重的困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Serious</b> matters are important and deserve careful and thoughtful consideration. 重要的","examples":["I regard this as a serious matter. 我認為這是一件重要的事情。","Don't laugh boy. This is serious. 不要笑，夥計。這事很重要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When important matters are dealt with in a <b>serious</b> way, they are given careful and thoughtful consideration. 認真的; 嚴肅的","examples":["My parents never really faced up to my drug use in any serious way. 我的父母從未真正認真面對我吸毒的問題。","It was a question which deserved serious consideration. 這是一個值得認真考慮的問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Serious</b> music or literature requires concentration to understand or appreciate it. 嚴肅的","examples":["...serious classical music. …嚴肅的古典音樂。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone is <b>serious</b> <b>about</b> something, they are sincere about what they are saying, doing, or intending to do. 真心的; 鄭重的","examples":["You really are serious about this, aren't you? 你對這事確實是認真的，是吧？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Serious</b> people are thoughtful and quiet, and do not laugh very often. 嚴肅的","examples":["He's quite a serious person. 他是一個相當嚴肅的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴重地; 危急地","examples":["If this ban was to come in it would seriously damage my business. 這項禁令如果實施，將會嚴重地損害我的生意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"認真地; 嚴肅地","examples":["The management will have to think seriously about their positions. 管理層將不得不認真考慮他們的立場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"真心地; 鄭重地","examples":["Are you seriously jealous of Erica? 你真的妒忌埃裡卡嗎?"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"嚴肅地","examples":["They spoke to me very seriously but politely. 他們非常嚴肅但又很有禮貌地與我談話。"]}]}]},"slender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"苗條的，纖細的；（尤指竿、枝或莖）細長的，狹窄的；微薄的，不足的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slender</b> person is attractively thin and graceful. 苗條的; 優美的","examples":["She was slender, with delicate wrists and ankles. 她身材苗條，有著纖細的手腕和腳踝。","...a tall, slender figure in a straw hat. …一個戴草帽的高挑的形象。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>slender</b> to describe a situation which exists but only to a very small degree. 微弱的","examples":["The United States held a slender lead. 美國稍微領先。"]}]}]},"southern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在南方的，向南的；南方的；美國南部地區的（Southern）；（風）從南面吹來的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"南方人（Southern）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Southern</b> means in or from the south of a region, state, or country. 南部的","examples":["The Everglades National Park stretches across the southern tip of Florida. 埃弗格萊茲國家公園一直延伸到佛羅里達州南端。"]}]}]},"sunny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陽光充足的，（地方）暖和的；（人，性格）開朗的，陽光的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When it is <b>sunny</b>, the sun is shining brightly. (天) 晴朗的","examples":["The weather was surprisingly warm and sunny. 天氣出奇地暖和晴朗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sunny</b> places are brightly lit by the sun. (地方) 陽光充足的","examples":["Most roses like a sunny position in a fairly fertile soil. 多數玫瑰喜歡土壤肥沃、陽光充足之地。"]}]}]},"strict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"要求嚴格的，嚴厲的；（命令或規則）必須嚴格遵守的；嚴謹的，精確的，嚴密的；恪守教規的，嚴格的；完全的，徹底的，絕對的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strict</b> rule or order is very clear and precise or severe and must always be obeyed completely. 嚴格的","examples":["The officials had issued strict instructions that we were not to get out of the jeep. 這些官員們發出了我們不能從那輛吉普車裡出來的嚴令。","French privacy laws are very strict. 法國的隱私法非常嚴格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a parent or other person in authority is <b>strict</b>, they regard many actions as unacceptable and do not allow them. 嚴厲的","examples":["My parents were very strict. 我的父母曾非常嚴厲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>strict</b> meaning of something, you mean the precise meaning of it. 確切的","examples":["It's not quite peace in the strictest sense of the word, rather the absence of war. 這個詞就其最確切的意義而言不完全是和平，更像是沒有戰爭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>strict</b> to describe someone who never does things that are against their beliefs. 恪守信條的","examples":["Millions of Americans are now strict vegetarians. 數百萬美國人現在都是嚴格的素食者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴格地","examples":["The acceptance of new members is strictly controlled. 接納新成員的工作受到嚴格控制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嚴厲地","examples":["My own mother was brought up very strictly and correctly. 我自己的母親是被非常嚴厲且正確地養大的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"確切地","examples":["Actually, that is not strictly true. 實際上，那並不完全是真的。"]}]}]},"talkative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛說話的，健談的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>talkative</b> talks a lot. 愛說話的","examples":["He suddenly became very talkative, his face slightly flushed, his eyes much brighter. 他突然變得很愛說話，他的臉頰稍微有點紅，他的眼睛明亮多了。"]}]}]},"tasty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"美味的；<非正式> 有趣的；<英，非正式> 性感的，迷人的；善戰的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that food is <b>tasty</b>, you mean that it has a fairly strong and pleasant flavour which makes it good to eat. 味美的","examples":["Try this tasty dish for supper with a crispy salad. 晚餐就著一道鮮脆色拉嚐嚐這道佳餚。"]}]}]},"social":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"社會的；社會地位的，社會階層的；社交的，交際的；好交際的，合群的；群居的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"社交聚會，聯歡會；<英>社會保障（the social）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Social</b> means relating to society or to the way society is organized. 社會的","examples":["...the worst effects of unemployment, low pay, and other social problems. …失業、低工資和其他社會問題造成的最壞影響。","...long-term social change. …長期的社會變革。","...changing social attitudes. …變化中的社會觀念。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Social</b> means relating to the status or rank that someone has in society. 與社會地位有關的","examples":["Higher education is unequally distributed across social classes. 高等教育是不平等分配給各社會各階層的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Social</b> means relating to leisure activities that involve meeting other people. 社交的","examples":["We ought to organize more social events. 我們應該組織更多的社交活動。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在社會上","examples":["Let's face it – drinking is a socially acceptable habit. 咱們來面對這個事實吧–飲酒是一種為社會所接受的習俗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"在社會地位上","examples":["For socially ambitious couples this is a problem. 對在社會地位方面有野心的夫婦來說，這是個問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"在社交方面","examples":["We have known each other socially for a long time. 我們在社交場合相識有很長時間了。"]}]}]},"successful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"成功的，如願以償的；事業有成的，飛黃騰達的；（公司、影片、產品等）利潤豐厚的，非常賺錢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>successful</b> achieves what it was intended to achieve. Someone who is <b>successful</b> achieves what they intended to achieve. 有成效的","examples":["How successful will this new treatment be? 這種新療法將會有多大成效？","I am looking forward to a long and successful partnership with him. 我期待著與他的長期而有成效的合作關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>successful</b> is popular or makes a lot of money. (事物) 成功的","examples":["...the hugely successful movie that brought Robert Redford an Oscar for his directing. …這部使羅伯特·雷德福獲得奧斯卡導演獎的極其成功的影片。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>successful</b> achieves a high position in what they do, for example in business or politics. (人在商業、政治等方面) 成功的","examples":["Women do not necessarily have to imitate men to be successful in business. 女人無須非得效仿男人才能在商界成功。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有成效地","examples":["The doctors have successfully concluded preliminary tests. 醫生們已成功完成了初步化驗。"]}]}]},"teenage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（用於名詞前）十幾歲的，青少年的（指13至19歲）；關於青少年的，面向青少年的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Teenage</b> children are aged between thirteen and nineteen years old. 十幾歲 (指13至19歲) 的","examples":["She looked like any other teenage girl. 她看上去和別的少女一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Teenage</b> is used to describe things such as movies, magazines, bands, or activities that are aimed at or are done by teenage children. 關於青少年的","examples":["...\"Smash Hits,\" a teenage magazine. …《流行金曲》,一本青少年雜誌。"]}]}]},"snowy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多雪的，下雪的；雪白的；白雪覆蓋的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snowy</b> place is covered in snow. A <b>snowy</b> day is a day when a lot of snow has fallen. 積雪覆蓋的; 下雪多的","examples":["...the snowy peaks of the Bighorn Mountains. …比格霍恩山白雪皚皚的群峰。"]}]}]},"terrific":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，了不起的；極大的，驚人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>terrific</b>, you are very pleased with them or very impressed by them. 極好的","examples":["What a terrific idea! 多好的主意啊！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Terrific</b> means very great in amount, degree, or intensity. 巨大的","examples":["All of a sudden there was a terrific bang and a flash of smoke. 忽然發出一聲巨響，還冒出一股煙。"]}]}]},"terrible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"糟糕的，令人極為不快的；極度的，極其嚴重的；劣質的，很差勁的；可怕的，駭人的；生病的，不高興的；危害極大的，造成極大傷害的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>terrible</b> experience or situation is very bad or very unpleasant. 可怕的","examples":["Tens of thousands more suffered terrible injuries in the world's worst industrial disaster. 還有數萬人在這場世界最嚴重的工業災難中受了重傷。","I often have terrible nightmares. 我經常做可怕的惡夢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>terrible</b>, it is very bad or of very poor quality. 糟糕的; 劣質的","examples":["She admits her French is terrible. 她承認自己的法語很糟糕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>terrible</b> to emphasize the great extent or degree of something. (程度) 十足的","examples":["I was a terrible fool, you know. 你知道，我那時是個十足的傻瓜。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可怕地","examples":["My son has suffered terribly. He has lost his best friend. 我兒子遭受了可怕的打擊，失去了最好的朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非常","examples":["I'm terribly sorry to bother you at this hour. 我非常抱歉這個時候來打攪您。"]}]}]},"thirsty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"渴的，口渴的；渴望的，渴求的；（植物或土地）缺水的，乾旱的；（引擎、植物或莊稼）耗油的，需水量大的；<非正式>（活動、天氣或時段）使人口渴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>thirsty</b>, you feel a need to drink something. 口渴的","examples":["Drink whenever you feel thirsty during exercise. 鍛鍊時一感到口渴就喝水。"]}]}]},"ugly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"醜陋的，難看的；（通常因涉及暴力、挑釁行為而）令人厭惡的，邪惡的，惡性的；無禮的；道德敗壞的；可怕的，恐怖的；難聽的，不悅耳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>ugly</b>, you mean that they are very unattractive and unpleasant to look at. 難看的; 醜的","examples":["...an ugly little hat. …一頂醜陋的小帽子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to an event or situation as <b>ugly</b>, you mean that it is very unpleasant, usually because it involves violent or aggressive behaviour. 醜惡的","examples":["There have been some ugly scenes. 出現了一些醜惡的場面。","The confrontation turned ugly. 衝突變得醜惡了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"醜陋","examples":["Dekkeret found the landscape startling in its ugliness. 德克雷特發現那風景難看得令人吃驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"醜惡","examples":["...the ugliness of sexual harassment. …性騷擾的醜惡。"]}]}]},"traditional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傳統的；根據傳統而製造（或使用）的；因襲的，守舊的；（活動）慣例的，經常從事的；典型的；（爵士樂）具20世紀早期風格的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Traditional</b> customs, beliefs, or methods are ones that have existed for a long time without changing. 傳統的","examples":["Traditional teaching methods sometimes only succeeded in putting students off learning. 傳統的教學方法有時只會使學生們厭學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>traditional</b> organization or person prefers older methods and ideas to modern ones. 守舊的","examples":["We're still a traditional school in a lot of ways. 我們在很多方面仍然是一所守舊的學校。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傳統地","examples":["Married women have traditionally been treated as dependent on their husbands. 已婚婦女傳統上被認為是依附於其丈夫的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"守舊地","examples":["He is loathed by some of the more traditionally minded officers. 他被一些思想更為守舊的官員所厭惡。"]}]}]},"upper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"上面的，上層的，較高的；頂部的，上部的；（在機構、體系等中）較高階的，上級的；上游的，北部的；（地質，考古）晚期的，較近期的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞋面，鞋幫；<非正式>興奮劑（尤指安非他明）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>upper</b> to describe something that is above something else. 上面的","examples":["There is a good restaurant on the upper floor. 樓上有一家很好的餐館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>upper</b> to describe the higher part of something. 較高的 (部位)","examples":["...the upper part of the foot. …腳面。","...the muscles of the upper back and chest. …上背部和胸部的肌肉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>the upper hand</b> in a situation, you have an advantage over the other people involved, for example because you have more power or success. 優勢","examples":["The home team was beginning to gain the upper hand. 主隊正開始佔上風。"]}]}]},"used":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用過的，舊的；二手的；習慣於，適應於"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使用，利用；消耗；說，寫，使用（詞語或語言）（use 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>used to</b> be done or <b>used to</b> be the case, it was done regularly in the past or was the case in the past. 過去慣常","examples":["People used to come and visit him every day. 過去人們每天都來看他。","He used to be one of my professors. 他過去是我的一個教授。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>did not use to</b> be done, <b>used to not</b> be done or <b>used not to</b> be done, it was not done in the past. 過去不曾","examples":["Borrowing used to not be recommended. 借東西在過去是不提倡的。","At some point kids start doing things they didn't use to do. They get more independent. 從某時起孩子們開始做他們過去沒做過的事情。他們變得更獨立。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are used to</b> something, you are familiar with it because you have done it or experienced it many times before. 習慣於","examples":["I'm used to having my sleep interrupted. 我習慣了睡覺時被吵醒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>get used to</b> something or someone, you become familiar with it or get to know them, so that you no longer feel that the thing or person is unusual or surprising. 變得習慣於","examples":["This is how we do things here. You'll soon get used to it. 這是我們這裡的做事風格。你很快就會習慣的。","You quickly get used to using the brakes. 你很快會習慣用剎車。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>used</b> object is dirty or spoiled because it has been used, and usually needs to be thrown away or washed. 用過的","examples":["...a used cotton ball stained with makeup. …一個用過的棉花球，沾著化妝品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>used</b> car has already had one or more owners. 二手的","examples":["Would you buy a used car from this man? 你會向這個人買輛二手車嗎？"]}]}]},"thick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"厚的，粗的；有……厚的；（衣服）厚重的，暖和的 ；（字型）粗體的；茂密的，繁茂的；（毛髮）濃密的；（煙、雲、霧等）渾濁的，能見度低的；（液體）稠的，濃的；<非正式> 愚鈍的，笨的；（尤指由於疾病、酗酒而使頭腦）隱痛的，思路不清的；充滿的，瀰漫的；（因為難過等而嗓音）沙啞的，低沉的；（口音）重的，難聽懂的；親密無間的，交情厚的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"在……最激烈時，在……最緊張的時刻（the thick）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"厚地，濃密地；大量地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>thick</b> has a large distance between its two opposite sides. 厚的","examples":["For breakfast I had a thick slice of bread and butter. 早餐我吃了一片厚厚的黃油麵包。","He wore thick glasses. 他戴著厚厚的眼鏡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>thick</b> to talk or ask about how wide or deep something is. 有…厚的","examples":["The folder was two inches thick. 那個資料夾有兩英寸厚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Thick</b> is also a combining form. 用以構成複合詞","examples":["His life was saved by a quarter-inch-thick bullet-proof vest. 他被0.25英寸厚的防彈背心救了一命。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something that consists of several things is <b>thick</b>, it has a large number of them very close together. 濃密的","examples":["She inherited our father's thick, wavy hair. 她繼承了我們父親濃密的捲髮。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>thick with</b> another thing, the first thing is full of or covered with the second. 充滿的","examples":["The air is thick with acrid smoke from the fires. 空氣中充滿了火災產生的刺鼻濃煙。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Thick</b> clothes are made from heavy cloth, so that they will keep you warm in cold weather. (衣服等) 厚的","examples":["In the winter she wears thick socks, boots and gloves. 冬天她穿著厚襪和靴子，還戴著手套。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Thick</b> smoke, fog, or cloud is difficult to see through. (煙、霧或雲) 濃的","examples":["The smoke was bluish-black and thick. 這煙霧呈藍黑色，而且很濃。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Thick</b> liquids are fairly stiff and solid and do not flow easily. (液體) 濃稠的","examples":["It had rained last night, so the garden was thick mud. 昨晚下了雨，所以花園裡全是濃稠的泥漿。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"厚厚地","examples":["Slice the meat thickly. 把肉切成厚片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"濃密地","examples":["I rounded a bend where the trees and brush grew thickly. 我在一個林木茂密的地方繞了個彎。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"厚度","examples":["The size of the fish will determine the thickness of the steaks. 魚的大小決定魚排的厚度。"]}]}]},"usual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"通常的，慣常的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常事（the usual）；<非正式>常喝的飲料（尤指酒）（the usual）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Usual</b> is used to describe what happens or what is done most often in a particular situation. 常見的; 平常的","examples":["It is a neighbourhood beset by all the usual inner-city problems. 這是個受所有常見市中心區問題所困擾的市區。","After lunch there was a little more clearing up to do than usual. 午餐之後有比平常多的清掃工作要做。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Usual</b> is also a noun. 往常的 (飯食、飲料等)","examples":["The stout barman in a bow tie presented himself to take their order. \"Good morning, sir. The usual?\" 那位繫著領結的粗壯的酒吧男招待走過來請他們點菜。“早上好，先生。跟以往一樣？”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>as usual</b> to indicate that you are describing something that normally happens or that is normally the case. 和往常一樣","examples":["As usual there will be the local and regional elections on June the twelfth. 和往常一樣，6月12日將舉行地方及地區選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>as usual</b>, it happens in the way that it normally does, especially when other things have changed. 照常","examples":["Surgery was scheduled, but life went on as usual. 手術定好了時間，而生活照常繼續。"]}]}]},"windy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多風的，風大的；誇誇其談的，空話連篇的；<英>胃內氣脹的；（道路，河流）蜿蜒的，彎彎曲曲的；<英，非正式>（人）緊張的，憂慮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>windy</b>, the wind is blowing a lot. 風大的","examples":["It was windy and Jake felt cold. 風很大，傑克覺得很冷。"]}]}]},"wooden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"木製的；（行為）僵硬的，呆板的；木頭似的，木頭特性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wooden</b> objects are made of wood. 木製的","examples":["...the shop's bare brick walls and faded wooden floorboards. …那家商店光禿禿的磚牆和褪了色的木地板。"]}]}]},"willing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"願意的，樂意的；樂於相助的，積極肯幹的；出於自願的，志願的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"希望，想要（某事發生）；憑意志促使……做某事；立遺囑遺贈（will 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>willing</b> <b>to</b> do something, they are fairly happy about doing it and will do it if they are asked or required to do it. 樂意的","examples":["There are, of course, questions which she will not be willing to answer. 當然，有些問題她不樂意回答。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Willing</b> is used to describe someone who does something fairly enthusiastically and because they want to do it rather than because they are forced to do it. 心甘情願的","examples":["Have the party on a Saturday, when you can get your partner and other willing adults to help. 把聚會安排在某個星期六吧，到時你就可以找你的夥伴以及其他願意相助的人幫忙。"]}]}]},"thin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"薄的，細的；（人或身體部分）瘦的；（毛髮）稀疏的；（液體）稀的，不粘稠的；能見度高的；（空氣）稀薄的；（解釋、觀點、陳述等）站不住腳的，缺乏說服力的；（笑容）勉強的，淡淡的；（聲音）尖細的；（數目或數量）少的，小量的；微弱的，暗淡的；（字型）細體的；（登山）難找到手攀（或腳踏）處的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（摻水等）使稀薄，使變淡；（頭髮）變稀疏；（使）（擁擠的人群、植物、物品等）變稀少，散去；（使）變薄，（使）變稀；給……間苗，間開；（使）變瘦；（高爾夫）打（球的）中上部位"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"薄薄地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>thin</b> is much narrower than it is long. 細的","examples":["A thin cable carries the signal to a computer. 一條細電纜把訊號傳給一臺計算機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person or animal that is <b>thin</b> has no extra fat on their body . (人或動物) 瘦的","examples":["He was a tall, thin man with grey hair that fell in a wild tangle to his shoulders. 他個子瘦高，灰白的頭髮亂蓬蓬地散落在肩上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something such as paper or cloth that is <b>thin</b> is flat and has only a very small distance between its two opposite surfaces. (紙或布等) 薄的","examples":["...a small, blue-bound book printed in fine type on thin paper. …一本紙質輕薄、用細小字型印刷而成的藍皮小書。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Liquids that are <b>thin</b> are weak and watery. (液體) 稀的","examples":["The soup was thin and clear, yet mysteriously rich. 那湯既稀又清，但味道卻出奇地足。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A crowd or audience that is <b>thin</b> does not have many people in it. 人數稀少的","examples":["The crowd, which had been thin for the first half of the race, had now grown considerably. 上半場比賽時觀眾稀稀拉拉的，現在則大大增多了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Thin</b> clothes are made from light cloth and are not warm to wear. (衣服) 薄的","examples":["Her gown was thin, and she shivered, partly from cold. 她的禮服很薄，她渾身發抖，部分是由於寒冷所致。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe an argument, an explanation, or evidence as <b>thin</b>, you mean that it is weak and difficult to believe. (論點、解釋或證據) 難以令人信服的","examples":["The DA was certain she had the right man, but the evidence was thin. 這位地方檢察官確信自己找對了人，但是證據卻難以令人信服。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone's hair is described as <b>thin</b>, they do not have a lot of hair. (頭髮) 稀疏的","examples":["She had pale thin yellow hair she pulled back into a bun. 她的頭髮稀疏、淡黃，往後梳成了一個圓髻。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"薄薄地","examples":["Peel and thinly slice the onion. 給洋蔥剝皮，切成薄片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"稀少地","examples":["The island is thinly populated. 這個島人口稀少。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"難以令人信服地","examples":["Much of the speech was a thinly disguised attack on environmentalists. 演講內容大多是對環保主義者幾乎不加掩飾的攻擊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>thin</b> something or when it <b>thins</b>, it becomes less crowded because people or things have been removed from it. 使變稀疏; 變稀疏","examples":["It would have been better to have thinned the trees over several winters rather than all at one time. 當初要是分幾個冬天來疏剪樹木，會比一次性疏剪要更好些。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thin out</b> means the same as . 使稀疏","examples":["NATO will continue to thin out its forces. 北約將繼續裁軍。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone's patience, for example, <b>is wearing thin</b>, they are beginning to become impatient or angry with someone. (耐心等) 消磨掉","examples":["War has achieved little, and public patience is wearing thin. 戰爭收穫甚微，公眾的耐心日漸消磨。"]}]}]},"wonderful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"絕妙的，令人驚歎的，極好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>wonderful</b>, you think they are extremely good. 極好的","examples":["The cold, misty air felt wonderful on his face. 那涼涼的霧氣使他臉上感覺好極了。","It's wonderful to see you. 見到你好極了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極好地","examples":["It's a system that works wonderfully well. 它是一個執行極好的系統。"]}]}]},"wise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（行為或決定）明智的，高明的；有學問的，精通的；<美，非正式>說話粗魯的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"瞭解，知道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wise</b> person is able to use their experience and knowledge in order to make sensible decisions and judgments. 有智慧的","examples":["She has the air of a wise woman. 她有才女的氣質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wise</b> action or decision is sensible. (行動或決定) 明智的","examples":["It's never wise to withhold evidence. 隱瞞證據絕不明智。","She had made a very wise decision. 她作出了一個非常明智的決定。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"英明地","examples":["The three of us stood around the machine nodding wisely. 我們3個人站在機器周圍，明白地點點頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"明智地","examples":["They've invested their money wisely. 他們明智地把錢做了投資。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"way, manner, fashion, or respect (esp in the phrases <b>any wise, in no wise</b>) 情況","examples":[]}]}]},"whatever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"任何……的事物，無論什麼"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何事物；究竟是什麼；無所謂，什麼都可以； <非正式>名叫某某的東西（用於指稱不知道的東西）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"任何，絲毫（表強調）；<非正式>不管怎樣"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"不管什麼，無論什麼；任何…...的事物，凡是…...的東西"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（表示勉強接受）隨便你怎麼說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whatever</b> to refer to anything or everything of a particular type. 任何事物","examples":["Franklin was free to do pretty much whatever he pleased. 富蘭克林幾乎可以做他想做的任何事情。","When you're older I think you're better equipped mentally to cope with whatever happens. 當你年齡再大一點兒，我想你在心理上就更有能力去應對所發生的任何事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>whatever</b> to say that something is the case in all circumstances. 不管情況怎樣","examples":["We shall love you whatever happens, Diana. 黛安娜，不管發生什麼事我們都會愛你的。","She runs on average about 15 miles a day every day, whatever the circumstances, whatever the weather. 她堅持每天平均跑15英里左右，不論什麼情況，不論什麼天氣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>whatever</b> when you are indicating that you do not know the precise identity, meaning, or value of the thing just mentioned. 不管什麼 (表示不知道所談論事物的確切身份、意義或價值)","examples":["I thought that my upbringing was \"normal,\" whatever that is. 我曾以為我的成長過程是“正常”的，不管“ 正常”是什麼意思。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whatever</b> is also a determiner. 任何","examples":["Whatever doubts he might have had about Ingrid were all over now. 他對英格麗德可能有過的任何疑問現在都煙消雲散了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whatever</b> after a noun group in order to emphasize a negative statement. 任何 (用於名詞片語後，強調否定陳述)","examples":["There is no evidence whatever that competition in broadcasting has ever reduced costs. 沒有任何證據證明廣播行業的競爭曾經使成本降低。"]}]},{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whatever</b> to ask in an emphatic way about something which you are very surprised about. 究竟 (表示對讓自己感動吃驚的事的強調)","examples":["Whatever can you mean? 你究竟是什麼意思？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>or whatever</b> to refer generally to something else of the same kind as the thing or things that you have just mentioned. 諸如此類","examples":["They're always protesting about something or saving the trees or whatever. 他們總是在抗議一些事情，或是在拯救樹木或諸如此類的事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>whatever</b> you <b>do</b> when giving advice or warning someone about something. 不管做什麼 (用於給出建議或警告)","examples":["Whatever you do, don't ask for a pay increase. 你不管做什麼，就是別要求漲工資。"]}]}]},"absent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"缺勤的，缺席的；不存在的，缺乏的；心不在焉的，出神的；不與子女一起住的"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"<美，正式>缺乏，沒有"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"缺席，離開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>absent</b> <b>from</b> a place or situation where they should be or where they usually are, they are not there. 缺席的","examples":["He has been absent from his desk for two weeks. 他已經兩個星期沒來了。","The pictures, too, were absent from the walls. 那些照片也不在那些牆上了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone appears <b>absent</b>, they are not paying attention because they are thinking about something else. 心不在焉的","examples":["\"Nothing,\" Rosie said in an absent way. “沒什麼，”羅茜心不在焉地說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>absent</b> parent does not live with his or her children. 不與孩子同住的","examples":["...absent fathers who fail to pay toward the costs of looking after their children. …未能支付撫養費的不與孩子同住的父親們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"心不在焉地","examples":["He nodded absently. 他心不在焉地點了點頭。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that <b>absent</b> one thing, another thing will happen, you mean that if the first thing does not happen, the second thing will happen. 倘若沒有…","examples":["Absent a solution, people like Sue Godfrey will just keep on fighting. 若沒有個解決方案，像休·戈弗雷這樣的人就會繼續爭鬥。"]}]}]},"baby-sit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"當臨時保姆，替人臨時照看（嬰兒或小孩）；<非正式>代人臨時承擔照料責任（如照看寵物、植物、房屋等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>babysit</b> <b>for</b> someone or <b>babysit</b> their children, you look after their children while they are out. 代人臨時照看 (別人的孩子); 代人臨時照看小孩","examples":["I promised to babysit for Mrs. Plunkett. 我答應了為普倫基特太太臨時照看孩子。","She had been babysitting him and his four-year-old sister. 她曾一直代為臨時照看他和他4歲的妹妹。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"臨時保姆","examples":["It can be difficult to find a good babysitter. 可能難以找到一個好的臨時保姆。"]}]}]},"apply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"申請；塗，敷；施加，實施；應用，運用；踩（剎車）；適用，適合；指稱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>apply</b> <b>for</b> something such as a job or membership of an organization, you write a letter or fill out a form in order to ask formally for it. 申請","examples":["I am continuing to apply for jobs. 我在繼續申請工作。","They may apply to join the organization. 他們可能申請加入該組織。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>apply</b> <b>yourself to</b> something or <b>apply</b> your mind <b>to</b> something, you concentrate hard on doing it or on thinking about it. 將…投入","examples":["Scymanski has applied himself to this task with considerable energy. 賽曼斯基已經花了相當多的精力致力於這項任務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>apply</b> something such as a rule, system, or skill, you use it in a situation or activity. 運用","examples":["The government appears to be applying the same principle. 政府似乎在運用同樣的原則。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A name that <b>is applied</b> <b>to</b> someone or something is used to refer to them. (在…上) 使用","examples":["...a biological term that cannot be applied to a whole culture. …一個不能用於整個培養物的生物學術語。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>apply</b> something <b>to</b> a surface, you put it on or rub it into the surface. 施用","examples":["The right thing would be to apply direct pressure to the wound. 正確的做法會是在傷口上施加直接壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a rule or a remark <b>applies</b> <b>to</b> a person or in a situation, it is relevant to the person or the situation. (對…) 適用","examples":["The convention does not apply to us. 該協定對我們不適用。","The rule applies where a person owns stock in a corporation. 該規定對於在公司裡擁有股份的人適用。"]}]}]},"bbq":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"barbecue 的縮寫：戶外燒烤，野外燒烤，燒烤聚會；燒烤食物（如烤排骨、烤肉等）；燒烤爐，燒烤架；（用於名詞前）燒烤的，燒烤風味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>BBQ</b> is the written abbreviation for . barbecue的縮寫","examples":[]}]}]},"argue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"主張，認為；說服；爭論，爭辯；爭吵；提出質疑；提出理由"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person <b>argues</b> <b>with</b> another, they speak angrily to each other about something that they disagree about. You can also say that two people <b>argue</b>. 爭吵","examples":["The committee is concerned about players' behaviour, especially arguing with referees. 該委員會擔心運動員的表現，尤其擔心他們與裁判爭吵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>argue</b> <b>with</b> someone <b>about</b> something, you discuss it with them, with each of you giving your different opinions. 討論","examples":["He was arguing with the king about the need to maintain the cavalry at full strength. 他在和國王討論保留騎兵全部兵力的必要性。","They are arguing over foreign policy. 他們在討論外交政策。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone not to <b>argue</b> <b>with</b> you, you want them to do or believe what you say without protest or disagreement. 爭辯","examples":["Don't argue with me. 不要和我爭辯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>argue for</b> something, you say why you agree with it, in order to persuade people that it is right. If you <b>argue against</b> something, you say why you disagree with it, in order to persuade people that it is wrong. 陳述理由","examples":["The report argues against tax increases. 該報告陳述理由反對增稅。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>argue</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you state it and give the reasons why you think it is true. 辯論","examples":["His lawyers are arguing that he is unfit to stand trial. 他的律師們在辯稱他不適宜受審。"]}]}]},"arrive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"到達，抵達；送達，寄到；發生，出現，誕生；開始，到來；成功，出名；作出（決定）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or vehicle <b>arrives</b> at a place, they come to it from somewhere else. 到達","examples":["Fresh groups of guests arrived. 新客成批到達了。","...a small group of commuters waiting for their train, which arrived on time. …幾個等候火車準點到達的通勤者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>arrive</b> at a place, you come to it for the first time in order to stay, live, or work there. 初次抵達","examples":["...in the old days before the European settlers arrived in the country. …在歐洲定居者們初次到這個國家之前的古老歲月。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as letter or meal <b>arrives</b>, it is brought or delivered to you. 送達","examples":["Breakfast arrived while he was in the bathroom. 早餐在他在浴室裡時送到了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When something such as a new product or invention <b>arrives</b>, it becomes available. (產品、發明) 問世","examples":["Several long-awaited movies will finally arrive in the stores this month. 幾部期盼已久的影片最終將於本月在各家商店露面。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a particular moment or event <b>arrives</b>, it happens, especially after you have been waiting for it or expecting it. 到來","examples":["The time has arrived when I need to give up smoking. 我需要戒菸的時候到了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>arrive at</b> something such as a decision, you decide something after thinking about it or discussing it. 達成","examples":["...if the jury cannot arrive at a unanimous decision. …如果陪審團不能達成一致判決。"]}]}]},"avoid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"避免，防止；迴避，避開；撤銷，使無效"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>avoid</b> something unpleasant that might happen, you take action in order to prevent it from happening. 避免 (壞事的發生)","examples":["The pilots had to take emergency action to avoid a disaster. 飛行員們不得不採取緊急措施以避免災難的發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>avoid</b> doing something, you choose not to do it, or you put yourself in a situation where you do not have to do it. 避免","examples":["By borrowing from dozens of banks, he managed to avoid giving any of them an overall picture of what he was up to. 透過向幾十家銀行借錢，他得以避免讓任何一家瞭解他要做事情的全貌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>avoid</b> a person or thing, you keep away from them. When talking to someone, if you <b>avoid</b> the subject, you keep the conversation away from a particular topic. 避開","examples":["She eventually had to lock herself in the women's restroom to avoid him. 她最後不得不把自己鎖在女廁所裡避開他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or vehicle <b>avoids</b> someone or something, they change the direction they are moving in, so that they do not hit them. (人或車) 避讓","examples":["The driver had ample time to brake or swerve and avoid the woman. 該司機有足夠的時間剎車或急轉來避讓那女子。"]}]}]},"arrange":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"安排，籌備；整理，佈置，排列；改編；商定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>arrange</b> an event or meeting, you make plans for it to happen. 安排 (活動、會議)","examples":["She arranged an appointment for Friday afternoon at four-fifteen. 她安排了一個星期五下午四點一刻的約會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>arrange</b> with someone <b>to</b> do something, you make plans with them to do it. 安排; 籌劃","examples":["I've arranged to see him on Friday morning. 我已經安排了星期五早上見他。","It was arranged that the party would gather for lunch in Grant Park. 已經安排好這一行人在格蘭特公園聚集吃午餐。","The city had arranged for the National Guard to be brought in. 該市已籌劃調入國民警衛隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>arrange</b> something <b>for</b> someone, you make it possible for them to have it or to do it. 安排好","examples":["I will arrange for someone to take you around. 我會安排好人領你轉轉。","The hotel manager will arrange for a babysitter. 賓館經理會安排一位保姆。","Mr. Dambar had arranged a dinner for the three of them. 丹姆巴爾先生已經為他們3人安排好了一頓晚餐。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>arrange</b> things somewhere, you place them in a particular position, usually in order to make them look attractive or neat. 佈置","examples":["When she has a little spare time she enjoys arranging dried flowers. 她有一點閒暇時間就喜歡插乾花。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a piece of music <b>is arranged</b> <b>by</b> someone, it is changed or adapted so that it is suitable for particular instruments or voices, or for a particular performance. 改編 (樂曲)","examples":["The songs were arranged by another well-known bass player, Ron Carter. 這些歌曲由另一位著名的貝司手羅恩·卡特改編。"]}]}]},"bake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"炎熱，灼熱；烤，烘，焙；炙烤，受曬"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"烤制食品；<美>烤餐會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bake</b>, you spend some time preparing and mixing together ingredients to make bread, cakes, pies, or other food which is cooked in the oven. 烤制 (麵包等食品)","examples":["How did you learn to bake cakes? 你是怎麼學會烤蛋糕的？","I love to bake. 我喜歡烤點心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a cake or bread <b>bakes</b> or when you <b>bake</b> it, it cooks in the oven without any extra liquid or fat. (指蛋糕或麵包) 烘烤","examples":["Bake the cake for 35 to 50 minutes. 把蛋糕烘烤35至50分鐘。","The batter rises as it bakes. 麵糊烘烤時膨脹。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"烘烤","examples":["On a Thursday she used to do all the baking. 她以前每個星期四做所有烘烤的活兒。"]}]}]},"accept":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"接受，收受；同意，贊成；相信，認為……正確；忍受，容忍；吸納，招收；接納；承擔（責任等），承認；承兌，認付（單據等）；不排斥；適配"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> something that you have been offered, you say yes to it or agree to take it. 接受","examples":["Eventually Esteban persuaded her to accept an offer of marriage. 最終埃斯特班說服她接受了求婚。","All those invited to next week's peace conference have accepted. 所有應邀參加下週和平會議的人都已接受了邀請。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> an idea, statement, or fact, you believe that it is true or valid. 相信","examples":["I do not accept that there is any kind of crisis in American science. 我不相信美國科學有任何危機。","I don't think they would accept that view. 我不認為他們會相信那個觀點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> a plan or an intended action, you agree to it and allow it to happen. 接受","examples":["The Council will meet to decide if it should accept his resignation. 委員會將開會來決定是否應該接受他的辭呈。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> an unpleasant fact or situation, you get used to it or recognize that it is necessary or cannot be changed. 容忍","examples":["People will accept suffering that can be shown to lead to a greater good. 人們將會容忍能被證明會帶來更大利益的苦難。","Urban dwellers often accept noise as part of city life. 城市居民常常將噪音作為城市生活的一部分來容忍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person, company, or organization <b>accepts</b> something such as a document, they recognize that it is genuine, correct, or satisfactory and agree to consider it or handle it. 接受","examples":["We took the unusual step of contacting newspapers to advise them not to accept the advertising. 我們採取了聯絡各家報社的非常規做法來勸阻他們不要承接這則廣告。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an organization or person <b>accepts</b> you, you are allowed to join the organization or use the services that are offered. 接納","examples":["All-male groups will not be accepted. 全男性的組合不會被接納。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a person or a group of people <b>accepts</b> you, they begin to be friendly toward you and are happy with who you are or what you do. 接納","examples":["As far as my grandparents were concerned, they've never had a problem accepting me. 至於我的祖父母，接納我對他們來說從來就不是問題。","Many men still have difficulty accepting a woman as a business partner. 很多男性依然難以接受女性作為自己的生意夥伴。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> the responsibility or blame for something, you recognize that you are responsible for it. 承擔 (責任等)","examples":["The company cannot accept responsibility for loss or damage. 該公司不能承擔遺失或損壞的責任。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>accept</b> someone's advice or suggestion, you agree to do what they say. 接受","examples":["The army refused to accept orders from the political leadership. 軍隊拒絕接受政界領導的命令。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If a machine <b>accepts</b> a particular kind of thing, it is designed to take it and deal with it or process it. 接受","examples":["The new parking meters don't accept dollar bills. 這種新型停車計時器不接受美元紙鈔。"]}]}]},"attend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"隨同，陪同；經常去，定期去(學校、教堂等)；伴隨……而至，（作為結果）伴隨；出席，參加；注意，專心；處理，照料；致力於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>attend</b> a meeting or other event, you are present at it. 參加; 出席","examples":["Thousands of people attended the funeral. 數千人參加了葬禮。","The meeting will be attended by finance ministers from many countries. 這次會議將有許多國家的財政部長出席。","The senator was invited but was unable to attend. 參議員受到了邀請，但是未能出席。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>attend</b> an institution such as a school, college, or church, you go there regularly. 上 (學); 去 (教堂)","examples":["They attended college together at the University of Pennsylvania. 他們一起就讀於賓夕法尼亞大學。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>attend</b> <b>to</b> something, you deal with it. If you <b>attend</b> <b>to</b> someone who is hurt or injured, you care for them. 處理; 照料","examples":["He took a short leave of absence to attend to personal business. 他休了一個短假去處理私事。"]}]}]},"arm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手臂，上肢；武器，軍備；扶手；袖子；職能部門；臂（狀部件）；盾徽，紋章；狹長港灣；臂力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"武裝，備戰；提供，配備；使（炸彈等）隨時爆炸，準備發射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>arms</b> are the two long parts of your body that are attached to your shoulders and that have your hands at the end. 手臂","examples":["She stretched her arms out. 她伸開了雙臂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>arm</b> of a chair is the part on which you rest your arm when you are sitting down. (椅子的) 扶手","examples":["Mack gripped the arms of the chair. 麥克抓緊了那把椅子的一對扶手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> an object is a long thin part of it that sticks out from the main part. (物體的) 臂狀物","examples":["...the lever arm of the machine. …該機器的槓桿臂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> land or water is a long thin area of it that is joined to a broader area. (陸地、水域的) 狹長區域","examples":["...a small area of woodland between two arms of a small stream. …一條小溪的兩條支流之間的一小塊林地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> an organization is a section of it that operates in a particular country or that deals with a particular activity. 部門; 分支機構","examples":["The agency is the central research and development arm of the Department of Defense. 該機構是國防部的核心研究與開發部門。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>arm</b> of a piece of clothing is the part of it that covers your arm. 袖子","examples":["...coats that were short in the arms. …袖子短的幾件大衣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Arms</b> are weapons, especially bombs and guns. 武器","examples":["Soldiers searched their house for illegal arms. 士兵們為找非法武器搜了他們的家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people are walking <b>arm in arm</b>, they are walking together with their arms linked. 臂挽臂地","examples":["He walked from the court arm in arm with his wife. 他和他妻子臂挽著臂從法院走來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you hold something <b>at arm's length</b>, you hold it away from your body with your arm straight. 以一臂之距","examples":["He struck a match, and held it at arm's length. 他劃了根火柴，然後伸長胳膊舉著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> someone <b>at arm's length</b>, you avoid becoming too friendly or involved with them. 同某人保持一定距離","examples":["She had always kept the family at arm's length. 她一直和家人保持一定距離。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you welcome some action or change <b>with open arms</b>, you are very pleased about it. If you welcome a person <b>with open arms</b>, you are very pleased about their arrival. 張開雙臂 (歡迎)","examples":["They would no doubt welcome the action with open arms. 他們毫無疑問會張開雙臂歡迎這項舉措。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> someone's <b>arm</b>, you persuade them to do something. 說服某人","examples":["She had twisted his arm to get him to invite her. 她已說服了他，讓他邀請她。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A person's right to <b>bear arms</b> is their right to own and use guns, as a means of defence. 持有武器","examples":["...a country where the right to bear arms is enshrined in the constitution. …把武器持有權載入憲法的一個國家。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If one group or country <b>takes up arms</b> <b>against</b> another, they prepare to attack and fight them. 拿起武器","examples":["They threatened to take up arms against the government if their demands were not met. 他們威脅說，如果要求得不到滿足就拿起武器對抗政府。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If people are <b>up in arms</b> <b>about</b> something, they are very angry about it and are protesting strongly against it. 憤怒抗議","examples":["Patient advocates are up in arms over the possible closure of the psychiatric hospital. 病人的支持者們憤怒抗議該精神病院的可能關閉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>arm</b> someone <b>with</b> a weapon, you provide them with a weapon. 武裝","examples":["She'd been so terrified that she had armed herself with a loaded rifle. 她是如此害怕，以至於用一支上了膛的步槍把自己武裝了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>arm</b> someone <b>with</b> something that will be useful in a particular situation, you provide them with it. 用…裝備","examples":["She thought that if she armed herself with all the knowledge she could gather she could handle anything. 她曾以為，如果她用其所能蒐集到的所有知識充實自己，她就能處理任何事。"]}]}]},"clothe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……穿衣；為……提供衣服；賦予（某人某品質）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clothe</b> someone means to provide them with clothes to wear. 穿衣","examples":["She was on her own with two kids to feed and clothe. 她自己一個人要招呼兩個孩子的衣食。"]}]}]},"beg":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"乞求，懇求；乞討，行乞；（狗）作乞求狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>beg</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you ask them very anxiously or eagerly to do it. 懇求","examples":["I begged him to come back to New York with me. 我請求他和我一起回紐約。","We are not going to beg for help anymore. 我們將不再請求幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who is poor <b>is begging</b>, they are asking people to give them food or money. 行乞","examples":["I was surrounded by people begging for food. 我被一群討飯的人圍住了。","...homeless people begging on the streets. …沿街乞討的無家可歸者。","She was living alone, begging food from neighbours. 她一個人生活，從鄰居那兒討些吃的。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a dog) to sit up with forepaws raised expectantly (狗)端坐將前爪舉起懇求","examples":[]}]}]},"borrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"借，借入；（向……）借貸；採用，借用；（演算減法時）借（位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> something that belongs to someone else, you take it or use it for a period of time, usually with their permission. 借","examples":["Can I borrow a pen please? 我可以借支筆嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> money <b>from</b> someone or <b>from</b> a bank, they give it to you and you agree to pay it back at some time in the future. 借 (錢)","examples":["Morgan borrowed $5,000 from his father to form the company 20 years ago. 摩根20年前向他父親借了$5000來建立這家公司。","It's so expensive to borrow from finance companies. 向金融公司借款費用真夠高的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> a book <b>from</b> a library, you take it away for a fixed period of time. 借 (書)","examples":["I couldn't afford to buy any, so I borrowed them from the library. 我一本也買不起，所以從圖書館借了這些。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> something such as a word or an idea from another language or from another person's work, you use it in your own language or work. 借用 (思想、詞等)","examples":["I borrowed his words for my book's title. 我借用他的話作為我的書名。"]}]}]},"bind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"捆綁，系；包紮；使緊密聯絡；迫使，使負有義務（或責任）；（使）凝結，（使）粘合；裝訂；給……鑲邊，給……滾邊；（量詞）適用於（給定的變數）；（規則，語法條件）決定（共指名詞片語）之間的關係；（食物，藥品）使便秘"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窘境，困境；令人不快的事情；法律約束；連結線；蔓，藤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>binds</b> people <b>together</b>, it makes them feel as if they are all part of the same group or have something in common. 使結合","examples":["It is the memory and threat of persecution that binds them together. 是受迫害的記憶和威脅將他們緊緊聯絡在一起。","...the social and political ties that bind the U.S. to Britain. …使美國與英國緊密聯絡在一起的社會與政治紐帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are bound</b> by something such as a rule, agreement, or restriction, you are forced or required to act in a certain way. 約束","examples":["All pharmacists are bound by the society's rules of confidentiality. 所有藥劑師都受到保密性這一社會規則的約束。","The authorities will be legally bound to arrest any suspects. 當局將依法逮捕任何可疑人員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bind</b> something or someone, you tie rope, string, tape, or other material around them so that they are held firmly. 捆綁","examples":["Bind the ends of the cord together with thread. 把細繩的兩端用線系在一起。","...the red tape which was used to bind the files. …曾用來捆綁檔案的紅色帶子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a book <b>is bound</b>, the pages are joined together and the cover is put on. 裝訂","examples":["Each volume is bound in bright-coloured cloth. 每一冊都用顏色鮮亮的布料裝訂。","Their business came from a few big publishers, all of whose books they bound. 他們的生意來自幾家大出版社，這些出版社所有的書都由其裝訂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受約束的","examples":["The world of advertising is obviously less bound by convention than the world of banking. 與銀行業相比，廣告業顯然較少受常規的約束。"]}]}]},"choose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"選擇，挑選；情願，決定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>choose</b> someone or something <b>from</b> several people or things that are available, you decide which person or thing you want to have. 挑選; 選擇","examples":["They will be able to choose their own leaders in democratic elections. 在民主選舉中他們將可以選出他們自己的領導人。","There are several patchwork cushions to choose from. 有幾種拼布工藝墊子可供選擇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>choose</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it because you want to or because you feel that it is right. 情願; 覺得應該 (做某事)","examples":["They knew that discrimination was going on, but chose to ignore it. 他們知道歧視仍然存在，但他們情願不去理會。","You have the right to remain silent if you choose. 如果你願意，你有權保持沉默。"]}]}]},"compare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"比較，對比；把……比作；（與……）相比；構成（形容詞或副詞）的比較級和最高階"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"比較"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>compare</b> things, you consider them and discover the differences or similarities between them. 比較","examples":["Compare the two illustrations in Figure 60. 比較一下圖60中的兩個圖示。","Managers analyse their company's data and compare it with data on their competitors. 經理們分析他們公司的資料並與其競爭者的資料進行比較。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>compare</b> one person or thing <b>to</b> another, you say that they are like the other person or thing. 認為…像…","examples":["Some commentators compared his work to that of James Joyce. 一些評論員認為他的作品像詹姆士·喬伊斯的作品。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something does not <b>compare with</b> something else, you mean that it is much worse. 比得上","examples":["The flowers here do not compare with those at home. 這兒的花比不上家裡的花。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>compares</b> favourably <b>with</b> another, it is better than the other thing. If it <b>compares</b> unfavourably, it is worse than the other thing. (與…) 比起來 (好、差)","examples":["Our road safety record compares favourably with that of other countries. 我們的道路安全紀錄比其他國家的好。"]}]}]},"collect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聚集，聚積；收集，採集；收藏；領取，接走；募捐，募集；使鎮定，使集中思想；贏得，獲得；收，收取；<古>推斷，推論；<非正式>和……互撞，和……發生衝突"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某些基督教儀式上的）短禱文；<非正式>打贏的賭，贏錢的賭注"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"對方付通話費的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"對方付通話費地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>collect</b> a number of things, you bring them together from several places or from several people. 採集; 收集","examples":["Two young girls were collecting firewood. 兩位年輕女孩在採集柴火。","Elizabeth had been collecting snails for a school project. 伊麗莎白為一個學校的專案在收集蝸牛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>collect</b> things, such as stamps or books, as a hobby, you get a large number of them over a period of time because they interest you. 收集 (郵票或書等)","examples":["I used to collect stamps. 我過去曾經集郵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a substance <b>collects</b> somewhere, or if something <b>collects</b> it, it keeps arriving over a period of time and is held in that place or thing. 積聚","examples":["Methane gas does collect in the mines around here. 沼氣確實積聚在這周圍的礦井中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>collects</b> light, energy, or heat, it attracts it. 聚集 (光、能量或熱量等)","examples":["Like a telescope, it has a curved mirror to collect the sunlight. 和望遠鏡一樣，它有一個曲面鏡來聚集太陽光。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>collect</b> <b>for</b> a charity or <b>for</b> a present for someone, you ask people to give you money for it. 募捐","examples":["Are you collecting for charity? 你是在為慈善募捐嗎？","The organization has collected $2.5 million for the relief effort. 該組織已經募集到了250萬美元用於救濟活動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>collect</b> someone or something, you go and get them from the place where they are waiting for you or have been left for you. 領走","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"收集","examples":["...hobbies like stamp collecting and fishing. …諸如集郵和釣魚之類的愛好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a short Church prayer generally preceding the lesson or epistle in Communion and other services 短禱文","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"adj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of telephone calls) on a reverse-charge basis (打電話)由對方付費","examples":[]}]}]},"complain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"訴說 （病痛）；<文>悲嘆，悲鳴；（構造，機械裝置）（因拉力或壓力）呻吟，咯吱作響；抱怨，投訴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>complain</b> <b>about</b> a situation, you say that you are not satisfied with it. 抱怨","examples":["Miners have complained bitterly that the government did not fulfil their promises. 礦工們已憤憤地抱怨政府沒有兌現他們的承諾。","The couple complained about the high cost of visiting Europe. 這對夫婦抱怨了遊覽歐洲的高昂花費。","I shouldn't complain, I've got a good job to go back to. 我不該抱怨，我已有可回去乾的一份好工作。","\"I wish someone would do something about it,\" he complained. “我希望有人能對此做點什麼，”他抱怨道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>complain of</b> pain or illness, you say that you are feeling pain or feeling ill. 訴說 (病痛)","examples":["He complained of a headache. 他說他頭疼。"]}]}]},"confirm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"確定，確認；證實，證明；批准，認可；使堅定，加強；給（某人）施堅信禮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>confirms</b> what you believe, suspect, or fear, it shows that it is definitely true. 證實 (某人的觀點、猜疑、擔心的事)","examples":["X-rays have confirmed that he has not broken any bones. X光片已經證實他沒有骨折。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>confirm</b> something that has been stated or suggested, you say that it is true because you know about it. 證實 (陳述或建議的事物)","examples":["The spokesman confirmed that the area was now in rebel hands. 該發言人證實該地區現在處於反叛者的控制之中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>confirm</b> an arrangement or appointment, you say that it is definite, usually in a letter or on the telephone. (常指透過信件或電話) 確認 (安排、預約)","examples":["You make the reservation, and I'll confirm it in writing. 你先預定，我再以書面形式確認。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is confirmed</b>, they are formally accepted as a member of a Christian church during a ceremony in which they say they believe what the church teaches. 給…施堅信禮","examples":["He was confirmed as a member of the Methodist Church. 他受了堅信禮成為衛理公會的一員。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>confirms</b> you <b>in</b> your decision, belief, or opinion, it makes you think that you are definitely right. 使…堅信 (其決定、信念、觀點的正確性)","examples":["It has confirmed me in my decision not to become a nun. 這已讓我堅信我不當修女的決定是正確的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>confirms</b> you <b>as</b> something, it shows that you definitely deserve a name, role, or position. 證明 (某人是當之無愧的…)","examples":["Her new role could confirm her as one of our leading actors. 她的新角色可以證明她是當之無愧的我們最好的演員之一。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"證實","examples":["They took her resignation as confirmation of their suspicions. 他們認為她的辭職證實了他們的猜疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"確認","examples":["She glanced over at James for confirmation. 她瞟了詹姆斯一眼尋求確認。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"確準","examples":["Travel arrangements are subject to confirmation by the head office. 旅行安排需經總公司確準。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"施堅信禮","examples":["...when I was being prepared for Confirmation. …當我為堅信禮作準備的時候。"]}]}]},"complete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全的，徹底的；全部的，完整的；完成的，結束的；技能全面的，技術嫻熟的；向前傳球成功的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使完整，使完美；填寫（表格）；完成，結束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>complete</b> to emphasize that something is as great in extent, degree, or amount as it possibly can be. 完全的","examples":["The house is a complete mess. 這房子實在太亂了。","The rebels had taken complete control. 叛亂者已經取得了完全的控制。","The resignation came as a complete surprise. 該辭職來得十分意外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>complete</b> to emphasize that you are referring to the whole of something and not just part of it. 整個的","examples":["A complete apartment complex was burned to the ground. 整座公寓大樓被燒成平地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>complete</b>, it contains all the parts that it should contain. 完整的","examples":["The list may not be complete. 這份清單可能不完整。","...a complete dinner service. …一整套餐具。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>complete</b> works of a writer are all their books or poems published together in one book or as a set of books. 全部的 (作品)","examples":["...the Complete Works of William Shakespeare. …威廉·莎士比亞全集。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something is <b>complete</b>, it has been finished. 完成了的","examples":["The work of restoring the farmhouse is complete. 修復該農舍的工作完成了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"完全地","examples":["Dozens of homes had been completely destroyed. 數十家房屋已被完全毀壞了。","Make sure that you defrost it completely. 確保將其徹底除霜。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>complete</b> a set or group means to provide the last item that is needed to make it a full set or group. 使齊全","examples":["Children don't complete their set of 20 baby teeth until they are two to three years old. 孩子到兩三歲時才長齊20顆乳牙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>complete</b> something, you finish doing, making, or producing it. 完成","examples":["Peter Mayle has just completed his first novel. 彼得·梅爾剛完成他的第一本小說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>complete</b> something, you do all of it. 完成","examples":["She completed her degree in two years. 她在兩年內修完了學位。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>complete</b> a form or questionnaire, you write the answers or information asked for in it. 填寫 (表格、問卷)","examples":["Simply complete part 1 of the application. 只填寫該申請表的第1部分即可。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"完成","examples":["The project is nearing completion. 該專案快完成了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing comes <b>complete with</b> another, it has that thing as an extra or additional part. 配有","examples":["The diary comes complete with a gold ballpoint pen. 該日記本還配有一支金圓珠筆。"]}]}]},"bear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"手持，攜帶；（車，船）運輸，運送；寫有，刻有；以（姓名，頭銜）相稱；見證，作證；承擔，擔負（責任）；經得起；承受，容忍；生育（孩子）；（樹，植物）結（果實），長出（花）；拐彎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"熊；粗暴無禮的人，沒教養的人；體格笨重的男人，行動遲緩的男人；（股票）賣空者，做空頭者；麻煩事，棘手之事；<非正式>“北極熊”（俄國的外號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bear</b> something somewhere, you carry it there or take it there. 運送","examples":["They bore the oblong hardwood box into the kitchen and put it on the table. 他們把那個長方形的硬木箱抬進了廚房，放在了餐桌上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bear</b> something such as a weapon, you hold it or carry it with you. 攜帶","examples":["...the constitutional right to bear arms. …攜帶武器的憲法權。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>bears</b> the weight of something else, it supports the weight of that thing. 承受; 支撐","examples":["The ice was not thick enough to bear the weight of marching men. 冰的厚度不足以支撐行軍隊伍的重量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>bears</b> a particular mark or characteristic, it has that mark or characteristic. 帶有 (標記或特徵)","examples":["The houses bear the marks of bullet holes and the streets are practically deserted. 房屋帶有子彈的痕跡，街道幾乎是被廢棄了。","...notepaper bearing the presidential seal. …蓋有總統印章的信箋。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>bear</b> an unpleasant experience, you accept it because you are unable to do anything about it. 忍受","examples":["They will have to bear the misery of living in constant fear of war. 他們將不得不忍受在沒完沒了的戰爭恐懼中生活的痛苦。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you can't <b>bear</b> someone or something, you dislike them very much. 容忍","examples":["I can't bear people who make judgements and label me. 我受不了那些對我評頭論足、亂貼標籤的人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When a woman <b>bears</b> a child, she gives birth to him or her. 生 (孩子)","examples":["Emma bore a son called Karl. 埃瑪生了個兒子，取名卡爾。","She bore him a daughter, Susanna. 她給他生了個女兒，叫蘇珊娜。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone <b>bears</b> the cost of something, they pay for it. 承擔(費用)","examples":["Patients should not have to bear the costs of their own treatment. 病人們不該需要承擔他們自己的醫療費。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>bear</b> the responsibility for something, you accept responsibility for it. 承擔 (責任)","examples":["If a woman makes a decision to have a child alone, she should bear that responsibility alone. 如果一名女子決定獨自養育小孩，她就必須獨自承擔這一責任。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If one thing <b>bears</b> no resemblance or no relationship to another thing, they are not at all similar. 具有 (相似之處或關係)","examples":["Their daily menus bore no resemblance whatsoever to what they were actually fed. 他們的日常選單與他們每天實際吃的東西完全不一樣。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When a plant or tree <b>bears</b> flowers, fruit, or leaves, it produces them. 開 (花); 結 (果); 長 (枝葉)","examples":["As the plants grow and start to bear fruit they will need a lot of water. 隨著植物的生長及開始結果，它們將需要大量的水分。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something such as a bank account or an investment <b>bears</b> interest, interest is paid on it. 產生 (利息)","examples":["The eight-year bond will bear annual interest of 10.5%. 這份8年期的債券將產生10.5%的年息。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bear</b> left or <b>bear</b> right when you are driving or walking along, you turn and continue in that direction. 向 (左或右) 轉","examples":["Travelling north on 309 to Centre Valley, bear right at the fork onto Route 378 North. 經309道向北去中央谷時，在378道北的岔口向右拐。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bear</b> is a large, strong wild animal with thick fur and sharp claws. 熊","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a teddy bear 泰迪熊","examples":[]}]}]},"cancel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"取消（計劃好的事情）；終止，廢除；蓋銷，登出；（因素，情況）抵消，對消"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"取消，撤銷；郵票登出章，戳記；經修正的版面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cancel</b> something that has been arranged, you stop it from happening. If you <b>cancel</b> an order for goods or services, you tell the person or organization supplying them that you no longer wish to receive them. 取消","examples":["The Russian foreign minister yesterday cancelled his visit to Washington. 俄外交部長昨天取消了對華盛頓的訪問。","Many trains have been cancelled and a limited service is operating on other lines. 許多列車都被取消了，少數班次在其他路線執行。","The customer called to cancel. 顧客打電話來取消了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>cancels</b> a document, an insurance policy, or a debt, they officially declare that it is no longer valid or no longer legally exists. 廢止; 廢除","examples":["He intends to try to leave the country, in spite of a government order cancelling his passport. 他不顧廢止他的護照的政府命令，仍打算要離開這個國家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>cancel</b> a stamp or a cheque means to mark it to show that it has already been used and cannot be used again. 蓋銷; 使作廢","examples":["The new device can also cancel the cheque after the transaction is complete. 這種新裝置還能在交易結束後將支票登出。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"取消","examples":["Outbursts of violence forced the cancellation of Haiti's first free elections in 1987. 暴力事件的爆發迫使海地取消了1987年的首次自由選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"廢止; 廢除","examples":["...a march by groups calling for cancellation of Third World debt. …要求解除第三世界的債務的一場集體遊行。"]}]}]},"consider":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"考慮，斟酌；認為，視為；體貼，顧及；細看，端詳；探討，討論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>consider</b> a person or thing <b>to</b> be something, you have the opinion that this is what they are. 認為","examples":["We don't consider our customers to be mere consumers; we consider them to be our friends. 我們沒有視我們的顧客為純粹的消費者；我們視他們為我們的朋友。","I had always considered myself a strong, competent woman. 我曾一直以為自己是個堅強能幹的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>consider</b> something, you think about it carefully. 仔細考慮 (某事物)","examples":["The administration continues to consider ways to resolve the situation. 政府繼續仔細考慮解決這種情況的辦法。","You do have to consider the feelings of those around you. 你真的得仔細考慮你身邊那些人的感受。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are considering</b> doing something, you intend to do it, but have not yet made a final decision whether to do it. 考慮 (做某事)","examples":["I had seriously considered telling the story from the point of view of the wives. 我曾認真考慮過從妻子們的角度來講述這個故事。"]}]}]},"create":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"創造，建立；設計，創作；造成，引起；授予，冊封；<英，非正式>大驚小怪，抱怨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>create</b> something means to cause it to happen or exist. 創造; 引起","examples":["We set business free to create more jobs. 我們讓企業自由以創造更多的就業機會。","She could create a fight out of anything. 她可以為了任何事製造爭鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>creates</b> a new product or process, they invent it or design it. 創造; 設計","examples":["It is really great for a radio producer to create a show like this. 一個電臺節目製作人能設計出這樣的節目真是太了不起了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"創造","examples":["These businesses stimulate the creation of local jobs. 這些企業刺激了當地就業機會的產生。"]}]}]},"crow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烏鴉；（公雞或像公雞的）啼叫聲；克勞人（分佈在美國西部的美洲土著居民）；<非正式>婦人，醜婦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"歡叫，高興地說；自鳴得意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crow</b> is a large black bird which makes a loud, harsh noise. 烏鴉","examples":["The crows roosted in Fonsa's Tower. 那些烏鴉棲息在風薩塔裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a cock <b>crows</b>, it makes a loud sound, often early in the morning. (公雞的報曉) 啼叫","examples":["The cock crows and the dawn chorus begins. 公雞叫了,眾鳥的清晨鳴唱隨之開始了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a person <b>crows</b>, they boast of their superiority. 自鳴得意","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>eats crow</b>, they admit that they have been wrong and apologize, especially in situations where this is humiliating or embarrassing for them. 被迫認錯","examples":["He wanted to make his critics eat crow. 他想迫使批評他的人們認錯。"]}]}]},"decorate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝飾，裝點；粉刷，裝修；授予（某人）勳章"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>decorate</b> something, you make it more attractive by adding things to it. 裝飾","examples":["He decorated his room with pictures of all his favourite sports figures. 他用他所喜愛的所有運動員的照片裝飾自己的房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>decorate</b> a room or the inside of a building, you put new paint or wallpaper on the walls and ceiling, and paint the woodwork. 裝修","examples":["When they came to decorate the rear bedroom, it was Jemma who had the final say. 他們開始裝修後臥室時，說了算的人是傑馬。","The boys are planning to decorate when they get the time. 男孩們正計劃在他們有時間的時候裝修。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"裝修","examples":["I did a lot of the decorating myself. 我自己幹了很多裝修的活兒。"]}]}]},"contain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包含，容納；遏制，防止……蔓延；抑制（感情）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a box, bag, room, or place <b>contains</b> things, those things are inside it. 有…在裡面","examples":["The envelope contained a Christmas card. 該信封裡裝有一張聖誕賀卡。","The first two floors of the building contain retail space and a restaurant. 該大樓最底下兩層有零售空間和一家餐館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a substance <b>contains</b> something, that thing is a part of it. 含有","examples":["Watermelon contains vitamins and also potassium. 西瓜含有維生素也有鉀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If writing, speech, or film <b>contains</b> particular information, ideas, or images, it includes them. (文章、演講、電影) 包含 (某些資訊、觀點、影象等)","examples":["This sheet contained a list of problems a patient might like to raise with the doctor. 這張紙寫有一個病人可能想向醫生提出的問題清單。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a group or organization <b>contains</b> a certain number of people, those are the people that are in it. (團體、組織等) 包括 (某數量的成員)","examples":["The committee contains 11 Democrats and nine Republicans. 該委員會包括11名民主黨人和9名共和黨人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>contain</b> something, you control it and prevent it from spreading or increasing. 控制; 阻止","examples":["More than a hundred firemen are still trying to contain the fire at the plant. 一百多名消防隊員仍在努力控制工廠火勢。"]}]}]},"deny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"否認；拒絕承認；拒絕給予"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>deny</b> something, you state that it is not true. 否認","examples":["She denied both accusations. 她否認對她的兩項指控。","The government has denied that the authorities have uncovered a plot to assassinate the president. 政府否認當局已經發現一個暗殺總統的陰謀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>deny</b> someone something that they need or want, you refuse to let them have it. 拒絕給予","examples":["Two federal courts ruled that the military cannot deny prisoners access to lawyers. 兩聯邦法院裁定軍方不能拒絕讓囚犯聘請律師。"]}]}]},"detect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"查明，察覺；測出，檢測，識別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>detect</b> something means to find it or discover that it is present somewhere by using equipment or making an investigation. 探測","examples":["...a sensitive piece of equipment used to detect radiation. …一臺探測輻射的敏感儀器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>detect</b> something, you notice it or sense it, even though it is not very obvious. 察覺","examples":["Arnold could detect a certain sadness in the old man's face. 阿諾德能察覺到老人臉上的某種悲傷。"]}]}]},"deliver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投遞，運送；履行，兌現；交付，移交；發表，宣佈；接生，分娩；解救，拯救；投擲，擊打；（法官或法庭）宣佈（判決）；拉（選票）；發行，釋出（計算機程式）；處理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deliver</b> something somewhere, you take it there. 遞送","examples":["The Canadians plan to deliver more food to southern Somalia. 加拿大人計劃向索馬利亞南部運送更多的食物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>deliver</b> something that you have promised to do, make, or produce, you do, make, or produce it. 實現; 履行","examples":["They have yet to show that they can really deliver working technologies. 他們仍需證明他們確實能夠實現可用的技術。","The question is, can he deliver? 問題是他能履行嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>deliver</b> a lecture or speech, you give it in public. 發表","examples":["The president will deliver a speech about schools. 校長將發表關於學校的演講。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone <b>delivers</b> a baby, they help the woman who is giving birth to the baby. 給 (產婦) 接生","examples":["Although we'd planned to have our baby at home, we never expected to deliver her ourselves! 儘管我們是打算在家生孩子，可我們從未想過要自己給她接生!"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>delivers</b> a blow to someone else, they hit them. 給予 (打擊)","examples":["Those blows to the head could have been delivered by a woman. 頭上挨的那些打可能是一個女人所為。"]}]}]},"describe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"描述，形容；做……運動，形成……形狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>describe</b> a person, object, event, or situation, you say what they are like or what happened. 描述","examples":["We asked her to describe what kind of things she did in her spare time. 我們請她描述她在閒暇時做些什麼。","She read a poem by Carver which describes their life together. 她讀了一首卡弗描寫他們在一起生活的詩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person <b>describes</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a particular thing, he or she believes that they are that thing and says so. 講成; 稱作","examples":["He described it as an extraordinarily tangled and complicated tale. 他把它講成了一個格外錯綜複雜的故事。","Even his closest allies describe him as forceful, aggressive, and determined. 甚至他最親密的同盟者們都說他強勢、好鬥且堅決。"]}]}]},"disagree":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"有分歧，意見不合；不一致；不適宜，使……不舒服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disagree</b> <b>with</b> someone or <b>disagree</b> <b>with</b> what they say, you do not accept that what they say is true or correct. You can also say that two people <b>disagree</b>. 不同意; 有分歧","examples":["You must continue to see them no matter how much you may disagree with them. 不管你與他們有多大分歧，都必須一如既往地去看他們。","They can communicate even when they strongly disagree. 他們即使是在有較大分歧時也能相互交流。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disagree</b> <b>with</b> a particular action or proposal, you disapprove of it and believe that it is wrong. 不贊成","examples":["I respect the president but I disagree with his decision. 我尊重總統，但我不贊成他的決定。"]}]}]},"depend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"取決於；依賴，依靠；相信，指望；那得看情況；（語法上）從屬（depend on/upon）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>depends</b> <b>on</b> another, you mean that the first thing will be affected or determined by the second. 根據…而定","examples":["The cooking time needed depends on the size of the potato. 烹飪時間長短取決於土豆的大小。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>depend</b> <b>on</b> someone or something, you need them in order to be able to survive physically, financially, or emotionally. 依靠","examples":["He depended on his writing for his income. 他靠寫作謀生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you can <b>depend</b> <b>on</b> a person, organization, or law, you know that they will support you or help you when you need them. 信任","examples":["\"You can depend on me,\" Cross assured him. “你可以信任我，”克羅斯向他保證。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>depend</b> in expressions such as <b>it depends</b> to indicate that you cannot give a clear answer to a question because the answer will be affected or determined by other factors. 視情況而定","examples":["\"But how long can you stay in the house?\"—\"I don't know. It depends.\" “但你能在這屋裡待多久？” — “不知道，這要看情況而定。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>depending on</b> when you are saying that something varies according to the circumstances mentioned. 根據…而定","examples":["I tend to have a different answer, depending on the family. 我傾向根據不同的家庭給出一個不同的答案。"]}]}]},"develop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成長，發育，發展；逐漸形成，逐漸養成；開發，研製；出現，產生；修建，開發土地；提高，加強；患病；闡釋，展開；沖洗，使底片顯影；（修改旋律、和聲或節奏以）展開（音樂主題）；（棋）出子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>develops</b>, it grows or changes over a period of time and usually becomes more advanced, complete, or severe. 發展","examples":["It's hard to say at this stage how the market will develop. 在現階段很難說市場會如何發展。","These clashes could develop into open warfare. 這些衝突可能會發展成公開的戰爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a problem or difficulty <b>develops</b>, it begins to occur. 產生","examples":["The space agency says a problem has developed with an experiment aboard the space shuttle. 航天局說在太空梭上做的一項實驗出了問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a country <b>develops</b>, you mean that it changes from being a poor agricultural country to being a rich industrial country. 發達","examples":["All countries, it was predicted, would develop and develop fast. 據預測，所有的國家都會發達起來，並且很迅速。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"發展的; 發育的","examples":["Their bodies were well developed and super fit. 他們的身體發育良好，極其健康。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"發達的","examples":["...the countries that have suffered the most from the absence of more developed financial systems. …因缺乏更發達的金融體系而受損最嚴重的國家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"已開發的","examples":["Developed land was to grow from 5.3% to 6.9%. 已開發的土地將從5.3%增長到6.9%。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"增長的; 增進的","examples":["...a highly developed instinct for self-preservation. …一種高度增長了的自衛本能。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>develop</b> a business or industry, or if it <b>develops</b>, it becomes bigger and more successful. 擴充套件","examples":["An amateur hatmaker has won a scholarship to pursue her dreams of developing her own business. 一位業餘制帽匠贏得了一筆獎學金，來實現她擴充套件自己企業的夢想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>develop</b> land or property means to make it more profitable, by building houses or factories or by improving the existing buildings. 開發 (房地產)","examples":["Local entrepreneurs developed fashionable restaurants, bars and discotheques in the area. 當地的企業家在這個地區開辦了時尚的餐館、酒吧和迪斯科舞廳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>develop</b> a habit, reputation, or belief, you start to have it and it then becomes stronger or more noticeable. 獲得; 形成","examples":["Mr. Robinson has developed the reputation of a ruthless cost-cutter. 魯賓遜先生已經有了毫不留情的成本削減者的名聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>develop</b> a skill, quality, or relationship, or if it <b>develops</b>, it becomes better or stronger. 增長; 增進","examples":["Now you have a good opportunity to develop a greater understanding of each other. 現在你們有了一個好機會來增進彼此的瞭解。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a piece of equipment <b>develops</b> a fault, it starts to have the fault. 發生","examples":["The aircraft made an unscheduled landing at Logan after developing an electrical fault. 飛機發生電氣故障後，臨時在洛根著陸。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>develops</b> a new product, they design it and produce it. 開發 (產品)","examples":["He claims that several countries have developed nuclear weapons secretly. 他聲稱幾個國家已經秘密開發了核武器。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>develop</b> an idea, theory, story, or theme, or if it <b>develops</b>, it gradually becomes more detailed, advanced, or complex. 展開","examples":["I would like to thank them for allowing me to develop their original idea. 我想感謝他們允許我展開他們最初的觀點。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>develop</b> photographs means to make negatives or prints from a photographic film. 沖洗","examples":["...after developing one roll of film. …沖洗了一卷膠捲後。"]}]}]},"disappear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"消失，不見；失蹤，丟失；不復存在，滅絕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>disappears</b>, you mean that you can no longer see them, usually because you or they have changed position. 消失","examples":["The black car drove away from them and disappeared. 黑色的小汽車駛離了他們便消失了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>disappears</b>, they go away or are taken away somewhere where nobody can find them. 失蹤","examples":["...a Japanese woman who disappeared thirteen years ago. …一位13年前失蹤的日本婦女。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>disappears</b>, it stops existing or happening. 滅絕","examples":["The immediate threat of the past has disappeared and the security situation in Europe has significantly improved. 過去的直接威脅不復存在了，歐洲的安全狀況有重大改善。"]}]}]},"discuss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"討論，辯論；詳述，論述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>discuss</b> something, they talk about it, often in order to reach a decision. 討論","examples":["I will be discussing the situation with colleagues tomorrow. 我將於明天和同事們討論這個情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>discuss</b> something, you write or talk about it in detail. 詳述","examples":["I will discuss the role of diet in cancer prevention in Chapter 7. 我將在第7章詳述飲食在癌症預防中的作用。"]}]}]},"earn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"賺得，掙錢；盈（利），生（利）；贏得，博得"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>earn</b> money, you receive money in return for work that you do. 掙 (錢)","examples":["What a lovely way to earn a living. 一個多好的謀生方式啊！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>earns</b> money, it produces money as profit or interest. 贏 (利)","examples":["...a bank account that earns little or no interest. …一個很少或不生利息的銀行賬戶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>earn</b> something such as praise, you get it because you deserve it. 贏得","examples":["Companies must earn a reputation for honesty. 公司必須贏得誠信。"]}]}]},"dull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"枯燥無聊的；無精打采的；不明亮的；（聲音）不清晰的；陰沉的；不明顯的，隱隱的；鈍的；遲鈍的，愚笨的；蕭條的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"減輕，緩解；使遲鈍；（使）變模糊，變暗淡；（使刀或刀片等）變鈍；（興趣、痛苦等）減少"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>dull</b>, you mean they are not interesting or exciting. 沉悶的; 乏味的","examples":["I felt she found me boring and dull. 我覺得她認為我令人厭煩而又乏味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>dull</b> is not very lively or energetic. 無精打采的; 無生氣的","examples":["The body's natural rhythms mean we all feel dull and sleepy between 1 and 3 pm. 身體的自然節律造成我們在下午1點至3點間都會感到無精打采、昏昏欲睡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dull</b> colour or light is not bright. 黯淡的","examples":["The stamp was a dark, dull blue colour with a heavy black postmark. 這枚郵票是模糊的暗藍色的，上面蓋著一個粗黑色的郵戳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say the weather is <b>dull</b> when it is very cloudy. (天氣) 陰沉的","examples":["It's always dull and raining. 天老是陰沉沉的，下著雨。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Dull</b> sounds are not very clear or loud. 低沉而模糊的","examples":["The coffin closed with a dull thud. 隨著一聲沉悶地撞擊聲，棺材合上了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Dull</b> feelings are weak and not intense. 微弱的","examples":["The pain, usually a dull ache, gets worse with exercise. 這種疼痛，通常是隱隱作痛，運動時會加劇。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沉悶; 乏味","examples":["They enjoy anything that breaks the dullness of their routine life. 他們喜愛能打破他們規律生活的沉悶的任何事情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無精打采地; 了無生氣地","examples":["His giant face had a rough growth of stubble, his eyes looked dully ahead. 他寬大的臉龐上長著粗硬的鬍子茬，眼睛黯然無神地看著前方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"黯淡地","examples":["The street lamps gleamed dully through the night's mist. 街燈透過夜的薄霧隱約地閃現。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"低沉而模糊地","examples":["He heard his heart thump dully but more quickly. 他聽見他的心跳低沉但卻更急速。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"微弱地","examples":["His arm throbbed dully. 他的手臂微微地顫動。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>dulls</b> or if it <b>is dulled</b>, it becomes less intense, bright, or lively. 使…變弱/變暗/變得無生氣; 變弱/變暗/變得無生氣","examples":["Her eyes dulled and she gazed blankly. 她雙目變得黯然無神，茫然凝神。"]}]}]},"encourage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鼓勵，激勵；鼓動，慫恿；刺激，促進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>encourage</b> someone, you give them confidence, for example by letting them know that what they are doing is good and telling them that they should continue to do it. 鼓勵","examples":["When things aren't going well, he encourages me, telling me not to give up. 當事情不順利的時候，他鼓勵我，告訴我不要放棄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is encouraged by</b> something that happens, it gives them hope or confidence. 鼓舞","examples":["Investors were encouraged by the news. 投資者被這條訊息所鼓舞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>encourage</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you try to persuade them to do it, for example, by telling them that it would be a pleasant thing to do, or by trying to make it easier for them to do it. You can also <b>encourage</b> an activity. 激勵","examples":["Herbie Hancock was encouraged by his family to learn music at a young age. 赫比·漢考克小時候受到家人鼓勵去學音樂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>encourages</b> a particular activity or state, it causes it to happen or increase. 促使.","examples":["...a natural substance that encourages cell growth. …促使細胞生長的一種天然物質。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受到鼓舞的","examples":["We were very encouraged after over 17,000 pictures were submitted. 我們深受鼓舞，17000多張照片已被提交了。"]}]}]},"elect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"選舉；選擇（做）；（上帝）挑選（某人）（而使其靈魂永遠得救）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"候任的；選中的，卓越的；蒙上帝挑選（而得救）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上帝的選民（the elect）；特權階層"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>elect</b> someone, they choose that person to represent them, by voting for them. 選舉","examples":["The people of the Philippines have voted to elect a new president. 菲律賓人民已經投票選舉出一位新總統。","The University of Washington elected him dean in 1956. 華盛頓大學在1956年選他為院長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>elect</b> <b>to</b> do something, you choose to do it. 選擇","examples":["Those electing to smoke will be seated at the rear. 選擇抽菸的人將坐在後面。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elect</b> is added after words such as \"president\" or \"governor\" to indicate that a person has been elected to the post but has not officially started to carry out the duties involved. 當選而尚未就職的","examples":["...the date when the president-elect takes office. …總統當選人的就職日。"]}]}]},"enjoy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"享受，欣賞，喜愛；過得愉快，玩得開心（enjoy oneself）；享有，擁有；<美，非正式>請盡情享用； <美，非正式>請盡情享用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>enjoy</b> something, you find pleasure and satisfaction in doing it or experiencing it. 享受…的樂趣","examples":["Ross had always enjoyed the company of women. 羅斯一直都很享受女人的陪伴。","He was a guy who enjoyed life to the full. 他是個盡情享受生活樂趣的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>enjoy</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do something that you like doing or you take pleasure in the situation that you are in. (自) 得其樂","examples":["I am really enjoying myself at the moment. 我此刻很是自得其樂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>enjoy</b> something such as a right, benefit, or privilege, you have it. 享有","examples":["The average German will enjoy 40 days' paid holiday this year. 德國人今年平均將享有40天帶薪假期。"]}]}]},"excite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使興奮，使激動；引起，激起；使（身體或身體系統某部份）活動，刺激……的活動；使產生性慾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>excites</b> you, it makes you feel very happy, eager, or enthusiastic. 使…激動; 使…興奮","examples":["I only take on work that excites me, even if it means turning down lots of money. 我只承接讓我感興趣的工作，即使這意味著損失很多錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>excites</b> a particular feeling, emotion, or reaction in someone, it causes them to experience it. 激起","examples":["Daniel's early exposure to motor racing did not excite his interest. 丹尼爾早期對賽車運動的接觸並沒有激起他的興趣。"]}]}]},"exist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"存在，實際上有；持續存在，生存"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>exists</b>, it is present in the world as a real thing. 存在","examples":["He thought that if he couldn't see something, it didn't exist. 他認為如果他看不見某種東西，它就不存在。","Research opportunities exist in a wide range of areas. 研究機會存在於廣泛的領域中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>exist</b> means to live, especially under difficult conditions or with very little food or money. (尤指在困境中) 生存","examples":["I was barely existing. 我幾乎活不下去了。","Some people exist on melons or coconuts for weeks at a time. 有些人一度數週靠各種瓜與椰子生存。"]}]}]},"forgive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"原諒，寬恕；免除，取消（債務）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>forgive</b> someone who has done something bad or wrong, you stop being angry with them and no longer want to punish them. 原諒","examples":["Hopefully Jane will understand and forgive you, if she really loves you. 如果簡真的愛你，希望她會理解並原諒你。","Irene forgave Terry for stealing her money. 艾琳原諒了特麗偷了她的錢。","He could forgive Petal anything if the children were safe. 只要孩子們安然無恙他什麼都可以原諒佩特爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Forgive</b> is used in polite expressions and apologies like \"<b>forgive me</b>\" and \"<b>forgive my ignorance</b>\" when you are saying or doing something that might seem rude, silly, or complicated. 請原諒","examples":["Forgive me, I don't mean to insult you. 請原諒我，我不是有意侮辱你。","I do hope you'll forgive me but I've got to leave. 我真的希望你能原諒我，不過我得走了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone could <b>be forgiven for</b> doing something, you mean that they were wrong or mistaken, but not seriously, because many people would have done the same thing in those circumstances. 諒解","examples":["Looking at the figures, you could be forgiven for thinking the recession is already over. 看著這些數字，你認為經濟衰退已經結束是情有可原的。"]}]}]},"explain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解釋，說明；說明（……的）原因，解釋（……的）理由"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>explain</b> something, you give details about it or describe it so that it can be understood. 解釋 (意思)","examples":["Not every judge, however, has the ability to explain the law in simple terms. 然而，並非每個法官都能用淺易的話來解釋法律。","Don't sign anything until your lawyer has explained the contract to you. 在你的律師向你解釋該合同之前什麼也別籤。","Professor Griffiths explained how the drug appears to work. 格里菲斯教授解釋了該藥似乎是怎樣起作用的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>explain</b>, or <b>explain</b> something that has happened, you give people reasons for it, especially in an attempt to justify it. 解釋 (原因)","examples":["\"Let me explain, sir.\"—\"Don't tell me about it. I don't want to know.\" “讓我來解釋，先生。”—“別跟我說那事。我不想知道。”","Before she ran away, she left a note explaining her actions. 逃走之前，她留下了張便條為她的行為作了解釋。","Explain why you didn't telephone. 解釋一下你為什麼不打電話。"]}]}]},"expect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"期待；預計；要求，指望；認為；懷孕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>expect</b> something <b>to</b> happen, you believe that it will happen. 預料","examples":["...a workman who expects to lose his job in the next few weeks. …一個預料會在接下來幾周裡失業的工人。","The talks are expected to continue until tomorrow. 會談預料將持續到明天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are expecting</b> something or someone, you believe that they will be delivered to you or come to you soon, often because this has been arranged earlier. (常指因已安排而) 預期","examples":["I wasn't expecting a visitor. 我沒有預期會有訪客。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>expect</b> something, or <b>expect</b> a person <b>to</b> do something, you believe that it is your right to have that thing, or the person's duty to do it for you. 期待","examples":["He wasn't expecting our hospitality. 他沒有期待我們的熱情款待。","I do expect to have some time to myself in the evenings. 我真期待晚上能有點兒自己的時間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone not to <b>expect</b> something, you mean that the thing is unlikely to happen as they have planned or imagined, and they should not hope that it will. 指望","examples":["Don't expect an instant cure. 別指望會有立竿見影的療效。","You cannot expect to like all the people you will work with. 你不能指望喜歡所有和你一起工作的人。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a woman <b>is expecting</b> a baby, or that she <b>is expecting</b>, you mean that she is pregnant. 懷上; 懷孕","examples":["She was expecting another baby. 她懷上又一個孩子了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>I expect</b>\" to suggest that a statement is probably correct, or a natural consequence of the present situation, although you have no definite knowledge. 我想","examples":["I expect you can guess what follows. 我想你能猜出下面會發生什麼。","I expect you're tired. 我想你是累了。"]}]}]},"govern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"統治，管理；控制，影響；（語法）支配；可用來裁定（某案例）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>govern</b> a place such as a country, or its people, means to be officially in charge of the place, and to have responsibility for making laws, managing the economy, and controlling public services. 統治","examples":["They go to the polls on Friday to choose the people they want to govern their country. 他們週五去投票站選出他們希望來治理國家的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation or activity <b>is governed</b> <b>by</b> a particular factor, rule, or force, it is controlled by that factor, rule, or force. 控制","examples":["Marine insurance is governed by a strict series of rules and regulations. 海上保險受一系列嚴格的規章條例所制約。"]}]}]},"greet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"歡迎，迎接；對……作出反應；映入眼簾，撲鼻而來；<蘇格蘭>痛哭，哭泣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>greet</b> someone, you say \"Hello\" or shake hands with them. 向…問好; 迎接","examples":["She liked to be home to greet Steve when he came in from school. 當史蒂夫從學校回來時，她喜歡在家迎接他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is greeted</b> in a particular way, people react to it in that way. 對…作出反應","examples":["His research was greeted with scepticism by advocates for children, who thought it was based on faulty data. 他的研究遭到兒童權益擁護者們的懷疑，他們認為那是基於錯誤資料得出的。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to weep; lament 哭泣","examples":[]}]}]},"frighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使驚嚇，使驚恐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>frightens</b> you, they cause you to suddenly feel afraid, anxious, or nervous. 使驚恐","examples":["He knew that Soli was trying to frighten him, so he smiled to hide his fear. 他知道索利想嚇唬他，因此微笑著掩飾自己的恐懼。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>frightens the life out of</b> you, <b>frightens the wits out of</b> you, or <b>frightens</b> you <b>out of your wits</b>, it causes you to feel suddenly afraid or gives you a very unpleasant shock. 使嚇得魂不附體","examples":["Fairground rides are intended to frighten the life out of you. 露天遊樂場的飛車就是要把你們嚇得魂不附體。"]}]}]},"gather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.&vi.","zh":"聚集，召集；收集，採集；認為，推斷；增加（速度、力量等）；給……打褶；收緊，拉近"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>gather</b> somewhere, or if someone <b>gathers</b> people somewhere, they come together in a group. 聚集","examples":["In the evenings, we gathered around the fireplace and talked. 晚上，我們聚在壁爐旁聊天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>gather</b> things, you collect them together so that you can use them. 收集","examples":["I suggest we gather enough firewood to last the night. 我建議我們撿拾足夠的木柴來度過這個夜晚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>gather</b> information or evidence, you collect it, especially over a period of time and after a lot of hard work. 蒐集","examples":["...a private detective using a hidden tape recorder to gather information. …一名用一部暗藏的磁帶錄音機來蒐集資訊的私家偵探。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>gathers</b> speed, momentum, or force, it gradually becomes faster or more powerful. 逐漸增加","examples":["Demands for his dismissal have gathered momentum in recent weeks. 要求把他免職的呼聲最近幾周越來越高。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>gather</b> something such as your strength, courage, or thoughts, you make an effort to prepare yourself to do something. 積聚","examples":["You must gather your strength for the journey. 你必須為此次行程打起精神來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>gather</b> in expressions such as \"<b>I gather</b>\" and \"<b>as far as I can gather</b>\" to introduce information that you have found out, especially when you have found it out in an indirect way. 猜想 (用於引出間接得到的資訊)","examples":["I gather his report is highly critical of the trial judge. 我猜想他的報告毫不留情地批判了庭審法官。","\"He speaks English,\" she said to Graham. \"I gathered that.\" “他說英語，”她對格雷厄姆說。“我料到了。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gather up</b> means the same as . 收集","examples":["When Steinberg had gathered up his papers, he went out. 斯坦伯格收好檔案後，走了出去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gather up</b> means the same as . 積聚","examples":["She was gathering up her courage to approach him when he called to her. 他喊她的時候，她正鼓起勇氣去接近他。"]}]}]},"blind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"失明的，盲的；未察覺的，視而不見的；未加思考的，莫名的（形容感情強烈）；（拐角）看不見的，隱蔽的；無窗的，無門的；（行動）未掌握一定資訊的；<英，非正式>絲毫的，一丁點兒的；盲飛的；（植物）無芽的，無頂生花的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變瞎，使失明；使眼花，使目眩；矇蔽，使無辨別力"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窗簾，（尤指）捲簾；<美>（狩獵時的）埋伏處，伏擊處；藉口，幌子"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"看不清地；失去理智地；盲目地，無準備地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>blind</b> is unable to see because their eyes are damaged. 失明的","examples":["I started helping him run the business when he went blind. 他失明以後，我就開始幫他打理生意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>blind</b> <b>with</b> something such as tears or a bright light, you are unable to see for a short time because of the tears or light. 因 (眼淚或強光) 而暫時看不見的","examples":["Her mother groped for the back of the chair, her eyes blind with tears. 她媽媽摸索著椅背，她的眼睛被眼淚遮住了視線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>blind to</b> a fact or a situation, you mean that they ignore it or are unaware of it, although you think that they should take notice of it or be aware of it. 視而不見的; 沒有覺察到的","examples":["David's good looks and impeccable manners had always made her blind to his faults. 大衛俊朗的外表和完美的風度總是令她對他的缺點視而不見。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe someone's beliefs or actions as <b>blind</b> when you think that they seem to take no notice of important facts or behave in an unreasonable way. 盲目的","examples":["...her blind faith in the wisdom of the church. …她對教會箴言的盲目信仰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The blind</b> are people who are blind. 盲人","examples":["He was a teacher of the blind. 他過去是位教盲人的老師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"失明","examples":["Early diagnosis and treatment can usually prevent blindness. 早期診斷和治療通常可以防止失明。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"忽視","examples":["...blindness in government policy to the very existence of the unemployed. …政府政策中對失業人員的存在這一事實的忽視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>blind</b> is a roll of cloth or paper which you can pull down over a window as a covering. 窗簾; 百葉窗簾","examples":["Pulling the blinds up, she let some of the bright sunlight in. 她拉起窗簾，讓一些明媚的陽光照進來。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>blinds</b> you, it makes you unable to see, either for a short time or permanently. 使看不見; 使失明","examples":["The sun hit the windshield, momentarily blinding him. 陽光射在擋風玻璃上，使他一時看不見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>blinds</b> you <b>to</b> the real situation, it prevents you from realizing that it exists or from understanding it properly. 使覺察不到; 使理解不當","examples":["He never allowed his love of Australia to blind him to his countrymen's faults. 他從來不因自己對澳大利亞的熱愛而無視同胞的過錯。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"暫時看不見地","examples":["Lettie groped blindly for the glass. 萊蒂瞎子似地摸索著找杯子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is turning a blind eye</b> <b>to</b> something bad or illegal that is happening, you mean that you think they are pretending not to notice that it is happening so that they will not have to do anything about it. 視而不見","examples":["Teachers are turning a blind eye to pupils smoking at school, a report reveals today. 今天的一篇報道稱，教師對學生在校抽菸視而不見。"]}]}]},"ignore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"佯裝未見，不理睬；忽視，對……不予理會；<法律>（因證據不足）駁回（訴訟）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ignore</b> someone or something, you pay no attention to them. 不理睬","examples":["She said her husband ignored her. 她說她丈夫對她置之不理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that an argument or theory <b>ignores</b> an important aspect of a situation, you are criticizing it because it fails to consider that aspect or to take it into account. (某論斷或理論) 忽視","examples":["Such arguments ignore the question of where ultimate responsibility lay. 此類爭論忽視了最終責任何在的問題。"]}]}]},"hide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……藏起來，隱藏；躲藏，躲避；遮住，遮擋；掩蓋，隱瞞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（可觀察鳥獸行動的）隱匿處，埋伏處；獸皮；<非正式>（困境中的）生命，人身安全"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hide</b> something or someone, you put them in a place where they cannot easily be seen or found. 把…藏起來","examples":["He hid the bicycle in the hawthorn hedge. 他把腳踏車藏進了山楂樹樹叢裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hide</b> or if you <b>hide</b> <b>yourself</b>, you go somewhere where you cannot easily be seen or found. 躲藏","examples":["At their approach the little boy scurried and hid. 當他們走近時，那個小男孩急忙跑開躲了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hide</b> your face, you press your face against something or cover your face with something, so that people cannot see it. 捂住; 把 (臉) 埋在","examples":["She hid her face under the collar of his jacket and started to cry. 她把臉埋在他的外套領子下哭了起來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>hide</b> what you feel or know, you keep it a secret, so that no one knows about it. 掩飾","examples":["Lee tried to hide his excitement. 李努力掩飾內心的激動。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>hides</b> an object, it covers it and prevents it from being seen. 遮蓋","examples":["The man's heavy moustache hid his upper lip completely. 那位男士濃密的八字鬍完全遮住了他的上嘴唇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"to flog 出售","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hide</b> is the skin of a large animal such as a cow, horse, or elephant, which can be used for making leather. 獸皮","examples":["...the process of tanning animal hides. …鞣製獸皮的過程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a place of concealment, usually disguised to appear as part of the natural environment, used by hunters, birdwatchers, etc 隱蔽處; 藏身處 (US and Canadian equivalent blind)","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an obsolete Brit unit of land measure, varying in magnitude from about 60 to 120 acres (英國，舊)海得; 土地面積單位，約合60至120英畝","examples":[]}]}]},"include":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包含；把……列為一部分，把……算入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>includes</b> another thing, it has the other thing as one of its parts. 包括","examples":["The trip has been extended to include a few other events. 行程已經延長以包括其他幾項活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is included</b> <b>in</b> a large group, system, or area, they become a part of it or are considered a part of it. 把…列為一部分","examples":["I had worked hard to be included in a project like this. 為了成為這樣的專案的一分子，我過去一直埋頭苦幹。"]}]}]},"humble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"謙虛的，謙卑的；（級別或地位）低下的，卑微的；簡陋的，沒有特別之處的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使謙卑，使感到自慚；（輕易）擊敗（強敵）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>humble</b> person is not proud and does not believe that they are better than other people. 謙卑的; 謙遜的","examples":["He gave a great performance, but he was very humble. 他的表演很精彩，但他卻很謙遜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People with low social status are sometimes described as <b>humble</b>. (社會地位) 低下的","examples":["Spyros Latsis started his career as a humble fisherman in the Aegean. 斯派羅斯·拉齊斯最初的職業是愛琴海的一名地位低微的漁夫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>humble</b> place or thing is ordinary and not special in any way. 普通的","examples":["There are restaurants, both humble and expensive, that specialize in noodles. 既有普通的也有昂貴的專營麵條的餐館。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"People use <b>humble</b> in a phrase such as <b>in my humble opinion</b> as a polite way of emphasizing what they think, even though they do not feel humble about it. 愚拙的 (用以自謙地表達想法)","examples":["It is, in my humble opinion, perhaps the best steak restaurant in the city. 以我之拙見，它也許是該市最好的牛排館。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"使羞辱的","examples":["Giving up an addiction is a humbling experience. 戒掉一種嗜好是一次令自尊心受挫的經歷。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"謙卑地; 謙遜地","examples":["\"I'm a lucky man, undeservedly lucky,\" he said humbly. “我是個幸運的人，不該這麼幸運，”他謙虛地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"愚拙地 (用以自謙地表達想法)","examples":["So may I humbly suggest we all do something next time. 那麼我可否愚拙地提議下次我們大家都做點什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>eat humble pie</b>, you speak or behave in a way which tells people that you admit you were wrong about something. 賠禮道歉","examples":["Anson was forced to eat humble pie and publicly apologize to her. 安森被迫認錯並公開向她道歉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>humble</b> someone who is more important or powerful than you, you defeat them easily. 輕易擊敗 (重要或強大對手)","examples":["Honda won fame in the 1980s as the little car company that humbled the industry giants. 20世紀80年代，本田作為一家小型汽車公司因一舉擊垮行業巨頭而聲名鵲起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>humbles</b> you, they make you realize that you are not as important or good as you thought you were. 使感到慚愧","examples":["Ted's words humbled me. 特德的一席話使我自感慚愧。"]}]}]},"improve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"康復，健康好轉；超過，勝過；提高……的價值；改善，變得更好"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>improves</b> or if you <b>improve</b> it, it gets better. 改進","examples":["Within a month, both the texture and condition of your hair should improve. 不出一個月，你頭髮的質地和狀況應該都會改善。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a skill you have <b>improves</b> or you <b>improve</b> a skill, you get better at it. 提高","examples":["Their French has improved enormously. 他們的法語水平提高了很多。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>improve</b> after an illness or an injury, your health gets better or you get stronger. 康復","examples":["He had improved so much the doctor had cut his dosage. 他康復了很多，醫生減少了他的用藥量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>improve</b> <b>on</b> a previous achievement of your own or of someone else, you achieve a better standard or result. 提高","examples":["We need to improve on our performance against Nabisco. 我們需根據納貝斯克公司標準來提高我們的業績。"]}]}]},"imagine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"想象，設想；料想，認為；誤以為，胡亂猜想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>imagine</b> something, you think about it and your mind forms a picture or idea of it. 想像","examples":["He could not imagine a more peaceful scene. 他想像不出比這更幽靜的場景。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>imagine</b> that something is the case, you think that it is the case. 猜想","examples":["I imagine you're referring to Jean-Paul Sartre. 我猜你指的是吉恩-保爾·薩特。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>imagine</b> something, you think that you have seen, heard, or experienced that thing, although actually you have not. 幻想","examples":["Looking back on it now, I realized that I must have imagined the whole thing. 現在回想起來，我意識到這整個事情一定是我幻想出來的。"]}]}]},"indicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"表明，標示；象徵，暗示；間接提及，示意；指示，指出；<英>（用燈光或手臂）打行車轉向訊號；有必要，被建議"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>indicates</b> another, the first thing shows that the second is true or exists. 表明","examples":["A survey of retired people has indicated that most are independent and enjoying life. 一項對退休人員的調查表明，他們中的大部分人生活自立而愉快。","Our vote today indicates a change in United States policy. 我們今天的投票表明了美國政策的變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>indicate</b> an opinion, an intention, or a fact, you mention it in an indirect way. 暗示","examples":["Mr. Rivers has indicated that he may resign. 裡弗斯先生已經暗示他可能要辭職。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>indicate</b> something to someone, you show them where it is, especially by pointing to it. 指示","examples":["He indicated a chair. \"Sit down.\" 他指著一把椅子說，“坐下。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>indicates</b> something else, it is a sign of that thing. 象徵; 代表","examples":["Dreams can help indicate your true feelings. 夢能代表你的真實情感。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a technical instrument <b>indicates</b> something, it shows a measurement or reading. (儀器等) 指示","examples":["...an instrument used to indicate wind direction. …一臺用於指示風向的儀器。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When drivers <b>indicate</b>, they make lights flash on one side of their vehicle to show that they are going to turn in that direction. (車輛打轉向燈) 指示轉向","examples":[]}]}]},"hang":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懸掛，吊；（使）掛在牆上；垂下，垂落；懸浮；絞死；貼，糊（牆紙）；安裝（門）；（決定）未做出；逗留，徘徊；投曲線球失敗；（尤指駕車時）拐彎；（使）宕機"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"懸掛方式；下垂，低垂；（畫展中畫作的）陳列，佈局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>hangs</b> in a high place or position, or if you <b>hang</b> it there, it is attached there so it does not touch the ground. 懸掛","examples":["Notices painted on sheets hang at every entrance. 寫在紙上的通告懸掛在每個入口處。","...small hanging lanterns. …幾盞小吊燈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a wall <b>is hung with</b> pictures or other objects, they are attached to it. 懸掛著 (畫等)","examples":["The walls were hung with huge modern paintings. 牆上掛著一些巨幅現代油畫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is hanged</b> or if they <b>hang</b>, they are killed, usually as a punishment, by having a rope tied around their neck and the support taken away from under their feet. 絞死; 吊死","examples":["The five were expected to be hanged at 7 a.m. on Tuesday. 這5個人將在星期二上午7:00被處以絞刑。","He hanged himself two hours after arriving at a mental hospital. 他到達精神病院兩小時後上吊自殺了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hang up</b> means the same as . 懸掛","examples":["I found his jacket, which was hanging up in the hallway. 我找到了他的夾克，它就掛在門廳裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a piece of clothing or fabric <b>hangs</b> in a particular way or position, that is how it is worn or arranged. (衣服或織物) 披垂","examples":["...a ragged fur coat that hung down to her calves. …一件垂到她的小腿的破舊皮大衣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>hangs</b> loose or <b>hangs</b> open, it is partly fixed in position, but is not firmly held, supported, or controlled, often in such a way that it moves freely. 垂下","examples":["...her long golden hair which hung loose about her shoulders. …她那鬆散著披在肩頭的金色長髮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as someone's breath or smoke <b>hangs</b> in the air, it remains there without appearing to move or change position. 懸浮","examples":["His breath was hanging in the air before him. 他撥出的水汽懸浮在他面前的空氣中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a possibility <b>hangs over</b> you, it worries you and makes your life unpleasant or difficult because you think it might happen. 使...憂慮","examples":["A constant threat of unemployment hangs over thousands of university researchers. 持續的失業威脅使數千名大學研究人員感到憂慮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get the hang of</b> something such as a skill or activity, you begin to understand or realize how to do it. 掌握…的竅門","examples":["It's a bit tricky at first till you get the hang of it. 它在一開始當你還沒掌握它的竅門的時候有些棘手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>hang in there</b> or to <b>hang on in there</b>, you are encouraging them to keep trying to do something and not to give up even though it might be difficult. 堅持下去","examples":["Hang in there and you never know what is achievable. 堅持下去，你永遠無法知道會有什麼樣的收穫。"]}]}]},"invent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發明，創造；編造，虛構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>invent</b> something such as a machine or process, you are the first person to think of it or make it. 發明","examples":["He invented the first electric clock. 他發明了第一個電動鍾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>invent</b> a story or excuse, you try to make other people believe that it is true when in fact it is not. 虛構","examples":["I stood still, trying to invent a plausible excuse. 我靜靜地站著，努力想編出一個聽上去可信的藉口。"]}]}]},"insist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"堅決要求，執意堅持；堅稱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>insist</b> <b>that</b> something should be done, you say so very firmly and refuse to give in about it. If you <b>insist</b> <b>on</b> something, you say firmly that it must be done or provided. 堅持認為; 執意要求","examples":["My family insisted that I should not give in, but stay and fight. 我家人堅持認為我不應該屈服，而應該留下來鬥爭。","She insisted on being present at all the interviews. 她堅決要求出席所有的採訪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>insist</b> that something is the case, you say so very firmly and refuse to say otherwise, even though other people do not believe you. 堅持說","examples":["The president insisted that he was acting out of compassion, not political opportunism. 總統堅持說他這麼做是出於同情而不是政治投機。","\"It's not that difficult,\" she insists. “事情並沒有像想的那麼難，”她堅持說。","He insisted on his innocence. 他堅持說自己是清白的。"]}]}]},"introduce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"介紹，引見；使初次瞭解，使嘗試；為（電視或廣播節目）做開場白，主持；實施，推行；首次引入（某物），使傳入；使開始，創始；將（法案）提交討論；將……放進，添入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>introduce</b> something means to cause it to enter a place or exist in a system for the first time. 引進","examples":["MGM introduced a new system for hiring writers. 米高梅公司引進了一項新的制度來僱人寫作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>introduce</b> one person <b>to</b> another, or you <b>introduce</b> two people, you tell them each other's names, so that they can get to know each other. If you <b>introduce</b> <b>yourself</b> to someone, you tell them your name. 介紹","examples":["Tim, may I introduce you to my uncle's secretary, Mary Waller? 蒂姆，我可以把你介紹給我叔叔的秘書瑪麗·沃勒嗎？","We haven't been introduced. My name is Nero Wolfe. 我們還沒有被介紹到。我叫尼羅·沃爾夫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>introduce</b> someone <b>to</b> something, you cause them to learn about it or experience it for the first time. 使初次接觸","examples":["He introduced us to the delights of natural food. 他使我們第一次享受到了品嚐天然食品的樂趣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The person who <b>introduces</b> a television or radio programme speaks at the beginning of it, and often between the different items in it, in order to explain what the programme or the items are about. 為 (電視或廣播節目) 作開場白; 主持","examples":["...chat shows introduced by women. …由女性主持的訪談節目。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"引進","examples":["What he is better remembered for is the introduction of the moving assembly-line in Detroit in 1913. 他更加令人銘記在心的是曾在1913年將流動生產線引入底特律。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"介紹","examples":["With considerable shyness, Elaine performed the introductions. 伊萊恩十分害羞地做了介紹。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"初次接觸","examples":["His introduction to fieldwork was a series of expeditions. 他初次參加的實地考察工作是一系列的探險活動。"]}]}]},"invite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"邀請，約請；徵求，請求；引起，招致"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>請柬，請帖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>invite</b> someone to something such as a party or a meal, you ask them to come to it. 邀請","examples":["She invited him to her 26th birthday party in New Jersey. 她邀請了他參加她在新澤西舉辦的26歲生日聚會。","Barron invited her to accompany him to the races. 巴倫邀請了她陪他去看比賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are invited</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are formally asked or given permission to do it. 邀請; 聘請","examples":["At a future date, managers will be invited to apply for a management buy-out. 在將來的某一天，經理們將受邀參加一項管理層控股收購。","He invited me to go into partnership with him. 他邀請了我與他合作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something you say or do <b>invites</b> trouble or criticism, it makes trouble or criticism more likely. 招致","examples":["Their refusal to compromise will inevitably invite more criticism from the UN. 他們的拒絕讓步將不可避免地招致來自聯合國的更多批評。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>invite</b> is an invitation to something such as a party or a meal. 請貼","examples":["She tried to wangle an invite to the party. 她試圖騙取一張聚會請柬。"]}]}]},"locate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"確定……的位置，探明；設立，建立；遷居，開辦公司；位於（be located in）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>locate</b> something or someone, you find out where they are. 找到","examples":["The scientists want to locate the position of the gene on a chromosome. 科學家們想找到該基因在染色體上的位置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>locate</b> something in a particular place, you put it there or build it there. 把…建在","examples":["Atlanta was voted the best city in which to locate a business by more than 400 chief executives. 亞特蘭大被四百多位企業執行長投票選為建立公司的最佳城市。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>locate</b> in a particular place, you move there or open a business there. 定居; 營業","examples":["...tax breaks for businesses that locate in run-down neighbourhoods. …對在衰落地段營業的公司的減稅。"]}]}]},"lend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"借給，借出；貸出，貸（款）；給……增加，增添（特色）；給予，提供（幫助、支援等）；使適合，使易遭受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or organizations such as banks <b>lend</b> you money, they give it to you and you agree to pay it back at a future date, often with an extra amount as interest. 出借; 貸款","examples":["The bank is reassessing its criteria for lending money. 銀行正在重新評估其貸款標準。","The government will lend you money at incredible rates, between zero percent and 3 percent. 政府將會以0到3%的利率貸款給你，這真是不可思議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lend</b> something that you own, you allow someone to have it or use it for a period of time. 出借","examples":["Will you lend me your jacket for a little while? 能把你的夾克借給我一會兒嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lend</b> your support <b>to</b> someone or something, you help them with what they are doing or with a problem that they have. 給予 (支援)","examples":["He was approached by the organizers to lend support to a benefit concert. 組織者接洽了他，希望他能支援一場慈善音樂會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>lends</b> <b>itself to</b> a particular activity or result, it is easy for it to be used for that activity or to achieve that result. 易於; 適合於","examples":["The room lends itself well to summer eating with its light, airy atmosphere. 這間屋子採光和通風都好，很適合夏天在這裡吃飯。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"出借; 貸款","examples":["...a financial institution that specializes in the lending of money. …一個專門貸款的金融機構。"]}]}]},"multiply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"大大增加，倍增；乘，乘以；繁殖，滋生"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"多樣地，多方面地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多層的（multi-ply）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>multiplies</b> or when you <b>multiply</b> it, it increases greatly in number or amount. 使大大增加; 大大增加","examples":["Such disputes multiplied in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries. 此類爭論在18世紀和19世紀大大增加。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>multiply</b> one number by another, you add the first number to itself as many times as is indicated by the second number. For example 2 multiplied by 3 is equal to 6. 乘","examples":["What do you get if you multiply six by nine? 6乘以9得多少？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals and insects <b>multiply</b>, they increase in number by giving birth to large numbers of young. 大量繁殖","examples":["These creatures can multiply quickly. 這些生物能迅速大量繁殖。"]}]}]},"lower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尤指在同類中處於）較下的，下方的；在底部的，近底部的；次重要的，較低階的；（數字或數量）較小的；向南的；早期的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"減少，降低；把……放低，使……降下；降低，貶低（身份）；變昏暗，變陰沉；露慍色"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"處於較低位置地，向低處下降地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lower</b> to refer to the bottom one of a pair of things. (一對物品中) 下面的","examples":["She bit her lower lip. 她咬著下唇。","...the lower of the two holes. …兩個洞中下面的那個。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>lower</b> to refer to the bottom part of something. 底部的","examples":["Use a small cushion to help give support to the lower back. 用一個小墊子來輔助支撐腰部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>lower</b> to refer to people or things that are less important than similar people or things. 下等的; 低階的","examples":["Already the awards are causing resentment in the lower ranks of council officers. 那些獎勵已經引起了委員會下層工作人員的不滿。","The nation's highest court reversed the lower court's decision. 該國的最高法院推翻了下級法院的判決。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lower</b> something, you move it slowly downward. (緩慢地) 放下; 降下","examples":["Two reporters had to help lower the coffin into the grave. 兩名記者不得不幫忙把棺材下放至墓穴中。","Sokolowski lowered himself into the black leather chair. 索科羅斯基緩緩地在黑皮椅裡坐下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lower</b> something, you make it less in amount, degree, value, or quality. 減少; 降低","examples":["The Central Bank has lowered interest rates by 2 percent. 中央銀行已經降低了2%的利率。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>lowers</b> their head or eyes, they look downward, for example, because they are sad or embarrassed. 垂下","examples":["She lowered her head and brushed past photographers as she went back inside. 當她走回屋裡時，她垂下了頭，與攝影師擦肩而過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you would not <b>lower</b> <b>yourself</b> by doing something, you mean that you would not behave in a way that would make you or other people respect you less. 貶低 (身份)","examples":["Don't lower yourself, don't be the way they are. 不要貶低自己的身份，別像他們那樣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>lower</b> your voice or if your voice <b>lowers</b>, you speak more quietly. 放低 (聲音); 降低","examples":["The man moved closer, lowering his voice. 那個男人走近了些，同時放低了聲音。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(緩慢地) 放下; 降下","examples":["...the extinguishing of the Olympic flame and the lowering of the flag. …熄奧運聖火和降奧運旗幟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"減少; 降低","examples":["...a package of social measures which included the lowering of the retirement age. …包括降低退休年齡在內的一系列社會措施。"]}]}]},"maintain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保持，維持；維修，保養；斷言，主張；贍養，撫養；<舊>支援，維護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>maintain</b> something, you continue to have it, and do not let it stop or grow weaker. 保持","examples":["After the divorce, their father still maintained close contact with the boys. 離婚後，他們的父親仍和兒子們保持著密切聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>maintains</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you mean that they have stated their opinion strongly but not everyone agrees with them or believes them. 堅持說; 堅持認為","examples":["He has maintained that the money was donated for international purposes. 他堅持說這筆錢是出於國際目的而捐助的。","\"Not all feminism has to be like this,\" Jo maintains. 喬堅持認為，“並非所有的女權運動都得像這樣。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>maintain</b> something <b>at</b> a particular rate or level, you keep it at that rate or level. 維持","examples":["The government was right to maintain interest rates at a high level. 該政府將利率維持在一個高的層面是正確的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>maintain</b> a road, building, vehicle, or machine, you keep it in good condition by regularly checking it and repairing it when necessary. 維修; 保養","examples":["The house costs a fortune to maintain. 維修這房子花費巨大。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>maintain</b> someone, you provide them with money and other things that they need. 供養","examples":["...the basic costs of maintaining a child. …供養一個孩子的基本費用。"]}]}]},"obey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遵守，服從，聽從；<非正式>順……的意，按……的通常情況行事；遵循（原則、自然規律等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>obey</b> a person, a command, or an instruction, you do what you are told to do. 順服; 遵守","examples":["Cissie obeyed her mother without question. 茜茜絕對服從她的母親。","Most people obey the law. 大多數人遵守法律。","It was his duty to obey. 服從是他的職責。"]}]}]},"lose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遺失，丟失；失去（某一特性、特點、態度或信念）；被剝奪，被損壞；失去（親人或朋友等）；輸掉（比賽、戰鬥、爭論等）；降低，減少；擺脫，甩掉（追趕者）；使不明白，使迷惑；去掉，拿掉；虧（本），賠（錢）；浪費，錯過；（鍾、表）走慢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> a contest, a fight, or an argument, you do not succeed because someone does better than you and defeats you. 輸掉; 失敗","examples":["The Golden Bears have lost three games this season. 金熊隊本賽季已輸了3場比賽。","The government lost the argument over the pace of reform. 政府輸掉了關於改革速度的辯論。","No one likes to lose. 沒人願意失敗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> something, you do not know where it is, for example, because you have forgotten where you put it. 丟失","examples":["I lost my keys. 我丟了鑰匙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that you <b>lose</b> something when you no longer have it because it has been taken away from you or destroyed. 失去","examples":["I lost my job when the company moved to another state. 當公司遷往另一個州時我失去了工作。","He lost his licence for six months. 他曾被吊銷執照6個月。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>loses</b> a quality, characteristic, attitude, or belief, they no longer have it. 喪失 (品質、特徵、態度或信仰等)","examples":["He lost all sense of reason. 他完全喪失了理智。","The government had lost all credibility. 政府完全喪失了信譽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> an ability, you stop having that ability because of something such as an accident. 失去 (能力)","examples":["They lost their ability to hear. 他們失聰了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something <b>loses</b> heat, their temperature becomes lower. 降低 (溫度)","examples":["Babies lose heat much faster than adults. 幼兒散熱比成人快得多。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> blood or fluid from your body, it leaves your body so that you have less of it. 失去 (血或體液)","examples":["The victim suffered a dreadful injury and lost a lot of blood. 受害人傷勢嚴重，失血很多。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> weight, you become less heavy, and usually look thinner. 減輕 (體重)","examples":["I have lost a lot of weight. 我體重減輕了不少。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone <b>loses</b> their life, they die. 失去 (生命)","examples":["...the ferry disaster in 1987, in which 192 people lost their lives. …1987年的渡船災難中有192人喪生。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> a close relative or friend, they die. 失去 (親人或朋友)","examples":["My Grandma lost her brother in the war. 我的祖母在戰爭中失去了弟弟。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If things <b>are lost</b>, they are destroyed in a disaster. (在災難中) 損毀","examples":["...the famous Nankin pottery that was lost in a shipwreck off the coast of China. …頗具名氣的白底青花瓷器，在中國沿海的沉船事故中被損毀。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> time, something slows you down so that you do not make as much progress as you hoped. 錯過 (時機)","examples":["They claim that police lost valuable time in the early part of the investigation. 他們聲稱，警察在調查初期錯失良機。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> an opportunity, you do not take advantage of it. 失去 (機會)","examples":["If you don't do it soon you're going to lose the opportunity. 如果你不盡快做，你會失去機會的。","They did not lose the opportunity to say what they thought of events. 他們抓住機會說出他們對事件的看法。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> <b>yourself in</b> something or if you <b>are lost</b> <b>in</b> it, you give a lot of attention to it and do not think about anything else. 使專注","examples":["Michael held on to her arm, losing himself in the music. 邁克爾挽著她的胳膊，陶醉於音樂之中。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If a business <b>loses</b> money, it earns less money than it spends, and is therefore in debt. 虧損","examples":["His stores stand to lose millions of dollars. 他的商店承受著數百萬美元的損失。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If something <b>loses</b> you a contest or <b>loses</b> you something that you had, it causes you to fail or to no longer have what you had. 使輸掉; 使失去","examples":["My own stupidity lost me the match. 我個人的愚蠢使我輸了這場比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> your <b>way</b>, you become lost when you are trying to go somewhere. 迷路","examples":["The men lost their way in a sandstorm. 那些人在沙塵暴中迷路了。"]}]}]},"omit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"省去，遺漏；不做，未能做"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>omit</b> something, you do not include it in an activity or piece of work, deliberately or accidentally. 刪節; 省略; 遺漏","examples":["Omit the salt in this recipe. 去掉這個食譜中的鹽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>omit</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do not do it. 未 (做)","examples":["His new girlfriend had omitted to tell him she was married. 他的新任女友沒有跟他說她已經結婚。"]}]}]},"narrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狹窄的，狹小的；（想法、態度或信仰）狹隘的；勉強的，（成敗）差距很小的；（種類或數目）有限的，範圍小的；嚴格的，精確的；（標音）嚴式的；（語音）窄的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人的眼睛）眯起來；使縮小，壓縮；使變窄，變窄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"海峽；狹窄部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>narrow</b> measures a very small distance from one side to the other, especially compared to its length or height. 狹窄的","examples":["...through the town's narrow streets. …穿過小鎮狹窄的街道。","She had long, narrow feet. 她有一雙瘦長的腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's ideas, attitudes, or beliefs as <b>narrow</b>, you disapprove of them because they are restricted in some way, and often ignore the more important aspects of an argument or situation. (想法、態度、信仰等) 狹隘的","examples":["...a narrow and outdated view of family life. …對家庭生活狹隘過時的一種看法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>narrow</b> victory, you succeed in winning but only by a small amount. 勉強的","examples":["Voters approved the plan by a narrow majority. 投票人以微弱的多數透過了這個方案。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>narrow</b> escape, something unpleasant nearly happens to you. 很險的 (逃脫)","examples":["Two police officers had a narrow escape when rioters attacked their vehicles. 暴徒們攻擊他們的車輛時，兩名警官死裡逃生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狹窄","examples":["...the narrowness of the river mouth. …河口的狹窄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"縮小","examples":["...a narrowing of the gap between rich members and poor. …貧富成員間差距的縮小。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>narrows</b>, it becomes less wide. 變窄","examples":["The wide track narrows before crossing another stream. 寬寬的路徑在穿越另一條小溪前變窄了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your eyes <b>narrow</b> or if you <b>narrow</b> your eyes, you almost close them, for example because you are angry or because you are trying to concentrate on something. 眯起","examples":["Coggins' eyes narrowed angrily. \"You think I'd tell you?\" 科金斯憤怒地眯起雙眼說，“你以為我會告訴你？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>narrows</b> or if you <b>narrow</b> it, its extent or range becomes smaller. 使…縮小; 縮小","examples":["Most recent opinion polls suggest that the gap between the two main parties has narrowed. 最近的民意調查表明，兩個主要政黨之間的分歧已經縮小。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狹隘地","examples":["They may define their contribution too narrowly. 他們可能把他們的貢獻說得太狹隘了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"勉強地","examples":["She narrowly failed to win enough votes. 她差點贏得足夠的選票。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"很險地 (逃脫)","examples":["Five firemen narrowly escaped death when a staircase collapsed beneath their feet. 一段樓梯在他們腳下坍塌時，五名消防隊員險些喪命。"]}]}]},"occur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指意外地）發生；存在，出現；（想法）產生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>occurs</b>, it happens. 發生","examples":["If headaches only occur at night, lack of fresh air and oxygen is often the cause. 如果頭痛只發生在晚上，缺少新鮮空氣和氧氣常常是其原因。","The crash occurred when the crew shut down the wrong engine. 機組人員關錯發動機後就墜毀了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>occurs</b> in a particular place, it exists or is present there. (某事物在某地) 出現","examples":["These snails do not occur on low-lying coral islands. 這些蝸牛不會出現在低窪的珊瑚島上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a thought or idea <b>occurs</b> <b>to</b> you, you suddenly think of it or realize it. (想法、主意在某人腦海中) 突然出現","examples":["It did not occur to me to check my insurance policy. 我沒想到要核對我的保險單。"]}]}]},"organize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"組織，籌備；設法提供；（按某一體系）整理，安排；規劃，照料；聚集，召集；（為特定人群）建立組織；<古>形成有機體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>organize</b> an event or activity, you make sure that the necessary arrangements are made. 組織","examples":["In the end, we all decided to organize a concert for Easter. 最後，我們一致決定為復活節組織一場音樂會。","...a two-day meeting organized by the United Nations. …一個由聯合國組織的，為期兩天的會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>organize</b> something that someone wants or needs, you make sure that it is provided. 安排","examples":["I will organize transportation. 我來安排運輸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>organize</b> a set of things, you arrange them in an ordered way or give them a structure. 整理","examples":["He began to organize his materials. 他開始整理他的材料。","She took a hasty cup of coffee and tried to organize her scattered thoughts. 她急急忙忙喝了杯咖啡，設法整理散亂的思緒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>organize</b> yourself, you plan your work and activities in an ordered, efficient way. 規劃 (自己的工作和活動)","examples":["...changing the way you organize yourself. …改變你規劃自己的方式。","Go right ahead, I'm sure you don't need me to organize you. 儘管幹，我確信你不需要我來幫你規劃。"]}]}]},"operate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"操縱，操作（機器或裝置）；（機器等）運轉，執行 ；管理，經營（企業、部門等）；（組織或公司）運營；（使）執行，（使）工作；起作用，發生影響；（以某種方式）行事；開刀，動手術；（士兵或警察在某地區）行動，執行公務"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>operate</b> a business or organization, you work to keep it running. If a business or organization <b>operates</b>, it carries out its work. 經營; 運營","examples":["Until his death in 1986 Greenwood owned and operated an enormous pear orchard. 直到1986年去世，格林伍德一直擁有並經營著一個規模巨大的梨園。","...allowing commercial banks to operate in the country. …允許商業銀行在本國運營。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>operate</b> a machine or device, or when it <b>operates</b>, you make it work. 操作; 運轉","examples":["A massive rock fall trapped the men as they operated a tunnelling machine. 那些男人在駕駛隧道掘進機時，一次大面積的巖崩困住了他們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"經營","examples":["Company finance is to provide funds for the everyday operation of the business. 公司財務將為公司業務的日常運轉提供資金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"執行","examples":["No money can be spent on the construction and operation of the tram. 沒有錢可以用於有軌電車的建設和執行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"操作","examples":["...over 1,000 dials monitoring every aspect of the operation of the aeroplane. …監控著飛機每項操作的1000多個調節控制器。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The way that something <b>operates</b> is the way that it works or has a particular effect. 起作用","examples":["Ceiling and wall lights can operate independently. 天花板和牆上的燈能夠獨立操控。","How do accounting records operate? 結算記錄是如何運作的？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When surgeons <b>operate</b> <b>on</b> a patient in a hospital, they cut open a patient's body in order to remove, replace, or repair a diseased or damaged part. 動手術","examples":["In March 2005, surgeons operated on Max for a brain aneurysm. 2005年3月，外科醫生們為馬克斯做了腦部動脈瘤手術。"]}]}]},"pray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"祈禱，禱告；渴望，祈望；祈求，懇求"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於詢問或指示）請問，請"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>pray</b>, they speak to God in order to give thanks or to ask for his help. 祈禱","examples":["He spent his time in prison praying and studying. 他把在獄中的時間花在了祈禱和學習上。","Now all we have to do is help ourselves and pray to God. 現在我們要做的是自救和向上帝祈禱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone is hoping very much that something will happen, you can say that they <b>are praying</b> that it will happen. 祈望","examples":["I'm just praying that somebody in Congress will do something before it's too late. 我只祈望國會中有人在還來得及的時候做點什麼。"]}]}]},"prefer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"更喜愛，寧可；<法律>舉報，提出（控告）；<古>提拔（某人），提升"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prefer</b> someone or something, you like that person or thing better than another, and so you are more likely to choose them if there is a choice. 更喜歡","examples":["Does he prefer a particular sort of music? 他更喜歡某種特別的音樂嗎？","I became a teacher because I preferred books and people to politics. 我成為了一名教師是因為我更喜歡書籍和人而不是政治。","I prefer to think of peace not war. 我更喜歡思考和平而不是戰爭。","I would prefer him to be with us next season. 我更希望他在下個賽季和我們在一起。"]}]}]},"pronounce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發（音），讀（音）；正式宣佈（或公佈、授予等）；發表意見，表態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>pronounce</b> a word means to say it using particular sounds. 發 (某字或詞的) 音","examples":["Have I pronounced your name correctly? 我把你的名字讀對了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pronounce</b> something to be true, you state that it is the case. 宣佈","examples":["A specialist has now pronounced him fully fit. 一位專家已宣佈他完全康復了。"]}]}]},"propose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提議，建議；提出（理論或解釋）；提名，推薦；計劃，打算；求婚；（向立法機構或委員會）提交（動議）；提議祝（酒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>propose</b> something such as a plan or an idea, you suggest it for people to think about and decide upon. 建議","examples":["Hamilton proposed a change in the traditional debating format. 漢密爾頓建議對傳統的辯論形式作一個改變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>propose</b> to do something, you intend to do it. 打算","examples":["It's still far from clear what action the government proposes to take over the affair. 尚不清楚政府打算採取什麼行動接手這件事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>propose</b> a motion for debate, or a candidate for election, you begin the debate or the election procedure by formally stating your support for that motion or candidate. 提出; 提名","examples":["He has proposed a resolution limiting the role of U.S. troops. 他提出了一項限制美軍作用的決議。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>propose to</b> someone, or <b>propose marriage</b> <b>to</b> them, you ask them to marry you. 求婚","examples":["He proposed to his girlfriend over a public-address system. 他在有線廣播系統上向女友求婚。"]}]}]},"protect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護，防護；（制訂法律）保護；投保，為……買保險；對……實行貿易保護；（計算機）保護（資料或儲存庫）；防守"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>protect</b> someone or something means to prevent them from being harmed or damaged. 保護","examples":["So, what can women do to protect themselves from heart disease? 那麼，女效能做什麼來保護自己不患心臟病呢？","A long thin wool coat and a purple headscarf protected her against the wind. 一件薄薄的羊毛長大衣和一條紫色頭巾為她擋風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an insurance policy <b>protects</b> you <b>against</b> an event such as death, injury, fire, or theft, the insurance company will give you or your family money if that event happens. 為…保險","examples":["Many manufacturers have policies to protect themselves against blackmailers. 許多製造商都有為敲詐勒索保險的保單。"]}]}]},"punish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"處罰，懲罰（做錯事或犯法的人）；懲處（犯罪行為）；<非正式>（尤指體育運動中）利用（對手的失誤）；粗暴地對待；使遭受嚴重打擊；自責；<非正式> 貪婪地吃喝；施加懲罰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>punish</b> someone means to make them suffer in some way because they have done something wrong. 懲罰","examples":["I don't believe that George ever had to punish the children. 我不相信喬治曾不得不懲罰這些孩子。","According to present law, the authorities can only punish smugglers with small fines. 根據現行法律，當局只能對走私者處以小額罰款。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>punish</b> a crime means to punish anyone who commits that crime. 懲處","examples":["...federal laws to punish crimes such as murder and assault. …懲處諸如謀殺和強姦等罪的聯邦法律。"]}]}]},"quit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>停止，戒掉；<非正式>離開（工作崗位、學校等），離任；搬離（租住的房子），離開（某地）；關閉，退出（計算機程式等）；使解除，使擺脫"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"擺脫了……的，已經了結的（quit of）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"辭職，離任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>quit</b>, or <b>quit</b> your job, you choose to leave it. 辭去 (工作); 辭職","examples":["He quit his job as an office boy. 他辭去了辦公室勤雜員的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>quit</b> an activity or <b>quit</b> doing something, you stop doing it. 停止","examples":["A nicotine spray can help smokers quit the habit. 一種尼古丁噴劑可以幫助吸菸者戒菸。","Quit acting like you didn't know. 別裝得像你不知道似的。","Quit it! That hurts! 戒掉它吧！這東西害人！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>quit</b> a place, you leave it completely and do not go back to it. 徹底離開","examples":["Science fiction writers have long dreamed that humans might one day quit the earth to colonize other planets. 科幻小說作家們長期以來一直夢想著人類有一天可以離開地球移居到其它星球上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are going to <b>call it quits</b>, you mean that you have decided to stop doing something or being involved in something. 叫停","examples":["They raised $630,000 through listener donations, and then called it quits. 他們透過聽眾募捐籌集到了63萬美元，之後就叫停了。"]}]}]},"provide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供，供給；配備，準備好；（法律或規章）規定；供養，提供生計；為（可能事件）作充分準備；<史>任命（牧師）擔任有俸神職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>provide</b> something that someone needs or wants, or if you <b>provide</b> them <b>with</b> it, you give it to them or make it available to them. 提供","examples":["I'll be glad to provide a copy of this. 我將很樂意提供這東西的一個副本。","They would not provide any details. 他們不肯提供任何細節。","They provided him with a car and driver. 他們為他提供了一輛汽車和一位司機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a law or agreement <b>provides</b> <b>that</b> something will happen, it states that it will happen. 規定","examples":["The treaty provides that, by the end of the century, the United States must have removed its bases. 這項條約規定，到本世紀末，美國必須撤走其基地。"]}]}]},"refuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拒絕，回絕（做某事）；不接受，拒絕（別人給的東西）；拒絕給（所需之物）；<非正式>（物體）未應要求起作用；<舊> 不接受（某人的）求婚；（馬）拒絕（跨欄或其他障礙物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"垃圾，廢棄物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"廢棄的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>refuse</b> <b>to</b> do something, you deliberately do not do it, or you say firmly that you will not do it. 拒絕","examples":["He refused to comment after the trial. 該審判之後他拒絕發表評論。","I could hardly refuse, could I? 我很難拒絕，是不是？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>refuses</b> you something, they do not give it to you or do not allow you to have it. 拒絕給予","examples":["The United States has refused him a visa. 美國當局已拒絕給予他簽證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>refuse</b> something that is offered to you, you do not accept it. 拒絕","examples":["The patient has the right to refuse treatment. 病人有權拒絕治療。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Refuse</b> consists of the rubbish and all the things that are not wanted in a house, shop, or factory, and that are regularly thrown away; used mainly in official language. 垃圾; 廢料","examples":["The town made a weekly collection of refuse. 該鎮每週收一次垃圾。"]}]}]},"reject":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拒絕，否決（提議、建議或請求）；擯棄，不接受（信仰或政治制度）；不僱用，不錄取；（因質量不好而）廢棄；冷落，嫌棄；排異，排斥（移植器官）；（投幣裝置）拒絕接受（硬幣）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"次品，廢品；不合格者，被排斥者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reject</b> something such as a proposal, a request, or an offer, you do not accept it or you do not agree to it. 拒絕; 不同意","examples":["The government is expected to reject the idea of state subsidy for a new high-speed railway. 預期該政府不會同意向一條新建高速鐵路提供國家補助的意見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reject</b> a belief or a political system, you refuse to believe in it or to live by its rules. 擯棄","examples":["...the children of Eastern European immigrants who had rejected their parents' political and religious beliefs. …已經擯棄了其父母的政治和宗教信仰的東歐移民的子女們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is rejected</b> for a job or course of study, it is not offered to them. 拒絕 (錄用或錄取)","examples":["One of my most able students was rejected by another university. 我的一個最有能力的學生被另外一所大學拒絕了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>rejects</b> another person who expects affection from them, they are cold and unfriendly toward them. 拒絕 (某人的愛情)","examples":["...people who had been rejected by their lovers. …遭到他們的戀人拒絕的人們。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person's body <b>rejects</b> something such as a new heart that has been transplanted into it, it tries to attack and destroy it. 排斥 (移植的器官等)","examples":["It was feared his body was rejecting a kidney he received in a transplant four years ago. 人們擔心他的身體在排斥他4年前在一項移植中接受的一個腎臟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"拒絕; 不同意","examples":["The rejection of such initiatives by no means indicates that voters are unconcerned about the environment. 對這些提案的不同意決不意味著選民們不關心環境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"擯棄","examples":["His rejection of our values is far more complete than that of D. H. Lawrence. 他對於我們價值觀的擯棄遠比D. H.勞倫斯更徹底。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"拒絕","examples":["Be prepared for lots of rejections before you land a job. 在你找到一份工作之前要做好多次被拒絕的準備。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"拒絕","examples":["These feelings of rejection and hurt remain. 這些遭到拒絕和傷害的感覺仍然存在。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"排斥","examples":["...a special drug which stops rejection of transplanted organs. …一種阻止對移植器官的排斥的專用藥物。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>reject</b> is a product that has not been accepted for use or sale, because there is something wrong with it. 不合格品","examples":["The check shirt is a reject - too small. 這件格子襯衣是個不合格品，太小。"]}]}]},"realize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"瞭解，意識到；（所擔心的事）發生，產生（be realized）；實現（目標、夢想等）；（充分）發揮出自己的潛力； 把（概念等）具體表現出來；用（語言特徵）表達；對（記譜不全的樂曲）做完整兌譜改編；獲得（金錢，利潤）；變現，變賣（資產）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>realize</b> that something is true, you become aware of that fact or understand it. 意識到","examples":["As soon as we realized something was wrong, we moved the children away. 我們一意識到出了問題，就立即把孩子們轉移開了。","People don't realize how serious this recession has actually been. 人們沒有意識到這次經濟衰退有多麼嚴重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your hopes, desires, or fears <b>are realized</b>, the things that you hope for, desire, or fear actually happen. (希望、渴望或恐懼) 變成現實","examples":["All his worst fears were realized. 他最擔心的事情都變成了現實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>realizes</b> a design or an idea, they make or organize something based on that design or idea. 使成為現實","examples":["I knew the technique that I would have to create in order to realize that structure. 我瞭解為了使這種結構成為現實，我必須開發的技術。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>realizes</b> their potential, they do everything they are capable of doing, because they have been given the opportunity to do so. 發揮 (潛能)","examples":["The support systems to enable women to realize their potential at work are seriously inadequate. 使婦女發揮其工作潛能的支援系統嚴重不足。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>realizes</b> a particular amount of money when it is sold, that amount of money is paid for it. 賺取 (指透過出售某物賺錢)","examples":["A selection of correspondence from P.G. Wodehouse realized 2,000 dollars. 佩·格·沃德豪斯的書信選集賣了2000美元。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"認識","examples":["There is now a growing realization that things cannot go on like this for much longer. 人們越來越認識到事情不可能再這樣發展下去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"成為現實","examples":["In Kravis's venomous tone he recognized the realization of his worst fears. 從克拉維斯惡毒的語調中他意識到他最害怕的事情發生了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"賺取","examples":["...a total cash realization of about $23 million. …一共賺了大約兩千三百萬美元的現金。"]}]}]},"require":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"需要；要求做（某事），規定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>require</b> something or if something <b>is required</b>, you need it or it is necessary. 需要","examples":["If you require further information, you should consult the registrar. 如果你需要進一步的資訊，你應該向註冊主任諮詢。","This isn't the kind of crisis that requires us to drop everything else. 這不是需要我們拋下其他一切的那種危機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a law or rule <b>requires</b> you <b>to</b> do something, you have to do it. 要求","examples":["The rules also require employers to provide safety training. 這些規定也要求僱主們提供安全訓練。","At least 35 manufacturers have flouted a law requiring prompt reporting of such malfunctions. 至少有三十五位製造商已經對要求即刻彙報這類故障的規定嗤之以鼻了。"]}]}]},"satisfy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使滿意，使滿足；滿足（要求、需要等）；符合（規定、條件或標準）；使確信，使信服；清償，償付；解，符合（方程式）；令人滿意，令人滿足"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>satisfies</b> you, they give you enough of what you want or need to make you pleased or contented. 使滿意","examples":["The pace of change has not been quick enough to satisfy everyone. 變化的速度還沒有快到讓所有人都滿意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>satisfy</b> someone <b>that</b> something is true or has been done properly means to convince them by giving them more information or by showing them what has been done. 使確信","examples":["He has to satisfy the environmental lobby that real progress will be made to cut emissions. 他必須使環境遊說團確信，將採取實質性行動來降低排放量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>satisfy</b> the requirements for something, you are good enough or have the right qualities to fulfil these requirements. 滿足 (要求)","examples":["The executive committee recommends that the procedures should satisfy certain basic requirements. 執行委員會建議，這些程式應該滿足某些基本要求。"]}]}]},"slim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"苗條的，纖細的；單薄的；（物）狹長的；（衣服）修長的，緊身的；（數量或數字）微小的；（公司或其他組織）精簡的；<南非>詭計多端的，狡猾的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（靠節食等）變苗條，減肥；減少（產品），縮減（人員）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（非洲）艾滋病；瘦身課程（或時期）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slim</b> person has an attractively thin and well-shaped body. 苗條的; 纖細的","examples":["The young woman was tall and slim. 那個年輕女子個子高挑，身材苗條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slim</b> book, wallet, or other object is thinner than usual. 薄的","examples":["The slim booklets describe a range of services and facilities. 那些薄薄的小冊子描述了一系列服務和設施。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>slim</b> chance or possibility is a very small one. (機會或可能性) 微小的","examples":["There's still a slim chance that he may become president. 仍然有微小的可能他會當上總統。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an organization <b>slims</b> its products or workers, it reduces the number of them that it has. 縮減","examples":["The company recently slimmed its product line. 該公司最近縮減了生產線。"]}]}]},"rock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"岩石；礁石；（尤指凸出地面的）巖塊，大石塊；碎石，石子；<非正式>鑽石，寶石；搖滾樂；可信賴的人，靠山；<英>棒棒糖；<非正式>石毒，強效可卡因塊；<俚>睪丸（rocks）；輕輕搖動，輕輕搖擺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）輕輕搖晃，緩緩擺動；（使）劇烈搖擺，猛烈晃動；使震驚，使害怕；<非正式>（尤指自信或惹人注目地）穿（衣）；<非正式>跳搖滾舞，奏搖滾樂；<俚>很好，棒極了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rock</b> is the hard substance which the earth is made of. 岩石","examples":["The hills above the valley are bare rock. 河谷上面的山是光禿禿的岩石。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rock</b> is a large piece of rock that sticks up out of the ground or the sea, or that has broken away from a mountain or a cliff. 巨石","examples":["She sat cross-legged on the rock. 她盤著腿坐在那塊巨石上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rock</b> is a piece of rock that is small enough for you to pick up. 小石塊","examples":["She bent down, picked up a rock, and threw it into the trees. 她彎下腰，揀起一塊小石頭，把它扔進樹林裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Rock</b> is loud music with a strong beat that is usually played and sung by a small group of people using instruments such as electric guitars and drums. 搖滾樂","examples":["...a rock concert. …一場搖滾音樂會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a rocking motion 前後搖動","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>rocks</b> or when you <b>rock</b> it, it moves slowly and regularly backward and forward or from side to side. 使搖晃; 搖晃","examples":["His body rocked from side to side with the train. 他的身體隨著火車左右晃動著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an explosion or an earthquake <b>rocks</b> a building or an area, it causes the building or area to shake. 使震動; 震動","examples":["Three people were injured yesterday when an explosion rocked the factory. 昨天，三名工人在爆炸引起的工廠震動時受傷。","In Taipei buildings rocked back and forth. 在臺北，建築物前後搖晃著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event or a piece of news <b>rocks</b> a group or society, it shocks them or makes them feel less secure. 震驚","examples":["His death rocked the fashion business. 他的死震驚了時裝界。"]}]}]},"select":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"選擇，挑選；（在計算機螢幕上）選定；（進化）決定（特徵，生物）是否繼續存在"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精選的，優等的；高階的，奢華的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>select</b> something, you choose it from a number of things of the same kind. 挑選; 選擇","examples":["Voters are selecting candidates for both U.S. Senate seats and for 52 congressional seats. 選民們正在選舉美國參議院議席的候選人和52個眾議院席位的候選人。","With a difficult tee shot, select a club which will keep you short of the trouble. 開球難度較大時，選擇一根用起來能不給你添亂的高爾夫球杆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>select</b> a file or a piece of text on a computer screen, you click on it so that it is marked in a different colour, usually in order for you to give the computer an instruction relating to that file or piece of text. (在計算機螢幕上) 選定 (某檔案或某段文章以作特別處理)","examples":["I selected a file and pressed the delete key. 我選定了一份檔案，然後按下了刪除鍵。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>select</b> group is a small group of some of the best people or things of their kind. 精選的","examples":["...a select group of French cheeses. …一組精選的的法國乳酪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>select</b>, you mean it has many desirable features, but is available only to people who have a lot of money or who belong to a high social class. 第一流的; 只為富人、上層人士而設的","examples":["Christian Lacroix is throwing a very lavish and very select party. 克里斯琴·拉克魯瓦正在舉行一個上層人士參加的非常豪華的聚會。"]}]}]},"subtract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"減去，刪減；減去，扣除"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>subtract</b> one number <b>from</b> another, you do a calculation in which you take it away from the other number. For example, if you subtract 3 from 5, you get 2. (從一數中) 減去 (另一數)","examples":["Mandy subtracted the date of birth from the date of death. 曼迪從死亡的日期減去了出生的日期。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"減法","examples":["She's ready to learn simple addition and subtraction. 她準備學習簡單的加法和減法。"]}]}]},"solve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解決，處理；解釋，解答"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>solve</b> a problem or a question, you find a solution or an answer to it. 解決","examples":["Their domestic reforms did nothing to solve the problem of unemployment. 他們的國內改革沒有采取任何措施以解決失業問題。"]}]}]},"separate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單獨的，分開的；不同的，不相關的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）分離；（把……）分成不同部分；隔開，阻隔；（夫妻）分居，（同居情侶）分手；區分，區別；<美>解僱，辭退"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可搭配穿著的單件衣服（separates）；獨立音響裝置（separates）；（按照顆粒大小、礦物組成等標準的）土壤劃分（separates）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>separate</b> <b>from</b> another, there is a barrier, space, or division between them, so that they are clearly two things. 分開的; 單獨的","examples":["They are now making plans to form their own separate party. 他們現在正制訂計劃單獨組建自己的政黨。","Business bank accounts were kept separate from personal ones. 銀行的商業賬戶同個人賬戶是分開存放的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to <b>separate</b> things, you mean several different things, rather than just one thing. 分開的; 不同的","examples":["Use separate chopping boards for raw meats, cooked meats, vegetables and salads. 用不同的砧板切生肉、熟肉、蔬菜和沙拉。","Men and women have separate exercise rooms. 男士和女士有分開的健身房。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>separate</b> people or things that are together, or if they <b>separate</b>, they move apart. 分開","examples":["Police moved in to separate the two groups. 警察插進來分開了那兩群人。","The pans were held in both hands and swirled around to separate gold particles from the dirt. 淘洗盤被端在兩手中旋轉，以便將金粒從泥沙中分離出來。","The front end of the car separated from the rest of the vehicle. 車的前端同車子的其他部分分開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>separate</b> people or things that have been connected, or if one <b>separates</b> <b>from</b> another, the connection between them is ended. 使分離; 脫離","examples":["They want to separate teaching from research. 他們要把教學與研究分離開來。","It's very possible that we may see a movement to separate the two parts of the country. 我們很有可能會看到一場運動將該國一分為二。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a couple who are married or living together <b>separate</b>, they decide to live apart. 分居","examples":["Her parents separated when she was very young. 在她很小的時候，父母就分居了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An object, obstacle, distance, or period of time which <b>separates</b> two people, groups, or things exists between them. 分隔","examples":["...the white-railed fence that separated the garden from the paddock. …把院子和圍場分隔開來的白色圍欄。","They had undoubtedly made progress in the six years that separated the two periods. 他們無疑在那兩個時期之間的6年裡取得了進步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>separate</b> one idea or fact <b>from</b> another, you clearly see or show the difference between them. 分辨; 區分","examples":["It is difficult to separate legend from truth. 傳說與事實很難分辨。","...learning how to separate real problems from imaginary illnesses. …學習如何分辨真實的與想像的疾病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A quality or factor that <b>separates</b> one thing <b>from</b> another is the reason why the two things are different from each other. 使不同","examples":["The single most important factor that separates ordinary photographs from good photographs is the lighting. 區分一般照片和好照片的惟一重要因素是光線效果。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a particular number of points <b>separate</b> two teams or competitors, one of them is winning or has won by that number of points. 使分出高下; 使分出輸贏","examples":["In the end only three points separated the two teams. 最後，兩隊只以3分之差分出了輸贏。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>separate</b> a group of people or things <b>into</b> smaller elements, or if a group <b>separates</b>, it is divided into smaller elements. 使分散; 分散","examples":["The police wanted to separate them into smaller groups. 警察想把他們分成更小的組。","Let's separate into smaller groups. 讓我們分成更小的組吧。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Separate out</b> means the same as . 分辨; 區分","examples":["How can one ever separate out the act from the attitudes that surround it? 如何才能將行動同圍繞著它的種種看法區分開來呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Separate out</b> means the same as . 分開; 分散","examples":["If prepared many hours ahead, the mixture may separate out. 如果提前很多小時配製，這種混合物就可能會分離。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Separates</b> are clothes such as skirts, trousers, and shirts which cover just the top half or the bottom half of your body. 單件衣服","examples":["She wears coordinated separates instead of a suit. 她不穿套裝，而穿著搭配協調的單件衣服。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two or more people who have been together for some time <b>go</b> their <b>separate ways</b>, they go to different places or end their relationship. 分道揚鑣","examples":["Sue was 27 when she and her husband decided to go their separate ways. 27歲時蘇與丈夫決定分道揚鑣。"]}]}]},"survive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（經歷事故、戰爭或疾病後）活下來，倖存；比……活得久，比……長壽；挺過，艱難度過；倖免於難，留存；（靠很少的錢）繼續維持生活；設法對付（困難或令人不愉快的事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or living thing <b>survives</b> in a dangerous situation such as an accident or an illness, they do not die. 存活","examples":["...the sequence of events that left the eight pupils battling to survive in icy seas for over four hours. …使4名小學生在冰冷的海洋中掙扎求生超過4個小時的一連串事件。","Those organisms that are most suited to the environment will be those that will survive. 那些最適應環境的生物將是那些存活下來的。","He had survived heart bypass surgery. 他在心臟搭橋手術中活了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>survive</b> in difficult circumstances, you manage to live or continue in spite of them and do not let them affect you very much. 挺過","examples":["On my first day here I thought, \"Ooh, how will I survive?\" 在這兒的第一天我想：“噢，我該怎麼挺過去呀？”","...people who are struggling to survive without jobs. …掙扎著以挺過失業的人們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>survives</b>, it continues to exist even after being in a dangerous situation or existing for a long time. 倖存","examples":["When the market economy is introduced, many factories will not survive. 一旦推行市場經濟，很多工廠將無法存活下去。","No one survived the crash. 無人在這次撞擊中倖免於難。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>survive</b> someone, you continue to live after they have died. 比…活得長","examples":["Most women will survive their spouses. 大多數女性比她們的配偶活得長。"]}]}]},"steal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偷竊，盜竊；剽竊，竊取（觀點）；悄悄地移動；（在棒球比賽中）偷（壘）；（在籃球或冰球比賽中）斷（球），截（球）；偷偷做；偷拿，私自拿；搶（鏡頭、戲等）；（體育運動中）意外贏得；騙走"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"極廉價的物品，低價；（尤指籃球比賽中的）斷球；（棒球比賽中的）偷壘；<美>偷竊，行竊；剽竊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>steal</b> something <b>from</b> someone, you take it away from them without their permission and without intending to return it. 偷","examples":["He was accused of stealing a small boy's bicycle. 他被指控偷了一個小男孩的腳踏車。","People who are drug addicts come in and steal. 吸毒成癮的人們進來偷東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>steal</b> someone else's ideas, you pretend that they are your own. 剽竊","examples":["A writer is suing director Steven Spielberg for allegedly stealing his film idea. 一個作家正在控告史蒂文·斯皮爾伯格導演剽竊了他的電影創意。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被盜的","examples":["We have now found the stolen car. 我們現已找到被盜的汽車。"]}]}]},"settle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解決，結束（爭端等）；確定，決定；定居，安家；殖民，移居於；安置，安頓；（使）平靜，（使）安定；降落，停留；（使）沉降，下陷；付清，結算；處理，分配（財產）；籠罩，穩定下來；把......放好，安放；（無可奈何地）接受（或答應）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"高背扶手木長椅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>settle</b> an argument or problem, or if something <b>settles</b> it, they solve it, for example, by making a decision about who is right or about what to do. 解決 (糾紛、問題等)","examples":["They agreed to try to settle their dispute by negotiation. 他們同意儘量透過談判解決他們之間的糾紛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>settle</b> a legal dispute or if they <b>settle</b>, they agree to end the dispute without going to a court of law, for example, by paying some money or by apologizing. (庭外) 和解","examples":["In an attempt to settle the case, Molken has agreed to pay restitution. 為了結此案，莫爾肯已同意賠償。","She got much less than she would have done if she had settled out of court. 她得到的遠不如她若庭外和解得到的多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>settle</b> a bill or debt, you pay the amount that you owe. 結算; 算清","examples":["I settled the bill for my coffee and his two glasses of wine. 我為我的咖啡和他的兩杯葡萄酒付了錢。","She has now settled with her landlord. 她現在已經和她的房東算清了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>is settled</b>, it has all been decided and arranged. 確定","examples":["As far as we're concerned, the matter is settled. 在我們看來，此事已定。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When people <b>settle</b> a place or in a place, or when a government <b>settles</b> them there, they start living there permanently. 定居於; 使定居; 定居","examples":["Refugees settling in a new country suffer from a number of problems. 在一個新國家定居的難民們面臨許多問題。","He visited Paris and eventually settled there. 他訪問了巴黎並最終在那兒定居了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>settle</b> <b>yourself</b> somewhere or <b>settle</b> somewhere, you sit down or make yourself comfortable. 安頓; 安坐","examples":["Albert settled himself on the sofa. 阿爾伯特在沙發安坐下來。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>settles</b> or if you <b>settle</b> it, it sinks slowly down and becomes still. 使沉降; 沉降","examples":["A black dust settled on the walls. 一團黑色粉塵落到了這些牆上。","Once its impurities had settled, the oil could be graded. 一旦雜質沉澱下去，油就可以定級了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your eyes <b>settle</b> <b>on</b> or <b>upon</b> something, you stop looking around and look at that thing for some time. (目光) 停留","examples":["The man let his eyes settle upon Blume's face. 那個人讓自己的目光落在了布盧姆的臉上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When birds or insects <b>settle on</b> something, they land on it from above. (鳥類或昆蟲) 飛落; 棲息","examples":["Moths flew in front of it, eventually settling on the rough painted metal. 飛蛾在它前面飛舞，最後落在了那塊粗糙的噴漆金屬上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a seat, for two or more people, usually made of wood with a high back and arms, and sometimes having a storage space in the boxlike seat 高背長靠椅","examples":[]}]}]},"succeed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"成功，達成；（學業、事業或其他活動）表現出色，有作為；取得預期效果，表現良好；繼任，接任；接替，隨後出現；結果卻是……；若一次不成功，要再接再厲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>succeed</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you manage to do it. (某人在做某事上) 成功","examples":["We have already succeeded in working out ground rules with the Department of Defense. 我們已和國防部成功地制定出了基本原則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>succeeds</b>, it works in a satisfactory way or has the result that is intended. (某事物) 成功","examples":["The talks can succeed if both sides are flexible and serious. 如果雙方都靈活並且認真，這些會談就能成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who <b>succeeds</b> gains a high position in what they do, for example in business or politics. (某人在商業、政治等方面) 成功","examples":["...the skills and qualities needed to succeed in small and medium-sized businesses. …在中小企業中要成功所需的技術和素質。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>succeed</b> another person, you are the next person to have their job or position. 接替","examples":["David Rowland is almost certain to succeed him as chairman on January 1. 戴維·羅蘭幾乎肯定會在1月1日接替他當主席。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>is succeeded</b> <b>by</b> another thing, the other thing happens or comes after it. 繼…之後","examples":["The presentation was succeeded by a roundtable discussion. 這個講演之後是一次圓桌討論。"]}]}]},"wed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"結婚，娶，嫁；（使）結合；堅持，專心於（活動、信仰或制度）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person <b>weds</b> another or if two people <b>wed</b> or <b>are wed</b>, they get married. 結婚","examples":["In 1952 she wed film director Roger Vadim. 1952年，她嫁給了電影導演羅傑·瓦丹。"]}]}]},"abroad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在國外，到國外；<舊>在室外，到室外；<正式> 廣為流傳，廣為人知；行動自由；<古> 未擊中目標，出錯"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外國"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>abroad</b>, you go to a foreign country, usually one that is separated from the country where you live by an ocean or a sea. 到國外","examples":["I would love to go abroad this year, perhaps to the South of France. 我今年想去國外，可能去法國南部。","He will stand in for Mr. Goh when he is abroad. 當高先生在國外時他將代行其職。"]}]}]},"widen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變寬，加寬；（使）擴充套件，程度加深，範圍擴大；（尤因驚訝或恐懼而眼睛）睜大"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>widen</b> something or if it <b>widens</b>, it becomes greater in measurement from one side or edge to the other. 使變寬; 變寬","examples":["He had an operation last year to widen a heart artery. 他去年動了一次擴張心臟動脈的手術。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>widen</b> something or if it <b>widens</b>, it becomes greater in range or it affects a larger number of people or things. 擴大","examples":["U.S. prosecutors have widened a securities-fraud investigation. 美國檢察官已經擴大了一個證券欺詐案的調查範圍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a difference or gap <b>widens</b> or if something <b>widens</b> it, it becomes greater. 拉大 (不同或差距)","examples":["Wage differences in the two areas are widening. 兩個地區之間的工資差距正在拉大。"]}]}]},"alike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相似的，相像的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相似地，相同地；兩者都，同樣地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more things are <b>alike</b>, they are similar in some way. 相似的","examples":["We looked very alike. 我們長得很相像。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alike</b> means in a similar way. 相似地","examples":["They even dressed alike. 他們甚至連穿著都相像。"]}]}]},"anyhow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不管怎樣，無論如何；無關緊要；至少；接著；總之；<英>隨便地，雜亂無章地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anyhow</b> means the same as . 反正 (同)(anyway)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>anyhow</b>, you do it in a careless or untidy way. 馬虎隨便地","examples":["Her discarded books were piled up just anyhow. 她丟棄的書被胡亂地堆了起來。"]}]}]},"wake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"喚醒，醒來；喚起，激起；<愛爾蘭，美>（方）為（死者）守夜，為……守靈；警覺"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（葬禮前後的）守夜，守靈；（航行中的船等留下的）尾流，航跡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wake</b> or when someone or something <b>wakes</b> you, you become conscious again after being asleep. 醒來; 喚醒","examples":["It was cold and dark when I woke at 6:30. 我6點30分醒來時，天又冷又黑。","She went upstairs to wake Milton. 她上樓去叫醒米爾頓。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wake up</b> means the same as . 醒來; 喚醒","examples":["One morning I woke up and felt something was wrong. 一天早上我醒來時感到有些不對勁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>wake</b> of a boat or other object moving in the water is the track of waves it makes behind it as it moves through the water. (船隻或其他物體在水中前行時留下的) 尾波","examples":["Dolphins sometimes play in the wake of the boats. 海豚有時跟著船隻的尾波戲水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wake</b> is a gathering or social event that is held before or after someone's funeral. 守靈","examples":["A funeral wake was in progress. 葬禮前在守靈。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing follows <b>in the wake of</b> another, it happens after the other thing is over, often as a result of it. 緊隨…之後","examples":["The governor has enjoyed a huge surge in the polls in the wake of last week's convention. 州長在上週大會之後的民意測驗中支援率激增。"]}]}]},"anytime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"隨時；任何時候；（anytime soon，常用於否定句或疑問句）近期內；短期內；（非正式，用於回答感謝）不客氣；隨時願意效勞"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"每當；無論何時"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anytime</b> to mean a point in time that is not fixed or set. 任何時候","examples":["The college admits students anytime during the year. 這所學院在全年裡任何時間都接收學生。","He can leave anytime he wants. 他可以在任何他想要的時間離開。"]}]}]},"anyplace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"任何地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anyplace</b> means the same as . 任何地方","examples":["She didn't have anyplace to go. 她沒有任何地方可去。"]}]}]},"aloud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大聲地，出聲地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you say something, read, or laugh <b>aloud</b>, you speak or laugh so that other people can hear you. 大聲地","examples":["When we were children, our father read aloud to us. 當我們是孩子時，我們的父親大聲地朗讀給我們聽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>think aloud</b>, you express your thoughts as they occur to you, rather than thinking first and then speaking. 邊想邊說出","examples":["He really must be careful about thinking aloud. Who knew what he might say? 他真地得對自言自語小心點。誰知道他可能會說什麼？"]}]}]},"altogether":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地；總共；總之"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>altogether</b> to emphasize that something has stopped, been done, or finished completely. 完全地","examples":["When Artie stopped calling altogether, Julie found a new man. 當阿蒂徹底不再來拜訪後，朱莉又找了個男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>altogether</b> in front of an adjective or adverb to emphasize a quality that someone or something has. 全然地","examples":["The choice of language is altogether different. 語言的選擇全然不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>altogether</b> to modify a negative statement and make it less forceful. (修飾否定陳述以減輕語氣) 十分","examples":["We were not altogether sure that the comet would miss the Earth. 我們不太確定這顆彗星是否會錯過地球。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>altogether</b> to introduce a summary of what you have been saying. 總體上講","examples":["Altogether, it was a delightful town garden, peaceful and secluded. 總體來說，這是一個賞心悅目的城市花園，安靜而幽僻。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If several amounts add up to a particular amount <b>altogether</b>, that amount is their total. 總共地","examples":["Brando received eight Oscar nominations altogether. 白蘭度總共獲得了8次奧斯卡提名。"]}]}]},"wet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"溼的，潮溼的；（天氣）下雨的，多雨的；（油漆、墨水等）未乾的；（嬰幼兒或尿片）尿溼的；軟弱的，優柔寡斷的；<非正式>允許售酒的，不禁酒的；（尤指被右翼保守派認為）具有自由主義傾向的保守派的；（人） 嗜好酒的；用水（或其他液體）的；（魚）新鮮的；（輪船）易（從船首或舷側）進水的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雨，雨天（the wet）；<英>保守黨溫和派成員；溼氣，水分，液體；<英>軟弱的人，窩囊廢（含貶義）；<英，非正式>酒；<美>反禁酒者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（某物）弄溼；（尤指嬰兒或小孩子）把……尿溼；（倒入滾燙的開水）沏（茶）；變溼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>wet</b>, it is covered in water, rain, sweat, tears, or another liquid. 溼的","examples":["He toweled his wet hair. 他用毛巾將溼頭髮擦乾。","I lowered myself to the water's edge, getting my feet wet. 我俯下身子靠近水邊，把雙腳弄溼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the weather is <b>wet</b>, it is raining. 下雨的","examples":["If the weather is wet or cold choose an indoor activity. 如果下雨或是天氣寒冷，就選擇室內活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as paint, ink, or cement is <b>wet</b>, it is not yet dry or solid. (油漆、墨水、水泥等) 未乾的","examples":["...leaves dipped in wet paint then pressed on white paper. …浸上未乾的油漆然後又按壓在白紙上的樹葉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>wet</b> something means to get water or some other liquid over it. 弄溼","examples":["When assembling the pie, wet the edges where the two crusts join. 包餡兒餅的時候，要把兩張餡餅皮捏合的地方弄溼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people, especially children, <b>wet</b> their beds or clothes or <b>wet</b> themselves, they urinate in their beds or in their clothes because they cannot stop themselves. (尤指孩子) 尿溼","examples":["A quarter of 4-year-olds frequently wet the bed. 4歲的孩子中有1/4經常性尿床。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The wet</b> is used to mean wet weather. 雨天","examples":["They had come in from the cold and the wet. 他們從寒冷又下著雨的外面走了進來。"]}]}]},"anywhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在任何地方；無論何處"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"任何地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anywhere</b> in statements with negative meaning to indicate that a place does not exist. 任何地方 (用於含有否定意義的陳述句中)","examples":["I haven't got anywhere to live. 我沒有任何地方住。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>anywhere</b> in questions and conditional clauses to ask or talk about a place without saying exactly where you mean. 某個地方 (用於疑問句或條件從句中)","examples":["Did you try to get help from anywhere? 你有沒有試著從某個地方獲得幫助？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>anywhere</b> before words that indicate the kind of place you are talking about. 任何…的地方","examples":["He'll meet you anywhere you want. 他會在任何你希望的地點見你。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>anywhere</b> to refer to a place when you are emphasizing that it could be any of a large number of places. 任何一個地方","examples":["...jokes that are so funny they always work anywhere. …如此有趣以致在哪裡都奏效的笑話。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you do not want to be exact, you use <b>anywhere</b> to refer to a particular range of things. (某範圍內的) 任何地方","examples":["His shoes cost anywhere from $200 up. 他的鞋價錢在$200以上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>anywhere</b> in expressions such as <b>anywhere near</b> and <b>anywhere close to</b> to emphasize a statement that you are making. 任何 (接近…的) 地方","examples":["There weren't anywhere near enough empty boxes. 根本沒有足夠的空盒子。"]}]}]},"anyway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不管怎樣，無論如何；而且，加之；儘管，即使這樣；對了，好吧（用於轉換話題或回到前一個話題）；（用於表明某事不重要）反正；至少；總之；（表示有意結束談話）那麼；究竟，到底；噢，啊（用於結束談話或離開）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous point. 反正 (用以表示某陳述解釋或支撐前一觀點)","examples":["I'm certain David's told you his business troubles. Anyway, it's no secret that he owes money. 我肯定戴維已經告訴了你他生意上的麻煩。反正他欠錢不是什麼秘密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to suggest that a statement is true or relevant in spite of other things that have been said. 不管怎樣 (用以表示某陳述是事實)","examples":["I don't know why I settled on Miami, but anyway I did. 我不知道為什麼我落戶到了邁阿密，但不管怎樣我做了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to correct or modify a statement, for example, to limit it to what you definitely know to be true. 用以糾正或限定某陳述","examples":["Mary Ann doesn't want to have children. Not right now, anyway. 瑪麗·安不想要孩子。至少眼下不要。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to indicate that you are asking what the real situation is or what the real reason for something is. 究竟","examples":["What do you want from me, anyway? 你究竟想從我這兒得到什麼？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to indicate that you are leaving out some details in a story and are passing on to the next main point or event. 如此這般之後 (用以表示略掉一些細節進入下一要點或事件)","examples":["I was told to go to Denver for this interview. It was a very amusing affair. Anyhow, I got the job. 我被告知去丹佛參加這個面試。那是件非常有意思的事。如此這般之後，我得到了這份工作。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to change the topic or return to a previous topic. 用以轉換話題或回到先前的話題","examples":["\"I've got a terrible cold.\"—\"Have you? Oh dear. Anyway, so you're not going to go away this weekend?\" “我得了重感冒。”—“是嗎？哦，真是的。如此的話，你這個週末就不走了吧？”"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>anyway</b> or <b>anyhow</b> to indicate that you want to end the conversation. 好了 (用以表示想結束對話)","examples":["\"Anyway, I'd better let you have your dinner. Bye.\" “好了，我最好讓你吃晚餐了。再見！”"]}]}]},"forwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（主要用於英式英語）向前，朝前方；今後，向將來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（forward 的複數）前鋒，鋒線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（forward 的第三人稱單數）轉寄，轉發；促進，推進"}],"sections":[]},"backwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向後；倒轉，相反；（時間上）回溯；倒退，每況愈下"}],"sections":[]},"backward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"向後的，朝後的；倒退的；落後的；遲鈍的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向後，朝後（=backwards）；反向地，逆向地（=backwards）；向過去（=backwards）；倒退地，退步地（=backwards）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"後面（或過去）的部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>backward</b> movement or look is in the direction that your back is facing. 向後的","examples":["He unlocked the door of apartment two and disappeared inside after a backward glance at Larry. 他開啟2號公寓的門鎖，向後瞥了拉里一眼之後走進去就不見了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone takes a <b>backward</b> step or a step <b>backward</b>, they do something that does not change or improve their situation, but causes them to go back a stage. 退步的","examples":["The current U.S. farm bill, however, is a big step backward. 然而，目前的美國農業法卻倒退了一大步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>backward</b> country or society does not have modern industries and machines. 落後的","examples":["We need to accelerate the pace of change in our backward country. 我們需要在我們這個落後的國家加快變革的步伐。。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>backward</b> child has difficulty in learning. (後進的) 學習","examples":["...research into teaching techniques to help backward children. …對幫助後進生的教學技巧的研究。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move or look <b>backward</b>, you move or look in the direction that your back is facing. 向後","examples":["The diver flipped over backward into the water. 跳水運動員向後翻轉跳入水中。","He took two steps backward. 他往後退了兩步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>backward</b>, you do it in the opposite way to the usual way. 倒著地","examples":["He works backward, building a house from the top downward. 他倒著幹活，從上往下蓋房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>backward</b> to indicate that something changes or develops in a way that is not an improvement, but is a return to old ideas or methods. 倒退地","examples":["This country is going backward. 這個國家正在倒退。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something moves <b>backward and forward</b>, they move repeatedly first in one direction and then in the opposite direction. 來回地","examples":["Using a gentle, sawing motion, draw the floss backward and forward between the teeth. 用輕柔的拉鋸的動作把牙線在牙齒間來回拉動。"]}]}]},"especially":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"尤其，特別；專門，特地；在很大程度上，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>especially</b> to emphasize that what you are saying applies more to one person, thing, time, or area than to any others. 特別是 (用於強調所指內容更適合)","examples":["Millions of wild flowers colour the valleys, especially in April and May. 成千上萬的野花使峽谷五彩斑斕，特別是在四五月份。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>especially</b> to emphasize a characteristic or quality. 尤其 (用於強調某種特質)","examples":["Babies lose heat much faster than adults, and are especially vulnerable to the cold in their first month. 嬰兒比成人散熱快得多，在出生第一個月裡尤其易受寒。"]}]}]},"increasingly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"越來越多地，不斷增加地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>increasingly</b> to indicate that a situation or quality is becoming greater in intensity or more common. 漸增地","examples":["He was finding it increasingly difficult to make decisions. 他發現決策越來越困難了。","The U.S. has increasingly relied on Japanese capital. 美國越來越依賴日本資本。"]}]}]},"cheap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"便宜的，廉價的；價低質劣的；小氣的，吝嗇的；卑劣的，可恥的；無足輕重的；簡單的，容易獲取的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"低價地，便宜地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Goods or services that are <b>cheap</b> cost less money than usual or than you expected. 便宜的","examples":["I'm going to live off campus if I can find somewhere cheap enough. 如果我能找到一個足夠便宜的地方，我打算住在校外。","Operating costs are coming down because of cheaper fuel. 經營成本在下降是因為燃料更便宜了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe goods as <b>cheap</b>, you mean they cost less money than similar products but their quality is poor. 價廉質劣的","examples":["Don't resort to cheap imitations; save up for the real thing. 不要買價廉質劣的贗品，把錢存起來買真貨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's remarks or actions as <b>cheap</b>, you mean that they are unkindly or insincerely using a situation to benefit themselves or to harm someone else. 損人利己的","examples":["These tests will inevitably be used by politicians to make cheap political points. 這些測試難免會被政客們利用以炮製損人利己的政治觀點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>cheap</b>, you are criticizing them for being unwilling to spend money. 小氣的","examples":["Oh, please, Dad, just this once don't be cheap. 哦，求求你，爸爸，就這一次，別小氣嘛。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"便宜地","examples":["It will produce electricity more cheaply than a nuclear plant. 它將以比核電廠更低廉的成本生產電力。"]}]}]},"further":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"更遠地，再往前地；進一步；此外，而且"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"更多的，進一步的；（距離上）更遠的，較遠的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"促進，推進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Further</b> means to a greater extent or degree. 在更大程度上","examples":["Inflation is below 5% and set to fall further. 通貨膨脹率低於5%，而且開始進一步下降。","The rebellion is expected to further damage the country's image. 該叛亂預計會進一步損害該國的形象。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go or get <b>further</b> <b>with</b> something, or take something <b>further</b>, you make some progress. 更進一步地","examples":["They lacked the scientific personnel to develop the technical apparatus much further. 他們缺少進一步研發這些技術裝置的科技人員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone goes <b>further</b> in a discussion, they make a more extreme statement or deal with a point more thoroughly. 更深入地","examples":["To have a better comparison, we need to go further and address such issues as repairs and insurance. 為了有一個更好的比較，我們需要更深入一步談談諸如維修和保險等問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Further</b> means a greater distance than before or than something else. 更遠地","examples":["People are living further away from their jobs. 人們住得離工作地點更遠了。","He came to a halt at a crossroads fifty yards further on. 他在50碼遠的十字路口停了下來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Further</b> is used in expressions such as \"<b>further back</b>\" and \"<b>further ahead</b>\" to refer to a point in time that is earlier or later than the time you are talking about. (時間上往前或往後) 更遠地","examples":["Looking still further ahead, by the end of the next century world population is expected to be about ten billion. 再往遠看，到下個世紀末，世界人口預期達到一百億左右。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>further</b> thing, number of things, or amount of something is an additional thing, number of things, or amount. 更多的","examples":["Further evidence of slowing economic growth is likely to emerge this week. 更多有關在減慢的經濟增長的證據本週可能出現。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>further</b> something, you help it to progress, to be successful, or to be achieved. 推進","examples":["Education needn't only be about furthering your career. 教育不必只是與推進你的事業有關。"]}]}]},"hardly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"幾乎不，幾乎沒有；剛剛，才；幾乎無法；差不多，大約；<古>嚴厲的，苛刻的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>hardly</b> to modify a statement when you want to emphasize that it is only a small amount or detail which makes it true, and that therefore it is best to consider the opposite statement as being true. 幾乎不","examples":["I hardly know you. 我幾乎不瞭解你。","I've hardly slept in three days. 我3天之中幾乎沒睡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>hardly</b> in expressions such as <b>hardly ever</b>, <b>hardly any</b>, and <b>hardly anyone</b> to mean almost never, almost none, or almost no one. (後接)(ever)(,)(any)(,)(anyone)(等表示) 幾乎從不","examples":["We hardly ever eat fish. 我們幾乎從不吃魚。","Most of the others were so young they had hardly any experience. 其他人中的大部分都太年輕，幾乎沒任何經驗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>hardly</b> before a negative statement in order to emphasize that something is usually true or usually happens. 幾乎沒有 (後接否定，表肯定)","examples":["Hardly a day goes by without a visit from someone. 幾乎沒有哪一天沒有來訪者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you say you can <b>hardly</b> do something, you are emphasizing that it is very difficult for you to do it. 很難地","examples":["My garden was covered with so many butterflies that I could hardly see the flowers. 我的花園裡飛滿了太多的蝴蝶，我幾乎看不到花了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>hardly</b> to mean \"not\" when you want to suggest that you are expecting your listener or reader to agree with your comment. 很難","examples":["We have not seen the letter, so we can hardly comment on it. 我們沒見過那封信，所以很難對其加以評論。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use \"<b>hardly</b>\" to mean \"no,\" especially when you want to express surprise or annoyance at a statement that you disagree with. 不可能","examples":["\"They all thought you were marvellous!\"—\"Well, hardly.\" “他們都覺得你真是太棒了！”—“喔，哪裡哪裡。”"]}]}]},"however":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"然而，可是，不過；無論如何；（用於表示驚訝）究竟怎樣；……左右，……上下"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"不管怎樣，無論如何；然而，可是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>however</b> when you are adding a comment which is surprising or which contrasts with what has just been said. 然而 (用以引出令人吃驚或形成對比的話語)","examples":["This was not an easy decision. It is, however, a decision that we feel is dictated by our duty. 這可不是一個輕鬆的決定。不過我們覺得我們有責任做出這樣的的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>however</b> before an adjective or adverb to emphasize that the degree or extent of something cannot change a situation. 不管多麼 (用於形容詞或副詞前表強調)","examples":["You should always strive to achieve more, however well you have done before. 不管以前做得多麼好，你應該始終爭取更大的進步。","However hard she tried, nothing seemed to work. 無論她多麼努力，好像都無濟於事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>however</b> in expressions such as <b>or however long it takes</b> and <b>or however many there were</b> to indicate that the figure you have just mentioned may not be accurate. 無論多久 (表示剛提到的數字不一定準確); 不管多少","examples":["Wait 30 to 60 minutes or however long it takes. 等30到60分鐘，或需要的不管多長的時間。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>however</b> when you want to say that it makes no difference how something is done. 不管用什麼方法 (用以表示沒有區別)","examples":["However we adopt healthcare reform, it isn't going to save major amounts of money. 不管我們採取什麼樣的醫療改革措施，它都不會節省太多的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>however</b> to ask in an emphatic way how something has happened which you are very surprised about. Some speakers of English think that this form is incorrect and prefer to use \"how ever.\" 究竟如何","examples":["However did you find this place in such weather? 在這樣的天氣裡你究竟是怎麼找到這個地方的？"]}]}]},"nearby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"附近的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在附近"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>nearby</b>, it is only a short distance away. 在附近","examples":["He might easily have been seen by someone who lived nearby. 他可能很容易被住在附近的人看到。","The helicopter crashed to earth nearby. 直升機墜毀在附近的地面上。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nearby</b> is also an adjective. 附近的","examples":["At a nearby table a man was complaining in a loud voice. 附近的一張餐桌旁一個男子在高聲抱怨著。"]}]}]},"firm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公司，商行；（以顧問醫師為首的）醫務小組；<英，非正式>（敵視敵對球隊球迷的）球迷俱樂部，球迷聯盟"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"結實的，堅硬的；牢固的，穩固的；堅定的，堅決的；強有力的；牢牢掌控的；堅挺的；確切的，可靠的；嚴厲的，強硬的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使強壯，使堅實；堅挺，穩步上漲；敲定"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"堅定地，堅決地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>firm</b> is an organization which sells or produces something or which provides a service which people pay for. 公司","examples":["The firm's employees were expecting large bonuses. 這家公司的僱員們正期待著大筆的獎金。","...a legal assistant at a Chicago law firm. …一家芝加哥律師事務所的一名法律助理。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>firm</b>, it does not change much in shape when it is pressed but is not completely hard. 結實的","examples":["Fruit should be firm and in excellent condition. 水果應該硬實且完好無損。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's grip is <b>firm</b> or if they perform a physical action in a <b>firm</b> way, they do it with quite a lot of force or pressure but also in a controlled way. 強有力的","examples":["The quick handshake was firm and cool. 那次迅速的握手有力而冷靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>firm</b>, you mean they behave in a way that shows that they are not going to change their mind, or that they are the person who is in control. 堅定的","examples":["She had to be firm with him. \"I don't want to see you again.\" 她不得不堅定地對他說：“我再也不想見到你。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>firm</b> decision or opinion is definite and unlikely to change. 確定的","examples":["He made a firm decision to leave Fort Multry by boat. 他作出了明確的決定，要乘船離開穆爾特里堡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Firm</b> evidence or information is based on facts and so is likely to be true. 確鑿的; 確切的","examples":["This man may have killed others but unfortunately we have no firm evidence. 這名男子可能還殺過別的人，只可惜我們沒有確鑿的證據。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>firm</b> to describe control or a basis or position when it is strong and unlikely to be ended or removed. (控制) 牢固的; (根基等) 穩固的","examples":["Although the Yakutians are a minority, they have firm control of the territory. 雖然雅庫特人是少數，但他們卻牢牢地控制著這個地區。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something is <b>firm</b>, it does not shake or move when you put weight or pressure on it, because it is strongly made or securely fastened. 穩固的","examples":["If you have to climb up, use a firm platform or a sturdy ladder. 如果你必須爬上去，就用一個穩固的平臺或者一個結實的梯子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"強有力地","examples":["She held me firmly by the elbow and led me to my aisle seat. 她使勁抓著我的胳膊肘，把我領到靠過道的座位上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"堅定地","examples":["\"A good night's sleep is what you want,\" he said firmly. “好好睡上一晚才是你需要的，”他堅定地說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"確定地","examples":["Political values and opinions are firmly held, and can be slow to change. 政治價值觀和主張是根深蒂固的，要改變可能會很慢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"牢固地; 穩固地","examples":["This tradition is also firmly rooted in the past. 這個傳統也牢固地植根於過去。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"穩固地","examples":["The front door is locked and all the windows are firmly shut. 前門被鎖，所有的窗戶都關得牢牢地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>stands firm</b>, they refuse to change their mind about something. 立場堅定","examples":["The council is standing firm against the protest. 市政會對抗議毫不讓步。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make or become firm 使堅固; 確實","examples":[]}]}]},"overseas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外國的，海外的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在國外，在海外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>overseas</b> to describe things that involve or are in foreign countries, usually across a sea or an ocean. 海外的","examples":["He has returned to South Africa from his long overseas trip. 他結束了漫長的海外旅行回到了南非。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>overseas</b> student or visitor comes from a foreign country, usually across a sea or an ocean. 海外的","examples":["Every year nine million overseas visitors come to the city. 每年有900萬的海外遊客來到這座城市。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overseas</b> is also an adverb. 在海外","examples":["If you're staying for more than three months or working overseas, a full 10-year passport is required. 如果你在海外居留超過3個月或工作，須持有效期整10年的護照。"]}]}]},"nearly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"幾乎，差不多；密切地，親密地；即將，就要"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nearly</b> is used to indicate that something is not quite the case, or not completely the case. 幾乎","examples":["Goldsworth stared at me in silence for nearly twenty seconds. 戈茲沃斯默默盯著我有差不多20秒鐘。","Hunter knew nearly all of this already. 亨特幾乎知道這事的全部了。","The beach was nearly empty. 海灘幾乎是空蕩蕩的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Nearly</b> is used to indicate that something will soon be the case. 即將","examples":["It was already nearly eight o'clock. 已經快8點鐘了。","I was nearly asleep. 我快睡著了。","I've nearly finished the words for your song. 我快要完成為你那首歌填詞了。"]}]}]},"none":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"全無"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"毫無，絕不（none the）；（與 too 加形容詞或副詞連用）絕不"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"申初經（天主教七段祈禱時間中的一部分，通常在一天中的第九個小時 下午3點）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>None of</b> something means not even a small amount of it. <b>None of</b> a group of people or things means not even one of them. 沒有任何","examples":["None of us knew how to treat her. 我們中沒有任何人知道該如何對待她。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"否定不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>None</b> is also a pronoun. 沒有任何人; 沒有任何事物","examples":["I searched bookstores and libraries for information, but found none. 我查詢了多家書店和圖書館，但沒查到任何資訊。","No one could imagine a great woman painter. None had existed yet. 沒人能想像會有出色的女畫家。還沒有那樣的人存在過。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>will have none of</b> something, or <b>is having none of</b> something, you mean that they refuse to accept it. 不接受","examples":["He knew his own mind and was having none of their attempts to keep him at home. 他知道自己想要什麼，不會接受他們要把他留在家裡的企圖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>none too</b> in front of an adjective or adverb in order to emphasize that the quality mentioned is not present. 毫不","examples":["He was none too thrilled to hear from me at that hour. 他在那個時刻接到我的電話不太高興。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>none the</b> to say that someone or something does not have any more of a particular quality than they did before. 一點也不比以前… (表示某原有特質沒有增)","examples":["You could end up none the wiser about managing your finances. 你最終可能一點兒也不會比以前更會理財。"]}]}]},"therefore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"因此，所以"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>therefore</b> to introduce a logical result or conclusion. 因此","examples":["Muscle cells need lots of fuel and therefore burn lots of calories. 肌肉細胞需要很多“燃料”，並因此燃燒大量卡路里。"]}]}]},"simply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"僅僅，只，不過；簡直，的確； 簡單地，簡明地；樸素地，簡樸地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>simply</b> to emphasize that something consists of only one thing, happens for only one reason, or is done in only one way. 只不過; 僅僅","examples":["The table is simply a chipboard circle on a base. 這張桌子只不過是基座加圓形刨花板。","Most of the damage that's occurred was simply because of fallen trees. 大部分損失僅僅是因橫倒在地面的樹木造成的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>simply</b> to emphasize what you are saying. 簡直; 完全地","examples":["This sort of increase simply cannot be justified. 這種增長完全沒有道理。"]}]}]},"besides":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除……之外（還）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"而且，再說；此外，也"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Besides</b> something or <b>beside</b> something means in addition to it. 除了","examples":["I think she has many good qualities besides being very beautiful. 我覺得她除了非常漂亮之外，還有許多好的品質。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Besides</b> is also an adverb. 此外","examples":["You get to sample lots of baked things and take home masses of cookies besides. 你可以品嚐許多烘烤食品，此外還能帶許多餅乾回家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Besides</b> is used to emphasize an additional point that you are making, especially one that you consider to be important. 而且","examples":["The house was out of our price range and too big anyway. Besides, I'd grown fond of our little rented house. 反正這個房子超出了我們的預算範圍，而且也太大了。再說，我已經漸漸喜歡上我們租的小房子了。"]}]}]},"per":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"每，每一；按照，根據；<古>經；（紋章）依……的方向"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每，每個"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"人（person）；時期（period）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>per</b> to express rates and ratios. For example, if something costs $50 <b>per</b> year, you must pay $50 each year for it. If a vehicle is travelling at 40 miles <b>per</b> hour, it travels 40 miles each hour. 每","examples":["...$6 per week for lunch. …每週$6吃午飯。"]}]}]},"rather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"頗，相當；寧願，最好（would rather）；而不是；更確切地說；（用以使表達的語氣婉轉）有幾分，有點兒；恰恰相反，而是"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英，舊>當然，的確（表同意）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>rather than</b> when you are contrasting two things or situations. <b>Rather than</b> introduces the thing or situation that is not true or that you do not want. 而不是","examples":["The problem was psychological rather than physiological. 這是個心理而不是生理問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>would rather</b> do something or you<b>'d rather</b> do it, you mean that you would prefer to do it. If you say that you <b>would rather not</b> do something, you mean that you do not want to do it. 寧願/寧願不","examples":["If it's all the same to you, I'd rather work at home. 如果對你來說都一樣，我寧願在家工作。","Kids would rather play than study. 孩子們寧願玩而不願學習。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rather</b> is also a conjunction. 而不是","examples":["She made students think for themselves, rather than telling them what to think. 她讓學生們自己思考，而不是告訴他們思考什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>rather</b> when you are correcting something that you have just said, especially when you are describing a particular situation after saying what it is not. (尤指修正上文時) 更確切地說","examples":["Twenty million years ago, Idaho was not the arid place it is now. Rather, it was warm and damp, populated by dense primordial forest. 2000萬年前，愛達荷州不像現在這樣乾旱。確切地說，它那時溫暖潮溼，生長著茂密的原始森林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>rather</b> to indicate that something is true to a fairly great extent, especially when you are talking about something unpleasant or undesirable. (尤指談論令人不快的事時) 相當地","examples":["I grew up in rather unusual circumstances. 我在相當不尋常的環境中長大。","I'm afraid it's a rather long story. 我恐怕這是個相當長的故事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>rather</b> before verbs that introduce your thoughts and feelings, in order to express your opinion politely, especially when a different opinion has been expressed. (尤指有禮貌地表達相反意見) 或多或少地","examples":["I rather think he was telling the truth. 我或多或少地相信他在說真話。"]}]}]},"throughout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"遍及，到處；自始至終，貫穿整個時期"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"遍及，到處；自始至終，貫穿整個時期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>throughout</b> a particular period of time, you mean that it happens during the whole of that period. 自始至終","examples":["The national tragedy of rival groups killing each other continued throughout 1990. 1990年全年，敵對組織互相殘殺的民族悲劇持續不斷。","Movie music can be made memorable because its themes are repeated throughout the film. 電影音樂可以製作得令人難忘，因為其主旋律在影片中反覆出現。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens or exists <b>throughout</b> a place, you mean that it happens or exists in all parts of that place. 遍及","examples":["\"Sight Savers,\" founded in 1950, now runs projects throughout Africa, the Caribbean and Southeast Asia. 國際防盲救盲組織成立於1950年，如今在非洲、加勒比海和東南亞各地區開展專案。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Throughout</b> is also an adverb. 自始至終","examples":["The first song, \"Blue Moon,\" didn't go too badly except that everyone talked throughout. 第一首歌《藍月亮》效果還不算太差，只是所有的人自始至終都在說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Throughout</b> is also an adverb. 到處","examples":["The route is well sign-posted throughout. 這條路線全程設有路標。"]}]}]},"beyond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（或向）……較遠的一邊；晚於，遲於；涵蓋，包括；除……之外；超出（範圍）；非（某人）所能理解"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在另一邊，在（或向）更遠處；（延續）到……之後"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"來生，再世（the beyond）；遠處的事物（the beyond）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>beyond</b> a place or barrier, it is on the other side of it. 在…的另一邊","examples":["On his right was a thriving vegetable garden and beyond it a small orchard of apple trees. 在他的右邊是一片長勢旺盛的菜園，另一頭是一小片蘋果樹林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>beyond</b> a particular time or date, it continues after that time or date has passed. (時間) 在…之後","examples":["Few jockeys continue race-riding beyond the age of 40. 很少有騎師在40歲以後還繼續賽馬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something extends <b>beyond</b> a particular thing, it affects or includes other things. 超出","examples":["His interests extended beyond the fine arts to international politics and philosophy. 他的興趣不僅限於美術，還包括國際政治和哲學。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>beyond</b> to introduce an exception to what you are saying. 除了","examples":["He appears to have almost no personal staff, beyond a secretary who can't make coffee. 他看來似乎沒有任何僱員，除了一個連咖啡都不會煮的秘書。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something goes <b>beyond</b> a particular point or stage, it progresses or increases so that it passes that point or stage. 超過","examples":["Their five-year relationship was strained beyond breaking point. 他們長達5年的關係緊張得超過了極限。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something is, for example, <b>beyond</b> understanding or <b>beyond</b> belief, it is so extreme in some way that it cannot be understood or believed. 超出 (理解或信任的範圍)","examples":["What Jock had done was beyond my comprehension. 喬克的所作所為讓我摸不著頭腦。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>beyond</b> someone, or <b>beyond</b> their control, you mean that they cannot deal with it. 超出 (能力所及)","examples":["The situation was beyond her control. 局勢非她所能控制。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beyond</b> is also an adverb. 在…的另一邊","examples":["The house had a fabulous view out to the Strait of Georgia and the Rockies beyond. 這座房子有很棒的景觀，可以看到喬治亞海峽以及另一頭的落基山脈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Beyond</b> is also an adverb. (時間) 在…之後","examples":["The financing of home ownership will continue through the 1990s and beyond. 房屋產權的融資將持續到20世紀90年代及以後。"]}]}]},"upon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……上；用在一些動詞後，與 on 同義；一……即……，一……就……；（用於兩個相同的名詞之間，強調數量之多）（一個）接（一個），……又……；將要發生，馬上來臨"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在上面地；此後"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>upon</b> another, it is on it. 在…上","examples":["He set the tray upon the table. 他把盤子放在桌上。","He bent forward and laid a kiss softly upon her forehead. 他俯下身，在她的前額溫柔地吻了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>upon</b> when mentioning an event that is followed immediately by another event. 一…就","examples":["The door on the left, upon entering the church, leads to the Crypt of St. Issac. 一進入教堂,左側的門就通往聖以撒之墓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>upon</b> between two occurrences of the same noun in order to say that there are large numbers of the thing mentioned. …又…","examples":["Row upon row of women surged forwards. 一排又一排的婦女向前湧去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an event is <b>upon</b> you, it is just about to happen. 即將發生","examples":["The long-threatened storm was upon us. 那場預示已久的暴風雨即將來臨。","The wedding season is upon us. 婚禮旺季即將來臨。"]}]}]},"somewhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在某處；到某處"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"某個地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>somewhere</b> to refer to a place without saying exactly where you mean. 某處","examples":["I've got a feeling I've seen him before somewhere. 我有一種感覺，我以前在某個地方見過他。","I'm not going home yet. I have to go somewhere else first. 我還不會回家。我得先去別的地方。","I needed somewhere to live. 我需要某個住的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>somewhere</b> when giving an approximate amount, number, or time. 大約","examples":["He is believed to be worth somewhere between seven million and ten million dollars. 據說他身價約在700萬到1000萬美元之間。","Caray is somewhere between 73 and 80 years of age. 凱瑞大約在73歲到80歲之間。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>are getting somewhere</b>, you mean that you are making progress toward achieving something. 有些進展","examples":["At last they were agreeing, at last they were getting somewhere. 最終他們取得了一致，最終他們取得了一些進展。"]}]}]},"wherever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"無論在哪裡，在任何地方；在任何情況下；不知在哪裡，不知在什麼地方"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"究竟在哪兒（用在疑問句句首，表示驚訝）；無論在哪裡，無論去哪裡；隨便什麼地方，無所謂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>wherever</b> to indicate that something happens or is true in any place or situation. 無論哪裡","examples":["Some people enjoy themselves wherever they are. 有些人無論在哪裡都很開心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>wherever</b> when you indicate that you do not know where a person or place is. 不管哪裡 (表示不知道在哪裡)","examples":["I'd like to leave as soon as possible and join my children, wherever they are. 我想盡快離開這裡，去和我的孩子們團聚，不管他們在哪裡。"]}]},{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>wherever</b> in questions as an emphatic form of \"where,\" usually when you are surprised about something. 究竟在哪裡 (在疑問句中作為where的強調形式，通常表示對某事感到吃驚)","examples":["Wherever did you get that idea? 你究竟從哪得來的那個想法？"]}]}]},"although":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"雖然，儘管；但是，然而"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>although</b> to introduce a subordinate clause which contains a statement that contrasts with the statement in the main clause. 儘管","examples":["Although he is known to only a few, his reputation among them is very great. 儘管只有幾個人知道他，但是他在他們之中的名聲很大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>although</b> to introduce a subordinate clause which contains a statement that makes the main clause of the sentence seem surprising or unexpected. 雖然","examples":["Although I was only six, I can remember seeing it on TV. 雖然當時我只有6歲，我還能記得在電視上看見過它。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>although</b> to introduce a subordinate clause which gives some information that is relevant to the main clause but modifies the strength of that statement. 雖然","examples":["He was in love with her, although a man seldom puts that name to what he feels. 他愛上了她，雖然一個男人很少用這個詞來形容他的感受。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>although</b> when admitting a fact about something that you regard as less important than a contrasting fact. 儘管","examples":["Although they're expensive, they last forever and never go out of style. 儘管它們貴，它們永遠耐用並且永不過時。"]}]}]},"within":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（某段時間）之內；在……限度內；在（某段距離）內；在（某區域或空間）裡；在（群體或組織）內部；在自己內心，在心靈深處；接近，誤差不到……"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在裡面，在內部；在內心深處，在思想上；在（某段時間）之內；（距離）在……之內；（某個地方）之內；在（群體或組織）內部；在……範圍內，在……限度內；誤差不到……"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"裡面，內部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>within</b> a place, area, or object, it is inside it or surrounded by it. 在…裡","examples":["Clients are entertained within private dining rooms. 客戶們在私人餐廳裡受到款待。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that happens or exists <b>within</b> a society, organization, or system, happens or exists inside it. 在 (社會、組織或體系) 中","examples":["...the spirit of self-sacrifice within an army. …軍隊裡的自我犧牲精神。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>within</b> a particular limit or set of rules, it does not go beyond it or is not more than what is allowed. 在 (某一限制或規則) 之內","examples":["Troops have agreed to stay within specific boundaries to avoid confrontations. 部隊已同意駐紮在特定地界內，以避免衝突。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>within</b> a particular distance of a place, you are less than that distance from it. 在 (一定距離) 之內","examples":["The man was within a few feet of him. 那名男子離他只有幾英尺。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Within</b> a particular length of time means before that length of time has passed. 在 (一定時間) 之內","examples":["About 40% of all students entering as freshmen graduate within 4 years. 所有新入學的學生中大約有40%在4年內畢業。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something is <b>within sight</b>, <b>within earshot</b>, or <b>within reach</b>, you can see it, hear it, or reach it. 在 (視線、聽力、手臂所及的範圍) 之內","examples":["His twenty-five-foot boat was moored within sight of his house. 他那隻25英尺長的小船停在他房子的視野範圍之內。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Within</b> is also an adverb. 在裡面","examples":["A small voice called from within. \"Yes, just coming.\" 從裡面傳出一個很小的聲音：“是的，就來了。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Within</b> is also an adverb. 在內部","examples":["The real dangers to these rebels came from within. 對於這些叛亂分子真正的危險來自內部。"]}]}]},"without":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"沒有，缺乏；不使用，不借助；在沒有（發生或做某事）的情況下；沒有，不帶（某種感情）；不和……在一起，無……相伴；在外面，在外部"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"沒有，缺乏；在外面"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"<古>（方）不那樣的話；除非，如果不"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外部，外面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>without</b> to indicate that someone or something does not have or use the thing mentioned. 沒有","examples":["I don't like myself without a beard. 我不喜歡自己一根鬍子沒有。","She wore a brown shirt pressed without a wrinkle. 她穿了一件熨得沒有一絲皺褶的棕色襯衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing happens <b>without</b> another thing, or if you do something <b>without</b> doing something else, the second thing does not happen or occur. 沒有","examples":["He was offered a generous pension provided he left without a fuss. 只要他毫無怨言地離開，他就會得到一筆豐厚的退休金。","They worked without a break until about eight in the evening. 他們不停地工作到大約晚上8點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>without</b> a particular feeling, you do not have that feeling when you do it. 沒有 (某種感覺)","examples":["Janet Magnusson watched his approach without enthusiasm. 珍尼特·馬格努森毫無熱情地看著他走近。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do something <b>without</b> someone else, they are not in the same place as you are or are not involved in the same action as you. 無 (某人) 在場","examples":["I told Franklin he would have to start dinner without me. 我告訴富蘭克林他得撇下我開飯了。"]}]}]},"neither":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"兩者都不"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（兩者中）無一個"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"既不……（也不……）；也不（用於否定句後，表示前句適用於所有提到的人或物）；也不（用於否定句後，強調要引出另一否定句）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（否定的陳述同樣適用於其他人或物）也不；（否定的陳述適用於兩方面）既不……也不……"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兩者都不的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>neither</b> in front of the first of two or more words or expressions when you are linking two or more things which are not true or do not happen. The other thing is introduced by \"nor.\" 既不… (也不…)","examples":["Professor Hisamatsu spoke neither English nor German. 久松教授既不講英語，也不講德語。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one person or thing does not do something and <b>neither</b> does another, what you say is true of all the people or things that you are mentioning. 也不 (用於否定句後，表示前句適用於所有提到的人或物)","examples":["I never learned to swim and neither did they. 我從沒學過游泳，他們也沒學過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>neither</b> after a negative statement to emphasize that you are introducing another negative statement. 也不 (用於否定句後，強調要引出另一否定句)","examples":["I can't ever recall Dad hugging me. Neither did I sit on his knee. 我記不得爸爸擁抱過我，也不曾在他膝上坐過。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>neither</b> to refer to each of two things or people, when you are making a negative statement that includes both of them. 兩者都不","examples":["At first, neither man could speak. 開始兩個人都不能說。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neither</b> is also a quantifier. 兩者都不","examples":["Neither of us felt like going out. 我們兩個都不願意出去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"否定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neither</b> is also a pronoun. 兩者都不","examples":["They both smiled; neither seemed likely to be aware of my absence for long. 他們兩個人都笑了，看來都沒意識到我離開了很長時間。"]}]}]},"absence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺席，缺勤，不在；缺乏，沒有；缺席期間，休假期間；不注意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>absence</b> from a place is the fact that they are not there. 缺席","examples":["...a bundle of letters which had arrived for me in my absence. …我不在的時候寄給我的一捆信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>absence</b> of something from a place is the fact that it is not there or does not exist. 不存在","examples":["The presence or absence of clouds can have an important impact on temperature. 雲的有無對氣溫會產生重要影響。"]}]}]},"ability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能力，能夠；才能，技能，本領"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ability</b> <b>to</b> do something is the fact that you can do it. 能力","examples":["The public never had faith in his ability to handle the job. 公眾從來都不相信他有處理這個工作的能力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>ability</b> is the quality or skill that you have which makes it possible for you to do something. 才能","examples":["Her drama teacher spotted her ability. 她的戲劇老師發現了她的才能。","Does the school cater to all abilities? 這所學校滿足各水平才能的人嗎?"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>to the best of</b> your <b>abilities</b> or <b>to the best of</b> your <b>ability</b>, you do it as well as you can. 盡某人所能","examples":["I take care of them to the best of my abilities. 我盡全力照顧他們。"]}]}]},"through":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"穿過，從一端到另一端；透過（玻璃、窗戶等）；越過（地區或空間），在……之間；斷開，洞穿；（在應停處）徑直透過；以，憑藉；貫穿，遍及；自始至終，從頭至尾；<美>直至；徹底地（檢視或檢查）；經歷，度過；勝利完成；（提議、觀點）獲得透過，得到批准"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"從一端到另一端；完全地，徹底地，十足地；接通電話；透過（障礙、階段或測試）；直達，逕直；從頭至尾；到（某個階段或某種程度）；切斷， 鑿穿；勝利完成"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完成的，結束的；直達的，直通的，中途不停的；斷絕的；（公路）對穿的，雙向的；（房間）與樓兩對面通透的；（競賽隊，競技者）進入下一輪（比賽）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To move <b>through</b> something such as a hole, opening, or pipe means to move directly from one side or end of it to the other. 穿過","examples":["The theatre was evacuated when rain poured through the roof. 雨水從屋頂灌下來，劇院就被撤空了。","Go straight through that door under the EXIT sign. 直著穿過那道上方有“安全出口”字樣的門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To cut <b>through</b> something means to cut it in two pieces or to make a hole in it. (切) 開; (鑽) 透","examples":["Use a genuine fish knife and fork if possible as they are designed to cut through the flesh but not the bones. 如果可能的話，使用一副真正的魚刀和魚叉，因為它們是專門設計用來切魚肉而非魚骨的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To go <b>through</b> a town, area, or country means to travel across it or in it. 穿越 (城鎮、地區或國家)","examples":["Go through North Carolina and into Virginia. 穿越北卡羅來納州進入弗吉尼亞州。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you move <b>through</b> a group of things or a mass of something, it is on either side of you or all around you. 穿過 (人群或物體)","examples":["We made our way through the crowd to the river. 我們穿過人群來到河邊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To get <b>through</b> a barrier or obstacle means to get from one side of it to the other. 越過 (障礙)","examples":["Allow twenty-five minutes to get through passport control and customs. 留出25分鐘透過護照檢查處和海關。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a driver goes <b>through</b> a red light, they keep driving even though they should stop. 闖 (紅燈)","examples":["He was killed at an intersection by a driver who went through a red light. 他在十字路口被一個闖紅燈的司機撞死了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something goes into an object and comes out of the other side, you can say that it passes <b>through</b> the object. 穿過 (物體內部)","examples":["The ends of the net pass through a wooden bar at each end. 這張網的兩端各穿著一根木棒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To go <b>through</b> a system means to move around it or to pass from one end of it to the other. 透過 (系統)","examples":["...electric currents travelling through copper wires. …透過銅導線的電流。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you see, hear, or feel something <b>through</b> a particular thing, that thing is between you and the thing you can see, hear, or feel. 透過","examples":["Alice gazed pensively through the wet glass. 艾麗斯透過溼漉漉的玻璃若有所思地凝視著。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something such as a feeling, attitude, or quality happens <b>through</b> an area, organization, or a person's body, it happens everywhere in it or affects all of it. 貫穿; 遍佈","examples":["An atmosphere of anticipation vibrated through the crowd. 人群中充滿著期盼的氣氛。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If something happens or exists <b>through</b> a period of time, it happens or exists from the beginning until the end. 從…的開始到結束","examples":["She kept quiet all through breakfast. 她吃早餐時始終保持沉默。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If something happens from a particular period of time <b>through</b> another, it starts at the first period and continues until the end of the second period. 直至","examples":["...open Monday through Friday from 9 to 5. …週一至週五9點到5點開放。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you go <b>through</b> a particular experience or event, you experience it, and if you behave in a particular way <b>through</b> it, you behave in that way while it is happening. (以某種行動方式) 經歷","examples":["Men go through a change of life emotionally just like women. 男人就和女人一樣會在情緒上經歷更年期。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>through</b> in expressions such as <b>half-way through</b> and <b>all the way through</b> to indicate to what extent an action or task is completed. 完成","examples":["A thirty-nine-year-old competitor collapsed half-way through the marathon. 一位39歲的參賽者在馬拉松賽跑的中途癱倒了。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"If something happens because of something else, you can say that it happens <b>through</b> it. 因為","examples":["I only succeeded through hard work. 我就是因為努力工作才成功的。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>through</b> when stating the means by which a particular thing is achieved. 憑藉; 透過","examples":["Those who seek to grab power through violence deserve punishment. 那些想憑藉暴力奪取權力的人應該受到懲罰。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you do something <b>through</b> someone else, they take the necessary action for you. 經由 (某人)","examples":["Do I need to go through my doctor to get an appointment? 我需要透過我的醫生來預約嗎？"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also a preposition. 得到…的批准","examples":["They want to get the plan through Congress as quickly as possible. 他們想讓這個計劃儘快獲得國會的批准。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If someone gets <b>through</b> an examination or a round of a competition, they succeed or win. 透過 (考試); (在比賽中) 勝出","examples":["She was bright, learned languages quickly, and sailed through her exams. 她聰明伶俐，學語言很快，順利透過了各門考試。"]},{"num":"20.","zh":"If you look or go <b>through</b> a lot of things, you look at them or deal with them one after the other. 逐個 (瀏覽、處理)","examples":["Let's go through the numbers together and see if a workable deal is possible. 讓我們一起把這些數字過一遍，看能否找出一個可行的方案。"]},{"num":"21.","zh":"If you read <b>through</b> something, you read it from beginning to end. 從頭到尾 (閱讀)","examples":["She read through pages and pages of the music I had brought her. 她一頁一頁地翻看我帶給她的樂譜。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 穿過","examples":["There was a hole in the wall and water was seeping through. 牆上有個洞，水正滲出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. (切) 開; (鑽) 透","examples":["Score lightly at first and then repeat, scoring deeper each time until the board is cut through. 先輕輕地劃一下，然後反覆劃，一次比一次劃得深些，直到木板被完全割開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 穿越","examples":["Few know that the tribe was just passing through. 幾乎沒人知道這個部落只是路過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 穿過","examples":["He pushed his way through to the edge of the crowd where he waited. 他擠到人群邊上，在那裡等候。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 越過","examples":["...a maze of concrete and steel barriers, designed to prevent vehicles driving straight through. …為防止車輛直接透過而設計的迷宮式鋼筋混凝土障礙物。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 穿過","examples":["I bored a hole so that the bolt would pass through. 我鑽了一個孔，這樣門閂就能穿過去。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 透過","examples":["Food should be allowed to go through immediately with fewer restrictions. 食品應允許快速流通，少受限制。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 自始至終","examples":["We'll be working right through to the summer. 我們會一直工作到夏季。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 完成","examples":["Stir the pork until it turns white all the way through. 攪拌豬肉直到完全變白為止。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something such as a proposal or idea goes <b>through</b>, it is accepted by people in authority and is made legal or official. (提議或想法等) 得到批准","examples":["We're waiting for the building permit to go through. 我們在等著工程許可證獲得批准。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 成功地","examples":["Only the top four teams go through. 僅4個頂尖隊伍勝出。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"When you get <b>through</b> while making a telephone call, the call is connected and you can speak to the person you are phoning. (電話) 接通","examples":["Telephones are down so he can't get through. 電話出了故障，所以他打不通。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"<b>Through</b> is also an adverb. 從頭到尾","examples":["The article had been authored by Raymond Kennedy. He read it right through, looking for any scrap of information that might have passed him by. 這篇文章是由雷蒙德·肯尼迪寫的。他從頭一直讀到尾，尋找任何可能遺漏的點滴資訊。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is wet <b>through</b>, you are emphasizing how wet they are. (溼) 透","examples":["I returned to the inn cold and wet, soaked through by the drizzling rain. 我回到那家小客棧，被毛毛雨淋透了，又冷又溼。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>through</b> <b>with</b> something or if it is <b>through</b>, you have finished doing it. 完成的","examples":["We're through with dinner. 我們吃完飯了。","Are you through with this? 你完成這個了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>through</b> <b>with</b> someone, you do not want to have anything to do with them again. 斷絕關係的","examples":["I'm through with her; she's bad news! 我和她斷絕關係了；她是個討厭鬼！"]}]}]},"addition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"增加物，新增人員；增加；加法；（建築物的）擴建部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in addition</b> when you want to mention another item connected with the subject you are discussing. 另外","examples":["The web site provides regional weather reports, a shipping forecast and gale warnings. In addition, visitors can download satellite images of the U.S. 這個網站提供地區天氣報道、出航預測和大風警報。另外，訪客可以下載美國的衛星影象。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>addition</b> <b>to</b> something is a thing which is added to it. 新增物","examples":["This is a fine book; a worthy addition to the series. 這是一本好書——是對這套叢書有價值的增補。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b> addition</b> is a new room or building which is added to an existing building or group of buildings. 擴建部分","examples":["The couple said they spent $20,000 on building an addition to their kitchen. 這對夫妻說他們花了2萬美元擴建他們的廚房。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>addition</b> <b>of</b> something is the fact that it is added to something else. 增添部分","examples":["It was completely refurbished in 1987, with the addition of a picnic site. 它於1987年被完全翻修，增添了一個野餐場所。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Addition</b> is the process of calculating the total of two or more numbers. 加法","examples":["...simple addition and subtraction problems using whole numbers. …運用整數的簡單加法和減法題。"]}]}]},"aircraft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飛機，航空器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>aircraft</b> is a vehicle that can fly, for example, an aeroplane or a helicopter. 飛機","examples":["The return flight of the aircraft was delayed. 飛機的返回航程被推遲了。"]}]}]},"airline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"航空公司；輸氣管（air line）；航線"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"航線的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>airline</b> is a company that provides regular services carrying people or goods in aeroplanes. 航空公司","examples":["...the world's largest discount airline. …世界上最大的折扣航空公司。"]}]}]},"whenever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"無論何時，無論什麼情況；每當；什麼時間都行；不知什麼時候"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"究竟什麼時候；不論何時，隨便什麼時候"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whenever</b> to refer to any time or every time that something happens or is true. 無論什麼時候","examples":["Whenever I talked to him, he seemed like a pretty regular guy. 我無論什麼時候同他講話，他都好像是個很正常的人。","You can stay at my cottage in the country whenever you like. 只要你願意，無論什麼時候都可以住在我鄉下的小屋裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>whenever</b> to refer to a time that you do not know or are not sure about. 什麼時候 (表示不知道或不確定的時間)","examples":["He married Miss Vancouver in 1963, or whenever it was. 他在1963年或什麼時候娶了溫哥華小姐。"]}]}]},"affair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公共事務，政治事務；事情，事件；個人的事，私事；私人業務；（尤指已婚男女的）私通，風流韻事；社交活動，喜慶事；<舊> 物件，東西；商務和金融交易"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event or a series of events has been mentioned and you want to talk about it again, you can refer to it as <b>the affair</b>. 事件","examples":["The administration has mishandled the whole affair. 政府錯誤地處理了整個事件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an important or interesting event or situation as \"<b>the</b> ... <b>affair</b>.\" (…) 事件","examples":["...the damage caused to the CIA and FBI in the aftermath of the Watergate affair. …水門事件過後對中情局和美國聯幫調查局造成的損害。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe the main quality of an event by saying that it is a particular kind of <b>affair</b>. (某種性質的) 事","examples":["Michael said that his planned 10-day visit would be a purely private affair. 邁克爾說他計劃的10天的訪問將是一件純粹私事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If two people who are not married to each other have an <b>affair</b>, they have a sexual relationship. 不正當關係","examples":["Married male supervisors were carrying on affairs with female subordinates in the office. 已婚男上司和辦公室裡的女下級在搞不正當關係。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>affairs</b> to refer to all the important facts or activities that are connected with a particular subject. (有關某話題的) 事務","examples":["He does not want to interfere in the internal affairs of another country. 他不想幹涉他國的內部事務。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Your <b>affairs</b> are all the matters connected with your life that you consider to be private and normally deal with yourself. (個人的) 事情","examples":["The unexpectedness of my father's death meant that his affairs were not entirely in order. 我父親的意外過世意味著他的個人事情不是完全有序。"]}]}]},"album":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"唱片，專輯；相簿，影集，集郵冊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>album</b> is a collection of songs that is available on a CD, record, or cassette. 唱片專輯","examples":["Chris likes music and has a large collection of albums and cassettes. 克里斯喜歡音樂，並且收藏了大量的唱片和磁帶。","Oasis release their new album on July 1. 綠洲樂隊將於7月1日發行他們的新專輯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>album</b> is a book in which you keep things such as photographs or stamps that you have collected. (收存照片或郵票的) 冊子","examples":["Theresa showed me her photo album. 特雷莎給我看了她的相簿。"]}]}]},"aim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目標，目的；瞄準，對準；槍法，擊中目標的能力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"瞄準，對準；旨在，致力於；針對，指向"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>aim</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>aim</b> <b>to</b> do something, you plan or hope to achieve it. 以…為目標","examples":["He said he would aim for the 100 metre world record at the world championships in August. 他說他將以在8月舉行的世界錦標賽上打破100米世界紀錄為目標。","Businesses will have to aim at long-term growth. 企業必須以長期增長為目標。","The programme aims to educate and prepare students for a challenging career. 這個專案旨在教育學生使其為一個具有挑戰性的職業做好準備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>aim</b> <b>to</b> do something, you decide or want to do it. 打算","examples":["I didn't aim to get caught. 我並不想被抓到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your actions or remarks <b>are aimed</b> <b>at</b> a particular person or group, you intend that the person or group should notice them and be influenced by them. 針對","examples":["His message was aimed at the undecided middle ground of Israeli politics. 他所傳達的資訊針對的是以色列政壇中尚未表態的中間派。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>aim</b> a weapon or object <b>at</b> something or someone, you point it toward them before firing or throwing it. 對…瞄準","examples":["When he appeared again, he was aiming the rifle at Wade. 他再次出現時，他正將步槍瞄準維德。","...a missile aimed at the arms factory. …一枚瞄準了軍工廠的導彈。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>aim</b> a kick or punch at someone, you try to kick or punch them. 對準","examples":["They set on him, punching him in the face and aiming kicks at his shins. 他們襲擊了他，猛打他的臉，並對準他的脛骨猛踢。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an action or plan <b>is aimed</b> <b>at</b> achieving something, it is intended or planned to achieve it. 旨在","examples":["The new measures are aimed at tightening existing sanctions. 這些新措施旨在加強現行的制裁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>aim</b> of something that you do is the purpose for which you do it or the result that it is intended to achieve. 目的","examples":["The aim of the festival is to increase awareness of Hindu culture and traditions. 這個慶祝活動的目的是增強人們對印度文化和傳統的認識。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>aim</b> is your skill or action in pointing a weapon or other object at its target. 瞄準","examples":["He stood with the gun gripped in his right hand and his left hand steadying his aim. 他站著用右手緊握住槍，用左手把穩瞄準。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>take aim</b>, you point a weapon or object at someone or something, before firing or throwing it. 瞄準","examples":["She had spotted a man with a shotgun taking aim. 她看見了一個正在用手持獵槍瞄準的男子。"]}]}]},"aid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幫助；援助，救助；輔助物，輔助設施；助手；特別津貼，國庫稅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"幫助，援助；促進，有助於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aid</b> is money, equipment, or services that are provided for people, countries, or organizations who need them but cannot provide them for themselves. 援助","examples":["...regular flights carrying humanitarian aid to Cambodia. …向柬埔寨運送人道主義援助的定期班機。","They have already pledged billions of dollars in aid. 他們已經承諾了數十億美元的援助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you perform a task <b>with the</b> <b>aid</b> <b>of</b> something, you need or use that thing to perform that task. 幫助","examples":["He succeeded with the aid of a completely new method he discovered. 藉助於一個他所發現的全新方法，他取得了成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Aid</b> is also a noun. 幫助","examples":["He was forced to turn for aid to his former enemy. 他被迫向他以前的敵人尋求幫助。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>aid</b> is an object, device, or technique that makes something easier to do. 輔助工具","examples":["The book is an invaluable aid to teachers of literature. 這本書對文學教師是一個非常有用的輔助工具。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>aid</b> a country, organization, or person means to provide them with money, equipment, or services that they need. 援助","examples":["...U.S. efforts to aid Kurdish refugees. …美國援助庫爾德難民的努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>aid</b> someone means to help or assist them. 幫助","examples":["...a software system to aid managers in advanced decision-making. …一個幫助經理們做高階決策的軟體系統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>aids</b> a process, it makes it easier or more likely to happen. 促使; 有助於 (事情發生)","examples":["The survey suggests that the export sector will continue to aid the economic recovery. 該調查表明出口產業將繼續促進經濟復甦。","Calcium may aid in the prevention of colon cancer. 鈣可能有助於預防結腸癌。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"援助的","examples":["...government-aided research. …政府援助的研究。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>come</b> or <b>go to</b> someone's <b>aid</b>, you try to help them when they are in danger or difficulty. 向某人提供幫助","examples":["Dr. Fox went to the aid of the dying man despite having been injured in the crash. 儘管他自己在撞車事故中也受了傷，福克斯醫生仍然去救助那個奄奄一息的男子。"]}]}]},"almond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"杏仁， 扁桃仁；杏樹，扁桃樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Almonds</b> are pale oval nuts. They are often used in cooking. 杏仁","examples":["...sponge cake flavoured with almonds. …帶杏仁味的鬆糕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>almond</b> or an <b>almond tree</b> is a tree on which almonds grow. 杏樹","examples":["On the left was a plantation of almond trees. 在左邊曾是一個杏樹種植園。"]}]}]},"alarm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"警報；警報器；鬧鐘；驚恐，擔憂"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使不安，使恐慌；給（門等）安裝警報器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alarm</b> is a feeling of fear or anxiety that something unpleasant or dangerous might happen. 驚恐","examples":["The news was greeted with alarm by senators. 參議員們聽到這個訊息後很驚恐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>alarm</b> is an automatic device that warns you of danger, for example, by ringing a bell. 警報器","examples":["He heard the alarm go off. 他聽見警報器響了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>alarm</b> is the same as an . 鬧鐘","examples":["Dad set the alarm for eight the next day. 爸爸把鬧鐘設到了第2天8點。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>alarms</b> you, it makes you afraid or anxious that something unpleasant or dangerous might happen. 使驚恐","examples":["We could not see what had alarmed him. 我們不明白是什麼嚇著他了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something sets <b>alarm bells</b> ringing, you mean that it makes people feel worried or concerned about something. 危險訊號","examples":["This has set the alarm bells ringing in Moscow. 這已給莫斯科拉響了警報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>raise the alarm</b> or <b>sound the alarm</b>, you warn people of danger. 發出警報","examples":["His family raised the alarm when he had not come home by 9 p.m. 當他到晚上9點還沒回家時，他的家人報了警。"]}]}]},"alphabet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"字母表；基本要素；初步，入門"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alphabet</b> is a set of letters usually presented in a fixed order which is used for writing the words of a particular language or group of languages. 字母表","examples":["The modern Russian alphabet has 31 letters. 現代俄語字母表有31個字母。"]}]}]},"ankle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳踝，踝關節"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>走；離開；（騎腳踏車時）踝關節曲起用力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ankle</b> is the joint where your foot joins your leg. 腳踝","examples":["John twisted his ankle badly. 約翰的腳踝嚴重扭傷。"]}]}]},"advance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）前進，（使）向前移動；發展，進步；預付；提前，提早；促進，推動；提出（想法或理論）；上漲，增加；提拔，晉升"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"前進；進步，進展；改善；預付款；勾引，追求；（價格、價值的）上漲；貸款"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"預先的，事先的；先行的，先遣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>advance</b> means to move forward, often in order to attack someone. (常指為攻擊而) 前進","examples":["Reports from Chad suggest that rebel forces are advancing on the capital. 來自查德的報導指出叛軍正在向首都挺進。","According to one report, the water is advancing at a rate of between 8 and 10 inches a day. 根據一份報告，大水在以每天8至10英寸的速度逼近。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>advance</b> means to make progress, especially in your knowledge of something. (尤指知識) 發展","examples":["Medical technology has advanced considerably. 醫學技術已大大發展了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>advance</b> someone a sum of money, you lend it to them, or pay it to them earlier than arranged. 提前借 (一筆錢給某人); 提前付 (一筆錢給某人)","examples":["I advanced him some money, which he would repay on our way home. 我先借了些錢給他，他會在回家的路上還給我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>advance</b> an event, or the time or date of an event, means to bring it forward to an earlier time or date. 使提前","examples":["Too much protein in the diet may advance the aging process. 飲食中過多的蛋白質會使衰老的過程提前。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>advance</b> a cause, interest, or claim, you support it and help to make it successful. 造成; 促成","examples":["When not producing art of his own, Oliver was busy advancing the work of others. 沒有創作自己的藝術品時，奧利弗就在忙於促成他人的作品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advance</b> is money lent or paid to someone before they would normally receive it. 預付款","examples":["She was paid a $100,000 advance for her next two novels. 她得到了其接下來的兩本小說的10萬美元的預付款。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>advance</b> is a forward movement of people or vehicles, usually as part of a military operation. (常指軍事行動中的) 前進","examples":["In an exercise designed to be as real as possible, they simulated an advance on enemy positions. 在一次設計得儘可能逼真的演習中，他們模擬了一次向敵方陣地的前進。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>advance</b> in a particular subject or activity is progress in understanding it or in doing it well. (在某科目、某活動中的) 發展","examples":["Air safety has not improved since the dramatic advances of the 1970s. 飛行安全自從20世紀70年代的急劇發展以來還沒有得到改善。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is an <b>advance</b> <b>on</b> what was previously available or done, it is better in some way. 改善","examples":["This could be an advance on the present situation. 這可能是對目前情況的一次改善。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Advance</b> booking, notice, or warning is done or given before an event happens. 事先的 (預定、通知、警告等)","examples":["They don't normally give any advance notice about which building they're going to inspect. 他們對要視察哪座大樓通常不作事先通知。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in advance</b>, you do it before a particular date or event. 提前","examples":["The subject of the talk is announced a week in advance. 會談的主題提前一週宣佈。"]}]}]},"apartment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公寓套房；（總統等要人的）房間，套間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apartment</b> is a separate set of rooms for living in, in a house or a building with other apartments. 公寓","examples":["Christina has her own apartment, with her own car. 克里斯蒂娜有她自己的公寓，有自己的車。"]}]}]},"appetite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"食慾，胃口；慾望，愛好"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>appetite</b> is your desire to eat. 胃口","examples":["He has a healthy appetite. 他有健康的胃口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>appetite</b> <b>for</b> something is their strong desire for it. 慾望","examples":["...his appetite for success. …他的成功慾望。"]}]}]},"amount":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"數量，量；金額，錢數；（感情、質量的）程度"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"達到，總計（amount to）；等於，意味著（amount to）；發展成，變成（amount to）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>amount</b> <b>of</b> something is how much there is, or how much you have, need, or get. 數量","examples":["He needs that amount of money to survive. 他需要那筆錢來維持生活。","I still do a certain amount of work for them. 我仍舊為他們做一定數量的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>amounts</b> <b>to</b> a particular total, all the parts of it add up to that total. 總計","examples":["Consumer spending on sports-related items amounted to $9.75 billion. 消費者在體育相關用品上的消費總共達到了97.5億美元。"]}]}]},"apron":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圍裙；舞臺前緣，臺唇；停機坪"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"著圍裙於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apron</b> is a piece of clothing that you put on over the front of your normal clothes and tie around your waist, especially when you are cooking, in order to prevent your clothes from getting dirty. 圍裙","examples":[]}]}]},"armchair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"扶手椅，單人沙發"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"空想的，無實際經驗的；誇誇其談的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>armchair</b> is a big comfortable chair that has a support on each side for your arms. 扶手椅","examples":["She was sitting in an armchair with blankets wrapped around her. 她當時正裹著毯子坐在一把扶手椅裡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>armchair</b> critic, fan, or traveller knows about a particular subject from reading or hearing about it rather than from practical experience. 足不出戶的","examples":["This great book is ideal for both the travelling supporter and the armchair fan. 這本了不起的書對於旅行的和足不出戶的支持者們都是理想的。"]}]}]},"argument":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爭論，爭吵；論據，理由；辯論，討論；自變數；主詞，受詞；<古>書的內容提要"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>argument</b> is a statement or set of statements that you use in order to try to convince people that your opinion about something is correct. 論據","examples":["There's a strong argument for lowering the price. 有一個支援降低價格的有力論據。","The doctors have set out their arguments against the proposals. 醫生們已經說明了反對這些提案的理由。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>argument</b> is a discussion or debate in which a number of people put forward different or opposing opinions. 討論; 辯論","examples":["The incident has triggered fresh arguments about the role of the extreme right in U.S. politics. 該事件引發了有關美國政治中極右勢力角色的新討論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>argument</b> is a conversation in which people disagree with each other angrily or noisily. 爭吵","examples":["Anny described how she got into an argument with one of the marchers. 安妮描述了她是如何與遊行者中的一個人爭吵起來的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you accept something without <b>argument</b>, you do not question it or disagree with it. 爭辯","examples":["He complied without argument. 他沒有爭辯就服從了。"]}]}]},"appearance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"露面，演出；出庭，到場；外表，外觀；表面現象，假象；出現；起源，問世；表現；出版，廣播"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone makes an <b>appearance</b> at a public event or in a broadcast, they take part in it. (在公共活動或廣播中的) 露面","examples":["It was the president's second public appearance to date. 這是迄今該總統的第二次公開露面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>appearance</b> is the way that they look. 外表; 外觀","examples":["She used to be so fussy about her appearance. 她過去過分在意自己的外表。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>appearance</b> <b>of</b> someone or something in a place is their arrival there, especially when it is unexpected. (尤指出人意料的) 出現","examples":["The sudden appearance of a few bags of rice could start a riot. 幾袋大米的突然出現會引起一場騷亂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>appearance</b> <b>of</b> something new is its coming into existence or use. 問世","examples":["Flowering plants were making their first appearance, but were still a rarity. 有花植物初現，但是依然少見。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something has the <b>appearance</b> <b>of</b> a quality, it seems to have that quality. 表象","examples":["We tried to meet both children's needs without the appearance of favouritism or unfairness. 我們試圖在沒有偏愛或不公平的表象下滿足兩個孩子的需要。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is true <b>by all appearances</b>, <b>from all appearances</b>, or <b>to all appearances</b>, it seems from what you observe or know about it that it is true. 從一切表象來看","examples":["He was a small and by all appearances an unassuming man. 他是個個子小並且從一切表象看來不裝腔作勢的人。"]}]}]},"arrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"箭，矢；箭頭，箭號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>arrow</b> is a long thin weapon that is sharp and pointed at one end and that often has feathers at the other end. An arrow is shot from a bow. 箭","examples":["Warriors armed with bows and arrows and spears have invaded their villages. 佩有弓箭和長矛的武士們已入侵了他們的村莊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>arrow</b> is a written or printed sign that consists of a straight line with another line bent at a sharp angle at one end. This is a printed arrow: →. The arrow points in a particular direction to indicate where something is. 箭頭","examples":["A series of arrows points the way to the modest grave of Andrei Sakharov. 一系列箭頭指示著通往簡樸的安德烈·薩哈羅夫之墓的路。"]}]}]},"arrangement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"安排，籌備；商定，約定；整理，排列，佈置；改編"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Arrangements</b> are plans and preparations that you make so that something will happen or be possible. 安排","examples":["The staff is working frantically on final arrangements for the summit. 工作人員在緊張忙碌地為該峰會做最後的安排。","She telephoned Ellen, but made no arrangements to see her. 她給埃倫打了電話，但沒安排見她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>arrangement</b> is an agreement that you make with someone to do something. 商定","examples":["The caves can be visited only by prior arrangement. 這些洞穴只能預約參觀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>arrangement</b> of things, for example, flowers or furniture, is a group of them displayed in a particular way. 佈置","examples":["The house was always decorated with imaginative flower arrangements. 該房子那時經常裝飾著富有創意的插花。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone makes an <b>arrangement</b> of a piece of music, they change it so that it is suitable for particular voices or instruments, or for a particular performance. (樂曲的) 改編","examples":["...an arrangement of a well-known piece by Mozart. …對莫扎特的一首名曲的改編。"]}]}]},"baby-sitter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臨時保姆，代人臨時照看小孩者"}],"sections":[]},"assistant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"助理，助手；店員，售貨員"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"助理的，副的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Assistant</b> is used in front of titles or jobs to indicate a slightly lower rank. For example, an assistant director is one rank lower than a director in an organization. 助理的 (用在頭銜或職位前，表示級別略低)","examples":["...the assistant secretary of defence. …助理國防部長。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>assistant</b> is a person who helps them in their work. 助理","examples":["Kalan called his assistant, Hashim, to take over while he went out. 卡蘭打電話給他的助理哈什姆以在他外出時接管。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>assistant</b> is a person who works in a shop selling things to customers. 售貨員","examples":["The assistant took the book and checked the price on the back cover. 售貨員拿起書，核對了封底上的價格。"]}]}]},"bakery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵包店；烘焙食品（如麵包，蛋糕）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bakery</b> is a building where bread, pastries, and cakes are baked, or the shop where they are sold. 麵包房; 麵包店","examples":["A smell of bread drifted from some distant bakery. 一股麵包的味道從遠處的某個麵包店飄來。"]}]}]},"attention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"注意；注意力；照料；興趣；立正；殷勤，關心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone or something your <b>attention</b>, you look at it, listen to it, or think about it carefully. 注意力","examples":["You have my undivided attention. 我全部的注意力都在你身上。","Later he turned his attention to the desperate state of housing in the city. 後來他把注意力轉向了該市極為嚴重的住房狀況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Attention</b> is great interest that is shown in someone or something, particularly by the general public. (尤指公眾的) 關注","examples":["Volume Two, subtitled \"The Lawyers,\" will also attract considerable attention. 副標題為《律師》的第2卷也將會引起極大的關注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is getting <b>attention</b>, they are being dealt with or cared for. 照料","examples":["Each year more than two million household injuries need medical attention. 每年有二百多萬起在家受傷、需要醫療救治的案例。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>bring</b> something <b>to</b> someone's <b>attention</b> or <b>draw</b> their <b>attention</b> <b>to</b> it, you tell them about it or make them notice it. (引起某人) 注意","examples":["If we don't keep bringing this to the attention of the people, nothing will be done. 如果我們無法讓公眾保持對此事的關注，那就將一事無成。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>attracts</b> your <b>attention</b> or <b>catches</b> your <b>attention</b>, you suddenly notice them. 突然引起某人的注意","examples":["A faint aroma of coffee attracted his attention. 一股淡淡的咖啡香味吸引了他的注意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pay attention</b> <b>to</b> someone, you watch them, listen to them, or take notice of them. If you <b>pay no attention</b> <b>to</b> someone, you behave as if you are not aware of them or as if they are not important. 注意","examples":["More than ever before, the food industry is paying attention to young consumers. 現在，食品業比以往任何時候都更加關注年輕的消費者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people <b>stand at attention</b>, they stand straight with their feet together and their arms at their sides. 立正","examples":["Soldiers in full combat gear stood at attention. 全副武裝計程車兵們立正站著。"]}]}]},"artist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藝術家，美術家；表演藝術家；大師，行家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>artist</b> is someone who draws or paints pictures or creates sculptures as a job or a hobby. 美術家","examples":["...the studio of a great artist. …一位偉大美術家的工作室。","Each poster is signed by the artist. 每張海報都由這位美術家簽了名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>artist</b> is a person who creates novels, poems, films, or other things which can be considered as works of art. 文學藝術家","examples":["His books are enormously easy to read, yet he is a serious artist. 他的書極易讀，然而他卻是一位嚴肅的文學藝術家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>artist</b> is a performer such as a musician, actor, or dancer. 表演藝術家","examples":["...a popular artist who has sold millions of records. …一位賣了上百萬張唱片的、受人歡迎的表演藝術家。"]}]}]},"bamboo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"竹，竹子；（制手杖或傢俱、器具用的）竹竿，竹筒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"竹製的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bamboo</b> is a tall tropical plant with hard, hollow stems. The young shoots of the plant can be eaten and the stems are used to make furniture. 竹子","examples":["...huts with walls of bamboo. …竹牆小屋。"]}]}]},"banker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行家，銀行要員；莊家；穩贏的賭注；捕鱈漁船；水漲齊岸的河流；輔動機車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>banker</b> is someone who works in banking at a senior level. 銀行家","examples":["...an investment banker. …一位投資銀行家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an official or player in charge of the bank in any of various games, esp gambling games 莊家; 賭博遊戲中做莊家的人","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a person or thing that appears certain to win or be successful 贏家; 勢在必贏的人或物","examples":[]}]}]},"balcony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"露臺，陽臺；樓座，樓廳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>balcony</b> is a platform on the outside of a building, above ground level, with a wall or railing around it. 陽臺","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>balcony</b> in a theatre or cinema is an area of seats above the main seating area. (戲院或電影院裡的) 樓座","examples":[]}]}]},"barbecue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戶外燒烤；（戶外燒烤用的）烤肉架；燒烤食物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在烤架上）燒烤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barbecue</b> is a piece of equipment which you use for cooking on in the open air. (戶外使用的) 烤架","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has a <b>barbecue</b>, they cook food on a barbecue in the open air. 燒烤","examples":["On New Year's Eve we had a barbecue on the beach. 除夕那天我們在海灘上舉行了燒烤野餐。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>barbecue</b> food, especially meat, you cook it on a barbecue. (用烤架) 燒烤","examples":["Tuna can be grilled, fried or barbecued. 金槍魚可以烤、煎或燒烤著吃。","Here's a way of barbecuing corn-on-the-cob that I learned from my uncle. 這是我向我叔叔學的一種烤玉米棒的方法。"]}]}]},"arrest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逮捕，拘留；阻止，抑制；吸引；心跳停止"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"逮捕，拘留；停止，終止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the police <b>arrest</b> you, they take charge of you and take you to a police station, because they believe you may have committed a crime. 逮捕","examples":["Police arrested five young men in connection with one of the attacks. 警方逮捕了與其中一起襲擊事件有關的5名年輕男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>arrests</b> a process, they stop it from continuing. 抑制","examples":["The sufferer may have to make major changes in his or her life to arrest the disease. 患者可能得對自身生活作大的調整以抑制病情。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Arrest</b> is also a noun. 逮捕","examples":["...a substantial reward for information leading to the arrest of the bombers. …用於獎勵為抓捕爆炸犯提供有效資訊的一大筆賞金。","Police chased the fleeing terrorists and later made two arrests. 警方追趕逃竄的恐怖分子，後來逮捕了兩個人。"]}]}]},"basement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地下室，地庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>basement</b> of a building is a floor built partly or completely below ground level. 地下室","examples":["They bought an old schoolhouse to live in and built a workshop in the basement. 他們買了座舊校舍居住，還在地下室建了個作坊。"]}]}]},"basics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基礎，基本要素（basic 的複數），基本原理；基本生活用品，必需品；（Basics）人名（匈牙利姓氏，常譯作“鮑希奇”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>basics</b> of something are its simplest, most important elements, ideas, or principles, in contrast to more complicated or detailed ones. 基本要點","examples":["They will concentrate on teaching the basics of reading, writing and arithmetic. 他們將重點教授閱讀、寫作和算術的基本要點。","A strong community cannot be built until the basics are in place. 只有等到基本要素都已就位，一個牢固的社會才能建立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Basics</b> are things such as simple food, clothes, or equipment that people need in order to live or to deal with a particular situation. 基本生活用品","examples":["...supplies of basics such as bread and milk. …麵包、牛奶等基本食品的供給。"]}]}]},"bark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"大聲嚷，吼叫；（狗）吠，叫；擦破（脛部的）皮；剝去（樹，木頭的）皮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"狗叫聲，吠聲；吼叫聲；樹皮；小帆船，三桅帆船"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a dog <b>barks</b>, it makes a short, loud noise, once or several times. (狗) 吠","examples":["Don't let the dogs bark. 別讓狗叫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bark</b> <b>at</b> someone, you shout at them aggressively in a loud, rough voice. 咆哮","examples":["I didn't mean to bark at you. 我不是有意吼你。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bark</b> is also a noun. 吠聲","examples":["The Doberman let out a string of roaring barks. 那條杜賓犬發出一連串的吼叫聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bark</b> is the tough material that covers the outside of a tree. 樹皮","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to scrape or rub off skin, as in an injury 擦傷; 刮傷","examples":[]}]}]},"bead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（有孔的）珠子；（液體的）小滴；（槍的）圓形準星；（輪胎的）胎圈，胎邊；凸圓線腳；念珠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"綴珠狀物於；把（珠）串在一起；在（平面上）覆蓋小珠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beads</b> are small pieces of coloured glass, wood, or plastic with a hole through the middle. Beads are often put together on a piece of string or wire to make jewellery. 中間有孔的小珠子","examples":["...a string of beads. …一串珠子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bead</b> <b>of</b> liquid or moisture is a small drop of it. (液體或溼氣的) 小滴","examples":["...beads of blood. …滴滴鮮血。"]}]}]},"bedroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臥室"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兩性關係的；城郊住宅區的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bedroom</b> is a room used for sleeping in. 臥室","examples":["...the spare bedroom. …那間空臥室。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bedroom</b> <b>community</b> or <b>suburb</b> is the same as a  <b>community</b> or <b>suburb</b>. (指通勤者居住的) 臥室社群","examples":["This town is becoming a bedroom community of Columbus, 20 miles to the north. 這座小鎮正成為距此北面20英里處哥倫布市的臥室社群。"]}]}]},"attack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"批評，抨擊；侵蝕，侵害；全力應對，奮力處理；襲擊，攻擊；（體育比賽中）進攻"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（疾病的）突然發作；（情感的）一陣突發；（體育運動中的）進攻；襲擊，攻擊；批評，抨擊；進攻隊員；（病蟲等的）損害，傷害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>attack</b> a person or place means to try to hurt or damage them using physical violence. 攻擊","examples":["Fifty civilians in Masawa were killed when government planes attacked the town. 馬薩瓦50名平民在政府飛機襲擊該市時喪生。","He bundled the old lady into her hallway and brutally attacked her. 他把老太太推進她家門廳裡，並且野蠻地襲擊了她。","They found the least defended area and attacked. 他們找到了防守最薄弱的地區發動了攻擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>attack</b> a person, belief, idea, or act, you criticize them strongly. 抨擊","examples":["He publicly attacked the people who've been calling for secret ballot nominations. 他公開抨擊了那些一直要求秘密投票提名的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a disease, a chemical, or an insect <b>attacks</b> something, it harms or spoils it. (疾病、化學藥品或昆蟲等) 侵害","examples":["The virus seems to have attacked his throat. 病毒似乎已侵害到他的咽喉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>attack</b> a job or a problem, you start to deal with it in an energetic way. 積極處理","examples":["Any attempt to attack the budget problem is going to have to in some way deal with those issues. 要想妥善處理預算問題，從某方面來說必須先解決那些問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In games such as soccer, when one team <b>attacks</b> the opponent's goal, they try to score a goal. (在足球等比賽中) 進攻","examples":["Now the U.S. is controlling the ball and attacking the opponent's goal. 現在美國隊在控球，正向對方球門發起進攻。","The goal was just reward for their decision to attack constantly in the second half. 這粒進球正是他們決定在下半場連續進攻的回報。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Attack</b> is also a noun. 攻擊","examples":["...a campaign of air attacks on strategic targets. …對戰略目標的空襲行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Attack</b> is also a noun. 抨擊","examples":["The role of the state as a prime mover in planning social change has been under attack. 國家作為規劃社會變革發起者的角色已經遭到抨擊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Attack</b> is also a noun. 侵害","examples":["The virus can actually destroy those white blood cells, leaving the body wide open to attack from other infections. 該病毒實際上能破壞那些白血球，使身體極易受到其他感染。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Attack</b> is also a noun. 進攻","examples":["Lee was at the hub of some incisive attacks in the second half. 李是下半場幾次犀利進攻中的主角。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>attack</b> <b>of</b> an illness is a short period in which you suffer badly from it. (疾病急性) 發作","examples":["It had brought on an attack of asthma. 這引起了一次哮喘發作。"]}]}]},"bean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豆，菜豆，豆科植物；籽實，豆形種子；用於強調絲毫，一點；<舊>腦袋；（Bean）描述Java的軟體元件模型（Enterprise Java Bean）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用某物）擊中（某人）頭部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Beans such as green <b>beans</b>, French <b>beans</b>, or fava <b>beans</b> are the seeds of a climbing plant or the long thin cases which contain those seeds. 豆; 豆莢","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Beans such as <b>soybeans</b> and kidney <b>beans</b> are the dried seeds of other types of bean plants. 幹豆","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Beans such as coffee <b>beans</b> or cocoa <b>beans</b> are the seeds of plants that are used to produce coffee, cocoa, and chocolate. (供製作咖啡、可可等飲料的) 豆形種子","examples":[]}]}]},"beard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬍鬚，絡腮鬍子；（動物的）頷毛，須；（植物的）芒，髯毛；替身；<非正式>名義女伴"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對抗（令人畏懼的人），頂撞；抓……的鬍鬚；提供鬍鬚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A man's <b>beard</b> is the hair that grows on his chin and cheeks. 鬍鬚","examples":["He's decided to grow a beard. 他已經決定蓄鬍須。"]}]}]},"beep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（機器）嗶嗶響，嘟嘟響；（使）（汽車喇叭）鳴響；用傳呼機召喚，呼（某人）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電子裝置的）嗶嗶聲；（汽車喇叭的）嘟嘟聲；警笛聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beep</b> is a short, loud sound like that made by a car horn or a telephone answering machine. 嘟嘟聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a horn <b>beeps</b>, or you <b>beep</b> it, it makes a short, harsh sound. 發出嘟嘟聲","examples":["My cell phone beeped. 我的手機嘟嘟響了。","He beeped the horn. 他按響了喇叭。"]}]}]},"basis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基礎，要素；基準，方式；理由，根據；主要成分（或部分）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>on</b> a particular <b>basis</b>, it is done according to that method, system, or principle. 按…原則; 以…方式","examples":["We're going to be meeting there on a regular basis. 我們將定期在那兒會面。","They want all groups to be treated on an equal basis. 他們要求所有的群體都能得到平等的對待。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are acting <b>on</b> the <b>basis</b> <b>of</b> something, you are giving that as the reason for your action. 以…為由","examples":["McGregor must remain confined, on the basis of the medical reports we have received. 基於我們所收到的醫療報告，麥格雷戈必須繼續臥床休息。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>basis</b> of something is its starting point or an important part of it from which it can be further developed. 基礎","examples":["Both factions have broadly agreed that the U.N. plan is a possible basis for negotiation. 兩派已大致同意該聯合國計劃是談判的可能基礎。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>basis</b> for something is a fact or argument that you can use to prove or justify it. 依據","examples":["...Japan's attempt to secure the legal basis to send troops overseas. …日本取得派遣軍隊的法律依據的企圖。"]}]}]},"beef":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牛肉；肌肉，力量，力氣；<非正式>抱怨，牢騷；<非正式>要點，關鍵；<美，非正式>犯罪指控，罪名"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>抱怨，發牢騷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beef</b> is the meat of a cow, bull, or ox. 牛肉","examples":["...roast beef. …烤牛肉。","...beef stew. …燉牛肉。"]}]}]},"battle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰役，戰爭；爭論，鬥爭；競賽，較量；拼搏，奮鬥"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與……作戰，和……鬥爭；搏鬥，奮鬥；爭吵，爭論；阻止，打敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>battle</b> is a violent fight between groups of people, especially one between military forces during a war. 戰役","examples":["...the victory of King William III at the Battle of the Boyne. …威廉三世國王在博因河戰役中所取得的勝利。","...a gun battle between police and drug traffickers. …警察和毒品販子之間的一場槍戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>battle</b> is a conflict in which different people or groups compete in order to achieve success or control. 鬥爭; 較量","examples":["...an unfolding political battle over jobs and the economy. …一場正在展開的關於就業和經濟的政治較量。","...the eternal battle between good and evil in the world. …世界上善惡之間永無休止的較量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>battle</b> to refer to someone's efforts to achieve something in spite of very difficult circumstances. 鬥爭","examples":["...the battle against crime. …制止犯罪的鬥爭。","She has fought a constant battle with her weight. 她一直在和自己的體重作鬥爭。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>battle</b> <b>with</b> an opposing group means to take part in a fight or contest against them. You can also say that one group or person <b>is battling</b> another. 與…搏鬥; 與…較量","examples":["In one town thousands of people battled with police and several were reportedly wounded. 在一個鎮子裡，成千上萬的人同警察展開搏鬥，據報道有幾人受傷。","The sides must battle again for a quarter-final place on December 16. 兩隊必須於12月16日再戰一次，來爭奪1/4決賽的位置。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>battle</b> means to try hard to do something in spite of very difficult circumstances. You can also <b>battle</b> something, or <b>battle</b> <b>against</b> something or <b>with</b> something. 與…作鬥爭; 鬥爭","examples":["Doctors battled throughout the night to save her life. 醫生們奮戰了整個晚上來搶救她的生命。","Firefighters are still battling the two blazes. 消防隊員們還在與兩處大火作鬥爭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one group or person <b>battles it out</b> <b>with</b> another, they take part in a fight or contest against each other until one of them wins or a definite result is reached. You can also say that two groups or two people <b>battle it out</b>. 戰鬥到底","examples":["She will now battle it out with 50 other hopefuls for a place in the last 10. 她現在將和另外50名有希望的候選人決戰最後10個位置中的一個。"]}]}]},"beer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"啤酒；一杯（或一瓶，一罐）啤酒；根汁啤酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beer</b> is an alcoholic drink made from grain. 啤酒","examples":["He sat in the kitchen drinking beer. 他坐在廚房裡喝啤酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A glass, can, or bottle of beer can be referred to as a <b>beer</b>. 一杯啤酒; 一罐啤酒; 一瓶啤酒","examples":["Would you like a beer? 你想來杯啤酒嗎？"]}]}]},"beginner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"初學者，新手，生手；（作定語）初級的，入門的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beginner</b> is someone who has just started learning to do something and cannot do it very well yet. 初學者","examples":["The course is suitable for both beginners and advanced students. 這門課程對初學者和高階學生都適合。"]}]}]},"beetle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"甲蟲；<英>畫甲蟲，拼甲蟲（一種擲骰子游戲）；大槌；捶布機；（大眾汽車公司生產的）甲殼蟲汽車（Beetle）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"匆匆地走；（人的眉毛）突出，懸垂；用大槌捶；用捶布機捶（布）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人的眉毛）粗濃而突出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beetle</b> is an insect with a hard covering to its body. 甲蟲","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a heavy hand tool, usually made of wood, used for ramming, pounding, or beating 大槌","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a game played with dice in which the players draw or assemble a beetle-shaped form 拼甲蟲(一種擲骰子的遊戲)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to scuttle or scurry; hurry 急促地跑","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to overhang; jut 突出","examples":[]}]}]},"blackboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黑板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blackboard</b> is a dark-coloured board that you can write on with chalk. Blackboards are often used by teachers in the classroom. 黑板","examples":["The menu was on a blackboard. 選單在黑板上。"]}]}]},"belief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"相信，信心；看法，信念，觀點；信仰，信條"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Belief</b> is a feeling of certainty that something exists, is true, or is good. 信仰","examples":["One billion people throughout the world are Muslims, united by belief in one god. 全世界有10億人是穆斯林，因為對一位神靈的信仰而團結在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your religious or political <b>beliefs</b> are your views on religious or political matters. (宗教或政治的) 觀念","examples":["He refuses to compete on Sundays because of his religious beliefs. 由於他的宗教觀念，他拒絕星期天進行比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If it is your <b>belief</b> that something is the case, it is your strong opinion that it is the case. 堅定的信念","examples":["It is our belief that improvements in health care will lead to a stronger, more prosperous economy. 我們堅定的信念是衛生保健的改善會帶來更加茁壯、繁榮的經濟。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>beyond belief</b> to emphasize that something is true to a very great degree or that it happened to a very great degree. 難以置信","examples":["We are devastated, shocked beyond belief. 我們遭到了挫敗，震驚得難以置信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>in the belief that</b> another thing is true or will happen, you do it because you think, usually wrongly, that it is true or will happen. (通常錯誤地) 相信","examples":["Civilians had broken into the building, apparently in the belief that it contained food. 老百姓已闖入這棟大樓，很明顯他們錯誤地相信這兒有食物。"]}]}]},"bench":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長凳，長椅；長方形工作臺；法官席（the bench）； 議員席；替補席；（磚石建築的）壁架，（斜坡上的）平臺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（場上隊員）換下；（在展覽會上）展覽（狗）；仰臥推舉；給……以席位；為……設定條凳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bench</b> is a long seat of wood or metal that two or more people can sit on. 長凳","examples":["He sat down on a park bench. 他在一條公園的長凳上坐下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bench</b> is a long, narrow table in a factory or laboratory. (工廠、實驗室的) 工作臺","examples":["...the laboratory bench. …實驗室工作臺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a court of law, <b>the bench</b> is the judge or magistrates. 法官","examples":["The chairman of the bench adjourned the case until October 27. 首席法官將該案延至到10月27日。"]}]}]},"belt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腰帶，皮帶；傳送帶；地帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用腰帶繫緊；狠打，猛擊；（尤指出於懲罰用皮帶）抽打，打擊（某人）；<非正式>飛馳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>belt</b> is a strip of leather or cloth that you fasten around your waist. 腰帶; 皮帶","examples":["He wore a belt with a large brass buckle. 他繫著一條綴有一顆大銅釦的皮帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>belt</b> in a machine is a circular strip of rubber that is used to drive moving parts or to move objects along. 輸送帶","examples":["The turning disc is connected by a drive belt to an electric motor. 轉盤與電動馬達之間由一條輸送帶連線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>belt</b> of land or sea is a long, narrow area of it that has some special feature. 狹長地帶","examples":["Miners in Zambia's northern copper belt have gone on strike. 尚比亞北部銅礦區的礦工們舉行了罷工。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Belt</b> is also a noun. 狠揍; 猛打","examples":["Father would give you a belt over the head with the scrubbing brush. 父親會拿板刷狠狠地敲你的頭。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>belts</b> you, they hit you very hard. If someone <b>belts</b> something, they hit it very hard. 狠揍; 猛打","examples":["\"Is it right she belted old George in the gut?\" she asked. “她狠揍老喬治的肚子對嗎？”她質問道。","Torrealba belted the ball into the left-field bleachers. 託雷爾巴把球猛打到左邊的看臺上。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>belt</b> somewhere, you move or travel there very fast. 飛奔","examples":["Darren and I belted down the stairs and ran out of the house. 達倫和我飛奔下樓，跑出了屋子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>below the belt</b> is cruel and unfair. 不公正的","examples":["Do you think it's a bit below the belt what they're doing? 你認為他們的所作所為有點不太公正嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have to <b>tighten</b> your <b>belt</b>, you have to spend less money and manage without things because you have less money than you used to have. 省吃儉用","examples":["Clearly, if you are spending more than your income, you'll need to tighten your belt. 很顯然，如果你現在花錢就入不敷出，以後就不得不勒緊腰帶了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have something <b>under</b> your <b>belt</b>, you have already achieved it or done it. 已成囊中之物","examples":["Clare is now a full-time author with six books, including four novels, under her belt. 克萊爾現在是個名下有6本書的專職作家，其中包括4本小說。"]}]}]},"bookcase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（傢俱）書櫃，書架，書櫥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bookcase</b> is a piece of furniture with shelves that you keep books on. 書櫥","examples":[]}]}]},"bend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"彎曲（身體關節）；（路）轉彎；歪曲（事實）；篡改；屈從；系，縛（帆，纜繩）；使彎曲，弄彎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（道路或河流的）拐彎，彎道；（身體的）彎曲（動作）；（尤指潛水員的）潛涵病，減壓病（the bends）；綁結；（紋章盾形）左上方至右下方的對角斜紋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bend</b>, you move the top part of your body downward and forward. Plants and trees also <b>bend</b>. 彎下","examples":["I bent over and kissed her cheek. 我俯身親吻了她的面頰。","She bent and picked up a plastic bucket. 她彎腰拎起一個塑膠桶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bend</b> your head, you move your head forward and downward. 低下 (頭)","examples":["Rick appeared, bending his head a little to clear the top of the door. 裡克來了，他稍稍低頭避開門框。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>bend</b> a part of your body such as your arm or leg, or when it <b>bends</b>, you change its position so that it is no longer straight. 彎曲 (身體某個部位); 彎曲","examples":["These cruel devices are designed to stop prisoners from bending their legs. 這些殘酷的刑具是設計來限制犯人彎腿的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bend</b> something that is flat or straight, you use force to make it curved or to put an angle in it. 使...彎曲","examples":["Bend the bar into a horseshoe. 把鋼條彎捲成馬蹄形。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a road, beam of light, or other long thin thing <b>bends</b>, or when something <b>bends</b> it, it changes direction to form a curve or angle. 彎向; 拐彎","examples":["The road bent slightly to the right. 公路微微向右彎。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>bend</b> rules or laws, you interpret them in a way that allows you to do something they would not normally allow you to do. 篡改; 歪曲 (規則等)","examples":["A minority of officers were prepared to bend the rules. 少數官員準備篡改規則。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"彎曲的","examples":["Keep your knees slightly bent. 保持兩膝微屈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"彎的","examples":["...a length of bent wire. ...一截彎曲的鐵絲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bend</b> in a road, pipe, or other long thin object is a curve or angle in it.  拐角","examples":["The crash occurred on a sharp bend. 碰撞發生在一個急轉彎處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If deep-sea divers suffer from <b>the</b> <b>bends</b>, they experience severe pain and difficulty in breathing as a result of coming to the surface of the ocean too quickly.  潛涵病; 呼吸減壓病","examples":["New evidence suggests that exercise could protect divers from the bends. 新證據表明鍛鍊可以防止潛水員得潛涵病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an ordinary consisting of a diagonal line traversing a shield","examples":[]}]}]},"bet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打賭，賭博；<非正式>敢肯定"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"下注；賭金；預計，猜想；<非正式>有可能成功的人選（或備選行動）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"在……之間（between）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bet</b> <b>on</b> the result of a horse race, football game, or other event, you give someone a sum of money which they give you back with extra money if the result is what you predicted, or which they keep if it is not. 對…下注; 下賭注","examples":["Jockeys are forbidden to bet on the outcome of races. 職業賽馬騎師們被禁止對比賽結果下注。","I bet $20 on a horse called Premonition. 我在那匹名叫“預言”的賽馬身上下了$20的賭注。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is betting</b> that something will happen, they are hoping or expecting that it will happen. 希望; 期待","examples":["The party is betting that the presidential race will turn into a battle for younger voters. 該黨希望這場總統競選會演變成對年輕選民的爭奪。","People were betting on a further easing of credit conditions. 人們期待信貸條件的進一步放寬。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bet</b> is also a noun. 下注","examples":["Do you always have a bet on the Kentucky Derby? 你總是在肯塔基賽馬大會上賭馬嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"賭注","examples":["...his thousand-dollar fine for illegal betting. …他因非法賭博而受的千元罰款。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bet</b> is a sum of money which you give to someone when you bet. 賭金","examples":["You can put a bet on almost anything these days. 如今，你幾乎可以就任何事下賭注。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as \"<b>I bet</b>,\" \"<b>I'll bet</b>,\" and \"<b>you can bet</b>\" to indicate that you are sure something is true. 我確信; 我敢說","examples":["I bet you were good at games when you were at school. 我敢說你上學時很擅長比賽。","I'll bet they'll taste out of this world. 我相信它們的味道一定鮮美極了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you tell someone that something is a <b>good bet</b>, you are suggesting that it is the thing or course of action that they should choose. 好的做法; 好的選擇","examples":["Your best bet is to choose a guest house. 你最好的選擇就是找一家賓館。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>a good bet</b> or <b>a safe bet</b> that something is true or will happen, you are saying that it is extremely likely to be true or to happen. 極有可能","examples":["It is a safe bet that the current owners will not sell. 現在的主人極有可能不賣了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>I bet</b> or <b>I'll bet</b> in reply to a statement to show that you agree with it or that you expected it to be true, usually when you are annoyed or amused by it. 說的是","examples":["\"I'd like to ask you something,\" I said. \"I bet you would,\" she grinned. “我想問你一件事，”我說道。“我猜你就會問的，”她笑道。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>I bet</b> or <b>I'll bet</b> in reply to a statement to show that you do not believe it or you doubt that it is true. 誰信啊","examples":["\"I only kiss girls,\" said John. Then he blushed. \"I'll bet,\" said Lisa. “我只吻女孩們，”約翰說著，臉就紅了。“誰信啊，”莉薩說。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>my bet is</b> or <b>it's my bet</b> to give your personal opinion about something, when you are fairly sure that you are right. 我認定","examples":["My bet is that next year will be different. 我確信明年將有所不同。"]}]}]},"bill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（商品、服務或餐館的）賬單；議案，法案；紙幣，鈔票；演出人員名單；廣告，傳單；票據，匯票；單子，清單；喙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開賬單；把……宣傳為；宣佈（某人）將參加演出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bill</b> is a written statement of money that you owe for goods or services. 賬單","examples":["They couldn't afford to pay the bills. 他們付不起賬。","He paid his bill for the newspapers promptly. 他立刻付了報紙的帳單。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bill</b> is a piece of paper money. 紙幣","examples":["The case contained a large quantity of U.S. dollar bills. 盒子裡裝有大量美鈔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In government, a <b>bill</b> is a formal statement of a proposed new law that is discussed and then voted on. 議案","examples":["This is the toughest crime bill that Congress has passed in a decade. 這是十年來國會透過的最強硬的有關犯罪的議案。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>bill</b> of a show or concert is a list of the entertainers who will take part in it. 演出人員名單","examples":["Bob Dylan topped the bill. 鮑勃·迪倫排在演員表的最前端。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The bill</b> in a restaurant is a piece of paper on which the price of the meal you have just eaten is written and which you are given before you pay. (餐館的) 賬單","examples":["After coffee, Gastler asked for the bill. 喝完咖啡，加斯特勒要了賬單。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"演員表","examples":["...their quarrels over star billing. …他們就演員表排名順序的爭吵。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A bird's <b>bill</b> is its beak. 喙","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bill</b> someone <b>for</b> goods or services you have provided them with, you give or send them a bill stating how much money they owe you for these goods or services. 給…開賬單","examples":["Are you going to bill me for this? 你會為這開帳單給我嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is billed</b> <b>to</b> appear in a particular show, it has been advertised that they are going to be in it. 宣傳 (某人出演某戲)","examples":["She was billed to play the Wicked Queen in \"Snow White.\" 她已被宣佈將出演《白雪公主》裡狠毒的王后。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bill</b> a person or event <b>as</b> a particular thing, you advertise them in a way that makes people think they have particular qualities or abilities. 把…宣傳為","examples":["They bill it as California's most exciting museum. 他們把這宣傳為加利福尼亞最令人激動的博物館。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>fits the bill</b> or <b>fills the bill</b>, you mean that they are suitable for a particular job or purpose. 符合要求","examples":["If you fit the bill, send a CV to Rebecca Rees. 如果你符合這些要求，送一份履歷給麗貝卡·里斯。"]}]}]},"blank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"空白的，空的；茫然的，毫無表情的；單調的，無活動的；斷然的，徹底的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"空白處，空格；（頭腦或記憶）一片空白；空彈；（金屬或木頭的）坯件，坯料"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成為空白，不記得；<英>冷落，不理睬；<美>阻止（對方）得分；切割（金屬坯件）；封鎖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>blank</b> has nothing on it. 空白的; 空的","examples":["We could put some of the pictures over on that blank wall over there. 我們可以在那邊的空牆上貼一些畫。","He tore a blank page from his notebook. 他從筆記本上撕下一頁白紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you look <b>blank</b>, your face shows no feeling, understanding, or interest. 茫然的; 無表情的; 漠然的","examples":["Abbot looked blank. \"I don't quite follow, sir.\" 阿博特一臉茫然，“我不太明白，先生。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blank</b> is a space which is left in a piece of writing or on a printed form for you to fill in particular information. (表格等的) 空白處","examples":["Put a word in each blank to complete the sentence. 在每個空格處填一個單詞完成句子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your mind or memory is <b>a blank</b>, you cannot think of anything or remember anything. (頭腦、記憶等的) 一片空白","examples":["I'm sorry, but my mind is a blank. 很抱歉，可是我腦子裡一片空白。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Blanks</b> are gun cartridges which contain explosive but do not contain a bullet, so that they cause no harm when the gun is fired. (有炸藥而無彈頭的) 空包彈","examples":["...a starter pistol which only fires blanks. …只發射空包彈的發令槍。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"茫然地; 面無表情地; 漠然地","examples":["She stared at him blankly. 她面無表情地盯著他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your mind <b>goes blank</b>, you are suddenly unable to think of anything appropriate to say, for example in reply to a question. (頭腦) 突然出現一片空白","examples":[]}]}]},"boil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）沸騰，煮沸，燒開；用開水煮；怒火中燒；（海，雲）翻騰"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"煮沸，沸騰；癤，皮下膿腫；激昂，興奮；突然浮上來食魚餌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a hot liquid <b>boils</b> or when you <b>boil</b> it, bubbles appear in it and it starts to change into steam or vapour. 使…沸騰; 沸騰","examples":["I stood in the kitchen, waiting for the water to boil. 我站在廚房裡等水開。","Boil the water in the saucepan and add the sage. 把湯鍋裡的水燒開，然後放進鼠尾草葉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>boil</b> a pot or a kettle, or put it on to <b>boil</b>, you heat the water inside it until it boils. 燒開","examples":["He had nothing to do but boil the kettle and make the tea. 他除了燒開水和沏茶以外無事可做。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>boil</b> food, or when it <b>boils</b>, it is cooked in boiling water. 煮","examples":["Boil the chick peas, add garlic and lemon juice. 把鷹嘴豆煮了，加進蒜和檸檬汁。","I'd peel potatoes and put them on to boil. 我會削土豆皮，然後把它們煮了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a pot <b>is boiling</b>, the water inside it has reached boiling point. 燒沸","examples":["The pot was boiling. 鍋裡的水燒開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are boiling</b> <b>with</b> anger, you are very angry. 發怒","examples":["I used to be all sweetness and light on the outside, but inside I would be boiling with rage. 我過去雖然表面上笑呵呵的，可是心裡卻怒火中燒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the state or action of boiling (esp in the phrases <b>on the boil, off the boil</b>) 沸騰","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>boil</b> is a red, painful swelling on your skin that contains a thick yellow liquid called pus. 癤子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bring</b> a liquid <b>to a boil</b>, you heat it until it boils. When it <b>comes to a boil</b>, it begins to boil. 燒沸/開始沸騰","examples":["Put water, butter and lard into a saucepan and bring slowly to the boil. 在湯鍋里加入水、黃油和豬油，慢慢煮開。"]}]}]},"bomb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"炸彈，爆炸裝置；失敗的東西；長傳，長傳球；大筆錢；高壓容器，噴霧器；<非正式>很好的人，很好的事；（形狀和威力）像炸彈樣的物體；<非正式>摻大麻的香菸"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"轟炸，炸燬；疾行，快速前進；<非正式>失敗；重擊（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bomb</b> is a device that explodes and damages or destroys a large area. 炸彈","examples":["Bombs went off at two London train stations. 炸彈在倫敦的兩個火車站爆炸了。","It's not known who planted the bomb. 不知是誰放置了這顆炸彈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Nuclear weapons are sometimes referred to as <b>the bomb</b>. 核武器","examples":["They are generally thought to have the bomb. 他們被普遍認為擁有核武器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"轟炸","examples":["Aerial bombing of rebel positions is continuing. 對叛軍陣地的空中轟炸仍在繼續。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>bomb</b> a place, they attack it with bombs. 轟炸","examples":["Air force jets bombed the airport. 空軍噴氣機轟炸了機場。"]}]}]},"boss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"上司，領導，領班；圓形裝飾物，浮雕裝飾；牛犢，奶牛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發號施令，對……頤指氣使；當首領"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很好的，出色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>boss</b> is the person in charge of the organization or department where you work. 老闆","examples":["He cannot stand his boss. 他受不了他的老闆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>the</b> <b>boss</b> in a group or relationship, you are the person who makes all the decisions. 頭兒","examples":["He thinks he's the boss. 他自以為是頭兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a knob, stud, or other circular rounded protuberance, esp an ornamental one on a vault, a ceiling, or a shield (穹頂、天花板等上的)圓形凸飾","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a calf or cow 牛犢; 奶牛","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to employ, supervise, or be in charge of 僱傭; 監督; 負責","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>bosses</b> you, you mean that they keep telling you what to do in a way that is irritating. 支使","examples":["We cannot boss them into doing more. 我們不能再支使他們幹其他事了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boss around</b> means the same as . 支使","examples":["He started bossing people around. 他開始支使大家了。"]}]}]},"board":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"板，木板；黑板，告示牌；董事會，理事會；膳食，伙食，膳食費用；局；<非正式>舞臺；<美>（冰球場周圍的）界牆；<舊>（美國大學的）入學考試"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"登上（火車、輪船或飛機）；讓乘客登機（或上船等）；寄宿；（在學校）住校；將（寵物）暫時寄養在他處；用木板覆蓋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>board</b> is a flat, thin, rectangular piece of wood or plastic which is used for a particular purpose. (木頭的或塑膠的) 板","examples":["...a cutting board. …一塊砧板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>board</b> is a square piece of wood or stiff cardboard that you use for playing games such as chess. (棋) 盤","examples":["...a chequers board. …一個跳棋盤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a blackboard or a bulletin board as a <b>board</b>. 黑板; 佈告欄","examples":["He wrote a few more notes on the board. 他在黑板上多寫了幾條筆記。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Boards</b> are long flat pieces of wood which are used, for example, to make floors or walls. (建築用的) 長條木板","examples":["The floor was draughty bare boards. 地板是有縫隙的裸板。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>board</b> of a company or organization is the group of people who control it and direct it. 董事會","examples":["Arthur has made a recommendation, which he wants her to put before the board at a special meeting scheduled for tomorrow afternoon. 阿瑟提了個建議，要她在明天下午擬定召開的特別會議上向董事會提出。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Board</b> is used in the names of various organizations which are involved in dealing with a particular kind of activity. 委員會; 局","examples":["The Scottish tourist board said 33,000 Japanese visited Scotland last year. 蘇格蘭旅遊局稱，33000名日本遊客去年到蘇格蘭旅遊。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Board</b> is the food which is provided when you stay somewhere, for example in a hotel. (在外住宿的) 膳食","examples":["Free room and board are provided for all hotel staff. 旅館的所有工作人員可以免費食宿。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>board</b> a train, ship, or aircraft, you get on it in order to travel somewhere. 登上 (火車、船或飛機)","examples":["I boarded the plane bound for Boston. 我登上了飛往波士頓的航班。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a policy or a situation applies <b>across the board</b>, it affects everything or everyone in a particular group. 全體地","examples":["There are hefty charges across the board for one-way rental. 對所有人的單程租都收高費。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>goes by the board</b>, it is rejected or ignored, or is no longer possible. 被拒絕; 落空","examples":["It's a case of not what you know but who you know in this world today and qualifications quite go by the board. 現在社會的情形不是看你知道什麼，而是看你認識誰，學位也基本被忽略了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you are <b>on board</b> a train, ship, or aircraft, you are on it or in it. 在 (火車、輪船或飛機) 上","examples":["All 269 people on board the plane were killed. 機上269人全部遇難。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>sweeps the board</b> in a competition or election, they win nearly everything that it is possible to win. (在比賽或選舉中) 大獲全勝","examples":["Spain swept the board in boys' team competitions. 西班牙隊在男子組的競賽中大獲全勝。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>take on board</b> an idea or a problem, you begin to accept it or understand it. 接受; 理解","examples":["You may have to accept their point of view, but hope that they will take on board some of what you have said. 你可能得接受他們的觀點，但是希望他們也會理解你講的一些話。"]}]}]},"bowling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保齡球運動；（板球）投球"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打保齡球（bowl 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bowling</b> is a game in which you roll a heavy ball down a narrow track toward a group of wooden objects and try to knock down as many of them as possible. 保齡球","examples":["I go bowling for relaxation. 我玩保齡球放鬆自己。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a sport such as cricket, <b>bowling</b> is the action or activity of bowling the ball toward the batsman. 投球","examples":["Much of the bowling today will be done by Phil Tufnell. 大多數投球今天將由菲爾·塔夫內爾完成。"]}]}]},"bother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"費心；（使）煩惱，（使）擔心；打擾，煩擾；使不舒服，使疼痛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"麻煩，不便；討厭的人（或事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do not <b>bother</b> <b>to</b> do something or if you do not <b>bother</b> <b>with</b> it, you do not do it, consider it, or use it because you think it is unnecessary or because you are too lazy. 費心","examples":["Lots of people don't bother to go through a marriage ceremony these days. 很多人如今不費心舉辦婚禮了。","Nothing I do makes any difference anyway, so why bother? 不管我做什麼都沒有區別，那為什麼還要費心去做呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>bothers</b> you, or if you <b>bother</b> about it, it worries, annoys, or upsets you. 使煩惱; 煩惱","examples":["Is something bothering you? 有什麼事讓你煩惱嗎？","It bothered me that boys weren't interested in me. 讓我煩惱的是，男孩們對我不感興趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>bothers</b> you, they talk to you when you want to be left alone or interrupt you when you are busy. 打擾","examples":["We are playing a trick on a man who keeps bothering me. 我們正在捉弄那個總是打攪我們的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bother</b> means trouble or difficulty. You can also use <b>bother</b> to refer to an activity which causes this, especially when you would prefer not to do it or get involved with it. 麻煩","examples":["I usually buy sliced bread – it's less bother. 我通常買切片面包–這樣可以少些麻煩。","The courts take too long and going to the police is a bother. 庭審太費時間，去警察局是件麻煩事。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"煩惱的","examples":["I was bothered about the blister on my hand. 我為手上的水皰感到很心煩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>can't be bothered</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you are not going to do it because you think it is unnecessary or because you are too lazy. 懶得","examples":["I just can't be bothered to look after the house. 我只是懶得照看那房子。"]}]}]},"bottle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓶子；一瓶（的量）；酒；奶瓶，乳飲品；<英，非正式>信心，勇氣；<非正式>酒癖，嗜酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝瓶；<非正式>用玻璃瓶砸；<英，非正式>喪失勇氣，洩氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bottle</b> is a glass or plastic container in which drinks and other liquids are kept. Bottles are usually round with straight sides and a narrow top. 瓶子","examples":["There were two empty beer bottles on the table. 桌上有兩個空啤酒瓶。","He was pulling the cork from a bottle of wine. 他在拔一瓶葡萄酒的瓶塞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>bottle</b> to refer to a bottle and its contents, or to the contents only. 瓶","examples":["She had drunk half a bottle of whisky. 她已經喝了半瓶威士忌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"nerve; courage (esp in the phrase <b>lose one's bottle</b>) 膽量; 勇氣","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bottle</b> is a drinking container used by babies. It has a special rubber part at the top through which they can suck their drink. 奶瓶","examples":["Gary was holding a bottle to the baby's lips. 加里正把奶瓶放到嬰兒的嘴邊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bottle</b> a drink or other liquid means to put it into bottles after it has been made. 使裝瓶","examples":["This is a large truck which has equipment to automatically bottle the wine. 這是輛有葡萄酒自動裝瓶裝置的大卡車。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to injure by thrusting a broken bottle into (a person) 用破玻璃瓶刺(某人)","examples":[]}]}]},"brick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磚，磚塊；<舊>熱心人，可靠的人；積木"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"似磚的；用磚做的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用磚牆圍起，用磚堵住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bricks</b> are rectangular blocks of baked clay used for building walls, which are usually red or brown. <b>Brick</b> is the material made up of these blocks. 磚","examples":["She built bookshelves out of bricks and planks. 她用磚和厚木板製作了書架。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hit a brick wall</b> or <b>come up against a brick wall</b>, you are unable to continue or make progress because something stops you. 碰壁","examples":["After that my career just seemed to hit a brick wall. 從那以後我的事業似乎碰了壁。"]}]}]},"brunch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"早午餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Brunch</b> is a meal that is eaten in the late morning. It is a combination of breakfast and lunch. 早午餐","examples":[]}]}]},"bow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鞠躬，點頭；低下（頭）；停止對抗，屈從於；（使）彎曲；用弓拉奏（樂曲）；<美>（新影片）首映，（新產品）投放市場"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞠躬，點頭；船頭；蝴蝶結；弓；琴弓；（用琴弓拉的）一段（音樂）；字母的一彎；（鑰匙、剪刀等的）金屬環狀柄，圓形拎環；<美>眼鏡架，眼鏡框"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bow</b> <b>to</b> someone, you briefly bend your body toward them as a formal way of greeting them or showing respect. 鞠躬","examples":["They bowed low to Louis and hastened out of his way. 他們向路易斯深深地鞠躬並迅速給他讓路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bow to</b> pressure or to someone's wishes, you agree to do what they want you to do. 屈從","examples":["Some stores are bowing to consumer pressure and stocking organically grown vegetables. 有些商店屈於消費者的壓力，供應有機蔬菜。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bow</b> is also a noun. 鞠躬","examples":["I gave a theatrical bow and waved. 我誇張地鞠了一躬，然後揮了揮手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The front part of a ship is called <b>the</b> <b>bow</b> or <b>the</b> <b>bows</b>. The plural <b>bows</b> can be used to refer either to one or to more than one of these parts. 船頭","examples":["The waves were about five feet high now, and the bow of the boat was leaping up and down. 浪頭現在約有五英尺高，船頭上下顛簸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bow</b> is a knot with two loops and two loose ends that is used in tying shoelaces and ribbons. 蝴蝶結","examples":["Add a length of ribbon tied in a bow. 加一段打成蝴蝶結的緞帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bow</b> is a weapon for shooting arrows that consists of a long piece of curved wood with a string attached to both its ends. 弓","examples":["Some of the raiders were armed with bows and arrows. 有些偷襲者配備了弓箭。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>bow</b> of a violin or other stringed instrument is a long thin piece of wood with fibres stretched along it that you move across the strings of the instrument in order to play it. 琴弓","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bow</b> your head, you bend it downward so that you are looking toward the ground, for example, because you want to show respect or because you are thinking deeply about something. 低下 (頭)","examples":["The Colonel bowed his head and whispered a prayer of thanksgiving. 上校低下頭，低聲感恩禱告。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to form or cause to form a curve or curves 使彎曲","examples":[]}]}]},"brain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腦；<非正式>智力，智慧；聰明的人，智者；<非正式>電腦；（供食用的）動物腦髓"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>猛擊……的頭部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>brain</b> is the organ inside your head that controls your body's activities and enables you to think and to feel things such as heat and pain. 腦","examples":["Her father died of a brain tumour. 他的父親死於腦瘤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>brain</b> is your mind and the way that you think. 腦筋","examples":["Once you stop using your brain you soon go stale. 一旦你停止動腦筋,你很快就會變遲鈍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone has <b>brains</b> or a good <b>brain</b>, they have the ability to learn and understand things quickly, to solve problems, and to make good decisions. 頭腦","examples":["They were not the only ones to have brains and ambition. 他們並非僅有的有頭腦、有抱負的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>the</b> <b>brains</b> behind an idea or an organization, he or she had that idea or makes the important decisions about how that organization is managed. 智囊","examples":["Mr. White was the brains behind the scheme. 懷特先生是這項計劃後面的智囊。"]}]}]},"branch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹枝，分枝；分支機構，分店；（政府或機構的）部門；分科，分支；（家族的）支系；支流，岔路"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分岔，岔開；出枝，發出新枝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>branches</b> of a tree are the parts that grow out from its trunk and have leaves, flowers, or fruit growing on them. 樹枝","examples":["...the upper branches of a row of pines. …一排松樹的上部枝條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>branch</b> <b>of</b> a business or other organization is one of the offices, stores, or groups which belong to it and which are located in different places. (企業或機構的) 分支","examples":["The local branch of Bank of America is handling the accounts. 美國銀行的本地分行正在處理這些賬目。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>branch</b> <b>of</b> an organization such as the government or the police force is a department that has a particular function. 分支部門","examples":["Senate employees could take their employment grievances to another branch of government. 參議院的僱員可以將他們對工作的不滿向另一政府分支部門申訴。","He had a fascination for submarines and joined this branch of the service. 他迷戀潛艇並加入了海軍的這個分支。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>branch of</b> a subject is a part or type of it. (學科的) 分科","examples":["Whole branches of science may not receive any grants. 很多整個科學分科可能都得不到撥款。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>branch</b> <b>of</b> your family is a group of its members who are descended from one particular person. (家族的) 支系","examples":["This is one of the branches of the Roosevelt family. 這是羅斯福家族的一個支系。"]}]}]},"brand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"品牌，商標；（獨特的）一種，一類；（動物身上標明所屬的）烙印，火印；獨特的個性，自成一格的形象；燃燒的木頭，燒焦的木頭；<古>（列印用的）烙鐵；火炬，劍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打烙印於（牲畜，以標明所屬）；給……冠以惡名，譴責；給……設計品牌，加商標於；銘刻，銘記"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brand</b> of a product is the version of it that is made by one particular manufacturer. 品牌","examples":["Winston is a brand of cigarette. 雲斯頓是一種香菸品牌。","I bought one of the leading brands. 我買了知名品牌中的一種。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>brand of</b> something such as a way of thinking or behaving is a particular kind of it. (思維或行為方式等的) 獨特型別","examples":["Joel Hatch brings his own unique brand of humour to the role. 喬爾·哈奇把他自己獨具一格的幽默帶進了這個角色。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Brand</b> is also a noun. 烙印","examples":["A brand was a mark of ownership burned into the hide of an animal with a hot iron. 烙印是用烙鐵燒在牲畜皮上的所有權標記。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is branded</b> as something bad, people think they are that thing. 歸為 (不好的事物)","examples":["I was instantly branded as a rebel. 我立刻被歸為造反者。","The company has been branded racist by some of its own staff. 這家公司被它自己的一些職員歸為種族主義者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>brand</b> an animal, you put a permanent mark on its skin in order to show who it belongs to, usually by burning a mark onto its skin. 給…打上烙印","examples":["The owner couldn't be bothered to brand the cattle. 主人懶得給這牛打上烙印。"]}]}]},"broadcast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"散佈，傳播（資訊等）；播撒（種子等）；廣播，播送"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電視節目，廣播節目；廣播，播出"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"廣播（或電視）節目的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"四散地，撒播地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>broadcast</b> is a program, performance, or speech on the radio or on television. (無線電或電視) 廣播節目","examples":["In a broadcast on state radio the government announced that it was willing to resume peace negotiations. 在國家電臺的廣播節目中，政府宣佈願意恢復和平談判。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>broadcast</b> a program means to send it out by radio waves, wires, or satellites so that it can be heard on the radio or seen on television. (由無線電或電視) 播放","examples":["The concert will be broadcast live on television and radio. 音樂會將透過電視和電臺現場直播。","CNN also broadcasts in Europe. 美國有線新聞網路也在歐洲進行廣播。"]}]}]},"brief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"短暫的；簡短的；（衣服）很短的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……指示，向……介紹情況；<英>向（辯護律師）提供案情摘要"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"指示，任務簡介；摘要，概要；短內褲（briefs）；辯護狀；辯護律師；<英>委託辯護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>brief</b> lasts for only a short time. 短暫的","examples":["She once made a brief appearance on television. 她曾在電視上短暫露面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>brief</b> speech or piece of writing does not contain too many words or details. (講話、文章) 簡短的","examples":["In a brief statement, he concentrated entirely on international affairs. 在一個簡短的陳述中,他完全集中在了國際事務上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>brief</b>, you say what you want to say in as few words as possible. (說話) 簡明扼要的","examples":["Now please be brief – my time is valuable. 現在請長話短說–我的時間很寶貴。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe a period of time as <b>brief</b> if you want to emphasize that it is very short. 短暫的","examples":["For a few brief minutes we forgot the anxiety and anguish. 短短的幾分鐘,我們忘卻了憂傷和痛苦。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Men's or women's underpants can be referred to as <b>briefs</b>. 短內褲","examples":["A bra and a pair of briefs lay on the floor. 一件胸罩和一條短內褲放在地板上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>brief</b> is a document containing all the information relating to a particular legal case, which is used by a lawyer to defend his or her client in court. 案情摘要","examples":["Griffith's expertise is in writing legal briefs. 格里菲思的專長在於撰寫法律案情摘要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone gives you a <b>brief</b>, they officially give you responsibility and instructions for dealing with a particular thing. 職責","examples":["...customs officials with a brief to stop foreign porn coming into Britain. …身擔阻止外國淫穢物品進入英國的職責的海關管員們。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>briefs</b> you, especially about a piece of work or a serious matter, they give you information that you need before you do it or consider it. 介紹; 提供 (資訊)","examples":["A Defense Department spokesman briefed reporters. 一位國防部發言人向記者們介紹了情況。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>in brief</b> to indicate that you are about to say something in as few words as possible or to give a summary of what you have just said. 簡言之","examples":["In brief, take no risks. 簡言之,別冒險。"]}]}]},"bun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小圓麵包，小長麵包；小圓甜蛋糕，小圓甜餅；圓髮髻；<北美><非正式>（人的）屁股，臀部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Buns</b> are small bread rolls. They are sometimes sweet and may contain dried fruit or spices. 小圓麵包","examples":["...a currant bun. …一塊含葡萄乾的小圓麵包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a woman has her hair in a <b>bun</b>, she has fastened it tightly on top of her head or at the back of her head in the shape of a ball. 圓髻","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>buns</b> are your buttocks. 屁股","examples":["I'd pinch his buns and kiss his neck. 我要擰他的屁股，親他的脖子。"]}]}]},"burger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漢堡包，夾心牛肉餅；（類似漢堡包的）餡餅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>burger</b> is a flat round mass of ground meat or minced vegetables that is fried and often eaten in a bread roll. 漢堡","examples":["...burger and fries. …漢堡和炸薯條。"]}]}]},"cabbage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"捲心菜，洋白菜；（作蔬菜食用的）捲心菜葉子，洋白菜葉子；<英，非正式>（冒犯）（因受傷或疾病而）身心殘損的人；<英，非正式>生活極乏味的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cabbage</b> is a round vegetable with white, green, or purple leaves that is usually eaten cooked. 捲心菜","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to steal; pilfer 偷; 偷竊","examples":[]}]}]},"brush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"刷子，畫筆；灌木叢；刷；輕擦，掠過；小衝突；狐狸尾巴；柴枝；<非正式>（性感的）女人（或女孩）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"刷，拂拭；刷掉，拂去；刷上；輕擦，觸碰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brush</b> is an object that has a large number of bristles or hairs fixed to it. You use brushes for painting, for cleaning things, and for making your hair neat. 畫筆; 刷子","examples":["We gave him paint and brushes. 我們給了他顏料和畫筆。","Stains are removed with buckets of soapy water and scrubbing brushes. 汙點用一桶桶的肥皂水和擦洗的刷子除掉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Brush</b> is also a noun. 刷; 梳理","examples":["I gave it a quick brush with my hairbrush. 我用發刷對它進行了一番迅速的梳理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>brush</b> <b>with</b> a particular situation, usually an unpleasant one, you almost experience it. 擦肩而過","examples":["...the trauma of a brush with death. …與死神擦肩而過後的創傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the bushy tail of a fox, often kept as a trophy after a hunt, or of certain breeds of dog (作為狩獵戰利品的)狐狸尾巴; 某些品種的狗的尾巴","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Brush</b> is an area of rough open land covered with small bushes and trees. You also use <b>brush</b> to refer to the bushes and trees on this land. 灌木叢地帶; 灌木叢","examples":["...the brush fire that destroyed nearly 500 acres. …燒燬了近五百英畝的灌木叢火災。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>brush</b> something or <b>brush</b> something such as dirt off it, you clean it or make it neat using a brush. 刷; 梳理","examples":["Have you brushed your teeth? 你刷過牙了嗎？","She brushed the powder out of her hair. 她把粉末從頭髮中梳掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>brush</b> something <b>with</b> a liquid, you apply a layer of that liquid using a brush. 用…塗刷","examples":["Brush the dough with beaten egg yolk. 在生麵糰上刷一層打好的蛋黃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>brush</b> something somewhere, you remove it with quick light movements of your hands. (用手) 輕輕拭去","examples":["He brushed his hair back with both hands. 他用雙手把頭髮輕輕地捋到後面去。","She brushed away tears as she spoke of him. 她在談起他的時候輕輕拭去眼淚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>brushes</b> <b>against</b> another or if you <b>brush</b> one thing <b>against</b> another, the first thing touches the second thing lightly while passing it. 輕輕擦過","examples":["Something brushed against her leg. 有什麼東西輕輕從她腿上擦過。","I felt her dark brown hair brushing the back of my shoulder. 我感覺到她深褐色的頭髮輕輕拂過我的肩後。"]}]}]},"bundle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"束，捆，包；非常；一套，一系列；大量；嬰兒；一大筆錢；軟體包"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"匆匆打發，亂塞；匆忙趕往；捆綁銷售；與某人和衣同睡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bundle</b> <b>of</b> things is a number of them that are tied together or wrapped in a cloth or bag so that they can be carried or stored. 包; 捆; 束","examples":["Lance pulled a bundle of papers out of a folder. 蘭斯從一個資料夾中拉出一疊檔案。","He gathered the bundles of clothing into his arms. 他把一捆捆衣物抱起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as, for example, a <b>bundle</b> <b>of</b> fun, you are emphasizing that they are full of fun. If you describe someone as a <b>bundle</b> <b>of</b> nerves, you are emphasizing that they are very nervous. (強調人的特點) 非常","examples":["I remember Mickey as a bundle of fun, great to have around. 我記得米基是個非常有趣的人，有他在身邊很開心。","Life at high school wasn't a bundle of laughs. 高中生活並不是充滿了笑聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is bundled</b> somewhere, someone pushes them there in a rough and hurried way. 塞","examples":["He was bundled into a car and driven 50 miles to a police station. 他被塞進一輛小汽車，被帶到50英里外的警察局。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>bundle</b> software means to sell it together with a computer, or with other hardware or software, as part of a set. 捆綁銷售","examples":["It's cheaper to buy software bundled with a PC than separately. 購買與計算機捆綁銷售的軟體比單獨買更便宜。"]}]}]},"button":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紐扣，釦子；按鈕；<美>徽章"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用紐扣扣住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Buttons</b> are small hard objects sewn onto shirts, coats, or other pieces of clothing. You fasten the clothing by pushing the buttons through holes called buttonholes. 紐扣","examples":["...a coat with brass buttons. …有銅紐扣的大衣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>button</b> is a small object on a machine or electrical device that you press in order to operate it. 按鈕","examples":["He reached for the remote control and pressed the \"play\" button. 他伸手去拿遙控器，按下播放按鈕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>button</b> is a small piece of metal or plastic that you wear in order to show that you support a particular movement, organization, or person. You fasten a button to your clothes with a pin. 小徽章","examples":["Wear a campaign button to show support for mothers in prison. 佩上活動徽章，以支援坐牢的母親們。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>button</b> a shirt, coat, or other piece of clothing, you fasten it by pushing its buttons through the buttonholes. 扣上","examples":["Ferguson stood up and buttoned his coat. 弗格森站起來，扣上大衣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Button up</b> means the same as . 扣上","examples":["I buttoned up my coat; it was chilly. 我扣上大衣；天冷嗖嗖的。","The young man slipped on the shirt and buttoned it up. 年輕人迅速套上襯衫，扣上釦子。"]}]}]},"caf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"成本加運費價格（cost and freight）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Caf）（美、土、瑞）察夫（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"cost and freight 成本加運費價格","examples":[]}]}]},"cable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電纜；鋼纜，纜繩；電報；有線電視"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……安裝有線電視；給……發電報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cable</b> is a kind of very strong, thick rope, made of wires twisted together. 纜繩","examples":["The miners rode a conveyance attached to a cable made of braided steel wire. 礦工們乘坐連著鋼索的纜車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cable</b> is a thick wire, or a group of wires inside a rubber or plastic covering, which is used to carry electricity or electronic signals. 電纜","examples":["...overhead power cables. …高架電纜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Cable</b> is used to refer to television systems in which the signals are sent along underground wires rather than by radio waves. 有線電視","examples":["They ran commercials on cable systems across the country. 他們在全國範圍內的有線電視上做廣告。"]}]}]},"cafeteria":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自助食堂，自助餐館"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cafeteria</b> is a restaurant where you choose your food from a counter and take it to your table after paying for it. Cafeterias are usually found in public buildings such as hospitals, colleges, and offices. 自助餐廳","examples":[]}]}]},"burst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"爆炸，爆裂，脹開；衝，闖，突然出現；猛然開啟；充滿，滿懷（be bursting with）；決堤；突然活躍起來；突然發生，突然發作；分頁，斷紙"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"突發，迸發；爆裂，裂口；一陣短促的射擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>bursts</b> or if you <b>burst</b> it, it suddenly breaks open or splits open and the air or other substance inside it comes out. 使爆裂; 爆裂","examples":["The driver lost control when a tire burst. 一隻輪胎爆裂時司機失去了控制。","It is not a good idea to burst a blister. 把水皰弄破不是個好主意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a dam <b>bursts</b>, or if something <b>bursts</b> it, it breaks apart because the force of the river is too great. 使潰決; 潰決","examples":["A dam burst and flooded their villages. 一個大壩決堤，淹沒了他們的村子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a river <b>bursts</b> its banks, the water rises and goes on to the land. 決 (堤)","examples":["Monsoons caused the river to burst its banks. 雨季使這條河決堤。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a door or lid <b>bursts</b> open, it opens very suddenly and violently because someone pushes it or there is great pressure behind it. (門、蓋子等) 猛然開啟","examples":["The door burst open and an angry young nurse appeared. 門突然開了，一個生氣的年輕護士出現了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>burst</b> <b>into</b> or <b>out</b> of a place means to enter or leave it suddenly with a lot of energy or force. 闖","examples":["Gunmen burst into his home and opened fire. 持槍歹徒闖入他家，開了槍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>bursts</b> onto the scene, you mean that it suddenly starts or becomes active, usually after developing quietly for some time. 突然活躍起來","examples":["He burst onto the fashion scene in the early 1980s. 20世紀80年代初他突然在時尚界活躍起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>burst</b> <b>of</b> something is a sudden short period of it. (突然的) 一陣","examples":["...a burst of machine-gun fire. …一陣機槍射擊。"]}]}]},"calendar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"日曆；日程表；記事錄，大事記；曆法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……排進日程表（或時間表），把……記入記事錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calendar</b> is a chart or device which displays the date and the day of the week, and often the whole of a particular year divided up into months, weeks, and days. 日曆","examples":["There was a calendar on the wall above, with large squares around the dates. 牆的上方曾有一本日曆，日期框在大方格里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>calendar</b> is a particular system for dividing time into periods such as years, months, and weeks, often starting from a particular point in history. 曆法","examples":["The Christian calendar was originally based on the Julian calendar of the Romans. 公曆最初是基於羅馬的儒略曆的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>calendar</b> to refer to a series or list of events and activities which take place on particular dates, and which are important for a particular organization, community, or person. 日程表","examples":["It is one of the hottest tickets on Washington's social calendar. 這是華盛頓社交日程表上最熱門的入場券之一。"]}]}]},"business":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商業，買賣，生意；商務，公事；公司，企業；行業，職業；事務，職責；私事；事情；（顧客對商店的）惠顧；系列事件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Business</b> is work relating to the production, buying, and selling of goods or services. 商業","examples":["Jennifer has an impressive academic and business background. 詹妮弗有著了不起的學術和商業背景。","...Harvard Business School. …哈佛商學院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Business</b> is used when talking about how many products or services a company is able to sell. If <b>business</b> is good, a lot of products or services are being sold and if <b>business</b> is bad, few of them are being sold. 生意","examples":["They worried that German companies would lose business. 他們擔心德國公司會失去生意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>business</b> is an organization that produces and sells goods or that provides a service. 企業","examples":["The company was a family business. 這家公司是一個家族企業。","The majority of small businesses fail within the first twenty-four months. 大多數小企業在最初的兩年內倒閉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Business</b> is work or some other activity that you do as part of your job and not for pleasure. 工作","examples":["I'm here on business. 我在這裡出差。","You can't mix business with pleasure. 你不能把工作和娛樂混在一起。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>business</b> to refer to a particular area of work or activity in which the aim is to make a profit. 行業","examples":["May I ask you what business you're in? 您能告訴我您從事哪個行業嗎？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>business</b> to refer to something that you are doing or concerning yourself with. 事務","examples":["...recording Ben as he goes about his business. …攝錄本做自己的事的樣子。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can use <b>business</b> to refer to important matters that you have to deal with. 要事","examples":["The most important business was left to the last. 最重要的事留到最後做。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that something is your <b>business</b>, you mean that it concerns you personally and that other people have no right to ask questions about it or disagree with it. 私事","examples":["My sex life is my business. 我的性生活是我的私事。","If she doesn't want the police involved, that's her business. 如果她不想讓警察牽扯進來，那是她自己的事。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can use <b>business</b> to refer in a general way to an event, situation, or activity. For example, you can say something is \"a wretched business\" or you can refer to \"this assassination business.\" 事件","examples":["We have sorted out this wretched business at last. 我們終於處理了這起惡劣的事件。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people or companies <b>do business</b> <b>with</b> each other, one sells goods or services to the other. 做生意","examples":["I was fascinated by the different people who did business with me. 我對跟我做生意的各種不同的人感到著迷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has no business</b> <b>to</b> be in a place or <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they have no right to be there or to do it. 無權","examples":["Really I had no business to be there at all. 其實我根本無權在那兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A company that is <b>in business</b> is operating and trading. 執行","examples":["You can't stay in business without cash. 沒有現金你無法繼續營業。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a shop or company goes <b>out of business</b> or is put <b>out of business</b>, it has to stop trading because it is not making enough money. 停業","examples":["Thousands of firms could go out of business. 數千家商號可能倒閉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a difficult situation, if you say it is <b>business as usual</b>, you mean that people will continue doing what they normally do. 一切照常","examples":["For the time being it's business as usual for consumers. 對於消費者來說暫時一切照常。"]}]}]},"cancer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"癌症；痼疾，社會惡習；巨蟹宮，巨蟹座（Cancer）；出生於巨蟹宮時段（即6月22日至7月22日）的人（Cancer）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cancer</b> is a serious disease in which cells in a person's body increase rapidly in an uncontrolled way, producing abnormal growths. 癌症","examples":["Her mother died of breast cancer. 她母親死於乳腺癌。","Jane was just 25 when she learned she had cancer. 珍妮得知自己患了癌症時才25歲。"]}]}]},"carrot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胡蘿蔔；（為鼓勵某人做某事而作出的）誘人的承諾；<非正式，貶>紅髮人（carrots）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Carrots</b> are long, thin, orange-coloured vegetables. They grow under the ground, and have green shoots above the ground. 胡蘿蔔","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is offered to people in order to persuade them to do something can be referred to as a <b>carrot</b>. Something that is meant to persuade people not to do something can be referred to in the same sentence as a \"stick.\" 誘餌","examples":["Why the new emphasis on sticks instead of diplomatic carrots? 為什麼不再丟擲外交誘餌，反而重新側重大棒威脅？"]}]}]},"candle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蠟燭；舊燭光，國際燭光（發光強度單位）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對著光檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>candle</b> is a stick of hard wax with a piece of string called a wick through the middle. You light the wick in order to give a steady flame that provides light. 蠟燭","examples":["The bedroom was lit by a single candle. 臥室被一支蠟燭照亮。"]}]}]},"captain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"隊長，首領；上尉，上校；船長，機長；<美>警局副官，消防署中隊長"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"率隊，指揮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the army, navy, and some other armed forces, a <b>captain</b> is an officer of middle rank. (陸軍、海軍及其他軍種的) 上尉","examples":["...Captain Mark Phillips. …馬克·菲利普斯上尉。","...a captain in the army. …一名陸軍上尉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>captain</b> <b>of</b> a sports team is the player in charge of it. (體育運動隊) 隊長","examples":["...Mickey Thomas, the captain of the tennis team. …米奇·托馬斯，這支網球隊的隊長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>captain</b> of a ship is the sailor in charge of it. 船長","examples":["...the captain of an excursion boat. …一艘遊船的船長。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>captain</b> of an aeroplane is the pilot in charge of it. 機長","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In the United States and some other countries, a <b>captain</b> is a police officer or firefighter of fairly senior rank. 警察局副巡官; 消防中隊長","examples":["...a former Honolulu police captain. …火奴魯魯警察局前任巡官。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>captain</b> a team or a ship, you are the captain of it. 率隊; 指揮","examples":["He captained the winning team in 1991. 他於1991年率隊奪得勝利。"]}]}]},"carpet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地毯；覆蓋地面的一層厚東西；<美，非正式>人工球場；地毯衣蛾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……鋪地毯；厚厚地鋪上；<英，非正式>訓斥，斥責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carpet</b> is a thick covering of soft material which is laid over a floor or a staircase. 地毯","examples":["They put down wooden boards, and laid new carpets on top. 他們安裝了木地板，還在上面鋪了新地毯。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a floor or a room <b>is carpeted</b>, a carpet is laid on the floor. 鋪地毯","examples":["The room had been carpeted and the windows glazed with coloured glass. 房間裡鋪上了地毯，彩色的玻璃令窗戶閃閃發亮。"]}]}]},"calm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鎮靜的，沉著的；平靜的，穩定的；風平浪靜的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（精神或情感狀態的）鎮靜，平和；寧靜，安靜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使平靜，使鎮靜；冷靜下來，鎮靜下來；恢復平靜，恢復正常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calm</b> person does not show or feel any worry, anger, or excitement. 冷靜的; 平靜的","examples":["She is usually a calm and diplomatic woman. 她通常是個冷靜而圓滑的女人。","Try to keep calm and just tell me what happened. 試著保持冷靜，告訴我發生了什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone says that a place is <b>calm</b>, they mean that it is free from fighting or public disorder, when trouble has recently occurred there or had been expected. 平靜的","examples":["The city of Sarajevo appears relatively calm today. 薩拉熱窩市今天顯得相對平靜了些。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the sea or a lake is <b>calm</b>, the water is not moving very much and there are no big waves. 平靜無波的","examples":["...the safe, calm waters protected by an offshore reef. …由近海礁脈保護的安全、平靜無波的海域。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Calm</b> weather is pleasant weather with little or no wind. 風和日麗的","examples":["Tuesday was a fine, clear and calm day. 星期二是晴空萬里、風和日麗的一天。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"使人鎮靜的","examples":["...a fresh, cool fragrance which produces a very calming effect on the mind. …有鎮靜作用的清新香氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Calm</b> is also a noun. 冷靜; 平靜","examples":["He felt a sudden sense of calm, of contentment. 他突然感受到了內心的平靜和滿足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Calm</b> is also a noun. 平靜","examples":["Community and church leaders have appealed for calm and no retaliation. 社群和教會領袖呼籲人們保持冷靜，不要採取報復行動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Calm</b> is used to refer to a quiet, still, or peaceful atmosphere in a place. 安寧","examples":["The house projects an atmosphere of calm and order. 整幢房子呈現出一種寧靜祥和、井然有序的氛圍。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"冷靜地; 平靜地","examples":["Alan looked at him and said calmly, \"I don't believe you.\" 艾倫看著他，平靜地說，“我不相信你。”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>calm</b> someone, you do something to make them feel less angry, worried, or excited. 使冷靜; 使鎮靜","examples":["The ruling party's veterans know how to calm their critics. 執政黨中的資深官員們深諳安撫批評者之道。","She was breathing quickly and tried to calm herself. 她呼吸急促，試圖使自己鎮定下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>calm</b> a situation means to reduce the amount of trouble, violence, or panic there is. 使平靜; 平息","examples":["Officials hoped admitting fewer foreigners would calm the situation. 官方希望透過招收較少的外國人來平息局面。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the sea <b>calms</b>, it becomes still because the wind stops blowing strongly. When the wind <b>calms</b>, it stops blowing strongly. (海或風) 平靜下來","examples":["Dawn came, the sea calmed but the cold was as bitter as ever. 破曉時分，大海平靜下來，但寒冷依然。"]}]}]},"cart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（馬拉的）大車，馬車；小型機動車；購物車，手推車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用車裝運；搬運，移動；挾持，帶走"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cart</b> is an old-fashioned wooden vehicle that is used for transporting goods or people. Some carts are pulled by animals. 老式板車","examples":["...a country where horse-drawn carts far outnumber cars. …一個馬拉車遠多於汽車的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cart</b> is a small vehicle with a motor. 小型機動車","examples":["Cars are prohibited, so transportation is by electric cart or by horse and buggy. 由於汽車被禁止使用，交通依賴於電車或輕便馬車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cart</b> or a <b>shopping cart</b> is a large metal basket on wheels which is provided by shops such as supermarkets for customers to use while they are in the shop. 購物推車","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"cartridge的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cart</b> things or people somewhere, you carry them or transport them there, often with difficulty. (常指費力地) 運送","examples":["After their parents died, one of their father's relatives carted off the entire contents of the house. 他們的父母死後，其父的一個親戚把這所房子裡所有的東西都運走了。","...a neat tote bag for carting around your child's books or toys. …用來裝孩子的書本和玩具的精緻手袋。"]}]}]},"burn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"燃燒，消耗；燒壞，燒燬，燒焦；曬傷，曬黑；火辣辣地發痛，發燙；發光，發亮；激怒；燒錄；渴望；迅速移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"灼傷，燒傷，燒痕；肌肉痠痛感；小溪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a fire or a flame somewhere, you say that there is a fire or flame <b>burning</b> there. 燃燒","examples":["Fires were burning out of control in the centre of the city. 火在市中心燃燒著,失去了控制。","There was a fire burning in the fireplace. 壁爐裡有火正燃著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is burning</b>, it is on fire. 燃燒","examples":["When I arrived one of the vehicles was still burning. 我到達時，其中的一輛車還在燃燒。","The building housed 1,500 refugees and it burned for hours. 這棟樓住著1500個難民，它燒了好幾個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a light <b>is burning</b>, it is shining. 發光","examples":["The building was darkened except for a single light burning in a third-storey window. 除了三樓的一扇窗戶透出一絲光亮，整棟樓一片漆黑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"燃燒","examples":["When we arrived in our village there was a terrible smell of burning. 我們到達村子的時候，那裡有一股難聞的燃燒的味道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"燒燬","examples":["The French government has criticized the burning of a U.S. flag outside the American embassy. 法國政府譴責了在美國大使館外焚燬美國國旗的行為。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Burn</b> is also a noun. 燒傷","examples":["She suffered appalling burns to her back. 她背部受了嚴重燒傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a small stream; brook 小溪","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>burn</b> something, you destroy or damage it with fire. 燒燬","examples":["Protesters set cars on fire and burned a building. 抗議者們焚燒汽車，燒燬了一棟建築。","Incineration plants should be built to burn household waste. 應該建焚化廠來焚燒生活垃圾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>burn</b> a fuel or if it <b>burns</b>, it is used to produce heat, light, or energy. 燒; 燃燒","examples":["The power stations burn coal from the Ruhr region. 這些電廠燒產自魯爾地區的煤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>burn</b> something that you are cooking or if it <b>burns</b>, you spoil it by using too much heat or cooking it for too long. 燒煳","examples":["I burned the toast. 我烤煳了麵包片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>burn</b> part of your body, <b>burn</b> <b>yourself</b>, or <b>are burned</b> or <b>burnt</b>, you are injured by fire or by something very hot. 燒傷","examples":["Take care not to burn your fingers. 小心別燒著你的手指。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>is burned</b> or <b>burned</b> to death, they are killed by fire. 燒死","examples":["Women were burned as witches in the Middle Ages. 在中世紀女人被當作巫婆燒死。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>burn</b> or get <b>burned</b> in the sun, the sun makes your skin become red and sore. 曬傷","examples":["Build up your tan slowly and don't allow your skin to burn. 將你的皮膚慢慢曬黑，不要讓皮膚曬傷。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>burns</b> or if something <b>burns</b> it, it has a painful hot or stinging feeling. 灼痛","examples":["My eyes burn from staring at the needle. 因為盯著針看，我的眼睛灼痛。","His face was burning with cold. 他的臉凍得灼痛。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"To <b>burn</b> a CD means to write or copy data onto it. 燒錄","examples":["You can use this software to burn custom compilations of your favourite tunes. 你可以用這個軟體刻制你最喜歡曲子的自選曲集。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"燒煳的","examples":["...the smell of burnt toast. …麵包片烤煳的氣味。"]}]}]},"catsup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"番茄醬，番茄沙司（ketchup 的異體拼寫，亦作 catchup）"}],"sections":[]},"cassette":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磁帶盒，盒式磁帶；膠片盒；（半導體）晶圓載具，晶舟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cassette</b> is a small, flat, rectangular plastic case containing magnetic tape which is used for recording and playing back sound or film. 磁帶","examples":["His two albums released on cassette have sold 10 million copies. 他以磁帶形式發行的兩張專輯已售出1000萬份。"]}]}]},"castle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"城堡，堡壘；（國際象棋中的）車；豪宅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（國際象棋中）王車易位；置……於城堡中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>castle</b> is a large building with thick, high walls. Castles were built by important people, such as kings, in former times, especially for protection during wars and battles. 城堡","examples":[]}]}]},"cartoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漫畫，諷刺畫；動畫片，卡通片；草圖，底圖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……畫漫畫；畫漫畫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cartoon</b> is a humorous drawing or series of drawings in a newspaper or magazine. 卡通; 漫畫","examples":["Mickey Mouse, Donald Duck, and other Disney cartoon characters gave endless delight to millions of children. 米老鼠、唐老鴨及其他迪斯尼卡通形象給數百萬的兒童帶來了無盡的歡樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cartoon</b> is a film in which all the characters and scenes are drawn rather than being real people or objects. 動畫片","examples":["...a TV set blares out a cartoon comedy. …一臺電視裡播放著一部動畫喜劇。"]}]}]},"ceiling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天花板，吊頂；上限，最高限度；最高飛行限度，升限"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ceiling</b> is the horizontal surface that forms the top part or roof inside a room. 天花板","examples":["The rooms were spacious, with tall windows and high ceilings. 房間很寬敞，且窗戶和屋頂都很高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ceiling</b> <b>on</b> something such as prices or wages is an official upper limit that cannot be broken. (價格、工資等的) 上限","examples":["...an informal agreement to put a ceiling on salaries. …一項規定工資上限的非正式協議。"]}]}]},"century":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"世紀；一百年；（板球）一百分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>century</b> is a period of a hundred years that is used when stating a date. For example, the 19th century was the period from 1801 to 1900. 世紀","examples":["The material position of the Church had been declining since the late eighteenth century. 自18世紀晚期以來，教堂的世俗地位一直在下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>century</b> is any period of a hundred years. 百年","examples":["The drought there is the worst in a century. 那裡的旱情百年不遇。"]}]}]},"cash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現款，現金；金錢，資金"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"兌現（支票）；支付現款"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cash</b> is money in the form of bills and coins rather than cheques. 現金","examples":["...two thousand dollars in cash. …2000美元現金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cash</b> means the same as money, especially money which is immediately available. 現錢","examples":["...a state-owned financial-services group with plenty of cash. …一家有大量現錢的國有金融機構。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various Chinese, Indonesian, or Indian coins of low value (中國、印度尼西亞或印度等國的)任何低價值硬幣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cash</b> a cheque, you exchange it at a bank for the amount of money that it is worth. 兌現","examples":["There are similar charges if you want to cash a cheque or withdraw money at a branch other than your own. 如果你在其他銀行兌現支票或支取現金，將會產生差不多的手續費。"]}]}]},"cave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洞穴，山洞；地窖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"洞穴探險；（在壓力下）屈服，屈從；挖洞；塌落"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英，俚>當心！"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cave</b> is a large hole in the side of a cliff or hill, or one that is under the ground. 洞穴","examples":["Outside the cave mouth the blackness of night was like a curtain. 洞口外面，漆黑的夜晚宛如一塊幕布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"guard or lookout (esp in the phrase <b>keep cave</b>) 守衛; 警戒","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hollow out 挖洞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"sentence substitute.","pos_name":"sentence substitute.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"watch out! 當心; 提防","examples":[]}]}]},"cereal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"穀類食物；穀類植物，穀物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"穀類的；穀類製成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cereal</b> or <b>breakfast cereal</b> is a food made from grain. It is mixed with milk and eaten for breakfast. 麥片","examples":["I have a bowl of cereal every morning. 我每天早上吃一碗麥片粥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cereals</b> are plants such as wheat, corn, or rice that produce grain. (小麥、高粱、米等) 穀類植物","examples":["...the cereal-growing districts of the Midwest. …中西部生產穀類植物的地區。"]}]}]},"cell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"細胞；小牢房；電解槽，電池；電芯；（政治組織的）小組，基層組織；（修道院中的）單人小室；（巢穴中單個的）巢室；（計算機螢幕上的）單元格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cell</b> is the smallest part of an animal or plant that is able to function independently. Every animal or plant is made up of millions of cells. 細胞","examples":["Those cells divide and give many other different types of cells. 那些細胞分裂後形成許多其他不同型別的細胞。","...blood cells. …血細胞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cell</b> is a small room in which a prisoner is locked. A <b>cell</b> is also a small room in which a monk or nun lives. 小牢房; 小禪房","examples":["Do you recall how many prisoners were placed in each cell? 你記得每間牢房裡關了多少犯人嗎？"]}]}]},"chalk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"白堊；粉筆；白堊地層；用粉筆劃的記號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用粉筆寫（或畫）；用粉筆做記號；用白堊粉擦（桌球杆等）；<英>把（酒錢）記於（某人）賬上；獲（勝），得（分）；變成白堊狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chalk</b> is a type of soft, white rock. You can use small pieces of it for writing or drawing with. 白堊","examples":["...white cliffs made of chalk. …白堊絕壁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chalk</b> is small sticks of chalk, or a substance similar to chalk, used for writing or drawing with. 粉筆","examples":["...somebody writing with a piece of chalk. …正用粉筆寫字的某人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chalk</b> something, you draw or write it using a piece of chalk. 用粉筆畫; 用粉筆寫","examples":["He chalked the message on the blackboard. 他用粉筆把這條訊息寫在黑板上。"]}]}]},"chess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國際象棋，西洋棋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chess</b> is a game for two people, played on a chessboard. Each player has 16 pieces, including a king. Your aim is to move your pieces so that your opponent's king cannot escape being taken. 國際象棋","examples":["He was playing chess with his uncle. 他在和伯父下國際象棋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a floorboard of the deck of a pontoon bridge 浮橋的一塊橋板","examples":[]}]}]},"chin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頦，下巴"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>擊打下巴；引體向上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>chin</b> is the part of your face that is below your mouth and above your neck. 下巴","examples":["...a double chin. …雙下巴。"]}]}]},"chemical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"化學的，與化學有關的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"化學品，化學制品；成癮的藥物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chemical</b> means involving or resulting from a reaction between two or more substances, or relating to the substances that something consists of. 化學的","examples":["...chemical reactions that cause ozone destruction. …導致臭氧破壞的化學反應。","...the chemical composition of the ocean. …海洋的化學成分。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"經化學方式","examples":["...chemically treated foods. …經化學方式處理過的食品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chemicals</b> are substances that are used in a chemical process or made by a chemical process. 化學物; 化學制品","examples":["The whole food chain is affected by the overuse of chemicals in agriculture. 整個食物鏈受到了化學物質在農業中過度使用的影響。","...a chemical company. …一家化學制品公司。"]}]}]},"chopstick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"筷子（常用複數形式 chopsticks 指一雙筷子；單數指其中一根）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chopsticks</b> are a pair of thin sticks which people in China and the Far East use to eat their food. 筷子","examples":[]}]}]},"chocolate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巧克力，朱古力；巧克力糖，夾心巧克力糖；巧克力飲料，一杯巧克力飲料；深褐色，巧克力色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巧克力的，巧克力味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chocolate</b> is a sweet, hard food made from cacao. It is usually brown in colour and is eaten as a sweet. 巧克力","examples":["...a bar of chocolate. …一條巧克力。","Do you want some chocolate? 你想吃點巧克力嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chocolate</b> or <b>hot chocolate</b> is a drink made from a powder containing chocolate. It is usually made with hot milk. 巧克力熱飲","examples":["...a small cafeteria where the visitors can buy tea, coffee and chocolate. …一家小規模的自助快餐店，在那裡遊客們可以買到茶、咖啡和巧克力熱飲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Chocolates</b> are small sweets or nuts covered with a layer of chocolate. They are usually sold in a box. 巧克力糖","examples":["...a box of chocolates. …一盒巧克力糖。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chocolate</b> is used to describe things that are dark brown in colour. 深褐色","examples":["The curtains and the bedspread were chocolate velvet. 窗簾和床罩是深褐色的天鵝絨。"]}]}]},"cheat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"欺騙，行騙；僥倖逃脫，逃避；作弊；對配偶（或伴侶）不忠"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"騙子，作弊者；欺騙手段，欺詐行為；秘技，作弊軟體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>cheats</b>, they do not obey a set of rules which they should be obeying, for example in a game or exam. 舞弊; 作弊","examples":["Students may be tempted to cheat in order to get into top schools. 學生們可能禁不住會作弊，以便能進一流學校。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"舞弊; 作弊","examples":["In an election in 1988, he was accused of cheating by his opponent. 在1988年的一次競選中，他被對手指控舞弊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>cheat</b> does not obey a set of rules which they should be obeying. 舞弊者","examples":["Cheats will be disqualified. 舞弊者將被取消資格。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>cheats</b> you <b>out of</b> something, they get it from you by behaving dishonestly. 詐取","examples":["The company engaged in a deliberate effort to cheat them out of their pensions. 該公司曾蓄意詐取他們的養老金。"]}]}]},"character":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"性格，品質；特色，特徵；人物，角色；勇氣，毅力；某種人，古怪有趣的人；（書寫或印刷）符號，文字，字型；名譽，名聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>刻，寫；描述；使具有特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>character</b> of a person or place consists of all the qualities they have that make them distinct from other people or places. 性格; 特性","examples":["Perhaps there is a negative side to his character that you haven't seen yet. 或許他性格中有你還未看到的消極一面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>character</b> to say what kind of person someone is. For example, if you say that someone is a strange <b>character</b>, you mean they are strange. (具有某種特性的) 人","examples":["It's that kind of courage and determination that makes him such a remarkable character. 正是那種勇氣和決心使他成為這樣卓越的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>characters</b> in a film, book, or play are the people that it is about. (電影、書、戲劇中的) 人物","examples":["The film is autobiographical and the central character is played by Collard himself. 這部影片是自傳式的，主角由科勒德親自扮演。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>character</b> is a letter, number, or other symbol that is written or printed. 字元","examples":["...a shopping list written in Chinese characters. …用漢字寫的一張購物單。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something has a particular <b>character</b>, it has a particular quality. 性質","examples":["The financial concessions were of a precarious character. 財政優惠具有不穩定性。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>character</b> to refer to the qualities that people from a particular place are believed to have. 特徵","examples":["Individuality is a valued and inherent part of the British character. 個性是英國人重視並固有的特徵。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>character</b> is your personality, especially how reliable and honest you are. If someone is <b>of</b> good <b>character</b>, they are reliable and honest. If they are <b>of</b> bad <b>character</b>, they are unreliable and dishonest. 人品","examples":["He's begun a series of personal attacks on my character. 他開始對我的人品進行一系列的人身攻擊。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>character</b>, you mean that they have the ability to deal effectively with difficult, unpleasant, or dangerous situations. 人格力量","examples":["She showed real character in her attempts to win over the crowd. 她在爭取民眾支援的努力中顯示出了真正的人格力量。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that a place has <b>character</b>, you mean that it has an interesting or unusual quality which makes you notice it and like it. 特色","examples":["A soulless shopping centre stands across from one of the few buildings with character, the town hall. 一座毫無生氣的購物中心對面就是少有的幾個別具特色的建築物之一：市政廳。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>character</b>, you mean that they are interesting, unusual, or amusing. (風趣、與眾不同的) 人物","examples":["He's a nut, a real character. 他是個怪人，一個真正與眾不同的人。"]}]}]},"citizen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"市民，城鎮居民；公民，國民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>citizen</b> of a particular country is legally accepted as belonging to that country. 公民","examples":["...American citizens. …美國公民。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>citizens</b> <b>of</b> a town or city are the people who live there. 市民","examples":["...the citizens of Buenos Aires. …布宜諾斯艾利斯的市民。"]}]}]},"choice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選擇，抉擇；選擇的機會，選擇權；選擇範圍，選擇餘地；入選者，被選中的東西；精選品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"上等的，優質的；尖刻的，刻薄的；精選的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>choice</b> <b>of</b> things, there are several of them and you can choose the one you want. 選擇","examples":["It's available in a choice of colours. 它有多種顏色可供選擇。","At lunchtime, there's a choice between the buffet or the set menu. 午飯時，可以選擇自助餐或套餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>choice</b> is someone or something that you choose from a range of things. 所挑選的人或物","examples":["Although he was only grumbling, his choice of words made Rodney angry. 儘管他只是在發牢騷，但他所用的字眼卻讓羅德尼很生氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Choice</b> means of very high quality. 優質的","examples":["...a box of their choicest chocolates. …他們的一盒上等巧克力。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have no choice</b> <b>but</b> to do something or <b>have little choice</b> <b>but</b> to do it, you cannot avoid doing it. 無選擇餘地","examples":["They had little choice but to agree to what he suggested. 除了同意他的意見，他們別無選擇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The thing or person <b>of</b> your <b>choice</b> is the one that you choose. 自己挑選的","examples":["...tickets to see the football team of your choice. …觀看你所中意的足球隊的門票。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The item <b>of choice</b> is the one that most people prefer. 受多數人歡迎的","examples":["The drug is set to become the treatment of choice for asthma worldwide. 這種藥就要成為全世界治療哮喘的首選藥物。"]}]}]},"charge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"充電；使……承擔責任，賦予……責任；控告，指控；（公開）指責，責備；進攻，衝鋒；把……記在賬上；要價，收費（金額）；<舊>給（槍炮）裝彈；斟滿（杯子）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電量，電荷；炸藥量；掌管，照管；費用，價錢；控告，指控；（書面或口頭的）指責，批評；需要照管的人；命令，指示；（人或動物的）猛攻，衝鋒；<美，非正式>快感，刺激；感召力，感染力；負載"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>charge</b> someone an amount of money, you ask them to pay that amount for something that you have sold to them or done for them. 要價; 收費","examples":["Even local nurseries charge $150 a week. 即便當地的託兒所每週也要收$150的費用。","Some banks charge if you access your account to determine your balance. 如果你進入自己的賬戶檢視餘額，有些銀行要收費。","The architect charged us a fee of seven hundred and fifty dollars. 建築師向我們收取了750美元的費用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>charge</b> something <b>to</b> a person or organization means to tell the people providing it to send the bill to that person or organization. To <b>charge</b> something <b>to</b> someone's account means to add it to their account so they can pay for it later. 開帳單; 記在…的賬上","examples":["Go out and buy a pair of glasses, and charge it to us. 出去買一副眼鏡，記在我們的賬上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When the police <b>charge</b> someone, they formally accuse them of having done something illegal. 指控","examples":["They have the evidence to charge him. 他們有證據來指控他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>charge</b> a battery means to pass an electrical current through it in order to make it more powerful or to make it last longer. 給…充電","examples":["Alex had forgotten to charge the battery. 亞歷克斯忘了給電池充電。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>charge</b> toward someone or something, you move quickly and aggressively toward them. 衝","examples":["He charged through the door to my mother's office. 他破門而入，進了我母親的辦公室。","He ordered us to charge. 他命令我們衝鋒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Charge</b> is also a noun. 衝","examples":["...a bayonet charge. …一次刺刀衝鋒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>charge</b> is an amount of money that you have to pay for a service. 費用","examples":["We can arrange this for a small charge. 我們收取少量的費用就可以安排這事"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>charge</b> is a formal accusation that someone has committed a crime. 指控","examples":["He may still face criminal charges. 他也許仍舊要面對刑事指控。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as your <b>charge</b>, they have been given to you to be taken care of and you are responsible for them. 受照料者","examples":["The coach tried to get his charges motivated. 該教練設法激勵他的隊員們。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An electrical <b>charge</b> is an amount of electricity that is held in or carried by something. 負荷","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you take <b>charge</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you make yourself responsible for them and take control over them. If someone or something is <b>in</b> your <b>charge</b>, you are responsible for them. 掌管; 負責","examples":["A few years ago Bacryl took charge of the company. 幾年前巴克萊爾掌管這家公司。","I have been given charge of this class. 我受命負責這個班。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Charge up</b> means the same as . 給…充電","examples":["There was nothing in the brochure about having to drive it every day to charge up the battery. 手冊裡沒寫它要每天開，給電池充電。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in charge</b> in a particular situation, you are the most senior person and have control over something or someone. 負責","examples":["Who's in charge here? 這裡誰負責？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>free of charge</b>, it does not cost anything. 免費","examples":["The leaflet is available free of charge from post offices. 小冊子可免費向郵局索取。"]}]}]},"change":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"改變，變化；更換，替換；換乘；兌換，找零；交換，互換"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"變化，變革；找回的錢，零錢；換乘；替代物，替換衣物；全新體驗；轉成新月；鐘樂敲打的一種套路"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>change</b> <b>in</b> something, it becomes different. 變化","examples":["The ambassador appealed for a change in U.S. policy. 該大使呼籲美國政策的變革。","There are going to have to be some drastic changes. 一定得有些重大變革。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>change</b> or <b>makes</b> a <b>change</b>, you mean that it is enjoyable because it is different from what you are used to. 改進","examples":["It is a complex system, but it certainly makes a change. 這是個複雜系統，但肯定有所改進。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Change</b> is also a noun. 更換","examples":["A change of leadership alone will not be enough. 僅僅更換領導將是不夠的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>change of</b> clothes is an extra set of clothes that you take with you when you go to stay somewhere or to take part in an activity. 替換 (衣服)","examples":["He stuffed a bag with a few changes of clothing. 他往包裡塞了幾件替換衣服。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>change</b> is the money that you receive when you pay for something with more money than it costs because you do not have exactly the right amount of money. 找回的錢","examples":["\"There's your change.\"—\"Thanks very much.\" “那是找你的錢。”— “非常感謝。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Change</b> is coins, rather than paper money. 硬幣","examples":["Thieves ransacked the office, taking a sack of loose change. 竊賊們洗劫了辦公室，拿走了一袋散幣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you have <b>change</b> <b>for</b> larger bills or coins, you have the same value in smaller bills or coins, which you can give to someone in exchange. 零錢","examples":["The courier had change for a $10 bill. 快遞員有$10的零錢。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>change</b> <b>from</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you stop using or doing the first one and start using or doing the second. 改換","examples":["His physician modified the dosage but did not change to a different medication. 他的醫生調整了劑量，但沒有改換成別的藥方。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>changes</b> or when you <b>change</b> it, it becomes different. 改變; 變化","examples":["We are trying to detect and understand how the climates change. 我們在努力探測並瞭解氣候是怎樣變化的。","In the union office, the mood gradually changed from resignation to rage. 在工會辦公室，情緒漸漸由依從變成了憤怒。","She has now changed into a happy, self-confident woman. 她現在已經變成了一個快樂、自信的女人。","They should change the law to make it illegal to own replica weapons. 他們應該修改法律，使擁有模擬武器非法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>change</b> something means to replace it with something new or different. 更換","examples":["I paid $80 to have my car radio fixed and I bet all they did was change a fuse. 我付了$80修車裡的收音機，我敢斷定他們只是換了根保險絲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> your clothes or <b>change</b>, you take some or all of your clothes off and put on different ones. 更換 (衣服); 更衣","examples":["Ben had merely changed his shirt. 本只換了他的襯衫。","They had allowed her to shower and change. 他們已允許她沐浴更衣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> a bed or <b>change</b> the sheets, you take off the dirty sheets and put on clean ones. 更換 (床單)","examples":["After changing the bed, I would fall asleep quickly. 更換床單後，我會很快入睡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> a baby or <b>change</b> its diaper, you take off the dirty one and put on a clean one. 給…換 (尿布)","examples":["She criticizes me for the way I feed or change him. 她批評我喂他或給他換尿布的方法。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> buses, trains, or planes or <b>change</b>, you get off one bus, train, or plane and get on to another in order to continue your journey. 換乘","examples":["At Glasgow I changed trains for Greenock. 在格拉斯哥我換乘去格里諾克的火車。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> gear or <b>change</b> into another gear, you move the gear lever on a car, bicycle, or other vehicle in order to use a different gear. 換 (擋); (車擋) 變換","examples":["He changes gear and pulls away slowly. 他換了擋，慢慢把車開走了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"When you <b>change</b> money, you exchange it for the same amount of money in a different currency, or in smaller bills or coins. 兌換","examples":["You can expect to pay the bank a fee of around 1% to 2% every time you change money. 每次兌換錢時，你要準備支付銀行約1%至2%的費用。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make change</b>, you give someone smaller bills or coins, in exchange for the same value of larger ones. 換零錢","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are doing something or something is happening <b>for a change</b>, you mean that you do not usually do it or it does not usually happen, and you are happy to be doing it or that it is happening. 變換一下","examples":["Now let me ask you a question, for a change. 換一下，現在讓我來問你一個問題。"]}]}]},"clap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拍手，鼓掌；快速（或用力）放置；輕拍（背或肩膀）；使……砰然相擊；（突然）把……關進監獄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼓掌，拍手；砰然巨響，霹靂聲；（友好的）用手輕拍；<非正式>淋病"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>clap</b>, you hit your hands together to express appreciation or attract attention. 拍 (手); 鼓掌","examples":["The men danced and the women clapped. 男人們跳舞，女人們鼓掌。","Midge clapped her hands, calling them back to order. 米琪拍著手，叫他們恢復秩序。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>clap</b> your hand or an object onto something, you put it there quickly and firmly. 猛然放置","examples":["I clapped a hand over her mouth. 我猛地用一隻手捂住了她的嘴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to make or cause to make a sharp abrupt sound, as of two nonmetallic objects struck together (兩個非金屬物相撞時)發出尖銳、突發的聲音","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clap of thunder</b> is a sudden and loud noise of thunder. 轟隆的雷聲","examples":[]}]}]},"circle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圓，圓形物；圈子，階層；弧形樓座；黑眼圈；迴圈，週期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"盤旋，環行；圍繞，圈起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>circle</b> is a shape consisting of a curved line completely surrounding an area. Every part of the line is the same distance from the centre of the area. 圓圈","examples":["The flag was red, with a large white circle in the centre. 那面旗子是紅色的，中間有一個白色的大圓圈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>circle</b> <b>of</b> something is a round, flat piece or area of it. 圓盤狀物","examples":["Cut out 4 circles of pastry. 切出4塊圓形油酥麵餅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>circle</b> <b>of</b> objects or people is a group of them arranged in the shape of a circle. 圈","examples":["...a circle of gigantic stones. …一圈巨石。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people as a <b>circle</b> when they meet each other regularly because they are friends or because they belong to the same profession or share the same interests. (相同興趣、職業等的人形成的) 圈子","examples":["He has a small circle of friends. 他有一個小小的朋友圈子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>circles</b> an object or a place, or <b>circles</b> <b>around</b> it, it forms a circle around it. 環繞","examples":["This is the road that circles the city. 這就是那條環城路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an aircraft or a bird <b>circles</b> or <b>circles</b> something, it moves around in a circle in the air. 圍著…轉圈; 盤旋","examples":["The plane circled, awaiting permission to land. 飛機盤旋著，等待著陸指令。","There were two helicopters circling around. 有兩架直升飛機在周圍盤旋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>circle</b> something on a piece of paper, you draw a circle around it. 把…圈出來","examples":["Circle the words on this list that you recognize. 把這張表上你認識的字圈出來。"]}]}]},"clay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黏土，陶土；（網球場的）硬固泥地，紅土網球場；<文>肉體；似黏土的東西；黃棕翼歐洲蛾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用黏土處理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clay</b> is a kind of earth that is soft when it is wet and hard when it is dry. Clay is shaped and baked to make things such as pots and bricks. 黏土","examples":["...the heavy clay soils of Georgia. …佐治亞州厚重的黏土的土壤。","As the wheel turned, the potter shaped and squeezed the lump of clay into a graceful shape. 隨著輪盤的轉動，陶工把那塊黏土塑造、擠捏成了一個優雅的造型。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In tennis, matches played on <b>clay</b> are played on courts whose surface is covered with finely crushed stones or brick. 紅土網球場","examples":["Most tennis is played on hard courts, but a substantial amount is played on clay. 大多數網球是在硬地球場上打，但相當多的是在紅土場地上打。"]}]}]},"claw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動物的）爪，爪子；（水生有殼動物的）螯，鉗；爪形器具，鉗形工具"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用爪）撕，抓；撓癢；（帆船）迎風而行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>claws</b> of a bird or animal are the thin, hard, curved nails at the end of its feet. (鳥、動物的) 爪","examples":["The cat tried to cling to the edge by its claws. 那隻貓試圖用爪子抓緊邊沿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>claws</b> of a lobster, crab, or scorpion are the two pointed parts at the end of its legs which are used for holding things. (龍蝦、蟹、蠍的) 鉗子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an animal <b>claws</b> <b>at</b> something, it scratches or damages it with its claws. (用爪) 抓","examples":["The wolf clawed at the tree and howled the whole night. 那隻狼在那顆樹上抓撓，還嗥叫了整整一個晚上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>claw</b> <b>at</b> something mean to try very hard to get hold of it. 用力抓住","examples":["His fingers clawed at Blake's wrist. 他的手指使勁抓住布萊克的手腕。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>claw</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you move there with great difficulty, trying desperately to find things to hold on to. (抓著東西艱難地) 挪到","examples":["From the flooded depths of the ship, some did manage to claw their way up iron ladders to the safety of the upper deck. 從被洪水淹了的船的深處，一些人著實艱難地爬上鐵梯來到上層甲板的安全處。"]}]}]},"classic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"典型的，有代表性的；一流的，經典的；古樸的，典雅的；<非正式>糟糕的，討厭的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"經典作品，傑作；傑出的事物，典範；傳統活動，傳統專案"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>classic</b> example of a thing or situation has all the features which you expect such a thing or situation to have. 典型的","examples":["The debate in the press has been a classic example of hypocrisy. 新聞界的這場爭論是虛偽的典型例子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>classic</b> film, piece of writing, or piece of music is of very high quality and has become a standard against which similar things are judged. 經典的","examples":["...the classic children's film Huckleberry Finn. …經典的兒童影片《哈克貝利•芬》。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Classic</b> is also a noun. 典範","examples":["It was a classic of interrogation: first the bully, then the kind one who offers sympathy. 這是審問的一種典範：開始是欺負人的人，然後那個和善的人再施予同情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Classic</b> is also a noun. 經典","examples":["The record won a gold award and remains one of the classics of modern popular music. 該唱片獲得過金獎，而且依舊是現代流行音樂的經典作品之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>classic</b> is a book which is well-known and considered to be of a high literary standard. You can refer to such books generally as <b>the classics</b>. 文學名著","examples":["As I grow older, I like to reread the classics regularly. 隨著我年齡的增長，我喜歡定期重讀文學名著。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Classics</b> is the study of the ancient Greek and Roman civilizations, especially their languages, literature, and philosophy. 古典學","examples":["...a Classics degree. …古典學學位。"]}]}]},"cleaner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"清潔工人；清潔劑，去汙劑；清潔器，清潔裝置；乾洗店（the cleaner's/cleaners）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"更清潔的，更乾淨的（clean 的比較級形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cleaner</b> is someone who is employed to clean the rooms and furniture inside a building. 清潔工","examples":["...the prison hospital where Sid worked as a cleaner. …錫德做清潔工的那家監獄醫院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cleaner</b> is someone whose job is to clean a particular type of thing. (清掃特定物品的) 清潔工","examples":["He was a window cleaner. 他是一名窗戶清潔工。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cleaner</b> is a device used for cleaning things. 清潔器","examples":["...an air cleaner. …空氣清新器。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>cleaner</b> or a <b>cleaner's</b> is a shop where things such as clothes are dry-cleaned. 乾洗店","examples":["Did you pick up my suit from the cleaner's? 你順便從乾洗店取我的西裝了嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>cleaner</b> is a substance used for cleaning things. 去汙劑","examples":["...oven cleaner. …烤箱去汙劑。"]}]}]},"clerk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"辦事員，職員；售貨員，店員；（賓館）接待員；（法庭、市政會等負責管理文書的）文書，書記員；<舊>（英國國教會的）牧師；<古>讀書識字的人，學者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當職員（或文書、書記員）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clerk</b> is a person who works in an office, bank, or law court and whose job is to keep the records or accounts. 文書; (法庭) 書記員","examples":["She was offered a job as a clerk with a travel agency. 她找到了在一家旅行社做文書的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a hotel, office, or hospital, a <b>clerk</b> is the person whose job is to answer the telephone and deal with people when they arrive. 接待員","examples":["...a hotel clerk. …一名賓館接待員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>clerk</b> is someone who sells things to customers in a shop. 售貨員","examples":["Now Thomas was working as a clerk in a shop that sold leather goods. 現在托馬斯在一家賣皮革品的店裡做售貨員。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clerk</b> means to work as a clerk. 做文書工作","examples":["Gene clerked at the auction. 吉恩在拍賣行做文書工作。"]}]}]},"claim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聲稱，斷言；索取，索要（錢）；要求（擁有），認領；使喪生，致命；贏得，獲得；值得，需要（花時間或精力）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聲稱，斷言；索要，索賠；權利，所有權；要求得到的土地使用權；專利新特徵申明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>claims</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you mean they say that it is true but you are not sure whether or not they are telling the truth. 聲稱","examples":["He claimed that it was all a conspiracy against him. 他聲稱這完全是一個針對他的陰謀。","A man claiming to be a journalist threatened to reveal details about her private life. 一個自稱是記者的男人威脅要公開她的私生活細節。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>claims</b> responsibility or credit for something, you mean they say that they are responsible for it, but you are not sure whether or not they are telling the truth. 聲稱 (對某事負責或應得榮譽)","examples":["An underground organization has claimed responsibility for the bomb explosion. 一個地下組織已聲稱對炸彈爆炸事件負責。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>claim</b> something, you try to get it because you think you have a right to it. 索取","examples":["Now they are returning to claim what was theirs. 現在他們回來索要原本屬於他們的東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>claims</b> a record, title, or prize, they gain or win it. 贏得","examples":["Zhuang claimed the record in 54.64 seconds. 莊創造了54.64秒的紀錄。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something or someone <b>claims</b> your attention, they need you to spend your time and effort on them. 需要","examples":["There is already a long list of people claiming her attention. 已經有太多人需要她的關注了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>claim</b> money from the government, an insurance company, or another organization, you officially apply to them for it, because you think you are entitled to it according to their rules. 索賠","examples":["Some 25 percent of the people who are entitled to claim benefits do not do so. 大約25℅有資格索賠的人沒有那樣做。","John had taken out insurance but when he tried to claim, the insurance company refused to pay. 約翰拿出保險單，但當他試圖索賠時，保險公司卻拒絕賠付。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>claim</b> money or other benefits from your employers, you demand them because you think you deserve or need them. 索要","examples":["The union claimed a raise worth four times the rate of inflation. 工會要求增長4倍於通貨膨脹率的工資。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that a war, disease, or accident <b>claims</b> someone's life, you mean that they are killed in it or by it. 奪走 (生命)","examples":["The civil war claimed the life of a U.N. interpreter yesterday. 昨天內戰奪走了一位聯合國譯員的生命。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Claim</b> is also a noun. 索賠","examples":["Last time we made a claim on our insurance, they paid up really quickly. 上次我們依據保險提出索賠時，他們賠付得很快。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Claim</b> is also a noun. 索要","examples":["They are making substantial claims for improved working conditions. 他們就改善工作條件提出了實質性要求。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>claim</b> is something which someone says which they cannot prove and which may be false. 聲稱","examples":["He repeated his claim that the people of Trinidad and Tobago backed his action. 他再三重複他所聲稱的：千里達及托巴哥的人民支援他的行動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>claim</b> is a demand for something that you think you have a right to. 索要","examples":["Rival claims to Macedonian territory caused conflict in the Balkans. 對馬其頓領土的爭奪導致了巴爾幹地區的衝突"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have a <b>claim on</b> someone or their attention, you have the right to demand things from them or to demand their attention. 索求權","examples":["She had no claims on him now. 現在她無權向他索取什麼了。"]}]}]},"cloth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"布，布料；一塊布，（尤指）一塊抹布；牧師，神父"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"布制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cloth</b> is fabric which is made by weaving or knitting a substance such as cotton, wool, silk, or nylon. Cloth is used especially for making clothes. 布","examples":["She began cleaning the wound with a piece of cloth. 她開始用一塊布清潔傷口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cloth</b> is a piece of cloth which you use for a particular purpose, such as cleaning something or covering something. (有特定用途的) 布","examples":["Clean the surface with a damp cloth. 用一塊溼布清洗表面。"]}]}]},"climate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣候；氣候區；氛圍，局勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>climate</b> of a place is the general weather conditions that are typical of it. 氣候","examples":["...the hot and humid climate of Florida. …佛羅里達炎熱潮溼的氣候。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>climate</b> to refer to the general atmosphere or situation somewhere. 氛圍; 形勢","examples":["The economic climate remains uncertain. 經濟氣候依然是不確定。","...the existing climate of violence and intimidation. … 現有的暴力與恐嚇的氛圍。"]}]}]},"clown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小丑；愛開玩笑的人，詼諧的人；蠢貨；<古>鄉下人，鄉巴佬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扮小丑，裝傻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clown</b> is a performer in a circus who wears funny clothes and bright makeup, and does silly things in order to make people laugh. 小丑","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>clown</b>, you mean that they say funny things or do silly things to amuse people. 滑稽的人","examples":["Chapman was the family clown, with a knack for making a joke out of any situation. 查普曼是家裡的詼諧人物，他有訣竅在任何場合開玩笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>clown</b>, you do silly things in order to make people laugh. 扮演小丑","examples":["He clowned with John Belushi and Bill Murray in National Lampoon shows. 他與約翰·貝魯西和比爾·默裡在全國諷刺作品表演會上一起扮演小丑。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clown around</b> means the same as . 扮演小丑","examples":["Bev made her laugh, the way she was always clowning around. 貝芙令她大笑，用她常用的扮小丑手法。"]}]}]},"clothing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣服，（尤指某種）服裝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……穿衣，為……提供衣服，賦予（某人某品質）（clothe 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clothing</b> is the things that people wear. 衣服","examples":["Some locals offered food and clothing to the refugees. 一些當地人向難民提供食物和衣服。","...the clothing industry. …服裝業。"]}]}]},"closet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壁櫥，儲藏室；隱秘狀態（尤指同性戀身份）；<古>盥洗室，廁所"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……關在房間；把……帶入房間密談"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"秘密的，不公開的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>closet</b> is a very small room for storing things, especially one without windows. 儲藏室","examples":[]}]}]},"clothes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣服，衣物；（在特定場合、特定時間或由特定人群穿著的）服裝，禮服；被褥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clothes</b> are the things that people wear, such as shirts, coats, trousers, and dresses. 衣服","examples":["Moira walked upstairs to change her clothes. 莫伊拉上樓去換衣服了。"]}]}]},"cockroach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蟑螂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cockroach</b> is a large brown insect that is sometimes found in warm places or where food is kept. 蟑螂","examples":[]}]}]},"cock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公雞；雄禽；<英>老兄，夥計；<英>雄龍蝦，雄螃蟹，雄鮭魚；<英，非正式>胡說，廢話；陰莖；龍頭，閥門；（槍的）擊鐵，撞針；頭目"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"豎起，歪著；扣（或扳）上扳機準備射擊；<英，非正式>把……搞糟，破壞（~ sth. up)；歪戴（帽子）；彎曲（臂、腿或關節）；（公狗）翹起（一條後腿）撒尿；大搖大擺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cock</b> is an adult male chicken. 公雞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to set the firing pin, hammer, or breech block of (a firearm) so that a pull on the trigger will release it and thus fire the weapon 扣扳機準備射擊","examples":[]}]}]},"coal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"煤；煤炭工業；（尤指燃燒著的）煤塊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"供煤；採煤，提煉煤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Coal</b> is a hard, black substance that is extracted from the ground and burned as fuel. 煤","examples":["Gas is cheaper than coal. 煤氣比煤便宜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Coals</b> are burning pieces of coal. 燃燒著的煤塊","examples":["The iron teakettle was hissing splendidly over live coals. 鐵茶壺在熊熊燃燒著的煤塊上“嘶嘶”作響。"]}]}]},"coach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教練；私人教師；長途客車，長途汽車；火車車廂；四輪大馬車；（飛機）經濟艙，（火車）普通車廂；<美>（體育隊的）領隊；（棒球運動中的）跑壘指揮員；教練"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"訓練，指導；（尤指私人）輔導；指示，專門傳授；乘火車（或汽車、馬車）旅行"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美>乘（飛機、火車的）經濟艙地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is someone who trains a person or team of people in a particular sport. 教練","examples":["Tony Woodcock has joined the team as coach. 託尼•伍德科克已經作為教練加入了隊伍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is a person who is in charge of a sports team. (體育隊的) 領隊","examples":["...the women's football coach at Rowan University. …羅恩大學女子足球隊的領隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is someone who gives people special teaching in a particular subject, especially in order to prepare them for an examination. (針對某科目，尤指進行考前指導的) 輔導員","examples":["What you need is a drama coach. 你需要的是一位戲劇指導。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is an enclosed vehicle with four wheels which is pulled by horses, and in which people used to travel. Coaches are still used for ceremonial events in some countries, such as Britain. (用於外出旅行或儀式活動的) 四輪馬車","examples":["...a coach pulled by six black horses. …一輛6匹黑馬拉的4輪馬車。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is a large, comfortable bus that carries passengers on long trips. 長途公共汽車; 大巴","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>coach</b> is one of the separate sections of a train that carries passengers. (火車的) 車廂","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>coaches</b> a person or a team, they help them to become better at a particular sport. (體育) 訓練","examples":["After her pro playing career, she coached a golf team in San Jose. 在職業球員生涯結束之後，她在聖何塞訓練一支高爾夫球隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>coach</b> someone, you give them special teaching in a particular subject, especially in order to prepare them for an examination. (針對某科目，尤指是考前進行的) 輔導","examples":["He gently coached me in French. 他和藹地輔導我法語。"]}]}]},"completion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"完成，結束；成功前傳；<英>（房地產等）完成交易，完成交割"}],"sections":[]},"coin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"硬幣，金屬貨幣；塔羅牌中的一種花色（coins）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"創造新詞，首次使用；鑄幣，造幣；<英，非正式>迅速而輕鬆地發財"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coin</b> is a small piece of metal which is used as money. 硬幣","examples":["...a few loose coins. …幾枚零錢。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>coin</b> a word or a phrase, you are the first person to say it. 創造 (新詞語)","examples":["Jaron Lanier coined the term \"virtual reality\" and pioneered its early development. 加隆·雷尼爾首創“虛擬現實”一詞，並率先進行早期開發。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>to coin a phrase</b>\" to show that you realize you are making a pun or using a cliché. 套用一個雙關語; 套用一句老話","examples":["Fifty local musicians have, to coin a phrase, banded together to form the Jazz Umbrella. 套用一句老話，５０位當地的音樂家們聯合在一起組成了爵士傘樂隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>the other side of the coin</b> to mention a different aspect of a situation. 另一方面","examples":["On the other side of the coin, there'll be tax incentives for small businesses. 另一方面，會有稅收政策激勵小型經營者。"]}]}]},"comb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"梳子；梳理；髮卡；梳狀物；雞冠；蜂巢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"梳，梳理；認真搜尋，仔細搜查；（浪）湧起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comb</b> is a flat piece of plastic or metal with narrow, pointed teeth along one side, which you use to make your hair neat. 梳子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>comb</b> your hair, you make it neat using a comb. 梳","examples":["Salvatore combed his hair carefully. 薩爾瓦多仔細地梳理了他的頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>comb</b> a place, you search everywhere in it in order to find someone or something. 徹底搜查","examples":["Officers combed the woods for the murder weapon. 警官們徹底搜查了那片樹林，尋找殺人兇器。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>comb</b> <b>through</b> information, you look at it very carefully in order to find something. 仔細檢視","examples":["Eight policemen then spent two years combing through the evidence. 8名警察後來用了兩年的時間仔細審查那些證據。"]}]}]},"computer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計算機，電腦，電子計算機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>computer</b> is an electronic machine that can store and deal with large amounts of information. 計算機","examples":["The data are then fed into a computer. 這些資料之後被輸入一臺計算機。","The company installed a $650,000 computer system. 該公司安裝了一套65萬美元的計算機系統。"]}]}]},"confucius":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孔子（中國哲學家，教育家）"}],"sections":[]},"club":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"俱樂部，社團；活動室，俱樂部大樓；職業運動俱樂部；夜總會；高爾夫球杆；擊棍；（紙牌中的）梅花"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"棒打；<非正式>泡夜總會；組成俱樂部；募集；集資"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is an organization of people interested in a particular activity or subject who usually meet on a regular basis. 會社","examples":["...the Young Republicans Club. … 青年共和黨會社。","...a youth club. …青年會社。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is a place where the members of a club meet. 俱樂部","examples":["I stopped in at the club for a drink. 我在俱樂部喝一杯歇歇腳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is a team which competes in sports competitions. 運動隊","examples":["...the New York Yankees baseball club. …紐約揚基棒球隊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is the same as a . 夜總會","examples":["It's a big dance hit in the clubs. 在各個夜總會這可是個熱門舞。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is a long, thin, metal stick with a piece of wood or metal at one end that you use to hit the ball in golf. 高爾夫球棒","examples":["...a six-iron club. …一把6號鐵頭球棒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is a thick, heavy stick that can be used as a weapon. 棍棒","examples":["Men armed with knives and clubs attacked his home. 一幫攜刀帶棍的人襲擊了他的家。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Clubs</b> is one of the four suits in a pack of playing cards. Each card in the suit is marked with one or more black symbols: ♣. (紙牌的) 梅花","examples":["...the ace of clubs. …梅花么。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>club</b> is a playing card of this suit. (單張) 梅花","examples":["The next player discarded a club. 接下來的那位玩家出了張梅花牌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>club</b> a person or animal means to hit them hard with a thick heavy stick or a similar weapon. (用棍棒或類似武器) 狠打","examples":["Two thugs clubbed him with baseball bats. 兩名暴徒用棒球棍狠打了他。"]}]}]},"congratulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恭喜，祝賀；恭賀，賀辭"}],"sections":[]},"company":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公司；陪伴，同伴；賓客，來賓；在一起的一群人；連隊；劇團，歌舞團；女童軍大隊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>結交，交往；<古>陪伴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>company</b> is a business organization that makes money by selling goods or services. 公司","examples":["Sheila found some work as a secretary in an insurance company. 希拉在一家保險公司找到了一份做秘書的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>company</b> is a group of opera singers, dancers, or actors who work together. 劇團","examples":["...the Phoenix Dance Company. …鳳凰舞蹈團。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>company</b> is a group of soldiers that is usually part of a battalion or regiment, and that is divided into two or more platoons. 連","examples":["The division will consist of two tank companies and one infantry company. 該師將由兩個坦克連和一個步兵連組成。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Company</b> is having another person or other people with you, usually when this is pleasant or stops you feeling lonely. 陪伴","examples":["\"I won't stay long.\"—\"No, please. I need the company.\" “我不會呆很久。” — “別，請別走。我需要陪伴。”","Ross had always enjoyed the company of women. 羅斯總是喜歡女人的陪伴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have company</b>, you have a visitor or friend with you. 有客人","examples":["He didn't say he had company. 他沒說他有客人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> someone <b>company</b>, you spend time with them and stop them from feeling lonely or bored. 陪某人做伴","examples":["Why don't you stay here and keep Emma company? 你為什麼不留在這兒陪埃瑪做伴？"]}]}]},"cooker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>炊具，鍋，廚灶；<英，非正式>適宜煮食而不宜生吃的水果（尤指某種蘋果）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cooker</b> is a large metal device for cooking food using gas or electricity. A cooker usually consists of an oven, a grill, and some gas burners or electric rings. 廚灶","examples":[]}]}]},"controller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"控制器，調節器；主管，管理員，控制者；主計長，財務總監；遊戲手柄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>controller</b> is a person who has responsibility for a particular organization or for a particular part of an organization. 主管","examples":["...the job of controller of BBC1. …BBC1的主管一職。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>controller</b> is the same as a . 審計員","examples":[]}]}]},"conflict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爭執，爭論，分歧；戰鬥，戰爭；牴觸，矛盾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"衝突，牴觸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conflict</b> is serious disagreement and argument about something important. If two people or groups are <b>in</b> <b>conflict</b>, they have had a serious disagreement or argument and have not yet reached agreement. 爭執; 分歧","examples":["Try to keep any conflict between you and your ex-partner to a minimum. 儘量把你和前合夥人之間的爭執控制到最少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Conflict</b> is a state of mind in which you find it impossible to make a decision. 矛盾心態","examples":["...the anguish of his own inner conflict. …他自己內心矛盾的痛苦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Conflict</b> is fighting between countries or groups of people. (國家或團體之間的) 衝突","examples":["...talks aimed at ending four decades of conflict. …旨在結束40年衝突的會談。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>conflict</b> is a serious difference between two or more beliefs, ideas, or interests. If two beliefs, ideas, or interests are <b>in</b> <b>conflict</b>, they are very different. (信念、觀點、利益之間的) 衝突","examples":["There is a conflict between what they are doing and what you want. 他們在做的和你想要的之間存在衝突。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If ideas, beliefs, or accounts <b>conflict</b>, they are very different from each other and it seems impossible for them to exist together or to each be true. (觀點、信念、陳述等) 相沖突","examples":["Personal ethics and professional ethics sometimes conflict. 個人道德與職業道德之間有時會相沖突。","He held firm opinions which usually conflicted with mine. 他持有堅定的、通常跟我的相沖突的觀點。"]}]}]},"conversation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（非正式的）談話，交談；<舊>社交，交際"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>conversation</b> <b>with</b> someone, you talk with them, usually in an informal situation. (非正式的) 交談","examples":["He's a talkative guy, and I struck up a conversation with him. 他是一個健談的人，我和他聊了起來。"]}]}]},"contact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯絡，聯絡；接觸，觸控；聯絡人，熟人，社會關係；會見，往來，接觸；傳染病接觸者；隱形眼鏡；接通電，觸點，接頭；（無線電）通訊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"聯絡，聯絡；接觸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"供聯絡的；接觸性的，透過接觸而起作用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Contact</b> involves meeting or communicating with someone, especially regularly. 往來","examples":["Opposition leaders are denying any contact with the government in Kabul. 反對黨領袖們在否認同喀布林政府有任何往來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you come <b>into contact with</b> someone or something, you meet that person or thing in the course of your work or other activities. (打) 交道","examples":["Doctors I came into contact with voiced their concern. 我打過交道的醫生們表達了他們的關注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people or things are in <b>contact</b>, they are touching each other. 接觸","examples":["They compared how these organisms behaved when left in contact with different materials. 他們比較了這些有機物在接觸不同材料時如何表現。","The cry occurs when air is brought into contact with the baby's larynx. 當空氣接觸到嬰兒的喉嚨時，哭聲就會響起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>contact</b> is someone you know in an organization or profession who helps you or gives you information. 聯絡人","examples":["Their contact at the United States embassy was Phillip Norton. 他們在美國大使館的聯絡人是菲利普·諾頓。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>contact</b> details or number are information such as a telephone number where you can be contacted. 聯絡用的","examples":["You must leave your full name and contact details when you phone. 你打電話時必須留下自己的完整姓名及用於聯絡的詳細資料。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in contact</b> <b>with</b> someone, you regularly meet them or communicate with them. 與…有聯絡","examples":["He was in direct contact with the kidnappers. 他與綁匪有直接聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make contact</b> <b>with</b> someone, you find out where they are and talk or write to them. （與某人）聯絡","examples":["How did you make contact with the author? 你怎麼跟這位作者聯絡的？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lose contact</b> <b>with</b> someone who you have been friendly with, you no longer see them, speak to them, or write to them. （與某人）失去聯絡","examples":["Though they all live nearby, I lost contact with them really quickly. 雖然他們都住在附近，我真地很快就與他們失去了聯絡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contact</b> someone, you telephone them, write to them, or go to see them in order to tell or ask them something. 聯絡","examples":["Contact the Women's Alliance for further details. 請聯絡婦女聯合會獲取詳情。"]}]}]},"cotton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棉，棉花；棉布；棉線，棉紗；脫脂棉，藥棉"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"棉的，棉製的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>開始領會，開始明白；<美，非正式>喜愛，喜歡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cotton</b> is a type of cloth made from soft fibres from a particular plant. 棉布","examples":["...a cotton shirt. …一件棉布襯衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cotton</b> is a plant which is grown in warm countries and which produces soft fibres used in making cotton cloth. 棉花","examples":["...a large cotton plantation in Tennessee. …位於田納西州的一個大棉花種植園。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Cotton</b> or <b>absorbent cotton</b> is a soft mass of cotton, used especially for applying liquids or creams to your skin. 脫脂棉; 藥棉","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Cotton</b> is thread that is used for sewing, especially thread that is made from cotton. 棉線","examples":[]}]}]},"countryside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鄉村，農村；鄉村居民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>countryside</b> is land which is away from towns and cities. 鄉村","examples":["I've always loved the English countryside. 我一直很喜歡英國的鄉村。"]}]}]},"county":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（英國、愛爾蘭的）郡，（美國的）縣；<英>郡運動隊，縣運動隊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英>有世家地位（或特點）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>county</b> is a region of the U.S., Britain, or Ireland, which has its own local government. (英國、愛爾蘭的) 郡; (美國的) 縣","examples":["He arrived at the Palm Beach County courthouse with his mother. 他和母親來到了棕櫚灘縣法院大樓。"]}]}]},"cough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"咳嗽；發出咳嗽般的聲音；<英，非正式>透露情報，供認；厲聲說出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"咳嗽（病）；咳，咳嗽聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>cough</b>, you force air out of your throat with a sudden, harsh noise. You often cough when you are ill, or when you are nervous or want to attract someone's attention. 咳嗽","examples":["Graham began to cough violently. 格雷厄姆開始劇烈地咳嗽。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cough</b> is also a noun. 咳嗽","examples":["Coughs and sneezes spread infections much faster in a warm atmosphere. 咳嗽和噴嚏在溫暖的空氣裡傳播疾病快得多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"咳嗽","examples":["He was then overcome by a terrible fit of coughing. 之後他一陣劇烈咳嗽，咳到無法控制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cough</b> is an illness in which you cough often and your chest or throat hurts. 咳嗽","examples":["I had a persistent cough for over a month. 我持續咳嗽已經一個多月了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cough</b> blood or mucus, it comes up out of your throat or mouth when you cough. 咳出 (血、痰等)","examples":["I started coughing blood so they transferred me to a hospital. 我開始咳血，所以他們把我送到了一家醫院。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cough up</b> means the same as . 咳嗽","examples":["On the chilly seas, Keats became feverish, continually coughing up blood. 在寒冷的海邊，濟慈開始發燒，不斷地咳血。"]}]}]},"copy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抄寫，謄寫；模仿，效法；作弊，抄襲；聽見（或明白）無線電收發報機中講話人的話；複製，複製"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一本，一冊，一份；影印件，副本；原稿，素材；廣告文字"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>copy</b> <b>of</b> something, you produce something that looks like the original thing. 複製品","examples":["The reporter apparently obtained a copy of Steve's resignation letter. 記者顯然得到了史蒂夫辭職信的復件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>copy</b> <b>of</b> a book, newspaper, or CD is one of many that are exactly the same. 一份 (書籍、報紙、CD等)","examples":["I bought a copy of \"USA Today\" from a street-corner machine. 我從售貨機上買了一份《今日美國》。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>copy</b> something, you produce something that looks like the original thing. 複製","examples":["...lawsuits against companies who have unlawfully copied computer programs. …對非法複製計算機程式的公司的訴訟。","He copied the chart from a book. 他從書上覆制了表格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>copy</b>, or <b>copy</b> a piece of writing, you write it again exactly. 抄寫","examples":["He copied the data into a notebook. 他把資料抄在了筆記本上。","We're copying from textbooks because we don't have enough to go round. 我們在抄寫課本，因為不夠每人一本。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>copy</b> a letter, document, or e-mail to someone, you send them a copy of a letter or document that you have sent to someone else. 抄送","examples":["He fired off a letter and copied it to the president. 他發出了一封信，並且抄送給了總裁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>copy</b> someone's answer, you look at what that person has written and write the same thing yourself, in order to cheat in a test or exam. 抄襲","examples":["He would allow John slyly to copy his answers to impossibly difficult algebra questions. 對於那些特別難的代數題，他允許約翰偷偷抄襲他的答案。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>copy</b> a person or what they do, you try to do what they do or try to be like them, usually because you admire them or what they have done. 效仿","examples":["Children can be seen to copy the behaviour of others whom they admire or identify with. 可以看到兒童效仿那些他們崇拜或認同的人。","He can claim to have been defeated by opponents copying his own tactics. 他可能會宣稱他已經被模仿他策略的對手打敗了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Copy out</b> means the same as . 抄寫","examples":["He wrote the title on the blackboard, then copied out the text, sentence by sentence. 他把題目寫在黑板上，然後一句一句地抄寫了整篇課文。"]}]}]},"courage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇氣，膽量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Courage</b> is the quality shown by someone who decides to do something difficult or dangerous, even though they may be afraid. 勇氣","examples":["General Lewis Mackenzie has impressed everyone with his authority and personal courage. 劉易斯·麥肯齊將軍以其權威和個人勇氣給每個人留下了深刻印象。"]}]}]},"control":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對國家、地區、機構等的）控制權，支配權；控制能力；操縱裝置；管理，管制；指揮（或檢查、控制）站，指揮（或檢查、控制）人員；（鍵盤上的）控制鍵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"控制，掌管；限制，限定；阻止蔓延（或惡化）；操縱，控制（機器或系統等）；抑制，剋制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Control</b> <b>of</b> an organization, place, or system is the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. (對某組織機構的) 控制","examples":["The restructuring involves Mr. Ronson giving up control of the company. 公司重組需要羅森先生放棄對公司的控制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>control</b> of something or someone, you are able to make them do what you want them to do. (對某物或某人的) 控制","examples":["He lost control of his car. 他失去了對他的車的控制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you show <b>control</b>, you prevent yourself behaving in an angry or emotional way. (對憤怒情緒等的) 剋制","examples":["He had a terrible temper, and sometimes he would completely lose control. 他脾氣暴躁，有時會完全失控。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Control</b> is also a noun. 管制","examples":["Control of inflation remains the government's absolute priority. 控制通貨膨脹仍然是政府的第一要務。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>control</b> is a device such as a switch or lever which you use in order to operate a machine or other piece of equipment. 控制裝置","examples":["I practised operating the controls. 我練習過操作這些控制裝置。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Controls</b> are the methods that a government uses to restrict increases, for example in prices, wages, or weapons. (政府的) 調控","examples":["Critics question whether price controls would do any good. 批評家們懷疑物價調控的作用。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Control</b> is used to refer to a place where your documents or luggage are officially checked when you enter a foreign country. 海關檢查處","examples":["He went straight through Passport Control without incident. 他順利透過了護照檢查。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>under</b> your <b>control</b>, you have the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. 處於…控制之下","examples":["All the newspapers are under government control. 所有的報紙都處在政府控制之下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in control</b> <b>of</b> something, you have the power to make all the important decisions about the way it is run. 掌管","examples":["Nobody knows who is in control of the club. 沒有人知道誰掌管這個俱樂部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>out of control</b>, no one has any power over it. 失控","examples":["The fire is burning out of control. 火勢失控。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something harmful is <b>under control</b>, it is being dealt with successfully and is unlikely to cause any more harm. 處在控制之下","examples":["The situation is under control. 局面得到了控制。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受控制的","examples":["...a controlled experiment. …一個受控制的試驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"剋制的","examples":["Her manner was quiet and very controlled. 她舉止恬靜很有涵養。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The people who <b>control</b> an organization or place have the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. 管理","examples":["He now controls the largest retail development empire in southern California. 他現在管理著加利福尼亞南部最大的零售業帝國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>control</b> a piece of equipment, process, or system means to make it work in the way that you want it to work. 控制 (裝置系統等)","examples":["...a computerized system to control the gates. …一個控制大門的計算機系統。","Scientists would soon be able to manipulate human genes to control the aging process. 科學家將很快能夠透過操控人類基因來控制衰老的過程。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a government <b>controls</b> prices, wages, or the activity of a particular group, it uses its power to restrict them. (政府) 管制 (價格、工資、團體活動等)","examples":["The federal government tried to control rising health-care costs. 聯邦政府努力控制不斷上漲的衛生保健費用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>control</b> <b>yourself</b>, or if you <b>control</b> your feelings, voice, or expression, you make yourself behave calmly even though you are feeling angry, excited, or upset. 抑制 (感情、聲音、表情)","examples":["Jo was advised to learn to control herself. 人們建議喬要學會控制自己的情緒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>control</b> something dangerous means to prevent it from becoming worse or from spreading. 抑制 (危險物)","examples":["...the need to control environmental pollution. …控制環境汙染的需要。"]}]}]},"corner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"角；嘴角，眼角；街角，拐角；角落，偏僻處；困境，窘境；角球；場角，場角的輔助人員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……逼入死角，使走投無路；硬要與某人說話；壟斷；轉彎，拐彎；囤積；相交成角"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>corner</b> is a point or an area where two or more edges, sides, or surfaces of something join. 角","examples":["He saw the corner of a magazine sticking out from under the blanket. 他看到毯子下露出了雜誌的一角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>corner</b> of a room, box, or similar space is the area inside it where its edges or walls meet. 角落","examples":["...a card table in the corner of the living room. …客廳角落裡的一張牌桌。","The ball hurtled into the far corner of the net. 球直飛入球門的遠角。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>corner</b> <b>of</b> your mouth or eye is the side of it. (眼睛、嘴巴的) 角","examples":["She flicked a crumb off the corner of her mouth. 她輕輕擦去了嘴角的麵包屑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>corner</b> of a street is the place where one of its sides ends as it joins another street. (街道的) 拐角","examples":["She would spend the day hanging around street corners. 她常一整天在街頭的各個角落閒逛。","We can't have police officers on every corner. 我們不可能在每一個路口都有警察。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>corner</b> is a bend in a road. (路的) 拐彎處","examples":["...a sharp corner. …一個急拐彎。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In football, hockey, and some other sports, a <b>corner</b> is a free shot or kick taken from the corner of the field. (足球、曲棍球等的) 角球","examples":["McPherson took the corner and James crashed his header off the crossbar and over the line. 麥克弗森踢了個角球，詹姆斯頭球頂出橫樑後出界。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>corner</b> a person or animal, you force them into a place they cannot escape from. 使走投無路","examples":["A police motorcycle chased his car twelve miles, and cornered him near Gainsborough. 一輛警車追蹤他的汽車12英里，在蓋恩斯堡附近把他逼得走投無路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>corner</b> someone, you force them to speak to you when they have been trying to avoid you. 強求與…交談","examples":["Thomas managed to corner the young producer-director for an interview. 湯馬斯纏著年輕的製片兼導演給了他一次面試的機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a company or place <b>corners</b> an area of trade, they gain control over it so that no one else can have any success in that area. 壟斷","examples":["Sony has cornered the market in chic-looking MP3 players. 索尼已經壟斷了時尚MP3播放器市場。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a car, or the person driving it, <b>corners</b> in a particular way, the car goes around bends in roads in this way. 轉彎","examples":["Peter drove jerkily, cornering too fast and fumbling the gears. 彼得開車很不平穩，轉彎太快，換檔也不熟練。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>around the corner</b>, you mean that it will happen very soon. 即將到來","examples":["Economic recovery is just around the corner. 經濟復甦即將到來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>around the corner</b>, you mean that it is very near. 在附近","examples":["My new place is just around the corner. 我的新房子就在附近。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>cut corners</b>, you do something quickly by doing it in a less thorough way than you should. 走捷徑","examples":["Take your time, don't cut corners, and follow instructions to the letter. 慢慢來，不要走捷徑。要嚴格按要求完成。"]}]}]},"crayon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"彩色粉筆（或炭筆、蠟筆）；彩色粉筆（或炭筆、蠟筆）畫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用彩色蠟筆畫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crayon</b> is a rod of coloured wax used for drawing. 彩色蠟筆","examples":[]}]}]},"crab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螃蟹，蟹肉；<美，非正式>脾氣乖戾的人，易怒的人；陰蝨病；起重機，絞車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"橫行，作蟹行；捕蟹，抓蟹；<美，非正式>抱怨，煩擾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crab</b> is a sea creature with a flat round body covered by a shell, and five pairs of legs with large claws on the front pair. Crabs usually move sideways. 螃蟹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Crab</b> is the flesh of this creature eaten as food. 蟹肉","examples":["I can't remember when I last had crab. 我不記得上次吃蟹是什麼時候了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"crab apple的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hunt or catch crabs 捕蟹","examples":[]}]}]},"couple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兩個，幾個；一對夫婦，一對情侶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加上，結合；（把裝置等）連線；形成一雙，配成一對；<舊>交配，交媾；（用電磁感應，靜電荷或光學通訊線路）將（電路元件）耦合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>a couple of</b> people or things, you mean two or approximately two of them, although the exact number is not important or you are not sure of it. 一兩個; 幾個","examples":["Across the street from me there are a couple of police officers standing guard. 我所在的街對面有一兩個警察在站崗。","I think the trouble will clear up in a couple of days. 我想幾天內麻煩就會消除。"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Couple</b> is also a determiner in spoken American English, and is often used before \"more\" and \"less.\" 幾個","examples":["...a couple weeks before the election. …選舉前的幾周。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Couple</b> is also a pronoun. 幾個","examples":["I've got a couple that don't look too bad. 我有幾個，看上去還不錯。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>couple</b> is two people who are married, living together, or having a sexual relationship. 一對夫婦","examples":["The couple have no children. 這對夫婦沒有孩子。","Burglars ransacked an elderly couple's home. 竊賊們洗劫了一對老夫婦的家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>couple</b> is two people that you see together on a particular occasion or that have some association. (特定場合或有特定聯絡的) 一對人","examples":["...as the four couples began the opening dance. …隨著4對舞伴跳起開場舞蹈。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing produces a particular effect when it <b>is coupled with</b> another, you mean that the two things combine to produce that effect. 與…結合","examples":["...a problem that is coupled with lower demand for the machines themselves. …一個與對機器本身需求量減少連在一起的問題。"]}]}]},"crane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鶴；起重機，吊車；機動升降臺架"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"伸長（脖子）看，探頭看；（用起重機）吊運；（行動前）遲疑，躊躇（crane at）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crane</b> is a large machine that moves heavy things by lifting them in the air. 起重機","examples":["The little prefabricated hut was lifted away by a huge crane. 那間小小的預製棚屋被一臺巨大的起重機吊走了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crane</b> is a kind of large bird with a long neck and long legs. 鶴","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>crane</b> your neck or head, you stretch your neck in a particular direction in order to see or hear something better. 伸長 (脖子)","examples":["She craned her neck to get a better view. 她伸長脖子以便看得清楚一些。","Children craned to get close to him. 孩子們伸長脖子想靠近他。"]}]}]},"cousin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"堂（表）兄弟，堂（表）姐妹；遠房親戚；兄弟民族（或國家）的人（來自不同國家但文化近似）；相似的人（物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>cousin</b> is the child of your uncle or aunt. 堂兄弟姐妹; 表兄弟姐妹","examples":["My cousin Mark helped me to bring in the bags. 我表弟馬克幫我把包提了進來。"]}]}]},"crime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"罪，罪行；犯罪，犯罪活動；可恥行為，錯誤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>（尤指在軍隊裡）指控……有罪，判……有罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crime</b> is an illegal action or activity for which a person can be punished by law. 罪行","examples":["He and Lieutenant Cassidy were checking the scene of the crime. 當時他正與卡西迪中尉一起檢查犯罪現場。","...the growing problem of organized crime. …越來越嚴重的有組織犯罪問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that doing something is a <b>crime</b>, you think it is very wrong or a serious mistake. 嚴重錯誤","examples":["It would be a crime to travel all the way to Australia and not stop in Sydney. 如果千里迢迢去澳大利亞而不在悉尼停留，那就是大錯特錯。"]}]}]},"crisis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"危機，緊要關頭；決定性時刻，關鍵時刻；（病情的）轉折點，危象"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用於處理危機的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crisis</b> is a situation in which something or someone is affected by one or more very serious problems. 危機","examples":["Natural disasters have obviously contributed to the continent's economic crisis. 自然災害顯然促使了該大陸的經濟危機。","...someone to turn to in moments of crisis. …在危機時刻可以向其求助的人。"]}]}]},"court":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"法院，法庭；球場；王宮，宮廷；朝臣；全體審判人員；庭院，院子；董事（會），理事（會）；（用於大型宅第和公寓街區的名稱中）宅第，公寓大樓"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"奉承，討好；設法取得，追求；招致，引起（不愉快的事）；談戀愛，求愛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>court</b> is a place where legal matters are decided by a judge and jury or by a magistrate. 法庭","examples":["At this rate, we could find ourselves in the divorce courts! 照這樣下去，我們可能會在離婚法庭上對簿公堂！","...a county court judge. …一名縣法院的法官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the people in a court, especially the judge, jury, or magistrates, as a <b>court</b>. (一次開庭的) 全體審判人員","examples":["A court at Tampa, Florida has convicted five officials on charges of handling millions of dollars earned from illegal drug deals. 佛羅里達州坦帕市的一個法庭宣佈被指控透過非法毒品買賣獲取上百萬美元的5名官員罪名成立。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>court</b> is an area in which you play a game such as tennis, basketball, badminton, or squash. 球場","examples":["The hotel has several tennis and squash courts. 該旅館有幾個網球場和壁球場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>court</b> of a king or queen is the place where he or she lives and carries out ceremonial or administrative duties. 王宮","examples":["She came to visit England, where she was presented at the court of James I. 她來訪問英格蘭，在詹姆斯一世的王宮受到了接見。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>go to court</b> or <b>take</b> someone <b>to court</b>, you take legal action against them. 起訴","examples":["They have received at least twenty thousand dollars each but went to court to demand more. 他們每人至少已經得到了兩萬美元，但還起訴以求得到更多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a legal matter is decided or settled <b>out of court</b>, it is decided without legal action being taken in a court of law. 不經法院庭審的","examples":["The Government is anxious to keep the whole case out of court. 政府急於把整個案子庭外了結。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>court</b> a particular person, group, or country means to try to please them or improve your relations with them, often so that they will do something that you want them to do. 討好; 取悅","examples":["Both Democratic and Republican parties are courting former supporters of Ross Perot. 民主黨和共和黨都在討好以前羅斯·佩羅的支持者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>court</b> something such as publicity or popularity, you try to attract it. 設法獲得","examples":["Having spent a lifetime avidly courting publicity, Paul has suddenly become secretive. 花了一生的時間狂熱地追求出名之後，保羅突然變得遮遮掩掩起來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>court</b> something unpleasant such as disaster or unpopularity, you act in a way that makes it likely to happen. 招致","examples":["If he thinks he can remain in power by force, he is courting disaster. 如果他認為可以透過武力維持權力的話，那就是在招災惹禍。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are courting</b> someone of the opposite sex, you spend a lot of time with them, because you are intending to get married. You can also say that a man and a woman <b>are courting</b>. 對…求愛; 談戀愛","examples":["I was courting Billy at 19 and married him when I was 21. 我19歲時和比利談戀愛，21歲時嫁給了他。"]}]}]},"cream":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奶油，乳脂；霜，膏；奶油色，淡黃色；含奶油食品；乳皮"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奶油色的，淡黃色的，米黃色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……攪成奶油狀；<美，非正式>輕易徹底打敗；狠撞；加奶油；捈乳霜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cream</b> is a thick yellowish-white liquid taken from milk. You can use it in cooking or put it on fruit or desserts. 奶油","examples":["...strawberries and cream. …草莓加奶油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cream</b> is used in the names of soups that contain cream or milk. 奶油湯","examples":["...cream of mushroom soup. …奶油蘑菇湯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cream</b> is a substance that you rub into your skin, for example, to keep it soft or to heal or protect it. 膏; 霜","examples":["Gently apply the cream to the affected areas. 輕輕地把藥膏塗抹於患處。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>cream</b> is yellowish-white in colour. 奶油色","examples":["...cream silk stockings. …乳白色的長筒絲襪。"]}]}]},"crop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"莊稼；（穀物或水果的）收成，產量；（同時湧現的）一批，一幫；平頭，短髮；（尤指頭髮）大量，豐富；短馬鞭；（鳥的）嗉囊；（農場一年的）牲口總數；鞣製的整張獸皮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"剪短；剪裁（照片）；（牲畜）啃吃（草）；種植（莊稼）；收穫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crops</b> are plants such as wheat and potatoes that are grown in large quantities for food. 莊稼","examples":["Rice farmers here still plant and harvest their crops by hand. 這裡的稻農仍然用手工種植和收割莊稼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The plants or fruits that are collected at harvest time are referred to as a <b>crop</b>. 收成","examples":["Each year it produces a fine crop of fruit. 每年這裡的水果收成都不錯。","The U.S. government says that this year's corn crop should be about 8 percent more than last year. 美國政府稱今年的玉米產量應該比去年增長約8﹪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>crop</b> is a short hairstyle. 短髮","examples":["She had her long hair cut into a boyish crop. 她讓人把她的長髮剪成了像男孩子的短髮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people or things that have appeared together as a <b>crop of</b> people or things. 一群 (人); 一堆 (物)","examples":["The present crop of books and documentaries about Marilyn Monroe exploit the thirtieth anniversary of her death. 現在這批有關瑪麗蓮·夢露的書籍和記錄片是借她去世三十週年紀念之機而發行的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a plant <b>crops</b>, it produces fruits or parts which people want. 收穫","examples":["Although these vegetables adapt well to our temperate climate, they tend to crop poorly. 雖然這些蔬菜能夠適應我們這裡的溫和氣候，但它們的產量常常不高。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>crop</b> someone's hair means to cut it short. 把…剪短","examples":["She cropped her hair and dyed it blonde. 她把頭髮剪短並染成了金色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>crop</b> a photograph, you cut part of it off, in order to get rid of part of the picture or to be able to frame it. 裁切","examples":["I decided to crop the picture just above the water line. 我決定把這張照片裁切到剛剛高於水位線的地方。"]}]}]},"culture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文化，文明；（團體或組織中共同的）態度，習俗；文化群落，（處於歷史上特定時期的）社會；藝術活動；修養；（細胞、細菌等的）培養，培養物；栽培，養殖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"培育，養殖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Culture</b> consists of activities such as the arts and philosophy, which are considered to be important for the development of civilization and of people's minds. 文化","examples":["There is just not enough fun and frivolity in culture today. 當今文化中太缺少樂趣和輕鬆。","...aspects of popular culture. …大眾文化的方方面面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>culture</b> is a particular society or civilization, especially considered in relation to its beliefs, way of life, or art. (與某種特定信仰、生活方式或藝術相連的) 社會或文明","examples":["...people from different cultures. …來自不同文化的人們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>culture</b> of a particular organization or group consists of the habits of the people in it and the way they generally behave. (組織或團體的) 習慣和行為方式","examples":["But social workers say that this has created a culture of dependency, particularly in urban areas. 但是社會工作者說，這造成了一種依賴習慣，在城區尤其如此。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In science, a <b>culture</b> is a group of bacteria or cells which are grown, usually in a laboratory as part of an experiment. 一組培養菌; 一組培養細胞","examples":["...a culture of human cells. …一組人類培養細胞。"]}]}]},"cure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥物，療法；對策，措施；治癒，治療；（對橡膠、塑膠或其他材料的）熟化；（基督教牧師的）牧師責任（或責任區）；教區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"治癒（病人），治好（疾病）；解決；控制，消除（不良的習慣、情感或態度）；加工貯藏；變乾硬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If doctors or medical treatments <b>cure</b> an illness or injury, they cause it to end or disappear. 治癒 (疾病、損傷)","examples":["An operation finally cured his shin injury. 手術最終治癒了他的脛骨損傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If doctors or medical treatments <b>cure</b> a person, they make the person well again after an illness or injury. 治癒 (病人)","examples":["It is an effective treatment and could cure all the leprosy sufferers worldwide. 那是一種有效的療法，可以治癒全世界的麻瘋病患者。","Almost overnight I was cured. 幾乎在一夜之間我被治癒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>cures</b> a problem, they bring it to an end. 解決","examples":["Private firms are willing to make large scale investments to help cure Russia's economic troubles. 私有公司願意進行大規模投資來幫助解決俄羅斯的經濟困難。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When food, tobacco, or animal skin <b>is cured</b>, it is dried, smoked, or salted so that it will last for a long time. 加工處理 (食物、菸草、動物皮等)","examples":["Legs of pork were cured and smoked over the fire. 豬腿在火上經過了煙燻處理。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cure</b> <b>for</b> an illness is a medicine or other treatment that cures the illness. (有治癒效果的) 藥物、療法","examples":["There is still no cure for a cold. 治感冒仍然沒有特效藥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cure</b> <b>for</b> a problem is something that will bring it to an end. 解決方法","examples":["The magic cure for inflation does not exist. 解決通貨膨脹的神奇方法並不存在。"]}]}]},"crowd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人群；一夥人；百姓，凡夫俗子；（尤指體育運動賽事的）觀眾，聽眾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"聚集，群集；靠近，盯著；催促，催逼（因而把人激怒或惹惱）；擠滿，塞滿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crowd</b> is a large group of people who have gathered together, for example, to watch or listen to something interesting, or to protest about something. 人群","examples":["A huge crowd gathered in a square outside the Kremlin walls. 一大群人聚集在了克里姆林宮牆外的廣場上。","It took some two hours before the crowd was fully dispersed. 用了大約兩個小時才把人群完全驅散。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>crowd</b> is a group of friends, or a set of people who share the same interests or job. 一幫 (朋友); 一群 (志趣相投的人)","examples":["All the old crowd have come out for this occasion. 所有老朋友都前來參加了這次活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an ancient bowed stringed instrument; crwth 克魯斯琴","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>crowd</b> <b>around</b> someone or something, they gather closely together around them. 聚集","examples":["The hungry refugees crowded around the tractors. 飢餓的難民們圍在拖拉機旁。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>crowd</b> <b>into</b> a place or <b>are crowded</b> <b>into</b> a place, large numbers of them enter it so that it becomes very full. 擠滿; 擠進","examples":["Hundreds of thousands of people have crowded into the centre of the Lithuanian capital, Vilnius. 幾十萬人湧進了立陶宛首都維爾紐斯的中心。","One group of journalists were crowded into a minibus. 一群記者擠滿了一輛麵包車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a group of people <b>crowd</b> a place, there are so many of them there that it is full. 擠滿","examples":["Thousands of demonstrators crowded the streets shouting slogans. 數千名示威者喊著口號，擠滿了街道。"]}]}]},"curtain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"窗簾，門簾；簾狀物，幕狀物（如濃煙或大雨等）；紗幔，帷幔；（舞臺上的）幕，幕布；開幕，落幕；災難性結局"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（窗戶或房間）裝上簾子；（用簾子）隔開，覆蓋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curtains</b> are pieces of material which you hang from the top of a window. 窗簾","examples":["Her bedroom curtains were drawn. 她臥室的窗簾拉上了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a theatre, <b>the curtain</b> is the large piece of material that hangs in front of the stage until a performance begins. 幕布","examples":["The curtain rises toward the end of the Prelude. 前奏接近尾聲時幕布升起。"]}]}]},"customer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧客；（某一型別的）傢伙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>customer</b> is someone who buys goods or services, especially from a shop. 顧客","examples":["...a satisfied customer. …一位滿意的顧客。","The quality of customer service is extremely important. 客戶服務質量極其重要。"]}]}]},"daily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每日的，日常的；一天的，按天計算的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每日，每天；日常地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"日報；<英>日工，女傭；（每天拍攝的）電影樣片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>daily</b>, it happens every day. 每天地","examples":["Cathay Pacific flies daily nonstop to Hong Kong. 國泰航空的航班每天直飛香港。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Daily</b> is also an adjective. 每天的","examples":["They held daily press briefings. 他們召開了每日例行的新聞釋出會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Daily</b> quantities or rates relate to a period of one day. 一天的","examples":["...a diet containing adequate daily amounts of fresh fruit. …包含一天足量新鮮水果的飲食。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>daily life</b> is the things that you do every day as part of your normal life. 日常生活","examples":["All of us in our daily life react favourably to people who take us and our views seriously. 日常生活中，對於那些認真對待我們和我們的意見的人，我們都會與之交好。"]}]}]},"custom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風俗，習俗；習慣；光顧，惠顧；<法律>慣例，習慣法；（經常性的）顧客"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"定做的，量身設計的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>custom</b> is an activity, a way of behaving, or an event which is usual or traditional in a particular society or in particular circumstances. 風俗","examples":["The custom of lighting the Olympic flame goes back centuries. 點燃奧運聖火的風俗可追溯到幾個世紀前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If it is your <b>custom</b> <b>to</b> do something, you usually do it in particular circumstances. 習慣","examples":["It was his custom to approach every problem cautiously. 謹慎地處理每個問題是他的習慣。"]}]}]},"data":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資料，資料；（儲存在計算機中的）資料資料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to information as <b>data</b>, especially when it is in the form of facts or statistics that you can analyse. 資料","examples":["The study was based on data from 2,100 women. 此項研究以從2100位女性身上獲得的資料為依據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Data</b> is information that can be stored and used by a computer program. 資料","examples":["This system uses powerful microchips to compress huge amounts of data onto a CD-ROM. 這一系統使用功能強大的微晶片來把大量資料壓縮到CD-ROM上。"]}]}]},"cross":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"反對；雜交；在（支票）上劃線（表示只能轉入銀行帳戶）；超過，超出（極限或範圍）；（表情）掠過，閃過；（基督教徒）畫十字；橫傳；（兩封來往的信）相互錯過，相互交錯；做鬥雞眼；穿越，橫渡；交叉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十字標記，十字形（或叉形）物；雜交，混合物；十字架；苦難；橫傳；（拳擊中的）鉤拳迎擊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"惱怒的；脾氣壞的，易怒的；（街道）交叉的，十字的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cross</b> something such as a room, a road, or an area of land or water, you move or travel to the other side of it. If you <b>cross</b> <b>to</b> a place, you move or travel over a room, road, or area of land or water in order to reach that place. 穿過; 穿過去","examples":["She was partly to blame for failing to look as she crossed the road. 她橫穿馬路時沒有看車，應承擔部分責任。","Egan crossed to the drinks cabinet and poured a Scotch. 伊根穿過去，來到酒櫃旁，倒了一杯蘇格蘭威士忌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A road, railway, or bridge that <b>crosses</b> an area of land or water passes over it. 橫跨","examples":["The road crosses the river half a mile outside the town. 這條路橫跨城外半英里處的那條河。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>crosses</b> a limit or boundary, for example, the limit of acceptable behaviour, they go beyond it. 越過 (可以被容忍的限度)","examples":["I normally never write into magazines but Mr. Stubbs has finally crossed the line. 我通常是從不給雜誌寫信的，但斯塔布斯先生最後太出格了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an expression <b>crosses</b> someone's face, it appears briefly on their face. 閃過","examples":["Berg tilts his head and a mischievous look crosses his face. 伯格歪著腦袋，一種淘氣的表情在他的臉上一閃而過。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>cross</b> your arms, legs, or fingers, you put one of them on top of the other. 交叉","examples":["Jill crossed her legs and rested her chin on one fist, as if lost in deep thought. 吉爾兩腿交叉，下巴抵在拳頭上，似乎陷入了沉思。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Lines or roads that <b>cross</b> meet and go across each other. 相交","examples":["...the intersection where Main and Centre streets cross. …主幹街和中心街相交的十字路口。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cross</b> is a shape that consists of a vertical line or piece with a shorter horizontal line or piece across it. It is the most important Christian symbol. 十字架 (基督教最重要的標誌)","examples":["Around her neck was a cross on a silver chain. 她脖子上戴著一個垂掛著十字架的銀鏈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cross</b> is a written mark in the shape of an X. You can use it, for example, to indicate that an answer to a question is wrong, to mark the position of something on a map, or to indicate your vote on a ballot. 叉形記號 (X)","examples":["Put a cross next to those activities you like. 在你喜歡的活動旁邊劃個叉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some team sports such as football and hockey, a <b>cross</b> is the passing of the ball from the side of the field to a player in the centre, usually in front of the goal. (足球、曲棍球等的) 橫傳","examples":["Johnson hit an accurate cross to Groves. 約翰遜將球精準地橫傳給格羅夫斯。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>a cross between</b> two things is neither one thing nor the other, but a mixture of both. 混合物","examples":["\"Ha!\" It was a cross between a laugh and a bark. “哈！”那是一種一半是笑一半是厲聲喊叫的混雜聲。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cross</b> street is a road that crosses another more important road. (與主要道路) 交叉的","examples":["The Army boys had personnel carriers blockading the cross streets. 士兵們用運兵車封堵了與主道交叉的道路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cross</b> is angry or irritated. 憤怒的","examples":["The women are cross and bored. 這些婦女們感到憤怒和厭煩。","I'm terribly cross with him. 我對他非常生氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"憤怒地","examples":["\"No, no, no,\" Morris said crossly. “不，不，不，”莫里斯憤怒地說。"]}]}]},"damage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（有形的）損壞，損失；損害，傷害；損害賠償金；費用，代價"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"損壞，損害；對……造成壞影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>damage</b> an object means to break it, spoil it physically, or stop it from working properly. 破壞; 損壞","examples":["He maliciously damaged a car with a baseball bat. 他用棒球棍惡意地損壞了一輛汽車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>damage</b> something means to cause it to become less good, pleasant, or successful. 損害; 傷害","examples":["...the electoral chaos that damaged Florida's reputation. …損害佛羅里達州聲譽的選舉騷亂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有損害性的","examples":["The weakened currency could have damaging effects for the economy. 貨幣貶值可能會對經濟造成破壞性的影響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Damage</b> is physical harm that is caused to an object. 破壞; 損壞","examples":["The blast had serious effects with quite extensive damage to the house. 爆炸影響嚴重，對房屋造成了大面積破壞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Damage</b> consists of the unpleasant effects that something has on a person, situation, or type of activity. 傷害","examples":["Incidents of this type cause irreparable damage to relations with the community. 此類事件對與該團體的關係造成不可挽回的傷害。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a court of law awards <b>damages</b> to someone, it orders money to be paid to them by a person who has damaged their reputation or property, or who has injured them. 賠償金","examples":["She is seeking more than $75,000 in damages. 她要求$75000以上的賠償金。"]}]}]},"dawn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"變得明朗，開始清楚；破曉，開始"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拂曉，黎明；曙光，開端"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dawn</b> is the time of day when light first appears in the sky, just before the sun rises. 黎明","examples":["Nancy woke at dawn. 天剛亮南希就醒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>dawn</b> <b>of</b> a period of time or a situation is the beginning of it. 開端","examples":["...the dawn of the radio age. …無線通訊時代的開端。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"開端","examples":["...the dawning of the space age. …太空時代的開始。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is dawning</b>, it is beginning to develop or come into existence. 開始","examples":["A new century was dawning. 一個新的世紀開始了。"]}]}]},"debt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"欠款，債務；負債情況；人情債"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>debt</b> is a sum of money that you owe someone. 債","examples":["Three years later, he is still paying off his debts. 三年後，他仍舊在還他的債務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Debt</b> is the state of owing money. 負債","examples":["...a monthly report on the amount of debt owed by consumers. …一份消費者欠款數額月報。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>debt</b> in expressions such as <b>I owe you a debt</b> or <b>I am in your debt</b> when you are expressing gratitude for something that someone has done for you. 人情債","examples":["He was so good to me that I can never repay the debt I owe him. 那時他對我太好了，我永遠都還不清欠他的人情債。","I owe a debt of thanks to Joyce Thompson, whose careful and able research was of great help. 我欠喬伊斯·湯普森一份感謝之情，他謹慎傑出的研究是極大的幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in debt</b> or <b>get into debt</b>, you owe money. If you are <b>out of debt</b> or <b>get out of debt</b>, you succeed in paying all the money that you owe. 負債; 還清債務","examples":["He was already deeply in debt through gambling losses. 賭博輸的錢讓他已經負債累累。"]}]}]},"dentist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牙科醫生；牙醫診所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dentist</b> is a medical practitioner who is qualified to examine and treat people's teeth. 牙科醫生","examples":["Visit your dentist twice a year for a checkup. 每年看兩次牙醫做檢查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The dentist</b> or <b>the dentist's</b> is used to refer to the office or clinic where a dentist works. 牙醫診所","examples":["It's worse than being at the dentist's. 這比在牙醫診所還要糟。"]}]}]},"debate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"討論，辯論"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"反覆思考，斟酌；討論，辯論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>debate</b> is a discussion about a subject on which people have different views. 辯論","examples":["An intense debate is going on within the Israeli government. 一場激烈的爭論正在以色列政府內部進行。","There has been a lot of debate among scholars about this. 在學者中有很多關於此問題的辯論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>debate</b> is a formal discussion, for example, in a parliament or institution, in which people express different opinions about a particular subject and then vote on it. (議會投票前的) 正式討論","examples":["He is expected to force a debate in Congress on his immigration reform. 他預期會推動一個關於他的移民改革的正式討論。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>debate</b> a topic, they discuss it fairly formally, putting forward different views. You can also say that one person <b>debates</b> a topic <b>with</b> another person. 辯論","examples":["The United Nations Security Council will debate the issue today. 聯合國安理會今天將辯論該問題。","Scientists were debating whether an asteroid was about to hit the Earth. 科學家們在爭論一顆小行星是否要撞上地球。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>debate</b> whether to do something or what to do, you think or talk about possible courses of action before deciding exactly what you are going to do. 考慮","examples":["Taggart debated whether to have yet another double vodka. 塔格特考慮著是否要再來一杯雙份伏特加。"]}]}]},"decision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"決定，抉擇；判決，裁定；果斷，決斷力；作決定，決策"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you make a <b>decision</b>, you choose what should be done or which is the best of various possible actions. 決定","examples":["I don't want to make the wrong decision and regret it later. 我不想作出錯誤的決定，以後後悔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Decision</b> is the act of deciding something or the need to decide something. 作決定","examples":["The growing pressures of the crisis may mean that the moment of decision can't be too long delayed. 這次危機不斷增長的壓力可能意味著作決定的時刻不會拖延很久。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Decision</b> is the ability to decide quickly and definitely what to do. 果斷","examples":["He is very quick-thinking and very much a man of decision. 他思維很敏捷，是個很果斷的人。"]}]}]},"degree":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"度，度數（溫度單位）；（角的）度，度數；學位課程，學位；程度；音級；次，次數；（形容詞或副詞的）級；共濟會職務；<舊>社會地位，官銜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>degree</b> to indicate the extent to which something happens or is the case, or the amount which something is felt. 程度","examples":["These man-made barriers will ensure a very high degree of protection for several hundred years. 這些人造屏障將會確保幾百年的高度保護。","Recent presidents have used television, as well as radio, with varying degrees of success. 新近的總統們已經利用了電視和收音機，取得了不同程度的成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>degree</b> is a unit of measurement that is used to measure temperatures. It is often written as °, for example, 23°. (指溫度) 度","examples":["It's over 80 degrees outside. 外面超過80度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>degree</b> is a unit of measurement that is used to measure angles, and also longitude and latitude. It is often written as °, for example, 23°. (指角度、經緯度) 度","examples":["It was pointing outward at an angle of 45 degrees. 它以45度角指向外側。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>degree</b> is a title or rank given by a university or college when you have completed a course of study there. It can also be given as an honorary title. 學位","examples":["...an engineering degree. …工程學學位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something has <b>a degree of</b> a particular quality, it has a small but significant amount of that quality. 一定程度的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>to some degree</b>, <b>to a large degree</b>, or <b>to a certain degree</b> in order to indicate that something is partly true, but not entirely true. 在某種程度上","examples":["These statements are, to some degree, all correct. 這些陳述在某種程度上都正確。"]}]}]},"department":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（組織或機構中的）部，司，系，處，科；（商場裡的）部；<非正式>專長，專責；（法國等國的）省"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>department</b> is one of the sections in an organization such as a government, business, or university. A department is also one of the sections in a large shop. (政府、企業等機構的) 部; (大學的) 系; (大型商店的) 部門","examples":["...the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services. …美國健康和公共事業部。","He moved to the sales department. 他調到了銷售部。"]}]}]},"delay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推遲，延期；延誤，耽擱；（故意）拖延，磨蹭"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"延期，推遲；延誤，耽擱；延遲器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>delay</b> doing something, you do not do it immediately or at the planned or expected time, but you leave it until later. 推遲","examples":["For sentimental reasons I wanted to delay my departure until June 1980. 由於感情上的原因，我想把啟程時間推遲到1980年6月。","They had delayed having children, for the usual reason, to establish their careers. 他們推遲了要孩子，為了要建立事業這個通常的理由。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>delay</b> someone or something means to make them late or to slow them down. 延誤; 耽擱","examples":["Can you delay him in some way? 你能用什麼辦法耽擱他一下嗎？","Various setbacks and problems delayed production. 各種各樣的挫折和問題延誤了生產。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>delay</b>, you deliberately take longer than necessary to do something. 拖延","examples":["If he delayed any longer, the sun would be up. 如果他再拖延下去，太陽就要升起來了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>delay</b>, something does not happen until later than planned or expected. 耽擱","examples":["They claimed that such a delay wouldn't hurt anyone. 他們聲稱這樣的耽擱不會傷害任何人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Delay</b> is a failure to do something immediately or in the required or usual time. 延誤","examples":["We'll send you a quote without delay. 我們會立即向你方報價。"]}]}]},"dessert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（正餐後的）甜點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dessert</b> is something sweet, such as fruit, pastry, or ice cream, that you eat at the end of a meal. 餐後甜點","examples":["She had homemade ice cream for dessert. 她吃了些自制冰淇淋當餐後甜點。"]}]}]},"dew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"露水；（似露珠的）小水珠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>用水珠弄溼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dew</b> is small drops of water that form on the ground and other surfaces outdoors during the night. 露水","examples":["The dew gathered on the leaves. 露水在葉片上聚集。"]}]}]},"desire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"願望，慾望，渴望；情慾，性慾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"渴望，想望；<正式>要求，請求；被……吸引，對……產生性慾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>desire</b> is a strong wish to do or have something. 願望","examples":["I had a strong desire to help and care for people. 我有一股強烈的幫助和關心別人的願望。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Desire</b> for someone is a strong feeling of wanting to have sex with them. 性慾","examples":["It's common to lose your sexual desire when you have your first child. 有了第一個孩子後，喪失性慾是常見的事。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>desire</b> something, you want it. 想要","examples":["She had remarried and desired a child with her new husband. 她再婚了，想跟新任丈夫生一個孩子。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"想要的; 渴望的","examples":["You may find that just threatening this course of action will produce the desired effect. 你會發現僅僅是威脅要採取這個行動就能產生想要的效果。"]}]}]},"depth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"深度，縱深；深刻，深奧；深厚，深切；（聲音的）低沉；濃度，強度；嚴重性，嚴峻性；淵博，老練；縱深感，景深；最深處，極限；低迷狀態，非常糟糕的狀態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>depth</b> of something such as a river or hole is the distance downward from its top surface, or between its upper and lower surfaces. 深度","examples":["The depth of the shaft is 520 yards. 這個通道的深度是520碼。","The smaller lake ranges from five to fourteen feet in depth. 這個較小的湖的深度在5至14英尺之間。","The depth of a standard straight valance is usually about 12 inches. 標準直邊床幔的高度通常是12英寸左右。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>depth</b> of something such as a wardrobe or drawer is the distance between its front surface and its back. 厚度","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an emotion is very strongly or intensely felt, you can talk about its <b>depth</b>. (感情的) 深厚","examples":["I am well aware of the depth of feeling that exists in Ontario. 我深知安大略人情感的深厚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>depth</b> of a situation is its extent and seriousness. 強烈程度","examples":["The country's leadership had underestimated the depth of the crisis. 這個國家的領導層低估了這次危機的嚴重程度。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>depth</b> of someone's knowledge is the great amount that they know. (知識的) 淵博","examples":["We felt at home with her and were impressed with the depth of her knowledge. 我們和她一見如故，並且被她知識的淵博所折服。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The depths</b> are places that are a long way below the surface of the sea or earth. (指遠離表面) 深處","examples":["Leaves, brown with long immersion, rose to the surface and vanished back into the depths. 長時間浸泡而成褐色的葉子浮上了水面，又消失在了水的深處。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you talk about <b>the depths of</b> an area, you mean the parts of it which are very far from the edge. (指距地區邊緣) 深處","examples":["...the depths of the countryside. …鄉村深處。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you are <b>in</b> <b>the depths of</b> an unpleasant emotion, you feel that emotion very strongly. (不快情緒的) 深重","examples":["I was in the depths of despair when the baby was terribly sick every day, and was losing weight. 寶寶每天都病得很重並且體重在下降的時候，我陷入絕望的深處。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you deal with a subject <b>in depth</b>, you deal with it very thoroughly and consider all the aspects of it. 全面透徹地","examples":["We will discuss these three areas in depth. 我們將全面透徹地討論這3個領域。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>out of</b> their <b>depth</b>, you mean that they are in a situation that is much too difficult for them to be able to cope with it. 力所不及","examples":["Mr. Gibson is clearly intellectually out of his depth. 吉布森先生顯然在智慧上有所不及。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>out of</b> your <b>depth</b>, you are in water that is deeper than you are tall, with the result that you cannot stand up with your head above water. 在沒頂的水中","examples":["Somehow I got out of my depth in the pool. 不知什麼原因我在池子裡沒了頂。"]}]}]},"desert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙漠，荒漠；荒涼的地方；應得的賞罰"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"離棄，捨棄（某地）；拋棄，遺棄（某人）；背棄，放棄；擅離，開小差；突然喪失"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無人居住的，荒涼的；像沙漠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>desert</b> is a large area of land, usually in a hot region, where there is almost no water, rain, trees, or plants. 沙漠","examples":["...the Sahara Desert. …撒哈拉沙漠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"遺棄","examples":["It was a long time since she'd referred to her father's desertion. 自從她談到被父親遺棄已經很長時間了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"放棄","examples":["They blamed his proposal for much of the mass desertion by the Republican electorate. 他們把共和黨選民的大批離棄主要原因歸咎於他的提議。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or animals <b>desert</b> a place, they leave it and it becomes empty. 遺棄","examples":["Poor farmers are deserting their parched farm fields and coming here looking for jobs. 貧窮的農民丟下乾旱的農田，來這裡尋找工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>deserts</b> you, they go away and leave you, and no longer help or support you. 拋棄","examples":["Mrs. Roding's husband deserted her years ago. 羅丁太太的丈夫數年前拋棄了她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>desert</b> something that you support, use, or are involved with, you stop supporting it, using it, or being involved with it. 放棄","examples":["The sport is being written off as boring and predictable and the fans are deserting in droves. 這項運動因為枯燥且易於預測而不再吸引人，愛好者們正成批地退出。","He was pained to see many youngsters deserting kibbutz life. 他痛心地看到許多年輕人放棄集體農場生活。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>deserts</b>, or <b>deserts</b> a job, especially a job in the armed forces, they leave that job without permission. 開小差","examples":["He was a second lieutenant in the army until he deserted. 他在開小差之前是個少尉。","He deserted from army intelligence last month. 他上個月從軍隊情報部門開了小差。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被遺棄的","examples":["She led them into a deserted sidestreet. 她領他們來到一條廢棄的小巷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone got their <b>just deserts</b>, you mean that they deserved the unpleasant things that happened to them, because they did something bad. 應受的懲罰","examples":["At the end of the book the child's true identity is discovered, and the bad guys get their just deserts. 在書的結尾，這孩子的真實身份被揭開了，那些壞人也受到了應有的懲罰。"]}]}]},"diary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"日記；<英>日程簿；專欄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diary</b> is a book which has a separate space for each day of the year. You use a diary to write down things you plan to do, or to record what happens in your life day by day. 日記","examples":["I had earlier read the entry from Harold Nicholson's diary for July 10, 1940. 我早就在哈羅德·尼科爾森1940年7月10日的日記裡讀到過那則記錄。"]}]}]},"development":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發育，成長，發達；發展，進步；動態，進展；開發，研製；研製成果；（土地）開發；新建住宅區，新開發區；開始，出現；顯影；出子佈局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Development</b> is the gradual growth or formation of something. 發育; 逐漸形成","examples":["...an ideal system for studying the development of the embryo. …研究胚胎髮育的理想系統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Development</b> is the growth of something such as a business or an industry. 發展","examples":["He firmly believes that education and a country's economic development are key factors to progress. 他堅信教育和一個國家的經濟發展是通向進步的關鍵因素。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Development</b> is the process of making an area of land or water more useful or profitable. 開發","examples":["The talks will focus on economic development of the region. 會談將聚焦於該地區的經濟開發。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Development</b> is the process or result of making a basic design gradually better and more advanced. 改良","examples":["It is spending $850M on research and development to get to the market place as soon as possible with faster microprocessors. 研發上投入了$8.5億，以期儘快將更快速的微處理器投放市場。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>development</b> is an event or incident which has recently happened and is likely to have an effect on the present situation. 進展","examples":["The police spokesman said: \"We believe there has been a significant development in the case.\" 警方發言人說：“我們認為此案已有重大進展。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>development</b> is an area of houses or buildings which have been built by property developers. 開發區","examples":["...a 16-house development planned by Everlast Enterprises. …Everlast公司規劃的一個擁有16幢房子的住宅區。"]}]}]},"diamond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鑽石；菱形；（紙牌的）方塊；（棒球場的）內場；菱形鐵路道口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diamond</b> is a hard, bright, precious stone which is clear and colourless. Diamonds are used in jewellery and for cutting very hard substances. 鑽石","examples":["...a pair of diamond earrings. …一對鑽石耳環。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>diamond</b> is a shape with four straight sides of equal length where the opposite angles are the same, but none of the angles is equal to 90°: ♦. 菱形","examples":["...forming his hands into the shape of a diamond. …用他的雙手比劃出一個菱形。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Diamonds</b> is one of the four suits of cards in a pack of playing cards. Each card in the suit is marked with one or more red symbols in the shape of a diamond. 方塊 (撲克牌中的4個花色之一)","examples":["He drew the seven of diamonds. 他抽了方塊7。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>diamond</b> is a playing card of this suit. (撲克牌中的) 方塊牌","examples":["...win the ace of clubs and play a diamond. …贏了梅花A，打出一張方塊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In baseball, the <b>diamond</b> is the square formed by the four bases, or the whole of the playing area. (棒球) 內野; 棒球場","examples":["He would be the best ever to walk out onto the diamond. 他將是棒球場上最出色的球員。","Just drive around the city and see all the empty baseball diamonds there are. 就開車在城裡轉轉，看看所有空閒的棒球場。"]}]}]},"dial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"撥號"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鐘面，儀表盤；調節器；（老式電話機的）撥號盤；<英，非正式>（人的）臉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dial</b> is the part of a machine or instrument such as a clock or watch which shows you the time or a measurement that has been recorded. 刻度盤","examples":["The luminous dial on the clock showed five minutes to seven. 發光的錶盤上顯示6：55。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dial</b> is a control on a device or piece of equipment which you can move in order to adjust the setting, for example, to select or change the frequency on a radio or the temperature of a heater. (收音機、加熱器等的) 調諧鈕","examples":["He turned the dial on the radio. 他轉動著收音機的調諧鈕。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dial</b> or if you <b>dial</b> a number, you turn the dial or press the buttons on a telephone in order to phone someone. 撥號","examples":["He lifted the phone and dialled her number. 他拿起電話，撥她的號碼。"]}]}]},"design":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"設計，佈局，安排；設計藝術，構思；設計圖，圖紙；圖案，花紋；計劃，意圖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設計，製圖，構思；籌劃，制訂；預定，指定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>designs</b> a garment, building, machine, or other object, they plan it and make a detailed drawing of it from which it can be built or made. 設計","examples":["They wanted to design a machine that was both attractive and practical. 他們想設計一臺既美觀又實用的機器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>designs</b> a survey, policy, or system, they plan and prepare it, and decide on all the details of it. 策劃","examples":["We may be able to design a course to suit your particular needs. 我們也許能策劃一個課程來滿足你的特定需求。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is designed</b> for a particular purpose, it is intended for that purpose. 旨在","examples":["This project is designed to help homeless people. 這個專案旨在幫助無家可歸的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Design</b> is the process and art of planning and making detailed drawings of something. 設計","examples":["He was a born mechanic with a flair for design. 他天生是個有設計才華的機械師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>design</b> of something is the way in which it has been planned and made. 設計","examples":["...a new design of clock. …一種新款時鐘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>design</b> is a drawing which someone produces to show how they would like something to be built or made. 設計圖","examples":["When Bernardello asked them to build him a home, they drew up the design in a week. 伯納德羅請他們給他建一所房子，他們在一週內畫出了設計圖。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>design</b> is a pattern of lines, flowers, or shapes which is used to decorate something. 圖案","examples":["Many pictures have been based on simple geometric designs. 許多圖畫是以簡單的幾何圖案為基礎的。"]}]}]},"dictionary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"字典，詞典；專業詞典，術語大全；電子詞典；雙語詞典"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dictionary</b> is a book in which the words and phrases of a language are listed alphabetically, together with their meanings or their translations in another language. 詞典","examples":["...a Spanish-English dictionary. …一本西班牙語—英語詞典。"]}]}]},"dinosaur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恐龍；守舊落伍的人，過時落後的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dinosaurs</b> were large reptiles which lived in prehistoric times. 恐龍","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to an organization as a <b>dinosaur</b>, you mean that it is large, inefficient, and out of date. 龐大、低效且落後的機構","examples":["...industrial dinosaurs. …龐大臃腫的工業企業。"]}]}]},"disagreement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分歧，爭論；不符，不一致"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disagreement</b> means objecting to something such as a proposal. 反對","examples":["Britain and France have expressed some disagreement with the proposal. 英、法兩國已表示了對這項提議的一些反對意見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When there is <b>disagreement</b> about something, people disagree or argue about what should be done. 爭執","examples":["The United States Congress and the president are still locked in disagreement over proposals to reduce the massive budget deficit. 美國國會與總統對減少鉅額預算赤字的提議各持己見，僵持不下。"]}]}]},"difficulty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"難題，困難"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>difficulty</b> is a problem. 難題","examples":["...the difficulty of getting accurate information. …獲得準確資訊的困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>difficulty</b> doing something, you are not able to do it easily. 困難","examples":["Do you have difficulty getting up? 你起床有困難嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in difficulty</b>, they are having a lot of problems. 在困境中","examples":["The city's film industry is in difficulty. 該市的電影業舉步維艱。"]}]}]},"director":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導演；管理者，負責人；董事，理事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>director</b> of a play, film, or television programme is the person who decides how it will appear on stage or screen, and who tells the actors and technical staff what to do. 導演","examples":["\"Cut!\" the director yelled. \"That was perfect.\" “停！”導演叫道。“太好了！”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In some organizations and public authorities, the person in charge is referred to as <b>the</b> <b>director</b>. 主任; 主管","examples":["...the director of the intensive care unit at Buffalo General Hospital. …布法羅總醫院重症監護室的主任。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>directors</b> of a company are its most senior managers, who meet regularly to make important decisions about how it will be run. 董事","examples":["He served on the board of directors of a local bank. 他在當地一家銀行的董事會擔任董事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>director</b> of a choir is the person who is conducting it. (合唱團的) 指揮","examples":[]}]}]},"discussion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"討論；論述，詳述；談話，辯論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>discussion</b> about something, people talk about it, often in order to reach a decision. 討論","examples":["There was a lot of discussion about the wording of the report. 有很多關於該份報告措詞的討論。","Board members are due to have informal discussions later on today. 董事會成員們預定在今天稍後進行非正式討論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>discussion</b> <b>of</b> a subject is a piece of writing or a lecture in which someone talks about it in detail. 詳述","examples":["For a discussion of biology and sexual politics, see chapter 4. 欲獲得一個生物學與性別政治學的論述，請看第4章。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>under discussion</b>, it is still being talked about and a final decision has not yet been reached. 在討論中","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>discussion</b> document or paper is one that contains information and usually proposals for people to discuss. 供討論的","examples":["...a NASA discussion paper on long-duration ballooning. …一份美國國家航空航天局關於長時間氣球飛行的討論檔案。"]}]}]},"difference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"差異，不同之處；差額；分歧"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕> 區分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>difference</b> between two things is the way in which they are unlike each other. 差異","examples":["That is the fundamental difference between the two societies. 那是兩個社會之間的根本差別。","...the vast difference in size. …在大小方面的巨大差別。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people have their <b>differences</b> about something, they disagree about it. 分歧","examples":["The two communities are learning how to resolve their differences. 這兩個團體正在學會如何消除它們之間的分歧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>difference</b> between two quantities is the amount by which one quantity is less than the other. 差額","examples":["The difference is 8532. 差額是8532。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>makes</b> a <b>difference</b> or <b>makes</b> a lot of <b>difference</b>, it affects you and helps you in what you are doing. If something <b>makes</b> no <b>difference</b>, it does not have any effect on what you are doing. 有 (某程度的) 影響/毫無影響","examples":["Where you live can make such a difference to the way you feel. 你居住的位置會對你的感覺產生很大的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is a <b>difference of opinion</b> between two or more people or groups, they disagree about something. 意見分歧","examples":["Was there a difference of opinion over what to do with the Nobel Prize money? 對於怎麼使用諾貝爾獎金有不同的意見嗎？"]}]}]},"direction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方向，方位；趨勢，動向；指示，說明；目標；方面；管理，指導；導演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>direction</b> is the general line that someone or something is moving or pointing in. 方向","examples":["St. Andrews was ten miles in the opposite direction. 聖安德魯斯在相反方向的10英里處。","He got into Margie's car and swung out onto the road in the direction of Larry's shop. 他鑽進瑪吉的汽車，搖晃著開上馬路，朝拉里商店的方向駛去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>direction</b> is the general way in which something develops or progresses. 發展方向","examples":["They threatened to lead a mass walk-out if the party did not sharply change direction. 他們威脅說，如果該黨對其發展方向不作大的調整，他們就發動大家集體退黨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Directions</b> are instructions that tell you what to do, how to do something, or how to get somewhere. 說明書; (指示路線的) 說明","examples":["I should know by now not to throw away the directions until we've finished cooking. 我現在應該明白，飯沒做完之前，不要把食譜扔掉。"]}]}]},"dolphin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海豚；鯕鰍，又稱鬼頭刀（dolphinfish 或 mahi-mahi）；（水運）系船柱，靠船墩；（Dolphin，英人名）多爾芬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dolphin</b> is a mammal which lives in the sea and looks like a large fish with a pointed mouth. 海豚","examples":[]}]}]},"donkey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"驢；<非正式>蠢人，傻瓜；<非正式>發動機；（尤指在藝術學校中供藝術家跨坐的）低凳；（兒童玩的）換牌紙牌戲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>donkey</b> is an animal which is like a horse but which is smaller and has longer ears. 驢","examples":[]}]}]},"display":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"展示，陳列；顯露，表現；（計算機）顯示；（為求偶）作炫耀行為"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"展覽，陳列；表演；（計算機螢幕上的）顯示，顯示器；流露，表現；炫耀行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>display</b> something that you want people to see, you put it in a particular place, so that people can see it easily. 陳列; 展出","examples":["Among the protesters and war veterans proudly displaying their medals was Aubrey Rose. 在抗議人群和自豪地展示勳章的退伍軍人中的是奧布里∙羅斯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>display</b> something, you show it to people. 展示","examples":["She displayed her wound to the twelve gentlemen of the jury. 她向陪審團的12位男士展示她的傷痕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>display</b> a characteristic, quality, or emotion, you behave in a way which shows that you have it. 表露 (特點、素質、情感)","examples":["It was unlike Gordon to display his feelings. 表露自己的感情這點可不像戈登。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a computer <b>displays</b> information, it shows it on a screen. (在計算機螢幕上) 顯示","examples":["They started out by looking at the computer screens which display the images. 他們從觀看顯示影象的計算機螢幕開始。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Display</b> is also a noun. 陳列; 展出","examples":["Most of the other artists whose work is on display were his pupils or colleagues. 其他有作品展出的藝術家大多數是他的學生或同事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Display</b> is also a noun. 表露","examples":["Normally, such an outward display of affection is reserved for his mother. 通常，他只在他母親前才情感外露。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>display</b> is an arrangement of things that have been put in a particular place, so that people can see them easily. 陳列","examples":["...a display of your work. …你作品的陳列。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>display</b> is a public performance or other event which is intended to entertain people. 表演","examples":["...the fireworks display. …煙火表演。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>display</b> on a computer screen is the information that is shown there. The screen itself can also be referred to as the <b>display</b>. (螢幕) 顯示內容; (計算機) 螢幕","examples":["A hard copy of the screen display can also be obtained from a printer. 螢幕顯示的硬複製也可從印表機那裡獲得。"]}]}]},"distance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遠處；疏遠，隔閡；（人或物之間的）差別，差距；進展；距離"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"疏遠，遠離"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遠距離的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>distance</b> <b>between</b> two points or places is the amount of space between them. 距離","examples":["...the distance between the island and the nearby shore. …島嶼和附近海岸之間的距離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When two things are very far apart, you talk about the <b>distance</b> between them. 遠離","examples":["The distance wouldn't be a problem. 距離遙遠不是問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you want to emphasize that two people or things do not have a close relationship or are not the same, you can refer to the <b>distance</b> <b>between</b> them. 差距","examples":["There was a vast distance between psychological clues and concrete proof. 心理線索和現實證據之間存在著巨大差距。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Distance</b> is coolness or unfriendliness in the way that someone behaves toward you. 疏遠; 冷淡","examples":["There were periods of sulking, of pronounced distance, of coldness. 出現階段性的慍怒、明顯的疏遠和冷淡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you can see something <b>in the distance</b>, you can see it, far away from you. 在遠處","examples":["We suddenly saw her in the distance. 我們突然看見遠處的她。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Distance</b> learning or <b>distance</b> education involves studying at home and sending your work to a college or university, rather than attending the college or university in person. 遠端的","examples":["The Internet is often used as a resource and as a tool for distance learning. 網際網路通常被用作遠端學習的資源和工具。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"疏遠的; 有距離的","examples":["Clough felt he'd become too distanced from his fans. 克拉夫覺得他變得太疏遠他的仰慕者們。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>distance</b> <b>yourself from</b> a person or thing, or if something <b>distances</b> you <b>from</b> them, you feel less friendly or positive toward them, or become less involved with them. 疏遠","examples":["The author distanced himself from some of the comments in his book. 作者在他的書裡對某些評論淡然處之。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>at a distance</b> from something, or if you see it or remember it <b>from a distance</b>, you are a long way away from it in space or time. 在/從遠處; 在/從很久以前","examples":["The only way I can cope with my mother is at a distance. 我應付我媽媽的惟一方法就是與她保持距離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>distance</b> from someone or something or <b>keep</b> them <b>at a distance</b>, you do not become involved with them. 保持距離","examples":["Jay had always tended to keep his girlfriends at a distance. 傑伊一直傾向於同他的女朋友們保持一定的距離。"]}]}]},"division":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分開，分配；除法；部門；分歧，不和；分界線；（軍隊編制中的）師；（英國議會的）分組表決；（足球等體育運動中聯賽的）級"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>division</b> <b>of</b> a large unit <b>into</b> two or more distinct parts is the act of separating it into these parts. 分割; 分裂","examples":["...the unification of Germany, after its division into two states at the end of World War Two. …德國在二戰結束時分裂成兩個國家，之後又統一了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>division</b> <b>of</b> something among people or things is its separation into parts which are distributed among the people or things. 分配","examples":["The current division of labour between workers and management will alter. 勞資雙方目前的勞動分配將會改變。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Division</b> is the arithmetical process of dividing one number into another number. 除法","examples":["I taught my daughter how to do division at the age of six. 我女兒6歲時，我就教她怎樣做除法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>division</b> is a significant distinction or argument between two groups, which causes the two groups to be considered as very different and separate. 分歧; 不和","examples":["The division between the prosperous west and the impoverished east remains. 富裕的西部和貧窮的東部之間的對立依然存在。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a large organization, a <b>division</b> is a group of departments whose work is done in the same place or is connected with similar tasks. 部門","examples":["...the bank's Latin American division. …該銀行的拉丁美洲部。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>division</b> is a group of military units which fight as a single unit. 師 (軍隊的作戰單位)","examples":["Several armoured divisions are being moved from Germany. 幾個裝甲師正從德國調來。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In some sports, such as football, baseball, and basketball, a <b>division</b> is one of the groups of teams which make up a league. The teams in each division are of the same level, and they all play against each other during the season. (球隊的) 分級","examples":["Chico State reached the NCAA Division II national finals last season. 奇科加州大學上個賽季進入了全國大學體育協會乙級全國決賽。"]}]}]},"divide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）分開，分散；分配，分擔；使分離；分隔，隔開；使產生分歧；除，除以；分岔"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"差異，分歧；（兩事物間的）界限；<美>分水嶺，分水線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or things <b>are divided</b> or <b>divide</b> <b>into</b> smaller groups or parts, they become separated into smaller parts. 分割; 分離","examples":["The physical benefits of exercise can be divided into three factors. 鍛鍊對身體的好處可以分成3個方面。","Divide the pastry in half and roll out each piece. 把麵糰一分為二，把每塊都擀平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>divide</b> something <b>among</b> people or things, you separate it into several parts or quantities which you distribute to the people or things. 分配","examples":["Divide the sauce among 4 bowls. 把調味汁分到4個碗裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>divide</b> a larger number <b>by</b> a smaller number or <b>divide</b> a smaller number <b>into</b> a larger number, you calculate how many times the smaller number can fit exactly into the larger number. 除; 除盡","examples":["Measure the floor area of the greenhouse and divide it by six. 測量溫室的地表面積，再除以6。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a border or line <b>divides</b> two areas or <b>divides</b> an area into two, it keeps the two areas separate from each other. 分隔","examples":["...remote border areas dividing Tamil and Muslim settlements. …把泰米爾人和穆斯林居住地分隔開的偏僻邊界地區。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If people <b>divide</b> over something or if something <b>divides</b> them, it causes strong disagreement between them. 使不和; 不和","examples":["...the major issues that divided the country. …造成國家分裂的重大問題。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>divide</b> is a significant distinction between two groups, often one that causes conflict. (引發衝突的) 重大差異","examples":["...a deliberate attempt to create a Hindu-Muslim divide in India. …蓄意在印度製造印度教徒和穆斯林教徒之間差異的企圖。"]}]}]},"doughnut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"炸麵包圈，甜甜圈；環狀物，（尤指某些型別的粒子加速器的真空）環形室（=donut）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doughnut</b> is a breadlike cake, often in the shape of a ring, made from sweet dough that has been cooked in hot fat. 甜面圈","examples":[]}]}]},"dot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"點，小圓點，點狀物；頓音記號；（摩爾斯電碼、因特網或電子郵件地址中的）點；嫁妝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加點；散佈於，遍佈；給音符加附點；<古>擊打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dot</b> is a very small round mark, for example, one that is used as the top part of the letter \"i,\" as a period, or in the names of websites. 點","examples":["...a system of painting using small dots of colour. …一套運用小色點作畫的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a woman's dowry 女人的嫁妝","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to mark or form with a dot 用小圓點標記; 由點形成","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When things <b>dot</b> a place or an area, they are scattered or spread all over it. 遍佈於","examples":["Small coastal towns dot the landscape. 海濱小鎮到處都是。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you arrive somewhere or do something <b>on the dot</b>, you arrive there or do it at exactly the time that you were supposed to. 準時地","examples":["They appeared on the dot of 9:50 p.m. as always. 他們同往常一樣在晚上9點50分準時出現了。"]}]}]},"downtown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"市中心的，商業區的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向（在）市中心，向（在）城鎮商業中心區"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"城鎮的中心區，商業區，鬧市區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Downtown</b> places are in or toward the centre of a large town or city, where the stores and places of business are. 市中心的","examples":["...an office in downtown Chicago. …芝加哥市中心的一間辦公室。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Downtown</b> is also an adverb. 在市中心","examples":["By day he worked downtown for American Standard. 白天，他在市中心為美國標準公司工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Downtown</b> is also a noun. 市中心","examples":["...in a large vacant area of the downtown. …在市中心的一大塊空地上。"]}]}]},"dragonfly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜻蜓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dragonflies</b> are brightly coloured insects with long, thin bodies and two sets of wings. Dragonflies are often found near slow-moving water. 蜻蜓","examples":[]}]}]},"drawer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽屜；<舊>襯褲，內褲；製圖員；開票人；起草者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drawer</b> is part of a desk, chest, or other piece of furniture that is shaped like a box and is designed for putting things in. You pull it toward you to open it. 抽屜","examples":["She opened her desk drawer and took out the manual. 她開啟書桌抽屜，拿出手冊。"]}]}]},"doubt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懷疑，不確定；不信任"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"懷疑，不確定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>doubt</b> or <b>doubts</b> about something, you feel uncertain about it and do not know whether it is true or possible. If you say you have <b>no</b> <b>doubt</b> <b>about</b> it, you mean that you are certain it is true. 懷疑","examples":["This raises doubts about the point of advertising. 這引起了人們對於廣告作用的懷疑。","There is little doubt that man has had an impact on the Earth's climate. 毫無疑問人類對地球上的氣候造成了影響。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>doubt</b> whether something is true or possible, you believe that it is probably not true or possible. 懷疑","examples":["Others doubted whether that would happen. 其他人都懷疑那會不會發生。","He doubted if he would learn anything new from Marie. 他懷疑自己是否能從瑪麗那裡學到什麼新東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>doubt</b> something, you believe that it might not be true or genuine. 懷疑","examples":["No one doubted his ability. 沒有人懷疑他的能力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>doubt</b> someone or <b>doubt</b> their word, you think that they may not be telling the truth. 不信","examples":["No one directly involved with the case doubted him. 直接涉及此案的人都沒有懷疑他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that something is <b>beyond doubt</b> or <b>beyond reasonable doubt</b> when you are certain that it is true and it cannot be contradicted or disproved. 無疑","examples":["A referendum showed beyond doubt that voters wanted independence. 全民公決毫無疑問地顯示，選民要求獨立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in doubt</b> about something, you feel unsure or uncertain about it. 不肯定的","examples":["He is in no doubt as to what is needed. 他對需要些什麼心中有數。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in doubt</b> or <b>open to doubt</b>, you consider it to be uncertain or unreliable. 不確定的","examples":["The outcome was still in doubt. 結果仍不確定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>no doubt</b> to emphasize that something seems certain or very likely to you. 毫無疑問地","examples":["The contract for this will no doubt be widely advertised. 就此達成的協議無疑會被廣泛宣傳。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>no doubt</b> to indicate that you accept the truth of a particular point, but that you do not think it is important or contradicts the rest of what you are saying. 的確","examples":["No doubt many will regard these as harsh words, but regrettably they are true. 的確很多人會覺得這些話刺耳，可惜它們卻是事實。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>without doubt</b> or <b>without a doubt</b>, you are emphasizing that it is definitely true. 毋庸置疑地","examples":["This was without doubt the most interesting situation that Amanda had ever found herself in. 這無疑是阿曼達遇到過的最有趣的情況。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>I doubt it</b> as a response to a question or statement about something that you think is untrue or unlikely. 我不信","examples":["\"Somebody would have seen her.\"—\"I doubt it, not on Monday.\" “有人可能見過她。”—“我不信，不可能在星期一。”"]}]}]},"dragon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（傳說中的）西方的龍；惡龍；悍婦，母夜叉；<澳>蜥蜴（=flying dragon）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In stories and legends, a <b>dragon</b> is an animal like a big lizard. It has wings and claws, and breathes out fire. 龍","examples":[]}]}]},"drama":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇本，戲劇；戲劇研究，戲劇藝術；戲劇性場面，戲劇性事件；激動，刺激"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drama</b> is a serious play for the theatre, television, or radio, or a serious film. 戲劇","examples":["He acted in radio dramas. 他演過廣播劇。","The film is a drama about a woman searching for her children. 這部電影是關於一個女人尋找她孩子的戲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>drama</b> to refer to plays in general or to work that is connected with plays and the theatre, such as acting or producing. 戲劇; 戲劇工作","examples":["He knew nothing of Greek drama. 他對希臘戲劇一無所知。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a real situation which is exciting or distressing as <b>drama</b>. 戲劇性場面","examples":["There was none of the drama and relief of a hostage release. 絲毫沒有人質釋放的戲劇性場面和放鬆。"]}]}]},"drawing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖畫，素描畫；繪畫（藝術），製圖技巧；抽籤，抽獎；圖畫，素描畫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"畫；拉；吸引（draw 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drawing</b> is a picture made with a pencil or pen. 素描","examples":["She did a drawing of me. 她為我畫了張素描。"]}]}]},"double":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兩倍的，雙的；供兩人用的；雙重的；（花）重瓣的；（多米諾骨牌）兩邊點數相同的；低八度的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"兩倍地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加倍；對摺；擊出二壘安打；兼任；握緊；兼奏，重複（一個音符）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"兩倍，兩倍量；酷似的人；替身演員；臥室；雙打；雙料冠軍；一杯雙份的烈酒；（擲鏢遊戲中的）得雙倍分的一擲；（擲骰子游戲中的）兩骰子點數相同的一擲；（賽馬中的）複式下注；（棒球比賽中的）二壘打"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"是……兩倍"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"雙倍數（或量）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>double</b> to indicate that something includes or is made of two things of the same kind. 雙的","examples":["...a pair of double doors into the room from the new entrance hall. …一道從新門廊進入房間的雙扇門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>double</b> before a singular noun to refer to two things of the same type that occur together, or that are connected in some way. 成對的","examples":["...an extremely nasty double murder. …一起極殘忍的雙人謀殺案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>double</b> to describe something which is twice the normal size or can hold twice the normal quantity of something. 雙倍的","examples":["...a double helping of ice cream. …雙份冰激凌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>double</b> room is a room intended for two people, usually a couple, to stay or live in. 雙人的","examples":["...bed and breakfast for $180 for two people in a double room. …給兩個人共用一個雙人間的價格為$180的住宿加早餐。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>double</b> bed is a bed that is wide enough for two people to sleep in. 雙人的","examples":["One bedroom had a double bed and the other had single beds for the boys. 一間臥室裡擺放了一張雙人床，另一間則放著男孩們的幾張單人床。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>double</b> to describe a drink that is twice the normal measure. (酒類飲料) 雙份的","examples":["He was drinking his double whisky too fast and scowling. 他大口喝著雙份威士忌，雙眉緊皺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Double</b> is also a noun. 雙人房間","examples":["The Great Western Hotel is ideal, costing around 90 a night for a double. 大西酒店是理想的，雙人房間每晚約£90。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Double</b> is also a noun. 雙份酒類飲料","examples":["\"Give me a whisky,\" Debilly said to Francis. \"Make it a double.\" “給我來杯威士忌，”德比利對弗朗西斯說。“要雙份的。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a person's <b>double</b>, you mean that they look exactly like them. 一模一樣的人","examples":["Your mother sees you as her double. 你母親把你看成是她的翻版。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In tennis or badminton, when people play <b>doubles</b>, two teams consisting of two players on each team play against each other on the same court. 雙打","examples":["In the doubles, the pair beat Hungary's Renata Csay and Kornelia Szanda. 在雙打比賽中，那對選手戰勝了匈牙利的雷納塔·賽伊和科尼利婭·薩恩達。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>double</b> <b>the</b> amount or size of another thing, it is twice as large. 雙倍的","examples":["The offer was to start a new research laboratory at double the salary he was then getting. 提議當時是他創辦一個新實驗室拿雙倍工資。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Double</b> is also a pronoun. 兩倍","examples":["On average doctors write just over seven prescriptions each year per patient; in Germany it is double. 一個醫生平均一年僅為每個病人開大約七個處方；而德國是這個數字的兩倍。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>doubles</b> or when you <b>double</b> it, it becomes twice as great in number, amount, or size. 使加倍; 翻倍","examples":["The number of managers must double to 100 within 3 years. 3年之內管理人員的數量要翻倍，達到100名。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>doubles</b> <b>as</b> someone or something else, they have a second job or purpose as well as their main one. 兼職; 兼作","examples":["Lots of homes in town double as businesses. 許多市區的住房還兼作商鋪。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Double up</b> means the same as . 兼職; 兼作 (同)(double)","examples":["The lids of the casserole dishes are designed to double up as baking dishes. 這些砂鍋蓋子的設計使它們可以兼作烤盤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on the double</b>, you do it very quickly or immediately. 快速地","examples":["I need a copy of the police report on the double. 我急需一份警方報告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>bent double</b>, the top half of your body is bent downward so that your head is close to your knees. 彎腰的","examples":["I was bent double in agony. 我痛苦地彎下了腰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are seeing double</b>, there is something wrong with your eyes, and you can see two images instead of one. 看到重影","examples":["For 35 minutes I was walking around in a daze. I was dizzy, seeing double. 長達35分鐘我茫然地走著。我頭暈目眩，看東西有重影。"]}]}]},"drugstore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>藥店，藥房，雜貨店（出售藥品，兼售化妝品、日用品、雜誌、飲料及小吃等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drugstore</b> is a shop where drugs and medicines are sold, and where you can buy cosmetics, some household goods, and also drinks and snacks. (兼營雜貨、小吃的) 藥店","examples":[]}]}]},"dumpling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"湯糰，餃子；水果布丁，水果餡點心；矮胖的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dumplings</b> are small lumps of dough that are cooked and eaten, either with meat and vegetables or as a fruit-filled dessert. 餃子; 水果布丁","examples":[]}]}]},"dryer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烘乾機；乾燥劑，催幹劑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dryer</b> is a machine for drying things. There are different kinds of dryers, for example, ones designed for drying clothes, crops, or people's hair or hands. 乾燥器","examples":["...hot air electric hand dryers. …熱風電動幹手機。"]}]}]},"drag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拖，拽；生拉硬拽，強迫；硬撐著行進，費勁地移動；拖沓；用滑鼠拖動；用網（或鉤）搜尋；（使）拖地而行；把……扯進（談話中）；（船）拖錨，走錨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>乏味無聊的事（人）；累贅，拖累；吸一口（煙）；阻力，抗力；穿異性服裝；<非正式>街，路；<英，非正式>汽車；<美，非正式>（對其他人的）影響（力）；（用力或費力的）拖，曳；（拉釣線時引起的假蠅的）異動；<史>（四匹馬拉的）高大私人馬車；被拖（或拉）之物；<史>重型耙，耮；（拖在獵犬前面代替狐狸用的具有強烈氣味的）人工臭跡；每次敲擊前用另一隻鼓槌先擊兩個裝飾音（基本的擊鼓模式之一）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>drag</b> something, you pull it along the ground, often with difficulty. (費力地) 拖","examples":["He got up and dragged his chair toward the table. 他站起來，把椅子拖向桌子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>drag</b> a computer image means to use the mouse to move the position of the image on the screen, or to change its size or shape. (用滑鼠) 拖","examples":["Use your mouse to drag the pictures to their new size. 用滑鼠拖拽圖片到新尺寸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>drags</b> you somewhere, they pull you there, or force you to go there by physically threatening you. 硬拉; 硬拽","examples":["The vigilantes dragged the men out of the vehicles. 治安聯防員將這些人從車裡拽了出來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>drags</b> you somewhere you do not want to go, they make you go there. 強迫","examples":["When you can drag him away from his work, he can also be a devoted father. 當你能強迫他遠離工作的時候，他也可以是個充滿愛心的父親。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>drag</b> <b>yourself</b> somewhere, you are emphasizing that you have to make a very great effort to go there. 勉強","examples":["I find it really hard to drag myself out and exercise regularly. 我發現實在很難強迫自己定期出來鍛鍊。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>drag</b> your foot or your leg behind you, you walk with great difficulty because your foot or leg is injured in some way. 拖著 (受傷的腳或腿) 行走","examples":["He was barely able to drag his poisoned leg behind him. 他勉強拖著中了毒的腿向前走。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If the police <b>drag</b> a river or lake, they pull nets or hooks across the bottom of it in order to look for something. (用網或鉤) 在水中搜尋","examples":["Police are planning to drag the pond later this morning. 警方正計劃今天上午晚些時候在池塘裡進行打撈搜尋。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a period of time or an event <b>drags</b>, it is very boring and seems to last a long time. (時間或事件) 拖沓","examples":["The minutes dragged past. 時間一分一分地過去了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>a drag on</b> the development or progress of something, it slows it down or makes it more difficult. 阻礙","examples":["The satellite acts as a drag on the shuttle. 衛星是對太空梭發展的阻礙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a drag</b>, you mean that it is unpleasant or very dull. 討厭的事; 很沒意思的事","examples":["As far as shopping for clothes goes, it's a drag. 買衣服在某種程度上是個挺沒意思的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you take a <b>drag</b> <b>on</b> a cigarette or pipe that you are smoking, you take in air through it. (抽菸時的) 一咂","examples":["He took a drag on his cigarette, and exhaled the smoke. 他咂了口煙，然後吐出煙霧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Drag</b> is the wearing of women's clothes by a male entertainer. (喜劇演員) 男扮女裝","examples":["Drag has been with us since the birth of comedy, because it's funny to see a man pretending to be a woman. 自喜劇誕生時就有男演員反串的表演, 因為看男人假扮女人很有趣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a man is <b>in drag</b>, he is wearing women's clothes. (男子) 穿著女裝","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>drag</b> your <b>feet</b> or <b>drag</b> your <b>heels</b>, you delay doing something or do it very slowly because you do not want to do it. 拖延","examples":["The government was dragging its feet, and this was threatening moves toward peace. 政府一拖再拖，這是有礙和平的行徑。"]}]}]},"drug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毒品；藥物；運動禁藥；成癮之事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使服麻醉藥；（在食物或飲料中）投放麻醉藥；<非正式>吸毒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drug</b> is a chemical which is given to people in order to treat or prevent an illness or disease. 藥物","examples":["The drug will be useful to hundreds of thousands of infected people. 這種藥物將會對成千上萬感染者有用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Drugs</b> are substances that some people take because of their pleasant effects, but which are usually illegal. 毒品","examples":["His mother was on drugs, on cocaine. 他的母親吸毒，吸可卡因。","She was sure Leo was taking drugs. 她肯定利奧在吸毒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>drug</b> a person or animal, you give them a chemical substance in order to make them sleepy or unconscious. 用藥麻醉","examples":["She was drugged and robbed. 她被下了迷藥，遭到搶劫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If food or drink <b>is drugged</b>, a chemical substance is added to it in order to make someone sleepy or unconscious when they eat or drink it. 下麻醉藥於 (食物或飲料)","examples":["I wonder now if that drink had been drugged. 我現在懷疑那飲料是否已被人下了麻醉藥。"]}]}]},"dress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"連衣裙，套裙；（特定種類的）服裝，衣服；（統指）服裝；（上下連身的）女裝，童裝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿衣；給……穿衣服；穿正式服裝；清洗包紮（傷口）；調製；加工，處理（食材、材料等）；整隊；佈置，裝飾；為……製作或挑選衣服；做頭髮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dress</b> is a piece of clothing worn by a woman or girl. It covers her body and part of her legs. 連衣裙","examples":["She was wearing a black dress. 她穿著一套黑色連衣裙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to clothes worn by men or women as <b>dress</b>. 服裝","examples":["He wore formal evening dress. 他穿了正式的晚禮服。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dress</b> or <b>dress</b> <b>yourself</b>, you put on clothes. 穿衣服","examples":["He told Sarah to wait while he dressed. 他讓莎拉等著他穿好衣服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dress</b> someone, for example, a child, you put clothes on them. 給…穿衣","examples":["She bathed her and dressed her in clean clothes. 她給她洗了澡並穿上乾淨衣服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>dresses</b> a wound, they clean it and cover it. 清理包紮 (傷口)","examples":["The poor child never cried or protested when I was dressing her wounds. 在我為那個可憐的女孩清理包紮傷口時，她不哭不鬧。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>dresses</b> in a particular way, they wear clothes of a particular style or colour. 打扮; 穿著","examples":["He dresses in a way that lets everyone know he's got authority. 他著裝的式樣讓每個人都知道他已掌有權力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dress</b> <b>for</b> something, you put on special clothes for it. 穿禮服","examples":["We don't dress for dinner here. 我們這兒參加晚宴不穿禮服。"]}]}]},"drum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼓；大桶；敲擊聲；鼓狀物；<史>軍鼓手；<英，非正式>一套房間，（公寓）套間；<澳，非正式>（可靠的）內部訊息；（18世紀末、19世紀初流行的）傍晚茶會，下午茶會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不停地擊打；擊鼓，打鼓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drum</b> is a musical instrument consisting of a skin stretched tightly over a round frame. You play a drum by beating it with sticks or with your hands. 鼓","examples":["...a worker who died after collapsing while beating a drum during a demonstration. …一個在遊行時因擊鼓過度勞累而倒斃的工人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drum</b> is a large cylindrical container which is used to store fuel or other substances. 鼓狀容器","examples":["...an oil drum. …一隻油桶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>drums</b> <b>on</b> a surface, or if you <b>drum</b> something <b>on</b> a surface, it hits it regularly, making a continuous beating sound. 連續敲擊","examples":["He drummed his fingers on the leather top of his desk. 他用手指不停地敲擊皮桌面。"]}]}]},"earthquake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地震；大動盪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>earthquake</b> is a shaking of the ground caused by movement of the Earth's crust. 地震","examples":["...the San Francisco earthquake of 1906. …1906年的舊金山地震。"]}]}]},"duty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"責任，義務；上班，值班；職責，任務；稅，關稅；兵役；（牧師的）行禮拜式；（發動機的）功率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Duty</b> is work that you have to do for your job. 工作","examples":["Staff must report for duty at their normal place of work. 職員必須到他們平常的崗位報到上班。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>duties</b> are tasks which you have to do because they are part of your job. 職責","examples":["I carried out my duties conscientiously. 我認真執行了我的各項職責。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is your <b>duty</b>, you believe that you ought to do it because it is your responsibility. 責任","examples":["I consider it my duty to write to you and thank you. 我覺得我有責任給你寫信表示感謝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Duties</b> are taxes which you pay to the government on goods that you buy. 稅","examples":["Import duties still average 30%. 進口關稅平均仍為30%。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone such as a police officer or a nurse is <b>off duty</b>, they are not working. If someone is <b>on duty</b>, they are working. 下班; 上班","examples":["I'm off duty. 我下班了。"]}]}]},"education":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指學校）教育；培養，訓練；教育機構，教育界人士；教育學；有教益的經歷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Education</b> involves teaching people various subjects, usually at a school or college, or being taught. 教育","examples":["They're cutting funds for education. 他們正在削減教育經費。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Education</b> of a particular kind involves teaching the public about a particular issue. 教育","examples":["...better health education. …更好的健康教育。"]}]}]},"elevator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電梯；（運送糧食、液體或卸船的）升降機，起卸機；糧倉，穀倉；（飛行器的）升降舵；（上）提肌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>elevator</b> is a device that carries people or goods up and down inside tall buildings. 電梯","examples":["We took the elevator to the fourteenth floor. 我們乘電梯到了第14層。"]}]}]},"effort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"努力，艱難的嘗試；力氣，精力；有組織的活動；努力的結果，成就"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make an <b>effort</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try very hard to do it. 努力","examples":["He made no effort to hide his disappointment. 他不試圖隱瞞自己的失望。","Finding a cure requires considerable time and effort. 找到一種治癒方法需要相當的時間和努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone did something <b>with</b> <b>effort</b> or <b>with</b> <b>an effort</b>, you mean it was difficult for them to do. 吃力","examples":["She took a deep breath and sat up slowly and with great effort. 她深吸一口氣，慢慢地、吃力地坐了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>effort</b> is a particular series of activities that is organized by a group of people in order to achieve something. 有組織的活動","examples":["...a famine relief effort in Angola. …一個在安哥拉的饑荒救援活動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>an effort</b>, you mean that an unusual amount of physical or mental energy is needed to do it. 極艱難的事","examples":["Even carrying the camcorder while hiking in the forest was an effort. 在森林徒步旅行時，即使揹著攝像機也是件極難的事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make the effort</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it, even though you need extra energy to do it or you do not really want to. 盡力","examples":["I don't get lonely now because I make the effort to see people. 我現在不寂寞了，因為我盡力與人接觸。"]}]}]},"encouragement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼓勵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Encouragement</b> is the activity of encouraging someone, or something that is said or done in order to encourage them. 鼓勵; 起鼓勵作用的事物","examples":["Friends gave me a great deal of encouragement. 朋友們給了我極大的鼓勵。"]}]}]},"emotion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"情感，情緒；激情，強烈的情感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emotion</b> is a feeling such as happiness, love, fear, anger, or hatred, which can be caused by the situation that you are in or the people you are with. 感情","examples":["Happiness was an emotion that Jerry was having to relearn. 幸福是一種傑瑞當時不得不再學習的感情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Emotion</b> is the part of a person's character that consists of their feelings, as opposed to their thoughts. (與思想相對的) 情感","examples":["...the split between reason and emotion. …理智與情感間的分離。"]}]}]},"elder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"年齡較大的；資格老的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長者，長輩；元老，長老；接骨木"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>elder</b> <b>of</b> two people is the one who was born first. 年長的","examples":["...his elder brother. …他的哥哥。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>elder</b> is someone who is older than them, especially someone quite a lot older. 長輩","examples":["They have no respect for their elders. 他們對長輩毫無敬意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In some societies, an <b>elder</b> is one of the respected older people who have influence and authority. 長老","examples":["...a meeting of political figures and tribal elders. …政界要人和部族長老的一次會晤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(in certain Protestant Churches) a lay office having teaching, pastoral, or administrative functions (在某些新教教會中持教導、牧會或管理職務的)長老","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"any of various caprifoliaceous shrubs or small trees of the genus <b>Sambucus,</b> having clusters of small white flowers and red, purple, or black berry-like fruits 接骨木屬植物 (Also called elderberry)","examples":[]}]}]},"drop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投，丟；躺倒；剔除，除名；停止，放棄；中途卸客，中途卸貨；寄，送，寫（信）；（道路、地面等）急劇向下傾斜；突然終止與（某人）的（戀愛）關係；（使）掉落；減少，降低"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"滴，少量；下降；落差；<非正式>遞送，交付；<美>郵政信箱，郵筒；（贓物、非法物、秘密物品的）藏匿處；垂幕，升降幕；（絞刑架的）下落板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a level or amount <b>drops</b> or if someone or something <b>drops</b> it, it quickly becomes less. 使迅速下降; 迅速下降","examples":["Temperatures can drop to freezing at night. 晚上氣溫能陡降到零度以下。","His blood pressure had dropped severely. 他的血壓嚴重地迅速下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>drop</b> something, you accidentally let it fall. 失手掉下","examples":["I dropped my glasses and broke them. 我不小心掉了眼鏡，把它摔破了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>drop</b> something somewhere or if it <b>drops</b> there, you deliberately let it fall there. 投下","examples":["Drop the noodles into the water. 把麵條下到水裡。","...television footage of bombs dropping on the city. …多枚炸彈投向該城市的電視片段。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or a part of their body <b>drops</b> to a lower position, or if they <b>drop</b> a part of their body to a lower position, they move to that position, often in a tired and lifeless way. (人) 癱下; (身體部位無力地) 垂下","examples":["Nancy dropped into a nearby chair. 南希在旁邊的椅子上癱坐了下去。","She let her head drop. 她把頭垂了下來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If your voice <b>drops</b> or if you <b>drop</b> your voice, you speak more quietly. 使 (聲音) 變小; (聲音) 變小","examples":["Her voice will drop to a dismissive whisper. 她的聲音將要降低成輕視性的低語。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>drop</b> someone or something somewhere, you take them somewhere and leave them there, usually in a car or other vehicle. 將…送到並放下","examples":["He dropped me outside the hotel. 他讓我在旅店外下了車。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>drop</b> an idea, course of action, or habit, you do not continue with it. 放棄 (想法、行動、習慣等)","examples":["He was told to drop the idea. 他被告知放棄這個想法。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If someone <b>is dropped</b> by a sports team or organization, they are no longer included in that team or employed by that organization. 把…除名; 把…解職","examples":["Alexander has been dropped from his multimillion-dollar-a-year job as spokesman for the company. 亞歷山大已經被拿掉了年薪數百萬的發言人的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drop</b> is also a noun. 迅速下降","examples":["He was prepared to take a drop in wages. 他準備好了接受一次工資的快速下調。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"下投","examples":["...the dropping of the first atomic bomb. …第一枚原子彈的投擲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"放棄","examples":["This was one of the factors that led to President Suharto's dropping of his previous objections. 這是導致蘇哈托總統放棄他先前反對意見的因素之一。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>drop</b> <b>of</b> a liquid is a very small amount of it shaped like a little ball. In informal English, you can also use <b>drop</b> when you are referring to a very small amount of something such as a drink. 滴; (如酒) 少量","examples":["...a drop of blue ink. …一滴藍墨水。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>drop</b> to talk about vertical distances. For example, a thirty-foot <b>drop</b> is a distance of thirty feet between the top of a cliff or wall and the bottom of it. 垂直距離","examples":["There was a sheer drop just outside my window. 我的窗外就是一個絕對垂直的落差。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Drops</b> are a kind of medicine which you put drop by drop into your ears, eyes, or nose. (滴入的) 藥水","examples":["And he had to have these drops in his eyes as well. 而且他還必須把這些藥水滴進眼睛裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>drops</b> <b>onto</b> something else, it falls onto that thing. If something <b>drops</b> <b>from</b> somewhere, it falls from that place. 掉","examples":["He felt hot tears dropping onto his fingers. 他感到熱淚滴在他的手指上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>drop</b> is used in expressions such as <b>to be about to drop</b> and <b>to dance until you drop</b> to emphasize that you are exhausted and can no longer continue doing something. (由於精疲力竭而) 放棄","examples":["She looked about to drop. 她看上去要放棄了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>drop</b> to a lower position in a sports competition, you move to that position. (在比賽中) 名次下降","examples":["She has dropped to third in the world ranking. 她已跌至世界排名第三。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drop off</b> means the same as . 將…送到並放下","examples":["Just drop me off at the airport. 把我送到飛機場下車就行。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>drop a hint</b>, you give a hint or say something in a casual way. 露口風","examples":["Jerry dropped hints that he and Julie were talking about getting married. 傑裡露出口風說他同朱莉已談婚論嫁了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you want someone to <b>drop the subject</b>, <b>drop it</b>, or <b>let it drop</b>, you want them to stop talking about something, often because you are annoyed that they keep talking about it. 別再討論某事","examples":["Mary Ann wished he would just drop it. 瑪麗安希望他不要再談這事。"]}]}]},"ending":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結尾，結局；字尾，詞尾；終止，終結；末梢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結束；終止（end 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the last part of a book, story, play, or film as the <b>ending</b>, especially when you are considering the way that the story ends. 結局","examples":["The film has a Hollywood happy ending. 這部電影具有好萊塢式的美滿結局。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>ending</b> of a word is the last part of it. 詞尾","examples":["...common word endings, like \"ing\" in walking. …常見詞尾，比如中的-。"]}]}]},"element":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基本部分，要素；元素；有點，少量；一群人；惡劣天氣（the elements）；基本原理；適宜的環境；電熱元件，電熱絲；（基督教聖餐中的）麵包和酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The different <b>elements</b> of something are the different parts it contains. 組成部分","examples":["The exchange of prisoners of war was one of the key elements of the UN's peace plan. 交換戰俘是聯合國和平計劃的主要內容之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>element</b> of a situation, activity, or process is an important quality or feature that it has or needs. 要素; 特點","examples":["Physical fitness has now become an important element in our lives. 身體健康現已成為我們生活中的重要元素。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you talk about <b>elements</b> within a society or organization, you are referring to groups of people who have similar aims, beliefs, or habits. (具有相似目標、信仰或者習慣的) 群體; 分子","examples":["The government must weed out criminal elements from within the security forces. 政府必須剔除保安隊伍內部的犯罪分子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something has an <b>element</b> <b>of</b> a particular quality or emotion, it has a certain amount of this quality or emotion. 成分","examples":["These reports clearly contain elements of propaganda. 這些報告明顯帶有宣傳的成分。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>element</b> is a substance such as gold, oxygen, or carbon that consists of only one type of atom. 元素","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>element</b> in an electric or water heater is the metal part that changes the electric current into heat. 電阻絲","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can refer to the weather, especially wind and rain, as <b>the elements</b>. 天氣 (尤指風雨)","examples":["The area where most refugees are waiting is exposed to the elements. 大部分難民滯留的地區暴露在風雨之中。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>in</b> their <b>element</b>, you mean that they are in a situation they enjoy. 如魚得水","examples":["My stepmother was in her element, organizing everything. 我繼母那時如魚得水，安排著所有一切。"]}]}]},"enemy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敵人，反對者；敵國，敵軍；大敵，危害物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"敵人的，敵方的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is your <b>enemy</b>, they hate you or want to harm you. 仇敵","examples":["Imagine loving your enemy and doing good to those who hated you. 想像著愛你的敵人，為仇人做好事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is your <b>enemy</b>, they are opposed to you and to what you think or do. 反對者","examples":["Her political enemies were quick to pick up on this series of disasters. 她的政敵很快注意到這一系列的災難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>enemy</b> is an army or other force that is opposed to you in a war, or a country with which your country is at war. 敵軍","examples":["The enemy were pursued for two miles. 敵軍被追趕了兩英里。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing is the <b>enemy of</b> another thing, the second thing cannot happen or succeed because of the first thing. 敵對面","examples":["Reform, as we know, is the enemy of revolution. 革新，如我們所知，是革命的敵對面。"]}]}]},"effect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"作用，影響；（刻意製造的）效果，印象；所有物，財產；生效，實行"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"實現，引起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>effect</b> <b>of</b> one thing <b>on</b> another is the change that the first thing causes in the second thing. 影響","examples":["Parents worry about the effect of music on their adolescent's behaviour. 家長們擔心音樂對於其青少年子女行為的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>effect</b> is an impression that someone creates deliberately, for example in a place or in a piece of writing. 印象","examples":["The whole effect is cool, light, and airy. 整體印象是涼爽、明亮和通風。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A person's <b>effects</b> are the things that they have with them at a particular time, for example when they are arrested or admitted to a hospital, or the things that they owned when they died. 個人財物","examples":["His daughters were collecting his effects. 他的女兒們正在收集他的個人物品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>effects</b> in a film are the specially created sounds and scenery. (影片中音響或佈景的) 特殊效果","examples":["It's got a gripping story, great acting, superb sets, and stunning effects. 電影有扣人心絃的故事情節、精湛的表演、絕妙的佈景和驚人的特效。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>effect</b> something that you are trying to achieve, you succeed in causing it to happen. 實現","examples":["Prospects for effecting real political change seemed to have taken a major step backwards. 實現真正政治變革的前景似乎暗淡了許多。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is doing something <b>for effect</b>, you mean that they are doing it in order to impress people and to draw attention to themselves. 為了加深印象; 為了引人注目","examples":["The southern accent was put on for effect. 假操南方口音以引人注意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You add <b>in effect</b> to a statement or opinion that is not precisely accurate, but that you feel is a reasonable description or summary of a particular situation. 實際上","examples":["That deal would create, in effect, the world's biggest airline. 那筆交易實際上將造就世界最大的航空公司。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>put</b>, <b>bring</b>, or <b>carry</b> a plan or idea <b>into effect</b>, you cause it to happen in practice. 實施","examples":["These and other such measures ought to have been put into effect in 1985. 這些及其他此類措施本應於1985年付諸實施。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a law or policy <b>takes effect</b> or <b>comes into effect</b> at a particular time, it officially begins to apply or be valid from that time. If it <b>remains in effect</b>, it still applies or is still valid. 實施; 生效","examples":["...the ban on new logging permits which will take effect in July. …將於7月生效的新伐木許可證禁止令。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that something <b>takes effect</b> when it starts to produce the results that are intended. 見效","examples":["The second injection should only have been given once the first drug had taken effect. 第2針本應只在第1針見效後才能注射。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>effect</b> in expressions such as <b>to good effect</b> and <b>to no effect</b> in order to indicate how successful or impressive an action is. 有 (無) 效地","examples":["Mr. Morris feels the museum is using advertising to good effect. 莫里斯先生感到博物館正在有效地利用廣告。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>to this effect</b>, <b>to that effect</b>, or <b>to the effect that</b> to indicate that you have given or are giving a summary of something that was said or written, and not the actual words used. 大意是","examples":["I understand that a circular to this effect will be issued in the next few weeks. 我得知，接下來的幾星期內將釋出大意如此的傳閱檔案。"]}]}]},"eraser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橡皮擦，黑板擦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>eraser</b> is an object, for example, a piece of rubber or a felt pad, that is used for removing something that has been written using a pencil or chalk. 橡皮擦; 板擦","examples":[]}]}]},"enjoyment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樂趣，樂事；享受，享有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enjoyment</b> is the feeling of pleasure and satisfaction that you have when you do or experience something that you like. 愉快","examples":["I apologize if your enjoyment of the film was spoiled. 我感到抱歉，如果打擾了你們對電影的欣賞。"]}]}]},"envelope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信封，封皮；氣囊；（彗核）包層，彗發；（數學）包絡線，包絡面；（生物）包膜；極限資料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>envelope</b> is the rectangular paper cover in which you send a letter to someone through the mail. 信封","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>pushes the envelope</b>, they do something to a greater degree or in a more extreme way than it has ever been done before. 挑戰極限; 突破常規","examples":["There's a valuable place for fashion and design that pushes the envelope a bit. 突破點兒常規的時尚和設計有其寶貴地位。"]}]}]},"energy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能力，力氣；精力，活力；能源；能，能量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Energy</b> is the ability and strength to do active physical things and the feeling that you are full of physical power and life. 精力","examples":["He was saving his energy for next week's race in Tuscon. 他正為下週在特斯康舉行的比賽養精蓄銳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Energy</b> is determination and enthusiasm about doing things. 幹勁","examples":["You have drive and energy for those things you are interested in. 你對那些你感興趣的事情有動力、有幹勁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>energies</b> are the efforts and attention that you can direct toward a particular aim. 精力","examples":["She had started to devote her energies to teaching rather than performing. 她已經開始將精力投入到教學而不是表演中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Energy</b> is the power from sources such as electricity and coal that makes machines work or provides heat. 能","examples":["...those who favour nuclear energy. …那些擁護核能的人們。"]}]}]},"environment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自然環境，生態環境；周圍狀況，條件；工作平臺，軟體包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>environment</b> is all the circumstances, people, things, and events around them that influence their life. 環境","examples":["Students in our schools are taught in a safe, secure environment. 我校學生在安全無憂的環境中接受教育。","The moral characters of men are formed not by heredity but by environment. 人的品德不是由遺傳而是由環境形成的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>environment</b> consists of the particular natural surroundings in which you live or exist, considered in relation to their physical characteristics or weather conditions. 生存環境","examples":["...a safe environment for marine mammals. …一個適合海洋哺乳動物的安全環境。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The environment</b> is the natural world of land, sea, air, plants, and animals. 自然環境","examples":["...persuading people to respect the environment. …勸人們重視自然環境。"]}]}]},"entrance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"入口，進口；進入，進門；（演員的）登臺，登場；進入權，進入許可；捲入，參與；著手，開始；就任，就職"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使入迷，使狂喜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>entrance</b> <b>to</b> a place is the way into it, for example, a door or gate. 入口","examples":["Beside the entrance to the church, turn right. 在教堂入口邊向右轉。","He was driven out of a side entrance with his hand covering his face. 他被從邊門趕了出來，一隻手還捂著臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's arrival in a place as their <b>entrance</b>, especially when you think that they are trying to be noticed and admired. 登場; 蒞臨","examples":["If she had noticed her father's entrance, she gave no indication. 關於她是否曾注意到她父親的蒞臨，她未作表示。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a performer makes his or her <b>entrance</b> onto the stage, he or she comes onto the stage. 出場","examples":["When he made his entrance on stage there was uproar. 他出場時譁然。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you gain <b>entrance</b> <b>to</b> a particular place, you manage to get in there. 進入許可","examples":["Hewitt had gained entrance to the Hall by pretending to be a heating engineer. 休伊特曾假裝成供暖技師得到進入那個大廳的許可。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you gain <b>entrance</b> <b>to</b> a particular profession, society, or institution, you are accepted as a member of it. 入 (行、會、學) 許可","examples":["Many students have insufficient science and mathematics background to gain entrance to engineering school. 許多學生沒有足夠的科學和數學知識背景得到進入工程學院的許可。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you make an <b>entrance</b> <b>into</b> a particular activity or system, you succeed in becoming involved in it. 進入","examples":["The acquisition helped BCCI make its initial entrance into the U.S. market. 這次接管幫助國際信貸銀行首次進入了美國市場。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>entrances</b> you, they cause you to feel delight and wonder, often so that all your attention is taken up and you cannot think about anything else. 使著迷","examples":["As soon as I met Dick, he entranced me because he has a lovely voice. 我一見到迪克，他就使我著迷，因為他有好聽的嗓音。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"著迷的","examples":["He is entranced by the kindness of her smile. 她善意的微笑令他著迷。"]}]}]},"error":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯誤，差錯；（棒球、網球等運動中的）失誤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>error</b> is something you have done that is considered to be incorrect or wrong, or that should not have been done. 錯誤","examples":["NASA discovered a mathematical error in its calculations. 美國國家航空航天局發現了其計算中的一個數學錯誤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in error</b> or if it happens <b>in error</b>, you do it or it happens because you have made a mistake, especially in your judgment. 錯誤地","examples":["The plane was shot down in error by a NATO missile. 那架飛機被北大西洋公約組織的一顆導彈錯誤地擊落了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone sees <b>the error of</b> their <b>ways</b>, they realize or admit that they have made a mistake or behaved badly. 認識到自身錯誤","examples":["I wanted an opportunity to talk some sense into him and try to make him see the error of his ways. 我想找個機會給他講講道理，儘量讓他認識到自身的錯誤。"]}]}]},"excitement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"令人激動（或興奮）的事，刺激因素；激動，興奮；性興奮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>excitement</b> to refer to the state of being excited, or to something that excites you. 興奮; 令人興奮的事物","examples":["Everyone is in a state of great excitement. 人人都處於極度興奮之中。"]}]}]},"event":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事件，大事；社交場合，既定活動；賽事，比賽專案；<古>結果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>event</b> is something that happens, especially when it is unusual or important. You can use <b>events</b> to describe all the things that are happening in a particular situation. (尤指特殊、重大) 事件","examples":["A new inquiry into the events of the day was opened in 2002. 對那天發生的事件的新一輪調查於2002年開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>event</b> is a planned and organized occasion, for example a social gathering or a sports tournament. (有計劃、有組織的) 活動","examples":["...major sporting events. …重大體育賽事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>event</b> is one of the races or competitions that are part of an organized occasion such as a sports tournament. 比賽專案","examples":["The main events start at 1 p.m. 主賽專案下午1點開始。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in the event of</b>, <b>in the event that</b>, and <b>in that event</b> when you are talking about a possible future situation, especially when you are planning what to do if it occurs. 倘若發生…","examples":["The bank has agreed to give an immediate refund in the unlikely event of an error being made. 銀行已同意倘若出現不太可能的錯誤便立即退款。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>in any event</b> after you have been discussing a situation, in order to indicate that what you are saying is true or possible, in spite of anything that has happened or may happen. 不管怎樣","examples":["In any event, the bowling alley restaurant proved quite acceptable. 不管怎樣，那家保齡球館的餐廳證明是很受歡迎的。"]}]}]},"expert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專家，能手，權威"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"專業的，熟練的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當專家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>expert</b> is a person who is very skilled at doing something or who knows a lot about a particular subject. 專家; 行家","examples":["...a yoga expert. …一位瑜伽專家。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>expert</b> <b>at</b> doing something is very skilled at it. 在行的","examples":["The Japanese are expert at lowering manufacturing costs. 日本人在降低生產成本方面很在行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>expert</b> hands or an <b>expert</b> eye, you mean that they are very skilful or experienced in using their hands or eyes for a particular purpose. 行家的","examples":["Harvey cured the pain with his own expert hands. 哈維用他那行家之手治癒了那病痛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Expert</b> advice or help is given by someone who has studied a subject thoroughly or who is very skilled at a particular job. 專家的","examples":["We'll need an expert opinion. 我們將需要專家的意見。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在行地","examples":["Shopkeepers expertly rolled spices up in bay leaves. 店主在行地把各種香料捲進了月桂葉中。"]}]}]},"eyebrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"眉，眉毛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>eyebrows</b> are the lines of hair that grow above your eyes. 眉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something causes you to <b>raise an eyebrow</b> or to <b>raise</b> your <b>eyebrows</b>, it causes you to feel surprised or disapproving. 揚起眉毛 (表示驚訝、不贊成)","examples":["An intriguing item on the news pages caused me to raise an eyebrow over my morning coffee. 喝早咖啡時，新聞頁面上的一條趣聞讓我驚訝。","He raised his eyebrows over some of the suggestions. 他不贊成其中的一些建議。"]}]}]},"excuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藉口，託詞；正當理由；寬恕，赦免；拙劣樣品，蹩腳貨；<美>（醫生或父母為學生寫的）病假條，請假條"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"原諒，寬恕；辯解，開脫；准許……離開；同意免除"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>excuse</b> is a reason that you give in order to explain why something has been done or has not been done, or in order to avoid doing something. 藉口","examples":["It is easy to find excuses for his indecisiveness. 為他的優柔寡斷尋找藉口是件容易的事。","If you stop making excuses and do it you'll wonder what took you so long. 如果你停止辯解而開始行動，你就會驚訝是什麼讓你耗費了這麼長的時間。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>no excuse</b> <b>for</b> something, you are emphasizing that it should not happen, or expressing disapproval that it has happened. 沒有理由","examples":["There's no excuse for behaviour like that. 像那樣的行為毫無道理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>excuse me</b> to apologize when you have bumped into someone, or when you need to move past someone in a crowd. 抱歉; 借過 (用於因撞上別人或需要從人群中擠過表示歉意)","examples":["Saying excuse me, Seaton pushed his way into the crowded living room. 西頓一邊嘴裡說著“借過”，一邊奮力擠進了擁擠的客廳。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>excuse</b> someone or <b>excuse</b> their behaviour means to provide reasons for their actions, especially when other people disapprove of these actions. 為…開脫","examples":["He excused himself by saying he was \"forced to rob to maintain my wife and cat.\" 他為自己開脫，說是“為養活妻子和貓才迫不得已去搶劫的”。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>excuse</b> someone <b>for</b> something wrong that they have done, you forgive them for it. 原諒","examples":["Many people might have excused them for shirking some of their responsibilities. 很多人也許已經原諒他們逃避一些責任的行為了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is excused</b> <b>from</b> a duty or responsibility, they are told that they do not have to carry it out. 免除…的責任","examples":["She is usually excused from her duties during the summer holiday. 在暑期她一般不必擔負責任。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>excuse</b> <b>yourself</b>, you use a phrase such as \"Excuse me\" as a polite way of saying that you are about to leave. 准許…離開","examples":["He excused himself and went up to his room. 他禮貌地告辭後便上樓去了自己的房間。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Excuse me</b>\" when you want to politely get someone's attention, especially when you are about to ask them a question. 打擾一下 (用於禮貌地引起某人的注意)","examples":["Excuse me, but are you Mr. Honig? 打擾一下，請問您就是霍尼格先生嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>excuse me</b> to apologize to someone when you have disturbed or interrupted them. 對不起 (用於因打擾或打斷某人而表示歉意)","examples":["Excuse me interrupting, but there's something I need to say. 恕我打斷一下，但有件事我需要說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>excuse me</b> or a phrase such as <b>if you'll excuse me</b> as a polite way of indicating that you are about to leave or that you are about to stop talking to someone. 失陪 (用於禮貌地表示要離開或中斷談話)","examples":["\"Excuse me,\" she said to José, and left the room. “失陪了，”她對喬賽說，然後離開了那個房間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>excuse me, but</b> to indicate that you are about to disagree with someone. 抱歉，不過 (用於禮貌地表示不贊成)","examples":["Excuse me, but I want to know what all this has to do with us. 抱歉，不過我想知道這一切和我們有什麼關係。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You say <b>excuse me</b> to apologize when you have done something slightly embarrassing or impolite, such as burping, hiccuping, or sneezing. 不好意思 (用於因打嗝、打噴嚏等尷尬失禮行為而表示歉意)","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say \"<b>Excuse me?</b>\" to show that you want someone to repeat what they have just said. 請再說一遍","examples":["\"Excuse me?\" Kate said, not sure she'd heard correctly. “能再說一遍嗎？”凱特說道，不確信自己有沒有聽對。"]}]}]},"experience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經歷，往事；經驗，閱歷；傳統"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"經歷，遭遇；體會到，感受到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Experience</b> is knowledge or skill in a particular job or activity that you have gained because you have done that job or activity for a long time. 經驗","examples":["He has also had managerial experience on every level. 他還具備各層次的管理經驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Experience</b> is used to refer to the past events, knowledge, and feelings that make up someone's life or character. 閱歷","examples":["I should not be in any danger here, but experience has taught me caution. 我在這裡應該沒有任何危險，但閱歷已教會我謹慎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>experience</b> is something that you do or that happens to you, especially something important that affects you. 經歷","examples":["His only experience of gardening so far proved immensely satisfying. 他僅有的園藝經歷到目前為止非常令人滿意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Experience</b> is also a noun. 感受","examples":["...the experience of pain. …痛苦的感受。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>experience</b> a particular situation, you are in that situation or it happens to you. 經歷","examples":["We had never experienced this kind of holiday before and had no idea what to expect. 我們以前從未經歷過這種假期，不知道有什麼可期待的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>experience</b> a feeling, you feel it or are affected by it. 感受","examples":["Widows seem to experience more distress than widowers. 寡婦似乎比鰥夫感受更多痛苦。"]}]}]},"extra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"額外的；另外收費的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"另收費的事物；臨時演員；（非擊球所得的）附加分；<舊>（報紙的）號外"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"額外；特別，格外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>extra</b> to describe an amount, person, or thing that is added to others of the same kind, or that can be added to others of the same kind. 多加的; 可另加的","examples":["Police warned motorists to allow extra time to get to work. 警察告誡開車上下班的人要留出富餘時間。","There's an extra blanket in the bottom drawer of the cupboard. 衣櫥的底櫃有一條備用毯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>extra</b>, you have to pay more money for it in addition to what you are already paying for something. (費用) 另計的","examples":["For foreign orders postage is extra. 對於國外訂單，郵資是另計的。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Extra</b> is also a pronoun. 額外費用","examples":["She won't pay any extra. 她不會支付任何額外費用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Extra</b> is also an adverb. 額外地","examples":["You may be charged 10% extra for this service. 你可能會因此項服務而被額外收取10%的費用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>extra</b> in front of adjectives and adverbs to emphasize the quality that they are describing. 格外地","examples":["I said you'd have to be extra careful. 我說過你必須格外小心。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Extras</b> are additional amounts of money that are added to the price that you have to pay for something. 額外費用","examples":["There are no hidden extras. 沒有任何隱蔽的額外費用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Extras</b> are things that are not necessary in a situation, activity, or object, but that make it more comfortable, useful, or enjoyable. 額外之物","examples":["Optional extras include cooking classes at a top restaurant. 可選的額外之物包括一家高階餐館的烹飪課程。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>extras</b> in a film are the people who play unimportant parts, for example, as members of a crowd. 臨時演員","examples":["In 1944, Kendall entered films as an extra. 1944年，肯德爾作為一名臨時演員進入電影界。"]}]}]},"exercise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動，鍛鍊；（一套）動作，體操；練習，演練；運用；活動，任務；典禮；宗教儀式，禮拜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"運動，鍛鍊；運用，行使；使擔憂，使煩惱；馴，遛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>exercise</b> something such as your authority, your rights, or a good quality, you use it or put it into effect. 行使; 運用","examples":["They are merely exercising their right to free speech. 他們僅僅是在行使言論自由的權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a movement or activity <b>exercises</b> a part of your body, it keeps it strong, healthy, or in good condition. 鍛鍊 (身體某一部位)","examples":["They call rowing the perfect sport. It exercises every major muscle group. 他們把划船稱之為完美的運動。它鍛鍊身體的各主要肌肉群。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exercise</b> is also a noun. 行使; 運用","examples":["Social structures are maintained through the exercise of political and economic power. 社會結構是透過政治和經濟權力的運用來維護的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Exercise</b> is also a noun. 鍛鍊","examples":["Lack of exercise can lead to feelings of depression and exhaustion. 鍛鍊的缺乏會導致抑鬱和疲倦感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Exercises</b> are a series of movements or actions that you do in order to get in shape, remain healthy, or practise for a particular physical activity. 鍛鍊","examples":["I do special neck and shoulder exercises. 我做專門針對頸部與肩部的鍛鍊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Exercises</b> are military activities and operations that are not part of a real war, but that allow the armed forces to practise for a real war. (軍事) 演習","examples":["General Powell predicted that in the future it might even be possible to stage joint military exercises. 鮑威爾將軍預言將來甚至可能舉行聯合軍事演習。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>exercise</b> is a short activity or piece of work that you do, in school for example, which is designed to help you learn a particular skill. 練習","examples":["Try working through the opening exercises in this chapter. 努力完成本章開頭部分的各個練習。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>exercise</b>, you move your body energetically in order to get in shape and to remain healthy. 鍛鍊","examples":["She exercises two or three times a week. 她一週鍛鍊兩三次。"]}]}]},"failure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"失敗；失敗的人（或企業、事物）；未做到；缺乏，不足；故障，衰退；公司倒閉；歉收；突然失去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Failure</b> is a lack of success in doing or achieving something, especially in relation to a particular activity. 失敗","examples":["This policy is doomed to failure. 這項政策註定要失敗。","Three attempts on the 200-metre record ended in failure. 3次向200米紀錄的衝擊以失敗告終。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>failure</b> <b>to</b> do a particular thing is the fact that you do not do it, even though you were expected to do it. 未成","examples":["They see their failure to produce an heir as a curse from God. 他們將自己未能生育一個後嗣看作是來自上帝的一個詛咒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>a</b> <b>failure</b>, it is not a success. 失敗","examples":["The marriage was a failure and they both wanted to be free of it. 這段婚姻是個失敗，他們倆都想從中解放出來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>a</b> <b>failure</b>, you mean that they have not succeeded in a particular activity, or that they are unsuccessful at everything they do. 失敗者","examples":["Elgar received many honours and much acclaim and yet he often considered himself a failure. 埃爾加獲得了很多榮譽和歡呼，但是他常常把自己看成一個失敗者。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If there is a <b>failure</b> of something, for example, a machine or part of the body, it goes wrong and stops working or developing properly. 故障","examples":["There were also several accidents mainly caused by engine failures on take-off. 還有一些事故主要是由起飛時引擎故障導致的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If there is a <b>failure</b> of a business or bank, it is no longer able to continue operating. 倒閉","examples":["Business failures rose 16% last month. 上個月公司倒閉上升了16%。"]}]}]},"favor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"較喜歡，偏愛，偏袒；支援，贊同；有利於，有助於；（非正式）長得像（尤指親屬）；（尤指受傷部位）小心對待，愛護；（正式）賜予，給予；（固定搭配 curry favor (with)）討好，巴結，拍馬屁"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"幫助，恩惠，善舉；贊同，支援，好感（常用於 in favor of）；偏袒，偏愛；有利條件，好處，優勢（常用於 in someone's favor）；聚會小禮品，贈品（常作 party favor）；（委婉，常作 favors）性恩惠，性方面的允諾；（舊）表示支援或愛慕的飾帶，徽章"}],"sections":[]},"favorite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（美國英語）最受喜愛的，最中意的（同 favourite）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"受喜愛的人（或事物），最愛；（比賽或競賽中）最有希望的獲勝者，熱門；（計算機、網際網路）收藏夾；收藏項（如網頁書籤）；（Favorite）（美）費沃裡特（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（計算機、網際網路）把……新增到收藏夾，收藏（網頁等）"}],"sections":[]},"fail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"失敗；未能做到，未能做；辜負，使失望；不及格，未能透過；出故障，失靈；衰弱，衰退；破產，倒閉；歉收；不下雨，下雨少；忘記"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不及格；<非正式>過失，失敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fail</b> to do something that you were trying to do, you are unable to do it or do not succeed in doing it. 未能","examples":["The party failed to win the election. 該政黨未能贏得選舉。","He failed in his attempt to take control of the company. 他的掌控這家公司的企圖失敗了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>fails</b> to do a particular thing that they should have done, they do not do it. 未做","examples":["Some schools fail to require any homework. 有些學校沒有佈置任何家庭作業。","He failed to file tax returns for 1982. 他沒有填報1982年的納稅申報單。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>fails</b> you, they do not do what you had expected or trusted them to do. 辜負","examples":["We waited twenty-one years, don't fail us now. 我們等了21年，如今不要辜負我們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>fails</b> a test, examination, or course, they perform badly in it and do not reach the standard that is required. 使不及格","examples":["I lived in fear of failing my final exams. 我生活在期末考試不及格的擔憂中。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>fails</b> you in a test, examination, or course, they judge that you have not reached a high enough standard in it. 使不及格","examples":["...the two professors who had failed him during his first year of law school. …他上法學院第一年時使他不及格的兩位教授。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an activity, attempt, or plan <b>fails</b>, it is not successful. 失敗","examples":["We tried to develop plans for them to get along, which all failed miserably. 我們設法制定出讓他們相處融洽的計劃，但都慘敗了。","He was afraid the revolution they had started would fail. 他擔心他們發起的革命會失敗。","...a failed military coup. …一次失敗的軍事政變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>fails</b>, it stops working properly, or does not do what it is supposed to do. 失靈","examples":["The lights mysteriously failed, and we stumbled around in complete darkness. 燈神秘地熄滅了，我們在完全的黑暗中跌跌撞撞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a business, organization, or system <b>fails</b>, it becomes unable to continue in operation or in existence. 倒閉","examples":["So far this year, 104 banks have failed. 到今年為止，104家銀行已倒閉。","...a failed hotel business. …一家倒閉的酒店。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as your health or a physical quality <b>is failing</b>, it is becoming gradually weaker or less effective. 衰退","examples":["He was 58, and his health was failing rapidly. 他58歲，健康狀況每況愈下。","Here in the hills, the light failed more quickly. 在這兒的山裡，光線減弱得更快了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fail</b> is also a noun. 不及格","examples":["It's the difference between a pass and a fail. 這是及格和不及格的區別。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>if all else fails</b> to suggest what could be done in a certain situation if all the other things you have tried are unsuccessful. 迫不得已的話","examples":["If all else fails, I could always drive a truck. 迫不得已的話，我總可以開卡車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>without fail</b> to emphasize that something always happens. 必定","examples":["He attended every meeting without fail. 他逢會必參加。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>without fail</b> to emphasize an order or a promise. 務必","examples":["On the 30th you must without fail hand in some money for Alex. 在30號你務必親手交給亞歷克斯一些錢。"]}]}]},"fee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"費用，酬金；會費，入場費；封地，采邑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"付給（某人）費用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fee</b> is a sum of money that you pay to be allowed to do something. 費用","examples":["He paid his licence fee, and walked out with a brand-new driving licence. 他付了駕照費用，拿著一張全新的駕照走出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fee</b> is the amount of money that a person or organization is paid for a particular job or service that they provide. 酬金","examples":["Lawyer's fees can be substantial. 律師的酬金可以很豐厚。"]}]}]},"fault":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯誤；責任，過錯；缺點，故障；斷層；發球失誤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挑剔，指責；發球失誤；產生斷層；<古>犯錯誤，做錯事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a bad or undesirable situation is your <b>fault</b>, you caused it or are responsible for it. 過錯; 過失","examples":["There was no escaping the fact: it was all his fault. 無法逃避這一事實：這都是他的錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fault</b> is a mistake in what someone is doing or in what they have done. 錯誤","examples":["It is a big fault to think that you can learn how to manage people in business school. 認為你能在商學院學會如何管理人是一大錯誤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fault</b> in someone or something is a weakness in them or something that is not perfect. 缺點","examples":["His manners had always made her blind to his faults. 他的彬彬有禮總使她看不見他的缺點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>fault</b> is a large crack in the surface of the earth. 斷層","examples":["...the San Andreas Fault. …聖安德烈亞斯斷層。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>fault</b> in tennis is a service that is wrong according to the rules. (網球的) 發球失誤","examples":["He caught the ball on his first toss and then served a fault. 他擊中了第一次拋起的球，隨後發球失誤。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cannot</b> <b>fault</b> someone, you cannot find any reason for criticizing them or the things that they are doing. 批評","examples":["You can't fault them for lack of invention. 你不能因為他們沒有發明而加以批評他們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>at fault</b>, they are to blame or are responsible for a particular situation that has gone wrong. 有過錯","examples":["He could never accept that he had been at fault. 他永遠也無法接受他犯了過錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>find fault</b> <b>with</b> something or someone, you look for mistakes and complain about them. 挑剔; 指責","examples":["I was disappointed whenever the cook found fault with my work. 每當廚師挑我工作上的毛病時，我都很失望。"]}]}]},"express":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"表達，表露；表現，體現；（用數學方法）表示；壓榨，擠壓出（空氣或液體）；特快發運"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"快車；快遞；初速大的獵槍；專使；捷運公司"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"快遞的，特快的；明確的；特意的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"用快遞寄送"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>express</b> an idea or feeling, or <b>express</b> <b>yourself</b>, you show what you think or feel. 表達","examples":["He expressed grave concern at American attitudes. 他對美國的態度表達了嚴肅關注。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an idea or feeling <b>expresses</b> <b>itself</b> in some way, it can be clearly seen in someone's actions or in its effects on a situation. (想法、情感) 流露; 呈現","examples":["The anxiety of the separation often expresses itself as anger toward the child for getting lost. 對失散的焦慮常常表現成對孩子走失的憤怒。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>express</b> command or order is one that is clearly and deliberately stated. 明確陳述的 (命令、指令)","examples":["This mighty electricity-generating power station was built on the express orders of the president. 這一大型電力發電站是按照總統的明確指令修建的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to an <b>express</b> intention or purpose, you are emphasizing that it is a deliberate and specific one that you have before you do something. 特定的 (意圖、目的)","examples":["The express purpose of the flights was to get Americans out of the danger zone. 這些航班的特定目的是讓美國人離開該險區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Express</b> is used to describe special services provided by companies or organizations such as the U.S. Postal Service, in which things are sent or done faster than usual for a higher price. 快遞的","examples":["A special express service is available by fax. 一項特快服務透過傳真可以實現。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"明確陳述地","examples":["He has expressly forbidden her to go out on her own. 他已明確禁止她獨自外出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"特定地","examples":["...projects expressly designed to support cattle farmers. …為扶持養牛戶而特定規劃的專案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Express</b> is also an adverb. 快遞地","examples":["Send it express. 用快遞把它送出。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>express</b> or an <b>express</b> train is a fast train that stops at very few stations. 快速列車","examples":["Punctually at 7:45, the express to Kuala Lumpur left Singapore station. 開往吉隆坡的特快列車7：45準時從新加坡站駛出。"]}]}]},"fellow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小夥子，傢伙；同伴，同事，同學；研究員；男朋友；（研究期間領取津貼的）研究生；<英>（大學的）董事；（學術或專業團體）會員；對等者，對手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同類的，同伴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>fellow</b> to describe people who are in the same situation as you, or people you feel you have something in common with. 同種情況的; 同類的","examples":["She discovered to her pleasure, a talent for making her fellow guests laugh. 她高興地發現一個把她同來的客人逗笑的本事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fellow</b> is a man or boy. 傢伙; 小夥兒","examples":["By all accounts, Rodger would appear to be a fine fellow. 根據大家的說法，羅傑應該是個好小夥兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fellow</b> <b>of</b> an academic or professional association is someone who is a specially elected member of it, usually because of their work or achievements or as a mark of honour. 特別會員","examples":["...the fellows of the Zoological Society. …動物協會的特別會員們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>fellows</b> are the people who you work with, do things with, or who are like you in some way. 同事; 同伴","examples":["He stood out in terms of competence from all his fellows. 他在能力方面比他所有同事都突出。"]}]}]},"female":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"女性的，婦女的；女性特有的；由女性組成的；內孔的；雌性的，母的；雌蕊的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雌性動物，雌性植物；女子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>female</b> is a woman or a girl. 女性的","examples":["...a sixteen-piece dance band with a female singer. …一支有一名女歌手的16人伴舞樂隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Female</b> matters and things relate to, belong to, or affect women rather than men. 女性的","examples":["...female infertility. …女性不孕症。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Female</b> is also an adjective. 雌性的","examples":["...the scent given off by the female aphid to attract the male. …雌性蚜蟲為吸引雄性而發出的香味。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Women and girls are sometimes referred to as <b>females</b> when they are being considered as a type. 女性","examples":["Hay fever affects males more than females. 男性感染花粉熱多於女性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to any creature that can lay eggs or produce babies from its body as a <b>female</b>. 雌性生物","examples":["Each female will lay just one egg in April or May. 每隻雌性在4月或5月份將只產一顆卵。"]}]}]},"fence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"籬笆，柵欄，圍欄；（賽馬中的）障礙物；<非正式>買賣贓物者，銷贓犯；劍術；（刨子、鋸子或其他工具的）防護裝置，導向裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用柵欄、籬笆或圍欄）圍住，隔開；擊劍；巧妙回答，搪塞；出售（贓物）；防護，保衛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fence</b> is a barrier between two areas of land, made of wood or wire supported by posts. 柵欄","examples":["Villagers say the fence would restrict public access to the hills. 村民們說柵欄將限制公眾進入山區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fence</b> in show jumping or horse racing is an obstacle or barrier that horses have to jump over. 障礙物","examples":["The horse fell at the last fence. 這匹馬在最後一道障礙那裡跌倒了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fence</b> an area of land, you surround it with a fence. 圈起","examples":["The first task was to fence the wood to exclude sheep. 第一項任務是要把小樹林圈起來使羊進入。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sit on the fence</b>, you avoid supporting a particular side in a discussion or argument. 保持中立","examples":["They are sitting on the fence and refusing to commit themselves. 他們保持中立，拒絕明確表態。"]}]}]},"festival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"活動節期，紀念活動；節日，節慶"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"節日的，喜慶的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>festival</b> is an organized series of events such as musical concerts or drama productions. 節","examples":["Many towns hold their own summer festivals of music, theatre, and dance. 很多城市都舉辦自己的夏季音樂、戲劇和舞蹈節。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>festival</b> is a day or time of the year when people do not go to work or school and celebrate some special event, often a religious event. 節日","examples":["Shavuot is a two-day festival for Orthodox Jews. 五旬節是正統猶太教教民為期兩天的節日。"]}]}]},"fever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發燒，發熱；狂熱，高度興奮；熱病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使發燒，使激動不已"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>fever</b> when you are ill, your body temperature is higher than usual. 發燒","examples":["My Uncle Jim had a high fever. 我的叔叔吉姆發高燒了。"]}]}]},"firewoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"女消防員"}],"sections":[]},"fair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公平的；合理的，公正的；相當好的；（數量、大小）相當大的；淺色的，（膚色）白皙的，（頭髮）金色的；晴朗的；順風的；普通的；美麗的；界內的；<舊>（手段，方法）溫和的，非暴力的；<舊>（言語，談話，許諾）花言巧語的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"公平地，公正地；非常；正面地，直接地；清楚地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"集市，展覽會；露天遊樂場；廟會；義賣會；牲畜市場；美女；職業介紹會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"變得晴朗；使（車輛，船舶，飛機）具有流線型"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>fair</b> is reasonable, right, and just. 公平的","examples":["It didn't seem fair to leave out her father. 將她的父親排除在外似乎不公平。","Do you feel they're paying their fair share? 你覺得他們正支付自己應分擔的那一份嗎？","I wanted them to get a fair deal. 我希望他們得到一個公平的交易。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fair</b> amount, degree, size, or distance is quite a large amount, degree, size, or distance. 相當大的; 相當遠的","examples":["My neighbours across the street travel a fair amount. 我街對面的鄰居們去過相當多的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fair</b> guess or idea about something is one that is likely to be correct. 合理的","examples":["It's a fair guess to say that the damage will be extensive. 說破壞將很嚴重是合理的猜測。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>fair</b>, you mean that they are average in standard or quality, neither very good nor very bad. 一般的","examples":["Reimar had a fair command of English. 賴馬爾具備一般的英語水平。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone who is <b>fair</b>, or who has <b>fair</b> hair, has light-coloured hair. 淺色頭髮的","examples":["Both children were very like Robina, but were much fairer than she was. 兩個孩子都很像羅比娜，但是頭髮顏色比她的淺得多。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Fair</b> is also a combining form. 金髮的","examples":["...a tall, fair-haired man. …一個金髮的高個男人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Fair</b> skin is very pale and usually burns easily. 白皙的","examples":["It's important to protect my fair skin from the sun. 保護我白皙的皮膚不受日曬是很重要的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Fair</b> is also a combining form. 白皙的","examples":["Fair-skinned people who spend a great deal of time in the sun have the greatest risk of skin cancer. 皮膚白皙的人長時間待在太陽底下患皮膚癌的危險最大。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"When the weather is <b>fair</b>, it is quite sunny and not raining. 晴的","examples":["Weather conditions were fair. 天氣狀況晴好。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"公平地","examples":["...demonstrating concern for employees and solving their problems quickly and fairly. …證實對僱員的關注以及迅速公平地解決他們的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"in a fair way; correctly 恰當地","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"absolutely or squarely; quite 完全地; 直接地","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"really or very 真正地; 非常地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A county, state, or country <b>fair</b> is an event where there are, for example, displays of goods and animals, and amusements, games, and competitions. 集市","examples":["Every autumn I go to the county fair. 每個秋季我都去縣裡的集市。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fair</b> is an event at which people display and sell goods, especially goods of a particular type. 商品展銷會","examples":["...an antiques fair. …一個古董展銷會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>fair enough</b> when you want to say that a statement, decision, or action seems reasonable to a certain extent, but that perhaps there is more to be said or done. 說得過去","examples":["If you don't like it, fair enough, but that's hardly a justification to attack the whole thing. 如果你不喜歡它，可以，但把它說得一無是處就沒什麼道理了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone won a competition <b>fair and square</b>, you mean that they won honestly and without cheating. 正大光明地","examples":["There are no excuses. We were beaten fair and square. 沒有什麼藉口，我們被正大光明地打敗了。"]}]}]},"fighter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰士，鬥爭者，好戰者；（軍事）戰鬥機，殲擊機；（褒義）鬥士，奮鬥者；（體育）拳手，格鬥運動員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fighter</b> or a <b>fighter plane</b> is a fast military aircraft that is used for destroying other aircraft. 戰鬥機","examples":["...a fighter pilot. …一名戰鬥機飛行員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>fighter</b>, you approve of them because they continue trying to achieve things in spite of great difficulties or opposition. 鬥士","examples":["From the start it was clear this tiny girl was a real fighter. 從一開始，這個小女孩就顯然是一名真正的鬥士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fighter</b> is a person who physically fights another person, especially a professional boxer. 拳手","examples":["He was a real street fighter who'd do anything to win. 他是一名真正的街頭拳手，為了能贏會不擇手段。"]}]}]},"fireman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消防員，消防隊員，救火隊員；司爐，鍋爐工；（美式英語，棒球）救援投手；（Fireman）人名（姓氏），（英）法爾曼，亦譯費爾曼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fireman</b> is a person, usually a man, whose job is to put out fires. 消防員","examples":[]}]}]},"fisherman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漁夫，漁人，漁民；垂釣者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fisherman</b> is a person who catches fish as a job or for sport. 漁民; 垂釣者","examples":["The Algarve is a paradise for fishermen whether river anglers or deep-sea fishermen. 阿爾加維對河邊的垂釣者或深海的漁民都是一個天堂。"]}]}]},"film":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電影，影片；電影藝術，電影業；膠捲，底片；薄膜，薄層；紀實鏡頭，記錄畫面；<古>細絲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"錄製，拍攝電影；（似）被覆蓋上一薄層東西，變得朦朧；在……上覆以薄膜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>film</b> consists of moving pictures that have been recorded so that they can be shown in a theatre or on television. A film tells a story, or shows a real situation. 電影","examples":["Everything about the film was good. Good acting, good story, good fun. 這部電影樣樣都好：演技好，故事好，非常有趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>film</b> <b>of</b> powder, liquid, or oil is a very thin layer of it. 薄層","examples":["The sea is coated with a film of raw sewage. 海上覆蓋著薄薄一層未經處理的汙水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Film</b> of something is moving pictures of a real event that are shown on television or on a screen. 記實影片","examples":["He likes to look at film of old-time players. 他喜歡看那些以前運動員的影片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The making of films, considered as a form of art or a business, can be referred to as <b>film</b> or <b>films</b>. 電影藝術; 電影業","examples":["Film is a business with limited opportunities for actresses. 電影業對女演員來說機會有限。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Plastic <b>film</b> is a very thin sheet of plastic used to wrap and cover things. (塑膠) 薄膜","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>film</b> is the narrow roll of plastic that is used in a camera to take photographs. 膠捲","examples":["The photographers had already shot a dozen rolls of film. 攝影師們已經拍了一打膠捲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>film</b> something, you use a camera to take moving pictures which can be shown on a screen or on television. 把…拍攝成影片","examples":["He had filmed her life story. 他已經把她的人生故事拍成了電影。"]}]}]},"field":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"田地，田野；專業，領域；現場，實地；體育場；全體參賽者；礦場，油田；戰場；視野；（物理）場；資訊欄，欄位；外場員，防守隊；盾面，底"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"組建，派出；擔任守方；接（球），守（球）；處理，應付（問題或電話）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"實地的，野外的；（軍事裝備）輕便機動的，戰役用的；（比賽）田賽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>field</b> is an area of grass, for example, in a park or on a farm. A <b>field</b> is also an area of land on which a crop is grown. 草地; 田地","examples":["...a field of wheat. …一片麥田。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A sports <b>field</b> is an area of grass where sports are played. 運動場","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>field</b> is an area of land or sea bed under which large amounts of a particular mineral have been found. 礦田","examples":["...an extensive natural gas field in Alaska. …阿拉斯加的一個巨大的天然氣田。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A magnetic, gravitational, or electric <b>field</b> is the area in which that particular force is strong enough to have an effect. 場","examples":["Some people are worried that electromagnetic fields from electric power lines could increase the risk of cancer. 一些人擔心電源線的電磁場可能增加患癌症的風險。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A particular <b>field</b> is a particular subject of study or type of activity. 領域","examples":["Each of the authors of the tapes is an expert in his field. 這些磁帶的每一位作者都是其領域內的專家。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>field</b> is an area of a computer's memory or a program where data can be entered, edited, or stored. 欄位","examples":["Go to a site like Yahoo! Finance and enter \"AOL\" in the Get Quotes field. 登入雅虎財經那樣的一個網站，在報價欄輸入“AOL”。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>field</b> of vision or your visual <b>field</b> is the area that you can see without turning your head. 視野","examples":["Our field of vision is surprisingly wide. 我們的視野令人驚奇地廣闊。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>field</b> is a way of referring to all the competitors taking part in a particular race or sports contest. 所有參賽者","examples":["Going into the fourth lap, the two most broadly experienced riders led the field. 進入第4圈時，那兩名經驗最豐富的騎手領先。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>field</b> to describe work or study that is done in a real, natural environment rather than in a theoretical way or in controlled conditions. 現場的; 實地的","examples":["I also conducted a field study among the boys about their attitude to relationships. 我也在男生中進行了一項有關他們對人際關係態度的實地調查。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a game of baseball or cricket, the team that <b>is fielding</b> is trying to catch the ball, while the other team is trying to hit it. 防守","examples":["When we are fielding, the umpires keep looking at the ball. 當我們在防守時，裁判們都盯緊了球。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>fields</b> a question, you mean that they answer it or deal with it, usually successfully. 成功應對","examples":["He was later shown on television, fielding questions. 他後來在電視上露了面，答覆那些問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a sports team <b>fields</b> a particular number or type of players, the players are chosen to play for the team on a particular occasion. 使參賽","examples":["We're going to field an exciting and younger team. 我們將選派一支令人振奮的較年輕隊伍上場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a candidate in an election is representing a political party, you can say that the party <b>is fielding</b> that candidate. 使參加競選","examples":["There are signs that the new party aims to field candidates in elections scheduled for February next year. 有跡象表明，該新黨計劃為明年2月的選舉提名候選人。"]}]}]},"flashlight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手電筒（美國英語，英國英語通常用 torch）；閃光燈（攝影）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flashlight</b> is a small electric light which gets its power from batteries and which you can carry in your hand. 手電筒","examples":[]}]}]},"figure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"數字，數目，數值；數字符號，位數；身材，體型；（遠處的）人影；（重要的）人物；（繪畫或模型中）人像；（書中的）圖、表；（數學）圖形；價格，金額"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（以重要地位）出現；<美，非正式>認為，估計；理解，弄懂；計算；用圖畫（或圖形等）描繪，想象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>figure</b> is a particular amount expressed as a number, especially a statistic. 數字","examples":["It would be very nice if we had a true figure of how many people in this country haven't got a job. 要是我們有一個確切的數字反映這個國家到底有多少人沒有工作就好了。","It will not be long before the inflation figure starts to fall. 過不了多久，通貨膨脹的數字就會開始下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>figure</b> is any of the ten written symbols from 0 to 9 that are used to represent a number. 個位數字","examples":["...the glowing red figures on the radio alarm clock which read 4:22 a.m. …收音機鬧鐘上閃閃發光的紅色數字顯示凌晨4點22分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You refer to someone that you can see as a <b>figure</b> when you cannot see them clearly or when you are describing them. 身影","examples":["Ernie saw the dim figure of Rose in the chair. 厄尼看到了羅斯坐在椅子裡的模糊身影。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In art, a <b>figure</b> is a person in a drawing or a painting, or a statue of a person. 人像","examples":["...a life-size bronze figure of a brooding, hooded woman. …一個真人大小、戴著頭巾、正在沉思的女銅像。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>figure</b> is the shape of your body. 身材","examples":["Take pride in your health and your figure. 為你的健康和身材感到驕傲。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Someone who is referred to as a <b>figure</b> of a particular kind is a person who is well-known and important in some way. 重要人物","examples":["The movement is supported by key figures in the three main political parties. 這場運動由3個主要政黨的重要人物支援。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that someone is, for example, a mother <b>figure</b> or a hero <b>figure</b>, you mean that other people regard them as the type of person stated or suggested. 代表","examples":["Daniel Boone, the great hero figure of the frontier. 丹尼爾·布恩是偉大的前線英雄的代表。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"In books and magazines, the diagrams which help to show or explain information are referred to as <b>figures</b>. 圖表","examples":["If you look at a world map (see Figure 1) you can identify the major wine-producing regions. 如果你看看世界地圖（見圖1），你就能辨認出主要的葡萄酒生產地區。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"In geometry, a <b>figure</b> is a shape, especially a regular shape. 幾何圖形","examples":["Draw a pentagon, a regular five-sided figure. 畫一個五邊形，一個規則的五邊圖形。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"An amount or number that is in single <b>figures</b> is between zero and nine. An amount or number that is in double <b>figures</b> is between ten and ninety-nine. You can also say, for example, that an amount or number is in three <b>figures</b> when it is between one hundred and nine hundred and ninety-nine. 數字","examples":["Inflation, which has usually been in single figures, is running at more than 12%. 通貨膨脹率通常都是一位數字，正飆升至12%以上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>figure</b> that something is the case, you think or guess that it is the case. 想","examples":["She figured that both she and Ned had learned a lot from the experience. 她想她和內德都從這次經歷中學到了很多。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say \"<b>That figures</b>\" or \"<b>It figures</b>,\" you mean that the fact referred to is not surprising. 意料之中","examples":["When I finished, he said, \"Yeah. That figures.\" 我做完時，他說：“嗯，正如所料。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>figures</b> <b>in</b> something, they appear in or are included in it. 出現","examples":["Human rights violations figured prominently in the report. 侵犯人權出現在報告中的顯要位置。"]}]}]},"flag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旗幟；國旗；訊號旗，標誌旗；菖蒲，鳶尾；鋪路用的厚石板（多為矩形或正方形）；（在街上慈善捐贈後獲得的）小紙徽；（用作標誌的）旗狀裝置（或符號、圖畫）；計程車空車顯示器；特徵位；旗艦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……做標記；示意……停下來，揮手示停；（裁判向場內）丟旗判罰；疲乏，熱情衰減；引起對……的注意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flag</b> is a piece of cloth which can be attached to a pole and which is used as a sign, signal, or symbol of something, especially of a particular country. 旗幟","examples":["The Marines climbed to the roof of the embassy building to raise the American flag. 海軍陸戰隊士兵爬上使館大樓的樓頂去升美國國旗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Journalists sometimes refer to the <b>flag</b> of a particular country or organization as a way of referring to the country or organization itself and its values or power. 國家或組織 (新聞用語)","examples":["Every person who serves under the American flag will answer to his or her own superiors and to military law. 每一個在美軍服役的人都必須服從自己的上級和軍法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an indicator, that may be set or unset, used to indicate a condition or to stimulate a particular reaction in the execution of a computer program 指示器","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the conspicuously marked tail of a deer 鹿尾顯著標記","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"any of various plants that have long swordlike leaves, esp the iris <b>Iris pseudacorus</b> (<b>yellow flag</b>) 長有細長葉子的植物","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"flagstone的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flag</b> or if your spirits <b>flag</b>, you begin to lose enthusiasm or energy. (熱情、精力等) 衰退","examples":["His enthusiasm was in no way flagging. 他的熱情絲毫沒有減退。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to warn or signal (a vehicle) to stop 警示或指示(汽車)停下","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to mark (a page in a book, card, etc) for attention by attaching a small tab or flag (在書頁和卡片等)用標籤做記號","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to draw attention to (something) 引起注意(某物)","examples":[]}]}]},"flight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"航班，班機；飛行；逃走，逃避；（兩個樓層間的）一段樓梯；（一起飛行的）鳥群，機群；（貨幣或股票的）拋售，抽逃；<文>光陰的飛逝；（跑道）一組跨欄；（使運河水位逐級升高的）多級船閘；過分（或牽強）的想法（或描述）；鏢尾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（足球、板球等）將（球）準確吊傳；給（箭，鏢）裝羽毛（或箭翎）；射擊（飛行中的野禽）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flight</b> is a trip made by flying, usually in an aeroplane. 飛行","examples":["The flight will take four hours. 此次飛行將需要四個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an aeroplane carrying passengers on a particular trip as a particular <b>flight</b>. 航班","examples":["BA flight 286 was two hours late. 英國航空286次航班晚點兩個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>flight</b> <b>of</b> steps or stairs is a set of steps or stairs that lead from one level to another without changing direction. 一段 (臺階或樓梯)","examples":["We walked in silence up a flight of stairs and down a long corridor. 我們默默地走上一段樓梯，穿過一道長廊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Flight</b> is the action of flying, or the ability to fly. 飛行; 飛行能力","examples":["Supersonic flight could become a routine form of travel in the 21st century. 搭乘超音速飛機飛行會成為21世紀常見的旅行方式。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Flight</b> is the act of running away from a dangerous or unpleasant situation or place. 逃跑","examples":["The family was often in flight, hiding out in friends' houses. 這一家人經常逃來逃去，躲藏在朋友們的家裡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a feather or plastic attachment fitted to an arrow or dart to give it stability in flight 鏢尾","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a set of steps or stairs between one landing or floor and the next 一段(臺階或樓梯)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cause (a ball, dart, etc) to float slowly or deceptively towards its target 使(球，鏢等)慢慢移向目標","examples":[]}]}]},"flour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵粉，（穀物磨成的）粉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……上撒麵粉；<美>把（穀物）磨成粉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flour</b> is a white or brown powder that is made by grinding grain. It is used to make bread, cakes, and pastry. 麵粉","examples":[]}]}]},"flash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃光，閃亮；（快速）出示，顯示；飛馳，掠過；閃現；迅速播出，傳送（資訊）；突然顯露（強烈情感）；<非正式>當眾暴露（性器官）；<非正式>（為引人注目而）展示，炫耀；（尤指用無線電或光波）通訊，聯絡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃光；閃光燈；閃現；（軍裝上的）肩章；網站動畫程式；花哨，噱頭；突然理解，頓悟；（感情的）突發；<非正式>炫耀財富，誇富；（產品包裝上用來吸引顧客眼光的）色帶，突顯區域；（模塑過程中的）溢料，溢邊；（尤指為幫助行船而從堰閘裡放出的）水流；飛快的一瞥；（模塑過程中的）溢料，溢邊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"闊氣的，愛顯擺的；突然而短暫的；<美，非正式>非常有才能的，傑出的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flash</b> is a sudden burst of light or of something shiny or bright. 閃光","examples":["A sudden flash of lightning lit everything up for a second. 突然的一道閃電剎那間把一切照亮了。","The wire snapped at the wall plug with a blue flash. 隨著一道藍色的閃光，牆上插座處的電線啪地一聲斷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flash</b> is the use of special bulbs to give more light when taking a photograph. 閃光燈","examples":["He was one of the first people to use high speed flash in bird photography. 他是鳥類攝影中最先使用高速閃光燈的人之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>flash</b> is the same as a . 手電筒","examples":["Stopping to rest, Pete shut off the flash. 停下來休息的時候，皮特關掉了手電筒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a light <b>flashes</b> or if you <b>flash</b> a light, it shines with a sudden bright light, especially as quick, regular flashes of light. 閃光","examples":["Lightning flashed among the distant dark clouds. 遠處的烏雲中電光閃閃。","He lost his temper after a driver flashed her headlights as he overtook. 他因為在超車時一個女司機閃車頭燈而大為光火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>flash</b> something such as an identification card, you show it to people quickly and then put it away again. 快速亮一下 (證件等)","examples":["Halim flashed his official card, and managed to get hold of a soldier to guard the Land Rover. 哈利姆亮了他的證件，並設法找來一名士兵守衛那輛路虎越野車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a picture or message <b>flashes</b> <b>up on</b> a screen, or if you <b>flash</b> it <b>onto</b> a screen, it is displayed there briefly or suddenly, and often repeatedly. 使閃現; 閃現","examples":["The figures flash up on the scoreboard. 數字閃現在記分牌上。","The words \"Good Luck\" were flashing on the screen. “祝你好運”的字樣正在螢幕上閃現。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>flash</b> a look or a smile at someone, you suddenly look at them or smile at them. 突然投去 (一瞥或一笑)","examples":["I flashed a look at Sue. 我突然瞥了休一眼。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>flashes</b> past or by, it moves past you so fast that you cannot see it properly. 飛馳","examples":["It was a busy road, cars flashed by every few minutes. 這是條繁忙的公路，每隔幾分鐘就有一些汽車飛馳而過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>flashes through</b> or <b>into</b> your mind, you suddenly think about it. 閃現","examples":["A ludicrous thought flashed through Harry's mind. 一個可笑的想法在哈里的腦子裡閃過。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>in a flash</b>, you mean that it happens suddenly and lasts only a very short time. 轉瞬間","examples":["The answer had come to him in a flash. 他一下子就有了答案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone reacts to something <b>quick as a flash</b>, you mean that they react to it extremely quickly. 反應神速地","examples":["Quick as a flash, the man said, \"I have to, don't I?\" 那人反應神速地說：“我不得不這麼做，是不是？”"]}]}]},"flu":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流行性感冒，流感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flu</b> is an illness which is similar to a bad cold but more serious. It often makes you feel very weak and makes your muscles hurt. 流感","examples":["I got the flu. 我得了流感。"]}]}]},"flute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長笛；細長酒杯，高腳玻璃酒杯；長笛音栓；（柱上的）凹槽；（裙子等衣物的）褶子，圓凹褶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>吹笛子（或管樂器）；用長笛般優美的聲音說話；製作凹槽；給（衣服）加褶邊，加荷葉邊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flute</b> is a musical instrument of the woodwind family. You play it by blowing over a hole near one end while holding it sideways to your mouth. 長笛","examples":[]}]}]},"fit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"適合，合身；適應，合得來；可容納，裝進；試穿（衣服）；和……相稱，符合；為放置（於……）而設計；安置，安裝（在某處）；安排時間會面，安排時間做（某事）；（疾病）發作"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"健康的，健壯的；合適的，適當的；合格的，勝任的；<俚>性感的；<非正式>快要，就要"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"適合，合身；匹配，相配；痙攣，昏厥；一陣，突發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>fits</b>, it is the right size and shape to go onto a person's body or onto a particular object. 合身; 合適","examples":["The sash, kimono, and other garments were made to fit a child. 這些腰帶、和服和其他衣服都做得適合孩子穿。","She has to go to the men's department to find trousers that fit at the waist. 她得去男裝部找腰圍合適的褲子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are fitted for</b> a particular piece of clothing, you try it on so that the person who is making it can see where it needs to be altered. 試穿","examples":["She was being fitted for her wedding dress. 她正在試穿她的結婚禮服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fit</b> something into a particular space or place, you put it there. 放置","examples":["...she fitted her key in the lock. …她把鑰匙插進鎖孔。","Who could cut the millions of stone blocks and fit them together? 誰能切割這數百萬的石塊並將它們壘在一起呢？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>fit</b> something somewhere, you attach it there, or put it there carefully and securely. 安裝; 小心放置","examples":["Fit hinge bolts to give extra support to the door lock. 裝上鉸鏈螺栓，使門鎖更牢固。","Peter had built the overhead ladders, and the next day he fitted them to the wall. 彼得已經造好了懸掛梯，第二天他就把它們裝在了牆上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>fits</b> something else or <b>fits</b> into it, it goes together well with that thing or is able to be part of it. 相配; 符合","examples":["Her daughter doesn't fit the current feminine ideal. 她女兒不符合當今女性觀念。","Fostering is a full-time job and you should carefully consider how it will fit into your career. 收養孩子是一份全職工作，你應該仔細考慮如何把它跟你的事業協調起來。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can say that something <b>fits</b> a particular person or thing when it is appropriate or suitable for them or it. 適合","examples":["The punishment must always fit the crime. 刑罰必須總是量罪而定。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>fits</b> someone for a particular task or role, it makes them good enough or suitable for it. 使勝任 (任務、角色)","examples":["...a man whose past experience fits him for the top job in education. …其過去的經歷使之勝任教育界最高職位的一名男子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>fits</b> somewhere, it can be put there or is designed to be put there. 合適於 (某地)","examples":["...a pocket computer which is small enough to fit into your pocket. …一臺小得足以放進你口袋裡的袖珍電腦。","He folded his long legs to fit under the table. 他把腿彎起來伸到桌下。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is a good <b>fit</b>, it fits well. 適合","examples":["Eventually he was happy that the sills and doors were a reasonably good fit. 最後他高興了，窗臺和門配得相當合適。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"勝任","examples":["There is a debate about his fitness for the highest office. 關於他擔任最高職務的勝任與否發生了一場爭論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"健康","examples":["Squash was once thought to offer all-round fitness. 壁球曾一度被認為可以提供全面的健康。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>fit of</b> coughing or laughter, you suddenly start coughing or laughing in an uncontrollable way. 一陣 (咳嗽、大笑)","examples":["Halfway down the cigarette she had a fit of coughing. 煙抽到一半時，她一陣咳嗽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something in a <b>fit of</b> anger or panic, you are very angry or afraid when you do it. 一陣 (憤怒、恐慌等)","examples":["Pattie shot Tom in a fit of jealous rage. 帕蒂在一陣嫉恨中開槍打了湯姆。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone has a <b>fit</b> they suddenly lose consciousness and their body makes uncontrollable movements. 昏厥; 痙攣","examples":["About two in every five epileptic fits occur during sleep. 每五例癲癇昏厥中，約有兩例是在睡眠中發作的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>has</b> a <b>fit</b> or <b>throws</b> a <b>fit</b>, they suddenly become very agitated because they are angry or worried about something. 大發脾氣; 狂躁不安","examples":["When my landlady said she wanted to keep $380 of my deposit to paint the walls, I threw a fit. 當女房東說她要用我的$380押金來粉刷牆壁時，我大發脾氣。","\"Cathy will have a fit when she finds out you bought all that fishing gear,\" Harrington said. “凱茜發現你買了那整套漁具一定會發火的。”哈林頓說。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>fit</b> for a particular purpose, it is suitable for that purpose. 適合的","examples":["Of the seven bicycles we had, only two were fit for the road. 我們的七輛腳踏車中，只有兩輛適合這種路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>fit</b> to do something, they have the appropriate qualities or skills that will allow them to do it. 勝任的","examples":["You're not fit to be a mother! 你不適合做母親！","In a word, this government isn't fit to rule. 總之，這屆政府不勝任執政之事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>fit</b> is healthy and physically strong. 健康的; 強健的","examples":["An averagely fit person can master easy ski runs within a few days. 中等健康的人幾天內就能駕馭初級的滑雪道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(of a person) sexually attractive (人)性感誘人的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>sees fit</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they are entitled to do it, but that you disapprove of their decision to do it. 執意","examples":["He's not a friend, you say, yet you saw fit to lend him money. 你說他不是你的朋友，你卻執意借錢給他。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to have a sudden attack or convulsion, such as an epileptic seizure 突發驚厥","examples":[]}]}]},"flood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）淹沒；氾濫；大量湧來，大量湧去；（感覺或回憶）湧上心頭；（光線）傾瀉，照亮；（使）溢流；（產後等）子宮出血過多，月經過多"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"洪水，水災；大批，大量（的人或事物）；<文>（海洋、江河等）大水體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>flood</b>, a large amount of water covers an area which is usually dry, for example, when a river flows over its banks or a pipe bursts. 洪水","examples":["More than 70 people were killed in the floods, caused when a dam burst. 大壩決堤引發的洪水災吞噬了七十多人的生命。","This is the type of flood dreaded by cavers. 這正是探察洞穴者懼怕的那種洪水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a <b>flood</b> <b>of</b> people or things arrive somewhere, you are emphasizing that a very large number of them arrive there. 一大批","examples":["The administration is trying to stem the flood of refugees out of Haiti and into Florida. 政府正設法阻止大批逃離海地的難民湧入佛羅里達。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a river or a burst pipe <b>floods</b> an area that is usually dry or if the area <b>floods</b>, it becomes covered with water. 為水所淹; 淹沒","examples":["The kitchen flooded. 廚房被水淹了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>flood</b> a place <b>with</b> a particular type of thing, or if a particular type of thing <b>floods</b> a place, the place becomes full of so many of them that it cannot hold or deal with any more. 使充滿; 充斥","examples":["Manufacturers are destroying American jobs by flooding the market with cheap imports. 製造商們在以廉價進口貨充斥市場，破壞了美國人的就業機會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a river <b>floods</b>, it overflows, especially after very heavy rain. 氾濫","examples":["...the relentless rain that caused twenty rivers to flood. …導致20條河流泛濫的那場持續不斷的雨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that people or things <b>flood</b> into a place, you are emphasizing that they arrive there in large numbers. 湧入","examples":["Large numbers of immigrants flooded into the area. 大批移民湧入了這個地區。","Inquiries flooded in from all over the world. 問詢從世界各地如潮水般湧來。"]}]}]},"following":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"之後的，接下來的；下列的，以下的；順風的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"追隨者，擁護者"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……之後，緊接著"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跟隨；沿行；（時間、順序）排在……之後（follow 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Following</b> a particular event means after that event. 在…之後","examples":["In the centuries following Christ's death, Christians genuinely believed the world was about to end. 在耶穌死後的幾個世紀裡，基督徒們真地認為世界將要消亡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>following</b> day, week, or year is the day, week, or year after the one you have just mentioned. 其後的 (日、月、年等)","examples":["The following day the picture appeared on the front pages of every newspaper in the world. 次日，照片出現在世界各地報紙的頭版。","We went to dinner the following Monday evening. 在接下來的那個週一晚上我們一起共進晚餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>following</b> to refer to something that you are about to mention. 以下的","examples":["Write down the following information: name of product, type, date purchased and price. 寫下以下資訊：產品名稱、型號、購買日期和價格。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The following</b> refers to the thing or things that you are about to mention. 以下的事或物","examples":["The following is a paraphrase of what was said. 以下是對所說內容的解釋。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or organization that has a <b>following</b> has a group of people who support or admire their beliefs or actions. 支持者","examples":["Australian rugby league enjoys a huge following in New Zealand. 澳大利亞橄欖球隊在紐西蘭有一大批支持者。"]}]}]},"flow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"流動，流淌；（人，物）湧向，湧進；（車輛）暢通無阻；持續抵達，持續供應；（資訊）傳播，（資金）流通；飄垂，飄拂；強烈感到；（說話或思想）流暢；引發，來自；充滿，滿是；暢飲；漲潮；永久性變形；<非正式>來月經"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"流，流動；持續生產，不斷供應；車流，人流；（語言、思路等的）連貫；流速，流率；流動物；流量；漲潮；<蘇格蘭>溼地，沼澤；形變；<非正式>月經；大量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid, gas, or electrical current <b>flows</b> somewhere, it moves there steadily and continuously. 流動","examples":["A stream flowed gently down into the valley. 一條小溪緩緩地流進山谷。","The current flows into electric motors that drive the wheels. 電流流進電機，驅動輪子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a number of people or things <b>flow</b> from one place to another, they move there steadily in large groups, usually without stopping. (大量人或物) 流動","examples":["Large numbers of refugees continue to flow from the troubled region into the no-man's land. 大批的難民持續從騷亂地區湧進無人區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If information or money <b>flows</b> somewhere, it moves freely between people or organizations. (資訊) 傳播; (資金) 流通","examples":["A lot of this information flowed through other police departments. 該資訊大批地傳到了其他警務部門。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flow</b> is also a noun. 流動","examples":["It works only in the veins, where the blood flow is slower. 它只在血液流動較緩的靜脈中起作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flow</b> is also a noun. 流動","examples":["She watched the frantic flow of cars and buses along the street. 她注視著街道上川流不息的小車和巴士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Flow</b> is also a noun. 傳播; 流通","examples":["...the opportunity to control the flow of information. …控制資訊傳播的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that an activity, or the person who is performing the activity, is <b>in full flow</b>, you mean that the activity has started and is being carried out with a great deal of energy and enthusiasm. 熱火朝天的","examples":["Lunch at Harry's Bar was in full flow when Irene made a splendid entrance. 艾琳光彩奪目地進門時，哈里酒吧的午餐已進行得熱火朝天了。"]}]}]},"fix":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修理，維修；確定（時間、地點、價格等）；安排，組織；處理，解決（問題等）；固定，安裝；使（目光、注意力或思想）集中於；牢記，銘記；把（槍、相機、雷達）瞄準；操縱，作弊；梳洗，整理；整容，矯正（牙齒）；提供，準備（飲食等）；<非正式>懲罰，收拾；固著（顏色），定（影）；<美>閹割（動物）；<非正式>介紹物件；<俚>注射毒品"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"解決方案（或措施）；窘境，困境；（毒品或致癮物的）一次用量；方位確定，定位；理解，瞭解；受操縱的事，勾當"}],"sections":[]},"flat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平的，水平的；平坦的；（水面）平靜的，波瀾不興的；平滑的；平放的，平躺的，平臥的；足弓平坦的；扁平的；（鞋）平跟的，低跟的；斷然的，直截了當的；（費率、價格等）統一的，固定的；（市場、價格等）疲軟的，蕭條的；枯燥的，無趣的，缺乏熱情的；（飲品）走了氣的；（輪胎）沒氣的，癟的；（電池）電力不足的，沒電的；平淡的，無變化的；（音符）降半音的；音調偏低的；色彩單調的，無反差的，無景深的；無光澤的；（圖表上的線）平的，無變化的；（組織或系統）內部層次不多的；（關於）無障礙平地賽馬的；（麵包）未發酵的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"水平地；平整地；平貼著；正好；完全地，徹底地；音調偏低地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>公寓，單元房；（通常指近水的）淺灘，窪地；（某物的）平面部份；（音符的）降半音；降半音符號；<美>淺箱，淺苗床；平底鞋，低跟鞋（flats）；漏氣輪胎；平板列車，敞車，平臺貨車；平面佈景，佈景屏；無障礙平地賽馬季節（the Flat）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"住公寓，夥住公寓；<美>（樂）把（音調）降半音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>flat</b> is level, smooth, or even, rather than sloping, curved, or uneven. 平的","examples":["Tiles can be fixed to any surface as long as it's flat, firm and dry. 瓷磚可以固定在任何表面上，只要這些表面是平整、堅固、乾燥的。","...windows which a thief can reach from a drainpipe or flat roof. …小偷從排水管或平屋頂可以夠得到的窗戶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flat</b> means horizontal and not upright. 水平的","examples":["Two men near him threw themselves flat. 他旁邊的兩個人一下子平趴在了地上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> object is not very tall or deep in relation to its length and width. 扁平的","examples":["Ellen is walking down the drive with a square flat box balanced on one hand. 埃倫正沿著車道走著，一隻手上託著一個扁平的方盒子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Flat</b> land is level, with no high hills or other raised parts. (地勢) 平坦的","examples":["To the north lie the flat and fertile farmlands of Nebraska. 北面是內布拉斯加州平坦肥沃的農田。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Flat</b> shoes have no heels or very low heels. 平底的","examples":["People wear slacks, sweaters, flat shoes, and all manner of casual attire for travel. 人們旅行時穿寬鬆長褲、運動衫、平底鞋和各式休閒服裝。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> tyre, ball, or balloon does not have enough air in it. 癟的","examples":["One vehicle with a flat tyre can bring the motorway to a standstill. 一輛輪胎癟掉的汽車就能導致公路交通的停頓。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you have <b>flat</b> feet, the arches of your feet are too low. 平足的","examples":["The condition of flat feet runs in families. 平足會在家族中遺傳。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A drink that is <b>flat</b> has lost its fizz. (飲料) 走了汽的","examples":["Could this really stop the champagne from going flat? 這真的能使香檳酒不走汽了嗎？"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> battery has lost some or all of its electrical charge. (電池) 電力不足的; (電池) 電力耗盡的","examples":[]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you say that something happened, for example, in ten seconds <b>flat</b> or ten minutes <b>flat</b>, you are emphasizing that it happened surprisingly quickly and only took ten seconds or ten minutes. 僅僅","examples":["You're sitting behind an engine that'll move you from 0 to 60mph in six seconds flat. 你現在坐的這輛車的引擎只需6秒鐘就能從0加速到每小時60英里。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> rate, price, or percentage is one that is fixed and which applies in every situation. (費率、價格或百分比) 固定的","examples":["Fees are charged at a flat rate, rather than on a percentage basis. 費用按固定的費率收取，不是按百分比。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If trade or business is <b>flat</b>, it is slow and inactive, rather than busy and improving or increasing. (貿易或商業) 不景氣的","examples":["During the first eight months of this year, sales of big pickups were up 14% while car sales stayed flat. 今年的頭8個月，大貨車的銷售量增長了14%，而轎車的銷售仍不景氣。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"<b>Flat</b> is used after a letter representing a musical note to show that the note should be played or sung half a tone lower than the note which otherwise matches that letter. <b>Flat</b> is often represented by the symbol♭after the letter. (用在表示音符的字母后) 降半音的","examples":["...Schubert's B flat Piano Trio (Opus 99). …舒伯特的降B調鋼琴三重奏（作品第99號）。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"<b>Flat</b> is also an adjective. (演唱或樂器) 比標準音低的","examples":["He had been fired because his singing was flat. 他因為唱音偏低已被解僱。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> denial or refusal is definite and firm, and is unlikely to be changed. (否認或拒絕) 斷然的","examples":["The Foreign Ministry has issued a flat denial of any involvement. 外交部已斷然否認與此有任何牽連。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>flat</b>, you mean that it is dull and not exciting or interesting. 平淡無趣的","examples":["The past few days have seemed comparatively flat and empty. 過去的幾天似乎比較平淡和無聊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fall flat</b> on your face, you fall over. 臉朝下摔倒","examples":["A man walked in off the street and fell flat on his face, unconscious. 一個男人從街上走進來，臉朝下摔倒在地上，昏了過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or attempt <b>falls flat</b> or <b>falls flat on</b> its <b>face</b>, it is unsuccessful. 失敗","examples":["Liz meant it as a joke but it fell flat. 莉茲的本意是把它當作笑話來講的，但沒成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>flat out</b>, you do it as fast or as hard as you can. 竭盡全力地; 全速地","examples":["Everyone is working flat out to try to trap those responsible. 每個人都在竭盡全力地工作，試圖捉住那些應負責任的人。","...a flat-out sprint. …一次全速衝刺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>flat out</b> to emphasize that something is completely the case. 徹底的","examples":["That allegation is a flat-out lie. 那一個指控是徹底的謊言。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flats</b> are flat shoes. 平底鞋","examples":["His mother looked ten years younger in jeans and flats. 他的母親穿著牛仔褲和平底鞋，看上去年輕了10歲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to one of the broad flat surfaces of an object as <b>the flat of</b> that object. 平面","examples":["He slammed the counter with the flat of his hand. 他用手掌猛擊櫃檯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> is a tyre that does not have enough air in it. 癟胎","examples":["Then, after I finally got back on the motorway, I developed a flat. 後來，等我終於回到公路上時，我有一個輪胎癟了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A low flat area of uncultivated land, especially an area where the ground is soft and wet, can be referred to as <b>flats</b> or a <b>flat</b>. 低窪沼澤地","examples":["The salt marshes and mud flats attract large numbers of waterfowl. 鹽鹼地和淤泥灘吸引來大量水鳥。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>flat</b> is a set of rooms for living in, usually on one floor and part of a larger building. A flat usually includes a kitchen and bathroom. 公寓套房","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone sings <b>flat</b> or if a musical instrument is <b>flat</b>, their singing or the instrument is slightly lower in pitch than it should be. (演唱或樂器) 比標準音低地","examples":["She had a tendency to sing flat. 她的唱音傾向於偏低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"斷然地","examples":["He flatly refused to discuss it. 他斷然拒絕討論此事。"]}]}]},"foreigner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外國人；外來人，外地人；<英，非正式>私活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>foreigner</b> is someone who belongs to a country that is not your own. 外國人","examples":["They are discouraged from becoming close friends with foreigners. 他們被勸不要同外國人成為密友。"]}]}]},"football":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"足球運動；橄欖球運動；足球，橄欖球；屢起爭議的課題，被踢來踢去的難題；（尤指別具一格的）足球風格，踢法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Football</b> is a game played by two teams of eleven players using a round ball. Players kick the ball to each other and try to score goals by kicking the ball into a large net. 足球運動","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>American football</b> is a game played by two teams of eleven players using an oval ball. Players carry the ball in their hands or throw it to each other as they try to score goals that are called touchdowns. 橄欖球運動","examples":["Two blocks beyond our school was a field where boys played football. 離我們學校兩個街區遠，有一個男孩子們玩橄欖球的場地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>football</b> is a ball that is used for playing football. 橄欖球","examples":["...a heavy leather football. …一個沉甸甸的皮質橄欖球。"]}]}]},"focus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重點，中心點；關注，注意；震源；目的，意圖；焦距；病灶；調焦裝置；目的明確，專注；（橢圓、拋物線等曲線的）焦點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"集中，關注；聚焦，調焦；<語言學>以（句子的一部分）為焦點（或重心）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>focus</b> <b>on</b> a particular topic or if your attention <b>is focused</b> <b>on</b> it, you concentrate on it and think about it, discuss it, or deal with it, rather than dealing with other topics. 關注","examples":["The research effort has focused on tracing the effects of growing levels of five compounds. 研究集中跟蹤5種化合物水平上升帶來的影響。","Today he was able to focus his message exclusively on the economy. 今天他能夠將重點聚焦在經濟方面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>focus</b> your eyes or if your eyes <b>focus</b>, your eyes adjust so that you can clearly see the thing that you want to look at. If you <b>focus</b> a camera, telescope, or other instrument, you adjust it so that you can see clearly through it. 使 (眼睛、相機、望遠鏡或其它儀器) 對焦; 聚焦","examples":["Kelly couldn't focus his eyes well enough to tell if the figure was male or female. 凱利無法看清那個人影是男的還是女的。","His eyes slowly began to focus on what looked like a small dark ball. 他的眼睛開始慢慢聚焦到那個小黑球似的東西上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>focus</b> rays of light on a particular point, you pass them through a lens or reflect them from a mirror so that they meet at that point. 把 (光線) 聚焦","examples":["Magnetic coils focus the electron beams into fine spots. 磁線圈將電子束聚焦成細小的點。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>focus</b> of something is the main topic or main thing that it is concerned with. 焦點","examples":["The UN's role in promoting peace is increasingly the focus of international attention. 聯合國在促進和平方面的作用越來越成為國際關注的焦點。","The new system is the focus of controversy. 新系統是爭議的焦點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>focus</b> on something is the special attention that you pay it. 關注","examples":["He said his sudden focus on foreign policy was not motivated by presidential politics. 他說他突然關注外交政策並不是受總統政治的驅使。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something has a <b>focus</b>, you mean that you can see a purpose in it. 訴求點","examples":["Somehow, though, their latest CD has a focus that the others have lacked. 但是，不管怎麼說，他們的最新鐳射唱片具備別人沒有的訴求點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>focus</b> to refer to the fact of adjusting your eyes or a camera, telescope, or other instrument, and to the degree to which you can see clearly. 焦點; 對焦","examples":["His focus switched to the little white ball. 他的焦點轉移到了那個小白球上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an image or a camera, telescope, or other instrument is <b>in focus</b>, the edges of what you see are clear and sharp. (影象) 清晰; (相機、望遠鏡或其他儀器) 對準焦點","examples":["Pictures should be in focus, with realistic colours and well composed groups. 照片應該成像清晰，色彩逼真，構圖合理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>in focus</b>, it is being discussed or its purpose and nature are clear. 受關注","examples":["We want to keep the real issues in focus. 我們要讓真正的問題受到關注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an image or a camera, telescope, or other instrument is <b>out of focus</b>, the edges of what you see are unclear. (影象) 模糊; (相機、望遠鏡或其他儀器) 對焦不準","examples":["In some of the pictures the subjects are out of focus while the background is sharp. 在一些照片中，主體對焦不準，背景反而很清晰。"]}]}]},"freezer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰箱，冰櫃，冷凍櫃；冰箱冷凍室；冷凍庫；製冷工（罕用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>freezer</b> is a large container like a refrigerator in which the temperature is kept below freezing point so that you can store food inside it for long periods. 冷櫃","examples":[]}]}]},"fridge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fridge</b> is the same as a . 冰箱","examples":[]}]}]},"fool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傻瓜，笨蛋；<美，非正式>（對某物）有癖好的人，……迷；（舊時宮廷裡的）弄臣，小丑；<英>奶油果子泥； 傻瓜，笨蛋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開玩笑，戲謔；愚弄，欺騙；瞎弄，瞎折騰（fool with）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<美，非正式>愚蠢的，傻的；愚蠢的，傻的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>fool</b>, you are indicating that you think they are not at all sensible and show a lack of good judgment. 笨蛋","examples":["\"You fool!\" she shouted. “你這個笨蛋！”她叫道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(formerly) a professional jester living in a royal or noble household (舊時)弄臣","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a dessert made from a purée of fruit with cream or custard 奶油果泥","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fool</b> is used to describe an action or person that is not at all sensible and shows a lack of good judgment. 愚蠢的","examples":["What a damn fool thing to do! 這樣做真是愚蠢得要死！"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>fools</b> you, they deceive or trick you. 欺騙; 愚弄","examples":["Art dealers fool a lot of people. 藝術品經銷商會愚弄許多人。","Don't be fooled by his appearance. 不要被他的外表所矇蔽。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person <b>is fooling with</b> something or someone, you mean that the way they are behaving is likely to cause problems. 瞎弄","examples":["What are you doing fooling with such a staggering sum of money? 你拿這麼驚人的一大筆錢瞎折騰什麼？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make a fool of</b> someone, you make them seem silly by telling people about something stupid that they have done, or by tricking them. 戲弄 (某人)","examples":["Your brother is making a fool of you. 你哥哥在戲弄你呢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make a fool of</b> yourself, you behave in a way that makes other people think that you are silly or lacking in good judgment. 讓 (自己) 出醜","examples":["He was drinking and making a fool of himself. 他喝酒的時候洋相百出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>play the fool</b> or <b>act the fool</b>, you behave in a playful, childish, and foolish way, usually in order to make other people laugh. 胡鬧逗樂","examples":["They used to play the fool together, calling each other silly names and giggling. 他們過去常常一起胡鬧，互相起綽號取笑。"]}]}]},"fox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狐狸；狐裘；狡猾的人；<非正式> 妖精，性感的人；福克斯族，福克斯族語；<非正式>妖精，性感的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"欺騙，耍弄；把……難住，使……猜不透"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fox</b> is a wild animal which looks like a dog and has reddish-brown fur, a pointed face and ears, and a thick tail. Foxes eat smaller animals. 狐狸","examples":[]}]}]},"fright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚駭，恐怖，驚嚇；恐怖的經歷；<舊>不整潔的人，奇怪、醜陋的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>使驚恐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fright</b> is a sudden feeling of fear, especially the fear that you feel when something unpleasant surprises you. 驚嚇","examples":["The steam pipes rattled suddenly, and Franklin jumped with fright. 蒸汽管突然發出咯咯的聲音，弗蘭克林嚇得跳了起來。","The birds smashed into the top of their cages in fright. 鳥兒們嚇得猛撞籠頂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>fright</b> is an experience which makes you suddenly afraid. 驚嚇","examples":["The snake picked up its head and stuck out its tongue which gave everyone a fright. 那條蛇昂起頭，吐出信子，把每個人都嚇了一大跳。"]}]}]},"freedom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自由權，自主權；（狀態）自由，自主；行動自由（指不在獄中）；擺脫，免受；自由使用權；<英>榮譽市民稱號；<古>（講話，行為）過分親密，放肆；直率，坦率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Freedom</b> is the state of being allowed to do what you want to do. <b>Freedoms</b> are instances of this. 自由","examples":["...freedom of speech. …言論自由。","The United Nations Secretary-General has spoken of the need for individual freedoms and human rights. 聯合國秘書長談到了個人自由和人權的必要性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When prisoners or slaves are set free or escape, they gain their <b>freedom</b>. 人身自由","examples":["...the agreement worked out by the UN, under which all hostages and detainees would gain their freedom. …聯合國制定的協議，據此所有人質和被扣押者應獲得自由。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Freedom from</b> something you do not want means not being affected by it. 免除","examples":["...all the freedom from pain that medicine could provide. …藥物所能免除的所有痛苦。"]}]}]},"function":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"功能，職責；宴會，典禮；函式，應變數；由其他事情造成的結果；子例行程式，子例程；官能團，功能團"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"工作，運轉；行使職責，發揮功能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>function</b> of something or someone is the useful thing that they do or are intended to do. 作用","examples":["The main function of the investment banks is to raise capital for industry. 各投資銀行的主要作用是為產業籌集資金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>function</b> is a large formal dinner or party. 宴會; 社交聚會","examples":["...a private function hosted by one of his students. …由他的一個學生做東的一場私人宴會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a machine or system <b>is functioning</b>, it is working or operating. 運轉","examples":["The authorities say the prison is now functioning normally. 當局稱該監獄現在在正常運轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>functions</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing, they do the work or fulfil the purpose of that thing. (作為某物) 起作用","examples":["On weekdays, one third of the room functions as workspace. 在工作日，這個房間的三分之一充當工作場所。"]}]}]},"gardener":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"園丁，花匠；園藝愛好者；園藝家；（Gardener）英語姓氏，加德納"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gardener</b> is a person who is paid to work in someone else's garden. 園丁","examples":["She employed a gardener. 她僱了一個園丁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gardener</b> is someone who enjoys working in their own garden growing flowers or vegetables. 園藝愛好者","examples":["The majority of sweet peas are still bred by enthusiastic amateur gardeners. 大部分甜豌豆仍然是由熱衷園藝的業餘愛好者培育的。"]}]}]},"forward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向前；在船頭，朝飛機頭部；按順序地；有進展地，前進地；向將來，往後；提前；（鐘錶）往前（撥）；從……起，自……以來"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"向前的，前進的；在前部的，位於前面的；（電子）正向的；未來的，將來的；期貨的，預先的；早的，早熟的；魯莽的，冒失的；熱心的，動輒就……的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（足球、籃球等運動的）前鋒；（尤指金融市場）遠期協議，遠期交易"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"轉交，轉寄；寄，傳送；促進，推進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move or look <b>forward</b>, you move or look in a direction that is in front of you. 向前 (移動、看)","examples":["He came forward with his hand out. \"Mr. and Mrs. Selby?\" he said. 他伸著手走上前來，“塞爾比先生和夫人吧？”他說。","She fell forward on to her face. 她臉著地向前摔倒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Forward</b> means in a position near the front of something such as a building or a vehicle. 靠前地","examples":["The best seats are in the aisle and as far forward as possible. 最好的座位在過道處儘可能靠前的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone looks <b>forward</b>, you approve of them because they think about what will happen in the future and plan for it. (看) 向前地","examples":["Now the leadership wants to look forward, and to outline a strategy for the rest of the century. 現在領導層想要向前看，為本世紀餘下的時間勾畫一個戰略框架。","People should forget and look forward. 人們應當忘記過去向前看。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you move a clock or watch <b>forward</b>, you change the time shown on it so that it shows a later time, for example, when the time changes to daylight saving time. (撥鐘錶) 向前地","examples":["When we put the clocks forward in March we go into daylight saving time. 當我們在3月份把鍾向前撥以後，我們就進入了夏令時。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you are referring to a particular time, if you say that something was true <b>from</b> that time <b>forward</b>, you mean that it became true at that time, and continued to be true afterward. (從某時刻) 起","examples":["Velzquez's work from that time forward was confined largely to portraits of the royal family. 從那以後，委拉斯開茲的作品就很大程度上僅限於王室的肖像畫了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>forward</b> to indicate that something progresses or improves. 向前 (進展、進步)","examples":["And by boosting economic prosperity in Mexico, Canada and the United States, it will help us move forward on issues that concern all of us. 而且透過推動墨西哥、加拿大和美國的經濟繁榮，它將會幫助我們在解決與我們大家有關的問題上取得進展。","They just couldn't see any way forward. 他們就是看不到任何前進之路。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something or someone is put <b>forward</b>, or comes <b>forward</b>, they are suggested or offered as suitable for a particular purpose. (呈、走) 上前; (提) 出來","examples":["Over the years several similar theories have been put forward. 多年來幾種類似理論被提了出來。","Investigations have ground to a standstill because no witnesses have come forward. 調查已陷入一種停滯狀態，因為沒有證人出來作證。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Forward</b> is also an adjective. 靠前的","examples":["Reinforcements were needed to allow more troops to move to forward positions. 需要增援以便讓更多的部隊推進至前沿陣地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Forward</b> is also an adjective. 向前的","examples":["The university system requires more forward planning. 大學體制要求更具前瞻性的規劃。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a letter or message <b>is forwarded</b> <b>to</b> someone, it is sent to the place where they are, after having been sent to a different place earlier. 轉發","examples":["When he's out on the road, office calls are forwarded to the cellular phone in his truck. 當他外出在路上時，打到辦公室的電話便被轉到他卡車中的行動電話上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In basketball, football, or hockey, a <b>forward</b> is a player whose usual position is in the opponents' half of the field, and whose usual job is to attack or score goals. (籃球、足球、曲棍球等運動的) 前鋒","examples":["Junior forward Sam McCracken added 14 points for the home team. 前鋒小薩姆·麥克拉肯為主隊添了14分。"]}]}]},"garage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"車庫；加油站，汽車修理廠；車庫音樂"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……送入車庫（或修車廠）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>garage</b> is a building in which you keep a car. A garage is often built next to or as part of a house. 車庫","examples":["They have turned the garage into a study. 他們把車庫改建成了書房。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>garage</b> is a place where you can get your car repaired. 汽車修理廠","examples":["Nancy took her car to a local garage for a check-up. 南希把她的車開到一家當地的汽車修理廠檢查。"]}]}]},"future":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"未來，將來；前途，前景；期貨；（動詞的）將來時態"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"將來的，未來的；（動詞）將來時態的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The future</b> is the period of time that will come after the present, or the things that will happen then. 將來","examples":["The spokesman said no decision on the proposal was likely in the immediate future. 該發言人稱近期不太可能有有關該提案的決議。","He was making plans for the future. 他正在為將來制定計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>future</b>, or <b>the</b> <b>future</b> <b>of</b> something, is what will happen to them or what they will do after the present time. (某人、某事物的) 未來","examples":["His future depends on the outcome of the elections. 他的未來取決於該選舉的結果。","...a proposed national conference on the country's political future. …一次擬議的有關該國政治未來的全國會議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people trade in <b>futures</b>, they buy stocks and shares, commodities such as coffee or oil, or foreign currency at a price that is agreed at the time of purchase for items which are delivered some time in the future. 期貨","examples":["This report could spur some buying in corn futures when the market opens today. 這份報告會在今天開市時刺激玉米期貨的一些購買行為。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Future</b> things will happen or exist after the present time. 未來的","examples":["She said if the world did not act conclusively now, it would only bequeath the problem to future generations. 她說如果這個世界現在不採取正確的行動，那隻會把問題遺留給後代。","...the future king and queen. …未來的國王和王后。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in the future</b> when saying what will happen from now on, which will be different from what has previously happened. 在將來","examples":["I asked her to be more careful in the future. 我叫她將來更仔細一些。"]}]}]},"form":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）出現；（使）（關係、習慣或想法）形成；構成，是……的組成部分；陶冶，培養；組織，建立"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"表，表格；類別，種類；形狀，外形；體形；（存在的）形態，形式；（尤指藝術作品或文章的）結構；體能，良好的健康狀態；良好表現；詞形；慣常做法，習俗；（英國的）班級，年級；不禮貌的行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>form</b> <b>of</b> something is a type or kind of it. 種類","examples":["He contracted a rare form of cancer. 他患上了一種罕見的癌症。","I am against hunting in any form. 我反對任何形式的狩獵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something can exist or happen in several possible ways, you can use <b>form</b> to refer to one particular way in which it exists or happens. 方式","examples":["They received a benefit in the form of a tax reduction. 他們以減稅的方式獲得了收益。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>form</b> of something is its shape. 形狀","examples":["...the form of the body. …體型。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to something that you can see as a <b>form</b> if you cannot see it clearly, or if its outline is the clearest or most striking aspect of it. 外形","examples":["His form lay still under the blankets. 他的身形一動不動地躺在毯子下面。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>form</b> is a paper with questions on it and spaces marked where you should write the answers. Forms usually ask you to give details about yourself, for example, when you are applying for a job or joining an organization. 表格","examples":["You will be asked to fill in a form with details of your birth and occupation. 你會被要求填寫一張有關你的出生和職業詳情的表格。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In sports, <b>form</b> refers to the ability or success of a person or animal over a period of time. 競技狀態","examples":["His form this season has been brilliant. 他在本賽季的競技狀態一直很好。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a particular shape <b>forms</b> or <b>is formed</b>, people or things move or are arranged so that this shape is made. 編排成 (某形狀); (某形狀) 編排成","examples":["A line formed to use the bathroom. 排成了一條隊來使用這個洗手間。","They formed a circle and sang \"Auld Lang Syne.\" 他們圍成一圈，唱起了《友誼地久天長》。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is arranged or changed so that it becomes similar to a thing with a particular structure or function, you can say that it <b>forms</b> that thing. (某物) 改變而形成 (另一物)","examples":["These panels folded up to form a screen some five feet tall. 這些嵌板折起來形成了一個高約五英尺的屏風。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something consists of particular things, people, or features, you can say that they <b>form</b> that thing. 構成","examples":["...the articles that formed the basis of Randolph's book. …構成倫道夫的書的基礎的那些文章。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>form</b> an organization, group, or company, you start it. 組建","examples":["They tried to form a study group on human rights. 他們試圖組建一個人權研究小組。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When something natural <b>forms</b> or <b>is formed</b>, it begins to exist and develop. 形成 (某自然物); (某自然物) 形成","examples":["The stars must have formed 10 to 15 billion years ago. 這些恆星一定形成於100億至150億年前。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>form</b> a relationship, a habit, or an idea, or if it <b>forms</b>, it begins to exist and develop. 形成 (某關係、習慣、想法); (某關係、習慣、想法) 形成","examples":["She had formed the habit of giving herself freely to men. 她已養成了隨意委身於男人的習慣。","An idea formed in his mind. 一個想法在他的腦子裡形成了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something <b>forms</b> a person's character or personality, you mean that it has a strong influence on them and causes them to develop in a particular way. 塑造","examples":["Anger at injustice formed his character. 對不公正行為的憤怒塑造了他的性格。"]}]}]},"gate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大門；登機口；閘門，閥門；（體育比賽的）觀眾人數；（體育比賽的）門票收入"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"……門事件（表示政治醜聞）(-gate)"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gate</b> is a structure like a door which is used at the entrance to a field, a garden, or the grounds of a building. 大門","examples":["He opened the gate and started walking up to the house. 他開啟大門並邁步向那房子走去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In an airport, a <b>gate</b> is a place where passengers leave the airport and get on their aeroplane. 登機口","examples":["Passengers with hand luggage can go straight to the departure gate to check in there. 攜帶手提行李的乘客可以直接到登機口辦理登機手續。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>gate </b> is the total amount of money that is paid by the people who go to a sports match or other event. 門票收入","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the channels by which molten metal is poured into a mould 熔化金屬澆模時的通道","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to provide with a gate or gates 給…裝門","examples":[]}]}]},"garbage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>垃圾，廢物；<美>垃圾箱；<非正式>廢話，無聊的東西；無用資訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Garbage</b> is waste material, especially waste from a kitchen. (尤指廚房的) 垃圾","examples":["This morning a bomb in a garbage bag exploded and injured 15 people. 今天早上一顆放在垃圾袋中的炸彈爆炸，炸傷15人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone says that an idea or opinion is <b>garbage</b>, they are emphasizing that they believe it is untrue or unimportant. 廢話","examples":["I personally think this is complete garbage. 我個人認為這純屬無稽之談。"]}]}]},"gain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得，贏得；受益；增加，增長；（經過努力）到達；（鐘錶）走快；持球前進，推進（一段距離）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"增加；好處，改進；收益；將球推進的距離；（常用對數表示的功率或電壓的）增益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or place <b>gains</b> something such as an ability or quality, they gradually get more of it. 獲得","examples":["Students can gain valuable experience by working on the campus radio or magazine. 學生們透過在校園廣播臺或校刊工作能夠獲得寶貴的經驗。","His reputation abroad has gained in stature. 他在國外的聲望提高了檔次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>gain</b> <b>from</b> something such as an event or situation, you get some advantage or benefit from it. 受益","examples":["The company didn't disclose how much it expects to gain from the two deals. 該公司沒有透露它期望從這兩筆交易中獲利多少。","There is absolutely nothing to be gained by feeling bitter. 感受痛苦絕對是毫無益處的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>gain</b> something such as weight or speed means to have an increase in that particular thing. 增加","examples":["Some people do gain weight after they stop smoking. 有些人戒菸後的確增加體重了。","The BMW started coming forward, passing the other cars and gaining speed as it approached. 寶馬車開始向前趕，超越了其它車，並且在接近時加速。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>gain</b> something, you obtain it, especially after a lot of hard work or effort. (尤指經過努力) 得到","examples":["To gain a promotion, you might have to work overtime. 為了得到晉升，你可能得加班。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gain</b> is also a noun. 增加","examples":["News on new home sales is brighter, showing a gain of nearly 8% in June. 有關新房銷售的新聞更加樂觀，顯示6月份有近8%的增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a notch, mortise, or groove, esp one cut to take the flap of a butt hinge 腰槽","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as an idea or an ideal <b>gains ground</b>, it gradually becomes more widely known or more popular. (想法或理想等) 越來越流行","examples":["There are strong signs that his views are gaining ground. 有明顯的跡象表明他的觀點正越來越深入人心。"]}]}]},"geography":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地理，地理學；地形，地貌；地理環境"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Geography</b> is the study of the countries of the world and of such things as the land, seas, climate, towns, and population. 地理學","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>geography</b> of a place is the way that features such as rivers, mountains, towns, or streets are arranged within it. 地形","examples":["...policemen who knew the local geography. …瞭解當地地形的警察們。"]}]}]},"gentleman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（稱呼或指男子，尤其是不認識的）先生；彬彬有禮的人，有教養的人；<舊>有身份的人，富紳；（古時用語）出身高貴的男子；<美，非正式>（對立法機構男性議員的稱呼）先生，閣下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a man is a <b>gentleman</b>, you mean he is polite and educated, and can be trusted. 有教養的人","examples":["He was always such a gentleman. 他總是這樣一個彬彬有禮的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gentleman</b> is a man who comes from a family of high social standing. 紳士","examples":["...this wonderful portrait of English gentleman Joseph Greenway. …這幅英國紳士約瑟夫·格林韋的絕妙肖像畫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can address men as <b>gentlemen</b>, or refer politely to them as <b>gentlemen</b>. 先生 (一種對人禮貌的稱呼)","examples":["This way, please, ladies and gentlemen. 請這邊走，女士們先生們。","It seems this gentleman was waiting for the doctor. 這位先生似乎那時正在等醫生。"]}]}]},"giraffe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長頸鹿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>giraffe</b> is a large African animal with a very long neck, long legs, and dark patches on its body. 長頸鹿","examples":[]}]}]},"giant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（傳說中的）巨人；高大健壯的人；巨獸，巨型植物；大公司，大國；卓越人物，偉人；（天文）巨星"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大的，偉大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is described as <b>giant</b> is much larger or more important than most others of its kind. 巨大的; 重大的","examples":["...America's giant car maker, General Motors. …美國的汽車製造巨頭——通用汽車公司。","...a giant oak table. …一張巨大的櫟木桌。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Giant</b> is often used to refer to any large, successful business organization or country. 大企業; 大國","examples":["...Japanese electronics giant, Sony. …日本的電子業巨頭——索尼公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>giant</b> is an imaginary person who is very big and strong, especially one mentioned in old stories. (尤指古老故事中虛構的) 巨人","examples":["...a Nordic saga of giants. …一部關於巨人的北歐傳奇。"]}]}]},"general":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總體的，普遍的；一般的，常規的；大致的，大概的；綜合的，廣泛的；首席的，總管的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上將，將軍；半軍事化管理的宗教組織（如耶穌會修士、多明我會修士或救世軍）的領袖；<古>大眾，公眾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>general</b> is a high-ranking officer in the armed forces, usually in the army. 將軍","examples":["The General's visit to Sarajevo is part of preparations for the deployment of extra troops. 那位將軍對薩拉熱窩的訪問是為部署更多軍隊所做的準備工作的一部分。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>general</b> situation somewhere or talk about something in <b>general</b> terms, you are describing the situation as a whole rather than considering its details or exceptions. 大體的","examples":["The figures represent a general decline in employment. 這些數字表明就業率的總體下降。","...a general deterioration in the quality of life. …生活質量的總體下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>general</b> to describe several items or activities when there are too many of them or when they are not important enough to mention separately. 多種的","examples":["$2,500 for software is soon swallowed up in general costs. 用於軟體的$2500很快被各種花銷耗盡了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>general</b> to describe something that involves or affects most people, or most people in a particular group. 普遍的","examples":["The project should raise general awareness about bullying. 這個專案應該引起對恃強凌弱現象的普遍注意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>general</b>, you mean that it is not restricted to any one thing or area. 整體的","examples":["...a general ache radiating from the back of the neck. …從後頸部擴散開的全身疼痛。","...a general sense of well-being. 總體上的幸福感"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>General</b> is used to describe a person's job, usually as part of their title, to indicate that they have complete responsibility for the administration of an organization or business. 總管的","examples":["He joined Sanders Roe, moving on later to become general manager. 他加入桑德斯雷奧，之後一路升任至總經理。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something <b>in general terms</b>, you describe it without giving details. 籠統地說","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>in general</b> to indicate that you are talking about something as a whole, rather than about part of it. 總體上","examples":["I think we need to improve our educational system in general. 我認為我們需要從總體上改進我們的教育體制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>in general</b> to indicate that you are referring to most people or things in a particular group. 總的來說 (指某一群體的大多數)","examples":["People in general will support us. 總體而言，人們會支援我們的。"]}]}]},"glove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（分手指的）手套；（拳擊、棒球等所用的）加墊防護手套"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……戴手套；（比賽中用戴手套的手）接（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gloves</b> are pieces of clothing which cover your hands and wrists and have individual sections for each finger. You wear gloves to keep your hands warm or dry or to protect them. 分指手套","examples":["He stuck his gloves in his pocket. 他把手套塞進了口袋裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>fits like a glove</b>, you are emphasizing that it fits exactly. 正合適","examples":["I gave one of the bikinis to my sister Sara and it fit like a glove. 我把其中一件比基尼給了妹妹薩拉，她穿正合身。"]}]}]},"glue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膠水；凝聚力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"膠合，貼上；<非正式>專注於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glue</b> is a sticky substance used for joining things together, often for repairing broken things. 膠; 膠水","examples":["...a tube of glue. …一管膠水。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>glue</b> one object to another, you stick them together using glue. 用膠粘","examples":["Glue the fabric around the window. 用膠把這布粘在窗戶四周。","The material is cut and glued in place. 材料被剪開並粘到合適的位置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is glued to</b> something, you mean that they are giving it all their attention. 使全神貫注","examples":["They are all glued to the Olympic Games. 他們都全神貫注於奧運會。"]}]}]},"goat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"山羊；<非正式>老色鬼；<美，非正式>替罪羊；<英，非正式>愚蠢的人；摩羯（星）座（the Goat）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>goat</b> is a farm animal or a wild animal that is about the size of a sheep. Goats have horns, and hairs on their chin which resemble a beard. 山羊","examples":[]}]}]},"golf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高爾夫球運動；（無線通訊中的）字母G的程式碼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打高爾夫球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Golf</b> is a game in which you use long sticks called clubs to hit a small, hard ball into holes that are spread out over a large area of grassy land. 高爾夫運動","examples":["\"Do you play golf?\" he asked me suddenly. “你打高爾夫嗎？”他突然問我。"]}]}]},"goal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"球門；進球得分；目標，目的；（旅行）目的地；（賽跑的）終點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"射門，射門得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In games such as football or hockey, the <b>goal</b> is the space into which the players try to get the ball in order to score a point for their team. 球門","examples":["The Dragons had only one shot on goal. 龍隊只有一次射門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In games such as football or hockey, a <b>goal</b> is when a player gets the ball into the goal, or the point that is scored by doing this. 進球","examples":["They scored five goals in the first half of the match. 他們在上半場進了5個球。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is your <b>goal</b> is something that you hope to achieve, especially when much time and effort will be needed. 目標","examples":["It's a matter of setting your own goals and following them. 這是一個設定自己的目標並努力實現它們的問題。"]}]}]},"grape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葡萄；葡萄酒（the grape）；霰彈，葡萄彈（grapeshot 的簡稱）；葡萄樹；葡萄色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grapes</b> are small green or purple fruit which grow in bunches. Grapes can be eaten raw, used for making wine, or dried. 葡萄","examples":["...a bunch of grapes. …一串葡萄。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's attitude as <b>sour grapes</b>, you mean that they say something is worthless or undesirable because they want it themselves but cannot have it. 酸葡萄 (喻指得不到而加以貶低的東西)","examples":["These accusations have been going on for some time now, but it is just sour grapes. 這些指控到現在已經持續有一段時間了，但那不過是酸葡萄心理而已。"]}]}]},"guava":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"番石榴（熱帶水果，果皮黃綠色，果肉白色、粉紅色或紅色，內有硬籽，可鮮食或制果汁、果醬）；番石榴樹（桃金娘科番石榴屬灌木或小喬木，原產熱帶美洲，結可食果實）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guava</b> is a round, yellow, tropical fruit with pink or white flesh and hard seeds. 番石榴","examples":[]}]}]},"government":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"政府，內閣；政體，國家體制；（國家等的）治理，管理；政府掌控經濟和社會活動的程度；（語法）支配關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>government</b> of a country is the group of people who are responsible for governing it. 政府","examples":["The Government has insisted that confidence is needed before the economy can improve. 政府強調需要有信心經濟狀況才能改善。","...democratic governments in countries like Britain and the U.S. …英美等國的民主政府。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Government</b> consists of the activities, methods, and principles involved in governing a country or other political unit. 治理","examples":["The first four years of government were completely disastrous. 頭4年的治理徹底失敗了。"]}]}]},"growth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成長，生長；增長，發展；腫瘤，贅生物；生長物，產物；種植，栽培"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"發展的，增長的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>growth</b> <b>of</b> something such as an industry, organization, or idea is its development in size, wealth, or importance. 發展","examples":["...the growth of nationalism. …民族主義的高漲。","...Japan's enormous economic growth. …日本經濟巨大的發展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>growth</b> in something is the increase in it. 增長","examples":["A steady growth in the popularity of two smaller parties may upset the polls. 兩個較小政黨聲譽的持續增長也許會攪亂大選。","The area has seen a rapid population growth. 這個地區人口快速增長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>growth</b> is the development and progress of their character. (性格的) 成長","examples":["...the child's emotional and intellectual growth. …孩子情感和智力方面的成長。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Growth</b> in a person, animal, or plant is the process of increasing in physical size and development. 生長","examples":["...hormones which control fertility and body growth. …控制生育力和身體發育的荷爾蒙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>growth</b> to refer to plants that have recently developed or that developed at the same time. 植物","examples":["This helps to ripen new growth and makes it flower profusely. 這有助於新植物成熟並且開出繁茂的花朵。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>growth</b> is a lump that grows inside or on a person, animal, or plant, and that is caused by a disease. 腫瘤","examples":["This type of surgery could even be used to extract cancerous growths. 這類外科手術甚至可以用來摘除惡性腫瘤。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>growth</b> industry, area, or market is one that is increasing in size or activity. 發展的","examples":["Computers and electronics are growth industries and need skilled technicians. 計算機與電子屬於發展中的行業，需要熟練的技術人員。"]}]}]},"guitar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"吉他，六絃琴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guitar</b> is a musical instrument with six strings and a long neck. You play the guitar by plucking or strumming the strings. 吉他","examples":[]}]}]},"grade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"等級，品級；（工作崗位，官銜等的）級別，職別；成績，分數；（美國學制）年級；斜坡，坡度；（疾病的）程度，階段；與純種雜交改良的牛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"按照級別安排或分配，分類；給……評分；設定（路面）坡度；（尤指色彩）從一個等級逐漸進入另一個等級；（家畜）與優良品種雜交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is graded</b>, its quality is judged, and it is often given a number or a name that indicates how good or bad it is. 將…分等級; 給…評分","examples":["Dust masks are graded according to the protection they offer. 防塵面具根據其提供的防護而分級。","Hampshire College does not grade the students' work. 漢普郡學院不對學生們的作業評分。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>grade</b> of a product is its quality, especially when this has been officially judged. 質量等級","examples":["...a good grade of plywood. …高品質的膠合板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>grade</b> in an examination or piece of written work is the mark you get, usually in the form of a letter or number, that indicates your level of achievement. (用字母或數字表示的) 成績","examples":["What grade are you hoping to get? 你希望得到什麼樣的成績？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>grade</b> in a company or organization is your level of importance or your rank. (職員的) 等級","examples":["Staff turnover is particularly high among junior grades. 員工流動率在級別低的職員中特別高。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In the United States, a <b>grade</b> is a group of classes in which all the children are of a similar age. When you are six years old you go into the first grade and you leave school after the twelfth grade. (美國學校中的) 年級","examples":["Mr. White teaches first grade in south Georgia. 懷特先生在佐治亞州南部教一年級。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>grade</b> is a slope. 斜坡","examples":["She drove up a steep grade and then began the long descent into the desert. 她駕車爬上一個陡坡，然後開始長長的下坡進入沙漠。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Someone's <b>grade</b> is their military rank. 軍銜","examples":["I was a naval officer, lieutenant junior grade. 我曾是名海軍軍官，中尉軍銜。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grade</b> is also a combining form. 也用於組合式構詞","examples":["...weapons-grade plutonium. …武器級鈽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>makes the grade</b>, they succeed, especially by reaching a particular standard. 成功","examples":["She had a strong desire to be a dancer but failed to make the grade. 她渴望成為一名舞蹈家但沒有成功。"]}]}]},"guy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>男人，傢伙；<美，非正式>夥計們，兄弟（或姐妹）們；<英>蓋伊模擬像；（帳篷或杆柱的）固定拉繩，牽索"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘲笑，戲弄；用支索穩定（加固）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guy</b> is a man. 傢伙","examples":["I was working with a guy from Milwaukee. 我跟一個從密爾沃基來的傢伙一起工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Americans sometimes address a group of people, whether they are male or female, as <b>guys</b> or <b>you guys</b>. 夥計們","examples":["Hi, guys. How are you doing? 嗨，夥計們，你們好嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a rope, chain, wire, etc, for anchoring an object, such as a radio mast, in position or for steadying or guiding it while being hoisted or lowered 拉繩; 牽索","examples":[]}]}]},"hamburger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漢堡包；碎牛肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hamburger</b> is ground meat which has been shaped into a flat circle. Hamburgers are fried or grilled and then eaten, often on a bun. 漢堡包","examples":[]}]}]},"handkerchief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手帕；頭巾，圍巾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handkerchief</b> is a small square piece of fabric which you use for blowing your nose. 手帕","examples":[]}]}]},"hall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禮堂，大廳；門廳；走廊，過道；（大學的）學生宿舍；府邸，莊園"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>hall</b> in a house or an apartment is the area just inside the front door, into which some of the other rooms open. 門廳","examples":["The lights were on in the hall and in the bedroom. 門廳和臥室的燈亮著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hall</b> in a building is a long passage with doors into rooms on both sides of it. (樓裡的) 過道","examples":["There are 10 rooms along each hall. 每條過道兩側都有10個房間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hall</b> is a large room or building which is used for public events such as concerts, exhibitions, and meetings. 大廳; 禮堂","examples":["We picked up our conference materials and filed into the lecture hall. 我們拿了會議材料，魚貫進入禮堂。"]}]}]},"habit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"習慣；（吸毒、喝酒、抽菸的）癮；道袍，道服；<古>體質，體型"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>給……穿衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>habit</b> is something that you do often or regularly. 習慣","examples":["He has an endearing habit of licking his lips when he's nervous. 他有個緊張時舔嘴唇的可愛習慣。","Many people add salt to their food out of habit, without even tasting it first. 許多人出於習慣往他們的食物中加鹽，甚至都不先品嚐一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>habit</b> is an action considered bad that someone does repeatedly and finds it difficult to stop doing. 壞習慣","examples":["A good way to break the habit of eating too quickly is to put your knife and fork down after each mouthful. 一個改掉吃飯太快的壞習慣的好方法是每吃一口後放下刀叉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A drug <b>habit</b> is an addiction to a drug such as heroin or cocaine. 毒癮","examples":["She became a prostitute in order to pay for her cocaine habit. 她為花錢過可卡因毒癮而成了一名妓女。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>a creature of habit</b>, you mean that they usually do the same thing at the same time each day, rather than doing new and different things. 按習慣行事的人","examples":["Jesse is a creature of habit and always eats breakfast. 傑西是按習慣行事的人，每天都吃早餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in the habit of</b> doing something, you do it regularly or often. If you <b>get</b> <b>into the habit of</b> doing something, you begin to do it regularly or often. 習慣於…/養成…的習慣","examples":["They were in the habit of giving two or three dinner parties a month. 他們習慣於每月舉辦兩三次晚宴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make a habit of</b> doing something, you do it regularly or often. 使成為習慣","examples":["You can phone me at work as long as you don't make a habit of it. 你可以在上班時給我打電話，只要你別讓這成為習慣就行。"]}]}]},"guard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衛兵，警衛；看守，保衛，警戒；列車長；保護裝置；（英國的）禁衛軍；（籃球）後衛；（拳擊運動員的）防禦姿勢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"守衛，保衛；看守，監視；警惕，防範；保護，維護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>guard</b> a place, person, or object, you stand near them in order to watch and protect them. 守衛; 護衛","examples":["Gunmen guarded homes near the cemetery with shotguns. 槍手攜帶獵槍守衛著公墓附近的住宅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>guard</b> someone, you watch them and keep them in a particular place to stop them from escaping. 看守","examples":["Marines with rifles guarded them. 持步槍的海軍陸戰隊士兵看守他們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>guard</b> some information or advantage that you have, you try to protect it or keep it for yourself. 保護; 保守","examples":["He closely guarded her identity. 他嚴密地保守她的身份。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guard</b> is someone such as a soldier, police officer, or prison officer who is guarding a particular place or person. 衛兵","examples":["The prisoners overpowered their guards and locked them in a cell. 囚犯們制服了衛兵，並把他們鎖在一個牢房裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>guard</b> is a specially organized group of people, such as soldiers or police officers, who protect or watch someone or something. (一隊) 衛兵","examples":["We have a security guard around the whole area. 我們在整個地區周圍配有保安人員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>guard</b> is a protective device which covers a part of someone's body or a dangerous part of a piece of equipment. 防護裝置","examples":["...the chin guard of my helmet. …我頭盔上的下巴防護罩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"On a train, a <b>guard</b> is a person whose job is to travel on the train in order to help passengers, check tickets, and make sure that the train travels safely and on time. 列車員","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>catches</b> you <b>off guard</b>, they surprise you by doing something you do not expect. If something <b>catches</b> you <b>off guard</b>, it surprises you by happening when you are not expecting it. 乘某人不備使其大吃一驚","examples":["Charm the audience and catch them off guard. 讓觀眾陶醉，然後出其不意使他們大吃一驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lower</b> your <b>guard</b>, <b>let</b> your <b>guard</b> <b>down</b> or <b>drop</b> your <b>guard</b>, you relax when you should be careful and alert, often with unpleasant consequences. 放鬆警惕","examples":["The ANC could not afford to lower its guard until everything had been carried out. 在所有任務完成之前，非洲人國民大會絲毫不敢放鬆警惕。","You can't let your guard down. 你不能掉以輕心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>on</b> your <b>guard</b> or <b>on guard</b>, you are being very careful because you think a situation might become difficult or dangerous. 警惕","examples":["The police have questioned him thoroughly, and he'll be on his guard. 警察已仔細盤問了他，因此他會保持警惕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>on guard</b>, they are on duty and responsible for guarding a particular place or person. 值守","examples":["Police were on guard at Barnet town hall. 警察在巴尼特市政廳值守。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>stand guard</b>, you stand near a particular person or place because you are responsible for watching or protecting them. 站崗","examples":["One young policeman stood guard outside the locked embassy gates. 一名年輕的警察在大門緊閉的使館外站崗。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone is <b>under guard</b>, they are being guarded. 受到看守","examples":["Three men were arrested and one was under guard in a hospital. 有三人被捕，一人在醫院裡受到監視。"]}]}]},"hanger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣架；掛鉤，吊架；絞刑執行者；（Hanger）人名；<英>漢格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hanger</b> is the same as a . 衣架","examples":[]}]}]},"heater":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加熱器，取暖器；加熱工，司爐工；（棒球俚語）快速球；希特（英語姓氏）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>heater</b> is a piece of equipment or a machine which is used to raise the temperature of something, especially of the air inside a room or a car. 加熱器","examples":["There's an electric heater in the bedroom. 臥室裡有一臺電暖器。"]}]}]},"hammer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錘子，榔頭；（拍賣用的）木槌；鏈球；擊鐵；音槌；鑼錘"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用錘子）敲擊；用力敲打，猛踢；強行灌輸，反覆強調；（在體育比賽中）使慘敗，大敗；使（企業）受到打擊；嚴厲批評，指責；（心臟）劇烈跳動；壓低（某股票）的價格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hammer</b> is a tool that consists of a heavy piece of metal at the end of a handle. It is used, for example, to hit nails into a piece of wood or a wall, or to break things into pieces. 錘子","examples":["He used a hammer and chisel to chip away at the wall. 他用錘子和鑿子將牆壁一點點鑿掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In track and field, a <b>hammer</b> is a heavy weight on a piece of wire, which the athlete throws as far as possible. 鏈球","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The hammer</b> also refers to the sport of throwing the hammer. 鏈球運動","examples":["Events like the hammer and the discus are not traditional crowd-pleasers in the West. 鏈球和鐵餅之類的運動專案在西方通常不是很吸引觀眾。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hammer</b> an object such as a nail, you hit it with a hammer. 用錘擊","examples":["To avoid damaging the tree, hammer a wooden peg into the hole. 為了避免毀壞這棵樹，把一隻木釘敲進那個洞裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hammer</b> something such as an idea <b>into</b> people or you <b>hammer</b> <b>at</b> it, you keep repeating it forcefully so that it will have an effect on people. 把…灌輸給…","examples":["He hammered it into me that I had not suddenly become a rotten goalkeeper. 他反覆向我灌輸，我並沒有突然變成一個糟糕的守門員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>hammers</b> another person, you mean that they attack, criticize, or punish the other person severely. 猛烈攻擊; 嚴厲批評; 嚴厲懲罰","examples":["Democrats insisted they will continue to hammer Bush on his tax plan. 民主黨人堅稱，他們將繼續抨擊布什的稅收計劃。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In sports, if you say that one player or team <b>hammered</b> another, you mean that the first player or team defeated the second completely and easily. (在體育比賽中) 輕鬆擊潰","examples":["He hammered the young left-hander in three straight sets. 他連勝3局，輕鬆擊潰了這位年輕的左撇子選手。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hammer</b> <b>on</b> a surface, you hit it several times in order to make a noise, or to emphasize something you are saying when you are angry. 砰砰敲擊","examples":["We had to hammer and shout before they would open up. 我們不得不砰砰敲打併大喊大叫，他們才會開門。","A crowd of reporters was hammering on the door. 一群記者在砰砰敲那扇門。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>was going at</b> something <b>hammer and tongs</b>, you mean that they were doing it with great enthusiasm or energy. 勁頭十足地","examples":["He loved gardening. He went at it hammer and tongs as soon as he got back from work. 他喜愛園藝，下班一回到家，就勁頭十足地幹起來。"]}]}]},"hen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"母雞；雌禽；<蘇格蘭>（小）姑娘；用於其他鳥的名稱（尤指秧雞科水鳥）；雌龍蝦（或螃蟹、鮭魚）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hen</b> is a female chicken. People often keep hens in order to eat or sell their eggs. 母雞","examples":[]}]}]},"heroine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女英雄；女主角，女主人公；女偶像；（神話和傳說中的）女超人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>heroine</b> of a book, play, film, or story is the main female character, who usually has good qualities. 女主人公","examples":["The heroine is a senior TV executive. 女主人公是一位電視臺高階主管。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>heroine</b> is a woman who has done something brave, new, or good, and who is therefore greatly admired by a lot of people. 女英雄","examples":["The national heroine of the day was Xing Fen, winner of the first gold medal of the Games. 當時的民族女英雄是在亞運會上奪得第一塊金牌的邢芬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a woman as your <b>heroine</b>, you mean that you admire her greatly, usually because of a particular quality or skill that she has. 女性偶像","examples":["My heroine was Elizabeth Taylor. 我崇拜的女性是伊麗莎白·泰勒。"]}]}]},"hippo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式> 河馬（hippopotamus 的簡稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hippo</b> is a hippopotamus. 河馬","examples":[]}]}]},"highway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>公路，幹道；公用通道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>highway</b> is a main road, especially one that connects towns or cities. (尤指城市間的) 公路","examples":["I crossed the highway, dodging the traffic. 我閃身避讓著來往的車輛，穿過了公路。"]}]}]},"handle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拿；處理，應付；操縱；觸（球）；經營，管理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"把手，拉手；柄，提手；（理解、解決問題的）方法，途徑；<非正式>（尤指奇怪的）名字，名稱；（織物等的）手感；<美，非正式>賭注總額"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"有……個柄的，有……柄的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handle</b> is a small round object or a lever that is attached to a door and is used for opening and closing it. 門把手","examples":["I turned the handle and found the door was open. 我轉動把手，發現門是開著的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>handle</b> is the part of an object such as a tool, bag, or cup that you hold in order to be able to pick up and use the object. 柄; 把","examples":["...a broom handle. …一個掃帚柄"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"應付","examples":["The family has criticized the military's handling of Robert's death. 羅伯特的家人批評軍方沒有處理好羅伯特的死亡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone can <b>handle</b> a problem or situation, you mean that they have the ability to deal with it successfully. (成功地) 處理","examples":["To tell the truth, I don't know if I can handle the job. 說實話，我不知道我能否做好這份工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the way that someone <b>handles</b> a problem or situation, you mention whether or not they are successful in achieving the result they want. 應付","examples":["I think I would handle a meeting with Mr. Siegel very badly. 我覺得我可能應付不了與西格爾先生的會談。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>handle</b> a particular area of work, you have responsibility for it. 負責","examples":["She handled travel arrangements for the press corps during the presidential campaign. 她負責安排新聞報道團在總統競選期間的出行事宜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>handle</b> something, you hold it or move it with your hands. 拿; 用手移動","examples":["Wear rubber gloves when handling cat litter. 撿拾貓糞時要帶橡皮手套。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fly off the handle</b>, you suddenly and completely lose your temper. 突然大發脾氣","examples":["He flew off the handle at the slightest thing. 他為一點小事就突然大發雷霆。"]}]}]},"hippopotamus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"河馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hippopotamus</b> is a very large African animal with short legs and thick, hairless skin. Hippopotamuses live in and near rivers. 河馬","examples":[]}]}]},"height":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"身高；高；高度；高處，高地；極佳狀況；極端例子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>height</b> of a person or thing is their size or length from the bottom to the top. 高度","examples":["Her weight is about normal for her height. 按她的身高，她的體重大體正常。","I am 5'6'' in height. 我的身高是5英尺6英寸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Height</b> is the quality of being tall. 高","examples":["She admits that her height is intimidating for some men. 她承認自己的高個兒對一些男人而言是嚇人的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular <b>height</b> is the distance that something is above the ground or above something else mentioned. 高度","examples":["At the speed and height at which he was moving, he was never more than half a second from disaster. 以這樣的速度在這麼高的地方移動，他離災難永遠只有半步之遙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>height</b> is a high position or place above the ground. 高處","examples":["I'm not afraid of heights. 我不恐高。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When an activity, situation, or organization is <b>at</b> its <b>height</b>, it is at its most successful, powerful, or intense. 頂點; 高潮","examples":["At its height, the antiwar movement drew supporters from nearly every political camp. 在高潮階段，反戰運動從幾乎每個政治派別那裡都吸引來了支持者。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>the height of</b> a particular quality, you are emphasizing that it has that quality to the greatest degree possible. 頂點","examples":["The hip-hugging black and white polka-dot dress was the height of fashion. 黑白圓點緊身連衣裙當時是最新潮的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something reaches great <b>heights</b>, it becomes very extreme or intense. 極點","examples":["...the mid-1980s, when prices rose to absurd heights. …物價上升至荒謬極點的20世紀80年代中期。"]}]}]},"hip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臀部，髖；屋脊；野薔薇果"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"時髦的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"加油！ 好哇！"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>hips</b> are the two areas at the sides of your body between the tops of your legs and your waist. 臀部","examples":["Tracey put her hands on her hips and sighed. 特蕾西把手放在自己的臀部上嘆了口氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You refer to the bones between the tops of your legs and your waist as your <b>hips</b>. 髖","examples":["Eventually, surgeons replaced both hips and both shoulders. 最後，外科醫生把兩側的髖骨和兩邊的肩骨都換了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the berry-like brightly coloured fruit of a rose plant: a swollen receptacle, rich in vitamin C, containing several small hairy achenes 野薔薇果 (Also called rosehip)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>hip</b>, you mean that they are very modern and follow all the latest fashions, for example in clothes and ideas. 時髦的","examples":["...a hip young character with tight-cropped blond hair and stylish glasses. …一個留著修剪得很短的金髮、戴著時尚眼鏡的時髦青年。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a large group of people want to show their appreciation or approval of someone, one of them says \"<b>Hip hip</b>\" and they all shout \"<b>hooray</b>.\" 好啊 (表示欣賞或讚許的呼聲)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>shoots from the hip</b>, you mean that they react to situations or give their opinion very quickly, without stopping to think. 倉促行事; 倉促表態","examples":["Judges don't have to shoot from the hip. They have the leisure to think, to decide. 法官們不必倉促作決定。他們有的是時間去思考、去裁決。"]}]}]},"hobby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"業餘愛好，嗜好；<古> 小馬，馬駒；燕隼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hobby</b> is an activity that you enjoy doing in your spare time. 業餘愛好","examples":["My hobbies are letter writing, music, photography, and tennis. 我的業餘愛好是寫信、音樂、攝影和網球。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any of several small Old World falcons, esp the European <b>Falco subbuteo,</b> formerly used in falconry 小鷹","examples":[]}]}]},"hire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>租用，租借；聘用，錄用"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"租借，租金；<美>被僱用的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hire</b> someone, you employ them or pay them to do a particular job for you. 僱用","examples":["Sixteen of the contestants have hired lawyers and are suing the organizers. 參賽者中有16人已經聘了律師，正在起訴主辦方。","He will be in charge of all hiring and firing at PHA. 他將負責公眾房產管理局裡的一切人事任免事務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hire</b> something, you pay money to the owner so that you can use it for a period of time. 租用","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>hire</b> to refer to the activity or business of hiring something. 租用","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>for hire</b>, it is available for you to hire. 供出租","examples":["Helmets will be available for hire at all Vail Resort ski areas. 在韋爾度假村的所有滑雪場裡都有頭盔供出租。"]}]}]},"holder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"持有者，佔有者；支託物；小農，小佃農"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>holder</b> is someone who owns or has something. 持有者","examples":["This season the club has had 73,500 season-ticket holders. 本季該俱樂部已經有73500名季票持有者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>holder</b> is a container in which you put an object, usually in order to protect it or to keep it in place. 支援物; 支架","examples":["...a toothbrush holder. …一隻牙刷座。"]}]}]},"honey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜂蜜；親愛的，寶貝兒；<非正式>極好的事物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……說甜言蜜語；加蜜使甜；奉承，"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"甘美的；蜂蜜似的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Honey</b> is a sweet, sticky, yellowish substance that is made by bees. 蜂蜜","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You call someone <b>honey</b> as a sign of affection. (用作稱呼) 親愛的","examples":["Honey, I don't really think that's a good idea. 親愛的，我不認為那是個好主意。"]}]}]},"hotel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅館，酒店，飯店；（無線電通訊中）字母H的程式碼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hotel</b> is a building where people stay, for example on holiday, paying for their rooms and meals. 旅館","examples":[]}]}]},"hostess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女主人，女東道主；女主持人；（餐館的）女迎賓，女門迎；（夜總會的）女招待；（飛機，火車等上的）女服務員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>hostess</b> at a party is the woman who has invited the guests and provides the food, drink, or entertainment. (聚會的) 女主人","examples":["The hostess introduced them. 女主人介紹了他們。"]}]}]},"hospital":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醫院；青年教育慈善機構；<史>（尤指僧侶騎士團所辦的）慈善招待所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hospital</b> is a place where people who are ill are cared for by nurses and doctors. 醫院","examples":["...a children's hospital with 120 beds. …一個有120張床位的兒童醫院。"]}]}]},"hero":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英雄，勇士；男主角，男主人公；偶像，崇拜物件；（夾有冷切肉、乳酪、沙拉等的）長卷三明治；（神話或傳說中的）超人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>hero</b> of a book, play, film, or story is the main male character, who usually has good qualities. 男主人公","examples":["The hero of Doctor Zhivago dies in 1929. 《日瓦戈醫生》的男主人公於1929年去世。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hero</b> is someone, especially a man, who has done something brave, new, or good, and who is therefore greatly admired by a lot of people. 英雄","examples":["He called Mr. Mandela a hero who had inspired millions. 他稱曼德拉先生是一個曾激勵千百萬人的英雄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as your <b>hero</b>, you mean that you admire them a great deal, usually because of a particular quality or skill that they have. 偶像","examples":["My boyhood hero was Kit Carson. 我孩提時的偶像是基特·卡森。"]}]}]},"hum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"哼（曲子）；發嗡嗡聲；活躍，繁忙；<英，非正式>發出難聞的氣味"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嗡嗡聲，嘈雜聲"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於表示猶豫或不同意）嗯，哼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>hums</b>, it makes a low continuous noise. 發出連續低沉的聲音","examples":["The birds sang, the bees hummed. 鳥兒唱歌，蜜蜂蜂鳴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>hums</b>, you mean that it is full of activity. (地方) 繁忙","examples":["The place is really beginning to hum. 這個地方真的開始熱鬧繁忙起來了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hum</b> is also a noun. 連續低沉的聲音","examples":["...the hum of traffic. …低沉的車流聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>hum</b>, or <b>hum</b> a tune, you sing a tune with your lips closed. 哼 (曲子)","examples":["She was humming a merry little tune. 她輕輕地哼著一首歡快的小曲兒。"]}]}]},"humor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幽默，詼諧，幽默感；心情，情緒，心境；（醫學）體液；（中世紀醫學）認為決定體質與情緒的四種體液之一"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"迎合，遷就，順應"}],"sections":[]},"hop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"單腳跳行；齊足（或雙足）跳行；快速移動，快速前往；登上（飛機、火車等）；（尤指搭乘飛機）短途旅行；換來換去；<非正式>速遞，快運；用啤酒花調味"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"單腳跳；（鳥、小動物）雙腳跳；短途旅行；忽布，啤酒花；舞會；霍普舞；毒品（尤指鴉片）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hop</b>, you move along by jumping on one foot. (人) 單腳跳行","examples":["I hopped down three steps. 我單腳跳下3級臺階。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When birds and some small animals <b>hop</b>, they move along by jumping on both or all four feet. (鳥和其他小動物) 齊足跳行","examples":["A small brown fawn hopped across the trail in front of them. 一隻小棕鹿在他們面前蹦跳著穿過了小路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hop</b> somewhere, you move there quickly or suddenly. 快速移動","examples":["My wife and I were the first to arrive and hopped on board. 我和妻子是最先到達並跳上車的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hop</b> is also a noun. (人) 單腳跳行","examples":["\"This really is a catching rhythm, huh?\" he added, with a few little hops. “這節奏可真有感染力，是吧？”他補充說道，單腳小步跳了幾下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hop</b> is also a noun. (鳥和其他小動物的) 齊足跳行","examples":["The rabbit got up, took four hops and turned around. 兔子直起身子，蹦跳了4下，然後轉過身。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hop</b> is a short, quick trip, usually by plane. (通常指乘飛機的) 短途快速旅行","examples":["It is a three-hour drive but can be reached by a 20-minute hop in a private helicopter. 這段路程開車需要3個小時，而乘坐私人直升飛機20分鐘就可以到達。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Hops</b> are flowers that are dried and used for making beer. 啤酒花","examples":[]}]}]},"icebox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（舊式，尤指美式英語）冰箱；（舊時）用冰塊冷藏食物的櫃子（也作 ice box 或 ice-box）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>icebox</b> is the same as a . 同refrigerator","examples":[]}]}]},"hunter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獵人，捕獵者；搜尋者，尋找者；獵狐馬；獵犬；有護蓋的手錶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hunter</b> is a person who hunts wild animals for food or as a sport. 獵人","examples":["The hunters stalked their prey. 獵人們隱伏跟蹤獵物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People who are searching for things of a particular kind are often referred to as <b>hunters</b>. 搜尋者","examples":["...job-hunters. …求職者。"]}]}]},"importance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要，重要性；傲慢；名望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>importance</b> of something is its quality of being significant, valued, or necessary in a particular situation. 重要","examples":["China has been stressing the importance of its ties with third world countries. 中國一貫強調與第三世界國家聯絡的重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Importance</b> means having influence, power, or status. 名望","examples":["Obviously a man of his importance is going to be missed. 顯然，他這麼一位重要人士將會被緬懷。"]}]}]},"hunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打獵，獵取；搜尋，搜尋；追蹤，追捕；（騎馬用獵犬）獵（狐）；擺動，振盪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搜尋，尋找；打獵，狩獵；（英國）獵狐活動；（英國經常舉行獵狐運動的）獵狐隊伍；獵區，狩獵場；擺動，振盪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hunt</b> <b>for</b> something or someone, you try to find them by searching carefully or thoroughly. 搜尋","examples":["A forensic team was hunting for clues. 法醫小組正在搜尋線索。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hunt</b> is also a noun. 搜尋","examples":["The couple had helped in the hunt for the toddlers. 這對夫婦曾幫著尋找那些蹣跚學步的孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hunt</b> is also a noun. 追捕","examples":["Despite a nationwide hunt for the kidnap gang, not a trace of them was found. 儘管已對這幫綁架團伙實行了全國範圍的大搜捕，但絲毫沒有發現他們的蛛絲馬跡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hunt</b> is also a noun. 打獵","examples":["He set off for a nineteen-day moose hunt in Nova Scotia. 他開始了在新斯科舍為期19天的獵駝鹿行程。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hunt</b> a criminal or an enemy, you search for them in order to catch or harm them. 追捕 (罪犯、敵人等)","examples":["Detectives have been hunting him for seven months. 7個月來警探們一直在追捕他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people or animals <b>hunt</b>, or <b>hunt</b> something, they chase and kill wild animals for food or as a sport. 獵殺 (野生動物); 打獵","examples":["As a child I learned to hunt and fish. 我孩提時代就學會了打獵和捕魚。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a team or competitor is <b>in the hunt</b> <b>for</b> something, they still have a chance of winning it. (參賽隊或競爭者) 有機會獲得","examples":["Six teams were still in the hunt for the team title. 6支隊伍仍然有機會獲得團體冠軍。"]}]}]},"independence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨立，自主；（國家的）獨立；（國家或地區的）政治獨立日期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country has or gains <b>independence</b>, it has its own government and is not ruled by any other country. (國家的) 獨立","examples":["In 1816, Argentina declared its independence from Spain. 1816年，阿根廷宣佈脫離西班牙而獨立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>independence</b> is the fact that they do not rely on other people. (人的) 自立","examples":["He was afraid of losing his independence. 他擔心喪失自己的獨立。"]}]}]},"income":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收入，收益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's or organization's <b>income</b> is the money that they earn or receive, as opposed to the money that they have to spend or pay out. 收入","examples":["Many families on low incomes will be unable to afford to buy their own home. 許多低收入家庭根本無力購買房子。"]}]}]},"hunger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飢餓感；飢餓，饑荒；渴求，渴望"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"渴求，渴望；捱餓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hunger</b> is the feeling of weakness or discomfort that you get when you need something to eat. 飢餓","examples":["Hunger is the body's signal that levels of blood sugar are too low. 飢餓感是體內發出的血糖濃度太低的訊號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hunger</b> is a severe lack of food which causes suffering or death. 饑荒","examples":["Three hundred people in this town are dying of hunger every day. 該鎮每天有300人因飢餓而死。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>hunger</b> <b>for</b> something, you want or need it very much. 渴望","examples":["Geffen has a hunger for success that seems bottomless. 格芬對成功的渴望似乎永無止境。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>hungers</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>hungers</b> <b>after</b> it, you are emphasizing that they want it very much. 渴望","examples":["But Jules was not eager for classroom learning, he hungered for adventure. 但是朱爾斯並不熱衷於課堂學習，他渴望冒險。"]}]}]},"improvement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"改善；改進之處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>improvement</b> <b>in</b> something, it becomes better. If you make <b>improvements</b> <b>to</b> something, you make it better. 改進","examples":["...the dramatic improvements in organ transplantation in recent years. …近幾年器官移植上令人矚目的改進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>an</b> <b>improvement</b> <b>on</b> a previous thing or situation, you mean that it is better than that thing. 改進的事物; 勝過他人的人","examples":["The new governor is an improvement on his predecessor. 新任總督勝過他的前任。"]}]}]},"ill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有病的，不舒服的；壞的，有害的；不友好的，不友善的；不吉祥的，不利的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"壞，惡劣地；艱難地，幾乎不；不友好地，不友善地；不祥地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"問題，困難；傷害，厄運；病人，患者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>ill</b> is suffering from a disease or a health problem. 患病的","examples":["In November 1941 Payne was seriously ill with pneumonia. 1941年11月，佩恩患了嚴重的肺炎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>ill</b> in front of some nouns to indicate that you are referring to something harmful or unpleasant. 有害的; 令人不快的","examples":["She had brought ill luck into her family. 她給家庭帶來了厄運。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who are ill in some way can be referred to as, for example, <b>the</b> mentally <b>ill</b>. 患…病的人","examples":["The hospice provides care for the terminally ill. 救濟院為身患絕症的人們提供護理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Difficulties and problems are sometimes referred to as <b>ills</b>. 難題","examples":["His critics maintain that he's responsible for many of Algeria's ills. 他的批評者堅持認為他對阿爾及利亞的許多問題負有責任。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ill</b> is evil or harm. 惡行; 傷害","examples":["They say they mean you no ill. 他們說他們對你沒有惡意。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ill</b> means the same as \"badly.\" 不合適地 (同badly)","examples":["The company's conservative instincts sit ill with competition. 該公司的保守本性不適合競爭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>can ill afford</b> <b>to</b> do something, or <b>can ill afford</b> something, you mean that they must prevent it from happening because it would be harmful or embarrassing to them. 難以承受","examples":["It's possible he won't play but I can ill afford to lose him. 他有可能不會出場，但我難以承受失去他的損失。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fall ill</b> or <b>are taken ill</b>, you suddenly become ill. 突然病倒","examples":["Shortly before Christmas, he was mysteriously taken ill. 聖誕節前不久，他突然莫名其妙地病了。"]}]}]},"hurry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"匆忙，急忙；催促；（朝某方向）迅速移動；迅速處理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"急忙；緊急，趕緊的理由"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hurry</b> somewhere, you go there as quickly as you can. 匆忙而行","examples":["Claire hurried along the road. 克萊爾匆匆地沿路而行。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hurry</b> <b>to</b> do something, you start doing it as soon as you can, or try to do it quickly. 趕緊（做）","examples":["Mrs. Hardie hurried to make up for her tactlessness by asking her guest about his holiday. 哈迪太太趕緊問她的客人假期過得如何，以彌補此前不得體的言行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>hurry</b> something means the same as to  something. 使加快進行","examples":["...the president's attempt to hurry the process of independence. …總統加快獨立程序的企圖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hurry</b> someone to a place or into a situation, you try to make them go to that place or get into that situation quickly. 催促","examples":["They say they are not going to be hurried into any decision. 他們說不會迫於壓力而倉促做出任何決定。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in a</b> <b>hurry</b> <b>to</b> do something, you need or want to do something quickly. If you do something <b>in a</b> <b>hurry</b>, you do it quickly or suddenly. 急忙","examples":["Kate was in a hurry to grow up, eager for knowledge and experience. 凱特急切地想長大，渴望獲得知識和經驗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say to someone \"<b>There's no hurry</b>\" or \"<b>I'm in no hurry</b>\" you are telling them that there is no need for them to do something immediately. 不著急","examples":["I'll need to talk with you, but there's no hurry. 我得找你談談，但不著急。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in no hurry</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are very unwilling to do it. 不想（做）","examples":["I love it here so I'm in no hurry to go anywhere. 我喜歡在這裡生活，所以我哪裡都不想去。"]}]}]},"industry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工業，生產製造；行業，產業；勤奮，勤勞；範圍，領域"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Industry</b> is the work and processes involved in collecting raw materials, and making them into products in factories. 工業","examples":["Our industry suffers through insufficient investment in research. 我們的工業因研究投入不足而大吃苦頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>industry</b> consists of all the people and activities involved in making a particular product or providing a particular service. 行業","examples":["...the motor vehicle and textile industries. …機動車與紡織行業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a social or political activity as an <b>industry</b>, you are criticizing it because you think it involves a lot of people in unnecessary or useless work. 興師動眾","examples":["...the industry of western capitalism. …西方資本主義的大張旗鼓。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Industry</b> is the fact of working very hard. 勤奮","examples":["No one doubted his ability, his industry or his integrity. 沒有人懷疑他的能力、勤奮和正直。"]}]}]},"increase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"增長，增強，增大"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"增長；增長量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>increases</b> or you <b>increase</b> it, it becomes greater in number, level, or amount. 使增加; 增加","examples":["The population continues to increase. 人口持續增長。","Japan's industrial output increased by 2%. 日本的工業產量增長了2%。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>increase</b> <b>in</b> the number, level, or amount of something, it becomes greater. 增加","examples":["...a sharp increase in productivity. …生產率的急速增長。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>on the increase</b>, it is happening more often or becoming greater in number or intensity. 正在增長","examples":["Crime is on the increase. 犯罪活動日益猖獗。"]}]}]},"insect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"昆蟲；類似昆蟲的小動物（如蜘蛛）；卑鄙的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>insect</b> is a small animal that has six legs. Most insects have wings. Ants, flies, butterflies, and beetles are all insects. 昆蟲","examples":[]}]}]},"ink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"墨水，油墨；<非正式>文字宣傳，紙媒宣傳；（章魚、烏賊等海洋生物分泌出的）墨汁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"簽訂，簽署（合同等）；塗墨水於（某物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ink</b> is the coloured liquid used for writing or printing. 墨水; 油墨","examples":["The letter was handwritten in black ink. 這封信是用黑墨水手寫的。"]}]}]},"instance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"例子，例項"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"舉……為例"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>for instance</b> to introduce a particular event, situation, or person that is an example of what you are talking about. 例如","examples":["In sub-Saharan Africa today, for instance, gross investment accounts for roughly 15% of national income. 例如，在如今的撒哈拉以南的非洲國家，總投資大約佔國民收入的15％。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say <b>in the first instance</b> to mention something that is the first step in a series of actions. 首先","examples":["In the first instance your child will be seen by an ear, nose and throat specialist. 你的孩子首先要由耳鼻喉專家診查。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>instance</b> is a particular example or occurrence of something. 例子","examples":["...an investigation into a serious instance of corruption. …對一例嚴重腐敗事件的調查。"]}]}]},"instant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"立刻的，馬上的；速食的，即食的；緊急的，緊迫的；<舊>（商業信函用語）本月的；<舊>此刻的，現時的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"瞬間，片刻；當時，那一刻；<非正式>速溶咖啡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>instant</b> is an extremely short period of time. 瞬間; 剎那","examples":["For an instant, Barney was tempted to flee. 那一瞬間，巴尼很想逃走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>at</b> a particular <b>instant</b>, you mean that it happens at exactly the time you have been referring to, and you are usually suggesting that it happens quickly or immediately. 時刻","examples":["At that instant the museum was plunged into total darkness. 在那一刻，博物館陷入一片黑暗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To do something <b>the instant</b> something else happens means to do it immediately. 一…就…","examples":["I bolted the door the instant I saw the bat. 我一看到那隻蝙蝠就把門閂上了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>instant</b> to describe something that happens immediately. 立即的","examples":["Mr. Porter's book was an instant hit. 波特先生的書立刻引起了轟動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Instant</b> food is food that you can prepare very quickly, for example, by just adding water. 調製快速方便的 (食品)","examples":["He stirred instant coffee into a mug of hot water. 他將速溶咖啡攪入一大杯熱水中。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"立即地","examples":["The man was killed instantly. 那人立即被殺死了。"]}]}]},"island":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"島，島嶼；島狀物，孤立體；腦島，胰島"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成島（狀），使孤立"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>island</b> is a piece of land that is completely surrounded by water. 島","examples":["...the Canary Islands. …加那利群島。"]}]}]},"invitation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邀請；引起，招致；（尤指正式地）徵求，請求；請帖，請柬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>invitation</b> is a written or spoken request to come to an event such as a party, a meal, or a meeting. 邀請","examples":["...an invitation to lunch. …午餐邀請。","The Syrians have not yet accepted an invitation to attend. 那些敘利亞人還沒有接受邀請。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>invitation</b> is the card or paper on which an invitation is written or printed. 請貼","examples":["Hundreds of invitations are being sent out this week. 本週數百張請貼正在發出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you believe that someone's action is likely to have a particular result, especially a bad one, you can refer to the action as an <b>invitation to</b> that result. 招惹","examples":["Don't leave your shopping on the back seat of your car – it's an open invitation to a thief. 不要把買好的東西放在車的後座上–這很容易招惹小偷。"]}]}]},"instrument":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"器械；樂器；儀器；促成某事的人（或事物），手段；受利用（或控制）的人，工具；文據，正式法律檔案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……裝備測量儀器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>instrument</b> is a tool or device that is used to do a particular task, especially a scientific task. 器械","examples":["...instruments for cleaning and polishing teeth. …清潔和拋光牙齒的各種器械。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A musical <b>instrument</b> is an object such as a piano, guitar, or flute, which you play in order to produce music. 樂器","examples":["Learning a musical instrument introduces a child to an understanding of music. 學習一種樂器能引導孩子對音樂有所瞭解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>instrument</b> is a device that is used for making measurements of something such as speed, height, or sound, for example, on a ship or plane or in a car. 儀器","examples":["The design of crucial instruments on the control panel will have to be improved. 控制板上關鍵儀器的設計必須要改進。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is an <b>instrument</b> for achieving a particular aim is used by people to achieve that aim. 手段","examples":["The veto has been a traditional instrument of diplomacy for centuries. 數世紀以來，否決已經成為一種傳統的外交手段。"]}]}]},"influence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"影響，作用；勢力，影響力；有影響的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"影響，對……起作用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Influence</b> is the power to make other people agree with your opinions or do what you want. 權勢","examples":["He used his influence to get his son into medical school. 他利用權勢把兒子弄進了醫學院。","He denies exerting any political influence over them. 他否認曾向他們施加過政治影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To have an <b>influence</b> <b>on</b> people or situations means to affect what they do or what happens. 影響","examples":["Van Gogh had a major influence on the development of modern painting. 凡·高對現代繪畫的發展有著重大的影響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone or something that is a good or bad <b>influence</b> <b>on</b> people has a good or bad effect on them. 有影響的人 (或事物)","examples":["I thought Sonny would be a good influence on you. 我認為桑尼對你會有好的影響。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>influence</b> someone, you use your power to make them agree with you or do what you want. 影響","examples":["He is trying to improperly influence a witness. 他正試圖不適當地影響一名證人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>influences</b> a person or situation, they have an effect on that person's behaviour or that situation. 影響","examples":["We became the best of friends and he influenced me deeply. 我們成了最好的朋友，而他深深地影響了我。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>under the influence of</b> someone or something, you are being affected or controlled by them. 在…影響之下","examples":["He was arrested on suspicion of driving under the influence of alcohol. 他因涉嫌酒後駕車而被捕。"]}]}]},"item":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專案，條款；一件商品（或物品）；一則，一條（新聞）；（關係親密的）一對"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於介紹清單上逐個專案之前）又，此外還有"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"逐條列出，記下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>item</b> is one of a collection or list of objects. 一些物品中的一項","examples":["The most valuable item on show will be a Picasso drawing. 展覽中最有價值的作品將是畢加索的一幅畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>item</b> is one of a list of things for someone to do, deal with, or talk about. 專案","examples":["The other item on the agenda is the tour. 另一項議程是旅行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>item</b> is a report or article in a newspaper or magazine, or on television or radio. (報刊、電視或廣播中的) 一篇報道或文章","examples":["There was an item in the paper about him. 報紙上有一篇關於他的報道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that two people are an <b>item</b>, you mean that they are having a romantic or sexual relationship. (在戀愛或有性關係的) 一對","examples":["She and Gino were an item. 她和吉諾曾是一對。"]}]}]},"jeep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"吉普車；吉普（美國汽車品牌，即 Jeep）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>Jeep</b> is a type of car that can travel over rough ground. 吉普車","examples":["...a U.S. Army Jeep. …一輛美軍吉普車。"]}]}]},"jacket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夾克衫，短上衣；書皮，護封；<英> 馬鈴薯皮；（機器或裝置的）絕熱罩，隔離罩；碟片套；（海上採油平臺的）支架"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……裝護套；給……穿短上衣；<非正式>打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jacket</b> is a short coat with long sleeves. 短上衣; 夾克","examples":["...a black leather jacket. …一件黑色皮夾克。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>jacket</b> of a book is the paper cover that protects the book. (書的) 護封","examples":["A beautiful girl gazes from the jacket of this book. 一位漂亮的女孩從這本書的護封裡凝視過來。"]}]}]},"interview":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"面試，面談；採訪，訪問；訊問，審問；接見，會見"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"面試，面談；採訪，訪談；問訊，口頭審訊；接見，會見"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interview</b> is a formal meeting at which someone is asked questions in order to find out if they are suitable for a job or school. 面試","examples":["The interview went well. 面試很順利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>interview</b> is a conversation in which a journalist puts questions to someone such as a famous person or politician. 採訪","examples":["The trouble began when Allan gave an interview to the Chicago Tribune last month. 麻煩開始於艾倫上個月接受《芝加哥論壇報》的採訪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are interviewed</b> for a particular job or school, someone asks you questions about yourself to find out if you are suitable for it. 對…面試","examples":["When Wardell was interviewed, he was impressive, and on that basis, he was hired. 當沃德爾接受面試時，他給人印象深刻，因此他被僱用了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a journalist <b>interviews</b> someone such as a famous person, they ask them a series of questions. 採訪","examples":["I'd interviewed him often in the past. 我過去經常採訪他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When the police <b>interview</b> someone, they ask them questions about a crime that has been committed. 詢問","examples":["The police interviewed the driver, but had no evidence to go on. 警察詢問了司機，但沒有得到繼續調查的證據。"]}]}]},"jeans":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牛仔褲；工裝褲；（Jeans）人名；（英、意）瓊斯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jeans</b> are casual trousers that are usually made of strong cotton cloth called denim. 牛仔褲","examples":["...a young man in jeans and a worn T-shirt. …一個穿著牛仔褲和破舊T恤衫的年輕人。"]}]}]},"jazz":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爵士樂；爵士樂舞蹈（jazz ballet/jazz dance）；毫無意義的話；諸如此類的事情"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"爵士樂的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>演奏爵士樂；<舊>跳爵士舞；使活潑；遊蕩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jazz</b> is a style of music that was invented by African American musicians in the early part of the twentieth century. Jazz music has very strong rhythms and often involves improvisation. 爵士樂","examples":["The club has live jazz on Sundays. 該俱樂部每個星期天都有現場爵士樂演奏。"]}]}]},"jog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"慢跑；輕推，輕撞；（多指緩慢地）顛簸著行進；（上下）顛動；使顛簸"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"慢跑鍛鍊；輕推；平穩的慢速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jog</b>, you run slowly, often as a form of exercise. 慢跑","examples":["I got up early the next morning to jog. 我次日清晨早起去慢跑了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jog</b> is also a noun. 慢跑","examples":["He went for another early morning jog. 他又去晨跑了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"慢跑","examples":["It isn't the walking and jogging that got his weight down. 不是散步和慢跑使他體重下降了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a sharp protruding point in a surface; jag 突出端","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jog</b> something, you push or bump it slightly so that it moves. 輕推; 輕撞","examples":["Avoid jogging the camera. 不要碰攝像機。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>jogs</b> your <b>memory</b>, they cause you to suddenly remember something that you had forgotten. 喚起某人的記憶","examples":["Police have planned a reconstruction of the crime tomorrow in the hope that this will jog the memory of passersby. 警方已計劃明天再現犯罪過程，希望以此喚起過路人的記憶。"]}]}]},"jam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"果醬；堵塞，擁擠；麻煩，困境；<非正式>爵士樂（搖滾樂）即興演奏會；卡住，軋住"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"塞滿，擠滿；卡住，發生故障；壓進，塞入；干擾（無線電或電子訊號）；（電話系統因很多人同時打電話而）癱瘓；擠傷，壓傷；<非正式> 即興表演；（向擊球手）投（內角球）；猛推（身體部位、槓桿等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jam</b> something somewhere, you push or put it there roughly. 胡亂地塞","examples":["Pete jammed his hands into his pockets. 皮特把他的雙手胡亂塞進了他的兜裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a part of a machine <b>jams</b>, or if something <b>jams</b> it, the part becomes fixed in position and is unable to move freely or work properly. 卡住","examples":["The second time he fired his gun jammed. 他開第二槍時，槍卡殼了。","A rope jammed the boat's propeller. 一條繩子卡住了船的推進器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If vehicles <b>jam</b> a road, there are so many of them that they cannot move. (車輛) 堵塞","examples":["Hundreds of departing motorists jammed roads that had been closed during the height of the storm. 數百名要開走的駕車者堵住了在風暴最猛烈時被關閉了的那些公路。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a lot of people <b>jam</b> a place, or <b>jam</b> <b>into</b> a place, they are pressed tightly together so that they can hardly move. 擠滿","examples":["Hundreds of people jammed the boardwalk to watch. 上百人擠在木板道上觀看。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>jam</b> a radio or electronic signal means to interfere with it and prevent it from being received or heard clearly. 干擾 (無線電、電子訊號等)","examples":["They will try to jam the transmissions electronically. 他們會設法用電子手段干擾這些發射。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If callers <b>are jamming</b> telephone lines, there are so many callers that the people answering the telephones find it difficult to deal with them all. 堵塞 (電話線路)","examples":["Hundreds of callers jammed the switchboard for more than an hour. 上百個來電者堵塞了總機一個多小時。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jam</b> is also a noun. 堵塞","examples":["400 trucks may sit in a jam for ten hours waiting to cross the limited number of bridges. 400 輛卡車可能會堵上10個小時才能透過有限的幾座橋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"干擾","examples":["The plane is used for electronic jamming and radar detection. 這架飛機用於進行電子干擾和雷達探測。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Jam</b> is a sweet food consisting of pieces of fruit cooked with a large amount of sugar until it is thickened. It is usually spread on bread. 果醬","examples":["I had two jam sandwiches. 我吃了兩個花生醬果醬三明治。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堵塞了的","examples":["Nearby roads and the dirt track to the beach were jammed with cars. 附近的公路和通往海灘的土路都堵滿了汽車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"擠滿的","examples":["The stadium was jammed and they had to turn away hundreds of disappointed fans. 該體育場擠滿了人，他們不得不謝絕上百名失望的球迷入場。"]}]}]},"kindergarten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幼兒園"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kindergarten</b> is a school or class for children aged 4 to 6 years old. It prepares them to go into the first grade. 幼兒園","examples":["She's in kindergarten now. 她現在在上幼兒園。"]}]}]},"ketchup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"番茄醬，番茄沙司（不可數；亦作 catsup）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ketchup</b> is a thick, cold sauce, usually made from tomatoes, that is sold in bottles. 番茄醬","examples":[]}]}]},"judgement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"意見，判斷，評價（同 judgment）；判斷力，辨別力；審判；判決"}],"sections":[]},"joint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聯合的，共同的，共有的；連帶的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"關節；（一般帶有骨頭的）一大塊肉；（兩個物體或部分的）接合處，接縫；<美，非正式>廉價娛樂場所，下等娛樂場所；<美，非正式>大麻煙卷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……切成帶骨的大塊肉；接合，聯合；使有接頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Joint</b> means shared by or belonging to two or more people. 聯合的; 共同的","examples":["She and Frank had never got around to opening a joint account. 她和弗蘭克還沒能抽出時間開個聯名賬戶。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聯合地; 共同地","examples":["The Port Authority is an agency jointly run by New York and New Jersey. 該港務局是紐約和新澤西共管的機構。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>joint</b> is a part of your body such as your elbow or knee where two bones meet and are able to move together. 關節","examples":["Her joints ache if she exercises. 她的關節一運動就疼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>joint</b> is the place where two things are fastened or joined together. 連線處","examples":["...the joint between the inner and outer panels. …內外嵌板的連線處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a cheap place where people go for some form of entertainment as a <b>joint</b>. 低檔娛樂場所","examples":["They had come to the world's most famous pick-up joint. 他們來到了世界上最有名的聲色場所。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>joint</b> is a cigarette that contains cannabis or marijuana. 大麻煙卷","examples":["He's smoking a joint. 他在吸大麻煙。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something puts someone's <b>nose out of joint</b>, it upsets or offends them because it makes them feel less important or less valued. 使某人價值被貶低","examples":["Barry had his nose put out of joint by Lucy's aloof sophistication. 露西的冷漠世故讓巴里顯得很不重要。"]}]}]},"judgment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"判斷，看法；判斷力，識別力；判決，裁決；報應，天譴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>judgment</b> is an opinion that you have or express after thinking carefully about something. 看法","examples":["In your judgment, what has changed over the past few years? 依你看，過去幾年裡發生了哪些變化？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Judgment</b> is the ability to make sensible guesses about a situation or sensible decisions about what to do. 判斷力","examples":["I respect his judgment and I'll follow any advice he gives me. 我敬重他的判斷力，並將聽從他給我的任何建議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>judgment</b> is a decision made by a judge or by a court of law. 判決","examples":["We are awaiting a judgment from the Supreme Court. 我們正等著最高法院的判決。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>against</b> your <b>better judgment</b>, you believe that it would be more sensible or better not to do it. 明知不可取","examples":["Against our better judgment, we buy the products of manufacturers whose claims seem too good to be true. 明知不可取，我們還是買了那些自我宣傳好得令人難以置信的廠家的產品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pass judgment</b> on someone or something, you give your opinion about it, especially if you are making a criticism. 對…做出評論","examples":["They won't pass judgment on their friends or family. 他們不願評論他們的朋友或家庭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>reserve judgment</b> <b>on</b> something, you refuse to give an opinion about it until you know more about it. 保留看法","examples":["I think I'd have to reserve judgment on whether it'll make any difference until I see some of those key details. 至於它是否會有影響，我想在我看到一些關鍵細節之前我會保留看法。"]}]}]},"kingdom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王國；自然三界之一；（神統治的）天國；管轄範圍，領域；界（生物的五大類別之一）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kingdom</b> is a country or region that is ruled by a king or queen. 王國","examples":["The kingdom's power declined. 王國的勢力衰落了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"All the animals, birds, and insects in the world can be referred to together as the animal <b>kingdom</b>. All the plants can be referred to as the plant <b>kingdom</b>. (動物或植物) 界","examples":["The animal kingdom is full of fine and glorious creatures. 動物界有很多精巧而美妙的生物。"]}]}]},"judge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"法官，審判官；裁判員，評判員；鑑定人，行家；士師（古猶太人領袖稱謂）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"判斷，認為；裁判，評判；估計，估算（數量、距離、尺寸等）；批評，指責；審判，審理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>judge</b> is the person in a court of law who decides how the law should be applied, for example how criminals should be punished. 法官","examples":["The judge adjourned the hearing until next Tuesday. 法官將聽證延至下星期二。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>judge</b> is a person who decides who will be the winner of a competition. 裁判員","examples":["A panel of judges is now selecting the finalists. 裁判組現在正在選拔參加決賽的選手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is a good <b>judge</b> <b>of</b> something, they understand it and can make sensible decisions about it. If someone is a bad <b>judge</b> <b>of</b> something, they cannot do this. 鑑定人","examples":["I'm a pretty good judge of character. 我非常善於判別性格。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>judge</b> something such as a competition, you decide who or what is the winner. 評判","examples":["He was asked to judge a literary competition. 他被邀請評判一場文學競賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>judge</b> something or someone, you form an opinion about them after you have examined the evidence or thought carefully about them. 判斷","examples":["It will take a few more years to judge the impact of these ideas. 還需要再過幾年才能判斷這些思想的影響。","I am ready to judge any book on its merits. 我會根據每本書自身的性質來對其進行評判。","It's for other people to judge how much I have improved. 應當由別人來評判我進步的大小。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>judge</b> something, you guess its amount, size, or value or you guess what it is. 估計","examples":["It is important to judge the weight of your washing load correctly. 正確估計你的待洗衣物的量很重要。","I judged him to be about forty. 我估計他四十歲左右。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>judging by</b>, <b>judging from</b>, or <b>to judge from</b> to introduce the reasons why you believe or think something. 根據…判斷","examples":["Judging by the opinion polls, he seems to be succeeding. 根據民意調查判斷，他似乎穩操勝券。","Judging from the way he laughed as he told it, it was meant to be humorous. 從他講述時笑的方式看來，那是為逗人發笑。"]}]}]},"ladybug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓢蟲，瓢蟲科小型甲蟲的通稱，體半球形，常為紅、黃色並帶黑斑，多以蚜蟲等小型害蟲為食，美國英語常用，英國英語常作 ladybird。"}],"sections":[]},"ladybird":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓢蟲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ladybird</b> is a small round beetle that is red with black spots. 瓢蟲","examples":[]}]}]},"koala":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹袋熊，無尾熊（產於澳大利亞，又名考拉）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>koala</b> or a <b>koala bear</b> is an Australian animal which looks like a small bear with grey fur and lives in trees. 樹袋熊","examples":[]}]}]},"lantern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燈籠，提燈；（燈塔上的）燈室；天窗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lantern</b> is a lamp in a metal frame with glass sides and with a handle on top so you can carry it. 燈籠","examples":[]}]}]},"knowledge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"知識，學問；知道，瞭解；計算機系統儲存的資訊；（與見解相對的）認知"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Knowledge</b> is information and understanding about a subject which a person has, or which all people have. 知識; 學識","examples":["She disclaims any knowledge of her husband's business concerns. 她自稱不知道丈夫生意上的顧慮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>to</b> your <b>knowledge</b> or <b>to the best of</b> your <b>knowledge</b>, you mean that you believe it to be true but it is possible that you do not know all the facts. 據某人所知","examples":["Alec never carried a gun to my knowledge. 亞歷克據我所知從不帶槍。"]}]}]},"lane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鄉間）小路；（用於路名）道，路；車道；（比賽的）跑道，泳道；航道，航線；<美>（保齡球）球道；收銀通道；（電泳）泳道；（尤指漩渦星系中的）暗條；（籃球的）罰球區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lane</b> is a narrow road, especially in the country. (尤指鄉間的) 小路","examples":["...a quiet country lane. …一條安靜的鄉間小路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lane</b> is also used in the names of roads, either in cities or in the country. 用於街路名","examples":["They had a house on Spring Park Lane in East Hampton. 他們曾在東漢普頓的春園路有一幢房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lane</b> is a part of a main road which is marked by the edge of the road and a painted line, or by two painted lines. 車道","examples":["The truck was travelling at 20 mph in the slow lane. 那輛卡車以每小時20英里的速度行駛在慢車道上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"At a swimming pool, athletics track, or bowling alley, a lane is a long narrow section which is separated from other sections, for example by lines or ropes. 泳道; 跑道; 保齡球道","examples":["...after being disqualified for running out of his lane in the 200 metres. …在200米比賽中由於衝出跑道而被取消比賽資格以後。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>lane</b> is a route that is frequently used by aircraft or ships. 航線","examples":["The collision took place in one of the busiest shipping lanes in the world. 撞船事件發生在世界上最繁忙的一條船運航道上。"]}]}]},"lemonade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>檸檬味汽水；檸檬汁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lemonade</b> is a drink that is made from lemons, sugar, and water. 檸檬汽水","examples":["He was pouring ice and lemonade into tall glasses. 他正往高腳杯中倒冰和檸檬汽水。"]}]}]},"lawyer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"律師"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"從事法律工作，當律師；（律師）處理法律事務"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lawyer</b> is a person who is qualified to advise people about the law and represent them in court. 律師","examples":["Prosecution and defence lawyers are expected to deliver closing arguments next week. 原告律師和被告律師下週將要作終結辯論。"]}]}]},"lemon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"檸檬；檸檬汁；檸檬色；檸檬樹（=lemon tree）；<非正式>蹩腳的人（或物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"檸檬色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lemon</b> is a bright yellow fruit with very sour juice. Lemons grow on trees in warm countries. 檸檬","examples":["...a slice of lemon. …一片檸檬。","...oranges, lemons and other citrus fruits. …橘子、檸檬和其他的柑橘屬水果。"]}]}]},"leadership":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"領導，領導地位；領導才能；領導人員，領導層；領先地位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to people who are in control of a group or organization as the <b>leadership</b>. 領導人; 領導層","examples":["He is expected to hold talks with both the Croatian and Slovenian leaderships. 人們希望他能與克羅埃西亞和斯洛維尼亞兩國的領導人舉行會談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>leadership</b> is their position or state of being in control of a group of people. 領導地位","examples":["He praised her leadership during the crisis. 他稱讚了她在危機中的領導作用。"]}]}]},"leopard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豹；豹斑；（紋章）斑豹造型"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>leopard</b> is a type of large, wild cat. Leopards have yellow fur and black spots, and live in Africa and Asia. 豹","examples":[]}]}]},"lap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人坐下時的）大腿面，膝上；（比賽中的）一圈；一段旅程；水流沖刷；重疊部分；折皺；（線繩纏繞）一圈；（研磨機）磨盤；拋光工具；（裙裝）下襬；（馬鞍）翹邊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（水）輕拍，輕打；（動物）舔，舐；領先一圈（或數圈）；使部分重疊；用精研機拋光；欣然接受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something on your <b>lap</b> when you are sitting down, it is on top of your legs and near to your body. (人坐著時的) 大腿部","examples":["She waited quietly with her hands in her lap. 她雙手放在大腿上靜靜地等候。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a race, a competitor completes a <b>lap</b> when they have gone around a course once. (跑道的) 一圈","examples":["...that last lap of the race. …比賽的最後一圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lap</b> of a long journey is one part of it, between two points where you stop. 一段行程","examples":["I had thought we might travel as far as Oak Valley, but we only managed the first lap of the journey. 我原以為我們可以到達橡樹谷，但是我們僅僅完成了行程的第一段。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"輕拍","examples":["The only sound was the lapping of the waves. 惟一的聲音是浪濤的拍打聲。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the act or sound of lapping 拍打; 拍打聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a race, if you <b>lap</b> another competitor, you go past them while they are still on the previous lap. 比…領先一圈","examples":["He then built a 10-bike lead before lapping his first rider on lap 14. 他領先了10輛腳踏車的距離，然後在第14圈又超過了前一個車手一圈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an animal <b>laps</b> a drink, it uses short quick movements of its tongue to take liquid up into its mouth. (動物) 舐食","examples":["It lapped milk from a dish. 它從一個盤子裡舐食牛奶。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When water <b>laps</b> against something such as the shore or the side of a boat, it touches it gently and makes a soft sound. 輕拍","examples":["...the water that lapped against the pillars of the boathouse. …水輕拍著船屋的柱子。","With a rising tide the water was lapping at his chin before rescuers arrived. 在救生員到達之前，上漲的潮水打著了他的下巴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lap up</b> means the same as . 舐食","examples":["She poured some water into a plastic bowl. Faust, her Great Dane, lapped it up with relish. 她往一個塑膠碗裡倒了些水，她的丹麥大狗福斯特津津有味地舐食起來。"]}]}]},"lettuce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生菜，萵苣（一年生或二年生草本植物，葉大而可食，常作蔬菜栽培）；生菜（指萵苣的食用葉片，常生食，多用於製作沙拉）；（美式俚語）錢，紙幣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lettuce</b> is a plant with large green leaves that is the basic ingredient of many salads. 萵苣","examples":[]}]}]},"language":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"語言，語言文字；言語，說話；（某一領域的）全部詞彙，術語；計算機語言；語言風格，措辭；<非正式>粗話，髒話；（使用手勢、動作或聲音的）表達方式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>language</b> is a system of communication which consists of a set of sounds and written symbols which are used by the people of a particular country or region for talking or writing. 語言","examples":["...the English language. …英語。","Students are expected to master a second language. 學生們應該掌握一門第二語言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Language</b> is the use of a system of communication which consists of a set of sounds or written symbols. 語言的使用","examples":["Students examined how children acquire language. 學生們調查了兒童是怎樣學習語言的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the words used in connection with a particular subject as <b>the</b> <b>language</b> <b>of</b> that subject. 專門用語","examples":["...the language of business. …商業用語。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to someone's use of rude words or swearing as <b>bad language</b> when you find it offensive. 粗話","examples":["Television companies tend to censor bad language in feature films. 電視公司往往把故事片中的粗話刪掉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>language</b> of a piece of writing or speech is the style in which it is written or spoken. 語言風格","examples":["...a booklet summarizing it in plain language. …用平實的語言對其進行概述的一本小冊子。","The tone of his language was diplomatic and polite. 他說話的語調既圓滑又有禮貌。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can use <b>language</b> to refer to various means of communication involving recognizable symbols, nonverbal sounds, or actions. 交流語言","examples":["Some sign languages are very sophisticated means of communication. 一些手勢語是非常複雜的交流方式。","...the digital language of computers. …計算機數碼語言。"]}]}]},"knock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"敲，擊；碰撞，碰倒；把……撞擊成（某種狀態）；敲動，打破；打，鑿（洞）；（尤指因故障）發碰撞聲，嘭嘭作響；挑剔，無端指責；踢（球）；<非正式>達到（一定年齡）；（心）怦怦跳，（膝蓋）打哆嗦"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"敲打聲，（尤指）敲門聲；打擊，捶擊，撞擊；<非正式>困難，挫折；（發動機）轟鳴聲；<非正式>批評；<非正式>（尤指單個擊球手的）擊球回合；撞傷，撞壞之處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knock</b> <b>on</b> something such as a door or window, you hit it, usually several times, to attract someone's attention. 敲","examples":["She went directly to Simon's apartment and knocked on the door. 她徑直走到西蒙的住處，敲了敲門。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Knock</b> is also a noun. 敲的聲音","examples":["They heard a knock at the front door. 他們聽到前門有一敲門聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"敲的聲音","examples":["They were wakened by a loud knocking at the door. 他們被一陣很響的敲門聲吵醒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Knock</b> is also a noun. 碰撞","examples":["The bags have tough exterior materials to protect against knocks, rain, and dust. 這些袋子結實的外層材料有防撞、防雨、防塵的作用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone receives a <b>knock</b>, they have an unpleasant experience which prevents them from achieving something or which causes them to change their attitudes or plans. 打擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knock</b> something, you touch or hit it roughly, especially so that it falls or moves. 碰撞","examples":["She accidentally knocked the glass off the shelf. 她無意中把架子上的玻璃杯碰了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>knock</b> someone into a particular position or condition means to hit them very hard so that they fall over or become unconscious. 重擊","examples":["The third wave was so strong it knocked me backwards. 第3個浪頭如此猛烈，把我擊得往後退。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>knock</b> a particular quality or characteristic <b>out of</b> someone means to make them lose it. 使失去","examples":["The school system is designed to knock passion out of people. 學校體制是設計來抹殺人的激情的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>knock</b> something or someone, you criticize them and say unpleasant things about them. 批評; 指責","examples":["I'm not knocking them: if they want to do it, it's up to them. 我不是在說他們的壞話：如果他們打算做這件事，由他們決定。"]}]}]},"length":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長，長度；（持續）時間的長短；（書或檔案等的）篇幅，（電影的）片長；（游泳池的）池長；（馬或船的）自身長度；（行動的）程度；細長的一段（根，條）；（頭髮、衣服等）到身體某部位的長度；手中牌長（多指五張以上某同花牌）；（板球）球距；（母音或音節的）節奏音長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>length</b> of something is the amount that it measures from one end to the other along the longest side. 長度","examples":["It is about a metre in length. 它大約有一米長。","...the length of the fish. …魚的長度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>length</b> of something such as a piece of writing is the amount of writing that is contained in it. 篇幅","examples":["...a book of at least 100 pages in length. …一本至少有100頁篇幅的書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>length</b> of an event, activity, or situation is the period of time from beginning to end for which something lasts or during which something happens. (事件、活動等) 持續時間","examples":["The exact length of each period may vary. 每一時期的確切持續時間可能有所不同。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>length</b> <b>of</b> rope, cloth, wood, or other material is a piece of it that is intended to be used for a particular purpose or that exists in a particular situation. 一段 (繩子、布、木頭等)","examples":["...a 30 feet length of rope. …一段30英尺長的繩子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>length</b> <b>of</b> something is its quality of being long. 長度","examples":["Many have been surprised at the length of time it has taken him to make up his mind. 很多人都為他用這麼長的時間才下定決心感到吃驚。"]}]}]},"lightning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃電；意外的幸運"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"閃電般的，很快的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃電"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lightning</b> is the very bright flashes of light in the sky that happen during thunderstorms. 閃電","examples":["One man died when he was struck by lightning. 一個人遭雷擊身亡。","Another flash of lightning lit up the cave. 又一道閃電照亮了那個洞穴。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lightning</b> describes things that happen very quickly or last for only a short time. 飛快的","examples":["Driving today demands lightning reflexes. 如今駕車需要飛快的反應。"]}]}]},"library":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖書館，藏書樓；（書、鐳射唱片等的）私人收藏；書房，書齋；文庫，系列叢書（鐳射唱片集，成套錄影等）；軟體庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A public <b>library</b> is a building where things such as books, newspapers, videos, and music are kept for people to read, use, or borrow. 圖書館","examples":["...the local library. …當地的圖書館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A private <b>library</b> is a collection of things such as books or music, that is normally only used with the permission of the owner. 收藏品","examples":["The company owns a very diverse library of Arabic music. 公司收藏有多種多樣的阿拉伯音樂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>library</b> is a public building or a room, for example in a school or hospital, where things such as books, newspapers, videos, and music are kept for people to read, use, or borrow. 圖書館; 圖書室","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In some large houses the <b>library</b> is the room where most of the books are kept. 書房","examples":["Guests were rarely entertained in the library. 很少會在書房招待客人。"]}]}]},"lid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（容器的）蓋，蓋子；眼瞼；抑制，隱瞞；（對開支的）控制，封頂；餡餅的硬皮；蒴蓋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……蓋蓋子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lid</b> is the top of a box or other container which can be removed or raised when you want to open the container. 蓋子","examples":["She lifted the lid of the box and displayed the contents. 她把盒蓋掀起，展示了裡邊的東西。"]}]}]},"lick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"舔，舔吃；成功地處理（難題或困境）；揍，打敗；（火焰）燎著，（波浪）輕拍；砍倒，擊倒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"舔；少量，一點；（狠狠的）一擊，一撞；（吉他演奏的歌曲）小過門"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or animals <b>lick</b> something, they move their tongue across its surface. 舔","examples":["She folded up her letter, licking the envelope flap with relish. 她把信折起來，享受地舔著信封蓋。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lick</b> is also a noun. 舔","examples":["It's incredible how long a cat can go without more than a lick of milk or water. 不可思議的是，貓不舔一口奶或一滴水能活這麼久。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lick</b> of something is a small amount of it. 少量","examples":["It could do with a lick of paint to brighten up its premises. 用一點塗料就可以讓房子明亮起來。"]}]}]},"listener":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聽者，認真傾聽的人；聽眾，收聽廣播（或音訊）節目的人；（計算機）事件監聽器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>listener</b> is a person who listens to the radio or to a particular radio programme. 聽眾","examples":["I'm a regular listener to her show. 我是她節目的一名固定聽眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a good <b>listener</b>, you mean that they listen carefully and sympathetically to you when you talk, for example, about your problems. 傾聽者","examples":["Dr. Brian was a good listener. 布賴恩醫生是一位不錯的傾聽者。"]}]}]},"liquid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"液體，液態物；流音"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"液態的，液化的；（資金等）流動的，易變為現金的；流暢自如的，舒展的；明亮的，清澈的；清脆的，流暢的；（市場）活躍的；液態的，液化的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>liquid</b> is a substance which is not solid but which flows and can be poured, for example, water. 液體","examples":["Drink plenty of liquid. 飲用大量液體。","Boil for 20 minutes until the liquid has reduced by half. 煮沸20分鐘直到液體減少一半為止。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>liquid</b> substance is in the form of a liquid rather than being solid or a gas. 液體的","examples":["Wash in warm water with liquid detergent. 用液體清潔劑在溫水中清洗。","The tanker was carrying liquid nitrogen. 油輪那時正在運送液態氮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Liquid</b> assets are the things that a person or company owns which can be quickly turned into cash if necessary. (資金等) 流動的","examples":["The bank had sufficient liquid assets to continue operations. 該銀行擁有足夠的流動資產來繼續運轉。"]}]}]},"loaf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一條，一塊（麵包）；（美味食物切碎壓成塊後烹製成的）糕"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"遊蕩，閒逛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>loaf</b> of bread is bread which has been shaped and baked in one piece. It is usually large enough for more than one person and can be cut into slices. (一) 條 (麵包)","examples":["...a loaf of crusty bread. …一條硬皮面包。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>loaf</b>, you spend time in a lazy way, doing nothing in particular, especially when you should be working. 閒著","examples":["There were always a lot of men loafing in the shop. 總有許多人在商店裡閒逛。"]}]}]},"lover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（非婚的）情人；愛好者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>lover</b> is someone who they are having a sexual relationship with but are not married to. 情人","examples":["Every Thursday she would meet her lover Leon. 每個星期四她都去約會她的情人利昂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are a <b>lover</b> of something such as animals or the arts, you enjoy them very much and take great pleasure in them. 愛好者","examples":["She is a great lover of horses and horse racing. 她非常喜歡馬，並熱衷於賽馬。"]}]}]},"loser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比賽、競爭或鬥爭中的失敗者，輸家（常構成 good loser（輸得起的人）、sore loser（輸不起的人）等搭配）；<非正式>老是失敗的人，一事無成者（多含貶義）；因某項行動或事件而受損者，損失者；遺失者，丟失某物的人；（Loser）人名；（德、捷）洛澤；（英）洛瑟；（法）洛塞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>losers</b> of a game, contest, or struggle are the people who are defeated or beaten. 失敗者","examples":["...the Dallas Cowboys and Buffalo Bills, the winners and losers of this year's Super Bowl. …達拉斯牛仔隊和布法羅比利隊，今年超級盃賽的獲勝者和失敗者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>loser</b>, you have a low opinion of them because you think they are always unsuccessful. 老是失敗的人","examples":["They've only been trained to compete with other men, so a successful woman can make them feel like a real loser. 他們只被訓練與其他的男性競爭，所以一個成功的女性會讓他們覺得自己確實是失敗者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People who are <b>losers</b> as the result of an action or event, are in a worse situation because of it or do not benefit from it. 損失者","examples":["Some of the top business successes of the 1980s became the country's greatest losers in the recession. 20世紀80年代的一些極其成功的商人在該國經濟蕭條時期淪為損失最慘重的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is a <b>good loser</b>, they accept that they have lost a game or contest without complaining. If someone is a <b>bad loser</b>, they hate losing and complain about it. 輸得起的人/輸不起的人","examples":["I'm a great winner and I try to be a good loser. 我贏得起，也要努力做一個輸得起的人。"]}]}]},"link":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"連線；與……有關聯；挽住，鉤住"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（事物間的）聯絡，關係；（交通上的）聯絡；（鏈狀物的）環，節；（超文字）連結；<美>一節香腸；令（長度單位，1令等於1測鏈的百分之一，即7.92英寸）；（行路時照明用）瀝青和麻屑火把"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>link</b> <b>between</b> two things or situations, there is a relationship between them, for example, because one thing causes or affects the other. 關係","examples":["...the link between smoking and lung cancer. …吸菸和肺癌之間的關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>link</b> <b>between</b> two things or places is a physical connection between them. 連線物","examples":["...the railway link between Boston and New York. …波士頓與紐約之間的鐵路連線線。","Drivers ran into a field of weeds at the state border, where no link with the neighbouring state had yet been planned. 司機們闖入了州界處一塊雜草叢生的原野，在那裡還沒有計劃修建連線鄰州的道路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>link</b> between two people, organizations, or places is a friendly or business connection between them. 關係","examples":["Kiev hopes to cement close links with Bonn. 基輔希望鞏固與波恩之間的密切關係。","In 1984 the long link between AC Cars and the Hurlock family was severed. 1984年AC汽車公司與赫洛克家族間的長期關係中斷了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>link</b> to another person or organization is something that allows you to communicate with them or have contact with them. 聯絡","examples":["She was my only link with the past. 她是我和過去的惟一聯絡。","The Red Cross was created to provide a link between soldiers in battle and their families at home. 紅十字會被創立來為前線士兵與其家鄉的親人之間提供聯絡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In computing, a <b>link</b> is a connection between different documents, or between different parts of the same document, using hypertext. 連結","examples":["Available in English, French, German and Italian, it has links to other relevant tourism sites. 它有可供閱讀的英文、法文、德文和義大利文版本，也有通向其它相關旅遊網站的連結。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>link</b> is one of the rings in a chain. (鏈的) 環","examples":["...a chain of heavy gold links. …一串沉重的金鍊環。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"(formerly) a torch used to light dark streets (舊時火把式的)街燈","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>links</b> two things or situations, there is a relationship between them, for example, because one thing causes or affects the other. 使聯絡起來","examples":["The U.N. Security Council has linked any lifting of sanctions to compliance with the ceasefire terms. 聯合國安全理事會將任何制裁的解除與遵守停火條款聯絡起來。","The study further strengthens the evidence linking smoking with early death. 這項研究進一步加強了聯絡吸菸與早亡的證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two places or objects <b>are linked</b> or something <b>links</b> them, there is a physical connection between them. 連線","examples":["...the Rama Road, which links the capital, Managua, with the Caribbean coast. …連線首都馬那瓜與加勒比海岸的拉瑪公路。","Seven miles of track were installed to link the hotel to the golf course. 七英里的軌道被鋪設來連線賓館和高爾夫球場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>link</b> one person or thing to another, you claim that there is a relationship or connection between them. 認為…有關聯","examples":["Criminologist Dr. Ann Jones has linked the crime to social circumstances. 犯罪學家安·瓊斯博士認為這起犯罪與社會環境有關。","They've linked her with various men, including magnate Donald Trump. 他們認為她和多個男人有關係，包括巨頭唐納德·特朗普。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Link</b> is also a verb. 連結","examples":["Certainly, Andreessen didn't think up using hypertext to link Internet documents. 當然，安德森並沒想到用超文字連結網際網路文件。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>link</b> one thing with another, you join them by putting one thing through the other. 將…套在一起","examples":["She linked her arm through his. 她用自己的胳膊挽住他的胳膊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more people <b>link arms</b>, or if one person <b>links arms</b> with another, they stand next to each other, and each person puts their arm around the arm of the person next to them. 挽著胳膊","examples":["It was so slippery that some of the walkers linked arms and proceeded very carefully. 地太滑了，所以一些行人挽著胳膊小心翼翼地前行。"]}]}]},"limit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"限度，限制；極限，限量；（區域的）界限，邊界；（法律允許的機動車駕駛員血液的）最高酒精濃度；（可能行動或結果的）範圍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"限制，限定；制約（某人的發展等）；減少"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>limit</b> is the greatest amount, extent, or degree of something that is possible. 極限","examples":["Her love for him was being tested to its limits. 她對他的愛正在考驗著極限。","There is no limit to how much fresh fruit you can eat in a day. 你一天內能吃多少新鮮水果並無上限。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>limit</b> of a particular kind is the largest or smallest amount of something such as time or money that is allowed because of a rule, law, or decision. 限制","examples":["The three month time limit will be up in mid-June. 3個月的時間限制將於6月中旬到期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>limit</b> of an area is its boundary or edge. 界限","examples":["...the city limits of Baghdad. …巴格達的城市邊界。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>limits</b> <b>of</b> a situation are the facts involved in it which make only some actions or results possible. 範圍","examples":["She has to work within the limits of a fairly tight budget. 她不得不在一個相當緊張的預算範圍內工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>limit</b> something, you prevent it from becoming greater than a particular amount or degree. 限制","examples":["He limited payments on the country's foreign debt. 他限制了國家外債的支付。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>limit</b> <b>yourself</b> to something, or if someone or something <b>limits</b> you, the number of things that you have or do is reduced. 對…作出限制","examples":["Please limit letters to 125 words or less. 請把信函限制到125字或更少的字數內。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is limited</b> <b>to</b> a particular place or group of people, it exists only in that place, or is had or done only by that group. 僅限於 (某地、某團體)","examples":["The protests were not limited to New York. 抗議活動並不僅限於紐約。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"限制的","examples":["The conditions laid down to me were not too limiting. 給我定下的條件沒有太大的限制性。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an area or a place is <b>off limits</b>, you are not allowed to go there. 禁止入內","examples":["A one-mile area around the wreck is still off limits. 沉船周圍一英里的地區仍然禁止入內。"]}]}]},"log":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"原木，圓材；正式記錄，航海日誌；對數；（定期或系統的）觀察記錄；船舶測速儀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"正式記錄；行駛，行進（若干距離或時間）；伐木，砍伐；<美>成功獲得，取得（成就）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>log</b> is a piece of a thick branch or of the trunk of a tree that has been cut so that it can be used for fuel or for making things. 木柴; 原木","examples":["He dumped the logs on the big stone hearth. 他把木柴扔進那個大石爐裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>log</b> is an official written account of what happens each day, for example, on board a ship. 日誌","examples":["The family made an official complaint to a ship's officer, which was recorded in the log. 這家人向一位高階船員提出過正式投訴，此事記入了航行日誌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"logarithm的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>log</b> an event or fact, you record it officially in writing or on a computer. 把…載入日誌","examples":["They log everyone and everything that comes in and out of here. 他們把在這裡出入的人和發生的事都記入日誌。"]}]}]},"local":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"當地的，地方的；區域性的；（汽車或火車）每站都停的，慢的；（計算機）局域的；（食品或飲料）低熱量的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"當地人，本地人；<英>住處附近的酒吧；<美>（工會的）地方分會；慢車，市內公交車；<俚>炒股散戶；本地新聞；區域性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Local</b> means existing in or belonging to the area where you live, or to the area that you are talking about. 本地的; 當地的","examples":["We'd better check on the game in the local paper. 我們最好在本地報紙上查一下這場比賽。","Some local residents joined the students' protest. 一些當地居民加入了學生的抗議活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Local</b> government is elected by people in one area of a country and controls aspects such as education, housing, and transportation within that area. 地方的","examples":["Education comprises two-thirds of all local government spending. 教育經費佔地方政府所有開銷的2/3。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>local</b> anaesthetic or condition affects only a small area of your body. (身體上) 區域性的","examples":["The procedure was done under local anaesthetic in the physician's office. 在醫師診所裡經過區域性麻醉完成了手術。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>locals</b> are local people. 當地居民","examples":["Camping is a great way to meet the locals as the Portuguese themselves are enthusiastic campers. 野營是與當地居民接觸的好途徑，因為葡萄牙人本身就是熱情的露營者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在當地","examples":["We've got cards which are drawn and printed and designed by someone locally. 我們得到了由某人在當地繪製、印刷和設計的紙牌。"]}]}]},"loss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"失去，喪失；虧損；死亡，去世；失落，傷感；（因某人的離去或某物的挪移而造成的）損失；（比賽等的）失敗，失利；戰鬥中死亡（受傷或被俘）計程車兵；減少，降低；（進攻推進不成卻被逼）後退的距離；損耗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Loss</b> is the fact of no longer having something or having less of it than before. 喪失","examples":["...loss of sight. …失明。","...hair loss. …脫髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Loss</b> of life occurs when people die. 死亡","examples":["...a terrible loss of human life. …人員死亡慘重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>loss</b> of a relative or friend is their death. (親人、朋友的) 亡故","examples":["They took the time to talk about the loss of Thomas and how their grief was affecting them. 他們花時間來談論托馬斯的去世以及悲傷給他們帶來的影響。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Loss</b> is the feeling of sadness you experience when someone or something you like is taken away from you. 失落感","examples":["Talk to others about your feelings of loss and grief. 和別人說說你失落和悲傷。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>loss</b> is the disadvantage you suffer when a valuable and useful person or thing leaves or is taken away. 損失","examples":["She said his death was a great loss to herself. 她說他的去世對於她來說是個巨大的損失。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>loss</b> of something such as heat, blood, or fluid is the gradual reduction of it or of its level in a system or in someone's body. (熱量、血液或液體等的) 流失","examples":["...blood loss. …失血。","...a rapid loss of heat from the body. …體內熱量迅速流失。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a business makes a <b>loss</b>, it earns less than it spends. 虧損","examples":["In 1986 Rover made a loss of nine hundred million dollars. 1986年，羅孚集團虧損9億美元。","The company said it will stop producing fertilizer in 1990 because of continued losses. 該公司稱，由於持續虧損而將於1990年停止生產化肥。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a business produces something <b>at a loss</b>, they sell it at a price which is less than it cost them to produce it or buy it. 虧本地","examples":["Timber owners have often produced lumber at a loss and survived these down cycles in demand. 木場主經常賠本生產木料，以便在需求低迷期挺過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>at a loss</b>, you mean that you do not know what to do in a particular situation. 不知所措","examples":["I was at a loss for what to do next. 我不知道下一步該怎麼辦。"]}]}]},"magazine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雜誌，期刊；（電視、廣播）專題節目；彈匣，彈倉；膠捲盒，底片盒；彈藥庫，軍火庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>magazine</b> is a publication with a paper cover which is issued regularly, usually every week or every month, and which contains articles, stories, photographs, and advertisements. 雜誌","examples":["Her face is on the cover of a dozen or more magazines. 她的面孔出現在10多種雜誌的封面上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In an automatic gun, the <b>magazine</b> is the part that contains the bullets. 彈匣","examples":["The corporal ignored him, sliding the empty magazine from his weapon and replacing it with a fresh one. 那個下士沒理睬他，把空彈匣從他的武器上卸下來並換上了一個新的。"]}]}]},"magician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魔術師，變戲法的人；巫師，術士；奇才，能手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>magician</b> is a person who entertains people by doing magic tricks. 魔術師","examples":[]}]}]},"mango":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芒果；芒果樹（=mango tree）；芒果蜂鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mango</b> is a large, sweet, yellowish fruit which grows on a tree in hot areas. 芒果","examples":["Peel, stone, and dice the mango. 把芒果削皮、去核、切成丁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mango</b> is the tree that this fruit grows on. 芒果樹","examples":["...orchards of lime and mango trees. …有酸橙樹和芒果樹的果園。"]}]}]},"lock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鎖住，把……鎖起來；固定，卡住；陷入，捲入（困境、爭論、爭執等）；被緊緊抓住（或抱住）；給（計算機資料）加密；過船閘；<文>對視"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鎖；一縷頭髮；<文>頭髮；船閘；（摔跤中的）抱，夾；<英>前輪轉向角度（=full lock）；（並列爭球的）第二排前鋒（=lock forward）；<美>必定成功的人（或事）（(a lock）；車鎖，制動器；（機器部件等的）鎖定；<美>（對某物的）完全控制；<古>槍栓；（計算機資料的）加密；<古>（交通）堵塞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>lock</b> something such as a door, drawer, or case, you fasten it, usually with a key, so that other people cannot open it. 鎖","examples":["Are you sure you locked the front door? 你確定鎖前門了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lock</b> something or someone in a place, room, or container, you put them there and fasten the lock. 將…鎖起來","examples":["Her maid locked the case in the safe. 她的女僕把那盒子鎖進了保險箱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lock</b> something in a particular position, or if it <b>locks</b> there, it is held or fitted firmly in that position. 鎖定","examples":["He leaned back in the swivel chair and locked his fingers behind his head. 他向後靠在轉椅上，兩手手指交叉鎖定在腦後。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>lock</b> on something such as a door or a drawer is the device which is used to keep it shut and prevent other people from opening it. Locks are opened with a key. 鎖","examples":["At that moment he heard Gill's key turning in the lock of the door. 那時他聽到吉爾的鑰匙在門鎖裡轉動的聲音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"On a canal or river, a <b>lock</b> is a place where walls have been built with gates at each end so that boats can move to a higher or lower section of the canal or river, by gradually changing the water level inside the gates. 水閘","examples":["As the lock filled, the ducklings rejoined their mother to wait for another vessel to go through. 水閘裡注滿水時，小鴨子們回到它們的媽媽身旁等待另一艘船透過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lock</b> <b>of</b> hair is a small bunch of hairs on your head that grow together and curl or curve in the same direction. (一) 綹","examples":["She brushed a lock of hair off his forehead. 她拂開他額頭的一綹頭髮。"]}]}]},"mandarin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高階官員，政界要員；（中文）普通話；（舊時中國的）官吏；柑橘；橘樹；（用作傳統中式服裝飾件的）擺頭人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mandarin</b> is the official language of China. (中國)普通話","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mandarin</b> or a <b>mandarin orange</b> is a small orange whose skin comes off easily. 柑橘","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mandarin</b> was, in former times, an important government official in China. (舊中國的)官員","examples":[]}]}]},"luck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幸運，好運；機遇，運氣；成功"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>湊巧碰上；<美，非正式>靠運氣成功"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Luck</b> or <b>good luck</b> is success or good things that happen to you, that do not come from your own abilities or efforts. 運氣","examples":["I knew I needed a bit of luck to win. 我知道我得靠點運氣才能取勝。","The Sri Lankans have been having no luck with the weather. 斯里蘭卡人一直沒運氣碰上好天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bad luck</b> is lack of success or bad things that happen to you, that have not been caused by yourself or other people. 黴運","examples":["I had a lot of bad luck during the first half of this season. 我在這一季節的前半季遭了很多黴運。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you ask someone the question \"<b>Any luck?</b>\" or \"<b>No luck?</b>,\" you want to know if they have been successful in something they were trying to do. 運氣如何","examples":["\"Any luck?\"—\"No.\" “運氣如何？”— “不好。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Bad luck</b>\" or \"<b>Hard luck</b>\" to someone when you want to express sympathy to them. 運氣不好 (表同情)","examples":["Bad luck, man, just bad luck. 運氣不好，老弟，只是運氣不好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say \"<b>Good luck</b>\" or \"<b>Best of luck</b>\" to someone, you are telling them that you hope they will be successful in something they are trying to do. 祝你好運","examples":["He kissed her on the cheek. \"Best of luck!\" 他吻了一下她的面頰：“祝你好運！”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say someone <b>is in luck</b> when they are in a situation where they can have what they want or need. 交好運","examples":["You're in luck. The doctor's still in. 你運氣不錯，醫生還在。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is out of luck</b>, you mean that they cannot have something which they can normally have. 運氣不佳","examples":["\"What do you want, Roy? If it's money, you're out of luck.\" “你想要什麼，羅伊？如果是錢，你的運氣不怎麼樣。”"]}]}]},"male":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"男性的；（動物）公的，雄性的；只有雄蕊的；全由男性組成的；（工具部件等）凸形的，陽的；男性特有的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"男子，男孩；雄性動物；雄性植物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>male</b> is a man or a boy. 男性的","examples":["Many women achievers appear to pose a threat to their male colleagues. 許多女性成功者似乎對她們的男同事造成一種威脅。","The company has engaged two male dancers from the Bolshoi. 該公司聘了兩名來自波修瓦劇院的男舞蹈演員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Male</b> means relating to, belonging to, or affecting men rather than women. 男性的","examples":["Massive male unemployment has diminished the status of men in the family. 大量男性失業已經降低了男人在家庭中的地位。","...male violence. …男性暴力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Male</b> is also an adjective. 雄性的","examples":["After mating, the male wasps tunnel through the sides of their nursery. 交配後，雄黃蜂們從育蜂室的兩側鑽過。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Men and boys are sometimes referred to as <b>males</b> when they are being considered as a type. 男性","examples":["...the remains of a Caucasian male, aged 65-70. …一個年齡在65至70歲之間的高加索男子的遺骸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to any creature that belongs to the sex that cannot lay eggs or have babies as a <b>male</b>. 雄性","examples":["Males and females take turns brooding the eggs. 雌雄輪流孵卵。"]}]}]},"magic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魔法，法術；魔術，戲法；魅力，魔力；傑出技能，罕見才能"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"魔術的，戲法的；魔法的，魔力的；神奇的，有奇效的；非常好的，令人十分愉快的；重要的，關鍵的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（像）用魔法變出（或使消失、使變成……等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Magic</b> is the power to use supernatural forces to make impossible things happen, such as making people disappear or controlling events in nature. 魔力","examples":["They believe in magic. 他們相信魔力。","...the use of magic to combat any adverse powers or influences. …魔力在抗擊敵對力量或有害影響中的作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>magic</b> when you are referring to an event that is so wonderful, strange, or unexpected that it seems as if supernatural powers have caused it. You can also say that something happens <b>as if by magic</b> or <b>like magic</b>. 魔法","examples":["All this was supposed to work like magic. 這一切應該魔法般地起作用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Magic</b> is the art and skill of performing mysterious tricks to entertain people, for example by making things appear and disappear. 魔術","examples":["His secret hobby: performing magic tricks. 他的秘密嗜好：表演魔術。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to <b>the</b> <b>magic</b> <b>of</b> something, you mean that it has a special mysterious quality which makes it seem wonderful and exciting to you and which makes you feel happy. 魔力; 神秘之處","examples":["It infected them with some of the magic of a lost age. 它使之有了逝去歲月的些許神秘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to a person's <b>magic</b>, you mean a special talent or ability that they have, which you admire or consider very impressive. 特殊才能; 神奇功能","examples":["The 32-year-old Jamaican-born fighter believes he can still regain some of his old magic. 那個32歲、生於牙買加的鬥士相信自己仍能重拾一些昔日的神奇功能。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>magic</b> to describe something that does things, or appears to do things, by magic. 有魔力的","examples":["So it's a magic potion? 這麼說它是一種魔藥？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Magic</b> is also an adjective. 有魔力的; 神秘的","examples":["Then came those magic moments in the rose garden. 接著就是玫瑰園裡的魔力時刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use expressions such as <b>the magic number</b> and <b>the magic word</b> to indicate that a number or word is the one which is significant or desirable in a particular situation. 關鍵的; 嚮往的","examples":["...their quest to gain the magic number of 270 electoral votes on Election Day. …他們渴求在大選日獲得關鍵的270張選票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Magic</b> is used in expressions such as <b>there is no magic formula</b> and <b>there is no magic solution</b> to say that someone will have to make an effort to solve a problem, because it will not solve itself. 有魔力的 (解決方案)","examples":["There is no magic formula for producing winning products. 生產受歡迎的產品並沒有魔方。"]}]}]},"main":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要的，最大的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"總管道，主線路；（電、氣、水的）供應系統（the mains）；<英>電源插座；<古>海洋，公海（the main）；（主桅上的）主帆；（擲骰子游戲中，擲者在投擲前的）叫數（須是5，6，7，8，9中的任何一個數）；鬥雞比賽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>main</b> thing is the most important one of several similar things in a particular situation. 最重要的; 主要的","examples":["...one of the main tourist areas of San Francisco. …舊金山的主要旅遊區之一。","My main concern now is to protect the children. 我現在最關心的是保護這些孩子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>in the main</b>, you mean that it is generally true, although there may be exceptions. 大體上","examples":["Tourists are, in the main, sympathetic people. 遊客們大都是有同情心的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>mains</b> are the pipes which supply gas or water to buildings, or which take sewage away from them. 總管道","examples":["...the water supply from the mains. …總管道的水供應。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a throw of the dice in dice games (骰子游戲的)一擲","examples":[]}]}]},"marriage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結婚，婚姻；婚禮；緊密結合；配對（指伯齊克和其他牌戲中同花色K與Q組合）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>marriage</b> is the relationship between a husband and wife. 婚姻","examples":["In a good marriage, both husband and wife work hard to solve any problems that arise. 在一樁美滿的婚姻中，夫妻雙方共同致力於解決出現的任何問題。","When I was 35 my marriage broke up. 35歲時我的婚姻破裂了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>marriage</b> is the act of marrying someone, or the ceremony at which this is done. 結婚; 婚禮","examples":["I opposed her marriage to Darryl. 我反對她嫁給達里爾。"]}]}]},"manner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"態度，舉止；禮貌；方式；（文學或藝術的）風格；習俗；<正式>種類；（語法）方式狀語，方式副詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>manner</b> in which you do something is the way that you do it. 方式","examples":["She smiled again in a friendly manner. 她又友好地笑了笑。","I'm a professional and I have to conduct myself in a professional manner. 我是專業人士，必須以專業方式行事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>manner</b> is the way in which they behave and talk when they are with other people, for example whether they are polite, confident, or bad-tempered. 舉止","examples":["His manner was self-assured and brusque. 他的舉止自負而且粗魯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone has <b>good manners</b>, they are polite and observe social customs. If someone has <b>bad manners</b>, they are impolite and do not observe these customs. 禮貌","examples":["He dressed well and had impeccable manners. 他穿著得體，舉止無可挑剔。","The manners of many doctors were appalling. 許多醫生很沒禮貌。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"…的態度","examples":["Forrest was normally mild-mannered, affable, and untalkative. 福里斯特通常態度溫和，和藹可親，不善言辭。"]}]}]},"mat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地墊，墊子；團，簇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mat</b> is a small piece of something such as cloth, card, or plastic which you put on a table to protect it from plates or cups. (杯、盤的) 墊子","examples":["The food is served on polished tables with mats. 食物被擺放在擦得光亮的餐桌的墊子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mat</b> is a small piece of carpet or other thick material which is put on the floor for protection, decoration, or comfort. 小地毯; 厚墊子","examples":["There was a letter on the mat. 地毯上有一封信。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to tangle or weave or become tangled or woven into a dense mass 纏結; 使...纏結","examples":[]}]}]},"mask":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"面罩，口罩；防毒面具，呼吸面罩；面膜；假面具，假面；偽裝，掩飾；表情，面容；遮蓋物，遮蔽物；（古希臘和羅馬演員佩戴的）人頭面具；遮光板，遮光片；（製造微電路用）模板；（蜻蜓幼蟲）臉蓋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"掩飾，偽裝，隱瞞；蓋住（氣味、味道、聲音等）；遮蓋；戴面具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mask</b> is a piece of cloth or other material, which you wear over your face so that people cannot see who you are, or so that you look like someone or something else. 面具","examples":["The gunman, whose mask had slipped, fled. 面具滑落的持槍歹徒逃走了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mask</b> is a piece of cloth or other material that you wear over all or part of your face to protect you from germs or harmful substances. 防護面具","examples":["You must wear goggles and a mask that will protect you against the fumes. 你必須帶上護目鏡和防護面具，以保護你不被煙燻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour as a <b>mask</b>, you mean that they do not show their real feelings or character. 偽裝","examples":["His mask of detachment cracked, and she saw for an instant an angry and violent man. 他冷靜超然的偽裝破碎了，她一瞬間看到了一個憤怒而又狂暴的男人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>mask</b> is a thick cream or paste made of various substances, which you spread over your face and leave for some time in order to improve your skin. 面膜","examples":["This mask leaves your complexion feeling soft and supple. 這種面膜使你的皮膚變得柔軟嬌嫩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mask</b> your feelings, you deliberately do not show them in your behaviour, so that people cannot know what you really feel. 掩飾","examples":["Dina lit a cigarette, trying to mask her agitation. 黛娜點燃了一支菸，試圖掩飾她的不安。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>masks</b> another, it prevents people from noticing or recognizing the other thing. 遮掩","examples":["He was squinting through the smoke that masked the enemy. 他眯眼看著遮住敵人的那片煙霧。"]}]}]},"mate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>朋友，夥伴；同伴，同事；配偶，伴侶；配對物，一對中的一個；<英，非正式>（男人之間常用）哥兒們，夥計；<英>助手，下手；（船上的）大副；（美國海軍的）軍士；（國際象棋比賽中的）將死"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）交配；連線，配備；（國際象棋中把對方）將死"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's wife, husband, or sexual partner can be referred to as their <b>mate</b>. 配偶; 性伴侶","examples":["He has found his ideal mate. 他已經找到了理想的配偶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An animal's <b>mate</b> is its sexual partner. 交配物件","examples":["The males guard their mates zealously. 雄性動物熱情地守護它們的交配物件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a friend, usually of the same sex: often used between males in direct address (同性稱呼語，常用於男性間)哥們; 老兄; 老弟; 朋友","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an associate, colleague, fellow sharer, etc 同事; 工友","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals <b>mate</b>, a male and a female have sex in order to produce young. 交配","examples":["This allows the pair to mate properly and stops the hen from staying in the nest. 這可以使這一對正常交配同時也阻止雌禽待在窩裡。","They want the males to mate with wild females. 他們想讓這些雄性動物和野生的雌性動物交配。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to pair (a male and female animal) or (of animals) to pair for reproduction 使成為配偶; 使交配","examples":[]}]}]},"meal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一餐，進餐（時間）；一餐所吃的食物；磨成粗粉的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>meal</b> is an occasion when people sit down and eat, usually at a regular time. 一頓飯","examples":["She sat next to him throughout the meal. 她在這一頓飯的時間裡坐在他旁邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>meal</b> is the food you eat during a meal. (一餐所吃的) 食物","examples":["The waiter offered him red wine or white wine with his meal. 那位侍者為他的餐配了紅葡萄酒或白葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the edible part of a grain or pulse (excluding wheat) ground to a coarse powder, used chiefly as animal food 動物飼料","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>square meal</b>, you have a large, healthy meal. 豐盛的一餐","examples":["The troops are very tired. They haven't had a square meal for four or five days. 這些部隊非常疲憊。他們已經四五天沒有豐盛食物了。"]}]}]},"mass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"團，塊；大量，許多；（常指混亂的）一群，一堆；大量的東西；群眾，平民百姓；大多數，多數；質量；（尤指羅馬天主教的）彌撒；彌撒曲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"民眾的，大量的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）聚集，（使）集結"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mass</b> <b>of</b> things is a large number of them grouped together. 一堆","examples":["On his desk is a mass of books and papers. 在他書桌上有大堆的書和檔案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mass</b> <b>of</b> something is a large amount of it. 許多","examples":["She had a mass of auburn hair. 她有一頭濃密的棕發。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mass</b> <b>of</b> a solid substance, a liquid, or a gas is an amount of it, especially a large amount which has no definite shape. 塊; 團; 堆","examples":["...before it cools and sets into a solid mass. …在它冷卻成為一塊固體之前。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you talk about <b>the masses</b>, you mean the ordinary people in society, in contrast to the leaders or the highly educated people. 普通百姓","examples":["His music is commercial. It is aimed at the masses. 他的音樂很商業化，針對的是一般大眾。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mass</b> <b>of</b> people are most of the people in a country, society, or group. 大多數","examples":["The 1939-45 world war involved the mass of the population. 1939至1945年間的世界大戰捲入了多數民眾。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a</b> <b>mass of</b> things, you mean that it is covered with them or full of them. 充滿","examples":["His body was a mass of sores. 他渾身傷痛。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In physics, the <b>mass</b> of an object is the amount of physical matter that it has. 質量","examples":["Astronomers know that Pluto and Triton have nearly the same size, mass, and density. 天文學家們知道冥王星和海王衛一擁有幾乎相同的體積、質量和密度。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Mass</b> is a Christian church ceremony, especially in a Roman Catholic or Orthodox church, during which people eat bread and drink wine in order to remember the last meal of Jesus Christ. 彌撒","examples":["She attended a convent school and went to Mass each day. 她上了一所女修道院設立的學校，每天都去作彌撒。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Masses</b> <b>of</b> something means a great deal of it. 大量","examples":["There's masses of work for her to do. 她有一大堆的工作去做。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mass</b> is used to describe something which involves or affects a very large number of people. 人數眾多的","examples":["...ideas on combating mass unemployment. …對付失業人數眾多的方法。","All the lights went off, and mass hysteria broke out. 所有的燈都熄滅了，大家變得歇斯底里起來了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or things <b>mass</b>, or when you <b>mass</b> them, they gather together into a large crowd or group. 聚集","examples":["Shortly after the workers went on strike, police began to mass at the shipyard. 工人罷工後不久，警察開始在造船廠集結。"]}]}]},"measurement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常以數字形式呈現的）測量結果；三圍，（身材）尺寸；測量，計量；測量單位，度量制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>measurement</b> is a result, usually expressed in numbers, that you obtain by measuring something. 測量的結果","examples":["We took lots of measurements. 我們得到了許多測量的結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Measurement</b> of something is the process of measuring it in order to obtain a result expressed in numbers. 測量","examples":["Tests include measurement of height, weight, and blood pressure. 檢查包括對身高、體重和血壓的測量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>measurement</b> of the quality, value, or effect of something is the activity of deciding how great it is. 評估","examples":["The measurement of intelligence has been the greatest achievement of twentieth-century scientific psychology. 對智商的評估一直是20世紀科學心理學的最大成就。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>measurements</b> are the size of your waist, chest, hips, and other parts of your body, which you need to know when you are buying clothes. (身體) 尺寸","examples":["I know all her measurements and find it easy to buy stuff she likes. 我知道她所有的身體尺寸，覺得買到她喜歡的東西很容易。"]}]}]},"meaning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"意思，意義，含義；真正重要性，價值；原因"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<舊>意味深長的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"表示……的意思，作……的解釋；意味著；打算，意欲（mean 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>meaning</b> of a word, expression, or gesture is the thing or idea that it refers to or represents and which can be explained using other words. 意思","examples":["I hadn't a clue as to the meaning of \"activism.\" 我對的意思一無所知。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>meaning</b> of what someone says or of something such as a book or film is the thoughts or ideas that are intended to be expressed by it. 含義","examples":["Unsure of the meaning of this remark, Ryle chose to remain silent. 由於對這個評論的含義不確定，賴爾選擇了保持沉默。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an activity or action has <b>meaning</b>, it has a purpose and is worthwhile. 價值","examples":["Art has real meaning when it helps people to understand themselves. 當藝術有助於人們瞭解自身時，才有真正的價值。"]}]}]},"means":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手段，方法；金錢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"意味著；表示……的意思，作……的解釋；打算，意欲（mean 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>means</b> of doing something is a method, instrument, or process which can be used to do it. <b>Means</b> is both the singular and the plural form for this use. 方法; 手段; 過程","examples":["The move is a means to fight crime. 這個行動是打擊犯罪的一種手段。","The army had perfected the use of terror as a means of controlling the population. 軍隊已經能很好地利用恐怖手段來控制這裡的人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the money that someone has as their <b>means</b>. 財富","examples":["...a person of means. …一個富有的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>by means of</b> a particular method, instrument, or process, you do it using that method, instrument, or process. 透過 (方法、手段或過程)","examples":["This is a two-year course taught by means of lectures and seminars. 這是一門透過講座和研討會形式講授的兩年制課程。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>by all means</b>\" to tell someone that you are very willing to allow them to do something. 當然可以","examples":["\"Can I come and have a look at your house?\"—\"Yes, by all means.\" “我能過來看看你的房子嗎？”—“可以，當然可以。”"]}]}]},"medicine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥物，藥劑；醫療，醫學；內科；（北美印第安人等民族所信奉的具有治療或保護效力的）咒語，魔法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用藥物治療，給……用藥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Medicine</b> is the treatment of illness and injuries by doctors and nurses. 醫療","examples":["He pursued a career in medicine. 他從事了醫務工作。","I was interested in alternative medicine and becoming an aromatherapist. 我對替代療法感興趣，想成為一名芳香療法治療師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Medicine</b> is a substance that you drink or swallow in order to cure an illness. 藥","examples":["People in hospitals are dying because of shortages of medicine. 各醫院的病人們因藥物短缺正瀕臨死亡。"]}]}]},"meeting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"會議，集會；偶遇，會面；與會者（the meeting）；<英>運動會，賽馬會；宗教聚會；交鋒，比賽；交匯處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"會面；會合（meet 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>meeting</b> is an event in which a group of people come together to discuss things or make decisions. 會議","examples":["Can we have a meeting to discuss that? 我們可以開個會來討論那件事嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can also refer to the people at a meeting as <b>the meeting</b>. 參會人員","examples":["The meeting decided that further efforts were needed. 與會者認為進一步的努力是需要的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you meet someone, either by chance or by arrangement, you can refer to this event as a <b>meeting</b>. 碰見","examples":["In January, 37 years after our first meeting, I was back in the studio with Dennis. 1月份，在我們初次相遇的37年後，我和丹尼斯一起回到了工作室。"]}]}]},"match":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比賽，競賽；火柴；敵手，旗鼓相當的人；相配的人（或物）；非常相似的東西；婚姻，配偶；適合，匹配"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"比得上，敵得過；使成對，使相配，使相稱；與……一致，與……相符；使較量，使競賽；適應，滿足；等額提供"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>match</b> is an organized game of tennis, football, cricket, or some other sport. 比賽","examples":["He was watching a football match. 他正在看一場英式足球比賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>match</b> is a small wooden stick with a substance on one end that produces a flame when you rub it along the rough side of a matchbox or a matchbook. 火柴","examples":["...a pack of cigarettes and a book of matches. …一包香菸和一包火柴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a combination of things or people is a good <b>match</b>, they have a pleasing effect when placed or used together. 相配的人或物","examples":["Helen's choice of lipstick was a good match for her skin tone. 海倫選擇的唇膏與她的膚色是很好的搭配。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something of a particular colour or design <b>matches</b> another thing, they have the same colour or design, or have a pleasing appearance when they are used together. 和…相配","examples":["\"The shoes are too tight.\"—\"Well, they do match your dress.\" “這雙鞋太緊了。” — “不過，它們確實和你的裙子相配。”","All the chairs matched. 所有的椅子都相配。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as an amount or a quality <b>matches</b> <b>with</b> another amount or quality, they are both the same or equal. If you <b>match</b> two things, you make them the same or equal. 與…一樣; 使一樣","examples":["Their strengths in memory and spatial skills matched. 他們的記憶力和空間技能一樣。","Our value system does not match with their value system. 我們的價值體系與他們的價值體系不一樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>matches</b> another, they are connected or suit each other in some way. 使對應","examples":["The students are asked to match the books with the authors. 學生們被要求把書和作家一一對應起來。","It can take time and effort to match buyers and sellers. 匹配買主和賣主可能需要花費一些時間和精力。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Match up</b> means the same as . 和…相配","examples":["The pillow cover can match up with the sheets. 這個枕巾可以和這些被單相配。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Match up</b> means the same as . 使對應","examples":["The consultant seeks to match up jobless professionals with small companies in need of expertise. 這名顧問力求使失業的專業人員對應需要專門技術的小公司。","They compared the fat intake of groups of vegetarians and meat eaters, and matched their diets up with levels of harmful blood fats. 他們比較了素食者組和肉食者組的脂肪攝入量，並把他們的膳食和血脂危險水平對應起來。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>match</b> something, you are as good as it or equal to it, for example in speed, size, or quality. 比得上","examples":["They played some fine offensive football, but I think we matched them in every department. 他們踢了一些漂亮的攻勢足球，但我認為我們各方面都比得上他們。"]}]}]},"melody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主旋律，曲調；歌，曲子；婉轉，悅耳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>melody</b> is a tune. 旋律","examples":["I whistle melodies from Beethoven and Vivaldi and the more popular classical composers. 我用口哨吹貝多芬、維瓦爾迪和更大眾化一些的古典作曲家的曲子。"]}]}]},"melon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓜，香瓜，甜瓜；瓜類植物；（動）額隆體；圓鼓鼓像瓜似的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>melon</b> is a large fruit which is sweet and juicy inside and has a hard green or yellow skin. 甜瓜","examples":["...some juicy slices of melon. …幾片多汁的甜瓜。"]}]}]},"menu":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選單；飯菜，菜餚；（電腦螢幕上的）選單，功能選擇單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a restaurant or café or at a formal meal, the <b>menu</b> is a list of the meals and drinks that are available. 選單","examples":["A waiter offered him the menu. 一個侍者給他送上了選單。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>menu</b> is the food that you serve at a meal. 飯菜","examples":["Try out the menu on a few friends. 請幾個朋友來嚐嚐這道菜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On a computer screen, a <b>menu</b> is a list of choices. Each choice represents something that you can do using the computer. (電腦螢幕上的) 選單","examples":["Hold down the shift key and press F7 to display the print menu. 按住鍵的同時按下鍵，以顯示列印選單。"]}]}]},"member":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成員，一分子；會員；<英>議員；用於表示榮譽的頭銜（尤指最低階）勳章獲得者；（建築或橋的）構件；（句子）成分；（方程式）端邊；（一組數字）項；（數學集合）元；<舊>身體的一部分（如胳膊或腿）；陰莖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>member</b> of a group is one of the people, animals, or things belonging to that group. (某群體的) 成員","examples":["He refused to name the members of staff involved. 他拒絕說出所涉職員的名字。","Their lack of training could put members of the public at risk. 他們訓練的缺乏會使公眾成員面臨風險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>member</b> of an organization such as a club or a political party is a person who has officially joined the organization. 會員; 成員","examples":["The support of our members is of great importance to the association. 我們會員的支援對協會來說非常重要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>member</b> or <b>Member</b> is a person who has been elected to a legislature or parliament. 議員","examples":["He was elected to Parliament as the Member for Leeds. 他被選入國會作為利茲市的議員。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>member country</b> or <b>member state</b> is one of the countries that has joined an international organization or group. 會員國","examples":["...the member countries of the North American Free Trade Association. …北美自由貿易聯盟的會員國。"]}]}]},"memory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"記憶力，記性；記憶，回憶；（計算機儲存器的）儲存量；（計算機的）儲存器；對死者的記憶；記憶所及的時間（或範圍）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>memory</b> is your ability to remember things. 記憶力","examples":["All the details of the meeting are fresh in my memory. 會議的所有細節我都記憶猶新。","But locals with long memories thought this was fair revenge for the injustice of 1961. 但是記憶力好的當地人認為這是對1961年那起不公正事件的合理報復。","He had a good memory for faces. 他對相貌有很好的記憶力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>memory</b> is something that you remember from the past. 記憶","examples":["She cannot bear to watch the film because of the bad memories it brings back. 由於這部電影勾起的糟糕回憶，她不能忍受觀看它。","Her earliest memory is of singing at the age of four to wounded soldiers. 她最早的記憶是在4歲時為受傷計程車兵唱歌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A computer's <b>memory</b> is the part of the computer where information is stored, especially for a short time before it is transferred to disks or magnetic tapes. 記憶體","examples":["The data are stored in the computer's memory. 這些資料儲存在計算機的記憶體中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>memory</b> of someone who has died, especially someone who was loved or respected, you are referring to the thoughts, actions, and ceremonies by which they are remembered. 懷念","examples":["She remained devoted to his memory. 她依然對他十分懷念。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is taking a walk or trip <b>down memory lane</b>, you mean that they are talking, writing, or thinking about something that happened to them a long time ago. 沿著記憶的軌跡","examples":["His 1998 memoir is a delightful trip down memory lane. 他1998年的回憶錄是一次愉快的懷舊之旅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>from memory</b>, for example speak the words of a poem or play a piece of music, you do it without looking at it, because you know it very well. 憑記憶","examples":["Many members of the church sang from memory. 許多教徒都是憑記憶唱頌歌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is, for example, the best, worst, or first thing of its kind <b>in living memory</b>, you are emphasizing that it is the only thing of that kind that people can remember. 在人們的記憶裡","examples":["The floods are the worst in living memory. 那次洪水在人們的記憶中是最嚴重的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>lose your memory</b>, you forget things that you used to know. 失去記憶","examples":["His illness caused him to lose his memory. 他的病使他失去了記憶。"]}]}]},"mark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痕跡，汙點；標識，記號；印記，特徵；（品質或情感的）標誌，跡象；分數；水平，標準點；（後接數詞）型號；<英>燃氣擋，溫度刻度；（代替簽名的）畫押；目標，靶子；（比賽的）起點；<美>容易受騙的人；（賽馬）附加重量級；（業餘英橄）截球后喊 \"Mark\"射門；馬克（德國貨幣單位，合100芬尼）；馬克（舊時西歐使用的金銀重量單位）；波黑馬克（波斯尼亞和黑塞哥維納基本貨幣單位）；（尤指體育比賽的）最好成績，紀錄"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做記號，做標記；留下痕跡，弄汙；標明方位，標示；分隔，標出（區域）；紀念，慶賀；表明，是……的跡象；成為……的特徵；打分，評成績；注意，留心；盯人防守，盯住（對手）；挑選，指定（mark sb. out for）；認定……為（某一類人）（mark sb. down as）；劃掉，勾銷；（澳橄）接球；（對人或物）造成永久性傷害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mark</b> is a small area of something such as dirt that has accidentally got onto a surface or piece of clothing. 斑點","examples":["The dogs are always rubbing against the wall and making dirty marks. 這些狗總是往牆上蹭，留下了點點汙斑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mark</b> is a written or printed symbol, for example a letter of the alphabet. 記號","examples":["He made marks with a pencil. 他用鉛筆作了記號。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mark</b> is a point that is given for a correct answer or for doing something well in an exam or competition. A <b>mark</b> can also be a written symbol such as a letter that indicates how good a student's or competitor's work or performance is. 分數","examples":["...a simple scoring device of marks out of 10, where \"1\" equates to \"Very poor performance.\" …一個簡單的十分制評分體系，其中1分相當於表現“很差”。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone gets good or high <b>marks</b> for doing something, they have done it well. If they get poor or low <b>marks</b>, they have done it badly. 評價","examples":["You have to give her top marks for moral guts. 你必須給她的道德勇氣最高的評價。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"打分","examples":["For the rest of the lunch break I do my marking. 在剩餘的午休時間，我批改作業。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A particular <b>mark</b> is a particular number, point, or stage which has been reached or might be reached, especially a significant one. (重要的) 指標","examples":["Unemployment is rapidly approaching the one million mark. 失業人數正迅速接近百萬大關。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>mark</b> <b>of</b> something is the characteristic feature that enables you to recognize it. 特徵","examples":["The mark of a civilized society is that it looks after its weakest members. 文明社會的特徵是它關心最弱勢群體。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that a type of behaviour or an event is <b>a</b> <b>mark</b> <b>of</b> a particular quality, feeling, or situation, you mean it shows that that quality, feeling, or situation exists. 表示","examples":["It was a mark of his unfamiliarity with Hollywood that he didn't understand that an agent was paid out of his client's share. 他不知道經紀人的報酬由客戶支付，這就是他對好萊塢並不熟悉的表現。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>marks</b> a surface, or if the surface <b>marks</b>, the surface is damaged by marks or a mark. 玷汙; 留下汙痕","examples":["Leather overshoes were put on the horses' hooves to stop them from marking the turf. 皮套子被套在了馬蹄上，防止它們弄髒了跑馬場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mark</b> something with a particular word or symbol, you write that word or symbol on it. 在…上作記號","examples":["The bank marks the cheque \"certified.\" 銀行在支票上標有“保付”的字樣。","Mark them with a symbol. 用個記號把他們標出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a teacher <b>marks</b> a student's work, the teacher decides how good it is and writes a number or letter on it to indicate this opinion. 打分","examples":["He was marking essays in his small study. 他正在他的小書房裡批閱文章。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>marks</b> a place or position, it shows where something else is or where it used to be. 標明 (位置)","examples":["A huge crater marks the spot where the explosion happened. 一個巨大的彈坑標明瞭爆炸發生的地點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An event that <b>marks</b> a particular stage or point is a sign that something different is about to happen. 標誌 (轉折點)","examples":["The announcement marks the end of an extraordinary period in European history. 這個宣告標誌著歐洲歷史上一個偉大時代的終結。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you do something to <b>mark</b> an event or occasion, you do it to show that you are aware of the importance of the event or occasion. 紀念","examples":["Hundreds of thousands of people took to the streets to mark the occasion. 數十萬人走上了街頭紀念這一時刻。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Something that <b>marks</b> someone <b>as</b> a particular type of person indicates that they are that type of person. 表明 (為某一種類的人)","examples":["Her opposition to abortion and feminism marks her as a convinced traditionalist. 她對墮胎和女權主義的反對錶明她是一個堅定的傳統主義者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>leaves</b> their <b>mark</b> or <b>leaves a mark</b>, they have a lasting effect on another person or thing. 留下深遠的影響","examples":["Years of conditioning had left their mark on her, and she never felt inclined to talk to strange men. 多年的薰陶給她留下了深遠的影響，她從來不願意和陌生男人說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> your <b>mark</b> or <b>make a mark</b>, you become noticed or famous by doing something impressive or unusual. 獲得名望","examples":["She made her mark in the film industry in the 1960s. 20世紀60年代她在電影界頗有名望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a claim or estimate is <b>wide of the mark</b>, it is incorrect or inaccurate. 離譜","examples":["That comparison isn't as wide of the mark as it seems. 那種比較不像看上去那麼離譜。"]}]}]},"metro":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指法國的）地鐵，地鐵系統；大城市"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大都會的，大城市的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>metro</b> is the subway system in some cities, for example in Washington or Paris. 地鐵","examples":["A new metro runs under the square, carrying hundreds of thousands who used to cycle to work. 一條新地鐵在廣場下面執行，載著數以千計過去騎腳踏車上班的人們。"]}]}]},"metal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重金屬音樂；金屬色；築路碎石；玻璃液；（鐵路的）鋼軌；金屬，合金"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用金屬做，用金屬包；<英>用碎石築路，用碎石修路"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"金屬製的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Metal</b> is a hard substance such as iron, steel, gold, or lead. 金屬","examples":["...pieces of furniture in wood, metal, and glass. …用木料、金屬和玻璃製成的一件件傢俱。"]}]}]},"message":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口信，訊息；（書籍、演講等的）要旨，主題思想；（從大腦發給身體某部位或身體某部位向大腦傳送的）資訊；購物；<美>電視廣告；<英>差使；啟示，教訓；（先知的）預言"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指以電子形式）傳送（資訊）；通報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>message</b> is a piece of information or a request that you send to someone or leave for them when you cannot speak to them directly. 留言","examples":["I got a message you were trying to reach me. 我得到了一條留言，說你在設法聯絡我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>message</b> that someone is trying to communicate, for example in a book or play, is the idea or point that they are trying to communicate. 資訊","examples":["The report's message was unequivocal. 報告中傳達的資訊相當明確。","I no longer want to be friends with her but I don't know how to get the message across. 我再也不想和她做朋友了，但我不知道如何告訴她。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>message</b> someone, you send them a message electronically using a computer or another device such as a mobile phone. 發簡訊","examples":["People who message a lot feel unpopular if they don't get many back. 如果傳送許多簡訊的人並未得到很多回復，他們會覺得自己不受歡迎。"]}]}]},"method":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方法，辦法；條理；體驗派表演方法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>method</b> is a particular way of doing something. 方法","examples":["The pill is the most efficient method of birth control. 避孕藥是最有效的節育辦法。"]}]}]},"military":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"軍事的，軍隊的；陸軍的；軍人般的，軍人作風的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"軍人，軍方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Military</b> means relating to the armed forces of a country. 軍事的","examples":["Military action may become necessary. 軍事行動可能會成為必要。","The president is sending in almost 20,000 military personnel to help with the relief efforts. 總統將派遣近20000名軍事人員來協助救援行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Military</b> means well organized, controlled, or neat, in a way that is typical of a soldier. 軍人般的","examples":["Your working day will need to be organized with military precision. 你們的工作日需要以軍人般的精確性來安排。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在軍事上","examples":["They remain unwilling to intervene militarily in what could be an unending war. 他們仍然不願意對一場可能無休止的戰爭進行軍事幹預。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The military</b> are the armed forces of a country, especially officers of high rank. 軍方 (尤指高階軍官)","examples":["The bombing has been far more widespread than the military will admit. 爆炸波及的範圍遠大於軍方願意承認的範圍。"]}]}]},"meter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計量器，儀，表；停車收費器；<美>米；<美>（詩歌的）韻律，格律"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用儀表計量（測量），透過計量器計（價）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>meter</b> is a device that measures and records something such as the amount of gas or electricity that you have used. 表","examples":["He was there to read the electricity meter. 他在那兒讀電錶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>meter</b> is the same as a . 停車收費器","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>meter</b> is the same as a . 同metre","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>meter</b> something such as gas or electricity means to use a meter to measure how much of it people use, usually in order to calculate how much they have to pay. 用表測量","examples":["Only a third of these households thought it reasonable to meter water. 這些使用者中只有1/3認為用水錶計量是合理的。"]}]}]},"million":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"一百萬，一百萬個"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"百萬，百萬個（人或物）；許多，無數；百萬英鎊（或美元）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"許多的，無數的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>million</b> or one <b>million</b> is the number 1,000,000. 百萬","examples":["Up to five million people a year visit the county. 每年多達500萬人到這個縣遊覽。"]}]},{"pos":"quant-plural.","pos_name":"複數型數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about <b>millions of</b> people or things, you mean that there is a very large number of them but you do not know or do not want to say exactly how many. 大量","examples":["The program was viewed on television in millions of homes. 無數的家庭從電視上收看了這個節目。"]}]}]},"mosquito":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蚊子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mosquitos</b> are small flying insects which bite people and animals in order to suck their blood. 蚊子","examples":[]}]}]},"moth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飛蛾，蛾；<非正式>衣蛾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>moth</b> is an insect like a butterfly which usually flies around at night. 蛾","examples":[]}]}]},"mine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我的；<英，非正式>我的家"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"礦，礦井；地雷，水雷；寶庫，源泉；<史>炸藥坑道"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"採（煤等礦物）；佈雷，用雷炸燬（車輛）；尋找（某事物中）蘊含的價值；在（地下）挖洞（或坑道）；挖掘（資料）；挖礦（獲取加密貨幣的勘探方式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mine</b> is the first person singular possessive pronoun. A speaker or writer uses <b>mine</b> to refer to something that belongs or relates to himself or herself. 我的","examples":["Her right hand is inches from mine. 她的右手離我的幾英寸遠。","That wasn't his fault, it was mine. 那不是他的錯，是我的錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mine</b> is a place where deep holes and tunnels are dug under the ground in order to obtain a mineral such as coal, diamonds, or gold. 礦","examples":["...coal mines. …煤礦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a lucrative source or abundant supply 搖錢樹 ; 充足的供應","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>mine</b> is a bomb which is hidden in the ground or in water and which explodes when people or things touch it. 地雷; 水雷","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a mineral such as coal, diamonds, or gold <b>is mined</b>, it is obtained from the ground by digging deep holes and tunnels. 採掘","examples":["The pit is being shut down because it no longer has enough coal that can be mined economically. 那個煤礦要關閉了，因為儲量不足，難以經濟開採。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an area of land or water <b>is mined</b>, mines are placed there which will explode when people or things touch them. 佈雷","examples":["The approaches to the garrison have been heavily mined. 進入駐地的幾條通道都已佈滿了雷。"]}]}]},"minus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"減，減去；<非正式>沒有，缺少；零下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>缺點，不利條件；減號，負號"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小於零的，負的；不利的，負面的；（指分數或等級）略低於某標準的，稍差的；陰性的，負電的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>minus</b> to show that one number or quantity is being subtracted from another. 減","examples":["One minus one is zero. 一減一等於零。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Minus</b> before a number or quantity means that the number or quantity is less than zero. 負的","examples":["The aircraft was subjected to temperatures of minus 65 degrees and plus 120 degrees. 該飛機經受了零下65 度和零上120度的溫度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Teachers use <b>minus</b> in grading work in schools and colleges. \"B minus\" is not as good as \"B,\" but is a better grade than \"C.\" 略低的","examples":["I'm giving him a B minus. 我打算給他一個B-。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>minus</b> something means not to have that thing. 失去","examples":["The film company collapsed, leaving Chris jobless and minus his life savings. 這家電影公司垮了，使克里斯失業了，同時也失去了他的生活積蓄。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>minus</b> is a disadvantage. 不利因素","examples":["The minuses far outweigh that possible gain. 不利因素遠遠超過了那可能獲得的收益。"]}]}]},"monster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"怪獸，怪物；殘忍的人，惡魔；小惡棍，搗蛋鬼；巨大的東西，龐然大物；難以駕馭的人，難以掌控的事物；畸形動物（或植物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很受歡迎的；龐大的，巨大的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"嚴厲批評，斥責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monster</b> is a large imaginary creature that looks very ugly and frightening. 怪物","examples":["Both movies are about a monster in the bedroom cupboard. 兩部電影都是關於臥室櫥櫃裡的一個怪物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>monster</b> is something which is extremely large, especially something that is difficult to manage or which is unpleasant. 龐然大物 (尤指棘手的事物)","examples":["...the monster which is now the Boston marathon. …波士頓馬拉松賽現在成了棘手的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>monster</b>, you mean that they are cruel, frightening, or evil. 惡魔","examples":["Galbraith said that her husband was a depraved monster who threatened and humiliated her. 加爾佈雷思說她丈夫是個沒有人性的惡魔，威脅她並羞辱她。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Monster</b> means extremely and surprisingly large. 龐大的","examples":["...a monster weapon. …一個巨型武器。"]}]}]},"motorcycle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"摩托車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎摩托車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>motorcycle</b> is a vehicle with two wheels and an engine. 摩托車","examples":[]}]}]},"mirror":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鏡子；寫照，真實反映；（計算機）映象網點；榜樣"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"反射，映照；反映；與……十分相似；（計算機）做……的映象；（計算機）在（兩個或數個硬碟）中做備份"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mirror</b> is a flat piece of glass which reflects light, so that when you look at it you can see yourself reflected in it. 鏡子","examples":["He went into the bathroom absent-mindedly and looked at himself in the mirror. 他心不在焉地走進了浴室，照著鏡子看了看自己。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>mirrors</b> something else, it has similar features to it, and therefore seems like a copy or representation of it. 反映","examples":["Despite the fact that I have tried to be objective, the book inevitably mirrors my own interests and experiences. 儘管我曾努力做到客觀，但這本書還是不可避免地反映出了我自己的興趣和經歷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you see something reflected in water, you can say that the water <b>mirrors</b> it. (水) 映出","examples":["...the sudden glitter where a newly flooded field mirrors the sky. …那突然的閃光，使新近被水淹沒的田地映出了天空。"]}]}]},"mule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"騾，騾子；越境運毒者；（室內使用的）拖鞋；雜交動物，雜交植物；走錠紡紗機；（尤指電動的）小型拖拉機，小型電動機車；（正、反兩面的圖案不相配的）錯鑄硬幣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mule</b> is an animal whose parents are a horse and a donkey. 騾","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mule</b> is a shoe or slipper which is open around the heel. 拖鞋式便鞋; 拖鞋","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a person who is paid to transport illegal drugs for a dealer 受僱販運毒品者","examples":[]}]}]},"mix":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）混合，（使）調和；使結合，組合；調製，配製；混合錄音；（尤指與不相熟的人）交往，相處；不合，不相容；<非正式>打起來，爭吵起來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"混合體；（製作糕點、調味汁等的）混合原料，混合配料；（特定社會或團體內）各色人混雜的一群；（人群、混合物的）成分比例；混音，混錄；樂曲組合，連奏；疊化影象，疊化聲音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two substances <b>mix</b> or if you <b>mix</b> one substance <b>with</b> another, you stir or shake them together, or combine them in some other way, so that they become a single substance. 混合","examples":["Oil and water don't mix. 油與水無法混合。","A quick stir will mix them thoroughly. 快速攪拌會使它們完全混合。","Mix the cinnamon with the rest of the sugar. 把肉桂與剩餘的糖混合起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two things or activities do not <b>mix</b>, it is not a good idea to have them or do them together, because the result would be unpleasant or dangerous. 相協調","examples":["Politics and sports don't mix. 政治與體育無法協調一致。","Some of these pills don't mix with drink. 有些藥片不能和酒混飲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>mix</b> <b>with</b> other people, you meet them and talk to them. You can also say that people <b>mix</b>. 交往","examples":["I ventured the idea that the secret of staying young was to mix with older people. 我大膽地提出這樣一個觀點，即保持年輕的秘訣是和比自己年長的人交往。","People are supposed to mix, do you understand? 人們應該多交往，明白嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mix</b> something, you prepare it by mixing other things together. 調製","examples":["He had spent several hours mixing cement. 他用了幾個小時的時間來攪拌水泥。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mix</b> is a powder containing all the substances that you need in order to make something such as a cake or a sauce. When you want to use it, you add liquid. (製作蛋糕或調味汁等的) 混合幹配料","examples":["For speed we used packets of pizza dough mix. 為了趕速度，我們用了幾包做比薩餅的混合麵粉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mix</b> <b>of</b> different things or people is two or more of them together. 混合體","examples":["The story is a magical mix of fantasy and reality. 這個故事是一個幻想與現實的奇妙組合。"]}]}]},"museum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"博物館"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>museum</b> is a building where a large number of interesting and valuable objects, such as works of art or historical items, are kept, studied, and displayed to the public. 博物館","examples":["For months Malcolm had wanted to visit the New York art museums. 馬爾科姆想參觀紐約的藝術博物館有好幾個月了。"]}]}]},"motion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動，移動；手勢，動作；提議，議案；<英>排便，大便；轉動的機械裝置；（當庭提出裁決或命令的）請求，申請"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打手勢，示意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Motion</b> is the activity or process of continually changing position or moving from one place to another. 運動","examples":["...the laws governing light, sound, and motion. …支配光、聲和運動的規律。","One group of muscles sets the next group in motion. 一組肌肉帶動下一組肌肉運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>motion</b> is an action, gesture, or movement. 動作; 手勢","examples":["He made a neat chopping motion with his hand. 他用手做了一個乾淨利落的砍的動作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>motion</b> is a formal proposal or statement in a meeting, debate, or trial, which is discussed and then voted on or decided on. 動議","examples":["The conference is now debating the motion and will vote on it shortly. 大會現在正在討論這個動議，並將馬上就此投票。","Opposition parties are likely to bring a no-confidence motion against the government. 反對黨可能會對政府提出一項不信任議案。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>motion</b> to someone, you move your hand or head as a way of telling them to do something or telling them where to go. (用手勢或頭) 示意","examples":["She motioned for the locked front doors to be opened. 她打手勢示意把鎖著的前門開啟。","He stood aside and motioned Don to the door. 他站在一邊，示意唐到門口。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is going through the motions</b>, you think they are only saying or doing something because it is expected of them without being interested, enthusiastic, or sympathetic. 敷衍了事","examples":["\"You really don't care, do you?\" she said quietly. \"You're just going through the motions.\" “你真的不在意，是嗎？”她平靜地說。“你只是在敷衍了事。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a process or event is <b>in motion</b>, it is happening. If it is set <b>in motion</b>, it is happening or beginning to happen. 在進行中","examples":["The current chain of events was set in motion by that kidnapping. 目前的一系列事件都是由那次綁架引發的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>sets the wheels in motion</b>, they take the necessary action to make something start happening. 開動","examples":["I have set the wheels in motion to sell their Arizona ranch. 我已著手出售他們在亞利桑那州的大農場。"]}]}]},"model":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模型；模式；（機器等的）型號；模範，典型；模特兒；樣本，範例；（小說中人物或地點的）原型；（著名設計師設計的）款式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（為藝術家）當模特兒；模特兒展示（服裝）；（用黏土、木頭等）做……的模型，塑造；（用計算機）做出（情景、事件）的模型；使仿效，使模仿"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"模範的，榜樣的；模型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>model</b> of an object is a physical representation that shows what it looks like or how it works. The model is often smaller than the object it represents. 模型","examples":["...an architect's model of a wooden house. …一名建築師的木屋模型。","I made a model out of paper and glue. 我用紙和膠水做了一個模型。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>model</b> is a system that is being used and that people might want to copy in order to achieve similar results. 模式","examples":["...the Chinese model of economic reform. …中國經濟改革的模式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>model</b> of a system or process is a theoretical description that can help you understand how the system or process works, or how it might work. 理論模式","examples":["Darwin eventually put forward a model of biological evolution. 達爾文最終提出了一套生物進化的理論模式。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>a</b> <b>model</b> <b>of</b> a particular quality, you are showing approval of them because they have that quality to a large degree. 典範","examples":["A model of good manners, he has conquered any inward fury. 作為禮貌行為的典範，他已經克服了內心的狂怒情緒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A particular <b>model</b> of a machine is a particular version of it. 型號","examples":["To keep the cost down, opt for a basic model. 為了降低成本，就選擇一個基本型號吧。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An artist's <b>model</b> is a person who stays still in a particular position so that the artist can make a picture or sculpture of them. (藝術家據以繪畫或雕塑的) 模特兒","examples":["...the model for his portrait of Mary Magdalene, the Marchesa Attavanti. …他繪製瑪麗·馬格達萊妮，即阿塔凡蒂侯爵夫人肖像畫的模特兒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A fashion <b>model</b> is a person whose job is to display clothes by wearing them. (時裝) 模特兒","examples":["...Paris's top fashion model. …巴黎的頂級時裝模特兒。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"當模特兒","examples":["She was being offered a modelling contract. 她得到一份當模特兒的合同。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Model</b> is also an adjective. 模型的","examples":["...a model railway. …一個鐵路模型。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>model</b> to express approval of someone when you think that they perform their role or duties extremely well. 模範的","examples":["As a girl she had been a model student. 還是女孩的時候她一直是模範學生。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone such as a scientist <b>models</b> a system or process, they make an accurate theoretical description of it in order to understand or explain how it works. 建立…的理論模式","examples":["I have moved from trying to model and understand the distribution and evolution of water vapour. 我已經不再試圖構建和理解水汽的分佈和演變的理論模式了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>is modelled</b> <b>on</b> another, the first thing is made so that it is like the second thing in some way. 使仿造","examples":["The quota system was modelled on those operated in America and continental Europe. 配額制是仿照美國和歐洲大陸所施行的那些制度制定出來的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>model</b> yourself <b>on</b> someone, you copy the way that they do things, because you admire them and want to be like them. 以…為榜樣","examples":["You have been modelling yourself on others all your life. 你一輩子都在以別人為榜樣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>models</b> clothes, they display them by wearing them. 當模特兒展示 (服裝); 當時裝模特兒","examples":["She began modelling in Paris at age 15. 她15歲就開始在巴黎當時裝模特兒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>model</b> shapes or figures, you make them out of a substance such as clay or wood. (用黏土或木頭等) 塑造; 做模型","examples":["There she began to model in clay. 她開始在那兒用黏土做模型。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>models</b> for an artist, they stay still in a particular position so that the artist can make a picture or sculpture of them. 當模特兒","examples":["Tullio has been modelling for Sandra for eleven years. 圖利奧已經為桑德拉當了11年的模特兒。"]}]}]},"necklace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"項鍊；（主要指南非的）火項鍊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（主要指南非）用火項鍊處決（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>necklace</b> is a piece of jewellery such as a chain or a string of beads which someone, usually a woman, wears around their neck. 項鍊","examples":["...a diamond necklace and matching earrings. …一條鑽石項鍊和與之相配的耳環。"]}]}]},"musician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"音樂家，樂師，作曲家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>musician</b> is a person who plays a musical instrument as their job or hobby. 音樂家; 音樂演奏者","examples":["He was a brilliant musician. 他曾是一位出色的音樂家。"]}]}]},"napkin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餐巾紙；<英，舊> 尿布；衛生巾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>napkin</b> is a square of cloth or paper that you use when you are eating to protect your clothes, or to wipe your mouth or hands. 餐巾; 餐巾紙","examples":["...taking tiny bites of a hot dog and daintily wiping my lips with a napkin. …小口咬著熱狗並用餐巾文雅地擦著我的嘴唇。"]}]}]},"nail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"釘子；指甲，趾甲；（一些軟喙鳥類）上喙的硬甲殼；納爾（布匹長度單位）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用釘子）釘住，釘牢；抓住，證明……有罪；戳穿，揭露；（尤指體育運動中）獲得，贏得；（選手）鎖定（勝局）；<非正式>用力擊打；<美，非正式>完美地完成，漂亮地做；(棒球)（外場手）把（跑壘者）殺出局；<美>（選手）擊敗（或智勝）（對手）；<美，俚>（男性）與……性交；（外場手）把（跑壘者）殺出局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nail</b> is a thin piece of metal with one pointed end and one flat end. You hit the flat end with a hammer in order to push the nail into something such as a wall. 釘子","examples":["A mirror hung on a nail above the sink. 鏡子掛在水池上方的一枚釘子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>nails</b> are the thin hard parts that grow at the ends of your fingers and toes. 指甲; 趾甲","examples":["Keep your nails short and your hands clean. 指甲要短，保持雙手清潔。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nail</b> something somewhere, you fasten it there using one or more nails. (用釘子) 釘住","examples":["Frank put the first plank down and nailed it in place. 弗蘭克放下第一塊木板，把它釘到位。","They nail shut the front door. 他們將前門釘死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>nail</b> someone means to catch them and prove that they have been breaking the law. 逮住並證明…犯法","examples":["The prosecution still managed to nail him for robberies at the homes of leading industrialists. 原告律師仍設法證明他因在知名實業家的家中搶劫而犯法。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has hit the nail on the head</b>, you think they are exactly right about something. 正中要害","examples":["\"I think it would civilize people a bit more if they had decent conditions.\"—\"I think you've hit the nail on the head.\" “我認為如果人們有好的條件，就會使其更有教養一點。”—“我想你說到點子上了。”"]}]}]},"needle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"縫衣針；編織針；注射針；（針灸療法用的）刺針；唱針；（儀器上的）指標；針葉；<英，非正式>（尤指競爭所引發的）針鋒相對，敵意；氣針；（蝕刻中的）刻針；撞針；尖巖，尖頂；撐木；方尖塔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"刺激，（尤指）不斷地數落；用針穿刺（某物），像針一樣地刺（某物）；用針縫；縫紉，做針線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>needle</b> is a small, very thin piece of polished metal which is used for sewing. It has a sharp point at one end and a hole in the other for a thread to go through. 針","examples":["He took a needle and thread and sewed it up. 他取來一根針和線並把它縫起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>needle</b> is a thin hollow metal rod with a sharp point, which is part of a medical instrument called a syringe. It is used to put a drug into someone's body, or to take blood out. 注射針","examples":["...the transmission of the AIDS virus through dirty needles. …愛滋病病毒透過不潔注射針頭的傳播。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Knitting <b>needles</b> are thin sticks that are used for knitting. They are usually made of plastic or metal and have a point at one end. (編織) 針","examples":["...a pair of knitting needles. …一副編織針。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>needle</b> is a thin metal rod with a point which is put into a patient's body during acupuncture. (針灸用的) 銀針","examples":["I gave Kevin a course of acupuncture using six needles strategically placed on the scalp. 我給凱文進行了一個療程的針灸治療，把6支銀針分別紮在頭皮的關鍵穴位上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"On an instrument which measures something such as speed or weight, the <b>needle</b> is the long strip of metal or plastic on the dial that moves backward and forward, showing the measurement. (儀表上的) 指標","examples":["She kept looking at the dial on the boiler. The needle had reached 250 degrees. 她一直看著鍋爐上的刻度盤，指標已經到達250度。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>needles</b> of a fir or pine tree are its thin, hard, pointed leaves. (杉樹、松樹等的) 針葉","examples":["The carpet of pine needles was soft underfoot. 松針鋪成的地毯在腳下軟軟的。"]}]}]},"nephew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"侄子，外甥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>nephew</b> is the son of their sister or brother. 侄子; 外甥","examples":["I am planning a 25th birthday party for my nephew. 我正在為侄子籌劃他25歲的生日聚會。"]}]}]},"neighbor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鄰居，鄰人，鄰舍；鄰國等鄰近的人或物；（Neighbor）人名，音譯內伯"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鄰近的，相鄰的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（及物）鄰接；（不及物）住在附近，毗鄰而居；<舊，罕見>與……友好相處"}],"sections":[]},"niece":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外甥女，侄女"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>niece</b> is the daughter of their sister or brother. 侄女; 外甥女","examples":["...his niece, the daughter of his eldest sister. …他的外甥女，他大姐的女兒。"]}]}]},"nobody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"沒有人（=no one）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"小人物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"否定不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nobody</b> means not a single person, or not a single member of a particular group or set. 沒有人","examples":["They were shut away in a little room where nobody could overhear. 他們躲在一個小屋子裡，沒有人能偷聽得到。","Nobody realizes how bad things are. 沒人意識到事情有多麼糟糕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone says that a person is a <b>nobody</b>, they are saying in an unkind way that the person is not at all important. 無名之輩","examples":["A man in my position has nothing to fear from a nobody like you. 在我這樣職位的一個男人沒什麼好怕像你這樣一個無名之輩的。"]}]}]},"nest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"窩，巢，穴；舒適的居所，安樂窩；（套疊的）一套物件，一組物件；藏匿處，秘密窩點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鳥類）築巢，做窩；（一套物件）逐個套疊；巢狀（資訊）；找鳥巢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A bird's <b>nest</b> is the home that it makes to lay its eggs in. (鳥類的) 巢","examples":["I can see an eagle's nest on the rocks. 我能看到岩石上的一個鷹巢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>nest</b> is a home that a group of insects or other creatures make in order to live in and give birth to their young in. (昆蟲或其他動物的) 巢穴","examples":["Some solitary bees make their nests in burrows in the soil. 一些獨居的蜜蜂將它們的巢築在土壤中的洞穴裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a bird <b>nests</b> somewhere, it builds a nest and settles there to lay its eggs. 築巢","examples":["Some species may nest in close proximity to each other. 一些鳥類可能彼此緊挨著築巢。"]}]}]},"noodle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵條；<非正式>笨蛋，蠢人；<非正式>人頭，腦袋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>（隨意地）撥弄樂器；<美，非正式>（隨意地）思考，醞釀；<澳，非正式>搜尋（蛋白石等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Noodles</b> are long, thin strips of pasta. They are used especially in Chinese and Italian cooking. 麵條","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to improvise aimlessly on a musical instrument 即興彈奏","examples":[]}]}]},"notebook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"筆記本；膝上型電腦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>notebook</b> is a small book for writing notes in. 筆記本","examples":["He brought out a notebook and pen from his pocket. 他從口袋裡掏出了一個筆記本和一支鋼筆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>notebook</b> computer is a small personal computer. 筆記本 (電腦)","examples":["...a range of notebook computers which allows all your important information to travel safely with you. …使你的所有重要資訊和你一起安全旅行的一系列膝上型電腦。"]}]}]},"nod":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打盹，打瞌睡；上下晃動；（足球中）頂（球）；一時疏忽；點頭，點頭示意"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"點頭，點頭同意；被選中，得到許可；打盹；擺動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nod</b>, you move your head downward and upward to show that you are answering \"yes\" to a question, or to show agreement, understanding, or approval. 點頭","examples":["\"Are you okay?\" I asked. She nodded and smiled. “你還好吧？”我問道。她點點頭笑了。","Jacques tasted one and nodded his approval. 雅克品嚐了一個並點頭表示讚許。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>nod</b>, you bend your head once, as a way of saying hello or goodbye. 點頭 (以示打招呼或告別)","examples":["All the girls nodded and said \"Hi.\" 所有女孩們都點頭說:“你好。”","Both of them smiled and nodded at friends. 他們兩個都微笑著朝朋友們點了點頭。","Tom nodded a greeting. 湯姆點頭打了個招呼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nod</b> is also a noun. 點頭","examples":["She gave a nod and said, \"I see.\" 她點了一下頭說：“我明白了。”","\"Probably,\" agreed Hunter, with a slow nod of his head. “可能，”亨特慢慢點了一下頭贊同地說道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nod</b> in a particular direction, you bend your head once in that direction in order to indicate something or to give someone a signal. (朝某方向) 點頭示意","examples":["\"Does it work?\" he asked, nodding at the piano. “它能彈嗎？”他問道，點頭指向那架鋼琴。","She nodded toward the dining room. \"He's in there.\" 她朝餐廳點了點頭說：“他在那裡面。”"]}]}]},"negative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有害的，負面的；悲觀的，消極的；否定的，拒絕的；否定式的；（結果）陰性的；負極的，陰極的；負的，小於零的；虧損的；負像的，底片的；（天文）負的；<英>（立法）自動生效的；Rh陰性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"底片，負片；否定詞，否定句；壞處，害處；陰性結果；（邏）（對命題的）否定；負電；負數"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拒絕，否定；推翻，證偽；消除，抵消"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A fact, situation, or experience that is <b>negative</b> is unpleasant, depressing, or harmful. 負面的; 消極的","examples":["The news from overseas is overwhelmingly negative. 來自海外的訊息完全不容樂觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>negative</b> or has a <b>negative</b> attitude, they consider only the bad aspects of a situation, rather than the good ones. 消極的; 持否定態度的","examples":["When asked for your views about your current job, on no account must you be negative about it. 當被問及你對自己目前工作的看法時，你無論如何都不能持否定態度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>negative</b> reply or decision indicates the answer \"no.\" 否定的","examples":["Dr. Velayati gave a vague but negative response. 韋拉亞提醫生做出了一個含糊但否定的答覆。","Upon a negative decision, the applicant loses the protection offered by Belgian law. 一旦得到否定裁決，申請人就失去了比利時法律所給予的保護。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>negative</b> clause contains a word such as \"not,\" \"never,\" or \"no one.\" (語法中) 含否定詞的","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a medical test or scientific test is <b>negative</b>, it shows no evidence of the medical condition or substance that you are looking for. (醫檢、試驗等) 呈陰性的","examples":["So far 57 have taken the test and all have been negative. 到目前為止已有57人進行了這項檢驗，所有人都呈陰性反應。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>negative</b> charge or current has the same electrical charge as an electron. (電荷或電流) 負極的","examples":["Stimulate the injury or site of greatest pain with a small negative current. 用一股微弱的負電流刺激傷處或最疼的地方。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>negative</b> number, quantity, or measurement is less than zero. 負數的","examples":["Difficult texts record a positive score and simple ones score negative numbers. 難度大的文字標為正值，簡單的文字標為負值。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"負面地","examples":["This will negatively affect the result over the first half of the year. 這將會給前半年的結果帶來負面影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"消極地","examples":["A few weeks later he said that maybe he viewed all his relationships rather negatively. 幾個星期後，他說或許他把自己和他人的各種關係看得太消極了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"否定地","examples":["Sixty percent of people answered negatively. 60%的人做出了否定回答。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"帶負電荷地","examples":["As these electrons are negatively charged they will attempt to repel each other. 由於這些電子都帶負電荷，它們會相互排斥。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>negative</b> is a word, expression, or gesture that means \"no\" or \"not.\" 否定詞; 表示否定的動作或姿態","examples":["In the past we have heard only negatives when it came to following a healthy diet. 過去一談到遵循健康飲食我們就只聽到否定的意見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In photography, a <b>negative</b> is an image that shows dark areas as light and light areas as dark. Negatives are made from camera film, and are used to print photographs. 底片","examples":["...negatives of Diana's wedding dress. …戴安娜婚紗照的底片。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an answer is <b>in the negative</b>, it is \"no\" or means \"no.\" (回答等) 否定的","examples":["The Council answered those questions in the negative. 理事會對那些問題做出了否定回答。"]}]}]},"novel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（長篇）小說"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"新穎的，珍奇的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>novel</b> is a long written story about imaginary people and events. 長篇小說","examples":["...a novel by Herman Hesse. …一部赫爾曼·赫西寫的長篇小說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a new decree or an amendment to an existing statute 新法; 附律","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Novel</b> things are new and different from anything that has been done, experienced, or made before. 新奇的","examples":["Protesters found a novel way of demonstrating against steeply rising oil prices. 抗議者們找到一種新奇的示威方式來反對石油價格的飆升。"]}]}]},"net":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網，網狀物；因特網；球網，球門網；廣播網，通訊網；安全網；捕魚總量；淨賺，純利；（板球）練球場；（板球）一次練球；網眼織物；陷阱；候選人的選擇面"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淨得的；淨重的；最後的，最終的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"淨賺，淨得；設法獲得，巧妙地做；（用網）捕捉；（籃球或足球）得分，進（球）；用網覆蓋；（計算時）扣除……（以得出淨額）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"淨賺地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Net</b> is a kind of cloth that you can see through. It is made of fine threads woven together so that there are small equal spaces between them. 網","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>net</b> is a piece of netting which is used as a protective covering for something, for example to protect vegetables from birds. (保護性的) 網罩","examples":["I threw aside my mosquito net, jumped out of bed and drew up the blind. 我撩開蚊帳，跳下床，拉開百葉窗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>net</b> is a piece of netting which is used for catching fish, insects, or animals. (用於捕獵的) 羅網","examples":["Several fishermen sat on wooden barrels, tending their nets. 幾個漁民坐在木桶上修補他們的魚網。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The Net</b> is the same as the . 網際網路","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>net</b> a fish or other animal, you catch it in a net. 捕撈","examples":["I'm quite happy to net a fish and then let it go. 我特別喜歡撈到一條魚後再把它放了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>net</b> something, you manage to get it, especially by using skill. (尤指運用技巧) 獲取","examples":["Two fourth-quarter drives netted a grand total of 21 yards. 第4節的兩次擊球總計獲得了21碼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>net</b> a particular amount of money, you gain it as profit after all expenses have been paid. 淨賺","examples":["He netted profit of $1.85 billion from three large sales of stock. 他透過3大筆股票銷售，淨賺了18.5億美元。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>net</b> amount is one which remains when everything that should be subtracted from it has been subtracted. 淨數的","examples":["...a rise in sales and net profit. …銷售和純利潤的增長。","What you actually receive is net of deductions. 你實際上得到的是淨扣除額。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>net</b> weight of something is its weight without its container or the material that has been used to wrap it. (重量) 淨的","examples":["...350 mg net weight. …淨重350毫克。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>net</b> result is a final result after all the details have been considered or included. 最終的 (結果)","examples":["There has been a net gain in jobs in our country. 我們國家的工作機會最終還是增多了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Net</b> is also an adverb. 淨數地","examples":["Balances of $5,000 and above will earn 11 percent gross, 8.25 percent net. 賬戶餘額為$5000或以上時，會獲得11%的毛利息，8.25%的淨利息。","They pay him around $2 million net. 他們淨付給他約兩百萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a company or organization 公司; 組織","examples":[]}]}]},"nut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"堅果（仁）；螺母，螺帽；<非正式>瘋子，怪人；<非正式>入迷的人，狂熱分子；<英>頭，頭腦；<非正式>營運經費，開銷；難事，難題，難對付的人；<非正式>睪丸；（尤指煤的）塊，團；（小提琴或類似樂器琴弓末端的）鬆緊螺絲；（絃樂器上的）琴馬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>用頭撞；<古>採堅果，採乾果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The firm shelled fruit of some trees and bushes are called <b>nuts</b>. Some nuts can be eaten. 堅果","examples":["Nuts and seeds are good sources of vitamin E. 堅果和種子是維生素E的良好來源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>nut</b> is a thick metal ring which you screw onto a metal rod called a bolt. Nuts and bolts are used to hold things such as pieces of machinery together. 螺母","examples":["If you want to repair the wheels you just undo the four nuts. 如果你要修理輪子，只擰下那4個螺母就行了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as, for example, a baseball <b>nut</b> or a health <b>nut</b>, you mean that they are extremely enthusiastic about the thing mentioned. 狂熱者","examples":["...Annie, the girlfriend who was a true baseball nut. …女朋友安妮，一個十足的棒球迷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>nuts</b> <b>about</b> something or someone, you like them very much. 狂熱於…的","examples":["They're nuts about the car. 他們酷愛那輛車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone goes <b>nuts</b> or is <b>nuts</b>, you mean that they go crazy or are very foolish. 發瘋的; 愚蠢的","examples":["You guys are nuts. 你們這些傢伙瘋了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>goes nuts</b>, they become extremely angry. 大發雷霆","examples":["My father would go nuts if he saw bruises on me. 要是我父親看見我身上的淤傷，他會大發雷霆的。"]}]}]},"onion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洋蔥，洋蔥頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>onion</b> is a round vegetable with a light brown skin. It has many white layers on its inside which have a strong, sharp smell and taste. 洋蔥","examples":["You grind the onion and the raw cranberries together. 你把洋蔥和新鮮越橘一起磨碎。"]}]}]},"object":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"物體，實物；目的，目標；賓語；（引發某種情感或行為的）物件；客體；（計算機）物件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"反對；反對說，反對的理由是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>object</b> is anything that has a fixed shape or form, that you can touch or see, and that is not alive. 物體","examples":["He squinted his eyes as though he were studying an object on the horizon. 他眯著眼睛，好像在研究地平線上的某個物體。","...an object the shape of a coconut. …一個椰子狀的物體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>object</b> of what someone is doing is their aim or purpose. 目的","examples":["The object of the exercise is to raise money for the charity. 此項活動的目的是為慈善籌款。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>object of</b> a particular feeling or reaction is the person or thing it is directed toward or that causes it. (某情感或反應的) 物件","examples":["The object of her hatred was 24-year-old model Ros French. 她憎恨的物件是24歲的模特羅斯·弗倫奇。","The object of great interest at the temple was a large marble tower built in memory of Buddha. 那廟裡使人極感興趣的東西是一座為紀念佛陀而修建的大理石巨塔。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In grammar, the <b>object</b> of a verb or a preposition is the word or phrase which completes the structure begun by the verb or preposition. 賓語","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>object</b> to something, you express your dislike or disapproval of it. 反對","examples":["A lot of people will object to the book. 很多人會反對這本書。","Cullen objected that his small staff would be unable to handle the added work. 卡倫反對說，他職員少，將無法應付增多的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that <b>money is no object</b> or <b>distance is no object</b>, you are emphasizing that you are willing or able to spend as much money as necessary or travel whatever distance is required. …不成問題","examples":["This was a very impressive programme in which money seems to have been no object. 這是一項頗具影響的計劃，錢似乎從來不成問題。"]}]}]},"overpass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>立交橋，天橋（同 flyover）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕>超過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>overpass</b> is a structure which carries one road over the top of another one. 高架橋","examples":["...a £16 million motorway overpass over Route 1. …一座跨越一號線的耗資1600萬美元的公路高架橋。"]}]}]},"official":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正式的，官方的，官方授權的；公務的，公職的；據官方的，公開宣稱的（但可能並非事實）；官方場合的，（常指）正式公開的；被正式選用的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"官員，高階職員；（體育比賽中的）執法人，裁判員；<英>（大主教法庭，主教法庭或會吏總法庭的）主持法官"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Official</b> means approved by the government or by someone in authority. 官方的; 正式的","examples":["According to the official figures, over one thousand people died during the revolution. 根據官方數字，有一千多人在革命中喪命。","An official announcement is expected in the next few days. 一份官方宣告預計會在接下來的幾天內發表。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Official</b> activities are carried out by a person in authority as part of their job. 公務的","examples":["The president is in Brazil for an official two-day visit. 總統正在巴西進行為期兩天的正式訪問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Official</b> things are used by a person in authority as part of their job. 官員的","examples":["...the official residence of the head of state. …國家元首的官邸。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone's explanation or reason for something as the <b>official</b> explanation, you are suggesting that it is probably not true, but is used because the real explanation is embarrassing. 對外宣稱的","examples":["They realized that the official explanation left facts unexplained. 他們意識到那個對外宣稱的解釋沒有對事實做出解釋。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"正式地","examples":["The election results have still not been officially announced. 選舉結果仍未正式宣佈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"對外宣稱地","examples":["Officially, the guard was to protect us. In fact, they were there to report on our movements. 據宣稱，警衛是來保護我們的。實際上，他們是來監視我們的行動的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>official</b> is a person who holds a position of authority in an organization. 官員","examples":["A senior UN official hopes to visit Baghdad this month. 聯合國一位高階官員希望本月訪問巴格達。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>official</b> at a sports event is a referee, umpire, or other person who checks that the players follow the rules. 裁判","examples":["Officials suspended the game because of safety concerns. 出於安全考慮，裁判暫停了那場比賽。"]}]}]},"owl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鴞，貓頭鷹；<非正式>夜貓子（喜歡熬夜的人）（=night owl）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>owl</b> is a bird with a flat face, large eyes, and a small sharp beak. Most owls obtain their food by hunting small animals at night. 貓頭鷹","examples":[]}]}]},"oven":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烤爐，烤箱；小熔爐，小窯；（納粹集中營的）火化室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oven</b> is a device for cooking that is like a box with a door. You heat it and cook food inside it. 烤箱","examples":["Put the onions and ginger in the oven and let them roast for thirty minutes. 把洋蔥與生薑放入烤箱中烤30分鐘。"]}]}]},"organ":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人體或動植物的）器官；陰莖，陽物；風琴，管風琴；<正式>  （官方的）機構，機關；<正式>機關報刊，宣傳工具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>organ</b> is a part of your body that has a particular purpose or function, for example, your heart or lungs. 器官","examples":["...damage to the muscles and internal organs. …對肌肉和內臟的損傷。","...the reproductive organs. …生殖器官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>organ</b> is a large musical instrument with pipes of different lengths through which air is forced. It has keys and pedals like a piano. 風琴; 管風琴","examples":["...the church organ. …教堂管風琴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You refer to a newspaper or organization as <b>the</b> <b>organ</b> <b>of</b> the government or another group when it is used by them as a means of giving information or getting things done. (政府、集團的) 新聞媒體","examples":["The publication is the official organ of the American Association for Cancer Research. 該出版物是美國癌症研究協會的官方報刊。"]}]}]},"organization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組織，機構；組織工作，籌備工作；編排，配置，結構；條理，邏輯性；機化（醫學術語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>organization</b> is an official group of people, for example, a political party, a business, a charity, or a club. 組織 (指團體機構等)","examples":["Most of the food for the homeless is provided by voluntary organizations. 給無家可歸者的大部分食物是由志願組織提供的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>organization</b> of an event or activity involves making all the necessary arrangements for it. (活動的) 組織","examples":["...the exceptional attention to detail that goes into the organization of this event. …對此項活動組織細節的格外關注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>organization</b> <b>of</b> something is the way in which its different parts are arranged or relate to each other. 結構","examples":["I am aware that the organization of the book leaves something to be desired. 我知道這本書的結構還有待完善。"]}]}]},"opinion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"意見，看法；（群體的）觀點，信仰；專家意見，專業意見；（對某人的）評價，印象；（法官或法院說明判決理由的）判決意見書"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>opinion</b> about something is what you think or believe about it. 看法","examples":["I wasn't asking for your opinion, Mike. 我不是在問你的看法，邁克。","He held the opinion that a government should think before introducing a tax. 他的看法是政府在推行一項稅制前應先作考慮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>opinion</b> <b>of</b> someone is your judgment of their character or ability. 評價","examples":["That improved Mrs. Goole's already favourable opinion of him. 那更提高了古爾太太對他原有的好評。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the beliefs or views that people have as <b>opinion</b>. 輿論","examples":["Some, I suppose, might even be in positions to influence opinion. 我認為，有些甚至可以影響輿論。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>opinion</b> from an expert is the advice or judgment that they give you in the subject that they know a lot about. (專家的) 意見","examples":["Even if you have had a regular physical check-up recently, you should still seek a medical opinion. 即使你最近已經進行了常規體檢，也還是應該聽聽醫學專家的意見。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You add expressions such as \"<b>in my opinion</b>\" or \"<b>in their opinion</b>\" to a statement in order to indicate that it is what you or someone else thinks, and is not necessarily a fact. 據…的意見","examples":["The book is, in Henry's opinion, the best book on the subject. 在亨利看來，這本書是關於這個學科最好的一本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>of the opinion</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, that is what they believe. 持…觀點","examples":["Frank is of the opinion that Romero should have won. 弗蘭克認為，羅梅羅本來應該獲勝的。"]}]}]},"owner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"所有人，物主"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are the <b>owner</b> of something, it belongs to you. 所有者","examples":["The owner of the shop was sweeping his floor when I walked in. 我走進去的時候店主正在掃地。"]}]}]},"ox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"去勢公牛，閹牛；牛（指大的母牛或公牛）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ox</b> is a bull that has been castrated. Oxen are used in some countries for pulling vehicles or carrying things. 閹公牛","examples":[]}]}]},"offer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供，給予；提議，表示願意（做某事）；出（價），開（價）；提出，作出；表示（愛、友誼等）；（向上帝或神）奉獻（祈禱、讚美），祭獻（犧牲）； 試圖（使用暴力，進行抵抗）；<古>發動，挑起（戰爭）；把……擺好（或放到位）（以便檢測或評估其外觀或狀況）；<舊>（機會）出現；求婚"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"主動提議，提供； 出價，報價； （商品的）特價，特惠；求婚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>offer</b> something to someone, you ask them if they would like to have it or use it. 提供 (某物給某人)","examples":["He has offered seats at the conference table to the Russian leader and the president of Kazakhstan. 他已給俄羅斯領導人和哈薩克總統提供了大會席位。","The number of companies offering them work increased. 給他們提供工作的公司的數量增多了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>offer</b> <b>to</b> do something, you say that you are willing to do it. 表示願意 (做某事)","examples":["Peter offered to teach them water-skiing. 彼得表示願意教他們滑水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>offer</b> someone information, advice, or praise, you give it to them, usually because you feel that they need it or deserve it. 提供 (資訊、忠告等); 給予 (表揚等)","examples":["They manage a company offering advice on mergers and acquisitions. 他們經營一家公司，為併購和收購提供諮詢。","She offered him emotional and practical support in countless ways. 她以無數種方式給予他情感支援和實際支援。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>offer</b> someone something such as love or friendship, you show them that you feel that way toward them. 表示 (愛、友誼等)","examples":["The president has offered his sympathy to the Georgian people. 總統已對喬治亞人民表示了同情。","It must be better to be able to offer them love and security. 能給他們愛心和安全感肯定會更好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If people <b>offer</b> prayers, praise, or a sacrifice to God or a god, they speak to or give something to their god. (向上帝或神) 奉上 (祈禱、讚美、祭品等)","examples":["Church leaders offered prayers and condemned the bloodshed. 教會領袖們奉上祈禱並譴責了那次流血事件。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If an organization <b>offers</b> something such as a service or product, it provides it. 提供 (服務、產品等)","examples":["We have been successful because we are offering a quality service. 我們一直是成功的，因為我們在提供優質服務。","The grocery shop is offering customers 5 cents for each shopping bag re-used. 該雜貨店為顧客重複使用每個購物袋給5美分。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>offer</b> a particular amount of money for something, you say that you will pay that much to buy it. 出價 (某數量的錢)","examples":["He is in a position to offer $825,000 for the bankrupt airline's assets. 他能為這家破產航空公司的資產出價82.5萬美元。","They are offering farmers $2.15 a bushel for corn. 他們給農民們出每蒲式爾$2.15的價購買玉米。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>offer</b> is something that someone says they will give you or do for you. 提議; 提供物","examples":["The offer of talks with Moscow marks a significant change from the previous Western position. 與莫斯科會談的提議標誌著先前西方立場的一個重大轉變。","\"I ought to reconsider her offer to move in,\" he mused. “我應該重新考慮她搬進來的提議，”他若有所思地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>offer</b> in a shop is a specially low price for a specific product or something extra that you get if you buy a certain product. (商店提供的) 特價; 贈品","examples":["This month's offers include a pork loin and avocados. 這個月的特價品包括豬後臀肉和鱷梨。","Today's special offer gives you a choice of three destinations. 今天的特惠為您提供3個可選目的地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>offer</b> is the amount of money that someone says they will pay to buy something. 出價","examples":["The real estate agents say no one else will make me an offer. 各房產中介說別人都不會給我出價了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Offer up</b> means the same as . 同(offer)","examples":["He should consider offering up a prayer to St. Lambert. 他該考慮向聖·蘭伯特奉上祈禱。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have</b> something <b>to offer</b>, you have a quality or ability that makes you important, attractive, or useful. 有某種重要的品質或能力","examples":["In your free time, explore all that this incredible city has to offer. 閒暇時,探索一下這座美妙城市的所有奇妙之處吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is something <b>on offer</b>, it is available to be used or bought. (某物) 在供","examples":["They are making trips to check out the merchandise on offer. 他們奔波各地，檢查供售商品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>open to offers</b>, you are willing to do something if someone will pay you an amount of money that you think is reasonable. 願考慮買主的出價","examples":["It seems that while the Dodgers are eager to have him, he is still open to offers. 似乎道奇隊很想要他，而他仍在考慮其他隊的出價。"]}]}]},"painter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"畫家；油漆匠；系船索，纜索；美洲豹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>painter</b> is an artist who paints pictures. 畫家","examples":["...the French painter Claude Monet. …法國畫家克勞德·莫奈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>painter</b> is someone who paints walls, doors, and some other parts of buildings as their job. 油漆工","examples":["...the son of a painter and decorator. …一個油漆工兼裝修工的兒子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a line attached to the bow of a boat for tying it up 船頭上系船的繩子","examples":[]}]}]},"painting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（一幅）畫，繪畫作品；繪畫創作，繪畫；粉刷，上油漆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……上油漆（或塗料）；（用顏料）繪，畫；往（指甲、嘴唇等上）施化妝品（paint 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>painting</b> is a picture that someone has painted. 畫作","examples":["...a large painting of Dwight Eisenhower. …一幅巨大的德懷特·艾森豪威爾的畫像。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Painting</b> is the activity of painting pictures. 繪畫","examples":["...two hobbies she really enjoyed, painting and gardening. …她真正樂此不疲的兩個愛好：繪畫和園藝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Painting</b> is the activity of painting doors, walls, and some other parts of buildings. 刷油漆","examples":["...painting and decorating. …刷漆和裝修。"]}]}]},"pajamas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常用複數）睡衣，睡衣褲；（舊時或某些東方地區穿的）寬鬆長褲"}],"sections":[]},"papaya":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"番木瓜，木瓜；番木瓜樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>papaya</b> is a fruit with a green skin, sweet orange flesh, and small black seeds. Papayas grow on trees in hot countries. 木瓜","examples":[]}]}]},"package":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"包裹；<美>（包裝食物等的）盒，包；（建議或提供的想法或服務的）一套，一攬子；包價（旅遊）；成套出售的東西，套餐；軟體包"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……打包，把……裝箱（以便出售）；包裝（產品或想法等）；配套銷售（商品）；承攬圖書（尤指插圖多的圖書）的約稿和印製並整體打包出售給出版商"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>package</b> is something wrapped in paper, in a bag or large envelope, or in a box, usually so that it can be sent to someone by mail. 包裹","examples":["I tore open the package. 我撕開了那個包裹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>package</b> is a small container in which a quantity of something is sold. Packages are either small boxes made of thin cardboard, or bags or envelopes made of paper or plastic. 小包","examples":["...a package of doughnuts. …一包炸面圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>package</b> is a set of proposals that are made by a government or organization and that must be accepted or rejected as a group. 一攬子建議","examples":["...a package of measures to help the film industry. …一攬子幫助電影業的措施。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>package</b> tour is a holiday in which your travel and your accommodations are booked for you. 包價 (旅遊)","examples":["...package tours to Egypt. …去埃及的包價旅遊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a product <b>is packaged</b>, it is put into containers to be sold. 包裝 (產品)","examples":["The beans are then ground and packaged for sale as ground coffee. 咖啡豆接著被磨碎、包裝，以研磨咖啡銷售。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is packaged</b> in a particular way, it is presented or advertised in that way in order to make it seem attractive or interesting. (為使某物吸引人而) 包裝","examples":["A city is like any product, it has to be packaged properly to be attractive to the consumer. 一座城市就像任何產品一樣，需要適當地加以包裝來吸引消費者。"]}]}]},"panda":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熊貓，大熊貓，貓熊；小熊貓（red panda），紅熊貓；Panda（人名）潘達（印、塞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>panda</b> or a <b>giant panda</b> is a large animal like a bear that has black and white fur and lives in the bamboo forests of China. 大熊貓","examples":[]}]}]},"pain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疼痛，傷痛；苦惱，悲痛；<非正式>討厭的人（或事）（=pain in the neck）；努力，苦心（pains）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>使痛苦，使苦惱；<正式>使疼痛；<美>（身體某一部分）感到疼痛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pain</b> is the feeling of great discomfort you have, for example, when you have been hurt or when you are ill. 疼痛","examples":["...back pain. …背痛。","To help ease the pain, heat can be applied to the area with a hot water bottle. 可以用一個熱水瓶在疼痛部位熱敷來緩解疼痛。","I felt a sharp pain in my lower back. 我感到背的下部一陣劇痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pain</b> is the feeling of unhappiness that you have when something unpleasant or upsetting happens. 痛苦","examples":["...grey eyes that seemed filled with pain. …似乎充滿了痛苦的灰色眼睛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in pain</b>, you feel pain in a part of your body because you are injured or ill. 感到疼痛","examples":["She was writhing in pain, bathed in perspiration. 她正痛得扭動著，大汗淋漓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In informal English, if you call someone or something <b>a pain</b> or <b>a pain in the neck</b>, you mean that they are very annoying or irritating. Expressions such as <b>a pain in the arse</b> are also used, but most people consider them offensive. 討厭鬼; 煩心事","examples":["Getting rid of unwanted applications from your PC can be a real pain. 從你的個人電腦上刪除不需要的應用程式可以是一件很煩人的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>take pains</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>go to great pains</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try hard to do it, because you think it is important to do it. 下苦功","examples":["He took great pains to see that he got it right. 他下了很大的功夫以確保他弄對了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a fact or idea <b>pains</b> you, it makes you feel upset and disappointed. 使痛苦; 使苦惱","examples":["This public acknowledgment of Ted's disability pained my mother. 特德殘疾的公開使我母親感到痛苦。"]}]}]},"pan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平底鍋；一鍋的量；<美> 烤盤，盤狀器皿；（天平的）秤盤；（淘金用的）淘選盤；煉鍋；<英> 馬桶；鋼鼓（主要為演奏者用語）；土磐，磐層；窪地，曬鹽池；（舊式槍的）火藥池；搖攝動作；<美，非正式> 臉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"移動拍攝，搖攝；用淘金盤淘洗，淘金；<非正式> 嚴厲批評（書、電影、戲劇等）；在淺鍋中烹調（食物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pan</b> is a round metal container with a long handle, that is used for cooking things in, usually on top of a stove. 平底鍋","examples":["Heat the butter and oil in a large pan. 在一個大平底鍋里加熱黃油和食用油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the act of panning 搖攝","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(<b>as modifier</b>) 搖攝","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the leaf of the betel tree 檳榔葉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a film or a book <b>is panned</b> by journalists, they say it is very bad. 抨擊; 批評","examples":["His first high-budget film, called \"Brain Donors,\" was panned by the critics. 他的第一部巨資電影名為《撞板三舞男》，遭到了批評家們的抨擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pan</b> a film or television camera or if it <b>pans</b> somewhere, it moves slowly around so that a wide area is filmed. 使 (攝像機) 搖攝; 搖攝","examples":["The camera panned along the line of players. 攝像機沿著球員們的佇列搖攝。","A television camera panned the stadium. 一臺電視攝像機搖攝體育場。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to wash (gravel) in a pan to separate particles of (valuable minerals) from it 淘(貴金屬)","examples":[]}]}]},"palm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手掌，手心；（手套的）掌部；（制帆工用的）護掌；棕櫚樹；（作為獎賞或勝利象徵的）棕櫚葉；鹿角的扁平部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……藏在手中（尤指玩戲法）；（籃球）持球犯規；用手擋（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>palm</b> or a <b>palm tree</b> is a tree that grows in hot countries. It has long leaves growing at the top, and no branches. 棕櫚樹","examples":["...golden sands and swaying palms. …金色的沙灘和搖曳的棕櫚樹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>palm</b> <b>of</b> your hand is the inside part of your hand, between your fingers and your wrist. 手掌","examples":["Dornberg slapped the table with the palm of his hand. 多恩伯格用他的手掌拍了一下桌子。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to conceal in or about the hand, as in sleight-of-hand tricks 把···藏在手中","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have someone or something <b>in the palm of</b> your <b>hand</b>, you have control over them. 在 (某人的) 掌控之中","examples":["Johnson thought he had the board of directors in the palm of his hand. 約翰遜以為他已把董事會控制在他的掌中。"]}]}]},"parrot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鸚鵡；學舌者，機械模仿別人的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"機械地模仿，鸚鵡學舌般重複"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>parrot</b> is a tropical bird with a curved beak and brightly-coloured or grey feathers. Parrots can be kept as pets. Some parrots are able to copy what people say. 鸚鵡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you disapprove of the fact that someone is just repeating what someone else has said, often without really understanding it, you can say that they <b>are parroting</b> it. 鸚鵡學舌般地重複","examples":["Generations of students have learned to parrot the standard explanations. 一屆又一屆的學生學會了鸚鵡學舌般地重複標準的解釋。"]}]}]},"passenger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乘客，旅客；（團體中）不幹活的人，閒散人員"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"乘客的，旅客的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>passenger</b> in a vehicle such as a bus, boat, or plane is a person who is travelling in it, but who is not driving it or working on it. 乘客","examples":["Mr. Fullemann was a passenger in the car when it crashed. 汽車撞毀時，富勒曼先生是這輛車裡的一名乘客。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Passenger</b> is used to describe something that is designed for passengers, rather than for drivers or freight. 旅客的","examples":["I sat in the passenger seat. 我坐在旅客座位上。"]}]}]},"pardon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"赦免；寬恕，原諒；（中世紀歐洲出售的）贖罪券，赦罪符"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"赦免；寬恕，原諒；免除（債務）；請原諒（表示禮貌，用於所問或所說的話有可能被認為無禮時）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（用於請求別人重複某事）什麼，請再說一遍；對不起，不好意思（發出不雅聲音之後的道歉用語）；你說什麼？（表示驚訝或者受到冒犯）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>Pardon?</b>, <b>I beg your pardon?</b>, or <b>Pardon me?</b> when you want someone to repeat what they have just said because you have not heard or understood it. (表示沒有聽見或不明白，請求重說一遍) 對不起","examples":["\"Will you let me open it?\"—\"Pardon?\"—\"Can I open it?\" “讓我來開啟它，好嗎？”——“對不起，你說什麼？”——“我能開啟它嗎？”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People say \"<b>I beg your pardon?</b>\" when they are surprised or offended by something that someone has just said. (表示驚訝或者受了冒犯) 什麼","examples":["\"Would you get undressed, please?\"—\"I beg your pardon?\"—\"Will you get undressed?\" “請你脫下衣服，好嗎？” —“什麼？”—“你能脫下衣服嗎？”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say \"<b>I beg your pardon</b>\" as a way of apologizing for accidentally doing something wrong, such as disturbing someone or making a mistake. 對不起","examples":["I beg your pardon. I thought you were someone else. 對不起，我把你當成別人了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>Pardon me</b>\" instead of \"Excuse me\" when they want to politely get someone's attention or interrupt them. 對不起 (以引起注意或者打斷一下)","examples":["Pardon me, are you finished, madam? 對不起，您好了嗎，太太？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who has been found guilty of a crime <b>is pardoned</b>, they are officially allowed to go free and are not punished. 赦免","examples":["Hundreds of political prisoners were pardoned and released. 許多政治犯被赦免和釋放了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pardon</b> is also a noun. 赦免","examples":["They lobbied the government on his behalf and he was granted a presidential pardon. 他們為他遊說政府，他因之得到了總統特赦。"]}]}]},"paste":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵糊，糊狀物；糨糊； 肉（或魚等）醬（作塗抹料或烹飪用）；（製作人造寶石用的）鉛質玻璃；（製陶、瓷器用的）溼黏土"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指用漿糊）黏，貼；（在計算機上螢幕上）貼上（文字、圖片等）；<非正式> 狠狠地打，徹底打敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Paste</b> is a soft, wet, sticky mixture of a substance and a liquid, that can be spread easily. Some types of paste are used to stick things together. 麵糰; 糨糊","examples":["Blend a little milk with the custard powder to form a paste. 用蛋奶粉和一點牛奶混合成一個麵糰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Paste</b> is a soft smooth mixture made of crushed meat, fruit, or vegetables. You can, for example, spread it onto bread or use it in cooking. 醬","examples":["...tomato paste. …番茄醬。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>paste</b> something on a surface, you put glue or paste on it and stick it on the surface. (用膠水或糨糊) 貼上","examples":["...pasting labels on bottles. …在瓶子上貼標籤。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hit, esp with the fists; punch or beat soundly (尤指用拳頭)重擊; 重重地敲打","examples":[]}]}]},"partner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（跳舞、玩遊戲等的）搭檔，同伴；（合夥企業的）合夥人；（生意、組織或國家的）夥伴；配偶，（同居的）伴侶，情人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成為搭檔，合夥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>partner</b> is the person you are married to or are having a romantic or sexual relationship with. 配偶; 情人; 性伴侶","examples":["Wanting other friends doesn't mean you don't love your partner. 需要其他朋友並不意味著你不愛你的伴侶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>partner</b> is the person you are doing something with, for example, dancing with or playing with in a game against two other people. 搭檔","examples":["...to dance with a partner. …與一名搭檔跳舞。","Her partner for the game was Venus Williams. 她的比賽搭擋是維納斯•威廉姆斯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>partners</b> in a firm or business are the people who share the ownership of it. 合夥人","examples":["He's a partner in a Chicago law firm. 他是芝加哥一家律師事務所的合夥人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>partner</b> of a country or organization is another country or organization with which they work or do business. 盟友","examples":["Spain has been one of Cuba's major trading partners. 西班牙一直是古巴的主要貿易伙伴之一。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>partner</b> someone, you are their partner in a game or in a dance. 與…搭擋","examples":["He had partnered the famous Russian ballerina. 他曾與著名的俄羅斯芭蕾舞女演員搭擋。","He will be partnered by Ian Baker, the defending champion. 他將與衛冕冠軍伊恩•貝克搭檔。"]}]}]},"pack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（把……）打包，收拾（行李）；包裝，裝箱；（用柔軟材料）把……裹（包）起來；在（容器中的食物）上覆蓋物質（以防止腐爛）；可摺疊運輸（或存放）；擠進，塞滿；聚集；把……蓋上，填封；把……大量放進，裝滿；（把……）壓實，（使）堆積；在（委員會或會議）中安插（支持者、利己的人或事物）；<非正式>具有，能產生（強大之物或能量）；<美，非正式>攜帶（武器）；（橄欖球）形成對陣爭球"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"包，包裹，捆；（尤指士兵或野外徒步者的）揹包；（一般為紙質的）小盒，小包；一副紙牌；（一起生活獵食的）獸群（尤指狼群）；（尤指不受人喜歡的）一幫，一夥；（比賽或競賽中的）叢集，集團；（放在傷口上止血或消腫的）裹布，敷料；（美容用的）面膜，貼膜；一隊（男或女幼童軍）；（軍事交通工具，尤指飛機或潛水艇的）一組，一隊；（英橄）全體前鋒；（極地海洋中的）流冰群，浮冰群"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>pack</b> a bag, you put clothes and other things into it, because you are leaving a place or going on holiday. 打點 (行裝)","examples":["When I was 17, I packed my bags and left home. 在我17歲的時候，打起行囊離開了家。","I began to pack a few things for the trip. 我開始為旅行收拾些東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>pack</b> things, for example, in a factory, they put them into containers or boxes so that they can be shipped and sold. 包裝; 把…裝箱","examples":["They offered me a job packing boxes in a warehouse. 他們為我提供了一份在倉庫裝箱的工作。","Machines now exist to pack olives in jars. 現在有可以把橄欖裝進罐裡的機器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people or things <b>pack into</b> a place or if they <b>pack</b> a place, there are so many of them that the place is full. 擠滿","examples":["Hundreds of people packed into the mosque. 成百上千的人擠進了清真寺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"打包; 包裝","examples":["She left Frances to finish her packing. 她讓弗朗西斯把她的行李收拾完。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"包裝; 裝箱","examples":["The shipping and packing costs are passed along in the item price. 運輸和裝箱費用已經含在單價中了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pack</b> <b>of</b> things is a collection of them that is sold or given together in a box or bag. 盒; 包","examples":["The club will send a free information pack. 俱樂部將贈送一個免費的資訊包。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people who go around together as a <b>pack</b>, especially when it is a large group that you feel threatened by. 一群 (尤指令人感到受到威脅的)","examples":["He thus avoided a pack of journalists eager to question him. 他就這樣避開了一群急於向他提問的記者。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a bundle or load, esp one carried on the back (背的)一捆","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"(<b>as modifier</b>) 馱","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>pack</b> <b>of</b> wolves or dogs is a group of them that hunt together. 一群 (狼或狗)","examples":["...a pack of stray dogs. …一群流浪狗。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>pack</b> <b>of</b> playing cards is a complete set of playing cards. 一副 (紙牌)","examples":["Matt picked up the cards and shuffled the pack. 馬特收齊紙牌，洗了這付牌。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fill (a legislative body, committee, etc) with one's own supporters 把自己的支持者安插進(立法機構等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that an account is <b>a pack of lies</b>, you mean that it is completely untrue. 一派胡言","examples":["You told me a pack of lies. 你跟我說的是一派胡言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>send</b> someone <b>packing</b>, you make them go away. 打發 (某人) 離開","examples":["I decided I wanted to live alone and I sent him packing. 我決定要獨自生活，所以我把他打發走了。"]}]}]},"path":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小徑，小道；（開出的）通道；（事物或人移動的）路線，軌跡；（有助於實現某事的）道路，途徑；通勤火車時刻表；（計算機）路徑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>path</b> is a long strip of ground that people walk along to get from one place to another. 小徑","examples":["We followed the path along the clifftops. 我們沿著懸崖頂的小徑行進。","Feet had worn a path in the rock. 腳步已在岩石裡踏出一條小徑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>path</b> is the space ahead of you as you move along. (前面的) 道路","examples":["A group of reporters blocked his path. 一群記者堵住了他的路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>path</b> of something is the line that it moves along in a particular direction. 路線; 軌道","examples":["He stepped without looking into the path of a reversing car. 他一步邁了出去，連看都沒看一眼一輛正在倒車的汽車。","...people who live near airports or under the flight path of aeroplanes. …住在機場附近或者飛機的飛行線路下面的人們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>path</b> that you take is a particular course of action or way of achieving something. 行動路線; 途徑","examples":["They appear to have chosen the path of cooperation rather than confrontation. 他們好像選擇了合作而不是對抗的行動路線。"]}]}]},"patient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"能忍耐的，有耐心的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"病人，患者；（語言學）受動者，承受者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>patient</b> is a person who is receiving medical treatment from a doctor or hospital. A <b>patient</b> is also someone who is taken care of by a particular doctor. 病人","examples":["The earlier the treatment is given, the better the patient's chances. 治療給得越早，病人機遇越好。","She was tough but wonderful with her patients. 她很嚴厲，但對病人很好。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>patient</b>, you stay calm and do not get annoyed, for example, when something takes a long time, or when someone is not doing what you want them to do. 耐心的","examples":["Please be patient – your cheque will arrive. 請耐心點兒–你的支票會到的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"耐心地","examples":["She waited patiently for Frances to finish. 她耐心地等弗朗西絲完成。"]}]}]},"peach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桃子；桃樹；桃紅色；<非正式>極好的人（或物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"桃紅色的；用桃子製成的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"告密，告發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a small rosaceous tree, <b>Prunus persica,</b> with pink flowers and rounded edible fruit: cultivated in temperate regions 桃樹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>peach</b> is a soft, round, slightly furry fruit with sweet yellow flesh and pinky-orange skin. Peaches grow in warm countries. 桃","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a person or thing that is especially pleasing","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>peach</b> is pale pinky-orange in colour. 桃紅色的","examples":["...a peach silk blouse. …一件桃紅色的絲綢衫。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to inform against an accomplice 揭發同謀","examples":[]}]}]},"pear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"梨，梨樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pear</b> is a sweet, juicy fruit that is narrow near its stalk, and wider and rounded at the bottom. Pears have white flesh and thin green, yellow, or brown skin. 梨","examples":[]}]}]},"penguin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"企鵝；<非正式>空軍地勤人員；企鵝出版社（Penguin Books，英國出版機構）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>penguin</b> is a type of large black and white sea bird found mainly in the Antarctic. Penguins cannot fly but use their short wings for swimming. 企鵝","examples":[]}]}]},"pat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕拍（以示喜愛、贊同或安慰）；輕拍（以引起注意或檢查安放好的物品）；愛撫（狗或馬等動物）；輕拍撫平，輕拍成形；拍幹"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（表示友善的）輕拍；小塊（黃油等）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（回答或解釋）脫口而出的，敷衍的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"記得一清二楚地；及時地，適時地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pat</b> something or someone, you tap them lightly, usually with your hand held flat. 輕拍","examples":["\"Don't you worry about any of this,\" she said patting me on the knee. “不要為這事操什麼心了，”她說道，輕輕拍了拍我的膝蓋。","The landlady patted her hair nervously. 女房東不安地輕拍著她的頭髮。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pat</b> is also a noun. 輕拍","examples":["He gave her an encouraging pat on the shoulder. 他輕拍她肩膀以示鼓勵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pat</b> <b>of</b> butter or something else that is soft is a small lump of it. (奶油等) 小塊","examples":["Terreano put a pat of butter on his plate. 特里諾把一小塊奶油放在他盤子裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"alone; on one's own 獨自","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"exactly or fluently memorized or mastered 準確記憶的; 熟練掌握的 (Also off pat)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"exactly right for the occasion; apt 適合場合的; 恰當的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"too exactly fitting; glib 適合的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone <b>a pat on the back</b> or if you <b>pat</b> them <b>on the back</b>, you show them that you think they have done well and deserve to be praised. 表揚","examples":["The players deserve a pat on the back. 運動員們值得表揚。"]}]}]},"peanut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花生，花生米；<非正式>很少的錢（peanuts）；小片聚苯乙烯泡沫塑膠（peanuts）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Peanuts</b> are small nuts that grow under the ground. Peanuts are often eaten as a snack, especially roasted and salted, and their oil is used in cooking. 花生","examples":["...a packet of peanuts. …一袋花生。"]}]}]},"pattern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模式，方式；圖案，花樣；模範，典範；模型，底樣；（布或牆紙的）樣品；樣式；（聲音或詞彙有規則排列的）模式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用圖案裝飾，給……加上花樣；仿照，模仿；賦予……以固定（或易辨認）的形式；使形成，促成（某行為模式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pattern</b> is the repeated or regular way in which something happens or is done. 模式","examples":["All three attacks followed the same pattern. 3次襲擊都依照同一模式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pattern</b> is an arrangement of lines or shapes, especially a design in which the same shape is repeated at regular intervals over a surface. 圖案","examples":["...a golden robe embroidered with red and purple thread stitched into a pattern of flames. …一件用紅紫相間的線鑲了火焰圖案的邊的金色長袍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pattern</b> is a diagram or shape that you can use as a guide when you are making something such as a model or a piece of clothing. 參照圖形","examples":["...cutting out a pattern for slacks. …剪出一個便褲的紙樣。","Send for our free patterns to knit yourself. 索取我們免費的參照圖形以便自己織。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an outdoor assembly with religious practices, traders' stalls, etc on the feast day of a patron saint 聖人日戶外集會; 集會上有宗教儀式和集市攤檔等 (Also patron)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to model 形成圖案","examples":[]}]}]},"pepper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胡椒粉；辣椒，甜椒，燈籠椒；胡椒；辣椒粉；（棒球）熱身投擊球練習"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在食物上）撒胡椒粉；連續射擊；在……上撒，使佈滿； （演講、文章等）充滿……"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pepper</b> or <b>black pepper</b> is a hot-tasting spice used to flavour food. 胡椒","examples":["Season with salt and pepper. 用鹽和胡椒調味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pepper</b>, or a <b>bell pepper</b>, is a hollow green, red, or yellow vegetable with seeds inside it. 椒類","examples":["...2 red or green peppers, sliced. …2個切成片了的紅椒或青椒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is peppered with</b> small objects, a lot of those objects hit it. (以小物體) 大量擊中","examples":["He was wounded in both legs and severely peppered with shrapnel. 他兩條腿都受傷了，受到了彈片重創。"]}]}]},"peace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"和平，太平；平靜，安寧；（心情）平靜，平和；和約；和平時期；治安；和睦，和諧；平安禮（the peace）；和平運動，裁軍運動（尤指核裁軍運動）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"安靜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If countries or groups involved in a war or violent conflict are discussing <b>peace</b>, they are talking to each other in order to try to end the conflict. 和平問題","examples":["Peace talks involving other rebel leaders and government representatives broke up without agreement last week, but are due to resume shortly. 有其他叛軍領袖和政府代表參加的和平談判於上週未能達成協議而破裂，但不久之後將恢復。","Leaders of some rival factions signed a peace agreement last week. 一些對立派別的領導人於上週簽署了一項和平協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is <b>peace</b> in a country or in the world, there are no wars or violent conflicts going on. 和平狀態","examples":["The president spoke of a shared commitment to world peace and economic development. 總統談到了一項促進世界和平和經濟發展的共同承諾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you disapprove of weapons, especially nuclear weapons, you can use <b>peace</b> to refer to campaigns and other activities intended to reduce their numbers or stop their use. (尤指阻止核武器使用的) 和平運動","examples":["...two peace campaigners accused of causing damage to an F1-11 nuclear bomber. …被指控造成一架F1-11核轟炸機受損的兩位和平運動家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>peace</b>, you are not being disturbed, and you are in calm, quiet surroundings. 安寧","examples":["All I want is to have some peace and quiet and spend a couple of nice days with my grandchildren. 我只想有一些安寧與平靜並和我的孫子孫女們過幾天好日子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have a feeling of <b>peace</b>, you feel contented and calm and not at all worried. You can also say that you are <b>at peace</b>. 平和","examples":["I had a wonderful feeling of peace and serenity when I saw my husband. 我看到我的丈夫就有一種平和安詳的美妙感覺。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If there is <b>peace</b> among a group of people, they live or work together in a friendly way and do not argue. You can also say that people live or work <b>in peace with</b> each other. 相安無事","examples":["...a period of relative peace in the country's industrial relations. …該國產業關係中一段相對平靜的時期。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority, such as the army or the police, <b>keeps the peace</b>, they make sure that people behave and do not fight or quarrel with each other. 維持和平","examples":["...the first U.N. contingent assigned to help keep the peace in Cambodia. …第一支派往柬埔寨幫助維持和平的聯合國分隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something gives you <b>peace of mind</b>, it stops you from worrying about a particular problem or difficulty. 心靈的平靜","examples":["The main appeal these bonds hold for individual investors is the safety and peace of mind they offer. 這些債券對於個人投資者的主要吸引力在於它們提供的安全感和心靈的平靜。"]}]}]},"photographer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拍照者，攝影師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>photographer</b> is someone who takes photographs as a job or hobby. 攝影師; 攝影愛好者","examples":["...a professional photographer. …一名專業攝影師。","...an amateur photographer. …一名業餘攝影愛好者。"]}]}]},"period":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一段時間，時期；（人生或國家歷史的）階段，時代；（地質年代劃分的）紀；課時，節；（練習、訓練或學習的）時段；（婦女的）月經，經期；（體育比賽的）局；<美>句號，句點；（物理）（振動或迴圈的）週期；（天文）自轉（或公轉）週期；（數學）（週期函式的）週期；（化學）週期元素；（修辭）完整句；（樂）樂段，樂節"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"具有某個時代特徵的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美>到此為止，不再說了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>period</b> is a length of time. 一段時間","examples":["This crisis might last for a long period of time. 此次危機可能會持續很長一段時間。","...a period of a few months. …幾個月的時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>period</b> in the life of a person, organization, or society is a length of time that is remembered for a particular situation or activity. (個人、組織或社會的) 時期","examples":["...a period of economic good health and expansion. …一段經濟健康發展和擴張時期。","He went through a period of wanting to be accepted. 他經歷了一段渴望得到接受的時期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular length of time in history is sometimes called a <b>period</b>. For example, you can talk about <b>the Civil War period</b> or <b>the Prohibition period</b> in the U.S. (歷史) 時期","examples":["The novel is set in the Roman period. 該小說的背景是羅馬時期。","No reference to their existence appears in any literature of the period. 該時期的任何文獻中都沒有提及他們的存在。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Exercise, training, or study <b>periods</b> are lengths of time that are set aside for exercise, training, or study. (練習、訓練或學習的) 時段","examples":["They accompanied him during his exercise periods. 在他的練習時段，他們都陪著他。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>period</b> is the punctuation mark (.) that you use at the end of a sentence when it is not a question or an exclamation. 句號","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When a woman has a <b>period</b>, she bleeds from her uterus. This usually happens once a month, unless she is pregnant. 經期","examples":["Can you get pregnant if you have sex during your period? 經期性交會懷孕嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Period</b> costumes, furniture, and instruments were made at an earlier time in history, or look as if they were made then. 具特定歷史時期特點的","examples":["The characters were dressed in full period costume. 劇中人物全都身著具有時代特色的服裝。"]}]}]},"photograph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"照片，相片"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拍照，照相；在照片上顯出某種樣子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>photograph</b> is a picture that is made using a camera. 照片","examples":["He wants to take some photographs of the house. 他想給這所房子拍一些照片。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>photograph</b> someone or something, you use a camera to obtain a picture of them. 給…照相","examples":["She photographed the children. 她給孩子們照了相。","I hate being photographed. 我討厭被拍照。"]}]}]},"phrase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短語，片語；慣用語，習語；樂句；（芭蕾）舞句"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用……方式表達，以……措辭表達；把（樂曲）分成短句"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>phrase</b> is a short group of words that people often use as a way of saying something. The meaning of a phrase is often not obvious from the meaning of the individual words in it. 慣用語; 警句","examples":["He used a phrase I hate: \"You have to be cruel to be kind.\" 他用了一句我討厭的習語：“要想善良，就得殘忍。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>phrase</b> is a small group of words that forms a unit, either on its own or within a sentence. 短語; 片語","examples":["A writer spends many hours going over and over a scene—changing a phrase here, a word there. 作家花許多個小時反覆潤色一個場景—這兒改個短語，那兒改個單詞。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>phrase</b> something in a particular way, you express it in words in that way. 用言語表達","examples":["I would have phrased it quite differently. 我則會用完全不同的話來表達它。","The speech was carefully phrased. 這篇講話措辭謹慎。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has a particular <b>turn of phrase</b>, they have a particular way of expressing themselves in words. 表述方式","examples":["...Schwarzkopf's distinctive turn of phrase. …施瓦茨科普夫與眾不同的表述方式。"]}]}]},"pigeon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鴿子；<非正式，美>（容易）上當受騙的人；<英>（自己的）責任，分內之事；<俚>己方飛機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pigeon</b> is a bird, usually grey in colour, that has a fat body. Pigeons often live in cities and towns. 鴿子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"concern or responsibility (often in the phrase <b>it's his, her,</b> etc, <b>pigeon</b>) 問題或責任(常出現在“這是他的、她的”等短語中)","examples":[]}]}]},"perfect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無瑕的，完好的；完全正確的，極其準確的；完美的，理想的；最佳的，絕配的；十足的，完全的；通常的，大體的；（語法）完成時的，完成式的；（數字）完全的；（花）有雌雄蕊的；（昆蟲）性成熟的；（真菌）有性孢子形成階段的，有性的；完成時的，完成式的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"完善，使完美；雙面印完（一頁紙）；<法律>使（禮物、頭銜等）合法轉移"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（語法）完成時，完成體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>perfect</b> is as good as it could possibly be. 完美的","examples":["He spoke perfect English. 他講一口純正的英語。","Nobody is perfect. 人無完人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>perfect</b> <b>for</b> a particular person, thing, or activity, you are emphasizing that it is very suitable for them or for that activity. 最適合的","examples":["The pool area is perfect for entertaining. 游泳池一帶最適合娛樂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an object or surface is <b>perfect</b>, it does not have any marks on it, or does not have any lumps, hollows, or cracks in it. 無瑕疵的","examples":["Use only clean, Grade A, perfect eggs. 只用潔淨的、一級的、無瑕疵的雞蛋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>perfect</b> to give emphasis to the noun following it. (用以強調所修飾名詞) 完全的","examples":["She was a perfect fool. 她是個十足的傻瓜。","Some people are always coming up to perfect strangers and asking them what they do. 有些人總是走近完全不認識的人跟前，問人家是幹什麼的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>perfect</b> something, you improve it so that it becomes as good as it can possibly be. 使完美","examples":["We perfected a hand-signal system so that he could keep me informed of hazards. 我們完善了一套手語體系，以便他能告知我危險。","I removed the fibroid tumours, using the techniques that I have perfected. 我用我完善過的技術切除了這些纖維瘤。"]}]}]},"phone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電話，電話系統；受話器，聽筒；（語音）音子，音素"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給…...打電話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>phone</b> is an electrical system that you use to talk to someone else in another place, by dialling a number on a piece of equipment and speaking into it. 電話","examples":["\"I didn't tell you over the phone,\" she said. \"I didn't know who might be listening.\" “我沒有在電話裡告訴你，”她說。“我不知道誰會在聽。”","She looked forward to talking to her daughter by phone. 她盼望著和她女兒通電話交談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>phone</b> is the piece of equipment that you use when you dial someone's phone number and talk to them. 電話機","examples":["Two minutes later the phone rang. 兩分鐘後，電話鈴響了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone picks up or puts down <b>the phone</b>, you mean that they lift or replace the receiver. 電話聽筒","examples":["She picked up the phone, and began to dial Maurice's number. 她拿起電話聽筒，開始撥莫里斯的號碼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a single uncomplicated speech sound 單音; 音素; 音子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>phone</b> someone, you dial their phone number and speak to them by phone. 給…打電話","examples":["He'd phoned Laura to see if she was better. 他給勞拉打電話，看她是不是好些了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>on the phone</b>, you mean that they are speaking to someone by phone. 在打電話","examples":["She's always on the phone, wanting to know what I've been up to. 她總是打電話，想知道我忙了些什麼。"]}]}]},"picnic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"野餐，野餐活動；野餐食物；<非正式>愉快事物，輕鬆事物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"參加野餐活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people have a <b>picnic</b>, they eat a meal outdoors, usually in a park or a forest, or at the beach. 野餐","examples":["We're going on a picnic tomorrow. 我們明天去野餐。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>picnic</b> somewhere, they have a picnic. 野餐","examples":["Afterwards, we picnicked on the riverbank. 之後，我們在河岸上野餐。"]}]}]},"photo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"照片，相片"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>拍照；給……拍照"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>photo</b> is the same as a . 照片","examples":["Let's take a photo! 我們拍張照片吧！"]}]}]},"ping-pong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乒乓球，桌球（等於 table tennis）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>來回移動，彈跳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ping-Pong</b> is the game of . 乒乓球","examples":[]}]}]},"pineapple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"[園藝] 菠蘿；[園藝] 鳳梨"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鳳梨科的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pineapple</b> is a large oval fruit that grows in hot countries. It is sweet, juicy, and yellow inside. It has a thick brownish skin. 菠蘿","examples":[]}]}]},"pizza":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比薩餅，披薩（一種義大利烤餅，用扁平的麵餅鋪上番茄醬、乳酪及其他配料烤制而成）；（Pizza）皮扎（義大利人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pizza</b> is a flat, round piece of dough covered with tomatoes, cheese, and other toppings, and then baked in an oven. 比薩餅","examples":["...the last piece of pizza. …最後一塊比薩餅。"]}]}]},"pile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一堆，一疊；一大堆，大量；大筆錢財；（地毯的）絨面；地樁；宏偉建築物；痔瘡；（紋章）（尖頭朝下的）楔形普通圖記；電池組"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"堆放；堆滿；聚集；將（女子頭髮）高高盤起；蜂擁，擁擠；（車）撞（~ into）；<非正式>誇大（~ something on）；用樁加固（或支撐）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pile of</b> things is a mass of them that is high in the middle and has sloping sides. 堆","examples":["...a pile of sand. …一堆沙子。","...a little pile of crumbs. …一小堆麵包屑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pile of</b> things is a quantity of things that have been put neatly somewhere so that each thing is on top of the one below. 疊","examples":["...a pile of boxes. …一疊盒子。","We sat in Sam's study, among the piles of books. 我們坐在薩姆的書房裡，在一疊疊的書中間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Piles</b> are wooden, concrete, or metal posts that are pushed into the ground and on which buildings or bridges are built. Piles are often used in very wet areas so that the buildings do not flood.  地樁","examples":["...settlements of wooden houses, set on piles along the shore. …沿岸而建的吊腳木屋居民區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Piles</b> is an informal word meaning <b> haemorrhoids</b>. 痔瘡","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>pile</b> of a carpet or of a fabric such as velvet is its soft surface. It consists of a lot of little threads standing on end.  絨面","examples":["...the carpet's thick pile. …地毯厚厚的絨面。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pile</b> things somewhere, you put them there so that they form a pile. 堆放","examples":["He was piling clothes into the suitcase. 他正把衣服疊放到手提箱中去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is piled with</b> things, it is covered or filled with piles of things. 堆滿","examples":["Tables were piled high with local produce. 桌子上高高地堆滿了土特產。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people <b>pile into</b> or <b>out of</b> a vehicle, they all get into it or out of it in a disorganized way. 湧入/出","examples":["They all piled into Jerry's car. 他們都擠進了傑裡的車裡。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to drive (piles) into the ground 將(地樁)打進地裡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>at the bottom of the pile</b> is low down in society or low down in an organization. Someone who is <b>at the top of the pile</b> is high up in society or high up in an organization. 處於...的下層或上層","examples":["These workers are fed up with being at the bottom of the pile when it comes to pay. 這些工人受夠了收入水平處於底層的苦惱。"]}]}]},"pink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粉紅色的；（因窘迫、憤怒或劇烈活動而）臉色發紅的；同性戀的；<非正式，貶>左傾的；石竹科的；興奮的（tickled pink）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"粉紅色；粉紅色衣服或衣料；<非正式>粉紅色葡萄酒；石竹；<史>尖尾帆船；滿面紅光，容光煥發（in the pink (of)）；粉紅色桌球；<舊>微黃顏料；<非正式>左傾的人；<舊>精英，典範"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>（車輛引擎）發響爆聲，爆震；變成粉紅色；<澳新>（貼身地）剪（羊毛）；剪成鋸齒狀；<罕>（用武器或投擲物）刺，戳，扎；嘲笑，批評；<古>裝飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pink</b> is the colour between red and white. 粉紅色","examples":["...pink lipstick. …粉紅色口紅。","...white flowers edged in pink. …帶粉邊的白花。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pink</b> is used to refer to things relating to or connected with gay people. 與男同性戀有關的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to prick lightly with a sword or rapier 用劍輕刺","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a sailing vessel with a narrow overhanging transom 帶氣窗的帆船","examples":[]}]}]},"pillow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"枕頭；蕾絲枕頭（lace pillow的簡稱）；<美>坐墊，靠墊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將（頭）枕在……上，枕著（某物）；<文>為……當枕頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pillow</b> is a rectangular cushion that you rest your head on when you are in bed. 枕頭","examples":[]}]}]},"pipe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"管子，管道；菸斗；管樂器；（管風琴的）音管；（蘇格蘭的）風笛（pipes）；（人或動物的）叫聲，歌聲；葡萄酒桶；（計算機）管線命令；符號\"|\""},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用管道運輸；傳送，播送（音樂、錄音）；用管樂器吹奏；（吹長口哨）召集，召喚；高聲說話，尖聲唱；在食品（尤指蛋糕）上裱花；（為衣服或室內陳設品）拷邊，滾邊；插枝繁殖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pipe</b> is a long, round, hollow object, usually made of metal or plastic, through which a liquid or gas can flow. 管子","examples":["The liquid can't escape into the air, because it's inside a pipe. 液體不會漏到空氣中，因為它在管子裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pipe</b> is an object that is used for smoking tobacco. You put the tobacco into the cup-shaped part at the end of the pipe, light it, and breathe in the smoke through a narrow tube. 菸斗","examples":["Do you smoke a pipe? 你抽菸鬥嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pipe</b> is a simple musical instrument in the shape of a tube with holes in it. You play a pipe by blowing into it while covering and uncovering the holes with your fingers. 管樂器","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>organ pipe</b> is one of the long hollow tubes in which air vibrates and produces a musical note. 管風琴的音管","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a large cask for wine, oil, etc 裝酒、油等的大桶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If liquid or gas <b>is piped</b> somewhere, it is transferred from one place to another through a pipe. 用管道輸送","examples":["The heated gas is piped through a coil surrounded by water. 受熱氣體透過水中的一根螺旋管輸送。","The Communists brought electricity to his village and piped in drinking water from the reservoir. 共產黨員們把電接入了他的村子，還用管道從水庫引來飲用水。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to play (music) on a pipe 以管樂器吹奏(音樂)","examples":[]}]}]},"planet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行星；地球（the planet）；<史>命運星辰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>planet</b> is a large, round object in space that moves around a star. The Earth is a planet. 行星","examples":["The picture shows six of the nine planets in the solar system. 這張圖片展示太陽系9個行星中的6個行星。"]}]}]},"pin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指做衣服時固定布料用的）別針，大頭針；<美>胸針，飾針；徽章，像章；釘，楔，銷，栓；（接骨用的）鋼釘，鋼針；（插頭的）管腳；（手榴彈的）保險針，保險銷；（高爾夫球場地內的）旗杆；（保齡球）瓶柱；（人或動物的）雙腿；（棋）牽制；（樂）絃軸，琴軫；<英，史>加侖啤酒桶；（PIN）個人身份識別號碼（用於在自動取款機上取款的私人密碼）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用釘子）釘住，別住；按住，使不能動彈；（棋）牽制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pins</b> are very small thin pointed pieces of metal. They are used in sewing to fasten pieces of material together until they have been sewn. 別針","examples":["...a box of needles and pins. …一盒縫衣針和別針。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pin</b> is any long narrow piece of metal or wood that is not sharp, especially one that is used to fasten two things together. (把兩件物品固定在一起的) 銷; 釘; 栓","examples":["...the 18-inch steel pin holding his left leg together. …將他的左腿固定起來的18英寸長的鋼釘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pin</b> is something worn on your clothing, for example, as jewellery, which is fastened with a pointed piece of metal. 胸針","examples":["...necklaces, bracelets, and pins. …項鍊、手鐲和胸針。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pin</b> something <b>on</b> or <b>to</b> something, you attach it with a pin, a safety pin or a thumbtack. 用別針別住; 用圖釘釘住","examples":["They pinned a notice to the door. 他們把通知釘在門上。","Everyone was supposed to dance with the bride and pin money on her dress. 每個人都應該和新娘跳舞並把錢別在她的衣服上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>pins</b> you to something, they press you against a surface so that you cannot move. 按住; 使不能動彈","examples":["I pinned him against the wall. 我把他按在牆上。","I'd try to get away and he'd pin me down, saying he would kill me. 我會試圖逃走，而他會把我按倒，說要殺了我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone tries to <b>pin</b> something <b>on</b> you or to <b>pin the blame on</b> you, they say, often unfairly, that you were responsible for something bad or illegal. 把…歸罪於","examples":["They're trying to pin it on us. 他們正試圖把這件事歸罪於我們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pin</b> your hopes <b>on</b> something or <b>pin</b> your faith <b>on</b> something, you hope very much that it will produce the result you want. 寄 (希望、信念) 於","examples":["The Democrats are pinning their hopes on the next election. 民主黨人正寄希望於下一次選舉。"]}]}]},"pick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"採，摘（花、果）；（用手指）弄掉；找茬；撿，抱起；選擇；彈，撥（弦）；撬開（鎖），扒竊……中的東西；小心走路（~ one's way）；（反覆地）拔，拉，撕，扯；沒胃口地吃；（高爾夫）拾球（尤指認輸的拾球）（~ up）；採，摘（花、果等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"精華（the pick of）；選擇，選擇權；被選中的人（或事物）；鶴嘴鋤；（吉他的）撥子；（尖狀的）挖撬工具；（籃球）掩護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pick</b> a particular person or thing, you choose that one. 挑選","examples":["Mr. Nowell had picked ten people to interview for six sales jobs in Dallas. 諾埃爾先生為在達拉斯的六個銷售職位挑選了十人進行面試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>pick</b> flowers, fruit, or leaves, you break them off the plant or tree and collect them. 採摘","examples":["She used to pick flowers in the Adirondacks. 她以前常去阿迪朗達克山採花。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pick</b> something from a place, you remove it from there with your fingers or your hand. 拿走","examples":["He picked the napkin from his lap and placed it alongside his plate. 他從腿上拿起餐巾，放在他的盤子旁邊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pick</b> your <b>nose</b> or <b>teeth</b>, you remove substances from inside your nose or between your teeth. 摳 (鼻子); 剔 (牙)","examples":["Edgar, don't pick your nose, dear. 埃德加，不要摳鼻子，親愛的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>pick</b> a fight <b>with</b> someone, you deliberately cause one. 挑釁","examples":["He picked a fight with a waiter and landed in jail. 他找茬兒和服務員打架，結果鋃鐺入獄。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone such as a thief <b>picks</b> a lock, they open it without a key, for example, by using a piece of wire. 撬 (鎖)","examples":["He picked each lock deftly, and rifled the papers within each drawer. 他熟練地撬開每一把鎖，偷走了每個抽屜裡的檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the best things or people in a particular group as <b>the pick</b> <b>of</b> that group. 精華; 精英","examples":["The boys here are the pick of the high school's football players. 這兒的男孩都是該中學足球隊的精英。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pick</b> is the same as a . 同 pickax","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"one casting of a shuttle 投梭","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to pierce, dig, or break up (a hard surface) with a pick (用鶴嘴鋤)鑿; 掘; 挖","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to cast (a shuttle) 投(梭)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are told to <b>take</b> your <b>pick</b>, you can choose any one that you like from a group of things. 任意挑選","examples":["Accountants can take their pick of company cars. 會計們可以任意挑選公司的汽車。"]}]}]},"poet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>poet</b> is a person who writes poems. 詩人","examples":["He was a painter and poet. 他是一位畫家兼詩人。"]}]}]},"platform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平臺；講臺，舞臺；講臺上的人（the platform）；（火車站的）月臺；<英>（公共汽車上供乘客上下車的）踏腳臺；發言機會，論壇；契機；（政黨的）綱領；厚底鞋；計算機平臺；（海上）鑽井平臺；（供人上下小船的）水上平臺；（火箭或導彈的）衛星發射平臺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>platform</b> is a flat raised structure, usually made of wood, that people stand on when they make speeches or give a performance. 講臺; 舞臺","examples":["Nick finished what he was saying and jumped down from the platform. 尼克講完話，從講臺上跳了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>platform</b> is a flat raised structure or area, usually one that something can stand on or land on. (用於放置物品或著陸的) 平臺","examples":["They found a spot on a rocky platform where they could pitch their tents. 他們在一個岩石平臺上找到了一處可以搭帳篷的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>platform</b> is a structure built for people to work and live on when drilling for oil or gas at sea, or when extracting it. (在海上為鑽探石油或天然氣而建的) 平臺","examples":["The platform began to produce oil in 1994. 1994年，這個鑽井平臺開始產油。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>platform</b> in a train or subway station is the area beside the tracks where you wait for or get off a train. (火車或地鐵站的) 站臺","examples":["The train was about to leave and I was not even on the platform. 火車就要開了，而我甚至還沒有趕到站臺上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>platform</b> of a political party is what they say they will do if they are elected. (政黨的) 施政綱領","examples":["The party has announced a platform of political and economic reforms. 該黨已宣佈了一份關於政治和經濟改革的施政綱領。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone has a <b>platform</b>, they have an opportunity to tell people what they think or want. 發表意見的機會","examples":["The demonstration provided a platform for a broad cross-section of speakers. 那次示威為廣泛代表各方的發言者們提供了一個發表意見的機會。"]}]}]},"poem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩，韻文"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>poem</b> is a piece of writing in which the words are chosen for their beauty and sound and are carefully arranged, often in short lines that rhyme. 詩","examples":["...a book of love poems. …一本愛情詩集。"]}]}]},"pitch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>體育場地，球場；程度，強度；音準，音高；推銷用語；投球；瀝青，柏油；（船或飛機的）顛簸；傾斜度，高度；<英>攤位，（街頭藝人的）表演場所；（高爾夫）下旋高球；<英>露營地；（技）螺距，節距"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扔，拋，擲；（棒球中）投（球）；擊地，（使球）定點落地；重跌，墜落；（船或飛機）顛簸；把……定於某水平；使（產品）針對，面向；推銷；為……定音高；向下傾斜；扎，搭建；（高爾夫）擊下旋高球；用石頭鋪（路）；（釀酒用語）給（麥芽汁）加酵母；<古或西印度>蓋上瀝青，塗上瀝青"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pitch</b> something somewhere, you throw it with some force, usually aiming it carefully. 投擲","examples":["Simon pitched the empty bottle into the lake. 西蒙把空瓶子投進湖裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the game of baseball, when you <b>pitch</b> the ball, you throw it to the batter for them to hit it. 投 (球) 給擊球手","examples":["We passed long, hot afternoons pitching a baseball. 我們以打棒球來消磨一個個漫長的炎熱午後。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>pitch</b> somewhere means to fall forwards suddenly and with a lot of force. (向前) 跌倒","examples":["The movement took him by surprise, and he pitched forward. 突然的移動讓他猝不及防，向前跌倒。","Alan staggered sideways, pitched head-first over the low wall and fell into the lake. 艾倫兩側搖晃著，一頭栽過矮牆，掉進湖裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is pitched into</b> a new situation, they are suddenly forced into it. 迫使進入 (一種新的處境)","examples":["They were being pitched into a new adventure in which they would have to fight the whole world. 他們當時正被脅迫參與到一次不得不與整個世界抗衡的新冒險中。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a sound <b>is pitched at</b> a particular level, it is produced at the level indicated. 使 (音調)達到(指定水準)","examples":["His cry is pitched at a level that makes it impossible to ignore. 他哭聲之大讓人不可能置若罔聞。","His voice was pitched high, the words muffled by his crying. 他的嗓門提得很高，說的話都被他的叫喊聲壓得聽不清了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>is pitched</b> <b>at</b> a particular level or degree of difficulty, it is set at that level. 給…設定水平 (或難度)","examples":["While this is very important material I think it's probably pitched at too high a level for our students. 儘管這是個很重要的材料，但我認為它的難度太大，不適合我們的學生。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone <b>pitches</b> an idea for something such as a new product, they try to persuade people to accept the idea. 力薦(某主張)","examples":["My agent has pitched the idea to my editor in New York. 我的代理人已向我在紐約的編輯力薦這個想法。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the degree of elevation or depression 程度","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pitch</b> of a sound is how high or low it is. 音調","examples":["He raised his voice to an even higher pitch. 他將嗓門提得更高了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a feeling or a situation rises to a high <b>pitch</b>, it rises to a high level. (感情或形勢等的) 程度","examples":["The public's feelings were at a high pitch of indignation. 公眾的憤怒情緒達到了極點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pitch</b> is an area of ground that is marked out and used for playing a game such as football, cricket, or hockey. 比賽場地","examples":["...a football pitch. …一個足球場。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"any of various heavy dark viscid substances obtained as a residue from the distillation of tars 瀝青","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to apply pitch to (something) 用瀝青覆蓋(某物)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>makes a pitch</b> <b>for</b> something, they try to persuade people to do or buy it. 遊說","examples":["The president speaks in New York today, making another pitch for his economic programme. 總統今天在紐約發表講話，再一次遊說他的經濟計劃。"]}]}]},"pleasure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"快樂，滿足，欣慰；樂事，趣事；（尤指工作、職責之外的）娛樂，消遣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遊樂的，非公務的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"從……中獲得樂趣；（使）高興"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something gives you <b>pleasure</b>, you get a feeling of happiness, satisfaction, or enjoyment from it. 愉悅","examples":["Watching sports gave him great pleasure. 觀看體育運動帶給他極大的愉悅。","Everybody takes pleasure in eating. 每個人都在吃中獲得愉悅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pleasure</b> is the activity of enjoying yourself, especially rather than working or doing what you have a duty to do. 娛樂","examples":["He mixed business and pleasure in a perfect and dynamic way. 他把工作和娛樂以一種完美而活躍的方式結合了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pleasure</b> is an activity, experience, or aspect of something that you find very enjoyable or satisfying. 樂事","examples":["Watching TV is our only pleasure. 看電視是我們惟一的樂趣。","...the pleasure of seeing a smiling face. …看到一張笑臉的那種愉悅。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you meet someone for the first time, you can say, as a way of being polite, that it is <b>a pleasure to meet</b> them. You can also ask for <b>the pleasure of</b> someone's <b>company</b> as a polite and formal way of inviting them somewhere. 榮幸 (用於初次見面禮貌地打招呼)","examples":["\"A pleasure to meet you, sir,\" he said. “很榮幸見到您，先生，”他說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>It's a pleasure</b>\" or \"<b>My pleasure</b>\" as a polite way of replying to someone who has just thanked you for doing something. 樂意效勞 (用作回應別人的感謝時的禮貌用語)","examples":["\"Thanks very much anyhow.\"—\"It's a pleasure.\" “無論如何，非常感謝你。”—“不客氣。”"]}]}]},"policy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"政策，方針；(處事) 原則，策略；保險單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>policy</b> is a set of ideas or plans that is used as a basis for making decisions, especially in politics, economics, or business. 政策","examples":["...plans that include changes in foreign policy and economic reforms. …包括外交政策調整和經濟改革的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An official organization's <b>policy</b> on a particular issue or toward a country is their attitude and actions regarding that issue or country. 方針","examples":["...the organization's future policy toward South Africa. …該組織未來的南非政策。","...the government's policy on repatriation. …該政府的遣返政策。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An insurance <b>policy</b> is a document that shows the agreement that you have made with an insurance company. 保險單","examples":["You are advised to read the small print of homeowner and car insurance policies. 建議你讀一下房主保險單和汽車保險單上的小號印刷字。"]}]}]},"plus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"加；外加，而且；（溫度）零上"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（在數字後）多，餘；略高於標準的；零上的，正的；有利的；正電的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"加號，正號；（數字的）加法；好處"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"而且；加上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>plus</b> to show that one number or quantity is being added to another. 加","examples":["...$5 for a small locker, plus a $3 deposit. …帶鎖的小櫃子$5，外加$3的押金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>plus</b> when mentioning an additional item or fact. 外加","examples":["There's easily enough room for two adults and three children, plus a dog in the boot. 有足夠的空間容納2個大人和3個小孩。另外，行李箱裡還能容納1只狗。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Plus</b> before a number or quantity means that the number or quantity is greater than zero. 正的","examples":["The aircraft was subjected to temperatures of minus 65 degrees and plus 120 degrees. 這架飛機經受過零下65度和零上120度的考驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>plus</b> after a number or quantity to indicate that the actual number or quantity is greater than the one mentioned. 略多一些的","examples":["There are only 35 staff to serve 30,000-plus customers. 只有35名員工為3萬多位顧客服務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Teachers use <b>plus</b> in grading work in schools and colleges. \"B plus\" is a better grade than \"B,\" but it is not as good as \"A.\" 略好一些的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plus</b> is an advantage or benefit. 優勢; 益處","examples":["Well-known figures would be a big plus for the new board. 名人會成為新董事會的一大優勢。"]}]}]},"plate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盤，碟；一盤（食物）；<美>一道主菜；奉獻盤，捐款盤；金屬護板（片）；金屬牌；（車輛的）號碼牌；鍍金（或鍍銀）金屬；金/銀餐具；盾片，鱗甲；（地質）板塊；（書中的）插圖；印版；感光板；假牙託；牙箍；<非正式>全口假牙；（棒球）本壘板；（銀質或金質）獎盃；盃賽；橫木；（生物）培養皿；載物片，玻璃片；極板；<美>陽極"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……鍍（金屬）；給……加上裝甲；用鱗片覆蓋；擺盤；（棒球）跑壘得分；（生物）製作顯微片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plate</b> is a round or oval flat dish that is used to hold food.  盤子","examples":["Anita pushed her plate away; she had eaten virtually nothing. 安妮塔把盤子推開；她其實什麼都沒吃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>plate</b> <b>of</b> food is the amount of food on a plate. 一盤子的量","examples":["...a huge plate of bacon and eggs. …一大盤子培根和雞蛋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plate</b> is a flat piece of metal, especially on machinery or a building. 金屬片","examples":["...a recess covered by a brass plate. …一個被一塊銅板覆蓋著的壁龕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>plate</b> is a small, flat piece of metal with someone's name written on it, which you usually find beside the front door of an office or house. 金屬牌子","examples":["...a brass plate by the front door bearing his name. …大門旁一塊刻有他名字的銅牌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"On a road vehicle, the <b>plates</b> are the panels on the front and back that display the registration number. 牌照","examples":["...dusty-looking cars with New Jersey plates. …掛著新澤西牌照的落滿灰塵的汽車。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>plate</b> in a book is a picture or photograph that takes up a whole page and is usually printed on better quality paper than the rest of the book.  整頁插圖","examples":["The book has 55 colour plates. 這本書有55頁彩色整頁插圖。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have enough on</b> your <b>plate</b> or <b>have a lot on</b> your <b>plate</b>, you have a lot of work to do or a lot of things to deal with. 有許多事等著做","examples":["We have enough on our plate. There is plenty of work to be done on what we have. 我們有許多事幹。我們手頭就有大量的工作要做。"]}]}]},"population":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（地區、國家等的）人口，人口數量；（某領域的）生物，族群，人口；（統計）總體，母體；（天文）星族；（物理）布居數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>population</b> of a country or area is all the people who live in it. 人口","examples":["Bangladesh now has a population of about 110 million. 孟加拉國現有約一億一千萬人口。","...the annual rate of population growth. …人口年增長率。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a particular type of <b>population</b> in a country or area, you are referring to all the people or animals of that type there. (某種) 人群; 種群","examples":["...75.6 percent of the male population over sixteen. …16歲以上男性人群的75.6％。","...areas with a large black population. …有大批黑人群體的的各地區。"]}]}]},"pork":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豬肉；<美，非正式>政府恩惠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>暴食（pork out）；<美，俚>（男人）跟……性交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pork</b> is meat from a pig, usually fresh and not smoked or salted. (常為新鮮的未燻過、未醃過的) 豬肉","examples":["...fried pork chops. …炸豬排。"]}]}]},"poison":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毒藥；有害的思想；惡毒的言辭（或行動）；（化）抑制劑；（物理）中子吸收劑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"毒殺；在……下毒；毒化，敗壞；汙染（環境）；抑制"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有毒的"}],"sections":[]},"postcard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"明信片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>postcard</b> is a thin card, often with a picture on one side, which you can write on and mail to people without using an envelope. 明信片","examples":[]}]}]},"port":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"港口，避風港；口岸，港口城市；（計算機）埠，介面；波爾圖葡萄酒（產自葡萄牙）（=port wine）；（船、飛機等的）舷門，舷窗；射擊孔，槍眼（=gun port）；通道，排氣口；<蘇格蘭>城門，城門洞；（計算機）移植（軟體）；<文>姿勢，姿態；（軍）斜持槍位置；<澳大利亞，非正式>旅行箱，旅行包"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"轉移，移植（軟體）；使（船，舵）向左轉；（軍）斜持槍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>port</b> is a town by the sea or on a river that has a harbour. 港口城市","examples":["...the Mediterranean port of Marseilles. …地中海港口城市馬賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>port</b> is a harbour area where ships load and unload goods or passengers. 港口","examples":["...the bridges that link the port area to the rest of the city. …連線港口和城市的其餘地區的各橋樑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>port</b> on a computer is a place where you can attach another piece of equipment such as a printer.  埠","examples":["The devices, attached to a PC through standard ports, print bar codes onto envelopes. 這些裝置透過標準埠和電腦相連，將條形碼列印到信封上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Port</b> is also a noun. 左舷","examples":["USS Ogden turned to port. 美國奧格登號艦向左轉了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Port</b> is a type of strong, sweet red wine. 波爾特 (葡萄酒)","examples":["He asked for a glass of port after dinner. 他飯後要了一杯波爾特葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"an opening in the side of a ship, fitted with a watertight door, for access to the holds (通向貨倉、安裝放水門的)船側通口","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"this position 槍口靠近左肩，以斜背的姿勢持槍","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"(esp in Queensland) a suitcase or school case (尤指昆士蘭的)皮箱; 書包","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to change (programs) from one system to another 改變(系統程式)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to turn or be turned towards the port 轉向左舷","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to carry (a rifle, etc) in a position diagonally across the body with the muzzle near the left shoulder (槍口靠近左肩，以斜背的姿勢)持槍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In sailing, the <b>port</b> side of a ship is the left side when you are on it and facing toward the front. (輪船) 左舷的","examples":["Her official number is carved on the port side of the forecabin. 她的正式編號刻在前艙的左舷上。"]}]}]},"pose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"造成，引起（威脅、危險、問題等）；提出（問題）；（為照相、畫像等）擺好姿勢；假扮，冒充（pose as）；（舉止或穿戴）裝腔作勢，招搖過市；<古>把……難住，使為難"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（為拍照、畫像等擺的）姿勢；故作姿態，裝腔作勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>poses</b> a problem or a danger, it is the cause of that problem or danger. 造成 (問題或危險)","examples":["This could pose a threat to jobs in the coal industry. 這可能對煤炭行業的就業造成威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pose</b> a question, you ask it. If you <b>pose</b> an issue that needs considering, you mention the issue. 提出 (問題)","examples":["When I finally posed the question, \"Why?\" he merely shrugged. 當我最終提出“為什麼？”這個問題時，他只是聳聳肩。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pose as</b> someone, you pretend to be that person in order to deceive people. 假扮","examples":["The team posed as drug dealers to trap the ringleaders. 該專案組成員們假扮毒品販子來誘捕犯罪頭目。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pose for</b> a photograph or painting, you stay in a particular position so that someone can photograph you or paint you. 擺姿勢","examples":["Before going into their meeting the six foreign ministers posed for photographs. 開會前，六國外長一起合影。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to puzzle or baffle 使迷惑; 使困惑","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pose</b> is a particular way that you stand, sit, or lie, for example, when you are being photographed or painted. 姿勢","examples":["We have had several preliminary sittings in various poses. 我們已經預拍了幾種不同的姿勢。"]}]}]},"possibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能，可能性；可能的選項，可能的途徑；發展前景，潛能；可能發生的事；機會，契機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say there is a <b>possibility</b> <b>that</b> something is the case or <b>that</b> something will happen, you mean that it might be the case or it might happen. 可能性","examples":["We were not in the least worried about the possibility that sweets could rot the teeth. 我們一點也不擔心糖果可能會腐蝕牙齒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>possibility</b> is one of several different things that could be done. 可以做的事","examples":["There were several possibilities open to each manufacturer. 每個製造商都有幾種可能的選擇。"]}]}]},"potato":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"馬鈴薯，土豆，洋芋；馬鈴薯植株；<英，非正式>（尤指腳後跟部的）襪子破洞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Potatoes</b> are round vegetables with brown or red skins and white insides. They grow under the ground. 土豆","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a difficult subject that people disagree on as a <b>hot potato</b>. 燙手山芋","examples":["...a political hot potato such as abortion. …像墮胎這樣的政治性燙手山芋。"]}]}]},"positive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"樂觀的，有信心的；積極的，建設性的；良好的，有助益的；贊成的，支援的；確信的，肯定的；完全的，絕對的；證據確鑿的，明確的；陽性的；正數的，大於零的；正電的，正極的；（攝影）正片的，正像的；（語法）（形容詞，副詞）原級的；（主哲）實證的，實在的；（占星）（風宮，火宮）積極的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"優勢，優點；陽性結果；正片；正極，陽極；正數；（語法）原級形容詞，原級副詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>positive</b> <b>about</b> things, you are hopeful and confident, and think of the good aspects of a situation rather than the bad ones. (心態) 積極的","examples":["Be positive about your future and get on with living a normal life. 要積極面對未來，習慣過一種平常生活。","Her husband became much more positive and was soon back in full-time employment. 她丈夫變得積極多了，並且很快又幹起了全職工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>positive</b> fact, situation, or experience is pleasant and helpful to you in some way. 積極的 (事實、情形、經歷)","examples":["The parting from his sister had a positive effect on John. 和姐姐的分開對約翰有積極的影響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you make a <b>positive</b> decision or take <b>positive</b> action, you do something definite in order to deal with a task or problem. 積極的 (決定、行動等)","examples":["There are positive changes that should be implemented in the rearing of animals. 應該積極改變動物的飼養方式。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>positive</b> response to something indicates agreement, approval, or encouragement. 積極的 (回應)","examples":["There's been a positive response to the U.N. Secretary-General's recent peace efforts. 對聯合國秘書長最近的和平努力已有積極回應。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>positive</b> about something, you are completely sure about it. 肯定的","examples":["\"Judith's never late. You sure she said eight?\"—\"Positive.\" “朱迪絲從來不遲到，你肯定她說的是8點？”—“肯定。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Positive</b> evidence gives definite proof of the truth or identity of something. 確鑿的 (證據)","examples":["There was no positive evidence that any birth defects had arisen as a result of Vitamin A intake. 沒有確鑿證據表明攝入維生素A會導致先天缺陷。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If a medical or scientific test is <b>positive</b>, it shows that something has happened or is present. (化驗結果) 陽性的","examples":["If the test is positive, a course of antibiotics may be prescribed. 如果化驗結果呈陽性，可能要開一個療程的抗生素。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>positive</b> number is greater than zero. 正的 (數字)","examples":["It's really a simple numbers game with negative and positive numbers. 這其實是一種正負數的簡單數字遊戲。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something has a <b>positive</b> electrical charge, it has the same charge as a proton and the opposite charge to a neutron. 正的 (電荷)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"積極地","examples":["You really must try to start thinking positively. 你真得開始努力地積極思考問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"積極地","examples":["He responded positively and accepted the fee of $1,000 I had offered. 他作出了積極回應，接受了我提供的$1000的費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"確鑿地","examples":["He has positively identified the body as that of his wife. 他已確認那具屍體是他妻子的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The positive</b> in a situation is the good and pleasant aspects of it. 積極面","examples":["He prefers to focus on the positive. 他更願意關注積極面。"]}]}]},"praise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指公開地）讚美，表揚；（用語言或音樂）讚美（上帝）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"表揚，讚美；（對上帝的）感謝，崇拜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>praise</b> someone or something, you express approval for their achievements or qualities. 稱讚","examples":["The American president praised Turkey for its courage. 美國總統稱讚了土耳其的勇氣。","Many others praised Sanford for taking a strong stand. 還有許多人稱讚桑福德立場堅定。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Praise</b> is what you say or write about someone when you are praising them. 讚美","examples":["All the ladies are full of praise for the staff and service they received. 所有女士對工作人員和她們得到的服務讚不絕口。","I have nothing but praise for the police. 我對警察只有讚揚。"]}]}]},"plain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無裝飾的，樸素的；單色的，無花紋的；單純的，不摻雜的；顯而易見的；（書面或口頭用法）表達清楚的；直截了當的，坦率的；相貌平平的；普通的；直呼其名的；完全的；（編織）平針的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地，簡直；明白地，不含糊地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大）平原；（編織的）平針；樸實無華的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plain</b> object, surface, or fabric is entirely in one colour and has no pattern, design, or writing on it. 純色的","examples":["In general, a plain carpet makes a room look bigger. 一般來講，純色的地毯使房間顯得更大。","He placed the paper in a plain envelope. 他把論文放在一個空白信封裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>plain</b> is very simple in style. 樸素的","examples":["It was a plain, grey stone house. 這是一座簡樸的灰色石頭房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a fact, situation, or statement is <b>plain</b>, it is easy to recognize or understand. 清楚的","examples":["It was plain to him that I was having a nervous breakdown. 我那時神經衰弱，他是清楚的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>plain</b>, you think they look ordinary and not at all beautiful. 相貌平平的","examples":["...a shy, rather plain girl with a pale complexion. …一個害羞、相貌平平、臉色蒼白的女孩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"flat or smooth; level 平的; 平坦的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"樸素地","examples":["He was very tall and plainly dressed. 他個子很高，穿著樸素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(intensifier) (用以加強語氣)顯然; 非常","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plain</b> is a large flat area of land with very few trees on it. 平地","examples":["Once there were 70 million buffalo on the plains. 在這片平原上曾經生活著7000萬頭水牛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a police officer is <b>in plain clothes</b>, he or she is wearing ordinary clothes instead of a police uniform.  穿便衣的","examples":["Three officers in plain clothes told me to get out of the car. 三名便衣軍官叫我從車上下來。"]}]}]},"pound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磅（重量單位）；英鎊（英國貨幣單位）；一英鎊紙幣（或硬幣），一鎊紙幣（或硬幣）；英鎊與外幣的比值（the pound）；（流浪貓狗的）收留所，待領場；（違規停放車輛的）臨時扣押場；鎊（英國以外某些國家的貨幣單位）；井號鍵；<古> 拘留所，監禁所；重擊，重擊聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"連續重擊，猛打；（心臟）劇烈地跳動；（頭）劇痛；腳步聲沉重地走（跑）；連續轟炸，猛烈襲擊；搗碎，擊碎；長時間苦幹；<美，非正式> 快速地喝；<非正式> 徹底打敗（對手）；大聲播放；監禁，拘留"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pound</b> is a unit of weight used mainly in the U.S., Britain and other countries where English is spoken. One pound is equal to 0.454 kilograms. A <b>pound of</b> something is a quantity of it that weighs one pound. 磅 (英美等國的重量單位，等於0.454公斤); 一磅的量","examples":["Her weight was under ninety pounds. 她的體重不足90磅。","...a pound of cheese. …一磅乳酪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pound</b> is the unit of money which is used in Britain. It is represented by the symbol £. One British pound is divided into a hundred pence. Some other countries, for example, Egypt, also have a unit of money called a <b>pound</b>. 英鎊 (英國貨幣單位，等於100便士)","examples":["...multi-million pound profits. …數百萬英鎊的利潤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The pound</b> is used to refer to the British currency system, and sometimes to the currency systems of other countries which use pounds. 鎊制 (英國等國的幣制)","examples":["The pound is expected to continue to increase against most other currencies. 英鎊對多數其他貨幣的匯率有望繼續上升。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pound</b> is a place where dogs and cats found wandering in the street are taken and kept until they are claimed by their owners. (走失貓狗的) 認領處","examples":["...cages at the local pound. …本地走失貓狗認領處的籠子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>pound</b> is a place where cars that have been parked illegally are taken by the police and kept until they have been claimed by their owners. (被扣押的違章停放車輛的) 認領處","examples":["The car remained in the police pound for a month. 那輛汽車在警察局違章車輛認領處停放了一個月。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a heavy blow; thump 一次沉重打擊; 錘擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pound</b> something or <b>pound on</b> it, you hit it with great force, usually loudly and repeatedly. 連續重擊","examples":["He pounded the table with his fist. 他用拳頭猛扎桌子。","Somebody began pounding on the front door. 有人開始猛敲前門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pound</b> something, you crush it into a paste or a powder or into very small pieces. 搗碎","examples":["She pounded the corn kernels. 她搗碎了玉米粒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your heart <b>is pounding</b>, it is beating with an unusually strong and fast rhythm, usually because you are afraid. (心臟) 怦怦跳","examples":["I'm sweating, my heart is pounding. I can't breathe. 我在流汗、心臟也怦怦跳，透不過氣來。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to confine in or as if in a pound; impound, imprison, or restrain 扣押; 拘禁; 限制","examples":[]}]}]},"president":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"總統，國家主席；（機構、俱樂部、學院等的）負責人，會長，院長，主席；（公司）董事長，（銀行）行長，總裁；（基督教）聖餐主持教士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>president</b> of a country that has no king or queen is the person who is the head of state of that country. 總統","examples":["...President Mubarak. …穆巴拉克總統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>president</b> of an organization is the person who has the highest position in it. (某組織的) 最高權力人","examples":["...Alexandre de Merode, the president of the medical commission. …亞歷山大·德梅羅德，醫學委員會主席。"]}]}]},"presence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出席，存在；<正式>（某人的）所在地方；<文>感覺中的存在物（如鬼魂）；駐紮部隊，駐紮的警力；風度，氣質；（公司在某地的）工人（或產品），勢力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>presence</b> in a place is the fact that they are there. 在場","examples":["They argued that his presence in the town could only stir up trouble. 他們爭辯說他在城裡出現只會攪起麻煩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>presence</b>, you mean that they impress people by their appearance and manner. 風采","examples":["They do not seem to have the vast, authoritative presence of those great men. 他們似乎沒有那些大人物的軒昂威嚴的風采。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>presence</b> is a person or creature that you cannot see, but that you are aware of. 幽靈","examples":["She started to be affected by the ghostly presence she could feel in the house. 她開始受到那個幽靈的困擾，她能感覺到它就在屋子裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a country has a military <b>presence</b> in another country, it has some of its armed forces there. 駐紮","examples":["The Philippine government wants the U.S. to maintain a military presence in Southeast Asia. 菲律賓政府希望美國保留在東南亞的駐軍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>presence</b> of a substance in another thing, you mean that it is in that thing. 存在","examples":["The somewhat acid flavour is caused by the presence of lactic acid. 略有的酸味是由乳酸的存在造成的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in</b> someone's <b>presence</b>, you are in the same place as that person, and are close enough to them to be seen or heard. 在某人面前","examples":["The talks took place in the presence of a diplomatic observer. 會談是在一位外交觀察家在場的情況下進行的。"]}]}]},"post":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>郵政，郵遞；<英>郵件，包裹；<英>收集（或投遞）郵件，郵班；職位，要職；崗位，哨所；柱，杆，樁；（賽馬的）終點；球門柱；郵報（用於某些報紙名稱中）；帖子，線上留言板上的資訊；籃球場上籃筐附近的區域；策應位置；<美>退伍軍人協會地方分會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>郵寄；把……放入（或塞入）；派駐，委派；使駐守，設定（崗哨等）；張貼，公佈；釋出，發帖子；交付（保釋金）；（運動員，參賽隊）取得（成績），創造（紀錄）；（記賬用語）將……入賬"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……之後"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>post</b> notices, signs, or other pieces of information somewhere, you attach them to a wall or board so that everyone can see them. 張貼","examples":["Officials began posting warning notices. 官員們開始張貼警示佈告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>post</b> information on the Internet, you make the information available to other people on the Internet. (在網際網路上)發帖子","examples":["A consultation paper has been posted on the Internet inviting input from users. 一份諮詢檔案已經貼上了網際網路，懇請使用者們提供資訊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>post</b> a letter or package, you send it to someone by putting it in a postbox or by taking it to a post office. 投寄; 郵寄","examples":["Last year, he posted the documents to French journalists. 去年，他把這些檔案寄給了法國記者。","He mailed me the contract. 他把合同寄給了我。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are posted</b> somewhere, you are sent there by the organization that you work for and usually work there for several years. 派遣","examples":["After training she was posted to Biloxi. 培訓之後，她被派到了比洛克西。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a soldier, guard, or other person <b>is posted</b> somewhere, they are told to stand there, in order to supervise an activity or guard a place. 安置…站崗","examples":["Police have now been posted outside all temples. 已經在所有廟宇外安置了警察站崗。","They had to post a signalman at the entrance to the tunnel. 他們不得不在隧道入口處安置一名訊號員站崗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Post up</b> means the same as . 同post","examples":["He has posted a sign up that says \"No Fishing.\" 他已經張貼了一個標牌，寫著“禁止釣魚。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> someone <b>posted</b>, you keep giving them the latest information about a situation that they are interested in. 讓 (某人) 及時獲悉","examples":["Keep me posted on your progress. 讓我及時知道你的進展。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>post</b> to refer to letters and packages that are delivered to you. 郵件","examples":["There was no post except the usual junk addressed to the occupant. 除了寄給住戶的常見的垃圾郵件之外，沒有其他郵件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>post</b> in a company or organization is a job or official position in it, usually one that involves responsibility. 職位; 職務","examples":["She had earlier resigned her post as President Menem's assistant. 她已於早些時候辭去了梅內姆總統助理的職務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>post</b> is a strong upright pole made of wood or metal that is dug into the ground.  柱子","examples":["The device is fixed to a post. 該裝置固定在一根柱子上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>post</b> is the same as a . 球門柱","examples":["Jenkins missed a penalty, hitting the post in the thirteenth minute. 詹金斯在第十三分鐘時罰球不中，打在了門柱上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"On a horse-racing track, <b>the post</b> is a pole that marks the finishing point.  終點柱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"with speed; rapidly 快速地; 迅速地","examples":[]}]}]},"pot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鍋；（盛食品的）罐，瓶；壺；花盆；陶盆，陶罐，碗；一罐，一壺（的量）；（紙牌遊戲的）全部賭注；湊集的資金；<非正式>大麻；<非正式>大量；大肚子；（球等的）擊球入袋；幼兒用便盆；<非正式>發動機氣缸；<非正式>（體育運動的）獎品，獎盃；射擊；（主要用於橄欖球）射門"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（植物）栽入盆中；將（食物）用密封罐煮（或儲存）；射殺（動物）；擊（球）入袋；製陶；<非正式>成功獲得，贏得；把（電子元件，電路）密封於絕緣材料中；<英>使（小孩）坐便盆；得（分）"}],"sections":[]},"princess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（除女王或王后外的）王室女成員，（尤指）公主；王妃，王公貴族夫人；（受寵溺而自以為優越的）嬌小姐；<英，非正式>大小姐；小國女君主；出眾的婦女（或事物），巾幗英雄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>princess</b> is a female member of a royal family, usually the daughter of a king or queen or the wife of a prince. 公主; 王妃","examples":["Princess Anne topped the guest list. 安妮公主的名字位於來賓名單之首。"]}]}]},"pride":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自豪（感）；自尊（心）；傲慢，自負；<文>最佳狀態，全盛期；獅群；引以為傲的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以……自豪（pride oneself on/upon）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pride</b> is a feeling of satisfaction that you have because you or people close to you have done something good or possess something good. 自豪","examples":["...the sense of pride in a job well done. …因一項工作完成得很好而感到的自豪。","We take pride in offering you the highest standards. 我們以向您提供最高標準的服務而自豪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pride</b> is a sense of the respect that other people have for you, and that you have for yourself. 尊嚴","examples":["Davis had to salvage his pride. 戴維斯不得不挽回自己的尊嚴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>pride</b> is the feeling that they have that they are better or more important than other people. 傲慢","examples":["His pride may still be his downfall. 他的傲慢仍可能是他垮臺的原因。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pride</b> yourself <b>on</b> a quality or skill that you have, you are very proud of it. 以…而自豪","examples":["Suarez prides himself on being able to organize his own life. 蘇亞雷斯為能安排好自己的生活而自豪。"]}]}]},"prince":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王子，王孫；（小國的）國君，親王；佼佼者，名家； （某些歐洲國家的）貴族"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prince</b> is a male member of a royal family, especially the son of the king or queen of a country. 王子","examples":["...Prince Edward and other royal guests. …愛德華王子和其他王室貴賓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>prince</b> is the male royal ruler of a small country or state. (小國的) 君王","examples":["He was speaking without the prince's authority. 他在未經君王許可而發言。"]}]}]},"printer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"印表機；印刷商，印刷工人，印刷公司"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>printer</b> is a machine that can be connected to a computer in order to make copies on paper of documents or other information held by the computer. 印表機","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>printer</b> is a person or company whose job is printing things such as books. 印刷工; 印刷公司","examples":["The manuscript had already been sent off to the printer. 手稿已經送到印刷廠去了。"]}]}]},"present":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）在場的，出席的；（事物）存在的；現在的，目前的；考慮中的，正在討論的；（語法）現在時（態）的；歷歷在目的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"現在，目前；禮物，贈品；（語法）現在時；（舉槍的）瞄準（姿勢）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"頒發，贈送；出示（護照等供檢查）；正式提交（支票，賬單）；<正式> 正式引見，介紹；正式出席，到場；引起，造成；<正式>表達（歉意等）；提出，陳述；上映，播出；展示，表現；<英> 主持（廣播或電視節目）；把……對準；<醫>（病人）呈現症狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>present</b> to describe things and people that exist now, rather than those that existed in the past or those that may exist in the future. 目前的","examples":["He has brought much of the present crisis on himself. 他目前的危機大多是他自己造成的。","...the government's present economic difficulties. …政府目前的經濟困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>present at</b> an event, they are there. 在場的","examples":["The president was not present at the meeting. 總統沒有出席該會議。","Nearly 85 percent of men are present at the birth of their children. 將近85%的男性在他們的孩子出生時在場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something, especially a substance or disease, is <b>present in</b> something else, it exists within that thing. 存在的","examples":["This special form of vitamin D is naturally present in breast milk. 這種特殊形式的維生素D天然存在於母乳中。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The present</b> is the period of time that we are in now and the things that are happening now. 現在","examples":["...his struggle to reconcile the past with the present. …他將過去和現在調和的鬥爭。","...continuing right up to the present. …一直持續到現在。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>present</b> is something that you give to someone, for example, at Christmas or when you visit them. 禮物","examples":["The carpet was a wedding present from Jack's parents. 地毯是傑克的父母送的結婚禮物。","She bought a birthday present for her mother. 她為她母親買了一件生日禮物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"頒發","examples":["Then came the presentation of the awards by the First Lady. 接下來是第一夫人的頒獎。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"陳述","examples":["...in his first presentation of the theory to the Berlin Academy. …在他第一次向柏林科學院陳述該理論時。","...a fair presentation of the facts to a jury. …向陪審團對事實的公正的陳述。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A situation that exists <b>at present</b> exists now, although it may change. 目前","examples":["There is no way at present of predicting which individuals will develop the disease. 目前還沒有辦法預言哪些人會患這種病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The present day</b> is the period of history that we are in now. 現代","examples":["...Western European art from the period of Giotto to the present day. …從喬託時代到現代的西歐藝術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that exists or will be done <b>for the present</b> exists now or will continue for a while, although the situation may change later. 暫時","examples":["The cabinet had expressed the view that sanctions should remain in place for the present. 內閣曾表示說制裁會暫時保留。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>present</b> someone <b>with</b> something such as a prize or document, or if you <b>present</b> it <b>to</b> them, you formally give it to them. 頒發","examples":["The mayor presented him with a gold medal at an official city reception. 市長在一次正式的市招待會上給他頒發了一枚金質獎章。","Betty will present the prizes to the winners. 貝蒂將給獲勝者頒獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>presents</b> a difficulty, challenge, or opportunity, it causes it or provides it. 帶來","examples":["This presents a problem for many financial consumers. 這給許多金融消費者帶來了麻煩。","The future is going to be one that presents many challenges. 未來將會帶來許多挑戰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an opportunity or problem <b>presents</b> <b>itself</b>, it occurs, often when you do not expect it. (機會、問題) 呈現出來","examples":["Their colleagues insulted them whenever the opportunity presented itself. 他們的同事們一有機會就侮辱他們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>present</b> information, you give it to people in a formal way. 展示","examples":["We spend the time collating and presenting the information in a variety of chart forms. 我們把時間花在以各種圖表形式比照和展示資訊上。","We presented three options to the unions for discussion. 我們向工會提出了3種選擇以供討論。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>present</b> someone or something in a particular way, you describe them in that way. 描述","examples":["The government has presented these changes as major reforms. 政府將這些變化描述成重大改革。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The way you <b>present yourself</b> is the way you speak and act when meeting new people. 展示 (自己)","examples":["...all those tricks which would help him to present himself in a more confident way in public. …所有那些可以幫助他在公共場合更自信地展示自己的竅門。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If someone or something <b>presents</b> a particular appearance or image, that is how they appear or try to appear. 表現出","examples":["The small group of onlookers presented a pathetic sight. 那一小撮旁觀者表現出一副可憐的樣子。","Cohen was making an effort to present a kinder, gentler image. 科恩在努力表現出一副更和善、更溫柔的形象。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>present yourself</b> somewhere, you officially arrive there, for example, for an appointment. 出席","examples":["Get word to him right away that he's to present himself at City Hall by tomorrow afternoon. 立即通知他，他得於明天下午之前到市政廳來。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If someone <b>presents</b> a programme on television or radio, they introduce each item in it. 主持 (電視或廣播節目)","examples":["She also presents a show on St Petersburg Radio. 她還在聖彼得斯堡電臺主持一個節目。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"When someone <b>presents</b> something such as a production of a play or an exhibition, they organize it. 上演; 展出","examples":["They threatened to close any theatre presenting a play with gay characters. 他們威脅要關閉任何上演有同性戀角色戲劇的劇院。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you <b>present</b> someone <b>to</b> someone else, often an important person, you formally introduce them. 正式介紹","examples":["Fox stepped forward, welcomed him in Malay, and presented him to Jack. 福克斯向前跨了一步，用馬來語對他表示了歡迎，接著把他正式介紹給了傑克。"]}]}]},"principal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最重要的，首要的；本金的，母金的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（美國公立中小學的）校長；<英>（英國的）大學校長，學院院長；（企業或機構的）負責人；（音樂會、戲劇、芭蕾舞劇、歌劇中的）主角演員；（管絃樂隊每一樂器組的）首席演奏者；（有利息的）本金，資金；（法律和商業事務中的）當事人，委託人；關鍵人物；（某些行業）完全合格的開業者；<英>（負責某一部門的）高階公務員；主犯，首犯；<史>決鬥者；（支撐檁的）主椽；（管風琴的）主音栓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Principal</b> means first in order of importance. 最重要的","examples":["The principal reason for my change of mind is this. 我改變主意的最重要原因就是這個。","...the country's principal source of foreign exchange earnings. …該國最重要的外匯交易收入來源。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>principal</b> of a school is the person in charge of the school or college. 校長","examples":["Donald King is the principal of Dartmouth High School. 唐納德·金是達特茅斯中學的校長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>principal</b> of a loan is the original amount of the loan, on which you pay interest. (貸款的) 本金","examples":[]}]}]},"prison":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監獄，牢房；監禁，監獄制度；難以脫身的地方（或處境），牢籠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>禁錮，關押"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prison</b> is a building where criminals are kept as punishment. 監獄","examples":["The prison's inmates are being kept in their cells. 監獄裡的囚犯們被關在各自的牢房裡。"]}]}]},"prisoner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犯人，囚犯；俘虜，戰俘；為……所困的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prisoner</b> is a person who is kept in a prison as a punishment for a crime that they have committed. 囚犯","examples":["The committee is concerned about the large number of prisoners sharing cells. 該委員會很關心共用牢房的大量犯人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>prisoner</b> is a person who has been captured by an enemy, for example, in war. 俘虜","examples":["...wartime hostages and concentration-camp prisoners. …戰時的人質們和集中營的戰俘們。"]}]}]},"principle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（行為）準則，（道德）原則；道義，正直；基本原則，基本法則；（機器等或自然界的）原理，定律；（宗教或政治的）主義，信條；起源，本原；本質，實質；（化）成分，要素"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>principle</b> is a general belief about the way you should behave, which influences your behaviour. 原則","examples":["Buck never allowed himself to be bullied into doing anything that went against his principles. 巴克從來不讓自己被迫做任何違背自己原則的事。","It's not just a matter of principle. 這不僅僅是個原則問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>principles</b> <b>of</b> a particular theory or philosophy are its basic rules or laws. (理論或哲學) 原理","examples":["...a violation of the basic principles of Marxism. …對馬克思主義基本原理的一種違背。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Scientific <b>principles</b> are general scientific laws which explain how something happens or works. (科學) 原理","examples":["These people lack all understanding of scientific principles. 這些人缺乏對科學原理的全面理解。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you agree with something <b>in principle</b>, you agree in general terms to the idea of it, although you do not yet know the details or know if it will be possible. 原則上","examples":["I agree with it in principle but I doubt if it will happen in practice. 我原則上是同意它的，但我懷疑在實踐中它是否會發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is possible <b>in principle</b>, there is no known reason why it should not happen, even though it has not happened before. 在理論上","examples":["Even assuming this to be in principle possible, it will not be achieved soon. 即使假定這在理論上是可能的，它也不會很快就能實現。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refuse to do something <b>on principle</b>, you refuse to do it because of a particular belief that you have. 依據原則","examples":["He would vote against it on principle. 他會依據原則投票反對它。"]}]}]},"press":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞工作者，新聞界，報刊（the press）；新聞報道；新聞輿論，媒體評論；印刷機；出版社，印刷廠；印刷；按，壓，熨；壓平器，熨燙機；人群，擁擠；<愛，蘇格蘭>大壁櫥，衣櫃，書櫃；（籃球）緊逼；（舉重）推舉；<史>（尤指海軍的）強行徵兵；<舊>商業壓力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓，擠，推，貼；按，撳；困擾，嚴重影響；擠著走；敦促，逼迫；堅持，竭力要求；壓平，熨平；壓榨，榨汁；CD 製作，壓制（唱片）；（深情地）緊握（某人的手或臂）；前進，推進；（敵人，對手）進逼，進攻；（高爾夫）過猛擊球；徵用，臨時使用；（舉重）推舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> something somewhere, you push it firmly against something else. 推; 擠","examples":["He pressed his back against the door. 他將背頂在了門上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> a button or switch, you push it with your finger in order to make a machine or device work. 按壓","examples":["Drago pressed a button and the door closed. 德拉戈按了一個按鈕，門關上了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> something or <b>press down on</b> it, you push hard against it with your foot or hand. 用力按; 用力踩","examples":["The engine stalled. He pressed the accelerator hard. 引擎熄火了。他猛踩油門。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> someone, you try hard to persuade them to do something. 極力勸說","examples":["Trade unions are pressing him to stand firm. 各工會在極力勸說他堅持立場。","Mr. Kurtz seems certain to be pressed for further details. 庫爾茨先生似乎肯定會被極力勸說說出更多細節。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>presses</b> their claim, demand, or point, they state it in a very forceful way. 有力陳述","examples":["The protest campaign has used mass strikes and demonstrations to press its demands. 抗議活動採用了大規模罷工和示威遊行來有力地表明其要求。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> something <b>on</b> someone, you give it to them and insist that they take it. 硬塞","examples":["All I had was money, which I pressed on her reluctant mother. 我只有錢，硬塞給了她那不肯接受我錢的母親。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>press</b> clothes, you iron them in order to get rid of the creases. 熨","examples":["Vera pressed his shirt. 薇拉熨了他的襯衣。","There's a couple of dresses to be pressed. 有幾條連衣裙要熨。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Press</b> is also a noun. 按壓","examples":["...a TV which rises from a table at the press of a button. …按一個按鈕就會從桌上升起的一臺電視機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any machine that exerts pressure to form, shape, or cut materials or to extract liquids, compress solids, or hold components together while an adhesive joint is formed 擠壓機; 壓力機; 打包機","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Newspapers are referred to as <b>the press</b>. 報紙","examples":["...interviews in the local and foreign press. …當地和國外報紙中的採訪。","...freedom of the press. …新聞自由。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Journalists and reporters are referred to as <b>the press</b>. 新聞工作者","examples":["Christie looked relaxed and calm as she faced the press afterwards. 克里斯蒂之後面對新聞工作者時看上去輕鬆平靜。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>press</b> or a <b>printing press</b> is a machine used for printing things such as books and newspapers. 印刷機","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"recruitment into military service by forcible measures, as by a press gang 抓丁入伍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>press for</b> something, you try hard to persuade someone to give it to you or to agree to it. 竭力爭取","examples":["Police might now press for changes in the law. 警方現在可能會竭力爭取法律的修改。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to recruit (men) by forcible measures for military service (對男人)強征服兵役","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>gets bad press</b>, they are criticized, especially in the newspapers, on television, or on radio. If they <b>get good press</b>, they are praised. 受到媒體批評/好評","examples":["...the bad press that career women consistently get in this country. …在這個國家職業女性一貫受到的媒體批評一家先前不知名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>press charges</b> <b>against</b> someone, you make an official accusation against them that has to be decided in a court of law. 起訴","examples":["I could have pressed charges against him. 我原本可以起訴他的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a newspaper or magazine <b>goes to press</b>, it starts being printed. 付印","examples":["We check prices at the time of going to press. 我們在付印時核對價格。"]}]}]},"producer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生產者製造商，生產公司（國）；（人或物）造成者，生產者；（電影、廣播戲劇、歌劇等的）製片主任，監製人；（音樂錄音的）監製人；發生器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>producer</b> is a person whose job is to produce plays, movies, programmes, or CDs. (戲劇、電影、節目、唱片等的) 製作人","examples":["...a freelance film producer. …一名獨立電影製片人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>producer</b> of a food or material is a company or country that grows or manufactures a large amount of it. (食品、材料等的) 生產者","examples":["...Saudi Arabia, the world's leading oil producer. …沙烏地阿拉伯，世界上最重要的石油生產國。"]}]}]},"prize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎品，獎項；非常珍貴的人（或物），十分重要的人（或物）；<史>（海戰中）繳獲的敵船"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可獲獎的，優等的；作為獎品的；獲獎的；有獎的；<英，非正式>完全的；非常重要的，珍貴的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"珍視，高度重視；<美>撬開；竭力打探（訊息等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prize</b> is money or something valuable that is given to someone who has the best results in a competition or game, or as a reward for doing good work. 獎品; 獎金","examples":["You must claim your prize by telephoning our claims line. 你必須透過打我們的領獎熱線來領取獎品。","He was awarded the Nobel Prize for Physics in 1985. 他獲得了1985年諾貝爾物理學獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone or something as a <b>prize</b> when people consider them to be of great value or importance. 有價值之人; 有價值之物","examples":["With no lands of his own, he was no great matrimonial prize. 沒有自己的土地，他絕不是個有價值的結婚物件。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>prize</b> to describe things that are of such good quality that they win prizes or deserve to win prizes. 獲獎的; 應獲獎的","examples":["...a prize bull. …一頭獲獎的公牛。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>is prized</b> is wanted and admired because it is considered to be very valuable or very good quality. 青睞","examples":["Military figures made out of lead are prized by collectors. 用鉛做的軍人塑像很受收藏者們青睞。"]}]}]},"pumpkin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"南瓜，倭瓜；南瓜藤；<美>小南瓜（一種稱呼所愛的人的方式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pumpkin</b> is a large, round, orange vegetable with a thick skin. 南瓜","examples":["Quarter the pumpkin and remove the seeds. 把南瓜一切四塊，把南瓜子取出來。"]}]}]},"progress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"進步，進展；前進，行進；（社會的）進步"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進步，進展；使（任務，事業）取得持續進展；（時間）推移，流逝；緩慢行進；（占星）計算行星（或星象圖各星及座標）的位置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Progress</b> is the process of gradually improving or getting nearer to achieving or completing something. 進步","examples":["The medical community continues to make progress in the fight against cancer. 醫學界繼續在抗癌鬥爭中取得進步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>progress</b> <b>of</b> a situation or action is the way in which it develops. 進展","examples":["The president is reported to have been delighted with the progress of the first day's talks. 據報道，總統對第一天會談的進展很滿意。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>progress</b> means to move over a period of time to a stronger, more advanced, or more desirable state. 進展","examples":["He will visit once every two weeks to see how his new employees are progressing. 他將每兩週視察一次以看看他的新僱員們進展如何。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If events <b>progress</b>, they continue to happen gradually over a period of time. 繼續進行","examples":["As the evening progressed, sadness turned to rage. 隨著夜晚的來臨，悲傷變成了憤怒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>progress</b> something, you cause it to develop. 使…發展","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in progress</b>, it has started and is still continuing. 在進行中","examples":["The game was already in progress when we took our seats. 比賽在我們坐下時已經在進行了。"]}]}]},"produce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引起，造成；（自然地）生產，產生；（尤指用機器）生產，製造；（運用技巧）製作，造出；（某地、某過程或制度）出產，產出；出示，拿出；監製，製作（電影或戲劇）；生育；<舊>使（線段）延長"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"農產品；（尤指某人工作或努力的）成果，結果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>produce</b> something means to cause it to happen. 使發生","examples":["The drug is known to produce side-effects in women. 眾所周知，這種藥會在女性身上產生各種副作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>produce</b> something, you make or create it. 生產","examples":["The company produced circuitry for communications systems. 這家公司為通訊系統生產電路系統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When things or people <b>produce</b> something, it comes from them or slowly forms from them, especially as the result of a biological or chemical process. 生長出; 生育出","examples":["These plants are then pollinated and allowed to mature and produce seed. 這些植物之後被授粉，使其成熟、結籽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>produce</b> evidence or an argument, you show it or explain it to people in order to make them agree with you. 給出 (證據、論據等)","examples":["They challenged him to produce evidence to support his allegations. 他們要求他給出證據來支撐他的斷言。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>produce</b> an object from somewhere, you show it or bring it out so that it can be seen. 出示","examples":["To rent a car you must produce a passport and a current driving licence. 要租一輛車你必須出示護照和現有駕照。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>produces</b> something such as a movie, a magazine, or a CD, they organize it and decide how it should be done. 製作 (電影、雜誌、唱片等)","examples":["He has produced his own sports magazine. 他已經創辦了自己的體育雜誌。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Produce</b> is fruit and vegetables that are grown in large quantities to be sold. 農產品","examples":["We manage to get most of our produce in farmers' markets. 我們設法在農貿市場弄到大部分我們需要的農產品。"]}]}]},"pudding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"布丁（用大米、麵包等做成的甜食）；<美>（餐後）冷布丁（一種黏稠的乳脂狀甜食）；<英>（餐末的）甜食，甜點；<英>肉餡布丁；<英>血香腸，黑香腸；<英，非正式>矮胖子，呆頭呆腦的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pudding</b> is a cooked sweet food made from ingredients such as milk, sugar, flour, and eggs, and is served either hot or cold. 布丁","examples":["...a banana vanilla pudding. …一份香蕉香草布丁。"]}]}]},"pupil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學生，（尤指）小學生；弟子，門生；瞳孔；<英>見習律師；<法律>未成年人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pupil</b> of a painter, musician, or other expert is someone who studies under that expert and learns his or her skills. (畫家、音樂家等的) 弟子","examples":["After his education, Goldschmidt became a pupil of the composer Franz Schreker. 上完學後，戈爾德施密特成了作曲家弗朗茲·施雷克的弟子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pupils</b> of a school are the children who go to it. 學生","examples":["...schools with over 1,000 pupils. …有1000多名學生的學校。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>pupils</b> of your eyes are the small, round, black holes in the centre of them. 瞳孔","examples":["The sick man's pupils were dilated. 病人的瞳孔放大了。"]}]}]},"punishment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懲罰手段，處罰；粗暴對待，糟蹋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Punishment</b> is the act of punishing someone or of being punished. 懲罰","examples":["...a group that campaigns against the physical punishment of children. …一個發起運動反對體罰兒童的組織。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>punishment</b> is a particular way of punishing someone. 處罰方式","examples":["The government is proposing tougher punishments for officials convicted of corruption. 該政府正在提議對被判貪汙罪的官員予以更嚴厲的處罰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>punishment</b> to refer to severe physical treatment of any kind. 虐待; 糟蹋","examples":["Don't expect these boots to take the punishment that gardening will give them. 別指望這樣的靴子能經得起園藝活兒的糟蹋。"]}]}]},"puppy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小狗，幼犬（=pup）；<非正式，舊>自負（或傲慢）的年輕人；玩意兒（戲謔語）；人，傢伙（戲謔語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>puppy</b> is a young dog. 幼犬","examples":["One Sunday he began trying to teach the two puppies to walk on a leash. 一個星期天，他開始試著教兩隻幼犬栓著皮帶走路。"]}]}]},"puppet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木偶；傀儡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>puppet</b> is a doll that you can move, either by pulling strings that are attached to it or by putting your hand inside its body and moving your fingers. 木偶","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a person or country as a <b>puppet</b> when you mean that their actions are controlled by a more powerful person or government, even though they may appear to be independent. 傀儡","examples":["When the invasion occurred he seized power and ruled the country as a puppet of the occupiers. 他趁入侵之時奪取了政權，作為佔領者的傀儡統治著這個國家。"]}]}]},"promise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"承諾，保證；使很可能，預示；指望，期待（promise oneself）；<古>把（某人，尤指女人）許配給；有指望，有前途"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"承諾，諾言；前途，指望；跡象，預示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>promise</b> <b>that</b> you will do something, you say to someone that you will definitely do it. 承諾","examples":["The post office has promised to resume first class mail delivery to the area on Friday. 郵局已承諾在星期五恢復該地區第一類郵件的遞送。","He had promised that the rich and privileged would no longer get preferential treatment. 他已承諾富人和特權階層將不會再得到優待。","Promise me you will not waste your time. 向我承諾你不會浪費你的時間。","I'll call you back, I promise. 我會給你回電話的，我保證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>promise</b> someone something, you tell them that you will definitely give it to them or make sure that they have it. 向 (某人) 承諾 (給予他們某物); 向 (某人) 保證 (他們獲得某物)","examples":["In 1920 the great powers promised them an independent state. 1920年，列強們曾答應讓他們成為一個獨立國家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a situation or event <b>promises</b> <b>to</b> have a particular quality or <b>to</b> be a particular thing, it shows signs that it will have that quality or be that thing. 預示","examples":["While it will be fun, the seminar also promises to be most instructive. 這次專題討論會將會很有趣，也一定會非常有啟發性。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>promise</b> is a statement that you make to a person in which you say that you will definitely do something or give them something. 諾言","examples":["If you make a promise, you should keep it. 如果你許下一個諾言，你就應該遵守它。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something shows <b>promise</b>, they seem likely to be very good or successful. (顯示出) 成功的跡象","examples":["The boy first showed promise as an athlete in grade school. 這個男孩最初是在小學顯示出成為一名成功的運動員的跡象。"]}]}]},"pump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泵，抽水機；<英>平底鞋，輕軟舞鞋；<美>高跟無帶女鞋；抽吸，泵送；（生理）泵（指特定離子逆濃度梯度進行的跨膜主動運輸機制）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用泵（或泵樣器官等）輸送；快速上下（或內外）運動；湧出，湧流；<非正式> 盤問，套問；<非正式> 讓某人使用大量藥物；<非正式> 舉重（pump iron）；給......洗胃；<非正式> 不斷製造（pump out）；<非正式>大量增加（pump up）；<非正式>接連發射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pump</b> is a machine or device that is used to force a liquid or gas to flow in a particular direction. 泵","examples":["...pumps that circulate the fuel around in the engine. …使燃料在發動機內迴圈的壓泵。","There was no water in the building, just a pump in the courtyard. 樓裡沒水，只在院子裡有個水泵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A fuel or petrol <b>pump</b> is a machine with a tube attached to it that you use to fill a car with petrol. 加油泵","examples":["The average price for all grades of petrol at the pump was $3.49 a gallon. 加油泵所有等級的汽油平均價格為1加侖3.49美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Pumps</b> are the same as. 同court shoes","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a low-cut low-heeled shoe without fastenings, worn esp for dancing 舞鞋","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>pump</b> a liquid or gas in a particular direction means to force it to flow in that direction using a pump.  抽送","examples":["It's not enough to get rid of raw sewage by pumping it out to sea. 僅用水泵將未經處理的汙水排入海中是不夠的。","The money raised will be used to dig bore holes to pump water into the dried-up lake. 籌到的錢款將用來挖井眼，再將水抽入乾涸的湖中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>has</b> their stomach <b>pumped</b>, doctors remove the contents of their stomach, for example, because they have swallowed poison or drugs. 洗胃","examples":["One woman was rushed to the emergency room to have her stomach pumped. 一名婦女被緊急送進急診室去洗胃。"]}]}]},"project":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專案，計劃；（學校的）課題，研究專案；<美>廉租房區，公共房屋區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"預計，推算；計劃，規劃；伸出，突出；投擲，噴射；投射，投影；展現，表現；使（聲音，尤指嗓音）擴及遠處；傳播；想像（自己、場景等）在另一地點或時間；（尤指無意地把情感、願望）投射轉移（給別人）；使（某人）迅速成功，讓（某人）獲得更好的工作；作（曲線）的射影圖；把（地球，天空等）投影在平面上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>project</b> is a task that requires a lot of time and effort. 專案","examples":["Money will also go into local development projects in Vietnam. 資金也會流入越南本地開發專案。","...an international science project. …一個國際科研專案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>project</b> is a detailed study of a subject by a student. (學生研究的) 課題","examples":["Students complete projects for a personal tutor, working at home at their own pace. 學生們為個人導師完成課題研究，在家裡按自己的速度工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is projected</b>, it is planned or expected. 計劃; 預計","examples":["13% of Americans are over 65; this number is projected to reach 22% by the year 2030. 13%的美國人在65歲以上；這個數字預計到2030年會達到22%。","The government had been projecting a 5% consumer price increase for the entire year. 政府一直在預計全年5%的消費價格增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>project</b> someone or something in a particular way, you try to make people see them in that way. If you <b>project</b> a particular feeling or quality, you show it in your behaviour. (以某方式) 呈現","examples":["Bradley projects a natural warmth and sincerity. 布拉德利表現出一種自然的熱情和真誠。","He just hasn't been able to project himself as the strong leader. 他只是還沒能把自己表現得是個強有力的領導。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>project</b> a film or picture <b>onto</b> a screen or wall, you make it appear there. 投映","examples":["The team tried projecting the maps with two different projectors onto the same screen. 該組嘗試用兩臺不同的放映機將地圖投映在同一螢幕上。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>projects</b>, it sticks out above or beyond a surface or edge. 突出","examples":["...a narrow ledge that projected out from the bank of the river. …河岸邊突出來的一塊狹長的巖脊。"]}]}]},"purse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>錢包，皮夾子（尤指女用的）；<美>（女用）手提包，手袋；資金，財源；（體育競賽中的）獎金"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"噘嘴，撮起嘴唇（以表示反對等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>purse</b> is a small bag or a handbag that women carry. 女式手袋","examples":["She looked at me and then reached in her purse for cigarettes. 她看了看我，然後從手袋裡掏香菸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>purse</b> is a very small bag that people, especially women, keep their money in. (尤指女式) 錢包","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Purse</b> is used to refer to the total amount of money that a country, family, or group has. (國家、家庭、團體等的) 財力","examples":["The money could simply go into the public purse, helping to lower taxes. 這筆錢可以直接劃入國庫，來幫助降低稅收。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>purse</b> your <b>lips</b>, you move them into a small, rounded shape, usually because you disapprove of something or when you are thinking. 撅 (嘴)","examples":["She pursed her lips in disapproval. 她噘起嘴唇反對。"]}]}]},"puzzle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使困惑，使迷惑；（因迷惑而）苦思，冥思苦想；（透過苦苦思索）解決（或弄清楚），理出頭緒（puzzle sth. out）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"測驗智力（或知識）的遊戲（或玩具，問題）；拼圖遊戲，拼圖玩具；令人費解的人（或事物），難題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>puzzles</b> you, you do not understand it and feel confused. 使…迷惑不解","examples":["My sister puzzles me and causes me anxiety. 我的妹妹常會讓我不解，使我焦慮。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人迷惑不解的","examples":["His letter poses a number of puzzling questions. 他的信中提出了幾個令人迷惑不解的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>puzzle over</b> something, you try hard to think of the answer to it or the explanation for it. 對…苦苦思索","examples":["In rehearsing Shakespeare, I puzzle over the complexities of his verse and prose. 排演莎士比亞戲劇時，我苦苦地思索著他詩歌和散文中的複雜難懂之處。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>puzzle</b> is a question, game, or toy that you have to think about carefully in order to answer it correctly or put it together properly. 智力問題 (或遊戲、玩具)","examples":["...a word puzzle. …一條字謎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a person or thing that is hard to understand as <b>a puzzle</b>. 謎一樣的人或事物","examples":["The rise in accidents remains a puzzle. 事故的增多仍是個謎。"]}]}]},"quantity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"量，數目；大量，大批；（尤指和質量相對的）數量；（語音）音量；值，參量；代表數量（或參量）的數（或符號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quantity</b> is an amount. 數量","examples":["...a small quantity of water. …少量的水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Things that are produced or available in <b>quantity</b> are produced or available in large amounts. 大量","examples":["After some initial problems, acetone was successfully produced in quantity. 解決了最初的一些問題後，成功地生產出了大量丙酮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>quantity</b> to refer to the amount of something that there is, especially when you want to contrast it with its quality. (尤指相對於質量而言的) 數量","examples":["...the less discerning drinker who prefers quantity to quality. …重量不重質、識別力較差的飲酒者。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is an <b>unknown quantity</b>, you mean that not much is known about what they are like or how they will behave. 未知量; 未知數","examples":["She had known Max for some years now, but he was still pretty much an unknown quantity. 她現在認識馬克斯也好幾年了，但是他仍然是個大大的未知數。"]}]}]},"quality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"質量，品質；優質，上乘；素質，品德；特徵，特質；（語音）音質，音色；<英>（供有品位者閱讀的）高質量報紙（=quality newspaper）；（占星）黃道宮運動三大特徵之一"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"優質的，高質量的；<英>（報紙）內容嚴肅的，高階的；<英，俚>棒極了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>quality</b> of something is how good or bad it is. 質量","examples":["Everyone can greatly improve the quality of life. 人人都能大幅提高生活質量。","Other services vary dramatically in quality. 其它服務在質量上差異很大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something of <b>quality</b> is of a high standard. 優質","examples":["...a college of quality. …一所優質學院"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>qualities</b> are the good characteristics that they have which are part of their nature. 優良品質","examples":["Sometimes you wonder where your kids get their good qualities. 有時候你會奇怪，自己的孩子是在哪裡養成那些優良品德的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe a particular characteristic of a person or thing as a <b>quality</b>. 個性; 特性","examples":["...a childlike quality. …孩子般的個性"]}]}]},"rabbit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兔；兔肉，兔毛；<非正式>（運動）新手，蹩腳運動員（尤指蹩腳板球擊球手）；<英，非正式>閒聊，拉呱；<美>（長跑頭幾圈的）領跑者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獵兔；<英，非正式>喋喋不休，嘮叨；<非正式>快速移動，逃跑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rabbit</b> is a small, furry animal with long ears. Rabbits are sometimes kept as pets, or live wild in holes in the ground. 兔子","examples":[]}]}]},"quiz":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"問答比賽，智力競賽；<美>小測驗；<英，非正式>（尤指警方調查或正式調查中的）詢問，審問；<古>惡作劇，戲弄；<古>戲弄他人者，惡作劇者；<古>（性格、相貌）古怪的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"詢問，審問；<美>測驗（學生，班級）；<古>（透過鏡片）好奇地（或仔細地）打量；<古>戲弄，取笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quiz</b> is a test, game, or competition in which someone tests your knowledge by asking you questions. 測試; 知識競賽","examples":["We'll have a quiz at the end of class. 下課前我們將進行一次測試。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are quizzed</b> by someone about something, they ask you questions about it. 詢問","examples":["He was quizzed about his income, debts and eligibility for financial aid. 他被詢問了收入、債務以及經濟補助資格等。"]}]}]},"rectangle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矩形，長方形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rectangle</b> is a four-sided shape whose corners are all ninety-degree angles. Each side of a rectangle is the same length as the one opposite to it. 長方形","examples":[]}]}]},"reality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"真實，現實；實際經歷，見到的事物；真實感，逼真性；存在；（哲學）實在，實在性"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真人秀節目的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>reality</b> to refer to real things or the real nature of things rather than imagined, invented, or theoretical ideas. 現實","examples":["Fiction and reality were increasingly blurred. 小說與現實越來越混淆難分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>reality</b> <b>of</b> a situation is the truth about it, especially when it is unpleasant or difficult to deal with. (尤指令人不快或難對付的) 真實情形","examples":["...the harsh reality of top international competition. …頂級的國際競爭的殘酷現實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that something has become a <b>reality</b> when it actually exists or is actually happening. 事實存在; 真實發生的事","examples":["...the whole procedure that made this book become a reality. …使這本書的出版成為現實的整個過程。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>in reality</b> to introduce a statement about the real nature of something, when it contrasts with something incorrect that has just been described. 事實上; 實際上","examples":["He came across as streetwise, but in reality he was not. 他看似適應都市的生活，但事實上他不是。"]}]}]},"refrigerator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰箱，冷藏庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>refrigerator</b> is a large container which is kept cool inside, usually by electricity, so that the food and drink in it stays fresh. 冰箱","examples":[]}]}]},"quarter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"四分之一；一刻鐘，十五分鐘；季度，三個月；<美>學季，四分之一學年；（城鎮中的）區；個人，群體；（士兵、服務人員等的）營房；上弦（或下弦）月；（美式足球的）一節；（美國和加拿大的）二十五分硬幣；四分之一磅；（對敗者的）寬恕，仁慈；四分之一畜體（或鳥身）；（馬的）腰腿，臀部及後腿（quarters）；（羅盤上四個點之一所指的）方向；船側後部；盾的四分之一"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……四等分；把……降至原先的四分之一；提供食宿；在（某處）來回走動；移動，斜向行進；展示，炫耀（盾的四分之一部位上的不同紋章）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"四分之一的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"fraction.","pos_name":"分數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarter</b> is one of four equal parts of something. 1/4","examples":["A quarter of the residents are over 55 years old. 1/4的居民在55歲以上。","Prices have fallen by a quarter since January. 自1月份以來，物價下降了1/4。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quarter</b> is also a predeterminer. 四分之一","examples":["The largest asteroid is Ceres, which is about a quarter the size of the moon. 最大的小行星是穀神星，其體積大約是月球的四分之一。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quarter</b> is also an adjective. 四分之一的","examples":["...the past quarter century. …過去的四分之一世紀。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarter</b> is an American or Canadian coin that is worth 25 cents. (美國或加拿大) 25分的硬幣","examples":["I dropped a quarter into the slot of the pay phone. 我往付費電話的投幣口裡投了一枚25分的硬幣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>quarter</b> is a fixed period of three months. Companies often divide their financial year into four quarters. 季度","examples":["The group said results for the third quarter are due on October 29. 該集團說第3季度的結果將於10月29日公佈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you are telling the time, you use <b>quarter</b> to talk about the fifteen minutes before or after an hour. For example, 8:15 is <b>quarter after</b> eight and 8:45 is a <b>quarter</b> <b>of</b> or a <b>quarter</b> <b>to</b> nine. You can also say that 8:15 is <b>quarter</b> <b>past</b> eight, and 8:45 is <b>quarter</b> <b>to</b> nine. 一刻鐘","examples":["It was a quarter to six. 當時是5:45。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A particular <b>quarter</b> of a town is a part of the town where a particular group of people traditionally live or work. (某一人群生活或工作的) 地區","examples":["We wandered through the Chinese quarter. 我們在華人區逛了一圈。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>quarter</b> something such as a fruit or a vegetable, you cut it into four roughly equal parts. 把…切成4等份","examples":["Chop the mushrooms and quarter the tomatoes. 把蘑菇剁碎，把番茄切成四塊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the number or size of something <b>is quartered</b>, it is reduced to about a quarter of its previous number or size. 把…減至四分之一","examples":["The doses I suggested for adults could be halved or quartered. 我建議的成人劑量可以減半或減至四分之一。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>at close quarters</b>, you do it very near to a particular person or thing. 接近地","examples":["You can watch aircraft take off or land at close quarters. 你可以近距離地觀看飛機起飛或降落。"]}]}]},"record":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"記錄，記載；（某人或某物過去的）記錄，經歷；（尤指體育運動中的）最佳紀錄，最好成績；唱片；前科，犯罪記錄；唱片樂曲；（計算機）記錄（指作為一個單位處理的一批相關資訊）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"記錄，記載；錄製；（儀器）顯示，標示；（尤指體育上）獲得（好成績）；發表正式（或法律方面的）宣告，申明；演奏音樂供錄製"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"創紀錄的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you keep a <b>record</b> <b>of</b> something, you keep a written account or photographs of it so that it can be referred to later. 記錄; 記載","examples":["Keep a record of all the payments. 對所有付款做一個記錄。","There's no record of any marriage or children. 沒有任何有關結婚或子女的記錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>record</b> is a round, flat piece of black plastic on which sound, especially music, is stored, and which can be played on a record player. You can also refer to the music stored on this piece of plastic as a <b>record</b>. 唱片","examples":["This is one of my favourite records. 這是我最喜歡的唱片之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>record</b> is the best result that has ever been achieved in a particular sport or activity, for example the fastest time, the farthest distance, or the greatest number of victories. 紀錄","examples":["Roger Kingdom set the world record of 12.92 seconds. 羅傑·金頓創下了12.92秒的世界紀錄。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>record</b> is the facts that are known about their achievements or character. 經歷; 履歷","examples":["His record reveals a tough streak. 他的經歷說明他個性堅強。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a criminal <b>record</b>, it is officially known that they have committed crimes in the past. (犯罪) 記錄","examples":["...a heroin addict with a criminal record going back 15 years. …一名15年前留有案底的海洛因吸食成癮者。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>record</b> a piece of information or an event, you write it down, photograph it, or put it into a computer so that in the future people can refer to it. 記錄; 記載","examples":["Her letters record the domestic and social details of diplomatic life in China. 她的信件記錄了在中國的外交生活中家庭和社會活動的細節。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>record</b> something such as a speech or performance, you put it on tape or film so that it can be heard or seen again later. 錄音; 錄影","examples":["There is nothing to stop viewers from recording the films on videotape. 沒有辦法阻止觀眾用錄影帶錄下電影。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a musician or performer <b>records</b> a piece of music or a television or radio show, they perform it so that it can be put onto CD, tape, or film. 錄製","examples":["It took the musicians two and a half days to record their soundtrack for the film. 音樂家們花了兩天半的時間錄製電影的配樂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a dial or other measuring device <b>records</b> a certain measurement or value, it shows that measurement or value. 標明; 顯示","examples":["The test records the electrical activity of the brain. 這個測試顯示出大腦的電流活動。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>record</b> to say that something is higher, lower, better, or worse than has ever been achieved before. 創紀錄的","examples":["Profits were at record levels. 利潤水平是創紀錄的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that what you are going to say next is <b>for the record</b>, you mean that you are saying it publicly and officially and you want it to be written down and remembered. 供記錄在案","examples":["We're willing to state for the record that it has enormous value. 我們願意申明它有巨大的價值並望其能被記錄在案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give some information <b>for the record</b>, you give it in case people might find it useful at a later time, although it is not a very important part of what you are talking about. 順便說一下; 僅供參考","examples":["For the record, most Moscow girls leave school at about 18. 隨便說一下，多數莫斯科女孩大約十八歲離開學校。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something that you say is <b>off the record</b>, you do not intend it to be considered as official, or published with your name attached to it. 非正式的; 不得公開引用的","examples":["May I speak off the record? 我可以私下裡說嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>on record</b> <b>as</b> saying something, you have said it publicly and officially and it has been written down. 公開宣佈並記錄在案的","examples":["The president is on record as saying that the increase in unemployment is \"a price worth paying\" to keep inflation down. 總統公開說失業率的上升是遏制通貨膨脹“值得付出的代價”。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you keep information <b>on record</b>, you write it down or store it in a computer so that it can be used later. 記錄在案的","examples":["The practice is to keep on record any analysis of samples. 這項工作是為了記錄下對樣品的所有分析。"]}]}]},"region":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地區，區域；行政區；<英>（首都以外的）地方（the regions）；身體部位；領域，界"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>region</b> is a large area of land that is different from other areas of land, for example because it is one of the different parts of a country with its own customs and characteristics, or because it has a particular geographical feature. 地區","examples":["...Barcelona, capital of the autonomous region of Catalonia. …巴塞羅那，加泰羅尼亞自治區的首府。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a part of your body as a <b>region</b>. (身體) 部位","examples":["...the pelvic region. …骨盆部位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>in the region of</b> to indicate that an amount that you are stating is approximate. (數量) 在…左右","examples":["The plan will cost in the region of six million dollars. 這項計劃將花費大約六百萬美元。"]}]}]},"relationship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人、團體、國家等相互間的）關係；（人或事物之間的）關聯，關係；戀人關係，性愛關係；血緣關係，姻親關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>relationship</b> between two people or groups is the way in which they feel and behave toward each other. 關係","examples":["...the friendly relationship between France and Britain. …英法間的友好關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>relationship</b> is a close friendship between two people, especially one involving romantic or sexual feelings. (尤指愛情或性的) 關係","examples":["We had been together for two years, but both of us felt the relationship wasn't really going anywhere. 我們在一起已經兩年了，但是我們倆都覺得這種關係實在不會有什麼結果。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>relationship</b> between two things is the way in which they are connected. 聯絡","examples":["A number of small-scale studies have already indicated that there is a relationship between diet and cancer. 一些小規模的研究已經表明，飲食和癌症之間有一種聯絡。"]}]}]},"relation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或物間的）聯絡；（國家、公司、組織等之間的）（正式）關係；<正式> 性關係；親戚，親屬；講述，敘述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Relations</b> between people, groups, or countries are contacts between them and the way in which they behave toward each other. 關係","examples":["Greece has established full diplomatic relations with Israel. 希臘已經和以色列建立了全面的外交關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>relation</b> <b>of</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you are talking about the ways in which they are connected. 關係","examples":["It is a question of the relation of ethics to economics. 這是個道德和經濟之間關係的問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>relations</b> are the members of your family. 親屬","examples":["...visits to friends and relations. …對親友的拜訪。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can talk about something <b>in relation to</b> something else when you want to compare the size, condition, or position of the two things. 與…相比","examples":["The money he'd been ordered to pay was minimal in relation to his salary. 他被要求支付的錢與他的薪水相比是少的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is said or done <b>in relation to</b> a subject, it is said or done in connection with that subject. 關於","examples":["...a question that has been asked many times in relation to Irish affairs. …一個多次被問到的關於愛爾蘭事務的問題。"]}]}]},"regard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"認為，把……看作；<正式>（尤指以某種方式）注視，凝視；<古>注意，留心；<古>與……有關，涉及"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式> 尊重，敬佩；<正式> 關心，關注；注視，凝視；（用於信函結尾或轉達問候）致意，問候（regards）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>regard</b> someone or something <b>as</b> being a particular thing or <b>as</b> having a particular quality, you believe that they are that thing or have that quality. 看待","examples":["He was regarded as the most successful president of modern times. 他被看成是近代最成功的總統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>regard</b> something or someone <b>with</b> a feeling such as dislike or respect, you have that feeling about them. (以某種感情) 看待","examples":["He regarded drug dealers with loathing. 他帶著憎惡去看待毒販子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>regard</b> <b>for</b> someone or something, you respect them and care about them. If you hold someone <b>in</b> high <b>regard</b>, you have a lot of respect for them. 尊重","examples":["I have a very high regard for him and what he has achieved. 我非常尊重他和他所取得的成就。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Regards</b> are greetings. You use <b>regards</b> in expressions such as <b>best regards</b> and <b>with kind regards</b> as a way of expressing friendly feelings toward someone, especially in a letter. 用在(best regards)和(with kind regards)等表達方式中，表示對某人的良好祝願，多用於書信中","examples":["Give my regards to your family. 請代我向您的家人問好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>as regards</b> to indicate the subject that is being talked or written about. 關於; 至於","examples":["As regards the war, Haig believed in victory at any price. 關於這場戰爭，黑格認為應不惜任何代價獲勝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>with regard to</b> or <b>in regard to</b> to indicate the subject that is being talked or written about. 關於; 至於","examples":["The department is reviewing its policy with regard to immunization. 該部門正在重新審查其有關免疫注射的政策。"]}]}]},"range":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（變動或浮動的）範圍，界限；視覺（或聽覺）範圍；射程，射擊距離；一系列；成套產品，系列商品；山脈；牧場，牧區；靶場，射擊場，炸彈試驗場；（尤指舊時的）爐灶；一排建築物；<古>方向，走向；（飛機等交通工具的）續航距離"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在一定的範圍內）變化，變動；（按一定位置或順序）排列，排序；徘徊，四處移動；（文章或講話）涉及，包括 ；（槍、炮、射擊後校準）測距，（用雷達或鐳射）測距；支援，反對；自然生長，分佈；與……聯合起來，加入……行列"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<文>（生活方式）有秩序的，安定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>range</b> <b>of</b> things is a number of different things of the same general kind. (同類事物的) 一系列","examples":["A wide range of colours and patterns are available. 一系列各種各樣的顏色和圖案都有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>range</b> is the complete group that is included between two points on a scale of measurement or quality. 範圍","examples":["The average age range is between 35 and 55. 平均年齡範圍是35至55歲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>range</b> <b>of</b> something is the maximum area in which it can reach things or detect things. (能夠到達或探知的) 最大範圍","examples":["The 120mm mortar has a range of 18,000 yards. 口徑120毫米的迫擊炮的射程是1.8萬碼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>range</b> of mountains or hills is a line of them. 山脈","examples":["...the massive mountain ranges to the north. …連綿向北的巨大山脈。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A rifle <b>range</b> or a shooting <b>range</b> is a place where people can practise shooting at targets. 射擊場","examples":["It reminds me of my days on the rifle range preparing for duty in Vietnam. 這使我回想起在射擊場上訓練準備去越南服役的那些日子。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>range</b> is a large area of open land, especially land in the United States, where cattle are kept. (尤指美國的) 大牧場","examples":["He grazed his cattle on the open range. 他在開闊的大牧場上放牧他的牛群。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>range</b> or <b>kitchen range</b> is a large metal device for cooking food using gas or electricity. A range consists of a grill, an oven, and some gas or electric burners. 爐灶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things <b>range</b> <b>between</b> two points or <b>range</b> <b>from</b> one point <b>to</b> another, they vary within these points on a scale of measurement or quality. (在一定幅度內) 變化","examples":["They range in price from $3 to $15. 它們的價格在$3到$15之間變化。","...offering merchandise ranging from the everyday to the esoteric. …出售的商品包括日常用品到少數人使用的特別物品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in range</b> or <b>within range</b>, it is near enough to be reached or detected. If it is <b>out of range</b>, it is too far away to be reached or detected. 在可觸及的範圍內/外","examples":["Cars are driven through the mess, splashing everyone within range. 車子從泥濘中開過，把泥點濺到附近能濺得到的每個人身上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you see or hit something <b>at close range</b> or <b>from close range</b>, you are very close to it when you see it or hit it. If you do something <b>at a range of</b> half a mile, for example, you are half a mile away from it when you do it. 近距離內","examples":["He was shot in the head at close range. 他被近距離射中頭部。"]}]}]},"reply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"回答，答覆；（以行動）作出回應，回擊；（在體育比賽中）以得分回應，回敬"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（口頭或書面）回答，答覆；回應，作出反應；<英>（比賽）一方得分（進球）但對方未得分（進球）；<法律>（原告對被告抗辯的）駁復，答辯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>reply</b> <b>to</b> something that someone has said or written to you, you say or write an answer to them. 回答; 答覆","examples":["\"That's a nice dress,\" said Michael. \"Thanks,\" she replied solemnly. “那連衣裙很漂亮，”邁克爾說。“謝謝，”她鄭重地回答。","He replied that this was absolutely impossible. 他回答說這絕對不可能。","He never replied to the letters. 他從來都不回信。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reply</b> is something that you say or write when you answer someone or answer a letter or advertisement. 回答; 答覆","examples":["I called out a challenge, but there was no reply. 我發起了一個挑戰，但是沒人回應。","He said in reply that the question was unfair. 他回答說這個問題不公平。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reply</b> <b>to</b> something such as an attack <b>with</b> violence or <b>with</b> another action, you do something in response. 做出回應; (以行動) 回擊","examples":["During a number of violent incidents farmers threw eggs and empty bottles at police, who replied with tear gas. 在多次暴力事件中，農場主們朝警察扔雞蛋和空瓶子，而警察則以催淚瓦斯回擊。"]}]}]},"reporter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"記者，通訊員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reporter</b> is someone who writes news articles or who broadcasts news reports. 記者","examples":["...a TV reporter. …一名電視臺記者。"]}]}]},"regular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"定期的，規律的；經常的，頻繁的；慣常的，通常的；持久的，固定的；標準尺寸的，中號的；普通的，平凡的；常備軍的，正規軍的；（動詞）規則的；（人）正常通便的，月經正常的；完全的，徹底的；均勻的，端正的；正規的，正當的；（衝浪等）左腿在前的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常客，老主顧；主演，主力隊員；正規軍人，職業軍人；普通產品，普通裝；（區別於世俗教士的）修道者，教士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Regular</b> events have equal amounts of time between them, so that they happen, for example, at the same time each day or each week. 定期的","examples":["Get regular exercise. 定期進行鍛鍊。","We're going to be meeting there on a regular basis. 我們將定期在那裡見面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Regular</b> events happen often. 經常的","examples":["Although it may look unpleasant, this condition is harmless and usually clears up with regular shampooing. 這可能不好看，但這種情況是無害的並且經常的洗頭通常可以消除它。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are, for example, a <b>regular</b> customer at a shop or a <b>regular</b> visitor to a place, you go there often. 經常的 (顧客或來訪者)","examples":["She has become a regular visitor to Houghton Hall. 她已成為霍頓府邸的一名常客。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>regular</b> when referring to the thing, person, time, or place that is usually used by someone. For example, someone's <b>regular</b> place is the place where they usually sit. 固定的","examples":["The man shook his hand and then sat at his regular table near the windows. 這個人握了握他的手，然後坐在他固定的靠窗的桌子旁。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>regular</b> rhythm consists of a series of sounds or movements with equal periods of time between them. 均勻的","examples":["...a very regular beat. …非常均勻的節拍。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Regular</b> is used to mean \"normal.\" 普通的","examples":["The product looks and burns like a regular cigarette. 這種產品看上去和點起來都像一支普通的香菸。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"In some restaurants, a <b>regular</b> drink or quantity of food is of medium size. 中份的","examples":["...a cheeseburger and regular fries. …一個乾酪漢堡包和中份的炸薯條。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>regular</b> pattern or arrangement consists of a series of things with equal spaces between them. 間隔一致的","examples":["The village was laid out in regular patterns. 這個村莊街道和房屋被以相等的間隔整齊地加以佈局。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If something has a <b>regular</b> shape, both halves are the same and it has straight edges or a smooth outline. 規則的","examples":["...some regular geometrical shape. …一些規則的幾何圖形。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>regular</b> verb, noun, or adjective inflects in the same way as most verbs, nouns, or adjectives in the language. (動詞、名詞或形容詞) 按規則變化的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"定期地","examples":["He also writes regularly for \"International Management\" magazine. 他也定期為《國際管理》雜誌寫稿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"經常地","examples":["Fox, badger, and weasel are regularly seen here. 這裡經常看得到狐狸、獾和黃鼠狼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"均勻地","examples":["Remember to breathe regularly. 記住要均勻地呼吸。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>regulars</b> at a place or on a team are the people who often go to the place or are often on the team. 常客; 正式隊員","examples":["Regulars at his local bar have set up a fund to help out. 他的當地酒吧的常客們已經設立了一項基金來幫忙解決困難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"規則性","examples":["...the chessboard regularity of their fields. …國際象棋棋盤的規則性。"]}]}]},"restroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（公共場所的）盥洗室，洗手間；<英>（尤指公共建築內的）休息室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a restaurant, theatre, or other public place, a <b>restroom</b> is a room with a toilet for customers to use. 公共廁所","examples":[]}]}]},"requirement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"要求，必要條件；需要（要求）的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>requirement</b> is a quality or qualification that you must have in order to be allowed to do something or to be suitable for something. 必備條件","examples":["Its products met all legal requirements. 它的產品滿足了所有法定的必備條件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>requirements</b> are the things that you need. 需要; 必需品","examples":["Variations of this programme can be arranged to suit your requirements. 這個軟體可以被設定成各種各樣的形式以適應你們的需要。"]}]}]},"repeat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"重複，重說；複述，跟讀（尤指為學習）；轉述，轉告；（強調說過的話）再說一遍；重新做，使再次發生；重播；重讀，重修；<美>（選舉中違法）重複投票；<美>再次成功，兩連冠；<英>（吃下的食物因打嗝或消化不良）在口中留下餘味；（鐘錶按要求）連打"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（事件的）重演，重現；重播節目；（同類貨物的）再次運送；重複裝飾圖案；（樂譜的）反覆符號，重複段"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>repeat</b> something, you say or write it again. You can say <b>I repeat</b> to show that you feel strongly about what you are repeating. 重複; 重說; 重寫","examples":["He repeated that he had been misquoted. 他反覆地說他的話被錯誤地引用了。","She repeated her call yesterday for an investigation into the incident. 她昨天反覆要求對那起事件進行調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>repeat</b> something that someone else has said or written, you say or write the same thing, or tell it to another person. 照著說; 照著寫; 把…告訴別人","examples":["She had an irritating habit of repeating everything I said to her. 她有個令人惱火的毛病，就是把我對她說的每一件事都告訴別人。","I trust you not to repeat that to anyone else. 我相信你不會把這事告訴別人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>repeat</b> <b>yourself</b>, you say something which you have said before, usually by mistake. (常指失誤造成的) 反覆地講","examples":["He spoke well to begin with, but then started rambling and repeating himself. 開始他說得很好，但是後來開始閒扯，一句話翻來覆去地講。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>repeat</b> an action, you do it again. 再做; 重做","examples":["The next day I repeated the procedure. 第二天我重複了這個程式。","Move the leg up and down several times and rotate the foot. Repeat on the right leg. 把腿上下移動幾次並轉動腳。然後換右腿重做一遍。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an event or series of events <b>repeats</b> <b>itself</b>, it happens again. 再次發生; 重演","examples":["The UN will have to work hard to stop history from repeating itself. 聯合國必須努力工作以阻止歷史重演。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>repeat</b> <b>of</b> an event, usually an undesirable event, it happens again. (尤指不受歡迎的事情的) 重演","examples":["There were fears that there might be a repeat of last year's campaign of strikes. 有人擔心去年的罷工或許會重演。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>repeat</b> is a television or radio programme that has been broadcast before. (電視或電臺節目的) 重播","examples":["There's nothing except sports and repeats on TV. 電視上只有一些體育節目和重播節目。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company gets <b>repeat</b> business or <b>repeat</b> customers, people who have bought their goods or services before buy them again. (顧客) 回頭的; (生意) 回頭客的","examples":["Nearly 60% of our bookings come from repeat business and personal recommendation. 我們近60％的預訂來自於回頭客生意或個人推薦。"]}]}]},"restaurant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"餐館，飯店"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>restaurant</b> is a place where you can eat a meal and pay for it. In restaurants, your food is usually served to you at your table by a waiter or waitress. 餐館","examples":["They ate in an Italian restaurant in Forth Street. 他們在福斯大街的一家義大利餐館吃了飯。"]}]}]},"riches":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"財富，富有（通常作複數）；（Riches）人名（英：裡奇斯；意：裡凱斯）"}],"sections":[]},"respect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尊敬，敬重；重視，尊重；方面，著眼點；問候，敬意（respects）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"尊敬，敬佩；慎重對待，尊重；遵守；避免破壞（或干擾）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式> 真了不起（因敬重或贊同而發出的感嘆）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>respect</b> someone, you have a good opinion of their character or ideas. 尊重","examples":["I want him to respect me as a career woman. 我要他把我作為一個職業女性來尊重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>respect</b> someone's wishes, rights, or customs, you avoid doing things that they would dislike or regard as wrong. 尊重","examples":["Finally, trying to respect her wishes, I said I'd leave. 最後，設法尊重她的意願，我說我會離開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>respect</b> a law or moral principle, you agree not to break it. 遵守","examples":["It is about time tour operators respected the law and their own code of conduct. 現在該是旅行社經營者們遵守法律和他們自己的行業規範的時候了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>respect</b> <b>for</b> someone, you have a good opinion of them. 敬重","examples":["I have tremendous respect for Dean. 我非常敬重迪安。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you show <b>respect</b> <b>for</b> someone's wishes, rights, or customs, you avoid doing anything they would dislike or regard as wrong. 尊重","examples":["They will campaign for respect for aboriginal rights and customs. 他們將開展尊重土著居民權利和風俗的活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Respect</b> is also a noun. 遵守","examples":["...respect for the law and the rejection of the use of violence. …對法律的遵守和對使用暴力的摒棄。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>with all due respect</b> when you are politely disagreeing with someone or criticizing them. 請恕我冒犯","examples":["With all due respect, I hardly think that's the point. 請恕我冒犯，我不認為那是要點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pay</b> your <b>respects</b> <b>to</b> someone, you go to see them or speak to them. You usually do this to be polite, and not necessarily because you want to do it. 表示某人的敬意","examples":["Carl had asked him to visit the hospital and to pay his respects to Francis. 卡爾已要求他去那所醫院向弗朗西斯表示他的敬意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use expressions like <b>in this respect</b> and <b>in many respects</b> to indicate that what you are saying applies to the feature you have just mentioned or to many features of something. 在這方面; 在許多方面","examples":["Within the Department of Justice are several drug-fighting agencies. The lead agency in this respect is the DEA. 司法部內部有幾個禁毒機構，在這方面的領導機構是禁毒執行中心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>with respect to</b> to say what something relates to. 關於; 至於","examples":["Parents often have little choice with respect to the way their child is medically treated. 至於他們孩子被醫治的方式,父母通常少有選擇的餘地。"]}]}]},"role":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（演員的）角色；作用，職責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>role</b> in a situation or in society, you have a particular position and function in it. 功能; 作用","examples":["Until now scientists had very little clear evidence about the drug's role in preventing more serious effects of infection. 到目前為止，科學家們幾乎沒有該藥物在防止更嚴重的感染後果的功能的明確證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>role</b> is one of the characters that an actor or singer can play in a movie, play, or opera. 角色","examples":["She has just landed the lead role in their latest production. 她剛在他們最新的作品中取得了主角。"]}]}]},"ruler":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"統治者，管理者；尺子，直尺；（計算機螢幕的）標尺；劃線板，劃線的人；主導行星（對黃道十二宮圖的宮、房子、生活等有特別影響的行星）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>ruler</b> of a country is the person who rules the country. 統治者","examples":["The former military ruler of Lesotho has been placed under house arrest. 賴索托前軍事統治者已被軟禁了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ruler</b> is a long, flat piece of wood, metal, or plastic with straight edges marked in or inches or centimetres. Rulers are used to measure things and to draw straight lines. 尺","examples":["...a twelve-inch ruler. …一把12英寸長的尺子。"]}]}]},"roach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美）蟑螂；[魚]斜齒鯿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Roach）人名；（英、西）羅奇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>roach</b> is the same as a . 同cockroach","examples":["He found his brother in a seedy, roach-infested apartment. 他發現他的兄弟住在一套骯髒的、蟑螂橫行的公寓裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a European freshwater cyprinid food fish, <b>Rutilus rutilus</b>, having a deep compressed body and reddish ventral and tail fins 斜齒鯿魚","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the amount by which the leech of a fore-and-aft sail projects beyond an imaginary straight line between the clew and the head (航海)橫帆下緣的弧形缺口。","examples":[]}]}]},"result":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結果，後果；（比賽或選舉的）結果；（透過調查、研究、計算而獲得的）結果；<英> 考試成績；成效，成果（results）；經營業績（results）；<英，非正式>（體育比賽中）勝局，獲勝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發生，產生；導致，造成（註明的結局或結果）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式> 成功了！（Result!）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>result</b> is something that happens or exists because of something else that has happened. 結果","examples":["Compensation is available for people who have developed asthma as a direct result of their work. 直接因工作原因患哮喘的人會獲得賠償。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>result</b> is the situation that exists at the end of a contest. 結果","examples":["The final election results will be announced on Friday. 最終選舉結果將在週五被公佈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>result</b> is the number that you get when you do a calculation. 答案","examples":["They found their computers producing different results from exactly the same calculation. 他們發現他們的電腦從完全相同的計算得出了不同的答案。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>results</b> are the marks or grades that you get for examinations you have taken. 成績","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>results</b> <b>in</b> a particular situation or event, it causes that situation or event to happen. 致使","examples":["Fifty percent of road accidents result in head injuries. 50%的公路交通事故致使頭部受傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>results</b> <b>from</b> a particular event or action, it is caused by that event or action. 起因","examples":["Many hair problems result from what you eat. 很多頭髮問題是由你吃的東西引起的。"]}]}]},"review":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"審查，檢查；評論，評論文章；（時事、藝術等的）評論期刊；述評，回顧；<美>複習，溫習；<美>（一門課程的）材料，練習；閱兵，閱兵式；中止快速倒帶（或卷帶）重放裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細研究，審視；給（書、戲劇、電影等）寫評論；回顧，反思；<美>（為考試而）複習，溫習；<美>校閱，稽核；<英>複查（病人）；檢閱（軍隊）；<法律>將（判決、案件等）提交上級法院（或權力機構）複審"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>review</b> <b>of</b> a situation or system is its formal examination by people in authority. This is usually done in order to see whether it can be improved or corrected. (上級的) 審查","examples":["The president ordered a review of U.S. economic aid to Jordan. 總統下令對美國向約旦提供的經濟援助進行一次審查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>review</b> is a report in the media in which someone gives their opinion of something such as a new book or movie. 評論","examples":["We've never had a good review in the music press. 我們在音樂媒體內未曾得到過好評。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Review</b> is also a noun. 複習","examples":["If you have to cover 12 chapters in American history, begin by planning on three two-hour reviews with four chapters per session. 如果你必須涵蓋美國史的12個章節，首先計劃3次2小時的複習，每次4章。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>review</b> a situation or system, you consider it carefully to see what is wrong with it or how it could be improved. 審裁; 審度","examples":["The president reviewed the situation with his cabinet yesterday. 總統昨天與他的內閣成員審度了局勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>reviews</b> something such as a new book or movie, they write a report or give a talk on television or radio in which they express their opinion of it. 對 (新作品) 作評論","examples":["Richard Coles reviews all the latest video releases. 理查德•科爾斯對最近發行的所有錄影做了評論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>review</b> <b>for</b> an examination, you read things again and make notes in order to be prepared for the examination. 複習","examples":[]}]}]},"runner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"跑步者；賽馬；走私者；送信人，信差；跑壘員；跑動板球員；滑動裝置；長條地毯；纖匐枝；跑鞋，運動鞋；效能良好的車；<英，非正式>競爭者；<英，非正式>可能被接受的想法；（熱帶海洋的）青鰺；迴轉磨石（=runner stone）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>runner</b> is a person who runs, especially for sport or pleasure. 跑步者","examples":["...a marathon runner. …一個馬拉松賽跑選手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>runners</b> in a horse race are the horses taking part. 賽馬","examples":["There are 18 runners in the top race of the day. 在那天的最高階別的比賽中有18匹賽馬參加。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A drug <b>runner</b> or gun <b>runner</b> is someone who illegally takes drugs or guns into a country. 走私者","examples":["...a gang of evil gun runners. …一夥邪惡的走私槍支的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>runner</b> for a particular person or company is employed to take messages, collect money, or do other small tasks for them. 聽差","examples":["...a bookie's runner. …一名賭注登記人的聽差。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Runners</b> are thin strips of wood or metal underneath something which help it to move smoothly. 滑板","examples":["...the runners of his sled. …他雪橇下面的滑板。"]}]}]},"safety":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"安全；安全性；安全場所，安全的地方；安全方法，安全措施； <美>（槍炮的）保險栓，保險機（=safety catch ）；<美>安全分（持球進攻隊員在己方端線後被攔截，防守方得兩分）；<美>（位置遠離爭球線的）安全衛；<美，非正式> 安全套；（棒球）安打；安全裝置"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（特徵、措施）保障安全的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Safety</b> is the state of being safe from harm or danger. 安全; 平安","examples":["The report goes on to make a number of recommendations to improve safety on aircraft. 該報告接著提出了幾點建議來加強飛行安全。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you reach <b>safety</b>, you reach a place where you are safe from danger. 安全場所","examples":["He stumbled through smoke and fumes to pull her to safety. 他跌跌撞撞地穿過重重煙霧把她拖到了安全的地方。","People scurried for safety as the firing started. 人們在交火發生時急忙跑向安全地帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are concerned about the <b>safety</b> of something, you are concerned that it might be harmful or dangerous. 安全性","examples":["...consumers are showing growing concern about the safety of the food they buy. …消費者越來越關注所購食品的安全性。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are concerned for someone's <b>safety</b>, you are concerned that they might be in danger. 安危","examples":["There is grave concern for the safety of witnesses. 證人們的安危受到嚴重關注。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Safety</b> features or measures are intended to make something less dangerous. 安全的 (特性或措施)","examples":["The built-in safety device compensates for a fall in water pressure. 這個內建的安全裝置可以補償水壓的下降。"]}]}]},"sailor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水手，船員；駕船人，帆船駕駛者；喜好航海的人（尤指富有經驗者）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sailor</b> is someone who works on a ship or sails a boat. 船員; 船隻駕駛員","examples":["...sailors, marines and Coast Guard personnel. …船員們、海軍陸戰隊士兵們和海岸警衛隊人員。"]}]}]},"salad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙拉，色拉，沙律（一種常加調味汁的涼拌食物）；生菜，萵苣（尤指適合拌沙拉的綠葉蔬菜）；（Salad）人名，薩拉德（尤指阿拉伯人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>salad</b> is a mixture of cold foods such as lettuce, tomatoes, or cold cooked potatoes, cut up and mixed with a dressing. It is often served with other food as part of a meal. 色拉","examples":["...a salad of tomato, onion and cucumber. …一份番茄、洋蔥和黃瓜色拉。"]}]}]},"sauce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醬，調味汁；<美，非正式>烈酒（the sauce）；<英，非正式> 無禮的話（或舉動）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加醬汁於，用醬汁調味；使增加趣味；<非正式>對……粗暴無禮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sauce</b> is a thick liquid which is served with other food. 醬; 調味汁","examples":["...pasta cooked in a sauce of garlic, tomatoes, and cheese. …用大蒜、番茄和乳酪調味汁煮的義大利麵。"]}]}]},"sandwich":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"三明治，夾心麵包片；<英>果醬（或奶油）夾心鬆蛋糕；<美>夾心餅乾；三明治狀物；<英>教學與實習交替培訓課程"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"插入，夾入；粘合（sandwich sth. together）；把……做成三明治"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sandwich</b> usually consists of two slices of bread with a layer of food such as cheese or meat between them. 三明治","examples":["...a ham sandwich. …一個火腿三明治。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sandwich</b> two things <b>together</b> with something else, you put that other thing between them. If you <b>sandwich</b> one thing between two other things, you put it between them. 夾住; 把…插入 (兩者之間)","examples":["Carefully split the sponge ring, then sandwich the two halves together with whipped cream. 小心地切開海綿蛋糕圈，然後在兩半中間夾上生奶油。"]}]}]},"sample":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樣本，樣品；試用產品，試樣；（供科學或醫學檢測用的）抽樣樣本；（抽查的）樣本，抽選人員；（用於新樂曲中的）選錄的歌曲片段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"品嚐，嘗試（食品、飲料）；體驗（活動）；對……作抽樣調查；節錄，選錄（歌曲等，用於其他錄音）；確定（模擬訊號）瞬時值"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"樣品的，例項的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sample</b> of a substance or product is a small quantity of it that shows you what it is like. 樣品; 樣本","examples":["You'll receive samples of paint, curtains and upholstery. 你將收到塗料、窗簾和座套的樣品。","We're giving away 2,000 free samples. 我們正在贈送2000件免費樣品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sample</b> of a substance is a small amount of it that is examined and analysed scientifically. (用於檢驗、分析的) 試樣","examples":["They took samples of my blood. 他們採了我的血樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sample</b> of people or things is a number of them chosen out of a larger group and then used in tests or used to provide information about the whole group. 抽樣","examples":["We based our analysis on a random sample of more than 200 males. 我們把我們的分析基於二百多名男性的一組隨機抽樣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sample</b> food or drink, you taste a small amount of it in order to find out if you like it. 品嚐","examples":["We sampled a selection of different bottled waters. 我們品嚐了挑選出來的各種瓶裝水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sample</b> a place or situation, you experience it for a short time in order to find out about it. 體驗","examples":["...the chance to sample a different way of life. …體驗一種不同生活方式的機會。"]}]}]},"rush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"衝，奔；把（某人或某物）迅速送往；趕緊做，倉促做；催促，使趕緊；（水、液體等）快速流動；（因感到尷尬）某人的臉/面頰漲紅；向……猛衝，猛攻；<美>（大學生聯誼會透過舉辦聚會等）招納，招收（新會員）；辦理手續加入（大學生聯誼會）；（美橄）突襲（對方隊員，尤指樞紐前衛）；（美式橄欖中）跑動帶（球）；倉促生產並分發，匆匆出售（rush something out）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指一群人的）衝，奔；（空氣、水等）湍流；匆忙，趕緊；（人流或交通的）高峰時間（the rush）；（很多人）爭做，急需；迸發的情緒，情緒迸發；（因吸食毒品或因興奮事物產生的）一陣激動；工作樣片（rushes）；燈心草（常用來編筐）；（美橄）突襲對方隊員（尤指樞紐前衛）；（美式橄欖球中的）跑動帶球；（大學生聯誼會的）招新活動；（美國大學生聯誼會的）納新活動（時間）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rush</b> somewhere, you go there quickly. 迅速地走","examples":["A schoolgirl rushed into a burning apartment to save a man's life. 一名女學童衝進一棟著火的公寓去救一個男子的命。","I've got to rush. Got a meeting in a few minutes. 我得趕快走。幾分鐘後有一個會。","I rushed to get the 7:00 a.m. train. 我急急忙忙去趕早上7點的火車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>rush</b> <b>to</b> do something, they do it as soon as they can, because they are very eager to do it. 急著 (做)","examples":["Russian banks rushed to buy as many dollars as they could. 俄羅斯各銀行急著儘可能多地買入美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>rush</b> something, you do it in a hurry, often too quickly and without much care. 忙碌","examples":["You can't rush a search. 你不能匆忙做搜尋工作。","Instead of rushing at life, I wanted something more meaningful. 我不想在生活中忙忙碌碌，而想做更有意義的事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>rush</b> someone or something to a place, you take them there quickly. 迅速送","examples":["They had rushed him to a hospital for a lifesaving operation. 他們迅速送他到了醫院進行急救手術。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>rush</b> <b>into</b> something or <b>are rushed</b> <b>into</b> it, you do it without thinking about it for long enough. 使倉促行事; 倉促行事","examples":["He will not rush into any decisions. 他不會倉促做出任何決定。","They had rushed in without adequate appreciation of the task. 他們沒有充分了解這項任務就倉促行動了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>rush</b> something or someone, or <b>rush</b> <b>at</b> them, you move quickly and forcefully at them, often in order to attack them. 衝向; 衝","examples":["They rushed the entrance and forced their way in. 他們衝向了入口並強行闖了進去。","Reporters rushed at him and he ran back inside. 記者向他衝，他就跑回裡面去了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rush</b> is a situation in which you need to go somewhere or do something very quickly. 匆忙","examples":["The men left in a rush. 這些男人在匆忙中離開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is a <b>rush</b> <b>for</b> something, many people suddenly try to get it or do it. 爭搶","examples":["Record shops are expecting a huge rush for the single. 各唱片店正期待著這張單曲唱片的一個大搶購。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>rush</b> is a period of time when many people go somewhere or do something. 高峰期","examples":["The shop's opening coincided with the Christmas rush. 這家商店的開張正趕上聖誕節購物高峰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Rush</b> is also a noun. 急流","examples":["A rush of air on my face woke me. 臉上的一股急促的氣流驚醒了我。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you experience a <b>rush</b> <b>of</b> a feeling, you suddenly experience it very strongly. (感情) 迸發","examples":["A rush of pure affection swept over him. 一股強烈的真愛掠過了他的心田。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"any annual or perennial plant of the genus <b>Juncus</b>, growing in wet places and typically having grasslike cylindrical leaves and small green or brown flowers: family <b>Juncaceae</b> Many species are used to make baskets 燈芯草","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"忙碌的","examples":["The report had all the hallmarks of a rushed job. 這份報告有著急就章的一切特點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"requiring speed or urgency 緊急的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"倉促的","examples":["At no time did I feel rushed or under pressure. 我從未感到倉促或有壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If air or liquid <b>rushes</b> somewhere, it flows there suddenly and quickly. 奔湧","examples":["Water rushes out of huge tunnels. 水從巨大的隧道奔湧而出。"]}]}]},"science":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"科學，科學知識；專門科學；（大學學習的）學科；理科；技術，技巧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Science</b> is the study of the nature and behaviour of natural things and the knowledge that we obtain about them. 科學","examples":["The best discoveries in science are very simple. 科學上最好的發現都是非常簡單的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>science</b> is a particular branch of science such as physics, chemistry, or biology. (科學的) 學科","examples":["Physics is the best example of a science which has developed strong, abstract theories. 物理學是一個發展出了強有力的抽象理論的學科的最好例證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>science</b> is the study of some aspect of human behaviour, for example, sociology or anthropology. (人類行為的) 科學研究","examples":["...the modern science of psychology. …現代心理學。"]}]}]},"scissors":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剪刀；（英橄）交叉配合，交叉移動；（跳高）剪式跳法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用剪刀剪；使（腿）作剪式運動（scissor 的第三人稱單數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scissors</b> are a small cutting tool with two sharp blades that are screwed together. You use scissors for cutting things such as paper and cloth. 剪刀","examples":["He told me to get some scissors. 他叫我去拿幾把剪刀。"]}]}]},"roll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）翻滾，滾動；（使）翻身，翻轉；行駛，開動；（機器）轉動，運轉；（液體）滾落，滑落；使……成球狀（或管狀）；使平坦，壓平；把（衣服的邊）捲起來；（使）搖擺，搖晃；（使）原地轉圈，翻白眼；搖（車窗），卷（窗簾等）；發出持續的聲音；（時間）流逝；（產品）從（流水線，機器）產出；<非正式>盜竊；連獲成功"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"卷，卷軸；卷狀食品；贅肉，肥肉；名單，花名冊；一管；滾動，翻滾；左右搖晃，振盪；隆隆聲，轟轟響；擲骰子；壓路機，輥軋機；（地形的）延綿起伏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>rolls</b> or when you <b>roll</b> it, it moves along a surface, turning over many times. 滾動","examples":["The ball rolled into the net. 球滾進了網。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>roll</b> something flexible <b>into</b> a cylinder or a ball, you form it into a cylinder or a ball by wrapping it several times around itself or by shaping it between your hands. 卷; 繞 (成柱形或團)","examples":["He took off his sweater, rolled it into a pillow, and lay down on the grass. 他脫下毛衣，捲成一個枕頭，然後在草地上躺了下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>roll</b> <b>up</b> something such as a car window or a blind, you cause it to move upward by turning a handle. If you <b>roll</b> it <b>down</b>, you cause it to move downward by turning a handle. 搖 (車窗、捲簾等)","examples":["In mid-afternoon, shopkeepers began to roll down their shutters. 下午三點鐘左右，店主們開始搖下百葉窗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>roll</b> your eyes or if your eyes <b>roll</b>, they move around and upward. People sometimes roll their eyes when they are frightened, bored, or annoyed. (指眼睛) 翻轉","examples":["People may roll their eyes and talk about overprotective, interfering grandmothers. 人們可能會翻著白眼討論過分呵護、事事插手的祖母們。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>roll</b> somewhere, you move on a surface while lying down, turning your body over and over, so that you are sometimes on your back, sometimes on your side, and sometimes on your front. 打滾","examples":["When I was a little kid I rolled down a hill and broke my leg. 我小的時候曾滾下山摔斷了腿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When vehicles <b>roll</b> along, they move along slowly. (車輛) 緩行","examples":["The truck quietly rolled forward and demolished all the old wooden fencing. 卡車靜靜地緩慢前行，毀了所有舊木柵欄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a machine <b>rolls</b>, it is operating. (機器) 運轉","examples":["He slipped and fell on the step as the cameras rolled. 在相機拍攝時，他滑倒在了臺階上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If drops of liquid <b>roll</b> down a surface, they move quickly down it. (液體) 滾落","examples":["She looked at Ginny and tears rolled down her cheeks. 她看著金尼，淚珠順著臉頰淌下。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Roll up</b> means the same as . 卷; 繞 (成柱形或團)","examples":["Stein rolled up the paper bag with the money inside. 斯坦把裝著錢的紙袋捲了起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>roll</b> <b>of</b> paper, plastic, cloth, or wire is a long piece of it that has been wrapped many times around itself or around a tube. (一) 卷","examples":["The photographers had already shot a dozen rolls of film. 攝影師們已經拍完了一打膠捲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>roll</b> is a small piece of bread that is round or long and is made to be eaten by one person. Rolls can be eaten plain, with butter, or with a filling. 麵包卷","examples":["He sipped at his coffee and spread butter and marmalade on a roll. 他抿了一口咖啡，將黃油和果醬塗在了麵包捲上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>roll</b> <b>of</b> drums is a long, low, fairly loud sound made by drums. 低緩的轟隆鼓聲","examples":["As the town clock struck two, they heard the roll of drums. 當鎮上的鐘敲響了兩點時，他們聽到了隆隆的鼓聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>roll</b> is an official list of people's names. 名冊","examples":["Pro-democracy activists say a new electoral roll should be drawn up. 親民主派活動分子們說應當起草一份新的候選人名單。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is several things <b>rolled into one</b>, it combines the main features or qualities of those things. 集於一體","examples":["This is our kitchen, living room, and dining room all rolled into one. 這是我們的廚房、客廳和餐廳都融為一體的房間。"]}]}]},"scientist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"科學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scientist</b> is someone who has studied science and whose job is to teach or do research in science. 科學家","examples":["Scientists say they've already collected more data than had been expected. 科學家們說他們已經蒐集到比預期更多的資料。"]}]}]},"secretary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"秘書；書記員，幹事；部長，大臣；（英國大使、大臣的）助理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>secretary</b> is a person who is employed to do office work, such as typing letters, answering phone calls, and arranging meetings. 秘書","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>secretary</b> of a company is the person who has the legal duty of keeping the company's records. (公司負責保管各種記錄的) 幹事","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Secretary</b> is used in the titles of high officials who are in charge of main government departments. 大臣; 部長","examples":["...a former Venezuelan foreign secretary. …一位前任委內瑞拉外交部長。"]}]}]},"semester":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學期，半學年"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In colleges and universities in some countries, a <b>semester</b> is one of the two main periods into which the year is divided. 學期","examples":["...February 22nd when most of their students begin their spring semester. …2月22日，大多數學生開始春季學期時。"]}]}]},"selection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選擇，挑選；被挑選的人（或物），精選品；可供選擇的事物；（比賽中值得賭的）看好的馬；所選資料；（英國的）學校入學選拔；<澳/新，史>（以優越條件）選購土地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Selection</b> is the act of selecting one or more people or things from a group. 挑選; 選擇","examples":["...Darwin's principles of natural selection. …達爾文的物競天擇理論。","Dr. Sullivan's selection to head the Department of Health was greeted with satisfaction. 由沙利文博士擔任衛生部部長的這項選擇很令人滿意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>selection</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a set of them that have been selected from a larger group. 挑選出的一群","examples":["...this selection of popular songs. …這組精選的通俗歌曲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>selection</b> <b>of</b> goods in a shop is the particular range of goods that it has available and from which you can choose what you want. (商店內) 可供選擇的商品範圍","examples":["It offers the widest selection of antiques of every description in a one day market. 在為時一天的集市上，它提供了選擇範圍廣泛的各式古董。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In computing, a <b>selection</b> is an area of the screen that you have highlighted, for example because you want to copy it to another file. (計算機螢幕上) 選定的板塊","examples":[]}]}]},"secret":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"秘密的，保密的；（感情、擔心、行動）不公開的，暗自的；（某人的行為）詭秘的，神秘的；善於掩飾自己的，嚴守秘密的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"秘密，內情；神秘，奧秘；秘訣，訣竅；（羅馬天主教彌撒捐獻儀式後牧師的）默禱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>secret</b>, it is known about by only a small number of people, and is not told or shown to anyone else. 秘密的; 保密的","examples":["Soldiers have been training at a secret location. 士兵們一直在一個秘密的地方訓練。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"秘密地","examples":["He wore a hidden microphone to secretly tape-record conversations. 他戴了一個竊聽器秘密錄下了談話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>secret</b> is a fact that is known by only a small number of people, and is not told to anyone else. 秘密","examples":["I think he enjoyed keeping our love a secret. 我想他喜歡對我們的戀情保密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a particular way of doing things is <b>the secret</b> <b>of</b> achieving something, you mean that it is the best or only way to achieve it. 秘訣","examples":["The secret of success is honesty and fair dealing. 成功的秘訣是誠實和公平交易。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something's <b>secrets</b> are the things about it which have never been fully explained. 奧秘","examples":["We have an opportunity now to really unlock the secrets of the universe. 我們現在有機會真正揭開宇宙的奧秘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in secret</b>, you do it without anyone else knowing. 秘密地","examples":["Dan found out that I had been meeting my ex-boyfriend in secret. 丹發現了我一直和前男友秘密見面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone can <b>keep a secret</b>, you mean that they can be trusted not to tell other people a secret that you have told them. 保守秘密","examples":["Tom was utterly indiscreet, and could never keep a secret. 湯姆言行完全不慎重，從來守不住秘密。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>make no secret</b> of something, you tell others about it openly and clearly. 不保密","examples":["His wife made no secret of her hatred for the formal occasions. 他的妻子不隱瞞她對正式場合的厭惡。"]}]}]},"score":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（遊戲或比賽中的）得分，比分；（測驗的）評分，分數；<非正式>實情，真相（the score）；<非正式>毒品到手；<非正式>犯罪所得；<正式>二十，約二十個（複數 score）；<正式>很多，大量（scores）；（一首樂曲的）總譜；（電影或戲劇的）配樂；刻痕，劃痕；宿怨；<史>（尤指酒館中有對應顧客名字刻痕的）往來賬戶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在運動、比賽或考試中）得（分）；評分，打分數；（在遊戲或比賽中）記分；（棒球）使（隊友）得分；<非正式>（使）成功，贏得；<英，非正式> （尤指在辯論等活動中機靈地）駁倒，挫敗（score off）；<非正式>購買，弄到（毒品）；<美，非正式>得到（某事物）；<非正式>（通常指與新認識的人）發生性關係；為……寫總譜，為……配樂；（在表面上）刻痕，畫線；畫掉，刪去（score sth. out/through）；檢測（實驗細胞、菌落等），並記錄有某種特徵的數量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a sport or game, if a player <b>scores</b> a goal or a point, they gain a goal or point. (比賽中) 得分; 進球","examples":["Patten scored his second touchdown of the game. 帕頓在比賽中第2次持球觸地得分。","He scored late in the third quarter to cut the gap to 10 points. 他在第3節快結束時進了一球，把分差縮小到10分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>score</b> a particular number or amount, for example, as a mark in a test, you achieve that number or amount. (測試) 得分","examples":["Kelly had scored an average of 147 on three separate IQ tests. 凱利在3次單獨進行的智商測試中平均得到147分。","Congress scores low in public opinion polls. 國會在民意測驗中得分很低。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>score</b> a success, a victory, or a hit, you are successful in what you are doing. 贏得","examples":["His abiding passion was ocean racing, at which he scored many successes. 他長期的愛好是海上賽艇，並曾贏得多次勝利。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>score</b> a surface with something sharp, you cut a line or number of lines in it. 劃線於; 刻痕於","examples":["Lightly score the surface of the steaks with a sharp cook's knife. 用一把鋒利的菜刀在牛排表面上輕輕打花刀。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>score</b> in a game or test is a number, for example, a number of points or runs, which shows what they have achieved or what level they have reached. 得分; 分數","examples":["The U.S. Open golf tournament was won by Ben Hogan, with a score of 287. 美國高爾夫球公開賽由本·霍根以287分奪冠。","He won this year's title with a score of 9.687. 他以9.687分贏得本年度的冠軍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>score</b> in a game is the result of it or the current situation, as indicated by the number of goals, runs, or points obtained by the two teams or players. 比分","examples":["4-1 was the final score. 最終比分是4：1。","They beat the Giants by a score of 7 to 3. 他們以7比3戰勝了巨人隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>score</b> of a movie, play, or similar production is the music which is written or used for it. (電影、戲劇等演出的) 配樂","examples":["The dance is accompanied by an original score by Henry Torgue. 舞蹈由亨利·托爾格的一支原創配樂作搭配。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>score</b> of a piece of music is the written version of it. 樂譜","examples":["He recognizes enough notation to be able to follow a score. 他認識足夠多的音樂符號，能看懂樂譜。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>scores of</b> things or people, you are emphasizing that there are very many of them. 大量","examples":["Campaigners lit scores of bonfires in ceremonies to mark the anniversary. 參加活動的人們在儀式上點起了許多堆篝火，以慶祝這一週年紀念日。"]}]},{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>score</b> is twenty or approximately twenty. 二十; 二十左右","examples":["A score of countries may be either producing or planning to obtain chemical weapons. 約有二十個國家可能在生產或計劃獲取化學武器。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep score</b> of the number of things that are happening in a certain situation, you count them and record them. 記數","examples":["You can keep score of your baby's movements before birth by recording them on a kick chart. 你可以在胎動圖表上記下分娩前胎兒的活動次數。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>know the score</b>, you know what the real facts of a situation are and how they affect you, even though you may not like them. 瞭解實情","examples":["I don't feel sorry for Carl. He knew the score, he knew what he had to do and couldn't do it. 我並不為卡爾感到難過。他了解實情，他知道他必須做什麼，但又沒能做成。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>on that score</b> or <b>on this score</b> to refer to something that has just been mentioned, especially an area of difficulty or concern. 在那/這一點上","examples":["I became pregnant easily. At least I've had no problems on that score. 我很容易就懷孕了。至少在那一點上我是沒問題的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>settle a score</b> or <b>settle an old score</b> <b>with</b> someone, you take revenge on them for something they have done in the past. 報復","examples":["The groups had historic scores to settle with each other. 這兩夥人之間有一些陳年老賬要算。"]}]}]},"servant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僕人，傭人；（公司或機構的）僱員，職員；獻身……的人，受……指引的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>servant</b> is someone who is employed to work at another person's home, for example, as a cleaner or a gardener. 僕人; 傭人","examples":["...a large Victorian family with several servants. …一個擁有幾名傭人的維多利亞時代的大家庭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>servant</b> to refer to someone or something that provides a service for people or can be used by them. 僱員","examples":["Like any other public servants, police must respond to public demand. 像任何其他公務員一樣，警察必須對公眾要求作出反應。"]}]}]},"screen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螢幕，熒光屏；銀幕；電影（總稱）；屏風，隔板；掩蔽物，屏障；紗窗，紗門；（醫療）化驗，檢查；（機動車的）擋風玻璃；（籃球、冰球等運動的）掩護；掩護部隊，護航艦隊；大篩子，濾網；（紗門或紗窗的）金屬絲，塑膠線；（印刷）網屏，網版；遮蔽器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"隱藏，遮蔽；庇護，包庇；檢查，篩查；審查，甄別；篩選，檢查排除；防止（或免受）電磁干擾；放映（影片），播放（電視節目）；分析，評估；加網印刷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>screen</b> is a flat vertical surface on which pictures or words are shown. Television sets and computers have screens, and movies are shown on a screen in movie theatres. (電視、電腦、影院等的) 螢幕","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to movies or television as <b>the screen</b>. 影視","examples":["Many viewers have strong opinions about violence on the screen. 許多觀眾對影視暴力有強烈意見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"放映; 播放","examples":["The film-makers will be present at the screenings to introduce their works. 電影製作人將在放映時到場介紹他們的作品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>screen</b> is a vertical panel which can be moved around. It is used to keep cold air away from part of a room, or to create a smaller area within a room. 屏風","examples":["They put a screen in front of me so I couldn't see what was going on. 他們在我面前放置了一扇屏風，因此我看不見在發生什麼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"檢查","examples":["Our country has an enviable record on breast screening for cancer. 我們國家在乳腺癌檢查方面有著令人羨慕的紀錄。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a movie or a television programme <b>is screened</b>, it is shown in the movie theatre or broadcast on television. 上映 (影片); 播放 (電視節目)","examples":["The series is likely to be screened in January. 這部系列劇可能在1月份播放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is screened</b> <b>by</b> another thing, it is behind it and hidden by it. 遮蔽; 遮擋","examples":["Most of the road behind the hotel was screened by an apartment block. 旅館後面那條路的大部分都被一排公寓樓擋住了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When an organization <b>screens</b> people who apply to join it, it investigates them to make sure that they are not likely to cause problems. 審查 (申請加入者)","examples":["They will screen all their candidates. 他們將審查他們所有的求職者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>screen</b> people or luggage means to check them using special equipment to make sure they are not carrying a weapon or a bomb. (為確保沒有攜帶武器等而) 檢查 (人、行李)","examples":["The airline had not been searching unaccompanied baggage by hand, but only screening it on X-ray machines. 這家航空公司一直沒有手工檢查非隨身行李，只是在X光機上檢查。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>screen</b> <b>for</b> a disease means to examine people to make sure that they do not have it. (為確定是否患有某病而) 做檢查","examples":["...a quick saliva test that would screen for people at risk of tooth decay. …一項能查出有患牙蝕風險的人群的快速唾液化驗。"]}]}]},"settlement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（解決爭端的）協議，和解；定居點，聚居地 ；殖民，開拓； <法律>（關於錢財轉讓的）協議（書）；（欠款的）支付，償付；（地面或建築物的）下沉，下陷；（按照協議規定收到的）金額；定居行動；結算，清賬；解決，處理；<美>部落，村落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>settlement</b> is an official agreement between two sides who were involved in a conflict or argument. 協議","examples":["Our objective must be to secure a peace settlement. 我們的目標必須是確保達成一個和平協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>settlement</b> is an agreement to end a disagreement or dispute without going to a court of law, for example, by offering someone money. (庭外) 和解","examples":["She accepted an out-of-court settlement of $40,000. 她接受了4萬美元庭外和解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>settlement</b> <b>of</b> a debt is the act of paying back money that you owe. 清償","examples":["...ways to delay the settlement of debts. …拖延債務清償的辦法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>settlement</b> is a place where people have come to live and have built homes. 定居地","examples":["The village is a settlement of just fifty houses. 這個村子是個僅有50家住戶的定居地。"]}]}]},"section":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"部分；散件，部件；（書、報等的）節，欄；一部分人；（樂隊的）組；斷面圖，剖面圖；（手術中的）開刀，切開；（供顯微鏡下觀察的）切片；<美>（柑橘類水果的）一瓣；（法律檔案的）款，項；地段，區域；部門，科；<新西> 建房用地；（生物）組（尤指亞屬）；<美> 一平方英里的土地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>  強制（精神病人）入院；將……製成切片；切開，切斷；分開，給……分割槽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>section</b> of something is one of the parts into which it is divided or from which it is formed. 部分","examples":["He said it was wrong to single out any section of society for AIDS testing. 他說挑出社會任何一部份人做艾滋病檢查都是錯誤的。","...the Georgetown section of Washington, D.C. …華盛頓特區的喬治敦區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>section</b> is a diagram of something such as a building or a part of the body. It shows how the object would appear to you if it were cut from top to bottom and looked at from the side. 剖面圖","examples":["For some buildings a vertical section is more informative than a plan. 對一些建築物來說，垂直剖面圖比平面圖提供的資訊更多。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is sectioned</b>, it is divided into sections. 分 (成若干部分)","examples":["It holds vegetables in place while they are being peeled or sectioned. 它在蔬菜被去皮或切分時將他們固定。"]}]}]},"shelf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擱板，架子；（尤指水中）陸架，底巖；<非正式>告密者（複數 shelfs）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>告發（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shelf</b> is a flat piece of wood, metal, or glass which is attached to a wall or to the sides of a cabinet. Shelves are used for keeping things on. 架子","examples":["He took a book from the shelf. 他從那個架上拿了一本書。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you buy something <b>off the shelf</b>, you buy something that is not specially made for you. 現貨出售的","examples":["Lower-priced jewellery will be sold off the shelf by this autumn. 低價的珠寶到今年秋天就將現貨出售。"]}]}]},"search":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搜查，搜尋；搜查（地方，車輛），搜……的身；思索，細想（問題答案等）；細察，細查；（用計算機）搜尋，檢索"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搜尋，搜查；探索，尋求；（計算機的）搜尋，檢索；<律>調查地產負擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>search</b> <b>for</b> something or someone, you look carefully for them. 搜尋","examples":["The Turkish security forces have started searching for the missing men. 土耳其安全部隊已經開始搜尋失蹤人員。","They searched for a spot where they could sit on the floor. 他們在地板上尋找一個能夠坐下的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>search</b> <b>for</b> information on a computer, you give the computer an instruction to find that information. (在計算機上) 搜尋","examples":["You can use a directory service to search for people on the Internet. 你可以使用目錄服務在因特網上搜尋人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>search</b> a place, you look carefully for something or someone there. 在 (某地) 搜尋; 搜查 (某地)","examples":["Armed troops searched the hospital yesterday. 武裝部隊昨天搜查了這家醫院。","She searched her desk for the necessary information. 她在她的書桌裡搜尋必要的資料。","Relief workers are still searching through collapsed buildings. 救援人員仍在塌了的建築物裡搜尋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a police officer or someone else in authority <b>searches</b> you, they look carefully to see whether you have something hidden on you. 搜 (某人) 身","examples":["The man took her suitcase from her and then searched her. 那個人從她手上拿走了她的手提箱然後搜了她的身。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>search</b> is an attempt to find something or someone by looking for them carefully. 搜尋","examples":["There was no chance of him being found alive and the search was abandoned. 沒有他活著被找到的可能了，於是放棄了搜尋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Search</b> is also a noun. 搜尋","examples":["He came across this story while he was doing a computer search of local news articles. 他在電腦上搜尋地方新聞文章時碰到了這篇報道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>in search of</b> something or someone, you try to find them. 尋找","examples":["Miserable, and unexpectedly lonely, she went in search of Jean-Paul. 由於痛苦和突如其來的孤獨，她去找讓–保羅了。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>search me</b>\" when someone asks you a question and you want to emphasize that you do not know the answer. 我哪知道","examples":["\"So why did he get interested all of a sudden?\"— \"Search me.\" “那麼他為什麼突然感興趣了呢？”—“我哪知道。”"]}]}]},"sidewalk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>人行道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sidewalk</b> is a path with a hard surface by the side of a road. 人行道","examples":[]}]}]},"shrimp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蝦，小蝦；<非正式> 矮子，無足輕重的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捕蝦"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"與蝦有關的；有蝦的，蝦制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shrimps</b> are small shellfish with long tails and many legs. 小蝦","examples":[]}]}]},"shell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（蛋、堅果、某些種子和某些動物的）殼；（甲蟲的）鞘翅；（尤指建築物等遭破壞後剩下的）框架，骨架；殼狀物；（人的）表面性格，表面感情；空軀殼；（物理）殼層；炮彈；<美>子彈，彈藥筒；輕型賽艇；內棺，粗製棺材；（劍的）護手；（計算機）SHELL PROGRAM 的簡稱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"剝……殼；炮轟；（從對方投手）大量得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>shell</b> of a nut or egg is the hard covering which surrounds it. (堅果或蛋的) 殼","examples":["They cracked the nuts and removed their shells. 他們打破堅果並剝掉果殼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shell</b> is the substance that a shell is made of. 殼料","examples":["...beads made from ostrich egg shell. …鴕鳥蛋殼做成的珠子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>shell</b> of an animal such as a tortoise, snail, or crab is the hard protective covering that it has around its body or on its back. (動物的) 甲殼","examples":["...the spiral form of a snail shell. …蝸牛殼的螺旋形狀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Shells</b> are hard objects found on beaches. They are usually pink, white, or brown and are the coverings which used to surround small sea creatures. 貝殼","examples":["I collect shells and interesting seaside items. 我收集貝殼以及海邊有趣的東西。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone comes out of their <b>shell</b>, they become more friendly and interested in other people and less quiet, shy, and reserved. 矜持","examples":["Her normally shy son had come out of his shell. 她那平時害羞的兒子已經開始活躍起來了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>shell</b> of a building, boat, car, or other structure is the outside frame of it. 框架","examples":["...the shells of burned buildings. …被燒燬的建築物的框架。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>shell</b> is a weapon consisting of a metal container filled with explosives that can be fired from a large gun over long distances. 炮彈","examples":["Tanks fired shells at the house. 坦克向那座房子發射炮彈。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"炮擊","examples":["Out on the streets, the shelling continued. 在外面街道上，炮擊在繼續。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shell</b> nuts, peas, shrimp, or other food, you remove their natural outer covering. 剝…的殼","examples":["She shelled and ate a few nuts. 她剝了一些堅果吃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>shell</b> a place means to fire explosive shells at it. 炮擊","examples":["The rebels shelled the densely-populated suburbs near the port. 那些叛亂者炮擊了港口附近人口稠密的郊區。"]}]}]},"shorts":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短褲；<美>男內褲（同 boxer shorts）；短片（short 的複數）；細麩粉；短期證券；（Shorts）<英>肖茨（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）短路（short 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[]},"shower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"淋浴器，花灑；淋浴間，淋浴室；淋浴，洗澡；陣雨，陣雪；（落下的東西）一大批，一陣； 流星雨；<美>（為即將結婚或分娩的女子舉行的）送禮聚會；<英，非正式> 一群烏合之眾，一群笨蛋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"淋浴，洗澡；灑落，（使）紛紛降落；朝......陣雨般地扔（大量小東西）（shower sb. with）；大量給予，慷慨給予"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shower</b> is a device for washing yourself. It consists of a pipe which ends in a flat cover with a lot of holes in it so that water comes out in a spray. 淋浴器","examples":["She heard him turn on the shower. 她聽見他擰開了淋浴器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shower</b> is a small enclosed area containing a shower. 淋浴間","examples":["Do you sing in the shower? 你在淋浴間裡唱歌嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>showers</b> or <b>the</b> <b>shower</b> in a place such as a gym is the area containing showers. (體育館等的) 浴室","examples":["The showers are a mess. 那些浴室一片狼藉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you take a <b>shower</b>, you wash yourself by standing under a spray of water from a shower. 淋浴","examples":["I think I'll take a shower before dinner. 我想晚飯前我要來次淋浴。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>shower</b> is a short period of rain, especially light rain. 陣雨","examples":["There'll be bright or sunny spells and scattered showers this afternoon. 今天下午將放晴，間有零星陣雨。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You can refer to a lot of things that are falling as a <b>shower</b> <b>of</b> them. 大量下落","examples":["Showers of sparks flew in all directions. 無數火星兒向四處飛濺。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>shower</b> is a party or celebration at which the guests bring gifts. 送禮會","examples":["...a baby shower. …為嬰兒舉行的送禮會。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"a derogatory term applied to a person or group, esp to a group considered as being slack, untidy, etc 懶散邋遢鬼","examples":[]},{"num":"9.","zh":"a large number of particles formed by the collision of a cosmic-ray particle with a particle in the atmosphere 鏃射粒子","examples":[]},{"num":"10.","zh":"a person or thing that shows 演出者; 展示物品","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shower</b>, you wash yourself by standing under a spray of water from a shower. 洗澡","examples":["There wasn't time to shower or change clothes. 沒時間洗澡或換衣服了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are showered with</b> a lot of small objects or pieces, they are scattered over you. 拋撒","examples":["They were showered with rice in the traditional manner. 人們按照傳統習俗朝他們拋撒大米。"]}]}]},"share":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"共享，合用；分享；分配；分擔（責任），分攤（費用）；共同擁有（看法、特質或經歷）；傾訴，吐露"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"股份，股票；（共有財產的）部分所有權；責任，貢獻；份額；（某物的）一個合理（或正常）的量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A company's <b>shares</b> are the many equal parts into which its ownership is divided. Shares can be bought by people as an investment. 股份; 股票","examples":["People in China are eager to buy shares in new businesses. 中國民眾熱衷於購買新企業的股票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is divided or distributed among a number of different people or things, each of them has, or is responsible for, a <b>share</b> <b>of</b> it. (若干中的) 一份","examples":["Sara also pays a share of the gas, electricity and phone bills. 薩拉也交一份煤氣、電和電話的費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have or do your <b>share</b> <b>of</b> something, you have or do an amount that seems reasonable to you, or to other people. (應擁有或承擔的) 一份","examples":["Women must receive their fair share of training for good-paying jobs. 婦女必須獲得找到高收入工作需要的應有的培訓。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> something <b>with</b> another person, you both have it, use it, or occupy it. You can also say that two people <b>share</b> something. 共有; 共用; 共享","examples":["...the small income he had shared with his brother from his father's estate. …他和他兄弟分享從他父親的地產中得來的一小筆收入。","Two Americans will share this year's Nobel Prize for Medicine. 兩位美國人將共同摘得今年的諾貝爾醫學獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> a task, duty, or responsibility <b>with</b> someone, you each carry out or accept part of it. You can also say that two people <b>share</b> something. 共同承擔; 分攤","examples":["You can find out whether they are prepared to share the cost of the flowers with you. 你會發現他們是否準備與你分攤鮮花的費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> an experience <b>with</b> someone, you have the same experience, often because you are with them at the time. You can also say that two people <b>share</b> something. 共享 (經歷)","examples":["Yes, I want to share my life with you. 是的，我想和你共享生活。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one person or thing <b>shares</b> a quality or characteristic <b>with</b> another, they have the same quality or characteristic. You can also say that two people or things <b>share</b> something. 共有 (特點)","examples":["La Repubblica and El Pais are politically independent newspapers which share similar characteristics. 《共和國報》和《國家報》是政治獨立的報紙，具有相似特徵。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> someone's opinion, you agree with them. 贊同 (某人的觀點)","examples":["The forum's members share his view that business can be a positive force for change in developing countries. 論壇的成員們都贊同他的觀點，即商業在發展中國家可以成為變革的積極推動力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> something that you have <b>with</b> someone, you give some of it to them or let them use it. 分享","examples":["He shared his food with the family. 他和家人分享了他的食物。","Scientists now have to compete for funding, and do not share information among themselves. 科學家們現在不得不為了資金而相互競爭，彼此間不共享資訊。","I wanted everybody to share. 我希望大家一起分享。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>share</b> something personal such as a thought or a piece of news <b>with</b> someone, you tell them about it. 分享 (個人感情、訊息等)","examples":["It can be beneficial to share your feelings with someone you trust. 與你信任的人分享你的情感會是有益的。"]}]}]},"silk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"絲綢，絲線；（騎手在賽馬時穿的）彩色絲綢賽馬服（silks）；綢制賽馬帽頂（蓋）；<英，非正式>王室律師；（雌玉米穗的）穗絲；蜘蛛絲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"絲的，絲制的"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（玉米）處於長鬚的階段中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Silk</b> is a substance which is made into smooth fine cloth and sewing thread. You can also refer to this cloth or thread as <b>silk</b>. 絲綢; 絲線","examples":["They continued to get their silks from China. 他們繼續從中國獲取絲綢。","Pauline wore a silk dress with a strand of pearls. 保利娜穿了一條帶有一串珍珠的絲綢連衣裙。"]}]}]},"shock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"令人震驚的事；吃驚，震驚；休克；電擊，觸電；減震器；（對經濟、傳統、生活方式的）衝擊，撞擊；（爆炸、地震等引起的）劇烈震動；濃密的頭髮；憤怒，生氣；衝擊力 ；（豎放在地裡促使穀物更快曬乾和成熟的）禾束堆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使震驚，使難以置信；（言語或行為）（使）憤慨，（使）生氣；使觸電，使遭電擊；使恐懼（或厭惡）；使生理休克；把......堆成禾束堆"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人震驚的，令人大感意外的（尤用於新聞報道）；濃密的，蓬亂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>shock</b>, something suddenly happens which is unpleasant, upsetting, or very surprising. 震驚","examples":["The extent of the violence came as a shock. 暴力的程度令人震驚。","He has never recovered from the shock of your brother's death. 他從來沒有從你兄弟的死所帶來的震驚中恢復過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shock</b> is a person's emotional and physical condition when something very frightening or upsetting has happened to them. (身心受到的) 驚嚇","examples":["The little boy was speechless with shock. 這個小男孩被嚇得說不出話來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>in</b> <b>shock</b>, they are suffering from a serious physical condition in which their blood is not flowing around their body properly, for example, because they have had a bad injury. 休克","examples":["He was found beaten and in shock. 他被發現遭到毆打，處於休克中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>shock</b> is the force of something suddenly hitting or pulling something else. 衝擊力","examples":["Steel barriers can bend and absorb the shock. 鐵柵欄會彎曲並吸收衝擊力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>shock</b> is the same as an . 電擊","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a thick bushy mass, esp of hair (尤指頭髮)濃密厚重的一把","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shocks</b> you, it makes you feel very upset, because it involves death or suffering and because you had not expected it. 使震驚","examples":["After forty years in the police force nothing much shocks me. 在警察部門幹了40年後，沒有什麼能令我非常震驚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>shocks</b> you, it upsets or offends you because you think it is vulgar or morally wrong. 使不快; 不快","examples":["You can't shock me. 你不會讓我生氣。","They were easily shocked in those days. 他們那時候容易被激怒。","...the desire to shock …發怒的慾望。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"震驚的","examples":["This was a nasty attack and the woman is still very shocked. 這是一次嚴重的襲擊，這個女人仍然感到非常震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"生氣的","examples":["Don't look so shocked. 別這麼生氣。"]}]}]},"silence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寂靜，無聲；沉默，默不作聲；保持沉默，拒絕回答；無音信，失去聯絡；默哀，靜默"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使安靜，使不說話；壓制，使不再發表（反對意見）；殺……滅口；給（槍，排氣系統）裝消音器"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<正式>（用以讓人們安靜）安靜，靜下來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>silence</b>, nobody is speaking. 沉默","examples":["They stood in silence. 他們默默地站著。","He never lets those long silences develop during dinner. 他在晚餐時從不會讓長時間的沉默出現。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>silence</b> about something is their failure or refusal to speak to other people about it. 緘默","examples":["The district court ruled that Popper's silence in court today should be entered as a plea of not guilty. 該區法院裁決波珀今天在法庭中的緘默應被看作是進行無罪抗辯。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>breaks</b> their <b>silence</b> about something, they talk about something that they have not talked about before or for a long time. 打破沉默; 開口講話","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>silences</b> you, they stop you from expressing opinions that they do not agree with. 制止 (發表不同意見)","examples":["Like other tyrants, he tried to silence anyone who spoke out against him. 像其他暴君一樣，他試圖壓制任何公開反對他的人。"]}]}]},"skirt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女裙，半身裙；（連衣裙、外衣等的）下襬（skirts）；（車輛或機器基座的）擋板，裙板；（供食用的）多筋動物肉；<英> 腰窩肉；（馬鞍的）垂邊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"環繞……的四周，沿……的邊緣走；繞開，迴避（話題）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>skirt</b> is a piece of clothing worn by women and girls. It fastens at the waist and hangs down around the legs. 裙子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>skirts</b> an area is situated around the edge of it. 位於…的邊緣; 圍繞","examples":["We raced across a large field that skirted the slope of a hill. 我們快速穿越山坡邊的一大片曠野。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>skirt</b> a problem or question, you avoid dealing with it. 迴避 (問題等)","examples":["He skirted the hardest issues, concentrating on areas of possible agreement. 他避開最難的問題，而專注於可能達成一致意見的領域。"]}]}]},"slipper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"室內便鞋，拖鞋；輕便舞鞋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用拖鞋打（人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slippers</b> are loose, soft shoes that you wear at home. 拖鞋","examples":["...a pair of old slippers. …一雙舊拖鞋。"]}]}]},"shoot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開（槍），射擊；射殺，射傷；狩獵，打獵；投（球），射門；玩，打（某種遊戲）；拍攝；（使）急速移動；突然把……投向；迅速成名；（疼痛）穿刺；閂上，拔出（門閂）；（植物，種子）發芽；<非正式>注射（毒品）；準確刨平（木板的邊角）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嫩芽，新枝；拍攝；狩獵，射獵場，射擊比賽；斜道，滑運道（=chute）；急流，奔流"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"說吧，請講；<美>糟糕，哎呀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>shoots</b> a person or an animal, they kill them or injure them by firing a bullet or arrow at them. 射死; 射傷","examples":["The police had orders to shoot anyone who attacked them. 警察得到命令可以向任何襲擊他們的人開槍。","The man was shot dead by the police during a raid on his house. 這個人在一次對他家的突擊搜查時被警察擊斃了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shoot</b> something somewhere or if it <b>shoots</b> somewhere, it moves there quickly and suddenly. 猛然移動","examples":["Masters shot a hand across the table and gripped his wrist. 師傅突然把一隻手伸過桌子，抓住他的手腕。","As soon as she got close, the old woman's hand shot out. 她一靠近，那個老婦人的手就猛地伸了出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>shoot</b> a look at someone, you look at them quickly and briefly, often in a way that expresses your feelings. 瞥","examples":["Mary Ann shot him a rueful look. 瑪麗·安悔恨地瞥了他一眼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When people <b>shoot</b> a movie or <b>shoot</b> photographs, they make a movie or take photographs using a camera. 拍攝","examples":["He'd love to shoot his film in Cuba. 他很樂意在古巴拍攝他的電影。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>shoot</b> means to fire a bullet from a weapon such as a gun. 射擊","examples":["He taunted armed officers by pointing to his head, as if inviting them to shoot. 他指著自己的頭來奚落武裝警察，彷彿是在招惹他們開槍一樣。","The police came around the corner and they started shooting at us. 警察來到拐角，他們開始朝我們開槍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>shoots</b> in a particular direction, they move in that direction quickly and suddenly. 猛衝","examples":["They had almost reached the boat when a figure shot past them. 他們幾乎快要到達船上時，一個人影衝過他們身旁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>shoots</b> <b>to</b> fame, they become famous or successful very quickly. 迅速 (成名)","examples":["Alina Reyes shot to fame a few years ago with her extraordinary first novel. 阿麗娜·雷耶斯幾年前憑藉她那非凡的小說處女作迅速成名。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In sports such as football or basketball, when someone <b>shoots</b>, they try to score by kicking or throwing the ball toward the goal or hoop. 射門; 投籃","examples":["Spencer scuttled away from Singh to shoot wide when he should have scored. 斯賓塞快速晃開辛格卻射門偏出，而他本應該得分的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shoot</b> is also a noun. 拍攝","examples":["...a barn presently being used for a video shoot. …一個目前被用於電視拍攝的穀倉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shoots</b> are plants that are beginning to grow, or new parts growing from a plant or tree. 新芽","examples":["Prune established plants annually as new shoots appear. 每年嫩芽長出來時，要給長成的植物剪枝。"]}]}]},"single":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單一的，單個的；單身的，未婚的；各自的，分別的；單人的，單人用的；<英>（票）單程的；統一的；由一個部分構成的；（花）單瓣的；唯一的；（酒的）一份"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"單曲唱片；（板球中的）一分打，（棒球中的）一壘打；單身者，未婚者；<英> 單程票；（旅館等的）單人房間；單打（比賽）；<美，非正式> 一元紙幣；（鳴鐘術）不同次序鳴鐘法；<美>（影劇院的）一張票，一個座位；一份酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挑選，選出；（棒球）擊出一壘打；對（幼苗，幼樹）進行間苗；將（鐵軌）變成單線；以一壘打使（跑壘）得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>single</b> to emphasize that you are referring to one thing, and no more than one thing. 單個的; 一個的","examples":["A single shot rang out. 一聲槍響。","Over six hundred people were wounded in a single day. 一天內六百多人受傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>single</b> to indicate that you are considering something on its own and separately from other things like it. 個別的; 一個個的; 每一個的","examples":["Every single house in town had been damaged. 鎮上的每一座房子都被毀壞了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>single</b> is not married. You can also use <b>single</b> to describe someone who does not have a girlfriend or boyfriend. 未婚的; 單身的","examples":["Is it difficult being a single mother? 當單身母親難嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>single</b> room is a room intended for one person to stay or live in. 單人的 (房間)","examples":["Each guest has her own single room, or shares, on request, a double room. 每位客人都有自己的單人房間，經要求也可共用雙人間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>single</b> bed is wide enough for one person to sleep in. 單人的 (床)","examples":["...his bedroom with its single bed. …他那間有一張單人床的臥室。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>single</b> ticket is a ticket for a trip from one place to another but not back again. 單程的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Single</b> is also a noun. 單人間","examples":["It's $65 for a single, $98 for a double and $120 for an entire suite. 單人間$65，雙人間$98，套房$120。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Single</b> is also a noun. 單程票","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>single</b> is a small record which has one song on each side. A <b>single</b> is also a CD which has a few short songs on it. You can also refer to the main song on a record or CD as a <b>single</b>. 單曲唱片; 鐳射唱片; 唱片主歌","examples":["The winners will pocket a cash sum and get a chance to release their debut CD single. 獲勝者將獲得一筆現金，並有機會發行他們的首張鐳射唱片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Singles</b> is a game of tennis or badminton in which one player plays another. The plural <b>singles</b> can be used to refer to one or more of these matches. (網球、羽毛球等的) 單打比賽","examples":["Lleyton Hewitt won the men's singles. 雷頓·休伊特贏得了男子單打比賽。"]}]}]},"snack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"零食，點心，小吃；快餐；<澳，非正式>易辦到的事，小菜一碟"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吃點心，吃零食"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snack</b> is a simple meal that is quick to cook and to eat. 快餐","examples":["Lunch was a snack in the fields. 午飯是在野外吃的快餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>snack</b> is something such as a chocolate bar that you eat between meals. (正餐之間的) 小吃","examples":["Do you eat sweets, cakes or sugary snacks? 你吃糖果、糕點或甜點心嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>snack</b>, you eat snacks between meals. 吃小吃","examples":["Instead of snacking on crisps and chocolate, nibble on celery or carrot. 不要吃炸薯片和巧克力這些零食，要啃點芹菜或胡蘿蔔。"]}]}]},"snail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蝸牛；遲鈍的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩慢移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snail</b> is a small animal with a long, soft body, no legs, and a spiral-shaped shell. Snails move very slowly. 蝸牛","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>at a snail's pace</b>, you are emphasizing that they are doing it very slowly, usually when you think it would be better if they did it much more quickly. 慢吞吞地","examples":["The train was moving now at a snail's pace. 火車現在正緩慢行駛。"]}]}]},"sign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指示牌，標誌；跡象，徵兆；示意動作，手勢；手語動作；符號，記號；蹤跡，蹤影；（醫）徵，體徵；神蹟（主要用於《聖經》和文學作品中）；<美>（野生動物的）足跡，臭跡；（占星）（黃道12宮中的）宮，星座；（數）正負號；暗號，訊號；（表示某人狀況或經歷的）動作，反應"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"簽名，署名；（與機構、公司等）簽約；示意，打手勢；打手語；用標誌杆（或其他記號）表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sign</b> is a mark or shape that always has a particular meaning, for example, in mathematics or music. 符號","examples":["Equations are generally written with an equal sign. 等式通常用等號來寫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sign</b> is a movement of your arms, hands, or head which is intended to have a particular meaning. 姿勢; 手勢","examples":["They gave Lavalle the thumbs-up sign. 他們給拉瓦列做了一個豎起大拇指的手勢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sign</b> is a piece of wood, metal, or plastic with words or pictures on it. Signs give you information about something, or give you a warning or an instruction. 指示牌","examples":["...a sign saying that the motorway was closed because of snow. …一個寫著公路因大雪封閉的指示牌。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If there is a <b>sign</b> <b>of</b> something, there is something which shows that it exists or is happening. 跡象; 徵兆","examples":["They are prepared to hand back a hundred prisoners of war a day as a sign of good will. 作為一種友好的表示，他們準備一天遣返100名戰犯。","His face and movements rarely betrayed a sign of nerves. 他的表情和行為很少流露出緊張的跡象。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In astrology, a <b>sign</b> or a <b>sign</b> <b>of the zodiac</b> is one of the twelve areas into which the heavens are divided. 星座","examples":["The new moon takes place in your opposite sign of Libra on the 15th. 15日新月會出現在天秤座的對面。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sign</b>, you communicate with someone using sign language. If a programme or performance <b>is signed</b>, someone uses sign language so that deaf people can understand it. 打手勢; (節目或表演) 配手勢語","examples":["All programmes will be either \"signed\" or subtitled. 所有的節目都配有手勢語或者字幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>sign</b> a document, you write your name on it, usually at the end or in a special space. You do this to indicate that you have written the document, that you agree with what is written, or that you were present as a witness. 在…上簽名; 簽署","examples":["World leaders are expected to sign a treaty pledging to increase environmental protection. 人們期望世界領導人們能簽署一份承諾加強環境保護的條約。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an organization <b>signs</b> someone or if someone <b>signs</b> for an organization, they sign a contract agreeing to work for that organization for a specified period of time. 簽約僱用; 簽約受僱","examples":["The Minnesota Vikings signed Herschel Walker from the Dallas Cowboys. 明尼蘇達維京人隊簽約僱用了達拉斯牛仔隊的赫舍爾·沃克。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>no sign of</b> someone, you mean that they have not yet arrived, although you are expecting them to come. 不見某人的蹤影","examples":["The train was on time, but there was no sign of my Finnish friend. 火車準時到達了，但還沒有見到我芬蘭朋友的蹤影。"]}]}]},"soccer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英式足球，足球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soccer</b> is a game played by two teams of eleven players using a round ball. Players kick the ball to each other and try to score goals by kicking the ball into a large net. Outside the United States, this game is also referred to as . 英式足球","examples":["...a soccer match. …一場英式足球比賽。"]}]}]},"slide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）滑行，滑動；滑落；迅速熟練地進出；（使）快捷而悄聲地移動；（價格等）下滑，下跌；逐漸敗壞，開始出現問題；滑壘"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"滑梯；滑道；滑行，滑動；（價格、數量等的）下降，跌落，減少；幻燈片；（情況）變糟，惡化，（人）出現問題；（顯微鏡的）載物玻璃片；（樂器或機器上的）滑動裝置；（岩石，土等的）崩落；小發夾；（棒球）滑壘；（吉他）滑奏；無後幫涼鞋（或輕便鞋）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>slides</b> somewhere or when you <b>slide</b> it there, it moves there smoothly over or against something. 使滑動; 滑動","examples":["She slid the door open. 她把門滑開了。","I slid the wallet into his pocket. 我把那錢包滑進了他的口袋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If currencies or prices <b>slide</b>, they gradually become worse or lower in value. 使減少; 下跌","examples":["The dollar continued to slide. 美元繼續下跌。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slide</b> somewhere, you move there smoothly and quietly. 悄悄地溜到","examples":["He slid into the driver's seat. 他悄悄地坐到了司機的座位上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>slide into</b> a particular mood, attitude, or situation means to gradually start to have that mood, attitude, or situation often without intending to. 不知不覺地陷入 (某種情緒、態度或情形)","examples":["She had slid into a depression. 她不知不覺地抑鬱寡歡起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slide</b> is also a noun. 下跌","examples":["...the dangerous slide in oil prices. …石油價格危險的下跌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slide</b> is a small piece of photographic film which you project onto a screen so that you can see the picture. 幻燈片","examples":["...a slide show. …幻燈片放映。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>slide</b> is a piece of glass on which you put something that you want to examine through a microscope. (顯微鏡的) 載物玻璃片","examples":["...a drop of blood on a slide. …載物玻璃片上的一滴血。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>slide</b> is a piece of playground equipment that has a steep slope for children to go down for fun. 滑梯","examples":["...two young children playing on a slide. …在玩滑梯的兩個年幼的孩子。"]}]}]},"sock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短襪；<非正式>猛擊，重擊；（馬小腿處的）白色標記；<美>實力，重點；鞋墊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>猛擊；<非正式>使遭損失，損害；<美>（棒球運動中）猛擊，狠打（球）；給……穿襪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Socks</b> are pieces of clothing which cover your foot and ankle and are worn inside shoes. 短襪","examples":["...a pair of knee-high socks. …一雙齊膝的短襪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a forceful blow 勁風","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sock</b> someone or something, you hit them hard. 重擊","examples":["Once, after a boy made a comment, she socked him. 有一次，一個男孩子發表了一點意見，她就揮拳猛擊他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is socked</b> <b>with</b> something bad, it happens to them. (遭不利的事) 打擊","examples":["Phil got socked with a bill for nearly $1,000. 菲爾因一張近$1000的賬單蒙受損失。"]}]}]},"sink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"下沉，沉沒；使失敗，受挫；下降，下陷；倒下，坐下；衰退，惡化；滲透，漸漸陷入；減少，降低；（聲音）變低，變小；墮落，沉淪；挖掘；插入，打入；投進，滾進；投資；<英，非正式>喝（酒）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英>貧困的，貧民窟的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水槽，水池；窪地，滲坑；<英，喻>位於社會貧困地區的學校或房產；<喻>藏垢的場所；<技>匯，壑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sink</b> is a large fixed container in a kitchen or bathroom, with faucets to supply water. In the kitchen, it is used for washing dishes, and in the bathroom, it is used to wash your hands and face. (固定在廚房裡的) 洗滌槽; (固定在浴室裡的) 洗臉盆","examples":["The sink was full of dirty dishes. 水池裡滿是髒碟子。","The bathroom is furnished with 2 toilets, 2 showers, and 2 sinks. 衛生間裡裝有2個便池，2個淋浴器和2個洗臉盆。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a boat <b>sinks</b> or if someone or something <b>sinks</b> it, it disappears below the surface of a mass of water. 使沉沒; 下沉","examples":["In a naval battle your aim is to sink the enemy's ship. 在海戰中，你的目標是要擊沉敵艦。","The boat was beginning to sink fast. 那艘船開始迅速下沉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something sharp <b>sinks</b> or <b>is sunk</b> <b>into</b> something solid, it goes deeply into it. 深深切入","examples":["I sank my teeth into a peppermint cream. 我的牙齒咬住了一塊薄荷奶油糖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>sinks</b> a well, mine, or other large hole, they make a deep hole in the ground, usually by digging or drilling. 打 (水井); 挖 (礦井)","examples":["...the site where Stephenson sank his first mineshaft. …斯蒂芬森挖第一口礦井時的舊址。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>sink</b> money <b>into</b> a business or project, you spend money on it in the hope of making more money. 投入 (資金)","examples":["He has already sunk $25 million into the project. 他已經在這個專案投入了2500萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>sinks</b>, it disappears below the surface of a mass of water. 沉沒","examples":["A fresh egg will sink and an old egg will float. 新鮮雞蛋會下沉，舊雞蛋會浮起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>sinks</b>, it moves slowly downward. 下沉","examples":["Far off to the west the sun was sinking. 遠遠的，太陽在西邊落下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>sinks</b> <b>to</b> a lower level or standard, it falls to that level or standard. 下降","examples":["Share prices would have sunk – hurting small and big investors. 股票價格本來會下跌–傷及大大小小的投資者。","Pay increases have sunk to around seven percent. 工資增長已下降到7％左右。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your heart or your spirits <b>sink</b>, you become depressed or lose hope. (心情) 沮喪; (情緒) 低落","examples":["My heart sank because I thought he was going to dump me for another girl. 我的心情沮喪，因為我認為他要把我甩了，去追求另一個姑娘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone will have to <b>sink or swim</b>, you mean that they will have to succeed through their own efforts, or fail. 自主沉浮","examples":["I think athletes sink or swim depending on how they motivate themselves. 我認為運動員的成敗取決於他們如何激勵自己。"]}]}]},"somebody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"某人，有人；重要人物，當權人物"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大人物，重要人物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Somebody</b> means the same as . 某人","examples":[]}]}]},"society":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社會（以群體形式生活在一起的人的總稱）；社群（某國家、地區、時期等的群體組織）；社團，協會；上層社會；交往，相伴；階層，界；植物的群落，動物的群體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Society</b> is people in general, thought of as a large organized group. 社會 (指社會中所有的人)","examples":["This reflects attitudes and values prevailing in society. 這反映出社會上普遍流行的態度和價值觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>society</b> is the people who live in a country or region, their organizations, and their way of life. 社會; (生活於某個地區、有自己生活方式的) 群體","examples":["We live in a capitalist society. 我們生活在資本主義社會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>society</b> is an organization for people who have the same interest or aim. 社團; 協會","examples":["...the Atlanta Horticultural Society. …亞特蘭大園藝協會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Society</b> is the rich, fashionable people in a particular place who meet on social occasions. 上流社會","examples":["The couple quickly became a fixture in society. 這對夫婦很快就成為上流社會的常客。"]}]}]},"soldier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"士兵，軍人；（昆） 兵蟻；垂直的磚（或木頭等建築材料）；<英，非正式>麵包條，土司條；懶漢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當兵；堅持不懈，迎難而上（~ on）；假稱害病；磨洋工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>soldier</b> is a member of an army, especially a person who is not an officer. 士兵","examples":[]}]}]},"soy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大豆，豆製品（soya 的別名）；醬油"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soy</b> is the same as . 同soya","examples":[]}]}]},"solution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（問題、困難等的）解決辦法；（練習或競賽的）解答，答案；溶液；溶解過程，溶解狀態；（滿足特定需要的）產品（或服務）（solutions）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>solution</b> <b>to</b> a problem or difficult situation is a way of dealing with it so that the difficulty is removed. 解決辦法","examples":["Although he has sought to find a peaceful solution, he is facing pressure to use greater military force. 雖然他已設法尋找一個和平的解決辦法，但他正面臨著使用更大軍事力量的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>solution</b> <b>to</b> a puzzle is the answer to it. 謎底","examples":["We invited readers who completed the puzzle to send in their solutions. 我們邀請解完謎的讀者交出謎底。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>solution</b> is a liquid in which a solid substance has been dissolved. 溶液","examples":["...a warm solution of liquid detergent. …液體洗潔精的溫熱稀釋溶液。"]}]}]},"slip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"滑倒，失足；滑落，脫落；溜走，悄悄地走；偷偷塞進；滑行，打滑；下降，變差；陷入；迅速穿上，迅速脫下；擺脫，掙脫；飛逝，過得飛快；被（某人）忘記；放出（動物，尤指獵狗）；（身體部分）移位，脫臼；（編織）挑過一針不結；略微鬆動（汽車離合器）；（動物）流產"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"疏漏，差錯；小紙條；滑，滑倒；滑動；襯裙；（擊球員後側的）守場員；（製陶器用的）泥漿，泥釉；（飛機飛行中的）側滑；牽狗皮帶；（兩個碼頭之間）泊位；（編織）挑針；變糟，下跌；接枝，插枝；瘦小的年輕人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slip</b>, you accidentally slide and lose your balance. 滑; 滑倒","examples":["He had slipped on an icy pavement. 他在結冰的人行道上滑倒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>slips</b>, it slides out of place or out of your hand. 滑走; 滑落","examples":["His glasses had slipped. 他的眼鏡滑落了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>slip</b> somewhere, you go there quickly and quietly. 溜走","examples":["Amy slipped downstairs and out of the house. 埃米悄悄地下樓，溜出了屋子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>slip into</b> a particular state or situation means to pass gradually into it, in a way that is hardly noticed. (不知不覺地) 陷入","examples":["It amazed him how easily one could slip into a routine. 一個人如此容易就能陷入俗套，這使他感到吃驚。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slip</b> something somewhere, you put it there quickly in a way that does not attract attention. 把…悄悄地放在","examples":["I slipped a note under Louise's door. 我悄悄地把一張字條塞到了路易絲的門下。","He found a coin in his pocket and slipped it into her hand. 他在口袋裡找到一枚硬幣，把它悄悄塞進她的手裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>slip</b> something <b>to</b> someone, you give it to them secretly. 偷偷地給","examples":["Robert had slipped her a note in school. 羅伯特上學時偷偷地塞給了她一張字條。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>slips</b> <b>to</b> a lower level or standard, it falls to that level or standard. 使下降; 下降","examples":["Shares slipped to $1.17. 股票下跌至$1.17。","In June, producer prices slipped 0.1% from May. 六月份，生產商的價格從五月份下降了0.1%。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>slip</b> <b>into</b> or <b>out of</b> clothes or shoes, you put them on or take them off quickly and easily. 迅速輕鬆地穿上; 迅速輕鬆地脫下","examples":["She slipped out of the jacket and tossed it on the couch. 她快速脫下了那件上衣，把它丟在沙發上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slip</b> is also a noun. 下降","examples":["...a slip in consumer confidence. …消費者信心的一次下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slip</b> is a small or unimportant mistake. 差錯; 疏漏","examples":["We must be well prepared, there must be no slips. 我們必須好好準備，一定不要有差錯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>slip</b> <b>of</b> paper is a small piece of paper. 紙條","examples":["...little slips of paper he had torn from a notebook. …他從筆記本上撕下的幾張小紙片。","I put her name on the slip. 我把她的名字寫在那張紙條上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>slip</b> is a thin piece of clothing that a woman wears under her dress or skirt. 襯裙","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"clay mixed with water to a creamy consistency, used for decorating or patching a ceramic piece 粘土與水的混合物","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a part of a plant that, when detached from the parent, will grow into a new plant; cutting; scion 接枝; 插枝","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to detach (portions of stem, etc) from (a plant) for propagation (從植物)取接枝","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>let slip</b> information, you accidentally tell it to someone, when you wanted to keep it secret. 無意中說出 (秘密)","examples":["I bet he let slip that I'd gone to America. 我確信他無意中說出了我已去了美國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>slips</b> your <b>mind</b>, you forget about it. 被遺忘","examples":["The reason for my visit had obviously slipped his mind. 我到訪的原因顯然被他忘了。"]}]}]},"soybean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大豆，黃豆（一年生豆科植物；也指這種植物富含蛋白質和油脂的種子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soybeans</b> are the same as <b>soya beans</b>. 同soya beans","examples":[]}]}]},"spinach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"菠菜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>未必很有趣但有益的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spinach</b> is a vegetable with large dark green leaves. 菠菜","examples":[]}]}]},"source":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"來源，出處；（問題的）原因，根源；訊息人士，資訊來源；河流源頭，發源地；源（代）碼；（電子）源極，電源；（技）源"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（從某地）獲得；找出……的來源"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>source</b> <b>of</b> something is the person, place, or thing which you get it from. 來源","examples":["...over 40 percent of adults use television as their major source of information about the arts. …超過40%的成年人利用電視作為他們瞭解藝術資訊的主要來源。","Renewable sources of energy must be used. 可再生的能源必須利用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>source</b> is a person or book that provides information for a news story or for a piece of research. 訊息來源","examples":["Military sources say the boat was heading south at high speed. 軍方的訊息來源說船正向南方快速駛去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>source of</b> a difficulty is its cause. 根源","examples":["This gave me a clue as to the source of the problem. 這給了我一個關於問題根源的線索。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>source</b> of a river or stream is the place where it begins. 源頭","examples":["...the source of the Tiber. …臺伯河的源頭。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In business, if a person or firm <b>sources</b> a product or a raw material, they find someone who will supply it. 尋找…的來源","examples":["Together they travel the world, sourcing clothes for the small, privately owned company. 他們一起環遊世界，為那家小私營公司尋找服裝貨源。"]}]}]},"spelling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拼寫，拼寫能力；拼法，拼讀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用字母）拼寫，拼出；招致，意味著（通常指壞事）；替換，頂替（spell 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spelling</b> is the correct order of the letters in a word. 拼寫","examples":["In most languages adjectives have slightly different spellings for masculine and feminine. 在大多數語言中形容詞對於陽性和陰性有略微不同的拼寫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spelling</b> is the ability to spell words in the correct way. It is also an attempt to spell a word in the correct way. 拼寫能力; 拼寫","examples":["His spelling is very bad. 他的拼寫能力很差。"]}]}]},"spider":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜘蛛；（搜尋引擎的）蜘蛛程式，（計算機）爬蟲程式；狀似蜘蛛的物體；<英>蛛網形系索；檯球棒三腳架；設圈套者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（似蜘蛛般）急促爬動；設網，設圈套；（在因特網上）快速搜尋（crawl 的別名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spider</b> is a small creature with eight legs. Most types of spiders make structures called webs in which they catch insects for food. 蜘蛛","examples":[]}]}]},"speaker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發言者，演講者；說話者；講某種語言的人；揚聲器，喇叭；（議會或立法機構的）議長（Speaker）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>speaker</b> at a meeting, conference, or other gathering is a person who is making a speech or giving a talk. 演講者; 發言者","examples":["Among the speakers at the gathering was Treasury Secretary Nicholas Brady. 在那次聚會上發言的人當中有財政部長尼古拉斯•布雷迪。","Bruce Wyatt will be the guest speaker at next month's meeting. 布魯斯•懷亞特將是下月會議上的特邀發言人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>speaker</b> <b>of</b> a particular language is a person who speaks it, especially one who speaks it as their first language. 說某種語言者","examples":["...in the Ukraine, where a fifth of the population are Russian speakers. …在有五分之一的人口說俄語的烏克蘭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the legislature or parliament of many countries, the <b>Speaker</b> is the person who is in charge of meetings. (立法機構或議會的) 議長","examples":["...the Speaker of the House. …議院議長。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>speaker</b> is a person who is speaking. 說話者","examples":["From a simple gesture or the speaker's tone of voice, the Japanese listener gleans the whole meaning. 從一個簡單的手勢或說話者的聲調這位日本聽者捕捉到全部含義。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>speaker</b> is a piece of electrical equipment, for example part of a radio or set of equipment for playing CDs or tapes, through which sound comes out. 揚聲器","examples":["For a good stereo effect, the speakers should not be too wide apart. 為了取得好的立體聲效果，揚聲器之間不應該間隔太寬。"]}]}]},"sort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"種類，品種；某一種（或某一類）人；（計算機對資訊的）分類，排序；<古>程度，方式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"整理，把……分類，揀選；妥善處理，安排妥當；交往；協調"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a particular <b>sort</b> <b>of</b> something, you are talking about a class of things that have particular features in common and that belong to a larger group of related things. 種類","examples":["What sort of school did you go to? 你上的是哪一類學校？","There are so many different sorts of mushrooms available these days. 這些日子可買到各種各樣的蘑菇。","A dozen trees of various sorts were planted. 各型別共12棵樹被種下了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You describe someone as a particular <b>sort</b> when you are describing their character. 型別","examples":["He seemed to be just the right sort for the job. 他似乎就是該工作的合適人選。","She was a very vigorous sort of person. 她是那種精力非常旺盛的人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sort</b> things, you separate them into different classes, groups, or places, for example so that you can do different things with them. 分類","examples":["He sorted the materials into their folders. 他將材料分類放入他們的資料夾裡。","He unlatched the box and sorted through the papers. 他開啟盒子的鎖，在檔案裡分類揀選。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>All sorts</b> <b>of</b> things or people means a large number of different things or people. 各種各樣","examples":["There are all sorts of animals, including bears, pigs, kangaroos, and penguins. 有各種各樣的動物，包括熊、豬、袋鼠和企鵝。","It was used by all sorts of people. 它被各種人使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as a thing <b>of sorts</b> or as a thing <b>of a sort</b>, you are suggesting that the thing is of a rather poor quality or standard. (質量) 不怎麼樣","examples":["He made a living of sorts selling encyclopedias door-to-door. 他靠挨家挨戶推銷百科全書勉強謀生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>sort of</b> when you want to say that your description of something is not very accurate. 有點兒像","examples":["You could even order windows from a catalogue – a sort of mail order stained glass service. 你甚至可以從目錄上預訂窗戶–有點兒像郵購彩色玻璃服務。"]}]}]},"speed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（運動）速度；（某事發生或進行的）速度；快，迅速；排擋，變速器；快門速度；感光度；照片曝光的時間；<非正式>安非他明；<古>成功，繁榮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"快速移動；快速運送；超速駕駛；（使）加速，促進；<古>使興旺發達，幫助成功；<非正式>用（脫氧麻黃鹼之類的）興奮劑成癮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>speed</b> of something is the rate at which it moves or travels. (移動、執行的) 速度","examples":["He drove off at high speed. 他高速駕車離去了。","Wind speeds reached force five. 風速達到了5級。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>speed</b> of something is the rate at which it happens or is done. (發生、完成的) 速度","examples":["In the late 1850s the speed of technological change quickened. 在19世紀50年代末，技術變革的速度加快了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Speed</b> is very fast movement or travel. 快速","examples":["Speed is the essential ingredient of all athletics. 速度是所有體育運動的基本要素。","He put on a burst of speed. 他暴發出一陣猛衝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Speed</b> is a very fast rate at which something happens or is done. (發生、完成的) 高速","examples":["I was amazed at his speed of working. 我對他工作的高速感到驚訝。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"超速駕駛","examples":["He was fined for speeding last year. 他去年因超速駕駛被罰了款。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Speed</b> is an illegal drug such as amphetamine which some people take to increase their energy and excitement. 快速丸","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>speed</b> somewhere, you move or travel there quickly, usually in a vehicle. (通常指乘車) 迅速疾馳","examples":["Trains will speed through the tunnel at 186 mph. 火車將以每小時186英里的速度快速穿過隧道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>is speeding</b> is driving a vehicle faster than the legal speed limit. 超速駕駛","examples":["This man was not qualified to drive and was speeding. 這個男子沒有資格開車， 而且還在超速駕駛。"]}]}]},"squirrel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"松鼠；松鼠的毛皮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"貯藏（供以後使用）；不停（或不安）地探尋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>squirrel</b> is a small animal with a long furry tail. Squirrels live mainly in trees. 松鼠","examples":[]}]}]},"spirit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精神，心靈；情緒，心境；勇氣，意志，活力；（對團體、隊伍、社會的）忠心，（群體中的）態度，精神；心態，態度；本質，精髓，基本精神；真實意義，實質；靈魂，鬼魂；具有特別品質的人物，在群體或活動中發揮特殊作用的人物；烈酒；揮發性液體（尤指用蒸餾法提煉的燃料）；神靈；聖靈（Spirit，Holy Spirit 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"偷偷帶走，秘密弄走；鼓勵，鼓舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>spirit</b> is the part of you that is not physical and that consists of your character and feelings. 精神 (包括性格、情感等)","examples":["The human spirit is virtually indestructible. 人的精神實際上是不可摧毀的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>spirit</b> is the nonphysical part of them that is believed to remain alive after their death. 靈魂","examples":["His spirit has left him and all that remains is the shell of his body. 他的靈魂已經離開了他，所剩的是他的軀殼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>spirit</b> is a ghost or supernatural being. 幽靈","examples":["In the Middle Ages branches were hung outside country houses as a protection against evil spirits. 在中世紀樹枝被掛在村舍外面作為對邪惡幽靈的防範。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Spirit</b> is the courage and determination that helps people to survive in difficult times and to keep their way of life and their beliefs. 毅力","examples":["She was a very brave girl and everyone who knew her admired her spirit. 她是個很勇敢的女孩，每個認識她的人都欽佩她的毅力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Spirit</b> is the liveliness and energy that someone shows in what they do. 活力","examples":["They played with spirit. 他們充滿活力地進行了比賽。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>spirit</b> in which you do something is the attitude you have when you are doing it. 態度","examples":["Their problem can only be solved in a spirit of compromise. 他們的問題只能以折衷的態度解決。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>spirit</b> is the feeling of loyalty to a group that is shared by the people who belong to the group. 忠誠","examples":["There is a great sense of team spirit in the squad. 這個班有很高的團隊忠誠度。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>spirit</b> is the set of ideas, beliefs, and aims that are held by a group of people. 群體的觀念、信仰和目的","examples":["...the real spirit of the anti-war movement. …反戰運動的真正精神。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>The spirit of</b> something such as a law or an agreement is the way that it was intended to be interpreted or applied. 宗旨","examples":["The requirement for work permits violates the spirit of the 1950 treaty. 對工作許可證的要求違反了1950年條約的宗旨。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You can refer to a person as a particular kind of <b>spirit</b> if they show a certain characteristic or if they show a lot of enthusiasm in what they are doing. (具有某種特質或熱情的) 人","examples":["I like to think of myself as a free spirit. 我喜歡把自己看成一個無拘無束的人。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Your <b>spirits</b> are your feelings at a particular time, especially feelings of happiness or unhappiness. 情緒","examples":["At supper, everyone was in high spirits. 晚飯時每個人都情緒高昂。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"<b>Spirits</b> are strong alcoholic drinks such as whisky and gin. 烈酒","examples":["The only problem here is that they don't serve beer - only wine and spirits. 這兒惟一的問題是他們不供應啤酒——只供應葡萄酒和烈酒。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to carry off mysteriously or secretly (神秘地或秘密地)竊走","examples":[]}]}]},"spot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地點，場所；點，斑點；汙點，汙漬；丘疹，皰疹；某演員的固定節目；排名位置； <英>少量，一點；幾滴，少許（液體）；困境，窘境；現貨交易，現金交易；聚光燈（spotlight 的簡稱）；<美>（多米諾牌、紙牌或骰子上的）點；調灰泥板，調石膏板；<美，非正式>（特定面值的）鈔票；（英足）點球點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看見，注意到；讓分，讓步；飄了幾滴雨；<美，非正式>借（錢）給；使有斑點，使有汙跡；稀疏地點綴；在場監護（運動員）；（軍）確定敵人的位置；將（球）放在適當位置"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"現貨交易的，立即支付的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spots</b> are small, round, coloured areas on a surface. 斑點","examples":["The leaves have yellow areas on the top and underneath are powdery orange spots. 葉子上端有黃色斑塊，下方有粉狀橙色斑點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spots</b> on a person's skin are small lumps or marks. (皮膚上的) 小疙瘩; 斑","examples":["My brother's face was covered with spots. 我弟弟曾滿臉疙瘩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a particular place as a <b>spot</b>. 地點","examples":["They stayed at several of the island's top tourist spots. 他們在島上幾個最好的旅遊景點呆過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>spot</b> in a television or radio show is a part of it that is regularly reserved for a particular performer or type of entertainment.  固定節目檔","examples":["Unsuccessful at screen writing, he got a spot on a CNN show. 電影劇本創作方面未能成功，之後他在CNN得到了一個固定節目檔。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>spot of</b> a liquid is a small amount of it.  滴; 點","examples":["Spots of rain had begun to fall. 雨點已經開始落下來了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spot</b> something or someone, you notice them. 發現","examples":["Vicenzo failed to spot the error. 維森佐沒能發現這個錯誤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on the spot</b>, you do it immediately. 當即; 當場","examples":["James was called to see the producer and got the job on the spot. 詹姆斯被叫去見那個製片人，當即得到了那份工作。"]}]}]},"steak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肉排，（尤指）牛排；魚排，魚塊；（常指切成塊出售、供燉燜用的）牛肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>steak</b> is a large flat piece of beef without much fat on it. You cook it by grilling or frying it. 牛排","examples":["...a steak sizzling on the grill. …一塊兒在烤架上滋滋作響的牛排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A fish <b>steak</b> is a large piece of fish that contains few bones. (魚) 排","examples":["...fresh salmon steaks. …新鮮的三文魚排。"]}]}]},"spring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"春天，春季；泉，泉水；源泉，根源；彈簧，發條；彈性，彈力；跳，躍；活力，朝氣；<罕>一群水鴨；朔望潮，大潮（spring tide 的簡稱）；（船甲板）翹曲，彎曲；（厚木板、圓材的）裂開，裂縫；（航海）倒纜，斜系船纜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"春天的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳，躍；突然彈開，突然移動；突然出現，湧現；突然啟動，突然運轉；突然向某人提供（或提出）；<非正式>幫助……逃跑（或越獄），營救；發源於，來自；<美，非正式>付賬（尤指請客）；<古>花錢；<澳，非正式>突然發現，撞見（不正當活動或違法者）；驚起（獵鳥），使（獵鳥）從躲藏處飛出；使爆炸；（尤指木料）翹曲，裂開；（船的桅杆或其他部分）翹曲，裂開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spring</b> is the season between winter and summer when the weather becomes warmer and plants start to grow again. 春季","examples":["They are planning to move house next spring. 他們在計劃明年春天搬家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spring</b> is a spiral of wire which returns to its original shape after it is pressed or pulled. 彈簧","examples":["Unfortunately, as a standard mattress wears, the springs soften and so do not support your spine. 不幸的是，當一張標準床墊用舊後，其彈簧變軟，因而不能支撐你的背脊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>spring</b> is a place where water comes up through the ground. It is also the water that comes from that place. 泉; 泉水","examples":["To the north are the hot springs. 北面是溫泉。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or animal <b>springs</b>, they jump upward or forward suddenly or quickly. (人、動物) 跳","examples":["He sprang to his feet, grabbing his keys off the coffee table. 他跳了起來，從咖啡桌上抓起他的鑰匙。","The lion roared once and sprang. 獅子吼了一聲，跳了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>springs</b> in a particular direction, it moves suddenly and quickly. 彈 (向某方向)","examples":["Sadly when the lid of the boot sprang open, it was empty. 可惜，當後備箱蓋彈開時，裡面是空的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>springs from</b> another thing, it is the result of it. 起源","examples":["Ethiopia's art springs from its early Christian as well as its Muslim heritage. 衣索比亞的藝術起源於其早期的基督教和穆斯林教遺產。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spring</b> some news or a surprise <b>on</b> someone, you tell them something that they did not expect to hear, without warning them. 出其不意地告知; 冷不防給","examples":["McLaren sprang a new idea on him. 麥克拉倫突然告訴他一個新想法。"]}]}]},"spread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"展開，開啟；張開，伸開（手臂、手指、腿）；擴散，蔓延；傳播，傳染；散佈，（使）流傳；（人，動物，植物）分佈，分散開來；撒，散播；傳遞；（臉上）露出，漸漸表現出；塗，敷；分攤，分配；延伸，伸展，擴張；分散（於某一時段內），分期還清（債務）；分散（風險）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴散，蔓延；範圍，幅度，種類；延展度，寬度，覆蓋面；塗抹食品的醬類；盛宴，酒席；（尤指橫貫兩版的）文章，廣告；<美>床罩；<美>大農場，大牧場；翼展；一大片；（兩種價格或比率的）差額，差幅；（兩支對抗的運動隊之間比分的）差距；（物理，生理）點源能量傳播"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"伸展的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> something somewhere, you open it out or arrange it over a place or surface, so that all of it can be seen or used easily. 鋪開","examples":["She spread a towel on the sand and lay on it. 她把一塊浴巾鋪在沙地上，然後躺在上面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> your arms, hands, fingers, or legs, you stretch them out until they are far apart. 伸展開 (手臂、手、手指、腿等)","examples":["Sitting on the floor, spread your legs as far as they will go without overstretching. 坐在地板上，儘可能分開雙腿，但不要過度拉伸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> a substance on a surface or <b>spread</b> the surface <b>with</b> the substance, you put a thin layer of the substance over the surface. 攤; 抹; 敷","examples":["Spread the mixture in the cake pan and bake for 30 minutes. 將該混合物攤在蛋糕烤盤裡，烤30分鐘。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>spreads</b> or <b>is spread</b> by people, it gradually reaches or affects a larger and larger area or more and more people. 使擴散; 擴散; 傳播","examples":["The industrial revolution, which started a couple of hundred years ago in Europe, is now spreading across the world. 幾百年前始於歐洲的工業革命現在正向全世界擴散。","...the sense of fear spreading in residential neighbourhoods. …在住宅區蔓延的恐懼感。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something such as a liquid, gas, or smoke <b>spreads</b> or <b>is spread</b>, it moves outward in all directions so that it covers a larger area. 使蔓延; 蔓延","examples":["Fire spread rapidly after a chemical truck exploded. 一輛裝有化學品的卡車爆炸後火勢迅速蔓延開來。","A dark red stain was spreading across his shirt. 一個暗紅色的汙漬正在他的襯衫上滲開。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> something <b>over</b> a period of time, it takes place regularly or continuously over that period, rather than happening at one time. 分散 (於某一時段內)","examples":["There seems to be little difference whether you eat all your calorie allowance at once, or spread it over the day. 無論你是一次性吃完全天的卡路里限量還是分散在一天裡吃，似乎沒多大區別。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> something such as wealth or work, you distribute it evenly or equally. 均分","examples":["...policies that spread the state's wealth more evenly. …更加平均地分配國家財富的政策。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spread out</b> means the same as . 鋪開 (同)(spread)","examples":["He extracted several glossy prints and spread them out on a low coffee table. 他抽出幾張光面照片鋪在一張矮咖啡桌上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spread out</b> means the same as . 伸展開","examples":["David made a gesture, spreading out his hands as if he were showing that he had no explanation to make. 大衛做了個手勢，雙手一攤，似乎表示他沒有什麼可解釋的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spread</b> is also a noun. 擴散; 傳播","examples":["The greatest hope for reform is the gradual spread of information. 改革的最大希望就是資訊的逐漸傳播。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spread</b> is also a noun. 蔓延","examples":["The situation was complicated by the spread of a serious forest fire. 形勢因一場嚴重的森林火災的蔓延而複雜化了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Spread</b> is also a noun. 均分","examples":["There are easier ways to encourage the even spread of wealth. 有更簡單的方法來促進財富的平均分配。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>spread</b> <b>of</b> ideas, interests, or other things is a wide variety of them. 多樣","examples":["A topic-based approach can be hard to assess in schools with a typical spread of ability. 在以典型的能力多元化為特徵的學校裡很難評估一種基於話題的教學方法。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>spread</b> is two pages of a book, magazine, or newspaper that are opposite each other when you open it at a particular place. (書籍、雜誌、報紙等的) 相對的兩頁","examples":["There was a double-page spread of a dinner for 46 people. 有一篇關於46人共進晚餐的橫貫兩版的文章。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Spread</b> is used to refer to the difference between the price that a seller wants someone to pay for a particular stock or share and the price that the buyer is willing to pay. (股票買賣的) 價差","examples":["Market makers earn their livings from the spread between buying and selling prices. 炒股者賺取股票買賣的價格差。"]}]}]},"standard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（品質的）標準，水平，規範；正常的水平，應達到的標準；行為標準，道德水準（standards）；<英，史>（小學）（考試達到的）級別；法定度量衡標準；旗杆；流行曲調（或歌曲）；莖幹挺直的樹（或灌木）；（植）（蝶形花的）旗瓣；（植）（鳶尾屬植物的）直立花瓣；直立水管（或煤氣管）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普通的，標準的；（大小、尺寸、式樣等）常規的，一般性的；權威的，廣泛認可的；（語言）合乎規範的，符合標準的；莖幹挺直的樹（或灌木）；（整成樹形並嫁接於挺直莖幹上的）灌木"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>standard</b> is a level of quality or achievement, especially a level that is thought to be acceptable. (尤指可被接受的) 水平","examples":["The standard of professional cricket has never been lower. 職業板球的水平從來沒這麼低過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>standard</b> is something that you use in order to judge the quality of something else. 標準","examples":["...systems that were by later standards absurdly primitive. …按照後來的標準衡量顯得極其原始的系統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Standards</b> are moral principles which affect people's attitudes and behaviour. 道德水準","examples":["My father has always had high moral standards. 我父親一直有著很高的道德水準。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>standard</b> to describe things which are usual and normal. 常規的","examples":["It was standard practice for untrained clerks to advise in serious cases such as murder. 讓未經訓練的職員們在諸如謀殺等重案中提出建議是常規的做法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>standard</b> work or text on a particular subject is one that is widely read and often recommended. 權威的; 廣泛認可的","examples":["At twenty he translated Euler's standard work on algebra into English. 20歲時，他把尤勒的權威代數著作譯成了英語。"]}]}]},"stage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"階段，時期；旅程（或賽跑中）的一段；舞臺；戲劇，戲劇表演；（尤指政治）舞臺，活動領域；（火箭的）級；層，樓層，塔層；演員職業；<非正式>馬車；（顯微鏡的）鏡臺；（電子）（電路的）級；（地質）（年代地質學用語）與某時代對應的一段地層，層"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"上演，演出；主辦，舉行；使發生；成功做成（某事）；（醫）把（疾病，病人）診斷（或歸類）為疾病的特定期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stage</b> <b>of</b> an activity, process, or period is one part of it. (活動、過程、時期的) 階段","examples":["The way children talk about or express their feelings depends on their age and stage of development. 孩子們談論或表達情感的方式取決於他們的年齡和成長階段。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a theatre, the <b>stage</b> is an area where actors or other entertainers perform. 舞臺","examples":["The road crew needed more than 24 hours to move and rebuild the stage after a concert. 勤務組在每一場音樂會結束後需要 24個小時以上的時間搬運和重搭舞臺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a particular area of activity as a particular <b>stage</b>, especially when you are talking about politics. (尤指政治上的) 活動領域; 舞臺","examples":["He was finally forced off the political stage last year by the deterioration of his physical condition. 他最終因身體狀況惡化於去年被迫離開了政治舞臺。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>stages</b> a play or other show, they organize and present a performance of it. 將 (戲劇等) 搬上舞臺; 上演","examples":["Maya Angelou first staged the play \"And I Still Rise\" in the late 1970s. 瑪雅•安吉羅在20世紀70年代末首次將戲劇《我仍將奮起》搬上舞臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stage</b> an event or ceremony, you organize it and usually take part in it. 主辦; 舉行","examples":["Russian workers have staged a number of strikes in protest at the republic's declaration of independence. 俄羅斯工人已經舉行了多次罷工，抗議該共和國宣佈獨立。"]}]}]},"stamp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵票；印記，戳記；印，章，戳；跺腳（聲），跺蹄（聲）；特徵，痕跡，烙印；型別，種類，類別；表明，表示；重要影響，持久影響；（搗礦機中用於搗碎礦石的）鐵砧；購物券，購買券"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"跺（腳），重踩，重踏；邁著重步走，跺著腳走；在……上面印蓋（圖案、記號、字母等）；顯示出（感情）；表明（某人）是……；（用印模）衝壓；對…有重要（永久性）的影響；在……上貼郵票；搗碎（礦石），壓碎（礦石）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stamp</b> or a <b>postage stamp</b> is a small piece of paper which you lick and stick on an envelope or package before you mail it to pay for the cost of the postage. 郵票","examples":["...a book of stamps. …一本郵票冊。","As of February 3rd, the price of a first class stamp will go up to 29 cents. 自2月3日起，每張一等郵票的價格將上漲到29分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stamp</b> is a small block of wood or metal which has a pattern or a group of letters on one side. You press it onto an pad of ink and then onto a piece of paper in order to produce a mark on the paper. The mark that you produce is also called a <b>stamp</b>. 印章; 印記","examples":["...a date stamp and an ink pad. …一個日期印章和一個印泥。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Stamp</b> is also a noun. 跺腳","examples":["...hearing the creak of a door and the stamp of cold feet. …聽到門的吱嘎聲和因腳冷而跺腳的聲音。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something bears <b>the</b> <b>stamp</b> <b>of</b> a particular quality or person, it clearly has that quality or was done by that person. 印記","examples":["Most of us want to make our home a familiar place and put the stamp of our personality on its walls. 我們大多數人都想把我們的家佈置成溫馨的地方並在牆壁上留下我們個性的印記。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stamp</b> a mark or word on an object, you press the mark or word onto the object using a stamp or other device. 蓋 (章); 印 (某標記); 打上 (某字)","examples":["Car manufacturers stamp a vehicle identification number at several places on new cars to help track down stolen vehicles. 汽車生產商們在新車車身的幾個地方打上車輛識別碼以幫助追查被盜車輛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stamp</b> or <b>stamp</b> your <b>foot</b>, you lift your foot and put it down very hard on the ground, for example because you are angry or because your feet are cold. 跺 (腳); 跺腳; 重重地踩","examples":["Often he teased me till my temper went and I stamped and screamed, feeling furiously helpless. 他過去經常取笑我直到我生氣，又跺腳又尖叫，感覺非常無助。","His foot stamped down on the accelerator. 他一腳猛地踩下油門。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stamp</b> somewhere, you walk there putting your feet down very hard on the ground because you are angry. (因生氣而) 頓足","examples":["\"I'm going before things get any worse!\" he shouted as he stamped out of the bedroom. “我要在情況變得更糟前離開！”他叫嚷著頓足走出了臥室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stamp on</b> something, you put your foot down on it very hard. (在…上) 用力踩","examples":["He received the original ban last week after stamping on the referee's foot during the final. 在決賽中狠狠地踩了裁判的腳之後，他上週受到首次禁賽處罰。"]}]}]},"steam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蒸汽，水蒸氣；水汽，霧氣；蒸汽動力（壓力）；力量，勢頭；蒸汽機車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"散發蒸汽，冒熱氣；蒸（食物）；（以蒸汽為動力）行駛；快速行走，疾行；（使）蒙上水汽；蒸汽洗滌，蒸汽處理；用蒸汽軟化（尤指膠水）；<英，非正式>開始戰鬥，投入戰鬥；<非正式>（一群賊）（在匆忙透過公共場所時）順路盜竊（或搶劫）；用蒸汽開動（機車）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"蒸汽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Steam</b> is the hot mist that forms when water boils. <b>Steam</b> vehicles and machines are operated using steam as a means of power. 蒸汽","examples":["In an electric power plant the heat converts water into high-pressure steam. 在發電廠裡，熱把水轉換成高壓水蒸汽。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>steams</b>, it gives off steam. 冒蒸汽","examples":["...restaurants where coffee pots steamed on their burners. …飯店裡咖啡壺在爐子上冒著熱氣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>steam</b> food or if it <b>steams</b>, you cook it in steam rather than in water. 蒸","examples":["Steam the carrots until they are just beginning to be tender. 把胡蘿蔔蒸到剛好變軟。","Leave the vegetables to steam over the rice for the 20 minutes cooking time. 把蔬菜放在米飯上蒸20分鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a plan or a project goes <b>full steam ahead</b>, it progresses quickly. 全速推進","examples":["The administration was determined to go full steam ahead with its reform programme. 當局決心全速推進其改革方案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>run out of steam</b>, you stop doing something because you have no more energy or enthusiasm left. 筋疲力盡","examples":["I decided to paint the bathroom ceiling but ran out of steam halfway through. 我決定要粉刷浴室天花板，但幹了一半就筋疲力盡了。"]}]}]},"square":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正方形的，四方形的；成直角的；平方的；兩清的，互不欠賬的；誠實公正的；<非正式>古板守舊的；平行的，水平的；寬闊結實的；打平的，平局的；一致的，可共存的；長寬為…...的；整齊的；（韻律）簡單易懂的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"正方形，四方形；廣場；平方，二次冪；<非正式>古板守舊的人；（棋盤上的）方格；直角尺，丁字尺；<史>（步兵的）方陣；方圍巾；<英>託灰板，灰漿板；（板球）內場；（軍營中的）操練場；<美>街區；（占星）90度星位；<美，非正式>美餐，飽餐"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成平方，使成二次冪；使（比賽的比分）打平；挺起胸膛；使成正方形，使成方形；<非正式>賄賂，收買；使諧調，符合；就…...徵得…...的同意；結賬，付清欠款；橫（向）傳（球）；（占星）處於方照位置"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"直接地；成直角，垂直地；<非正式>公正地，誠實地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>square</b> is a shape with four sides that are all the same length and four corners that are all right angles. 正方形","examples":["Serve the cake warm or at room temperature, cut in squares. 端上溫的或房間溫度的蛋糕，把它切成正方形。","There was a calendar on the wall, with large squares around the dates. 牆上有一副日曆，日期周圍是大的方框。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a town or city, a <b>square</b> is a flat open place, often in the shape of a square. 廣場","examples":["The house is located in one of the city's prettiest squares. 該房子位於市區最漂亮的廣場之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>square</b> <b>of</b> a number is the number produced when you multiply that number by itself. For example, the square of 3 is 9. 二次方; 平方","examples":["...the square of the speed of light, an exceedingly large number. …光速的平方，一個極大的數字。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>square</b> has a shape the same as a square or similar to a square. 正方形的; 方形的","examples":["Round tables seat more people in the same space as a square table. 在同一空間裡，圓桌比方桌可以坐更多的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Square</b> is used before units of length when referring to the area of something. For example, if something is three feet long and two feet wide, its area is six square feet. 平方的 (用於長度單位前表示面積)","examples":["The new complex will provide 10 million square feet of office space. 這座新的綜合建築群將提供1千萬平方英尺的辦公空間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Square</b> is used after units of length when you are giving the length of each side of something that is square in shape. 平方的 (用於長度單位前表示某面面積)","examples":["...a linen cushion cover, 45 cm. square. …一個亞麻坐墊套子，45平方釐米。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>square</b> a number means to multiply it by itself. For example, <b>3 squared</b> is 3 x 3, or 9. <b>3 squared</b> is usually written as 3<b>2</b>. 乘二次方","examples":["Take the time in seconds, square it, and multiply by 5.12. 以秒計時，乘二次方，然後乘以5.12。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>square</b> two different ideas or actions <b>with</b> each other or if they <b>square with</b> each other, they fit or match each other. 使相適配; 適配","examples":["That explanation squares with the facts, doesn't it. 那種解釋與事實相符，是吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>square</b> something <b>with</b> someone, you ask their permission or check with them that what you are doing is acceptable to them. (就某事) 徵求 (某人) 許可","examples":["I squared it with Dan, who said it was all right so long as I was back next Monday morning. 我就此事徵求過丹的許可，他說只要我能在下週一上午回來就行。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>back to square one</b>, you have to start dealing with something from the beginning again because the way you were dealing with it has failed. (因處理失敗而) 重新開始","examples":["If your complaint is not upheld, you may feel you are back to square one. 如果你的投訴沒有得到支援，你可能覺得你又得從新開始。"]}]}]},"steel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋼，鋼鐵；鋼鐵工業；（用來磨刀的）鋼棒；鋼製器具；鋼做的部分；<文>兵器；（鋼鐵般的）堅強，堅定"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使堅強地做（或面對）；鋼化"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鋼製的；鋼鐵業的；堅強的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Steel</b> is a very strong metal which is made mainly from iron. Steel is used for making many things, for example bridges, buildings, vehicles, and cutlery. 鋼","examples":["...steel pipes. …鋼管。","...the iron and steel industry. …鋼鐵工業。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>steel</b> <b>yourself</b>, you prepare to deal with something unpleasant. 使準備應對 (不愉快之事)","examples":["Those involved are steeling themselves for the coming battle. 那些參與者正準備應對即將到來的戰鬥。"]}]}]},"stove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（取暖或烹飪用的）爐子，火爐；廚灶，爐頭；窯；<英>溫室"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（為了噴塗表層而）在爐中對（物體）進行熱處理；（用硫磺等煙霧）煙燻，消毒（房屋）；<英>在溫室中加速（植物）生長，培植（植物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擊穿；擋開，延緩（stave 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stove</b> is a piece of equipment which provides heat, either for cooking or for heating a room. 爐","examples":["She put the kettle on the gas stove. 她把水壺放在煤氣爐上。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to process (ceramics, metalwork, etc) by heating in a stove 在爐中燒製(陶瓷器、金屬製品等)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"stave的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]}]},"strawberry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"草莓；草莓色，紫紅色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strawberry</b> is a small red fruit which is soft and juicy and has tiny yellow seeds on its skin. 草莓","examples":["...strawberries and cream. …奶油草莓。"]}]}]},"stranger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陌生人；新來者，異鄉人；從未經歷某事的人 ；稀客（用於和好久不見的人打招呼）；用於表示希望很快再見到某人；非眾議院議員者，非眾議院官員者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stranger</b> is someone you have never met before. 陌生人","examples":["Telling a complete stranger about your life is difficult. 向一位完全陌生的人講述自己的生活是困難的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people are <b>strangers</b>, they do not know each other. 互不相識者","examples":["The women knew nothing of the dead girl. They were strangers. 這些婦女對那個死去的女孩一無所知。她們互不相識。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are a <b>stranger</b> <b>to</b> something, you have had no experience of it or do not understand it. 生手","examples":["He is no stranger to controversy. 他對爭議一點都不陌生。"]}]}]},"straw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（乾燥的）麥稈，稻草；（喝飲料用的）吸管；稻草色，淡黃色；一文不值的東西"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"稻草的；無價值的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Straw</b> consists of the dried, yellowish stalks from crops such as wheat or barley. 麥杆; 稻草","examples":["The barn was full of bales of straw. 這個穀倉堆滿了成捆的麥杆。","I stumbled through mud to a garden strewn with straw. 我跌跌撞撞地走過泥濘來到一個散滿稻草的院子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>straw</b> is a thin tube of paper or plastic, which you use to suck a drink into your mouth. 吸管","examples":["...a bottle of lemonade with a straw in it. …一瓶插著吸管的檸檬汽水。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"having little value or substance 無價值的; 無實質的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are clutching at straws</b> or <b>grasping at straws</b>, you are trying unusual or extreme ideas or methods because other ideas or methods have failed. 抓救命稻草","examples":["...a badly thought-out plan from an administration clutching at straws. …一個管理部門抓救命稻草而制定的一個考慮不周的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event is <b>the last straw</b> or <b>the straw that broke the camel's back</b>, it is the latest in a series of unpleasant or undesirable events, and makes you feel that you cannot tolerate a situation any longer. 使人一忍再忍的一系列事件的最後一件","examples":["For him the Church's decision to allow the ordination of women had been the last straw. 對他來說，教堂允許婦女被授予聖職的決定使他再也不能容忍下去了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>draw</b> <b>the short straw</b>, you are chosen from a number of people to perform a job or duty that you will not enjoy. 下下籤","examples":["...if a few of your guests have drawn the short straw and agreed to drive others home after your summer barbecue. …如果你的幾位客人抽到了下下籤，並同意在你的夏日燒烤聚會後開車送其他人回家。"]}]}]},"storm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴風雨，暴風雪，風暴；（感情或反應的）爆發，迸發；強低氣壓天氣，旋風；暴雨般的飛彈（或打擊）；（軍隊的）強擊，猛攻；<美>（防雨雪寒風的）外重窗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛烈攻擊，突然襲擊；氣沖沖地走；非常生氣地說，怒罵；暴風雨來臨；迅速獲得成功；（遊戲或競賽中）強有力並且胸有成竹地行動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>storm</b> is very bad weather, with heavy rain, strong winds, and often thunder and lightning. 暴風雨","examples":["...the violent storms which whipped the East Coast. …席捲東海岸的猛烈暴風雨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something causes a <b>storm</b>, it causes an angry or excited reaction from a large number of people. 強烈的反響","examples":["The photos caused a storm when they were first published. 那些照片最初出版時引起強烈的反響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>storm</b> <b>of</b> applause or other noise is a sudden loud amount of it made by an audience or other group of people in reaction to something. 暴風雨般的聲音","examples":["His speech was greeted with a storm of applause. 他的演講博得暴風雨般的掌聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"猛攻","examples":["...the storming of the Bastille. …對巴士底獄的猛攻。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>storm</b> <b>into</b> or <b>out of</b> a place, you enter or leave it quickly and noisily, because you are angry. 氣沖沖地走","examples":["After a bit of an argument, he stormed out. 一次小小的爭吵之後，他就氣沖沖地走出去。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place that is being defended <b>is stormed</b>, a group of people attack it, usually in order to get inside it. 猛攻","examples":["Government buildings have been stormed and looted. 政府大樓已遭到猛攻和搶掠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>takes</b> a place <b>by storm</b>, they are extremely successful. 在某處大獲成功","examples":["Kenya's long distance runners have taken the athletics world by storm. 肯亞的長跑運動員在田徑界大獲成功。"]}]}]},"stream":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小河，小溪；一連串，源源不斷（的事情）；（煙、氣、液體的）流，股；（同齡學生按能力劃分的）班，組；音像流；資料流，指令流"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人，東西）流動，湧動；不斷地流出（液體），不斷地排出（氣體）；（光線）照射，照耀；（尤指在風中或水中）飄動，流動；線上收聽（或收看）；按能力分班（或分組）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stream</b> is a small narrow river. 溪流","examples":["There was a small stream at the end of the garden. 這個花園的盡頭有一條小溪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stream</b> of smoke, air, or liquid is a narrow moving mass of it. 一股 (煙、氣或液體)","examples":["He breathed out a stream of cigarette smoke. 他吐出一縷香菸的煙霧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stream</b> of vehicles or people is a long moving line of them. (車或人) 流","examples":["There was a stream of traffic behind him. 他身後有一股車流。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>stream</b> <b>of</b> things is a large number of them occurring one after another. 一連串","examples":["The discovery triggered a stream of readers' letters. 這個發現引來一連串的讀者來信。","...a never-ending stream of jokes. …接連不斷的笑話。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid <b>streams</b> somewhere, it flows or comes out in large amounts. 流","examples":["Tears streamed down their faces. 淚水順著他們的臉頰流下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your eyes <b>are streaming</b>, liquid is coming from them, for example because you have a cold. You can also say that your nose <b>is streaming</b>. 流眼淚; 流鼻涕","examples":["Her eyes were streaming now from the wind. 她的眼睛現在被風吹得直流淚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people or vehicles <b>stream</b> somewhere, they move there quickly and in large numbers. (人或車輛) 大批流動","examples":["Refugees have been streaming into Travnik for months. 難民幾個月來一直大量流入特拉弗尼克。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When light <b>streams</b> into or out of a place, it shines strongly into or out of it. 照射","examples":["Sunlight was streaming into the courtyard. 陽光正照進那院子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a new factory or a new system comes <b>on stream</b> or is brought <b>on stream</b>, it begins to operate or becomes available. 投入生產","examples":["As new mines come on stream, Chile's share of world copper output will increase sharply. 隨著新礦投產，智利在世界銅產量中所佔的份額將大幅度增長。"]}]}]},"subway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>地鐵；<英>地下通道"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘地鐵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>subway</b> is an underground railway. 地鐵","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>subway</b> is the same as an . 地下通道","examples":[]}]}]},"straight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"直的，筆直的；端正的，豎直的；（裙、褲等）直筒型的；坦誠的，直率的；簡單的，非此即彼的；正中目標的；整潔的；連續的；（訊息）正確的，可靠的；互不欠債的；不吸毒的，不酗酒的；（酒）純的；純正的，純粹的；正統的，嚴肅的；<非正式>正經的；異性戀的；（神態）從容的；（思維）清晰的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"直線地，徑直地；豎直地，直立地；立即，馬上；誠實地，坦率地；連續地；準確地，清晰地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"異性戀者；直線跑道；（撲克牌的）順子；<南非，非正式>750毫升瓶裝酒；<非正式>老實人；直立形態；直線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變直"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>straight</b> line or edge continues in the same direction and does not bend or curve. 筆直的","examples":["Keep the boat in a straight line. 讓小船直線行駛。","His teeth were perfectly straight. 他的牙齒非常整齊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> hair has no curls or waves in it. (發) 直","examples":["Grace had long straight dark hair which she wore in a bun. 格雷斯有一頭又長又直的黑髮，她把它盤成了一個髮髻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>straight</b> answer, you answer them clearly and honestly. (回答) 直截了當的","examples":["What a shifty arguer he is, refusing ever to give a straight answer to a straight question. 他真是一個狡猾的辯手，一直拒絕對一個直接的問題給予直截了當的回答。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> means following one after the other, with no gaps or intervals. 連續的","examples":["They'd won 12 straight games before they lost. 他們在輸掉之前已贏了連續12場比賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>straight</b> choice or a <b>straight</b> fight involves only two people or things. 有關兩者的","examples":["It's a straight choice between low-paid jobs and no jobs. 這是一個有關低收入工作和沒有工作兩者之間的選擇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>straight</b>, you mean that they are normal and conventional, for example in their opinions and in the way they live. 正統的","examples":["Dorothy was described as a very straight woman, a very strict Christian who was married to her job. 多蘿西被描述成一位非常正統的女人，一位非常誠篤全心撲在工作上的基督徒。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>straight</b>, you mean that they are heterosexual rather than homosexual. 異性戀的","examples":["His sexual orientation was a lot more gay than straight. 他的性取向更像是同性戀的而非異性戀的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> is also an adverb. 直地","examples":["Stand straight and stretch the left hand to the right foot. 站直，伸左手夠右腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>straight</b> to indicate that the way from one place to another is very direct, with no changes of direction. 徑直地","examples":["...squirting the medicine straight to the back of the child's throat. …把藥直接噴到小孩喉嚨後部。","He finished his conversation and stood up, looking straight at me. 他結束了談話站起來，直視著我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you go <b>straight</b> to a place, you go there immediately. 立即","examples":["As always, we went straight to the experts for advice. 像平時一樣，我們立即向那些專家們做了諮詢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> is also an adverb. 直截了當地","examples":["I lost my temper and told him straight that I hadn't been looking for any job. 我生氣了，直截了當地告訴他我一直沒找過任何工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> is also an adverb. 連續地","examples":["He called from Washington, having been there for 31 hours straight. 他從華盛頓打來了電話，他已在那裡連續呆了31個小時了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Straight</b> is also a noun. 異性戀者","examples":["...a standard of sexual conduct that applies equally to gays and straights. …一個同等適用於同性戀者和異性戀者的性行為標準。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> something <b>straight</b>, you make sure that you understand it properly or that someone else does. 把某事弄清楚","examples":["You need to get your facts straight. 你需要把你的事實弄清楚。"]}]}]},"stress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精神壓力，緊張；壓力，應力；強調，重要性；（單詞）重音，重讀，（音樂）加強音；壓強；環境惡劣引起的疾病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強調，著重；重讀；焦慮，緊張；使受壓力，使受重壓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stress</b> a point in a discussion, you put extra emphasis on it because you think it is important. 強調","examples":["The spokesman stressed that the measures did not amount to an overall ban. 發言人強調說，這些措施並不等於全面禁止。","China's leaders have stressed the need for increased co-operation between Third World countries. 中國領導人已經強調了增進第三世界國家之間合作的需要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stress</b> a word or part of a word when you say it, you put emphasis on it so that it sounds slightly louder. 重讀","examples":["She stresses the syllables as though teaching a child. 她重讀這些音節，像教小孩似的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stress</b> is also a noun. 重點","examples":["Japanese car makers are laying ever more stress on overseas sales. 日本的汽車製造商們把更多的重點放在海外銷售上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel under <b>stress</b>, you feel worried and tense because of difficulties in your life. 精神壓力","examples":["Katy could think clearly when not under stress. 凱泰在沒有精神壓力時能夠清晰地思考。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Stress</b> is also a noun. 重讀","examples":["...the misplaced stress on the first syllable of this last word. …這個最末單詞的第1個音節上的重讀錯誤。"]}]}]},"stick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"粘，貼；刺，戳，插；（隨便）擺放，放置；伸出，突出；卡住，釘住；<英，非正式>容忍，忍受；被接受，被眾人採用；（牌戲中）不再要牌；停頓下來，沒有進展；<非正式>（生氣地）放棄（和打發）；<非正式>使支付，導致損失"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"枯枝，枝條；條狀物，棍狀物；（用於某特定用途的）棍，條，籤；球棍，球棒；變速桿，操縱桿；批評，懲罰；<非正式>邊遠地區（the sticks）；<非正式>（傢俱的）件；非常瘦的人（或四肢）；畫著短細直線的；<非正式>球門柱（the sticks）；（股票）大宗死股"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stick</b> is a thin branch which has fallen off a tree. 枝條","examples":["...people carrying bundles of dried sticks to sell for firewood. …揹著成捆枯枝當柴火賣的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stick</b> is a long thin piece of wood which is used for a particular purpose. 棍","examples":["...lollipop sticks. …棒棒糖棍。","...drum sticks. …鼓槌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Some long thin objects that are used in sports are called <b>sticks</b>. 球棒","examples":["...lacrosse sticks. …長曲棍球球球棒。","...hockey sticks. …曲棍球棒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>stick</b> <b>of</b> something is a long thin piece of it. 條狀物","examples":["...a stick of celery. …一根芹菜。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>stick</b> is a long thin piece of wood which is used for supporting someone's weight or for hitting people or animals. 柺杖; (襲擊用的) 棍子","examples":["He wore a grey suit and leaned heavily on his stick. 他身著灰色西服，吃力地倚著手杖。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>gets the wrong end of the stick</b> or <b>gets hold of the wrong end of the stick</b>, they do not understand something correctly and get the wrong idea about it. 誤解","examples":["I think someone has got the wrong end of the stick. They should have established the facts before speaking out. 我想有人誤解了。他們本應該在查證事實之後再發表意見。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stick</b> something somewhere, you put it there in a rather casual way. 隨意放置","examples":["He folded the papers and stuck them in his desk drawer. 他把檔案折起扔進書桌抽屜裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stick</b> a pointed object <b>in</b> something, or if it <b>sticks</b> <b>in</b> something, it goes into it or through it by making a cut or hole. 使扎入; 扎入","examples":["They sent in loads of male nurses and stuck a needle in my back. 他們派來很多男護士，在我的背部紮了根針。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stick</b> one thing to another, you attach it using glue, Scotch tape, or another sticky substance. 貼上","examples":["Don't forget to clip the token and stick it on your card. 別忘了剪下代金券，並貼在你的卡上。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is sticking out</b> from a surface or object, it extends up or away from it. If something <b>is sticking into</b> a surface or object, it is partly in it. 伸出","examples":["They lay where they had fallen from the crane, sticking out of the water. 他們位於從那臺起重機上摔下的地方，部分露在水面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>sticks</b> <b>to</b> another, it becomes attached to it and is difficult to remove. 粘住","examples":["The soil sticks to the blade and blocks the plough. 土粘在刃上，卡住了犁。","Peel away the waxed paper if it has stuck to the bottom of the cake. 如果蠟紙粘住蛋糕底部，就把它撕掉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>sticks in</b> your mind, you remember it for a long time. 經久留駐","examples":["The incident stuck in my mind because it was the first example I had seen of racism in that country. 那個事件令我難以忘懷，因為那是我看到的那個國家的第一例種族歧視事件。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something which can usually be moved <b>sticks</b>, it becomes fixed in one position. 卡住","examples":["The needle on the dial went right around to fifty feet, which was as far as it could go, and there it stuck. 刻度盤上的指標一下轉到了50英尺處，即其所能達到的最大刻度，然後卡在了那裡。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to support (a plant) with sticks; stake 用小棍支撐(植物)","examples":[]}]}]},"struggle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"奮鬥，努力；搏鬥，扭打，掙扎脫身；爭奪，爭搶；奮力前進，艱難行進"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"奮鬥，鬥爭；難事；搏鬥，扭打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>struggle</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try hard to do it, even though other people or things may be making it difficult for you to succeed. 努力; 鬥爭","examples":["They had to struggle against all kinds of adversity. 他們不得不同各種困境鬥爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>struggle</b> <b>to</b> move yourself or <b>to</b> move a heavy object, you try to do it, but it is difficult. 艱難地移動","examples":["I could see the young boy struggling to free himself. 我能看見這個小男孩正使勁掙脫他自己。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person or organization <b>is struggling</b>, they are likely to fail in what they are doing, even though they might be trying very hard. 在困境中掙扎; 竭力維持","examples":["The company is struggling to find buyers for its new product. 這個公司正竭力為它的新產品尋找買主。","One in five young adults was struggling with everyday mathematics. 每5個年輕人中就有1個做日常的數學計算很費勁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>struggle</b> is a long and difficult attempt to achieve something such as freedom or political rights. 努力; 鬥爭","examples":["Life became a struggle for survival. 生活變成了一場爭取生存的鬥爭。","...a young boy's struggle to support his poverty-stricken family. …一個年輕男孩為支撐自己貧窮的家庭所做的努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Struggle</b> is also a noun. 扭打","examples":["He died in a struggle with prison officers less than two months after coming to Britain. 他來英國不到兩個月就死於一次與獄警們的扭打。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An action or activity that is <b>a struggle</b> is very difficult to do. 很費勁的事","examples":["Losing weight was a terrible struggle. 減肥是件很費勁的事。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>struggle</b> when you are being held, you twist, kick, and move violently in order to get free. 掙扎","examples":["I struggled, but he was a tall man, well built. 我掙扎了，但他是一個高個子男人，很強壯。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>struggle</b> <b>with</b> each other, they fight. 扭打","examples":["She screamed at him to \"stop it\" as they struggled on the ground. 他們在地上扭打時，她衝他尖叫著“住手”。"]}]}]},"stretch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變大，拉長；（布料）可伸縮，有彈性；伸展肢體；伸出，伸長（胳膊或腿）；拉緊，拽緊；（時間上）延續；（空間上）延伸，綿延；使竭盡所能，使施展本領；耗盡，竭盡（財力或物力）；（使）延長使用，節儉地使用；（資金，資源）足夠，夠用；放寬，放鬆；誇大，誇張；涉及，囊括"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（土地或水域的）一片，一段；（時間）連續的一段，持續；（肢體）伸展，伸開；彈性，伸縮性；服刑期；（終點前的）直線跑道；言過其實的話；困難的任務，苛求的任務；<非正式>加長轎車；搶風航行的距離"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（織物）有彈性的，有彈力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>stretches</b> over an area or distance covers or exists in the whole of that area or distance. 延伸","examples":["The procession stretched for several miles. 遊行隊伍延伸了數英里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>stretches</b> <b>from</b> one time <b>to</b> another, it begins at the first time and ends at the second, which is longer than expected. 持續","examples":["...a working day that stretches from seven in the morning to eight at night. …從早上7點持續到晚上8點的一個工作日。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a group of things <b>stretch</b> <b>from</b> one type of thing <b>to</b> another, the group includes a wide range of things. 涉及","examples":["...a trading empire, with interests that stretched from chemicals to sugar. …一個興趣範圍從化學品到食糖的貿易帝國。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stretch</b> <b>of</b> road, water, or land is a length or area of it. 一段","examples":["It's a very dangerous stretch of road. 這是一段非常危險的路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Stretch</b> is also a noun. 伸展","examples":["At the end of a workout spend time cooling down with some slow stretches. 在健身的末尾花時間用一些緩慢的伸展來做緩和。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stretch</b> <b>of</b> time is a period of time. 一段 (時間)","examples":["...after an 18-month stretch in the army. …在部隊呆了18個月後。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>stretch</b>, you put your arms or legs out straight and tighten your muscles. 伸直","examples":["He yawned and stretched. 他打了個哈欠，伸了伸腰。","Try stretching your legs and pulling your toes upwards. 試著伸直雙腿並向上拉拉腳趾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something soft or elastic <b>stretches</b> or <b>is stretched</b>, it becomes longer or bigger as well as thinner, usually because it is pulled. 有彈性","examples":["The cables are designed not to stretch. 這些纜繩被設計成沒有彈性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stretch</b> an amount of something or if it <b>stretches</b>, you make it last longer than it usually would by being careful and not wasting any of it. 儉省","examples":["They're used to stretching their budgets. 他們習慣於精打細算。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>stretches</b> your money or resources, it uses them up so you have hardly enough for your needs. 耗盡 (錢或資源)","examples":["The drought there is stretching resources. 那裡的乾旱正在耗盡財力物力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that a job or task <b>stretches</b> you, you mean that you like it because it makes you work hard and use all your energy and skills so that you do not become bored or achieve less than you should. 使充分發揮","examples":["I'm trying to move on and stretch myself with something different. 我正試圖換個工作，使自己在不同的事情上得到充分發揮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is not true or possible <b>by any stretch of the imagination</b>, you are emphasizing that it is completely untrue or absolutely impossible. 無論如何想像","examples":["Her husband was not a womanizer by any stretch of the imagination. 她的丈夫無論如何想像也不會是個玩弄女性的人。"]}]}]},"subject":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主題，話題；學科，科目，課程；主語；（繪畫、攝影等的）主題，題材；實驗物件；（批評、學習、調查的）物件；國民；起因；（邏）主詞，主項，主概念；（樂）主旋律；（哲）主體，主觀；中心實體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使臣服，征服，壓服；使經受，使遭受"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"隸屬的，臣服的；可能受……影響的，易遭受……的；受……支配的，服從於……的；取決於，視……而定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>subject</b> of something such as a conversation, letter, or book is the thing that is being discussed or written about. 話題; 主題","examples":["It was I who first raised the subject of plastic surgery. 是我首先提起了整形手術這個話題。","...the president's own views on the subject. …該總統對此問題的個人觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is the <b>subject of</b> criticism, study, or an investigation is being criticized, studied, or investigated. (批評、研究或調查的) 物件","examples":["Over the past few years, some of the positions Mr. Meredith has adopted have made him the subject of criticism. 在過去的幾年裡，梅雷迪恩先生所採取的一些立場已使他成為了被批評的物件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>subject</b> is an area of knowledge or study, especially one that you study in school, or college. (尤指在學校學習的) 科目","examples":["Surprisingly, maths was voted their favourite subject. 令人吃驚的是，數學被評為他們喜愛的科目。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In an experiment or piece of research, the <b>subject</b> is the person or animal that is being tested or studied. 實驗物件; 研究物件","examples":["\"White noise\" was played into the subject's ears through headphones. “白色噪音”透過耳機被送進實驗物件的耳朵裡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An artist's <b>subjects</b> are the people, animals, or objects that he or she paints, models, or photographs. (繪畫、攝影等的) 題材","examples":["Sailboats and fish are popular subjects for local artists. 帆船和魚是當地藝術家們喜愛的題材。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In grammar, the <b>subject</b> of a clause is the noun group that refers to the person or thing that is doing the action expressed by the verb. For example, in \"My cat keeps catching birds,\" \"my cat\" is the subject. 主語","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The people who live in or belong to a particular country, usually one ruled by a monarch, are the <b>subjects</b> of that monarch or country. (常指君主制國家的) 臣民","examples":["...his subjects regarded him as a great and wise monarch. …他的臣民把他看成了一位偉大而英明的君主。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>subject to</b> something means to be affected by it or to be likely to be affected by it. (可能) 受…影響的","examples":["Prices may be subject to alteration. 價格可能會受變更影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>subject to</b> a particular set of rules or laws, they have to obey those rules or laws. 受…支配的","examples":["The tribunal is unique because Mr. Jones is not subject to the normal police discipline code. 這個審判很特別，因為瓊斯先生不受一般的警務紀律約束。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>subject</b> someone <b>to</b> something unpleasant, you make them experience it. 使遭受","examples":["...the man who had subjected her to four years of beatings and abuse. …那個使她遭受了4年毆打和辱罵的男人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone involved in a conversation <b>changes the subject</b>, they start talking about something else, often because the previous subject was embarrassing. 轉變話題","examples":["He tried to change the subject, but she wasn't to be put off. 他試圖轉變話題，但她不願被打斷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event will take place <b>subject to</b> a condition, it will take place only if that thing happens. 取決於","examples":["They denied a report that Egypt had agreed to a summit, subject to certain conditions. 他們否認了埃及已同意在特定條件下參加峰會的報道。"]}]}]},"supermarket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"超級市場，超市"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>supermarket</b> is a large shop which sells all kinds of food and some household goods. 超市","examples":["Most of us do our food shopping in the supermarket. 我們大多數人在這家超市採購食品。"]}]}]},"success":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成功，勝利；發財，成名；成功的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Success</b> is the achievement of something that you have been trying to do. 成效","examples":["It's important for the success of any diet that you vary your meals. 膳食多樣化對任何飲食的成效都是重要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Success</b> is the achievement of a high position in a particular field, for example in business or politics. (在商業、政治等領域的) 成功","examples":["We all believed that work was the key to success. 我們都曾經相信工作是成功的關鍵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>success</b> of something is the fact that it works in a satisfactory way or has the result that is intended. (某事物的) 成功","examples":["We were amazed by the play's success. 我們驚歎該劇的成功。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone or something that is a <b>success</b> achieves a high position, makes a lot of money, or is admired a great deal. 成功的人; 成功的事物","examples":["We hope it will be a commercial success. 我們希望它會是一次商業成功。"]}]}]},"string":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"線，細繩，帶子；一連串（類似事件）；一系列（類似的事物）；字串，資訊串；一串；弦；絃樂器，絃樂組；（網拍的）羊腸線，網線；小隊，候補隊員；特定條件（或限制）；（類似細繩的）細長物；（蔬菜、肉等食物的）纖維；（物理）一種假設的亞原子粒子；樓梯側基板（stringboard 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用線穿，串起；使排成一排，把……連在一起；懸掛，系，扎；給（樂器或球拍）串弦；去掉（豆莢）的筋；當特約記者；確定擊球順序；拖延……的時間；<美，非正式>欺騙"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"由絃樂器組成的，絃樂器的；線織的，線的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>String</b> is thin rope made of twisted threads, used for tying things together or tying up packages. 細繩","examples":["He held out a small bag tied with string. 他遞出一個用細繩繫著的小包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>string</b> <b>of</b> things is a number of them on a piece of string, thread, or wire. 串","examples":["She wore a string of pearls around her neck. 她戴了一串珍珠在她的脖子上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>string</b> <b>of</b> places or objects is a number of them that form a line. 排","examples":["The landscape is broken only by a string of villages. 這風景僅僅是被一排村莊所破壞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>string</b> <b>of</b> similar events is a series of them that happen one after the other. 一連串","examples":["The incident was the latest in a string of attacks. 該事件是一連串攻擊中最近的一起。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>strings</b> on a musical instrument such as a violin or guitar are the thin pieces of wire or nylon stretched across it that make sounds when the instrument is played. (樂器的) 弦","examples":["He went off to change a guitar string. 他離開了去換一根吉他弦。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>strings</b> are the section of an orchestra which consists of stringed instruments played with a bow. 絃樂器","examples":["The strings provided a melodic background to the passages played by the soloist. 這些絃樂器為那個獨奏演員演奏的幾個樂段提供了的背景樂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is offered to you with <b>no strings attached</b> or with <b>no strings</b>, it is offered without any special conditions. 不帶附加條件","examples":["Aid should be given to developing countries with no strings attached. 援助應該不帶附加條件地被提供給發展中國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pull strings</b>, you use your influence with other people in order to get something done, often unfairly. 動用關係","examples":["Tony is sure he can pull a few strings and get you in. 託尼確信他能動用一些關係把你弄進來。"]}]}]},"sudden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"突然的，意外的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"突然發生的事（用於 all of a sudden，表示突然、忽然）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<文，非正式>突然地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sudden</b> means happening quickly and unexpectedly. 突然的","examples":["He had been deeply affected by the sudden death of his father-in-law. 他深受其岳父突然辭世的影響。","It was all very sudden. 一切都非常突然。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"突然性","examples":["The enemy seemed stunned by the suddenness of the attack. 敵人似乎被這次襲擊的突如其來驚呆了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>all of a sudden</b>, it happens quickly and unexpectedly. 突然地","examples":["All of a sudden she didn't look sleepy any more. 突然她看上去不再睏倦了。"]}]}]},"suit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"套裝，西裝；（從事特定活動時穿的）成套服裝；訴訟；同花色的一組紙牌；<非正式>（企業或機構中的）高階管理人員；一套蓬帆；追求（常指求婚）；<文>（向當權者提出的）請願，請求"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（服裝、風格、顏色）使顯得漂亮，與……相配；對（某人）方便，滿足（某人）需要，合（某人）心意；適合，適宜；隨自己的意願，隨性子；<美>（尤指為特定的活動）穿衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A man's <b>suit</b> consists of a jacket, trousers, and sometimes a vest, all made from the same fabric. (男) 套裝","examples":["...a dark pin-striped business suit. …一套黑色細條紋男職業裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A woman's <b>suit</b> consists of a jacket and skirt, or sometimes trousers, made from the same fabric. (女) 套裝","examples":["I was wearing my tweed suit. 我那時穿著我的花呢套裝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular type of <b>suit</b> is a piece of clothing that you wear for a particular activity. (特定活動時穿的) 服裝","examples":["The six survivors only lived through their ordeal because of the special rubber suits they were wearing. 6位倖存者因穿著特殊橡膠服度過了大難。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In a court of law, a <b>suit</b> is a case in which someone tries to get a legal decision against a person or company, often so that the person or company will have to pay them money for having done something wrong to them. 訴訟案","examples":["Up to 2,000 former employees have filed personal injury suits against the company. 多達2千名前僱員已對該公司提起了個人傷害訴訟。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can also say that someone <b>files</b> or <b>brings</b> <b>suit</b> <b>against</b> another person. 訴訟","examples":["One insurance company has already filed suit against the city of Chicago. 一家保險公司已對芝加哥市提起訴訟。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>suits</b> you, it is convenient for you or is the best thing for you in the circumstances. (某事物) 適合 (某人)","examples":["They will only release information if it suits them. 他們只會釋出合他們意的訊息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>suits</b> you, you like it. (某事物) 合 (某人) 心意","examples":["I don't think a sedentary life would altogether suit me. 我認為久坐不動的生活方式完全不適合我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a piece of clothing or a particular style or colour <b>suits</b> you, it makes you look attractive. (衣服、款式、顏色等) 適合 (某人)","examples":["Green suits you. 綠色適合你。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>suit</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do something just because you want to do it, without bothering to consider other people. 按照自己的意願","examples":["People have tended to suit themselves, not paying much heed to the reformers. 人們已趨向於按自己的意願行事，不太在意改革者們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>follow suit</b>, they do the same thing that someone else has just done. 跟著做","examples":["Efforts to persuade the remainder to follow suit have continued. 說服其餘的人也跟著做的努力在繼續。"]}]}]},"sweater":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"針織套衫，毛線衫；大量出汗的人；發汗劑；厚運動衫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sweater</b> is a warm knitted piece of clothing which covers the upper part of your body and your arms. 毛線衫","examples":[]}]}]},"swan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天鵝；天鵝星座（Swan）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>無目的地漫遊，閒逛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>swan</b> is a large bird with a very long neck. Swans live on rivers and lakes and are usually white. 天鵝","examples":[]}]}]},"supply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"供給量，儲備；（商品、服務的）供應量；供應，補給；生活必需品，日用品（supplies）；供應（的）；臨時替代者（尤指代課教師）；<英>議會撥給政府作開支的款項（supplies）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"供應，提供，供給；補充，填充；滿足要求（或需要）；提供援助；替代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>supply</b> someone with something that they want or need, you give them a quantity of it. 供應","examples":["...an agreement not to produce or supply chemical weapons. …一份不生產或不供應化學武器的協議。","...a pipeline which will supply the major Greek cities with Russian natural gas. …一條將為希臘各主要城市供應俄羅斯天然氣的管道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>supplies</b> to refer to food, equipment, and other essential things that people need, especially when these are provided in large quantities. 補給品","examples":["What happens when food and petrol supplies run low? 食物和汽油這些補給品減少時會發生什麼情況呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>supply</b> <b>of</b> something is an amount of it which someone has or which is available for them to use. 供應","examples":["The brain requires a constant supply of oxygen. 大腦需要持續的供氧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Supply</b> is the quantity of goods and services that can be made available for people to buy. 供應量","examples":["Prices change according to supply and demand. 價格根據供應量和需求量而變化。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in short supply</b>, there is very little of it available and it is difficult to find or obtain. 供應不足","examples":["Food is in short supply all over the country. 食品在全國各地都供應不足。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"in a supple manner 柔軟地","examples":[]}]}]},"strike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擊，撞；（用手或武器等）打；罷工；突然想到，突然意識到；突擊，襲擊，進攻；（疾病、災難等）侵襲；讓（某人）覺得；引起（強烈感情）；達成，達到；行進；（時鐘）敲響；發現（黃金，礦物，石油）；鑄造，衝制；刪除；踢球，擊球；使處於特定狀態；擺出（姿態）；照在……上；彈奏，奏出；劃（火柴）, 擊出（火星）；拆除（帳篷、帆等）；生根，附著；（漁）急拉釣線把魚鉤住；來到"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"罷工，罷市，罷課；襲擊，攻擊；擊，踢；（石油等寶貴資源的）發現；（投出的）好球；（棒球中的）擊空；（十柱保齡球）一投全倒；不利因素；拒絕，抗拒；（地層、斷層等地質特徵的）走向"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is a <b>strike</b>, workers stop doing their work for a period of time, usually in order to try to get better pay or conditions for themselves. 罷工","examples":["Air traffic controllers have begun a three-day strike in a dispute over pay. 空中交通管制員在一場薪酬糾紛中開始了為時3天的罷工。","Staff at the hospital went on strike in protest at the incidents. 這個醫院的員工舉行罷工，抗議這些事件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A military <b>strike</b> is a military attack, especially an air attack. 襲擊","examples":["...a punitive air strike. …一次懲罰性空襲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the act or an instance of knocking down all the pins with the first bowl of a single frame 第一球全中","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the score thus made","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"罷工者","examples":["The strikers want higher wages, which state governments say they can't afford. 這些罷工者要求得到更高的工資，州政府說他們無力支付。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When workers <b>strike</b>, they go on strike. 罷工","examples":["...their recognition of the workers' right to strike. …他們對工人罷工權利的承認。","They shouldn't be striking for more money. 他們不該為更多的錢而罷工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>strike</b> means to attack someone or something quickly and violently. 攻擊","examples":["He was the only cabinet member out of the country when the terrorists struck. 他在恐怖分子襲擊時是惟一人在國外的內閣成員。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> someone or something, you deliberately hit them. 打; 擊","examples":["She took two quick steps forward and struck him across the mouth. 她向前快走兩步，打了他一記耳光。","It is impossible to say who struck the fatal blow. 不可能確定是誰給了那致命的一擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something that is falling or moving <b>strikes</b> something, it hits it. 碰撞; 擊中","examples":["His head struck the bottom when he dived into the 6 ft end of the pool. 當他跳入水池6英尺深的那端時，頭撞到池底。","One 16-inch shell struck the control tower. 一發16英寸的炮彈擊中了那座指揮塔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> one thing against another, or if one thing <b>strikes</b> against another, the first thing hits the second thing. 碰撞","examples":["Wilde fell and struck his head on the stone floor. 懷爾德跌倒了，頭撞在石頭地板上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as an illness or disaster <b>strikes</b>, it suddenly happens. (疾病或災難) 爆發","examples":["Fed officials continued to insist that the dollar would soon return to stability but disaster struck. 聯邦政府的官員們仍堅持說美元會很快恢復平穩，但災難卻爆發了。","A moderate earthquake struck the northeastern United States early on Saturday. 美國東北部週六早晨遭遇了一次中等強度的地震。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an idea or thought <b>strikes</b> you, it suddenly comes into your mind. 使突然想到","examples":["A thought struck her. Was she jealous of her mother, then? 她突然冒出一個念頭。那她是在嫉妒自己的母親嗎?"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>strikes</b> you <b>as</b> being a particular thing, it gives you the impression of being that thing. 給…印象","examples":["He struck me as a very serious but friendly person. 他在我眼裡是個非常嚴肅但友好的人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>are struck</b> by something, you think it is very impressive, noticeable, or interesting. 把…迷住","examples":["She was struck by his simple, spellbinding eloquence. 她被他簡潔、富有鼓動性的口才迷住了。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> a balance, you do something that is halfway between two extremes. 找到 (某種平衡)","examples":["At times like that you have to strike a balance between sleep and homework. 在那樣的時候，你得在睡眠和家庭作業之間找到一種平衡。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> a pose or attitude, you put yourself in a particular position, for example when someone is taking your photograph. 擺出 (姿態)","examples":["She struck a pose, one hand on her hip and the other waving an imaginary cigarette. 她擺出一個姿勢，一隻手叉腰，另一隻手揮動著一支假想的香菸。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If something <b>strikes</b> fear <b>into</b> people, it makes them very frightened or anxious. 引起 (恐懼)","examples":["If there is a single subject guaranteed to strike fear in the hearts of parents, it is drugs. 如果只有一個話題能保證在家長們的心中引起恐懼的話，那就是毒品。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"When a clock <b>strikes</b>, its bells make a sound to indicate what the time is. (鍾) 敲響","examples":["The clock struck nine. 鐘敲了9下。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> words <b>from</b> a document or an official record, you remove them. 刪除","examples":["Strike that from the minutes. 從會議記錄中把那個刪除。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"When you <b>strike</b> a match, you make it produce a flame by moving it quickly against something rough. 擦 (火柴)","examples":["Robina struck a match and held it to the crumpled newspaper in the grate. 羅比納擦了一根火柴，將它伸向壁爐中的那些皺報紙。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"If someone <b>strikes</b> oil or gold, they discover it in the ground as a result of mining or drilling. 發現 (石油或黃金)","examples":["Oil industry sources say that Marathon Oil Company has struck oil in Syria. 石油業訊息人士稱馬拉松石油公司在敘利亞發現了石油。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>strike</b> a deal or a bargain with someone, you come to an agreement with them. 達成 (交易或協議)","examples":["They struck a deal with their paper supplier, getting two years of newsprint on credit. 他們與其紙張供應商達成一個協議，可以賒購兩年的新聞紙。","The two struck a deal in which Rendell took half of what a manager would. 這兩個人達成一項協議，倫德爾拿一名經理將能得到的一半。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Strike out</b> means the same as . 刪除","examples":["The censor struck out the next two lines. 審查員刪除了下面那兩行。"]}]}]},"surface":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"表面；水面，地面；桌面，檯面；（物體的）一個面；外表，表象；表面積；運動場地，運動場地面鋪設材料"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"浮出水面；（資訊、情感或問題）顯露，暴露，公開；（失蹤或隱藏後）出現；<非正式>（尤指長睡後）起床；給（道路等）鋪上硬麵"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"表面上的，外表上的；表面的；（與空中運輸相對的）水陸運輸的；水面艦船的（與潛水艇相對）；表層的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>surface</b> of something is the flat top part of it or the outside of it. 表面","examples":["Ozone forms a protective layer between 12 and 30 miles above the Earth's surface. 臭氧在距地球表面12至30英里的地方形成一個保護層。","...tiny little waves on the surface of the water. …水面的細小波浪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A work <b>surface</b> is a flat area, for example the top of a table, desk, or kitchen counter, on which you can work. 檯面","examples":["It can simply be left on the work surface. 把它放在操作檯面上就行了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you refer to <b>the</b> <b>surface</b> of a situation, you are talking about what can be seen easily rather than what is hidden or not immediately obvious. 表面","examples":["Back home, things appear, on the surface, simpler. 回到家後，事情表面上看起來簡單一些。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something under water <b>surfaces</b>, they come up to the surface of the water. 浮出水面","examples":["He surfaced, gasping for air. 他浮出了水面，大口喘著氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something such as a piece of news, a feeling, or a problem <b>surfaces</b>, it becomes known or becomes obvious. 顯現","examples":["The paper says the evidence, when it surfaces, is certain to cause uproar. 該報紙說，該證據一旦出現肯定會引起騷動。"]}]}]},"table tennis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乒乓球：一種類似網球的室內球類運動，由兩人或四人分站球檯兩端，用球拍將輕質空心小球擊過檯面中央的矮網。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Table tennis</b> is a game played inside by two or four people. The players stand at each end of a table which has a low net across the middle and hit a small light ball over the net, using small paddles. 乒乓球","examples":[]}]}]},"swallow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吞下，嚥下；（由於緊張等）做吞嚥動作，咽口水；吞沒，淹沒；耗盡（金錢，資源）；完全相信，信以為真；抑制（感情、言語）；默默忍受（侮辱、批評等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吞，一口；燕子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>swallow</b> something, you cause it to go from your mouth down into your stomach. 吞嚥","examples":["You are asked to swallow a capsule containing vitamin B. 你被要求吞下一顆含維生素B的膠囊。","Polly took a bite of the apple, chewed, and swallowed. 波莉咬了一口那個蘋果，嚼了嚼吞了下去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>swallows</b> a story or a statement, they believe it completely. 完全相信","examples":["They cast doubt on his words when it suited their case, but swallowed them whole when it did not. 他的話與他們的情況吻合時他們就懷疑，但不吻合時他們卻完全相信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to engulf or destroy as if by ingestion 吞併; 侵吞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Swallow</b> is also a noun. 吞嚥","examples":["Jan lifted her glass and took a quick swallow. 簡舉起杯子，迅速嚥了一口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>swallow</b> is a kind of small bird with pointed wings and a forked tail. 燕子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>swallow</b>, you make a movement in your throat as if you are swallowing something, often because you are nervous or frightened. (常因緊張或害怕而) 做吞嚥動作","examples":["Nancy swallowed hard and shook her head. 南希艱難地嚥了一下口水，搖了搖她的頭。"]}]}]},"tangerine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橘子，柑橘；柑橘樹，橘樹；橘黃色，橘紅色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tangerine</b> is a small sweet orange. 蜜橘","examples":[]}]}]},"symbol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"象徵，標誌；符號；代表性的人（物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is a <b>symbol</b> <b>of</b> a society or an aspect of life seems to represent it because it is very typical of it. 象徵","examples":["To them, the monarchy is the special symbol of nationhood. 對他們而言，君主政體是國家的特殊象徵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>symbol</b> <b>of</b> something such as an idea is a shape or design that is used to represent it. 象徵物","examples":["Later in this same passage Yeats resumes his argument for the Rose as an Irish symbol. 後來在這同一篇文章裡，葉芝再次提到把玫瑰作為愛爾蘭象徵的觀點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>symbol</b> <b>for</b> an item in a calculation or scientific formula is a number, letter, or shape that represents that item. 符號","examples":["What's the chemical symbol for mercury? 水銀的化學符號是什麼？"]}]}]},"support":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"支援，擁護，鼓勵；幫助，援助；支撐，承受（人或建築物等的重量）；供養，贍養；資助，贊助；追隨（或支援）（某個運動隊）；證實，確認；（計算機，作業系統）支援（程式，語言，裝置的）執行 ；支援……的生存；忍受，容忍；（在流行音樂會上）當助演，擔任演出嘉賓；支付……費用，（尤指）用錢維持（不良嗜好，如毒品）；勝任"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"支援，擁護；幫助，援助；贊助，資助；支撐物，支柱；（身體部位的）支援器，託；支撐，支承；（音樂會、演出的）助演演員，助演樂隊；證實，證明；資訊供應，資訊支援；（戰爭中的）支援；撫養，供養；支持者，擁護者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>support</b> someone or their ideas or aims, you agree with them, and perhaps help them because you want them to succeed. 支援","examples":["The vice president insisted that he supported the hard-working people of New York. 副總統堅持認為他支援勤勞的紐約人民。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>support</b> someone, you provide them with money or the things that they need. 資助; 供養","examples":["I have children to support, money to be earned, and a home to be maintained. 我有一群孩子要供，要賺錢，還要養一所房子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a fact <b>supports</b> a statement or a theory, it helps to show that it is true or correct. 證實","examples":["The Freudian theory about daughters falling in love with their father has little evidence to support it. 弗洛伊德關於女兒戀父的理論沒有什麼證據來證實。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>supports</b> an object, it is underneath the object and holding it up. 支撐","examples":["...the thick wooden posts that supported the ceiling. …支撐天花板的那些粗木柱子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>support</b> <b>yourself</b>, you prevent yourself from falling by holding onto something or by leaning on something. 倚著","examples":["He supported himself by means of a nearby post. 他倚在旁邊的一根柱子上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>support</b> a sports team, you always want them to win and perhaps go regularly to their games. 支援 (運動隊等)","examples":["Tim, 17, supports the Knicks. 17歲的蒂姆支援尼克斯隊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Support</b> is also a noun. 支援","examples":["The president gave his full support to the reforms. 該總統對改革予以了全力的支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give <b>support</b> to someone during a difficult or unhappy time, you are kind to them and help them. (給處境困難或不幸者的) 幫助","examples":["It was hard to come to terms with her death after all the support she gave to me and the family. 她曾給我和這個家庭很大的幫助，她的去世讓人難以接受。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Financial <b>support</b> is money provided to enable an organization to continue. (給組織的) 資助","examples":["State agencies continue to cut budgets and support to a number of organizations. 國家機關繼續削減對一些組織的預算和資助。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Support</b> is also a noun. 證明","examples":["The two largest powers in any system must always be major rivals. History offers some support for this view. 任何體制下的兩個最高權力者必然永遠是主要競爭對手。歷史提供了這種觀點的一些佐證。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>support</b> is a bar or other object that supports something. 支撐物","examples":["Each slab was nailed to two straight wooden supports. 每塊板都釘在兩根垂直的木製支撐物上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Support</b> is also a noun. 倚靠","examples":["Alice, very pale, was leaning against him as if for support. 愛麗絲臉色非常蒼白，正靠在他身上，好像是在尋求倚靠。"]}]}]},"talent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天賦，才能；天才，人才；<英，俚>性感的人；（尤指古羅馬人和古希臘人使用的重量和貨幣單位）塔蘭特"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Talent</b> is the natural ability to do something well. 天賦","examples":["She is proud that both her children have a talent for music. 她為自己的兩個孩子都有音樂天賦感到自豪。","He's got lots of talent. 他有許多天賦。"]}]}]},"tank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（儲存液體或氣體的）箱，罐，缸；一箱，一罐（的量）；坦克；人工蓄水池；<美，非正式> （警察局或監獄的）牢房；（養魚、蛇等用的）玻璃容器，玻璃缸；水櫃機車（tank engine 的簡稱）；緊身背心（多為羊毛的外罩）（tank top 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"徹底失敗，破產；故意輸掉比賽；給車輛加油；<英，非正式> 喝醉；<主蘇格蘭，非正式> 使慘敗；把······貯放在櫃（或箱，缸，罐）內；<英，非正式>乘車快速行進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tank</b> is a large container for holding liquid or gas. (盛放液體或氣體的) 罐; 箱; 槽","examples":["...an empty fuel tank. …一個空的燃料罐。","Two water tanks provide a total capacity of 400 litres. 兩個水箱的總容量為400升。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tank</b> is a large military vehicle that is equipped with weapons and moves along on metal tracks that are fitted over the wheels. 坦克","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a stock price or a movie <b>tanks</b>, it performs very badly, for example because it loses a lot of money. 表現得很糟糕","examples":["Tech stocks have tanked. 科技股票已經表現得很糟糕了。","The movie, which cost $137 million, tanked, grossing only $32 million. 這部電影，花了1.37億美元，表現得很糟糕，票房總收入只有3200萬美元。","His career tanked after the show left the air. 這個節目不再播放後，他的事業就變得很糟糕。"]}]}]},"swing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）擺動，搖盪；（使）改變（意見、情緒等）；做弧線運動，轉彎；（揮動某物）朝……打去；<非正式>熱鬧，令人開心；（使）突然轉向，突然轉身；以強勁的節奏演奏；（邁著有節奏的步伐）行進；<非正式>（有時略微不正當地）獲得；盪鞦韆；縱身躍向；絞死；<非正式>男女亂交；移轉（船，飛機）至各方位點"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搖擺，擺動；揮舞，揮動；揮杆動作；改變，變化；鞦韆；搖擺樂；以強勁的節奏演奏；<美>巡遊，競選旅行；（板球）側飛球；（音樂劇）替補"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"搖擺樂的；（在投票選舉中）搖擺不定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>swings</b> or if you <b>swing</b> it, it moves repeatedly backward and forward or from side to side from a fixed point. 使搖擺; 搖擺","examples":["The sail of the little boat swung crazily from one side to the other. 這艘小船的船帆發瘋似地左右搖晃著。","She was swinging a bottle of wine by its neck. 她當時正在握著瓶頸搖晃酒瓶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>swings</b> in a particular direction or if you <b>swing</b> it in that direction, it moves in that direction with a smooth, curving movement. 轉動; 成弧線運動","examples":["The torchlight swung across the little beach and out over the water, searching. 手電筒的光旋轉掠過這片小海灘，而後越到水面上搜尋著。","The canoe found the current and swung around. 獨木舟遇上了急流，打著轉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>swings</b> in a particular direction, or if the driver <b>swings</b> it in a particular direction, they turn suddenly in that direction. 使急轉向; 轉向","examples":["Joanna swung back on to the main approach and headed for the airport. 喬安娜把車急轉回主幹道，向機場開去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Swing</b> is also a noun. 搖擺","examples":["...a woman in a tight red dress, walking with a slight swing to her hips. …一位穿著緊身紅色連衣裙、走路時輕扭臀部的女子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Swing</b> is also a noun. 轉動","examples":["When he's not on the tennis court, you'll find him practising his golf swing. 當他不在網球場時，你會發現他在練高爾夫揮杆動作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Swing</b> is also a noun. 擊打","examples":["I often want to take a swing at someone to relieve my feelings. 我老想打誰一頓來發洩我的情緒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>swing</b> is a seat hanging by two ropes or chains from a metal frame or from the branch of a tree. You can sit on the seat and move forward and backward through the air. 鞦韆","examples":["Go to the neighbourhood park. Run around, push the kids on the swings. 到附近的公園去吧。跑跑步，幫孩子們推一推鞦韆。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>swing</b> in people's opinions, attitudes, or feelings is a change in them, especially a sudden or big change. (突然的或大的) 改變","examples":["Educational practice is liable to sudden swings and changes. 教育實踐活動易出現突然的轉向和變化。","Dieters suffer from violent mood swings. 節食者們經受劇烈的情緒變化的折磨。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>swings</b> <b>around</b>, they turn around quickly, usually because they are surprised. (因驚訝而) 急轉身","examples":["She swung around to him, spilling her tea without noticing it. 她急轉過身來對著他，茶水灑了出來她都沒注意到。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>swing</b> <b>at</b> a person or thing, you try to hit them with your arm or with something that you are holding. 擊打","examples":["Blanche swung at her but she moved her head back and Blanche missed. 布蘭奇向她打去，但她把頭向後一閃，布蘭奇沒打中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people's opinions, attitudes, or feelings <b>swing</b>, they change, especially in a sudden or extreme way. 改變","examples":["In two years' time there is a presidential election, and the voters could swing again. 兩年後有一次總統競選，選民們有可能再次大轉向。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in full swing</b>, it is operating fully and is no longer in its early stages. 正在熱烈進行中","examples":["When we returned, the party was in full swing and the dance floor was crowded. 我們回來的時候，聚會正開得起勁，舞池裡擠滿了人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get into the swing of</b> something, you become very involved in it and enjoy what you are doing. 全力投入","examples":["Everyone understood how hard it was to get back into the swing of things after such a long absence. 每個人都明白離開這麼長一段時間後要重新全力投入有多難。"]}]}]},"sweep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打掃，清除；（迅猛地）帶走，捲走；（風浪等）席捲，橫掃；風行，迅速蔓延；（闊步或輕盈地）走；揮動，擺動；（情感）突然襲來；掃視，搜尋；（使）輕輕擦過；延伸，蜿蜒；<美，非正式> 大獲全勝；梳，攏（頭髮）；掃射；徹底刪除；（板球）半跪揮棒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"打掃，清掃；揮動；巡行，掃蕩；綿延彎曲的地帶； 廣度，範圍；車道的弧形部分；<美> 收視率調查時段；<美> （系列比賽中）全勝；<非正式> 賭金全贏制；煙囪清潔工；（用以操舵的）大槳；（板球）以半跪姿勢擊球；風車的翼板；水井的長杆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sweep</b> an area of floor or ground, you push dirt or rubbish off it using a brush with a long handle. 打掃","examples":["The owner of the shop was sweeping his floor when I walked in. 當我走進來時，那個店的店主正在掃地板。","She was in the kitchen sweeping crumbs into a dust pan. 她在廚房裡正把麵包屑掃到一個簸箕裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sweep</b> things off something, you push them off with a quick smooth movement of your arm. 拂去","examples":["I swept rainwater off the flat top of a gravestone. 我拂去一塊墓碑平頂上的雨水。","With a gesture of frustration, she swept the cards from the table. 她沮喪地把桌上的那張卡片拂開。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone with long hair <b>sweeps</b> their hair into a particular style, they put it into that style. 梳 (頭髮)","examples":["...stylish ways of sweeping your hair off your face. …把頭髮梳開不擋住臉的時髦髮式。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your arm or hand <b>sweeps</b> in a particular direction, or if you <b>sweep</b> it there, it moves quickly and smoothly in that direction. 揮動","examples":["His arm swept around the room. 他的手臂向房間來回揮動。","Daniels swept his arm over his friend's shoulder. 丹尼爾斯一把將手臂搭在他朋友的肩上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If wind, a stormy sea, or another strong force <b>sweeps</b> someone or something along, it moves them quickly along. (風、海浪等) 捲走","examples":["...landslides that buried homes and swept cars into the sea. …掩埋了住宅並把汽車捲入海里的山體滑坡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>are swept</b> somewhere, you are taken there very quickly. 快速地帶到","examples":["The visitors were swept past various monuments. 那些遊客們被快速地帶著遊覽了各種紀念碑。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If events, ideas, or beliefs <b>sweep</b> through a place or <b>sweep</b> a place, they spread quickly through it. 使迅速傳播; 迅速傳播","examples":["A flu epidemic is sweeping through Moscow. 一場流感正在莫斯科迅速傳播。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If a person or group <b>sweeps</b> an election or <b>sweeps</b> <b>to</b> victory, they win the election easily. 輕鬆贏得","examples":["...a man who's promised to make radical changes to benefit the poor has swept the election. …一個承諾過要進行徹底的變革以造福窮人的男子已輕鬆贏得該選舉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sweep</b> is also a noun. 揮動","examples":["With one sweep of her hand she threw back the sheets. 她手一揮把那些床單扔了回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone makes a <b>sweep</b> <b>of</b> a place, they search it, usually because they are looking for people who are hiding or for an illegal activity. 搜查","examples":["Two of the soldiers swiftly began making a sweep of the premises. 其中的兩名士兵立即開始對該場所進行搜查。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>sweeps</b> from one place to another, it moves there extremely quickly. 極快速地移動","examples":["An icy wind swept through the streets. 一陣寒風掃過那些街道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>sweeps</b> something bad or wrong <b>under the carpet</b>, or if they <b>sweep</b> it <b>under the rug</b>, they try to prevent people from hearing about it. 試圖掩蓋某事","examples":["For a long time this problem has been swept under the carpet. 很長一段時間這個問題一直被掩蓋著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> <b>a clean sweep</b> <b>of</b> something such as a series of games or tournaments, you win them all. 徹底的勝利","examples":["...the first club to make a clean sweep of all three trophies. …第1個贏得全部3個獎盃的俱樂部。"]}]}]},"teen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"十幾歲，青少年時期（指從13歲到19歲）；（青）少年，十幾歲的孩子；傷害；憤怒；悲哀"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"青少年的，十幾歲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are a <b>teen</b> in your <b>teens</b>, you are between thirteen and nineteen years old. Teen is informal for teenager. 十幾歲 (指13至19歲); 十幾歲的人","examples":["Most people who smoke began smoking in their teens. 大多數吸菸的人都是在十幾歲時開始吸的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Teen</b> is used to describe things such as movies, magazines, bands, or activities that are aimed at or are done by people who are in their teens. 有關青少年的","examples":["...a new teen centre. …一個新的青少年中心。"]}]}]},"teenager":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青少年，十幾歲的孩子（13到19歲之間的孩子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>teenager</b> is someone who is between thirteen and nineteen years old. 十幾歲 (指13至19歲) 的人","examples":["As a teenager he attended Tulse Hill Senior High School. 十幾歲時，他上了塔爾斯山高階中學。"]}]}]},"tape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磁帶，錄音帶；錄了音的盒式磁帶，錄了像的盒式磁帶；膠帶，膠布；（用來綁東西或作界限標記的）布條，線帶；（賽跑中的）終點線；捲尺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用磁帶）錄音，錄影；用膠帶貼上；用帶子繫緊；<美> 用（繃帶）包紮（受傷部位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tape</b> is a sticky strip of plastic used for sticking things together. 膠帶","examples":["...strong adhesive tape. …黏性很強的膠帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tape</b> is a narrow plastic strip covered with a magnetic substance. It is used to record sounds, pictures, and computer information. 磁帶","examples":["Tape is expensive and loses sound quality every time it is copied. 磁帶很貴，而且每被複制一次，音質就會有所降低。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tape</b> is a cassette or spool with magnetic tape wound around it. 盒式磁帶","examples":["...a new cassette tape. …一盤新的盒式磁帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>tape</b> is a ribbon that is stretched across the finishing line of a race. (賽跑的) 終點線","examples":["...the finishing tape. …終點線。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tape</b> music, sounds, or television pictures, you record them using a tape recorder or a video recorder. (用磁帶錄音機或錄影機) 錄製","examples":["She has just taped an interview. 她剛剛錄製了一次採訪。","He shouldn't be taping without the singer's permission. 他不應該未經歌手允許就錄音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tape</b> one thing to another, you attach it using adhesive tape. 用膠帶貼上","examples":["I taped the base of the feather onto the velvet. 我用膠帶把羽毛的根部粘到天鵝絨上。"]}]}]},"team":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（遊戲或體育運動的）隊，小組；工作隊，工作組；（套在一起拉車的）一組牲口（尤指馬）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"協作，合作；使（顏色、布料、衣服）相配；（套在一起拉車的）一組牲口（尤指馬）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>team</b> is a group of people who play a particular sport or game together against other similar groups of people. 運動隊","examples":["...football team. …一支足球隊。","...the swim team. …那支游泳隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to any group of people who work together as a <b>team</b>. 團隊; 組","examples":["Each specialist has a team of doctors under him or her. 每位專家手下都有一組醫生。"]}]}]},"task":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指困難的或必須定期做的）工作，任務；（尤指語言教學中旨在幫助達到某一學習目的的）活動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"派給……任務；對（手段，能力）要求極高，考驗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>task</b> is an activity or piece of work which you have to do, usually as part of a larger project. 任務","examples":["Walker had the unenviable task of breaking the bad news to Mark. 沃克得把這個壞訊息告訴馬克，這可不是什麼美差。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are tasked</b> <b>with</b> doing a particular activity or piece of work, someone in authority asks you to do it. 委派任務 (給…)","examples":["Jen was tasked with running a charity basketball tournament. 珍被委以舉辦一場慈善籃球賽的任務。"]}]}]},"target":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目標，指標；（攻擊的）目標；（批評、嘲笑等的）物件；靶子；目標受眾，受影響的人（或群體）；<史> 圓形小盾；（語音）目標"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……作為攻擊目標，把……作為批評的物件；面向，把……對準（某群體）；將（錢款或援助）用於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>target</b> is something at which someone is aiming a weapon or other object. 靶; (攻擊的) 目標","examples":["The village lies beside a main road, making it an easy target for bandits. 該村位於大路邊，容易成為匪徒攻擊的目標。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>target</b> is a result that you are trying to achieve. (試圖達成的) 目標","examples":["She's won back her place too late to achieve her target of 20 goals this season. 她贏回她的位置為時已晚,無法實現她本賽季打進20個球的目標。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Target</b> is also a noun. (攻擊、批評的) 物件","examples":["In the past they have been the target of racist abuse. 過去他們一直是種族虐待的物件。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Target</b> is also a noun. (針對的) 目標","examples":["Yuppies are a prime target group for marketing strategies. 雅皮士是市場營銷策略的主要目標群體。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>target</b> a particular person or thing means to decide to attack or criticize them. 把…作為攻擊目標; 把…作為批評物件","examples":["Republicans targeted her as vulnerable in her bid for reelection this year. 共和黨人認為她在今年的再次參選中是不堪一擊的攻擊目標。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>target</b> a particular group of people, you try to appeal to those people or affect them. 以 (某特定人群) 為目標; 針對","examples":["The campaign will target American insurance companies. 這場運動將以美國的保險公司為目標。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on target</b>, they are making good progress and are likely to achieve the result that is wanted. 有望達到目標","examples":["We were still right on target for our deadline. 我們那時仍然很有希望在最後期限之前完成目標。"]}]}]},"tennis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網球，網球運動；（Tennis）<英>坦尼斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tennis</b> is a game played by two or four players on a rectangular court. The players use an oval racket with strings across it to hit a ball over a net across the middle of the court. 網球運動","examples":[]}]}]},"telephone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電話通訊系統；電話；（電話機的）話筒，受話器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給……）打電話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>telephone</b> is the electrical system of communication that you use to talk directly to someone else in a different place. You use the telephone by dialling a number on a piece of equipment and speaking into it. 電話","examples":["It's easier to reach her by telephone than by mail or email. 打電話比寫信或發電子郵件更容易聯絡上她。","I hate to think what our telephone bill is going to be. 我不願去想我們的電話費將會是多少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>telephone</b> is the piece of equipment that you use when you talk to someone by telephone. 電話機","examples":["He got up and answered the telephone. 他站起來接了電話。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>telephone</b> someone, you dial their telephone number and speak to them by telephone. 打電話給 (某人); 打電話","examples":["I felt so badly I had to telephone Owen to say I was sorry. 我感到很糟糕，必須給歐文打電話道個歉。","They usually telephone first to see if she's home. 他們通常先打電話看她是否在家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the telephone</b>, you are speaking to someone by telephone. 在通話中","examples":["Linda remained on the telephone to the police for three hours. 琳達和警察通了3個小時的電話。"]}]}]},"television":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電視（電視廣播系統）；電視機（電視接收機）；電視節目；電視業"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>television</b> or <b>television set</b> is a piece of electrical equipment consisting of a box with a glass screen on it on which you can watch programmes with pictures and sounds. 電視機","examples":["She turned the television on and flicked around between news programmes. 她開啟電視機，不停地在新聞節目間切換。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Television</b> is the system of sending pictures and sounds by electrical signals over a distance so that people can receive them on a television in their home. 電視","examples":["Toy manufacturers began promoting some of their products on television. 玩具製造商們開始在電視上促銷他們的一些產品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Television</b> refers to all the programmes that you can watch. 電視節目","examples":["I don't have much time to watch very much television. 我沒有很多時間看很多電視節目。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Television</b> is the business or industry concerned with making programmes and broadcasting them on television. 電視行業","examples":["I'd like a job in television. 我想有份電視行業的工作。"]}]}]},"theater":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電影院，戲院，劇場；戲劇；手術室（常作 operating theater，英式 operating theatre）；戰區（常作 theater of operations，英式 theatre of operations）"}],"sections":[]},"textbook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教科書，課本"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"規範的，典型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>textbook</b> is a book containing facts about a particular subject that is used by people studying that subject. 教科書","examples":["She wrote a textbook on international law. 她寫了一本國際法的教科書。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>textbook</b> case or example, you are emphasizing that it provides a clear example of a type of situation or event. 典型的","examples":["The house is a textbook example of medieval domestic architecture. 這座房子是中世紀民居建築的典型範例。"]}]}]},"tear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"撕碎，撕裂；撕破，劃破；撕掉，扯掉；拉傷，撕裂（肌肉或韌帶）；狂奔，疾馳；（眼睛）流眼淚；深受……之苦的，飽經……摧殘的；（尤指選擇或做決定）使折磨，使無法抉擇"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"淚水；哭泣（tears）；裂口，破洞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tears</b> are the drops of salty liquid that come out of your eyes when you are crying. 眼淚","examples":["Her eyes filled with tears. 她眼裡噙滿了淚水。","I just broke down and wept with tears of joy. 我實在控制不住，流下了高興的眼淚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>tears</b> in expressions such as <b>in tears</b>, <b>burst into tears</b>, and <b>close to tears</b> to indicate that someone is crying or is almost crying. 哭泣","examples":["He was in floods of tears on the phone. 他在電話裡大哭。","She burst into tears and ran from the kitchen. 她突然哭了起來，跑出了廚房。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tear</b> in paper, cloth, or another material is a hole that has been made in it. 破洞","examples":["I peered through a tear in the van's curtains. 我透過貨車窗簾上的一個破洞偷偷窺視。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tear</b> paper, cloth, or another material, or if it <b>tears</b>, you pull it into two pieces or you pull it so that a hole appears in it. 撕破 (紙、布等); 撕開","examples":["I tore my coat on a nail. 我的外套在一個釘子上掛破了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tear</b> one of your muscles or ligaments, or if it <b>tears</b>, you injure it by accidentally moving it in the wrong way. 拉傷 (肌肉或韌帶); (肌肉或韌帶) 拉傷","examples":["He tore a muscle in his right thigh. 他拉傷了右大腿的一塊肌肉。","If the muscle is stretched again it could even tear. 這塊肌肉再受到拉伸的話，它甚至可能會拉傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>tear</b> something from somewhere means to remove it roughly and violently. (猛烈地) 撕掉","examples":["She tore the windscreen wipers from his car. 她猛地扯掉了他車上的雨刮器。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>is torn</b> <b>by</b> particular events, you mean that unpleasant events which cause suffering and division among people are happening there. 折磨","examples":["...a country that has been torn by civil war and foreign invasion since its independence. …一個自獨立以來飽受內戰外擾之苦的國家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tear up</b> means the same as . 撕破","examples":["She tore the letter up. 她把那封信撕了。","Don't you dare tear up her ticket. 你竟敢撕壞她的票。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>tears at</b> something, they pull it violently and try to break it into pieces. 撕扯","examples":["Female fans fought their way past bodyguards and tore at his clothes. 女性仰慕者拼命繞過保鏢，撕扯他的衣服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tear</b> somewhere, you run, drive, or move there very quickly. 奔; 衝","examples":["The door flew open and Miranda tore into the room. 門猛地開了，米蘭達衝進了房間。"]}]}]},"temple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廟宇，寺院；太陽穴，鬢角；猶太教堂；教堂，禮拜堂（尤指法國新教教堂）；<美>（寺廟舉行的）宗教儀式；耶路撒冷古神殿，猶太古聖殿（the Temple）；律師協會會所（the Temple）；被視為聖靈的殿堂的物體（尤指人的身體）；專供某種活動之用的場所；邊撐，伸幅器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>temple</b> is a building used for the worship of a god or gods, especially in the Buddhist, Jewish, Mormon, and Hindu religions, and in ancient Greek and Roman times. 神殿; 寺廟","examples":["...a small Hindu temple. …一座小的印度教寺廟。","We go to temple on Saturdays. 我們每個星期六去寺廟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>temples</b> are the flat parts on each side of the front part of your head, near your forehead. 太陽穴","examples":["Threads of silver ran through his beard and the hair at his temples. 縷縷銀絲已爬上了他的鬍鬚和兩鬢的頭髮。"]}]}]},"thief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賊，小偷，偷竊犯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>thief</b> is a person who steals something from another person. 小偷","examples":["The thieves snatched the camera. 那些小偷搶走了照相機。"]}]}]},"term":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詞語，術語；措辭（terms）；學期，開庭期；期限，任期；到期，期滿；方面，角度（terms）；條件，條款（terms）；（人們之間的）關係（terms）；（數列、方程等的）項；（三段論中的）項；（建築）界標"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……稱為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about something <b>in terms of</b> something or <b>in</b> particular <b>terms</b>, you are specifying which aspect of it you are discussing or from what point of view you are considering it. 從…角度來看","examples":["Our goods compete in terms of product quality, reliability and above all variety. 我們的產品從質量、可靠性、尤其是多樣性來看很有競爭力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say something <b>in</b> particular <b>terms</b>, you say it using a particular type or level of language or using language which clearly shows your attitude. 以某種語言","examples":["The video explains in simple terms how the new tax works. 該錄影以淺顯易懂的語言解釋了新稅法的運作方式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>come to terms with</b> something difficult or unpleasant, you learn to accept and deal with it. 接受","examples":["She had come to terms with the fact that her husband would always be crippled. 她已接受了丈夫將終生跛足這個事實。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If two people or groups compete <b>on equal terms</b> or <b>on the same terms</b>, neither of them has an advantage over the other. 在同等條件下","examples":["I had at last found a sport where I could compete on equal terms with able-bodied people. 我終於找到一種體育運動，能和身體健全的人公平競賽"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If two people are <b>on good terms</b> or <b>on friendly terms</b>, they are friendly with each other. 關係好","examples":["Madeleine is on good terms with Sarah. 馬德琳和薩拉關係很好。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use the expressions <b>in the long term</b>, <b>in the short term</b>, and <b>in the medium term</b> to talk about what will happen over a long period of time, over a short period of time, and over a medium period of time. 從長遠/短期/中期來看","examples":["Organic fertilizers will have very positive results in the long term. 有機肥料從長遠來看將產生非常積極的效果。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you do something <b>on</b> your <b>terms</b>, you do it under conditions that you decide because you are in a position of power. 按照自己的意願","examples":["They will sign the union treaty only on their terms. 他們在符合自己意願的條件下才會簽署聯合條約。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you say that you <b>are thinking in terms of</b> doing a particular thing, you mean that you are considering it. 考慮","examples":["You should be thinking in terms of graduating next year. 你應該考慮明年畢業的事了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>term</b> is a word or expression with a specific meaning, especially one which is used in relation to a particular subject. 術語","examples":["Myocardial infarction is the medical term for a heart attack. 心肌梗塞是心臟病發作的醫學術語。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>term</b> is one of the periods of time that a school, college, or university divides the year into. 學期","examples":["...the summer term. …夏季學期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>term</b> is a period of time between two elections during which a particular party or government is in power. (政黨或政府的) 任期","examples":["Nixon never completed his term of office. 尼克松沒有完成自己的任期。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>term</b> is a period of time that someone spends doing a particular job or in a particular place. (工作或居住) 期間","examples":["...a 12 month term of service. …12個月的任職期。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>term</b> is the period for which a legal contract or insurance policy is valid. (合同或保險的) 有效期","examples":["Premiums are guaranteed throughout the term of the policy. 在保單的有效期內保證支付保險費。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>term</b> of a woman's pregnancy is the nine month period that it lasts. <b>Term</b> is also used to refer to the end of the nine month period. 懷孕期; 臨產","examples":["That makes her the first TV presenter to work the full term of her pregnancy. 那使她成了第一個在整個懷孕期間一直工作的電視節目主持人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>terms</b> of an agreement, treaty, or other arrangement are the conditions that must be accepted by the people involved in it. 條款","examples":["...the terms of the Helsinki agreement. …《赫爾辛基協議》的各項條款。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is termed</b> a particular thing, you mean that that is what people call it or that is their opinion of it. 把…稱作","examples":["He had been termed a temporary employee. 他曾被稱為臨時工。"]}]}]},"throat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喉嚨，咽喉；喉部，頸前部；咽喉狀部分（尤指狹窄通道、進出管路）；<文>嗓音，嗓門，歌喉；（肋材、錨臂或前後帆等的）彎曲處，凹口"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用喉音說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>throat</b> is the back of your mouth and the top part of the tubes that go down into your stomach and your lungs. 喉嚨","examples":["She had a sore throat. 她喉嚨痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>throat</b> is the front part of your neck. 喉部","examples":["His striped tie was loosened at his throat. 他脖子上的條紋領帶鬆開著。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>clear</b> your <b>throat</b>, you cough once either to make it easier to speak or to attract people's attention. 清喉嚨","examples":["Cross cleared his throat and spoke in low, polite tones. 克羅斯清了清喉嚨，低聲禮貌地說起話來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>ram</b> something <b>down</b> someone's <b>throat</b> or <b>force</b> it <b>down</b> their <b>throat</b>, you keep mentioning a situation or idea in order to make them accept it or believe it. 反覆灌輸以讓人接受或相信","examples":["I've always been close to my dad but he's never rammed his career down my throat. 我和父親一直很親近，但是他從來沒有強迫我繼承他的事業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two people or groups are <b>at each other's throats</b>, they are arguing or fighting violently with each other. 激烈爭吵; 激烈打鬥","examples":["The idea that we are at each other's throats couldn't be further from the truth. 認為我們在激烈爭吵的想法簡直是無稽之談。"]}]}]},"thunder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雷，雷聲；雷鳴般的響聲，轟隆聲；怒容滿面，（雷鳴般的）怒吼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打雷；發出雷鳴般的響聲，轟隆地響；轟隆隆地快速移動，使快速移動；憤怒地大叫，怒吼；砰然重擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thunder</b> is the loud noise that you hear from the sky after a flash of lightning, especially during a storm. 雷","examples":["There was thunder and lightning, and torrential rain. 雷電交加，暴雨傾盆而下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>thunder of</b> something that is moving or making a sound is the loud deep noise it makes. 轟隆聲","examples":["The thunder of the sea on the rocks seemed to blank out other thoughts. 海浪拍擊礁石的轟隆聲似乎要把其他的思緒都淹沒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When <b>it</b> <b>thunders</b>, a loud noise comes from the sky after a flash of lightning. 打雷","examples":["The day was heavy and still. It would probably thunder later. 天陰沉沉的，一絲風也沒有。等會兒可能會打雷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>thunders</b> somewhere, they move there quickly and with a lot of noise. 轟隆隆地快速移動","examples":["The horses thundered across the valley floor. 馬群轟隆隆地從谷底奔跑而過。"]}]}]},"test":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書面或口頭的）測驗，考試；（醫療上的）檢查，化驗，檢驗；（對機器或武器等的）試驗，檢驗；（對水、土壤、空氣等的）檢測，檢驗；（衡量能力或技能等的）測試，考驗；醫療檢查裝置；化驗結果；（常指板球、橄欖球的）國際錦標賽（Test）；準則，標準；（冶）烤缽，灰皿；（一些無脊椎動物和原生動物的）甲殼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"試驗，測試；測驗，考查（熟練程度，知識）；檢測，檢驗（質量或含量）；檢查（身體），（用試劑）化驗；考驗；嘗，（觸）試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>test</b> something, you try it, for example, by touching it or using it for a short time, in order to find out what it is, what condition it is in, or how well it works. 試驗","examples":["Either measure the temperature with a thermometer or test the water with your wrist. 要麼用溫度計測量水溫，要麼用你的手腕來試水溫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>test</b> someone, you ask them questions or tell them to perform certain actions in order to find out how much they know about a subject or how well they are able to do something. 測試","examples":["There was a time when each teacher spent an hour, one day a week, testing students in every subject. 曾有一段時間，每個老師每週都花一小時來測驗學生的各門功課。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>test</b> someone, you deliberately make things difficult for them in order to see how they react. 考驗","examples":["From the first day, Rudolf was testing me, seeing if I would make him tea, bring him a Coke. 從第一天起，魯道夫就在考驗我，看我會不會給他泡茶，給他拿可樂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are tested</b> <b>for</b> a particular disease or medical condition, you are examined or go through various procedures in order to find out whether you have that disease or condition. 檢查 (身體)","examples":["My doctor wants me to be tested for diabetes. 我的醫生要我去做糖尿病檢查。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>test</b> is a deliberate action or experiment to find out how well something works. 試驗","examples":["...the banning of nuclear tests. …對核試驗的禁止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>test</b> is a series of questions that you must answer or actions that you must perform in order to show how much you know about a subject or how well you are able to do something. 測試","examples":["Out of a total of 25 students only 15 passed the test. 所有25個學生中只有15個透過了測試。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event or situation is a <b>test</b> <b>of</b> a person or thing, it reveals their qualities or effectiveness. 考驗","examples":["It is a fact that holidays are a major test of any relationship. 這是事實，節假日是對任何情感關係的重大考驗。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A medical <b>test</b> is an examination of a part of your body in order to check that you are healthy or to find out what is wrong with you. (醫療) 檢查","examples":["If necessary, X-rays and blood tests will also be used to aid diagnosis. 如有必要的話，X光檢查和血液檢查也會被用來幫助診斷。","...a pregnancy test. …妊娠檢查。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the hard or tough outer covering of certain invertebrates and tunicates (無脊椎動物和被囊類的)堅硬表皮","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> something <b>to the test</b>, you find out how useful or effective it is by using it. 檢驗某物","examples":["The team are now putting their theory to the test. 該團隊正在檢驗他們的理論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If new circumstances or events <b>put</b> something or someone <b>to the test</b>, they put a strain on it and indicate how strong or stable it really is. 考驗某事/某人","examples":["Multiple hijackings are putting air traffic controllers to the test. 連環劫機案正在考驗航空排程員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>will stand the test of time</b>, you mean that it is strong or effective enough to last for a very long time. 經受時間的考驗","examples":["It says a lot for her cooking skills that so many of her recipes have stood the test of time. 她的很多食譜經受了時間的考驗，這很能證明她的廚藝。"]}]}]},"thumb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拇指；（手套的）拇指部分；（靈長目動物或其他哺乳動物的）第一指；豎起大拇指，翹起大拇指（以表示贊成或說明沒問題）；將拇指指向（所談論的物件）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"豎起大拇指請求搭便車；用拇指摸，用拇指捋；用拇指示意；用拇指翻動，翻閱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your hand has four fingers and one <b>thumb</b>. 大拇指","examples":["She bit the tip of her left thumb, not looking at me. 她咬著左手的大拇指頭，也不看我。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>thumb</b> a lift or <b>thumb</b> a ride, you stand by the side of the road holding out your thumb until a driver stops and gives you a lift. (站在公路邊) 豎起大拇指請求 (搭便車)","examples":["It may interest you to know that a boy answering Rory's description thumbed a ride to San Antonio. 可能讓你感興趣的是，有個和羅裡描述相符的男孩豎起大拇指請求搭便車到聖安東尼奧。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>under</b> someone's <b>thumb</b>, you are under their control, or very heavily influenced by them. 在…的控制下; 深受…的影響","examples":["I cannot tell you what pain I feel when I see how much my mother is under my father's thumb. 我無法向你形容，當我看到母親完全在父親的控制之下時我有多麼痛苦。"]}]}]},"tofu":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豆腐（由大豆製成的柔軟食品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tofu</b> is a soft white or brown food made from soybeans. 豆腐","examples":["...alternative foods like tofu, couscous, and hummus. ...可選擇的食物諸如豆腐、蒸粗麥粉和鷹嘴豆沙。"]}]}]},"toe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人的）腳趾，（獸、鳥的）趾；（襪、鞋等的）足尖部；端部，尖部；（高爾夫球的）球棒尖；坡腳，基腳，堤腳；（曲線的）趾區；肉質根部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用腳尖推（或觸碰、踢、踩）；足尖朝內（或外）行走；（一對車輪）前束（或反前束，後束）；（高爾夫）用球棒尖擊（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>toes</b> are the five movable parts at the end of each foot. 腳趾","examples":["She wiggled her toes against the packed sand. 她用腳趾撥弄著板結的沙子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>keeps</b> you <b>on</b> your <b>toes</b>, you mean that they cause you to remain alert and ready for anything that might happen. 使保持警覺","examples":["His fiery campaign rhetoric has kept opposition parties on their toes for months. 他激烈的競選言辭使反對黨數月保持警覺。"]}]}]},"title":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書籍、詩歌、圖畫、樂曲等的）名稱，標題；（書刊的）一種，一本；（人名前表示地位、職業或婚姻狀況的）頭銜，稱謂；職位名稱；稱號；（競賽、體育比賽的）冠軍；（尤指土地或財產的）所有權；（財產的）所有權憑證；（電影、電視的）字幕；（教會用語）就任聖職需具備的資格；（羅馬紅衣主教下轄的）教區，教堂"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給書籍、樂曲等）加標題，定題目；賦予頭銜，把……稱為"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"與（電影、戲劇等）同名的；冠軍的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>title</b> of a book, play, movie, or piece of music is its name. (書、戲劇、電影或樂曲的) 標題","examples":["\"Patience and Sarah\" was first published in 1969 under the title \"A Place for Us.\" 《耐心與薩拉》於1969年以《我們的地方》為書名首次出版。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Publishers and booksellers often refer to books or magazines as <b>titles</b>. (某種) 書刊","examples":["The magazine has become the biggest publisher of new poetry, with 50 new titles a year. 該雜誌已成了最大的新詩出版商，每年出版50種雜誌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>title</b> is a word such as \"Mr,\" \"Mrs,\" or \"Doctor,\" that is used before their own name in order to show their status or profession. 稱呼","examples":["Please fill in your name and title. 請填上你的名字和稱呼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>title</b> is a name that describes their job or status in an organization. 職位名稱","examples":["He was given the title of assistant manager. 他被授予經理助理的職位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person or team wins a particular <b>title</b>, they win a sports competition that is held regularly. Usually a person keeps a title until someone else defeats them. (體育比賽的) 冠軍","examples":["He became Jamaica's first Olympic gold medallist when he won the 400 metre title in 1948. 他在1948年贏得400米賽跑冠軍,成為牙買加首位奧運金牌得主。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In Britain, and some other countries, a person's <b>title</b> is a word such as \"Sir,\" \"Lord,\" or \"Lady\" that is used in front of their name, or a phrase that is used instead of their name, and indicates that they have a high rank in society. 頭銜","examples":["Her husband was also honoured with his title \"Sir Denis.\" 她的丈夫也被授予頭銜，尊稱為“丹尼斯爵士”。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a writer, composer, or artist <b>titles</b> a work, they give it a name. 給…加標題","examples":["Pirandello titled his play \"Six Characters in Search of an Author.\" 皮蘭德婁將其戲劇命名為《六個尋找作者的劇中人》。","The single is titled \"White Love.\" 這支單曲名為《白色之戀》。"]}]}]},"tent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帳篷；西班牙紅葡萄酒；（外科）塞條，塞子；（醫院裡給重病病人用的）氧氣帳（oxygen tent 的簡稱）；住處；帷幕"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"由帳篷組成，用帳篷（或帳篷狀物）遮蓋；使成帳篷狀；（尤指馬戲團）住帳篷，在帳篷裡宿營；暫時居住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tent</b> is a shelter made of canvas or nylon which is held up by poles and ropes, and is used mainly by people who are camping. 帳篷","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a plug of soft material for insertion into a bodily canal, etc, to dilate it or maintain its patency 傘狀物; 放在人體器官管道內用於擴張或保持其通暢","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to insert such a plug into (a bodily canal, etc) 將此傘形物放進(人體器官管道)","examples":[]}]}]},"tomato":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"番茄，西紅柿；番茄紅，鮮紅色；番茄植株；番茄，西紅柿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tomatoes</b> are soft, red fruit that you can eat raw in salads or cooked as a vegetable. 番茄; 西紅柿","examples":[]}]}]},"topic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"題目，主題；一般規則，總論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>topic</b> is a particular subject that you discuss, study, or write about. 話題","examples":["The weather is a constant topic of conversation in Alaska. 天氣在阿拉斯加是一個永恆的交談話題。"]}]}]},"tip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）傾斜，（使）斜側；給小費；<英>扔掉，倒掉（垃圾）；傾倒，倒出；打翻；（用液體、顏色等）覆蓋……的尖端；預言……獲勝；輕觸，輕碰；密報，透露訊息，告誡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"指點，訣竅，建議；小費；末梢，尖端；<英>垃圾場；<英，非正式>髒亂的地方；（對賽馬、比賽結果的）預測，內幕訊息；頂端附加物；（尤指給警方的）密報；（對運動的球或冰球的）輕碰，輕擊；手觸帽簷，脫帽（致敬、問好或道別的動作）；擦棒球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tip</b> of something long and narrow is the end of it. 尖端","examples":["The sleeves covered his hands to the tips of his fingers. 衣袖遮住了他的手，一直蓋到他的手指尖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a light blow 輕輕地一擊","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you give a <b>tip</b> to someone such as a waiter in a restaurant, you give them some money to thank them for their services. 小費","examples":["I gave the barber a tip. 我給了理髮師小費。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>tip</b> is a useful piece of advice. 建議","examples":["It shows how to prepare a resume, and gives tips on applying for jobs. 它說明了如何準備一份簡歷，並提了一些有關求職的建議。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>tip</b> is the same as a . 垃圾場","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tip</b> an object or part of your body or if it <b>tips</b>, it moves into a sloping position with one end or side higher than the other. 傾","examples":["He leaned away from her, and she had to tip her head back to see him. 他側身避開她，她只得向後側過頭來看他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tip</b> something somewhere, you pour it there. 傾倒","examples":["Tip the vegetables into a bowl. 把這些蔬菜倒進一個碗裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>tip</b> someone such as a waiter in a restaurant, you give them some money in order to thank them for their services. 給…小費","examples":["We usually tip 18-20%. 我們通常付18-20%的小費。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hit or strike lightly 輕輕地打","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a problem is <b>the tip of the iceberg</b>, you mean that it is one small part of a much larger problem. (問題的) 冰山一角","examples":["Unless we're all a lot more careful, the people who have died so far will be just the tip of the iceberg. 除非我們大家都更加小心，否則迄今為止已經死去的人數將只是冰山一角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>tips the scales</b> or <b>tips the balance</b>, it gives someone a slight advantage. 使稍佔優勢","examples":["Today's slightly shorter race could well help to tip the scales in her favour. 今日稍短程的比賽將很有可能使她稍佔優勢。"]}]}]},"tooth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牙，齒；（工具邊緣、梳子、鋸、拉鍊等的）齒狀物，齒；（官方組織、法律等的）威力，效力（teeth）；口味，愛好；粗糙面（顏料、膠水能黏附於上）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……裝齒；齧合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>teeth</b> are the hard white objects in your mouth, which you use for biting and chewing. 牙齒","examples":["She had very pretty straight teeth. 她有非常漂亮整齊的牙齒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>teeth</b> of something such as a comb, saw, cog, or zipper are the parts that stick out in a row on its edge. (梳子、鋸子、齒輪或拉鍊等物的) 齒","examples":["The front cog has 44 teeth. 前齒輪有44個齒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>a sweet tooth</b>, you like sweet food very much. 吃甜食的嗜好","examples":["Add more honey if you have a sweet tooth. 如果你嗜好甜食就多加些蜂蜜。"]}]}]},"toast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烤麵包片，吐司；乾杯，祝酒，敬酒；極受敬慕的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……舉杯敬酒，為……乾杯；烤，烘（食品，尤指麵包、乾酪）；使暖和，給……烤火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Toast</b> is bread which has been cut into slices and made brown and crisp by cooking at a high temperature. 烤麵包片","examples":["...a piece of toast. …一片烤麵包片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you drink a <b>toast</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you drink some wine or another alcoholic drink as a symbolic gesture, in order to show your appreciation of them or to wish them success. 敬酒","examples":["Eleanor and I drank a toast to the bride and groom. 埃莉諾和我給新郎和新娘敬了酒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>toast</b> something such as bread, you cook it at a high temperature so that it becomes brown and crisp. 烤 (麵包等)","examples":["Toast the bread lightly on both sides. 把麵包的兩面稍微烤一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>toast</b> someone or something, you drink a toast to them. 為…舉杯祝酒","examples":["We all toasted his health. 我們大家為他的健康舉杯祝酒。"]}]}]},"toilet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽水馬桶，坐便器；廁所，洗手間；梳洗，打扮；（治療過程中對身體部位的）清洗；上廁所，解手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"照料（人，尤其是嬰兒或傷病人士）上廁所；上廁所；梳妝，打扮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toilet</b> is a large bowl with a seat, or a platform with a hole, which is connected to a water system and which you use when you want to get rid of urine or faeces from your body. 抽水馬桶","examples":["She made Tina flush the pills down the toilet. 她讓蒂娜把藥丸衝下抽水馬桶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>toilet</b> is a room in a house or public building that contains a toilet. 廁所","examples":["She had gone in to use the toilet. 她已經去上洗手間了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>goes to the toilet</b> to mean that they get rid of waste substances from their body, especially when you want to avoid using words that you think may offend people. 上廁所","examples":["Although he had been treated with antibiotics, he went to the toilet repeatedly. 儘管已經用抗菌素治療過了，他還是頻繁地去洗手間。","I had to go to the toilet, but I didn't want to use that awful outhouse. So I went off in the woods. 我不得不上衛生間，但是我不想用那糟糕的戶外廁所，所以我到樹林裡去了。"]}]}]},"tongue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"舌，舌頭；（供食用的動物的）舌頭，口條；語言，方言；說話方式，寫作風格；鞋舌；舌狀物；（延伸入湖、海等中的）長條狀陸地，舌狀陸地；榫舌，雄榫；（脊椎動物的）齒舌；（昆蟲的）喙；鍾錘；（樂器、風琴管的）簧片；搭扣銷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用運舌法吹奏（管樂器）；用舌頭觸碰，舔；說話；<舊>斥責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>tongue</b> is the soft movable part inside your mouth which you use for tasting, eating, and speaking. 舌頭","examples":["I walked over to the mirror and stuck my tongue out. 我走到鏡子前伸出舌頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>tongue</b> to refer to the kind of things that a person says. 話語","examples":["She had a nasty tongue. 她滿口髒話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tongue</b> is a language. 語言","examples":["The French feel passionately about their native tongue. 法國人非常熱愛他們的母語。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tongue-in-cheek</b> remark or attitude is not serious, although it may seem to be. 無誠意的","examples":["...a lighthearted, tongue-in-cheek approach. …一種漫不經心、無誠意的態度。"]}]}]},"towel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毛巾，抹布，紙巾；<英，舊>衛生巾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用毛巾擦，用毛巾擦乾；<非正式，澳新>鞭打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>towel</b> is a piece of thick soft cloth that you use to dry yourself. 毛巾","examples":["...a bath towel. …一條浴巾。","...a hand towel. …一塊手巾。","...a beach towel. …一條沙灘浴巾。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>towel</b> something or <b>towel</b> it dry, you dry it with a towel. 用毛巾擦乾","examples":["James came out of his bedroom, towelling his wet hair. 詹姆斯走出他的臥室，用毛巾擦乾他那溼漉漉的頭髮。","I towelled myself dry. 我用毛巾把自己擦乾。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>throw in the towel</b>, you stop trying to do something because you realize that you cannot succeed. 認輸","examples":["It seemed as if the police had thrown in the towel and were abandoning the investigation. 看起來好象警察已經認輸了，並且要放棄調查。"]}]}]},"tower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"塔，塔樓；（傳送訊號等的）塔臺；塔狀堆積物；高櫃，高架子；高層建築，辦公大樓；立式機箱；倫敦塔（the Tower）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（比周圍的人或物）高出許多，屹立；勝過，超過（其他人或機構）；（尤指獵鷹為捕抓獵物俯衝前）高飛，翱翔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tower</b> is a tall, narrow building, that either stands alone or forms part of another building such as a church or castle. 塔","examples":["...an eleventh century castle with 120-foot high towers. …一座11世紀的城堡，有著120英尺高的塔樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tower</b> is a tall structure that is used for sending radio or television signals. (無線電或電視訊號的) 發射塔","examples":["Troops are still in control of the television and radio tower. 軍隊仍然控制著電視和無線電的發射塔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tower</b> is a tall box that contains the main parts of a computer, such as the hard disk and the drives. (計算機) 機箱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that <b>towers</b> <b>over</b> surrounding people or things is a lot taller than they are. 高出許多","examples":["He stood up and towered over her. 他站起來，高出她許多。"]}]}]},"tour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行，旅遊；遊覽，參觀，觀光；巡迴比賽（或演出等），巡視；任職期，服役期；（政治家或領導人的）訪問；錦標賽（the tour）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"旅遊，觀光，參觀；（在……）進行巡迴演出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tour</b> is an organized trip that people such as musicians, politicians, or theatre companies go on to several different places, stopping to meet people or perform. 巡迴訪問; 巡迴演出","examples":["The band is currently on a two-month tour of Europe. 這個樂隊目前正在歐洲進行為期兩個月的巡迴演出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tour</b> is a trip during which you visit several places that interest you. 旅行","examples":["It was week five of my tour of the major cities of Europe. 這是我在歐洲主要城市旅行的第5周。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tour</b> is a short trip that you make around a place, for example, around a historical building, so that you can look at it. 遊覽","examples":["...a guided tour. …一次有導遊帶領的遊覽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people are travelling on a tour, you can say that they are <b>on tour</b>. 進行巡迴訪問; 進行巡迴演出","examples":["The band will be going on tour. 這個樂隊將要進行巡迴演出。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people such as musicians, politicians, or theatre companies <b>tour</b>, they go on a tour, for example, in order to perform or to meet people. 巡迴演出","examples":["A few years ago they toured the country with a roadshow. 幾年前他們在該國巡迴流動演出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tour</b> a place, you go on a trip or journey around it. 遊覽","examples":["You can also tour the site on bicycle. 你也可以騎腳踏車遊覽那處遺址。"]}]}]},"tradition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳統，慣例；傳統故事，傳說，傳統信仰；和著名歷史人物有共同品質的人；（神學）聖傳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tradition</b> is a custom or belief that has existed for a long time. 傳統","examples":["...the rich traditions of Afro-Cuban music and dance. …非裔古巴人多姿多彩的音樂和舞蹈傳統。"]}]}]},"treasure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金銀財寶，珠寶，財富；（尤指藝術或有歷史價值的）珍品；得力幫手，心肝寶貝；珍藏品，珍貴之物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"珍愛，珍藏；珍惜，珍視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Treasure</b> is a collection of valuable old objects such as gold coins and jewels that has been hidden or lost. 財寶","examples":["It was here, the buried treasure, she knew it was. 那些埋藏的珍寶就在這兒，她知道就在這兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Treasures</b> are valuable objects, especially works of art and items of historical value. 珍品 (尤指藝術品和有歷史價值的物品)","examples":["The house was large and full of art treasures. 那棟房子很大，裡面滿是藝術珍品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Treasure</b> is also a noun. 珍愛之物","examples":["His greatest treasure is his collection of rock records. 他最珍愛的東西就是他收藏的搖滾唱片。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>treasure</b> something that you have, you keep it or care for it carefully because it gives you great pleasure and you think it is very special. 珍惜","examples":["She treasures her memories of those joyous days. 她珍惜那些快樂時光的記憶。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"珍貴的","examples":["These books are still among my most treasured possessions. 這些書仍然是我最珍貴的財產之一。"]}]}]},"traffic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"路上行駛的車輛，交通；（沿固定路線的）航行，行駛，飛行；運輸量；非法交易；資訊流量，通訊（量）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（非法）進行……交易，做……買賣；在……通行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Traffic</b> refers to all the vehicles that are moving along the roads in a particular area. 交通","examples":["There was heavy traffic on the roads. 路上的交通很擁擠。","Traffic was unusually light for that time of day. 交通在白天的那個時段有些異常地順暢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Traffic</b> refers to the movement of ships, trains, or aircraft between one place and another. <b>Traffic</b> also refers to the people and goods that are being transported. 運輸; 人流; 貨流","examples":["Air traffic had returned to normal. 空中交通已恢復正常。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Traffic</b> <b>in</b> something such as drugs or stolen goods is an illegal trade in them. (毒品或贓物等的) 非法買賣","examples":["...the widespread traffic in stolen cultural artefacts. …被盜文物非法買賣氾濫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"非法買賣","examples":["He was sentenced to ten years in prison on charges of drug trafficking. 他被指控販毒，被判10年徒刑。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>traffics</b> <b>in</b> something such as drugs or stolen goods buys and sells them even though it is illegal to do so. 從事 (毒品或贓物等的) 非法買賣","examples":["The president said illegal drugs are hurting the entire world and anyone who traffics in them should be brought to justice. 總統說毒品正在危害全世界，毒品非法交易者都應該繩之以法。"]}]}]},"trade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貿易，買賣；行業；同行業者，同仁（the trade）；營業額，交易量；（尤指需要特殊技術和手工勞動的）職業，行當；交換，交易；<美> （體育界）轉會，交換運動員；<英> 執照酒商；信風，貿易風（trades）；股票交易"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做買賣，做生意；營運，營業；（在證券交易所）交易，買賣；用……進行交換，互相交換；（某物）替代（某物）；對打，對罵；<美> 將（運動員）轉會（或轉隊）；交換，對換（位置或處境）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trade</b> is the activity of buying, selling, or exchanging goods or services between people, companies, or countries. 貿易; 買賣","examples":["Texas has a long history of trade with Mexico. 得克薩斯與墨西哥有著悠久的貿易史。","...negotiations on a new international trade agreement. …關於一個新的國際貿易協定的談判。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"交易","examples":["Trading on the stock exchange may be suspended. 股票交易可能被暫停。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>trade</b> is a particular area of business or industry. 生意; 行業","examples":["They've ruined the tourist trade for the next few years. 他們已經毀掉了以後幾年的旅遊生意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone's <b>trade</b> is the kind of work that they do, especially when they have been trained to do it over a period of time. 職業; 手藝","examples":["He learned his trade as a diver in the North Sea. 他在北海當上了潛水員。","Alicia was a jeweler by trade. 艾麗西亞是個珠寶商。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Trade</b> is also a noun. 交易","examples":["I am willing to make a trade with you. 我願意和你做個交易。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people, companies, or countries <b>trade</b>, they buy, sell, or exchange goods or services between themselves. 做生意","examples":["They may refuse to trade, even when offered attractive prices. 他們有可能拒絕做生意，即便是報價很有吸引力。","They had years of experience of trading with the West. 他們有數年與西方做生意的經驗。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>trades</b> one thing <b>for</b> another or if two people <b>trade</b> things, they agree to exchange one thing for the other thing. 互相交換","examples":["They traded land for goods and money. 他們用土地來換取商品和金錢。","Kids used to trade baseball cards. 孩子們過去常互相交換棒球卡片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trade</b> places <b>with</b> someone or if the two of you <b>trade</b> places, you move into the other person's position or situation, and they move into yours. 交換 (位置)","examples":["Mike asked George to trade places with him so he could ride with Tomas. 邁克請喬治跟他交換位置，這樣他就能和托馬斯同車了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two people or groups <b>trade</b> something such as blows, insults, or jokes, they hit each other, insult each other, or tell each other jokes. 對打; 互罵; 互開玩笑","examples":["Children would settle disputes by trading punches or insults in the schoolyard. 孩子們透過在校園裡打架或對罵來解決爭端。"]}]}]},"triangle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"三角形；三角形物體；三角鐵（打擊樂器）；<美>三角板，三角尺；三角關係；（擺放斯諾克和落袋檯球撞球位置的）三角框；小型歐亞紫刺蛾；<史>（繫縛士兵以鞭打的）三戟刑具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>triangle</b> is an object, arrangement, or flat shape with three straight sides and three angles. 三角形","examples":["This design is in pastel colours with three rectangles and three triangles. 這個圖案色彩柔和淡雅，有3個長方形和3個三角形。","Its outline roughly forms an equilateral triangle. 它的大致輪廓是一個等邊三角形。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>triangle</b> is a musical instrument that consists of a piece of metal shaped like a triangle. You play it by hitting it with a short metal bar. 三角鐵 (一種打擊樂器)","examples":["My musical career consisted of playing the triangle in kindergarten. 我的音樂生涯包括在幼兒園演奏三角鐵。"]}]}]},"track":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小道，小徑；蹤跡，足跡，車轍；（鐵路的）軌道；（窗簾、推拉門等的）滑竿，滑軌；<美>（火車站的）站臺；賽道，跑道；（移動的）路徑，方向；（唱片或光碟等上的）歌曲，曲子；音軌，聲道；（推土機等的）履帶；徑賽運動，田徑運動；<美>（同齡學生依智力編排的）班，組；思路，行為方式；<美>（分軌制教育的）課程；（機動車輛輪胎的橫向）輪距"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"追查，追蹤；（尤指用特殊電子裝置）跟蹤；記錄……的進展；跟蹤攝影，移動攝影；（錄製裝置的移動部件）運轉正常；<美>把（學生）按能力分班（或組）；<美>留下（髒）足跡；（以某方式或沿某方向）移動；跟隨（利率，股價等）；（電子）統調；從岸上拉（獨木舟）前進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>track</b> is a rough, unpaved road or path. (崎嶇不平的) 小路","examples":["We set off once more, over a rough mountain track. 我們又一次出發了，走在一條崎嶇不平的山間小路上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>track</b> is a piece of ground, often oval-shaped, that is used for races involving running, cars, bicycles, horses, or dogs called greyhounds. 跑道","examples":["...the athletics track. …那條運動員跑道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Railway <b>tracks</b> are the rails that a train travels along. 鐵軌","examples":["A cow stood on the tracks. 一頭奶牛站在鐵軌上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>track</b> is one of the songs or pieces of music on a CD, record, or tape. (錄製在CD、唱片或磁帶上的) 一首歌曲; 一首樂曲","examples":["I only like two of the ten tracks on this CD. 我只喜歡這張CD上的10首歌曲中的2首。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Tracks</b> are marks left in the ground by the feet of animals or people. 足跡","examples":["The only evidence of pandas was their tracks in the snow. 有熊貓活動的惟一證據就是它們在雪中的足跡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>track</b> animals or people, you try to follow them by looking for the signs that they have left behind, for example, the marks left by their feet. 跟蹤","examples":["He thought he had better track this wolf and see where it lived. 他認為他最好跟蹤這隻狼，並看看它在哪兒生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>track</b> someone or something means to follow their movements by means of a special device, such as a satellite or radar. (用衛星、雷達等特殊裝置) 追蹤","examples":["Our radar began tracking the jets. 我們的雷達開始追蹤那些噴氣式飛機。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep track of</b> a situation or a person, you make sure that you have the newest and most accurate information about them all the time. 瞭解…的動向","examples":["With eleven thousand employees, it's very difficult to keep track of them all. 有11000名員工，很難了解他們所有人的動向。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lose track of</b> someone or something, you no longer know where they are or what is happening. 不瞭解…的進展","examples":["You become so deeply absorbed in an activity that you lose track of time. 你是那麼專注於一項活動，以致忘了時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on track</b>, they are acting or progressing in a way that is likely to result in success. 步入正軌","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>on the right track</b>, you are acting or progressing in a way that is likely to result in success. If you are <b>on the wrong track</b>, you are acting or progressing in a way that is likely to result in failure. 做得正確/不正確","examples":["Guests are returning in increasing numbers – a sure sign that we are on the right track. 回頭客越來越多–一個我們做得對的確鑿跡象。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>stops</b> you <b>in</b> your <b>tracks</b>, or if you <b>stop dead in</b> your <b>tracks</b>, you suddenly stop moving because you are very surprised, impressed, or frightened. (因吃驚、感動或驚恐) 突然停住腳步","examples":["This magnificent church cannot fail to stop you in your tracks. 這座宏偉的教堂一定會讓你歎為觀止。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone or something <b>stops</b> a process or activity <b>in its tracks</b>, or if it <b>stops dead in its tracks</b>, they prevent the process or activity from continuing. 中斷","examples":["Francis felt he would like to stop this conversation in its tracks. 弗朗西斯覺得他想中斷這次談話。"]}]}]},"trap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（捕捉動物的）陷阱，網，夾子；圈套，詭計；伏擊；牢籠，困境；<俚>嘴；（尤指舊時使用的）雙輪輕便馬車；（應該避免的）錯誤，問題；（賽狗開始時的）放狗隔欄；（高爾夫球場的）沙坑，凹地；容器，存貯裝置；（水管）存水彎，U形管；拋靶器（將泥鴿等拋於空中以打靶）；<史>（射球戲用的）拋球器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設陷阱（或夾子、捕捉器）捕捉；使陷入圈套，使中計；誘捕，抓捕；使無力改變，使受限制；把……困在，使陷於（尤指危險之地）；（尤指身體某部位等）被卡住；聚集（空氣、氣體或能量等）；（英足）停（球）；（棒球）抓住（從地上彈起的球）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>暗色巖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trap</b> is a device which is placed somewhere or a hole which is dug somewhere in order to catch animals or birds. (捉捕動物或鳥類的) 捕捉器; 陷阱","examples":["Nathan's dog got caught in a trap. 內森的狗被捕捉器夾住了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trap</b> is a trick that is intended to catch or deceive someone. 圈套","examples":["He failed to keep a rendezvous after sensing a police trap. 他覺察到是警察的圈套後，就未去赴約。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>trap</b> is an unpleasant situation that you cannot easily escape from. 困境","examples":["The government has found that it's caught in a trap of its own making. 政府已經發現其陷入了自己造成的困境中。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person <b>traps</b> animals or birds, he or she catches them using traps. 用捕捉器捕捉; 設陷阱捕捉","examples":["The locals were encouraged to trap and kill mice to stop the spread of the virus. 當地人被鼓勵用捕捉器捕殺老鼠以阻止病毒的傳播。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trap</b> someone <b>into</b> doing or saying something, you trick them so that they do or say it, although they did not want to. 誘騙","examples":["Were you just trying to trap her into making some admission? 你僅僅是在試圖誘騙她招供嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>trap</b> someone, especially a criminal, means to capture them. 抓捕","examples":["The police knew they had to trap the killer. 警察知道他們得抓住那個兇手。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are trapped</b> somewhere, something falls onto you or blocks your way and prevents you from moving or escaping. 困住","examples":["The train was trapped underground by a fire. 列車被一場大火困在了地下。","The light aircraft then cartwheeled, trapping both men. 那架輕型飛機隨後側翻，把兩個人困住了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When something <b>traps</b> gas, water, or energy, it prevents it from escaping. 留住 (氣體、水或能量)","examples":["Wool traps your body heat, keeping the chill at bay. 羊毛織物能留住你的身體熱量，阻擋寒氣。"]}]}]},"treatment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對待，待遇；處理，討論；治療，醫治；（淨化或防治）處理，加工；護理，護理品；<非正式>極致； 對待，待遇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Treatment</b> is medical attention given to a sick or injured person or animal. 治療","examples":["Many patients are not getting the medical treatment they need. 許多病人都沒有得到他們需要的醫療。","...a veterinary surgeon who specializes in the treatment of caged birds. …一個專長治療籠養鳥的獸醫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>treatment</b> of someone is the way you behave toward them or deal with them. 對待; 處理","examples":["We don't want any special treatment. 我們不需要任何特殊待遇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Treatment</b> of something involves putting a particular substance onto or into it, in order to clean it, to protect it, or to give it special properties. (採用某種物質的) 處理","examples":["There should be greater treatment of sewage before it is discharged. 汙水排放前應該進行更充分的處理。"]}]}]},"treat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"對待，看待；治療，醫治；請客，招待；（利用化學物質或反應）處理，保護；把……看作，把……視為；處理，探討，論述；做使自己快樂的事；把（某物）給某人以示好感；提供（娛樂）；（尤指與對手）商談，談判"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不同一般的）樂事，享受；款待，招待；請客，做東；零食；<美>甜食；（尤指不經常吃的）美味佳餚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>treat</b> someone or something in a particular way, you behave toward them or deal with them in that way. 對待; 處理","examples":["Artie treated most women with indifference. 阿蒂對待大多數女性頗為冷淡。","Police say they're treating it as a case of attempted murder. 警方說他們正將其作為謀殺未遂案件來處理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a doctor or nurse <b>treats</b> a patient or an illness, he or she tries to make the patient well again. 治療","examples":["Doctors treated her with aspirin. 醫生用阿斯匹林給她治療。","The boy was treated for a minor head wound. 那個男孩因頭部輕傷而接受治療。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is treated</b> <b>with</b> a particular substance, the substance is put onto or into it in order to clean it, to protect it, or to give it special properties. (用某種物質) 處理","examples":["About 70% of the cocoa acreage is treated with insecticide. 大約70%的可可豆種植區都用殺蟲劑處理過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>treat</b> someone <b>to</b> something special which they will enjoy, you buy it or arrange it for them. 款待","examples":["She was always treating him to ice cream. 她總請他吃冰淇淋。","Tomorrow I'll treat myself to a day's gardening. 明天我要好好享受一天的園藝活兒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>treat</b>, you buy or arrange something special for them which they will enjoy. 款待","examples":["Lettie had never yet failed to return from town without some special treat for him. 萊蒂每次從城裡回來都要帶一些特別的禮物送給他。"]}]}]},"travel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指長途）旅行；走動，移動；（以某速度、朝某方向或在某距離內）行進；（光或聲音）傳播；（食品等）經得起長途運輸；周遊，走遍；（尤指車輛）快速行進；（訊息）流傳；盛行各地；（籃球運動中）走步；（目光）掃視，移動；交往；想象來到"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行；（出國）旅遊；（機器部件的）運動範圍，運動速度，運動模式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>travel</b>, you go from one place to another, often to a place that is far away. 旅行","examples":["You had better travel to Nova Scotia tomorrow. 你最好明天去新斯科舍。","I've been travelling all day. 我一整天都在旅行。","Students often travel hundreds of miles to get here. 學生們常常要旅行數百英里才能到這兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>travel</b> the world, the country, or the area, you go to many different places in the world or in a particular country or area. 遊歷","examples":["He was a very wealthy man who had traveled the world. 他是個非常富有的人，曾經周遊過世界。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Travel</b> is the activity of travelling. 旅行","examples":["Information on travel in New Zealand is available at the hotel. 紐西蘭的旅遊資訊在該酒店可以查到。","He detested air travel. 他厭惡空中旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>travels</b> are the trips that they make to places a long way from their home. 旅遊","examples":["He also collects things for the house on his travels abroad. 他在國外旅遊時也為家人收集些東西。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When light or sound from one place reaches another, you say that it <b>travels</b> to the other place. (光或聲音) 傳播","examples":["When sound travels through water, strange things can happen. 當聲音在水中傳播時，奇怪的事情會發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When news becomes known by people in different places, you can say that it <b>travels</b> to them. (訊息) 流傳","examples":["News of his work traveled all the way to Asia. 有關他工作的訊息一直傳到了亞洲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>travel light</b>, you travel without taking much luggage. 輕裝旅行","examples":["It would be good to be able to travel light, but I end up taking too many clothes. 能夠輕裝旅行再好不過，但我最終還是帶了太多衣服。"]}]}]},"trial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"審判，審理；試驗，試用；（對人的忍耐、自制力的）考驗，磨練；煩人的事，惹麻煩的人；預賽，選拔賽；（檢驗車手技能的）摩托車障礙檢驗賽；（動物的）比賽，表演"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"測試，試驗；（馬、狗等動物）參加比賽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"試驗性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trial</b> is a formal meeting in a law court, at which a judge and jury listen to evidence and decide whether a person is guilty of a crime. 審判","examples":["New evidence showed the police lied at the trial. 新的證據表明警方在審判時撒了謊。","I have the right to a trial with a jury of my peers. 我有權要求由和我一樣的平民組成的陪審團參加審判。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trial</b> is an experiment in which you test something by using it or doing it for a period of time to see how well it works. If something is <b>on trial</b>, it is being tested in this way. 試驗","examples":["They have been treated with this drug in clinical trials. 他們在臨床試驗中一直接受這種藥物的治療。","I took the car out for a trial on the roads. 我把車開出去在公路上試了一下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>trials</b> <b>of</b> a situation, you mean the unpleasant things that you experience in it. 磨難","examples":["...the trials of adolescence. …青春期的磨難。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a grammatical number occurring in some languages for words in contexts where exactly three of their referents are described or referred to (某些語言中正好描述或提到三個指示物的)試驗語法數字","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to test or make experimental use of (something) 試驗","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>by</b> <b>trial and error</b>, you try several different methods of doing it until you find the method that works best. 反覆試驗","examples":["Many drugs were found by trial and error. 許多藥物都是經過反覆試驗後才被發現的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>on trial</b>, they are being tried in a court of law. 在受審","examples":["He is currently on trial for drunk driving. 他目前因酒後駕車而受審。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>on trial</b>, you mean that they are in a situation where people are observing them to see whether they succeed or fail. 在試驗中; 在考驗中","examples":["The president will be drawn into a damaging battle in which his credentials will be on trial. 總統將被拖入一場破壞性的鬥爭，他正陷入信任危機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>stands trial</b>, they are tried in court for a crime they are accused of. 受審判","examples":["He was found to be mentally unfit to stand trial. 發現他精神狀況不適合接受審判。"]}]}]},"trousers":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"褲子，長褲； 褲子，長褲（trouser 的複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trousers</b> are a piece of men's clothing that cover the body from the waist downward, and that cover each leg separately. 褲子","examples":["He was dressed in a shirt, dark trousers and boots. 他穿著襯衣、深色褲子和靴子。"]}]}]},"truck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"卡車，載重汽車；<英>（鐵路）運貨車皮，敞篷貨運火車；（運送東西的）手推車，手拉車；火車轉向架；（滑板的）輪轉軸；（桅杆或旗杆頂端有孔可穿升降索的）桅冠，旗杆冠；<古>交易，買賣；<美>商品菜園產物（尤指蔬菜）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>用卡車裝運；<美>駕駛卡車；輕鬆前進，平穩前進；<古>交換，交易"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>truck</b> is the same as a . 卡車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>truck</b> is a vehicle with a large area in the back for carrying things with low sides to make it easy to load and unload. A <b>truck</b> is the same as a . 敞篷貨車","examples":["We can only seat two in the truck. 我們的敞篷貨車裡只能坐兩個人。","Throw the dogs in the back of the truck. 把狗都扔到敞篷車的後面去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>truck</b> is an open vehicle used for carrying goods on a railway. 敞蓬貨運火車","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something or someone <b>is trucked</b> somewhere, they are driven there in a truck. 用卡車運送","examples":["The liquor was sold legally and trucked out of the state. 這種酒合法出售，由卡車運出該州。"]}]}]},"trumpet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小號，喇叭；喇叭形物（尤指黃水仙的管狀冠）；喇叭似的響聲（尤指大象的吼聲）；（風琴的）小號音栓；北美黃瓶子草（trumpets）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鼓吹，大肆宣揚；（尤指大象）吼叫；吹喇叭，吹小號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trumpet</b> is a musical instrument of the brass family which plays comparatively high notes. 小號","examples":["I played the trumpet in the school orchestra. 我在學校管絃樂隊吹小號。"]}]}]},"turkey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火雞；火雞肉；<美，非正式>（電影或戲劇的）失敗之作；笨蛋，傻瓜；土耳其（Turkey）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>turkey</b> is a large bird that is kept on a farm for its meat. 火雞","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Turkey</b> is the meat of this bird eaten as food. 火雞肉","examples":["They will sit down to a traditional turkey dinner early this afternoon. 他們今天下午早些時候將坐下來吃一頓傳統的火雞宴。"]}]}]},"turtle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海龜；海龜肉；<美>龜；淡水龜；（計算機）龜標"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"翻到背面或頂部；（尤指在水中）捕捉海龜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>turtle</b> is the same as a . 同sea turtle","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>turtle</b> is any reptile that has a thick shell around its body, for example a tortoise or terrapin, and can pull its whole body into its shell. 龜","examples":["...a pet turtle. …一隻寵物龜。","...the giant sea turtle. …那隻巨大的海龜。"]}]}]},"trick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花招，詭計，騙局；竅門，技巧；戲法，把戲；惡作劇，戲弄；引起錯覺（或記憶紊亂）的事物；（紙牌的）一圈，一墩；（特別的）習慣，方式；舵手的一班（一般為二或四小時）；<非正式>嫖客"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"欺騙，哄騙；（紋章）（用由字母、符號標明的顏色）給（盾形徽章）勾勒輪廓"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"騙人的，使人產生錯覺的；<美>（身體部位）虛弱的，有毛病的；巧妙的，取樂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trick</b> is an action that is intended to fool or deceive someone. 捉弄; 詭計","examples":["We are playing a trick on a man who keeps bothering me. 我們正耍弄著一個人，因為他一直煩擾我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trick</b> is a clever or skillful action that someone does in order to entertain people. 戲法","examples":["...magic tricks. …魔術戲法。","He shows me card tricks. 他向我表演紙牌戲法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>trick</b> is a clever way of doing something. 竅門","examples":["Everything I cooked was a trick of my mother's. 我烹飪都是沿用了我母親的訣竅。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>tricks</b> you, they deceive you, often in order to make you do something. 欺騙","examples":["Stephen is going to be pretty upset when he finds out how you tricked him. 當斯蒂芬發現你是如何欺騙他時，他會非常不高興的。","His family tricked him into going to Pakistan, and once he was there, they took away his passport. 他的家人騙他去了巴基斯坦，他一到那裡，他們便拿走了他的護照。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>does the trick</b>, it achieves what you wanted. 達到目的","examples":["Sometimes a few choice words will do the trick. 有時斟酌得當的隻言片語就能達到目的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone tries <b>every trick in the book</b>, they try every possible thing that they can think of in order to achieve something. 渾身解數","examples":["Companies are using every trick in the book to stay one step in front of their competitors. 各公司正用盡渾身解數想領先競爭對手一步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>tricks of the trade</b> are the quick and clever ways of doing something that are known by people who regularly do a particular activity. 行業訣竅","examples":["To get you started, we have asked five successful writers to reveal some of the tricks of the trade. 為了幫你起步，我們請了5位成功作家來揭示一些訣竅。"]}]}]},"tunnel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"隧道，地道；（動物的）洞穴通道；運動場運動員通道；套管；風洞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開鑿隧道，挖地道；（物理）（粒子）穿透勢壘，隧（道貫）穿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tunnel</b> is a long passage which has been made under the ground, usually through a hill or under the sea. 隧道","examples":["Boston drivers love the tunnel. 波士頓的司機們喜歡那條隧道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>tunnel</b> somewhere means to make a tunnel there. 挖掘隧道","examples":["The thieves tunnelled under all the security devices. 小偷們在所有的那些安全裝置下面都挖了地道。"]}]}]},"tube":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（金屬、塑膠、玻璃等材料制的）管，管子；管狀物；（裝柔軟物質的）軟管；管狀器官；<英>（倫敦）地鐵；<美>電視機（the tube）；緊身女衣；<澳，非正式>一聽（或一罐）啤酒；陰極射線管，電視映象管；<美>熱離子管；（散浪頭下的）空心浪；<非正式>香菸"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用管道運輸；<英，非正式>乘地鐵；使成管狀；玩內胎漂流；<非正式>（給做過喉剖開術的人或動物）插管（以助呼吸）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tube</b> is a long hollow object that is usually round, like a pipe. 管子","examples":["He is fed by a tube that enters his nose. 他透過一根插入鼻子的管子進食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tube</b> <b>of</b> something such as paste is a long, thin container which you squeeze in order to force the paste out. (裝膏狀物體的) 管子","examples":["I went out today and bought a tube of toothpaste. 我今天出去買了一管牙膏。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Some long, thin, hollow parts in your body are referred to as <b>tubes</b>. (人體內的) 管狀器官","examples":["The lungs are in fact constructed of thousands of tiny tubes. 肺其實是由數千個細小管狀器官構成的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to the television as <b>the tube</b>. 電視機","examples":["The only baseball he saw was on the tube. 他只在電視上看過棒球比賽。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The tube</b> is the underground railway system in London. 倫敦地鐵","examples":[]}]}]},"typhoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（印度洋及西太平洋的）颱風"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>typhoon</b> is a very violent tropical storm. 颱風","examples":[]}]}]},"truth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事實，真相；真實性；真理，原理；的確，事實上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>truth</b> about something is all the facts about it, rather than things that are imagined or invented. 實情; 真相","examples":["Is it possible to separate truth from fiction? 有可能區分事實和謊言嗎？","I must tell you the truth about this business. 我必須告訴你這樁交易的真相。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that there is some <b>truth</b> <b>in</b> a statement or story, you mean that it is true, or at least partly true. 真實性","examples":["There is no truth in this story. 這個故事不具備真實性。","Is there any truth to the rumours? 這些謠傳有事實根據嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>truth</b> is something that is believed to be true. 真理","examples":["It is an almost universal truth that the more we are promoted in a job, the less we actually exercise the skills we initially used to perform it. 一個幾乎普遍的真理是，工作上提升得越高，我們最初的那些工作技能實際上就用得越少。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>to tell you the truth</b> or <b>truth to tell</b> in order to indicate that you are telling someone something in an open and honest way, without trying to hide anything. 跟你說實話","examples":["To tell you the truth, I was afraid to see him. 跟你說實話，我怕見到他。"]}]}]},"underwear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"內衣，襯衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Underwear</b> is items of clothing that you wear next to your skin and under your other clothes. 內衣","examples":["For Christmas my brother and I got new underwear, one toy and one book. 作為聖誕禮物，我弟弟和我得到了新內衣、一件玩具和一本書。"]}]}]},"type":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"型別，種類；具有某種特徵的人，典型；（印刷的）文字，字型；（印刷）鉛字，活字；象徵；（藝術的）典型，榜樣；（宗教學）預兆；（植，動）型，模式標本；（獎章或硬幣）圖案；（語言學）型別，型"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用計算機或打字機）打字；測定……的型別，分型"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>type</b> <b>of</b> something is a group of those things that have particular features in common. 型別; 種類","examples":["...several types of lettuce. …生菜的幾個品種。","There are various types of the disease. 該疾病有各種型別。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a particular thing or person as a <b>type</b> <b>of</b> something more general, you are considering that thing or person as an example of that more general group. 某類 (人或事物)","examples":["Have you done this type of work before? 你以前做過這種工作嗎？","Rates of interest for this type of borrowing can be high. 這種貸款的利率可能會很高。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a person as a particular <b>type</b>, you mean that they have that particular appearance, character, or type of behaviour. 具有某種特點的人","examples":["It's the first time I, a fair-skinned, freckly type, have sailed in the sun without burning. 這是第一次，我這樣一個皮膚白皙、有雀斑的人，頂著太陽航海而沒有曬傷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Type</b> is printed text as it appears in a book or newspaper, or the small pieces of metal that are used to create this. 印刷文字; 鉛字","examples":["The correction had already been set in type. 校正稿已經排好版了。","I can't read this small type. 我無法讀這種小號字型。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>type</b> something, you use a typewriter or computer keyboard to write it. 打字","examples":["I can type your essays for you. 我可以為你打文章。","I had never really learned to type properly. 我從未真正地學會正確地打字。"]}]}]},"umbrella":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傘，雨傘，陽傘；綜合體，總體；保護傘，庇護；（有眾多附屬小機構或小群體的）傘形組織；（戰鬥機或高射炮構成的）掩護幕，防空火網；（動）（水母）傘膜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（大的組織）包括許多小團體的；（詞彙）總稱的，總括的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>umbrella</b> is an object which you use to protect yourself from the rain or hot sun. It consists of a long stick with a folding frame covered in cloth. 傘","examples":["Harry held an umbrella over Denise. 哈里為丹尼斯撐著傘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Umbrella</b> is used to refer to a single group or description that includes a lot of different organizations or ideas. 總組織; 總稱","examples":["The country's blood banks are under the umbrella of the American Red Cross. 該國的血庫均屬於美國紅十字會。"]}]}]},"trust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信任，信賴；（金錢或財產的）信託，託管；受託基金機構，受託團體；代管的財物，託管的財物；公立醫院（由政府資助、獨立經營）；<美>托拉斯托拉斯，壟斷企業；受託，受委任；<文>被託付的人，被賦予的職責；<文>希望，期待"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"信任，相信；對……有把握，信得過；堅信，信仰；希望，盼望；託交，託付；<古>賒賬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trust</b> someone, you believe that they are honest and sincere and will not deliberately do anything to harm you. 信任","examples":["\"I trust you completely,\" he said. “我完全信任你。”他說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trust</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you believe that they will do it. 相信 (某人會做某事)","examples":["That's why I must trust you to keep this secret. 這就是我一定相信你會保守此秘密的原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>trust</b> someone <b>with</b> something important or valuable, you allow them to look after it or deal with it. 託付","examples":["This could make your superiors hesitate to trust you with major responsibilities. 這可能會使你的上司猶豫著不願把重大職責託付給你。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you do not <b>trust</b> something, you feel that it is not safe or reliable. (不) 相信 (某物安全或可靠)","examples":["She nodded, not trusting her own voice. 她點了點頭，無法相信自己的聲音。","For one thing, he didn't trust his legs to hold him up. 首先，他不相信自己的腿能站起來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>trust</b> someone's judgment or advice, you believe that it is good or right. 相信 (某人的判斷或建議)","examples":["Jake has raised two incredible kids and I trust his judgement. 傑克已經撫養了兩個極好的孩子，我相信他的判斷。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say you <b>trust that</b> something is true, you mean you hope and expect that it is true. 相信 (某事的真實性)","examples":["I trust you will take the earliest opportunity to make a full apology. 我相信你會抓住最早的機會來一次徹底的道歉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>trust</b> <b>in</b> someone is your belief that they are honest and sincere and will not deliberately do anything to harm you. 信任","examples":["He destroyed me and my trust in men. 他毀了我，也毀了我對男人的信任。","You've betrayed their trust. 你辜負了他們的信任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Trust</b> is also a noun. 託付","examples":["She was organizing and running a large household, a position of trust which was generously paid. 她那時正在照管一個大家庭，那是一個報酬優厚的要職。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>trust</b> is a financial arrangement in which a group of people or an organization keeps and invests money for someone. 信託","examples":["You could also set up a trust so the children can't spend any inheritance until they are a certain age. 你也可以建立信託，那樣孩子們到了一定的年齡以後才可以用任何遺產。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>trust</b> is a group of people or an organization that has control of an amount of money or property and invests it on behalf of other people or as a charity. 信託人員; 信託機構","examples":["He had set up two charitable trusts. 他已經成立了兩家慈善信託機構。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trust in</b> someone or something, you believe strongly in them, and do not doubt their powers or their good intentions. 信任","examples":["For a believer, replies to all the questions about life and work are far different because he trusts in God. 對一個信徒來說，對所有生活和工作問題的回答是大不一樣的，因為他相信上帝。"]}]}]},"user":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"使用者，使用者；（User）（土）烏塞爾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>user</b> is a person or thing that uses something such as a place, facility, product, or machine. 使用者; 使用物","examples":["Beach users have complained that the bikes are noisy. 去海灘的人已在抱怨那些腳踏車太吵。","...a regular user of the subway. …一個定期乘坐地鐵的人。"]}]}]},"underground":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在地（面）下；；隱蔽地，隱匿地；在地（面）下"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地（面）下的；秘密的，地下的；標新立異的，小眾的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鋪（電纜）於地下；；鋪（電纜）於地下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英> 地鐵；（反政府的）地下組織；先鋒派團體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>underground</b> is below the surface of the ground. 在地下","examples":["Solid low-level waste will be disposed of deep underground. 低放射性固體廢物將被棄置在地下深處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you go <b>underground</b>, you hide from the authorities or the police because your political ideas or activities are illegal. 秘密地; 在地下","examples":["After the violent clashes of 1981 they either went underground or left the country. 1981年的暴力衝突之後，他們要麼轉入地下了，要麼離開了這個國家。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Underground</b> is also an adjective. 地下的","examples":["...an underground parking garage for 2,100 vehicles. …一座能停放2100輛車的地下停車庫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Underground</b> groups and activities are secret because their purpose is to oppose the government and they are illegal. 秘密的; 地下的","examples":["...the underground Kashmir Liberation Front. 秘密的克什米爾解放陣線。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>underground</b> in a city is the railway system in which electric trains travel below the ground in tunnels. 地鐵","examples":["I don't travel on the underground late at night. 我深夜不坐地鐵。"]}]}]},"valley":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"山谷，溪谷，谷地；流域，河谷地區；（Valley）人名；<英>瓦利；<法>瓦萊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>valley</b> is a low stretch of land between hills, especially one that has a river flowing through it. 山谷","examples":["...a wooded valley set against the backdrop of Monte Rosa. …羅莎峰前一個林木繁茂的山谷。"]}]}]},"vacation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（學校的）假期，（法院的）休庭期；<美>休假，假期；騰出，辭去"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>度假"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vacation</b> is a period of time during which you relax and enjoy yourself away from home. 休假","examples":["They planned a late summer vacation in Europe. 他們計劃了一個夏末在歐洲的休假。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vacation</b> is a period of the year when schools, universities, and colleges are officially closed. (學校的) 假期","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a particular number of days' or weeks' <b>vacation</b>, you do not have to go to work for that number of days or weeks. (工作中的) 假期","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are vacationing</b> in a place away from home, you are on vacation there. 度假","examples":[]}]}]},"victory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勝利，成功，獲勝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>victory</b> is a success in a struggle, war, or competition. 勝利","examples":["Union leaders are heading for victory in their battle over workplace rights. 工會領袖們在爭取工作場所權利的鬥爭中正邁向勝利。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has won a <b>moral victory</b>, you mean that although they have officially lost a contest or dispute, they have succeeded in showing they are right about something. 精神勝利","examples":["She said her party had won a moral victory. 她說她的黨已贏得了精神上的勝利。"]}]}]},"violin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小提琴（一種弓弦樂器，為提琴家族中音區最高的成員，通常有四根弦，以琴弓擦弦發聲）；小提琴手；(Violin)（意）維奧林（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>violin</b> is a musical instrument. Violins are made of wood and have four strings. You play the violin by holding it under your chin and moving a bow across the strings. 小提琴","examples":["Lizzie used to play the violin. 莉齊過去常拉小提琴。"]}]}]},"video":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某個事件或場合的）錄影；（指方法）錄影；錄影帶；音樂錄影；<英>錄影機；影片播放軟體"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"電視的，影片的；影象的，畫面的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"錄下（電視節目）；（用攝像機）拍攝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>video</b> is a movie or television programme recorded on tape for people to watch on a television set. 錄影帶","examples":["...sports and exercise videos. …體育和運動錄影帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Video</b> is the system of recording movies and events on tape so that people can watch them on a television set. 錄影","examples":["She has watched the race on video. 她已觀看了比賽的錄影。","...manufacturers of audio and video equipment. …錄音和錄影裝置製造商。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>video</b> is a machine that you can use to record television programmes and play videotapes on a television set. 錄影機","examples":["Panasonic's Programme Director lets you program your video so easily! 松下的程式設定指南讓你如此輕鬆地設定自己的卡式錄影機！"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>video</b> a television programme or event, you record it on tape using video recorder or video camera, so that you can watch it later. 錄製","examples":[]}]}]},"value":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"價值；等值，等價，物有所值；重要性，有用性；重要特點，顯著特點；價值觀（values）；（數學中的）值；（音樂中的）時值（指音符的時間長度）；（詞或其他語言單位）確切意義；（色彩）明暗度"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"尊重，重視；給……估價，給……定價"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>value</b> of something such as a quality, attitude, or method is its importance or usefulness. If you place a particular <b>value</b> on something, that is the importance or usefulness you think it has. 重要性; 益處","examples":["The value of this work experience should not be underestimated. 這項工作經驗的重要性不應該被低估。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>value</b> of something is how much money it is worth. 價值","examples":["The value of his investment has risen by more than $50,000. 他的投資價值已經增長$50000多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>value</b> in certain expressions to say whether something is worth the money that it costs. For example, if something is <b>good value</b>, or if you get <b>good value</b> for your money when you buy something, then it is worth the money that it costs. (與價格相比的) 合算程度","examples":["We believe that is good value for money for our customers. 我們認為我們顧客的錢在那上面花得很值。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>values</b> of a person or group are the moral principles and beliefs that they think are important. 價值觀念","examples":["The countries of South Asia also share many common values. 南亞各國也有許多共同的價值觀念。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Value</b> is used after another noun when mentioning an important or noticeable feature about something. 特色","examples":["The script has lost all of its shock value over the intervening 24 years. 在這期間的24年中，該劇本已完全失去了它驚世駭俗的特色。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>of value</b>, it is useful or important. If it is <b>of no value</b>, it has no usefulness or importance. 重要的/不重要的","examples":["This weekend course will be of value to everyone interested in the Pilgrim Route. 這個週末課程對於每一個對朝聖路線感興趣的人來說都將是重要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>of value</b>, it is worth a lot of money. If it is <b>of no value</b>, it is worth very little money. 值錢的/不值錢的","examples":["...a brooch that is really of no value. …一枚根本不值錢的胸針。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>value</b> something or someone, you think that they are important and you appreciate them. 重視","examples":["I value the opinion of my husband and we agree on most things. 我重視我丈夫的意見，而且我們在大多數事情上看法一致。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When experts <b>value</b> something, they decide how much money it is worth. 為…估價","examples":["The school board valued the property at $130,000. 這所學校的董事會將這項財產估價為$130000。","I asked him to have my jewelry valued. 我請求他為我的珠寶估價。"]}]}]},"uniform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"制服，校服；<非正式>穿制服的警官；（某一群體的人穿的）典型服裝，特有服裝；（無線電通訊）字母 U 的程式碼"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全部相同的，始終如一的；制服式的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使一致；使穿制服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>uniform</b> is a special set of clothes which some people, for example soldiers or the police, wear to work in and which some children wear in school. 制服","examples":["The police wear dark blue uniforms. 警察穿深藍色制服。","Felipe was in uniform for the parade. 費利佩穿著遊行服裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"一致性","examples":["...the caramel that was used to maintain uniformity of colour in the brandy. …為保持白蘭地色澤一致而新增的焦糖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"相同性","examples":["...the dull uniformity of the houses. …那些房子的單調雷同。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>uniform</b>, it does not vary, but is even and regular throughout. 一致的","examples":["Cut down between the bones so that all the chops are of uniform size. 在骨頭之間砍削，使所有的排骨大小一致。","All flowing water, though it appears to be uniform, is actually divided into extensive inner surfaces, or layers, moving against one another. 所有流水儘管看起來是一樣的，實際上是分成了大量相互碰撞的內在表層。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a number of things as <b>uniform</b>, you mean that they are all the same. 同樣的","examples":["Along each wall stretched uniform green metal filing cabinets. 沿每堵牆擺放著清一色的綠色金屬檔案櫃。"]}]}]},"village":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鄉村，村莊；在鄉村的，鄉村的；村民；（城市中帶有村莊特點的）生活小區，居民區；<美>（有有限自治權的）小自治市；<澳新>高階城郊購物中心；（動物的）群落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>village</b> consists of a group of houses, together with other buildings such as a church and a school, in a country area. 村莊","examples":["He lives quietly in the country in a village near Lahti. 他在鄉下拉赫蒂附近的一個村莊裡過著平靜的生活。"]}]}]},"vocabulary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某人掌握或使用的）全部詞彙；（某一語言的）詞彙；（某個學科的）專業詞彙，術語；（尤指外語教科書中的）詞彙表；（美術、音樂等領域的）表現形式，表達手段"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>vocabulary</b> is the total number of words you know in a particular language. 詞彙量","examples":["His speech is immature, his vocabulary limited. 他講話不成熟，詞彙量也有限。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>vocabulary</b> of a language is all the words in it. 某一語言的總詞彙量","examples":["...a new word in the German vocabulary. …德語詞彙中的一個新詞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>vocabulary</b> of a subject is the group of words that are typically used when discussing it. (某學科的) 專門詞彙","examples":["...the vocabulary of natural science. …自然科學詞彙。"]}]}]},"voter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選民，選舉人，投票人；有投票權者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Voters</b> are people who have the legal right to vote in elections, or people who are voting in a particular election. 選民","examples":["The turnout was at least 62 percent of registered voters. 至少有62%的登記選民參加了投票。"]}]}]},"waist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腰，腰圍；（衣服的）腰部，腰身；船腰，飛機機身中部，（提琴、沙漏等的）中間細部，（黃蜂等的）細腰；<美>女襯衫，緊身胸衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>waist</b> is the middle part of your body where it narrows slightly above your hips. 腰部","examples":["Ricky kept his arm around her waist. 裡基摟著她的腰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>waist</b> of a garment such as a dress, coat, or pair of trousers is the part of it which covers the middle part of your body. (衣服的) 腰部","examples":["She tucked her thumbs into the waist of her trousers. 她把拇指插進褲腰裡。"]}]}]},"waitress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女服務員，女侍者"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"做女服務生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>waitress</b> is a woman who works in a restaurant, serving people food and drink. 女侍者","examples":[]}]}]},"waterfall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瀑布；瀑布似的東西"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（一種專案管理方法）瀑布式的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>waterfall</b> is a place where water flows over the edge of a steep, high cliff in hills or mountains, and falls into a pool below. 瀑布","examples":["...Angel Falls, the world's highest waterfall. …安赫爾瀑布，世界上最高的瀑布。"]}]}]},"volleyball":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"排球運動；排球（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Volleyball</b> is a game in which two teams hit a large ball with their hands back and forth over a high net. If you allow the ball to touch the ground, the other team wins a point. 排球","examples":[]}]}]},"wallet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錢包，皮夾；（裝檔案的）皮夾，塑膠夾；<古>（尤指商販和朝拜者用的）行囊，旅行袋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wallet</b> is a small flat folded case, usually made of leather or plastic, in which you can keep money and credit cards. 錢包","examples":[]}]}]},"waiter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"服務員，侍者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>waiter</b> is a man who works in a restaurant, serving people food and drink. 男侍者","examples":[]}]}]},"visitor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訪問者，參觀者；（網站的）瀏覽者；客隊隊員（visitors）；候鳥；<英>（大學或其他學術機構的）督察員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>visitor</b> is someone who is visiting a person or place. 訪問者","examples":["The other day we had some visitors from Switzerland. 前幾天我們接待了一些瑞士的來訪者。"]}]}]},"weekday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平日，普通日，工作日（週一至週五）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平日的，工作日的（常作定語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weekday</b> is any of the days of the week except Saturday and Sunday. 工作日 (指星期一至星期五的任何一天)","examples":["If you want to avoid the crowds, it's best to come on a weekday. 如果你想避開人流，最好在工作日來。"]}]}]},"watermelon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"西瓜（果實，亦可指食用的瓜瓤）；西瓜植株。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>watermelon</b> is a large, heavy fruit with green skin, pink flesh, and black seeds. 西瓜","examples":[]}]}]},"weapon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"武器，兵器，兇器；（用於應付困境的）工具，手段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"武裝，裝備"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weapon</b> is an object such as a gun, a knife, or a missile, which is used to kill or hurt people in a fight or a war. 武器","examples":["...nuclear weapons. …核武器。"]}]}]},"whale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鯨；<非正式>巨大的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>毆打，猛擊；捕鯨；使慘敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whales</b> are very large mammals that live in the sea. 鯨魚","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is having a whale of a time</b>, you mean that they are enjoying themselves very much. 玩得非常愉快","examples":["I had a whale of a time in Fargo. 我在法戈過得非常快樂。"]}]}]},"western":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"西方的，西部的；（Western）西方國家的（指與北美、西歐、北歐、南歐各國相關的）；美國西部的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（關於19世紀美國西部生活，尤指牛仔生活的）西部電影、西部小說；西方人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Western</b> means in or from the west of a region, state, or country. 西部的","examples":["...hand-made rugs from Western and Central Asia. …來自西亞和中亞的手工地毯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Western</b> is used to describe things, people, ideas, or ways of life that come from or are associated with the United States, Canada, and the countries of Western, Northern, and Southern Europe. 西方國家的 (指與北美、西歐、北歐、南歐各國相關的)","examples":["Mexico had the support of the big western governments. 墨西哥得到了西方大國政府的支援。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>western</b> is a book or movie about life in the western United States and territories in the nineteenth century, especially the lives of cowboys. (有關19世紀美國西部的生活，尤指牛仔生活的) 西部小說; 西部影片","examples":["John Agar starred in westerns, war films and low-budget science fiction pictures. 約翰·阿加出演過西部片、戰爭片和低投入的科幻片。"]}]}]},"width":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寬度，廣度；（布料等）按尺寸剪裁的材料；（游泳池的）池寬；寬闊，寬大；整幅的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>width</b> of something is the distance it measures from one side or edge to the other. 寬度","examples":["Measure the full width of the window. 測量一下窗戶的總寬度。","The road was reduced to 18 ft in width by adding parking bays. 這條路增加了停車區域後，寬度減少為18英尺。"]}]}]},"vote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投票選舉，投票表決；投票評選；（透過投票）決定給予（資助），同意提供（款項）；表明，公認（某事好或壞）；投票同意；建議，主張"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"選票，票；投票，表決；（選舉中的）選票總數（the vote）；選舉權，表決權；投票結果，表決結果；投票者，選民（the vote）；特定投票群體，特定選民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vote</b> is a choice made by a particular person or group in a meeting or an election. 選票","examples":["He walked to the local polling place to cast his vote. 他走到當地的投票點去投票。","Mr. Reynolds was re-elected by 102 votes to 60. 雷諾茲先生以102票對60票再次當選。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>vote</b> is an occasion when a group of people make a decision by each person indicating his or her choice. The choice that most people support is accepted by the group. 投票表決","examples":["Why do you think we should have a vote on that? 你為什麼認為我們應該對那件事進行投票表決？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>vote</b> is the total number of votes or voters in an election, or the number of votes received or cast by a particular group. 投票總數; 得票總數","examples":["Opposition parties won about fifty-five percent of the vote. 反對黨贏得大約55％的選票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>the</b> <b>vote</b> in an election, or have <b>a</b> <b>vote</b> in a meeting, you have the legal right to indicate your choice. 選舉權","examples":["Before that, women did not have a vote at all. 在那之前，婦女根本就沒有選舉權。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"投票","examples":["Voting began about two hours ago. 投票開始於約兩個小時前。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>vote</b>, you indicate your choice officially at a meeting or in an election, for example, by raising your hand or writing on a piece of paper. 投票; 表決","examples":["Two-thirds of the national electorate had the chance to vote in these elections. 全國2/3的選民有機會在這些選舉中投票。","Nearly two-thirds of this group voted for Buchanan. 這一組幾乎2/3的人將票投給了布坎南。","The residents of Leningrad voted to restore the city's original name of St. Petersburg. 列寧格勒的居民投票贊成恢復該市原來的名字聖彼得堡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>vote</b> a particular political party or leader, or <b>vote</b> <b>yes</b> or <b>no</b>, you make that choice with the vote that you have. 投票支援","examples":["52.5% of those questioned said they'd vote Republican. 52.5%的受訪者說他們將投票支援共和黨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>vote</b> someone a particular title, they choose that person to have that title. 投票授予…稱號","examples":["His class voted him the man \"who had done the most for Yale.\" 他所在的班級投票授予他“耶魯最大貢獻者”稱號。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>vote with</b> your <b>feet</b>, you show that you do not support something by leaving the place where it is happening or leaving the organization that is supporting it. (以離去或退出的方式) 反對","examples":["Thousands of citizens are already voting with their feet, and leaving the country. 成千上萬的公民已表明了他們的反對意見，要離開這個國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say, for example, \"<b>I vote</b> <b>that</b> we go\" or \"<b>I vote</b> we stay,\" you are suggesting that you should go or stay. 我建議","examples":["I vote that we all go to Houston immediately. 我建議我們都馬上去休斯敦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>One man one vote</b> or <b>one person one vote</b> is a system of voting in which every person in a group or country has the right to cast their vote, and in which each individual's vote is counted and has equal value. 一人一票制","examples":["Mr. Gould called for a move toward \"one man one vote.\" 古爾德先生要求向“一人一票”制邁出一步。"]}]}]},"whisper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"耳語，低語，小聲說；（私下或秘密地）傳說（某事），謠傳；（樹葉）發沙沙聲，（風）發颯颯聲，（水）發潺潺聲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"耳語（聲），低語（聲），私語（聲）；沙沙聲，颯颯聲，潺潺聲；傳聞，謠言；蛛絲馬跡，暗示；少許，微量；少量資訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>whisper</b>, you say something very quietly, using your breath rather than your throat, so that only one person can hear you. 悄聲說出; 悄聲說","examples":["\"Keep your voice down,\" I whispered. “小聲點，”我悄聲說。","She sat on Rossi's knee as he whispered in her ear. 她坐在羅西的膝蓋上，羅西在對她嚅嚅耳語。","He whispered the message to David. 他悄聲把訊息告訴了戴維。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whisper</b> is also a noun. 悄聲說話","examples":["Men were talking in whispers in every office. 男人們在每個辦公室裡悄聲交談著。"]}]}]},"wave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"揮手；揮手示意；揮舞，揮動；飄揚，擺動，搖晃；使（頭髮）略呈波形；（威脅地）舉起（某物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"海浪；大海（the waves）；（活動、行為的）爆發，浪潮；湧現的人（或物）；揮手；波，波狀運動；（頭髮的）捲曲；波浪形；（地震、爆炸的）衝擊波；人浪（the wave）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wave</b> or <b>wave</b> your hand, you move your hand from side to side in the air, usually in order to say hello or goodbye to someone. 揮 (手以示意)","examples":["Jessica caught sight of Lois and waved to her. 傑茜卡看到洛伊絲，向她揮了揮手。","He grinned, waved, and said, \"Hi!\" 他咧嘴笑笑，揮揮手，說道：“嗨！”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wave</b> someone away or <b>wave</b> them on, you make a movement with your hand to indicate that they should move in a particular direction. 揮手 (示意某人離開、前進等)","examples":["Leshka waved him away with a show of irritation. 廖什卡生氣地揮手示意他離開。","He waited for a policeman to stop the traffic and wave the people on. 他等著一位警察來讓車輛停下，揮手讓眾人前行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>wave</b> something, you hold it up and move it rapidly from side to side. 揮舞","examples":["Hospital staff were outside to welcome him, waving flags and applauding. 醫院工作人員在院外迎接他，一邊揮舞旗幟一邊鼓掌。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wave</b> is also a noun. 揮 (手)","examples":["Steve stopped him with a wave of the hand. 史蒂夫把手一揮，制止了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wave</b> is a raised mass of water on the surface of water, especially the sea, which is caused by the wind or by tides making the surface of the water rise and fall. 波浪; (尤指) 海浪","examples":["...the sound of the waves breaking on the shore. …波浪拍打海岸的聲響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone's hair has <b>waves</b>, it curves slightly instead of being straight. (頭髮的) 波浪卷; 鬈曲","examples":["Her blue eyes shone and caught the light, and so did the platinum waves in her hair. 她藍色的眼睛閃閃發光，白金色的波浪髮捲也閃閃發光。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>wave</b> is a sudden increase in heat or energy that spreads out from an earthquake or explosion. (地震、爆炸的) 衝擊波","examples":["The shock waves of the earthquake were felt in Teheran. 在德黑蘭感覺到了地震的震波。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Waves</b> are the form in which things such as sound, light, and radio signals travel. (光、聲、無線電等的) 波","examples":["Regular repeating actions such as sound waves, light waves, or radio waves have a certain frequency, or number of waves per second. 有規律的重複活動如聲波、光波、無線電波都有一個特定的頻率，或者說是每秒的波動次數。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you refer to a <b>wave</b> <b>of</b> a particular feeling, you mean that it increases quickly and becomes very intense, and then often decreases again. (情緒的) 波動","examples":["She felt a wave of panic, but forced herself to leave the room calmly. 她感到一陣驚慌，但是強迫自己鎮靜地離開了房間。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>wave</b> is a sudden increase in a particular activity or type of behaviour, especially an undesirable or unpleasant one. (活動或行為的) 突然爆發; 浪潮","examples":["...the current wave of violence. …當前的暴力浪潮。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>waves</b>, it moves gently from side to side or up and down. 飄揚; 擺動","examples":["...grass and flowers waving in the wind. …隨風擺動的花草。"]}]}]},"winner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獲勝的人（或隊、動物等），優勝者；（體育比賽中）致勝的一分，制勝的進球；<非正式>可能成功的人（或事物），極好的人（或事物），成功的人（或事物）；獲益者，贏家；（橋牌）能贏的牌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>winner</b> of a prize, race, or competition is the person, animal, or thing that wins it. 獲勝者","examples":["She will present the trophies to the award winners. 她將給獲勝者頒獎。"]}]}]},"wheel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輪子，車輪；汽車（wheels）；機輪，齒輪，傳動輪；（汽車、輪船等的）方向盤，轉向盤；系統，機構；輪狀物；輪盤（一種旋轉的賭具）；輪；重要人物，大亨；輪式機械（或器具）；旋轉，迴旋；（詩歌等的）疊句；<史>（用於牽拉或分裂肢體的）輪式刑車（the wheel）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"推，拉（帶輪運輸工具）；用有輪之物推動（或拉動、移動）……；（鳥或飛機）盤旋；（使）迅速轉身，猛然轉身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>wheels</b> of a vehicle are the circular objects that are attached underneath it and that enable it to move along the ground. 車輪","examples":["The car wheels spun and slipped on some oil on the road. 小汽車的車輪在路面的油跡上空轉打了滑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wheel</b> is a circular object that forms a part of a machine, usually a moving part. 機輪","examples":["The wheels are usually fairly large. 該機輪通常相當大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The wheel</b> of a car or other vehicle is the circular object that is used to steer it. <b>The wheel</b> is used in expressions to talk about who is driving a vehicle. For example, if someone is <b>at the wheel</b> or <b>behind the wheel</b> of a car, they are driving it. 方向盤","examples":["My co-pilot suddenly grabbed the wheel. 我的副駕駛突然搶過了方向盤。","Curtis got behind the wheel and they started back toward the cottage. 柯蒂斯開車，他們啟程返回小屋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"People talk about <b>the wheels of</b> an organization or system to mean the way in which it operates. (組織或系統的) 運作方式","examples":["He knows the wheels of administration turn slowly. 他知道行政機構運作緩慢。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wheel</b> an object that has wheels somewhere, you push it along. 推 (帶輪子的物體)","examples":["He wheeled his bike into the alley at the side of the house. 他把腳踏車推進了房屋一側的衚衕裡。"]}]}]},"wolf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狼；色狼，色鬼；（喻）殘忍兇狠的人；<美，非正式>同性戀者；狼音，不諧和音，粗厲音"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"狼吞虎嚥地吃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wolf</b> is a wild animal that looks like a large dog. 狼","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>wolfs</b> their food, they eat it all very quickly and greedily. 狼吞虎嚥","examples":["Hotels were full of rich people wolfing expensive meals. 酒店滿是狼吞虎嚥昂貴飯菜的有錢人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wolf down</b> means the same as . 狼吞虎嚥","examples":["He wolfed down the rest of the biscuit and cheese. 他狼吞虎嚥地吃下了剩餘的餅乾和乳酪。"]}]}]},"wool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羊毛，動物毛；毛線，絨線；毛料，毛織物；金屬（或礦）絲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wool</b> is the hair that grows on sheep and on some other animals. (羊等動物的) 毛","examples":["A new invention means sheep do not have to be sheared – the wool just falls off. 一項新的發明意味著羊不必被剪毛–羊毛就會脫落下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wool</b> is a material made from animal's wool that is used to make things such as clothes, blankets, and carpets. 毛料","examples":["...a wool overcoat. …一件毛料大衣。"]}]}]},"wild":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（動植物）自然生長的，野生的；（土地）無人煙的，未開墾的；（人）未開化的，野蠻的；不受控制的，放蕩的；暴風雨的，狂暴的；（做事或說話）輕率的，缺乏根據的；激動人心的；滿腔熱情的，十分熱衷的；感情強烈的（尤指生氣、高興或激動）；（表情、外表等）走神的，不專注的；特別的，怪異的；（紙牌）百搭的；嘈雜混亂的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"自然地，不受控制地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"偏遠地區，人煙稀少的地區；自然環境，野生狀態"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<西印度> 野蠻對待，殘酷對待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wild</b> animals or plants live or grow in natural surroundings and are not taken care of by people. (動物或植物) 野生的","examples":["We saw two more wild cats creeping toward us in the darkness. 我們看見還有兩隻野貓在黑暗中向我們爬來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wild</b> land is natural and is not used by people. 荒蕪的","examples":["...a wild area of woods and lakes. …一片荒蕪的森林和湖泊區域。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Wild</b> is used to describe the weather or the sea when it is stormy. (天氣或海面) 狂風暴雨的","examples":["The wild weather did not deter some people from taking an unseasonable dip in the sea. 狂風暴雨的天氣並沒有使一些不合時宜地到海里游泳的人卻步。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Wild</b> behaviour is uncontrolled, excited, or energetic. (行為) 狂熱的","examples":["The children are wild with joy. 孩子們欣喜若狂。","As George himself came on stage they went wild. 當喬治本人登上舞臺的時候，他們都發狂了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe someone or their behaviour as <b>wild</b>, you mean that they behave in a very uncontrolled way. (指人或其行為) 瘋狂的","examples":["The house is in a mess after a wild party. 一次瘋狂的聚會之後，房子裡一片狼藉。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>wild</b> idea is unusual or extreme. A <b>wild</b> guess is one that you make without much thought. 不尋常的 (想法); 胡亂的 (猜測)","examples":["Browning's prediction is no better than a wild guess. 布朗寧的預言只不過是胡亂猜測而已。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The wilds</b> of a place are the natural areas that are far away from cities and towns. 荒野","examples":["They went canoeing in the wilds of Canada. 他們在加拿大的荒野地區劃獨木舟。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狂熱地","examples":["As she finished each song, the crowd clapped wildly. 她每唱完一首歌，人群就狂熱地鼓起掌來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"瘋狂地","examples":["Five people were injured as Reynolds slashed out wildly with a kitchen knife. 五個人因雷諾茲拿著菜刀瘋狂亂砍而受傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"不尋常地; 胡亂地","examples":["\"Thirteen?\" he guessed wildly. “十三？”他胡亂猜道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Animals that live <b>in the wild</b> live in a free and natural state and are not taken care of by people. 處於野生狀態","examples":["Fewer than a thousand giant pandas still live in the wild. 不到1000只的大熊貓還處於野生狀態。"]}]}]},"wing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鳥、昆蟲或蝙蝠的）翅膀，翼；（飛機的）機翼；（建築的）側翼，耳房，廂房，配樓；（舞臺的）側面，側翼（the wings）；（組織或政黨的）派系，翼；<英>（汽車等的）擋泥板，翼子板；（運動場的）邊沿；飛行徽章；禽類翅膀，（尤指供食用的）雞翅；空軍聯隊；（鳥或昆蟲）在飛行中；（蝙蝠或翼手龍的）翼膜；翅膀（指飛翔的能力、手段或快速）；（剖）翼狀部，翼狀結構，翅狀部；（植）翼瓣，翅，氣囊；側翼部隊；一群鴴（鳥）；（冰球、足球等運動中的）邊鋒，側翼隊員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"飛，飛行；被迅速送往；擦傷（尤指手臂或翅膀）；用力扔（某物）；射傷（鳥的）翅膀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>wings</b> of a bird or insect are the two parts of its body that it uses for flying. 翅膀","examples":["The bird flapped its wings furiously. 那隻鳥使勁地拍打著翅膀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>wings</b> of an aeroplane are the long flat parts sticking out of its side which support it while it is flying. 機翼","examples":["The plane made one pass, dipped its wings, then circled back. 飛機掠過去，垂下機翼，然後盤旋而回。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>wing</b> of a building is a part of it that sticks out from the main part. (建築的) 側翼","examples":["We were given an office in the empty west wing. 我們在空蕩蕩的西側廳得到了一間辦公室。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>wing</b> of an organization, especially a political organization, is a group within it which has a particular function or particular beliefs. (尤指政治組織中有某種作用或信仰的) 派系","examples":["...the military wing of the African National Congress. ...非洲國民大會的武裝派。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a theatre, <b>the wings</b> are the sides of the stage that are hidden from the audience by curtains or scenery. (舞臺被簾幕或佈景遮擋的) 側面","examples":["Most nights I watched the start of the play from the wings. 大多數晚上，我都從舞臺的側面觀看演出的開場。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is waiting <b>in the wings</b>, you mean that they are ready and waiting for an opportunity to take action. 準備就緒","examples":["There are now more than 20 big companies waiting in the wings to take over some of its business. 現在有二十多家大公司正等著隨時接手它的一些業務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>spread</b> your <b>wings</b>, you do something new and somewhat difficult or move to a new place, because you feel more confident in your abilities than you used to and you want to gain wider experience. (在陌生領域或到新的地方) 施展身手","examples":["I led a very confined life in my village so I suppose that I wanted to spread my wings. 我在自己的村莊裡過著非常封閉的生活，所以我覺得我想要出去施展一下身手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone <b>under</b> your <b>wing</b>, you look after them, help them, and protect them. 把某人置於自己的保護之下","examples":["Her boss took her under his wing after fully realizing her potential. 她的老闆充分意識到她的潛力後就把她招到自己的旗下。"]}]}]},"wire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金屬絲，金屬線；電線，導線；隱蔽式電子收聽器；<美>電報；<美>（賽馬）起跑線，終點線（the wire）；鐵絲網（the wire）；用金屬絲制的，用金屬線制的；<美>通訊社"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……接上電線，接通（電源）；（用電線）接通，連線；電匯（錢款）；發電報給（某人）；用金屬線固定（或加固）；給……安裝竊聽器；用金屬網誘捕（動物）；（槌球）在拱門邊阻擋（球，射球，選手）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wire</b> is a long thin piece of metal that is used to fasten things or to carry electric current. (用以綁東西或導電的) 金屬絲","examples":["...fine copper wire. …細銅絲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wire</b> is a cable that carries power or signals from one place to another. 電線; 電纜","examples":["I ripped out the telephone wire that ran through to his office. 我拔掉連線到他辦公室的電話線。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wire</b> something such as a building or piece of equipment, you put wires inside it so that electricity or signals can pass into or through it. 在…裡裝設電線","examples":["...learning to wire and plumb the house herself. …她學會自己在房子裡裝設電線和水管。","Each of the homes has a security system and is wired for cable television. 每一家都有安全系統，並裝設了有線電視線。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wire up</b> means the same as . 在…裡裝設電線","examples":["Wire the thermometers up to trigger off an alarm bell if the temperature drops. 把溫度計的電線連線上，當溫度下降時，就會觸發警報。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something goes <b>to the wire</b>, it continues until the last possible moment. 直至最後一刻","examples":["Negotiators again worked right down to the wire to reach an agreement. 談判者們再次一直工作到最後達成協議為止。"]}]}]},"youth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青少年時期；早期，初期；小夥子；（總稱）青年人；青春，朝氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>youth</b> is the period of their life during which they are a child, before they are a fully mature adult. 年輕時期","examples":["In my youth my ambition had been to be an inventor. 在我年輕時我的抱負曾是當一名發明家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Youth</b> is the quality or state of being young. 年輕","examples":["The team is now a good mixture of experience and youth. 這支隊伍現在是經驗與年輕的一個良好結合體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Journalists often refer to young men as <b>youths</b>, especially when they are reporting that the young men have caused trouble. 年輕人 (尤用於新聞報道中指惹了麻煩的年輕人)","examples":["A 17-year-old youth was arrested yesterday. 一個17歲的年輕人昨天被逮捕了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>youth</b> are young people considered as a group. 青年人","examples":["He represents the opinions of the youth of today. 他代表瞭如今的青年人的意見。"]}]}]},"wound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（刀、槍或其他武器所致的）創傷，傷口；（感情或名譽的）損害，痛苦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（武器或其他利器）傷害，使受傷；（在感情上）使受創傷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"蜿蜒；使喘不過氣；纏繞（wind 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wound</b> is the past tense and past participle of <b>wind</b> (wind)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wound</b> is damage to part of your body, especially a cut or a hole in your flesh, which is caused by a gun, knife, or other weapon. 傷口","examples":["The wound is healing nicely and the patient is healthy. 傷口在很好地癒合，病人情況良好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The wounded</b> are people who are wounded. 受傷的人","examples":["Hospitals said they could not cope with the wounded. 各醫院說他們不能處理傷員。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a weapon or something sharp <b>wounds</b> you, it damages your body. 使受傷","examples":["A bomb exploded in a hotel, killing six people and wounding another five. 一顆炸彈在一家旅館爆炸，致6人死亡、另5人受傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are wounded</b> by what someone says or does, your feelings are deeply hurt. 傷害 (感情)","examples":["He was deeply wounded by his son's comments. 他被他兒子的評論深深地刺傷了。"]}]}]},"zebra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"斑馬；斑馬紋蝶；<南非>斑馬魚，重牙鯛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>zebra</b> is an African wild horse that has black and white stripes. 斑馬","examples":[]}]}]},"wonder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"想知道，好奇，琢磨；不知是否（用於提問或禮貌地提出請求）；感到疑惑，（對…）感到不安；感到驚訝，覺得驚奇"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚訝，驚歎；奇觀，奇蹟；令人驚訝的事物，令人難以置信的事物；能人，奇才，有特效的東西"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，靈驗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wonder</b> about something, you think about it, either because it interests you and you want to know more about it, or because you are worried or suspicious about it. 想知道","examples":["I wondered what that noise was. 我想知道那噪音是什麼。","\"He claims to be her father,\" said Max. \"We've been wondering about him.\" “他聲稱是她的父親，”馬克斯說，“我們一直想知道是否如此。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wonder</b> <b>at</b> something, you are very surprised about it or think about it in a very surprised way. 對…感到驚訝","examples":["I could only wonder at how far this woman had come. 我只能對這名婦女遠道而來感到驚訝。","I wonder you don't feel it too. 我驚訝於你也感覺不到它。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that it is a <b>wonder</b> <b>that</b> something happened, you mean that it is very surprising and unexpected. 奇事","examples":["It's a wonder that it took almost ten years. 花了幾乎十年時間，真是樁奇事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wonder</b> is a feeling of great surprise and pleasure that you have, for example, when you see something that is very beautiful, or when something happens that you thought was impossible. 驚奇","examples":["\"That's right!\" Bobby exclaimed in wonder. \"How did you remember that?\" “對呀！”鮑勃驚奇地喊道，“你怎麼記得那件事？”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>wonder</b> is something that causes people to feel great surprise or admiration. 奇蹟","examples":["...a lecture on the wonders of space and space exploration. …一個關於太空奇蹟和太空探險的講座。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer, for example, to a young man as a <b>wonder</b> boy, or to a new product as a <b>wonder</b> drug, you mean that they are believed by many people to be very good or very effective. 神奇的","examples":["Mickelson was hailed as the wonder boy of American golf. 米克爾森被稱頌為美國高爾夫球界的神奇男孩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I wonder</b>\" if you want to be very polite when you are asking someone to do something, or when you are asking them for their opinion or for information. 不知 (表示禮貌地提問或求助)","examples":["I was just wondering if you could help me. 不知你是否能幫助我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say \"<b>no wonder</b>,\" \"<b>little wonder</b>,\" or \"<b>small wonder</b>,\" you mean that something is not surprising. 難怪 (表示某事不足為奇)","examples":["No wonder my brother wasn't feeling well. 難怪我兄弟當時感覺不舒服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say \"<b>No wonder</b>\" when you find out the reason for something that has been puzzling you for some time. (表示弄清了困惑已久的事) 難怪","examples":["Brad was Jane's brother! No wonder he reminded me so much of her! 布拉德是簡的哥哥！難怪他很多方面使我想起她！"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing <b>works wonders</b> or <b>does wonders</b>, you mean that they have a very good effect on something. 產生奇效","examples":["A few moments of relaxation can work wonders. 短暫的放鬆能產生奇效。"]}]}]},"yard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碼（長度單位，等於 3 英尺或 0.91 米）；（尤指沙等建築材料的）平方碼，立方碼；（某種用途的）區域，場地；（小屋的）後院，院子；<北美> 庭院花園；<西印度> 包括房子的庭院；<南非> 出租庭院；城市小區；帆桁；<美，非正式> 100美元，百元鈔票；<英，非正式> 蘇格蘭場（the Yard）；（尤指牙買加僑民之間所指的）祖國，牙買加（Yard）；<美> 庭院花園"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美> 把（木材）堆放（或運至）場內；把（家畜）驅入圈欄；（麋鹿）冬令集居"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yard</b> is a unit of length equal to thirty-six inches or approximately 91.4 centimetres. 碼","examples":["The incident took place about 500 yards from where he was standing. 該事件發生在距他所站位置約五百碼處。","...a long narrow strip of linen two or three yards long. …一條兩三碼長的細長亞麻布條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>yard</b> is a flat area of concrete or stone that is next to a building and often has a wall around it. 院子","examples":["I saw him standing in the yard. 我看見他站在院子裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a large open area where a particular type of work is done as a <b>yard</b>. (進行某種作業的) 場地","examples":["...a rail yard. …一個鐵路調車場。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>yard</b> is a piece of land next to someone's house, with grass and plants growing in it. 庭院","examples":["He dug a hole in our yard on Edgerton Avenue to plant a maple tree when I was born. 他在我出生時在埃傑頓大道我家的院子裡挖了個坑，種了一棵楓樹。"]}]}]},"acceptable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可接受的，（大多數人）認同的；合意的，令人滿意的；尚可的，勉強的；可容忍的，可允許的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Acceptable</b> activities and situations are those that most people approve of or consider to be normal. 可接受的","examples":["It is becoming more acceptable for women to drink. 女性飲酒越來越為人接受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>acceptable</b> <b>to</b> someone, they agree to consider it, use it, or allow it to happen. 可接受的","examples":["They have thrashed out a compromise formula acceptable to Moscow. 他們反覆討論確定了一個莫斯科可以接受的妥協方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>acceptable</b>, you mean that it is good enough or fairly good. 足夠好的; 相當好的","examples":["On the far side of the street was a restaurant that looked acceptable. 在這條街的另一頭有家餐館看起來還可以。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可接受性","examples":["This assumption played a considerable part in increasing the social acceptability of divorce. 這種假設對增加社會對離婚的接納起了相當大的作用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"足夠好地; 相當好地","examples":["...a method that provides an acceptably accurate solution to a problem. …一個可以足以準確地解決問題的方法。"]}]}]},"worth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"價值……的，值……錢的；值得的，具有……價值的；擁有……財產的；（尤指合同）毫無價值的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"價格，價值；重要性，作用；能用（一個星期、一個月等）的東西"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"價值……；值得"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>worth</b> a particular amount of money, it can be sold for that amount or is considered to have that value. 值…錢","examples":["A local jeweler says the pearl is worth at least $500. 一位本地珠寶商說這顆珍珠至少值$500。","His mother inherited a business worth 15,000 dollars a year. 他的母親繼承了一個每年盈利15000美元的商行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>worth</b> having, you mean that it is pleasant or useful, and therefore a good thing to have. 值得 (擁有)","examples":["He's decided to get a look at the house and see if it might be worth buying. 他已經決定去看一下那所房子，看看是否值得買。","Most things worth having never come easy. 大多數值得擁有的東西一向來之不易。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>worth</b> a particular action, or if an action is <b>worth</b> doing, it is considered to be important enough for that action. 值得 (做…)","examples":["I am spending a lot of money and time on this boat, but it is worth it? 我正把大量的金錢和時間花在這艘船上，但這樣做值得。","This restaurant is well worth a visit. 這家飯店很值得光顧。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in quant.","pos_name":"與數量詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worth</b> combines with amounts of money, so that when you talk about a particular amount of money<b>'s</b> <b>worth of</b> something, you mean the quantity of it that you can buy for that amount of money. 價值…的","examples":["I went and bought about six dollars' worth of potato chips. 我去買了價值約六美元的土豆片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Worth</b> combines with time expressions, so you can use <b>worth</b> when you are saying how long an amount of something will last. For example, a week's <b>worth of</b> food is the amount of food that will last you for a week. 可維持 (一段時間) 的東西","examples":["You've got three years' worth of research money to do what you want with. 你有可維持3年的研究經費來做你想做的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worth</b> is also a pronoun. 價值…的","examples":["Gold reserves had fallen to less than $3 billion worth. 黃金儲備已經降價至30億美元以下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Worth</b> is also a pronoun. 可維持 (一段時間) 的…","examples":["There's really not very much food down there. About two weeks' worth. 那裡真的沒什麼食物了。大約能維持兩週的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an action or activity is <b>worth</b> someone's <b>while</b>, it will be helpful, useful, or enjoyable for them if they do it, even though it requires some effort. 值得 (花某人精力) 的","examples":["It might be worth your while to go to court and ask for the agreement to be changed. 你花精力上法庭請求更改協議可能會是值得的。"]}]}]},"additional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"附加的，額外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Additional</b> things are extra things apart from the ones already present. 額外的","examples":["The U.S. is sending additional troops to the region. 美國正在往該地區派遣額外的部隊。"]}]}]},"accurate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"準確的，精確的；（工具，方法）精密的；正確無誤的；（武器、投擲）精準的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Accurate</b> information, measurements, and statistics are correct to a very detailed level. An <b>accurate</b> instrument is able to give you information of this kind. 精確的","examples":["Police have stressed that this is the most accurate description of the killer to date. 警方已強調這是到目前為止對這名殺人犯最精確的描述。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>accurate</b> statement or account gives a true or fair judgment of something. 準確的","examples":["Stalin gave an accurate assessment of the utility of nuclear weapons. 斯大林對核武器的效用作了一個準確的評估。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>accurate</b> to describe the results of someone's actions when they do or copy something correctly or exactly. 正確無誤的","examples":["We require grammar and spelling to be accurate. 我們要求語法與拼寫正確無誤。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>accurate</b> weapon or throw reaches the exact point or target that it was intended to reach. You can also describe a person as <b>accurate</b> if they fire a weapon or throw something in this way. 精準的","examples":["His throws were long, hard and accurate, as always. 像往常一樣，他的投擲遠、有力又精準。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精確地","examples":["The test can accurately predict what a bigger explosion would do. 這項測試能精確地預測一場更大的爆炸可能產生的後果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"準確地","examples":["What many people mean by the word \"power\" could be more accurately described as \"control.\" 許多人對“權力”這個詞的理解可以更為準確地用“控制”來形容。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"精準地","examples":["He hit the golf ball powerfully and accurately. 他有力而準確地擊中了那個高爾夫球。"]}]}]},"actual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真實的，實際的，現實的；（用於對比主次方面）真正的；現存的，當前的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>actual</b> to emphasize that you are referring to something real or genuine. 真實的","examples":["The segments are filmed using either local actors or the actual people involved. 這些片段是用當地的演員或真實的當事人拍攝的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>actual</b> to contrast the important aspect of something with a less important aspect. 實際的","examples":["She had compiled pages of notes, but she had not yet got down to doing the actual writing. 她已輯錄了多篇筆記，但她還沒有著手實際的寫作。"]}]}]},"advanced":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"先進的；高階的，高等的；晚期的，狀況不佳的；高齡的；新提出（尚未被廣泛接受）的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"行進；發展，進步；預付（advance 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advanced</b> system, method, or design is modern and has been developed from an earlier version of the same thing. 先進的 (系統、方法、設計等)","examples":["...a superpower equipped with the most advanced military technology in the world. …一個擁有世界上最先進的軍事技術的超級大國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A country that is <b>advanced</b> has reached a high level of industrial or technological development. (國家) 發達的","examples":["Agricultural productivity remained low by comparison with advanced countries like the United States. 與美國等發達國家相比，農業生產率仍很低。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>advanced</b> student has already learned the basic facts of a subject and is doing more difficult work. An <b>advanced</b> course of study is designed for such students. 高階的 (學生、課程)","examples":["The course is suitable for beginners and advanced students. 該課程適合初學者和高階學生。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is at an <b>advanced</b> stage or level is at a late stage of development. 晚期的","examples":["Medicare is available to victims of advanced kidney disease. 晚期腎病患者可獲得醫療保障。"]}]}]},"apparent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"顯而易見的，易懂的；貌似的，表面上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apparent</b> situation, quality, or feeling seems to exist, although you cannot be certain that it does exist. 未必真實的","examples":["I was a bit depressed by our apparent lack of progress. 我對我們表面上的缺乏進展感到有點沮喪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>apparent</b> to you, it is clear and obvious to you. 明顯的","examples":["It has been apparent that in other areas standards have held up well. 顯然在其他領域標準保持得良好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>for no apparent reason</b>, you cannot understand why it happens. 莫名其妙地","examples":["The person may become dizzy for no apparent reason. 此人可能會莫名其妙地變得頭暈目眩。"]}]}]},"attractive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"吸引人的，有吸引力的；（人）迷人的，有魅力的；值得考慮的，值得做的；（與）引力（有關）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person who is <b>attractive</b> is pleasant to look at. 有魅力的","examples":["She's a very attractive woman. 她是一個非常有魅力的女人。","I thought he was very attractive and obviously very intelligent. 我認為他很有魅力，而且顯然也很聰明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>attractive</b> has a pleasant appearance or sound. 外表漂亮的; 聲音優美的","examples":["The apartment was small but attractive, if rather shabby. 這套公寓不大卻滿漂亮，儘管已相當陳舊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe something as <b>attractive</b> when it seems worth having or doing. 有誘惑力的","examples":["Smoking is still attractive to many young people who see it as glamorous. 吸菸仍然對很多年輕人有誘惑力，他們將之視為魅力標誌。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"魅力","examples":["Most of us would maintain that physical attractiveness does not play a major part in how we react to the people we meet. 我們中大多數人都會認為，外表的魅力在我們待人接物方面並不起主要作用。"]}]}]},"automatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自動的；必然的；無意識的，不假思索的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"自動換擋汽車；自動武器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>automatic</b> machine or device is one that has controls that enable it to perform a task without needing to be constantly operated by a person. <b>Automatic</b> methods and processes involve the use of such machines. (機器或裝置) 自動的","examples":["Modern trains have automatic doors. 現代火車都有自動門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>automatic</b> weapon is one that keeps firing shots until you stop pulling the trigger. (武器) 自動的","examples":["Three gunmen with automatic rifles opened fire. 3名手持自動步槍的歹徒開了火。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>automatic</b> action is one that you do without thinking about it. (行動) 無意識的","examples":["All of the automatic body functions, even breathing, are affected. 所有無意識的身體功能，甚至呼吸，都受到影響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Automatic</b> is also a noun. 自動槍","examples":["He drew his automatic and began running in the direction of the sounds. 他拔出自動槍，朝發出聲音的方向跑去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>automatic</b> is a car in which the gears change automatically as the car's speed increases or decreases. 自動換檔汽車","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無意識地","examples":["You will automatically wake up after this length of time. 你將在這段時間之後自然醒來。"]}]}]},"available":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可用的，可獲得的；有空的，有閒暇的；未婚的，單身的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something you want or need is <b>available</b>, you can find it or obtain it. 可獲得的","examples":["Since 1978, the amount of money available to buy books has fallen by 17%. 自1978年以來，可供買書的錢已減少了17%。","The shop has about 500 autographed copies of the book available for purchase. 這家書店有大約500本該書的簽名版本可供購買。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>available</b> is not busy and is therefore free to talk to you or to do a particular task. 有空的","examples":["Mr. Leach is on holiday and was not available for comment. 利奇先生在休假，沒空作評論。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可獲得性","examples":["...the easy availability of guns. …獲取槍支的容易性。"]}]}]},"aware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"知道的，明白的；察覺到的，意識到的；有……意識的，有……知識的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>aware</b> <b>of</b> something, you know about it. 意識到…的","examples":["Smokers are well aware of the dangers to their own health. 吸菸者們都很清楚吸菸對其自身健康的那些危害。","He should have been aware of what his junior officers were doing. 他本該意識到自己部下在做什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>aware</b> <b>of</b> something, you realize that it is present or is happening because you hear it, see it, smell it, or feel it. 感受到…的","examples":["She was acutely aware of the noise of the city. 她敏銳地感受到了城市的噪音。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"意識","examples":["The 1980s brought an awareness of green issues. 20世紀80年代有了環保意識。"]}]}]},"awful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"讓人討厭的，糟糕的；駭人聽聞的，可怕的；生病的，不舒服的；非常的，很多的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，極其"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>awful</b>, you dislike that person or thing or you think that they are not very good. 令人討厭的","examples":["We met and I thought he was awful. 我們見了面，我覺得他令人討厭。","...an awful smell of paint. …一股難聞的油漆味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>awful</b>, you mean that it is extremely unpleasant, shocking, or bad. 糟透的","examples":["Her injuries were massive. It was awful. 她的傷勢很嚴重，糟透了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you look or feel <b>awful</b>, you look or feel ill. 難受的","examples":["I hardly slept at all and felt pretty awful. 我幾乎沒睡，感覺挺難受。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>awful</b> with noun groups that refer to an amount in order to emphasize how large that amount is. 極度的","examples":["I've got an awful lot of work to do. 我有極多的工作要做。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極度地","examples":["The caramel looks awfully good. 這種黃油奶糖看上去棒極了。"]}]}]},"bold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大膽自信的，敢於冒險的；冒失的，魯莽的；明顯的，輪廓突出的；粗體的，黑體的；<文>陡峭的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"黑體，粗體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bold</b> is not afraid to do things that involve risk or danger. 無畏的; 大膽的","examples":["Amrita becomes a bold, daring rebel. 阿莫瑞塔成了一位英勇無畏的反叛者。","In 1960 this was a bold move. 在1960年，這是一個大膽的舉動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bold</b> is not shy or embarrassed in the company of other people. 大膽的","examples":["I don't feel I'm being bold, because it's always been natural for me to just speak out about whatever disturbs me. 我並不認為自己莽撞，因為無論什麼事令我不安我就說出來，對我這一直以來是很自然的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bold</b> colour or pattern is very bright and noticeable. (色彩或圖案) 鮮明的; 醒目的","examples":["...bold flowers in various shades of red, blue or white. …各種深淺不同的紅色、藍色和白色的醒目的花朵。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Bold</b> lines or designs are drawn in a clear, strong way. 清晰的; (線條、輪廓) 剛勁的; 大膽的","examples":["Each picture is shown in colour on one page and as a bold outline on the opposite page. 每幅畫在一頁上是彩色的，在相對的一頁上則是清晰剛勁的輪廓。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無畏地; 大膽地","examples":["You must act boldly and confidently. 你必須表現得大膽、自信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"大膽地","examples":["\"You should do it,\" the girl said, boldly. 這個女孩大膽地說道：“你應該這麼做。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bold</b> is print which is thicker and looks blacker than ordinary printed letters. 粗體","examples":["When a candidate is elected his or her name will be highlighted in bold. 當候選人被選中時，他或她的名字就用粗體來突出。"]}]}]},"capable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有能力的；有本領的，能幹的；可以……的，容許……的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>capable of</b> doing something, they have the ability to do it. 有能力的","examples":["He appeared hardly capable of conducting a coherent conversation. 他看起來幾乎沒有能力進行連貫的談話。","The kitchen is capable of catering for several hundred people. 這間廚房可為數百人提供飲食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>capable</b> has the skill or qualities necessary to do a particular thing well, or is able to do most things well. 有才能的; 有才幹的","examples":["She's a very capable speaker. 她是一個非常有能力的演說者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有能力地; 能幹地","examples":["It was all dealt with very capably by the police and security people. 警方和治安人員極其出色地處理了這一切。"]}]}]},"changeable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可改變的，可被改變的；變化無常的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>changeable</b> is likely to change many times. 多變的","examples":["The forecast is for changeable weather. 未來一段時間天氣多變。"]}]}]},"brilliant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巧妙的，使人印象深的；成功的，輝煌的；聰穎的，技藝高超的；明亮的，鮮豔的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brilliant</b> person, idea, or performance is extremely clever or skilful. 極有才智的; 絕妙的","examples":["She had a brilliant mind. 她有極聰明的頭腦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>brilliant</b> career or success is very successful. 非常成功的","examples":["He served four years in prison, emerging to find his brilliant career in ruins. 他在監獄服了4年刑,出獄後發現他的輝煌事業已經毀了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>brilliant</b> colour is extremely bright. 鮮亮的","examples":["The woman had brilliant green eyes. 這個女人有一雙亮晶晶的綠眼睛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You describe light, or something that reflects light, as <b>brilliant</b> when it shines very brightly. 燦爛的","examples":["The event was held in brilliant sunshine. 這次活動在燦爛的陽光下舉行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>brilliant</b> when you are very pleased about it or think that it is very good. 真棒的","examples":["If you get a chance to see the show, do go – it's brilliant. 如果你有機會去看那場演出,一定要去–它太棒了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極有才智地; 絕妙地","examples":["It is a very high quality production, brilliantly written and acted. 這是一部非常高質量的演出,絕妙地編寫而成並被表演出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非常成功地","examples":["The strategy worked brilliantly. 這項策略非常成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"鮮亮地","examples":["Many of the patterns show brilliantly coloured flowers. 許多圖案都有絢麗多彩的花。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"燦爛地","examples":["It's a brilliantly sunny morning. 這是個陽光燦爛的早晨。"]}]}]},"ceramic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陶瓷製品，陶瓷器；製陶藝術"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陶瓷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ceramic</b> is clay that has been heated to a very high temperature so that it becomes hard. 陶瓷","examples":["...ceramic tiles. …瓷磚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ceramics</b> are ceramic ornaments or objects. 陶瓷製品","examples":["...a collection of Chinese ceramics. …中國陶瓷收藏品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ceramics</b> is the art of making artistic objects out of clay. 製陶藝術","examples":["...a degree in ceramics. …陶藝學學位。"]}]}]},"chilly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陰冷的，寒冷的；有寒意的；不友好的，冷淡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>chilly</b> is unpleasantly cold. 陰冷的","examples":["It was a chilly afternoon. 那是一個陰冷的下午。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel <b>chilly</b>, you feel rather cold. 寒冷的","examples":["I'm a bit chilly. 我感到有點兒冷。"]}]}]},"countable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可數的，可計算的，能算的；（語法）可數名詞的，有單複數形式並可與數詞或 a/an 等限定詞連用的；（數學）可數的，可列的（指有限集或能與自然數一一對應的集合）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"capable of being counted 可數的","examples":[]}]}]},"civil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公民的，國民的，國內的；平民的，民用的；文明的，有禮貌的；民法的（非刑法的），民事的；習俗規定的，曆法規定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>civil</b> to describe events that happen within a country and that involve the different groups of people in it. 國民的","examples":["...civil unrest. …民眾的騷亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>civil</b> to describe people or things in a country that are not connected with its armed forces. 民用的","examples":["...the U.S. civil aviation industry. …美國民用航空工業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>civil</b> to describe things that are connected with the state rather than with a religion. 民政的","examples":["They were married on August 9 in a civil ceremony in Venice. 他們於8月9日在威尼斯透過民政儀式結了婚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>civil</b> to describe the rights that people have within a society. 公民的","examples":["...a United Nations covenant on civil and political rights. …一份關於民權和政治權利的聯合國公約。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone who is <b>civil</b> is polite in a formal way, but not particularly friendly. 文明的","examples":["As visitors, the least we can do is be civil to the people in their own land. 作為遊客，我們至少要能做到文明地對待當地人民。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"禮貌","examples":["...civility to underlings. …對下屬的禮待。"]}]}]},"cheerful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"歡快的，高興的；令人高興的，令人愉快的；樂觀的，開朗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cheerful</b> is happy and shows this in their behaviour. 高興的","examples":["Paddy was always cheerful and jolly. 帕迪總是很高興，很開心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>cheerful</b> is pleasant and makes you feel happy. 令人愉快的","examples":["The nursery is bright and cheerful, with plenty of toys. 該託兒所明亮宜人，有許多玩具。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's attitude as <b>cheerful</b>, you mean they are not worried about something, and you think that they should be. 樂觀的","examples":["There is little evidence to support his cheerful assumptions. 幾乎沒有證據來支援他樂觀的設想。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"高興地","examples":["\"We've come with good news,\" Pat said cheerfully. “我們帶來了好訊息。”帕特高興地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"樂觀地","examples":["He cheerfully ignored medical advice which could have prolonged his life. 他對本可能延長他壽命的醫療建議樂觀地置之不理。"]}]}]},"considerable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相當大的，相當重要的；（人）顯要的，值得尊敬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Considerable</b> means great in amount or degree. 相當多的; 相當大的","examples":["To be without Pearce would be a considerable blow. 要是缺了皮爾斯，那會是相當大的打擊。","Doing it properly makes considerable demands on our time. 把這件事做得到位，要花我們相當多的時間。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"相當多地; 相當大地","examples":["Children vary considerably in the rate at which they learn these lessons. 孩子們學習這些課的速度差別相當大。"]}]}]},"casual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"休閒的，便裝的；隨便的，非正式的；漫不經心的，隨意的；臨時的，短期的；碰巧的，偶然的；不認真的，馬虎的；不定期的，偶爾的；感情不深的，疏遠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"便服，便裝（casuals）；臨時工；<英>散漫青年；待命士兵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>casual</b>, you are, or you pretend to be, relaxed and not very concerned about what is happening or what you are doing. 放鬆的","examples":["It's difficult for me to be casual about anything. 要我輕鬆待事有難度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>casual</b> event or situation happens by chance or without planning. 不經意的","examples":["What you mean as a casual remark could be misinterpreted. 你不經意所說的話可能會被誤解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Casual</b> clothes are ones that you normally wear at home or on holiday, and not on formal occasions. (服裝) 休閒的","examples":["I also bought some casual clothes for the weekend. 我還買了些休閒服準備週末穿。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Casual</b> work is done for short periods and not on a permanent or regular basis. 臨時的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"放鬆地","examples":["\"No need to hurry,\" Ben said casually. “不必匆忙，”本輕鬆地說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"休閒地","examples":["They were casually dressed. 他們穿著休閒。"]}]}]},"confident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（性格，態度）自信的，充滿信心的；堅信的，肯定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>密友，知己"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>confident</b> about something, you are certain that it will happen in the way you want it to. 有信心的","examples":["I am confident that everything will come out right in time. 我相信最終一切都會好起來的。","Mr. Ryan is confident of success. 瑞安先生對成功有信心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or their manner is <b>confident</b>, they feel sure about their own abilities, qualities, or ideas. 自信的","examples":["In time he became more confident and relaxed. 最終他變得更加自信而從容了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>confident</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you are sure that it is true. A <b>confident</b> statement is one that the speaker is sure is true. 確信的","examples":["She is confident that everybody is on her side. 她確信每個人都在她那一邊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有信心地","examples":["I can confidently promise that this year is going to be very different. 我可以有信心地保證今年將大不一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"自信地","examples":["She walked confidently across the hall. 她自信地走過大廳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"確信地","examples":["I can confidently say that none of them were or are racist. 我可以確信地說他們當中沒有人過去或現在是種族主義者。"]}]}]},"classical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經典的，傳統的；和古希臘與古羅馬文化相關的；（音樂）古典的；文科的，人文科學的；典型的，有代表性的；相對論和量子力學理論前的概念、理論的，古典力學的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>classical</b> to describe something that is traditional in form, style, or content. 傳統的","examples":["Fokine did not change the steps of classical ballet; instead he found new ways of using them. 福金沒有改變傳統芭蕾的舞步；取而代之的是他發現了使用傳統舞步的新方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Classical</b> music is music that is considered to be serious and of lasting value. (指音樂) 古典的","examples":["...a classical composer like Beethoven. …諸如貝多芬的一名古典作曲家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Classical</b> is used to describe things which relate to the ancient Greek or Roman civilizations. (指古希臘羅馬) 古典文化的","examples":["...the healers of ancient Egypt and classical Greece. …古埃及和古希臘的療愈者們。"]}]}]},"conscious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"意識到的；神志清醒的，有知覺的；關注的；刻意的，慎重的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>conscious</b> <b>of</b> something, you notice it or realize that it is happening. 意識到的","examples":["He was conscious of the faint, musky aroma of aftershave. 他留意到鬚後水那淡淡的、似麝香的芳香。","She was very conscious of Max studying her. 她十分清楚馬克斯在仔細端詳著她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>conscious</b> <b>of</b> something, you think about it a lot, especially because you are unhappy about it or because you think it is important. (尤指因為自認不滿意或很重要而) 在意的","examples":["I'm very conscious of my weight. 我很在意自己的體重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>conscious</b> decision or action is made or done deliberately with you giving your full attention to it. 刻意的","examples":["I don't think we ever made a conscious decision to have a big family. 我不認為我們曾刻意下決定要成為一大家子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>conscious</b> is awake rather than asleep or unconscious. 神志清醒的","examples":["She was fully conscious throughout the surgery and knew what was going on. 她在整個手術過程中神志完全清醒，知道發生了什麼。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Conscious</b> memories or thoughts are ones that you are aware of. 清楚的 (記憶、想法)","examples":["He had no conscious memory of his four-week stay in the hospital. 他對自己住院的4個星期記不大清了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"刻意地","examples":["Sophie was not consciously seeking a replacement after her father died. 索菲在父親去世後沒有刻意地找一個代替的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"清楚地 (記得、想起)","examples":["Most people cannot consciously remember much before the ages of 3 to 5 years. 多數人不能清楚地記得3到5歲之前的多少事情。"]}]}]},"creative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"創造（性）的，創作的；有創造力的，有想象力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"創作者；創意，創作素材"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>creative</b> person has the ability to invent and develop original ideas, especially in the arts. 有創造力的","examples":["Like so many creative people, he was never satisfied. 正如許多有創造力的人一樣，他永不滿足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Creative</b> activities involve the inventing and making of new kinds of things. 創新性的","examples":["...creative writing. …創新寫作。","...creative arts. …創新藝術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you use something in a <b>creative</b> way, you use it in a new way that produces interesting and unusual results. 獨創的","examples":["...his creative use of words. …他獨創的詞彙用法。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"創造力","examples":["American art reached a peak of creativity in the '50s and '60s. 20世紀五六十年代，美國藝術的創造力達到了頂峰。"]}]}]},"crunchy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"硬脆的，鬆脆的；<美，非正式> 政治上自由主義且注重環保的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Food that is <b>crunchy</b> is pleasantly hard or crisp so that it makes a noise when you eat it. 脆的","examples":["...fresh, crunchy vegetables. …鮮脆的蔬菜。"]}]}]},"crispy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（食物的外皮）鬆脆的；生氣勃勃的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Food that is <b>crispy</b> is pleasantly hard, or has a pleasantly hard surface. 酥脆的","examples":["...crispy fried onions. ...炸得酥脆的洋蔥。","...crispy bread rolls. ...酥脆的麵包卷。"]}]}]},"crisp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"爽口的，脆生的；脆的，易碎的；潔淨的，挺括的；（圖片或聲音）清晰的，清脆悅耳的；清新的，涼爽的；（言行）乾脆利落的；輕快的，利索的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>炸薯片；鬆脆食品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）發脆；<舊>（使）變卷，（使）變捲曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Food that is <b>crisp</b> is pleasantly hard, or has a pleasantly hard surface. 脆的","examples":["Bake the potatoes for 15 minutes, till they're nice and crisp. 把土豆烤15分鐘，直到變得香脆可口。","...crisp bacon. …香脆的燻肉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Weather that is pleasantly fresh, cold, and dry can be described as <b>crisp</b>. 清爽的 (天氣)","examples":["...a crisp autumn day. …一個清爽的秋日。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Crisp</b> cloth or paper is clean and has no creases in it. 乾淨挺括的 (紙、布等)","examples":["He wore a panama hat and a crisp white suit. 他戴著一頂巴拿馬帽，穿著一身挺括的白西裝。","I slipped between the crisp clean sheets. 我鑽進了乾淨平整的被單中。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If food <b>crisps</b> or if you <b>crisp</b> it, it becomes pleasantly hard, for example, because you have heated it at a high temperature. 變脆; 使…變脆","examples":["Cook the bacon until it begins to crisp. 烤制燻肉直到變脆。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crisps</b> are very thin slices of fried potato that are eaten cold as a snack. 炸薯片","examples":["...a packet of onion-flavoured crisps. …一包洋蔥味的薯片。"]}]}]},"cultural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"文化的，與文化有關的；藝術的，文藝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cultural</b> means relating to a particular society and its ideas, customs, and art. 文化的","examples":["...a deep sense of personal honour which was part of his cultural heritage. …成為他文化遺產中一部分的強烈的個人榮譽感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cultural</b> means involving or concerning the arts. 文化藝術的","examples":["...the sponsorship of sports and cultural events by tobacco companies. …菸草公司對體育和文藝活動的贊助。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"文化上地","examples":["...an informed guide to culturally and historically significant sites. …一份介紹文化和歷史名勝內容豐富的指南。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"文化藝術上地","examples":["...one of our better-governed, culturally active regional centres. …管理較好、文化藝術活動活躍的地區中心之一。"]}]}]},"desirable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人嚮往的，值得擁有的；可取的；性感的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"稱心合意的人（或物），好的品質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>desirable</b> is worth having or doing because it is useful, necessary, or popular. 值得擁有的; 值得做的","examples":["Prolonged negotiation was not desirable. 拖得很長的談判是不受歡迎的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>desirable</b> is considered to be sexually attractive. 性感的","examples":["...the young women of his own age whom his classmates thought most desirable. …與他同齡的、在他的同學們看來最性感的年輕女子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可取性","examples":["...the desirability of democratic reform. …民主改革的可取性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"性感","examples":["He had not at all overrated Veronica's desirability. 他絲毫沒有高估韋羅妮卡的性感。"]}]}]},"democratic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平等的，有民主精神的；民主政體的；（美國）民主黨的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>democratic</b> country, government, or political system is governed by representatives who are elected by the people. 民主的","examples":["Bolivia returned to democratic rule in 1982, after a series of military governments. 玻利維亞經歷了一系列軍事政府統治後於1982年恢復了民主統治。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>democratic</b> is based on the idea that everyone should have equal rights and should be involved in making important decisions. 民主精神的","examples":["Education is the basis of a democratic society. 教育是民主社會的基礎。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"民主地","examples":["That June, Yeltsin became Russia's first democratically elected president. 那年6月，葉利欽成為俄羅斯第一位透過民主選舉產生的總統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"民主精神地","examples":["This committee will enable decisions to be made democratically. 這個委員會將保證決策是民主地產生的。"]}]}]},"diligent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勤奮的，勤勉的；細緻的，潛心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>diligent</b> works hard in a careful and thorough way. 勤奮的","examples":["Meyers is a diligent and prolific worker. 邁耶斯是個勤奮而且出活多的工人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"勤奮","examples":["The police are pursuing their inquiries with great diligence. 警察正以不懈的努力進行著調查。"]}]}]},"drowsy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"昏昏欲睡的，睏倦的；令人鬆弛的，令人睏倦欲睡的；（尤指地方）靜謐的，平靜的，安靜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>drowsy</b>, you feel sleepy and cannot think clearly. 昏昏欲睡的","examples":["He felt pleasantly drowsy and had to fight off the urge to sleep. 他感覺舒適地昏昏欲睡，不得不擊退睡意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"睡意","examples":["Big meals during the day cause drowsiness. 白天的大餐會讓人犯困。"]}]}]},"eager":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱切的，渴望的，渴求的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>eager</b> <b>to</b> do or have something, you want to do or have it very much. 渴望的","examples":["Robert was eager to talk about life in the Army. 羅伯特渴望談論軍旅生活。","When my own son was five years old, I became eager for another baby. 當我兒子５歲的時候，我開始渴望要另一個寶寶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you look or sound <b>eager</b>, you look or sound as if you expect something interesting or enjoyable to happen. 熱切的","examples":["Arty sneered at the crowd of eager faces around him. 阿蒂對周圍滿臉熱切的人們報以冷笑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"渴望","examples":["...an eagerness to learn. …一種學習的渴望。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"熱切地","examples":["\"So what do you think will happen?\" he asked eagerly. “那麼你認為會發生什麼事呢？” 他熱切地問道。"]}]}]},"doubtful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"懷疑的，不確定的；未必的，不大可能的；不可靠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>doubtful</b> <b>that</b> something will happen, it seems unlikely to happen or you are uncertain whether it will happen. 不大可能的","examples":["For a time it seemed doubtful that he would move at all. 短期內他似乎不大可能搬走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>doubtful</b> <b>about</b> something, you feel unsure or uncertain about it. 不能肯定的","examples":["I was still very doubtful about the chances for success. 我仍然不能肯定成功的可能性有多大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>of</b> <b>doubtful</b> quality or value, you mean that it is of low quality or value. 有問題的","examples":["...selling something that is overpriced or of doubtful quality. …銷售價格過高或質量有問題的東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a sports player is <b>doubtful</b> <b>for</b> a match or event, he or she seems unlikely to play, usually because of injury. 不太可能的","examples":["Forsyth is doubtful for tonight's game with a badly bruised leg. 福賽斯因為嚴重的腿傷不太可能參加今晚的比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不能肯定地","examples":["Keeton shook his head doubtfully. 基頓將信將疑地搖了搖頭。"]}]}]},"domestic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"國內的，本國的；家用的，家庭的；喜愛家庭生活的，樂於操持家務的；非野生的，馴養的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"家庭糾紛，家庭矛盾；傭人，家僕；<美>國貨，本地產品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Domestic</b> political activities, events, and situations happen or exist within one particular country. 國內的","examples":["...over 100 domestic flights a day to 30 leading U.S. destinations. …每天飛往美國30個主要目的地的100多個國內航班。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Domestic</b> duties and activities are concerned with the running of a home and family. 家務的","examples":["...a plan for sharing domestic chores. …一份分擔家務的計劃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Domestic</b> items and services are intended to be used in people's homes rather than in factories or offices. 家用的","examples":["...domestic appliances. …家用電器。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>domestic</b> situation or atmosphere is one which involves a family and their home. 家庭的","examples":["It was a scene of such domestic bliss. 這是一幕家庭美滿的場景。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>domestic</b> animal is one that is not wild and is kept either on a farm to produce food or in someone's home as a pet. 家養的; 飼養的","examples":["...a domestic cat. …一隻家貓。"]}]}]},"dramatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大而突然的，急劇的；激動人心的，引人注目的，給人深刻印象的；有關戲劇的，戲劇表演的；誇張的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dramatic</b> change or event happens suddenly and is very noticeable and surprising. 突然引人注目的","examples":["A fifth year of drought is expected to have dramatic effects on the California economy. 預計連續乾旱的第五個年頭將對加利福尼亞州的經濟產生引人注目的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dramatic</b> action, event, or situation is exciting and impressive. 緊張刺激的; 扣人心絃的","examples":["He witnessed many dramatic escapes as people jumped from as high as the fourth floor. 當人們從4層樓那麼高的地方跳下來的時侯，他目睹了許多驚心動魄的逃生情景。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>dramatic</b> to describe things connected with or relating to the theatre, drama, or plays. 戲劇的; 有關戲劇的","examples":["...a dramatic arts major in college. …一個在學院主修戲劇藝術專業的學生。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"突然引人注目地","examples":["At speeds above 50 mph, serious injuries dramatically increase. 時速超過50英里時，重傷機率急劇上升。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"戲劇性地","examples":["He tipped his head to one side and sighed dramatically. 他把頭偏向一側，戲劇性地嘆了口氣。"]}]}]},"educational":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"教育的；有教育意義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Educational</b> matters or institutions are concerned with or relate to education. 教育的","examples":["...the Japanese educational system. …日本教育體制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>educational</b> experience teaches you something. 有教育意義的","examples":["The staff should make sure the kids have an enjoyable and educational day. 教職員要確保孩子們度過愉快的、有教育意義的一天。"]}]}]},"elderly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"上了年紀的；老掉牙的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"老人（the elderly）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>elderly</b> as a polite way of saying that someone is old. 上年紀的","examples":["There was an elderly couple on the terrace. 露臺上有一對上年紀的老人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The elderly</b> are people who are old. 老年人","examples":["The elderly are a formidable force in any election. 老年人在任何選舉中都是一股強大的力量。"]}]}]},"electrical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"電的，與電有關的；生產或銷售電器的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電氣裝置，電路；電器公司發行的股票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Electrical</b> goods, equipment, or appliances work by means of electricity. 電力的","examples":["...shipments of electrical equipment. …電器裝置的運輸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Electrical</b> systems or parts supply or use electricity. 電的","examples":["...lighting and other electrical systems on the new runway. …新跑道上的照明和其他電力系統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Electrical</b> energy is energy in the form of electricity. 電的","examples":["...brief pulses of electrical energy. …短暫的電能脈衝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Electrical</b> industries, engineers, or workers are involved in the production and supply of electricity or electrical products. 與電有關的","examples":["...company representatives from the electrical industry. …來自電力行業的公司代表。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"電力地","examples":["...electrically powered vehicles. …電動車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"電地","examples":["...electrically charged particles. …帶電的粒子。"]}]}]},"efficient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生效的，效率高的；（人）有能力的，能勝任的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>efficient</b>, they are able to do tasks successfully, without wasting time or energy. 高效的","examples":["With today's more efficient contraception women can plan their families and careers. 有了當今更為高效的避孕方法婦女們能夠規劃好自己的家庭和事業。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"高效地","examples":["I work very efficiently and am decisive, and accurate in my judgement. 我工作高效、決策果斷而且判斷準確。"]}]}]},"enjoyable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人愉快的，有樂趣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>enjoyable</b> gives you pleasure. 令人愉快的","examples":["It was much more enjoyable than I had expected. 它比我原先想的要令人愉快得多。"]}]}]},"energetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精力充沛的，充滿活力的；積極的；（活動）劇烈的，費力氣的；高能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>energetic</b> in what you do, you have a lot of enthusiasm and determination. 精力充沛的","examples":["Ibrahim is 59, strong looking, enormously energetic and accomplished. 伊卜拉希姆59歲，健壯的樣子，精力極其充沛且富有才華。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>energetic</b> person is very active and does not feel at all tired. An <b>energetic</b> activity involves a lot of physical movement and power. 精力旺盛的; 劇烈的","examples":["Ten year-olds are incredibly energetic. 10歲的孩子精力非常旺盛。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精力充沛地","examples":["He had worked energetically all day on his new book. 他一整天幹勁十足地寫他的新書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"幹勁十足地","examples":["David chewed energetically on the gristly steak. 大衛幹勁十足地嚼著盡是軟骨的牛排。"]}]}]},"electric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"電的；令人激動的；電子擴音的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電路系統；電氣交通工具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>electric</b> device or machine works by means of electricity, rather than using some other source of power. 電動的","examples":["...her electric guitar. …她的電吉他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>electric</b> current, voltage, or charge is one that is produced by electricity. 由電產生的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Electric</b> plugs, sockets, or power lines are designed to carry electricity. 帶電的","examples":["More people are deciding that electric power lines could present a health risk. 更多的人在認為電線可能會帶來健康隱患。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Electric</b> is used to refer to the supply of electricity. 供電的","examples":["An average electric bill might go up $2 or $3 per month. 一張普通電費單可能每月上漲$2或$3。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe the atmosphere of a place or event as <b>electric</b>, you mean that people are in a state of great excitement. (氣氛) 火爆的","examples":["The mood in the hall was electric. 禮堂裡的氣氛極為熱烈。"]}]}]},"electronic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"電子的，電子學的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>electronic</b> device has transistors or silicon chips that control and change the electric current passing through the device. 電子的","examples":["...expensive electronic equipment. …昂貴的電子裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>electronic</b> process or activity involves the use of electronic devices. 電子的","examples":["...electronic music. …電子音樂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"電子地","examples":["Data is transmitted electronically. 資料是電子傳輸。"]}]}]},"expressive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"富於表情的，富於表現力的；表現的，表達的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>expressive</b>, you mean that their behaviour clearly indicates their feelings or intentions. 富於表現力的","examples":["You can train people to be more expressive. 你可以培訓人們使其更富於表現力。","...the present fashion for intuitive, expressive painting. …當前憑直覺的、富於表現力的繪畫風尚。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"富於表現力地","examples":["He moved his hands expressively. 他很有表現力地移動了雙手。"]}]}]},"environmental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自然環境的，生態環境的；環保的，生態環境保護的；與周圍環境有關的，由生存環境引起的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Environmental</b> means concerned with the protection of the natural world of land, sea, air, plants, and animals. 環保的","examples":["Environmental groups plan to stage public protests during the conference. 各環保組織計劃在會議期間舉行一些公眾抗議行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Environmental</b> means relating to or caused by the surroundings in which someone lives or something exists. 生存環境的","examples":["It protects against environmental hazards such as wind and sun. 它防範諸如狂風和烈日等環境危害。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"環保地","examples":["...the high price of environmentally friendly goods. …環保商品的高昂價格。"]}]}]},"fashionable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"流行的，時髦的；有錢人光顧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>fashionable</b> is popular or approved of at a particular time. 時髦的","examples":["It became fashionable to eat certain kinds of fish. 吃某些種類的魚變得時髦了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"時髦地","examples":["...women who are perfectly made up and fashionably dressed. …化妝完美、穿著入時的女人們。"]}]}]},"familiar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熟悉的；常見的，普通的；非正式的，隨和的；過分親密的，隨便的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（與女巫共居的）妖精；知交，密友；（在教皇或主教家服務的）僕人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>familiar</b> to you, you recognize them or know them well. 熟悉的","examples":["He talked of other cultures as if they were more familiar to him than his own. 他談起其他文化就像它們對於他比他自己的文化還熟悉。","They are already familiar faces on our TV screens. 他們已經是我們電視螢幕上熟悉的面孔了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>familiar with</b> something, you know or understand it well. 對…是熟悉的","examples":["Most people are familiar with this figure from Wagner's opera. 多數人對瓦格納歌劇中的這個人物是熟悉的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone you do not know well behaves in a <b>familiar</b> way toward you, they treat you very informally in a way that you might find offensive. 隨便的","examples":["It isn't appropriate for an officer to be overly familiar with an enlisted man. 軍官對入伍士兵過分隨便是不合適的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"熟悉","examples":["Tony was unnerved by the uncanny familiarity of her face. 託尼被她不尋常的熟悉面孔弄得心煩意亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熟悉","examples":["The enemy would always have the advantage of familiarity with the rugged terrain. 敵人會一直在對崎嶇地形的熟悉上佔有優勢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"隨便","examples":["She needed to control her surprise at the easy familiarity with which her host greeted the head waiter. 她需要在看到主人對領班打招呼的親熱隨便時控制自己的驚訝。"]}]}]},"fond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"喜愛的，喜歡做……的；美好的，愉悅的；慈愛的，深情的；天真的，不切實際的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>盲目地喜歡；呵護，撫弄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"烹飪後鍋中的棕色殘留物；（資訊科學）全宗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>fond of</b> someone, you feel affection for them. 喜愛的","examples":["I am very fond of Michael. 我很喜歡邁克爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>fond</b> to describe people or their behaviour when they show affection. 慈愛的","examples":["...a fond father. …一個慈愛的父親。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>fond of</b> something, you like it or you like doing it very much. 很喜歡","examples":["He was fond of marmalade. 他很喜歡橘子醬。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have <b>fond</b> memories of someone or something, you remember them with pleasure. (回憶) 美好的","examples":["I have very fond memories of living in our village. 我對在我們村的生活有著美好的回憶。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>fond</b> to describe hopes, wishes, or beliefs which you think are foolish because they seem unlikely to be fulfilled. (希望、想法或信仰等) 不切實際的","examples":["My fond hope is that we will be ready by Christmastime. 我的不切實際的願望就是我們能在聖誕節假期前準備好。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"喜愛","examples":["...a great fondness for children. …對孩子們的一種深深喜愛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"鍾愛","examples":["I've always had a fondness for chocolate cake. 我一直對巧克力蛋糕情有獨鍾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the background of a design, as in lace (如花邊)設計背景","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"慈愛地","examples":["Liz saw their eyes meet fondly across the table. 利茲看到他們隔著桌子深情地對視著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"愉快地","examples":["My dad took us there when I was about four and I remembered it fondly. 我爸爸在我四歲左右時帶我去過那裡，想起來很愉悅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"不切實際地","examples":["I fondly imagined that surgery meant a few stitches and an overnight stay in the hospital. 我不切實際地以為外科手術就是縫幾針並在醫院呆上一夜。"]}]}]},"handy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有用的，方便的，便於使用的；手巧的，有手藝的；手邊的，附近的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>handy</b> is useful. 有用的","examples":["The book gives handy hints on looking after indoor plants. 這本書提供了關於如何照料室內植物的有用資訊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A thing or place that is <b>handy</b> is nearby and therefore easy to get or reach. 手邊的","examples":["It would be good to have a pencil and paper handy. 把鉛筆和紙放在手邊會很有好處。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>comes in handy</b>, it is useful in a particular situation. 派上用場","examples":["The £20 cheque came in very handy. 這張$20的支票正好派上用場。"]}]}]},"gradual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"逐漸的，漸進的；平緩的，不陡的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"彌撒升階聖歌集"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gradual</b> change or process occurs in small stages over a long period of time, rather than suddenly. 逐漸的","examples":["Losing weight is a slow, gradual process. 減肥是一個緩慢而逐漸的過程。"]}]}]},"harmful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有害的，造成傷害的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>harmful</b> has a bad effect on something else, especially on a person's health. (尤指對健康) 有害的","examples":["...the harmful effects of smoking. …吸菸的危害。"]}]}]},"hasty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"匆忙的，倉促的；草率的，輕率的；<古>易怒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hasty</b> movement, action, or statement is sudden, and often done in reaction to something that has just happened. 匆忙的","examples":["Donald had overturned a chair in his hasty departure. 唐納德倉促離開時撞翻了一把椅子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>hasty</b>, you mean that they are acting too quickly, without thinking carefully, for example because they are angry. 草率的","examples":["A number of the United States' allies had urged him not to make a hasty decision. 美國的一些盟友都力勸其不要作出草率的決定。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"匆忙地","examples":["The council was hastily convened after his father said he was resigning. 在他父親宣佈他將辭職後，理事會被匆忙召集起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"草率地","examples":["I decided that nothing should be done hastily, that things had to be sorted out carefully. 我決定不草率的採取任何行動，先得認真地理清頭緒。"]}]}]},"global":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全球的，全世界的；全面的，整體的；（計算機）全域性的；球形的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>global</b> to describe something that happens in all parts of the world or affects all parts of the world. 全球的","examples":["...a global ban on nuclear testing. …一項全球性核試驗禁令。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>global</b> view or vision of a situation is one in which all the different aspects of it are considered. 全面的","examples":["...a global vision of contemporary societies. …對當代社會的全面認識。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"全球地","examples":["...a globally familiar trade name. …一個全球熟知的商標名。"]}]}]},"historic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"歷史上重要的；過去的，與歷史（或過去）有關的；（時態）歷史的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>historic</b> is important in history, or likely to be considered important at some time in the future. 有重大歷史意義的","examples":["...the historic changes in Eastern Europe. …東歐有歷史性意義的變化。"]}]}]},"historical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（有關）歷史的；歷史學的；（書籍、電影或圖片）描述歷史的，基於史實的；按歷史順序排列的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Historical</b> people, situations, or things existed in the past and are considered to be a part of history. 歷史上的","examples":["...an important historical figure. …一位重要的歷史人物。","...the historical impact of Western capitalism on the world. …西方資本主義對全世界的歷史影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Historical</b> books, movies, or pictures describe or represent people, situations, or things that existed in the past. 歷史題材的","examples":["He is writing a historical novel about nineteenth-century France. 他正在寫一部關於19世紀的法國的歷史小說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Historical</b> information, research, and discussion is related to the study of history. 史學的","examples":["...historical records. …史學記錄。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在歷史上","examples":["Historically, royal marriages have been cold, calculating affairs. 從歷史上來看，王室婚姻一直都是冷酷、精心策劃的結合。"]}]}]},"holy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"神聖的；聖潔的；<非正式>（表示驚訝、恐慌等）天啊，上帝啊；<非正式>用於強調"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"神聖的東西，聖所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>holy</b>, you mean that it is considered to be special because it is connected with God or a particular religion. 有關上帝的; 神聖的","examples":["To them, as to all Poles, this is a holy place. 正如對所有的極地人一樣，對他們來說，這裡是個神聖的地方。"]}]}]},"icy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冰冷的；結冰的；不友好的，冷漠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>icy</b> or <b>icy cold</b>, you mean that it is extremely cold. 冰冷的","examples":["An icy wind blew hard across the open spaces. 一陣寒風猛烈地吹過開闊的空地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>icy</b> road has ice on it. 結冰的","examples":["The roads were icy. 道路都結冰了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>icy</b>, you mean that they are not affectionate or friendly, and they show their dislike or anger in a quiet, controlled way. 冷漠的","examples":["His response was icy. 他的反應很冷漠。"]}]}]},"indoor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"室內的，戶內的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Indoor</b> activities or things are ones that happen or are used inside a building and not outside. 室內的","examples":["No smoking in any indoor facilities. 在任何室內場所都禁止抽菸。"]}]}]},"humorous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幽默的，詼諧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>humorous</b>, they are amusing, especially in a clever or witty way. 幽默的","examples":["He was quite humorous, and I liked that about him. 他很幽默，我喜歡他這一點。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"幽默地","examples":["He looked at me humorously as he wrestled with the door. 他一邊用力地開門，一邊表情滑稽地看著我。"]}]}]},"horrible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可怕的，令人恐懼的；糟糕的，討厭的；不友好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>horrible</b>, you do not like them at all. 令人討厭的","examples":["Her voice sounds horrible. 她的嗓音難聽死了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can call something <b>horrible</b> when it causes you to feel great shock, fear, and disgust. 令人恐懼的","examples":["Still the horrible shrieking came out of his mouth. 嚇人的尖叫聲還是從他嘴裡發出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Horrible</b> is used to emphasize how bad something is. 糟透的","examples":["That seems like a horrible mess that will drag on for years. 那看來像是一個將要延續多年的糟糕困境。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人討厭地","examples":["When trouble comes they behave selfishly and horribly. 困難來臨時，他們就表現得很自私，很令人厭惡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"令人恐懼地","examples":["A two-year-old boy was horribly murdered. 一個兩歲的男孩慘遭殺害。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"糟透了地","examples":["Our plans have gone horribly wrong. 我們的計劃已出了大問題。"]}]}]},"impressive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"給人印象深刻的，令人欽佩的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>impressive</b> impresses you, for example, because it is great in size or degree, or is done with a lot of skill. 令人敬佩的; 給人印象深刻的","examples":["It is an impressive achievement. 這是一項令人敬佩的成就。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人敬佩地; 給人印象深刻地","examples":["...an impressively bright and energetic woman called Cathie Gould. …一個聰明過人而又精力充沛、名叫凱茜·古爾德的女人。"]}]}]},"industrial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"工業的，產業的；有很多產業的，工業發達的；工業用的，用於工業的；（與）工業搖滾（有關）的；因勤勞而得到的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"從事工業的公司；工業股票；工業工人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>industrial</b> to describe things that relate to or are used in industry. 工業的","examples":["...industrial machinery and equipment. …工業機械及裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>industrial</b> city or country is one in which industry is important or highly developed. 工業高度發達的","examples":["...leading western industrial countries. …主要的西方工業發達國家。"]}]}]},"immediate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"立刻的，即時的；目前的，緊迫的；附近的，緊接的；（關係或級別）最接近的，直系的；（兩者間）直接的；（感知，反應）直覺的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>immediate</b> result, action, or reaction happens or is done without any delay. 立即的","examples":["These tragic incidents have had an immediate effect. 這些悲慘事件已經有了立杆見影的結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Immediate</b> needs and concerns exist at the present time and must be dealt with quickly. 緊急的","examples":["Relief agencies say the immediate problem is not a lack of food, but transportation. 救援機構稱當務之急不是食品匱乏，而是交通運輸不足。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>immediate</b> person or thing comes just before or just after another person or thing in a sequence. 緊接的","examples":["In the immediate aftermath of the riots, a mood of hope and reconciliation sprang up. 暴亂之後緊接的是一股希望與和解情緒的產生。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>immediate</b> to describe an area or position that is next to or very near a particular place or person. 緊鄰的","examples":["Only a handful had returned to work in the immediate vicinity. 只有少數幾個人回到附近地區工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>immediate</b> family are the members of your family who are most closely related to you, such as your parents, children, brothers, and sisters. 直系的","examples":["The presence of his immediate family is obviously having a calming effect on him. 他直系親屬的到場顯然對他產生了鎮定的效果。"]}]}]},"inner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內部的，靠近中心的；內心的，未表達出來的；存在於性格中的，骨子裡的；隱蔽的，內在的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部，內裡；靶子內圈；命中靶子內圈的一發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>inner</b> parts of something are the parts contained or enclosed inside the other parts, closest to the centre. 內部的; 裡面的","examples":["She got up and went into an inner office. 她起身走進裡間辦公室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>inner</b> feelings are feelings that you have but do not show to other people. 內心的","examples":["Loving relationships that a child makes will give him an inner sense of security. 兒童所建立的友愛關係會使他的內心有一種安全感。"]}]}]},"joyful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高興的，令人愉快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>joyful</b> causes happiness and pleasure. 令人喜悅的","examples":["A wedding is a joyful celebration of love. 婚禮是令人喜悅的愛情慶典。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>joyful</b> is extremely happy. 非常快樂的","examples":["We're a very joyful people; we're very musical people and we love music. 我們是非常快樂的民族；我們是音樂之族；我們熱愛音樂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非常快樂地","examples":["They greeted him joyfully. 他們非常快樂地跟他打了招呼。"]}]}]},"jealous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"妒忌的，好嫉妒的；珍惜的；猜疑的，留意提防的；（神祇）要求絕對忠實和崇敬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>jealous</b>, they feel angry or bitter because they think that another person is trying to take a lover or friend, or a possession, away from them. 好猜忌的","examples":["She got insanely jealous and there was a terrible fight. 她變得過分地猜忌，接著是一場激烈的打鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>jealous</b> <b>of</b> another person's possessions or qualities, you feel angry or bitter because you do not have them. 嫉妒的","examples":["She was jealous of his wealth. 她嫉妒他的富有。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"好猜忌地","examples":["The formula is jealously guarded. 對該配方戒備森嚴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嫉妒地","examples":["Gloria eyed them jealously. 格洛麗亞當時嫉妒地看著他們。"]}]}]},"innocent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天真的，幼稚的；清白的，無罪的；無辜受害的；沒有惡意的，無冒犯之意的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"天真無邪的人，幼稚的人；無辜的受害者（尤指犯罪或戰爭的受害者）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>innocent</b>, they did not commit a crime that they have been accused of. 清白的","examples":["He was sure that the man was innocent of any crime. 他確信此人是清白無罪的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>innocent</b>, they have no experience or knowledge of the more complex or unpleasant aspects of life. 閱歷淺的; 天真的","examples":["They seemed so young and innocent. 他們看上去如此少不更事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Innocent</b> people are those who are not involved in a crime or conflict, but are injured or killed as a result of it. 無辜受害的","examples":["All those wounded were innocent victims. 所有受傷的人都是無辜的受害者。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>innocent</b> question, remark, or comment is not intended to offend or upset people, even if it does so. 無惡意的","examples":["It was probably an innocent question, but Michael got flustered anyway. 那也許是個沒有惡意的問題，但邁克爾還是變得緊張不安。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>innocent</b> is someone who is innocent. 閱歷淺的人; 天真的人","examples":["She had always regarded Greg as a hopeless innocent where women were concerned. 她過去一直認為格雷格在關於女人方面是一個不可救藥的無知者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"天真地","examples":["The baby gurgled innocently on the bed. 那個嬰兒在床上天真地咯咯笑。"]}]}]},"latter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（兩者之中的）後者的；末期的，後期的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（兩者之間的）後者（the latter）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two people, things, or groups have just been mentioned, you can refer to the second of them as <b>the latter</b>. 後者","examples":["He tracked down his cousin and uncle. The latter was sick. 他追蹤找到了他的堂兄和叔叔。後者病了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Latter</b> is also an adjective. 後面的","examples":["There are the people who speak after they think and the people who think while they're speaking. Mike definitely belongs in the latter category. 有些人先想後說，有些人邊想邊說。邁克當然屬於後一類人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>latter</b> to describe the later part of a period of time or event. 晚期的","examples":["He is getting into the latter years of his career. 他正進入職業生涯的晚期。"]}]}]},"internal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內部的，體內的；內政的，國內的；本身的，本質的；內心的；<英>（大學生）本校生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部部件，內部特徵；內臟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Internal</b> is used to describe things that exist or happen inside a country or organization. 國內的; 組織內部的","examples":["The country stepped up internal security. 該國加強了國內安全防衛。","...Russia's Ministry of Internal Affairs. …俄羅斯內務部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Internal</b> is used to describe things that exist or happen inside a particular person, object, or place. 體內的; 內部的","examples":["The doctor said the internal bleeding had been massive. 醫生說內出血的量很大。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在國內; 在組織內部","examples":["The state is not a unified and internally coherent entity. 這個國家不是一個內部凝聚的統一體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"在體內; 在內部","examples":["Evening primrose oil is used on the skin as well as taken internally. 夜來香油可外用在皮膚上，也可內服。"]}]}]},"manageable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易管理的，易控制的；能應付的，易辦的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>manageable</b> is of a size, quantity, or level of difficulty that people are able to deal with. 能應付的","examples":["He will now try to cut down the task to a manageable size. 他現在將盡力把任務縮減到能應對的程度。"]}]}]},"magical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"魔法的，魔術的；神奇的，迷人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>magical</b> seems to use magic or to be able to produce magic. 魔法般的","examples":["...the story of Sin-Sin, a little boy who has magical powers. …一個有魔力的小男孩辛辛的故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that a place or object is <b>magical</b> when it has a special mysterious quality that makes it seem wonderful and exciting. 神奇的","examples":["The beautiful island of Bermuda is a magical place to get married. 美麗的百慕大島是締結良緣的神奇之地。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"魔法般地","examples":["During the holiday season the town is magically transformed into a Christmas wonderland. 在節日期間該鎮魔法般地變成了聖誕仙境。"]}]}]},"lively":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"活潑的，生氣勃勃的；熱鬧的，激烈的；生動有趣的；思維活躍的，興趣廣泛的；鮮豔的；味濃的；<英>困難重重的；（船）乘風而行的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe someone as <b>lively</b> when they behave in an enthusiastic and cheerful way. 活潑的","examples":["She had a sweet, lively personality. 她有著可愛活潑的性格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lively</b> event or a <b>lively</b> discussion, for example, has lots of interesting and exciting things happening or being said in it. 熱烈的","examples":["It turned out to be a very interesting session with a lively debate. 結果成了一次充滿激烈辯論、非常有意思的會議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>lively</b> mind is intelligent and interested in a lot of different things. 活躍的","examples":["She was a very well educated girl with a lively mind, a girl with ambition. 她是一個非常有教養、頭腦活躍、有抱負的女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"活潑","examples":["Amy could sense his liveliness even from where she stood. 艾米甚至能從她所站的地方感受到他的勃勃生氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熱烈","examples":["Some may enjoy the liveliness of such a restaurant for a few hours a day or week. 有人每天或每週都會來這樣一個餐館，享受幾小時熱烈氛圍。"]}]}]},"marvelous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"了不起的，極好的；非凡的，令人驚異的，不平常的；（較罕見、書面）奇蹟般的"}],"sections":[]},"liberal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"思想開明的；自由主義的，支援變革的；（加拿大、英國等國）自由黨的；慷慨的，大量給予的；通識（教育）的，文科的；不確切的，不拘泥字面的；自由主義神學的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"思想開明的人；自由主義者，支援變革的人；（加拿大、英國等國的）自由黨黨員，自由黨支持者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who has <b>liberal</b> views believes people should have a lot of freedom in deciding how to behave and think. 開明的","examples":["She is known to have liberal views on divorce and contraception. 大家知道，她對於離婚和避孕持開明的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>liberal</b> system allows people or organizations a lot of political or economic freedom. 自由的","examples":["...a liberal democracy with a multiparty political system. …多黨政體的自由民主國家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>Liberal</b> politician or voter is a member of a Liberal Party or votes for a Liberal Party. 自由黨的","examples":["She withdrew because she did not wish to split the Liberal vote. 她退出是因為不想分散自由黨的選票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Liberal</b> means giving, using, or taking a lot of something, or existing in large quantities. 慷慨的; 大量的","examples":["As always he is liberal with his jokes. 他總有講不完的笑話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Liberal</b> is also a noun. 開明者","examples":["...a nation of free-thinking liberals. …一個思想自由的開明者的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Liberal</b> is also a noun. 自由主義者","examples":["These kinds of price controls go against all the financial principles of the free market liberals. 這些價格控制違反了支援自由市場的自由主義者的所有金融原則。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Liberal</b> is also a noun. 自由黨人","examples":["The Liberals hold twenty-three seats. 自由黨擁有23個席位。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"慷慨地; 大量地","examples":["Chemical products were used liberally over agricultural land. 化學產品被大量用於農田。"]}]}]},"mathematical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有關數學的；具有數學頭腦的；精確的，完整的；可能性極小的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>mathematical</b> involves numbers and calculations. 數學的","examples":["...mathematical calculations. …數學計算。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>mathematical</b> abilities or a <b>mathematical</b> mind, you are good at doing calculations or understanding problems that involve numbers. 具有數學頭腦的","examples":["...a mathematical genius. …一個數學天才。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在數學上地","examples":["...a mathematically complicated formula. …一個在數學上覆雜的公式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"具有數學頭腦地","examples":["Anyone can be an astrologer as long as they are mathematically minded. 任何人都可能成為占星家，只要他們具有數學頭腦。"]}]}]},"meaningful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有意義的，重要的；（指眼神、姿勢）意味深長的，意在言外的；淺顯易懂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>meaningful</b>, you mean that it is serious, important, or useful in some way. 嚴肅的; 重要的; 有用的","examples":["She believes these talks will be the start of a constructive and meaningful dialogue. 她相信這些談話將是一次建設性的、重要的對話的開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>meaningful</b> look or gesture is one that is intended to express something, usually to a particular person, without anything being said. 意味深長的","examples":["Upon the utterance of this word, Dan and Harry exchanged a quick, meaningful look. 這個字一出口，丹和哈里馬上交換了一個意味深長的眼神．"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"意味深長地","examples":["He glanced meaningfully at the other policeman, then he went up the stairs. 他向另一名警察意味深長地掃了一眼，然後走上樓去。"]}]}]},"mighty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"強大的，巨大的；（動作）用力的，需用力的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很，非常，十分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mighty</b> is used to describe something that is very large or powerful. 強大的","examples":["There was a flash and a mighty bang. 一道閃光伴隨著一聲轟然巨響。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mighty</b> is used in front of adjectives and adverbs to emphasize the quality that they are describing. 非常","examples":["It's something you'll be mighty proud of. 這是個你會非常驕傲的事。"]}]}]},"loose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"未固定牢的，鬆動的；零散的，鬆脫的；不受束縛的，未拴住的；（衣服）寬鬆的；疏鬆的；組織不嚴密的；不嚴謹的，不精確的；不道德的，放蕩的；無球員控制的；稀的；說話隨便的；（身體）懶散的，放鬆的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"釋放，發洩；鬆開，解開；發射（子彈、箭等）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"寬鬆地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"在逃；（箭的）發射；放縱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>loose</b> is not firmly held or fixed in place. 松的","examples":["If a tooth feels very loose, your dentist may recommend that it's taken out. 如果有顆牙齒非常鬆動，你的牙醫可能會建議拔掉它。","Two wooden beams had come loose from the ceiling. 天花板上的兩根木樑鬆動了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>loose</b> is not attached to anything, or held or contained in anything. 零散的","examples":["Frank emptied a handful of loose change on the table. 弗蘭克將一把零錢全部放在了桌子上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people or animals break <b>loose</b> or are set <b>loose</b>, they are no longer held, tied, or kept somewhere and can move around freely. 自由的","examples":["She broke loose from his embrace and crossed to the window. 她從他的擁抱中掙脫出來，穿過房間走到窗邊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Clothes that are <b>loose</b> are somewhat large and do not fit closely. 寬鬆的","examples":["A pistol wasn't that hard to hide under a loose shirt. 把一支手槍藏在寬鬆的襯衣裡面並沒那麼難。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If your hair is <b>loose</b>, it hangs freely around your shoulders and is not tied back. 披散的","examples":["She was still in her nightgown, with her hair hanging loose over her shoulders. 她仍穿著睡衣，頭髮披散在肩上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>loose</b> grouping, arrangement, or organization is flexible rather than strictly controlled or organized. 鬆散的 (分組、安排、組織)","examples":["Murray and Alison came to some sort of loose arrangement before he went home. 在他回家之前，默裡和艾莉森做了些鬆散的安排。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鬆鬆地","examples":["Tim clasped his hands together and held them loosely in front of his belly. 蒂姆十指交叉搭在腹前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"寬鬆地","examples":["His shirt hung loosely over his thin shoulders. 他的襯衣鬆鬆垮垮地掛在他瘦削的雙肩上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"鬆散地","examples":["The investigation had aimed at a loosely organized group of criminals. 該調查曾是針對一群組織鬆散的罪犯的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or an animal is <b>on the loose</b>, they are free because they have escaped from a person or place. 在逃; 行動自由","examples":["Up to a thousand prisoners may be on the loose inside the jail. 多達一千名的囚犯可能在監獄裡行動自由。"]}]}]},"merry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<舊>愉快的，高興的；<舊>令人愉快的；<英，非正式>微醉的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's character or behaviour as <b>merry</b>, you mean that they are happy and cheerful. 歡快的","examples":["From the house come bursts of merry laughter. 從房子裡傳出陣陣歡快的笑聲。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"歡快地","examples":["Chris threw back his head and laughed merrily. 克里斯開心地仰天大笑。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Just before Christmas and on Christmas Day, people say \"<b>Merry Christmas</b>\" to other people to express the hope that they will have a happy time. 祝聖誕快樂","examples":["Merry Christmas, everyone. 祝大家聖誕快樂。"]}]}]},"mature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"成熟的，理智的；成年的，發育完全的；發酵成熟的，釀成的；中老年的；技藝精湛的，技巧嫻熟的；審慎考慮的，深思熟慮的；到期（應該支付）的；（某些食品或飲料）可立即食用的；（經濟，行業，市場）成熟的，發展餘地不大的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成熟，（使）長成；變理智，（舉止）變成熟；釀成，製成；到期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a child or young animal <b>matures</b>, it becomes an adult. (小孩、幼崽) 發育成熟","examples":["You will learn what to expect as your child matures physically. 當你的孩子身體發育成熟時，你將知道會發生什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>matures</b>, it reaches a state of complete development. (某物) 長成","examples":["When the trees matured they were cut. 當這些樹長成時，它們就會被砍掉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>matures</b>, they become more fully developed in their personality and emotional behaviour. 成熟","examples":["They have matured way beyond their age. 他們已經成熟得遠遠超過了他們的年齡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When an investment such as an insurance policy or bond <b>matures</b>, it reaches the stage when the company pays you back the money you have saved, and the interest your money has earned. (保險單、債券等) 到期","examples":["These bonuses will be paid when your savings plan matures in ten years' time. 當你的儲蓄計劃在10年後到期時，這些紅利將會被支付。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>mature</b>, you think that they are fully developed and balanced in their personality and emotional behaviour. 成熟的","examples":["They are emotionally mature and should behave responsibly. 他們在情感上是成熟的，應該負責任地行事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Mature</b> cheese or wine has been left for a time to allow its full flavour or strength to develop. 釀熟的","examples":["Grate some mature cheddar cheese. 磨碎一些釀熟的切達乾酪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>mature</b> or of <b>mature</b> years, you are saying politely that they are middle-aged or old. 成年的 (中年和老年的禮貌說法)","examples":["...a man of mature years who had been in the job for longer than most of the members could remember. …一個成年男子，從事這項工作的時間已經長得大部分成員都記不清了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as wine or cheese <b>matures</b> or <b>is matured</b>, it is left for a time to allow its full flavour or strength to develop. 使釀熟; 釀成","examples":["Unlike wine, brandy matures only in wood, not glass. 和葡萄酒不同，白蘭地只能在木質容器裡釀成，玻璃容器不行。"]}]}]},"medical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"醫學的，醫療的；內科的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"體格檢查，健康檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Medical</b> means relating to illness and injuries and to their treatment or prevention. 醫學的; 醫療的","examples":["Several police officers received medical treatment for cuts and bruises. 幾位警官接受了割傷和瘀傷的治療。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"醫學上地; 醫療上地","examples":["Therapists cannot prescribe drugs as they are not necessarily medically qualified. 治療師們不能開藥方，因為他們不一定具備醫療資格。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>medical</b> is a thorough examination of your body by a doctor, for example before you start a new job. 全面體檢","examples":[]}]}]},"missing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"找不到的，丟失的；缺少的，缺損的；（人）失蹤的，下落不明的；遺漏的，未被包括在內的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"未擊中，未抓住；未做，錯過；思念，懷念（miss 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>missing</b> or has <b>gone</b> <b>missing</b>, it is not in its usual place, and you cannot find it. 找不到的","examples":["It was only an hour or so later that I discovered that my gun was missing. 也就是一個小時左右後，我發現自己的槍不見了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a part of something is <b>missing</b>, it has been removed or has come off, and has not been replaced. 缺失的","examples":["Three buttons were missing from his shirt. 他的襯衫少了3顆紐扣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>missing</b>, you mean that it has not been included, and you think that it should have been. 遺漏的","examples":["She had given me an incomplete list. One name was missing from it. 她給了我一份不全的名單，上面漏掉了一個名字。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>missing</b> cannot be found, and it is not known whether they are alive or dead. (人) 失蹤的","examples":["Five people died in the explosion and more than one thousand were injured. One person is still missing. 爆炸中5人喪生，一千多人受傷，還有1人失蹤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a member of the armed forces is <b>missing in action</b>, they have not returned from a battle, their body has not been found, and they are not thought to have been captured. (士兵) 在戰鬥中失蹤的","examples":[]}]}]},"mental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"存在於大腦中的，思考的；精神的，思想的，智力的；精神病治療的，精神健康的；<非正式>瘋癲的，不正常的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mental</b> means relating to the process of thinking. 智力的","examples":["The intellectual environment has a significant influence on the mental development of the children. 知識環境對孩子智力的發展有著重大的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Mental</b> means relating to the state or the health of a person's mind. 心理上的","examples":["The mental state that had created her psychosis was no longer present. 導致她精神錯亂的那種心理狀態已經不見了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mental</b> act is one that involves only thinking and not physical action. 在頭腦中進行的","examples":["Practise mental arithmetic when you go out shopping. 外出購物時練習一下心算。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"智力地","examples":["I think you are mentally tired. 我覺得你的頭腦累了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"心理上地","examples":["...an inmate who is mentally disturbed. …一個心理不正常的病人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"在頭腦中進行地","examples":["This technique will help people mentally organize information. 這個技術會幫助人們在頭腦裡組織資訊。"]}]}]},"moist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"潮潤的，微溼的；（地區或空氣）潮溼的，多雨的；（眼睛）含淚的，淚汪汪的；溼（性）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>moist</b> is slightly wet. 溼潤的","examples":["The soil is reasonably moist after the September rain. 9月的雨水之後，土壤適度溼潤。"]}]}]},"mobile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"活動的，可移動的；行動方便的，行動自如的；流動性強的；（面部表情）易變的，多變的；機動的，車載的；與行動電話（或掌上電腦等技術）有關的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"活動的裝飾品，懸掛飾物；行動電話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>mobile</b> to describe something large that can be moved easily from place to place. 可移動的","examples":["...the four-hundred seat mobile theatre. …擁有400個座位的活動劇場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>mobile</b>, you can move or travel easily from place to place, for example because you are not physically disabled or because you have your own transportation. 行動方便的","examples":["I'm still very mobile. 我仍然行動很方便。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a <b>mobile</b> society, people move easily from one job, home, or social class to another. 流動性的 (指工作、住所或社會地位可變動的)","examples":["We are a very mobile society and can't resist trying to take everything with us. 我們是個流動性很強的社會，所以忍不住想攜帶一切東西。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"行動方便","examples":["Two cars gave them the freedom and mobility to go their separate ways. 兩輛汽車給了他們自由和行動的便利，使得他們能夠各走各的路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"流動性","examples":["Prior to the nineteenth century, there were almost no channels of social mobility. 19世紀以前，幾乎沒有社會流動的渠道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mobile</b> is a decoration that you hang from a ceiling. It usually consists of several small objects which move as the air around them moves. (通常由幾個小物件組成的可隨風擺動的) 懸掛在天花板的裝飾物","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>mobile</b> is the same as a . 行動電話","examples":[]}]}]},"outdoor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"戶外的，露天的；喜歡戶外活動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outdoor</b> activities or things happen or are used outside and not in a building. 戶外的","examples":["If you enjoy outdoor activities, this is the trip for you. 如果你喜歡戶外活動，那麼這個旅行適合你。"]}]}]},"optimistic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"樂觀的，樂觀主義的；（估計）過於樂觀的，高估的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>optimistic</b> is hopeful about the future or the success of something in particular. 樂觀主義的","examples":["The president says she is optimistic that an agreement can be worked out soon. 總統說，她對很快能達成協議持樂觀態度。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"樂觀主義地","examples":["Both sides have spoken optimistically about the talks. 雙方都對本次會談表示樂觀。"]}]}]},"obvious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明顯的，顯然的；明確表示的，毫不掩飾的；平淡無奇的，缺乏想象力的；合情合理的，當然的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>obvious</b>, it is easy to see or understand. 明顯的","examples":["...the need to rectify what is an obvious injustice. …糾正明顯不公行為的必要性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something that someone says as <b>obvious</b>, you are being critical of it because you think it is unnecessary or shows lack of imagination. 無新意的","examples":["Such an explanation seems too simple, and too obvious. 這樣的一個解釋似乎太簡單而且太沒新意。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is stating the obvious</b>, you mean that they are saying something that everyone already knows and understands. 說人人皆知的事","examples":[]}]}]},"outer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外面的，外部的；遠離中心的，外圍的；客觀外界的，非主觀的；（尤用於地名）更遠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>外衣，穿在外面的服飾的一部分；<英>靶子的外圈，外圈命中；<英>貨箱，轉運箱；<澳，非正式>跑馬場圍欄外部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>outer</b> parts of something are the parts which contain or enclose the other parts, and which are furthest from the centre. 外面的","examples":["He heard a voice in the outer room. 他聽到外屋有人聲。"]}]}]},"normal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正常的，標準的；（身心）健康的，（人）普通的；（線或線性特徵）正交的，垂直的；（鹽溶液）與血液的鹽濃度相同的；正（斷層）的；平常的，通常的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常態，通常標準；<非正式>正常人，循規蹈矩者；法線，正交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>normal</b> is usual and ordinary, and is what people expect. 正常的; 平常的","examples":["The two countries resumed normal diplomatic relations. 這兩個國家恢復了正常的外交關係。","Her height and weight are normal for her age. 她的身高和體重對於她的年齡來說是正常的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>normal</b> person has no serious physical or mental health problems. 身心正常的","examples":["Statistics indicate that depressed patients are more likely to become ill than are normal people. 統計表明抑鬱的患者比正常人更可能得病。"]}]}]},"nervous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"神經緊張的，擔憂的；神經質的，神經過敏的；神經的，神經系統的；（疾病）由精神緊張引起的，由精神壓力造成的；易激動的，易興奮的；強健有力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>nervous</b>, they are frightened or worried about something that is happening or might happen, and show this in their behaviour. 神經緊張的","examples":["The party has become deeply nervous about its prospects of winning the next election. 該黨對其贏得下一屆大選的前景極其緊張。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>nervous</b> person is very tense and easily upset. 神經質的","examples":["She was apparently a very nervous woman, and that affected her career. 她顯然是個很神經質的女人，這影響到了她的事業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>nervous</b> illness or condition is one that affects your emotions and your mental state. 神經性的","examples":["The number of nervous disorders was rising in the region. 該地區神經紊亂的病例數正在上升。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"神經緊張地","examples":["Brunhilde stood up nervously as the men came into the room. 那些人進屋時布倫希爾德緊張地站了起來。"]}]}]},"political":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"政治（上）的，政府的；政黨的，黨派的；對政治感興趣的，參與政治的；反政府的；（組織內部人際間）牽涉權力關係的，爭權奪利的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Political</b> means relating to the way power is achieved and used in a country or society. 政治的","examples":["All other political parties there have been completely banned. 那裡的其他所有政黨都已經完全被取締了。","The government is facing another political crisis. 該政府正面臨著另一場政治危機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>political</b> is interested or involved in politics and holds strong beliefs about it. 對政治感興趣的; 有堅定政治信仰的","examples":["Oh I'm not political, I take no interest in politics. 哦，我不關心政治，對政治不感興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"政治上地","examples":["They do not believe the killings were politically motivated. 他們相信這些謀殺案沒有什麼政治動機。"]}]}]},"pale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（臉色）蒼白的；（顏色）淺的，淡的；（光線）暗淡的，微弱的；較差的，遜色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（臉色）變蒼白；（顏色）變淡，變淺；使褪色；顯得遜色，相形見絀；用板條圍"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（做樁籬用的）板條，尖樁；（喻）界限，範圍；（紋章）（盾形中部的）垂直寬條；（俄國）猶太人居住區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>pale</b>, it is very light in colour or almost white. 淺色的; 灰白的","examples":["Migrating birds filled the pale sky. 遷徙的鳥佈滿了灰白的天空。","As we age, our skin becomes paler. 隨著我們變老，我們的皮膚變得更加蒼白。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone looks <b>pale</b>, their face looks a lighter colour than usual, usually because they are ill, frightened, or shocked. (臉色) 蒼白的","examples":["She looked pale and tired. 她看起來蒼白而疲憊。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pale</b> is also a combining form. (用於構成合成詞) 淺…色的","examples":["...a pale blue sailor dress. …一件淺藍色的水手服。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make or become pale or paler; blanch 變白","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>pales</b> in comparison with another, it is made to seem much less important, serious, or good by it. 顯得遜色; 相形見絀","examples":["When someone you love has a life-threatening illness, everything else pales in comparison. 當你所愛的人得了致命的疾病時，其他的一切就都顯得不重要了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a wooden post or strip used as an upright member in a fence (藩籬上的)木條; 木樁","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"outside the limits of social convention","examples":[]}]}]},"odd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇怪的，反常的；偶然出現的，偶爾發生的；奇形怪狀的，各種各樣的；不成對的，不同類的；奇數的；可得到的，可用的；少量的，不重要的；（尤指在雙方至少各進一球的情況下）一球險勝的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於數字後）大約，左右"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>odd</b>, you think that they are strange or unusual. 古怪的; 不尋常的","examples":["He'd always been odd, but not to this extent. 他曾一直很古怪，但沒到這種程度。","What an odd coincidence that he should have known your family. 他已認識你的家人，多麼不尋常的巧合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>odd</b> before a noun to indicate that you are not mentioning the type, size, or quality of something because it is not important. (用於名詞前) 任意的","examples":["...moving from place to place where she could find the odd bit of work. …在她能找到點事做的地方搬來搬去。","He had various odd cleaning jobs around the place. 他在該地附近做過各種不同的清潔工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Odd</b> numbers, such as 3 and 17, are those which cannot be divided exactly by the number two. 奇數的","examples":["The odd numbers are on the left as you walk up the street. 你沿這條街走時，單號在左邊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that two things are <b>odd</b> when they do not belong to the same set or pair. 單的","examples":["I'm wearing odd socks today by the way. 順便說一下，我今天穿著兩隻不成對兒的襪子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"古怪地; 不尋常地","examples":["...an oddly shaped hill. …一座形狀奇怪的小山。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>odd</b> after a number to indicate that it is only approximate. …左右 (用於數字後)","examples":["How many pages was it, 500 odd? 它多少頁，500左右？","He has now appeared in sixty odd films. 他如今已在六十部左右的電影中露過面。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The odd man out</b>, <b>the odd woman out</b>, or <b>the odd one out</b> in a particular situation is a person who is different from the other people in it. 與眾不同者","examples":["Azerbaijan has been the odd man out, the one republic not to hold democratic elections. 亞塞拜然一直是個與眾不同者，一個不舉行民主選舉的共和國。"]}]}]},"previous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"以前的，先前的；（時間或順序上）稍前的；<非正式>過早的，過急的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>前科，犯罪記錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>previous</b> event or thing is one that happened or existed before the one that you are talking about. 前一次的","examples":["She has a teenage daughter from a previous marriage. 她有個出自前一次婚姻的十幾歲的女兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You refer to the period of time or the thing immediately before the one that you are talking about as the <b>previous</b> one. 前一個的","examples":["It was a surprisingly dry day after the rain of the previous week. 這是繼前一週的降雨之後出奇乾燥的一天。"]}]}]},"probable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很可能發生（或存在等）的，大概的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能獲勝的人（或動物），可能入選者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>probable</b>, you mean that it is likely to be true or likely to happen. 可能 (是真實、發生) 的","examples":["It is probable that the medication will suppress the symptom without treating the condition. 可能該藥物只治標而不治本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>probable</b> to describe a role or function that someone or something is likely to have. 可能 (擁有) 的","examples":["...their probable presidential candidate. …他們可能的總統候選人。"]}]}]},"precious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寶貴的，珍貴的；珍視的，重要的；珍稀的，珍奇的；<非正式>（表示氣憤）寶貝似的；（言行）矯揉造作的，過分講究的；<美，非正式>可愛的，討人喜歡的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（用作稱呼）寶貝，親愛的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，極其"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something such as a resource is <b>precious</b>, you mean that it is valuable and should not be wasted or used badly. (資源等) 寶貴的","examples":["After four months in foreign parts, every hour at home was precious. 在境外待了4個月之後，在家的每個小時都是寶貴的。","A family break allows you to spend precious time together. 一次家庭休假使你有機會和家人共度寶貴時光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Precious</b> objects and materials are worth a lot of money because they are rare. (物品、材料等) 珍貴的","examples":["...jewellery and precious objects belonging to her mother. …屬於她母親的首飾和珍貴物品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>precious</b> to you, you regard it as important and do not want to lose it. (對某人來講) 珍貴的","examples":["Her family's support is particularly precious to Josie. 家人的支援對喬茜尤為珍貴。"]}]}]},"practical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真實的，實際的；（計劃、方法等）切實有效的，切實可行的；（人）明智的，務實的；合適的，適用的；心靈手巧的，善於製作（或修補）的；幾乎完全的，實際上的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（科學、烹飪等的）實踐課，實用知識考試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>practical</b> aspects of something involve real situations and events, rather than just ideas and theories. 實際的","examples":["...practical suggestions on how to increase the fibre in your daily diet. …有關如何增加日常飲食中的纖維素的實際建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You describe people as <b>practical</b> when they make sensible decisions and deal effectively with problems. 務實的","examples":["You were always so practical, Maria. 你總是那麼務實，瑪麗亞。","How could she be so practical when he'd just told her something so shattering? 他剛對她講了那麼令人震驚的事情，她怎麼還能這麼務實？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Practical</b> ideas and methods are likely to be effective or successful in a real situation. (主意、方法) 有實效的","examples":["Although the causes of cancer are being uncovered, we do not yet have any practical way to prevent it. 儘管癌症的病因正被揭開，但我們還沒有任何預防它的有效的方法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe clothes and things in your house as <b>practical</b> when they are suitable for a particular purpose rather than just being fashionable or attractive. (衣物等) 實用的","examples":["...lightweight, practical clothes. …質輕、實用的服裝。"]}]}]},"racial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"種族關係的，種族之間的；人種的，種族的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Racial</b> describes things relating to people's race. 種族的","examples":["...the protection of national and racial minorities. …對少數民族和少數種族的保護。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"種族地","examples":["We are both children of racially mixed marriages. 我們倆都是不同種族通婚所生的孩子。"]}]}]},"protective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"保護的，防護的；呵護的，有保護欲的；有貿易保護傾向的，實行關稅保護的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>保護物，防護物；<舊>避孕套"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Protective</b> means designed or intended to protect something or someone from harm. 起保護作用的","examples":["Protective gloves reduce the absorption of chemicals through the skin. 防護手套可以減少皮膚對化學物質的吸收。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>protective</b> <b>toward</b> you, they look after you and show a strong desire to keep you safe. 愛護備至的","examples":["He is very protective toward his mother. 他對母親愛護備至。"]}]}]},"primary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要的，首要的；<英>小學教育的，初級教育的；初級的，原發性的；最基本的，最根本的；第一手的，直接的；（有機化合物）連上一個碳原子的；（多指胺）（氨基酸順序）一級的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（選舉過程中的黨內）初選（=primary election）；原色；初級飛羽；主星；初級線圈，原線圈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>primary</b> to describe something that is very important. 首要的","examples":["That's the primary reason the company's share price has held up so well. 這就是那家公司的股票價格一直保持得這麼好的首要原因。","His misunderstanding of language was the primary cause of his other problems. 他對語言的誤解是他其他問題的主要原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Primary</b> education is the first few years of formal education for children. 初級的","examples":["The content of primary education should be the same for everyone. 初級教育的內容對每個人都應該是相同的。","Ninety-nine percent of primary pupils now have hands-on experience of computers. 99%的小學生如今都有電腦實際操作經驗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Primary</b> is used to describe something that occurs first. 最初的","examples":["It is not the primary tumour that kills, but secondary growths elsewhere in the body. 致命的並不是原發腫瘤，而是在身體其他部位的繼發。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>primary</b> or a <b>primary election</b> is an election in an American state in which people vote for someone to become a candidate for a political office. Compare . (美國各州的) 初選","examples":["...the 1968 New Hampshire primary. …1968年新罕布什爾州的初選。"]}]}]},"proper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真正的，像樣的；實際上的，嚴格意義上的；正確的，合適的；合理的，合乎體統的；非常有禮貌的，循規蹈矩的；<正式> 特有的，專有的；完全的，徹底的；<英，非正式> 用於強調地道的；（聖詩、教義、禱詞等）用於某特定場合的；（紋章）原色的；（數）真的，正常的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<英，非正式> 完全地，徹底地；<英，非正式> 正確地，恰當地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"特定季節（或節日）的禮儀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>proper</b> to describe things that you consider to be real and satisfactory rather than inadequate in some way. 像樣的","examples":["Two out of five people lack a proper job. 2/5的人缺乏一份像樣的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>proper</b> thing is the one that is correct or most suitable. 正規的","examples":["The Supreme Court will ensure that the proper procedures have been followed. 最高法院將保證正規的程式得到遵守。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a way of behaving is <b>proper</b>, you mean that it is considered socially acceptable and right. 適宜的","examples":["In those days it was not thought entirely proper for a woman to be on the stage. 在那時，女人登臺演出不被認為是完全適宜的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can add <b>proper</b> after a word to indicate that you are referring to the central and most important part of a place, event, or object and want to distinguish it from other things that are not regarded as being important or central to it. 嚴格意義上的","examples":["A distinction must be made between archaeology proper and science-based archaeology. 必須對嚴格意義上的考古學和以科學為基礎的考古學加以區分。"]}]}]},"pure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"純的，不摻雜質的；血統純的，純種的；純真的，貞潔的；乾淨的，不含有害物質的；無雜色的，清晰而優美的；完全的，純粹的；（科學或研究）純理論的，抽象的；（母音）單音的，純音的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pure</b> substance is not mixed with anything else. 純粹的","examples":["...a carton of pure orange juice. …一箱純橙汁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>pure</b> is clean and does not contain any harmful substances. 潔淨的","examples":["In remote regions, the air is pure and the crops are free of poisonous insecticides. 在偏遠地區，空氣是純淨的，莊稼也不用有毒的殺蟲劑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as a colour, a sound, or a type of light as <b>pure</b>, you mean that it is very clear and represents a perfect example of its type. 純的","examples":["She was dressed in pure white clothes. 她穿著純白的衣服。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Pure</b> science or <b>pure</b> research is concerned only with theory and not with how this theory can be used in practical ways. 純理論的","examples":["Physics isn't just about pure science with no immediate applications. 物理學並非沒有直接應用價值的純科學。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Pure</b> means complete and total. 完全的","examples":["The old man turned to give her a look of pure surprise. 那位老人回過頭來非常吃驚地看了她一眼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"潔淨","examples":["They worried about the purity of tap water. 他們擔心自來水是否潔淨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"清亮","examples":["The soaring purity of her voice conjured up the frozen bleakness of the Far North. 她高亢、清亮的聲音使人們想到了遙遠的北方蕭瑟的冰天雪地。"]}]}]},"regional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地區的，區域的；（與）首都以外各地（有關）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（郵票、報紙等）地方版；<美>地區性體育競賽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Regional</b> is used to describe things which relate to a particular area of a country or of the world. 地區的","examples":["The Garden's menu is based on Hawaiian regional cuisine. 花園飯店的菜餚以夏威夷地區的烹飪風格為基礎。"]}]}]},"reasonable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有道理的，合情理的；（人）通情達理的，講道理的；適度的，合適的；（價格）公道的；還算好的，尚可的；相當大的，（數量）不少的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you think that someone is fair and sensible you can say that they are <b>reasonable</b>. 通情達理的","examples":["He's a reasonable sort of person. 他是那種通情達理的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a decision or action is <b>reasonable</b>, you mean that it is fair and sensible. (決定或行動) 合理的","examples":["...a perfectly reasonable decision. …一個完全合理的決定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that an expectation or explanation is <b>reasonable</b>, you mean that there are good reasons why it may be correct. (期望或解釋) 有道理的","examples":["It seems reasonable to expect rapid urban growth. 看起來期待城市會飛速發展是有道理的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that the price of something is <b>reasonable</b>, you mean that it is fair and not too high. (價錢) 公道的","examples":["You get a good meal for a reasonable price. 你能以公道的價格好好地吃一頓。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>reasonable</b> to describe something that is fairly good, but not very good. 還算好的","examples":["The boy answered him in reasonable French. 那男孩用過得去的法語回答了他的問題。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>reasonable</b> amount of something is a fairly large amount of it. 相當大的","examples":["They will need a reasonable amount of desk area and good light. 他們將需要相當大的桌區和充足的光線。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"通情達理地","examples":["\"I'm sorry, Andrew,\" she said reasonably. “對不起，安德魯，”她通情達理地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"有道理地","examples":["You can reasonably expect your goods to arrive within six to eight weeks. 你有理由預期你的貨品會在6至8周內運到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"公道地","examples":["...reasonably priced accommodations. …定價公道的住宿。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"還算好地","examples":["I can dance reasonably well. 我舞跳得還算不錯。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"相當地","examples":["From now on events moved reasonably quickly. 從此，事情發展得相當快。"]}]}]},"queer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<舊>奇怪的，異常的；<非正式>男同性戀的；<英，舊，非正式>略感不適的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>同性戀者；偽造的貨幣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>毀壞，搞糟（協議、事件、局面）；使陷於不利地位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>queer</b> is strange. 奇怪的","examples":["If you ask me, there's something kind of queer going on. 如果問起來的話，是有點奇怪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Queer</b> is also an adjective. 男同性戀的","examples":["...America's first queer country music star. …美國頭號男同性戀、鄉村樂手。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes call homosexual men <b>queers</b>. 男同性戀","examples":[]}]}]},"religious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"宗教的，與宗教相關的；篤信宗教的，虔誠的；極其嚴謹的，十分認真的；<非正式>小心的，謹慎的 ；<非正式>對……很感興趣的，熱衷……的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"修士，修女"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>religious</b> to describe things that are connected with religion or with one particular religion. 宗教的","examples":["Religious groups are now able to meet quite openly. 宗教團體現在可以公開集會了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>religious</b> has a strong belief in a god or gods. 虔誠的; 篤信宗教的","examples":["They are both very religious and felt it was a gift from God. 他們倆都很虔誠，覺得這是上帝賜予的禮物。"]}]}]},"reliable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可靠的，可信賴的；真實可信的，確鑿的；（汽車、裝置、系統等）耐用的，效能穩定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可靠的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People or things that are <b>reliable</b> can be trusted to work well or to behave in the way that you want them to. 可靠的","examples":["She was efficient and reliable. 她既能幹又可靠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Information that is <b>reliable</b> or that is from a <b>reliable</b> source is very likely to be correct. (資訊) 可靠的","examples":["There is no reliable information about civilian casualties. 還沒有關於平民傷亡的可靠資訊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可靠地","examples":["It's been working reliably for years. 它多年來一直可靠地運轉著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"可靠地","examples":["Sonia, we are reliably informed, loves her family very much. 我們得到可靠訊息，索尼亞非常愛她的家人。"]}]}]},"raw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生的，未煮過的；天然的，未經加工的；（資訊）未經處理的，原始的；（感情，品質）強烈的，不掩飾的；（皮膚）刺痛的；（人）生疏無知的，未經訓練的；（天氣）陰冷的；（音樂、藝術、語言等）質樸的，未經琢磨的；<美，非正式>（語言）粗俗的；（布料邊緣）無褶邊的；（文字）不加掩飾的，如實坦陳的；<南非>（非洲黑人）源自傳統部落（或鄉村）文化的；強大的，真實的；（汙水）未經處理的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擦傷處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> materials or substances are in their natural state before being processed or used in manufacturing. 未加工的","examples":["We import raw materials and energy and export mainly industrial products. 我們進口原材料和能源，主要出口工業產品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> food is food that is eaten uncooked, that has not yet been cooked, or that has not been cooked enough. (食物) 生的","examples":["...a popular dish made of raw fish. …由生魚做的一道很受歡迎的菜餚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a part of your body is <b>raw</b>, it is red and painful, perhaps because the skin has come off or has been burned. (身體某部因破皮或燙著等) 紅且疼的","examples":["...the drag of the rope against the raw flesh of my shoulders. …繩子勒磨在我肩上又紅又疼的肉上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> emotions are strong basic feelings or responses which are not weakened by other influences. 強烈直露的 (情感)","examples":["Her grief was still raw and he did not know how to help her. 她的悲傷仍然強烈直露，他不知道如何幫助她好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>raw</b>, you mean that it is simple, powerful, and real. (用以描述事物) 質樸的; 強大的; 真實的","examples":["...the raw power of instinct. …本能的強大力量。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> data is facts or information that has not yet been sorted, analysed, or prepared for use. (資料等) 未整理的; 原始的","examples":["Analyses were conducted on the raw data. 對原始資料進行了分析。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe someone in a new job as <b>raw</b>, or as a <b>raw</b> recruit, you mean that they lack experience in that job. 無經驗的","examples":["...replacing experienced men with raw recruits. …用沒有經驗的新成員代替有經驗的人。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> weather feels unpleasantly cold. 陰冷的","examples":["...a raw December morning. …12月份一個陰冷的早晨。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"<b>Raw</b> sewage is sewage that has not been treated to make it cleaner. 未處理的 (汙水)","examples":["...contamination of drinking water by raw sewage. …飲用水被未處理的汙水所汙染。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are getting <b>a raw deal</b>, you mean that you are being treated unfairly. 不公平的待遇","examples":["I think women have a raw deal. 我認為婦女受到了不公平的待遇。"]}]}]},"ripe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（水果、穀物等）成熟的；（乳酪）熟的，（酒）芳醇的；（氣味）濃烈的，刺鼻的，（香氣）馥郁的；時機成熟的，適宜的；充滿……的（ripe with）；高齡的，高壽的；（雌性魚， 昆蟲）快要產卵的；<非正式> (言語) 下流的，粗俗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ripe</b> fruit or grain is fully grown and ready to eat. (水果、穀物) 成熟的","examples":["Always choose firm, but ripe fruit. 總該挑選堅挺但成熟的水果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation is <b>ripe for</b> a particular development or event, you mean that development or event is likely to happen soon. (事態) 成熟的","examples":["A hospital consultant said conditions were ripe for an outbreak of cholera and typhoid. 一位醫院的專家醫師說霍亂和傷寒爆發的條件已經成熟。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone lives to a <b>ripe old age</b>, they live until they are very old. 高齡","examples":["He lived to the ripe old age of 95. 他活到了95歲的高齡。"]}]}]},"remote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"邊遠的，偏僻的；（距離或空間上）遙遠的；（時間上）久遠的；（機會或可能性）渺茫的；差別很大的，很不相同的；不友好的，冷漠的；遠親關係的；（電子裝置）遙控的；（計算機）遠端的，遠端連線的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"遙控裝置，遙控器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Remote</b> areas are far away from cities and places where most people live, and are therefore difficult to get to. 邊遠的; 偏僻的","examples":["Landslides have cut off many villages in remote areas. 滑坡阻隔了許多邊遠地區的村子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>remote</b> past or <b>remote</b> future is a time that is many years distant from the present. 遙遠的; 久遠的","examples":["Slabs of rock had slipped sideways in the remote past and formed this hole. 在遙遠的過去，大塊的岩石向旁邊滑落，形成了這個洞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>remote</b> <b>from</b> a particular subject or area of experience, it is not relevant to it because it is very different. (關係) 疏遠的","examples":["This government depends on the wishes of a few who are remote from the people. 這個政府按照那幾個疏遠群眾之人的願望行事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that there is a <b>remote</b> possibility or chance that something will happen, you are emphasizing that there is only a very small chance that it will happen. 極小的; (可能性或機會) 微乎其微的","examples":["I use sunscreen whenever there is even a remote possibility that I will be in the sun. 我無論什麼時候都用防曬霜，哪怕是有一點點曬到太陽的可能。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>remote</b>, you mean that they behave as if they do not want to be friendly or closely involved with other people. 與人疏遠的; 孤傲的","examples":["She looked so beautiful, and at the same time so remote. 她看上去如此漂亮，但同時又那麼孤傲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>remote</b> is the same as a . 遙控器","examples":["He flipped through the channels with the remote. 他用遙控器快速瀏覽了各個頻道。"]}]}]},"rotten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"腐爛的，發臭的；（道德、社會或政治）腐敗的，墮落的；<非正式>令人不快的，討厭的；<非正式>質量差的，水平低的；<非正式>（人）不友善的，不誠實的；<非正式>身體不適的，有病的；<非正式>感到內疚（或慚愧）的； <非正式> （強調非常生氣或沮喪）倒黴的，破爛的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>非常；<非正式>惡劣地，糟糕地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If food, wood, or another substance is <b>rotten</b>, it has decayed and can no longer be used. 腐爛了的","examples":["The smell outside this building is overwhelming – like rotten eggs. 這棟大樓外的氣味勢不可擋–像臭雞蛋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>rotten</b>, you think it is very unpleasant or of very poor quality. 極差的","examples":["I personally think it's a rotten idea. 我個人認為這是個餿主意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you feel <b>rotten</b>, you feel bad, either because you are ill or because you are sorry about something. 糟糕的","examples":["I had rheumatic fever and spent that year feeling rotten. 我得了風溼熱，那一年感覺很糟。"]}]}]},"rusty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生鏽的，鏽跡斑斑的；鐵鏽色的，赭色的；（技術、知識等）荒廢的，生疏的；（人）不熟練的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rusty</b> metal object such as a car or a machine is covered with rust, which is a brown substance that forms on iron or steel when it comes into contact with water. 生鏽的","examples":["...a rusty iron gate. …一扇生鏽的鐵門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a skill that you have or your knowledge of something is <b>rusty</b>, it is not as good as it used to be, because you have not used it for a long time. 生疏的","examples":["You may be a little rusty, but past experience and teaching skills won't have been lost. 你可能會有點生疏，但過去的經驗和教學技巧不會丟了的。"]}]}]},"satisfactory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人滿意的，合適的；（病人）未惡化的，沒有生命危險的；（證據，判決）滿足案情需要的；贖罪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>satisfactory</b> is acceptable to you or fulfils a particular need or purpose. 令人滿意的; 合適的","examples":["I never got a satisfactory answer. 我從未得到過一個滿意的回答。"]}]}]},"scarce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"缺乏的，不足的；稀有的，少見的；故意缺席的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<文>幾乎不"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>scarce</b>, there is not enough of it. 短缺的","examples":["Food was scarce and expensive. 食物匱乏而且昂貴。","Jobs are becoming increasingly scarce. 工作職位變得越來越少。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>scarce</b>, you quickly leave the place you are in, usually in order to avoid a difficult or embarrassing situation. 溜走","examples":["It probably would be a good idea if you made yourself scarce. 如果你溜走倒可能是個好主意。"]}]}]},"scary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"駭人的，恐怖的；<非正式>異乎尋常的，令人驚奇的；膽小的，易受驚嚇的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>scary</b> is rather frightening. 可怕的","examples":["I think prison is going to be a scary thing for Harry. 我認為蹲監獄對哈利來說會是件很可怕的事。","There's something very scary about him. 他身上有種非常嚇人的東西。"]}]}]},"scientific":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"科學的，與科學有關的；細緻嚴謹的，使用科學方法的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scientific</b> is used to describe things that relate to science or to a particular science. 科學的","examples":["Scientific research is widely claimed to be the source of the high standard of living in the U.S. 在美國，科學研究被廣泛宣稱為高生活水平的來源。","...the use of animals in scientific experiments. …科學實驗中對動物的使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something in a <b>scientific</b> way, you do it carefully and thoroughly, using experiments or tests. 仔細嚴謹的; 使用科學方法的","examples":["It's not a scientific way to test their opinions. 這樣檢驗他們的觀點不是一個科學的方式。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"科學地","examples":["...scientifically advanced countries. …科學發達的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"細緻嚴謹地; 使用科學方法上","examples":["Efforts are being made to research it scientifically. 正在努力對它進行科學研究。"]}]}]},"secondary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（教育）中等的，中學的；次要的， 第二位的；（疾病、感染）繼發性的，第二期的；間接的；（化學反應）副的；（有機化合物）二代的；（主要指胺）仲的；（電）次級的；<舊>（地質）中生代的（Secondary）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"副手，下屬；第二防線；<英>中學（secondary school 的簡稱）；（鳥）次級飛羽（secondary feather 的簡稱）；（變壓器中的）次級線圈；<舊>（地質）中生代（the Secondary）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>secondary</b>, you mean that it is less important than something else. 次要的","examples":["The street erupted in a huge explosion, with secondary explosions in the adjoining buildings. 街上突然發生了一次巨大爆炸，相鄰的建築物裡伴隨有一些次級爆炸。","They argue that human rights considerations are now of only secondary importance. 他們爭辯說人權考慮現在只是次要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Secondary</b> diseases or infections happen as a result of another disease or infection that has already happened. (疾病、感染等) 續發性的","examples":["These patients had been operated on for the primary cancer but there was evidence of secondary tumours. 這些病人曾因原發性癌症做過手術，但是又有了繼發性腫瘤跡象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Secondary</b> education is given to students between the ages of 11 or 12 and 17 or 18. (教育) 中等的","examples":["Examinations are taken after about five years of secondary education. 經過約五年的中等教育後參加考試。"]}]}]},"shady":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陰涼的，背陰的；（樹等）成蔭的；<非正式>可疑的，非法的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe a place as <b>shady</b> when you like the fact that it is sheltered from bright sunlight, for example, by trees or buildings. 陰涼的; 背陰的","examples":["After flowering, place the pot in a shady spot in the garden. 花開過之後，把花盆放到花園的陰涼處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe activities as <b>shady</b> when you think that they might be dishonest or illegal. You can also use <b>shady</b> to describe people who are involved in such activities. 可疑的; 不法的","examples":["In the 1980s, the company was notorious for shady deals. 在20世紀80年代，這個公司因不法交易而臭名昭著。"]}]}]},"sexual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"性的，性行為的；性別的；性取向的；生殖的，有性繁殖的；（繁殖）配子融合的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sexual</b> feelings or activities are connected with the act of sex or with people's desire for sex. 有關性行為的; 有關性慾的","examples":["This was the first sexual relationship I'd had. 這是我第一次與人發生性關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sexual</b> means relating to the differences between male and female people. 與性別有關的","examples":["Women's groups denounced sexual discrimination. 婦女組織譴責性別歧視。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sexual</b> means relating to the differences between heterosexuals and homosexuals. 有關性取向的","examples":["...couples of all sexual persuasions. …有各種性取向的情侶們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Sexual</b> means relating to the biological process by which people and animals produce young. 有關性繁殖的","examples":["Girls generally reach sexual maturity two years earlier than boys. 女孩子通常比男孩子早兩年達到性成熟。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"與性行為有關地; 與性慾有關地","examples":["...sexually transmitted diseases. …性傳播疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"性別上地","examples":["If you're sexually harassed, you ought to do something about it. 如果遭到性騷擾，你應該對其採取行動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有關性繁殖地","examples":["The first organisms that reproduced sexually were free-floating plankton. 最早的有性繁殖生物是自由漂浮的浮游生物。"]}]}]},"sensible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"理智的，合理的； 樸素而實用的；<正式>可感覺到的，明顯的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可感覺到的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sensible</b> actions or decisions are good because they are based on reasons rather than emotions. 明智的","examples":["It might be sensible to get a lawyer. 找個律師可能會是明智的。","The sensible thing is to leave them alone. 明智的做法是不理他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sensible</b> people behave in a sensible way. 理智的","examples":["She was a sensible girl and did not panic. 她是個理智的女孩子，並沒有驚慌失措。","Oh come on, let's be sensible about this. 哦，得了吧，關於這事我們還是理智一點吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sensible</b> shoes or clothes are practical and strong rather than fashionable and attractive. 實用耐穿的","examples":["Wear loose clothing and sensible footwear. 穿寬鬆的衣服和實用耐穿的鞋子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"明智地","examples":["He sensibly decided to lie low for a while. 他明智地決定先躲避一段時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"實用耐穿地","examples":["They were not sensibly dressed. 他們穿得不實用。"]}]}]},"shallow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淺的，不深的；膚淺的，淺薄的；（呼吸）淺的，微弱的；平緩的；靠近內線的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（海、湖或河的）淺水處，淺灘（shallows）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變淺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shallow</b> container, hole, or area of water measures only a short distance from the top to the bottom. 淺的","examples":["Put the milk in a shallow dish. 把牛奶倒進一個淺盤裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person, piece of work, or idea as <b>shallow</b>, you disapprove of them because they do not show or involve any serious or careful thought. (人、作品、主意等) 淺薄的","examples":["I think he is shallow, vain and untrustworthy. 我認為他淺薄、虛榮、不可信。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your breathing is <b>shallow</b>, you take only a very small amount of air into your lungs at each breath. (呼吸) 淺的","examples":["She began to hear her own taut, shallow breathing. 她開始聽到自己緊張、短促的呼吸。"]}]}]},"shiny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"光滑發亮的，有光澤的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shiny</b> things are bright and reflect light. 閃亮的","examples":["Her blonde hair was shiny and clean. 她的金髮閃亮而整齊。"]}]}]},"sexy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"性感的，引起性慾的；性興奮的，性衝動的；<非正式>讓人興奮的，吸引人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe people and things as <b>sexy</b> if you think they are sexually exciting or sexually attractive. 性感的","examples":["She was one of the sexiest women I had seen. 她是我所見過的最性感的女人之一。"]}]}]},"sensitive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過敏的，易受影響的；靈敏的；善解人意的，體恤的；（問題、話題）敏感的，須謹慎對待的；機密的，保密的；理解的，意識到的；（對藝術、音樂、文學等）感受力強的，有悟性的；需保護的；小心謹慎的；（照相材料）感光的；（市場）脆弱的；神經過敏的，敏感的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"具有超自然通靈能力的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sensitive</b> <b>to</b> other people's needs, problems, or feelings, you show understanding and awareness of them. 有感知力的; 能理解的","examples":["The classroom teacher must be sensitive to a child's needs. 課堂教師必須理解孩子的需求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>sensitive</b> <b>about</b> something, you are easily worried and offended when people talk about it. 敏感的","examples":["Young people are very sensitive about their appearance. 年輕人對自己的外貌很敏感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sensitive</b> subject or issue needs to be dealt with carefully because it is likely to cause disagreement or make people angry or upset. 敏感的; 棘手的","examples":["Employment is a very sensitive issue. 就業是一個非常敏感的問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Sensitive</b> documents or reports contain information that needs to be kept secret and dealt with carefully. 機密的","examples":["He instructed staff to shred sensitive documents. 他指示員工用碎紙機粉碎機密檔案。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>sensitive</b> <b>to</b> a physical force, substance, or treatment is easily affected by it and often harmed by it. 敏感的","examples":["...a chemical which is sensitive to light. …一種對光敏感的化學品。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>sensitive</b> piece of scientific equipment is capable of measuring or recording very small changes. 靈敏的","examples":["...an extremely sensitive microscope. …一臺極為靈敏的顯微鏡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有感知力地; 能理解地","examples":["The abuse of women needs to be treated seriously and sensitively. 虐待婦女的問題需要嚴肅、小心地對待。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"敏感","examples":["...people who suffer extreme sensitivity about what others think. …對別人的看法極為敏感的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"敏感性","examples":["Due to the obvious sensitivity of the issue he would not divulge any details. 由於問題帶有明顯的敏感性，他不肯透露任何細節。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"敏感性","examples":["...the sensitivity of cells damaged by chemotherapy. …被化療損害了的細胞敏感性。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"靈敏度","examples":["...the sensitivity of the detector. …該探測器的靈敏度。"]}]}]},"significant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"顯著的，相當數量的；重要的，意義重大的； 別有含義的，意味深長的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>象徵，有意義的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>significant</b> amount or effect is large enough to be important or affect a situation to a noticeable degree. 重大的; 顯著的","examples":["Most 11-year-olds are not encouraged to develop reading skills; a small but significant number are illiterate. 大多數11歲的兒童沒有被鼓勵去培養閱讀技能。有為數不多、但足以引起人們注意的數目的兒童是文盲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>significant</b> fact, event, or thing is one that is important or shows something. 重要的; 說明問題的","examples":["I think it was significant that he never knew his own father. 我想他從不瞭解自己的父親這一點就很說明問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"重大地; 顯著地","examples":["The number of Senators now supporting him had increased significantly. 現在支援他的參議員人數已經顯著增加了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"重要地; 說明問題地","examples":["Significantly, the company recently opened a huge shop in Atlanta. 重要的是，這家公司最近在亞特蘭大開了一家大商店。"]}]}]},"slippery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"溼滑的，容易打滑的；<非正式>狡猾的，不可靠的；模稜兩可的，模糊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>slippery</b> is smooth, wet, or oily and is therefore difficult to walk on or to hold. 滑的; 溼滑的","examples":["The tiled floor was wet and slippery. 那磁磚地板又溼又滑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone as <b>slippery</b> if you think that they are dishonest in a clever way and cannot be trusted. 狡猾的; 不可靠的","examples":["He is a slippery customer, and should be carefully watched. 他可是個狡猾的主顧，得小心看著他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is on a <b>slippery slope</b>, they are involved in a course of action that is difficult to stop and that will eventually lead to failure or trouble. 不斷惡化的局勢","examples":["The company started down the slippery slope of believing that they knew better than the customer. 該公司開始走下坡路了，他們相信自己比顧客更明白。"]}]}]},"sincere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"衷心的，誠摯的；（人）真誠的，誠懇的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>sincere</b>, you approve of them because they really mean the things they say. You can also describe someone's behaviour and beliefs as <b>sincere</b>. (指人) 真誠的; (指行為、信仰) 誠摯的","examples":["He's sincere in his views. 他的意見是誠懇的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"真誠; 誠摯","examples":["I was impressed with his deep sincerity. 讓我銘記在心的是他深切的誠意。"]}]}]},"stale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（食物）不新鮮的，變味的；氣味不清新的，難聞的；沒有新意的，老掉牙的；（因長期從事同一工作而）疲沓的，厭倦的；（支票，合法要求）（因過期而）失效的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）不新鮮，（使）走味，（使）陳舊；（動物，尤指馬）撒尿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"尿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stale</b> food is no longer fresh or good to eat. (食物) 不新鮮的; 變味的","examples":["Their daily diet consisted of a lump of stale bread, a bowl of rice, and stale water. 他們的日常飲食包括一塊不新鮮的麵包、一碗米飯，還有不新鮮的水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Stale</b> air or smells are unpleasant because they are no longer fresh. (空氣或氣味) 不新鮮的","examples":["...the smell of stale sweat. …汗臭味。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a place, an activity, or an idea is <b>stale</b>, you mean that it has become boring because it is always the same. (地方、活動、主意) 缺乏新鮮感的","examples":["Her relationship with Mark has become stale. 她和馬克的關係已變得乏味了。"]}]}]},"specific":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明確的，具體的；特定的；特有的，獨特的；有特殊功能的，有特效的；（生物）種的；（關稅，稅）按數量（根據固定稅率）徵取而非按貨價徵取的；（物理）（與參照物同一性質成）比率的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"細節，詳情；特效藥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>specific</b> to refer to a particular exact area, problem, or subject. 特定的 (部位、問題、主題等)","examples":["Massage may help to increase blood flow to specific areas of the body. 按摩也許會幫助加快血液流向身體各個特定部位。","There are several specific problems to be dealt with. 有好幾個特定問題要解決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>specific</b>, they give a description that is precise and exact. You can also use <b>specific</b> to describe their description. 確切的","examples":["She declined to be more specific about the reasons for the separation. 她拒絕給出導致分手的更確切的原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>specific</b> <b>to</b> a particular thing is connected with that thing only. 針對…的","examples":["Send your resume with a cover letter that is specific to that particular job. 將你的簡歷和專門為那份工作而寫的附信一併寄送。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Specific</b> is also used after nouns. 針對…的 (用於名詞後)","examples":["Most studies of trade have been country-specific. 大多數貿易研究一直都是針對某個國家的。"]}]}]},"sticky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"黏性的，塗有黏性物質的；（皮膚因熱而）黏溼的；（天氣）溼熱的，悶熱的；（處境、問題等）難辦的，棘手的；（網站）吸引人的，吸引人長時間瀏覽的；（食物）甜膩的；（價格，利率，薪水）變化緩慢的，對變化反應緩慢的；<英，非正式>持有異議的，抱不合作態度的；持久的；<非正式>感到熱得難受的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"告事貼；置頂留言"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sticky</b> substance is soft, or thick and liquid, and can stick to other things. <b>Sticky</b> things are covered with a sticky substance. 粘的","examples":["...sticky toffee. …粘乎乎的太妃糖。","If the dough is sticky, add more flour. 如果麵糰很粘，就再加些麵粉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sticky</b> weather is unpleasantly hot and damp. (天氣) 溼熱的","examples":["...four desperately hot, sticky days in the middle of August. …8月中旬極其溼熱的4天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sticky</b> situation involves problems or is embarrassing. 棘手的; 令人尷尬的","examples":["Inevitably the transition will yield some sticky moments. 轉型過程中難免會有棘手的時候。"]}]}]},"stormy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有暴風雨的，風暴的；激烈的，衝動的；（海）波濤洶湧的，（天空）烏雲密佈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>stormy</b> weather, there are strong winds and heavy rain. 有暴風雨的","examples":["It had been a night of stormy weather, with torrential rain and high winds. 這是一個暴風雨之夜，下著傾盆大雨，颳著強風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Stormy</b> seas have very large strong waves because there are strong winds. 巨浪滔天的","examples":["They make the treacherous journey across stormy seas. 他們穿越巨浪滔天的大海進行這次危險的旅行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>stormy</b>, you mean it involves a lot of angry argument or criticism. 群情激憤的","examples":["The letter was read at a stormy meeting. 這封信是在一次群情激憤的會上讀的。"]}]}]},"steep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（路、山等）陡峭的；（價格，需求）難以接受的，過高的；（增加或減少）急劇的，大幅度的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"浸泡（食物）；使沉浸，使沉湎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>懸崖，陡坡；用於浸泡的溶液"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>steep</b> slope rises at a very sharp angle and is difficult to go up. 陡峭的","examples":["San Francisco is built on 40 hills and some are very steep. 舊金山建在40座山丘上，其中有些非常陡峭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>steep</b> increase or decrease in something is a very big increase or decrease. 急劇的","examples":["Consumers are rebelling at steep price increases. 消費者們正在抗議急劇的物價上漲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that the price of something is <b>steep</b>, you mean that it is expensive. (價格) 高昂的","examples":["The annual premium can be a little steep, but will be well worth it if your dog is injured. 每年的保險費可能有點貴，但是如果您的狗受了傷就很值了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"陡峭地","examples":["The road climbs steeply, with good views of Orvieto through the trees. 這條路陡直地向上延伸，透過樹叢可以一覽奧維多的景色。","...steeply terraced valleys. …陡峭的梯形山谷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"急劇地","examples":["Unemployment is rising steeply. 失業率正在急劇上升。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to soak or be soaked in a liquid in order to soften, cleanse, extract an element, etc 浸; 泡","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to saturate; imbue 使浸透","examples":[]}]}]},"stubborn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）固執的，倔強的；難以去除（對付，使用）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>stubborn</b> or who behaves in a <b>stubborn</b> way is determined to do what they want and is very unwilling to change their mind. 固執的","examples":["He is a stubborn character used to getting his own way. 他是一個固執的人，過去常常隨心所欲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stubborn</b> stain or problem is difficult to remove or to deal with. 難去除的; 難對付的","examples":["This treatment removes the most stubborn stains. 這種處理去掉了最難以去除的汙漬。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"固執地","examples":["He stubbornly refused to tell her how he had come to be in such a state. 他固執地拒絕告訴她自己是如何落到這種地步的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"難去除地; 難對付地","examples":["Some interest rates have remained stubbornly high. 一些利率仍然一直居高不下。"]}]}]},"sufficient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"足夠的，充足的；（理由、條件）充足的，充分的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>sufficient</b> <b>for</b> a particular purpose, there is enough of it for the purpose. 足夠的","examples":["One yard of fabric is sufficient to cover the exterior of an 18-in.-diameter hatbox. 一碼的布料足夠罩住18英寸直徑帽盒的外部。","Lighting levels should be sufficient for photography without flash. 照明程度對無閃光燈攝影應該足夠了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"足夠地","examples":["She recovered sufficiently to accompany Chou on his tour of Africa in 1964. 她康復到足以在周的1964年非洲之旅中伴隨他。"]}]}]},"stable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"穩定的，牢固的；穩重的，沉穩的；（化學結構或物理狀態）穩定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"馬廄；（屬同一馬主或馴馬師的）一群賽馬；（在同一地方工作或訓練的）一批人，（同一公司生產的）系列產品；賽馬訓練場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（馬）入廄，把（馬）拴在馬廄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>stable</b>, it is not likely to change or come to an end suddenly. 穩定的","examples":["The price of oil should remain stable for the rest of 1992. 石油價格在1992年餘下時間裡應該保持穩定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has a <b>stable</b> personality, they are calm and reasonable and their mood does not change suddenly. 穩重的","examples":["Their characters are fully formed and they are both very stable children. 他們的性格已完全定型，倆人都是很穩重的孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe someone who is seriously ill as <b>stable</b> when their condition has stopped getting worse. (病情) 穩定的","examples":["The injured man was in a stable condition. 該受傷男子處於穩定狀態。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Chemical substances are described as <b>stable</b> when they tend to remain in the same chemical or atomic state. (化學物質) 穩定的","examples":["The less stable compounds were converted into a compound called Delta-A THC. 不太穩定的化合物被轉變成了一種稱為Delta-A THC的化合物。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If an object is <b>stable</b>, it is firmly fixed in position and is not likely to move or fall. 穩固的","examples":["This structure must be stable. 這種結構一定很穩固。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"穩定","examples":["It was a time of political stability and progress. 那是一個政治穩定和進步的時期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stable</b> or <b>stables</b> is a building in which horses are kept. 馬廄","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stable</b> or <b>stables</b> is an organization that breeds and trains horses for racing. (養殖並訓練賽馬的) 養馬場","examples":["Miss Curling won on two horses from Mick Trickey's stable. 柯林小姐憑藉兩匹米克•特里克養馬場的馬獲勝了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to put, keep, or be kept in a stable (使)關進畜舍; (被)關進畜舍","examples":[]}]}]},"solid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"固體的，堅硬的；結實的，牢固的；實心的，無空隙的；純質的；純色的，單色的；可靠的，可信賴的；一致的，堅定的；不中斷的，連續的；相當不錯（但談不上出色或獨特）的；立體的，立方的；<美，非正式>關係融洽的；<澳新，非正式>嚴厲的，不公平的；<英，非正式>很難的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"立體（圖形）；固體；固體食物；（液體中的）固形物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>solid</b> substance or object stays the same shape whether it is in a container or not. 固體的","examples":["...the potential of greatly reducing our solid waste problem. …大幅度減少我們的固體垃圾問題的可能性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A substance that is <b>solid</b> is very hard or firm. 堅固的","examples":["The snow had melted, but the lake was still frozen solid. 雪已經融化了，但是湖面上凍得結結實實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>solid</b> object or mass does not have a space inside it, or holes or gaps in it. 實心的","examples":["...a tunnel carved through 50 ft of solid rock. …一條鑿通了50英尺厚的實心岩石的隧道。","The train station was packed solid with people. 火車站上人擠得水洩不通。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an object is made of <b>solid</b> gold or <b>solid</b> wood, for example, it is made of gold or wood all the way through, rather than just on the outside. 純質的","examples":["The faucets appeared to be made of solid gold. 這些水龍頭看上去是純金做成的。","...solid wood doors. …純木門。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A structure that is <b>solid</b> is strong and is not likely to collapse or fall over. 堅固的","examples":["Banks are built to look solid to reassure their customers. 銀行修建得看上去很堅固，以使顧客放心。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>solid</b>, you mean that they are very reliable and respectable. 可靠的; 可敬的","examples":["You want a husband who is solid and stable, someone who will devote himself to you. 你需要一個可靠而穩重的丈夫，一個全心全意為你的人。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Solid</b> evidence or information is reliable because it is based on facts. (證據或資訊) 真實可靠的","examples":["We don't have good solid information on where the people are. 我們並不掌握有關這些人在哪兒的確切訊息。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>solid</b> to describe something such as advice or a piece of work which is useful and reliable. (建議或工作) 有用可靠的","examples":["The organization provides churches with solid advice on a wide range of subjects. 該組織在一系列問題上為教堂提供切實有用的建議。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>solid</b> to describe something such as the basis for a policy or support for an organization when it is strong, because it has been developed carefully and slowly. 堅定的","examples":["...a Democratic nominee with solid support within the party and broad appeal beyond. …一位在黨內有堅定支援、在黨外有廣泛吸引力的民主黨被提名人。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you do something for a <b>solid</b> period of time, you do it without any pause or interruption throughout that time. 連續的","examples":["We had worked together for two solid years. 我們在一起連續工作了兩年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>solid</b> is a substance that stays the same shape whether it is in a container or not. 固體","examples":["Solids turn to liquids at certain temperatures. 固體在一定溫度下轉變成液體。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堅固地","examples":["Their house, which was solidly built, resisted the main shock. 他們的房子修建得很堅固，經受住了主震。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"可靠地; 可敬地","examples":["Graham is so solidly consistent. 格雷厄姆非常可靠穩定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"可靠地","examples":["She's played solidly throughout the spring. 她整個春季都表現得很穩健。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"堅定地","examples":["The Los Alamos district is solidly Republican. 洛斯阿拉莫斯地區是堅定的共和黨地盤。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"連續地","examples":["People who had worked solidly since Christmas enjoyed the chance of a Friday off. 自聖誕節連續工作到現在的人們星期五可以有機會放假一天。"]}]}]},"stiff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（肌肉或關節）痠痛的，僵硬的；不易彎曲的，硬的；艱難的，嚴厲的；無禮的，生硬的；（酒）烈性的；稠的，難攪拌的；難移動的，不順滑的；昂貴的；（風）強勁的，猛烈的；過於正式的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<俚>死屍；<美，非正式>……的人；<非正式>無趣的人，令人討厭的人；<英>（體育俱樂部的）後備隊，候補隊 (the stiffs)"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>詐騙，不還錢，（尤指）不給小費；<非正式>（新產品、電影、節目等）不暢銷，徹底失敗；<美，非正式>冷落，怠慢；<非正式>殺害某人"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，徹底地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>stiff</b> is firm or does not bend easily. 硬的; 不易彎曲的","examples":["The furniture was stiff, uncomfortable, too delicate, and too neat. 這傢俱又硬又不舒服，過分易碎且過於光潔。","His gaberdine trousers were brand new and stiff. 他的華達呢褲子嶄新筆直。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something such as a door or drawer that is <b>stiff</b> does not move as easily as it should. (門或抽屜) 難移動的","examples":["Train doors have handles on the inside. They are stiff so that they cannot be opened accidentally. 火車車門內側有把手。把手很緊，這樣就不會被意外開啟了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>stiff</b>, your muscles or joints hurt when you move, because of illness or because of too much exercise. 痠痛的","examples":["The mud bath is particularly recommended for relieving tension and stiff muscles. 泥浴被特別推薦用於緩解緊張和肌肉痠痛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Stiff</b> behaviour is rather formal and not very friendly or relaxed. 拘謹的; 生硬的","examples":["They always seemed a little awkward with each other, a bit stiff and formal. 他們總是彼此顯得有點兒彆扭，有幾分拘謹，不太隨意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Stiff</b> can be used to mean difficult or severe. 艱難的; 激烈的","examples":["She faces stiff competition in the Best Actress category. 她在最佳女演員這個獎項上面臨著激烈的競爭。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Stiff</b> is also an adjective. 極度的","examples":["Even if he bores you stiff, it is good manners not to let him know it. 即使他把你煩透了，出於禮貌你也不能讓他看出來。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"硬地; 不易彎曲地","examples":["Moira sat stiffly upright in her straight-backed chair. 莫伊拉直挺挺地坐在直背椅上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"痠痛地","examples":["He climbed stiffly from the Volkswagen. 他渾身痠痛地從大眾汽車裡爬出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"拘謹地; 生硬地","examples":["\"Why don't you borrow your sister's car?\" said Cassandra stiffly. “為什麼不借你姐姐的車？”卡珊德拉生硬地說道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are bored <b>stiff</b>, worried <b>stiff</b>, or scared <b>stiff</b>, you are extremely bored, worried, or scared. 極度地","examples":["Anna tried to look interested. Actually, she was bored stiff. 安娜試圖裝出感興趣的樣子。實際上她都厭煩透了。"]}]}]},"thankful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感謝的，感激的；（表示）感謝（或感激）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>thankful</b>, you are very happy and relieved to have something, or that something has happened. 感到慶幸的","examples":["Most of the time I'm just thankful that I've got a job. 大部分時候我慶幸自己有了份工作。"]}]}]},"suitable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"適宜的，合適的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>suitable</b> <b>for</b> a particular purpose or occasion is right or acceptable for it. 適合的","examples":["Employers usually decide within five minutes whether someone is suitable for the job. 僱主們通常在5分鐘內判斷出某人是否適合那份工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"適合","examples":["...information on the suitability of a product for use in the home. …有關一項產品家庭適用性的資訊。"]}]}]},"swift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"迅速的，立刻的；快速移動的，速度非常快的；<美，非正式>機靈的，聰明的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雨燕；蝙蝠蛾；繃架"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<文> （在組合形式以外為詩歌或文學用於）迅速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>swift</b> event or process happens very quickly or without delay. 迅速的","examples":["Our task is to challenge the U.N. to make a swift decision. 我們的任務是敦促聯合國做出迅速的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>swift</b> moves very quickly. 快速移動的","examples":["With a swift movement, Matthew Jerrold sat upright. 馬修·傑羅德迅速地坐直了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"迅速地","examples":["Wall Street reacted swiftly to yesterday's verdict. 華爾街對昨天的裁決迅速地做出了反應。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"快速移動地","examples":["Lenny moved swiftly and silently across the front lawn. 蘭尼快速並且無聲地穿過前面的草坪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>swift</b> is a small bird with long curved wings. 雨燕","examples":[]}]}]},"tropical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱帶的，熱帶地區的；（天氣）溼熱的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tropical</b> means belonging to or typical of the tropics. 熱帶的","examples":["...tropical diseases. …熱帶疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tropical</b> weather is hot and damp weather typical of the tropics. 溼熱的","examples":["The cool, sweet milk is just what you need in the tropical heat. 清涼的甜牛奶正是你在溼熱的高溫中所需要的。"]}]}]},"tricky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難對付的，棘手的；狡猾的，詭計多端的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a task or problem as <b>tricky</b>, you mean that it is difficult to do or deal with. 難對付的","examples":["Parking can be tricky downtown. 在市中心停車會很難。"]}]}]},"temporary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"暫時的，臨時的；短期的，短暫的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"臨時僱員，臨時工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>temporary</b> lasts for only a limited time. 暫時的","examples":["His job here is only temporary. 他在這兒的工作只是暫時的。","Most adolescent problems are temporary. 多數青春期的問題都是暫時的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"暫時地","examples":["The peace agreement has at least temporarily halted the civil war. 該和平協議至少已暫時中止了內戰。"]}]}]},"technical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"工藝的，技術的；專業的，專門的；嚴格按照法律意義的，嚴格按字面解釋的；（尤指體育或藝術等活動）技巧（上）的；與機器（或系統）執行相關的，技術性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（車後架設有機槍的）小卡車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Technical</b> means involving the sorts of machines, processes, and materials that are used in industry, transportation, and communications. 技術的; 工藝的","examples":["In order to reach this limit a number of technical problems will have to be solved. 為了達到這個限度，有許多技術問題得解決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>technical</b> to describe the practical skills and methods used to do an activity such as an art, a craft, or a sport. 技巧的","examples":["Their technical ability is exceptional. 他們的技能是非凡的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Technical</b> language involves using special words to describe the details of a specialized activity. 專業的 (語言)","examples":["The technical term for sunburn is erythema. 曬斑的專業術語是紅斑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"技術上地; 工藝上地","examples":["...the largest and most technically advanced furnace company in the world. …世界上規模最大、技術最先進的鍋爐公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"技巧上地","examples":["While Sade's voice isn't technically brilliant it has a quality which is unmistakable. 雖然薩德的嗓音從技巧上講不是很出色，但它有一種獨特的音質。"]}]}]},"truthful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"誠實的，講真話的；真實的，如實的；（電影、戲劇、書籍等）真實再現的，現實主義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or their comments are <b>truthful</b>, they are honest and do not tell any lies. 誠實的","examples":["Most religions teach you to be truthful. 大多數宗教都教你要誠實。","We've all learned to be fairly truthful about our personal lives. 我們都已學會了對我們的個人生活要相當誠實。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"誠實地","examples":["I answered all their questions truthfully. 我如實地回答了他們的所有問題。"]}]}]},"tender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"溫柔的，親切的；（食物）嫩的，軟的；年幼的，未成熟的；（身體部位）易痛的，一觸即痛的；（植物）纖弱的，嬌嫩的；微妙的，棘手的；（航海）易傾斜的，不穩的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>提出，提供；投標；付錢，償還；出價購買（股票等）；使變脆弱；<古>溫柔地對待"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"投標，投標書；<英>（期貨交易中的）交割意向通知書；（尤指掛在火車頭後的）煤水車；（在大船和口岸之間載運人或貨物的）供應船，補給船；（裝有特別裝置的）輔助救火車；服務車，輔助車輛；照料人，照管人；<美，非正式>（通常裹有麵包屑的）炸雞塊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>tender</b> expresses gentle and caring feelings. 溫柔的","examples":["Her voice was tender, full of pity. 她的聲音很溫柔，充滿了憐憫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone does something at a <b>tender</b> age, you mean that they do it when they are still young and have not had much experience. 幼小的","examples":["He took up the game at the tender age of seven. 他在7歲的小小年紀就開始從事這項運動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Meat or other food that is <b>tender</b> is easy to cut or chew. (肉等食物) 嫩的; 易嚼的","examples":["Cook for a minimum of 2 hours, or until the meat is tender. 至少煮兩個小時，或一直煮到肉軟了為止。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If part of your body is <b>tender</b>, it is sensitive and painful when it is touched. (身體部位) 敏感的; 易觸痛的","examples":["My tummy felt very tender. 我的肚子一碰就痛。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"溫柔地","examples":["Mr. White tenderly embraced his wife. 懷特先生溫柔地擁抱了妻子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"觸痛","examples":["There is still some tenderness in her ankle. 她的腳踝還有些觸痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tender</b> is a formal offer to supply goods or to do a particular job, and a statement of the price that you or your company will charge. If a contract is <b>put out to tender</b>, formal offers are invited. If a company <b>wins a tender</b>, their offer is accepted. 投標","examples":["Builders will then be sent the specifications and asked to submit a tender for the work. 然後建築商們將會接到設計說明並被邀請參與此項工程的投標。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a small boat, such as a dinghy, towed or carried by a yacht or ship 小艇","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company <b>tenders for</b> something, it makes a formal offer to supply goods or do a job for a particular price. 投標","examples":["The staff are forbidden to tender for private-sector work. 員工們禁止投標私營部門的工程。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to give, present, or offer 提出; 提供","examples":[]}]}]},"vacant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（地方）空著的，無人用的；（職位，工作）空缺的；茫然的，失神的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>vacant</b>, it is not being used by anyone. 空著的","examples":["Halfway down the bus was a vacant seat. 這輛公共汽車中部有個空座。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a job or position is <b>vacant</b>, no one is doing it or in it at present, and people can apply for it. 空缺的","examples":["The position of chairman has been vacant for some time. 主席的職位已經空缺一段時間了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>vacant</b> look or expression is one that suggests that someone does not understand something or that they are not thinking about anything in particular. 茫然的","examples":["She had a kind of vacant look on her face. 在她臉上有一種茫然的表情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"茫然地","examples":["He looked vacantly out of the window. 他茫然地望著窗外。"]}]}]},"wealthy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"富有的，豐富的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"富人（the wealthy）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>wealthy</b> has a large amount of money, property, or valuable possessions. 富有的","examples":["...a wealthy international businessman. …一個富有的跨國商人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The wealthy</b> are people who are wealthy. 富人","examples":["The best education should not be available only to the wealthy. 不應該只有富人才能得到最好的教育。"]}]}]},"visible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"看得見的；明顯的，引人注目的；（進出口貿易）有形商品的；（物理）（光）可見的；現有的，可得到的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有形進出口貨物（visibles）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>visible</b>, it can be seen. 可見的","examples":["The warning lights were clearly visible. 警示燈清晰可見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>visible</b> to describe something or someone that people notice or recognize. 明顯的","examples":["The most visible sign of the intensity of the crisis is unemployment. 危機加劇的最明顯跡象是失業情況。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"明顯地","examples":["The Russians were visibly wavering. 俄國人顯然猶豫不決。"]}]}]},"vivid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生動的，逼真的；（顏色）鮮豔的，明亮的；（人的想像）豐富的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe memories and descriptions as <b>vivid</b>, you mean that they are very clear and detailed. (記憶和描寫) 清晰的; 生動逼真的","examples":["People of my generation who lived through World War II have vivid memories of confusion and incompetence. 我們這一代經歷過第二次世界大戰的人都還清晰地記得當時的混亂和無能為力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>vivid</b> is very bright in colour. (顏色) 鮮豔的","examples":["...a vivid blue sky. …碧藍的天空。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"清晰地","examples":["I can vividly remember the feeling of panic. 我能清晰地回憶起那恐慌感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"鮮豔地","examples":["...vividly coloured birds. …色彩豔麗的鳥兒。"]}]}]},"valuable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"值錢的，貴重的；有益的，寶貴的；重要的，珍貴的；可估價的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"貴重品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>valuable</b>, you mean that they are very useful and helpful. 有益的","examples":["Many of our teachers also have valuable academic links with Heidelberg University. 我們的許多教師也和海德堡大學保持著有價值的學術聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Valuable</b> objects are objects that are worth a lot of money. 值錢的","examples":["Just because a camera is old does not mean it is valuable. 並不能因為照相機樣式老就以為它是值錢的。"]}]}]},"violent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"暴力的；（人）有暴力傾向的；含暴力行為的；劇烈的；（風、暴風雨或爆炸）強烈的，猛烈的；帶有強烈憤怒情緒的，激烈的；（顏色的）鮮豔的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>violent</b>, or if they do something that is <b>violent</b>, they use physical force or weapons to hurt, injure, or kill other people. 暴力的","examples":["A quarter of current inmates have committed violent crimes. 四分之一的在押囚犯實施過暴力犯罪。","...violent anti-government demonstrations. …反政府的暴力示威。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>violent</b> event happens suddenly and with great force. 猛烈的","examples":["A violent impact hurtled her forward. 一股劇烈的衝擊力將她猛地向前拋了出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>violent</b>, you mean that it is said, done, or felt very strongly. 強烈的","examples":["Violent opposition to the plan continues. 對該計劃的強烈反對在持續。","He had violent stomach pains. 他有過劇烈的胃痛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>violent</b> death is painful and unexpected, usually because the person who dies has been murdered. 暴力引起的","examples":["...an innocent man who had met a violent death. …一名遭暴力致死的無辜男子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>violent</b> movie or television programme contains a lot of scenes that show violence. 多暴力場景的 (電影或電視節目)","examples":["It was the most violent movie that I have ever seen. 這是我看過的最暴力的電影。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"暴力地","examples":["Some opposition activists have been violently attacked. 一些反對派激進分子遭到了暴力襲擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"劇烈地","examples":["A nearby volcano erupted violently, sending out a hail of molten rock and boiling mud. 一座附近的火山猛烈爆發，噴出大量熔岩和沸騰的泥漿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"強烈地","examples":["He was violently scolded. 他受到了嚴厲叱責。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"謀殺性地","examples":["...a girl who had died violently nine years earlier. …9年前暴亡的一個女孩。"]}]}]},"various":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"各種各樣的；迥異的，千差萬別的"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"不止一個的，各別的"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"不止一個的，各別的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there are <b>various</b> things, you mean there are several different things of the type mentioned. 各種不同的","examples":["His plan is to spread the capital between various building society accounts. 他的計劃是把資金分散到型別不同的建房互助會的賬戶中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a number of things are described as <b>various</b>, they are very different from one another. 非常不同的","examples":["The methods are many and various. 方法很多而且各不相同。"]}]}]},"wicked":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"邪惡的，不道德的；惡作劇的，淘氣的，調皮的；<非正式>很壞的，惡劣的；<非正式>很棒的，極好的；<非正式>令人不快的，令人厭惡的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>極其，非常"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"惡人，邪惡的人（the wicked）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>wicked</b> to describe someone or something that is very bad and deliberately harmful to people. 邪惡的","examples":["She described the shooting as a wicked attack. 她把那次射擊描述成一次邪惡的攻擊。"]}]}]},"typical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"典型的，有代表性的；一貫的，平常的；不出所料，特有的；象徵性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>typical</b> to describe someone or something that shows the most usual characteristics of a particular type of person or thing, and is therefore a good example of that type. (某人或某物) 有典型性的; 有代表性的","examples":["Cheney is everyone's image of a typical cop: a big white guy, six feet, 220 pounds. 切尼是每個人心目中典型的警察形象：高大的白人，身高6英尺，體重220磅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a particular action or feature is <b>typical</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, it shows their usual qualities or characteristics. (行為或特徵) 典型的","examples":["This reluctance to move toward a democratic state is typical of totalitarian regimes. 這種不願朝民主國家邁進的態度是極權主義政體的典型特徵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>typical</b> <b>of</b> a person, situation, or thing, you are criticizing them or complaining about them and saying that they are just as bad or disappointing as you expected them to be. 一貫的 (用於批評或抱怨)","examples":["She threw her hands into the air. \"That is just typical of you, isn't it?\" 她往空中揮揮雙手說，“你一貫就是這個樣子，是不是？”"]}]}]},"admire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"欽佩，仰慕；欣賞，觀賞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>admire</b> someone or something, you like and respect them very much. 欽佩","examples":["I admired her when I first met her and I still think she's marvellous. 我第一次見到她時就欽佩她，而且我現在依然認為她很了不起。","He admired the way she had coped with life. 他欽佩她應對生活的方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>admire</b> someone or something, you look at them with pleasure. 欣賞","examples":["We took time to stop and admire the view. 我們特意停下來欣賞風景。"]}]}]},"achieve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（經努力）達到，取得，實現；獲得成功"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>achieve</b> a particular aim or effect, you succeed in doing it or causing it to happen, usually after a lot of effort. 實現","examples":["There are many who will work hard to achieve these goals. 有很多人會努力工作來實現這些目標。"]}]}]},"amaze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使驚奇，使驚愕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>amazes</b> you, it surprises you very much. 使吃驚; 感到驚訝","examples":["He amazed us by his knowledge of Colorado history. 他對於科羅拉多州歷史的瞭解讓我們吃驚。","The \"Riverside\" restaurant promises a variety of food that never ceases to amaze! “河畔”餐廳承諾提供永遠給人驚奇的多種食品。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"吃驚的","examples":["Most of the cast was amazed by the play's success. 演員班子中的大多數人對這出戏的成功感到吃驚。"]}]}]},"advertise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……做廣告，登廣告；公佈，徵聘；宣揚；使變得顯眼；<古>提醒……注意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>advertise</b> something such as a product, an event, or a job, you tell people about it in newspapers, on television, or on posters in order to encourage them to buy the product, go to the event, or apply for the job. 為…做廣告; 做廣告","examples":["The company is spending heavily to advertise its strongest brands. 該公司在花重金為其最強勢的品牌做廣告。","In 1991, the house was advertised for sale at $49,000. 在1991年，這所房子登出以4.9萬美元出售的廣告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do not <b>advertise</b> the fact that something is the case, you try not to let other people know about it. 宣傳","examples":["There is no need to advertise the fact that you are a single woman. 沒必要宣傳你是個單身女性這一事實。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>advertise</b> <b>for</b> someone to do something for you, for example, to work for you or share your accommodation, you announce it in a newspaper, on television, or on a bulletin board. 登廣告 (尋求職員、合住者等)","examples":["We advertised for staff in a local newspaper. 我們在一份地方報紙上登了廣告招聘員工。"]}]}]},"adopt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"收養；採取，採納，接受；正式透過；選定（名字），承襲（風俗）；移居，定居；提名（某人）為候選人；保持（姿勢）；<英>（地方當局）承擔（道路）維修保養責任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>adopt</b> a new attitude, plan, or way of behaving, you begin to have it. 採納; 採用","examples":["The United Nations General Assembly has adopted a resolution calling on all parties in the conflict to seek a political settlement. 聯合國大會已採納了一項呼籲所有衝突各方尋求政治解決的決議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>adopt</b> someone else's child, you take it into your own family and make it legally your son or daughter. 收養","examples":["There are hundreds of people desperate to adopt a child. 有數以百計的人極其渴望收養小孩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"採納; 採用","examples":["The group is working to promote the adoption of broadband wireless access over long distances. 該集團正在致力於推廣遠距離寬頻無線訪問的採用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"收養","examples":["They gave their babies up for adoption. 他們放棄了自己的嬰兒讓別人收養。"]}]}]},"advise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"通知，告知；勸告，建議"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>advise</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you tell them what you think they should do. 建議","examples":["The minister advised him to leave as soon as possible. 部長建議他儘快離開。","I would strongly advise against it. 我會強烈建議不要這樣做。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an expert <b>advises</b> people <b>on</b> a particular subject, he or she gives them help and information on that subject. (就某話題向某人) 提供諮詢","examples":["...an officer who advises undergraduates from the University on money matters. …一位在錢的問題上向該大學本科生提供諮詢的官員。"]}]}]},"afford":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"買得起；有（時間）做某事；承擔得起；<正式>提供，給予"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Afford）（英、美）阿福德（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cannot afford</b> something, you do not have enough money to pay for it. 支付得起","examples":["My parents can't even afford a new refrigerator. 我父母甚至買不起一臺新冰箱。","The arts should be available to more people at prices they can afford. 藝術品應該以人們支付得起的價格提供給更多人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you cannot <b>afford</b> <b>to</b> do something or allow it to happen, you mean that you must not do it or must prevent it from happening because it would be harmful or embarrassing to you. 承擔得起","examples":["We can't afford to wait. 我們等不起。"]}]}]},"affect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"影響；（疾病）侵襲，感染；（在感情上）深深打動，震撼；<正式> 假裝，佯裝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指影響行為或行動的）情感，感情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>affects</b> a person or thing, it influences them or causes them to change in some way. (某事物) 影響 (某人或物)","examples":["Nicotine adversely affects the functioning of the heart and arteries. 尼古丁對心臟和動脈功能有負面影響。","More than seven million people have been affected by drought. 七百多萬多人受到了乾旱的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a disease <b>affects</b> someone, it causes them to become ill. (疾病) 困擾 (某人)","examples":["Arthritis is a crippling disease which affects people all over the world. 關節炎是一種嚴重影響健康、困擾全人類的疾病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something or someone <b>affects</b> you, they make you feel a strong emotion, especially sadness or pity. (某事物或人) 影響 (某人)","examples":["If Jim had been more independent, the divorce would not have affected him as deeply. 如果吉姆曾經更獨立一些，離婚就不會對他有這麼深的影響了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"to put on an appearance or show of; make a pretence of 假裝","examples":[]}]}]},"announce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"宣佈，公佈；聲稱，鄭重地說；（尤指透過廣播）通知；播報，講解（體育賽事）；通報……的到來；顯示；告知；宣佈競選公職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>announce</b> something, you tell people about it publicly or officially. 宣佈","examples":["He will announce tonight that he is resigning from office. 他今晚將宣佈他要辭職。","She was planning to announce her engagement to Peter. 她在計劃宣佈她與彼得的婚約。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>announce</b> a piece of news or an intention, especially something that people may not like, you say it loudly and clearly, so that everyone you are with can hear it. 宣告","examples":["Peter announced that he had no intention of wasting his time at any university. 彼得宣告他無意在任何一所大學裡浪費他的時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an airport or rail employee <b>announces</b> something, they tell the public about it by means of a loudspeaker system. 廣播","examples":["The loudspeaker announced the arrival of the train. 揚聲器宣佈了那列火車的到達。"]}]}]},"attract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸引；（物體間）產生引力；引起；有吸引力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>attracts</b> people or animals, it has features that cause them to come to it. 吸引","examples":["The Cardiff Bay project is attracting many visitors. 加的夫灣工程吸引著眾多的參觀者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>attracts</b> you, they have particular qualities which cause you to like or admire them. If a particular quality <b>attracts</b> you <b>to</b> a person or thing, it is the reason why you like them. 引起…的興趣","examples":["He wasn't sure he'd got it right, although the theory attracted him by its logic. 他不能確定自己理解是否正確，儘管該理論的邏輯推理引起了他的興趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are attracted</b> <b>to</b> someone, you are interested in them sexually. (性的) 吸引","examples":["In spite of her hostility, she was attracted to him. 儘管心存敵意，她還是被他吸引住了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>attracts</b> support, publicity, or money, it receives support, publicity, or money. 吸引 (支援或資金等)","examples":["President Mwinyi said his country would also like to attract investment from private companies. 姆維尼總統說他的國家也願意吸引私企的投資。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被吸引的","examples":["He was nice looking, but I wasn't deeply attracted to him. 他長得挺好看，但我並沒有被他深深吸引。"]}]}]},"awaken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"喚醒；喚起；使認識到，使意識到"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"醒來；覺醒；意識到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>awaken</b> a feeling in a person means to cause them to start having this feeling. 喚醒(某種感覺)","examples":["The aim of the cruise was to awaken an interest in and an understanding of foreign cultures. 此次巡遊旨在喚起我們對外國文化的興趣和理解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>awaken</b>, or when something or someone <b>awakens</b> you, you wake up. 叫醒","examples":["Unfortunately, Grandma always seems to awaken at awkward moments. 可惜的是，奶奶好像總是在不合適的時間叫醒我。","He was snoring when José awakened him. 侯賽叫醒他的時候他還在打呼嚕。"]}]}]},"approve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"同意，贊成；批准，透過；核准；喜歡，讚賞；<古>證明，顯示；使（廢品或公共土地）升值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>approve of</b> an action, event, or suggestion, you like it or are pleased about it. 喜歡","examples":["Not everyone approves of the festival. 不是每個人都喜歡這個節日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>approve of</b> someone or something, you like and admire them. 讚賞","examples":["You've never approved of Henry, have you? 你從未讚賞過亨利，是吧？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to improve or increase the value of (waste or common land), as by enclosure 使(廢品或公共土地)升值","examples":[]}]}]},"assist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"幫助，協助；<古>參加，出席"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（球賽中的）助攻；資助，幫助"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>assist</b> someone, you help them to do a job or task by doing part of the work for them. (透過分擔一部分工作以) 幫助","examples":["The family decided to assist me with my chores. 家人決定分擔我的瑣事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>assist</b> someone, you give them information, advice, or money. (提供資訊、建議、資金等以) 協助","examples":["The public is urgently requested to assist police in tracing this man. 公眾被緊急要求協助警方追蹤這名男子。","International organizations intensified their activities to locate victims and assist with relief efforts. 各國際組織加強了他們的活動以尋找受害者並協助救援工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>assists</b> <b>in</b> doing a task, it makes the task easier to do. (在做某任務中) 有助益","examples":["...a chemical that assists in the manufacture of proteins. …一種有助於蛋白質的製造的化學物。","Our sales representatives can assist you in selecting suitable investments. 我們的銷售代表在選擇合適的投資方面能幫到您。"]}]}]},"appreciate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"欣賞，鑑賞；理解，明白；感謝，感激；升值，增值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>appreciate</b> something, for example, a piece of music or good food, you like it because you recognize its good qualities. 欣賞","examples":["Anyone can appreciate our music. 任何人都能欣賞我們的音樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>appreciate</b> a situation or problem, you understand it and know what it involves. 理解","examples":["She never really appreciated the depth and bitterness of the family's conflict. 她從未真正理解該家庭矛盾的深度與激烈程度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>appreciate</b> something that someone has done for you or is going to do for you, you are grateful for it. 感激","examples":["Peter stood by me when I most needed it. I'll always appreciate that. 彼得在我最需要時支援了我。我對此將永遠感激。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something that you own <b>appreciates</b> over a period of time, its value increases. 增值","examples":["They don't have any confidence that houses will appreciate in value. 他們對房屋增值沒有一點信心。"]}]}]},"awake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"醒著的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）醒來，喚醒；喚起，激發起；意識到（awake to）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>awake</b> is not sleeping. 醒著的","examples":["I don't stay awake at night worrying about that. 我才不會徹夜不眠為那事兒擔心呢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>wide awake</b> is fully awake and unable to sleep. 毫無睡意的","examples":["I could not relax and still felt wide awake. 我不能放鬆下來，仍然覺得沒有一點兒睡意。"]}]}]},"admit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（勉強）承認；招認，招供；准許進入（某處）；接納，接收（入學）；收治，接收入院；承認……有效；容許，為……留有餘地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>admit</b> that something bad, unpleasant, or embarrassing is true, you agree, often unwillingly, that it is true. 承認 (不好、不快或尷尬的事實)","examples":["I am willing to admit that I do make mistakes. 我願意承認我確實會犯錯誤。","Up to two thirds of 14 to 16 year olds admit to buying alcohol illegally. 14至16歲的少年中有多達2/3的少年承認非法買過酒。","None of these people will admit responsibility for their actions. 這些人中沒有人原意承認為他們的行為負有的責任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is admitted</b> <b>to</b> a hospital, they are taken into the hospital for treatment and kept there until they are well enough to go home. 接收 (入院)","examples":["She was admitted to the hospital with a soaring temperature. 她因高燒被接收入院。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is admitted</b> <b>to</b> an organization or group, they are allowed to join it. 接收 (加入)","examples":["He was admitted to the Académie Culinaire de France. 他被接收加入法國廚藝學會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>admit</b> someone <b>to</b> a place means to allow them to enter it. 准許進入","examples":["Embassy security personnel refused to admit him or his wife. 使館保安人員拒絕讓他或他的妻子進入。"]}]}]},"behave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"行為，表現；起反應，起作用；守規矩，舉止得體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The way that you <b>behave</b> is the way that you do and say things, and the things that you do and say. 行為; 表現","examples":["I couldn't believe these people were behaving in this way. 我無法相信這些人竟這樣行事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In science, the way that something <b>behaves</b> is the things that it does. (科學領域) 運動表現","examples":["Under certain conditions, electrons can behave like waves rather than particles. 在某些條件下，電子能像波而不是粒子那樣運動。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>behave</b> or <b>behave</b> <b>yourself</b>, you act in the way that people think is correct and proper. 使…規矩; 規矩地行事","examples":["You have to behave. 你得守規矩。"]}]}]},"bare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"赤裸的；光禿禿的；無遮蓋的，無裝飾的；僅最基本的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使暴露，使露出"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，許多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body is <b>bare</b>, it is not covered by any clothing. 赤裸的","examples":["She was wearing only a thin robe over a flimsy nightgown, and her feet were bare. 她只在薄薄的睡衣外面穿了件薄袍子，還光著雙腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bare</b> surface is not covered or decorated with anything. 無遮蓋的; 無裝飾的","examples":["They would have liked bare wooden floors throughout the house. 他們本想把整個房子都鋪不加裝飾的原木地板。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a tree or a branch is <b>bare</b>, it has no leaves on it. (樹或樹枝) 沒有樹葉的","examples":["...an old, twisted tree, many of its limbs brittle and bare. …一棵扭曲的老樹，它的樹枝很多是脆弱而光禿的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a room, cupboard, or shelf is <b>bare</b>, it is empty. 空的","examples":["His fridge was bare apart from three very withered tomatoes. 他的冰箱裡除了3個乾癟的番茄之外什麼也沒有。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An area of ground that is <b>bare</b> has no plants growing on it. (土地) 光禿的","examples":["That's probably the most bare, bleak, barren and inhospitable island I've ever seen. 那可能是我見過的最光禿、最荒涼、最貧瘠和最不適合居住的島嶼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone gives you the <b>bare</b> facts or the <b>barest</b> details of something, they tell you only the most basic and important things. 最簡要的","examples":["Newspaper reporters were given nothing but the bare facts by the superintendent in charge of the investigation. 報社記者們只提供了負責該項調查的監管人所提供的一些簡要事實。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>bare</b> minimum or the <b>bare</b> essentials, you mean the very least that is necessary. 基本的","examples":["The army would try to hold the western desert with a bare minimum of forces. 軍隊將盡量用最少的兵力控制西部沙漠。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Bare</b> is used in front of an amount to emphasize how small it is. 僅僅的","examples":["Sales are growing for premium wines, but at a bare 2 percent a year. 優質葡萄酒的銷量在上漲，但每年僅漲2%。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bare</b> something, you uncover it and show it. 使露出","examples":["Walsh bared his teeth in a grin. 沃爾什一笑露出了牙齒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does something <b>with</b> their <b>bare hands</b>, they do it without using any weapons or tools. 徒手","examples":["Police believe the killer punched her to death with his bare hands. 警方認為兇手是徒手擊她至死的。"]}]}]},"bleed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"流血，出血；給……放血；散開，滲開，滲透；榨取（錢財）；（金錢）不斷流失，持續損失；抽掉（氣體或液體）；印成出血版"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"流血，出血；洩出（液體，氣體）；（染料，顏料）滲色，滲開；出血版"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bleed</b>, you lose blood from your body as a result of injury or illness. 流血","examples":["His head had struck the sink and was bleeding. 他的頭撞到了洗臉池上，正在流血。","He was bleeding profusely. 他正大量流血。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the colour of one substance <b>bleeds</b> <b>into</b> the colour of another substance that it is touching, it goes into the other thing so that its colour changes in an undesirable way. (顏色) 摻混","examples":["The colouring pigments from the skins are not allowed to bleed into the grape juice. 這些果皮的色素不允許摻混進葡萄汁中。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"出血","examples":["This results in internal bleeding. 這導致內部出血。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is being bled</b>, money or other resources are gradually being taken away from them. 榨取 (錢財)","examples":["We have been gradually bled for twelve years. 12年來，我們被逐漸榨盡了錢財。"]}]}]},"celebrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"慶祝，慶賀；讚揚，讚美；主持（宗教儀式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>celebrate</b> an occasion or if you <b>celebrate</b>, you do something enjoyable because of a special occasion or to mark someone's success. 慶祝","examples":["I was in a mood to celebrate. 我很想慶祝一番。","Dick celebrated his 60th birthday Monday. 迪克星期一慶祝了他的60歲生日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an organization or country <b>is celebrating</b> an anniversary, it has existed for that length of time and is doing something special because of it. 慶祝 (週年紀念日)","examples":["The society is celebrating its tenth anniversary this year. 該學會今年將舉行10週年年慶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When priests <b>celebrate</b> Holy Communion or Mass, they officially perform the actions and ceremonies that are involved. 主持 (聖餐或彌撒等宗教儀式)","examples":["Pope John Paul celebrated mass today in a city in central Poland. 約翰·保羅教皇今天在位於波蘭中心的一個城市主持了彌撒。"]}]}]},"bless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"求上帝保佑，祈神賜福，祝福；祝聖，使聖潔；讚美上帝；<非正式>（表示驚奇）；將……賜予，使有幸得到；同意，贊成"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英>哎呀，太好啦，太謝謝了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone such as a priest <b>blesses</b> people or things, he or she asks for God's favour and protection for them. 祈求上帝祝福","examples":["...asking for all present to bless this couple and their loving commitment to one another. …請所有在場的人祈求上帝祝福這對夫婦及其對彼此愛的承諾。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bless</b> is used in expressions such as \"God bless\" or \"bless you\" to express affection, thanks, or good wishes. 用於(God bless)，(bless you##bless)等短句中，以表達友愛、謝意或祝福","examples":["\"Bless you, Eva,\" he whispered. “願上帝保佑你，伊娃，”他低聲說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>bless you</b>\" to someone who has just sneezed. 長命百歲 (對打噴嚏的人說的話)","examples":[]}]}]},"breathe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"呼吸；撥出，吐出；吸入；低聲說；透氣；（酒）通氣透香；將……注入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or animals <b>breathe</b>, they take air into their lungs and let it out again. When they <b>breathe</b> smoke or a particular kind of air, they take it into their lungs and let it out again as they breathe. 呼吸","examples":["He stood there breathing deeply and evenly. 他站在那裡深深地、均勻地呼吸。","No American should have to drive out of town to breathe clean air. 任何美國人都不應非得開車出城去呼吸清潔的空氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"呼吸","examples":["Her breathing became slow and heavy. 她的呼吸變得緩慢而沉重。"]}]}]},"compete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"競爭，對抗；爭奪；參加比賽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When one firm or country <b>competes</b> <b>with</b> another, it tries to get people to buy its own goods in preference to those of the other firm or country. You can also say that two firms or countries <b>compete</b>. (與…) 競爭","examples":["The banks have long competed with American Express's charge cards and various shop cards. 這些銀行長期以來一直與美國運通公司的記賬卡和各種商店卡競爭。","Hardware shops are competing fiercely for business. 各五金店正在為搶生意而激烈競爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>compete</b> <b>with</b> someone <b>for</b> something, you try to get it for yourself and stop the other person from getting it. You can also say that two people <b>compete</b> <b>for</b> something. 爭奪","examples":["Kangaroos compete with sheep and cattle for sparse supplies of food and water. 袋鼠與綿羊和牛爭奪為數不多的食物和水的供應。","Young men compete with each other for membership in these societies and fraternities. 年輕人為獲取這些社團和兄弟會的會員身份而相互爭奪。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>compete</b> in a contest or a game, you take part in it. 參加 (競賽或比賽)","examples":["He will be competing in the 100-metre race. 他將參加100米比賽。"]}]}]},"bury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"埋，埋葬；埋藏，隱藏；掩藏情感；把頭/臉埋進……；嵌入，插入；埋頭於，專心於（bury oneself in）；證明……是錯的；<非正式>輕鬆戰勝，擊敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bury</b> something means to put it into a hole in the ground and cover it up with earth. 埋","examples":["They make the charcoal by burying wood in the ground and then slowly burning it. 他們製作木炭時要把木頭埋進地裡，然後讓它慢慢燃燒。","...squirrels who bury nuts and seeds. …將堅果和種子埋起來的松鼠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>bury</b> a dead person means to put their body into a grave and cover it with earth. 埋葬","examples":["Soldiers helped to bury the dead in large communal graves. 士兵們協助將死者埋葬在大型公共墓地裡。","I was horrified that people would think I was dead and bury me alive. 人們會以為我死了而將我活埋的想法讓我極度恐懼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone says they <b>have buried</b> one of their relatives, they mean that one of their relatives has died. 喪失 (親人)","examples":["He had buried his wife some two years before he retired. 他大約在退休前兩年喪妻。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>bury</b> something under a large quantity of things, you put it there, often in order to hide it. 埋藏","examples":["She buried it under some leaves. 她把它埋藏在一些樹葉下。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>buries</b> a place or person, it falls on top of them so that it completely covers them and often harms them in some way. 掩埋","examples":["Latest reports say that mud slides buried entire villages. 最新的報道說泥石流將好幾個村莊整個吞沒。","Their house was buried by a landslide. 他們的房子被一次山體滑坡掩埋了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>bury</b> your head or face in something, you press your head or face against it, often because you are unhappy. 埋進…中","examples":["She buried her face in the pillows. 她把臉埋進枕頭中。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>buries</b> <b>itself</b> somewhere, or if you <b>bury</b> it there, it is pushed very deeply in there. 嵌入","examples":["The missile buried itself deep in the grassy hillside. 導彈深深地嵌入綠色的山坡中。"]}]}]},"combine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）結合，組合；（使）化合；合併，協力；兼有，兼備；兼做，兼辦"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯盟，聯合體；聯合收割機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>combine</b> two or more things or if they <b>combine</b>, they exist together. 使…結合; 結合","examples":["The Church has something to say on how to combine freedom with responsibility. 教會要講一講如何使自由和責任相結合。","Relief workers say it's worse than ever as disease and starvation combine to kill thousands. 援助人員說情況比以往任何時候都糟，因為疾病和飢餓致使數以千計的人死亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>combine</b> two or more things or if they <b>combine</b>, they join together to make a single thing. 使…合為一體; 合為一體","examples":["David Jacobs was given the job of combining the data from these 19 studies into one giant study. 大衛·雅各布斯分到的工作是把這19項研究中的資料合為一項大型研究。","Combine the flour with 3 tablespoons water to make a paste. 把麵粉和3大湯匙的水混合起來做成一個麵糰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two or more groups or organizations <b>combine</b> or if someone <b>combines</b> them, they join to form a single group or organization. 使…合併; 合併","examples":["...an announcement by Steetley and Tarmac of a joint venture that would combine their brick, tile, and concrete operations. …一份由斯蒂特利和塔瑪克公司釋出的將要組建一個將他們的磚、瓦和混凝土生產業務合併起來的合資企業的通知。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>combines</b> two qualities or features, they have both those qualities or features at the same time. 同時具有","examples":["Their system seems to combine the two ideals of strong government and proportional representation. 他們的體制似乎同時具有強有力的政府與比例代表制這兩種理想狀況。","...a clever, far-sighted lawyer who combines legal expertise with social concern. …一位同時具有法律專業知識和社會責任感的聰明而有遠見的律師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>combines</b> two activities, they do them both at the same time. 同時做","examples":["It is possible to combine a career with being a mother. 同時既幹事業又做母親是可能的。"]}]}]},"confuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使糊塗，使迷惑；混淆，弄錯；使複雜化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>confuse</b> two things, you get them mixed up, so that you think one of them is the other one. 混淆","examples":["I always confuse my left with my right. 我總是混淆左右。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>confuse</b> someone means to make it difficult for them to know exactly what is happening or what to do. 使困惑","examples":["My words surprised and confused him. 我的話使他既驚訝又困惑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>confuse</b> a situation means to make it complicated or difficult to understand. 使複雜化","examples":["To further confuse the issue, there is an enormous variation in the amount of sleep people feel happy with. 使這個問題進一步複雜化的是，人們感覺愉快的睡眠時間相差很大。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"混淆","examples":["Use different colours of felt pen on your sketch to avoid confusion. 在草圖上使用不同顏色的氈筆以免混淆。"]}]}]},"communicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳遞資訊，通訊；傳達，傳遞（想法或感情）；傳染（疾病）；（房間或建築）相通，相連；傳輸（熱，力），傳遞（運動）；領受聖餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>communicate</b> <b>with</b> someone, you share or exchange information with them, for example by speaking, writing, or using equipment. You can also say that two people <b>communicate</b>. 交流","examples":["My birth mother has never communicated with me. 我的生母從未與我交流過。","Officials of the CIA depend heavily on e-mail to communicate with each other. 中情局的官員們很大程度上靠電子郵件相互交流。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person <b>communicates</b> <b>with</b> another, they successfully make each other aware of their feelings and ideas. You can also say that two people <b>communicate</b>. 溝通","examples":["He was never good at communicating with the players. 他從不擅長和隊員溝通。","Family therapy showed us how to communicate with each other. 家庭療法向我們展示瞭如何相互溝通。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"交流","examples":["Lithuania hasn't had any direct communication with Moscow. 立陶宛與莫斯科還沒有任何直接的交流。","...use of the radio telephone for communication between controllers and pilots. …無線電話在控制員和飛行員聯絡中的運用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"溝通","examples":["There was a tremendous lack of communication between us. 我們之間極其缺乏溝通。","Good communication with people around you could prove difficult. 與你周圍的人的良好溝通會被證明是很難的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>communicate</b> information, a feeling, or an idea <b>to</b> someone, you let them know about it. 傳達","examples":["They successfully communicate their knowledge to others. 他們成功地把他們的知識傳達給別人。"]}]}]},"deafen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使聾，震聾；（聲音）淹沒，蓋過；使（房間等）隔音"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"變聾，喪失聽覺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a noise <b>deafens</b> you, it is so loud that you cannot hear anything else at the same time. 使…震聾","examples":["The noise of the typewriters deafened her. 打字機的噪音震得她都要聾了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are deafened</b> <b>by</b> something, you are made deaf by it, or are unable to hear for some time. 使聾","examples":["He was deafened by the noise from the gun. 槍聲把他震聾了。"]}]}]},"conclude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"斷定，推斷出；結束，終止；達成，做成，完成；<美>決定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>conclude</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you decide that it is true using the facts you know as a basis. 斷定","examples":["Larry had concluded that he had no choice but to accept Paul's words as the truth. 拉里斷定他別無選擇，只能相信保羅所說為實。","So what can we conclude from this debate? 那麼從這場辯論中我們能推斷出什麼呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>conclude</b>, you say the last thing that you are going to say. 結束 (說話)","examples":["\"It's a waste of time,\" he concluded. “這是浪費時間，”他最後說道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>concludes</b>, or when you <b>conclude</b> it, you end it. 使…結束; 結束","examples":["The evening concluded with dinner and speeches. 這個夜晚以晚宴和演講告一段落。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one person or group <b>concludes</b> an agreement, such as a treaty or business deal, <b>with</b> another, they arrange it. You can also say that two people or groups <b>conclude</b> an agreement. 達成 (協議)","examples":["Mexico and the Philippines have both concluded agreements with their commercial bank creditors. 墨西哥和菲律賓雙方都與他們的商業銀行債權人達成了協議。"]}]}]},"connect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）連線；（使）相通；使接通（電源、水源等）；與……有關係；把……聯絡起來；銜接，聯運；（使）換乘（飛機或火車）；給……接通電話；產生共鳴，契合；建立良好關係；擊中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>connects</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, or if one thing <b>connects</b> <b>to</b> another, or if two things <b>connect</b>, the two things are joined together. (某物、某人) 連線 (某物); (一物與另一物) 相連","examples":["You can connect the speakers to your CD player. 你可以將這些揚聲器與你的鐳射唱機連線起來。","I connected the wires for the transformer. 我給變壓器接上了電線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two things or places <b>connect</b> or if something <b>connects</b> them, they are joined and people or things can pass between them. (兩物或兩地) 相連通","examples":["...the long hallway that connects the rooms. …連線這些房間的長長的過道。","A pedestrian bridge now connects the parking garage with the mall. 現在一座人行橋連通車庫和購物中心。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one train or plane, for example, <b>connects</b> <b>with</b> another, it arrives at a time which allows passengers to change to the other one in order to continue their trip. (與火車、飛機等) 聯運","examples":["...a train connecting with a ferry to Ireland. …一列與通往愛爾蘭的渡船聯運的火車。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a piece of equipment or a place <b>is connected</b> <b>to</b> a source of power or water, it is joined to that source so that it has power or water. 將 (裝置、某地與水源、電源等) 接通","examples":["These appliances should not be connected to power supplies. 這些裝置不應該接通電源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>connect</b> a person or thing <b>with</b> something, you realize that there is a link or relationship between them. 將 (某人、某物與某事物) 聯絡起來","examples":["I hoped he would not connect me with that now-embarrassing review I'd written seven years earlier. 我希望他不會把我和我7年前寫的、現在讀起來令人難堪的評論聯絡起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that <b>connects</b> a person or thing <b>with</b> something else shows or provides a link or relationship between them. 顯示 (某人、某物與某事物) 有關聯","examples":["A search of Brady's house revealed nothing that could connect him with the robberies. 對布雷迪住處的搜查沒有查出可以顯示他同這些搶劫案有關聯的任何線索。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Connect up</b> means the same as . 接通","examples":["The shower is easy to install – it needs only to be connected up to the hot and cold water supply. 淋浴器很容易安裝–只需接上冷熱水即可。"]}]}]},"deepen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變深，加深；（使）變糟，惡化，嚴重；（使）（感情或關係）變深（或更強烈）；加深，完善（瞭解、理解等）；（使）（光線或顏色）變暗，（使）變深；（使）（聲音）變得低沉；深（呼吸），喘（大氣）；（使）（神秘的事物）變得更神秘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation or emotion <b>deepens</b> or if something <b>deepens</b> it, it becomes stronger and more intense. 使加劇; 加劇","examples":["If this is not stopped, the financial crisis will deepen. 如果不加以阻止，金融危機將加劇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>deepen</b> your knowledge or understanding of a subject, you learn more about it and become more interested in it. 使加深","examples":["The course is an exciting opportunity for anyone wishing to deepen their understanding of themselves and other people. 這門課程對於希望加深瞭解自己和他人的人們來說，是個令人興奮的機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a sound <b>deepens</b> or <b>is deepened</b>, it becomes lower in tone. 使變低沉; 變低沉","examples":["The music room had been made to reflect and deepen sounds. 音樂室被打造成可以產生迴音並使聲音變得低沉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If people <b>deepen</b> something, they increase its depth by digging out its lower surface. 加深","examples":["The project would deepen the river from 40 to 45 feet, to allow for larger ships. 這一工程將把河從40英尺加深到45英尺，以透過更大型的船隻。"]}]}]},"define":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……下定義，解釋；闡明，使清楚；標明……界限，明確顯出……輪廓；是……的特徵，為……的特色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>define</b> something, you show, describe, or state clearly what it is and what its limits are, or what it is like. 給…下定義; 解釋","examples":["The Convention Against Torture defines torture as any act that inflicts severe pain or suffering, physical or mental. 《反酷刑條約》把酷刑定義為任何造成嚴重身心疼痛和受苦的行為。"]}]}]},"creep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"爬行，匍匐；躡手躡腳地移動；不知不覺地到來，漸漸出現；蔓生，蔓延；諂媚奉承，巴結；（由於恐懼、厭惡等）起雞皮疙瘩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"討厭的人，獻媚者；（樹籬或牆壁上供動物透過的）牆洞；給幼畜斷奶時吃的固體食物；爬行，緩慢行進；<非正式>毛骨悚然的感覺，戰慄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or animals <b>creep</b> somewhere, they move quietly and slowly. 悄悄地緩慢行進","examples":["Back I go to the hotel and creep up to my room. 我回到旅館，躡手躡腳地進了房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>creeps</b> somewhere, it moves very slowly. 漸漸蔓延","examples":["Mist had crept in again from the sea. 大霧再次從海上漸漸蔓延過來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>creeps</b> in or <b>creeps</b> back, it begins to occur or becomes part of something without people realizing or without them wanting it. 悄悄出現","examples":["Insecurity might creep in. 不安全感可能會悄然而生。","An increasing ratio of mistakes, perhaps induced by tiredness, crept into her game. 可能是因為疲勞，她在比賽中的錯誤率不知不覺地升高了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a rate or number <b>creeps</b> <b>up</b> to a higher level, it gradually reaches that level. 攀升","examples":["The inflation rate has been creeping up to 9.5 per cent. 通貨膨脹率已攀升至9.5％。"]}]}]},"dine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"進餐，吃飯；宴請"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dine</b>, you have dinner. 吃飯","examples":["He dines alone most nights. 大多數晚上他都獨自進餐。"]}]}]},"disappoint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使失望；使破滅，使落空"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things or people <b>disappoint</b> you, they are not as good as you had hoped, or do not do what you hoped they would do. 使失望","examples":["She would do anything she could to please him, but she knew that she was fated to disappoint him. 她願意做任何事情來討好他，但她知道她註定會讓他失望。"]}]}]},"determine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"決定，控制；查明，確定；下定決心；判決，裁定；求出，解出；限定；<古>終止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a particular factor <b>determines</b> the nature of a thing or event, it causes it to be of a particular kind. 決定","examples":["The size of the chicken pieces will determine the cooking time. 雞塊的大小決定烹飪時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>determine</b> a fact means to discover it as a result of investigation. 查明","examples":["The investigation will determine what really happened. 該調查將查明真相。","Experts say testing needs to be done on each contaminant to determine the long-term effects on humans. 專家說需要對每種汙染物進行測試，以查明對人類的長期影響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>determine</b> something, you decide about it or settle it. 決定","examples":["The Baltic people have a right to determine their own future. 波羅的海人民有權決定他們自己的未來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>determine</b> <b>to</b> do something, you make a firm decision to do it. 決心","examples":["He determined to rescue his two countrymen. 他決心要援救他的兩位同胞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"決定","examples":["...the gene which is responsible for male sex determination. …決定男性性別的基因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"決定","examples":["We must take into our own hands the determination of our future. 我們必須將我們未來的決定權掌握在自己手中。"]}]}]},"drown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（聲音）壓過，蓋過；沉浸於，淹沒於；（使）淹死"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>drowns</b> or <b>is drowned</b>, they die because they have gone or been pushed under water and cannot breathe. 溺死","examples":["A child can drown in only a few inches of water. 兒童在僅僅幾英寸深的水中就能溺死。","Last night a boy was drowned in the river. 昨晚一名男孩在那條河裡溺水身亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>drowns</b> a sound, it is so loud that you cannot hear that sound properly. (一聲音) 蓋過 (另一聲音)","examples":["Clapping drowned the speaker's words for a moment. 掌聲蓋過了發言人的說話聲有一陣兒。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing <b>is drowning</b> <b>in</b> something, you are emphasizing that they have a very large amount of it, or are completely covered in it. 淹沒於","examples":["...people who gradually find themselves drowning in debt. …逐漸發現自己深陷債務的人們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drown out</b> means the same as <b>drown</b>. 淹沒 (同drown)","examples":["Their cheers drowned out the protests of demonstrators. 他們的歡呼聲淹沒了示威者的抗議。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is drowning</b> their <b>sorrows</b>, you mean that they are drinking alcohol in order to forget something sad or upsetting that has happened to them. 借酒澆愁","examples":["Carly drowned her sorrows in vodka cocktails at a South Beach nightclub. 卡莉在一家南海灘夜總會喝伏特加雞尾酒藉以消愁。"]}]}]},"destroy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破壞，毀滅；殺死，人道毀滅（受傷、生病或危險的動物）；徹底打敗，擊潰；毀掉……的生活，使垮掉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>destroy</b> something means to cause so much damage to it that it is completely ruined or does not exist any more. 摧毀","examples":["That's a sure recipe for destroying the economy and creating chaos. 那是一個摧毀經濟、製造混亂的註定因素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>destroy</b> someone means to ruin their life or to make their situation impossible to bear. 毀掉","examples":["If I was younger or more naive, the criticism would have destroyed me. 要是我年輕點兒或幼稚點兒，這批評可能已經把我毀了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an animal <b>is destroyed</b>, it is killed, either because it is ill or because it is dangerous. 宰殺","examples":["Lindsay was unhurt but the horse had to be destroyed. 林賽沒被傷著，但那匹馬不得不被宰掉。"]}]}]},"dim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"暗淡的，昏暗的；模糊的，看不清的；<非正式>愚笨的，遲鈍的；前景暗淡的，不樂觀的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變暗；變淡漠，失去光澤；（使）變模糊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dim</b> light is not bright. 昏暗的","examples":["She stood waiting in the dim light. 她站在昏暗的燈光下等待著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dim</b> place is rather dark because there is not much light in it. 黑暗的","examples":["The room was dim and cool and quiet. 這房間昏暗、陰冷且安靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dim</b> figure or object is not very easy to see, either because it is in shadow or darkness, or because it is far away. 蒙朧的","examples":["Pete's flashlight picked out the dim figures of Bob and Chang. 皮特的手電筒照射出鮑勃和常的蒙朧身影。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>dim</b> memory or understanding of something, it is difficult to remember or is unclear in your mind. 模糊的","examples":["It seems that the '60s era of social activism is all but a dim memory. 60年代的社會激進主義時代似乎只剩下模糊的記憶。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If the future of something is <b>dim</b>, you have no reason to feel hopeful or positive about it. 悲觀的","examples":["The prospects for a peaceful solution are dim. 找到和平解決方案的前景渺茫。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>dim</b>, you think that they are stupid. 愚蠢的","examples":["Sometimes he thought George was a bit dim. 有時他覺得喬治有點兒笨。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"昏暗地","examples":["Two lamps burned dimly. 兩盞油燈昏暗地燃燒著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"蒙朧地","examples":["The shoreline could be dimly seen. 海岸線隱約可見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"模糊地","examples":["Christina dimly recalled the procedure. 克里斯蒂娜隱約地記起了那個步驟。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dim</b> a light or if it <b>dims</b>, it becomes less bright. 使變暗; 變暗","examples":["Dim the lighting – it is unpleasant to lie with a bright light shining in your eyes. 把燈光調暗–在刺眼的燈光下躺著不舒服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your future, hopes, or emotions <b>dim</b> or if something <b>dims</b> them, they become less good or less strong. 使變暗淡; 變暗淡","examples":["Their economic prospects have dimmed. 他們的經濟前景變得暗淡了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your memories <b>dim</b> or if something <b>dims</b> them, they become less clear in your mind. 使變模糊; 變模糊","examples":["Their memory of what happened has dimmed. 他們對所發生的事的記憶變得模糊了。"]}]}]},"educate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在學校）教育；教導，培養；教導，培養"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone, especially a child, <b>is educated</b>, he or she is taught at a school or college. 教育","examples":["He was educated at Yale and Stanford. 他是在耶魯和斯坦福接受的教育。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>educate</b> people means to teach them better ways of doing something or a better way of living. 教育","examples":["...World AIDS Day, an event designed to educate people about AIDS. …世界艾滋病日，一項旨在教育人們瞭解艾滋病的活動。"]}]}]},"edit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"編輯，校訂；編選；剪輯；主編"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"編輯，校訂，剪輯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>edit</b> a text such as an article or a book, you correct and adapt it so that it is suitable for publishing. 編輯","examples":["The majority of contracts give the publisher the right to edit a book after it's done. 大多數合同都會賦予出版商在書稿完成後進行編輯的權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>edit</b> a book or a series of books, you collect several pieces of writing by different authors and prepare them for publishing. 編選","examples":["This collection of essays is edited by Ellen Knight. 這本散文集是由埃倫·奈特編選的。","He edits the literary journal, Murmur. 他編輯了《私語》這本文學雜誌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>edit</b> a film or a television or radio programme, you choose some of what has been filmed or recorded and arrange it in a particular order. 剪輯","examples":["He taught me to edit and splice film. 他教我剪輯合成影片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who <b>edits</b> a newspaper, magazine, or journal is in charge of it. 主編","examples":["I used to edit the college paper in the old days. 我過去曾主編過大學校報。"]}]}]},"employ":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"僱用；使用，利用；忙於，從事（be employed in）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"受僱（in the employ of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or company <b>employs</b> you, they pay you to work for them. 僱用","examples":["The company employs 18 workers. 該公司僱用18位職工。","More than 3,000 local workers are employed in the tourism industry. 超過3000名本地工人受僱於旅遊業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>employ</b> certain methods, materials, or expressions, you use them. 使用","examples":["The group will employ a mix of tactics to achieve its aim. 該團體將運用混合策略來實現其目標。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your time <b>is employed</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you are using the time you have to do that thing. 利用","examples":["Your time could be usefully employed in attending night classes. 你的時間可以被有效地利用來上夜課。"]}]}]},"emphasize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"強調，著重；重讀（單詞或短語）；使突出（或明顯）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>emphasize</b> something means to indicate that it is particularly important or true, or to draw special attention to it. 強調","examples":["But it's also been emphasized that no major policy changes can be expected to come out of the meeting. 但是也強調，這次會議預期不會做出重大政策改變。"]}]}]},"enable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使能夠，使可能；啟用，啟動；准許，授權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>enables</b> you <b>to</b> do a particular thing, they give you the opportunity to do it. 使能夠","examples":["The new test should enable doctors to detect the disease early. 新的檢驗使醫生能在早期發現該種疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>enable</b> something <b>to</b> happen means to make it possible for it to happen. 使成為可能","examples":["The hot sun enables the grapes to reach optimum ripeness. 炙熱的陽光使葡萄能達到最佳成熟狀態。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>enable</b> someone <b>to</b> do something means to give them permission or the right to do it. 允許","examples":["...legislation which enables young people to do a form of alternative service. …允許年輕人透過一種替代性服務來服刑的立法。"]}]}]},"erase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抹去，擦掉；刪除；忘卻；消除，消滅；（易）被擦掉，（易）被抹去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>erase</b> a thought or feeling, you destroy it completely so that you can no longer remember something or no longer feel a particular emotion. 抹去; 消除","examples":["They are desperate to erase the memory of that last defeat. 他們急於抹去上次失敗的記憶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>erase</b> sound that has been recorded on a tape or information which has been stored in a computer, you completely remove or destroy it. 抹掉; 刪除","examples":["An intruder broke into the campaign headquarters and managed to erase 17,000 names from computer files. 一名入侵者闖入作戰指揮部，設法刪除了電腦檔案中的17000個名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>erase</b> something such as writing or a mark, you remove it, usually by rubbing it with a cloth. 擦掉 (字跡)","examples":[]}]}]},"engage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"僱用，聘請；參加，從事；吸引，引起；與……交戰，開戰；（使）（機器）齧合，接合；<舊>預定（膳食，地方等）；適應，與……有密切關係；允諾，簽約保證；（運動員或擊劍手）使（兵器）交結在一起；佔用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>engage in</b> an activity, you do it or are actively involved with it. 從事","examples":["I have never engaged in drug trafficking. 我從來沒有從事過販毒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>engage with</b> something or <b>with</b> a group of people, you get involved with that thing or group and feel that you are connected with it or have real contact with it. 使融入","examples":["She found it hard to engage with office life. 她發現難以融入辦公室生活。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>engages</b> you or your attention or interest, it keeps you interested in it and thinking about it. 吸引","examples":["They never learned skills to engage the attention of the others. 他們從來沒有學過吸引別人注意的技巧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>engage</b> someone <b>in</b> conversation, you have a conversation with them. 使加入","examples":["They tried to engage him in conversation. 他們試圖使他加入談話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>engage</b> someone to do a particular job, you appoint them to do it. 聘","examples":["We engaged the services of a famous engineer. 我們聘了一位有名的工程師來幫忙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"密切關係","examples":["...the candidate's apparent lack of engagement with younger voters. …該候選人明顯缺乏與年輕選民的接觸。"]}]}]},"empty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"空的；空洞的，無意義的；空虛的；無知的，愚蠢的；無用的，徒勞的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"清空；變空；流入；使失去"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"空容器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>empty</b> place, vehicle, or container is one that has no people or things in it. 空的","examples":["The room was bare and empty. 房間空蕩蕩的。","...empty cans of beer. …空啤酒罐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>empty</b> gesture, threat, or relationship has no real value or meaning. 無實在意義的","examples":["His father had threatened disinheritance, but both men had known it was an empty threat. 他父親威脅要剝奪他的繼承權，但是兩人都知道這是虛張聲勢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person's life or a period of time as <b>empty</b>, you mean that nothing interesting or valuable happens in it. 空虛的","examples":["My life was very hectic but empty before I met him. 我的生活在遇見他之前忙碌卻空虛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>feel</b> <b>empty</b>, you feel unhappy and have no energy, usually because you are very tired or have just experienced something upsetting. 消沉的","examples":["I feel so empty, my life just doesn't seem worth living any more. 我感到非常消沉，我的生活簡直好像不值得再過下去了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>empty</b> a container, or <b>empty</b> something out of it, you remove its contents, especially by tipping it up. 倒空","examples":["I emptied the ashtray. 我倒空了菸灰缸。","Empty the noodles and liquid into a serving bowl. 將麵條和湯全部倒入一個上菜的碗中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>empties</b> a room or place, or if it <b>empties</b>, everyone in it goes away. 清場","examples":["The stadium emptied at the end of the first day of games. 體育館在第一天比賽結束的時候清場了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A river or canal that <b>empties into</b> a lake, river, or sea flows into it. 流入","examples":["The Milwaukee River empties into Lake Michigan near that pipe. 密爾沃基河在那條管道附近流入密歇根湖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Empties</b> are bottles or containers that no longer have anything in them. 空容器","examples":["After breakfast we'll take the empties down in the sack. 早餐後我們要用袋子把空瓶子拿下去。"]}]}]},"explode":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）爆炸，（使）爆破；急劇擴大，激增；（情感）迸發，爆發；推翻，破除；爆響，發出巨響；迅速移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object such as a bomb <b>explodes</b> or if someone or something <b>explodes</b> it, it bursts loudly and with great force, often causing damage or injury. 使爆炸; 爆炸","examples":["They were clearing up when the second bomb exploded. 他們在清理時第二顆炸彈爆炸了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>explodes</b> a theory or myth, they prove that it is wrong or impossible. 推翻 (理論等)","examples":["Electricity privatization has exploded the myth of cheap nuclear power. 電力私有化打破了廉價核電力的神話。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>explodes</b>, they express strong feelings suddenly and violently. (情感) 迸發","examples":["Do you fear that you'll burst into tears or explode with anger in front of her? 你害怕在她面前突然大哭或勃然大怒嗎？","\"What happened!\" I exploded. “出什麼事了！”我情緒爆發了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>explodes</b>, it increases suddenly and rapidly in number or intensity. 暴漲","examples":["The population explodes to 40,000 during the tourist season. 旅遊季節人數暴漲至4萬。"]}]}]},"frustrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使懊惱，使沮喪；挫敗，阻撓；受挫"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古>痛苦的，受挫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>frustrates</b> you, it upsets or angers you because you are unable to do anything about the problems it creates. 使懊喪","examples":["These questions frustrated me. 這些問題使我懊喪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>frustrates</b> a plan or attempt to do something, they prevent it from succeeding. 挫敗","examples":["The government has deliberately frustrated his efforts to gain work permits for his foreign staff. 政府蓄意挫敗了他為其外國員工取得工作許可證的努力。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"懊喪的","examples":["Roberta felt frustrated and angry. 羅伯塔感到又懊喪又生氣。"]}]}]},"fade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逐漸消失；（使）褪色，（使）變暗；枯萎，凋謝；變得虛弱；退步；（車輛的剎車因摩擦發熱而）暫時失靈；（使）（電影或電視畫面）淡入（或淡出）另一畫面；變得默默無聞，變得無關緊要；（高爾夫球）偏離直線；<美，非正式>接受（擲骰子者）的打賭"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"淡入，淡出；褪色，變暗；（高爾夫球運動員故意擊出的）向右偏離球"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平淡的，乏味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a coloured object <b>fades</b> or when the light <b>fades</b> it, it gradually becomes paler. 使褪色; 褪色","examples":["All colour fades – especially under the impact of direct sunlight. 所有顏色都會褪色–尤其是在直射陽光的影響下。","No matter how soft the light is, it still fades carpets and curtains in every room. 不論光線多麼柔和，它仍然會使每個房間的地毯和窗簾褪色。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"褪色的","examples":["...a girl in a faded dress. …一個穿褪色連衣裙的女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When light <b>fades</b>, it slowly becomes less bright. When a sound <b>fades</b>, it slowly becomes less loud. 逐漸變暗; 逐漸變弱","examples":["Seaton lay on his bed and gazed at the ceiling as the light faded. 西頓躺在床上凝視著天花板， 那時光線逐漸變暗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If memories, feelings, or possibilities <b>fade</b>, they slowly become less intense or less strong. 逐漸變弱","examples":["Sympathy for the rebels, the government claims, is beginning to fade. 政府聲稱對造反者的同情在開始減弱。","Prospects for peace had already started to fade. 和平的前景已開始變得暗淡。"]}]}]},"found":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"創辦，成立；建造，興建；根據，以……為基礎；熔鑄，鑄造"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偶然（或意外）發現的；（藝術）原汁原味的；裝備好的；<英>（用餐、供暖）不另外收費的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"找到，找回；發現，發覺；（經過研究）找出，查明（find 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Found</b> is the past tense and past participle of . find的過去時和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an institution, company, or organization <b>is founded</b> by someone or by a group of people, they get it started, often by providing the necessary money. 成立","examples":["The New York Free-Loan Society was founded in 1892. 紐約無息貸款協會成立於1892年。","His father founded the American Socialist Party. 他的父親建立了美國社會黨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a town, important building, or other place <b>is founded</b> by someone or by a group of people, they cause it to be built. 興建","examples":["The town was founded in 1610. 該城鎮興建於1610年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"成立","examples":["...the foundation of the National Association of Evangelicals in 1942. …1942年全國福音協會的成立。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cast (a material, such as metal or glass) by melting and pouring into a mould (將金屬或玻璃熔化後倒進模型裡)澆鑄","examples":[]}]}]},"frequent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"頻繁的，經常性的；<古>間隔很近的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"常去，常出入於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>frequent</b>, it happens often. 頻繁的","examples":["Bordeaux is on the main Paris-Madrid line so there are frequent trains. 波爾多位於巴黎至馬德里的鐵路主幹線上，因此有頻繁的列車。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"經常地","examples":["Iron and folic acid supplements are frequently given to pregnant women. 鐵和葉酸補充劑常給孕婦服用。"]}]}]},"fasten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"關緊，鎖好（門窗）；（使）牢固，（使）固定；握住，咬住；盯住……不放，集中注意力於……；纏著，糾纏；繫牢，扣緊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>fasten</b> something, you close it by means of buttons or a strap, or some other device. If something <b>fastens</b> with buttons or straps, you can close it in this way. 扣緊; 繫牢","examples":["She got quickly into her Mini and fastened the seat-belt. 她迅速鑽進她的迷你車並繫好安全帶。","Her long fair hair was fastened at the nape of her neck by an elastic band. 她長長的金髮用一根橡皮筋紮在了脖子後面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fasten</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you attach the first thing to the second, for example, with a piece of string or tape. 把…系在","examples":["There were no instructions on how to fasten the carrying strap to the box. 沒有如何把揹帶系在箱子上的說明。"]}]}]},"heal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"痊癒，康復；（感情創傷）癒合，（情感）恢復常態；（使）（裂痕、創傷）彌合，（使）和好；止息（爭鬥），調停；修復（對土地的破壞）；減輕（痛苦）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a broken bone or other injury <b>heals</b>, or if someone or something <b>heals</b> it, it becomes healthy and normal again. 治癒; 痊癒","examples":["Within six weeks the bruising had gone, but it was six months before it all healed. 6周內青瘀已經消退了，可是傷在6個月後才完全癒合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>heal</b> something such as a rift or a wound, or if it <b>heals</b>, the situation is put right so that people are friendly or happy again. 彌合","examples":["We have begun to heal the wounds of war in our society. 我們已經開始撫平戰爭帶給這個社會的創傷。"]}]}]},"hesitate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猶豫，不願意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hesitate</b>, you do not speak or act for a short time, usually because you are uncertain, embarrassed, or worried about what you are going to say or do. 遲疑","examples":["The telephone rang. Catherine hesitated, debating whether to answer it. 電話響了。凱瑟琳遲疑著，考慮是否接聽。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遲疑","examples":["Asked if he would go back, Mr. Searle said after some hesitation, \"I'll have to think about that.\" 當被問及他是否願意回去時，瑟爾先生遲疑了一下後說：“我得考慮一下。”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hesitate</b> <b>to</b> do something, you delay doing it or are unwilling to do it, usually because you are not certain it would be right. If you do not <b>hesitate</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it immediately. 遲疑; 不願意","examples":["Some parents hesitate to take these steps because they suspect that their child is exaggerating. 一些家長遲遲不肯採取這些措施，因為他們懷疑自己的孩子在誇大其詞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>hesitate</b> in expressions such as \"<b>don't hesitate to call me</b>\" or \"<b>don't hesitate to contact us</b>\" when you are telling someone that they should do something as soon as it needs to be done and should not worry about disturbing other people. 遲疑 (僅用於否定祈使句)","examples":["In the event of difficulties, please do not hesitate to contact our Customer Service Department. 如有困難，請不要遲疑，與我們的客戶服務部聯絡。"]}]}]},"inform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"通知，告知；告發，檢舉（inform on）；賦特徵於，滲透；瞭解，熟悉；影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>inform</b> someone <b>of</b> something, you tell them about it. 告知","examples":["They would inform him of any progress they had made. 他們將把自己所取得的任何進展都告訴他。","My daughter informed me that she was pregnant. 我女兒告訴我她懷孕了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation or activity <b>is informed</b> by an idea or a quality, that idea or quality is very noticeable in it. 瀰漫 (思想或品質等)","examples":["All great songs are informed by a certain sadness and tension. 所有動聽的歌曲無不瀰漫著某種傷感和緊繃感。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>informs on</b> a person, they give information about the person to the police or another authority, which causes the person to be suspected or proved guilty of doing something bad. 檢舉","examples":["Thousands of American citizens have informed on these organized crime syndicates. 成千上萬的美國公民檢舉了這些有組織的犯罪集團。"]}]}]},"kneel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跪著，跪下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>kneel</b>, you bend your legs so that your knees are touching the ground. 跪下","examples":["She knelt by the bed and prayed. 她跪在床邊禱告。","Other people were kneeling, but she just sat. 別人都跪下，但她只是坐著。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kneel down</b> means the same as . 跪下","examples":["She kneeled down beside him. 她在他身邊跪下。"]}]}]},"lengthen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使延長，加長"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"延長，變長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>lengthens</b> or when you <b>lengthen</b> it, it increases in length. 使變長; 變長","examples":["The evening shadows were lengthening. 傍晚的影子正在變長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>lengthens</b> or when you <b>lengthen</b> it, it lasts for a longer time than it did previously. 使延長; 延長","examples":["Vacations have lengthened and the work week has shortened. 假期延長了，工作周變短了。"]}]}]},"impress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使欽佩，使留下深刻印象；使意識到（重要性或嚴重性等）；使銘記；壓，壓印；外加（電流，電勢）；傳送；強徵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"壓印，印記"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>impresses</b> you, you feel great admiration for it. 使欽佩","examples":["What impressed him most was their speed. 最令他欽佩的是他們的速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>impress</b> something <b>on</b> someone, you make them understand its importance or degree. 使明白 (重要性或程度)","examples":["I had always impressed upon the children that if they worked hard they would succeed in life. 我過去總是讓孩子們明白，生活中如果他們努力就會成功。","I've impressed upon them the need for more professionalism. 我已讓他們明白更高專業性的需要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>impresses</b> <b>itself on</b> your mind, you notice and remember it. 使銘記在心","examples":["But this change has not yet impressed itself on the minds of the public. 但是這種變化仍沒有使公眾對此銘記在心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>impresses</b> you <b>as</b> a particular thing, usually a good one, they give you the impression of being that thing. 使留下印象","examples":["It didn't impress me as a good place to live. 那地方沒有給我留下適合居住的印象。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"to commandeer or coerce (men or things) into government service; press-gang 橫徵暴斂; 強徵入伍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"使欽佩的","examples":["I was very impressed by one young man at my lectures. 來上我課的一個年輕人讓我很欽佩。"]}]}]},"inspect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"檢查，審視；檢閱，視察；進行檢查，進行視察"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>inspect</b> something, you look at every part of it carefully in order to find out about it or check that it is all right. 檢查; 檢驗","examples":["Elaine went outside to inspect the playing field. 伊萊恩到外邊去檢查運動場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an official <b>inspects</b> a place or a group of people, they visit it and check it carefully, for example, in order to find out whether regulations are being obeyed. 視察","examples":["The Public Utilities Commission inspects us once a year. 公用設施委員會每年到我們這裡視察一次。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"檢查; 檢驗","examples":["\"Excellent work,\" he said when he had completed his inspection of the painted doors. “幹得好，”他在檢查完刷過油漆的門之後說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"視察","examples":["Officers making a routine inspection of the vessel found fifty kilograms of cocaine. 對船隻做例行檢查的警官們發現了50公斤可卡因。"]}]}]},"injure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使受傷，弄傷；損害，傷害（名譽、自尊等）；<古>冤枉（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>injure</b> a person or animal, you damage some part of their body. 使受傷; 傷害","examples":["A number of bombs have exploded, seriously injuring at least five people. 一些炸彈爆炸了，至少5人嚴重受傷。"]}]}]},"investigate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偵察（某事）；調查（某人）；研究"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone, especially an official, <b>investigates</b> an event, situation, or claim, they try to find out what happened or what is the truth. 調查","examples":["They're still investigating the accident. 他們還在調查這個事故。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"調查","examples":["He ordered an investigation into the affair. 他下令對此事進行調查。"]}]}]},"loosen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變鬆，（使）鬆開；放寬（限制、法律等）；使（關係）弱化，疏遠；使（腸道）在排洩前暢通"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>loosens</b> restrictions or laws, for example, they make them less strict or severe. 放寬 (限制或法律)","examples":["Many business groups have been pressing the Federal Reserve to loosen interest rates. 許多商業團體一直在施加壓力要求聯邦儲備局放寬利率。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>loosens</b> the ties between people or groups of people, or if the ties <b>loosen</b>, they become weaker. 疏遠; 減弱","examples":["The Federal Republic must loosen its ties with the United States. 聯邦共和國必須疏遠同美國的關係。","The deputy leader is cautious about loosening the links with the unions. 副領導對疏遠和工會的關係持謹慎態度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>loosen</b> your clothing or something that is tied or fastened, you undo it slightly so that it is less tight or less firmly held in place. 略微鬆開","examples":["He reached up to loosen the scarf around his neck. 他抬手鬆了鬆脖子上的圍巾。","Loosen the bolt so the bars can be turned. 鬆開螺栓，這樣那些木板就能被翻過來了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>loosen</b> your grip on something, or if your grip <b>loosens</b>, you hold it less tightly. 放開","examples":["Harry loosened his grip momentarily and Anna wriggled free. 哈里剛鬆了一下手，安娜就掙脫了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a government or organization <b>loosens</b> its grip on a group of people or an activity, or if its grip <b>loosens</b>, it begins to have less control over it. 放鬆 (控制)","examples":["There is no sign that the party will loosen its grip on the country. 沒有任何跡象表明該黨會放鬆對這個國家的控制。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"放寬","examples":["Domestic conditions did not justify a loosening of monetary policy. 國內的條件不適宜放寬貨幣政策。"]}]}]},"interrupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打斷，打擾；使暫停，使中斷；阻斷，遮擋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>interrupt</b> someone who is speaking, you say or do something that causes them to stop. 打斷","examples":["Turkin tapped him on the shoulder. \"Sorry to interrupt, Colonel.\" 圖爾金拍了拍他肩膀說：“對不起，上校，打斷你一下。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>interrupts</b> a process or activity, they stop it for a period of time. 妨礙","examples":["People kept nosing around the place, interrupting my work. 人們在這周圍不斷檢視著，打斷了我的工作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>interrupts</b> a line, surface, or view, it stops it from being continuous or makes it look irregular. 遮住","examples":["Taller plants interrupt the views from the house. 高的樹木遮住了房子外的視線。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"打斷","examples":["The sudden interruption stopped Justin in mid-sentence. 賈斯廷話說到一半時被突然打斷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"中斷","examples":["...interruptions in the supply of food and fuel. …食品和燃料供應的中斷。"]}]}]},"memorize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"記住，熟記"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>memorize</b> something, you learn it so that you can remember it exactly. 記住","examples":["He studied his map, trying to memorize the way to Rose's street. 他研究了地圖，努力記住去羅絲家那條街的路。"]}]}]},"manage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"管理，處理；操縱，控制；設法做到，勉力完成；騰出時間參加；湊合著活下去，支撐；調教（人或動物）；竟搞得，竟做出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>manage</b> an organization, business, or system, or the people who work in it, you are responsible for controlling them. 管理; 經營 (機構、企業、系統等)","examples":["Within two years he was managing the shop. 兩年內他經營著該商店。","There is a lack of confidence in the government's ability to manage the economy. 對政府管理經濟的能力缺乏信心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>manage</b> time, money, or other resources, you deal with them carefully and do not waste them. 管理 (時間、金錢等)","examples":["In a busy world, managing your time is increasingly important. 在一個忙碌的世界裡，管理好你的時間越來越重要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>manage</b> <b>to</b> do something, especially something difficult, you succeed in doing it. 設法 (做成某事)","examples":["Somehow, he'd managed to persuade Kay to buy one for him. 不管怎麼說，他已設法說服了凱給他買一個。","I managed to pull myself up onto a wet, sloping ledge. 我設法爬上了一個潮溼的傾斜巖脊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you can <b>manage</b> an amount of time or money for something, you mean that you can afford to spend that time or money on it. 騰出 (時間、金錢等)","examples":["I try to manage about five hours a week on my bike. 我儘量每週抽出約五小時騎腳踏車。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>managed</b> a particular response, such as a laugh or a greeting, you mean that it was difficult for them to do it because they were feeling sad or upset. 勉強做出 (某種回應)","examples":["He looked dazed as he spoke to reporters, managing only a weak smile. 他和記者說話時顯得恍惚，只勉強做了個淡淡的微笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>manage</b>, you succeed in coping with a difficult situation. 成功應對","examples":["She had managed perfectly well without medication for three years. 她3年沒用藥，卻成功地挺了過來。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>I can manage</b>\" or \"<b>I'll manage</b>\" as a way of refusing someone's offer of help and insisting on doing something by yourself. 我能應付","examples":["I know you mean well, but I can manage by myself. 我知道你是好意，但我自己能應付得了。"]}]}]},"mend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"縫補，修補；修理；癒合，痊癒；彌合（分歧），解決（爭端）；（給火）添燃料"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"好轉，復甦；修理過的地方，補丁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mend</b> a tear or a hole in a piece of clothing, you repair it by sewing it. 修補","examples":["Men say that we are only good for cooking their meals and mending their socks. 男人們說我們只擅長給他們做飯和補襪子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or a part of their body <b>mends</b> or <b>is mended</b>, they get better after they have been ill or have had an injury. 使 (病情、傷情) 好轉; (病情、傷情) 好轉","examples":["I'm feeling a lot better. The cut aches, but it's mending. 我感覺好多了。傷口還疼，但正在好轉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you try to <b>mend</b> divisions between people, you try to end the disagreements or quarrels between them. 彌合 (分歧)","examples":["He sent Evans as his personal envoy to discuss ways to mend relations between the two countries. 他派埃文斯作為他的私人代表去商討改善兩國關係的途徑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>mend</b> something that is broken or not working, you repair it, so that it works properly or can be used. 修理","examples":["They took a long time to mend the roof. 他們花了好長時間修繕房頂。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a relationship or situation is <b>on the mend</b> after a difficult or unsuccessful period, it is improving. (關係) 在改善; (形勢) 在好轉","examples":["More evidence that the economy was on the mend was needed. 需要更多表明經濟在好轉的證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>on the mend</b> after an illness or injury, you are recovering from it. (病情、傷情) 在好轉","examples":["The baby had been ill but seemed to be on the mend. 這嬰兒生病了，但看起來病情正在好轉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone who has been behaving badly <b>mends</b> their <b>ways</b>, they begin to behave well. 改過自新","examples":["He has promised drastic disciplinary action if they do not mend their ways. 如果他們不改過自新的話，他已保證會嚴懲不貸。"]}]}]},"melt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）熔化，融化；（逐漸）減少，消失；（使）軟化，變得溫柔；變成，融入"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"融化，融合；熔化的金屬，熔化物；一次的熔化量；<美>乳酪三明治"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a solid substance <b>melts</b> or when you <b>melt</b> it, it changes to a liquid, usually because it has been heated. 使融化; 融化","examples":["The snow had melted, but the lake was still frozen solid. 雪已經融化了，但湖面仍然凍得結結實實。","Meanwhile, melt the white chocolate in a bowl suspended over simmering water. 同時，把碗架在快燒開的水上，融化碗裡的白巧克力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as your feelings <b>melt</b>, they suddenly disappear and you no longer feel them. 消散","examples":["His anxiety about the outcome melted, only to return later. 他對結果的焦慮消失了，但過後又來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>melts into</b> something such as darkness or a crowd of people, they become difficult to see, for example because they are moving away from you or are the same colour as the background. 消失 (在黑暗、人群等中)","examples":["The youths dispersed and melted into the darkness. 年輕人們散開了，消失在夜色中。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Melt away</b> means the same as . 同(melt)","examples":["When he heard these words, Scot felt his inner doubts melt away. 聽到這些話，斯科特覺得內心的疑慮消失了。"]}]}]},"participate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"參加，參與；<古>分擔，分享；<古>具有，帶有（特殊的性質）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>participate</b> <b>in</b> an activity, you take part in it. 參加","examples":["They expected him to participate in the ceremony. 他們希望他參加這個典禮。","Over half the population of this country participate in sports. 這個國家一半以上的人參加體育運動。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"參加","examples":["...participation in religious activities. …對宗教活動的參與。"]}]}]},"pave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"用石板（或磚）鋪（路）；為……鋪平道路，創造條件（pave the way for sth./sb.）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a road or an area of ground <b>has been paved</b>, it has been covered with asphalt or concrete, so that it is suitable for walking or driving on. 鋪 (路)","examples":["The avenue had never been paved, and deep mud made it impassable in winter. 這條大街從來沒有鋪過，深泥使其在冬天無法通行。"]}]}]},"owe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"欠（錢），負賬；應該做，應給予；欠（人情），應該感激；歸因於，歸功於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>owe</b> money <b>to</b> someone, they have lent it to you and you have not yet paid it back. 欠","examples":["The company owes money to more than 60 banks. 這家公司欠六十多家銀行的錢。","Blake already owed him nearly $50. 布萊克已經欠了他近$50。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>owes</b> a particular quality or their success <b>to</b> a person or thing, they only have it because of that person or thing. 把…歸功於","examples":["I always suspected she owed her first job to her friendship with Roger. 我總是覺得她得到她的第一份工作是由於她與羅傑的友誼。","He owed his survival to his strength as a swimmer. 他把自己倖免遇難歸功於自己會游泳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>owe</b> a great deal <b>to</b> someone or something, you mean that they have helped you or influenced you a lot, and you feel very grateful to them. 感激","examples":["As a musician I owe much to the radio station in my home town. 作為一名音樂家，我非常感激我家鄉的廣播電臺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something <b>owes</b> a great deal to a person or thing, you mean that it exists, is successful, or has its particular form mainly because of them. 得益於","examples":["The island's present economy owes a good deal to tourism. 該島現在的經濟大大得益於旅遊業。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that you <b>owe</b> someone gratitude, respect, or loyalty, you mean that they deserve it from you. 應給予","examples":["Perhaps we owe these people more respect. 也許我們應該給予這些人更多的尊敬。","I owe you an apology; you must have found my attitude very annoying. 我應向你道歉，你一定覺得我的態度挺讓人討厭的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that you <b>owe it to</b> someone to do something, you mean that you should do that thing because they deserve it. 該為 (某人做某事)","examples":["I can't go; I owe it to him to stay. 我不能走，為了他我該留下來。","You owe it to yourself to get some professional help. 你為了自己著想也該去尋求一些專業的幫助了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>owing to</b> when you are introducing the reason for something. 由於","examples":["Owing to staff shortages, there was no food on the plane. 由於工作人員不足，飛機上沒有食物。"]}]}]},"observe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"注意到，觀察到；注視，監視；（在科學研究中）觀測，發現；說話，評論；遵守（規則、法律等）；慶祝（節日），紀念（某人或事件）；靜默，默哀；舉行，參加"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>observe</b> a person or thing, you watch them carefully, especially in order to learn something about them. 觀察","examples":["Olson also studies and observes the behaviour of babies. 奧爾森還研究並觀察嬰兒的行為。","Are there any classes I could observe? 有我可以觀摩的課嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>observe</b> someone or something, you see or notice them. 觀察到","examples":["In 1664 Hooke observed a reddish spot on the surface of the planet. 1664年，胡克觀察到了那顆行星表面的一個微紅的斑點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>observe</b> that something is the case, you make a remark or comment about it, especially when it is something you have noticed and thought about a lot. 評述","examples":["We observe that the first calls for radical transformation did not begin until the period of the industrial revolution. 我們認為，首次要求徹底改革的呼聲直到工業革命時期才出現。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>observe</b> something such as a law or custom, you obey it or follow it. 遵從","examples":["Imposing speed restrictions is easy, but forcing drivers to observe them is trickier. 實行速度限制容易，而迫使司機遵守較難。","The army was observing a ceasefire. 軍隊當時在遵守一項停火協議。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>observe</b> an important day such as a holiday or anniversary, you do something special in order to honour or celebrate it. 慶祝","examples":["...where he will observe Thanksgiving with family members. …在那裡他將與家人一起慶祝感恩節。"]}]}]},"pollute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"汙染，弄髒；玷汙，敗壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>pollute</b> water, air, or land means to make it dirty and dangerous to live in or to use, especially with poisonous chemicals or sewage. 汙染","examples":["Heavy industry pollutes our rivers with noxious chemicals. 重工業排放的有毒化學物質汙染著我們的河流。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受汙染的","examples":["The police have warned the city's inhabitants not to bathe in the polluted river. 警方已經警告本市居民不要在那條被汙染的河裡游泳。"]}]}]},"persuade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"說服，勸服；使相信，使信服；（情形，事件）驅使，敦促"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>persuade</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you cause them to do it by giving them good reasons for doing it. 說服","examples":["My husband persuaded me to come. 我丈夫說服我來的。","We're trying to persuade manufacturers to sell them here. 我們正試圖說服製造商們在這裡銷售它們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>persuades</b> someone <b>to</b> take a particular course of action, it causes them to take that course of action because it is a good reason for doing so. 引發 (某人採取行動)","examples":["It was the lack of privacy that eventually persuaded us to move after Ben was born. 正是因為缺少隱私感才最終迫使我們在本出生後搬了家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>persuade</b> someone that something is true, you say things that eventually make them believe that it is true. 使相信","examples":["I've persuaded Mrs. Tennant that it's time she retired. 我已經使坦南特夫人相信是她該退休的時候了。","We had managed to persuade them that it was worth working with us. 我們已經設法使他們相信和我們一起共事是值得的。"]}]}]},"postpone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推遲，延緩；把……放在次要地位；把……放在後面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>postpone</b> an event, you delay it or arrange for it to take place at a later time than was originally planned. 推遲","examples":["He decided to postpone the expedition until the following day. 他決定將探險活動推遲到第二天。"]}]}]},"perform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"演出，表演；執行，履行（尤指複雜的任務或行動）；執行，表現；起…...作用，有…...功能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>perform</b> a task or action, especially a complicated one, you do it. 做; 執行 (尤指複雜的任務或行動)","examples":["We're looking for people of all ages who have performed outstanding acts of bravery, kindness, or courage. 我們正在尋找各個年齡的、曾有過無畏、善良或英勇之舉的傑出人士。","His council had had to perform miracles on a tiny budget. 他的委員會不得不靠一筆微薄的預算來創造奇蹟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>performs</b> a particular function, it has that function. 行使 (某種功能)","examples":["An engine has many parts, each performing a different function. 一部發動機有很多部件，各自行使不同的功能。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>perform</b> a play, a piece of music, or a dance, you do it in front of an audience. 演出; 演奏","examples":["Gardiner has pursued relentlessly high standards in performing classical music. 加德納在演奏古典音樂方面始終不懈地追求高標準。","This play was first performed in 411 BC. 該劇於公元前411年首次上演。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>performs well</b>, they work well or achieve a good result. If they <b>perform badly</b>, they work badly or achieve a poor result. 表現 (好/不好)","examples":["He had not performed well in his exams. 過去考試他都考得不好。","State-owned industries will always perform poorly. 國有工業將始終經營不善。"]}]}]},"prevent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻止，阻礙；防止，預防；設定障礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>prevent</b> something means to ensure that it does not happen. 預防","examples":["These methods prevent pregnancy. 這些方法預防懷孕。","Further treatment will prevent cancer from developing. 進一步治療將預防癌症惡化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>prevent</b> someone <b>from</b> doing something means to make it impossible for them to do it. 阻止","examples":["He said this would prevent companies from creating new jobs. 他說這將阻止各公司創造新的職位。","Its nationals may be prevented from leaving the country. 其公民可能會被阻止離開該國。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"預防","examples":["...the prevention of heart disease. …心臟病的預防。"]}]}]},"pretend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偽裝，假裝；（玩遊戲時）假扮，裝扮；自詡，自稱（pretend to）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>假裝的，假想的（尤為兒童使用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pretend</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you act in a way that is intended to make people believe that it is the case, although in fact it is not. 假裝 (某事是事實)","examples":["I pretend that things are really okay when they're not. 我在情況不好的時候假裝一切真地沒事。","Sometimes the boy pretended to be asleep. 有時候那個男孩子假裝睡著了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If children or adults <b>pretend</b> <b>that</b> they are doing something, they imagine that they are doing it, for example, as part of a game. 假裝 (在做某事)","examples":["She can sunbathe and pretend she's in Cancun. 她會進行日光浴並假裝她是在坎昆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do not <b>pretend</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you do not claim that it is the case. 假稱","examples":["We do not pretend that the past six years have been without problems for us. 我們不假稱過去的6年對我們來講是沒有問題的。"]}]}]},"pour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傾倒，倒出；（給……）斟，倒（飲料等）；傾瀉，湧流；（人，物）接踵而至，紛至沓來；（雨）傾盆而下；大量注入（資金），捐獻（pour sth. into）；傾訴，傾吐（pour sth. out）；穿上（緊身衣）（pour oneself into）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"灌，注；傾瀉；傾盆大雨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pour</b> a liquid or other substance, you make it flow steadily out of a container by holding the container at an angle. 倒 (液體等)","examples":["Pour a pool of sauce on two plates and arrange the meat neatly. 倒一些醬到兩個盤子裡，然後把肉擺放整齊。","Don poured a generous measure of scotch into a fresh glass. 唐往新杯子裡倒了很多蘇格蘭威士忌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pour</b> someone a drink, you put some of the drink in a cup or glass so that they can drink it. (給某人) 倒 (一杯飲料)","examples":["He got up and poured himself another drink. 他站起身來，給自己又倒了一杯。","She asked Tillie to pour her a cup of coffee. 她叫蒂莉給她倒一杯咖啡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a liquid or other substance <b>pours</b> somewhere, for example, through a hole, it flows quickly and in large quantities. 噴湧","examples":["Blood was pouring from his broken nose. 血正從他破了的鼻子裡噴湧而出。","Tears poured down both our faces. 眼淚在我們兩人臉上嘩嘩地流。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When it rains very heavily, you can say that <b>it is pouring</b>. (雨) 傾盆而下","examples":["It was still pouring outside. 外面依舊大雨傾盆。","The rain was pouring down. 雨在傾盆而下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>pour</b> into or out of a place, they go there quickly and in large numbers. (人) 大量湧至","examples":["Any day now, the Northern forces may pour across the new border. 如今任何一天，北方軍隊都可能大量湧過新邊界。","At six p.m. large groups poured from the numerous offices. 下午6：00，大批人群從無數的辦公室湧出。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as information <b>pours</b> into a place, a lot of it is obtained or given. (資訊等) 大量湧至","examples":["Martin, 78, died yesterday. Tributes poured in from around the globe. 78歲的馬丁於昨日辭世，各種弔唁從全球各地大量湧來。"]}]}]},"pursue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"追求，致力於，執行；繼續探討（或追究、從事）；追逐，跟蹤，追趕；沿著……前行；追求（某人）；力勸（某人）接受聘用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pursue</b> an activity, interest, or plan, you carry it out or follow it. 執行; 貫徹","examples":["He said Japan would continue to pursue the policies laid down at the London summit. 他說日本將繼續貫徹倫敦峰會上確定的方針。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pursue</b> a particular aim or result, you make efforts to achieve it, often over a long period of time. 追求; 努力實現","examples":["He will pursue a trade policy that protects American workers. 他將努力實行保護美國工人的貿易政策。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pursue</b> a particular topic, you try to find out more about it by asking questions. 追問","examples":["If your original request is denied, don't be afraid to pursue the matter. 如果你最初的要求被拒絕了，不要害怕去追問這件事情。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pursue</b> a person, vehicle, or animal, you follow them, usually in order to catch them. 追趕","examples":["She pursued the man who had stolen a woman's bag. 她追趕那個偷了一女士錢包的男子。"]}]}]},"promote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"促進，提倡；升職，晉升；促銷，推廣； 將（運動隊）晉級；使（學生）升年級；負責籌辦，主辦（大型活動，如音樂會或體育比賽）；促使（議會私法議案）透過；使（卒）升格為（尤指後等）；<英>（先打大牌）使（小牌）贏得一墩；使（催化劑）更活潑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>promote</b> something, they help or encourage it to happen, increase, or spread. 促進","examples":["You don't have to sacrifice environmental protection to promote economic growth. 你們沒有必要犧牲環保來促進經濟增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a firm <b>promotes</b> a product, it tries to increase the sales or popularity of that product. 促銷","examples":["...a tour to promote his second solo album. …一場促銷他第二張個人專輯的巡迴演出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is promoted</b>, they are given a more important job or rank in the organization that they work for. 晉升","examples":["I was promoted to editor and then editorial director. 我晉升為編輯，之後又晉升為編輯部主任。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"促進","examples":["The government has pledged to give the promotion of democracy higher priority. 政府已承諾要給民主的促進以更高的優先順序。"]}]}]},"react":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（作出）反應；起化學反應； (對食物等）不良反應，過敏；（股票價格）回跌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>react</b> <b>to</b> something that has happened to you, you behave in a particular way because of it. 作出反應","examples":["They reacted violently to the news. 他們對這條新聞反應強烈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>react against</b> someone's way of behaving, you deliberately behave in a different way because you do not like the way they behave. 反抗","examples":["My father never saved money and perhaps I reacted against that. 我父親從不攢錢，也許我反對這種做法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>react</b> <b>to</b> a substance such as a drug, or <b>to</b> something you have touched, you are affected unpleasantly or made ill by it. (對藥物或其他所碰觸的東西等) 起不良反應","examples":["Someone allergic to milk is likely to react to cheese. 對牛奶過敏的人可能會對乳酪也有不良反應。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When one chemical substance <b>reacts</b> <b>with</b> another, or when two chemical substances <b>react</b>, they combine chemically to form another substance. 起化學反應","examples":["Calcium reacts with water but less violently than sodium and potassium do. 鈣能與水產生化學反應但不如鈉以及鉀那麼劇烈。"]}]}]},"recognize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"認識，辨別出；承認，意識到；（正式或在法律上）認可，承認；讚賞，公認；表揚，表彰；（會議或辯論主席）邀請……發言；（計算機等）自動識別（聲音、印刷字型等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recognize</b> someone or something, you know who that person is or what that thing is. 認出","examples":["The receptionist recognized him at once. 那名接待員馬上認出了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone says that they <b>recognize</b> something, they acknowledge that it exists or that it is true. 承認","examples":["I recognize my own shortcomings. 我承認我自己的那些缺點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people or organizations <b>recognize</b> something as valid, they officially accept it or approve of it. 承認; 贊成","examples":["Many doctors recognize homeopathy as a legitimate form of medicine. 許多醫生承認順勢療法是一種合理的醫療形式。","France is on the point of recognizing the independence of the Baltic States. 法國即將承認波羅的海各國的獨立。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When people <b>recognize</b> the work that someone has done, they show their appreciation of it, often by giving that person an award of some kind. 賞識; 表彰","examples":["The army recognized him as an outstandingly able engineer. 軍隊稱讚他為傑出能幹的工程師。"]}]}]},"recover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"恢復（健康，精神，體力）；康復，復原（be recovered）；（從不愉快的經歷中）恢復；（從弱勢或困境中）好轉，扭轉；重新獲得，尋回；收回（開支、投資等）；恢復（意識、神志或身體狀態）；挽回（地位），彌補（時間損失）；提取（能源或化工品等），回收利用； 給……換上新面"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（軍事操練）槍還原，收槍（the recover）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>recover</b> <b>from</b> an illness or an injury, you become well again. 痊癒; 恢復健康","examples":["He is recovering from a knee injury. 他的膝傷正在痊癒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>recover</b> <b>from</b> an unhappy or unpleasant experience, you stop being upset by it. (從不愉快的經歷中) 恢復","examples":["...a tragedy from which he never fully recovered. …一場他再也沒有完全從中恢復過來的悲劇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>recovers</b> <b>from</b> a period of weakness or difficulty, it improves or gets stronger again. (從弱勢或困境中) 好轉","examples":["He recovered from a 4-2 deficit to reach the quarter-finals. 他從4－2的失利中恢復過來，進入1/4決賽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recover</b> something that has been lost or stolen, you find it or get it back. 重新找回","examples":["Police raided five houses in Brooklyn and recovered stolen goods. 警察突擊搜查了位於布魯克林的5棟住宅，找回了被盜物品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>recover</b> a mental or physical state, it comes back again. For example, if you <b>recover</b> consciousness, you become conscious again. 恢復 (身心狀態或意識)","examples":["She had a severe attack of asthma and it took an hour to recover her breath. 她犯了一次嚴重的哮喘，一個小時之後才恢復正常呼吸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>recover</b> money that you have spent, invested, or lent to someone, you get the same amount back. 收回 (花掉、投資或借出的錢)","examples":["Legal action is being taken to recover the money. 正採取法律措施來收回那筆錢。"]}]}]},"relate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聯絡，使有聯絡；涉及，關於；敘述，講述；認同，理解；相處，交往（描述人們如何交談、相處和對待他人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>relates to</b> a particular subject, it concerns that subject. 與…有關","examples":["Other recommendations relate to the details of how such data is stored. 其他建議與如何儲存這種資料的一些細節有關。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The way that two things <b>relate</b>, or the way that one thing <b>relates</b> <b>to</b> another, is the sort of connection that exists between them. 發生聯絡; 與…相聯絡","examples":["I don't think he understood the dynamics of how the police and the city administration relate. 我認為他不理解警方與市政部門如何發生聯絡的動態原理。","Trainees should be invited to relate new ideas to their past experiences. 應該要求實習生把新想法與他們的以往經歷相聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>relate</b> <b>to</b> someone, you can understand how they feel or behave so that you are able to communicate with them or deal with them easily. 與…息息相通","examples":["He is unable to relate to other people. 他不能夠與別人溝通。"]}]}]},"reduce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"減少，降低；（烹調中）使變濃稠，收汁；<美>節食減肥；使淪為，使陷入（不好的境地）；迫使，使不得不（做）；（透過破裂、燃燒等）使變成，使化為；歸納，簡化；將分數約到（最小項）；（使）進行還原反應；減薄（底片或圖片）；（語音）弱化；使（脫臼，斷骨）復位；<古>攻克，征服（尤指圍攻並佔領城鎮或要塞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reduce</b> something, you make it smaller in size or amount, or less in degree. 使變小","examples":["It reduces the risks of heart disease. 它減小了犯心臟病的危險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is reduced</b> <b>to</b> a weaker or inferior state, they become weaker or inferior as a result of something that happens to them. 使陷入","examples":["They were reduced to extreme poverty. 他們淪落到極度貧困的地步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is reduced</b> <b>to</b> doing something, you mean that they have to do it, although it is unpleasant or embarrassing. 迫使","examples":["He was reduced to begging for a living. 他不得不以乞討為生。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is changed to a different or less complicated form, you can say that it <b>is reduced</b> <b>to</b> that form. 使變成; 使簡化為","examples":["All the buildings in the town have been reduced to rubble. 鎮上所有的建築都變成了瓦礫。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>reduce</b> liquid when you are cooking, or if it <b>reduces</b>, it is boiled in order to make it less in quantity and thicker. 使變稠; 收汁","examples":["Boil the liquid in a small saucepan to reduce it by half. 在小燉鍋中煮沸湯汁使其收到一半的量。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>reduces</b> you <b>to tears</b>, they make you feel so unhappy that you cry. 使…流淚","examples":["The attentions of the media reduced her to tears. 媒體的關注使她流下了眼淚。"]}]}]},"rely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"相信，信賴；依靠，依賴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rely</b> <b>on</b> someone or something, you need them and depend on them in order to live or work properly. 依賴; 依靠","examples":["They relied heavily on the advice of their professional advisers. 他們非常依賴專業顧問的建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>rely</b> <b>on</b> someone to work well or to behave as you want them to, you can trust them to do this. 信任; 信賴","examples":["I know I can rely on you to sort it out. 我知道我可以信賴你來處理此事。"]}]}]},"relax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"休息，（使）放鬆；放心，鎮定；鬆開，（使）鬆弛；放寬（規則或法律等）； 減少（關注），分散（注意力）；燙直（頭髮）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>relax</b> or if something <b>relaxes</b> you, you feel more calm and less worried or tense. 使放心; 放心","examples":["I ought to relax and stop worrying about it. 我應該放心，不再為它擔憂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a part of your body <b>relaxes</b>, or when you <b>relax</b> it, it becomes less stiff or firm. 使放鬆; 放鬆","examples":["Massage is used to relax muscles, relieve stress and improve the circulation. 按摩可用於放鬆肌肉、減輕壓力和促進血液迴圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>relax</b> your grip or hold on something, you hold it less tightly than before. 鬆開","examples":["He gradually relaxed his grip on the arms of the chair. 他漸漸鬆開了那把椅子的一對扶手。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>relax</b> a rule or your control over something, or if it <b>relaxes</b>, it becomes less firm or strong. 放鬆 (規定或控制); 變寬鬆","examples":["Rules governing student conduct have relaxed somewhat in recent years. 管理學生操行的規定最近幾年已經稍微變得寬鬆了。"]}]}]},"remind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提醒，使想起；（因相像）使聯想起（remind sb. of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>reminds</b> you <b>of</b> a fact or event that you already know about, they say something which makes you think about it. 使記起; 使想起","examples":["So she simply welcomed Tim and reminded him of the last time they had met. 因此她只是歡迎了蒂姆，讓他想起他們上次的相遇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>remind</b> in expressions such as <b>Let me remind you that</b> and <b>May I remind you that</b> to introduce a piece of information that you want to emphasize. It may be something that the hearer already knows about or a new piece of information. Sometimes these expressions can sound unfriendly. 提醒 (表強調，語氣較強硬)","examples":["\"Let me remind you,\" said Marianne, \"that Milwaukee is also my home town.\" “讓我提醒你，”瑪麗安娜說，“密爾沃基也是我的家鄉。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>reminds</b> you <b>to</b> do a particular thing, they say something which makes you remember to do it. 提醒","examples":["Can you remind me to buy a bottle of wine? 你能提醒我買一瓶葡萄酒嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>reminds</b> you <b>of</b> another person or thing, you mean that they are similar to the other person or thing and that they make you think about them. 使想起","examples":["She reminds me of the wife of the pilot who used to work for you. 她使我想起曾為你工作過的飛行員之妻。"]}]}]},"renew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"重新開始，中止後繼續；恢復，重新建立（關係）；使（受到損毀或丟失後）重獲新生；更換，更新；重申，重複強調；延長（執照、合同等）的有效期，使續簽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>renew</b> an activity, you begin it again. 重新開始","examples":["He renewed his attack on government policy toward Europe. 他重新開始抨擊政府的歐洲政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>renew</b> something such as a licence or a contract, you extend the period of time for which it is valid. 延長 (執照、合同的) 有效期","examples":["Larry's landlord threatened not to renew his lease. 拉里的房東威脅說不再讓他續租。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that something <b>is renewed</b> when it grows again or is replaced after it has been destroyed or lost. 獲得新生; (遭毀壞或損失後) 再生","examples":["Nature's repair process is slow and steady, with cells being constantly renewed. 自然的修復過程緩慢而穩定，在此過程中細胞不斷再生。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>renew</b> a relationship <b>with</b> someone, you start it again after you have not seen them or have not been friendly with them for some time. 恢復 (關係)","examples":["When the two men met again after the war they renewed their friendship. 當這兩個男人戰後重逢時，他們恢復了友誼。"]}]}]},"remain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逗留，留下；剩餘，遺留；保持不變，一直是；仍需去做（或處理）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"剩餘（物），遺蹟；遺體，殘骸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>remains</b> in a particular state or condition, they stay in that state or condition and do not change. 繼續; 保持","examples":["The three men remained silent. 這3個人保持沉默。","The government remained in control. 政府繼續控制著局勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>remains</b> <b>to be</b> done, it has not yet been done and still needs to be done. 剩下; 餘留; 待做","examples":["Major questions remain to be answered about his work. 關於他工作的主要問題仍有待回答。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>remain</b> in a place, you stay there and do not move away. 留在; 停留","examples":["They have asked the residents to remain in their homes. 他們已經要求居民待在自己家裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that something <b>remains</b> when it still exists. 繼續存在; 仍然存在","examples":["The wider problem remains. 更廣泛的問題依然存在。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>remains</b> <b>of</b> something are the parts of it that are left after most of it has been taken away or destroyed. 殘餘; 殘跡","examples":["They were cleaning up the remains of their picnic. 他們正在打掃野餐的殘餘物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>remains</b> of a person or animal are the parts of their body that are left after they have died, sometimes after they have been dead for a long time. (人的) 遺體; (動物的) 殘骸","examples":["The unrecognizable remains of a man had been found. 發現了一具無法辨認的男子的遺體。"]}]}]},"remove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"移開，拿開；除去，廢除；把……免職，開除；脫下，摘下；<史，南非> 依法迫遷；遠離；不同於，迥異於；<舊> 搬家"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式> 距離，間距；<史>（一些英國學校中的）年級"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>remove</b> something from a place, you take it away. 移開","examples":["As soon as the cake is done, remove it from the oven. 蛋糕一烤好，就把它從烤箱裡移出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>remove</b> clothing, you take it off. 脫下; 摘下","examples":["He removed his jacket. 他脫掉了夾克。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>remove</b> a stain from something, you make the stain disappear by treating it with a chemical or by washing it. 去除 (痕跡); 洗掉 (汙漬)","examples":["This treatment removes the most stubborn stains. 這個處理方法能洗掉最頑固的汙漬。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If people <b>remove</b> someone <b>from</b> power or <b>from</b> something such as a committee, they stop them from being in power or being a member of the committee. 把…免職","examples":["The student senate voted to remove Fuller from office. 大學評議會投票將富勒免職了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>remove</b> an obstacle, a restriction, or a problem, you get rid of it. 去除 (障礙或限制); 解決 (問題)","examples":["The agreement removes the last serious obstacle to the signing of the arms treaty. 該協議為武器條約的簽署去除了最後一個重大障礙。"]}]}]},"replace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"取代；（用……）替換，（以……）接替；更換， 賠還；把......放回原處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person <b>replaces</b> another, the first is used or acts instead of the second. 代替; 取代","examples":["One species of tree replaces another as a forest ages. 隨著森林老化，一種樹會取代另一種樹。","...the lawyer who replaced Robert as chairman of the company. …取代羅伯特成為公司主席的那位律師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>replace</b> one thing or person <b>with</b> another, you put something or someone else in their place to do their job. 用…代替; 用…替換","examples":["I clean out all the grease and replace it with oil so it works better in very low temperatures. 我清除掉了所有的油脂，以油替換，因此它在很低的溫度下運轉得更好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>replace</b> something that is broken, damaged, or lost, you get a new one to use instead. 換下 (壞的); 換上 (新的)","examples":["The shower that we put in a few years back has broken and we cannot afford to replace it. 我們幾年前安裝的淋浴器壞了，但沒錢換新的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>replace</b> something, you put it back where it was before. 把…放回原處","examples":["Replace the caps on the bottles. 把瓶蓋蓋回到瓶子上。"]}]}]},"restrict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"限制，控制（大小、數量、範圍）；限制（活動或行為），妨礙；約束，管束；（以法規）限制；封鎖（訊息）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>restrict</b> something, you put a limit on it in order to reduce it or prevent it from becoming too great. 限制","examples":["There is talk of raising the admission requirements to restrict the number of students on campus. 有提高錄取條件來限制校園裡學生數量的說法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>restrict</b> the movement or actions of someone or something means to prevent them from moving or acting freely. 限制","examples":["The government imprisoned dissidents, forbade travel, and restricted the press. 政府關押了持不同政見者，禁止了出遊，限制了新聞自由。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>restrict</b> someone or their activities <b>to</b> one thing, they can only do, have, or deal with that thing. If you <b>restrict</b> them <b>to</b> one place, they cannot go anywhere else. 限制 (在某範圍)","examples":["For the first two weeks, patients are restricted to the grounds. 最初兩週病人們被限制在院內活動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>restrict</b> something <b>to</b> a particular group, only that group can do it or have it. If you <b>restrict</b> something <b>to</b> a particular place, it is allowed only in that place. 限定","examples":["Trustees had decided to restrict university entry to about 30 percent of applicants. 董事們已經決定把大學入學率限定在申請人數的30％左右。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"限制","examples":["Since the costs of science were rising faster than inflation, some restriction on funding was necessary. 既然科學成本上漲快於通貨膨脹，資助上的一些限制是必要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"限制","examples":["...the justification for this restriction of individual liberty. …對限制個人自由的辯護。"]}]}]},"resist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻擋，抵制；抵抗，回擊；耐得住，抵擋；使不受……的傷害，抗（傷害）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"保護塗層（防染色、著釉等），防染材料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>resist</b> something such as a change, you refuse to accept it and try to prevent it. 抵制","examples":["They resisted our attempts to modernize the distribution of books. 他們抵制我們將書籍發行現代化的努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>resist</b> someone or <b>resist</b> an attack by them, you fight back against them. 反抗","examples":["The man was shot outside his house as he tried to resist arrest. 那個男人因為試圖拒捕在他住宅外被擊中。","When she attempted to cut his nails he resisted. 當她試圖給他剪指甲時，他反抗了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>resist</b> doing something, or <b>resist</b> the temptation to do it, you stop yourself from doing it although you would like to do it. 抗拒","examples":["Congress should resist the temptation to try quick economic fixes. 國會應該抗拒嘗試快速經濟調整的誘惑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>resists</b> damage of some kind, they are not damaged. 抵抗住","examples":["...bodies trained and toughened to resist the cold. …經過鍛鍊和強化能抵抗寒冷的身體。"]}]}]},"respond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（口頭或書面）回答，回應；作出反應，回應；（對某種治療）有良好反應；（橋牌）（對同伴的叫牌）作應叫；（會眾對牧師）應答，唱和；承擔責任"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（教堂用語）應答，唱和；（建築）壁聯（與牆相連支承拱的半柱或半墩，尤指在拱廊兩端）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>respond</b> to something that is done or said, you react to it by doing or saying something yourself. 回應","examples":["They are likely to respond positively to the president's request for aid. 他們有可能積極地回應該總統的援助請求。","The army responded with gunfire and tear gas. 軍方以炮火和催淚彈回應。","\"I have no idea,\" she responded. “我不知道，”她回應道。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>respond</b> <b>to</b> a need, crisis, or challenge, you take the necessary or appropriate action. 應對","examples":["This modest group size allows our teachers to respond to the needs of each student. 這個適中的小組規模使得我們的老師們可以應對每個學生的需要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a patient or their injury or illness <b>is responding</b> <b>to</b> treatment, the treatment is working and they are getting better. 作出反映","examples":["I'm pleased to say that he is now doing well and responding to treatment. 我很高興地說他現在正在順利恢復，治療是有效果的。"]}]}]},"rid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……去掉，使……去除；擺脫，消除"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"得到解脫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>get rid of</b> something that you do not want or do not like, you take action so that you no longer have it or suffer from it. 處理掉某物; 擺脫掉某物","examples":["The owner needs to get rid of the car for financial reasons. 出於經濟原因，車主需要處理掉這輛車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get rid of</b> someone who is causing problems for you or who you do not like, you do something to prevent them from affecting you anymore, for example by making them leave. 擺脫掉某人; 攆走某人","examples":["He believed that his manager wanted to get rid of him for personal reasons. 他認為他的經理出於個人原因想要攆走他。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rid</b> a place or person <b>of</b> something undesirable or unwanted, you succeed in removing it completely from that place or person. 使 (某地、某人) 擺脫","examples":["The proposals are an attempt to rid the country of political corruption. 這些提議是使該國擺脫政治腐敗的一種嘗試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rid</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>of</b> something you do not want, you take action so that you no longer have it or are no longer affected by it. 使 (自己) 擺脫","examples":["Why couldn't he ever rid himself of those thoughts, those worries? 為什麼他始終擺脫不了那些想法、那些擔憂呢？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are rid of</b> someone or something that you did not want or that caused problems for you, they are no longer with you or causing problems for you. 擺脫了的","examples":["The family had sought a way to be rid of her and the problems she had caused them. 這家人尋求了一個擺脫她以及她給他們製造的麻煩的辦法。"]}]}]},"reveal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"揭示，透露；表明，證明；展示，顯示；（透過神或超自然手段）啟示"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電視節目最後的）揭示；門側，窗側"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>reveal</b> something means to make people aware of it. 透露; 顯示","examples":["She has refused to reveal the whereabouts of her daughter. 她已拒絕透露她女兒的行蹤。","A survey of the American diet has revealed that a growing number of people are overweight. 一項有關美國人日常飲食的調查表明越來越多的人超重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reveal</b> something that has been out of sight, you uncover it so that people can see it. 使顯露; 揭露","examples":["In the principal room, a grey carpet was removed to reveal the original pine floor. 在主房間裡，一塊灰色的地毯被挪開了，使原有的松木地板露了出來。"]}]}]},"rob":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搶劫，盜取；使喪失，剝奪；<英>（足球）奪（對手）的球；<非正式> 敲……竹槓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is robbed</b>, they have money or property stolen from them. 盜竊; 搶劫","examples":["Mrs. Yacoub was robbed of her designer watch at her Westchester home. 雅各布夫人的名牌手錶在她威斯特切斯特的家中被人盜走了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is robbed</b> <b>of</b> something that they deserve, have, or need, it is taken away from them. 搶走","examples":["When Miles Davis died jazz was robbed of its most distinctive voice. 當邁爾斯•戴維斯去世時，爵士樂裡最具特色的聲音也被奪走了。"]}]}]},"represent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"代表；為……代言（辯護）；代表（選區、政黨、群體）任國會議員（或其他立法機構議員）；代表（國家、學校、城鎮等參加比賽）；作為某人的代表（尤指在正式場合或儀式中）；等於，相當於；（符號或象徵）代表，表示；象徵，體現；展示，描繪；（尤指不真實地）描述，描寫；扮演；<正式>明確講述，清楚說明；聲稱；正式提出（意見、抗議等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone such as a lawyer or a politician <b>represents</b> a person, a group of people, or a place, they act on behalf of that person, group, or place. 代表; 代理","examples":["...the politicians we elect to represent us. …我們所選的代表我們的政治家。","...Richard Bolling, a Democrat who represented Missouri in Congress. …理查德•博林，一個在國會中代表密蘇里州的民主黨人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>represent</b> a person or group at an official event, you go there on their behalf. 代表 (出席)","examples":["The general secretary may represent the president at official ceremonies. 秘書長可以在官方儀式上代表主席。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>represent</b> your country or city in a competition or sports event, you take part in it on behalf of the country or city where you live. 代表 (參賽)","examples":["My only aim is to represent the United States at the Olympics. 我惟一的目標就是代表美國參加奧運會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a group of people or things <b>is</b> well <b>represented</b> in a particular activity or in a particular place, a lot of them can be found there. 使有代表性","examples":["Women are already well represented in the area of TV drama. 女性在電視戲劇領域已經佔有很大比例。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a sign or symbol <b>represents</b> something, it is accepted as meaning that thing. 代表; 表示; 象徵","examples":["...a black dot in the middle of the circle is supposed to represent the source of the radiation. …圓圈中央的黑點應該表示射線的來源。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>represent</b> an idea or quality means to be a symbol or an expression of that idea or quality. 代表; 象徵; 反映","examples":["New York represents everything that's great about America. 紐約象徵著美國偉大的一切。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>represent</b> a person or thing <b>as</b> a particular thing, you describe them as being that thing. 描寫; 描繪","examples":["The popular press tends to represent him as an environmental guru. 大眾媒體傾向於把他描繪成環保領袖。"]}]}]},"seek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"尋找；尋求，謀求；請求（幫助），徵求（意見）；試圖，設法；找出，找到（seek sb./sth. out）；自然地向……移動；<古>去，前往（某地）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>seek</b> something such as a job or a place to live, you try to find one. 尋找","examples":["They have had to seek work as labourers. 他們只好找體力活來做。","Four people who sought refuge in the Italian embassy have left voluntarily. 到義大利大使館尋求避難的四個人已經自願離開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>seeks</b> something, they try to obtain it. 謀求","examples":["The prosecutors have warned they will seek the death penalty. 原告已警告說他們會努力爭取死刑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>seek</b> someone's help or advice, you contact them in order to ask for it. 請求; 徵求","examples":["Always seek professional legal advice before entering into any agreement. 在簽訂任何協議之前，一定要徵求法律專家的意見。","On important issues, they seek a second opinion. 在重要問題上，他們都徵求別人的意見。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>seek</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try to do it. 力圖; 設法","examples":["He also denied that he would seek to annex the country. 他還否認了他企圖併吞該國。"]}]}]},"shorten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"縮短，使變短，減少；縮寫（名字、單詞等），刪節"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"縮短，變短"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shorten</b> an event or the length of time that something lasts, or if it <b>shortens</b>, it does not last as long as it would otherwise do or as it used to do. 縮短","examples":["Smoking can shorten your life. 吸菸會縮短你的壽命。","The trading day is shortened in observance of the Labour Day holiday. 交易日為了慶祝勞動節而縮短。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shorten</b> an object or if it <b>shortens</b>, it becomes smaller in length. 使變短; 變短","examples":["Her father paid $5,000 for an operation to shorten her nose. 她父親為一個縮短她的鼻子的手術花了$5000。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>shorten</b> a name or other word, you change it by removing some of the letters. 縮寫","examples":["Originally called Lili, she eventually shortened her name to Lee. 她原本叫莉莉，最後她把名字縮寫成了莉。"]}]}]},"sew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"縫，縫紉，縫補"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sew</b> something such as clothes, you make them or repair them by joining pieces of cloth together by passing thread through them with a needle. 縫製; 縫補","examples":["She sewed the dresses on the sewing machine. 她在縫紉機上縫製了這些衣服。","Anyone can sew on a button, including you. 任何人都能縫鈕釦，包括你。"]}]}]},"seize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抓住，捉住；（用武力）奪取，佔領；逮捕，捉拿；沒收，扣押；把握（機會等）；（感覺、疼痛）侵襲，控制；吸引（注意力），喚起（想象力）；<正式>理解，掌握；意識到，得知（be seized of）；（有活動部件的機器，機器的活動部件）咬住，卡住；<英，法律>依法佔有（be seized of）；<史>具有（財產）的終身保有權（be seized of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>seize</b> something, you take hold of it quickly, firmly, and forcefully. 抓住","examples":["\"Leigh,\" he said seizing my arm to hold me back. “莉，”他說著便抓住我的胳膊把我拉了回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a group of people <b>seize</b> a place or <b>seize</b> control of it, they take control of it quickly and suddenly, using force. 攻佔; 奪取","examples":["Troops have seized the airport and railway terminals. 軍隊已經佔領了機場和鐵路終點站。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a government or other authority <b>seize</b> someone's property, they take it from them, often by force. 沒收; 查封","examples":["Police were reported to have seized all copies of this morning's edition of the newspaper. 據報道警方已沒收了該報紙今早所有的出刊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone <b>is seized</b>, they are arrested or captured. 逮捕; 俘獲","examples":["UN officials say two military observers were seized by the Khmer Rouge yesterday. 聯合國官員稱，昨天有兩名軍事觀察員被紅色高棉組織俘獲。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>seize</b> an opportunity, you take advantage of it and do something that you want to do. 抓住 (機會)","examples":["During the riots hundreds of people seized the opportunity to steal property. 暴亂期間數以百計的人乘機竊取財物。"]}]}]},"shrink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）縮小，減少；（通常指布料、衣服等洗後）縮水，皺縮；退縮，畏縮；畏避，迴避（工作、責任等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式> 精神病學家，心理學家；收縮；畏縮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If cloth or clothing <b>shrinks</b>, it becomes smaller in size, usually as a result of being washed. 縮水","examples":["People were short in those days – or else those military uniforms all shrank in the wash! 那個年代人們很矮–要麼就是那些軍裝在洗滌時全都縮水了！"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shrink</b> <b>away from</b> someone or something, you move away from them because you are frightened, shocked, or disgusted by them. (因害怕、震驚或厭惡) 避開","examples":["One child shrinks away from me when I try to talk to him. 我試著和這個孩子說話時，他避開了我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do not <b>shrink</b> <b>from</b> a task or duty, you do it even though it is unpleasant or dangerous. 逃避 (不愉快或危險的事)","examples":["He is decisive and won't shrink from a fight. 他很果斷，而且不會逃避戰鬥。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shrinks</b> or something else <b>shrinks</b> it, it becomes smaller. 使縮小; 縮小","examples":["The vast forests of West Africa have shrunk. 西非那片廣袤的森林已經縮小了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shrink</b> is a psychiatrist. 精神病醫生","examples":["I've seen a shrink already. 我已經看過了精神病醫生。"]}]}]},"starve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）捱餓，餓死；使極其缺乏，需要"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>starve</b>, they suffer greatly from lack of food which sometimes leads to their death. 捱餓; 餓死","examples":["A number of the prisoners we saw are starving. 我們看到的許多囚犯都快餓死了。","In the 1930s, millions of Ukrainians starved to death or were deported. 在20世紀30年代，數百萬烏克蘭人或因飢餓而死，或被驅逐出境。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>starve</b> someone means not to give them any food. 使捱餓","examples":["He said the only alternative was to starve the people, and he said this could not be allowed to happen. 他說惟一的其他辦法是餓那些人，但他說這種做法是不允許的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is starved</b> <b>of</b> something that they need, they are suffering because they are not getting enough of it. 使極其缺乏","examples":["The electricity industry is not the only one to have been starved of investment. 電力行業並不是惟一極其缺乏投資的行業。"]}]}]},"spoil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破壞，糟蹋；溺愛，寵壞；善待，格外關照；（食物）變質，腐敗；使（選票）作廢；極度渴望，躍躍欲試；<古>搶劫（人，地方），掠奪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"贓物，戰利品（the spoils）；成功所帶來的好處（spoils）；（開掘時挖出的）廢土，廢泥土"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spoil</b> something, you prevent it from being successful or satisfactory. 毀壞; 破壞","examples":["It's important not to let mistakes spoil your life. 重要的是不要讓錯誤毀了你的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>spoil</b> children, you give them everything they want or ask for. This is considered to have a bad effect on a child's character. 嬌慣","examples":["Grandparents are often tempted to spoil their grandchildren whenever they come to visit. 每次祖父母來訪，常常禁不住要嬌慣孫輩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>spoil</b> <b>yourself</b> or <b>spoil</b> another person, you give yourself or them something nice as a treat or do something special for them. 犒勞; 優待","examples":["Spoil yourself with a new perfume this summer. 今年夏天買瓶新香水犒勞一下自己吧。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If food <b>spoils</b> or if it <b>is spoiled</b>, it is no longer fit to be eaten. 使 (食物) 變壞; (食物) 變壞","examples":["We all know that fats spoil by becoming rancid. 我們都知道油脂發臭就變壞了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>spoiled for choice</b> or <b>spoilt for choice</b>, you mean that they have a great many things of the same type to choose from. (因可選的太多而) 不知作何選擇是好","examples":[]}]}]},"suffer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因疾病、痛苦、悲傷等）受苦，受折磨；經受，遭受（壞事）；變差，變糟；<古>容許，允許；<古>受處決"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>suffer</b> pain, you feel it in your body or in your mind. 經受 (痛苦); 受苦","examples":["Within a few days she had become seriously ill, suffering great pain and discomfort. 在幾天時間裡她已病得很重，經受了極大的痛苦和不適。","He suffered terribly the last few days. 他過去的幾天痛苦不堪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>suffer</b> something bad, you are in a situation in which something painful, harmful, or very unpleasant happens to you. 遭受","examples":["The peace process has suffered a serious blow now. 該和平程序現已受到一次沉重的打擊。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>suffer from</b> an illness or from some other bad condition, you are badly affected by it. (因疾病等糟糕的處境而) 受苦","examples":["He was eventually diagnosed as suffering from terminal cancer. 他最後被診斷為癌症晚期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>suffer</b>, you are badly affected by an event or situation. 受難","examples":["There are few who have not suffered. 幾乎無人免於受難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>suffers</b>, it becomes worse because it has not been given enough attention or is in a bad situation. 變差","examples":["I'm not surprised that your studies are suffering. 你功課變差，我並不感到驚訝。"]}]}]},"suggest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提議，建議；推薦，舉薦；顯示，表明；暗示，暗指；使人想到，使人聯想到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>suggest</b> something, you put forward a plan or idea for someone to think about. 建議","examples":["He suggested a link between class size and test results of seven-year-olds. 他建議把7歲兒童的班級大小和考試結果相關聯。","I suggest you ask him some specific questions about his past. 我建議你問問他有關他的過去的一些具體問題。","No one has suggested how this might occur. 沒有人提議過這事如何開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>suggest</b> the name of a person or place, you recommend them to someone. 推薦","examples":["Could you suggest someone to advise me how to do this? 你能推薦一個人來建議我怎麼做這件事嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>suggest</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you say something which you believe is the case. 認為是","examples":["I'm not suggesting that is what is happening. 我並不是說那就是所發生的情況。","It is wrong to suggest that there are easy alternatives. 認為有容易的選擇是錯誤的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>suggests</b> another, it implies it or makes you think that it might be the case. 暗示","examples":["Earlier reports suggested that a meeting would take place on Sunday. 早期的報道暗示了一次會議將在週日舉行。"]}]}]},"smooth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（表面）光滑的，平坦的，平整的；順利的，無困難的；（動作等）流暢的，（騎馬、航行等）平穩的；（人）圓滑的，八面玲瓏的；（液體混合物）均勻的，不結塊的；（聲音）圓潤的，悅耳的；（味道、氣味等）醇和的，不烈的；（網球拍或軟式壁球拍無線結的一面）光面，滑面"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撫平，弄平滑；輕輕地塗擦（液體、面霜等）；解決問題，消除困難；修改（圖表、曲線等）以減少不規則現象；緩和；使優雅"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"平滑部分"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"光滑地，平穩地，流暢地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>smooth</b> surface has no roughness, lumps, or holes. 光滑的","examples":["...a rich cream that keeps skin soft and smooth. …一種可以保持皮膚柔軟光滑的富含營養的護膚霜。","...a smooth surface such as glass. …玻璃般光滑的表面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>smooth</b> liquid or mixture has been mixed well so that it has no lumps. 均勻的; (液體或混合物) 細膩的","examples":["Continue whisking until the mixture looks smooth and creamy. 繼續攪拌直至混合物看上去均勻且呈奶油狀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a drink such as wine, whisky, or coffee as <b>smooth</b>, you mean that it is not bitter and is pleasant to drink. (酒或咖啡等飲料) 醇和的","examples":["This makes the whiskies much smoother. 這使威士忌酒醇和得多。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>smooth</b> line or movement has no sudden breaks or changes in direction or speed. (線條或動作) 流暢的","examples":["This exercise is done in one smooth motion. 這套體操是由一個流暢的動作完成的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>smooth</b> ride, flight, or sea crossing is very comfortable because there are no unpleasant movements. (乘車﹑飛行或航海) 舒適平穩的","examples":["The active suspension system gives the car a very smooth ride. 活動的懸掛系統使汽車行駛起來非常平穩。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>smooth</b> to describe something that is going well and is free of problems or trouble. 順利的","examples":["Political hopes for a swift and smooth transition to democracy have been dashed. 向民主快速順利的過渡的政治願望已經破滅了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you describe a man as <b>smooth</b>, you mean that he is extremely smart, confident, and polite, often in a way that you find rather unpleasant. 精明的; 圓滑的","examples":["Twelve extremely good-looking, smooth young men have been picked as finalists. 12個非常英俊精明的男青年已被選為參加決賽的選手。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"流暢地","examples":["Make sure that you execute all movements smoothly and without jerking. 確保你流暢、無顫動地完成所有動作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"順利地","examples":["So far, talks at GM have gone smoothly. 迄今，在通用汽車公司的會談進展順利。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smooth</b> something, you move your hands over its surface to make it smooth and flat. (用手) 弄平","examples":["She stood up and smoothed down her frock. 她站了起來，撫平了自己的連衣裙。"]}]}]},"tame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"馴服的，不怕人的；平淡無奇的，枯燥乏味的；聽使喚的，溫順的；<美> （植物）經栽培的；（土地）經開墾的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"馴化，馴服；制服，控制；開墾，開闢；使變得平淡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tame</b> animal or bird is one that is not afraid of humans. 馴服的","examples":["They never became tame; they would run away if you approached them. 它們從沒有被馴服，如果你靠近，它們就跑開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>tame</b>, you are criticizing them for being weak and uninteresting, rather than forceful or shocking. 軟弱的; 乏味的","examples":["These ideas may seem tame today, but they were inflammatory in his time. 這些想法今天看來也許是平淡乏味的，但在他那個時代卻是很有煽動性的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>tames</b> a wild animal or bird, they train it not to be afraid of humans and to do what they say. 馴化","examples":["The Amazons were believed to have been the first to tame horses. 亞馬遜人被認為是最早馴化了馬的人。"]}]}]},"surround":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"圍繞，環繞；（軍隊，警察等）包圍；與……緊密相連（或相關）；喜歡結交（某類人），身邊總有（某類東西）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（物品的）邊，飾邊；周圍的事物，環境"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is surrounded</b> by something, that thing is situated all around them. 圍繞","examples":["The small churchyard was surrounded by a rusted wrought-iron fence. 這個小墓地被一道生鏽的鍛鐵柵欄圍著。","The shell surrounding the egg has many important functions. 包著蛋的外殼有很多重要功能。","...Chicago and the surrounding area. …芝加哥及其周邊地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are surrounded</b> by soldiers or police, they spread out so that they are in positions all the way around you. 包圍","examples":["When the car stopped in the town square it was surrounded by soldiers and militiamen. 當這輛車在城鎮廣場停下時，它被戰士和民兵們包圍了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The circumstances, feelings, or ideas which <b>surround</b> something are those that are closely associated with it. 與…緊密聯絡","examples":["The decision had been agreed in principle before today's meeting, but some controversy surrounded it. 在今天的會議之前該決定原則上已獲同意，但圍繞這項決定還存在一些爭議。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>surround</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>with</b> certain people or things, you make sure that you have a lot of them near you all the time. 確保身邊總有","examples":["He had made it his business to surround himself with a hand-picked group of bright young officers. 他把確保身邊有自己親手挑選的一群聰明的年輕軍官當作自己的職責。"]}]}]},"swear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"咒罵，詛咒；鄭重承諾，發誓；保證（所說屬實）；使起誓（保密）；（尤指在法庭）宣誓，起誓"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"宣誓；詛咒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>swears</b>, they use language that is considered to be vulgar or offensive, usually because they are angry. 咒罵","examples":["It's wrong to swear and shout. 罵人和喊叫是不對的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>swear</b> <b>to</b> do something, you promise in a serious way that you will do it. 鄭重許諾","examples":["Alan swore that he would do everything in his power to help us. 艾倫鄭重許諾他會盡其所能幫助我們。","We have sworn to fight cruelty wherever we find it. 我們已鄭重許諾，無論在哪兒發現暴行我們都要與其鬥爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>swear</b> that something is true or that you can <b>swear</b> to it, you are saying very firmly that it is true. 發誓","examples":["I swear I've told you all I know. 我發誓我已經把我所知道的都告訴你了。","I swear on all I hold dear that I had nothing to do with this. 我拿我所在乎的一切發誓我與這件事情無關。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is sworn</b> <b>to</b> secrecy or <b>is sworn</b> <b>to</b> silence, they promise another person that they will not reveal a secret. 使承諾 (保密)","examples":["She was bursting to announce the news but was sworn to secrecy. 她忍不住想要釋出這條訊息，但發過誓要保密。"]}]}]},"suppose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推斷，料想，猜想；假設，假定，設想；預期，需要，以……為條件；相信，認為（某事物是可能的）；（婉轉表達）我看，要我說，要不；（因處於某種境地或因約定）必須做（be supposed to do sth.）；我看（用於生氣地表示預料某事屬實）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>suppose</b> or <b>supposing</b> before mentioning a possible situation or action. You usually then go on to consider the effects that this situation or action might have. 假設","examples":["Suppose someone gave you an egg and asked you to describe exactly what was inside. 假設某人給你一個蛋並要你準確描述裡面的東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>suppose</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you believe that it is probably true, because of other things that you know. (根據所知) 料想","examples":["The policy is perfectly clear and I see no reason to suppose that it isn't working. 這項政策非常明瞭，我看不出有何理由認為它行不通。","I knew very well that the problem was more complex than he supposed. 我很清楚這個問題比他料想的更復雜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I suppose</b>\" when you want to express slight uncertainty. 我想 (表示不太確定)","examples":["I suppose I'd better do some homework. 我想我最好做點家庭作業。","\"Is that the right way up?\"—\"Yeah. I suppose so.\" “那是上去的路嗎？”— “是的。我想是。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I suppose</b>\" or \"<b>I don't suppose</b>\" before describing someone's probable thoughts or attitude, when you are impatient or slightly angry with them. 我想 (表示不耐煩或有點生氣)","examples":["I suppose you think you're funny. 我想你認為自己很有趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say \"<b>I don't suppose</b>\" as a way of introducing a polite request. 不知 (表示一種禮貌的請求)","examples":["I don't suppose you could tell me where James Street is, could you? 不知你能不能告訴我詹姆士街在哪兒？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use \"<b>do you suppose</b>\" to introduce a question when you want someone to give their opinion about something, although you know that they are unlikely to have any more knowledge or information about it than you. 你認為 (用於引出他人觀點)","examples":["Do you suppose he was telling the truth? 你認為他在說真話嗎？"]}]}]},"threaten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"威脅，恐嚇；危及，對……構成威脅；預示凶兆，有……危險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person <b>threatens</b> <b>to</b> do something bad to you, or if they <b>threaten</b> you, they say or imply that they will hurt you in some way, especially if you do not do what they want. 威脅","examples":["He said army officers had threatened to destroy the town. 他說軍官們已威脅要摧毀這座小鎮。","He tied her up and threatened her with a six-inch knife. 他把她綁起來，拿著一把6英寸長的刀威脅她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>threatens</b> a person or thing, they are likely to harm that person or thing. 威脅到","examples":["The newcomers directly threaten the livelihood of the established workers. 新來的人直接威脅到原有工人的生計。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something bad <b>threatens</b> <b>to</b> happen, it seems likely to happen. (壞事) 可能發生","examples":["It's threatening to rain. 天可能要下雨。","The fighting is threatening to turn into full-scale war. 這次衝突可能要演變成全面戰爭。"]}]}]},"tend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傾向於，往往會；照顧，護理；走向，趨向；<美>招待，照料（商店、酒吧等的顧客）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>tends</b> <b>to</b> happen, it usually happens or it often happens. 傾向於; 往往會","examples":["A problem for manufacturers is that lighter cars tend to be noisy. 製造商遇到的一個問題是重量較輕的汽車往往噪音大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>tend</b> <b>to</b> think something when you want to give your opinion, but do not want it to seem too forceful or definite. 傾向於 (認為)","examples":["I tend to think that our Representatives by and large do a good job. 我傾向於認為我們的眾議員們總體上幹得不錯。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tend</b> <b>toward</b> a particular characteristic, you often display that characteristic. 趨向…","examples":["Artistic and intellectual people tend toward left-wing views. 藝術人士和知識分子趨向左翼觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to attend (to) 照顧; 照管","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to care for 護理","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to handle or control 處理; 控制","examples":[]}]}]},"tighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變緊，（使）緊固；旋緊，擰緊；抓緊，攥緊；（由於生氣而）（嘴巴）撅起，（雙唇）緊閉；（使）（肌肉或身體某部位）變得僵硬，繃緊；使（規定、政策、制度）更加嚴格，使更加有效；（對……）嚴加控制，（使）加強控制；<美>（比賽）變得激烈（緊張）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tighten</b> your grip on something, or if your grip <b>tightens</b>, you hold the thing more firmly or securely. 抓緊","examples":["Luke answered by tightening his grip on her shoulder. 盧克回應了，緊緊抓住她的肩膀。","Her arms tightened about his neck in gratitude. 她的雙臂緊緊摟住他的脖子，充滿感激。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tighten</b> a rope or chain, or if it <b>tightens</b>, it is stretched or pulled hard until it is straight. 使 (繩或鏈) 拉緊; 拉緊","examples":["The anchorman flung his whole weight back, tightening the rope. 這位排尾壓陣隊員用盡全部的力氣往後拽，把繩子拉緊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a government or organization <b>tightens</b> its grip on a group of people or an activity, or if its grip <b>tightens</b>, it begins to have more control over it. 對…加強控制; 加強控制","examples":["He knows he has considerable support for his plans to tighten his grip on the machinery of central government. 他知道他那些對中央政府加強控制的計劃擁有相當多的支援。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>tighten</b> a screw, nut, or other device, you turn it or move it so that it is more firmly in place or holds something more firmly. 擰緊 (螺絲、螺帽等)","examples":["I used my thumbnail to tighten the screw on my lamp. 我用拇指指甲擰緊了燈上的螺絲。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>tightens</b> a rule, a policy, or a system, they make it stricter or more efficient. 使 (規定、政策或制度) 更嚴格; 使更有效","examples":["The United States plans to tighten the economic sanctions currently in place. 美國計劃使現行的經濟制裁更加嚴厲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tighten up</b> means the same as . 擰緊 (同 )(tighten)","examples":["It's important to tighten up the wheels properly, otherwise they vibrate loose and fall off. 把車輪擰緊很重要，否則它們會振動而鬆脫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tighten up</b> means the same as . 使…更嚴格","examples":["Until this week, every attempt to tighten up the law had failed. 到本週為止，一切嚴格執法的努力都失敗了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>tightens</b>, the muscles in it become tense and stiff, for example, because you are angry or afraid. (身體部位因生氣或害怕) 變得僵硬","examples":["Sofia's throat had tightened and she couldn't speak. 索菲婭的喉嚨哽住了，說不了話。"]}]}]},"tidy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"整潔的，有條理的；（人）愛整潔的，愛整齊的；<非正式>（款額）巨大的；相當好的，令人滿意的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使整潔，整理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"盛零碎物品的容器；<英>整理，收拾；<美>（椅子靠背的）罩單，套子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>tidy</b> likes everything to be neat and arranged in an organized way. 愛整潔的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>tidy</b> is neat and is arranged in an organized way. 整潔的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"整潔","examples":["I'm very impressed by your tidiness and order. 你的整潔和條理性給我留下了非常深刻的印象。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"整潔地","examples":["...books and magazines stacked tidily on shelves. …整齊地擺放在架子上的書和雜誌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>tidy</b> a place such as a room or cupboard, you make it neat by putting things in their proper places. 整理 (房間、櫥櫃等)","examples":[]}]}]},"vanish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"突然不見，消失；不復存在，滅絕；（數學）變為零；使不見，使消失"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"弱化音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>vanishes</b>, they disappear suddenly or in a way that cannot be explained. 突然消失; 神秘失蹤","examples":["He just vanished and was never seen again. 他就這麼突然消失了，再也沒有人見到過他。","Anne vanished from outside her home last Wednesday. 上週三安妮在自己家門外神秘失蹤了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a species of animal or a tradition <b>vanishes</b>, it stops existing. 消亡","examples":["Many of these species have vanished or are facing extinction. 這些物種中的許多已經消亡或是正瀕臨滅絕。"]}]}]},"waken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"喚醒，醒來；喚起（記憶）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>waken</b>, or when someone or something <b>wakens</b> you, you wake from sleep. 使醒來; 醒來","examples":["The noise outside wakened her. 那外面的噪聲吵醒了她。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Waken up</b> means the same as . 使醒來; 醒來","examples":[]}]}]},"unite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）聯合，（使）團結；統一，使統一"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people or things <b>unite</b> or if something <b>unites</b> them, they join together and act as a group. 使聯合; 聯合","examples":["We need to unite against terrorism. 我們需要團結起來反對恐怖主義。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an English gold coin minted in the Stuart period, originally worth 20 shillings 統一金幣; 英國斯圖爾特時期的金幣，約合20先令","examples":[]}]}]},"vary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）不同，（使）呈現差異；（根據情況而）變化，改變；改變，使……變化；變奏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things <b>vary</b>, they are different from each other in size, amount, or degree. 各不相同","examples":["As they're handmade, each one varies slightly. 由於它們是手工製作的，每一件都會略有不同。","The text varies from the earlier versions. 這一文字有別於那些早期的版本。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>varies</b> or if you <b>vary</b> it, it becomes different or changed. 變化; 使變化","examples":["The cost of the alcohol duty varies according to the amount of wine in the bottle. 這項酒稅的額度根據瓶中酒量的不同而變化。"]}]}]},"afterward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以後，後來，其後"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something or if something happens <b>afterward</b>, you do it or it happens after a particular event or time that has already been mentioned. (某事件、某時間) 之後","examples":["Shortly afterward, police arrested four suspects. 之後不久，警方逮捕了４名嫌疑犯。"]}]}]},"ought":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"應該（表義務、責任、必要等）；應該（表期望）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>零（=nought）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何事物（=aught）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> to mean that it is morally right to do a particular thing or that it is morally right for a particular situation to exist, especially when giving or asking for advice or opinions. (指合乎道義) 應該","examples":["Mark, you've got a good wife. You ought to take care of her. 馬克，你娶了個好太太，應該好好照顧她啊。","The people who already own a bit of money or land ought to have a voice in saying where it goes. 已經有了點兒錢或土地的人對之有發言權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> when saying that you think it is a good idea and important for you or someone else to do a particular thing, especially when giving or asking for advice or opinions. (表示建議、願望) 應該","examples":["You don't have to be alone with him and I don't think you ought to be. 你沒必要和他單獨相處，而且我認為你不應該和他單獨相處。","You ought to ask a lawyer's advice. 你應該去問問律師的意見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> to indicate that you expect something to be true or to happen. (表示可能性、希望) 該","examples":["\"This ought to be fun,\" he told Alex, eyes gleaming. “這應該會有趣。”　他對亞歷克斯說著，兩眼閃著光。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> to indicate that you think that something should be the case, but might not be. (表示推測) 應該","examples":["They ought to win easily today, but nothing in life is certain. 他們今天應該能輕而易舉地取勝，但世事難料。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> to indicate that you think that something has happened because of what you know about the situation, but you are not certain. (對已發生的事情做出推測) 應該","examples":["He ought to have reached the house some time ago. 他到達那所房子應該有一段時間了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>ought to have</b> with a past participle to indicate that something was expected to happen or be the case, but it did not happen or was not the case. (某事) 本應該 (表示虛擬語氣)","examples":["Basically the system ought to have worked. 實際上，這個制度本來應該可行。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>ought to have</b> with a past participle to indicate that although it was best or correct for someone to do something in the past, they did not actually do it. (某人) 本應該 (表示虛擬語氣)","examples":["I realize I ought to have told you about it. 我意識到我本該告訴你這件事的。","I ought not to have asked you a thing like that. I'm sorry. 我本不應該問你這樣一件事。對不起。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>ought to</b> when politely telling someone that you must do something, for example, that you must leave. 應當 (禮貌用語)","examples":["I really ought to be getting back now. 現在我真應該回去了。"]}]}]},"afterwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"過後，後來"}],"sections":[]},"weaken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）虛弱，（使）衰弱；（使）變弱，削弱；使（肯定程度）減弱，動搖，猶豫；（使）（大樓 、結構體等）不結實；（使）（股票等）疲弱，疲軟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>weaken</b> something or if it <b>weakens</b>, it becomes less strong or less powerful. 使虛弱; 變得虛弱","examples":["The recession has weakened so many businesses that many can no longer survive. 經濟衰退削弱了很多企業的實力，以至於很多無法再生存下去。","Family structures are weakening and breaking up. 家庭結構正在弱化、崩潰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your resolve <b>weakens</b> or if something <b>weakens</b> it, you become less determined or less certain about taking a particular course of action that you had previously decided to take. 動搖","examples":["I looked at the list and felt my resolve weakening. 我看著那張單子，感到我的決心開始動搖。","Jennie weakened, and finally relented. 珍妮猶豫一下，最終不再拒絕了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>weakens</b> you, it causes you to lose some of your physical strength. 使虛弱","examples":["Malnutrition obviously weakens the patient. 營養不良明顯使病人虛弱無力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>weakens</b> an object, it does something to it that causes it to become less firm and more likely to break. 使鬆動","examples":["A bomb blast had weakened an area of brick on the back wall. 炸彈爆炸使後牆的塊磚都鬆動了。"]}]}]},"warn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提醒，使警惕；警告，告誡（不要做……）；預先通知；（體育運動）警告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>warn</b> someone about something such as a possible danger or problem, you tell them about it so that they are aware of it. 警告; 提醒","examples":["When I had my first baby friends warned me that children were expensive. 當我有了第一個孩子時，朋友們提醒我說養小孩是很花錢的。","They warned him of the dangers of sailing alone. 他們警告他獨自航行的重重危險。","He warned of a possibility of a new terrorist attack. 他警告說可能會有一次新的恐怖襲擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>warn</b> someone not to do something, you advise them not to do it so that they can avoid possible danger or punishment. 告誡","examples":["Mrs. Blount warned me not to interfere. 布朗特太太告誡我不要插手。","\"Don't do anything yet,\" he warned. \"Too risky.\" “先別行動，”他警告道，“太冒險了。”"]}]}]},"aside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在旁邊，到（或向）一邊；積攢，留出；除……以外"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（戲劇或電影中的）旁白；低語，悄悄話；離題話，題外話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move something <b>aside</b>, you move it to one side of you. (把某物移或放) 到一邊地","examples":["Sarah closed the book and laid it aside. 薩拉合上書並將其放到了一邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you take or draw someone <b>aside</b>, you take them a little way away from a group of people in order to talk to them in private. (把某人帶或拉) 到一旁地","examples":["Latoya grabbed him by the elbow and took him aside. 拉託亞抓住他的胳膊肘把他帶到了一旁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you move <b>aside</b>, you get out of someone's way. 向一旁地","examples":["She had been standing in the doorway, but now she stepped aside to let them pass. 她一直站在門道里，不過現在她讓到一邊讓他們過去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you set something such as time, money, or space <b>aside</b> for a particular purpose, you save it and do not use it for anything else. (存留) 在一邊地","examples":["While many parents are putting money aside for college tuition, some are taking on another big expense: buying cars for their teenagers. 許多父母在將錢留作大學學費時，然而有些則在進行另一項巨大開支：為他們十幾歲的孩子們買車。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you brush or sweep <b>aside</b> a feeling or suggestion, you reject it. (拒絕而) 置於一旁地","examples":["Talk to a friend who will really listen and not brush aside your feelings. 跟一個願意真正傾聽並不會置你的感受於不顧的朋友談談。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>aside</b> to indicate that you have finished talking about something, or that you are leaving it out of your discussion, and that you are about to talk about something else. 除了","examples":["Leaving aside the tiny minority who are clinically depressed, most people who have bad moods also have very good moods. 先不談極少數患有臨床抑鬱症的人，大多數有壞情緒的人也有很好的情緒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>aside from</b> when you are making an exception to a general statement. 除…以外","examples":["The room was empty aside from one man seated beside the fire. 這個房間別無他人，除了一個坐在爐火旁的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>aside from</b> to indicate that you are aware of one aspect of a situation, but that you are going to focus on another aspect. 除…以外還","examples":["Quite aside from her tiredness, Amanda seemed unnaturally abstracted. 除了疲憊不堪，阿曼達看上去還一反常態地心不在焉。"]}]}]},"dare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"激，激將；敢於，膽敢"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"挑戰，激將"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do not <b>dare</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do not have enough courage to do it, or you do not want to do it because you fear the consequences. If you <b>dare</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do something which requires a lot of courage. 敢於","examples":["Most people hate Harry but they don't dare to say so. 多數人都討厭哈里，但他們不敢說出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dare</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you challenge them to prove that they are not frightened of doing it. 向…挑戰","examples":["Over coffee, she lit a cigarette, her eyes daring him to comment. 她一邊喝著咖啡，一邊點了支菸，用目光激他作出評價。"]}]},{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dare</b> is also a modal. 敢; 竟敢","examples":["Dare she risk staying where she was? 她敢冒險呆在原地不動嗎？","The yen is weakening. But Tokyo dare not raise its interest rates again. 日元在貶值。但東京不敢再次上調利率。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dare</b> is a challenge which one person gives to another to do something dangerous or frightening. 挑戰","examples":["Jones broke into a military base on a dare. 約翰接受了挑戰，衝進一個軍事基地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say to someone \"<b>don't you dare</b>\" do something, you are telling them not to do it and letting them know that you are angry. 看你敢…","examples":["Allen, don't you dare go anywhere else, you hear? 艾倫，你哪兒都不許去，聽見了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say \"<b>how dare you</b>\" when you are very shocked and angry about something that someone has done. 你竟敢…","examples":["How dare you pick up the phone and listen in on my conversations! 你竟敢拿起電話偷聽我的談話！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use \"<b>I daresay</b>\" or \"<b>I dare say</b>\" before or after a statement to indicate that you believe it is probably true. 我相信","examples":["I daresay that the computer would provide a clear answer to that. 我相信電腦會對此給出明確的答案。"]}]}]},"apart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（空間或時間）相隔，相距；拆開，成碎片；解體，崩潰；分開，分離；與眾不同地，獨特地；除了……外；遠遠地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"意見不一致的，有分歧的；分開的；與眾不同的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or things are <b>apart</b>, they are some distance from each other. 分開地","examples":["He was standing a bit apart from the rest of us, watching us. 他和我們其餘人分開一點站著看著我們。","Ray and sister Renee lived just 25 miles apart from each other. 雷和姊妹勒妮住得彼此僅隔25英里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people or things move <b>apart</b> or are pulled <b>apart</b>, they move away from each other. 分離地","examples":["John and Isabelle moved apart, back into the sun. 約翰和伊莎貝爾彼此分開了，回到陽光下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two people are <b>apart</b>, they are no longer living together or spending time together, either permanently or just for a short time. 不在一起地","examples":["It was the first time Jane and I had been apart for more than a few days. 這是我和簡第一次分開超過了幾天。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you take something <b>apart</b>, you separate it into the pieces that it is made of. If it comes or falls <b>apart</b>, its parts separate from each other. 散開地","examples":["When the clock stopped he took it apart, found what was wrong, and put the whole thing together again. 鐘停了之後他把它拆開，找出了問題，然後又全部裝好了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something such as an organization or relationship falls <b>apart</b>, or if something tears it <b>apart</b>, it can no longer continue because it has serious difficulties. 破裂地","examples":["Any manager knows that his company will start falling apart if his attention wanders. 任何經理都知道如果他的注意力分散了他的公司將會開始分崩離析。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something sets someone or something <b>apart</b>, it makes them different from other people or things. 區分開地","examples":["What really sets Mr. Thaksin apart is that he comes not from Southern China, but from northern Thailand. 真正使他信先生與眾不同的是他並非來自中國南方，而是來自泰國北方。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>apart</b> when you are making an exception to a general statement. 除…以外","examples":["This was, New York apart, the first American city I had ever been in where people actually lived downtown. 這是除紐約以外我所呆過的居民實際住在市中心的第一座美國城市。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or groups are a long way <b>apart</b> on a particular topic or issue, they have completely different views and disagree about it. 有分歧的","examples":["Their concept of a performance and our concept were miles apart. 他們對一場表演的概念和我們的概念相去甚遠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you can't <b>tell</b> two people or things <b>apart</b>, they look exactly the same to you. 不能區分","examples":["I can still only tell Mark and Dave apart by the colour of their shoes! 我依然只能透過馬克和戴夫的鞋的顏色區分他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Apart from</b> means the same as <b>aside from</b>. 除…以外","examples":[]}]}]},"farther":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"較遠地，更遠地；更進一步；此外，而且"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較遠的，更遠的；另外的，更多的；另外的，更多的（far 的比較級形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Farther</b> is a comparative form of <b>far</b>. (far)的比較級","examples":[]}]}]},"barely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"勉強才能；幾乎不，幾乎沒有；剛剛；僅僅，只有；貧乏地，光禿禿；<古>公開地，不加掩飾地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>barely</b> to say that something is only just true or only just the case. 僅僅; 幾乎不","examples":["Anastasia could barely remember the ride to the hospital. 阿納斯塔西婭只勉強記得被送到了醫院。","It was 90 degrees and the air conditioning barely cooled the room. 氣溫是90度，空調幾乎沒有使房間涼快下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one thing had <b>barely</b> happened when something else happened, you mean that the first event was followed immediately by the second. 剛剛","examples":["The water had barely come to a simmer when she cracked four eggs into it. 水剛開她就打了4個雞蛋進去。"]}]}]},"badly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"嚴重地；差，拙劣地；很，非常；不友好地，惡劣地；不利地，負面地；（支付薪水）低地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>badly</b> or goes <b>badly</b>, it is not very successful or effective. 不令人滿意地","examples":["I was angry because I played so badly. 我生氣因為我彈得這麼糟。","The whole project was badly managed. 整個專案管理得差勁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>badly</b> hurt or <b>badly</b> affected, they are severely hurt or affected. 嚴重地","examples":["The bomb destroyed a police station and badly damaged a church. 炸彈炸燬了一個警察局，還嚴重毀壞了一座教堂。","One man was killed and another badly injured. 一男子死亡，另一個受重傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you want or need something <b>badly</b>, you want or need it very much. 非常","examples":["Why do you want to go so badly? 你為什麼要這麼急著走？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone behaves <b>badly</b> or treats other people <b>badly</b>, they act in an unkind, unpleasant, or unacceptable way. 不友善地; (待人) 惡劣地","examples":["They have both behaved very badly and I am very hurt. 他們倆都表現得極不友善，這令我很傷心。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something reflects <b>badly</b> on someone or makes others think <b>badly</b> of them, it harms their reputation. 不利地","examples":["Teachers know that low exam results will reflect badly on them. 老師們知道低的考試成績會對他們不利。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a person or their job is <b>badly</b> paid, they are not paid very much for what they do. (支付薪水) 低地","examples":["You may have to work part-time, in a badly paid job. 你也許不得不做兼職，幹報酬低的工作。"]}]}]},"fairly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相當地，頗；公平地，公正地；<舊>（用以強調）完全，簡直；令人愉快地，讓人喜歡地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fairly</b> means to quite a large degree. For example, if you say that something is <b>fairly</b> old, you mean that it is old but not very old. 在很大程度上","examples":["We did fairly well but only fairly well. 我們做得尚可，但僅僅是尚可。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>fairly</b> instead of \"very\" to add emphasis to an adjective or adverb without making it sound too forceful. 相當","examples":["Were you always fairly bright at school? 你上學時一直挺聰明吧？","You've got to be fairly single-minded about it. 你必須對此事專心一些。"]}]}]},"forth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"離去，外出；（帶）來，（拿）出；自……以後，向前；產生，得出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone goes <b>forth</b> from a place, they leave it. 離開","examples":["Go forth into the desert. 去進入沙漠"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing brings <b>forth</b> another, the first thing produces the second. (得) 出來","examples":["My reflections brought forth no conclusion. 我的思考沒有得出任何結論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone or something is brought <b>forth</b>, they are brought to a place or moved into a position where people can see them. (帶) 出來","examples":["Pilate ordered Jesus to be brought forth. 彼拉多命令將耶穌帶上來。"]}]}]},"forever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"永遠；完全地，永恆地；<非正式>長久地；<非正式>老是，沒完沒了地；萬歲（用在物或人名後，表示支援的口號）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"極長的時間，永恆"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"長期的，永久的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will happen or continue <b>forever</b>, you mean that it will always happen or continue. 永遠地","examples":["I think that we will live together forever. 我想我們會永遠生活在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something has gone or changed <b>forever</b>, it has gone or changed completely and permanently. 永久地; 徹底地","examples":["The old social order was gone forever. 舊的社會秩序一去不復返了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something takes <b>forever</b> or lasts <b>forever</b>, you are emphasizing that it takes or lasts a very long time, or that it seems to. 很長久地; 似乎沒完沒了地","examples":["The drive seemed to take forever. 這車好像永遠也開不到頭似的。"]}]}]},"indoors":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在室內，進入室內"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"室內，戶內"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>indoors</b>, it happens inside a building. 在室內","examples":["I think perhaps we should go indoors. 我想也許我們該進屋了。"]}]}]},"hourly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每小時的；按小時計算的；頻繁的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每小時；按小時；頻繁地，不斷地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>hourly</b> event happens once every hour. 每小時的","examples":["He flipped on the radio to get the hourly news broadcast. 他把收音機開啟，收聽整點新聞廣播。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>hourly</b> earnings are the money that you earn in one hour. 按小時計算的","examples":["They have little prospect of finding new jobs with the same hourly pay. 他們找到時薪同原來一樣的新工作的機會很渺茫。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hourly</b> is also an adverb. 每小時地","examples":["The hospital issued press releases hourly. 這家醫院每小時釋出一次新聞稿。"]}]}]},"indeed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"確實，的確；實際上；真正地；<非正式> 真的嗎（表示驚訝或覺得某事物荒謬）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>indeed</b> to confirm or agree with something that has just been said. (用於強調真實性) 確實","examples":["Later, he admitted that the payments had indeed been made. 後來，他承認說的確是付過款了。","\"Did you know him?\"—\"I did indeed.\" “你認識他嗎？”—“我確實認識他。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>indeed</b> to introduce a further comment or statement that strengthens the point you have already made. (表示遞進語氣) 其實","examples":["We have nothing against diversity; indeed, we want more of it. 我們並不反對多樣化；其實，我們希望有更多的多樣化。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>indeed</b> at the end of a clause to give extra force to the word \"very,\" or to emphasize a particular word. 真正地 (用於句末修飾)(very)(或強調某詞以加強語氣)","examples":["The results are often strange indeed. 結果往往真是奇怪。"]}]}]},"seldom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不常，很少"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>seldom</b> happens, it happens only occasionally. 很少; 不常","examples":["They seldom speak. 他們很少說話。","I've seldom felt so happy. 我很少感到過這麼快樂了。"]}]}]},"outdoors":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在戶外，在野外"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"野外，曠野（the outdoors）；野外活動，戶外休閒 （the outdoors）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"戶外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>outdoors</b>, it happens outside in the fresh air rather than in a building. 在戶外","examples":["It was warm enough to be outdoors all afternoon. 天氣暖洋洋的，整個下午都可以在戶外。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to <b>the outdoors</b> when talking about activities that take place outside away from buildings. 戶外活動","examples":["I'm a lover of the outdoors. 我是個戶外活動愛好者。"]}]}]},"shortly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不久，很快，立刻；簡短地，扼要地；（說話）不耐煩地，不友善地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>shortly</b> after or before something else, it happens not long after or before it. If something is going to happen <b>shortly</b>, it is going to happen soon. 不久","examples":["Their trial will shortly begin. 他們的審訊很快就要開始。","Shortly after moving into her apartment, she found a job. 搬進公寓後不久她就找到了一份工作。"]}]}]},"somewhat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"稍微，有點"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"幾分；某物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>somewhat</b> to indicate that something is the case to a limited extent or degree. 稍微","examples":["He concluded that Oswald was somewhat abnormal. 他斷定奧斯瓦德有點不正常。","He explained somewhat unconvincingly that the company was paying for everything. 他有點不令人相信地解釋說公司正在支付一切費用。"]}]}]},"threateningly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"威脅地；危險地；險惡地"}],"sections":[]},"somehow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以某種方式，用某種方法；由於某種不明原因，不知為什麼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>somehow</b> to say that you do not know or cannot say how something was done or will be done. 不知怎地; 不知以什麼方式","examples":["We'll manage somehow, you and me. I know we will. 我們總會應付過去的，你和我。我知道我們會的。","Somehow Karin managed to cope with the demands of her career. 不知怎麼地，卡林設法應付了那些來自工作的要求。"]}]}]},"sometime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在（將來或過去的）某個時候"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"曾經的，以前的；<美>偶爾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>sometime</b> to refer to a time in the future or the past that is unknown or that has not yet been decided. 某個時候","examples":["The sales figures won't be released until sometime next month. 銷售資料要到下個月的某個時候才會公佈。","Why don't you come and see me sometime. 你何不在某個時間來看看我？"]}]}]},"instead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"代替，頂替，反而"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>instead of</b> another, you do the first thing and not the second thing, as the result of a choice or a change of behaviour. 而不是…","examples":["They raised prices and cut production, instead of cutting costs. 他們提高了價格，減少了產量，而沒有削減成本。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do not do something, but do something else <b>instead</b>, you do the second thing and not the first thing, as the result of a choice or a change of behaviour. 而","examples":["My husband asked why I couldn't just forget about dieting and eat normally instead. 丈夫問我為什麼就不能忘掉節食而正常吃飯。"]}]}]},"someday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有一天，有朝一日，總有一天"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Someday</b> means at a date in the future that is unknown or that has not yet been decided. 將來有一天","examples":["Someday I'll be a pilot. 將來有一天我將成為一名飛行員。"]}]}]},"aboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在（船、飛機、火車等）上；上（船、飛機、火車等）；騎在（馬）上，跨上（馬）；（棒球）在壘上；加入，加盟"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在（船、飛機、火車等）上；上（船、飛機、火車等）；騎在（馬）上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>aboard</b> a ship or plane, you are on it or in it. 在 (船或飛機) 上","examples":["She invited 750 people aboard the luxury yacht, the Savarona. 她邀請了750人登上這艘豪華遊艇，薩瓦羅納號。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aboard</b> is also an adverb. 在 (船或飛機) 上","examples":["It had taken two hours to load all the people aboard. 用了兩個小時才讓所有的人上了船。"]}]}]},"beneath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……下方；在……表面之下，隱藏在……之下；（對某人來說）不夠好，不相稱；低於，次於"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在下面，在底下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>beneath</b> another thing is under the other thing. 在…之下","examples":["She could see the muscles of his shoulders beneath his T-shirt. 她可以看到他T恤衫下的肩部肌肉。","Four levels of parking beneath the theatre was not enough. 劇院底下的四層停車庫還不夠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about what is <b>beneath</b> the surface of something, you are talking about the aspects of it which are hidden or not obvious. 在 (表面) 之下","examples":["...emotional strains beneath the surface. …表面下的情感壓力。","Somewhere deep beneath the surface lay a caring character. 在其外表下心靈深處的某個地方保留著一種關愛別人的品格。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>beneath</b> you, you feel that they are not good enough for you or not suitable for you. 不如; 配不上","examples":["They decided she was marrying beneath her. 他們認定她嫁的是一個配不上她的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beneath</b> is also an adverb. 在下方","examples":["On a shelf beneath he spotted a photo album. 在下方的書架上他發現了一本相簿。"]}]}]},"pop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"流行音樂的；通俗的，大眾的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"流行音樂；砰的響聲；<非正式> 汽水；<非正式> 爸爸；鮮豔的一小塊；（一系列事情中的）一次，一項；（棒球）小騰空球；打，敲擊；<美> 通俗古典樂，流行古典樂（pops）；<非正式> 嘗試，努力；<非正式> 批評；老人家（用作稱呼）（pops）；槍擊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）砰地爆開，砰地脫落；迅速去，短暫逗留；突然出現，短暫出現；<非正式> 突然放置，迅速放入；（使）發出砰的響聲，（使）啪的一聲爆裂；（因飛機起飛、降落或上下陡坡等）耳壓變化，耳脹；（因驚訝或興奮而）瞪大眼睛；<非正式> 過於頻繁地服用（藥片）；打（某人）；爆（玉米花）；擊出小騰空球；射擊，開槍；開啟瓶子喝（啤酒）；<英，非正式> 典當，抵押"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"砰的響聲（go pop）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"郵局協議 （post office protocol）；人口 （population）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pop</b> is modern music that usually has a strong rhythm and uses electronic equipment. 流行樂","examples":["...the perfect combination of Caribbean rhythms, European pop, and American soul. …加勒比旋律、歐洲流行樂及美國靈樂的完美結合。","...a life-size poster of a pop star. …一張如真人大小的流行歌星海報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to carbonated drinks such as cola as <b>pop</b>. 碳酸飲料","examples":["...a can of pop. …一聽碳酸飲料。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Pop</b> is used to represent a short sharp sound such as the sound made by bursting a balloon or by pulling a cork out of a bottle. 爆裂聲","examples":["Each corn kernel will make a loud pop when cooked. 每顆玉米粒炒熟的時候都會發出很響的爆裂聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people call their father <b>pop</b>. 爸爸","examples":["I looked at Pop and he had big tears in his eyes. 我看了看爸爸，他眼裡噙著大滴的淚珠。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>pops</b>, it makes a short sharp sound. 發爆裂聲","examples":["He untwisted the wire off the champagne bottle, and the cork popped and shot to the ceiling. 他擰開香檳瓶子上的鐵絲，瓶塞砰的一聲衝到了天花板上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your eyes <b>pop</b>, you look very surprised or excited when you see something. (因驚訝或興奮而)睜大眼","examples":["My eyes popped at the sight of the rich variety of food on show. 我瞪大眼睛看著各色各樣的食物展品。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"with a popping sound 砰的一聲地; 啪的一聲地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an exclamation denoting a sharp explosive sound (感嘆詞，表示)砰的爆炸聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pop</b> something somewhere, you put it there quickly. 迅速放置","examples":["Marianne got a couple of mugs from the cupboard and popped a teabag into each of them. 瑪麗安娜從碗櫃中拿出了幾個杯子，把茶袋迅速地放入每個杯子中。"]}]}]},"onto":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"到……之上，向……之上，到，朝；（建築物、房間、門或窗）面朝，通向；發現（某人做了壞事）；瞭解，掌握，處於有利地位；與……談話，詢問；到（交通工具）上；（重心移動）到（身體某部位）上；成為（列表、系統等）的一部分；轉到（其他話題）；抓住；（數）對映到的"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"對映的，映成的，滿射的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something moves <b>onto</b> or is put <b>onto</b> an object or surface, it is then on that object or surface. 到…之上","examples":["I took my bags inside, lowered myself onto the bed and switched on the TV. 我把我的包拿進去，坐到了床上，開啟了電視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can sometimes use <b>onto</b> to mention the place or area that someone moves into. 移向 (某處)","examples":["The players jogged onto the field. 運動員們慢慢跑進賽場。","At exactly 6:00 p.m., Marcia drove onto the motorway. 下午6點整，馬西婭開車上了高速公路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>onto</b> to introduce the place toward which a light or someone's look is directed. (光線或視線) 朝向","examples":["...the metal part of the door onto which the sun had been shining. …陽光一直照耀著的門的金屬部分。","The colours rotated around on a disc and were reflected onto the wall behind. 那些色彩在一張圓盤上旋轉，並被反射到後面的牆上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a door or room opens <b>onto</b> a place, that place is directly in front of it. (門或房間) 對著…","examples":["The door opened onto a well-lit hallway. 這扇門對著一個照明很好的門廳。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you change the position of your body, you use <b>onto</b> to introduce the part your body which is now supporting you. (身體重心) 移向","examples":["As he stepped backwards she fell onto her knees, then onto her face. 他往後退步時，她雙膝跪倒在地，接著臉也著地。","Puffing a little, Mabel shifted her weight onto her feet. 梅布林有些氣喘,將她身體的重量移到了雙腳上。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you get <b>onto</b> a bus, train, or plane, you enter it in order to travel somewhere. 登上 (交通工具)","examples":["As he got on to the plane, he asked me how I was feeling. 他上飛機時問我感覺如何。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Onto</b> is used after verbs such as \"hold,\" \"hang,\" and \"cling\" to indicate what someone is holding firmly or where something is being held firmly. 用於(hold)，(hang)，(cling)等動詞之後，表示某人緊握或某物被緊握","examples":["The reflector is held onto the sides of the spacecraft with a frame. 反光器被一個框緊緊地固定在宇宙飛船的各個側面。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If people who are talking get <b>onto</b> a different subject, they begin talking about it. 轉向 (新的話題)","examples":["Let's get on to more important matters. 咱們談些更重要的事吧。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You can sometimes use <b>onto</b> to indicate that something or someone becomes included as a part of a list or system. 成為…的一部分","examples":["The Macedonian question had failed to get on to the agenda. 馬其頓問題沒能提到議事日程上來。","The pill itself has changed a lot since it first came onto the market. 自從投放市場以來，這種片劑本身已經改變了許多。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>is onto</b> something, they are about to discover something important. 將要發現","examples":["He leaned across the table and whispered to me, \"I'm really onto something.\" 他隔著桌子探過身悄悄地跟我說，“我真的要有重大發現了。”"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If someone <b>is onto</b> you, they have discovered that you are doing something illegal or wrong. (對某人做的壞事) 已經明白了","examples":["I had told people what he had been doing, so now the police were onto him. 我已經告訴人們他一直在從事的勾當，所以現在警察都對他很清楚了。"]}]}]},"unless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"除非，除非在……情況下；若非，如果不"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除……之外；除……之外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>unless</b> to introduce the only circumstances in which an event you are mentioning will not take place or in which a statement you are making is not true. 除非; 如果不","examples":["Unless you are trying to lose weight to please yourself, it's going to be tough to keep your motivation level high. 除非你在為了讓自己開心而努力減肥，否則要保持驅動力很高將很難。","We cannot understand disease unless we understand the person who has the disease. 除非我們瞭解有某種疾病的人，否則我們不會了解疾病。"]}]}]},"accident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交通事故，車禍；（不幸的）意外遭遇，不測事件；意外，偶然的事；運氣，機遇；大便（或小便）失禁；（亞里士多德思想中的）非本質屬性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accident</b> happens when a vehicle hits a person, an object, or another vehicle, causing injury or damage. 交通事故","examples":["She was involved in a serious car accident last week. 她上個星期捲入了一場嚴重的車禍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has an <b>accident</b>, something unpleasant happens to them that was not intended, sometimes causing injury or death. 事故","examples":["5,000 people die every year because of accidents in the home. 每年有5千人死於家庭意外事故。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>by</b> <b>accident</b>, it happens completely by chance. 偶然","examples":["She discovered the problem by accident during a visit to a nearby school. 她在去附近一所學校參觀時偶然發現了這個問題。"]}]}]},"ache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（隱隱地、持續地）疼痛；渴望；哀痛，憐憫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（身體某部位的）疼痛；（心中的）苦痛，痛苦；<文>渴望； <文>渴望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ache</b> or a part of your body <b>aches</b>, you feel a steady, fairly strong pain. 疼痛","examples":["The glands in her neck were swollen, her head was throbbing and she ached all over. 她脖子裡的淋巴腺腫了，頭一跳一跳地作痛而且全身疼痛。","My leg is giving me much less pain but still aches when I sit down. 我的腿疼痛減輕了許多，但是當我坐下時還是會疼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ache</b> is a steady, fairly strong pain in a part of your body. 疼痛","examples":["You feel nausea and aches in your muscles. 你覺得噁心而且肌肉疼痛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>aches and pains</b> to refer in a general way to any minor pains that you feel in your body. (泛指不嚴重的) 疼痛","examples":["It seems to ease all the aches and pains of a hectic and tiring day. 它似乎可以減輕繁忙疲勞的一天帶來的所有疼痛。"]}]}]},"achievement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成績，成就；完成，實現；（紋章）紋章牌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>achievement</b> is something that someone has succeeded in doing, especially after a lot of effort. 成就","examples":["It was a great achievement that a month later a global agreement was reached. 一個月後一個全球協議達成了，這是一個巨大的成就。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Achievement</b> is the process of achieving something. 實現","examples":["It is only the achievement of these goals that will finally bring lasting peace. 只有這些目標的實現才會最終帶來持久的和平。"]}]}]},"tight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"牢固的，不鬆動的；緊身的；拉緊的，繃緊的；嚴厲的，嚴格的；緊的，拮据的；密集的，擠滿的；親密的，緊密的；急轉的，陡的；憋悶的，不適的；緊張的，生氣的；勢均力敵的；困難的，棘手的；準確的，緊湊的；<非正式>吝嗇的；<非正式>醉醺醺的；結實的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"緊緊地，牢固地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tight</b> clothes or shoes are small and fit closely to your body. (衣服或鞋子) 緊貼的","examples":["She walked off the plane in a miniskirt and tight top. 她穿著迷你裙和緊身上衣走下飛機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tight</b> is also an adjective. 緊緊的","examples":["As he and Hannah passed through the gate he kept a tight hold of her arm. 他和漢娜經過大門時，他緊抓著她的胳膊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Tight</b> controls or rules are very strict. 嚴格的","examples":["The measures include tight control of media coverage. 這些措施包括對媒體報道的嚴格管理。","The government was prepared to keep a tight hold on public sector pay rises. 政府準備保持對公共部門薪資增長的嚴格控制。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Skin, cloth, or string that is <b>tight</b> is stretched or pulled so that it is smooth or straight. (皮膚、布或繩線等) 繃緊的","examples":["My skin feels tight and lacking in moisture. 我的皮膚感覺緊巴巴的，缺乏水分。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Tight</b> is used to describe a group of things or an amount of something that is closely packed together. 密集的; 裝得滿滿的","examples":["She curled up in a tight ball, with her knees tucked up at her chin. 她蜷縮成緊緊的一團，膝蓋頂著下巴。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a part of your body is <b>tight</b>, it feels uncomfortable and painful, for example, because you are sick, anxious, or angry. (身體部位因生病、焦慮或生氣) 僵硬的","examples":["It is better to stretch the tight muscles first. 最好先舒展一下僵硬的肌肉。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>tight</b> group of people is one whose members are closely linked by beliefs, feelings, or interests. 關係緊密的","examples":["We're a tight group, so we do keep in touch. 我們是一個親密的團體，所以我們的確保持著聯絡。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>tight</b> bend or corner is one that changes direction very quickly so that you cannot see very far around it. (彎道或拐角) 急轉的","examples":["They collided on a tight bend and both cars were extensively damaged. 他們在一個急轉彎處相撞，兩輛車都嚴重受損。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>tight</b> schedule or budget allows very little time or money for unexpected events or expenses. (日程或預算) 緊的","examples":["It's difficult to cram everything into a tight schedule. 難以把所有的事都排進一個緊張的日程。","Emma is on a tight budget for clothes. 埃瑪手頭很緊，沒錢買衣服。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"緊貼地","examples":["He buttoned his collar tightly round his thick neck. 他把衣領緊緊地扣在自己的粗脖子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you hold someone or something <b>tight</b>, you hold them firmly and securely. 緊緊地","examples":["She just fell into my arms, clutching me tight for a moment. 她就倒在了我的懷裡，一時間緊緊地抓著我。","Just hold tight to my hand and follow along. 只要緊緊地抓住我的手，跟著我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"緊緊地","examples":["She climbed back into bed and wrapped her arms tightly around her body. 她爬回床上，用雙臂緊緊地抱住自己的身體。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"嚴格地","examples":["The internal media was tightly controlled by the government during the war. 國內媒體在戰爭期間被政府嚴格地控制著。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is shut <b>tight</b> is shut very firmly. 緊緊地 (關閉)","examples":["The baby lay on his back with his eyes closed tight. 這個嬰兒平躺著，兩眼緊閉。","I keep the flour and sugar in individual jars, sealed tight with their glass lids. 我把麵粉和糖分別放在罐子裡，並用玻璃蓋密封。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"緊緊地","examples":["Pemberton frowned and closed his eyes tightly. 彭伯頓皺著眉頭，緊緊地閉上雙眼。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"繃緊地","examples":["Her sallow skin was drawn tightly across the bones of her face. 她蠟黃的皮膚緊緊地繃在臉骨上。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Tight</b> is also an adverb. 緊密地","examples":["The people sleep on army cots packed tight, end to end. 這些人睡在首尾緊挨著的行軍床上。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"緊密地","examples":["Many animals travel in tightly packed trucks and are deprived of food, water and rest. 許多動物被裝在擁擠不堪的卡車裡運送，沒吃沒喝，也不能休息。"]}]}]},"activity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"活躍狀況，熱鬧；活動；（Activity）熱力活性，活度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Activity</b> is a situation in which a lot of things are happening or being done. 活躍狀況","examples":["Changes in the money supply affect the level of economic activity and the interest rate. 貨幣供給的變化影響經濟活動水平和利率。","Children are supposed to get 60 minutes of physical activity every day. 兒童應該每天獲得60分鐘的體育活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>activity</b> is something that you spend time doing. (個體性的) 活動","examples":["For lovers of the great outdoors, activities range from canoeing to bird watching. 對於戶外活動的愛好者們來說，有從划船到觀鳥的各種活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>activities</b> of a group are the things that they do in order to achieve their aims. (群體性的) 活動","examples":["...a jail term for terrorist activities. …一個針對恐怖主義活動的刑期。"]}]}]},"ad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廣告；促銷活動；<非正式>預告片（同 advertisement）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"優勢（advantage）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ad</b> is an advertisement. 廣告","examples":["She replied to a lonely hearts ad she spotted in the New York Times. 她回覆了在《紐約時報》上看到的一則求友廣告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"advantage的縮寫 (Brit equivalent van)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Andorra 安道爾公國","examples":[]}]}]},"adventure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冒險（經歷），奇遇；冒險的刺激，冒險欲；<古>生意"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"冒險；大膽說出；去（某地）探險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has an <b>adventure</b>, they become involved in an unusual, exciting, and somewhat dangerous trip or series of events. 冒險經歷","examples":["I set off for a new adventure in Alaska on the first day of the new year. 我在新年第一天出發去阿拉斯加進行一次新的冒險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Adventure</b> is excitement and willingness to do new, unusual, or somewhat dangerous things. 冒險精神","examples":["Their cultural backgrounds gave them a spirit of adventure. 他們的文化背景賦予了他們一種冒險精神。"]}]}]},"advertisement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廣告；（某一類事物的）活廣告；廣告活動，廣告宣傳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advertisement</b> is an announcement in a newspaper, on television, or on a poster about something such as a product, event, or job. 廣告; 啟事","examples":["Miss Parrish recently placed an advertisement in the local newspaper. 帕裡什小姐最近在當地報紙上登出了一則啟事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that an example of something is <b>an</b> <b>advertisement</b> <b>for</b> that thing in general, you mean that it shows how good that thing is. 宣傳","examples":["The Treviso team was an effective advertisement for the improving state of Italian club rugby. 特雷維索隊是義大利俱樂部橄欖球改進狀況的一個有效展示。"]}]}]},"advisor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧問，勸告者；導師，指導教師"}],"sections":[]},"adviser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧問，指導者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adviser</b> is an expert whose job is to give advice to another person or to a group of people. 顧問","examples":["In Washington, the president and his advisers spent the day in meetings. 在華盛頓，總統和他的顧問們開了一天的會。"]}]}]},"advice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忠告，勸告，建議；（金融交易）正式通知；訊息"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone <b>advice</b>, you tell them what you think they should do in a particular situation. 建議","examples":["Don't be afraid to ask for advice about ordering the meal. 別怕就點餐尋求建議。","Take my advice and stay away from him! 聽我的忠告，離他遠點！"]}]}]},"advantage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"有利條件，優勢；優點；利益；（局末平分後）佔先，優勢分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"有利於，有助於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advantage</b> is something that puts you in a better position than other people. 有利條件","examples":["They are breaking the law in order to obtain an advantage over their competitors. 他們為了獲得超越其競爭對手的有力條件在違犯法律。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>advantage</b> is a way in which one thing is better than another. 優勢","examples":["The great advantage of home-grown oranges is their magnificent flavour. 自產橙子的巨大優勢是其極好的味道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Advantage</b> is the state of being in a better position than others who are competing against you. 佔優勢","examples":["Men have created a social and economic position of advantage for themselves over women. 男性創造了相對於女性的社會和經濟上的優勢地位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take advantage of</b> something, you make good use of it while you can. 利用 (某事物)","examples":["I intend to take full advantage of this trip to buy the things we need. 我打算充分利用這次旅行來購買我們需要的物品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>takes advantage of</b> you, they treat you unfairly for their own benefit, especially when you are trying to be kind or to help them. 利用 (某人)","examples":["She took advantage of him even after they were divorced. 她甚至在他們離婚以後仍然利用他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you use or turn something <b>to</b> your <b>advantage</b>, you use it in order to benefit from it, especially when it might be expected to harm or damage you. 對 (某人) 有利","examples":["The government has not been able to turn today's demonstration to its advantage. 政府還未能將今天的遊行示威轉化為對其有利。"]}]}]},"agriculture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"農業，農學，農藝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Agriculture</b> is farming and the methods that are used to raise and take care of crops and animals. 農業","examples":["Strong both in industry and agriculture, Ukraine produces much of the grain for the nation. 工業與農業雙強的烏克蘭為其國民生產大部分穀物。"]}]}]},"account":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賬戶，戶頭；客戶，老主顧；網路賬號；描述，報道；賬目；賬單；賒購賬，賒購；理由，解釋；重要性；（定期結付的）交易合同；演奏（音樂）；<英>賬期交易期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……視作，認為；解釋，說明（account for）；佔（一定數量或比例）（account for）；<古>報賬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>account</b> with a bank or a similar organization, you have an arrangement to leave your money there and take some out when you need it. 賬戶","examples":["Some banks make it difficult to open an account. 有些銀行使開一個賬戶困難重重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In business, a regular customer of a company can be referred to as an <b>account</b>, especially when the customer is another company. 客戶","examples":["All three Internet agencies boast they've won major accounts. 所有的三家網路代理公司都誇口說他們已贏得了大客戶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Accounts</b> are detailed records of all the money that a person or business receives and spends. 賬目","examples":["He kept detailed accounts. 他儲存了詳細的賬目。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>account</b> is a written or spoken report of something that has happened. 報道","examples":["He gave a detailed account of what happened on the fateful night. 他對那個決定命運的夜晚所發生的事情做了一個詳細的報道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>by all accounts</b> or <b>from all accounts</b>, you believe it is true because other people say so. 據說","examples":["He is, by all accounts, a superb teacher. 據說，他是一名優秀的教師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>of no account</b> or <b>of little account</b>, you mean that it is very unimportant and is not worth considering. 無足輕重的","examples":["These obscure groups were of little account in either national or international politics. 這些無名的組織在國內或國際政治中都是無足輕重的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you buy or pay for something <b>on account</b>, you pay nothing or only part of the cost at first, and pay the rest later. 以賒賬方式","examples":["He was ordered to pay the company $500,000 on account pending a final assessment of his liability. 在對他的債務做最後的評估期間，他被命令先付這家公司50萬美元。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>on account of</b> to introduce the reason or explanation for something. 由於","examples":["The president declined to deliver the speech himself, on account of a sore throat. 那位總統由於嗓子疼拒絕親自發表演講。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your feelings <b>on</b> someone's <b>account</b> are the feelings you have about what they have experienced or might experience, especially when you imagine yourself to be in their situation. 為 (某人的) 緣故 (而感到…)","examples":["Mollie told me what she'd done and I was really scared on her account. 莫麗告訴了我她做過的事情，我真為她感到害怕。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you tell someone not to do something <b>on</b> your <b>account</b>, you mean that they should do it only if they want to, and not because they think it will please you. (不) 為 (某人的) 緣故 (而做某事)","examples":["Don't leave on my account. 不要因為我而離開。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that something should <b>on no account</b> be done, you are emphasizing that it should not be done under any circumstances. 絕對不","examples":["On no account should the mixture come near boiling. 這種混合物絕對不應當接近沸點。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If you do something <b>on</b> your <b>own account</b>, you do it because you want to and without being asked, and you take responsibility for your own action. 隨 (某人) 自己","examples":["I told him if he withdrew it was on his own account. 我告訴他，如果他退出那麼他要自負其則。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something <b>into account</b>, or <b>take account of</b> something, you consider it when you are thinking about a situation or deciding what to do. 考慮到","examples":["The defendant asked for 21 similar offences to be taken into account. 該被告請求將21項相似的犯罪罪行考慮在內。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If someone <b>is called, held,</b> or <b>brought to account</b> for something they have done wrong, they are made to explain why they did it, and are often criticized or punished for it. 追究","examples":["Individuals who repeatedly provide false information should be called to account for their actions. 反覆提供虛假情報的人應為其行為而受到追究。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>gave a good account of</b> themselves in a particular situation, you mean that they performed well, although they may not have been completely successful. 表現很好","examples":["We have been hindered by our lack of preparation, but I'm sure we will give a good account of ourselves. 我們曾經為缺乏準備所阻，但我肯定我們會表現很好的。"]}]}]},"amazement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚詫，驚奇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Amazement</b> is the feeling you have when something surprises you very much. 吃驚","examples":["I stared at her in amazement. 我驚訝地盯著她。"]}]}]},"alley":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小巷，衚衕；（兩旁有樹木、灌木或石頭的）小徑；（九柱戲和保齡球等遊戲的）球道；<美>雙打網球場兩邊的狹長地帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alley</b> is a narrow passage or street with buildings or walls on both sides. 小巷","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a large playing marble 大彈珠","examples":[]}]}]},"ambition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"追求的目標，抱負；雄心，野心；幹勁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"追求，有……野心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>ambition</b> <b>to</b> do or achieve something, you want very much to do it or achieve it. 理想","examples":["His ambition is to sail around the world. 他的理想是航行環遊世界。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ambition</b> is the desire to be successful, rich, or powerful. 雄心","examples":["Even when I was young I never had any ambition. 即使當我年輕的時候我也從未有過什麼雄心。"]}]}]},"ambassador":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大使，使節；（體育專案、行業等的）代表人物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ambassador</b> is an important official who lives in a foreign country and represents his or her own country's interests there. 大使","examples":["...the German ambassador to Poland. …德國駐波蘭大使。"]}]}]},"aquarium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水族箱，養魚缸；水族館"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>aquarium</b> is a building, often in a zoo, where fish and underwater animals are kept. 水族館","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>aquarium</b> is a glass tank filled with water, in which people keep fish. 魚缸","examples":[]}]}]},"angel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天使；仁慈的人，善人；寶貝，乖乖；（尤指仁慈的）精靈，保護神；<非正式>仙波，雷達迴響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Angels</b> are spiritual beings that some people believe are God's servants in heaven. 天使","examples":["The artist usually painted his angels with multi-coloured wings. 這位藝術家通常給他的天使畫上多彩的翅膀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can call someone you like very much an <b>angel</b> in order to show affection, especially when they have been kind to you or done you a favour. 天使","examples":["Thank you a thousand times, you're an angel. 千恩萬謝了，你是個天使。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as an <b>angel</b>, you mean that they seem to be very kind and good. 大好人","examples":["Papa thought her an angel. 爸爸認為她是個大好人。"]}]}]},"announcement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公告；（報紙上的）佈告；宣佈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>announcement</b> is a statement made to the public or to the media that gives information about something that has happened or that will happen. 公告","examples":["She made her announcement after talks with the president. 她在與總統的會談後釋出了公告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>announcement</b> in a public place, such as a newspaper or the window of a shop, is a short piece of writing telling people about something or asking for something. 通告","examples":["The Seattle Times publishes brief announcements of religious events every Saturday. 《西雅圖時報》每週六刊登簡短的宗教活動通告。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>announcement</b> <b>of</b> something that has happened is the act of telling people about it. 宣佈","examples":["...the announcement of their engagement. …他們婚約的宣佈。"]}]}]},"arithmetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"算術；演算，計算；資料統計"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"算術的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Arithmetic</b> is the part of mathematics that is concerned with the addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division of numbers. 算術","examples":["...teaching the basics of reading, writing and arithmetic. …教授讀、寫、算的基本知識。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>arithmetic</b> to refer to the process of doing a particular sum or calculation. 計算","examples":["4,000 women put in ten rupees each, which if my arithmetic is right adds up to 40,000 rupees. 4千名婦女每人交10盧比，如果我的計算準確的話加起來總共是4萬盧比。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to <b>the</b> <b>arithmetic</b> of a situation, you are concerned with those aspects of it that can be expressed in numbers, and how they affect the situation. (某形勢的) 資料","examples":["The arithmetic was discouraging. In less than two months, they had used up six months' worth of food. 資料不容樂觀。在不到兩個月裡，他們已經吃完了6個月的食物。"]}]}]},"angle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"角；傾斜，斜角；角度；視角，立場；<美>不可告人的動機；<美>詭計，狡猾的手段；角鐵，角鋼；<古>魚鉤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"斜移，斜置；向（特定人群）提供資訊，定位於；博取，謀取；垂釣，釣魚；（使）朝向，（使）轉向"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>angle</b> is the difference in direction between two lines or surfaces. Angles are measured in degrees. 角","examples":["The boat is now leaning at a 30 degree angle. 這條船現在正以30度角傾斜著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>angle</b> is the shape that is created where two lines or surfaces join together. 角","examples":["...the angle of the blade. …刀刃的尖角。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>angle</b> is the direction from which you look at something. 角度","examples":["Thanks to the angle at which he stood, he could just see the sunset. 多虧他站的角度，他剛好能看到日落。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a way of presenting something or thinking about it as a particular <b>angle</b>. 視角","examples":["He was considering the idea from all angles. 他從所有的視角考慮著這個觀點。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"any piece of fishing tackle, esp a hook 漁具中的任何部分，尤指魚鉤","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"to fish with a hook and line 用魚鉤和魚線釣魚","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"to move in or bend into angles or an angle 斜移進來; 折彎成角","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>at an angle</b>, it is leaning in a particular direction so that it is not straight, horizontal, or vertical. 成一定角度","examples":["An iron bar stuck out at an angle. 一根鐵條成一定角度地突出來。"]}]}]},"athlete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動員，體育健將；擅長運動的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>athlete</b> is a person who does any kind of physical sports, exercise, or games, especially in competitions. 運動員","examples":["Mark Spitz was a great athlete. 馬克·斯皮茨是一名偉大的運動員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone who is fit and athletic as an <b>athlete</b>. 運動型人","examples":["I was no athlete. 我完全不是運動型的人。"]}]}]},"arrival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"到達，到來；到達者，加入者；產生，出現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or vehicle arrives at a place, you can refer to their <b>arrival</b>. 到達","examples":["...the day after his arrival in Wichita. …他到達威奇托的第二天。","He was dead on arrival at the nearby hospital. 他在到達附近的醫院時已死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone starts a new job, you can refer to their <b>arrival</b> in that job. 到任","examples":["...the power vacuum created by the arrival of a new president. …由一位新總統到任造成的權力真空。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something is brought to you or becomes available, you can refer to its <b>arrival</b>. 到達","examples":["I was flicking idly through a newspaper while awaiting the arrival of orange juice and coffee. 我在等橙汁和咖啡送達的同時漫不經心地翻閱一份報紙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a particular time comes or a particular event happens, you can refer to its <b>arrival</b>. 來臨","examples":["He celebrated the arrival of the New Year with a bout of drinking that nearly killed him. 他以一番狂飲慶祝新年的來臨，這幾乎要了他的命。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to someone who has just arrived at a place as a new <b>arrival</b>. 到來者","examples":["A high proportion of the new arrivals are skilled professionals. 很大一部分新來的人們是技術熟練的專業人士。"]}]}]},"ash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（香菸或木頭等的）灰；灰燼，廢墟；骨灰，遺骸；梣樹，白蠟樹；（古英語中的一個字母，也為音標）æ"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……化為灰燼；以灰覆蓋，撒灰於；撣（煙）灰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ash</b> is the grey or black powdery substance that is left after something is burned. You can also refer to this substance as <b>ashes</b>. 灰","examples":["A cloud of volcanic ash is spreading across wide areas of the Philippines. 一大片火山灰正在向菲律賓的大塊區域擴散。","He brushed the cigarette ash from his sleeve. 他撣掉了袖子上的菸灰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A dead person's <b>ashes</b> are their remains after their body has been cremated. 骨灰","examples":["And she asks him to go back there after her death and scatter her ashes on the lake. 她還要求他在她死後回到那裡並把她的骨灰撒在那個湖上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"ruins or remains, as after destruction or burning 廢墟; 灰燼; 這座城市成了一片廢墟。","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>ash</b> is a tree that has smooth grey bark and loses its leaves in winter. 梣樹","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Ash</b> is the wood from this tree. 梣木","examples":["The rafters are made from ash. 這些椽是用梣木做的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"the digraph <b>æ</b>, as in Old English, representing a front vowel approximately like that of the <b>a</b> in Modern English <b>hat.</b> The character is also used to represent this sound in the International Phonetic Alphabet 母音æ","examples":[]}]}]},"appeal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"呼籲，懇求；上訴，申訴；吸引力，感染力；（為慈善或正義事業的）募捐；啟發，打動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"呼籲，懇求；上訴，申訴；有吸引力，引起興趣；啟發，打動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>appeal</b> <b>to</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you make a serious and urgent request to them. 呼籲","examples":["He appealed to voters to go to the polls tomorrow. 他呼籲選民們明天去投票站。","He will appeal to the state for an extension of unemployment benefits. 他將呼籲國家延長失業救濟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>appeals</b> <b>to</b> you, you find it attractive or interesting. 有吸引力","examples":["On the other hand, the idea appealed to him. 另一方面，這個主意對他有吸引力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>appeal</b> a decision <b>to</b> someone in authority, you formally ask them to change it. 申訴","examples":["We intend to appeal the verdict. 我們打算對此裁決提出申訴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>appeal</b> is a serious and urgent request. 呼籲","examples":["He has a message from King Fahd, believed to be an appeal for Arab unity. 他有個來自法赫德國王的口信，相信是對阿拉伯團結的呼籲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>appeal</b> is an attempt to raise money for a charity or for a good cause. (為慈善或好的事業所做的) 籌款努力","examples":["...an appeal to save a library containing priceless manuscripts. …為挽救一個藏有無價手稿圖書館的一次籌款努力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>appeal</b> is a formal request for a decision to be changed. 申訴","examples":["They took their appeal to the Supreme Court. 他們上訴到了最高法院。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>appeal</b> of something is a quality that people find attractive or interesting. 吸引力","examples":["Its new title was meant to give the party greater public appeal. 其新的名字意在給予該黨更大的公眾吸引力。"]}]}]},"approach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"靠近，臨近；接洽，交談；對付，處理；近似，接近於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"方法，態度；靠近，接近；接洽，要求；通道，路徑；進場著陸；近似物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>approach</b> something, you get closer to it. 走近","examples":["He didn't approach the front door at once. 他沒有立即走近前門。","When I approached, they grew silent. 當我走近時，他們變得沉默了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>approach</b> someone <b>about</b> something, you speak to them about it for the first time, often making an offer or request. 與…接洽","examples":["When Brown approached me about the job, my first reaction was of disbelief. 當布朗為這份工作找我時，我的第一反應是不相信。","He approached me to create and design the restaurant. 他來找我創辦並設計那家餐館。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>approach</b> a task, problem, or situation in a particular way, you deal with it or think about it in that way. 處理","examples":["The Bank has approached the issue in a practical way. 該銀行已經務實地處理了這個問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"As you <b>approach</b> a future time or event, time passes so that you get gradually nearer to it. 逐漸接近 (某時間或事件)","examples":["There is a need for understanding and cooperation as we approach the summit. 在我們即將參加峰會之際需要理解與合作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>approaches</b> a particular level or state, it almost reaches that level or state. 幾乎達到 (某水平或狀態)","examples":["Oil prices have approached their highest level for almost ten years. 石油價格已幾乎達到近十年來的最高水平。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Approach</b> is also a noun. 走近","examples":["At their approach the little boy ran away and hid. 當他們走近時，那個小男孩跑開了並藏了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Approach</b> is also a noun. 接洽","examples":["There had already been approaches from buyers interested in the whole of the group. 已經有一些對整個集團感興趣的買主來接洽了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Approach</b> is also a noun. 臨近","examples":["...the festive spirit that permeated the house with the approach of Christmas. …隨著聖誕節的臨近而瀰漫在這所房子裡的節日氣氛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>approach</b> <b>to</b> a place is a road, path, or other route that leads to it. 路徑","examples":["The path serves as an approach to the boathouse. 這條小路是通向那個船庫的一條路徑。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>approach</b> <b>to</b> a task, problem, or situation is the way you deal with it or think about it. 方式","examples":["We will be exploring different approaches to gathering information. 我們將探索收集資訊的不同方法。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"As a future time or event <b>approaches</b>, it gradually gets nearer as time passes. 臨近","examples":["As autumn approached, the plants and colours in the garden changed. 秋天漸近，花園裡的植物與色調發生了變化。"]}]}]},"attitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"態度，看法；姿勢；個人風格；<非正式>敵視的態度；（飛機或宇宙飛船飛行時的）姿態；（芭蕾）鶴立式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>attitude</b> <b>to</b> something is the way that you think and feel about it, especially when this shows in the way you behave. 態度","examples":["...the general change in attitude toward handicapped people. …對殘疾人態度的普遍轉變。","Being unemployed produces negative attitudes to work. 失業會對工作產生消極態度。"]}]}]},"audience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀眾，聽眾；讀者；覲見，拜見；擁護者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>audience</b> at a play, concert, film, or public meeting is the group of people watching or listening to it. 觀眾","examples":["The entire audience broke into loud applause. 全場觀眾爆發出響亮的掌聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>audience</b> for a television or radio programme consists of all the people who watch or listen to it. 觀眾; 聽眾","examples":["The concert will be broadcast to a worldwide television audience estimated at one billion. 這場音樂會將向全世界大約十億電視觀眾轉播。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>audience</b> of a writer or artist is the people who read their books or look at their work. 讀者; 欣賞者","examples":["Say's writings reached a wide audience during his lifetime. 塞伊的作品在他有生之年就擁有了廣泛讀者。"]}]}]},"attempt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"努力，嘗試"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"試圖，努力；企圖殺害；（運動員創造記錄的）嘗試，衝擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>attempt</b> <b>to</b> do something, especially something difficult, you try to do it. 試圖 (尤指做困難的事)","examples":["The only time that we attempted to do something like that was in the city of Philadelphia. 我們惟一一次試圖做那樣的事是在費城。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make an <b>attempt</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try to do it, often without success. (常指不成功的) 企圖","examples":["...a deliberate attempt to destabilize the defence. …蓄意削弱防禦的企圖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>attempt on</b> someone's life is an attempt to kill them. (殺人) 企圖","examples":["...an attempt on the life of the former Iranian prime minister. …刺殺伊朗前總理的企圖。"]}]}]},"author":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"作者，著者；作家；發起者，創始人；作品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撰寫，寫作；發起，創造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>author</b> <b>of</b> a piece of writing is the person who wrote it. 作者","examples":["...Jill Phillips, author of the book \"Give Your Child Music.\" …吉爾·菲利浦斯，《把音樂給你的孩子》一書的作者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>author</b> is a person whose job is writing books. 作家","examples":["Haruki Murakami is Japan's best-selling author. 村上春樹是日本的暢銷書作家。"]}]}]},"auto":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"汽車的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"汽車"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"與汽車相關的；自動的；自身的；自發的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>auto</b> is a car. 汽車","examples":["...the auto industry. …汽車工業。"]}]}]},"automobile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汽車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>automobile</b> is a car. 汽車","examples":["...the automobile industry. …汽車工業。"]}]}]},"avenue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大街；（通向大宅子的）林蔭道；途徑，渠道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名稱內的名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Avenue</b> is sometimes used in the names of streets. The written abbreviation  is also used. 大街","examples":["...the most expensive apartments on Park Avenue. …派克大街上最昂貴的公寓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>avenue</b> is a wide, straight road, especially one with trees on either side. 林蔭大道","examples":[]}]}]},"ax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"削減，刪除；用斧修整；解僱；詢問"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"斧頭；爵士樂器（尤指吉他或薩克斯管）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Ax）（德、芬）阿克斯（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"award":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎，獎品；（收入的）增加；（賠償）裁定額；（畢業證書等的）授予；獎學金"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"授予，頒發；判給，裁定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>award</b> is a prize or certificate that a person is given for doing something well. 獎","examples":["The Institute's annual award is presented to organizations that are dedicated to democracy and human rights. 該協會的年度獎授予致力於民主與人權的組織。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In law, an <b>award</b> is a sum of money that a court decides should be given to someone. (賠償金等的) 裁定額","examples":["...worker's compensation awards. …工人的賠償金裁定額。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is awarded</b> something such as a prize or an examination mark, it is given to them. 被授予","examples":["She was awarded the prize for both films. 她因這兩部電影而獲獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>award</b> something <b>to</b> someone means to decide that it will be given to that person. 給予","examples":["We have awarded the contract to a New York-based company. 我們已經把這份合同給了一家總部設在紐約的公司。"]}]}]},"badminton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羽毛球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Badminton</b> is a game played by two or four players on a rectangular court with a high net across the middle. The players try to score points by hitting a small object called a shuttlecock across the net using a racket. 羽毛球運動","examples":[]}]}]},"bacon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"培根，煙燻鹹肉片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bacon</b> is salted or smoked meat which comes from the back or sides of a pig. 醃豬肉; 燻豬肉","examples":["...bacon and eggs. …醃豬肉和雞蛋。"]}]}]},"bacteria":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"細菌（bacterium的複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bacteria</b> are very small organisms. Some bacteria can cause disease. 細菌","examples":["Chlorine is added to kill bacteria. 加入氯以殺菌。"]}]}]},"axe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"斧，斧子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"削減，撤銷；解僱，開除；（用斧）砍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>axe</b> is a tool used for cutting wood. It consists of a heavy metal blade that is sharp at one edge and attached by its other edge to the end of a long handle. 斧子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone's job or something such as a public service or a television programme <b>is axed</b>, it is ended suddenly and without discussion. 被砍掉","examples":["Community projects are being axed by hard-pressed social services departments. 社群專案正遭到受困社會服務部門的削減。"]}]}]},"bait":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"用作誘餌的人（或物）；餌，誘餌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"放誘餌；激怒，故意惹惱；縱犬襲擊（動物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bait</b> is food which you put on a hook or in a trap in order to catch fish or animals. 餌","examples":["Vivien refuses to put down bait to tempt wildlife to the waterhole. 維維恩拒絕放餌到水坑引誘野生動物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To use something as <b>bait</b> means to use it to trick or persuade someone to do something. 誘餌","examples":["Television programmes are essentially bait to attract an audience for commercials. 電視節目本質上是用來吸引觀眾看商業廣告的誘餌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bait</b> a hook or trap, you put bait on it or in it. 放誘餌於","examples":["He baited his hook with pie. 他把餡餅放在釣鉤上作餌。","The boys dug pits and baited them so that they could spear their prey. 男孩子們挖了陷阱，在裡面放上誘餌，以便用矛刺殺獵物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bait</b> someone, you deliberately try to make them angry by teasing them. 故意惹怒","examples":["He delighted in baiting his mother. 他以惹他媽媽生氣為樂。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bait and switch</b> is used to refer to a sales technique in which goods are advertised at low prices in order to attract customers, although only a small number of the low-priced goods are available. 誘導轉向法 (以廉價商品誘使顧客上門的銷售方法)","examples":["The classy piano bar next to Maddalena's really sells 11 dishes for the advertised price at lunch. There's no bait and switch here. 馬達萊納隔壁的高階鋼琴酒吧按廣告中的價位售賣11道午餐菜餚。在這沒有用廉價品招攬生意的幌子。"]}]}]},"baggage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行李；思想包袱，成見"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>baggage</b> consists of the bags that you take with you when you travel. 行李","examples":["The passengers went through immigration control and collected their baggage. 乘客們透過了移民管理站然後領取了行李。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>baggage</b> to refer to someone's emotional problems, fixed ideas, or prejudices. (感情或思想上的) 包袱","examples":["How much emotional baggage is he bringing with him into the relationship? 他正把多少感情包袱帶入這個關係？"]}]}]},"average":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平均水平，一般標準；平均數，平均值；（海損的）平均分擔；（按保單規定應付賠償額的）降減，均減"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普通的，平常的；不好不壞的；平均（數）的；中等的，適中的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"平均為，平均達到；計算平均值；將……平均分配；（行情下跌時）買進更多的證券（或商品）以降低平均進價"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>average</b> is the result that you get when you add two or more numbers together and divide the total by the number of numbers you added together. 平均數","examples":["Take the average of those ratios and multiply by a hundred. 取那些比例的平均數再乘以100。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>average</b> to refer to a number or size that varies but is always approximately the same. 平均值","examples":["It takes an average of ten weeks for a house sale to be completed. 平均需要10周的時間才能完成一幢房子的銷售。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An amount or quality that is <b>the average</b> is the normal amount or quality for a particular group of things or people. 一般水平","examples":["35% of staff time was being spent on repeating work, about the average for a service industry. 員工35%的時間花費在重複勞動上，大約是服務業的一般水平。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Average</b> is also an adjective. 平均的","examples":["The average price of goods rose by just 2.2%. 商品的平均價格僅上漲了2.2%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Average</b> is also an adjective. 正常標準的","examples":["$2.20 for a beer is average. 一瓶啤酒$2.20是一般價位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>average</b> person or thing is typical or normal. 普通的","examples":["The average adult man burns 1,500 to 2,000 calories per day. 一個普通成年男子每天消耗1500到2000卡路里熱量。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>average</b> is neither very good nor very bad, usually when you had hoped it would be better. 平平的","examples":["I was only average academically. 我的學業成績只能算平平。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>average</b> a particular amount means to do, get, or produce that amount as an average over a period of time. 平均為","examples":["We averaged 42 miles per hour. 我們平均時速為42英里。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>on average</b> or <b>on the average</b> to indicate that a number is the average of several numbers. 按平均值","examples":["Shares rose, on average, by 38%. 股值平均上漲了38%。"]}]}]},"background":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出身背景，學歷，經歷；（事件或情況的）背景；背景聲音；（畫等的）後景；底色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"背景的，事先的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"作……的背景"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>background</b> is the kind of family you come from and the kind of education you have had. It can also refer to such things as your social and racial origins, your financial status, or the type of work experience that you have. (家庭、職業) 出身","examples":["The Warners were from a Jewish working-class background. 沃納一家人是猶太工人階級出身。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>background</b> to an event or situation consists of the facts that explain what caused it. 背景","examples":["The background to the current troubles is provided by the dire state of the country's economy. 目前這些問題的背景是嚴峻的國家經濟形勢。","The meeting takes place against a background of continuing political violence. 這次會議是在持續的政治暴力背景下召開的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>background</b> is sounds, such as music, that you can hear but that you are not listening to with your full attention. 背景聲音","examples":["I kept hearing the sound of applause in the background. 我不斷聽到背景音中有掌聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>background</b> to refer to the things in a picture or scene that are less noticeable or important than the main things or people in it. (圖畫、佈景等的) 背景","examples":["...roses patterned on a blue background. …印在藍色背景上的玫瑰。"]}]}]},"barn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"畜棚，穀倉；空蕩蕩的大建築；<美>（停放汽車、火車等的）大車庫；（尤用於粒子物理學）靶（恩）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>把……貯存入倉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barn</b> is a building on a farm in which animals, animal food, or crops can be kept. 穀倉; 牲口房","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any large building, esp an unattractive one 大倉棚","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a unit of nuclear cross section equal to 10<b>–</b> <b>28</b> square metre 靶; 核反應截面單位 ( symbol: b)","examples":[]}]}]},"bandage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繃帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用繃帶包紮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bandage</b> is a long strip of cloth that is wrapped around a wounded part of someone's body to protect or support it. 繃帶","examples":["We put some ointment and a bandage on his knee. 我們在他的膝蓋上塗了些藥膏，還纏了一條繃帶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bandage</b> a wound or part of someone's body, you tie a bandage around it. 用繃帶包紮","examples":["Apply a dressing to the wound and bandage it. 在傷口上敷上敷料並用繃帶包紮起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bandage up</b> means the same as . 用繃帶包紮","examples":["I bandaged the leg up and gave her aspirin for the pain. 我用繃帶把她的腿包紮起來，又給她阿斯匹林鎮痛。"]}]}]},"beast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"野獸，猛獸，牲畜；兇暴殘忍的人，道德敗壞的人；（具有某種特性的）東西，貨色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to an animal as a <b>beast</b>, especially if it is a large, dangerous, or unusual one. (尤指罕見或巨大凶猛的) 獸","examples":["...the threats our ancestors faced from wild beasts. …我們祖輩所面臨的來自野獸的威脅。"]}]}]},"barrel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桶；一桶（的量）；槍管，炮管；（馬等四足動物的）軀幹"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"飛奔，高速行駛；把……裝入桶內"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barrel</b> is a large, round container for liquids or food. 桶","examples":["The wine is aged for almost a year in oak barrels. 這葡萄酒在橡木桶裡陳了將近一年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the oil industry, a <b>barrel</b> is a unit of measurement equal to 42 gallons (159 litres). 桶 (石油計量單位，等於42 加侖或159升)","examples":["In 1989, Kuwait was exporting 1.5 million barrels of oil a day. 1989年，科威特每天出口150萬桶石油。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>barrel</b> of a gun is the tube through which the bullet moves when the gun is fired. 槍管; 炮管","examples":["He pushed the barrel of the gun into the other man's open mouth. 他把槍管插入另一個人張開著的嘴裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle or person <b>is barrelling</b> in a particular direction, they are moving very quickly in that direction. 高速行駛","examples":["The car was barrelling down the street at a crazy speed. 汽車沿著街道發瘋一般地高速行駛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say, for example, that someone moves or buys something <b>lock, stock, and barrel</b>, you are emphasizing that they move or buy every part or item of it. 完全","examples":["They received a verbal offer to buy the company lock, stock and barrel. 他們收到全盤收購公司的口頭承諾。"]}]}]},"beggar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乞丐，叫花子；<英，非正式>傢伙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使貧窮，使匱乏；難以相信，無法相容"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beggar</b> is someone who lives by asking people for money or food. 乞丐","examples":["There are no beggars on the street in Vienna. 維也納的街道上沒有乞丐。"]}]}]},"being":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物；存在；本質，本性"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"因為，由於（用於非限定分句）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"存在，生存；位於（be 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Being</b> is the present participle of . be的現在分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Being</b> is used in nonfinite clauses where you are giving the reason for something. 用於非限定分句，表示原因","examples":["It being a Sunday, the old men had the day off. 因為是星期天，老人們休了一天假。","Little boys, being what they are, might decide to play on it. 小男孩們也許會決定耍弄它，因為他們就是這樣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to any real or imaginary creature as a <b>being</b>. (任何真實或虛構的) 生物","examples":["People expect a horse to perform like a car, with no thought for its feelings as a living being. 人們期望一匹馬能表現得像一輛車那樣，卻沒考慮到它作為一個活的生物的感受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Being</b> is existence. Something that is <b>in being</b> or comes <b>into being</b> exists. 存在","examples":["Abraham Maslow described psychology as \"the science of being.\" 亞伯拉罕•馬斯洛將心理學描述為“存在科學”。"]}]}]},"belly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或動物的）腹部，肚子；胃，胃口；（物體的）腹狀部分；腹部豬肉切；（絃樂器的）面板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鼓起，張滿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>belly</b> of a person or animal is their stomach or abdomen. 肚子; 腹部","examples":["She laid her hands on her swollen belly. 她把手放在隆起的肚子上。","...a horse with its belly ripped open. …一匹被破開了肚子的馬。"]}]}]},"bay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（海或湖的）灣；山脈的低凹處，山間平地；（裝窗的）房間突出部分；間隔區，限定區域；月桂樹；棗紅馬，栗色馬；（尤指教堂中殿牆壁的）柱間距；（船或飛機上的）貨艙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（犬）連續吠，（狼）連續嚎叫；（尤指要求懲罰某人時）大聲叫嚷"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"棗紅色的，深棕色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bay</b> is a part of a coast where the land curves inward. 海灣","examples":["...a short ferry ride across the bay. …一趟跨海灣的短途渡輪旅程。","...the Bay of Bengal. …孟加拉灣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bay</b> is a partly enclosed area, inside or outside a building, that is used for a particular purpose. (建築物內或外闢作特定用途的) 隔區","examples":["The animals are herded into a bay, then butchered. 動物被趕到隔欄內，然後被屠宰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bay</b> is an area of a room that extends beyond the main walls of a house, especially an area with a large window at the front of a house. (尤指位於房屋前端並裝有大窗的) 凸出部分","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bay</b> horse is reddish-brown in colour. 紅棕色的","examples":["...a 10-year-old bay mare. …一匹10歲的紅棕色母馬。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a number of people <b>are baying</b> <b>for</b> something, they are demanding something angrily, usually that someone should be punished. 憤怒地要求","examples":["The referee ignored voices baying for a penalty. 裁判對憤怒要求懲罰的呼聲置之不理。","Opposition politicians have been baying for his blood. 反對派的政客們一直怒氣衝衝地要他的命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a dog or wolf <b>bays</b>, it makes loud, long cries. (犬或狼等) 嚎叫","examples":["A dog suddenly howled, baying at the moon. 一隻狗忽然嚎叫起來，對月長嗥。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> something or someone <b>at bay</b>, or <b>hold</b> them <b>at bay</b>, you prevent them from reaching, attacking, or affecting you. 使無法近身","examples":["Eating oranges keeps colds at bay. 吃橘子可防感冒。"]}]}]},"bang":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"突然的巨響；重擊，猛撞；劉海（bangs）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛敲，砰然重擊；猛摔；很響地使勁關上；（意外地）撞擊；與……性交；砰砰作響"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"恰好，正好；完全，徹底；突然，猛然"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"砰；突然，猛然"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bang</b> is a sudden loud noise such as the noise of an explosion. (突然的) 巨響","examples":["I heard four or five loud bangs. 我聽到四五聲巨響。","She slammed the door with a bang. 她砰地一聲關上門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bang</b> is also a noun. 撞傷","examples":["...a nasty bang on the head. …頭部可惡的撞傷。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>bangs</b>, it makes a sudden loud noise, once or several times. 砰然作響","examples":["The engine spat and banged. 引擎發出劈啪聲和砰砰巨響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bang</b> <b>into</b> something or someone, you bump or knock them hard, usually because you are not looking where you are going. (不小心) 猛撞上","examples":["I didn't mean to bang into you. 我不是故意撞你的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bang</b> a door or if it <b>bangs</b>, it closes suddenly with a loud noise. 砰地關上","examples":["...the sound of doors banging. …砰砰的關門聲。","All up and down the street the windows bang shut. 整條街的窗戶都砰砰關上了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bang</b> <b>on</b> something or if you <b>bang</b> it, you hit it hard, making a loud noise. 大聲猛擊","examples":["We could bang on the desks and shout till they let us out. 我們會大聲猛拍桌子，大聲喊叫，直到他們放我們出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bang</b> something on something or if you <b>bang</b> it down, you quickly and violently put it on a surface, because you are angry. (因生氣而) 猛然用力放","examples":["She banged his dinner on the table. 她猛地用力把他的晚飯砸在桌上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>bang</b> a part of your body, you accidentally knock it against something and hurt yourself. (無意中) 撞傷","examples":["She'd fainted and banged her head. 她暈了過去，撞傷了頭部。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>bang</b> to emphasize expressions that indicate an exact position or an exact time. 正好","examples":["...bang in the middle of the track. …在路的正中央。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something begins or ends <b>with a bang</b>, it begins or ends with a lot of energy, enthusiasm, or success. 轟轟烈烈地","examples":["Her career began with a bang in 1986. 她的事業在1986年轟轟烈烈地開始了。"]}]}]},"balance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平衡，均衡，均勢；平衡能力；賬戶餘額，結存；結欠，餘款；天平，秤；（樂器）平衡器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保持平衡；權衡，斟酌；使收支平衡；均衡，抵消"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>balance</b> something somewhere, or if it <b>balances</b> there, it remains steady and does not fall. 使平衡; 平衡","examples":["I balanced on the ledge. 我在巖脊上站穩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>balance</b> one thing <b>against</b> another, you consider its importance in relation to the other one. 權衡; 使協調","examples":["She carefully tried to balance religious sensitivities against democratic freedom. 她小心翼翼地試著協調宗教敏感性與民主自由。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>balances</b> their budget or if a government <b>balances</b> the economy of a country, they make sure that the amount of money that is spent is not greater than the amount that is received. 使 (收支) 平衡","examples":["He balanced his budgets by rigid control over public expenditure. 他透過嚴格控制公共開支來平衡預算。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>balance</b> your books or make them <b>balance</b>, you prove by calculation that the amount of money you have received is equal to the amount that you have spent. 使 (賬目) 平衡; (賬目) 平衡","examples":["...teaching them to balance the books. …教他們平衡賬目。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Balance</b> is the ability to remain steady when you are standing up. 平衡能力","examples":["The medicines you are currently taking could be affecting your balance. 你現在吃的藥可能會影響你的平衡能力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>balance</b> is a situation in which all the different parts are equal in strength or importance. 均衡","examples":["...the ecological balance of the forest. …森林的生態平衡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that <b>the</b> <b>balance</b> tips in your favour, you start winning or succeeding, especially in a conflict or contest. (表示衝突中的形勢) 天平","examples":["...a powerful new gun which could tip the balance of the war in their favour. …可能會使戰爭的天平向他們那邊傾斜的一種威力強大的新型炮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>balance</b> in your bank account is the amount of money you have in it. (賬戶上的) 餘額","examples":["I'd like to check the balance in my account please. 我想查一下我賬戶的餘額。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>balance</b> of an amount of money is what remains to be paid for something or what remains when part of the amount has been spent. 餘款; 結餘","examples":["They were due to pay the balance on delivery. 他們定在貨到時支付餘款。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>balance</b> one thing <b>with</b> something different, each of the things has the same strength or importance. 使均衡","examples":["Balance spicy dishes with mild ones. 使辛辣的菜和清淡的菜均衡。","The government has to find some way to balance these two needs. 政府得找到某種方法來平衡這兩種需求。","Supply and demand on the currency market will generally balance. 貨幣市場上的供需關係將會大致平衡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"均衡的","examples":["This book is a well balanced biography. 這是一本很公正的傳記。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>balance</b>, for example, when standing in a moving vehicle, you remain steady and do not fall over. If you <b>lose</b> your <b>balance</b>, you become unsteady and fall over. 保持/失去平衡","examples":["She was holding onto the rail to keep her balance. 她抓著欄杆來保持身體平衡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>off balance</b>, you are in an unsteady position and about to fall. 失去平衡","examples":["A gust of wind knocked him off balance and he fell face down in the mud. 一陣大風吹得他失去了平衡，臉朝下摔在了泥裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say <b>on balance</b> to indicate that you are stating an opinion after considering all the relevant facts or arguments. 總的說來","examples":["On balance he agreed with Christine. 總的說來，他同意克里斯蒂娜的看法。"]}]}]},"bingo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賓果遊戲（一種賭博遊戲）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"贏啦（用於宣佈在賓戈遊戲中獲勝）；（表示驚訝、得意）瞧，嘿；好，妙（成功做成某事後發出的高興的叫聲）；對，好（用於表示對方的說法正確）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bingo</b> is a game in which each player has a card with numbers on it. Someone calls out numbers and if you are the first person to have all your numbers called out, you win the game. 賓戈遊戲 (一種賭博遊戲)","examples":["...a bingo hall. …一間賓戈遊戲廳。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>\"bingo!\"</b> when something pleasant happens, especially in a surprising, unexpected, or sudden way, or to show that you have just achieved or discovered something. 因突然出現的好事或成功所發出的叫聲","examples":["She grinned. \"Wow, bingo! Got it in one.\" 她咧嘴笑了。“哇，好！一下就中了。”"]}]}]},"billion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"num.","zh":"十億；<舊>萬億"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"十億；億萬，大量（billions）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>billion</b> is a thousand million. 10億","examples":["The Ethiopian foreign debt stands at 3 billion dollars. 衣索比亞的外債達30億美元。"]}]},{"pos":"quant-plural.","pos_name":"複數型數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about <b>billions of</b> people or things, you mean that there is a very large number of them but you do not know or do not want to say exactly how many. 億萬","examples":["Biological systems have been doing this for billions of years. 生物系統億萬年來都在這樣做。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can also use <b>billions</b> as a pronoun. 億萬","examples":["He thought that it must be worth billions. 他認為它一定值億萬元。"]}]}]},"biscuit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英> 餅乾，薄薄一片的甜餅；<美> 鬆餅(食用時常佐以肉汁)；陶瓷素燒坯（經燒製但未上釉的陶瓷土坯）；淡褐色，灰黃色；（嵌入兩塊木板中的溝槽將其連線起來的）小木片，木榫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>biscuit</b> is a small flat cake that is crisp and usually sweet. (扁平、鬆脆的) 小甜餅","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>biscuit</b> is a small round dry cake that is made with baking powder, baking soda, or yeast. 小圓餅乾","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has done something very stupid, rude, or selfish, you can say that they <b>take the biscuit</b> or that what they have done <b>takes the biscuit</b>, to emphasize your surprise at their behaviour. 糟糕透頂","examples":[]}]}]},"berry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漿果，莓；果仁，果核；蝦子，魚子；無核漿果"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"採集漿果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Berries</b> are small, round fruit that grow on a bush or a tree. Some berries are edible, for example, blackberries and raspberries. 莓","examples":[]}]}]},"bible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"權威著作，寶典；《聖經》（the Bible）；一本《聖經》，《聖經》的一個版本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>Bible</b> is the holy book on which the Jewish and Christian religions are based. 《聖經》","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bible</b> is a copy of the Bible. (一本) 《聖經》","examples":["...a publisher of bibles and hymn books. …一家《聖經》冊本和聖歌集出版商。"]}]}]},"blouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（女式）短上衣，襯衫；寬鬆上衣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（衣服）松垂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blouse</b> is a kind of shirt worn by a girl or woman. 女式襯衫","examples":[]}]}]},"benefit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"好處，益處；救濟金，補助金；額外獎勵，保險金；慈善活動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對（某人）有用，使受益；得益於，得利於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>benefit</b> <b>of</b> something is the help that you get from it or the advantage that results from it. 益處; 成效","examples":["Each family farms individually and reaps the benefit of its labour. 每個家庭獨立耕作，收穫各自的勞動成果。","I'm a great believer in the benefits of this form of therapy. 我對這種療法的益處深信不疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>to</b> your <b>benefit</b> or is <b>of</b> <b>benefit</b> <b>to</b> you, it helps you or improves your life. 好處","examples":["This could now work to Albania's benefit. 這可能現在對阿爾巴尼亞有利。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have the <b>benefit of</b> some information, knowledge, or equipment, you are able to use it so that you can achieve something. 優勢","examples":["Steve didn't have the benefit of a formal college education. 史蒂夫沒有接受過正規大學教育的優勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Benefits</b> are money or other advantages which come from your job, the government, or an insurance company. 福利","examples":["McCary will receive about $921,000 in retirement benefits. 麥克卡里將獲得大約九十二萬一千美元的退休福利。","...the skyrocketing cost of health care and medical benefits. …一路飈升的健康保健和醫療保險福利金。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>benefit</b>, or a <b>benefit</b> concert or dinner, is an event that is held in order to raise money for a particular charity or person. 義演","examples":["...a memorial benefit concert for the Bonhoeffer endowment. …一場紀念邦赫費爾基金的慈善音樂會。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>benefit</b> <b>from</b> something or if it <b>benefits</b> you, it helps you or improves your life. 有益於; 得益","examples":["Both sides have benefited from the talks. 雙方都從會談中獲益。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone <b>the benefit of the doubt</b>, you treat them as if they are telling the truth or as if they have behaved properly, even though you are not sure that this is the case. 姑且信其為真","examples":["At first I gave him the benefit of the doubt. 起初我姑且信了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is doing something <b>for the benefit of</b> a particular person, you mean that they are doing it for that person. 為了某人的利益","examples":["You need people working for the benefit of the community. 你需要一些為公眾利益服務的人。"]}]}]},"blanket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毯子，毛毯；厚層，覆蓋層；氣氛，氛圍；障礙，障礙物；（平版印刷的）橡皮布；（平版印刷的）橡皮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"覆蓋，蓋住，籠罩；消除（聲音），使（聲音）模糊不清；迎風航行搶（他船）的上風"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總括的，全面的，通用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blanket</b> is a large square or rectangular piece of thick cloth, especially one that you put on a bed to keep you warm. 毯子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>blanket</b> <b>of</b> something such as snow is a continuous layer of it which hides what is below or beyond it. 覆蓋層","examples":["The mud disappeared under a blanket of snow. 泥地在一層白雪的覆蓋下消失不見了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as snow <b>blankets</b> an area, it covers it. 覆蓋","examples":["More than a foot of snow blanketed parts of Michigan. 一英尺多厚的白雪覆蓋了密歇根州的部分地區。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>blanket</b> to describe something when you want to emphasize that it affects or refers to every person or thing in a group, without any exceptions. 適用於全體的","examples":["There's already a blanket ban on foreign unskilled labour in Japan. 日本已經有一項禁止使用外國非熟練工人的通用禁令。"]}]}]},"bravery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇敢的行為（態度），勇氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bravery</b> is brave behaviour or the quality of being brave. 勇敢之舉; 勇敢","examples":["He deserves the highest praise for his bravery. 他為其勇敢應該得到至高的讚揚。"]}]}]},"blame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"責怪，歸咎於；怨，怪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"責備，過錯，罪責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blame</b> a person or thing <b>for</b> something bad, or if you <b>blame</b> something bad <b>on</b> somebody, you believe or say that they are responsible for it or that they caused it. 指責; 把…歸咎於","examples":["The commission is expected to blame the army for many of the atrocities. 該委員會預計會將大量暴行歸咎於軍隊。","Ms. Carey appeared to blame her breakdown on EMI's punishing work schedule. 凱麗女士看來是將自己的崩潰歸咎於百代公司緊張的工作安排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you do not <b>blame</b> someone <b>for</b> doing something, you mean that you consider it was a reasonable thing to do in the circumstances. 責怪","examples":["I do not blame them for trying to make some money. 我不怪他們想要掙些錢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Blame</b> is also a noun. 責備","examples":["Nothing could relieve my terrible sense of blame. 沒什麼能把我從極度自責中解脫出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>blame</b> <b>for</b> something bad that has happened is the responsibility for causing it or letting it happen. (事故、過失等的) 責任","examples":["I'm not going to sit around and take the blame for a mistake he made. 我不會閒坐著，為他犯的錯誤承擔責任。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>to blame</b> <b>for</b> something bad that has happened, they are responsible for causing it. 該受責備","examples":["If their forces were not involved, then who is to blame? 如果他們的軍隊沒有參與，那麼誰應該受到指責呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has only</b> themselves <b>to blame</b> or <b>has no one but</b> themselves <b>to blame</b>, you mean that they are responsible for something bad that has happened to them and that you have no sympathy for them. 只能責怪自己","examples":["My life is ruined and I suppose I only have myself to blame. 我的一生都毀了，我想這隻能怪我自己。"]}]}]},"brass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃銅；銅管樂器；黃銅器，黃銅飾品；<非正式>高階官員，高階軍官；<英，非正式>錢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Brass</b> is a yellow-coloured metal made from copper and zinc. It is used especially for making ornaments and musical instruments. 黃銅","examples":["The instrument is beautifully made in brass. 這個樂器是用黃銅精緻鑄造成的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>brass</b> is the section of an orchestra which consists of brass wind instruments such as trumpets and horns. 銅管樂器","examples":["Consequently even this vast chorus was occasionally overwhelmed by the brass. 結果連這個大合唱偶爾也被銅管樂所壓倒。"]}]}]},"boot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靴子；猛踢；（汽車的）行李箱，後備箱；車輪固定夾；解僱；再者，除此之外（to boot）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛踢；鎖住（非法停車的輪子）；啟動（電腦）；在車輪上裝制動裝置；解僱；（使）穿靴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boots</b> are shoes that cover your whole foot and the lower part of your leg. 靴子","examples":["He sat in a kitchen chair, reached down and pulled off his boots. 他坐在廚房的椅子上，彎腰脫掉了靴子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Boots</b> are strong, heavy shoes that cover your ankle and that have thick soles. You wear them to protect your feet, for example, when you are walking or taking part in sports. (步行或運動時穿的) 厚底靴","examples":["The soldiers' boots resounded in the street. 士兵們的厚底靴在街道上發出迴響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a kick 踢","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>boot</b>\nof a car is a covered space at the back or front in which you put luggage or other things.\n (\n汽車的\n)\n行李箱","examples":["She opened the boot of the car and started to take out a bag of groceries. 她開啟汽車的行李箱，開始拿出一袋雜貨。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(esp in football) to kick (尤指足球中)踢","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to be of advantage or use to (a person) 成為(某人的)優勢; 對(某人)有用","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>boot</b> a car means the same as to  a car. 用車輪鉗鎖鎖住 (車輛)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a computer <b>boots</b> or you <b>boot</b> it, it is made ready to use by putting in the instructions it needs in order to start working. 啟動","examples":["The computer won't boot. 計算機無法啟動。","Put the CD into the drive and boot the machine. 把光碟放進驅動器，然後啟動機器。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boot up</b> means the same as . 啟動","examples":["Go over to your PC and boot it up. 到你的個人電腦那兒，啟動它。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get the boot</b> or <b>are given the boot</b>, you are told that you are not wanted anymore, either in your job or by someone you are having a relationship with. 被解僱; 被拋棄","examples":["She was a disruptive influence, and after a year or two she got the boot. 她是個搗亂分子，一兩年後就被解僱了。"]}]}]},"breast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乳房；胸部，胸脯；心情，內心"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"登上……的頂部；挺胸頂著……；與……搏鬥，迎……而上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A woman's <b>breasts</b> are the two soft, round parts on her chest that can produce milk to feed a baby. (女性的) 乳房","examples":["She wears a low-cut dress which reveals her breasts. 她穿著一件低胸露乳的連衣裙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>breast</b> is the upper part of his or her chest. (人的) 胸部","examples":["He struck his breast in a dramatic gesture. 他以戲劇性的姿態捶他的胸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A bird's <b>breast</b> is the front part of its body. (鳥的) 胸脯","examples":["The cock's breast is tinged with chestnut. 這隻公雞的胸脯帶點栗色。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>breast</b> of a shirt, jacket, or coat is the part which covers the top part of the chest. (襯衫、外套、大衣等的) 胸部","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to a piece of meat that is cut from the front of a bird or lamb as <b>breast</b>. (禽類或羔羊的) 胸脯肉","examples":["...a chicken breast with vegetables. …配著蔬菜的一塊雞胸肉。"]}]}]},"bore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使厭煩，使討厭；鑽（孔），挖（洞）；盯著看"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"令人討厭的人；使人厭煩的事；內徑，口徑；探孔，鑽孔；湧潮，激潮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>bores</b> you, you find them dull and uninteresting. 使厭煩","examples":["Dickie bored him all through the meal with stories of the navy. 迪基整整一頓飯都在講海軍的故事，讓他厭煩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>bore</b> a hole in something, you make a deep round hole in it using a special tool. 鑽 (孔)","examples":["Get the special drill bit to bore the correct size hole for the job. 找個特殊的鑽頭，鑽個尺寸合適的孔。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>bores</b> you <b>to tears</b>, <b>bores</b> you <b>to death</b>, or <b>bores</b> you <b>stiff</b>, they bore you very much. 使…厭煩至極","examples":["Monuments and museums bore him to tears. 紀念碑和博物館讓他厭煩透了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe someone as a <b>bore</b> when you think that they talk in a very uninteresting way. 無聊的傢伙","examples":["There is every reason why I shouldn't enjoy his company – he's a bore and a fool. 我有充分的理由不和他在一起–他是個無聊的傢伙，一個傻瓜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a situation as <b>a bore</b> when you find it annoying. 令人討厭的事","examples":["It's a bore to be sick, and the novelty of lying in bed all day wears off quickly. 生病是件無趣的事，整天躺在床上的新鮮感很快就沒了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a high steep-fronted wave moving up a narrow estuary, caused by the tide 湧潮","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bore</b> is the past tense of <b>bear</b>. (bear)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"border":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國境，邊界；鑲邊，包邊；狹長花壇，花帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"接壤，毗鄰；環繞，沿……的邊緣；近似，相像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>border</b> between two countries or regions is the dividing line between them. Sometimes <b>the border</b> also refers to the land close to this line. 邊界; 邊界地區","examples":["They fled across the border. 他們越過邊界逃走了。","Soldiers had temporarily closed the border between the two countries. 士兵們已暫時封閉了兩國的邊界。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>border</b> is a strip or band around the edge of something. 飾邊","examples":["...pillowcases trimmed with a hand-crocheted border. …鑲有一道手工鉤制花邊的枕套。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a garden, a <b>border</b> is a long strip of ground planted with flowers, along the edge of a path or lawn. (小路或草地邊) 狹長花壇","examples":["...a lawn flanked by wide herbaceous borders. …一片兩側有草本植物花壇的草坪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A country that <b>borders</b> another country, a sea, or a river is next to it. 與…接壤","examples":["...the European and Arab countries bordering the Mediterranean. …地中海沿岸的歐洲國家和阿拉伯國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is bordered</b> by another thing, the other thing forms a line along the edge of it. 給…鑲邊","examples":["...the mile of white sand beach bordered by palm trees and tropical flowers. …環繞著棕櫚樹和熱帶花卉的一英里白色沙灘。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Border on</b> means the same as . 與…接壤","examples":["Both republics border on the Black Sea. 這兩個共和國都與黑海毗鄰。"]}]}]},"brake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剎車，車閘；阻礙，抑制；<史>敞篷四輪馬車；（亞麻纖維等的）搗碎機；<古>灌木叢；歐洲蕨，鳳尾蕨"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"剎車，用閘減速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Brakes</b> are devices in a vehicle that make it go slower or stop. 剎車","examples":["A seagull swooped down in front of her car, causing her to slam on the brakes. 一隻海鷗突然飛撲到她的車前,導致她猛踩剎車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>brake</b> in a number of expressions to indicate that something has slowed down or stopped. 停止; 減速","examples":["Illness had put a brake on his progress. 疾病中止了他的進展。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an area of dense undergrowth, shrubs, brushwood, etc; thicket 灌木叢","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a vehicle or its driver <b>brakes</b>, or when a driver <b>brakes</b> a vehicle, the driver makes it slow down or stop by using the brakes. 剎車","examples":["He heard tyres squeal as the car braked to avoid a collision. 他聽到當汽車剎車為避免撞車時輪胎髮出了刺耳的尖聲。","He braked the car slightly. 他稍稍剎車。"]}]}]},"bride":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新娘，即將（或剛）結婚的女子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bride</b> is a woman who is getting married or who has just got married. 新娘","examples":["Guests toasted the bride and groom with champagne. 客人們以香檳為新娘新郎敬酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a thread or loop that joins parts of a pattern 花邊上連線花紋用的窄條 (Also called bar)","examples":[]}]}]},"breeze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"微風，和風；輕而易舉的事；煤屑，焦炭渣；<英，非正式>騷動，爭吵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕盈而自信地走；輕鬆過關，輕易透過；吹微風"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>breeze</b> is a gentle wind. 微風","examples":["...a cool summer breeze. …一陣涼爽的夏風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an easy task or state of ease","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"ashes of coal, coke, or charcoal used to make breeze blocks (做空心煤渣磚用的)煤炭灰","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>breeze</b> <b>into</b> a place or a position, you enter it in a very casual or relaxed manner. 輕而易舉","examples":["Lopez breezed into the quarter-finals of the tournament. 洛佩斯輕鬆進入了那次錦標賽的四分之一決賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>breeze through</b> something such as a game or test, you cope with it easily. 輕鬆應付","examples":["John seems to breeze effortlessly through his many commitments at work. 約翰似乎對他工作中的許多職責應付自如。"]}]}]},"brook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小溪，小河"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>容忍，允許（尤指不同意見或反對意見）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brook</b> is a small stream. 小溪","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in a position of authority will <b>brook no</b> interference or opposition, they will not accept any interference or opposition from others. 允許","examples":["From childhood on, she'd had a plan of action, one that would brook no interference. 從兒時起，她已有了一個行動計劃，不容干預。"]}]}]},"broom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"掃帚；金雀花"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>broom</b> is a kind of brush with a long handle. You use a broom for sweeping the floor. 掃帚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Broom</b> is a wild bush with a lot of tiny yellow flowers. 金雀花","examples":[]}]}]},"breath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"呼吸，氣息；一次吸入的空氣；（風或氣流的）一絲，絲毫；微量，跡象；一瞬間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>breath</b> is the air that you let out through your mouth when you breathe. If someone has <b>bad breath</b>, their breath smells unpleasant. 呼氣","examples":["I could smell the whisky on his breath. 我能從他的呼氣中聞到威士忌酒味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you take a <b>breath</b>, you breathe in once. 呼吸","examples":["He took a deep breath, and began to climb the stairs. 他深深地吸了一口氣,然後開始爬樓梯。","Gasping for breath, she leaned against the door. 她靠在門上,大口喘著氣,"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go outside <b>for a breath of fresh air</b> or <b>for a breath of air</b>, you go outside because it is unpleasantly warm indoors. (到戶外) 透口氣","examples":["I had to step outside for a breath of fresh air. 我得到外面去透口氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something new or different as <b>a breath of fresh air</b>, you mean that it makes a situation or subject more interesting or exciting. 帶來新氣象","examples":["Her brisk treatment of an almost taboo subject was a breath of fresh air. 她對一個幾乎是禁忌話題的乾脆處理令人耳目一新。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>get</b> your <b>breath back</b> after doing something energetic, you start breathing normally again. 緩過氣來","examples":["I reached out a hand to steady myself against the house while I got my breath back. 我伸出一隻手撐在房子上使自己站穩,緩口氣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>out of breath</b>, you are breathing very quickly and with difficulty because you have been doing something energetic. 喘不過氣","examples":["She was slightly out of breath from running. 她跑過後有點上氣不接下氣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>in the same breath</b> or <b>in the next breath</b> to indicate that someone says two very different or contradictory things, especially when you are criticizing them. 自相矛盾","examples":["He hailed this week's arms agreement but in the same breath expressed suspicion about the motivations of the United States. 他讚揚了這周的武器協定,可自相矛盾的是又表示了對美國的動機的懷疑。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you are <b>short of breath</b>, you find it difficult to breathe properly, for example, because you are ill. You can also say that someone suffers from <b>shortness of breath</b>. 氣短","examples":["She felt short of breath and flushed. 她感到氣短,臉也紅了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say something <b>under</b> your <b>breath</b>, you say it in a very quiet voice, often because you do not want other people to hear what you are saying. 低聲地","examples":["Walsh muttered something under his breath. 沃爾什低聲嘀咕了什麼。"]}]}]},"brow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>額；眉毛；坡頂；（從船到岸上的）跳板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>brow</b> is your forehead. 額頭","examples":["He wiped his brow with the back of his hand. 他用手背擦了擦額頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>brows</b> are your eyebrows. 眉毛","examples":["He had thick brown hair and shaggy brows. 他長著濃密褐色的頭髮和濃粗雜亂的眉毛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>brow</b> <b>of</b> a hill is the top part of it. 頂部","examples":["He was on the lookout just below the brow of the hill. 他就在山頂之下放哨。"]}]}]},"bud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芽，花蕾；<美，非正式>夥計，老兄；芽體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發芽，長出花蕾；為……進行芽接"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bud</b> is a small pointed lump that appears on a tree or plant and develops into a leaf or flower. 芽; 花蕾","examples":["Rosanna's favourite time is early summer, just before the buds open. 羅莎娜最喜歡的時節是初夏，就在花蕾開放之前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"buddy的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nip</b> something such as bad behaviour <b>in the bud</b>, you stop it before it can develop very far. 把某事物掐滅於萌芽狀態","examples":["It is important to recognize jealousy and to nip it in the bud before it gets out of hand. 意識到嫉妒並在它發展到無法控制之前就把它消滅於萌芽狀態，這一點至關重要。"]}]}]},"bucket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桶；一桶之量；（機器的）挖鬥，剷鬥；大量；投籃得分；儲存桶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>快速顛簸著行駛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bucket</b> is a round metal or plastic container with a handle attached to its sides. Buckets are often used for holding and carrying water. (有提樑的) 桶","examples":["We drew water in a bucket from the well outside the door. 我們用水桶從門外的井裡提水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bucket</b> <b>of</b> something such as water is the amount of it that is contained in a bucket. 一桶之量","examples":["She threw a bucket of water over them. 她向他們潑了一桶水。"]}]}]},"buffalo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"野牛，犎牛；水牛；牛胭魚"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為難，使困惑；<美，非正式>嚇唬，威嚇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>buffalo</b> is a wild animal like a large cow with horns that curve upwards. Buffalo are usually found in southern and eastern Africa. 水牛","examples":[]}]}]},"bulb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電燈泡；（植物的）鱗莖，球莖；球狀物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bulb</b> is the glass part of an electric light or lamp, which gives out light when electricity passes through it. 電燈泡","examples":["The stairwell was lit by a single bulb. 樓梯間只有一盞燈照明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bulb</b> is a root shaped like an onion that grows into a flower or plant. 球莖","examples":["...tulip bulbs. …鬱金香球莖。"]}]}]},"budget":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預算；政府預算案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"制定預算，制定開支計劃；計劃，安排"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"廉價的，經濟型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>budget</b> is the amount of money that you have available to spend. The <b>budget</b> for something is the amount of money that a person, organization, or country has available to spend on it. 預算","examples":["She will design a fantastic new kitchen for you – and all within your budget. 她將為你設計一個嶄新的漂亮廚房–所有的花費都將在你的預算之內。","Someone had furnished the place on a tight budget. 有人用不多的錢把那個地方佈置了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>budget</b> of an organization or country is its financial situation, considered as the difference between the money it receives and the money it spends. (機構、政府等的) 財政收支狀況","examples":["The hospital obviously needs to balance the budget each year. 該醫院顯然每年都需要平衡其財務收支。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"預算","examples":["We have continued to exercise caution in our budgeting for the current year. 在今年的預算方面，我們繼續小心謹慎。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>budget</b> certain amounts of money for particular things, you decide that you can afford to spend those amounts on those things. 安排開支; 編制預算","examples":["The company has budgeted $10 million for advertising. 公司已經安排了1千萬美元的廣告預算。","The film is only budgeted at $10 million. 這部電影的預算只有1千萬美元。","I'm learning how to budget. 我正在學習怎樣編制預算。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Budget</b> is used in advertising to suggest that something is being sold cheaply. 價格低廉的","examples":["Cheap flights are available from budget travel agents from $240. 起價$240的廉價機票可從一些經濟旅行社那裡買到。"]}]}]},"bubble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣泡，泡沫；經濟泡沫；（欲表達的）一點感情；氣泡框；泡狀物；安全的地方（或位置）；泡螺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"冒泡，沸騰；發出冒泡的聲音；忙碌，活躍；興奮，激動；（情緒、感情等）湧動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bubbles</b> are small balls of air or gas in a liquid. (液體中的) 氣泡","examples":["Ink particles attach themselves to air bubbles and rise to the surface. 墨點吸附在氣泡上，升到表面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bubble</b> is a hollow ball of soapy liquid that is floating in the air or standing on a surface. 肥皂泡","examples":["With soap and water, bubbles and boats, children love bathtime. 因為有肥皂、水、肥皂泡和小船，孩子們都喜歡洗澡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a cartoon, a speech <b>bubble</b> is the shape which surrounds the words which a character is thinking or saying. (圈注漫畫中人物心理活動或對白的) 泡狀框","examples":["All that was missing were speech bubbles saying, \"Golly!\" and \"Wow!\" 漏掉的都是寫著“呀！”和“哇！”的泡狀話框。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a liquid <b>bubbles</b>, bubbles move in it, for example, because it is boiling or moving quickly. 冒泡; 沸騰","examples":["Heat the seasoned stock until it is bubbling. 把這些調了味的湯汁加熱至沸騰為止。","The fermenting wine has bubbled up and over the top. 這些發酵的酒已經冒泡溢位來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A feeling, influence, or activity that <b>is bubbling</b> away continues to occur. 繼續發生","examples":["...political tensions that have been bubbling away for years. …持續了若干年的政治緊張局勢。"]}]}]},"buffet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自助餐；快餐部，點心櫃；<美>餐具架，餐具櫃；<舊>打擊；<蘇格蘭>矮凳，踏腳凳"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"連續猛擊，打擊；<文>虐待，不公正地對待"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自助的；自助餐的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>buffet</b> is a meal of food that is displayed on a long table at a party or public occasion. Guests usually serve themselves. 自助餐","examples":["...a buffet lunch. …自助午餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>buffet</b> is a café, usually in a hotel or station. (旅館、車站等處的) 餐飲部","examples":["We sat in the station buffet sipping tea. 我們坐在車站餐飲部喝茶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a blow, esp with a fist or hand (尤指用拳頭或手的)一擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is buffeted</b> by strong winds or by stormy seas, it is repeatedly struck or blown around by them. (狂風、巨浪) 反覆襲擊","examples":["Their plane had been severely buffeted by storms. 他們的飛機遭到了暴風雨的猛烈襲擊。"]}]}]},"bullet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"子彈，彈丸；（標示用的）黑圓點；<美>（運動中）高速球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bullet</b> is a small piece of metal with a pointed or rounded end, which is fired out of a gun. 子彈","examples":["Two of the police fired 16 bullets each. 兩名警察各發射了16枚子彈。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>bites the bullet</b>, they accept that they have to do something unpleasant but necessary. 硬著頭皮接受","examples":["Tour operators may be forced to bite the bullet and cut prices. 旅遊社的經營者們不得不忍痛降價。"]}]}]},"bull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公牛；雄性大型動物；買空者，多頭；教皇詔書，教皇訓諭；<非正式>廢話，胡說八道；靶心"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>用力推，猛推；（母牛）發情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bull</b> is a male animal of the cow family. 公牛","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some other male animals, including elephants and whales, are called <b>bulls</b>. 巨大的雄性動物","examples":["Suddenly a massive bull elephant with huge tusks charged us. 突然，一隻體形壯碩、長著巨型象牙的雄象朝我們衝了過來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the stock market, <b>bulls</b> are people who buy shares in expectation of a price rise, in order to make a profit by selling the shares again after a short time. Compare <b>bear</b>. (股票市場上) 買空的人","examples":["The bulls argue stock prices are low and there are bargains to be had. 那些買空者認為股價很低，有些便宜股可以買進。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In the Roman Catholic church, a papal <b>bull</b> is an official statement on a particular subject that is issued by the pope. 教皇訓諭","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>bull</b> or a load of <b>bull</b>, you mean that it is complete nonsense or absolutely untrue. 胡說八道","examples":["I think it's a load of bull. 我覺得那是一派胡言。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"male; masculine 男性的; 雄性的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to raise or attempt to raise the price or prices of (a stock market or a security) by speculative buying (透過投機)推高股價","examples":[]}]}]},"burglar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"入室行竊者，竊賊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>burglar</b> is a thief who enters a house or other building by force. 強行入室的竊賊","examples":["Burglars broke into their home. 竊賊闖進了他們家。"]}]}]},"bump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使身體部位等）碰上，撞上；（無意地）碰，撞；顛簸行進；拖拽；擠出，擠掉；改變（廣播或電視節目的時間）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"腫塊；隆起，凸塊；碰撞，撞擊；輕微撞車事故；屁股向前扭動的性感動作；<美，非正式>增加；絨布"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bump</b> into something or someone, you accidentally hit them while you are moving. 撞上","examples":["They stopped walking and he almost bumped into them. 他們停下了腳步，這下他幾乎撞到他們。","She bumped her head against a low branch. 她的頭撞到一根低矮的樹枝上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bump</b> is also a noun. 碰撞","examples":["Small children often cry after a minor bump. 小孩子們在輕微的碰撞後常常會哭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bump</b> is the action or the dull sound of two heavy objects hitting each other. 碰撞; 碰撞聲","examples":["I felt a little bump and I knew instantly what had happened. 我感到了一下輕輕的撞擊，立刻就明白髮生了什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bump</b> is a minor injury or swelling that you get if you bump into something or if something hits you. 腫塊","examples":["She fell against our coffee table and got a large bump on her forehead. 她撞到了我們的咖啡桌跌倒了，前額起了一個大包。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bump</b> on a road is a raised, uneven part. (路面) 隆起部分","examples":["The truck hit a bump and bounced. 卡車開到了路面上一塊隆起的地方，顛簸起來。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>bumps</b> <b>over</b> a surface, it travels in a rough, bouncing way because the surface is very uneven. 顛簸行駛","examples":["We left the road, and again bumped over the mountainside. 我們離開公路，又一次在山坡上顛簸行駛。"]}]}]},"cabin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小木屋；船艙；機艙，客艙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>使身居斗室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cabin</b> is a small wooden house, especially one in an area of forests or mountains. 小木屋","examples":["...a log cabin. … 一間小木屋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cabin</b> is a small room in a ship or boat. 船艙","examples":["He showed her to a small cabin. 他把她帶到一間小房艙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cabin</b> is one of the areas inside a plane. 機艙","examples":["He sat quietly in the first class cabin of the flight looking tired. 他靜靜地坐在班機的頭等艙內，看上去有些疲憊。"]}]}]},"campus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大學或學院的）校園；大學生活；大學（學校、醫院等機構的）場地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>campus</b> is an area of land that contains the main buildings of a university or college. (大學的) 校園","examples":["...during a rally at the campus. …在一次校園集會時。"]}]}]},"canoe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨木舟，小划子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"劃獨木舟，乘獨木舟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>canoe</b> is a small, narrow boat that you move through the water using a stick with a wide end called a paddle. 划子; 獨木舟","examples":[]}]}]},"cane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"莖；藤條；（舊時用於懲罰學生的）笞杖，笞條；柺杖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用藤條鞭打；<英，非正式>大敗，重創；<英，非正式>大量飲酒，大量吸毒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cane</b> is used to refer to the long, hollow, hard stems of plants such as bamboo. Strips of cane are often used to make furniture, and some types of cane can be crushed and processed to make sugar. (竹或甘蔗的) 莖","examples":["...cane furniture. …藤製傢俱。","...cane sugar. …蔗糖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cane</b> is a long thin stick with a curved or round top which you can use to support yourself when you are walking, or which in the past was fashionable to carry with you. 手杖","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to whip or beat with or as if with a cane 用笞杖打; 鞭打","examples":[]}]}]},"bunch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"束，串，扎；一夥，一群；大量；<英>髮辮（bunches）；突起"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捆，扎，使集中；收緊，起褶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bunch</b> <b>of</b> people is a group of people who share one or more characteristics or who are doing something together. 夥","examples":["My neighbours are a bunch of busybodies. 我的鄰居們都是一夥愛管閒事的人。","We were a pretty inexperienced bunch of people really. 我們實際上是一群相當沒有經驗的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bunch</b> <b>of</b> flowers is a number of flowers with their stalks held or tied together. 束","examples":["He had left a huge bunch of flowers in her hotel room. 他在她的賓館房間裡留了一大束花。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bunch</b> <b>of</b> bananas or grapes is a group of them growing on the same stem. 串","examples":["Lili had fallen asleep clutching a fat bunch of grapes. 莉莉手裡抓著一大串葡萄睡著了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bunch</b> <b>of</b> keys is a set of keys kept together on a metal ring. 串","examples":["George took out a bunch of keys and went to work on the complicated lock. 喬治掏出一串鑰匙，去設法開這把複雜的鎖。"]}]}]},"burden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"負擔，責任；負重，負荷；船的載重量，噸位；（演講、書或辯論的）主題，主旨（the burden）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"煩擾，使負重擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a problem or a responsibility as a <b>burden</b>, you mean that it causes someone a lot of difficulty, worry, or hard work. 負擔","examples":["The developing countries bear the burden of an enormous external debt. 發展中國家揹負著鉅額外債的負擔。","Her death will be an impossible burden on Paul. 她的去世會成為保羅難以承受的負擔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>burden</b> is a heavy load that is difficult to carry. 重負","examples":["...African women carrying burdens on their heads. …頭頂重物的非洲婦女。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a line of words recurring at the end of each verse of a ballad or similar song; chorus or refrain 疊句","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>burdens</b> you <b>with</b> something that is likely to worry you, for example, a problem or a difficult decision, they tell you about it. 使煩惱","examples":["We decided not to burden him with the news. 我們決定不拿這個訊息去煩他。"]}]}]},"bush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"灌木，灌木叢；荒野，叢林地帶；襯套；絕緣套管；濃密的頭髮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"蓬鬆；伸展，叢生；以灌木裝飾"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"如灌木般長得低矮的；<非正式>粗野的；<美>低劣的，便宜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bush</b> is a large plant which is smaller than a tree and has a lot of branches. 灌木","examples":["Trees and bushes grew down to the water's edge. 樹和灌木叢一直向下長到了水邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The wild, uncultivated parts of some hot countries are referred to as <b>the</b> <b>bush</b>. 灌木叢區","examples":["They walked through the dense Mozambican bush for thirty-six hours. 他們步行穿過茂密的莫三比克灌木叢區，走了36個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a thin metal sleeve or tubular lining serving as a bearing or guide 軸襯; 套管 (Also called (esp US and Canadian) bushing)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fit a bush to (a casing, bearing, etc) 安裝套管","examples":[]}]}]},"canyon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（兩邊為峭壁、谷底通常有溪流的）峽谷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>canyon</b> is a long, narrow valley with very steep sides. 峽谷","examples":["...the Grand Canyon. …大峽谷。"]}]}]},"buzz":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發嗡嗡聲，發蜂鳴聲；匆忙走動；充滿嘈雜聲；充滿想法；繁忙，充滿活力；<非正式>給（某人）打電話；<非正式>（飛機）低空飛過；（用蜂鳴器）呼叫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嗡嗡聲，蜂鳴聲；嘰嘰喳喳聲，嘈雜聲；<非正式>興奮，快樂；熱鬧有趣的氣氛，時尚氛圍；<非正式>電話；<非正式>流言，傳聞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（詞語、想法或活動）時髦的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>buzzes</b> or <b>buzzes</b> somewhere, it makes a long continuous sound, like the noise a bee makes when it is flying. 嗡嗡地響","examples":["The intercom buzzed and he pressed down the appropriate switch. 對講機嗡嗡地響起來，他按下了相應的開關。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>are buzzing</b> <b>around</b>, they are moving around quickly and busily. 匆忙地跑來跑去","examples":["A few tourists were buzzing around. 幾名遊客在匆忙地跑來跑去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If questions or ideas <b>are buzzing</b> <b>around</b> your head, or if your head <b>is buzzing</b> <b>with</b> questions or ideas, you are thinking about a lot of things, often in a confused way. 翻騰","examples":["Many more questions were buzzing around in my head. 更多的問題在我頭腦中翻騰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a place <b>is buzzing</b> <b>with</b> activity or conversation, there is a lot of activity or conversation there, especially because something important or exciting is about to happen. 充滿興奮","examples":["The rehearsal studio is buzzing with lunchtime activity. 排練場被午餐時段活動搞得很熱鬧。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Buzz</b> is also a noun. 嗡嗡聲","examples":["...the irritating buzz of an insect. …一隻昆蟲的煩人的嗡嗡聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>buzz</b> to refer to a long continuous sound, usually caused by lots of people talking at once. 嘈雜聲","examples":["A buzz of excitement filled the courtroom as the defendant was led in. 被告被帶進來時，法庭內充滿激動的嘈雜聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place or event has <b>a buzz</b> around it, it has a lively, interesting, and modern atmosphere. 活躍氣氛","examples":["There is a real buzz around the place. Everyone is really excited. 這地方實在充滿活力，大家真的很興奮。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>buzz</b> to refer to a word, idea, or activity which has recently become extremely popular. 流行的","examples":["...the latest buzz phrase in garden design circles. …園林設計圈子裡的最新流行語。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an aircraft <b>buzzes</b> a place, it flies low over it, usually in a threatening way. 低空掠過","examples":["American fighter planes buzzed the city. 美國戰機低空掠過該城市。"]}]}]},"carpenter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木匠，木工"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以木工活製作；做木工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carpenter</b> is a person whose job is making and repairing wooden things. 木匠","examples":[]}]}]},"caterpillar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毛蟲,蠋（蝴蝶或蛾的幼蟲）；（重型車輛的）履帶；履帶式車輛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>caterpillar</b> is a small, worm-like animal that feeds on plants and eventually develops into a butterfly or moth. 毛蟲","examples":[]}]}]},"centimeter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計量）釐米，公分（公制長度單位，等於一米的百分之一）"}],"sections":[]},"ceramics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"制瓷藝術，陶藝；陶器，陶瓷製品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the art and techniques of producing articles of clay, porcelain, etc 製陶工藝","examples":[]}]}]},"cattle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牛；家牛（包括犛牛、犎牛及水牛）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cattle</b> are cows and bulls. 牛","examples":["...the finest herd of beef cattle for two hundred miles. …方圓200英里內最佳的肉牛群。"]}]}]},"carriage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（舊時的）馬車；（火車）車廂；滑架，託板；炮架，托架；嬰兒車；運費，運輸；儀態，姿態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carriage</b> is an old-fashioned vehicle, usually for a small number of passengers, which is pulled by horses. 馬車","examples":["The president-elect followed in an open carriage drawn by six beautiful grey horses. 新當選的總統緊隨其後，坐著6匹灰色駿馬開道的敞篷馬車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>carriage</b> is one of the separate, long sections of a train that carries passengers. 火車車廂","examples":["The company manufactured elegant railway carriages. 該公司生產雅緻的火車車廂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Carriage</b> is the cost of transporting or delivering goods. 運輸費用","examples":["Again, buyers need to check if carriage is included in the price. 此外，買主需要核實售價中是否包含運費。"]}]}]},"capture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"俘獲，捕獲；奪取，佔領；吸引，引起；記錄，體現；拍攝，錄製；吃掉（國際象棋棋子）；使（資料）儲存於電腦中；俘獲（原子，亞原子粒）；（河流）襲奪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"捕獲，被捕獲；被捕獲的人（或物）；佔領，攻佔；奪取，搶佔；（資料）儲存"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>capture</b> someone or something, you catch them, especially in a war. 俘虜; 捕獲","examples":["The guerrillas shot down one aeroplane and captured the pilot. 那些游擊隊員擊落了一架飛機，並俘虜了飛行員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>captures</b> a particular quality, feeling, or atmosphere, they represent or express it successfully. 充分體現","examples":["Chef Idris Caldora offers an inspired menu that captures the spirit of the Mediterranean. 伊德里斯·卡爾多拉廚師的選單很有創意，充分體現了地中海風情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>captures</b> your attention or imagination, you begin to be interested or excited by it. If someone or something <b>captures</b> your heart, you begin to love them or like them very much. 吸引","examples":["...the great names of the past who usually capture the historian's attention. …那些常常為史學家所關注的偉人們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If an event <b>is captured</b> in a photograph or on film, it is photographed or filmed. 拍攝","examples":["The incident was captured on videotape. 這一事件被拍攝下來。","The images were captured by TV crews filming outside the base. 這些鏡頭被正在基地外拍攝的電視臺工作人員捕捉到了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Capture</b> is also a noun. 佔領","examples":["...the final battles which led to the army's capture of the town. …部隊奪取該鎮的最後幾場戰鬥。"]}]}]},"capital":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資本，資金；資本家，資方；首都，首府，省會；活動（或生產）中心；大寫字母；柱頂，柱頭"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可處死刑的；大寫的；首府的，省會的；<舊>頂好的，極好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Capital</b> is a large sum of money which you use to start a business, or which you invest in order to make more money. 資本; 資金","examples":["Companies are having difficulty in raising capital. 各公司在融資方面遇到麻煩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>capital</b> to refer to buildings or machinery which are necessary to produce goods or to make companies more efficient, but which do not make money directly. 資產","examples":["...capital equipment that could have served to increase production. …可用於提高產量的資產裝置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Capital</b> is the part of an amount of money borrowed or invested which does not include interest. 本金; 本錢","examples":["With a conventional mortgage, the payments consist of both capital and interest. 一般的抵押借款，償還包括本金和利息兩部分。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>capital</b> of a country is the city or town where its government or legislature meets. 首都","examples":["...Kathmandu, the capital of Nepal. …加德滿都，尼泊爾的首都。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a place is <b>the</b> <b>capital</b> <b>of</b> a particular industry or activity, it is the place that is most famous for it, because it happens in that place more than anywhere else. (某一產業或活動的) 有名之地; …之都","examples":["Colmar has long been considered the capital of the wine trade. 科爾馬長久以來一直被譽為葡萄酒貿易之都。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Capitals</b> or <b>capital letters</b> are written or printed letters in the form which is used at the beginning of sentences or names. \"T,\" \"B,\" and \"F\" are capitals. 大寫字母","examples":["The name and address are written in capitals. 姓名和地址都大寫。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"the upper part of a column or pier that supports the entablature 柱頂 (Also called chapiter, cap)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>capital</b> offence is one that is so serious that the person who commits it can be punished by death. 可處死刑的","examples":["Espionage is a capital offence in this country. 間諜活動在這個國家是死罪。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is making capital out of</b> a situation, you disapprove of the way they are gaining an advantage for themselves through other people's efforts or bad luck. 利用","examples":["He rebuked the president for trying to make political capital out of the hostage situation. 他指責總統想利用人質事件撈取政治資本。"]}]}]},"champion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冠軍，第一名；擁護者，鬥士"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捍衛，擁護，支援"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英，非正式>極好的；冠軍的，得一等獎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>champion</b> is someone who has won the first prize in a competition, contest, or fight. 冠軍","examples":["...a former Olympic champion. …一位前奧運冠軍。","Kasparov became world champion. 卡斯帕羅夫成了世界冠軍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are a <b>champion</b> <b>of</b> a person, a cause, or a principle, you support or defend them. 擁護者; 捍衛者","examples":["He received acclaim as a champion of the oppressed. 他作為被壓迫者的捍衛者而受到了讚譽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>champion</b> a person, a cause, or a principle, you support or defend them. 擁護; 捍衛","examples":["He passionately championed the poor. 他曾熱情地捍衛窮人。"]}]}]},"chapter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"章，回，篇；階段，時期；分會，分部；議會法案；一系列，一連串（a chapter of）；全體教士；宗教團體理事會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……分成章節"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chapter</b> is one of the parts that a book is divided into. Each chapter has a number, and sometimes a title. 章","examples":["Chromium supplements were used successfully in the treatment of diabetes (see Chapter 4). 鉻補充劑成功地用在了糖尿病的治療上(參見第4章)。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chapter</b> <b>in</b> someone's life or <b>in</b> history is a period of time during which a major event or series of related events takes place. (事件發生的) 時期","examples":["This had been a particularly difficult chapter in Lebanon's recent history. 這是黎巴嫩近代史上的一個特別困難的時期。"]}]}]},"chain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鏈，鏈條；一連串，一系列；連鎖商店；鐐銬；測鏈；連環式（指一群房主先售後購的置屋方式）；<文>約束，束縛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用鎖鏈拴住；拘禁，束縛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chain</b> consists of metal rings connected together in a line. 鏈子","examples":["His open shirt revealed a fat gold chain. 他敞開的襯衣裡露出一條粗大的金鍊子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chain of</b> things is a group of them existing or arranged in a line. 一連串","examples":["...a chain of islands known as the Windward Islands. …被稱為“向風群島”的列島。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>chain</b> <b>of</b> stores, hotels, or other businesses is a number of them owned by the same person or company. 連鎖","examples":["...a large supermarket chain. …一家大型連鎖超市。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If prisoners are <b>in chains</b>, they have thick rings of metal around their wrists or ankles to prevent them from escaping. 鐐銬","examples":["He'd spent four and a half years in windowless cells, much of the time in chains. 他在無窗的牢房裡呆了4年半，大部分時間是手銬腳鐐。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>chain of</b> events is a series of them happening one after another. 一連串","examples":["...the bizarre chain of events that led to his departure in January 1938. …導致他1938年1月離去的一連串怪異事件。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"(of reasoning) a sequence of arguments each of which takes the conclusion of the preceding as a premise (推理中的)連鎖詭辯","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is chained</b> <b>to</b> something, they are fastened to it with a chain. 用鏈條拴住","examples":["The dogs were chained to a fence. 狗被拴在柵欄上。","We were sitting together in our cell, chained to the wall. 我們一起坐在牢房裡，銬在牆上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chain up</b> means the same as . 用鏈條拴住","examples":["They kept me chained up every night and released me each day. 他們每天晚上把我銬起來，白天再把我解開。"]}]}]},"charm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魅力，魔力；護身符，咒語；小掛件，小飾物；粲，粲數"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸引，迷住；誘使，哄誘；向……施魔法，用魔法控制；有魔力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Charm</b> is the quality of being pleasant or attractive. 魅力","examples":["\"Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs,\" the 1937 Disney classic, has lost none of its original charm. 迪斯尼1937年的經典之作《白雪公主和七個小矮人》從未喪失其最初的魅力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who has <b>charm</b> behaves in a friendly, pleasant way that makes people like them. (人的) 魅力","examples":["He was a man of great charm and distinction. 他是一個魅力十足、地位顯赫的男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>charm</b> is a small ornament that is fixed to a bracelet or necklace. (手鍊或項鍊上的) 掛墜","examples":["Inside was a gold charm bracelet, with one charm on it - a star. 裡面是個金制掛墜手鍊，上面有一個掛墜——一顆星星。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>charm</b> is an act, saying, or object that is believed to have magic powers. 符咒","examples":["They cross their fingers and spit over their shoulders as charms against the evil eye. 他們交叉手指，往肩後吐口水，以此作為對抗兇眼的符咒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a loud noise, as of a number of people chattering or of birds singing (眾人說話或群鳥發出的)噪聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>charm</b> someone, you please them, especially by using your charm. (用魅力) 取悅","examples":["He even charmed Mrs. Prichard, carrying her groceries and flirting with her, though she's 83. 他甚至去取悅普里查德夫人，幫她搬雜貨、與她調情，雖然她已經83歲了。"]}]}]},"cast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投射（光，影）；將（視線，目光）投向；澆鑄，鑄造；分配角色；扔，擲，拋；描述，描寫；投票；使人懷疑；使（魔咒）生效，施法；拋（釣絲），撒（網）；（生長過程中）蛻（皮），脫（角）；（馬）失（蹄鐵）；用（星相）占卜；（鄉村舞蹈中的）轉向；（獵）（狗）四處探尋失蹤的嗅跡；放開（獵狗）以探尋嗅跡；用繩子絆倒（動物，尤指母牛）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"演員陣容；鑄型，模型；（固定斷骨用的）石膏； 特性，外貌；（眼睛）斜視；擲，投，拋；淺淡的色調；（獵狗）探尋嗅跡；（蚯蚓鑽洞時拱到地面的）小土堆；（鷹或貓頭鷹的）顆粒狀嘔吐物；<罕>一群鷹，隼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>cast</b> of a play or film is all the people who act in it. 全體演員","examples":["The show is very amusing and the cast is very good. 表演非常有趣，演員都很優秀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cast</b> is a model that has been made by pouring a liquid such as plaster or hot metal onto something or into something, so that when it hardens it has the same shape as that thing. 模型","examples":["An orthodontist took a cast of the inside of Billy's mouth to make a dental plate. 正牙醫師從比利的口腔內部取了模型來製作齒板。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cast</b> is the same as a . 石膏模型","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>cast</b> an actor <b>in</b> a play or film means to choose them to act a particular role in it. 選…扮演角色","examples":["The world premiere of Harold Pinter's new play casts Ian Holm in the lead role. 哈羅德·品特新戲的首次全球公演選擇伊恩·霍姆扮演主要角色。","He was cast as a college professor. 他被選扮演大學教授這個角色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cast</b> your eyes or <b>cast</b> a look in a particular direction, you look quickly in that direction. 掃視","examples":["He cast a stern glance at the two men. 他嚴厲地瞪了那兩名男子一眼。","I cast my eyes down briefly. 我往下瞅了瞅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>casts</b> a light or shadow somewhere, it causes it to appear there. 投射","examples":["The moon cast a bright light over the garden. 月亮在院子裡撒下清輝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>cast</b> doubt <b>on</b> something means to cause people to be unsure about it. 使人生疑","examples":["Last night a top criminal psychologist cast doubt on the theory. 昨晚，一位頂級的犯罪心理學家讓人對該理論生疑。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When you <b>cast</b> your vote in an election, you vote. 投票","examples":["About ninety-five per cent of those who cast their votes approve the new constitution. 95%的人投票贊成新憲法。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>cast</b> an object means to make it by pouring a liquid such as hot metal into a specially shaped container and leaving it there until it becomes hard. 鑄造","examples":["Our door knocker is cast in solid brass. 我們的門環是純銅鑄造的。"]}]}]},"challenge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"挑戰，難題；挑戰書，比賽邀請；質疑，質詢；喝停盤查"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挑戰，向……下戰書；質疑，拒絕接受；盤問，查問；考驗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>challenge</b> is something new and difficult which requires great effort and determination. 挑戰","examples":["The new government's first challenge is the economy. 新政府面臨的第一項挑戰是經濟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>challenge</b> <b>to</b> something is a questioning of its truth or value. A <b>challenge</b> <b>to</b> someone is a questioning of their authority. 質疑","examples":["The demonstrators have now made a direct challenge to the authority of the government. 示威者現已對該政府的權威性提出了直截了當的質疑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Challenge</b> is also a noun. 挑戰","examples":["A third presidential candidate emerged to mount a serious challenge and throw the campaign wide open. 第3位總統候選人上場鄭重發出挑戰，令這次競選充滿懸念。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>rises to the challenge</b>, they act in response to a difficult situation which is new to them and are successful. 奮起應對挑戰","examples":["The new Germany must rise to the challenge of its enhanced responsibilities. 新德國必須奮起應對更艱鉅的挑戰。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>challenge</b> ideas or people, you question their truth, value, or authority. 質疑","examples":["Democratic leaders have challenged the president to sign the bill. 民主黨領導人對總統簽署這項法案存有質疑。","The move was immediately challenged by two of the republics. 這項提案立即遭到了這兩個共和國的質疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>challenge</b> someone, you invite them to fight or compete with you in some way. 向…發出挑戰","examples":["Marsyas thought he could play the flute better than Apollo and challenged the god to a contest. 瑪息阿覺得他長笛吹得比阿波羅好，便向這位神發出挑戰。","He left a note at the scene of the crime, challenging detectives to catch him. 他在作案現場留了一張紙條，挑釁偵探們去抓他。"]}]}]},"channel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頻道，電影片道；管道，通道，航道；渠道，手段；溝渠，溝槽；河床；海峽；通道；電子溝道；輸液道"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"引導，把……用於；輸送，傳送；通靈；努力趕上，受啟發；形成凹槽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>channel</b> is a television station. 電影片道","examples":["...the only serious current affairs programme on either channel. …任一頻道上惟一嚴肅的時事節目。","...the proliferating number of television channels in America. …美國電影片道的激增數量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>channel</b> is a band of radio waves on which radio messages can be sent and received. 波段","examples":["The radio channels were filled with the excited, jabbering voices of men going to war. 收音機各波段滿是即將參戰的男人們激動喧譁的聲音。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something through a particular <b>channel</b>, or particular <b>channels</b>, that is the system or organization that you use to achieve your aims or to communicate. 渠道; 途徑","examples":["The government will surely use the diplomatic channels available. 政府肯定會採用現有的外交途徑。","The Americans recognize that the U.N. can be the channel for greater diplomatic activity. 美國人承認聯合國可以是更重要的外交活動的渠道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>channel</b> is a passage along which water flows. 水渠","examples":["Keep the drainage channel clear. 保持排水管渠道暢通。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>channel</b> is a route used by boats. 航道","examples":["...the busy shipping channels of the harbour. …港口繁忙的船運航道。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a broad strait connecting two areas of sea 海峽","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a flat timber or metal ledge projecting from the hull of a vessel above the chainplates to increase the angle of the shrouds 護桅索承扣板","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>channel</b> money or resources into something, you arrange for them to be used for that thing, rather than for a wider range of things. 調撥 (錢、資源)","examples":["Jacques Delors wants a system set up to channel funds to the poor countries. 雅克·迪洛斯想要建立一種體制，以便調撥資金幫助窮國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>channel</b> your energies or emotions <b>into</b> something, you concentrate on or do that one thing, rather than a range of things. 集中 (精力、情感)","examples":["Stephen is channelling his energies into a novel called Blue. 斯蒂芬正集中精力寫一本名為《藍色》的小說。"]}]}]},"chat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閒聊，聊天"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閒聊，聊天；鳴禽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>chat</b>, they talk to each other in an informal and friendly way. 聊天","examples":["The women were chatting. 婦女們在聊天。","I was chatting to him the other day. 我那天正和他聊天。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chat</b> is also a noun. 聊天","examples":["I had a chat with John. 我和約翰聊了會兒天。"]}]}]},"cheek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臉頰，面頰；厚顏無恥，放肆；半邊屁股"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……無禮，對……不懂規矩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>cheeks</b> are the sides of your face below your eyes. 面頰","examples":["Tears were running down her cheeks. 眼淚順著她面頰流下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>cheeks</b> are your buttocks. 臀部","examples":["My butt cheeks are sore from sitting on this bench too long. 我屁股痛，因為在長凳上坐得太久了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that someone has <b>cheek</b> when you are annoyed or shocked at something unreasonable that they have done. 厚臉皮","examples":["I'm amazed they had the cheek to ask in the first place. 我很吃驚，他們最初竟有臉問。"]}]}]},"cheese":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乾酪，乳酪；（拍照時讓人微笑的用語）笑一笑；大人物，大亨；截然不同；（表示不同情）抱歉啦，真倒黴；帶皮的乳酪塊；<英>（黏稠度像乳酪的）膏，醬；原裝乳酪樣的扁圓物（如九柱戲等遊戲中使用的木圓盤）；<非正式>過分的溫情"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>激怒，使厭煩；停止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cheese</b> is a solid food made from milk. It is usually white or yellow. 乳酪","examples":["...bread and cheese. …麵包和乳酪","...delicious French cheeses. …美味的法式乳酪。"]}]}]},"cherry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"櫻桃；櫻桃樹；櫻桃木；櫻桃色，鮮紅色；果實與櫻桃相似的植物；<非正式>童貞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"櫻桃色的，鮮紅色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cherries</b> are small, round fruit with red skins. 櫻桃","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cherry</b> or a <b>cherry tree</b> is a tree that cherries grow on. 櫻桃樹","examples":[]}]}]},"cheer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歡呼聲，喝彩聲；加油口號，加油歌；歡快，愉快的情緒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"歡呼，喝彩；鼓勵，鼓舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>cheer</b>, they shout loudly to show their approval or to encourage someone who is doing something such as taking part in a game. 歡呼","examples":["The crowd cheered as she went up the steps to the bandstand. 當她走上演奏臺的臺階時，人群歡呼起來。","Hundreds of thousands of jubilant Americans cheered him on his return. 成千上萬歡騰的美國人為他的歸來而歡呼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are cheered</b> <b>by</b> something, it makes you happier or less worried. 感到振奮","examples":["Stephen noticed that the people around him looked cheered by his presence. 斯蒂芬注意到周圍的人因為他的到場而振奮起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cheer</b> is also a noun. 歡呼","examples":["The colonel was rewarded with a resounding cheer from the men. 上校被這些人們報以一陣響亮的歡呼。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人振奮的","examples":["...very cheering news. …非常令人振奮的訊息。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say \"<b>Cheers</b>\" to each other just before they drink an alcoholic drink. 乾杯","examples":[]}]}]},"chimney":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"煙囪，煙道；（可容人攀登的）岩石裂縫；玻璃燈罩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chimney</b> is a pipe through which smoke goes up into the air, usually through the roof of a building. 煙囪","examples":["Thick, yellow smoke pours constantly out of the chimneys at the steel plant in Katowice. 濃密的黃煙不斷地從卡托維茲鋼鐵廠的煙囪裡噴吐出來。"]}]}]},"chest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胸部，胸膛；箱子，盒子，櫃子；<英>金庫，錢庫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以胸部推（球）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>chest</b> is the top part of the front of your body where your ribs, lungs, and heart are. 胸部","examples":["He crossed his arms over his chest. 他在胸前交叉雙臂。","He was shot in the chest. 他胸部中彈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chest</b> is a large, heavy box used for storing things. 儲物箱","examples":["At the very bottom of the chest were his carving tools. 在儲物箱的最底部有他的雕刻工具。","...a treasure chest. …一個珍寶箱。"]}]}]},"childhood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"童年，幼年時代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>childhood</b> is the period of their life when they are a child. 童年","examples":["She had a happy childhood. 她有過一個快樂的童年。","He was remembering a story heard in childhood. 他一直記著童年時聽過的一個故事。"]}]}]},"china":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓷，瓷料；瓷器，瓷製品；<英，非正式>朋友；中國（China）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瓷制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>China</b> is a hard white substance made from clay. It is used to make things such as cups, bowls, plates, and ornaments. 瓷","examples":["...a small bowl made of china. …一個小瓷碗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Cups, bowls, plates, and ornaments made of china are referred to as <b>china</b>. 瓷器","examples":["Judy collects blue and white china. 朱迪收集青花瓷器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a friend or companion 朋友; 夥伴","examples":[]}]}]},"chew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"咀嚼，嚼碎；（為了品嚐或因緊張而）不停地嚼，咬；（人或動物）咬，啃"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"咀嚼；口香糖；供嚼用的菸草；咀嚼物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>chew</b> food, you use your teeth to break it up in your mouth so that it becomes easier to swallow. 咀嚼","examples":["Be certain to eat slowly and chew your food extremely well. 一定要慢慢吃，特別細地咀嚼食物。","Daniel leaned back on the sofa, still chewing on his apple. 丹尼爾仰靠在沙發上，還在嚼著蘋果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>chew</b> gum or tobacco, you keep biting it and moving it around your mouth to taste the flavour of it. You do not swallow it. 嚼 (口香糖、煙)","examples":["One girl was chewing gum. 一個女孩在嚼口香糖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>chew</b> your lips or your fingernails, you keep biting them because you are nervous. 咬 (嘴唇、手指)","examples":["He chewed his lower lip nervously. 他緊張地咬著下唇。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>chews</b> an object or <b>chews</b> <b>on</b> it, they bite it with their teeth. 咬","examples":["They pause and chew their pencils. 他們停了下來，咬著鉛筆。","She chewed through the tape that bound her. 她咬斷了捆綁她的帶子。"]}]}]},"chill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寒冷，寒意；著涼，受寒；害怕，擔心；冷漠，敵意；冷模，冷模部件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）冷卻，冰鎮；使很冷；驚嚇，使恐懼；<非正式>放鬆；（使）沮喪，（使）掃興"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冷颼颼的；令人緊張的，令人害怕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>chill</b> something or when it <b>chills</b>, you lower its temperature so that it becomes colder but does not freeze. 使冷卻; 冷卻","examples":["Chill the fruit salad until serving time. 上菜前把水果色拉冷卻。","These doughs can be rolled out while you wait for the pastry to chill. 當你等待油酥麵糰冷卻時，可以擀平這些生麵糰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When cold weather or something cold <b>chills</b> a person or a place, it makes that person or that place feel very cold. 使很冷","examples":["The marble floor was beginning to chill me. 大理石的地板開始讓我感到很冷。","Wade placed his chilled hands on the radiator and warmed them. 韋德把他冰冷的雙手放到散熱器上取暖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something sends a <b>chill</b> through you, it gives you a sudden feeling of fear or anxiety. 害怕的感覺","examples":["The violence used against the students sent a chill through Indonesia. 對學生使用暴力使得整個印度尼西亞不寒而慄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chill</b> is a mild illness which can give you a slight fever and headache. 風寒","examples":["He caught a chill while performing at a rain-soaked open-air venue. 他在一個被雨浸溼的露天場地表演時著了風寒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Chill</b> is also a noun. 寒冷","examples":["September is here, bringing with it a chill in the mornings. 9月到了，帶來了清晨的寒意。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chill</b> weather is cold and unpleasant. 寒冷的","examples":["...chill winds, rain and choppy seas. …寒冷的風、雨以及波浪起伏的大海。"]}]}]},"cigarette":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香菸，紙菸；麻醉煙，草藥煙，藥性煙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cigarettes</b> are small tubes of paper containing tobacco which people smoke. 香菸","examples":["He went out to buy a packet of cigarettes. 他出去買了一包香菸。"]}]}]},"circus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"馬戲團，馬戲演員；馬戲表演；亂哄哄的人群，熱鬧的場面；圓形廣場，環形交叉口；（古羅馬）露天圓形競技場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>circus</b> is a group that consists of clowns, acrobats, and animals that travels around to different places and performs shows. 馬戲團","examples":["My real ambition was to work in a circus. 我真正的理想是去馬戲團工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The circus</b> is the show performed by these people. 馬戲","examples":["My dad took me to the circus. 我爸爸帶我去看馬戲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a group of people or an event as a <b>circus</b>, you disapprove of them because they attract a lot of attention but do not achieve anything useful. 鬧劇","examples":["It could well turn into some kind of a media circus. 這很可能會發展成某種媒體鬧劇。"]}]}]},"client":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"客戶，委託人；客戶機，使用者端；（古羅馬）貴族庇護下的平民；<古>受贍養者，食客"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>client</b> of a professional person or organization is a person or company that receives a service from them in return for payment. 客戶","examples":["...a lawyer and his client. …一位律師和他的委託人。"]}]}]},"chip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"炸薯條，炸薯片；晶片；碎塊，碎屑；缺口，豁口；籌碼；撮球，切球；木條"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打破，弄缺；（尤指用工具）削下，鑿下；切成細條；撮球，挑球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chips</b> are long, thin pieces of potato fried in oil or fat and eaten hot, usually with a meal. 炸薯條","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chips</b> or <b>potato chips</b> are very thin slices of fried potato that are eaten as a snack. 炸薯片","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A silicon <b>chip</b> is a very small piece of silicon with electronic circuits on it which is part of a computer or other piece of machinery. 晶片 (計算機或其他機器中帶有電子電路的細小矽片)","examples":["...an electronic card containing a chip. …一張帶有晶片的電子卡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>chip</b> is a small piece of something or a small piece which has been broken off something. 小塊東西; 碎屑","examples":["It contains real chocolate chips. 它裡面含有純正的巧克力顆粒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>chip</b> in something such as a piece of china or furniture is where a small piece has been broken off it. 小缺口","examples":["The cup had a small chip. 這個杯子有個小缺口。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Chips</b> are plastic counters used in gambling to represent money. (作賭注用的) 籌碼","examples":["He put the pile of chips in the centre of the table and drew a card. 他把那堆籌碼放在桌子中間，然後抽了一張牌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chip</b> something or if it <b>chips</b>, a small piece is broken off it. 把…碰掉一小塊; 碎掉一小塊","examples":["The blow chipped the woman's tooth. 這一擊把那個女人的牙齒打掉了一小塊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有缺口的; 有缺損的","examples":["The wagon's paint was badly chipped on the outside. 這輛四輪馬車外殼的油漆嚴重地剝落。"]}]}]},"clinic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"診所，門診部；門診時間；臨床實習；講習班；（醫院的）科，室；減免費用的專業服務機構；健康講座"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clinic</b> is a building where people go to receive medical advice or treatment. 診所","examples":["...a family planning clinic. …計劃生育診所。"]}]}]},"chop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"剁，砍，劈；大幅削減；強行廢止，取消；削（球）；<英，非正式>變化無常（chop and change）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（羊或豬）排；剁，砍，劈；掌劈；（人或動物）嘴周圍的地方；碎浪；動物飼料；<古>商標"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chop</b> something, you cut it into pieces with strong, downward movements of a knife or an axe. (用力) 切; 砍","examples":["Chop the butter into small pieces. 把黃油切成小塊。","Visitors were set to work chopping wood. 參觀者們被安排去砍木頭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chop</b> is a small piece of meat cut from the ribs of a sheep or pig. 排骨","examples":["...grilled lamb chops. …烤羔羊排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a design stamped on goods as a trademark, esp in the Far East (特指用在遠東的)商標","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to change direction suddenly; vacillate (esp in the phrase <b>chop and change</b>) 變化無常","examples":[]}]}]},"choke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"窒息，噎住，卡住；說不出話，哽咽；掐死，扼死；堵塞，塞滿；（管子、渠道等）被阻塞，被塞滿；失敗；阻止，抑制；悶住，撲滅（火等）；窒息，噎住"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窒息，噎住的聲音；阻氣門"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>choke</b> or when something <b>chokes</b> you, you cannot breathe properly or get enough air into your lungs. 使窒息; 窒息","examples":["A small child could choke on the doll's hair. 小孩子可能會因玩具娃娃的頭髮而窒息。","Dense smoke swirled and billowed, its rank fumes choking her. 濃密的煙霧盤旋翻騰，刺鼻的煙味使她窒息。","The girl choked to death after breathing in smoke. 那位女孩吸入煙霧後窒息而亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>choke</b> someone means to squeeze their neck until they are dead. (卡住喉嚨) 使停止呼吸","examples":["The men pushed him into the entrance of a nearby building, where they choked him with his tie. 那些男人把他推進了附近一座大樓的入口處，然後在那裡用他的領帶將他勒死了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place <b>is choked</b> <b>with</b> things or people, it is full of them and they prevent movement in it. 使阻塞","examples":["The village's roads are choked with traffic. 那個村莊的道路被車輛阻塞住了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>choke</b> in a car, truck, or other vehicle is a device that reduces the amount of air going into the engine and makes it easier to start. 阻氣門","examples":["It is like driving your car with the choke out all the time. 就像一直松著阻氣門在開車一樣。"]}]}]},"click":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用滑鼠）點選；發出咔嗒聲；一見如故，受歡迎；突然明白，恍然大悟；配合默契，進展順利；得到關注，引起興趣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"短而尖的聲音，咔噠聲；點選；（南非語等語言的）倒吸氣音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>clicks</b> or if you <b>click</b> it, it makes a short, sharp sound. 使發咔嚓聲; 發出咔嚓聲","examples":["The applause rose to a crescendo and cameras clicked. 掌聲越來越來響，照相機咔嚓咔嚓地響。","He clicked off the radio. 他咔嗒一聲關上了收音機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>click</b> on an area of a computer screen, you point the cursor at that area and press one of the buttons on the mouse in order to make something happen. (用滑鼠) 點選","examples":["I clicked on a link and recent reviews of the production came up. 我點選了一個連結，最近的演出評論就出來了。","Click the link and see what happens. 點選那個連結，看看會發生什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Click</b> is also a noun. 咔嚓聲","examples":["The telephone rang three times before I heard a click and then her recorded voice. 電話響了3次後我聽到了咔嗒一聲響，然後是她的錄音留言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Click</b> is also a noun. 點選","examples":["You can check your e-mail with a click of your mouse. 透過滑鼠的一點你就能查電子郵件。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you suddenly understand something, you can say that it <b>clicks</b>. 恍然大悟","examples":["When I saw the television report, it all clicked. 當我看到電視報道時，一下就恍然大悟了。"]}]}]},"clue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"線索，提示；理解，想法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（某人）提供線索，使（某人）瞭解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clue</b> <b>to</b> a problem or mystery is something that helps you to find the answer to it. (解決問題或疑團時的) 線索","examples":["Geneticists in Canada have discovered a clue to the puzzle of why our cells get old and die. 加拿大的遺傳學家已經發現瞭解開我們細胞衰老死亡之迷的線索。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clue</b> is an object or piece of information that helps someone solve a crime. (破案中的) 線索","examples":["The vital clue to the killer's identity was his nickname, Peanuts. 關於殺手身份的重大線索是他的綽號——花生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>clue</b> in a crossword or game is information which is given to help you to find the answer to a question. (縱橫字謎或遊戲中的) 提示","examples":["Give me a clue. What's it begin with? 給我點提示。是什麼開頭？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>haven't a clue</b> about something, you do not know anything about it or you have no idea what to do about it. 毫無頭緒","examples":["I haven't a clue what I'll give Carl for his birthday next year. 對於明年該送什麼生日禮物給卡爾我毫無頭緒。"]}]}]},"coconut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"椰子（果實）；椰子肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coconut</b> is a very large nut with a hairy shell, which has white flesh and milky juice inside it. 椰子","examples":["...the smell of roasted meats mingled with spices, coconut oil, and ripe tropical fruits. …烤肉夾雜著香料、椰子油和成熟的熱帶水果的味道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Coconut</b> is the white flesh of a coconut. 椰子肉","examples":["Put 2 cups of grated coconut into a blender or food processor. 把兩杯碎椰子肉放進攪拌器或食品加工機內。"]}]}]},"clip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夾子，別針；（電影、電視節目等的）片段；彈夾，彈匣；猛擊，抽打；修剪；<非正式>（行動）速度（尤指快速）；一次；（從羊或羊群）剪下的羊毛量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"修剪；剪下；減少，縮短；（意外地）斜撞，側擊；<美，非正式>詐騙（某人），搶劫（某人）；擷取（影象）；擷取（訊號）的標準振幅，限幅；夾住，固定住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clip</b> is a small device, usually made of metal or plastic, that is specially shaped for holding things together. 夾子; 回形針","examples":["She took the clip out of her hair. 她從頭髮裡取出髮夾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clip</b> from a film or a radio or television programme is a short piece of it that is broadcast separately. (電影、廣播、電視節目的) 片斷","examples":["...an historical film clip of Lenin speaking. …一段列寧講話的歷史電影片斷。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>clip</b> things together or when things <b>clip</b> together, you fasten them together using a clip or clips. 用夾子夾住; 夾緊","examples":["He clipped his safety belt to a fitting on the deck. 他把安全帶扣在甲板的一個固定拴上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>clip</b> something, you cut small pieces from it, especially in order to shape it. 修剪","examples":["I saw an old man out clipping his hedge. 我看見一個老人正在外面修剪他的樹籬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>clip</b> something out of a newspaper or magazine, you cut it out. (從報紙、雜誌上) 剪下","examples":["Kids in his neighbourhood clipped his picture from the newspaper and carried it around. 他的街區裡的孩子們從報紙上剪下他的照片，隨身攜帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>clips</b> something else, it hits it accidentally at an angle before moving off in a different direction. 意外碰撞 (使改變方向)","examples":["The truck clipped the rear of a tanker and then crashed into a second truck. 卡車意外地撞上了燃料車的尾部，然後又撞上了另一輛卡車。"]}]}]},"cocktail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雞尾酒；混合物；雜錦冷盤"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雞尾酒的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>喝雞尾酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cocktail</b> is an alcoholic drink which contains several ingredients. 雞尾酒","examples":["On arrival, guests are offered wine or a champagne cocktail. 到達時，客人們可以享用葡萄酒或一份香檳雞尾酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cocktail</b> is a mixture of a number of different things, especially ones that do not go together well. (尤指不太容易融合的幾種物品的) 混合物","examples":["The court was told she had taken a cocktail of drugs and alcohol. 法庭被告知她服用了藥酒混合劑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a horse with a docked tail 尾巴被剪斷的馬","examples":[]}]}]},"collar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣領，領口；頸圈；（動物頸部顏色異樣的）色圈，頸鎖形條紋；箍，套管；（股票交易的）項圈策略；<英>肉卷；豬頸部的燻肉塊；（植物的）根頸"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>抓住，逮捕；<非正式>攔住（以便與之談話）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>collar</b> of a shirt or coat is the part which fits around the neck and is usually folded over. 衣領","examples":["His tie was pulled loose and his collar hung open. 他的領帶被扯鬆了，衣領敞開著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>collar</b> is a band of leather or plastic which is put around the neck of a dog or cat. (狗或貓的) 項圈","examples":[]}]}]},"colony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"殖民地；殖民團，移民隊；聚集人群，聚居地（區）；群體，群落；（統稱）英屬殖民地；（美國獨立前的）北美十三州"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>colony</b> is a country which is controlled by a more powerful country. 殖民地","examples":["In France's former North African colonies, anti-French feeling is growing. 在法國的各前北非殖民地，反法情緒正在增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a place where a particular group of people lives as a particular kind of <b>colony</b>. (某一類人的) 聚居區","examples":["In 1932, he established a school and artists' colony in Stone City, Iowa. 1932年，他在愛荷華州的小石城建立了一所學校和藝術家聚居區。","...a penal colony. …一個罪犯的流放地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>colony</b> <b>of</b> birds, insects, or animals is a group of them that live together. (生物) 居住在一起的群體","examples":["The islands are famed for their colonies of sea birds. 這些島嶼因有成群的海鳥居住而聞名。"]}]}]},"column":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圓柱，紀念柱；柱狀物；縱隊，縱行（列）；（報紙、雜誌上的）欄；（報紙或雜誌的）專欄（文章）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>column</b> is a tall, often decorated cylinder of stone which is built to honour someone or forms part of a building. 紀念柱; 圓形支柱","examples":["Seven massive columns rise up from a marble floor. 七根巨大的圓柱從大理石地面拔地而起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>column</b> is something that has a tall, narrow shape. 柱狀物","examples":["The explosion sent a column of smoke thousands of feet into the air. 爆炸造成的煙柱升入幾千英尺的高空。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>column</b> is a group of people or animals which moves in a long line. (人或動物行進的) 長隊","examples":["There were reports of columns of military vehicles appearing on the streets. 有報道稱街道上出現了多列軍車車隊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"On a printed page such as a page of a dictionary, newspaper, or printed chart, a <b>column</b> is one of two or more vertical sections which are read downward. (詞典、報紙或圖表等版面上的) 豎欄","examples":["We had stupidly been looking at the wrong column of figures. 我們真笨，一直看錯了數字的欄。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a newspaper or magazine, a <b>column</b> is a section that is always written by the same person or is always about the same topic. (報刊的) 專欄","examples":["His name features frequently in the social columns of the tabloid newspapers. 他的名字常常顯著出現在通俗小報的社會專欄中。"]}]}]},"collection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收藏品，收集物；募捐；一堆（東西），一群（人）；系列時裝；專輯，作品集；領取，收取；收集，採集；收賬，收債；<英>（尤指牛津大學的）學院期初（或期末）考試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>collection</b> <b>of</b> things is a group of similar things that you have deliberately acquired, usually over a period of time. 收藏品","examples":["Robert's collection of prints and paintings has been bought over the years. 羅伯特的印刷收藏品和藏畫是多年來花錢買的。","The Art Gallery of Ontario has the world's largest collection of sculptures by Henry Moore. 安大略美術館關於亨利•摩爾的雕塑收藏品居世界之最。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>collection</b> <b>of</b> stories, poems, or articles is a number of them published in one book. (作品) 集","examples":["Two years ago he published a collection of short stories called \"Facing The Music.\" 兩年前，他出版了一本題為《願賭服輸》的短篇小說集。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>collection</b> <b>of</b> things is a group of things. 組群","examples":["...a collection of modern glass office buildings. …一組玻璃幕牆的現代辦公樓群。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A fashion designer's new <b>collection</b> consists of the new clothes they have designed for the next season. 時裝系列","examples":["Her spring/summer collection for this year deliberately uses both simple and rich fabrics. 她今年的春／夏裝系列故意使用了既簡單又華貴的材質。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you organize a <b>collection</b> for charity, you collect money from people to give to charity. 募捐","examples":["I asked my principal if he could arrange a collection for a refugee charity. 我問我的校長能否為難民組織一次慈善募捐。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>collection</b> is money that is given by people in church during some Christian services. (某些基督儀式中人們給教堂的) 捐款","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Collection</b> is the act of collecting something from a place or from people. 收集; 採集","examples":["Money can be sent to any one of 22,000 agents worldwide for collection. 錢款可以送交全世界22000個代理機構中的任何一個來收集。","...computer systems to speed up collection of information. …用於加快資訊採集速度的電腦系統。"]}]}]},"college":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大學，專科學校；學院，分院；公學；學會，社團；學院的全體師生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>college</b> is an institution where students study after they have left secondary school. 大學; 學院","examples":["Their daughter Joanna is taking business courses at a local college. 他們的女兒喬安娜正在當地一所大學修習商務課程。","Stephanie took up making jewellery after leaving art college this summer. 斯特凡妮今年夏天從藝術學院畢業以後開始從事珠寶的製作工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"At some universities in the United States, <b>colleges</b> are divisions which offer degrees in particular subjects. (美國某些大學中的) 學院","examples":["...a professor at the University of Florida College of Law. …一位佛羅里達大學法學院的教授。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>college</b> is one of the institutions which some British universities are divided into. (英國某些大學中的) 學院","examples":["He was educated at Balliol College, Oxford. 他畢業於牛津大學貝列爾學院。"]}]}]},"comma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"逗號；間歇，音差；銀紋多角蛺蝶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comma</b> is the punctuation mark , which is used to separate parts of a sentence or items in a list. 逗號","examples":[]}]}]},"comfort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"舒服，舒適；安慰，慰藉；令人感到安慰的人（或事物）；舒適的設施（或條件）；生活富足"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"安慰，撫慰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are doing something <b>in</b> <b>comfort</b>, you are physically relaxed and contented, and are not feeling any pain or other unpleasant sensations. 舒服","examples":["This will enable the audience to sit in comfort while watching the shows. 這能使觀眾看演出時舒服地坐著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Comfort</b> is a style of life in which you have enough money to have everything you need. 舒適","examples":["Surely there is some way of ordering our busy lives so that we can live in comfort and find spiritual harmony too. 一定會有辦法把我們繁忙的生活安排得既舒適又能找到內心平靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Comfort</b> is what you feel when worries or unhappiness stop. 安慰","examples":["He welcomed the truce, but pointed out it was of little comfort to families spending Christmas without a loved one. 他歡迎休戰，但指出這對於沒有親人共度聖誕節的家庭並無多少安慰。","They will be able to take some comfort from inflation figures due on Friday. 他們將會從預定在週五釋出的通貨膨脹數字中得到些安慰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to a person, thing, or idea as a <b>comfort</b>, you mean that it helps you to stop worrying or makes you feel less unhappy. 安慰","examples":["It's a comfort talking to you. 與你談談是一種安慰。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Comforts</b> are things which make your life easier and more pleasant, such as electrical devices you have in your home. 使生活舒適的東西","examples":["She enjoys the material comforts married life has brought her. 她享受著婚姻生活帶給她的物質上的舒適。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>comfort</b> someone, you make them feel less worried, unhappy, or upset, for example by saying kind things to them. 安慰","examples":["Ned put his arm around her, trying to comfort her. 內德摟著她，試圖安慰她。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is, for example, <b>too</b> close <b>for comfort</b>, you mean you are worried because it is closer than you would like it to be. 因 (比如太近) 而使人不安的","examples":["The bombs fell in the sea, many too close for comfort. 那些炸彈落進了海里，很多落得太近而使人不安。"]}]}]},"commercial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"商業的，商務的；商業化的，以獲利為目的的；由廣告商支付的；（化學制品）大量供應且純度不高的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"電視廣告，電臺廣告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Commercial</b> means involving or relating to the buying and selling of goods. 商業的","examples":["Baltimore in its heyday was a major centre of industrial and commercial activity. 巴爾的摩在其鼎盛時期曾是工商業活動的主要中心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Commercial</b> organizations and activities are concerned with making money or profits, rather than, for example, with scientific research or providing a public service. 商業化的","examples":["The company has indeed become more commercial over the past decade. 這個公司在過去的十年裡確實已變得越來越商業化了。","Conservationists in Chile are concerned over the effect of commercial exploitation of forests. 智利的自然保護者對森林商業化開發的後果感到擔憂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>commercial</b> product is made to be sold to the public. 商業性的","examples":["They are the leading manufacturer in both defence and commercial products. 他們在防禦性和商業性的產品方面都是領先的製造商。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>commercial</b> vehicle is a vehicle used for carrying goods, or passengers who pay. 商用的","examples":["The route is used every day by many hundreds of commercial vehicles. 這條路線每天都有成百輛商用車透過。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Commercial</b> television and radio are paid for by the broadcasting of advertisements, rather than by the government. 商業化的 (電視或廣播)","examples":["There were no commercial radio stations until 1920. 直到1920年才有了商業電臺。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Commercial</b> is used to describe something such as a film or a type of music that it is intended to be popular with the public, and is not very original or of high quality. 商業化的 (電影或音樂)","examples":["There's a feeling among a lot of people that music has become too commercial. 許多人都感到音樂已變得太商業化了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"商業化地","examples":["The plane will be commercially viable if 400 can be sold. 這飛機若能售出400架從商業上看就可行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"商業性地","examples":["It was the first commercially available machine to employ artificial intelligence. 這是第一臺具有商業價值的人工智慧機器。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>commercial</b> is an advertisement that is broadcast on television or radio. 電視或電臺廣告","examples":["Turn the channel – there are too many commercials. 轉換一下頻道–太多廣告了。"]}]}]},"complaint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抱怨，投訴；不滿的緣由，抱怨的問題；疾病，不適"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>complaint</b> is a statement in which you express your dissatisfaction with a situation. 怨言; 投訴","examples":["There's been a record number of complaints about the standard of service. 已有對服務水準的創紀錄數量的投訴。","People have been reluctant to make formal complaints to the police. 人們一直不願正式向警方投訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>complaint</b> is a reason for complaining. 抱怨的緣由","examples":["My main complaint is that we can't go out on the racecourse anymore. 我抱怨的主要緣由是我們無法再去外面的賽道了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to an illness as a <b>complaint</b>, especially if it is not very serious. (尤指不嚴重的) 疾病","examples":["Eczema is a common skin complaint which often runs in families. 溼疹是一種常見的皮膚病，常會遺傳。"]}]}]},"comparison":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比較，對照；相提並論，相比；比喻，比擬；（副詞或形容詞的）比較（變化）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you make a <b>comparison</b>, you consider two or more things and discover the differences between them. 比較","examples":["...a comparison of the Mexican and Guatemalan economies. …墨西哥與瓜地馬拉經濟的比較。","Its recommendations are based on detailed comparisons between the public and private sectors. 其建議是以公有和私有部門之間的詳細比較為根據的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you make a <b>comparison</b>, you say that one thing is like another in some way. 相似對比","examples":["It is demonstrably an unfair comparison. 這顯然是一種不公平的相似對比。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say, for example, that something is large or small <b>in comparison</b> <b>with</b>, <b>in comparison</b> <b>to</b>, or <b>by comparison</b> <b>with</b> something else, you mean that it is larger or smaller than the other thing. 相比之下","examples":["The amount of carbon dioxide released by human activities such as burning coal and oil is small in comparison. 相比之下人類燃燒煤、石油等活動所釋放的二氧化碳的量是少的。"]}]}]},"committee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"委員會；<英>受託人，監護人；<美>精神病者監護人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>committee</b> is a group of people who meet to make decisions or plans for a larger group or organization that they represent. 委員會","examples":["...the school yearbook committee. …學校年鑑編委會。"]}]}]},"concert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"音樂會，演奏會；一致，和諧；（尤指犯罪時的）聯合行動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"共同議定，協調"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>concert</b> is a performance of music. 音樂會","examples":["...a short concert of piano music. …一場簡短的鋼琴音樂會。","I've been to plenty of live rock concerts. 我到過很多現場搖滾音樂會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a musician or group of musicians appears <b>in concert</b>, they are giving a live performance. 現場演出","examples":["I want people to remember Elvis in concert. 我希望人們記住現場表演的埃爾維斯。"]}]}]},"command":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"命令，下令；統率，指揮；博得，贏得；控制，掌管；居高臨下，俯瞰；值（高價）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"命令，指示；（計算機的）指令；控制，管轄；指揮權，控制權；兵團，軍區；指揮部，司令部；掌握，精通"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>commands</b> you to do something, they tell you that you must do it. 命令","examples":["He commanded his troops to attack. 他命令他的部隊進攻。","\"Get in your car and follow me,\" she commanded. “上車然後跟我來，”她命令道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>command</b> something such as respect or obedience, you obtain it because you are popular, famous, or important. 博得","examples":["...an excellent physician who commanded the respect of all her colleagues. …一位博得所有同事尊敬的傑出醫生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an army or country <b>commands</b> a place, they have total control over it. 完全控制","examples":["Yemen commands the strait at the southern end of the Red Sea. 葉門完全控制著紅海南端的海峽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An officer who <b>commands</b> part of an army, navy, or air force is responsible for controlling and organizing it. 指揮","examples":["...the French general who commands the U.N. troops in the region. …指揮著這一地區聯合國部隊的法國將軍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Command</b> is also a noun. 命令","examples":["The tanker failed to respond to a command to stop. 油輪未能對停止前進的指令做出反應。","I closed my eyes at his command. 我聽從他的命令閉上了眼睛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Command</b> is also a noun. 完全控制權","examples":["...the struggle for command of the air. …對制空權的爭奪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Command</b> is also a noun. 指揮","examples":["...a small garrison under the command of Major James Craig. …一小支在詹姆斯·克雷格少校指揮下的衛戍部隊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In the armed forces, a <b>command</b> is a group of officers who are responsible for organizing and controlling part of an army, navy, or air force. 指揮部","examples":["He had authorization from the military command to retaliate. 他得到了軍事指揮部進行還擊的授權。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In computing, a <b>command</b> is an instruction that you give to a computer. 指令","examples":["I entered the command into my navigational computer. 我把指令輸入了我的導航計算機。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone has <b>command</b> of a situation, they have control of it because they have, or seem to have, power or authority. 控制 (局面等)","examples":["Mr. Baker would take command of the campaign. 貝克先生將負責這次運動。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Your <b>command of</b> something, such as a foreign language, is your knowledge of it and your ability to use this knowledge. 掌握","examples":["His command of English was excellent. 他的英語相當出色。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a particular skill or particular resources <b>at</b> your <b>command</b>, you have them and can use them fully. 掌控","examples":["The country should have the right to defend itself with all legal means at its command. 這個國家應該有權動用它所掌控的所有法律手段來捍衛自己。"]}]}]},"complex":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"複雜的，難懂的；組合的，合成的；（句子）複合的；複數的，復的；配合的，絡合的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"綜合大樓，建築群；複合體，綜合體；情結；強烈（或過度）的關心（或憂慮）；配合物，絡合物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>complex</b> has many different parts, and is therefore often difficult to understand. 複雜的","examples":["...in-depth coverage of today's complex issues. …對當今複雜問題的深入報道。","...a complex system of voting. …一套複雜的選舉體制。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>complex</b> is a group of buildings designed for a particular purpose, or one large building divided into several smaller areas. 建築群","examples":["...a low-cost apartment complex. …一個低價公寓樓群。"]}]}]},"conclusion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結論，推論；結局，結尾；締結，商定；（根據所給前提得出的）命題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you come to a <b>conclusion</b>, you decide that something is true after you have thought about it carefully and have considered all the relevant facts. 結論","examples":["Over the years I've come to the conclusion that she's a very great musician. 這些年我得出的結論是，她是位非常偉大的音樂家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>conclusion</b> of something is its ending. 結束; 結局","examples":["At the conclusion of the programme, I asked the children if they had any questions they wanted to ask me. 節目結束時我問孩子們是否有要問我的問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>conclusion</b> of a treaty or a business deal is the act of arranging it or agreeing on it. (條約、交易等的) 達成","examples":["...the expected conclusion of a free-trade agreement between Mexico and the United States. …墨西哥和美國之間自由貿易協議的如期達成。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>in conclusion</b>\" to indicate that what you are about to say is the last thing that you want to say. 最後 (用以表明講話即將結束)","examples":["In conclusion, walking is a cheap, safe, enjoyable, and readily available form of exercise. 綜上所述，散步是一種廉價、安全、有趣而又隨時可以開展的運動形式。"]}]}]},"cone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圓錐體；圓錐形物；錐形路標；（松樹或冷杉的）球果；（盛冰淇淋的）錐形蛋卷筒，蛋筒冰激凌；視錐細胞；圓錐形山脈（或山峰）（尤指）火山錐；錐體，錐面；（在既定溫度下融化的，用以測量窯溫的）測溫錐，示溫錐；芋螺（=cone shell）；（尤指啤酒花藤的）球花"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>用錐形交通路標分隔（或標明）道路（cone sth. off）；使成錐形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cone</b> is a shape with a circular base ending in a point at the top. 圓錐體","examples":["...orange traffic cones. …橙色的交通錐形警示標。","...the streetlight's yellow cone of light. …街燈的黃色錐形光柱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cone</b> is the fruit of a tree such as a pine or fir. (松樹、冷杉等的) 球果","examples":["...a bowl of fir cones. …一碗冷杉球果。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cone</b> is a thin, cone-shaped biscuit that is used for holding ice cream. You can also refer to ice cream that you eat in this way as a <b>cone</b>. 錐形蛋卷筒; 蛋卷冰淇淋","examples":["She stopped by the ice-cream shop and had a chocolate cone. 她在冰淇淋店停下買了個巧克力蛋卷冰淇淋。"]}]}]},"continent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洲，大陸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有排便節制力的；<舊>節制性慾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>continent</b> is a very large area of land, such as Africa or Asia, that consists of several countries. 洲","examples":["She loved the African continent. 她熱愛非洲大陸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>the Continent</b> to refer to the continent of Europe except for Britain. (除英國外的) 歐洲大陸","examples":["Its shops are among the most stylish on the Continent. 其商店位列歐洲大陸最時尚的商店之中。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"able to control urination and defecation 能控制大小便的","examples":[]}]}]},"concern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擔心，憂慮；使人擔憂的事物；關心，關愛；重要的事物，關心的事；（某人）負責的事，涉及的事；公司，企業；<非正式>複雜的物體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"有關，關於；涉及，影響；使憂慮，使擔心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Concern</b> is worry about a situation. 擔憂","examples":["The group has expressed concern about reports of political violence in Africa. 該集團已對有關非洲政治暴力的報道表示擔憂。","The move follows growing public concern over the spread of the disease. 該行動是針對公眾日益增長的對該疾病傳播的擔憂而採取的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>concern</b> is a fact or situation that worries you. 令人擔憂的事","examples":["His concern was that people would know that he was responsible. 他擔憂的是人們會知道他應該負責任。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a company or business as a <b>concern</b>, usually when you are describing what type of company or business it is. 公司; 生意","examples":["If not a large concern, the Potomac Nursery was at least a successful one. 雖不是一個大生意，波托馬克幼兒園至少是一個成功的公司。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Concern</b> <b>for</b> someone is a feeling that you want them to be happy, safe, and well. If you do something out of <b>concern</b> <b>for</b> someone, you do it because you want them to be happy, safe, and well. 關心","examples":["Without her care and concern, he had no chance at all. 沒有她的照顧和關心，他根本就沒有機會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a situation or problem is your <b>concern</b>, it is something that you have a duty or responsibility to be involved with. 負責任的事","examples":["The technical aspects were the concern of the Army. 技術方面是軍方負責的事。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>concerns</b> you, it worries you. 使擔憂","examples":["The growing number of people seeking refuge in Thailand is beginning to concern Western aid agencies. 日益增多的到泰國尋求避難的人數開始讓西方援助機構感到擔憂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>concern</b> <b>yourself with</b> something, you give it attention because you think that it is important. 關心","examples":["I didn't concern myself with politics. 我不關心政治。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a book or a piece of information <b>concerns</b> a particular subject, it is about that subject. 有關於","examples":["The bulk of the book concerns Sandy's two middle-aged children. 這本書的主要部分講的是桑迪的兩個中年孩子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a situation, event, or activity <b>concerns</b> you, it affects or involves you. (情況、事件、活動等) 與…有關","examples":["It was just a little unfinished business from my past, and it doesn't concern you at all. 這只是我過去沒有了結的一件小事，完全跟你沒關。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"感到擔憂的","examples":["Academics and employers are concerned that students are not sufficiently prepared for college courses. 學術界和用人單位都擔心學生們對大學課程沒有做好足夠準備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"關心的","examples":["The agency is more concerned with making arty ads than understanding its clients' businesses. 這家代理商更關心製作附庸風雅的廣告而不是理解其客戶的生意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有關於…的","examples":["Randolph's work was exclusively concerned with the effects of pollution on health. 倫道夫的作品全部講的是汙染對健康的影響。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"有關的","examples":["It's a very stressful situation for everyone concerned. 這對所有相關人員來說都是一個非常有壓力的情況。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company is a <b>going concern</b>, it is actually doing business, rather than having stopped trading or not yet having started trading. 在運營的公司","examples":["The receivers will always prefer to sell a business as a going concern. 接管人總是更希望出售仍然在運營的公司。"]}]}]},"constant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"持續不斷的，經常發生的；恆定的，不變的；忠誠的，忠實的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常數，恆量；不變的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>constant</b> to describe something that happens all the time or is always there. 常發生的; 常存在的","examples":["She suggests that women are under constant pressure to be abnormally thin. 她提出女性受持續的壓力之下要異常苗條。","Inflation is a constant threat. 通貨膨脹是一種持續的威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or level is <b>constant</b>, it stays the same over a particular period of time. (在某時段內) 保持不變的","examples":["The body feels hot and the temperature remains more or less constant at the new elevated level. 身體感到熱，可體溫保持在升高後的新高度上差不多穩定不變。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"持續不斷地","examples":["The direction of the wind is constantly changing. 風的方向在不斷地變。"]}]}]},"coward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膽小鬼，懦夫"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<文>膽小的，怯懦的；（動物形象）夾著尾巴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>coward</b>, you disapprove of them because they are easily frightened and avoid dangerous or difficult situations. 膽小鬼","examples":["She accused her husband of being a coward. 她指責自己的丈夫是個膽小鬼。"]}]}]},"consideration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"考慮，斟酌；考慮因素；體貼，關心；報酬，酬金；（合同協議中的）對價，約因；<舊>重要（性）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Consideration</b> is careful thought about something. 仔細考慮","examples":["There should be careful consideration about the use of such toxic chemicals. 應有對這些有毒化學品的使用的慎重考慮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>under consideration</b>, it is being discussed. 在討論中","examples":["Several proposals are under consideration by the state assembly. 幾項提案正由州議會審議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you show <b>consideration</b>, you pay attention to the needs, wishes, or feelings of other people. 體貼","examples":["Show consideration for your neighbours. 要表示出對鄰居們的體貼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>consideration</b> is something that should be thought about, especially when you are planning or deciding something. 考慮因素","examples":["Price has become a more important consideration for shoppers in choosing which shop to visit than it was before the recession. 比起經濟蕭條前，價格已成為購物者們選擇光顧哪家商店的一個更重要的考慮因素。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something <b>into consideration</b>, you think about it because it is relevant to what you are doing. 考慮到某事物","examples":["Safe driving is good driving because it takes into consideration the lives of other people. 安全駕駛是良好駕駛，因為它顧及到了他人的生命。"]}]}]},"couch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長沙發，長榻；診察臺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"表達，措辭；<文>躺下，躺臥；<古>平端（矛或槍）（準備攻擊）；用下壓及後壓晶狀體的方式治療（白內障）；貼線縫繡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>couch</b> is a long, comfortable seat for two or three people. 長沙發","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>couch</b> is a narrow bed which patients lie on while they are being treated by a psychoanalyst. (精神科醫生的) 診察臺","examples":["Between films he often winds up spending every single morning on his psychiatrist's couch. 在拍電影的間隔期間，他經常是在心理醫生的診察臺上度過每一個早晨。"]}]}]},"connection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"關係，聯絡；連線，接通；連線物，接頭；聯運，轉車，轉機；交通線；人際關係，人脈；親戚，旁系親屬；<美，非正式>毒品販子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>connection</b> is a relationship between two things, people, or groups. 關係","examples":["There was no evidence of a connection between BSE and the brain diseases recently confirmed in cats. 沒有有關瘋牛病和最近證實的貓類腦部疾病之間的關係的證據。","I felt a strong connection between us. 我感覺到了我們之間的強烈關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>connection</b> is a joint where two wires or pipes are joined together. 連線處","examples":["Check all radiators for small leaks, especially round pipework connections. 檢查所有的暖氣裝置，尤其是圓形管道的接頭處，看是否有小裂縫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place has good road, rail, or air <b>connections</b>, many places can be directly reached from there by car, train, or plane. (道路、軌道、航道) 連線","examples":["Mexico City has excellent air and rail connections to the rest of the country. 墨西哥城有很好的空運和鐵路連線全國各地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you get a <b>connection</b> at a station or airport, you catch a train, bus, or plane, after getting off another train, bus, or plane, in order to continue your trip. (火車、輪船、飛機等的) 聯運","examples":["My flight was late and I missed the connection. 我乘坐的航班晚點了，因此我錯過了聯運航班。"]}]}]},"cradle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"搖籃；吊架，吊籃；發源地；（電話的）聽筒架； 搖籃"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕輕抱著"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cradle</b> is a baby's bed with high sides. Cradles often have curved bases so that they rock from side to side. 搖籃","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cradle</b> someone or something <b>in</b> your arms or hands, you hold them carefully and gently. (小心輕柔地) 抱著","examples":["I cradled her in my arms. 我把她小心輕柔地抱在懷中。"]}]}]},"condition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狀況，狀態；條件，環境；疾病；條款；<舊>社會地位"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"訓練，使習慣於；控制，制約；護理，保養；影響；加條件於；使（人，動物）健康；（發酵後，在酵母仍存在時）使（啤酒，黑啤酒）釀熟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>condition</b> of a person or thing, you are talking about the state that they are in, especially how good or bad their physical state is. (尤指健康) 狀況","examples":["He remains in a critical condition in a California hospital. 他在加利福尼亞的一家醫院裡，仍處於危急的狀況。","I received several compliments on the condition of my skin. 我得到好幾次有關我皮膚的狀況的誇讚。","The two-bedroom chalet is in good condition. 這個有兩間臥室的小屋狀況良好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>conditions</b> under which something is done or happens are all the factors or circumstances which directly affect it. (某事完成或發生的) 條件","examples":["It's easy to make a wrong turn here even under ideal weather conditions. 即使在非常理想的天氣條件下，也很容易在這裡拐錯彎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>conditions</b> in which people live or work are the factors which affect their comfort, safety, or health. (生活或工作的) 環境","examples":["People are living in appalling conditions. 人們生活在極其惡劣的環境中。","I could not work in these conditions any longer. 我再也不能在這樣的環境中工作了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>condition</b> is something which must happen or be done in order for something else to be possible, especially when this is written into a contract or law. (尤指寫進合同或法律中的某事發生的) 條件","examples":["Argentina failed to hit the economic targets set as a condition for loan payments. 阿根廷沒能達到作為貸款償還條件而設的的經濟目標。","...terms and conditions of employment. …僱用條款和條件。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has a particular <b>condition</b>, they have an illness or other medical problem. 疾病; 問題","examples":["Doctors suspect he may have a heart condition. 醫生懷疑他可能有心臟病。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"長期影響","examples":["Because of social conditioning, men don't expect to be managed by women. 由於社會的長期影響，男人不希望被女人管。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is conditioned</b> by their experiences or environment, they are influenced by them over a period of time so that they do certain things or think in a particular way. 習慣於 (以某種方式做事或思考)","examples":["We are all conditioned by early impressions and experiences. 我們都受早年印象和經歷的長期影響。","I just feel women are conditioned into doing housework. 我只是覺得女人習慣於做家務。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you agree to do something <b>on condition that</b> something else happens, you mean that you will only do it if this other thing also happens. 在 (某事發生的) 條件下","examples":["He agreed to speak to reporters on condition that he was not identified. 他同意在不暴露身份的條件下和記者談話。"]}]}]},"creator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"創作者，發明者；造物主，上帝（the Creator）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>creator</b> of something is the person who made it or invented it. 創作者","examples":["...Ian Fleming, the creator of James Bond. …伊恩·弗萊明，詹姆斯·邦德的創作者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"God is sometimes referred to as <b>the</b> <b>Creator</b>. 造物主","examples":["This was the first object placed in the heavens by the Creator. 這是造物主置於天上的第一個物體。"]}]}]},"contract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"合同，契約；<非正式>暗殺協議；（橋牌）定約墩數；婚約，訂婚"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）收縮，縮小；籤合同，訂立契約；患上，感染；訂立婚約（或盟約）；欠負（債）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>contract</b> is a legal agreement, usually between two companies or between an employer and employee, which involves doing work for a stated sum of money. 合同","examples":["The company won a hefty contract for work on Chicago's tallest building. 公司贏得了芝加哥最高建築的重要施工合同。","Have you read the contract? 你看過這份合同了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"收縮","examples":["...the contraction and expansion of blood vessels. …血管的收縮與擴張。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contract</b> <b>with</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you legally agree to do it for them or for them to do it for you. (與某人) 簽訂合同","examples":["You can contract with us to deliver your cargo. 你們可以和我們簽訂合同，由我們負責運輸你們的貨物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something <b>contracts</b> or when something <b>contracts</b> it, it becomes smaller or shorter. 縮小; 縮短; 使縮小; 使縮短","examples":["Blood is only expelled from the heart when it contracts. 心臟收縮時，血液才從心臟射出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>contract</b> a serious illness, you become ill with it. 染 (重病)","examples":["He contracted AIDS from a blood transfusion. 他因一次輸血感染了艾滋病。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as an economy or market <b>contracts</b>, it becomes smaller. (經濟、市場等) 萎縮","examples":["The manufacturing economy contracted in October for the sixth consecutive month. 製造業經濟到10月份已連續萎縮6個月了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>under contract</b> <b>to</b> someone, you have signed a contract agreeing to work for them, and for no one else, during a fixed period of time. 已經與…簽訂合同","examples":["The director wanted Olivia de Havilland, then under contract to Warner Brothers. 導演想要奧莉維亞·德·哈維蘭，但是那時她已經簽約華納兄弟公司。"]}]}]},"creature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物，動物；（具有某種特徵的）人；怪物；受支配的人，產物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to any living thing that is not a plant as a <b>creature</b>, especially when it is of an unknown or unfamiliar kind. People also refer to imaginary animals and beings as <b>creatures</b>. (尤指不明的或想像中的) 生物; 動物","examples":["Alaskan Eskimos believe that every living creature possesses a spirit. 阿拉斯加的愛斯基摩人認為每個活著的動物都有靈魂。"]}]}]},"cricket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蟋蟀；板球（運動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cricket</b> is an outdoor game played between two teams. Players try to score points, called runs, by hitting a ball with a wooden bat. 板球","examples":["During the summer term we would play cricket at the village ground. 夏季學期裡我們常在村裡的空地上玩板球。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cricket</b> is a small jumping insect that produces short, loud sounds by rubbing its wings together. 蟋蟀","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a small low stool 小矮凳","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to play cricket 打板球","examples":[]}]}]},"crawl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"爬行，匍匐前進；緩慢移動，緩慢行進；擠滿，爬滿；諂媚奉承，卑躬屈膝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"緩慢移動，徐行；爬泳，自由泳；（海邊淺灘的魚、龜等）圍養池"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>crawl</b>, you move forward on your hands and knees. 爬","examples":["Don't worry if your baby seems a little reluctant to crawl or walk. 如果你的小寶寶看起來有點不願爬或走，不用擔心。","I began to crawl on my hands and knees toward the door. 我開始手腳並用向門爬去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an insect <b>crawls</b> somewhere, it moves there quite slowly. 爬行","examples":["I watched the moth crawl up the outside of the lampshade. 我看著蛾子爬上燈罩表面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>crawls</b> somewhere, they move or progress slowly or with great difficulty. 緩慢行進","examples":["I crawled out of bed at nine-thirty. 9：30我才慢慢地爬下床。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>is crawling with</b> people or animals, you are emphasizing that it is full of them. 到處都是","examples":["This place is crawling with police. 這個地方警察到處都是。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crawl</b> is also a noun. 緩慢行進","examples":["The traffic on the off-ramp slowed to a crawl. 駛出匝道的交通慢得在爬進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The crawl</b> is a kind of swimming stroke which you do lying on your front, swinging one arm over your head, and then the other arm. 自由泳","examples":["I expected him to do 50 lengths of the crawl. 我希望他以自由泳遊50趟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an enclosure in shallow, coastal water for fish, lobsters, etc 養魚(及龍蝦等的)池","examples":[]}]}]},"crutch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"柺杖；支柱；依靠；胯部"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用柺杖支撐；支援"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crutch</b> is a stick whose top fits around or under the user's arm, which someone with an injured foot or leg uses to support their weight when walking. 柺杖","examples":["I can walk without the aid of crutches. 我能夠不借助柺杖走路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone or something as a <b>crutch</b>, you mean that they give you help or support. (提供幫助、支援的) 人或物","examples":["He gave up the crutch of alcohol. 他不再依賴酒精。"]}]}]},"criminal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"罪犯"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"犯法的，犯罪的；刑事的；應受責備的，可恥的；罪犯的，犯人的；<非正式>（行為或情形）令人遺憾的，令人震驚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>criminal</b> is a person who has committed a crime. 罪犯","examples":["A group of gunmen attacked a prison and set free nine criminals. 一夥持槍歹徒襲擊了一所監獄並放走了9名罪犯。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Criminal</b> means connected with crime. 犯罪的; 刑事的","examples":["Her husband faces various criminal charges. 她丈夫面臨多項刑事的指控。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an action as <b>criminal</b>, you think it is very wrong or a serious mistake. 嚴重錯誤的","examples":["He said a full-scale dispute involving strikes would be criminal. 他說一個捲入罷工的全面抗爭將是極其錯誤的。"]}]}]},"crew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"全體船員，全體機組人員；一組工作人員；一夥人，一幫人；全體划船隊員；賽艇運動；<美，非正式>（尤指演奏車庫音樂的）一群樂師"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當船員，當空乘人員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>crew</b> of a ship, an aircraft, or a spacecraft is the people who work on and operate it. 全體船員; 全體機務人員","examples":["The mission for the crew of the space shuttle is essentially over. 太空梭全體機務人員的使命基本完成。","Despite their size, these vessels carry small crews, usually of around twenty men. 雖然個頭大，這些輪船載船員卻很少，一般只有二十人左右。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crew</b> is a group of people with special technical skills who work together on a task or project. 一組工作人員","examples":["...a two-man film crew making a documentary. …一個製作紀錄片的兩人攝製組。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>crew</b> a boat, you work on it as part of the crew. 當船員; 充當…的船員","examples":["This neighbour crewed on a ferryboat. 這位鄰居在一艘渡船上當船員。","There were to be five teams of three crewing the boat. 將有5個3人組做這艘船的船員。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"crow的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"cupboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"櫥櫃，衣櫃；壁櫥；小儲藏室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cupboard</b> is a piece of furniture that has one or two doors, usually contains shelves, and is used to store things. 櫥櫃","examples":["The kitchen cupboard was stocked with cans of soup and food. 廚房食櫥裡儲存著一罐罐的湯和食物。"]}]}]},"dairy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奶制的，乳品的；乳品業的，生產乳品的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"乳品公司，乳品店；乳製品；牛奶場，乳品場；<紐西蘭>地方小店；乳牛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dairy</b> is a company that sells milk and food made from milk, such as butter, cream, and cheese. 乳品公司","examples":["In my childhood, local dairies bought milk from local farmers. 在我小時候，本地的乳品公司向當地農場主收購牛奶。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dairy</b> is used to refer to foods such as butter and cheese that are made from milk. 奶制的","examples":["He avoids all meat and dairy products. 他不吃任何肉類和奶製品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dairy</b> is used to refer to the use of cattle to produce milk rather than meat. 產乳的","examples":["...a small vegetable and dairy farm. …一個種菜、養奶牛的小農場。"]}]}]},"crash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"撞車，墜毀；猛撞，發出巨響；破產，倒閉，暴跌；（計算機）癱瘓，宕機；（在體育比賽中）慘敗；過夜，入睡；心臟停止跳動；不請自來，偷偷混入（派對）；闖紅燈"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"撞車事故，失事；巨響，碰撞聲；（計算機）癱瘓，宕機；破產，暴跌；（做毛巾、窗簾等用的）粗布"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"應急的，速成的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"嘩啦一聲地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crash</b> is an accident in which a moving vehicle hits something and is damaged or destroyed. 撞車; 墜機","examples":["His elder son was killed in a car crash a few years ago. 他大兒子幾年前死於一次車禍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crash</b> is a sudden, loud noise. 突然的巨響","examples":["Two people recalled hearing a loud crash about 1:30 a.m. 兩人回憶說大約凌晨1：30時聽到一聲巨響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Crash</b> is also a noun. 崩潰","examples":["He predicted correctly that there was going to be a stock market crash. 他正確地預測到將出現股市崩潰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a coarse cotton or linen cloth used for towelling, curtains, etc 粗棉布; 粗亞麻布","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a moving vehicle <b>crashes</b> or if the driver <b>crashes</b> it, it hits something and is damaged or destroyed. 使…撞毀; 撞毀","examples":["The plane crashed mysteriously near the island of Ustica. 飛機在烏斯蒂卡島附近神秘地墜毀了。","Her car crashed into the rear of a van. 她的汽車撞毀了一輛麵包車的尾部。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>crashes</b> somewhere, it moves and hits something else violently, making a loud noise. (發出巨響的) 猛撞","examples":["The door swung inwards to crash against a chest of drawers behind it. 門擺向裡面，砰的一聲猛力撞上了門後的五斗櫥。","My words were lost as the walls above us crashed down, filling the cellar with brick dust. 隨著上面的牆體轟隆一聲倒塌下來，地窖裡充滿磚灰，我嚇得說不出話來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a business or financial system <b>crashes</b>, it fails suddenly, often with serious effects. (企業、金融機構) 突然垮臺","examples":["When the market crashed, they assumed the deal would be cancelled. 市場崩盤時，他們以為那筆交易會取消。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a computer or a computer program <b>crashes</b>, it fails suddenly. (計算機或系統) 宕機","examples":["The computer crashed for the second time in 10 days. 計算機10天內第2次宕機了。"]}]}]},"dam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"堤，壩；母獸，母畜；<南非>水庫；（牙科手術中的）橡皮障"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在河上）築壩；阻止，抑制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dam</b> is a wall that is built across a river in order to stop the water from flowing and to make a lake. 水壩","examples":["Before the dam was built, Campbell River used to flood in the spring. 大壩建好之前，坎貝爾河常在春季發大水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a reservoir of water created by such a barrier 壩中的水","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to obstruct or restrict by or as if by a dam 築壩阻攔","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"symbol for.","pos_name":"symbol for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"decametre(s) 十米","examples":[]}]}]},"credit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信用，信貸，賒購；讚揚，信譽，聲望；存款金額，餘額；補助；退稅，抵免；學分；帶來榮耀的人（或事）；作品（指影片、電視節目、戲劇等）；信任，相信"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（錢）記入總賬，把錢存入（賬戶）；相信，信任；認為是……的功勞，給予承認；認為……有特定品質（或效果）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are given <b>credit</b>, you are allowed to pay for goods or services several weeks or months after you have received them. 賒購","examples":["The group can't get credit to buy farming machinery. 該集團無法以賒購方式購買農業機械。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you get <b>the</b> <b>credit</b> <b>for</b> something good, people praise you because you are responsible for it, or are thought to be responsible for it. 讚揚","examples":["We don't mind who gets the credit so long as we don't get the blame. 只要我們不挨批評，誰受到表揚我們都不在乎。","It would be wrong for us to take all the credit. 我們把所有的功勞都攬到自己身上就不對了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>credit</b> is a sum of money which is added to an account. 貸方款額","examples":["The statement of total debits and credits is known as a balance. 總的借貸報表稱作借貸平衡表。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>credit</b> is an amount of money that is given to someone. 補助","examples":["Senator Bill Bradley outlined his own tax cut, giving families $350 in tax credits per child. 參議員比爾·布拉德利簡述了自己的減稅計劃，給家庭中每一個孩子$350稅款補助。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The list of people who helped to make a film, a CD, or a television programme is called <b>the</b> <b>credits</b>. 攝製人員名單","examples":["It was fantastic seeing my name in the credits. 在攝製人員名單中看到我的名字真是太好了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>credit</b> is a successfully completed part of a higher education course, representing about one hour of instruction a week. At universities and colleges you need a certain number of credits to be awarded a degree. 學分","examples":["Through the AP programme students can earn college credits in high school. 透過大學預修課程計劃，學生在中學就可以拿到大學的學分。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>a credit to</b> someone or something, you mean that their qualities or achievements will make people have a good opinion of the person or thing mentioned. 為…增光的人","examples":["He is one of the greatest players of recent times and is a credit to his profession. 他是近年來最棒的選手之一，是為他的職業增光的人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a sum of money <b>is credited</b> <b>to</b> an account, the bank adds that sum of money to the total in the account. 存入","examples":["She noticed that only $80,000 had been credited to her account. 她注意到只有$80000存入了她的賬戶。","Midland decided to change the way it credited payments to accounts. 米德蘭公司決定改變將所付款項存入賬戶的方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>credit</b> someone <b>with</b> an achievement or if it <b>is credited to</b> them, people say or believe that they were responsible for it. 歸功於","examples":["The staff are crediting him with having saved Hythe's life. 海斯能得救全體人員都歸功於他。","The 74-year-old mayor is credited with helping make Los Angeles the financial capital of the West Coast. 74歲的市長被歸功為幫助洛杉磯成為西海岸金融中心的人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>give</b> someone <b>credit for</b> a good quality means to believe that they have it. 相信某人有","examples":["Bratbakk had more ability than the media gave him credit for. 布拉特巴克有比媒體所宣傳的還要強的能力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>to</b> someone's <b>credit</b>, they deserve praise for it. 值得讚揚","examples":["She had managed to pull herself together and, to her credit, continued to look upon life as a positive experience. 她努力使自己振作起來，並且值得稱讚的是，她一如既往地積極面對人生。"]}]}]},"crown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王冠，冕；王位，王權（the crown）；王國政府，王國（the Crown）；冠軍寶座，桂冠；頭頂，帽頂；頂部；5先令的英國舊幣；（受損牙齒的）人造冠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……加冕，立……為王；形成……頂部，給……加頂；使圓滿，使完美；（在牙齒上）鑲人造冠；<非正式>打……的頭部；（分娩時胎兒的頭）露頂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crown</b> is a circular ornament, usually made of gold and jewels, which a king or queen wears on their head at official ceremonies. You can also use <b>crown</b> to refer to anything circular that is worn on someone's head. 王冠; 冠","examples":["...a crown of flowers. …一個花冠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>crown</b> is the top part of your head, at the back. 頭頂後部","examples":["He laid his hand gently on the crown of her head. 他把手輕輕地放在她的頭頂後部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>crown</b> is an artificial top piece fixed over a broken or decayed tooth. 齒冠","examples":["How long does it take to have crowns fitted? 鑲齒冠需要多長時間？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The government of a country that has a king or queen is sometimes referred to as <b>the Crown</b>. 王國政府","examples":["She says the sovereignty of the Crown must be preserved. 她說君主政權必須予以保留。","...a minister of the Crown. …王國政府的一位大臣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a king or queen <b>is crowned</b>, a crown is placed on their head as part of a ceremony in which they are officially made king or queen. 為…加冕","examples":["Two days later, Juan Carlos was crowned king. 兩天後，胡安·卡洛斯被加冕為國王。"]}]}]},"current":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"現行的，當前的；通用的，流行的；最近的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水流，氣流；電流；思潮，趨勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>current</b> is a steady and continuous flowing movement of some of the water in a river, lake, or ocean. 水流","examples":["Under normal conditions, the ocean currents of the tropical Pacific travel from east to west. 在正常情況下，太平洋熱帶洋流自東流向西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>current</b> is a steady flowing movement of air. 氣流","examples":["I felt a current of cool air blowing in my face. 我感到一股涼氣吹在臉上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An electric <b>current</b> is a flow of electricity through a wire or circuit. 電流","examples":["A powerful electric current is passed through a piece of graphite. 一股強大的電流被傳導經過一塊石墨。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A particular <b>current</b> is a particular feeling, idea, or quality that exists within a group of people. 傾向","examples":["Each party represents a distinct current of thought. 每個黨派都代表一種獨特的思想傾向。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Current</b> means happening, being used, or being done at the present time. 當前的","examples":["The current situation is very different to that in 1990. 當前的形勢與1990年大不相同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Ideas and customs that are <b>current</b> are generally accepted and used by most people. 流行的","examples":["Current thinking suggests that toxins only have a small part to play in the build-up of cellulite. 流行的觀點認為毒素只對脂肪團形成起很小的作用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"目前","examples":["Twelve potential vaccines are currently being tested on human volunteers. 12種潛在疫苗目前正在人體志願者身上測試。"]}]}]},"cycle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳踏車，摩托車；迴圈，週期；組詩，組歌；整套，系列；腳踏車騎行；一段時間"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎腳踏車；迴圈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cycle</b> is a series of events or processes that is repeated again and again, always in the same order. 週期","examples":["...the life cycle of the plant. …植物的生命週期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cycle</b> is a single complete series of movements in an electrical, electronic, or mechanical process. 圈","examples":["...10 cycles per second. …每秒10圈。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cycle</b> is a bicycle. 腳踏車","examples":["We supply the travel ticket for you and your cycle. 我們為您和您的腳踏車提供旅行票。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"騎腳踏車","examples":["The quiet country roads are ideal for cycling. 安靜的鄉村道路很適合騎腳踏車。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cycle</b>, you ride a bicycle. 騎腳踏車","examples":["He cycled to Ingwold. 他騎車去了英格沃爾德。"]}]}]},"dealer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商人，交易商；<非正式>毒品販子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dealer</b> is a person whose business involves buying and selling things. 商人","examples":["...an antique dealer. …一位古董商。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dealer</b> is someone who buys and sells illegal drugs. 毒品販子","examples":["They will stay on the job for as long as it takes to clear every dealer from the street. 他們將堅持工作，直到街道上所有的毒品販子都被清除。"]}]}]},"darling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"親愛的，寶貝；親切友好的人；寵兒，紅人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"親愛的，心愛的；可愛的，迷人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You call someone <b>darling</b> if you love them or like them very much. 親愛的","examples":["Thank you, darling. 謝謝你，親愛的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>darling</b>, you are fond of them and think that they are nice. 心愛的人","examples":["He's such a darling. 他真是個寶貝。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people use <b>darling</b> to describe someone or something that they love or like very much. 心愛的","examples":["To have a darling baby boy was the greatest gift I could imagine. 擁有一個心愛的小男孩是我所能想像的最好的禮物。"]}]}]},"decade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"十年，十年期；十進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>decade</b> is a period of ten years, especially one that begins with a year ending in 0, for example, 1980 to 1989. 10年 (尤指起始年末尾為0)","examples":["...the last decade of the nineteenth century. …19世紀的最後10年。"]}]}]},"deed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為，行動；契約，證書；功績，英勇事蹟"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"立契轉讓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deed</b> is something that is done, especially something that is very good or very bad. 行為","examples":["The perpetrators of this evil deed must be brought to justice. 這件惡行的兇手必須接受法律的制裁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>deed</b> is a document containing the terms of an agreement, especially an agreement concerning the ownership of land or a building. 契約; 證書","examples":["He asked if I had the deeds to his father's property. 他問我是否有他父親財產的各種證書。"]}]}]},"democracy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"民主政體；民主國家；民主，民主精神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Democracy</b> is a system of government in which people choose their rulers by voting for them in elections. 民主政體","examples":["The spread of democracy in Eastern Europe appears to have had negative as well as positive consequences. 東歐民主政體的蔓延看來既有消極也有積極的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>democracy</b> is a country in which the people choose their government by voting for it. 民主國家","examples":["The new democracies face tough challenges. 新生的民主國家面臨嚴峻的挑戰。"]}]}]},"definition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"定義，釋義；榜樣，典範；清晰，清晰度，鮮明度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>definition</b> is a statement giving the meaning of a word or expression, especially in a dictionary. 定義","examples":["There is no general agreement on a standard definition of intelligence. 對智力的標準定義意見不統一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Definition</b> is the quality of being clear and distinct. 清晰度","examples":["The first speakers at the conference criticized Prof. Johnson's new programme for lack of definition. 會上的首批發言者批評約翰遜教授的新專案沒有清晰度。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something has a particular quality <b>by definition</b>, you mean that it has this quality simply because of what it is. 按照釋義","examples":[]}]}]},"delivery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遞送，投遞；遞送物；演講風格，演說方式；分娩，生產；投球方式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"運送的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Delivery</b> or a <b>delivery</b> is the bringing of letters, packages, or other goods to someone's house or to another place where they want them. 遞送","examples":["Please allow 28 days for delivery. 請留出28天的遞送時間。","The uprising is threatening the delivery of humanitarian supplies of food and medicine. 這場暴亂正威脅到食物和藥品等人道主義物資的運送。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Delivery</b> is the process of giving birth to a baby. 分娩","examples":["In the end, it was an easy delivery: a fine baby boy. 最終，分娩順利——一個健康的男嬰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>delivery</b> of something is the goods that are delivered. 遞送的貨物","examples":["I got a delivery of fresh eggs this morning. 今天早上我收到了一批新鮮雞蛋。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You talk about someone's <b>delivery</b> when you are referring to the way in which they give a speech or lecture. 演講方式","examples":["His speeches were magnificently written but his delivery was hopeless. 他的演講辭寫得很好，但他的演講卻不可救藥。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>delivery</b> person or service delivers things to a place. 送貨的","examples":["...a pizza delivery man. …一個送比薩餅的男子。"]}]}]},"deck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"甲板，艙面；（船或公共汽車的）層；<美>一副牌；（屋後供休息的）木製平臺；（唱機的）盤裝置，（音響系統的）走帶機構"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝飾，打扮；<非正式>用力擊倒；裝甲板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deck</b> on a vehicle such as a bus or ship is a lower or upper area of it. (公共汽車或船的) 層","examples":["...a luxury liner with five passenger decks. …一艘有5層艙位樓層的豪華遊輪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>deck</b> of a ship is the top part of it that forms a floor in the open air which you can walk on. 甲板","examples":["She stood on the deck and waved her hand to them as the steamer moved off. 汽船駛離時，她站在甲板上和他們揮手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>deck</b> is a flat wooden area next to a house, where people can sit and relax or eat. (屋邊供休息的木製) 平臺","examples":["A natural timber deck leads into the main room of the home. 一個天然木頭平臺通向家裡的主室。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>deck</b> of cards is a complete set of playing cards. (紙牌) 付","examples":[]}]}]},"description":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"描述，形容，說明；型別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>description</b> of someone or something is an account which explains what they are or what they look like. 描述","examples":["Police have issued a description of the man who was aged between fifty and sixty. 警方已已公佈了這一年齡在50至60之間的男子的相貌特徵。","The paper provides a detailed description of how to create human embryos by cloning. 這篇論文對如何透過克隆製造人類胚胎提供詳細的描述。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>of</b> a particular <b>description</b>, it belongs to the general class of items that are mentioned. 屬…種類","examples":["Events of this description occurred daily. 這類事件每天都有發生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>beyond</b> <b>description</b>, or that it <b>defies</b> <b>description</b>, to emphasize that it is very unusual, impressive, terrible, or extreme. 無法形容","examples":["His face is weary beyond description. 他臉上的疲憊無法形容。"]}]}]},"deposit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放下，放置；儲蓄；存放，寄存；沉積，沉澱；支付（押金、訂金或預繳費用）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"沉積物，沉積層；訂金；押金；存款；競選保證金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deposit</b> is a sum of money which is part of the full price of something, and which you pay when you agree to buy it. 保證金","examples":["The initial deposit required to open an account is a minimum 100 dollars. 開戶需要的首筆存入額是至少100美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>deposit</b> is a sum of money which is in a bank account or savings account, especially a sum which will be left there for some time. 存款","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>deposit</b> is an amount of a substance that has been left somewhere as a result of a chemical or geological process. 沉積物; 礦床","examples":["...underground deposits of gold and diamonds. …黃金和鑽石的地下礦床。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>deposit</b> is a sum of money which you pay when you start renting something. The money is returned to you if you do not damage what you have rented. 押金","examples":["I put down a $500 security deposit for another apartment. 我為另一套公寓支付了$500押金。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>deposit</b> is a sum of money which you put into a bank account. 銀行存款","examples":["She told me I should make a deposit every week and they'd stamp my book. 她告訴我我每週都要存一次錢，而他們會在我的存摺上蓋印。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deposit</b> a sum of money, you put it into a bank account or savings account. 儲存","examples":["The customer has to deposit a minimum of $100 monthly. 顧客每月必須至少存入$100。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>deposit</b> someone or something somewhere means to put them or leave them there. 放置","examples":["Mr. Crenshaw deposited the boys and their suitcases on Mr. Peck's lawn. 克倫肖先生把男孩子和他們的手提箱留在了派克先生的草坪上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>deposit</b> something somewhere, you put it where it will be safe until it is needed again. 寄存","examples":["You are advised to deposit valuables in the hotel safe. 建議您將貴重物品寄存在旅館的保險櫃裡。"]}]}]},"dash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛衝，急奔；猛撞，撞擊；使（希望或期望）破滅；迅速寫或畫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"猛衝，飛奔；少量，少許（新增物）；破折號；<舊>衝勁，銳氣；<美>短跑；<非正式>（汽車的）儀表盤；（莫爾斯電碼中的）長劃；（Dash）達世幣（一種網路加密貨幣）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英，非正式>用於表示輕微的惱怒，該死的"},{"pos":"","zh":"【英】（Dash）（英、美、印）達什（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dash</b> somewhere, you run or go there quickly and suddenly. 猛衝","examples":["Suddenly she dashed down to the cellar. 她猛地朝地窖衝過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you have to <b>dash</b>, you mean that you are in a hurry and have to leave immediately. 趕緊離開","examples":["Oh, Tim! I'm sorry but I have to dash. 噢，蒂姆！很抱歉，但我得趕緊走了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dash</b> is also a noun. 猛衝","examples":["...a 160-mile dash to the hospital. …飛奔160英里趕向醫院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dash</b> <b>of</b> something is a small quantity of it which you add when you are preparing food or mixing a drink. 少量","examples":["Pour over olive oil and a dash of balsamic vinegar to accentuate the sweetness. 倒入橄欖油和少量香醋以使甜味更濃些。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dash</b> <b>of</b> a quality is a small amount of it that is found in something and often makes it more interesting or distinctive. 一點 (趣味或特色)","examples":["...a story with a dash of mystery thrown in. …加入了一抹神秘色彩的故事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>dash</b> is a straight, horizontal line used in writing, for example, to separate two main clauses whose meanings are closely connected. 破折號","examples":["...the dash between the birth date and death date. …生卒日期之間的破折號。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>dash</b> of a car is its . 儀表板","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dash</b> something <b>against</b> a wall or other surface, you throw or push it violently, often so hard that it breaks. 猛撞; 猛摔","examples":["She seized the doll and dashed it against the stone wall with tremendous force. 她抓起洋娃娃，使勁往石牆上摔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or person <b>dashes</b> someone's hopes or expectations, it destroys them by making it impossible that the thing that is hoped for or expected will ever happen. 使破滅","examples":["Renewed fighting has dashed hopes for a United Nations-organized interim government. 重燃的戰火粉碎了在聯合國的組織下建立臨時政府的希望。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make a dash for</b> a place, you run there very quickly, for example, to escape from someone or something. 衝","examples":["I made a dash for the front door but he got there before me. 我向前門衝去，但他卻已先我而到。"]}]}]},"designer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"設計師，設計者；謀劃者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"由著名設計師設計的，標有設計師姓名的；時尚的，時髦的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>designer</b> is a person whose job is to design things by making drawings of them. 設計師","examples":["Carolyne is a fashion designer. 卡羅琳是位時裝設計師。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Designer</b> clothes or <b>designer</b> labels are expensive, fashionable clothes made by a famous designer, rather than being made in large quantities in a factory. 名師設計的","examples":["He wears designer clothes and drives an antique car. 他穿著名師設計的服裝，開著一輛老爺車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>designer</b> to describe things that are worn or bought because they are fashionable. 時尚的","examples":["She sat up and removed her designer sunglasses. 她坐起來，摘掉她的時尚墨鏡。"]}]}]},"dime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國、加拿大的）十分硬幣；<非正式>小錢，少量的錢；<非正式>（就尺寸、面積或程度而言的）小東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dime</b> is a U.S. coin worth ten cents. 10美分硬幣","examples":["The penny meters are slowly being replaced by electronic ones that take nickels, dimes, and quarters. 接受1美分硬幣的收費表正逐漸被接受5美分、10美分和25美分的電子收費計所取代。"]}]}]},"dialogue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對白；對話，交換意見"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>（為解決問題而）參加對話，進行討論；<美>為（電影、戲劇）配上對白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dialogue</b> is communication or discussion between people or groups of people such as governments or political parties. 對話","examples":["People of all social standings should be given equal opportunities for dialogue. 社會各階層的人都應該被給予平等對話的機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dialogue</b> is a conversation between two people in a book, film, or play. (書籍、影視、戲劇中的) 對白","examples":["Although the dialogue is sharp, the actors move too awkwardly around the stage. 儘管對白很清晰，但演員們在舞臺上的動作卻太不自然。"]}]}]},"discotheque":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"迪斯科舞廳，迪斯科夜總會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>discotheque</b> is the same as a . 同disco","examples":[]}]}]},"devil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魔鬼；魔王，撒旦（the Devil）；傢伙，人；惡棍；淘氣鬼，冒失鬼；棘手的事，麻煩事；<非正式，舊>（出庭律師或其他專業人士的）助手；切碎機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>困擾，使擔憂；抹辣味料烤（肉等）；（用扯碎機）扯碎（破布）；做律師（或作家等）的助手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In Judaism, Christianity, and Islam, <b>the Devil</b> is the most powerful evil spirit. 魔鬼","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>devil</b> is an evil spirit. (猶太教、基督教、伊斯蘭教中的) 魔王","examples":["...the idea of angels with wings and devils with horns and hoofs. …天使長翅膀、魔鬼長角生蹄的觀念。"]}]}]},"detail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"細節，細微之處；詳情，資料；（軍隊中的）任務，特遣隊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"詳細說明，詳述；徹底清洗（汽車）；（尤指軍隊中）派遣，選派"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>details</b> <b>of</b> something are its individual features or elements. 細節","examples":["The details of the plan are still being worked out. 計劃的細節還在制定中。","No details of the discussions have been given. 會談的細節尚未透露。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>detail</b> is a minor point or aspect of something, as opposed to the central ones. 枝節","examples":["Only minor details now remain to be settled. 只有細枝末節還沒確定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Details</b> about someone or something are facts or pieces of information about them. 詳情","examples":["See the bottom of this page for details of how to apply for this exciting offer. 關於如何申請這個令人激動的機會，詳情請參看本頁末。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to the small features of something which are often not noticed as <b>detail</b>. 細微處","examples":["We like his attention to detail and his enthusiasm. 我們喜歡他對細微之處的關注，以及他的熱情。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>detail</b> of people such as soldiers or prisoners is a small group of them who have been given a special task to carry out. 分遣隊","examples":["...a sergeant with a detail of four men. …1個帶4人分遣隊的中士。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>detail</b> things, you list them or give information about them. 詳細列舉; 詳細說明","examples":["The report detailed the human rights abuses committed during the war. 這份報告詳述了戰時進行的人權踐踏。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does not <b>go into detail</b> about a subject, or does not <b>go into the details</b>, they mention it without explaining it fully or properly. 詳細敘述","examples":["He doesn't wish to go into detail about all the events of those days. 他不想詳述那些天發生的所有事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you examine or discuss something <b>in detail</b>, you do it thoroughly and carefully. 詳細地","examples":["We examine the wording in detail before deciding on the final text. 我們詳細檢查了措辭，才確定了最終文字。"]}]}]},"diet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"規定飲食；大量單調的活動；日常飲食"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"節食"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"低脂的，低糖的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>diet</b> is the type and variety of food that you regularly eat. 日常飲食","examples":["It's never too late to improve your diet. 改善飲食什麼時候都不嫌晚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are on a <b>diet</b>, you eat special kinds of food or you eat less food than usual because you are trying to lose weight. (因減肥而吃的) 規定飲食","examples":["Have you been on a diet? You've lost a lot of weight. 你在節食嗎？你瘦了很多。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a doctor puts someone on a <b>diet</b>, he or she makes them eat a special type or variety of foods in order to improve their health. (醫生為病人規定的) 特種飲食","examples":["Certain chronic conditions, such as diabetes, require special diets that should be monitored by your physician. 一些慢性病，如糖尿病，要求病人食用由醫生指導的特定食物。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are fed on a <b>diet</b> <b>of</b> something, especially something unpleasant or of poor quality, you receive or experience a very large amount of it. 大量 (不愉快的事或質量差的東西)","examples":["The radio had fed him a diet of pop songs. 收音機沒完沒了地向他播放流行音樂。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a legislative assembly in various countries, such as Japan 議會","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are dieting</b>, you eat special kinds of food or you eat less food than usual because you are trying to lose weight. 節食","examples":["I've been dieting ever since the birth of my fourth child. 自從我第4個孩子出生以後，我就一直在節食。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Diet</b> drinks or foods have been specially produced so that they do not contain many calories. (飲食) 低熱量的","examples":["...sugar-free diet drinks. …無糖的低熱量飲料。"]}]}]},"disco":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"迪斯科，計程車高，迪斯科舞曲；迪斯科舞廳或迪斯科舞會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳迪斯科舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disco</b> is a place or event at which people dance to pop music. 迪斯科舞廳; 迪斯科舞會","examples":["Fridays and Saturdays are regular disco nights. 星期五和星期六是固定的迪斯科之夜。"]}]}]},"dirt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙物，塵土；泥土，鬆土；醜聞，流言蜚語"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"土的，泥的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>dirt</b> on something, there is dust, mud, or a stain on it. 灰塵; 汙垢","examples":["I started to scrub off the dirt. 我開始擦除灰塵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the earth on the ground as <b>dirt</b>, especially when it is dusty. 泥土","examples":["They all sit on the dirt in the dappled shade of a tree. 他們都坐在斑駁的樹蔭下的地上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you have <b>the</b> <b>dirt</b> <b>on</b> someone, you mean that you have information that could harm their reputation or career. 流言蜚語","examples":["...a sleazy reporter assigned to dig up dirt on Jack. …一名受人指使去挖掘有關傑克的流言蜚語的低階庸俗的記者。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dirt</b> road or track is made from hard earth. A <b>dirt</b> floor is made from earth without any cement, stone, or wood laid on it. 泥土的","examples":["I drove along the dirt road. 我行駛在一條土路上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>treats</b> you <b>like dirt</b>, you are angry with them because you think that they treat you unfairly and with no respect. 把…看得一錢不值","examples":["People think they can treat me like dirt! 人們竟然認為可以把我完全不當一回事！"]}]}]},"disappointment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"失望，沮喪；令人失望的人，讓人掃興的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disappointment</b> is the state of feeling disappointed. 失望","examples":["Despite winning the title, their last campaign ended in great disappointment. 儘管得了冠軍，他們最後一場比賽卻在極度失望中完結。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something or someone that is a <b>disappointment</b> is not as good as you had hoped. 令人失望的人; 令人失望的物","examples":["For many, their long-awaited homecoming was a bitter disappointment. 對很多人來說，他們期盼已久的返鄉成了一件令人傷心失望的事。"]}]}]},"disc":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圓盤，圓片；唱片，光碟，碟片；磁碟；椎間盤（亦作 disk）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"灌唱片"}],"sections":[]},"dip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"浸，蘸；下降，下沉；伸進，伸入；<英>將（汽車前燈）調為近光；給（動物）洗藥浴；減少，降低；瀏覽，翻看；動用（款項等）；<非正式>扒竊；<非正式，舊>給（某人）施洗禮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"遊一遊，泡一泡；減少，下降；調味醬；凹陷處，低窪處；藥浴液；<美>傻瓜，笨蛋；翻閱，瀏覽；一勺（的量）；（降而復升的）一動；短距離的下坡；<技>（向下的）傾角；<非正式，舊>扒手；<古>製作（蠟燭）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dip</b> something <b>in</b> a liquid, you put it into the liquid for a short time, so that only part of it is covered, and take it out again. 蘸","examples":["Dip each apple in the syrup until thickly coated. 把每個蘋果在糖漿裡蘸一下，直到被厚厚地裹上糖漿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dip</b> your hand <b>into</b> a container or <b>dip</b> <b>into</b> the container, you put your hand into it in order to take something out of it. (將手) 伸入","examples":["She dipped a hand into the jar of candies and pulled one out. 她把手伸進糖罐裡掏出一顆糖來。","Nancy dipped into the bowl of popcorn that Hannah had made for them. 南希把手伸進盛著漢娜給她們做的爆米花的碗裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dip</b> is also a noun. 蘸","examples":["...a quick dip of his toe into the water. …他的腳趾頭在水裡快速的一蘸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dip</b> is also a noun. (突然的) 下沉","examples":["I noticed little things, a dip of the head, a twitch in the shoulder. 我注意到一些小動作，腦袋向下的一沉、肩膀的一抽動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dip</b> is also a noun. (土地、地段、道路等的) 突陷","examples":["Where the road makes a dip, soon after a small vineyard on the right, turn right. 過了右邊的小葡萄園不久，在路面陡降的地方朝右轉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Dip</b> is also a noun. (暫時的) 下降","examples":["...the current dip in farm spending. …農場開支目前的暫時下降。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you have or take a <b>dip</b>, you go for a quick swim in the ocean, a lake, a river, or a swimming pool. 快遊","examples":["She flicked through a romantic paperback between occasional dips in the pool. 她在泳池裡偶爾的快遊的間歇之中快速翻完了一本平裝本的愛情小說。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>dips</b>, it makes a downward movement, usually quickly. (突然) 下沉","examples":["Blake jumped in expertly; the boat dipped slightly under his weight. 布萊克熟練地跳了進來；船由於他的體重微微沉了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an area of land, a road, or a path <b>dips</b>, it goes down quite suddenly to a lower level. (土地、地段、道路等) 突陷","examples":["The road dipped and rose again as it neared the top of Parker Mountain. 快到帕克山山頂的時候，山路突降，繼而又突升。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the amount or level of something <b>dips</b>, it becomes smaller or lower, usually only for a short period of time. (暫時) 下降","examples":["Unemployment dipped to 6.9 percent last month. 上個月，失業率降到了6.9%。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>dip into</b> a book, you take a brief look at it without reading or studying it seriously. 瀏覽","examples":["...a chance to dip into a wide selection of books on Tibetan Buddhism. …一次瀏覽有關藏傳佛教的各種各樣書籍的機會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>dip into</b> a sum of money that you had intended to save, you use some of it to buy something or pay for something. 動用 (積蓄)","examples":["Just when she was ready to dip into her savings, Greg hastened to her rescue. 就在她準備動用積蓄時，格雷格趕來救了她的急。"]}]}]},"ditch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溝渠，壕溝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挖溝，修渠；<非正式>擺脫，拋棄；<美，非正式>逃學，曠工；<美，非正式>不辭而別；（使）在水上迫降；<美>使（火車）脫軌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ditch</b> is a long narrow channel cut into the ground at the side of a road or field. 道溝; 溝渠","examples":["Both vehicles ended up in a ditch. 兩輛車都掉進了溝裡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ditch</b> something that you have or are responsible for, you abandon it or get rid of it, because you no longer want it. 丟棄","examples":["I decided to ditch the sofa bed. 我決定把沙發床扔掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>ditches</b> someone, they end a relationship with that person. 拋棄","examples":["I can't bring myself to ditch him and start again. 我不能說服自己拋棄他，又重新開始。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a pilot <b>ditches</b> an aircraft or if it <b>ditches</b>, the pilot makes an emergency landing. (飛機) 緊急迫降","examples":["One American pilot was forced to ditch his jet in the Gulf. 一個美國飛行員被迫在海灣緊急迫降其噴氣式飛機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>ditches</b> school or work, they decide not to go to school or work, although they are supposed to go there. 逃學; 曠工","examples":["What do you say we ditch school and go to the mall? 我們逃學去商場，你覺得怎樣？"]}]}]},"disk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機的）磁碟，磁碟；（計算機的）磁碟，磁碟（=disc）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disc</b> is a flat, circular shape or object. 盤狀物","examples":["The food processor has thin, medium, and thick slicing discs. 這個食品加工機有薄、中、厚的切片盤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>disc</b> is one of the thin, circular pieces of cartilage which separates the bones in your back. 椎間盤","examples":["I had slipped a disc and was frozen in a spasm of pain. 我的一塊椎間盤脫臼了，突然一陣疼痛使我動彈不得。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a computer, the <b>disk</b> is the part where information is stored. (電腦) 磁碟","examples":["The program takes up 2.5 megabytes of disk space and can be run on a standard personal computer. 這個程式佔用2.5 兆位元組的磁碟空間，可以在標準個人電腦上執行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A disc is the same as a . 光碟","examples":[]}]}]},"discount":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"減價，折扣；（匯票或期票到期前轉手的）貼現率"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"打折的，減價出售的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打折，減價；不重視，忽視；否定，懷疑；貼現；（持票人或受票人）把（票據）貼現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>discount</b> is a reduction in the usual price of something. 折扣","examples":["They are often available at a discount. 它們經常可以以折扣價買到。","All full-time staff get a 20 percent discount. 所有全職員工都可以享受8折優惠。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a shop or company <b>discounts</b> an amount or percentage from something that they are selling, they take the amount or percentage off the usual price. 對…打折","examples":["This has forced airlines to discount fares heavily in order to spur demand. 這已經迫使多家航空公司對機票大幅打折以刺激需求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>discount</b> an idea, fact, or theory, you consider that it is not true, not important, or not relevant. 不理會，否定，懷疑","examples":["However, traders tended to discount the rumour. 但是，商人們傾向於不理會這個傳聞。"]}]}]},"discovery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發現，被發現的事物；（法律）強制性透露"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone makes a <b>discovery</b>, they become aware of something that they did not know about before. 發現","examples":["I felt I'd made an incredible discovery. 我感到自己有了一個驚人的發現。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone makes a <b>discovery</b>, they are the first person to find or become aware of a place, substance, or scientific fact that no one knew about before. 新發現","examples":["In that year, two momentous discoveries were made. 那年有2項重大的新發現。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When the <b>discovery</b> of people or objects happens, someone finds them, either by accident or as a result of looking for them. 發現","examples":["...the discovery and destruction by soldiers of millions of marijuana plants. …士兵們對數百萬株大麻的發現和摧毀。"]}]}]},"dislike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"不喜歡，厭惡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不喜歡，反感；不喜歡的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dislike</b> someone or something, you consider them to be unpleasant and do not like them. 不喜愛","examples":["Liver is a great favourite of his and we don't serve it often because so many people dislike it. 肝臟是他的一種最愛，但我們不常供應這道菜，因為有那麼多人不愛吃。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dislike</b> is the feeling that you do not like someone or something. 厭惡","examples":["My dislike of thunder and even small earthquakes was due to Mother. 我對雷聲甚至於輕微地震的厭惡都歸因於我的母親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>dislikes</b> are the things that you do not like. 不喜歡的事物","examples":["Consider what your likes and dislikes are about your job. 考慮一下，對於你的工作哪些是你喜歡的，哪些是不喜歡的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take a dislike</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you decide that you do not like them. 討厭","examples":["He may suddenly take a dislike to foods that he's previously enjoyed. 他也許會突然討厭他以前喜歡吃的食物。"]}]}]},"disease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疾病，病害；弊病，惡習"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳染，使……有病"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disease</b> is an illness which affects people, animals, or plants, for example, one which is caused by bacteria or infection. 疾病","examples":["...the rapid spread of disease in the area. …疾病在這一地區的迅速傳播。"]}]}]},"dodge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃開，躲開；巧妙躲避，施計迴避；按變換序列鳴鐘；（沖洗或放大時）區域性遮光"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"逃避的詭計，騙人的伎倆；躲閃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dodge</b>, you move suddenly, often to avoid being hit, caught, or seen. 躲閃","examples":["I dodged back into the alley and waited a minute. 我往後一閃，躲進衚衕裡等了一會兒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dodge</b> something, you avoid it by quickly moving aside or out of reach so that it cannot hit or reach you. 閃開","examples":["He desperately dodged a speeding car trying to run him down. 他拼命地閃身躲開一輛高速撞向自己的汽車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dodge</b> something, you deliberately avoid thinking about it or dealing with it, often by being deceitful. 逃避","examples":["He boasts of dodging military service by feigning illness. 他吹噓說自己裝病逃過了兵役。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dodge</b> is also a noun. 逃避","examples":["This was not just a tax dodge. 這不僅僅是逃稅的問題。"]}]}]},"dock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碼頭，船埠，船塢；港區；（供上下船或系船用的）突堤，棧橋；供船隻、卡車、火車等裝卸貨物用的）月臺；（尤指私家）泊位； 酸模（一種植物）；動物尾巴（除毛髮外的）骨肉部分；被告席；被告席"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使船）靠碼頭，進港；（航天器）在太空對接；將電子裝置（如電腦、數碼相機）相接；扣工資，扣分；剪短（動物的尾巴）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dock</b> is an enclosed area in a harbour where ships go to be loaded, unloaded, and repaired. 碼頭","examples":["She headed for the docks, thinking that Ricardo might be hiding in one of the boats. 她朝著碼頭走去，心想裡卡多可能藏在其中的一條船上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dock</b> is a platform for loading vehicles or trains. 裝車平臺","examples":["The truck left the loading dock with hoses still attached. 卡車離開了裝貨平臺，軟管還掛在車上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dock</b> is a small structure at the edge of water where boats can tie up, especially one that is privately owned. (尤指私家) 泊位","examples":["He had a house there and a dock and a little aluminium boat. 他在那兒有一幢房、一個泊位和一條鋁艇。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"any of various temperate weedy plants of the polygonaceous genus <b>Rumex,</b> having greenish or reddish flowers and typically broad leaves 酸模屬\n植物","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a law court, <b>the</b> <b>dock</b> is where the person accused of a crime stands or sits. 被告席","examples":["What about the odd chance that you do put an innocent man in the dock? 萬一你真的將一個無辜的人送上了被告席可怎麼辦呢？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a ship <b>docks</b> or <b>is docked</b>, it is brought into a dock. 停靠碼頭","examples":["The crash happened as the ferry attempted to dock on Staten Island. 這次碰撞發生於渡船試圖停靠在斯塔滕島時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dock</b> someone's pay or money, you take some of the money away. 扣 (錢)","examples":["He threatens to dock her fee. 他威脅要扣她的費用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>dock</b> someone points in a contest, you take away some of the points that they have. 扣 (分)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When one spacecraft <b>docks</b> or <b>is docked</b> <b>with</b> another, the two crafts join together in space. (宇宙飛船) 對接","examples":["The space shuttle Atlantis is scheduled to dock with Russia's Mir space station. 亞特蘭蒂斯號太空梭計劃與俄羅斯的米爾號空間站對接。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to remove (the tail or part of the tail) of (an animal) by cutting through the bone 切除動物的尾巴; 切除動物的尾巴的一段","examples":[]}]}]},"dive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳水；潛水；突然大幅貶值，暴跌；下降，下潛；撲向，衝向；（飛機，鳥）俯衝；熱情投身於；快速伸入（包、口袋等）；（對方阻截時）假摔"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跳水；潛水；俯衝；突降，暴跌；衝，撲；（遇到阻截時的）假摔；低階的餐館（或酒吧、娛樂場所）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dive</b> <b>into</b> some water, you jump in head first with your arms held straight above your head. 跳水","examples":["He tried to escape by diving into a river. 他企圖跳入河中逃走。","She was standing by a pool, about to dive in. 她正站在池邊，準備跳進去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dive</b>, you go under the surface of the sea or a lake, using special breathing equipment. 潛水","examples":["Bezanik is diving to collect marine organisms. 貝贊尼克正在潛水採集海洋生物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When birds and animals <b>dive</b>, they go quickly downward, head first, through the air or through water. (鳥等動物) 俯衝","examples":["...a pelican which had just dived for a fish. …一隻剛剛下潛捕魚的鵜鶘。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>dive</b> in a particular direction or into a particular place, you jump or move there quickly. 躍向; 衝向","examples":["They dived into a taxi. 他們衝進了計程車。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If shares, profits, or figures <b>dive</b>, their value falls suddenly and by a large amount. (股票、利潤、數字等) 突然暴跌","examples":["They feared the stock could dive after its first day of trading. 他們擔心這支股票在其第一個交易日後會暴跌。","Profits have dived from $7.7m to $7.1m. 利潤從770萬美元驟跌至710萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dive</b> is also a noun. 跳水","examples":["Pat had earlier made a dive of 80 feet from the Chasm Bridge. 早些時，帕特曾從卡澤姆大橋進行過80英尺高的跳水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dive</b> is also a noun. 潛水","examples":["This sighting occurred during my dive to a sunken wreck off Sardinia. 這次親眼所見發生在我向撒丁島外一艘沉船潛水的期間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dive</b> is also a noun. 衝; 撲","examples":["He made a sudden dive for Uncle Jim's legs to try to trip him up. 他猛地撲向吉姆大叔的雙腿，試圖絆倒他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Dive</b> is also a noun. (股票、利潤、數字等) 驟降","examples":["Stock prices took a dive. 股票價格暴跌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe a bar or club as a <b>dive</b>, you mean it is dirty and dark, and not very respectable. 低階酒吧; 低階夜總會","examples":["We've played in all the little clubs and dives around Philadelphia. 我們玩遍了費城所有的小酒吧和低階夜總會。"]}]}]},"drunk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"喝醉的，醉酒的；陶醉的，沉醉的，忘乎所以"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"酗酒者，酒鬼；<非正式>縱飲，醉酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"喝，飲；喝酒（drink 的過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>drunk</b> has drunk so much alcohol that they cannot speak clearly or behave sensibly. 醉了的","examples":["I got drunk and had to be carried home. 我喝醉了，只得被攙扶回家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drunk</b> is someone who is drunk or frequently gets drunk. 醉酒者; 酗酒者","examples":["A drunk lay in the alley. 一個醉漢倒在巷子裡。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drunk</b> is the past participle of . (drink)的過去分詞","examples":[]}]}]},"dose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一劑，一服；一次，一點；花柳病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……服藥；摻入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dose</b> <b>of</b> medicine or a drug is a measured amount of it which is intended to be taken at one time. 一次用量","examples":["One dose of penicillin can wipe out the infection. 一劑青黴素即可消除感染。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dose</b> a person or animal <b>with</b> medicine, you give them an amount of it. 給 (藥)","examples":["The doctor fixed the rib, dosed him heavily with drugs, and said he would probably get better. 醫生給他固定好肋骨後，又給他服了大劑量的藥，說他可能會好起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dose up</b> means the same as . 給 (藥)","examples":["I dosed him up with Valium. 我給他服了安定。"]}]}]},"earnings":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薪水，工資，收入；利潤，收益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>earnings</b> are the sums of money that you earn by working. 薪金","examples":["Average weekly earnings rose by 1.5% in July. 平均週薪7月份上漲了1.5%。"]}]}]},"drip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"滴下，滴出；含有，充滿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水滴，滴液；滴水聲，滴落；（醫用）滴注器；笨蛋，懦夫，平庸乏味者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When liquid <b>drips</b> somewhere, or you <b>drip</b> it somewhere, it falls in individual small drops. 使滴下; 滴下","examples":["Blood dripped from the corner of his mouth. 血從他嘴角滴下來。","Amid the trees the sea mist was dripping and moisture formed on Tom's glasses. 樹林中海霧正滴著，水氣蒙上了湯姆的眼鏡片。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>drips</b>, drops of liquid fall from it. 滴下","examples":["A tap in the kitchen was dripping. 廚房的水龍頭在滴水。","Lou was dripping with perspiration. 盧汗流浹背。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is dripping with</b> a particular thing, you mean that it contains a lot of that thing. 充滿; 佈滿","examples":["They were dazed by window displays dripping with diamonds and furs. 他們被佈滿鑽石和毛皮的櫥窗展示弄得眼花繚亂。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drip</b> is a small individual drop of a liquid. 滴","examples":["Drips of water rolled down the trousers of his uniform. 水珠從他的制服褲子上滾下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drip</b> is a piece of medical equipment by which a liquid is slowly passed through a tube into a patient's blood. 滴注器","examples":["He was put on intravenous drip to treat his dehydration. 他打點滴來治療脫水。"]}]}]},"edition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"版本，版次；一集，一期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>edition</b> is a particular version of a book, magazine, or newspaper that is printed at one time. 版本","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>edition</b> is the total number of copies of a particular book or newspaper that are printed at one time. 版次","examples":["The second edition was published only in Canada. 第2版只在加拿大出版。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>edition</b> is a single television or radio programme that is one of a series about a particular subject. 集","examples":["...an interview featured on last week's edition of \"60 Minutes.\" …一次以上週那集《60分鐘》節目為主的訪談。"]}]}]},"due":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"到期的，預期的；應有的，應得的；應付的，應給的；適當的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"正對著"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"應得，所得；會費"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event is <b>due to</b> something, it happens or exists as a direct result of that thing. 是…的結果","examples":["The country's economic problems are largely due to the weakness of the recovery. 該國的經濟問題很大程度上是復甦乏力的結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say <b>due to</b> to introduce the reason for something happening. Some speakers of English believe that it is not correct to use <b>due to</b> in this way. 由於","examples":["Due to the large volume of letters he receives Dave regrets he is unable to answer queries personally. 由於收到的來信數量太多，戴夫很遺憾不能親自回覆各種詢問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something will happen or take place <b>in due course</b>, you mean that you cannot make it happen any quicker and it will happen when the time is right for it. 在適當的時候","examples":["In due course the baby was born. 嬰兒如期降生了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can say \"<b>to give</b> him his <b>due</b>,\" or \"<b>giving</b> him his <b>due</b>,\" when you are admitting that there are some good things about someone, even though there are things that you do not like about them. 給某人應得的評價","examples":["To give Linda her due, she had tried to encourage John in his school work. 為琳達說句公道話，她曾盡力在學習方面鼓勵約翰。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say \"<b>with due respect</b>\" when you are about to disagree politely with someone. 請恕冒昧; 斗膽","examples":["With all due respect I submit to you that you're asking the wrong question. 恕我斗膽直言，我認為您在問錯誤的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>due</b> at a particular time, it is expected to happen, be done, or arrive at that time. 預期的","examples":["The results are due at the end of the month. 結果預期於月底揭曉。","Mr. Carter is due in Washington on Monday. 卡特先生預計週一到達華盛頓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Due</b> attention or consideration is the proper, reasonable, or deserved amount of it under the circumstances. 適當的; 應有的","examples":["After due consideration it was decided to send him away to live with foster parents. 經過充分考慮，決定將他送去與養父母生活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>due</b>, or that is <b>due</b> <b>to</b> someone, is owed to them, either as a debt or because they have a right to it. 應得的","examples":["I was sent a cheque and advised that no further pension was due. 我收到了一張支票並被告知不再有應領的養老金了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>due for</b> something, that thing is planned to happen or be given to them now, or very soon, often after they have been waiting for it for a long time. (經長久等待後) 預期發生的","examples":["Although not due for release until 2001, he was let out of his low-security prison to spend a weekend with his wife. 雖然要等到2001年才能獲釋，他卻被允許離開看守寬鬆的監獄去和妻子共度一個週末。"]}]}]},"drain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）排出，濾幹；喝光，喝乾；使勞累，使疲憊；（使）逐漸消失；使降低，消耗；（通常指因驚嚇或疾病而臉色）變蒼白；漂亮地完成（投籃、射門等）；將（球）輕擊入穴"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"下水道，排水管；流失，消耗；（將體內液體排走的）導管，引流管；（場效應電晶體的）漏極；使人疲倦的事物，負擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>drain</b> a liquid from a place or object, you remove the liquid by causing it to flow somewhere else. If a liquid <b>drains</b> somewhere, it flows there. 使流走; 流走","examples":["Miners built the tunnel to drain water out of the mines. 礦工們開掘了隧道以將水排出礦井。","Now the focus is on draining the water. 現在的焦點是排水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>drain</b> a place or object, you dry it by causing water to flow out of it. If a place or object <b>drains</b>, water flows out of it until it is dry. 排幹; 流乾","examples":["The authorities have mobilized vast numbers of people to drain flooded land and build or repair dikes. 當局動員了大批民眾為遭受洪災的地區排澇並修建或修復堤壩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>drain</b> food or if food <b>drains</b>, you remove the liquid that it has been in, especially after it has been cooked or soaked in water. 使瀝乾; 瀝乾","examples":["Drain the pasta well, arrange on four plates and pour over the sauce. 把義大利麵條瀝乾水，擺放在4個盤子裡，倒上調味品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If the colour or the blood <b>drains</b> or <b>is drained</b> <b>from</b> someone's face, they become very pale. You can also say that someone's face <b>drains</b> or <b>is drained</b> <b>of</b> colour. 使 (色澤) 消退; (色澤) 消退","examples":["Harry felt the colour drain from his face. 亨利感到臉上沒有了血色。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>drains</b> you, it leaves you feeling physically and emotionally exhausted. 使心力交瘁","examples":["My emotional turmoil had drained me. 困惑焦灼的情緒使我心力交瘁。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that a country's or a company's resources or finances <b>are drained</b>, you mean that they are used or spent completely. 耗盡 (資源、資金)","examples":["The state's finances have been drained by drought and civil disorder. 國家財政已經被旱災和內亂消耗殆盡了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"使心力交瘁的","examples":["I began to suffer from headaches, which left me feeling completely drained. 我開始感到頭痛，它使我感到精疲力竭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drain</b> is a pipe that carries water or sewage away from a place, or an opening in a surface that leads to the pipe. 排水管; 下水道; 排水溝","examples":["Tony built his own house and laid his own drains. 託尼蓋了自己的房子,鋪設了自己的排水管道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a</b> <b>drain</b> <b>on</b> an organization's finances or resources, you mean that it costs the organization a large amount of money, and you do not think that it is worth it. (資源、資金的) 外流; 消耗","examples":["...an ultramodern printing plant, which has been a big drain on resources. …一個消耗大量資源的超級現代化印刷廠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is going</b> <b>down the drain</b>, you mean that it is being destroyed or wasted. 被破壞掉; 被浪費掉","examples":["They were aware that their public image was rapidly going down the drain. 他們意識到自己的公眾形象正被迅速地破壞掉。"]}]}]},"dump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"丟棄，扔掉；亂堆，亂放；丟下，拋棄；分手，甩掉；傾銷，拋售；轉儲，轉存（計算機資料）；（尤指系統發生故障後記憶體的）列印輸出，卸出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"垃圾場；廢料堆場；（金礦開採作業堆積而成的）礦山廢石堆；<非正式>髒地方；軍需品臨時存放處；轉存；<美，非正式>拉屎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dump</b> something somewhere, you put it or unload it there quickly and carelessly. 扔下; 傾倒","examples":["We dumped our bags at the nearby Grand Hotel and hurried toward the market. 我們把包扔在附近的格蘭德旅館，急匆匆地向市場趕去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is dumped</b> somewhere, it is put or left there because it is no longer wanted or needed. 丟棄","examples":["The getaway car was dumped near the motorway. 那輛逃亡的小汽車被丟棄在高速公路附近。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>dump</b> something such as an idea, policy, or practice means to stop supporting or using it. 拋棄 (念頭、政策或慣例)","examples":["The party dumped the policy of nationalization in favour of the free market. 該黨拋棄了國有化政策，轉而支援自由市場政策。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a firm or company <b>dumps</b> goods, it sells large quantities of them at prices far below their real value, usually in another country, in order to gain a bigger market share or to keep prices high in the home market. 傾銷","examples":["It produces more than it needs, then dumps its surplus onto the world market. 它出產過剩，於是就將過剩的產品傾銷到全球市場。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>dump</b> someone, you end your relationship with them. 拋棄 (某人)","examples":["My heart sank because I thought he was going to dump me for another girl. 想到他將拋棄我去追求另一個女孩，我的心沉了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"To <b>dump</b> computer data or memory means to copy it from one storage system onto another, such as from disk to magnetic tape. 轉儲","examples":["All the data is then dumped into the main computer. 所有的資料接著被轉儲到主計算機中。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傾倒; 丟棄","examples":["German law forbids the dumping of hazardous waste on German soil. 德國法律禁止在德國國土上倒棄危險廢棄物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dump</b> is a place where rubbish and waste material are left, for example, on open ground outside a town. 垃圾場","examples":["...companies that bring their waste straight to the dump. …將廢棄物直接運到垃圾場的公司。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a place is a <b>dump</b>, you think it is ugly and unpleasant to live in or visit. 骯髒不堪的地方","examples":["\"What a dump!\" Christabel said, standing in the doorway of the youth hostel. 克麗絲特布尓站在青年旅舍的門口說道：“真是個骯髒的地方！”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>dump</b> is a list of the data that is stored in a computer's memory at a particular time. <b>Dumps</b> are often used by computer programmers to find out what is causing a problem with a program. (常用來發現程式問題) 資料轉儲","examples":["...print it out and it'll do a screen dump of what's there. 把它列印出來，它會將所在的資訊進行螢幕轉儲。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"an act of defecation 排便","examples":[]}]}]},"dust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙塵；灰塵；粉末；塵霧；除塵，撣灰；<文>屍骨，遺骸；<文>凡身，肉體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擦去……的灰塵；把粉末撒於；<美，非正式>狠揍，殺死（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dust</b> is very small dry particles of earth or sand. 沙塵","examples":["Tanks raise huge trails of dust when they move. 坦克移動時掀起滾滾的塵土。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dust</b> is the very small pieces of dirt which you find inside buildings, for example, on furniture, floors, or lights. 灰塵","examples":["I could see a thick layer of dust on the stairs. 我能看見樓梯上厚厚的一層灰塵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dust</b> is a fine powder which consists of very small particles of a substance such as gold, wood, or coal. 粉末","examples":["The air is so black with diesel fumes and coal dust, I can barely see. 天空由於充滿柴油機的濃煙和煤灰而如此黑，我幾乎看不見。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>dust</b> something such as furniture, you remove dust from it, usually using a cloth. 去除灰塵","examples":["I vacuumed and dusted and polished the living room. 我把起居室吸了塵、撣了灰並且擦亮了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dust</b> something <b>with</b> a fine substance such as powder or if you <b>dust</b> a fine substance <b>onto</b> something, you cover it lightly with that substance. 用 (粉狀物) 擦塗; 把 (粉狀物) 撒於","examples":["Lightly dust the fish with flour. 輕輕地把魚撒上面粉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>has bitten the dust</b>, you are emphasizing that it no longer exists or that it has failed. 不復存在; 失敗","examples":["In the last 30 years many cherished values have bitten the dust. 過去30年裡許多值得珍惜的價值觀已經不復存在。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something will happen when <b>the dust settles</b>, you mean that a situation will be clearer after it has calmed down. If you let <b>the dust settle</b> before doing something, you let a situation calm down before you try to do anything else. 塵埃落定","examples":["Once the dust had settled Beck defended his decision. 一旦塵埃落定，貝克就為自己的決定進行了辯護。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is gathering dust</b>, you mean that it has been left somewhere and nobody is using it or doing anything with it. 閒置","examples":["Many of the machines are gathering dust in basements. 很多的機器閒置在地下室裡。"]}]}]},"editor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"編輯；記者；剪輯師；編輯程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is the person who is in charge of a newspaper or magazine and who decides what will be published in each edition of it. 主編","examples":["Her father was the former editor of the Saturday Review. 她的父親是《星期六評論》的前任主編。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a journalist who is responsible for a particular section of a newspaper or magazine. 欄目編輯","examples":["Mike later became the sports editor for The Beacon. 邁克後來成為《烽火》的體育欄目編輯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a person who checks and corrects texts before they are published. 編輯","examples":["Your role as editor is important, for you can look at a piece of writing objectively. 你作為編輯的角色是重要的，因為你可以客觀地看一篇文字。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a radio or television journalist who reports on a particular type of news. 廣播或電視記者","examples":["...our economics editor, Tom Goldberg. …我們的經濟節目記者，湯姆·戈德堡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a person who prepares a film, or a radio or television programme, by selecting some of what has been filmed or recorded and putting it in a particular order. 剪輯師","examples":["A few years earlier, she had worked at 20th Century Fox as a film editor. 幾年前，她曾是20世紀福克斯公司的一名電影剪輯師。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a person who collects pieces of writing by different authors and prepares them for publication in a book or a series of books. (書籍、叢書) 主編","examples":["Michael Rosen is the editor of the anthology. 邁克爾·羅森是該文集的主編。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"An <b>editor</b> is a computer program that enables you to change and correct stored data. 編輯程式","examples":["To edit it, you need to run the built-in Windows Registry editor. 要編輯，就需要啟動內建的視窗註冊編輯程式。"]}]}]},"echo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"回聲，迴音，餘音繞樑；重複，附和，共鳴；相似之處，再現；回聲插入；（話語結構和內容的）重複；（橋牌）回聲訊號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迴響，發出回聲；重複，附和"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>echo</b> is a sound caused by a noise being reflected off a surface such as a wall. 回聲","examples":["He listened and heard nothing but the echoes of his own voice in the cave. 他聽了聽，除了自己聲音在山洞裡的迴響什麼都沒聽見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A detail or feature that reminds you of something else can be referred to as an <b>echo</b>. 啟示","examples":["The accident has echoes of past disasters. 該事故讓人想到過去的那些災難。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a sound <b>echoes</b>, it is reflected off a surface and can be heard again after the original sound has stopped. 迴響","examples":["His feet echoed on the hardwood floor. 他的腳步聲在硬木地板上回響著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a place that <b>echoes</b>, a sound is reflected off a surface, and is repeated after the original sound has stopped. 發出回聲","examples":["The room echoed. 房間發出了回聲。","The corridor echoed with the barking of a dozen dogs. 走廊裡迴盪著十幾條狗的吠聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>echoes</b>, it continues to be discussed and remains important or influential in a particular situation or among a particular group of people. 流傳","examples":["The old fable continues to echo down the centuries. 這一古老的寓言流傳了數個世紀。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>echo</b> someone's words, you repeat them or express agreement with their attitude or opinion. 附和","examples":["Their views often echo each other. 他們的見解常常彼此附和。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>echoes</b> another, the first is a copy of a particular detail or feature of the other. 反映","examples":["Pinks and beiges were chosen to echo the colours of the ceiling. 粉色和米色被選來反映天花板的那些顏色。"]}]}]},"elbow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肘，肘部；彎處，肘狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用肘推擠，用肘擊打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>elbow</b> is the part of your arm where the upper and lower halves are joined. 肘","examples":["He slipped and fell, badly bruising an elbow. 他滑倒了，嚴重挫傷了一隻胳膊肘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>elbow</b> people <b>aside</b> or <b>elbow</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you push people with your elbows in order to move somewhere. (用肘部) 推","examples":["They also claim that the security team elbowed aside a steward. 他們還聲稱治安隊把一名乘務員推到了一邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>elbows</b> their <b>way</b> somewhere, or <b>elbows</b> other people or things <b>out of the way</b>, they achieve success by being aggressive and determined. (用肘部) 擠","examples":["Non-state firms gradually elbow aside the inefficient state-owned ones. 非國有企業逐漸排擠掉了那些低效率的國有企業。"]}]}]},"election":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選舉；當選；選舉權；上帝的選拔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>election</b> is a process in which people vote to choose a person or group of people to hold an official position. 選舉","examples":["...Poland's first fully free elections for more than fifty years. …五十多年來波蘭首次完全自由選舉。","During his election campaign he promised to put the economy back on its feet. 在競選活動期間他承諾要重振經濟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>election</b> of a particular person or group of people is their success in winning an election. 當選","examples":["...the election of the Democrat candidate last year. …去年民主黨候選人的當選。","...Vaclav Havel's election as president of Czechoslovakia. …瓦茨拉夫·哈維爾當選捷克斯洛伐克總統。"]}]}]},"electricity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電，電流，電力；強烈感情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Electricity</b> is a form of energy that can be carried by wires and is used for heating and lighting, and to provide power for machines. 電","examples":["We moved into a cabin with electricity but no running water. 我們搬進了一間有電但是沒有自來水的小木屋。"]}]}]},"emperor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"皇帝；（北美的）麗蝶，皇蝶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emperor</b> is a man who rules an empire or is the head of state in an empire. 皇帝","examples":["...the emperor of Japan. …日本天皇。"]}]}]},"employee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僱員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>employee</b> is a person who is paid to work for an organization or for another person. 僱員","examples":["He is an employee of Fuji Bank. 他是富士銀行的一位僱員。"]}]}]},"employer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僱主"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>employer</b> is the person or organization that you work for. 僱主","examples":["He had been sent to Rome by his employer. 他被僱主派到羅馬去了。"]}]}]},"emergency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"突發事件，緊急情況；急症病人，急診病人；<美>（醫院的）急診室"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"緊急情況下的；應急的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emergency</b> is an unexpected and difficult or dangerous situation, especially an accident, that happens suddenly and that requires quick action to deal with it. 突發事件; 緊急情況","examples":["He deals with emergencies promptly. 他迅速地應對突發事件。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emergency</b> action is one that is done or arranged quickly and not in the normal way, because an emergency has occurred. 緊急的","examples":["Yesterday, the centre's board held an emergency meeting. 昨天，中心的董事會召開了一次緊急會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Emergency</b> equipment or supplies are those intended for use in an emergency. 應急的","examples":["The plane is carrying emergency supplies for refugees. 這架飛機載著給難民的應急物資。"]}]}]},"employment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僱用；使用，利用；工作，就業；就業人數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Employment</b> is the fact of having a paid job. 工作","examples":["She was unable to find employment. 她沒能找到工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Employment</b> is the fact of employing someone. 僱用","examples":["...the employment of children under nine. …9歲以下兒童的僱用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Employment</b> is the work that is available in a country or area. 就業","examples":["...economic policies designed to secure full employment. …為確保充分就業而制定的經濟政策。"]}]}]},"engagement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"婚約，訂婚；約會，約定；交戰，戰鬥；演出任務；聘用，僱用；參加，從事；(與……的)密切關係，(對……的)瞭解；齧合；（與……的）密切關係，（對……的）瞭解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>engagement</b> is an arrangement that you have made to do something at a particular time. 約會","examples":["He had an engagement at a restaurant at eight. 他8點鐘在一家餐館有一個約會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>engagement</b> is an agreement that two people have made with each other to get married. 訂婚約定","examples":["I've broken off my engagement to Arthur. 我已經解除了於阿瑟的訂婚約定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the period of time during which two people are engaged as their <b>engagement</b>. 訂婚時期","examples":["We spoke every night during our engagement. 我們訂婚期間每晚都交談。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A military <b>engagement</b> is an armed conflict between two enemies. 交戰","examples":["The constitution prohibits them from military engagement on foreign soil. 憲法禁止他們在外國領土上的軍事交戰。"]}]}]},"engine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發動機，引擎；機車，火車頭；專用裝備，器械；工具，手段；驅動力，推動力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>engine</b> of a car or other vehicle is the part that produces the power which makes the vehicle move. 引擎","examples":["He got into the driving seat and started the engine. 他坐上駕駛座椅，發動了引擎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>engine</b> is also the large vehicle that pulls a train. 機車","examples":["In 1941, the train would have been pulled by a steam engine. 1941年，火車可能已由蒸汽機車來牽引了。"]}]}]},"excellence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傑出，卓越；<古>優點，美德"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something has the quality of <b>excellence</b>, they are extremely good in some way. 優秀; 卓越","examples":["...the top award for excellence in journalism and the arts. …新聞與藝術界的最高傑出獎。"]}]}]},"engineer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工程師，設計師；（航班）機械師，（輪船）輪機長；技師，機修工；工兵；機車司機，火車司機；責任人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設計，建造；策劃，精心安排；改變……的基因(或遺傳)結構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>engineer</b> is a person who uses scientific knowledge to design, construct, and maintain engines and machines or structures such as roads, railroads, and bridges. 工程師","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>engineer</b> is a person who repairs mechanical or electrical devices. 維修師","examples":["They send a service engineer to fix the disk drive. 他們派一位維修師來修理磁碟驅動器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>engineer</b> is a person who is responsible for maintaining the engine of a ship while it is at sea. 輪機師","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a vehicle, bridge, or building <b>is engineered</b>, it is planned and constructed using scientific methods. 設計製造","examples":["Its spaceship was engineered by Bert Rutan, renowned for designing the Voyager. 它的飛船由伯特·魯坦設計建造，此人因設計“旅行者”號飛船而聞名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>engineer</b> an event or situation, you arrange for it to happen, in a clever or indirect way. 策劃","examples":["His family believe that his murder was engineered by a business rival. 他的家人認為他的死是由一位商業競爭對手一手策劃的。"]}]}]},"envy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"羨慕，忌妒；嚮往，渴望（別人的東西）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"妒忌，羨慕；令人羨慕的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Envy</b> is the feeling you have when you wish you could have the same thing or quality that someone else has. 羨慕","examples":["Gradually he began to acknowledge his feelings of envy towards his mother. 漸漸地他開始承認自己對母親的羨慕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a thing or quality is <b>the envy of</b> someone, they wish very much that they could have or achieve it. 羨慕之處","examples":["Their economy is the envy of the developing world. 他們的經濟令發展中國家羨慕。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>envy</b> someone, you wish that you had the same things or qualities that they have. 羨慕","examples":["I don't envy the young ones who've become TV superstars and know no other world. 我不羨慕那些成為電視超級明星而對其他世界一無所知的年輕人。"]}]}]},"entry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"進入，加入；出場，蒞臨；門，入口；進入權，進入許可；參賽；參賽作品，競賽答題；參賽人數，報名人數；登記，錄入；條目，賬目，記錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you gain <b>entry</b> <b>to</b> a particular place, you are able to go in. 進入許可","examples":["You can gain entry to the club only through a member. 你只有透過一位會員才能進入該俱樂部。","Entry to the museum is free. 這座博物館免費參觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's arrival in a place as their <b>entry</b>, especially when you think that they are trying to be noticed and admired. 駕到; 蒞臨","examples":["He made his triumphal entry into Mexico City. 他勝利進入了墨西哥城。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>entry</b> <b>into</b> a particular society or group is their joining of it. 加入","examples":["...China's entry into the World Trade Organization. …中國的入世。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>entry</b> in a diary, account book, computer file, or reference book is a short piece of writing in it. (日記中的) 簡短記錄; (賬簿中的) 賬目; (計算機文件或參考書中的) 條目","examples":["Violet's diary entry for April 20, 1917 records Brigit admitting to the affair. 維奧莉特1917年4月20日的日記簡短記錄著布里吉特承認此事。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>entry</b> <b>for</b> a competition is a piece of work, a story or drawing, or the answers to a set of questions, which you complete in order to take part in the competition. 參賽作品; 參賽答卷","examples":["The closing date for entries is December 31. 參賽作品提交的截止日期是12月31日。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Journalists sometimes use <b>entry</b> to refer to the total number of people taking part in an event or competition. For example, if a competition has an <b>entry</b> of twenty people, twenty people take part in it. 參加總人數","examples":["Our competition has attracted a huge entry. 我們的比賽已吸引了大量參賽者。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Entry</b> in a competition is the act of taking part in it. 參加","examples":["Entry to this competition is by invitation only. 此次競賽的參賽只憑邀請函。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>entry</b> <b>to</b> a place is the way into it, for example a door or gate. 入口","examples":["...the towering marble archway that marked the entry to the Pelican Point development. …標誌著鵜鶘頂開發區入口的、高聳的大理石拱門。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>No Entry</b> is used on signs to indicate that you are not allowed to go into a particular area or go through a particular door or gate. 禁止入內","examples":[]}]}]},"evil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"惡毒的，邪惡的；有害的，易造成傷害的；討厭的，令人不舒服的；惡魔的，不祥的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有害（或不受歡迎）的事；邪惡，罪惡；壞事，惡行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Evil</b> is a powerful force that some people believe to exist, and that causes wicked and bad things to happen. 惡; 邪惡","examples":["There's always a conflict between good and evil in his plays. 他的戲劇中總是有善與惡的衝突。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Evil</b> is used to refer to all the wicked and bad things that happen in the world. 惡行","examples":["He could not, after all, stop all the evil in the world. 他畢竟不能阻止世上所有的惡行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to an <b>evil</b>, you mean a very unpleasant or harmful situation or activity. 不愉快的事; 有害的事","examples":["Higher taxes may be a necessary evil. 提高稅率雖不是件令人愉快的事，但可能是必要的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>evil</b>, you mean that they are very wicked by nature and take pleasure in doing things that harm other people. 邪惡的; 兇惡的","examples":["...the country's most evil terrorists. …該國最兇惡的恐怖分子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>evil</b>, you mean that you think it causes a great deal of harm to people and is morally bad. 傷天害理的","examples":["A judge yesterday condemned heroin as evil. 一名法官昨天譴責海洛因傷天害理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>evil</b>, you mean that you think it is influenced by the devil. 受惡魔影響的","examples":["I think this is an evil spirit at work. 我想這是惡魔在作祟。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have two choices, but think that they are both bad, you can describe the less bad one as <b>the lesser of two evils</b>, or <b>the</b> <b>lesser evil</b>. 兩害之中的輕者","examples":["People voted for him as the lesser of two evils. 人們投票選他只是出於兩害相權取其輕罷了。"]}]}]},"exhibition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"展覽，展出；表現，展示；<美>表演賽；<英>獎學金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>exhibition</b> is a public event at which pictures, sculptures, or other objects of interest are displayed, for example at a museum or art gallery. 展覽會","examples":["...an exhibition of expressionist art. …一場印象主義藝術展覽會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>exhibition of</b> a particular skilful activity is a display or example of it that people notice or admire. (技能的) 展示","examples":["He responded in champion's style by treating the fans to an exhibition of power and speed. 他回報以冠軍的風格，為仰慕者們呈現了一次力量與速度的展示。"]}]}]},"existence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"存在，實有；生存，生活，生活方式；<古>存在物，實體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>existence</b> of something is the fact that it is present in the world as a real thing. 存在","examples":["...the existence of other galaxies. …其他星系的存在。","Public worries about accidents are threatening the very existence of the nuclear power industry. 公眾對事故的擔心正威脅著核電工業的生存。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's way of life as an <b>existence</b>, especially when they live under difficult conditions. (尤指困境中的) 生活方式","examples":["You may be stuck with a miserable existence for the rest of your life. 你的餘生可能會陷入悲慘的生活。"]}]}]},"escape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逃跑，逃脫；逃避，擺脫；避開，避免（疾病或受傷等）；洩露，逸出；不自覺地說出；被遺忘，被忽略；去度假；退出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"逃跑，逃離；逃避現實，暫時解脫；漏出，逸出；Esc退出鍵；度假；逃跑工具，逃跑方法；野化的植物（或寵物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>escape</b> <b>from</b> a place, you succeed in getting away from it. 逃走","examples":["A prisoner has escaped from a jail in northern Texas. 一名囚犯已經從北德克薩斯州的一個監獄逃走。","They are reported to have escaped to the other side of the border. 據報道他們已經逃過了邊境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When gas, liquid, or heat <b>escapes</b>, it comes out from a pipe, container, or place. 漏出; 逸出","examples":["Leave a vent open to let some moist air escape. 讓一個排氣口開著以便讓一些溼氣逸出。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>escape</b> is the act of escaping from a particular place or situation. 逃脫","examples":["The man made his escape. 那個人逃走了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Escape</b> is also a noun. 逃脫","examples":["I hear you had a very narrow escape on the bridge. 我聽說你在橋上勉強逃過一難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is an <b>escape</b>, it is a way of avoiding difficulties or responsibilities. 逃避現實的方法","examples":["But for me television is an escape. 但對我而言，電視是個逃避現實的方法。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say that you <b>escape</b> when you survive something such as an accident. 逃脫","examples":["The two officers were extremely lucky to escape serious injury. 那兩名官員非常幸運地逃過了嚴重傷害。","The man's girlfriend managed to escape unhurt. 那人的女友成功逃脫了，沒有受傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>escapes</b> you or <b>escapes</b> your attention, you do not know about it, do not remember it, or do not notice it. 被忘掉; 被忽視","examples":["It was an actor whose name escapes me for the moment. 那是個我一時想不起名字的演員。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>escape</b> to describe things that allow you to avoid difficulties or problems. For example, an <b>escape route</b> is an activity or opportunity that lets you improve your situation. An <b>escape clause</b> is part of an agreement that allows you to avoid having to do something that you do not want to do. 逃避的","examples":["We all need the occasional escape route from the boring, routine aspects of our lives. 我們都需要偶爾地逃避生活中的無聊和平淡。"]}]}]},"expectation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"期待，預期；期望，指望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>expectations</b> are your strong hopes or beliefs that something will happen or that you will get something that you want. 期盼","examples":["Their hope, and their expectation, was that she was going to be found safe and that she would be returned to her family. 他們的希望和期盼是她被找到時安全無恙並被送回她家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>expectations</b> are strong beliefs they have about the proper way someone should behave or something should happen. 期望","examples":["Stephen Chase had determined to live up to the expectations of the company. 斯蒂芬·蔡斯已決心不辜負公司的期望。"]}]}]},"exit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出口，通道，太平門；（車輛駛出公路的）出路；離去；退出；<文>去世，死亡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"退出（電腦程式）；退場（劇本里的舞臺指示）；<文>去世，死亡；攤牌讓分；離去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>exit</b> is the door through which you can leave a public building. 出口","examples":["He picked up the case and walked toward the exit. 他提起箱子朝出口走去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>exit</b> on a motorway is a place where traffic can leave it. (公路的) 出口","examples":["She continued to the next exit, got off the motorway and pulled into a parking lot. 她繼續開到下個出口，出了公路，駛入一個停車場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>exit</b>, you are referring to the way that they left a room or building, or the fact that they left it. 離場","examples":["I made a hasty exit and managed to open the gate. 我匆忙離場，設法開啟了大門。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>exit</b>, you are referring to the way that they left a situation or activity, or the fact that they left it. 退場; 退出","examples":["It's her earliest exit from Wimbledon since going out in the opening round in 1997. 這是她自1997年首輪出局以來最早一次從溫布林頓網球賽出局。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Exit</b> is also a noun. 退出","examples":["Press Exit to return to your document. 按“退出”鍵返回到你的文件。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>exit</b> from a room or building, you leave it. 離開","examples":["She exits into the tropical storm. 她走出去，進入熱帶風暴。","As I exited the final display, I entered a hexagonal room. 走出最後一個展覽我便進入了一間六角形的房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>exit</b> a computer program or system, you stop running it. 退出","examples":["I can open other applications without having to exit WordPerfect. 我可以在不退出的情況下開啟其他應用程式。"]}]}]},"exchange":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交換，互換；短暫的交談，爭吵；交戰，交火；兌換，匯兌；交流，互訪；交易所；（商品的）調換；電話局，電話交換臺；換子，兌子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"調換，更換；交流，交談；交換，互換；兌換，交易"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more people <b>exchange</b> things of a particular kind, they give them to each other at the same time. 交換","examples":["We exchanged addresses. 我們交換了地址。","The two men exchanged glances. 那兩個人交換了眼神。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exchange</b> is also a noun. 交換","examples":["He ruled out any exchange of prisoners with the militants. 他拒絕考慮與好戰分子交換囚犯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>exchange</b> is a brief conversation, usually an angry one. 短暫的交談; 爭吵","examples":["There've been some bitter exchanges between the two groups. 兩組之間有過些激烈的爭吵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>exchange</b> <b>of</b> fire, for example, is an incident in which people use guns or missiles against each other. 交火","examples":["There was an exchange of fire during which the gunman was wounded. 發生了一場交火，其間那名槍手受傷了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>exchange</b> is an arrangement in which people from two different countries visit each other's country, to strengthen links between them. 交流","examples":["...a series of sporting and cultural exchanges with Seoul. …與首爾的一系列體育和文化交流。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>exchange</b> something, you replace it with a different thing, especially something that is better or more satisfactory. 調換; 更換","examples":["...the chance to sell back or exchange goods. …回售或調換貨物的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do or give something <b>in exchange</b> <b>for</b> something else, you do it or give it in order to get that thing. 作為交換","examples":["It is illegal for public officials to solicit gifts or money in exchange for favours. 公務員以提供便利來索取禮物或金錢作為交換是非法的。"]}]}]},"experiment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"實驗，試驗；嘗試，實踐"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進行實驗，做試驗；試，嘗試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>experiment</b> is a scientific test done in order to discover what happens to something in particular conditions. 實驗","examples":["The astronauts are conducting a series of experiments to learn more about how the body adapts to weightlessness. 那些宇航員正在進行一系列實驗，以便更多地瞭解人體如何適應失重狀態。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"實驗","examples":["...the ethical aspects of animal experimentation. …動物實驗的倫理視角。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>experiment</b> is the trying out of a new idea or method in order to see what it is like and what effects it has. 嘗試","examples":["As an experiment, we bought Ted a watch. 作為嘗試，我們給特德買了塊手錶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"嘗試","examples":["Decentralization and experimentation must be encouraged. 權力下放和嘗試必須予以鼓勵。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>experiment with</b> something or <b>experiment on</b> it, you do a scientific test on it in order to discover what happens to it in particular conditions. 做實驗","examples":["In 1857 Mendel started experimenting with peas in his monastery garden. 1857年孟德爾開始在其修道院菜園裡用豌豆做實驗。","The scientists have experimented on the tiny neck arteries of rats. 那些科學家已在老鼠細小的頸動脈上做了實驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>experiment</b> means to try out a new idea or method to see what it is like and what effects it has. 嘗試","examples":["...if you like cooking and have the time to experiment. …如果你喜歡烹飪並且有時間嘗試的話。"]}]}]},"export":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"出口；傳播，輸出；（在計算機中）匯出，輸出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"出口，輸出；出口物，輸出品；出口量，出口收入"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"出口的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>export</b> products or raw materials means to sell them to another country. 出口","examples":["The nation also exports beef. 該國也出口牛肉。","They expect the antibiotic products to be exported to Southeast Asia and Africa. 他們期望抗生素產品出口到東南亞和非洲。","The company now exports to Japan. 該公司現在對日本出口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>export</b> something means to introduce it into another country or make it happen there. 引入他國","examples":["It has exported inflation at times. 它有時將通貨膨脹引入他國。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In computing, if you <b>export</b> files or information from one type of software into another type, you change their format so that they can be used in the new software. 匯出 (檔案、資訊)","examples":["Files can be exported in ASCII or PCX formats. 檔案可用ASCII或PCX格式匯出。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Export</b> is also a noun. 出口","examples":["...the production and export of cheap casual wear. …廉價休閒服的生產與出口。","A lot of our land is used to grow crops for export. 我們很多的土地用來種植出口作物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Exports</b> are goods sold to another country and sent there. 出口品","examples":["Ghana's main export is cocoa. 迦納的主要出口產品是可可。"]}]}]},"expense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代價，費用；業務費用，報銷（expenses）；需要花錢的東西，花銷的東西"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>把……記入費用賬戶；向……收取費用；被花掉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Expense</b> is the money that something costs you or that you need to spend in order to do something. 花費","examples":["He's bought a big TV at vast expense so that everyone can see properly. 他花了很多錢買了臺大電視，這樣人人都可以看清楚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Expenses</b> are amounts of money that you spend while doing something in the course of your work, which will be paid back to you afterwards. (由僱主報銷的工作) 開支","examples":["Her airfare and hotel expenses were paid by the committee. 她乘飛機及住酒店的費用由該委員會支付了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>at</b> someone's <b>expense</b>, they provide the money for it. 由…付費","examples":["Should architects continue to be trained for five years at public expense? 建築師繼續受訓5年應由公眾付費嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone laughs or makes a joke <b>at</b> your <b>expense</b>, they do it to make you seem foolish. 捉弄 (某人)","examples":["I think he's having fun at our expense. 我看他是在拿咱們尋開心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you achieve something <b>at the expense of</b> someone, you do it in a way that might cause them some harm or disadvantage. 以犧牲 (某人的利益) 為代價","examples":["According to this study, women have made notable gains at the expense of men. 根據這項研究，女性以犧牲男性的利益為代價而取得了顯著收益。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>at the expense of</b> another thing, you are expressing concern that they are not doing the second thing, because the first thing uses all their resources. 以犧牲 (某物) 為代價","examples":["The orchestra has more discipline now, but at the expense of spirit. 該管絃樂隊現在更有紀律了，但卻犧牲了士氣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>go to</b> <b>the</b> <b>expense</b> <b>of</b> doing something, you do something that costs a lot of money. If you <b>go to</b> great <b>expense</b> <b>to</b> do something, you spend a lot of money in order to achieve it. 花大錢 (做某事)","examples":["Why go to the expense of buying an electric saw when you can borrow one? 你能借到電鋸，卻為何去花錢買呢？"]}]}]},"fable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寓言；謊言，無稽之談；神話，傳說"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"虛構，撒謊；講寓言，編寓言；煞有介事地講述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fable</b> is a story which teaches a moral lesson. Fables sometimes have animals as the main characters. 寓言","examples":["...the fable of the tortoise and the hare. …烏龜和兔子的寓言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a statement or explanation that is untrue but that many people believe as <b>fable</b>. 謠傳","examples":["Is reincarnation fact or fable? 轉世投胎是事實還是謠傳？"]}]}]},"expression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"表達，表示；表情，神情；（表演、歌唱或演奏時的）情感表現；詞語，措詞；式，表示式；擠壓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>expression</b> <b>of</b> ideas or feelings is the showing of them through words, actions, or artistic activities. 表達","examples":["Laughter is one of the most infectious expressions of emotion. 笑是最具感染力的感情表達方式之一。","...the rights of the individual to freedom of expression. …個人表達自由權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>expression</b> is the way that your face looks at a particular moment. It shows what you are thinking or feeling. 神情","examples":["Levin sat there, an expression of sadness on his face. 萊文坐在那裡，神情憂傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Expression</b> is the showing of feeling when you are acting, singing, or playing a musical instrument. (藝術表演中的) 情感表現","examples":["I think I put more expression into my lyrics than a lot of other singers do. 我認為我比許多其他歌手在歌詞中注入了更多的情感表達。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>expression</b> is a word or phrase. 字詞; 言辭","examples":["She spoke in a quiet voice but used remarkably coarse expressions. 她說話聲音很輕，但使用了非常粗俗的言辭。"]}]}]},"factor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"因素，要素；等級，係數；因數，因子；遺傳因子，基因；（血液中的）凝血因子；代理公司，代理商；<蘇格蘭>地產管理人，管家；測量水平"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……作為因素計入，把……包括在內（factor in）；把……作為因素排除，不把……包括在內（factor out）；將……分解為因子；代理經營，（代管）產業；做代理商"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>factor</b> is one of the things that affects an event, decision, or situation. 因素","examples":["Physical activity is an important factor in maintaining fitness. 體育活動是保持健康的一個重要因素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount increases by <b>a</b> <b>factor</b> <b>of</b> two, for example, or by <b>a</b> <b>factor</b> <b>of</b> eight, then it becomes two times bigger or eight times bigger. 倍數","examples":["The cost of butter quadrupled and bread prices increased by a factor of five. 黃油的價格是原來的4倍，麵包的價格上漲了5倍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>factor</b> to refer to a particular level on a scale of measurement. 係數","examples":["A sunscreen with a protection factor of 30 allows you to stay in the sun without burning. 一種防護係數為30的防曬霜使你能夠待在太陽底下而不被曬傷。"]}]}]},"fairy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"仙子，小精靈；兔子（對男同性戀者的蔑稱）；仙蜂鳥"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"仙女的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fairy</b> is an imaginary creature with magical powers. Fairies are often represented as small people with wings. 仙女","examples":[]}]}]},"extreme":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極大的，極度的；極端的，嚴重的；過分的，偏激的；盡頭的，末端的；極限的，從事極限運動的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（觀點或行為方式的）極端；（事物的）極度；端頂，端詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Extreme</b> means very great in degree or intensity. 極大的","examples":["The girls were afraid of snakes and picked their way along with extreme caution. 那些女孩們害怕蛇，一路極其謹慎地看好每一步走。","...people living in extreme poverty. …活在極度貧窮中的人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>extreme</b> to describe situations and behaviour that are much more severe or unusual than you would expect, especially when you disapprove of them because of this. 過激的","examples":["The extreme case was Poland, where 29 parties won seats. 過激的案例是波蘭，那裡有29個政黨獲得席位。","It is hard to imagine Jesse capable of anything so extreme. 很難想像傑西能做這樣過激的事情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>extreme</b> to describe opinions, beliefs, or political movements that you disapprove of because they are very different from those that most people would accept as reasonable or normal. 偏激的","examples":["This extreme view hasn't captured popular opinion. 這種偏激的觀點還沒有贏得大眾的認同。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>extreme</b> end or edge of something is its farthest end or edge. 極遠的 (端、邊緣)","examples":["...the room at the extreme end of the corridor. …走廊最盡頭的房間。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>extremes</b> to refer to situations or types of behaviour that have opposite qualities to each other, especially when each situation or type of behaviour has such a quality to the greatest degree possible. 極端","examples":["...a \"middle way\" between the extremes of success and failure, wealth and poverty. …成功與失敗、富裕與貧窮兩個極端之間的“中道”。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person <b>goes to extremes</b> or <b>takes</b> something <b>to extremes</b>, they do or say something in a way that people consider to be unacceptable, unreasonable, or foolish. (行動、說話) 走極端","examples":["The police went to the extremes of installing the most advanced safety devices in the man's house. 警察走了極端，在這個人的房屋裡安裝了最先進的安全裝置。"]}]}]},"faith":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信任，信心，信念；宗教；宗教信仰；忠誠"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<愛爾蘭>用以表示驚訝或強調千真萬確"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>faith</b> <b>in</b> someone or something, you feel confident about their ability or goodness. 信心","examples":["People have lost faith in the government. 人們已失去了對政府的信心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Faith</b> is strong religious belief in a particular God. 宗教信仰","examples":["Umberto Eco's loss of his own religious faith is reflected in his novels. 翁貝託·埃科宗教信仰的喪失在他的小說當中得到了反映。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>faith</b> is a particular religion, for example, Christianity, Buddhism, or Islam. 宗教","examples":["England shifted officially from a Catholic to a Protestant faith in the 16th century. 英格蘭在16世紀正式從信仰天主教改信新教。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in good faith</b>, you seriously believe that what you are doing is right, honest, or legal, even though this may not be the case. 真心實意地","examples":["This report was published in good faith but we regret any confusion which may have been caused. 發表這份報告出自誠意，但是我們對可能引發的任何混亂而感到遺憾。"]}]}]},"fanatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狂熱入迷者，狂熱愛好者；狂熱分子，盲信者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狂熱的；盲信的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>fanatic</b>, you disapprove of them because you consider their behaviour or opinions to be very extreme, for example, in the way they support particular religious or political ideas. 狂熱分子","examples":["I am not a religious fanatic but I am a Christian. 我不是個宗教狂熱分子，但我是個基督徒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>fanatic</b>, you mean that they are very enthusiastic about a particular activity, sport, or way of life. 入迷者","examples":["Both Rod and Phil are football fanatics. 羅德和菲爾兩人都是足球迷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fanatic</b> means the same as . 狂熱的","examples":[]}]}]},"faucet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>水龍頭，旋塞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>faucet</b> is a device that controls the flow of a liquid or gas from a pipe or container. Sinks and baths have faucets attached to them. 龍頭; 閥門; 旋塞","examples":[]}]}]},"fare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交通費用；乘客；飯菜；常見的東西；供大眾使用的東西（尤指娛樂活動）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進展，表現；<古> 發生，結果；<古>出遊，旅行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fare</b> is the money that you pay for a trip that you make, for example, in a bus, train, or taxi. 車費","examples":["He could barely afford the fare. 他幾乎付不起車費。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>fares</b> well or badly, you are referring to the degree of success they achieve in a particular situation or activity. 進展","examples":["It is unlikely that the marine industry will fare any better in September. 海運業不大可能在9月份有所好轉。"]}]}]},"fan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風扇，扇子；粉絲，狂熱愛好者；扇形；（使風車頭迎風的）風葉；（山坡腳下的）地帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扇，為……扇風；煽（火）；煽動，激起；（擊球手）三擊不中出局；（呼吸，微風）吹拂；驅散，扇走；<美>擊球不中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are a <b>fan</b> of someone or something, especially a famous person or a sport, you like them very much and are very interested in them. 狂熱愛好者","examples":["If you're a Billy Crystal fan, you'll love this film. 如果你是比利·克里斯特爾的影迷，你就會喜歡這部電影。","I am a great fan of rave music. 我是個狂歡音樂的狂熱樂迷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fan</b> is a piece of electrical or mechanical equipment with blades that go around and around. It keeps a room or machine cool or gets rid of unpleasant smells. 風扇","examples":["He cools himself in front of an electric fan. 他在一個電扇前面吹涼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>fan</b> is a flat object that you hold in your hand and wave in order to move the air and make yourself feel cooler. 扇子","examples":["...hundreds of dancing girls waving peacock fans. …數百名揮動著孔雀扇的舞女。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fan</b> yourself or your face when you are hot, you wave a fan or other flat object in order to make yourself feel cooler. 給…扇風","examples":["She would have to wait in the truck, fanning herself with a piece of cardboard. 她只得在卡車裡等候，用一塊紙板給自己扇風。"]}]}]},"fate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"命運"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"註定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fate</b> is a power that some people believe controls and decides everything that happens, in a way that cannot be prevented or changed. You can also refer to <b>the fates</b>. 命運","examples":["I see no use arguing with fate. 我認為與命運抗爭沒有什麼用。","...the fickleness of fate. …命運的變化無常。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's or thing's <b>fate</b> is what happens to them. 命運; 遭遇","examples":["The Russian Parliament will hold a special session later this month to decide his fate. 俄羅斯議會本月晚些時候將舉行一次特別會議來決定他的命運。","He seems for a moment to be again holding the fate of the country in his hands. 有那麼一刻他似乎又把國家的命運掌握在自己手中。"]}]}]},"faint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"模糊的，微弱的；微小的，可能性不大的；虛弱的，頭暈目眩的；不熱情的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"暈倒，昏厥"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"昏厥；<古>變得微弱，衰落；變得沒有氣力"}],"sections":[]},"fax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳真機；傳真信件；傳真"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳真（文件、信件等）；用傳真與（某人）聯絡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fax</b> or a <b>fax machine</b> is a piece of equipment used to copy documents by sending information electronically along a telephone line, and to receive copies that are sent in this way. 傳真機","examples":["...a modern reception desk with telephone and fax. …一個有電話和傳真機的現代化接待臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a copy of a document that is transmitted by a fax machine as a <b>fax</b>. 傳真件","examples":["I sent him a long fax, saying I didn't need a maid. 我發給他一份長長的傳真，說我不需要女傭。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fax</b> a document to someone, you send it from one fax machine to another. 發傳真","examples":["I faxed a copy of the agreement to each of the investors. 我給每位投資者都傳真了一份協議副本。","Did you fax him a reply? 你發傳真給他答覆了嗎？"]}]}]},"fake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偽造的，冒充的；（動作或感情）虛假的，做作的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"假貨，贗品；騙子，冒充者；假動作；（繩索、水龍帶等的）一圈（=flake）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"偽造，冒充；假裝，佯裝；（尤指體育運動中）做假動作；不懂裝懂，不會裝會；盤卷（=flake）"}],"sections":[]},"fashion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時髦打扮，流行裝扮；時尚，時興；（做事的）方式；時裝領域，時尚界"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指用手工）製作，使成形；塑造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fashion</b> is the area of activity that involves styles of clothing and appearance. 時尚界","examples":["There are 20 full-colour pages of fashion for men. 有20張男士時尚動態的全綵頁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fashion</b> is a style of clothing or a way of behaving that is popular at a particular time. 時尚","examples":["In the early seventies I wore false eyelashes, as was the fashion. 70年代初我戴假睫毛，那是當時的時尚。","The demand for perfume resulted in a fashion for fancy scent bottles. 對香水的需求使別緻的香水瓶成為一種時尚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>in</b> a particular <b>fashion</b> or <b>after</b> a particular <b>fashion</b>, you do it in that way. 方式","examples":["There is another drug called DHE that works in a similar fashion. 另有一種叫作二氫埃託啡的藥作用相似。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in fashion</b>, it is popular and approved of at a particular time. If it is <b>out of fashion</b>, it is not popular or approved of. 流行/過時","examples":["That sort of house is back in fashion. 那種房子又時興起來了。"]}]}]},"feather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羽毛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用羽毛裝飾；長羽毛；使（螺旋槳）順流交距；使（旋翼）週期變距；（划船）平掠回（槳）；如羽毛般浮動（或移動、飄動）；小心翼翼地把……混合起來（或把……弄平）；（油墨、口紅等抹上後）化開，變模糊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A bird's <b>feathers</b> are the soft covering on its body. Each <b>feather</b> consists of a lot of smooth hairs on each side of a thin stiff centre. 羽毛","examples":["...a hat that she had made herself from black ostrich feathers. …她用黑色鴕鳥羽毛為自己做的一頂帽子。"]}]}]},"fancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式> 喜歡，想要；<英，非正式> 愛戀，愛慕；<英，非正式> 認為……會成功（贏）；<文> 認為，想象；<英，非正式>自負，自命不凡（fancy oneself）；<英> （表示驚奇或震驚）真想不到，竟然；愛戀，愛慕（常用於英式口語中）； <英，非正式>喜歡，想要（常用於英式口語中）；<英，非正式>愛戀，愛慕（常用於英式口語中）；<英，非正式>認為……會成功（贏）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜歡，想要；想象，想象力，想象的事物；<舊> （無根據的）想法，空想；花色小蛋糕；（賽馬或其他體育比賽中）最被看好的人（或動物）；<舊> 喜愛的人（或事物）；（16和17世紀音樂用語）幻想曲；（無根據的）想法，空想"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"時髦的，奢華的；華麗的，花哨的；複雜的，高難度的；（食品）特級的，優質的；嫻熟的，巧妙的；（花）雜色的；（動物）供觀賞的；（畫，雕塑）憑想像創作的，想像出來的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>fancy</b>, you mean that it is special, unusual, or elaborate, for example because it has a lot of decoration. 別緻的","examples":["The magazine was packaged in a fancy plastic case with attractive graphics. 這本雜誌裝在一個帶有漂亮圖紋的別緻塑膠盒子裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>fancy</b>, you mean that it is very expensive or of very high quality, and you often dislike it because of this. 闊氣的","examples":["My parents sent me to a fancy private school. 我父母把我送到了一所闊氣的私立學校。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fancy</b> <b>yourself as</b> a particular kind of person or fancy <b>yourself</b> doing a particular thing, you like the idea of being that kind of person or doing that thing. 認為 (自己)","examples":["So you fancy yourself as the boss someday? 那麼你認為自己有一天會成老闆？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>fancies</b> <b>themselves as</b> a particular kind of person, you mean that they think, often wrongly, that they have the good qualities which that kind of person has. (自) 認為是","examples":["She fancies herself a bohemian. 她自命為一個放蕩不羈的藝術家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fancy</b> something, you want to have it or to do it. 想要","examples":["I just fancied a drink. 我只是想要杯飲料。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>fancy</b> someone, you feel attracted to them, especially in a sexual way. 愛慕","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>fancy</b>\" or \"<b>fancy that</b>\" when you want to express surprise or disapproval. (表示驚訝或反對) 真沒想到","examples":["\"Fancy that!\" smiled Conti. “真沒想到！” 康蒂笑著說。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take a fancy to</b> someone or something, you start liking them, usually for no understandable reason. (通常指沒有道理的) 愛上","examples":["Sylvia took quite a fancy to him. 西爾維婭完全愛上了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>takes</b> your <b>fancy</b> or <b>tickles</b> your <b>fancy</b>, you like it a lot when you see it or think of it. 中某人的意","examples":["She makes most of her own clothes, copying any fashion which takes her fancy. 她大部分的衣服是模仿中意的時裝自己做的。"]}]}]},"firework":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"煙火，煙花；焰火表演（fireworks）；（憤怒等情緒的）爆發，（才智、活力的）展現（fireworks）；精彩難忘的演出（或作品）（fireworks）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fireworks</b> are small objects that are lit to entertain people on special occasions. They contain chemicals and burn brightly or attractively, often with a loud noise, when you light them. 煙花","examples":["They drank champagne, set off fireworks and tooted their car horns. 他們喝香檳、放煙花，還按他們的車喇叭。"]}]}]},"fist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拳，拳頭；抓住，抓牢；<非正式>手跡，筆跡；指標參見號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用拳頭打；握成拳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your hand is referred to as your <b>fist</b> when you have bent your fingers in toward the palm in order to hit someone, to make an angry gesture, or to hold something. 拳頭","examples":["Angry protestors with clenched fists shouted their defiance. 憤怒的抗議者們緊握拳頭高聲抗議。"]}]}]},"flea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"跳蚤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flea</b> is a very small jumping insect that has no wings and feeds on the blood of humans or animals. 跳蚤","examples":[]}]}]},"flavor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"味道，滋味；口味，風味；情味，特色，氣息；（對某事物的）初步感受；香料，調味料，香精"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"給……調味，加味於；為……增添風味（或趣味）"}],"sections":[]},"feature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特點，特徵；五官，面貌（特徵）；地貌；特寫，專題節目；正片； 特點，特徵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以……為特色，以……為主要組成；起重要作用，佔重要地位；放映，上演；擔任主演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>feature</b> <b>of</b> something is an interesting or important part or characteristic of it. 特點","examples":["Patriotic songs have long been a feature of Kuwaiti life. 愛國歌曲長期以來一直是科威特人生活的一個特點。","The spacious gardens are a special feature of this property. 寬敞的花園是這處房產的一大特色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>feature</b> is a special article in a newspaper or magazine, or a special programme on radio or television. (報紙、雜誌的) 特寫; (廣播、電視的) 特別節目","examples":["We are delighted to see the Sunday Times running a long feature on breast cancer. 我們高興地看到《星期日泰晤士報》刊登了關於乳腺癌的一篇長長的特寫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>feature</b> or a <b>feature</b> film or movie is a full-length film about a fictional situation, as opposed to a short film or a documentary. 正片; 故事片","examples":["...the first feature-length cartoon, Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs. …第一部故事片長度的卡通片《白雪公主和七個小矮人》。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A geographical <b>feature</b> is something noticeable in a particular area of country, for example, a hill, river, or valley. (地理) 特徵","examples":["...one of the area's oddest geographical features - an eight-mile bank of pebbles shelving abruptly into the sea. …這個地區最奇怪的地理特徵之一，一條8英里長的鵝卵石堤岸陡然傾斜伸到海里。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>features</b> are your eyes, nose, mouth, and other parts of your face. 容貌","examples":["His features seemed to change. 他的容貌似乎變了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as a film or exhibition <b>features</b> a particular person or thing, they are an important part of it. (電影等) 由…主演; (展覽會等) 以…為重點","examples":["It's a great film and it features a Spanish actor who is going to be a world star within a year. 那是一部精彩的電影，它由一位西班牙演員主演，他一年之內就會成為國際明星。","The hour-long programme will be updated each week and feature highlights from recent games. 這個一小時的節目將每週更新，重點介紹近期比賽的精彩部分。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>features</b> <b>in</b> something such as a show, exhibition, or magazine, they are an important part of it. 擔任主演; 是 (展覽、雜誌等) 的重要內容","examples":["Jon featured in one of the show's most thrilling episodes. 喬恩主演了該劇中最驚悚的幾集之一。"]}]}]},"file":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資料夾（或箱、櫃等）；（計算機的）文件；檔案；縱列；銼刀；（與某政策領域相關的）議題，職責"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（把檔案等）歸檔，存檔；提起（訴訟），提出（申請）；傳送（訊息或報道）給報社；列隊行進；銼平"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>file</b> is a box or a folded piece of heavy paper or plastic in which letters or documents are kept. 檔案盒; 資料夾","examples":["...a file of insurance papers. …一個保險單資料夾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>file</b> is a collection of information about a particular person or thing. 卷宗","examples":["We already have files on people's tax details. 我們已經有了人們付稅詳情的卷宗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In computing, a <b>file</b> is a set of related data that has its own name. 檔案","examples":["Be sure to save the revised version of the file under a new filename. 確保將改過的檔案版本另存在一個新的檔名下。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>file</b> is a hand tool which is used for rubbing hard objects to make them smooth, shape them, or cut through them. 銼刀","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>file</b> a document, you put it in the correct file. 使歸檔","examples":["They are all filed alphabetically under author. 它們都是在作者一欄下面按字母順序來歸檔的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>file</b> a formal or legal accusation, complaint, or request, you make it officially. 提起","examples":["I filed for divorce on the grounds of adultery a few months later. ，我幾個月後以通姦為由提起了離婚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>files</b> a report or a news story, they send or give it to their employer. 提交","examples":["He had to rush back to the office and file a housing story before the secretaries went home. 他不得不趕回辦公室，在秘書們回家之前提交一份有關住房的報道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>file</b> an object, you smooth it, shape it, or cut it with a file. 銼","examples":["Manicurists are skilled at shaping and filing nails. 美甲師對修剪、銼光指甲很在行。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to march or walk in a file or files 排成縱隊行進","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A group of people who are walking or standing <b>in single file</b> or <b>single file</b> are in a line, one behind the other. 成單行","examples":["We were walking in single file to the lake. 我們排成單行走向湖邊。"]}]}]},"flame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火焰，火舌；強烈的感情，激情；含辱罵內容的電子郵件；<非正式>戀人，情人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"燃燒；（感情）爆發；（因激動而）變紅；傳送辱罵資訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flame</b> is a hot bright stream of burning gas that comes from something that is burning. 火焰","examples":["The heat from the flames was so intense that roads melted. 火焰的熱度如此高以至於路面融化了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>flame</b> is an e-mail message which severely criticizes or attacks someone. 攻擊性電子郵件","examples":["The best way to respond to a flame is to ignore it. 回應攻擊性電子郵件的最好方式就是置之不理。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flame</b> is also a verb. 傳送攻擊性電子郵件","examples":["Ever been flamed? 收到過攻擊性電子郵件嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>bursts into flames</b> or <b>bursts into flame</b>, it suddenly starts burning strongly. 突然猛烈燃燒起來","examples":["She managed to scramble out of the vehicle as it burst into flames. 她設法從突然起火的車裡爬了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>in flames</b> is on fire. 著火","examples":["I woke to a city in flames. 我醒來時看到一座燃燒著的城市。"]}]}]},"flock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鳥或羊等動物）群；一大群人；（某個教堂的）會眾，全體教徒；（填充墊子的）絮屑，毛棉填料；（植絨用的）短絨，絨屑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"群集，蜂擁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flock</b> <b>of</b> birds, sheep, or goats is a group of them. 一群 (鳥或羊等)","examples":["They kept a small flock of sheep. 他們養了一小群綿羊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people or things as a <b>flock of</b> them to emphasize that there are a lot of them. 一群; 一批 (人或物)","examples":["These cases all attracted flocks of famous writers. 這些案例均吸引了大批知名作家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a body of Christians regarded as the pastoral charge of a priest, a bishop, the pope, etc 基督徒的一個機構，視為一個牧師、一個主教，教皇等的牧區","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a tuft, as of wool, hair, cotton, etc 一簇","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"very small tufts of wool applied to fabrics, wallpaper, etc, to give a raised pattern 織物或牆紙等凸起的小簇毛絨","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>flock</b> <b>to</b> a particular place or event, a very large number of them go there, usually because it is pleasant or interesting. 雲集於","examples":["The public has flocked to the show. 公眾蜂擁而去看那場演出。","The criticisms will not stop people flocking to see the film. 這些批評阻止不了湧向看這部影片的人潮。"]}]}]},"forehead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"前額"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>forehead</b> is the area at the front of your head between your eyebrows and your hair. 前額","examples":["...the lines on her forehead. …她前額上的皺紋。"]}]}]},"flesh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或動物的）肉；（人體的）皮膚；果肉；肉體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使充實，使具體（flesh out）；<文>激起……的殺性，使投入血戰；刮掉（皮上的）肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flesh</b> is the soft part of a person's or animal's body between the bones and the skin. 肉","examples":["...the pale pink flesh of trout and salmon. …鱒魚和鮭魚粉白色的肉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>flesh</b> to refer to human skin and the human body, especially when you are considering it in a sexual way. 肌膚; 肉體","examples":["...the warmth of her flesh. …她肌膚的溫暖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>flesh</b> of a fruit or vegetable is the soft inside part of it. 果肉; 蔬菜的可食部分","examples":["Cut the flesh from the olives and discard the stones. 切下橄欖的果肉，扔掉果核。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>flesh and blood</b> to emphasize that someone has human feelings or weaknesses, often when contrasting them with machines. 血肉之軀","examples":["I'm only flesh and blood, like anyone else. 我只是血肉之軀，跟其他人一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is your <b>own flesh and blood</b>, you are emphasizing that they are a member of your family. 親骨肉","examples":["The kid, after all, was his own flesh and blood. He deserved a second chance. 這個孩子畢竟是他的親骨肉，他應該得到再一次機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>makes</b> your <b>flesh creep</b> or <b>makes</b> your <b>flesh crawl</b>, it makes you feel disgusted, shocked or frightened. 使厭惡; 使心驚肉跳","examples":["It makes my flesh creep to think of it. 一想起它我就心驚肉跳。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you meet or see someone <b>in the flesh</b>, you actually meet or see them, rather than, for example, seeing them in a film or on television. 本人","examples":["The first thing viewers usually say when they see me in the flesh is \"You're smaller than you look on TV.\" 觀眾見到我本人時常說的第一句話往往是“你比在電視上看上去矮小一些”。"]}]}]},"follower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"追隨者，擁護者；信徒；（社交媒體）粉絲，關注者；屬下，下級，隨從；（機械/電子）從動件，隨動件，跟隨器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>follower</b> of a particular person, group, or belief is someone who supports or admires this person, group, or belief. 追隨者","examples":["...followers of the Zulu Inkatha movement. …祖魯印卡加運動的追隨者。"]}]}]},"folk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人們；家人，雙親；民間音樂；諸位，大夥兒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"民俗的，傳統的；流傳民間的，普通百姓的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to people as <b>folk</b> or <b>folks</b>. 人","examples":["Country folk can tell you that there are certain places which animals avoid. 鄉下人會告訴你有些地方動物是不去的。","These are the folks from the local TV station. 這些是從當地電視臺來的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to your close family, especially your mother and father, as your <b>folks</b>. 家人","examples":["I've been avoiding my folks lately. 我最近一直在避開家人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>folks</b> as a term of address when you are talking to several people. 各位","examples":["\"It's a question of money, folks,\" I said. “這是錢的問題，各位。”我說道。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Folk</b> is also a noun. 民間 (音樂)","examples":["...a variety of music including classical and folk. …包括古典音樂和民間音樂在內的各種音樂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Folk</b> art and customs are traditional or typical of a particular community or nation. 民間的","examples":["...South American folk art. …南美民間藝術。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Folk</b> music is music which is traditional or typical of a particular community or nation. 民間的 (音樂)","examples":[]}]}]},"fountain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噴泉；噴射；天然泉；源泉；（紋章）銀藍相間波狀紋圓盾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"噴射，噴流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fountain</b> is an ornamental feature in a pool or lake which consists of a long narrow stream of water that is forced up into the air by a pump. 噴泉","examples":["...the fountains on the 16th Street Mall. …第16街商業區的噴泉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fountain</b> <b>of</b> a liquid is an amount of it which is sent up into the air and falls back. 噴射","examples":["The volcano spewed a fountain of molten rock 650 feet in the air. 這座火山噴射出的熔岩高達650英尺。"]}]}]},"float":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）漂浮，（使）浮動；輕盈走動，飄然移動；提出（想法或計劃）；發行（股票）上市；使（貨幣匯率）自由浮動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"彩車；魚漂，浮子；（學游泳用的）浮板；<美，非正式>頂端加冰激凌的飲料；<英，非正式>（商店的）備用零錢；（公司股票）上市，開始發行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is floating</b> in a liquid, they are in the liquid, on or just below the surface, and are being supported by it. You can also <b>float</b> something on a liquid. 漂浮","examples":["They noticed fifty and twenty dollar bills floating in the water. 他們注意到水中漂浮著一些50和20美元的紙幣。","It's below freezing and small icebergs are floating by. 氣溫在冰點以下，一座座小冰山正漂過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>float</b> a project, plan, or idea, you suggest it for others to think about. 提出","examples":["The French had floated the idea of placing the diplomatic work in the hands of the UN. 法國人提出了將外交工作交由聯合國處理的意見。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a company director <b>floats</b> their company, they start to sell shares in it to the public. 使 (公司) 上市","examples":["He floated his firm on the stock market. 他讓自己的公司上市了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a government <b>floats</b> its country's currency or allows it to <b>float</b>, it allows the currency's value to change freely in relation to other currencies. 使 (貨幣) 自由浮動","examples":["On January 15th Brazil was forced to float its currency. 1月15日巴西被迫讓其貨幣自由浮動。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>floats</b> lies on or just below the surface of a liquid when it is put in it and does not sink. (在水面或水中) 漂浮","examples":["They will also float if you drop them in the water. 如果你把它們丟進水裡，它們也會浮起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>floats</b> in or through the air hangs in it or moves slowly and gently through it. (在空中) 飄浮","examples":["The white cloud of smoke floated away. 那團白色的煙霧飄走了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>float</b> is a light object that is used to help someone or something float. 救生圈","examples":["Floats will provide confidence in the water. 救生圈可以增強在水中的信心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>float</b> is a small object attached to a fishing line which floats on the water and moves when a fish has been caught. 浮子; 魚漂","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>float</b> is a truck on which displays and people in special costumes are carried in a parade. 遊行彩車","examples":["...a procession of makeshift floats bearing loudspeakers and banners. …臨時代用的裝有高音喇叭、掛有橫幅的遊行彩車佇列。"]}]}]},"fortune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時運，命運；好運，機遇；財富，鉅款；未來，前途"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給予財富；偶然發生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a large sum of money as <b>a</b> <b>fortune</b> or <b>a</b> small <b>fortune</b> to emphasize how large it is. 大筆錢","examples":["He made a small fortune in the property boom. 他在房地產繁榮期發了一小筆財。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>fortune</b> has a very large amount of money. 很大數額的錢","examples":["He made his fortune in car sales. 他在汽車銷售中發了財。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fortune</b> or good <b>fortune</b> is good luck. Ill <b>fortune</b> is bad luck. 好運; 運氣","examples":["Investors are starting to wonder how long their good fortune can last. 投資者們開始懷疑他們的好運還能持續多久。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you talk about someone's <b>fortunes</b> or the <b>fortunes</b> of something, you are talking about the extent to which they are doing well or being successful. 運勢","examples":["The company had to do something to reverse its sliding fortunes. 該公司不得不採取措施來逆轉其下滑的運勢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>tells</b> your <b>fortune</b>, they tell you what they think will happen to you in the future, which they say is shown, for example, by the lines on your hand. 算命","examples":["I was just going to have my fortune told by a gypsy. 我正要去找一個吉普賽人給我算命。"]}]}]},"fold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"摺疊，對摺；倒閉，垮掉；交叉，交疊；包，裹；擁抱；拌入；認輸；抽筋，雙腿發軟；使（岩石層）形成褶皺；（尤指運動員或運動隊）突然不在狀態（或發揮失常）；把（牲畜）圈在欄中"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"褶，褶皺；摺疊；志趣相同的人；山窪，山谷；羊圈；岩層褶皺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fold</b> something such as a piece of paper or cloth, you bend it so that one part covers another part, often pressing the edge so that it stays in place. 摺疊","examples":["He folded the paper carefully. 他小心地把那張紙折起來。","Fold the omelette in half. 把煎蛋對摺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a piece of furniture or equipment <b>folds</b> or if you can <b>fold</b> it, you can make it smaller by bending or closing parts of it. 翻折","examples":["The back of the bench folds forward to make a table. 長椅的靠背可向前翻折成一張桌子。","This portable seat folds flat for easy storage. 這張行動式座椅可折平，便於存放。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fold</b> your arms or hands, you bring them together and cross or link them, for example, over your chest. 交疊 (雙臂或雙手)","examples":["Meer folded his arms over his chest and turned his head away. 米爾把雙臂交疊在胸前，扭開頭去。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fold up</b> means the same as . fold up同fold","examples":["When not in use it folds up out of the way. 不用的時候，它折起來不會擋路。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to mix (a whisked mixture) with other ingredients by gently turning one part over the other with a spoon (將被攪拌過的混合物)拌入 (Also fold in)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fold</b> in a piece of paper or cloth is a bend that you make in it when you put one part of it over another part and press the edge. 摺痕","examples":["Make another fold and turn the ends together. 再折一次，然後把兩端疊在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>folds</b> in a piece of cloth are the curved shapes which are formed when it is not hanging or lying flat. 褶皺","examples":["The priest fumbled in the folds of his gown. 這位牧師胡亂地整了整長袍上的褶皺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a small enclosure or pen for sheep or other livestock, where they can be gathered (圈養羊等其他家畜的)小圍欄","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the sheep or other livestock gathered in such an enclosure (羊等其他家畜)聚集於小圍欄裡","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a flock of sheep 羊群","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a herd of Highland cattle 一群高地牛群","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a church or the members of it 一個教會; 教會成員","examples":[]}]}]},"friendship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"友誼，朋友關係；友情，友好；（國家或政府之間的）友好關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>friendship</b> is a relationship between two or more friends. 友誼","examples":["Giving advice when it's not called for is the quickest way to end a good friendship. 在不需要時給予建議是了結一段友誼的最快方式。","She struck up a close friendship with Desiree during the week of rehearsals. 她在那一週的排練中和德西蕾建立起親密的友誼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Friendship</b> is a relationship between two countries in which they help and support each other. 友好關係","examples":["The president set the targets for the future to promote friendship with East Europe. 總統確定了與東歐增進友好關係的未來目標。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>friendship</b> to refer in a general way to the state of being friends, or the feelings that friends have for each other. 友情","examples":["...a hobby which led to a whole new world of friendship and adventure. …一個通向友情和冒險的一個全新世界的愛好。"]}]}]},"gallon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加侖（液量單位，英制合 4.55 升，美製合 3.79 升）；<非正式>大量液體（gallons of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gallon</b> is a unit of measurement for liquids that is equal to eight pints or 3.785 litres. 加侖 (液體計量單位，合八品脫或3.785升)","examples":["...80 million gallons of water a day. …一天8千萬加侖水。"]}]}]},"fry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"油煎，油炸；<非正式>（人）被曬傷；<非正式>（被）以電刑處死，坐電椅"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>炸薯條（=french fry）；魚苗，魚秧；油煎食品；<英>炒雜碎；<美>油炸食品聚餐會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>fry</b> food, you cook it in a pan that contains hot fat or oil. 炸","examples":["Fry the breadcrumbs until golden brown. 把這些麵包屑炸到金褐色為止。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to kill or be killed by electrocution, esp in the electric chair (用電椅)殺死; (被電椅)殺死","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act of preparing a mixed fried dish or the dish itself 炒雜燴菜","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fries</b> are the same as . 同French fries","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the young of various species of fish 魚苗","examples":[]}]}]},"furniture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傢俱；裝置；慣常的見解；貯藏物，內容；步槍底託；（排版用的）大空鉛，填空材料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Furniture</b> consists of large objects such as tables, chairs, or beds that are used in a room for sitting or lying on or for putting things on or in. 傢俱","examples":["Each piece of furniture in their home suited the style of the house. 他們家的每件傢俱都與房子的風格相稱。"]}]}]},"fur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某些動物的）軟毛，柔毛；毛皮，裘皮；毛皮衣服，皮草；<英> 水垢，水鹼；舌苔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"積垢，生苔；透過插木條使（地板，牆面木料）齊平；用某種毛皮覆蓋（或製成）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fur</b> is the thick and usually soft hair that grows on the bodies of many mammals. (哺乳動物身上的) 毛","examples":["This creature's fur is short, dense and silky. 這種動物的毛短、濃密且柔順。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fur</b> is an artificial fabric that looks like fur and is used, for example, to make clothing, soft toys, and seat covers. (用以製造服裝、軟玩具、座套等的) 人造毛","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fur</b> is the fur-covered skin of an animal that is used to make clothing or small carpets. (動物的) 毛皮","examples":["She had on a black coat with a fur collar. 她穿著一件有毛皮領子的黑色外套。","...the trading of furs from Canada. …與加拿大的毛皮貿易。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>fur</b> is a coat made from real or artificial fur, or a piece of fur worn around your neck. 毛皮外套; 毛皮圍脖","examples":["There were women in furs and men in comfortable overcoats. 有身穿毛皮外套的女人們和身穿舒適大衣的男人們。"]}]}]},"fund":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基金，專款；資金，錢款；基金會；儲備量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"資助，為……提供資金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Funds</b> are amounts of money that are available to be spent, especially money that is given to an organization or person for a particular purpose. (尤指為特定目的而給予某組織的) 資金","examples":["The concert will raise funds for research into AIDS. 這場音樂會將為艾滋病研究籌集資金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fund</b> is an amount of money that is collected or saved for a particular purpose. (為特定目的而籌集或保留的) 專項資金","examples":["...a scholarship fund for undergraduate engineering students. …一筆用於工程學本科生的獎學金專項資金。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or organization <b>funds</b> something, they provide money for it. 資助","examples":["The Bush Foundation has funded a variety of faculty development programmes. 布什基金會已經資助了各種教職工發展專案。","The airport is being privately funded by a construction group. 該機場正由一建築集團私家資助。"]}]}]},"garlic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大蒜；大蒜頭；用於有相似氣味的植物名中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Garlic</b> is the small, white, round bulb of a plant that is related to the onion plant. Garlic has a very strong smell and taste and is used in cooking. 大蒜","examples":["...a clove of garlic. …一瓣大蒜。"]}]}]},"gamble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"冒險假設；賭博；冒險，投機"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"冒險，賭博"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gamble</b> is a risky action or decision that you take in the hope of gaining money, success, or an advantage over other people. 冒險","examples":["Yesterday, he named his cabinet and took a big gamble in the process. 昨天他冒了很大的風險任命了他的內閣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gamble</b> <b>on</b> something, you take a risky action or decision in the hope of gaining money, success, or an advantage over other people. 冒險; 以…為賭注","examples":["Few firms will be willing to gamble on new products. 很少有公司願意在新產品上冒險。","They are not prepared to gamble their careers on this matter. 他們沒準備為此事拿自己的事業來當賭注。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>gamble</b> an amount of money, you bet it in a game such as cards or on the result of a race or competition. People who <b>gamble</b> usually do it frequently. (紙牌、比賽等) 賭博","examples":["Most people visit Las Vegas to gamble their hard-earned money. 多數人去拉斯維加斯是為了用他們辛苦賺來的錢賭博。","John gambled heavily on the horses. 約翰在這幾匹馬上下了大賭注。"]}]}]},"freeze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"結冰；凍住；冷藏，冷凍；感到很冷，凍僵；突然停止，呆住；使（物價或工資等）固定不動；凍結（錢財）；使定格；（計算機螢幕因系統故障）被暫時鎖定"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"凍結；停止；冰凍期；霜凍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid or a substance containing a liquid <b>freezes</b>, or if something <b>freezes</b> it, it becomes solid because of low temperatures. 結冰","examples":["If the temperature drops below 0°C, water freezes. 如果溫度降到攝氏零度以下，水就會結冰。","The ground froze solid. 地面凍硬了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>freeze</b> something such as food, you preserve it by storing it at a temperature below freezing point. You can also talk about how well food <b>freezes</b>. 冷藏","examples":["You can freeze the soup at this stage. 你此時可以把湯冷藏。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the government or a company <b>freeze</b> things such as prices or wages, they state officially that they will not allow them to increase for a fixed period of time. 凍結 (物價或工資)","examples":["They want the government to freeze prices. 他們要政府凍結物價。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>freezes</b> something such as a bank account, fund, or property, they obtain a legal order which states that it cannot be used or sold for a particular period of time. 凍結 (銀行賬戶、基金或財產)","examples":["The governor's action freezes 300,000 accounts. 州長採取行動凍結了30萬個賬戶。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When <b>it freezes</b> outside, the temperature falls below freezing point. 結冰","examples":["What if it rained and then froze all through those months? 如果那幾個月一直下雨然後又結冰該怎麼辦？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>freeze</b>, you feel extremely cold. 感到極冷","examples":["The windows didn't fit at the bottom so for a while we froze even in the middle of summer. 那些窗子的底部關不嚴，所以有段時間我們甚至在仲夏時節也感到極冷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone who is moving <b>freezes</b>, they suddenly stop and become completely still and quiet. 呆住不動","examples":["She froze when the beam of the flashlight struck her. 當手電筒的光柱照到她時，她呆住了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Freeze</b> is also a noun. 冰凍","examples":["The trees were damaged by a freeze in December. 那些樹被12月的一次冰凍凍壞了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Freeze</b> is also a noun. 凍結","examples":["A wage freeze was imposed on all staff earlier this month. 本月早些時候，所有員工的工資都被凍結了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Freeze</b> is also a noun. 凍結","examples":["...a freeze on private savings. …對私人儲蓄的凍結。"]}]}]},"gang":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（青少年的）幫派，團伙；犯罪團伙；一群（體力勞動者）；<非正式>一夥（常聚會的朋友）；（安裝在一起的）一套開關，插座（或其他電氣、機械裝置）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成群，結夥；將（電氣裝置或機器）連線，編組"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gang</b> is a group of people, especially young people, who go around together and often deliberately cause trouble. (尤指滋事的青少年的) 團伙","examples":["During the fight with a rival gang he lashed out with his flick knife. 和對立幫派群毆時，他用彈簧刀猛烈攻擊。","Gang members were behind a lot of the violence. 流氓團伙暗中策劃了許多暴力行為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gang</b> is a group of criminals who work together to commit crimes. 犯罪團伙","examples":["Police were hunting for a gang that had allegedly stolen fifty-five cars. 警察正在追捕一個涉嫌偷竊55輛汽車的犯罪團伙。","...an underworld gang. …一個地下犯罪團伙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>gang</b> is a group of friends who frequently meet. (經常聚會的) 一幫朋友","examples":["Come on over, we've got lots of the old gang here. 過來吧，我們這裡有很多老朋友。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>gang</b> is a group of workers who do physical work together. (一) 隊 (一起幹體力活的工人)","examples":["...a gang of labourers. …一群勞工。"]}]}]},"gasoline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>汽油（=gasolene）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gasoline</b> is the same as . 汽油","examples":[]}]}]},"gap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"縫隙，缺口；（時間上的）間隔；空白，缺漏；隔閡，差距"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gap</b> is a space between two things or a hole in the middle of something solid. 缺口; 裂縫","examples":["He pulled the thick curtains together, leaving just a narrow gap. 他把厚厚的窗簾拉到一起，只留了一條窄縫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gap</b> is a period of time when you are not busy or when you stop doing something that you normally do. 間隔期","examples":["There followed a gap of four years, during which William joined the Army. 之後有4年的間隔，期間威廉參軍了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is something missing from a situation that prevents it from being complete or satisfactory, you can say that there is a <b>gap</b>. 缺漏","examples":["The manifesto calls for a greater effort to recruit young scientists to fill the gap left by a wave of retirements expected over the next decade. 該宣告呼籲加大力度招募年輕的科學家，以填補預期未來十年內一波退休高峰所留下的空缺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>gap</b> <b>between</b> two groups of people, things, or sets of ideas is a big difference between them. 差距","examples":["...the gap between rich and poor. …貧富差距。","America's trade gap widened. 美國的貿易差額加大了。"]}]}]},"gesture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手勢，姿勢；姿態，表示"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打手勢，用動作示意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gesture</b> is a movement that you make with a part of your body, especially your hands, to express emotion or information. 手勢","examples":["Sarah made a menacing gesture with her fist. 薩拉用拳頭做了個威脅的手勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gesture</b> is something that you say or do in order to express your attitude or intentions, often something that you know will not have much effect. 姿態; 表示","examples":["He questioned the government's commitment to peace and called on it to make a gesture of good will. 他質疑政府的和平承諾，並呼籲其擺出善意姿態。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gesture</b>, you use movements of your hands or head in order to tell someone something or draw their attention to something. 打手勢; 用動作示意","examples":["I gestured toward the boathouse, and he looked inside. 我朝停船小屋打手勢，他在裡面看了看。"]}]}]},"glory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"光榮，榮譽；（對上帝的）讚頌；壯麗，輝煌；值得稱讚的事，引以為豪的成就；欣喜；天堂的榮耀（或福祉）；（尤指耶穌基督或聖人頭頂的）光環，光輪"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因某事而）欣喜；自豪，得意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glory</b> is the fame and admiration that you gain by doing something impressive. 榮耀","examples":["Walsham had his moment of glory when he won a 20km race. 沃爾沙姆有過贏得20公里賽跑的光榮時刻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>glories</b> are the occasions when they have done something people greatly admire which makes them famous. 輝煌成就","examples":["The album sees them re-living past glories but not really breaking any new ground. 在這張專輯中他們重溫了昔日的輝煌成就，卻沒有任何真正新的突破。"]}]}]},"glance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"一瞥，看一眼；瀏覽；擊中.......後彈開，擦過；反光， 閃爍；（球類運動用語）輕擦，輕抹（球，以調整其方向）；斜擊（球）；提到，影射"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一瞥，很快的一看；（光的）閃爍，閃耀；（板球）斜擊；（鉛、銅或其他金屬的）輝礦類，硫化礦類；<文>（光的）閃爍，閃耀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>glance</b> <b>at</b> something or someone, you look at them very quickly and then look away again immediately. 瞥","examples":["He glanced at his watch. 他看了一下手錶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>glance through</b> or <b>at</b> a newspaper, report, or book, you spend a short time looking at it without reading it very carefully. 瀏覽","examples":["I picked up the phone book and glanced through it. 我拿起電話簿，瀏覽了一下。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glance</b> is a quick look at someone or something. 一瞥","examples":["Trevor and I exchanged a glance. 特雷弗和我相互瞥了一眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any mineral having a metallic lustre, esp a simple sulphide 輝金屬","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you see something <b>at a glance</b>, you see or recognize it immediately, and without having to think or look carefully. 看(一眼就...)","examples":["One could tell at a glance that she was a compassionate person. 一眼就能看出她是一個富有同情心的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is true or seems to be true <b>at first glance</b>, you mean that it seems to be true when you first see it or think about it, but that your first impression may be wrong. 乍一看","examples":["At first glance, organic farming looks much more expensive for the farmer. 乍一看，有機耕作對農民來說似乎昂貴得多。"]}]}]},"gown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女裙服，女禮服；（法官、教師、律師及大學成員穿的）長袍，長外衣；（尤指在醫院穿的）罩衣，外罩；睡衣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使穿長袍，使穿禮服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gown</b> is a dress, usually a long dress, which women wear on formal occasions. (女用) 長禮服","examples":["The new ball gown was a great success. 那件新款長禮服非常成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gown</b> is a loose black garment worn on formal occasions by people such as lawyers and academics. (律師、大學教師等在正式場合穿的) 黑色禮袍","examples":["...an old headmaster in a flowing black gown. …一位身著飄垂黑色禮袍的老校長。"]}]}]},"governor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"州長，省長，總督；理事，董事；<英>主管，機構負責人；<英，非正式>老闆；調速器，調節器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In some systems of government, a <b>governor</b> is a person who is in charge of the political administration of a state, colony, or region. 州長; 總督","examples":["He was governor of Iowa in the late 1970s. 他是20世紀70年代末愛荷華州的州長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>governor</b> is a member of a committee which controls an organization such as a university or a hospital. (學校、醫院等的) 董事","examples":["Wayne Hansen was added to the board of governors at City University, Bellevue. 韋恩•漢森已被增補為貝爾維尤城市大學的董事會成員。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>governor</b> of a prison is the person in charge of it. 監獄長; 看守長","examples":["A new governor took over the prison. 新一任獄長接管了這所監獄。"]}]}]},"gossip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流言蜚語，小道訊息；愛說三道四的人；閒聊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"閒聊，說三道四"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gossip</b> is informal conversation, often about other people's private affairs. (說別人的) 閒話","examples":["He spent the first hour talking gossip. 他頭一個小時盡在說人閒話。","There has been much gossip about the possible reasons for his absence. 關於他缺席的原因已經有多種傳聞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>gossip</b>, you mean that they enjoy talking informally to people about the private affairs of others. 愛講人閒話的人","examples":["He was a vicious gossip. 他是個可惡的饒舌者。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gossip with</b> someone, you talk informally, especially about other people or local events. You can also say that two people <b>gossip</b>. 閒聊","examples":["We spoke, debated, gossiped into the night. 我們交談、爭論、閒聊到夜間。","Eva gossiped with Sarah. 伊娃與薩拉閒聊。"]}]}]},"glow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發出微弱而穩定的光；（臉部或身體）發紅，發熱；喜形於色，容光煥發；發出豔麗色彩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"微弱穩定的光；（臉部或身體發出的）紅潤光澤；興高采烈；金色，紅色；灼熱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glow</b> is a dull, steady light, for example the light produced by a fire when there are no flames. 暗淡的光","examples":["The cigarette's red glow danced about in the darkness. 香菸的紅色暗光在黑暗中閃爍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>glow</b> is a pink colour on a person's face, usually because they are healthy or have been exercising. (臉上的) 紅光","examples":["The moisturizer gave my face a healthy glow that lasted all day. 這種潤膚霜給我臉上帶來了持續整天的一種健康的紅光。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you feel a <b>glow</b> <b>of</b> satisfaction or achievement, you have a strong feeling of pleasure because of something that you have done or that has happened. 喜悅","examples":["Exercise will give you a glow of satisfaction at having achieved something. 體育鍛煉會帶給你一種有所成就的喜悅。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>glows</b>, it produces a dull, steady light. 發出微弱穩定的光","examples":["The night lantern glowed softly in the darkness. 夜燈在黑暗中發出微弱的光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's skin <b>glows</b>, it looks pink because they are healthy or excited, or have been doing physical exercise. (皮膚) 泛出紅光","examples":["Her freckled skin glowed with health again. 她那有雀斑的皮膚又泛起健康的紅色。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>glows</b> <b>with</b> an emotion such as pride or pleasure, the expression on their face shows how they feel. 容光煥發","examples":["The expectant mothers that Amy had encountered positively glowed with pride. 埃米遇見的孕婦們個個臉上都洋溢著幸福和自豪。"]}]}]},"grasshopper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蚱蜢，蝗蟲；小型偵察機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grasshopper</b> is an insect with long back legs that jumps high into the air and makes a high, vibrating sound. 蚱蜢","examples":[]}]}]},"gas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣體；氣體燃料；（手術）麻醉氣；毒氣，瓦斯；汽油；有趣的人（或事）；脹氣，胃氣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用毒氣殺死；閒聊，空談"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gas</b> is a substance like air that is neither liquid nor solid and burns easily. It is used as a fuel for cooking and heating. 煤氣","examples":["Coal is actually cheaper than gas. 煤炭實際上比煤氣便宜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gas</b> is any substance that is neither liquid nor solid, for example oxygen or hydrogen. 氣體","examples":["Helium is a very light gas. 氦是一種很輕的氣體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Gas</b> is a poisonous gas that can be used as a weapon. 毒氣","examples":["The problem was that the exhaust gases contain many toxins. 問題是廢氣含有很多毒素。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Gas</b> is the same as . 汽油","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>gas</b> a person or animal means to kill them by making them breathe poisonous gas. 用毒氣殺死","examples":["Her husband ran a pipe from her car exhaust to the bedroom in an attempt to gas her. 她丈夫將一根管子從她的汽車排氣管匯入臥室，試圖用毒氣殺死她。"]}]}]},"grab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攫取，抓住；（尤指匆忙地）取，吃，喝；霸佔，強奪；利用，抓住（機會）；引人注意，吸引"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"攫取，賺取；抓具，抓鬥；抓取（或截獲、採集）的影象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grab</b> something, you take it or pick it up suddenly and roughly. 抓住","examples":["I managed to grab her hand. 我設法抓住了她的手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grab</b> someone who is walking past, you succeed in getting their attention. 引起…的注意","examples":["Grab that waiter, Mary Ann. 瑪麗•安，叫住那個服務生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>grab</b> someone's attention, you do something in order to make them notice you. 引起 (注意)","examples":["I jumped on the wall to grab the attention of the crowd. 我跳上牆頭以引起眾人的注意。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>grab</b> something such as food, drink, or sleep, you manage to get some quickly. 匆忙地做","examples":["Grab a beer. 快喝杯啤酒吧。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grab at</b> something, you try to grab it. (設法) 抓住","examples":["He was clumsily trying to grab at Alfred's arms. 他正笨手笨腳地試圖抓住艾爾弗雷德的手臂。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grab</b> is also a noun. 抓住","examples":["I made a grab for the knife. 我伸手去抓那把刀。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>up for grabs</b>, it is available to anyone who is interested. 任何人都可競購的","examples":["The famous Ritz hotel is up for grabs for $100 million. 著名的裡茨大飯店出價1億美元供人競購。"]}]}]},"gram":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"克（公制重量單位，1000克等於1公斤）；（用作食物的）鷹嘴豆（或其他豆類植物）；<美，非正式>奶奶，外婆（同 gramma）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gram</b> is a unit of weight. One thousand grams are equal to one kilogram. 克","examples":["A football weighs about 400 grams. 一個足球重約400克。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any of several leguminous plants, such as the beans <b>Phaseolus mungo</b> (<b>black gram</b> or <b>urd</b>) and <b>P. aureus</b> (<b>green gram</b>), whose seeds are used as food in India 豆科植物","examples":[]}]}]},"greenhouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溫室，暖房"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"溫室效應的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>greenhouse</b> is a glass building in which you grow plants that need to be protected from bad weather. 溫室","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Greenhouse</b> means relating to or causing the greenhouse effect. 溫室的; 造成溫室效應的","examples":["...controls on greenhouse emissions. …對溫室氣體排放量的控制。"]}]}]},"graduate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大學畢業生，學士學位獲得者；畢業生"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得學位（尤指學士），大學畢業；畢業（尤指中學）；授予（某人）學位（或畢業文憑等）；（從……）進步到，升級到；按序列或規模安排；（在儀器或容器上）刻度，做標記；逐漸（或逐步）改變（某物，尤指顏色或色調）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（課程、學業）研究生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>graduate</b> is a student who has successfully completed a course at a high school, college, or university. 畢業生","examples":["The top one-third of all high school graduates are entitled to an education at California State University. 全部高中畢業生當中排名前三分之一的有資格到加利福尼亞州立大學學習。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a student <b>graduates</b>, they complete their studies successfully and leave their school or university. 畢業","examples":["When the boys graduated from high school, Ann moved to a small town in Vermont. 男孩們中學畢業後安遷到了佛蒙特州的一座小鎮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>graduate</b> <b>from</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you go from a less important job or position to a more important one. 升遷","examples":["Bruce graduated to chef at the Bear Hotel. 布魯斯晉升為大熊酒店的廚師長。"]}]}]},"grin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"露齒而笑，咧著嘴笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"露齒的笑，咧著嘴笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>grin</b>, you smile broadly. 咧嘴笑","examples":["He grins, delighted at the memory. 想起往事，他咧嘴笑了。","Sarah tried several times to catch Philip's eye, but he just grinned at her. 薩拉幾次試圖吸引菲利普的注意，但他只是對她咧嘴笑笑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grin</b> is a broad smile. 咧嘴笑","examples":["...a big grin on her face. …她臉上一個大大的笑容。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grin and bear it</b>, you accept a difficult or unpleasant situation without complaining because you know there is nothing you can do to make things better. 默默地忍受","examples":["They cannot stand the sight of each other, but they will just have to grin and bear it. 他們看都不想看對方一眼，但又不得不默默忍受。"]}]}]},"grocery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"食品雜貨店，食品雜貨業；食品雜貨（groceries）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grocery</b> or a <b>grocery store</b> is a small shop that sells foods such as flour, sugar, and canned goods. 食品雜貨店","examples":["They run a small grocery store. 他們經營一家小食品雜貨店。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Groceries</b> are foods you buy at a grocery or at a supermarket. 食品雜貨","examples":["...a small bag of groceries. …一小袋食品雜貨。"]}]}]},"grain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"穀物，穀粒；顆粒，細粒；少量；紋理；（表面的）質地，觸感；格令（舊的重量單位，一格令相當於0.065克）；（照片、底片的）顯影顆粒；（用於火箭發動機的）固體推進劑；（皮革或其他類似人工材料的）粗糙面，皺面；（石頭和煤等原料的）解理面，劈理面；<古>（人的）性格，天性；<史>胭脂蟲，胭脂蟲紅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使表面（或紋理）粗糙；成粒狀；（尤指將傢俱或內表面）漆成木紋（或大理石紋）；將（生皮）去毛；<美>用穀物喂（馬）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grain</b> <b>of</b> wheat, rice, or other cereal crop is a seed from it. (麥、米等) 粒","examples":["...a grain of wheat. …一顆麥粒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Grain</b> is a cereal crop, especially wheat or corn, that has been harvested and is used for food or in trade. 穀物","examples":["...a bag of grain. …一袋穀物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>grain of</b> something such as sand or salt is a tiny, hard piece of it. 細粒","examples":["...a grain of sand. …一粒沙子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>grain of</b> a quality is a very small amount of it. 一點","examples":["There's more than a grain of truth in that. 其中包含不少真理。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The grain</b> of a piece of wood is the direction of its fibres. You can also refer to the pattern of lines on the surface of the wood as <b>the grain</b>. (木材的) 紋理","examples":["Brush the paint generously over the wood in the direction of the grain. 順著木材的紋理刷上厚厚的漆。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that an idea or action <b>goes against the grain</b>, you mean that it is very difficult for you to accept it or do it, because it conflicts with your previous ideas, beliefs, or principles. 同…格格不入","examples":["Privatization goes against the grain of their principle of opposition to private ownership of industry. 私有化與他們反對產業私有制的原則相違背。"]}]}]},"grasp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抓牢，握緊；理解，領會；抓住（機會）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"緊抓，緊握；理解（力），領會；能力所及，伸手可及的距離；控制，權力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grasp</b> something, you take it in your hand and hold it very firmly. 抓牢","examples":["He grasped both my hands. 他緊緊地抓住我的雙手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grasp</b> something that is complicated or difficult to understand, you understand it. 理解","examples":["The government has not yet grasped the seriousness of the crisis. 政府還不明白這場危機的嚴重性。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grasp</b> is a very firm hold or grip. 緊握","examples":["His hand was taken in a warm, firm grasp. 他的手被熱情地、緊緊地握住了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>in</b> someone's <b>grasp</b>, you disapprove of the fact that they possess or control it. If something slips <b>from</b> your <b>grasp</b>, you lose it or lose control of it. 掌控","examples":["The people in your grasp are not guests, they are hostages. 在你控制之下的這些人並非賓客，而是人質。","She allowed victory to slip from her grasp. 她聽任勝利從手中溜走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>grasp</b> <b>of</b> something is an understanding of it. 理解","examples":["They have a good grasp of foreign languages. 他們很好地掌握了各門外語。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>within</b> someone's <b>grasp</b>, you mean that it is very likely that they will achieve it. 為某人所能及","examples":["Peace is now within our grasp. 我們現在和平在望。"]}]}]},"guardian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監護人；守衛者，保護者；（方濟各會隱修院的）院長"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"守護的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guardian</b> is someone who has been legally appointed to take charge of the affairs of another person, for example a child or someone who is mentally ill. 監護人","examples":["Destiny's legal guardian was her grandmother. 德斯蒂妮的法定監護人是她的祖母。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>guardian</b> <b>of</b> something is someone who defends and protects it. 保護者","examples":["...an institution acting as the guardian of democracy in Europe. …一個在歐洲扮演民主捍衛者的機構。"]}]}]},"guidance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指導，指引；（火箭等的）制導"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Guidance</b> is help and advice. 指導","examples":["...an opportunity for young people to improve their performance under the guidance of professional coaches. …一個讓年輕人在專業教練指導下提高成績的機會。"]}]}]},"gym":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體育館，健身房；（尤指學校的）體育活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gym</b> is a club, building, or large room, usually containing special equipment, where people go to do physical exercise and get fit. 健身房","examples":["While the boys are golfing, I work out in the gym. 當男孩子們在打高爾夫球時，我在健身房裡鍛鍊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gym</b> is the activity of doing physical exercises in a gym, especially at school. (尤指學校的) 體操","examples":["...gym classes. …體操課。"]}]}]},"hallway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（住宅的）門廳，（正門入口處的）走廊；（建築物內的）過道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hallway</b> in a building is a long passage with doors into rooms on both sides of it. 過道","examples":["They took the lift up to the third floor and walked along the quiet hallway. 他們乘電梯到了3樓，然後走過寂靜的過道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hallway</b> in a house or an apartment is the area just inside the front door, into which some of the other rooms open. 門廳","examples":["...the coats hanging in the hallway. …那些掛在門廳裡的上衣。"]}]}]},"hairdresser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美髮師，理髮師；理髮店，美髮店（the hairdresser's）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hairdresser</b> is a person who cuts, colours, and arranges people's hair. 理髮師","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hairdresser</b> or a <b>hairdresser's</b> is a place where a hairdresser works. 理髮店","examples":["I work in this new hairdresser's. 我在這個新開的理髮店工作。"]}]}]},"gum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牙齦，牙床；口香糖；樹膠；黏膠；透明果味糖；桉樹，樹膠樹；眼屎"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用黏膠粘；（因沒有牙齒）用牙齦咀嚼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gum</b> is a substance, usually tasting of mint, which you chew for a long time but do not swallow. 口香糖","examples":["I do not chew gum in public. 我不在公共場合嚼口香糖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>gums</b> are the areas of firm, pink flesh inside your mouth, which your teeth grow out of. 齒齦","examples":["The toothbrush gently removes plaque without damaging the gums or causing bleeding. 牙刷輕輕地刷去齒菌斑，沒有傷及牙床或引起出血。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various sticky substances that exude from certain plants, hardening on exposure to air and dissolving or forming viscous masses in water 樹膠","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to stick together or in place with gum 用樹膠粘","examples":[]}]}]},"harbor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"港，海港，港灣；避難所，避風港；（Harbor）<美>哈伯（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"庇護，窩藏；懷有，心懷（想法、情緒）；攜帶，藏有（病原體、寄生蟲等）；入港停泊"}],"sections":[]},"handful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一把；少數，少量； 難以控制的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handful</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a small number of them. 少數","examples":["He surveyed the handful of customers at the bar. 他打量著吧檯邊僅有的幾位顧客。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>handful</b> <b>of</b> something is the amount of it that you can hold in your hand. 一把","examples":["She scooped up a handful of sand and let it trickle through her fingers. 她抓了一把沙子，然後讓它們從指縫間慢慢漏掉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone, especially a child, is a <b>handful</b>, you mean that they are difficult to control. 難管的人 (尤指小孩)","examples":["Zara can be a handful sometimes. 扎拉有時會很難管教。"]}]}]},"gymnasium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體育館，健身房"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gymnasium</b> is the same as a . 健身房","examples":[]}]}]},"harvest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收穫；收穫量，捕獲量；成果，收穫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"收割，收穫；採集，蒐集；收採（人的器官、細胞等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The harvest</b> is the gathering of a crop. 收割","examples":["There was about 300 million tons of grain in the fields at the start of the harvest. 收割伊始田間大約有三億噸的穀物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>harvest</b> is the crop that is gathered in. 收成","examples":["Millions of people are threatened with starvation as a result of drought and poor harvests. 數百萬人因乾旱和歉收正受到飢餓的威脅。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>harvest</b> a crop, you gather it in. 收割","examples":["Rice farmers here still plant and harvest their crops by hand. 這兒的稻農仍然靠雙手種植和收割莊稼。"]}]}]},"hay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（用作飼料的）乾草；<美，非正式> 少量的錢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"割草曬乾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hay</b> is grass which has been cut and dried so that it can be used to feed animals. (作飼料用的) 乾草","examples":["...bales of hay. …一捆捆的乾草。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a circular figure in country dancing (鄉村舞中的)圓圈舞步型","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is making hay</b> or <b>is making hay while the sun shines</b>, you mean that they are taking advantage of a situation that is favourable to them while they have the chance to. 曬草要趁好太陽; 抓緊時機","examples":["We knew war was coming, and were determined to make hay while we could. 我們知道戰爭即將來臨，所以決定儘可能抓緊時機。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut, dry, and store (grass, clover, etc) as fodder 把(青草、苜蓿等)製成乾草","examples":[]}]}]},"hatch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"孵化，孵出；密謀，策劃"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（船甲板或飛機底部裝貨物的）艙口；（尤指廚房和餐廳之間供傳遞食物的）兩室之間的小視窗；（飛機或宇宙飛船的）艙門；（地面或天花板的）開口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a baby bird, insect, or other animal <b>hatches</b>, or when it <b>is hatched</b>, it comes out of its egg by breaking the shell. 使孵出; 孵出","examples":["The young disappeared soon after they were hatched. 幼崽孵出後不久就不見了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an egg <b>hatches</b> or when a bird, insect, or other animal <b>hatches</b> an egg, the egg breaks open and a baby comes out. 孵化","examples":["The eggs hatch after a week or ten days. 這些蛋1周或10天后孵化。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hatch</b> a plot or a scheme, you think of it and work it out. 策劃","examples":["He has accused opposition parties of hatching a plot to assassinate the pope. 他曾指責各反對黨陰謀策劃暗殺教皇。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"to mark (a figure, shade, etc) with fine parallel or crossed lines to indicate shading 在(圖形、投影等上)畫影線","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hatch</b> is an opening in the deck of a ship, through which people or cargo can go. You can also refer to the door of this opening as a <b>hatch</b>. 艙口; 艙口蓋","examples":["He stuck his head up through the hatch. 他把腦袋伸出艙口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the act or process of hatching 孵化","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"hatchback的縮寫","examples":[]}]}]},"headquarters":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"總部，總公司；司令部，指揮部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>headquarters</b> of an organization are its main offices. 總部","examples":["...fraud squad officers from Chicago's police headquarters. …來自芝加哥警察局總部的詐騙偵查組的警官們。"]}]}]},"hawk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鷹，隼；鷹派分子，主戰分子；（似鷹般）貪婪的人；灰泥託板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"叫賣，兜售；咳痰；（人）帶鷹出獵；（鳥，蜻蜓）飛行覓食"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hawk</b> is a large bird with a short, hooked beak, sharp claws, and very good eyesight. Hawks catch and eat small birds and animals. 鷹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In politics, if you refer to someone as a <b>hawk</b>, you mean that they believe in using force and violence to achieve something, rather than using more peaceful or diplomatic methods. Compare . (主張使用武力或強硬手段的) 鷹派人物","examples":["Both hawks and doves have expanded their conditions for ending the war. 鷹派和鴿派都已詳述了他們結束戰爭的條件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a noisy clearing of the throat 清嗓聲","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a small square board with a handle underneath, used for carrying wet plaster or mortar 灰泥託板 (Also called mortar board)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hunt with falcons, hawks, etc 放鷹行獵","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to clear the throat noisily 大聲清嗓","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to offer (goods) for sale, as in the street (沿街)兜售","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>watch</b> someone <b>like a hawk</b>, you observe them very carefully, usually to make sure that they do not make a mistake or do something you do not want them to do. 密切監視","examples":["If we hadn't watched him like a hawk, he would have escaped. 如果我們不是密切監視他，他早逃跑了。"]}]}]},"headline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（報紙的）標題，大字標題；（廣播或電視裡的）新聞提要，頭條新聞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（報道、文章）加標題；在（演出）中擔任主演；大肆宣傳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>headline</b> is the title of a newspaper story, printed in large letters at the top of the story, especially on the front page. (尤指報紙頭版的) 標題","examples":["The Sydney Morning Herald carried the headline: \"Sorry Ma'am, Most Australians Want a Republic.\" 《悉尼先驅晨報》有這樣一則頭版標題：“對不起，夫人，大多數澳大利亞人想要一個共和國。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>headlines</b> are the main points of the news which are read on radio or television. 新聞提要","examples":["I'm Claudia Polley with the news headlines. 我是克勞迪婭•波莉，以下是新聞提要。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a newspaper or magazine article <b>is headlined</b> a particular thing, that is the headline that introduces it. 為…加標題","examples":["The article was headlined \"Tell us the truth.\" 該文章題為“告訴我們真相。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that <b>hits the headlines</b> or <b>grabs the headlines</b> gets a lot of publicity from the media. 成為新聞焦點","examples":["El Salvador first hit the world headlines at the beginning of the 1980s. 薩爾瓦多首度成為國際媒體的焦點是在20世紀80年代初。"]}]}]},"harm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傷害，損害"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"危害，損害（某事物）；傷害（人或動物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>harm</b> a person or animal means to cause them physical injury, usually on purpose. (故意地) 傷害","examples":["The hijackers seemed anxious not to harm anyone. 劫機犯們似乎並不急於傷害任何人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>harm</b> a thing, or sometimes a person, means to damage them or make them less effective or successful than they were. 損害","examples":["...a warning that the product may harm the environment. …一則該產品可能會破壞環境的警告。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Harm</b> is physical injury to a person or an animal which is usually caused on purpose. (故意的) 傷害","examples":["All dogs are capable of doing harm to human beings. 所有的狗都能對人造成傷害。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Harm</b> is the damage to something which is caused by a particular course of action. 損害","examples":["The abuse of your powers does harm to all other officers who do their job properly. 你濫用權力有損於所有其他好好工作的政府官員。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say <b>it does no harm</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>there is no harm</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you mean that it might be worth doing, and you will not be blamed for doing it. 不妨 (做某事)","examples":["They are not always willing to take on untrained workers, but there's no harm in asking. 他們一般不願意僱傭沒有受過訓練的工人，但是問問也無妨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>out of harm's way</b>, they are in a safe place away from danger or from the possibility of being damaged. 免於傷害","examples":["For parents, it is an easy way of keeping their children entertained, or simply out of harm's way. 對父母而言，這是一個保持孩子們愉悅或僅僅讓他們免於傷害的簡便方法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>no harm done</b>, you are telling someone not to worry about something that has happened because it has not caused any serious injury or damage. 沒有造成傷害 (或損害)","examples":["There, now, you're all right. No harm done. 好了，現在你沒事了。沒出什麼事。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>will come to no harm</b> or that <b>no harm will come</b> <b>to</b> them, you mean that they will not be hurt or damaged in any way. 將不受傷害; 將不受損害","examples":["There is always a lifeguard to ensure that no one comes to any harm. 任何時候都有一名救生員以確保沒有人會受到傷害。"]}]}]},"heaven":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天堂，天國；<非正式>極樂之地，極樂；<文>天空；神，諸神；與上帝同享永福"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（表示驚訝或強調）天哪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In some religions, <b>heaven</b> is said to be the place where God lives, where good people go when they die, and where everyone is always happy. It is usually imagined as being high up in the sky. 天堂","examples":["I believed that when I died I would go to heaven and see God. 我相信我死後會進入天堂，見到上帝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>heaven</b> to refer to a place or situation that you like very much. 極好的地方 (或情況)","examples":["I would go to movies in the afternoon and to ball games in the evening. It was heaven. 我下午去看電影，晚上去看球賽，真是享受。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Good heavens!</b>\" or \"<b>Heavens!</b>\" to express surprise or to emphasize that you agree or disagree with someone. (表示驚奇等) 天哪","examples":["Good Heavens! That explains a lot! 天哪！那很說明問題！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Heaven help</b> someone\" when you are worried that something bad is going to happen to them, often because you disapprove of what they are doing or the way they are behaving. (表示擔心某人將有難) 老天幫幫某人吧","examples":["If this makes sense to our leaders, then heaven help us all. 如果這對我們的領導們來說是可行的，那真是老天幫助大家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Heaven knows</b>\" to emphasize that you do not know something, or that you find something very surprising. 天知道","examples":["Heaven knows what they put in it. 天知道他們往裡面放了些什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Heaven knows</b>\" to emphasize something that you feel or believe very strongly. 確實","examples":["Heaven knows they have enough money. 確實他們有足夠的錢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If <b>the heavens open</b>, it suddenly starts raining very heavily. 突然下起傾盆大雨","examples":["The match had just begun when the heavens opened and play was suspended. 比賽才剛剛開始，就突然下起傾盆大雨，於是比賽暫停。"]}]}]},"heap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（凌亂的）一堆；許多，大量；<非正式>破舊的汽車，老爺車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"堆積，堆放；對……大加讚揚（或指責等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>heap</b> <b>of</b> things is a pile of them, especially a pile arranged in a rather messy way. 一堆","examples":["...a heap of bricks. …一堆磚。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>heap</b> things in a pile, you arrange them in a large pile. 堆放","examples":["Mrs. Madrigal heaped more carrots onto Michael's plate. 馬德里加爾太太往邁克爾的盤子裡放了更多的胡蘿蔔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>heap</b> praise or criticism <b>on</b> someone or something, you give them a lot of praise or criticism. 大量地給予 (讚揚、批評等)","examples":["The head of the navy heaped scorn on both the methods and motives of the conspirators. 這位海軍首領對密謀分子的做法和動機都給予了極大的蔑視。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heap up</b> means the same as . 堆起","examples":["Off to one side, the militia was heaping up wood for a bonfire. 在一側，民兵們正在堆起木柴，準備生起篝火。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heaps of</b> something or a <b>heap of</b> something is a large quantity of it. 許多","examples":["You have heaps of time. 你有很多時間。"]}]}]},"helmet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頭盔，安全帽；（尤指唇形科和蘭科花朵的）花冠盔瓣，唇瓣；冠螺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>helmet</b> is a hat made of a strong material which you wear to protect your head. 頭盔","examples":[]}]}]},"historian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歷史學家，史學工作者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>historian</b> is a person who specializes in the study of history, and who writes books and articles about it. 歷史學家","examples":[]}]}]},"hike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"徒步旅行，遠足；（價格、花費等的）大幅度提高，猛增"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"遠足，徒步旅行；突然增加，突然提高；拉起，提起（尤指衣物）；後傳（發球）給四分衛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hike</b> is a long walk in the country, especially one that you go on for pleasure. 遠足","examples":["The site is reached by a 30-minute hike through dense forest. 要花30分鐘徒步穿過密林才能到達那個地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"遠足","examples":["...some harder, more strenuous hiking on cliff pathways. …在懸崖峭壁的小路上進行的更艱難、更費力的長途行走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hike</b> is a sudden or large increase in prices, rates, taxes, or quantities. 突然上漲","examples":["...a sudden 1.75 percent hike in interest rates. …利率突漲1.75%。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hike</b>, you go for a long walk in the country. 遠足","examples":["You could hike through the Fish River Canyon – it's entirely up to you. 你可以遠足穿越菲什幹河大峽谷–這全由你自己決定。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>hike</b> prices, rates, taxes, or quantities means to increase them suddenly or by a large amount. 使大幅上升","examples":["It has now been forced to hike its rates by 5.25 percent. 它現在被迫將其稅率提高5.25%。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hike up</b> means the same as . 使大幅上升","examples":["The insurers have started hiking up premiums by huge amounts. 保險公司已經開始大幅度地提高保險費。"]}]}]},"hint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暗示，提示；徵兆，跡象；少許，少量；秘訣，竅門"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"暗示，示意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hint</b> is a suggestion about something that is made in an indirect way. 暗示","examples":["I'd dropped a hint about having an exhibition of his work up here. 我暗示要在這裡舉辦一次他的作品展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hint</b> is a helpful piece of advice, usually about how to do something. 建議","examples":["Here are some helpful hints to make your journey easier. 這裡是一些有用的建議，可以使你的旅途更舒適。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hint</b> <b>of</b> something is a very small amount of it. 微量","examples":["She added only a hint of vermouth to the gin. 她往杜松子酒裡只加了一點兒苦艾酒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a <b>hint</b>, you understand something that is suggested to you indirectly. 領會暗示","examples":["\"I think I hear the telephone ringing.\"—\"Okay, I can take a hint.\" “我想我聽見了電話在響。”—“好的，我明白你的意思。”"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hint</b> <b>at</b> something, you suggest it in an indirect way. 暗示","examples":["She hinted at the possibility of a treat of some sort. 她暗示可以找找樂子什麼的。"]}]}]},"hometown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家鄉，故鄉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>hometown</b> is the town where they live or the town that they come from. 家鄉","examples":[]}]}]},"hive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忙碌的場所，繁忙的地方；蜂房，蜂箱；蜂群；蜂窩狀物體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（蜜蜂）入蜂箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hive</b> is a structure in which bees are kept, which is designed so that the beekeeper can collect the honey that they produce. 蜂箱","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place as a <b>hive</b> <b>of</b> activity, you approve of the fact that there is a lot of activity there or that people are busy working there. 忙碌的地方","examples":["In the morning the house was a hive of activity. 早上，這幢房子是忙碌的地方。"]}]}]},"heel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳後跟；鞋後跟；高跟鞋；手掌根；<舊>壞蛋，無賴；襪子後跟；（船的）傾側度；（小提琴琴弓的）弓跟；（高爾夫）棒杆彎頭；麵包硬頭，乾酪硬皮；（植物的）踵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"傾斜；給（鞋等）修理後跟；用棒杆彎頭擊（球）；並列爭球時用腳後跟往回傳（球）；跳舞時以後跟觸地；（喚狗用語）跟上；（由於風力或裝載不平衡而）傾側；使（船）傾側"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"跟著我（讓狗緊跟在身後的命令）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>heel</b> is the back part of your foot, just below your ankle. 腳後跟","examples":["He had an operation on his heel last week. 他上星期腳後跟做了手術。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>heel</b> of a shoe is the raised part on the bottom at the back. 鞋後跟","examples":["...the shoes with the high heels. …那些高跟的鞋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Heels</b> are women's shoes that are raised very high at the back. 女高跟鞋","examples":["She was dressed in heels and a clingy dress. 她穿著高跟鞋和一件貼身連衣裙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"inclined position from the vertical 傾側(位置)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to repair or replace the heel of (shoes, boots, etc) 給(鞋、靴子等)修跟; 換跟","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(of a vessel) to lean over; list (船)傾斜; 使(船)傾斜","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dig</b> your <b>heels in</b> or <b>dig in</b> your <b>heels</b>, you refuse to do something such as change your opinions or plans, especially when someone is trying very hard to make you do so. 固執己見","examples":["It was really the British who, by digging their heels in, prevented any last-minute deal. 正是英國人，因其固執己見，妨礙了最後一刻交易的達成。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one event follows <b>hard on the heels of</b> another or <b>hot on the heels of</b> another, you mean that one happens very quickly or immediately after another. 接踵而至","examples":["Unfortunately, bad news has come hard on the heels of good. 遺憾的是，壞訊息緊接著好訊息而來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>hot on</b> your <b>heels</b>, you are emphasizing that they are chasing you and are not very far behind you. 緊跟…之後","examples":["They sped through the southwest with the law hot on their heels. 他們飛速穿越西南部，警察緊隨其後。"]}]}]},"honesty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誠實，正直；銀扇草，金錢花"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Honesty</b> is the quality of being honest. 誠實","examples":["They said the greatest virtues in a politician were integrity, correctness, and honesty. 他們說政治家最重要的美德就是正直、得體和誠實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a purple-flowered SE European plant, <b>Lunaria annua,</b> cultivated for its flattened silvery pods, which are used for indoor decoration: family <b>Brassicaceae</b> (crucifers) (Also called moonwort, satinpod)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>in all honesty</b> when you are saying something that might be disappointing or upsetting, and you want to soften its effect by emphasizing your sincerity. 坦白地說","examples":[]}]}]},"hollow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"空的，空心的；凹的，凹陷的；虛偽的，不真誠的；無用的，無價值的；（聲音）沉悶迴盪的；空腹的；沉悶迴盪的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使凹陷，使下陷；挖洞（成某物）；形成空洞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"凹陷處，坑窪處；坑，洞；山谷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>hollow</b> has a space inside it, as opposed to being solid all the way through. 空心的","examples":["...a hollow tree. …一棵空心樹"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A surface that is <b>hollow</b> curves inward. 凹陷的","examples":["He looked young, dark and sharp-featured, with hollow cheeks. 他看起來很年輕，膚色黝黑，面部稜角分明，雙頰凹陷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a statement, situation, or person as <b>hollow</b>, you mean they have no real value, worth, or effectiveness. 空洞的; 沒有價值的","examples":["Any threat to bring in the police is a hollow one. 任何要叫警察來的威脅都是虛張聲勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone gives a <b>hollow</b> laugh, they laugh in a way that shows that they do not really find something amusing. 虛偽的","examples":["Murray Pick's hollow laugh had no mirth in it. 默裡·皮克虛偽的笑聲裡沒有一點快樂。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>hollow</b> sound is dull and echoing. (聲音) 空洞而沉悶的","examples":["...the hollow sound of a gunshot. …空悶的槍聲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hollow</b> is an area that is lower than the surrounding surface. 凹陷處","examples":["Below him the town lay warm in the hollow of the hill. 在他的下面，小鎮溫暖地坐落在山坳裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"空洞","examples":["One month before the deadline we see the hollowness of these promises. 截止期限前一個月我們看出了這些承諾的空洞性。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is hollowed</b>, its surface is made to curve inward or downward. 使凹陷","examples":["The mule's back was hollowed by the weight of its burden. 騾子的背被所載重物壓得彎了下去。"]}]}]},"housekeeper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"管家，女管家；主婦，持家者；（酒店、醫院等）客房部主管，客房部經理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>housekeeper</b> is a person whose job is to cook, clean, and take care of a house for its owner. 管家","examples":[]}]}]},"honor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"榮譽，光榮；名譽，信用，正直；殊榮，榮幸；榮譽稱號，頭銜，獎章"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"尊敬，尊重；向……致敬；給……以榮譽，表彰；（金融）承兌；履行，遵守"}],"sections":[]},"hell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地獄；苦難的經歷；（有人認為含冒犯意）該死，見鬼"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"見鬼（用於表示生氣或惱怒）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"過放蕩生活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In some religions, <b>hell</b> is the place where the Devil lives, and where wicked people are sent to be punished when they die. Hell is usually imagined as being under the ground and full of flames. 地獄","examples":["I've never believed. Not in heaven or hell or God or Satan until now. 我以前一直都不信。直到現在我才相信有天堂、地獄、上帝和撒旦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a particular situation or place is <b>hell</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely unpleasant. 令人痛苦不堪的處境 (或地方)","examples":["...the hell of the Siberian labour camps. …西伯利亞勞改營那個活地獄。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hell</b> is used by some people when they are angry or excited, or when they want to emphasize what they are saying. This use could cause offence. 該死","examples":["\"Hell, no!\" the doctor snapped. “該死，不！”醫生厲聲說。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>as hell</b> after adjectives or some adverbs to emphasize the adjective or adverb. 很","examples":["The men might be armed, but they sure as hell weren't trained. 這些男人也許被武裝了，但他們當時確確實實沒受訓練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something <b>for the hell of it</b>, or <b>just for the hell of it</b>, they do it for fun or for no particular reason. 只是為了好玩","examples":["I started shouting in German, just for the hell of it. 我當時開始用德語喊叫，只是為了好玩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>from hell</b> after a noun when you are emphasizing that something or someone is extremely unpleasant or evil. 極壞","examples":["He's a child from hell. 他這個孩子壞透了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>go to hell</b>, you are angrily telling them to go away and leave you alone. 滾開","examples":["\"Well, you can go to hell!\" He swept out of the room. “行了，滾開！”他大模大樣地走出房間。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone can <b>go to hell</b>, you are emphasizing angrily that you do not care about them and that they will not stop you doing what you want. 見鬼去吧","examples":["Peter can go to hell. It's my money and I'll leave it to who I want. 讓彼得見鬼去吧。那是我的錢，我想留給誰就留給誰。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is going</b> <b>hell for leather</b>, you are emphasizing that they are doing something or are moving very quickly and perhaps carelessly. 飛快地","examples":["The first horse often goes hell for leather, hits a few fences but gets away with it. 第一匹馬往往跑得飛快，會撞落幾根橫杆，但一般不會被罰分。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"Some people say <b>like hell</b> to emphasize that they strongly disagree with you or are strongly opposed to what you say. 絕不會","examples":["\"I'll go myself.\"—\"Like hell you will!\" “我會自己去。”—“可你絕不會！”"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"Some people use <b>like hell</b> to emphasize how strong an action or quality is. 非常","examples":["It hurts like hell. 這兒非常痛。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"If you say that <b>all hell breaks loose</b>, you are emphasizing that a lot of arguing or fighting suddenly starts. 大亂起來","examples":["He had an affair, I found out and then all hell broke loose. 他有了外遇，我發現了，接著便鬧翻了天。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you talk about <b>a hell of a lot of</b> something, or <b>one hell of a lot of</b> something, you mean that there is a large amount of it. 許多","examples":["The manager took a hell of a lot of money out of the club. 經理從夜總會拿走了許多錢。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"Some people use <b>a hell of</b> or <b>one hell of</b> to emphasize that something is very good, very bad, or very big. 極度的","examples":["Whatever the outcome, it's going to be one hell of a fight. 不管結果如何，那都將是一場惡戰。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"Some people use <b>the hell out of</b> for emphasis after verbs such as \"scare,\" \"irritate,\" and \"beat.\" 非常 (用於)(scare)(,)(irritate)(,和)(beat)(等動詞之後表強調)","examples":["I patted the top of her head in the condescending way I knew irritated the hell out of her. 我以降尊紆貴的姿態拍了她的頭頂，知道這會讓她氣得七竅生煙。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"If you say <b>there'll be hell to pay</b>, you are emphasizing that there will be serious trouble. 會有大麻煩","examples":["There would be hell to pay when Ferguson and Tony found out about it. 要是弗格森和託妮發現了這事，那麻煩可就大了。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"To <b>play hell</b> <b>with</b> something means to have a bad effect on it or cause great confusion. 造成混亂","examples":["The rain had played hell with business. 這場雨把事情搞得一團糟。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>the hell</b> for emphasis in questions, after words such as \"what,\" \"where,\" and \"why,\" often in order to express anger. 究竟","examples":["Where the hell have you been? 你究竟去了哪裡？"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"If you <b>go through hell</b>, or if someone <b>puts</b> you <b>through hell</b>, you have a very difficult or unpleasant time. 經受苦難","examples":["All of you seem to have gone through hell making this record. 看來在灌製這張唱片時你們經受了重重困難。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"If you say you <b>hope to hell</b> or <b>wish to hell</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you are emphasizing that you strongly hope or wish it is true. 打心底裡盼望","examples":["I hope to hell you're right. 我打心底裡希望你是對的。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"You can say \"<b>what the hell</b>\" when you decide to do something in spite of the doubts that you have about it. 不管它","examples":["What the hell, I thought, at least it will give the lazy old man some exercise. 不管它，我想，至少這會讓那個懶老頭活動活動筋骨。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"If you say \"<b>to hell with</b>\" something, you are emphasizing that you do not care about something and that it will not stop you from doing what you want to do. 讓…見鬼去","examples":["To hell with this, I'm getting out of here. 讓它見鬼去吧，我要離開這裡了。"]}]}]},"horn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"角；角質；號角；喇叭；角狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（動物）用角抵撞（或頂撞）；對（丈夫或妻子）不忠誠；裝角於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"On a vehicle such as a car, the <b>horn</b> is the device that makes a loud noise as a signal or warning. (汽車等的) 喇叭","examples":["He sounded the car horn. 他按響了汽車喇叭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>horns</b> of an animal such as a cow or deer are the hard pointed things that grow from its head. (牛、鹿等動物頭上的) 角","examples":["A mature cow has horns. 成年母牛頭上長有角。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>horn</b> is a musical instrument of the brass family. It is a long circular metal tube, wide at one end, which you play by blowing. 號 (銅管樂器)","examples":["He started playing the horn when he was eight. 他8歲時就開始吹號。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>horn</b> is a simple musical instrument consisting of a metal tube that is wide at one end and narrow at the other. You play it by blowing into it. 號 (一種以一頭寬一頭窄的金屬管制成的簡單的吹奏樂器)","examples":["...a hunting horn. …獵號。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>lock horns</b>, they argue about something. 爭論","examples":["During his six years in office, Seidman has often locked horns with lawmakers. 在任的6年裡，塞德曼經常與立法者進行爭論。"]}]}]},"hut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（簡陋的）小屋；（花園中的）木屋，（建築工人等住的）臨時工棚"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"供給……小屋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hut</b> is a small house with only one or two rooms, especially one which is made of wood, mud, grass, or stones. (木頭、泥、草或石頭搭成的) 小屋","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hut</b> is a small wooden building in someone's garden, or a temporary building used by builders or repair workers. () 木屋; (工人住的) 臨時工棚","examples":[]}]}]},"hush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）安靜下來，（使）停止說話；（用於告訴別人保持安靜）噓；用水清洗礦石"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"寂靜，鴉雀無聲；（人造的）噴水"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Hush!</b>\" to someone when you are asking or telling them to be quiet.  噓！","examples":["Hush, my love, it's all right. 噓，親愛的，沒事。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hush</b> someone or if they <b>hush</b>, they stop speaking or making a noise. 使安靜下來; 安靜下來","examples":["She tried to hush her noisy father. 她試圖讓吵吵嚷嚷的父親安靜下來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say there is a <b>hush</b> in a place when everything is quiet and peaceful, or suddenly becomes quiet. 安靜; (突然的) 寂靜","examples":["A hush fell over the crowd and I knew something terrible had happened. 人群突然一片肅靜，我便知道一定發生了什麼可怕的事情了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a gush of water, esp when artificially produced (尤指人造的)噴水","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to run water over the ground to erode (surface soil), revealing the underlying strata and any valuable minerals present 用水清洗礦石","examples":[]}]}]},"hug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擁抱；抱住，抱在胸前；緊靠，緊挨；（衣服）纏緊，縛緊；暗自慶幸，沾沾自喜；抱有，持有（信念等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擁抱，緊抱；（摔跤中的）抓握"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>hug</b> someone, you put your arms around them and hold them tightly, for example because you like them or are pleased to see them. You can also say that two people <b>hug</b> each other or that they <b>hug</b>. 擁抱","examples":["She had hugged him exuberantly and invited him to dinner the next day. 她興高采烈地擁抱了他，並邀請他第二天一起用晚餐。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hug</b> is also a noun. 擁抱","examples":["She leapt out of the back seat, and gave him a hug. 她從後座上跳了出來，給了他一個擁抱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hug</b> something, you hold it close to your body with your arms tightly around it. 抱住","examples":["Shaerl trudged toward them, hugging a large box. 謝爾抱著一個大盒子，蹣跚地向他們走來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>hugs</b> the ground or a stretch of land or water stays very close to it. 緊靠著","examples":["The road hugs the coast for hundreds of miles. 公路緊挨著海岸線，長達幾百英里。"]}]}]},"horror":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"震驚，恐懼；懼怕，憎惡；恐怖性；極其不愉快的（或可怕的）經歷；恐怖故事（或電影等）；<非正式>調皮搗蛋的孩子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Horror</b> is a feeling of great shock, fear, and worry caused by something extremely unpleasant. 震驚; 恐懼","examples":["I felt numb with horror. 我驚呆了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>horror of</b> something, you are afraid of it or dislike it very much. 恐懼; 憎惡","examples":["...his horror of death. …他對死亡的恐懼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>horror</b> <b>of</b> something, especially something that hurts people, is its very great unpleasantness. 恐怖性","examples":["...the horror of this most bloody of civil wars. …這場極其血腥的內戰的慘狀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to extremely unpleasant or frightening experiences as <b>horrors</b>. 令人恐怖的經歷","examples":["Can you possibly imagine all the horrors we have undergone since I last wrote you? 你能想像得出自從上次我寫信給你以來，我們所經歷的所有恐怖的事情嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>horror</b> film or story is intended to be very frightening. (影片或故事) 內容恐怖的","examples":["...a psychological horror film. …一部心理恐怖電影。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an account of a very unpleasant experience or event as a <b>horror</b> story. (經歷或事件) 非常不愉快的","examples":["...a horror story about lost luggage while flying. …一次關於乘飛機旅行丟失行李的糟糕經歷。"]}]}]},"ignorance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"無知，愚昧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ignorance</b> <b>of</b> something is lack of knowledge about it. 無知","examples":["I am beginning to feel embarrassed by my complete ignorance of world history. 我開始為自己對世界歷史的一無所知感到尷尬。"]}]}]},"humankind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人類（總稱）"}],"sections":[]},"identity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"身份，本體；個性，特性；同一性，一致；恆等運算，恆等式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>identity</b> is who you are. 身份","examples":["Abu is not his real name, but it's one he uses to disguise his identity. 阿布不是他的真名，而是一個他用來掩蓋自己身份的假名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>identity</b> of a person or place is the characteristics that distinguish them from others. 特性","examples":["I wanted a sense of my own identity. 我需要確立自身的個性意識。"]}]}]},"ideal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"理想的，最佳的；想象的，不切實際的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"理想；典範，完美典型"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ideal</b> is a principle, idea, or standard that seems very good and worth trying to achieve. 理想","examples":["Walt Disney stayed true to his ideals. 沃爾特·迪斯尼堅持他的理想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>ideal</b> <b>of</b> something is the person or thing that seems to you to be the best possible example of it. 完美典範","examples":["Her features were almost the opposite of the Japanese ideal of beauty in those days. 她的容貌幾乎和當時日本的美人典範正好相反。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>ideal</b> person or thing for a particular task or purpose is the best possible person or thing for it. 理想的","examples":["She decided that I was the ideal person to take over the job. 她認定我是接管這項工作的最佳人選。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>ideal</b> society or world is the best possible one that you can imagine. 完美的","examples":["We do not live in an ideal world. 我們並非生活在一個完美的世界裡。"]}]}]},"inn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指鄉村的）小旅館，小酒館；（用於旅館的名字中）酒店，飯店"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inn</b> is a hotel, bar, or restaurant, often one in the country. (常指鄉村的) 小旅店; 小酒館; 小餐廳","examples":["...the Waterside Inn. …水濱旅館。"]}]}]},"imagination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"想象力，想象；幻覺，空想，幻想物；興趣；創造力，創作力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>imagination</b> is the ability that you have to form pictures or ideas in your mind of things that are new and exciting, or things that you have not experienced. 想像力","examples":["Latanya is a woman with a vivid imagination. 拉坦尼婭是一個想像力豐富的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>imagination</b> is the part of your mind that allows you to form pictures or ideas of things that do not necessarily exist in real life. 想像","examples":["Long before I ever went there, Africa was alive in my imagination. 早在我去非洲之前，它就栩栩如生地在我的腦海中了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>captured</b> your <b>imagination</b>, you mean that you thought they were interesting or exciting when you saw them or heard them for the first time. 引起某人的興趣","examples":["Their music continues to capture the imagination of the American public. 他們的音樂持續吸引著美國公眾的興趣。"]}]}]},"import":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"進口，進口商品；輸入，引進；重要性；意思，含意"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進口，輸入，引進；匯入（計算機）；<舊>意味，表明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>import</b> products or raw materials means to buy them from another country for use in your own country. 進口","examples":["Rich countries benefited from importing Indonesia's timber. 富國從進口印度尼西亞木材中獲利。","To import from Russia, a Ukrainian firm needs Russian roubles. 要從俄羅斯進口，烏克蘭公司需要俄羅斯盧布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>import</b> files or information into one type of software from another type, you open them in a format that can be used in the new software. 匯入","examples":["Users can import files made in other packages. 使用者能夠匯入其他程式包裡的檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Import</b> is also a noun. 進口","examples":["Germany, however, insists on restrictions on the import of Polish coal. 然而德國堅持對波蘭煤炭的進口限制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"進口","examples":["...restrictions concerning the importation of birds. …關於鳥類進口的種種限制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Imports</b> are products or raw materials bought from another country for use in your own country. 進口商品","examples":["...cheap imports from other countries. …來自其他國家的廉價進口商品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>import</b> of something is its importance. 重要性","examples":["Such arguments are of little import. 這種爭論幾乎不具重要性。"]}]}]},"image":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"形象，印象；影像，映像，影象；比喻，意象；畫像，塑像，雕像；酷似另一個人的人；（人或事物）外形，外表；像點；硬碟備份；（聖經）偶像"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"作……的像，描繪……的形象；（以探測器或電磁束）掃描出……的直觀圖；幻想，想像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>image</b> of something or someone, you have a picture or idea of them in your mind. (頭腦裡的) 形象; 概念","examples":["The image of art theft as a gentleman's crime is outdated. 藝術品盜竊是紳士犯罪這一觀念已經過時了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>image</b> of a person, group, or organization is the way that they appear to other people. (個人、團體或組織的) 形象","examples":["...the government's negative public image. …政府負面的公眾形象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>image</b> is a picture of someone or something. 畫像","examples":["...photographic images of young children. …小孩子們的攝影影象。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>image</b> is a poetic description of something. 生動的描繪","examples":["The natural images in the poem are meant to be suggestive of realities beyond themselves. 詩中自然景象的描寫意在使人聯想起那以外的現實。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are the image of</b> someone else, you look very much like them. 酷似某人","examples":["Marianne's son was the image of his father. 瑪麗安娜的兒子酷似他的父親。"]}]}]},"inferior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"次的，較差的；低等的，下級的；自卑的；（法庭，特別法庭）下級的；（商品，服務）需求量在衰退期中較之繁榮期更大的，低檔的；（位置）下方的，下位的，靠下的；（字母，數字，符號）下標的；低等的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"下級，（地位或成就）低於他人者；下標字母，下標數字，下標符號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>inferior</b> is not as good as something else. 較差的","examples":["The cassettes were of inferior quality. 這些盒式磁帶質量較差。","This resulted in overpriced and often inferior products. 這就導致產品標價過高而往往質量較次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person is regarded as <b>inferior</b> <b>to</b> another, they are regarded as less important because they have less status or ability. 低等的; 次要的","examples":["He preferred the company of those who were intellectually inferior to himself. 他喜歡與那些智力不如他的人為伍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inferior</b> is also a noun. (能力或地位) 低於他人者; 部下","examples":["It was a gentleman's duty always to be civil, even to his inferiors. 一個紳士的責任是一直保持彬彬有禮，即使是對比自己地位低的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"自卑","examples":["I found it difficult to shake off a sense of social inferiority. 我發現很難擺脫社會地位低下的自卑感。"]}]}]},"inspector":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"檢查員，督察員；（警察）巡官；（英國公共汽車或火車上的）查票員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inspector</b> is a person, usually employed by a government agency, whose job is to find out whether people are obeying official regulations. 檢查員; 督察員","examples":["The mill was finally shut down by state safety inspectors. 這家工廠最終被州安全檢查官關閉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>inspector</b> is an officer in the police who is next in rank to a superintendent or police chief. 巡官 (官階僅次於警長或警察局長的警官)","examples":["...San Francisco police inspector Tony Camileri. …舊金山市巡官託尼·卡米勒瑞。"]}]}]},"individual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單獨的，個別的；個人的；獨特的，與眾不同的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"個人，個體；與眾不同的人，有個性的人；某種型別的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Individual</b> means relating to one person or thing, rather than to a large group. 單獨的","examples":["...waiting for the group to decide rather than making individual decisions. …等待集體作決定而不是作單獨的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>individual</b>, you mean that you admire them because they are very unusual and do not try to imitate other people or things. 獨特的","examples":["It was really all part of her very individual personality. 那確實是她非常獨特個性的全部。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"單獨地","examples":["...individually crafted tiles. …一塊塊單獨製作的瓦片。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>individual</b> is a person. 個人","examples":["...anonymous individuals who are doing good things within our community. …一些在我們社群裡做好事不留名人士。"]}]}]},"injury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（身體上的）傷，損害；<法律>（對感情的）傷害，挫傷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>injury</b> is damage done to a person's or an animal's body. 傷害; 損害","examples":["Four police officers sustained serious injuries in the explosion. 四名警官在爆炸中受了重傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone suffers <b>injury</b> <b>to</b> their feelings, they are badly upset by something. If they suffer <b>injury</b> <b>to</b> their reputation, their reputation is seriously harmed. (對感情或名譽等的) 傷害","examples":["She was awarded $3,500 for injury to her feelings. 她獲得了3500美元的精神損傷費。"]}]}]},"inventor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發明者，發明家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inventor</b> is a person who has invented something, or whose job is to invent things. 發明者","examples":["...Alexander Graham Bell, the inventor of the telephone. …亞歷山大·格雷厄姆·貝爾，電話的發明者。"]}]}]},"ivory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"象牙，（其他動物的）長牙；象牙製品；象牙色，乳白色；<非正式>鋼琴鍵；<非正式>（人的）牙齒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"象牙色的，乳白色的；象牙製成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ivory</b> is a hard cream-coloured substance that forms the tusks of elephants and some other animals. It is valuable and can be used for making carved ornaments. (象或其他一些動物的) 長牙","examples":["...the international ban on the sale of ivory. …禁止銷售象牙的國際禁令。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ivory</b> is a creamy-white colour. 乳白色 (的)","examples":["...small ivory flowers. …乳白色的小花。"]}]}]},"instruction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"用法說明；指示，吩咐；教授，指導；（計算機的）指令，命令；給初級律師（或辯護律師、陪審團）的指示"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"說明用法的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>instruction</b> is something that someone tells you to do. 指示","examples":["Two lawyers were told not to leave the building but no reason for this instruction was given. 兩位律師被告知不要離開這座建築，但沒被告知這一指示的原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone gives you <b>instruction</b> in a subject or skill, they teach it to you. 講授; 指導","examples":["Each candidate is given instruction in safety. 每位候選人都被給予了安全指導。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Instructions</b> are clear and detailed information on how to do something. 用法說明","examples":["This book gives instructions for making a wide range of skin and hand creams. 這本書給出了多種護膚霜和護手霜的製作說明。"]}]}]},"introduction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"初次投入使用，採用；介紹，引見；初次經歷，首次體驗；序言，引言；導讀，入門指導；前奏；介紹信；外來品，新引進的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>introduction</b> <b>to</b> a book or talk is the part that comes at the beginning and tells you what the rest of the book or talk is about. 引言; 序","examples":["Ellen Malos, in her introduction to \"The Politics of Housework,\" provides a summary of the debates. 埃倫·馬洛斯在她的《家務政治學》一書的引言中對這些爭論做了一個概述。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a book as an <b>introduction</b> <b>to</b> a particular subject, you mean that it explains the basic facts about that subject. (書) 入門","examples":["The book is a friendly, down-to-earth introduction to physics. 這是一本簡明、實用的物理學入門書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a new product as an <b>introduction</b> when it becomes available in a place for the first time. 引進品","examples":["There are two among their recent introductions that have greatly impressed me. 他們最新引進的產品中有兩件給我留下了深刻的印象。"]}]}]},"jail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監獄；監禁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"監禁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jail</b> is a place where criminals are kept in order to punish them, or where people waiting to be tried are kept. 監獄","examples":["Three prisoners escaped from a jail. 3個囚犯從一個監獄逃跑了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is jailed</b>, they are put into jail. 監禁","examples":["He was jailed for twenty years. 他被監禁了20年。"]}]}]},"jelly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"果凍；（常塗於麵包上的）果醬；肉凍；膠狀物；輕便塑膠鞋；明膠基軟糖；<美，非正式>輕鬆愉快的事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（食物）做成膠凍（或果凍），把（食物）包上膠凍（或果凍）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jelly</b> is a transparent, usually coloured food that is eaten as a dessert. It is made from gelatin, fruit juice, and sugar. 果凍","examples":["...a bowl of jelly. …一碗果凍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Jelly</b> is a sweet food that is made by cooking fruit or fruit juice with a large amount of sugar until it is thickened. It is usually spread on bread. 果醬","examples":["I had two peanut butter and jelly sandwiches. 我吃了兩個花生醬果醬三明治。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to jellify 使凝成膠狀","examples":[]}]}]},"jaw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頜，顎；下巴；（機器的）鉗口；危險的局面；口部；<非正式> 閒聊；<非正式>饒舌，喋喋不休；<非正式>閒聊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>喋喋不休"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>jaw</b> is the lower part of your face below your mouth. The movement of your jaw is sometimes considered to express a particular emotion. For example, if your <b>jaw drops</b>, you are very surprised. 下頜","examples":["He thought for a moment, stroking his well-defined jaw. 他撫摸著他稜角分明的下巴想了一會兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's or animal's <b>jaws</b> are the two bones in their head that their teeth are attached to. 頜骨","examples":["...a forest rodent with powerful jaws. …一種長著強勁有力的頜骨的森林齧齒動物。"]}]}]},"jewel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寶石；珠寶首飾；難能可貴的人，珍貴的東西；（手錶的）寶石軸承"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用寶石裝飾；把寶石承軸裝進手錶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jewel</b> is a precious stone used to decorate valuable things that you wear, such as rings or necklaces. 寶石","examples":["...a golden box containing precious jewels. …一個裝著貴重寶石的金盒子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as a <b>jewel</b>, you mean that they are better, more beautiful, or more special than other similar things or than other people. 寶貝 (指寶貴的物或難能可貴的人)","examples":["...a small jewel of a theatre. …劇場的一個小寶貝。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to an achievement or thing as the <b>jewel in</b> someone's <b>crown</b>, you mean that it is considered to be their greatest achievement or the thing they can be most proud of. 最耀眼的成就; 最得意之物","examples":["His achievement is astonishing and this book is the jewel in his crown. 他成就斐然，這本書是他的最得意之作。"]}]}]},"jewelry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"珠寶，首飾"}],"sections":[]},"jet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噴氣式飛機；噴射流；煤玉，黑玉；噴嘴，噴射口"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘噴氣式飛機旅行；噴射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jet</b> is an aircraft that is powered by jet engines. 噴氣式飛機","examples":["Her private jet landed in the republic on the way to Japan. 她的私人噴氣式飛機在去日本的途中在該共和國降落。","He had arrived from Key West by jet. 他已乘噴氣式飛機從基韋斯特來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>jet</b> of liquid or gas is a strong, fast, thin stream of it. 噴射流","examples":["A jet of water poured through the windows. 一股水柱從窗戶噴了過來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a hard black variety of coal that takes a brilliant polish and is used for jewellery, ornaments, etc 黑玉","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(<b>as modifier</b>) 黑玉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>jet</b> somewhere, you travel there in a fast plane. 乘噴氣式飛機前往","examples":["The president will be jetting off to Germany today. 總統今天要乘噴氣式飛機去德國。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to issue or cause to issue in a jet 噴出; 使噴出","examples":[]}]}]},"jar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玻璃罐，廣口瓶；一瓶，一罐（的量或物）；震動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撞擊，震動；刺激，對……產生不好的影響；不和諧，不相配；發出刺耳聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jar</b> is a glass container with a lid that is used for storing food. (用於存放食物的) 玻璃罐","examples":["...cucumbers in glass jars. …玻璃罐裡的黃瓜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>jar</b> to refer to a jar and its contents, or to the contents only. 一罐的量或物","examples":["She opened up a jar of plums. 她開啟了一罐李子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(of a door) slightly open; ajar (門)微開的","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a jolt or shock 顛簸; 搖晃","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>jars</b>, or <b>jars</b> you, you find it unpleasant, disturbing, or shocking. 令人不快; 產生不快影響","examples":["...televised congressional hearings that jarred the nation's faith in the presidency. …令國民對總統執政產生動搖的電視國會聽證會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>jars</b>, or if something <b>jars</b> it, the object moves with a fairly hard shaking movement. 震動","examples":["The ship jarred a little. 船輕微震了一下。","The sudden movement jarred the box and it fell off the table. 這突然一動震動了那個箱子，然後它從桌上掉了下去。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人不快的","examples":["In the context of this chapter, Dore's comments strike a jarring note. 在本章的語境中，多爾的評論顯得刺耳。"]}]}]},"kangaroo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"袋鼠，大袋鼠（原產於澳大利亞和新幾內亞的大型有袋類動物，後肢強健善跳躍，雌獸腹部有育兒袋）；袋鼠肉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（汽車）因離合控制不當而前移；使（汽車）突然猛地短距離前移；對嬰兒進行袋鼠式護理；捕獵袋鼠；像袋鼠一樣蹦跳移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kangaroo</b> is a large Australian animal which moves by jumping on its back legs. Female kangaroos carry their babies in a pouch on their stomach. 袋鼠","examples":[]}]}]},"jungle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（熱帶）叢林；弱肉強食的地方；雜草叢生的地方；雜亂無章的一堆；叢林音樂（一種快速舞蹈音樂）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jungle</b> is a forest in a tropical country where large numbers of tall trees and plants grow very close together. 叢林","examples":["...the mountains and jungles of Papua New Guinea. …巴布亞紐幾內亞的山脈和叢林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place as <b>a</b> <b>jungle</b>, you are emphasizing that it is full of lots of things and very messy. 雜亂之地","examples":["...a jungle of stuffed sofas, stuffed birds, knick-knacks, potted plants. …一個堆滿沙發、標本鳥、小擺設、盆栽植物的雜亂之地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>a</b> <b>jungle</b>, you dislike it because it is complicated and difficult to get what you want from it. 一團糟","examples":["Social Security law and procedure remain a jungle of complex rules. 社會保障法律和程式仍然是充滿複雜規定的一團糟。"]}]}]},"kilogram":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"千克，公斤（=kilogramme）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kilogram</b> is a metric unit of weight. One kilogram is a thousand grams, or a thousandth of a metric ton, and is equal to 2.2 pounds. 公斤","examples":["...a parcel weighing around 4.5 kilograms. …一個重約4.5公斤的包裹。"]}]}]},"journal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雜誌，期刊，報紙；日記，日誌；（會計）日記賬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>journal</b> is a magazine, especially one that deals with a specialized subject. 期刊","examples":["All our results are published in scientific journals. 我們所有的結果都發表在科學刊物上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>journal</b> is a daily or weekly newspaper. The word journal is often used in the name of the paper. 日報; 週報","examples":["...ads in The New York Times, the Wall Street Journal and other publications. …紐約時報、華爾街日報和其他出版物上的廣告。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>journal</b> is an account that you write of your daily activities. 日記","examples":["Sara confided to her journal. 薩拉在日記中傾吐心事。"]}]}]},"kettle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水壺；鍋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kettle</b> is a covered container that you use for boiling water. It has a handle, and a spout for the water to come out of. 水壺","examples":["I'll put the kettle on and make us some tea. 我來燒壺水給咱們沏點兒茶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>kettle</b> <b>of</b> water is the amount of water contained in a kettle. 一壺的量","examples":["Pour a kettle of boiling water over the onions. 往這些洋蔥上倒一壺開水。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a different kettle of fish</b>, you mean that it is very different from another related thing that you are talking about. 兩碼事","examples":["Banking today is a very different kettle of fish from the industry of the past. 如今的銀行業與過去的已是兩碼事了。"]}]}]},"junk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廢舊雜物；垃圾，破爛；毫無價值的事物；<非正式>毒品，（尤指）海洛因；中國式帆船；（含有鯨腦油的）抹香鯨頭部纖維組織"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>拋棄，丟掉（廢舊物品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Junk</b> is old and used things that have little value and that you do not want any more. 廢舊物品","examples":["Rose finds her furniture in junk shops. 羅絲在舊貨店裡找到她的傢俱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any narcotic drug, esp heroin 毒品(尤指海洛因)","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a sailing vessel used in Chinese waters and characterized by a very high poop, flat bottom, and square sails supported by battens 中國式帆船","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>junk</b> something, you get rid of it or stop using it. 丟掉","examples":["Consumers will not have to junk their old cassettes to use the new format. 消費者們將不必為了使用新制式而丟掉他們的老盒式磁帶。"]}]}]},"keyboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（打字機或計算機的）鍵盤；（鋼琴或風琴的）琴鍵；鍵盤樂器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用鍵盤輸入；用鍵盤操作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>keyboard</b> of a typewriter or computer is the set of keys that you press in order to operate it. (打字機、計算機等的) 鍵盤","examples":["He was in his office, battering the keyboard of his computer as if it were an old manual typewriter. 他在辦公室重重地敲打著他的計算機鍵盤，好像在用一部老式的手動打字機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>keyboard</b> of a piano or organ is the set of black and white keys that you press in order to play it. (鋼琴等的) 鍵盤","examples":["Tanya's hands rippled over the keyboard. 坦尼婭的雙手在鍵盤上起伏擺動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People sometimes refer to musical instruments that have a keyboard as <b>keyboards</b>. 鍵盤樂器","examples":["...Sean O'Hagan on keyboards. …演奏鍵盤樂器的肖恩·奧黑根。"]}]}]},"kidney":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腎，腎臟；（食用的）動物腰子；性格，脾氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>kidneys</b> are the organs in your body that take waste matter from your blood and send it out of your body as urine. 腎臟","examples":["...a kidney transplant. …一次腎臟移植。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Kidneys</b> are the kidneys of an animal, for example a lamb, calf, or pig, that are eaten as meat. 腰子","examples":["...lambs' kidneys. …羊腰子。"]}]}]},"journey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行，旅程；歷程，過程"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"旅行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you make a <b>journey</b>, you travel from one place to another. 旅行","examples":["There is an express service from Paris that completes the journey to Bordeaux in under 4 hours. 有一趟從巴黎開出的快車，到波爾多全程不到4小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a person's experience of changing or developing from one state of mind to another as a <b>journey</b>. (心路) 歷程","examples":["My films try to describe a journey of discovery, both for myself and the viewer. 我的影片力圖為我自己和觀眾描述一段自我發現的心路歷程。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>journey</b> somewhere, you travel there. 旅行","examples":["In February 1935, Naomi journeyed to the United States for the first time. 1935年2月，內奧米第一次踏入美國。"]}]}]},"km":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（計量）公里，千米（kilometer）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>km</b> is a written abbreviation for . 公里","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Comoros 葛摩","examples":[]}]}]},"kilometer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"千米，公里（同 kilometre）"}],"sections":[]},"justice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公平，正義；公道，合理；司法，法律制裁；<美>法官"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Justice</b> is fairness in the way that people are treated. 公正","examples":["He has a good overall sense of justice and fairness. 他有良好的公正和公平的整體意識。","He only wants freedom, justice and equality. 他只要自由、公正和平等。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>justice</b> <b>of</b> a cause, claim, or argument is its quality of being reasonable, fair, or right. 正當性","examples":["We are a minority and must convince people of the justice of our cause. 我們是少數，必須讓人們相信我們動機的正當性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Justice</b> is the legal system that a country uses in order to deal with people who break the law. 司法","examples":["Many in Toronto's black community feel that the justice system does not treat them fairly. 多倫多黑人社群的很多人覺得司法制度對他們不公正。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>justice</b> is a judge. 法官","examples":["Thomas will be sworn in today as a justice on the Supreme Court. 托馬斯將在今天宣誓就任最高法院法官。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Justice</b> is used before the names of judges. 法官 (表示頭銜)","examples":["A preliminary hearing was due to start today before Justice Hutchison, but was adjourned. 預審原定由哈奇森法官今天開始審理，但延期了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a criminal is <b>brought to justice</b>, he or she is punished for a crime by being arrested and tried in a court of law. 依法懲處","examples":["They demanded that those responsible be brought to justice. 他們要求那些責任人應依法予以懲處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>do justice</b> to a person or thing means to reproduce them accurately and show how good they are. 準確再現優點","examples":["The photograph I had seen didn't do her justice. 我看到的那張照片不如她本人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>do justice</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you deal with them properly and completely. 恰如其分地處理","examples":["No one article can ever do justice to the topic of fraud. 沒有一篇文章能恰如其分地處理欺詐這一主題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>do</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>justice</b>, you do something as well as you are capable of doing it. 充分發揮某人能力","examples":["I don't think he did himself justice in the game today. 我認為今天他在比賽中沒有充分發揮出自己的實力。"]}]}]},"kit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成套工具，成套裝置；配套元件；<英>全套衣服及裝備；成套資料，成套材料；<英>（尤指盛魚的）大籃子，箱子；（尤指職業舞蹈教師用的）小型小提琴；（海狸、白鼬、貂等動物的）幼崽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝備；預備"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kit</b> is a group of items that are kept together, often in the same container, because they are all used for similar purposes. 成套用具","examples":["Make sure you keep a well-stocked first aid kit ready to deal with any emergency. 確保你有一套足夠庫存的急救用具，隨時應對任何突發情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>kit</b> is a set of parts that can be put together in order to make something. 配套元件","examples":["Her popular potholder is also available in do-it-yourself kits. 在自己動手的配套元件中也有她最喜歡的防燙布墊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Kit</b> is special clothing and equipment that you use when you take part in a particular activity, especially a sport. 裝束","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a cub of various small mammals, such as the ferret or fox 幼仔","examples":[]}]}]},"knob":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"球形把手；旋鈕；<英>小塊（黃油等）；球形突出物；<英，非正式>陰莖；<美>圓形小山"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>knob</b> is a round handle on a door or drawer which you use in order to open or close it. 球形把手","examples":["He turned the knob and pushed against the door. 他轉動門把手，推了那扇門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>knob</b> is a round switch on a piece of machinery or equipment. 旋鈕","examples":["...the volume knob. …音量旋鈕。"]}]}]},"knight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"騎士，武士；（國際象棋中的）馬；爵士（其名前冠以 Sir）；代表郡或縣的議會議員；<文>護花使者，（事業的）投身者；（古羅馬）騎士階層，（古希臘）雅典的第二等公民"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"封（某人）為爵士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In medieval times, a <b>knight</b> was a man of noble birth, who served his king or lord in battle. (中世紀的) 騎士","examples":["...King Arthur's faithful knight, Gawain. …亞瑟王的忠實騎士高文。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In chess, a <b>knight</b> is a piece which is shaped like a horse's head. (國際象棋中的) 馬","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is knighted</b>, they are given a knighthood. 授予爵士稱號","examples":["He was knighted in June 1988. 他於1988年6月被授予爵士稱號。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>knight in shining armour</b>, you mean that they are kind and brave, and likely to rescue you from a difficult situation. 困境中救助人的勇士","examples":["The love songs tricked us all into believing in happy endings and knights in shining armour. 那些情歌騙我們都去相信有幸福的結局和於危難中救助我們的勇士。"]}]}]},"knit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"編織，針織；織平針；（使）緊密結合；（骨頭）癒合；皺緊，皺（眉）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"編織的衣物，織物；編織法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knit</b> something, especially an article of clothing, you make it from wool or a similar thread by using two knitting needles or a machine. 編織","examples":["I had endless hours to knit and sew. 我有無數的時間來縫縫織織。","I have already started knitting baby clothes. 我已經開始織嬰兒的衣服了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>knits</b> things or people <b>together</b>, they make them fit or work together closely and successfully. 緊密連線","examples":["The best thing about sports is that they knit the whole family close together. 體育運動最大的好處就是將全家緊密連線在一起。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Knit</b> is also a combining form. 編織 (用於合成詞中)","examples":["Ferris wore a heavy knit sweater. 菲立斯穿著一件織得厚厚的毛衣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Knit</b> is also a combining form. 緊密連線 (用於合成詞中)","examples":["...a closer-knit family. …一個連線更為緊密的家庭。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When broken bones <b>knit</b>, the broken pieces grow together again. (骨頭) 癒合","examples":["The bone hasn't knitted together properly. 骨頭還沒有完全癒合。"]}]}]},"laundry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"待洗（或正在洗滌、洗完）的衣物；洗衣房，洗衣店；洗衣物，洗衣物的活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Laundry</b> is used to refer to clothes, sheets, and towels that are about to be washed, are being washed, or have just been washed. (待洗、正在洗或剛洗過的) 衣物","examples":["I'll do your laundry. 我會給你洗衣服的。","...the room where I hang the laundry. …我晾衣服的房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>laundry</b> is a business that washes and irons clothes, sheets, and towels for people. 洗衣店","examples":["We had to have the washing done at the laundry. 我們不得不把衣服放在洗衣店裡洗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>laundry</b> or a <b>laundry room</b> is a room in a house, hotel, or institution where clothes, sheets, and towels are washed. 洗衣間","examples":["He worked in the laundry at Oxford prison. 他曾在牛津監獄的洗衣房工作。"]}]}]},"laughter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"笑，笑聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Laughter</b> is the sound of people laughing, for example, because they are amused or happy. 笑聲","examples":["Their laughter filled the corridor. 他們的笑聲充滿了走廊。","He delivered the line perfectly, and everybody roared with laughter. 他完美地演繹了這句臺詞，所有的人都哈哈大笑起來。"]}]}]},"ladder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"梯子；（職位晉升的）階梯，（發展的）階段；<英>（織物）抽絲，脫線；（體育競賽中的）階梯晉級賽；梯狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（褲襪等）抽絲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ladder</b> is a piece of equipment used for climbing up something or down from something. It consists of two long pieces of wood, metal, or rope with steps fixed between them. 梯子","examples":["He climbed the ladder to the next deck. 他登上梯子爬到了上一層甲板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>the</b> <b>ladder</b> to refer to something such as a society, organization, or system which has different levels that people can progress up or drop down. 階梯","examples":["If they want to climb the ladder of success they should be given that opportunity. 如果他們想攀登成功的階梯，他們應該被給與那個機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>ladder</b> is a hole or torn part in a woman's stocking or tights, where some of the vertical threads have broken, leaving only the horizontal threads. (長筒絲襪等的) 脫絲","examples":["I had a ladder in my stocking. 我的長筒襪有抽絲了。"]}]}]},"knot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（用繩索等打的）結，絞成亂團的頭髮（線等）；節子，節疤；（身體某部位的）痙攣，難受；節（速度計量單位，每小時一海里）；髮髻；一小群人；（肌肉上的）硬結，隆起物；飾帶；測速繩節"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打結，（使）纏結；（因害怕、激動等而）痙攣，緊縮；打發髻；使比分持平"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tie a <b>knot</b> in a piece of string, rope, cloth, or other material, you pass one end or part of it through a loop and pull it tight. 結","examples":["One lace had broken and been tied in a knot. 一根帶子已經斷了，被打成一個結。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a tangle, as in hair or string (頭髮或絲絃上的)結","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you feel a <b>knot</b> in your stomach, you get an uncomfortable tight feeling in your stomach, usually because you are afraid or excited. 痙攣","examples":["There was a knot of tension in his stomach. 他心裡一陣緊張。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>knot</b> in a piece of wood is a small hard area where a branch grew. 節疤","examples":["A carpenter often rejects half his wood because of knots or cracks. 木匠常常因為有節疤或裂縫而把一半的木材都扔掉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>knot</b> is a unit of speed. The speed of ships, aircraft, and wind is measured in knots. 節 (航速和風速單位)","examples":["They travel at speeds of up to 30 knots. 他們以高達30節的航速行進。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a small northern sandpiper, <b>Calidris canutus,</b> with a short bill and grey plumage 磯鷂","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knot</b> a piece of string, rope, cloth, or other material, you pass one end or part of it through a loop and pull it tight. 把…打成結","examples":["He knotted the laces securely together. 他把帶子牢牢地系在一起。","He knotted the bandanna around his neck. 他把印花大圍巾系在他的脖子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your stomach <b>knots</b> or if something <b>knots</b> it, it feels tight because you are afraid or excited. 使 (心) 揪緊; 揪緊","examples":["I felt my stomach knot with apprehension. 我感到心裡因為擔心而揪緊。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If part of your face or your muscles <b>knot</b>, they become tense, usually because you are worried or angry. (臉部或肌肉) 緊皺","examples":["His forehead knotted in a frown. 他的眉頭緊皺。"]}]}]},"label":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"標籤，標牌；稱號，綽號；商標，品牌；唱片公司；（計算機）標記；示蹤劑；帶垂飾的橫帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"貼標籤；把……不公正地稱為；用示蹤劑使（物質等）示蹤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>label</b> is a piece of paper or plastic that is attached to an object in order to give information about it. 標籤","examples":["He peered at the label on the bottle. 他注視著瓶子上的標籤。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is labelled</b>, a label is attached to it giving information about it. 貼標籤於","examples":["It requires foreign frozen-food imports to be clearly labelled. 它要求外國進口冷凍食品要貼上明確的標籤。","The produce was labelled \"Made in China.\" 該產品上貼有“中國製造”的標籤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>is labelled</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing, you mean that people generally describe them that way and you think that this is unfair. 把…稱為","examples":["It won't be labelled in any way as a military expedition. 它無論如何也稱不上是一次軍事遠征。","It does not matter whether these duties are labelled \"duties\" or \"tasks\". 這些義務被稱作“義務”還是“任務”都無關緊要。"]}]}]},"lawn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"草坪，草地；上等細棉布，上等細麻布"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lawn</b> is an area of grass that is kept cut short and is usually part of someone's garden, or part of a park. 草坪","examples":["They were sitting on the lawn under a large beech tree. 他們當時正坐在一棵大山毛櫸樹下的草坪上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a fine linen or cotton fabric, used for clothing (衣服用)細麻","examples":[]}]}]},"lace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網眼織物，蕾絲；鞋帶，繫帶；少量烈酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用繫帶束緊，用鞋帶系（鞋）；把（少量酒、藥品或毒藥等烈性物質）摻入；使編織（或交織、纏繞）在一起；加入……使有味（或有趣）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lace</b> is a very delicate cloth which is made with a lot of holes in it. It is made by twisting together very fine threads of cotton to form decorative patterns. 花邊","examples":["She finally found the perfect gown, a beautiful creation trimmed with lace. 她最終找到了那件完美的大衣，款式漂亮、飾有花邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Laces</b> are thin pieces of material that are put through special holes in some types of clothing, especially shoes. The laces are tied together in order to tighten the clothing. 繫帶","examples":["Barry was sitting on the bed, tying the laces of an old pair of running shoes. 巴里正坐在床上系一雙舊跑鞋的鞋帶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lace</b> something such as a pair of shoes, you tighten the shoes by pulling the laces through the holes, and usually tying them together. 系…的帶子","examples":["I have a good pair of skates, but no matter how tightly I lace them, my ankles wobble. 我有一雙很好的溜冰鞋，但是無論我把鞋帶系得多麼緊，我的腳踝還是在裡面晃盪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>lace</b> food or drink with a substance such as alcohol or a drug means to put a small amount of the substance into the food or drink. 在 (食物、飲料) 中新增","examples":["She laced his food with sleeping pills. 她在他的食物里加了安眠藥。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lace up</b> means the same as . 系…的帶子 (同)(lace)","examples":["He sat on the steps, and laced up his boots. 他坐在臺階上繫好靴子。"]}]}]},"leather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"皮，皮革；（騎摩托車穿的）皮衣，皮夾克"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>抽打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leather</b> is treated animal skin, usually from cows, which is used for making shoes, clothes, bags, and furniture. 皮革","examples":["He wore a leather jacket and dark trousers. 他穿著皮夾克和黑褲子。"]}]}]},"leak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"滲入，漏出；漏，滲漏；洩露，透露"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"漏洞，裂縫；洩漏出的液體（或氣體）；洩密；<俚>撒尿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a container <b>leaks</b>, there is a hole or crack in it which lets a substance such as liquid or gas escape. You can also say that a container <b>leaks</b> a substance such as liquid or gas. 滲漏 (液體或氣體); (容器) 滲漏","examples":["The roof leaked. 屋頂漏了。","The pool's fibreglass sides had cracked and the water had leaked out. 池子的玻璃纖維側面裂了，水已經滲了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a secret document or piece of information <b>leaks</b> or <b>is leaked</b>, someone lets the public know about it. 洩露","examples":["Mr. Ashton accused police of leaking information to the press. 艾什頓先生指控警察向媒體洩露了訊息。","We don't know how the transcript leaked. 我們不知道抄本是怎樣洩露的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leak</b> is also a noun. 滲漏","examples":["It's thought a gas leak may have caused the blast. 人們認為可能是煤氣洩漏引起了爆炸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>leak</b> is a crack, hole, or other gap that a substance such as a liquid or gas can pass through. 裂縫; 漏洞","examples":["...a leak in the radiator. …散熱器上的裂縫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Leak</b> is also a noun. 洩露","examples":["More serious leaks, possibly involving national security, are likely to be investigated by the police. 可能涉及國家安全的更嚴重洩密會受到警方的調查。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leak out</b> means the same as . 洩露","examples":["More details are now beginning to leak out. 更多的細節現在開始洩露出來。"]}]}]},"librarian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖書館館長，圖書館管理員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>librarian</b> is a person who is in charge of a library or who has been specially trained to work in a library. 圖書管理員","examples":["The new librarian is a friend of mine. 這位新來的圖書管理員是我的朋友。"]}]}]},"lifeboat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（航海）救生艇：船上配備的小型船隻，供船舶遇險時人員撤離或海上救援使用；救生船：由港口或海岸派出、用於救助海上遇險人員的中型船隻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lifeboat</b> is a medium-sized boat that is sent out from a port or harbour in order to rescue people who are in danger at sea. 救生船","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lifeboat</b> is a small boat that is carried on a ship, which people on the ship use to escape when the ship is in danger of sinking. 救生艇","examples":["The captain ordered all passengers and crew into lifeboats. 船長命令所有的乘客和船員上救生艇。"]}]}]},"lifeguard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"救生員；（舊）警衛"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"當救生員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lifeguard</b> is a person who works at a beach or swimming pool and rescues people when they are in danger of drowning. 救生員","examples":[]}]}]},"leisure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"閒暇，業餘時間；休閒活動"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"空閒的，有閒的；業餘的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leisure</b> is the time when you are not working and you can relax and do things that you enjoy. 空閒時間","examples":["...a relaxing way to fill my leisure time. …我消磨空閒時間的一種放鬆方式。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does something <b>at leisure</b> or <b>at</b> their <b>leisure</b>, they enjoy themselves by doing it when they want to, without hurrying. 悠閒地","examples":["You will be able to stroll at leisure through the gardens. 你將能在花園裡悠閒地散步。"]}]}]},"lens":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"透鏡，鏡片；（相機的）鏡頭；（眼球的）晶狀體；隱形眼鏡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……攝影"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lens</b> is a thin curved piece of glass or plastic used in things such as cameras, telescopes, and pairs of glasses. You look through a lens in order to make things look larger, smaller, or clearer. 鏡頭","examples":["...a camera lens. …一個照相機鏡頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In your eye, the <b>lens</b> is the part behind the pupil that focuses light and helps you to see clearly. (眼睛的) 晶狀體","examples":["...degenerative changes in the lens of the eye. …眼睛晶狀體的退化。"]}]}]},"leap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛衝，突然而迅速地移動；劇增，猛漲；趕緊抓住（機會）；（心）猛跳；跳，跳躍"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跳躍，跳高；驟變，激增；（對新事物的）認真嘗試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>leap</b>, you jump high in the air or jump a long distance. 跳躍","examples":["He leaped in the air and waved his fists to the fans as he ran out of the stadium. 他跑出體育館，跳起來向他的崇拜者們揮舞著拳頭。","Frederick leaped 22 feet, 7¼ inches on his second attempt. 弗雷德裡克第2次試跳跳了22英尺7.25英寸。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leap</b> is also a noun. 跳躍","examples":["The suspect took a leap out of a third-storey window. 那個犯罪嫌疑人從三樓的視窗跳了出去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>leap</b> is a large and important change, increase, or advance. 鉅變; 劇增","examples":["The result has been a giant leap in productivity. 其結果就是生產力的大幅度提高。","...the leap in the unemployed from 35,000 to 75,000. …失業人數從3.5萬人猛增到7.5萬人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>leap</b> somewhere, you move there suddenly and quickly. 急速移動","examples":["The two men leaped into the jeep and roared off. 那兩個人飛快地跳上吉普車呼嘯而去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>leaps</b> somewhere, it moves there in a short sudden movement. (車輛) 突然移動","examples":["The car leaped forward. 汽車突然向前衝去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>leap</b> <b>to</b> a particular place or position, you make a large and important change, increase, or advance. 鉅變; 劇增","examples":["Bush's approval rating leaped to an astounding 88 percent. 布什的支援率令人吃驚地劇增到了88%。"]}]}]},"liar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"騙子，說謊者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>liar</b>, you mean that they tell lies. 說謊的人","examples":["He was a liar and a cheat. 他是一個說謊的人，一個騙子。"]}]}]},"lifetime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一生，終生；壽命，有效期，使用期；很長一段時間"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一生的，終身的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lifetime</b> is the length of time that someone is alive. 一生","examples":["During my lifetime I haven't got around to much travelling. 我一生中沒有旅行過多少。","...a trust fund to be administered throughout his wife's lifetime. …在他妻子一生中都要管理的一份信託基金。"]}]}]},"liberty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自由，自由權；（某種）合法權利；冒犯行為（或言語），失禮；意志自由，選擇自由；<非正式> 自以為是的言語，專斷的行動；（水手的）上岸休假"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Liberty</b> is the freedom to live your life in the way that you want, without interference from other people or the authorities. 自由","examples":["...the ideal of equality and the appreciation of liberty. …對平等的嚮往及對自由的欣賞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Liberty</b> is the freedom to go wherever you want, which you lose when you are a prisoner. 人身自由","examples":["Why not say that three convictions before court for stealing cars means three months' loss of liberty. 為什麼不說法庭上關於盜車的3項判決就意味著失去了3個月的人身自由。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>at liberty</b> <b>to</b> do something, they have been given permission to do it. 獲得許可的","examples":["The island's in the Pacific Ocean; I'm not at liberty to say exactly where, because we're still negotiating for its purchase. 這個島嶼在太平洋上；我還不能說具體在哪裡，因為我們仍然在就它的購買問題進行談判。"]}]}]},"lighthouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燈塔（建於海岸或小島上，裝有強光燈具的塔式航標，用於引導船舶或警示航行危險）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lighthouse</b> is a tower containing a powerful flashing lamp that is built on the coast or on a small island. Lighthouses are used to guide ships or to warn them of danger. 燈塔","examples":[]}]}]},"linen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"亞麻布；家庭日用織品；<舊>內衣褲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"亞麻的，亞麻布制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Linen</b> is a kind of cloth that is made from a plant called flax. It is used for making clothes and things such as tablecloths and sheets. 亞麻布","examples":["...a white linen suit. …一套白色亞麻衣服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Linen</b> is tablecloths, sheets, pillowcases, and similar things made of cloth that are used in the home. 亞麻織品","examples":["...embroidered bed linen. …刺繡的亞麻布床上用品。"]}]}]},"lipstick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口紅，唇膏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lipstick</b> is a coloured substance in the form of a stick which women put on their lips. 唇膏","examples":["She was wearing red lipstick. 她塗著紅色唇膏。"]}]}]},"limb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肢；大樹枝；（某物的）突出部，延伸部分；十字形四個分支中的一個；弓把的上部（或下部）；（日月等天體的）邊緣；冠簷，萼簷；（管狀花的）瓣片；（四分儀等科學儀器上測量角度的）分度弧"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"切斷……的手足；從……上截下樹枝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>limbs</b> are your arms and legs. 四肢","examples":["She would be able to stretch out her cramped limbs and rest for a few hours. 她將可以伸開蜷縮的四肢，休息幾個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the edge of the apparent disc of the sun, a moon, or a planet (星體盤面的)邊緣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone goes <b>out on a limb</b>, they do something they strongly believe in even though it is risky or extreme, and is likely to fail or be criticized by other people. (因大膽冒險而) 處於困境","examples":["They can see themselves going out on a limb, voting for a very controversial energy bill. 他們會發現自己由於投票贊成一個有爭議的能源法案而陷入困境。"]}]}]},"lobster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"龍蝦；（食用）龍蝦肉；<澳，紐西蘭>小龍蝦；龍蝦紅；<澳新>小龍蝦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捕龍蝦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lobster</b> is a sea creature that has a hard shell, two large claws, and eight legs. 龍蝦","examples":["She sold me a couple of live lobsters. 她賣給了我幾隻活龍蝦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lobster</b> is the flesh of a lobster eaten as food. 龍蝦肉","examples":["...lobster on a bed of fresh vegetables. …放在一層新鮮蔬菜上的龍蝦肉。"]}]}]},"lollipop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棒棒糖（=lollypop）；<英>棒冰；<非正式>通俗易懂的短小古典音樂樂曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lollipop</b> is a sweet consisting of a hard disc or ball of a sugary substance on the end of a stick. 棒棒糖","examples":[]}]}]},"loudspeaker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴音器，喇叭；<舊>（收音機或樂器的）揚聲器，喇叭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>loudspeaker</b> is a piece of electronic equipment that forms part of a public address system and transmits sound. 揚聲器","examples":["The loudspeaker announced the arrival of the train. 廣播說火車進站了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>loudspeaker</b> is a piece of equipment, for example, part of a radio or hi-fi system, through which sound comes out. 喇叭","examples":[]}]}]},"lobby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遊說（政治家或政府）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"遊說團體，活動集團；大堂，大廳；（旨在對政治家施加影響的）遊說；（英國議會的）接見廳，表決廳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lobby</b> someone such as a member of a government or council, you try to persuade them that a particular law should be changed or that a particular thing should be done. 遊說","examples":["The Wilderness Society lobbied Congress to authorize the Endangered Species Act. 荒野協會遊說國會批准《瀕危物種法》。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lobby</b> is a group of people who represent a particular organization or campaign, and try to persuade a government or council to help or support them. 遊說團體","examples":["Agricultural interests are some of the most powerful lobbies in Washington. 農業利益集團是華盛頓最有影響力的遊說團體中的一部分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a hotel or other large building, the <b>lobby</b> is the area near the entrance that usually has corridors and staircases leading off it. 大廳","examples":["I met her in the lobby of the museum. 我在博物館大廳遇到了她。"]}]}]},"luggage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行李；精神負擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Luggage</b> is the suitcases and bags that you take with you when travel. 行李","examples":["Leave your luggage in the hotel. 把你的行李留在旅館吧。"]}]}]},"lullaby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"搖籃曲，催眠曲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕>唱搖籃曲使（人）入睡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lullaby</b> is a quiet song which is intended to be sung to babies and young children to help them go to sleep. 搖籃曲; 催眠曲","examples":[]}]}]},"liver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肝臟；（供食用的）動物肝臟；生活者，居民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>liver</b> is a large organ in your body which processes your blood and helps to clean unwanted substances out of it. 肝臟","examples":["Three weeks ago, it was discovered the cancer had spread to his liver. 三週前，發現癌已擴散到了他的肝臟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Liver</b> is the liver of some animals, especially lambs, pigs, and cows, which is cooked and eaten. (供食用的動物) 肝臟","examples":["...grilled calves' liver. …烤牛肝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a person who lives in a specified way 以某種方式生活的人","examples":[]}]}]},"lord":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主，上帝；（英國）貴族，勳爵；大人，閣下（英國對某些官員的尊稱）；（中世紀歐洲的）領主，莊園主；（英國）上議院議員；（某一領域的）巨頭，巨擘"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對某人舉止霸道（或逞威風）；把……封為貴族"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"天哪，上帝啊（表示對某事的驚訝、惱怒或憂慮）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lord</b> is a man who has a high rank in the nobility, for example, an earl, a viscount, or a marquis. 貴族","examples":["She married a lord and lives in this huge house in the Cotswolds. 她嫁給了一個貴族，現住在科茨沃爾德的這所大房子裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the Christian church, people refer to God and to Jesus Christ as the <b>Lord</b>. 上帝; 耶穌","examples":["I know the Lord will look after him. 我知道上帝會照顧他的。","She prayed now. \"Lord, help me to find courage.\" 這時她祈禱道：“上帝啊，賜給我勇氣吧。”"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lord</b> is used in exclamations such as \"<b>good Lord!</b>\" and \"<b>oh Lord!</b>\" to express surprise, shock, frustration, or annoyance about something. (表示吃驚、震驚或懊惱) 天哪","examples":["\"Good lord, that's what he is: he's a policeman.\" “天哪，原來他是幹這個的，他是個警察。”"]}]}]},"lung":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肺；呼吸器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>lungs</b> are the two organs inside your chest which fill with air when you breathe in. 肺","examples":["...a smoker who died of lung cancer. …一位死於肺癌的吸菸者。"]}]}]},"litter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公共場所內亂扔的）垃圾，廢棄物；一堆雜亂的東西；（同時出生的）一窩（小動物）；貓砂；（森林裡的）落葉，落葉層；（家畜睡覺用的）褥草，墊草；轎子；擔架"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"散亂覆蓋；（在公共場所）亂扔（垃圾）；使（某事物）充滿；（狗、貓等動物）產仔；<古>（為馬或其他動物）鋪褥草"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Litter</b> is rubbish or waste that is left lying around outside. 垃圾","examples":["If you see litter in the corridor, pick it up. 如果你看到走廊裡有垃圾，就把它撿起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>litter</b> is a group of animals born to the same mother at the same time. 一窩","examples":["...a litter of pups. …一窩小狗。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a number of things <b>litter</b> a place, they are scattered around it or over it. 散放在","examples":["Glass from broken bottles litters the sidewalk. 碎瓶子的玻璃渣散落在人行道上。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"散放的","examples":["The entrance hall is littered with toys. 入口大廳裡散落著玩具。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>littered with</b> things, it contains many examples of it. 充滿的","examples":["History is littered with men and women spurred into achievement by a father's disregard. 歷史上常有受父親漠視的刺激而取得成就的男男女女。"]}]}]},"magnet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磁體，磁鐵；有吸引力的人（或地方、事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>magnet</b> or is like a <b>magnet</b>, you mean that people are very attracted by it and want to go to it or look at it. 有吸引力的事物","examples":["Prospect Park, with its vast lake, is a magnet for all health freaks. 擁有大片湖區的展望公園是所有健身迷的嚮往之地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>magnet</b> is a piece of iron or other material which attracts iron toward it. 磁體","examples":["It's possible to hang a nail from a magnet and then use that nail to pick up another nail. 把一顆釘子掛在一個磁體上再用這顆釘子去吸起另一顆釘子是可能的。"]}]}]},"maid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女僕，女傭；<舊>少女，年輕姑娘；<古>處女"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>maid</b> is a woman who works as a servant in a hotel or private house. 女侍者; 女僕","examples":["A maid brought me breakfast at nine o'clock. 一個女侍者9點鐘給我送來了早餐。"]}]}]},"load":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"負載，重荷；一批待洗的衣物；工作量；發電量，電荷；承載量；大量，許多；負擔，壓力；胡說八道，廢話"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝上，裝進；承載，裝載；大量給予；裝上（底片），上（子彈）；滿（壘）；載入（計算機程式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>load</b> a vehicle or a container, you put a large quantity of things into it. (向車輛或容器裡) 大量裝入","examples":["The three men seemed to have finished loading the truck. 這3個人好像已經裝好了那輛卡車。","Mr. Dambar had loaded his plate with lasagne. 丹巴先生已經往他的盤子裡盛了很多義大利千層麵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>loads</b> a weapon such as a gun, they put a bullet or missile in it so that it is ready to use. (給武器) 裝彈藥","examples":["I knew how to load and handle a gun. 我知道怎麼裝子彈和使用槍支。","He carried a loaded gun. 他帶著一支裝了子彈的槍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>load</b> a camera or other piece of equipment means to put film, tape, or data into it so that it is ready to use. 裝填 (膠捲、磁帶或資料)","examples":["A photographer from the newspaper was loading his camera with film. 那家報社的一個攝影師正在給他的攝像機裝膠捲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>load</b> is something, usually a large quantity or heavy object, which is being carried. 裝載物","examples":["He drove by with a big load of hay. 他開著裝滿乾草的車過去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the amount of work you have to do as a <b>load</b>. 工作量","examples":["She's taking some of the load off the secretaries. 她正給秘書們減少一些工作量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>load</b> of a system or piece of equipment, especially a system supplying electricity or a computer, is the extent to which it is being used at a particular time. 負荷量","examples":["An efficient bulb may lighten the load of power stations. 節能燈可減輕發電站的負荷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>load</b> <b>on</b> something is the amount of weight that is pressing down on it or the amount of strain that it is under. 壓力","examples":["Some of these chairs have flattened feet which spread the load on the ground. 這些椅子中有些是平腳的，這樣可分散地面所受的壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to <b>a load of</b> people or things or <b>loads of</b> them, you are emphasizing that there are a lot of them. 許多","examples":["I've got loads of money. 我有許多錢。","...a load of kids. …許多小孩。"]}]}]},"mall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"購物中心，步行商業區；（有遮蔽設施的）步行道，散步場所；鐵圈球球場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mall</b> is a very large, enclosed shopping area. 大型購物區","examples":[]}]}]},"mankind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人類；<古>男人，男子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to all human beings as <b>mankind</b> when considering them as a group. Some people dislike this use. 人類","examples":["...the evolution of mankind. …人類的進化。"]}]}]},"manager":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司、部門等的）經理；（藝人或運動員的）經紀人；（運動隊的）管理人，主教練；管理某物的人；（計算機）管理程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>manager</b> is a person who is responsible for running part of or the whole of a business organization. 經理","examples":["The chef, staff, and managers are all Chinese. 廚師、工作人員和經理都是中國人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>manager</b> of a pop star or other entertainer is the person who takes care of their business interests. (明星等藝人的) 經紀人","examples":["...the star's manager and agent, Anne Chudleigh. …那位明星的經紀人兼代理人安妮·查德利。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>manager</b> of a sports team is the person responsible for training the players and organizing the way they play. (棒球隊) 教練","examples":["The team expects to have a new manager before spring training. 隊員們期待著春訓前能有一位新的教練。"]}]}]},"manners":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禮貌，禮節，規矩（manner 的複數）；行為舉止，待人接物；社會風俗；bad manners：無禮，失禮；table manners：餐桌禮儀；（Manners）曼納斯（姓氏）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"social conduct 社會行為","examples":[]}]}]},"majority":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大多數；<英>多數票；成年的法定年齡；多數黨；少校軍銜，少校職位"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多數人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>majority</b> of people or things in a group is more than half of them. 多數","examples":["The majority of my patients come to me from out of town. 我的多數病人來自市區外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>majority</b> is the difference between the number of votes or seats in a legislature or parliament that the winner gets in an election, and the number of votes or seats that the next person or party gets. 多得的票數; 多獲得的席位","examples":["Members of parliament approved the move by a majority of ninety-nine. 國會議員們以99票的多數批准了該提案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Majority</b> is the state of legally being an adult. In most states in the United States, people reach their majority at the age of eighteen. 成年","examples":["...a citizen of Russia who has reached the age of majority. …一個已成年的俄羅斯公民。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group is <b>in a majority</b> or <b>in the majority</b>, they form more than half of a larger group. 佔多數","examples":["Surveys indicate that supporters of the treaty are still in the majority. 調查顯示該條約的支持者仍佔多數。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Majority</b> is used to describe opinions, decisions, and systems of government that are supported by more than half the people involved. 多數人支援的","examples":["...her continuing disagreement with the majority view. …她與多數人觀點的持續不一致。"]}]}]},"management":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經營，管理，安排；管理人員，管理層；（成功的）處理手段，（有效的）處理能力；治療，監控；<古>欺騙，欺詐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Management</b> is the control and organizing of a business or other organization. (對企業等組織的) 管理","examples":["The zoo needed better management rather than more money. 動物園需要更好的管理而非更多的錢。","The dispute is about wages, working conditions, and the management of the mining industry. 這場爭端涉及工資、工作環境和採礦業的管理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the people who control and organize a business or other organization as the <b>management</b>. 管理層","examples":["The management is doing its best to improve the situation. 管理層正在盡全力改善局面。","We need to get more women into top management. 我們需要讓更多的女性進入高管層。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Management</b> is the way people control different parts of their lives. (對生活的) 管理","examples":["...her management of her professional life. …她對自己職業生涯的管理。"]}]}]},"marble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大理石；大理石雕像；（玻璃）彈珠，彈球遊戲；<非正式>理智，智力"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冷酷無情的；大理石的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……顯得斑駁，使……有大理石花紋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Marble</b> is a type of very hard rock which feels cold when you touch it and which shines when it is cut and polished. Statues and parts of buildings are sometimes made of marble. 大理石","examples":["The house has a superb staircase made from oak and marble. 這座房子裡有用櫟木和大理石做成的一流的樓梯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Marbles</b> are sculptures made of marble. 大理石雕像","examples":["...marbles and bronzes from the Golden Age of Athens. …雅典全盛時期的大理石雕像和青銅像。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Marbles</b> is a children's game played with small balls, usually made of coloured glass. You roll a ball along the ground and try to hit an opponent's ball with it. 彈子游戲","examples":["On the far side of the street, two boys were playing marbles. 在這條街的那一頭，兩個男孩子正在玩彈子游戲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>marble</b> is one of the small balls used in the game of marbles. 彈子","examples":["...a glass marble. …一個玻璃彈子。"]}]}]},"major":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重大的，主要的；嚴重的；大調的，大音階的； <舊>（公立學校中置於學生姓氏後，表示兩兄弟中）大的，年長的；主修的；大（項）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"主修科目，專業；陸軍少校，（美國）空軍少校；（某專業的）主修學生；<美，非正式>職業棒球大聯盟；大型公司，重要企業；成年人，已達到法定年齡者；（軍樂隊中主管某一樂器部的）樂器長；大調，大音程； 大項，大前提；主要世界性組織（或公司、比賽）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在美國大學）主修，專攻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>major</b> when you want to describe something that is more important, serious, or significant than other things in a group or situation. 主要的; 重大的","examples":["The major factor in the decision to stay or to leave was usually professional. 決定去留的主要因素通常與職業相關。","Drug abuse has long been a major problem for the authorities there. 毒品濫用長期以來一直是那裡的當局的一大難題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In music, a <b>major</b> scale is one in which the third note is two tones higher than the first. (音樂) 大調的","examples":["The orchestra played Mozart's Symphony No. 35 in D Major. 該管絃樂隊演奏了莫扎特D大調第35交響曲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>major</b> is an officer who is one rank above captain in the United States Army, Air Force, or Marines. 少校","examples":["I was a major in the war, you know. 你知道，我在那場戰爭期間是個少校。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"At a university or college in the United States, a student's <b>major</b> is the main subject that they are studying. 專業","examples":["English majors would be asked to explore the roots of language. 英語專業的學生會被要求探究語言的根源。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"At a university or college in the United States, if a student is, for example, a geology <b>major</b>, geology is the main subject they are studying. …專業的學生","examples":["She was a history major at the University of Oklahoma. 她曾是俄克拉何馬大學歷史專業的學生。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The majors</b> are groups of professional sports teams that compete against each other, especially in baseball. (尤指棒球中的) 職業總會","examples":["I knew what I could do in the minor leagues, I just wanted a chance to prove myself in the majors. 我知道我能在小聯合會中做些什麼，我只是想要一個在大型職業總會中證明自己的機會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>major</b> is an important sports competition, especially in golf or tennis. (尤指高爾夫球或網球中的) 大賽","examples":["Sarazen became the first golfer to win all four majors. 薩拉曾成為了第一個贏得全部4場大賽的高爾夫球員。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a student at a university or college in the United States <b>majors</b> <b>in</b> a particular subject, that subject is the main one they study. 以…為專業","examples":["He majored in finance at Claremont Men's College in California. 他在加利福尼亞州的克萊爾蒙特男子大學主修金融。"]}]}]},"math":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>數學（等於 mathematics）；（Math）人名：（德）馬特；（柬）馬；（英）馬思"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Math</b> is the same as . 數學","examples":[]}]}]},"meadow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"草地，牧場；河邊低窪地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>meadow</b> is a field which has grass and flowers growing in it. 草地","examples":[]}]}]},"mayor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（英格蘭、威爾士和北愛爾蘭由議員選舉產生的）鎮長，市長；（美國、加拿大等國家公眾選舉的）市長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>mayor</b> of a town or city is the person who has been elected for a fixed period of time to run its government. 市長","examples":["...the new mayor of New York. …新任紐約市長。"]}]}]},"mathematics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"數學；數學運算"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mathematics</b> is the study of numbers, quantities, or shapes. 數學","examples":["...a professor of mathematics at Boston College. …一位波士頓大學的數學教授。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mathematics</b> <b>of</b> a problem is the calculations that are involved in it. 數學運算","examples":["Once you understand the mathematics of debt you can work your way out of it. 一旦你理解了債務的數學計算，你就能解決它。"]}]}]},"meanwhile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"與此同時；在此期間；另一方面"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"其間，其時"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Meanwhile</b> means while a particular thing is happening. 同時","examples":["Brush the eggplant with oil, add salt and pepper, and bake till soft. Meanwhile, heat the remaining oil in a heavy pan. 給茄子刷好油，加鹽和胡椒粉，烤到軟。同時，加熱厚底鍋中剩餘的油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Meanwhile</b> means in the period of time between two events. 在此期間","examples":["You needn't worry; I'll be ready to greet them. Meanwhile, I'm off to discuss the Fowler's party with Felix. 你不用擔心；我會做好準備迎接他們的。在此期間，我會去和費利克斯商量在福勒家聚會的事情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>meanwhile</b> to introduce a different aspect of a particular situation, especially one that is completely opposite to the one previously mentioned. 另一方面","examples":["He had always found his wife's mother a bit annoying. The mother-daughter relationship, meanwhile, was close. 他總是覺得他的岳母有點煩人。另一方面，她們母女之間的關係很親近。"]}]}]},"medal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎牌，勳章，紀念章"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贏得獎章"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>medal</b> is a small metal disc which is given as an award for bravery or as a prize in a sports event. 獎章","examples":["Dufour was awarded his country's highest medal for bravery. 杜富爾被授予他的國家的最高英勇獎章。"]}]}]},"media":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞媒體，傳媒（medium的複數形式）；媒體工作者；（尤指血管壁的）中間層（複數mediae）；濁塞音；中脈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to television, radio, newspapers, and magazines as <b>the media</b>. 媒體","examples":["It is hard work and not a glamorous job as portrayed by the media. 這份工作很辛苦，並不是一份像媒體描述的那樣令人嚮往的工作。","They are wondering whether bias in the news media contributed to the president's defeat. 他們正在想是否新聞媒體的偏見導致了總統的失敗。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"of or relating to the mass media 公共媒體的; 與公共媒體有關的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Media</b> is a plural of . 媒體 (medium)(的複數形式)","examples":[]}]}]},"march":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"齊步走，行軍；快步走；強迫（某人）一起走，押送；遊行示威；進行，進展"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"三月（March）；示威遊行；行進，行軍；穩步發展；進行曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When soldiers <b>march</b> somewhere, or when a commanding officer <b>marches</b> them somewhere, they walk there with very regular steps, as a group. 使齊步走; 行軍","examples":["A U.S. infantry battalion was marching down the street. 一個美軍步兵營沿著街道行進。","Captain Ramirez called them to attention and marched them off to the main camp. 拉米雷斯上校命令他們立正，然後讓他們向主營地行進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>march</b> someone somewhere, you force them to walk there with you, for example by holding their arm tightly. 迫使…同行","examples":["They were marched through a crocodile-infested area and, if they slowed down, were beaten with sticks. 他們被迫一同穿過一個鱷魚出沒的地區，如果走得慢了，就會遭到棍棒責打。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>March</b> is also a noun. 行軍","examples":["After a short march, the column entered the village. 短途行軍之後，隊伍進入了村子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a frontier, border, or boundary or the land lying along it, often of disputed ownership (所有權常有爭議的)邊界; 邊疆; 邊地 (Also called marchland)","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>March</b> is also a noun. 遊行","examples":["Organizers expect up to 300,000 protesters to join the march. 組織者預計多達30萬的抗議者參加這次遊行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"遊行者","examples":["Fights between police and marchers lasted for three hours. 警察和遊行者之間的戰鬥持續了3個小時。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>march</b> <b>of</b> something is its steady development or progress. 進展","examples":["It is easy to feel trampled by the relentless march of technology. 技術日新月異的發展容易讓人感到壓抑。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>march</b> is a piece of music with a regular rhythm that you can march to. 進行曲","examples":["A military band played Russian marches and folk tunes at the parade last Sunday. 一個軍樂團在上週日的遊行中演奏了俄羅斯的進行曲和民樂。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a large group of people <b>march</b> for a cause, they walk somewhere together in order to express their ideas or to protest about something. 遊行","examples":["The demonstrators then marched through the capital chanting slogans and demanding free elections. 示威者然後穿越首都遊行，反覆喊著口號，要求進行自由選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>marches</b> somewhere, you mean that they walk there quickly and in a determined way, for example because they are angry. (堅定地) 快步走","examples":["He marched into the kitchen without knocking. 他沒敲門就快步走進了廚房。"]}]}]},"membership":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"會員身份，會籍；會員數；（全體）會員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Membership</b> in an organization is the state of being a member of it. 成員身份","examples":["...his membership in the Communist Party. …他的共產黨黨員身份。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>membership</b> of an organization is the people who belong to it, or the number of people who belong to it. 全體成員; 成員數","examples":["By 1890 the organization had a membership of 409,000. 到1890年該組織有409000名成員。"]}]}]},"merchant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商人，（尤指外貿）批發商；<美>商店老闆；<英，非正式>對（令人討厭之事）入迷的人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"海上貨運的；商業的，商人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>merchant</b> is a person who buys or sells goods in large quantities, especially one who imports and exports them. 商人","examples":["Any knowledgeable wine merchant would be able to advise you. 任何一位內行的葡萄酒商人都能為你提出建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>merchant</b> is a person who owns or runs a shop, or other business. 店主","examples":["The family was forced to live on credit from local merchants. 這家人不得不靠向當地的商家賒賬過活。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Merchant</b> seamen or ships are involved in carrying goods for trade. 商船的","examples":["There's been a big reduction in the size of the merchant fleet in recent years. 近年來商船隊的數量大為縮減。"]}]}]},"medium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"媒介，媒體；方法，手段；（藝術創作）材料，素材；靈媒，巫師；培養基；環境；中等，中號；儲存（或列印）介質；（顏料）溶劑（如油或水）；（品質、狀態）中等，中庸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中等的，中間的，適中的；五分熟的，半熟的；（程度、強度或數量）平均的；（顏色）不深不淺的，適中的；（投球，投球手）中速的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is of <b>medium</b> size, it is neither large nor small, but approximately halfway between the two. 中等的","examples":["A medium dose produces severe nausea within hours. 中等劑量會在幾小時內引起嚴重的噁心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>medium</b> to describe something that is average in degree or amount, or approximately halfway along a scale between two extremes. 中等程度的","examples":["Foods that contain only medium levels of sodium are bread, cakes, milk, butter, and margarine. 含鈉量僅為中等水平的食物有面包、蛋糕、牛奶、黃油和人造黃油。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Medium</b> is also an adverb. 中等程度地","examples":["Toast by stirring in a medium-hot skillet for a few minutes. 在中溫的長柄平鍋裡攪拌烤焙幾分鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is of a <b>medium</b> colour, it is neither light nor dark, but approximately halfway between the two. (顏色) 中度的","examples":["Andrea has medium brown hair, grey eyes, and very pale skin. 安德烈婭有著中褐色的頭髮、灰色的眼睛和非常蒼白的皮膚。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>medium</b> is a way or means of expressing your ideas or of communicating with people. 表現方式; 交流手段","examples":["In Sierra Leone, English is used as the medium of instruction for all primary education. 在獅子山，所有基礎教育都用英語授課。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>medium</b> is a substance or material which is used for a particular purpose or in order to produce a particular effect. 媒介物","examples":["Blood is the medium in which oxygen is carried to all parts of the body. 血液是把氧氣輸送到身體各部分的媒介。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>medium</b> is a person who claims to be able to contact and speak to people who are dead, and to pass messages between them and people who are still alive. 靈媒 (自稱能夠在死者與生者之間傳遞資訊的人)","examples":["Bruce Willis says he has been talking to his dead brother through a medium. 布魯斯·威利斯說他一直在透過一位靈媒和他死去的兄弟交談。"]}]}]},"microwave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"微波爐；微波"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用微波爐烹調（或加熱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>microwave</b> or a <b>microwave oven</b> is an oven which cooks food very quickly by electromagnetic radiation rather than by heat. 微波爐","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>microwave</b> food or drink means to cook or heat it in a microwave oven. 用微波爐 (烹調或加熱)","examples":["Steam or microwave the vegetables until tender. 蒸或用微波爐加熱蔬菜，直至蔬菜變得軟嫩。"]}]}]},"mike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴音器，麥克風；話筒；休息, 遊手好閒"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"使用擴音器；偷懶, 遊手好閒"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用擴音器傳送；用竊聽器竊聽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mike</b> is the same as a . 麥克風","examples":[]}]}]},"mention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提到，談到；提名，推薦；傳令嘉獎，提名錶揚"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"提及，說起，寫上一筆；提名錶揚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mention</b> something, you say something about it, usually briefly. 提到","examples":["She did not mention her mother's absence. 她沒有提到她母親的缺席。","I may not have mentioned it to her. 我可能沒有和她提過此事。","I had mentioned that I didn't really like contemporary music. 我曾經說過我並不真正喜歡現代音樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is mentioned</b> in writing, a reference is made to them by name, often to criticize or praise something that they have done. 提及 (某人的名字)","examples":["I was absolutely outraged that I could be even mentioned in an article of this kind. 我十分惱火，我的名字居然出現在這種文章裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mention</b> is a reference to something or someone. 提及","examples":["The statement made no mention of government casualties. 這項宣告沒有提及政府方面的傷亡情況。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A special or honourable <b>mention</b> is formal praise that is given for an achievement that is very good, although not usually the best of its kind. 提名錶揚","examples":["Two of the losers deserve special mention: Caroline Swaithes, of Kingston, and Maria Pons, of Valley Stream. 其中的兩位失敗者值得特別表揚：來自金斯頓的卡羅琳·斯威西斯和來自谷溪鎮的瑪麗亞·龐斯。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say \"<b>don't mention it</b>\" as a polite reply to someone who has just thanked them for doing something. 不必客氣","examples":["\"Thank you very much.\"—\"Don't mention it.\" “非常感謝你。”—“不必客氣。”"]}]}]},"millionaire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"富豪，百萬富翁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>millionaire</b> is a very rich person who has money or property worth at least a million dollars. 百萬富翁","examples":["By the time he died, he was a millionaire. 到他去世的時候，他已是一位百萬富翁。"]}]}]},"microphone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴音器，麥克風"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>microphone</b> is a device that is used to make sounds louder or to record them on a tape recorder. 麥克風","examples":[]}]}]},"might":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"可能，可以（may 的過去式）；（表示可能性）可能，也許；（用於禮貌地建議）可以，也許；（對某人未做某事表示不滿）應該；也許，可能（表示某情況屬實，另一情況也屬實）；可以，能（用於說明目的）；究竟，到底；可以，能夠（預料）；我可以這麼說（表示強調接下來的陳述）；好像，似乎；也許不會/也許永遠不會做某事；用於禮貌地談論某人或某事物"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"強大力量，威力"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"(Might) （美）邁特（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> to indicate that something will possibly happen or be true in the future, but you cannot be certain. 有可能會; 也許會","examples":["There's a report today that smoking might be banned in most buildings. 今日有報道說大多數建築裡有可能要禁止吸菸。","I might well regret it later. 我以後也許會對此很後悔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> to indicate that there is a possibility that something is true, but you cannot be certain. 或許 (是)","examples":["She and Robert's father had not given up hope that he might be alive. 她和羅伯特的父親都沒有放棄他可能還活著的希望。","You might be right. 你或許是對的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> to indicate that something could happen or be true in particular circumstances. 可能 (發生)","examples":["America might sell more cars to the islands if they were made with the steering wheel on the right. 如果把方向盤裝在右側，美國有可能在這些島嶼銷售更多的車輛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>might have</b> with a past participle to indicate that it is possible that something happened or was true, or when giving a possible explanation for something. 可能 (對過去的事進行推測或提供解釋)","examples":["I heard what might have been an explosion. 我聽到的可能是爆炸的聲音。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>might have</b> with a past participle to indicate that something was a possibility in the past, although it did not actually happen. (表示與過去事實相反的虛擬語氣) 本來可能","examples":["If she had had to give up riding she might have taken up sailing competitively. 如果當時她不得不放棄馬術，她可能就已經從事帆船競賽了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> in statements where you are accepting the truth of a situation, but contrasting it with something that is more important. 也許 (接受事實，但與更重要的事對比)","examples":["They might not have two cents to rub together, but at least they have a kind of lifestyle that is different. 他們也許手裡沒有幾個錢，但至少他們過著一種與眾不同的生活方式。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> when you are saying emphatically that someone ought to do the thing mentioned, especially when you are annoyed because they have not done it. 應該 (做但還沒做)","examples":["You might have told me that before! 你以前就該告訴我這件事！"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> to make a suggestion or to give advice in a very polite way. (表示禮貌的建議) 可以","examples":["They might be wise to stop advertising on television. 他們可以明智些，停止在電視上做廣告。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> as a polite way of interrupting someone, asking a question, making a request, or introducing what you are going to say next. (禮貌地打斷、提問等) 可以","examples":["Might I make a suggestion? 我可以提個建議麼？","Might I ask what you're doing here? 我可以問問你在這裡做什麼嗎？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>might</b> in expressions such as <b>I might have known</b> and <b>I might have guessed</b> to indicate that you are not surprised at a disappointing event or fact. 早該 (表示不感到意外)","examples":["I might have known I'd find you with some little slut. 我早該知道會發現你跟某個小蕩婦在一起。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Might</b> is power or strength. 力量","examples":["The might of the army could prove a decisive factor. 軍隊的力量最終可能成為一個決定性的因素。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>with all</b> your <b>might</b>, you do it using all your strength and energy. 竭盡全力地","examples":["She swung the hammer at his head with all her might. 她用盡全力掄起錘子砸向他的腦袋。"]}]}]},"mill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磨坊，磨粉廠；工廠，製造廠；<非正式> 一百萬；磨粉機，磨麵機；<美>密爾，釐；機器，銑床；<非正式>引擎；<非正式>一百萬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用磨粉機）碾碎，磨成粉；（一大群人）閒逛，轉悠；碾（軋，銑）（金屬）；軋出（硬幣的）邊紋；使（羊毛或其他動物纖維）縮絨（或縮呢）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mill</b> is a building in which grain is crushed to make flour. 磨坊","examples":["There was an old mill that really did grind corn. 有一個真正碾磨玉米的老磨坊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mill</b> is a small device used for grinding something such as coffee beans or pepper into powder. 碾磨器","examples":["...a pepper mill. …一個胡椒碾磨器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mill</b> is a factory used for making and processing materials such as steel, wool, or cotton.  工廠","examples":["...a steel mill. …一家鋼廠。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a US and Canadian monetary unit used in calculations, esp for property taxes, equal to one thousandth of a dollar 密爾 ; 美國和加拿大的貨幣計算單位，尤其用於計算房產稅，相當於一美元的千分之一","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mill</b> something such as wheat or pepper means to grind it in a mill. 碾磨","examples":["They do not have the capacity to mill the grain. 他們沒有碾磨穀物的能力。"]}]}]},"miner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"礦工，採礦工人；開礦機，採礦機械（continuous miner 即連續採煤機）；（Miner，首字母大寫）人名：（英）邁納，（西）米內爾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>miner</b> is a person who works underground in mines in order to obtain minerals such as coal, diamonds, or gold. 礦工","examples":[]}]}]},"mess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"骯髒，雜亂；不整潔或邋遢的人（或物）；掉落的東西，濺出的東西；（動物的）糞便；困境，混亂局面；處於困境的人；（軍隊的）食堂，交誼廳；<美，非正式> 大量；（尤指引不起食慾的）半乾半稀的一份食物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弄髒，弄亂；玩弄；隨地便溺；在軍人食堂就餐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a</b> <b>mess</b> or <b>in a</b> <b>mess</b>, you think that it is not neat. 凌亂","examples":["The house is a mess. 這個房間又髒又亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a situation is <b>a</b> <b>mess</b>, you mean that it is full of trouble or problems. You can also say that something is <b>in a</b> <b>mess</b>. 困境","examples":["I've made such a mess of my life. 我把自己的生活弄得一團糟。","...the many reasons why the economy is in such a mess. …經濟陷入如此困境的諸多原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>A</b> <b>mess</b> is something liquid or sticky that has been accidentally dropped on something. (意外滴落的) 液體; (意外滴落的) 黏稠物","examples":["I'll clear up the mess later. 我過會兒會把滴落的東西擦乾淨。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>mess</b> at a military base or military barracks is the building in which members of the armed forces can eat or relax. (軍隊的) 餐廳","examples":["...a party at the officers' mess. …在軍官餐廳裡舉辦的晚會。"]}]}]},"minority":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"少數，少數派；少數民族，少數群體；未成年時期，未成年身份；唯一持不同意見者；（議會）少數黨得（或投）的票"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"少數的；少數民族的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about a <b>minority</b> of people or things in a larger group, you are referring to a number of them that forms less than half of the larger group, usually much less than half. 少數","examples":["Local authority child-care provision covers only a tiny minority of working mothers. 地方政府提供的兒童保育服務只惠及了極少數上班族母親們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>minority</b> is a group of people of the same race, culture, or religion who live in a place where most of the people around them are of a different race, culture, or religion. 少數民族; 信仰其他宗教的少數派","examples":["...the region's ethnic minorities. …這個地區的少數民族。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people are <b>in a minority</b> or <b>in the minority</b>, they belong to a group of people or things that form less than half of a larger group. 佔少數","examples":["Even in the 1960s, politically active students and academics were in a minority. 即使是在20世紀60年代，政治上活躍的學生和高校教師也是佔少數。"]}]}]},"minor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較小的，次要的，輕微的；（疾病）不嚴重的，（手術）小的；小調的，小音階的；未成年的；數量少的，範圍小的；（邏）小（項）；<英，舊>（兩兄弟或同姓男生中）年齡更小的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"未成年人；輔修課程；（美國大學中的）輔修生；（樂）小調，小音程；（邏）小項，小前提；禾夜蛾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輔修"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>minor</b> when you want to describe something that is less important, serious, or significant than other things in a group or situation. 次要的","examples":["She is known in Italy for a number of minor roles in films. 她因擔任電影中一些配角而聞名義大利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>minor</b> illness or operation is not likely to be dangerous to someone's life or health. 不嚴重的","examples":["Sarah had been plagued continually by a series of minor illnesses since her mid teens. 自從十四五歲起薩拉就一直小病不斷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>minor</b> scale is one in which the third note is three semitones higher than the first. 小調的","examples":["...the unfinished sonata movement in F minor. …未完成的F小調奏鳴曲樂章。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>minor</b> is a person who is still legally a child. In most states in the United States, people are minors until they reach the age of eighteen. 未成年者","examples":["The approach has virtually ended cigarette sales to minors. 這一作法實際上已經終止了向未成年人出售香菸。"]}]}]},"missile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導彈，飛彈；投擲物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可投擲的；用以發射導彈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>missile</b> is a tube-shaped weapon that travels long distances through the air and explodes when it reaches its target. 導彈","examples":["The authorities offered to stop firing missiles if the rebels agreed to stop attacking civilian targets. 當局提出如果叛亂者同意停止襲擊民用目標，他們就停止發射導彈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Anything that is thrown as a weapon can be called a <b>missile</b>. (作為武器的) 投擲物","examples":["The football fans began throwing missiles, one of which hit the referee. 足球球迷們開始扔東西，其中的一個打中了裁判。"]}]}]},"miracle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奇蹟，不可思議的事；傑出例子，精品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（藥物或產品）神奇的，不可思議的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a good event is a <b>miracle</b>, you mean that it is very surprising and unexpected. 奇蹟","examples":["It is a miracle no one was killed. 沒有人死亡真是個奇蹟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>miracle</b> is a wonderful and surprising event that is believed to be caused by God. 上帝創造的奇蹟","examples":["...Jesus's ability to perform miracles. …耶穌行神的能力。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>miracle</b> drug or product does something that was thought almost impossible. 神奇的","examples":["...the miracle drugs that keep his 94-year-old mother healthy. …使他那94歲高齡的老母親保持健康的神奇藥物。"]}]}]},"misery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痛苦，苦難；窮困，悲慘境遇；<英，非正式>老發牢騷的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Misery</b> is great unhappiness. 苦難","examples":["All that money brought nothing but sadness and misery and tragedy. 那些錢帶來的只有悲哀、苦難和不幸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Misery</b> is the way of life and unpleasant living conditions of people who are very poor. 窮困","examples":["A tiny, educated elite profited from the misery of their two million fellow countrymen. 一個小小的受過教育的精英團體從他們兩百萬同胞的窮困中獲了利。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>makes</b> your <b>life a misery</b>, they behave in an unpleasant way towards you over a period of time and make you very unhappy. 使某人的生活非常不開心","examples":["I would really like living here if it wasn't for the gangs of kids who make our lives a misery. 要不是那一群群的孩子攪得我們生活不寧，我還是挺喜歡住在這裡的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> someone <b>out of</b> their <b>misery</b>, you tell them something that they are very anxious to know. 告知情況 (使不再焦慮)","examples":["Please put me out of my misery. How do you do it? 請別讓我著急了。你是怎麼做的呀？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>put</b> an animal <b>out of</b> its <b>misery</b>, you kill it because it is sick or injured and cannot be cured or healed. 殺死 (動物) 以使其擺脫痛苦","examples":["He notes grimly that the Watsons have called the vet to put their dog out of its misery. 他難過地記錄下沃森家已經給獸醫打了電話，要永遠結束他們家狗的痛苦。"]}]}]},"monk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"僧侶，修道士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monk</b> is a member of a male religious community that is usually separated from the outside world. 僧侶","examples":["...saffron-robed Buddhist monks. …身穿黃袍的和尚們。"]}]}]},"moisture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潮氣，水分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Moisture</b> is tiny drops of water in the air, on a surface, or in the ground. 潮氣; 水分","examples":["When the soil is dry, more moisture is lost from the plant. 土壤乾燥時，植物就會失去更多的水分。"]}]}]},"mob":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人群，（尤指）暴民；<非正式>一群人，幫派，團伙；普通群眾，大眾（含貶義，the mob）；犯罪集團，黑社會（the Mob）；<澳>（動物）群"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"團團圍住；（鳥或獸群）圍攻，成群襲擊；蜂擁進入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mob</b> is a large, disorganized, and often violent crowd of people. 一大群亂民","examples":["The inspectors watched a growing mob of demonstrators gathering. 這些監察員看著越來越多的粗暴的示威人群聚集在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the people involved in organized crime as <b>the Mob</b>. 犯罪團伙","examples":["He makes ends meet by working as a forger for the Mob. 他透過為犯罪團伙造假來養家餬口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>the mob</b> to refer in a disapproving way to the majority of people in a country or place, especially when these people are behaving in a violent or uncontrolled way. 暴民","examples":["If they continue like this there is a danger of the mob taking over. 如果他們繼續如此，就有被暴民接管的危險。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is being mobbed</b> <b>by</b> a crowd of people, you mean that the people are trying to talk to them or get near them in an enthusiastic or threatening way. 成群圍住","examples":["Her car was mobbed by the media. 她的汽車被媒體團團圍住。"]}]}]},"mist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薄霧，水汽；霧狀物；使視線模糊的東西；迷霧，難以透徹瞭解的事物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……蒙上霧氣；（使）充滿淚水；給……噴水；下毛毛細雨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mist</b> consists of a large number of tiny drops of water in the air, which make it difficult to see very far. 霧","examples":["Thick mist made flying impossible. 濃霧使得無法飛行。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a piece of glass <b>mists</b> or <b>is misted</b>, it becomes covered with tiny drops of moisture, so that you cannot see through it easily. 使蒙上薄霧; 蒙上薄霧","examples":["The windows misted, blurring the stark streetlight. 窗戶蒙上了一層水汽，使得明亮的街燈模糊了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mist over</b> means the same as . 同(mist)","examples":["The front windshield was misting over. 前擋風玻璃蒙上了一層水汽。"]}]}]},"mission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指赴他國的）使命，重要任務；職責，天職；（軍用飛機或航天火箭的）飛行任務；軍事行動；（一個組織的）目的，宗旨；外交使團，代表團；駐外機構，使館；（尤指在海外的）傳教，佈道；傳教團，佈道團；佈道所，傳教所"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"作艱苦的長途旅行（尤指去許多地方）；派遣；向……傳教"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mission</b> is an important task that people are given to do, especially one that involves travelling to another country. (尤指遠赴他國的) 使命","examples":["Salisbury sent him on a diplomatic mission to North America. 索爾茲伯裡派他到北美執行一項外交使命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mission</b> is a group of people who have been sent to a foreign country to carry out an official task. 駐外使團","examples":["...a senior member of a diplomatic mission. …外交使團中的一名高階成員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mission</b> is a special journey made by a military aeroplane or spacecraft. (軍用飛機或宇宙飛船的) 飛行任務","examples":["...a bomber that crashed during a training mission in the west Texas mountains. …在德克薩斯州西部山區執行訓練任務時墜毀的一架轟炸機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that you have a <b>mission</b>, you mean that you have a strong commitment and sense of duty to do or achieve something. 使命; 天職","examples":["He viewed his mission in life as protecting the weak from the evil. 他把保護弱者不受壞人傷害看作自己一生的使命。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>mission</b> is the activities of a group of Christians who have been sent to a place to teach people about Christianity. 傳教活動","examples":["They say God spoke to them and told them to go on a mission to the poorest country in the Western Hemisphere. 他們說上帝向他們開口講話，告訴他們到西半球最貧窮的國家繼續進行傳教活動。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>mission</b> is a building or group of buildings in which missionary work is carried out. 佈道所","examples":["I reside at the mission at St. Michael's. 我住在聖邁克爾教堂的佈道所。"]}]}]},"mixture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"混合體，結合體；混合物，混合料；混合；（未經化學反應而形成的）混合物；（內燃機汽缸中）混合氣；混合音栓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mixture</b> <b>of</b> things consists of several different things together. 混合","examples":["They looked at him with a mixture of horror, envy, and awe. 他們帶著害怕、羨慕和敬畏的混合表情看著他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mixture</b> is a substance that consists of other substances which have been stirred or shaken together. 混合物","examples":["...a mixture of water and sugar and salt. …水、糖和鹽的混合物。"]}]}]},"motel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汽車旅館"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>motel</b> is a hotel intended for people who are travelling by car. 汽車旅館","examples":[]}]}]},"mop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拖把；蓬亂濃密的頭髮；清掃；洗碗刷；（秋季僱傭農工或僕役的）僱工市場；鬼臉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用拖把拖；擦掉，抹掉；結束，完成；扮鬼臉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mop</b> is a piece of equipment for washing floors. It consists of a sponge or many pieces of string attached to a long handle. 拖把","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mop</b> a surface such as a floor, you clean it with a mop. 用拖把擦","examples":["There was a woman mopping the stairs. 有個女人正在拖樓梯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mop</b> sweat from your forehead or <b>mop</b> your forehead, you wipe it with a piece of cloth. 擦拭","examples":["He mopped perspiration from his forehead. 他擦去額頭上的汗水。"]}]}]},"mood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心境，情緒；氣氛，情感基調；心情不好，壞脾氣；想（做某事），有興致（做某事）；（尤指音樂）激發……情感的，暗示……心境的；（群體的）態度，意願；表達語氣的動詞屈折變化；（語法的）式，語氣； 想（做某事），有興致（做某事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>mood</b> is the way you are feeling at a particular time. If you are <b>in</b> a good <b>mood</b>, you feel cheerful. If you are <b>in</b> a bad <b>mood</b>, you feel angry and impatient. 情緒","examples":["He is clearly in a good mood today. 顯然他今天心情不錯。","Lily was in one of her aggressive moods. 莉莉又在咄咄逼人了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>in a</b> <b>mood</b>, the way they are behaving shows that they are feeling angry and impatient. 心情不好","examples":["She was obviously in a mood. 顯然她心情不好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mood</b> of a group of people is the way that they think and feel about an idea, event, or question at a particular time. (群體的) 想法","examples":["The government seemed to be in tune with the popular mood. 政府似乎與公眾的想法一致。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>mood</b> of a place is the general impression that you get of it. 氣氛","examples":["First set the mood with music. 首先用音樂製造氣氛。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a category of the verb or verbal inflections that expresses semantic and grammatical differences, including such forms as the indicative, subjunctive, and imperative 語氣(如陳述語氣、虛擬語氣等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>in the mood</b> <b>for</b> something, you mean that you want to do it or have it. If you say that you are <b>in no mood</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that you do not want to do it or have it. 有/無心情 (做某事)","examples":["After a day of air and activity, you should be in the mood for a good meal. 在戶外活動了一天，你應該想好好吃一頓。"]}]}]},"nanny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保姆；母山羊（nanny goat 的簡稱）；nanny state（管理過度的）保姆式國家"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"當保姆，照看孩子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nanny</b> is a woman who is paid by parents to take care of their child or children. (受僱照看小孩的) 保姆","examples":[]}]}]},"moral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有關道德的；基於道德的，道義上的；品行端正的，有道德的；倫理的；能辨別是非的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"道德準則（標準）；寓意，道德上的教訓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Morals</b> are principles and beliefs concerning right and wrong behaviour. 道德","examples":["...Western ideas and morals. …西方的思想和道德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>moral</b> of a story or event is what you learn from it about how you should or should not behave. 道德寓意","examples":["I think the moral of the story is let the buyer beware. 我想這個故事的寓意是提醒購買者當心。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Moral</b> means relating to beliefs about what is right or wrong. 道德的","examples":["She describes her own moral dilemma in making the film. 她描述了自己拍攝這部電影時面臨的道德困境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Moral</b> courage or duty is based on what you believe is right or acceptable, rather than on what the law says should be done. 道義上的","examples":["The government had a moral, if not a legal, duty to pay compensation. 政府即使沒有法律上的義務也有道義上的義務進行賠償。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>moral</b> person behaves in a way that is believed by most people to be good and right. 有道德的","examples":["The people who will be on the committee are moral, cultured, competent people. 將要加入委員會的是那些有道德、有文化、有能力的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you give someone <b>moral</b> support, you encourage them in what they are doing by expressing approval. 道義上的 (支援)","examples":["Moral as well as financial support is what the West should provide. 道義上和經濟上的支援是西方國家應該提供的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"道德上","examples":["When, if ever, is it morally justifiable to allow a patient to die? 假如可以的話，什麼情況下允許病人放棄生命在道德上是正當的？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"道德上地","examples":["Art is not there to improve you morally. 藝術不是從道德上提升你。"]}]}]},"mushroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蘑菇，傘菌；蘑菇形物；淡褐色，棕灰色；暴發戶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迅速成長，大量湧現；採蘑菇；（子彈擊中目標時）開花擴散"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"蘑菇形的；蘑菇的；迅速生長的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mushrooms</b> are fungi that you can eat. They have short stems and round tops. 蘑菇","examples":["There are many types of wild mushrooms. 有許多種野生蘑菇。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as an industry or a place <b>mushrooms</b>, it grows or comes into existence very quickly. 迅速發展","examples":["The media training industry has mushroomed over the past decade. 媒體培訓業在過去的十年中迅速發展。"]}]}]},"musical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"音樂的，配樂的；喜愛音樂的，精通音樂的；悅耳的，動聽的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"音樂劇，音樂片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>musical</b> to indicate that something is connected with playing or studying music. 關於音樂的","examples":["We have a wealth of musical talent in this region. 我們在該地區有豐富的音樂人才。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>musical</b> has a natural ability and interest in music. 有音樂天賦的; 喜愛音樂的","examples":["I came from a musical family. 我來自一個音樂家庭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Sounds that are <b>musical</b> are light and pleasant to hear. 悅耳的","examples":["He had a soft, almost musical voice. 他有著輕柔悅耳的嗓音。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"關於音樂地","examples":["Musically there is a lot to enjoy. 在音樂方面有許多可欣賞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>musical</b> is a play or film that uses singing and dancing in the story. 音樂劇; 音樂歌舞片","examples":["...the smash hit musical, Miss Saigon. …轟動一時的音樂劇《西貢小姐》。"]}]}]},"murder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"謀殺，兇殺；<非正式>困難的事，討厭的事；一群烏鴉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"謀殺，兇殺；糟蹋，毀壞；<非正式>徹底擊敗；<非正式>對……大發雷霆；<非正式>貪婪地吃（或喝）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Murder</b> is the deliberate and illegal killing of a person. 謀殺","examples":["The three accused, aged between 19 and 20, are charged with attempted murder. 3名年齡在19到20歲之間的被告被指控蓄意謀殺。","She refused to testify, unless the murder charge against her was dropped. 她拒絕作證，除非取消她的謀殺指控。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>murder</b> someone means to commit the crime of killing them deliberately. 謀殺","examples":["...a thriller about two men who murder a third to see if they can get away with it. …一部驚悚電影，關於兩人謀殺了第3個人並看他們是否能逃脫懲罰。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>gets away with murder</b>, you are complaining that they can do whatever they like without anyone trying to control them or punish them. 無法無天為所欲為","examples":["His charm and the fact that he is so likeable often allows him to get away with murder. 他的魅力和受寵程度常讓他無法無天為所欲為。"]}]}]},"motor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發動機，馬達；汽車，轎車；原動力"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"機動的；汽車的，車輛的；肌肉運動的，運動神經的；原動的，引起運動的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘車旅行，駕車旅行；使用發動機駕駛帆船；<非正式>快速移動，迅速增加；<英>用汽車運送"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>motor</b> in a machine, vehicle, or boat is the part that uses electricity or fuel to produce movement, so that the machine, vehicle, or boat can work. 發動機","examples":["She got in and started the motor. 她上了車，發動了引擎。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Motor</b> vehicles and boats have a petrol or diesel engine. 機動的","examples":["Theft of motor vehicles is up by 15.9%. 機動車盜竊案增加了15.9%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Motor</b> is used to describe activities relating to vehicles such as cars and buses. 汽車的","examples":[]}]}]},"mystery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"難以理解（或解釋）的事物，奧秘；神秘的人（或事物）；不可思議；疑案小說（或電影、戲劇）；（宗教信仰的）奧義，真諦；聖餐禮"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"神秘的，身份不明的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mystery</b> is something that is not understood or known about. 迷","examples":["The source of the gunshots still remains a mystery. 槍彈來自何處依然是一個迷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>mystery</b> of someone or something, you are talking about how difficult they are to understand or know about, especially when this gives them a rather strange or magical quality. 神秘 (性)","examples":["She's a lady of mystery. 她是一個神秘的女人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mystery</b> is a story in which strange things happen that are not explained until the end. 懸疑 (推理) 故事","examples":["His fourth novel is a murder mystery set in London. 他的第4本小說是一個以倫敦為背景的兇殺疑案。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mystery</b> person or thing is one whose identity or nature is not known. 來歷不明的","examples":["The mystery hero immediately alerted police after spotting a bomb. 那個不知名的英雄發覺炸彈後馬上報了警。"]}]}]},"muscle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肌肉；體力，力氣；權力，影響力；<非正式>身強力壯的男子（們）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用力搬動；擠；<美，非正式> 以經濟（或政治）壓力迫使；加強"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>muscle</b> is a piece of tissue inside your body that connects two bones and which you use when you make a movement. 肌肉","examples":["Keeping your muscles strong and in tone helps you to avoid back problems. 保持強壯有力的肌肉有助於防範背疾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>muscle</b>, you mean that they have power and influence, which enables them to do difficult things. 影響力","examples":["Eisenhower used his muscle to persuade Congress to change the law. 艾森豪威爾施展了他的影響力來說服國會修改該法律。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group, organization, or country <b>flexes</b> its <b>muscles</b>, it does something to impress or frighten people, in order to show them that it has power and is considering using it. 顯示實力","examples":["The Fair Trade Commission has of late been flexing its muscles, cracking down on cases of corruption. 公平交易委員會最近一展雄威，對腐敗案件進行了嚴懲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone did not <b>move a muscle</b>, you mean that they stayed absolutely still. 動一下","examples":["He stood without moving a muscle, unable to believe what his eyes saw so plainly. 他一動也不動地站著，不敢相信自己的眼睛。"]}]}]},"necktie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"領帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>necktie</b> is a narrow piece of cloth that someone, usually a man, puts under his shirt collar and ties so that the ends hang down in front. 領帶","examples":[]}]}]},"nap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指在白天）小睡，打盹；（織物、地毯等表面的）絨毛；<英>賽馬情報；<澳，非正式>睡袋（野外用）；納普牌戲（類似惠斯特牌戲，玩家自報可贏之墩數，全勝五墩）；<英>孤注一擲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指在白天）小睡，打盹；不留神，無準備；（馬）（尤指習慣性地）不聽從指令，徘徊不前；<英>預測（賽馬，賽狗）獲勝；使起絨，使拉毛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you take or have a <b>nap</b>, you have a short sleep, usually during the day. (通常指白天的) 小睡","examples":["I might take a little nap. 我可能會打個盹兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the raised fibres of velvet or similar cloth (天鵝絨等織物表面的)絨毛","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a card game similar to whist, usually played for stakes 拿破崙牌戲 (Also called napoleon)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nap</b>, you sleep for a short period of time, usually during the day. (通常指在白天) 小睡","examples":["An elderly person may nap during the day and then sleep only five hours a night. 上了年紀的人白天會小睡一會兒，然後晚上只睡5個小時。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is caught napping</b>, something happens when they are not prepared for it, although they should have been. 使…措手不及","examples":["The security services were clearly caught napping. 安全服務人員顯然被弄得措手不及。"]}]}]},"navy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海軍；深藍色；艦隊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A country's <b>navy</b> consists of the people it employs to fight at sea, and the ships they use. 海軍","examples":["The operation was organized by the US Navy. 這次行動是由美國海軍組織的。","Her own son was also in the navy. 她自己的兒子也曾在海軍裡。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>navy</b> or <b>navy-blue</b> is very dark blue. 深藍色的","examples":["When I was a fashion editor, I mostly wore white shirts and black or navy trousers. 當時尚編輯的時候，我大多數時間穿白襯衫和黑色或深藍色褲子。"]}]}]},"neighborhood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"街區，社群（城鎮中人們居住的地區）；附近，鄰近地區；街坊，鄰里（居住在同一地區的人們）；接近，大約（用於 in the neighborhood of，表示數量、價格等的約數）；鄰域（數學、電腦科學中指一點附近的點集）"}],"sections":[]},"necessity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"必需品，必需的事物；必要，需要；必然性，不可避免的情況"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>necessity</b> of something is the fact that it must happen or exist. 必要性","examples":["There is agreement on the necessity of reforms. 關於改革的必要性有一致意見。","As soon as the necessity for action is over the troops must be withdrawn. 一旦軍事行動的必要性不復存在，部隊必須撤離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>necessity</b> is something that you must have in order to live properly or do something. 必需品","examples":["Water is a basic necessity of life. 水是一種基本生活必需品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A situation or action that is a <b>necessity</b> is necessary and cannot be avoided. 不可避免","examples":["The president pleaded that strong rule from the centre was a necessity. 總統爭辯說來自中央的強有力的統治是一種必然。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>of necessity</b> the case, you mean that it is the case because nothing else is possible or practical under the circumstances. 勢必","examples":["...large families where children, of necessity, shared a bed. …孩子們必定共睡一張床的大型家庭。"]}]}]},"nickname":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"綽號，外號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……起綽號；叫錯名字"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nickname</b> is an informal name for someone or something. 綽號","examples":["Red got his nickname for his red hair. “紅紅”因為他的紅頭髮而得了這個綽號。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nickname</b> someone or something, you give them an informal name. 給…起綽號","examples":["When he got older I nicknamed him Little Alf. 他長大些後，我給他起了綽號“小阿爾夫”。"]}]}]},"novelist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小說家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>novelist</b> is a person who writes novels. 小說家","examples":["The key to success as a romantic novelist is absolute belief in your story. 一個浪漫派小說家成功的關鍵在於對自己故事的絕對信念。"]}]}]},"nun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"修女，尼姑；希伯來字母表中的第十四個字母（拉丁轉寫為 n）；（航海）錐形浮標，常作 nun buoy"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nun</b> is a member of a female religious community. 尼姑; 修女","examples":["Mr. Thomas was taught by the Catholic nuns whose school he attended to work and study hard. 托馬斯先生受教於天主教修女。在修女開辦的學校裡他專心工作，刻苦學習。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the 14th letter in the Hebrew alphabet (נ or, at the end of a word, ן), transliterated as <b>n</b> 希伯來文字母表中第十四個字母","examples":[]}]}]},"native":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"本地出生的，出生地的；天生的，天賦的；原產於某地的，土產的；母語的；土著的，土著人的；<澳> （動、植物）像外地物種的；（金屬或其他礦物）天然的，呈天然純態的；（計算機）本機器碼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"土生土長者，本地人；當地居民；土著人；土生植物（或動物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>native</b> country or area is the country or area where you were born and brought up. 出生並從小長大的 (國家或地方)","examples":["It was his first visit to his native country since 1948. 這是1948年以來他首次訪問祖國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Native</b> is also an adjective. 本國的; 本地的","examples":["Joshua Halpern is a native Northern Californian. 喬舒亞·哈爾彭是土生土長的北加州人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Native</b> is also an adjective. 土著的","examples":["Native people were allowed to retain some sense of their traditional culture and religion. 土著人被允許保留一些自己的傳統文化和宗教。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>native</b> language or tongue is the first language that you learned to speak when you were a child. 第一 (語言)","examples":["She spoke not only her native language, Swedish, but also English and French. 她不僅講她的母語瑞典語，還講英語和法語。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Plants or animals that are <b>native to</b> a particular region live or grow there naturally and were not brought there. 當地土生的 (動、植物)","examples":["...a project to create a 50 acre forest of native Caledonian pines. …一個營造50英畝喀裡多尼亞土生松林的專案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>native of</b> a particular country or region is someone who was born in that country or region. 本國人; 本地人","examples":["Dr. Aubin is a native of St. Louis. 奧賓醫生是聖路易斯人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some European people use <b>native</b> to refer to a person living in a non-Western country who belongs to the race or tribe that the majority of people there belong to. This use could cause offence. 土著","examples":["They used force to banish the natives from the more fertile land. 他們用武力將土著人驅逐出更加肥沃的土地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Native</b> is also a noun. 土生動植物","examples":["The coconut palm is a native of Malaysia. 這棵椰子樹是馬來西亞的土生植物。"]}]}]},"network":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網路，網狀系統；人際關係網，聯絡網；計算機網路，網際網路；廣播網，電視網"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（計算機）聯網；（尤指工作中）建立關係網，建立人脈；對（電視或廣播節目）進行聯播"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A radio or television <b>network</b> is a company or group of companies that broadcast radio or television programmes throughout an area. (廣播或電視) 網","examples":["Los Angeles-based Univision is a Spanish-language broadcast television network. 位於洛杉磯的”聯合視野”是一家西班牙語的廣播電視網。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>network</b> <b>of</b> people or institutions is a large number of them that have a connection with each other and work together as a system. (由許多人或機構組成的) 組織網路","examples":["Distribution of the food is going ahead using a network of local church people and other volunteers. 食品的分發正在透過當地教會人士和其他志願者組織網路進行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular <b>network</b> is a system of things which are connected and which operate together. For example, a <b>computer network</b> consists of a number of computers that are part of the same system. 網路系統","examples":["...a computer network with 154 terminals. …一個有154臺終端的計算機網路。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>network</b> <b>of</b> lines, roads, veins, or other long thin things is a large number of them which cross each other or meet at many points. (線路、道路、血管等的) 網狀系統","examples":["...Strasbourg, with its rambling network of medieval streets. …斯特拉斯堡，有著修建於中世紀的不規則街網。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>network</b>, you try to meet new people who might be useful to you in your job. 建立關係網","examples":["In business, it is important to network with as many people as possible on a face to face basis. 在生意場上，與儘可能多的人建立面對面的關係網是重要的。"]}]}]},"noble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"崇高的，高尚的；宏偉的，卓越的；貴族的，高貴的；惰性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（舊時的）貴族"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>noble</b> person, you admire and respect them because they are unselfish and morally good. 高尚的","examples":["He was an upright and noble man who was always willing to help in any way he could. 他是一個正直、高尚的人，總是願意盡其所能來幫忙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>noble</b> idea, goal, or action, you admire it because it is based on high moral principles. 崇高的","examples":["He had implicit faith in their noble intentions. 他對他們的崇高目標深信不疑。","We'll always justify our actions with noble sounding theories. 我們將始終用崇高的理論思想指導我們的行動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>noble</b>, you think that its appearance or quality is very impressive, making it superior to other things of its type. 卓越的; 超群的","examples":["...the great parks with their noble trees. …樹木參天的大公園。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Noble</b> means belonging to a high social class and having a title. 高貴的; 貴族的","examples":["...rich and noble families. …富有而高貴的家族。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"高尚地","examples":["Eric's sister had nobly volunteered to help with the gardening. 埃裡克的姐姐無私地主動幫忙做些園藝工作。"]}]}]},"nerve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"神經；勇氣，膽量；神經緊張，情緒不安；魯莽，冒失；（葉）脈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使鼓起勇氣，使振作精神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nerves</b> are long thin fibres that transmit messages between your brain and other parts of your body. 神經","examples":["...spinal nerves. …脊椎神經。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>nerves</b>, you mean their ability to cope with problems such as stress, worry, and danger. (對壓力、煩惱和危險等的) 精神承受力","examples":["Jill's nerves are stretched to breaking point. 吉爾的神經緊張得快到極點了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to someone's feelings of anxiety or tension as <b>nerves</b>. 神經緊張","examples":["I just played badly. It wasn't nerves. 我就是演得不好，不是緊張。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Nerve</b> is the courage that you need in order to do something difficult or dangerous. 勇氣","examples":["The brandy made him choke, but it restored his nerve. 白蘭地嗆到他了，但恢復了他的勇氣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>gets on</b> your <b>nerves</b>, they annoy or irritate you. 惹…心煩","examples":["Lately he hasn't done a thing and it's getting on my nerves. 最近他什麼都沒做，這讓我大為惱火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has a nerve</b> or <b>has the nerve</b> to do something, you are criticizing them for doing something which you feel they had no right to do. 放肆","examples":["He told his critics they had a nerve complaining about him. 他對他的批評者說，他們對他抱怨真是放肆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> your <b>nerve</b>, you suddenly panic and become too afraid to do something that you were about to do. 驚慌失措","examples":["The bomber had lost his nerve and fled. 投炸彈的人驚惶失措地逃走了。"]}]}]},"oak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橡樹，櫟樹；橡木，櫟木；（櫟木桶裡陳年老酒的）煙香氣；櫟棕色；櫟木傢俱，櫟木製品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"櫟樹的；櫟木製的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oak</b> or an <b>oak tree</b> is a large tree that often grows in forests and has strong, hard wood. 橡樹","examples":["Many large oaks were felled during the war. 許多大橡樹在那場戰爭期間被砍伐了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Oak</b> is the wood of this tree. 橡木","examples":["The cabinet was made of oak and was hand-carved. 這個櫃子是橡木做的，並且經手工雕刻而成。"]}]}]},"operator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（裝置、機器的）操作員；經營者；精明圓滑的人，善於取巧的人；電話員，接線員；運算子號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>operator</b> is a person who connects telephone calls at a telephone exchange or in a place such as an office or hotel. 電話接線員","examples":["He dialled the operator and put in a call to Rome. 他撥通了接線員，往羅馬打了一個電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>operator</b> is a person who is employed to operate or control a machine. 操作員","examples":["...computer operators. …電腦操作員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>operator</b> is a person or a company that runs a business. 經營者","examples":["...the nation's largest cable TV operator. …全國最大的有線電視運營商。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you call someone a smooth or shrewd <b>operator</b>, you mean that they are skilful at achieving what they want, often in a slightly dishonest way. 精明圓滑的人","examples":["He is a smooth operator. Don't underestimate him. 他是個精明圓滑的人，別低估他。"]}]}]},"overcoat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大衣，外套； 外層塗料，保護層"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>overcoat</b> is a thick warm coat that you wear in winter. 大衣","examples":[]}]}]},"occasion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某事發生的）時刻，時候；<正式>時機，適當的機會；特殊（或重大）場合，特殊（或重大）事件；<正式>理由，原因"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 引起，惹起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>occasion</b> is a time when something happens, or a case of it happening. (某事發生的) 時候; 場景","examples":["I often think fondly of an occasion some years ago in New Orleans. 我經常深情地想起一些年前在新奧爾良所發生的一幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>occasion</b> is an important event, ceremony, or celebration. 重大場合","examples":["Taking her with me on official occasions has been a challenge. 在正式場合帶上她對我而言是一種挑戰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>occasion for</b> doing something is an opportunity for doing it. 機會","examples":["It is an occasion for all the family to celebrate. 那是個全家慶祝的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have occasion</b> <b>to</b> do something, you have the opportunity to do it or have a need to do it. 有機會; 有必要","examples":["Over the next few years many people had occasion to reflect on the truth of his warnings. 在隨後的幾年裡許多人有機會反思他那些警告的真相。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>rose to the occasion</b>, you mean that they did what was necessary to successfully overcome a difficult situation. 應付自如","examples":["Colorado rose to the occasion with four players scoring 16 points or more. 科羅拉多隊從容應對，4個隊員贏得16分或更多得分。"]}]}]},"opportunity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時機，機會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>opportunity</b> is a situation in which it is possible for you to do something that you want to do. 機會","examples":["I had an opportunity to go to New York and study. 我曾有過一個去紐約學習的機會。","...equal opportunities in employment. …平等的就業機會。"]}]}]},"origin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"起源，起因；出身，血統；（原）產地；肌肉起端；神經（或血管）起端；（數）原點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the beginning, cause, or source of something as its <b>origin</b> or <b>origins</b>. 起源; 起因","examples":["...theories about the origin of life. …有關生命起源的各種理論。","Their medical problems are basically physical in origin. 他們的疾病基本是身體上的問題造成的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you talk about a person's <b>origin</b> or <b>origins</b>, you are referring to the country, race, or living conditions of their parents or ancestors. 出身; 血統","examples":["Thomas has not forgotten his humble origins. 托馬斯沒有忘記他卑微的出身。","...people of Asian origin. …亞洲血統的人。"]}]}]},"orphan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孤兒；（印刷）孤行"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成為孤兒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"孤兒的，無雙親的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orphan</b> is a child whose parents are dead. 孤兒","examples":["...a young orphan girl brought up by peasants. …她是由農民養大的孤兒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"被動及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a child <b>is orphaned</b>, their parents die, or their remaining parent dies. 使成為孤兒","examples":["...a fifteen-year-old boy left orphaned by the recent disaster. …這個15歲的男孩因最近的災難而成為孤兒。"]}]}]},"ownership":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"所有權，物主身份"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ownership</b> of something is the state of owning it. 所有權","examples":["On January 23rd, the U.S. decided to relax its rules on the foreign ownership of its airlines. 1月23日，美國決定放寬對其航空公司外國所有權的規定。","...the growth of home ownership. …住房擁有率的增長。"]}]}]},"outline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輪廓，外形；輪廓圖，草圖；提綱，大綱；梗概，要點；（詞的）速記形式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"概述，略述；勾勒，描畫……的輪廓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>outline</b> an idea or a plan, you explain it in a general way. 概述","examples":["The mayor outlined his plan to clean up the town's image. 市長概述了他清理整頓該市形象的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that an object <b>is outlined</b> when you can see its general shape because there is light behind it. 映襯出…的輪廓","examples":["The Ritz was outlined against the lights up there. 里茲飯店的輪廓被上方的燈光映襯了出來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outline</b> is a general explanation or description of something. 概要","examples":["Following is an outline of the survey findings. 以下是調查結果的概要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>outline</b> of something is its general shape, especially when it cannot be clearly seen. 輪廓","examples":["He could see only the hazy outline of the goalposts. 他只能看見球門柱模糊的輪廓。"]}]}]},"pail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桶，提桶；一桶的量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pail</b> is a bucket, usually made of metal or wood. (木或鐵)桶","examples":[]}]}]},"opposite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全相反的，截然不同的；相反的，另一邊的；（在說話者、所指的人或物）對面的；（角）對的；（葉，芽）對生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"對立的人（或物），對立面；反義詞"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在對面，在對過"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……對面，與……相對；與……合演，與……聯袂演出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>opposite</b> another, it is on the other side of a space from it. 在…對面","examples":["Jennie had sat opposite her at breakfast. 吃早餐時，珍妮已坐在她的對面。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Opposite</b> is also an adverb. 在對面地","examples":["He looked up at the buildings opposite, but could see no open window. 他抬頭看了看對面那些樓，但看不見一扇開著的窗戶。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>opposite</b> side or part of something is the side or part that is furthest away from you. 對面的","examples":["...the opposite corner of the room. …房間裡的另一個對角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Opposite</b> is used to describe things of the same kind which are completely different in a particular way. For example, north and south are opposite directions, and winning and losing are opposite results in a game. 截然相反的","examples":["All the cars driving in the opposite direction had their headlights on. 所有迎面開來的車都開著前燈。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>opposite</b> <b>of</b> someone or something is the person or thing that is most different from them. 正好相反的人或事物","examples":["Ritter was a very complex man but Marius was the opposite, a simple farmer. 裡特是個非常複雜的人，而馬裡厄斯則恰恰相反，是個單純的農民。","Well, whatever he says you can bet he's thinking the opposite. 哦，無論他說什麼，你都能肯定他想的是另外一套。"]}]}]},"original":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"起初的，原先的；原作的，真跡的；新創作的，未發表的；獨創的，新穎的；有獨到見解的，有獨創性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（藝術作品或檔案的）原件，原稿；（文學作品中人物或地點的）原型；原版書，原版唱片；（根據服裝展特製圖樣定做的）真品原板服裝；<非正式>（舉止、服裝等）怪異滑稽的人，獨特有趣的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>original</b> when referring to something that existed at the beginning of a process or activity, or the characteristics that something had when it began or was made. 起初的","examples":["The original plan was to go by bus. 起初的計劃是乘公交車去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>original</b> document or work of art is not a copy. 原件的; 原作的","examples":["...an original film poster. …一張原版的電影海報。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>original</b> piece of writing or music was written recently and has not been published or performed before. 新創作的","examples":["...with catchy original songs by Richard Warner. …配有幾首由理查德·沃納新創作的朗朗上口的歌曲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone or their work as <b>original</b>, you mean that they are very imaginative and have new ideas. 原創的; 創新的","examples":["It is one of the most original works of imagination in the language. 這是用這種語言創作的最具想像力的原創作品之一。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a document, a work of art, or a piece of writing is an <b>original</b>, it is not a copy or a later version. 原件; 原作","examples":["When you have filled in the questionnaire, copy it and send the original to your employer. 填好問卷調查表之後，影印並將原件交給你的僱主。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"原創性","examples":["He was capable of writing things of startling originality. 他能寫出有驚人原創性的作品。"]}]}]},"pancake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薄煎（烤，烙）餅；<美>（當早點吃的）厚煎餅（通常和楓糖漿一起食用）；（尤為演員化裝用的）粉餅；平墜降落（同 pancake landing）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（飛機）平墜降落；（飛行員）駕機平墜降落；<非正式>使平展，把……壓平"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pancake</b> is a thin, flat, circular piece of cooked batter made from milk, flour, and eggs. Pancakes are usually eaten for breakfast, with butter and syrup. 薄煎餅","examples":[]}]}]},"pal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>朋友，夥伴；<非正式>（對男子的不友好的稱呼）傢伙，小子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成為夥伴（或朋友）（pal up）；結伴一起玩（pal around）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>pals</b> are your friends. 朋友","examples":["They talked like old pals. 他們像老朋友一樣交談。"]}]}]},"palace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王宮，（官位極高者的）府邸；住在王宮裡的人，王室（the Palace）；大廈，豪宅"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"王宮的，（總統）官邸的；與政府人員有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>palace</b> is a very large impressive house, especially one that is the official home of a king, queen, or president. 宮殿","examples":["...Buckingham Palace. …白金漢宮。"]}]}]},"panic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恐慌，驚慌；人心惶惶，惶恐不安；忙亂，慌亂；粟，稷，糜子"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"恐慌的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）恐慌，（使）驚慌失措"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Panic</b> is a very strong feeling of anxiety or fear that makes you act without thinking carefully. 驚慌","examples":["An earthquake has hit the capital, causing damage to buildings and panic among the population. 一場地震襲擊了首都，造成建築物的損壞和人們的驚慌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Panic</b> or <b>a</b> <b>panic</b> is a situation in which people are affected by a strong feeling of anxiety. 恐慌局面","examples":["There was a moment of panic as it became clear just how vulnerable the nation was. 隨著國家如此脆弱變得明顯，出現了一陣恐慌局面。","I'm in a panic about getting everything done in time. 我處於一陣要把一切及時安排就緒的恐慌中。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>panic</b> or if someone <b>panics</b> you, you suddenly feel anxious or afraid, and act quickly and without thinking carefully. 使驚慌; 驚慌","examples":["Guests panicked and screamed when the bomb exploded. 炸彈爆炸的時候，客人們驚慌失措，驚聲尖叫。","The unexpected and sudden memory briefly panicked her. 這突如其來的記憶使她一時驚慌失措。"]}]}]},"pad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（吸收液體、保潔或保護用的）軟墊，墊狀物；（動物的）肉掌，（人的）手指肚；便箋本，拍紙簿；發射臺，停機坪；（睡蓮的）浮葉；低沉的腳步聲；（電子）焊接區，焊接點；<非正式，舊>住處，寓所"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用軟物）填塞，墊襯；（新增不必要的資訊以）拉長（pad sth. out）；<美>虛報（開支、賬單）；沿著（路、路線）走；放輕腳步走；在比賽（尤指板球賽）前穿上防護墊（pad up）；（板球）（擊球手）有意用護墊擋球（pad up）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（PAD）外周動脈疾病（peripheral arterial disease）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pad</b> is a fairly thick, flat piece of a material such as cloth or rubber. Pads are used, for example, to clean things, to protect things, or to change their shape. (清洗、保護或防止變形用的) 墊; 護墊","examples":["He withdrew the needle and placed a pad of cotton over the spot. 他把針拔出來，將一塊藥棉蓋在針眼上。","...a scouring pad. …一個擦洗墊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pad</b> <b>of</b> paper is a number of pieces of paper attached together along the top or the side, so that each piece can be torn off when it has been used. 便箋簿","examples":["She wrote on a pad of paper. 她寫在了一本便箋簿上。","Have a pad and pencil ready and jot down some of your thoughts. 準備一本便箋簿和一支鉛筆，迅速地記下你的一些想法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a dull soft sound, esp of footsteps 低沉的(腳步)聲音","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pad</b> is a platform or an area of flat, hard ground where helicopters take off and land or rockets are launched. (直升機) 停機坪; (火箭) 發射臺","examples":["...a little round helicopter pad. …一個小的圓形直升機停機坪。","...a landing pad on the back of the ship. …一個位於船尾的停機坪。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>pads</b> <b>of</b> a person's fingers and toes or of an animal's feet are the soft, fleshy parts of them. 指頭肚; 爪墊","examples":["Tap your cheeks all over with the pads of your fingers. 用你的指頭肚輕拍你的整個面頰。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>pads</b> somewhere, they walk there with steps that are fairly quick, light, and quiet. 輕步快走","examples":["Freddy speaks very quietly and pads around in soft velvet slippers. 弗雷迪一邊非常小聲地說著，一邊穿著柔軟的天鵝絨拖鞋輕快地四處走著。","...a dog padding through the streets. …一隻輕快穿過街道的狗。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pad</b> something, you put something soft in it or over it in order to make it less hard, to protect it, or to give it a different shape. (用軟物) 填充; 墊襯","examples":["Pad the back of a car seat with a pillow. 在汽車座椅靠背上墊一個頭枕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pad</b> or <b>pad out</b> a piece of writing or a speech <b>with</b> unnecessary words or pieces of information, you include them to make it longer and hide the fact that you do not have very much to say. (新增不必要的詞句或資訊以) 拉長 (文章或演講)","examples":["Quotations should be used to make points, not to pad the essay. 引語應該是用來陳述觀點的，而不是為了拉長文章。","The reviewer padded out his review with a lengthy biography of the author. 那位評論家用冗長的作者生平來拉長他的評論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an employee with an expense account <b>pads</b> their expenses, they claim that their expenses are greater than they really are in order to get more money from their employer. 虛報 (花費)","examples":["She was fired for padding her expenses. 她因為虛報她的花費而被解僱。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"填充的; 有襯墊的","examples":["...a padded jacket. …一件有襯墊的夾克。"]}]}]},"paradise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某些宗教所指的）天堂，天國；樂土（指美好的環境）；（某類活動或某類人的）樂園，完美去處；至福，極樂；（《聖經》中的）伊甸園（Paradise）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"According to some religions, <b>paradise</b> is a wonderful place where people go after they die, if they have led good lives. 天堂","examples":["The Koran describes paradise as a place containing a garden of delight. 《古蘭經》把天堂描繪成一個擁有快樂花園的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a place or situation that seems beautiful or perfect as <b>paradise</b> or <b>a paradise</b>. 樂園; 至福境地","examples":["Bali is one of the world's great natural paradises. 巴厘島是世界最大的自然樂園之一。"]}]}]},"password":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"密碼；口令，暗語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>password</b> is a secret word or phrase that you must know in order to be allowed to enter a place such as a military base, or to be allowed to use a computer system. 口令","examples":["Advance and give the password. 向前走，說口令！"]}]}]},"parcel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>包裹，郵包；一批，一群；一塊土地（尤指地產的一部分）；<英>有餡料的食品（通常指油酥點心）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>把……包起來（parcel sth. up）；分配（parcel sth. out）；（航海）用塗油帆布條纏包（繩索）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>parcel</b> is something wrapped in paper, in a bag or large envelope, or in a box, usually so that it can be sent to someone by mail. 包裹; 郵包","examples":["They also sent parcels of food and clothing. 他們還寄送了成包的食物和衣物。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>part and parcel</b> <b>of</b> something else, you are emphasizing that it is involved or included in it. 重要部分","examples":["Learning about life in a new culture is part and parcel of what newcomers to America face. 學習在一種新的文化中生活是每一個新來美國的人要面對的事情中的重要部分。"]}]}]},"parade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遊行；列隊表演，展示；檢閱，閱兵；閱兵場；一系列（人或事）；誇示，炫耀；<英>（用於街道名稱中）商業街，公共廣場；<英>（常指遠離大街的）一小排店鋪"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"遊行；（使）列隊行進，接受檢閱；招搖過市，大搖大擺；把（囚犯）示眾；展示，展覽；誇示，炫耀（財產、知識等）；（使）冒充，偽裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>parade</b> is a procession of people or vehicles moving through a public place in order to celebrate an important day or event. 遊行","examples":["A military parade marched slowly and solemnly down Pennsylvania Avenue. 一個軍事閱兵隊伍沿著賓夕法尼亞大街緩慢而莊嚴地行進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Parade</b> is a formal occasion when soldiers stand in lines to be seen by an officer or important person, or march in a group. 閱兵式","examples":["He had them on parade at six o'clock in the morning. 他讓他們在早上6點接受檢閱。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>parade</b> somewhere, they walk together in a formal group or a line, usually with other people watching them. 遊行","examples":["More than four thousand soldiers, sailors, and airmen paraded down the Champs Elysées. 超過四千名士兵、水手和飛行員沿著香榭麗舍大街遊行。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If prisoners <b>are paraded</b> through the streets of a town or on television, they are shown to the public, usually in order to make the people who are holding them seem more powerful or important. 把…遊街; 把…示眾","examples":["Five leading fighter pilots have been captured and paraded before the media. 5名領先的戰鬥機飛行員被俘，並在媒體前示眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>parades</b> a person, you mean that they show that person to others only in order to gain some advantage for themselves. (為使自己獲益而) 展示","examples":["Captured prisoners were paraded before television cameras. 被捕獲的罪犯們被展示在電視攝像機前。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>parade</b> something, they show it in public so that it can be admired. (為炫耀而) 展示","examples":["Valentino is eager to see celebrities parading his clothes at big occasions. 瓦倫蒂諾渴望看到名人們在盛大場合展示他的服裝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something <b>parades as</b> or <b>is paraded as</b> a good or important thing, you mean that some people say that it is good or important but you think it probably is not. 吹噓; 誇耀","examples":["...all the fashions that parade as modern movements in art. …所有被吹噓成現代藝術運動的風尚。"]}]}]},"passport":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"護照；途徑，手段"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>passport</b> is an official document containing your name, photograph, and personal details, which you need to show when you enter or leave a country. 護照","examples":["You should take your passport with you when changing money. 你換錢的時候應該帶著護照。"]}]}]},"passion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛戀，情慾；激情，熱情；酷愛，熱衷的愛好（或活動等）；盛怒，激憤；耶穌的受難（the Passion）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Passion</b> is strong sexual feelings toward someone. 強烈的情慾","examples":["...my passion for a dark-haired, slender boy named Josh. …我對一個黑頭髮、身材修長名叫喬希的男孩的強烈的情慾。","...the expression of love and passion. …愛與情慾的表白。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Passion</b> is a very strong feeling about something or a strong belief in something. 強烈的感情; 強烈的信任","examples":["He spoke with great passion. 他激情洋溢地講話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>passion for</b> something, you have a very strong interest in it and like it very much. 酷愛","examples":["She had a passion for gardening. 她對於園藝有一份熱愛。"]}]}]},"passage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過道，走廊；（人體的）管道；段落，章節；通道，通路；通行權，通行許可；經過，穿過；（時間的）流逝；（法案的）透過；航程，船票；過渡，轉變；（候鳥的）遷徙；<醫>（微生物的）傳代；巴沙基（盛裝舞步和古典騎術的高抬腿舞步）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<醫>使（微生物）繼代移種"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>passage</b> is a long narrow space with walls or fences on both sides, that connects one place or room with another. 過道; 走廊","examples":["Harry stepped into the passage and closed the door behind him. 哈里走進走廊，關上他身後的門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>passage</b> in a book, speech, or piece of music is a section of it that you are considering separately from the rest. 章節; 段落; 樂段","examples":["He read a passage from Emerson. 他讀了一段愛默生的作品。","...the passage in which the author speaks of the world of imagination. …作者談論幻想世界的那個段落。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>passage</b> is a long narrow hole or tube in your body, that air or liquid can pass along. (人體內的) 道","examples":["...cells that line the air passages. …沿著通氣管排列的細胞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>passage</b> <b>through</b> a crowd of people or things is an empty space that allows you to move through them. 通路","examples":["He cleared a passage for himself through the crammed streets. 他在擁擠的大街他為自己清出一條通路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>passage</b> of someone or something is their movement from one place to another. 透過; 經過","examples":["Germany had not requested Franco's consent for the passage of troops through Spain. 德國未曾請求弗朗哥同意他們的軍隊透過西班牙。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>passage</b> of someone or something is their progress from one situation or one stage in their development to another. 過渡","examples":["...to ease their passage to a market economy. …使他們向市場經濟平穩過渡。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>passage</b> of a bill is its progress through Congress so that it can become a law. (法案等的) 透過","examples":["...a Medicare bill expected to get final passage in Congress today. …一個預期今天在國會得到最後透過的醫保法案。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>The passage of</b> a period of time is its passing. (時間的) 推移","examples":["...an asset that increases in value with the passage of time. …一項隨著時間的推移而增值的資產。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"A <b>passage</b> is a journey by ship. 航程","examples":["We'd arrived the day before after a 10-hour passage from Anchorage. 從安克雷奇出發經過10小時航程後，我們於前天到達。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you are granted <b>passage</b> through a country or area of land, you are given permission to go through it. 通行許可","examples":["Mr. Thomas would be given safe passage to and from Jaffna. 托馬斯先生將會得到往返於賈夫納的安全通行許可。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"a sideways walk in which diagonal pairs of feet are lifted alternately 正步","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to move or cause to move at a passage 以正步跑","examples":[]}]}]},"pavement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>人行道；<美>（公路或街道的）硬路面；鋪過的表面（地方）；（水平分佈的）裸露巖面，礫石灘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>pavement</b> is the hard surface of a road. 路面","examples":["The tyres of Lenny's bike hissed over the wet pavement. 倫尼的腳踏車輪胎嘶嘶地駛過溼漉漉的路面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pavement</b> is a path with a hard surface, usually by the side of a road. 人行道","examples":["Two men and a woman were walking briskly down the pavement towards him. 兩個男子和一個女子正輕快地沿著人行道朝他走去。"]}]}]},"patience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耐心；耐性；忍耐力；考驗某人的耐心；<英>單人紙牌遊戲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>patience</b>, you are able to stay calm and not get annoyed, for example, when something takes a long time, or when someone is not doing what you want them to do. 耐心","examples":["He doesn't have the patience to wait. 他沒有耐心等。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>tries</b> your <b>patience</b> or <b>tests</b> your <b>patience</b>, they annoy you so much that it is very difficult for you to stay calm. 考驗某人的耐心極限","examples":["He tended to stutter whenever he spoke to her, which tried her patience. 他一跟她講話就結巴，這考驗了她耐心極限。"]}]}]},"paw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動物的）爪子；<非正式>（人的）手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用爪子抓（或撓）；摸弄，猥褻地動手動腳；胡亂地翻找；（用手指）觸碰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>paws</b> of an animal such as a cat, dog, or bear are its feet, which have claws for gripping things and soft pads for walking on. 腳爪","examples":["The kitten was black with white front paws and a white splotch on her chest. 那隻小貓除了白色前爪和胸部的一塊白色區域外是黑色的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an animal <b>paws</b> something, or <b>paws</b> at it, it draws its foot over it or down it. 用腳抓; 用腳刨","examples":["Madigan's horse pawed the ground. 馬迪根的馬刨了地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person <b>paws</b> another, or <b>paws</b> at them, they touch or stroke them in a way that the other person finds offensive. (冒犯性地) 撫摸","examples":["Stop pawing me, Geraldo! 傑拉爾多，別摸我！"]}]}]},"pea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豌豆（粒）；豆角；<西印度>豆莢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Peas</b> are round green seeds that grow in long thin cases and are eaten as a vegetable. 豌豆","examples":[]}]}]},"pause":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暫停，停頓；暫停鍵；延長記號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"暫停，停頓；（按暫停鍵）暫停；躊躇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pause</b> while you are doing something, you stop for a short period and then continue. 停頓","examples":["\"It's rather embarrassing,\" he began, and paused. “這很讓人尷尬，” 他開始說道，又停頓了片刻。","He talked for two hours without pausing for breath. 他談了兩個小時，沒有停下來喘口氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pause</b> is a short period when you stop doing something before continuing. 停頓","examples":["After a pause Al said sharply: \"I'm sorry if I've upset you.\" 停了一下之後艾爾突然說：“如果我讓你不安了，我很抱歉。”"]}]}]},"pearl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"珍珠；珍珠母；珠狀物；極其優秀的人，珍貴的東西；人造珍珠；珠灰色；珍珠項鍊，珍珠首飾（pearls）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>成珠狀滴；使呈珠灰色，使呈藍灰色；（潛水）採珍珠；用珍珠裝飾"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"珍珠般的；鑲珍珠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pearl</b> is a hard round object that is shiny and creamy white in colour. Pearls grow inside the shell of an oyster and are used for making expensive jewellery. 珍珠","examples":["She wore a string of pearls at her throat. 她那時脖子上帶著一串珍珠。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pearl</b> is used to describe something that looks like a pearl. 珍珠般的","examples":["...tiny pearl buttons. …珍珠般的小釦子"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"of, made of, or set with pearl or mother-of-pearl 珍珠的; 貝母的; 鑲珠的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to set with or as if with pearls 用珍珠鑲嵌; 仿珍珠鑲嵌","examples":[]}]}]},"peak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巔峰，頂點；山頂；有尖峰的山；尖端，尖頂；帽簷，帽舌；極值，峰值；（艏或艉的）尖艙；斜桁外端，（帆的）後上角"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"達到高峰，達到最大值；<古>消瘦，衰弱，精神萎靡"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巔峰狀態的，最高的；高峰時期的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>peak</b> of a process or an activity is the point at which it is at its strongest, most successful, or most fully developed. (過程、活動的) 頂峰","examples":["The firm has slashed its workforce from a peak of 150,000 in 2000. 2000年那家公司把其員工從15萬峰值進行了大幅裁減。","...a flourishing career that was at its peak at the time of his death. …在他去世時處於鼎盛時期的興旺事業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>peak</b> is a mountain or the top of a mountain. 山峰","examples":["...the snow-covered peaks. …白雪覆蓋的山峰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>peak</b> of a cap is the part at the front that sticks out over your eyes. 帽簷","examples":["His eyes were shaded by the peak of his cap. 他的眼睛被帽簷遮住。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>peaks</b>, it reaches its highest value or its highest level. 達到峰值","examples":["Temperatures have peaked at over 90 degrees. 溫度已達到峰值，超過了90度。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>peak</b> level or value of something is its highest level or value. 峰值的","examples":["Today's price is 59% lower than the peak level of $1.5 million. 今天的價格比150萬美元的峰值水平低了59%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Peak</b> times are the times when there is most demand for something or most use of something. 高峰的 (時期)","examples":["It's always crowded at peak times. 在高峰期總是很擁擠。"]}]}]},"peel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"除去，剝去（水果、蔬菜等的）皮；去掉，剝掉，揭掉；剝落，脫落，脫皮；（水果，蔬菜）有可被除掉的皮；（槌球）把（另一球員的球）傳過拱門"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（水果、蔬菜的）皮，外皮；去角質；（16世紀時建在英格蘭和蘇格蘭交界各郡的）堡塔，堡寨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>peel</b> of a fruit such as a lemon or an apple is its skin. You can also refer to a <b>peel</b>. (果) 皮","examples":["...grated lemon peel. …磨碎了的檸檬皮。","...a banana peel. …一塊香蕉皮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a long-handled shovel used by bakers for moving bread, in an oven (烤麵包時用的)長柄鏟","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(in Britain) a fortified tower of the 16th century on the borders between England and Scotland, built to withstand raids (英國)防禦堡塔; 16世紀，建於英格蘭和蘇格蘭交界處","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>peel</b> fruit or vegetables, you remove their skins. 削皮","examples":["She sat down in the kitchen and began peeling potatoes. 她在廚房裡坐下，開始削土豆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>peel</b> <b>off</b> something that has been sticking to a surface or if it <b>peels</b> <b>off</b>, it comes away from the surface. 剝掉; 剝落","examples":["One of the kids was peeling plaster off the wall. 其中一個孩子在剝牆上的灰泥。","It took me two days to peel off the labels. 我花了兩天時間才剝掉那些標籤。","Paint was peeling off the walls. 牆上的漆正在剝落。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a surface <b>is peeling</b>, the paint on it is coming away.  掉漆","examples":["Its once-elegant white pillars are peeling. 曾一度典雅的白色立柱在掉漆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are peeling</b> or if your skin <b>is peeling</b>, small pieces of skin are coming off, usually because you have been burned by the sun. (人) 脫皮; (皮) 脫落","examples":["His face was peeling from sunburn. 他的臉因日曬而在脫皮。"]}]}]},"permission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同意，許可；許可證，書面許可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who has authority over you gives you <b>permission</b> <b>to</b> do something, they say that they will allow you to do it. 許可","examples":["He asked permission to leave the room. 他請求離開房間的許可。","They cannot leave the country without permission. 沒有許可他們不得離開這個國家。"]}]}]},"penny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"便士（英國貨幣單位，100便士等於1英鎊）；便士（英國1971年前使用的硬幣，12便士等於1先令）；分（美國和加拿大貨幣單位）；一小筆錢（pennies）；一分一毫（用於強調沒錢）（a penny）；迪納裡厄斯（古羅馬的金幣或銀幣）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>penny</b> is one cent, or a coin worth one cent. 便士","examples":["Unleaded petrol rose more than a penny a gallon. 無鉛汽油每加侖漲了一個多便士。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say, for example, that you do not have <b>a penny</b>, or that something does not cost <b>a penny</b>, you are emphasizing that you do not have any money at all, or that something did not cost you any money at all. 分文","examples":["From the day you arrive at my house, you need not spend a single penny. 從你到我家的那一天起，你就分文不需花了。"]}]}]},"pest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"害蟲，有害動物；<非正式>討厭的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pests</b> are insects or small animals that damage crops or food supplies. 害蟲; 有害的小動物","examples":["...crops which are resistant to some of the major insect pests and diseases. …能抵抗一些主要病蟲害的莊稼。","Each year ten percent of the crop is lost to a pest called corn rootworm. 每年有10%的作物受損於一種叫做玉米根蟲的害蟲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone, especially a child, as a <b>pest</b> if they keep bothering you. 討厭鬼 (尤指小孩)","examples":["He climbed on the table, pulled my hair, and was generally a pest. 他爬上桌子，揪我的頭髮，真是個討厭鬼。"]}]}]},"performance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"表演，演出；工作情況，表現；（投資的）業績；執行，履行；麻煩，苦差事（a performance）；藝術上的表現，演技；（汽車的）效能；（語言學）語言表現，言語行為"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"效能卓越的，高效能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>performance</b> involves entertaining an audience by doing something such as singing, dancing, or acting. 表演","examples":["Inside the theatre, they were giving a performance of Bizet's Carmen. 他們正在劇院裡演出比才的《卡門》。","...her performance as the betrayed Medea. …她出演被出賣的美狄亞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>performance</b> is how successful they are or how well they do something. 業績; 效能","examples":["That study looked at the performance of 18 surgeons. 那項研究著眼於18位外科醫生的業績。","The poor performance has been blamed on the recession and cheaper sports car imports. 業績慘淡歸咎於經濟衰退和更便宜跑車的進口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>performance</b> <b>of</b> a task is the fact or action of doing it. 執行; 實施","examples":["He devoted in excess of seventy hours a week to the performance of his duties. 他每週在自己職責的執行上投入超過70個小時。"]}]}]},"peep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"窺視，偷看；隱現，微現；看；（使）發出喇叭聲；（使）發出尖細的聲音"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一瞥；<非正式>說話，聲音；吱吱聲，啾啾聲；（汽車的）喇叭聲；<非正式>人（雜誌用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>peep</b>, or <b>peep at</b> something, you take a quick look at it, often secretly and quietly.  瞥一眼","examples":["Children came to peep at him around the doorway. 孩子們來到門口偷看他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>peeps</b> out from behind or under something, a small part of it is visible or becomes visible. (從後面或下面) 探出; 露出","examples":["Purple and yellow flowers peeped up between rocks. 紫色與黃色的花從岩石之間探出頭來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Peep</b> is also a noun. 一瞥","examples":["\"Fourteen minutes,\" Chris said, taking a peep at his watch. “十四分鐘，”克里斯瞥了一眼手錶說道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a peeping sound 唧唧聲; 啾啾聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(esp of young birds) to utter shrill small noises (尤指幼鳥)唧唧叫; 啾啾叫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>don't hear a peep</b> <b>from</b> someone, you mean that they do not say anything or make any noise. 聽到一點聲音","examples":["You don't hear a peep from her once she's gone to bed. 她一上床，你就不會聽見她吭一聲。"]}]}]},"personality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"個性，性格；魅力，品格（如活力、友好、幽默等）；（地方或事物的）特色；有突出個性的人；名人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>personality</b> is your whole character and nature. 性格; 品性","examples":["She has such a kind, friendly personality. 她有著如此友善的性格。","The contest was as much about personalities as it was about politics. 這次競賽既比政治策略，又比品質性格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has <b>personality</b> or is <b>a personality</b>, they have a strong and lively character. (堅強、活潑的) 個性","examples":["...a woman of great personality. …一個很有個性的女人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a famous person, especially in entertainment, broadcasting, or sports, as a <b>personality</b>. (尤指娛樂、廣播、體育界) 名人","examples":["...the radio and television personality, Johnny Carson. …廣播電視名人約翰尼·卡森。"]}]}]},"permit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"批准，許可；（使）成為可能；破例做，放縱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"執照，許可證；古氏鯧鰺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>permits</b> something, they allow it to happen. If they <b>permit</b> you <b>to</b> do something, they allow you to do it. 允許","examples":["He can let the court's decision stand and permit the execution. 他能讓法院的判決成立，並允許處決。","The guards permitted me to bring my camera and tape recorder. 守衛允許我帶上相機和錄音機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation <b>permits</b> something, it makes it possible for that thing to exist, happen, or be done or it provides the opportunity for it. 使成為可能; 成為可能","examples":["Try to go out for a walk at lunchtime, if the weather permits. 如果天氣條件允許，午飯時儘量出去散散步。","This method of cooking also permits heat to penetrate evenly from both sides. 這種烹調方法還能使兩面均勻受熱。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>permit</b> is an official document which says that you may do something. For example, you usually need a <b>permit</b> to work in a foreign country. 許可證","examples":["He has to apply for a permit, and we have to find him a job. 他必須申請一個許可證，而我們必須給他找一份工作。"]}]}]},"pay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"支付，付；償還，繳納；給予，致以；給……付工資；（投資等）產生……利潤，（工作等）有……報酬；划算，有好處；付出代價；盈利；用瀝青（或焦油）填塞（甲板或木船接縫）以防止漏水；（政府或機構透過提高價格、稅率等使某人）為......買單；儲蓄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"工資，薪水；付款；回報"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（電視節目）付費的，收費的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>pay</b> an amount of money <b>to</b> someone, you give it to them because you are buying something from them or because you owe it to them. When you <b>pay</b> something such as a bill or a debt, you pay the amount that you owe. 支付; 償還","examples":["Owners who have already paid for repairs will be reimbursed. 已經付了修繕費的業主將會得到退費。","The wealthier may have to pay a little more in taxes. 更有錢的人可能得多交點稅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>are paid</b>, you get your wages or salary from your employer. 給…支付工薪","examples":["The lawyer was paid a huge salary. 這個律師拿了很高的薪金。","I get paid monthly. 我拿月薪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are paid</b> <b>to</b> do something, someone gives you some money so that you will help them or perform some service for them. 僱傭","examples":["There are people who are paid to sit around and play games. 有人受僱閒坐著玩遊戲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a job, deal, or investment <b>pays</b> a particular amount, it brings you that amount of money. 帶來 (某數量的錢); 帶來錢","examples":["We're stuck in jobs that don't pay very well. 我們被困在錢給得很少的工作中。","The banks don't pay interest on those accounts. 銀行對那些賬戶不支付利息。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a course of action <b>pays</b>, it results in some advantage or benefit for you. (某種做法) 有好處","examples":["It pays to invest in protective clothing. 在防護服上投資值。","We must demonstrate that aggression will not pay. 我們必須證明侵犯是沒有好處的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>pay</b> <b>for</b> something that you do or have, you suffer as a result of it. (為…) 付出代價","examples":["He was to pay dearly for his lack of resolve. 他將為自己缺乏決心付出高昂的代價。","Why should I pay the penalty for somebody else's mistake? 我為什麼要為別人的錯誤而受罰呢？"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>pay</b> money <b>down</b> when you are buying something, you pay only a part of the total cost. You then finish paying for it later, usually by paying a certain amount every month. 首付 (商品部份金額)","examples":["We paid $500 down and $100 a month after that. 我們首付了$500，以後每月付$100。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>pay</b> with some nouns, such as in the expressions <b>pay a visit</b> and <b>pay attention</b>, to indicate that something is given or done. (與名詞連用) 進行; 給予","examples":["Pay us a visit next time you're in Portland. 下次來波特蘭的時候來看看我們。","He felt a heavy bump, but paid no attention to it. 他感覺重重地撞了一下，但沒有在意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>pay</b> is the money that you get from your employer as wages or salary. 薪水","examples":["...their complaints about their pay and conditions. …他們對薪水和工作條件的不滿。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a government or organization makes someone <b>pay</b> <b>for</b> something, it makes them responsible for providing the money for it, for example, by increasing prices or taxes. 承擔費用","examples":["...a legally binding international treaty that establishes who must pay for environmental damage. …一項規定誰必須為環境的破壞承擔費用的具有法律約束力的國際公約。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a job, deal, or investment <b>pays</b>, it brings you a profit or earns you some money. 給報酬","examples":["There are some agencies now specializing in helping older people to find jobs which pay. 現在有一些機構專門幫助年紀較大的人找到有酬工作。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to caulk (the seams of a wooden vessel) with pitch or tar 用瀝青或焦油堵(木船的船縫)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something that you buy or invest in <b>pays for itself</b> after a period of time, the money you gain from it, or save because you have it, is greater than the amount you originally spent or invested. 賺回本錢","examples":["...investments in energy efficiency that would pay for themselves within five years. …5年內能回本的、在能效方面的投資。"]}]}]},"pickle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泡菜，醃菜；菜醬，泡菜汁；<美>醃黃瓜；<非正式>困境；<英，非正式，舊>搗蛋鬼，討厭鬼；（用來清洗金屬物體的）淡酸水"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鹽醃製，醋漬；酸洗（金屬）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pickles</b> are vegetables or fruit, sometimes cut into pieces, which have been kept in vinegar or salt water for a long time so that they have a strong, sharp taste. 泡菜","examples":["...a bowl of sliced pickles in lemon juice. …一碗浸在檸檬汁中的泡菜片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pickle</b> is a cold spicy sauce with pieces of vegetables and fruit in it. 泡菜醬","examples":["...jars of pickle. …成罐的泡菜醬。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>pickle</b> food, you keep it in vinegar or salt water so that it does not go bad and it develops a strong, sharp taste. 醃製","examples":["Select your favourite fruit or veg and pickle them while they are still fresh. 挑選你最喜歡的水果或蔬菜，趁新鮮醃製起來。"]}]}]},"pill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥片，藥丸；（女用）口服避孕藥 （the pill）；<美>（衣服或布料上的）球粒，纖維絨球； <美>討厭的傢伙；<非正式>（某些運動用的）球，彈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（衣服或布料）起球粒，結絨；把……製成丸劑；（使）服用藥丸；<古>搶劫，掠奪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pills</b> are small solid round masses of medicine or vitamins that you swallow without chewing. 藥丸","examples":["Why do I have to take all these pills? 我為什麼非得全部吃了這些藥丸？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a woman is <b>on</b> <b>the pill</b>, she takes a special pill that prevents her from becoming pregnant. 避孕藥","examples":["She had been on the pill for three years. 她曾服了3年的避孕藥。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to give pills to 開藥給","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to peel or skin (something) 剝(或削)皮","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or group has to accept a failure or an unpleasant piece of news, you can say that it was <b>a bitter pill</b> or <b>a bitter pill to swallow</b>. 苦果","examples":["You're too old to be given a job. That's a bitter pill to swallow. 你年齡太大，不能給你工作了。那樣的事情是吞苦果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something to <b>sweeten the pill</b>, they do it to make some unpleasant news or an unpleasant measure more acceptable. 讓壞訊息或措施變得容易接受","examples":["A few words of praise help to sweeten the pill of criticism. 幾句讚賞的話有助於使批評更容易被接受。"]}]}]},"pint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"品脫（液量單位，約等於半升）；<英>一品脫啤酒；<英>一品脫牛奶；<英>一品脫大的杯子所能盛下的量（貝類計量單位）；一品脫容器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pint</b> is a unit of measurement for liquids. It is equal to 473 cubic centimetres or one eighth of a gallon. 品脫 (液量單位，1品脫等於473立方厘米或1/8加侖)","examples":["...a pint of ice cream. …一品脫冰淇淋。"]}]}]},"pine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"松樹；松木；……松（用於其他科針葉類樹木名稱中）；……松（用於某方面類似松樹而與松樹無關的植物名稱中）；有松針香味；<非正式>鳳梨"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因死亡、離別） 難過，悲傷；苦苦思念；<古>為……悲哀，哀悼；渴望，苦苦盼望（尤指不太可能擁有的東西）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pine tree</b> or a <b>pine</b> is a tall tree that has very thin, sharp leaves called needles and a fresh smell. Pine trees have leaves all year round. 松樹","examples":["...high mountains covered in pine trees. …長滿松樹的高山。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pine</b> is the wood of this tree. 松木","examples":["...a big pine table. …一張大松木桌子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pine for</b> someone who has died or gone away, you want them to be with you very much and feel sad because they are not there. 苦苦思念","examples":["She'd be sitting at home pining for her lost husband. 她會一直坐在家裡苦苦思念著她死去的丈夫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pine for</b> something, you want it very much, especially when it is unlikely that you will be able to have it. 渴望 (尤指不可能得到的東西)","examples":["I pine for the countryside. 我渴望鄉下的生活。"]}]}]},"pilot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飛行員；領航員；（船隻的）領航員；（電視）試播節目；常燃小火；航海手冊；<非正式>職業騎師；<古>嚮導；（火車頭前端的）排障器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"試點的；（電信）控制引導訊號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"駕駛（飛行器）；領航；試驗，試行；使（新法律）順利透過；<文>帶領，指引"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pilot</b> is a person who is trained to fly an aircraft. 飛行員","examples":["He spent seventeen years as an airline pilot. 他當了17年的航空公司飛行員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pilot</b> is a person who steers a ship through a difficult stretch of water, for example, the entrance to a harbour. 領航員","examples":["It seemed that the pilot had another ship to take up the river that evening. 似乎該領航員那天晚上還要引領另一艘船沿河而上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>pilots</b> an aircraft or ship, they act as its pilot. 駕駛 (飛機); 為 (船隻) 領航","examples":["He piloted his own plane part of the way to Washington. 他駕駛自己的飛機飛行了去華盛頓的部分路程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a government or organization <b>pilots</b> a programme or project, they test it, before deciding whether to introduce it on a larger scale. 試行 (計劃或方案)","examples":["Teachers are piloting a literature-based reading programme. 老師們正在試開一門以文學為基礎的閱讀課程。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pilot</b> plan or a <b>pilot</b> project is one that is used to test an idea before deciding whether to introduce it on a larger scale. 試驗性的","examples":["The plan is to launch a pilot programme next summer. 計劃是在明年夏天實施一個試驗性方案。"]}]}]},"plum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"李子，李樹；紫紅色，李子色；<非正式>令人垂涎之物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"稱心的，值得擁有的；紫紅色的，李子色的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美，非正式>正好地，準確地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plum</b> is a small, sweet fruit with a smooth purple, red, or yellow skin and a pit in the middle. 李子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a small rosaceous tree, <b>Prunus domestica,</b> with white flowers and an edible oval fruit that is purple, yellow, or green and contains an oval stone 西洋李; 歐洲李","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>plum</b> or <b>plum-coloured</b> is a dark reddish-purple colour. 紫紅色的","examples":["...plum-coloured silk. …紫紅色的絲綢。"]}]}]},"plumber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水管工人，水電工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plumber</b> is a person whose job is to connect and repair things such as water and drainage pipes, bathtubs, and toilets. 管子工; 水暖工","examples":[]}]}]},"pity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同情，憐憫；可惜的事，遺憾的事；仁慈，慈悲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"同情，憐憫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>pity</b> <b>for</b> someone, you feel very sorry for them. 同情心","examples":["He felt a sudden tender pity for her. 他突然對她起了溫柔的同情心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that it is <b>a pity</b> that something is the case, you mean that you feel disappointment or regret about it. 遺憾的事","examples":["It is a great pity that all students in the city cannot have the same chances. 很遺憾的是，並非該市所有學生都能擁有同樣的機會。","It's a pity you've arrived so late in the year. 真遺憾，你這一年來得太遲了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone shows <b>pity</b>, they do not harm or punish someone they have power over. 仁慈; 憐憫","examples":["Noncommunist forces have some pity toward people here. 非共產主義者的軍隊有些憐憫這裡的人們。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pity</b> someone, you feel very sorry for them. 同情","examples":["I don't know whether to hate or pity him. 我不知道是該恨他還是該同情他。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take pity on</b> someone, you feel sorry for them and help them. 同情","examples":["No woman had ever felt the need to take pity on him before. 之前，沒有哪個女人覺得有必要同情他。"]}]}]},"plastic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"塑膠；信用卡；塑膠製造業（plastics）；塑膠學（plastics）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"塑膠制的；人造的，不自然的；可塑的；（藝術用語）造型的，塑造的；（科技用語）範性的，塑性的；適應環境多樣性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Plastic</b> is a material that is produced from oil by a chemical process and that is used to make many objects. It is light in weight and does not break easily. 塑膠","examples":["...a wooden crate, sheltered from rain by sheets of plastic. …一隻板條木箱，用塑膠膜蓋著遮雨。","A lot of the plastics that carmakers are using cannot be recycled. 汽車製造商們正在使用的很多塑膠製品是無法回收再用的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you use <b>plastic</b> or <b>plastic money</b> to pay for something, you pay for it with a credit card instead of using cash. 信用卡","examples":["Using plastic to pay for an order is simplicity itself. 使用信用卡支付訂單本身就很簡單。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>plastic</b>, you mean that you think it looks or tastes unnatural or not real. (樣子或味道) 不自然的","examples":["You wanted proper home-cooked meals, you said you had enough plastic hotel food and airline food. 你想吃地道的家常飯菜，你說你吃夠了賓館裡和航班上味道不純的食品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>plastic</b> is soft and can easily be made into different shapes. 柔軟易塑的","examples":["You can also enjoy mud packs with the natural mud, smooth, grey, soft, and plastic as butter. 你還可以享受天然泥制面膜，灰色的泥，光滑、柔軟, 像黃油一樣易塑。"]}]}]},"plenty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"富裕，充裕"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"大量，眾多"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大量，很多；<非正式>非常，十分；<非正式>足夠有餘"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"<非正式>很多，大量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>plenty of</b> something, there is a large amount of it. If there are <b>plenty of</b> things, there are many of them. <b>Plenty</b> is used especially to indicate that there is enough of something, or more than you need. 大量的; 充裕的","examples":["There was still plenty of time to take Jill out for pizza. 還有充裕的時間帶吉爾出去吃比薩。","Most businesses face plenty of competition. 多數企業都面臨大量的競爭。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Plenty</b> is also a pronoun. 充裕","examples":["I don't believe in long interviews. Fifteen minutes is plenty. 我不相信長時間的面試會有什麼好處，15分鐘就足夠了。"]}]}]},"pit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"坑，窪；（表面上的）疤痕，凹陷；礦井；<非正式>異常凌亂的地方；樂池，樂隊席；<非正式>糟糕的事物（the pits）；<美>（水果或蔬菜的）核；<非正式>腋窩，心窩；（賽車道旁的）檢修加油站；深淵，絕境；交易場所；鬥獸場；<英，舊>（劇場）正廳後座；無底洞，巨庫；<英，非正式>床"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使競爭，使對立；去除……的果核；（使）有疤痕，（使）凹陷；停車加油，停車檢修；窖藏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pit</b> is the underground part of a mine, especially a coal mine.  礦井","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gravel pit</b> or <b>clay pit</b> is a very large hole that is left where gravel or clay has been dug from the ground. (挖出沙礫或黏土後留下的) 大坑","examples":["This area of former farmland was worked as a gravel pit until 1964. 這片昔日的農田在1964年前是被用作採礫坑的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pit</b> is a large hole that is dug in the ground. 大坑","examples":["Eric lost his footing and began to slide into the pit. 埃裡克一失足，開始滑進坑裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In motor racing, <b>the</b> <b>pits</b> are the areas at the side of the track where drivers stop to get more fuel and to repair their cars during races. (賽車道旁的) 檢修加油站","examples":["He moved quickly into the pits and climbed rapidly out of the car. 他急速駛入檢修加油站，迅速爬出賽車。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The pits is a slang word for the worst possible person, place, or thing. (俗語)最糟的人、地方或事情","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>pit</b> is the large hard seed of a fruit or vegetable. 核","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two opposing things or people <b>are pitted against</b> one another, they are in conflict. 使對立","examples":["You will be pitted against two, three, or four people who are every bit as good as you are. 你將和兩個、三個或者四個跟你一樣好的人對決。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to extract the stone from (a fruit) 除去(水果的)核","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pit</b> your <b>wits against</b> someone, you compete with them in a test of knowledge or intelligence. 與…鬥智","examples":["I'd like to manage at the very highest level and pit my wits against the best. 我希望在最高水平上管理，與最優秀的人鬥智。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a feeling <b>in the pit of</b> your <b>stomach</b>, you have a tight or sick feeling in your stomach, usually because you are afraid or anxious. (因恐懼或焦慮而生的)異於平常的感覺","examples":["I had a funny feeling in the pit of my stomach. 我內心深處有種奇怪的感覺。"]}]}]},"politician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"從政者，政治家；政客，善於玩弄權術者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>politician</b> is a person whose job is in politics, especially a member of the government. 政客 (尤指政府成員); 政治家","examples":["They have arrested a number of leading opposition politicians. 他們已經逮捕了一些主要的反對黨政治家。"]}]}]},"pole":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"杆，柱；地極；截然相反的兩極之一；磁極；滑雪杖（ski pole 的簡稱）；簡易魚竿；直幹幼樹；電極；車轅；（幾何）（球體的）軸極；（幾何）（極座標的）極點；（細胞、器官、身體部分的）極；杆（尤指用來測量土地長度的單位）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用篙撐（船）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Pole）波蘭人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pole</b> is a long thin piece of wood or metal, used especially for supporting things. 柱; 杆","examples":["The truck crashed into a telegraph pole. 卡車撞上了電線杆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The Earth's <b>poles</b> are the two opposite ends of its axis, its most northern and southern points. 地極","examples":["For six months of the year, there is hardly any light at the poles. 一年中的6個月裡，地球的兩極幾乎沒有任何光線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The two <b>poles</b> of a magnet are the two ends of the magnet where the magnetic force is strongest. 磁極","examples":["The important fact is that the two poles of the magnet work in opposite ways. 重要的事實是，磁體兩極的執行方式完全相反。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The two <b>poles</b> of a range of qualities, opinions, or beliefs are the completely opposite qualities, opinions, or beliefs at either end of the range. (品質、觀點或信仰) 截然相反的兩極","examples":["The two politicians represent opposite poles of the political spectrum. 這兩位政治家代表了各種政治傾向中的兩個極端。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that two people or things are <b>poles apart</b>, you mean that they have completely different beliefs, opinions, or qualities. (信仰、觀點或品質) 截然相反的","examples":[]}]}]},"pony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矮種馬，小型馬； <美，非正式>賽馬（the ponies）；<非正式>小酒杯，一小杯酒；<英>25 英鎊；馬尾辮； <非正式>小酒杯，一小杯酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>（為……）付款（pony up）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pony</b> is a small or young horse. 小馬","examples":[]}]}]},"porcelain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瓷；瓷器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瓷制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Porcelain</b> is a hard, shiny substance made by heating clay. It is used to make delicate cups, plates, and ornaments. 瓷","examples":["There were lilies everywhere in tall white porcelain vases. 到處都是插在白瓷高花瓶裡的百合花。"]}]}]},"postage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵資，郵費；一定面額的郵票；郵寄，郵遞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Postage</b> is the money that you pay for sending letters and packages by mail. 郵資","examples":["All prices include postage and handling. 所有價格都包含郵資和手續費。"]}]}]},"portion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某物的）一部分；（尤指餐館中食物的）一份，一客；（責任、過失、職責等的）一份，一部分；<法律>（根據法律贈與或遺留給繼承人的）一份財產；<古> 命運，天數"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分配；<古> 給（新娘）嫁妝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>portion of</b> something is a part of it. 部分","examples":["Damage was confined to a small portion of the castle. 城堡僅有一小部分受到了損壞。","I have spent a considerable portion of my life here. 我已在這裡度過了一生中的大部分時光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>portion</b> is the amount of food that is given to one person at a meal. (食物的) 一份","examples":["Desserts can be substituted by a portion of fresh fruit. 甜點可以替換成一份新鮮水果。","The portions were generous. 份量很足。"]}]}]},"politics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"政治，政治活動（事務）；政治事業；政治學；(某團體、組織等內的）爭權活動，權術；政治信仰，政治觀點；（尤指跟社會權力和地位有關的領域、理論或活動的）主張，觀（念）；政治思想體系，政治局勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Politics</b> are the actions or activities concerned with achieving and using power in a country or society. The verb that follows <b>politics</b> may be either singular or plural. 政治","examples":["Many people think Nixon transformed American politics. 許多人認為尼克松改變了美國的政治。","He quickly involved himself in local politics. 他很快就參與到地方政治活動中去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>politics</b> are your beliefs about how a country ought to be governed. 政治觀點","examples":["My politics are well to the left of centre. 我的政治觀點很靠左翼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Politics</b> is the study of the ways in which countries are governed. 政治學","examples":["He began studying politics and medieval history. 他開始學習政治學和中世紀史。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Politics</b> can be used to talk about the ways that power is shared in an organization and the ways it is affected by personal relationships between people who work together. The verb that follows <b>politics</b> may be either singular or plural. 權術","examples":["You need to understand how office politics influence the working environment. 你需要明白辦公室權術怎樣影響工作環境。"]}]}]},"poll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"民意調查，民意測驗；選舉投票，計票；投票數；投票點（the polls）；頭頂，頭皮；無角動物（尤指無角牛）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……進行民意測驗（調查）；獲得（票數）；（電信，計算機）輪詢，探詢；截掉（動物，尤指小牛）的角；<古>修枝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>poll</b> is a survey in which people are asked their opinions about something, usually in order to find out how popular something is or what people intend to do in the future. 民意測驗","examples":["Polls show that the European treaty has gained support in Denmark. 民意測驗顯示，歐洲條約已經在丹麥獲得支援。","We are doing a weekly poll on the president, and clearly his popularity has declined. 我們正在對總統進行每週一次的民意測驗，很顯然他的受歡迎度已經下降了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The polls</b> means an election for a country's government, or the place where people go to vote in an election. 政治大選; 投票地點","examples":["Incumbent officeholders are difficult to defeat at the polls. 現任官員很難在選舉中被擊敗。","Voters are due to go to the polls on Sunday to elect a new president. 選民們按計劃將於週日前往投票站選舉新總統。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are polled</b> <b>on</b> something, you are asked what you think about it as part of a survey. 對…進行民意測驗","examples":["More than 18,000 people were polled. 18000多人接受了民意測驗。","Audiences were going to be polled on which of three pieces of contemporary music they liked best. 聽眾將就3首現代樂曲中最喜歡哪一首接受民意調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a political party or a candidate <b>polls</b> a particular number or percentage of votes, they get that number or percentage of votes in an election. 獲得…選票","examples":["The result showed he had polled enough votes to force a second ballot. 結果顯示他獲得了足夠的選票來促使第二輪選舉。"]}]}]},"portrait":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指只刻畫臉、頭和肩部的）肖像，照片，雕像；描繪，描述；（檔案的）縱向列印格式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（紙張、頁面、照片等）豎式的，縱向的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>portrait</b> is a painting, drawing, or photograph of a particular person. 畫像; 像片","examples":["...badly painted family portraits. …繪製得很差的全家福畫像。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>portrait</b> of a person, place, or thing is a verbal description of them. 文字描述","examples":["...this gripping, funny portrait of Jewish life in 1950s Hoboken. …這段文字引人入勝、妙趣橫生地描述了20世紀50年代霍博肯猶太人的生活。"]}]}]},"poster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海報，招貼畫；大幅裝飾畫；發帖人，跟帖人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"張貼海報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>poster</b> is a large notice or picture that you stick on a wall or board, often in order to advertise something. 海報; 招貼","examples":["I had seen the poster for the jazz festival in Monterey. 我已經見到了蒙特雷爵士音樂節的海報。"]}]}]},"postponement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"推遲，延緩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>postponement</b> of an event is the act of delaying it or arranging for it to take place at a later time than originally planned. 延期","examples":["The postponement was due to a dispute over where the talks should be held. 延期是因為在會議地點上有爭議。"]}]}]},"plug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"插頭；插座；（洗滌槽或浴缸的）塞子；堵塞物；棉球，藥棉；螺釘楔子；（車輛引擎的）火花塞；推銷，宣傳；（壓實的）塊，口嚼煙；<美，非正式>（嬰兒的）橡皮奶頭；巖頸；（供移植的）幼苗，草皮；魚餌；<美>消防栓；<美，非正式>疲憊的馬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"堵，塞；補足；接電源，插插頭；推廣，宣傳；<美，非正式>射擊，射殺；<非正式>艱難地走，埋頭於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plug</b> on a piece of electrical equipment is a small plastic object with two or three metal pins that fit into the holes of an electric outlet and connects the equipment to the electricity supply. 插頭","examples":["I used to go around and take every plug out at night. 過去我常在夜裡巡視一番，拔掉所有的插頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>plug</b> is an electric outlet. 插座","examples":["Then Bob spotted the problem - the plug in the wall hadn't been switched on. 然後鮑勃發現了問題——牆上的插座沒有開啟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plug</b> is a thick, circular piece of rubber or plastic that you use to block the hole in a bathtub or sink when it is filled with water. (浴缸、洗滌槽的) 塞子","examples":["She put the plug in the sink and filled it with cold water. 她用塞子塞住水池，並將其注滿冷水。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>plug</b> is a small, round piece of wood, plastic, or wax that is used to block holes. (木頭、塑膠或臘制的) 塞子","examples":["A plug had been inserted in the drill hole. 那個鑽孔裡已經塞上了塞子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Plug</b> is also a noun. 大力宣傳","examples":["Let's do this show tonight and it'll be a great plug, a great promotion. 讓我們今晚進行這場演出吧。這將會是一場盛大而絕妙的宣傳。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plug</b> a hole, you block it with something. 堵; 塞","examples":["Crews are working to plug a major oil leak. 機組人員正在努力堵一個漏油的大洞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>plugs</b> a commercial product, especially a book or a film, they praise it in order to encourage people to buy it or see it because they have an interest in it doing well. 大力宣傳 (商品，尤為圖書或電影)","examples":["We did not want people on the show who are purely interested in plugging a book or film. 我們不想讓那種純粹只對宣傳某書籍或電影感興趣的人上節目。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in a position of power <b>pulls the plug on</b> a project or <b>on</b> someone's activities, they use their power to stop them from continuing. (利用權力) 終止 (方案或活動)","examples":["The banks have the power to pull the plug on the project. 銀行有權終止該專案。"]}]}]},"pottery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陶器；陶土，黏土；製陶，陶藝；陶瓷廠；陶瓷之都（斯塔福德郡特倫特河畔斯托克市周邊地區，為英國陶瓷工業基地）（the Potteries）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>pottery</b> to refer to pots, dishes, and other objects made from clay and then baked in an oven until they are hard. 陶器","examples":["...a fine range of pottery. …一系列的優質陶器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>pottery</b> to refer to the hard clay that some pots, dishes, and other objects are made of. 陶土","examples":["Some bowls were made of pottery and wood. 一些碗是用陶土和木頭做的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Pottery</b> is the craft or activity of making objects out of clay. 製陶; 陶器製造術","examples":["He became interested in sculpting and pottery. 他變得對雕刻和製陶感興趣了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>pottery</b> is a factory or other place where pottery is made. 製陶廠","examples":["...the many galleries and potteries which sell pieces by local artists. …出售本地藝術家作品的諸多畫廊和製陶廠。"]}]}]},"poverty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貧窮，貧困；<正式>貧乏，低劣；個人財產權的放棄（作為宗教誓約的一部分）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Poverty</b> is the state of being extremely poor. 貧窮","examples":["According to World Bank figures, 41 percent of Brazilians live in absolute poverty. 根據世界銀行的統計數字，41％的巴西人生活在極度貧困之中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>poverty</b> to refer to any situation in which there is not enough of something or its quality is poor. 貧乏","examples":["...a poverty of ideas. …思想的貧乏。"]}]}]},"priest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牧師，神職人員；木漁槌（垂釣時用以打死已上鉤的魚）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>任命……為司鐸（或祭司）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>priest</b> is a member of the Christian clergy in the Catholic, Anglican, or Orthodox church. (聖公會教的) 牧師; (天主教、東正教的) 神父","examples":["He had trained to be a Catholic priest. 他接受培訓成了一名天主教神父。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In many non-Christian religions a <b>priest</b> is a man who has particular duties and responsibilities in a place where people worship. (非基督教的) 祭司","examples":["...a New Age priest or priestess. …一個“新世紀”男祭司或女祭司。"]}]}]},"prayer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禱文，禱詞；祈禱，禱告；祈禱儀式，祈禱會（prayers）；願望，祈望；極小的機會，極小的可能性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prayer</b> is the activity of speaking to God. 祈禱","examples":["They had joined a religious order and dedicated their lives to prayer and good works. 他們參加了一個宗教團體，獻身於祈禱和做善事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>prayer</b> is the words a person says when they speak to God. 禱詞","examples":["They should take a little time and say a prayer for the people on both sides. 他們應該花點兒時間為雙方人民祈禱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a strong hope that you have as your <b>prayer</b>. 祈求","examples":["This drug could be the answer to our prayers. 這種藥也許是對我們的祈求的回答。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A short religious service at which people gather to pray can be referred to as <b>prayers</b>. 祈禱儀式","examples":["He promised that the boy would be back at school in time for evening prayers. 他承諾孩子會及時回到學校參加晚上的祈禱儀式。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a person who prays 祈禱者","examples":[]}]}]},"powder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"粉，粉末；撲面粉，美容粉；細雪，粉狀雪；火藥，炸藥"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"往（臉或身體）上搽粉；撒粉（狀物）於（表面），以粉（狀物）覆蓋；使（某物）成粉狀；變成粉末"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Powder</b> consists of many tiny particles of a solid substance. 粉末","examples":["Put a small amount of the powder into a container and mix with water. 將少許該粉末放入容器裡與水混合。","...cocoa powder. …可可粉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a woman <b>powders</b> her face or some other part of her body, she puts face powder or talcum powder on it. 往…上搽粉","examples":["She powdered her face and applied her lipstick and rouge. 她往臉上搽了粉，又塗了她的口紅和胭脂。"]}]}]},"preparation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"準備（指動作或過程）；準備工作，籌備工作（preparations）；（食物、醫藥、化妝品的）製劑，配製品；（為科學實驗或醫藥檢驗預備的）標本；（樂）準備音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Preparation</b> is the process of getting something ready for use or for a particular purpose, or making arrangements for something. 準備","examples":["Rub the surface of the wood in preparation for the varnish. 打摩木頭的表面為上油漆做準備。","Few things distracted the pastor from the preparation of his weekly sermons. 幾乎沒有什麼事情使該牧師從他每週佈道的準備中分心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Preparations</b> are all the arrangements that are made for a future event. 準備工作","examples":["The United States is making preparations for a large-scale airlift of 1,200 American citizens. 美國在為一次1200名美國公民的大規模空運做準備。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>preparation</b> is a mixture that has been prepared for use as food, medicine, or a cosmetic. (用作食品、藥品或化妝品的) 配製品","examples":["...anti-aging creams and sensitive-skin preparations. …抗衰老面霜和針對敏感皮膚的製劑。"]}]}]},"profit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"利潤，盈利；<正式> 利益，好處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲益，得益（於）；贏利，獲利"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>profit</b> is an amount of money that you gain when you are paid more for something than it cost you to make, get, or do it. 利潤","examples":["The bank made pre-tax profits of $6.5 million. 該銀行獲得了稅前650萬美元的利潤。","You can improve your chances of profit by sensible planning. 你可以透過合理的計劃增加盈利的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>profit</b> <b>from</b> something, you earn a profit from it. (從…中) 獲利","examples":["No one was profiting inordinately from the war effort. 沒有人在從戰爭中發大財。","He has profited by selling his holdings to other investors. 他已透過將他所持有的賣給其他投資者們而獲利。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>profit</b> <b>from</b> something, or it <b>profits</b> you, you gain some advantage or benefit from it. 使 (某人) 獲利; 獲利","examples":["Jennifer wasn't yet totally convinced that she'd profit from a more relaxed lifestyle. 珍妮弗還沒有完全相信她會從更放鬆的生活方式中獲益。","So far the French alliance had profited the rebels little. 到那時為止，法聯盟還沒讓叛軍得到多少好處。"]}]}]},"process":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"步驟，程式；（自然或偶然的）變化過程；（為達到某目標的）過程，程序；製作方法，加工方法；<法律>傳票；（生，剖）端突，突起"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（印刷）三原色的，三色版的； 經過特殊加工的；照相板的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用化學物品或機器）處理，加工；稽核，受理（正式檔案或請求）；（計算機）處理（資料）；沖洗（照片）；加工（食品）；<正式>列隊行進；把（頭髮）弄成直髮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>process</b> is a series of actions which are carried out in order to achieve a particular result.  過程","examples":["There was total agreement to start the peace process as soon as possible. 全體同意儘快啟動和平程序。","They decided to spread the building process over three years. 他們決定在三年內分期完成該建造過程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>process</b> is a series of things that happen naturally and result in a biological or chemical change. 程序","examples":["It occurs in elderly men, apparently as part of the aging process. 作為衰老程序的一部分，它明顯發生在老年男性身上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Process</b> is also a noun. 過程","examples":["...the cost of reengineering the production process. …重新設計生產過程的成本。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"加工","examples":["America sent cotton to England for processing. 美國把棉花運到英格蘭加工。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"處理","examples":["...data processing. …資料處理。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When raw materials or foods <b>are processed</b>, they are prepared in factories before they are used or sold. 加工","examples":["...fish which are processed by the best methods: from freezing to canning and smoking. …用從冷凍到裝罐和熏製等最好的方法加工的魚。","The material will be processed into plastic pellets. 該原料將被加工成塑膠顆粒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>process</b> information, they put it through a system or into a computer in order to deal with it. 處理","examples":["...facilities to process the data, and the right to publish the results. …處理資料的裝置和公佈結果的權利。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people <b>are processed</b> by officials, their case is dealt with in stages and they pass from one stage of the process to the next. 按程式處理","examples":["Patients took more than two hours to be processed through the department. 病人們花了兩個多小時才走完那個科室程式。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to subject to a routine procedure; handle 工藝流程; 處理","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to proceed in or as if in a procession 列隊行進","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in the process of</b> doing something, you have started to do it and are still doing it. 在…過程中","examples":["The administration is in the process of drawing up a peace plan. 該政府正在起草一項和平計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are doing something and you do something else <b>in the process</b>, you do the second thing as part of doing the first thing. 在此過程中","examples":["You have to let us struggle for ourselves, even if we must die in the process. 你得讓我們自己去奮鬥，即使在此過程中我們必須死亡。"]}]}]},"product":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"產品，製品；（自然、化學或工業過程的）生成物；（特定行動、影響或事件的）結局；（受某種環境或經歷影響而形成的）產物；積，乘積；總稱（商業性）音樂製品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>product</b> is something that is produced and sold in large quantities, often as a result of a manufacturing process. 產品","examples":["Try to get the best product at the lowest price. 盡力以最低的價格買到最好的產品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is a <b>product of</b> a situation or process, you mean that the situation or process has had a significant effect in making them what they are. 產物","examples":["We are all products of our time. 我們都是我們時代的產物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a substance formed in a chemical reaction (化學反應)生成物","examples":[]}]}]},"pressure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壓力，擠壓；（氣體或液體形成的）壓力，壓強；心理壓力，緊張；催促，要求；氣壓"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……施加壓力，強迫；使……增壓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pressure</b> is force that you produce when you press hard on something. (用力按壓而產生的) 壓力","examples":["She kicked at the door with her foot, and the pressure was enough to open it. 她用腳踢門，其產生的壓力足以把門開啟。","The pressure of his fingers had relaxed. 他手指的壓力已經減弱了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pressure</b> in a place or container is the force produced by the quantity of gas or liquid in that place or container. (某地或某容器內的氣體或液體產生的) 壓力","examples":["The window in the cockpit had blown in and the pressure dropped dramatically. 駕駛艙的窗子已向內破裂，氣壓驟然下降。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is <b>pressure</b> <b>on</b> a person, someone is trying to persuade or force them to do something. (因極力勸說或強迫某人做某事而造成的) 壓力","examples":["He may have put pressure on her to agree. 他可能已對她施壓讓她同意。","A lot of dot-coms were under pressure from their investors. 很多網路公司那時都在承受著來自其投資者的壓力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are experiencing <b>pressure</b>, you feel that you must do a lot of tasks or make a lot of decisions in very little time, or that people expect a lot from you. (因任務緊、決策時間短或別人的期望多而感到的) 壓力","examples":["Can you work under pressure? 你能在壓力下工作嗎？","Even if I had the talent to play tennis I couldn't stand the pressure. 即使我有打網球的天資，我也承受不了那種壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pressure</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you try forcefully to persuade them to do it. 對…施加壓力","examples":["He will never pressure you to get married. 他永遠也不會給你施加壓力讓你結婚。","The Senate should not be pressured into making hasty decisions. 參議院不應受壓而做出草率的決定。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受壓的","examples":["You're likely to feel anxious and pressured. 你可能會感到焦慮並且有壓力。"]}]}]},"proof":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"證明，證據；檢驗，證實；（數學）驗算，驗證；校樣，樣張；（酒的）標準酒精度；<蘇格蘭>法官單獨聽證"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"防……的，耐……的；試印的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護……免受影響（或損害）；印……的校樣；校對；<美>加水使（酵母）活化；<美>揉（麵糰）；<美>（麵糰）發酵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Proof</b> is a fact, argument, or piece of evidence showing that something is definitely true or definitely exists. 證明","examples":["You have to have proof of residence in the state of Texas, such as a Texas ID card. 你必須有在德克薩斯州的居住證明，例如一張得克薩斯州的身份證。","This is not necessarily proof that he is wrong. 這未必是他錯了的證明。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Proof</b> is used after a number of degrees or a percentage, when indicating the strength of a strong alcoholic drink such as whisky. (用於度數或百分比之後) 標準酒精度的","examples":["...a glass of Wild Turkey bourbon: 101 proof. …一杯101標準酒精度的野火雞牌波旁威士忌。"]}]}]},"pub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酒吧，酒館；酒店，旅館；路人局（遊戲術語）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"公眾的；公開的（public 的縮寫）；出版，發行；出版物，發行物；（資訊的） 刊登，公佈 （publication 的縮寫）；（媒體的）關注，報道；宣傳業，廣告行業；引起公眾關注的事物（publicity的縮寫）；宣傳， 推廣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>時常出入於酒吧，泡酒吧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pub</b> is a building where people can have drinks, especially alcoholic drinks, and talk to their friends. Many pubs also serve food. 酒館","examples":["He was in the pub until closing time. 他在酒館裡待到打烊。"]}]}]},"proposal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"提議，建議；提案；（計劃、建議等的）提出；求婚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>proposal</b> is a plan or an idea, often a formal or written one, which is suggested for people to think about and decide upon. (常為正式書面的) 提議","examples":["The president is to put forward new proposals for resolving the country's constitutional crisis. 總統將提出解決國家憲法危機的新議案。","...the governor's proposal to restrict cigarette sales. …州長關於限制香菸銷售的提案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>proposal</b> is the act of asking someone to marry you. 求婚","examples":["After a three-weekend courtship, Pam accepted Randy's proposal of marriage. 經過一段為期3個週末的戀愛，帕姆接受了蘭迪的求婚。"]}]}]},"program":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）程式（=programme）；計劃，規劃；（音樂會、戲劇等演出的）節目單，（體育運動、比賽等的）專案介紹；（電視或廣播）節目；<美>課程，大綱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給計算機）編寫程式，設計程式；設定，預設；使……有傾向；為……安排節目"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>program</b> a machine or system, you set its controls so that it will work in a particular way. 設定 (機器、系統等的) 程式","examples":["Parents can program the machine not to turn on at certain times. 父母可設定機器在某些時候不啟動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>program</b> a computer, you give it a set of instructions to make it able to perform a particular task. 給 (計算機) 程式設計","examples":["He programmed his computer to compare the 1,431 possible combinations of pairs in this population. 他給他的計算機編了程來比較這些人中1431種可能的成對組合。","...45 million people, about half of whom can program their own computers. 4500萬人，其中約有一半會給他們自己的計算機程式設計。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>program</b> is a set of instructions that a computer follows in order to perform a particular task. (計算機) 程式","examples":["The chances of an error occurring in a computer program increase with the size of the program. 計算機程式出錯的機率隨程式的增大而增高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"程式設計","examples":["...programming skills. …程式設計技巧。"]}]}]},"protection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保護，防護；保護物，護身符；保險；避孕（措施）；保護費；貿易保護，關稅保護制；保護條例，保護措施；（登山）安全保護器材數量與質量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To give or be <b>protection</b> against something unpleasant means to prevent people or things from being harmed or damaged by it. 保護","examples":["Such a diet is widely believed to offer protection against a number of cancers. 這樣的日常飲食被廣泛認為可以預防多種癌症。","It is clear that the primary duty of parents is to provide protection for our children. 很明顯，父母的首要職責就是為孩子提供保護。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an insurance policy gives you <b>protection</b> <b>against</b> an event such as death, injury, fire, or theft, the insurance company will give you or your family money if that event happens. (保險單提供的) 保險","examples":["Insurance can be purchased to provide protection against such risks. 買保險可以應對此類風險。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a government has a policy of <b>protection</b>, it helps its own industries by putting a tax on imported goods or by restricting imports in some other way. 貿易保護","examples":["Over the same period trade protection has increased in the rich countries. 在同一時期，富國的貿易保護增強了。"]}]}]},"property":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"所有物，財產；地產，房地產；房地產股票（或投資）（properties）；<法律> 所有權，處置權；特性，性質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>property</b> is all the things that belong to them or something that belongs to them. 財產","examples":["Richard could easily destroy her personal property to punish her for walking out on him. 理查德可以輕而易舉地毀掉她的私有財產作為對她背叛他的懲罰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>property</b> is a building and the land belonging to it. 房地產","examples":["Cecil inherited a family property near Stamford. 塞西爾繼承了斯坦福附近的一處家族房產。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>properties</b> of a substance or object are the ways in which it behaves in particular conditions. (物質、物體的) 特性","examples":["A radio signal has both electrical and magnetic properties. 無線電訊號既具有電的特性也具有磁的特性。"]}]}]},"radar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雷達，無線電探測系統；（人的）直覺感知能力，（對因素或潮流等的）敏感性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Radar</b> is a way of discovering the position or speed of objects such as aircraft or ships when they cannot be seen, by using radio signals. 雷達","examples":["...a ship's radar screen. …一艘船的雷達顯示屏。"]}]}]},"raisin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葡萄乾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Raisins</b> are dried grapes. 葡萄乾","examples":["...homemade oatmeal with brown sugar and raisins. …自家煮的放有紅糖和葡萄乾的麥片粥。"]}]}]},"quarrel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爭吵，拌嘴；抱怨（或不贊成）的理由；<史>（用石弓或勁弩發射的）方鏃箭，方頭投射物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"爭吵，吵架；不同意，反對；抱怨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarrel</b> is an angry argument between two or more friends or family members. 爭吵","examples":["I had a terrible quarrel with my other brothers. 我和其他幾個兄弟大吵了一架。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you have no <b>quarrel</b> with someone or something, you mean that you do not disagree with them. 分歧","examples":["We have no quarrel with the people of Spain or of any other country. 我們和西班牙人民或其它任何國家的人民都沒有分歧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Quarrels</b> between countries or groups of people are disagreements, which may be diplomatic or include fighting. 爭端","examples":["New Zealand's quarrel with France over the Rainbow Warrior incident was formally ended. 紐西蘭和法國之間關於“彩虹勇士號”事件的爭端已經正式了結。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an arrow having a four-edged head, fired from a crossbow (用弩射出的)箭頭上有四條刀口的箭","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When two or more people <b>quarrel</b>, they have an angry argument. 爭論","examples":["At one point we quarrelled, over something silly. 有一次，我們為了一件愚蠢的事爭論起來。"]}]}]},"razor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剃（須）刀，刮鬍刀；處於險境，境況岌岌可危（on a razor edge）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用剃刀剃，用刮鬍刀刮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>razor</b> is a tool that people use for shaving. 剃刀","examples":["...a plastic disposable razor. …一把一次性的塑膠剃刀。"]}]}]},"rag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抹布，破布； 破衣爛衫（rags）；<非正式>服裝（rags）；<非正式>質量低劣的報紙，小報；雷格泰姆樂曲；<英>（學生每年組織的）慈善募捐活動；石板瓦；<英>堅硬石灰岩，硬質岩石（=ragstone）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，舊，非正式> 嘲笑，戲弄；責罵，呵斥；用碎布將（油漆）擦在表面上；（冰球）（為掌握比賽節奏）運球，帶球；變破碎"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（RAG）檢索增強生成（retrieval-augmented generation）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rag</b> is a piece of old cloth which you can use to clean or wipe things. 抹布","examples":["He was wiping his hands on an oily rag. 他正用一塊油膩膩的抹布擦手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rags</b> are old torn clothes. 破爛衣服","examples":["There were men, women, and small children, some dressed in rags. 有男人、女人和孩子，其中一些人穿著破爛的衣服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People refer to a newspaper as a <b>rag</b> when they have a poor opinion of it. 質量低劣的報紙","examples":["\"This man Tom works for a local rag,\" he said. “那個叫湯姆的人為當地一家小報幹活，”他說。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a boisterous practical joke, esp one on a fellow student (對同學的)惡作劇; 玩笑","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a period, usually a week, in which various events are organized to raise money for charity, including a procession of decorated floats and tableaux (英國大學的)慈善籌款周; 慈善籌款期","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"(<b>as modifier</b>) 慈善籌款周的; 慈善籌款期的","examples":[]},{"num":"7.","zh":"a piece of ragtime music 一首拉格泰姆音樂","examples":[]},{"num":"8.","zh":"a roofing slate that is rough on one side 屋頂石板","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>rags</b> you, they tease you in a friendly way. (善意地) 揶揄","examples":["\"They always rag me about my car,\" he says. “他們總拿我的汽車取笑我，”他說。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to compose or perform in ragtime 譜寫拉格泰姆音樂; 演奏拉格泰姆音樂","examples":[]}]}]},"quote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引用，引述；舉例說明；將......描述為；開價，報價；為（股票、黃金或外匯）報價；為......打出（某投注賠率）； 為（企業的股份）上市，掛牌"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"引文，引語；報價，開價；（股票）報價，牌價；（建成某物或修理某物的）報價單；引號（quotes）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>quote</b> someone as saying something, you repeat what they have written or said. 引用; 引述","examples":["He quoted Mr. Polay as saying that peace negotiations were already underway. 他引用波利先生的話說，和平談判已在進行。","I gave the letter to the local press and they quoted from it. 我把信交給了當地的報社，他們從中引用了內容。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>quote</b> something such as a law or a fact, you state it because it supports what you are saying. 引用 (法律條款、事實等)","examples":["The Congresswoman quoted statistics saying that the standard of living of the poorest people had fallen. 這位女國會議員援引統計資料說，赤貧人口的生活水平已經下降。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>quotes</b> a price <b>for</b> doing something, they say how much money they would charge you for a service they are offering or a for a job that you want them to do. 報 (價)","examples":["A travel agent quoted her $260 for a flight from Boston to New Jersey. 一家旅行社給她從波士頓到新澤西的航班報價$260。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a company's shares, a substance, or a currency <b>is quoted</b> at a particular price, that is its current market price. 報 (公司股票、物質、貨幣) 的牌價","examples":["In early trading in Hong Kong yesterday, gold was quoted at $368.20 an ounce. 昨天在香港早市的交易中，黃金被報出每盎司$368.20的牌價。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quote</b> <b>from</b> a book, poem, play, or speech is a passage or phrase from it. 引文; 引語","examples":["The paper starts its editorial comment with a quote from an unnamed member of the House. 該報社論以一位匿名議員的引語展開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>quote</b> <b>for</b> a piece of work is the price that someone says they will charge you to do the work. 報價","examples":["Always get a written quote for any repairs needed. 對任何所需的修理都索取一份書面報價。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Quotes</b> are the same as <b>quotation marks</b>. 引號","examples":["The word \"remembered\" is in quotes. “”一詞是打了引號的。"]}]}]},"punch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一拳，一擊；<非正式>（出拳打擊時所需要的）力量；感染力，活力；打孔器，穿孔機；孔洞；壓印器，衝壓機；潘趣酒（由果汁和酒製成的甜味飲品）；龐奇（奇形怪狀、鉤鼻、駝背的小丑，木偶戲《龐奇和朱迪》中的男主角）（Punch）；（矮壯的）薩福克馱馬（Suffolk punch）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用拳猛擊（某人或某物）；按（按鈕或鍵）；（用工具或機器）打孔，扎眼；<美>（用刺棒）趕（牲口）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>punch</b> someone or something, you hit them hard with your fist. 用拳猛擊","examples":["After punching him on the chin she wound up hitting him over the head. 她對準他的下巴猛擊一拳，最後又在他的頭上打了一拳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>punch</b> something such as the buttons on a keyboard, you touch them in order to store information on a machine such as a computer or to give the machine a command to do something. 按 (鍵或鈕)","examples":["Mrs. Baylor strode to the lift and punched the button. 貝勒太太大步走到電梯前按了一下按鈕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>punch</b> holes <b>in</b> something, you make holes in it by pushing or pressing it with something sharp. 在…上打孔","examples":["I took a ballpoint pen and punched a hole in the carton. 我拿了一支圓珠筆在紙板箱上戳了個孔。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Punch</b> is also a noun. 一拳","examples":["He was hurting Johansson with body punches in the fourth round. 他在第4個回合猛擊約翰遜的身體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>punch</b> is a tool that you use for making holes in something. 打孔器","examples":["Make two holes with a hole punch. 用打孔器打兩個孔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something has <b>punch</b>, you mean that it has force or effectiveness. 力量; 效力","examples":["My nervousness made me deliver the vital points of my address without sufficient punch. 我太緊張，講到演說關鍵地方時不夠有力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Punch</b> is a drink made from wine, spirits, or fruit juice, mixed with things such as sugar and spices. 潘趣酒","examples":["...a bowl of punch. …一碗潘趣酒。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Punch out</b> means the same as . 用拳猛擊","examples":["\"I almost lost my job today.\"—\"What happened?\"—\"Oh, I punched out this guy.\" “我今天差點丟了工作。”—“怎麼回事？” —“噢，我把那個傢伙狠揍了一頓。”"]}]}]},"ray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"光束，光線；（熱、電或其他能源的）射線；一絲，一線（希望、慰藉等）；<非正式>（日光浴用語）陽光（rays）；半直線；長音階第二音，C大調第二音；鰩，魟；輻射狀東西；（菊科植物頭狀花序的）舌狀花，（盤）邊花；輻肋，鰭刺；（海星的）放射形口腕，輻腕"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文> 放射，射出（光線）；呈輻射狀伸出，從中心四下延展"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rays</b> of light are narrow beams of light. 光線","examples":["The sun's rays can penetrate water up to 10 feet. 陽光的光線一直能透射到水下10英尺處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ray of</b> hope, comfort, or other positive quality is a small amount of it that you welcome because it makes a bad situation seem less bad. 一絲 (希望、安慰等其他積極因素)","examples":["They could provide a ray of hope amid the general economic gloom. 他們能在普遍的經濟低迷中帶來一絲希望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various marine selachian fishes typically having a flattened body, greatly enlarged winglike pectoral fins, gills on the undersurface of the fins, and a long whiplike tail. They constitute the orders <b>Torpediniformes</b> (<b>electric rays</b>) and <b>Rajiformes</b> 鰩魚","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(in tonic sol-fa) the second degree of any major scale; supertonic (首調唱名法的)大音階的二度; 超音","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of an object) to emit (light) in rays or (of light) to issue in the form of rays 發出光束; 閃光","examples":[]}]}]},"receipt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發票，收據；<正式>收到，接收；(企業、銀行、政府等）收到的款項，收入（receipts）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（賬單）上註明收訖字樣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>receipt</b> is a piece of paper that you get from someone as proof that they have received money or goods from you. 收據","examples":["I wrote her a receipt for the money. 我為那筆錢給她開了張收據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Receipts</b> are the amount of money received during a particular period, for example by a shop or theatre. 收入","examples":["He was tallying the day's receipts. 他正在結算當天的收入。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>receipt</b> of something is the act of receiving it. 收到","examples":["Goods should be supplied within 28 days after the receipt of your order. 收到你的訂單28天內供貨。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in receipt of</b> something, you have received it or you receive it regularly. 已收到; 定期收到","examples":["We are taking action, having been in receipt of a letter from him. 收到他的信之後，我們正採取行動。"]}]}]},"rank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軍銜，軍階；（社會、團體中的）地位，等級；（尤指較高的）地位；（警察、士兵等的）佇列，行列；排，列；橫排，棋盤橫格；組織（或機構等）中的全體人員（ranks）；普通士兵（the ranks）；<英>計程車候車站（=taxi rank）；（數）秩；（統計）次序排列；（系統語法用語）（一個或一組語言單位的）階，級"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……分等級，屬於某等級；<美>級別高於，地位高於；排列，使排成行"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（植被）茂密的，蕪生蔓長的；難聞的，惡臭的；（強調質量、狀況等）極端的，糟糕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>rank</b> is the position or grade that they have in an organization. 職位; 級別","examples":["He eventually rose to the rank of captain. 他最終升到了船長的職位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>rank</b> is the social class, especially the high social class, that they belong to. (尤指較高的) 社會地位","examples":["He must be treated as a hostage of high rank, not as a common prisoner. 他一定要作為一個高階人質而不是一般囚徒來對待。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>ranks</b> of a group or organization are the people who belong to it. 成員","examples":["There were some misgivings within the ranks of the media too. 媒體內部成員也有一些擔憂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The ranks</b> are the ordinary members of an organization, especially of the armed forces. 普通成員 (尤指軍隊的普通士兵)","examples":["Most shop managers have worked their way up through the ranks. 大部分的商店經理都是從普通員工幹上來的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>rank</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a row of them. 排","examples":["Ranks of police in riot gear stood nervously by. 一排排配有防暴裝置的警察緊張地站在一邊。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>taxi</b> <b>rank</b> is a place on a city street where taxis park when they are available. 計程車停車處","examples":["Luckily there was a taxi rank nearby. 幸好附近有個計程車候客處。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an official organization <b>ranks</b> someone or something 1st, 5th, or 50th, for example, they calculate that the person or thing has that position on a scale. You can also say that someone or something <b>ranks</b> 1st, 5th, or 50th, for example. 給…排名; 名列","examples":["The report ranks the U.S. 20th out of 22 advanced nations. 這份報告把美國排在22個發達國家的第20位。","...the only Canadian woman to be ranked in the top 50 of the women's world rankings. …進入世界婦女排行榜前50名的惟一的加拿大婦女。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>ranks</b> high or low on a scale, you are saying how good or important you think they are. 給…排等級; 位列","examples":["His prices rank high among those of other contemporary photographers. 他的要價與其他同時代的攝影師相比居高。","Investors ranked South Korea high among Asian nations. 投資者在亞洲國家中更看重韓國。","St. Petersburg's night life ranks as more exciting than the capital's. 聖彼得堡的夜生活比首都的更令人激動。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to arrange (people or things) in rows or lines; range (把人或物)排成行; 排成列","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"showing vigorous and profuse growth 繁茂的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"highly offensive or disagreeable, esp in smell or taste 難聞的; 難吃的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"complete or absolute; utter 完全的; 絕對的; 徹頭徹尾的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a member of a group or organization <b>breaks ranks</b>, you mean that they disobey the instructions of their group or organization. 違背指令","examples":["Britain appears unlikely to break ranks with other members of the European Union. 英國似乎不會背棄歐盟其他成員國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that the members of a group <b>close ranks</b>, you mean that they are supporting each other only because their group is being criticized. (受批評時) 緊密團結","examples":["Institutions tend to close ranks when a member has been accused of misconduct. 各個機構在其某一成員被指控行為不當時都會同心合力。"]}]}]},"recorder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錄音機，錄影機；豎笛，直笛；記錄器；記錄員，記錄人；（某些法院的）法官；<英>被任命為兼職法官的大律師（Recorder）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a cassette recorder, a tape recorder, or a video recorder as a <b>recorder</b>. 錄音機; 錄影機","examples":["Rodney put the recorder on the desk top and pushed the play button. 羅德尼把錄音機放在桌面上，按下了播放鍵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>recorder</b> is a wooden or plastic musical instrument in the shape of a pipe. You play the recorder by blowing into the top of it and covering and uncovering the holes with your fingers. 豎笛","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>recorder</b> is a machine or instrument that keeps a record of something, for example in an experiment or on a vehicle. 記錄儀器","examples":["Data recorders also pinpoint mechanical faults rapidly, reducing repair times. 資料記錄儀器也能很快查明機械故障，減少維修時間。"]}]}]},"receiver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電話）聽筒；（無線電或電視）接收器，接收機；（法庭指定的）破產接管人；收受者，收件人；買賣贓物者，收贓人；接球手，外接手；接受罐，聚集器；（安置槍栓並與槍管等部件相連線的）機閘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A telephone's <b>receiver</b> is the part that you hold near to your ear and speak into. 電話聽筒","examples":["She picked up the receiver and started to dial. 她拿起聽筒開始撥號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>receiver</b> is the part of a radio or television that picks up signals and converts them into sound or pictures. (收音機或電視機的) 訊號接收器","examples":["Auto-tuning VHF receivers are now common in cars. 自動調諧的超高頻訊號接收器現普遍使用在小汽車上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>receiver</b> is someone who is appointed by a court of law to manage the affairs of a business, usually when it is facing financial failure. (法庭指定的) 破產接管人","examples":["...the receivers handling his bankruptcy case. …處理他破產案子的接管人員們。"]}]}]},"reaction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反應，回應；反應能力（reactions）；（藥物或食物引起的）不良反應；化學反應；反作用力；（對舊觀念等的）抗拒；反動，守舊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>reaction</b> <b>to</b> something that has happened or something that you have experienced is what you feel, say, or do because of it. 反應","examples":["Reaction to the visit is mixed. 對這次訪問的反應不一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reaction against</b> something is a way of behaving or doing something that is deliberately different from what has been done before. 反抗","examples":["All new fashion starts out as a reaction against existing convention. 所有新時尚都是從反抗現存習俗開始的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>reaction against</b> something, it becomes unpopular. 牴觸","examples":["Premature moves in this respect might well provoke a reaction against the reform. 在這方面過早的行動可能會激起對改革的牴觸。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>reactions</b> are your ability to move quickly in response to something, for example when you are in danger. 反應能力; 應變能力","examples":["The sport requires very fast reactions. 這項運動要求很快的反應能力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Reaction</b> is the belief that the political or social system of your country should not change. 保守思想","examples":["Thus, he aided reaction and thwarted progress. 所以他支援保守思想，反對進步。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A chemical <b>reaction</b> is a process in which two substances combine together chemically to form another substance. (化學) 反應","examples":["Ozone is produced by the reaction between oxygen and ultraviolet light. 臭氧是氧氣與紫外線發生化學反應而產生的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you have a <b>reaction</b> <b>to</b> a substance such as a drug, or <b>to</b> something you have touched, you are affected unpleasantly or made ill by it. (對藥物或所碰觸的東西等的) 不良反應","examples":["Every year, 5,000 people have life-threatening reactions to anaesthetics. 每年，有5000人會對麻醉劑產生致命的不良反應。"]}]}]},"regret":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懊悔，惋惜；（用於正式書面語）對......感到抱歉，對......感到遺憾；<古>對（損失或缺乏）感到痛惜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"遺憾，惋惜；（因無法出席會議、聚會等的）致歉語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>regret</b> something that you have done, you wish that you had not done it. 後悔","examples":["I simply gave in to him, and I've regretted it ever since. 當時我輕易向他屈服了，到現在我一直後悔。","Ellis seemed to be regretting that he had asked the question. 埃利斯當時似乎正後悔不該問那個問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>regret</b> something as a polite way of saying that you are sorry about it. You use expressions such as <b>I regret to say</b> or <b>I regret to inform you</b> to show that you are sorry about something. 對…感到遺憾","examples":["\"I very much regret the injuries he sustained,\" he said. 他說：“我對他所遭受的傷害感到非常遺憾。”","I regret that the United States has added its voice to such protests. 我很遺憾美國也附和了這樣的抗議。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Regret</b> is a feeling of sadness or disappointment, which is caused by something that has happened or something that you have done or not done. 遺憾; 惋惜; 後悔","examples":["Larry said he had no regrets about retiring. 拉里曾說他對於退休沒有任何遺憾。"]}]}]},"religion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宗教信仰；宗教，教派；<非正式>痴迷的活動，極愛好的活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Religion</b> is belief in a god or gods and the activities that are connected with this belief, such as praying or worshipping in a building such as a church or temple. 宗教","examples":["...his understanding of Indian philosophy and religion. …他對於印度哲學和宗教的理解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>religion</b> is a particular system of belief in a god or gods and the activities that are connected with this system. (一種) 宗教","examples":["...the Christian religion. …基督教。"]}]}]},"replacement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代替，更換；取代（或代替）的人（或物）；補充兵員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>replacement</b> of one thing by another, you mean that the second thing takes the place of the first. 代替; 取代; 更換","examples":["...the replacement of damaged or lost books. …受損或遺失書籍的更換。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who takes someone else's place in an organization, government, or team can be referred to as their <b>replacement</b>. 接替者","examples":["Taylor has nominated Adams as his replacement. 泰勒已經提名亞當斯為接替者。"]}]}]},"relief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（因恐懼、憂慮或痛苦的消除而感到的）寬慰，輕鬆；（疼痛或不快的）減輕，緩解；救濟品（如食品、衣物、金錢等）；換班的人，替換者；浮雕，浮雕品；軍事援助，解圍；稅款減免（權）；（暫時的）緩解（物），（短時間的）調劑；（對困苦、不公正遭遇等的）依法補償；<英>（高峰時或緊急需要時的）臨時加班公交車，機動車；凸現（用線條、顏色或明暗表現的立體效果）；（地形的）凹凸，高低；輪廓分明，對比鮮明；突出的品質，令人注目的特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel a sense of <b>relief</b>, you feel happy because something unpleasant has not happened or is no longer happening. 寬慰; 安心","examples":["I breathed a sigh of relief. 我安心地鬆了一口氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something provides <b>relief</b> <b>from</b> pain or distress, it stops the pain or distress. (痛苦、悲痛的) 解除","examples":["...a self-help programme which can give lasting relief from the torment of hay fever. …一個可以永久解除花粉熱折磨的自助療方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Relief</b> is money, food, or clothing that is provided for people who are very poor, or who have been affected by war or a natural disaster. 救濟金; 救濟物資","examples":["Relief agencies are stepping up efforts to provide food, shelter, and agricultural equipment. 救濟機構正在加緊努力提供食物、住處和農業裝置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>relief</b> worker is someone who does your work when you go home, or who is employed to do it instead of you when you are sick. 換班人; 接替人","examples":["No relief drivers were available. 沒有換班的司機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the projection of forms or figures from a flat ground, so that they are partly or wholly free of it","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a piece of work of this kind","examples":[]}]}]},"rate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"速度，速率；比率，率；費用，價格；費率；（英國）地方稅，房地產稅（rates）；<罕>等級"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"評價，評定；被認為，被列為；<英，非正式> 看好； 對（影片、影片遊戲等）分級；劃分等級，分等；值得，應得；<英>給（財產）核定應繳地方稅款；（機器、發動機等的）額定功率（極限）為；<美，非正式>受器重，受青睞（rate with）"}],"sections":[]},"republic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"共和國，共和政體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>republic</b> is a country where power is held by the people or the representatives that they elect. Republics have presidents who are elected, rather than kings or queens. 共和國","examples":["In 1918, Austria became a republic. 1918年奧地利成為共和國。","...the Baltic republics. …波羅的海各共和國。"]}]}]},"release":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"釋放，放走；放開，鬆開；公佈，釋出；發行，上映；發洩，宣洩；排放（物質）；免除，解僱；放棄，讓予；放鬆，使鬆弛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"釋放，獲釋；排放，洩漏；釋放裝置；表達，宣洩；解脫，輕鬆感；新發行的東西；發表，釋出；（責任等的）免除；<法律> 放棄，讓予；<美> 傳球；（裝置的）鬆開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>is released</b> from somewhere where they have been locked up or cared for, they are set free or allowed to go. 放走","examples":["He was released from custody the next day. 他第二天被從拘留中釋放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>releases</b> you <b>from</b> a duty, task, or feeling, they free you from it. 解除","examples":["Divorce releases both the husband and wife from all marital obligations to each other. 離婚解除了夫妻相互之間的所有婚姻義務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>release</b> feelings or abilities means to allow them to be expressed. 釋放","examples":["Becoming your own person releases your creativity. 保持你自己的本色可以釋放出你的創造力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>releases</b> something such as a document or information, they make it available. 發放","examples":["They're not releasing any more details yet. 他們還不準備發放更多詳情。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>release</b> someone or something, you stop holding them. 放開","examples":["He stopped and faced her, releasing her wrist. 他停下來面對著她，放開了她的手腕。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>releases</b> gas, heat, or a substance, it causes it to leave its container or the substance that it was part of and enter the surrounding atmosphere or area. 釋放","examples":["...a weapon that releases toxic nerve gas. …一種釋放神經毒氣的武器。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"When an entertainer or company <b>releases</b> a new CD, DVD, or movie, it becomes available so that people can buy it or see it. 發行","examples":["He is releasing an album of love songs. 他將發行一張情歌專輯。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone is released, you refer to their <b>release</b>. 釋放","examples":["He called for the immediate release of all political prisoners. 他要求立即釋放所有的政治犯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Release</b> is also a noun. 解除","examples":["Our therapeutic style offers release from stored tensions, traumas, and grief. 我們的治療方式意在解除蓄積的壓力、創傷和悲痛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Release</b> is also a noun. 釋放","examples":["She felt the sudden sweet release of her own tears. 她感到自己的眼淚突然而甜蜜地流出來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Release</b> is also a noun. 發放","examples":["Action had been taken to speed up the release of cheques. 已採取行動來加速支票的發放。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Release</b> is also a noun. 釋放","examples":["Under the agreement, releases of cancer-causing chemicals will be cut by about 80 percent. 根據這個協議，致癌化學物的釋放將被削減80％左右。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A new <b>release</b> is a new CD, DVD, or movie that has just become available for people to buy or see. 發行物","examples":["Of the new releases that are out there now, which do you think are really good? 現在外面新的發行物中，你覺得哪些真正好呢？"]}]}]},"rent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"租金，租用費；（布等上面的）破洞，裂口"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"租用，租借；出租，將……租給； 可租用，租金為"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撕裂，扯碎；（聲音）響徹，刺破；<文>使心碎（rend 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rent</b> something, you regularly pay its owner a sum of money in order to be able to have it and use it yourself. 租; 租借","examples":["She rents a house with three other girls. 她和另外3個女孩合租了一套房子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rent</b> something <b>to</b> someone, you let them have it and use it in exchange for a sum of money which they pay you regularly. 租給; 出租","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rent out</b> means the same as . 租給; 出租","examples":["Last summer Brian Williams rented out his house and went camping. 去年夏天，布賴恩•威廉斯把自己的房子租出去，然後去露營。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rent</b> is the amount of money that you pay regularly to use a house, apartment, or piece of land. 租金; 房租","examples":["She worked to pay the rent while I went to college. 當我讀大學時，她工作掙錢來付租金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a slit or opening made by tearing or rending; tear 縫; 裂縫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"rend的過去式及過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>for rent</b>, it is available for you to use in exchange for a sum of money. 待租的; 供出租的","examples":[]}]}]},"repair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修理，修補；補救，挽救（關係或聲譽）；<舊，正式>（結伴）去，赴（repair to）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"修理，補救；修補過的地方；維修狀態，保養情況；<古> 常去；常去的場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>repair</b> something that has been damaged or is not working properly, you fix it. 修理; 修補; 整修","examples":["Goldsmith has repaired the roof to ensure the house is windproof. 戈德史密斯已經修理了房頂以確保房子可以抵禦狂風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>repair</b> a relationship or someone's reputation after it has been damaged, you do something to improve it. 彌補; 補救","examples":["The administration continued to try to repair the damage caused by the secretary's interview. 該政府繼續努力去彌補因秘書訪談而造成的損失。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"修理工","examples":["...services provided by builders, plumbers, and TV repairers. …建築工、水暖工和電視修理工提供的服務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>repair</b> is something that you do to mend a machine, building, piece of clothing, or other thing that has been damaged or is not working properly. 修理; 修補; 整修","examples":["Many women know how to make repairs on their cars. 很多女性知道如何修理汽車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the act of going or returning 往返","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to go (to a place) 去; 往(某地)","examples":[]}]}]},"representative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"典型的，有代表性的；代表各類人（或事物）的；由代表組成的，代議制的；表現的，體現的；（藝術）具象派的；（哲） （與）表象（有關）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"代表，代理人；代表他人者；銷售代表，銷售代理；典型人物，有代表性的事物；（美國）眾議院議員；（類或群的）樣本，代表物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>representative</b> is a person who has been chosen to act or make decisions on behalf of another person or a group of people. 代表; 代理人","examples":["...trade union representatives. …工會代表們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>representative</b> is a person whose job is to sell a company's products or services, especially by travelling around and visiting other companies. 銷售代理","examples":["She had a stressful job as a sales representative. 作為一名銷售代理，她的工作壓力很大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the United States, a <b>representative</b> is a member of the House of Representatives, the less powerful of the two parts of Congress. 眾議院議員","examples":["...a Republican representative from Wyoming. …一位來自懷俄明州的共和黨眾議員。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>representative</b> group consists of a small number of people who have been chosen to make decisions on behalf of a larger group. 代表制的; 代議制的","examples":["The new head of state should be chosen by an 87-member representative council. 新的國家元首應該由87人組成的代表委員會選出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is typical of the group to which they belong can be described as <b>representative</b>. 有代表性的","examples":["He was in no way representative of dog trainers in general. 他絕不能代表大多數的馴狗師。"]}]}]},"request":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"要求，請求；要求的事，點播的歌曲；（要求計算機提供資訊或執行另一任務的）指令"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>請求，要求；要求（某人）做……，請求（某人）做……；點播（樂曲）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>request</b> something, you ask for it politely or formally. 請求; 正式要求","examples":["Mr. Dennis said he had requested access to a telephone. 丹尼斯先生說他已正式要求要能夠使用一部電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>request</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you politely or formally ask them to do it. 要求","examples":["Students are requested to park at the rear of the building. 學生們被要求在那座樓後面停車。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>request</b>, you politely or formally ask someone to do something. 請求","examples":["France had agreed to his request for political asylum. 法國已經同意了他政治避難的請求。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>at</b> someone's <b>request</b>, you do it because they have asked you to. 應某人的要求","examples":["The evacuation is being organized at the request of the United Nations Secretary General. 應聯合國秘書長的要求，該撤離正在進行中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is given or done <b>on request</b>, it is given or done whenever you ask for it. 應要求","examples":["Details are available on request. 詳情備索。"]}]}]},"response":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反應，響應；（口頭或書面的）回覆，答覆；（考試題的）答案；（教堂中人們對牧師所說的話作出的）唱和，應答"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>response</b> to an event or to something that is said is your reply or reaction to it. 反應","examples":["There has been no response to his remarks from the government. 政府方面對他的評論一直沒有反應。"]}]}]},"resource":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自然資源；資源（指錢、物、人等）；有助於實現目標的東西，資料；（對付困境所需的）個人素質（resources）；（逆境中的）出路，應付辦法；<正式> 謀略，智謀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……提供資金（或裝置）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>resources</b> of an organization or person are the materials, money, and other things that they have and can use in order to function properly. 財力","examples":["Some families don't have the resources to feed themselves adequately. 一些家庭沒有錢填飽肚子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A country's <b>resources</b> are the things that it has and can use to increase its wealth, such as coal, oil, or land. 資源","examples":["...resources like coal, tungsten, oil, and copper. …像煤、鎢、石油和銅等資源。"]}]}]},"reserve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預訂；保留，預留；擁有，保留（某種權利）；留作，用於（特定場合）；保留（意見），推遲作出（決定或判斷）；貯存，貯藏；（教會用語）彌撒儀式後保留部分聖餐"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"儲備（量），儲藏（量）；含蓄，寡言；保留意見，異議；（野生生物）保護區；替補隊員，後備隊員；後備隊，替補隊（the reserves）；預備役部隊，後備部隊；（尤指拍賣時的）底價，最低價；（美洲土著居民的）居留地；（陶瓷裝飾或紡織品印染中保留原色的）防染本色區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is reserved</b> <b>for</b> a particular person or purpose, it is kept specially for that person or purpose. 預留","examples":["A double room with a balcony overlooking the sea had been reserved for him. 一個帶一座陽臺的海景雙人間已被預留給他了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reserve</b> something such as a table, ticket, or magazine, you arrange for it to be kept specially for you, rather than sold or given to someone else. 預訂","examples":["I'll reserve a table for five. 我要預訂一個5人的餐位。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reserve</b> is a supply of something that is available for use when it is needed. 儲備","examples":["The Persian Gulf has 65 percent of the world's oil reserves. 波斯灣擁有全世界石油儲備的65%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A nature <b>reserve</b> is an area of land where the animals, birds, and plants are officially protected. 保護區","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone shows <b>reserve</b>, they keep their feelings hidden. 矜持","examples":["I hope that you'll overcome your reserve and let me know. 我希望你能克服矜持，讓我知道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something <b>in reserve</b>, you have it available for use when it is needed. 保留備用","examples":["He poked around the top of his cabinet for the bottle of whisky that he kept in reserve. 他在壁櫥的上面翻找他留的那瓶威士忌。"]}]}]},"riddle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"謎語；謎一般的人（或事）；（篩分土石的）粗篩"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猜（某人）出的（謎），為（某人）解（謎）；<古> 打謎語般地說，出謎；把……打得滿是窟窿；（尤指令人不快之事）充斥，佈滿；用粗篩篩；搖動（爐柵）使灰落下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>riddle</b> is a puzzle or joke in which you ask a question that seems to be nonsense but which has a clever or amusing answer. 謎語","examples":["All comers to the Sphinx were asked a riddle, and failure to solve it meant death. 所有來到斯芬克斯面前的人都被問了一個謎語，解答不了就意味著死亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe something as a <b>riddle</b> if people have been trying to understand or explain it but have not been able to. 謎","examples":["Scientists claimed yesterday to have solved the riddle of the birth of the universe. 科學家們昨天宣佈已經解開了宇宙誕生之謎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a sieve, esp a coarse one used for sand, grain, etc 粗篩","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to solve, explain, or interpret (a riddle or riddles) 猜(謎); 解(謎)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>riddles</b> something <b>with</b> bullets or bullet holes, they fire a lot of bullets into it. (用子彈) 把…打得千瘡百孔","examples":["Unknown attackers riddled two homes with gunfire. 不明來路的襲擊者用槍把兩座房屋打得千瘡百孔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to put through a sieve; sift","examples":[]}]}]},"responsibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"責任，負責；（對不良事件所負的）責任；（道義上或法律規定的）責任（responsibility to/towards）；職責，任務；重任，職權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>responsibility</b> for something or someone, or if they are your <b>responsibility</b>, it is your job or duty to deal with them and to make decisions relating to them. 責任","examples":["Each manager had responsibility for just under 600 properties. 每位經理對差一點不到六百處房產負責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you accept <b>responsibility</b> <b>for</b> something that has happened, you agree that you were to blame for it or you caused it. 責任","examples":["No one admitted responsibility for the attacks. 沒有人對這些襲擊負責。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>responsibilities</b> are the duties that you have because of your job or position. 職責","examples":["I am told that he handled his responsibilities as a counsellor in a highly intelligent and caring fashion. 我被告知，他以一種高度的智慧和富有同情心的方式對待他作為一名顧問的職責。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is given <b>responsibility</b>, they are given the right or opportunity to make important decisions or to take action without having to get permission from anyone else. 職權","examples":["She would have loved to have a better-paying job with more responsibility. 她本想有一份薪水更高職權更多的工作。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you think that you have a <b>responsibility</b> <b>to</b> do something, you feel that you ought to do it because it is morally right to do it. 責任","examples":["The court feels it has a responsibility to ensure that customers are not misled. 該法院覺得其有責任確保消費者們不被誤導。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you think that you have a <b>responsibility to</b> someone, you feel that it is your duty to take action that will protect their interests. 義務","examples":["She had decided that as a doctor she had a responsibility to her fellow creatures. 她決定作為一名醫生她對同胞們負有義務。"]}]}]},"ribbon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"絲帶，綢帶；（表示軍功的）綬帶，勳帶；（作為比賽獎品的）綬帶；（表明支援某一組織、原則或目標而配帶的）飾帶；帶狀物，狹長的東西；（打字機用的）色帶；碎片（ribbons）；獎品，榮譽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成帶狀延伸（或運動）；把…撕成條帶；用緞帶裝飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ribbon</b> is a long, narrow piece of cloth that you use for tying things together or as a decoration. 裝飾帶","examples":["She had tied back her hair with a peach satin ribbon. 她用一條桃紅色的緞帶把頭髮紮在了腦後。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A typewriter or printer <b>ribbon</b> is a long, narrow piece of cloth containing ink and is used in a typewriter or printer. 色帶","examples":[]}]}]},"robber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"強盜，搶劫犯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>robber</b> is someone who steals money or property from a bank, shop, or vehicle, often by using force or threats. 搶劫者","examples":["Armed robbers broke into a jeweller's through a hole in the wall. 武裝劫匪從牆上的一個洞闖入了一家珠寶行。"]}]}]},"roast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"炙，烘（食物，尤指肉）；<非正式> 嚴厲批評，斥責；<美， 非正式> 和善地戲弄；<非正式> （尤指透過暴露在太陽下或爐火前）使受熱發燙；以火刑折磨；烘乾，烘焙（食品原料，金屬礦等）；焙，炒（堅果、豆子等）；變熱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大塊）烤肉，待烤的肉；<美>（講述主角趣事的）慶祝會；戶外燒烤野餐；烤，炙，烘（尤指咖啡）；（某種）烘過的咖啡"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"烘烤的，烤制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>roast</b> meat or other food, you cook it by dry heat in an oven or over a fire. 烤","examples":["I personally would rather roast a chicken whole. 我個人更願意烤整雞。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Roast</b> meat has been cooked by roasting. 烤熟了的","examples":["They serve the most delicious roast beef. 他們做最美味的烤牛肉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>roast</b> is a piece of meat that is cooked by roasting. 烤肉","examples":["Come into the kitchen. I've got to put the roast in. 到廚房裡來。我得把烤肉放進去。"]}]}]},"roar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吼叫，咆哮；（人群）用歡呼聲激勵，為......喝彩，為加油；鬨笑，大笑；（尤指車輛）轟鳴著疾駛，呼嘯而過；果斷行事，迅速發生；熊熊燃燒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吼叫聲， 咆哮聲；（風或海的）呼嘯聲，（機器的）隆隆聲；（獅等的）吼叫聲；爆笑聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something, usually a vehicle, <b>roars</b> somewhere, it goes there very fast, making a loud noise. (常指車輛) 呼嘯疾馳","examples":["A police car roared past. 一輛警車呼嘯而過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>roars</b>, it makes a very loud noise. 咆哮; 轟鳴","examples":["The engine roared, and the vehicle leapt forward. 引擎轟鳴，車子猛地向前駛去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>roars</b> <b>with</b> laughter, they laugh in a very noisy way. 鬨然 (大笑)","examples":["Max threw back his head and roared with laughter. 馬克斯把頭向後一甩，鬨然大笑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a lion <b>roars</b>, it makes the loud sound that lions typically make. (獅子) 吼叫","examples":["The lion roared once, and sprang. 獅子吼了一聲，跳了起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Roar</b> is also a noun. 咆哮聲; 轟鳴聲","examples":["...the roar of traffic. …車輛的轟鳴聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Roar</b> is also a noun. (笑聲) 鬨然","examples":["There were roars of laughter as he stood up. 他站起來時出現陣陣鬨堂大笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Roar</b> is also a noun. 吼叫聲","examples":["There was a roar of approval. 響起了一片表示贊成的喊叫聲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Roar</b> is also a noun. (獅子的) 吼叫聲","examples":["...the roar of lions in the distance. …遠處的獅吼聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>roars</b>, they shout something in a very loud voice. (人) 吼道; 吼","examples":["\"I'll kill you for that,\" he roared. “我要為此殺了你，” 他吼道。","During the playing of the national anthem the crowd roared and whistled. 奏國歌時，人群又吼又吹口哨。"]}]}]},"robbery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盜竊，搶劫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Robbery</b> is the crime of stealing money or property from a bank, shop, or vehicle, often by using force or threats. 搶劫; 搶劫罪","examples":["The gang members committed dozens of armed robberies over the past year. 該團伙成員在過去一年中犯下了數十起持械搶劫罪。"]}]}]},"robe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"袍服，禮袍；睡袍，浴衣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿，披（袍服或其他特殊衣服）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>robe</b> is a loose piece of clothing that covers all of your body and reaches the ground. You can describe someone as wearing a <b>robe</b> or as wearing <b>robes</b>. 長袍","examples":["Pope John Paul II knelt in his white robes before the simple altar. 約翰•保羅二世教皇身著白色長袍跪在簡樸的祭壇前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>robe</b> is a piece of clothing, usually made of towelling, which people wear in the house, especially when they have just got up or taken a bath. 睡袍; 浴衣","examples":["Kyle put on a robe and went down to the kitchen. 凱爾穿上睡袍，下樓去了廚房。"]}]}]},"risk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"危險，風險；危險的人（或事物），隱患；（按風險大小評估的）被保險物件，受貸者；（保險業承保的）險；金融風險"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使遭受（失去、毀壞或傷害的）危險；冒......的危險，擔......的風險；冒險做，（明知結果而）大膽做"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>risk</b> <b>of</b> something unpleasant, there is a possibility that it will happen. 風險","examples":["There is a small risk of brain damage from the procedure. 存在該手術導致腦損傷的小風險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something that you do is a <b>risk</b>, it might have unpleasant or undesirable results. 危險","examples":["You're taking a big risk showing this to Kravis. 你在冒很大的危險把這給克拉維斯看。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is a <b>risk</b>, you mean they are likely to cause harm. 風險因素","examples":["It's being obese that constitutes a health risk. 是痴肥構成的健康風險。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are considered a good <b>risk</b>, a bank or shop thinks that it is safe to lend you money or let you have goods without paying for them at the time. (風險大或小的) 信貸物件","examples":["Before providing the cash, they will have to decide whether you are a good or bad risk. 提供資金之前，他們得確定你是風險小還是大的信貸物件。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>risk</b> something unpleasant, you do something which might result in that thing happening or affecting you. 冒遭受…的風險","examples":["Those who fail to register risk severe penalties. 那些沒登記的人冒著受重罰的風險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>risk</b> doing something, you do it, even though you know that it might have undesirable consequences. 冒險 (做某事)","examples":["The skipper was not willing to risk taking his ship through the straits until he could see where he was going. 這位船長不願意冒險在看不見方向之前將船開過海峽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>risk</b> your life or something else important, you behave in a way that might result in it being lost or harmed. 冒失去…的危險","examples":["She risked her own life to help a disabled woman. 她冒著失去自己生命的危險幫助了一位殘疾婦女。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>at risk</b> means to be in a situation where something unpleasant might happen. 受到威脅","examples":["Up to 25,000 jobs are still at risk. 多達25000職位仍受到威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>at the risk of</b> something unpleasant happening, you do it even though you know that the unpleasant thing might happen as a result. 冒著 (發生不快事件的) 風險地","examples":["At the risk of being repetitive, I will say again that statistics are only a guide. 儘管會被認為羅嗦，我還得再說一遍：統計數字只是指向。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you tell someone that they are doing something <b>at</b> their <b>own risk</b>, you are warning them that, if they are harmed, it will be their own responsibility. 自擔風險地","examples":["Those who wish to come here will do so at their own risk. 那些想來這裡的人來的話將要自擔風險。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>run</b> the <b>risk</b> <b>of</b> doing or experiencing something undesirable, you do something knowing that the undesirable thing might happen as a result. 冒著風險","examples":["The officers had run the risk of being dismissed. 官員們曾冒著被解職的風險。"]}]}]},"rot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）腐敗，（使）腐爛；逐漸衰弱（或憔悴）；<英，舊，非正式>取笑，開玩笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"腐爛，腐爛物；<英>腐化，墮落（the rot）；<美>官員腐敗（the rot）；（尤指植物的）枯病；羊肝蛭病；<英，非正式，舊>蠢話，廢話"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式>胡說，廢話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When food, wood, or another substance <b>rots</b>, or when something <b>rots</b> it, it becomes softer and is gradually destroyed. 腐爛","examples":["If we don't unload it soon, the grain will start rotting in the silos. 如果我們不馬上卸貨，這些糧食在倉中將開始腐爛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>rot</b> in something, especially something that is made of wood, parts of it have decayed and fallen apart. 腐朽","examples":["Investigations had revealed extensive rot in the beams under the ground floor. 檢測顯示一樓下面的橫樑已經有大面積的腐爛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>the rot</b> to refer to the way something gradually gets worse. For example, if you are talking about the time when <b>the rot</b> <b>set in</b>, you are talking about the time when a situation began to get steadily worse and worse. 逐步惡化","examples":["In many schools, the rot is beginning to set in. Standards are falling all the time. 在許多學校，情況正在逐步惡化，水準在不斷降低。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is being left to <b>rot</b> in a particular place, especially in a prison, you mean that they are being left there and their physical and mental condition is being allowed to get worse and worse. 身心退化","examples":["Most governments simply leave the long-term jobless to rot. 大多數政府只能任由長期失業者頹廢下去。"]}]},{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"rotation (of a mathematical function) (數學函式上的)迴圈","examples":[]}]}]},"rumor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"謠言，傳聞，傳言；魯莫爾（人名，義大利語、葡萄牙語）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"謠傳，傳說（常用被動語態）"}],"sections":[]},"rocket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火箭；火箭發動機（=rocket engine/rocket motor）；火箭武器，火箭彈；火箭式焰火，流星焰火（=skyrocket）；<英>芝麻菜，大蒜芥；<英，非正式>嚴厲的斥責；（像火箭般）快速行動者，飛快行進的物體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"快速增長，猛增；迅速移動，飛速行進；用火箭武器攻擊；（使）迅速成功，迅速提高地位；用火箭運載"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rocket</b> is a space vehicle that is shaped like a long tube. 火箭","examples":["...the Apollo 12 rocket that took astronauts to the moon. …將宇航員送上了月球的阿波羅12號火箭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rocket</b> is a missile containing explosives that is powered by gas. 火箭彈","examples":["There has been a renewed rocket attack on the capital. 發生了對首都的新一輪火箭彈攻擊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rocket</b> is a firework that quickly goes high into the air and then explodes. 火箭彈煙花","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Rocket</b> is a vegetable with green leaves that are used in salads. 芝麻菜","examples":["...a small salad of rocket and chopped tomato. ...一小盤芝麻菜和西紅柿碎片色拉。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things such as prices or social problems <b>rocket</b>, they increase very quickly and suddenly. 飛速增加; 飛速上漲","examples":["Fresh food is so scarce that prices have rocketed. 新鮮食物如此稀缺以致價格飛漲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a vehicle <b>rockets</b> somewhere, it moves there very quickly. (車輛等) 疾馳; 飛奔","examples":["A train rocketed by, shaking the walls of the row houses. 一輛火車疾馳而過，震動著排房的牆壁。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to propel (a missile, spacecraft, etc) by means of a rocket 用火箭運送","examples":[]}]}]},"rug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小地毯，墊子；<英> （蓋腿的）厚毯子，毛毯；<美，非正式>（男子的）遮禿假髮；（馬的）披毯，裹毯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rug</b> is a piece of thick material that you put on a floor. It is like a carpet but covers a smaller area. 小地毯","examples":["A Persian rug covered the hardwood floors. 一張波斯小地毯鋪在了那硬木地板上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rug</b> is a small blanket which you use to cover your shoulders or your knees to keep them warm. (蓋在肩上或膝上的) 小毛毯","examples":["The old lady was seated in her chair at the window, a rug over her knees. 這位老婦人坐在靠窗的椅子上，膝上蓋著一塊小毛毯。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>pulls the rug from under</b> a person or thing or <b>pulls the rug from under</b> someone's <b>feet</b>, they stop giving their help or support. 不再幫助或支援某人","examples":["If the banks opt to pull the rug from under the ill-fated project, it will go into liquidation. 如果這些銀行選擇不再支援那項倒黴的工程，它就將破產。"]}]}]},"romantic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）浪漫的，有情調的；（事物）富有浪漫色彩的，充滿浪漫氣息的；愛情的，情愛的；不切實際的，空想的；（文學、藝術和音樂）浪漫主義的（Romantic）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"浪漫的人；愛幻想的人，空想者； 浪漫主義作家（或音樂家、藝術家）（Romantic）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>romantic</b> or does <b>romantic</b> things says and does things that make their wife, husband, girlfriend, or boyfriend feel special and loved. 浪漫的","examples":["When we're together, all he talks about is business. I wish he were more romantic. 我們在一起時，他只談生意上的事。我希望他能更浪漫一點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Romantic</b> means connected with sexual love. 有關性愛的","examples":["He was not interested in a romantic relationship with Ingrid. 他不想和英格麗德有性愛關係。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>romantic</b> play, movie, or story describes or represents a love affair. 關於愛情的 (戲劇、影片或故事)","examples":["It is a lovely romantic comedy, well worth seeing. 這是一部好看的愛情喜劇，很值得一看。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has a <b>romantic</b> view or idea of something, you are critical of them because their view of it is unrealistic and they think that thing is better or more exciting than it really is. 浪漫主義的; 不切實際的","examples":["He has a romantic view of rural society. 他對於鄉村地區有種不切實際的看法。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Something that is <b>romantic</b> is beautiful in a way that strongly affects your feelings. 有浪漫情調的","examples":["It is considered one of the most romantic restaurants in the city. 它被認為是這座城市裡最有浪漫情調的餐廳之一。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"性愛上地","examples":["We are not romantically involved. 我們沒有性愛關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"有浪漫情調地","examples":["...the romantically named, but very muddy, Cave of the Wild Horses. …這個取名浪漫但泥濘不堪的“野馬洞”。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>romantic</b> is a person who has romantic views. 浪漫主義者; 不切實際的人","examples":["You're a hopeless romantic. 你是個無可救藥的浪漫主義者。"]}]}]},"routine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"常規，慣例；生活乏味，無聊；（演出中的）一套動作，一系列笑話（等）；（為達到特定目的的）老一套，俗套；（計算機）例行程式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"常規的，例行的；平常的，毫不特別的；平淡乏味的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕> 按慣例安排"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>routine</b> is the usual series of things that you do at a particular time. A <b>routine</b> is also the practice of regularly doing things in a fixed order. 慣例; 常規","examples":["The players had to change their daily routine and lifestyle. 這些運動員不得不改變他們的每日常規和生活方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>routine</b> to refer to a way of life that is uninteresting and ordinary, or hardly ever changes. 平淡乏味","examples":["...the mundane routine of her life. …她生活的平常乏味。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>routine</b> is a computer program, or part of a program, that performs a specific function. 程式","examples":["...an installation routine. …一個安裝程式。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>routine</b> is a short sequence of jokes, remarks, actions, or movements that forms part of a longer performance. (一) 套","examples":["...an athletic dance routine. …一套體育舞蹈動作。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>routine</b> to describe activities that are done as a normal part of a job or process. 常規的","examples":["...a series of routine medical tests including X-rays and blood tests. …一系列包括X光和驗血在內的常規醫學檢查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>routine</b> situation, action, or event is one which seems completely ordinary, rather than interesting, exciting, or different. 平淡的","examples":["So many days are routine and uninteresting, especially in winter. 太多的日子都是平淡和無趣，尤其是在冬季。"]}]}]},"rust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鏽，鐵鏽；（植物的）鏽病，鏽菌；鐵鏽色，赭色"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）生鏽；成鐵鏽色；（因疏忽或不用而）衰退，變遲鈍；（因長時間不用或有害使用而）損害，腐蝕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rust</b> is a brown substance that forms on iron or steel, for example when it comes into contact with water. 鏽","examples":["...a decaying tractor, red with rust. …一輛腐朽的拖拉機，因生鏽而呈紅色。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a metal object <b>rusts</b>, it becomes covered in rust and often loses its strength. 生鏽","examples":["Copper nails are better than iron nails because the iron rusts. 銅釘比鐵釘好，因為鐵釘會生鏽。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rust</b> is sometimes used to describe things that are reddish brown in colour. 鐵鏽色 (的)","examples":["...rust and gold leaves from the maples. …鐵鏽色和金黃色相間的楓葉。"]}]}]},"saucer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"茶碟，茶托，碟狀物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saucer</b> is a small curved plate on which you stand a cup. 茶碟","examples":["Rae's coffee cup clattered against the saucer as she picked it up. 蕾把咖啡杯拿起來的時候杯子碰響了茶碟。"]}]}]},"sack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麻布（或厚紙、塑膠等）大袋；一袋（的量）；<非正式> 解僱（the sack）；<非正式> 床（the sack）；（通常指在戰爭中）洗劫，劫掠；<非正式>（棒球）壘；（在爭球線後對四分衛的）擒殺；寬鬆直筒連衣裙（=sack dress）；<史>寬鬆女袍；<史>（流行於18世紀、繫於禮服裙裙肩上的）寬褶後拖曳地裙裾；<史>薩克葡萄酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式> 解僱，開除；（軍隊或軍事集團）劫掠，洗劫；（在美式足球中）擒抱（四分衛）；<美，非正式>把……裝進袋裡；<美，非正式>上床睡覺（sack out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sack</b> is a large bag made of thick paper or rough material. Sacks are used to carry or store things such as food or groceries. 大麻袋; 大厚紙袋","examples":["...a sack of potatoes. …一大袋土豆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a tackle on a quarterback which brings him down before he has passed the ball 擒殺四分衛","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sack</b> is also a noun. 開除","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the plundering of a place by an army or mob, usually involving destruction, slaughter, etc 洗劫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your employers <b>sack</b> you, they tell you that you can no longer work for them because you have done something that they did not like or because your work was not good enough. 開除","examples":["If he hadn't been so good at the rest of his job, I probably would have sacked him. 如果他不是在工作的其他方面做得這麼好，我可能已經把他解僱了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to plunder and partially destroy (a place) 劫掠(某處)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to tackle and bring down a quarterback before he has passed the ball 四分衛擒抱","examples":[]}]}]},"scarecrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（插在田裡嚇鳥的）稻草人；<非正式>衣著破爛的人，容貌古怪的人，骨瘦如柴的人；<古>讓人莫名害怕的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scarecrow</b> is an object in the shape of a person, which is put in a field where crops are growing in order to frighten birds away. 稻草人","examples":[]}]}]},"rough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（表面）粗糙的，不平的；（網球或軟式牆網球拍）粗麵的；粗暴的，猛烈的；（地方）多暴力的，犯罪盛行的；洶湧的，風浪很大的；粗製的，不完善的；粗俗的，不講究的；粗略的，大致的；<非正式> 艱難的，不愉快的；<英，非正式> 身體不適的；（聲音）粗啞的，不悅耳的；（酒）澀味的；未經加工的；（文具）用以打草稿的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（高爾夫球場的）深草區（the rough）；草稿，草圖；<舊，非正式> 粗野的人，暴徒；未加工的寶石；高低不平的地面；粗糙的部分；艱苦，不愉快"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"粗製，對……粗加工；草擬，畫……的輪廓；使不平，把……弄毛糙；<非正式> 因陋就簡地生活；粗暴地對待；（在美式橄欖球、冰球等比賽中對對手）動粗"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式> 粗糙地，粗暴地；<英> 風餐露宿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a surface is <b>rough</b>, it is uneven and not smooth. 粗糙的","examples":["His hands were rough and callused, from years of karate practice. 他的雙手由於多年的空手道練習，粗糙而佈滿老繭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You say that people or their actions are <b>rough</b> when they use too much force and not enough care or gentleness. 粗暴的; 粗野的","examples":["American football's a rough game at the best of times. 在最好的情況下足球也是一項粗野的運動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rough</b> area, city, school, or other place is unpleasant and dangerous because there is a lot of violence or crime there. (治安) 亂的","examples":["It was quite a rough part of our town. 那是我們鎮上相當亂的一個地方。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has had a <b>rough</b> time, you mean that they have had some difficult or unpleasant experiences. 艱難的","examples":["All women have a rough time in our society. 我們社會所有婦女都過著艱難的日子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>rough</b> calculation or guess is approximately correct, but not exact. 粗略的","examples":["We were only able to make a rough estimate of how much fuel would be required. 我們只能對所需燃料的量作一個粗略估計。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>rough</b> idea, description, or drawing of something, you indicate only the most important features, without much detail. 大致的","examples":["I've got a rough idea of what he looks like. 我對他的樣子有了個大致的概念。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>rough</b> when it is not neat and well made. 粗糙的","examples":["The bench had a rough wooden table in front of it. 那長椅前有張粗糙的木桌。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If the sea or the weather at sea is <b>rough</b>, the weather is windy or stormy and there are very big waves. 風浪大的","examples":["A fishing vessel and a cargo ship collided in rough seas. 一艘漁船與一艘貨輪在風大浪急的海上相撞了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗糙","examples":["She rested her cheek against the roughness of his jacket. 她把臉靠在了他粗糙的夾克上。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗暴地; 粗野地","examples":["They roughly pushed her forward. 他們粗暴地向前推她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"粗略地","examples":["Gambling and tourism pay roughly half the entire state budget. 博彩業和旅遊業為整個國家預算提供大致一半的資金來源。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"大致地","examples":["He knew roughly what was about to be said. 他大致知道該說些什麼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"粗糙地","examples":["Roughly chop the tomatoes and add them to the casserole. 把這些西紅柿粗切一下，添到那個砂鍋裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have to <b>rough it</b>, you have to live without the possessions and comforts that you normally have. 將就","examples":["There is a campsite but, if you prefer not to rough it, the Lake Hotel is nearby. 有一個營地，不過如果你不想將就，湖濱酒店就在附近。"]}]}]},"sausage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香腸，臘腸；香腸形狀；<英>用作親密稱呼小傢伙，小子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sausage</b> consists of minced meat, usually pork, mixed with other ingredients and is contained in a tube made of skin or a similar material. 香腸; 臘腸","examples":["...sausages and fries. …香腸和炸薯條。"]}]}]},"sake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"利益，好處；目的；為了便於討論（for the sake of argument）；（強調重要或表示惱火）看在上帝分上，天哪（for God's/goodness'/Christ's/heaven's/Pete's etc. sake）；日本米酒，日本清酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>for the sake of</b> something, you do it for that purpose or in order to achieve that result. You can also say that you do it <b>for</b> something's <b>sake</b>. 為了…的目的","examples":["Let's assume for the sake of argument that we manage to build a satisfactory database. 讓我們為了討論假定我們設法構建了一個令人滿意的資料庫。","For the sake of historical accuracy, please permit us to state the true facts. 為了歷史的準確性，請允許我們說出事實真相。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>for</b> its <b>own sake</b>, you do it because you want to, or because you enjoy it, and not for any other reason. You can also talk about, for example, <b>art for art's sake</b> or <b>sport for sport's sake</b>. 由於自身原因","examples":["Economic change for its own sake did not appeal to him. 經濟變化本身並沒有吸引他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you do something <b>for</b> someone's <b>sake</b>, you do it in order to help them or make them happy. 為幫助某人; 為使某人開心","examples":["I trust you to do a good job for Stan's sake. 我相信你會為了斯坦把工作做好。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people use expressions such as <b>for God's sake</b>, <b>for heaven's sake</b>, <b>for goodness' sake</b>, or <b>for Pete's sake</b> in order to express annoyance or impatience, or to add force to a question or request. The expressions \"for God's sake\" and \"for Christ's sake\" could cause offence. (用以加強質問或請求的語氣，表示厭惡或煩躁) 看在上帝的份上","examples":["For goodness' sake, why didn't you call me? 天哪，你為什麼沒給我打電話？"]}]}]},"saving":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（錢、時間或其他資源的）節約，節省；儲蓄金，存款；<法律> 保留，例外；存錢"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"節約的，節省的；節儉的，省錢的"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"除了，除……外"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"救援，挽救；節省；儲存（save 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saving</b> is a reduction in the amount of time or money that is used or needed. 節省","examples":["You can enjoy a year's membership for just $28 – a saving of $7 off the regular rate. 你只需花$28就可以享受一年的會員資格–比正常會費節省了$7。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>savings</b> are the money that you have saved, especially in a bank or a building society. 積蓄; 存款","examples":["Her savings were in the First National Bank. 她的存款以前在第一國民銀行。"]}]}]},"scarf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圍巾，披巾，頭巾；（嵌接的）斜面，斜嵌槽；鯨脂的切口"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>狼吞虎嚥地吃；嵌接，斜接（木材，金屬）；切割（鯨）脂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scarf</b> is a piece of cloth that you wear around your neck or head, usually to keep yourself warm. 圍巾","examples":["He reached up to loosen the scarf around his neck. 他伸出手鬆開圍在脖子上的圍巾。"]}]}]},"scatter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"撒，播撒；（使）散開，（使）散佈在各處；（物理）散射（電磁輻射或粒子）；（棒球）（被擊中但沒有得分的）有效投（球）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"零星散佈的東西；（統計）（對某一變數作反覆測量或觀察所得數值的）離差；（物理）（光、其他電磁波或粒子的）散射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scatter</b> things over an area, you throw or drop them so that they spread all over the area. 撒","examples":["She tore the rose apart and scattered the petals over the grave. 她掰開玫瑰花，把花瓣撒在墳墓上。","They've been scattering toys everywhere. 他們總是把玩具分散得到處都是。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a group of people <b>scatter</b> or if you <b>scatter</b> them, they suddenly separate and move in different directions. 使散開; 散開","examples":["After dinner, everyone scattered. 吃完飯，每個人都散開了。"]}]}]},"scholar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學者；有學問的人；獎學金獲得者；<非正式>聰穎勤奮的學生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scholar</b> is a person who studies an academic subject and knows a lot about it. 學者","examples":["The library attracts thousands of scholars and researchers. 這家圖書館吸引了數千名學者和研究人員。"]}]}]},"scholarship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎學金；學問，學術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get a <b>scholarship</b> to a school or university, your studies are paid for by the school or university or by some other organization. 獎學金","examples":["He got a scholarship to the Pratt Institute of Art. 他得到了一筆普拉特藝術學院的獎學金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Scholarship</b> is serious academic study and the knowledge that is obtained from it. 學術研究; 學問成就","examples":["I want to take advantage of your lifetime of scholarship. 我想從您一生的學術成就中獲益。"]}]}]},"scout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偵察兵，偵察機；偵查（尤指勘察地區）；童子軍（the Scouts）；（英國大學裡清掃學生房間的）校工；（演員、運動員等的）人才發掘者，星探；偵查蜂；童子軍隊員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在某個地區）尋找，搜尋；物色（尤指體育或娛樂）人才；<罕> 輕蔑地拒絕（建議，想法）；探查，偵查；跟蹤，監視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scout</b> is someone who is sent to an area of countryside to find out the position of an enemy army. 偵察員","examples":["They set off, two men out in front as scouts, two behind in case of any attack from the rear. 他們出發了，兩人在前作為偵察員，兩人殿後以防後方攻擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person employed by a club to seek new players (俱樂部尋找新成員時僱傭的)星探","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the act or an instance of scouting 偵察","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scout</b> somewhere <b>for</b> something, you go through that area searching for it. 搜尋","examples":["I wouldn't have time to scout the area for junk. 我不會有時間在那個地區找廢物。","A team of four was sent to scout for a nuclear test site. 一個四人小組被派去尋找核試驗基地。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to act as a scout for a sports club 物色(運動員)","examples":[]}]}]},"scoop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勺，球形勺；鏟，剷鬥；<非正式>（搶先報道的）獨家新聞；<美，非正式>（尤指私人的）最新內幕（the scoop）；一勺，一剷鬥（的量）；舀的動作，鏟的動作；（唱歌中）誇張的上滑音"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用勺舀，用鏟子鏟；挖出，挖空；（急速地）撿起，抱起；<非正式>搶先報道（新聞）；<非正式>贏得（金錢、獎品或勝利紀念品）；（唱歌）使用誇張的上滑音作為曲調的前奏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scoop</b> something from a container, you remove it with something such as a spoon. (用勺子) 舀","examples":["...the sound of a spoon scooping dog food out of a can. …用勺子從罐子裡舀狗糧的聲音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>scoop</b> a person or thing somewhere, you put your hands or arms under or around them and quickly move them there. (敏捷地) 抱住","examples":["Michael knelt next to her and scooped her into his arms. 邁克爾跪在她旁邊，一下子把她抱在懷裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scoop</b> is an object like a spoon which is used for picking up a quantity of a food such as ice cream or an ingredient such as flour. 勺","examples":["...a small ice-cream scoop. …一把小冰淇淋勺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>scoop</b> to refer to an exciting news story which is reported in one newspaper or on one television programme before it appears anywhere else. 獨家新聞","examples":["...one of the biggest scoops in the history of newspapers. …報業史上最大的獨家新聞之一。"]}]}]},"schedule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計劃（表），進度表；<美>（公共汽車、火車等的）時間表；（價目、費用等的）清單，一覽表；（電視或電臺的）節目表；<美>（學校的）課程表；<法律> 附件（尤指表格、單據等）；（英國所得稅制的）報稅單"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"安排，預定；列入，收進（正式目錄、清單等中）；<英> 把（建築物）列為文物保護單位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>schedule</b> is a plan that gives a list of events or tasks and the times at which each one should happen or be done. 日程安排","examples":["He has been forced to adjust his schedule. 他已被迫調整了日程安排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>schedule</b> to refer to the time or way something is planned to be done. For example, if something is completed <b>on schedule</b>, it is completed at the time planned. 計劃的時間","examples":["The jet arrived in Johannesburg two minutes ahead of schedule. 那架噴氣式飛機比預定時間提前兩分鐘到達了約翰內斯堡。","Everything went according to schedule. 一切都是按計劃進行的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>schedule</b> is a written list of things, for example, a list of prices, details, or conditions. (價格、細節或條件的) 明細表","examples":["Ticket plans and a pricing schedule will not be released until later this year. 售票計劃和價目表要到今年晚些時候才會公佈。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>schedule</b> is a list of all the times when trains, boats, buses, or aircraft are supposed to arrive at or leave a particular place. 時刻表","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a school or college, a <b>schedule</b> is a diagram that shows the times in the week at which particular subjects are taught. 課程表","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is scheduled</b> to happen at a particular time, arrangements are made for it to happen at that time. 計劃; 安排","examples":["The space shuttle had been scheduled to blast off at 04:38. 這架太空梭計劃於04:38發射升空。","A presidential election was scheduled for last December. 一場總統大選計劃在去年12月舉行。"]}]}]},"scale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"規模，範圍；等級，級別；刻度，標度；秤；比例，比例尺；音階；鱗，鱗片；水垢；牙垢；天平盤；天秤（星）座（the Scales）；（加熱後金屬上形成的）氧化皮；（數）進位制；（攝）影調範圍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"攀登，翻越；刮鱗；剔除（牙垢）；（按比例）縮小（或放大）；（尤指皮膚）生成鱗屑；（成片狀）脫落，剝落；稱得重量為；（數量，財產） 按一定比例調節；<美>估算（樹木的）產木材量"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（模型或複製品）按比例縮小的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>scale</b> of something, you are referring to its size or extent, especially when it is very big. 規模; 範圍","examples":["However, he underestimates the scale of the problem. 然而，他卻低估了問題的嚴重性。","The break-down of law and order could result in killing on a massive scale. 法律和秩序的崩潰可能會導致大規模的殺戮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scale</b> is a set of levels or numbers which are used in a particular system of measuring things or are used when comparing things. 等級","examples":["...an earthquake measuring 5.5 on the Richter scale. …一次里氏5.5級地震。","The patient rates the therapies on a scale of zero to ten. 這位患者按0到10分給這些療法分級。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A pay <b>scale</b> or <b>scale</b> <b>of</b> fees is a list that shows how much someone should be paid, depending, for example, on their age or what work they do. 工資級別","examples":["...those on the high end of the pay scale. …那些在高工資級別端的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>scale</b> of a map, plan, or model is the relationship between the size of something in the map, plan, or model and its size in the real world. 比例尺","examples":["The map, on a scale of 1:10,000, shows over 5,000 individual paths. 這張比例尺為1:10000的地圖顯示了5000條以上的獨立小徑。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the notation of a given number system 進位制","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In music, a <b>scale</b> is a fixed sequence of musical notes, each one higher than the next, which begins at a particular note. 音階","examples":["...the scale of C major. …C大調音階。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"The <b>scales</b> of a fish or reptile are the small, flat pieces of hard skin that cover its body. 鱗","examples":["Remove any excess scales from the fish skin. 刮掉魚皮上任何多餘的鱗。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"A <b>scale</b> is a piece of equipment used for weighing things, for example, for weighing amounts of food that you need in order to make a particular meal. 秤","examples":["...a pair of kitchen scales. …一臺廚用天平秤。","...a bathroom scale. …一臺浴室磅秤。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scale</b> model or <b>scale</b> replica of a building or object is a model of it which is smaller than the real thing but has all the same parts and features. 按比例縮小的","examples":["Franklin made his mother an intricately detailed scale model of the house. 富蘭克林為他的母親製作了一個按這座房子比例縮小的精巧逼真的模型。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scale</b> something such as a mountain or a wall, you climb up it or over it. 攀登","examples":["...Rebecca Stephens, the first British woman to scale Everest. …麗貝卡·斯蒂芬斯，第一位登上珠穆朗瑪峰的英國女性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to remove the scales or coating from 刮掉···的鱗片; 去掉···的塗層","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to weigh with or as if with scales (似)用天平稱重","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>out of scale</b> <b>with</b> the things near it, it is too big or too small in relation to them. 與…不成比例; 與…不相稱","examples":["The tiny church was out of scale with the new banks and offices around it. 這座小教堂與周圍那些新的銀行和辦公樓很不相稱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the different parts of a map, drawing, or model are <b>to scale</b>, they are the right size in relation to each other. 按比例","examples":["...a miniature garden, with little pagodas and bridges all to scale. …一個盆景，裡面的小寶塔和小橋也都是按比例製作的。"]}]}]},"separation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分開，分隔；分離，離別；（夫婦的）分居；離析；分色（colour separation 的簡稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>separation</b> <b>of</b> two or more things or groups is the fact that they are separate or become separate, and are not linked. 分離; 分開; 隔離","examples":["He believes in the separation of the races. 他信奉種族隔離政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"During a <b>separation</b>, people who usually live together are not together. 分離期間","examples":["She wondered if Harry had been unfaithful to her during this long separation. 她想知道，在分開的漫長歲月裡哈里是否已經對她不忠了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a couple who are married or living together have a <b>separation</b>, they decide to live apart. 分居","examples":["They agreed to a trial separation. 他們同意嘗試一次分居。"]}]}]},"scrub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指用硬刷子）擦洗，擦淨；（醫生在做手術前）仔細擦洗手和手臂（scrub up）；<非正式>取消（計劃等）；用水淨化（汽油，蒸汽）；（騎手用手臂與腿緊迫地摩擦馬的頸部和兩側）催馬（快行）；（賽車）（司機）讓輪胎滑行（或劃擦路面）以減速"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"矮樹叢，灌木叢；灌木叢地帶；刷洗，擦洗；磨砂膏；<美>醫院工作服（scrubs）；<非正式>無足輕重的人，可鄙的人；<美>二流球隊（或隊員）；<美>（在公共場所舉行的）兒童非正式團體比賽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（植物）矮小的；<美>（動物）劣等的，發育不良的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scrub</b> something, you rub it hard in order to clean it, using a stiff brush and water. 用力刷洗","examples":["Surgeons began to scrub their hands and arms with soap and water before operating. 外科醫生們在手術前開始用肥皂和水清洗他們的手和手臂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>scrub</b> dirt or stains <b>off</b> something, you remove them by rubbing hard. (將汙漬等從某物上) 用力擦 (除)","examples":["I started to scrub off the dirt. 我開始用力擦除汙物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to delete or cancel 刪除; 取消","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scrub</b> is also a noun. 用力刷洗","examples":["The walls needed a good scrub. 這些牆需要一次好好的刷洗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Scrub</b> consists of low trees and bushes, especially in an area that has very little rain. (尤指少雨地區的) 矮灌木叢","examples":["There is an area of scrub and woodland beside the railway line. 那條鐵路旁邊有一片矮灌木叢和林地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Scrubs</b> are the protective clothes that surgeons and other hospital staff wear in operating rooms. 手術服","examples":["...a man wearing blue hospital scrubs. …一個穿著藍色的醫院手術服的男子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a small or insignificant person 小人物","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"anything stunted or inferior 次貨","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a player not in the first team 二流隊員","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"small, stunted, or inferior 矮小的; 低劣的","examples":[]}]}]},"security":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保護措施，安全工作；保安部門；安檢處；保障，保證；安全，安全感；抵押品，保證金；證券，債券"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Security</b> refers to all the measures that are taken to protect a place, or to ensure that only people with permission enter it or leave it. 保安措施; 安全措施","examples":["They are now under a great deal of pressure to tighten their airport security. 他們目前承受著加強機場保安措施的巨大壓力。","Strict security measures are in force in the capital. 嚴格的安全措施在首都實施。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A feeling of <b>security</b> is a feeling of being safe and free from worry. 安全感","examples":["He loves the security of a happy home life. 他非常喜歡幸福的家庭生活所來的那種安全感。","If an alarm gives you that feeling of security, then it's worth carrying. 如果一個報警器能給你那種安全感，那就值得攜帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>security</b> for a loan, you promise to give that thing to the person who lends you money, if you fail to pay the money back. 抵押品","examples":["The central bank will provide special loans, and the banks will pledge the land as security. 中央銀行將提供特別貸款,而各家銀行將以土地作為抵押品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Securities</b> are stocks, shares, bonds, or other certificates that you buy in order to earn regular interest from them or to sell them later for a profit. 有價證券","examples":["National banks can package their own mortgages and underwrite them as securities. 國家銀行可以組合包裝自己的的抵押貸款,以證券形式承銷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something gives you <b>a false sense of security</b>, it makes you believe that you are safe when you are not. 虛假的安全感","examples":[]}]}]},"screw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螺絲（釘）；螺桿，螺絲桿；螺旋槳；螺旋體，螺旋狀物；螺旋運動，擰緊螺旋；<非正式>監獄看守人，獄警（尤為囚犯用語）；<非正式>性行為，性伴侶；<英>旋轉球，倒旋；<英>（多指包有鹽或菸草的）小紙卷；<英，非正式>工資，工錢；<英，非正式>卑鄙的人，吝嗇鬼；<英，非正式>疲馬；拇指夾（舊時的一種刑具）（the screws）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用螺絲固定；擰緊，旋緊；（物體）旋上，旋開；把（紙等）揉成一團；扭曲（臉），眯起（眼睛）；<非正式>（和某人）性交；<非正式>欺騙，詐騙；<非正式>敲詐，勒索（錢財等）；<非正式>毀掉，搞砸；<非正式>見鬼去；使（球）旋轉，使（擊球）偏轉；<英>打旋轉球；猛回頭，急轉身（screw sth. around/round）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>screw</b> is a metal object similar to a nail, with a raised spiral line around it. You turn a screw using a screwdriver so that it goes through two things, for example, two pieces of wood, and fastens them together. 螺釘","examples":["Each bracket is fixed to the wall with just three screws. 每個托架只用3顆螺釘固定在牆上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>screw</b> something somewhere or if it <b>screws</b> somewhere, you fix it in place by means of a screw or screws. 用螺釘固定","examples":["I had screwed the shelf on the wall myself. 我自己用螺釘把架子固定在了牆上。","Screw down any loose floorboards. 用螺釘釘緊任何鬆動的地板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>screw</b> something somewhere or if it <b>screws</b> somewhere, you fix it in place by twisting it around and around. 擰緊","examples":["\"Yes, I know that,\" Kelly said, screwing the silencer onto the pistol. “是的，我知道那事。”凱利一邊把消音器擰到手槍上一邊說道。","Screw down the lid fairly tightly. 把蓋子擰到很緊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>screw</b> something such as a piece of paper <b>into</b> a ball, you squeeze it or twist it tightly so that it is in the shape of a ball. 把 (紙片等) 揉成 (一團)","examples":["He screwed the paper into a ball and tossed it into the fire. 他把那片紙揉成一團扔進了火裡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>screw</b> your face or your eyes <b>into</b> a particular expression, you tighten the muscles of your face to form that expression, for example, because you are in pain or because the light is too bright. 把 (臉、眼睛等) 扭曲成 (某表情)","examples":["He screwed his face into an expression of mock pain. 他把他的臉扭曲成假痛苦狀。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Some people use <b>screw</b> in expressions such as <b>screw you</b> or <b>screw that</b> to show that they are not concerned about someone or something or that they feel contempt for them. 去 (你、它等) 的 (表示不關心或蔑視)","examples":["Something inside me snapped. \"Well, screw you then!\" 我忍不住爆發了。“好，那麼去你的吧！”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>screws</b> something, especially money, <b>out of</b> you, they get it from you by putting pressure on you. 敲詐","examples":["After decades of rich nations screwing money out of poor nations, it's about time some went the other way. 富國從窮國敲詐錢財已數十年，該是有些國家反其道而行之的時候了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>screw</b> lid or fitting is one that has a raised spiral line on the inside or outside of it, so that it can be fixed in place by twisting. 帶螺旋的 (蓋子、配件等)","examples":["...an ordinary jam jar with a screw lid. …一個帶螺旋蓋的普通果醬罐。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>screws</b> someone else or if two people <b>screw</b>, they have sex together. 與…性交; 性交","examples":["\"Are you screwing her?\" she said. “你是不是和她上床了？”她說。"]}]}]},"scream":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因傷痛、害怕、激動等）尖叫；（向某人或為某事）高聲喊，大聲叫；發出尖銳的響聲；呼嘯而過；（使）醒目，（使）觸目驚心（=scream out）；呼籲，抗議；清晰地表明；顏色不相配"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（因疼痛、驚恐、興奮等發出的）尖叫聲；（動物的）高聲尖叫；尖銳刺耳的聲音；<非正式，舊>極其滑稽可笑的人（或事物、場面）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>screams</b>, they make a very loud, high-pitched cry, for example, because they are in pain or are very frightened. (人因痛苦或恐懼而) 尖叫","examples":["Women were screaming; some of the houses nearest the bridge were on fire. 女人們在尖叫；最靠近橋的一些房屋在燃燒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scream</b> is also a noun. 尖叫","examples":["Hilda let out a scream. 希爾達發出了一聲尖叫。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scream</b> something, you shout it in a loud, high-pitched voice. 尖聲說","examples":["\"Brigid!\" she screamed. \"Get up!\" “布里吉德！”她尖聲叫道。“起床！”"]}]}]},"sex":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"性行為，性交；性，性別；雄性，雌性；性器官（用於小說中避免更粗俗或更露骨的措詞）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"辨別......的性別，辨識......的雌雄；<非正式> 引起……的性慾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The two <b>sexes</b> are the two groups, male and female, into which people and animals are divided according to the function they have in producing young. (雌、雄、男、女) 性","examples":["...a movie star who appeals to all ages and both sexes. …一個吸引男女老少的電影明星。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>sex</b> of a person or animal is their characteristic of being either male or female. 性別","examples":["She continually failed to gain promotion because of her sex. 由於性別的原因，她頻頻得不到升職。","The new technique has been used to identify the sex of fetuses. 這項新技術已被用來鑑定胎兒的性別。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sex</b> is the physical activity by which people can produce young. 性行為","examples":["He was very open in his attitudes about sex. 他對性的態度很開放。","The entire film revolves around drugs, sex and violence. 整部電影都圍繞著毒品、色情和暴力展開。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people <b>have sex</b>, they perform the act of sex. 進行性交","examples":["Have you ever thought about having sex with someone other than your husband? 你想過與丈夫之外的人發生性關係嗎？"]}]}]},"seal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"印章，圖章；表示確認的事物；密封裝置，密封物；密封，密封狀態；水止，水封（根據排汙管道深度U形管中防止臭氣上升的存水）；封蠟，火漆；封蠟模（印），封鉛模（印）；海豹；海豹皮；裝飾性的背面塗膠水的郵票（印花）；（美國海軍）海豹特種部隊士兵（SEAL）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"封上（信封）；密封（容器）；確定，使成定局；給……塗上保護層；（給檔案）加封，蓋印；封鎖；（為避免烹調時失去過多水分，將食物放在熱油中）快速煎炸；獵捕海豹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>seal</b> an envelope, you close it by folding part of it over and sticking it down, so that it cannot be opened without being torn. 封 (信封)","examples":["He sealed the envelope and put on a stamp. 他封好信封，貼了張郵票。","Write your letter and seal it in a blank envelope. 寫好你的信，然後將其封入一個空信封。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>seal</b> a container or an opening, you cover it with something in order to prevent air, liquid, or other material from getting in or out. If you <b>seal</b> something <b>in</b> a container, you put it inside and then close the container tightly. 封 (容器、開口); 將 (某物) 封入 (某容器中)","examples":["She filled the containers, sealed them with a cork, and stuck on labels. 她裝滿那些容器，用塞子封了口，然後貼上了標籤。","A woman picks them up and seals them in plastic bags. 一位女士揀起它們，然後把它們封入各塑膠袋中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>seals</b> an area, they stop people entering or passing through it, for example, by placing barriers in the way. 封鎖 (某地區)","examples":["The soldiers were deployed to help paramilitary police seal the border. 這些士兵們被調去協助準軍事警察封鎖邊境。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>seal</b> something means to make it definite or confirm how it is going to be. 確定","examples":["McLaren are close to sealing a deal with Renault. 麥克拉倫即將和雷諾爾特達成一筆交易。","A general election will be held which will seal his destiny one way or the other. 一場將左右他命運的大選即將舉行。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"to affix a seal to, as proof of authenticity 加封印(以示真偽)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>seal</b> on a container or opening is the part where it has been sealed. (容器、開口等) 封了的部分","examples":["When assembling the pie, wet the edges where the two crusts join, to form a seal. 捏合餡餅時，弄溼兩塊麵皮封合的邊緣，以形成一個封口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>seal</b> is a device or a piece of material, for example, in a machine, which closes an opening tightly so that air, liquid, or other substances cannot get in or out. (機器上防止氣體或液體滲入或露出的) 密封裝置","examples":["Check seals on fridges and freezers regularly. 定期檢查冰箱和冰櫃的密封裝置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>seal</b> is something such as a piece of sticky paper or wax that is fixed to a container or door and must be broken before the container or door can be opened. (封條、封蠟等) 封口物","examples":["The seal on the box broke when it fell from its hiding-place. 盒子從隱藏處掉下時上面的封口破了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>seal</b> is a special mark or design, for example, on a document, representing someone or something. It may be used to show that something is genuine or officially approved. 印章","examples":["...a supply of note paper bearing the presidential seal. …一批蓋有總統印章的便條紙。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>seal</b> is a large animal with a rounded body and flat legs called flippers. Seals eat fish and live in and near the sea, usually in cold parts of the world. 海豹","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Seal off</b> means the same as . 封鎖 (某地區)","examples":["Police and troops sealed off the area after the attack. 警察和軍隊在襲擊發生後封鎖了該地區。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to hunt for seals 獵取海豹","examples":[]}]}]},"shampoo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洗髮劑，香波；洗髮，洗滌；（清洗地毯等的）洗滌劑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用洗髮劑洗，用洗滌劑洗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shampoo</b> is a soapy liquid that you use for washing your hair. 洗髮液","examples":["...a bottle of shampoo. …一瓶洗髮水。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>shampoo</b> your hair, you wash it using shampoo. 用洗髮水洗","examples":["Shampoo your hair and dry it. 用洗髮水洗洗你的頭髮，然後把頭髮弄乾。"]}]}]},"shame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羞恥，羞愧；羞恥心，羞恥感；令人惋惜的事，讓人遺憾的事；恥辱，丟臉；帶來恥辱的人（或行為、局面）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使感到羞恥（或羞愧）；使蒙羞，使丟臉；使黯然失色，使相形見絀"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<南非>（表示讚歎或喜愛）真可惜，好極了；（用於表示不贊同演講者所說的話）可恥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shame</b> is an uncomfortable feeling that you get when you have done something wrong or embarrassing, or when someone close to you has. 羞恥; 羞愧","examples":["She felt a deep sense of shame. 她深感羞恥。","Her father and her brothers would die of shame. 她的父親和兄弟們會羞愧死的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone brings <b>shame</b> <b>on</b> you, they make other people lose their respect for you. 恥辱","examples":["I don't want to bring shame on the family name. 我不想給家庭的聲譽帶來恥辱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a</b> <b>shame</b>, you are expressing your regret about it and indicating that you wish it had happened differently. 令人遺憾的事","examples":["It's a crying shame that police have to put up with these mindless attacks. 警察不得不容忍這些無謂的攻擊，真是件太令人遺憾的事。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shames</b> you, it causes you to feel shame. 使羞愧","examples":["Her son's affair had humiliated and shamed her. 她兒子的事丟了她的臉、令她羞愧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shame</b> someone <b>into</b> doing something, you force them to do it by making them feel ashamed not to. 使…感到羞愧 (而做某事)","examples":["He would not let neighbours shame him into silence. 他不會因為鄰居的羞辱而默不作聲。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>shame</b> in expressions such as <b>shame on you</b> and <b>shame on him</b> to indicate that someone ought to feel shame for something they have said or done. 恥辱","examples":["He tried to deny it. Shame on him! 他想否認此事。真丟人！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>puts</b> you <b>to shame</b>, they make you feel ashamed because they do something much better than you do. 使自愧不如","examples":["His playing really put me to shame. 他的表現真讓我自愧不如。"]}]}]},"shepherd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牧羊人，羊倌；牧師；指導者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"牧（羊）；帶領，引領，護送；（尤指精神方面）給……指導"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shepherd</b> is a person, especially a man, whose job is to take care of sheep. 牧羊人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are shepherded</b> somewhere, someone takes you there to make sure that you arrive at the right place safely. 護送","examples":["She was shepherded by her guards up the rear ramp of the aircraft. 她由她的警衛們護送登上飛機後部的活動舷梯。"]}]}]},"shave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"剃（須），颳去（毛髮）；削去，刮掉（薄層）；（少量地）減去，削減；掠過，擦過"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"刮臉，剃毛髮 ；剃刀，刮刀； <非正式> 僥倖逃過，倖免（close shave）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a man <b>shaves</b>, he removes the hair from his face using a razor or shaver so that his face is smooth. 刮 (臉); 剃鬚","examples":["He took a bath and shaved before dinner. 他在晚餐前洗了澡並颳了臉。","He had shaved his face until it was smooth. 他把臉刮到光滑為止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shave off</b> part of a piece of wood or other material, you cut very thin pieces from it. 削掉; 刨掉","examples":["I set the log on the ground and shaved off the bark. 我把原木放在地上，然後刨掉樹皮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>shave</b> a small amount <b>off</b> something such as a record, cost, or price, you reduce it by that amount. 少量削減; 略微降低","examples":["She's already shaved four seconds off the national record for the mile. 她已經把1英里賽跑的全國紀錄減少了4秒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shave</b> is also a noun. 剃鬚; 刮臉","examples":["He never seemed to need a shave. 他似乎從不需要刮臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"剃鬚; 刮臉","examples":["...a range of shaving products. …一系列剃鬚產品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>a</b> <b>close shave</b>, you mean that there was nearly an accident or a disaster but it was avoided. 僥倖脫險","examples":["I can't quite believe the close shaves I've had just recently. 我幾乎不能相信我最近剛經歷的幾次僥倖脫險。"]}]}]},"shadow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陰影，影子；暗處，陰影處（=shadows）；黑眼圈；壞影響；茫然，悲傷；一點點，絲毫；大不如從前的人（或事物）；虛幻的事物，不可能得到的東西；形影不離的人（或動物）；暗地跟蹤者，尾隨者；（跟隨別人學習的）實習生；眼影（eyeshadow 的簡稱）；庇護；幽靈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"被……陰影籠罩，投陰影於；暗地跟蹤；跟隨……實地學習（或參觀）；<英>（反對黨成員）擔任影子內閣大臣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"影子內閣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shadow</b> is a dark shape on a surface that is made when something stands between a light and the surface. 影子; 陰影","examples":["An oak tree cast its shadow over a tiny round pool. 一棵橡樹在一個小圓池塘上投下了它的影子。","Nothing would grow in the shadow of the grey wall. 沒有任何東西會在那堵灰牆的陰影裡生長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shadow</b> is darkness in a place caused by something preventing light from reaching it. 背陰","examples":["Most of the lake was in shadow. 那個湖的大部分都在背陰中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Shadow</b> is also a noun. 在野內閣成員","examples":["Clarke swung at his shadow the accusation that he was \"a tabloid politician.\" 克拉克指責其在野對手為“煽情政客”。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shadows</b> a thing or place, it covers it with a shadow. 遮住","examples":["The hood shadowed her face. 風帽遮住了她的臉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>shadows</b> you, they follow you very closely wherever you go. 尾隨","examples":["The president is constantly shadowed by bodyguards. 該總統總是有保鏢緊隨其後。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A British Member of Parliament who is a member of the <b>shadow</b> cabinet or who is a <b>shadow</b> cabinet minister belongs to the main opposition party and takes a special interest in matters which are the responsibility of a particular government minister. 在野黨派的 (內閣)","examples":["...the shadow chancellor. …在野黨派的財政大臣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>without</b> <b>a shadow of a doubt</b> or <b>without</b> <b>a shadow of doubt</b>, you are emphasizing that there is no doubt at all that it is true. 一絲懷疑","examples":["It was without a shadow of a doubt the best we've played. 那毫無疑問是我們表現最出色的一次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you live <b>in the shadow of</b> someone or <b>in</b> their <b>shadow</b>, their achievements and abilities are so great that you are not noticed or valued. 在某人的陰影下","examples":["He has always lived in the shadow of his brother. 他一直生活在他哥哥的陰影之下。"]}]}]},"shade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背陰處，陰涼處；（圖畫中的）暗處；遮光物，燈罩；<美>（能上下卷疊的）窗簾，百葉窗；<非正式>太陽鏡，墨鏡（shades）；（色彩的）濃淡深淺，色度；差別，不同；略微，少量（a shade）；讓人想起……的事物（shades of）；次要地位，不顯眼；<文>鬼，幽靈；地獄，冥府（the Shades）；<史>剪影"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……遮陽（擋光），遮蔽（光線）；（用鉛筆或加色）描黑，描影；使陰暗，使陰鬱；（色彩）漸變；<非正式>（比賽）稍勝一籌，略佔優勢；（數量、速度或價格）略降；<美>細微改動以掩蓋事實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shade</b> <b>of</b> a particular colour is one of its different forms. For example, emerald green and olive green are shades of green. 色調","examples":["In the mornings the sky appeared a heavy shade of mottled grey. 清晨，天空看上去是斑駁的深灰色調。","The walls were painted in two shades of green. 這些牆壁被塗成了兩種色調不同的綠色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Shade</b> is an area of darkness under or next to an object such as a tree, where sunlight does not reach. 陰涼處","examples":["Temperatures in the shade can reach forty-eight degrees Celsius at this time of year. 一年中的這個時候，陰涼處的溫度能達到48攝氏度。","Alexis walked up the coast, and resumed his reading in the shade of an overhanging cliff. 亞歷克西斯沿著海岸向前走，然後在一塊凸出的懸崖下的陰涼處重新看起書來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Shade</b> is darkness or shadows as they are shown in a picture. (圖畫中的) 暗部; 投影","examples":["...Rembrandt's skilful use of light and shade to create the atmosphere of movement. …倫勃朗巧妙的運用了明與暗來營造動感。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>shades</b> <b>of</b> something abstract are its many, slightly different forms. (抽象事物的) 略有差異的形式","examples":["...the capacity to convey subtle shades of meaning. …表達略有微妙差異的意義的能力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>shade</b> is a piece of stiff cloth or heavy paper that you can pull down over a window as a covering. 遮簾","examples":["Nancy left the shades down and the lights off. 南希放下簾子，關了燈。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a place or person <b>is shaded</b> by objects such as trees, you mean that the place or person cannot be reached, harmed, or bothered by strong sunlight because those objects are in the way. 形成陰蔽","examples":["...a health resort whose beaches are shaded by palm trees. …一個海灘上棕櫚成陰蔭的療養勝地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shade</b> your eyes, you put your hand or an object partly in front of your face in order to prevent a bright light from shining into your eyes. 遮蔽 (使不受陽光傷害)","examples":["You can't look directly into it; you've got to shade your eyes or close them altogether. 你不能直視它；你得遮住雙眼或者完全閉上眼睛。"]}]}]},"shovel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鏟子，鐵鍬；（推土機、挖土機等的）鏟，鏟形部分；一鏟（的量）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用鏟子）剷起，鏟去；把……大量送入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shovel</b> is a tool with a long handle that is used for lifting and moving earth, coal, or snow. 鏟","examples":["...a coal shovel. …一把煤鏟。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shovel</b> earth, coal, or snow, you lift and move it with a shovel. 用鏟挖; 剷起","examples":["He has to get out and shovel snow. 他不得不出去剷雪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shovel</b> something somewhere, you push a lot of it quickly into that place. 把…大量送入","examples":["There was silence, except for Randall, who was obliviously shovelling food into his mouth. 到處一片寂靜，除了正在忘乎所以地把食物大口大口地塞進嘴裡的蘭德爾。"]}]}]},"sigh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘆氣，嘆息；（風）呼嘯，嗚咽；嘆息著說；<文> 渴望，思慕"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘆氣，嘆息（聲）；（尤指風發出的）嘆息般的聲音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sigh</b>, you let out a deep breath, as a way of expressing feelings such as disappointment, tiredness, or pleasure. 嘆氣","examples":["Michael sighed wearily. 邁克爾疲憊地嘆了口氣。","Roberta sighed with relief. 羅伯塔鬆了口氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sigh</b> is also a noun. 嘆氣","examples":["She kicked off her shoes with a sigh. 她嘆著氣踢掉了鞋子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people breathe or heave a <b>sigh of relief</b>, they feel happy that something unpleasant has not happened or is no longer happening. 鬆了口氣","examples":["With monetary mayhem now retreating into memory, European countries can breathe a collective sigh of relief. 隨著金融混亂已成往事，歐洲國家全都可以鬆口氣了。"]}]}]},"similarity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"相似性；相似點，類似的地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>similarity</b> <b>between</b> two or more things, they are similar to each other. 相似; 類似","examples":["...the astonishing similarity between my brother and my first-born son. …我弟弟和我大兒子的驚人相似。","There was a very basic similarity in our philosophy. 我們的人生哲學在根本上很相似。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Similarities</b> are features that things have which make them similar to each other. 相似之處","examples":["There were significant similarities between mother and son. 母子間有著極其相似的地方。"]}]}]},"sin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（違背宗教或道德的）罪，罪惡；過錯，過失"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"犯戒律，犯過失；褻瀆，冒犯（上帝，人，原則）（sin against）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"正弦（sine 的縮寫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sin</b> or a <b>sin</b> is an action or type of behaviour which is believed to break the laws of God. 罪過; 罪孽","examples":["The Vatican's teaching on abortion is clear: it is a sin. 梵蒂岡有關墜胎的教義是清楚的：這是個罪過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"罪人","examples":["I was shown that I am a sinner, that I needed to repent of my sins. 我被證明是個罪人，需要為我的罪孽懺悔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sin</b> is any action or behaviour that people disapprove of or consider morally wrong. 違背道德原則的行為","examples":["...the sin of arrogant hard-heartedness. …狂妄冷酷的惡行。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sin</b>, you do something that is believed to break the laws of God. 犯戒律","examples":["The Spanish Inquisition charged him with sinning against God and man. 西班牙宗教法庭指控他違背了上帝和人類的律法。"]}]},{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"sine sine的縮寫","examples":[]}]}]},"sip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"小口喝，抿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一小口（飲料），一啜之量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sip</b> a drink or <b>sip at</b> it, you drink by taking just a small amount at a time. 小口地喝","examples":["Jessica sipped her drink thoughtfully. 傑西卡若有所思地喝了一小口飲料。","He sipped at the glass and then put it down. 他抿了一口，然後放下杯子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sip</b> is a small amount of drink that you take into your mouth. 一小口的量","examples":["Harry took a sip of bourbon. 哈里喝了一小口波旁威士忌酒。"]}]}]},"skyscraper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"摩天大樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>skyscraper</b> is a very tall building in a city. 摩天樓","examples":[]}]}]},"ski":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"滑雪（水）板；（車輛的）滑橇；水橇，滑水撬（=waterski）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滑雪，滑水"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滑雪的，滑水的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Skis</b> are long, flat, narrow pieces of wood, metal, or plastic that are fastened to boots so that you can move easily on snow or water. 滑雪板; 滑水板","examples":["...a pair of skis. …一副滑雪板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"滑雪者; 滑水者","examples":["He is an enthusiastic skier. 他是個熱情的滑雪愛好者。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>ski</b>, they move over snow or water on skis. 滑雪; 滑水","examples":["They surf, ski and ride. 他們衝浪、滑水和騎馬。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>ski</b> to refer to things that are concerned with skiing. 滑雪用的; 滑水用的","examples":["...the Swiss ski resort of Klosters. …瑞士的克洛斯特斯滑雪勝地。","...a private ski instructor. …一位私人滑雪教練。"]}]}]},"skate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溜冰鞋，滑冰鞋； 四輪溜冰鞋，旱冰鞋；（滑冰鞋上的）冰刀；（載笨重物的）滑板車；滑板（skateboard 的簡稱）；鰩魚（一種扁平狀海魚）；鰩魚肉；<非正式>（南非）聲名狼藉的粗魯白人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滑冰，溜冰；在滑板上滑行，溜出（花樣）；滑行；一筆帶過，迴避（skate over/round）；（喻）一蹴而就（skate through）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Skates</b> are ice-skates. 冰鞋; 冰刀","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Skates</b> are roller-skates. 旱冰鞋","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"滑冰","examples":["They all went skating together in the winter. 他們冬天都一起去滑冰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"any large ray of the family <b>Rajidae,</b> of temperate and tropical seas, having flat pectoral fins continuous with the head, two dorsal fins, a short spineless tail, and a long snout 鰩魚","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>skate</b>, you move around wearing ice-skates or roller-skates. 滑冰","examples":["I actually skated, and despite some teetering I did not fall on the ice. 我的確滑冰了。儘管有些搖搖晃晃，我還是沒有摔倒在冰上。"]}]}]},"situation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"情況，形勢；重要問題，突發情況；（建築物或城鎮的）地理位置，環境特點；<舊，正式>工作，職位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>situation</b> to refer generally to what is happening in a particular place at a particular time, or to refer to what is happening to you. 情況; 形勢","examples":["Army officers said the situation was under control. 軍方官員說局勢已得到控制。","And now for a look at the travel situation in the rest of the country. 現在來看一看該國其他地區的旅行條件。"]}]}]},"signal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訊號，暗號；標誌，預示；（尤指鐵路和公路上的）指示燈，訊號燈；（無線電、電視等的）訊號，訊號；起因，導火線；（橋牌）訊號；（傳遞的）資訊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發訊號，示意；標誌，預示；告知，表示；（車輛轉方向時）打燈示意"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重大的，顯要的；作為訊號的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>signal</b> is a gesture, sound, or action which is intended to give a particular message to the person who sees or hears it. 訊號","examples":["They fired three distress signals. 他們發射了3次遇難求救訊號。","As soon as it was dark, Mrs. Evans gave the signal. 天一黑，埃文斯夫人就發出了那個訊號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or action is a <b>signal</b> <b>of</b> something, it suggests that this thing exists or is going to happen. 訊號","examples":["Kurdish leaders saw the visit as an important signal of support. 庫爾德領導人把這次訪問看作是表示支援的重要訊號。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>signal</b> is a piece of equipment beside a railway, which indicates to train drivers whether they should stop the train or not. 鐵路的訊號燈","examples":["A signal failure contributed to the crash. 訊號燈故障導致了這次撞車事故。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>signal</b> is a series of radio waves, light waves, or changes in electrical current which may carry information. (傳輸資訊的無線電、光波或電流) 訊號","examples":["...high-frequency radio signals. …高頻無線電訊號。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>signal</b> <b>to</b> someone, you make a gesture or sound in order to send them a particular message. (打手勢或發聲音) 向…示意; 發訊號","examples":["Mandy started after him, signalling to Jesse to follow. 曼迪開始追趕他，示意傑西跟上。","She signalled to Ted that she was moving forward. 她向特德示意她要向前走。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>signals</b> an event, they suggest that the event is happening or likely to happen. 表示","examples":["He seemed to be signalling important shifts in U.S. government policy. 他似乎在表示美國政府的政策將會有些重大變化。"]}]}]},"slave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奴隸，苦工；完全受（某事物）控制的人；從動裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"苦幹，拼命幹；使（裝置）從屬於（另一裝置）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slave</b> is someone who is the property of another person and has to work for that person. 奴隸","examples":["The state of Liberia was formed a century and a half ago by freed slaves from the United States. 賴比瑞亞國家是一個半世紀前由來自美國的獲得自由的奴隸建立的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone as a <b>slave</b> when they are completely under the control of another person or of a powerful influence. 奴隸般受控制的人","examples":["She may no longer be a slave to the studio system, but she still has a duty to her fans. 她也許不再受制片公司制度的控制了，但她對其粉絲還負有責任。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person <b>is slaving</b> <b>over</b> something or <b>is slaving</b> <b>for</b> someone, you mean that they are working very hard. 苦幹","examples":["When you're busy all day the last thing you want to do is spend hours slaving over a hot stove. 當你忙碌了一整天后，你最不願意做的事就是花好幾個鐘頭在灼熱的火爐邊辛苦地勞作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slave away</b> means the same as . 苦幹","examples":["He stares at the hundreds of workers slaving away in the intense sun. 他凝視著幾百個正在烈日下苦幹的工人們。"]}]}]},"skip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"蹦蹦跳跳地走；跳繩；不做（應做的事等），不參加；跳過，略過；快速轉移，驟然轉換（話題）；悄悄溜走，突然離開；打水漂；當（運動隊的）領隊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蹦跳；（計算機）跳躍（進位），跳行；<美，非正式>違約者，討債者；<英> 廢料桶；罐籠，箕斗，吊斗；（草地滾木球或冰壺運動隊的）領隊，隊長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>skip</b> along, you move almost as if you are dancing, with a series of little jumps from one foot to the other. 蹦跳; 蹦跳著走","examples":["They saw the man with a little girl skipping along behind him. 他們看到那個男人身後跟著一個蹦蹦跳跳的小女孩。","We went skipping down the street arm in arm. 我們挽著臂蹦蹦跳跳地沿大街走著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>skip</b> <b>from</b> one subject or activity <b>to</b> another, you move quickly from one to the other, although there is no obvious connection between them. (無條理地) 快速轉換","examples":["She kept up a continuous chatter, skipping from one subject to the next. 她嘰嘰咕咕地說個不停，從一個話題跳到另一個話題。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Skip</b> is also a noun. 蹦跳","examples":["The boxer gave a little skip as he came out of his corner. 那位拳擊手輕快地跳出了場角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"跳繩","examples":["We did rope skipping and things like that. 我們跳繩或做類似的活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>skip</b> is a large, open, metal container which is used to hold and take away large unwanted items and rubbish. (盛大體積廢棄物的) 廢料桶; 大鐵桶","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the captain of a curling or bowls team 冰壺隊隊長","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a cage used as a lift in mines, etc (礦上用的)料車","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>skips</b>, they jump up and down over a rope which they or two other people are holding at each end and turning around and around. 跳 (繩)","examples":["They skip and play catch, waiting for the bell. 他們又是跳繩又是玩捉迷藏，等著鈴聲響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>skip</b> something that you usually do or something that most people do, you decide not to do it. 不做; 逃避","examples":["It is important not to skip meals. 重要的是，不能不吃飯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>skip</b> or <b>skip over</b> a part of something you are reading or a story you are telling, you miss it out or pass over it quickly and move on to something else. 匆匆翻閱; 略過","examples":["You might want to skip the exercises in this chapter. 你可能想把這一章的練習跳過去。"]}]}]},"sleeve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"袖子；袖套；（機器的）套筒，套管；唱片套；風向袋；（機尾的）減速傘，制動傘"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……裝套筒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>sleeves</b> of a coat, shirt, or other item of clothing are the parts that cover your arms. 袖子","examples":["His sleeves were rolled up to his elbows. 他的兩隻袖子被挽到了肘部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A record <b>sleeve</b> is the stiff cover in which a record is kept. (唱片的) 套子","examples":["...an album sleeve. …一個唱片套。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something <b>up</b> your <b>sleeve</b>, you have an idea or plan which you have not told anyone about. You can also say that someone has <b>an ace, card,</b> or <b>trick up</b> their <b>sleeve</b>. 有錦囊妙計; 對…胸有成竹","examples":["He wondered what tricks Shearson had up his sleeve. 他想知道希爾森有何錦囊妙計。"]}]}]},"sorrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"悲傷，悲痛，悲哀；傷心事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"感到（或表示）悲傷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sorrow</b> is a feeling of deep sadness or regret. 悲傷; 歉疚","examples":["Words cannot express my sorrow. 語言不能表達我的悲傷。"]}]}]},"slope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"斜坡，斜面；山坡；滑雪斜坡；斜度，坡度；（電子）斜率；扛槍姿勢；<美，非正式> 東方人（尤指越南人）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"傾斜，成斜坡；歪斜；悄悄地走，溜；<英，非正式> 逛，隨意走動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slope</b> is the side of a mountain, hill, or valley. (山丘或山谷的) 斜坡","examples":["Saint-Christo is perched on a mountain slope. 聖克里斯托坐落在山坡上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slope</b> is a surface that is at an angle, so that one end is higher than the other. 斜面","examples":["The street must have been on a slope. 那條街一定是一直在一個斜坡上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>slope</b> of something is the angle at which it slopes. 斜度; 坡度","examples":["The slope increases as you go up the curve. 你順著那條彎路往上走，坡度越來越大。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a surface <b>slopes</b>, it is at an angle, so that one end is higher than the other. 傾斜","examples":["The bank sloped down sharply to the river. 那座堤岸陡峭地朝著那條河傾斜下去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>slopes</b>, it leans to the right or to the left rather than being upright. 歪斜","examples":["The writing sloped backwards. 那字跡向後斜了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傾斜的","examples":["...a brick building, with a sloping roof. …一幢斜頂的磚建築。"]}]}]},"sore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（發炎）疼痛的，痠痛的；<美，非正式>惱火的，惱怒的；（精神上）痛苦的，困擾的；極度的，非常的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"傷處，痛處，瘡；痛處，傷心事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If part of your body is <b>sore</b>, it causes you pain and discomfort. 疼痛的","examples":["It's years since I've had a sore throat like I did last night. 我已經好多年沒有像昨晚那樣嗓子痛了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>sore</b> about something, you are angry and upset about it. 惱怒的","examples":["The result is that they are now all feeling very sore at you. 結果是他們現在都很生你的氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sore</b> is a painful place on the body where the skin is infected. 痛處","examples":["Our backs and hands were covered with sores and burns from the ropes. 我們的背和手到處是繩索導致的傷口和灼傷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>a sore point</b> <b>with</b> someone, it is likely to make them angry or embarrassed if you try to discuss it. 令人惱怒的事; 令人尷尬的事","examples":["The continuing presence of American troops on Korean soil remains a very sore point with these students. 美國軍隊繼續駐留在韓國領土依然是令這些學生極其惱怒的事情。"]}]}]},"slice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（切下的食物）薄片，片；（蛋糕等的）小塊 ；水果切塊；部分，份；<非正式>例子；（體育運動中的）斜切球，削球，側旋球；（切片用的）薄刀，（鏟食物用的）鏟子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……切成薄片；切，割，劃；輕易快速穿過（空氣或水等）；削（球），斜切打；（無意中）打出弧線球；減少（時間、錢等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slice</b> <b>of</b> bread, meat, fruit, or other food is a thin piece that has been cut from a larger piece. (切下的食物) 薄片","examples":["Try to eat at least four slices of bread a day. 每天儘量吃至少4片面包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>slice</b> to refer to a part of a situation or activity. (情況或活動的) 部分","examples":["Fiction takes up a large slice of the publishing market. 小說佔出版市場的一大部分。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slice</b> bread, meat, fruit, or other food, you cut it into thin pieces. 把 (食物) 切成薄片","examples":["Helen sliced the cake. 海倫把蛋糕切成了薄片。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slice up</b> means the same as . 把 (食物) 切成薄片","examples":["I sliced up an onion. 我把洋蔥切成了片。"]}]}]},"spaghetti":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不可數）義大利式細麵條（一種細長實心的義大利麵食，常與醬汁同食）；（Spaghetti，首字母大寫）義大利語人名或姓氏，音譯“斯帕蓋蒂”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spaghetti</b> is a type of pasta. It looks like long pieces of string and is usually served with a sauce. 義大利式細麵條","examples":[]}]}]},"spade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鍬，鏟；（紙牌中的）黑桃（spades）；黑桃牌；<舊>黑人，黑鬼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用鍬挖（地），用鍬鏟（土）；把……弄實抹平"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spade</b> is a tool used for digging, with a flat metal blade and a long handle. 鍬","examples":["...a garden spade. …一把花園裡使用的鍬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spades</b> is one of the four suits in a deck of playing cards. Each card in the suit is marked with one or more black symbols: ♠. (撲克牌中的) 黑桃","examples":["...the ace of spades. …黑桃A。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>spade</b> is a playing card of this suit. 黑桃牌","examples":["He would have done better to play a spade now. 他要是現在出一張黑桃牌就更好了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to use a spade on 用鍬","examples":[]}]}]},"sprain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扭傷（關節）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"扭傷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sprain</b> a joint such as your ankle or wrist, you accidentally damage it by twisting it or bending it violently. 扭傷 (關節)","examples":["He fell and sprained his ankle. 他跌了一跤，扭傷了腳踝。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sprain</b> is the injury caused by spraining a joint. 扭傷","examples":["Rubin suffered a right ankle sprain when she rolled over on her ankle. 魯賓摔倒時身體壓到了腳踝上導致右腳踝扭傷。"]}]}]},"spice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香料，調味品；情趣，趣味；赤褐色；<北英格蘭>糖果；<罕>少許"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……增添趣味；在……中加香料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spice</b> is a part of a plant, or a powder made from that part, which you put in food to give it flavour. Cinnamon, ginger, and paprika are spices. 香料","examples":["...herbs and spices. …各種香草和香料。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spice</b> something that you say or do, you add excitement or interest to it. 給…增加趣味","examples":["They spiced their conversations and discussions with intrigue. 他們透過設謎為他們的談話和討論增加樂趣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spice up</b> means the same as . 給…增加趣味 (同)(spice)","examples":["Her publisher wants her to spice up her stories with sex. 她的出版商想要她用色情給她的故事增添趣味。"]}]}]},"snap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使咔嚓）斷裂，繃斷；（使啪地）開啟，關上，移動；厲聲說，怒氣衝衝地說；突然失控，精神崩潰；（狗等動物）突然咬；拍照，攝影；<美>使……終結；噼啪地響；打響指；<美>快速後傳（球）；用子母扣扣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喀嚓聲，啪嗒聲；快照，照片；<美>摁釦，搭扣；呼“同”牌遊戲；<美，非正式>容易的事；某種短時期的天氣；迅速的動作；（襠下後傳）發球；（風格或動作）充滿活力；不耐煩的語調（或樣子）；<北英格蘭>食物；薄脆餅乾；突然折斷"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"突然的，倉促的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<英>真巧啊，一模一樣；（呼“同”牌遊戲中的）“同！”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>snaps</b> or if you <b>snap</b> it, it breaks suddenly, usually with a sharp cracking noise. 使喀嚓折斷; 喀嚓折斷","examples":["He shifted his weight and a twig snapped. 他挪了挪身子，一根樹枝隨即喀嚓一聲折斷了。","The brake pedal had just snapped off. 制動踏板剛才突然斷裂了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>snap</b> something into a particular position, or if it <b>snaps</b> into that position, it moves quickly into that position, with a sharp sound. 使發出啪的一聲; 發出啪的一聲","examples":["He snapped the notebook shut. 他啪的一聲合上筆記本。","He snapped the cap on his ballpoint. 他吧嗒一聲扣上圓珠筆的筆帽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>snap</b> your <b>fingers</b>, you make a sharp sound by moving your middle finger quickly across your thumb, for example, in order to accompany music or to order someone to do something. 打響指","examples":["She had millions of listeners snapping their fingers to her first single. 數百萬的聽眾和著她的首張單曲打響指。","He snapped his fingers, and Wilson produced a sheet of paper. 他打了一個響指，威爾遜便拿出一張紙來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>snaps</b> <b>at</b> you, they speak to you in a sharp, unfriendly way. 聲色俱厲地說","examples":["\"Of course I don't know her,\" Roger snapped. “我當然不認識她，”羅傑惡聲惡氣地說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Snap</b> is also a noun. 喀嚓的斷裂聲","examples":["Every minute or so I could hear a snap, a crack and a crash as another tree went down. 幾乎每隔一分鐘，我就會聽見又有一棵樹倒下時發出的折斷聲、噼啪聲和塌倒聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Snap</b> is also a noun. 吧嗒聲","examples":["He shut the book with a snap and stood up. 他啪的一聲合上書，站了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Snap</b> is also a noun. 打響指","examples":["I could obtain with the snap of my fingers anything I chose. 只要打一下響指，我就可以得到我選中的任何東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>snap</b> is the same as a . 按扣","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>snap</b> is a photograph. 相片","examples":["...a snap my mother took last year. …我母親去年拍的一張相片。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>snaps</b>, or if something <b>snaps</b> inside them, they suddenly stop being calm and become very angry because the situation has become too tense or too difficult for them. (人) 突然發怒; (物) 突然爆發","examples":["He finally snapped when she prevented their children from visiting him one weekend. 當她阻止孩子們在一週末來探望他時，他終於失控發怒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an animal such as a dog <b>snaps</b> <b>at</b> you, it opens and shuts its jaws quickly near you, as if it were going to bite you. 作勢猛咬","examples":["His teeth clicked as he snapped at my ankle. 他作勢猛咬我的腳踝時，牙齒咔嚓作響。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snap</b> decision or action is one that is taken suddenly, often without careful thought. 倉促的","examples":["I think this is too important for a snap decision. 我認為此事非常重要，不宜倉促地做決定。"]}]}]},"spite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"惡意，怨恨；不顧，儘管；不由自主地"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"刁難，使惱怒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in spite of</b> to introduce a fact which makes the rest of the statement you are making seem surprising. 儘管","examples":["Josef Krips at the State Opera hired her in spite of the fact that she had never sung on stage. 國家歌劇院的約瑟夫•克里普斯僱傭了她，儘管她從未在臺上演唱過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>in spite of</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do it although you did not really intend to or expect to. 不由自主地","examples":["The blunt comment made Richard laugh in spite of himself. 那率直的評論使得理查德不由自主地笑了起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something cruel out of <b>spite</b>, you do it because you want to hurt or upset someone. 惡意","examples":["I refused her a divorce, out of spite I suppose. 我拒絕了她離婚的要求，我想是出於怨恨。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something cruel <b>to</b> <b>spite</b> someone, you do it in order to hurt or upset them. 存心傷害","examples":["Pantelaras was giving his art collection away for nothing, to spite Marie and her husband. 潘特拉拉斯將他的藝術收藏品無償贈送了，存心惹怒瑪麗和她的丈夫。"]}]}]},"spill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）灑出，潑出，溢位；（東西）倒出，灑落；湧出，蜂擁而出；（光線）透進，傾瀉在……上；向（某人）說出秘密；使（某人）從馬上（或腳踏車上）摔下來；（球賽中）掉球；（航海）減少（帆）的受風壓力（多指把帆放鬆）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"灑出（量），溢位（量）；（從馬、腳踏車上等的）摔下，跌下；<澳>職位空缺；（點火用的）紙捻，木片；小塞子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid <b>spills</b> or if you <b>spill</b> it, it accidentally flows over the edge of a container. 無意灑落; 意外溢位","examples":["Seventy thousand tons of oil spilled from the tanker. 7萬噸油從油輪漏出。","He always spilled the drinks. 他總是不小心把飲料給灑了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the contents of a bag, box, or other container <b>spill</b> or <b>are spilled</b>, they come out of the container onto a surface. 使散落; 散落","examples":["A number of bags had split and were spilling their contents. 許多包裂開了，裡面的東西正在散落出來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spill</b> is an amount of liquid that has spilled from a container. 灑落的液體","examples":["She wiped a spill of milkshake off the counter. 她擦掉櫃檯上灑落的奶昔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a splinter of wood or strip of twisted paper with which pipes, fires, etc, are lit (點菸、點火用的)木頭碎片或廢紙","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things <b>spill</b> out of a place, they come out of it in large numbers. 湧出","examples":["Tears began to spill out of the boy's eyes. 淚水開始從男孩的眼裡湧出。"]}]}]},"sprinkle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"撒，灑；用……點綴，在……中隨意穿插；零星分佈；下小雨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"少量，一點；稀疏小雨；（撒在糕餅上作裝飾用的）彩糖，糖屑（sprinkles）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sprinkle</b> a thing <b>with</b> something such as a liquid or powder, you scatter the liquid or powder over it. (給…) 灑 (液體); (給…) 撒 (粉末狀物)","examples":["Sprinkle the meat with salt and place in the pan. 給肉撒點鹽，然後放進平鍋裡。","At the festival, candles are blessed and sprinkled with holy water. 在節日裡，蠟燭被聖化並被灑上聖水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is sprinkled</b> <b>with</b> particular things, it has a few of them throughout it and they are far apart from each other. 零星分佈","examples":["Unfortunately, the text is sprinkled with errors. 遺憾的是，文字有零星的錯誤。"]}]}]},"spit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啐唾沫（常表示憤怒或鄙視）；吐出（食物，液體）；怒斥；（火，煮物）爆出火花，發出噼啪聲，（使）迸濺；（發怒時）發呼嚕呼嚕聲；下小雨；將烤肉扦子戳入（肉）中以便放在火上烤；表演說唱音樂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"唾液，口水；烤肉扦子；岬角，海岬；幾乎長得一模一樣的人；鍬深的泥土層；啐唾沫，吐痰，吐食物；沙嘴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spit</b> is the watery liquid produced in your mouth. You usually use <b>spit</b> to refer to an amount of it that has been forced out of someone's mouth. 口水","examples":["A trickle of spit collected at the corner of her mouth. 一小股口水積聚在了她的嘴角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spit</b> is a long rod which is pushed through a piece of meat and hung over an open fire to cook the meat. 烤肉扦子","examples":["She roasted the meat on a spit. 她在烤肉扦子上烤了那塊肉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the depth of earth cut by a spade; a spade's depth 一鐵鍬深的土; 一鐵鍬深","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>spits</b>, they force an amount of liquid out of their mouth, often to show hatred or contempt. 吐唾沫","examples":["The gang thought of hitting him too, but decided just to spit. 那個團伙也想到揍他，但決定只朝他吐唾沫。","They spat at me and taunted me. 他們又朝我吐唾沫又嘲弄我。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to utter (short sharp words or syllables), esp in a violent manner 粗暴地講(短句或音節)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to rain very lightly 下毛毛細雨","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spit</b> liquid or food somewhere, you force a small amount of it out of your mouth. 吐出","examples":["Spit out that gum and pay attention. 吐掉那口香糖，專心點。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one person is <b>the spitting image of</b> another, you mean that they look very similar. 與某人簡直一模一樣","examples":["Nina looks the spitting image of Sissy Spacek. 尼娜看上去簡直和茜茜•斯派塞克一模一樣。"]}]}]},"splash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（液體）稀里嘩啦地濺落，飛濺；朝……潑灑，使……濺溼；潑濺著水行進，拍打著水遊；以顯著版面刊載，以大篇幅報道；使有色塊，使有光斑；<英，非正式> 在（某物）上花很多錢"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"落水聲，濺潑聲；濺上的液體，濺灑後留下的汙漬；摻入飲料的少量液體；色塊，光斑；（報章等旨在招徠讀者的）重點文章；拍水，戲水；引人注目的效果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>splash</b> around or <b>splash</b> about in water, you hit or disturb the water in a noisy way, causing some of it to fly up into the air. 潑打戲水","examples":["A lot of people were in the water, swimming or simply splashing about. 很多人在水裡游泳或者只是戲水。","She could hear the voices of her friends as they splashed in a nearby rock pool. 她能聽到她的朋友們在附近的岩石泳池裡戲水的聲音。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>splash</b> a liquid somewhere or if it <b>splashes</b>, it hits someone or something and scatters in a lot of small drops. 使潑濺; 濺落","examples":["He closed his eyes tight, and splashed the water on his face. 他緊緊地閉上眼睛，把水潑到臉上。","A little wave, the first of many, splashed in my face. 層層波浪中的第一層小浪濺在了我的臉上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a magazine or newspaper <b>splashes</b> a story, it prints it in such a way that it is very noticeable. (報刊) 以顯眼方式刊登","examples":["The newspapers splashed the story all over their front pages. 各報都在頭版全版以顯眼的方式刊登了這個故事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>splash</b> is the sound made when something hits water or falls into it. 拍打水的聲音; 落入水的聲音","examples":["There was a splash and something fell clumsily into the water. 撲通一聲，什麼東西重重地掉進了水裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>splash</b> of a liquid is a small quantity of it that falls on something or is added to something. (少量液體的) 濺落; (少量液體的) 新增","examples":["Wallcoverings and floors should be able to withstand steam and splashes. 牆紙和地板應該能承受得住蒸汽和液體的潑濺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>splash</b> <b>of</b> colour is an area of a bright colour which contrasts strongly with the colours around it. (與周圍顏色形成鮮明對比的) 亮色塊","examples":["...shady walks punctuated by splashes of colour. …由鮮豔色彩點綴的條條林蔭小徑。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make a splash</b>, you become noticed or become popular because of something that you have done. 引起關注","examples":["Now she's made a splash in the television show \"Civil Wars.\" 如今她因在電視節目《內戰》中的出現而引起了人們的關注。"]}]}]},"spin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）快速旋轉；（使）急轉身；（頭感到）眩暈；紡紗，紡織；飛馳，疾馳；編故事；有傾向性地陳述；（用甩幹機或洗衣機）甩幹（衣服）；（昆蟲）吐（絲），結（網）；（用旋式誘餌）釣魚；播放（唱片）；拋（硬幣）；（球）旋轉；（用車床將金屬薄板）旋壓成形"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"高速旋轉；兜風；帶傾向性的解釋（或說法）；（政治上的）傾向性報道；（尤指板球、網球、斯諾克球中的）旋轉球；（飛機的）旋衝，螺旋下降；暈頭轉向，焦慮不安；（物理）核素總角動量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>spins</b> or if you <b>spin</b> it, it turns quickly around a central point. 轉動","examples":["The latest disks, used for small portable computers, spin 3,600 times a minute. 用於小型手提電腦的最新磁碟每分鐘轉動3600次。","He spun the wheel sharply and made a U turn in the middle of the road. 他猛打方向盤，在路中間掉了個頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>spin</b>, they make thread by twisting together pieces of a fibre such as wool or cotton using a device or machine. 紡; 紡線","examples":["Michelle will also spin a customer's wool fleece to specification at a cost of $2.25 an ounce. 米歇爾也將以每盎司$2.25的價格按照顧客的要求為其紡羊毛呢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spin</b> is also a noun. 旋轉","examples":["This driving mode allows you to move off in third gear to reduce wheel-spin in icy conditions. 這種駕駛方法可以讓你用三檔發動汽車以減少結冰情況下的車輪打滑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone puts a certain <b>spin</b> on an event or situation, they interpret it and try to present it in a particular way. (特意做的) 詮釋與宣傳","examples":["He interpreted the vote as support for the constitution and that is the spin his supporters are putting on the results today. 他把這次投票結果解釋為對憲法的支援，這也是他的支持者們對今天的結果所做的詮釋與宣傳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In politics, <b>spin</b> is the way in which political parties try to present everything they do in a positive way to the public and the media. (政治) 粉飾","examples":["The public is sick of spin and tired of promises. 公眾厭倦了粉飾和許諾。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you go for <b>a spin</b> or take a car for <b>a spin</b>, you make a short trip in a car just to enjoy yourself. 兜風","examples":["Tom Wright celebrated his 99th birthday by going for a spin in his sporty Mazda. 湯姆•賴特開著他的運動型馬自達車出去兜風以慶祝其99歲生日。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a game such as tennis or baseball, if you put <b>spin</b> on a ball, you deliberately make it spin rapidly when you hit it or throw it. (擊球或投球時故意使球做出的) 快速旋轉","examples":["He threw it back again, putting a slight spin on the ball. 他把球略帶旋轉地又投擲了回去。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your head <b>is spinning</b>, you feel unsteady or confused, for example because you are drunk, ill, or excited. 眩暈","examples":["My head was spinning from the wine. 當時我因喝了酒而感到眩暈。"]}]}]},"spray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噴霧液體，噴劑；噴霧器；噴，噴塗；噴霧狀物；浪花，飛沫；（用作裝飾的）小樹枝，小花枝；（戴在身上的）一簇花，枝狀飾物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"噴，噴灑（液體）；（使）飛濺，（使）飛散；噴農藥；在……上噴塗料（或油漆）；向……掃射（子彈）；用於體育運動中踢（或擊、扔）（方向不定或不準的球）；撒尿（以示領地佔有）；（臭鼬）用臭液弄溼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spray</b> is a lot of small drops of water which are being thrown into the air. 水霧","examples":["The moon was casting a rainbow through the spray from the waterfall. 月亮在瀑布濺起的水霧中映出了一道彩虹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spray</b> is a liquid kept under pressure in a can or other container, which you can force out in very small drops. 噴劑","examples":["...hair spray. …頭髮噴劑"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>spray</b> is a piece of equipment for spraying water or another liquid, especially over growing plants. 噴霧器","examples":["Farmers can use the spray to kill weeds without harming the soy crop. 農民們能用噴霧器來除草而不傷大豆作物。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a small decorative bouquet or corsage of flowers and foliage (用作裝飾的)花枝束","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spray</b> a liquid somewhere or if it <b>sprays</b> somewhere, drops of the liquid cover a place or shower someone. 噴 (液體); (液體) 噴出","examples":["A sprayer hooked to a tractor can spray five gallons onto ten acres. 掛在拖拉機上的噴霧器用五加侖液量能噴灑十英畝地。","Inmates threw bricks at prison officers who were spraying them with a hose. 囚犯們朝那些用水管向他們噴水的獄警們拋擲磚頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a lot of small things <b>spray</b> somewhere or if something <b>sprays</b> them, they are scattered somewhere with a lot of force. 使濺出; 濺出","examples":["A shower of mustard seeds sprayed into the air and fell into the grass. 許多芥籽濺到空中，然後掉進草地裡。","The intensity of the blaze shattered windows, spraying glass on the streets below. 熊熊烈焰燒碎了窗戶，玻璃碎片飛濺到了下面的街道上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>sprays</b> bullets somewhere, they fire a lot of bullets at a group of people or things. 掃射","examples":["He ran to the top of the building, spraying bullets into shoppers below. 他衝向樓頂，向下面的購物者掃射。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>is sprayed</b>, it is painted using paint kept under pressure in a container. 噴漆","examples":["The bare metal was sprayed with several coats of primer. 裸露的金屬被噴了幾層底漆。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When someone <b>sprays</b> against insects, they cover plants or crops with a chemical which prevents insects from feeding on them. 給 (作物等) 噴藥; 噴藥","examples":["He doesn't spray against pests or diseases. 他沒有噴農藥來防治害蟲或疾病。","Confine the use of insecticides to the evening and do not spray plants that are in flower. 只限晚間使用殺蟲劑，並且不要對花期植物噴藥。"]}]}]},"spy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"間諜，密探；暗中監視者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"從事間諜活動；突然看見，認出；秘密監視；探明，查明"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（衛星、飛機）執行間諜任務的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spy</b> is a person whose job is to find out secret information about another country or organization. 間諜","examples":["He was jailed for five years as an alleged spy. 他被指控為間諜而被監禁了5年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"從事間諜活動","examples":["...a ten-year sentence for spying. …因從事間諜活動被判的10年監禁。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spy</b> satellite or <b>spy</b> plane obtains secret information about another country by taking photographs from the sky. 承擔間諜任務的 (衛星、飛機)","examples":["...pictures from unmanned spy planes operated by the U.S. military. …美國軍方操控的無人間諜飛機拍攝到的圖片。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>spies</b> <b>for</b> a country or organization tries to find out secret information about another country or organization. (為某國、某組織) 從事間諜活動","examples":["The agent spied for East Germany for more than twenty years. 該特工為東德從事了二十多年的間諜活動。","East and West are still spying on one another. 東方和西方仍在相互暗中監視著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>spy on</b> someone, you watch them secretly. 秘密監視","examples":["That day he spied on her while pretending to work on the shrubs. 那天他假裝修剪灌木，卻秘密地監視著她。"]}]}]},"stadium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體育場，運動場；（古希臘或古羅馬的）競走跑道，戰車賽道；斯塔德（古希臘或古羅馬長度單位，約185米）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stadium</b> is a large sports field with rows of seats all around it. (周圍有看臺的) 體育場","examples":["...a baseball stadium. …一個棒球體育場。"]}]}]},"stab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用刀等銳器）刺，戳，捅；（用手指或尖物）戳，捅，刺；（疼痛或痛苦的東西）刺痛；（話語）刺傷，刺痛；突然感到（一陣不愉快或負面的感情）；（迅速地）擊（球），踢（球）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺，戳，捅，刺（或戳、捅）的傷口；突然一陣劇痛（或難受的感覺）；<非正式>嘗試，企圖；（流行音樂）樂節間的斷音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>stabs</b> you, they push a knife or sharp object into your body. (用刀等利器) 刺; 捅","examples":["Somebody stabbed him in the stomach. 有人刺了他的腹部。","Dean tried to stab him with a screwdriver. 迪安試圖用一把螺絲刀捅他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stab</b> something or <b>stab at</b> it, you push at it with your finger or with something pointed that you are holding. (用手指或手中尖物) 戳; 捅; 按","examples":["Bess stabbed a slice of cucumber. 貝斯戳起一片黃瓜。","Goldstone flipped through the pages and stabbed his thumb at the paragraph he was looking for. 戈德斯通快速翻動書頁，用拇指按住他正在尋找的段落。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>a stab at</b> something, you try to do it. 嘗試","examples":["Several tennis stars have had a stab at acting. 幾位網球明星曾嘗試過演戲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a sudden, usually unpleasant feeling as <b>a stab of</b> that feeling. 刺痛","examples":["...a stab of pain just above his eye. …他眼睛上方的一陣刺痛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has stabbed</b> you <b>in the back</b>, you mean that they have done something very harmful to you when you thought that you could trust them. You can refer to an action of this kind as <b>a stab in the back</b>. 在背後捅某人一刀","examples":["She felt betrayed, as though her daughter had stabbed her in the back. 她感到被出賣了，彷彿是她的女兒在背後捅了她一刀。"]}]}]},"statue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（石或金屬做的動物或人的）雕像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>statue</b> is a large sculpture of a person or an animal, made of stone or metal. (石或金屬做的動物或人的) 雕像","examples":["...a bronze statue of an Arabian horse. …一座阿拉伯馬青銅雕像。"]}]}]},"stepchild":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼子或繼女，配偶前次婚姻所生的孩子；<喻>受到冷落、不受重視的人或事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>stepchild</b> is a child that was born to their husband or wife during a previous relationship. 繼子; 繼女","examples":[]}]}]},"stepmother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼母，後母"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>stepmother</b> is the woman who has married their father after the death or divorce of their mother. 繼母","examples":[]}]}]},"stare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"凝視，盯著看；瞪眼看，茫然地看；（事物）惹眼，顯眼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"凝視，注視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stare</b> <b>at</b> someone or something, you look at them for a long time. 盯著看; 凝視","examples":["Tamara stared at him in disbelief, shaking her head. 塔瑪拉搖著頭不相信地盯著他看。","Ben continued to stare out the window. 本繼續凝視著窗外。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stare</b> is also a noun. 盯著看; 凝視","examples":["Hlasek gave him a long, cold stare. 赫拉塞克冷冷地盯著他看了很久。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation or the answer to a problem <b>is staring</b> you <b>in the face</b>, it is very obvious, although you may not be immediately aware of it. (形勢、答案) 明擺在某人面前","examples":["Then the answer hit me. It had been staring me in the face ever since Lullington. 之後我突然想到了這個答案。自路林頓起這答案就一直明擺在我面前。"]}]}]},"squeeze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擠壓，捏；擠出，榨出（液體等）；（使）擠入，塞入；為……擠出時間（squeeze someone/something in）；排擠出（squeeze someone/something out）；敲詐勒索，榨取；嚴格限制，緊縮（資金）；好不容易取得，勉強成功；緊緊閉上雙眼；扣扳機射擊，打一整發（子彈）；拍照；（橋牌）逼（對方）放棄一張贏墩牌，逼牌"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擠壓，捏；擁擠，塞滿；擠出來的少量事物；緊縮，拮据；<美，非正式> 男朋友，女朋友；<非正式> 勒索（或敲詐）的錢；擁抱；（橋牌）緊逼打法（逼對手扔掉一張重要的牌）；壓模，拓印；（棒球）搶分戰術； <舊> 擁擠的社交舞會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>squeeze</b> something, you press it firmly, usually with your hands. (常指用手) 擠壓; 緊捏","examples":["He squeezed her arm reassuringly. 他安慰地捏了捏她的手臂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>squeeze</b> a liquid or a soft substance out of an object, you get the liquid or substance out by pressing the object. 擠; 壓榨 (液體等)","examples":["Joe put the plug in the sink and squeezed some detergent over the dishes. 喬把塞子插進水槽，往盤子上擠了些洗潔精。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>squeeze</b> a person or thing somewhere or if they <b>squeeze</b> there, they manage to get through or into a small space. 塞進; 擠進","examples":["They lowered him gradually into the cockpit. Somehow they squeezed him in the tight space, and strapped him in. 他們緩緩地把他向下放入駕駛艙，設法把他塞進那狹小的空間，並給繫上了安全帶。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Squeeze</b> is also a noun. 緊捏; 擠壓","examples":["I liked her way of reassuring you with a squeeze of the hand. 我喜歡她捏捏手來安慰人的方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that getting a number of people into a small space is <b>a squeeze</b>, you mean that it is only just possible for them all to get into it. 滿塞","examples":[]}]}]},"stereo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立體聲，立體聲效果；立體聲音響裝置（器材）；（攝影）立體視鏡；（印刷）鉛版（stereotype 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"立體聲的（stereophonic 的簡稱）；立體的，體視鏡的，有立體感覺的（stereoscopic 的簡稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stereo</b> is used to describe a sound system in which the sound is played through two speakers. Compare . 立體聲的","examples":["...loudspeakers that give all-around stereo sound. …發出環繞立體聲的喇叭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stereo</b> is a CD player with two speakers. 立體音響","examples":[]}]}]},"stepfather":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼父（母親再婚後的丈夫，對子女而言並非親生父親）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>stepfather</b> is the man who has married their mother after the death or divorce of their father. 繼父","examples":[]}]}]},"steady":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平穩的，穩步的，持續的；穩定的，恆定的；穩固的，牢固的；沉著的，冷靜的；（人）穩重的，可靠的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使平穩，穩住；（使）穩定，（使）固定（一段時間）；（使）鎮定，（使）冷靜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>關係確定的情侶；（支撐大篷車或其他車輛的）支架，撐竿"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"當心，冷靜點"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"穩定地，持續地，穩固地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>steady</b> situation continues or develops gradually without any interruptions and is not likely to change quickly. 穩定的","examples":["Despite the steady progress of building work, the campaign against it is still going strong. 儘管建築工程穩步進行，反工運動卻仍然高漲。","The improvement in standards has been steady and persistent, but has attracted little comment from educationalists. 雖然標準在持續穩步提高，但教育者並未對此有何評論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object is <b>steady</b>, it is firm and does not shake or move around. 平穩的","examples":["Get as close to the subject as you can and hold the camera steady. 儘可能靠近物件，拿穩相機。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you look at someone or speak to them in a <b>steady</b> way, you look or speak in a calm, controlled way. 鎮定的","examples":["\"Well, go on,\" said Camilla, her voice fairly steady. “嗯，繼續吧。”卡米拉說道，聲音相當鎮定。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a person as <b>steady</b>, you mean that they are sensible and reliable. 可靠的","examples":["He was firm and steady unlike other men she knew. 他堅定、可靠，和她所認識的其他男人不同。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"穩定地","examples":["Relax as much as possible and keep breathing steadily. 儘量放鬆，保持呼吸平穩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"鎮定地","examples":["He moved back a little and stared steadily at Elaine. 他往後退了點，鎮定地盯著依萊恩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>steady</b> something or if it <b>steadies</b>, it stops shaking or moving around. 使平穩; 平穩","examples":["Two men were on the bridge-deck, steadying a ladder. 兩人站在船橋甲板上，扶穩一個梯子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>steady</b> <b>yourself</b>, you control your voice or expression, so that people will think that you are calm and not nervous. 使鎮定","examples":["Somehow she steadied herself and murmured, \"Have you got a cigarette?\" 她設法使自己鎮定下來，並低聲問道,“你有香菸嗎？”"]}]}]},"stocking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（女式）長筒襪；（裝禮物用的）聖誕襪；<舊> 男襪；（尤指用於治療靜脈病的）襪狀彈性繃帶；（馬小腿部的）白斑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指為某個特定時刻或目的而）備貨，囤積 （stock的現在分詞形式）；儲存，貯備；（為銷售而）備有，存有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stockings</b> are items of women's clothing which fit closely over their feet and legs. Stockings are usually made of nylon and are held in place by garters. 長襪","examples":["...a pair of nylon stockings. …一雙尼龍長襪。"]}]}]},"sting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（昆蟲、動植物）叮，刺，蜇；（使）刺痛，（使）產生劇痛；向……索要驚人高價，敲詐；（使）生氣，（使）心煩；刺激"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺傷處，蜇傷處；（植物、水母等的）刺毛； 刺痛，灼痛；（身體或心靈的）劇痛，痛苦；（警察為抓住罪犯而設計的）圈套，騙局；<美>（罪犯詐騙錢財的）騙局，詭計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a plant, animal, or insect <b>stings</b> you, a sharp part of it, usually covered with poison, is pushed into your skin so that you feel a sharp pain. 刺; 叮","examples":["The nettles stung their legs. 蕁麻刺了他們的腿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>stings</b>, or if a substance <b>stings</b> it, you feel a sharp pain there. 使刺痛","examples":["His cheeks were stinging from the icy wind. 他的雙頰被冰冷的寒風刺痛了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone's remarks <b>sting</b> you, they make you feel hurt and annoyed. (話語) 刺傷","examples":["Some of the criticism has stung him. 有些批評刺傷了他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>sting</b> of an insect or animal is the part that stings you. 蟄刺","examples":["Remove the bee sting with tweezers. 用鑷子拔掉蜜蜂的蟄刺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel a <b>sting</b>, you feel a sharp pain in your skin or other part of your body. 刺; 叮","examples":["This won't hurt – you will just feel a little sting. 不會痛的–你只會覺得被輕輕刺了一下。"]}]}]},"stool":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"凳子；大便，糞便；（生長新芽的）根株，母株；<美>（用來誘捕鳥的）囮子；廁所"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（為了長出新芽）從靠近地面處砍斷（植物）；（植物）從根株長出新苗；引誘，誘捕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stool</b> is a seat with legs but no support for your arms or back. 凳子","examples":["O'Brien sat on a bar stool and leaned his elbows on the counter. 奧布賴恩坐在酒吧凳上，肘部依在櫃檯上。"]}]}]},"stitch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（縫紉的）針腳，一針；（縫合傷口的）縫線；縫紉法，編結法；（肋部）突然劇痛；<非正式>（最少的）一件衣服，一塊布；（編織的）一針"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"縫，縫補；縫合（傷口）；<英，非正式>操縱局勢使……處於劣勢，陷害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stitch</b> cloth, you use a needle and thread to join two pieces together or to make a decoration. 縫","examples":["Fold the fabric and stitch the two layers together. 把布料對摺，將兩層縫在一起。","We stitched incessantly. 我們縫個不停。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When doctors <b>stitch</b> a wound, they use a special needle and thread to sew the skin together. 縫合 (傷口)","examples":["Jill washed and stitched the wound. 吉爾清洗並縫合了傷口。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stitches</b> are the short pieces of thread that have been sewn in a piece of cloth. 針腳","examples":["...a row of straight stitches. …一排直直的針腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In knitting and crochet, a <b>stitch</b> is a loop made by one turn of wool around a knitting needle or crochet hook. 一針","examples":["Her mother counted the stitches on her knitting needles. 她的母親數了數編織針上的針數。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you sew or knit something in a particular <b>stitch</b>, you sew or knit in a way that produces a particular pattern. 編織法","examples":["The design can be worked in cross stitch. 該圖案可以用十字針法編織出來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>stitch</b> is a piece of thread that has been used to sew the skin of a wound together. (縫合傷口的) 一針","examples":["He had six stitches in a head wound. 他頭部的傷口縫了6針。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>stitch</b> is a sharp pain in your side, usually caused by running or laughing a lot. (跑步或大笑引起的) 肋部劇痛","examples":["One of them was laughing so much he got a stitch. 他們當中有一個人笑得肋部都疼了。"]}]}]},"staff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"全體員工，全體僱員；<美>（大、中、小學的）管理人員，行政人員；（軍隊的）全體參謀人員；陸軍上士；手杖，柺杖；權杖，笏；旗杆；（測繪）標杆，標尺；<英>（鐘錶的）小軸杆；<英>（鐵路的）路籤；五線譜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"職員的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……配備員工；是……的職員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>staff</b> of an organization are the people who work for it. 全體職員","examples":["The staff were very good. 員工們都很棒。","The outpatient programme has a staff of six people. 這個門診部有6名員工。","...staff members. …職工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People who are part of a particular staff are often referred to as <b>staff</b>. 員工","examples":["10 staff were allocated to the task. 10名員工被分派做這項任務。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an organization <b>is staffed</b> <b>by</b> particular people, they are the people who work for it. 擔當 (某機構的) 職員","examples":["They are staffed by volunteers. 他們的員工都是志願者。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"配備了職員的","examples":["The house allocated to them was pleasant and spacious, and well staffed. 分給他們的房子既舒適又寬敞，員工也配備良好。"]}]}]},"strategy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指為獲得某物制定長期的）策略，行動計劃；戰略，戰略學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strategy</b> is a general plan or set of plans intended to achieve something, especially over a long period. 策略","examples":["The energy secretary will present the strategy tomorrow afternoon. 能源部長將於明天下午提出該策略。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Strategy</b> is the art of planning the best way to gain an advantage or achieve success, especially in war. 戰略","examples":["I've just been explaining the basic principles of strategy to my generals. 我剛才一直在向我的將軍們解釋戰略的基本原則。"]}]}]},"stir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攪拌，攪和（液體等物質）；激發，打動；（情感）逐漸產生，萌發；（使）行動，活動；（使）微動；離開；<英，非正式>挑撥，惹是生非"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"攪動，攪拌；激動（情緒），憤怒（情緒）；微動，顫動；輕微的感覺；監獄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stir</b> a liquid or other substance, you move it around or mix it in a container using something such as a spoon. 攪動; 攪拌","examples":["Stir the soup for a few seconds. 把湯攪動幾秒鐘。","There was Mrs. Bellingham, stirring sugar into her tea. 貝林漢姆太太在那兒把糖加入茶中攪拌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>stirs</b> or if the wind <b>stirs</b> it, it moves gently in the wind. 使輕輕拂動; 輕輕拂動","examples":["Palm trees stir in the soft Pacific breeze. 棕櫚樹在太平洋和煦的微風裡輕輕搖動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a particular memory, feeling, or mood <b>stirs</b> or <b>is stirred</b> <b>in</b> you, you begin to think about it or feel it. 喚起; 萌生","examples":["Then a memory stirs in you and you start feeling anxious. 接著你腦海中湧現出一段回憶，並開始感到不安。","Amy remembered the anger he had stirred in her. 艾米記得他曾惹自己生氣。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stir</b>, you move slightly, for example because you are uncomfortable or beginning to wake up. 微動","examples":["Eileen shook him, and he started to stir. 艾琳搖了搖他，他開始動了動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do not <b>stir</b> <b>from</b> a place, you do not move from it. 離開","examples":["She had not stirred from the house that evening. 她那天晚上沒有離開過那座房子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event causes a <b>stir</b>, it causes great excitement, shock, or anger among people. 轟動; 憤怒","examples":["His movie has caused a stir. 他的電影引起了轟動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the act or an instance of stirring or the state of being stirred 攪動; 撥動","examples":[]}]}]},"studio":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錄音室，播音室，演播室；（電影）攝影棚，電影公司，電影製片廠；（畫家、攝影師、雕塑家等的）工作室；（舞蹈）練習室；單室公寓房；（公司新產品的）設計室，工作室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>studio</b> is a room where a painter, photographer, or designer works. 工作室","examples":["She was in her studio again, painting onto a large canvas. 她又在她的工作室裡了，在一塊大帆布上畫畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>studio</b> is a room where radio or television programmes are recorded, CDs are produced, or movies are made. 演播室; 製作室","examples":["She's much happier performing live than in a recording studio. 她現場表演比在錄音棚裡更開心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can also refer to film-making or recording companies as <b>studios</b>. 電影公司; 錄音公司","examples":["She wrote to Paramount Studios and asked if they would audition her. 她寫了信給派拉蒙電影公司，問他們是否能讓她試鏡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>studio</b> or a <b>studio</b> apartment is a small apartment with one room for living and sleeping in, a kitchen, and a bathroom. You can also talk about a <b>studio apartment</b>. 單間公寓","examples":["Home for a couple of years was a studio apartment. 幾年來的家就是一個單間公寓。"]}]}]},"suburb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"城郊，近郊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>suburb</b> <b>of</b> a city or large town is a smaller area which is part of the city or large town but is outside its centre. 市郊","examples":["Anna was born in 1923 in a suburb of Philadelphia. 安娜1923年出生在費城市郊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you live <b>in the</b> <b>suburbs</b>, you live in an area of houses outside the centre of a city or large town. 郊區","examples":["His family lived in the suburbs. 他家住在郊區。"]}]}]},"structure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結構，構造；結構體，（尤指）大型建築物；周密安排，精心組織；機構，組織，體系"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"計劃，組織，安排"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>structure</b> <b>of</b> something is the way in which it is made, built, or organized. 結構","examples":["The typical family structure of Freud's patients involved two parents and two children. 弗洛伊德的病人們的典型家庭結構包括一對父母和兩個孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>structure</b> is something that consists of parts connected together in an ordered way. 結構體","examples":["The feet are highly specialized structures made up of 26 small delicate bones. 腳是非常特殊的、由26塊細小骨頭組成的結構體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>structure</b> is something that has been built. 建築物","examples":["About half of those funds has gone to repair public roads, structures, and bridges. 那些資金中大約一半用於維修公路、建築物和橋樑。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>structure</b> something, you arrange it in a careful, organized pattern or system. 精心安排; 系統組織","examples":["By structuring the course this way, we're forced to produce something the companies think is valuable. 透過這樣精心安排程序，我們不得不生產出公司認為有價值的東西。"]}]}]},"stomach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胃；腹部；（低階動物的）類胃器官；（反芻動物的）四胃之一；心窩，內臟； 食慾，胃口；（對有衝突、困難或不快之事的）慾望，傾向；（做困難或不愉快的事所需的）意願，勇氣，決心；（對令人反胃的東西的）承受能力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"忍受，承受；吃得下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>stomach</b> is the organ inside your body where food is digested before it moves into the intestines. 胃","examples":["He had an upset stomach. 他胃部不適。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the front part of your body below your waist as your <b>stomach</b>. 肚子","examples":["The children lay down on their stomachs. 孩子們俯身趴著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the front part of your body below your waist feels uncomfortable because you are feeling worried or frightened, you can refer to it as your <b>stomach</b>. 心窩","examples":["His stomach was in knots. 他的心揪得緊緊的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has a strong <b>stomach</b>, you mean that they are not disgusted by things that disgust most other people. 忍耐力","examples":["Surgery often demands actual physical strength, as well as the possession of a strong stomach. 外科手術常常要求有實際體力，也要有很強的忍耐力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cannot <b>stomach</b> something, you cannot accept it because you dislike it or disapprove of it. 忍受","examples":["I could never stomach the cruelty involved in the wounding of animals. 我永遠無法忍受傷害動物的殘暴行為。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on an empty stomach</b>, you do it without having eaten. 空腹","examples":["Avoid drinking on an empty stomach. 避免空腹喝酒。"]}]}]},"substance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"物質，材料；主旨，主要內容；重要性；真實性，可信性；毒品；財富，財產；實質，（實在的）東西；<哲> 實體；可靠，穩定；（哲）實體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>substance</b> is a solid, powder, liquid, or gas with particular properties. 物質","examples":["There's absolutely no regulation of cigarettes to make sure that they don't include poisonous substances. 絕對沒有確保香菸不含有毒物質的規定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Substance</b> is the quality of being important or significant. 實質","examples":["It's questionable whether anything of substance has been achieved. 是否已取得任何實質性的進展值得質疑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The substance of</b> what someone says or writes is the main thing that they are trying to say. 要旨","examples":["The substance of his discussions doesn't really matter. 他討論的要旨實際並不重要。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something has no <b>substance</b>, you mean that it is not true. 正確性","examples":["There is no substance in any of these allegations. 這些指控沒有一個是正確的。"]}]}]},"strength":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體力，力量；實力，影響力；長處，優勢；意志力，毅力；（情感或意見的）強烈程度；（物體或物質的）強度；（食物、藥等的）濃度，（酒的）烈度；（風等的）速度，力度；人數，人力；（貨幣的）價值，堅挺程度；球隊的板凳深度，替補隊員的水平；<文>力量源泉；（手中所持好牌數目和花色的）牌力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>strength</b> is the physical energy that you have, which gives you the ability to perform various actions, such as lifting or moving things. 力量","examples":["She has always been encouraged to swim to build up the strength of her muscles. 她總是被鼓勵去游泳以增強肌肉力量。","He threw it forward with all his strength. 他使盡全部的力氣把它向前扔出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>strength</b> in a difficult situation is their confidence or courage. (困境中的) 勇氣","examples":["Something gave me the strength to overcome the difficulty. 有件事給了我克服困難的勇氣。","He copes incredibly well. His strength is an inspiration to me in my life. 他處理得非常好。他的勇氣對我的人生是一種鼓舞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>strength</b> of an object or material is its ability to be treated roughly, or to carry heavy weights, without being damaged or destroyed. 強度","examples":["He checked the strength of the cables. 他檢查了纜繩的強度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>strength</b> of a person, organization, or country is the power or influence that they have. 實力","examples":["America values its economic leadership, and the political and military strength that goes with it. 美國重視它的經濟領導地位以及與其相配的政治和軍事實力。","The alliance, in its first show of strength, drew a hundred thousand-strong crowd to a rally. 該聯盟在首次實力展示時吸引了多達10萬的人群來參加集會。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>strength</b> <b>of</b> a feeling, opinion, or belief, you are talking about how deeply it is felt or believed by people, or how much they are influenced by it. (感情、觀點或信念的) 強烈程度","examples":["He was surprised at the strength of his own feeling. 他對自己感情的強烈程度感到吃驚。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Someone's <b>strengths</b> are the qualities and abilities that they have which are an advantage to them, or which make them successful. 長處","examples":["Take into account your own strengths and weaknesses. 考慮一下你自己的長處和弱點。","Tact was never Mr. Moore's strength. 老練從來不是穆爾先生的長處。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>strength</b> of a currency, economy, or industry, you mean that its value or success is steady or increasing. (貨幣、經濟或行業的) 走強","examples":["...the long-term competitive strength of the economy. …該經濟的有競爭力的長期走強。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>strength</b> of a group of people is the total number of people in it. 人數","examples":["...elite forces, comprising about one-tenth of the strength of the army. …約佔軍隊總人數1/10的精銳部隊。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"The <b>strength</b> of a wind, current, or other force is its power or speed. 力","examples":["Its oscillation depends on the strength of the gravitational field. 它的擺動取決於重力場的力。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"The <b>strength</b> of a drink, chemical, or drug is the amount of the particular substance in it that gives it its particular effect. 濃度","examples":["It is very alcoholic, sometimes near the strength of port. 它的酒精度很高，有時接近於波爾圖葡萄酒的濃度。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or organization <b>goes from strength to strength</b>, they become more and more successful or confident. 越來越興旺","examples":["A decade later, the company has gone from strength to strength. 10年後，該公司越來越興旺了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a team or army is at <b>full strength</b>, all the members that it needs or usually has are present. 滿員","examples":["He needed more time to bring U.S. forces there up to full strength. 他需要更多的時間使駐紮在那裡的美國部隊達到滿員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing is done <b>on the strength of</b> another, it is done because of the influence of that other thing. 憑藉","examples":["He was elected to power on the strength of his charisma. 他憑藉個人魅力當選。"]}]}]},"suck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸，吮，啜；含在嘴裡吸食；抽，吸（空氣或液體）；（空氣或液體的壓力）將……捲入，吞沒；使捲入；<非正式>糟糕，差勁；收緊，收縮（身體某部分）；把（空氣或煙）吸進肺部；吸納，吸收，吸取；巴結；（水泵）空抽"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吮，吸，啜；（水流的）沖刷聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>suck</b> something, you hold it in your mouth and pull at it with the muscles in your cheeks and tongue, for example in order to get liquid out of it. 吮吸","examples":["They waited in silence and sucked their sweets. 他們靜靜地等著，吮著糖果。","He sucked on his cigarette. 他吸了吸他的香菸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>sucks</b> a liquid, gas, or object in a particular direction, it draws it there with a powerful force. 吸 (物體); 抽 (液體、氣體)","examples":["The pollution-control team is at the scene and is due to start sucking up oil any time now. 這個汙染控制小組已在現場，隨時可以開始抽油。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are sucked</b> <b>into</b> a bad situation, you are unable to prevent yourself from becoming involved in it. 使捲入","examples":["...the extent to which they have been sucked into the cycle of violence. …他們被捲入暴力迴圈的程度。"]}]}]},"strip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"除去，撕掉（外皮或表層）；奪去，剝奪（地位，權力，財產）；脫衣服，脫光……的衣服；表演脫衣舞；為（奶牛）收奶；拆卸，拆開（機器、車輛或引擎 ）；<美>拆散（汽車等）賣零件；使空無一物，搬光（傢俱、裝置等）；（使）（螺絲或齒輪）受損；（為利潤）出售（公司資產）；分離（債券的）息票使二者分開出售；（子彈出膛時因膛面磨損而）不旋轉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（紙、金屬、織物等）條，帶；帶狀地帶；<英>（比賽時穿的）隊服，球衣；商業街；脫衣舞；連環漫畫；<英>（定時播出的）廣播節目；飛機跑道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strip</b> <b>of</b> something such as paper, cloth, or food is a long, narrow piece of it. (紙、布或食物的) 條","examples":["...a new kind of manufactured wood made by pressing strips of wood together and baking them. …一種透過把木條擠壓並烘乾而製成的新型人造木材。","The simplest rag-rugs are made with strips of fabric braided together. 這些最簡單的碎布地毯是由織物條編織而成的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>strip</b> <b>of</b> land or water is a long narrow area of it. 狹長 (地帶或水域)","examples":["The coastal cities of Liguria sit on narrow strips of land lying under steep mountains. 利古里亞的那些海濱城市坐落在陡峭山脈下的狹長地帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>strip</b> is a long street in a city or town, where there are a lot of stores, restaurants, and hotels. 商業街","examples":["...Goff's Charcoal Hamburgers on Lover's Lane, a busy commercial strip in North Dallas. …在北達拉斯的一條繁忙的商業街——“情人巷”上的戈夫炭烤漢堡店。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In a newspaper or magazine, a <b>strip</b> is a series of drawings which tell a story. The words spoken by the characters are often written on the drawings. 連環畫","examples":["...the Doonesbury strip. …杜恩斯伯利的連環畫。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the act or an instance of undressing or of performing a striptease 脫衣; 脫衣舞表演","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>strip</b>, you take off your clothes. 脫衣服","examples":["They stripped completely, and lay and turned in the damp grass. 他們脫光了衣服，躺在潮溼的草地上翻滾。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Strip off</b> means the same as . 脫衣服","examples":["The children were brazenly stripping off and leaping into the sea. 這些孩子們那時正無所顧忌地脫掉衣服，跳進海里。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Strip down</b> means the same as . 拆卸","examples":["In five years I had to strip the water pump down four times. 在5年裡我不得不拆卸了那個水泵4次。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is stripped</b>, their clothes are taken off by another person, for example in order to search for hidden or illegal things. 脫掉…的衣服","examples":["One prisoner claimed he'd been dragged to a cell, stripped, and beaten. 一個犯人聲稱他曾被拖進一間牢房，被脫掉衣服毆打。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>strip</b> something means to remove everything that covers it. 剝離","examples":["After Mike left for work I stripped the beds and vacuumed the carpets. 邁克去上班後，我揭下了床罩並吸了地毯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>strip</b> an engine or a piece of equipment, you take it to pieces so that it can be cleaned or repaired. 拆卸","examples":["Volvo's three-man team stripped the car and treated it to a restoration. 沃爾沃的3人小組拆了那輛汽車並對它進行了修復。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>strip</b> someone <b>of</b> their property, rights, or titles means to take those things away from them. 剝奪 (財產、權利); 撤銷 (頭銜)","examples":["The soldiers have stripped the civilians of their passports, and every other type of document. 那些士兵們已經奪走了市民的護照以及所有其他證件。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut or divide into strips 切成或分成條","examples":[]}]}]},"style":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方式，作風；款式，樣式；（尤指服裝上的）風尚，流行式樣；風格，體；輕鬆優雅的方式；生活方式；髮型；氣派，優雅格調；文風，文體；稱號，稱謂；（植）（花的）花柱；（無脊椎動物的）尾片，尾須"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設計，給……造型；稱呼，命名；使合潮流；用刻刀作裝飾畫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>style</b> of something is the general way in which it is done or presented, which often shows the attitudes of the people involved. 方式","examples":["Our children's different needs and learning styles created many problems. 我們孩子們不同的需要和學習方式引起了許多問題。","Belmont Park is a broad sweeping track which will suit the European style of running. 貝爾蒙特公園是一條寬闊的弧形跑道，它將會適合歐式的跑步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people or places have <b>style</b>, they are fashionable and elegant. 風度; 格調","examples":["Boston, you have to admit, has style. 你得承認波士頓很有格調。","Both love doing things in style. 兩人都喜愛有風度地做事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>style</b> of a product is its design. 款式","examples":["His 50 years of experience have given him strong convictions about style. 他50年的經驗已使他對款式有著堅定的主張。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In the arts, a particular <b>style</b> is characteristic of a particular period or group of people. (某個時期或群體的藝術) 風格","examples":["...six scenes in the style of a classical Greek tragedy. …古典希臘悲劇風格的6個場景。","...a mixture of musical styles. …多種音樂風格的混合。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a piece of clothing, a vehicle, or someone's hair <b>is styled</b> in a particular way, it is designed or shaped in that way. 設計式樣","examples":["His thick blond hair had just been styled before his trip. 他濃密的金髮在他旅行前剛被設計了式樣。"]}]}]},"stuff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"東西，物品；基本特徵，特質，根本；<非正式>（某人從事的）活動，事情；<非正式>原材料；投球能力；<非正式>作品，樂曲，藝術；胡說八道，廢話，荒謬的想法；<非正式>飲料，毒品；<英，舊>毛料，呢絨"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"塞進，填進；填滿，裝滿；填作料，填餡；製作（動物）標本；<非正式>（使）吃撐，吃足；不稀罕，不在乎；<非正式>把同樣的印刷品裝進（信封）；<美>把偽造選票投入（票箱）；<英，俚>性交（一個男人和一個女人性交）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>stuff</b> to refer to things such as a substance, a collection of things, events, or ideas, or the contents of something in a general way without mentioning the thing itself by name. 東西","examples":["I'd like some coffee, and I don't object to the powdered stuff if it's all you've got. 我想要點咖啡，如果你們只有粉狀的東西，我也不反對。","He pointed to a duffle bag. \"That's my stuff.\" 他指著一個旅行袋。“那是我的東西。”"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stuff</b> something somewhere, you push it there quickly and roughly. 把…塞進","examples":["I stuffed my hands in my pockets. 我把雙手塞進了我的口袋裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stuff</b> a container or space <b>with</b> something, you fill it with something or with a quantity of things until it is full. 把…裝滿","examples":["He grabbed my purse, opened it and stuffed it full, then gave it back to me. 他搶走我的錢包，開啟並把它裝得滿滿的，然後還給了我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>stuff</b> <b>yourself</b>, you eat a lot of food. 使吃飽","examples":["I could stuff myself with ten chocolate bars and half an hour later eat a big meal. 我可以給自己塞下10塊巧克力，並在半小時後再大吃一頓。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>stuff</b> a bird such as a chicken or a vegetable such as a pepper, you put a mixture of food inside it before cooking it. 把填料塞入 (雞或辣椒等)","examples":["Will you stuff the turkey and shove it in the oven for me? 你能幫我把填料塞進火雞裡，然後把它放進烤箱嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a dead animal <b>is stuffed</b>, it is filled with a substance so that it can be preserved and displayed. 把…製成標本","examples":["...his collections of stamps and books and stuffed birds. …他的郵票、書和標本鳥的收藏品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>knows</b> their <b>stuff</b>, you mean that they are good at doing something because they know a lot about it. 懂行","examples":["These guys know their stuff after seven years of war. 這些傢伙在7年的戰爭之後便懂行了。"]}]}]},"suicide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自殺；自殺者；自殺性的行為，自取滅亡的行為；<美>（籃球中的）自殺訓練"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自殺的，與自殺有關的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"自殺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who commit <b>suicide</b> deliberately kill themselves because they do not want to continue living. 自殺","examples":["She tried to commit suicide on several occasions. 她曾幾次試圖進行自殺。","...a case of attempted suicide. …一個自殺未遂的案子。"]}]}]},"summit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（政府間的）首腦會議，峰會；山頂，頂峰；（成就的）頂點，最高點；最高階層"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最高階的，政府首腦的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"登上（頂峰）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>summit</b> is a meeting at which the leaders of two or more countries discuss important matters. 峰會","examples":["...next week's Washington summit. …下週的華盛頓峰會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>summit</b> of a mountain is the top of it. (山) 峰","examples":["He made it to the summit of Kilimanjaro before collapsing. 他成功登上乞力馬扎羅山峰頂後倒下了。"]}]}]},"summary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"總結，概要"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總結性的，概括的；（司法程式）即決的，簡易的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>summary</b> <b>of</b> something is a short account of it, which gives the main points but not the details. 總結","examples":["What follows is a brief summary of the process. 接下來是對該過程的一個簡短總結。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in summary</b> to indicate that what you are about to say is a summary of what has just been said. 總之","examples":["In summary, it is my opinion that this complete treatment process was very successful. 總之，我認為這整個治療過程非常成功。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Summary</b> actions are done without delay, often when something else should have been done first or done instead. 從簡的","examples":["It says torture and summary execution are common. 據說酷刑和草草處決很常見。"]}]}]},"survivor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（災難性事故中的）倖存者，生還者，倖存物；能在艱苦環境中生存的人，挺過困難者；（死者的）尚在世的家人，遺屬；遭遇過（不幸經歷）的人，經受過（苦難）的人；留存的人（或物），繼續發揮作用的人（或物），競賽中的過關者；倖存的公司；<法律>（共有財產產主中的）存者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>survivor</b> <b>of</b> a disaster, accident, or illness is someone who continues to live afterward in spite of coming close to death. 倖存者","examples":["Officials said there were no survivors of the plane crash. 官員們說這次飛機失事中沒有倖存者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>survivor</b> <b>of</b> a very unpleasant experience is a person who has had such an experience, and who is still affected by it. 經受過不幸的人","examples":["This book is written with survivors of child sexual abuse in mind. 這本書寫的是關於童年時經受過性虐待的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A person's <b>survivors</b> are the members of their family who continue to live after they have died. (家中) 尚活著的人","examples":["The compensation bill offers the miners or their survivors as much as $100,000 apiece. 這筆賠償款提供給這些礦工或其尚活著的家人每人$100000。"]}]}]},"superior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（規模或實力）更大的，更強的，(在品質上)更好的；（尤用於廣告中指產品或服務）高質量的，優質的；上級的，（在級別、重要性或職位上）更高的；有優越感的，高傲的，傲慢的；在其他器官之上的；（字母，數字，符號）上標的；（花的子房）上位的，（子房）在萼上的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上級，上司；<正式>優勝者，高手；修道院院長（或其他宗教機構的負責人）；（印刷）上標字母（或數字、符號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person is <b>superior</b> <b>to</b> another, the first is better than the second. 比…好的","examples":["We have a relationship infinitely superior to those of many of our friends. 我們之間的關係遠比我們許多朋友之間的關係好得多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>superior</b>, you mean that it is good, and better than other things of the same kind. 上好的","examples":["A few years ago it was virtually impossible to find superior quality coffee in local shops. 幾年前在當地的商店裡幾乎不可能買到上好的咖啡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>superior</b> person or thing is more important than another person or thing in the same organization or system. 上級的","examples":["...negotiations between the mutineers and their superior officers. …那些反叛者和他們的上級軍官們之間的談判。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>superior</b>, you disapprove of them because they behave as if they are better, more important, or more intelligent than other people. 有優越感的","examples":["Finch gave a superior smile. 芬奇富有優越感地一笑。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If one group of people has <b>superior</b> numbers to another group, the first has more people than the second, and therefore has an advantage over it. (人數) 佔優勢的","examples":["The demonstrators fled when they saw the authorities' superior numbers. 示威者們看到官方佔優勢的人數時就逃跑了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"優越性","examples":["The technical superiority of laser discs over tape is well established. 光碟相對磁帶在技術上的優越性是確定無疑的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>superior</b> in an organization that you work for is a person who has a higher rank than you. 上級","examples":["Other army units are completely surrounded and cut-off from communication with their superiors. 其他部隊完全被包圍，與上級的聯絡也被切斷了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"優越","examples":["...a false sense of his superiority over mere journalists. …他在記者面前才有的虛假的優越感。"]}]}]},"sum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金額，款項；算術，簡單計算；總數，總和；全部，一切（尤指數量不大）；<英>計算失誤；<英>計算費用"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"概括，總結；求……的和，計算……的總數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sum</b> <b>of</b> money is an amount of money. (一) 筆 (錢)","examples":["Large sums of money were lost. 大筆大筆的錢損失了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In mathematics, <b>the sum of</b> two or more numbers is the number that is obtained when they are added together. (數字的) 和","examples":["The sum of all the angles of a triangle is 180 degrees. 一個三角形的所有角度之和是180度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The sum of</b> something is all of it. You often use <b>sum</b> in this way to indicate that you are disappointed because the extent of something is rather small, or because it is not very good. 全部","examples":["To date, the sum of my gardening experience had been futile efforts to rid the flower beds of grass. 迄今為止，我全部的園藝經驗就是給花圃徒勞地除草。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>sum</b> is a simple calculation in arithmetic. 簡單運算","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the standard monetary unit of Uzbekistan, divided into 100 tiyin 烏茲別克琛","examples":[]}]}]},"survival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼續生存，存活，倖存；遺留物，倖存物，殘存物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"倖存的，賴以生存的，救生用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>survival</b> of something or someone, you mean that they manage to continue or exist in spite of difficult circumstances. (在困境中的) 生存","examples":["...companies which have been struggling for survival in the advancing recession. …在不斷惡化的蕭條期中一直掙扎求生的各家公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>survival</b> of a person or living thing, you mean that they live through a dangerous situation in which it was possible that they might die. 存活","examples":["If cancers are spotted early there's a high chance of survival. 如果癌症早被發現，存活的機率就高。"]}]}]},"survey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"民意調查，民意測驗；考察，調查；（對課題或情況的）全面考察，概述；測量，勘測；測繪圖，勘測記錄；測量部門；<英> （尤指為欲購房者所做的）房屋鑑定；查勘報告"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做民意測驗，做民意調查；（尤指認真地）審視，檢查；測量，勘測；<英> （尤指為可能的買家）查勘，檢視（建築物的狀況）；全面評述，概述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you carry out a <b>survey</b>, you try to find out detailed information about a lot of different people or things, usually by asking people a series of questions. 調查","examples":["The council conducted a survey of the uses to which farm buildings are put. 該委員會對農場建築的用途進行了一個調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone carries out a <b>survey</b> of an area of land, they examine it and measure it, usually in order to make a map of it. 勘測","examples":["...the organizer of the geological survey of India. …印度地質勘測的組織者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>survey</b> is a careful examination of the condition and structure of a house, usually carried out in order to give information to a person who wants to buy it. (對房屋的) 鑑定","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>survey</b> a number of people, companies, or organizations, you try to find out information about their opinions or behaviour, usually by asking them a series of questions. 調查","examples":["Business Development Advisers surveyed 211 companies for the report. 企業發展顧問為這份報告調查了211家公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>survey</b> something, you look at or consider the whole of it carefully. 審視","examples":["He pushed himself to his feet and surveyed the room. 他站起來審視這個房間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>surveys</b> an area of land, they examine it and measure it, usually in order to make a map of it. 勘測","examples":["The city council commissioned geological experts earlier this year to survey the cliffs. 該市議會今年早些時候委託地質專家們對這些懸崖進行勘測。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>surveys</b> a house, they examine it carefully and report on its structure, usually in order to give advice to a person who is thinking of buying it. 鑑定 (房屋)","examples":[]}]}]},"suspicion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不好的預感，猜想；（對某人有罪、不誠實等的）懷疑；不信任，猜疑；少量，一點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<方> 懷疑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Suspicion</b> or a <b>suspicion</b> is a belief or feeling that someone has committed a crime or done something wrong. 懷疑","examples":["There was a suspicion that this runner attempted to avoid the procedures for drug testing. 存在這名賽跑運動員試圖逃避藥檢的懷疑。","The police said their suspicions were aroused because Mr. Owens had other marks on his body. 警方說他們的懷疑產生於歐文斯先生身上留有其他印跡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is <b>suspicion</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, people do not trust them or consider them to be reliable. 猜疑","examples":["This tendency in his thought is deepened by his suspicion of all Utopian political programmes. 他思想中這種傾向因他對所有烏托邦政治計劃的猜疑而加深。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>suspicion</b> is a feeling that something is probably true or is likely to happen. 不確定的感覺","examples":["I have a sneaking suspicion that they are going to succeed. 我有種隱約的感覺他們會成功。"]}]}]},"suspect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猜想，認為（某事有可能）；懷疑……有罪，認為……有嫌疑；不信任，懷疑……的真實性"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嫌疑犯，可疑分子；（某壞事物的）可能導致者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不可靠的，不可信的；可疑的，可能有危險的；有問題的，運轉不好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>suspect</b> when you are stating something that you believe is probably true, in order to make it sound less strong or direct. 覺得","examples":["I suspect they were right. 我覺得他們是正確的。","The above complaints are, I suspect, just the tip of the iceberg. 上述的這些抱怨，我覺得，不過是冰山的一角。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>suspect</b> that something dishonest or unpleasant has been done, you believe that it has probably been done. If you <b>suspect</b> someone <b>of</b> doing an action of this kind, you believe that they probably did it. 懷疑","examples":["He suspected that the woman staying in the flat above was using heroin. 他懷疑住在樓上公寓裡的那位女子在吸食海洛因。","It was perfectly all right, he said, because the police had not suspected him of anything. 一點兒沒事，他說，因為警察對他沒有任何懷疑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>suspect</b> is a person who the police or authorities think may be guilty of a crime. 嫌疑犯","examples":["Police have arrested a suspect in a series of killings and sexual assaults in the city. 警方逮捕了該城市一系列殺人強姦案件中的一名嫌疑犯。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Suspect</b> things or people are ones that you think may be dangerous or may be less good or genuine than they appear. 可疑的","examples":["Delegates evacuated the building when a suspect package was found. 一個可疑包裹被發現後，代表們撤離了這棟大樓。"]}]}]},"sword":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劍，刀；<文> 武力，暴力（the sword）；塔羅紙牌中一組牌中的一張（swords）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sword</b> is a weapon with a handle and a long sharp blade. 劍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cross swords</b> <b>with</b> someone, you disagree with them and argue with them about something. 爭論","examples":["...a candidate who's crossed swords with labour by supporting the free-trade pact. …一位因支援自由貿易協定而與工黨爭論的候選人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>double-edged sword</b>, you mean that it has negative effects as well as positive effects. 雙刃劍","examples":["A person's looks are a double-edged sword. Sometimes it works in your favour, sometimes it works against you. 一個人的相貌是一把雙刃劍。有時它對你有利，有時又對你不利。"]}]}]},"tablet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥片，片劑；丸；（石頭、黏土等制的刻字的）牌，碑，匾；平板電腦；<美> 便箋簿，拍紙簿；<舊> 一塊肥皂；（單線）路牌；簷板；<蘇格蘭> 乳脂軟糖；（計算機的）輸入板，手寫板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tablet</b> is a small solid mass of medicine which you swallow. 藥片","examples":["...half a tablet of aspirin. …半片阿斯匹林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Clay <b>tablets</b> or stone <b>tablets</b> are the flat pieces of clay or stone which people used to write on before paper was invented. (黏土或石頭制的、用以銘刻文字的) 匾; 碑","examples":[]}]}]},"swell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（身體部位）腫脹，膨脹， 使（某物）膨脹，使腫脹；（使）鼓起，（使）隆起；（使）增長，增加，擴大；（聲音）逐漸增強，變響亮；（情緒）高漲，充滿；波濤洶湧"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"海浪的湧動，湧浪；（音量的）增強；感情的高漲；（規模或數量的）增長，增加；（尤指身體部位）凸起的形狀，鼓出處，隆起處；<舊> 重要人士，時髦人物；（管風琴、簧風琴的）音量調節器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<美，舊> 第一流的，極好的；<美，非正式，古> 漂亮的，時髦的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美，非正式，舊> 極好地，非常順利地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the amount or size of something <b>swells</b> or if something <b>swells</b> it, it becomes larger than it was before. 使增大; 增大","examples":["The human population swelled, at least temporarily, as migrants moved south. 隨著移民們南移，人口便增加了，至少是暫時增加了。","His bank balance has swelled by $222,000 in the last three weeks. 他的銀行存款在過去的3周裡增加了$222,000。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a part of your body <b>swells</b>, it becomes larger and rounder than normal. (身體部位等) 腫脹","examples":["Do your ankles swell at night? 你的腳踝晚上會腫嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Swell up</b> means the same as . 腫脹","examples":["When you develop a throat infection or catch a cold the glands in the neck swell up. 當你咽喉發炎或感冒時, 脖子上的腺體會腫起來。"]}]}]},"sweat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"流汗，出汗，冒汗；透過出汗排除；（透過運動或費力）使（人，動物）出汗；（食品，物體）滲出水分；辛苦工作，拼命幹活；（人）（多指長時間的）處於極度焦慮中；<非正式> 擔心，焦慮，緊張；熔焊（金屬）；用文火燉（肉或蔬菜）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"汗水，汗液；一身汗，滿身大汗；<非正式> 艱難的工作，累活，繁重的工作；<美> 田徑服，運動服，運動褲（sweats）；（用羊毛似的厚棉布做的）寬鬆休閒服裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sweat</b> is the salty colourless liquid which comes through your skin when you are hot, sick, or afraid. 汗","examples":["Both horse and rider were dripping with sweat within five minutes. 馬和騎手不到5分鐘都大汗淋漓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"出汗","examples":["...symptoms such as sweating, irritability, anxiety, and depression. …如出汗、易怒、焦慮和抑鬱等症狀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>in</b> a <b>sweat</b>, they are sweating a lot. 滿身汗","examples":["Every morning I would break out in a sweat. 每天早上我都會突然滿身大汗。","Cool down very gradually after working up a sweat. 大量出汗後要慢慢地涼下來。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sweat</b>, sweat comes through your skin. 出汗","examples":["Already they were sweating as the sun beat down upon them. 太陽照在他們身上時，他們已經在冒汗了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>in a cold sweat</b> or <b>in a sweat</b>, they feel frightened or embarrassed. (害怕或尷尬時) 出冷汗","examples":["The very thought brought me out in a cold sweat. 這個念頭讓我出了一身冷汗。"]}]}]},"tack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大頭釘，圖釘；（為定樣臨時縫上的）粗縫針腳；馬具，鞍轡；（航海）搶風調向，搶風航行路線，搶風航程；（繫住帆角的）系帆索；（用系帆索）繫住的帆角；行動方針，策略；廉價且難看的物品；黏著性，黏著力；（航海）（繫住帆角的）系帆索"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用平頭釘）釘上，固定住；（為定樣而）用粗縫針腳縫；戧風行駛，蜿蜒航行；（尤指畫蛇添足地）增補，附加"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tack</b> or a <b>thumbtack</b> is a short pin with a wide head that you can push with your thumb, especially for a bulletin board. 圖釘","examples":["...a box of carpet tacks. …一盒地毯釘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tack</b> is a short nail with a broad, flat head, especially one that is used for fastening carpets to the floor. 平頭釘","examples":["...a box of carpet tacks. …一盒地毯釘。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"food, esp when regarded as inferior or distasteful 粗劣食品","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you change <b>tack</b> or try a different <b>tack</b>, you try a different method for dealing with a situation. 方法","examples":["Seeing the puzzled look on his face, she tried a different tack. 看到他臉上困惑的神情，她試了一個不同的方法。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tack</b> something to a surface, you pin it there with tacks or thumbtacks. 用平頭釘或圖釘釘住","examples":["He had tacked this note to her door. 他已經把這張便條用圖釘釘在了她的門上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tack</b> pieces of material together, you sew them together with big, loose stitches in order to hold them firmly or check that they fit, before sewing them permanently. 用粗線腳縫","examples":["Tack them together with a 1 cm seam. 用1釐米的針腳把它們粗縫上。"]}]}]},"switch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"開關，電閘；驟變，突變；交換機；（計算機）切換；<美> （鐵路的）轉轍器，道岔；（細軟的）枝條，鞭子；假髮；（在英國使用簽帳金融卡付賬的一種）轉換系統（Switch）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用開關）開啟，關閉；（使）改變，轉變；交換，調換；轉移（注意力）；（與某人）交換工作，調班；<古> 用枝條擊打，輕拂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>switch</b> is a small control for an electrical device which you use to turn the device on or off. 開關","examples":["Leona put some detergent into the dishwasher, shut the door, and pressed the switch. 利昂娜在洗碗機裡放了些清潔劑，關上門，然後按下開關。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"On a railway track, the <b>switches</b> are the levers and rails at a place where two tracks join or separate. The <b>switches</b> enable a train to move from one track to another. 轉轍器","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Switch</b> is also a noun. 轉變","examples":["The spokesman implicitly condemned the United States policy switch. 這位發言人含蓄地譴責了美國政策上的轉變。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>switch</b> <b>to</b> something different, for example to a different system, task, or subject of conversation, you change to it from what you were doing or saying before. 轉向","examples":["Estonia is switching to a market economy. 愛沙尼亞正在向市場經濟轉變。","The law would encourage companies to switch from coal to cleaner fuels. 法律會鼓勵各公司從用煤轉向使用更清潔的燃料。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>switch</b> your attention from one thing <b>to</b> another or if your attention <b>switches</b>, you stop paying attention to the first thing and start paying attention to the second. 轉移 (注意力)","examples":["My mother's interest had switched to my health. 我母親的興趣已轉移到我的健康上來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>switch</b> two things, you replace one with the other. 調換","examples":["In half an hour, they'd switched the tags on every cable. 半個小時內，他們換了每根電纜的標籤。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Switch over</b> means the same as . 轉變","examples":["Within a few years the whole country will switch over to digital television. 幾年內全國將會換上數字電視。"]}]}]},"system":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（協同工作的）系統；（計算機、警報器等的）系統；體制，制度，方式，方法；現行體制，既成制度（the system）；身體，（器官）系統；人體的活動方式（尤指消化和排洩方式）；（度量，分類中的）方法（或規則）；條理，秩序；（交通、通訊）網，網路；（地質）（年代地層學用語）系；（天文）系；下賭注法；（樂）用弧線連為一體的譜表；晶系（crystal system 的簡稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>system</b> is a way of working, organizing, or doing something which follows a fixed plan or set of rules. You can use <b>system</b> to refer to an organization or institution that is organized in this way. 體制","examples":["The present system of funding for higher education is unsatisfactory. 目前高等教育的經費體制並不令人滿意。","...a flexible and relatively efficient filing system. …一個靈活且相對高效的檔案歸檔方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>system</b> is a set of devices powered by electricity, for example a computer or an alarm. 系統","examples":["Viruses tend to be good at surviving when a computer system crashes. 病毒往往在電腦系統癱瘓時仍然存在。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>system</b> is a set of equipment or parts such as water pipes or electrical wiring, which is used to supply water, heat, or electricity. (水管或電線等的) 系統","examples":["...a central heating system. …一箇中央供暖系統。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>system</b> is a network of things that are linked together so that people or things can travel from one place to another or communicate. 網路","examples":["...Australia's road and rail system. …澳大利亞的公路網和鐵路網。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>system</b> is your body's organs and other parts that together perform particular functions. 身體系統","examples":["He had slept for over fourteen hours, and his system seemed to have recuperated admirably. 他已睡了超過十四個小時，他的身體系統看起來已經恢復得很好了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>system</b> is a particular set of rules, especially in mathematics or science, which is used to count or measure things. (計算或測量用的) 體系","examples":["...the decimal system of metric weights and measures. …公制度量衡的十進位制體系。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"People sometimes refer to the government or administration of a country as <b>the system</b>. 政府","examples":["These feelings are likely to make people attempt to overthrow the system. 這些情緒可能促使人們試著去推翻政府。"]}]}]},"tag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"標籤，標牌；稱呼，諢名；（電子）追蹤器；帶創作者名字的塗鴉；（計算機）識別符號；（兒童玩的）捉人遊戲； 附加疑問句；一小部分；（棒球）觸殺；引語，格言，諺語；<美>（機動車的）牌照；一簇糾結的羊毛；（動物顏色鮮豔的）尾尖；（鞋帶上的金屬或塑膠）包頭；（戲劇的）終場詞；疊歌，副歌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加上標籤；把……稱作；塗鴉； 給（計算機程式或檔案）加標記；（在捉人遊戲中）觸控；觸殺（跑壘員）；（跑壘員）用腳觸壘；<英，非正式> 尾隨；（尤指沒被邀請而）跟隨（或陪伴）；新增；給……裝跟蹤器；給（羊）剪去糾結的毛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tag</b> is a small piece of card or cloth which is attached to an object or person and has information about that object or person on it. 標籤","examples":["Staff wore name tags and called inmates by their first names. 工作人員戴著姓名標籤，對同僚直呼其名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An electronic <b>tag</b> is a device that is firmly attached to someone or something and sets off an alarm if that person or thing moves away or is removed. (電子) 跟蹤器","examples":["Ranchers are testing electronic tags on animals' ears to create a national cattle-tracking system. 牧場主正在檢測動物耳朵上的跟蹤器，以建立一個全國性的家畜跟蹤系統。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Tag</b> is a children's game where one child runs to touch or tag the others. (兒童玩的) 觸碰捉人遊戲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tag</b> something, you attach something to it or mark it so that it can be identified later. 給…貼標籤","examples":["Professor Orr has developed interesting ways of tagging chemical molecules using existing laboratory lasers. 奧爾教授已經研發出了用現有的實驗室鐳射給化學分子貼標籤的有趣方法。"]}]}]},"tease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"取笑，嘲笑；逗弄（動物）；（尤指性方面）挑逗，撩撥；哄，逗；撥，分離；梳理（羊毛、頭髮等）；<美>（為了使頭髮顯厚）回梳"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛開玩笑的人，愛戲弄別人的人；玩笑，戲弄；賣弄風騷的人；<非正式>激起興趣的廣告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>tease</b> someone means to laugh at them or make jokes about them in order to embarrass, annoy, or upset them. 嘲笑; 取笑","examples":["He told her how the boys had set on him, teasing him. 他告訴她那些男孩曾是如何攻擊他、取笑他的。","He teased me mercilessly about going Hollywood. 他無情地取笑我想去好萊塢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>teases</b> their hair, they separate the individual strands from each other, for example by combing it. 梳理","examples":["Her hair was teased until it stood out and around her face. 她的頭髮被梳得直垂在臉旁。","...two women in party dresses and teased hair. …兩位身著禮服、頭髮梳理整齊的婦女。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tease</b> is also a noun. 嘲笑; 取笑","examples":["Calling her by her real name had always been one of his teases. 稱呼她的真名曾是他一貫的取笑方式之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>tease</b>, you mean that they like laughing at people or making jokes about them. 愛嘲笑他人者; 愛取笑他人者","examples":["My brother's such a tease. 我弟弟就愛取笑他人。"]}]}]},"technique":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"技巧，工藝；（尤指體育或藝術方面的）技巧，技術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>technique</b> is a particular method of doing an activity, usually a method that involves practical skills. 技術","examples":["...tests performed using a new technique. …採用一種新技術做的試驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Technique</b> is skill and ability in an artistic, sporting, or other practical activity that you develop through training and practice. 技藝; 技能","examples":["He went off to the Amsterdam Academy to improve his technique. 他去了阿姆斯特丹學院以提高技藝。"]}]}]},"technology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"科技，技術；技術裝置，先進機器；技術學，工藝學；術語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Technology</b> refers to methods, systems, and devices which are the result of scientific knowledge being used for practical purposes. 技術","examples":["Technology is changing fast. 技術日新月異。","They should be allowed to wait for cheaper technologies to be developed. 他們應該被允許等待更廉價的技術開發出來。"]}]}]},"tax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"稅款；負擔，重負"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……徵稅；繳納車輛牌照稅；使負重擔，使費力氣；責備；<法律>審定（訴訟費用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tax</b> is an amount of money that you have to pay to the government so that it can pay for public services such as road and schools. 稅","examples":["No-one enjoys paying tax. 沒人喜歡繳稅。","...a pledge not to raise taxes on people below a certain income. …一個對收入低於一定水平的人不提高稅收的承諾。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or company <b>is taxed</b>, they have to pay a part of their income or profits to the government. When goods <b>are taxed</b>, a percentage of their price has to be paid to the government. (對個人、公司、貨物) 徵稅","examples":["Husband and wife may be taxed separately on their incomes. 丈夫和妻子可能會分別被徵收所得稅。"]}]}]},"tailor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指男裝）裁縫；藍魚（Tailorfish 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"定做（衣服）；迎合，使適應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tailor</b> is a person whose job is to make men's clothes. (縫製男裝的) 裁縫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tailor</b> something such as a plan or system <b>to</b> someone's needs, you make it suitable for a particular person or purpose by changing the details of it. 調整","examples":["We can tailor the programme to the patient's needs. 我們可以根據病人的需要調整這個方案。"]}]}]},"temperature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溫度，氣溫；體溫；發燒；熱烈程度，情緒激烈程度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>temperature</b> of something is a measure of how hot or cold it is. 溫度","examples":["Winter closes in and the temperature drops below freezing. 冬天來臨，氣溫降至冰點以下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>temperature</b> is the temperature of your body. A normal temperature is about 98.6° Fahrenheit. 體溫","examples":["His temperature continued to rise and the cough worsened until Tania finally persuaded him to see a doctor. 他的體溫持續升高且咳嗽加重，直到塔妮婭最終說服了他去看醫生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>temperature</b> to talk about the feelings and emotions that people have in particular situations. (特定場合的) 氛圍","examples":["There's also been a noticeable rise in the political temperature. 政治氣氛也明顯升溫。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are running a temperature</b> or if you <b>have a temperature</b>, your temperature is higher than it should be. 發燒","examples":["He began to run an extremely high temperature. 他開始發嚴重高燒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone's <b>temperature</b> you use an instrument called a thermometer to measure the temperature of their body in order to see if they are ill. 量某人的體溫","examples":["He will probably take your child's temperature too. 他可能也會量你孩子的體溫。"]}]}]},"temper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壞脾氣，暴躁脾氣；心情，情緒；怒氣，火氣；<正式>（時代的）氣息，特徵；（人或動物的）性格，性情；（鋼等的）硬度，回火性；沉著，冷靜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使緩和，使溫和；使（金屬）回火，鍛造；給（鋼琴等）調音，調整（音階）；回火，調和"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>temper</b> or say that they have a <b>temper</b>, you mean that they become angry very easily. 暴躁的脾氣","examples":["He had a temper and could be nasty. 他脾氣暴躁，會令人討厭。","His short temper had become notorious. 他的急性子已臭名遠揚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>temper</b> is the way you are feeling at a particular time. If you are <b>in</b> a good <b>temper</b>, you feel cheerful. If you are <b>in</b> a bad <b>temper</b>, you feel angry and impatient. 情緒","examples":["I was in a bad temper last night. 我昨晚情緒不好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>in a temper</b> or gets <b>into a temper</b>, the way that they are behaving shows that they are feeling angry and impatient. 在發脾氣中","examples":["She was still in a temper when Colin arrived. 科林到的時候她還在發脾氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> your <b>temper</b>, you become so angry that you shout at someone or show in some other way that you are no longer in control of yourself. 發脾氣","examples":["I've never seen him get mad or lose his temper. 我從未見過他發瘋或發火。"]}]}]},"territory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"領土，版圖，領地；（美國、加拿大等的）準州；（某些國家劃分的）地區；（某一動物或人想控制的）領地，地盤；（某人負責的）區域，地區；（具有某種特性的）地區，地方；（知識等的）領域，範圍；（體育運動中的）防守區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Territory</b> is land which is controlled by a particular country or ruler. 領土","examples":["The government denies that any of its territory is under rebel control. 該政府否認有任何領土被叛亂者控制。","...the view that the US should use military force only when our borders or US territories are attacked. …那種觀點認為只有我們的邊界或美國領土受到襲擊時美國才應該使用武力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>territory</b> is a country or region that is controlled by another country. 屬地","examples":["He toured some of the disputed territories now under UN control. 他巡訪過一些現歸聯合國管轄的有爭議的屬地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>territory</b> to refer to an area of knowledge or experience. 領域","examples":["Following the futuristic \"The Handmaid's Tale,\" Margaret Atwood's seventh novel, \"Cat's Eye,\" returns to more familiar territory. 在推出具有未來主義色彩的《女僕的故事》之後，瑪格麗特·阿特伍德的第7部小說《貓眼》返回了更為熟悉的領域。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An animal's <b>territory</b> is an area which it regards as its own and which it defends when other animals try to enter it. (動物的) 地盤","examples":["The territory of a cat only remains fixed for as long as the cat dominates the area. 貓的地盤只在它佔據那個地方的時候才保持穩定不變。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Territory</b> is land with a particular character. (具有某種特徵的) 地帶","examples":["...mountainous territory. …多山地帶。"]}]}]},"theory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學說，理論；（某一學科基於的）理論，原理；觀點，見解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>theory</b> is a formal idea or set of ideas that is intended to explain something. 理論","examples":["Marx produced a new theory about historical change based upon conflict between competing groups. 馬克思提出了一個新理論，認為歷史變革是由於對立集團的衝突而產生的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>theory</b> about something, you have your own opinion about it which you cannot prove but which you think is true. 觀點","examples":["There was a theory that he wanted to marry her. 有種觀點認為他想娶她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>theory</b> of a practical subject or skill is the set of rules and principles that form the basis of it. 基礎理論","examples":["He taught us music theory. 他教我們樂理。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in theory</b> to say that although something is supposed to be true or to happen in the way stated, it may not in fact be true or happen in that way. 從理論上說","examples":["Achieving these goals is relatively easy in theory, yet quite difficult in practice. 實現這些目標從理論上說比較容易，但在實踐上卻相當困難。"]}]}]},"text":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書、雜誌等中區別於圖片的）正文，文字材料；（演說等的）原文；（學習某課程必讀的）課本，教科書；（供討論或回答問題的）文字，文章；（討論等的）題目，主題；（尤指科學或學術方面的）文獻；（計算機、手機等）文件；簡訊；（尤指引作佈道主題的）聖經經文；（尤指用於手稿的）粗體正楷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用手機）給……發簡訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The text</b> of a book is the main part of it, rather than the introduction, pictures, or notes. 正文","examples":["The text was informative and well written. 正文資訊量大，寫得很好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Text</b> is any written material. 文字材料; 文字","examples":["The machine can recognize handwritten characters and turn them into printed text. 這臺機器能識別手寫的文字並將其轉換為列印文字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>text</b> of a speech, broadcast, or recording is the written version of it. (演講、廣播或錄音的) 文字稿","examples":["The text of his recent speech was circulated among leading republicans. 他新近演講的文字稿在共和黨領導人之間傳閱。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>text</b> is a book or other piece of writing, especially one connected with science or learning. (尤指與科學或學術相關的) 文稿","examples":["Her text is believed to be the oldest surviving manuscript by a female physician. 她的文稿被認為是女性內科醫生寫的現存最古老的手稿。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>text</b> is the same as a . 簡訊","examples":["The new system can send a text to a mobile phone, or to another landline phone. 新系統可以向手機或向另一臺座機發簡訊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>text</b> someone, you send them a text message on a mobile phone. (用手機) 給…發簡訊","examples":["Mary texted me when she got home. 瑪麗到家時給我發了簡訊。"]}]}]},"thirst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"渴，口渴；乾渴，缺水；渴望，渴求"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>渴望，渴求；<舊>渴，口渴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thirst</b> is the feeling of wanting to drink something. 口渴","examples":["Instead of tea or coffee, drink water to quench your thirst. 別喝茶或者咖啡，喝水來解渴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Thirst</b> is the condition of not having enough to drink. 缺水","examples":["They died of thirst on the voyage. 他們在旅行途中因缺水而死。"]}]}]},"threat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"威脅，恐嚇；構成威脅的人（或事物）；凶兆，徵兆；（律）恐嚇，威脅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>威脅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>threat</b> <b>to</b> a person or thing is a danger that something bad might happen to them. A <b>threat</b> is also the cause of this danger. 威脅; 造成威脅的原因","examples":["Some couples see single women as a threat to their relationships. 有些夫婦把單身女子看作是對他們夫妻關係的一種威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>threat</b> is a statement by someone that they will hurt you in some way, especially if you do not do what they want. 威脅的言論","examples":["He may be forced to carry out his threat to resign. 他可能會迫不得已將自己揚言要辭職的威脅付諸實施。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>under threat</b>, there is a danger that something bad might be done to them, or that they might cease to exist. 受到威脅","examples":["His position as leader is under threat. 他的領導職位受到威脅。"]}]}]},"timber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木材，原木；（用於生產木材的）林木，樹林；（造屋或造船用的）大木料，棟木；（砍伐樹木時說）倒啦，小心大樹倒下；<美>（尤指人適於某角色的）素質，性格，才幹"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用木料支撐或建造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Timber</b> is wood that is used for building houses and making furniture. You can also refer to trees that are grown for this purpose as <b>timber</b>. 木材","examples":["These Michigan woods have been exploited for timber since the Great Fire of Chicago. 自芝加哥大火災之後，密歇根的森林一直被砍伐作木材用。"]}]}]},"tickle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使覺得癢，撓（某人）的癢癢；（使）發癢；使滿足，使高興；使發笑；引發（品味，幽默感，好奇心）；用手捉（鱒魚）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"癢（感）； 呵癢，胳肢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>tickle</b> someone, you move your fingers lightly over a sensitive part of their body, often in order to make them laugh. 胳肢","examples":["I was tickling him, and he was laughing and giggling. 我在胳肢他，他咯咯笑起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>tickles</b> you or <b>tickles</b>, it causes an irritating feeling by lightly touching a part of your body. 使發癢; 發癢","examples":["...a yellow hat with a great feather that tickled her ear. …一頂黃帽子上飾有一根大羽毛，扎得她發癢。"]}]}]},"thread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"線；細線，線狀物；思路，貫穿的主線；（網際網路留言板上的）同主題帖子，系列相關帖子；少量，較低水平；螺紋；<英，舊> 衣服；（計算機）執行緒，排程單位"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿線於，使穿過；將（珠子等）穿起來；裝好（膠捲或錄音帶）；穿行，曲折穿過；使夾雜（線狀物）；用手指梳理（尤指頭髮）；刻螺紋於（孔、螺絲等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thread</b> or a <b>thread</b> is a long very thin piece of a material such as cotton, nylon, or silk, especially one that is used in sewing. (尤指用於縫紉的) 線","examples":["This time I'll do it right with a spool of thread. 這次我會用一軸線把它弄好的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>thread</b> of an argument, a story, or a situation is an aspect of it that connects all the different parts together. 主線","examples":["The thread running through many of these proposals was the theme of individual power and opportunity. 貫穿眾多提案的主線，是個人權力與機遇的主題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>thread</b> <b>of</b> something such as liquid, light, or colour is a long thin line or piece of it. 線狀物; 一線","examples":["A thin, glistening thread of moisture ran along the rough concrete sill. 一條細細亮亮的水印爬過粗糙的水泥窗臺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>thread</b> on a screw, or on something such as a lid or a pipe, is the raised spiral line of metal or plastic around it which allows it to be fixed in place by twisting. 螺紋","examples":["The screw threads will be able to get a good grip. 這些螺紋可以咬合得很緊。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"On websites such as newsgroups, a <b>thread</b> is one of the subjects that is being written about. (新聞組等網站上的) 話題","examples":["The dialogues are organized by month so you can go back to previous threads and read them. 這些對話是按月份編排的，所以你可以找以前的話題來讀一讀。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>thread</b> a needle, you put a piece of thread through the hole in the top of the needle in order to sew with it. 穿 (針)","examples":["I sit down, thread a needle, snip off an old button. 我坐下來，穿好針，剪下了一粒舊鈕釦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>thread</b> your <b>way</b> through a group of people or things, or <b>thread</b> <b>through</b> it, you move through it carefully or slowly, changing direction frequently as you move. 穿行","examples":["Slowly she threaded her way back through the moving mass of bodies. 她在行人中緩慢穿行，擠了回來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>thread</b> a long thin object <b>through</b> something, you pass it through one or more holes or narrow spaces. 把 (細長物體) 穿進","examples":["...threading the laces through the eyelets of his shoes. …把鞋帶穿進他的鞋眼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>thread</b> small objects such as beads onto a string or thread, you join them together by pushing the string through them. 把 (珠子等) 串起來","examples":["Wipe the mushrooms clean and thread them on a string. 把蘑菇擦乾淨，然後把它們串在細繩上。"]}]}]},"tissue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紙巾，面巾紙；（動物或植物的細胞）組織；（用於包裝易碎物品的）薄紙，綿紙；薄紗，薄織物；（羅織編造的）一套，一系列"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用化妝紙揩去；飾以薄紗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In animals and plants, <b>tissue</b> consists of cells that are similar to each other in appearance and that have the same function. (動植物的) 組織","examples":["As we age we lose muscle tissue. 隨著年紀的增大，我們會失去一些肌肉組織。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tissue paper</b> is thin paper that is used for wrapping things that are easily damaged, such as objects made of glass or china. (包裝易碎物品的) 薄棉紙","examples":["...a small package wrapped in tissue paper. …一個小包裹，用薄棉紙包著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tissue</b> is a piece of thin soft paper that you use to blow your nose. 面巾紙","examples":["...a box of tissues. …一盒面巾紙。"]}]}]},"tide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潮汐；潮水；潮流，趨勢；怒潮，（難以控制的）浪潮；高漲的情緒；潮水般的人流，洪流"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>順潮水漂浮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>tide</b> is the regular change in the level of the ocean on the beach. You say the tide is in when water reaches a high point on the land or out when the water leaves the land. 潮水","examples":["The tide was at its highest. 潮水那時正處於最高位。","The tide was going out, and the sand was smooth and glittering. 潮水正在退去，沙灘平坦，閃閃發亮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tide</b> is a current in the sea that is caused by the regular and continuous movement of large areas of water toward and away from the shore. (不斷沖刷海岸的) 海浪","examples":["Roman vessels used to sail with the tide from Boulogne to Richborough. 羅馬的船只過去常常乘著海浪從布洛涅航行到裡奇伯勒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>tide of</b> opinion, for example, is what the majority of people think at a particular time. (觀點的) 潮流","examples":["The tide of opinion seems overwhelmingly in his favour. 大部分人的觀點似乎對他極為有利。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to carry or be carried with or as if with the tide (用潮水)沖走; (像潮水般)被帶走","examples":[]}]}]},"tobacco":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"菸草，菸葉；菸草製品；菸草植株；抽菸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tobacco</b> is dried leaves which people smoke in pipes, cigars, and cigarettes. You can also refer to pipes, cigars, and cigarettes as a whole as <b>tobacco</b>. 菸葉; 菸草製品","examples":["Try to do without tobacco and alcohol. 儘量不要抽菸喝酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tobacco</b> is the plant from which tobacco is obtained. 菸草","examples":["...Cuba's tobacco crop. …古巴的菸草作物。"]}]}]},"tortoise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"龜，（烏）龜（等於 testudo）；<澳>淡水龜；遲緩的人；陸龜，（烏）龜（= testudo）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tortoise</b> is a slow-moving animal with a shell into which it can pull its head and legs for protection. 龜","examples":[]}]}]},"tourism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅遊業，觀光業；旅遊，觀光"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tourism</b> is the business of providing services for people on holiday, for example, hotels, restaurants, and trips. 旅遊業","examples":["Tourism is vital for the economy. 旅遊業對於經濟至關重要。"]}]}]},"tourist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行者，觀光客；<英>（在國外參加）巡迴比賽的運動隊隊員；經濟艙"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"旅遊者的，遊客的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕>旅行"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"坐旅遊車廂，坐經濟艙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tourist</b> is a person who is visiting a place for pleasure and interest, especially when they are on holiday. 遊客","examples":["...a tourist attraction. …一處旅遊景點。"]}]}]},"ton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英噸，長噸（等於1016公斤）；美噸，短噸（等於907公斤）；公噸（等於1000公斤）；毛噸，噸位（船舶大小的計量單位，1噸等於100立方英尺）；（船舶的）排水噸；冷噸；<非正式>大量，許多；<非正式，英>一百"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ton</b> is a unit of weight that is equal to 2,240 pounds. 噸","examples":["Hundreds of tons of oil spilled into the ocean. 數百噸石油溢位流入大海。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ton</b> is the same as a  or , which is 1,000 kilograms. 噸","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a score or achievement of a hundred, esp a hundred miles per hour, as on a motorcycle 一百(英里每小時)","examples":[]}]}]},"trader":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商人，貿易商；（金融）交易者，交易員；商船；（Trader）特雷德（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trader</b> is a person whose job is to trade in goods or stocks. 商人; 證券交易人","examples":["Market traders display an exotic selection of the island's produce. 市場商家們展示了該島具有異國情調的農產品系列。"]}]}]},"tow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拖，牽引（車、船等）；（人）牽引，拖帶（某人，某物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對車船等的）牽引，拖；牽引繩，拖鏈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one vehicle <b>tows</b> another, it pulls it along behind it. 拖","examples":["He had been using the vehicle to tow his work trailer.. 他一直用那輛車來拖他的活動工作室。","They threatened to tow away my car. 他們威脅說要拖走我的車。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"something used for towing 拖具","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"something towed 被拖物","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the act or an instance of towing 拖動","examples":[]}]}]},"toss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（輕輕地或隨意地）扔，拋，擲；向後甩（頭髮或身體部位）；（使）搖擺，揮動，顛簸；（在液體中）攪拌（食物），拌勻；（為……）擲硬幣決定，擲幣猜邊兒；<英>把（煎餅）顛起翻面；<美，非正式>除掉，拋棄；（馬）摔下（騎手）；<美，非正式>搜（某地）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擲硬幣決定；（輕輕的或隨意的）扔，拋，擲；向上甩頭，猛仰頭；（尤指比賽或遊戲中）投擲；<英>根本不在乎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>toss</b> something somewhere, you throw it there lightly, often in a careless way. 扔","examples":["Just toss it in the rubbish. 把它扔進垃圾桶就可以了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>toss</b> your head or <b>toss</b> your hair, you move your head backward, quickly and suddenly, often as a way of expressing an emotion such as anger or contempt. 甩 (表達憤怒、蔑視等情感)","examples":["\"I'm sure I don't know.\" Deb tossed her head. “我確實不知道。”德布甩頭說道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports and informal situations, if you decide something by <b>tossing</b> a coin, you spin a coin into the air and guess which side of the coin will face upward when it lands. 拋 (硬幣)","examples":["We tossed a coin to decide who would go out and buy the bagels. 我們拋硬幣來決定誰出去買百吉圈。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Toss</b> is also a noun. 後甩","examples":["With a toss of his head and a few hard gulps, Bob finished the last of his beer. 鮑勃仰頭咕咚咕咚幾大口喝完了剩下的啤酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Toss</b> is also a noun. 拋硬幣的方法","examples":["It would be better to decide it on the toss of a coin. 最好用拋硬幣的方式來對此事做決定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>toss and turn</b>, you keep moving around in bed and cannot sleep, for example, because you are sick or worried. 輾轉反側","examples":["I try to go back to sleep and toss and turn for a while. 我努力重新入睡，輾轉反側了一會兒。"]}]}]},"traveler":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行者，旅客，遊客；旅行推銷員（等於 traveller）"}],"sections":[]},"trash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"垃圾，廢物；<美>垃圾桶；劣質的東西，（尤指）拙劣的作品；<美>廢物，窩囊廢；（西印度）（作燃料的）甘蔗葉（梢），甘蔗渣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>損壞，毀壞；<非正式>抨擊，譴責；<非正式>丟棄，去除；（計算機）把（檔案，程式）送進回收站刪除，清空（磁碟）；剝（甘蔗）皮以使其更快成熟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trash</b> consists of unwanted things or waste material such as used paper, empty containers and bottles, and waste food. 垃圾; 廢物","examples":["The yards are overgrown and cluttered with trash. 院子雜草叢生，堆滿了垃圾。","Would you take out the trash? 你可以把垃圾帶出去嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a book, painting, or movie is <b>trash</b>, you mean that it is of very bad quality. 劣質的東西","examples":["Pop music doesn't have to be trash; it can be art. 流行音樂並不一定是劣質的東西，它可以是藝術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The trash</b> means the dustbin. 垃圾桶","examples":["I threw it in the trash. 我把它扔進了垃圾桶。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to attack or destroy (someone or something) wilfully or maliciously 蓄意搗毀(某物); 蓄意攻擊(某人)","examples":[]}]}]},"tray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"托盤，碟；檔案盤，公文格；（各種用途的）淺盤子，淺塑膠盒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tray</b> is a flat piece of wood, plastic, or metal, which usually has raised edges and which is used for carrying things, especially food and drinks. 托盤","examples":[]}]}]},"trail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痕跡，蹤跡；（人或動物的）足跡，嗅跡；（鄉間的）小路，小徑；（特定）路線，路徑；一系列（壞事或有害事件）；（尤指細長）一縷，一串；<美>滑雪坡，滑雪道，越野滑雪路線；電影或廣播的預告片；（炮架的）架尾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拖，拉；沒精打采地走，拖沓地走；（在競賽或選舉中）落後，輸；跟蹤，追蹤；蔓生，蔓延，被擱置；垂下；慢慢移動，緩緩流動；（聲音，喇叭）漸弱；事先宣傳，預告（影片，節目等）；噴注（泥釉）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trail</b> is a rough path across open country or through forests. (鄉間或林中的) 崎嶇小路","examples":["He was following a trail through the trees. 他正沿著一條崎嶇小路穿過樹林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trail</b> is a route along a series of paths or roads, often one that has been planned and marked out for a particular purpose. (有特定目的的) 路線; 路徑","examples":["...a large area of woodland with hiking and walking trails. …有徒步旅行和散步路線的大片林區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>trail</b> is a series of marks or other signs of movement or other activities left by someone or something. 痕跡","examples":["Everywhere in the house was a sticky trail of orange juice. 房子裡到處都是粘乎乎的橙汁印跡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to all the places that a politician visits in the period before an election as their campaign <b>trail</b>. (競選巡迴宣傳) 路線","examples":["During a recent speech on the campaign trail, he was interrupted by hecklers. 在最近的一次競選巡迴演講中，他被詰問者打斷了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trail</b> someone or something, you follow them secretly, often by finding the marks or signs that they have left. 跟蹤","examples":["Two detectives were trailing him. 兩個偵探正在跟蹤他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trail</b> something or it <b>trails</b>, it hangs down loosely behind you as you move along. 拖","examples":["She came down the stairs slowly, trailing the coat behind her. 她慢慢地走下樓梯，身後拖著大衣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the trail of</b> a person or thing, you are trying hard to find them or find out about them. 追蹤","examples":["The police were hot on his trail. 警方正緊緊跟蹤他。"]}]}]},"trace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"查出，發現，追蹤；追溯，追究；描繪（事物的過程或發展），記述；（尤指用手指、腳趾）畫（圖，線）；勾畫……的輪廓，勾勒；（用透明紙覆蓋在地圖、繪畫等上）複製，描摹；（手指、嘴唇等）沿著……移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"痕跡，遺蹟，蹤跡；微量，少許；描記圖，掃描線；挽繩，韁繩；跟蹤，追查；（大腦上的學習或記憶）痕跡，印跡；<西印度，美>小徑，小道；交線，跡線；（數）跡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trace</b> the origin or development of something, you find out or describe how it started or developed. 追溯","examples":["The exhibition traces the history of graphic design in America from the 19th century to the present. 這個展覽會追溯了從19世紀到現在美國平面設計的歷史。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trace</b> someone or something, you find them after looking for them. 找到","examples":["Police are anxious to trace two men seen leaving the house just before 8am. 警察急切想找到在接近早晨8點前被人看到離開那幢房子的兩名男子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>trace</b> something such as a pattern or a shape, for example, with your finger or toe, you mark its outline on a surface. 勾畫出 (輪廓)","examples":["I traced the course of the river on the map spread out on my briefcase. 我在自己公文包上鋪展開的地圖中勾畫出了這條河的流向。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>trace</b> a picture, you copy it by covering it with a piece of transparent paper and drawing over the lines underneath. (用透明紙蓋在底樣上) 描摹","examples":["She learned to draw by tracing pictures out of old storybooks. 她透過描摹舊故事書上的圖畫來學繪畫。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trace back</b> means the same as . 追溯","examples":["...Bronx residents who trace their families back to Dutch settlers. …將自己的家族追溯到荷蘭移民者們的布朗克斯居民。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trace</b> <b>of</b> something is a very small amount of it. 少許","examples":["Wash them in cold water to remove all traces of sand. 用冷水清洗它們以清除所有的沙子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>disappears without a trace</b>, you mean that they stop existing or stop being successful very suddenly and completely. 消失得無影無蹤","examples":["One day he left, disappeared without a trace. 有一天他離開了，消失得無影無蹤。"]}]}]},"tribe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"部落，宗族；一大群人，一大夥人；大家庭；<非正式>許多人；（動物或植物的）群，族；（古羅馬）行政部門；<貶>組織嚴密的社會（或政治）群體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tribe</b> is sometimes used to refer to a group of people of the same race, language, and customs, especially in a developing country. Some people disapprove of this use. 部落","examples":["...three-hundred members of the Xhosa tribe. …科薩族部落的3百名成員。"]}]}]},"tremble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因害怕、緊張、興奮等）顫抖，哆嗦；顫動，輕輕搖晃；害怕，緊張；（聲音）顫抖"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"顫抖，戰慄； <非正式>震顫病 (the trembles)；乳毒病（同 milk sickness）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tremble</b>, you shake slightly because you are frightened or cold. 顫抖","examples":["His mouth became dry, his eyes widened, and he began to tremble all over. 他嘴巴乾澀，眼睛睜大，而且開始全身發抖。","Lisa was white and trembling with anger. 莉薩氣得臉色發白，身體顫抖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>trembles</b>, it shakes slightly. (輕微地) 顫動","examples":["He felt the earth tremble under him. 他感覺大地在腳下顫動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your voice <b>trembles</b>, it sounds unsteady and uncertain, usually because you are upset or nervous. (聲音) 發顫","examples":["His voice trembled, on the verge of tears. 他的聲音顫抖著，就要落下淚來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tremble</b> is also a noun. 顫抖","examples":["I will never forget the look on the patient's face, the tremble in his hand. 我將永遠不會忘記那病人臉上的表情和他顫抖的手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tremble</b> is also a noun. (聲音的) 發顫","examples":["\"Please understand this,\" she began, a tremble in her voice. “請理解這個”，她開始用顫抖的聲音說道。"]}]}]},"transport":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運輸，運送；交通工具，運輸方式；交通運輸系統；（運送部隊、給養等的）運輸船，運輸機；強烈的感情，狂喜；<史>流放犯"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用交通工具）運輸，運送；（以自然方式）運輸，傳播；使產生身臨其境的感覺；流放，放逐（犯人）；使狂喜，使（某人）充滿強烈情感（尤指快樂）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>transport</b> people or goods somewhere is to take them from one place to another in a vehicle. 運送","examples":["They are banned from launching any flights except to transport people. 他們被禁止飛行任何航班，運送人除外。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Transport</b> refers to any vehicle that you can travel in or carry goods in. 交通工具","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Transport</b> is a system for taking people or goods from one place to another, for example, using buses or trains. 交通運輸系統","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Transport</b> is the activity of taking goods or people from one place to another in a vehicle. 運輸","examples":[]}]}]},"trend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"趨勢，動態；時尚，風尚；熱門話題"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>趨向，傾向；（尤指地理特徵的）走向；成為熱門話題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trend</b> is a change or development toward something new or different. 趨勢","examples":["This is a growing trend. 這是一個不斷增長的趨勢。","...a trend toward part-time employment. …非全日制就業的趨勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To set a <b>trend</b> means to do something that becomes accepted or fashionable, and that a lot of other people copy. 時尚","examples":["The latest trend is gardening. 最新的時尚是園藝。"]}]}]},"tub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盆，桶；（用來盛食品的小型）帶蓋容器；浴缸；一盒的容量，一盆的容量；<非正式>行駛緩慢的舊船，老爺船（貶）；<非正式>矮胖子；（礦）礦車，礦鬥"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式> 浴缸，浴盆；盆栽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tub</b> is the same as a . 浴缸","examples":["She lay back in the tub. 她仰靠在浴缸裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tub</b> is a deep container of any size. 深的容器","examples":["He peeled the paper top off a little white tub and poured the cream into his coffee. 他撕去一個白色小杯的紙蓋子，把奶油倒進他的咖啡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>tub</b> to refer to a tub and its contents, or to the contents only. (一) 容器","examples":["She would eat four tubs of ice cream in one sitting. 她會一口氣吃下4杯冰淇淋。"]}]}]},"troop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軍隊，士兵；部隊，（尤指）騎兵連，裝甲連；童子軍中隊；一組，一群"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"成群結隊地走，列隊行進；（孤身一人）緩步前行，穩步前行；（尤指被告知）成群前往"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"軍隊的，有關或涉及軍隊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Troops</b> are soldiers, especially when they are in a large organized group doing a particular task. 士兵","examples":["The next phase of the operation will involve the deployment of more than 35,000 troops from a dozen countries. 下階段的行動包括部署來自12個國家的三萬五千多名士兵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>troop</b> is a group of soldiers. 一群士兵","examples":["...a troop of American Marines. …一群美國海軍陸戰隊士兵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>troop of</b> people or animals is a group of them. (一) 群","examples":["The whole troop of men and women wore their hair fairly short. 那一整群男女都留著相當短的頭髮。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>troop</b> somewhere, they walk there in a group, often in a sad or tired way. (尤指悲傷或疲憊地) 成群結隊地走","examples":["They all trooped back to the house for a rest. 他們都成群結隊地回房子裡休息。"]}]}]},"trunk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹幹；（人或動物的）軀幹；象鼻；<美>（汽車後部的）行李箱，後備箱；旅行箱，衣箱；男式游泳褲（trunks）；大血管，神經幹；電纜管道，通風管；拳擊手短褲（trunks）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幹線的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>trunk</b> of a tree is the large main stem from which the branches grow. 樹幹","examples":["...the gnarled trunk of a birch tree. …一棵長滿節瘤的樺樹的樹幹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trunk</b> is a large, strong case or box used for storing things or for taking on a trip. 大箱子","examples":["Maloney unlocked his trunk and took out some coveralls. 馬洛尼把他的大箱子的鎖開啟了，拿出了一些工作服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An elephant's <b>trunk</b> is its very long nose that it uses to lift food and water to its mouth. 象鼻","examples":["Manfred the elephant reached out with his trunk and gently scooped up the baby. 大象曼弗雷德伸出它的鼻子，輕輕地抱起了幼仔。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Trunks</b> are shorts that a man wears when he goes swimming. 男式游泳褲","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>trunk</b> is the central part of your body, from your neck to your waist. (人體的) 軀幹","examples":["The leg to be stretched should be positioned behind your trunk with your knee bent. 要伸展的那條腿應該放在軀幹的後面並彎曲膝蓋。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>trunk</b> of a car is the same as the . 後備箱","examples":[]}]}]},"tulip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬱金香"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tulips</b> are flowers that grow in the spring from bulbs, and have oval or pointed petals packed closely together. 鬱金香","examples":[]}]}]},"tummy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肚子，胃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>tummy</b> is the part of the front of your body below your waist. <b>Tummy</b> is often used by children or by adults talking to children. 肚子 (兒童化用語)","examples":["Your baby's tummy should feel warm, but not hot. 你寶寶的肚子摸起來應該是溫的，而不是熱的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>tummy</b> to refer to the parts inside your body where food is digested. <b>Tummy</b> is often used by children or by adults talking to children. 胃 (兒童化用語)","examples":["I've got a sore tummy. 我胃痛。","...a tummy ache. …胃痛。"]}]}]},"tug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用力地）拉，拖，拽；（迅速地）穿（衣服）；用拖船拖（船）；努力做"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拖船；猛拉，拽；一股強烈的感情；強大的吸引力；（滑翔機的）拖航飛機；（系在馬鞍上支承車槓或挽繩的）圓環；苦幹；競爭，較量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tug</b> something or <b>tug</b> <b>at</b> it, you give it a quick and usually strong pull. 猛拉; 拽","examples":["A little boy came running up and tugged at his sleeve excitedly. 一個小男孩跑了過來，興奮地拽著他的袖子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tug</b> is also a noun. 猛拉; 拽","examples":["I felt a tug at my sleeve. 我感覺我的袖子被拽了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tug</b> or a <b>tug boat</b> is a small powerful boat which pulls large ships, usually when they come into a port. 拖船","examples":["...a 76,000-ton barge pulled by five tug boats. …被5艘拖船拖拉著的一艘76000噸的駁船。"]}]}]},"twig":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小枝，嫩枝；（剖）血管小支，神經小支"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>頓悟，突然明白；<古>察覺，觀察"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>twig</b> is a very small thin branch that grows out from a main branch of a tree or bush. 細枝","examples":["There is the bird, sitting on a twig halfway up the tree. 鳥兒在那裡，棲息在樹中段的一根細枝上。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to understand (something) 理解","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to find out or suddenly comprehend (something) 發現; 頓悟","examples":[]}]}]},"tutor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家庭教師，私人教師；導師，指導教師；<美>大學助教；<英>（負責成人教育或在大中學中有特別任務的）教師；（尤指音樂）課本"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"指導，輔導，擔任私人教師；當家庭教師，當大學助教，當大學導師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tutor</b> is someone who gives private lessons to one student or a very small group of students. 家庭教師","examples":["...a Spanish tutor. …一位西班牙語家庭教師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In some American universities or colleges, a <b>tutor</b> is a teacher of the lowest rank. (一些美國大學或學院的) 助教","examples":[]}]}]},"tumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跌倒，滾落；倒塌，坍塌；（價值）暴跌；跌跌撞撞地走；（水）快速移動；（興奮或傷心地）快速說；翻跟頭；（頭髮）垂落；用滾筒甩幹；弄亂，弄皺；<非正式>性交；用滾筒把（寶石等）弄乾淨；"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跌倒，滾落，暴跌；混亂，雜亂；翻跟頭；<美，非正式>示好；<非正式>性交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>tumbles</b> somewhere, they fall there with a rolling or bouncing movement. 摔倒","examples":["A small boy tumbled off the porch. 一個小男孩從門廊上摔了下去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If prices or levels of something <b>are tumbling</b>, they are decreasing rapidly. (價格或水平) 暴跌","examples":["Profit after taxes tumbled by half to $15.8 million. 稅後利潤猛降了一半，跌到了1580萬美元。","Share prices continued to tumble today on the Tokyo stock market. 東京股市今天的股票價格繼續暴跌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If water <b>tumbles</b>, it flows quickly over an uneven surface. (水流) 翻滾","examples":["Waterfalls crash and tumble over rocks. 瀑布在岩石上撞擊翻滾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tumble</b> is also a noun. 摔","examples":["He injured his ribs in a tumble from his horse. 他從馬上摔下來傷了肋骨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tumble</b> is also a noun. (價格或水平的) 暴跌","examples":["Oil prices took a tumble yesterday. 石油價格昨天一陣暴跌。"]}]}]},"twin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雙胞胎之一，孿生兒之一；兩個極相似的事物之一，兩個非常相像的人中的一個；（有一對單人床的）雙人間；雙引擎飛機；孿晶體；雙子星座（the Twins）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雙胞胎的，孿生的；成對的，成雙的；雙重的，相關聯的，同時出現的；<英>（鎮或市）友好的，姐妹的；（植物）雙生的；（臥室）有兩張單人床的；（晶體）孿晶的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使結成姐妹城市，使結成友好城市；使（兩人或兩事物）緊密結合，使相連；生雙胞胎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twins</b> are two people who were born at the same time from the same mother. 雙胞胎","examples":["Sarah was looking after the twins. 薩拉當時正在照看雙胞胎。","I think there are many positive aspects to being a twin. 我認為作為雙胞胎之一有很多積極的方面。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twin</b> is used to describe a pair of things that look the same and are close together. 成對的; 成雙的","examples":["...the twin spires of the cathedral. …那座大教堂的雙尖頂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Twin</b> is used to describe two things or ideas that are similar or connected in some way. 相似的; 相關的","examples":["...the twin concepts of liberty and equality. …自由和平等這兩個相關的概念。"]}]}]},"universe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宇宙，天地萬物（the universe）；領域，體系；（已知宇宙以外的）宇宙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>universe</b> is the whole of space and all the stars, planets, and other forms of matter and energy in it. 宇宙","examples":["Einstein's equations showed the universe to be expanding. 愛因斯坦的方程式表明宇宙正在擴大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about someone's <b>universe</b>, you are referring to the whole of their experience or an important part of it. (某人的) 經歷","examples":["Good writers suck in what they see of the world, re-creating their own universe on the page. 好的作家吸收他們所看到的世界，在書裡重新創造自己的世界。"]}]}]},"typewriter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"打字機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>typewriter</b> is a machine with keys which are pressed in order to print letters, numbers, or other characters onto paper. 打字機","examples":[]}]}]},"tune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"曲調，曲子；歌曲，樂段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給樂器）調音，校音；（給收音機、電視等）調諧，調頻道；調整，調節（發動機）；調整，使適合；<南非，非正式>告訴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tune</b> is a series of musical notes that is pleasant and easy to remember. 曲調","examples":["She was humming a merry little tune. 她正哼著一曲歡快的小調。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a song or a short piece of music as a <b>tune</b>. 歌曲; 樂段","examples":["She'll also be playing your favourite pop tunes. 她也將演奏你最喜歡的流行歌曲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>tunes</b> a musical instrument, they adjust it so that it produces the right notes. 為 (樂器) 調音","examples":["\"We do tune our guitars before we go on,\" he insisted. “我們繼續演奏之前一定要為吉他定音，”他堅持說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an engine or machine <b>is tuned</b>, it is adjusted so that it works well. 調整 (發動機或機器)","examples":["Drivers are urged to make sure that car engines are properly tuned. 司機們被要求要確保把汽車發動機調整好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your radio or television <b>is tuned</b> <b>to</b> a particular channel or broadcasting station, you are listening to or watching the programmes being broadcast by that station. 調整 (頻道或頻率)","examples":["A small colour television was tuned to an afternoon soap opera. 一臺小彩電被調到了一個午後肥皂劇頻道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tune up</b> means the same as . 調音","examples":["Others were quietly tuning up their instruments. 其他人正安靜地為他們的樂器調音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tune up</b> means the same as . 調整","examples":["The shop charges up to $500 to tune up a Porsche. 該店除錯一輛保時捷的收費高達$500。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or organization <b>is calling the tune</b>, you mean that they are in a position of power or control in a particular situation. 定調子; 發號施令","examples":["It is Coulthard who is calling the tune so far this season. 本賽季到目前為止一直是庫特爾哈德發號施令。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has changed</b> their <b>tune</b>, you are criticizing them because they have changed their opinion or way of doing things. 改變調子 (指改變態度)","examples":["You've changed your tune since this morning, haven't you? 自從今天早上起你就改變了調子，不是嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A person or musical instrument that is <b>in tune</b> produces exactly the right notes. A person or musical instrument that is <b>out of tune</b> does not produce exactly the right notes. 合調的; 不合調的","examples":["It was just an ordinary voice, but he sang in tune. 嗓音只是一般，但他唱得很合調。"]}]}]},"unity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"團結，統一；整體性，統一性；三一律（指戲劇在時間、地點和情節三點上的統一性）；統一體；（數目或數字）一"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Unity</b> is the state of different areas or groups being joined together to form a single country or organization. 統一","examples":["We have to act to preserve the unity of this nation. 我們必須行動起來以維護這個國家的統一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When there is <b>unity</b>, people are in agreement and act together for a particular purpose. 團結; 一致","examples":["...a renewed unity of purpose. …目的的重新統一。","Speakers at the rally expressed sentiments of unity. 集會上的發言者們表達了團結的觀點。"]}]}]},"union":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工會；聯邦，聯盟；協會，俱樂部；聯合，合併；結婚，婚姻；美利堅合眾國（the Union）；（數）並，並集；聯管節，接頭；（印度次大陸）村落聯合體；<英，史>教區聯合濟貧組織；旗幟上象徵國家統一的部分；混紡織物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>union</b> is a workers' organization which represents its members and which tries to improve things such as their working conditions and pay. 工會","examples":["Do all teachers have a right to join a union? 所有的教師都有權利加入工會嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the <b>union</b> of two or more things occurs, they are joined together and become one thing. 合併","examples":["In 1918 the Romanian majority in this former czarist province voted for union with Romania. 1918年，這個前沙俄省份的大多數羅馬尼亞人投票支援與羅馬尼亞合併。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When two or more things, for example countries or organizations, have been joined together to form one thing, you can refer to them as a <b>union</b>. 聯盟","examples":["Tanzania is a union of the states of Tanganyika and Zanzibar. 坦尚尼亞是坦噶尼喀州和桑給巴爾州的聯盟。"]}]}]},"vase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花瓶，（裝飾用的）瓶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vase</b> is a jar, usually made of glass or pottery, used for holding cut flowers or as an ornament. 花瓶","examples":["...a vase of red roses. …一個插著紅玫瑰的花瓶。"]}]}]},"van":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（廂式）小型貨車；<美>麵包車；<英>（鐵路上運送包裹、郵件等的）車廂；<英>拖車；先鋒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用車搬運"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>van</b> is a small or medium-sized road vehicle with one row of seats at the front and a space for carrying goods behind. 中小型貨車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>van</b> is a railway wagon, often without windows, which is used to carry luggage, goods, or mail. 行李車廂","examples":["The coffin was loaded into the van of the train. 棺材被裝進了火車的行李車廂內。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"caravan的縮寫","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"vanguard的縮寫","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"advantage的縮寫 (Usual US and Canadian word ad)","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"any device for winnowing corn 揚穀機","examples":[]}]}]},"upset":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使心煩意亂，使生氣；打亂，攪亂；打翻，使傾覆；翻倒；意外擊敗（強對手）；使（腸胃）不適；製造麻煩，破壞某人的計劃；鐓鍛，鐓粗"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不高興的，心煩意亂的；（腸胃）不適的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"煩惱，失望；腸胃不適；爆冷門；混亂，麻煩；翻倒，顛覆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>upset</b>, you are unhappy or disappointed because something unpleasant has happened to you. 難過的; 沮喪的","examples":["After she died I felt very, very upset. 她死後，我感覺非常非常難過。","Marta looked upset. 瑪爾塔看起來很沮喪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"令人煩惱的; 使人不高興的","examples":["Childhood illness can be upsetting for children and parents alike. 童年的疾病能使孩子和父母同樣苦惱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Upset</b> is also an adjective. 不舒服的","examples":["Larry has an upset stomach. 拉里胃不舒服。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Upset</b> is also a noun. 煩惱; 失望","examples":["...stress and other emotional upsets. …壓力和其他情感上的煩惱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Upset</b> is also a noun. 混亂","examples":["Markets are very sensitive to any upsets in the Japanese economic machine. 市場對日本經濟機器裡的任何混亂都是非常敏感的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A stomach <b>upset</b> is a slight illness in your stomach caused by an infection or by something that you have eaten. (胃) 不舒服","examples":["Paul was unwell last night with a stomach upset. 保羅昨晚胃不舒服。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>upsets</b> you, it makes you feel worried or unhappy. 使…煩惱; 使…不高興","examples":["The whole incident had upset me and my fiancée terribly. 整個事件已使我和我的未婚妻非常煩惱。","She warned me not to say anything to upset him. 她警告我不要說任何讓他心煩的話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If events <b>upset</b> something such as a procedure or a state of affairs, they cause it to go wrong. 攪亂","examples":["These latest comments could upset the peace negotiations which are due to begin next week. 這些最新的評論可能攪亂定於下週開始的和平談判。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>upset</b> an object, you accidentally knock or push it over so that it scatters over a large area. 弄翻","examples":["Don't upset the piles of sheets under the box. 別碰亂了盒子下面的那幾摞紙。"]}]}]},"twist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使彎曲；（使）扭曲變形；扭動身體；扭傷（腳踝等）；旋轉，轉動；編織，捻在一起；纏繞；歪曲，曲解；蜿蜒，曲折；<英，非正式>欺詐；牌面朝上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"扭動，轉動；彎曲處，拐彎處；轉折，變化；螺旋形物體；扭擺舞（the twist）；扭歪，（性格）反常；（棉，絲） 合股線；<英>混合酒；<英，非正式>欺詐；（棍棒或其他物體） 扭轉度；扭轉力，轉矩；繞軸旋轉前進"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> something, you turn it to make a spiral shape, for example, by turning the two ends of it in opposite directions. 扭曲; 擰","examples":["Her hands began to twist the handles of the bag she carried. 她的雙手開始擰她拎著的那個包的拎柄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> something, especially a part of your body, or if it <b>twists</b>, it moves into an unusual, uncomfortable, or bent position, for example, because of being hit or pushed, or because you are upset. 扭彎; 扭曲","examples":["He twisted her arms behind her back and clipped a pair of handcuffs on her wrists. 他把她的雙臂扭到她的背後，把一副手銬扣在她的手腕上。","Sophia's face twisted in perplexity. 索菲婭的臉因困惑而扭曲著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> part of your body such as your head or your shoulders, you turn that part while keeping the rest of your body still. 轉動 (身體某部分)","examples":["She twisted her head sideways and looked toward the door. 她把頭轉向一邊，朝門口看去。","Susan twisted round in her seat until she could see Graham behind her. 蘇珊在她的座位上轉過身去，直到她能看見她身後的格雷厄姆。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> a part of your body such as your ankle or wrist, you injure it by turning it too sharply, or in an unusual direction. 扭傷 (腳踝或手腕等)","examples":["He fell and twisted his ankle. 他摔了一跤，扭傷了腳踝。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> something, you turn it so that it moves around in a circular direction. 旋轉","examples":["She was staring down at her hands, twisting the ring on her finger. 她往下盯著自己的手，旋轉著手指上的戒指。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has twisted</b> something that you have said, you disapprove of them because they have repeated it in a way that changes its meaning, in order to harm you or benefit themselves. 歪曲","examples":["It's a shame the way the media can twist your words and misrepresent you. 媒體歪曲人們的話語及誤傳人們的本意的作風是可恥的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twist</b> is also a noun. 旋轉","examples":["Just a twist of the handle is all it takes to wring out the mop. 只需旋轉一下那個手柄就可以擰乾拖把。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Twist</b> is also a noun. (道路或河流的) 迂迴曲折","examples":["It allows the train to maintain a constant speed through the twists and turns of existing track. 它可以讓火車在現有蜿蜒盤旋的軌道上保持勻速。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>twist</b> in something is an unexpected and significant development. 意外進展","examples":["The battle of the sexes also took a new twist. 性別之戰也有了意想不到的新進展。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a road or river <b>twists</b>, it has a lot of sudden changes of direction in it. (道路或河流) 迂迴曲折","examples":["The roads twist around hairpin bends. 那些道路有很多險彎。"]}]}]},"vice-president":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"副總裁；副總統；副校長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an officer ranking immediately below a president and serving as his deputy. A vice president takes the president's place during his absence or incapacity, after his death, and in certain other circumstances 副總統; 副主席; 副總裁 (Abbreviation VP, V. Pres)","examples":[]}]}]},"variety":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"多樣化，變化；種類，品種；（人或物的）各式各樣；綜藝表演，雜耍表演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something has <b>variety</b>, it consists of things that are different from each other. 多樣化","examples":["Susan's idea of freedom was to have variety in her life style. 蘇珊對自由的理解就是擁有生活方式的多樣化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>variety</b> <b>of</b> things is a number of different kinds or examples of the same thing. (同一事物的) 一些不同種類","examples":["West Hampstead has a variety of good stores and supermarkets. 西漢普斯特德有幾家不同的高品質商店和超市。","The island offers such a wide variety of scenery and wildlife. 這座島嶼有如此豐富多樣的景色和野生動植物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>variety</b> of something is a type of it. 品種","examples":["I'm always pleased to try out a new variety. 我一直樂於嘗試新的品種。"]}]}]},"verse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩，韻文；詩節，（歌曲的）節；（《聖經》或其他經文的）節，句；（讚美詩的）獨唱部，小組唱部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>作詩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Verse</b> is writing arranged in lines that have rhythm and that often rhyme at the end. 詩; 韻文","examples":["I have been moved to write a few lines of verse. 我曾經被感動得寫了幾行詩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>verse</b> is one of the parts into which a poem, a song, or a chapter of the Bible or the Koran is divided. 詩節; 歌曲的段落; (《聖經》、《古蘭經》的) 節","examples":["This verse describes three signs of spring. 這節詩描述了春天的3個徵兆。"]}]}]},"vest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英> 背心，汗衫； <美>馬甲，西裝背心；坎肩，（特製的）背心；（無袖保暖）內衣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>授予，賦予，給予（權利或責任）；（權力、財產等）交給，歸屬；（唱詩班歌手，神職人員）穿聖衣，穿法衣；<文>給……穿衣服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vest</b> is a piece of underwear that you can wear on the top half of your body in order to keep warm. 背心","examples":["He put on a pair of boxer shorts and a vest. 他穿上一條平腿短褲和一件背心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vest</b> is a sleeveless piece of clothing with buttons that people usually wear over a shirt. 馬甲","examples":[]}]}]},"vehicle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交通工具，車輛；（實現目的的）工具，媒介；（為展露主演者才華而）度身定製的創作（電影、電視節目、歌曲等）；賦形藥，調漆料；（個人，組織從事經營、尤指投資的）公司"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vehicle</b> is a machine with an engine, such as a bus, car, or truck, that carries people or things from place to place. 機動車輛","examples":["...a vehicle that was somewhere between a tractor and a truck. …一輛介於拖拉機和卡車之間的機動車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>vehicle</b> to refer to something that you use in order to achieve a particular purpose. 媒介","examples":["Her art became a vehicle for her political beliefs. 她的藝術成了她政治信仰的媒介。"]}]}]},"victim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"受害者，罹難者；（面對不幸事件或虐待時的）無助者，患病者；犧牲品，祭品；受騙者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>victim</b> is someone who has been hurt or killed. 受害者","examples":["Statistically our chances of being the victims of violent crime are remote. 從統計上來看，我們成為暴力犯罪受害者的可能性是微乎其微的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>victim</b> is someone who has suffered as a result of someone else's actions or beliefs, or as a result of unpleasant circumstances. 犧牲品","examples":["He was a victim of racial prejudice. 他是種族偏見的一個犧牲品。","He described himself and Altman as victims rather than participants in the scandal. 他把自己和奧爾特曼描述成這一醜聞的受害者，而不是參與者。"]}]}]},"violence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴力，暴行；（言行的）狂暴，激烈，憤怒；巨大的破壞力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Violence</b> is behaviour that is intended to hurt, injure, or kill people. 暴力行為","examples":["Twenty people were killed in the violence. 有20人在這起暴力事件中被殺害。","...domestic violence between husband and wife. …夫妻間的家庭暴力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do or say something with <b>violence</b>, you use a lot of force and energy in doing or saying it, often because you are angry. 激烈","examples":["The violence in her tone gave Tyler a shock. 她語氣激烈，使泰勒大為震驚。"]}]}]},"violet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紫羅蘭，堇菜；藍紫色，紫羅蘭色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紫色的，紫羅蘭色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>violet</b> is a small plant that has purple or white flowers in the spring. 紫羅蘭","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>violet</b> is a bluish-purple colour. 紫羅蘭色的","examples":["The light was beginning to drain from a violet sky. 光線正開始從紫羅蘭色的天空中漸漸消失。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is no <b>shrinking violet</b>, you mean that they are not at all shy. 羞澀的人","examples":["When it comes to expressing himself he is no shrinking violet. 他表達自己看法時一點都不羞澀。"]}]}]},"vitamin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"維生素，維他命；維生素片，維生素丸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vitamins</b> are substances that you need in order to remain healthy, which are found in food or can be eaten in the form of pills. 維生素","examples":["Lack of vitamin D is another factor to consider. 缺乏維生素D是另一個需要考慮的因素。"]}]}]},"wages":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（wage 的複數）工資，報酬，工錢；<書面>應得的報償或懲罰（如 the wages of sin）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開展，發動（運動、戰爭等）（wage 的第三人稱單數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>wages</b> are the amount of money that is regularly paid to them for the work that they do. 工資","examples":["His wages have gone up. 他的工資漲了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, group, or country <b>wages</b> a campaign or a war, they start it and continue it over a period of time. 發動 (運動或戰爭)","examples":["The government, along with the three factions that had been waging a civil war, signed a peace agreement. 政府和發動了內戰的3方一起簽訂了1份和平協議。"]}]}]},"wag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搖擺（尾巴）；（手指或頭部）搖擺；<澳新，非正式>逃學；議論紛紛（tongues are wagging）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搖動，擺動；<舊>老開玩笑的人；老婆俱樂部"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"甘比亞（國際車輛登記程式碼）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a dog <b>wags</b> its tail, it repeatedly waves its tail from side to side. (狗) 搖擺 (尾巴)","examples":["The dog was biting, growling and wagging its tail. 那條狗咬著叫著，還搖著尾巴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wag</b> your finger, you shake it repeatedly and quickly from side to side, usually because you are annoyed with someone. 搖晃 (手指)","examples":["He wagged a disapproving finger. 他搖搖手指表示不贊成。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act or an instance of wagging 搖擺","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a humorous or jocular person; wit 愛說笑打趣的人","examples":[]}]}]},"wagon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（一般由馬拉的）四輪運貨車；<英>（無頂的）鐵路貨車車廂，車皮；旅行轎車（station wagon 的簡稱）；<美>（用作食品貨攤的）手推車；兒童玩具小車；（吉卜賽人或馬戲團用的）大篷車；<愛爾蘭，非正式>令人不快的女人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用運貨馬車運輸貨物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wagon</b> is a strong vehicle with four wheels, usually pulled by horses or oxen and used for carrying heavy loads. 四輪運貨馬 (或牛) 車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wagon</b> is a large container on wheels which is pulled by a train. (火車的) 貨車車廂","examples":[]}]}]},"volume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體積，容積；總數，總量；音量，響度；（控制音量的）旋鈕，控制桿；（成套圖書中的）卷，冊；（期刊）合訂本；書籍；<史>（寫在羊皮紙或紙草紙上的）書卷；（尤指頭髮的）厚，多"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大量的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以卷的形式發出；成團捲起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>volume</b> <b>of</b> something is the amount of it that there is. 量","examples":["Senior officials will be discussing how the volume of sales might be reduced. 高階官員們將討論如何才能減少銷售量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>volume</b> of an object is the amount of space that it contains or occupies. 容積","examples":["When egg whites are beaten they can rise to seven or eight times their original volume. 打過的蛋清，體積可以漲到原來的七八倍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>volume</b> is one book in a series of books. (書籍的) 卷","examples":["...the first volume of his autobiography. …他自傳的第一卷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>volume</b> is a collection of several issues of a magazine, for example, all the issues for one year. 合訂本","examples":["...bound volumes of the magazine. …雜誌的合訂本。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>volume</b> of a radio, television, or sound system is the loudness of the sound it produces. (收音機、電視機或音響系統的) 音量","examples":["He turned down the volume. 他調低了音量。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as an action <b>speaks volumes</b> <b>about</b> a person or thing, it gives you a lot of information about them. 充分表明","examples":["What you wear speaks volumes about you. 你的穿戴能充分表明你的方方面面。"]}]}]},"wage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工資，報酬；（經濟）工資總額；（喻）報應"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"進行，發動（戰爭，運動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>wages</b> are the amount of money that is regularly paid to them for the work that they do. 工資","examples":["His wages have gone up. 他的工資漲了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, group, or country <b>wages</b> a campaign or a war, they start it and continue it over a period of time. 發動 (運動或戰爭)","examples":["The government, along with the three factions that had been waging a civil war, signed a peace agreement. 政府和發動了內戰的3方一起簽訂了1份和平協議。"]}]}]},"vision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幻想，想象；幻覺，幻象；構想，展望；眼力，遠見卓識；視力，視覺；視野；美好的人（或事物）；（電視或電影的）影象"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<罕>想像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>vision</b> <b>of</b> a future situation or society is what you imagine or hope it would be like, if things were very different from the way they are now. 憧憬","examples":["I have a vision of a society that is free of exploitation and injustice. 我憧憬一個沒有剝削和不公的社會。","That's my vision of how the world could be. 那就是我對這個世界未來的憧憬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>vision</b> <b>of</b> someone in a particular situation, you imagine them in that situation, for example because you are worried that it might happen, or hope that it will happen. 想像","examples":["He had a vision of Cheryl, slumped on a plastic chair in the waiting room. 他想像謝麗爾跌坐在候診室的一把塑膠椅子上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>vision</b> is the experience of seeing something that other people cannot see, for example in a religious experience or as a result of madness or taking drugs. 幻覺","examples":["It was on June 24, 1981 that young villagers first reported seeing the Virgin Mary in a vision. 那是在1981年的6月24日，年輕的村民們首次報告說在幻覺中看到了聖母瑪利亞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>vision</b> is your ability to see clearly with your eyes. 視力","examples":["It causes blindness or serious loss of vision. 這會引起失明或嚴重的視力衰退。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>vision</b> is everything that you can see from a particular place or position. 視野","examples":["Jane blocked Craig's vision and he could see nothing. 簡擋住了克雷格的視線，他什麼也看不見了。"]}]}]},"warmth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溫暖，暖和；熱情，友好；激動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>warmth</b> of something is the heat that it has or produces. 溫暖","examples":["She went further into the room, drawn by the warmth of the fire. 她被火的溫暖吸引著，走進了房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>warmth</b> of something such as a garment or blanket is the protection that it gives you against the cold. 保暖","examples":["The blanket will provide additional warmth and comfort in bed. 毯子能讓你睡覺時感覺更溫暖更舒適。"]}]}]},"wander":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"漫遊，遊蕩，漫步，流浪；走神，開小差；偏離，走偏（道路、航線等）；（目光）遊移，往別處看；（河流、道路等）蜿蜒曲折；離題；（因年老而）神志恍惚，精神錯亂；在人的身上摸來摸去（尤指他人不情願時）；（對固定的性伴侶）不忠"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"遊蕩，漫步"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wander</b> in a place, you walk around there in a casual way, often without intending to go in any particular direction. 漫步","examples":["When he got bored he wandered around the fair. 煩悶時，他便在集市上四處閒逛。","They wandered off in the direction of the nearest shop. 他們朝著最近那家店鋪的方向閒逛去了。","People wandered the streets aimlessly. 人們在街上漫無目的地閒逛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wander</b> is also a noun. 漫步","examples":["A wander around any market will reveal stalls piled high with vegetables. 在哪個市場上閒逛都會發現高高堆著蔬菜的攤子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>wanders</b> from a place where they are supposed to stay, they move away from the place without going in a particular direction. 走開","examples":["Because Mother is afraid we'll get lost, we aren't allowed to wander far. 母親因為害怕我們走丟了，不准我們走遠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your mind <b>wanders</b> or your thoughts <b>wander</b>, you stop concentrating on something and start thinking about other things. 心不在焉","examples":["His mind would wander, and he would lose track of what he was doing. 他會心不在焉起來，忘了自己剛才正在幹什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your eyes <b>wander</b>, you stop looking at one thing and start looking around at other things. (目光) 無目的地移動","examples":["His eyes wandered restlessly around the room. 他的眼睛不停地打量著房間。"]}]}]},"wax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蠟，蜂蠟；耳垢； <英，非正式，舊>一陣憤怒；<非正式>唱片；類似蠟的黏性物質（尤指液體或碳氫化合物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……上（或打）蠟；用蠟除去（身體部位）的毛髮；（月亮）漸圓，漸滿；（帶著某種情緒）說，寫；（數量、規模等）增加，變大；<非正式>把……灌製成唱片"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"蠟制的，似蠟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wax</b> is a solid, slightly shiny substance made of fat or oil that is used to make candles and polish. It melts when it is heated. 蠟","examples":["There were coloured candles which had spread pools of wax on the furniture. 彩色蠟燭在傢俱上留下了一攤攤的蠟油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wax</b> is the sticky yellow substance found in your ears. 耳垢","examples":["Use a cotton bud to remove the wax from your ears. 用棉花棒挖掉你耳朵裡的耳垢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a fit of rage or temper 發怒; 生氣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wax</b> a surface, you put a thin layer of wax onto it, especially in order to polish it. 給…上蠟","examples":["We'd have long talks while she helped me wax the floor. 她幫我給地板上蠟時，我們閒聊了很長時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a part of your body <b>waxed</b>, for example your legs, you have the hair removed from the area by having wax put on it and then pulled off quickly. (用蠟) 去毛","examples":["She has just had her legs waxed at the local beauty parlour. 她剛在當地的美容院用蠟去了腿毛。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to become larger, more powerful, etc 變更大; 變更強大","examples":[]}]}]},"wealth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"財富；富有；大量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wealth</b> is the possession of a large amount of money, property, or other valuable things. You can also refer to a particular person's money or property as their <b>wealth</b>. 財富","examples":["Economic reform has brought relative wealth to peasant farmers. 經濟改革使農民相對富裕起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>a wealth of</b> good qualities or things, you are emphasizing that they have a very large number or amount of them. 大量的","examples":["Their websites contain a wealth of information on the topic. 他們的網站上有大量與該主題相關的資訊。","The city boasts a wealth of beautiful churches. 該城引以為榮的是有大量漂亮的教堂。"]}]}]},"wheat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小麥（植物），小麥（籽實）；<美>小麥麵包；小麥色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wheat</b> is a cereal crop grown for food. <b>Wheat</b> is also used to refer to the grain of this crop, which is usually ground into flour and used to make bread. 小麥","examples":["...farmers growing wheat, corn, or other crops. …種小麥、玉米或其他農作物的農民們。"]}]}]},"web":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（蜘蛛）網；網狀物，錯綜複雜的事物；網路；（鳥獸的）蹼；連線板，金屬薄條（片）；（連續印刷用）一卷紙；（製造捲筒紙的造紙機上的）無端金屬絲網；織物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用網（或網狀物）覆蓋；使中圈套；形成網"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The Web</b> is a computer system that links documents and pictures into a database that is stored in computers in many different parts of the world and that people everywhere can use. It is also referred to as the <b>World Wide Web</b>. 網際網路","examples":["The handbook is available on the Web. 這本手冊網際網路上有。","She recommended the service on her Web journal after trying it out. 在經過試用後，她在自己的網路雜誌中推薦了這項服務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>web</b> is a complicated pattern of connections or relationships, sometimes considered as an obstacle or a danger. 錯綜複雜的事物","examples":["He's forced to untangle a complex web of financial dealings. 他被迫去理順一大堆錯綜複雜的金融交易。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>web</b> is the thin net made by a spider from a sticky substance that it produces in its body. 蜘蛛網","examples":["...the spider's web in the window. …窗戶上的蜘蛛網。"]}]}]},"weave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用織布機）編，織；（用……）編成；編造（故事或計劃）；將（素材等）編入（故事或設計中）；迂迴行進，穿行（以避開障礙）；（蜘蛛）結網；（駕機）繞飛，作閃避動作；（馬）不斷左右搖晃頭部和前身"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"編法，織法，編織式樣；編織圖案；（使頭髮顯得厚密或更長的）織發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>weave</b> cloth or a carpet, you make it by crossing threads over and under each other using a frame or machine called a loom. 織","examples":["They would spin and weave cloth, cook and attend to the domestic side of life. 他們紡紗、織布、做飯，還料理家務。","She sat at her loom and continued to weave. 她坐在織布機前，繼續織布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>weave</b> something such as a basket, you make it by crossing long plant stems or fibers over and under each other. 編織 (籃子等)","examples":["Jenny weaves baskets from willow she grows herself. 珍妮用自己栽種的柳樹的枝條編織籃子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>weave</b> your way somewhere, you move between and around things as you go there. 迂迴行進","examples":["The cars then weaved in and out of traffic at top speed. 汽車然後在車流中高速穿梭前進。","He weaved around the tables to where she sat with Bob. 他在桌子間穿梭走動，來到她和鮑勃坐的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"編織的","examples":["...woven cotton fabrics. …棉織物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"編織的","examples":["The floors are covered with woven straw mats. 地板上鋪著用草編織的墊子。"]}]}]},"weed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"野草，雜草；<非正式>香菸，菸草（the weed）；水草，水生植物；大麻；<非正式>瘦弱的人，懦弱的人；<非正式>（長腿）瘦弱的馬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"除草，為……除雜草"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weed</b> is a wild plant that grows in gardens or fields of crops and prevents the plants that you want from growing properly. 雜草","examples":["With repeated applications of weedkiller, the weeds were overcome. 反覆的施除草劑後，雜草終於被消滅了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>weed</b> an area, you remove the weeds from it. 除草","examples":["Caspar was weeding the garden. 卡斯帕正在給花園除草。","Try not to walk on the flowerbeds while weeding. 除草的時候儘量不要在花壇上走。"]}]}]},"weep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（通常因悲傷）哭泣，流淚；（傷口）流出液體，滲出膿液；哭著說；<古>哀悼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"哭泣，落淚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>weeps</b>, they cry. 哭泣","examples":["She wanted to laugh and weep all at once. 她哭笑不得。","The weeping family hugged and comforted each other. 一家人相擁而泣，互相安慰著。","She wept tears of joy. 她喜極而泣。"]}]}]},"willow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"柳，柳樹；柳木（常用以製作板球拍）；柳木製品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>willow</b> or a <b>willow tree</b> is a type of tree with long branches and long narrow leaves that grows near water. 柳樹","examples":[]}]}]},"wink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"眨眼示意，使眼色；（燈光）閃爍，明滅"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"眨眼（示意），眼色；<非正式>一會兒，一瞬間；小憩；閃爍；彈塑膠片遊戲中用的塑膠圓片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wink</b> <b>at</b> someone, you look toward them and close one eye very briefly, usually as a signal that something is a joke or a secret. 眨眼示意","examples":["Brian winked at his bride-to-be. 布賴恩向他的準新娘眨眼示意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wink</b> is also a noun. 眨眼","examples":["I gave her a wink. 我向她眨了眨眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a disc used in the game of tiddlywinks 彈塑膠片遊戲中用的塑膠圓片","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>did not sleep a wink</b> or <b>did not get a wink of sleep</b>, you mean that you tried to go to sleep but could not. 沒合一下眼","examples":["I didn't get a wink of sleep on the flight. 我在飛行過程中沒有合一下眼。"]}]}]},"whip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞭子，皮鞭；黨鞭，政黨紀律委員；（用雞蛋、鮮奶油與水果混合製成的）甜品；書面通知；鞭打，抽打；<喻>鞭策物，刺激物；鞭狀枝，鞭狀植物；<美>（用於割某些莊稼的）長柄大鐮刀，釤刀；<英>黨員資格（the whip）；定單絞轆；<非正式>車；（專管把離群獵狗趕回狗群的）獵人副手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鞭打，抽；快速移開，快速拿走；快速移動（某物）；攪打（奶油或蛋清使成糊狀）；<非正式>偷盜，盜取；（在外力作用下）猛然移動；（柔韌性的物體、雨、風等）拍打，猛打；（故意）激起（情緒）；<非正式>徹底擊敗；急投，急傳；將細繩纏繞於（某物），用細繩纏繞加固"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>whip</b> is a long thin piece of material such as leather or rope, fastened to a stiff handle. It is used for hitting people or animals. 鞭子","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"鞭打","examples":["He threatened to give her a whipping. 他威脅要鞭打她一頓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a member of a party chosen to organize and discipline the members of his faction, esp in voting and to assist in the arrangement of the business 在議會中負責組織工作的議員","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a call issued to members of a party, insisting with varying degrees of urgency upon their presence or loyal voting behaviour 發給黨員的召喚","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"(in the British Parliament) a schedule of business sent to members of a party each week. Each item on it is underlined to indicate its importance: one line means that no division is expected, two lines means that the item is fairly important, and three lines means that the item is very important and every member must attend and vote according to the party line (英國國會)政黨每週發給本黨議員有關下週議事日程的通知","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>whips</b> a person or animal, they beat them or hit them with a whip or something like a whip. 鞭打","examples":["Eye-witnesses claimed Mr. Melton whipped the horse up to 16 times. 目擊者聲稱梅爾頓先生抽打那匹馬達16鞭之多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>whips</b> something out or <b>whips</b> it off, they take it out or take it off very quickly and suddenly. 猛地拿出; 猛地脫掉","examples":["Bob whipped out his notebook. 鮑勃猛地拿出他的筆記本。","Players were whipping their shirts off. 選手們正麻利地脫掉襯衣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>whip</b> something liquid such as cream or an egg, you stir it very fast until it is thick or stiff. 攪打 (奶油或雞蛋等液體使粘稠)","examples":["Whip the cream until thick. 將奶油打稠。","Whip the eggs, oils and honey together. 將雞蛋、油和蜂蜜攪打在一起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>whip</b> people <b>into</b> an emotional state, you deliberately cause and encourage them to be in that state. 慫恿","examples":["He could whip a crowd into hysteria. 他可以慫恿一群人，使他們變得歇斯底里。"]}]}]},"whistle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"哨子；口哨聲；哨子聲；（火車、船或工廠等地的）汽笛，警笛；汽笛聲，警笛聲；呼嘯聲；小豎笛；（鳥的）囀鳴聲；<英>一套衣服，一手同花色牌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吹口哨，用口哨吹奏（曲調）；（向某人）吹口哨（以喚起注意或表示愛憎）；吹哨示意；鳴響；（鳥）囀鳴；迅速移動，呼嘯而過；得不到，空指望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>whistle</b> or when you <b>whistle</b> a tune, you make a series of musical notes by forcing your breath out between your lips, or your teeth. 用口哨吹出; 吹口哨","examples":["He whistled and sang snatches of songs. 他邊用口哨吹邊唱了幾個歌曲的片段。","He was whistling softly to himself. 他自娛自樂地輕聲吹著口哨。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>whistles</b>, they make a sound by forcing their breath out between their lips or their teeth. People sometimes whistle when they are surprised, or to call a dog, to get someone's attention, or to show that they are impressed. 吹口哨 (表示吃驚、呼喚小狗、引人注意或表示欣賞)","examples":["He whistled, surprised but not shocked. 他吹了聲口哨，有些驚訝，但並不震驚。","Jenkins whistled through his teeth, impressed at last. 詹金斯從齒間吹了一聲口哨，總算被打動了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a train or a kettle <b>whistles</b>, it makes a loud, high sound. (火車等) 鳴汽笛; (水開時水壺) 發出尖嘯聲","examples":["Somewhere a train whistled. 某個地方響起了火車的鳴笛聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as the wind or a bullet <b>whistles</b> somewhere, it moves there, making a loud, high sound. (風、子彈等) 呼嘯而過","examples":["The wind was whistling through the building. 風呼嘯著穿過那座大樓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whistle</b> is also a noun. 口哨","examples":["Jackson gave a low whistle. 傑克遜低聲地吹了一下口哨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>whistle</b> is a loud sound produced by air or steam being forced through a small opening, or by something moving quickly through the air. (某物在空中疾馳而過的) 呼嘯聲; (空氣、蒸汽透過狹小孔道時的) 尖嘯聲","examples":["...the whistle of the wind. …風的呼嘯聲。","...a shrill whistle from the boiling kettle. …燒開的水壺發出的刺耳的尖嘯聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>whistle</b> is a small metal tube that you blow in order to produce a loud sound and attract someone's attention. 哨子","examples":["On the platform, the guard blew his whistle. 站臺上，警衛吹響了他的哨子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blow the whistle</b> <b>on</b> someone, or on something secret or illegal, you tell another person, especially a person in authority, what is happening. (尤指向當局) 揭發","examples":["Companies should protect employees who blow the whistle on dishonest workmates and work practices. 公司應該保護那些揭發不誠實的同事和不良工作行為的員工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>clean as a whistle</b>, you mean that it is completely clean. 一塵不染","examples":["The kitchen was clean as a whistle. 廚房裡一塵不染。"]}]}]},"x-ray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"X 射線，X 光；X 光照片；X 光檢查；（無線電通訊中使用的）字母 X 的程式碼詞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用 X 光檢查，使用 X 光，給…拍 X 光片"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"X 光的，與 X 射線有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>X-rays</b> are a type of radiation that can pass through most solid materials. X-rays are used by doctors to examine the bones or organs inside your body and are also used at airports to see inside people's luggage. X射線","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>X-ray</b> is a picture made by sending X-rays through something, usually someone's body. X光片","examples":["She was advised to have an abdominal X-ray. 她被建議拍個腹部X光片。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is X-rayed</b>, an X-ray picture is taken of them. 給…拍攝X光片","examples":["All hand baggage would be x-rayed. 所有手提行李都要拍X光片。"]}]}]},"wrist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手腕，腕關節；（四足動物前腿的）膝關節，（鳥翅膀的）腕；袖口，腕部；（機器的）曲柄銷，肘節銷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>wrist</b> is the part of your body between your hand and your arm that bends when you move your hand. 手腕","examples":["He broke his wrist climbing rocks for a cigarette ad. 他為了一個香菸廣告攀巖折斷了手腕。"]}]}]},"wisdom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"智慧，才智；明智；學問，知識；普遍看法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wisdom</b> is the ability to use your experience and knowledge in order to make sensible decisions or judgments. 智慧","examples":["...the patience and wisdom that comes from old age. …老年的耐心和智慧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about <b>the wisdom of</b> a particular decision or action, you are talking about how sensible it is. 明智","examples":["Many Lithuanians have expressed doubts about the wisdom of the decision. 許多立陶宛人都已經對這個決定是否明智表示了懷疑。"]}]}]},"yawn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打哈欠；（開口、洞穴等）豁開，裂開"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"哈欠；<非正式>乏味的事物（或人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>yawn</b>, you open your mouth very wide and breathe in more air than usual, often when you are tired or when you are not interested in something. 打哈欠","examples":["She yawned, and stretched lazily. 她打了個哈欠，伸了個懶腰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yawn</b> is also a noun. 哈欠","examples":["Rosanna stifled a huge yawn. 羅莎娜忍住了一個大哈欠。"]}]}]},"yell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"叫喊，大喊；<非正式> 喊叫幫忙"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"叫喊，吼叫；<美>（為運動隊加油的）吶喊，歡呼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>yell</b>, you shout loudly, usually because you are excited, angry, or in pain. (因興奮、生氣或痛苦) 大聲叫喊","examples":["\"Eva!\" he yelled. “伊娃！”他大聲叫道。","I'm sorry I yelled at you last night. 很抱歉我昨晚對你大喊大叫了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yell out</b> means the same as . 大聲叫","examples":["\"Are you coming or not?\" they yelled out after him. “你來還是不來？”他們在他身後大聲叫喊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yell</b> is a loud shout given by someone who is afraid or in pain. (恐懼或痛苦中的人發出的) 大聲叫喊","examples":["Something brushed past Bob's face and he let out a yell. 什麼東西擦過了鮑勃的臉，他發出了一聲大叫。"]}]}]},"yolk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛋黃；（生物學）卵黃；（紡織）羊毛脂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>yolk</b> of an egg is the yellow part in the middle. 蛋黃","examples":["Only the yolk contains cholesterol. 只有蛋黃含膽固醇。"]}]}]},"zipper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拉鍊；（新聞或廣告的）建築物外牆滾動亮屏顯示"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拉上……的拉鍊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>zipper</b> is the same as a . 拉鎖","examples":["...the metal zipper on his jacket. …他的夾克上的金屬拉鎖。"]}]}]},"youngster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"年輕人，少年"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Young people, especially children, are sometimes referred to as <b>youngsters</b>. 年輕人 (尤指小孩)","examples":["Other youngsters are not so lucky. 其他的年輕人沒有這麼幸運。"]}]}]},"wipe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用布、手等）擦乾淨，抹掉；擦掉（液體、汙垢、印跡）；把（某物）擦乾淨；消除，抹去（計算機、磁帶或錄影機上的資訊等）；擦乾（洗過的碟子、杯子）；抹去（舊事）；徹底去除（或消滅）（某物）；塗抹（液體）；<澳/新，非正式>拒絕（某人，觀點），解僱（某人）；刷（卡）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（溼）抹布，紙巾；擦，拭，擦淨；劃變"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wipe</b> something, you rub its surface to remove dirt or liquid from it. 擦拭","examples":["I'll just wipe the table. 我只擦擦桌子。","When he had finished washing he began to wipe the basin clean. 他洗漱完後開始把水盆擦乾淨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wipe</b> dirt or liquid from something, you remove it by using a cloth or your hand. (用布或手) 擦去","examples":["Gleb wiped the sweat from his face. 格萊布擦去了臉上的汗水。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wipe</b> is also a noun. 擦拭","examples":["Tomorrow I'm going to give the toys a good wipe as some seem a bit greasy. 明天我會把那些玩具好好擦拭一番，因為有些看上去有點油膩了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wipe</b> is a small moist cloth for cleaning things and is designed to be used only once. 一次性溼巾","examples":["...antiseptic wipes. …一次性殺菌溼巾。"]}]}]},"wrap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包，裹，包裝；用（手臂、指頭或腿）圍緊，用……繞住；繞……走；完成拍攝，殺青 ；<非正式>使（車輛）撞上（固定物體）；（使文字）換行"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"披肩，圍巾； 包裹（或包裝）材料；寬鬆外套，浴衣；面捲餅（一種三明治，由薄面包包著肉、蔬菜等）；拍攝（或錄音）結束，停機；（全身覆蓋溼布或海草等進行的）皮膚護理；（喻）秘密；<英，非正式>一小包白粉（毒品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wrap</b> something, you fold paper or cloth tightly around it to cover it completely, for example, in order to protect it or so that you can give it to someone as a present. 包","examples":["Harry had carefully bought and wrapped presents for Mark to give the children. 哈里已精心為馬克買好、包好那些給孩子們的禮物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>wrap</b> something such as a piece of paper or cloth around another thing, you put it around it. 用…包裹","examples":["She wrapped a handkerchief around her bleeding palm in an effort to protect it. 她用手帕包紮她那流血的手掌來保護它。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wrap up</b> means the same as . 包","examples":["Diana is taking the opportunity to wrap up the family presents. 戴安娜正在利用這個機會包裝給家人的禮物。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you keep something <b>under wraps</b>, you keep it secret, often until you are ready to announce it at some time in the future. 保密","examples":["The bids were submitted in May and were kept under wraps until October. 標書是5月遞交的，直到10月都秘而不宣。"]}]}]},"accidental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"意外的，偶然的；非主要的，附帶的；（亞里士多德思想中的）非本質屬性的；臨時記號的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"臨時記號；次要方面，非主要的特性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accidental</b> event happens by chance or as the result of an accident, and is not intended. 意外的","examples":["...the tragic accidental shooting of his younger brother. …對他弟弟的悲劇性意外槍擊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"意外地","examples":["A policeman accidentally killed his two best friends with a single bullet. 一位警察意外地用一顆子彈殺死了他的兩個最好的朋友。"]}]}]},"absolute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全的，純粹的；絕對的，無疑的；十足的；不受任何限制的，專制獨裁的；（結構）獨立的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"絕對真理，絕對原則"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Absolute</b> means total and complete. 完全的","examples":["It's not really suited to absolute beginners. 這對於純粹的初學者們不太適合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>absolute</b> to emphasize something that you are saying. 絕對的","examples":["About 12 inches wide is the absolute minimum you should consider. 12英寸左右的寬度是你應該考慮的絕對最小尺寸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>absolute</b> ruler has complete power and authority over his or her country. 獨裁的","examples":["He ruled with absolute power. 他實行獨裁統治。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Absolute</b> is used to say that something is definite and will not change even if circumstances change. 確鑿的","examples":["John brought the absolute proof that we needed. 約翰拿出了我們需要的確鑿證據。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An amount that is expressed in <b>absolute</b> terms is expressed as a fixed amount rather than referring to variable factors such as what you earn or the effects of inflation. 絕對的","examples":["In absolute terms their wages remain low by national standards. 他們工資的絕對值根據國家標準仍然是低的。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Absolute</b> rules and principles are believed to be true, right, or relevant in all situations. 絕對的","examples":["There are no absolute rules. 沒有絕對的準則。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>absolute</b> is a rule or principle that is believed to be true, right, or relevant in all situations. 絕對原則","examples":["This is one of the few absolutes in U.S. constitutional law. 這是美國憲法中少有的幾項絕對原則之一。"]}]}]},"academic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"學業的，學術的；學校的，學院的；學業（成績）優秀的，善於學習的；不切實際的，空談的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大學教師，學者；（學校或學院的）課程；大學生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Academic</b> is used to describe things that relate to the work done in schools, colleges, and universities, especially work that involves studying and reasoning rather than practical or technical skills. 學術上的","examples":["Their academic standards are high. 他們的學術水平很高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Academic</b> is used to describe things that relate to schools, colleges, and universities. 學校的","examples":["...the start of the last academic year. …上一個學年的開始。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Academic</b> is used to describe work, or a school, college, or university, that places emphasis on studying and reasoning rather than on practical or technical skills. 學術的","examples":["The author has settled for a more academic approach. 該作者已經確定了一種更學術的方法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>academic</b> is good at studying. 學習好的","examples":["The system is failing most disastrously among less academic children. 這種制度在學習不太好的學生中最失敗。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can say that a discussion or situation is <b>academic</b> if you think it is not important because it has no real effect or cannot happen. 空談的","examples":["Who wants to hear about contracts and deadlines that are purely academic? 誰想聽那些完全不切實際的合同和最後期限呢?"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"學術上地","examples":["He is academically gifted. 他在學術方面有天份。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>academic</b> is a member of a university or college who teaches or does research. 學者","examples":["A group of academics say they can predict house prices through a computer program. 一批學者聲稱，他們可以透過一種電腦程式預測房價。"]}]}]},"admirable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人欽佩的，極其出色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>admirable</b> quality or action is one that deserves to be praised and admired. 值得欽佩的","examples":["She did an admirable job of holding the audience's attention. 她做了件值得欽佩的事：吸引了觀眾的注意力。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"值得欽佩地","examples":["Peter had dealt admirably with the sudden questions about Keith. 彼得對關於基思的突如其來的問題處理得值得人欽佩。"]}]}]},"agreeable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愉悅的，討人喜歡的；欣然同意的；可接受的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>agreeable</b>, it is pleasant and you enjoy it. 怡人的","examples":["...workers in more agreeable and better paid occupations. …從事更舒適並且報酬更好的職業的工作人員們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>agreeable</b>, they are pleasant and try to please people. 討人喜歡的","examples":["...sharing a bottle of wine with an agreeable companion. …和一個令人愉快的同伴共享一瓶葡萄酒。"]}]}]},"abstract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"抽象的，純概念的；（藝術）抽象派的；理論上的，不切實際的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"摘要，梗概；抽象畫，抽象派藝術作品；抽象的概念"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"抽象化，從理論上（或孤立地）考慮；提取，使分離；寫……的摘要；偷走，竊取；退出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>abstract</b> idea or way of thinking is based on general ideas rather than on real things and events. 抽象的","examples":["...starting with a few abstract principles. …以幾條抽象的原則開始。","It's not a question of some abstract concept of justice. 這不是一個有關正義的某一抽象概念的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, an <b>abstract</b> noun refers to a quality or idea rather than to a physical object. 抽象的 (名詞)","examples":["...abstract words such as glory, honour, and courage. …諸如光榮、榮譽、勇氣這樣的抽象詞彙。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Abstract</b> art makes use of shapes and patterns rather than showing people or things. 抽象的 (藝術)","examples":["A modern abstract painting takes over one complete wall. 一幅現代抽象畫佔了整整一面牆。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk or think about something <b>in the abstract</b>, you talk or think about it in a general way, rather than considering particular things or events. 在抽象意義上","examples":["Money was a commodity she never thought about except in the abstract. 金錢是她從未具體想過的一種商品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>abstract</b> is an abstract work of art. 抽象作品","examples":["His abstracts are held in numerous collections. 他的抽象畫被納入到很多收藏中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>abstract</b> <b>of</b> an article, document, or speech is a short piece of writing that gives the main points of it. 摘要","examples":["It might also be necessary to supply an abstract of the review of the literature as well. 可能也有必要提供這篇文學評論的摘要。"]}]}]},"adequate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"足夠的，適當的，合乎需要的；（品質）足夠好的，令人滿意的；（質量）達到要求的，勉強過關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>adequate</b>, there is enough of it or it is good enough to be used or accepted. 足夠的","examples":["One in four people worldwide are without adequate homes. 世界上1/4的人沒有足夠的住房。","She is prepared to offer me an amount adequate to purchase another house. 她準備好了給我一筆足以購買另一所房子的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"足夠地","examples":["Many students are not adequately prepared for higher education. 很多學生沒有為高等教育做足準備。"]}]}]},"zone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（有某特色或作用的）地區，地帶；（允許或禁止某種活動的）範圍；（尤指有別於周圍的）區域，部分；（規劃的）區域，分割槽；（地球的）氣候帶；時區；（動植物）環帶，帶；（尤作體育用語）巔峰狀態"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……劃為某種用途的區域；將……分成區（或劃成帶）；<古>用帶子圍繞，環繞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>zone</b> is an area that has particular features or characteristics. (有某些特徵或特點的) 地帶","examples":["Many people have stayed behind in the potential war zone. 許多人留在了可能交戰的地帶。","The area has been declared a disaster zone. 該地區已被宣佈為災難帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"分割槽制","examples":["...the use of zoning to preserve agricultural land. …使用分割槽制以保留農業用地。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an area of land <b>is zoned</b>, it is formally set aside for a particular purpose. 將…劃為特殊區域","examples":["The land was not zoned for commercial purposes. 這塊地未被劃為商業用地。"]}]}]},"aggressive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好鬥的，挑釁的；積極進取的；非常嚴重的；強烈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>aggressive</b> person or animal has a quality of anger and determination that makes them ready to attack other people. 好鬥的","examples":["Some children are much more aggressive than others. 一些孩子比其他孩子好鬥得多。","These fish are very aggressive. 這些魚十分好鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People who are <b>aggressive</b> in their work or other activities behave in a forceful way because they are very eager to succeed. 好強的","examples":["He is respected as a very aggressive and competitive executive. 他被尊認為一位十分好強好勝的主管。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"好鬥地","examples":["They'll react aggressively. 他們會兇猛地作出反應。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"好強地","examples":["...countries noted for aggressively pursuing energy efficiency. …以拼命追求能效著稱的國家。"]}]}]},"artistic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"藝術的，藝術家的；有藝術鑑賞力的，有藝術天賦的；有藝術性的，精美的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>artistic</b> is good at drawing or painting, or arranging things in a beautiful way. 有美術才能的","examples":["They encourage boys to be sensitive and artistic. 他們鼓勵男孩子們要反應敏感並有美術才能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Artistic</b> means relating to art or artists. 藝術的; 藝術家的","examples":["...the campaign for artistic freedom. …藝術自由運動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>artistic</b> design or arrangement is beautiful. (設計、佈局) 有藝術性的","examples":["...an artistic arrangement of stone paving. …石頭鋪路的藝術性佈局。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"藝術方面地","examples":["...artistically gifted children. …有藝術天賦的兒童。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"有藝術性地","examples":["...artistically carved vessels. …藝術性地刻成的船隻。"]}]}]},"athletic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"運動的，體育的；強壯的，健壯的；運動員用的；（在體育、比賽或身體鍛鍊等方面）行動敏捷的，活躍的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Athletic</b> means relating to athletes and athletics. 運動的; 運動員的","examples":["They have been given college scholarships purely on athletic ability. 他們完全憑他們的運動才能獲得了大學獎學金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>athletic</b> person is fit, and able to perform energetic movements easily. 運動型的 (人)","examples":["Xandra is an athletic 36-year-old with a 21-year-old's body. 贊德拉是位36歲卻有著21歲人體格的運動型人。"]}]}]},"annual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一年一度的；年度的；（植物）一年生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一年生植物；年刊，年鑑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Annual</b> events happen once every year. 每年一次的","examples":["The issues will be voted on at the company's annual meeting on April 21 in Wilmington. 這些問題將在該公司4月21日在威爾明頓的年會上投票表決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Annual</b> quantities or rates relate to a period of one year. 年度的","examples":["The electronic and printing unit has annual sales of about $80 million. 電子與印刷部有約八千萬美元的年度銷售額。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"每年一次地","examples":["Companies report to their shareholders annually. 各公司每年向其股東們彙報一次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"年度地","examples":["El Salvador produces 100,000 tons of refined copper annually. 薩爾瓦多一年生產10萬噸精煉銅。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>annual</b> is a book or magazine that is published once a year. 年鑑; 年刊","examples":["I looked for Wyman's picture in my high-school annual. 我在我的中學年鑑裡找過懷曼的照片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>annual</b> is a plant that grows and dies within one year. 一年生植物","examples":["Maybe this year I'll sow brilliant annuals everywhere. 也許今年我會到處種上鮮豔的一年生植物。"]}]}]},"atomic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原子的，與原子有關的；原子能的，核能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Atomic</b> means relating to power that is produced from the energy released by splitting atoms. 原子能的","examples":["...atomic energy. …原子能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Atomic</b> means relating to the atoms of substances. 原子的","examples":["...the atomic number of an element. …一種元素的原子序數。"]}]}]},"anxious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"焦慮的，擔心的；渴望的，急切的；（時間或局勢）緊張的，令人焦慮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>anxious</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>anxious</b> <b>that</b> something should happen, you very much want to do it or very much want it to happen. 焦急的","examples":["Both the Americans and the Russians are anxious to avoid conflict in South Asia. 美國人與俄國人都急於避免南亞衝突。","He is anxious that there should be no delay. 他急切希望不會有任何延誤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>anxious</b>, you are nervous or worried about something. 焦慮的","examples":["The foreign minister admitted he was still anxious about the situation in the country. 外交部長承認他對該國的局勢依然感到焦慮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"焦慮地","examples":["They are waiting anxiously to see who will succeed him. 他們在焦慮不安地等著看誰將接替他。"]}]}]},"ashamed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感到羞愧，感到羞恥；羞於（做某事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>ashamed</b>, they feel embarrassed or guilty because of something they do or they have done, or because of their appearance. 尷尬的; 慚愧的","examples":["I felt incredibly ashamed of myself for getting so angry. 我為自己發了這麼大的脾氣而感到極為慚愧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>ashamed of</b> someone, you feel embarrassed to be connected with them, often because of their appearance or because you disapprove of something they have done. 感到羞恥的","examples":["I've never told this to anyone, but it's true, I was terribly ashamed of my mom. 我從未告訴過任何人，但這是真的，我特別以自己的母親為恥。"]}]}]},"ambitious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有抱負的，野心勃勃的；費勁的，艱鉅的；熱望的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>ambitious</b> has a strong desire to be successful, rich, or powerful. 雄心勃勃的","examples":["Chris is so ambitious, so determined to do it all. 克里斯是如此雄心勃勃，如此堅決地要把它做完。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>ambitious</b> idea or plan is on a large scale and needs a lot of work to be carried out successfully. 宏大的","examples":["The ambitious project was completed in only nine months. 這個宏大的專案在僅僅9個月之內就完成了。"]}]}]},"appropriate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合適的，相稱的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撥出（款項）；私佔，挪用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>appropriate</b> is suitable or acceptable for a particular situation. 適當的","examples":["It is appropriate that Hispanic names dominate the list. 西班牙人的名字在這個名單中占主導地位是適當的。","Dress neatly and attractively in an outfit appropriate to the job. 穿適合於這份工作的整潔美觀的套裝。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"適當地","examples":["Behave appropriately and ask intelligent questions. 舉止要得體，提問要機智。"]}]}]},"artificial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人造的，人工的；人為的；不真摯的，矯揉造作的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Artificial</b> objects, materials, or processes do not occur naturally and are created by human beings, often using science or technology. 人造的 (物體、材料、工藝等)","examples":["The city is dotted with small lakes, natural and artificial. 這座城市滿是天然和人造的小湖泊。","...a wholefood diet free from artificial additives, colours and flavours. …一種無人造新增劑、色素及味素的全天然食物飲食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>artificial</b> state or situation exists only because someone has created it, and therefore often seems unnatural or unnecessary. 人為的 (狀態、狀況)","examples":["Even in the artificial environment of an office, our body rhythms continue to affect us. 即便在辦公室的人為環境中，我們的身體節律繼續影響我們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"人造地","examples":["...artificially sweetened lemonade. …人工加了糖的檸檬汽水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"人為地","examples":["...state subsidies that have kept retail prices artificially low. …人為地將零售價格保持在低水平的國家補貼。"]}]}]},"audio":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聲音的，音訊的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聲音，音訊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Audio</b> equipment is used for recording and reproducing sound. 錄音的","examples":["The software was the first to offer access to audio and video files. 這是第一種可以訪問音影片檔案的軟體。"]}]}]},"bald":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"禿頭的；光禿的，磨光的，掉光的；不加修飾的，直截了當的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bald</b> has little or no hair on the top of their head. 禿頂的","examples":["The man's bald head was beaded with sweat. 這位男子的禿頭上滿是汗珠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a tyre is <b>bald</b>, its surface has worn down and it is no longer safe to use. (輪胎表面) 磨平的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bald</b> statement is in plain language and contains no extra explanation or information. (陳述等) 直白的","examples":["The bald truth is he's just not happy. 明擺著的事實是他就是不高興。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"禿頂","examples":["He wears a cap to cover a spot of baldness. 他戴一頂帽子來遮住一小塊禿頂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(陳述等) 直白地","examples":["\"The leaders are outdated,\" he stated baldly. \"They don't relate to young people.\" “領導們落伍了。”他直白地說，“他們不理解年輕人。”"]}]}]},"broke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>身無分文的，一文不名的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弄壞；打碎；違反（break 的過去式形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Broke</b> is the past tense of <b>break</b>. (break)的過去式","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>broke</b>, you have no money. 一文不名的","examples":["What do you mean, I've got enough money? I'm as broke as you are. 你什麼意思啊，我有足夠的錢？我和你一樣一文不名。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company or person <b>goes broke</b>, they lose money and are unable to continue in business or to pay their debts. 破產","examples":["Balton went broke twice in his career. 伯頓在他的職業生涯中破產過兩次。"]}]}]},"brutal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"野蠻的，兇殘的；毫不掩飾的，直截了當的；令人不快的，糟糕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brutal</b> act or person is cruel and violent. 殘暴的","examples":["He was the victim of a very brutal murder. 他是一樁異常殘暴的謀殺案的受害者。","...the brutal suppression of anti-government protests. …對反政府抗議行動的殘酷鎮壓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone expresses something unpleasant with <b>brutal</b> honesty or frankness, they express it in a clear and accurate way, without attempting to disguise its unpleasantness. 不留情面的 (誠實、直白)","examples":["It was refreshing to talk about themselves and their feelings with brutal honesty. 不留情面的誠實地談論他們自己和他們的感情令人耳目一新。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"殘暴地","examples":["Her real parents had been brutally murdered. 她的親生父母已被殘暴地殺害了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不留情面地","examples":["The talks had been brutally frank. 那些談話不留情面地坦率。"]}]}]},"circular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"圓形的，環形的；迴圈的，繞圈的；迴圈論證的；傳閱的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（同時送達多人的）印刷品，宣傳單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>circular</b> is shaped like a circle. 圓形的","examples":["...a circular hole twelve feet wide and two feet deep. …一個12英尺寬、2英尺深的圓洞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>circular</b> journey or route is one in which you go to a place and return by a different route. (旅行或路線) 環行的","examples":["Both sides of the river can be explored on this circular walk. 沿著這條環形步行道走，河的兩邊就都可以看得到了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>circular</b> is an official letter or advertisement that is sent to a large number of people at the same time. 函件; 通告","examples":["The proposal has been widely publicized in press information circulars sent to 1,800 newspapers. 透過向1800份報紙傳送新聞通告，這項提議得到了廣泛地宣傳。"]}]}]},"consequent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"隨之發生的，由此引起的；（河流，山谷）順向的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"後件，推斷；（音樂）答題，答句"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Consequent</b> means happening as a direct result of an event or situation. 作為結果的","examples":["The warming of the Earth and the consequent climatic changes affect us all. 全球變暖以及隨之而來的氣候變化影響我們每個人。"]}]}]},"clumsy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"笨拙的，不靈活的；不得體的；難處理的，難使用的；難以移動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clumsy</b> person moves or handles things in a careless, awkward way, often so that things are knocked over or broken. 笨拙的","examples":["I'd never seen a clumsier, less coordinated boxer. 我還從未見過更加笨拙、更不協調的拳擊手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clumsy</b> action or statement is not skilful or is likely to upset people. 笨拙的; 不得當的","examples":["The action seemed a clumsy attempt to topple the government. 那個企圖推翻政府的行動似乎並不得當。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"笨拙地","examples":["In the sudden pitch darkness, she scrambled clumsily toward the ladder. 在突如其來的一片漆黑中，她笨手笨腳地爬向梯子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"笨拙地; 不得當地","examples":["If the matter were handled clumsily, it could cost Miriam her life. 如果問題處理不當，可能會斷送米里亞姆的性命。"]}]}]},"coarse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗糙的，粗織的；粗的，大顆粒的；粗魯的，粗俗的；（人的容貌）難看的，不雅的；（食物，飲料）粗劣的；<英>與釣淡水魚有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Coarse</b> things have a rough texture because they consist of thick threads or large pieces. 粗糙的","examples":["...a jacket made of very coarse cloth. …用非常粗糙的布做成的一件夾克衫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>coarse</b>, you mean that he or she talks and behaves in a rude and offensive way. 粗魯的; 粗俗的","examples":["The soldiers did not bother to moderate their coarse humour in her presence. 士兵們沒有費神去約束他們的粗俗幽默，儘管她在場。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗糙地","examples":["...coarsely ground black pepper. …粗糙磨製的黑胡椒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"粗魯地; 粗俗地","examples":["The women laughed coarsely at some vulgar joke. 女人們聽到某個庸俗笑話後便粗俗地笑了起來。"]}]}]},"awkward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人尷尬的，使人難堪的；難對付的，難處理的；侷促不安的；不方便的；笨拙的，不雅觀的；不舒適的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>awkward</b> situation is embarrassing and difficult to deal with. 令人尷尬的","examples":["I was the first to ask him awkward questions but there'll be harder ones to come. 我是第一個問他尷尬問題的人，但後面還會有更棘手的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>awkward</b> <b>to</b> use or carry is difficult to use or carry because of its design. A job that is <b>awkward</b> is difficult to do. (使用) 不便的; 棘手的 (工作)","examples":["It was small but heavy enough to make it awkward to carry. 它雖然小，卻沉重得不便攜帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>awkward</b> movement or position is uncomfortable or clumsy. 笨拙的","examples":["Amy made an awkward gesture with her hands. 艾米用雙手做了一個笨拙的手勢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who feels <b>awkward</b> behaves in a shy or embarrassed way. 難為情的","examples":["Women frequently say that they feel awkward taking the initiative in sex. 女性經常說她們覺得在性方面採取主動令人難為情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人尷尬地","examples":["There was an awkwardly long silence. 有一段令人尷尬的長時間的沉默。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不便地; 棘手地","examples":["The front window switches are awkwardly placed on the dashboard. 前窗的開關安裝在儀表板上，使用不便。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"笨拙地","examples":["He fell awkwardly and went down in agony clutching his right knee. 他笨拙地摔倒了，緊抓住右膝蓋痛苦地蹲了下去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"難為情地","examples":["\"This is Malcolm,\" the girl said awkwardly, to fill the silence. “這是馬爾科姆，”女孩子為了打破沉默難為情地說道。"]}]}]},"competitive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"競爭的；好競爭的，好勝的；有競爭力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Competitive</b> is used to describe situations or activities in which people or companies compete with each other. 競爭的","examples":["Only by keeping down costs will America maintain its competitive advantage over other countries. 只有透過保持低成本美國才能保持對其他國家的競爭優勢。","Japan is a highly competitive market system. 日本實行的是一個高度競爭的市場體制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>competitive</b> person is eager to be more successful than other people. 好勝的","examples":["He has always been ambitious and fiercely competitive. 他一直很有抱負，極度好勝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Goods or services that are at a <b>competitive</b> price or rate are likely to be bought, because they are less expensive than other goods of the same kind. (商品、服務) 有競爭力的","examples":["Only those homes offered for sale at competitive prices will secure interest from serious purchasers. 只有那些以具有競爭力的價格出售的房子才能抓住真正購買者的興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"競爭地","examples":["He's now back up on the slopes again, skiing competitively in events for the disabled. 他如今又回到了滑坡上，在殘疾人賽事上賽滑雪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"好勝地","examples":["They worked hard together, competitively and under pressure. 他們一起努力工作，一心求勝，也承受壓力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有競爭力地","examples":["...a number of early Martin and Gibson guitars, which were competitively priced. …許多定價富有競爭力的早期馬丁吉他和吉布森吉他。"]}]}]},"courageous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勇敢的，有膽量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>courageous</b> shows courage. 勇敢的","examples":["The children were very courageous. 孩子們都很勇敢。"]}]}]},"constructive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"建設性的，有助益的；<法律>推定的；（與）推斷（有關）的，以推斷為基礎的；構造上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>constructive</b> discussion, comment, or approach is useful and helpful rather than negative and unhelpful. 建設性的","examples":["She welcomes constructive criticism. 她歡迎建設性的批評意見。","After their meeting, both men described the talks as frank, friendly and constructive. 會見之後，兩位男士都形容這次會談坦誠、友好且富有建設性。"]}]}]},"courteous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有禮貌的，謙恭的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>courteous</b> is polite and respectful to other people. 彬彬有禮的","examples":["He was a kind and courteous man. 他善良且彬彬有禮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"彬彬有禮地","examples":["Then he nodded courteously to me and walked off to perform his unpleasant duty. 他彬彬有禮地向我點點頭，然後就走開去執行他令人討厭的任務。"]}]}]},"continual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多次重複的，頻繁的；持續的，不間斷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>continual</b> process or situation happens or exists without stopping. 持續不斷的","examples":["The school has been in continual use since 1883. 該校自1883年以來一直在不斷使用中。","They felt continual pressure to perform well. 他們感受到持續不斷的、要表演得好的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Continual</b> events happen again and again. 頻繁的","examples":["...the government's continual demands for cash to finance its chronic deficit. …政府為負擔其長期的財政赤字而對現金不斷的需求。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"持續不斷地","examples":["She cried almost continually and threw temper tantrums. 她幾乎哭個不停，還大發脾氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"頻繁地","examples":["Malcolm was continually changing his mind. 馬爾科姆頻頻改變其主意。"]}]}]},"consistent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"始終如一的，一貫的；持續的，連續的；固守的，堅持的；一致的，吻合的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>consistent</b> always behaves in the same way, has the same attitudes towards people or things, or achieves the same level of success in something. 始終如一的","examples":["Becker was never the most consistent of players anyway. 貝克爾不管怎麼說從來就不是一個很穩定的球員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one fact or idea is <b>consistent</b> <b>with</b> another, they do not contradict each other. 相符的","examples":["This result is consistent with the findings of Garnett & Tobin. 該結果與加尼特和託賓的發現相符合。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An argument or set of ideas that is <b>consistent</b> is one in which no part contradicts or conflicts with any other part. (論點、觀點) 前後一致的","examples":["A theory should be internally consistent. 一套理論應當內在一致。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"始終如一地","examples":["It's something I have consistently denied. 這是我始終否認的事。"]}]}]},"defensible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可辯解的，有正當理由的；可防禦的，可守護的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An opinion, system, or action that is <b>defensible</b> is one that people can argue is right or good. 能辯護的","examples":["Her reasons for acting are morally defensible. 她表演的理由道德上講是合乎情理的。"]}]}]},"continuous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"連續不斷的，持續的；（語法）進行式的；（函式）連續的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>continuous</b> process or event continues for a period of time without stopping. 持續的 (過程、事件)","examples":["Residents report that they heard continuous gunfire. 居民們說他們聽到了持續的槍聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>continuous</b> line or surface has no gaps or holes in it. 連續的 (線條或平面)","examples":["...a continuous line of boats. …絡繹不絕的船隻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In English grammar, <b>continuous</b> verb groups are formed using the auxiliary \"be\" and the present participle of a verb, as in \"I'm feeling a bit tired\" and \"She had been watching them for some time.\" Continuous verb groups are used especially when you are focusing on a particular moment. Compare . 進行 (時態) 的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"持續地","examples":["The civil war has raged almost continuously since 1976. 自1976年以來，激烈的內戰幾乎持續不斷。"]}]}]},"defensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"防禦的，戒備的；生氣的，發怒的；（比賽中）防守的，防禦的；百般辯解的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"防禦態勢，守勢；辯護，辯解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>defensive</b> to describe things that are intended to protect someone or something. 防禦性的; 防衛用的","examples":["The Government hastily organized defensive measures, deploying searchlights and antiaircraft guns around the target cities. 政府匆忙組織了防禦措施，在目標城市周圍部署了探照燈和高射炮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>defensive</b> is behaving in a way that shows they feel unsure or threatened. 自衛的","examples":["Like their children, parents are often defensive about their private lives. 跟孩子們一樣，家長們對他們的私生活通常也是自衛的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports, <b>defensive</b> play is play that is intended to prevent your opponent from scoring points against you. 防守的","examples":["I'd always played a defensive game, waiting for my opponent to make a mistake. 我總是打防守戰，等著對手出錯。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自衛地","examples":["\"Oh, I know, I know,\" said Kate, defensively. 凱特心存戒備地說道：“啊，知道，知道。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"防守地","examples":["We didn't play well defensively in the first half. 我們上半場防守不佳。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>on the defensive</b>, they are trying to protect themselves or their interests because they feel unsure or threatened. 採取防衛措施","examples":["The administration has been on the defensive about the war. 行政部門一直在為戰爭辯解。"]}]}]},"conventional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"依照慣例的，遵循習俗的；老一套的，習慣的；（武器等）常規的，非核的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>conventional</b> has behaviour or opinions that are ordinary and normal. (行為觀念等) 傳統的","examples":["...a respectable married woman with conventional opinions. …一個可敬的觀念傳統的已婚婦女。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>conventional</b> method or product is one that is usually used or that has been in use for a long time. 傳統的 (方法或產品等)","examples":["...the risks and drawbacks of conventional family planning methods. …傳統計劃生育方法的風險和缺陷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Conventional</b> weapons and wars do not involve nuclear explosives. 常規的 (武器); 不用核武器的 (戰爭)","examples":["We must reduce the danger of war by controlling nuclear, chemical, and conventional arms. 我們必須透過控制核武器、化學武器和常規武器來降低戰爭的危險。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傳統地","examples":["Men still wore their hair short and dressed conventionally. 男人還是留著短髮，著裝傳統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"傳統地","examples":["Organically grown produce does not differ greatly in appearance from conventionally grown crops. 有機農產品與傳統方法種植的農產品在外觀上沒有太大的區別。"]}]}]},"dependable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可靠的，可信賴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>dependable</b>, you approve of them because you feel that you can be sure that they will always act consistently or sensibly, or do what you need them to do. 可靠的","examples":["He was a good friend, a dependable companion. 他是個好朋友，一個可以信賴的同伴。"]}]}]},"delightful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人愉快的，宜人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>delightful</b>, you mean they are very pleasant. 令人愉快的","examples":["It was the most delightful garden I had ever seen. 這是我見過的最討人喜歡的花園。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人愉快地","examples":["This delightfully refreshing cologne can be splashed on liberally. 這種清爽怡人的古龍香水可以盡情噴灑。"]}]}]},"critical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"批判的，愛挑剔的；極其重要的，關鍵的；嚴重的，危急的；病重的，重傷的；評論性的，評論家的；臨界的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>critical</b> time, factor, or situation is extremely important. 關鍵的","examples":["The incident happened at a critical point in the campaign. 該事件發生在運動的關鍵時刻。","He says setting priorities is of critical importance. 他說確定輕重緩急至關重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>critical</b> situation is very serious and dangerous. 危急的","examples":["The German authorities are considering an airlift if the situation becomes critical. 德國當局正在考慮如果形勢危急時進行空運。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person is <b>critical</b> or in a <b>critical</b> condition in a hospital, they are seriously ill. 病危的","examples":["Ten of the injured are said to be in critical condition. 據說傷者中有十人情況危急。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To be <b>critical</b> <b>of</b> someone or something means to criticize them. 批評的","examples":["His report is highly critical of the trial judge. 他的報道對承審法官是高度批判的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>critical</b> approach to something involves examining and judging it carefully. 批判性的","examples":["We need to become critical text-readers. 我們需要成為批判性的文字閱讀者。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something or someone receives <b>critical</b> acclaim, critics say that they are very good. 獲好評的","examples":["The film met with considerable critical and public acclaim. 這部電影深得評論和公眾的讚揚。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"關鍵地","examples":["Economic prosperity depends critically on an open world trading system. 經濟繁榮關鍵取決於一個開放的世界貿易體系。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"危急地","examples":["Moscow is running critically low on food supplies. 莫斯科的食品供應正嚴重匱乏。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"病危地","examples":["She was critically ill. 她病情危急。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"批評地","examples":["She spoke critically of Lara. 她以批評的口吻談到拉臘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"批判性地","examples":["Wyman watched them critically. 懷曼批判地注視著他們。"]}]}]},"definite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"清晰的，明晰的；確定的，不會改變的；肯定的，一定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"確定之事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a decision or an arrangement is <b>definite</b>, it is firm and clear, and unlikely to be changed. 明確的","examples":["It's too soon to give a definite answer. 現在給予明確答覆還為時尚早。","She made no definite plans for her future. 她對自己的未來沒有明確的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Definite</b> evidence or information is true, rather than being someone's opinion or guess. 確切的","examples":["We didn't have any definite proof. 我們沒有任何確鑿的證據。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>definite</b> to emphasize the strength of your opinion or belief. 無疑的","examples":["There has already been a definite improvement. 已經有了顯著的改善。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>definite</b> behaves or talks in a firm, confident way. 肯定的","examples":["Mary is very definite about this. 瑪麗對此非常肯定。"]}]}]},"dense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"稠密的；濃密的，濃重的；密度大的；（文字）難懂的；愚鈍的，笨拙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>dense</b> contains a lot of things or people in a small area. 稠密的","examples":["Where Bucharest now stands, there once was a large, dense forest. 現在的布加勒斯特所在地曾經是一片茂密的大森林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dense</b> fog or smoke is difficult to see through because it is very heavy and dark. (煙、霧等) 濃重的","examples":["A dense column of smoke rose several miles into the air. 一柱濃煙升上幾英里高的天空。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In science, a <b>dense</b> substance is very heavy in relation to its volume. (物質) 密度大的","examples":["...a small dense star. …一顆密度大的小恆星。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"稠密地","examples":["Java is a densely populated island. 爪哇是一個人口稠密的島嶼。"]}]}]},"delicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"柔和的，清淡的；虛弱的，纖弱的；脆弱的，易碎的；小巧玲瓏的，纖細的；微妙的，棘手的；精緻的，精巧的；靈巧的，熟練的；（儀器）靈敏的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"精美的衣物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>delicate</b> is small and beautifully shaped. 精巧的; 精美的","examples":["He had delicate hands. 他有一雙纖細的手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>delicate</b> has a colour, taste, or smell which is pleasant and not strong or intense. 柔和的 (顏色); 清淡可口的 (味道)","examples":["Young haricot beans have a tender texture and a delicate, subtle flavour. 嫩扁豆肉質細嫩，味道清淡可口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>delicate</b>, it is easy to harm, damage, or break, and needs to be handled or treated carefully. 易碎的; 脆弱的","examples":["Although the coral looks hard, it is very delicate. 雖然那珊瑚看起來堅硬，它其實非常易碎。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>delicate</b> is not healthy and strong, and becomes ill easily. 病弱的","examples":["She was physically delicate and psychologically unstable. 她身體纖弱，而且心理也不穩定。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>delicate</b> to describe a situation, problem, matter, or discussion that needs to be dealt with carefully and sensitively in order to avoid upsetting things or offending people. 微妙的","examples":["Ottawa and Washington have to find a delicate balance between the free flow of commerce and legitimate security concerns. 渥太華和華盛頓必須在自由貿易流通和司法安全事務之間找到一個微妙的平衡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>delicate</b> task, movement, action, or product needs or shows great skill and attention to detail. 棘手的; 需要小心處理的","examples":["...a long and delicate operation carried out at a hospital in Pittsburgh. …匹茲堡市一家醫院裡進行的一項耗時且棘手的手術。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精巧地; 精美地","examples":["She was a shy, delicately pretty girl with enormous blue eyes. 她是個羞怯纖美的姑娘，長著一雙藍色的大眼睛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"清淡可口地","examples":["...a soup delicately flavoured with nutmeg. …以肉桂清淡地調味的一道湯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"微妙地","examples":["Clearly, the situation remains delicately poised. 顯而易見，形勢仍然保持著微妙的平衡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"棘手地","examples":["...the delicately embroidered sheets. …那些刺繡繁複的床單。"]}]}]},"desperate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不顧一切的，拼命的；極需要的，渴望的；極嚴重的，極危險的；絕望的，無望的；絕望的，無望的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>desperate</b>, you are in such a bad situation that you are willing to try anything to change it. 不顧一切的","examples":["Troops are needed to help get food into Kosovo where people are in desperate need. 需要軍隊協助將食物運進科索沃，那裡的人們迫切需要食物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>desperate</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>desperate</b> <b>to</b> do something, you want or need it very much indeed. 極度渴望的","examples":["They'd been married nearly four years and June was desperate to start a family. 他們結婚快4年了，瓊非常想生個孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>desperate</b> situation is very difficult, serious, or dangerous. 危急的","examples":["India's United Nations ambassador said the situation is desperate. 印度駐聯合國大使說局勢危急。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不顧一切地","examples":["Thousands are desperately trying to leave their battered homes and villages. 成千上萬的人們正不顧一切地試圖逃離他們滿目瘡痍的家園和村莊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"極其","examples":["He was a boy who desperately needed affection. 他是個極度需要關愛的孩子。"]}]}]},"distinguished":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"卓越的，傑出的；高貴的，尊貴的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"區別，分清；使有別於；看清，認出（distinguish 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or their work as <b>distinguished</b>, you mean that they have been very successful in their career and have a good reputation. 卓著的","examples":["...a distinguished academic family. …一個卓越的學術之家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>distinguished</b>, you mean that they look very noble and respectable. 高貴的","examples":["His suit was immaculately cut and he looked very distinguished. 他的西服剪裁完美，人顯得十分高貴。"]}]}]},"dusty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"佈滿灰塵的；土灰色的；缺乏活力的，枯燥無味的；塵般的，粉狀的；不明確的，不能令人滿意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If places, roads, or other things outside are <b>dusty</b>, they are covered with tiny bits of earth or sand, usually because it has not rained for a long time. 覆有塵土的","examples":["They started strolling down the dusty road in the moonlight. 他們開始在月光下滿是塵土的道路上漫步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a room, house, or object is <b>dusty</b>, it is covered with very small pieces of dirt. 佈滿灰塵的","examples":["...a dusty attic. …一個佈滿灰塵的閣樓。"]}]}]},"durable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"持久的，耐用的；<非正式>（人）有耐力的，堅韌不拔的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"耐用品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>durable</b> is strong and lasts a long time without breaking or becoming weaker. 耐用的","examples":["Fine bone china is eminently practical, since it is strong and durable. 精細骨瓷是非同一般地實用，因為它堅固耐用。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"耐用性","examples":["Airlines recommend hard-sided cases for durability. 航空公司推薦使用硬邊的提箱以求耐用。"]}]}]},"digital":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"數字的，數碼的；數字顯示的；指頭的，手指的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"數字電視，數位電視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Digital</b> systems record or transmit information in the form of thousands of very small signals. 數碼的","examples":["The new digital technology would allow a rapid expansion in the number of TV channels. 新的數碼技術可使電影片道的數量得以快速增多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Digital</b> devices such as watches or clocks give information by displaying numbers rather than by having a pointer which moves round a dial. Compare . 數字的","examples":["...a digital display. …數字顯示。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes refer to poorer people's lack of access to the latest computer technology as <b>the</b> <b>digital divide</b>. 數字鴻溝","examples":["...an attempt to reduce the \"digital divide\" between poor students who have no computers and those from well-off families who do. …縮小沒有電腦的貧困生和有電腦的富裕家庭學生之間的“數字鴻溝”的努力。"]}]}]},"divine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"神的，天賜的；絕妙的，極令人愉快的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（憑直覺）猜測，推測；占卜，預測；（透過探礦術）發現（水源）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>牧師，神學家；天意，上帝（the Divine）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>divine</b> to describe something that is provided by or relates to a god or goddess. 神的; 神聖的","examples":["He suggested that the civil war had been a divine punishment. 他暗示此次內戰是上天的懲罰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People use <b>divine</b> to express their pleasure or enjoyment of something. 極好的; 絕妙的","examples":["Her carrot cake is divine. 她的胡蘿蔔餅好吃極了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"如神般地; 神聖地","examples":["The law was divinely ordained. 此法律為神授。"]}]}]},"dominant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"佔支配地位的，佔優勢的；（基因）顯性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"顯性（性狀），顯性基因"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>dominant</b> is more powerful, successful, influential, or noticeable than other people or things. 處於支配地位的","examples":["...a change which would maintain his party's dominant position in Scotland. …鞏固他的政黨在蘇格蘭支配地位的一場變革。"]}]}]},"dynamic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"充滿活力的，精力充沛的；動態的，發展變化的；力的，動力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"動力，活力；相互作用，動態；動力學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>dynamic</b>, you approve of them because they are full of energy or full of new and exciting ideas. (人) 有活力的; 有創新思維的","examples":["He seemed a dynamic and energetic leader. 他看來是個富有創新力與活力的領導。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>dynamic</b>, you approve of it because it is very active and energetic. (事物) 有活力的","examples":["South Asia continues to be the most dynamic economic region in the world. 南亞仍然是世界上最具活力的經濟區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dynamic</b> process is one that constantly changes and progresses. 動態的","examples":["...a dynamic, evolving worldwide epidemic. …一次不斷變化發展的、世界範圍內的疾疫流行。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有活力地; 有創新思維地","examples":["He's one of the most dynamically imaginative jazz pianists of our time. 他是我們這個時代最具活躍想像力的爵士樂鋼琴演奏家之一。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>dynamic</b> of a system or process is the force that causes it to change or progress. 動力","examples":["The dynamic of the market demands constant change and adjustment. 市場的動力要求有不斷的變化和調整。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>dynamics</b> of a situation or group of people are the opposing forces within it that cause it to change. (引發變革的) 反動力","examples":["What is needed is insight into the dynamics of the social system. 所需要的就是對社會制度反動力的洞悉。"]}]}]},"economical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經濟實惠的；節約的；簡練的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>economical</b> does not require a lot of money to operate. For example, a car that only uses a small amount of petrol is <b>economical</b>. 經濟的; 節省的","examples":["...plans to trade in their car for something smaller and more economical. …用他們的車抵價購買更小且更經濟型轎車的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>economical</b> spends money sensibly and does not want to waste it on things that are unnecessary. A way of life that is <b>economical</b> does not require a lot of money. 節儉的","examples":["...ideas for economical housekeeping. …節儉持家的一些想法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Economical</b> means using the minimum amount of time, effort, or language that is necessary. 簡練的","examples":["His gestures were economical, his words generally mild. 他的手勢簡練，言語通常是溫和的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"經濟地; 節省地","examples":["Services could be operated more efficiently and economically. 可以更有效、更經濟地提供服務。"]}]}]},"distinct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不同的，有區別的；清楚的，明顯的；確切的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>distinct</b> <b>from</b> something else of the same type, it is different or separate from it. 有區別的","examples":["Engineering and technology are disciplines distinct from one another and from science. 工程學和工藝學是互不相同的學科，也不同於理科。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>distinct</b>, you can hear, see, or taste it clearly. 清楚的","examples":["...to impart a distinct flavour with a minimum of cooking fat. …加入最少量的烹調油脂做出獨特的風味。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an idea, thought, or intention is <b>distinct</b>, it is clear and definite. 明顯的; 確切的","examples":["Now that Tony was no longer present, there was a distinct change in her attitude. 現在託尼不在場了，她的態度就發生了明顯變化。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>distinct</b> to emphasize that something is great enough in amount or degree to be noticeable or important. 顯著的","examples":["Being 6ft 3in tall has some distinct disadvantages! 身高6英尺3英寸有明顯的劣勢！"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不同地","examples":["...a banking industry with two distinctly different sectors. …有兩個截然不同部門的銀行業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"清楚地","examples":["I distinctly heard the loudspeaker calling passengers for the Washington-Miami flight. 我清楚地聽到擴音器在呼叫由華盛頓飛往邁阿密的旅客。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"明顯地; 確切地","examples":["I distinctly remember wishing I had not got involved. 我清楚地記得我巴不得自己沒有參與進去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"顯著地","examples":["His government is looking distinctly shaky. 他的政府看起來顯然岌岌可危。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are talking about one thing <b>as distinct from</b> another, you are indicating exactly which thing you mean. 與…有區別的","examples":["There's a lot of evidence that oily fish, as distinct from fatty meat, has a beneficial effect. 大量證據顯示，含油的魚與肥肉不同，具有益處。"]}]}]},"elementary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"簡單的，基本的；基礎的，初級的；小學的；單一元素的，非化合物的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>elementary</b> is very simple and basic. 基本的","examples":["Literacy now includes elementary computer skills. 有文化現在包括基本的計算機技能。"]}]}]},"elegant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）高雅的，舉止優雅的；精美的，雅緻的；簡練的，巧妙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or thing as <b>elegant</b>, you mean that they are pleasing and graceful in appearance or style. 優雅的","examples":["Patricia looked beautiful and elegant as always. 帕特麗夏看上去跟往常一樣美麗優雅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a piece of writing, an idea, or a plan as <b>elegant</b>, you mean that it is simple, clear, and clever. 精妙的","examples":["The document impressed me with its elegant simplicity. 這份檔案以其精妙的簡約給我留下了深刻的印象。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"優雅","examples":["The furniture managed to combine practicality with elegance. 這傢俱結合了實用與優雅。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精妙地","examples":["...an elegantly simple idea. …一個精妙地簡單的主意。"]}]}]},"eventual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最終的，結局的；<古>有條件的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>eventual</b> to indicate that something happens or is the case at the end of a process or period of time. 最終的","examples":["There are many who believe that civil war will be the eventual outcome of the racial tension in the country. 有許多人認為內戰將是該國種族關係緊張的最終結果。"]}]}]},"enormous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大的，極大的；<古>兇暴的，極惡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>enormous</b> is extremely large in size or amount. 巨大的","examples":["The main bedroom is enormous. 主臥室大極了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>enormous</b> to emphasize the great degree or extent of something. (程度、範圍) 極大的","examples":["It was an enormous disappointment. 這是件令人極為失望的事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極其地","examples":["This book was enormously influential. 這本書影響極大。"]}]}]},"envious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"羨慕的，嫉妒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>envious</b> <b>of</b> someone, you want something that they have. 羨慕的","examples":["I don't think I'm envious of your success. 我不認為我羨慕你的成功。","Do I sound envious? I pity them, actually. 我聽起來像是羨慕嗎？其實，我可憐他們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"羨慕地","examples":["\"You haven't changed,\" I am often enviously told. “你沒變，”我常被羨慕地告知。"]}]}]},"economic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經濟的，經濟學的；有利可圖的；節約的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Economic</b> means concerned with the organization of the money, industry, and trade of a country, region, or society. 經濟的","examples":["...Poland's radical economic reforms. …波蘭激進的經濟改革。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>economic</b>, it produces a profit. 盈利的","examples":["Critics say that the new system may be more economic but will lead to a decline in programme quality. 批評家們說該新系統也許更有利可圖，卻會導致專案質量的下降。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"經濟地","examples":["...an economically depressed area. …一個經濟蕭條地區。"]}]}]},"emotional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"情感的，情緒的；激動人心的，有感染力的；情緒激動的（尤指哭泣），情感流露的；（人）易動感情的，感情用事的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Emotional</b> means concerned with emotions and feelings. 情感上的","examples":["I needed this man's love, and the emotional support he was giving me. 我那時需要這個男人的愛，以及他當時給予我的情感支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>emotional</b> situation or issue is one that causes people to have strong feelings. 引起情緒激動的","examples":["Abortion is a very emotional issue. 墮胎是個令人情緒十分激動的問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is or becomes <b>emotional</b>, they show their feelings very openly, especially because they are upset. 易情緒激動的; 易動情的","examples":["He is a very emotional man. 他是個易動情的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"情感上地","examples":["Are you saying that you're becoming emotionally involved with me? 你是說你對我產生感情了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"引起情緒激動地","examples":["In an emotionally charged speech, he said he was resigning. 在一次情緒激動的發言中，他說他要辭職。"]}]}]},"evident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"清楚的，顯然的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>evident</b>, you notice it easily and clearly. 清晰易見的","examples":["His footprints were clearly evident in the heavy dust. 他的腳印在厚厚的灰塵中清晰可見。","The threat of inflation is already evident in bond prices. 通貨膨脹的威脅在證券價格上已經是明顯可見的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>evident</b> to show that you are certain about a situation or fact and your interpretation of it. 顯然的","examples":["It was evident that she had once been a beauty. 很顯然的，她曾經是個美人。"]}]}]},"favorable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有利的，順利的，適宜的；贊成的，讚許的，肯定的；良好的，討人喜歡的"}],"sections":[]},"facial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"面部的，面部用的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"面部護理，美容"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Facial</b> means appearing on or being part of your face. 面部的","examples":["Cross didn't answer; his facial expression didn't change. 克羅斯沒有回答；他的面部表情沒有改變。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>facial</b> is a sort of beauty treatment in which someone's face is massaged, and creams and other substances are rubbed into it. 美容","examples":["Where's the best place to get a facial in New York City? 在紐約做美容最好的地方在哪兒？"]}]}]},"fantastic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，非常棒的；極大的，極高的；不切實際的，異想天開的；奇異的，怪誕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>fantastic</b>, you are emphasizing that you think it is very good or that you like it a lot. 極好的","examples":["I have a fantastic social life. 我有著極好的社交生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fantastic</b> amount or quantity is an extremely large one. 極大的 (量)","examples":["...fantastic amounts of money. …幾筆鉅款。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極其","examples":["...a fantastically expensive restaurant. …一家極其昂貴的餐館。"]}]}]},"faithful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"忠實的，忠誠的；如實的，忠於原事（物）的；忠貞的；可信任的，可信賴的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"忠實支持者（the faithful）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>faithful</b> <b>to</b> a person, organization, idea, or activity remains firm in their belief in them or support for them. 忠實的","examples":["She had been faithful to her promise to guard this secret. 她一直信守諾言保守著這個秘密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>faithful</b> <b>to</b> their husband, wife, or lover does not have a sexual relationship with anyone else. 忠貞的","examples":["I'm very faithful when I love someone. 當我愛一個人時我是非常忠貞的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>faithful</b> account, translation, or copy of something represents or reproduces the original accurately. 忠實於原文的","examples":["Colin Welland's screenplay is faithful to the novel. 科林·韋蘭的電影劇本是忠實於小說原文的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The faithful</b> are people who are faithful to someone or something. 忠實的人","examples":["He spends his time making speeches at factories or gatherings of the Party faithful. 他花時間在工廠或者在該黨忠實擁護者的集會上發表演講。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"忠實地","examples":["He has since 1965 faithfully followed and supported every twist and turn of government policy. 他從1965年起忠實地追隨並支援政府政策的每一次重大轉變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"忠實於原文地","examples":["When I adapt something I translate from one meaning to another as faithfully as I can. 我在改編的時候，我用盡量忠實於原文的方式把一種含義翻譯為另一種。"]}]}]},"fertile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"肥沃的，富饒的；可繁殖的，能結果的；能產生好結果的，促進的；點子多的，想象力豐富的；（核材料）能產生裂變物質的，增殖性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Land or soil that is <b>fertile</b> is able to support the growth of a large number of strong healthy plants. 肥沃的","examples":["...fertile soil. …肥沃的土壤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fertile</b> mind or imagination is able to produce a lot of good, original ideas. 豐富的","examples":["...a product of Flynn's fertile imagination. …弗林極富想像力的一個作品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A situation or environment that is <b>fertile</b> in relation to a particular activity or feeling encourages the activity or feeling. 促進的","examples":["...a fertile breeding ground for this kind of violent racism. …一個培養這種暴力種族主義的溫床。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A person or animal that is <b>fertile</b> is able to reproduce and have babies or young. 能生育的","examples":["The operation cannot be reversed to make her fertile again. 手術不可逆轉，無法使她重獲生育能力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"肥沃","examples":["He was able to bring large sterile acreages back to fertility. 他能把大片不毛之地變回沃土。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"生育能力","examples":["Doctors will tell you that pregnancy is the only sure test for fertility. 醫生們會告訴你懷孕是測試生育能力的惟一準確的方法。"]}]}]},"fatal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"致命的；導致失敗的，災難性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fatal</b> action has very undesirable effects. 後果嚴重的","examples":["It would be fatal for the nation to overlook the urgency of the situation. 國家若忽視這一局勢的緊迫性，後果將會非常嚴重。","He made the fatal mistake of compromising early. 他犯了妥協早了的致命錯誤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fatal</b> accident or illness causes someone's death. (事故、疾病) 致命的","examples":["...the fatal stabbing of a police sergeant. …對一名警官的致命一刺。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"後果嚴重地","examples":["Failure now could fatally damage his chances in the future. 現在的失敗能嚴重地毀掉他將來的機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(事故、疾病) 致命地","examples":["The dead soldier is reported to have been fatally wounded in the chest. 報道說死去的那名士兵胸部受到了致命傷。"]}]}]},"fierce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（動作或情感）強烈的，激烈的；（人或動物）兇猛的，狂怒的；（天氣等）狂暴的，惡劣的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<美，非正式>很，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fierce</b> animal or person is very aggressive or angry. 兇猛的; 狂怒的","examples":["They look like the teeth of some fierce animal. 它們看上去像是某種猛獸的牙齒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fierce</b> feelings or actions are very intense or enthusiastic, or involve great activity. 激烈的; 狂熱的","examples":["Consumers have a wide array of choices and price competition is fierce. 消費者的選擇面很廣，價格競爭也很激烈。","The town was captured after a fierce battle with rebels. 與叛軍的一場激戰後，這個城市被佔領了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"兇猛地; 狂怒地","examples":["\"I don't know,\" she said fiercely. “我不知道。”她非常憤怒地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"激烈地; 狂熱地","examples":["He has always been ambitious and fiercely competitive. 他一直都野心勃勃，極其爭強好鬥。"]}]}]},"experimental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"實驗性的，試驗性的；<古>根據經驗的，經驗上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>experimental</b> is new or uses new ideas or methods, and might be modified later if it is unsuccessful. 試驗性的","examples":["...an experimental air-conditioning system. …一種試驗性的空調系統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Experimental</b> means using, used in, or resulting from scientific experiments. 實驗的","examples":["...the main techniques of experimental science. …實驗科學的主要技術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>experimental</b> action is done in order to see what it is like, or what effects it has. 試驗性的","examples":["The senator is ready to argue for an experimental lifting of the ban. 該參議員已準備好爭取那條禁令的試驗性解除。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"實驗地","examples":["...an ecology laboratory, where communities of species can be studied experimentally under controlled conditions. …一個可在受控條件下對物種群落進行實驗研究的生態實驗室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"試驗性地","examples":["This system is being tried out experimentally at many universities. 該系統正在很多大學試用。"]}]}]},"financial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"財政的，金融的；<澳新，非正式>有錢的；<澳新>（俱樂部或社團成員）已繳費的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（組織或個人的）財務狀況；金融公司股票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Financial</b> means relating to or involving money. 金融的; 財政的","examples":["The company is in financial difficulties. 這個公司處於財務困難之中。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"金融上; 財政上","examples":["She would like to be more financially independent. 她想要在財政上更加獨立。"]}]}]},"fluent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（說話）流利的；（表達思想）熟練的，流暢的；（做事）嫻熟的；暢流的，能流動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>fluent</b> <b>in</b> a particular language can speak the language easily and correctly. You can also say that someone speaks <b>fluent</b> French, Chinese, or some other language. 流利的","examples":["She studied eight foreign languages but is fluent in only six of them. 她學了8種外語，但流利的只有其中的6種。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your speech, reading, or writing is <b>fluent</b>, you speak, read, or write easily, smoothly, and clearly with no mistakes. 流暢的","examples":["He had emerged from being a hesitant and unsure candidate into a fluent debater. 他從一個吞吞吐吐、毫不自信的候選人成長為一位流暢的辯手。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"流利","examples":["To work as a translator, you need fluency in at least one foreign language. 要做一名譯員，你至少要一門外語流利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"流暢","examples":["His son was praised for speeches of remarkable fluency. 他的兒子非常流利的發言受到了表揚。"]}]}]},"fragrant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"芳香的；愉快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>fragrant</b> has a pleasant, sweet smell. 芳香的","examples":["...fragrant oils and perfumes. …香精油和香水。"]}]}]},"fortunate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幸運的；帶來幸運的，吉利的；富足的；僥倖的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>fortunate</b>, you mean that they are lucky. 幸運的","examples":["He was extremely fortunate to survive. 她極為幸運地活了下來。","She is in the fortunate position of having plenty of choice. 她處在一個可有很多選擇的幸運位置上。"]}]}]},"flexible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"靈活的；柔韌的，易彎曲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flexible</b> object or material can be bent easily without breaking. 柔韌的","examples":["...brushes with long, flexible bristles. …毛長而柔韌的刷子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>flexible</b> is able to change easily and adapt to different conditions and circumstances as they occur. 靈活的","examples":["...flexible working hours. …彈性工作時間。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"柔韌性","examples":["The flexibility of the lens decreases with age; it is therefore common for our sight to worsen as we get older. 眼球晶狀體的柔韌性隨著年齡的增長而降低；因此普遍的情況是隨著我們年紀變老，我們的視力就會變差。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"靈活性","examples":["The flexibility of distance learning would be particularly suited to busy managers. 遠端學習的靈活性尤其會適合忙碌的經理們。"]}]}]},"furious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狂怒的，暴怒的；狂暴的，猛烈的；喧鬧的，熱烈興奮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>furious</b> is extremely angry. 狂怒的","examples":["He is furious at the way his wife has been treated. 他因妻子所受到的對待方式而狂怒不已。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Furious</b> is also used to describe something that is done with great energy, effort, speed, or violence. 激烈的; 玩命的; 迅猛的","examples":["A furious gunbattle ensued. 接下來的一場激烈槍戰。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狂怒地","examples":["He stormed out of the apartment, slamming the door furiously behind him. 他衝出了公寓，狂怒地把門從身後撞上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"激烈地; 玩命地; 迅猛地","examples":["Officials worked furiously to repair the centre court. 官員們玩命工作整修中央球場。"]}]}]},"gigantic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大的，龐大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>gigantic</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely large in size, amount, or degree. 巨大的","examples":["In Red Rock Valley the road is bordered by gigantic rocks. 在紅巖谷，道路兩邊都是巨大的岩石。"]}]}]},"functional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"實用的；功能的，機能的；運轉正常的；函式的；（精神病）找不出器質性原因的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Functional</b> things are useful rather than decorative. 實用的","examples":["...modern, functional furniture. …現代、實用的傢俱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Functional</b> equipment works or operates in the way that it is supposed to. 起作用的","examples":["We have fully functional smoke alarms on all staircases. 我們在所有樓梯上都裝有運轉完全正常的煙霧報警器。"]}]}]},"gifted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有天賦的，有才華的；聰慧的，有特長的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贈送；（無意中）讓（對手）獲得（gift 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>gifted</b> has a natural ability to do something well. 有天賦的","examples":["...one of the most gifted players in the world. …世界上最有天賦的運動員之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gifted</b> child is much more intelligent or talented than average. (兒童) 天資聰慧的","examples":["...a state programme for gifted children. …一項培養天才兒童的國家計劃。"]}]}]},"genuine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"真正的，非偽造的；真誠的，真心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Genuine</b> is used to describe people and things that are exactly what they appear to be, and are not false or an imitation. 真正的","examples":["There was a risk of genuine refugees being returned to Vietnam. 有把真正的難民遣送回越南的風險。","...genuine leather. …真皮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Genuine</b> refers to things such as emotions that are real and not pretended. 真誠的","examples":["If this offer is genuine, I will gladly accept it. 如果這份幫助是真誠的，我將愉快地接受它。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person as <b>genuine</b>, you approve of them because they are honest, truthful, and sincere in the way they live and in their relationships with other people. 誠實可靠的","examples":["She is very caring and very genuine. 她很有同情心，也非常誠實可靠。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"真誠地","examples":["He was genuinely surprised. 他真得吃了一驚。"]}]}]},"glorious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"光榮的，值得稱道的；輝煌的，絢麗的；極其愉快的；（天氣）陽光燦爛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>glorious</b> is very beautiful and impressive. 壯麗的","examples":["...a glorious rainbow in the air. …空中一道壯麗的彩虹。","She had missed the glorious blooms of the desert spring. 她錯過了沙漠春天的繁花美景。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>glorious</b>, you are emphasizing that it is wonderful and it makes you feel very happy. 極好的","examples":["The win revived glorious memories of his championship-winning days. 這次獲勝勾起了他對那些奪冠歲月的美好記憶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>glorious</b> career, victory, or occasion involves great fame or success. 輝煌的","examples":["Harrison had a glorious career spanning more than six decades. 哈里森有過一段長達六十餘年的輝煌的職業生涯。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"壯麗地","examples":["A tree, gloriously lit by autumn, pressed against the windowpane. 一棵被秋色染得絢麗多彩的樹壓在窗玻璃上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"極好地","examples":["...her gloriously happy love life. …她那極其幸福的愛情生活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"輝煌地","examples":["But the mission was successful, gloriously successful. 但這次任務很成功，輝煌地成功。"]}]}]},"grammatical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"語法的，和語法有關的；語法正確的，符合語法的；語法詞彙的，虛詞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grammatical</b> is used to indicate that something relates to grammar. 語法上的","examples":["Should the teacher present grammatical rules to students? 老師應該向學生講解語法規則嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's language is <b>grammatical</b>, it is considered correct because it obeys the rules of grammar. 合乎語法的","examples":["...a new test to determine whether students can write grammatical English. …一項測定學生能否寫出合乎語法的英語的新測試。"]}]}]},"gracious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有禮貌的，和藹的；豪華舒適的，富足安逸的；（上帝）慈悲的；尊貴的，仁慈的（用於對王室成員的稱呼）"},{"pos":"inter.","zh":"天哪，哎呀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>gracious</b>, you mean that they are very well-mannered and pleasant. 和藹可親的","examples":["She is a lovely and gracious woman. 她是個可愛而和藹的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe the behaviour of someone in a position of authority or high social standing as <b>gracious</b>, you mean that they behave in a polite and considerate way. 有禮貌的","examples":["She closed with a gracious speech of thanks. 她以彬彬有禮的致謝辭作結。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>gracious</b> to describe the comfortable way of life of wealthy people. (生活) 舒適的","examples":["He drove through the gracious suburbs with the swimming pools and tennis courts. 他開車穿過了建有游泳池和網球場的舒適的城郊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有禮貌地","examples":["Hospitality at the presidential guest house was graciously declined. 總統套房裡的款待被婉言謝絕了。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say <b>good gracious</b> or <b>goodness gracious</b> in order to express surprise or annoyance. 天哪 (表示驚訝、不滿等)","examples":["Good gracious, look at that specimen, will you? 天哪，你看看那個傢伙，好嗎？"]}]}]},"grateful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感謝的，感激的；（尤用於書信或正式場合提出請求）感激不盡，請；<古>令人獲得快意的，受歡迎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>grateful</b> <b>for</b> something that someone has given you or done for you, you have warm, friendly feelings towards them and wish to thank them. 感激的","examples":["She was grateful to him for being so good to her. 她很感激他對她這麼好。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"感激地","examples":["\"That's kind of you, Sally,\" Claire said gratefully. “你真好，薩莉”，克萊爾感激地說。"]}]}]},"greasy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"沾油脂的，油汙的；含脂肪的，油膩的；油性的；滑的；圓滑的，虛情假意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>greasy</b> has grease on it or in it. 有油脂的","examples":["He propped his elbows upon a greasy counter. 他把胳膊肘撐在油膩膩的櫃檯上。"]}]}]},"habitual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"習慣性的，慣常的；上癮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>habitual</b> action, state, or way of behaving is one that someone usually does or has, especially one that is considered to be typical or characteristic of them. 習慣性的","examples":["If bad posture becomes habitual, you risk long-term effects. 如果不良姿勢成為習慣，你會有遭受長期影響的危險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>habitual</b> to describe someone who usually or often does a particular thing. 積習難改的","examples":["Three out of four of them would become habitual criminals if actually sent to jail. 如果真的被投入監獄，他們中3/4的人會成為積習難改的罪犯。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"習慣性地","examples":["His mother had a patient who habitually flew into rages. 她的母親有一個習慣性地陷入狂怒的病人。"]}]}]},"healthful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有益於健康的，促進健康的；健全的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>healthful</b> is good for your health. 有益健康的","examples":["Does the college cafeteria provide a healthful diet? 此大學餐廳是否供應有益健康的膳食？"]}]}]},"graceful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"優美的，優雅的；得體的，有風度的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>graceful</b> moves in a smooth and controlled way that is attractive to watch. 優雅的","examples":["His movements were so graceful they seemed effortless. 他的動作如此優雅，看似非常從容自如。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>graceful</b> is attractive because it has a pleasing shape or style. 優美的","examples":["His handwriting, from earliest young manhood, was flowing and graceful. 從他剛剛成年時起，他的書法就流暢而優美。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"優雅地","examples":["She stepped gracefully onto the stage. 她步態優雅地走上舞臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"優美地","examples":["She loved the gracefully high ceiling, with its white-painted cornice. 她喜歡那雅緻的、簷口被漆成白色的高高的天花板。"]}]}]},"guilty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內疚的，羞愧的；有罪的，有過失的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>guilty</b>, you feel unhappy because you think that you have done something wrong or have failed to do something which you should have done. 內疚的","examples":["I feel so guilty, leaving all this to you. 把所有這一切都留給了你，我覺得很內疚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Guilty</b> is used of an action or fact that you feel guilty about. 罪惡的","examples":["Many may be keeping it a guilty secret. 許多人可能將它作為一個罪惡的秘密保守著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>guilty</b> <b>of</b> a crime or offence, they have committed that crime or offence. 犯罪的","examples":["They were found guilty of murder. 他們被判犯有謀殺罪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>guilty</b> <b>of</b> doing something wrong, they have done that thing. 有過失的","examples":["He claimed Mr. Brooke had been guilty of a \"gross error of judgment.\" 他聲稱布魯克先生犯有“判決上的重大過失”。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"內疚地","examples":["He glanced guiltily over his shoulder. 他內疚地向後瞥了一眼。"]}]}]},"harsh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（環境）惡劣的，艱苦的；嚴厲的，殘酷的；刺耳的，難聽的；刺眼的，耀眼的；醜陋的；刺激性強的，太強力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Harsh</b> climates or conditions are very difficult for people, animals, and plants to live in. 嚴酷的","examples":["...the harsh desert environment. …嚴酷的沙漠環境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Harsh</b> actions or speech are unkind and show no understanding or sympathy. 殘酷的","examples":["He said many harsh and unkind things about his opponents. 他說了許多關於他對手的嚴厲且殘酷的話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>harsh</b> is so hard, bright, or rough that it seems unpleasant or harmful. (因過於刺激、明亮或粗糙而) 令人不快的","examples":["Tropical colours may look rather harsh in our dull northern light. 熱帶叢林的色彩在我們暗淡的北極光下也許會顯得很刺眼。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Harsh</b> voices and sounds are ones that are rough and unpleasant to listen to. 刺耳的","examples":["It's a pity she has such a loud harsh voice. 可惜她有這麼一種響亮刺耳的聲音。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you talk about <b>harsh</b> realities or facts, or the <b>harsh</b> truth, you are emphasizing that they are true or real, although they are unpleasant and people try to avoid thinking about them. 殘酷的 (事實、情況)","examples":["The harsh truth is that luck plays a big part in who will live or die. 殘酷的現實是，運氣在很大程度上決定著誰生誰死。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"艱苦","examples":["...the harshness of their living conditions. …他們生活條件之艱苦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不快","examples":["As the wine ages, it loses its bitter harshness. 隨著葡萄酒變陳，酒中的苦澀味就會消失。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"殘酷地","examples":["She's been told that her husband is being harshly treated in prison. 她被告知她丈夫正在監獄裡遭受嚴酷的對待。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"刺耳地","examples":["Chris laughed harshly. 克里斯大笑，聲音刺耳。"]}]}]},"honorable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"光榮的；可敬的；高貴的；正直的，值得尊敬的；尊敬的（用於法官、議員等尊稱，常寫作 the Honorable）（honourable 的美式寫法）"}],"sections":[]},"imaginable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可想象的，想象得到的；可能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>imaginable</b> after a superlative such as \"best\" or \"worst\" to emphasize that something is extreme in some way. 可想像的 (常與)(best)(、)(worst)(等形容詞最高階連用表示強調)","examples":["...their imprisonment under some of the most horrible circumstances imaginable. …他們在能想像得出的最恐怖的環境裡蹲監獄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>imaginable</b> after a word like \"every\" or \"all\" to emphasize that you are talking about all the possible examples of something. You use <b>imaginable</b> after \"no\" to emphasize that something does not have the quality mentioned. (用於)(every) 一切可能的; (用於)(no)(之後表示強調) 毫無","examples":["Parents encourage every activity imaginable. 父母鼓勵一切可能的活動。","...a place of no imaginable strategic value. …一個毫無戰略價值的地方。"]}]}]},"hopeful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滿懷希望的；有希望的，有前途的；（行動）被寄予希望的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"希望成功的人，有前途的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>hopeful</b>, you are fairly confident that something that you want to happen will happen. 滿懷希望的","examples":["I am hopeful this misunderstanding will be rectified very quickly. 我滿懷希望這一誤解很快就能得到澄清。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a sign or event is <b>hopeful</b>, it makes you feel that what you want to happen will happen. (事物) 給人以希望的","examples":["The result of the election is yet another hopeful sign that peace could come to the Middle East. 這次選舉的結果是和平有希望降臨中東的又一個徵兆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hopeful</b> action is one that you do in the hope that you will get what you want to get. (行為) 被寄予希望的","examples":["We've chartered the aircraft in the hopeful anticipation that the government will allow them to leave. 我們包租了那架飛機，希望政府會允許他們離開。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"滿懷希望地","examples":["\"Am I welcome?\" He smiled hopefully, leaning on the door. “歡迎我嗎？”他倚著門，滿懷希望地笑著問道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>hopeful</b>, you mean that they are hoping and trying to achieve success in a particular career, election, or competition. 有希望成功的人","examples":["His skills continue to be put to good use in his job as coach to young hopefuls. 作為有望成功的年輕人的教練，他的技能繼續得到充分利用。"]}]}]},"ignorant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無知的，（對某事物）不瞭解的；<非正式>無禮的，粗魯的；暴躁的，易怒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>ignorant</b>, you mean that they do not know things they should know. If someone is <b>ignorant</b> <b>of</b> a fact, they do not know it. 無知的","examples":["People don't like to ask questions for fear of appearing ignorant. 人們不喜歡問問題，生怕顯得自己無知。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People are sometimes described as <b>ignorant</b> when they do something that is not polite or kind. 不禮貌的","examples":["I met some ignorant people who called me all kinds of names. 我碰見了一些粗魯人，他們用各種名稱叫我。"]}]}]},"identical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全相同的；同一的；（雙胞胎）同卵的；恆等的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Things that are <b>identical</b> are exactly the same. 完全相同的","examples":["The three bombs were virtually identical. 這3個炸彈幾乎一模一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"完全相同地","examples":["...nine identically dressed female dancers. …9個著裝相同的女舞蹈演員。"]}]}]},"imaginary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"想象的，虛構的；虛數的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>imaginary</b> person, place, or thing exists only in your mind or in a story, and not in real life. 假想的","examples":["Lots of children have imaginary friends. 許多孩子都有假想的朋友。"]}]}]},"imaginative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"富於想象力的，創新的；運用想象（力）的，虛構的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or their ideas as <b>imaginative</b>, you are praising them because they are easily able to think of or create new or exciting things. 富於想像力的","examples":["...an imaginative writer. …一位富有想像力的作家。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"富於想像力地","examples":["The hotel is decorated imaginatively and attractively. 這家旅館裝飾得很有想像力和吸引力。"]}]}]},"informative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"提供有用資訊的，增長見聞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>informative</b> gives you useful information. 提供有用資訊的; 使人增進知識的","examples":["Both men termed the meeting friendly and informative. 他們兩人都稱這次會晤親切友好，使雙方增進了解。"]}]}]},"influential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有影響力的，有勢力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有影響力的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>influential</b> has a lot of influence over people or events. 有影響力的; 有權勢的","examples":["It helps to have influential friends. 交上幾個有權勢的朋友很有好處。","He had been influential in shaping economic policy. 他在制定經濟政策方面曾起過很大作用。"]}]}]},"intense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很大的，十分強烈的；嚴肅緊張的，激烈的；熱情的，熱切的；專注的，認真的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intense</b> is used to describe something that is very great or extreme in strength or degree. 劇烈的; 極度的","examples":["He was sweating from the intense heat. 由於劇烈的熱量，他一直出汗。","Stevens's murder was the result of a deep-seated and intense hatred. 史蒂文斯兇殺案源於深仇大恨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an activity as <b>intense</b>, you mean that it is very serious and concentrated, and often involves doing a lot in a short time. 集中的; 緊張的","examples":["The battle for third place was intense. 競爭第3名的較量很緊張。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe the way someone looks at you as <b>intense</b>, you mean that they look at you very directly and seem to know what you are thinking or feeling. 熱切的","examples":["I felt so self-conscious under Luke's mother's intense gaze. 在盧克母親熱切的注視下，我感到很不自在。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a person as <b>intense</b>, you mean that they appear to concentrate very hard on everything that they do, and they feel their emotions very strongly. 很認真的","examples":["I know he's an intense player, but he does enjoy what he's doing. 我知道他是名很認真的選手，可他確實喜歡他所做的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"劇烈地; 極度地","examples":["The fast-food business is intensely competitive. 快餐業競爭非常激烈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"熱切地","examples":["He sipped his drink, staring intensely at me. 他一邊小口喝著飲料，一邊熱切地盯著我。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"過分認真","examples":["His intensity and the ferocity of his feelings alarmed me. 他的過分認真和激烈的感受令我恐慌。"]}]}]},"lawful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合法的，法律許可的；法定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an activity, organization, or product is <b>lawful</b>, it is allowed by law. 合法的","examples":["The detention of the fugitive was lawful. 對逃亡者的拘留是合法的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合法地","examples":["Amnesty International is trying to establish whether the police acted lawfully in shooting him. 大赦國際正試圖證實警察向他開槍是否合法。"]}]}]},"intensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"加強的，集中的，深入細緻的；精耕細作的，集約的；加強詞意的；以強度測量的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"加強語勢的形容詞（或副詞、小品詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intensive</b> activity involves concentrating a lot of effort or people on one particular task in order to try to achieve a lot in a short time. 集中的","examples":["...after several days and nights of intensive negotiations. …在幾個日夜的集中談判之後。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Intensive</b> farming involves producing as many crops or animals as possible from your land, usually with the aid of chemicals. 集約的","examples":["...intensive methods of rearing poultry. …集約飼養家禽的方法。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"集中地","examples":["Caitlin's parents opted to educate her intensively at home. 凱特林的父母選擇在家對她進行強化教育。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"集約地","examples":["Will they farm the rest of their land less intensively? 他們會在耕種其餘土地時不這麼集約嗎？"]}]}]},"intelligent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聰明的；有智力的；智慧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or animal that is <b>intelligent</b> has the ability to think, understand, and learn things quickly and well. 有智慧的","examples":["Susan's a very bright and intelligent woman who knows her own mind. 蘇珊是一個非常聰明伶俐而且清楚自己想法的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>intelligent</b> can think and understand instead of doing things automatically or by instinct. 有智慧的","examples":["Intelligent computers will soon be an indispensable diagnostic tool for every doctor. 智慧計算機很快將會成為每位醫生必不可少的診斷工具。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有頭腦地","examples":["They are incapable of thinking intelligently about politics. 他們在考慮政治問題時缺乏頭腦。"]}]}]},"literary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"文學的，文學上的；書面的；愛好文學的，從事文學研究（或寫作）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Literary</b> means concerned with or connected with the writing, study, or appreciation of literature. 文學的","examples":["Her literary criticism focuses on the way great literature suggests ideas. 她的文學批評集中於偉大文學作品表達思想的方法。","She's the literary editor of the \"Sunday Review.\" 她是《週日評論》的文學編輯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Literary</b> words and expressions are often unusual in some way and are used to create a special effect in a piece of writing such as a poem, speech, or novel. 書面的","examples":["...archaic, literary words from the Tang dynasty. …唐代的古文書面用詞。"]}]}]},"lousy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>極壞的，惡劣的；<非正式>令人厭惡的，討厭的；<非正式>（讓人不快的事物）很多的；<非正式>不擅長的；<非正式>微薄的，不起眼的；<非正式>很難受的，非常不舒服的；<非正式>不開心的；<非正式>不正確的，不恰當的；滿是蝨子的；<非正式>感到不適的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>lousy</b>, you mean that it is of very bad quality or that you do not like it. 糟糕的","examples":["He blamed Fiona for a lousy weekend. 他指責菲奧娜讓他過了一個糟糕的週末。","At Billy's Café, the menu is limited and the food is lousy. 比利餐館飯菜品種有限，質量也很糟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>lousy</b>, you mean that they are very bad at something they do. 蹩腳的","examples":["I was a lousy secretary. 我曾是個蹩腳的秘書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe the number or amount of something as <b>lousy</b>, you mean it is smaller than you think it should be. 微薄的","examples":["The pay is lousy. 薪水少得可憐。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you feel <b>lousy</b>, you feel very ill. 極不舒服的","examples":["I wasn't actually sick but I felt lousy. 我其實沒有生病，但感覺很不舒服。"]}]}]},"logical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合情合理的；合乎邏輯的；邏輯（上）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a <b>logical</b> argument or method of reasoning, each step must be true if the step before it is true. 邏輯的 (觀點或推理方式)","examples":["Only when each logical step has been checked by other mathematicians will the proof be accepted. 只有在每個邏輯步驟都由其他數學家驗證之後，該證明才會被接受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>logical</b> conclusion or result of a series of facts or events is the only one which can come from it, according to the rules of logic. 合乎邏輯的 (結論或結果等)","examples":["If the climate gets drier, then the logical conclusion is that even more drought will occur. 如果氣候變得更乾燥，那麼符合邏輯的結論就是甚至更多的旱災將會發生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>logical</b> seems reasonable or sensible in the circumstances. 合理的; 明智的","examples":["Connie suddenly struck her as a logical candidate. 她突然想到康尼是個合適的人選。","There was a logical explanation. 存在一個合理的解釋。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"邏輯地","examples":["My professional training has taught me to look at things logically. 我的專業訓練教會了我邏輯地看待事物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"合乎邏輯地","examples":["From that it followed logically that he would not be meeting Hildegarde. 從那一點看來，他不會見希爾德加德是合乎邏輯的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"合理地; 明智地","examples":["This was the one possibility I hadn't taken into consideration, though logically I should have. 這是一種我沒有考慮到的可能性，儘管按道理我本該考慮到的。"]}]}]},"loyal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"忠誠的，忠貞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>loyal</b> remains firm in their friendship or support for a person or thing. 忠誠的","examples":["They had remained loyal to the president. 他們一直忠於總統。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"忠誠地","examples":["They have loyally supported their party and their leader. 他們忠心耿耿地支援自己的政黨和領導人。"]}]}]},"keen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"渴望的，熱衷的；喜愛的，著迷的；熱情的，熱心的；（興趣或感情）濃厚的，強烈的；思維敏捷的，敏銳的；（目光或聽覺）靈敏的；（戰鬥或競爭）激烈的，緊張的；<英>（價格）低廉的，有競爭力的；<舊>寒冷刺骨的；鋒利的，銳利的；（氣味、光或聲音）有穿透力的，強烈的，明淨的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（為死者）慟哭，哀號"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"痛哭，輓歌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone has a <b>keen</b> mind, you mean that they are very clever and aware of what is happening around them.  敏銳的","examples":["They described him as a man of keen intellect. 他們把他描述成一個才思敏銳的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>keen</b> eye or ear, you are able to notice things that are difficult to detect.  靈敏的","examples":["...an amateur artist with a keen eye for detail. …一位對細節有敏銳洞察力的業餘藝術家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>keen</b> interest or emotion is one that is very intense.  強烈的","examples":["He had retained a keen interest in the progress of the work. 他一直對工作的進展保持著強烈的興趣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you are <b>keen</b> <b>on</b> doing something, you very much want to do it. 渴望的","examples":["You're not keen on going, are you? 你不是很想走，對嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you are <b>keen on</b> something, you like it a lot and are very enthusiastic about it. 熱衷的","examples":["I wasn't too keen on physics and chemistry. 我對物理和化學並不太熱衷。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>keen</b> to indicate that someone has a lot of enthusiasm for a particular activity and spends a lot of time doing it. 著迷的","examples":["She was a keen amateur photographer. 她是一個痴迷的業餘攝影師。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>keen</b> fight or competition is one in which the competitors are all trying very hard to win, and it is not easy to predict who will win. 激烈的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"敏銳地","examples":["They're keenly aware that whatever they decide will set a precedent. 他們敏銳地意識到無論他們決定怎麼做，都會開創先例。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"靈敏地","examples":["Charles listened keenly. 查爾斯豎起耳朵聽著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"強烈地","examples":["She remained keenly interested in international affairs. 她一直對國際事務有強烈的興趣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"激烈地","examples":["The contest should be very keenly fought. 比賽應該爭奪很激烈。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"渴望","examples":["...Doyle's keenness to please. …多伊爾的極欲討好心態。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to lament the dead 哀悼","examples":[]}]}]},"lunar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"月亮的，月球的；銀的；陰曆的；似月的，月牙形的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lunar</b> means relating to the moon. 月球的","examples":["The vast volcanic slope was eerily reminiscent of a lunar landscape. 巨大的火山坡很奇怪地讓人想起月球上的景觀。"]}]}]},"luxurious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奢侈的，豪華的；心滿意足的，舒適的；辭藻華麗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>luxurious</b>, you mean that it is very comfortable and expensive. 豪華的","examples":["Our honeymoon was two days in Las Vegas at a luxurious hotel called Le Mirage. 我們的蜜月為期兩天，是在拉斯維加斯一家名為“幻影”的豪華酒店度過的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Luxurious</b> means feeling or expressing great pleasure and comfort. 心情舒暢的","examples":["Amy tilted her wine in her glass with a luxurious sigh. 埃米把杯中的葡萄酒斜向一邊，適意地嘆了口氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"豪華地","examples":["The dining-room is luxuriously furnished and carpeted. 餐廳裡的傢俱和地毯非常豪華。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"心情舒暢地","examples":["Liz laughed, stretching luxuriously. 莉茲一邊大笑，一邊心情舒暢地伸了個懶腰。"]}]}]},"memorable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難忘的，值得紀念的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>memorable</b> is worth remembering or likely to be remembered, because it is special or very enjoyable. 值得記住的; 易記住的","examples":["...the perfect setting for a nostalgic memorable day. …作為懷念難忘的一天的最佳景場。"]}]}]},"magnificent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"宏偉的，壯麗的；令人印象深刻的，出色的；高尚的，高貴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>magnificent</b>, you mean that you think they are extremely good, beautiful, or impressive. 出色的; 壯麗的","examples":["...a magnificent country house in wooded grounds. …林地中一座漂亮的村宅。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"出色; 壯麗","examples":["I shall never forget the magnificence of the Swiss mountains and the beauty of the lakes. 我永遠也不會忘記瑞士山嶽的壯美和湖泊的秀麗。"]}]}]},"magnetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"磁的，磁性的；磁化的；有吸引力的，有魅力的；（航向）根據磁北測定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something metal is <b>magnetic</b>, it acts like a magnet. 有磁性的","examples":["...magnetic particles. …磁性粒子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>magnetic</b> to describe something that is caused by or relates to the force of magnetism. 有磁力的","examples":["The electrically charged gas particles are affected by magnetic forces. 帶電的氣體粒子受磁力的影響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>magnetic</b> to describe tapes and other objects which have a coating of a magnetic substance and contain coded information that can be read by computers or other machines. (磁帶、卡等) 有磁的","examples":["...her magnetic-strip ID card. …她的帶磁條的身份證。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>magnetic</b>, you mean that it is very attractive to people because it has unusual, powerful, and exciting qualities. 有吸引力的","examples":["...the magnetic effect of the prosperous American economy on would-be immigrants. …繁榮的美國經濟對未來移民的吸引力。"]}]}]},"learned":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"博學的；學術性的，學者的；後天的，習得的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"學習，學會；得知，獲悉；背熟，熟記；認識到，（從……）吸取教訓 （learn 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>learned</b> person has gained a lot of knowledge by studying. 博學的","examples":["He is a scholar, a genuinely learned man. 他是個學者，一個真正博學的人。"]}]}]},"mere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"僅僅，只不過；只憑……就足以"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>小湖，池塘；（尤指毛利人用綠巖制的武器）石棒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>mere</b> to emphasize how unimportant or inadequate something is, in comparison to the general situation you are describing. 只不過","examples":["...successful exhibitions which go beyond mere success. …不僅僅是成功，而是大獲成功的展覽。","There is more to good health than the mere absence of disease. 健康不僅僅指不生病，還包括更多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>mere</b> to indicate that a quality or action that is usually unimportant has a very important or strong effect. 單單的 (用來指某事雖小卻有重要影響)","examples":["The mere mention of food had triggered off hunger pangs. 單單提到食物就引起了陣陣的飢餓感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>mere</b> to emphasize how small a particular amount or number is. 只不過 (用於強調數量之少)","examples":["Sixty percent of teachers are women, but a mere five percent of women are principals. 60％的教師是女性，但只有5％的女性是校長。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a lake or marsh 湖; 沼澤","examples":[]}]}]},"messy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"髒的，凌亂的；使髒亂的，使不整潔的；棘手的，令人厭煩的；馬虎的，不精確的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>messy</b> person or activity makes things dirty or not neat. 邋遢的","examples":["She was a good, if messy, cook. 儘管有點邋遢，她還是一名好廚師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>messy</b> is dirty or not neat. 髒的","examples":["Don't worry if this first coat of paint looks messy. 如果這第一層油漆看上去有點髒的話，不用擔心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>messy</b>, you are emphasizing that it is confused or complicated, and therefore unsatisfactory. 混亂而複雜的","examples":["John had been through a messy divorce himself. 約翰自己經歷過一次棘手的離婚。"]}]}]},"mechanical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"機械（方面）的；機械般的，呆板的；精通機械的；機械學的，力學的；獨家灌錄權的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"技工，機修工；勞工，工匠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mechanical</b> device has parts that move when it is working, often using power from an engine or from electricity. 機械的","examples":["...a small mechanical device that taps out the numbers. …一種能夠敲打出數字的小型機械裝置。","This is the oldest working mechanical clock in the world. 這是世界上最古老的還可以使用的機械鐘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Mechanical</b> means relating to machines and engines and the way they work. 機械方面的","examples":["...mechanical engineering. …機械工程學。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person as <b>mechanical</b>, you mean they are naturally good at understanding how machines work. 天生對機械擅長的","examples":["He was a very mechanical person, who knew a lot about sound. 他是個非常精通機械的人，對聲音很瞭解。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone's action as <b>mechanical</b>, you mean that they do it automatically, without thinking about it. 機械似的","examples":["It is real prayer, and not mechanical repetition. 這是真正的祈禱，而不是機械式的重複。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"機械地","examples":["The air was circulated mechanically. 空氣是用機械推動迴圈的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"機械方面地","examples":["The car was mechanically sound, he decided. 這輛車從機械的角度來說是非常可靠的，他判定道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"天生對機械擅長地","examples":["I'm not mechanically minded. 我沒有機械方面的頭腦。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"機械似地","examples":["He nodded mechanically, his eyes fixed on the girl. 他機械地點點頭，眼睛盯著那個女孩。"]}]}]},"mountainous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多山的；巨大的，山一般的；波濤洶湧的，萬丈波濤的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mountainous</b> place has a lot of mountains. 多山的","examples":["...the mountainous region of New Mexico. …新墨西哥州的多山地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>mountainous</b> to emphasize that something is great in size, quantity, or degree. 巨大的; 大量的","examples":["The plan is designed to reduce some of the company's mountainous debt. 制定這個計劃是為了減少該公司的一部分鉅額債務。"]}]}]},"nearsighted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"近視的；目光短淺的，缺乏遠見的，淺見的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>nearsighted</b> cannot see distant things clearly. 近視的","examples":[]}]}]},"mild":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（傷病）不嚴重的，輕微的；（感覺或表情）不強烈的，微弱的；（懲罰或批評）不嚴厲的；輕的，不過度的；（味道）清淡的，不刺激的；（藥物、化妝品等）柔和的，無副作用的；（肥皂、洗滌液）溫和的，不傷皮膚的；（天氣）和煦的，溫暖的；（人或其行為）和善的，隨和的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>淡味黑啤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mild</b> is used to describe something such as a feeling, attitude, or illness that is not very strong or severe. 輕微的","examples":["Teddy turned to Mona with a look of mild confusion. 特迪轉向莫娜，臉上帶著些許困惑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mild</b> person is gentle and does not get angry easily. 性情溫和的","examples":["He is a mild man, who is reasonable almost to the point of blandness. 他是個性情溫和、理智到了近乎呆板的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Mild</b> weather is pleasant because it is neither extremely hot nor extremely cold. 溫暖的","examples":["The area is famous for its very mild winter climate. 這個地區以其非常溫暖的冬季氣候而聞名。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You describe food as <b>mild</b> when it does not taste or smell strong, sharp, or bitter, especially when you like it because of this. 味淡的","examples":["This cheese has a soft, mild flavour. 這種乳酪有種柔和的、淡淡的味道。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕微地","examples":["Josephine must have had the disease very mildly as she showed no symptoms. 約瑟芬那時一定病得很輕，因為她沒表現出什麼症狀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"溫和地","examples":["\"I'm not meddling,\" Ken said mildly, \"I'm just curious.\" “我不是在管閒事，”肯溫和地說，“我只是好奇。”"]}]}]},"miserable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"痛苦的，使人難受的；（人）乖戾的，總是抱怨的；少得可憐的，太少的；糟糕的，差勁的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>miserable</b>, you are very unhappy. 痛苦的","examples":["I took a series of badly paid secretarial jobs which made me really miserable. 我連著幹了幾份工資很低的秘書工作，這讓我感到真的很痛苦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place or situation as <b>miserable</b>, you mean that it makes you feel unhappy or depressed. 令人憂傷的","examples":["There was nothing at all in this miserable place to distract him. 在這個令人憂傷的地方，根本沒什麼東西可以轉移他的注意力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe the weather as <b>miserable</b>, you mean that it makes you feel depressed, because it is raining or dull. 陰冷多雨的","examples":["On a grey, wet, miserable day our teams congregated in Port Townsend. 在灰暗、潮溼而又陰冷的一天，我們幾隊人聚集在了湯森港。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>miserable</b>, you mean that you do not like them because they are bad-tempered or unfriendly. 脾氣不好的; 不友好的","examples":["He always was a miserable man. He never spoke to me nor anybody else, not even to pass the time of day. 他總是不友好。他從不和我說話，也不和別人說話，那怕是為了打發時光。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can describe a quantity or quality as <b>miserable</b> when you think that it is much smaller or worse than it ought to be. 少得可憐的","examples":["Our speed over the ground was a miserable 2.2 knots. 我們在地面上的速度只有區區的2.2節。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>miserable</b> failure is a very great one. 慘痛的","examples":["The film was a miserable commercial failure both in Italy and in the United States. 這部電影在義大利和美國票房收入都遭到了慘敗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"痛苦地","examples":["He looked miserably down at his plate. 他痛苦地低頭看著自己的盤子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"少得可憐地","examples":["...the miserably inadequate supply of books now provided for schools. …現在提供給學校的書籍少得可憐。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"悲慘地","examples":["Some manage it. Some fail miserably. 有人成功了。有些人敗得很慘。"]}]}]},"muddy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"泥濘的，多泥的；含泥的，渾濁的；灰暗的，暗淡的；模糊的，不清晰的；（聲音，尤指樂聲）重濁的；像泥土般的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變得泥濘，使渾濁；使模糊，使混亂；使（顏色）變暗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>muddy</b> contains mud or is covered in mud. 泥濘的","examples":["...a muddy track. …一條泥濘的小路。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>muddy</b> something, you cause it to be muddy. 使沾上泥巴","examples":["The ground still smelled of rain and they muddied their shoes. 地面仍散發著雨水的氣息，他們的鞋沾上了泥巴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>muddies</b> a situation or issue, they cause it to seem less clear and less easy to understand. 攪亂 (局勢、問題等)","examples":["It's difficult enough without muddying the issue with religion. 即使不和宗教攪在一起，這個問題也已夠難的了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>muddies the waters</b>, they cause a situation or issue to seem less clear and less easy to understand. 攪渾水","examples":[]}]}]},"modest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不太多的，適中的；謙虛的，謙遜的；保守的，端莊的；不錯的；（服裝）不顯身材的；羞怯的，靦腆的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>modest</b> house or other building is not large or expensive. 適度的","examples":["They had spent the night at a modest hotel. 他們在一家普通的旅館過夜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>modest</b> to describe something such as an amount, rate, or improvement which is fairly small. (數量、比率或改進幅度等) 較小的","examples":["Unemployment rose to the still modest rate of 0.7%. 失業率升高到0.7%這個還算低的水平。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>modest</b>, you approve of them because they do not talk much about their abilities or achievements. 謙虛的","examples":["He's modest, as well as being a great player. 他是一個謙虛而且出色的運動員。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"較小地","examples":["The nation's balance of payments improved modestly last month. 這個國家上個月的國際收支有了較小的改善。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"謙虛地","examples":["\"You really must be very good at what you do.\"—\"I suppose I am,\" Kate said modestly. “你確實非常擅長你所做的。” —“我覺得是吧。”凱特謙虛地說。"]}]}]},"multiple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多個的，多種的；多人共有的；影響身體許多部位的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"倍數；<英>連鎖商店；（電信）復聯，復接"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>multiple</b> to describe things that consist of many parts, involve many people, or have many uses. 多部分的; 涉及多人的; 多功能的","examples":["He died of multiple injuries. 他死於多處受傷。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one number is a <b>multiple of</b> a smaller number, it can be exactly divided by that smaller number. 倍數","examples":["Their numerical system, derived from the Babylonians, was based on multiples of the number six. 他們的數制是襲用巴比倫人的，以數字6的倍數為基準。"]}]}]},"moderate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普通的，中等的；不偏激的，溫和的；有節制的，不過分的；（變化）不大的，有限的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩和，使適中；主持（討論或會議）；稽核評分（檢視不同閱卷人所打分數是否公平一致）；（物理）使（中子）減速"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"持溫和政見者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Moderate</b> political opinions or policies are not extreme. (政見或政策) 溫和的","examples":["He was an easygoing man of very moderate views. 他是一個有著溫和觀點性情隨和的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>moderate</b> to describe people or groups who have moderate political opinions or policies. (人或團體) 溫和的","examples":["...a moderate Democrat. …溫和的民主黨人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>moderate</b> to describe something that is neither large nor small in amount or degree. (數量或程度) 適中的","examples":["While a moderate amount of stress can be beneficial, too much stress can exhaust you. 適當的壓力可能有益，而壓力過大會讓你筋疲力盡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>moderate</b> change in something is a change that is not great. (變化) 不大的","examples":["Most drugs offer either no real improvement or, at best, only moderate improvements. 大多數藥或者沒有真正療效，或者最多也就是稍有療效。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>moderate</b> is someone with moderate political opinions. 溫和派","examples":["If he presents himself as a radical he risks scaring off the moderates whose votes he so desperately needs. 如果他表現出自己是個激進分子的話，他就有可能嚇跑那些溫和派，而他急需那些人的選票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"緩和","examples":["A moderation in food prices helped to offset the first increase in energy prices. 食品價格的降低有助於抵消能源價格的第一次上漲。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"適中地","examples":["Both are moderately large insects, with a wingspan of around four centimetres. 這兩隻都是中等大小的昆蟲，翼幅大約為四釐米。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不大地","examples":["Share prices on the Tokyo Exchange declined moderately. 東京股票交易所的股票價格稍有下降。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>moderate</b> something or if it <b>moderates</b>, it becomes less extreme or violent and easier to deal with or accept. 使緩和; 變得緩和","examples":["They are hoping that once in office he can be persuaded to moderate his views. 他們希望他一上臺後就能他說服，使他的觀點變得溫和些。"]}]}]},"needy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）貧困的；（環境）貧窮的；需要關注的，需要情感支援的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Needy</b> people do not have enough food, medicine, or clothing, or adequate houses. 貧困的","examples":["...a multinational force aimed at ensuring that food and medicine get to needy Somalis. …旨在確保食品和藥品送到索馬利亞貧民手中的一支多國部隊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The needy</b> are people who are needy. 窮人","examples":["There will be efforts to get larger amounts of food to the needy. 將努力把更多的食品送給窮人。"]}]}]},"mutual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相互的，彼此的；共同的，共有的；（保險公司、建築協會等）互助的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"互助公司"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>mutual</b> to describe a situation, feeling, or action that is experienced, felt, or done by both of two people mentioned. 相互的","examples":["The East and the West can work together for their mutual benefit and progress. 東西方可以為互惠和進步而合作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>mutual</b> to describe something such as an interest which two or more people share. 共同的","examples":["They do, however, share a mutual interest in design. 然而，他們確實對設計有共同的興趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an insurance company or savings bank has <b>mutual</b> status, it is not owned by shareholders but by its customers, who receive a share of the profits. (保險公司或儲蓄銀行) 互助的","examples":["...a mutual company based in Columbus, Ohio. …一家總部在俄亥俄州哥倫布市的互助公司。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"相互地","examples":["Attempts to reach a mutually agreed solution had been fruitless. 想要達成一個彼此同意的解決方案，卻無果而終。"]}]}]},"mysterious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不可思議的，難以理解的；（人）神秘的，陌生的；保密的，故弄玄虛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>mysterious</b> is strange and is not known about or understood. 神秘的; 難以理解的","examples":["He died in mysterious circumstances. 他死得蹊蹺。","A mysterious illness confined him to bed for over a month. 一種怪病讓他臥床一個多月。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>mysterious</b> about something, they deliberately do not talk much about it, sometimes because they want to make people more interested in it. 詭秘的","examples":["As for his job – well, he was very mysterious about it. 至於他的工作–嘿，他對此十分詭秘。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"神秘地","examples":["A couple of messages had mysteriously disappeared. 幾條資訊已經神秘地消失了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"詭秘地","examples":["Asked what she meant, she said mysteriously: \"Work it out for yourself.\" 當被問及她什麼意思時，她詭秘地說：“你自己想想吧。”"]}]}]},"numerous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"眾多的，許多的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things are <b>numerous</b>, they exist or are present in large numbers. 許多的","examples":["Sex crimes were just as numerous as they are today. 當時的性犯罪與現在一樣多。"]}]}]},"occasional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偶爾的，不經常的；（傢俱）特定場合才使用的； （文章、演講或宗教儀式等）在特殊場合所作的，為特殊場合所準備的；非定時的，臨時的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Occasional</b> means happening sometimes, but not regularly or often. 偶爾的","examples":["I've had occasional mild headaches all my life. 我此生一直有偶爾的輕微頭疼。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"偶爾地","examples":["He still misbehaves occasionally. 他仍偶爾行為不乖。"]}]}]},"obedient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"服從的，順從的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or animal who is <b>obedient</b> does what they are told to do. 順從的; 服從的","examples":["He was very respectful at home and obedient to his parents. 他在家裡很尊重人而且順從父母。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"順從; 服從","examples":["...unquestioning obedience to the law. …對法律的絕對服從。"]}]}]},"nuclear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"核子的，原子核的；核武器的；原子能的，核能的；核心的，中心的；細胞核的，構成細胞核的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nuclear</b> means relating to the nuclei of atoms, or to the energy released when these nuclei are split or combined. 核的","examples":["...a nuclear power station. …一座核電站。","...nuclear energy. …核能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Nuclear</b> means relating to weapons that explode by using the energy released when the nuclei of atoms are split or combined. 核武器的","examples":["They rejected a demand for the removal of all nuclear weapons. 他們拒絕了清除所有核武器的要求。"]}]}]},"offensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無禮的，冒犯的；令人不快（討厭）的；攻擊的，進攻性的； <美>（體育比賽中）進攻的，攻勢的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（軍事）進攻，攻勢；  （引人注意的）系列行動，攻勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>offensive</b> upsets or embarrasses people because it is rude or insulting. 冒犯性的","examples":["Some friends of his found the play horribly offensive. 他的一些朋友覺得那部戲讓人很不舒服。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A military <b>offensive</b> is a carefully planned attack made by a large group of soldiers. (軍事) 進攻","examples":["Its latest military offensive against rebel forces is aimed at re-opening important trade routes. 其最近對叛軍的軍事進攻旨在重新開闢重要的貿易路線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you conduct an <b>offensive</b>, you take strong action to show how angry you are about something or how much you disapprove of something. 強硬行動","examples":["Republicans acknowledged that they had little choice but to mount an all-out offensive on the Democratic nominee. 共和黨人承認他們別無選擇，只有對民主黨提名人全力發起一場強硬行動。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>go on the offensive</b>, <b>go over to the offensive</b>, or <b>take the offensive</b>, you begin to take strong action against people who have been attacking you. 採取攻勢","examples":["The West African forces went on the offensive in response to attacks on them. 西非武裝力量發起進攻以回應襲擊。"]}]}]},"partial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"部分的，不完全的；偏袒的，不公平的；偏愛的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（樂）分音，泛音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>partial</b> to refer to something that is not complete or whole. 部分的","examples":["He managed to reach a partial agreement with both republics. 他設法跟兩個共和國達成了部分共識。","...a partial ban on the use of cars in the city. …城市內部分地區禁止使用轎車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>partial to</b> something, you like it. 偏愛的","examples":["He's partial to sporty women with blue eyes. 他對藍眼睛的、運動型的女人是偏愛的。","Mollie confesses she is rather partial to pink. 莫莉承認她對粉紅色是相當偏愛的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>partial</b> supports a particular person or thing, for example, in a competition or dispute, instead of being completely fair. 偏袒的","examples":["I might be accused of being partial. 我可能會被人指責是偏袒的。"]}]}]},"passive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"消極的，被動的；被動語態的；（抵抗）非暴力的；（電路，裝置）無源的；（金屬）經表面鈍化處理的，鈍化的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動詞的）被動語態形式；被動語態（the passive）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>passive</b>, you mean that they do not take action but instead let things happen to them. 被動的","examples":["His passive attitude made things easier for me. 他的被動態度使我辦起事來容易多了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>passive</b> activity involves watching, looking at, or listening to things rather than doing things. 消極的","examples":["They want less passive ways of filling their time. 他們需要不那麼消極的方式來打發時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Passive</b> resistance involves showing opposition to the people in power in your country by not cooperating with them and protesting in nonviolent ways. 非暴力的","examples":["They made it clear that they would only exercise passive resistance in the event of a military takeover. 他們宣告假若發生軍事接管，他們只採取非暴力抵抗行動。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被動地","examples":["He sat there passively, content to wait for his father to make the opening move. 他被動地坐在那裡，心滿意足地等著他父親走第一步棋。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In grammar, <b>the passive</b> or <b>the passive voice</b> is formed using \"be\" and the past participle of a verb. The subject of a passive clause does not perform the action expressed by the verb but is affected by it. For example, in \"He's been murdered,\" the verb is in the passive. Compare . 被動語態","examples":[]}]}]},"organic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有機的，綠色的；有機物的，生物的；構成有機整體的，不可分割的；（發生、發展過程）自然的，演進的；器官的，器質性的；仿自然形態的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有機物質；有機食品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Organic</b> methods of farming and gardening do not use pesticides, chemical fertilizers, growth hormones, or antibiotics, so that the food produced does not contain toxic chemicals. 有機種植的","examples":["Organic farming is expanding everywhere. 有機農業在各處發展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Organic</b> substances are produced by or found in living things. 有機的","examples":["Incorporating organic material into chalky soils will reduce the alkalinity. 將有機物質摻入白堊質土壤中將會降低鹼性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Organic</b> change or development happens gradually and naturally rather than suddenly. 自然演進的","examples":["...to manage the company and supervise its organic growth. …管理公司並指導其逐步發展。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有機地","examples":["...organically grown vegetables. …有機種植的蔬菜。"]}]}]},"persuasive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有說服力的，能使人信服的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>persuasive</b> is likely to persuade a person to believe or do a particular thing. 有說服力的","examples":["What do you think were some of the more persuasive arguments on the other side? 你覺得對方哪些論點更有說服力？","I can be very persuasive when I want to be. 當我想要的時候，我會很有說服力的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有說服力地","examples":["...a trained lawyer who can present arguments persuasively. …一位訓練有素、能令人信服地陳述辯詞的律師。"]}]}]},"outstanding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傑出的，優秀的；顯著的，突出的；未解決的，未完成的；（款項）未支付的，未結清的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>outstanding</b>, you think that they are very remarkable and impressive. 傑出的","examples":["Derartu is an outstanding athlete and deserved to win. 德拉圖是位傑出的運動員，他理應獲勝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Money that is <b>outstanding</b> has not yet been paid and is still owed to someone. 尚未償還的","examples":["The total debt outstanding is $70 billion. 尚未償還的總債務額是700億美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Outstanding</b> issues or problems have not yet been resolved. 尚未解決的","examples":["We still have some outstanding issues to resolve before we'll have a treaty that is ready to sign. 我們在簽署這份條約之前還有一些懸而未決的問題要解決。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Outstanding</b> means very important or obvious. 突出的","examples":["The company is an outstanding example of a small business that grew into a big one. 該公司是小企業成長為大公司的突出例子。"]}]}]},"peculiar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇怪的，不尋常的；特別的，獨特的；不舒服的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>特殊教區（或教堂）；特權，特有財產"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>peculiar</b>, you think that they are strange or unusual, sometimes in an unpleasant way. 不尋常的; 古怪的","examples":["Mr. Kennet has a rather peculiar sense of humour. 肯尼特先生有一種相當不尋常的幽默感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>peculiar</b> <b>to</b> a particular thing, person, or situation, it belongs or relates only to that thing, person, or situation. 特有的; 獨特的","examples":["Punks, soldiers, hippies, and Sumo wrestlers all have distinct hair styles, peculiar to their group. 朋克搖滾歌手、士兵、嬉皮士和相撲手都留著他們那個群體特有的獨特髮型。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不尋常地; 奇怪地","examples":["His face had become peculiarly expressionless. 他的臉變得異乎尋常地毫無表情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"特有地; 獨特地","examples":["...a peculiarly American conservatism. …一種美國特有的保守主義。"]}]}]},"pessimistic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲觀的，悲觀主義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>pessimistic</b> thinks that bad things are going to happen. 悲觀的","examples":["Not everyone is so pessimistic about the future. 並非每個人都對未來如此悲觀。","Hardy has often been criticized for an excessively pessimistic view of life. 哈迪因其過分悲觀的人生觀而經常受到批評。"]}]}]},"philosophical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"哲學的；達觀的，處亂不驚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Philosophical</b> means concerned with or relating to philosophy. 哲學的","examples":["He was more accustomed to cocktail party chatter than to political or philosophical discussions. 比起政治或者哲學討論，他更習慣於雞尾酒會上的閒談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>philosophical</b> does not get upset when disappointing or disturbing things happen. 泰然自若的","examples":["Lewis has grown philosophical about life. 劉易斯對生活已經變得豁達了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"哲學地","examples":["Wilbur says he's not a coward, but that he's philosophically opposed to war. 威爾伯說他不是個懦夫，但他在哲學觀念上反對戰爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"泰然自若地","examples":["She says philosophically: \"It could have been far worse.\" 她泰然自若地說，“情況本來可能會糟得多。”"]}]}]},"plentiful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"豐富的，眾多的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Things that are <b>plentiful</b> exist in such large amounts or numbers that there is enough for people's wants or needs. 富足的","examples":["Fish are plentiful in the lake. 這個湖裡魚很多。"]}]}]},"permanent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"永久的，永恆的；（尤指問題或困難）不斷出現的，一直存在的；（員工）終生的，長期的；（家庭住址）固定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>燙髮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>permanent</b> lasts forever. 永久的","examples":["Heavy drinking can cause permanent damage to the brain. 飲酒過量可能造成永久性腦損傷。","...a permanent solution to the problem. …一個解決該問題的永久性辦法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>permanent</b> to describe situations or states that keep occurring or that seem to exist all the time; used especially to describe problems or difficulties. (問題或困難) 不斷髮生的; 一直存在的","examples":["...a permanent state of tension. …長期的緊張狀態。","They feel under permanent threat. 他們感覺處在持續不斷的威脅之下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>permanent</b> employee is one who is employed for an unlimited length of time. 終身的","examples":["At the end of the probationary period you will become a permanent employee. 試用期結束後，你將成為終身僱員。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>permanent</b> home or your <b>permanent</b> address is the one at which you spend most of your time or the one that you return to after having stayed in other places. 固定的 (住所或地址)","examples":["They had no permanent address. 他們沒有固定的地址。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"永久地","examples":["His confidence had been permanently affected by the ordeal. 他的信心已永久地被這次磨難影響了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(問題或困難) 不斷發生地; 一直存在地","examples":["...the heavy, permanently locked gate. …這扇厚重的、長年鎖著的大門。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"終身地","examples":["...permanently employed lifeguards. …終身僱用的救生員。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>permanent</b> is a treatment in which a hairstylist curls your hair and treats it with a chemical so that it stays curly for several months. 燙髮","examples":["Her hair had had a permanent, but had grown out. 她的頭髮曾經燙捲過，但又長出新的了。"]}]}]},"preferable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"更好的，更合適的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing is <b>preferable</b> <b>to</b> another, you mean that it is more desirable or suitable. 更合心意的; 更適合的","examples":["A big earthquake a long way off is preferable to a smaller one nearby. 遠處的大地震要比近處的小地震好。","Prevention of a problem is always preferable to trying to cure it. 防止出現問題總是比試圖解決問題更可取。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"更可取地","examples":["Do something creative or take exercise, preferably in the fresh air. 做一些有創意的事或者進行體育鍛煉，在新鮮的空氣中更好。"]}]}]},"poisonous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有毒的；會產生毒素的；惡毒的，令人很不愉快的；有許多危害的，惡性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>poisonous</b> will kill you or make you ill if you swallow or absorb it. (某物) 有毒的","examples":["All parts of the yew tree are poisonous, including the berries. 紫杉樹全身都有毒，包括其果實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An animal that is <b>poisonous</b> produces a poison that will kill you or make you ill if the animal bites you. (動物) 產生毒的","examples":["There are hundreds of poisonous spiders and snakes. 有數百種毒蜘蛛和毒蛇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>poisonous</b>, you mean that it is extremely unpleasant and likely to spoil or destroy a good relationship or situation. 令人厭惡的; 惡毒的","examples":["...poisonous comments. …惡毒的評論。","...lying awake half the night tormented by poisonous suspicions. …半個晚上躺著都不能入眠，被惡毒的猜疑所煎熬。"]}]}]},"pregnant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"懷孕的，妊娠的；意味深長的，意義重大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a woman or female animal is <b>pregnant</b>, she has a baby or babies developing in her body. 懷孕的","examples":["Lena got pregnant and married. 莉娜懷了孕並結了婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pregnant</b> silence or moment has a special meaning that is not obvious but that people are aware of. 耐人尋味的","examples":["There was a long, pregnant silence, which Mrs. Madrigal punctuated by reaching for the cheque. 馬德里加爾太太伸手去拿那支票，打破了那一陣長時間的、耐人尋味的沉默。"]}]}]},"portable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"行動式的，輕便的；可移植的，可在不同計算機上使用的；（變更工作或情景時）可轉移的，可隨帶的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"手提式電器；<美>活動教室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>portable</b> machine or device is designed to be easily carried or moved. 行動式的","examples":["There was a little portable television switched on behind the bar. 吧檯後有一臺行動式小電視機開著。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>portable</b> is something such as a television, radio, or computer that can be easily carried or moved. 行動式裝置","examples":["We bought a portable for the bedroom. 我們臥室裡買了臺便攜裝置。"]}]}]},"precise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精確的，準確的；恰好的，確切的；（人）嚴格的，一絲不苟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>precise</b> to emphasize that you are referring to an exact thing, rather than something vague. 確切的","examples":["I can remember the precise moment when my daughter came to see me and her new baby brother in the hospital. 我還記得我女兒來醫院看望我和她剛出生的弟弟的那確切的一刻。","The precise location of the wreck was discovered in 1988. 船舶失事的確切地點是在1988年發現的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>precise</b> is exact and accurate in all its details. 精確的","examples":["They speak very precise English. 他們說非常標準的英語。"]}]}]},"physical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"身體的，肉體的；物質的，有形的；外形的，外在的；物理的，物理學的；根據自然規律的，符合自然法則的；粗暴的，粗野的；性慾的，肉慾的；（人）喜歡動手動腳的；肢體活動的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"體格檢查；（股票）（與期貨相對的）現貨股票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Physical</b> qualities, actions, or things are connected with a person's body, rather than with their mind. 肉體的; 身體的","examples":["...the physical and mental problems caused by the illness. …這種疾病引起的生理和心理問題。","Physical activity promotes good health. 身體運動促進健康。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Physical</b> things are real things that can be touched and seen, rather than ideas or spoken words. 實物的; 有形的","examples":["Physical and ideological barriers had come down in Eastern Europe. 物質和意識形態上的障礙在東歐都已減少。","...physical evidence to support the story. …支援這種說法的實物證據。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Physical</b> means relating to the structure, size, or shape of something that can be touched and seen. 物理的","examples":["...the physical characteristics of the terrain. …這一地形的物理特點。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Physical</b> means connected with physics or the laws of physics. 物理學的","examples":["...the physical laws of combustion and thermodynamics. …燃燒和熱力學的物理定律。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Someone who is <b>physical</b> touches people a lot, either in an affectionate way or in a rough way. (以溫柔或粗魯的方式) 有大量身體接觸的","examples":["We decided that in the game we would be physical and aggressive. 我們決定，在比賽中我們將積極拼搶，大膽進攻。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Physical</b> is used in expressions such as <b>physical love</b> and <b>physical relationships</b> to refer to sexual relationships between people. 性的","examples":["It had been years since they had shared any meaningful form of physical relationship. 他們已經多年沒有真正意義上的性關係了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"身體上地","examples":["You may be physically and mentally exhausted after a long flight. 長途飛行後你可能身心都很疲憊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"有形地","examples":["...physically cut off from every other country. …地理上與所有其他國家分割開來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>physical</b> is a medical examination by your doctor to make sure that there is nothing wrong with your health, or a medical examination to make sure you are fit enough to do a particular job. 體格檢查","examples":["Bob failed his physical. 鮑勃沒有透過體格檢查。"]}]}]},"profitable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"盈利的，有利可圖的；有益的，有用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>profitable</b> organization or practice makes a profit. 可盈利的","examples":["Drug manufacturing is the most profitable business in the U.S. 藥品生產是美國最賺錢的行業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>profitable</b> results in some benefit for you. 能帶來利益的","examples":["...close collaboration with industry which leads to a profitable exchange of personnel and ideas. …能帶來人員和理念上有益交流的與企業的密切合作。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可盈利地","examples":["The 28 French stores are trading profitably. 那28家法國商店在盈利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"能帶來利益地","examples":["In fact he could scarcely have spent his time more profitably. 事實上他幾乎不可能把他的時間花得更有益了。"]}]}]},"productive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多產的，豐饒的；有效益的，富有成效的；生產（成品、莊稼或財富）的，生產性的；產生……的，引起……的（productive of）；有構詞能力的；（咳嗽）生痰的，分泌黏液的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>productive</b> produces or does a lot for the amount of resources used. 生產力高的","examples":["Training makes workers highly productive. 培訓使工人們生產力很高。","More productive farmers have been able to provide cheaper food. 生產力更高的農民們已能提供更便宜的食品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a relationship between people is <b>productive</b>, you mean that a lot of good or useful things happen as a result of it. 富有成效的","examples":["He was hopeful that the next round of talks would also be productive. 他對下一輪會談也會富有成效充滿了希望。"]}]}]},"primitive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原始的，遠古的；（器物等）粗糙的，簡陋的；（人、動物或植物發展）早期的；（行為，思想，情感）本能的，自然的；（藝術風格）樸實無華的；原來的，原有的；（語言學）根詞的，非派生的；（數）（代數或幾何表示式）本原的；（生）原生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>原始人，未開化的土人；原始派藝術家（或其作品）；文藝復興前的藝術家（或作品），模仿文藝復興前藝術風格的現代畫家；早期風格物品；詞根，原（詞）素；（數）基本式，初基；（計算機）圖元，原語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Primitive</b> means belonging to a society in which people live in a very simple way, usually without industries or a writing system. 原始的 (社會)","examples":["...studies of primitive societies. …對原始社會的研究。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Primitive</b> means belonging to a very early period in the development of an animal or plant. 原始的 (動物、植物)","examples":["...primitive whales. …原始鯨。","Primitive humans needed to be able to react like this to escape from dangerous animals. 原始人們需要能夠像這樣反應以逃脫危險的動物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>primitive</b>, you mean that it is very simple in style or very old-fashioned. 簡陋的; 舊式的","examples":["The conditions are primitive by any standards. 這些條件以任何標準衡量都是簡陋的。"]}]}]},"promising":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有希望的，有前途的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"承諾，答應；使很可能，預示（promise 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>promising</b> seems likely to be very good or successful. 有望成功的; 前景很好的","examples":["A school has honoured one of its brightest and most promising former students. 一所學校給其培養過的最聰明、最有前途的學生中的一位頒了獎。"]}]}]},"prominent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重要的，著名的；顯眼的，突出的；突起的，高聳的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"舟蛾（=prominent moth）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>prominent</b> is important and well-known. 重要的; 著名的","examples":["...the children of very prominent or successful parents. …非常知名或成功的人士們的孩子們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>prominent</b> is very noticeable or is an important part of something else. 突出的","examples":["Here the window plays a prominent part in the design. 這裡，窗戶在設計中有著突出的作用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"突出地","examples":["Trade will figure prominently in the second day of talks in Washington. 貿易在華盛頓會談的第二天將成為突出的議題。"]}]}]},"prosperous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"繁榮的，富足的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prosperous</b> people, places, and economies are rich and successful. 富裕的; 成功的","examples":["...the youngest son of a relatively prosperous family. …一個相對富裕的家庭裡的小兒子。"]}]}]},"reluctant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勉強的，不情願的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>reluctant</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are unwilling to do it and hesitate before doing it, or do it slowly and without enthusiasm. 不願意的; 勉強的","examples":["Mr. Spero was reluctant to ask for help. 斯珀洛先生不願意請求幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不願意地; 勉強地","examples":["We have reluctantly agreed to let him go. 我們已勉強同意讓他走了。"]}]}]},"psychological":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"心理的，精神的；心理學的，關於心理學的；由焦慮（或悲傷）引起的，存在於心理上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Psychological</b> means concerned with a person's mind and thoughts. 心理的","examples":["John received constant physical and psychological abuse from his father. 約翰受到來自他父親的不斷的身心摧殘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Psychological</b> means relating to psychology. 心理學的","examples":["...psychological testing. …心理學測試。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"心理上地","examples":["It was very important psychologically for us to succeed. 取得成功，在心理上對我們非常重要。"]}]}]},"remarkable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"引人注目的，非凡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>remarkable</b> is unusual or special in a way that makes people notice them and be surprised or impressed. 不同尋常的; 非凡卓越的; 引人注目的","examples":["He was a remarkable man. 他是個非凡卓越的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不同尋常地; 非凡卓越地; 引人注目地","examples":["Herbal remedies are remarkably successful in treating eczema. 草藥療法醫治溼疹非常成功。"]}]}]},"respectful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"表示敬意的，尊敬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>respectful</b>, you show respect for someone. 恭敬的","examples":["The children in our family are always respectful to their elders. 我們家的孩子們總是很尊敬他們的長輩。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"恭敬地","examples":["\"You are an artist,\" she said respectfully. “您是一位藝術家，”她畢恭畢敬地說。"]}]}]},"realistic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"務實的，實事求是的；實際的，現實可行的；寫實的，逼真的；實在論的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>realistic</b> about a situation, you recognize and accept its true nature and try to deal with it in a practical way. 現實的; 務實的","examples":["Police have to be realistic about violent crime. 警察對暴力犯罪不得不採取務實的態度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something such as a goal or target that is <b>realistic</b> is one that you can sensibly expect to achieve. 現實可行的","examples":["A more realistic figure is 11 million. 一個更現實可行的數字是1100萬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that a painting, story, or movie is <b>realistic</b> when the people and things in it are like people and things in real life. 逼真的","examples":["...extraordinarily realistic paintings of Indians. …關於印第安人的極其逼真的繪畫。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"現實地; 務實地","examples":["As an adult, you can assess the situation realistically. 作為成年人，你可以現實地估量這個局勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"逼真地","examples":["The film starts off realistically and then develops into a ridiculous fantasy. 電影開始的時候比較逼真，然後卻發展成為荒謬的幻想。"]}]}]},"shameful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"丟臉的，可恥的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person's action or attitude as <b>shameful</b>, you think that it is so bad that the person ought to be ashamed. 可恥的","examples":["...the most shameful episode in U.S. naval history. …美國海軍史上最恥辱的一段歷史。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可恥地","examples":["At times they have been shamefully neglected. 有時他們被可恥地忽略了。"]}]}]},"respectable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"值得尊敬的，體面的；相當好的，不錯的；有一定價值的，相當重要的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可敬的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>respectable</b> is approved of by society and considered to be morally correct. 體面的","examples":["He came from a perfectly respectable middle-class family. 他來自一個非常體面的中產階級家庭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>respectable</b> when you mean that it is good enough or acceptable. 可接受的","examples":["...investments that offer respectable and highly attractive rates of return. …提供不錯的、極具吸引力的回報率的投資。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"體面","examples":["If she divorced Tony, she would lose the respectability she had as Mrs. Tony Tatterton. 如果她和託尼離婚，她將會失去作為託尼•塔特頓太太的體面。"]}]}]},"shortsighted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"目光短淺的，無遠見的；（英國英語）近視的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>shortsighted</b> about something, or if their ideas are <b>shortsighted</b>, they do not make proper or careful judgments about the future. 目光短淺的","examples":["Environmentalists fear that this is a shortsighted approach to the problem of global warming. 環境保護主義者們擔心這會是解決全球變暖問題的一個目光短淺的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>shortsighted</b>, you cannot see things properly when they are far away, because there is something wrong with your eyes. 近視的","examples":["As you get older, you may become long-sighted or shortsighted. 隨著年齡的增長，你可能變得遠視或近視。"]}]}]},"rural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"農村的，鄉村的；有鄉村特色的，有鄉土氣息的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rural</b> places are far away from large towns or cities. 鄉村的","examples":["These plants have a tendency to grow in the more rural areas. 這些植物傾向於生長在更偏遠的鄉村地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rural</b> means having features which are typical of areas that are far away from large towns or cities. 有鄉村特色的","examples":["...the old rural way of life. …古老的鄉村生活方式。"]}]}]},"sorrowful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲傷的，悲痛的，悲哀的；使人悲傷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sorrowful</b> means very sad. 悲傷的","examples":["His father's face looked suddenly soft and sorrowful. 他父親的面容忽然變得溫柔而悲傷。"]}]}]},"spicy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"加有香料的，辛辣的；刺激的，粗俗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spicy</b> food is strongly flavoured with spices. 香料味重的","examples":["Thai food is hot and spicy. 泰國食品很辛辣。"]}]}]},"solar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"太陽的，和太陽有關的；（與）太陽能（有關）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（中世紀房屋的）屋頂室，頂層房間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Solar</b> is used to describe things relating to the sun. 太陽的","examples":["A total solar eclipse is due to take place some time tomorrow. 預計日全食會出現在明天的某個時候。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Solar</b> power is obtained from the sun's light and heat. 太陽產生的","examples":["...the financial savings from solar energy. …使用太陽能帶來的資金節約。"]}]}]},"stingy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"吝嗇的，小氣的；小的，少的；有刺的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>stingy</b>, you are criticizing them for being unwilling to spend money. 吝嗇的","examples":["The West is stingy with aid. 西方在援助上很吝嗇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"stinging or capable of stinging 有刺的; 刺人的","examples":[]}]}]},"severe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十分嚴重的，極為惡劣的；艱鉅的，嚴峻的；（懲罰、批評）嚴厲的，重的；嚴厲的，苛刻的；不加裝飾的，樸素的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>severe</b> to indicate that something bad or undesirable is great or intense. 嚴重的","examples":["...a business with severe cash flow problems. …一個有嚴重現金流轉問題的企業。","Shortages of professional staff are very severe in some places. 專業人員的短缺在一些地方十分嚴重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Severe</b> punishments or criticisms are very strong or harsh. (懲罰、批評) 嚴厲的","examples":["This was a dreadful crime and a severe sentence is necessary. 這是一種駭人聽聞的罪行，重判是必要的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴重地","examples":["The UN wants to send food aid to 10 countries in Africa severely affected by the drought. 聯合國想給予10個受旱災嚴重影響的非洲國家食品援助。","An aircraft overshot the runway and was severely damaged. 一架飛機衝出了跑道後嚴重受損。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嚴厲地","examples":["...a campaign to try to change the law to punish dangerous drivers more severely. …一場試圖修改法律以更加嚴厲地懲罰危險駕車者的運動。"]}]}]},"spiritual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精神的，心靈的；宗教的；（人）高尚的，不為物慾所動的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（原為美國黑人所唱的）聖歌，靈歌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spiritual</b> means relating to people's thoughts and beliefs, rather than to their bodies and physical surroundings. 精神的","examples":["She lived entirely by spiritual values, in a world of poetry and imagination. 她完全靠著精神價值生活在一個詩歌和想像的世界裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spiritual</b> means relating to people's religious beliefs. 宗教的","examples":["He is the spiritual leader of the world's Catholics. 他是世界天主教的宗教領袖。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精神地","examples":["Our whole programme is spiritually oriented but not religious. 我們的整個節目以精神而不是宗教為導向。"]}]}]},"splendid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極佳的，非常好的；壯麗的，燦爛的，輝煌的；（一段時光）令人愉快的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"（表示讚許或滿意）好極了，痛快"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>splendid</b>, you mean that it is very good. 極好的","examples":["The book includes a wealth of splendid photographs. 這本書有大量非常好的照片。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極好地","examples":["I have heard him tell people that we get along splendidly. 我聽見他跟人說我們相處得非常好。"]}]}]},"systematic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有系統的，有條理的，仔細周到的；一貫的，慣常的；分類的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is done in a <b>systematic</b> way is done according to a fixed plan, in a thorough and efficient way. 有計劃的","examples":["They went about their business in a systematic way. 他們按部就班地做生意。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有計劃地","examples":["The army has systematically violated human rights. 軍隊已有計劃地侵犯了人權。"]}]}]},"suspicious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感覺可疑的，懷疑的；不信任的，持懷疑態度的；令人懷疑的，引起懷疑的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>suspicious</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you do not trust them, and are careful when dealing with them. 懷疑的","examples":["He was rightly suspicious of meeting me until I reassured him I was not writing about him. 他對於見我充滿疑慮，直到我向他再次保證我不是在寫有關他的東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"懷疑地","examples":["\"What is it you want me to do?\" Adams asked suspiciously. “你要我去幹的是什麼？”亞當斯懷疑地問道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>suspicious</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you believe that they are probably involved in a crime or some dishonest activity. 起疑心的","examples":["Two officers on patrol became suspicious of two men in a car. 兩位巡警對一輛小汽車內的兩名男子起了疑心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>suspicious</b>, you mean that there is some aspect of them which makes you think that they are involved in a crime or a dishonest activity. 可疑的","examples":["He reported that two suspicious-looking characters had approached Callendar. 他報告說兩名看似可疑的人曾靠近過卡蘭德。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可疑地","examples":["They'll question them as to whether anyone was seen acting suspiciously in the area over the last few days. 他們將詢問這些人過去幾天是否在該地區發現行跡可疑的人。"]}]}]},"sympathetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同情的，有同情心的；贊同的，支援的；（電影或小說中的人物）討人喜歡的，可愛的；合意的，合適的；（結構）和諧的；交感神經的，自主神經系統的；（與）交感性（有關）的，（產生）交感性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"交感神經"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>sympathetic</b> to someone who is in a bad situation, you are kind to them and show that you understand their feelings. 同情的","examples":["She was very sympathetic to the problems of adult students. 她對成年學生的問題很同情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>sympathetic</b> <b>to</b> a proposal or action, you approve of it and are willing to support it. 贊同的","examples":["Many of these early visitors were sympathetic to the Chinese socialist experiment. 這些早期訪問者中的很多人都贊同中國的社會主義實驗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"同情地","examples":["She nodded sympathetically. 她同情地點了點頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"贊同地","examples":["After a year we will sympathetically consider an application for reinstatement. 一年以後我們會考慮贊同復職申請。"]}]}]},"technological":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"技術的，科技的，工藝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Technological</b> means relating to or associated with technology. 與技術有關的","examples":["...an era of very rapid technological change. …一個技術飛速變革的時代。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"技術上地","examples":["...technologically advanced aircraft. …技術先進的飛機。"]}]}]},"timid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"羞怯的，膽小的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Timid</b> people are shy, nervous, and lack courage or confidence in themselves. 羞怯的","examples":["A timid child, Isabella had learned obedience at an early age. 伊莎貝拉是一個羞怯的孩子，很小的時候就已經學會了順從。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"羞怯","examples":["She doesn't ridicule my timidity. 她不會嘲笑我的羞怯。"]}]}]},"thoughtful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"體貼入微的，考慮周到的；沉思的，思考的；縝密思考過的，深思熟慮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>thoughtful</b>, you are quiet and serious because you are thinking about something. 沉思的","examples":["Nancy, who had been thoughtful for some time, suddenly spoke. 南希沉思半晌後，突然開口說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>thoughtful</b>, you approve of them because they remember what other people want, need, or feel, and try not to upset them. 考慮周到的","examples":["...a thoughtful and caring man. …一個考慮周到、關心體貼的男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as a book, film, or speech as <b>thoughtful</b>, you mean that it is serious and well thought out. (書籍、電影或講話等) 有思想深度的","examples":["...a thoughtful and scholarly book. …一本既有思想深度又有學術價值的書。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沉思地","examples":["Daniel nodded thoughtfully. 丹尼爾若有所思地點點頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"考慮周到地","examples":["...the bottle of wine he had thoughtfully purchased for the celebrations. …他為慶祝活動特地購買的這瓶葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有思想深度地","examples":["...these thoughtfully designed machines. …這些經縝密思考而設計的機器。"]}]}]},"tiresome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"煩人的，令人厭煩的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>tiresome</b>, you mean that you find them irritating or boring. 討厭的; 無聊的","examples":["...the tiresome old lady next door. …隔壁的那個討厭的老婦人。"]}]}]},"thorough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"徹底的，全面的；徹頭徹尾的，十足的；仔細的，縝密的；仔細周到，工作縝密"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>thorough</b> action or activity is one that is done very carefully and in a detailed way so that nothing is forgotten. 徹底的","examples":["We are making a thorough investigation. 我們正在進行徹底的調查。","This very thorough survey goes back to 1784. 這項非常徹底的調查可追溯到1784年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>thorough</b> is always very careful in their work, so that nothing is forgotten. 細心的","examples":["Martin would be a good judge, I thought. He was calm and thorough. 我想馬丁會是個好法官。他既沉著又細心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Thorough</b> is used to emphasize the large degree or extent of something. (用於強調程度或範圍) 完全的","examples":["To me, this seemed like a thorough waste of time. 在我看來，這好像完全是浪費時間。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"徹底地","examples":["Food that is being offered hot must be reheated thoroughly. 熱熟食拿到手後必須重新熱透。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"完全地","examples":["I thoroughly enjoy your programme. 我非常喜歡你們的節目。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"細心","examples":["His thoroughness and attention to detail is legendary. 他的細心和對細節的關注是很有名的。"]}]}]},"tolerable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"尚好的，還可以的；可接受的，可忍受的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>tolerable</b>, you mean that you can bear it, even though it is unpleasant or painful. 可忍受的","examples":["Our living conditions are tolerable, but I can't wait to leave. 我們的居住條件還是可忍受的，但是我迫不及待地想離開。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可忍受地","examples":["Their captors treated them tolerably well. 俘獲他們的人待他們勉強還過得去。"]}]}]},"tribal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"部落的，部族的；；<貶>有組成集團傾向的，集團意識強的； 部落的，部族的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指印度次大陸的）部落成員（tribals）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tribal</b> is used to describe things relating to or belonging to tribes and the way that they are organized. 部落的","examples":["...tribal warfare. …部落戰爭。","...the Navajo Tribal Council. …納瓦霍人的部落會。"]}]}]},"tolerant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寬容的，容忍的；（植物、動物、機器）能耐……的，有耐受性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>tolerant</b>, you approve of the fact that they allow other people to say and do as they like and that they are willing to accept different races, religions, and lifestyles. 寬容的","examples":["They need to be tolerant of different points of view. 他們需要容忍不同的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a plant, animal, or machine is <b>tolerant of</b> particular conditions or types of treatment, it is able to bear them without being damaged or hurt. 能耐…的","examples":["...plants which are more tolerant of dry conditions. …更耐乾旱的植物。"]}]}]},"troublesome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"引起麻煩的，（尤指）令人討厭的；（形勢、問題等）麻煩的，困難的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>troublesome</b> to describe something or someone that causes annoying problems or difficulties. 令人煩惱的","examples":["He needed surgery to cure a troublesome back injury. 他需要動手術來醫治煩人的背部傷痛。"]}]}]},"tragic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲慘的，悲痛的，可悲的；悲劇的；糟透了的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<澳新，非正式>無趣的人，不善社交的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tragic</b> event or situation is extremely sad, usually because it involves death or suffering. 悲慘的; 不幸的","examples":["It was just a tragic accident. 這只是一場悲慘的事故。","...the tragic loss of so many lives. …如此多人的不幸喪生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tragic</b> is used to refer to tragedy as a type of literature. 悲劇的","examples":["...Shakespeare's tragic hero, Hamlet. …莎士比亞的悲劇主人公哈姆雷特。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悲慘地; 不幸地","examples":["Tragically, she never saw the completed building because she died before it was finished. 不幸的是，她未能見到完工的大樓，因為她在大樓竣工前就去世了。"]}]}]},"tremendous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大的，極大的；極好的，精彩的；令人望而生畏的，可怕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>tremendous</b> to emphasize how strong a feeling or quality is, or how large an amount is. 非常的; 巨大的","examples":["I felt a tremendous pressure on my chest. 我感到胸口有股巨大的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone or something as <b>tremendous</b> when you think they are very good or very impressive. 極好的; 精彩的","examples":["I thought it was absolutely tremendous. 我覺得它絕對精彩。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非常地; 極大地","examples":["I thought they played tremendously well, didn't you? 我認為他們表演得非常好，你不覺得嗎？"]}]}]},"urban":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"城市的，城鎮的；黑人音樂的；住在都市的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Urban</b> means belonging to, or relating to, a city or town. 城市的","examples":["For a small state it has a large urban population. 作為一個小州，其城市人口算是很多了。","Most urban areas are close to a park. 大多數城區都靠近公園。"]}]}]},"urgent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"緊急的，急迫的；急切的，催促的；<正式>（尤指某人的行動）執著的，堅定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>urgent</b>, it needs to be dealt with as soon as possible. 緊急的; 迫切的","examples":["There is an urgent need for food and water. 有著對食品和水的迫切需要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you speak in an <b>urgent</b> way, you show that you are anxious for people to notice something or to do something. 急切的","examples":["His voice was low and urgent. 他的聲音低沉而急切。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"緊急性; 迫切性","examples":["The urgency of finding a cure attracted some of the best minds in medical science. 因迫切需要找到一種治療方法，醫學界的一些最優秀的人才前仆後繼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"急切","examples":["She was surprised at the urgency in his voice. 她對他聲音的急切感到吃驚。"]}]}]},"youthful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"年輕人的，青春的，天真的；年輕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>youthful</b> behaves as if they are young or younger than they really are. 顯得年輕的","examples":["I'm a very youthful 50. 我是個顯得很年輕的50歲的人。","...youthful enthusiasm and high spirits. …青春的激情和昂揚的情緒。"]}]}]},"tough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（物質，物體）堅韌的，堅固的；（政策或行動）強硬的，嚴厲的；吃苦耐勞的，堅韌不拔的；頑固的，固執的；困難的，棘手的；艱難的，困苦的，難熬的；（食物）老的，不易切開的，嚼不動的；（人）粗暴的，粗魯的；（地區）充滿暴力與犯罪的；不幸的，倒黴的，活該（表示不同情）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"惡棍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"堅持，忍受，忍耐"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"堅強地，堅定地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tough</b> person is strong and determined, and can tolerate difficulty or suffering. 堅強的","examples":["He built up a reputation as a tough businessman. 他樹立起了一個堅強生意人的名聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>tough</b>, you mean that they are rough and violent. 粗暴的","examples":["He had shot three people dead earning himself a reputation as a tough guy. 他已開槍打死了3個人，為自己贏得了一個硬漢的名聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tough</b> place or area is considered to have a lot of crime and violence. 治安很差的","examples":["She doesn't seem cut out for this tough neighbourhood. 她似乎不適合這個治安很差的社群。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>tough</b> way of life or period of time is difficult or full of suffering. 艱苦的","examples":["She had a pretty tough childhood. 她度過了一個非常艱苦的童年。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>tough</b> task or problem is difficult to do or solve. 困難的","examples":["It was a very tough decision but we feel we made the right one. 這是一個非常困難的決定，但我們覺得自己做出了正確的選擇。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Tough</b> policies or actions are strict and firm. (政策或行動) 強硬的","examples":["He is known for taking a tough line on security. 他以在安全方面採取強硬路線而聞名。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"A <b>tough</b> substance is strong, and difficult to break, cut, or tear. (物質) 堅硬的","examples":["In industry, diamond can form a tough, non-corrosive coating for tools. 在工業中，鑽石可以製成工具上的一層堅硬且耐腐蝕的塗層。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>Tough</b> meat is difficult to cut and chew. (肉) 嚼不動的","examples":["The steak was tough and the peas were like bullets. 牛排硬得嚼不動，豌豆就像子彈。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堅強","examples":["Ms. Potter has won a reputation for toughness and determination on her way to the top. 波特小姐在奮鬥到頂層的過程中贏得了堅強和果斷的名聲。"]}]}]},"vain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"虛榮的，自負的；徒勞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vain</b> attempt or action is one that fails to achieve what was intended. 徒勞的","examples":["The drafting committee worked through the night in a vain attempt to finish on schedule. 起草委員會徒勞地通宵工作想按期完成工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a hope that something will happen as a <b>vain</b> hope, you mean that there is no chance of it happening. 徒然的","examples":["He married his fourth wife, Susan, in the vain hope that she would improve his health. 他懷著她能改善自己健康的徒然希望娶了第4個妻子蘇珊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>vain</b>, you are critical of their extreme pride in their own beauty, intelligence, or other good qualities. 自負的","examples":["He wasn't so vain as to think he was smarter than his boss. 他還沒有自負到以為他比自己的上司還精明。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"徒勞地","examples":["He hunted vainly through his pockets for a piece of paper. 他徒勞地摸索著自己的口袋想找到一張紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"徒然地","examples":["He then set out for Virginia for what he vainly hoped would be a peaceful retirement. 於是他出發前往弗吉尼亞，徒然地希望這會是一次平靜的引退。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in vain</b>, you do not succeed in achieving what you intend. 徒然","examples":["He stopped at the door, waiting in vain for her to acknowledge his presence. 他停在門口，徒然地等著她跟自己打招呼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as someone's death, suffering, or effort was <b>in vain</b>, you mean that it was useless because it did not achieve anything. 無意義的","examples":["He wants the world to know his son did not die in vain. 他想讓世人知道他兒子的死不是毫無意義的。"]}]}]},"vast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巨大的，廣大的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>廣闊空間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>vast</b> is extremely large. 巨大的","examples":["...Afrikaner farmers who own vast stretches of land. …擁有廣闊土地的南非白人農場主們。"]}]}]},"visual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"視覺的，視力的；栩栩如生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"視覺資料（指說明性的圖片、影片等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Visual</b> means relating to sight, or to things that you can see. 視覺的","examples":["...the graphic visual depiction of violence. …對暴力生動的視覺描繪。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"視覺地","examples":["...visually handicapped boys and girls. …有視力障礙的男孩女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>visual</b> is something such as a picture, diagram, or piece of film that is used to show or explain something. 視覺資料 (展示或解釋用的圖畫、圖表或電影片段等)","examples":["Remember you want your visuals to reinforce your message, not detract from what you are saying. 要記住，你是要用視覺資料來強化你的資訊，而不是削弱你所講述的內容。"]}]}]},"voluntary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自願的，自發的，主動的；（機構或組織）志願的，義務性的；（工作）志願的，無償的，義務的；（工作者）志願的，無償服務的；（人體活動）隨意的，可以控制的；<法律>（讓與）自願的，無償的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（教堂裡管風琴演奏的）儀式終始曲；<史>（尤指作為其他作品的序曲，或自由創作的）即興曲，自由調；（比賽中的）自選表演；自願行動；志願者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Voluntary</b> actions or activities are done because someone chooses to do them and not because they have been forced to do them. 自願的","examples":["Attention is drawn to a special voluntary course in Commercial French. 注意力被吸引到一門特別的商務法語選修課上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Voluntary</b> work is done by people who are not paid for it, but who do it because they want to do it. 義務的","examples":["In her spare time she does voluntary work. 她在業餘時間做義工。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>voluntary</b> organization is controlled and organized by the people who have chosen to work for it, often without being paid, rather than receiving help or money from the government. 志願的","examples":["Some voluntary organizations run workshops for disabled people. 一些志願組織為殘障人士開辦講習班。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自願地","examples":["I would never leave here voluntarily. 我永遠不會自願地離開這裡。"]}]}]},"vital":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"至關重要的，必不可少的；生機勃勃的，充滿活力的；生命的，維持生命所必需的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"身體的重要內臟，維持生命的重要器官（vitals）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>vital</b>, you mean that it is necessary or very important. 至關重要的","examples":["The port is vital to supply relief to millions of drought victims. 這個港口至關重要，給數百萬旱災民提供救濟物資。","It is vital that parents give children clear and consistent messages about drugs. 至關重要的是，父母們給子女提供關於毒品明確一致的觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"至關重要地","examples":["Lesley's career in the church is vitally important to her. 萊斯利的教會生涯對於她而言至關重要。"]}]}]},"very":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於強調形容詞或副詞）很，非常；極其，完全地；<非正式>顯著的，典型的；顯然，確實，真正地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同一的，恰好的，正是的；（加強名詞的語氣）僅僅的，唯獨的，甚至於；（強調極限的地點或時間）最……的，極端的，十足的；最遠端的，末端的；<古>真正的，真實的；最佳的，最合適的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Very</b> is used to give emphasis to an adjective or adverb. 很","examples":["The problem and the answer are very simple. 這個問題及其答案都很簡單。","I'm very sorry. 我很抱歉。","They are getting the hang of it very quickly. 他們會很快地掌握它的竅門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>very</b> to give emphasis to a superlative adjective or adverb. For example, if you say that something is <b>the very best</b>, you are emphasizing that it is the best. 最 (在形容詞或副詞最高階前表示強調)","examples":["They will be helped by the very latest in navigation aids. 他們將得到最新的導航裝置的幫助。","I am feeling in the very best of spirits. 我感覺自己正處於最佳的精神狀態。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Not very</b> is used with an adjective or adverb to say that something is not at all true, or that it is true only to a small degree. 一點兒也不; 不太…","examples":["She's not very impressed with them. 她對他們沒有什麼印象。","\"How well do you know her?\"—\"Not very.\" “你對她有多瞭解？” —“不是很多。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The expression <b>very much so</b> is an emphatic way of answering \"yes\" to something or saying that it is true or correct. 確實如此","examples":["\"Are you enjoying your vacation?\"—\"Very much so.\" “你假期過得愉快嗎？” —“非常愉快。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>cannot very well</b> do something, you mean that it would not be right or possible to do it. 不可能 (做某事)","examples":["I said yes. I can't very well say no under the circumstances. 我答應了。在當時那種情形下我不可能不答應。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>very</b> with certain nouns in order to specify an extreme position or extreme point in time. (置於某些名詞前表示極限) 最","examples":["At the very back of the garden was a wooden shack. 在院子的最後面是一間小木屋。","I turned to the very end of the book, to read the final words. 我翻到書的最後面，讀了最後的那些話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>very</b> with nouns to emphasize that something is exactly the right one or exactly the same one. (置於名詞前表示強調) 最佳的; 最合適的","examples":["Everybody says he is the very man for the case. 人人都說他是這件案子的最佳人選。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>very</b> with nouns to emphasize the importance or seriousness of what you are saying. (置於名詞前表示重要性) 甚至","examples":["At one stage his very life was in danger. 有一個階段甚至連他的生命都處於危險之中。","History is taking place before your very eyes. 歷史甚至就在你的眼前發生著。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Very well</b> is used to say that you agree to do something or you accept someone's answer, even though you might not be completely satisfied with it. (表示勉強同意或接受) 好吧","examples":["\"We need proof, sir.\" Another pause. Then, \"Very well.\" “我們需要證據，先生。” 又頓了一下。然後說道，“好吧。”"]}]}]},"abandon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拋棄，遺棄；（因危險）離開，捨棄；中止，不再有；放棄（信念、信仰或看法）；陷入，沉湎於（某種情感）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"放任，放縱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>abandon</b> a place, thing, or person, you leave the place, thing, or person permanently or for a long time, especially when you should not do so. 拋棄","examples":["He claimed that his parents had abandoned him. 他聲稱他的父母拋棄了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>abandon</b> an activity or piece of work, you stop doing it before it is finished. 中途放棄","examples":["The authorities have abandoned any attempt to distribute food in an orderly fashion. 當局中途放棄了任何有序地分發食品的嘗試。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>abandon</b> an idea or way of thinking, you stop having that idea or thinking in that way. 放棄 (想法或思想方式)","examples":["Logic had prevailed and he had abandoned the idea. 理性佔了上風，他放棄了該想法。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>with</b> <b>abandon</b>, you mean that they behave in a wild, uncontrolled way and do not think or care about how they should behave. 放縱","examples":["He approached life with reckless abandon–I don't think he himself knew what he was going to do next. 他以不計後果的放縱態度對待生活–我想他自己都不知道他接下來要做什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>abandon ship</b>, they get off a ship because it is sinking. (因船舶下沉而) 棄船","examples":["At the captain's order, they abandoned ship. 在船長的命令下，他們棄船離開了。"]}]}]},"accomplish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"完成，實現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>accomplish</b> something, you succeed in doing it. 完成","examples":["If we'd all work together, I think we could accomplish our goal. 如果我們齊心協力，我想我們能實現我們的目標。"]}]}]},"accuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"控告，指控；指責，譴責，歸咎於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>accuse</b> someone <b>of</b> doing something wrong or dishonest, you say or tell them that you believe that they did it. 指責","examples":["My mom was really upset because he was accusing her of having an affair with another man. 我媽媽真的很難過，因為他指責她和另一個男人有曖昧關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are accused</b> <b>of</b> a crime, a witness or someone in authority states or claims that you did it, and you may be formally charged with it and put on trial. 指控","examples":["Her assistant was accused of theft and fraud by the police. 她的助手被警方指控偷竊和詐騙。","He faced a total of seven charges, all accusing him of lying in his testimony. 他面臨共7項控告，都指控他作偽證。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>stands accused</b> <b>of</b> something, they have been accused of it. 被譴責","examples":["The candidate stands accused of breaking promises even before he's in office. 這位候選人甚至在他就職前就因違背諾言而被譴責。"]}]}]},"accompany":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"陪伴，陪同；伴隨，與……一起發生；為……伴奏（或伴唱）；附帶，補充"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>accompany</b> someone, you go somewhere with them. 陪伴","examples":["Ken agreed to accompany me on a trip to Africa. 肯同意陪我去非洲旅行。","She was accompanied by her younger brother. 她由她的弟弟陪著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>accompanies</b> another, it happens or exists at the same time, or as a result of it. 與…相伴","examples":["This volume of essays was designed to accompany an exhibition in Seattle. 這部論文集是為配合西雅圖的展覽設計的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>accompany</b> a singer or a musician, you play one part of a piece of music while they sing or play the main tune. 為…伴奏","examples":["On Meredith's new recording, Eddie Higgins accompanies her on all but one song. 在梅瑞迪斯的新唱片中，艾迪·希金斯為她伴奏了除一首歌以外的所有歌曲。"]}]}]},"absorb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸收；使併入，納入；同化，汲取；消減，緩衝（外力、震動等）；理解，掌握（資訊）；使全神貫注，使專心；承受（變革、影響等），承擔（費用等）；花掉（大量金錢），耗費"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>absorbs</b> a liquid, gas, or other substance, it soaks it up or takes it in. 吸收 (液體、氣體等)","examples":["Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the air and moisture from the soil. 植物從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，從泥土中吸收水分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>absorbs</b> light, heat, or another form of energy, it takes it in. 吸取 (光、熱等能量)","examples":["A household radiator absorbs energy in the form of electric current and releases it in the form of heat. 家用暖氣以電流的形式吸收能量，然後以熱量的形式將其釋放出去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a group <b>is absorbed</b> <b>into</b> a larger group, it becomes part of the larger group. 使併入","examples":["City schools were absorbed into the countywide school district. 市立學校被併入了郡學區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>absorbs</b> a force or shock, it reduces its effect. 使緩衝","examples":["...footwear which does not absorb the impact of the foot striking the ground. …不能緩衝腳踏在地面上所產生的衝擊力的鞋子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a system or society <b>absorbs</b> changes, effects, or costs, it is able to deal with them. 能應付","examples":["The banks would be forced to absorb large losses. 這些銀行將被迫承擔那些巨大的損失。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>absorbs</b> something valuable such as money, space, or time, it uses up a great deal of it. 大量消耗","examples":["It absorbed vast amounts of capital that could have been used for investment. 它消耗掉了原本可以用作投資的大量資本。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>absorb</b> information, you learn and understand it. 理解","examples":["Too often he only absorbs half the information in the manual. 通常，他對手冊裡的資訊只是一知半解。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>absorbs</b> you, it interests you a great deal and takes up all your attention and energy. 使專注","examples":["...a second career which absorbed her more completely than her acting ever had. …一個比其演藝事業更讓她全身心投入的第二職業。"]}]}]},"acquaint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使熟悉，使瞭解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>acquaint</b> someone <b>with</b> something, you tell them about it so that they know it. If you <b>acquaint</b> <b>yourself with</b> something, you learn about it. 使瞭解","examples":["Have steps been taken to acquaint breeders with their right to apply for licenses? 已經採取措施讓飼養動物者瞭解他們申請執照的權利了嗎？"]}]}]},"acquire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得，得到；學到，習得；患上（疾病）；逐漸具有，開始學會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>acquire</b> something, you buy or obtain it for yourself, or someone gives it to you. 獲得","examples":["General Motors acquired a 50% stake in Saab for about $400m. 通用汽車公司以大約4億美元獲得了薩博50%的股份。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>acquire</b> something such as a skill or a habit, you learn it, or develop it through your daily life or experience. 習得","examples":["I've never acquired a taste for wine. 我從未養成對葡萄酒的愛好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>acquires</b> a certain reputation, they start to have that reputation. 獲得 (名聲)","examples":["During her film career, she acquired a reputation as a strong-willed, outspoken woman. 在她的銀幕生涯中，她獲得了一個意志堅定、坦率直言的名聲。"]}]}]},"adjust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"調整，調節；整理（衣服）；適應，習慣；（保險理賠時）理算，評估（損失，損害）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>adjust</b> <b>to</b> a new situation, you get used to it by changing your behaviour or your ideas. 調整以適應","examples":["We have been preparing our fighters to adjust themselves to civil society. 我們一直在讓我們的戰士們準備好自我調整以適應普通社會。","I felt I had adjusted to the idea of being a mother very well. 我感到我已經很好地適應了做母親的想法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>adjust</b> something, you change it so that it is more effective or appropriate. 調整","examples":["To attract investors, Panama has adjusted its tax and labour laws. 為了吸引投資者，巴拿馬已經調整了其稅務及勞動法規。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>adjust</b> something such as your clothing or a machine, you correct or alter its position or setting. 調節","examples":["Liz adjusted her mirror and then edged the car out of its parking space. 莉茲調節了她的後視鏡，然後把車慢慢地開出了停車位。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>adjust</b> your vision or if your vision <b>adjusts</b>, the muscles of your eye or the pupils alter to cope with changes in light or distance. 適應","examples":["He stopped to try to adjust his vision to the faint starlight. 他停下來，試著使眼睛適應昏暗的星光。"]}]}]},"adapt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"適應；調整，使適合；改編；改造，改裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>adapt</b> <b>to</b> a new situation or <b>adapt</b> <b>yourself to</b> it, you change your ideas or behaviour in order to deal with it successfully. 適應","examples":["The world will be different, and we will have to be prepared to adapt to the change. 這個世界將會不同，所以我們必須準備好適應變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>adapt</b> something, you change it to make it suitable for a new purpose or situation. 改裝","examples":["Shelves were built to adapt the library for use as an office. 做了個書架，以便將這個圖書館改作一個辦公室用。"]}]}]},"analyze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"對……進行分析，剖析，研究（等於 analyse）；對……進行分解，解析（常用於科學、數學、語法、化學等領域）；（心理學）對……進行精神分析"}],"sections":[]},"annoy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使惱怒，使煩惱；打擾，騷擾；<古>侵擾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>annoys</b> you, it makes you fairly angry and impatient. 使心煩","examples":["Try making a note of the things that annoy you. 試著把讓你心煩的事記下來。","It annoyed me that I didn't have time to do more ironing. 沒有時間熨更多的衣服讓我心煩了。"]}]}]},"apologize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"道歉，謝罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>apologize</b> <b>to</b> someone, you say that you are sorry that you have hurt them or caused trouble for them. You can say \"<b>I apologize</b>\" as a formal way of saying sorry. 表達歉意","examples":["I apologize for being late, but I have just had a message from the hospital. 我為遲到表示歉意，但我剛得到了來自醫院的一個訊息。","He apologized to the people who had been affected. 他向受到了影響的人道了歉。"]}]}]},"appoint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"任命，指派；約定，安排（日期、時間）；裝飾，佈置（房間或空間）；<古>命令，頒佈法令；受權處置（財產）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>appoint</b> someone <b>to</b> a job or official position, you formally choose them for it. 任命","examples":["It made sense to appoint a banker to this job. 任命一位銀行家做這項工作是合理的。","The president has appointed a civilian as defence secretary. 總統任命了一位平民做國防部長。"]}]}]},"amuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逗樂，逗笑；（提供）消遣，（使）娛樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>amuses</b> you, it makes you want to laugh or smile. 使發笑","examples":["The thought seemed to amuse him. 這個想法好像讓他覺得好笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>amuse</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do something in order to pass the time and not become bored. 使消遣","examples":["I need distractions. I need to amuse myself so I won't keep thinking about things. 我需要娛樂。我需要自我消遣，這樣我才不會一直想事情。"]}]}]},"arouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引起，激起；叫醒，喚醒；激起……的性慾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>arouses</b> a particular reaction or attitude in people, it causes them to have that reaction or attitude. 引起","examples":["His revolutionary work in linguistics has aroused intense scholarly interest. 他在語言學方面的革命性著作引起了強烈的學術興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>arouses</b> a particular feeling or instinct that exists in someone, it causes them to experience that feeling or instinct strongly. 激起","examples":["The smell of frying bacon aroused his hunger. 煎鹹肉的味道激起了他的飢餓感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are aroused</b> by something, it makes you feel sexually excited. 激起性慾","examples":["Some men are aroused when their partner says erotic words to them. 一些男人在性夥伴對他們說色情話時會被撩起性慾。"]}]}]},"arise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"產生，出現；起源（於），由……引出；起床，起立；上升"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation or problem <b>arises</b>, it begins to exist or people start to become aware of it. 出現","examples":["...if a problem arises later in the pregnancy. …如果在懷孕後期出現問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>arises from</b> a particular situation, or <b>arises out of</b> it, it is created or caused by the situation. (由…) 產生","examples":["This serenity arose in part from Rachel's religious beliefs. 這種平和部分由於雷切爾的宗教信仰。"]}]}]},"assemble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）集合，（使）聚集；裝配，組裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>assemble</b> or when someone <b>assembles</b> them, they come together in a group, usually for a particular purpose such as a meeting. 集合","examples":["There wasn't even a convenient place for students to assemble between classes. 甚至沒有一個學生們課間集合的方便的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>assemble</b> something means to collect it together or to fit the different parts of it together. 聚集; 組裝","examples":["Greenpeace managed to assemble a small flotilla of inflatable boats to waylay the ship at sea. 綠色和平組織設法聚集了一支充氣艇小艦隊去攔截海上的那艘船。"]}]}]},"broil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"烤，焙，炙烤（肉或魚等）；（使）變得灼熱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"炙烤，燒烤；灼熱，酷熱；〈舊〉爭吵，爭辯；騷動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>broil</b> food, you cook it using very strong heat directly above it. 烤","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the process of broiling 烤","examples":[]}]}]},"await":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"等待，期待；將發生在，將降臨到……身上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>await</b> someone or something, you wait for them. 等候","examples":["Very little was said as we awaited the arrival of the chairman. 我們在等候主席的到來時幾乎沒說什麼話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>awaits</b> you is going to happen or come to you in the future. 將發生在…身上","examples":["A surprise awaited them in Wal-Mart. 一件意想不到的事情正在沃爾瑪裡等待著他們。"]}]}]},"assign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"分派，佈置（工作、任務）；分配（某物）；指派，派遣；確定（價值、功能、時間、地點）；轉讓（財產、權利）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>assign</b> a piece of work <b>to</b> someone, you give them the work to do. 佈置 (任務)","examples":["When I taught, I would assign a topic to children that they would write about. 教書時，我會給孩子們佈置個寫作題。","Later in the year, she'll assign them research papers. 今年晚些時候，她將給他們佈置論文。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>assign</b> something <b>to </b>someone, you say that it is for their use. 分配 (某物)","examples":["The selling broker is then required to assign a portion of the commission to the buyer broker. 賣方經紀人則被要求分給買方經紀人一部分佣金。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is assigned</b> <b>to</b> a particular place, group, or person, they are sent there, usually in order to work at that place or for that person. 分派","examples":["I was assigned to Troop A of the 10th Cavalry. 我被分派到了第10裝甲部隊的A大隊。","Did you choose Russia or were you simply assigned there? 你選擇了俄羅斯還是隻是被派到了那裡？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>assign</b> a particular function or value <b>to</b> someone or something, you say they have it. 賦予 (某功能或價值)","examples":["Under the system, each business must assign a value to each job. 在這種制度下，每家企業必須賦予每份工作某種價值。"]}]}]},"assure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使確信，向……保證；確保，使確定；給……保險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>assure</b> someone <b>that</b> something is true or will happen, you tell them that it is definitely true or will definitely happen, often in order to make them less worried. (向…) 保證","examples":["He hastened to assure me that there was nothing traumatic to report. 他急忙向我保證沒有任何不快的事要報告。","\"Are you sure the raft is safe?\" she asked anxiously. \"Couldn't be safer,\" Max assured her confidently. “你確定這筏子安全嗎？”她不安地問。“再安全不過了，”馬克斯自信地向她保證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>assure</b> someone <b>of</b> something means to make certain that they will get it. 確保得到","examples":["His performance yesterday morning assured him of a record eighth medal. 他昨天上午的成績確保了他得到創紀錄的第8枚獎牌。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use phrases such as <b>I can assure you</b> or <b>let me assure you</b> to emphasize the truth of what you are saying. 我可以向你保證/讓我向你保證","examples":["I can assure you that the animals are well cared for. 我可以向你保證這些動物都被照看得很好。"]}]}]},"attach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繫上，貼上，連線；附上（附件）；賦予，認為……具有； 和……在一起，纏著； 附帶（條件)；附屬，依附；與……有關聯；委派；扣押（債務人或其財產)；使依戀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>attach</b> something <b>to</b> an object, you join it or fasten it to the object. 附; 貼; 系","examples":["We attach labels to things before we file them away. 我們在把東西歸檔前先給它們貼上標籤。","For further information, please contact us on the attached form. 如需更多資訊，請憑附表聯絡我們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In computing, if you <b>attach</b> a file <b>to</b> a message that you send to someone, you send it with the message but separate from it. (在計算機中) 附上 (檔案)","examples":["It is possible to attach executable program files to e-mail. 可以在電子郵件上附上可執行程式檔案。"]}]}]},"calculate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"計算，核算；預測，推測"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>calculate</b> a number or amount, you discover it from information that you already have, by using arithmetic, mathematics, or a special machine. 計算","examples":["From this you can calculate the total mass in the Galaxy. 據此，你可以計算出銀河系的總質量。","We calculate that the average size farm in Lancaster County is 65 acres. 我們算出蘭開斯特郡的農場平均面積為65英畝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>calculate</b> the effects of something, especially a possible course of action, you think about them in order to form an opinion or decide what to do. 估計; 推測","examples":["I believe I am capable of calculating the political consequences accurately. 我認為自己能夠正確地預測出各種政治後果。"]}]}]},"assume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"假定，假設，認為；裝出，做出；承擔，就職；呈現，具有；奪取，篡奪"}],"sections":[]},"classify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……分類，把……分級；把（資訊）歸入保密級別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>classify</b> things means to divide them into groups or types so that things with similar characteristics are in the same group. 把…分類","examples":["It is necessary initially to classify the headaches into certain types. 起初把頭疼分成若干類別是有必要的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"分類","examples":["...the arbitrary classification of knowledge into fields of study. …把知識歸入研究領域的任意分類。"]}]}]},"carve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"雕，刻；切下，割下；開創，贏得（carve out）；鋪（路），修（路）；侵蝕，沖刷；減少，削減"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>carve</b> an object, you make it by cutting it out of a substance such as wood or stone. If you <b>carve</b> something such as wood or stone into an object, you make the object by cutting it out. 雕刻","examples":["One of the prisoners has carved a beautiful wooden chess set. 有名囚犯雕刻了一副精美的木製國際象棋。","I picked up a piece of wood and started carving. 我撿起一塊木頭，刻了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>carve</b> writing or a design <b>on</b> an object, you cut it into the surface of the object. 刻上","examples":["He carved his name on his desk. 他在書桌上刻了自己的名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>carve</b> a piece of cooked meat, you cut slices from it so that you can eat it. 切","examples":["Andrew began to carve the chicken. 安德魯動手切雞肉。"]}]}]},"circulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（液體或氣體）環流，迴圈；傳播，流傳；傳閱，傳送；來往應酬，周旋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a piece of writing <b>circulates</b> or <b>is circulated</b>, copies of it are passed around among a group of people. 散發; 流傳","examples":["The document was previously circulated in New York at the United Nations. 這份檔案過去曾在紐約的聯合國總部傳閱過。","Public employees, teachers and liberals are circulating a petition for his recall. 公務員、教師和自由主義者們正在傳籤一份請求召回他的請願書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a rumour <b>circulates</b> or <b>is circulated</b>, the people in a place tell it to each other. 散佈; 流傳","examples":["Rumours were already beginning to circulate that the project might have to be abandoned. 有關這個專案可能被迫放棄的流言已經開始在四處傳播。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"流傳","examples":["...an inquiry into the circulation of \"unacceptable literature.\" …對於“不可接受的文學”的流傳所進行的調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"迴圈","examples":["The north pole is warmer than the south and the circulation of air around it is less well contained. 北極比南極溫暖，其周圍的空氣迴圈更為暢通。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>circulates</b>, it moves easily and freely within a closed place or system. 迴圈","examples":["...a virus which circulates via the bloodstream and causes ill health in a variety of organs. …一種透過血流在體內迴圈而導致許多器官病變的病毒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>circulate</b> at a party, you move among the guests and talk to different people. (在聚會上) 往來應酬","examples":["If you'll excuse me, I really must circulate. 對不起，我真得去應酬一下了。"]}]}]},"clarify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"澄清，闡明；（透過加熱）使淨化，使純淨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clarify</b> something means to make it easier to understand, usually by explaining it in more detail. 澄清","examples":["Thank you for writing and allowing me to clarify the present position. 謝謝你來信並允許我澄清目前的狀況。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"澄清","examples":["The union has written to Detroit asking for clarification of the situation. 工會已經寫信給底特律，要求對此情況給予澄清。"]}]}]},"complicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使複雜化，使難以理解；引起併發症；使捲入，使陷入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>complicate</b> something means to make it more difficult to understand or deal with. 使複雜化","examples":["What complicates the issue is the burden of history. 使問題複雜化是歷史的重負。","The day's events, he said, would only complicate the task of the peacekeeping forces. 他說那天的事件只會使維和部隊的任務複雜化。"]}]}]},"cherish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"珍視，珍愛；懷念（過去），抱有（希望）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cherish</b> something such as a hope or a pleasant memory, you keep it in your mind for a long period of time. 珍藏 (希望、記憶等)","examples":["The president will cherish the memory of this visit to Ohio. 總統將銘記這次對俄亥俄州的訪問。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cherish</b> someone or something, you take good care of them because you love them. 珍愛","examples":["He genuinely loved and cherished her. 他真愛並珍惜過她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>cherish</b> a right, a privilege, or a principle, you regard it as important and try hard to keep it. 珍視","examples":["Chinese people cherish their independence and sovereignty. 中國人民珍視他們的獨立和主權。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(對希望、記憶等) 珍藏的","examples":["...the cherished dream of a world without wars. …久藏心中的夢想：一個沒有戰爭的世界。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"珍愛的","examples":["He described the picture as his most cherished possession. 他說這張照片是他最珍愛的財產。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"珍視的","examples":["Freud called into question some deeply cherished beliefs. 弗洛伊德對某些人們一直深信不疑的觀念提出了質疑。"]}]}]},"compose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"組成，構成；作曲；撰寫（信、詩或演講稿）；使鎮靜，使平靜；為（照片、影象）構圖；排版，排稿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The things that something <b>is composed</b> <b>of</b> are its parts or members. The separate things that <b>compose</b> something are the parts or members that form it. 組成","examples":["The force would be composed of troops from NATO countries. 該部隊將由北約各國的軍隊組成。","Protein molecules compose all the complex working parts of living cells. 蛋白質分子構成了活細胞所有複雜的工作部件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>composes</b> a piece of music or <b>composes</b>, they write music. 創作 (樂曲); 作曲","examples":["Vivaldi composed a large number of very fine concertos. 維瓦爾蒂創作了大量非常優美的協奏曲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>compose</b> something such as a letter, poem, or speech, you write it, often using a lot of concentration or skill. (用心) 寫 (信、詩、演講稿)","examples":["He started at once to compose a reply to Anna. 他立刻開始給安娜寫回信。"]}]}]},"commit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"犯（罪、錯）；調撥，投入；（使）承諾，承擔義務；鄭重承諾，忠於；把……關進醫院（監獄），監禁；傳喚（某人）到法院受審；訂婚，決定與（某人）保持長期感情；把……託付給"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>commits</b> a crime or a sin, they do something illegal or bad. 犯 (罪); 做 (壞事)","examples":["I have never committed any crime. 我從沒有犯過任何罪。","This is a man who has committed murder. 這是個犯了謀殺罪的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>commits</b> <b>suicide</b>, they deliberately kill themselves. 進行 (自殺)","examples":["There are unconfirmed reports he tried to commit suicide. 有未經證實的報道說他曾企圖自殺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> money or resources <b>to</b> something, you decide to use them for a particular purpose. 調撥 (錢、資源)","examples":["They called on Western nations to commit more money to the poorest nations. 他們號召西方國家為最貧困國家撥更多的款。","The company had committed thousands of dollars for a plan to reduce mercury emissions. 該公司已經為了一項減少汞排放的計劃調撥了數千美元。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> <b>yourself to</b> something, you say that you will definitely do it. If you <b>commit</b> <b>yourself to</b> someone, you decide that you want to have a long-term relationship with them. 使 (自己) 致力於; 使 (自己) 承諾 (與某人的長期關係)","examples":["I would advise people to think very carefully about committing themselves to working Sundays. 我會建議人們認真考慮答應週日工作。","I'd like a friendship that might lead to something deeper, but I wouldn't want to commit myself too soon. 我想要可能發展到更深層關係的友誼，但我不想太快做出承諾。","He won't commit. 他不會承諾。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do not want to <b>commit</b> <b>yourself on</b> something, you do not want to say what you really think about it or what you are going to do. (就某事) 表態","examples":["It isn't their diplomatic style to commit themselves on such a delicate issue. 就如此微妙的問題表態不是他們的外交風格。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>is committed</b> <b>to</b> a mental hospital, prison, or other institution, they are officially sent there for a period of time. 送交 (到精神病院、監獄等)","examples":["Arthur's drinking caused him to be committed to a psychiatric hospital. 阿瑟酗酒導致他被關進了一家精神病院。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> something <b>to</b> paper or <b>to</b> writing, you record it by writing it down. If you <b>commit</b> something <b>to</b> memory, you learn it so that you will remember it. 記 (在紙上、記憶中)","examples":["She had not committed anything to paper about it. 她還沒有把關於它的任何東西記在紙上。"]}]}]},"confess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"供認，招供；承認，坦白；懺悔，告解；聆聽懺悔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>confesses</b> to doing something wrong, they admit that they did it. 承認 (做了某事)","examples":["He had confessed to seventeen murders. 他已供認了17項謀殺罪。","I had expected her to confess that she only wrote these books for the money. 我曾期望她承認她寫這些書僅僅是為了錢。","Ray changed his mind, claiming that he had been forced into confessing. 雷改變了主意，聲稱他是被迫承認的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>confesses</b> or <b>confesses</b> their sins, they tell God or a priest about their sins so that they can be forgiven. 懺悔","examples":["You just go to the church and confess your sins. 你就去教堂懺悔你的罪過吧。"]}]}]},"congratulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"祝賀，向……道賀；感到高興（或自豪）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>congratulate</b> someone, you say something to show you are pleased that something nice has happened to them. 祝賀","examples":["She congratulated him on the birth of his son. 她對他兒子的出生表示了祝賀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>congratulate</b> someone, you praise them for something good that they have done. 稱讚","examples":["I really must congratulate the organizers for a well run and enjoyable event. 我真的必須稱讚這次組織良好且有趣的活動的組織者們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"祝賀","examples":["We have received many letters of congratulation. 我們收到了許多祝賀信。"]}]}]},"confine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"限制，侷限；防止……擴散；關押，監禁；使離不開（或受困於床、輪椅等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊界，範圍；限制，侷限"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>confine</b> something <b>to</b> a particular place or group means to prevent it from spreading beyond that place or group. 將 (某事物) 控制 (在某地範圍內)","examples":["Health officials have successfully confined the epidemic to the Tabatinga area. 衛生官員們已經成功地將該傳染病控制在塔巴廷加地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>confine</b> somebody or something, you prevent them from leaving or escaping. 監禁","examples":["He was confined in an internment camp in Utah. 他被監禁在猶他州的一個拘留營裡。","They decided not to let their new dog run loose, confining it to a fenced enclosure during the day. 他們決定不讓他們的新狗亂跑，白天把它關在有圍欄的圍圈裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>confine</b> <b>yourself</b> or your activities <b>to</b> something, you do only that thing and are involved with nothing else. 將 (自己或自己的活動) 侷限於","examples":["He did not confine himself to the one language. 他沒把自己侷限於這一門語言。"]}]}]},"conquer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"佔領，攻克，征服；擊敗，戰勝；克服（恐懼），解決（問題）；成功攀登；在……很受歡迎，在……取得成功"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one country or group of people <b>conquers</b> another, they take complete control of their land. 征服; 攻佔","examples":["During 1936, Mussolini conquered Abyssinia. 1936年墨索里尼攻佔了阿比西尼亞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>conquer</b> something such as a problem, you succeed in ending it or dealing with it successfully. 克服","examples":["I was certain that love was quite enough to conquer our differences. 我確信愛頗足以消除我們的分歧。","He has never conquered his addiction to smoking. 他從未戒除過煙癮。"]}]}]},"concentrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"集中注意力，聚精會神；使集中，聚集；濃縮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"濃縮物，濃縮液"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>concentrate</b> <b>on</b> something, or <b>concentrate</b> your mind <b>on</b> it, you give all your attention to it. 集中 (心思); 專心","examples":["It was up to him to concentrate on his studies and make something of himself. 他能否專心學習並有所成就取決於他自己。","At work you need to be able to concentrate. 工作時你要能專心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is concentrated</b> <b>in</b> an area, it is all there rather than being spread around. 集中","examples":["Italy's industrial districts are concentrated in its north-central and northeastern regions. 義大利的工業區集中在該國中北部和東北部地區。"]}]}]},"constitute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"組成，構成；是，被視為；成立，設立；任命"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>constitutes</b> a particular thing, it can be regarded as being that thing. 構成","examples":["Testing patients without their consent would constitute a professional and legal offence. 未得病人同意即對其進行試驗會構成職業和法律犯罪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a number of things or people <b>constitute</b> something, they are the parts or members that form it. (某數量的物或人) 構成 (某事物)","examples":["China's ethnic minorities constitute less than 7 percent of its total population. 中國的少數民族構成總人口的不到7%。"]}]}]},"consist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"由……組成，由……構成；在於，存在於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鐵路）車列"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>consists of</b> particular things or people is formed from them. (以…) 為組成部分","examples":["My diet consisted almost exclusively of chocolate-covered cookies and glasses of milk. 我的飲食幾乎只包含裹上巧克力的曲奇餅和一杯杯牛奶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>consists in</b> something else has that thing as its main or only part. (以…) 為主要組成部分","examples":["His work as a consultant consisted in advising foreign companies on the siting of new factories. 他做顧問的工作主要包括就新工廠選址為外國公司提出意見。"]}]}]},"construct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"建造，修建；組成，創立，構思；繪製，作圖"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"構想，觀念；建築物，創造物；結構體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>construct</b> something such as a building, road, or machine, you build it or make it. 建造","examples":["His company recently constructed an office building in downtown Denver. 他的公司最近在丹佛市中心建造了一座辦公樓。","The boxes should be constructed from rough-sawn timber. 這些箱子應該用粗鋸木材來做。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>construct</b> something such as an idea, a piece of writing, or a system, you create it by putting different parts together. 構建","examples":["He eventually constructed a huge business empire. 他最終構建了一個龐大的商業王國。","The novel is constructed from a series of on-the-spot reports. 這部小說是由一系列現場報道構思而成的。"]}]}]},"consult":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"諮詢，請教；商量，商討；查詢，查閱；當顧問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>consult</b> an expert or someone senior to you or <b>consult</b> <b>with</b> them, you ask them for their opinion, advice, or permission. 諮詢","examples":["Consult your doctor about how much exercise you should get. 諮詢你的醫生你應做多少運動。","He needed to consult with an attorney. 他需要和律師諮詢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>consult</b> a book or a map, you look in it or look at it in order to find some information. 查閱","examples":["Consult the chart on page 44 for the correct cooking times. 查閱第44頁的圖表找正確的烹調時間。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or group of people <b>consults</b> <b>with</b> other people or <b>consults</b> them, or if two people or groups <b>consult</b>, they talk and exchange ideas and opinions about what they might decide to do. 商量","examples":["After consulting with her daughter and manager, she decided to take on the part, on her terms. 同她的女兒兼經紀人商量之後，她決定按她的要求接受那個角色。","The two countries will have to consult their allies. 兩國得同各自的盟友協商。"]}]}]},"consume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"消耗，消費；吃，喝；吞噬，燒燬；使……著迷，充滿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>consume</b> something, you eat or drink it. 吃; 喝","examples":["Martha would consume nearly a pound of cheese per day. 瑪莎那時每天吃將近一磅乳酪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>consume</b> an amount of fuel, energy, or time means to use it up. 消耗","examples":["Some of the most efficient refrigerators consume 70 percent less electricity than traditional models. 一些能效最高的冰箱比傳統型號少消耗70%的電。"]}]}]},"converse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"談話，交談"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"相反的事物，反面說法；<舊>談話，交談；逆命題"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相反的，顛倒的，逆向的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>converse</b> <b>with</b> someone, you talk to them. You can also say that two people <b>converse</b>. 交談","examples":["Luke sat directly behind the pilot and conversed with him. 盧克坐在飛行員的正後方和他交談。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The converse</b> of a statement is its opposite or reverse. 相反的說法","examples":["What you do for a living is critical to where you settle and how you live – and the converse is also true. 你的工作決定你在哪裡定居和怎樣生活–反之亦然。"]}]}]},"cooperate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"合作，協作；配合，協助"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cooperate</b> <b>with</b> someone, you work with them or help them for a particular purpose. You can also say that two people <b>cooperate</b>. 合作","examples":["The U.N. had been cooperating with the State Department on a plan to find countries willing to take the refugees. 聯合國和美國國務院合作，制定計劃來尋找願意接納難民的國家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合作","examples":["A deal with Japan could open the door to economic cooperation with East Asia. 與日本的交易可以開啟與東亞經濟合作的大門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"協作","examples":["The police underlined the importance of the public's cooperation in the hunt for the bombers. 在尋找安置炸彈的人時，警察強調了公眾協作的重要性。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cooperate</b>, you do what someone has asked or told you to do. 配合","examples":["He agreed to cooperate with the police investigation. 他同意配合警方調查。"]}]}]},"contribute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"捐贈，捐助；（為……）做貢獻；促成，是……的原因之一；撰稿，投稿；發表意見，提議"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contribute</b> <b>to</b> something, you say or do things to help to make it successful. 貢獻; 做出貢獻","examples":["The three sons also contribute to the family business. 3個兒子也為家族企業做貢獻。","I believe that each of us can contribute to the future of the world. 我相信我們每一個人都能為世界的未來做出貢獻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>contributes</b> <b>to</b> an event or situation, it is one of the causes of it. 是 (造成某情況) 的一個原因","examples":["The report says design faults in both the vessels contributed to the tragedy. 報道稱兩艘船在設計上的缺陷是造成悲劇的原因。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>contribute</b> money or resources <b>to</b> something means to give money or resources to help pay for something or to help achieve a particular purpose. 捐助","examples":["The U.S. is contributing $4 billion in loans, credits, and grants. 美國以信貸和贈與的方式捐助了40億美元。","Local businesses have agreed to contribute. 當地的公司已經同意捐助了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"捐助者","examples":["Candidates for Congress received 53 percent of their funds from individual contributors. 國會候選人接受的捐款中有53%來自個人捐助者。"]}]}]},"convey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳送，運輸；表達，傳遞；<法律>轉讓（土地、財產等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>convey</b> information or feelings means to cause them to be known or understood by someone. 傳達","examples":["When I returned home, I tried to convey the wonder of this machine to my husband. 回到家之後，我設法讓我丈夫知道這臺機器的神奇之處。","In every one of her pictures she conveys a sense of immediacy. 她的每一張畫都有一種直觀性。"]}]}]},"convince":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使確信，使信服；說服，勸服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>convinces</b> you <b>to</b> do something, they persuade you to do it. 說服","examples":["That weekend in Plattsburgh, he convinced her to go ahead and marry Bud. 在普拉茨堡的那個週末，他說服了她嫁給巴德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>convinces</b> you <b>of</b> something, they make you believe that it is true or that it exists. 使信服","examples":["Although I soon convinced him of my innocence, I think he still has serious doubts about my sanity. 儘管我很快就使他相信我是清白的，但是他還是非常懷疑我精神是否正常。"]}]}]},"cope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"對付，處理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長袍，法衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cope</b> <b>with</b> a problem or task, you deal with it successfully. (妥善地) 處理","examples":["It was amazing how my mother coped with bringing up three children on less than thirty dollars a week. 讓人驚歎的是我媽媽怎樣以每週不到30美元的開銷養大了3個孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have to <b>cope with</b> an unpleasant situation, you have to accept it or bear it. 應付 (困難局面)","examples":["Never before has the industry had to cope with war and recession at the same time. 企業以前從來沒有同時應付過戰爭和經濟衰退。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a machine or a system can <b>cope</b> <b>with</b> something, it is large enough or complex enough to deal with it satisfactorily. (用機器) 處理","examples":["A giant washing machine copes with the mountain of laundry created by their nine boys and five girls. 一臺大容量洗衣機能夠清洗他們9個男孩和5個女孩換下的堆積如山的髒衣服。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a large ceremonial cloak worn at solemn liturgical functions by priests of certain Christian sects (基督教教士的)法衣","examples":[]}]}]},"cram":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"塞進，擠滿；臨時死記硬背，填鴨式學習；匆忙戴上；貪婪地吃"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（應考）突擊準備，死記硬背；極度擁擠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cram</b> things or people <b>into</b> a container or place, you put them into it, although there is hardly enough room for them. 把…塞進","examples":["Terry crammed the dirty clothes into his bag. 特里把髒衣服塞進了包裡。","She crammed her mouth with caviar. 她塞了一嘴魚子醬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>cram</b> <b>into</b> a place or vehicle or <b>cram</b> a place or vehicle, so many of them enter it at one time that it is completely full. 擠滿; 塞進","examples":["We crammed into my car and set off. 我們擠進我的汽車，出發了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are cramming for</b> an examination, you are learning as much as possible in a short time just before you take the examination. 突擊準備 (考試)","examples":["She was cramming for her Economics exam. 她正為了應付經濟學考試而臨時抱佛腳。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(考試的) 突擊準備","examples":["It would take two or three months of cramming to prepare for Vermont's bar exam. 佛蒙特州的律師考試需要2到3個月時間的突擊準備。"]}]}]},"correspond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"類似於，相當於；通訊；相一致，符合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>corresponds</b> <b>to</b> another, there is a close similarity or connection between them. You can also say that two things <b>correspond</b>. 相一致; 相對應","examples":["Racegoers will be given a number which will correspond to a horse running in a race. 觀看賽馬的觀眾將領到一個與參賽馬匹相對應的號碼。","The two maps of the Rockies correspond closely. 這兩張落基山脈的地圖極為相似。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>correspond</b> <b>with</b> someone, you write letters to them. You can also say that two people <b>correspond</b>. 通訊","examples":["She still corresponds with friends she met in Majorca nine years ago. 她依然和9年前在馬略卡島遇到的朋友們通訊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"相應的","examples":["The rise in interest rates was not reflected in a corresponding rise in the dollar. 利率上調沒有反映在相應的美元增值上。"]}]}]},"criticize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"批評，指責；評論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>criticize</b> someone or something, you express your disapproval of them by saying what you think is wrong with them. 批評","examples":["His mother had rarely criticized him or any of her other children. 他母親很少批評他或她的其他孩子。"]}]}]},"depress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使抑鬱，使沮喪；降低，抑制；使蕭條，使不景氣；按下，壓下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>depresses</b> you, they make you feel sad and disappointed. 使沮喪","examples":["I must admit the state of the country depresses me. 我必須承認國家的形勢令我沮喪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>depresses</b> prices, wages, or figures, it causes them to become less. 使降低","examples":["The stronger U.S. dollar depressed sales. 更堅挺的美元使銷售量下降。"]}]}]},"depart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啟程，出發；背離，違背；離職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something or someone <b>departs</b> <b>from</b> a place, they leave it and start a trip to another place. You can also say that someone <b>departs</b> a place 離開; 起程","examples":["Flight 43 will depart from Denver at 11:45 a.m. and arrive in Honolulu at 4:12 p.m. 43號航班將於上午11:45從丹佛起飛，並於下午4:12到達檀香山。","In the morning Mr. McDonald departed for Sydney. 麥克唐納先生早上起程去了悉尼。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>depart</b> <b>from</b> a traditional, accepted, or agreed way of doing something, you do it in a different or unexpected way. 偏離; 違背","examples":["Why is it in this country that we have departed from good educational sense? 為什麼我們這個國家偏離了良好的教育觀念？"]}]}]},"devise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"設計，發明；<法律>（透過遺囑）遺贈（不動產）；<古>圖謀"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<法律>（遺囑中）遺贈不動產的條款"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>devise</b> a plan, system, or machine, you have the idea for it and design it. 構思; 設計","examples":["We devised a scheme to help him. 我們想出了一個計劃來幫助他。"]}]}]},"deserve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"值得，應受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or thing <b>deserves</b> something, you mean that they should have it or receive it because of their actions or qualities. 應得","examples":["Government officials clearly deserve some of the blame as well. 政府官員們顯然也應受到某些譴責。","These people deserve to make more than the minimum wage. 這些人應該得到高於最低工資的報酬。"]}]}]},"declare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"宣佈，宣告；斷言，宣稱；申報；放棄擊球，宣佈結束賽局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>declare</b> that something is true, you say that it is true in a firm, deliberate way. You can also <b>declare</b> an attitude or intention. 宣告; 表明","examples":["He declared he would not run for a second term as president. 他宣告不再競選連任總統。","He declared his intention to become the best golfer in the world. 他表明了要成為世界上最佳高爾夫球手的意願。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>declare</b> something, you state officially and formally that it exists or is the case. 宣告","examples":["The government is ready to declare a permanent ceasefire. 政府已經準備好宣佈永久停火。","His lawyers are confident that the judges will declare Mr. Stevens innocent. 他的律師們確信法官們會宣佈史蒂文斯先生無罪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>declare</b> goods that you have bought in another country or money that you have earned, you say how much you have bought or earned so that you can pay tax on it. 申報 (在國外所購之物或收入等)","examples":["Declaring the wrong income by mistake will no longer lead to an automatic fine. 由於失誤申報收入不符的不再予以自動罰款。"]}]}]},"defend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保衛，防禦；捍衛，維護；（在比賽中）防守，防衛；參加衛冕賽，蟬聯；做……的辯護律師，為……辯解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>defend</b> someone or something, you take action in order to protect them. 保護","examples":["His courage in defending religious and civil rights inspired many outside the church. 他捍衛宗教權和公民權的勇氣鼓舞了許多非教會人士。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>defend</b> someone or something when they have been criticized, you argue in support of them. 為…爭辯","examples":["He defended his administration's response to the disaster against critics who charge the federal government is moving too slowly. 他為他的行政部門對災難的反應做了爭辯，反駁批評人士指控聯邦政府行動過於遲緩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a lawyer <b>defends</b> a person who has been accused of something, the lawyer argues on their behalf in a court of law that the charges are not true. 為…辯護","examples":["...a lawyer who defended political prisoners during the military regime. …一位在軍權時期為政治犯進行辯護的律師。","He has hired a lawyer to defend him against the allegation. 他已聘請一位律師為他所受的指控辯護。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a sports player plays in the tournament which they won the previous time it was held, you can say that they <b>are defending</b> their title. 衛冕","examples":["Torrence expects to defend her title successfully in the next Olympics. 託倫斯希望下屆奧運會能成功衛冕。"]}]}]},"devote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獻身，致力；用於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>devote</b> yourself, your time, or your energy <b>to</b> something, you spend all or most of your time or energy on it. 把…奉獻給","examples":["He decided to devote the rest of his life to scientific investigation. 他決定把餘生奉獻給科學研究。","Considerable resources have been devoted to proving him a liar. 大量的資源已被用來證明他是個撒謊者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>devote</b> a particular proportion of a piece of writing or a speech <b>to</b> a particular subject, you deal with the subject in that amount of space or time. 作…專用","examples":["He devoted a major section of his massive report to an analysis of U.S. aircraft design. 他在那份厚重的報告中用一個主要章節分析了美國的飛機設計。"]}]}]},"demonstrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"證明；示範，演示；表露；遊行，示威"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>demonstrate</b> a fact means to make it clear to people. 證明","examples":["The study also demonstrated a direct link between obesity and mortality. 這項研究也證明了肥胖和死亡率之間的直接關係。","They are anxious to demonstrate to the voters that they have practical policies. 他們急於向選民證明他們有切實可行的政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>demonstrate</b> a particular skill, quality, or feeling, you show by your actions that you have it. 展現 (才能、品質、感情)","examples":["Have they, for example, demonstrated a commitment to democracy? 例如，他們展現了對民主的奉獻嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>demonstrate</b> something, you show people how it works or how to do it. 展示","examples":["A selection of cosmetic companies will be there to demonstrate their new products. 一些化妝品公司會在那裡展示他們的新產品。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>demonstrate</b>, they march or gather somewhere to show their opposition to something or their support for something. 遊行示威","examples":["Some 30,000 angry farmers arrived in Brussels yesterday to demonstrate against possible cuts in subsidies. 昨天大約三萬名憤怒的農民到布魯塞爾遊行示威，反對可能的補貼削減。","In the cities vast crowds have been demonstrating for change. 在各城市，已經有大量的群眾舉行示威遊行要求變革。"]}]}]},"differ":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"不同於；意見有分歧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more things <b>differ</b>, they are unlike each other in some way. 不同","examples":["The story he told police differed from the one he told his mother. 他告訴警察的話和告訴他母親的不同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>differ</b> about something, they do not agree with each other about it. 有異議","examples":["The two leaders had differed on the issue of sanctions. 就制裁問題兩位領導持不同意見。","That is where we differ. 那就是我們的分歧所在。"]}]}]},"disconnect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"切斷（機器或裝置電力、煤氣、水等的供應）；（尤指因未繳費而）停止供應（電、氣、水、電話等服務）；使（電話）斷線，將（電話）中斷； 使分離，使脫離；切斷（與系統、網路的）聯絡；（使）脫離，（使）不聯絡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"斷開連線；差異，缺乏聯絡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>disconnect</b> a piece of equipment means to separate it from its source of power or to break a connection that it needs in order to work. 斷開","examples":["The device automatically disconnects the ignition when the engine is switched off. 該裝置在引擎被關閉時會自動斷開點火裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are disconnected</b> by a gas, electricity, water, or telephone company, they turn off the connection to your house, usually because you have not paid the bill. 切斷 (煤氣、電、水、電話等的) 供應","examples":["You are likely to be given almost three months – until the time of your next bill – before you are disconnected. 你很可能會得到將近3個月的時間–即直到你下一張賬單寄發為止——才會被切斷供應。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>disconnect</b> something <b>from</b> something else, you separate the two things. 使分離","examples":["He disconnected the IV bottle from the overhead hook and carried it beside the moving cart. 他從頭頂的鉤子上取下輸液瓶，並在移動的手推車旁提著它。"]}]}]},"discourage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使洩氣，使灰心；使打消念頭，勸阻；阻礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>discourages</b> you, they cause you to lose your enthusiasm about your actions. 使氣餒","examples":["It may be difficult to do at first. Don't let this discourage you. 開始時做起來也許比較困難。不要讓這個洩你的氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>discourage</b> an action or to <b>discourage</b> someone <b>from</b> doing it means to make them not want to do it. 阻攔","examples":["...typhoons that discouraged shopping and leisure activities. …打消購物和休閒活動的念頭的數起颱風。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"氣餒的","examples":["She was determined not to be too discouraged. 她下了決心不要太氣餒。"]}]}]},"dismiss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開除，解僱；不考慮，不理會；駁回，停止受理；讓……離開，解散；（板球）使退場，使出局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dismiss</b> something, you decide or say that it is not important enough for you to think about or consider. 不予理會","examples":["Mr. Wakeham dismissed the reports as speculation. 韋克厄姆先生把這些報道當作臆測而不予理會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dismiss</b> something <b>from</b> your mind, you stop thinking about it. 不再考慮","examples":["I dismissed the problem from my mind. 我從心中摒除了這個問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When an employer <b>dismisses</b> an employee, the employer tells the employee that they are no longer needed to do the job that they have been doing. 解僱","examples":["...the power to dismiss civil servants who refuse to work. …解僱拒絕工作的公務員們的權力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are dismissed</b> by someone in authority, they tell you that you can go away from them. 准予…離去","examples":["Two more witnesses were called, heard, and dismissed. 又有兩名證人被傳訊後獲准離開了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a judge <b>dismisses</b> a case against someone, he or she formally states that there is no need for a trial, usually because there is not enough evidence for the case to continue. 不受理","examples":["A federal judge dismissed the charges against the doctor yesterday. 一名聯邦法官昨天駁回了對該醫生的指控。"]}]}]},"download":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"下載"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"下載，下載的檔案或程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>download</b> data means to transfer it to or from a computer along a line such as a telephone line, a radio link, or a computer network. 下載","examples":["Users can download their material to a desktop PC back in the office. 使用者們可以將他們的資料下載到辦公室的臺式計算機上。"]}]}]},"disturb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打擾，妨礙；使焦慮，使煩惱；移動，弄亂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disturb</b> someone, you interrupt what they are doing and upset them. 打擾","examples":["Did you sleep well? I didn't want to disturb you. You looked so peaceful. 你睡得好嗎？我不想打擾你。你看起來如此平靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>disturbs</b> you, it makes you feel upset or worried. 使不安; 使煩惱","examples":["I dream about him, dreams so vivid that they disturb me for days. 我夢到他了，夢是那麼栩栩如生以至於困擾了我好幾天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is disturbed</b>, its position or shape is changed. 使紊亂","examples":["He'd placed his notes in the brown envelope. They hadn't been disturbed. 他已把票據放在那個棕色信封裡了。票據沒有被動過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>disturbs</b> a situation or atmosphere, it spoils it or causes trouble. 使混亂","examples":["What could possibly disturb such tranquillity? 有什麼能破壞這種寧靜？"]}]}]},"distribute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"分發，分配；配送，分銷；散佈，使分佈；（印刷）拆（版）還字；周延"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>distribute</b> things, you hand them or deliver them to a number of people. 分發","examples":["Students shouted slogans and distributed leaflets. 學生們高呼口號，散發傳單。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a company <b>distributes</b> goods, it supplies them to the stores or businesses that sell them. 配銷","examples":["We didn't understand how difficult it was to distribute a national paper. 我們不明白配銷一份全國性的報紙有多麼困難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>distribute</b> a substance <b>over</b> something means to scatter it over it. 散佈","examples":["Distribute the topping evenly over the fruit. 將澆頭均勻地澆在水果上。"]}]}]},"distinguish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使有別於；看清，認出；區別，分清"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you can <b>distinguish</b> one thing <b>from</b> another or <b>distinguish</b> <b>between</b> two things, you can see or understand how they are different. 辨別; 區分","examples":["Could he distinguish right from wrong? 他能辨別是非嗎？","Research suggests that babies learn to see by distinguishing between areas of light and dark. 研究顯示嬰兒是透過區分明亮區域和黑暗區域來學會觀看的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A feature or quality that <b>distinguishes</b> one thing <b>from</b> another causes the two things to be regarded as different, because only the first thing has the feature or quality. 有別於","examples":["There is something about music that distinguishes it from all other art forms. 音樂中一些因素使之有別於其他藝術形式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you can <b>distinguish</b> something, you can see, hear, or taste it although it is very difficult to detect. 辨別出","examples":["There were cries, calls. He could distinguish voices. 有各種各樣的哭聲和叫喊聲。他能從中分辨出聲音。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>distinguish</b> <b>yourself</b>, you do something that makes you famous or important. 使著名","examples":["Over the next few years he distinguished himself as a leading constitutional scholar. 在隨後的幾年中，他作為憲法學的權威學者而享有盛譽。"]}]}]},"dominate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"統治，支配；在……中佔首要地位；俯視，高聳於；佔絕對優勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>dominate</b> a situation means to be the most powerful or important person or thing in it. 佔據支配地位","examples":["The book is expected to dominate the best-seller lists. 這本書預期將佔據暢銷書榜首的位置。","...countries where life is dominated by war. …飽受戰亂的國家。","Selling could continue to dominate as investors play it safe. 因為投資者們謹慎行事,售出可能會繼續佔主流。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one country or person <b>dominates</b> another, they have power over them. 控制","examples":["He denied that his country wants to dominate Europe. 他否認他的國家想稱霸歐洲。","Women are no longer dominated by the men in their relationships. 在兩性的相互關係中，女性已不再受制於男性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a building, mountain, or other object <b>dominates</b> an area, it is so large or impressive that you cannot avoid seeing it. 俯視; 高出","examples":["It's one of the biggest buildings in this area, and it really dominates this whole place. 這是該地區最大的建築物之一，俯視著整個地區。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"支配","examples":["...the domination of the market by a small number of organizations. …少數機構對市場的支配。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"統治","examples":["They had five centuries of domination by the Romans. 他們被羅馬人統治了5個世紀。"]}]}]},"embarrass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）尷尬，窘迫；使難堪，使為難；<古>妨礙（人，移動，行動）；<古>使困難重重，使複雜化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>embarrasses</b> you, they make you feel shy or ashamed. 使…尷尬","examples":["His clumsiness embarrassed him. 他的笨拙令他尷尬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>embarrasses</b> a public figure such as a politician or an organization such as a political party, it causes problems for them. 使…陷入麻煩","examples":["Aides spoke of disposing of records that would embarrass the governor. 助手們談到了要處理掉那些會給州長找麻煩的記錄。"]}]}]},"eliminate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"剔除，根除；對……不予考慮，把……排除在外；（比賽中）淘汰；剷除，殺害；（生理）排除，排洩；消去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>eliminate</b> something, especially something you do not want or need, means to remove it completely. 根除","examples":["Recent measures have not eliminated discrimination in employment. 最近的舉措還未能根除就業歧視。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a person or team <b>is eliminated</b> <b>from</b> a competition, they are defeated and so stop participating in the competition. 淘汰","examples":["I was eliminated from the 400 metres in the semi-finals. 我在400米半決賽中被淘汰了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone says that they <b>have eliminated</b> an enemy, they mean that they have killed them. By using the word \"eliminate,\" they are trying to make the action sound more positive than if they used the word \"kill.\" 消滅","examples":["He declared war on the government and urged right-wingers to eliminate their opponents. 他向政府宣戰並且力勸右翼分子們消滅他們的對手。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"根除","examples":["...the prohibition and elimination of chemical weapons. …對化學武器的禁止和銷燬。"]}]}]},"emerge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"浮現，出現；顯露，知悉；恢復過來，倖存下來；形成，興起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>emerge</b> means to come out from an enclosed or dark space such as a room or a vehicle, or from a position where you could not be seen. (從視線以外的地方) 出現; 出來","examples":["Richard was waiting outside the door as she emerged. 當她出現的時候，理查德正等候在門外。","She then emerged from the courthouse to thank her supporters. 於是她從法院大樓出來向支持者們表示感謝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>emerge from</b> a difficult or bad experience, you come to the end of it. 擺脫","examples":["There is growing evidence that the economy is at last emerging from recession. 有越來越多的跡象表明經濟將最終擺脫蕭條。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something <b>emerges</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing, they become recognized as that thing. 立足成為","examples":["Vietnam has emerged as the world's third-biggest rice exporter. 越南已立足成為世界第三大稻米出口國。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When something such as an organization or an industry <b>emerges</b>, it comes into existence. 興起","examples":["...the new republic that emerged in October 1917. …1917年10月成立的新共和國。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a fact or result <b>emerges</b> from a period of thought, discussion, or investigation, it becomes known as a result of it. 顯露 (事實、結果)","examples":["...the growing corruption that has emerged in the past few years. …過去幾年中暴露出來的日趨嚴重的腐敗。","It soon emerged that neither the July nor August mortgage payment had been collected. 很快顯示的是7月和8月的抵押款都沒有被收取。"]}]}]},"enclose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包圍，圍住；隨信附上，隨信裝入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or object <b>is enclosed</b> by something, the place or object is inside that thing or completely surrounded by it. 包圍; 裝","examples":["The rules state that samples must be enclosed in two watertight containers. 條例規定樣品必須用兩個不漏水的容器封裝起來。","Enclose the flower in a small muslin bag. 把這花用一個小棉袋包起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>enclose</b> something with a letter, you put it in the same envelope as the letter. (隨信) 附上","examples":["I have enclosed a cheque for £100. 我信裡附上了一張$100的支票。"]}]}]},"endanger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使處於險境，危及"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>endanger</b> something or someone means to put them in a situation where they might be harmed or destroyed completely. 危害","examples":["The debate could endanger the proposed Mideast peace talks. 這場爭論可能會危害中東和談的倡議。"]}]}]},"enforce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"實施，執行（法律、規章）；強迫，迫使；<舊>竭力使人接受（要求，論點）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people in authority <b>enforce</b> a law or a rule, they make sure that it is obeyed, usually by punishing people who do not obey it. 施行","examples":["Boulder was one of the first cities in the nation to enforce a ban on smoking. 博爾德是該國率先施行禁菸令的城市之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>enforce</b> something means to force or cause it to be done or to happen. 強制執行","examples":["They struggled to limit the cost by enforcing a low-tech specification. 他們透過強制執行一種低技術規範來竭力限制成本。"]}]}]},"equip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝備，配備；使有所準備，使能夠勝任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>equip</b> a person or thing <b>with</b> something, you give them the tools or equipment that are needed. 裝備; 配備","examples":["They try to equip their vehicles with gadgets to deal with every possible contingency. 他們儘量給他們的車輛配備各種小裝置以應付任何可能的突發狀況。","Owners of restaurants have to equip them to admit disabled people. 餐館老闆們必須給餐館配備接納殘疾人的設施。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>equips</b> you <b>for</b> a particular task or experience, it gives you the skills and attitudes you need for it, especially by educating you in a particular way. 訓練","examples":["Relative poverty, however, did not prevent Martin from equipping himself with an excellent education. 然而相對的貧窮並沒有妨礙馬丁接受良好教育。"]}]}]},"endure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"持續存在，持久；忍受，忍耐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>endure</b> a painful or difficult situation, you experience it and do not avoid it or give up, usually because you cannot. 承受","examples":["The company endured heavy financial losses. 公司承受了沉重的財務損失。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>endures</b>, it continues to exist without any loss in quality or importance. 延續","examples":["Somehow the language endures and continues to survive. 由於某種原因，這種語言持續生存下來了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"持久的","examples":["This chance meeting was the start of an enduring friendship. 這次偶然的相遇是一段持久友情的開始。"]}]}]},"entertain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使有興趣，使快樂；心存，懷有（想法、希望、感覺等）；招待，請客"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a performer, performance, or activity <b>entertains</b> you, it amuses you, interests you, or gives you pleasure. 使娛樂; 娛樂","examples":["They were entertained by top singers, dancers and celebrities. 他們饒有興趣地看了頂級歌手、舞蹈演員和名流們的演出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>entertain</b>, or <b>entertain</b> people, you provide food and drink for them, for example, when you have invited them to your house. 招待; 宴客","examples":["I don't like to entertain guests anymore. 我不再喜歡招待客人。","He loves to entertain. 他喜歡宴客。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>entertain</b> an idea or suggestion, you allow yourself to consider it as possible or as worth thinking about seriously. 心存","examples":["How foolish I am to entertain doubts. 我心存疑慮是多麼愚蠢啊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"娛樂的","examples":["To generate new money the sport needs to be more entertaining. 想生更多的財，這項運動得更有娛樂性。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"招待; 宴客","examples":["...a cosy area for entertaining and relaxing. …一個宴客與休閒的舒適場所。"]}]}]},"enlarge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擴大，增大，放大；詳述（enlarge on）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>enlarge</b> something or when it <b>enlarges</b>, it becomes bigger. 擴大","examples":["The college has announced its intention to enlarge its stadium. 該學院已宣佈了擴建其體育館的打算。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>enlarge</b> <b>on</b> something that has been mentioned, you give more details about it. 詳述","examples":["He didn't enlarge on the form that the interim government and assembly would take. 他未詳述臨時政府和議會將會採取的形式。"]}]}]},"establish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"建立，設立；證實，確定；發現，找出；使被接受，使得到承認；使（故事的角色）真實；（橋牌）（透過出大牌）使（某）花色所剩的牌都能贏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>establishes</b> something such as an organization, a type of activity, or a set of rules, they create it or introduce it in such a way that it is likely to last for a long time. 建立; 確立","examples":["The UN has established detailed criteria for who should be allowed to vote. 聯合國就誰應當被允許投票確立了詳細標準。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>establish</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you discover facts that show that it is definitely true. 證實","examples":["Medical tests established that she was not their own child. 醫學檢測證實她不是他們的親生孩子。","It will be essential to establish how the money is being spent. 搞清這筆錢是如何被花費的將至關重要。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>establish</b> <b>yourself</b>, your reputation, or a good quality that you have, you succeed in doing something, and achieve respect or a secure position as a result of this. 確立 (地位)","examples":["This is going to be the show where up-and-coming comedians will establish themselves. 這會是一場很有前途的喜劇演員們將在此確立他們地位的演出。","He has established himself as a pivotal figure in state politics. 他作為國家政治中的一位軸心人物的地位已經確立。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>establish</b> contact with someone, you start to have contact with them. You can also say that two people, groups, or countries <b>establish</b> contact. 建立 (聯絡)","examples":["We had already established contact with the museum. 我們已經與那個博物館建立了聯絡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被證實了的","examples":["That link is an established medical fact. 那種聯絡是被證實了的醫學事實。"]}]}]},"exaggerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"誇大，言過其實；使擴大"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>exaggerate</b>, you indicate that something is, for example, worse or more important than it really is. 誇大","examples":["He thinks I'm exaggerating. 他認為我在誇大其詞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>exaggerates</b> a situation, quality, or feature, it makes the situation, quality, or feature appear greater, more obvious, or more important than it really is. 誇大","examples":["These figures exaggerate the loss of competitiveness. 這些數字誇大了競爭力的下降。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"誇大","examples":["Like many stories about him, it smacks of exaggeration. 像很多有關他的故事一樣，這個也有點兒誇大的意味。"]}]}]},"evaluate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"評價，評估，估值；求（方程式，公式，函式）的數值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>evaluate</b> something or someone, you consider them in order to make a judgment about them, for example about how good or bad they are. 評價; 評估","examples":["The market situation is difficult to evaluate. 市場形勢難以評估。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"評價; 評估","examples":["...the opinions and evaluations of college supervisors. …學院督導們的意見和評價。"]}]}]},"expand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擴大，增加；擴充套件，發展；細談，詳述；變得更自信（善談）；（宇宙）膨脹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>expands</b> or <b>is expanded</b>, it becomes larger. 擴大; 膨脹","examples":["Engineers noticed that the pipes were not expanding as expected. 工程師們注意到管子並未像預期的那樣膨脹。","We have to expand the size of the image. 我們不得不擴大影象的尺寸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a business, organization, or service <b>expands</b>, or if you <b>expand</b> it, it becomes bigger and includes more people, goods, or activities. 使…發展; 發展","examples":["The popular ceramics industry expanded toward the middle of the 19th century. 大眾陶瓷業在19世紀中葉得到了發展。"]}]}]},"explore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"探討，探究；考察，探索；（用手或身體其他部位）探查，仔細檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>explore</b>, or <b>explore</b> a place, you travel around it to find out what it is like. 考察","examples":["I just wanted to explore on my own. 我只是想獨自考察一下。","After exploring the old part of town there is a guided tour of the cathedral. 考察老城區之後，有到大教堂的導覽之旅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>explore</b> an idea or suggestion, you think about it or comment on it in detail, in order to assess it carefully. 探討","examples":["The film is eloquent as it explores the relationship between artist and instrument. 這部影片探討藝術家與樂器之間的關係，意味深長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>explore</b> something with your hands or fingers, you touch it to find out what it feels like. 摸索","examples":["He explored the wound with his finger, trying to establish its extent. 他用手指探查傷口，試圖確定受傷的程度。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"考察","examples":["We devote several days to the exploration of the magnificent Maya sites of Copan. 我們投入了幾天時間在科潘宏偉的瑪雅遺址考察。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"探討","examples":["I looked forward to the exploration of their theories. 我期待著對他們的理論進行探討。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"勘探","examples":["Oryx is a Dallas-based oil and gas exploration and production concern. 奧瑞克斯公司是一家以達拉斯為基地的石油和天然氣勘探及生產公司。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>explore for</b> a substance such as oil or minerals, they study an area and do tests on the land to see whether they can find it. 勘探","examples":["Central to the operation is a mile-deep well, dug originally to explore for oil. 那次行動的重點是一口原本為勘探石油而挖的一英里深的井。"]}]}]},"flee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逃離，逃避，逃跑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flee</b> <b>from</b> something or someone, or <b>flee</b> a person or thing, you escape from them. 逃離","examples":["He slammed the bedroom door behind him and fled. 他砰地關上臥室的門就逃走了。","...refugees fleeing persecution or torture. …逃避迫害或折磨的難民們。"]}]}]},"flatter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"奉承，討好；使高興，使感到榮幸；使顯得更漂亮；使（某物）顯得更重要（更好）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>flatters</b> you, they praise you in an exaggerated way that is not sincere, because they want to please you or to persuade you to do something. 奉承","examples":["I knew she was just flattering me. 我知道她只是在奉承我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>flatter</b> <b>yourself that</b> something good is the case, you believe that it is true, although others may disagree. If someone says to you \"<b>you're flattering yourself</b>\" or \"<b>don't flatter yourself</b>,\" they mean that they disagree with your good opinion of yourself. 自以為是; 高看自己","examples":["I flatter myself that this campaign will put an end to the war. 我自以為這次戰役將結束這場戰爭。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to show to advantage 凸顯","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a blacksmith's tool, resembling a flat-faced hammer, that is placed on forged work and struck to smooth the surface of the forging 平面錘","examples":[]}]}]},"furnish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為（房間或房屋）配備傢俱；提供，供應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>furnish</b> a room or building, you put furniture and furnishings into it. 裝潢; 佈置 (房間、建築物)","examples":["Many proprietors try to furnish their hotels with antiques. 許多企業主儘可能用古董裝飾他們的旅館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>furnish</b> someone <b>with</b> something, you provide or supply it. 提供","examples":["They'll be able to furnish you with the rest of the details. 他們將能夠給你提供其餘的細節。"]}]}]},"forbid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"禁止；使不可能，妨礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>forbid</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, or if you <b>forbid</b> an activity, you order that it must not be done. 禁止","examples":["They'll forbid you to marry. 他們會不許你結婚。","She was shut away and forbidden to read. 她被關起來不許讀書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>forbids</b> a particular course of action or state of affairs, it makes it impossible for the course of action or state of affairs to happen. 使…不可能","examples":["His own pride forbids him to ask Arthur's help. 他自己的傲慢使他不可能尋求亞瑟的幫助。"]}]}]},"grieve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指因某人亡故而）感到悲痛；使傷心"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<蘇格蘭>農莊總管"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grieve</b> <b>over</b> something, especially someone's death, you feel very sad about it.  感到悲痛","examples":["He's grieving over his dead wife and son. 他因喪妻失子而悲痛不已。","I didn't have any time to grieve. 我沒有時間去悲傷。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a farm manager or overseer 農場經理; 農場監工","examples":[]}]}]},"expose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"暴露，使顯露；使面臨，使遭受（危險或不快）；揭露，揭發；接觸，體驗；露出，顯露（感情）；使（膠捲）曝光；棄（嬰孩）於戶外讓其死去"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"揭露，曝光"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>expose</b> something that is usually hidden means to uncover it so that it can be seen. 使顯露","examples":["Lowered sea levels exposed the shallow continental shelf beneath the Bering Sea. 下降了的海平面使白令海底的淺大陸架露了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>expose</b> a person or situation means to reveal that they are bad or immoral in some way. 揭露","examples":["...the story of how the press helped expose the truth about the Nixon administration. …關於新聞界如何協助揭露尼克松政府真相的報道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is exposed to</b> something dangerous or unpleasant, they are put in a situation in which it might affect them. 使暴露於 (危險或令人不快的境地)","examples":["They had not been exposed to most diseases common to urban populations. 他們未曾遭遇城市人口常得的大多數疾病。","A wise mother never exposes her children to the slightest possibility of danger. 一個明智的母親從不會置其孩子於絲毫可能的危險中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is exposed to</b> an idea or feeling, usually a new one, they are given experience of it, or introduced to it. 使體驗 (觀念、情感); 引入 (觀念、情感)","examples":["...local people who've not been exposed to glimpses of Western life before. …以前從未領略過西方生活方式的當地人。"]}]}]},"fulfill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"履行（諾言、義務、職責等），執行（任務、命令等）；實現（夢想、願望、抱負、潛能等）；滿足（要求、需要、條件、期望等），達到（標準）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"fulfill oneself：充分發揮自己的才能，實現自己的抱負"}],"sections":[]},"extend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"延伸；擴大，延長；持續；包括，波及；提供，表示；伸出；使竭盡全力；對……估價；繼承（面嚮物件語言中的一種概念）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something, usually something large, <b>extends</b> <b>for</b> a particular distance or <b>extends</b> <b>from</b> one place <b>to</b> another, you are indicating its size or position. 延伸","examples":["The caves extend for some 12 miles. 這些洞穴延伸約12英里。","The main stem will extend to around 12 ft, if left to develop naturally. 如果讓其自然生長，主幹會延伸到12英尺左右。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>extends from</b> a surface or place, it sticks out from it. 伸出; 凸出","examples":["A table extended from the front of her desk to create a T-shaped seating arrangement. 一張桌子從她的辦公桌前端伸出，形成T型的座位排列。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event or activity <b>extends</b> <b>over</b> a period of time, it continues for that time. 持續","examples":["The normal cyclone season extends from December to April. 正常的颶風季節從12月持續到4月。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>extends</b> <b>to</b> a group of people, things, or activities, it includes or affects them. 包括; 涉及","examples":["The service also extends to wrapping and delivering gifts. 這項服務還包括包裝及遞送禮物。","The talks will extend to the church, human rights groups, and other social organizations. 這些會談將涉及教會、人權組織和其他的社會組織。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a piece of equipment or furniture <b>extends</b>, its length can be increased. 能伸展","examples":["...a table that extends to accommodate extra guests. …一張能伸展以容納更多客人的桌子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>extend</b> something, you make it longer or bigger. 延長; 擴大","examples":["This year they have introduced three new products to extend their range. 今年他們已引入了3種新產品以擴大他們的範圍。","The building was extended in 1500. 該建築於1500年擴建。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>extend</b> something, you make it last longer than before or end at a later date. 延長期限","examples":["They have extended the deadline by twenty-four hours. 他們已經將最後期限延長了24小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>extend</b> something <b>to</b> other people or things, you make it include or affect more people or things. 擴延 (到其他人或物)","examples":["It might be possible to extend the technique to other crop plants. 把該技術擴延到其它農作物上也許是可能的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>extends</b> their hand, they stretch out their arm and hand to shake hands with someone. 伸出","examples":["The man extended his hand: \"I'm Chuck.\" 這位男士伸出了他的手：“我是查克。”"]}]}]},"harden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變硬，堅固；（使）更堅定，更強硬；使變得冷酷無情，使麻木不仁；（使聲音，面孔等）更嚴肅，更嚴厲；變明確；（價格、經濟）變得更穩定；（股票、商品價格等）升水（上漲並保持高價位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>hardens</b> or when you <b>harden</b> it, it becomes stiff or firm. 使變硬; 變硬","examples":["Mould the mixture into shape while hot, before it hardens. 在混合物變硬之前，趁熱將其塑造成形。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an attitude or opinion <b>hardens</b> or <b>is hardened</b>, it becomes harsher, stronger, or fixed. (使) 更堅定; (使) 更強硬","examples":["Their action can only serve to harden the attitude of landowners. 他們的舉動只會使土地所有者們的態度變得強硬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When events <b>harden</b> people or when people <b>harden</b>, they become less easily affected emotionally and less sympathetic and gentle than they were before. 使變得冷酷無情; 變得冷酷無情","examples":["Her years of drunken bickering hardened my heart. 她常年醉酒吵鬧讓我的心麻木了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"強硬化","examples":["...a hardening of the government's attitude toward rebellious parts of the army. …政府對軍隊中反叛分子的態度的強硬化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a rough fabric made from hards 亞麻織物","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone's face or eyes <b>harden</b>, you mean that they suddenly look serious or angry. (表情或目光) 突然顯得嚴峻","examples":["His smile died and the look in his face hardened. 他的微笑消失了，臉上的表情突然顯得嚴峻。"]}]}]},"horrify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使感到震驚，使產生反感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is horrified</b>, they feel shocked or disgusted, usually because of something that they have seen or heard. 使感到驚駭","examples":["His family was horrified by the change. 他的家人對這一變化感到震驚。"]}]}]},"hasten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"促進，使加快；急忙進行，趕緊說（或做）；趕往（某地）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hasten</b> an event or process, often an unpleasant one, you make it happen faster or sooner. 加速","examples":["But if he does this, he may hasten the collapse of his own country. 但是如果他這樣做，他也許就會加速自己國家的滅亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hasten</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are quick to do it. 急忙","examples":["She more than anyone had hastened to sign the contract. 她比任何人都急著去籤那份合同。"]}]}]},"immigrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（從外地）移居，移民；使移居入境"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>immigrates</b> to a particular country, they come to live or work in that country, after leaving the country where they were born. 移居國外; 移民","examples":["...a Russian-born professor who had immigrated to the United States. ...一位生於俄羅斯而後來移居到美國的教授。","He immigrated from India at age 18. 他18歲時從印度移民出來。","10,000 people are expected to immigrate in the next two years. 在今後兩年裡，一萬人有望移民。"]}]}]},"illustrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"加插圖於；說明，闡明；證明，證實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>illustrates</b> a situation that you are drawing attention to, you mean that it shows that the situation exists. 表明; 顯示","examples":["The example of the United States illustrates this point. 美國的例子表明了這一點。","The situation illustrates how vulnerable the president is. 這個情況顯示總統是多麼地不堪一擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you use an example, story, or diagram to <b>illustrate</b> a point, you use it to show that what you are saying is true or to make your meaning clearer. (用例子、故事或圖表) 闡明","examples":["Let me give another example to illustrate this difficult point. 讓我舉另一個例子來闡明這個難點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>illustrate</b> a book, you put pictures, photographs or diagrams into it. 給 (書) 加插圖","examples":["She went on to art school and is now illustrating a book. 她接著上了美術學校，現在正在給一本書畫插圖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"例證","examples":["Here, by way of illustration, are some extracts from our new catalogue. 這裡引為例證的是摘自我們新目錄的部分內容。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(書的) 插圖","examples":["...the world of children's book illustration. …兒童書籍插圖的世界。"]}]}]},"idle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無事可做的；懶惰的；閒置的；空閒的；瑣碎無聊的，毫無意義的；虛張聲勢的，唬人的；（錢）現金儲存的，存於無息賬戶的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"閒混，無所事事；使……停止工作，使閒散；（發動機、車輛）空轉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people who were working are <b>idle</b>, they have no jobs or work. 無事可做的","examples":["4,000 workers have been idle for 12 of the first 27 weeks of this year. 4千名工人在今年最初的27個星期中有12個星期無事可幹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If machines or factories are <b>idle</b>, they are not working or being used. (機器或工廠) 閒置的","examples":["Now the machine is lying idle. 現在這臺機器正處於閒置狀態。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>idle</b>, you disapprove of them because they are not doing anything and you think they should be. 無所事事的","examples":["...idle bureaucrats who spent the day reading newspapers. …整天看報紙，無所事事的官僚們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Idle</b> is used to describe something that you do for no particular reason, often because you have nothing better to do. 無聊的","examples":["Brian kept up the idle chatter for another five minutes. 布賴恩又無聊地閒扯了5分鐘。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You refer to an <b>idle</b> threat or boast when you do not think the person making it will or can do what they say. 虛張聲勢的","examples":["It was more of an idle threat than anything. 那不過是虛張聲勢的威脅。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無所事事地","examples":["We were not idly sitting around. 我們並非坐著沒事幹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"無聊地","examples":["We talked idly about magazines and baseball. 我們閒聊著雜誌和棒球。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an engine or vehicle <b>is idling</b>, the engine is running slowly and quietly because it is not in gear, and the vehicle is not moving. (發動機等) 低速空轉","examples":["Beyond a stand of trees a small plane idled. 在樹叢的那一邊，一架小飛機的發動機空轉著。"]}]}]},"imitate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"模仿，仿效；作滑稽模仿；仿造，偽造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>imitate</b> someone, you copy what they do or produce. 模仿","examples":["...a genuine German musical that does not try to imitate the American model. …一部不試圖模仿美國模式的正宗德國音樂劇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>imitate</b> a person or animal, you copy the way they speak or behave, usually because you are trying to be funny. (常為逗樂) 學…的樣","examples":["Clarence screws up his face and imitates the Colonel again. 克拉倫斯又板起面孔，模仿上校的樣。"]}]}]},"industrialize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）工業化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a country <b>industrializes</b> or <b>is industrialized</b>, it develops a lot of industries. 使工業化; 實現工業化","examples":["Energy consumption rises as countries industrialize. 能源消耗隨著各國工業化而增加。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"工業化","examples":["Industrialization began early in Spain. 工業化很早就在西班牙開始了。"]}]}]},"host":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主人；主持人；主辦者，東道主；寄主，宿主；接受移植組織（或器官）的受體；主機；（某種特別生物的）生存地；許多人（或物）；<古>軍隊；（聖餐儀式中的）聖餅，聖體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"主辦，做……的東道主；做節目主持人；作為主人組織（聚會），做東；（通常收費在與網際網路連線的計算機上）儲存網站"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>host</b> at a party is the person who has invited the guests and provides the food, drink, or entertainment. (聚會的) 主人","examples":["Apart from my host, I didn't know a single person there. 除了主人，那兒的人我一個也不認識。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A country, city, or organization that is the <b>host</b> of an event provides the facilities for that event to take place. (舉辦某活動的) 東道主","examples":["Atlanta was chosen to be host of the 1996 Olympic games. 亞特蘭大被選為1996年奧運會的東道主。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>host</b> of a radio or television show is the person who introduces it and talks to the people who appear in it. (廣播或電視的) 節目主持人","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>host</b> or a <b>host computer</b> is the main computer in a network of computers, which controls the most important files and programs. 計算機主機","examples":["Subscribers dial directly from their computers into the BBS host computer. 使用者直接從自己的計算機撥號接入公告版系統的主機。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>hosts</b> a party, dinner, or other function, they have invited the guests and provide the food, drink, or entertainment. 主辦 (聚會、宴會或其他集會)","examples":["Tonight she hosts a ball for 300 guests. 今晚她做東辦一場有300名來賓參加的舞會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a country, city, or organization <b>hosts</b> an event, they provide the facilities for the event to take place. 主辦","examples":["New Bedford hosts a number of lively festivals throughout the summer months. 新貝德福德整個夏天舉辦了許多個歡快有趣的藝術節。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The person who <b>hosts</b> a radio or television show introduces it and talks to the people who appear in it. 主持 (廣播或電視節目)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or country <b>plays host to</b> an event or an important visitor, they host the event or the visit. 主辦 (活動); 款待 (重要賓客)","examples":["Bush played host to Russian President Vladimir Putin. 布什款待了俄羅斯總統弗拉基米爾·普京。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>host</b> <b>of</b> things is a lot of them. 大量","examples":["A host of problems may delay the opening of the new bridge. 一大堆問題也許會延遲新建橋樑的開通。"]}]}]},"imply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"暗示，暗指；意味著；必然包含"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>imply</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you say something that indicates that it is the case in an indirect way. 暗指","examples":["\"Are you implying that I have something to do with those attacks?\" she asked coldly. “你在暗指我和那些襲擊有關嗎？”她冷冷地問道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event or situation <b>implies</b> that something is the case, it makes you think that it is the case. 意味著","examples":["Exports in June rose 1.5%, implying that the economy was stronger than many investors had realized. 6月份的出口額增加了1.5%，這意味著經濟比許多投資者所瞭解的要強勁。"]}]}]},"infect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳染，浸染；汙染，敗壞；（某種感情或興趣）影響；感染（計算機病毒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>infect</b> people, animals, or plants means to cause them to have a disease or illness. 傳染","examples":["A single mosquito can infect a large number of people. 一隻蚊子就能傳染很多人。","...objects used by an infected person. …一名感染者使用過的物品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>infect</b> a substance or area means to cause it to contain harmful germs or bacteria. 使感染有害菌","examples":["The birds infect the milk. 鳥使牛奶受汙染。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people, places, or things <b>are infected</b> by a feeling or influence, it spreads to them. 使受影響","examples":["For an instant I was infected by her fear. 一瞬間，我被她的恐懼所感染。","He thought they might infect others with their bourgeois ideas. 他認為他們可能用中產階級思想去影響別人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a virus <b>infects</b> a computer, it damages or destroys files or programs. 使 (計算機) 中毒","examples":["This virus infected thousands of computers across the U.S. and Europe within days. 這種病毒幾天之內就使美國和歐洲成千上萬臺電腦中毒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傳染","examples":["...plants that are resistant to infection. …抗感染的植物。"]}]}]},"identify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"認出，識別；查明，確認；發現；證明（身份），表明；認同，理解；認為……和……一致；和（某人）打成一片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you can <b>identify</b> someone or something, you are able to recognize them or distinguish them from others. 識別","examples":["There are a number of distinguishing characteristics by which you can identify a Hollywood epic. 透過其諸多與眾不同的特點,你可以識別出好萊塢的史詩影片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>identify</b> someone or something, you name them or say who or what they are. 確認","examples":["Police have already identified 10 murder suspects. 警方已經確認了10名謀殺嫌疑犯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>identify</b> something, you discover or notice its existence. 發現; 察覺","examples":["Scientists claim to have identified chemicals produced by certain plants which have powerful cancer-fighting properties. 科學家們聲稱已經發現某些植物產生的化學物質有強大的抗癌功能。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a particular thing <b>identifies</b> someone or something, it makes them easy to recognize, by making them different in some way. 是…的標誌; 使易於辨認","examples":["She wore a little nurse's hat on her head to identify her. 她頭上戴了一頂小護士帽，這使她易於辨認。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>identify</b> one person or thing <b>with</b> another, you think that they are closely associated or involved in some way. 認為…密切相關","examples":["Moore really hates to play the sweet, passive women that audiences have identified her with. 穆爾非常討厭飾演觀眾已將她定型的溫柔可愛、逆來順受的女性角色。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>identify with</b> someone or something, you feel that you understand them or their feelings and ideas. 理解; 認同","examples":["She would only play a role if she could identify with the character. 她只願扮演自己認同的人物角色。"]}]}]},"inspire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"激勵，鼓舞；賦予靈感，激發（想法）；使產生（感覺或情感）；引起，導致；吸氣，吸入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>inspires</b> you <b>to</b> do something new or unusual, they make you want to do it. 鼓舞; 激勵","examples":["Our challenge is to motivate those voters and inspire them to join our cause. 我們的艱鉅任務是要激勵那些投票者並鼓勵他們加入我們的事業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>inspires</b> you, they give you new ideas and a strong feeling of enthusiasm. 喚起; 激起","examples":["In the 1960s, the electric guitar virtuosity of Jimi Hendrix inspired a generation. 20世紀60年代，吉米·亨德里克斯演奏電吉他的精湛技巧激發了一代人的熱情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a book, work of art, or action <b>is inspired</b> <b>by</b> something, that thing is the source of the idea for it. 賦…以靈感; 給…以啟示","examples":["The book was inspired by a real person, namely Tamara de Treaux. 這本書是受一個叫塔瑪拉·德特羅的人啟發而寫成的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone or something that <b>inspires</b> a particular emotion or reaction in people makes them feel that emotion or reaction. 喚起; 激起","examples":["The car's performance is effortless and its handling is precise and quickly inspires confidence. 這輛車開起來毫不費勁且精確到位，能很快激起駕駛員的信心。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受…靈感啟示的","examples":["...Mediterranean-inspired ceramics in bright yellow and blue. …源自地中海風格靈感的明黃色和藍色瓷器。"]}]}]},"install":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"安裝，設定；（計算機）安裝（新軟體）；正式任命，使正式就職；安頓，安置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>install</b> a piece of equipment, you put it somewhere so that it is ready to be used. 安裝","examples":["They had installed a new phone line in the apartment. 他們在公寓裡安裝了一根新的電話線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is installed</b> in a new job or important position, they are officially given the job or position, often in a special ceremony. 正式任命","examples":["A temporary government was installed. 一屆臨時政府被正式任命。","Professor Sawyer was formally installed as president last Thursday. 上星期二，索耶教授被正式任命為校長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>install</b> <b>yourself</b> in a particular place, you settle there and make yourself comfortable. 安頓","examples":["Before her husband's death she had installed herself in a modern villa. 在丈夫去世之前她就已經在一所現代的別墅裡安頓了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"安裝","examples":["Hundreds of lives could be saved if the installation of alarms was more widespread. 如果警報器的安裝範圍更為廣泛，成百上千人的生命就可能獲救。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"任命儀式; 就職儀式","examples":["He sent a letter inviting Naomi to attend his installation as chief of his tribe. 他給娜奧米寄了封信，邀請她來參加他就任部落酋長的儀式。"]}]}]},"intensify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"加劇，增強；增強（底片）的阻光度，增加（底片）的厚度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>intensify</b> something or if it <b>intensifies</b>, it becomes greater in strength, amount, or degree. 加強; 強化","examples":["I jump, intensifying the pain in all my muscles. 我跳起來，渾身的肌肉更加疼痛了。"]}]}]},"instruct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"指示，吩咐；教授，指導；聘請（律師），託辦；通知；（法官向陪審團）建議，作說明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>instruct</b> someone to do something, you formally tell them to do it. 指示; 吩咐","examples":["A doctor will often instruct patients to exercise. 醫生將經常囑咐病人要鍛鍊身體。","\"Go and have a word with her, Ken,\" Wojtowicz instructed. “去跟她談談，肯，”沃耶托維奇吩咐道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>instructs</b> people <b>in</b> a subject or skill teaches it to them. 教","examples":["He instructed family members in nursing techniques. 他教家人們護理技術。"]}]}]},"intend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打算，想要；意指，意思是；準備，預留（作某種用途或給某人用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>intend</b> to do something, you have decided or planned to do it. 打算","examples":["Maybe he intends to leave her. 也許他打算離開她。","What do you intend doing when you get to this place? 你打算到這裡幹什麼？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is intended</b> for a particular purpose, it has been planned to fulfil that purpose. If something <b>is intended</b> for a particular person, it has been planned to be used by that person or to affect them in some way. 被用於 (某目的或某人)","examples":["This money is intended for the development of the tourist industry. 這筆錢是準備用於發展旅遊業的。","Columns are usually intended in architecture to add grandeur and status. 柱子被用於建築通常是為了增添宏偉和高貴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>intend</b> a particular idea or feeling in something that you say or do, you want to express it or want it to be understood. 想要","examples":["He didn't intend any sarcasm. 他沒有任何諷刺的意思。","Barzun's response seemed a little patronizing, though he undoubtedly hadn't intended it that way. 巴曾的反應好像顯得有點屈尊俯就，但無疑他不是想要那樣。"]}]}]},"interact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"相互交流，互動；相互作用，相互影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>interact</b> <b>with</b> each other or <b>interact</b>, they communicate as they work or spend time together. 相互交往","examples":["While the other children interacted and played together, Ted ignored them. 當其他孩子們相互交往、一起玩耍時，泰德卻不理他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When one thing <b>interacts</b> <b>with</b> another or two things <b>interact</b>, the two things affect each other's behaviour or condition. 相互作用","examples":["You have to understand how cells interact. 你必須得了解細胞之間是如何相互作用的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"相互交往","examples":["...superficial interactions with other people. …和其他人的表面交往。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"互動","examples":["...experts on human-computer interaction. …人機互動專家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"相互作用","examples":["...the interaction between physical and emotional illness. …生理疾病和心理疾病之間的相互作用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the transfer of energy between elementary particles, between a particle and a field, or between fields","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>interact</b> <b>with</b> computers, or when computers <b>interact</b> <b>with</b> other machines, information or instructions are exchanged. 互動","examples":["...new, simplified ways of interacting with a computer. …與計算機互動的簡化新方法。"]}]}]},"interfere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"干涉，干擾；阻礙，妨害；（未經允許）擺弄，（尤指）弄壞；（光或其他電磁波）相互作用，相互干擾；（指馬）碰踝，絆腳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>interferes</b> <b>in</b> a situation, you mean they get involved in it although it does not concern them and their involvement is not wanted. 干涉","examples":["I wish everyone would stop interfering and just leave me alone. 我希望所有人都不再幹涉我，讓我一個人靜一靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>interferes with</b> a situation, activity, or process has a damaging effect on it. 妨礙","examples":["Smoking and drinking interfere with your body's ability to process oxygen. 吸菸和喝酒妨礙身體對氧的吸收能力。"]}]}]},"interpret":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解釋，說明；口譯；把……理解為；演繹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>interpret</b> something in a particular way, you decide that this is its meaning or significance. 解釋","examples":["The fact that they had decided to come was interpreted as a positive sign. 他們已經決定要來的事實可被解釋為一個積極的訊號。","The judge quite rightly says that he has to interpret the law as it's been passed. 法官很有理地說他必須按照法律被透過時的意義進行解釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>interpret</b> what someone is saying, you translate it immediately into another language. 口譯; 作口譯","examples":["The chambermaid spoke little English, so her husband came with her to interpret. 那個女服務員幾乎不會說英語，所以她丈夫來給她作口譯。"]}]}]},"invade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"武力入侵，侵略；大量湧入，蜂擁而入；侵擾，干擾；擴散，滲入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>invade</b> a country means to enter it by force with an army. 侵入","examples":["In autumn 1944 the Allies invaded the Italian mainland at Anzio and Salerno. 1944年秋，盟軍從安齊奧和薩萊諾侵入義大利大陸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that people or animals <b>invade</b> a place, you mean that they enter it in large numbers, often in a way that is unpleasant or difficult to deal with. 擁入","examples":["People invaded the streets in victory processions almost throughout the day. 幾乎一整天，大街上擠滿了歡慶勝利的遊行隊伍。"]}]}]},"invest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投資；投入（時間或精力）；賦予，授予；<舊>給……穿衣；<舊>包圍，圍攻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>invest</b> <b>in</b> something, or if you <b>invest</b> a sum of money, you use your money in a way that you hope will increase its value, for example, by putting it in a bank, or buying securities or property. 投 (資); 投資","examples":["Many people don't like to invest in stocks. 許多人不喜歡投資股票。","I'm tired of watching you invest our money in insane projects. 我看夠了你將我們的錢投到一些荒唐的專案上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>invest in</b> something useful, you buy it, because it will help you to do something more efficiently or more cheaply. 購買","examples":["The company has invested a six-figure sum in an electronic order-control system which is used to keep stores stocked. 這家公司已經耗資6位數購買了電子定單控制系統來為商店進貨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a government or organization <b>invests</b> <b>in</b> something, it gives or lends money for a purpose that it considers useful or profitable. (政府或機構) 投資","examples":["...the need to invest in new technology. …這種投資於新技術的需要。","Government agencies must invest more funds in training and development programmes. 政府機構必須將更多的資金投入到培訓和開發專案中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>invest</b> time or energy <b>in</b> something, you spend a lot of time or energy on it because you think it will be useful or successful. 投入 (時間、精力)","examples":["I would rather invest time in Rebecca than in the kitchen. 我寧願把時間花在麗貝卡身上，也不願花在廚房裡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>invest</b> someone <b>with</b> rights or responsibilities means to give them those rights or responsibilities legally or officially. 賦予","examples":["The constitution invested him with certain powers. 憲法賦予了他一些權力。"]}]}]},"mislead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"誤導，將……引入歧途"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>has misled</b> you, you mean that they have made you believe something that is not true, either by telling you a lie or by giving you a wrong idea or impression. 誤導","examples":["It's this legend which has misled scholars. 正是這個傳奇故事誤導了學者們。"]}]}]},"lighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"減輕；發亮；變輕鬆"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使變輕，減輕（重量、負擔、壓力等）；使照亮；使輕鬆，緩和"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>lightens</b> or when you <b>lighten</b> it, it becomes less dark in colour. 使變明亮; 變得明亮","examples":["The sky began to lighten. 天空開始變得明亮了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>lightens</b> a situation, they make it less serious or less boring. 緩和","examples":["Anthony felt the need to lighten the atmosphere. 安東尼覺得需要緩和一下氣氛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your attitude or mood <b>lightens</b>, or if someone or something <b>lightens</b> it, they make you feel more cheerful, happy, and relaxed. 使輕鬆; 變得輕鬆","examples":["As they approached the outskirts of the city, Ella's mood visibly lightened. 隨著他們越來越接近市郊，埃拉的心情明顯變得輕鬆了。"]}]}]},"isolate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"孤立，分離；隔離；單獨考慮，區別看待；使（某物質、細胞等）分離"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"被隔離的人（或物）；（用於研究的）分離菌，隔離群"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"孤獨的，孤立的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>isolate</b> a person or organization means to cause them to lose their friends or supporters. 孤立","examples":["This policy could isolate the country from the other permanent members of the United Nations Security Council. 這項政策可能會將這個國家從聯合國安理會的其他常任理事國中孤立出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>isolate</b> <b>yourself</b>, or if something <b>isolates</b> you, you become physically or socially separated from other people. 使孤立; 孤立","examples":["She seemed determined to isolate herself from everyone, even him. 她似乎決心要與每個人，甚至是他割斷聯絡。","His radicalism and refusal to compromise isolated him. 他的激進和拒絕讓步使他受到了孤立。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>isolate</b> something such as an idea or a problem, you separate it from others that it is connected with, so that you can concentrate on it or consider it on its own. 單獨考慮","examples":["Our anxieties can also be controlled by isolating thoughts, feelings and memories. 我們的焦慮也可以透過對思想、感情和記憶分別進行考慮來加以控制。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>isolate</b> a substance means to obtain it by separating it from other substances using scientific processes. 使離析","examples":["We can use genetic engineering techniques to isolate the gene that is responsible. 我們可以用遺傳工程技術將起作用的基因離析出來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>isolate</b> a sick person or animal means to keep them apart from other people or animals, so that their illness does not spread. 隔離","examples":["Patients will be isolated from other people for between three days and one month after treatment. 治療之後，患者將被與他人隔離3天到1個月。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"孤立的","examples":["They are finding themselves increasingly isolated within the teaching profession. 他們發現自己在教育界中越來越孤立。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"隔離","examples":["Hayley contracted tuberculosis and had to be put in an isolation ward. 海利感染了肺結核而不得不被送進一個隔離病房。"]}]}]},"misunderstand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"誤解，誤會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>misunderstand</b> someone or something, you do not understand them properly. 誤解","examples":["I misunderstood you. 我誤會你了。","They have simply misunderstood what rock and roll is. 他們完全誤解了搖滾樂是什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>don't misunderstand me</b> when you want to correct a wrong impression that you think someone may have got about what you are saying. 別誤會 (用以糾正別人對自己所說話的錯誤理解)","examples":[]}]}]},"involve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"牽涉，涉及；包含，需要；使陷入，使捲入；（使）參加，加入；使承擔，使面對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation or activity <b>involves</b> something, that thing is a necessary part or consequence of it. 需要","examples":["Running a kitchen involves lots of discipline and speed. 管理廚房需要講究紀律和速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation or activity <b>involves</b> someone, they are taking part in it. 涉及","examples":["If there was a cover-up, it involved people at the very highest levels of government. 如果有掩蓋真相的行為，它就牽扯到了處於政府最高層的那些人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>involves</b> themselves <b>in</b> something, you mean that they take part in it, often in a way that is unnecessary or unwanted. 使捲入","examples":["I seem to have involved myself in something I don't understand. 我似乎已經將自己捲入了我不瞭解的事情當中。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>involve</b> someone <b>in</b> something, you get them to take part in it. 使參與","examples":["Nasser and I do everything together, he involves me in everything. 納薩和我做什麼事都在一起，他讓我參與所有的事情。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If one thing <b>involves</b> you <b>in</b> another thing, especially something unpleasant or inconvenient, the first thing causes you to do or deal with the second. 使陷入","examples":["I don't want to do anything that will involve me in a long-term commitment. 我不想做任何會使自己做出長期承諾的事情。"]}]}]},"mow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"刈，割（草）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"修剪，割；<美>乾草（或穀物）堆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mow</b> an area of grass, you cut it using a machine called a lawn mower. (用割草機) 割草","examples":["He continued to mow the lawn and do other routine chores. 他繼續給草坪割草，並做其他日常雜務。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the part of a barn where hay, straw, etc, is stored (穀倉內)乾草、麥稈等堆放處","examples":[]}]}]},"lean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（身體）傾斜；傾向於做；倚靠，靠在"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瘦且健康的；（肉）瘦的，脂肪少的；不景氣的，貧乏的；精簡的，效率高的；（混合汽化燃料）空氣所佔比例高的，稀化的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"傾斜，歪曲；瘦肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>lean</b> in a particular direction, you bend your body in that direction. (身體) 傾斜","examples":["Eileen leaned across and opened the passenger door. 艾琳探過身來開啟了乘客門。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lean</b> <b>on</b> or <b>against</b> someone or something, you rest against them so that they partly support your weight. If you <b>lean</b> an object <b>on</b> or <b>against</b> something, you place the object so that it is partly supported by that thing. 把…靠 (在…上); 靠 (在…上)","examples":["She was feeling tired and was glad to lean against him. 她感到累了，樂意靠在他身上。","Lean the plants against a wall and cover the roots with peat. 把這些植物靠在牆上，用泥炭蓋住根部。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the condition of inclining from a vertical position 傾斜","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the part of meat that contains little or no fat 瘦肉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>lean</b>, you mean that they are thin but look strong and healthy. 清瘦而且健康","examples":["Like most athletes, she was lean and muscular. 像大部分運動員一樣，她清瘦而且肌肉強健。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If meat is <b>lean</b>, it does not have very much fat. 少脂肪的","examples":["It is a beautiful meat, very lean and tender. 這是一塊好肉，又瘦又嫩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe an organization as <b>lean</b>, you mean that it has become more efficient and less wasteful by getting rid of staff, or by dropping projects which were unprofitable. 高效的","examples":["...reforms which turned us into a lean and competitive nation. …使我們成為高效率、競爭力強的國家的改革。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe periods of time as <b>lean</b>, you mean that people have less of something such as money or are less successful than they used to be. 貧乏的","examples":["My parents lived through the lean years of the 1930s. 我的父母經歷了20世紀30年代的蕭條期。"]}]}]},"negotiate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指在商業或政治上）談判，磋商，洽談；商定，達成協議；順利透過，成功越過；解決（難題）；議付，洽兌；轉讓（支票、匯票或票據）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>negotiate</b> <b>with</b> each other or <b>negotiate</b> an agreement, they talk about a problem or a situation such as a business arrangement in order to solve the problem or complete the arrangement. 談判","examples":["It is not clear whether the president is willing to negotiate with the Democrats. 尚不清楚總統是否願意與民主黨人進行談判。","When you have two adversaries negotiating, you need to be on neutral territory. 在你讓敵對雙方談判時，你應該採取中間立場。","The local government and the army negotiated a truce. 該地方政府和軍方談判達成了休戰協定。","Western governments have this week urged him to negotiate and avoid force. 西方國家政府本週已敦促他進行談判並且避免使用武力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>negotiate</b> an area of land, a place, or an obstacle, you successfully travel across it or around it. 成功越過","examples":["Frank Mariano negotiates the desert terrain in his battered pickup. 弗蘭克·馬里亞諾駕駛他那輛破舊的敞篷小貨車成功地穿越了沙漠地區。","I negotiated the corner on my motorcycle and pulled to a stop. 我騎著摩托車順利地繞過彎道，停了下來。"]}]}]},"motivate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"成為……的動機，是……的原因；激勵，激發；<南非>申請"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are motivated</b> by something, especially an emotion, it causes you to behave in a particular way. 激發…的積極性","examples":["They are motivated by a need to achieve. 他們被成功的需要激勵著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>motivates</b> you to do something, they make you feel determined to do it. 激起 (某行動)","examples":["How do you motivate people to work hard and efficiently? 你是如何激勵人們努力而高效地工作的？"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有積極性的","examples":["...highly motivated employees. …積極性很高的員工。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"激起行動","examples":["Given parental motivation, we are optimistic about the ability of people to change. 有了父母的激勵，我們對於人們改變的能力很樂觀。"]}]}]},"nevertheless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"然而，不過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>nevertheless</b> when saying something that contrasts with what has just been said. 然而","examples":["Although the market has been flat, residential property costs remain high. Nevertheless, the fall-off in demand has had an impact on resale values. 儘管市場一直疲軟，房價持續偏高。然而需求的減少還是對二手房價格產生了影響。"]}]}]},"obtain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指透過艱難的過程）得到，獲得；<正式>（規則或情況）存在，通用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>obtain</b> something means to get it or achieve it. 獲得","examples":["Evans was trying to obtain a false passport and other documents. 埃文斯當時正試圖獲取假護照和其他檔案。"]}]}]},"offend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"得罪，冒犯；令人不悅，令人不舒服；<正式> 犯罪，違法；<正式> 違犯，違反"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>offend</b> someone, you say or do something rude which upsets or embarrasses them. 冒犯; 使人不安","examples":["He apologizes for his comments and says he had no intention of offending the community. 他為自己的評論道歉，並且說他無意冒犯那個團體。","In the great effort not to offend, we end up saying nothing. 為了儘量不冒犯人，我們最終什麼也沒說。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被冒犯了的","examples":["She is terribly offended, angered and hurt by this. 她被此深深地觸犯、觸怒並傷害了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>offends</b>, they commit a crime. 犯罪","examples":["In Western countries girls are far less likely to offend than boys. 在西方國家，女孩們遠不像男孩們那樣容易犯罪。"]}]}]},"oppose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"反抗，阻礙；與……競爭，與……角逐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>oppose</b> someone or <b>oppose</b> their plans or ideas, you disagree with what they want to do and try to prevent them from doing it. 反對","examples":["Mr. Taylor was not bitter toward those who had opposed him. 泰勒先生並不仇恨那些曾經反對過他的人。"]}]}]},"overcome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"克服，解決；征服，戰勝；使受不了，使無法行動（或思考）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>overcome</b> a problem or a feeling, you successfully deal with it and control it. 克服","examples":["Molly had fought and overcome her fear of flying. 莫莉經過努力克服了對飛行的恐懼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are overcome</b> <b>by</b> a feeling or event, it is so strong or has such a strong effect that you cannot think clearly. 困擾","examples":["The night before the test I was overcome by fear and despair. 考試的前一晚我被恐懼與絕望困擾著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are overcome</b> <b>by</b> smoke or a poisonous gas, you become very ill or die from breathing it in. 燻倒; 燻死","examples":["The residents were trying to escape from the fire but were overcome by smoke. 居民們正設法逃出大火，卻被煙燻倒了。"]}]}]},"occupy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使用（房屋、建築），居住；佔據（空間，時間）；使忙於（做某事）；使一直在想；（軍事）佔領，佔據；（尤指為表示抗議而）非法強佔（建築物）；任職，位居"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The people who <b>occupy</b> a building or a place are the people who live or work there. 佔用 (某建築、某地)","examples":["There were over 40 tenants, all occupying one wing of the building. 有40多位房客，都住在該大樓的一翼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a room or something such as a seat <b>is occupied</b>, someone is using it, so that it is not available for anyone else. 佔用 (座位等)","examples":["The hospital bed is occupied by his wife. 那張病床由他妻子佔用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a group of people or an army <b>occupies</b> a place or country, they move into it, using force in order to gain control of it. 佔領","examples":["U.S. forces now occupy a part of the country. 美國軍隊現在佔領著該國的一部分地區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>occupies</b> a particular place in a system, process, or plan, they have that place. 佔有 (某位置)","examples":["Many men still occupy more positions of power than women. 許多男性仍比女性佔有更多的權力職位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> you, or if you <b>occupy</b> yourself, your time, or your mind with it, you are busy doing that thing or thinking about it. (某事物) 佔據 (某人); 使 (自己、自己的時間、自己的思維) 被 (某事物) 佔據","examples":["Her career occupies all of her time. 她的事業佔用了她所有的時間。","He occupied himself with packing the car. 他忙於裝那輛車。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> you, it requires your efforts, attention, or time. (某事物) 佔用 (某人)","examples":["I had other matters to occupy me, during the day at least. 我有別的事要做，至少白天要被佔用。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> a particular area or place, it fills or covers it, or exists there. (某事物) 佔據 (某區域、某地)","examples":["Even small aircraft occupy a lot of space. 即便小飛機也佔很多空間。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"佔用的","examples":["Keep the brain occupied. 不讓腦子閒下來。"]}]}]},"overlook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"忽視，忽略；（工作、職位、提拔等）不考慮（某人）；（對不良現象等）不予理會，視而不見；眺望，俯瞰；<古>監督；<罕>檢查；<古>用邪惡的眼睛施魔法於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美> 居高臨下的位置，從高處能看到的景色；眺望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a building or window <b>overlooks</b> a place, you can see the place clearly from the building or window. 俯瞰","examples":["Pretty and comfortable rooms overlook a flower-filled garden. 那些漂亮、舒適的房間俯瞰著一個花團錦簇的花園。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>overlook</b> a fact or problem, you do not notice it, or do not realize how important it is. 忽視","examples":["We overlook all sorts of warning signals about our own health. 我們會忽視關於我們健康的各種警報訊號。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>overlook</b> someone's faults or bad behaviour, you forgive them and take no action. 不理會","examples":["...satisfying relationships that enable them to overlook each other's faults. …能使他們忽略彼此過錯的稱心如意的關係。"]}]}]},"overtake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"追上， 趕上並超過（汽車或人）；（發展或增長）超越，超過；突然降臨於，意外發生在；（情感等）壓倒，使難以承受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>overtakes</b> a competitor, they become more successful than them. 超過","examples":["Lung cancer has now overtaken breast cancer as a cause of death for women in the U.S. 肺癌作為一種美國女性死亡原因現已超過了乳腺癌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a feeling <b>overtakes</b> you, it affects you very strongly. 強烈影響","examples":["Something like panic overtook me in a flood. 一種類似恐慌的感覺在一次洪水中壓倒了我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>overtake</b>, or <b>overtake</b> a vehicle or a person that is ahead of you and moving in the same direction, you pass them. 超過","examples":[]}]}]},"portray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"描繪，描寫；（在藝術或文學作品中）描述，刻畫；（在電影、戲劇等中）扮演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an actor or actress <b>portrays</b> someone, he or she plays that person in a play or movie. 扮演","examples":["In 1975 he portrayed the king in a Los Angeles revival of \"Camelot.\" 1975年他在洛杉磯重演的戲劇《卡米洛特》中扮演國王。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a writer or artist <b>portrays</b> something, he or she writes a description or produces a painting of it. 描繪 (事物)","examples":["The film portrays a culture of young people who live in lower Manhattan. 這部電影描繪了在下曼哈頓地區生活的青年人文化。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a movie, book, or television programme <b>portrays</b> someone in a certain way, it represents them in that way. (以某種方式) 刻畫 (某人)","examples":["...complaints about the way women are portrayed in ads. …不滿於廣告中對婦女的刻畫方式。"]}]}]},"overthrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推翻，打倒；背棄，摒棄（規則、觀念或社會制度）；投（球）過猛，投球超過（接手或目標）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"推翻，打倒；投球過遠，投球過猛；（因對方投球過遠而得的）分；（拱門、門廊上方的）鐵藝裝飾板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a government or leader <b>is overthrown</b>, they are removed from power by force. 顛覆","examples":["That government was overthrown in a military coup three years ago. 該政府在3年前的一次軍事政變中被顛覆了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overthrow</b> is also a noun. 顛覆","examples":["They were charged with plotting the overthrow of the state. 他們被控密謀顛覆國家。"]}]}]},"prosper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繁榮，成功；蓬勃發展，健康成長；<古>使成功，使興旺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or businesses <b>prosper</b>, they are successful and do well. 興隆; 成功","examples":["His business continued to prosper. 他的生意持續興隆。"]}]}]},"possess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 擁有，持有；具有（品質或能力）；（尤指邪惡的鬼魅或精靈）纏住，迷住；受（感情）支配，受（感情）影響；瞭解，懂得;"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>possess</b> something, you have it or own it. 擁有","examples":["He was then arrested and charged with possessing an offensive weapon. 他之後被逮捕了並被指控擁有攻擊性武器。"]}]}]},"predict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預言，預計，預卜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>predict</b> an event, you say that it will happen. 預言","examples":["The latest opinion polls are predicting a very close contest. 最新的民意測驗預言將是一場勢均力敵的競賽。","He predicted that my hair would grow back \"in no time.\" 他預言我的頭髮會“馬上”再長出來。"]}]}]},"recite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"背誦，朗誦；詳述，列舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>recites</b> a poem or other piece of writing, they say it aloud after they have learned it. 出聲背誦","examples":["They recited poetry to one another. 他們互相為對方背誦詩歌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>recite</b> something such as a list, you say it aloud. 說出; 口頭列舉","examples":["All he could do was recite a list of government failings. 他所有能做的就是逐一說出政府的過失。"]}]}]},"proceed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始行動，開展；<正式>繼續做（或從事、進行）；（完成其他事後）繼續做某事；<正式>行進，前往；起訴某人；來自，出自"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某個事件或活動的）收入，收益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>proceed</b> <b>to</b> do something, you do it, often after doing something else first. (做完某事之後) 接著 (做另一事)","examples":["He proceeded to tell me of my birth. 他接著給我講了我的出生。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>proceed with</b> a course of action, you continue with it. 繼續進行 (某行動)","examples":["The group proceeded with a march they knew would lead to bloodshed. 這群人繼續進行他們知道會導致流血事件的一次遊行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an activity, process, or event <b>proceeds</b>, it goes on and does not stop. (活動、過程、事件等) 繼續","examples":["The ideas were not new. Their development had proceeded steadily since the war. 這些想法並不新。它們的發展自開戰以來一直在穩步地繼續。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The proceeds</b> of an event or activity are the money that has been obtained from it. (某事件或活動帶來的) 收入","examples":["The proceeds of the concert went to charity. 音樂會的收入給了慈善機構。"]}]}]},"preserve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護，維護；保持，維持；醃製，儲存（食物）；禁止他人捕獵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"果醬，醃菜；（某人或某個團體的）專屬領域，獨有活動；動物保護區，外人禁入的獵地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>preserve</b> a situation or condition, you make sure that it remains as it is, and does not change or end. 維護","examples":["We will do everything to preserve peace. 我們將竭盡全力維護和平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>preserve</b> something, you take action to save it or protect it from damage or decay. 保護","examples":["We need to preserve the forest. 我們需要保護森林。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>preserve</b> food, you treat it in order to prevent it from decaying so that you can store it for a long time. 保藏","examples":["I like to make puree, using only enough sugar to preserve the plums. 我喜歡做果醬，只用足夠的糖來保藏李子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"維護","examples":["...the preservation of the status quo. …現狀的維護。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"保護","examples":["...the preservation of buildings of architectural or historic interest. …對具有建築學或歷史意義的建築物的保護。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Preserves</b> are foods made by cooking fruit with a large amount of sugar so that they can be stored for a long time. 果醬","examples":["She decided to make peach preserves for Christmas gifts. 她決定做桃子果醬作聖誕禮物。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that a job or activity is the <b>preserve of</b> a particular person or group of people, you mean that they are the only ones who take part in it. 獨攬之事; 獨佔的活動","examples":["The making and conduct of foreign policy is largely the preserve of the president. 外交政策的制定和實施很大程度上是總統的獨攬之事。"]}]}]},"publish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"出版，發行（書、雜誌等）；（作家、 音樂家等）發表（自己的作品），使（作品）出版；（在網際網路上）發表；（在報紙或雜誌上）刊登，登載；公佈，公開；頒佈（法令），宣讀（法令，結婚預告）；<法律>向第三方傳佈（誹謗）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a company <b>publishes</b> a book or magazine, it prints copies of it, which are sent to stores to be sold. 出版","examples":["They publish reference books. 他們出版參考書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the people in charge of a newspaper or magazine <b>publish</b> a piece of writing or a photograph, they print it in their newspaper or magazine. 刊登","examples":["Womens' magazines just don't publish articles on the harmful effects of smoking. 女性雜誌就是不刊登關於吸菸有害的文章。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>publishes</b> a book or an article that they have written, they arrange to have it published. 出版; 發表","examples":["Walker has published four books of her verse. 沃克已經出版了4本詩集。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>publish</b> information or an opinion, you make it known to the public by having it printed in a newspaper, magazine, or official document. 公開","examples":["The demonstrators called on the government to publish a list of registered voters. 示威者要求政府公開已登記的選民名單。"]}]}]},"recycle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"回收利用，再利用；（將可回收物品）送入回收加工廠；使再迴圈；再次應用，重新使用（觀念、文章等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"回收利用，迴圈使用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recycle</b> things that have already been used, such as bottles or sheets of paper, you process them so that they can be used again. 回收利用; 迴圈使用","examples":["The objective would be to recycle 98 percent of domestic waste. 該目標是迴圈使用98%的生活垃圾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"回收利用; 迴圈使用","examples":["...a recycling plan. …一項回收利用計劃。"]}]}]},"refresh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使恢復精神，使消除疲勞；使記起，提醒；翻新，使變新；重新整理，更新（網頁）；<美> 再斟滿（飲料）；把（食物）浸入冷水冷卻（或保鮮）；恢復精神；喝飲料，吃點心；補充給養"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）重新整理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>refreshes</b> you when you are hot, tired, or thirsty, it makes you feel cooler or more energetic. 使清爽; 使精神振作","examples":["The lotion cools and refreshes the skin. 潤膚液使皮膚涼爽清新。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>refresh</b> something old or dull, you make it as good as it was when it was new. 使更新","examples":["Many view these meetings as an occasion to share ideas and refresh friendship. 很多人把這些聚會看作是交流思想、重敘友情的機會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>refreshes</b> your memory, they tell you something that you had forgotten. 使重新想起","examples":["He walked on the opposite side of the street to refresh his memory of the building. 他走在街對面，以喚起對這棟大樓的記憶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>refresh</b> a web page, you click a button in order to get the most recent version of the page. 重新整理","examples":["I've refreshed the page a few times and still see no comments. 這一頁我已經反覆重新整理了幾次，但是仍未見到任何評論。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"清爽的; 精神振作的","examples":["He awoke feeling completely refreshed. 他醒來感覺精神完全恢復了。"]}]}]},"refer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提到，談及（refer to）；描述，涉及（refer to）；查閱，參考（refer to）；將……送交給（以求獲得幫助等）；讓（某人）注意；<古>把……歸因於；（考試中）淘汰（應試者）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> <b>to</b> a particular subject or person, you talk about them or mention them. 談及","examples":["In his speech, he referred to a recent trip to Canada. 在他的講話中，他提到了最近的加拿大之行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> <b>to</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a particular thing, you use a particular word, expression, or name to mention or describe them. 稱","examples":["Marcia had referred to him as a dear friend. 瑪西婭把他稱為好朋友。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a word <b>refers</b> <b>to</b> a particular thing, situation, or idea, it describes it in some way. 描述","examples":["The term electronics refers to electrically induced action. 電子學描述的是電力產生的作用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> <b>to</b> a book or other source of information, you look at it in order to find something out. 參考; 檢視","examples":["He referred briefly to his notebook. 他迅速檢視了一下他的筆記。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person who is ill <b>is referred</b> <b>to</b> a hospital or a specialist, they are sent there by a doctor in order to be treated. 把…送往","examples":["She was referred to the hospital by a neighbourhood clinic. 她被一家社群診所送往醫院救診了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> a task or a problem <b>to</b> a person or an organization, you formally tell them about it, so that they can deal with it. 提交","examples":["He could refer the matter to the high court. 他可以把這件事提交高等法院。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> someone <b>to</b> a person or organization, you send them there for the help they need. 介紹","examples":["Now and then I referred a client to him. 我不時地介紹客戶給他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>refer</b> someone <b>to</b> a source of information, you tell them the place where they will find the information they need or that you think will interest them. 指點…查閱","examples":["Mr. Bryan also referred me to a book by the American journalist Anthony Scaduto. 布賴恩先生還要我去查閱美國記者安東尼·斯卡杜託寫的一本書。"]}]}]},"regulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用規則條例）控制，管理；調節，調整；監控，監管；校準，對準（時鐘或其他儀器）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>regulate</b> an activity or process means to control it, especially by means of rules. 控制 (尤指透過規則)","examples":["Under such a plan, the government would regulate competition among insurance companies so that everyone gets care at lower cost. 根據這樣一個計劃，政府會控制保險公司之間的競爭，這樣每個人都能以較低價格獲得保險。"]}]}]},"reflect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"反射（光、熱或聲音）；反映，照出（影像）；顯示，表明；深思，反省；深思後認為，深思後說；引起（某種）看法，帶來影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>reflects</b> an attitude or situation, it shows that the attitude or situation exists or it shows what it is like. 反映; 表現; 顯示","examples":["A newspaper report seems to reflect the view of most members of Congress. 報紙的一篇報導似乎反映了國會多數議員的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When light, heat, or other rays <b>reflect</b> off a surface or when a surface <b>reflects</b> them, they are sent back from the surface and do not pass through it. 反射","examples":["The sun reflected off the snow-covered mountains. 陽光從被雪覆蓋的山巒反射回來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>is reflected</b> in a mirror or in water, you can see its image in the mirror or in the water. 映出","examples":["His image was reflected many times in the mirror. 他的影像在那面鏡子裡映出了很多個。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>reflect</b> to indicate that a particular thought occurs to someone. 想到 (某事)","examples":["Things were very much changed since before the war, he reflected. 從戰爭開始前情況就已經發生了很大的變化，他想到。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>reflect</b> <b>on</b> something, you think deeply about it. 深思","examples":["We should all give ourselves time to reflect. 我們都應該給自己時間來深思。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an action or situation <b>reflects</b> in a particular way <b>on</b> someone or something, it gives people a good or bad impression of them. 使對…產生某種印象","examples":["The affair hardly reflected well on the president. 這個事件很難讓人對那位總統有好印象。"]}]}]},"resemble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"像，與……相似"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person <b>resembles</b> another, they are similar to each other. 像","examples":["Some of the commercially produced venison resembles beef in flavour. 一些商業化生產的鹿肉味道像牛肉。"]}]}]},"resign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"辭（職），放棄（工作或職位）；（使）聽任，（使）順從（~ oneself to）；（國際象棋）放棄，投子認輸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>resign</b> from a job or position, you formally announce that you are leaving it. 辭職","examples":["A hospital administrator has resigned over claims he lied to get the job. 一位醫院主管因為有人聲稱他的職位是騙來的而辭職了。","Mr Robb resigned his position last month. 羅布先生上個月辭去了他的職位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>resign</b> <b>yourself to</b> an unpleasant situation or fact, you accept it because you realize that you cannot change it. 使屈從","examples":["Pat and I resigned ourselves to yet another summer without a boat. 帕特和我將就著又過了一個沒有船的夏天。"]}]}]},"relieve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩解（疼痛或不快的感覺）；減輕（問題的嚴重性）；接替，替下；調劑，排遣； 給（城鎮）解圍，解救；救濟，救援；使某人擺脫（煩人的責任）；免去，解除；上廁所，排便"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>relieves</b> an unpleasant feeling or situation, it makes it less unpleasant or causes it to disappear completely. 緩解; 減輕; 解除","examples":["Drugs can relieve much of the pain. 藥物可以大大緩解疼痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>relieves</b> you <b>of</b> an unpleasant feeling or difficult task, they take it from you. 使解脫; 使擺脫","examples":["A part-time bookkeeper will relieve you of the burden of chasing unpaid invoices. 一名兼職簿記員將使你擺脫追討欠款的負擔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>relieve</b> someone, you take their place and continue to do the job or duty that they have been doing. 接 (某人) 的班; 接替","examples":["At seven o'clock the night nurse came in to relieve her. 7點鐘時值夜班的護士進來接了她的班。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>is relieved</b> <b>of</b> their duties or <b>is relieved</b> <b>of</b> their post, they are told that they are no longer required to continue in their job. 使解除 (職務); 使免除 (職位)","examples":["The officer involved was relieved of his duties because he had violated strict guidelines. 該名軍官因違反了嚴格的準則而被解除了職務。"]}]}]},"retain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保持，保留；儲存，儲存；記住；付定金聘定（尤指律師）；留用（員工）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>retain</b> something means to continue to have that thing. 保留","examples":["The interior of the shop still retains a nineteenth-century atmosphere. 那家商店內部依然保持著19世紀的格調。"]}]}]},"restore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"恢復（某種情況或感受）；使復原，使復位；修復，整修；重新採用，恢復使用；歸還"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>restore</b> a situation or practice means to cause it to exist again. 恢復","examples":["The army has recently been brought in to restore order. 該軍隊最近被調來恢復秩序。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>restore</b> someone or something <b>to</b> a previous condition or place means to cause them to be in that condition or place once again. 使復原","examples":["We will restore her to health but it may take time. 我們會讓她恢復健康，但這或許需要時間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>restores</b> something such as an old building, painting, or piece of furniture, they repair and clean it, so that it looks like it did when it was new. 修復","examples":["...experts who specialize in examining and restoring ancient parchments. …專門研究和修復古羊皮紙手稿的專家們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something that was lost or stolen <b>is restored</b> <b>to</b> its owner, it is returned to them. 歸還","examples":["The following day their horses and goods were restored to them. 第二天他們的馬匹和貨物被歸還給了他們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"恢復","examples":["His visit is expected to lead to the restoration of diplomatic relations. 他的訪問預計會導致外交關係的恢復。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"復原","examples":["I owe the restoration of my hearing to this remarkable new technique. 我把我聽力的復原歸功於這項非凡的新技術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"修復","examples":["I specialized in the restoration of old houses. 我擅長舊房的修復。"]}]}]},"strive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"努力，力爭；鬥爭，反抗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>strive</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>strive</b> <b>for</b> something, you make a great effort to do it or get it. 努力","examples":["He strives hard to keep himself very fit. 他努力使自己保持非常的健康。"]}]}]},"summarize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"總結，概述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>summarize</b> something, you give a summary of it. 總結","examples":["Table 3.1 summarizes the information given above. 表3.1總結了以上所給資訊。","Basically, the article can be summarized in three sentences. 基本上，這篇文章可用3句話概括。"]}]}]},"retire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（令）退職，（使）退休；（專業運動員）退役；（因受傷、生病而）退出比賽；使（擊球手）出局；<正式> 退出，離開（去安靜的地方）；<文> 睡覺，就寢；（陪審團）退庭表決；<正式>（軍隊）撤退；命令（部隊）撤退；停止使用，使報廢；收回（票據，紙幣），使停止流通；清償，付清（債務）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"退休，退隱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When older people <b>retire</b>, they leave their job and usually stop working completely. 退休","examples":["At the age when most people retire, he is ready to face a new career. 在大多數人退休的年紀，他準備要面對一項新事業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an athlete <b>retires</b> <b>from</b> their sport, they stop playing in competitions. When they <b>retire</b> <b>from</b> a race or a game, they stop competing in it. 退役","examples":["I have decided to retire from Formula One racing at the end of the season. 我已經決定這個賽季末退出一級方程式賽車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a jury in a court of law <b>retires</b>, the members of it leave the court in order to decide whether someone is guilty or innocent. (陪審團) 退庭","examples":["The jury will retire to consider its verdict today. 該陪審團今天將退庭來考慮其裁決。"]}]}]},"revise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"改變，修正；修改，修訂（書刊、估算等）；<英>溫習，複習"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"修訂，校訂；（印刷）改樣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>revise</b> the way you think about something, you adjust your thoughts, usually in order to make them better or more suited to how things are. 修正 (對某事的想法)","examples":["With time he came to revise his opinion of the profession. 隨著時間的推移，他開始修正自己對這一職業的看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>revise</b> a price, amount, or estimate, you change it to make it more fair, realistic, or accurate. 調整 (使更合理、實際、準確)","examples":["They realized that some of their prices were higher than their competitors' and revised prices accordingly. 他們意識到他們的部分價格比競爭對手的高，就相應地調整了價格。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>revise</b> an article, a book, a law, or a piece of music, you change it in order to improve it, make it more modern, or make it more suitable for a particular purpose. 修改; 修訂 (使改進、更時尚、更適於某目的)","examples":["Three editors handled the work of revising the articles for publication. 3名編輯負責對要出版的文章進行修訂的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>revise</b> <b>for</b> an examination, you read things again and make notes in order to be prepared for the examination. (為考試) 複習","examples":["Revising for exams gives you a chance to bring together all the individual parts of the course. 考前複習給你一個把課程各獨立部分融會貫通的機會。","Review all the notes you need to cover for each course. 複習所有你需要涵蓋的每門課的筆記。"]}]}]},"strengthen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（情感、決心等）更強烈，使（關係）更加緊密；鞏固（地位），加強（實力）；（貨幣）升值；增強（體質）；為……提供更有力的理由（證據）；（風力或水力）變強；使（法令或處罰）更有效；加強，加固（物體或結構）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> a person or group or if they <b>strengthen</b> their position, they become more powerful and secure, or more likely to succeed. 加強","examples":["Giving the president the authority to go to war would strengthen his hand for peace. 給予總統發動戰爭的權利會加強他對於和平的掌控權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> a case or argument, it supports it by providing more reasons or evidence for it. (提供更多的理由或證據) 支援","examples":["He does not seem to be familiar with research which might have strengthened his own arguments. 他對本來可使他的論證更有說服力的研究似乎不太熟悉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a currency, economy, or industry <b>strengthens</b>, or if something <b>strengthens</b> it, it increases in value or becomes more successful. 走強","examples":["The dollar strengthened against most other currencies. 美元與大多數其它貨幣相比升值了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> you or <b>strengthens</b> your resolve or character, it makes you more confident and determined. 使變得堅定","examples":["Any experience can teach and strengthen you, but particularly the more difficult ones. 任何經歷都可以讓你學到東西，使你變得堅定，那些更困難的經歷尤其如此。","This merely strengthens our resolve to win the pennant. 這只不過堅定了我們贏得錦旗的決心。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> a relationship or link, or if it <b>strengthens</b>, it makes it closer and more likely to last for a long time. 鞏固","examples":["It will draw you closer together, and it will strengthen the bond of your relationship. 它會拉近你們的距離，而且它會鞏固你們聯絡的紐帶。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> an impression, feeling, or belief, or if it <b>strengthens</b>, it becomes greater or affects more people. 加深; 增強; 他的講話加深了他是這個組織主要掌權人物的印象。","examples":["His speech strengthens the impression he is the main power in the organization. 他的講話加深了他是這個組織主要掌權人物的印象。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> your body or a part of your body, it makes it healthier, often in such a way that you can move or carry heavier things. 使強健","examples":["Cycling is good exercise. It strengthens all the muscles of the body. 騎車是好的鍛鍊。它使全身肌肉變得強健。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If something <b>strengthens</b> an object or structure, it makes it able to be treated roughly or able to support heavy weights, without being damaged or destroyed. 加固","examples":["The builders will have to strengthen the existing joists with additional timber. 建築工人們將不得不用額外的木料加固現有的接合處。"]}]}]},"terrify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使害怕，使恐懼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>terrifies</b> you, it makes you feel extremely frightened. 使非常害怕","examples":["Flying terrifies him. 坐飛機讓他非常害怕。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非常害怕的","examples":["He was terrified of heights. 他過去恐高。"]}]}]},"tense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"緊張的，焦慮的；（氣氛或局勢）令人緊張的，引發恐慌的；（身體或肌肉）僵直的，繃緊的；（金屬絲等）拉緊的，繃緊的；（語音，尤指母音）緊的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）（身體或肌肉）繃緊，（使）變得僵直；變得神經緊張"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動詞的）時態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tense</b> situation or period of time is one that makes people anxious, because they do not know what is going to happen next. 令人緊張的 (形勢、時期等)","examples":["This gesture of goodwill did little to improve the tense atmosphere at the talks. 這一友好姿態對改善談判的緊張氣氛幾乎沒起什麼作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>tense</b>, you are anxious and nervous and cannot relax. (人) 緊張的","examples":["Mark, who had at first been very tense, at last relaxed. 馬克起初非常緊張，最後終於放鬆了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your body is <b>tense</b>, your muscles are tight and not relaxed. (肌肉) 緊繃的","examples":["A bath can relax tense muscles. 泡個澡能放鬆緊繃的肌肉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your muscles <b>tense</b>, if you <b>tense</b>, or if you <b>tense</b> your muscles, your muscles become tight and stiff, often because you are anxious or frightened. 使 (肌肉) 繃緊; 繃緊","examples":["Newman's stomach muscles tensed. 紐曼的腹部肌肉繃緊了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tense up</b> means the same as . 繃緊","examples":["When we are under stress our bodies tend to tense up. 當我們處在壓力之下時，我們的身體往往會繃緊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tense</b> of a verb group is its form, which usually shows whether you are referring to past, present, or future time. (動詞的) 時態","examples":["It was as though Corinne was already dead: they were speaking of her in the past tense. 就好像科琳已經死了似的：他們當時在用過去時態談起她。"]}]}]},"tolerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"容許，允許（不同意或不喜歡的事物）；忍受，包容；（對藥物、毒物或環境狀況）產生耐受 ；敷衍，應付"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tolerate</b> a situation or person, you accept them although you do not particularly like them. 容忍","examples":["She can no longer tolerate the position that she's in. 她再也無法容忍自己目前的處境了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>tolerate</b> something bad or painful, you are able to bear it. 忍受 (壞的或痛苦的事物)","examples":["The ability to tolerate pain varies from person to person. 對疼痛的忍受力因人而異。"]}]}]},"transform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使改觀，使變形，使轉化；變換（電流）的電壓；（數）變換（數學實體）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（數，語言學）變換式，轉換句；（數，語言學）轉換規則"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>transform</b> something <b>into</b> something else means to change or convert it into that thing. 使改變; 使轉換","examples":["Your metabolic rate is the speed at which your body transforms food into energy. 你的新陳代謝率就是你身體將食物轉換成能量的速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>transform</b> something or someone means to change them completely and suddenly so that they are much better or more attractive. 徹底改變 (使更好、更有吸引力)","examples":["Industrialization transformed the world. 工業化徹底改變了世界。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"改變; 轉換","examples":["Norah made plans for the transformation of an attic room into a study. 諾拉制訂了將閣樓間改造為書房的幾個方案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"徹底改變","examples":["In the last five years he's undergone a personal transformation. 在過去的5年裡，他完全變了個人。"]}]}]},"upload":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"上載，上傳"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上載（上傳）的內容，上傳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>upload</b> data, you transfer it from a disk to your computer or from your computer to another computer. 上傳","examples":["All you need to do is upload the files on to your web space. 你所需要做的只是把檔案上傳到你的網路空間。"]}]}]},"tap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕拍，輕釦，輕敲；敲出節奏，打拍子；鑿孔裝（龍頭或旋塞）；旋開（桶等容器）放出液體；在（樹）上切口（匯出液體）；（在電話上）裝竊聽器，竊聽；開發，發掘，利用（資源、形勢）；<美> 委任，指定（某人做某事）；<英，非正式> 非法勸說（運動員）轉會（到另一俱樂部）；向（某人）索取， 從……處獲得錢（或資訊）；（使用鍵盤）輸入；給……攻絲；發出輕拍音"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水龍頭，閥門，旋塞；輕拍（聲），輕敲（聲）；竊聽，竊聽器；踢踏舞；（踢踏舞鞋尖或鞋跟上的）金屬片；（軍營裡晚上的）熄燈號，（軍隊的）葬禮號；<英>（女童子軍活動中）篝火晚會上（或集會上）唱的結束曲；<英> 酒吧；螺絲攻；<英>（電） 分接頭；輕拍音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tap</b> is a device that controls the flow of a liquid or gas from a pipe or container, for example, on a sink or on a cask or barrel. 閥門","examples":["She turned off the tap and dried her hands. 她關上水龍頭，把手擦乾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tap</b> is also a noun. 輕敲","examples":["A tap on the door interrupted him and Sally Pierce came in. 輕輕的敲門聲打斷了他，薩莉•皮爾斯進來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Tap</b> is also a noun. 電話竊聽","examples":["He assured us that we were not subjected to phone taps. 他向我們保證我們不會遭到電話竊聽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tap</b> something, you hit it with a quick light blow or a series of quick light blows. 輕敲","examples":["He tapped the table nervously with his fingers. 他緊張地用手指輕輕地敲打桌子。","Grace tapped on the bedroom door and went in. 格雷斯輕輕地敲臥室的門，然後進去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tap</b> your fingers or feet, you make a regular pattern of sound by hitting a surface lightly and repeatedly with them, especially while you are listening to music. (隨著音樂) 打拍子","examples":["The song's so catchy it makes you bounce around the living room or tap your feet. 這首歌很琅琅上口，它讓你在客廳裡跳躍或者用腳打拍子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>taps</b> your telephone, they attach a special device to the line so that they can secretly listen to your conversations. 竊聽 (電話)","examples":["The government passed laws allowing the police to tap telephones. 政府透過了允許警察竊聽電話的法律。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If drinks are <b>on tap</b>, they come from a tap rather than from a bottle. 從閥門流出","examples":["Filtered water is always on tap here. 在這兒，過濾過的水隨時可以從閥門流出。"]}]}]},"elsewhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在別處，去別處"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"別處，別的地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elsewhere</b> means in other places or to another place. 在別處地; 去別處地","examples":["Almost 80 percent of the state's residents were born elsewhere. 這個州幾乎百分之八十的居民是在其他地方出生的。","They were living well, in comparison with people elsewhere in the world. 和世界上其他地方的人們比起來，他們過著舒適的生活。"]}]}]},"translate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"譯，翻譯；（使）轉變，（使）變化；意同，相當於，（把……）解釋為；（以易於理解的方式）解釋，說明；導致，造成；改編，改寫；轉換（計算機程式或語言所含的資訊）；（生）轉譯（信使RNA中的一組核苷酸）；轉移，調動，轉變；<正式>調換（主教，蘇格蘭牧師）的教區；<正式>移葬（聖徒遺骸）；<文>送（人，尤指活人）進天堂；（物理）平移（主幹部分）；（數）平移（幾何圖形）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something said or written <b>is translated</b> <b>from</b> one language <b>into</b> another, it is said or written again in the second language. 翻譯","examples":["Only a small number of Kadare's books have been translated into English. 卡達萊的書只有一小部分被翻譯成了英文。","The Spanish word \"acequia\" is translated as \"irrigation ditch.\" 西班牙語中的“”一詞被譯為“灌溉渠”。","The girls waited for Mr. Esch to translate. 這些女孩們等著埃施先生來翻譯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>translates</b> or <b>is translated</b> <b>into</b> another, the second happens or is done as a result of the first. 轉變","examples":["Reforming the stagnant economy requires harsh measures that would translate into job losses. 改革停滯的經濟需要嚴厲措施，而這將造成失業。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"翻譯","examples":["The papers have been sent to Saudi Arabia for translation. 這些檔案已被送往沙烏地阿拉伯進行翻譯。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a name, a word, or an expression <b>translates</b> <b>as</b> something in a different language, that is what it means in that language. (翻譯過來) 意思是","examples":["His family's Cantonese nickname for him translates as Never Sits Still. 他家人為他起的廣東話綽號翻譯過來意思是“永遠坐不住”。"]}]}]},"violate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"違反，違背；侵犯，打擾；褻瀆，損毀（神聖之地等）；<文>強姦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>violates</b> an agreement, law, or promise, they break it. 違反","examples":["They went to prison because they violated the law. 他們因犯法而入獄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>violate</b> someone's privacy or peace, you disturb it. 侵犯","examples":["These men were violating her family's privacy. 這些男人在侵犯她的家庭隱私。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>violates</b> a special place such as a grave, they damage it or treat it with disrespect. 褻瀆","examples":["Detectives are still searching for those who violated the graveyard. 偵探們還在查詢那些褻瀆了墓地的傢伙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"違反","examples":["To deprive the boy of his education is a violation of state law. 剝奪這個男孩的受教育權是一種違反州法律的行為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"褻瀆","examples":["The violation of the graves is not the first such incident. 褻瀆墓地的事件這已不是第一回。"]}]}]},"furthermore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"此外，而且"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Furthermore</b> is used to introduce a piece of information or opinion that adds to or supports the previous one. 此外","examples":["Furthermore, they claim that any such interference is completely ineffective. 此外，他們聲稱任何此類干涉都是完全無效的。"]}]}]},"largely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很大程度上，主要地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>largely</b> to say that a statement is not completely true but is mostly true. 基本上","examples":["The fund is largely financed through government borrowing. 這項基金基本上靠政府借款資助。","I largely work with people who already are motivated. 我總是與積極性高的人一起工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Largely</b> is used to introduce the main reason for a particular event or situation. (用於說明原因) 主要地","examples":["Retail sales dipped six-tenths of a percent last month, largely because Americans were buying fewer cars. 零售額上個月下降了0.6%，主要是由於美國人汽車買得更少了。"]}]}]},"highly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極其，非常；高度地，高水平地；欽佩地，讚賞地；在高處，地位高"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Highly</b> is used before some adjectives to mean \"very.\" 非常","examples":["Mr. Singh was a highly successful salesman. 辛格先生曾是一位非常成功的推銷員。","It seems highly unlikely that she ever existed. 看來很有可能壓根兒就沒有過她這麼個人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>highly</b> to indicate that someone has an important position in an organization or set of people. 身居高位","examples":["...a highly placed government advisor. …高階政府顧問。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>highly</b> paid, they receive a large salary. 高水平地","examples":["...the 30 most highly paid athletes in the world. …世界30位薪酬最高的運動員。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you think <b>highly</b> of something or someone, you think they are extremely good. 極為讚許地","examples":["Daphne and Michael thought highly of the school. 達夫妮和邁克爾對那所學校評價很高。"]}]}]},"leisurely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"慢悠悠的，不慌不忙的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"從容地，閒適地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>leisurely</b> action is done in a relaxed and unhurried way. 從容的","examples":["Lunch was a leisurely affair. 吃午餐曾是一件從容的事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leisurely</b> is also an adverb. 從容地","examples":["We walked leisurely into the hotel. 我們從容地走進旅館。"]}]}]},"moreover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"此外，而且"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>moreover</b> to introduce a piece of information that adds to or supports the previous statement. 此外","examples":["She saw that there was indeed a man immediately behind her. Moreover, he was observing her strangely. 她看到的確有個男人緊跟在她身後。而且，他還在怪異地觀察著她。"]}]}]},"withdraw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提，取（銀行賬戶中的錢款）；停止提供，不再給予； 退出，不參加；（軍隊）撤離； 脫離（社會），不與人交往；離開；（將某物從某地或位置）抽回，移開；撤回，收回（前言）；（從某物中）拿出；停止提供，召回；退出，返回（至另一個房間）；（因對工作時間、報酬等不滿意而）罷工；取消（許可、邀請或提議）；戒毒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>withdraw</b> something from a place, you remove it or take it away. 移開; 拿走","examples":["He reached into his pocket and withdrew a sheet of notepaper. 他把手伸進口袋，拿出一張便籤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When groups of people such as troops <b>withdraw</b> or when someone <b>withdraws</b> them, they leave the place where they are fighting or where they are based and return nearer home. 使撤退; 撤退","examples":["He stated that all foreign forces would withdraw as soon as the crisis ended. 他宣告危機一結束所有外國軍隊就會撤退。","The United States has announced it is to withdraw forty-thousand troops from Western Europe in the next year. 美國已經宣佈第2年將從西歐撤回4萬軍隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>withdraw</b> money from a bank account, you take it out of that account. (從銀行) 取 (錢)","examples":["Open a savings account that does not charge ridiculous fees to withdraw money. 開立一個取錢時不荒唐地收取費用的儲蓄賬戶。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>withdraw</b> <b>from</b> an activity or organization, you stop taking part in it. (從活動或組織中) 退出","examples":["The African National Congress threatened to withdraw from the talks. 非洲國民大會威脅要從會談中退出。"]}]}]},"lately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"近來，最近；新近卸任，最近離任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>lately</b> to describe events in the recent past, or situations that started a short time ago. 最近","examples":["Dad's health hasn't been too good lately. 爸爸的身體最近一直不太好。","\"Have you talked to her lately?\"—\"Not lately, really.\" “最近你和她談過嗎？”—“最近沒談過，真的。”"]}]}]},"namely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"即，也就是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>namely</b> to introduce detailed information about the subject you are discussing, or a particular aspect of it. 即","examples":["A district should serve its clientele, namely students, staff, and parents. 一個學區應該服務於其主顧，即學生、教職員工和家長。"]}]}]},"nowadays":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"如今，現在"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nowadays</b> means at the present time, in contrast with the past. 如今","examples":["Nowadays it's acceptable for women to be ambitious. But it wasn't then. 如今女人有雄心是可以接受的。但在那時候不行。"]}]}]},"mostly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"多半，主要地；幾乎全部，幾乎所有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>mostly</b> to indicate that a statement is generally true, for example true about the majority of a group of things or people, true most of the time, or true in most respects. 主要地; 大多地","examples":["I am working with mostly highly motivated people. 我正與大多都積極性很高的人們共事。","Cars are mostly metal. 汽車大多是金屬製成的。"]}]}]},"amidst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……之中，在……中間；四周是（等於 amid）；在……氣氛下，在局勢或過程之中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Amidst</b> means the same as . 在...中","examples":[]}]}]},"yearly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一年一次的，每年的；年度的，一年的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一年一次地，每年地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"年刊，年鑑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yearly</b> event happens once a year or every year. 一年一度的","examples":["The two sisters looked forward to their yearly meetings. 姐妹倆期盼著她們一年一度的會面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>yearly</b> to describe something such as an amount that relates to a period of one year. 年度的","examples":["In Holland, the government sets a yearly budget for health care. 在荷蘭，政府設有一個保健年度預算。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yearly</b> is also an adverb. 一年一度地","examples":["Clients normally pay fees in advance, monthly, quarterly, or yearly. 客戶們通常提前付費，或按月，或按季度，或按年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Yearly</b> is also an adverb. 年度地","examples":["Novello says college students will spend $4.2 billion yearly on alcoholic beverages. 諾韋洛說大學生每年會在各種酒精飲料上花費42億美元。"]}]}]},"amid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……過程中，在……中；四周是，被……所環繞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>amid</b> noises or events of some kind, it happens while the other things are happening. 在…當中","examples":["Workers are sifting through the wreckage of the airliners amid growing evidence that the disasters were the work of terrorists. 在越來越多證據證明這些災難是恐怖分子所為的同時，工人們正在仔細檢查那些客機的殘骸。"]}]}]},"overnight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在夜間，在晚上；突然，一夜之間"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"夜間的，只供一夜的；突然的，一夜之間的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"過夜；<美>連夜快遞（貨物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一夜的逗留"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>overnight</b>, it happens throughout the night or at some point during the night. 通宵地; 在夜間","examples":["The decision was reached overnight. 這個決定是夜間做出的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that something happens <b>overnight</b> when it happens very quickly and unexpectedly. 突然地","examples":["The rules are not going to change overnight. 這些規則是不會突然改變的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overnight</b> is also an adjective. 通宵的; 夜間的","examples":["Travel and overnight accommodation are included. 旅行及夜間住宿是包含在內的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Overnight</b> is also an adjective. 突然的","examples":["In 1970 he became an overnight success in America. 1970年他在美國一夜之間成了成功人士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Overnight</b> bags or clothes are ones that you take when you go and stay somewhere for one or two nights. 外出住宿一兩晚的 (包或衣服)","examples":["He realized he'd left his overnight bag at Mary's house. 他意識到他把自己的短途旅行包落在瑪麗家裡了。"]}]}]},"roughly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"粗略地，大約；粗暴地，粗魯地；粗糙地，不精細地"}],"sections":[]},"scarcely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"勉強，幾乎不；剛……（就……），才；決不，一定不"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>scarcely</b> to emphasize that something is only just true or only just the case. 幾乎不; 簡直不","examples":["He could scarcely breathe. 他幾乎喘不過氣來。","I scarcely knew him. 我幾乎不認識他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>scarcely</b> to say that something is not true or is not the case, in a humorous or critical way. 決不","examples":["It can scarcely be coincidence. 這決不可能是巧合。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say <b>scarcely</b> <b>had</b> one thing happened when something else happened, you mean that the first event was followed immediately by the second. 剛…就…","examples":["Scarcely had the votes been counted, when the telephone rang. 選票剛一統計好，電話就響了。"]}]}]},"otherwise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"否則，不然；除此以外，在其他方面；不同地，另外地；以其他方式，用別的方法"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不是那樣的，另外情況下的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>otherwise</b> after mentioning a situation or telling someone to do something, in order to say what the result or consequence would be if the situation did not exist or the person did not do as you say. 否則","examples":["Make a note of the questions you want to ask; you will invariably forget some of them otherwise. 把你想問的問題記下來；否則你準會忘記其中幾個。","I'm lucky that I'm interested in school work, otherwise I'd go crazy. 幸好我對學校作業還感興趣，不然會瘋的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>otherwise</b> before stating the general condition or quality of something, when you are also mentioning an exception to this general condition or quality. 除此以外","examples":["The decorations for the games have lent a splash of colour to an otherwise drab city. 運動會的裝飾為這個平時乏味的城市增添了幾抹色彩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>otherwise</b> to refer in a general way to actions or situations that are very different from, or the opposite to, your main statement. 以不同方式","examples":["Take approximately 60 mg up to four times a day, unless advised otherwise by a doctor. 每天4次，每次約60毫克，或遵醫囑。","There is no way anything would ever happen between us, and believe me I've tried to convince myself otherwise. 無論如何，我們之間不會發生什麼。而且，相信我，我已經努力說服自己了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>otherwise</b> to indicate that other ways of doing something are possible in addition to the way already mentioned. 用別的方法","examples":["The studio could punish its players by keeping them out of work, and otherwise controlling their lives. 電影公司可以透過讓演員無角色可演或其他途徑控制他們的生活，以懲罰他們。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>or otherwise</b> or <b>and otherwise</b> to mention something that is not the thing just referred to or is the opposite of that thing. 或其相反","examples":["It was for the police to assess the validity or otherwise of the evidence. 應由警方來評價證據的有效與否。"]}]}]},"including":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"包括，包含"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"包含；把……列為一部分，把……算入（include 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>including</b> to introduce examples of people or things that are part of the group of people or things that you are talking about. 包括","examples":["Thousands were killed, including many women and children. 數千人被殺，包括許多婦女和兒童。"]}]}]},"despite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"儘管，即使；不由自主地，忍不住地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>褻瀆；<古>輕蔑，鄙視"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>蔑視；<古>激怒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>despite</b> to introduce a fact which makes the other part of the sentence surprising. 儘管","examples":["She has been under house arrest for most of the past decade, despite efforts by the United Nations to have her released. 她在過去10年裡大部分時間都被軟禁，儘管聯合國為她的釋放一直在做努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>despite</b> to introduce an idea that appears to contradict your main statement, without suggesting that this idea is true or that you believe it. 儘管","examples":["She told friends she will stand by husband, despite reports that he sent another woman love notes. 她告訴朋友說，她將支援丈夫，儘管有報道說他在給別的女人遞情書。"]}]}]},"abdomen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人體）腹，腹部；（昆蟲）腹部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>abdomen</b> is the part of your body below your chest where your stomach and intestines are. 腹部","examples":["He went into the hospital to undergo tests for a pain in his abdomen. 他去了醫院接受對他的腹部疼痛進行的各項檢查。"]}]}]},"regarding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"關於，至於"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看待，認為；<正式>（尤指以某種方式）注視，凝視；<古>注意，聽從（regard 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>regarding</b> to indicate the subject that is being talked or written about. 關於; 至於","examples":["He refused to divulge any information regarding the man's whereabouts. 他拒絕透露任何關於那個男人下落的訊息。"]}]}]},"accent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口音，腔調，土音；著重點，強調；重音；（字母上的）讀音符號；點綴，特色"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強調，突出；重讀；以重音演奏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who speaks with a particular <b>accent</b> pronounces the words of a language in a distinctive way that shows which country, region, or background they come from. 口音","examples":["He had developed a slight southern accent. 他有了一點南方口音。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>accent</b> is a short line or other mark which is written above certain letters in some languages and which indicates the way those letters are pronounced. 變音符號","examples":["...an acute accent. …一個尖音符。"]}]}]},"concerning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"關於，涉及"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"讓人不安的，令人擔憂的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"有關，關於；影響；使擔心（concern 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>concerning</b> to indicate what a question or piece of information is about. 關於","examples":["For more information concerning the club, contact Mr. Coldwell. 想了解更多有關該俱樂部的資訊，請跟科德韋爾先生聯絡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>concerning</b>, it causes you to feel concerned about it. 令人擔心的","examples":["It is particularly concerning that he is working for foreign companies while advising on foreign policy. 尤其令人擔心的是，他在為外交政策提供諮詢的同時也在為外國公司工作。"]}]}]},"accomplishment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成就，成績；技能，才藝；完成，實現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accomplishment</b> is something remarkable that has been done or achieved. 成就","examples":["For a novelist, that's quite an accomplishment. 對於一個小說家來說，那是一個了不起的成就。"]}]}]},"acceptance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接受；贊同，認可；容忍；接納；相信，承認"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Acceptance</b> <b>of</b> an offer or a proposal is the act of saying yes to it or agreeing to it. 接受","examples":["The Party is being degraded by its acceptance of secret donations. 該黨因接受秘密捐款而遭貶低。","...his acceptance speech for the Nobel Peace Prize. …他的諾貝爾和平獎受獎演說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is <b>acceptance</b> of an idea, most people believe or agree that it is true. 承認","examples":["...a theory that is steadily gaining acceptance. …一個正穩步得到承認的理論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>acceptance</b> <b>of</b> a situation, especially an unpleasant or difficult one, is an attitude or feeling that you cannot change it and that you must get used to it. 容忍","examples":["The most impressive thing about him is his calm acceptance of whatever comes his way. 他給人最深刻的印象是他對任何事情的從容接納。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Acceptance</b> of someone into a group means beginning to think of them as part of the group and to act in a friendly way toward them. 接納","examples":["A very determined effort by society will ensure that the disabled achieve real acceptance and integration. 社會堅定不移的努力將會確保殘障人員獲得真正的接納與融入。"]}]}]},"accountant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"會計，會計師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accountant</b> is a person whose job is to keep financial accounts. 會計師","examples":[]}]}]},"accuracy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"準確性，精確性；準確，精確"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>accuracy</b> <b>of</b> information or measurements is their quality of being true or correct, even in small details. 精確 (性); 準確 (性)","examples":["Every care has been taken to ensure the accuracy of all information given in this leaflet. 已經採取了一切措施來保證這張傳單上所有資訊的準確。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something performs a task, for example, hitting a target, <b>with</b> <b>accuracy</b>, they do it in an exact way without making a mistake. 準確無誤","examples":["...weapons that could fire with accuracy at targets 3,000 yards away. …那些可以準確無誤地射中3000碼以外的目標的武器。"]}]}]},"acre":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英畝；<非正式>大片，大量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>acre</b> is an area of land measuring 4,840 square yards or 4,047 square metres. 英畝","examples":["The property consists of two acres of land. 這片地產有兩英畝。"]}]}]},"acid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酸；<非正式>迷幻藥；尖刻（或尖酸）的言語（或語調）；質子供體，電子對受體"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"酸的；酸性的；尖酸的，刻薄的；（顏色）刺目的，鮮亮的；（岩石，尤指熔岩）含相當量矽石的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>acid</b> is a chemical substance, usually a liquid, which contains hydrogen and can react with other substances to form salts. Some acids burn or dissolve other substances that they come into contact with. 酸","examples":["...citric acid. …檸檬酸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"酸性","examples":["...the acidity of rainwater. …雨水的酸性。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>acid</b> substance contains acid. 酸性的","examples":["These shrubs must have an acid, lime-free soil. 這些灌木必須要有酸性、無石灰的土壤。"]}]}]},"access":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"入口，通道；獲得的機會，使用權；（對計算機儲存器的）訪問，存取；（情感）爆發，發作；探視權"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"接近，進入；獲取，訪問（計算機資訊）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<美>（電視節目或時間等）對外公開的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>access</b> <b>to</b> a building or other place, you are able or allowed to go into it. 進入手段; 進入權","examples":["The facilities have been adapted to give access to wheelchair users. 這些設施已經過改裝，使輪椅使用者們能夠進入。","For logistical and political reasons, scientists have only recently been able to gain access to the area. 因後勤與政治原因，科學家們直到最近才得以進入該地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>access</b> <b>to</b> something such as information or equipment, you have the opportunity or right to see it or use it. 使用權","examples":["...a Code of Practice that would give patients access to their medical records. …一個給病人們使用自己病歷權利的行業守則。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>access</b> <b>to</b> a person, you have the opportunity or right to see them or meet them. 接觸的機會; 接觸的權利","examples":["He was not allowed access to a lawyer. 他未被允許接觸律師。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>access</b> something, especially information held on a computer, you succeed in finding or obtaining it. 獲取 (尤其電腦資訊)","examples":["You've illegally accessed and misused confidential security files. 你已經非法獲取並盜用了機密檔案。"]}]}]},"acquaintance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"相識的人，泛泛之交；認識，相識；所知，瞭解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>acquaintance</b> is someone who you have met and know slightly, but not well. 相識之人","examples":["He exchanged a few words with the proprietor, an old acquaintance of his. 他跟一位業主，他的一位老相識交談了幾句。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have an <b>acquaintance</b> <b>with</b> someone, you have met them and you know them. 結識","examples":["...a writer who becomes involved in a real murder mystery through his acquaintance with a police officer. …一位透過他同一名警官的結識而捲入一起真正的謀殺謎案的作家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>make</b> someone's <b>acquaintance</b>, you meet them for the first time and get to know them a little. 與某人初次相識","examples":["I first made his acquaintance in the early 1960s. 我在20世紀60年代初第一次認識了他。"]}]}]},"adjective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"形容詞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"形容詞的；從屬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adjective</b> is a word such as \"big,\" \"dead,\" or \"financial\" that describes a person or thing, or gives extra information about them. Adjectives usually come before nouns or after linking verbs. 形容詞","examples":[]}]}]},"adverb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"副詞（修飾動詞、形容詞、其他副詞或整個句子的詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adverb</b> is a word such as \"slowly,\" \"now,\" \"very,\" \"politically,\" or \"fortunately\" which adds information about the action, event, or situation mentioned in a clause. 副詞","examples":[]}]}]},"admiration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"欽佩，讚美，欣賞；讚美物件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Admiration</b> is a feeling of great liking and respect for a person or thing. 欽佩","examples":["I have always had the greatest admiration for him. 我對他一直懷有最大的欽佩。"]}]}]},"adjustment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"調整，校正；（行為、思想的）調節，適應；調節器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adjustment</b> is a small change that is made to something such as a machine or a way of doing something. (對機器、做事方法等的) 調整","examples":["Compensation could be made by adjustments to taxation. 補償可由調稅實現。","Investment is up by 5.7% after adjustment for inflation. 投資在通貨膨脹調整之後增長了5.7%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>adjustment</b> is a change in a person's behaviour or thinking. (對行為、思想等的) 調整","examples":["He will have to make major adjustments to his thinking if he is to survive in office. 他要想繼續任職的話，就得對他的思維方式作大的調整。"]}]}]},"admission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"承認，供認；允許進入（加入），進入權；錄取，錄取人數；入場費；入院治療（檢查）；入場人數；入院病人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Admission</b> is permission given to a person to enter a place, or permission given to a country to enter an organization. <b>Admission</b> is also the act of entering a place. 進入許可; 加入許可; 進入","examples":["Students apply for admission to a particular college. 學生們申請某學院的入學許可。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>admission</b> is a statement that something bad, unpleasant, or embarrassing is true. 承認","examples":["By his own admission, he is not playing well. 據他自己承認，他表現不佳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Admissions</b> to a place such as a school or university are the people who are allowed to enter or join it. 獲准入學者; 獲准加入者","examples":["Each school sets its own admissions policy. 每所學校都設立自己的入學政策。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Admission</b> at a park, museum, or other place is the amount of money that you pay to enter it. (公園、博物館等地的) 門票價格","examples":["Gates open at 10:30 a.m. and admission is free. 上午10:30開門，免門費。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Admission</b> is also used before a noun. 門票價格 (用於名詞前)","examples":["The admission price is $8 for adults. 入場費成人是$8。"]}]}]},"agency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代理行，經銷處；政府專門機構，政府內的局，部，處；（尤指產生某效果的）作用；起作用的事物（或人）;社會行為者獨立選擇的能力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>agency</b> is a business that provides a service on behalf of other businesses. 代理公司","examples":["We had to hire maids through an agency. 我們得透過代理公司僱用女傭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>agency</b> is a government organization responsible for a certain area of administration. 地區政府","examples":["She is calling for a collaboration of local, state and federal agencies to deal with the problem. 她在呼籲地方、州和聯邦等各級政府通力合作來處理這個問題。"]}]}]},"aluminum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋁（化學元素，符號 Al，美國英語拼寫，英國英語作 aluminium）"}],"sections":[]},"alcohol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"含酒精飲品，酒；酒精，乙醇；醇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Drinks that can make people drunk, such as beer, wine, and whisky, can be referred to as <b>alcohol</b>. 酒","examples":["Do either of you smoke cigarettes or drink alcohol? 你們兩個人有人抽菸喝酒嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Alcohol</b> is a colourless liquid that is found in drinks such as beer, wine, and whisky. It is also used in products such as perfumes and cleaning fluids. 酒精","examples":["...low-alcohol beer. …低酒精度啤酒。"]}]}]},"agent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人工智慧領域）智慧體；代理人，代理商；（藝術界的）經紀人；間諜，特工；原動力，動因；劑；（語法）施動者；（美國某些政府部門的）官員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>agent</b> is a person who looks after someone else's business affairs or does business on their behalf. 代理商","examples":["You are buying direct, rather than through an agent. 你在直接購買，而不是透過代理商購買。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>agent</b> in the arts world is a person who gets work for an actor or musician, or who sells the work of a writer to publishers. (藝術界的) 經紀人","examples":["My literary agent thinks it is not unreasonable to expect $500,000 in total. 我的文學經紀人認為預期總共50萬美元並非不合情理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>agent</b> is a person who works for a country's secret service. 間諜","examples":["All these years he's been an agent for the East. 這些年來他一直為東方國家做間諜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A chemical that has a particular effect or is used for a particular purpose can be referred to as a particular kind of <b>agent</b>. 劑","examples":["...the bleaching agent in white flour. …白麵粉中的漂白劑。"]}]}]},"allowance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"津貼，補助；限額，定量；折價，折扣；免稅額；<美>零花錢；考慮到的事情；體諒，原諒；允許，認可；（賽馬）減載量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為（某人）提供津貼；定量供應（物品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>allowance</b> is money that is given to someone, usually on a regular basis, in order to help them pay for the things that they need. 補貼","examples":["She gets an allowance for taking care of Amy. 她照顧艾米是有津貼的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular type of <b>allowance</b> is an amount of something that you are allowed in particular circumstances. 限額","examples":["Most of our flights have a baggage allowance of 44 lbs per passenger. 我們大多數航班的行李限量是每位乘客44磅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your tax <b>allowance</b> is the amount of money that you are allowed to earn before you have to start paying income tax. 免稅額","examples":["Changes for this year include an increase in the tax allowance. 今年的變化是免稅額的增加。","Income taxes skyrocketed and tax allowances were lowered. 所得稅急劇上升而免稅額卻下降了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make allowances</b> <b>for</b> something, you take it into account in your decisions, plans, or actions. 考慮到某事","examples":["They'll make allowances for the fact it's affecting our performance. 他們會將影響我們表現的因素考慮進去的。","She tried to make allowances for his age. 她已經盡力考慮到他的年齡了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make allowances</b> <b>for</b> someone, you accept behaviour from them that you would not normally accept, because of a problem that they have. 體諒某人","examples":["He's tired so I'll make allowances for him. 他累了，所以我會體諒他的。"]}]}]},"amusement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"開心，娛樂；娛樂活動，娛樂設施"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Amusement</b> is the feeling that you have when you think that something is funny or amusing. 興味","examples":["He stopped and watched with amusement to see the child so absorbed. 他停下來饒有興味地看這個孩子如此全神貫注的樣子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Amusement</b> is the pleasure that you get from being entertained or from doing something interesting. 歡樂","examples":["I stumbled sideways before landing flat on my back, much to the amusement of the rest of the guys. 我向側面絆了一下，然後仰面摔倒了，這讓其餘人樂不可支。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Amusements</b> are ways of passing the time pleasantly. 消遣方式","examples":["People had very few amusements to choose from. There was no radio, or television. 那時人們可選擇的消遣方式很少。沒有收音機，也沒有電視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Amusements</b> are games, rides, and other things that you can enjoy, for example, at an amusement park or resort. 娛樂活動","examples":["...a place full of swings and amusements. …一個滿是鞦韆和娛樂活動的地方。"]}]}]},"alert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"警惕的，警覺的；機敏的，敏捷的；意識到，注意到（alert to）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……報警，使警覺；提示，提醒（某人）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"警報，警示；警戒，警惕；（電子裝置的）提示訊號；警戒期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>alert</b>, you are paying full attention to things around you and are able to deal with anything that might happen. 警覺的","examples":["We all have to stay alert. 我們都必須保持警覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>alert</b> <b>to</b> something, you are fully aware of it. 充分意識到的","examples":["The bank is alert to the danger. 該銀行對這種危險有警覺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"警覺性","examples":["The drug improved mental alertness. 這種藥物提高了大腦的靈敏度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>alert</b> is a situation in which people prepare themselves for something dangerous that might happen soon. 戒備狀態","examples":["There has been criticism of how his administration handled last week's terrorism alert. 對他的政府對待上週恐怖主義戒備狀態的方式有批評之辭。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>alert</b> someone <b>to</b> a situation, especially a dangerous or unpleasant situation, you tell them about it. 向…發出警報","examples":["He wanted to alert people to the activities of the group. 他想警告人們注意這個組織的行動。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the alert</b> <b>for</b> something, you are ready to deal with it if it happens. 準備應對","examples":["They want to be on the alert for similar buying opportunities. 他們要準備應對類似的購買機會。"]}]}]},"amateur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"業餘愛好者；生手，外行"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非專業的，業餘愛好的；不熟練的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>amateur</b> is someone who does something as a hobby and not as a job. 業餘愛好者","examples":["Jerry is an amateur who dances because he feels like it. 傑瑞是一位業餘舞蹈愛好者，他跳舞因為他喜歡跳。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Amateur</b> sports or activities are done by people as a hobby and not as a job. 業餘的","examples":["...professional athletes and amateur runners. …專業運動員和業餘賽跑運動員。"]}]}]},"anniversary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"週年紀念（日）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>anniversary</b> is a date that is remembered or celebrated because a special event happened on that date in a previous year. 週年紀念日","examples":["Vietnam is celebrating the one hundredth anniversary of the birth of Ho Chi Minh. 越南正在慶祝胡志明的百年誕辰。"]}]}]},"analysis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分析；化驗分析；心理分析，精神分析；分析報告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Analysis</b> is the process of considering something carefully or using statistical methods in order to understand it or explain it. 分析","examples":["Sporting greatness defies analysis – but we know it when we see it. 運動的偉大無法進行分析–但是我們一看就知道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Analysis</b> is the scientific process of examining something in order to find out what it consists of. 化驗分析","examples":["They collect blood samples for analysis at a national laboratory. 他們收集血樣以在一個國家實驗室做化驗分析。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>analysis</b> is an explanation or description that results from considering something carefully. 分析報告","examples":["Coming up after the newscast, an analysis of the president's domestic policy. 在新聞廣播之後是一個對總統國內政策的分析報告。"]}]}]},"ancestor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"祖先，祖宗；（動植物）原種；原型，雛形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ancestors</b> are the people from whom you are descended. 祖先","examples":["...our daily lives, so different from those of our ancestors. …我們的日常生活，與我們祖先的生活如此不同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>ancestor</b> <b>of</b> something modern is an earlier thing from which it developed. 物種原型","examples":["The direct ancestor of the modern cat was the Kaffir cat of ancient Egypt. 現代貓的直系物種原型是古代埃及的卡菲爾貓。"]}]}]},"apology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"道歉；（因不能赴會的）道歉信；辯護，辯解；勉強（或不適當的）替代物；<非正式>糟糕的例子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apology</b> is something that you say or write in order to tell someone that you are sorry that you have hurt them or caused trouble for them. 表達歉意的言辭","examples":["I didn't get an apology. 我沒有得到道歉之詞。","We received a letter of apology. 我們收到了一封致歉信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you offer or make your <b>apologies</b>, you apologize. (表達) 歉意","examples":["When Mary finally appeared, she made her apologies to Mrs. Velasquez. 當瑪麗最終露面時，她向委拉斯開茲夫人道了歉。"]}]}]},"anxiety":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"焦慮，憂慮；令人焦慮的事；渴望；焦慮症"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anxiety</b> is a feeling of nervousness or worry. 焦慮","examples":["Her voice was full of anxiety. 她的聲音飽含焦慮。"]}]}]},"appliance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家用電器，裝置；<英>應用；消防車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>appliance</b> is a device or machine in your home that you use to do a job such as cleaning or cooking. Appliances are often electrical. (常為用電的) 家用器械","examples":["He could also learn to use the vacuum cleaner, the washing machine and other household appliances. 他還能學習使用吸塵器、洗衣機和其他家用電器。"]}]}]},"appointment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"約會，約定；任命，委派；職務，職位；傢俱，陳設"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>appointment</b> of a person <b>to</b> a particular job is the choice of that person to do it. 任命","examples":["His appointment to the cabinet would please the right wing. 他進入內閣的任命會令右翼高興。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>appointment</b> is a job or position of responsibility. 職務; 職位","examples":["Mr. Fay is to take up an appointment as a researcher. 費伊先生將擔任研究員的職務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have an <b>appointment</b> <b>with</b> someone, you have arranged to see them at a particular time, usually in connection with their work or for a serious purpose. 約會","examples":["She has an appointment with her accountant. 她和她的會計師有個約會。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something can be done <b>by appointment</b>, people can arrange in advance to do it at a particular time. 透過預約","examples":["Viewing is by appointment only. 參觀須預約。"]}]}]},"approval":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"稱許，贊成；批准，許可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you win someone's <b>approval</b> <b>for</b> something that you ask for or suggest, they agree to it. 贊同","examples":["...efforts to win congressional approval for an aid package for Moscow. …為贏得國會贊同對莫斯科的一攬子援助計劃而做的努力。","The chairman has also given his approval for an investigation into the case. 該主席也對此案的調查表示贊同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something has your <b>approval</b>, you like and admire them. 讚賞","examples":["His son had an obsessive drive to gain his father's approval. 他兒子渴望得到他的讚賞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Approval</b> is a formal or official statement that something is acceptable. 批准","examples":["The testing and approval of new drugs will be speeded up. 新藥的檢測與審批將會加速。"]}]}]},"appreciation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"欣賞，鑑賞；感激，感謝；理解，領會；升值，增值；（讚賞性的）演講，文字"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Appreciation</b> <b>of</b> something is the recognition and enjoyment of its good qualities. 欣賞","examples":["...an investigation into children's understanding and appreciation of art. …關於孩子對藝術的理解與欣賞的一個調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>appreciation</b> <b>for</b> something that someone does for you is your gratitude for it. 感激","examples":["He expressed his appreciation for what he called Saudi Arabia's moderate and realistic oil policies. 他表達了對他所稱的沙烏地阿拉伯溫和而務實的石油政策的感激。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>appreciation</b> <b>of</b> a situation or problem is an understanding of what it involves. 瞭解","examples":["They have a stronger appreciation of the importance of economic incentives. 他們對經濟激勵的重要性有了更深的瞭解。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Appreciation</b> in the value of something is an increase in its value over a period of time. 增值","examples":["You have to take capital appreciation of the property into account. 你得將那個房產的資本增值考慮進來。"]}]}]},"aspirin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"阿司匹林（解熱鎮痛藥，化學名為乙醯水楊酸）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aspirin</b> is a mild drug that reduces pain and fever. 阿司匹林","examples":[]}]}]},"applicant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"申請人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>applicant</b> <b>for</b> something such as a job or a college is someone who makes a formal written request to be considered for it. 申請人","examples":["We have had lots of applicants for these positions. 對這些職位我們已有了很多申請人。"]}]}]},"application":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正式申請，書面申請；申請書，申請表；敷用，塗抹；應用，實施；指稱；應用軟體；勤奮，努力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>application</b> <b>for</b> something such as a job or membership of an organization is a formal written request for it. 申請","examples":["His application for membership of the organization was rejected. 他對該組織會員資格的申請被拒絕了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In computing, an <b>application</b> is a piece of software designed to carry out a particular task. 應用軟體","examples":["The service works as a software application that is accessed via the internet. 該業務是一個可以透過因特網訪問的軟體應用程式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>application</b> <b>of</b> a rule or piece of knowledge is the use of it in a particular situation. 應用","examples":["Students learned the practical application of the theory they had learned in the classroom. 學生們學會了課堂上學到的理論的實際應用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Application</b> is hard work and concentration on what you are doing over a period of time. 勤奮","examples":["...his immense talent, boundless energy and unremitting application. …他的巨大天資、無限精力與不懈努力。"]}]}]},"arms":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手臂，胳膊（arm 的複數）；（軍事）武器，軍械；紋章，徽記"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"武裝，配備（arm 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>arms</b> are the two long parts of your body that are attached to your shoulders and that have your hands at the end. 手臂","examples":["She stretched her arms out. 她伸開了雙臂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>arm</b> of a chair is the part on which you rest your arm when you are sitting down. (椅子的) 扶手","examples":["Mack gripped the arms of the chair. 麥克抓緊了那把椅子的一對扶手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> an object is a long thin part of it that sticks out from the main part. (物體的) 臂狀物","examples":["...the lever arm of the machine. …該機器的槓桿臂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> land or water is a long thin area of it that is joined to a broader area. (陸地、水域的) 狹長區域","examples":["...a small area of woodland between two arms of a small stream. …一條小溪的兩條支流之間的一小塊林地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>arm</b> <b>of</b> an organization is a section of it that operates in a particular country or that deals with a particular activity. 部門; 分支機構","examples":["The agency is the central research and development arm of the Department of Defense. 該機構是國防部的核心研究與開發部門。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>arm</b> of a piece of clothing is the part of it that covers your arm. 袖子","examples":["...coats that were short in the arms. …袖子短的幾件大衣。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Arms</b> are weapons, especially bombs and guns. 武器","examples":["Soldiers searched their house for illegal arms. 士兵們為找非法武器搜了他們的家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people are walking <b>arm in arm</b>, they are walking together with their arms linked. 臂挽臂地","examples":["He walked from the court arm in arm with his wife. 他和他妻子臂挽著臂從法院走來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you hold something <b>at arm's length</b>, you hold it away from your body with your arm straight. 以一臂之距","examples":["He struck a match, and held it at arm's length. 他劃了根火柴，然後伸長胳膊舉著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> someone <b>at arm's length</b>, you avoid becoming too friendly or involved with them. 同某人保持一定距離","examples":["She had always kept the family at arm's length. 她一直和家人保持一定距離。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you welcome some action or change <b>with open arms</b>, you are very pleased about it. If you welcome a person <b>with open arms</b>, you are very pleased about their arrival. 張開雙臂 (歡迎)","examples":["They would no doubt welcome the action with open arms. 他們毫無疑問會張開雙臂歡迎這項舉措。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>twist</b> someone's <b>arm</b>, you persuade them to do something. 說服某人","examples":["She had twisted his arm to get him to invite her. 她已說服了他，讓他邀請她。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A person's right to <b>bear arms</b> is their right to own and use guns, as a means of defence. 持有武器","examples":["...a country where the right to bear arms is enshrined in the constitution. …把武器持有權載入憲法的一個國家。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If one group or country <b>takes up arms</b> <b>against</b> another, they prepare to attack and fight them. 拿起武器","examples":["They threatened to take up arms against the government if their demands were not met. 他們威脅說，如果要求得不到滿足就拿起武器對抗政府。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"If people are <b>up in arms</b> <b>about</b> something, they are very angry about it and are protesting strongly against it. 憤怒抗議","examples":["Patient advocates are up in arms over the possible closure of the psychiatric hospital. 病人的支持者們憤怒抗議該精神病院的可能關閉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>arm</b> someone <b>with</b> a weapon, you provide them with a weapon. 武裝","examples":["She'd been so terrified that she had armed herself with a loaded rifle. 她是如此害怕，以至於用一支上了膛的步槍把自己武裝了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>arm</b> someone <b>with</b> something that will be useful in a particular situation, you provide them with it. 用…裝備","examples":["She thought that if she armed herself with all the knowledge she could gather she could handle anything. 她曾以為，如果她用其所能蒐集到的所有知識充實自己，她就能處理任何事。"]}]}]},"aspect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方面，特色；朝向，方位；外表，外觀；（動詞的）體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（行星與另一天體）形成角度關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>aspect</b> of something is one of the parts of its character or nature. 方面","examples":["Climate and weather affect every aspect of our lives. 氣候和天氣影響我們生活的每個方面。","He was interested in all aspects of the work here. 他對這裡工作的各方面都感興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>aspect</b> of a building or window is the direction in which it faces. (建築物或窗子的) 朝向","examples":["The house had a southwest aspect. 這房子為西南朝向。"]}]}]},"article":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文章，論文；物品；條款，條文；冠詞；見習契約，見習期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"見習，簽約做實習生；進行控告；使……受協議條款的約束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>article</b> is a piece of writing that is published in a newspaper or magazine. 文章","examples":["...a newspaper article. …一篇報上的文章。","According to an article in Newsweek the drug could have side effects. 據一篇《新聞週刊》上的文章，這種藥物可能有副作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to objects as <b>articles</b> of some kind. 物品","examples":["...articles of clothing. …衣物。","He had stripped the house of all articles of value. 他已把那所房子裡值錢的東西洗劫一空。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>article</b> <b>of</b> a formal agreement or document is a section of it that deals with a particular point. 條款","examples":["The country appears to be violating several articles of the convention. 該國看來正在違反該公約中的數個條款。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In grammar, an <b>article</b> is a kind of determiner. In English, \"a\" and \"an\" are called <b>the indefinite article</b>, and \"the\" is called <b>the definite article</b>. 冠詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>the genuine article</b>, you are emphasizing that it is genuine, and often that it is very good. 真品","examples":["The vodka was the genuine article. 這伏特加是真品。"]}]}]},"arch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拱門；拱頂；足弓；拱形物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成弓形，拱起"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淘氣的，調皮的；傲慢自大的；主要的"},{"pos":"comb.","zh":"極度的，為首的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>arch</b> is a structure that is curved at the top and is supported on either side by a pillar, post, or wall. 拱形結構","examples":["When she passed under the arch leading out of the park, Mira whooped with delight. 從通向公園外的拱門下走過時，米拉高興地喊叫起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>arch</b> is a curved line or movement. 弧線; 弧線運動","examples":["...the arch of the fishing rods. …釣魚竿的弧線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>arch</b> of your foot is the curved section at the bottom in the middle. (足) 弓","examples":["\"Good girl,\" said Frank, winding the bandages around the arch of her foot. “好姑娘，”弗蘭克說道，一邊把繃帶纏在她的足弓上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>arch</b> a part of your body such as your back or if it <b>arches</b>, you bend it so that it forms a curve. 弓著","examples":["Don't arch your back, keep your spine straight. 別弓著背，挺直脊樑。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"knowing or superior 知識淵博的; 優越的","examples":[]}]}]},"assurance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自信，把握；（人壽）保險；保證，確保"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone an <b>assurance</b> <b>that</b> something is true or will happen, you say that it is definitely true or will definitely happen, in order to make them feel less worried. 保證","examples":["He would like an assurance that other forces will not move into the territory that his forces vacate. 他想要其他部隊不會進入他的部隊撤出的那個領地的一個保證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> <b>assurance</b>, you do it with a feeling of confidence and certainty. 信心","examples":["Masur led the orchestra with assurance. 馬蘇爾很有信心地帶領了那個管絃樂隊。"]}]}]},"assistance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幫助，援助"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone <b>assistance</b>, you help them do a job or task by doing part of the work for them. (透過分擔一部分任務而給予的) 幫助","examples":["Since 1976 he has been operating the shop with the assistance of volunteers. 自1976年以來他一直在志願者的幫助下經營著這家商店。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give someone <b>assistance</b>, you give them information or advice. (透過提供資訊或建議而給予的) 協助","examples":["Any assistance you could give the police will be greatly appreciated. 您能給警方的任何幫助都將受到不勝感謝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone gives a person or country <b>assistance</b>, they help them by giving them money. (透過給予資金而提供的) 援助","examples":["...a viable programme of economic assistance. …一項切實可行的經濟援助計劃。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is done <b>with the</b> <b>assistance</b> <b>of</b> a particular thing, that thing is helpful or necessary for doing it. (某物提供的) 幫助","examples":["The translations were carried out with the assistance of a medical dictionary. 這些翻譯是在一本醫學詞典的幫助下完成的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that <b>is</b> <b>of</b> <b>assistance</b> to you is helpful or useful to you. 有助益","examples":["Can I be of any assistance? 我能有所幫助嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>come to</b> someone's <b>assistance</b>, you take action to help them. 來援助某人","examples":["They are appealing to the world community to come to Jordan's assistance. 他們正呼籲國際社會來援助約旦。"]}]}]},"assignment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"作業，任務；（工作等的）分配，指派；（財產、權利的）轉讓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>assignment</b> is a task or piece of work that you are given to do, especially as part of your job or studies. 任務; 作業","examples":["The assessment for the course involves written assignments and practical tests. 這門課程的評估包括各種書面作業和實踐測試。"]}]}]},"atom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"原子；微量，極小量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>atom</b> is the smallest amount of a substance that can take part in a chemical reaction. 原子","examples":["...the news that Einstein's former colleagues Otto Hahn and Fritz Strassmann had split the atom. …愛因斯坦的前同事奧托·哈恩和弗裡茨·斯特拉斯曼曾分裂了原子的訊息。"]}]}]},"assembly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"議會，代表大會；集會，集會者；裝配，組裝；（計算機）彙編"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>assembly</b> is a large group of people who meet regularly to make decisions or laws for a particular region or country. 議會","examples":["...the campaign for the first free election to the National Assembly. …為首次自由選舉入國民議會而進行的運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>assembly</b> is a group of people gathered together for a particular purpose. 集會者","examples":["He waited until complete quiet settled on the assembly. 他等到集會者完全安靜下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you refer to rights of <b>assembly</b> or restrictions on <b>assembly</b>, you are referring to the legal right that people have to gather together. 集會","examples":["The U.S. Constitution guarantees free speech, freedom of assembly and equal protection. 美國憲法保證自由言論、集會自由和平等保護權。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>assembly</b> of a machine, device, or object is the process of fitting its different parts together. 組裝","examples":["For the rest of the day, he worked on the assembly of an explosive device. 在那天餘下的時間裡，他在進行一個爆炸裝置的組裝。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a school, an <b>assembly</b> is a gathering of all the teachers and students for a particular purpose. (學校師生的) 大會","examples":["Recently named the nation's top girls' basketball player, she will be honoured this morning at a school assembly. 最近被命名為全國頂級女子籃球運動員的她將於今天上午在學校大會上被表彰。"]}]}]},"association":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"協會，社團，聯盟；交往，聯合；聯絡，因果關係；聯想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>association</b> is an official group of people who have the same job, aim, or interest. 協會","examples":["...the National Basketball Association. …全國籃球協會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>association</b> <b>with</b> a person or a thing such as an organization is the connection that you have with them. (與某人、某物的) 關聯","examples":["...the company's six-year association with retailer J.C. Penney Co. …這家公司與零售商彭尼公司6年的業務往來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something has particular <b>associations</b> for you, it is connected in your mind with a particular memory, idea, or feeling. (與某記憶、觀念、情感的) 關聯","examples":["He has a shelf full of things, each of which has associations for him. 他有一個擺滿了東西的架子，每一樣都與他的內心世界有關聯。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in association with</b> someone else, you do it together. 與…聯合","examples":["The changes I instigated in association with the board 18 months ago were because I love this company. 18個月前我聯合董事會發起的這些變革是出於我愛這家公司。"]}]}]},"associate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聯想，聯絡；支援，同意；交往，（尤指）混在一起"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同事，夥伴；副學士，準學士；副職，副手；準會員；聯想"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"副的，準的，非正式的；聯合的，有關連的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>associate</b> someone or something <b>with</b> another thing, the two are connected in your mind. 將 (…和…) 聯絡起來","examples":["Through science we've got the idea of associating progress with the future. 透過科學我們已有了將進步與未來聯絡起來的觀念。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are associated with</b> a particular organization, cause, or point of view, or if you <b>associate</b> <b>yourself with</b> it, you support it publicly. 使 (某人與某組織、事業、觀點等) 有關聯","examples":["I haven't been associated with the project over the last year. 我過去一年不曾跟這個專案有關聯。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is associating with</b> another person or group of people, you mean they are spending a lot of time in the company of people you do not approve of. (與某個或某群人) 混在一起","examples":["What would they think if they knew that they were associating with a murderer? 如果他們知道了他們正與一個殺人犯打成一片，他們會怎麼想？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>associates</b> are the people you are closely connected with, especially at work. (尤指工作中的) 夥伴","examples":["...the restaurant owner's business associates. …該餐館老闆的商業夥伴們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>associate</b> is a retail worker who does not have previous experience or qualifications. 準零售工","examples":["Be sure to get help from the sales associates before buying. 在購買前一定要得到準銷售人員的幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Associate</b> is used before a rank or title to indicate a slightly different or lower rank or title. 副的 (用在級別或頭銜前，表示稍有不同或略低的)","examples":["Mr. Lin is associate director of the Institute. 林先生是該研究所的副主任。"]}]}]},"atmosphere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（包圍地球或其他行星的）大氣，大氣層；（房間或其他場所內的）空氣；氣氛，環境；情調，感染力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A planet's <b>atmosphere</b> is the layer of air or other gases around it. (行星的) 大氣層","examples":["The shuttle Columbia will re-enter Earth's atmosphere tomorrow morning. 哥倫比亞號太空梭將在明天上午重進地球大氣層。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>atmosphere</b> of a place is the air that you breathe there. (某地的) 空氣","examples":["These gases pollute the atmosphere of towns and cities. 這些氣體汙染城鎮的空氣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>atmosphere</b> of a place is the general impression that you get of it. 氣氛","examples":["There's still an atmosphere of great hostility and tension in the city. 在這座城市裡依然有一種極其敵對和緊張的氣氛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a place or an event has <b>atmosphere</b>, it is interesting. 神韻","examples":["The old harbour is still full of atmosphere and well worth visiting. 舊港口依然充滿神韻，很值得參觀。"]}]}]},"attachment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"附加裝置，附屬物；（郵件）附件；檔案附件；喜歡，依戀；（臨時的）隸屬，委派；信念，擁護；連線，連線物；扣押"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>attachment</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you are fond of them or loyal to them. 愛慕; 忠誠","examples":["As a teenager she formed a strong attachment to one of her teachers. 十幾歲時她曾對自己的一位老師產生了強烈的愛慕之情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>attachment</b> is a device that can be fixed onto a machine in order to enable it to do different jobs. (機器的) 附加裝置","examples":["Some models come with attachments for dusting. 一些模型帶有附加的除塵裝置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In computing, an <b>attachment</b> is a file which is attached separately to a message that you send to someone. (電子郵件的) 附件","examples":["When you send an e-mail you can also send a file as an attachment and that file can be a graphic, a program, a sound or whatever. 當傳送電子郵件時，你還可以把一份檔案作為附件傳送，該檔案可以是圖片、程式、或聲音檔案等。"]}]}]},"autobiography":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自傳；自傳體寫作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>autobiography</b> is an account of your life, which you write yourself. 自傳","examples":["He published his autobiography last autumn. 他去年秋天出版了他的自傳。"]}]}]},"backpack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"揹包，行囊；揹負裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"揹包旅行；挑運，把……放入揹包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>backpack</b> is a bag with straps that go over your shoulders, so that you can carry things on your back when you are walking or climbing. 雙肩包","examples":[]}]}]},"attraction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"有吸引力的事物；吸引力；（兩性間的）吸引；（物體間的）引力；（錯誤的）形態同化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Attraction</b> is a feeling of liking someone, and often of being sexually interested in them. 吸引 (常指異性)","examples":["Our level of attraction to the opposite sex has more to do with our inner confidence than how we look. 我們對異性的吸引程度更多地與我們內心的自信有關，而不是外貌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>attraction</b> is a feature that makes something interesting or desirable. 吸引力","examples":["...the attractions of living on the waterfront. …濱水生活的吸引力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>attraction</b> is something that people can go to for interest or enjoyment, for example, a famous building. 遊覽勝地","examples":["The walled city is an important tourist attraction. 這座城牆圍繞的城市是一個重要的旅遊勝地。"]}]}]},"ballet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芭蕾舞劇；芭蕾舞團；芭蕾舞；芭蕾舞曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ballet</b> is a type of very skilled and artistic dancing with carefully planned movements. 芭蕾舞","examples":["I trained as a ballet dancer. 我受過做芭蕾舞演員的訓練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ballet</b> is an artistic work that is performed by ballet dancers. 芭蕾舞劇","examples":["The performance will include the premiere of three new ballets. 這次演出將包括3部新芭蕾舞劇的首演。"]}]}]},"bankrupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"破產的，倒閉的；淪喪的，無價值的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使破產，使極其貧困"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"破產者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People or organizations that go <b>bankrupt</b> do not have enough money to pay their debts. 破產的","examples":["If the firm cannot sell its products, it will go bankrupt. 如果這家公司無法銷售其產品，它將面臨破產。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>bankrupt</b>, you are emphasizing that it lacks any value or worth. 無價值的","examples":["He really thinks that European civilization is morally bankrupt. 他確實認為歐洲文明在道德上全無價值。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bankrupt</b> a person or organization means to make them go bankrupt. 使破產","examples":["The move to the market nearly bankrupted the firm and its director. 走向市場的行動幾乎使這家公司及其董事破產。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bankrupt</b> is a person who has been declared bankrupt by a court of law. 破產者","examples":["In total, 80% of bankrupts are men. 總體來看，有80%的破產者為男性。"]}]}]},"authority":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專家，權威人士；行政管理機構；權力，許可權；權威，威信；許可，授權；當局，官方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>authorities</b> are the people who have the power to make decisions and to make sure that laws are obeyed. 當局","examples":["This provided a pretext for the authorities to cancel the elections. 這給當局提供了一個取消選舉的藉口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>authority</b> is an official organization or government department that has the power to make decisions. 官方機構","examples":["...the Philadelphia Parking Authority. …費城停車管理局。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is an <b>authority on</b> a particular subject knows a lot about it. (某一學科的) 權威人士","examples":["He's universally recognized as an authority on Russian affairs. 他被公認為是俄羅斯事務的權威。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Authority</b> is the right to command and control other people. 職權","examples":["A family member in a family business has a position of authority and power. 家庭成員在家族企業中都有職有權。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone has <b>authority</b>, they have a quality which makes other people take notice of what they say. 威信","examples":["He had no natural authority and no capacity for imposing his will on others. 他天生沒有威信，也沒有將其意志強加於他人的能力。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Authority</b> is official permission to do something. 官方的許可","examples":["The prison governor has refused to let him go, saying he must first be given authority from his own superiors. 監獄長已拒絕釋放他，說他必須首先得到上級的許可。"]}]}]},"beak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鳥嘴，喙；鷹鈎鼻，尖鼻；<舊>法官，男教師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A bird's <b>beak</b> is the hard curved or pointed part of its mouth. 喙","examples":["...a black bird with a yellow beak. …一隻有著黃喙的黑鳥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person's nose, esp one that is large, pointed, or hooked 鷹鉤鼻","examples":[]}]}]},"barrier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"障礙，壁壘；障礙物，關卡；分界線，屏障；大關，界限"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barrier</b> is something such as a rule, law, or policy that makes it difficult or impossible for something to happen or be achieved. 障礙","examples":["Duties and taxes are the most obvious barrier to free trade. 關稅及其他各種稅是自由貿易最明顯的障礙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>barrier</b> is a problem that prevents two people or groups from agreeing, communicating, or working with each other. 障礙; 隔閡","examples":["There is no reason why love shouldn't cross the age barrier. 愛情沒有理由不應跨越年齡障礙。","She had been waiting for Simon to break down the barrier between them. 她一直在等著西蒙來破除他們之間的隔閡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>barrier</b> is something such as a fence or wall that is put in place to prevent people from moving easily from one area to another. 柵欄; 圍牆","examples":["The demonstrators broke through heavy police barriers. 示威者們衝破了警方的重重關卡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>barrier</b> is an object or layer that physically prevents something from moving from one place to another. 屏障","examples":["A severe storm destroyed a natural barrier between the house and the lake. 一場猛烈的暴風雨摧毀了房屋和湖泊之間的天然屏障。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to a particular number or amount as a <b>barrier</b> when you think it is significant, because it is difficult or unusual to go above it. (數量) 大關","examples":["They are fearful that unemployment will soon break the barrier of three million. 他們擔心失業人數不久將突破300萬大關。"]}]}]},"basin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盆；洗滌槽；流域；盆地，海盆；內港，內灣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>basin</b> is a large or deep bowl that you use for holding liquids. 盆","examples":["Water dripped into a basin at the back of the room. 水滴入房間後面的一個盆裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>basin</b> <b>of</b> something such as water is an amount of it that is contained in a basin. 一盆之量","examples":["We were given a basin of water to wash our hands in. 我們得到了一盆水洗手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>basin</b> is a sink. 洗滌槽","examples":["...a cast-iron bathtub with a matching basin. …一個配有洗滌槽的鑄鐵浴缸。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>basin</b> of a large river is the area of land around it from which streams run down into it. 流域","examples":["...the Amazon basin. …亞馬孫流域"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In geography, a <b>basin</b> is a particular region of the world where the Earth's surface is lower than in other places. 盆地","examples":["...countries around the Pacific Basin. …太平洋盆地周圍的國家。"]}]}]},"battery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電池，蓄電池；一組，一系列；炮組，排炮；毆打罪；（棒球隊的）投手和接球手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"籠養的，層架式養殖的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Batteries</b> are small devices that provide the power for electrical items such as radios and children's toys. 電池","examples":["The shavers come complete with batteries. 這些電動剃鬚刀帶有電池。","...a battery-operated cassette player. …用電池的磁帶放音機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A car <b>battery</b> is a rectangular box containing acid that is found in a car engine. It provides the electricity needed to start the car. (汽車) 蓄電池","examples":["...a car with a dead battery. …一輛蓄電池沒電了的汽車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Battery</b> is the crime of hitting or beating someone. 毆打罪","examples":["Lawrence punched a man in a Los Angeles nightclub and was charged with battery. 勞倫斯在洛杉磯的一家夜總會里打了人，結果被指控犯了毆打罪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>battery</b> <b>of</b> equipment such as guns, lights, or computers is a large set of it kept together in one place. 一排; 一套","examples":["They stopped beside a battery of abandoned guns. 他們停在一排廢棄的大炮旁。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>battery</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a very large number of them. 一大群; 一組","examples":["...a battery of journalists and television cameras. …一大群記者和電視攝像機。"]}]}]},"bargain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"便宜貨，減價品；協議，交易"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"討價還價，談判"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is a <b>bargain</b> is good value, usually because it has been sold at a lower price than normal. 物美價廉的商品","examples":["At this price the wine is a bargain. 以這個價格，這葡萄酒算是物美價廉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bargain</b> is an agreement, especially a formal business agreement, in which two people or groups agree what each of them will do, pay, or receive. 協議 (尤指正式商業合同)","examples":["I'll make a bargain with you. I'll play hostess if you'll include Matthew in your guest list. 我想和你達成個協議：如果你把馬修列入客人名單，我就充當女主人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"談判; 討價還價","examples":["The government has called for sensible pay bargaining. 政府已呼籲進行理性的工資談判。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>bargain</b> <b>with</b> each other, they discuss what each of them will do, pay, or receive. 談判; 討價還價","examples":["They prefer to bargain with individual clients, for cash. 他們更願意同個人客戶洽談，做現金交易。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>into the bargain</b> or <b>in the bargain</b> when mentioning an additional quantity, feature, fact, or action, to emphasize the fact that it is also involved. 而且還","examples":["This machine is designed to save you effort, and keep your work surfaces tidy into the bargain. 這種機器是為了省力而設計的，而且它還會使你的工作臺面保持整潔。"]}]}]},"biography":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳記，傳記文學；生平"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>biography</b> of someone is an account of their life, written by someone else. 傳記","examples":["...recent biographies of Stalin. …近年的斯大林傳記。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Biography</b> is the branch of literature which deals with accounts of people's lives. 傳記文學","examples":["...a volume of biography and criticism. …一冊傳記文學與評論。"]}]}]},"behavior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為，舉止，態度；（機器、物質等在特定條件下的）效能，性狀，反應；（心理學）有機體對刺激的可觀察反應或活動"}],"sections":[]},"biology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物學；生命機理，作用方式；生理習性；（某個地區的）生物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Biology</b> is the science which is concerned with the study of living things. 生物學","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"生物學家","examples":["...biologists studying the fruit fly. …研究果蠅的生物學家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>biology</b> of a living thing is the way in which its body or cells behave. (機體、細胞的) 作用方式","examples":["The biology of these diseases is terribly complicated. 這些疾病的作用方式極其複雜。"]}]}]},"blade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"刀片，刀刃；（草，小麥等的）葉片；（船或飛機螺旋槳的）槳葉；（溜冰鞋的）冰刀；<舊>花花公子，時髦男士；<文>劍；肩胛骨，肩胛；舌身"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>滑旱冰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>blade</b> of a knife, axe, or saw is the edge, which is used for cutting. 刃","examples":["Many of them will have sharp blades. 他們很多都會有鋒利的刃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>blades</b> of a propeller are the long, flat parts that turn around. (螺旋槳的) 槳葉","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>blade</b> of an oar is the thin flat part that you put into the water. (船槳的) 槳葉","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>blade</b> of grass is a single piece of grass. 草葉","examples":["Brian began to tear blades of grass from between the bricks. 布賴恩開始從磚縫兒裡拔草葉。"]}]}]},"beam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"梁，橫樑；<非正式>臀圍；光線，光柱；喜色，笑容；（體操的）平衡木"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"定向發出（無線電訊號）；（光，光源）照耀；喜笑顏開，面露喜色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is beaming</b>, you mean that they have a big smile on their face because they are happy, pleased, or proud about something. 綻開笑容","examples":["Frances beamed at her friend with undisguised admiration. 弗朗西絲用毫不掩飾的羨慕的神情朝她的朋友們綻開了笑容。","\"Welcome back,\" she beamed. “歡迎回來，”她笑容滿面地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If radio signals or television pictures <b>are beamed</b> somewhere, they are sent there by means of electronic equipment. 播送","examples":["The interview was beamed live across America. 那場訪談同步播送至全美。","The Sci-Fi Channel began beaming into 10 million American homes this week. 科幻頻道本週已經開始播送到1000萬個美國家庭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beam</b> is a line of energy, radiation, or particles sent in a particular direction. (能量、輻射、粒子) 束","examples":["...high-energy laser beams. …高能鐳射束。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>beam</b> <b>of</b> light is a line of light that shines from an object such as a lamp. (光) 束","examples":["A beam of light slices through the darkness. 一道光束劃破了黑暗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>beam</b> is a long thick bar of wood, metal, or concrete, especially one used to support the roof of a building. 梁","examples":["The ceilings are supported by oak beams. 天花板由橡木橫樑支撐著。"]}]}]},"blessing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幸事，福祉；支援，贊同；上帝的恩寵，祝福；禱告，祈禱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"求上帝保佑，祝福；祝聖，使聖潔；讚美上帝（bless 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blessing</b> is something good that you are grateful for. 幸事","examples":["Rivers are a blessing for an agricultural country. 河流是農業國的福祉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is done with someone's <b>blessing</b>, it is done with their approval and support. 同意; 支援","examples":["With the blessing of the White House, a group of Democrats in Congress is meeting to find additional budget cuts. 經白宮同意，國會中的一組民主黨人正開會尋求進一步削減預算。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>blessing</b> is a prayer asking God to look kindly upon the people who are present or the event that is taking place. 祈福禱告","examples":["The Reverend Chris Long led the prayers and pronounced the blessing. 克里斯·朗牧師帶領禱告並宣講了祈福禱詞。"]}]}]},"blend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）混合，調和；（使）協調，融合；調製，配製"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"混合物；交融，融合；混合詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blend</b> substances together or if they <b>blend</b>, you mix them together so that they become one substance. 混合","examples":["Blend the butter with the sugar and beat until light and creamy. 把黃油和糖混合起來，快速攪拌成鬆軟的糊狀。","Blend the ingredients until you have a smooth cream. 把這些配料調成均勻的糊狀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When colours, sounds, or styles <b>blend</b>, they come together or are combined in a pleasing way. (色彩、聲音或風格) 交融","examples":["You could paint the walls and ceilings the same colour so they blend together. 你可以把這些牆和天花板漆成相同的顏色，這樣它們就渾然一體。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blend</b> <b>of</b> things is a mixture or combination of them that is useful or pleasant. 調配; 美妙的結合","examples":["The public areas offer a subtle blend of traditional charm with modern amenities. 這些公共場所表現出對傳統魅力與現代設施的巧妙結合。","...a blend of wine and sparkling water. …葡萄酒與汽水的調配。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a word formed by joining together the beginning and the end of two other words  (用另外兩個詞的首尾連線而成的)混合詞; “早午餐”是“早餐”與“午餐”的混合詞。","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blend</b> ideas, policies, or styles, you use them together in order to achieve something. 融合 (不同的思想、政策或風格)","examples":["His vision is to blend Christianity with \"the wisdom of all world religions.\" 他的夢想是把世界上各種宗教的智慧融入到基督教。"]}]}]},"blink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"眨（眼）；（燈）閃爍；表示驚訝，顯出不安；退讓，讓步"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"眨眼；片刻的猶豫，舉棋不定；（光的）瞬間閃爍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>blink</b> or when you <b>blink</b> your eyes, you shut your eyes and very quickly open them again. 眨 (眼睛)","examples":["Kathryn blinked and forced a smile. 凱瑟琳眨了眨眼，擠出了一絲微笑。","She was blinking her eyes rapidly. 她一直在快速地眨眼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Blink</b> is also a noun. 眨眼","examples":["He kept giving quick blinks. 他不停地快速眨眼。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a light <b>blinks</b>, it flashes on and off. 閃爍","examples":["Green and yellow lights blinked on the surface of the harbour. 綠色和黃色的燈光在港灣水面上閃爍。","The plane was flying normally for about 15 minutes before a warning light blinked on. 飛機正常飛行15分鐘後警示燈開始閃爍。"]}]}]},"bloom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花，花朵；花期；青春煥發，風華正茂；（膚色的）紅潤；（一些水果和植物的）粉衣，粉霜；（尤指音樂錄音中）飽滿響亮的聲音；方坯"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開花，綻放；繁榮，興旺；精神煥發；給（透鏡）敷膜；把（鑄塊）鑄成方坯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bloom</b> is the flower on a plant. 花","examples":["The sweet fragrance of the white blooms makes this climber a favourite. 白色花朵散發出的甜香使這株藤蔓成了寵兒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as someone's skin has a <b>bloom</b>, it has a fresh and healthy appearance. 紅潤","examples":["The skin loses its youthful bloom. 皮膚失去了年輕時的紅潤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a fine whitish coating on the surface of fruits, leaves, etc, consisting of minute grains of a waxy substance","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a rectangular mass of metal obtained by rolling or forging a cast ingot 方坯","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A plant or tree that is <b>in bloom</b> has flowers on it. 開花","examples":["...a pink climbing rose in full bloom. …一朵盛開的粉色攀緣玫瑰。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a plant or tree <b>blooms</b>, it produces flowers. When a flower <b>blooms</b>, it opens. 開花; (花) 開","examples":["This plant blooms between May and June. 這種植物在五六月間開花。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>blooms</b>, they develop good, attractive, or successful qualities. 蓬勃發展","examples":["Not many economies bloomed in 1990, least of all gold exporters like Australia. 沒有幾個國家的經濟在1990年蓬勃發展，尤其是像澳大利亞這樣的金礦出口國。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to convert (an ingot) into a bloom by rolling or forging 把(鑄塊)鑄成方坯","examples":[]}]}]},"blossom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（樹木的）花，花簇；開花，花期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開花；成長，繁盛，興旺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Blossom</b> is the flowers that appear on a tree before the fruit. (果樹的) 花","examples":["The cherry blossom came out early in Washington this year. 華盛頓的櫻花今年開得早。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>blossoms</b>, they develop good, attractive, or successful qualities. 成功發展","examples":["Why do some people take longer than others to blossom? 為什麼有些人比其他人大器晚成呢？","What began as a local festival has blossomed into an international event. 開始時的一個地方節日已經發展成了一個國際盛會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a tree <b>blossoms</b>, it produces blossom. (樹) 開花","examples":["Rain begins to fall and peach trees blossom. 雨開始下，桃樹就開花了。"]}]}]},"boast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"有（值得自豪的東西）；吹噓，誇耀"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"誇耀，自吹自擂，感到自豪的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>boasts</b> about something that they have done or that they own, they talk about it very proudly, in a way that other people may find irritating or offensive. 吹噓","examples":["Witnesses said Furci boasted that he took part in killing them. 證人們說富爾西曾吹噓說他參與了殺人。","Carol boasted about her costume. 卡羅爾吹噓著她的戲裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something can <b>boast</b> a particular achievement or possession, they have achieved or possess that thing. 取得 (成功); 擁有","examples":["The houses will boast the latest energy-saving technology. 這些房屋將採用最新節能技術。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boast</b> is also a noun. 吹噓","examples":["It is the charity's proud boast that it has never yet turned anyone away. 該慈善機構自吹自擂，聲稱從來沒有拒絕過任何人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a stroke in which the ball is hit on to one of the side walls before hitting the front wall 弧線擊球","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to shape or dress (stone) roughly with a broad chisel 鑿(石頭)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to hit (the ball) in this way or make such a stroke 擊弧線(球)","examples":[]}]}]},"blush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因感到難堪或羞愧而）臉紅；慚愧，尷尬；使成紅色"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（因感到難堪或羞愧的）臉紅；胭紅，淡紅色；<美> 胭脂；玫瑰紅酒；<美>胭脂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>blush</b>, your face becomes redder than usual because you are ashamed or embarrassed. (因害羞、窘困等) 臉紅","examples":["\"Hello, Maria,\" he said, and she blushed again. 他說道：“瑪麗亞，你好！”然後她的臉又紅了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Blush</b> is also a noun. 臉紅","examples":["\"The most important thing is to be honest,\" she says, without the trace of a blush. “最重要的是要誠實。”她說道，絲毫不臉紅。"]}]}]},"bra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胸罩，文胸；（量子力學）左矢；（Bra）（科特）布拉（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bra</b> is a piece of underwear that women wear to support their breasts. 胸罩","examples":[]}]}]},"bracelet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手鐲，臂鐲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bracelet</b> is a chain or band, usually made of metal, that you wear around your wrist as jewellery. 手鐲","examples":[]}]}]},"brassiere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胸罩，乳罩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brassiere</b> is the same as a . 同bra","examples":[]}]}]},"bridegroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新郎，即將（或剛）結婚的男子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bridegroom</b> is a man who is getting married. 新郎","examples":[]}]}]},"bulletin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（廣播或電視中的）新聞簡報；公告，佈告；（機構或社團的）通訊，刊物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"透過公告公佈或告知"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bulletin</b> is a short news report on the radio or television. (電臺、電視臺的) 新聞快報","examples":["...the early morning news bulletin. …早間新聞快報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bulletin</b> is a short official announcement made publicly to inform people about an important matter. 公告","examples":["At 3:30 p.m. a bulletin was released announcing that the president was out of immediate danger. 下午3:30釋出了公告，宣佈總統暫時脫離了危險。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bulletin</b> is a regular newspaper or leaflet that is produced by an organization or group such as a school or church. (學校、教堂等機構發行的) 簡報或小冊子","examples":[]}]}]},"bond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紐帶，聯絡；公債，債券；結合，黏合；承諾，契約；枷鎖，桎梏"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）建立親密關係；與……黏合（或連線）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bond</b> <b>between</b> people is a strong feeling of friendship, love, or shared beliefs and experiences that unites them. (強烈的感情) 紐帶","examples":["The experience created a very special bond between us. 這段經歷構成了我們之間一條非常特殊的紐帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bond</b> <b>between</b> people or groups is a close connection that they have with each other, for example because they have a special agreement. 密切聯絡","examples":["...the strong bond between church and nation. …教會與國家的緊密聯絡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bond</b> <b>between</b> two things is the way in which they stick to one another or are joined in some way. 黏合","examples":["If you experience difficulty with the superglue not creating a bond with dry wood, moisten the surfaces with water. 如果你用強力膠難以粘上乾燥的木頭，就用水潤溼木頭表面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a government or company issues a <b>bond</b>, it borrows money from investors. The certificate that is issued to investors who lend money is also called a <b>bond</b>. (政府或公司發行的) 債券","examples":["Most of it will be financed by government bonds. 其主要資金來源於政府債券。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>bond</b> <b>with</b> each other, they form a relationship based on love or shared beliefs and experiences. You can also say that people <b>bond</b> or that something <b>bonds</b> them. 建立關係","examples":["Belinda was having difficulty bonding with the baby. 貝琳達難以和這個嬰兒建立親密關係。","They all bonded while writing graffiti together. 他們在一起塗鴉時相識。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When one thing <b>bonds</b> <b>with</b> another, it sticks to it or becomes joined to it in some way. You can also say that two things <b>bond</b> <b>together</b>, or that something <b>bonds</b> them <b>together</b>. (使) 黏合","examples":["In graphite sheets, carbon atoms bond together in rings. 在石墨片中，碳原子以環狀黏合在一起。"]}]}]},"calculator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計算器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calculator</b> is a small electronic device that you use for making mathematical calculations. 計算器","examples":["...a pocket calculator. …一個袖珍計算器。"]}]}]},"calculation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計算，運算；估算，預測；算計，盤算"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calculation</b> is something that you think about and work out mathematically. <b>Calculation</b> is the process of working something out mathematically. 計算","examples":["Leonard made a rapid calculation: he'd never make it in time. 倫納德做了個快速的估算：他不可能及時做完。"]}]}]},"breed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"交配繁殖；飼養，培育；養育，培養；引起，釀成；（透過核反應）增殖可裂變物質"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"品種；（人的）型別，種類"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>breed</b> of a pet animal or farm animal is a particular type of it. For example, terriers are a breed of dog. (動物的) 品種","examples":["...rare breeds of cattle. …稀有牛種。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"養殖","examples":["There is potential for selective breeding for better yields. 以優產為目的的精選養殖是有潛力的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"繁殖","examples":["During the breeding season the birds come ashore. 在繁殖期鳥兒們上岸。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>breed</b> animals or plants, you keep them for the purpose of producing more animals or plants with particular qualities, in a controlled way. 養殖","examples":["He lived alone, breeding horses and dogs. 他獨自生活,養殖馬和狗。","He used to breed dogs for the police. 他過去為警察部門養殖狗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>breeds</b> bad feeling or bad behaviour, you mean that it causes bad feeling or bad behaviour to develop. 釀成 (不良情緒或不良行為)","examples":["If they are unemployed it's bound to breed resentment. 如果他們失業了,一定會釀成怨恨。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals <b>breed</b>, they have babies. 繁殖","examples":["Frogs will usually breed in any convenient pond. 青蛙通常在任何適宜的水塘裡繁殖。"]}]}]},"bounce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"彈起，反彈；跳動，蹦；（使）上下晃動；（用膝蓋）顛動（孩子）；蹦蹦跳跳地去；拒付，退回（支票等）；退回（電子郵件）；驅逐，解僱；（向某人）透露主意（以試探其反應）；反覆跳槽，來回往返某地；（光線或聲音）反射；撞擊，碰撞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"彈跳，跳動；彈性，彈力；活力，精力；（頭髮的）彈性，蓬鬆；突然的增長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an object such as a ball <b>bounces</b> or when you <b>bounce</b> it, it moves upward from a surface or away from it immediately after hitting it. 使…彈起; 彈起","examples":["My father would burst into the kitchen bouncing a tennis ball. 我父親會拍打著網球闖進廚房。","...a falling pebble, bouncing down the eroded cliff. …彈跳著滾下被蝕懸崖的一塊卵石。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If sound or light <b>bounces off</b> a surface or <b>is bounced off</b> it, it reaches the surface and is reflected back. 使…反射; 反射","examples":["Your arms and legs need protection from light bouncing off glass. 你的雙臂和雙腿需要保護，免受玻璃反射光的照射。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>bounces</b> or if something <b>bounces</b> it, it swings or moves up and down. 使…跳動; 跳動","examples":["Her long black hair bounced as she walked. 她長長的黑髮在她走路時擺動著。","The car was bouncing up and down as if someone were jumping on it. 車上下顛簸，彷彿有人正在上面跳動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>bounce</b> your ideas <b>off</b> someone, you tell them to that person, in order to find out what they think about them. 徵求別人的看法","examples":["It was good to bounce ideas off another mind. 徵求別人的看法是好的。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a cheque <b>bounces</b> or if someone <b>bounces</b> it, the bank refuses to accept it and pay out the money, because the person who wrote it does not have enough money in their account. 拒付 (支票)","examples":["Our only complaint would be if the cheque bounced. 如果支票被拒收，這會是我們惟一的抱怨。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bounce</b> is also a noun. 彈","examples":["The wheelchair tennis player is allowed two bounces of the ball. 殘疾網球運動員可以有兩次彈球的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bounce</b> on a soft surface, you jump up and down on it repeatedly. 蹦跳","examples":["She lets us do anything, even bounce on our beds. 她允許我們做任何事，甚至是在床上蹦跳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>bounces</b> somewhere, they move there in an energetic way, because they are feeling happy. (因為開心) 蹦跳著走","examples":["Moira bounced into the office. 莫伊拉蹦蹦跳跳地走進辦公室。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an e-mail or other electronic message <b>bounces</b>, it is returned to the person who sent it because the address was wrong or because of a problem with one of the computers involved in sending it. 退回","examples":["...a message saying that your mail has bounced or was unable to be delivered. …一條說明你的郵件被退回或無法遞送的資訊。"]}]}]},"cabinet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"內閣；儲藏櫃，陳列櫃；<古>私人小房間，密室；機箱，機殼"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內閣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cabinet</b> is a cupboard used for storing things such as medicine or alcoholic drinks or for displaying decorative things in. 貯藏櫥; 陳列櫃","examples":["She looked in the medicine cabinet and found some aspirin. 她在藥櫥中翻看了一下，找到幾片阿司匹林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>cabinet</b> is a group of the most senior advisers or ministers in a government, who meet regularly to discuss policies. 內閣","examples":["The announcement came after a three-hour cabinet meeting. 這項公告是在3小時的內閣會議之後釋出的。"]}]}]},"calorie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"卡（路里）（熱量單位）；小卡（現一般定為4.1868焦耳）；大卡，千卡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Calories</b> are units used to measure the energy value of food. People who are on diets try to eat food that does not contain many calories. 卡路里 (食物的熱量單位)","examples":["Sweetened drinks contain a lot of calories. 含糖的飲料熱量很高。"]}]}]},"candidate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"候選人，申請者；有望體驗（得到）……的人（物）；投考者，考生；攻讀學位者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>candidate</b> is someone who is being considered for a position, for example someone who is running in an election or applying for a job. 候選人","examples":["The Democratic candidate is still leading in the polls. 那名民主黨候選人仍在民意測驗中領先。","He is a candidate for the office of governor. 他是州長的候選人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>candidate</b> is someone who is studying for a degree at a college. 攻讀學位者","examples":["He is now a candidate for a Master's degree in social work at San Francisco State University. 他目前在舊金山州立大學攻讀社會工作碩士學位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>candidate</b> is a person or thing that is regarded as being suitable for a particular purpose or as being likely to do or be a particular thing. 有望做…的人; 有望成為…的事","examples":["Those who are overweight or indulge in high-salt diets are candidates for hypertension. 那些身體超重或飲食偏鹹的人屬於易患高血壓症的人群。"]}]}]},"cape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海角，岬；披肩，斗篷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"揮動披肩鬥牛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cape</b> is a large piece of land that sticks out into the sea from the coast. 海角; 岬","examples":["Naomi James became the first woman to sail solo around the world via Cape Horn. 內奧米·詹姆斯成為第一位獨自經合恩角進行環球航行的女子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cape</b> is a short cloak. 披肩","examples":["...a woollen cape. …一件羊毛披肩。"]}]}]},"capitalism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資本主義"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Capitalism</b> is an economic and political system in which property, business, and industry are owned by private individuals and not by the state. 資本主義","examples":["...the two fundamentally opposed social systems, capitalism and socialism. …兩種根本對立的社會制度，資本主義與社會主義。"]}]}]},"capitalist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資本主義者；資本家"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"資本主義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>capitalist</b> country or system supports or is based on the principles of capitalism. 基於資本主義原則的","examples":["China has pledged to retain Hong Kong's capitalist system for 50 years. 中國政府已保證維持香港的資本主義制度50年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>capitalist</b> is someone who believes in and supports the principles of capitalism. 資本主義者; 資本主義擁護者","examples":["Lenin had hoped to even have a working relationship with the capitalists. 列寧甚至曾希望能與資本主義者建立合作關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>capitalist</b> is someone who owns a business which they run in order to make a profit for themselves. 資本家","examples":["They argue that only private capitalists can remake Poland's economy. 他們爭辯說只有個體資本家才能重振波蘭的經濟。"]}]}]},"campaign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（有計劃的）活動，運動；戰役，戰鬥"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"領導（參加）運動，從事競選活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>campaign</b> is a planned set of activities that people carry out over a period of time in order to achieve something such as social or political change. (有計劃的) 活動; 運動","examples":["During his election campaign he promised to put the economy back on its feet. 競選活動期間，他許諾要致力於恢復經濟。","...a campaign to improve the training of staff. …改進員工培訓的一個活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a war, a <b>campaign</b> is a series of planned movements carried out by armed forces. 一系列軍事行動; 戰役","examples":["The allies are intensifying their air campaign. 盟軍在加強他們的空中軍事活動。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>campaigns</b> <b>for</b> something, they carry out a planned set of activities over a period of time in order to achieve their aim. 從事運動","examples":["We are campaigning for law reform. 我們正從事法律改革運動。"]}]}]},"cargo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（船或飛機裝載的）貨物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>cargo</b> of a ship or plane is the goods that it is carrying. 貨物","examples":["The boat calls at the main port to load its regular cargo of bananas. 船停泊在那個大港，裝載其常規貨物香蕉。"]}]}]},"catalog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目錄，目錄冊，一覽表（如圖書館、商品等的目錄）；（計算機）系統目錄，資料字典；（音樂、影視、出版等）某藝術家或公司的全部作品，作品全集"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"為……編目錄，把……編入目錄，把……登記入目錄"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"編目錄；按確定價格收入目錄（等於 catalogue）"}],"sections":[]},"capacity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能力，才能；容積，容納能力；職位，職責；功率，容積；生產量，生產能力"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無虛席的，滿場的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>capacity</b> <b>for</b> something is your ability to do it, or the amount of it that you are able to do. 能力","examples":["Our capacity for giving care, love, and attention is limited. 我們給予照顧、愛護和關心的能力是有限的。","Her mental capacity and temperament are as remarkable as his. 她的智慧和氣質與他的同樣出眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>capacity</b> of a container is its volume, or the amount of liquid it can hold, measured in units such as quarts or gallons. 容量","examples":["...containers with a maximum capacity of 200 gallons of water. …最大容量為200加侖水的容器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>capacity</b> of something such as a factory, industry, or region is the quantity of things that it can produce or deliver with the equipment or resources that are available. 產量","examples":["...the amount of spare capacity in the economy. ...經濟中的過剩產能。","Bread factories are working at full capacity. 麵包廠正在滿負荷進行生產。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>capacity</b> of a piece of equipment is its size or power, often measured in particular units. 負載量","examples":["...an aircraft with a bomb-carrying capacity of 1000 pounds. …一架炸彈裝載量達1000磅的飛機。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do something <b>in</b> a particular <b>capacity</b>, you do it as part of a particular job or duty, or because you are representing a particular organization or person. 身份","examples":["Ms. Halliwell visited the Philippines in her capacity as a Special Representative of UNICEF. 哈利韋爾女士以聯合國兒童基金會特使的身份訪問了菲律賓。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"The <b>capacity</b> of a building, place, or vehicle is the number of people or things that it can hold. If a place is filled <b>to capacity</b>, it is as full as it can possibly be. 容納力","examples":["Each stadium had a seating capacity of about 50,000. 每個運動場能容納大約五萬座席。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>capacity</b> crowd or audience completely fills a theatre, sports stadium, or other place. 滿座的","examples":["A capacity crowd of 76,000 people was at the stadium for the event. 運動場內座無虛席，7.6萬人觀看了比賽。"]}]}]},"cd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"光碟，鐳射唱片（compact disc）；呼叫裝置（calling device）；中央地區（central district）；商務部（Commerce Department）；冷卻時間（cool down time，遊戲術語）；創意總監（creative director）；民防（civil defence）；外交團（corps diplomatique）；存單，存款單（certificate of deposit）；坎德拉，新燭光（candela，發光強度單位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"cash discount 現金折扣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"symbol for.","pos_name":"symbol for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"candela 坎德拉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Democratic Republic of Congo 多哥民主共和國","examples":[]}]}]},"career":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"職業，事業；職業生涯；<古>速度，行程"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"就業的，職業的；終身從事的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛衝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>career</b> is the job or profession that someone does for a long period of their life. 職業","examples":["She is now concentrating on a career as a fashion designer. 她現在專注於時裝設計這一行。","...a career in journalism. …新聞職業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>career</b> is the part of your life that you spend working. 職業生涯","examples":["During his career, he wrote more than fifty plays. 在他的創作生涯裡，他共寫了五十多部劇作。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Career</b> advice or guidance consists of information about different jobs and help with deciding what kind of job you want to do. 就業的","examples":["She received very little career guidance when young. 她年輕時沒受過什麼就業指導。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or vehicle <b>careers</b> somewhere, they move fast and in an uncontrolled way. 猛衝","examples":["His car careered into a river. 他的車猛地衝進了河裡。"]}]}]},"carrier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"搬運人，運輸工具；航空公司；軍車，運輸艦；購物袋；（腳踏車等的）置物架，載重架；帶菌者，病毒攜帶者，病媒；通訊公司；載體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carrier</b> is a vehicle that is used for carrying people, especially soldiers, or things. 運輸工具","examples":["There were armoured personnel carriers and tanks on the streets. 街上有裝甲車和坦克。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>carrier</b> is a company that provides telecommunications services, such as telephone and Internet services. 電信運營商","examples":["...Japan's top wireless carrier. …日本頭號無線通訊運營商。","Regional carriers get paid for calls that pass through their switches. 地方運營商向那些透過其轉接臺的電話收費。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>carrier</b> is a passenger airline. 客運航空公司","examples":["American Airlines is the third-largest carrier at Denver International Airport. 美國航空公司是丹佛國際機場第三大客運航空公司。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>carrier</b> is a company that transports goods from one place to another by truck. 卡車運輸公司","examples":["The Colorado Motor Carriers Association represents 450 trucking companies across the state. 科羅拉多汽車運輸協會代表了該州450家卡車運輸公司。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>carrier</b> is a person or an animal that is infected with a disease and so can make other people or animals ill. 病毒攜帶者","examples":["...an AIDS carrier. …一名艾滋病毒攜帶者。"]}]}]},"catalogue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目錄，目錄冊；一系列，一連串（壞事情）；<美>大學情況一覽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"列入目錄，編入目錄；列舉，記載"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>catalogue</b> is a list of things such as the goods you can buy from a particular company, the objects in a museum, or the books in a library. 目錄","examples":["...the world's biggest seed catalogue. …世界上最大的種子目錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>catalogue</b> <b>of</b> similar things, especially bad things, is a number of them considered or discussed one after another. 一連串 (尤指不幸的事)","examples":["His story is a catalogue of misfortune. 他的經歷中充滿了接二連三的厄運。"]}]}]},"celebration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"慶典，慶祝活動；慶祝，頌揚；宗教儀式的舉行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>celebration</b> is a special enjoyable event that people organize because something pleasant has happened or because it is someone's birthday or anniversary. 慶祝活動","examples":["I can tell you, there was a celebration in our house that night. 跟你說吧，那天晚上我們在家裡搞了個慶祝活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>celebration</b> <b>of</b> something is praise and appreciation which is given to it. 頌揚","examples":["This was not a memorial service but a celebration of his life. 這儀式不是追悼會，而是對他的生平的頌揚。"]}]}]},"cease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"終止，結束"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"停止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>ceases</b>, it stops happening or existing. 停止","examples":["At one o'clock the rain had ceased. 一點鐘時雨已經停了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cease</b> <b>to</b> do something, you stop doing it. 停止; 不再 (做某事)","examples":["He never ceases to amaze me. 他總讓我驚喜不斷。","The secrecy about the president's condition had ceased to matter. 有關總統健康狀況的秘密已經不再舉足輕重了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cease</b> something, you stop it happening or working. 停止","examples":["The Tundra Times, a weekly newspaper in Alaska, ceased publication this week. 阿拉斯加的週報——《苔原時報》於本週停刊。"]}]}]},"championship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錦標賽；冠軍稱號，冠軍地位；捍衛，擁護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>championship</b> is a competition to find the best player or team in a particular sport. 錦標賽","examples":["...the world chess championship. …世界國際象棋錦標賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The championship</b> refers to the title or status of being a sports champion. 冠軍稱號","examples":["He went on to take the championship. 他繼續衛冕了冠軍稱號。"]}]}]},"cement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水泥；膠合劑，接合劑；（對關係、看法等起鞏固作用的）紐帶；牙骨質；（黏附顆粒的）沉積岩基質；（填充牙齒齲洞的）黏固粉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用（水泥或膠合劑）黏結，膠合；鞏固，加強；決定，確立"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cement</b> is a grey powder which is mixed with sand and water in order to make concrete. 水泥","examples":["Builders have trouble getting the right amount of cement into their concrete. 建築工人們不知道該往混凝土中加入多少水泥才合適。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cement</b> is the same as . 混凝土","examples":["...the hard, cold cement floor. …堅硬冰冷的混凝土地面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Glue that is made for sticking particular substances together is sometimes called <b>cement</b>. 膠合劑","examples":["Stick the pieces on with tile cement. 用瓷磚膠合劑把這些碎片粘上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>cements</b> a relationship or agreement makes it stronger. 鞏固 (關係、協約)","examples":["Nothing cements a friendship between countries so much as trade. 沒有任何東西能比貿易更能鞏固國家間的友誼了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If things <b>are cemented</b> together, they are stuck or fastened together. 使黏結","examples":["Most artificial joints are cemented into place. 絕大部分人造關節是被黏結復位的。"]}]}]},"chamber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房間，室；會議廳，會所；議院；腔，膛；洞穴；<舊>臥室；法官辦公室，律師事務所（chambers）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把子彈送入彈膛；把……關在房間裡"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"室內的；私人的，秘密的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chamber</b> is a large room, especially one that is used for formal meetings. 會議廳","examples":["We are going to be in the council chamber every time he speaks. 我們每次都在會議廳聽他講話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a country's legislature or to one section of it as a <b>chamber</b>. 議院","examples":["More than 80 parties are contesting seats in the two-chamber parliament. 80多個政黨在競爭該議會兩院的席位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>chamber</b> is a room designed and equipped for a particular purpose. (作特殊用途的) 房間","examples":["For many, the dentist's office remains a torture chamber. 對許多人來說，牙科診室仍是一間行刑室。"]}]}]},"chore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家庭雜務，雜活；累活，苦差事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chore</b> is a task that you must do but that you find unpleasant or boring. 瑣事","examples":["She sees exercise primarily as an unavoidable chore. 她把鍛鍊主要看作是不得不做的瑣事。"]}]}]},"chirp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鳥）啁啾，（昆蟲）唧唧叫； 輕鬆愉快地說，嘁嘁喳喳地說；抱怨；故意惹怒（某人）而說，奚落"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吱吱聲，唧唧聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a bird or an insect such as a cricket or grasshopper <b>chirps</b>, it makes short, high-pitched sounds. 蟲鳴; 鳥叫","examples":["The crickets chirped faster and louder. 蟋蟀叫得越來越快，越來越響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chirp</b> is also a noun. 鳥的叫聲; 蟲的鳴叫聲","examples":["The chirps of the garden birds sounded distant. 花園的鳥鳴聽上去那樣的遙遠。"]}]}]},"charity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"慈善組織，慈善機構；慈善事業；仁慈，寬厚；賑濟，施捨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>charity</b> is an organization which raises money in order to help people who are ill, disabled, or very poor. 慈善機構","examples":["...an AIDS charity. …一個艾滋病慈善機構。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you give money <b>to</b> <b>charity</b>, you give it to one or more charitable organizations. If you do something <b>for</b> <b>charity</b>, you do it in order to raise money for one or more charitable organizations. 慈善","examples":["He made substantial donations to charity. 他做了大量的慈善捐贈。","Gooch will be raising money for charity. 古奇將為慈善籌集款項。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"People who live on <b>charity</b> live on money or goods which other people give them because they are poor. 救濟金; 救濟物","examples":["Her husband is unemployed and the family depends on charity. 她的丈夫失業了，全家靠救濟度日。"]}]}]},"cigar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雪茄煙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cigars</b> are rolls of dried tobacco leaves which people smoke. 雪茄煙","examples":["He was smoking a big cigar. 他在抽一隻大雪茄。"]}]}]},"chemistry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"化學；化學成分，化學反應；（彼此間的）吸引"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chemistry</b> is the scientific study of the structure of substances and of the way that they react with other substances. 化學","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>chemistry</b> of an organism or a material is the chemical substances that make it up and the chemical reactions that go on inside it. 化學成分; 化學反應","examples":["We have literally altered the chemistry of our planet's atmosphere. 我們實際上改變了地球大氣層的化學成分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>chemistry</b> between two people, you mean that it is obvious they are attracted to each other or like each other very much. (彼此間的) 吸引","examples":["...the extraordinary chemistry between Ingrid and Bogart. …英格麗德和博加特之間強烈的相互吸引。"]}]}]},"characteristic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特徵，特點，特色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨特的，典型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>characteristics</b> of a person or thing are the qualities or features that belong to them and make them recognizable. 特徵","examples":["Genes determine the characteristics of every living thing. 基因決定每個生物的特徵。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A quality or feature that is <b>characteristic</b> <b>of</b> someone or something is one which is often seen in them and seems typical of them. 典型的","examples":["...the absence of strife between the generations that was so characteristic of such societies. …代與代之間衝突的消失,而這種衝突曾是這些社會的典型特徵。","Windmills are a characteristic feature of the Mallorcan landscape. 風車是馬略卡島風光的一個典型的特色。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"典型地","examples":["He replied in characteristically robust style. 他以典型的堅定風格作答。"]}]}]},"chorus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"副歌，疊句；合唱團，歌詠隊；齊聲，異口同聲；合唱歌曲；（古希臘戲劇）合唱隊，解說演員；(伊麗莎白時期戲劇）旁白；樂器擴音器；（演出中伴舞的）歌舞隊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"齊聲說，齊唱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chorus</b> is a part of a song which is repeated after each verse. 副歌","examples":["Caroline sang two verses and the chorus of her song. 卡羅琳唱了她歌中的兩段主歌及副歌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chorus</b> is a large group of people who sing together. 合唱團","examples":["The chorus was singing \"The Ode to Joy.\" 合唱團那時正在唱著《歡樂頌》。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>chorus</b> is a piece of music written to be sung by a large group of people. 合唱曲","examples":["...the Hallelujah Chorus. …哈利路亞合唱曲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>chorus</b> is a group of singers or dancers who perform together in a show, in contrast to the soloists. 合唱團; 舞蹈隊","examples":["Students played the lesser parts and sang in the chorus. 學生們扮演了一些次要角色，並參加了合唱團的演唱。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In drama, a <b>chorus</b> is an actor or a group of actors who comment on the action of the play. (戲劇中的) 劇情解說演員","examples":["He decides to sort out her life for her, while a pushy Greek chorus dispenses advice from the sidelines. 他決定幫她理順一下生活，而一位愛管閒事的希臘劇情解說演員則從旁觀者的角度發表了建議。","...commanding performances from Joe Savino as the chorus and Stephen Brennan as the ghost. …由喬·薩維諾擔任劇情解說演員、斯蒂芬·布倫南扮演幽靈的給人深刻印象的演出。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When there is a <b>chorus</b> <b>of</b> criticism, disapproval, or praise, that attitude is expressed by a lot of people at the same time. 齊聲 (批評、反對或讚揚)","examples":["The government is defending its economic policies against a growing chorus of criticism. 面對日益高漲的齊聲批評，政府還在為其經濟政策辯護。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>chorus</b> something, they say it or sing it together. 齊聲說或唱","examples":["\"Hi,\" they chorused. “嗨，”他們齊聲說道。"]}]}]},"circulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發行量，銷售量；血液迴圈；流傳，流通；參加社交活動，交際；環流，迴圈；（圖書的）借出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>circulation</b> of a newspaper or magazine is the number of copies that are sold each time it is produced. 發行量","examples":["The Daily News once had the highest circulation of any daily in the country. 《每日新聞報》一度在該國所有日報中擁有最高發行量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>circulation</b> is the movement of blood through your body. 血液迴圈","examples":["Anyone with heart, lung, or circulation problems should seek medical advice before flying. 任何有心、肺或血液迴圈問題的人都應該在飛行前尋求醫生建議。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as money is <b>in circulation</b>, it is being used by the public. If something is <b>out of circulation</b> or has been <b>withdrawn from circulation</b>, it is no longer available for use by the public. 流通/停止流通","examples":["The supply of money in circulation was drastically reduced overnight. 一夜之間流通貨幣的供應就急劇減少了。","...a society like America, with perhaps 180 million guns in circulation. …像美國這樣的社會里，可能有1.8億支槍在流通之中。"]}]}]},"cinema":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電影院；電影（the cinema）；電影業，電影藝術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cinema</b> is the business and art of making films. 電影業; 電影製作藝術","examples":["Contemporary African cinema has much to offer. 當代非洲電影製作藝術有很多貢獻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cinema</b> is a place where people go to watch films for entertainment. 電影院","examples":["A cinema and roller rink attracted customers and profit. 一家兼作溜冰場的電影院吸引了顧客，也招來了利潤。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can talk about <b>the cinema</b> when you are talking about seeing a film. 電影","examples":["He took her to the cinema. 他帶她去看電影了。"]}]}]},"civilian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平民，百姓（區別于軍、警）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平民的，民用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a military situation, a <b>civilian</b> is anyone who is not a member of the armed forces. 平民","examples":["The safety of civilians caught up in the fighting must be guaranteed. 捲入戰鬥中的平民的安全必須得到保障。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a military situation, <b>civilian</b> is used to describe people or things that are not military. 平民的; 民用的","examples":["...the country's civilian population. …這個國家的平民人口。","...civilian casualties. …平民傷亡。"]}]}]},"cliff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懸崖，峭壁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cliff</b> is a high area of land with a very steep side, especially one next to the sea. (尤其指靠海的) 懸崖","examples":["The car rolled over the edge of a cliff. 汽車翻下了懸崖邊。"]}]}]},"civilization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文明；文明社會，文明國家；人類社會；舒適的生活環境；教化，開化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>civilization</b> is a human society with its own social organization and culture. 文明社會","examples":["The ancient civilizations of Central and Latin America were founded upon corn. 中美洲和拉丁美洲的古代文明社會是建立在玉米之上的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Civilization</b> is the state of having an advanced level of social organization and a comfortable way of life. 文明","examples":["...our advanced state of civilization. …我們高度的文明形態。"]}]}]},"classification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分類，分級；類別，級別；（動植物等的）分類學，分類法；（圖書館的書、磁帶、雜誌等的）分類系統，編目"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>classification</b> is a division or category in a system which divides things into groups or types. 類別","examples":["The government uses a classification system that includes both race and ethnicity. 政府採用一種既包括人種又包括種族的類別體系。"]}]}]},"circumstance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"條件，情況，環境；境況，經濟狀況；詳情，原委；命運，境遇"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"處於某種情況"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>circumstances</b> of a particular situation are the conditions which affect what happens. 情形","examples":["Recent opinion polls show that 60 percent favour abortion under certain circumstances. 最近的民意調查顯示60%的人贊同特定情況下的流產。","The strategy was too dangerous in the explosive circumstances of the times. 在當時爆炸性的形勢下，這一戰略太危險了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>circumstances</b> of an event are the way it happened or the causes of it. 詳情; 原委","examples":["I'm making inquiries about the circumstances of Mary Dean's murder. 我正在調查瑪麗·迪安謀殺案的原委。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>circumstances</b> are the conditions of your life, especially the amount of money that you have. 境況 (尤指經濟狀況)","examples":["...help and support for the single mother, whatever her circumstances. …提供給單身母親的幫助和支援，無論她們的境況如何。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Events and situations which cannot be controlled are sometimes referred to as <b>circumstance</b>. 命運; 客觀環境","examples":["There are those, you know, who, by circumstance, end up homeless. 你知道，有些人由於命運的原因最終變得無家可歸。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can emphasize that something must not or will not happen by saying that it must not or will not happen <b>under any circumstances</b>. 在任何情況下","examples":["Racism is wholly unacceptable under any circumstances. 在任何情況下種族主義都是完全不能被接受的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>in the circumstances</b> or <b>under the circumstances</b> before or after a statement to indicate that you have considered the conditions affecting the situation before making the statement. 在那種情況下","examples":["In the circumstances, Paisley's plans looked highly appropriate. 在那種情況下，佩斯利的計劃看起來非常合適。"]}]}]},"climax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高潮，頂點；性高潮；（植物群落演替達到平衡的）頂極（群落）；層進法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"達到性高潮；達到高潮，達到頂點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>climax</b> <b>of</b> something is the most exciting or important moment in it, usually near the end. 高潮","examples":["For Pritchard, reaching the Olympics was the climax of her career. 對普里查德來說，進軍奧林匹克運動會是她事業的巔峰。","It was the climax to 24 hours of growing anxiety. 這是24小時不斷升溫的焦慮的頂點。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The event that <b>climaxes</b> a sequence of events is an exciting or important event that comes at the end. You can also say that a sequence of events <b>climaxes</b> <b>with</b> a particular event. 使達到高潮; 達到高潮","examples":["The demonstration climaxed two weeks of strikes. 遊行示威達到了兩週罷工的高潮。"]}]}]},"comedy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜劇，喜劇片；滑稽的事物，搞笑的東西；滑稽，詼諧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Comedy</b> consists of types of entertainment, such as plays and film, or particular scenes in them, that are intended to make people laugh. 喜劇","examples":["Actor Dom Deluise talks about his career in comedy. 演員多姆·德盧斯談論他的喜劇事業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>comedy</b> is a play, film, or television programme that is intended to make people laugh. 喜劇","examples":["The movie is a romantic comedy. 這部電影是一個浪漫喜劇。"]}]}]},"clash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衝突，交戰；爭論，爭執；交鋒，比賽；分歧，差異；（金屬的）撞擊聲；（時間上的）衝突，撞期；（顏色、圖案等的）不相配"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迥然不同，牴觸；衝突，交戰；爭論，爭執；（時間上）相沖突，同時發生；（顏色、圖案等）不協調，不相配；（體育）交鋒，對陣；（使）撞擊發出鏗鏘聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>clash</b>, they fight, argue, or disagree with each other. 發生衝突; 產生矛盾","examples":["A group of 400 demonstrators ripped down the front gate and clashed with police. 400名示威者推倒前面的大前門，與警察發生了衝突。","Behind the scenes, Parsons clashed with almost everyone on the show. 幕後，帕森斯幾乎跟每個參與演出的人都產生過矛盾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Beliefs, ideas, or qualities that <b>clash</b> <b>with</b> each other are very different from each other and therefore are opposed. (因信仰、觀點或質量不同而) 產生分歧","examples":["Don't make any policy decisions which clash with official company thinking. 不要做與公司官方理念有分歧的任何政策性決定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one colour or style <b>clashes</b> <b>with</b> another, the colours or styles look ugly together. You can also say that two colours or styles <b>clash</b>. (顏色、風格等) 不協調","examples":["The red door clashed with the soft, natural tones of the stone walls. 這紅色的門與柔和自然色調的石牆不協調。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clash</b> is also a noun. 衝突","examples":["There have been a number of clashes between police in riot gear and demonstrators. 穿防暴服的警察和示威者之間發生過多次衝突。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Clash</b> is also a noun. 分歧","examples":["Inside government, there was a clash of views. 政府內部有意見分歧。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one event <b>clashes</b> <b>with</b> another, the two events happen at the same time so that you cannot attend both of them. (兩件事因發生的時間相同而) 產生衝突","examples":[]}]}]},"comic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滑稽的，好笑的；喜劇的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜劇演員；連環漫畫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>comic</b>, you mean that it makes you laugh, and is often intended to make you laugh. 喜劇的","examples":["The novel is comic and tragic. 這本小說兼有喜劇和悲劇的特點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Comic</b> is used to describe funny entertainment, and the actors and entertainers who perform it. 滑稽的","examples":["Grodin is a fine comic actor. 格羅丁是一位好的滑稽演員。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comic</b> is an entertainer who tells jokes in order to make people laugh. 喜劇演員","examples":["...the funniest comic in America. …美國最有趣的喜劇演員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>comics</b> is the part of a newspaper that contains the comic strips. (報刊的) 連環漫畫欄","examples":["She read the comics in the Philadelphia Inquirer. 她看了《費城調查者報》的連環漫畫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>comic</b> is a magazine that contains stories told in pictures. 連環漫畫","examples":[]}]}]},"combination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結合體，聯合體；結合，聯合；（用於開鎖的）數碼組合；化合作用；兩用（或多用的）物品；<舊>衫褲相連的內衣；組合；<英>附邊車的摩托車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>combination</b> <b>of</b> things is a mixture of them. 混合物","examples":["...a fantastic combination of colours. …一種奇妙的混合色。"]}]}]},"commander":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指揮官，長官；海軍中校；英國高階警官；高階騎士（或爵士）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>commander</b> is an officer in charge of a military operation or organization. 指揮官; 司令官","examples":["The commander and some of the men had been released. 指揮官和一些士兵已被釋放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commander</b> is an officer in the U.S. Navy or the Royal Navy. 海軍軍官","examples":[]}]}]},"code":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"密碼，暗碼；（郵政）編碼，（電話）區號；（計算機）編碼；道德準則，行為規範；法典，法規"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……編碼（或編號）；把……譯成密碼；（給計算機）編寫指令"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>code</b> is a set of rules about how people should behave or about how something must be done. 法典; 法規","examples":["...Article 159 of the state's penal code. …該國刑法第159條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>code</b> is a system of replacing the words in a message with other words or symbols, so that nobody can understand it unless they know the system. 密碼; 程式碼","examples":["They used elaborate secret codes, as when the names of trees stood for letters. 他們用的是精心設計的密碼，用樹木的名稱代表字母。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>code</b> is a group of numbers or letters which is used to identify something, such as a mailing address or part of a telephone system. 編號","examples":["Callers dialling the wrong area code will not get through. 打電話的人撥錯區號時電話就接不通。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>code</b> is any system of signs or symbols that has a meaning. 程式碼","examples":["It will need other chips to reconvert the digital code back into normal TV signals. 需要用其他晶片把數字程式碼重新轉換成普通的電視訊號。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The genetic <b>code</b> of a person, animal, or plant is the information contained in DNA which determines the structure and function of cells, and the inherited characteristics of all living things. 遺傳密碼","examples":["Scientists provided the key to understanding the genetic code that determines every bodily feature. 科學家們提供了線索來了解決定每個身體特徵的遺傳密碼。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Computer <b>code</b> is a system or language for expressing information and instructions in a form which can be understood by a computer. (電子計算機的) 編碼","examples":["She began writing software code at the age of nine. 她9歲就開始寫軟體編碼。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>code</b> something means to give it a code or to mark it with its code. 編碼","examples":["He devised a way of coding every statement uniquely. 他設計出一種把每句話進行獨特編碼的方法。"]}]}]},"commerce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貿易，商業；<舊>社交，交往；<舊>性交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Commerce</b> is the activities and procedures involved in buying and selling things. 商業","examples":["They have made their fortunes from industry and commerce. 他們從工商業中發了財。"]}]}]},"compact disk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"光碟：一種數字媒體，儲存在塑膠盤上，透過CD驅動器中的鐳射讀取。"}],"sections":[]},"collapse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"倒塌，塌下；崩潰，瓦解；突然倒下，昏倒；癱倒；突然貶值，暴跌；萎陷，癟掉；摺疊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"倒塌，塌陷；突然失敗，崩潰；病倒，垮掉；突然貶值，暴跌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a building or other structure <b>collapses</b>, it falls down very suddenly. 坍塌","examples":["A section of the Bay Bridge had collapsed. 海灣大橋有一部分坍塌了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something, for example a system or institution, <b>collapses</b>, it fails or comes to an end completely and suddenly. (系統或制度等) 崩潰; 瓦解","examples":["His business empire collapsed under a massive burden of debt. 他的商業帝國由於債臺高築而瓦解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>collapse</b>, you suddenly faint or fall down because you are very ill or weak. 暈倒; 倒下","examples":["He collapsed following a vigorous exercise session at his home. 他在家中進行了一段時間的劇烈運動後倒下了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>collapse</b> onto something, you sit or lie down suddenly because you are very tired. (因極度疲倦而) 癱坐; 癱倒","examples":["She arrived home exhausted and barely capable of showering before collapsing on her bed. 她到家的時候累極了，幾乎無法去淋浴就癱倒在床上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Collapse</b> is also a noun. 坍塌","examples":["The governor called for an inquiry into the motorway's collapse. 州長要求對高速公路的坍塌進行調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Collapse</b> is also a noun. (系統或制度等的) 崩潰; 瓦解","examples":["The coup's collapse has speeded up the drive to independence. 那次政變的失敗加速推動了獨立程序。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Collapse</b> is also a noun. 暈倒; 倒下","examples":["A few days after his collapse he was sitting up in bed. 他病倒後過了幾天就在床上起身坐著了。"]}]}]},"comment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"評論，意見；批評，指責；說明，寫照；<舊>解說，註釋；（計算機）註解"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"評論，發表意見；（計算機）註解，把（部分程式）轉成註解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>comment</b> <b>on</b> something, you give your opinion about it or you give an explanation for it. 評論; 解釋","examples":["So far, Mr. Cook has not commented on these reports. 到目前為止，庫克先生還未對這些報告進行過評論。","You really can't comment until you know the facts. 你的確不能在你知道事實之前進行評論。","One student commented that she preferred literature to social science. 一位學生解釋說，較之於社會科學她更喜歡文學。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comment</b> is something that you say which expresses your opinion of something or which gives an explanation of it. 評論; 解釋","examples":["He made his comments at a news conference in Amsterdam. 他在阿姆斯特丹的一次記者招待會上做了評論。","There's been no comment so far from police about the allegations. 到目前為止還沒有來自警方的對那些指控的任何解釋。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People say \"<b>no comment</b>\" as a way of refusing to answer a question, usually when it is asked by a journalist. 無可奉告","examples":["No comment. I don't know anything. 無可奉告。我什麼也不知道。"]}]}]},"composer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"創作者，作曲家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>composer</b> is a person who writes music, especially classical music. (尤指古典音樂) 作曲家","examples":["...music by Strauss, Mozart, Beethoven, and other great composers. …施特勞斯、莫扎特、貝多芬及其他偉大作曲家創作的音樂。"]}]}]},"competitor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"競爭者，對手；選手，參賽者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A company's <b>competitors</b> are companies who are trying to sell similar goods or services to the same people. 競爭對手","examples":["The bank isn't performing as well as some of its competitors. 這家銀行沒有它的一些競爭對手錶現好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>competitor</b> is a person who takes part in a competition or contest. 參賽者","examples":["One of the oldest competitors won the individual silver medal. 其中一個年紀最大的參賽者贏得了個人銀牌。"]}]}]},"communication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"表達，交流，交際；資訊，書信，電話；通訊，交通聯絡；傳播學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Communications</b> are the systems and processes that are used to communicate or broadcast information, especially by means of electricity or radio waves. 通訊","examples":["...a communications satellite. …一顆通訊衛星。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>communication</b> is a message. 資訊","examples":["The ambassador has brought with him a communication from the president. 該大使從總統那裡帶來了一則資訊。"]}]}]},"community":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社群，社會；（由同國籍、同宗教等構成的）群體，界；（多個國家的）共同體；歸屬感；（動植物的）群落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>community</b> is all the people who live in a particular area or place. 社群","examples":["He's well liked by people in the community. 他很受社群人們的喜愛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>community</b> is a group of people who are similar in some way. 團體","examples":["The police haven't really done anything for the black community in particular. 警方並沒有特別為黑人團體做什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Community</b> is friendship between different people or groups, and a sense of having something in common. 團體精神","examples":["Two of our greatest strengths are diversity and community. 我們的兩個最大優點是多樣性和團體精神。"]}]}]},"competition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"競爭；比賽，競賽；競爭者，對手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Competition</b> is a situation in which two or more people or groups are trying to get something which not everyone can have. (為獲取難得之物而進行的) 競爭","examples":["There's been some fierce competition for the title. 已有一些為此頭銜的激烈競爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Competition</b> is an activity involving two or more companies, in which each company tries to get people to buy its own goods in preference to the other companies' goods. (商業上的) 競爭","examples":["The deal would have reduced competition in the commuter-aircraft market. 該交易本可以減少通勤飛機市場的競爭。","The farmers have been seeking higher prices as better protection from foreign competition. 農場主們一直在尋求更高價格來作為對外來競爭的更好保護。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>competition</b> is the goods or services that a rival organization is selling. 競爭產品; 競爭服務","examples":["The American aerospace industry has been challenged by some stiff competition. 美國航空航天工業遭到了一些強勁競爭產品的挑戰。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>competition</b> is the person or people you are competing with. 競爭對手","examples":["I have to change my approach, the competition is too good now. 我得改變我的方法，競爭對手現在太好了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>competition</b> is an event in which many people take part in order to find out who is best at a particular activity. 競賽","examples":["...a surfing competition. …一項衝浪比賽。"]}]}]},"concept":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"概念，觀念"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（圍繞）某主題的；為表達一種想法而創造的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>想象，設想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>concept</b> is an idea or abstract principle. 概念; 觀念","examples":["She added that the concept of arranged marriages is misunderstood in the west. 她補充說包辦婚姻的概念在西方被誤解了。"]}]}]},"concentration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專心，專注；關注，重視；集中，聚集；含量，濃度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Concentration</b> on something involves giving all your attention to it. 專注","examples":["Neal kept interrupting, breaking my concentration. 尼爾不斷打擾，打斷我的注意力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>concentration</b> <b>of</b> something is a large amount of it or large numbers of it in a small area. 集中","examples":["The area has one of the world's greatest concentrations of wildlife. 該地區有世界上野生生物最集中的區域之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>concentration</b> <b>of</b> a substance is the proportion of essential ingredients or substances in it. 濃度","examples":["pH is a measure of the concentration of free hydrogen atoms in a solution. pH值是溶液中游離氫原子濃度的計量單位。"]}]}]},"composition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成分構成，成分；（音樂、藝術、詩歌的）作品；創作，作曲；構圖；作文"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>composition</b> of something, you are referring to the way in which its various parts are put together and arranged. 構成","examples":["Television has transformed the size and social composition of the audience at great sporting occasions. 電視改變了大型體育賽事觀眾的數量及其社會構成。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>compositions</b> of a composer, painter, or other artist are the works of art that they have produced. (作曲家、畫家等藝術家的) 作品","examples":["Mozart's compositions are undoubtedly among the world's greatest. 莫扎特的作品無疑位列於世界上最偉大的作品之中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>composition</b> is a piece of written work that children write at school. (學生的) 作文","examples":["We had to write a composition on the subject \"My Pet.\" 我們得就“我的寵物”這個主題寫一篇作文。"]}]}]},"conductor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（樂隊等的）指揮；售票員，檢票員；導體；<英>傳導教育的引導者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>conductor</b> is a person who stands in front of an orchestra or choir and directs its performance. (交響樂、合唱的) 指揮","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"On a train, a <b>conductor</b> is a person whose job is to travel on the train in order to help passengers and check tickets. 列車員","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On a tram or a bus, the <b>conductor</b> is the person whose job is to sell tickets to the passengers. (公共汽車等的) 售票員","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>conductor</b> is a substance that heat or electricity can pass through or along. (熱、電的) 導體","examples":["Graphite is a highly efficient conductor of electricity. 石墨是一種高效的電導體。"]}]}]},"congress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國會，議會；代表大會；美國國會（Congress）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>congress</b> is a large meeting that is held to discuss ideas and policies. 代表大會","examples":["A lot has changed after the party congress. 該黨代表大會後很多都變了。"]}]}]},"conference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大型、正式的）會議，研討會；（小型正式的）商討，討論；體育協會（或聯合會）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>conference</b> is a meeting, often lasting a few days, which is organized on a particular subject or to bring together people who have a common interest. 專題討論會","examples":["The president took the unprecedented step of summoning all the state governors to a conference on education. 總統採取了前所未有的舉措，召集所有的州長參加一次教育討論會。","...the Alternative Energy conference. …可替代能源討論會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>conference</b> is a meeting at which formal discussions take place. (進行正式討論的) 會議","examples":["They sat down at the dinner table for a conference. 他們在餐桌旁坐下開會。"]}]}]},"concrete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"確實的，具體的；實在的，有形的；混凝土的；物質的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"混凝土"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用混凝土覆蓋（或做成）；<舊>（使）凝固，（使）凝結；使真實（化），使具體（化）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Concrete</b> is a substance used for building which is made by mixing together cement, sand, small stones, and water. 混凝土","examples":["The posts have to be set in concrete. 這些柱子必須固定在混凝土中。","We sat on the concrete floor. 我們坐在混凝土地板上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>concrete</b> something such as a path, you cover it with concrete. 給 (道路等) 澆混凝土","examples":["He merely cleared and concreted the floors. 他只是清理了地板並澆上了混凝土。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>concrete</b> to indicate that something is definite and specific. 明確具體的","examples":["I had no concrete evidence. 我當時沒有明確而具體的證據。","There were no concrete proposals on the table. 沒有提交討論的具體提議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>concrete</b> object is a real, physical object. 實物的","examples":["...using concrete objects to teach addition and subtraction. …用實物教加減運算。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>concrete</b> noun is a noun that refers to a physical object rather than to a quality or idea. 具體的 (名詞)","examples":[]}]}]},"companion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同伴，伴侶；（受僱照料老人或病人的）陪護；成對的物品之一；同甘共苦的夥伴；（用於書名）指南，手冊；伴星；最低階爵士"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"陪伴"}],"sections":[]},"confusion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"困惑，不明確；混淆，混同；慌亂，窘迫；混亂局面，亂成一團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>confusion</b> about something, it is not clear what the true situation is, especially because people believe different things. 不明朗","examples":["There's still confusion about the number of students. 學生的人數依然不清楚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Confusion</b> is a situation in which everything is in disorder, especially because there are lots of things happening at the same time. 混亂","examples":["There was confusion when a man fired shots. 一名男子開了槍，出現了混亂。"]}]}]},"conjunction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結合，同時發生；連詞；（占星術中兩個天體的）相合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>conjunction</b> <b>of</b> two or more things is the occurrence of them at the same time or place. 同時發生; 同地發生","examples":["...the conjunction of two events. …兩事件的同時發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>conjunction</b> is a word or group of words that joins together words, groups, or clauses. In English, there are coordinating conjunctions such as \"and\" and \"but,\" and subordinating conjunctions such as \"although,\" \"because,\" and \"when.\" 連詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is done <b>in</b> <b>conjunction</b> <b>with</b> another, the two things are done or used together. 與…一起 (做、用)","examples":["Textbooks are designed to be used in conjunction with classroom teaching. 教科書被設計成與課堂教學配合使用。"]}]}]},"conscience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"良知，良心；內疚，愧疚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>conscience</b> is the part of your mind that tells you whether what you are doing is right or wrong. If you have a <b>guilty conscience</b>, you feel guilty about something because you know it was wrong. If you have a <b>clear conscience</b>, you do not feel guilty because you know you have done nothing wrong. 良知","examples":["I have battled with my conscience over whether I should actually send this letter. 我曾跟自己的良知鬥爭應否真的寄出這封信。","What if he got a guilty conscience and brought it back? 如果他問心有愧把它帶回來呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Conscience</b> is doing what you believe is right even though it might be unpopular, difficult, or dangerous. 憑良知行事","examples":["He refused for reasons of conscience to eat meat. 他為了良心好過而拒絕了吃肉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Conscience</b> is a feeling of guilt because you know you have done something that is wrong. 負疚感","examples":["I'm so glad he had a pang of conscience. 我實在高興他感到了一陣愧疚。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something <b>on</b> your <b>conscience</b>, you feel guilty because you know you have done something wrong. 引起內疚","examples":["The drunk driver has two deaths on his conscience. 這位醉酒的司機良心上揹負著兩條人命。"]}]}]},"consequence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結果，後果；重要性，價值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>consequences</b> <b>of</b> something are the results or effects of it. 結果; 後果","examples":["Her lawyer said she understood the consequences of her actions and was prepared to go to jail. 她的律師說她明白自己行為的後果並準備去坐牢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing happens and then another thing happens <b>in consequence</b> or <b>as a consequence</b>, the second thing happens as a result of the first. 結果","examples":["His death was totally unexpected and, in consequence, no plans had been made for his replacement. 他的死純粹出乎意料，因此還沒有為他的替代人定出計劃。","Maternity services were to be reduced as a consequence of falling birth rates. 孕產服務因下降的出生率而將被削減。"]}]}]},"confidence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自信，信心；信任，信賴；把握，肯定；保密，機密；秘密，知心話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>confidence</b> <b>in</b> someone, you feel that you can trust them. 信任","examples":["I have every confidence in you. 我對你有完全的信任。","This has contributed to the lack of confidence in the FDA. 這導致了對食品與藥品管理局信任的缺乏。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>confidence</b>, you feel sure about your abilities, qualities, or ideas. 自信心","examples":["The band is in excellent form and brimming with confidence. 該樂隊處於極好的狀態，表現得充滿信心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you can say something <b>with</b> <b>confidence</b>, you feel certain it is correct. 把握","examples":["I can say with confidence that such rumours were totally groundless. 我可以很有把握地說這些傳言完全沒有根據。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you tell someone something <b>in</b> <b>confidence</b>, you tell them a secret. 保密","examples":["We told you all these things in confidence. 我們告訴你的這些事情都是保密的。","Even telling Lois seemed a betrayal of confidence. 甚至告訴洛伊斯似乎也是對保密的背叛。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone <b>into</b> your <b>confidence</b>, you tell them a secret. 向某人吐露秘密","examples":[]}]}]},"consonant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"子音；子音字母"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一致的，相符的；（與）子音（有關）的；（樂）協和音的，和諧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consonant</b> is a sound such as \"p,\" \"f,\" \"n,\" or \"t\" which you pronounce by stopping the air flowing freely through your mouth. Compare . 子音","examples":[]}]}]},"consultant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧問；高階顧問醫師，會診醫師；諮詢者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consultant</b> is a person who gives expert advice to a person or organization on a particular subject. 顧問","examples":["She is a consultant to the government. 她是政府顧問。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>consultant</b> is an experienced doctor with a high position, who specializes in one area of medicine. 顧問醫生","examples":[]}]}]},"constitution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憲法，章程；體質，體格；組成，結構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>constitution</b> of a country or organization is the system of laws which formally states people's rights and duties. 憲法; 章程","examples":["The king was forced to adopt a new constitution which reduced his powers. 國王被迫透過了削減其權力的新憲法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>constitution</b> is your health. 體格","examples":["He must have an extremely strong constitution. 他必有極為強健的體格。"]}]}]},"conservative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"保守的；保守派的，保守主義的（認為政府應該實行政治保守主義）；（衣著）守舊的，傳統的；低估的；保守黨的；不願冒險的，謹慎的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"保守者，因循守舊者；保守黨黨員，保守黨支持者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>conservative</b> has views that are toward the political right. In the U.S. the Republicans are more conservative than the Democrats, who are more liberal. 持政治右傾觀點的","examples":["...counties whose citizens invariably support the most conservative candidate in any election. …公民們在任何選舉中都千篇一律地支援最保守的候選人的縣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>conservative</b> or has <b>conservative</b> ideas is unwilling to accept changes and new ideas. (觀點) 保守的","examples":["People tend to be more liberal when they're young and more conservative as they get older. 人們在年輕時常常更開放，年紀越大就越保守。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone dresses in a <b>conservative</b> way, their clothes are conventional in style. (衣著) 守舊的","examples":["The girl was well dressed, as usual, though in a more conservative style. 這個女孩像平常一樣穿著得體，但式樣則更守舊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>conservative</b> estimate or guess is one in which you are cautious and estimate or guess a low amount which is probably less than the real amount. 保守的 (估計、猜測)","examples":["The average fan spends $25 – a conservative estimate based on ticket price and souvenirs. 平均球迷花費$25–根據票價和紀念品的一個保守估計。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>Conservative</b> politician or voter is a member of or votes for the Conservative Party in Britain and in various other countries. (英國等) 保守黨的","examples":["Most Conservative MPs appear happy with the government's reassurances. 大多數保守黨的國會議員們看來對政府的保證感到滿意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conservative</b> is also a noun. 右傾人士","examples":["The new judge is 50-year-old David Suitor who's regarded as a conservative. 這名新法官是50歲的、被視為右傾人士的戴維·休特。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Conservative</b> is also a noun. 保守黨","examples":["In 1951 the Conservatives were returned to power. 1951年保守黨再度執政。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"保守地","examples":["She was always very conservatively dressed when we went out. 我們出門時她總是穿得很保守。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"保守地 (估計、猜測)","examples":["The bequest is conservatively estimated at $30 million. 這筆遺產被保守地估計為3000萬美元。"]}]}]},"consumer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消費者，顧客，使用者；食用者，使用者，消耗者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consumer</b> is a person who buys things or uses services. 消費者","examples":["...claims that tobacco companies failed to warn consumers about the dangers of smoking. …聲稱菸草公司沒有就吸菸的種種危險警告消費者。"]}]}]},"contentment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"滿足，滿意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Contentment</b> is a feeling of quiet happiness and satisfaction. 滿足","examples":["I cannot describe the feeling of contentment that was with me at that time. 我無法形容我當時的滿足感。"]}]}]},"container":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"容器；集裝箱，貨櫃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>container</b> is something such as a box or bottle that is used to hold or store things in. 容器","examples":["...the plastic containers in which fish are stored and sold. …儲藏和出售魚的塑膠容器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>container</b> is a very large metal or wooden box used for transporting goods so that they can be loaded easily onto ships and trucks. 集裝箱","examples":["The train, carrying loaded containers on flatcars, was 1.2 miles long. 那列在平車上載著裝得滿滿的集裝箱的火車長1.2英里。"]}]}]},"construction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建造，建築；創立，構建；構造，結構；建築物；語法結構；解釋，理解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Construction</b> is the building of things such as houses, factories, roads, and bridges. 建造","examples":["He'd already started construction on a hunting lodge. 他已經開始建造一個狩獵用的小屋。","...the downturn in the construction industry. …建造業的衰退。","Jim now works in construction. 吉姆現在從事建造業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>construction</b> of something such as a vehicle or machine is the making of it. (交通工具、機器等的) 製造","examples":["...companies who have long experience in the construction of those types of equipment. …在製造那種裝置方面有長久經驗的各公司。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>construction</b> of something such as a system is the creation of it. 創立","examples":["...the construction of a just system of criminal justice. …公正的刑事司法體制的建立。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>construction</b> to refer to the structure of something and the way it has been built or made. 構造","examples":["The Shakers believed that furniture should be plain, simple, useful, practical, and of sound construction. 震顫派教徒認為傢俱應當樸素、簡單、有用、實際，且構造很好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to an object that has been built or made as a <b>construction</b>. 建造物","examples":["...an impressive steel and glass construction. …一座令人印象深刻的鋼筋玻璃建造物。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A grammatical <b>construction</b> is a particular arrangement of words in a sentence, clause, or phrase. (語法) 結構","examples":["Avoid complex verbal constructions. 避免複雜的動詞結構。"]}]}]},"contest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比賽，競賽；爭奪，競爭；爭論，爭執"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"爭辯，提出異議；爭取贏得，角逐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>contest</b> is a competition or game that people try to win. 競賽; 比賽","examples":["Few contests in the recent history of boxing have been as thrilling. 在近期拳擊史上沒有幾場比賽曾如此驚心動魄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>contest</b> is a struggle to win power or control. 爭奪","examples":["The state election in November will be the last such ballot before next year's presidential contest. 11月的州選舉將是明年的總統競選前最後一輪這類投票。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contest</b> a statement or decision, you object to it formally because you think it is wrong or unreasonable. 對…提出抗辯","examples":["Your former employer has to reply within 14 days in order to contest the case. 你的前僱主得在14天內做出答覆以對本案提出抗辯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>contests</b> an election or competition, they take part in it and try to win it. 參加 (競選或比賽)","examples":["He quickly won his party's nomination to contest the elections. 他迅速贏得了其黨派的提名來參加競選。"]}]}]},"context":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背景，環境；上下文，語境"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>context</b> <b>of</b> an idea or event is the general situation that relates to it, and which helps it to be understood. 背景","examples":["We are doing this work in the context of reforms in the economic, social and cultural spheres. 我們正在經濟、社會和文化領域改革的背景下從事這項工作。","It helps to understand the historical context in which Chaucer wrote. 這有助於理解喬叟創作時的歷史背景。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>context</b> of a word, sentence, or text consists of the words, sentences, or text before and after it which help to make its meaning clear. 語境","examples":["Without a context, I would have assumed it was written by a man. 如果沒有一個語境，我會以為這是由一個男人寫的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is seen <b>in context</b> or if it is put <b>into context</b>, it is considered together with all the factors that relate to it. 聯絡背景地","examples":["Taxation is not popular in principle, merely acceptable in context. 徵稅原則上不受大眾歡迎，只是聯絡背景看是可接受的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a statement or remark is quoted <b>out of context</b>, the circumstances in which it was said are not correctly reported, so that it seems to mean something different from the meaning that was intended. 脫離語境地","examples":["Thomas says that he has been quoted out of context. 托馬斯說，他的話被斷章取義了。"]}]}]},"cooperation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"合作，協作；協助，配合"}],"sections":[]},"contribution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貢獻，促成作用；捐款，捐助；（保險金、養老金等的）定期繳款；稿件，投稿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>contribution</b> <b>to</b> something, you do something to help make it successful or to produce it. 貢獻","examples":["American economists have made important contributions to the field of financial and corporate economics. 美國經濟學家在金融社團經濟學領域做出了重要貢獻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>contribution</b> is a sum of money that you give in order to help pay for something. 捐款","examples":["This list ranked companies that make charitable contributions of a half million dollars or more. 這張清單列出了慈善捐款50萬美元及50萬美元以上的公司。"]}]}]},"convenience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方便，便利；便利的事物，便利設施；公共廁所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done for your <b>convenience</b>, it is done in a way that is useful or suitable for you. 便利","examples":["He was happy to make a detour for her convenience. 為了方便她，他樂意繞道而行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as a <b>convenience</b>, you mean that it is very useful. 方便","examples":["Mail order is a convenience for buyers who are too busy to shop. 郵購對於那些沒有時間購物的人來說是很方便的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Conveniences</b> are pieces of equipment designed to make your life easier. 便利設施","examples":["...an apartment with all the modern conveniences. …一套配備了各種現代便利設施的公寓。"]}]}]},"convention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"習俗，慣例；大會，集會；公約，協定；（文學、藝術上的）傳統手法，傳統風格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>convention</b> is a way of behaving that is considered to be correct or polite by most people in a society. 習俗","examples":["It's just a social convention that men don't wear skirts. 男人不穿裙子僅僅是一個社會習俗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In art, literature, or the theatre, a <b>convention</b> is a traditional method or style. 慣例","examples":["We go offstage and come back for the convention of the encore. 按照慣例，當要求我們再唱一次的時候，我們得先下臺然後再返回臺上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>convention</b> is an official agreement between countries or groups of people. 公約","examples":["...the U.N. convention on climate change. …關於氣候變化的聯合國公約。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>convention</b> is a large meeting of an organization or political group. 大型會議","examples":["...the annual convention of the Society of Professional Journalists. …職業新聞工作者協會的年會。"]}]}]},"contrary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相反的，相對的；乖戾的，好與人作對的；逆向的，逆行的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"相反的事實（或事情、情況）；對立命題，反對命題"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相反地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Ideas, attitudes, or reactions that are <b>contrary</b> <b>to</b> each other are completely different from each other. (觀點、態度、反應) 相對立的","examples":["This view is contrary to the aims of critical social research for a number of reasons. 許多原因證明這種觀點與批判性社會研究的目的截然相反。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is true <b>contrary to</b> other people's beliefs or opinions, you are emphasizing that it is true and that they are wrong. 與…相反","examples":["Contrary to popular belief, moderate exercise actually decreases your appetite. 與大部分人的想法相反，適度的運動實際上會降低食慾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>on the contrary</b> when you have just said or implied that something is not true and are going to say that the opposite is true. 恰恰相反","examples":["It is not an idea around which the community can unite. On the contrary, I see it as one that will divide us. 這不是一個可以讓我們的組織團結起來的主意。恰恰相反，我看它會分裂我們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>on the contrary</b> when you are disagreeing strongly with something that has just been said or implied, or are making a strong negative reply. 相反 (用於否定對方意見)","examples":["\"People just don't do things like that.\"—\"On the contrary, they do them all the time.\" “人們根本就不像那樣做事。” —“然而，他們卻一直在那麼做。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a particular idea is being considered, evidence or statements <b>to the contrary</b> suggest that this idea is not true or that the opposite is true. 相反 (用於否定前面的陳述)","examples":["He continued to maintain that he did nothing wrong, despite clear evidence to the contrary. 他仍堅持認為自己沒有做錯，儘管有確鑿的證據證明他做錯了。"]}]}]},"content":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滿足的，滿意的，甘願的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"目錄；所含物，容納的東西；（書、文章、演講、電影等的）內容；含量；滿足，滿意；投贊成票的貴族院議員；網上資訊，電子資訊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使滿意，使滿足"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>contents</b> of a container such as a bottle, box, or room are the things that are inside it. (瓶子、盒子或房間的) 所容之物","examples":["Empty the contents of the pan into the sieve. 將平鍋裡的東西全部倒入漏勺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>contents</b> of a book are its different chapters and sections, usually shown in a list at the beginning of the book. (書的) 目錄","examples":["There is no Table of Contents. 沒有目錄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>content</b> or <b>contents</b> of something such as a book, television programme, or website, you are referring to the subject that it deals with, the story that it tells, or the ideas that it expresses. (書、電視節目或網站等的) 內容","examples":["She is reluctant to discuss the content of the play. 她不願討論這部話劇的內容。","Stricter controls were placed on the content of videos. 對錄影的內容有了更嚴格的控制。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>content</b> of something such as an educational course or a programme of action is the elements that it consists of. (課程或計劃的) 內容","examples":["Previous students have had nothing but praise for the course content and staff. 以前的學生們對該課程的內容和教師只有稱讚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>content</b> to refer to the amount or proportion of something that a substance contains. 含量","examples":["Sunflower margarine has the same fat content as butter. 葵花籽人造黃油跟黃油的脂肪含量一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>content</b> <b>with</b> something, you are willing to accept it, rather than wanting something more or something better. 滿足的","examples":["I am content to admire the mountains from below. 我滿足於從山下觀賞群山。","I'm perfectly content with the way the campaign has gone. 我對這次活動開展的情況感到心滿意足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>content</b>, you are fairly happy or satisfied. 滿意的","examples":["He says his daughter is quite content. 他說他的女兒頗為滿意。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make (oneself or another person) content or satisfied 使滿足","examples":[]}]}]},"cooperative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合作的，協作的；樂於配合的；（企業或其他組織）合作性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"合作性組織"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cooperative</b> is a business or organization run by the people who work for it, or owned by the people who use it. These people share its benefits and profits. 合作性企業; 合作性組織","examples":["They decided a housing cooperative was the way to regenerate the area. 他們決定用合作建房的方式重建這一地區。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cooperative</b> activity is done by people working together. 合作的","examples":["He was transferred to FBI custody in a smooth cooperative effort between Egyptian and U.S. authorities. 經埃及和美國政府的順利合作，他被移交給了聯邦調查局關押。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>cooperative</b>, you mean that they do what you ask them to without complaining or arguing. 樂意合作的","examples":["I made every effort to be cooperative. 我盡力配合。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合作地","examples":["They agreed to work cooperatively to ease tensions wherever possible. 他們同意儘可能合作以緩解緊張局面。"]}]}]},"copper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銅；銅錢，銅幣；<非正式>警察；灰蝶，銅色蝶"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紫銅色的，紅棕色的"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用銅包，給……鍍銅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Copper</b> is reddish brown metal that is used to make things such as coins and electrical wires. 銅","examples":["Chile is the world's largest producer of copper. 智利是世界上最大的產銅國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(Often shortened to cop)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Copper</b> is sometimes used to describe things that are reddish-brown in colour. 銅色的","examples":["His hair has reverted back to its original copper hue. 他的頭髮恢復到了原來的銅色。"]}]}]},"contrast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"差異，對比；對照物，明顯不同的事物；（攝影或繪畫中的）顏色反差，明暗對比；（電視螢幕的）影象明暗對比度，反差"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對比，對照；顯出明顯的差異，形成對比"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>contrast</b> is a great difference between two or more things which is clear when you compare them. (巨大的) 差別","examples":["...the contrast between town and country. …城鄉差別。","The two visitors provided a startling contrast in appearance. 兩位來訪者的外貌有驚人的不同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Contrast</b> is the degree of difference between the darker and lighter parts of a photograph, television picture, or painting. (圖片、電視畫面、繪畫中深淺的) 對比度","examples":["...a television with brighter colours, better contrast, and digital sound. …一臺色彩更亮麗、顏色對比度更好、配有數字音響的電視。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>by contrast</b> or <b>in contrast</b>, or <b>in contrast to</b> something, to show that you are mentioning a very different situation from the one you have just mentioned. 相比之下","examples":["The private sector, by contrast, has plenty of money to spend. 私營部門相比之下有很多錢可花。","In contrast, the lives of girls in well-to-do families were often very sheltered. 相比之下，富裕家庭的女孩子們通常都過著養尊處優的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing is <b>in contrast</b> <b>to</b> another, it is very different from it. 與…截然不同","examples":["His public statements have always been in marked contrast to those of his son. 他在公共場合的發言總是和他兒子的話截然不同。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contrast</b> one thing <b>with</b> another, you point out or consider the differences between those things. 對比 (事物以指出不同點)","examples":["She contrasted the situation then with the present crisis. 她把過去的情況與現在的危機進行了對比。","Contrast that approach with what goes on in most organizations. 對比這個方法與大多陣列織運用的方法的不同之處。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>contrasts</b> <b>with</b> another, it is very different from it. 與…形成對比","examples":["Johnson's easy charm contrasted sharply with the prickliness of his boss. 約翰的隨和與他老闆的挑剔形成了鮮明的對比。"]}]}]},"cork":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"栓皮，軟木（南歐和北非的一種橡樹的樹皮）；瓶塞，軟木塞；軟木浮子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用瓶塞塞住；用軟木炭塗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cork</b> is a soft, light substance which forms the bark of a type of Mediterranean tree. 軟木橡樹皮","examples":["...cork floors. …軟木地板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cork</b> is a piece of cork or plastic that is pushed into the opening of a bottle to close it. 瓶塞","examples":["He popped the cork and the champagne fizzed out over the bottle. 他“砰”的一聲開啟瓶塞，香檳酒從瓶中噴出。"]}]}]},"cottage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小屋，村舍，鄉間別墅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cottage</b> is a small house, usually in the country. 村舍","examples":["They used to have a cottage in N.W. Scotland. 他們過去在蘇格蘭西北部有間村舍。"]}]}]},"cord":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"粗線，細繩；電線；燈芯絨褲子；索狀結構；考得（木材單位）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"燈芯絨的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用繩子連線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cord</b> is strong, thick string. 繩索","examples":["The door had been tied shut with a length of nylon cord. 這扇門已經被一段尼龍繩緊緊栓住了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Cord</b> is wire covered in rubber or plastic which connects electrical equipment to an electricity supply. 電線","examples":["...electrical cord. …電源接線。","...an extension cord. …電源延長線。"]}]}]},"costume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"服裝，裝束；戲服，表演服裝；泳衣，泳裝"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（某人）穿上特定服裝"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（戲劇）古裝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An actor's or performer's <b>costume</b> is the set of clothes they wear while they are performing. 戲裝","examples":["Even from a distance, the effect of his fox costume was stunning. 即使從遠處看，他的狐裝造型也非常漂亮。","The performers, in costume and makeup, were walking up and down backstage. 演員們穿著戲服化著妝，在後臺走來走去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The clothes worn by people at a particular time in history, or in a particular country, are referred to as a particular type of <b>costume</b>. (某一歷史時期或某一國家人們穿的) 服裝","examples":["...men and women in eighteenth-century costume. …身著18世紀服裝的男男女女。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>costume</b> drama is one which is set in the past and in which the actors wear the type of clothes that were worn in that period. 古裝的","examples":["...a lavish costume drama set in Ireland and the U.S. in the 1890s. …以19世紀90年代的愛爾蘭和美國為背景的一部大型古裝戲。"]}]}]},"council":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"委員會，理事會；政務委員會，地方議會；會議；（教會的）集會"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地方政府廉租的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>council</b> is a group of people who are elected to govern a local area such as a city. 政務委員會","examples":["The city council has voted almost unanimously in favour. 市議會幾乎全部投了贊成票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Council</b> is used in the names of some organizations. 委員會","examples":["...the National Council for Civil Liberties. …國家公民自由委員會。","...the Arts Council. …藝術委員會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some organizations, the <b>council</b> is the group of people that controls or governs it. 管理委員會","examples":["The permanent council of the Organization of American States meets today here in Washington. 美洲國家組織常務委員會今天在華盛頓召開會議。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>council</b> is a specially organized, formal meeting that is attended by a particular group of people. 會議","examples":["President Najibullah said he would call a grand council of all Afghans. 納吉布拉總統說他將召開全阿富汗人大會。"]}]}]},"courtesy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禮貌，彬彬有禮；禮貌的行為（言語）；<古>屈膝禮"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"免費提供的；禮節性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Courtesy</b> is politeness, respect, and consideration for others. 彬彬有禮","examples":["...a gentleman who behaves with the utmost courtesy towards ladies. …一位對女士極為彬彬有禮的紳士。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to <b>the</b> <b>courtesy</b> <b>of</b> doing something, you are referring to a polite action. 彬彬有禮的舉止","examples":["By extending the courtesy of a phone call to my clients, I was building a personal relationship with them. 透過給客戶打電話這樣有禮的行為，我漸漸和他們建立起私交。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Courtesy</b> is used to describe services that are provided free of charge by an organization to its customers, or to the general public. 免費的","examples":["A courtesy shuttle bus operates between the hotel and the town. 一輛免費運送班車在旅館和小鎮之間往返。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>courtesy</b> call or a <b>courtesy</b> visit is a formal visit that you pay someone as a way of showing them politeness or respect. 出於禮節的","examples":["The president paid a courtesy call on Emperor Akihito. 總統禮節性地拜訪了明仁天皇。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is provided <b>courtesy of</b> someone or <b>by courtesy of</b> someone, they provide it. You often use this expression in order to thank them. 蒙…的好意","examples":["The waitress brings over some congratulatory glasses of champagne, courtesy of the restaurant. 蒙飯店的好意，女侍者們送過來幾杯表示祝賀的香檳酒。"]}]}]},"creativity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"創造力，獨創性"}],"sections":[]},"creation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"創造，建立；作品，創作；（上帝）創造天地；宇宙，世界，天地萬物；授予，冊封"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In many religions, <b>creation</b> is the making of the universe, earth, and creatures by God. 上帝造物","examples":["...the Creation of the universe as told in Genesis Chapter One. …如《創世紀》第一章中講述的上帝創造天地萬物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People sometimes refer to the whole universe as <b>creation</b>. 全宇宙","examples":["The whole of creation is made up of energy. 全宇宙是由能量構成的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to something that someone has made as a <b>creation</b>, especially if it shows skill, imagination, or artistic ability. 創作","examples":["The bathroom is entirely my own creation. 這個浴室完全是我個人的創作。"]}]}]},"counter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"櫃檯；對立面；計數器，計算器；（棋盤遊戲的）籌碼；記分冰壺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"反駁，駁斥；抵制，抵消；（拳擊）還擊；逆向移動"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相反地，對立地；逆向地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反面的，對立的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a place such as a shop or café, a <b>counter</b> is a long narrow table or flat surface at which customers are served. 櫃檯","examples":["...those guys we see working behind the counter at our local video rental shop. …我們所見在本地音像出租商店櫃檯後工作的那些傢伙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>counter</b> is a mechanical or electronic device which keeps a count of something and displays the total. 計數器","examples":["The new answering machine has a call counter. 這種新型的電話答錄機有一個通話計數器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>counter</b> is a small, flat, round object used in board games. 棋子","examples":["...a versatile book which provides boards and counters for fifteen different games. …一本為15種不同棋類遊戲提供棋盤和棋子的多功能書。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is <b>a counter to</b> something else has an opposite effect to it or makes it less effective. 抵消物","examples":["...NATO's traditional role as a counter to the military might of the Warsaw Pact. …北大西洋公約組織作為華沙公約組織軍事力量的遏制力量的傳統角色。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something to <b>counter</b> a particular action or process, you do something which has an opposite effect to it or makes it less effective. 抵消; 抗衡","examples":["The leadership discussed a plan of economic measures to counter the effects of such a blockade. 領導層討論了一項經濟措施計劃來抵消如此封鎖的影響。","Sears countered by filing an antitrust lawsuit. 西爾斯透過提交反壟斷訴訟進行了反擊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a medicine can be bought <b>over the counter</b>, you do not need a prescription to buy it. 不用開處方地","examples":["Are you taking any other medicines whether on prescription or bought over the counter? 你還要其他藥嗎，不管是處方藥還是非處方藥？","...over-the-counter medicines. …非處方藥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Over-the-counter</b> shares are bought and sold directly rather than on a stock exchange. 不透過交易所的","examples":["In national over-the-counter trading yesterday, Clarcor shares tumbled $6.125 to close at $35.625. 昨天在全國場外交易中，克拉克股票跌$6.125，以$35.625收盤。"]}]}]},"cripple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘸子，殘疾人；感情殘廢者，感情有缺陷的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使殘疾，使成為跛子；使（心理上或情感上）出現問題；嚴重損壞，嚴重削弱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person with a physical disability or a serious permanent injury is sometimes referred to as a <b>cripple</b>. 殘疾人; 殘廢人","examples":["She has gone from being a healthy, fit, and sporty young woman to being a cripple. 她從一個健康、強壯、愛好體育運動的年輕姑娘變成了一個殘疾人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is crippled</b> by an injury, it is so serious that they can never move their body properly again. 使受傷致殘","examples":["Mr. Easton was crippled in an accident and had to leave his job. 伊斯頓先生在一場事故中受傷致殘，不得不離開了工作。","He had been warned that another bad fall could cripple him for life. 他被警告說再一次嚴重摔跤會使他終身殘疾。"]}]}]},"critic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"批評家，評論員；批評者，反對……的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>critic</b> is a person who writes about and expresses opinions about things such as books, movies, music, or art. 評論家","examples":["Mather was a film critic for many years. 馬瑟做過多年的電影評論家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>critic</b> of a person or system disapproves of them and criticizes them publicly. 批評者","examples":["The newspaper has been one of the most consistent critics ever of the government. 該報紙是政府最堅持的批評者之一。"]}]}]},"craft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工藝，手藝；船，艇，飛行器；詭計，騙術；行業，職業；手工藝品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"精心製作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a boat, a spacecraft, or an aircraft as a <b>craft</b>. 船; 航天器; 航空器","examples":["With great difficulty, the fisherman manoeuvred his small craft close to the reef. 漁夫艱難地駕著小船靠近了礁石。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>craft</b> is an activity such as weaving, carving, or pottery that involves making things skilfully with your hands. 工藝","examples":["...the arts and crafts of the North American Indians. …北美印第安人的美術工藝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>craft</b> to refer to any activity or job that involves doing something skilfully. 職業","examples":["...the craft of writing. …寫作工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is crafted</b>, it is made skilfully. 精心製作","examples":["The windows would probably have been crafted in the latter part of the Middle Ages. 這些窗戶可能是中世紀後期精製而成。","...original, hand-crafted bags at affordable prices. …價格適中的獨創手工包。"]}]}]},"cruelty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"殘酷，殘忍；不公，虐待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cruelty</b> is behaviour that deliberately causes pain or distress to people or animals. 殘忍","examples":["Britain had laws against cruelty to animals but none to protect children. 英國曾有反對虐待動物的法律，卻沒有一部保護兒童的法律。"]}]}]},"cucumber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃瓜，胡瓜；黃瓜植株（學名 Cucumis sativus）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cucumber</b> is a long thin vegetable with a hard green skin and wet transparent flesh. It is eaten raw in salads. 黃瓜","examples":["...a cheese and cucumber sandwich. …一個乳酪黃瓜三明治。"]}]}]},"criticism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"批評，批判；意見；評論，評價；（對文學作品和歷史文獻的）考證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Criticism</b> is the action of expressing disapproval of something or someone. A <b>criticism</b> is a statement that expresses disapproval. 批評; 反對意見","examples":["This policy had repeatedly come under strong criticism on Capitol Hill. 這項政策在國會反覆受到強烈批評。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Criticism</b> is a serious examination and judgment of something such as a book or play. 評論","examples":["She has published more than 20 books including novels, poetry and literary criticism. 她已出版了二十多本書，其中包括小說、詩歌和文學評論。"]}]}]},"cube":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立方體；立方，三次冪；<美，非正式>小室，小房間"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成立方；把（食物）切成小方塊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cube</b> is a solid object with six square surfaces which are all the same size. 立方體","examples":["...cold water with ice cubes in it. …加冰塊的冷水。","...a box of sugar cubes. …一盒方糖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>cube</b> <b>of</b> a number is another number that is produced by multiplying the first number by itself twice. For example, the cube of 2 is 8. 立方","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>cube</b> food, you cut it into cube-shaped pieces. 將…切成方塊","examples":["Remove the seeds and stones and cube the flesh. 去除籽和核，然後把果肉切成方塊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to raise (a number or quantity) to the third power 求…的立方","examples":[]}]}]},"crush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓壞，擠壓變形；搗碎，碾成粉末；把……擠入，將……塞進（狹小的空間內）；（使）變皺，起皺；制服，鎮壓；使心煩意亂，使消沉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擁擠的人群；（對某人短暫的）熱戀，迷戀；迷戀物件；果汁飲料；（牛，羊的）分群欄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>crush</b> something means to press it very hard so that its shape is destroyed or so that it breaks into pieces. 壓扁; 壓碎","examples":["Andrew crushed his empty can. 安德魯壓扁了他的空罐子。","...crushed ice. …碎冰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>crush</b> a protest or movement, or a group of opponents, means to defeat it completely, usually by force. 鎮壓","examples":["The military operation was the first step in a plan to crush the uprising. 這次軍事行動是鎮壓暴動計劃的第一步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are crushed</b> by something, it upsets you a great deal. 使精神崩潰","examples":["Listen to criticism but don't be crushed by it. 聽批評意見，但不要被它擊垮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are crushed</b> against someone or something, you are pushed or pressed against them. (與某人或某物) 擠在一起","examples":["We were at the front, crushed against the stage. 我們在前面, 被擠得緊挨著舞臺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鎮壓","examples":["...the violent crushing of anti-government demonstrations. …對反政府示威運動的武力鎮壓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crush</b> is a crowd of people close together, in which it is difficult to move. 擁擠的人群","examples":["His thirteen-year-old son somehow got separated in the crush. 他13歲的兒子不知怎麼在擁擠的人群裡走散了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>crush</b> <b>on</b> someone, you are in love with them but do not have a relationship with them. 暗戀","examples":["She had a crush on you, you know. 你知道吧，她曾暗戀過你。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a construction designed to confine and limit the movement of an animal, esp a large or dangerous animal, for examination or to perform a procedure on it 猛獸隔離區","examples":[]}]}]},"crack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破裂，裂開；崩潰，垮掉；砸開，砸碎；破譯，解決；重擊，猛擊；（使）發出爆裂聲，劈啪作響；（嗓音）變嘶啞；說（笑話），開（玩笑）；阻止，打擊；開瓶，（尤指）開瓶飲酒；使（碳氫化合物）裂化"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"裂縫，裂紋；縫隙，窄縫；瑕疵，缺點；爆裂聲，噼啪聲；嘗試，試圖；破解資訊，破解碼；俏皮話，粗魯的話；重擊，猛擊；好時光，友好愉快的交談；嗓音變啞；強效可卡因；<非正式>股溝"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"優秀的，訓練有素的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something hard <b>cracks</b>, or if you <b>crack</b> it, it becomes slightly damaged, with lines appearing on its surface. 使…破裂; 破裂","examples":["A gas main had cracked under my neighbour's garage and gas had seeped into our homes. 鄰居家車庫下的煤氣主管道破裂了，煤氣滲漏進我們家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>cracks</b>, or if you <b>crack</b> it, it makes a sharp sound like the sound of a piece of wood breaking. 使…噼啪作響; 發出闢裂聲","examples":["Thunder cracked in the sky. 空中雷聲炸響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>crack</b> a hard part of your body, such as your knee or your head, you hurt it by accidentally hitting it hard against something. 撞擊","examples":["He cracked his head on the pavement and was knocked cold. 他的頭撞著了路面，撞昏了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>crack</b> something that has a shell, such as an egg or a nut, you break the shell in order to reach the inside part. 叩開","examples":["Crack the eggs into a bowl. 把雞蛋打到碗中。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>crack</b> a problem or a code, you solve it, especially after a lot of thought. 破解 (難題、密碼)","examples":["He has finally cracked the system after years of painstaking research. 經過數年的艱苦研究，他最終破譯了該系統。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>crack</b> a joke, you tell it. 說 (笑話)","examples":["He drove a Volkswagen, cracked jokes, and talked about beer and girls. 那時他開著一輛大眾牌汽車，講著笑話，談論著啤酒和女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>cracks</b>, they lose control of their emotions or actions because they are under a lot of pressure. (精神) 垮掉","examples":["She's calm and strong, and she is just not going to crack. 她冷靜而堅強，決不會垮掉的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your voice <b>cracks</b> when you are speaking or singing, it changes in pitch because you are feeling a strong emotion. (嗓音) 突然變化","examples":["Her voice cracked and she began to cry. 她失聲哭了起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crack</b> is a very narrow gap between two things, or between two parts of a thing. 裂縫","examples":["Kathryn had seen him through a crack in the curtains. 凱瑟琳曾從簾子的裂縫看到過他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crack</b> is a line that appears on the surface of something when it is slightly damaged. 裂紋","examples":["The plate had a crack in it. 這盤子上有條裂紋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you open something such as a door, window, or curtain <b>a crack</b>, you open it only a small amount. 縫隙","examples":["He went to the door, opened it a crack, and listened. 他走到門邊，把門開啟一條縫，聽了起來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>crack</b> is a sharp sound, like the sound of a piece of wood breaking. 爆裂聲","examples":["Suddenly there was a loud crack and glass flew into the car. 突然一陣巨大的爆裂聲，碎玻璃飛濺進了車內。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Crack</b> is a very pure form of the drug cocaine. 強效純可卡因","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>crack</b> is a slightly rude or cruel joke. (挖苦人的) 笑話","examples":["Tell Tracy you're sorry for that crack about her weight. 告訴特蕾西你對那個有關她體重的玩笑感到抱歉。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crack</b> soldier or sportsman is highly trained and very skilful. 訓練有素的","examples":["...a crack undercover police officer. …一名訓練有素的臥底警察。"]}]}]},"cunning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狡猾的，詭詐的；靈巧的，巧妙的；<美>可愛的，好看的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"狡猾，詭詐；靈巧，巧妙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cunning</b> has the ability to achieve things in a clever way, often by deceiving other people. 狡猾的","examples":["These disturbed kids can be cunning. 這些心理失常的小孩可能會很狡猾。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狡猾地","examples":["They were cunningly disguised in golf clothes. 他們狡猾地穿上高爾夫球服把自己偽裝起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cunning</b> is the ability to achieve things in a clever way, often by deceiving other people. 狡猾","examples":["...one more example of the cunning of today's art thieves. …又一個關於當今藝術品大盜狡猾伎倆的例子。"]}]}]},"cue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暗示，提示；（戲劇或電影中的）尾白，提示；（檯球等的）球杆；線索；選聽（或選看）鍵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提示，暗示；用球杆擊球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the theatre or in a musical performance, a performer's <b>cue</b> is something another performer says or does that is a signal for them to begin speaking, playing, or doing something. (在戲劇或音樂表演中提示表演者說話、演奏或動作的) 提示","examples":["The actors not performing sit at the side of the stage in full view, waiting for their cues. 未表演的男演員們坐在舞臺邊，對舞臺一覽無餘，他們等待著上場的提示。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something that happens is a <b>cue</b> <b>for</b> an action, you mean that people start doing that action when it happens. 觸發事件","examples":["That was the cue for several months of intense bargaining. 此事觸發了此後數月激烈的討價還價。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cue</b> is a long, thin wooden stick that is used to hit the ball in games such as billiards, pool, and snooker. (檯球等所用的) 球杆","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one performer <b>cues</b> another, they say or do something which is a signal for the second performer to begin speaking, playing, or doing something. (為下一位演員) 提示","examples":["He read the scene, with Seaton cueing him. 在西頓提示下，他朗誦了這一場的臺詞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to drive (a ball) with a cue (用球杆)擊球","examples":[]}]}]},"curiosity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"好奇心，求知慾；珍品，奇事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curiosity</b> is a desire to know about something. 好奇心","examples":["Ryle accepted more out of curiosity than anything else. 賴爾接受更多是出於好奇心而不是別的原因。","...enthusiasm and genuine curiosity about the past. …對過去的熱情和真正的好奇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>curiosity</b> is something that is unusual, interesting, and fairly rare. 奇珍異寶","examples":["There is much to see in the way of castles, curiosities, and museums. 那裡有許多可看的城堡、奇珍異寶和博物館。"]}]}]},"curse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"罵人話，咒罵語；咒語，魔咒；禍根，禍因；月經，例假（the curse）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"詛咒，咒罵；（在心裡）臭罵；唸咒語詛咒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>curse</b>, you use very impolite or offensive language, usually because you are angry about something. 詛咒","examples":["I cursed and hobbled to my feet. 我詛咒著，蹣跚著站起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curse</b> is also a noun. 詛咒","examples":["He shot her an angry look and a curse. 他投給她憤怒的一瞥和一句詛咒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that there is a <b>curse</b> <b>on</b> someone, you mean that there seems to be a supernatural power causing unpleasant things to happen to them. (對某人的) 詛咒","examples":["Maybe there is a curse on my family. 也許存在對我的家族的詛咒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to something that causes a great deal of trouble or harm as a <b>curse</b>. 禍根","examples":["Apathy is the long-standing curse of democracy. 冷漠是民主的長期禍根。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>curse</b> someone, you say insulting things to them because you are angry with them. 咒罵 (某人)","examples":["Grandma protested, but he cursed her and rudely pushed her aside. 奶奶反對，但他咒罵她，還粗暴地把她推到一邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>curse</b> something, you complain angrily about it, especially using very impolite language. 詛咒 (某事)","examples":["So we set off again, cursing the delay, toward the west. 於是我們再次出發，詛咒著延誤，向西走。"]}]}]},"curl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）彎曲，捲曲；（使）盤繞，（使）彎彎曲曲移動；邊緣翹起；撇（嘴）；參加冰壺運動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬈髮，捲髮；（頭髮的）捲曲；捲曲物，螺旋狀物；（鍛鍊肌肉的）彎曲運動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>curls</b>, your hair is in the form of tight curves and spirals. 捲髮","examples":["...the little girl with blonde curls. …長著金黃色捲髮的小女孩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>curl</b> <b>of</b> something is a piece or quantity of it that is curved or spiral in shape. 捲曲狀或螺旋狀","examples":["A thin curl of smoke rose from a rusty stove. 一縷薄薄的青煙從生鏽的爐子裡冉冉升起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your hair has <b>curl</b>, it is full of curls. 捲曲","examples":["Dry curly hair naturally for maximum curl and shine. 讓捲髮自然地風乾以最大限度地增加頭髮的捲曲和光澤。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your hair <b>curls</b> or if you <b>curl</b> it, it is full of curls. 捲曲; 使捲曲","examples":["She has hair that refuses to curl. 她的頭髮怎麼也不卷。","Maria had curled her hair for the event. 瑪麗亞為這次活動捲了頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your toes, fingers, or other parts of your body <b>curl</b>, or if you <b>curl</b> them, they form a curved or round shape. 彎曲; 使彎曲","examples":["His fingers curled gently around her wrist. 他的手指輕握住她的手腕。","Raise one foot, curl the toes and point the foot downwards. 抬起一隻腳，將腳趾彎曲，將腳向下指。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>curls</b> somewhere, or if you <b>curl</b> it there, it moves there in a spiral or curve. 繚繞; 使纏繞","examples":["Smoke was curling up the chimney. 煙順著煙囪繚繞升起。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>curls into</b> a ball, they move into a position in which their body makes a rounded shape. 蜷作一團","examples":["He wanted to curl into a tiny ball. 他想把自己蜷成一個小團。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a leaf, a piece of paper, or another flat object <b>curls</b>, its edges bend toward the centre. 卷邊","examples":["The rose leaves have curled because of an attack by grubs. 玫瑰的葉子因蟲子的侵襲打了卷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curl up</b> means the same as . 蜷作一團","examples":["In colder weather, your cat will curl up into a tight, heat-conserving ball. 在更冷的天氣裡，你的貓會蜷縮成緊緊的一團來保暖。","She curled up next to him. 她蜷臥在他身邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Curl up</b> means the same as . 捲起","examples":["The corners of the rug were curling up. 地毯的各角捲起來了。"]}]}]},"deadline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"最後期限，截止日期；<史>（監獄周圍的）死線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deadline</b> is a time or date before which a particular task must be finished or a particular thing must be done. 最後期限","examples":["We were not able to meet the deadline because of manufacturing delays. 由於生產延誤，我們沒能在截止日期前完成工作。"]}]}]},"damp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"潮溼的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"溼氣，潮氣；沼氣；氣餒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使潮溼，弄溼；減弱，抑制；把（火）調小；限止（鋼琴或其他樂器琴絃）的音；減幅，阻尼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>damp</b> is slightly wet. 潮溼的","examples":["Her hair was still damp. 她的頭髮還有點溼。","...the damp, cold air. …又潮又冷的空氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Damp</b> is moisture on the inside walls of a house or in the air. 潮氣","examples":["There was damp everywhere and the entire building was in need of rewiring. 到處是潮氣，整座建築需要安裝新電線。"]}]}]},"curve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"曲線，弧線；轉彎，彎道；圖表曲線；曲線球；（身體的）曲線"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）彎曲，（使）呈曲線形"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"彎曲的，曲線形的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>curve</b> is a smooth, gradually bending line, for example, part of the edge of a circle. 曲線","examples":["...the curve of his lips. …他嘴唇的曲線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a change in something as a particular <b>curve</b>, especially when it is represented on a graph. (圖表中的) 曲線","examples":["Youth crime overall is on a slow but steady downward curve. 青年犯罪總體上呈一個緩慢但持續下降的曲線。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>curves</b>, or if someone or something <b>curves</b> it, it has the shape of a curve. 使彎曲; 變彎","examples":["Her spine curved. 她的脊柱彎了。","...a knife with a slightly curving blade. …一把刀刃略彎的刀。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>curves</b>, it moves in a curve, for example, through the air. 沿曲線運動","examples":["The ball curved strangely in the air. 球在空中劃出奇怪的弧線。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>throws</b> you <b>a curve</b> or <b>throws</b> you <b>a curve ball</b>, they surprise you by doing something that you do not expect. 給某人驚喜","examples":["At the last minute, I threw them a curve ball by saying, \"We're going to bring spouses.\" 在最後一刻，我給了他們一個驚喜，說：“我們會帶配偶。”"]}]}]},"decoration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"裝飾，裝飾品；勳章，獎章；裝潢，裝飾風格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>decoration</b> of a room is its furniture, wallpaper, and ornaments. 裝飾","examples":["The decoration and furnishings had to be practical enough for a family home. 裝修和傢俱陳設必須對一個家庭住房來說夠實用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Decorations</b> are features that are added to something in order to make it look more attractive. 裝飾品","examples":["The only wall decorations are candles and a single mirror. 牆上僅有的裝飾品就是一些蠟燭和一面鏡子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Decorations</b> are brightly coloured objects such as pieces of paper and balloons, which you put up in a room on special occasions to make it look more attractive. 顏色鮮豔的飾品","examples":["Colourful streamers and paper decorations had been hung from the ceiling. 五顏六色的飄帶和彩紙飾品被掛在天花板上。"]}]}]},"cushion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"墊子，坐墊；減震墊，緩衝墊；起緩解作用的東西；大比分領先，穩操勝券；（檯球桌的）彈性襯邊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩衝；減輕……的影響；給…安上墊子，把……安置在墊子上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cushion</b> is a fabric case filled with soft material, which you put on a seat to make it more comfortable. 坐墊","examples":["...a velvet cushion. …一個天鵝絨坐墊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cushion</b> is a soft pad or barrier, especially one that protects something. 軟墊","examples":["The company provides a styrofoam cushion to protect the tablets during shipping. 該公司提供一種聚苯乙烯泡沫塑膠墊層用來在裝運時保護牌匾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is a <b>cushion</b> <b>against</b> something unpleasant reduces its effect. 緩解物","examples":["Welfare provides a cushion against hardship. 福利給困苦提供了一個緩解。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>cushions</b> an object when it hits something protects it by reducing the force of the impact. 緩衝","examples":["There is also a new steering wheel with an energy-absorbing rim to cushion the driver's head in the worst impacts. 還有新式方向盤，其邊緣具有減震功能在最嚴重的衝擊中緩衝保護司機的頭部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>cushion</b> the effect of something unpleasant means to reduce it. 緩解","examples":["They said Western aid was needed to cushion the blows of vital reform. 他們說需要西方國家的援助以緩解重大變革的衝擊。"]}]}]},"damn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"該死，見鬼（表示很生氣或失望）；天啊（表示讚歎或驚奇）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"該死的（表示對某人或某物生氣）；（用於加強語氣）十足的，完全的；"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極其，非常；絲毫不"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"嚴厲批評，譴責；（表憤怒或厭煩）該死，討厭，混賬；令（某人）下地獄；（強調對某事毫不在意）不管，無所謂；真沒想到，真讓我吃驚；決不，絕對不；貶斥，把……說得很糟糕；左右為難，做也不是，不做也不是；註定受難（或失敗）；詛咒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一點點，絲毫；（對……）在乎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Damn</b>, <b>damn it</b>, and <b>dammit</b> are used by some people to express anger or impatience. 該死; 討厭 (口語中表達憤怒、厭煩等)","examples":["Don't be flippant, damn it! This is serious. 別吊兒郎當的，該死！這是很嚴肅的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Damn</b> is used by some people to emphasize what they are saying. 非常 (用以加強語氣)","examples":["There's not a damn thing you can do about it now. 在這件事上你現在根本什麼都做不了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Damn</b> is also an adverb. 非常地","examples":["As it turned out, I was damn right. 事實證明，我的做法完全正確。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person or a news report <b>damns</b> something such as a policy or action, you mean that they are very critical of it. 譴責","examples":["...a sensational book in which she damns the ultraright party. …她譴責極右黨派的一本聳人聽聞的書。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>does not give a damn</b> about something, you are emphasizing that they do not care about it at all. 毫不在乎","examples":["I don't give a damn about the money, Nicole. 我根本不是在乎錢，尼科爾。"]}]}]},"decrease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）減少，（使）降低"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"減少，降低"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>decreases</b> or when you <b>decrease</b> it, it becomes less in quantity, size, or intensity. 使降低; 降低","examples":["Population growth is decreasing by 1.4% each year. 人口增長每年下降1.4%。","The number of independent firms decreased from 198 to 96. 獨立公司的數量從198家減到了96家。","Since 1945 air forces have decreased in size. 1945年以來，空軍的規模已經縮小。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>decrease</b> <b>in</b> the quantity, size, or intensity of something is a reduction in it. 減少; 降低","examples":["In Spain and Portugal there has been a decrease in the number of young people out of work. 在西班牙和葡萄牙，失業青年人數已經有所下降。"]}]}]},"defense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"防禦，保衛；防禦物，防禦能力；國防機構，國防體系；辯解，辯白；被告，辯護律師；（法庭上的）辯護，答辯； 防守隊員，防守；（競賽中的）衛冕，（選舉中的）保住席位；戒備心理，自我防衛；國際象棋的防禦（黑棋的某種特定走法）"}],"sections":[]},"defeat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擊敗，戰勝；困惑，難住；使失敗，阻撓；反對（動議或提議）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"失敗，戰敗；戰勝，擊敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>defeat</b> someone, you win a victory over them in a battle, game, or contest. 擊敗","examples":["His guerrillas defeated the colonial army in 1954. 他的游擊隊在1954年打敗了殖民軍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a proposal or motion in a debate <b>is defeated</b>, more people vote against it than for it. (以多數票) 挫敗","examples":["The bill was defeated with support from only two congressmen. 由於只得到兩位議員的支援，那個議案被否決了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a task or a problem <b>defeats</b> you, it is so difficult that you cannot do it or solve it. 難倒","examples":["The book he most wanted to write was the one which nearly defeated him. 他最想寫的書恰恰是幾乎難倒他的那一本。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>defeat</b> an action or plan means to cause it to fail. 使受挫","examples":["The navy played a limited but significant role in defeating the rebellion. 在平息叛亂中海軍起了有限但卻重要的作用。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Defeat</b> is the experience of being beaten in a battle, game, or contest, or of failing to achieve what you wanted to. 失敗","examples":["The most important thing is not to admit defeat until you really have to. 最重要的事就是非到不得已不要認輸。","...the Sonics' 31-point defeat at Sacramento on Sunday. …超音速隊週日在薩克拉門託31分的挫敗。"]}]}]},"delight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高興；令人高興的人或物，樂事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使高興；以……為樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Delight</b> is a feeling of very great pleasure. 高興; 欣喜","examples":["Throughout the house, the views are a constant source of surprise and delight. 整個房子，目之所及不停帶來驚奇和欣喜。","Andrew roared with delight when he heard Rachel's nickname for the baby. 安德魯聽到雷切爾給那個嬰兒起的愛稱時，高興地叫起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone or something that gives you great pleasure or enjoyment as a <b>delight</b>. 樂事; 樂趣","examples":["The aircraft was a delight to fly. 駕乘這種飛機是一件樂事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>takes delight</b> or <b>takes a delight</b> <b>in</b> something, they get a lot of pleasure from it. 以…為樂","examples":["Haig took obvious delight in proving his critics wrong. 海格顯然以證明他的批評者是錯誤的為樂。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>delights</b> you, it gives you a lot of pleasure. 使高興; 使欣喜","examples":["She has created a style of music that has delighted audiences all over the world. 她創立了一種為全世界聽眾所喜愛的音樂風格。"]}]}]},"demonstration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"演示，展示；遊行，示威；證實；表達，表露"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>demonstration</b> is a march or gathering which people take part in to show their opposition to something or their support for something. 示威遊行; 示威集會","examples":["Riot police used tear gas to break up the demonstration. 防暴警察使用了催淚瓦斯驅散示威遊行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>demonstration</b> of something is a talk by someone who shows you how to do it or how it works. 展示","examples":["...a cooking demonstration. …一次烹調展示。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>demonstration</b> <b>of</b> a fact or situation is a clear proof of it. 證明","examples":["It was an unprecedented demonstration of people power by the citizens of Moscow. 這是莫斯科市民對人民力量史無前例的證明。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>demonstration of</b> a quality or feeling is an expression of it. (品質、感情的) 展現","examples":["There's been no public demonstration of opposition to the president. 還沒有反對總統的公開展現。"]}]}]},"dependent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"依賴的，依靠的；取決於；有癮的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"受供養者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>dependent</b> <b>on</b> something or someone means to need them in order to succeed or be able to survive. 依靠的","examples":["The local economy is overwhelmingly dependent on oil and gas extraction. 當地經濟嚴重依賴石油和天然氣提煉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing is <b>dependent</b> <b>on</b> another, the first thing will be affected or determined by the second. 取決於…的","examples":["...companies whose earnings are largely dependent on the performance of the Chinese economy. …盈利很大程度上取決於中國經濟表現的公司。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dependent</b> is the same as . 同dependant","examples":[]}]}]},"destruction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"破壞，摧毀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Destruction</b> is the act of destroying something, or the state of being destroyed. 毀滅","examples":["...an international agreement aimed at halting the destruction of the ozone layer. …一項旨在停止對臭氧層的破壞的國際協議。"]}]}]},"departure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背離；離開，啟程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Departure</b> or a <b>departure</b> is the act of going away from somewhere. 離開","examples":["...the president's departure for Helsinki. …總統前往赫爾辛基。","They hoped this would lead to the departure of all foreign forces from the country. 他們希望這會導致所有外國軍隊從該國的撤離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something different or unusual, you can refer to their action as a <b>departure</b>. 背離","examples":["Such a move would have been a startling departure from tradition. 這一舉措原本會是對傳統習俗驚人的背離。"]}]}]},"detective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偵探，警探；私家偵探"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有關調查工作的；刑偵的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>detective</b> is someone whose job is to discover what has happened in a crime or other situation and to find the people involved. Some detectives work in the police force and others work privately. 偵探","examples":["Now detectives are appealing for witnesses who may have seen anything suspicious last night. 現在偵探們正在呼籲昨晚可能看到任何可疑情況的人出來作證。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>detective</b> novel or story is one in which a detective tries to solve a crime. 偵探的","examples":["...Arthur Conan Doyle's classic detective novel. …阿瑟·柯南·道爾的經典偵探小說。"]}]}]},"depression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抑鬱，沮喪；蕭條（期），不景氣；低氣壓；凹陷，淺坑；俯角，俯視角"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Depression</b> is a mental state in which you are sad and feel that you cannot enjoy anything, because your situation is so difficult and unpleasant. 抑鬱","examples":["Mr. Thomas was suffering from depression. 托馬斯先生當時正受抑鬱症折磨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>depression</b> is a time when there is very little economic activity, which causes a lot of unemployment and poverty. 蕭條期","examples":["He never forgot the hardships he witnessed during the Great Depression of the 1930s. 他從未忘記20世紀30年代經濟大蕭條時期他所目睹的艱辛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>depression</b> in a surface is an area which is lower than the parts surrounding it. 窪地","examples":["...an area pockmarked by rain-filled depressions. …一個到處都是積滿雨水的窪坑的地帶。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>depression</b> is a mass of air that has a low pressure and that often causes rain. 低氣壓","examples":["To the northwest lies a depression with clouds and rain. 西北方向有一個雲雨密佈的低氣壓。"]}]}]},"diaper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>尿布；重複菱形花紋的棉麻織物；（裝飾面上）重複的幾何（或花卉）圖案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>給……墊尿布；用重複的幾何（或花卉）圖案裝飾（表面）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diaper</b> is a piece of soft towel or paper, which you fasten around a baby's bottom in order to contain its urine and faeces. 尿布; 紙尿片","examples":["He never changed her diapers, never bathed her. 他從不給她換尿布，也不給她洗澡。"]}]}]},"demand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"強烈要求；需要，需求"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"堅決的要求；需求，需求量；（困難的）要求"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>demand</b> something such as information or action, you ask for it in a very forceful way. 強烈要求","examples":["Human rights groups are demanding an investigation into the shooting. 人權組織正強烈要求對這一槍擊案進行調查。","Russia demanded that UNITA send a delegation to the peace talks. 俄羅斯強烈要求安哥拉徹底獨立全國同盟派遣一個代表團參加和談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>demands</b> another, the first needs the second in order to happen or be dealt with successfully. 需要","examples":["He said the task of reconstruction would demand much patience, hard work, and sacrifice. 他說重建工作會需要高度堅韌、勤勞和奉獻。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>demand</b> is a firm request for something. 堅決的要求","examples":["There have been demands for services from tenants up there. 那邊的房客們有服務的明確要求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to <b>demand</b>, or to the <b>demand</b> <b>for</b> something, you are referring to how many people want to have it, do it, or buy it. 需求量","examples":["Another flight would be arranged on Saturday if sufficient demand arose. 如果有足夠的需求量，週六就會安排另一個航班。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>demands</b> <b>of</b> something or its <b>demands</b> <b>on</b> you are the things which it needs or the things which you have to do for it. 要求","examples":["...the demands and challenges of a new job. …一份新工作的要求和挑戰。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in demand</b> or <b>in great demand</b>, they are very popular and a lot of people want them. 受歡迎的","examples":["He was much in demand as a lecturer in the U.S., as well as at universities all over Europe. 他在美國是個非常受歡迎的演講者，在全歐洲的大學中也是。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is available or happens <b>on demand</b>, you can have it or it happens whenever you want it or ask for it. 一經要求","examples":["...a new entertainment system that offers 25 movies on demand. …一經要求，即可播放25部電影的新的娛樂系統。"]}]}]},"determination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"決心，堅定；決定，裁定；測定，確定；<法律>（財產權、利息的）終止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Determination</b> is the quality that you show when you have decided to do something and you will not let anything stop you. 決心","examples":["Everyone concerned acted with great courage and determination. 每個相關的人都以巨大的勇氣和決心行動了。"]}]}]},"device":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"裝置，裝置；手段，方法；花招，詭計；炸彈，爆炸裝置；圖畫，設計；<古>（某物的）樣式，外表"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>device</b> is an object that has been invented for a particular purpose, for example, for recording or measuring something. 儀器","examples":["...the electronic device that tells the starter when an athlete has moved from his blocks prematurely. …能在運動員搶跑時通知發令員的電子儀器。"]}]}]},"digestion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消化；消化能力；（使用酶或溶劑的）分解，提煉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Digestion</b> is the process of digesting food. 消化","examples":["No liquids are served with meals because they interfere with digestion. 上菜時不提供飲料，因為會妨礙消化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>digestion</b> is the system in your body which digests your food. 消化系統","examples":["Keep your digestion working well by eating plenty of fibre. 吃大量的食物纖維來保持消化系統正常工作。"]}]}]},"diligence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勤奮，用功；公共馬車"}],"sections":[]},"dignity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尊嚴，自尊；莊嚴，端莊，莊重；尊貴，高貴，高尚；高位，顯職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone behaves or moves with <b>dignity</b>, they are calm, controlled, and admirable. 尊貴","examples":["...her extraordinary dignity and composure. …她無與倫比的高貴與冷靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>dignity</b> of people or their lives or activities, you mean that they are valuable and worthy of respect. 尊嚴","examples":["...the sense of human dignity. …人的尊嚴感。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>dignity</b> is the sense that you have of your own importance and value, and other people's respect for you. 自尊","examples":["She still has her dignity. 她還有自尊。"]}]}]},"diplomat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外交官，外交家；有手腕的人，善交際的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diplomat</b> is a senior official who discusses affairs with another country on behalf of his or her own country, usually working as a member of an embassy. 外交官","examples":["...a Western diplomat with long experience in Asia. …一名在亞洲有長期經驗的西方外交官。"]}]}]},"diploma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"畢業文憑，學位證書；文憑課程，職業課程；公文，文書"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diploma</b> is a document which may be awarded to a student who has completed a course of study by a university or college, or by a high school in the United States. 文憑","examples":["...a new two-year course leading to a diploma in social work. ...一門可以獲得社會工作文憑的2年制的新課程。"]}]}]},"digest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"理解，領悟；消化"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"文摘，摘要；分解物，提煉物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When food <b>digests</b> or when you <b>digest</b> it, it passes through your body to your stomach. Your stomach removes the substances that your body needs and gets rid of the rest. 消化","examples":["Do not undertake strenuous exercise for a few hours after a meal to allow food to digest. 飯後幾小時內不要做劇烈運動，以讓食物消化。","She couldn't digest food properly. 她無法正常消化食物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>digest</b> information, you think about it carefully so that you understand it. 領會","examples":["They learn well but seem to need time to digest information. 他們學得很好，但似乎需要時間來吃透這些知識。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>digest</b> some unpleasant news, you think about it until you are able to accept it and know how to deal with it. 承受 (壞訊息)","examples":["All this has upset me. I need time to digest it all. 這一切讓我心煩意亂。我需要時間來承受。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>digest</b> is a collection of pieces of writing. They are published together in a shorter form than they were originally published. 文摘","examples":["...the Middle East Economic Digest. …中東經濟文摘。"]}]}]},"discouragement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣餒，沮喪，灰心；令人氣餒的事物，障礙，挫折；勸阻，制止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Discouragement</b> is the act of trying to make someone not want to do something. (對某想法的) 打擊","examples":["He persevered in the face of active discouragement from those around him. 面對周圍人們的打擊，他鍥而不捨。"]}]}]},"disaster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"災難，災害；禍患，災難性事物；徹底的失敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disaster</b> is a very bad accident such as an earthquake or a plane crash, especially one in which a lot of people are killed. 災難","examples":["It was the second air disaster in the region in less than two months. 這是不到兩個月內該地區內的第2起空難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to something as a <b>disaster</b>, you are emphasizing that you think it is extremely bad or unacceptable. 極為糟糕的事; 不能接受的事","examples":["The whole production was just a disaster! 整部作品簡直是一團糟！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Disaster</b> is something which has very bad consequences for you. 災禍","examples":["The government brought itself to the brink of fiscal disaster. 該政府把自己帶到了財政災難的邊緣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a recipe for disaster</b>, you mean that it is very likely to have unpleasant consequences. 禍端","examples":["You give them a gun, and it's a recipe for disaster. 你給他們一把槍，那就是禍端。"]}]}]},"disadvantage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不利條件，劣勢；不利因素；損失，損害"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使處於不利地位，損害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disadvantage</b> is a factor which makes someone or something less useful, acceptable, or successful than other people or things. 不利條件","examples":["His two main rivals suffer the disadvantage of having been long-term political exiles. 他的兩名主要競爭對手由於長期被政治流放而處於不利地位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>at a disadvantage</b>, you have a problem or difficulty that many other people do not have, which makes it harder for you to be successful. 處於劣勢","examples":["The children from poor families were at a distinct disadvantage. 貧困家庭的孩子明顯處於劣勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>to</b> your <b>disadvantage</b> or works <b>to</b> your <b>disadvantage</b>, it creates difficulties for you. 對 (某人) 不利","examples":["We need a rethink of the present law which works so greatly to the disadvantage of women. 我們需要重新思考一下現行的法律，它使婦女處於非常不利的地位。"]}]}]},"disgust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反感，憎惡；厭惡，憎惡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使反感，使憎惡；使感到噁心（作嘔）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disgust</b> is a feeling of very strong dislike or disapproval. 厭惡","examples":["He spoke of his disgust at the incident. 他談到了對此事的厭惡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>disgust</b> someone means to make them feel a strong sense of dislike and disapproval. 使厭惡","examples":["He disgusted many with his boorish behaviour. 他以其粗魯的行為使許多人感到厭惡。"]}]}]},"disguise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"假扮，偽裝；掩飾，隱瞞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"偽裝物，偽裝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in</b> <b>disguise</b>, you are not wearing your usual clothes or you have altered your appearance in other ways, so that people will not recognize you. 偽裝","examples":["You'll have to travel in disguise. 你將不得不喬裝出行。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disguise</b> <b>yourself</b>, you put on clothes which make you look like someone else or alter your appearance in other ways, so that people will not recognize you. 喬裝","examples":["She disguised herself as a man so she could fight on the battlefield. 她女扮男裝以便能上戰場打仗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>disguise</b> something means to hide it or make it appear different so that people will not know about it or will not recognize it. 掩飾","examples":["He made no attempt to disguise his agitation. 他無意掩飾他的不安。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"喬裝的","examples":["The extremists entered the building disguised as medical workers. 極端分子們假扮成醫務人員，進入了大樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"掩飾的","examples":["The proposal is a thinly disguised effort to revive the price controls of the 1970s. 這項提議是恢復20世紀70年代物價控制的一種幾乎不加掩飾的努力。"]}]}]},"discipline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紀律，風紀；懲罰，處分；訓導，管教；訓練，鍛鍊；自制力，自律能力；（尤指大學的）科目，學科"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"懲罰，處分；訓練，管教"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Discipline</b> is the practice of making people obey rules or standards of behaviour, and punishing them when they do not. 紀律","examples":["Order and discipline have been placed in the hands of governing bodies. 秩序與紀律已交由管控機構負責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Discipline</b> is the quality of being able to behave and work in a controlled way which involves obeying particular rules or standards. 自律","examples":["It was that image of calm, control, and discipline that appealed to millions of voters. 正是那冷靜、剋制和自律的形象吸引了數以百萬計的選民。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to an activity or situation as a <b>discipline</b>, you mean that, in order to be successful in it, you need to behave in a strictly controlled way and obey particular rules or standards. 訓練; 磨練","examples":["The discipline of studying music can help children develop good work habits and improve self-esteem. 學習音樂的規範訓練能幫助孩子們養成良好的做事習慣和增強自尊心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>discipline</b> is a particular area of study, especially a subject of study in a college or university. (尤指大學裡的) 學科","examples":["We're looking for people from a wide range of disciplines. 我們正在尋找各類學科的人才。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is disciplined</b> for something that they have done wrong, they are punished for it. 處罰","examples":["The workman was disciplined by his company but not dismissed. 這名工人被他的公司處罰了，但沒有被開除。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>discipline</b> <b>yourself</b> to do something, you train yourself to behave and work in a strictly controlled and regular way. 訓練","examples":["Discipline yourself to check your messages once a day or every couple of days. 訓練你自己每天或每兩天檢視一次你的留言。"]}]}]},"disorder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"混亂，雜亂；騷亂，動亂；紊亂，疾病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打亂，使紊亂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disorder</b> is a problem or illness which affects someone's mind or body. 紊亂","examples":["...a rare nerve disorder that can cause paralysis of the arms. …一種罕見的能導致手臂癱瘓的神經紊亂疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Disorder</b> is violence or rioting in public. 動亂","examples":["Six months ago America's worst civil disorder in more than 100 years erupted in the city of Los Angeles. 6個月前，美國100多年來最嚴重的市民騷亂在洛杉磯市爆發了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Disorder</b> is a state of being untidy, badly prepared, or badly organized. 混亂","examples":["The emergency room was in disorder. 急救室一片混亂。"]}]}]},"dorm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宿舍（=dormitory）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dorm</b> is the same as a . 同dormitory","examples":[]}]}]},"distribution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分發；分銷，配送；（電影在各院線的）發行，上映；分配，分佈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>distribution</b> of things involves giving or delivering them to a number of people or places. 分發","examples":["...the council which controls the distribution of foreign aid. …掌管分發國外援助的委員會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>distribution</b> of something is how much of it there is in each place or at each time, or how much of it each person has. 分配; 分佈","examples":["Mr. Roh's economic planners sought to achieve a more equitable distribution of wealth. 羅歐先生的經濟規劃者們努力實現更公平的財富分配。"]}]}]},"district":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地區，區域；行政區，轄區；<英>（郡或區以下的）選區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>把……劃分成區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>district</b> is a particular area of a town or country. 地區","examples":["I drove around the business district. 我繞著商業區行駛。"]}]}]},"dispute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爭論，辯論，糾紛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……提出質疑，否認；爭論，辯論；爭奪，競爭；<舊>阻止（著陸），抵抗（進攻）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dispute</b> is an argument or disagreement between people or groups. 爭論","examples":["They have won previous pay disputes with the government. 他們曾贏過前幾起與政府的工資糾紛。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dispute</b> a fact, statement, or theory, you say that it is incorrect or untrue. 反駁","examples":["He disputed the allegations. 他駁斥了這些無根據的指控。","Nobody disputed that Davey was clever. 沒有人反駁戴維是聰明的。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>dispute</b> something, they fight for control or ownership of it. You can also say that one group of people <b>dispute</b> something with another group. 爭奪 (控制權、所有權)","examples":["Russia and Ukraine have been disputing the ownership of the fleet. 俄羅斯和烏克蘭一直在爭奪該艦隊的所有權。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more people or groups are <b>in dispute</b>, they are arguing or disagreeing about something. (人或組織) 有爭議的","examples":["The two countries are in dispute over the boundaries of their coastal waters. 兩國對它們沿海海域的邊界是有爭議的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>in dispute</b>, people are questioning it or arguing about it. (某事物) 有爭議的","examples":["The schedule for the talks has been agreed, but the location is still in dispute. 會談的時間表已經達成一致，但地點尚有爭議。"]}]}]},"doze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"小睡，打盹；打瞌睡度過"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"瞌睡，小睡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>doze</b>, you sleep lightly or for a short period, especially during the daytime. 打盹兒","examples":["For a while she dozed fitfully. 她斷斷續續地小睡了片刻。"]}]}]},"divorce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"離婚；離婚判決；分開，脫離"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與（某人）離婚；使分離，割裂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>divorce</b> is the formal ending of a marriage by law. 離婚","examples":["Numerous marriages now end in divorce. 現在許多婚姻都以離婚而告終。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>divorce</b> <b>of</b> one thing <b>from</b> another, or a divorce <b>between</b> two things is a separation between them which is permanent or is likely to be permanent. 分離; 脫離","examples":["...this divorce of Christian culture from the roots of faith. …基督教文化與信仰根源的分離。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a man and woman <b>divorce</b> or if one of them <b>divorces</b> the other, their marriage is legally ended. 離婚","examples":["He and Lillian had got divorced. 他和莉蓮離婚了。","I am absolutely furious that he divorced me to marry her. 我實在很生氣他和我離婚娶了她。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing cannot <b>be divorced from</b> another, you mean that the two things cannot be considered as different and separate things. 使分離; 使脫離","examples":["Good management in the police cannot be divorced from accountability. 警政的良好管理離不開問責制。","Democracy cannot be divorced from social and economic progress. 民主離不開社會和經濟的進步。"]}]}]},"doctor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醫生，大夫；診所（the doctor）；博士；<美>牙醫，獸醫 (Dr)；博學的人；（釣魚用）人造蠅；涼爽海風；<俚>船上的廚師"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"篡改，偽造；將有害物摻入（食物或飲料）中；閹割（動物）；為……治病，給……療傷；授以博士學位；修理（機器等），修復；當醫生，行醫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doctor</b> is someone who has a degree in medicine and treats people who are sick or injured. 醫生","examples":["Do not discontinue the treatment without consulting your doctor. 不要不徵求醫生的意見就中斷治療。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A  or  can also be called <b>doctor</b>. (牙醫、獸醫) 醫生","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>doctor's</b> is used to refer to the office where a doctor works. 診所","examples":["I have an appointment at the doctor's. 我在診所有個預約。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>doctor</b> is someone who has been awarded the highest academic or honorary degree by a university. 博士","examples":["He is a doctor of philosophy. 他是一位哲學博士。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>doctors</b> something, they change it in order to deceive people. 竄改","examples":["They doctored the prints, deepening the lines to make her look as awful as possible. 他們竄改了照片，加深皺紋使她儘可能地難看。"]}]}]},"dread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"畏懼，擔心；<古>敬畏"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"害怕，畏懼；令人生畏的人，可怕的事物；（鷗鳥等鳥群的）驚飛，驚起；<英，非正式>將頭髮編成“駭人”髮型的人，拉斯塔法裡派成員"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人生畏的，可怕的；惱火的，生氣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dread</b> something which may happen, you feel very anxious and unhappy about it because you think it will be unpleasant or upsetting. 害怕; 擔憂","examples":["I'm dreading Christmas this year. 我害怕今年的聖誕節。","I dreaded coming back, to be honest. 老實說，我很害怕回來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dread</b> is a feeling of great anxiety and fear about something that may happen. 憂慮; 恐懼","examples":["She thought with dread of the cold winters to come. 想到寒冬即將到來，她就感到恐懼。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>dread to think</b> what might happen, you mean that you are anxious about it because it is likely to be very unpleasant. 不敢想","examples":["I dread to think what will happen in the case of a major emergency. 我不敢想像萬一出現重大緊急情況會怎麼樣。"]}]}]},"dye":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……染色"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"染料，染液"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dye</b> something such as hair or cloth, you change its colour by soaking it in a special liquid. 染色","examples":["The women prepared, spun, and dyed the wool. 婦女們將羊毛預備、紡線並染色。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dye</b> is a substance made from plants or chemicals which is mixed into a liquid and used to change the colour of something such as cloth or hair. 染料","examples":["...bottles of hair dye. …一瓶瓶的染髮劑。"]}]}]},"earnest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"認真的，誠摯的，真誠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"預示，象徵；嚴肅，認真（in earnest）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done or happens <b>in earnest</b>, it happens to a much greater extent and more seriously than before. 嚴肅地; 正式地","examples":["Campaigning will begin in earnest tomorrow. 活動明天正式開始。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Earnest</b> people are very serious and sincere in what they say or do, because they think that their actions and beliefs are important. 真摯的","examples":["Catherine was a pious, earnest woman. 凱瑟琳是位虔誠、真摯的女子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a part or portion of something given in advance as a guarantee of the remainder 定金","examples":[]}]}]},"earphone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耳機；聽筒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Earphones</b> are a small piece of equipment that you wear over or inside your ears so that you can listen to a radio or recorded music without anyone else hearing. 耳機","examples":[]}]}]},"draft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"草稿，草案；匯票；<美>通風氣流，穿堂風（=draught）；徵兵；<美>（職業球隊的）選拔隊員制"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"起草，草擬；選派，派遣；<美>徵召，徵召……入伍；<美>挑選，選拔（運動員）；作草圖，繪樣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（動物）馱重物的，負重的；（啤酒）散裝的；草擬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>draft</b> is an early version of a letter, book, or speech. 草稿; 初稿","examples":["I rewrote his rough draft, which was published under my name. 我改寫了他那篇以我的名義發表了的初稿。","I faxed a first draft of this article to him. 我把這篇文章的初稿傳真給他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>draft</b> is a written order for payment of money by a bank, especially from one bank to another. 匯票","examples":["Payments must be made in U.S. dollars by a bank draft drawn to the order of the United Nations Postal Administration. 付款必須用開給聯合國郵政管理處的銀行匯票，並以美元支付。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>draft</b> is a current of air that comes into a place in an undesirable way. (鑽進某處的) 風","examples":["Block drafts around doors and windows. 擋住門窗周圍的風。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The draft</b> is the practice of ordering people to serve in the armed forces, usually for a limited period of time. 徵兵","examples":["...his effort to avoid the draft. …他逃避兵役的努力。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>draft</b> a letter, book, or speech, you write the first version of it. 起草","examples":["He drafted a letter to the editors. 他草擬了一封給編輯的信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are drafted</b>, you are ordered to serve in the armed forces, usually for a limited period of time. 徵兵","examples":["During the Second World War, he was drafted into the U.S. Army. 第二次世界大戰期間，他應徵加入美國陸軍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>are drafted</b> to do something, they are asked to do a particular job. 選派","examples":["She hoped that Fox could be drafted to run the organization. 她希望福克斯能夠被選派來掌管這個組織。"]}]}]},"economist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經濟學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>economist</b> is a person who studies, teaches, or writes about economics. 經濟學家","examples":[]}]}]},"drill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鑽，鑽機；訓練，演習；粗斜紋布；條播溝；條播機；條播作物；<非正式>常規，正確步驟；尾角螺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鑽孔；訓練，演習；條播"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drill</b> is a tool or machine that you use for making holes. 鑽孔機","examples":["...a dentist's drill. …一把牙鑽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drill</b> is a routine exercise or activity, in which people practise what they should do in dangerous situations. 操練","examples":["...a fire drill. …一場消防演習。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>drill</b> is repeated training for a group of people, especially soldiers, so that they can do something quickly and efficiently. 訓練","examples":["The Marines carried out landing exercises in a drill that includes 18 ships and 90 aircraft. 海軍陸戰隊在一場軍事訓練中進行了登陸練習，包括18艘軍艦和90架飛機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a machine for planting seeds in rows or depositing fertilizer 條播機","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a hard-wearing twill-weave cotton cloth, used for uniforms, etc 粗斜紋布","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"an Old World monkey, <b>Mandrillus leucophaeus,</b> of W Africa, related to the mandrill but smaller and less brightly coloured (西非)鬼狒","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>drill</b> <b>into</b> something or <b>drill</b> a hole in something, you make a hole in it using a drill. 鑽 (孔); 打 (眼)","examples":["He drilled into the wall of Lili's bedroom. 他在麗莉臥室的牆上打孔。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>drill</b> <b>for</b> oil or water, they search for it by drilling deep holes in the ground or in the bottom of the sea. 鑽探 (石油或地下水源)","examples":["There have been proposals to drill for more oil. 有人提出了鑽探更多石油的建議。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to teach by rigorous exercises or training (透過嚴格訓練來)教學","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to plant (seeds) by means of a drill 條播","examples":[]}]}]},"economics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經濟學；經濟情況；經濟體制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Economics</b> is the study of the way in which money, industry, and commerce are organized in a society. 經濟學","examples":["His younger sister is studying economics. 他的妹妹在學經濟學。"]}]}]},"drift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"飄移，漂流；任其自然地（或不知不覺地）進入（某種狀態）；流浪，漂泊；緩慢移動；傳出；吹積"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"流動，趨勢；吹積物，雪堆；主旨，大意；偏航；不作為，優柔寡斷；叢生的植物；冰磧；水平巷道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>drifts</b> somewhere, it is carried there by the movement of wind or water. 漂流","examples":["We proceeded to drift on up the river. 我們繼續在河上漂流著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>drifts</b> <b>into</b> a situation, they get into that situation in a way that is not planned or controlled. 脫離正途; 偏離","examples":["We need to offer young people drifting into crime an alternative set of values. 我們需要給誤入犯罪歧途的年輕人提供另一套價值觀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>drifts</b> around, you mean that they travel from place to place without a plan or settled way of life. 漂泊; 流浪","examples":["You've been drifting from job to job without any real commitment. 你頻頻換工作，全無恆心。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>drift</b> somewhere means to move there slowly or gradually. 緩慢地移動","examples":["As rural factories lay off workers, people drift toward the cities. 隨著鄉鎮企業裁員，人們陸續移向城市。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If sounds <b>drift</b> somewhere, they can be heard but they are not very loud. (聲音) 隱約傳出","examples":["Cool summer dance sounds are drifting from the stereo indoors. 屋內立體聲音響飄出美妙的夏季舞曲。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If snow <b>drifts</b>, it builds up into piles as a result of the movement of the wind. 吹積","examples":["The snow, except where it drifted, was only calf-deep. 除了被風吹積起來的地方外，積雪只深及小腿。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drift</b> is a movement away from somewhere or something, or a movement toward somewhere or something different. 移向; 移動","examples":["...the drift toward the cities. …向城市的流動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drift</b> is a mass of snow that has built up into a pile as a result of the movement of wind. (吹積成的) 雪堆","examples":["A nine-year-old boy was trapped in a snow drift. 一個9歲的男孩陷在雪堆裡了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>drift of</b> an argument or speech is the general point that is being made in it. (辯論、演說等的) 主旨","examples":["Grace was beginning to get his drift. 格雷斯開始抓住他的主旨了。"]}]}]},"dynasty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王朝；朝，代"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dynasty</b> is a series of rulers of a country who all belong to the same family. 王朝","examples":["The Seljuk dynasty of Syria was founded in 1094. 敘利亞的塞爾柱王朝建立於1094年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dynasty</b> is a period of time during which a country is ruled by members of the same family. 朝代","examples":["...carvings dating back to the Ming dynasty. …可以追溯到明朝的雕刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>dynasty</b> is a family which has members from two or more generations who are important in a particular field of activity, for example, in business or politics. 世家","examples":["This is a family-owned company – the current president is the fourth in this dynasty. 這是一個家族企業–現任總裁是該世家的第4代。"]}]}]},"electrician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電工，電氣技師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>electrician</b> is a person whose job is to install and repair electrical equipment. 電工","examples":[]}]}]},"elastic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有彈性的；靈活的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"彈性織物，鬆緊帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elastic</b> is a rubber material that stretches when you pull it and returns to its original size and shape when you let it go. Elastic is often used in clothes to make them fit tightly, for example, around the waist. 鬆緊帶","examples":["Make a mask with long ears and attach a piece of elastic to go around the back of the head. 做一個帶長耳朵的面具，安上一條鬆緊帶繞過後腦。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>elastic</b> is able to stretch easily and then return to its original size and shape. 有彈性的","examples":["Beat it until the dough is slightly elastic. 反覆捶打，直到麵糰略有彈性。"]}]}]},"electronics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電子學；電子裝置，電子器件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Electronics</b> is the technology of using transistors and silicon chips, especially in devices such as radios, televisions, and computers. 電子技術","examples":["...Ohio's three main electronics companies. …俄亥俄州三大電子技術公司。"]}]}]},"efficiency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"效率，效能；（機器的）功率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Efficiency</b> is the quality of being able to do a task successfully, without wasting time or energy. 效率","examples":["There are many ways to increase agricultural efficiency in the poorer areas of the world. 有許多提高世界較貧困地區農業效能的方法。"]}]}]},"e-mail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電子郵件，電子郵件系統；電子郵件資訊，一封電子郵件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……發電子郵件；用電子郵件傳送"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>E-mail</b> is a system of sending written messages electronically from one computer to another. <b>E-mail</b> is an abbreviation of . 電子郵件","examples":["You can contact us by e-mail. 你可以透過電子郵件跟我們聯絡。","Do you want to send an E-mail? 你想發一封電子郵件嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>e-mail</b> someone, you send them an e-mail. 給…發電子郵件","examples":["Jamie e-mailed me to say he couldn't come. 傑米給我發了一封電子郵件說他不能來了。"]}]}]},"economy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經濟；節省，簡練；經濟艙"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經濟實惠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>economy</b> is the system according to which the money, industry, and commerce of a country or region are organized. 經濟體制","examples":["Zimbabwe boasts Africa's most industrialized economy. 辛巴威自誇有著非洲最為工業化的經濟體制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A country's <b>economy</b> is the wealth that it gets from business and industry. 經濟狀況","examples":["The Japanese economy grew at an annual rate of more than 10 percent. 日本的經濟以每年10%以上的速度增長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Economy</b> is the use of the minimum amount of money, time, or other resources needed to achieve something, so that nothing is wasted. 節省","examples":["...improvements in the fuel economy of cars. …在節省汽車燃料方面的一些改進。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Economy</b> services such as travel are cheap and have no luxuries or extras. 經濟的; 便宜的","examples":["...the limitations that come with economy travel. …伴隨經濟艙的一些限制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Economy</b> is used to describe large packs of products that are cheaper than normal sized packs. 經濟裝的","examples":["...an economy pack containing 150 assorted screws. …內有150枚各式螺釘的一個經濟裝。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an attempt to save money as <b>a false economy</b>, you mean that you have not saved any money as you will have to spend a lot more later. 貌似省錢，長遠上卻費錢","examples":["A cheap bed can be a false economy, so spend as much as you can afford. 一張廉價的床長遠上並不省錢，所以要盡你所能買貴的。"]}]}]},"embarrassment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尷尬，難堪；使人難堪的人（或事）；拮据，經濟困難；（可供挑選的）眾多事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Embarrassment</b> is the feeling you have when you are embarrassed. 尷尬; 難堪","examples":["I think I would have died of embarrassment. 我覺得我一定會尷尬得要死。","We apologize for any embarrassment this may have caused. 我們為可能會帶來的任何尷尬而道歉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>embarrassment</b> is an action, event, or situation that causes problems for a politician, political party, government, or other public group. 難堪的事","examples":["The poverty figures were undoubtedly an embarrassment to the president. 這些貧困數字無疑是令總統難堪的一件事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a person as <b>an embarrassment</b>, you mean that you disapprove of them but cannot avoid your connection with them. 丟臉的人","examples":["You have been an embarrassment to us from the day Doug married you. 自從你和道格結婚的那天起你對我們來講一直是個丟臉的人。"]}]}]},"embassy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大使館工作人員；大使館；（外交）特別使團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>embassy</b> is a group of government officials, headed by an ambassador, who represent their government in a foreign country. The building in which they work is also called an <b>embassy</b>. 大使及其隨員; 大使館","examples":["The American embassy has already complained. 美國使館已經提出抗議。"]}]}]},"email":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電子郵件（通訊方式）；電子郵件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（某人）發電子郵件"}],"sections":[]},"enforcement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"執行，實施"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone carries out the <b>enforcement</b> <b>of</b> an act or rule, they enforce it. 執行","examples":["The doctors want stricter enforcement of existing laws. 醫生們希望現行法律的執行能更嚴格。"]}]}]},"empire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帝國；大企業，大集團；君權，最高統治權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>empire</b> is a number of individual nations that are all controlled by the government or ruler of one particular country. 帝國","examples":["...the Roman Empire. …羅馬帝國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of companies controlled by one person as an <b>empire</b>. 企業帝國","examples":["...the global Murdoch media empire. …默多克環球媒體帝國。"]}]}]},"emphasis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要性，重點強調；重讀，強調；（表達的）強有力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Emphasis</b> is special or extra importance that is given to an activity or to a part or aspect of something. 重點","examples":["Too much emphasis is placed on research. 把重點過多地放在研究上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Emphasis</b> is extra force that you put on a syllable, word, or phrase when you are speaking in order to make it seem more important. 重音","examples":["The emphasis is on the first syllable of the last word. 重音是在最末一個單詞的第一個音節上。"]}]}]},"enlargement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴大，增大，放大；放大的照片；增補物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>enlargement</b> <b>of</b> something is the process or result of making it bigger. 擴大","examples":["There is insufficient space for enlargement of the buildings. 沒有足夠的空間擴建這些大樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>enlargement</b> is a photograph that has been made bigger. 放大的照片","examples":["Ordering reprints and enlargements is easier than ever. 按需加洗和放大照片比以前要容易。"]}]}]},"engineering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工程，工程學；控制，引導，管理；籌劃，出謀劃策"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設計，建造；策劃，精心安排（engineer"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Engineering</b> is the work involved in designing and constructing engines and machinery or structures such as roads and bridges. <b>Engineering</b> is also the subject studied by people who want to do this work. 工程; 工程學","examples":["...graduates with degrees in engineering. …獲得工程學學位的畢業生。"]}]}]},"encounter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遭遇；偶遇，邂逅"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"偶遇，邂逅；經歷，體驗；衝突；比賽，交鋒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>encounter</b> problems or difficulties, you experience them. 遭遇","examples":["Every day of our lives we encounter major and minor stresses of one kind or another. 生活中的每一天，我們會遇到或大或小的這樣那樣的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>encounter</b> someone, you meet them, usually unexpectedly. 邂逅","examples":["Did you encounter anyone in the building? 你在那棟大樓裡偶然遇到什麼人了嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>encounter</b> <b>with</b> someone is a meeting with them, particularly one that is unexpected or significant. 邂逅","examples":["The author tells of a remarkable encounter with a group of South Vietnamese soldiers. 作者講述了他與一群南越士兵的驚人邂逅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>encounter</b> is a particular type of experience. 特殊經歷","examples":["...a sexual encounter. …一次性經歷。"]}]}]},"equality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"均等，平等；等式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Equality</b> is the same status, rights, and responsibilities for all the members of a society, group, or family. 平等","examples":["...equality of the sexes. …性別平等。"]}]}]},"escalator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自動扶梯，電動扶梯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>escalator</b> is a moving staircase on which people can go from one level of a building to another. 電梯","examples":["Take the escalator to the third floor and it's the last office on the left. 乘電梯到4樓，左邊最後的那個辦公室就是。"]}]}]},"errand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"差事，跑腿；<古>使命，任務"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>errand</b> is a short trip that you make in order to do a job, for example, when you go to a shop to buy something. (短程) 差使","examples":["She went off on some errand. 她出去辦事了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>run an errand</b> <b>for</b> someone, you do or get something for them, usually by making a short trip somewhere. 跑腿","examples":["Run an errand for me, will you? Go find Roger for me. 替我跑跑腿好嗎？幫我去找一下羅傑。"]}]}]},"entertainment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"娛樂，娛樂表演；招待，款待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Entertainment</b> consists of performances of plays and movies, and activities such as reading and watching television, that give people pleasure. 娛樂","examples":["...the world of entertainment and international stardom. …國際娛樂界及明星界。"]}]}]},"enthusiasm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熱情，熱忱；熱衷的活動，熱愛的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enthusiasm</b> is great eagerness to be involved in a particular activity that you like and enjoy or that you think is important. 熱情","examples":["Their skill and enthusiasm has got them on the team. 他們的技術和熱情使他們進了那支團隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>enthusiasm</b> is an activity or subject that interests you very much and that you spend a lot of time on. 熱衷的活動; 喜愛的科目","examples":["Draw him out about his current enthusiasms and future plans. 讓他暢談一下他當前喜愛的科目和將來的打算。"]}]}]},"equipment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"裝置，用具；（對某人或某物的）裝備過程；（做某事應具備的）素質，才能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Equipment</b> consists of the things that are used for a particular purpose, such as a hobby or job. 裝置; 裝備","examples":["...computers, electronic equipment and machine tools. …電腦、電子裝置和機床。"]}]}]},"era":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時代，年代，紀元"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a period of history or a long period of time as an <b>era</b> when you want to draw attention to a particular feature or quality that it has. 時代","examples":["...the nuclear era. …核時代。","...the Reagan-Bush era. …里根－布什時期。"]}]}]},"essay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（學生為某門課程所寫的）短文，論說文； （用來刊登的）散文，隨筆；企圖，嘗試；尚未採用的郵票設計圖案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"試圖，作……嘗試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>essay</b> is a short piece of writing on a particular subject written by a student. (學生寫的) 短文","examples":["We asked Jason to write an essay about his hometown. 我們讓傑森寫一篇關於他家鄉的短文。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>essay</b> is a short piece of writing on a particular subject that is written by a writer for publication. (作家寫的) 文章","examples":["...Thomas Malthus's essay on population. …托馬斯·馬爾薩斯關於人口的文章。"]}]}]},"examinee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"應試人，參加考試者；受檢查（或審查、查詢的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>examinee</b> is someone who is taking an exam. 考生","examples":[]}]}]},"establishment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建立，設立；權勢集團，現存體制；企業，公共機構，家庭；結婚；英國國教，蘇格蘭長老會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>establishment</b> <b>of</b> an organization or system is the act of creating it or beginning it. 建立; 創立","examples":["The establishment of the regional government in 1980 did not end terrorism. 1980年地區政府的成立並沒有結束恐怖主義。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>establishment</b> is a shop, business, or organization occupying a particular building or place. 商店; 企業; 機構","examples":["...a scientific research establishment. …一個科研機構。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You refer to the people who have power and influence in the running of a country, society, or organization as <b>the</b> <b>establishment</b>. 當權者","examples":["While scientists were once considered cranks and outsiders to the system, we are now part of the establishment. 雖然科學家曾被認為是怪人、是該體制的局外人，而如今我們已經是權力集團的一部分。"]}]}]},"evaluation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"評價，評估"}],"sections":[]},"examiner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"考官，主考人；審查人，檢查人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>examiner</b> is a person who conducts an examination. 檢查員; 考官","examples":["...FBI senior fingerprint examiner Terry Green. …聯邦調查局高階指紋檢驗官特里·格林。"]}]}]},"eve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"前夕，前一天；傍晚，黃昏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>eve</b> <b>of</b> a particular event or occasion is the day before it, or the period of time just before it. 前一天; 前夕","examples":["...on the eve of his 27th birthday. …在他27歲生日的前夕。"]}]}]},"estimate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"估計；判斷，評價"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"估計，估價；估價單；看法，判斷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>estimate</b> a quantity or value, you make an approximate judgment or calculation of it. 估計","examples":["Try to estimate how many steps it will take to get to a close object. 估計一下需要多少步才能到達一個近距目標。","I estimate that total cost for treatment will go from $9,000 to $12,500. 我估計治療費總額將在9千美元到1.25萬美元之間。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"估計的","examples":["There are an estimated 90,000 gangsters in the country. 這個國家估計有9萬名歹徒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>estimate</b> is an approximate calculation of a quantity or value. 估計","examples":["...the official estimate of the election result. …選舉結果的官方估計。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>estimate</b> is a judgment about a person or situation that you make based on the available evidence. 判斷","examples":["I hadn't been far wrong in my estimate of his grandson's capabilities. 我對他孫子能力的判斷沒有太離譜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>estimate</b> from someone who you employ to do a job for you, such as a builder or a plumber, is a written statement of how much the job is likely to cost. 估價","examples":["Quotes and estimates can be prepared by computer on the spot. 報價和估價可以當場用電腦做出來。"]}]}]},"essential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"必不可少的，非常重要的；基本的，精髓的；（氨基酸、脂肪酸）必需的；（疾病）自發的，原發的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"必不可少的東西，必需品；要素，本質；（某學科的）基礎，基本知識"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>essential</b> is extremely important or absolutely necessary to a particular subject, situation, or activity. 至關重要的","examples":["It was absolutely essential to separate crops from the areas that animals used as pasture. 把莊稼與牲畜的放牧區分開至關重要。","As they must also sprint over short distances, speed is essential. 由於他們還必須疾速短跑，因此速度是至關重要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>essential</b> aspects of something are its most basic or important aspects. 基本的; 重要的","examples":["Most authorities agree that play is an essential part of a child's development. 大多數權威人士認為玩耍是孩子成長的一個重要部分。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>essentials</b> are the things that are absolutely necessary for the situation you are in or for the task you are doing. 必需品","examples":["The apartment contained the basic essentials for bachelor life. 這套公寓配有單身生活的基本必需品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>essentials</b> are the most important principles, ideas, or facts of a particular subject. 要素; 要點","examples":["...the essentials of everyday life, such as eating and exercise. …飲食、運動等日常生活要素。"]}]}]},"exception":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"例外，除外"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>exception</b> is a particular thing, person, or situation that is not included in a general statement, judgment, or rule. 例外","examples":["Few guitarists can sing as well as they can play; Eddie, however, is an exception. 很少有吉他手唱歌能唱得跟彈得一樣好，而艾迪是個例外。","The law makes no exceptions. 法律不搞例外。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a general statement, and then say that something or someone is <b>no exception</b>, you are emphasizing that they are included in that statement. 不例外; 無例外","examples":["Marketing is applied to everything these days, and books are no exception. 現在市場營銷用於任何事物，圖書也不例外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take exception to</b> something, you feel offended or annoyed by it, usually with the result that you complain about it. 厭惡; 反感","examples":["He also took exception to having been spied on. 他也厭惡被暗中監視。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>with the exception of</b> to introduce a thing or person that is not included in a general statement that you are making. 除外","examples":["Yesterday was a day off for everybody, with the exception of Lorenzo. 昨天每個人休一天假，洛倫佐除外。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>without exception</b> to emphasize that the statement you are making is true in all cases. 無例外地","examples":["The vehicles are without exception old, rusty and dented. 這些車輛無一例外地破舊、鏽跡斑斑且有撞痕。"]}]}]},"expansion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擴大，擴張；擴充，展開；擴張物；膨脹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Expansion</b> is the process of becoming greater in size, number, or amount. 擴張; 發展","examples":["...the rapid expansion of private health insurance. …私人健康保險的快速發展。"]}]}]},"evidence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"根據，證明；（呈上法庭的）證據，證詞；跡象，痕跡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"證實，證明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Evidence</b> is anything that you see, experience, read, or are told that causes you to believe that something is true or has really happened. 證據; 依據","examples":["Ganley said he'd seen no evidence of widespread fraud. 甘利說他沒有看見欺騙行為氾濫的證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Evidence</b> is the information that is used in a court of law to try to prove something. Evidence is obtained from documents, objects, or witnesses. (法律上的) 證據","examples":["The evidence against him was purely circumstantial. 不利於他的證據純粹是間接證據。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give evidence</b> in a court of law or an official inquiry, you officially say what you know about people or events, or describe an occasion at which you were present. (在法庭上或官方調查中) 作證","examples":["The forensic scientists who carried out the original tests will be called to give evidence. 那些進行了原始化驗的法醫學家們將被叫去作證。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is in evidence</b>, they are present and can be clearly seen. 顯然可見","examples":["Few soldiers were in evidence. 幾乎看不見有士兵。"]}]}]},"exhibit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"表現出；賣弄，炫耀；提出（證據等）；展覽，展出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"展品；（法庭上出示的）證物；<美>展覽，展出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something shows a particular quality, feeling, or type of behaviour, you can say that they <b>exhibit</b> it. 表現出","examples":["He has exhibited symptoms of anxiety and overwhelming worry. 他已表現出焦慮和憂心如焚的症狀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a painting, sculpture, or object of interest <b>is exhibited</b>, it is put in a public place such as a museum or art gallery so that people can come to look at it. You can also say that animals <b>are exhibited</b> in a zoo. 展覽","examples":["His work was exhibited in the best galleries in America, Europe and Asia. 他的作品在美國、歐洲和亞洲最好的美術館展覽過。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"展覽","examples":["Five large pieces of the wall are currently on exhibition. 那堵牆的五塊大碎片目前在展覽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>exhibit</b> is a painting, sculpture, or object of interest that is displayed to the public in a museum or art gallery. 展覽品","examples":["Shona showed me around the exhibits. 肖納帶我參觀了展品。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>exhibit</b> is a public display of paintings, sculpture, or objects of interest in a museum or art gallery. 展覽","examples":["...an exhibit at the Metropolitan Museum of Art. …大都會藝術博物館的一場展覽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>exhibit</b> is an object that a lawyer shows in court as evidence in a legal case. (法庭上出示的) 證物","examples":["The jury has already asked to see more than 40 exhibits from the trial. 陪審團已經要求檢視了審判中超過40件的證物。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When artists <b>exhibit</b>, they show their work in public. 展出作品","examples":["He has also exhibited at galleries and museums in New York and Washington. 他還在紐約和華盛頓的美術館及博物館展出過作品。"]}]}]},"explosion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爆破，爆炸（聲）；激增；爆發，迸發；突發的巨響；某事證實是錯誤的，推翻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>explosion</b> is a sudden, violent burst of energy, such as one caused by a bomb. 爆炸","examples":["After the second explosion, all of London's main train and subway stations were shut down. 第二次爆炸後，倫敦所有的主要火車站及地鐵站都被關閉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Explosion</b> is the act of deliberately causing a bomb or similar device to explode. 引爆","examples":["Bomb disposal experts blew up the bag in a controlled explosion. 拆彈專家在一次控制爆破中炸掉了那個袋子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>explosion</b> is a large rapid increase in the number or amount of something. 暴增; 暴漲","examples":["The study also forecast an explosion in the diet soft-drink market. 這項研究還預測了低糖軟飲料市場的暴增。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>explosion</b> is a sudden violent expression of someone's feelings, especially anger. (情感、尤指憤怒的) 暴發","examples":["Every time they met, Myra anticipated an explosion. 每次他們相見，邁拉都預期會有一場怒火暴發。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>explosion</b> is a sudden and serious political protest or violence. (抗議、暴力行為的) 爆發","examples":["...the explosion of protest and violence sparked off by the killing of seven workers. …由7名工人被殺引起的抗議及暴力行為的爆發。"]}]}]},"explanation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解釋，說明；解釋性說法，說明性文字；理由，原因"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give an <b>explanation</b> of something that has happened, you give people reasons for it, especially in an attempt to justify it. 解釋 (原因)","examples":["She told the court she would give a full explanation of the prosecution's decision on Monday. 她告訴法庭她將在星期一就控方的決定做出詳盡的解釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say there is an <b>explanation</b> <b>for</b> something, you mean that there is a reason for it. 原因","examples":["The deputy airport manager said there was no apparent explanation for the crash. 機場副經理稱那次飛機墜毀沒有明顯的原因。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you give an <b>explanation</b> <b>of</b> something, you give details about it or describe it so that it can be understood. 詳細說明","examples":["He has given a very clear explanation of his remarks and the context in which they were made. 他對他的評論以及作出那些評論的情境已經作了非常清楚詳細的說明。"]}]}]},"explosive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易爆的，可能引起爆炸的；（局勢）一觸即發的，爆炸性的；暴躁的，易怒的；激增的；強有力的；（聲音）轟響的；（濁音）爆發的，破裂的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"炸藥，爆炸物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>explosive</b> is a substance or device that can cause an explosion. 炸藥; 爆炸物","examples":["...one-hundred-and-fifty pounds of Semtex explosive. …150磅的塞姆汀塑膠炸藥。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>explosive</b> is capable of causing an explosion. 能引起爆炸的","examples":["The explosive device was timed to go off at the rush hour. 該爆炸裝置定在交通高峰時間爆炸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>explosive</b> growth is a sudden, rapid increase in the size or quantity of something. 暴漲的","examples":["The explosive growth in casinos is one of the most conspicuous signs of Westernization. 賭場數量的暴漲是最明顯的西化標誌之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>explosive</b> situation is likely to have difficult, serious, or dangerous effects. 爆炸性的 (局勢)","examples":["He appeared to be treating the potentially explosive situation with some sensitivity. 他似乎正在有些敏感地處理潛在的爆炸性局面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>explosive</b>, you mean that they tend to express sudden violent anger. 脾氣暴躁的","examples":["He's inherited his father's explosive temper. 他遺傳了他父親的火暴性子。"]}]}]},"exhaust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使精疲力盡；耗盡；詳盡討論；排放，排出（氣體，蒸汽）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"廢氣；排氣管，排氣裝置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>exhausts</b> you, it makes you so tired, either physically or mentally, that you have no energy left. 使精疲力竭","examples":["Don't exhaust him. 別讓他精疲力竭了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>exhaust</b> something such as money or food, you use or finish it all. 用完","examples":["We have exhausted all our material resources. 我們已用完了所有的物資。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>have exhausted</b> a subject or topic, you have talked about it so much that there is nothing more to say about it. 說盡","examples":["She and Chantal must have exhausted the subject of clothes. 她和錢特爾肯定說盡了服裝這個主題。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精疲力竭的","examples":["She was too exhausted and distressed to talk about the tragedy. 她太疲憊和憂傷了，不想談論那場悲劇。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exhaust</b> is the gas or steam that is produced when the engine of a vehicle is running. 廢氣","examples":["...the exhaust from a car engine. …從汽車引擎排出的廢氣。","The city's streets are filthy and choked with exhaust fumes. 這座城市的街道骯髒不堪，充滿了廢氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>exhaust</b> is the same as the . 排氣管","examples":[]}]}]},"facility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"設施，裝置；衛生間；天賦，才能；（機器等的）特別裝置，（服務等的）特色；（用作某種用途的）場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Facilities</b> are buildings, pieces of equipment, or services that are provided for a particular purpose. 設施","examples":["What recreational facilities are now available? 什麼娛樂設施現在是可用的？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>facility</b> is something such as an additional service provided by an organization or an extra feature on a machine which is useful but not essential. 附加服務; 附加功能","examples":["One of the new models has the facility to reproduce speech as well as text. 新款型中的一款有複製言語和文字的附加功能。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have a <b>facility</b> for something, for example learning a language, you find it easy to do. 天賦","examples":["He and Marcia shared a facility for languages. 他和馬西婭都具有語言天賦。"]}]}]},"fame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名譽，名氣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使聞名，使有名望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you achieve <b>fame</b>, you become very well-known. 聲譽","examples":["At the height of his fame, his every word was valued. 在他聲名鼎盛時，他的每一句話都受到了重視。","The film earned him international fame. 這部影片為他贏得了國際聲譽。"]}]}]},"exposure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴露，接觸；曝光，揭發；報道，宣傳；單張膠片；曝光時間，曝光量；受凍；朝向"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exposure</b> <b>to</b> something dangerous means being in a situation where it might affect you. 暴露","examples":["Exposure to lead is known to damage the brains of young children. 已知接觸鉛會損害幼童的大腦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Exposure</b> is the harmful effect on your body caused by very cold weather. 受凍","examples":["He was suffering from exposure and shock but his condition was said to be stable. 他受凍休克，但他的狀態據說很穩定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>exposure</b> of a well-known person is the revealing of the fact that they are bad or immoral in some way. 揭發","examples":["He undertook increasingly dangerous assignments until his exposure as a spy. 在間諜身份暴露之前他一直從事日益危險的任務。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Exposure</b> is publicity that a person, company, or product receives. 宣傳","examples":["All the candidates have been getting an enormous amount of exposure on television and in the press. 所有候選人都在爭取大量的電視和新聞媒體宣傳。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In photography, an <b>exposure</b> is a single photograph. 底片","examples":["Larger drawings tend to require two or three exposures to cover them. 較大的圖畫需要兩到三張底片來覆蓋。"]}]}]},"fantasy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幻想，想象；想象產物，幻想作品；虛擬比賽（遊戲）；幻想曲，整合曲；期望"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"想象，幻想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fantasy</b> is a pleasant situation or event that you think about and that you want to happen, especially one that is unlikely to happen. 幻想","examples":["...fantasies of romance and true love. …對浪漫和真愛的幻想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a story or situation that someone creates from their imagination and that is not based on reality as <b>fantasy</b>. 虛幻的故事; 幻想的情境","examples":["The film is more of an ironic fantasy than a horror story. 這部電影比較像是諷刺的幻想故事，而不是恐怖片。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fantasy</b> is the activity of imagining things. 幻想","examples":["...a world of imagination, passion, fantasy, reflection. …一個想像、激情、幻想和反思的世界。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fantasy</b> football, baseball, or another sport is a game in which players choose an imaginary team and score points based on the actual performances of the members of their team in real games. 夢幻的 (運動類電子遊戲)","examples":["Haskins said he has been playing fantasy baseball for the past five years. 哈斯金斯說他在過去的５年裡一直在打夢幻棒球遊戲。"]}]}]},"farewell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"告別；離去；分別時的美好祝願"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"告別的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"告別，歡送"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"再見，一路順風"}],"sections":[{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Farewell</b> means the same as . 別了 (L>同)(goodbye)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Farewell</b> is also a noun. 告別","examples":["They said their farewells there at the cafe. 他們在咖啡館那兒道了別。"]}]}]},"ferry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"渡船，擺渡；渡口"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擺渡，渡運；空運"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ferry</b> is a boat that transports passengers and sometimes also vehicles, usually across rivers or short stretches of sea. 渡船; 渡輪","examples":["They had recrossed the River Gambia by ferry. 他們乘船又一次渡過了甘比亞河。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>ferries</b> people or goods, it transports them, usually by means of regular trips between the same two places. 運送","examples":["Every day, a plane arrives to ferry guests to and from Bird Island Lodge. 每天，一架飛機到達以運送進出鳥島賓館的客人。"]}]}]},"feast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宴會，筵席；盛會，特別的享受；宗教節日"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"飽餐，盡情享用；宴請，設宴招待（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>feast</b> is a large and special meal. 盛宴","examples":["Lunch was a feast of meat and vegetables, cheese, yoghurt and fruit, with unlimited wine. 午餐是一場盛宴，有肉、蔬菜、乳酪、酸奶和水果，以及不限量的葡萄酒。","The fruit was often served at wedding feasts. 婚宴上常有水果供應。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>feast</b> is a day or time of the year when a special religious celebration takes place. 宗教節日; 宗教節慶時期","examples":["The Jewish feast of Passover began last night. 猶太人的宗教節日逾越節昨晚開始了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"赴宴","examples":["The feasting, drinking, dancing and revelry continued for several days. 宴會、暢飲、跳舞和狂歡持續了幾天。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feast</b> <b>on</b> a particular food, you eat a large amount of it with great enjoyment. 盡情地吃","examples":["They feasted well into the afternoon on mutton and corn stew. 他們盡情享用玉米燉羊肉，一直吃到下午。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>feast</b>, you take part in a feast. 赴宴","examples":["Only a few feet away, their captors feasted in the castle's banqueting hall. 僅僅幾英尺外，俘獲他們的人在城堡的宴會廳裡大吃大喝。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feast</b> your <b>eyes on</b> something, you look at it for a long time with great attention because you find it very attractive. 盡情欣賞","examples":["She stood feasting her eyes on the view. 她站著盡情欣賞著那片景色。"]}]}]},"firecracker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞭炮，爆竹；傑出（或有吸引力）的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>firecracker</b> is a firework that makes several loud bangs when it is lit. 爆竹","examples":[]}]}]},"fireplace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壁爐；（作裝飾用的）壁爐架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a room, the <b>fireplace</b> is the place where a fire can be lit and the area on the wall and floor surrounding this place. 壁爐","examples":["In the evenings, we gathered around the fireplace and talked in hushed whispers. 晚上，我們聚集在壁爐周圍輕聲交談。"]}]}]},"fetch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（去）拿來，（去）找來；售得，賣得；推匯出，演繹出；吸引，迷住；抵達，到達；<非正式>給（某人）以（重重的一擊或一巴掌）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fetch</b> something or someone, you go and get them from the place where they are. 去取(某物); 去接(某人)","examples":["Sylvia fetched a towel from the bathroom. 西爾維婭從浴室拿來一條毛巾。","Fetch me a glass of water. 給我拿杯水來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>fetches</b> a particular sum of money, it is sold for that amount. 賣得","examples":["The painting is expected to fetch between two and three million dollars. 這幅畫預計能賣到兩百到三百萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the reach, stretch, etc, of a mechanism 機械裝置的延伸部分","examples":[]}]}]},"extent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"程度；範圍，長度"}],"sections":[]},"fiction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小說；虛構的事，謊言；杜撰，編造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fiction</b> refers to books and stories about imaginary people and events, rather than books about real people or events. 小說","examples":["Immigrant tales have always been popular themes in fiction. 移民故事一直是小說的流行主題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A statement or account that is <b>fiction</b> is not true. 虛構","examples":["The truth or fiction of this story has never been truly determined. 這個故事是真實還是虛構，一直沒有定論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is a <b>fiction</b>, it is not true, although people sometimes pretend that it is true. 假象","examples":["Total recycling is a fiction. 完全回收利用是假象。"]}]}]},"flunk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（非正式，多用於美國英語）考試不及格；失敗；放棄；flunk out：因成績不及格而退學（常接 out of）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（非正式，多用於美國英語）未透過（考試或課程）；給（學生）不及格成績"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（非正式，多用於美國英語）不及格；失敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flunk</b> an exam or a course, you fail to reach the required standard. 未透過 (考試或課程)","examples":["Your son is upset because he flunked a history exam. 你兒子很沮喪是因為他沒透過歷史考試。"]}]}]},"finance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"財政，金融；資金，財源；財務事務，經濟情況"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供資金；貸款購買，賒購"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>finances</b> something such as a project or a purchase, they provide the money that is needed to pay for them. 資助","examples":["The fund has been used largely to finance the construction of federal prisons. 該基金大部分已用於資助聯邦監獄的建造。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Finance</b> is also a noun. 資助","examples":["A United States delegation is in Japan seeking finance for a major scientific project. 1個美國代表團正在日本為一個重大科研專案尋求資助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Finance</b> is the commercial or government activity of managing money, debt, credit, and investment. 金融; 財政","examples":["...a major player in the world of high finance. …高層金融界的大腕。","The report recommends an overhaul of public finances. 這份報告建議對公共財政進行徹底檢視。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the amount of money that you have and how well it is organized as your <b>finances</b>. 財務狀況","examples":["Be prepared for unexpected news concerning your finances. 對關於你財務狀況的意外訊息要做好準備。"]}]}]},"fort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"堡壘，要塞；<美>兵營，軍營；<史>邊界貿易站"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fort</b> is a strong building or a place with a wall or fence around it where soldiers can stay and be safe from the enemy. 堡壘; 碉堡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hold the fort</b> for someone or if you <b>hold down the fort</b>, you take care of things for them while they are somewhere else or are busy doing something else. 代為處理事務","examples":["His business partner is holding the fort while he is away. 他的生意夥伴在他不在的時候代他處理事務。","\"I'll hold down the fort until he's back,\" Clark said. “在他回來之前我會代他處理事務，”克拉克說。"]}]}]},"foam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泡沫，氣泡；泡沫橡膠，海綿橡膠；泡沫劑，泡沫產品；唾液，汗沫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"起泡沫，有泡沫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Foam</b> consists of a mass of small bubbles that are formed when air and a liquid are mixed together. 泡沫 (橡膠); 海綿","examples":["The water curved round the rocks in great bursts of foam. 水流卷繞著岩石產生大量的泡沫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Foam</b> is used to refer to various kinds of manufactured products which have a soft, light texture like a thick liquid. 泡沫","examples":["...shaving foam. …剃鬚泡沫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Foam</b> or <b>foam rubber</b> is soft rubber full of small holes which is used, for example, to make mattresses and cushions. 泡沫 (橡膠); 海綿","examples":["...modern three-piece suites filled with foam rubber. …塞滿海綿的現代3件套。"]}]}]},"forecast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預測，預報"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"預測，預報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>forecast</b> is a statement of what is expected to happen in the future, especially in relation to a particular event or situation. 預報","examples":["...a forecast of a 2.25 percent growth in the economy. …2.25%經濟增長的預報。","He delivered his election forecast. 他作了他的選舉預報。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>forecast</b> future events, you say what you think is going to happen in the future. 預言","examples":["They forecast a humiliating defeat for the president. 他們預言總統蒙受羞辱的一次失敗。"]}]}]},"fossil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"化石；<非正式>思想僵化的人；僵化的事物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"化石的，從地下采掘出的；不變的，古老的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fossil</b> is the hard remains of a prehistoric animal or plant that are found inside a rock. 化石","examples":[]}]}]},"formula":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"計劃，方案；配方，處方；公式，方程式；分子式，結構式；配方奶，代乳品；（特定場合的）慣用詞語，套話；（影片、書籍等的）套路"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>formula</b> is a plan that is invented in order to deal with a particular problem. 方案","examples":["...a peace formula. …一項和平方案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>formula</b> is a group of letters, numbers, or other symbols which represents a scientific or mathematical rule. 公式","examples":["He developed a mathematical formula describing the distances of the planets from the Sun. 他提出了一個描述各行星與太陽之間距離的數學公式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In science, the <b>formula</b> for a substance is a list of the amounts of various substances which make up that substance, or an indication of the atoms that it is composed of. 分子式","examples":["Glucose and fructose have the same chemical formula but have very different properties. 葡萄糖和果糖具有相同的化學分子式但有很不同的特性。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>formula for</b> a particular situation, usually a good one, is a course of action or a combination of actions that is certain or likely to result in that situation. (達成通常為好的結局的) 行動方案","examples":["After he was officially pronounced the world's oldest man, he offered this simple formula for a long and happy life. 在他被正式宣佈為世界上最老的人之後，他提供了這一長壽和幸福生活的簡單方法。"]}]}]},"flush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人的皮膚或臉）發紅（尤指因病或激動）；沖洗（抽水馬桶），（抽水馬桶）被沖洗；（用水或其他液體）沖洗；（用液體）沖走；把（獵鳥，動物）趕出隱藏地，使暴露；（使）發光；使（液體）流過；（植物）綻出新芽；嵌平（接合處）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"臉紅，皮膚髮紅（因尷尬、發熱等原因）；一陣強烈情感；（尤指抽水馬桶的）沖洗；（廁所裡的）沖水裝置，抽水馬桶；旺盛期；（突如其來的）大量；急流；（樹葉或幼苗等）破土而出的時期，（葉、花或果的）繁茂生長；有暖色之處，光亮之處；同花的一手牌，同花順；驅趕（獵鳥）；（突如其來的）大批，大量"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（兩物體表面）完全齊平的；<非正式>（尤指錢）充裕的，大量的；（門）平的，無裝飾的；（印刷文字）不縮排的，齊頭排的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（與另一平面）齊平地；不偏不倚地，正好地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flush</b>, your face gets red because you are hot or ill, or because you are feeling a strong emotion such as embarrassment or anger. 臉紅","examples":["Do you sweat a lot or flush a lot? 你常出汗或是常臉紅嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flush</b> is also a noun. 臉紅","examples":["There was a slight flush on his cheeks. 他的面頰上有淡淡的紅暈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flush</b> is also a noun. 沖水","examples":["He heard the flush of a toilet. 他聽到馬桶的沖水聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a period of fresh growth of leaves, shoots, etc (樹葉或幼苗等)破土而出的時期","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(in poker and similar games) a hand containing only one suit (撲克牌等遊戲中的)一手同花牌","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"臉紅的","examples":["Her face was flushed with anger. 她氣得滿臉通紅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"level or even with another surface (與另一平面)平齊的","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"having plenty of money 富裕的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>flushes</b> a toilet after using it, they fill the toilet bowl with water in order to clean it, usually by pressing a handle or pulling a chain. You can also say that a toilet <b>flushes</b>. 衝 (馬桶)","examples":["She flushed the toilet and went back in the bedroom. 她衝了馬桶，然後回到臥室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>flush</b> something <b>down</b> the toilet, you get rid of it by putting it into the toilet bowl and flushing the toilet. (從馬桶裡) 沖掉","examples":["He was found trying to flush the pills down the toilet. 他被發現試圖從馬桶沖掉藥丸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>flush</b> a part of your body, you clean it or make it healthier by using a large amount of liquid to get rid of dirt or harmful substances. 沖洗 (身體某部位)","examples":["Flush the eye with clean cold water for at least 15 minutes. 用乾淨的冷水沖洗眼睛至少15分鐘。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>flush</b> dirt or a harmful substance <b>out</b> of a place, you get rid of it by using a large amount of liquid. 沖洗","examples":["That won't flush out all the sewage, but it should unclog some stinking drains. 那樣做不會沖走全部的汙水，但應該能疏通一下發臭的下水道。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>flush</b> people or animals <b>out</b> of a place where they are hiding, you find or capture them by forcing them to come out of that place. 把…趕出","examples":["They flushed them out of their hiding places. 他們將其趕出藏身之地。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flush out</b> means the same as . flush out同flush","examples":["...an \"alternative\" therapy that gently flushes out the colon to remove toxins. …透過溫和沖洗大腸排毒的一種“替代”療法。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"so as to be level or even 平齊地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cause (surfaces) to be on the same level or in the same plane 使在同一水平面上","examples":[]}]}]},"founder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鑄造工，鑄造廠業主（或廠長）；創立者，締造者；（動物）新群體建立者（尤指已受孕的雌性昆蟲）；（馬等有蹄動物的）蹄葉炎，馬跛病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（船）沉沒；（事業，計劃）失敗，垮掉；絆倒，摔倒；（尤指馬等有蹄動物的）患蹄葉炎；感到寒冷；（牲口）因過食而得病"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>founder</b> of an institution, organization, or building is the person who got it started or caused it to be built, often by providing the necessary money. 建立人","examples":["He was one of the founders of the university's medical faculty. 他是該大學醫學院的建立人之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person who makes metal castings 澆鑄工","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(<b>in combination</b>) 製造(某種)金屬鑄件的人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a plan or project <b>founders</b>, it fails because of a particular point, difficulty, or problem. 失敗","examples":["The talks have foundered, largely because of the reluctance of some members of the government to do a deal with criminals. 會談已經擱淺了，主要是因為一些政府成員不願意和罪犯們達成協議。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a ship) to sink (船隻)沉沒","examples":[]}]}]},"fragrance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芳香，香氣；香水"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fragrance</b> is a pleasant or sweet smell. 香味","examples":["...a shrubby plant with a strong characteristic fragrance. …一種有獨特濃郁香味的灌木。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fragrance</b> is a pleasant-smelling liquid which people put on their bodies to make themselves smell nice. 香水","examples":["The advertisement is for a men's fragrance. 這則廣告介紹一款男士香水。"]}]}]},"foundation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地基，基礎；基本原理，根據；基金會；建立，創辦；（化妝打底用的）粉底霜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>foundation</b> <b>of</b> something such as a belief or way of life is the things on which it is based. 基礎","examples":["Best friends are the foundation of my life. 良友們是我生活的基礎。","The issue strikes at the very foundation of our community. 這個問題嚴重影響到我們社會的基礎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>foundation</b> is an organization which provides money for a special purpose such as research or charity. 基金會","examples":["...the National Foundation for Educational Research. …全國教育研究基金會。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>foundations</b> of a building or other structure are the layer of bricks or concrete below the ground that it is built on. 地基","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a story, idea, or argument has <b>no</b> <b>foundation</b>, there are no facts to prove that it is true. 根據","examples":["The allegations were without foundation. 這些指控沒有根據。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Foundation</b> is a skin-coloured cream that you put on your face before putting on the rest of your makeup. 粉底霜","examples":["Use foundation and/or face powder afterwards for an even skin tone. 隨後使用粉底霜和（或）粉餅以使皮膚色調均勻。"]}]}]},"formation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組成物；構成；形成，產生；編隊，隊形；（社會、政治等的）形態"}],"sections":[]},"freshman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（中學或大學的）一年級學生；<美> 新手；新手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the United States, a <b>freshman</b> is a student who is in his or her first year at a high school or college. (美國中學或大學的)一年級學生","examples":[]}]}]},"frequency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出現次數；頻繁；頻率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>frequency</b> of an event is the number of times it happens during a particular period. 頻率","examples":["The frequency of Kara's phone calls increased rapidly. 卡拉打電話的頻率迅速增加。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In physics, the <b>frequency</b> of a sound wave or a radio wave is the number of times it vibrates within a specified period of time. (物理學) 頻率","examples":["You can't hear waves of such a high frequency. 你聽不到這麼高頻率的聲波。","...a frequency of 24 kilohertz. …24千赫的頻率。"]}]}]},"frustration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懊惱，沮喪；受阻，挫敗；令人懊喪（或懊惱、沮喪）的事物"}],"sections":[]},"freeway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>高速公路"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>freeway</b> is a major road that has been specially built for fast travel over long distances. Freeways have several lanes and special places where traffic gets on and leaves. Another word for freeway is motorway. 高速公路","examples":["The speed limit on the freeway is 55mph. 這條高速公路的限速為每小時55英里。"]}]}]},"frown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"皺眉，蹙額；皺眉對……表示不滿；不同意，不許可（frown on/upon）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"皺眉，蹙額"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>frowns</b>, their eyebrows become drawn together, because they are annoyed, worried, or puzzled, or because they are concentrating. 皺眉","examples":["Nancy shook her head, frowning. 南希搖搖頭，皺著眉頭。","He frowned at her anxiously. 他焦急地朝她皺了皺眉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Frown</b> is also a noun. 皺眉狀態","examples":["There was a deep frown on the boy's face. 那個男孩的臉上有深皺眉的表情。"]}]}]},"fulfillment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"履行，實行，完成（承諾、責任、要求等）；滿足（感），成就感；（物流）訂單履行"}],"sections":[]},"frost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嚴寒天氣，霜凍；霜；冷淡，冷漠；<英，非正式>失敗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）蒙上霜，結霜；<美>在（糕餅）上撒糖霜；<美>將（頭髮）挑染成淡色；為（玻璃）制毛面；受凍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is <b>frost</b> or a <b>frost</b>, the temperature outside falls below freezing point and the ground becomes covered in ice crystals. 霜","examples":["There is frost on the ground and snow is forecast. 地上有霜，預報有雪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>frost</b> a cake, you cover and decorate it with icing. 給 (蛋糕) 撒糖霜","examples":["She was frosting the cupcakes while we talked. 我們交談時，她在給杯形蛋糕撒糖霜。"]}]}]},"fundamental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"根本的，基本的；必需的，必不可少的；不能再分的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"基本原理；基音，基頻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>fundamental</b> to describe things, activities, and principles that are very important or essential. They affect the basic nature of other things or are the most important element upon which other things depend. 基本的","examples":["Our constitution embodies all the fundamental principles of democracy. 我們的憲法體現了民主的所有基本原則。","A fundamental human right is being withheld from these people. 這些人的一項基本人權正被剝奪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>fundamental</b> to describe something which exists at a deep and basic level, and is therefore likely to continue. 根本的","examples":["But on this question, the two leaders have very fundamental differences. 但在這個問題上，這兩位領導人有著極根本的分歧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>is fundamental to</b> another, it is absolutely necessary to it, and the second thing cannot exist, succeed, or be imagined without it. 絕對必要的","examples":["He believes better relations with China are fundamental to the well-being of the area. 他相信與中國的更好關係對這個地區的福祉是絕對必要的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>fundamental</b> to show that you are referring to what you consider to be the most important aspect of a situation, and that you are not concerned with less important details. 主要的","examples":["The fundamental problem lies in their inability to distinguish between reality and invention. 主要問題在於他們不能區分現實和虛構。"]}]}]},"funeral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葬禮，喪禮；<美>葬禮上的佈道；<古>出殯行列，送葬隊伍；<非正式>需要操心的事"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"葬禮的，似葬禮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>funeral</b> is the ceremony that is held when the body of someone who has died is buried or cremated. 葬禮","examples":["The funeral will be held in Joplin, Missouri. 該葬禮將在密蘇里州的喬普林市舉行。"]}]}]},"fuel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燃料，燃燒劑；刺激因素，刺激性言行；（為身體提供能量的）食物，飲料，藥劑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給……）提供燃料，加油；刺激，加劇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fuel</b> is a substance such as coal, oil, or petrol that is burned to provide heat or power. 燃料","examples":["They ran out of fuel. 他們用完了燃料。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>fuel</b> a situation means to make it become worse or more intense. 加劇","examples":["The result will inevitably fuel speculation about the prime minister's future. 該結果將不可避免地加劇人們對首相前途的猜測。"]}]}]},"gangster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歹徒，匪徒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gangster</b> is a member of an organized group of violent criminals. (結成團伙的) 匪徒","examples":["...a gangster film. …一部黑幫片。"]}]}]},"frame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"框架，邊框；（傢俱、建築物、車輛等的）構架，支架；體格，骨架；眼鏡框；（系統、概念或文章的）基本框架；鏡頭，畫面；（連環漫畫中的）一幅畫；（網頁的）一個區域；（斯諾克或保齡球的）一局；（玻璃或塑膠的箱式）輕便溫床；（紡織、編結或刺繡用的）框；替換框架；（計算機或通訊）幀，影格"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝框架；勾勒出；圍繞；<非正式>陷害，誣陷；制定，擬訂；（措詞謹慎地）表達"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有木架的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>frame</b> of a picture or mirror is the wood, metal, or plastic that is fitted around it, especially when it is displayed or hung on a wall. 框架","examples":["Estelle kept a photograph of her mother in a silver frame on the kitchen mantelpiece. 埃絲特爾把她母親的一張照片放在廚房壁爐架上的銀質相框裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>frame</b> of an object such as a building, chair, or window is the arrangement of wooden, metal, or plastic bars between which other material is fitted, and which give the object its strength and shape. 構架","examples":["He supplied housebuilders with modern timber frames. 他為建房者提供了現代化的木製構架。","With difficulty he released the mattress from the metal frame, and groped beneath it. 他費了很大勁把床墊從金屬架上卸下來，然後在下面摸索一番。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>frames</b> of a pair of glasses are all the metal or plastic parts of it, but not the lenses. 眼鏡框","examples":["He was wearing new glasses with gold wire frames. 他戴著一副新的金絲框眼鏡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>frame</b> of movie film is one of the many separate photographs that it consists of. 畫面","examples":["Standard 8mm projects at 16 frames per second. 標準的8毫米電影每秒放映16幀畫面。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to someone's body as their <b>frame</b>, especially when you are describing the general shape of their body. 身軀","examples":["Their belts are pulled tight against their bony frames. 他們的腰帶緊裹著瘦骨嶙峋的軀體。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"an enumeration of a population for the purposes of sampling, esp as the basis of a stratified sample 人口抽樣底冊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a picture or photograph <b>is framed</b>, it is put in a frame. 給 (圖畫或照片) 配框","examples":["The picture is now ready to be mounted and framed. 這幅畫現在可以裝裱、配框了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>is framed</b> by a particular thing, it is surrounded by that thing in a way that makes the object more striking or attractive to look at. 環繞","examples":["The swimming pool is framed by tropical gardens. 游泳池四周環繞著熱帶花園。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>frames</b> an innocent person, they make other people think that that person is guilty of a crime, by lying or inventing evidence. 誣陷","examples":["I need to find out who tried to frame me. 我需要查出誰試圖誣陷我。"]}]}]},"gene":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基因，遺傳因子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gene</b> is the part of a cell in a living thing which controls its physical characteristics, growth, and development. 基因","examples":["The gene for asthma has been identified. 哮喘病的基因已被識別。"]}]}]},"gaze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"凝視，注視"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"凝視，注視；特定視角，特定角度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gaze</b> <b>at</b> someone or something, you look steadily at them for a long time, for example because you find them attractive or interesting, or because you are thinking about something else. 凝視","examples":["...gazing at herself in the mirror. …凝視著鏡中的她自己。","Sitting in his wicker chair, he gazed reflectively at the fire. 坐在他的柳條椅中，他若有所思地凝視著火焰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can talk about someone's <b>gaze</b> as a way of describing how they are looking at something, especially when they are looking steadily at it. 凝視","examples":["The Monsignor turned his gaze from the flames to meet the Colonel's. 這位閣下把他凝視的目光從火焰上移開，與上校的目光相遇。","She felt increasingly uncomfortable under the woman's steady gaze. 她在那女人目不轉睛的凝視下感到愈發不舒服。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in the public gaze</b>, they are receiving a lot of attention from the general public. 受公眾關注","examples":["You won't find a couple more in the public gaze than Michael and Lizzie. 你找不到比邁克爾和莉齊更受公眾關注的夫妻了。"]}]}]},"gallery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美術館，畫廊；（大廳的）樓座，樓上旁聽席；（劇場中的）頂層樓座；陽臺，露臺；一群（相似的人或物）；長廊，走廊；（礦井下的）巷道；觀眾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gallery</b> is a place that has permanent exhibitions of works of art in it. (藝術作品的) 陳列室; 美術館","examples":["...an art gallery. …一座美術館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gallery</b> is a privately owned building or room where people can look at and buy works of art. 私人字畫店","examples":["The painting is in the gallery upstairs. 那幅畫在樓上的字畫店裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>gallery</b> is an area high above the ground at the back or at the sides of a large room or hall. 廊臺","examples":["A crowd already filled the gallery. 一群人已經擠滿了廊臺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The gallery</b> in a theatre or concert hall is an area high above the ground that usually contains the cheapest seats. (劇場或音樂廳內通常票價最低的) 頂層樓座","examples":["They had been forced to find cheap tickets in the gallery. 他們被迫去找頂層樓座的廉價票。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>play to the gallery</b>, you do something in public in a way which you hope will impress people. 譁眾取寵","examples":["...but I must tell you that in my opinion you're both now playing to the gallery. …但是我必須告訴你們，在我看來你們倆現在都是在譁眾取寵。"]}]}]},"generosity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"慷慨，大方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>generosity</b>, you mean that they are generous, especially in doing or giving more than is usual or expected. 慷慨","examples":["There are stories about his generosity, the massive amounts of money he gave to charities. 關於他的慷慨有些傳聞，說他向慈善機構捐獻鉅款。"]}]}]},"germ":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"病菌，細菌；起源，萌芽；極少量；胚芽，胚胎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>germ</b> is a very small organism that causes disease. 病菌","examples":["Chlorine is widely used to kill germs. 氯廣泛用於殺菌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>germ of</b> something such as an idea is something which developed or might develop into that thing. (思想等的) 萌芽","examples":["This was the germ of a book. 這是一本書的創作萌芽。"]}]}]},"generation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一代（人）；一代人的時間；（產品發展的）代；產生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>generation</b> is all the people in a group or country who are of a similar age, especially when they are considered as having the same experiences or attitudes. 一代人","examples":["...the younger generation of party members. …較年輕一代的黨員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>generation</b> is the period of time, usually considered to be about thirty years, that it takes for children to grow up and become adults and have children of their own. 代 (通常約為三十年)","examples":["Within a generation, flight has become the method used by many travellers. 在不到一代的時間裡，飛行已成為許多旅行者的出行方式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>generation</b> to refer to a stage of development in the design and manufacture of machines or equipment. (機械、裝置的設計和製造的) 一代","examples":["...a new generation of Apple computers. …新一代蘋果電腦。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Generation</b> is used to indicate how long members of your family have had a particular nationality. For example, second generation means that you were born in the country you live in, but your parents were not. (指家庭成員擁有某國國籍的時間) 代","examples":["...second-generation Jamaicans in New York. …在紐約的第二代牙買加人。"]}]}]},"gear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"排擋，齒輪；（用於特定目的的）裝備，服裝；（做事的）速度，努力；（特定用途的）器械，裝置；<非正式>毒品；<非正式>所有物，財物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使變速，使調擋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>gears</b> on a machine or vehicle are a device for changing the rate at which energy is changed into motion. 排擋","examples":["On hills, he must use low gears. 在山上，他必須用低速擋。","The car was in fourth gear. 那輛汽車處於第4擋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>gear</b> involved in a particular activity is the equipment or special clothing that you use. (用於特定活動的) 裝置、服裝","examples":["About 100 officers in riot gear were needed to break up the fight. 大約需要100名配備防暴裝備的警官來結束那場鬥毆。","...fishing gear. …釣魚用具。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Gear</b> means clothing. 衣服","examples":["I used to wear trendy gear but it just looked ridiculous. 我過去常穿時髦服裝，但那看起來簡直滑稽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"被動及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is geared to</b> or <b>toward</b> a particular purpose, they are organized or designed in order to achieve that purpose. 使適合","examples":["Colleges are not always geared to the needs of mature students. 大學並不總是去適應成年學生的需要。","My training was geared toward winning gold. 我的訓練是為贏得金牌去規劃的。"]}]}]},"giggle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"咯咯地笑，傻笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輕笑，傻笑；<非正式>有趣的人（或事），笑話；止不住的咯咯笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>giggles</b>, they laugh in a childlike way, because they are amused, nervous, or embarrassed. 咯咯地笑","examples":["Both girls began to giggle. 兩個女孩都咯咯地笑起來。","\"I beg your pardon?\" she giggled. “對不起，你說什麼？”她咯咯地笑著問。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Giggle</b> is also a noun. 咯咯的笑","examples":["She gave a little giggle. 她咯咯地笑了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>the giggles</b>, you mean they cannot stop giggling. 咯咯笑個不止","examples":["I was so nervous I got the giggles. 我緊張得咯咯笑個不止。"]}]}]},"ginger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生薑；姜（產於東南亞，外表似竹）；薑黃色；長著薑黃色頭髮的人；姜味汽水（ginger ale 的簡稱）；精神，活力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用姜給……調味；激勵，使有生氣（ginger sb./sth. up）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（主要指毛髮或動物毛皮）薑黃色的；姜味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ginger</b> is the root of a plant that is used to flavour food. It has a sweet, spicy flavour and is often sold in powdered form. 姜","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ginger</b> is used to describe things that are orangey brown in colour. 薑黃色的","examples":["She was a mature lady with dyed ginger hair. 她是個成年女子，頭髮染成了薑黃色。"]}]}]},"glide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"滑行，滑動；滑翔；做事順利；悄悄地走，流逝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"滑動，滑行；（滑翔機或無動力飛機的）飛行，滑翔；滑音，延音；（尤指向腿側的）斜擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>glide</b> somewhere, you move silently and in a smooth and effortless way. 滑行","examples":["Waiters glide between tightly packed tables bearing trays of pasta. 侍者們託著一盤盤的義大利麵食在擁擠的餐桌間自如穿行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When birds or aeroplanes <b>glide</b>, they float on air currents. 滑翔","examples":["Our only companion is the wandering albatross, which glides effortlessly and gracefully behind the yacht. 我們惟一的伴侶是那隻漂泊信天翁，它輕快優雅地滑翔在遊艇後面。"]}]}]},"globe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地球，世界；地球儀；球體，球狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成球狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the world as <b>the</b> <b>globe</b> when you are emphasizing how big it is or that something happens in many different parts of it. 全球","examples":["...bottles of beer from every corner of the globe. …一瓶瓶來自全球各個角落的啤酒。","70% of our globe's surface is water. 我們地球表面的70%是水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>globe</b> is a ball-shaped object with a map of the world on it. It is usually fixed on a stand. 地球儀","examples":["Three large globes stand on the floor. 地板上立著三個大地球儀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Any ball-shaped object can be referred to as a <b>globe</b>. 球狀物","examples":["The overhead light was covered now with a white globe. 頂燈現在被一個白色的球狀物罩了起來。"]}]}]},"grapefruit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"西柚，葡萄柚；葡萄柚樹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grapefruit</b> is a large, round, yellow fruit, similar to an orange, that has a sharp, slightly bitter taste. 葡萄柚","examples":[]}]}]},"goods":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商品；動產，私人財產；<英>（公路、鐵路等運輸的）貨物；<美，非正式>本領；<美，非正式>正要尋找的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Goods</b> are things that are made to be sold. 商品","examples":["Money can be exchanged for goods or services. 錢可以用來換取商品或服務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>goods</b> are the things that you own and that can be moved. 私人財產; 動產","examples":["You can give your unwanted goods to charity. 你可以把不需要的東西捐給慈善機構。"]}]}]},"glimpse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一瞥，一看；短暫的感受，短暫的體驗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"瞥見；開始理解；<古>閃爍，隱約出現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get a <b>glimpse</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you see them very briefly and not very well. 一瞥","examples":["Some of the fans had waited 24 hours outside the hotel to catch a glimpse of their heroine. 某些追星族為了一睹女傑的風采已在賓館外守候了24小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>glimpse</b> <b>of</b> something is a brief experience of it or an idea about it that helps you understand or appreciate it better. 初步的感受","examples":["As university campuses become increasingly multiethnic, they offer a glimpse of the conflicts society will face tomorrow. 大學校園種族群體日趨多樣化，使人們初步感受到未來社會面臨的諸多衝突。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>glimpse</b> someone or something, you see them very briefly and not very well. 瞥見","examples":["She glimpsed a group of people standing on the bank of a river. 她瞥見一群人站在河岸上。"]}]}]},"genius":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天賦，天資；天才，智商很高的人；（擅長做某事的）高手；精華，精髓；對某人有很大好（或壞）影響的人；（神話中某個人、地方或機構的）守護神；（民族或時代的）普遍特徵"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>天才的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Genius</b> is very great ability or skill in a particular subject or activity. 天賦","examples":["This is the mark of her real genius as a designer. 這是她作為一名設計師的真正天賦的標誌。","The man had genius and had made his mark in the aviation world. 那位男士擁有天賦，而且在航空界已經成名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>genius</b> is a highly talented, creative, or intelligent person. 天才","examples":["Chaplin was not just a genius, he was among the most influential figures in film history. 卓別林不僅是個天才，還是電影史上最有影響的人物之一。"]}]}]},"graduation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"畢業；畢業典禮；（容器或裝置上的）刻度；在刻度尺上按度數（或其他比例分配）的劃分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Graduation</b> is the successful completion of a course of study at a university, college, or school, for which you receive a degree or diploma. 畢業","examples":["They asked what his plans were after graduation. 他們問他畢業後有何打算。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>graduation</b> is a special ceremony at a university, college, or school, at which degrees and diplomas are given to students who have successfully completed their studies. 畢業典禮","examples":["...the graduation ceremony at Yale. …耶魯大學的畢業典禮。"]}]}]},"gratitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感激之情，感謝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gratitude</b> is the state of feeling grateful. 感激","examples":["I wish to express my gratitude to Kathy Davis for her immense practical help. 我想向凱西•戴維斯表達謝意，因為她給了我許多實際的幫助。"]}]}]},"grammar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"語法，文法；（人的）語言知識及運用能力；語法書；語法理論，語法學；（某門類知識和技能的）基本原理；<英，非正式>中學；（計算機）文法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grammar</b> is the ways that words can be put together in order to make sentences. 語法","examples":["He doesn't have mastery of the basic rules of grammar. 他沒有掌握語法的基本規則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>grammar</b> is the way in which they obey or do not obey the rules of grammar when they write or speak. 語法的運用","examples":["His vocabulary was sound and his grammar excellent. 他的詞彙量豐富而且語法也很棒。"]}]}]},"grace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"優美，優雅；文雅，高雅；風度，體面；恩寵，恩典；飯前感恩禱告；寬限期，延緩期；大人（用於對公爵、公爵夫人或大主教的尊稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為增色，裝飾；使增光，使榮耀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone moves with <b>grace</b>, they move in a smooth, controlled, and attractive way. 優美","examples":["He moved with the grace of a trained boxer. 他的動作帶有一個訓練有素的拳擊手的風采。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>graces</b> are the ways of behaving and doing things which are considered polite and well-mannered. 風度","examples":["She didn't fit in and she had few social graces. 她不適應而且沒有什麼社交風度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In Christianity and some other religions, <b>grace</b> is the kindness that God shows to people because He loves them. (上帝的) 恩惠","examples":["It was only by the grace of God that no one died. 正是承蒙上帝的恩惠才沒有人死去。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone says <b>grace</b> before or after a meal, they say a prayer in which they thank God for the food and ask Him to bless it. (飯前或飯後的) 謝恩禱告","examples":["Leo, will you say grace? 利奧，你要做禱告嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>graces</b> a place or a person, you mean that it makes them more attractive. 使優美","examples":["He went to the beautiful old Shaker dresser that graced this homely room. 他走向那個使這間陋室生輝的漂亮的夏克爾式舊櫥櫃。"]}]}]},"greeting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"問候，招呼；賀詞，祝福"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"歡迎，迎接；對……作出反應；映入眼簾，撲鼻而來（greet 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>greeting</b> is something friendly that you say or do when you meet someone. 問候","examples":["His greeting was familiar and friendly. 他的問候親切而友好。","They exchanged greetings. 他們相互問候。"]}]}]},"groom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給動物）擦洗，刷洗；（動物為自己或另一動物）梳理毛髮；梳妝，打扮；修飾，修整（某物）；培訓，使做好準備；（尤指透過網際網路）勾引，誘姦（兒童）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"新郎；馬伕；<英>王室侍從官"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>groom</b> is the same as a . 新郎","examples":["...the bride and groom. …新娘和新郎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>groom</b> is someone whose job is to look after the horses in a stable and to keep them clean. 馬伕","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>groom</b> an animal, you clean its fur, usually by brushing it. 給 (動物) 梳毛刷洗","examples":["The horses were exercised and groomed with special care. 這些馬受到特殊的訓練和照料。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are groomed</b> <b>for</b> a special job, someone prepares you for it by teaching you the skills you will need. 培訓","examples":["George was already being groomed for the top job. 喬治已經為擔任該要職接受培訓。"]}]}]},"gull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鳥）鷗，海鷗；笨人，易受騙的人；（Gull）人名；（意、羅、瑞典）古爾；（英）格爾"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"騙，欺詐，愚弄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gull</b> is a common sea bird. 海鷗","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person who is easily fooled or cheated 易上當受騙的人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fool, cheat, or hoax 欺騙; 愚弄","examples":[]}]}]},"grave":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"墳墓，墓穴；死亡，終結；（廢舊機器等的）堆積處；（法語等語言裡的）抑音符號，沉音符"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嚴峻的，嚴重的；嚴肅的，莊重的；認真的，深切的；帶鈍重音符的；（用作演奏演唱指示）緩慢的，莊嚴的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用作演奏演唱指示）緩慢地，莊嚴地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>銘記，銘刻；<古>刻（銘文，影象）；<史>（用燒掉附著物然後塗以瀝青的方法）清理（船底），拷鏟油漆（船底）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grave</b> is a place where a dead person is buried. 墳墓","examples":["They used to visit her grave twice a year. 他們以前每年給她上兩次墳。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grave</b> event or situation is very serious, important, and worrying. 嚴重的","examples":["He said that the situation in his country is very grave. 他說他的國家形勢很嚴峻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>grave</b> person is quiet and serious in their appearance or behaviour. 嚴肅的","examples":["Anxiously, she examined his unusually grave face. 她不安地審視著他那張異常嚴肅的臉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some languages, such as French, a <b>grave</b> accent is a symbol that is placed over a vowel in a word to show how the vowel is pronounced. For example, the word \"mère\" has a grave accent over the first \"e.\" 抑音符號","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴重地","examples":["They had gravely impaired the credibility of the government. 他們已嚴重地損害了政府的信用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嚴肅地","examples":["\"I think I've covered that business more than adequately,\" he said gravely. “我認為我已經把那件事搞得夠詳細的了，”他一臉嚴肅地說。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone who is dead would <b>turn</b> or <b>turn over in</b> their <b>grave</b> <b>at</b> something that is happening now, you mean that they would be very shocked or upset by it, if they were alive. (讓死者) 在九泉之下不得安寧","examples":["Darwin must be turning in his grave at the thought of what is being perpetrated in his name. 一想到冒他之名所做下的那些事，達爾文在九泉之下一定會不得安寧。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut, carve, sculpt, or engrave 鑿; 雕; 刻","examples":[]}]}]},"guilt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"內疚；罪行；罪責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Guilt</b> is an unhappy feeling that you have because you have done something wrong or think that you have done something wrong. 內疚","examples":["Her emotions had ranged from anger to guilt in the space of a few seconds. 她的情緒在幾秒鐘內由憤怒轉為內疚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Guilt</b> is the fact that you have done something wrong or illegal. 罪行","examples":["The trial is concerned only with the determination of guilt according to criminal law. 審判只是根據刑法進行定罪。"]}]}]},"grief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指因某人去世引起的）悲傷，悲痛；傷心事，悲痛事；<非正式>麻煩，煩惱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grief</b> is a feeling of extreme sadness. 悲痛","examples":["...a huge outpouring of national grief for the victims of the shootings. …舉國上下對槍殺案受害者們所表現出的巨大悲痛之情。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>comes to grief</b>, it fails. If someone <b>comes to grief</b>, they fail in something they are doing, and may be hurt. 失敗; 受傷","examples":["So many marriages have come to grief over lack of money. 如此多的婚姻因為缺錢而破裂。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>Good grief</b>\" when they are surprised or shocked. (表示驚奇或震驚) 哎呀","examples":["\"He's been arrested for theft and burglary.\"—\"Good grief!\" “他因為偷竊和入室盜竊被逮捕了。”—“我的天哪！”"]}]}]},"gulf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海灣；鴻溝，分歧；波斯灣；（地面的）裂口，深淵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gulf</b> is an important or significant difference between two people, things, or groups. 巨大的差距","examples":["Within society, there is a growing gulf between rich and poor. 在社會的內部，貧富之間有著一道日益加深的鴻溝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>gulf</b> is a large area of sea which extends a long way into the surrounding land. 海灣","examples":["Hurricane Andrew was last night heading into the Gulf of Mexico. 安德魯颶風昨晚進入墨西哥灣。"]}]}]},"handwriting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手寫，書寫；筆跡，書法；手稿"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"手寫，書寫（handwrite 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>handwriting</b> is your style of writing with a pen or pencil. 筆跡; 筆法","examples":["The address was in Anna's handwriting. 這個地址是安娜的筆跡。"]}]}]},"grind":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"磨碎，碾碎；使鋒利；用力擠壓；摩擦（發出刺耳聲）；<非正式>（跳舞者）扭擺臀部；搖動（碾磨機等機器的）手柄操作；用絞肉機絞（肉）；（機器或車輛伴有噪音地）緩慢運轉，費力移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"苦差事；摩擦（聲），碾磨（聲）；<美，非正式>埋頭苦讀的學生；磨製級別； <愛爾蘭>小型教學班；<非正式>（舞蹈中的）扭臀動作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grind</b> a substance such as corn, you crush it between two hard surfaces or with a machine until it becomes a fine powder. 把…磨碎","examples":["Store the peppercorns in an airtight container and grind the pepper as you need it. 將胡椒子儲藏在密封容器裡，當你需要的時候把它磨成粉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grind</b> something <b>into</b> a surface, you press and rub it hard into the surface using small circular or sideways movements. 碾壓","examples":["\"Well,\" I said, grinding my cigarette nervously into the granite step. “好吧，”我邊說邊緊張地把香菸在花崗岩臺階上碾滅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>grind</b> something, you make it smooth or sharp by rubbing it against a hard surface. 把…磨光; 把…磨鋒利","examples":["It was beyond my ability to grind a blade this broad. 把這麼寬的刀刃磨鋒利我做不到。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grind up</b> means the same as . 磨碎 (同)(grind)","examples":["He makes his own paint, grinding up the pigment with a little oil. 他把色料塊加少許油磨碎，自己製成繪畫顏料。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grind</b> your <b>teeth</b>, you rub your upper and lower teeth together as though you are chewing something. 磨牙","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a country's economy or something such as a process <b>grinds to a halt</b>, it gradually becomes slower or less active until it stops. (經濟或程序等) 漸漸地停止","examples":["The peace process has ground to a halt while Israel struggles to form a new government. 當以色列力圖建立新政府時，和平程序已逐漸停頓下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>grinds to a halt</b>, it stops slowly and noisily. (機動車) 轟隆隆地慢慢停下","examples":["The tanks ground to a halt after a hundred yards because the fuel had been siphoned out. 坦克在行駛100碼後由於燃料被抽走而轟隆隆地慢慢停了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>grinds</b> somewhere, it moves there very slowly and noisily. (機動車) 嘎嘎作響地緩慢移動","examples":["Tanks had crossed the border at five fifteen and were grinding south. 坦克已在5點15分穿過邊界，然後隆隆地向南開去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>grind</b> <b>of</b> a machine is the harsh, scraping noise that it makes, usually because it is old or is working too hard. (機器因年久或過度使用而發出的) 刺耳的磨擦聲","examples":["The grind of heavy machines could get on their nerves. 重型機器發出的嘎嘎磨擦聲會讓他們心煩意亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to routine tasks or activities as <b>the</b> <b>grind</b>, you mean they are boring and take up a lot of time and effort. 苦差事","examples":["Life continues to be a terrible grind for the ordinary person. 對於普通人來說，生活一直是個糟糕的苦差事。"]}]}]},"halt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）停止行進；阻止，中斷；（口令）立定；跛行；（尤指邏輯或詩韻）有缺陷；躊躇，猶豫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"停止，中止；<英>鄉間小火車站（只有站臺）；跛，瘸； 跛，瘸；（口令）立定"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"跛的，瘸的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or a vehicle <b>halts</b> or when something <b>halts</b> them, they stop moving in the direction they were going and stand still. 使停住; 停住","examples":["They halted at a short distance from the house. 他們停在離房子不遠處。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something such as growth, development, or activity <b>halts</b> or when you <b>halt</b> it, it stops completely. 使完全停止; 完全停止","examples":["Striking workers halted production at the auto plant yesterday. 昨天，汽車廠的罷工工人完全停止了生產。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(esp of logic or verse) to falter or be defective (尤指邏輯或詩韻)有缺陷; 不流暢","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an interruption or end to activity, movement, or progress (活動、運動或進展的)中止; 終止","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"lameness 跛; 瘸","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n/sentence substitute.","pos_name":"n/sentence substitute.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a command to halt, esp as an order when marching 立定！; 停止前進！(尤用於行軍中)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"lame 跛的; 瘸的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(<b>as collective noun;</b> preceded by <b>the</b>) (用作集體名詞，前面加)the","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>calls a halt</b> <b>to</b> something such as an activity, they decide not to continue with it or to end it immediately. 決定停止","examples":["The Russian government had called a halt to the construction of a new project in the Rostov region. 俄羅斯政府已經決定停止在羅斯托夫地區的一個新工程的修建。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something comes <b>to a halt</b>, they stop moving. 停止移動","examples":["The lift creaked to a halt at the ground floor. 電梯嘎吱一聲停在了底樓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as growth, development, or activity <b>comes</b> or <b>grinds</b> <b>to a halt</b> or <b>is brought</b> <b>to a halt</b>, it stops completely. 完全停止","examples":["Her political career came to a halt in December 1988. 她的政治生涯於1988年12月徹底結束了。"]}]}]},"harmonica":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口琴（等於 mouth organ）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>harmonica</b> is a small musical instrument. You play the harmonica by moving it across your lips and blowing and sucking air through it. 口琴","examples":[]}]}]},"hardship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"困苦，艱難"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hardship</b> is a situation in which your life is difficult or unpleasant, often because you do not have enough money. 困境","examples":["Many people are suffering economic hardship. 很多人正遭受著經濟困難。"]}]}]},"hatred":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"仇恨，憎恨，敵意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hatred</b> is an extremely strong feeling of dislike for someone or something. 憎恨","examples":["Her hatred of them would never lead her to murder. 她對他們的仇恨永遠不會將她引向兇殺。"]}]}]},"guarantee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"確保，保證；擔保，為……作保；保修，包換"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"保證，擔保；保修單，質量保證書；擔保金，抵押品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>guarantees</b> another, the first is certain to cause the second thing to happen. 確保","examples":["Surplus resources alone do not guarantee growth. 僅有富足的資源並不能確保發展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>guarantee</b> something, you promise that it will definitely happen, or that you will do or provide it for someone. 保證…必定發生; 保證…做某事或提供某物","examples":["Most states guarantee the right to free and adequate education. 大多數州都保證免費和適當教育的權利。","We guarantee that you will find a community with which to socialize. 我們保證你將找到一個可以社交的團體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a company <b>guarantees</b> its product or work, they provide a guarantee for it. 擔保","examples":["Some builders guarantee their work. 一些建築商為他們的工作擔保。","All Dreamland's electric blankets are guaranteed for three years. 所有“夢鄉”牌的電熱毯都保質3年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is a <b>guarantee</b> <b>of</b> something else makes it certain that it will happen or that it is true. 保證","examples":["A famous old name on a firm is not necessarily a guarantee of quality. 公司的老字號並不一定能保證質量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Guarantee</b> is also a noun. 保證","examples":["The editors can give no guarantee that they will fulfil their obligations. 這些編輯不能保證他們將履行職責。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>guarantee</b> is a written promise by a company to replace or repair a product free of charge if it has any faults within a particular time. 保修單","examples":["Whatever a guarantee says, when something goes wrong, you can still claim your rights from the shop. 不管保修單上怎麼說，當產品出現故障時，你仍然可以去商店維護自身的權益。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>guarantee</b> is money or something valuable that you give to someone to show that you will do what you have promised. 擔保物","examples":["Males between 18 and 20 had to leave a deposit as a guarantee of returning to do their military service. 18歲至20歲的男性必須留下押金作為回來服兵役的擔保。"]}]}]},"haste":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"倉促，急忙"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>趕緊，匆忙；<古>催促"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Haste</b> is the quality of doing something quickly, sometimes too quickly so that you are careless and make mistakes. 倉促","examples":["In their haste to escape the rising water, they dropped some expensive equipment. 在倉促逃離上漲的河水時，他們丟棄了一些貴重裝置。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in haste</b>, you do it quickly and hurriedly, and sometimes carelessly. 匆忙地","examples":["Don't act in haste or be hot-headed. 別匆忙行事，也別魯莽。"]}]}]},"hardware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）硬體；五金製品；裝備，裝置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In computer systems, <b>hardware</b> refers to the machines themselves as opposed to the programs which tell the machines what to do. Compare . 硬體","examples":["To be totally secure, you need a piece of hardware that costs about $200. 為保證絕對安全，你需要一個花費約為兩百美元的硬體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Military <b>hardware</b> is the machinery and equipment that is used by the armed forces, such as tanks, aircraft, and missiles. 裝備","examples":["...the billions which are spent on military hardware. …花費在軍事裝備上的數十億。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hardware</b> refers to tools and equipment that are used in the home and garden, for example nuts and bolts, screwdrivers, and hinges. 五金器具","examples":["...a shop from which an uncle had sold hardware and timber. …一家叔叔曾經在那裡賣五金器具和木材的店鋪。"]}]}]},"harmony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"和聲，和絃；融洽，和睦；和諧，協調；（內心的）平靜；四福音書的對照統一文字，（內容相似文字的）統一對照本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people are living <b>in</b> <b>harmony</b> <b>with</b> each other, they are living together peacefully rather than fighting or arguing. 融洽","examples":["...the notion that man should dominate nature rather than live in harmony with it. …人類應當支配自然而並非與自然和諧相處的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Harmony</b> is the pleasant combination of different notes of music played at the same time. 和聲","examples":["...singing in harmony. …和聲演唱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>harmony</b> of something is the way in which its parts are combined into a pleasant arrangement. 和諧","examples":["...the ordered harmony of the universe. …宇宙的有序和諧。"]}]}]},"headphone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耳機，雙耳式耳機，頭戴式耳機"}],"sections":[]},"helicopter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"直升機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用直升機運送；乘直升機飛至（某地）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>helicopter</b> is an aircraft with long blades on top that go around very fast. It is able to stay still in the air and to move straight upward or downward. 直升機","examples":[]}]}]},"honeymoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜜月"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"度蜜月"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>honeymoon</b> is a holiday taken by a man and a woman who have just got married. 蜜月","examples":["The next time I went abroad was on my honeymoon. 我接下來一次出國是去度蜜月。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>honeymoon</b> to refer to a period of time after the start of a new job or when a newly elected official takes office when everyone is pleased with the person or people concerned and is nice to them. 蜜月期 (指新的工作開始或新當選的官員任職後的和諧工作期)","examples":["Brett is enjoying a honeymoon period with both press and public. 佈雷特正在享受同媒體和公眾的蜜月期。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a recently married couple <b>honeymoon</b> somewhere, they go there on their honeymoon. 度蜜月","examples":["They honeymooned in Venice. 他們在威尼斯度了蜜月。"]}]}]},"homeland":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"祖國，家鄉；（某一特殊群體居住的）大片定居地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>homeland</b> is your native country. 祖國","examples":["Many are planning to return to their homeland. 很多人正計劃回到自己的祖國去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>homelands</b> were regions within South Africa in which black South Africans had a limited form of self-government. (過去南非種族隔離制度下的) 黑人家園","examples":[]}]}]},"herd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獸群，畜群；人群，民眾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"驅趕（獸群），放牧；使（人）成群移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>herd</b> is a large group of animals of one kind that live together. 畜群","examples":["Chobe is also renowned for its large herds of elephant and buffalo. 喬貝還以其大群的大象和水牛而聞名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a man or boy who tends livestock; herdsman 牧人; 放牧者","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(<b>in combination</b>) (用於組合詞)","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone has joined <b>the herd</b> or follows <b>the herd</b>, you are criticizing them because you think that they behave just like everyone else and do not think for themselves. (缺乏獨立思想的) 群眾","examples":["They are individuals; they will not follow the herd. 他們是獨立的個體；他們不會隨大流。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>herd</b> people somewhere, you make them move there in a group. 把…集中趕往","examples":["He began to herd the prisoners out. 他開始把囚犯集中起來趕出去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>herd</b> animals, you make them move along as a group. 驅趕 (畜群)","examples":["Stefano used a motorcycle to herd the sheep. 斯蒂芬諾騎一輛摩托車驅趕羊群。"]}]}]},"hostel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（免費或廉價的）旅社，招待所；青年旅舍；無家可歸者收容所，臨時收容所；<古>（提供食宿的）客棧"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"留宿於招待所，旅行時住在招待所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a building providing overnight accommodation, as for the homeless, etc (流浪者等的)過夜住宿處","examples":[]}]}]},"hose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軟管，水龍帶；<史>馬褲；連褲襪，長筒襪；（舊式的）男式緊身褲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用水管沖洗（或澆灌）；<美>欺騙，愚弄；痛打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hose</b> is a long, flexible pipe made of rubber or plastic. Water is directed through a hose in order to do things such as put out fires, clean cars, or water gardens. (橡膠或塑膠制的) 水管","examples":["You've left the garden hose on. 你沒有關花園的水管。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hose</b> is a pipe made of rubber or plastic, along which a liquid or gas flows, for example from one part of an engine to another. (用來輸送液體或氣體的) 軟管","examples":["Water in the engine compartment is sucked away by a hose. 發動機艙裡的水由一條軟管吸走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"stockings, socks, and tights collectively 襪子統稱","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hose</b> something, you wash or water it using a hose. 用水管沖洗; 用水管澆灌","examples":["We wash our cars and hose our gardens without even thinking of the water that uses. 我們沖洗汽車，澆灌花園，從沒考慮過所耗費的水。"]}]}]},"hesitation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"猶豫，不情願"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hesitation</b> is an unwillingness to do something, or a delay in doing it, because you are uncertain, worried, or embarrassed about it. 遲疑; 不願意","examples":["He promised there would be no more hesitations in pursuing reforms. 他保證在實行改革時不會再有遲疑。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have no hesitation</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you are emphasizing that you will do it immediately or willingly because you are certain that it is the right thing to do. 毫不猶豫","examples":["The board said it had no hesitation in unanimously rejecting the offer. 董事會說它毫不猶豫地一致否決了那項提議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone does something <b>without hesitation</b>, you are emphasizing that they do it immediately and willingly. 毫不猶豫地","examples":["The great majority of players would, of course, sign the contract without hesitation. 絕大多數運動員當然會毫不猶豫地籤這份合同。"]}]}]},"horizon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地平線；眼界；地平圈；地層；層位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>horizon</b> is the line in the far distance where the sky seems to meet the land or the sea. 地平線","examples":["In the distance, the dot of a boat appeared on the horizon. 遠處小黑點般的一條小船出現在地平線上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>horizons</b> are the limits of what you want to do or of what you are interested or involved in. 眼界; 閱歷","examples":["As your horizons expand, these new ideas can give a whole new meaning to life. 隨著你的眼界不斷開闊，這些新觀念將給你的生活賦予嶄新的意義。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>on the horizon</b>, it is almost certainly going to happen or be done quite soon. 即將來臨的","examples":["With breast cancer, as with many common diseases, there is no obvious breakthrough on the horizon. 就乳腺癌來說，如同許多常見病一樣，目前還看不到明顯的突破。"]}]}]},"housewife":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家庭主婦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>housewife</b> is a married woman who does not have a paid job, but instead takes care of her home and children. 家庭主婦","examples":["Married at nineteen, she was a traditional housewife and mother of four children. 她19歲就結婚了，是個傳統的家庭主婦和4個孩子的母親。"]}]}]},"household":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家庭，一家人；家務；王室（the Household）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"家用的，家務的；全家人的；家喻戶曉的；皇家的（Household）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>household</b> is all the people in a family or group who live together in a house. 家庭; 同住一所房子的人","examples":["...growing up in a male-only household. …在全體成員均為男性的家庭里長大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>household</b> is your home and everything that is connected with taking care of it. 家務","examples":["...household chores. …家務活。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is a <b>household</b> name or word is very well known. 家喻戶曉的","examples":["Today, fashion designers are household names. 如今，服裝設計師們家喻戶曉。"]}]}]},"housework":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家務勞動，家務事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Housework</b> is the work such as cleaning, washing, and ironing that you do in your home. 家務","examples":["Men are doing more housework nowadays. 現今男人正在承擔越來越多的家務。"]}]}]},"hydrogen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氫，氫氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hydrogen</b> is a colourless gas that is the lightest and commonest element in the universe. 氫","examples":[]}]}]},"hook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鉤，掛鉤；勾拳；曲線球；吸引人的東西；使（投手）下場；（尤指用於收割、剪羊毛）弧形切割工具；彎曲的筆畫；弧形岬（或沙嘴）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鉤住，掛住；（用手臂等身體部位）箍住；釣魚；打曲線球；彎成鉤狀；吸引；<非正式>偷竊；<非正式>賣淫；把……連線到（某裝置）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hook</b> is a bent piece of metal or plastic that is used for catching or holding things, or for hanging things up. 鉤子","examples":["One of his jackets hung from a hook. 他的一件夾克衫掛在掛鉤上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hook</b> is a short sharp blow with your fist that you make with your elbow bent, usually in a boxing match. (拳擊中的) 鉤拳","examples":["Lewis desperately needs to keep clear of Ruddock's big left hook. 劉易斯務必要拼命躲開拉多克強有力的左鉤拳。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hook</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you attach it there using a hook. If something <b>hooks</b> somewhere, it can be hooked there. 掛; 鉤","examples":["Paul hooked his tractor to the car and pulled it to safety. 保羅把他的拖拉機掛在那輛小汽車上，然後把它拖到安全的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hook</b> your arm, leg, or foot round an object, you place it like a hook round the object in order to move it or hold it. 使 (臂、腿、腳等) 成鉤狀","examples":["She latched on to his arm, hooking her other arm around a tree. 她一隻手抓住他的胳膊，另一隻胳膊抱住一棵樹。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hook</b> a fish, you catch it with a hook on the end of a line. 用魚鉤釣住","examples":["At the first cast I hooked a huge fish, probably a tench. 第一次拋竿我就釣到了一條大魚，可能是條丁鯛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>are hooked into</b> something, or <b>hook into</b> something, you get involved with it. 捲入; 涉足","examples":["I'm guessing again now because I'm not hooked into the political circles. 現在我又在猜測了，因為我沒有涉足政界。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone gets <b>off the hook</b> or is let <b>off the hook</b>, they manage to get out of the awkward or unpleasant situation that they are in. 脫身","examples":["Officials accused of bribery and corruption get off the hook with monotonous regularity. 被指控受賄和貪汙的官員無一例外總能脫身。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you take a phone <b>off the hook</b>, you take the receiver off the part that it normally rests on, so that the phone will not ring. (電話聽筒) 未掛上","examples":["I'd taken my phone off the hook in order to get some sleep. 我把電話聽筒拿了下來，以便可以睡會兒覺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your phone <b>is ringing off the hook</b>, so many people are trying to telephone you that it is ringing constantly. (電話) 響個不停","examples":["Since war broke out, the phones at donation centres have been ringing off the hook. 自從戰爭爆發以來，捐款中心的電話一直響個不停。"]}]}]},"hurricane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"颶風；爆發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hurricane</b> is an extremely violent storm that begins over ocean water. 颶風","examples":[]}]}]},"humidity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潮溼，溼氣；溼度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say there is <b>humidity</b> when the air feels very heavy and damp. 潮溼","examples":["The heat and humidity were insufferable. 炎熱與潮溼令人難以忍受。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Humidity</b> is the amount of water in the air. 溼度","examples":["The humidity is relatively low. 溼度相對較低。"]}]}]},"iceberg":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰山；微露端倪的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>iceberg</b> is a large tall mass of ice floating in the sea. 冰山","examples":[]}]}]},"humanity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人類（總稱）；人性，人的屬性；人道，仁慈；（歷史、哲學、文學等）人文學科"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"All the people in the world can be referred to as <b>humanity</b>. 人類","examples":["They face charges of committing crimes against humanity. 他們面臨犯有反人類罪的指控。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>humanity</b> is their state of being a human being, rather than an animal or an object. 人性","examples":["He was under discussion and it made him feel deprived of his humanity. 他受到議論，這使他覺得自己被剝奪了人格。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Humanity</b> is the quality of being kind, thoughtful, and sympathetic toward others. 仁慈; 博愛","examples":["Her speech showed great maturity and humanity. 她的演講表現出高度的成熟和博愛。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>humanities</b> are the subjects such as history, philosophy, and literature which are concerned with human ideas and behaviour. (歷史、哲學、文學等) 人文學科","examples":["The number of students majoring in the humanities has declined by about half. 主修人文學科的學生數量已經下降了近一半。"]}]}]},"idiom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"習語，成語；方言，土話；（個人、藝術形式等的）風格，特色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>idiom</b> is a group of words that have a different meaning when used together from the one they would have if you took the meaning of each word separately. 習語","examples":["...familiar idioms and metaphors, such as \"turning over a new leaf.\" …如“翻開新的一頁”這樣熟悉的習語和比喻。"]}]}]},"identification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"辨認，識別；確認，確定；身份證明；認同，強烈的同情感；密切關聯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>identification</b> of something is the recognition that it exists, is important, or is true. 確認","examples":["Early identification of a disease can prevent death and illness. 疾病的早期確認可避免死亡和病痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>identification</b> of a particular person or thing is the ability to name them because you know them or recognize them. 驗明","examples":["Officials are awaiting positive identification before charging the men with war crimes. 官員們正在等待這些人的身份得以驗明，然後再以戰爭罪起訴他們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone asks you for some <b>identification</b>, they want to see something such as a driving licence, that proves who you are. 身份證明","examples":["He did not have any identification when he arrived at the hospital. 他到醫院的時候沒有任何身份證明。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>identification</b> <b>of</b> one person or thing <b>with</b> another is the close association of one with the other. 密切關聯","examples":["...the identification of Spain with Catholicism. …西班牙與天主教的密切聯絡。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Identification with</b> someone or something is the feeling of sympathy and support for them. 同情; 支援","examples":["Marilyn had an intense identification with animals. 瑪麗蓮對動物有深切的同情。"]}]}]},"idol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偶像，受到熱愛和崇拜的人（或物）；聖像，神像；<美>幻象；<美>謬論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone such as a film, pop, or sports star as an <b>idol</b>, you mean that they are greatly admired or loved by their fans. 偶像","examples":["A great cheer went up from the crowd as they caught sight of their idol. 一看見他們的偶像，人群爆發出一陣熱烈的歡呼聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>idol</b> is a statue or other object that is worshipped by people who believe that it is a god. 神像","examples":[]}]}]},"illustration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"插圖，圖解；說明，例釋；例項，示例"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>illustration</b> is an example or a story that is used to make a point clear. 例項","examples":["An illustration of China's dynamism is that a new company is formed in Shanghai every 11 seconds. 說明中國活力的一個例項便是在上海每11秒鐘就有一家新公司成立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>illustration</b> in a book is a picture, design, or diagram. (書中的) 插圖","examples":["She looked like a princess in a nineteenth-century illustration. 她看上去像19世紀插圖裡的公主。"]}]}]},"immigrant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（外來）移民，僑民"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"移民的，遷入的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>immigrant</b> is a person who has come to live in a country from some other country. Compare . (外來) 移民","examples":["...illegal immigrants. …非法移民。"]}]}]},"immigration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移民（入境）；移民人數；移民局入境檢查，移民局入境檢查處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Immigration</b> is the coming of people into a country in order to live and work there. 移居","examples":["The government has decided to tighten its immigration policy. 政府已決定收緊其移民政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Immigration</b> or <b>immigration control</b> is the place at a port, airport, or international border where officials check the passports of people who wish to come into the country. 移民局的檢查","examples":["First, you have to go through immigration and customs. 首先你必須透過移民局和海關的檢查。"]}]}]},"imitation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模仿，仿效；滑稽模仿；仿製品，贗品；樂句重複"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人造的，仿製的，偽造的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>imitation</b> of something is a copy of it. 仿造品","examples":["...the most accurate imitation of Chinese architecture in Europe. …歐洲最逼真的仿中國建築。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Imitation</b> means copying someone else's actions. 動作模仿","examples":["They discussed important issues in imitation of their elders. 他們模仿長輩的口氣討論重大問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone does an <b>imitation</b> <b>of</b> another person, they copy the way they speak or behave, sometimes in order to be funny. (有時是為逗樂而) 學樣","examples":["One boy did an imitation of a soldier with a loudspeaker. 一個男孩拿著揚聲器學著士兵的樣子。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Imitation</b> things are not genuine but are made to look as if they are. 人造的; 仿造的","examples":["...a complete set of Dickens bound in imitation leather. …用人造革裝幀的一整套《狄更斯全集》。"]}]}]},"indication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指示，標示；象徵，暗示，跡象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>indication</b> is a sign that suggests, for example, what people are thinking or feeling. 象徵; 跡象","examples":["He gave no indication that he was ready to compromise. 他沒有流露出打算妥協的跡象。"]}]}]},"impact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"撞擊，衝擊力；巨大影響，強大作用"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"衝擊，撞擊；擠入，壓緊；（對……）產生影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>impact</b> that something has <b>on</b> a situation, process, or person is a sudden and powerful effect that it has on them. 影響","examples":["They say they expect the meeting to have a marked impact on the future of the country. 他們說期望這次會議對國家的未來產生顯著的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>impact</b> is the action of one object hitting another, or the force with which one object hits another. 撞擊; 撞擊力","examples":["The plane is destroyed, a complete wreck: the pilot must have died on impact. 飛機被毀，完全成了一堆殘骸：飛行員一定在撞擊中喪生了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>impact</b> a situation, process, or person means to affect them. 對…造成影響; 產生影響","examples":["Such schemes mean little unless they impact people. 除非能對人們造成影響，否則這樣的計劃意義不大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one object <b>impacts</b> <b>on</b> another, it hits it with great force. 撞擊","examples":["...the sharp tinkle of metal impacting on stone. …金屬撞擊石頭的刺耳叮噹聲。"]}]}]},"incident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"事件，事故；（兩國間的）衝突，嚴重摩擦；<法律>（職務、財產等所有物的）附屬特權"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"由……產生的；<法律>附屬的；入射的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>incident</b> is something that happens, often something that is unpleasant. 事件; 事故","examples":["These incidents were the latest in a series of disputes between the two nations. 這些事件是兩國一系列爭端中最近的幾起。"]}]}]},"infection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳染病；感染；玷汙，汙染"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>infection</b> is a disease caused by germs or bacteria. 傳染病","examples":["Ear infections are common in preschool children. 耳朵感染在學前兒童中很常見。"]}]}]},"inflation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"通貨膨脹，通脹率；充氣，膨脹，增大；（宇宙論某些理論）暴漲；誇張，自命不凡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inflation</b> is a general increase in the prices of goods and services in a country. 通貨膨脹","examples":["...rising unemployment and high inflation. …上漲的失業率和高通脹。"]}]}]},"impression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"印象，感想；影響，作用；印象畫；（對名人的）滑稽模仿；（通常有悖事實的）感覺，假象；壓印，印記；印次；（網路廣告）印象數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>impression</b> of a person or thing is what you think they are like, usually after having seen or heard them. Your <b>impression</b> of a situation is what you think is going on. 印象; 認識","examples":["What were your first impressions of college? 你對大學的第一印象是什麼？","My impression is that they are totally out of control. 我的認識是他們完全失去了控制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone gives you a particular <b>impression</b>, they cause you to believe that something is the case, often when it is not. (常指錯誤的) 印象","examples":["I don't want to give the impression that I'm running away from the charges. 我並不想給人留下一種我在逃避指控的印象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>impression</b> is an amusing imitation of someone's behaviour or way of talking, usually someone well-known. 滑稽模仿","examples":["I did an impression of daddy saying \"do as I say, not as I do.\" 我滑稽地模範爸爸說話，“照我說的做，別照我做的做。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>impression</b> of an object is a mark or outline that it has left after being pressed hard onto a surface. 壓印","examples":["...the world's oldest fossil impressions of plant life. …世界上最古老的植物化石印痕。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>makes an impression</b>, they have a strong effect on people or a situation. 造成強烈影響","examples":["The type of aid coming in makes no immediate impression on the horrific death rates. 這種即將到來的救助不會對恐怖的死亡率造成立杆見影的強烈影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>under the impression</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you believe that it is the case, usually when it is not actually the case. (通常是錯誤地) 認為","examples":["He had apparently been under the impression that a military coup was in progress. 他顯然一直認為一場軍事政變正在進行。"]}]}]},"infant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嬰兒，幼兒；（英國學校裡四至七歲的）學童；<法律>未成年人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"供嬰幼兒用的；初期的，初創期的；四歲至七歲幼兒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>infant</b> is a baby or very young child. 嬰兒; 幼兒","examples":["...holding the infant in his arms. …把嬰兒抱在他手裡。","They are saying that he is tiring of playing daddy to their infant son. 他們說他厭倦於在他們的幼兒面前裝扮爸爸的角色。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Infant</b> means designed especially for very young children. 供幼兒用的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>infant</b> organization or system is new and has not developed very much. 初期的","examples":["The infant company was based in Nebraska. 這家初創的公司總部設在內布拉斯加州。"]}]}]},"ingredient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（食品的）成分，原料；要素，因素"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"構成組成部分的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ingredients</b> are the things that are used to make something, especially all the different foods you use when you are cooking a particular dish. (尤指烹呼叫的) 原料","examples":["Mix in the remaining ingredients. 摻入剩下的原料。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>ingredient</b> of a situation is one of the essential parts of it. 要素","examples":["The meeting had all the ingredients of high political drama. 這次會議擁有了極富戲劇性的政治緊張場面的全部要素。"]}]}]},"information":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訊息，資料，情報；（計算機程式儲存和使用的）資料，資訊；問訊處，資訊臺；（向治安法院提起的）控告，起訴；知識"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Information</b> about someone or something consists of facts about them. 訊息; 資料","examples":["Pat refused to give her any information about Sarah. 帕特拒絕向她提供任何有關薩拉的訊息。","Each centre would provide information on technology and training. 每個中心都將提供有關技術與培訓的資料。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Information</b> consists of the facts and figures that are stored and used by a computer program. (電腦中儲存和使用的) 資料","examples":["Pictures are scanned into a form of digital information that computers can recognize. 圖片被掃描成一種計算機能識別的數字化資料。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Information</b> is a service that you can telephone to find out someone's telephone number. 問訊處","examples":["He called information, and they gave him the number. 他打電話給資訊臺，他們便給了他電話號碼。"]}]}]},"innocence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天真，單純；清白，無罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Innocence</b> is the quality of having no experience or knowledge of the more complex or unpleasant aspects of life. 天真","examples":["...the sweet innocence of youth. …青年時代的天真可愛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone proves their <b>innocence</b>, they prove that they are not guilty of a crime. 清白","examples":["He claims he has evidence which could prove his innocence. 他聲稱有證據能證明自己的清白。"]}]}]},"initial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"開始的，最初的；（字母）位於詞首的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（姓名的）首字母"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用姓名的首字母作標記（或簽名）於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>initial</b> to describe something that happens at the beginning of a process. 最初的","examples":["The initial reaction has been excellent. 最初的反應極好。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Initials</b> are the capital letters that begin each word of a name. For example, if your full name is Michael Dennis Stocks, your initials are M.D.S. (姓名的) 大寫首字母","examples":["...a silver Porsche with her initials JB on the side. …一輛銀色保時捷汽車，側面有她的姓名首字母JB。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>initials</b> an official document, they write their initials on it, to show that they have seen it or that they accept or agree with it. 籤姓名的首字母於","examples":["Would you mind initialling this voucher? 請您在這張單子上籤上姓名的首字母，好嗎？"]}]}]},"inspection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"視察；檢查，審視"}],"sections":[]},"input":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"投入，輸進；輸入的資訊；（為幫助某人做出決定而提供的）建議，意見；訊息輸入端；（輸入機器供其使用的）電力；輸入框"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輸入（資訊）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Input</b> consists of information or resources that a group or project receives. 資訊; 資源","examples":["It's up to the teacher to provide a variety of types of input in the classroom. 教師負責在課堂上提供各種各樣的資訊資源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Input</b> is information that is put into a computer. (計算機的) 輸入資訊","examples":["The x-ray detectors feed the input into computer programs. X射線探測器把輸入資訊傳入計算機程式。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>input</b> information into a computer, you feed it in, for example, by typing it on a keyboard. 輸入 (資訊)","examples":["The computer acts as a word processor where the text of a speech can be input at any time. 計算機起著文書處理器的作用，一篇講話的文字可隨時輸入。"]}]}]},"insert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"插入，嵌入；（在文章中）新增，加插；使參與（活動）；（肌肉或其他器官）附著於（尤指移動部分）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"插入物；（尤指）插頁，附加頁；（電影等的）插入鏡頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>insert</b> an object <b>into</b> something, you put the object inside it. 插入; 嵌入","examples":["He took a small key from his pocket and slowly inserted it into the lock. 他從衣袋裡掏出一把小鑰匙，然後緩緩地將其插入鎖孔裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>insert</b> a comment into a piece of writing or a speech, you add it. (在檔案或講話中) 插入; 新增","examples":["They joined with the monarchists to insert a clause calling for a popular vote on the issue. 他們與君主制主義者一起新增了一個條款，要求對該問題進行全民投票表決。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"插入; 嵌入","examples":["...the first experiment involving the insertion of a new gene into a human being. …首次把新基因嵌入人體的實驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"插入; 新增","examples":["...an item for insertion in the programme. …插入節目中的一則訊息。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>insert</b> is something that is inserted somewhere, especially an advertisement on a piece of paper that is placed between the pages of a book or magazine. 插入物; (尤指書刊中的) 活頁廣告","examples":["Sunday is the preferred day for advertising inserts in newspapers. 星期天是新增廣告插頁的最佳日子。"]}]}]},"instinct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"本能，天性；直覺；天分，天賦"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"充滿（某種品質，尤指好品質）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Instinct</b> is the natural tendency that a person or animal has to behave or react in a particular way. 本能","examples":["I didn't have as strong a maternal instinct as some other mothers. 我不像其他一些母親那樣有那麼強烈的母性本能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have an <b>instinct</b> <b>for</b> something, you are naturally good at it or able to do it. 天分","examples":["He seems to have an instinct for smart advertising and marketing. 他好像在廣告和營銷方面有天分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If it is your <b>instinct</b> <b>to</b> do something, you feel that it is right to do it. 本能的反應","examples":["I should've gone with my first instinct, which was not to do the interview. 我應該憑我的本能反應行事，那就是，不去面試。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Instinct</b> is a feeling, rather than an opinion or idea based on facts, that something is the case. 直覺","examples":["There is scientific evidence to support our instinct that being surrounded by plants is good for health. 有科學證據表明我們的直覺是正確的，即被植物環繞著有益健康。"]}]}]},"instructor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教練，導師；<美>大學講師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>instructor</b> is someone who teaches a skill such as driving or skiing. An <b>instructor</b> can also be used to refer to a schoolteacher or to a university teacher of low rank. 教練; 教師","examples":["...a fitness instructor. …一位健身教練。"]}]}]},"inspiration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靈感；啟發靈感的人（或事物）；鼓舞人心的人（或事物）；（突然想到的）好主意，妙計；吸氣，吸入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inspiration</b> is a feeling of enthusiasm you get from someone or something, that gives you new and creative ideas. 靈感","examples":["My inspiration comes from poets like Baudelaire and Jacques Prévert. 我的靈感來自像波德萊爾和雅克·普萊維爾這樣的詩人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something good as <b>an</b> <b>inspiration</b>, you mean that they make you or other people want to do or achieve something. 鼓舞人心的人 (或事物)","examples":["Powell's unusual journey to high office is an inspiration to millions. 鮑威爾升任高官的不尋常歷程對許多人來說是一種激勵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>the</b> <b>inspiration</b> <b>for</b> a particular book, work of art, or action, they are the source of the ideas in it or act as a model for it. 靈感來源; 原始動力","examples":["India's myths and songs are the inspiration for her books. 印度的神話與歌曲是她著書的靈感源泉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you suddenly have an <b>inspiration</b>, you suddenly think of an idea of what to do or say. (突然想到的) 妙計","examples":["She had an inspiration, \"Could we take Janice?\" 她靈機一動，“我們可以帶珍妮斯嗎？”"]}]}]},"insult":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"侮辱，冒犯；損害，危害"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"侮辱，冒犯；（醫）（對組織、器官的）損傷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>insults</b> you, they say or do something that is rude or offensive. 辱罵; 侮辱; 冒犯","examples":["I did not mean to insult you. 我並非故意要冒犯你。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被侮辱的","examples":["I mean, I was a bit insulted that they thought I needed bribing to shut up. 我的意思是，我感到有些受侮辱的是他們認為我收受賄賂才肯閉嘴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>insult</b> is a rude remark, or something a person says or does which insults you. 侮辱; 辱罵; 冒犯","examples":["Their behaviour was an insult to the people they represent. 他們的行為是對他們所代表的人們的一種侮辱。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>to add insult to injury</b> when mentioning an action or fact that makes an unfair or unacceptable situation even worse. 更糟糕的是","examples":["It is the victim who is often put on trial and, to add insult to injury, she is presumed guilty until proven innocent of provoking the rape. 受到審問的往往是受害者，更糟糕的是，她被假定為有罪，直到證明強姦並非由她挑逗而引起。"]}]}]},"insurance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保險；保險費；保險業；保險賠償金，保險金；保險單；預防措施，安全保障"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Insurance</b> is an arrangement in which you pay money to a company, and they pay you if something unpleasant happens to you, for example, if your property is stolen or damaged, or if you get a serious illness. 保險","examples":["The house was a total loss and the insurance company promptly paid us the policy limit. 房屋被定為全損，保險公司按保險限額迅速賠付了我們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something as <b>insurance</b> <b>against</b> something unpleasant happening, you do it to protect yourself in case the unpleasant thing happens. 預防措施","examples":["Attentive proofreading is the only insurance against the kind of omissions described in this section. 仔細校對是避免本節提到的那種遺漏問題的惟一預防措施。"]}]}]},"intellectual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"智力的，理智的；才智超群的；需智力的；思想的，思維的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"知識分子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intellectual</b> means involving a person's ability to think and to understand ideas and information. 智力的","examples":["High levels of lead could damage the intellectual development of children. 高含鉛量會損害兒童的智力發育。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Intellectual</b> is also an adjective. 有高智力的","examples":["They were very intellectual and witty. 他們非常聰明、機智。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"智力地","examples":["...intellectually satisfying work. …在智力上令人滿意的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intellectual</b> is someone who spends a lot of time studying and thinking about complicated ideas. 知識分子","examples":["Teachers, artists and other intellectuals urged political parties to launch a united movement against the government. 教師們、藝術家們和其他知識分子們敦促各政黨發動一場反政府的聯合運動。"]}]}]},"interaction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"互動，交流；相互影響，相互作用"}],"sections":[]},"intensity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"強烈，劇烈；（光、聲音等的）強度"}],"sections":[]},"intention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"意圖，目的，打算；癒合；意念"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intention</b> is an idea or plan of what you are going to do. 意圖","examples":["The company has every intention of keeping the share price high. 該公司有將自己的股票保持在高價的意圖。","It is my intention to remain in my position until a successor is elected. 我的打算是我繼續留任直到選出接班人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have no intention of</b> doing something, you are emphasizing that you are not going to do it. If you say that you <b>have every intention of</b> doing something, you are emphasizing that you intend to do it. 不打算/打算","examples":["I have no intention of allowing you to continue living here alone. 我不打算讓你繼續獨自生活在這裡。"]}]}]},"intelligence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"智力，才智；智慧；情報，諜報；情報機構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intelligence</b> is the quality of being intelligent or clever. 聰明","examples":["She's a woman of exceptional intelligence. 她是個格外聰明的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Intelligence</b> is the ability to think, reason, and understand instead of doing things automatically or by instinct. 智慧","examples":["Nerve cells, after all, do not have intelligence of their own. 神經元本身畢竟不具備智慧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Intelligence</b> is information that is gathered by the government or the army about their country's enemies and their activities. 情報","examples":["Why was military intelligence so lacking? 為什麼軍事情報如此缺乏？"]}]}]},"internet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網際網路，因特網（=the Internet）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The Internet</b> is the network that allows computer users to connect with computers all over the world, and that carries e-mail. 國際網際網路","examples":[]}]}]},"interruption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"打斷，插嘴；暫停；阻斷物，中斷期"}],"sections":[]},"intermediate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"居中的，中間的；中等程度的，中級的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"中級水平者，中級學生；中間事物；（化合物）中間體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"充當調解人，斡旋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intermediate</b> stage, level, or position is one that occurs between two other stages, levels, or positions. 中間的","examples":["Do you make any intermediate stops between your home and work? 你在住所和工作地點之間停留嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Intermediate</b> learners of something have some knowledge or skill but are not yet advanced. 中級的","examples":["Students are categorized as novice, intermediate, or advanced. 學生分為新生、中級生或高階生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intermediate</b> is an intermediate learner. 中級生","examples":["The ski school coaches beginners, intermediates, and advanced skiers. 滑雪學校訓練初級、中級和高階水平的滑雪者。"]}]}]},"intonation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聲調，語調；吟詠，吟誦；（素歌的）起始短句；（演奏或唱歌中的）音準"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>intonation</b> is the way that your voice rises and falls as you speak. 語調; 聲調","examples":["His voice had a very slight German intonation. 他的嗓音中有一點德語語調。"]}]}]},"invasion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"侵略，入侵；湧入，大批進入；侵犯，干預；侵襲，擴散"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>invasion</b> of a country, a foreign army enters it by force. 入侵","examples":["...seven years after the Roman invasion of Britain. …羅馬人入侵大不列顛島之後的7年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to the arrival of a large number of people or things as an <b>invasion</b>, you are emphasizing that they are unpleasant or difficult to deal with. 大群湧入","examples":["...this year's annual invasion of flies, wasps and ants. …今年蒼蠅、黃蜂和螞蟻像往年一樣的大量湧入。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe an action as an <b>invasion</b>, you disapprove of it because it affects someone or something in a way that is not wanted. 侵擾","examples":["Is reading a child's diary always a gross invasion of privacy? 看孩子的日記在任何情況下都是嚴重侵犯隱私的行為嗎？"]}]}]},"investigation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"調查，審查；科學研究，學術研究"}],"sections":[]},"invention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發明物；發明，創造；虛構，編造；發明才能，創造力；創意曲（短樂曲的題目）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>invention</b> is a machine, device, or system that has been invented by someone. 發明物","examples":["The spinning wheel was a Chinese invention. 紡車是中國人的一項發明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Invention</b> is the act of inventing something that has never been made or used before. 發明","examples":["...the invention of the telephone. …電話的發明。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to someone's account of something as an <b>invention</b>, you think that it is untrue and that they have made it up. 虛構","examples":["The story was certainly a favourite one, but it was undoubtedly pure invention. 這個故事的確是人們最喜歡的一個，但毫無疑問它純粹是虛構的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Invention</b> is the ability to invent things or to have clever and original ideas. 發明才能","examples":["Perhaps, with such powers of invention and mathematical ability, he will be offered a job in computers. 或許，擁有這樣的創造能力和數學才能，他會得到一份計算機方面的工作。"]}]}]},"involvement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"參與，介入；投入，沉迷；曖昧關係，戀愛關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>involvement</b> <b>in</b> or <b>with</b> something is the fact that you are taking part in it. 參與","examples":["She disliked his involvement with the group and disliked his friends. 她討厭他加入的那個團體，也不喜歡他的那些朋友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Involvement</b> is the enthusiasm that you feel when you care deeply about something. 感情投入","examples":["Ben has always felt a deep involvement with animals. 本一直對動物懷有很深的熱愛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>involvement</b> is a close relationship between two people, especially if they are not married to each other. 曖昧關係","examples":["They were very good friends but there was no romantic involvement. 他們是非常要好的朋友，但卻沒有發生過任何曖昧關係。"]}]}]},"intimate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"親密的；個人的，隱私的；溫馨的，幽靜舒適的；詳盡的，精通的；密切的，緊密的；有性關係的，曖昧的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"透露，暗示；宣佈，通告"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"密友，知己"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>intimate</b> friendship with someone, you know them very well and like them a lot. 親密的","examples":["I discussed with my intimate friends whether I would immediately have a baby. 我和我的密友們商量我是不是該馬上要孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two people are in an <b>intimate</b> relationship, they are involved with each other in a loving or sexual way. 有性關係的; 有戀愛關係的","examples":["...their intimate moments with their boyfriends. …她們和其男友們的私密時刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>intimate</b> conversation or detail, for example, is very personal and private. 個人的; 私下的","examples":["He wrote about the intimate details of his family life. 他寫下了家庭生活中一些私人的細節。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you use <b>intimate</b> to describe an occasion or the atmosphere of a place, you like it because it is quiet and pleasant, and seems suitable for close conversations between friends. 寧靜怡人的","examples":["...an intimate candlelit dinner for two. …寧靜怡人的一次二人燭光晚餐。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>intimate</b> connection between ideas or organizations, for example, is a very strong link between them. 密切的","examples":["...an intimate connection between madness and wisdom. …瘋狂和睿智之間的一種密切聯絡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An <b>intimate</b> knowledge of something is a deep and detailed knowledge of it. 深刻的; 精通的","examples":["He surprised me with his intimate knowledge of Kierkegaard and Schopenhauer. 他對克爾愷郭爾和叔本華的深刻了解令我感到驚奇。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"親密地","examples":["He did not feel he had got to know them intimately. 他覺得自己不必和他們親密熟悉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"在私密方面","examples":["You have to be willing to get to know yourself and your partner intimately. 你必須樂意在私密方面逐漸瞭解自己和伴侶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"個人地; 私下地","examples":["It was the first time they had attempted to talk intimately. 這是他們第一次試圖私下交談。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"密切地","examples":["Scientific research and conservation are intimately connected. 科學研究與環境保護聯絡密切。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"深刻地; 精通地","examples":["...a golden age of musicians whose work she knew intimately. …她熟知的那些音樂家們的一個黃金時代。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a close friend 密友","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>intimate</b> something, you say it in an indirect way. 暗示","examples":["He went on to intimate that he was indeed contemplating a shake-up of the company. 他接著暗示他確實在考慮對公司進行一次改組。"]}]}]},"investment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"投資；值得買的東西；（時間、精力的）投入；<舊>包圍，封鎖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Investment</b> is the activity of investing money. 投資","examples":["He said the government must introduce tax incentives to encourage investment. 他說，政府必須透過給予稅收利益來鼓勵投資。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>investment</b> is an amount of money that you invest, or the thing that you invest it in. 投資額","examples":["...an investment of twenty-eight million dollars. …2800萬美元的投資額。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something you buy as an <b>investment</b>, you mean that it will be useful, especially because it will help you to do a task more cheaply or efficiently. 有益的購買物","examples":["When selecting boots, fine, quality leather will be a wise investment. 在挑選靴子時，買精緻、質量上乘的皮靴會是明智的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Investment</b> of time or effort is the spending of time or effort on something in order to make it a success. 投入","examples":["I worry about this big investment of time not working. 我擔心這麼多的時間投入不起作用。"]}]}]},"jealousy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嫉妒，羨慕；吃醋，醋意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jealousy</b> is the feeling of anger or bitterness that someone has when they think that another person is trying to take a lover or friend, or a possession, away from them. 猜忌","examples":["At first his jealousy only showed in small ways – he didn't mind me talking to other guys. 開始時，他的猜忌只是小小地表現出來–他並不介意我和其他男孩子說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Jealousy</b> is the feeling of anger or bitterness that someone has when they wish that they could have the qualities or possessions that another person has. 嫉妒","examples":["Her beauty causes envy and jealousy. 她的美麗招人妒羨。"]}]}]},"itch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）發癢；渴望，熱望"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"癢；<非正式>渴望，熱望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a part of your body <b>itches</b>, you have an unpleasant feeling on your skin that makes you want to scratch. 發癢","examples":["When someone has hay fever, the eyes and nose will stream and itch. 當一個人染上花粉熱時，會流眼淚、流鼻涕，還會感到眼睛和鼻子發癢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Itch</b> is also a noun. 癢","examples":["Scratch my back – I've got an itch. 給我撓撓背–我癢癢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"癢","examples":["It may be that the itching is caused by contact with irritant material. 那兒的癢也許是由於接觸刺激物而引起的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Itch</b> is also a noun. 渴望","examples":["...cable TV viewers with an insatiable itch to switch from channel to channel. …難以滿足的、渴望不停變換頻道的有線電視觀眾。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are itching</b> to do something, you are very eager or impatient to do it. 渴望; 渴望","examples":["I was itching to get involved. 我渴望參與。"]}]}]},"knuckle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指關節；指節；（豬等動物的）腿部關節（作食物時常指豬肘、蹄髈）；（knuckle sandwich）<俚語>對準嘴的一拳"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用指關節敲打（或按壓、摩擦）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<非正式>（knuckle down）開始認真工作，埋頭苦幹；<非正式>（knuckle under）屈服，認輸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（near the knuckle）<口語>（笑話等）近乎猥褻、下流或粗鄙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>knuckles</b> are the rounded pieces of bone that form lumps on your hands where your fingers join your hands, and where your fingers bend. 指關節","examples":["Brenda's knuckles were white as she gripped the arms of the chair. 布倫達緊緊抓著椅子的兩個扶手時指關節白了。"]}]}]},"lab":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"實驗室 (=laboratory)；實驗課"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"工黨 (Lab)；工黨；拉布拉多尋回犬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lab</b> is the same as a . 實驗室","examples":[]}]}]},"labor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勞動，工作，勞作；勞工，勞動力；分娩，臨產；勞方，工會組織，勞工運動；（Labor）工黨，勞動黨；（Labor）人名：（德、塞、法）拉博爾，（英）拉博"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"勞動，努力，苦幹；分娩"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"詳細分析；使厭煩"}],"sections":[]},"isolation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"隔離，孤立；孤獨；絕緣；（尤指對混合物或微生物的）離析"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Isolation</b> is the state of feeling alone and without friends or help. 孤獨","examples":["Many deaf people have feelings of isolation and loneliness. 許多失聰的人有孤獨和寂寞的感覺。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is considered <b>in isolation</b> <b>from</b> other things that it is connected with, it is considered separately, and those other things are not considered. 孤立","examples":["Punishment cannot, therefore, be discussed in isolation from social and political theory. 因此，對懲罰進行討論不能脫離社會和政治理論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something <b>in isolation</b>, they do it without other people present or without their help. 單獨地","examples":["Malcolm, for instance, works in isolation but I have no doubts about his abilities. 例如，馬爾科姆雖然一個人獨立工作，但我絲毫不懷疑他的能力。"]}]}]},"laboratory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"實驗室，實驗大樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>laboratory</b> is a building or a room where scientific experiments, analyses, and research are carried out. 實驗室 (用於分析研究)","examples":["...a brain research laboratory at Columbia University. …哥倫比亞大學的一個大腦研究實驗室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>laboratory</b> in a school, college, or university is a room containing scientific equipment where students are taught science subjects such as chemistry. 實驗室 (用於教學)","examples":["...my old school chemistry laboratory. …我母校的化學實驗室。"]}]}]},"landslide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（地質）山崩，滑坡，山體滑坡；（選舉中的）壓倒性勝利，大勝利"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"發生山崩，發生滑坡；以壓倒優勢獲勝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>landslide</b> is a victory in an election in which a person or political party gets far more votes or seats than their opponents. (選舉中) 壓倒性優勢的勝利","examples":["He won last month's presidential election by a landslide. 他以絕對優勢贏得了上個月的總統選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>landslide</b> is a large amount of earth and rocks falling down a cliff or the side of a mountain. 山崩","examples":["The storm caused landslides and flooding in Savona. 暴風雨引發了薩沃納的山崩和水災。"]}]}]},"landmark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陸標，地標；里程碑，轉折點；<美>有歷史意義的建築（或遺址）；邊界，界碑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"賦予地標的地位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>landmark</b> is a building or feature which is easily noticed and can be used to judge your position or the position of other buildings or features. 地標","examples":["The Menger Hotel is a San Antonio landmark. 蒙爾飯店是聖安東尼奧的一個標誌性建築。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an important stage in the development of something as a <b>landmark</b>. 里程碑","examples":["...a landmark arms control treaty. …具有里程碑意義的武器控制條約。"]}]}]},"lag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"掉隊，落後於；給（管道等）加防凍保暖層；<非正式>使入獄，逮捕"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（兩件事的）時間間隔；<英，非正式>囚犯，慣犯；相位滯後；絕熱層，保溫套；桶板"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最後的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing or person <b>lags</b> <b>behind</b> another thing or person, their progress is slower than that of the other thing or person. 落後","examples":["Western banks still lag behind financial institutions in most other regions of the country. 西部地區的銀行仍然落後於這個國家其他大部分地區的金融機構。","The restructuring of the pattern of consumption also lagged behind. 消費結構的調整也落後了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to cover (a pipe, cylinder, etc) with lagging to prevent loss of heat 給(管子、柱子等)加防護套來保溫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A time <b>lag</b> or a <b>lag</b> of a particular length of time is a period of time between one event and another related event. 間隔","examples":["There's a time lag between infection with HIV and developing AIDS. 從感染艾滋病病毒到發展成為艾滋病病人有一定的時間間隔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a convict or ex-convict (esp in the phrase <b>old lag</b>) 犯人(尤其在短語 old lag 中); 前科犯人","examples":[]}]}]},"junior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"年齡較小的；地位（或級別）低的，資歷較淺的；（體育運動）青少年的；<英>（7-11歲的）學童的；<英>（學校或學校的一部分) 為11或13歲以下兒童設立的；<美>（四年制大學或中學）三年級學生的；小（用於與父親同名者的名字之後）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"較年幼者，年少者；地位（或級別）較低者，下屬；<美>（高中或大學的）三年級學生；青少年運動員；<美，非正式>男孩，（尤指）兒子；<英>（英國的）小學生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>junior</b> official or employee holds a low-ranking position in an organization or profession. 低階別的 (官員、職員)","examples":["A handful of junior officers were made to bear responsibility for the incident. 幾名下級軍官被迫對此事件負責。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Junior</b> is also a noun. 低階別者","examples":["He has said legal aid work is for juniors when they start out in the law. 他曾說過，法律援助工作適合初涉法律工作的低階別律師來做。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are someone's <b>junior</b>, you are younger than they are. 較年幼者","examples":["She now lives with actor Denis Lawson, 10 years her junior. 她現在和比她小10歲的演員丹尼斯·勞森同居。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the United States, a student in the third year of high school or college is called a <b>junior</b>. (美國中學、大學) 三年級學生","examples":["Their youngest daughter Amy's a junior at the University of Evansville in Indiana. 他們最小的女兒埃米是印第安納州埃文斯維爾大學的三年級學生。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Junior</b> is sometimes used after the name of the younger of two men in a family who have the same name, sometimes in order to prevent confusion. The abbreviation  is also used. 用於家族中同名兩男子中的較年幼者的姓名後","examples":["His son, Arthur Ochs Junior, is expected to succeed him as publisher. 他的兒子，小阿瑟·奧克斯，被期望來繼承他做出版商。"]}]}]},"landscape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（陸上，尤指鄉村的）風景，景色；形勢，情形；（陸上或鄉村）風景畫；橫向列印格式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……做景觀美化，美化……的環境；從事景觀美化工作"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"橫向列印的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>landscape</b> is everything you can see when you look across an area of land, including hills, rivers, buildings, trees, and plants. 風景","examples":["...Arizona's desert landscape. …亞利桑那州的沙漠風光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>landscape</b> is all the features that are important in a particular situation. 局面","examples":["June's events completely altered the political landscape. 6月的事件完全改變了政治局面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>landscape</b> is a painting which shows a scene in the countryside. 鄉村風景畫","examples":["Kenna's latest series of landscapes is on show at the Zelda Cheatle Gallery. 肯納的鄉村風景畫系列正在塞爾達·奇特爾畫廊展出。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"景觀美化","examples":["The landowner insisted on a high standard of landscaping. 土地所有人執意要求高標準的景觀美化。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a sheet of paper is in <b>landscape</b> format or mode, the longer edge of the paper is horizontal and the shorter edge is vertical. 橫排格式","examples":["Most powerpoint presentations are prepared for screens in landscape format. 大部分幻燈片演示在螢幕上都是橫排格式。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an area of land <b>is landscaped</b>, it is changed to make it more attractive, for example, by adding streams or ponds and planting trees and bushes. 對…做景觀美化","examples":["The gravel pits have been landscaped and planted to make them attractive to wildfowl. 這些亂石坑已經被美化，種了樹來吸引野生鳥類。","They had landscaped their property with trees, shrubs, and lawns. 他們種了樹、灌木和草坪來美化家園。"]}]}]},"lecturer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"講授者，講演者；（大學的）講師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lecturer</b> is a teacher at a university or college. 講師","examples":["...a lecturer in law. …法學講師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lecturer</b> is a person who gives lectures. 演講人","examples":[]}]}]},"learning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學習；知識，學問"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"學習，學會；得知，獲悉；背熟，熟記；認識到，（從……）吸取教訓 （learn 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Learning</b> is the process of gaining knowledge through studying. 學習","examples":["The brochure described the library as the focal point of learning on the campus. 這本小冊子把圖書館描述為校園學習的中心。"]}]}]},"lecture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"講座，講課，演講；訓斥，告誡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指在大學裡）開講座，講課；訓斥，告誡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lecture</b> is a talk someone gives in order to teach people about a particular subject, usually at a university or college. 講座","examples":["...a series of lectures by Professor Eric Robinson. …埃裡克·魯濱遜教授的系列講座。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lecture</b> is also a noun. 批評; 責備","examples":["Our captain gave us a stern lecture on safety. 我們的船長在安全問題上給了我們嚴厲的批評。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lecture</b> <b>on</b> a particular subject, you give a lecture or a series of lectures about it. 講授","examples":["She then invited him to Atlanta to lecture on the history of art. 她於是邀請他去亞特蘭大講授藝術史。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>lectures</b> you about something, they criticize you or tell you how they think you should behave. 批評; 責備","examples":["He used to lecture me about getting too much sun. 他過去經常批評我太陽曬得過多。","Chuck would lecture me, telling me to get a haircut. 查克會責備我，叫我去理髮。"]}]}]},"legend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳說，傳奇故事；傳奇人物；（標誌、徽記、硬幣等物品上的）刻印文字，銘文；（圖片或地圖的）文字說明，圖例"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"十分出名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>legend</b> is a very old and popular story that may be true. 傳說","examples":["...the legends of ancient Greece. …古希臘的傳說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>legend</b>, you mean that they are very famous and admired by a lot of people. 傳奇人物","examples":["...blues legends John Lee Hooker and B.B. King. …布魯斯音樂傳奇人物約翰·李·胡克和B·B·金。"]}]}]},"launch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發動，發起；上市，發行；使（船或艦）下水；發射（武器或宇宙飛船）；啟動（計算機程式）；投出，用力扔出；使投身於（事業等）；起飛，出海"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（航天器的）發射；（產品的）上市；（事件的）發起；汽艇，遊艇；（新產品，出版物）釋出會，推介會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>launch</b> a rocket, missile, or satellite means to send it into the air or into space. 發射","examples":["NASA plans to launch a satellite to study cosmic rays. 美國國家航空航天局計劃發射一顆衛星來研究宇宙射線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>launch</b> a ship or a boat means to put it into water, often for the first time after it has been built. 使 (新船等) 下水","examples":["There was no time to launch the lifeboats because the ferry capsized with such alarming speed. 因為渡船傾斜的速度如此之快，根本沒有時間把救生艇放下水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>launch</b> a large and important activity, for example, a military attack, means to start it. 發起","examples":["A group of 80 attackers launched an all-out assault just before dawn. 有80名攻擊者的一個小隊在黎明前發起了一次全面進攻。","The police have launched an investigation into the incident. 警察已經開始對此事件進行調查。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a company <b>launches</b> a new product, it makes it available to the public. 推出 (新產品)","examples":["...powerful allies to help the company launch a low-cost \"network computer.\" …幫助公司推出一種低價“網路電腦”的強大同盟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Launch</b> is also a noun. 發射","examples":["This morning's launch of the space shuttle Columbia has been delayed. 定於今天上午哥倫比亞號太空梭的發射已經被推遲了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Launch</b> is also a noun. 下水","examples":["The launch of a ship was a big occasion. 船下水曾是一件大事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Launch</b> is also a noun. 發起","examples":["...the launch of a campaign to restore law and order. …旨在恢復法律和秩序的運動的發起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Launch</b> is also a noun. 推出","examples":["The company's spending has also risen following the launch of a new Sunday magazine. 公司的花費也隨著一份新星期日雜誌的推出而增加。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a motor driven boat used chiefly as a transport boat 摩托艇","examples":[]}]}]},"license":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國英語）執照，許可證，特許證；特許（同 licence）；破格，自由（如 poetic license、artistic license）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"許可，特許，發許可證給"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>license</b> a person or activity means to give official permission for the person to do something or for the activity to take place. 准許","examples":["...a proposal that would require the state to license guns the way it does cars. …提案要求政府像發駕駛證一樣發放槍支許可證。"]}]}]},"liquor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烈性酒；酒精類飲料；（某種加工過程中所產生或使用的）液，汁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……浸於溶液中；<美，非正式>使喝醉；<非正式>灌酒；給（皮革）上油；在水中浸泡（麥芽等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Strong alcoholic drinks such as whisky, vodka, and gin can be referred to as <b>liquor</b>. 烈性酒","examples":["The room was filled with cases of liquor. 房間裡滿是一箱箱的烈性酒。"]}]}]},"limitation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"限制，制約；起限制作用的規則（或事實、條件）；侷限，缺陷；追訴時效"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>limitation</b> of something is the act or process of controlling or reducing it. 限制","examples":["All the talk had been about the limitation of nuclear weapons. 整個會談都是關於核武器的限制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>limitation</b> <b>on</b> something is a rule or decision which prevents that thing from growing or extending beyond certain limits. 限定","examples":["...a limitation on the tax deductions for people who make more than $100,000 a year. …對年收入高於10萬美元者在減稅上的限定。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>limitations</b> of someone or something, you mean that they can only do some things and not others, or cannot do something very well. 侷限","examples":["I realized how possible it was to overcome your limitations, to achieve well beyond what you believe yourself capable of. 我意識到如何有可能克服自身的侷限，取得自認為力不能及的成就。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>limitation</b> is a fact or situation that allows only some actions and makes others impossible. 限制因素","examples":["This drug has one important limitation. Its effects only last six hours. 這種藥物有一個很大的限制因素，其藥效只能持續6個小時。"]}]}]},"locker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鎖櫃，寄物櫃；<美>冷藏間；鎖具；（衣服、雜物、器械、軍火的）存放室，箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>locker</b> is a small metal or wooden cabinet with a lock, where you can put your personal possessions, for example in a school, place of work, or sports club. 鎖櫃","examples":[]}]}]},"literature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文學，文學作品；（某一學科的）文獻，著述；印刷品，宣傳品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Novels, plays, and poetry are referred to as <b>literature</b>, especially when they are considered to be good or important. 文學","examples":["...classic works of literature. …古典文學作品。","I have spent my life getting to know diverse literatures of different epochs. 我花費一生時間來逐漸瞭解不同時代形形色色的文學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>literature</b> on a particular subject of study is all the books and articles that have been published about it. 文獻","examples":["...the literature on immigration policy. …關於外來移民政策的文獻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Literature</b> is written information produced by people who want to sell you something or give you advice. 印刷品","examples":["I am sending you literature from two other companies that provide a similar service. 我在給你郵寄來自另外兩家提供類似服務的公司的宣傳單。"]}]}]},"loan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貸款，借款；借用，借出；<蘇格蘭>（尤指通向開闊地的）小徑；（未開墾的開闊的）擠奶牧場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"借出，借給"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>loan</b> is a sum of money that you borrow. 貸款","examples":["The country has no access to foreign loans or financial aid. 該國得不到外國貸款或財政援助。","The president wants to make it easier for small businesses to get bank loans. 總統想使小公司能更容易地獲得銀行貸款。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone gives you a <b>loan of</b> something, you borrow it from them. 借用","examples":["I am in need of a loan of a bike for a few weeks. 我需要借輛腳踏車來用幾周。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>loan</b> something to someone, you lend it to them. 借出","examples":["He had kindly offered to loan us all the plants required for the exhibit. 他友好地主動提出了借給我們展覽會所需的全部植物。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Loan out</b> means the same as . 借出","examples":["It is common practice for clubs to loan out players to sides in the lower divisions. 將球員借給下級球隊是俱樂部的慣例。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>on loan</b>, it has been borrowed. 借來的","examples":["...impressionist paintings on loan from the National Gallery. …從國家美術館借來的印象派畫作。"]}]}]},"lotion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潔膚液，護膚液，潤膚乳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lotion</b> is a liquid that you use to clean, improve, or protect your skin or hair. (塗在皮膚或頭髮以清潔或保護的) 塗劑","examples":["...suntan lotion. …防曬霜。"]}]}]},"location":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地點，位置；（電影的）外景拍攝地；定位；（計算機記憶體裡的）地址"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>location</b> is the place where something happens or is situated. 地點","examples":["The first thing he looked at was his office's location. 他首先看的是他辦公室的位置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>location</b> of someone or something is their exact position. 準確位置","examples":["She knew the exact location of The Eagle's headquarters. 她知道“飛鷹”總部的準確位置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>location</b> is a place away from a studio where a film or part of a film is made. 外景拍攝地","examples":["...an art film with dozens of exotic locations. …一部含有許多異國外景的藝術電影。"]}]}]},"loyalty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忠誠，忠貞；忠於……的強烈情感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Loyalty</b> is the quality of staying firm in your friendship or support for someone or something. 忠誠","examples":["I have sworn an oath of loyalty to the monarchy. 我已經發誓效忠君主制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Loyalties</b> are feelings of friendship, support, or duty toward someone or something. 效忠的義務","examples":["She had developed strong loyalties to the Manet family. 她深深感到對馬奈一家有效忠的義務。"]}]}]},"logic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邏輯，（做某事的）道理；推理方法，邏輯學；（事實或事件的）規律，相互聯絡；（計算機或電器的）邏輯操作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Logic</b> is a method of reasoning that involves a series of statements, each of which must be true if the statement before it is true. 邏輯 (學)","examples":["Apart from criminal investigation techniques, students learn forensic medicine, philosophy and logic. 除犯罪調查技術外，學生們還學習法醫學、哲學和邏輯學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>logic</b> of a conclusion or an argument is its quality of being correct and reasonable. (結論或觀點的) 邏輯","examples":["I don't follow the logic of your argument. 我不理解你觀點的邏輯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A particular kind of <b>logic</b> is the way of thinking and reasoning about things that is characteristic of a particular type of person or particular field of activity. (某種人或某行為領域的) 邏輯","examples":["The plan was based on sound commercial logic. 這個計劃建立在合理的商業邏輯之上。"]}]}]},"ma'am":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女士（madam 的縮約形式，對女性的禮貌稱呼）；夫人，太太；小姐；<英>對女王或王室女性的尊稱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say <b>ma'am</b> as a polite way of addressing a woman whose name they do not know, especially in the American South. 女士 (對不知其名的女子的禮貌稱呼)","examples":["Would you repeat that please, ma'am? 女士，請您重複一遍好嗎？"]}]}]},"makeup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組成，構造；化妝品；<美>補考；天性，性格；補給，補充"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Makeup</b> consists of things such as lipstick, eye shadow, and powder which some women put on their faces to make themselves look more attractive or which actors use to change or improve their appearance. 化妝品","examples":["Normally she wore little makeup, but this evening was clearly an exception. 通常她很少化妝，可今晚顯然是個例外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>makeup</b> is their nature and the various qualities in their character. 性格","examples":["There was some fatal flaw in his makeup, and as time went on he lapsed into long silences or became off-hand. 他性格中有某種致命的缺陷，隨著時間的推移，他要麼陷入長時間沉默要麼行為隨便。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>makeup</b> of something consists of its different parts and the way these parts are arranged. 構造; 組成","examples":["The ideological makeup of the unions is now radically different from what it had been. 這些協會的意識形態構成如今與過去大相徑庭。"]}]}]},"luxury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奢華，華貴；奢侈品；不常有的樂趣，難得的享受"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奢侈的，豪華的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Luxury</b> is very great comfort, especially among beautiful and expensive surroundings. 奢侈","examples":["By all accounts he leads a life of considerable luxury. 從方方面面來講，他都過著極為奢侈的生活。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>luxury</b> is something expensive which is not necessary but which gives you pleasure. 奢侈品","examples":["A week by the sea is a luxury they can no longer afford. 去海邊一週成了一種奢侈，他們再也負擔不起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>luxury</b> is a pleasure which you do not often have the opportunity to enjoy. 難得的享受","examples":["Hot baths are my favourite luxury. 熱水浴是我鍾愛而難得的享受。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>luxury</b> item is something expensive which is not necessary but which gives you pleasure. 奢侈的 (物品)","examples":["He could not afford luxury food on his pay. 憑他的薪水，他吃不起奢侈的食品。"]}]}]},"lead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引領，帶路；通向，通往；（與……）相連，相通；領導，指揮；導致，造成；促使，使得；過（某種生活）；領先，居於首位；開牌；對（證人）進行誘詢；用水砣測深"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"領先地位；超前量，領先的距離；範例，榜樣；線索；主角，扮演主角的演員；鉛；鉛筆芯；狗繩，牽狗帶；（報紙或電臺的）要聞，頭條；子彈；電線，導線；導語；（投球前跑壘員的）離壘；螺距，牙距；水渠，水道；行間距"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lead</b> a group of people, you walk or ride in front of them. 帶領","examples":["The president and vice president led the mourners. 總統和副總統帶領著送葬人群。","He walks with a stick but still leads his soldiers into battle. 儘管他拄著柺杖，但他仍帶領士兵上戰場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lead</b> someone to a particular place or thing, you take them there. 引領","examples":["He took Dickon by the hand to lead him into the house. 他拉著迪肯的手領他進了那幢房子。","She confessed to the killing and led police to his remains. 她承認殺了人，並且帶警察找到了他的遺骸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one company or country <b>leads</b> others in a particular activity such as scientific research or business, it is more successful or advanced than they are in that activity. (在某領域) 領先","examples":["In 1920, the United States led the world in iron and steel manufacturing. 美國的鋼鐵製造業在1920年領先於世界。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>lead</b> a group of people, an organization, or an activity, you are in control or in charge of the people or the activity. 領導","examples":["He led the country between 1949 and 1984. 他在1949到1984年間領導著這個國家。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>lead</b> when you are saying what kind of life someone has. For example, if you <b>lead</b> a busy life, your life is busy. 過…的生活","examples":["She led a normal, happy life with her sister and brother. 她和弟弟妹妹過著平常和幸福的生活。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>leads</b> you <b>to</b> do something, it influences or affects you in such a way that you do it. 促使","examples":["His abhorrence of racism led him to write \"The Algiers Motel Incident.\" 他對種族主義的痛恨促使他寫了《阿爾及爾汽車旅館事件》。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You can say that one point or topic in a discussion or piece of writing <b>leads</b> you <b>to</b> another in order to introduce a new point or topic that is linked with the previous one. 引導","examples":["Well, I think that leads me to the real point. 嗯，我想這把我引向要點。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a road, gate, or door <b>leads</b> somewhere, you can get there by following the road or going through the gate or door. 通往","examples":["...the door that led to the garden. …通往院子的門。","...a hallway leading to the living room. …通往客廳的過道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are leading</b> at a particular point in a race or competition, you are winning at that point. (在比賽中) 領先","examples":["He's leading in the presidential race. 他在總統競選中領先。","So far Fischer leads by five wins to two. 到目前為止，菲舍爾以５:２領先。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>leads</b> <b>to</b> a situation or event, usually an unpleasant one, it begins a process which causes that situation or event to happen. 導致 (通常為不愉快的情況)","examples":["Ethnic tensions among the republics could lead to civil war. 各共和國之間緊張的民族關係可能導致內戰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>the</b> <b>lead</b> or are <b>in the</b> <b>lead</b> in a race or competition, you are winning. 領先地位","examples":["Harvard took the lead and remained unperturbed by the repeated challenges. 哈佛取得了領先地位，經過再三挑戰後仍然鎮定自若。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you take <b>the</b> <b>lead</b>, you do something new or develop new ideas or methods that other people consider to be a good example or model to follow. 領先","examples":["The American and Japanese navies took the lead in the development of naval aviation. 美國和日本海軍在海軍航空的發展方面領先。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lead</b> is a piece of information or an idea which may help people to discover the facts in a situation where many facts are not known, for example, in the investigation of a crime or in a scientific experiment. 線索","examples":["The inquiry team is also following up possible leads after receiving 400 calls from the public. 調查組正在接到的400個公眾電話中追蹤可能的線索。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A dog's <b>lead</b> is a long, thin chain or piece of leather which you attach to the dog's collar so that you can control the dog. 牽狗的皮帶; 牽狗的鏈子","examples":["All dogs in public places should be on a lead. 所有的狗在公共場所必須拴上鍊子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>lead</b> in a piece of equipment is a piece of wire covered in plastic which supplies electricity to the equipment or carries it from one part of the equipment to another. 導線","examples":["...a lead that plugs into a socket on the camcorder. …一根插到行動式攝影機插孔上的導線。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>lead</b> in a play, film, or show is the most important part in it. The person who plays this part can also be called the <b>lead</b>. 主角; 扮演主角的演員","examples":["Nina Ananiashvili and Alexei Fadeyechev from the Bolshoi Ballet dance the leads. 來自莫斯科大劇院芭蕾舞團的妮娜·安娜尼雅什維莉和阿歷克謝·費德耶切夫擔任主角。","Neve Campbell is the lead, playing one of the dancers. 內芙·坎貝爾是主演，扮演其中一個舞蹈者。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Lead</b> is a soft, grey, heavy metal. 鉛","examples":["...drinking water supplied by old-fashioned lead pipes. …透過老式鉛管供應的飲用水。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"The <b>lead</b> in a pencil is the centre part of it which makes a mark on paper. 鉛筆芯","examples":["He grabbed a pencil, and the lead immediately broke. 他抓起一支鉛筆，鉛筆芯立刻就斷了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fill or treat with lead 填鉛的; 用鉛處理的","examples":[]}]}]},"madam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夫人，女士，太太（對不知名女子的禮貌稱呼）；鴇母，妓院女老闆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"稱呼名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say <b>Madam</b> as a very formal and polite way of addressing a woman whose name they do not know. For example, a shop assistant might address a woman customer as <b>Madam</b>. 女士 (對不知其名的女子的禮貌稱呼)","examples":["Try them on, madam. 試穿一下吧，女士。"]}]}]},"machinery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機器，機械（尤指大型機械）；體系，機制；運轉部份，裝置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>machinery</b> to refer to machines in general, or machines that are used in a factory or on a farm. 機器; 機械","examples":["...quality tools and machinery. …優質工具和機械。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>machinery</b> of a government or organization is the system and all the procedures that it uses to deal with things. (政府或組織的) 體制","examples":["The machinery of democracy could be created quickly. 民主體制很快就能建立起來。"]}]}]},"marathon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"馬拉松賽跑；馬拉松式的活動（或工作）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"馬拉松式的，漫長而累人的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"參加馬拉松賽跑（或馬拉松式的比賽、活動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>marathon</b> is a race in which people run a distance of 26 miles, which is about 42 km. 馬拉松賽跑","examples":["...running in his first marathon. …正在跑他的第一次馬拉松比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you use <b>marathon</b> to describe an event or task, you are emphasizing that it takes a long time and is very tiring. 漫長而累人的","examples":["People make marathon journeys to buy glass here. 人們經過漫長而艱辛的旅途到這兒來買玻璃。"]}]}]},"manual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"手工的，體力的；手動的，用手操作的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"使用手冊，說明書；手動換擋的車輛；風琴鍵盤；（牧師主持聖禮時用）禮儀書"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Manual</b> work is work in which you use your hands or your physical strength rather than your mind. 手工的; 靠勞力的","examples":["...skilled manual workers. …熟練的手工工人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Manual</b> is used to talk about movements which are made by someone's hands. 用手的","examples":["...toys designed to help develop manual dexterity. …旨在培養手的靈活性的玩具。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Manual</b> means operated by hand, rather than by electricity or a motor. 用手操作的","examples":["There is a manual pump to get rid of the water. 有一臺手動水泵用來排水。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"用手操作地","examples":["The device is manually operated, using a simple handle. 這個裝置利用一個簡單的手柄，可以用手操作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>manual</b> is a book which tells you how to do something or how a piece of machinery works. 使用手冊","examples":["...the instruction manual. …使用說明書。"]}]}]},"manufacturer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生產商，製造商"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>manufacturer</b> is a business or company which makes goods in large quantities to sell. 生產商","examples":["...the world's largest doll manufacturer. …世界上最大的玩偶生產商。"]}]}]},"manufacture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用機器大量）生產，製造；編造，捏造；生成，產生（一種物質）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大量製造，批次生產；工業品；製造業"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>manufacture</b> something means to make it in a factory, usually in large quantities. 生產","examples":["They manufacture the class of plastics known as thermoplastic materials. 他們生產被稱為熱塑材料的塑膠類製品。","The first three models are being manufactured at the factory in Dayton. 最初的3個型號正在代頓的工廠生產。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>manufactures</b> information, you are criticizing them because they invent information that is not true. 捏造","examples":["According to the prosecution, the officers manufactured an elaborate story. 根據起訴，軍官們精心編造了事情的經過。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Manufacture</b> is also a noun. 生產","examples":["...the manufacture of nuclear weapons. …核武器的生產。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"生產","examples":["...management headquarters for manufacturing in China. …設在中國的生產管理總部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In economics, <b>manufactures</b> are goods or products which have been made in a factory. 工業品","examples":["...a long-term rise in the share of manufactures in non-oil exports. …非石油出口產品中工業品份額的長期增長。"]}]}]},"maturity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（思想行為、作品等）成熟；發育成熟，長大成人；到期；（債券等）償還期；（保險單、證券等）有固定到期日的票據"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Maturity</b> is the state of being fully developed or adult. 發育成熟","examples":["Humans experience a delayed maturity; we arrive at all stages of life later than other mammals. 人類經歷著一個遲來的成熟；我們進入生命各個階段的時間比其他哺乳動物要晚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>maturity</b> is their quality of being fully developed in their personality and emotional behaviour. (性格、情感) 成熟","examples":["Her speech showed great maturity and humanity. 她的演講顯示出十足的成熟和博愛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When an investment such as an insurance policy or bond reaches <b>maturity</b>, it reaches the stage when the company pays you back the money you have saved, and the interest your money has earned. (保險單、債券等的) 到期","examples":["Customers are told what their policies will be worth on maturity, not what they are worth today. 客戶們被告知的是他們的保險單到期時的價值，不是現在的價值。"]}]}]},"margin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頁邊空白；差額，幅度；盈餘，利潤；餘地，備用的時間（或空間、金錢等）；邊緣，非主體部分；保證金，押金；<澳新>額外報酬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加上邊；預付定金，交押金；<古>頁邊做註釋或總結"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>margin</b> is the difference between two amounts, especially the difference in the number of votes or points between the winner and the loser in an election or other contest. 差數","examples":["They could end up with a 50-point winning margin. 他們最後可能會以50點的優勢獲勝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>margin</b> of a written or printed page is the empty space at the side of the page. 頁邊的空白","examples":["She added her comments in the margin. 她在頁邊空白處加上了她的評語。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>margin</b> for something in a situation, there is some freedom to choose what to do or decide how to do it. 餘地","examples":["The money is collected in a straightforward way with little margin for error. 這筆錢是直接募集上來的, 幾乎沒有出錯的餘地。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>margin</b> of a place or area is the extreme edge of it. 邊緣","examples":["...the low coastal plain along the western margin. …沿著西部邊緣地帶的低窪海岸平原。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To be <b>on the</b> <b>margins</b> of a society, group, or activity means to be among the least typical or least important parts of it. 非主體部分","examples":["Students have played an important role in the past, but for the moment, they're on the margins. 學生們過去發揮了重要的作用，但現在，他們不再重要了。"]}]}]},"mechanic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機械工，機修工；<舊>勞工，工匠；方法，手段"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"手工的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mechanic</b> is someone whose job is to repair and maintain machines and engines, especially car engines. 機修工","examples":["If you smell something unusual (gas fumes or burning, for instance), take the car to your mechanic. 如果你聞到了異味（例如汽油味或燃燒味），就把車帶給你的修理工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mechanics</b> <b>of</b> a process, system, or activity are the way in which it works or the way in which it is done. 運作方式","examples":["What are the mechanics of this new process? 這一新工序的運作方式是什麼？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Mechanics</b> is the part of physics that deals with the natural forces that act on moving or stationary objects. 力學","examples":["He has not studied mechanics or engineering. 他沒有學習過力學或者工程學。"]}]}]},"memorial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紀念的，追悼的；記憶的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"紀念碑，紀念館；紀念品，紀念物；紀念儀式；請願書；記錄，年代記"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>memorial</b> is a structure built in order to remind people of a famous person or event. 紀念碑","examples":["Building a memorial to Columbus has been his lifelong dream. 建一座哥倫布紀念碑一直是他一生的夢想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something will be a <b>memorial to</b> someone who has died, you mean that it will continue to exist and remind people of them. 紀念物","examples":["The museum will serve as a memorial to the millions who passed through Ellis Island. 這個博物館將成為曾經過埃利斯島的數百萬人的紀念館。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>memorial</b> event, object, or prize is in honour of someone who has died, so that they will be remembered. 紀念性的","examples":["A memorial service is being held for her at St. Paul's Church. 一場為她舉行的紀念儀式正在聖保羅教堂舉行。"]}]}]},"maximum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最大限度的；（數量）極大的，極多的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最大量，最大限度"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最多，充其量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>maximum</b> to describe an amount which is the largest that is possible, allowed, or required. 最大的","examples":["Under planning law the maximum height for a fence or hedge is 6 feet. 根據規劃法，柵欄或樹籬的最高高度為6英尺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>maximum</b> to indicate how great an amount is. 最大的","examples":["I need the maximum amount of information you can give me. 我需要你所能給我的最大的資訊量。","It was achieved with minimum fuss and maximum efficiency. 它以最少的慌亂和最高的效率被做到了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Maximum</b> is also a noun. 最大值","examples":["The law provides for a maximum of two years in prison. 法律規定監禁最長兩年。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is a particular amount <b>maximum</b>, you mean that this is the greatest amount it should be or could possibly be, although a smaller amount is acceptable or very possible. 最多","examples":["We need an extra 6 grams a day maximum. 我們一天最多還需要6克。"]}]}]},"messenger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"送信人，郵遞員，報信者；（體內傳遞資訊和刺激的）信使；<古>先驅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>（用信使）送（檔案，包裹）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>messenger</b> takes a message to someone, or takes messages regularly as their job. 信使","examples":["There will be a messenger at the airport to collect the photographs from our courier. 機場會有一名信使從我們的快遞員那兒取走照片。"]}]}]},"microscope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顯微鏡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>microscope</b> is a scientific instrument which makes very small objects look bigger so that more detail can be seen. 顯微鏡","examples":[]}]}]},"mercy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"仁慈，寬恕；<非正式>幸運，恩惠；慈善，憐憫"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"哎呀（表示驚訝、震驚或害怕）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority shows <b>mercy</b>, they choose not to harm someone they have power over, or they forgive someone they have the right to punish. 仁慈; 寬恕","examples":["Neither side took prisoners or showed any mercy. 雙方都沒有抓俘虜，也沒有表現出絲毫的仁慈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to an event or a situation as <b>a</b> <b>mercy</b>, you mean that it makes you feel happy or relieved, usually because it stops something unpleasant from happening. 幸運","examples":["It really was a mercy that he'd gone so rapidly at the end. 這真幸運，他最後走得那麼快。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mercy</b> is used to describe a special journey to help someone in great need, such as people who are sick or made homeless by war. 善行","examples":["She vanished nine months ago while on a mercy mission to West Africa. 她在9個月前去西非的慈善之旅中消失不見了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person or thing is <b>at the mercy</b> <b>of</b> another, the first person or thing is in a situation where they cannot prevent themselves from being harmed or affected by the second. 完全由…支配","examples":["Buildings are left to decay at the mercy of vandals and the weather. 這些建築物因人為的肆意破壞和日曬雨淋而破敗不堪。"]}]}]},"merit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"優秀品質，價值；優點，長處；<英>（成績等級）良好；事實真相，是非曲直；善行，善事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"值得，應受；應受賞（或罰）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something has <b>merit</b>, it has good or worthwhile qualities. 優點; 價值","examples":["The argument seemed to have considerable merit. 這個論點似乎有相當大的價值。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>merits</b> of something are its advantages or other good points. 好處","examples":["They have been persuaded of the merits of peace. 他們已經被說服，認識到了和平的好處。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>merits</b> a particular action or treatment, they deserve it. 應受到","examples":["He said he had done nothing wrong to merit a criminal investigation. 他說他沒有做錯任何事，不應該受到刑事調查。"]}]}]},"misfortune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"厄運，不幸；不幸事件，災難"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>misfortune</b> is something unpleasant or unlucky that happens to someone. 不幸","examples":["She seemed to enjoy the misfortunes of others. 她似乎很喜歡幸災樂禍。"]}]}]},"ministry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（政府的）部，部辦公樓；（全體）牧師；神職，神職任期；一任首相的執政期；照料，服務"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In many countries, a <b>ministry</b> is a government department which deals with a particular thing or area of activity, for example trade, defence, or transportation. (政府的) 部","examples":["...the Ministry of Justice. …司法部。"]}]}]},"mischief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"惡作劇，搗亂，胡鬧；頑皮，淘氣；傷害，麻煩，不和；（律）造成損害的行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mischief</b> is playing harmless tricks on people or doing things you are not supposed to do. It can also refer to the desire to do this. 惡作劇; 搗亂","examples":["The little boy was a real handful. He was always up to mischief. 這個小男孩真是難管教。他總是在搞惡作劇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Mischief</b> is behaviour that is intended to cause trouble for people. It can also refer to the trouble that is caused. 製造麻煩","examples":["The more sinister explanation is that he is about to make mischief in the Middle East again. 更為險惡的解釋是他又要在中東製造事端。"]}]}]},"minimum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最小的，最低限度的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最小值，最低限度"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最低，至少"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>minimum</b> to describe an amount which is the smallest that is possible, allowed, or required. 最小量的; 最低限度的","examples":["He was only five feet nine, the minimum height for a policeman. 他只有5.9英尺高，這是警察身高要求的底線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>minimum</b> to state how small an amount is. 很小的","examples":["The basic needs of life are available with minimum effort. 生活的基本需求花很小的力氣就能得到。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Minimum</b> is also a noun. 最小量; 最低限度","examples":["This will take a minimum of one hour. 這最少要用一個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Minimum</b> is also a noun. 很小量","examples":["With a minimum of fuss, she produced the grandson he had so desperately wished for. 她不聲不響地生出了他翹首以待的孫子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is a particular amount <b>minimum</b>, you mean that this is the smallest amount it should be or could possibly be, although a larger amount is acceptable or very possible. 至少","examples":["You're talking over a thousand dollars minimum for one course. 你們在討論一門課程至少一千美元。"]}]}]},"mineral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"礦物質；礦物；<英>汽水，蘇打水；無機物；礦泉水"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（與）礦物（有關）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mineral</b> is a substance such as tin, salt, or sulphur that is formed naturally in rocks and in the earth. Minerals are also found in small quantities in food and drink. 礦物","examples":[]}]}]},"minister":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（英國及其他許多國家的）部長，大臣；牧師；公使，外交使節"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滿足（……的需要），幫助；當牧師；執行（或主持）（聖餐式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>minister</b> is a member of the clergy, especially in Protestant churches. 牧師","examples":["His father was a Baptist minister. 他父親是一名浸禮會牧師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>minister</b> is a person who officially represents their government in a foreign country and has a lower rank than an ambassador. 公使","examples":["He concluded a deal with the Danish minister in Washington. 他在華盛頓與丹麥公使達成了一項協議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some countries outside the United States, a <b>minister</b> is a person who is in charge of a particular government department. 政府部門部長","examples":["When the government came to power, he was named minister of culture. 這屆政府上臺時，他被任命為了文化部長。"]}]}]},"modesty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"謙虛，謙遜；保守，端莊；適度，有限；羞怯，靦腆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who shows <b>modesty</b> does not talk much about their abilities or achievements. 謙虛","examples":["His modesty does him credit, for the food he produces speaks for itself. 他的謙虛為他贏得了信譽，他生產的食品就是最好的證明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the <b>modesty</b> of something such as a place or amount when it is fairly small. (某地或數量等) 小","examples":["The modesty of the town itself comes as something of a surprise. 這個城鎮的小巧挺讓人吃驚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone, especially a woman, shows <b>modesty</b>, they are cautious about the way they dress and behave because they are aware that other people may view them in a sexual way. (尤指婦女) 端莊","examples":["There were shrieks of embarrassment, mingled with giggles, from some of the girls as they struggled to protect their modesty. 有些女孩子努力要保持端莊，但還是發出了尷尬的尖叫聲，其中還夾雜著咯咯的笑聲。"]}]}]},"mudslide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"泥石流，泥流，塌方，山崩（大量泥土沿山坡或陡坡滑落，常造成破壞）；也指沿緩坡而下的徐緩黏滯泥流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mudslide</b> is a large amount of mud sliding down a mountain, usually causing damage or destruction. 泥流; 泥石流","examples":[]}]}]},"measure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"措施，辦法；適量，適度；判斷，衡量；度量單位，計量標準；（酒的）標準量；<美>小節，拍子；象徵，跡象；議案，法案；格律單位；計量工具，量器；<古>（尤指莊重或肅穆的）舞蹈，舞步；岩層；（數）除數；（印刷）行寬，頁寬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"測量；（指尺寸、長短、數量等）量度為；估量，判定（重要性、價值或影響等）；走過；顯示，記錄；用作……的量器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>measure</b> the quality, value, or effect of something, you discover or judge how great it is. 估量","examples":["I continued to measure his progress against the charts in the doctor's office. 我繼續根據醫生辦公室裡的圖表來估量他的進展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>measure</b> a quantity that can be expressed in numbers, such as the length of something, you discover it using a particular instrument or device, for example a ruler. 測量","examples":["Measure the length and width of the gap. 測量一下這個裂口的長度和寬度。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>measures</b> a particular length, width, or amount, that is its size or intensity, expressed in numbers. (長度、寬度、數量的) 數值為","examples":["It measures 20 yards from side to side. 從這邊到那邊的距離為20碼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>measure of</b> a particular quality, feeling, or activity is a fairly large amount of it. 一定數量; 一定程度","examples":["With the exception of Juan, each attained a measure of success. 除了胡安，每個人都取得了一定的成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one aspect of a situation is <b>a</b> <b>measure of</b> that situation, you mean that it shows that the situation is very serious or has developed to a very great extent. (嚴重程度的) 標準","examples":["That is a measure of how bad things have become at the bank. 那就是銀行的局面已經糟糕到何種程度的衡量標準。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone, usually a government or other authority, takes <b>measures</b> to do something, they carry out particular actions in order to achieve a particular result. 措施","examples":["The government warned that police would take tougher measures to contain the trouble. 政府警告說警察將採取更為強硬的措施來制止這場動亂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>measure</b> <b>of</b> a strong alcoholic drink such as brandy or whisky is an amount of it in a glass. In bars, a <b>measure</b> is an official standard amount. (標準量的) 一杯","examples":["He poured himself another generous measure of whisky. 他又給自己慷慨地倒了一杯威士忌。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In music, a <b>measure</b> is one of the several short parts of the same length into which a piece of music is divided. (音樂的) 小節","examples":["Malcolm wanted to mix the beginning of a sonata, then add Beethoven for a few measures, then go back to Bach. 馬爾科姆想要在開頭部分加入一段奏鳴曲，然後加上幾個小節的貝多芬作品，然後再回到巴赫的作品。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something has changed or that it has affected you <b>beyond measure</b>, you are emphasizing that it has done this to a great extent. 極度","examples":["Mankind's knowledge of the universe has increased beyond measure. 人類關於宇宙的知識已經極大增加。"]}]}]},"monthly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每月的，每月一次的；按月支付的，按月計算的；（票、通行證等）有效期為一個月的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"月刊"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每個月，每月一次"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monthly</b> event or publication happens or appears every month. 每月的; 每月一次的","examples":["Many people are now having trouble making their monthly house payments. 現在許多人都有支付按月房貸的困難。","Kidscape runs monthly workshops for teachers. 基德思加坡為教師舉行每月一次的研討會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Monthly</b> quantities or rates relate to a period of one month. 每月的","examples":["Consumers are charged a monthly fee above their basic cable costs. 消費者每月被收取高於基本有線費的一筆費用。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Monthly</b> is also an adverb. 每月地; 每月一次地","examples":["In some areas the property price can rise monthly. 有些地區，房價能每月都漲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a publication that is published monthly as a <b>monthly</b>. 月刊","examples":["...a satirical monthly. …一份諷刺月刊。"]}]}]},"murderer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兇手，謀殺犯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>murderer</b> is a person who has murdered someone. 謀殺者","examples":["One of these men may have been the murderer. 這些人中有一個可能就是謀殺者。"]}]}]},"mustache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鬍子，髭"}],"sections":[]},"motivation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動力，誘因；積極性，幹勁；<南非>（支援請求或倡議的）事實與理由"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>motivation</b> for doing something is what causes you to want to do it. 動力","examples":["Money is my motivation. 金錢就是我的動力。"]}]}]},"monument":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紀念碑，紀念館，紀念物；遺址，名勝古蹟；典範；塑像，墓碑；有永久價值的作品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……樹碑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monument</b> is a large structure, usually made of stone, which is built to remind people of an event in history or of a famous person. 紀念碑","examples":["...a newly restored monument commemorating a 119-year-old tragedy. …為紀念一起有著119年曆史的慘劇而新修復的一座紀念碑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>monument</b> is something such as a castle or bridge that was built a very long time ago and is regarded as an important part of a country's history. 歷史遺蹟","examples":["...the ancient monuments of Mexico and Peru. …墨西哥和秘魯的歷史古蹟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as a <b>monument</b> <b>to</b> someone's qualities, you mean that it is a very good example of the results or effects of those qualities. 典範","examples":["By his international achievements he leaves a fitting monument to his beliefs. 他在國際上的成就恰好成為他信仰的一個例證。"]}]}]},"monitor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顯示器，監控器；監視儀，監護儀；監督員，監察員；（學校裡的）班長，級長；（電臺的）監聽員；揚聲器；巨蜥；淺水重炮艦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"監視；監聽（外國廣播或電話）；監控（無線電或電視傳輸訊號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>monitor</b> something, you regularly check its development or progress, and sometimes comment on it. 監控","examples":["Officials had not been allowed to monitor the voting. 官員們未曾獲許監控選舉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>monitors</b> radio broadcasts from other countries, they record them or listen carefully to them in order to obtain information. 監聽","examples":["Peter Murray is in Washington and has been monitoring reports out of Monrovia. 彼得·默裡在華盛頓，一直監聽來自蒙羅維亞的報道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>monitor</b> is a machine that is used to check or record things, for example processes or substances inside a person's body. 監控器","examples":["The heart monitor shows low levels of consciousness. 心臟監控器顯示低意識水平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>monitor</b> is a screen which is used to display certain kinds of information, for example on a computer, in airports, or in television studios. 顯示屏","examples":["He was watching a game of tennis on a television monitor. 他那時正在電視監控器上觀看一場網球賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a person who checks that something is done correctly, or that it is fair, as a <b>monitor</b>. 監督員","examples":["Government monitors will continue to accompany reporters. 政府監督員們將繼續陪同記者們。"]}]}]},"murmur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"低語聲，輕柔的談話聲；持續輕柔的聲音；私下的抱怨，咕噥；（醫）（心臟的）雜音"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"低語，輕聲地說；私下抱怨，發牢騷；發出持續輕柔的聲音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>murmur</b> something, you say it very quietly, so that not many people can hear what you are saying. 小聲說","examples":["He turned and murmured something to the professor. 他轉過身，小聲對教授說了些什麼。","\"How lovely,\" she murmured. “多可愛呀，”她低聲說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>murmur</b> is something that is said but can hardly be heard. 低語","examples":["They spoke in low murmurs. 他們竊竊私語。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>murmur</b> is a continuous low sound, like the noise of a river or of voices far away. (河水、遠處談話等) 輕微連續的聲音","examples":["The piano music mixes with the murmur of conversation. 鋼琴音樂與輕輕的談話聲混合在一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>murmur</b> <b>of</b> a particular emotion is a quiet expression of it. (情感的) 預設","examples":["The promise of some basic working rights draws murmurs of approval. 對一些基本工作權利的承諾得到預設。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>murmur</b> is an abnormal sound which is made by the heart and which shows that there is probably something wrong with it. (心臟發出的) 雜音","examples":["The doctor said James had now developed a heart murmur. 醫生說詹姆斯心臟現在出現了雜音。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does something <b>without a murmur</b>, they do it without complaining. 毫無怨言","examples":["Then came the bill and my friend paid up without a murmur. 然後賬單來了，我朋友毫無怨言地結了帳。"]}]}]},"nightmare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噩夢；可怕的經歷，很難對付的人（或情形）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nightmare</b> is a very frightening dream. 惡夢","examples":["All the victims still suffered nightmares. 所有的受害者仍為惡夢所擾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a situation as a <b>nightmare</b>, you mean that it is very frightening and unpleasant. 噩夢 (指可怕處境)","examples":["The years in prison were a nightmare. 數年的鐵窗生涯是一場噩夢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a situation as a <b>nightmare</b>, you are saying in a very emphatic way that it is irritating because it causes you a lot of trouble. 噩夢 (指惱人的情況)","examples":["Taking my son Peter to a restaurant was a nightmare. 帶我兒子彼得去飯店吃飯真是一場噩夢。"]}]}]},"nationality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"族，民族；國籍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have the <b>nationality</b> of a particular country, you were born there or have the legal right to be a citizen. 國籍","examples":["Asked his nationality, he said American. 問到他的國籍，他說是美國人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to people who have the same racial origins as a <b>nationality</b>, especially when they do not have their own independent country. (尤指沒有自己獨立國家的) 民族","examples":["...the many nationalities that comprise Ethiopia. …組成衣索比亞的眾多民族。"]}]}]},"nylon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尼龍，（紡）聚醯胺纖維，錦綸；（舊式）尼龍襪（複數 nylons）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nylon</b> is a strong, flexible artificial fibre. 尼龍","examples":["The chair is made of lightweight nylon. 那把椅子是由輕質尼龍製作的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Nylons</b> are stockings made of nylon. 尼龍襪","examples":["She wore a long skirt with pink pumps and black nylons. 她穿了一條長裙，配粉色輕軟舞鞋和黑色尼龍襪。"]}]}]},"obedience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"服從，遵從"}],"sections":[]},"noun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名詞；努恩（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>noun</b> is a word such as \"car,\" \"love,\" or \"Anne\" which is used to refer to a person or thing. 名詞","examples":[]}]}]},"nursery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"託兒所，幼兒園；兒童房；<舊>兒童活動室；苗圃；（醫院裡的）育嬰室；動物繁殖場；溫床；兩歲的馬參加的賽馬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幼兒教育的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nursery</b> is a room in a family home in which the young children of the family sleep or play. 育兒室","examples":["He has painted murals in his children's nursery. 他在他家的育兒室畫上了壁畫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>nursery</b> is a place where children who are not old enough to go to school are cared for. 託兒所","examples":["She puts her baby in this nursery and then goes back to work. 她把孩子送到這家託兒所然後回去上班。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Nursery</b> is a school for very young children. 幼兒園","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>nursery</b> is a place where plants are grown in order to be sold. 苗圃","examples":["The garden, developed over the past 35 years, includes a nursery. 這個有35年曆史的園子裡有一個苗圃。"]}]}]},"nonsense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"荒謬的想法（看法），胡說；愚蠢的行為，胡鬧；無意義的話（字句）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無意義的，荒謬的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"胡說，廢話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something spoken or written is <b>nonsense</b>, you mean that you consider it to be untrue or silly. 胡言亂語; 蠢話","examples":["Most orthodox doctors however dismiss this as complete nonsense. 然而大多數傳統的醫生將此視為純粹的胡言亂語而不予考慮。","...all that poetic nonsense about love. …所有關於愛情的詩一般的傻話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>nonsense</b> to refer to something that you think is foolish or that you disapprove of. 蠢事","examples":["Surely it is an economic nonsense to deplete the world of natural resources. 耗盡世界的自然資源無疑是一件經濟上的愚蠢行為。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to spoken or written words that do not mean anything because they do not make sense as <b>nonsense</b>. 無意義的話","examples":["...a children's nonsense poem by Charles E Carryl. …查爾斯·E·卡里爾寫的一首兒童打油詩。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>make a nonsense of</b> something or to <b>make nonsense of</b> it means to make it seem ridiculous or pointless. 使…荒唐可笑; 使…失去意義","examples":["The fighting made a nonsense of peace pledges made last week. 這場戰鬥使上週做出的和平承諾失去了意義。"]}]}]},"objection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反對的理由；反對，異議；抗議（律師在審判中提出異議的插話）；惱火，煩心；缺點，缺陷；妨礙，障礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you express or raise an <b>objection</b> <b>to</b> something, you say that you do not like it or agree with it. 反對","examples":["Despite objections by the White House, the Senate voted today to cut off aid. 儘管白宮反對，參議院今天投票中斷援助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you have <b>no</b> <b>objection</b> <b>to</b> something, you mean that you are not annoyed or bothered by it. 反對意見","examples":["I have no objection to banks making money. 我對銀行賺錢沒有反對意見。"]}]}]},"neglect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"疏於照顧，未予看管；不予重視，忽視；漏做"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"忽略，忽視，未被重視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>neglect</b> someone or something, you fail to take care of them properly. 疏於照管","examples":["The woman denied that she had neglected her child. 那位婦女否認疏於照管她的孩子。","Feed plants and they grow, neglect them and they suffer. 給植物施肥，它們就生長；疏於照管，它們就遭殃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>neglect</b> someone or something, you fail to give them the amount of attention that they deserve. 忽視","examples":["He'd given too much to his career, worked long hours, neglected her. 他在事業上投入太多了，長時間地工作，冷落了她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>neglect</b> <b>to</b> do something that you ought to do or <b>neglect</b> your duty, you fail to do it. 疏忽","examples":["We often neglect to make proper use of our bodies. 我們經常疏忽了合理使用我們的身體。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neglect</b> is also a noun. 疏於照管","examples":["The town's old quayside is collapsing after years of neglect. 這座小鎮的舊碼頭區在多年疏於保養後快要坍塌了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被忽視的","examples":["The fact that she is not coming today makes her grandmother feel lonely and neglected. 她今天不來了，這讓她的祖母感到孤單，受到冷落。","...a neglected aspect of the city's forgotten history. …這座城市被遺忘的歷史中一個被忽視的方面。"]}]}]},"obstacle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"障礙，阻礙；障礙物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>obstacle</b> is an object that makes it difficult for you to go where you want to go, because it is in your way. 障礙物","examples":["Most competition cars will only roll over if they hit an obstacle. 多數賽車在撞到障礙物時都會翻車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to anything that makes it difficult for you to do something as an <b>obstacle</b>. 障礙","examples":["Overcrowding remains a large obstacle to improving conditions. 過度擁擠仍然是改善條件的一大障礙。"]}]}]},"offense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"違法，犯罪；冒犯，傷害；過錯，不當；討厭的東西，引起反感的事物；<正式> 進攻，攻擊行為；進攻隊員；（球隊的）進攻"}],"sections":[]},"occupation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"工作，職業；消遣，業餘活動；（尤指軍隊的）佔領，控制；（房屋等地方的）居住，使用"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英>僅供土地佔有者使用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>occupation</b> is your job or profession. 職業","examples":["I suppose I was looking for an occupation which was going to be an adventure. 我想我那時在尋找一份冒險型職業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>occupation</b> is something that you spend time doing, either for pleasure or because it needs to be done. 消遣","examples":["Parachuting is a dangerous occupation. 跳傘是一種危險的消遣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>occupation</b> of a country happens when it is entered and controlled by a foreign army. 佔領","examples":["...the occupation of Poland. …對波蘭的佔領。"]}]}]},"observation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀察，監視；觀察力；觀察資料，觀察結果；言論，評論；遵守，奉行；測天"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用於觀察的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Observation</b> is the action or process of carefully watching someone or something. 觀察","examples":["...careful observation of the movement of the planets. …對行星執行的仔細觀測。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>observation</b> is something that you have learned by seeing or watching something and thinking about it. 觀察結果","examples":["This book contains observations about the causes of addictions. 這本書包含關於上癮原因的觀察結果。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person makes an <b>observation</b>, they make a comment about something or someone, usually as a result of watching how they behave. 觀察評論","examples":["Is that a criticism or just an observation? 那是一種批評呢，還是一種觀察評論而已？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Observation</b> is the ability to pay a lot of attention to things and to notice more about them than most people do. 觀察力","examples":["She has good powers of observation. 她有很強的觀察力。"]}]}]},"opera":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歌劇演出，歌劇表演；歌劇團，歌劇院；歌劇藝術，歌劇劇本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>opera</b> is a play with music in which all the words are sung. 歌劇","examples":["...a one-act opera about contemporary women in America. …關於當代美國婦女的一部獨幕歌劇。","...an opera singer. …一名歌劇演員。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Opera</b> is an alternative plural of . (opus)的兩種複數形式之一","examples":[]}]}]},"orchestra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（大型的）管絃樂隊；樂池（=orchestra pit）；<美>（劇院中）靠近舞臺的座位；古希臘劇場舞臺前部半圓形的表演區（供合唱隊表演歌舞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orchestra</b> is a large group of musicians who play a variety of different instruments together. Orchestras usually play classical music. 管絃樂隊","examples":["...the Los Angeles Philharmonic Orchestra. …洛杉磯愛樂樂團。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>orchestra</b> or <b>the</b> <b>orchestra seats</b> in a theatre or concert hall are the seats on the first floor directly in front of the stage. 舞臺前方一樓座位","examples":["With the balcony blocked off, patrons filled most of the orchestra seats. 樓廳包廂被封閉了，贊助人幾乎坐滿了舞臺前方的一樓座位。"]}]}]},"oral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"口頭的，口述的；口的，口腔的；（藥物）口服的；（語音）口腔發聲的；（社會）沒有文字的；（心理分析）口欲的，口唇的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指外語）口試；<美>（大學裡的）口試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oral</b> communication is spoken rather than written. 口頭的","examples":["...the written and oral traditions of ancient cultures. …古代文化的文字記載和口述傳統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>oral</b> to indicate that something is done with a person's mouth or relates to a person's mouth. 用口的; 與口有關的","examples":["...good oral hygiene. …良好的口腔衛生。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"口頭地","examples":["...their ability to present ideas orally and in writing. …他們透過口頭和筆頭表達觀點的能力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"用口地; 與口有關地","examples":["...antibiotic tablets taken orally. …口服抗生素片。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oral</b> is an examination, especially in a foreign language, that is spoken rather than written. 口試","examples":["I spoke privately to the candidate after the oral. 口試結束後，我私下和那個考生說了幾句話。"]}]}]},"orbit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（環繞地球、太陽等執行的）軌道；勢力範圍，影響範圍；眼眶，眼窩"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"沿軌道執行，環繞……執行；使（衛星）進入軌道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orbit</b> is the curved path in space that is followed by an object going around and around a planet, moon, or star. (天體執行的) 軌道","examples":["Mars and Earth have orbits which change with time. 火星和地球的軌道隨著時間而發生改變。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a satellite <b>orbits</b> a planet, moon, or sun, it moves around it in a continuous, curving path. 環繞…的軌道執行","examples":["In 1957 the Soviet Union launched the first satellite to orbit the earth. 1957年，蘇聯發射了第一顆環繞地球執行的人造衛星。"]}]}]},"objective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目的，目標；出擊目標（尤指在軍事攻擊中)；（望遠鏡或顯微鏡中的）物鏡；出擊目標（尤指在軍事攻擊中）；賓格"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"客觀的，不帶個人情感的；客觀存在的；賓格的；目標的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>objective</b> is what you are trying to achieve. 目標","examples":["Our main objective was the recovery of the child safe and well. 我們的主要目標是讓這個孩子安然無恙地恢復健康。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Objective</b> information is based on facts. 客觀的","examples":["He had no objective evidence that anything extraordinary was happening. 他沒有客觀證據證明有什麼非同尋常的事情發生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>objective,</b> they base their opinions on facts rather than on their personal feelings. 客觀的","examples":["I believe that a journalist should be completely objective. 我認為一名記者應該完全客觀。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"客觀地","examples":["We simply want to inform people objectively about events. 我們只想客觀地把事件告之於眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"客觀地","examples":["Try to view situations more objectively, especially with regard to work. 儘量更客觀地看待情況，尤其對於工作。"]}]}]},"outcome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結果，效果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>outcome</b> of an activity, process, or situation is the situation that exists at the end of it. 結果","examples":["Mr. Singh said he was pleased with the outcome. 西恩先生說他對此結果感到滿意。","It's too early to know the outcome of her illness. 現在還不知道她的病情結果。"]}]}]},"operation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運作，實施；運轉，操作；手術；（有組織的）活動，行動；軍事行動；企業，公司；業務，經營 ；（數學）運算"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>operation</b> is a highly organized activity that involves many people doing different things. 行動","examples":["The rescue operation began on Friday afternoon. 營救行動星期五下午展開。","The soldiers were engaged in a military operation close to the Ugandan border. 士兵們在靠近烏干達邊界的地區開展軍事行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A business or company can be referred to as an <b>operation</b>. 公司","examples":["Thorn's electronics operation employs around 5,000 people. 索恩的電子公司僱傭了大約五千名員工。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a patient has an <b>operation</b>, a surgeon cuts open their body in order to remove, replace, or repair a diseased or damaged part. 手術","examples":["Charles was at the clinic recovering from an operation on his arm. 查爾斯在診所，進行手臂的術後恢復。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a system is <b>in</b> <b>operation</b>, it is being used. 實施中","examples":["...the free banking system that has been in operation since the early eighties. …從80年代初就開始實施的自由銀行制度。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a machine or device is <b>in</b> <b>operation</b>, it is working. 運轉中","examples":["There are three ski lifts in operation. 有3輛滑雪纜車在執行。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a rule, system, or plan <b>comes into operation</b> or you <b>put</b> it <b>into operation</b>, you begin to use it. 開始實施","examples":["The Financial Services Act came into operation four years ago. 《金融服務法》4年前開始生效。"]}]}]},"oxygen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氧，氧氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oxygen</b> is a colourless gas that exists in large quantities in the air. All plants and animals need oxygen in order to live. 氧氣","examples":["The human brain needs to be without oxygen for only four minutes before permanent damage occurs. 人腦缺氧只需4分鐘就會造成永久性損傷。"]}]}]},"participation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"參加，參與"}],"sections":[]},"parachute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"降落傘"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳傘；傘降，空投；緊急任命，臨危受命"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>parachute</b> is a device that enables a person to jump from an aircraft and float safely to the ground. It consists of a large piece of thin cloth attached to your body by strings. 降落傘","examples":["They fell 41,000 ft. before opening their parachutes. 他們下落了41000英尺才開啟他們的降落傘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person <b>parachutes</b> or someone <b>parachutes</b> them somewhere, they jump from an aircraft using a parachute. 使空降; 跳傘","examples":["He was a courier for the Polish underground and parachuted into Warsaw. 他是波蘭地下組織的信使，被空降到了華沙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>parachute</b> something somewhere means to drop it somewhere by parachute. 空投","examples":["Planes parachuted food, clothing, blankets, medicine, and water into the rugged mountainous border region. 飛機把食物、衣服、毯子、藥和水空投到崎嶇的邊界山區。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person <b>parachutes into</b> an organization or if they <b>are parachuted into</b> it, they are brought in suddenly in order to help it. 突然派到 (某機構以幫助該機構)","examples":["...a consultant who parachutes into corporations and helps provide strategic thinking. …一個突然派到公司去幫助提供戰略思想的顧問。","Executives with political influence are parachuted into the company. 有政治影響的主管們被突然被派進公司。"]}]}]},"participle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（語法）分詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>participle</b> is a form of a verb that can be used in compound tenses of the verb. There are two participles in English: the past participle, which usually ends in \"-ed,\" and the present participle, which ends in \"-ing.\" 分詞","examples":[]}]}]},"paragraph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（文章的）段，段落；段落符號；短評"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（文章）分段"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>paragraph</b> is a section of a piece of writing. A paragraph always begins on a new line and contains at least one sentence. 段落","examples":["The length of a paragraph depends on the information it conveys. 段落的長度取決於它傳達的資訊。"]}]}]},"oval":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"橢圓形的，卵形的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"橢圓形（物），卵形（物）；橢圓形體育場，橢圓形跑道；澳式橄欖球場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oval</b> things have a shape that is like a circle but is wider in one direction than the other. 橢圓的","examples":["...the small oval framed picture of a little boy. …一個小男孩的鑲在橢圓形框架裡的小幅照片。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oval</b> is also a noun. 橢圓","examples":["Using 2 spoons, form the cheese into small balls or ovals. 用兩把勺把乾酪擠成小圓球狀或橢圓球狀。"]}]}]},"panel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專家諮詢組，專題討論小組；（門等的）鑲板，嵌板；控制板，儀表盤；（車身的）金屬板；（衣服上的）鑲條，飾片；畫板；<美>陪審團；<英>國民保健制度（原國民健康保險）醫師名單；<蘇格蘭，法律>被告"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用（木板、金屬板等）覆蓋，鑲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>panel</b> is a small group of people who are chosen to do something, for example, to discuss something in public or to make a decision. 專門小組","examples":["He assembled a panel of scholars to advise him. 他集結了一個學者小組為他出謀劃策。","All the writers on the panel agreed that Quinn's book should be singled out for special praise. 專門小組中的所有作家都同意奎因的書應該被挑出來予以特別表揚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>panel</b> is a flat rectangular piece of wood or other material that forms part of a larger object such as a door. (門等的) 鑲板; 嵌板","examples":["...the frosted glass panel set in the centre of the door. …嵌在門中心的毛玻璃板。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A control <b>panel</b> or instrument <b>panel</b> is a board or surface that contains switches and controls to operate a machine or piece of equipment. (控制) 面板; (儀表) 板","examples":["The equipment was extremely sophisticated and was monitored from a central control panel. 這臺裝置極其複雜，是由中央控制面板監控的。"]}]}]},"pasta":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"義大利麵食；麵糰"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Pasta）人名；（英、意）帕斯塔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pasta</b> is a type of food made from a mixture of flour, eggs, and water that is formed into different shapes and then boiled. Spaghetti, macaroni, and noodles are types of pasta. 麵食","examples":[]}]}]},"pebble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鵝卵石，礫石；水晶透鏡"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用卵石鋪"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>（眼鏡片）很厚的，凸起的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pebble</b> is a small, smooth, round stone which is found on beaches and at the bottom of rivers. 卵石","examples":[]}]}]},"partnership":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"合夥（關係），合股；合夥企業；合夥人；（兩個人、組織或國家之間的）合作關係，夥伴關係；合夥契約；（板球）（回合結束前或其中一人被迫退場前）一對擊球手的跑動得分數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Partnership</b> or a <b>partnership</b> is a relationship in which two or more people, organizations, or countries work together as partners. 夥伴關係","examples":["...the partnership between Germany's banks and its businesses. …德國的各銀行與德國企業之間的夥伴關係。"]}]}]},"pace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"步速，（移動的）速度；（發生、進展、發展的）速度，節奏；一步，一步之距；（馬行走或奔跑的）步法；<文>步態；快節奏；快跑的能力；（板球）（影響球速的）兩個三柱門之間的場地狀況"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因擔憂、緊張或不耐煩而）踱步，踱步於；（在賽跑中）為……定速度；為……領跑；為（書、電影等中的故事）設定節奏；調整自己的工作（或活動）節奏；步測；（馬）走側對步（主見於專門飼養或訓練的馬）"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"<正式> （用於人名前，委婉提出不同意見）請……原諒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>pace</b> of something is the speed at which it happens or is done. 速度; 節奏","examples":["Many people were not satisfied with the pace of change. 許多人都不滿意變化的速度。","They could not stand the pace or the workload. 他們受不了工作的節奏和負荷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>pace</b> is the speed at which you walk. 步速","examples":["He moved at a brisk pace down the rue St. Antoine. 他沿著聖安託萬街輕快地走著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pace</b> is the distance that you move when you take one step. 步距","examples":["He'd only gone a few paces before he stopped again. 他只走了幾步就又停了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pace</b> a small area, you keep walking up and down it, because you are anxious or impatient. (因焦慮或不耐煩) 在…走來走去","examples":["As they waited, Kravis paced the room nervously. 在他們等著時，克拉維斯在房間裡緊張不安地走來走去。","He found John pacing around the house, unable to sleep. 他發現約翰正在房子裡四下踱步，無法入眠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pace</b> <b>yourself</b> when doing something, you do it at a steady rate. 放穩 (自己) 的步調","examples":["It was a tough race and I had to pace myself. 那是一場艱難的比賽，我必須放穩自己的步調。"]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"with due deference to: used to acknowledge politely someone who disagrees with the speaker or writer 尊敬的(用於禮貌提及持反對意見的某人)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>keeps pace</b> <b>with</b> something else that is changing, it changes quickly in response to it. 與…保持同步","examples":["The earnings of the average American have failed to keep pace with the rate of inflation. 一般美國人的收入跟不上通貨膨脹的速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep pace</b> <b>with</b> someone who is walking or running, you succeed in going as fast as them, so that you remain close to them. 與…並駕齊驅","examples":["With four laps to go, he kept pace with the leaders. 還有4圈要跑，他與那些領先者並駕齊驅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you do something <b>at</b> your <b>own pace</b>, you do it at a speed that is comfortable for you. 按自己的速度","examples":["The computer will give students the opportunity to learn at their own pace. 計算機將給予學生們按照自己的速度學習的機會。"]}]}]},"percent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"百分之……；部分"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"百分之……的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以百分之……地，每一百中有……地"}],"sections":[]},"pedal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（腳踏車、汽車或機器的）腳踏板；(鋼琴、風琴等的)踏板；（樂）PEDAL NOTE的簡稱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎腳踏車前進；踩（腳踏車等的）踏板；（尤指以某種特別方式）踩動鋼琴踏板"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"踏板的，腳踏的；腳的，關於腳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>pedals</b> on a bicycle are the two parts that you push with your feet in order to make the bicycle move. (腳踏車的) 踏板","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pedal</b> in a car or on a machine is a lever that you press with your foot in order to control the car or machine. (汽車或機器的) 踏板","examples":["...the brake or accelerator pedals. …剎車或加速器踏板。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>pedal</b> a bicycle, you push the pedals around with your feet to make it move. 踩 (腳踏車) 踏板","examples":["She climbed on her bike with a feeling of pride and pedalled the five miles home. 她懷著一種自豪感跨上腳踏車，蹬了5英里回到家。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"of or relating to the foot or feet 腳的; 與腳有關的","examples":[]}]}]},"peer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同齡人，同等地位的人，相匹敵的人；（英國）貴族"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"凝視，費力地看；隱現；<古>看見；<古>匹敵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>peer</b> <b>at</b> something, you look at it very hard, usually because it is difficult to see clearly. 費力地看; 盯著","examples":["I had been peering at a computer print-out that made no sense at all. 我一直在費力地看一份不知所云的電腦列印稿。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>peers</b> are the people who are the same age as you or who have the same status as you. 同齡人; 同等地位的人","examples":["His engaging personality made him popular with his peers. 他迷人的個性使他很受同齡人歡迎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a member of a nobility; nobleman 貴族","examples":[]}]}]},"petal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花瓣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>petals</b> of a flower are the thin coloured or white parts that together form the flower. 花瓣","examples":["...bowls of dried rose petals. …一碗碗幹玫瑰花瓣。"]}]}]},"perfection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"完美；完善；完美的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Perfection</b> is the quality of being as good as it is possible for something of a particular kind to be. 完美","examples":["His quest for perfection is relentless. 他對完美的追求是不懈的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The perfection of</b> something such as a skill, system, or product involves making it as good as it could possibly be. 完善","examples":["Madame Clicquot is credited with the perfection of this technique. 這項工藝的完善要歸功於克利科夫人。"]}]}]},"persuasion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"說服，勸服；說服力；（宗教或政治）信仰；教派；某種人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Persuasion</b> is the act of persuading someone to do something or to believe that something is true. 說服","examples":["Only after much persuasion from Ellis had she agreed to hold a show at all. 直到埃利斯進行了大量的遊說之後她才同意舉辦一次展覽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>of</b> a particular <b>persuasion</b>, you have a particular belief or set of beliefs. 信仰; 信念","examples":["It is a national movement and has within it people of all political persuasions. 這是一項全國性的運動，參加的人們政治信仰各不相同。"]}]}]},"percentage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"百分比，百分率；部分，比例；利潤分成，提成；<非正式>利益，好處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>percentage</b> is a fraction of an amount expressed as a particular number of hundredths of that amount. 百分比","examples":["Only a few vegetable-origin foods have such a high percentage of protein. 只有幾種來源於植物的食品含有如此高百分比的蛋白質。"]}]}]},"perfume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香水；芳香，香味，馨香；香精，香料"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使香氣瀰漫；在……上撒香水，抹香水"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Perfume</b> is a pleasant-smelling liquid that women put on their skin to make themselves smell nice. 香水","examples":["The hall smelled of her mother's perfume. 大廳裡瀰漫著她母親的香水味。","...a bottle of perfume. …一瓶香水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Perfume</b> is the ingredient that is added to some products to make them smell nice. 香料","examples":["...a delicate white soap without perfume. …一塊不含香料的氣味清淡的白色肥皂。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is used to <b>perfume</b> a product, it is added to the product to make it smell nice. 給…新增香味","examples":["The oil is used to flavour and perfume soaps, foam baths, and scents. 這種油用來給肥皂、泡沫浴液和香水新增特殊氣味和香味。"]}]}]},"phenomenon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現象；傑出的人，非凡的人（或事物）；（哲學）現象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>phenomenon</b> is something that is observed to happen or exist. 現象","examples":["...scientific explanations of natural phenomena. …自然現象的科學解釋。"]}]}]},"penalty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（因違反法律、規定或合同而受到的）處罰，刑罰；（行為、環境帶來的）不利後果，苦難；（體育運動中對犯規者的）判罰，處罰；（足球、橄欖球及類似運動中的）罰球；（橋牌）（叫牌者未完成定約時的）罰分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>penalty</b> is a punishment that someone is given for doing something which is against a law or rule. 刑罰","examples":["One of those arrested could face the death penalty. 那些被捕之人其中的一個可能會面臨死刑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In sports such as football, American football, and hockey, a <b>penalty</b> is a disadvantage forced on the team that breaks a rule. (體育比賽中的) 罰球","examples":["Referee Michael Reed had no hesitation in awarding a penalty. 裁判邁克爾·裡德毫不猶豫地判了罰球。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>penalty</b> that you pay for something you have done is something unpleasant that you experience as a result. 懲罰","examples":["Why should I pay the penalty for somebody else's mistake? 我為什麼要為別人的錯誤而接受懲罰呢？"]}]}]},"pickpocket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"扒手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扒竊（常用作動名詞或分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pickpocket</b> is a person who steals things from people's pockets or bags in public places. 扒手","examples":["Beware of pickpockets, especially when making a purchase. 當心扒手，尤其是在購物的時候。"]}]}]},"physicist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"物理學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>physicist</b> is a person who does research connected with physics or who studies physics. 物理學家","examples":["...a nuclear physicist. …一位核物理學家。"]}]}]},"philosopher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"哲學家，哲人；思想深刻的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>philosopher</b> is a person who studies or writes about philosophy. 哲學家","examples":["...the Greek philosopher Plato. …希臘哲學家柏拉圖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>philosopher</b>, you mean that they think deeply and seriously about life and other basic matters. 哲人","examples":["Carlos was something of a philosopher. 卡洛斯有幾分哲人氣質。"]}]}]},"pianist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋼琴家，鋼琴演奏者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pianist</b> is a person who plays the piano. 鋼琴演奏者","examples":["She was an accomplished pianist, a superb swimmer, and a gifted artist. 她曾是一位很有造詣的鋼琴家、一流的游泳健將和天才藝術家。"]}]}]},"photography":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"攝影，攝影術；攝影影像，攝影圖片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Photography</b> is the skill, job, or process of producing photographs. 攝影術; 攝影","examples":["Photography is one of her hobbies. 攝影是她的愛好之一。"]}]}]},"physician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醫生，（尤指）內科醫生；撫慰者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>physician</b> is a medical doctor. 內科醫生","examples":["...your family physician. …你的家庭醫生。"]}]}]},"philosophy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"哲學；哲學體系，思想體系；人生哲學，生活（工作）準則；（某一知識或經驗領域的）理論基礎研究，基本原理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Philosophy</b> is the study or creation of theories about basic things such as the nature of existence, knowledge, and thought, or about how people should live. 哲學","examples":["He studied philosophy and psychology at Yale. 他在耶魯大學學習哲學和心理學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>philosophy</b> is a particular set of ideas that a philosopher has. 哲學思想","examples":["...the philosophies of Socrates, Plato, and Aristotle. …蘇格拉底、柏拉圖和亞里士多德的哲學思想。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>philosophy</b> is a particular theory that someone has about how to live or how to deal with a particular situation. 人生哲學; 處事原則","examples":["The best philosophy is to change your food habits to a low-sugar diet. 最好的生活方式是將你的飲食習慣改成食用低糖食品。"]}]}]},"physics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"物理學；物理特性，物理現象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Physics</b> is the scientific study of forces such as heat, light, sound, pressure, gravity, and electricity, and the way that they affect objects. 物理學","examples":["...the laws of physics. …物理學定律。"]}]}]},"pregnancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懷孕（期），妊娠（期）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pregnancy</b> is the condition of being pregnant or the period of time during which a female is pregnant. 懷孕; 懷孕期","examples":["It would be wiser to cut out all alcohol during pregnancy. 懷孕期間最好完全戒酒。"]}]}]},"pioneer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拓荒者；先鋒；（前蘇聯等共產黨國家的）少年先鋒隊隊員；（先頭部隊的）工兵；<愛爾蘭>（天主教禁慾團體）完全禁慾先鋒聯盟的成員；先鋒號（Pioneer）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"先驅的；拓荒的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做先鋒，倡導；開闢（道路）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is referred to as a <b>pioneer</b> in a particular area of activity is one of the first people to be involved in it and develop it. 先驅","examples":["...one of the leading pioneers of photojournalism. …攝影新聞界的主要先驅之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pioneers</b> are people who leave their own country or the place where they were living, and go and live in a place that has not been lived in before. 拓荒者","examples":["...abandoned settlements of early European pioneers. …已廢棄的早期歐洲拓荒者的居住地。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>pioneers</b> a new activity, invention, or process is one of the first people to do it. 倡導","examples":["...Professor Alec Jeffreys, who invented and pioneered DNA tests. …發明和倡導DNA測試的亞歷克·傑弗里斯教授。"]}]}]},"plural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"複數（形式）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"複數的，複數形式的；多樣的，多元的；多數的，多種的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>plural</b> form of a word is the form that is used when referring to more than one person or thing. 複數的","examples":["\"Data\" is the Latin plural form of \"datum.\" “”是“”的拉丁語複數形式。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>plural</b> of a noun is the form of it that is used to refer to more than one person or thing. 複數形式","examples":["What is the plural of \"person\"? “”的複數形式是什麼？"]}]}]},"popularity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流行，普及，受歡迎"}],"sections":[]},"pollution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙染；汙染物；噪音汙染，（夜間擾人的）強烈燈光"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pollution</b> is the process of polluting water, air, or land, especially with poisonous chemicals. 汙染","examples":["The fine was for the company's pollution of the air near its plants. 公司被罰款是因為它的工廠汙染了周圍的空氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pollution</b> is poisonous or dirty substances that are polluting the water, air, or land somewhere. 汙染物","examples":["The level of pollution in the river was falling. 該河流受汙染的程度其時正在降低。"]}]}]},"porter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（火車站、機場等的）行李搬運工人，腳伕；<英>（市場的）搬運工；<英>（酒店、醫院等的）門房，守門人；<美>（火車臥鋪車廂的）乘務員；<英>（醫院的）護工，勤雜工；<美>（大樓的）雜物工；（登山探險中的）補給搬運員；<舊>黑啤酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>porter</b> is a person whose job is to carry things, for example, people's luggage at a train station or in a hotel. 搬運工","examples":["Our taxi pulled up at Old Delhi station and a porter sprinted to the door. 我們的計程車停在老德里車站，一個搬運工疾步跑向車門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a hospital, a <b>porter</b> is someone whose job is to move patients from place to place. (醫院裡的)護工","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>porter</b> is a person whose job is to be in charge of the entrance of a building such as a hotel. 門童","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a dark sweet ale brewed from black malt (用烤麥釀製的)黑啤酒","examples":[]}]}]},"pirate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海盜，海上劫掠者；盜版者，侵犯專利權者；非法制作電視或廣播節目的人（或組織）；道德敗壞者，違法者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"盜印，竊用；劫掠（船隻）；<舊>劫掠（船隻）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"盜版的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pirates</b> are sailors who attack other ships and steal property from them. 海盜","examples":["In the nineteenth century, pirates roamed the seas. 19世紀，海盜很猖獗。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>pirates</b> CDs, DVDs, books, or computer programs copies and sells them when they have no right to do so. 盜版 (CD、DVD、書籍、計算機程式等)","examples":["Computer crimes include data theft and pirating software. 計算機犯罪包括資料竊取和盜版軟體。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非法複製的","examples":["New technology makes it possible to make pirated copies of music and movies. 新技術使製作盜版音樂和影片成為可能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pirate</b> version of something is an illegal copy of it. 盜版的","examples":["Pirate copies of the DVD are already being sold. 該DVD的盜版已經有售了。"]}]}]},"polish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擦亮，磨光；改進，使完美，給……潤色；塗指甲油"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"上光劑，亮光劑；拋光，擦亮；擦光的面，打磨光亮的面；（表演或作品的）完美，優美；<舊>文雅，禮貌"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Polish）波蘭人；波蘭語"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（Polish）波蘭的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Polish</b> is a substance that you put on the surface of an object in order to clean it, protect it, and make it shine. 拋光劑; 亮漆","examples":["The still air smelled faintly of furniture polish. 久未流通的空氣中有股淡淡的傢俱漆的氣味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Polish</b> is also a noun. 擦亮; 磨光","examples":["He gave his counter a polish with a soft duster. 他用柔軟的抹布將櫃檯擦得亮亮的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a performance or piece of work has <b>polish</b>, you mean that it is of a very high standard. 完美; 上乘境界","examples":["The opera lacks the polish of his later work. 這部歌劇缺少他後期作品中所具有的上乘境界。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>polish</b> something, you put polish on it or rub it with a cloth to make it shine. (用拋光劑等) 擦亮","examples":["Each morning he shaved and polished his shoes. 每天早晨他都刮鬍子、擦皮鞋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>polish</b> your technique, performance, or skill at doing something, you work on improving it. 使完美; 改進","examples":["They just need to polish their technique. 他們只需要改進一下自己的技藝。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"擦亮的; 磨光的","examples":["...a highly polished floor. …一塊擦得很亮的地板。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Polish up</b> means the same as . 使完美; 改進","examples":["Polish up your writing skills on a one-week professional course. 上一週的專業課程來增強你的寫作技能。"]}]}]},"plot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陰謀，密謀；情節；（專用的）小塊地；（表現兩個變數關係的）圖表；<美>圖表，地圖；<美>底層平面圖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"密謀，暗中策劃；（在地圖上）畫出，標出；構思（情節）；繪製（曲線）；繪製（圖表）；在圖表上標記，佈置；用圖表說明；計劃，制訂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plot</b> is a secret plan by a group of people to do something that is illegal or wrong, usually against a person or a government. 陰謀","examples":["Security forces have uncovered a plot to overthrow the government. 安全部隊已經揭穿了一個推翻政府的陰謀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>plot</b> of a film, novel, or play is the connected series of events which make up the story.  情節","examples":["He began to tell me the plot of his new book. 他開始向我講述他新書的情節。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plot</b> <b>of</b> land is a small piece of land, especially one that has been measured or marked out for a special purpose, such as building houses or growing vegetables. 小塊圈地","examples":["I thought that I'd buy myself a small plot of land and build a house on it. 我覺得我應該給自己買一小塊地，在上面蓋一所房子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>plot</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>plot</b> something that is illegal or wrong, they plan secretly to do it. 密謀","examples":["Prosecutors in the trial allege the defendants plotted to overthrow the government. 審判的公訴人聲稱被告曾密謀推翻政府。","The military were plotting a coup. 該軍方當時正在密謀政變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>plot</b> a strategy or a course of action, they carefully plan each step of it. 制訂","examples":["Yesterday's meeting was intended to plot a survival strategy for the party. 昨天的會議旨在制訂該黨的生存策略。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>plots</b> something on a graph, they mark certain points on it and then join the points up. (在曲線圖上) 繪製","examples":["We plotted about eight points on the graph. 我們在圖表上繪出了大約有八個點的曲線。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When someone <b>plots</b> the position or course of a plane or ship, they mark it on a map using instruments to obtain accurate information.  標繪","examples":["We were trying to plot the course of the submarine. 我們當時正試圖示繪出那艘潛艇的航線。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>plots</b> the progress or development of something, they make a diagram or a plan which shows how it has developed in order to give some indication of how it will develop in the future. 用圖表展示 (發展趨勢)","examples":["They used a computer to plot the movements of everyone in the police station on December 24, 1990. 他們使用計算機繪製了圖表，來顯示1990年12月24日警察局中每個人的行動。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to arrange or divide (land) into plots 劃分(土地); 把(土地)分成小塊","examples":[]}]}]},"preposition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"介詞，前置詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>preposition</b> is a word such as \"by,\" \"for,\" \"into,\" or \"with\" that usually has a noun group as its object. 介詞","examples":["There is nothing in the rules of grammar to suggest that ending a sentence with a preposition is wrong. 在語法規則中沒有哪一條表明以介詞結束一個句子是錯誤的。"]}]}]},"possession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式> 擁有，持有；個人財產，所有物；持有違禁物，私藏毒品（或武器）；（對球的）控制，球權；進攻；領地，殖民地；鬼魂附體，著魔；（觀點或情感的）支配，控制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in</b> <b>possession</b> <b>of</b> something, you have it, because you have obtained it or because it belongs to you. 擁有","examples":["Those documents are now in the possession of the Washington Post. 那些檔案現在歸《華盛頓郵報》所有。","He was also charged with illegal possession of firearms. 他還被指控非法擁有火器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>possessions</b> are the things that you own or have with you at a particular time. 財產; 所有物","examples":["People had lost their homes and all their possessions. 人們已失去了家園和所有的財產。"]}]}]},"prevention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預防，防止"}],"sections":[]},"preservation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保護，維護；保留，維持；（食物的）儲存，保藏；儲存的狀況，保養的程度"}],"sections":[]},"privacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"隱私，秘密；清靜，（不受干擾的）獨處；<古>隱居處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>privacy</b>, you are in a place or situation that allows you to do things without other people seeing you or disturbing you. 隱私; 私人空間","examples":["He resented the publication of this book, which he saw as an embarrassing invasion of his privacy. 他憎恨這本書的出版，它將此看作是對其隱私的令人難堪的侵犯。","Thatched pavilions provide shady retreats for relaxing and reading in privacy. 茅亭為獨自放鬆和看書提供陰涼的幽僻之所。"]}]}]},"presentation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（頒獎等）儀式，典禮；授予，頒發；（在儀式上接受的）獎項，贈予物；展示會，介紹會，釋出會；陳述，報告，說明；（事物的）呈現方式；（證件等的）出示；（證物的）提交，提供；（戲劇的）演出；（胎兒的）先露位置，產位；（尤指在帝王前）正式引見，引……朝見；<史>（聖職等的）推薦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Presentation</b> is the appearance of something, that someone has worked to create. 外觀","examples":["We serve traditional French food cooked in a lighter way, keeping the presentation simple. 我們提供傳統法國美食，風味清淡，外觀簡潔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>presentation</b> is a formal event at which someone is given a prize or award. 頒獎儀式","examples":["...after receiving his award at a presentation in Kansas City yesterday. …昨天在堪薩斯城的一個頒獎儀式上接受了他的獎項之後。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone gives a <b>presentation</b>, they give a formal talk, often in order to sell something or get support for a proposal. 講座","examples":["James Watson, Philip Mayo and I gave a slide and video presentation. 詹姆斯·沃森、菲利普·梅奧和我一起做了一場有幻燈和錄影片的講座。"]}]}]},"privilege":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特權，特殊待遇；榮幸，光榮；（富人或上層階級的）權勢；（律師、醫生及其他專業人士的）保密權；言行免責權（尤指議員的權利）；<史>（授予個人，公司，某地的）特許經營權；（生活）優越"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 給予特權，特別優待；特免，免除（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>privilege</b> is a special right or advantage that only one person or group has. (某人、某團體擁有的) 特權","examples":["The Russian Federation has issued a decree abolishing special privileges for government officials. 俄羅斯聯邦已頒佈了一條取消政府官員特權的法令。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about <b>privilege</b>, you are talking about the power and advantage that only a small group of people have, usually because of their wealth or their connections with powerful people. (一小部分人因其財富或與有權人的關係而擁有的) 特權","examples":["Pironi was the son of privilege and wealth, and it showed. 皮羅尼是富貴人家的子弟，這一點明擺著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>privilege</b> in expressions such as <b>be a privilege</b> or <b>have the privilege</b> when you want to show your appreciation of someone or something, or to show your respect. 榮幸","examples":["It must be a privilege to know such a man. 認識這樣一個人必是一種榮幸。"]}]}]},"procedure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手續，步驟；（商業、法律或政治上的）程式；外科手術；（電腦的）應用程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>procedure</b> is a way of doing something, especially the usual or correct way. 程式","examples":["A biopsy is usually a minor surgical procedure. 活組織切除通常是一個較小的外科手術。","Police insist that Michael did not follow the correct procedure in applying for a visa. 警方堅持認為邁克爾沒有按正確的程式申請簽證。"]}]}]},"profession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指需要長期訓練和正規資格的）職業；（某）職業界同行，同業；（統稱，指需要較高教育水平的）職業（the professions）；（信念、觀點或感情的）公開表示，表白；入教誓言，修道誓約；入教儀式，入教"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>profession</b> is a type of job that requires advanced education or training. 職業","examples":["Harper was a teacher by profession. 哈珀的職業是教師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>profession</b> to refer to all the people who have the same profession. 同業的全體人員","examples":["The attitude of the medical profession is very much more liberal now. 醫學人士的態度如今開放多了。"]}]}]},"professor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教授；<美>（大學的）講師，教員；信仰表示者，宣稱信仰者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>professor</b> in an American or Canadian university or college is a teacher of the highest rank. (美國大學的) 教授","examples":["Robert Dunn is a professor of economics at George Washington University. 羅伯特·鄧恩是喬治·華盛頓大學的經濟學教授。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>professor</b> in a British university is the most senior teacher in a department. (英國大學的) 系主任","examples":["...Professor Cameron. …卡梅倫主任。"]}]}]},"prime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要的，首要的；優質的，第一流的；最可能的，最適合的；最理想的，最典型的；最初的，原始的；素（或質）數的（如2，3，5，7，11）；互為素或質數的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"事先指點，使（某人）做好準備；把（某事物）準備好，使備用；給（表面）塗上底色"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"盛年，壯年時期；質數，素數；上標符號（'），（數字後）分鐘（或英尺）符號；（八個防禦姿勢的）第一姿勢；（腳踏車比賽中設特別獎的）特設行程；<古>起始，原初；晨經，晨禱（傳統上於白天中的第一個小時即早晨六點所做的祈禱，現罕用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>prime</b> to describe something that is most important in a situation. 主要的","examples":["Political stability, meanwhile, will be a prime concern. 與此同時，政治穩定將是頭等大事。","It could be a prime target for guerrilla attack. 它會是游擊隊進攻的一個主要目標。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>prime</b> to describe something that is of the best possible quality. 最佳的","examples":["The location of these beaches makes them prime sites for development. 這些海灘的位置使它們成為開發的最佳選址。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>prime</b> to describe an example of a particular kind of thing that is absolutely typical. 最典型的","examples":["The prime example is Macy's, once the undisputed king of California retailers. 最典型的例子是梅西百貨，曾是加州零售商們公認的王者。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in</b> their <b>prime</b>, they are at the stage in their existence when they are at their strongest, most active, or most successful. 鼎盛時期","examples":["Maybe I'm just coming into my prime now. 可能我剛邁入我的最佳時期。","We've had a series of athletes trying to come back well past their prime. 我們有不少早已過了鼎盛時期的運動員在試圖復出。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prime</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you prepare them to do it, for example, by giving them information about it beforehand. 事先交代 (某人做某事)","examples":["Claire wished she'd primed Sarah beforehand. 克萊爾希望她事先交代過薩拉。","Marianne had not known until Arnold primed her for her duties that she was to be the sole female. 直到阿諾德向她交待她的職責時，瑪麗安娜才知道她將是惟一的女性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>primes</b> <b>a bomb</b> or <b>a gun</b>, they prepare it so that it is ready to explode or fire. 事先準備 (炸彈、槍)","examples":["He was priming the bomb to go off in an hour's time. 他在事先準備炸彈在一小時後爆炸。","He kept a primed shotgun in his office. 他在辦公室放了一杆裝好子彈的散彈獵槍。"]}]}]},"production":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（以銷售為目的的）生產，製造；（對自然物的）加工，採集，生產；產量；（自然的）產生；（交通工具的）大量生產；（戲劇、電影、電視節目、唱片等的）製作；（戲劇、電影等的）上映，上演；（尤指從製作與公演等特點來看）影片，戲劇；音響效果，製作方式；<正式>出示，提供；<非正式>非常費力的事，非常複雜的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Production</b> is the process of manufacturing or growing something in large quantities. 生產","examples":["That model won't go into production before late 2007. 那種型號要到2007年底才會投入生產。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Production</b> is the amount of goods manufactured or grown by a company or country. 產量","examples":["We needed to increase the volume of production. 我們必須增加產量。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>production of</b> something is its creation as the result of a natural process. 產生; 生成","examples":["These proteins stimulate the production of blood cells. 這些蛋白質促進血細胞的生成。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Production</b> is the process of organizing and preparing a play, movie, programme, or CD, in order to present it to the public. (戲劇、電影、節目等的) 製作","examples":["She is head of the production company. 她是該製片公司的頭兒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>production</b> is a play, opera, or other show that is performed in a theatre. 演出","examples":["...a critically acclaimed production of Othello. …一場受到評論界好評的《奧賽羅》的演出。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you can do something <b>on production of</b> or <b>on the production of</b> documents, you need to show someone those documents in order to be able to do that thing. 憑某物的出示","examples":["Entry to the show is free to members on production of their membership cards. 該演出會員憑其會員證的出示免費入場。"]}]}]},"pronoun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pronoun</b> is a word that you use to refer to someone or something when you do not need to use a noun, often because the person or thing has been mentioned earlier. Examples are \"it,\" \"she,\" \"something,\" and \"myself.\" 代詞","examples":[]}]}]},"promotion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"提拔，晉升；促銷，推銷； 促進，提倡；（體育運動隊的）晉級，升級；（為獲利而舉辦的）體育賽事（尤指系列拳擊賽）；（化學）助催化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are given <b>promotion</b> or <b>a promotion</b> in your job, you are given a more important job or rank in the organization that you work for. 晉升","examples":["Consider changing jobs or trying for promotion. 考慮換工作或者爭取晉升。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>promotion</b> is an attempt to make a product or event popular or successful, especially by advertising. 促銷; 推廣","examples":["Advertising and promotion are what American business does best. 打廣告和促銷是美國企業做得最好的事情。"]}]}]},"professional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"職業的，專業的；非常內行的，極為稱職的；（人）職業性的，非業餘的；由職業人員參加的；<非正式，貶>（人）堅持某種活動特徵（或特點）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"專業人員，專業人士；內行，專家；職業選手；（受僱於高爾夫或網球協會的）職業教練"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> means relating to a person's work, especially work that requires special training. 有關職業的","examples":["His professional career started at Colgate University. 他的職業生涯始於科爾蓋特大學。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> people have jobs that require advanced education or training. 專業的 (人士)","examples":["...highly qualified professional people like doctors and engineers. …像醫生和工程師這樣高資歷的專業人士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>professional</b> to describe people who do a particular thing to earn money rather than as a hobby. 職業的 (運動員等)","examples":["This has been my worst time for injuries since I started as a professional player. 這是我成為職業球員以來受傷最嚴重的一次。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> sports are played for money rather than as a hobby. 職業的 (運動等)","examples":["...an art student who had played professional football for a short time. …曾短期踢過職業足球的藝術生。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say something that someone does or produces is <b>professional</b>, you approve of it because you think that it is of a very high standard. 專業水準的","examples":["They run it with a truly professional but personal touch. 他們以真正專業而個性化的方式經營它。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"職業上地","examples":["...a professionally-qualified architect. …一名職業上合格的建築師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"作為職業地","examples":["By age 16 he was playing professionally with bands in Greenwich Village. 到16歲時，他已在與格林尼治村的各樂隊進行職業演出了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有專業水準地","examples":["These tickets have been produced very professionally. 這些標籤製作得很專業。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> is also a noun. 專業人士","examples":["My father wanted me to become a professional and have more stability. 我父親希望我成為一名專業人士，有更多穩定性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> is also a noun. 職業人士","examples":["He had been a professional since March 1985. 他自1985年3月以來一直是一名職業人士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Professional</b> is also a noun. 有專業水準的人","examples":["...a dedicated professional who worked harmoniously with the cast and crew. …一位和全體演職人員合作融洽、敬業、有專業水準的人。"]}]}]},"pronunciation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發音方法，讀法；（某人的）發音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>pronunciation</b> of a word or language is the way it is pronounced. 發音","examples":["She gave the word its French pronunciation. 她給出了這個單詞的法語發音。"]}]}]},"prosperity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繁榮，成功"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prosperity</b> is a condition in which a person or community is doing well financially. 繁榮","examples":["...a new era of peace and prosperity. …一個和平與繁榮的新時代。"]}]}]},"psychologist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心理學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>psychologist</b> is a person who studies the human mind and tries to explain why people behave in the way that they do. 心理學家","examples":[]}]}]},"proverb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"諺語，格言；典型，模範"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用諺語表達"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>proverb</b> is a short sentence that people often quote, because it gives advice or tells you something about life. 諺語","examples":["An old Arab proverb says, \"The enemy of my enemy is my friend.\" 有一句古老的阿拉伯諺語說：“我敵人的敵人是我的朋友。”"]}]}]},"prompt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"促使，導致；鼓勵，提示（說話者）；（計算機上）提示；（給演員）提詞，提白"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（給演員的）提詞；（計算機螢幕上顯示準備接受指令的）提示； 鼓勵，催促；（付款通知單上的）付款期限"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"迅速的，立刻的；（人）利索的，敏捷的；及時的，準時的；（商品）即期要送的，即期要付的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"準時地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>prompt</b> someone <b>to</b> do something means to make them decide to do it. 促使","examples":["Japan's recession has prompted consumers to cut back on buying cars. 日本的經濟衰退已促使消費者們削減購車花銷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>prompt</b> someone when they stop speaking, you encourage or help them to continue. If you <b>prompt</b> an actor, you tell them what their next line is when they have forgotten what comes next. 提示; 給 (演員) 提示詞","examples":["\"You wouldn't have wanted to bring those people to justice anyway, would you?\" Brand prompted him. “你本不想將那些人繩之以法的，是吧？”布蘭德提示他說。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prompt</b> action is done without any delay. 立即的 (行動)","examples":["It is not too late, but prompt action is needed. 還不太晚，但需要立即行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>prompt</b> to do something, you do it without delay or you are not late. (做某事) 迅速的","examples":["You have been so prompt in carrying out all these commissions. 你執行所有這些任務非常迅速。"]}]}]},"protein":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛋白質，朊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"蛋白質的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Protein</b> is a substance found in food and drink such as meat, eggs, and milk. You need protein in order to grow and be healthy. 蛋白質","examples":["Fish was a major source of protein for the working man. 魚曾是勞動者獲取蛋白質的主要來源。"]}]}]},"publisher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出版者，出版商，出版社；發行人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>publisher</b> is a person or a company that publishes books, newspapers, or magazines. 出版者; 出版公司","examples":["The publishers planned to produce the journal on a weekly basis. 出版社計劃將這份雜誌做成周刊。"]}]}]},"psychology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心理學；心理特點，心理狀態；心理影響；心計，善解人意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Psychology</b> is the scientific study of the human mind and the reasons for people's behaviour. 心理學","examples":["...Professor of Psychology at Haverford College. …海沃福德學院的心理學教授。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>psychology</b> <b>of</b> a person is the kind of mind that they have, which makes them think or behave in the way that they do. 心理","examples":["...a fascination with the psychology of murderers. …對謀殺犯心理的強烈興趣。"]}]}]},"publicity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（媒體的）關注，報道；宣傳， 推廣；宣傳業，廣告行業；宣傳品，廣告；引起公眾關注的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Publicity</b> is information or actions that are intended to attract the public's attention to someone or something. 宣傳","examples":["Much advance publicity was given to the talks. 會談之前做了大量的宣傳。","...government publicity campaigns. …政府的宣傳活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the news media and the public show a lot of interest in something, you can say that it is receiving <b>publicity</b>. 公眾的關注","examples":["The case has generated enormous publicity in Brazil. 這起犯罪事件已在巴西引起了公眾的極大關注。"]}]}]},"publication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出版，發行；出版物，發行物；（資訊的） 刊登，公佈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>publication</b> of a book or magazine is the act of printing it and sending it to stores to be sold. 出版","examples":["The guide is being translated into several languages for publication near Christmas. 這本指南正被翻譯成好幾種語言，準備在聖誕節前後出版。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>publication</b> is a book or magazine that has been published. 出版物","examples":["They have started legal proceedings against two publications which spoke of an affair. 他們已開始對提及一件緋聞的兩本出版物進行法律訴訟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>publication of</b> something such as information is the act of making it known to the public, for example, by informing journalists or by publishing a government document. 公開","examples":["A spokesman said: \"We have no comment regarding the publication of these photographs.\" 一位發言人說: “關於這些照片的公開，我們無可奉告。”"]}]}]},"protest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抗議，反對；抗議活動；宣告，斷言；<法律>（多指來自公證人的）拒付證書"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（公開）反對，抗議；堅決表示，嚴正申明；<法律> 宣告拒付（賬單），拒付"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>protest</b> something or <b>protest</b> <b>against</b> something, you say or show publicly that you object to it. 抗議","examples":["They were protesting soaring prices. 他們在抗議不斷飛漲的物價。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>protest</b> that something is the case, you insist that it is the case, when other people think that it may not be. 斷言","examples":["When we tried to protest that Mo was beaten up they didn't believe us. 當我們堅持說莫遭到了毒打時，他們都不相信。","\"I never said any of that to her,\" he protested. “我從來沒有對她說過那種話，”他斷然否認。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>protest</b> is the act of saying or showing publicly that you object to something. 抗議","examples":["The opposition now seems too weak to stage any serious protests against the government. 反對黨現在似乎太弱小，無力針對政府組織什麼重大的抗議。","The Mexican president cancelled a trip to Texas in protest at the state's execution of a Mexican national. 墨西哥總統取消了得克薩斯之行，以抗議該州對一名墨西哥僑民的處決。"]}]}]},"quilt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"被子，被褥；<英>羽絨被（=duvet）；編織床罩；絕緣層，絕緣墊；被狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"縫被子；（為縫製床罩、保暖衣，或為裝飾效果而）將（幾層織物或襯料）按線條圖案縫合；<澳，非正式>猛擊（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quilt</b> is a bed cover made by sewing layers of cloth together, usually with different colours sewn together to make a design. 被子","examples":["...an old patchwork quilt. …一條舊的拼布被子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A\n<b>\nquilt\n</b>\nis a thin cover filled with feathers or some other warm, soft material, which you put over your blankets when you are in bed.\n 羽絨床罩","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>quilt</b>, or if you <b>quilt</b> a piece of fabric, you make a quilt. 縫製 (被子); 縫製被子","examples":["Maggie knows how to quilt. 瑪吉知道怎樣縫被子。","Quilting a bed cover can be laborious. 縫製一個床罩會很費力的。"]}]}]},"quake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因恐懼、氣憤等）發抖，顫抖；（建築物等）震動，搖晃"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"地震；顫抖，搖晃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quake</b> is the same as an . 地震","examples":["The quake destroyed mud buildings in many remote villages. 地震摧毀了許多偏遠村莊的泥土房屋。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>quake</b>, you shake, usually because you are very afraid. (常指因害怕而) 發抖","examples":["I just stood there quaking with fear. 我站在那兒，嚇得發抖。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are quaking in</b> your <b>boots</b> or <b>quaking in</b> your <b>shoes</b>, you feel very nervous or afraid, and may be feeling slightly weak as a result. (因緊張、害怕而) 發抖","examples":["If you stand up straight, you'll give an impression of self-confidence, even if you're quaking in your boots. 只要你站直了，就會給人一種自信的印象，哪怕你正緊張得發抖。"]}]}]},"rainfall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"降雨；降雨量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rainfall</b> is the amount of rain that falls in a place during a particular period. 降雨量","examples":["There have been four years of below average rainfall. 已經有4年降雨量低於平均水平了。"]}]}]},"pursuit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"追求，尋找；繼續；追逐，追捕；實行，貫徹；消遣，業餘愛好；（腳踏車賽和滑冰競賽中的）追逐賽；（生理學）追視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>pursuit of</b> something is your attempts at achieving it. If you do something <b>in pursuit of</b> a particular result, you do it in order to achieve that result. 追求","examples":["...a young man whose relentless pursuit of excellence is conducted with single-minded determination. …一個一心一意不斷追求卓越的年輕男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>pursuit of</b> an activity, interest, or plan consists of all the things that you do when you are carrying it out. 執行","examples":["The vigorous pursuit of policies is no guarantee of success. 政策的嚴格執行並非成功的保障。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>in pursuit of</b> a person, vehicle, or animal is chasing them. 追趕","examples":["...a police officer who drove a patrol car at more than 120 mph in pursuit of a motorcycle. …一位開著巡邏車以120英里以上的時速追趕一輛摩托車的警官。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>pursuits</b> are your activities, usually activities that you enjoy when you are not working. 消遣活動","examples":["They both love outdoor pursuits. 他們倆都喜歡戶外活動。"]}]}]},"quotation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"引語，引文；音樂（或藝術品）片段的引用；引用，引述；報價單，估價；（股票）報價，牌價；（股票）上市許可登記"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quotation</b> is a sentence or phrase taken from a book, poem, speech, or play, which is repeated by someone else. 引文; 引語","examples":["He illustrated his argument with quotations from Martin Luther King Jr. 他引用小馬丁·路德·金的話闡述了自己的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone gives you a <b>quotation</b>, they tell you how much they will charge to do a particular piece of work. 報價","examples":["Get several written quotations and check exactly what's included in the cost. 弄幾份書面報價來，並查清楚成本中包含哪些內容。"]}]}]},"rage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盛怒，狂怒；粗暴的舉動，憤怒的行為；（喻）（自然事物的）狂暴，兇猛；<非正式>風靡一時，非常流行；強烈的慾望，激情；<文>（尤指預示的、詩意的或武力的）狂熱；<澳新，非正式> 歡樂聚會，熱鬧的活動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發脾氣，大怒；（戰鬥、爭論）激烈進行，（暴風雨）肆虐；（火災、疾病）迅速蔓延，快速擴散；（感情）強烈表現，變得強烈；<澳新，非正式>狂歡，出去作樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rage</b> is strong anger that is difficult to control. 盛怒","examples":["He was red-cheeked with rage. 他因盛怒而滿臉通紅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the strong anger that someone feels in a particular situation as a particular <b>rage</b>, especially when this results in violent or aggressive behaviour. (尤指導致暴力或侵略性行為的) 狂怒","examples":["Cabin crews are reporting up to nine cases of air rage a week. 乘務人員們報告每週有多達9起的乘客情緒失控事件。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that something powerful or unpleasant <b>rages</b> when it continues with great force or violence. 肆虐","examples":["Train service was halted as the fire raged for more than four hours. 火車停運了，因為大火肆虐了四個多小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rage</b> about something, you speak or think very angrily about it. 發怒; 怒斥","examples":["Monroe was on the phone, raging about her mistreatment by the brothers. 門羅正在打電話，憤怒地訴說兄弟們對她的虐待。","Inside, Frannie was raging. 內心裡，弗蘭尼怒不可遏。"]}]}]},"reception":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接待處，服務檯；歡迎會，招待會；歡迎，反響；（收音機或電視訊號）接收效果，接收質量；接收，接待；（美橄）接球；<英>（幼兒學校的）小班，學前班"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reception</b> is a formal party which is given to welcome someone or to celebrate a special event. 招待會","examples":["At the reception they served smoked salmon. 在招待會上，他們端上了燻三文魚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Reception</b> in a hotel is the desk or office that books rooms for people and answers their questions. (酒店) 接待處; 服務檯","examples":["Have him bring a car around to reception. 讓他開輛車到接待處附近來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Reception</b> in an office or hospital is the place where people's appointments and questions are dealt with. (辦公室或醫院的) 服務檯","examples":["Wait at reception for me. 在服務檯等我。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something has a particular kind of <b>reception</b>, that is the way that people react to them. 接待","examples":["Mr. Mandela was given a warm reception in Washington. 曼德拉先生在華盛頓受到了熱情接待。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you get good <b>reception</b> from your radio or television, the sound or picture is clear because the signal is strong. If the <b>reception</b> is poor, the sound or picture is unclear because the signal is weak. (收音機或電視機的) 接收效果","examples":["...poor radio reception. …糟糕的廣播接收效果。"]}]}]},"rebel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"造反者，反抗者；反抗權威者；叛逆者，不守規矩者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"反叛，造反；違抗，不服從（權威）；反對，反抗（規定、行為規範等）；（胃、腿、頭腦等）不聽使喚"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"造反的；反抗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rebels</b> are people who are fighting against their own country's army in order to change the political system there. 反叛者","examples":["...fighting between rebels and government forces. …叛軍與政府軍之間的戰鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Politicians who oppose some of their own party's policies can be referred to as <b>rebels</b>. (政黨內部的) 反對者","examples":["The rebels want another 1% cut in interest rates. 反對派希望能再降低1%的利率。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that someone is a <b>rebel</b> if you think that they behave differently from other people and have rejected the values of society or of their parents. 叛逆者","examples":["She had been a rebel at school. 她在學校時就是個叛逆者。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If politicians <b>rebel</b> against one of their own party's policies, they show that they oppose it. (因不同政見) 反對","examples":["Voters rebelled against high property taxes. 投票者們反對高額財產稅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>rebels</b>, they start to behave differently from other people and reject the values of society or of their parents. 叛逆","examples":["The child who rebels is unlikely to be overlooked. 叛逆的孩子不太可能被忽視。"]}]}]},"recipe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烹飪法，食譜；訣竅，秘訣；原因；<古>處方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>recipe</b> is a list of ingredients and a set of instructions that tell you how to cook something. 食譜","examples":["...a traditional recipe for buttermilk biscuits. …一個酪乳餅乾的傳統烹飪法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a recipe for</b> a particular situation, you mean that it is likely to result in that situation. 方法","examples":["Large-scale inflation is a recipe for disaster. 大規模的通貨膨脹有可能導致災難。"]}]}]},"recreation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"娛樂（活動），消遣（活動）；重現，重建"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Recreation</b> consists of things that you do in your spare time to relax. 娛樂","examples":["Saturday afternoon is for recreation and outings. 週六下午是娛樂和外出的時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>recreation</b> <b>of</b> something is the process of making it exist or seem to exist again in a different time or place. 重現; 重建","examples":["They are planning to build a faithful recreation of the original frontier town. 他們正計劃建造一座和原來邊境城鎮一模一樣的複製品。"]}]}]},"recall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"記起，回想起；使想起，使想到；召回，叫回（某人）；召回（運動員），使歸隊； 收回（有問題的產品）；檢索，呼叫（計算機儲存的資料）；<美> 罷免；使重新集中注意力；<古> 撤銷，廢止（行動，決定）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"記憶力，記性；召回；（因產品有問題的）收回；（將運動員的）召回歸隊；<美>（請願後經投票對政府官員的）罷免；回索率，檢索率；撤銷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>recall</b> something, you remember it and tell others about it. 記起; 回憶道","examples":["Henderson recalled that he first met Pollard during a business trip to Washington. 亨德森記起他是在一次去華盛頓出差的途中第一次與波拉德結識的。","His mother later recalled: \"He used to stay up until two o'clock in the morning playing these war games.\" 他的母親後來回憶道：“他過去常常熬夜到凌晨2點玩這些打仗的遊戲。”","\"What was his name?\"—\"I don't recall.\" “他叫什麼名字？”—“我想不起來了。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are</b> <b>recalled</b> to your home, country, or the place where you work, you are ordered to return there. 召回 (某人)","examples":["The U. S. envoy was recalled to Washington. 該美國特使被召回了華盛頓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a company <b>recalls</b> a product, it asks the stores or the people who have bought that product to return it because there is something wrong with it. 召回 (產品)","examples":["The company said it was recalling one of its drugs and had stopped selling two others. 該公司說它正在召回它的一種藥品，而且已經停售了另外兩種藥品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Recall</b> is the ability to remember something that has happened in the past or the act of remembering it. 記憶力; 回憶","examples":["He had a good memory, and total recall of her spoken words. 他有好記性，能完全回憶出她說過的話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Recall</b> is also a noun. 召回","examples":["The recall of Ambassador Alan Green is a public signal of America's concern. 艾倫·格林大使的召回是美國關注此事的公開訊號。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Recall</b> is also a noun. 召回","examples":["...a recall of the laptops due to defective supply parts. …因為有缺陷的配件而對膝上型電腦的召回。"]}]}]},"recovery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"康復，痊癒；戒除；恢復，復甦；（供剛做完手術的病人使用的）監護室；（被拿走或失去的東西的）復得，找回；收回的物品（資金）；（破損車輛或墜毀飛機）回收修理；（高爾夫）挽回敗局之擊，復原之擊（擊回球道或球穴區）；（美橄）重新獲球；（划船，腳踏車賽，游泳）還原至預備姿勢（如回槳等）；回收利用（能源、化工品等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a sick person makes a <b>recovery</b>, he or she becomes well again. 痊癒","examples":["He made a remarkable recovery from a shin injury. 他脛骨傷恢復得相當好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When there is a <b>recovery</b> in a country's economy, it improves. 好轉; 復甦","examples":["Interest-rate cuts have failed to bring about economic recovery. 利率的降低未能帶來經濟的復甦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You talk about the <b>recovery</b> <b>of</b> something when you get it back after it has been lost or stolen. 失而復得","examples":["A substantial reward is being offered for the recovery of a painting by Turner. 一筆鉅額懸賞正被用來找回特納的一幅油畫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You talk about the <b>recovery</b> <b>of</b> someone's physical or mental state when they return to this state. 復原; 恢復","examples":["...the abrupt loss and recovery of consciousness. …意識的突然失去和恢復。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>in recovery</b>, they are being given a course of treatment to help them recover from something such as a drug habit or mental illness. 在恢復中","examples":["...Carole, a compulsive pot smoker and alcoholic in recovery. …卡蘿爾，一名正在恢復的吸食大麻成癮者和酗酒者。"]}]}]},"reduction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"減小，降低；減價，折扣；（照片、地圖、圖片等的）縮圖，縮版；歸納，簡化；（數學）歸約，約化；染色體減半；簡編曲（管絃樂改編的鋼琴曲或小樂隊演奏曲）；濃湯，濃汁；脫臼（或斷骨）復位；（化學）還原，被還原；（語音）弱化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is a <b>reduction</b> <b>in</b> something, it is made smaller. 縮減","examples":["...a future reduction in interest rates. …一次未來利率的降低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Reduction</b> is the act of making something smaller in size or amount, or less in degree. (尺寸、數量或程度上的) 削減","examples":["...a new strategic arms reduction agreement. …一項新的戰略武器削減協議。"]}]}]},"recognition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"承認，接受；表彰，讚譽；認出，識別；（政府對他國的）外交認可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Recognition</b> is the act of recognizing someone or identifying something when you see it. 認出; 識別","examples":["He searched for a sign of recognition on her face, but there was none. 他在她的臉上搜尋她認出來的跡象，但沒有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Recognition</b> <b>of</b> something is an understanding and acceptance of it. 認可; 接受","examples":["Recognition of the importance of career development is increasing. 對職業發展重要性的認可在不斷增加。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a government gives diplomatic <b>recognition</b> to another country, they officially accept that its status is valid. (國際上的) 正式承認","examples":["His government did not receive full recognition by the United States until July. 他的政府直到7月才得到美國的完全承認。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a person receives <b>recognition</b> for the things that they have done, people acknowledge the value or skill of their work. 讚賞; 賞識","examples":["At last, her father's work has received popular recognition. 最終，她父親的工作得到了大家的普遍讚賞。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>in recognition of</b> someone's achievements, it is done as a way of showing official appreciation of them. 用以肯定","examples":["...a small plaque in recognition of her contribution to the university. …一枚用以肯定她對該大學所做貢獻的獎章。"]}]}]},"refugee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"難民，避難者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Refugees</b> are people who have been forced to leave their homes or their country, either because there is a war there, because of their political or religious beliefs, or because of natural disaster. 難民","examples":["A political refugee from Cameroon has moved into our neighbourhood. 一個喀麥隆的政治難民已經搬進了我們小區。"]}]}]},"refusal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拒絕，回絕；拒絕接受，拒絕給予；優先取捨權，優先購買權（first refusal）；選擇權；（馬）（對障礙物的）拒跳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>refusal</b> <b>to</b> do something is the fact of them showing or saying that they will not do it, allow it, or accept it. 拒絕","examples":["Her country suffered through her refusal to accept change. 她的國家因為她拒絕接受變革而受了害。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>first refusal</b> on something that is being sold or offered, they have the right to decide whether or not to buy it or take it before it is offered to anyone else. 優先購買權","examples":["A tenant may have a right of first refusal if a property is offered for sale. 如果房產要出售，房客可以有優先購買權。"]}]}]},"reflection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（光、熱或聲音的）反射；反射光，反射熱，回聲；（反射出來的）影像，倒影；深思，反省；（尤指見諸語言的）想法，意見；表現，反映；壞的印象；（數）鏡射，反射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reflection</b> is an image that you can see in a mirror or in glass or water. 影像; 映像","examples":["Meg stared at her reflection in the bedroom mirror. 梅格端詳著自己映在臥室鏡子中的影像。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Reflection</b> is the process by which light and heat are sent back from a surface and do not pass through it. 反射","examples":["...the reflection of a beam of light off a mirror. …一束光線在鏡面上的反射。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>reflection</b> <b>of</b> a particular person's attitude or <b>of</b> a situation, you mean that it is caused by that attitude or situation and therefore reveals something about it. 反映","examples":["Inhibition in adulthood seems to be a reflection of a person's experiences as a child. 成年期的壓抑似乎是一個人童年經歷的一種反映。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is a <b>reflection</b> or a <b>sad reflection</b> <b>on</b> a person or thing, it gives a bad impression of them. 壞的影響","examples":["Infection with head lice is no reflection on personal hygiene. 染上頭蝨並不會給個人衛生帶來不好的影響。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Reflection</b> is careful thought about a particular subject. Your <b>reflections</b> are your thoughts about a particular subject. 認真思考","examples":["After days of reflection she decided to write back. 經過幾天的認真思考，她決定回信。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone admits or accepts something <b>on reflection</b>, they admit or accept it after having thought carefully about it. 經過認真思考","examples":["While the news at first shocked me, on reflection it made perfect sense. 雖然一開始這個訊息令我震驚，但經過認真思考，覺得它也很有道理。"]}]}]},"rejection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對提議、建議或請求的）拒絕接受；（對求職者、求學等者的）拒絕；拒聘函，拒絕錄取函；嫌棄，厭棄；（對移植器官的）排斥；被拋棄的東西"}],"sections":[]},"registration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"登記，註冊，掛號；登記證，註冊證；<英>（汽車）牌照號碼（=registration number）；<英> （教師對上課學生的）點名；（管風琴）音栓配合（法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>registration</b> of something such as a person's name or the details of an event is the recording of it in an official list. 登記; 註冊","examples":["They have campaigned strongly for compulsory registration of dogs. 他們大力開展了狗的強制性登記活動。","With the high voter registration, many will be voting for the first time. 由於高的投票者登記率，很多人將是第一次投票。"]}]}]},"reform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"改革，革新；改邪歸正，改造；（石油煉製）重整"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"改革，改良"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"猶太教改革（僅保留猶太教部分的傳統信條和習俗）（Reform）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reform</b> consists of changes and improvements to a law, social system, or institution. A <b>reform</b> is an instance of such a change or improvement. 改革; 改良","examples":["The party embarked on a programme of economic reform. 這個政黨開始了一個經濟改革的計劃。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>reforms</b> something such as a law, social system, or institution, they change or improve it. 改革; 改良","examples":["...his plans to reform the country's economy. …他改革國家經濟的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>reforms</b> or when something <b>reforms</b> them, they stop doing things that society does not approve of, such as breaking the law or drinking too much alcohol. 改造; 改過自新","examples":["When his court case was coming up, James promised to reform. 當他的案件即將被審理時，詹姆斯承諾要改過自新。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"改過自新的","examples":["...a reformed alcoholic. …一個改過自新的酗酒者。"]}]}]},"regulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"規章制度，規則；（運用規則條例的）管理，控制"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（使用或穿戴）符合規定的，正規的；<非正式> 公式化的，用俗套話堆砌而成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Regulations</b> are rules made by a government or other authority in order to control the way something is done or the way people behave. 法規; 條例","examples":["The European Union has proposed new regulations to control the hours worked by its employees. 歐盟已經提出了新的法規來控制其僱員的工作時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Regulation</b> is the controlling of an activity or process, usually by means of rules. 管理","examples":["Some in the market now want government regulation in order to reduce costs. 市場上現在有人想要政府來管理以降低成本。"]}]}]},"relaxation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"休息，消遣；休閒活動，娛樂活動；（肌肉等的）鬆弛，放鬆；（規則或限制的）放寬；（物理）弛豫，重新平衡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Relaxation</b> is a way of spending time in which you rest and feel comfortable. 休息","examples":["You should be able to find the odd moment for relaxation. 你應該能找到零碎的休息時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is <b>relaxation</b> of a rule or control, it is made less firm or strong. (規定或控制的) 放鬆","examples":["The relaxation of travel restrictions means they are free to travel and work. 旅遊限制的放鬆意味著他們可以自由地旅遊和工作。"]}]}]},"remark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"言論，評述；（正式演講時的）言論（remarks）；<正式> 引人注目，顯耀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"談論，說起；注意到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>remark</b> that something is the case, you say that it is the case. 說; 評論","examples":["I remarked that I would go shopping that afternoon. 我說過那天下午我要去買東西。","On several occasions she had remarked on the boy's improvement. 有幾次她說起過那個男孩的進步。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>remark</b> about something, you say something about it. 議論; 評論","examples":["She has made outspoken remarks about the legalization of marijuana. 她直言不諱地評論過大麻合法化問題。"]}]}]},"reference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"提及，談到；參考，查閱；（引自書或詩歌的）引言，引文；引文的作者，參考書目；（幫助或意見的）徵求，徵詢； (為方便查詢所用的）標記，編號；推薦信，介紹信；介紹人，推薦人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"參考的，用於查閱的；文獻索引的，參照的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"列出……的參考書目；提及，提到；引用，參照（某書或某作者）"}],"sections":[]},"relative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"親戚，親屬；同類事物，親緣動物（或植物）；（語法）關係代詞，關係限定詞，關係副詞；（哲學）關係項；相關物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相比較而言的，比較的；相對的，相關聯的；（語法）（代詞、限定詞或副詞）關係的，（從句）由關係詞引導的；（樂）（大小調）調號相同的；（與不同軍種的軍階）相應（或對應）的；<正式> 關於（或涉及到）......的；相比之下存在（或有）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>relatives</b> are the members of your family. 親屬","examples":["Get a relative to look after the children. 找個親戚來照看這些孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one animal, plant, language, or invention is a <b>relative</b> <b>of</b> another, they have both developed from the same type of animal, plant, language, or invention. 親緣物種; 同源事物","examples":["The pheasant is a close relative of the guinea hen. 這種雉雞和這種珍珠雞是親緣物種。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>relative</b> to say that something is true to a certain degree, especially when compared with other things of the same kind. 相對的","examples":["The fighting resumed after a period of relative calm. 戰鬥在一段相對的平靜之後重新開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>relative</b> when you are comparing the quality or size of two things. 比較而言的","examples":["They chatted about the relative merits of London and Paris as places to live. 他們閒聊倫敦與巴黎作為居住地各自相對的優點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>relative</b>, you mean that it needs to be considered and judged in relation to other things. 相對的","examples":["Fitness is relative; one must always ask \"Fit for what?\" 適宜是相對的；始終必須問問：“適宜什麼？”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Relative to</b> something means with reference to it or in comparison with it. 與…相比","examples":["Japanese interest rates rose relative to America's. 日本的利率與美國相比有所上升。"]}]}]},"repetition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重複，重說，重做； 重做的事，重說的話；重複的事物，複製品；（樂）（章節或音節的）反覆；<古>教師指定的背誦材料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>repetition</b> <b>of</b> an event, usually an undesirable event, it happens again. (尤指令人不快的事情) 重演","examples":["Today the city government has taken measures to prevent a repetition of last year's confrontation. 今天市政府已經採取了措施來防止去年的衝突重演。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Repetition</b> means using the same words again. 重複的語句","examples":["He could also have cut out much of the repetition and thus saved many pages. 他本來也可以刪掉很多重複的語句，省去很多頁數。"]}]}]},"remedy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解決方法，糾正方法；法定補償（辦法）；治療（法），藥品；（硬幣的）公差"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"補救，糾正；治療"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>remedy</b> is a successful way of dealing with a problem. 解決辦法","examples":["The remedy lies in the hands of the government. 解決辦法就在政府手中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>remedy</b> is something that is intended to cure you when you are ill or in pain. 治療; 療法; 藥品","examples":["There are many different kinds of natural remedies to help overcome winter infections. 很多不同種類的天然藥物有助於克服冬季傳染病。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>remedy</b> something that is wrong or harmful, you correct it or improve it. 補救; 糾正; 改善","examples":["A great deal has been done internally to remedy the situation. 內部已經採取了很多措施來挽救局面。"]}]}]},"register":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"登記表，註冊簿；註冊員；（人或樂器的）聲區，音區；（適合特定場合使用的）語體風格，語域；（印刷，攝影）套準，疊合；<美>現金出納機；（電子裝置的）暫存器；<美>（供暖或製冷裝置的）調風口，節氣門；（設計圖案組成的）條，區域性"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"登記，註冊；（正式地或公開地）發表意見，提出主張；流露出，表達出；注意到，受到注意；（儀器上）顯出，顯示；把……掛號郵寄；取得（結果），得（分）；（印刷，攝影）套準，疊合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>register</b> is an official list or record of people or things. 登記簿","examples":["...registers of births, deaths, and marriages. …出生、死亡及結婚登記簿。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> to do something, you put your name on an official list, in order to be able to do that thing or to receive a service. 登記; 註冊","examples":["Have you come to register at the school? 你到學校來註冊過了嗎？","Thousands lined up to register to vote. 數千人排隊登記投票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> something, such as the name of a person who has just died or information about something you own, you have these facts recorded on an official list. 登記","examples":["In order to register a car in Japan, the owner must have somewhere to park it. 在日本要想登記一輛汽車，車主必須要有停車的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>registers</b> <b>on</b> a scale or measuring instrument, it shows on the scale or instrument. (在儀表上) 顯示","examples":["It will only register on sophisticated X-ray equipment. 只有在先進的X光裝置上它才會顯示出來。","The earthquake registered 5.7 on the Richter scale. 這次地震顯示為里氏5.7級。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> your feelings or opinions about something, you do something that makes them clear to other people. 表示 (感情或看法)","examples":["Voters wish to register their dissatisfaction with the ruling party. 選民們希望表達他們對執政黨的不滿。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a piece of information does not <b>register</b> or if you do not <b>register</b> it, you do not really pay attention to it, and so you do not remember it or react to it. 留意; 留下印象","examples":["It wasn't that she couldn't hear me, it was just that what I said sometimes didn't register in her brain. 並不是她聽不到我說話，而是我的話有時候沒有在她腦子裡留下印象。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a feeling <b>registers</b> <b>on</b> someone's face, their expression shows clearly that they have that feeling. (面部表情) 流露","examples":["Surprise again registered on Rodney's face. 羅德尼的臉上再次流露出驚訝的表情。"]}]}]},"representation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代理人，代表；描繪，表現；表示，象徵；表現物（尤指畫或模型）；<正式>抗議，陳述；（感知理論用語）表象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group or person has <b>representation</b> in a legislature or on a committee, someone in the legislature or on the committee supports them and makes decisions on their behalf. 代表","examples":["Puerto Ricans are U.S. citizens but they have no representation in Congress. 波多黎各人是美國公民，但是他們在國會中沒有代表。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a picture, model, or statue of a person or thing as a <b>representation</b> <b>of</b> them. 描寫; 描繪","examples":["...a lifelike representation of Christ. …對基督的生動描繪。"]}]}]},"reputation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名譽，名聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To have a <b>reputation</b> <b>for</b> something means to be known or remembered for it. 名聲","examples":["Alice Munro has a reputation for being a very depressing writer. 艾麗斯•門羅有文風抑鬱的名聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something's or someone's <b>reputation</b> is the opinion that people have about how good they are. If they have a good reputation, people think they are good. 聲譽","examples":["This college has a good academic reputation. 這所大學擁有良好的學術聲譽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you know someone <b>by reputation</b>, you have never met them but you have heard of their reputation. 久聞","examples":["She was by reputation a good organizer. 久聞她是個出色的組織者。"]}]}]},"researcher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"研究人員"}],"sections":[]},"rescue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"營救，援救；拯救，挽救（生意等）；<非正式>防止……丟失（或遭丟棄），取回"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"營救，救援；營救行動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rescue</b> someone, you get them out of a dangerous or unpleasant situation. 營救","examples":["Helicopters rescued nearly 20 people from the roof of the burning building. 直升機從著火的樓頂救出來了將近二十個人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"救援者","examples":["It took rescuers 90 minutes to reach the trapped men. 救援者們花了90分鐘才來到那些被困的男子身邊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rescue</b> is help which gets someone out of a dangerous or unpleasant situation. 營救","examples":["A big rescue operation has been launched for a trawler missing in the North Atlantic. 為了一艘在北大西洋失蹤的拖網漁船，已經開始了一項大的營救行動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rescue</b> is an attempt to save someone from a dangerous or unpleasant situation. 營救行動","examples":["A major air-sea rescue is under way. 一項重要的海空營救行動正在進行中。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>go to</b> someone's <b>rescue</b> or <b>come to</b> their <b>rescue</b>, you help them when they are in danger or difficulty. 營救某人","examples":["The 23-year-old's screams alerted a passerby who went to her rescue. 那名23歲女孩的尖叫聲引起了一個過路人的警覺，他救了她。"]}]}]},"resignation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"辭職； 辭職信，辭呈；順從，聽任；（棋）認輸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>resignation</b> is a formal statement of your intention to leave a job or position. 辭呈","examples":["Bob Morgan has offered his resignation and it has been accepted. 鮑勃•摩根已遞交了辭呈，並且已被批准了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Resignation</b> is the acceptance of an unpleasant situation or fact because you realize that you cannot change it. 無奈的順從","examples":["He sighed with profound resignation. 他極度無奈地嘆氣。"]}]}]},"research":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指大學或科研機構進行的）研究，探討；研究工作，調查工作"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"研究，探索；為……收集資料，調查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Research</b> is work that involves studying something and trying to discover facts about it. 研究","examples":["Sixty-five percent of the 1987 budget went for nuclear weapons research and production. 1987年預算的65%用在了核武器的研製上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"研究員","examples":["He chose to join the company as a market researcher. 他選擇加入這家公司當一名市場研究員。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>research</b> something, you try to discover facts about it. 研究","examples":["She spent two years in South Florida researching and filming her documentary. 她在南佛羅里達花了兩年的時間研究和拍攝紀錄片。"]}]}]},"reservation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保留，保護；（房間，座位等的）預訂；（美國印第安人的）居留地，保留地；（野生動物）保護區；<法律>（財產轉讓的）權益保留；聖餐保留（指彌撒完畢後部分聖餐留給病人或作為禮拜之用）；存疑，保留；（羅馬天主教高階聖職人員的）赦罪權的保留；（教皇的）任命權保留"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>reservations</b> <b>about</b> something, you are not sure that it is entirely good or right. 保留意見","examples":["I told him my main reservation about his film was the ending. 我告訴了他我主要對他電影的結局有所保留。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you make a <b>reservation</b>, you arrange for something such as a table in a restaurant or a room in a hotel to be kept for you. 預訂","examples":["He went to the desk to inquire and make a reservation. 他到前臺去諮詢並做了預訂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>reservation</b> is an area of land that is kept separate for a particular group of people to live in. 保留地","examples":["Seventeen thousand Indians live in Arizona on a reservation. 17000名印第安人居住在亞利桑那州的保留地內。"]}]}]},"restriction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"限制規定，限制法規；（受）限制（狀態），（受）約束（狀態）；制約因素"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>restriction</b> is an official rule that limits what you can do or that limits the amount or size of something. 限制條例","examples":["...the lifting of restrictions on political parties and the news media. …政黨和新聞媒體限制條例的取消。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to anything that limits what you can do as a <b>restriction</b>. 限制","examples":["His parents are trying to make up to him for the restrictions of urban living. 他的父母正試圖為城市生活的諸多限制而補償他。"]}]}]},"resolution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"決議，正式決定；（衝突、問題等的）解決，解決辦法；決心，決定；堅決，果斷；（電視、照相機、顯微鏡等的）清晰度，解析度；（故事中主要矛盾的）衝突解開；（樂）解決（指和聲中不協和音向協和音的進行）；（醫）（炎症或其他症狀的）消散，消退；（化）分解；（物理）（力或其他向量的）分解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>resolution</b> is a formal decision made at a meeting by means of a vote. 決議","examples":["He replied that the UN had passed two major resolutions calling for a complete withdrawal. 他回覆說聯合國已經透過要求完全撤軍的兩項重大決議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you make a <b>resolution</b>, you decide to try very hard to do something. 決心","examples":["They made a resolution to lose all the weight gained during the Christmas holidays. 他們下了一個決心要減掉聖誕節期間增加的全部體重。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Resolution</b> is determination to do something or not do something. 決心","examples":["\"I think I'll try a hypnotist,\" I said with sudden resolution. “我想我要找個催眠師試試，”我突然堅決地說。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>resolution</b> of a problem or difficulty is the final solving of it. 最終解決","examples":["...the successful resolution of a dispute involving UN inspectors in Baghdad. …對涉及聯合國駐巴格達調查員的一項爭議的成功解決。"]}]}]},"resistance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反對，抵制；抵抗，反抗；抵抗力，免疫力；阻力；電阻；（敵佔區的）秘密抵抗組織"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Resistance</b> to something such as a change or a new idea is a refusal to accept it. 抵制","examples":["The U.S. wants big cuts in European agricultural export subsidies, but this is meeting resistance. 美國想要在歐洲農業出口補貼上的大幅度削減，但這正遭遇抵制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Resistance</b> to an attack consists of fighting back against the people who have attacked you. 抵抗","examples":["A CBS correspondent in Colombo says the troops are encountering stiff resistance. 哥倫比亞廣播公司駐科倫坡的一名記者報道說，軍隊正遭遇頑強的抵抗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>resistance</b> of your body <b>to</b> germs or diseases is its power to remain unharmed or unaffected by them. 抵抗力; 免疫力","examples":["This disease is surprisingly difficult to catch, as most people have a natural resistance to it. 這種病令人驚訝的難以患上，因為大多數人對它有一種先天的免疫力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Wind or air <b>resistance</b> is a force which slows down a moving object or vehicle. 阻力","examples":["The design of the bicycle reduces the effects of wind resistance and drag. 這種腳踏車的設計減少了風阻及曳力的影響。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In electrical engineering or physics, <b>resistance</b> is the ability of a substance or an electrical circuit to stop the flow of an electrical current through it. 電阻","examples":["The salt reduces the electrical resistance of the water. 鹽使水的電阻減小。"]}]}]},"retirement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"退休，退職；退休生活，退休期間；（運動員）停止參賽，退役；（陪審團）退庭表決；退庭表決時間；引退，退隱；<古>退隱處，隱蔽處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Retirement</b> is the time when a worker retires. 退休","examples":["The proportion of the population who are over retirement age has grown tremendously in the past few years. 超過退休年齡的人口的比例在過去幾年中已急劇增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's <b>retirement</b> is the period in their life after they have retired. 退休生活","examples":["\"Growing Older\" considered the needs of the elderly for financial support during retirement. 《進入老年》考慮到了老年人在退休期間對經濟資助的需要。"]}]}]},"resolve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解決（問題或困難）；決定，下定決心；作出決議，表決；分解，轉化；（使）（症狀、病情）消散，消退；解析，解離；分析；（不協和音）轉向協和；（當遠處物體看得更清楚時）變成；（光學儀器等）分辨；辨析（圖表或光譜峰值）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>決心，堅定的信念；<美>正式決定，決議；決定要做的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>resolve</b> a problem, argument, or difficulty means to find a solution to it. 解決","examples":["We must find a way to resolve these problems before it's too late. 我們必須找到一個辦法去解決這些問題,不然就太晚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>resolve</b> <b>to</b> do something, you make a firm decision to do it. 下決心","examples":["She resolved to report the matter to the hospital's nursing supervisor. 她決心把這件事向該醫院的護士長彙報。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Resolve</b> is determination to do what you have decided to do. 決心","examples":["So you're saying this will strengthen the American public's resolve to go to war if necessary? 那麼你是說，這將會堅定美國公眾在必要時參戰的決心？"]}]}]},"reunion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（有組織的）聚會，團聚；重逢，團圓；再聯合，重新統一"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reunion</b> is a party attended by members of the same family, school, or other group who have not seen each other for a long time. (家庭、學校及其他團體成員的) 重聚會","examples":["The association holds an annual reunion. 這個協會每年舉行一次重聚會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reunion</b> is a meeting between people who have been separated for some time. 重逢","examples":["The children weren't allowed to see her for nearly a week. It was a very emotional reunion. 孩子們將近一週都沒被允許見她。這是一次非常令人激動的重逢。"]}]}]},"revision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"修改，修訂；修訂本，訂正版；複習，溫習"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To make a <b>revision</b> <b>of</b> something that is written or something that has been decided means to make changes to it in order to improve it, make it more modern, or make it more suitable for a particular purpose. 修改; 修正","examples":["The phase of writing that is actually most important is revision. 寫作中真正最重要的階段是修改。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people who are studying do <b>revision</b>, they read things again and make notes in order to prepare for an examination. 複習","examples":[]}]}]},"retreat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（軍隊）撤退；後退，離開；（水、雪或土地）範圍縮小；隱退，躲避；悔棋；改變意見，改變看法；（股價）下挫，下跌；向後傾"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"撤軍，撤兵；後退，離開；退隱處，靜居處；（主意、觀點、決定的）改變；（股票）貶值；靜修期間（或活動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>retreat</b>, you move away from something or someone. 退出; 離開","examples":["\"I've already got a job,\" I said quickly, and retreated from the room. “我已經有了工作，”我迅速說道，然後就從房間裡退了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an army <b>retreats</b>, it moves away from enemy forces in order to avoid fighting them. 撤退","examples":["The French, suddenly outnumbered, were forced to retreat. 法軍在人數上突然處於劣勢，被迫撤退了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>retreat</b> <b>from</b> something such as a plan or a way of life, you give it up, usually in order to do something safer or less extreme. 放棄","examples":["She retreated from public life. 她放棄了社會生活。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Retreat</b> is also a noun. 撤退","examples":["In June 1942, the British 8th Army was in full retreat. 1942年6月，英軍第8軍全線撤退。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Retreat</b> is also a noun. 放棄","examples":["The president's remarks appear to signal that there will be no retreat from his position. 總統的話似乎暗示他不會放棄自己的職位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>retreat</b> is a quiet, isolated place that you go to in order to rest or to do things in private. 隱居處; 休養處","examples":["He spent yesterday hidden away in his country retreat. 他躲在鄉間的休養地度過了昨天。"]}]}]},"revenge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"報復，報仇；報復慾望，復仇心；雪恥（指在比賽中戰勝曾擊敗自己的對手）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"復仇，報復；替（人）報仇；報（被冤枉，被傷害）之仇，洗雪（侮辱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Revenge</b> involves hurting or punishing someone who has hurt or harmed you. 報復","examples":["The attackers were said to be taking revenge on the 14-year-old, claiming he was a school bully. 攻擊者被稱是在報復一名14歲男孩，稱他是學校一霸。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>revenge</b> yourself on someone who has hurt you, you hurt them in return. 報復","examples":["The paper accused her of trying to revenge herself on her former lover. 這家報紙指責她企圖報復她以前的情人。"]}]}]},"revolutionary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"革命的；革命性的，突破性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"革命者，革命家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Revolutionary</b> activities, organizations, or people have the aim of causing a political revolution. 革命的","examples":["Do you know anything about the revolutionary movement? 你對這次革命運動有什麼瞭解嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Revolutionary</b> ideas and developments involve great changes in the way that something is done or made. 革命性的","examples":["Invented in 1951, the rotary engine is a revolutionary concept in internal combustion. 1951年發明的旋轉引擎是內燃領域的一個革命性觀念。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>revolutionary</b> is a person who tries to cause a revolution or who takes an active part in one. 革命者","examples":["The revolutionaries laid down their arms and their leaders went into voluntary exile. 這些革命者們放下了武器，他們的領袖們自願流亡。"]}]}]},"revolution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（思想、工作方式等的）徹底變革；（使用武力、暴力的）革命；旋轉；旋轉一週；（馬克思主義）共產主義革命（The Revolution）；迴圈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>revolution</b> is a successful attempt by a large group of people to change the political system of their country by force. 革命","examples":["The period since the revolution has been one of political turmoil. 自革命以來的這一段時期是一個政治動盪的時期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>revolution</b> in a particular area of human activity is an important change in that area. 重大變革","examples":["The nineteenth century witnessed a revolution in ship design and propulsion. 19世紀經歷了船舶設計和推進上的一次重大變革。"]}]}]},"rhyme":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"押韻短詩，（押韻的）兒歌；同韻詞，押韻詞；押韻，用韻"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"押韻，成韻；使押韻，使成韻；<文>寫韻文，作詩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one word <b>rhymes</b> <b>with</b> another or if two words <b>rhyme</b>, they have a very similar sound. Words that rhyme with each other are often used in poems. (字、詞) 押韻","examples":["June always rhymes with moon in old love songs. （六月）在古老的情歌中總是和（月亮）押韻。","...the sort of people who give their children names that rhyme: Donnie, Ronnie, Connie. …給孩子們起押韻名字（如多尼、羅尼、康尼）的那種人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a poem or song <b>rhymes</b>, the lines end with words that have very similar sounds. (詩、歌曲) 押韻","examples":["In his efforts to make it rhyme, he seems to have chosen the first word that came into his head. 為了努力使其押韻，他似乎選擇了進到他腦袋裡的第一個詞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rhyme</b> is a word which rhymes with another word, or a set of lines which rhyme. 押韻詞","examples":["The one rhyme for passion is fashion. 與passion押韻的詞是fashion。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rhyme</b> is a short poem which has rhyming words at the ends of its lines. 押韻短詩","examples":["He was teaching Helen a little rhyme. 他在教海倫一首短小的押韻詩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Rhyme</b> is the use of rhyming words as a technique in poetry. If something is written <b>in rhyme</b>, it is written as a poem in which the lines rhyme. (詩歌中的) 用韻; 押韻","examples":["The plays are in rhyme. 這些劇作是用韻文寫成的。"]}]}]},"reward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎勵，回報；賞格，懸賞金；報償，報應"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"酬謝，獎賞；獎勵（行動，品質）；（理所當然地）獲得，贏得（be rewarded）；值得（付出時間或精力）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reward</b> is something that you are given, for example because you have behaved well, worked hard, or provided a service to the community. 獎勵","examples":["A bonus of up to five percent can be added to a student's final exam score as a reward for good spelling, punctuation, and grammar. 作為對正確的拼寫、標點和語法的獎勵，多達5分的加分可以加到學生期末考試成績中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reward</b> is a sum of money offered to anyone who can give information about lost or stolen property, a missing person, or someone who is wanted by the police. 賞金","examples":["The firm last night offered a $10,000 reward for information leading to the conviction of the killer. 這家公司昨晚對能將兇手定罪的資訊懸賞1萬美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>rewards</b> of something are the benefits that you receive as a result of doing or having that thing. 回報","examples":["The company is just starting to reap the rewards of long-term investments. 這家公司正開始收穫長期投資的回報。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something and <b>are rewarded</b> with a particular benefit, you receive that benefit as a result of doing that thing. 回報","examples":["Make the extra effort to impress the buyer and you will be rewarded with a quicker sale at a better price. 格外賣力地給買主一個好印象，你就會被報以用更佳的價格更快地賣掉商品。"]}]}]},"rhythm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（聲音或運動的）節奏，韻律，節拍；節奏感；規則變化，節律；（藝術作品的）勻稱，和諧；（韻文或散文）抑揚節奏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rhythm</b> is a regular series of sounds or movements. 節奏","examples":["His music of that period fused the rhythms of Jazz with classical forms. 他那段時期的音樂融合了爵士樂的節奏和古典音樂的形式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rhythm</b> is a regular pattern of changes, for example changes in your body, in the seasons, or in the tides. (身體、季節等的) 規律性變化","examples":["Begin to listen to your own body rhythms. 開始聆聽你自己身體的規律性變化。"]}]}]},"salesman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"男推銷員；男售貨員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>salesman</b> is a man whose job is to sell things, especially directly to stores or other businesses on behalf of a company. 男推銷員","examples":["...an insurance salesman. …一位男保險推銷員。"]}]}]},"salesperson":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"售貨員，銷售員，推銷員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>salesperson</b> is a person who sells things, either in a shop or directly to customers on behalf of a company. 售貨員; 推銷員","examples":["They will usually send a salesperson out to measure your bathroom. 他們通常會派一名推銷員去測量你的浴室。"]}]}]},"route":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"路線，航線；道路，路途；常規路線，固定路線；<美>（尤指作為送貨工作的）例行拜訪，遞送路線；途徑，方法；（用於美國城市間幹線公路編號前）公路（Route）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"按特定路線傳送（車輛、貨物或乘客）；以......線路傳送（電話或其他電子訊號）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>route</b> is a way from one place to another. 路線","examples":["...the most direct route to the centre of town. …去鎮中心最直接的路線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A bus, air, or shipping <b>route</b> is the way between two places along which buses, planes, or ships travel regularly. (公共汽車的) 行車路線; (飛機、輪船的) 航線","examples":["...the main shipping routes to Japan. …去往日本的主要輪船航線。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In the United States, <b>Route</b> is used in front of a number in the names of main roads between major cities. (…號) 公路","examples":["From San Francisco take the motorway to the Broadway-Webster exit on Route 580. 從舊金山走高速公路到580號公路百老匯—韋伯斯特出口。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Your <b>route</b> is the series of visits you make to different people or places, as part of your job. 巡訪","examples":["He began cracking open big blue tins of butter cookies and feeding the dogs on his route. 他開始開啟裝著奶油曲奇的藍色大罐子，巡訪途中喂起那些狗來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can refer to a way of achieving something as a <b>route</b>. 途徑","examples":["Researchers are trying to get at the same information through an indirect route. 研究者們正試圖透過一條間接途徑獲取同樣的資訊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If vehicles, goods, or passengers <b>are routed</b> in a particular direction, they are made to travel in that direction. 為…規定路線","examples":["Trains are taking a lot of freight that used to be routed via trucks. 火車正在運送過去由卡車運送的大批貨物。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>En route</b> <b>to</b> a place means on the way to that place. <b>En route</b> is sometimes spelled <b>on route</b> in nonstandard English. 在途中","examples":["They have arrived in London en route to the United States. 他們在前往美國的途中已中途到達倫敦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Journalists sometimes use <b>en route</b> when they are mentioning an event that happened as part of a longer process or before another event. 在…的過程中; 在…之前","examples":["The German set three tournament records and equalled two others en route to grabbing golf's richest prize. 這個德國人在贏取高爾夫球賽最高獎的過程中重新整理了3項、平了2項錦標賽記錄。"]}]}]},"salary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薪金，薪水"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古> 給……薪金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>salary</b> is the money that someone earns each month or year from their employer. (按月或按年支付的) 薪水","examples":["The lawyer was paid a huge salary. 這位律師被付了一大筆薪水。"]}]}]},"sacrifice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犧牲，獻出；獻祭，供奉；祭牲，供品；基督的獻身（指耶穌被釘在十字架上）；（天主教作為獻祭聖體和聖血，或新教表示感恩的）聖餐禮；（棋）（為戰略或戰術原因所作出的）棄子，棄卒；（棒球中）犧牲打（sacrifice bunt/fly）；（橋牌）（指在對方叫到進局定約之後的）犧牲性叫牌（sacrifice bid）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"犧牲，獻出；獻祭，以……為祭品；（棋）（故意）棄子，棄卒；（棒球）做犧牲打；（棒球）以犧牲打使（跑壘者）進壘；（橋牌）作犧牲性叫牌；虧本出售"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>sacrifice</b> an animal or person means to kill them in a special religious ceremony as an offering to a god. 獻祭","examples":["The priest sacrificed a chicken. 牧師獻祭了一隻雞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sacrifice</b> something that is valuable or important, you give it up, usually to obtain something else for yourself or for other people. 捨棄; 犧牲","examples":["She sacrificed family life to her career. 她為了她的事業犧牲了家庭生活。","Kitty Aldridge has sacrificed all for her first film. 姬蒂•奧爾德里奇為了她的第一部電影犧牲了一切。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sacrifice</b> is also a noun. 祭品","examples":["...animal sacrifices to the gods. …獻給眾神的動物祭品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sacrifice</b> is also a noun. 捨棄; 犧牲","examples":["She made many sacrifices to get Anita a good education. 為了讓安尼塔受到良好教育，她做出了很多犧牲。"]}]}]},"saleswoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女售貨員，女店員，女推銷員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saleswoman</b> is a woman who sells things, either in a shop or directly to customers on behalf of a company. 女售貨員; 女推銷員","examples":["...an insurance saleswoman. …一位女保險推銷員。"]}]}]},"scenery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風景，景色；舞臺佈景"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>scenery</b> in a country area is the land, water, or plants that you can see around you. 風景; 景色","examples":["...the island's spectacular scenery. …島上壯美的景色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a theatre, the <b>scenery</b> consists of the structures and painted backgrounds that show where the action in the play takes place. 舞臺佈景","examples":["Instead of stagehands, the actors will move the scenery right in front of the audience. 演員們將替代舞臺工作人員，當著觀眾的面置換佈景。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>a change of scenery</b>, you go somewhere different after being in a particular place for a long time. 換個環境","examples":["A change of scenery might do you good. 換個環境可能會對你有好處。"]}]}]},"satellite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衛星；人造衛星；衛星國，附屬國；衛星城鎮，衛星郊區；衛星電視；隨體DNA"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"衛星傳送的，使用衛星技術的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>satellite</b> is an object which has been sent into space in order to collect information or to be part of a communications system. Satellites move continually around the earth or around another planet. 人造衛星","examples":["The rocket launched two communications satellites. 火箭發射了兩顆通訊衛星。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>satellite</b> is a natural object in space that moves around a planet or star. 衛星","examples":["...the satellites of Jupiter. …木星的衛星。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to a country, area, or organization as a <b>satellite</b> when it is controlled by or depends on a larger and more powerful one. 衛星國; 附屬區; 衛星組織","examples":["Some companies are outfitting their satellite offices with wireless LANs. 一些公司正在為其辦事處裝備無線區域網。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Satellite</b> television is broadcast using a satellite. 衛星的","examples":["They have four satellite channels. 他們有4個衛星頻道。"]}]}]},"seagull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海鷗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seagull</b> is a common kind of bird with white or grey feathers. 海鷗","examples":[]}]}]},"scold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"責罵，訓斥"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛訓斥人的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scold</b> someone, you speak angrily to them because they have done something wrong. 責罵","examples":["If he finds out, he'll scold me. 如果他發現了，他會責罵我。","Later she scolded her daughter for having talked to her father like that. 後來她因女兒對她父親那樣講話而訓斥了她。"]}]}]},"romance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常指短暫的）浪漫史，愛情關係，風流韻事；愛情，戀愛；傳奇色彩，浪漫情調；（對某物的）迷戀，鍾情；愛情故事；傳奇故事；浪漫曲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……求愛，追求（某人）；誇張，渲染；討好，奉承"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（語言）羅曼語的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>romance</b> is a relationship between two people who are in love with each other but who are not married to each other. 戀愛","examples":["After a whirlwind romance the couple announced their engagement in July. 在旋風式的戀愛之後，這對情侶在7月宣佈定婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Romance</b> refers to the actions and feelings of people who are in love, especially behaviour that is very caring or affectionate. (愛情中) 浪漫的感覺","examples":["He still finds time for romance by cooking candlelit dinners for his girlfriend. 他仍有時間為女友做燭光晚餐來製造浪漫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the pleasure and excitement of doing something new or exciting as <b>romance</b>. 浪漫新奇的感受","examples":["We want to recreate the romance and excitement that used to be part of rail journeys. 我們想重新營造過去乘火車旅行的那份浪漫新奇和刺激。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>romance</b> is a novel or movie about a love affair. 愛情小說; 愛情電影","examples":["Her taste in fiction was for chunky historical romances. 她喜愛的小說型別是厚重的歷史愛情小說。"]}]}]},"ruin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毀壞，毀滅；破產，身敗名裂；禍根； 殘垣斷壁，廢墟；殘存部分（ruins）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"毀壞，破壞；使（建築物，地方）破敗，使成為廢墟；使傾家蕩產，使破產；<文> 頭朝下跌落，嘩啦一聲掉下"}],"sections":[]},"sculpture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雕像，雕塑作品；雕刻藝術，雕塑藝術；（動，植）（貝殼、花粉粒、角質層或其他生物體表面凸起或凹陷的）雕飾，雕紋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"雕刻，雕塑；從事雕刻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sculpture</b> is a work of art that is produced by carving or shaping stone, wood, clay, or other materials. 雕塑","examples":["...stone sculptures of figures and animals. …人物及動物石雕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sculpture</b> is the art of creating sculptures. 雕塑 (藝術)","examples":["Both studied sculpture. 兩人都學過雕塑。"]}]}]},"satisfaction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"滿意，稱心；（對需求或慾望的）滿足；（抗議、投訴等的）妥善處理；樂事，快事；<法律>（債務等的）清償，（義務等的）履行；賠償，補償；<史>透過決鬥維護榮譽的機會；（基督教神學）基督替世人贖罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Satisfaction</b> is the pleasure that you feel when you do something or get something that you wanted or needed to do or get. 滿意","examples":["She felt a small glow of satisfaction. 她感到了一絲滿足的喜悅。","Both sides expressed satisfaction with the progress so far. 雙方都對目前的進展表示滿意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you get <b>satisfaction</b> from someone, you get money or an apology from them because you have been treated badly. 賠償; 補償","examples":["If you can't get any satisfaction, complain to the park owner. 如果你得不到任何賠償，就向公園的所有者投訴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>to</b> someone's <b>satisfaction</b>, they are happy with the way that you have done it. 令某人滿意","examples":["She never could seem to do anything right or to his satisfaction. 她似乎從來不會做任何正確或令他滿意的事情。"]}]}]},"settler":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移居者，定居者；殖民者，殖民地定居者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Settlers</b> are people who go to live in a new country. 移民者","examples":["The first German village in southwestern Siberia was founded a century ago by settlers from the Volga region. 西伯利亞西南部的第一個日爾曼村莊是一個世紀前由來自伏爾加地區的移民們建立的。"]}]}]},"shaver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電動剃鬚刀，剃毛器；理髮師；<非正式>小夥子；<舊>騙子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shaver</b> is an electric device, used for shaving hair from the face and body. 電動剃鬚刀","examples":["...men's electric shavers. …男用電動剃鬚刀。"]}]}]},"screwdriver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螺絲刀；螺絲起子（用伏特加和橙汁調製的雞尾酒）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>screwdriver</b> is a tool that is used for turning screws. It consists of a metal rod with a flat or cross-shaped end that fits into the top of the screw. 螺絲刀","examples":[]}]}]},"sightseeing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀光，遊覽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"觀光的，遊覽的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"觀光（sightsee 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>sightseeing</b> or do some <b>sightseeing</b>, you travel around visiting the interesting places that tourists usually visit. 觀光","examples":["...a day's sight-seeing in Venice. …在威尼斯的一日遊。"]}]}]},"shrug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（表示不知道或不感興趣）聳（肩）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聳肩；女式緊身短套衫，女式帶袖短披肩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shrug</b>, you raise your shoulders to show that you are not interested in something or that you do not know or care about something. 聳肩","examples":["I shrugged, as if to say, \"Why not?\" 我聳了聳肩，好像在說,“為什麼不？”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shrug</b> is also a noun. 聳肩","examples":["\"I suppose so,\" said Anna with a shrug. “我想是這樣，”安娜聳聳肩說道。"]}]}]},"scratch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用指甲）撓，輕抓；（用指甲或利器）抓破，劃破；劃出，刮出（痕跡）；（用爪子）抓，刨；（鳥、哺乳動物，尤指雞）用嘴（或爪子）扒地找食物；尋覓（難找的人或物）（scratch for）；艱難生活（scratch along）；勾掉，劃去（寫下的字）；<非正式> 倉促寫下；（用尖利物）刮擦出聲音；<非正式> 取消，撤銷（想法或計劃）；<非正式>（使）退出比賽；（用刮擦技法）播放唱片"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某人皮膚上的）劃痕，劃傷；刮痕，劃痕；抓，撓；刮擦聲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（球隊或一群人等）倉促拼湊的，匆匆組成的；（高爾夫球員）無讓杆的，無讓步優待的；碰巧的；打草稿用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scratch</b> <b>yourself</b>, you rub your fingernails against your skin because it is itching. 撓","examples":["He scratched himself under his arm. 他在自己腋下撓了撓。","The old man lifted his cardigan to scratch his side. 那位老人撩起他的開襟毛衣撓了撓身子側面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a sharp object <b>scratches</b> someone or something, it makes small shallow cuts on their skin or surface. 劃破","examples":["The branches tore at my jacket and scratched my hands and face. 那些樹枝掛了我的夾克，劃破了我的雙手和臉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scratches</b> on someone or something are small shallow cuts. 劃傷","examples":["The seven-year-old was found crying with scratches on his face and neck. 那個7歲的孩子被找到時正在哭，臉上和頸上都有劃傷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>from scratch</b>, you do it without making use of anything that has been done before. 從零開始","examples":["Building a home from scratch can be both exciting and challenging. 白手起家既激動人心又具有挑戰性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>scratching</b> their <b>head</b>, you mean that they are thinking hard and trying to solve a problem or puzzle. 絞盡腦汁思考","examples":["The Institute spends a lot of time scratching its head about how to boost American productivity. 這家研究所花大量時間絞盡腦汁思考怎樣推進美國的生產力。"]}]}]},"senior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"年齡大些的；（用在家庭內姓名相同的人名後表示）老，年長的；老年人的；（地位、水平或級別）較高的，高階的；（比賽）成人的，高水平的；<英>大於一定年齡（通常為11歲）的學童的；<美>（高中或大學）畢業年級的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"較年長的人；老年人，長者；地位（或級別）較高者，上司；<美>（中學或大學的）畢業班學生；資深成人運動員，高水平運動員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>senior</b> people in an organization or profession have the highest and most important jobs. 級別高的; 資深的","examples":["...senior officials in the Israeli government. ...以色列政府裡的高階官員們。","...the company's senior management. …該公司的高階管理人員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>senior</b> <b>to</b> you in an organization or profession, they have a higher and more important job than you or they are considered to be superior to you because they have worked there for longer and have more experience. 職務高於…的; 資格比…老的","examples":["The position had to be filled by an officer senior to Haig. 這個位置必須由一名職位比黑格高的軍官來填補。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you take part in a sport at <b>senior</b> level, you take part in competitions with adults and people who have reached a high degree of achievement in that sport. (體育比賽) 成人組的","examples":["This will be his fifth international championship and his third at senior level. 這將是他的第五次國際錦標賽，也是他的第三次成人級別比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>seniors</b> are the people who are senior to you. 上級; 地位較高者","examples":["He was described by his seniors as a model officer. 他被上級稱為模範軍官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Senior</b> is used when indicating how much older one person is than another. For example, if someone is ten years your <b>senior</b>, they are ten years older than you. 年長 (歲數) 的人","examples":["She became involved with a married man many years her senior. 她與一名比她年長很多的已婚男子墜入情網。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Seniors</b> are students in a high school, university, or college who are in their fourth year of study. (高中、大學的) 畢業班學生","examples":["...the number of high school seniors who go on to college. …高中畢業班上大學的學生人數。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>senior</b> is the same as a . 老年人","examples":["Tickets at the gate are $10, $7 for seniors (age 55 and up). 門票價格為$10，老年人(55歲及以上)為$7。"]}]}]},"shuttle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"太空梭（space shuttle 的簡稱）；往返於兩地的交通工具，擺渡車；（英法之間英吉利海峽隧道的）穿梭火車（the Shuttle）；（織機的）梭子；羽毛球（shuttlecock 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿梭，往返；穿梭運送"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shuttle</b> is the same as a . 太空梭","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shuttle</b> is a plane, bus, or train which makes frequent trips between two places. 穿梭班機; 穿梭班車; 穿梭火車","examples":["There is a free 24-hour shuttle between the airport terminals. 在機場的各航空站之間有24小時的免費穿梭巴士。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>shuttles</b> or <b>is shuttled</b> from one place to another place, they frequently go from one place to the other. 使頻頻往返於兩地之間; 頻頻往返於兩地之間","examples":["He and colleagues have shuttled back and forth between the three capitals. 他和同事們一直來回往返於3個首都之間。"]}]}]},"sincerity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"真誠，真摯"}],"sections":[]},"significance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要性，意義；意思，含義"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>significance</b> of something is the importance that it has, usually because it will have an effect on a situation or shows something about a situation. 重要性; 意義","examples":["Ideas about the social significance of religion have changed over time. 有關宗教的社會意義的觀念已隨時間的流逝發生了改變。"]}]}]},"shelter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"居所，住處；（尤指用以躲避風雨或攻擊的）遮蔽物，庇護處；遮蔽，庇護；（人或動物）收容所"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供庇護，提供保護；躲避，避難；使（某人）免遭（困難，討厭的事）；使免交稅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shelter</b> is a small building or covered place which is made to protect people from bad weather or danger. 躲避處","examples":["The city's bomb shelters were being prepared for possible air raids. 這座城市的防空掩體正在準備中，以防可能發生的空襲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place provides <b>shelter</b>, it provides you with a place to stay or live, especially when you need protection from bad weather or danger. 遮蔽; 庇護","examples":["The number of families seeking shelter rose by 17 percent. 尋求避難的家庭數目上升了17％。","Although horses do not generally mind the cold, shelter from rain and wind is important. 儘管馬通常不怕冷，但對風雨的遮擋還是很重要的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>shelter</b> is a building where homeless people can sleep and get food. 收容所","examples":["...a shelter for homeless women. …一個收留無家可歸婦女的收容所。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shelter</b> in a place, you stay there and are protected from bad weather or danger. 躲避","examples":["...a man sheltering in a doorway. …躲避在門廊裡的一名男子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or thing <b>is sheltered</b> by something, it is protected by that thing from wind and rain. 遮蔽","examples":["...a wooden house, sheltered by a low pointed roof. …一座由低矮的尖屋頂遮蔽的木房子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shelter</b> someone, usually someone who is being hunted by police or other people, you provide them with a place to stay or live. 窩藏; 庇護","examples":["A neighbour sheltered the boy for seven days. 一個鄰居將這個男孩藏了7天。"]}]}]},"singular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單數的，單數形式的；<正式>非凡的，突出的；<文>奇怪的，異常的；獨一無二的，獨特的；（數）（方陣）零行列式的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"單數，單數形式（the singular）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>singular</b> form of a word is the form that is used when referring to one person or thing. (名詞) 單數的","examples":["...the fifteen case endings of the singular form of the Finnish noun. …芬蘭語名詞單數形式的15種格結尾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The singular</b> of a noun is the form of it that is used to refer to one person or thing. (名詞的) 單數形式","examples":["The inhabitants of the Arctic are known as the Inuit. The singular is Inuk. 北極居民被稱作，其單數形式是。"]}]}]},"sledge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雪橇；大錘；（Sledge）（美、英）斯萊奇（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘雪橇；用雪橇搬運；用大錘打；（板球比賽中對對手）諷刺挖苦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sledge</b> is an object used for travelling over snow. It consists of a framework which slides on two strips of wood or metal. 雪橇","examples":["I saw her pulling three children through the snow on a sledge. 我看到她用雪橇拉著3個孩子穿過雪地。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sledge</b> or go <b>sledging</b>, you ride on a sledge. 滑雪橇","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to bait (an opponent, esp a batsman in cricket) in order to upset his concentration 使(對手，尤指板球擊球手)分散精力","examples":[]}]}]},"sled":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雪橇"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"乘雪橇"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用雪橇運"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sled</b> is the same as a . 雪橇","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sled</b> or go <b>sledding</b>, you ride on a sled. 乘雪橇","examples":["We got home and went sledding on the small hill in our back garden. 我們回到家，去後院的小山丘上滑雪橇。"]}]}]},"sketch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"素描，速寫，草圖；（任何作品的）粗樣，初稿；簡述，概述；幽默短劇，滑稽小品；<非正式，舊>滑稽的人（或物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給……）畫速寫，（給……）畫素描；簡述，概述；（用手或身體）做（姿勢）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sketch</b> is a drawing that is done quickly without a lot of details. Artists often use sketches as a preparation for a more detailed painting or drawing. 草圖; 略圖; 素描","examples":["...a sketch of a soldier by Orpen. …一幅奧彭畫的一位士兵的素描。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sketch</b> <b>of</b> a situation, person, or incident is a brief description of it without many details. 概述","examples":["...thumbnail sketches of heads of state and political figures. …國家首腦和政治要員們的簡要陳述。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sketch</b> is a short humorous piece of acting, usually forming part of a comedy show. 幽默短劇; 滑稽小品","examples":["...a five-minute sketch about a folk singer. …一出有關一位民間歌手的5分鐘幽默短劇。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sketch</b> something, you make a quick, rough drawing of it. 畫…的素描; 畫…的速寫","examples":["Clare and David Astor are sketching a view of far Spanish hills. 克萊爾和大衛·阿斯特正在素描遠處西班牙山巒景色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sketch</b> a situation or incident, you give a short description of it, including only the most important facts. 概述; 簡述","examples":["Cross sketched the story briefly, telling the facts just as they had happened. 克羅斯簡要地概述了這個事件，如實地講述了所發生的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sketch out</b> means the same as . 概述; 簡述","examples":["He sketched out plans to give consumers more affordable choices. 他簡述了幾個計劃，以給顧客提供更多符合其購買力的選擇。"]}]}]},"slogan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口號，標語；廣告語；<史>蘇格蘭高地的戰鬥吶喊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slogan</b> is a short phrase that is easy to remember. Slogans are used in advertisements and by political parties and other organizations who want people to remember what they are saying or selling. 口號; 廣告語","examples":["They could campaign on the slogan \"We'll take less of your money.\" 他們可以打著“我們將少賺你的錢”的廣告語開展宣傳攻勢。"]}]}]},"shift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）移動，（使）轉移；（使）轉換到（另一個人或另一事物）；（使）改變意見（或信仰等）；<英，非正式>趕快；<美>換（擋）；（計算機）移位；按（計算機鍵盤上的）Shift 鍵；<英，非正式>擺脫，消除；<英，非正式>（尤指大量）銷售，出售；<英，非正式>狼吞虎嚥地吃；<古>含糊其辭，拐彎抹角"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"改變，轉變；輪班工作時間；輪班工作的人；（計算機鍵盤上的）Shift 鍵；（計算機）移位；<美>（機動車的）換擋裝置；寬鬆直筒連衣裙（=shift dress）；<史>長而寬鬆的內衣；（建築）錯位；（美橄）（開賽前）球員位置的變換；（天文）（光譜線的）偏移；語音演變（sound shift 的簡稱）；<古>計謀，詭計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shift</b> something or if it <b>shifts</b>, it moves slightly. 稍微移動","examples":["He stopped, shifting his cane to his left hand. 他停下來，把手杖移到左手。","He shifted from foot to foot. 他從一隻腳換到另一隻腳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's opinion, a situation, or a policy <b>shifts</b> or <b>is shifted</b>, it changes slightly. 稍微改變","examples":["Attitudes to mental illness have shifted in recent years. 對精神病的態度近年來已稍微有所改變。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>shifts</b> the responsibility or blame for something onto you, they unfairly make you responsible or make people blame you for it, instead of them. 推卸; 轉嫁","examples":["It was a vain attempt to shift the responsibility for the murder to somebody else. 把這項謀殺的罪責轉嫁於他人是徒勞之舉。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>shift</b> gears in a car, you put the car into a different gear. 換 (擋)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shift</b> is also a noun. 稍微改變","examples":["...a shift in government policy. …政府政策的些許改變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a group of factory workers, nurses, or other people work <b>shifts</b>, they work for a set period before being replaced by another group, so that there is always a group working. Each of these set periods is called a <b>shift</b>. You can also use <b>shift</b> to refer to a group of workers who work together on a particular shift. 輪班","examples":["His father worked shifts in a steel mill. 他的父親在一家鋼鐵廠輪班工作。"]}]}]},"site":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（建築的）工地，用地；（某事發生的）地點，現場；（作某種用途的）場所，場地；網站，站點（=website）；（身體的某個）部位；（城鎮、建築物或紀念碑的）地基，選址；遺址，原址；（帳篷或大篷車內）歇腳的地方"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使坐落在，為......選址"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>site</b> is a piece of ground that is used for a particular purpose or where a particular thing happens. 場地; 場所","examples":["I was working as a foreman on a building site. 我在一個建築工地當工頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>site</b> <b>of</b> an important event is the place where it happened. (事件發生的) 現場; 場所","examples":["Scientists have described the Aral sea as the site of the worst ecological disaster on earth. 科學家們把鹹海描繪成地球上生態環境最差的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>site</b> is a piece of ground where something such as a statue or building stands or used to stand. 地點; 遺址; 原址","examples":["...the site of Moses' tomb. …摩西墓遺址。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>site</b> is the same as a . 網站","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"選址","examples":["...controls on the siting of gas storage vessels. …對煤氣儲存罐選址的種種限制。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is sited</b> in a particular place or position, it is put there or built there. 使坐落於; 把…置於","examples":["He said chemical weapons had never been sited in Germany. 他說從未在德國部署過化學武器。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>on site</b>, they are in a particular area or group of buildings where people work, study, or stay. 在工地上; 在現場","examples":["It is cheaper to have extra building work done when the builder is on site, rather than bringing him back for a small job. 趁建築工人在工地上時叫他們完成額外的建築工作要比叫他回來做一點小工便宜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>off site</b>, they are away from a particular area or group of buildings where people work, study, or stay. 不在工地上; 不在現場","examples":["There is ample car parking off site. 外面有個很大的停車場。"]}]}]},"sleigh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雪橇；（Sleigh）<英，美，加，澳，愛>斯萊（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘雪橇，滑雪橇，駕雪橇；用雪橇運輸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sleigh</b> is a vehicle which can slide over snow. Sleighs are usually pulled by horses. (通常由馬拉的) 雪橇","examples":[]}]}]},"slight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕微的，少量的；（人）瘦小的，纖弱的；（尤指創作）不深奧的，不重要的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"怠慢，輕視；<古>破壞，摧毀（防禦工事）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"冒犯，冷落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>slight</b> is very small in degree or quantity. 輕微的; 細微的","examples":["Doctors say he has made a slight improvement. 醫生說他已經有些輕微的好轉。","He's not the slightest bit worried. 他一點兒也不著急。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slight</b> person has a fairly thin and delicate looking body. 瘦小的; 纖細的","examples":["She is smaller and slighter than Christie. 她比克里斯蒂更瘦小更纖弱。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"瘦小地; 纖細地","examples":["...a slightly built man. …一個身材瘦小的男人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are slighted</b>, someone does or says something that insults you by treating you as if your views or feelings are not important. 輕蔑; 怠慢","examples":["They felt slighted by not being adequately consulted. 因為沒有充分地徵求他們的意見，他們感到被怠慢了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slight</b> is also a noun. 輕視; 冷落","examples":["It's difficult to persuade my husband that it isn't a slight on him that I enjoy my evening class. 很難勸說我丈夫相信我喜歡去上夜校課程並不是對他的冷落。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>in the slightest</b> to emphasize a negative statement. (用於加強否定的陳述語氣) 一點也","examples":["That doesn't interest me in the slightest. 那事兒一點也勾不起我的興趣。"]}]}]},"sneeze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打噴嚏"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"打噴嚏，噴嚏聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sneeze</b>, you suddenly take in your breath and then blow it down your nose noisily without being able to stop yourself, for example, because you have a cold. 打噴嚏","examples":["What exactly happens when we sneeze? 我們打噴嚏究竟是怎麼回事？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sneeze</b> is also a noun. 打噴嚏","examples":["Coughs and sneezes spread infections. 咳嗽和打噴嚏會傳播傳染病。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>not to be sneezed at</b>, you mean that it is worth having. 不容小視","examples":["The money's not to be sneezed at. 這筆錢可不容小視。"]}]}]},"sob":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啜泣，抽噎；哭訴，嗚咽地說；（風等）發出嗚咽聲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽噎（聲），嗚咽（聲）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>sobs</b>, they cry in a noisy way, breathing in short breaths. 抽噎","examples":["She began to sob again, burying her face in the pillow. 她又開始抽噎，把臉埋在枕頭裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"抽噎","examples":["The room was silent except for her sobbing. 房間裡除了她的啜泣聲一片寂靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sob</b> is one of the noises that you make when you are crying. 嗚咽聲","examples":["Her sobs grew louder. 她的嗚咽聲變得更大了。"]}]}]},"socket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電源）插座；（電器）插口，插孔；（人體的）窩，槽；（高爾夫插球杆的）棒頭承口；（用以插入某物使其轉動的）承窩，軸孔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"插入，使裝入插座"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>socket</b> is a device on a piece of electrical equipment into which you can put a bulb or plug. 插口; 燈座","examples":["On the stairway to the basement, he took the light bulb out of the socket. 在通向地下室的樓梯上，他把燈泡從燈座上擰了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>socket</b> is a device or point in a wall where you can connect electrical equipment to the power supply. (電源) 插座","examples":["Just plug it into any electrical socket. 就把它插入任何一個電源插座。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to any hollow part or opening in a structure which another part fits into as a <b>socket</b>. 承槽; 窩","examples":["Rotate the shoulders in their sockets five times. 將軸肩在承槽中轉動5次。"]}]}]},"sophomore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（高中或大學的）二年級學生；有兩年經驗的人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"第二張的，第二部的；二年級的，二年級學生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sophomore</b> is a student in the second year of college or high school. (大學或高中的)二年級學生","examples":[]}]}]},"software":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軟體；（計算機）程式及相關文件資料的總稱，與 hardware（硬體）相對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Computer programs are referred to as <b>software</b>. Compare . 軟體","examples":["...the people who write the software for big computer projects. …大型計算機專案的軟體開發人員。"]}]}]},"smog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常指城市中汽車、工廠等排出的）煙霧，霧霾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Smog</b> is a mixture of fog and smoke which occurs in some busy industrial cities. 煙霧","examples":["Cars cause pollution, both smog and acid rain. 汽車引起汙染，既有煙霧又有酸雨。"]}]}]},"souvenir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紀念品，紀念物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>把……作為紀念品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>souvenir</b> is something which you buy or keep to remind you of a holiday, place, or event. 紀念品","examples":["...a souvenir of the summer of 1992. …一個1992年夏天的紀念品。"]}]}]},"sparrow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麻雀；（任何在體積或顏色方面）像麻雀的鳥類"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sparrow</b> is a small brown bird that is very common in the United States. 麻雀","examples":[]}]}]},"sparkle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃爍，閃耀；生氣勃勃，熱情奔放；（眼睛）發亮；（酒類飲料）起泡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃耀，閃爍；（眼睛的）神采；生氣，活力；氣泡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>sparkles</b>, it is clear and bright and shines with a lot of very small points of light. 閃閃發光","examples":["The jewels on her fingers sparkled. 她手指上的珠寶閃閃發光。","His bright eyes sparkled. 他明亮的雙眼炯炯有神。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>sparkles</b> is lively, intelligent, and witty. 聰慧而有朝氣","examples":["She sparkles, and has as much zest as a person half her age. 她聰慧而有朝氣，且有著與比她年齡小一半的人一樣多的熱情。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sparkle</b> is also a noun. 閃光","examples":["...the sparkle of coloured glass. …彩色玻璃的閃光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sparkles</b> are small points of light caused by light reflecting off a clear bright surface. 閃光; 亮點","examples":["...sparkles of light. …光的閃爍"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sparkle</b> is also a noun. 才智與朝氣","examples":["There was little sparkle in their performance. 他們的表演平庸而了無生氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聰慧而有朝氣的","examples":["He is sparkling and versatile in front of the camera. 他在攝影機前聰穎機智、多才多藝。"]}]}]},"spear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矛，標槍；嫩枝，幼芽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用尖利的東西）刺，叉；（用鋒利的武器）刺，刺殺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spear</b> is a weapon consisting of a long pole with a sharp metal point attached to the end. 矛","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a shoot, slender stalk, or blade, as of grass, asparagus, or broccoli 嫩枝","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spear</b> something, you push or throw a pointed object into it. 刺; 叉 (某物)","examples":["Spear a piece of fish with a carving fork and dip it in the batter. 用切肉叉叉起一片魚並在麵糊裡蘸一下。"]}]}]},"sportsman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動員（通常指男性），運動家；有運動家風度的人，有體育精神的人；（Sportsman）人名；<英>斯波茨曼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sportsman</b> is a man who takes part in sports. 男運動員","examples":[]}]}]},"sportswoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女運動員，女運動家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sportswoman</b> is a woman who takes part in sports. 女運動員","examples":[]}]}]},"sportsmanship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體育精神，運動員風範，體育道德，指在體育比賽或競技活動中遵守規則、尊重對手、公平競賽的態度與行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sportsmanship</b> is behaviour and attitudes that show respect for the rules of a game and for the other players. 運動員風範; 運動員遵守比賽規則並互相尊重的態度與行為","examples":[]}]}]},"spark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導火線，誘因；火花，火星；電火花；一絲，略微；生氣，活力，才華；憤怒的情感，激烈的情緒；<非正式>軍隊中對無線電報務員（或電工）的暱稱（Sparks）；生龍活虎的小夥子；（內燃機裡火花塞的）放電"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"引發，觸發；產生火花（電火花）；點燃；增加趣味（或活力、風味等）；求婚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spark</b> is a tiny bright piece of burning material that flies up from something that is burning. 火花","examples":["The fire gradually got bigger and bigger. Sparks flew off in all directions. 火勢逐漸變得越來越大。火花四處飛濺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spark</b> is a flash of light caused by electricity. It often makes a loud sound. 電火花","examples":["He passed an electric spark through a mixture of gases. 他使一束電火花穿過一團氣體混合物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>spark of</b> a quality or feeling, especially a desirable one, is a small but noticeable amount of it. 一點 (品質或情感)","examples":["His music lacked that vital spark of imagination. 他的音樂缺乏那關鍵的一點想像力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>sparks</b>, sparks of fire or light come from it. 發出火花","examples":["The wires were sparking above me. 電線正在我頭頂上方冒火花。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a burning object or electricity <b>sparks</b> a fire, it causes a fire. 引發 (一場火)","examples":["A dropped cigarette may have sparked the fire. 一支丟棄的香菸可能引發了這場火災。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>sparks</b> another, the first thing cause the second thing to start happening. 引發","examples":["My teacher organized a unit on space exploration that really sparked my interest. 我的老師編排了一個關於太空探測的單元，它真正激發了我的興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spark off</b> means the same as . 引發 (同)(spark)","examples":["That incident sparked it off. 那一事件引發了它。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If <b>sparks fly</b> between people, they discuss something in an excited or angry way. 唇槍舌劍地爭論","examples":["They are not afraid to tackle the issues or let the sparks fly when necessary. 他們不怕應付這些問題, 必要時也不惜進行唇槍舌劍的激烈爭論。"]}]}]},"spare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"備用的，外加的；不用的，閒置的；空閒的，空餘的；多餘的；簡單的，簡樸的；瘦的，瘦高的；少量的；節約的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"抽出，拿出（時間、金錢等）；饒恕，赦免；省得，免去；節約，吝惜；保證（或滿足）自己的需要（spare oneself）；剩餘，剩下（時間、金錢或空間）；分讓；刪節"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"備用品；（車輛或機器的）零件，備件；（十柱保齡球戲中的）二擊全倒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>spare</b> to describe something that is the same as things that you are already using, but that you do not need yet and are keeping ready in case another one is needed. 備用的","examples":["If possible keep a spare pair of glasses accessible in case your main pair is broken or lost. 如有可能留一副備用眼鏡以防你常用的那副打碎或丟失。","He could have taken a spare key. 他原本可以帶上一把備用鑰匙的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>spare</b> to describe something that is not being used by anyone, and is therefore available for someone to use. 多餘的","examples":["They don't have a lot of spare cash. 他們並沒有很多多餘的現金。","The spare bedroom is on the second floor. 閒置的臥室在2樓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spare</b> is also a noun. 備用品","examples":["Give me the boot key and I'll get the spare. 給我行李箱鑰匙，我去配一把備用。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something such as time, money, or space <b>to spare</b>, you have some extra time, money, or space that you have not used or which you do not need. 剩下","examples":["You got here with ninety seconds to spare. 你們到達這裡時還剩有90秒鐘。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spare</b> time or another resource <b>for</b> a particular purpose, you make it available for that purpose. 抽出","examples":["She said that she could only spare 35 minutes for our meeting. 她說她只能抽出35分鐘給我們的會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or a place <b>is spared</b>, they are not harmed, even though other people or places have been. 使倖免","examples":["We have lost everything, but thank God, our lives have been spared. 我們失去了一切，但謝天謝地，我們保住了性命。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>spare</b> someone an unpleasant experience, you prevent them from suffering it. 使免遭","examples":["I wanted to spare Frances the embarrassment of discussing this subject. 我想使弗朗西絲免遭討論這個話題的尷尬。","Prisoners are spared the indignity of wearing uniforms. 囚犯們被免於遭受身穿統一服裝的侮辱。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>spare a thought for</b> an unfortunate person, you make an effort to think sympathetically about them and their bad luck. 為…著想","examples":["Spare a thought for the nation's shopkeepers – consumer sales slid again in May. 為這個國家的店主們著想一下–消費品銷售5月份又下滑了。"]}]}]},"species":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動植物的）種，物種；種類；（具有相同特徵的）一類人；（化學，物理）核素；（聖餐中用的）麵包和聖酒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原種的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>species</b> is a class of plants or animals whose members have the same main characteristics and are able to breed with each other. 物種","examples":["Pandas are an endangered species. 大熊貓是一種瀕危物種。"]}]}]},"submarine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潛艇，潛水艇；<美>潛艇三明治，長卷三明治；海底生物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"海面下的，海底的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用潛水艇攻擊；在下疾行，在下滑動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>submarine</b> is a type of ship that can travel both above and below the surface of the sea. The abbreviation  is also used. 潛水艇","examples":["...a nuclear submarine. …一艘核潛艇。"]}]}]},"status":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"法律地位（或身份）；（尤指在社會中的）地位，身份；高階職位，社會上層地位；重視（或崇尚）程度；狀況，情形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>status</b> is your social or professional position. 社會地位; 職業地位","examples":["People of higher status tend more to use certain drugs. 社會地位較高的人更傾向於使用某些藥物。","...women and men of wealth and status. …有錢有勢的男男女女。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Status</b> is the importance and respect that someone has among the public or a particular group. (在公眾中或某一團體中的) 威望; 地位","examples":["Nurses are undervalued, and they never enjoy the same status as doctors. 護士們沒有得到足夠重視，她們從未享受和醫生一樣的地位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>status</b> of something is the importance that people give it. 重要性","examples":["Those things that can be assessed by external tests are being given unduly high status. 那些能透過外部測試進行評估的東西受到過高重視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A particular <b>status</b> is an official description that says what category a person, organization, or place belongs to, and gives them particular rights or advantages. 身份","examples":["The Snoqualmie tribe regained its status as a federally recognized tribe. 斯諾夸爾米部落重新獲得了聯邦政府所承認的部落的身份。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>status</b> of something is its state of affairs at a particular time. 狀況","examples":["The council unanimously directed city staff to prepare a status report on the project. 該委員會成員一致要求市政人員準備一份關於這項工程的進展狀況報告。"]}]}]},"surf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"上網；衝浪；<非正式>坐在高速行駛的車輛（尤指火車）頂部（或外面）享受刺激感；<美，非正式>頻繁調換電影片道（同 channel-surf）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拍岸浪花；一次衝浪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Surf</b> is the mass of white bubbles that is formed by waves as they fall upon the shore. 拍岸浪花","examples":["...surf rolling onto white sand beaches. …翻滾到白色沙灘上的浪花。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"衝浪者","examples":["...this small fishing village, which continues to attract painters and surfers. …這個一直吸引著畫家和衝浪者的小漁村。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(網上) 衝浪者","examples":["Net surfers can use their credit cards to pay for anything from toys to train tickets. 網上衝浪者可用他們的信用卡購買從玩具到火車票的任何東西。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>surf</b>, you ride on big waves in the sea on a special board. 衝浪","examples":["I'm going to buy a surfboard and learn to surf. 我要去買個衝浪板來學衝浪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>surf</b> the Internet, you spend time finding and looking at things on the Internet. (網上) 衝浪","examples":["No one knows how many people currently surf the Net. 沒人知道現在有多少人在網上衝浪。"]}]}]},"stem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（植物、灌木的）莖，幹；（高腳酒杯的）柄腳；（語法中的）詞幹；菸斗柄；主幹；船頭，艏柱；（機械裝置的）閥杆，導杆，棒；<古，文>血統；<美>（手錶的）發條轉柄；（文字的）幹線，（音符的）符幹；<美，非正式>鴉片煙槍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻止，遏制；止住（液體的流動）；起源於；去梗，去柄；（船）逆流而行；（滑雪）向外轉動（滑雪屐）以便轉彎（或減速）；給……裝柄"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（STEM）理工科的統稱（science, technology, engineering, and mathematics）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a condition or problem <b>stems from</b> something, it was caused originally by that thing. 起源於","examples":["All my problems stem from drink. 我所有的問題都是酗酒引起的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stem</b> something, you stop it spreading, increasing, or continuing. 阻止","examples":["Austria has sent three army battalions to its border with Hungary to stem the flow of illegal immigrants. 奧地利已派遣3個營到達與匈牙利接壤的邊境處，以阻止非法移民的流入。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>stem</b> of a plant is the thin, upright part on which the flowers and leaves grow. 莖","examples":["He stooped down, cut the stem for her with his knife and handed her the flower. 他彎下腰，用刀替她割下花莖，然後把花遞給她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a technique in which the heel of one ski or both skis is forced outwards from the direction of movement in order to slow down or turn 轉動滑雪屐以減速或轉彎的技術","examples":[]}]}]},"surgeon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外科醫生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>surgeon</b> is a doctor who is specially trained to perform surgery. 外科醫生","examples":["...a heart surgeon. …一位心臟外科醫生。"]}]}]},"split":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）分裂，（使）產生分歧；（使）分開，分成（不同部分）；（使）撕裂；分擔，分享；劃破，割破；結束關係，分手；<非正式>迅速離開；使（原子）產生核裂變；<英，非正式>告發，揭發；<非正式>（頭）劇痛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"裂口，裂縫；分離，分裂，分歧；分配，份額；區分，不同；劈叉；分開（或切開）的東西；<美>錯層式房屋；分段耗時；<美>平局，連續打成平局的比賽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"分裂的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>splits</b> or if you <b>split</b> it, it is divided into two or more parts. 分開","examples":["In a severe gale the ship split in two. 在一次強勁的大風中那艘船斷成了兩半。","If the chicken is fairly small, you may simply split it in half. 要是雞不太大，你把它分成兩半就行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an organization <b>splits</b> or <b>is split</b>, one group of members disagree strongly with the other members, and may form a group of their own. 分裂","examples":["Yet it is feared the Republican leadership could split over the agreement. 然而人們擔心共和黨領導層可能會因該協議而出現分裂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as wood or a piece of clothing <b>splits</b> or <b>is split</b>, a long crack or tear appears in it. 使裂開; 裂開","examples":["The seat of his grey trousers split. 他的那條灰色褲子的臀部裂開了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If two or more people <b>split</b> something, they share it between them. 分攤; 分享","examples":["I would rather pay for a meal than watch nine friends pick over and split a bill. 我寧願付整頓飯錢而不願看著9個朋友仔細算計、分攤賬單。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Split</b> is also an adjective. 分裂的","examples":["The Kremlin is deeply split in its approach to foreign policy. 克里姆林宮在對外政策的看法上嚴重分歧。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>split</b> <b>in</b> an organization is a disagreement between its members. 分歧","examples":["They accused both radicals and conservatives of trying to provoke a split in the party. 他們指責激進人士和保守人士都企圖挑起黨內分歧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>split</b> <b>between</b> two things is a division or difference between them. 區分; 區別","examples":["...a split between what is thought and what is felt. …所想和所感之間的區別。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>split</b> is a long crack or tear. 裂縫","examples":["The plastic-covered seat has a few small splits around the corners. 那個有塑膠套的座位的角邊周圍有幾處小裂縫。"]}]}]},"surroundings":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"周圍環境，周圍事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are describing the place where you are at the moment, or the place where you live, you can refer to it as your <b>surroundings</b>. 環境","examples":["Schumacher adapted effortlessly to his new surroundings. 舒馬赫毫不費力地適應了他的新環境。"]}]}]},"suggestion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建議，意見；提議；微量；徵兆，細微的跡象；聯想，啟示；暗示；（尤指催眠術等療法中的）心理暗示；（心理）心理暗示（或提示）；"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>suggestion</b>, you put forward an idea or plan for someone to think about. 建議","examples":["The dietitian was helpful, making suggestions as to how I could improve my diet. 這位飲食學家很有幫助，就我如何能改善膳食提出了建議。","Perhaps he'd followed her suggestion of a stroll to the river. 也許他已聽從了她的到河邊散步的建議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>suggestion</b> is something that a person says which implies that something is the case. 暗示","examples":["We reject any suggestion that the law needs amending. 我們拒絕任何該法律需要修訂的暗示。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is no <b>suggestion</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, there is no reason to think that it is the case. 跡象","examples":["There is no suggestion whatsoever that the two sides are any closer to agreeing. 沒有該雙方更接近於達成一致的任何跡象。"]}]}]},"surgery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外科手術；<英>診所；（議員的）接待時間；應診時間；手術室"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Surgery</b> is medical treatment in which someone's body is cut open so that a doctor can repair, remove, or replace a diseased or damaged part. 外科手術","examples":["His father has just recovered from heart surgery. 他父親剛從心臟手術中恢復過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>surgery</b> is the room or house where a doctor or dentist works. 診室","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A doctor's <b>surgery</b> is the period of time each day when a doctor sees patients at his or her surgery. 診療時間","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>surgery</b> is the area in a hospital with operating rooms where surgeons operate on their patients. 手術室","examples":[]}]}]},"stroke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"中風；（使用武器的）擊，打；擊球，一擊，一抽；（划船用語）划槳，劃法，划槳法；泳式，游泳姿勢；（指揮船上其他槳手的）尾槳手；輕撫，撫摸；一筆，一劃；（靈感的）突發，（天才的）一舉；（突發或突然想到的）好事；斜線（號）；（雷電的）閃光；來回動作，上下動作；（一系列重複運動的）節奏，律動；（鳥翼的）一次撲打；準時，準點；（時鐘報時的）鳴響，鐘聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕撫，撫摸；輕挪，輕觸，輕拭；擊球；<美，非正式>討好，奉承；在……上輕輕塗抹；當……的尾槳手，當……的領槳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stroke</b> someone or something, you move your hand slowly and gently over them. 輕撫","examples":["Carla, curled up on the sofa, was smoking a cigarette and stroking her cat. 卡拉蜷曲在沙發上，抽著一支菸，輕撫著她的貓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has a <b>stroke</b>, a blood vessel in their brain bursts or becomes blocked, which may kill them or make them unable to move one side of their body. 中風","examples":["He had a minor stroke in 1987, which left him partly paralysed. 他在1987年患了輕度中風，這使他半身不遂了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>strokes</b> of a pen or brush are the movements or marks that you make with it when you are writing or painting. 筆畫","examples":["Fill in gaps by using short, upward strokes of the pencil. 用鉛筆畫出短的、向上的筆畫來填空。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you are swimming or rowing, your <b>strokes</b> are the repeated movements that you make with your arms or the oars. 划水; 划槳","examples":["I turned and swam a few strokes further out to sea. 我轉過身又向海裡遊了幾下。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A swimming <b>stroke</b> is a particular style or method of swimming. 游泳姿勢","examples":["She spent hours practising the breast stroke. 她花了幾個小時練習蛙泳。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"The <b>strokes</b> of a clock are the sounds that indicate each hour. 鐘聲","examples":["On the stroke of 12, fireworks suddenly exploded into the night. 12點的鐘聲敲響時，焰火突然衝破了夜空。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"In sports such as tennis, baseball, golf, and cricket, a <b>stroke</b> is the action of hitting the ball. 擊球","examples":["Compton was sending the ball here, there, and everywhere with each stroke. 康普頓把球發到這兒，發到那兒，每一次擊球都打到不同地方。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>A stroke of</b> luck or good fortune is something lucky that happens. 一次 (好運)","examples":["It didn't rain, which turned out to be a stroke of luck. 天沒下雨，結果成為一次好運。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"<b>A stroke of</b> genius or inspiration is a very good idea that someone suddenly has. (天才或靈感的) 一舉","examples":["At the time, his appointment seemed a stroke of genius. 當時，他的任命似乎是天才之舉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does not <b>do a stroke</b> <b>of</b> work, they are very lazy and do no work at all. 幹一點兒","examples":["I never did a stroke of work in college. 我在大學裡從來不幹一點兒活。"]}]}]},"syllable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"音節；隻言片語；表示音節的符號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"清晰地讀（詞，句），一個一個音節地讀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>syllable</b> is a part of a word that contains a single vowel sound and that is pronounced as a unit. So, for example, \"book\" has one syllable, and \"reading\" has two syllables. 音節","examples":["We children called her Oma, accenting both syllables. 我們這些孩子叫她，兩個音節都重讀。"]}]}]},"sway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搖擺，搖晃，擺動；影響（某人），使改變看法；<文> 統治，管理；（使）搖擺，搖動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"統治，勢力，支配，控制，影響；搖擺，擺動；統治，影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or things <b>sway</b>, they lean or swing slowly from one side to the other. 搖擺","examples":["The people swayed back and forth with arms linked. 人們手拉手前後搖擺著。","The whole boat swayed and tipped. 整條船搖晃著，然後翻了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are swayed</b> <b>by</b> someone or something, you are influenced by them. 影響","examples":["Don't ever be swayed by fashion. 不要受時尚的影響。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>holds sway</b>, they have great power or influence over a particular place or activity. 統治","examples":["Powerful traditional chiefs hold sway over more than 15 million people in rural areas. 有權勢的傳統首領們統治著鄉村地區的1500萬人。"]}]}]},"surrender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"投降；任憑擺佈，沉溺於；（被迫）交出，放棄；（向官員）交出（證件）；（體育運動中）失利（或丟分）；退保；期滿前就放棄（租借物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"投降，自首；屈服，屈從；（尤指在戰爭等過後）放棄，交出；退保"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>surrender</b>, you stop fighting or resisting someone and agree that you have been beaten. 投降; 屈服","examples":["General Martin Bonnet called on the rebels to surrender. 馬丁·邦尼特將軍要求反叛分子們投降。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Surrender</b> is also a noun. 投降; 屈服","examples":["...the government's apparent surrender to demands made by the religious militants. …政府對宗教好戰分子所提要求的明顯屈從。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Surrender</b> is also a noun. 放棄; 交出","examples":["...the sixteen-day deadline for the surrender of weapons and ammunition. …交出武器彈藥的16天期限。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>surrender</b> something you would rather keep, you give it up or let someone else have it, for example after a struggle. 放棄; 交出","examples":["Nadja had to fill out forms surrendering all rights to her property. 納賈不得不填寫表格，放棄對她財產的所有權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>surrender</b> something such as a ticket or your passport, you give it to someone in authority when they ask you to. 交出","examples":["They have been ordered to surrender their passports. 他們已被命令交出他們的護照。"]}]}]},"symphony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交響樂；<美>交響樂團（symphony orchestra 的簡稱）；和諧的東西；<史>大型聲樂作品中的過門"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>symphony</b> is a piece of music written to be played by an orchestra. Symphonies are usually made up of four separate sections called movements. 交響樂","examples":["...Beethoven's Ninth Symphony. …貝多芬的第九交響曲。"]}]}]},"telegram":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電報（經電報系統傳送的書面訊息，亦指電報通訊方式，如 by telegram）；Telegram（即時通訊軟體）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用電報傳送"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"發電報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>telegram</b> is a message that is sent by telegraph and then printed and delivered to someone's home or office. 電報","examples":["The president received a briefing by telegram. 總裁收到了一份電報簡報。"]}]}]},"syrup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"糖漿；糖水（有時加果汁）；藥用糖漿，糖漿劑；（風格，態度）過分甜蜜，過分多愁善感；<英，非正式>假髮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Syrup</b> is a sweet liquid made by cooking sugar with water, and sometimes with fruit juice as well. 糖水","examples":["...canned fruit with sugary syrup. …糖水水果罐頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Syrup</b> is a medicine in the form of a thick, sweet liquid. 藥用糖漿","examples":["...cough syrup. …止咳糖漿。"]}]}]},"technician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"技師，技術人員；（體育、藝術等方面）技巧精湛者，精於技巧者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>technician</b> is someone whose job involves skilled practical work with scientific equipment, for example, in a laboratory. 技術人員","examples":["...a laboratory technician. …一位實驗室技術人員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>technician</b> is someone who is very good at the detailed technical aspects of an activity. 精於某項技術的人","examples":["...a versatile, veteran player, a superb technician. …一個多才多藝、經驗豐富、技能超凡的高手。"]}]}]},"telegraph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電報（指通訊方式）；電報機；（運動比賽得分或其他資訊的）顯示板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發電報，用電報傳送（資訊）；流露，透露（計劃或意圖）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Telegraph</b> is a system of sending messages over long distances, either by means of electricity or by radio signals. Telegraph was used more often before the invention of telephones. 電報","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>telegraph</b> someone means to send them a message by telegraph. 發電報給","examples":["Churchill telegraphed an urgent message to Wavell. 丘吉爾給韋維爾發了一個急電。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>telegraphs</b> something that they are planning or intending to do, they make it obvious, either deliberately or accidentally, that they are going to do it. 流露 (要做某事)","examples":["The commission telegraphed its decision earlier this month by telling an official to prepare the order. 該委員會本月早些時候透過讓一個官員準備那項命令流露了其要做的決定。"]}]}]},"sympathy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同情（心），理解；贊同，支援；（與某人的）同感，共鳴；和應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>sympathy</b> for someone who is in a bad situation, you are sorry for them, and show this in the way you behave toward them. 同情","examples":["We expressed our sympathy for her loss. 我們對她的損失表示了同情。","I have had very little help from doctors and no sympathy whatsoever. 我從醫生那兒得到的幫助極少，而且沒得到任何同情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>sympathy</b> with someone's ideas or opinions, you agree with them. 贊同","examples":["I have some sympathy with this point of view. 我對這一觀點有些贊同。","Lithuania still commands considerable international sympathy for its cause. 立陶宛仍得到相當多對其事業的國際支援。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you take some action <b>in</b> <b>sympathy</b> <b>with</b> someone else, you do it in order to show that you support them. 支援","examples":["Several hundred workers struck in sympathy with their colleagues. 幾百名工人舉行罷工以示對其工友們的支援。"]}]}]},"telescope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"望遠鏡；射電望遠鏡，無線電望遠鏡（radio telescope 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"疊套縮短，疊縮；縮短，精簡；使（車輛）相撞而嵌進；壓縮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>telescope</b> is a long instrument shaped like a tube. It has lenses inside it that make distant things seem larger and nearer when you look through it. 望遠鏡","examples":["It's hoped that the telescope will enable scientists to see deeper into the universe than ever before. 希望該望遠鏡能讓科學家們比以往更深入地觀察宇宙。"]}]}]},"tomb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"墳墓，冢；土棺，石棺；墓碑；<文>死亡（the tomb）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"埋葬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tomb</b> is a grave, especially one that is above ground and that usually has a sculpture or other decoration on it. 墳墓 (尤指地面以上的部分)","examples":["...the continuing excavation of the emperor's tomb. …對這位皇帝的墳墓的不斷挖掘。"]}]}]},"tendency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經常性行為，偏好；趨勢，趨向；（性格中不良的）傾向；（政黨內的）極端派別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tendency</b> is a worrying or unpleasant habit or action that keeps occurring. 傾向","examples":["...the government's tendency to secrecy in recent years. …近年來政府的保密傾向。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tendency</b> is a part of your character that makes you often behave in an unpleasant or worrying way. (性格方面不好的) 傾向","examples":["He is spoiled, arrogant and has a tendency toward snobbery. 他被寵壞了，很傲慢，而且有勢利傾向。"]}]}]},"tolerance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忍受，容忍；（痛苦、困難等的）忍受程度，忍耐力；耐藥力，耐受性；公差，容許偏差"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tolerance</b> is the quality of allowing other people to say and do what they like, even if you do not agree with or approve of it. 寬容","examples":["...his tolerance and understanding of diverse human nature. …他對各種人性的寬容和理解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tolerance</b> is the ability to bear something painful or unpleasant. 忍耐力","examples":["There is lowered pain tolerance, lowered resistance to infection. 對痛苦的忍耐力和對感染的抵抗力下降了。"]}]}]},"terror":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚恐，恐懼；引起恐怖的人（或事物）；（尤指有政治目的的）恐怖活動，恐怖主義；<非正式>討厭鬼，搗蛋鬼（尤指小孩）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Terror</b> is very great fear. 恐懼","examples":["I shook with terror whenever I was about to fly in a plane. 我每次要坐飛機時都害怕得發抖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Terror</b> is violence or the threat of violence, especially when it is used for political reasons. 恐怖活動","examples":["...the war on terror. …反恐戰爭。","The bomb attack on the capital could signal the start of a pre-election terror campaign. 對首都的炸彈襲擊可能標誌著選舉前的恐怖活動的開始。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>terror</b> is something that makes you very frightened. 使人恐懼的事物","examples":["As a boy, he had a real terror of facing people. 他小時候其實非常害怕見人。"]}]}]},"tragedy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"悲慘事件，慘劇；悲劇（作品）；不幸，遺憾；令人非常煩亂（或生氣）的情形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tragedy</b> is an extremely sad event or situation. 災難","examples":["They have suffered an enormous personal tragedy. 他們遭受了一場巨大的個人災難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tragedy</b> is a type of literature, especially drama, that is serious and sad, and often ends with the death of the main character. 悲劇","examples":["The story has elements of tragedy and farce. 這個故事含有悲劇和鬧劇的成分。"]}]}]},"theme":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（談話、書籍、電影等的）題目，主題；（音樂的）主旋律；（電影、電視節目、廣播節目的）主題音樂，主題曲；（學生的）作文；（聚會、房間等的）風格；（句子的）主位；（名詞、動詞等的）詞幹；<史>（拜占庭帝國的）行政區"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"以奇想主題佈置的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（休閒場所、活動）以……主題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>theme</b> in a piece of writing, a talk, or a discussion is an important idea or subject that runs through it. (著作、談話或討論的) 主題","examples":["The theme of the conference is renaissance Europe. 該會議的主題是文藝復興時期的歐洲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>theme</b> in an artist's work or in a work of literature is an idea in it that the artist or writer develops or repeats. (藝術品或文學作品的) 主題","examples":["The novel's central theme is the ongoing conflict between men and women. 這部小說的主題是男女之間永無休止的衝突。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>theme</b> is a short simple tune on which a piece of music is based. (音樂的) 主旋律","examples":["...variations on themes from Mozart's The Magic Flute. …莫扎特的《魔笛》中主旋律的變奏曲。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Theme</b> music or a <b>theme</b> song is a piece of music that is played at the beginning and end of a movie or of a television or radio programme. (電影、電視節目或廣播節目的) 主題曲; 主題歌","examples":["...the theme from Dr. Zhivago. …《日瓦戈醫生》的主題曲。"]}]}]},"tension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"緊張，焦慮；緊張關係，緊張局勢；矛盾，衝突；（電線、繩子、肌肉等的）拉緊，繃緊；拉力，張力；（電影、書籍中的）緊張情緒，恐怖氣氛；（編織的）針織密度；電壓"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使拉緊，使緊張"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tension</b> is a feeling of worry and anxiety which makes it difficult for you to relax. (精神上的) 緊張","examples":["Smiling and laughing has actually been shown to relieve tension and stress. 微笑和大笑確實已證明能緩解緊張和壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tension</b> is the feeling that is produced in a situation when people are anxious and do not trust each other, and when there is a possibility of sudden violence or conflict. 緊張局面","examples":["The tension between the two countries is likely to remain. 兩國之間的緊張局面可能持續。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>tension</b> between forces, arguments, or influences, there are differences between them that cause difficulties. 衝突","examples":["The film explored the tension between public duty and personal affections. 該片探討了公共義務和個人情感之間的衝突。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>tension</b> in something such as a rope or wire is the extent to which it is stretched tight. 拉緊程度","examples":["As the cable wraps itself around the wheel, there is provision for adjusting the tension of the cable. 纜繩繞在輪子上時就留了調整纜繩鬆緊的餘地。"]}]}]},"translator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指從事筆譯的）譯者，翻譯家；翻譯機，翻譯程式；電視差頻轉播機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>translator</b> is a person whose job is translating writing or speech from one language to another. 譯員","examples":[]}]}]},"translation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"翻譯；譯文，譯本；譯詞，譯語；轉變，轉化；（生）轉譯；轉移；（數）平移；調任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>translation</b> is a piece of writing or speech that has been put into a different language. 譯文","examples":["...a translation of the Iliad. …《伊利亞特》的一種譯本。"]}]}]},"tug of war":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"拔河，拔河比賽；兩派間的激烈競爭"}],"sections":[]},"underpass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地下通道；（交）下穿交叉道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>underpass</b> is a road or path that goes underneath a railway or another road. (鐵路、公路等下的)下穿通道","examples":["The underpass was closed through flooding. 下穿通道在洪水期被封閉。"]}]}]},"transportation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運輸，運送；交通運輸系統；運輸工具，交通方式；（犯人的）流放，放逐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Transportation</b> refers to any type of vehicle that you can travel in or carry goods in. 交通工具","examples":["The company will provide transportation. 這家公司將提供交通工具。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Transportation</b> is a system for taking people or goods from one place to another, for example, using buses or trains. 交通運輸系統","examples":["Campuses are usually accessible by public transportation. 到校園通常可以乘坐公交。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Transportation</b> is the activity of taking goods or people from one place to another in a vehicle. 運輸","examples":["The baggage was being rapidly stowed away for transportation. 行李正迅速被裝好收起以便運輸。"]}]}]},"twinkle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃爍，閃耀；（眼睛因高興而）發亮，發光；（腳）輕快移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃爍，閃耀；（眼睛的）閃亮，欣喜的神情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a star or a light <b>twinkles</b>, it shines with an unsteady light which rapidly and constantly changes from bright to faint. 閃爍","examples":["At night, lights twinkle in distant cabins across the valleys. 晚上，燈光在山谷對面遠處的小木屋裡閃爍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone's eyes <b>twinkle</b>, you mean that their eyes express good humour or amusement. (眼睛) 閃爍","examples":["She saw her mother's eyes twinkle with amusement. 她看到她母親的雙眸愉快地閃爍著。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twinkle</b> is also a noun. 閃爍","examples":["A kindly twinkle came into her eyes. 她的眼睛裡閃爍著親切的光芒。"]}]}]},"typist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"打字員；打字者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>typist</b> is someone who works in an office typing letters and other documents. 打字員","examples":[]}]}]},"triumph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巨大成功，重大勝利；（勝利或成功的）喜悅，狂喜；（成功的）典範，楷模；古羅馬凱旋式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲勝，成功；（因勝利或成功而）欣喜，歡躍；（古羅馬將軍）凱旋而歸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>triumph</b> is a great success or achievement, often one that has been gained with a lot of skill or effort. 勝利; 成就","examples":["The championships proved to be a personal triumph for the coach, Dave Donovan. 那些冠軍稱號證明了教練戴夫·多諾萬的個人成就。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Triumph</b> is a feeling of great satisfaction and pride resulting from a success or victory. (成功或勝利的) 喜悅","examples":["Her sense of triumph was short-lived. 她喜悅的感覺是短暫的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>triumphs</b>, they gain complete success, control, or victory, often after a long or difficult struggle. 成功; 獲勝","examples":["All her life, Kelly had stuck with difficult tasks and challenges, and triumphed. 凱利在一生中遭遇了種種艱鉅任務與挑戰，但成功了。"]}]}]},"transfer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）轉移，搬遷；轉移（感情），傳染（疾病），轉讓（權力等）；（使）調動，轉職；轉會，使轉會（尤指職業足球隊）；（將所得學分）轉到（另一所學校）；轉接（電話）；將（錢）轉到（另一個賬戶上）；轉讓（財產，權利），移交（責任）；轉用；轉存，轉錄（資料、音樂等），改編；（旅途中）轉乘，換乘；轉印（圖畫，圖案）；（透過延伸、隱喻）轉變（詞義，短語義）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"轉移，轉讓，調動；（運動員）轉會；轉換，過渡；已調動的人，已轉移的東西；（旅行中）轉乘，轉搭；<美>轉車票，換乘票；紙上可轉印的圖畫或圖案；遷移（將已習得的行為在新的情況下應用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>transfer</b> something or someone <b>from</b> one place <b>to</b> another, or they <b>transfer</b> <b>from</b> one place <b>to</b> another, they go from the first place to the second. 轉移","examples":["Transfer the meat to a platter and leave in a warm place. 把肉轉到一個大淺盤中，然後擱在一個溫暖的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is transferred</b>, or <b>transfers</b>, <b>from</b> one person or group of people <b>to</b> another, the second person or group gets it instead of the first. 移交","examples":["The decision to transfer the investigation from the police to the district attorney's office is a mutual one. 將調查從警方移交到區律師辦公室的決定是共同做出的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are transferred</b>, or if you <b>transfer</b>, <b>to</b> a different job or place, the company moves you to a different job or you start working in a different part of the same company or organization. 調動","examples":["I was transferred to the book department. 我被調到了圖書部。","I suspect that she is going to be transferred to Fort Meyer. 我懷疑她將被調到邁耶堡。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When information <b>is transferred</b> <b>onto</b> a different medium, it is copied from one medium to another. 轉錄 (資訊)","examples":["Such information is easily transferred onto microfilm. 這樣的資訊很容易被轉錄到微縮膠片上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Transfer</b> is also a noun. 轉移","examples":["Arrange for the transfer of medical records to your new doctor. 安排把醫療記錄轉給你的新醫生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Transfer</b> is also a noun. 移交","examples":["...the transfer of power from the old to the new regimes. …從舊政權到新政權的權力移交。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Transfer</b> is also a noun. 調動","examples":["They will be offered transfers to other locations. 他們將得到去其他地方的調動令。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Transfer</b> is also a noun. 轉錄","examples":["It can be connected to a PC for the transfer of information. 它可以連線到個人電腦上進行資訊轉錄。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Transfers</b> are pieces of paper with a design on one side. The design can be transferred onto a surface by heating it, soaking it in water, or pressing it hard. 貼紙","examples":[]}]}]},"university":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大學，綜合性大學；大學校舍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>university</b> is an institution where students study for degrees and where academic research is done. 大學","examples":["Offenbacker earned an education degree at the University of Washington and taught elementary school. 奧芬巴克在華盛頓大學獲得了教育學位，教了小學。","She goes to Duke University. 她上杜克大學。"]}]}]},"vinegar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醋；尖酸，刻薄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vinegar</b> is a sharp-tasting liquid, usually made from sour wine or malt, that is used in cooking to make things such as salad dressing. 醋","examples":[]}]}]},"verb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動詞；動詞詞性；動詞性短語或從句；（Verb）（俄）韋爾布（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>verb</b> is a word such as \"sing,\" \"feel,\" or \"die\" that is used with a subject to say what someone or something does or what happens to them, or to give information about them. 動詞","examples":[]}]}]},"urge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"敦促，催促，力勸；竭力主張，強烈要求；驅趕，鞭策；鼓勵，激勵（~ sb. on）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"強烈的慾望，衝動；推動力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>urge</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you try hard to persuade them to do it. 敦促 (某人做某事)","examples":["They urged Congress to approve plans for their reform programme. 他們敦促國會批准他們有關改革專案的計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>urge</b> someone somewhere, you make them go there by touching them or talking to them. 鼓動 (某人去某地)","examples":["He slipped his arm around her waist and urged her away from the window. 他悄悄用一隻手臂攬住她的腰，勸她離開了視窗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>urge</b> a course of action, you strongly advise that it should be taken. 竭力主張","examples":["He urged restraint on the security forces. 他竭力主張限制安全部隊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>urge</b> <b>to</b> do or have something, you have a strong wish to do or have it. 強烈慾望","examples":["He had an urge to open a shop of his own. 他很想開一家自己的商店。"]}]}]},"vegetarian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"素食者，素食主義者；食草動物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"素食的，素的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>vegetarian</b> never eats meat or fish. 素食的","examples":["Yasmin sticks to a strict vegetarian diet. 亞斯敏堅持一種嚴格的純素飲食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Vegetarian</b> food does not contain any meat or fish. 素的","examples":["...vegetarian lasagnes. …素意式寬麵條。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vegetarian</b> is someone who is vegetarian. 素食者","examples":["...a special menu for vegetarians. …一份針對素食者的特殊選單。"]}]}]},"unique":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨一無二的，獨特的；非常特別的，極不尋常的；（某人、地或事物）獨具的，特有的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>獨一無二的人（或事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>unique</b> is the only one of its kind. 惟一的","examples":["Each person's signature is unique. 每個人的簽名是獨一無二的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>unique</b> to describe things that you admire because they are very unusual and special. 極不尋常的; 獨特的","examples":["She was a woman of unique talent and determination. 她是一個有獨特天賦和決心的女人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>unique to</b> one thing, person, group, or place, it concerns or belongs only to that thing, person, group, or place. 獨有的","examples":["No one knows for sure why adolescence is unique to humans. 沒人確切知道為什麼青春期是人類獨有的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"惟一地","examples":["Because of the extreme cold, the Antarctic is a uniquely fragile environment. 由於極端寒冷，南極州的生態環境尤其脆弱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"極不尋常地; 獨特地","examples":["There'll never be a shortage of people who consider themselves uniquely qualified to be president of the United States. 從不缺乏那種自認為特有資格成為美國總統的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"獨有地","examples":["The problem isn't uniquely American. 該問題並非美國獨有。"]}]}]},"universal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普遍的，全體的，全世界的；通用的，萬能的；（邏）全稱的，總稱的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"普遍原則，通用原理；普遍看法，普遍特徵；（邏）全稱命題；（哲）普遍，一般概念；（哲）共相；（語言學）普遍現象，通用規則"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>universal</b> relates to everyone in the world or everyone in a particular group or society. 全世界的; 普遍的","examples":["The insurance industry has produced its own proposals for universal health care. 保險業為全民保健提出了自己的建議。","The desire to look attractive is universal. 愛美之心人皆有之。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>universal</b> affects or relates to every part of the world or the universe. 全世界的; 普遍存在的","examples":["...universal diseases. …世界性的疾病。"]}]}]},"usage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（詞語的）用法；使用，用量；（尤指形成權利，義務，標準等的）常規做法，慣例；<正式>虐待，不公待遇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Usage</b> is the way in which words are actually used in particular contexts, especially with regard to their meanings. (詞在特定語境中的) 使用","examples":["He was a stickler for the correct usage of English. 他是一個堅持英語的正確使用的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>usage</b> is a meaning that a word has or a way in which it can be used. (詞的) 意義; 用法","examples":["It's very definitely a usage which has come over to Britain from America. 這肯定是從美國傳至英國的一種用法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Usage</b> is the degree to which something is used or the way in which it is used. (指某物的) 利用度; 使用","examples":["Parts of the motor wore out because of constant usage. 發動機的一些部件由於不斷使用而磨損了。"]}]}]},"vessel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"船，艦；（人或動物的）血管，（植物的）導管；（盛液體用的）容器，器皿；（有某種特質或用途的）人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vessel</b> is a ship or large boat. 船; 艦","examples":["...a New Zealand navy vessel. …一艘紐西蘭海軍艦艇。"]}]}]},"violation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對法律、協議、原則等的）違背，違反；侵權行為，（對人權的）侵犯；"}],"sections":[]},"walnut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胡桃，核桃；胡桃樹，核桃樹；胡桃木，核桃木；胡桃色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Walnuts</b> are edible nuts that have a wrinkled shape and a hard round shell that is light brown in colour. 胡桃; 核桃","examples":["...chopped walnuts. …砸碎了的核桃。"]}]}]},"volcano":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"火山"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>volcano</b> is a mountain from which hot melted rock, gas, steam, and ash from inside the earth sometimes burst. 火山","examples":["The volcano erupted last year killing about 600 people. 去年那座火山噴發導致大約六百人喪生。"]}]}]},"vowel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"母音，母音；母音字母，母音字母"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vowel</b> is a sound such as the ones represented in writing by the letters , , ,  and , that you pronounce with your mouth open, allowing the air to flow through it. Compare . 母音","examples":["The vowel in words like \"my\" and \"thigh\" is not very difficult. 在“”和“”這樣的單詞中的母音並不難發。"]}]}]},"virtue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高尚的道德，德行；美德，優秀品質；優點，長處；<古>（尤指婦女的）貞操；功效；（傳統基督教天使學）道德天使（天國九級制度的第七級）（virtues）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Virtue</b> is thinking and doing what is right and avoiding what is wrong. 正直的品性","examples":["Virtue is not confined to the Christian world. 正直的品性並不限於基督教世界。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>virtue</b> is a good quality or way of behaving. 美德","examples":["His virtue is patience. 他的美德就是耐心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>virtue</b> of something is an advantage or benefit that it has, especially in comparison with something else. 優勢; 益處","examples":["There was no virtue in returning to Calvi the way I had come. 按我來的路線返回卡爾維並不可取。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>by virtue of</b> to explain why something happens or is true. 因為","examples":["The article stuck in my mind by virtue of one detail. 該文章因一細節而印入我腦海。"]}]}]},"voyage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指坐船或飛往太空的）航行，旅行；（對某事或某人有大量新發現的）發現之旅"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"航行，遠行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>voyage</b> is a long journey on a ship or in a spacecraft. 航程","examples":["He aims to follow Columbus's voyage to the West Indies. 他打算沿著哥倫布的航程到達西印度群島。"]}]}]},"website":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"網站（全球資訊網的主機站）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>website</b> is a set of data and information about a particular subject that is available on the Internet. 網站","examples":["...a website devoted to hip-hop music. …一個嬉蹦樂專門網站。"]}]}]},"virgin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"處女，處男；無經驗的人，新手；（昆）孤雌生殖的雌蟲；聖母馬利亞（the Virgin）；室女宮（the Virgin）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原始狀態的，未開發的；處女的，處男的；（橄欖油）初榨的；（尤指白色物品）純潔的，未玷汙的；（黏土）未燒製的；（羊毛）未紡過的；（金屬）從礦石直接提取的，原生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>virgin</b> is someone, especially a woman or girl, who has never had sex. 處女","examples":["I was a virgin until I was thirty years old. 我到30歲時還是個處女。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>virgin</b> to describe someone who has never done or used a particular thing before. 生手","examples":["Until he appeared in \"In the Line of Fire\" Malkovich had been an action-movie virgin. 在出演《火線》之前，馬爾科維奇還是一個動作片的生手。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>virgin</b> to describe something such as land that has never been used or spoiled. (土地等) 未使用過的","examples":["Within 40 years there will be no virgin forest left. 過不了40年原始森林將所剩無幾。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a situation is <b>virgin territory</b>, you mean that you have no experience of it and it is completely new for you. 處女地; 全新領域","examples":["The World Cup is virgin territory for Ecuador. 世界盃對厄瓜多來說尚為一片全新的領域。"]}]}]},"virus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"病毒；病毒性疾病，病毒感染；（計算機）病毒，（手機的）簡訊病毒；有害影響，毒害；<古>毒液"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>virus</b> is a kind of germ that can cause disease. 病毒","examples":["There are many different strains of flu virus. 有許多不同型別的流感病毒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In computer technology, a <b>virus</b> is a program that introduces itself into a system, altering or destroying the information stored in the system. (計算機) 病毒","examples":["Hackers are said to have started a computer virus. 據說駭客們已開始傳播一種計算機病毒。"]}]}]},"volunteer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"志願者，義務工作者；自告奮勇者，主動做某事的人；志願兵，義勇兵；自生植物；<法律>無因受益人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"自願做，義務做，無償做；志願服役，志願參軍；主動提供（資訊），主動說出（或建議）；自作主張地說，（未經當事人同意）舉薦"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"志願（者）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>volunteer</b> is someone who does work without being paid for it, because they want to do it. 志願者","examples":["She now helps in a local school as a volunteer three days a week. 她現在作為一名志願者每週3天在當地一所學校幫忙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>volunteer</b> is someone who offers to do a particular task or job without being forced to do it. 自告奮勇者","examples":["Right. What I want now is two volunteers to come down to the front. 對了。我現在需要的就是兩個自告奮勇者到前面來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>volunteer</b> is someone who chooses to join the armed forces, especially during a war, as opposed to someone who is forced to join by law. 志願兵","examples":["They fought as volunteers with the Afghan guerrillas. 他們作為志願兵與阿富汗游擊隊一起戰鬥。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>volunteer</b> to do something, you offer to do it without being forced to do it. 主動要求做","examples":["Aunt Mary volunteered to clean up the kitchen. 瑪麗姨媽主動要求打掃廚房。","He volunteered for the army in 1939. 他在1939年自願參軍。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>volunteer</b> information, you tell someone something without being asked. 主動提供 (資訊)","examples":["The room was quiet; no one volunteered any further information. 房間裡很安靜；沒有人主動提供更多的資訊。","\"They were both great supporters of Franco,\" Ryle volunteered. “他們倆都是佛朗哥的堅定支持者，”賴爾主動說道。"]}]}]},"weekly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每週的，一週一次的；持續一週的，按周計算的；週刊的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"週報，週刊"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每週，每星期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weekly</b> event or publication happens or appears once a week or every week. 一週一次的; 每週的","examples":["Each course comprises 10-12 informal weekly meetings. 每門課程包括10至12次每週1次的非正式見面會。","We go and do the weekly shopping every Thursday. 我們每星期四採購一次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Weekly</b> quantities or rates relate to a period of one week. 按周計算的","examples":["Of course, in addition to my weekly pay, I got a lot of tips. 當然，除了週薪外，我還得到很多小費。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Weekly</b> is also an adverb. 每週一次地","examples":["The group meets weekly. 小組每週見面一次。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>weekly</b> is a newspaper or magazine that is published once a week. 週報; 週刊","examples":["Two of the four national daily papers are to become weeklies. 4家全國性的日報中有2家要改為週報。"]}]}]},"witch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巫婆，巫師；迷人的女子；美首鰈；（侮辱性用語）醜老太婆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（巫婆）施魔法於；（女子）把（男子）迷住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In fairy tales, a <b>witch</b> is a woman, usually an old woman, who has evil magic powers. Witches often wear a pointed black hat. (童話中的) 女巫","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>witch</b> is a man or woman who claims to have magic powers and to be able to use them for good or bad purposes. 巫師","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a flatfish, <b>Pleuronectes</b> (or <b>Glyptocephalus</b>) <b>cynoglossus,</b> of N Atlantic coastal waters, having a narrow greyish-brown body marked with tiny black spots: family <b>Pleuronectidae</b> (plaice, flounders, etc) (大西洋)灰鰈","examples":[]}]}]},"yogurt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酸奶，一罐酸奶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yogurt</b> is a food in the form of a thick, slightly sour liquid that is made by adding bacteria to milk. A <b>yogurt</b> is a small container of yogurt. 酸奶; 小包裝酸奶","examples":[]}]}]},"welfare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幸福，安康；福利救濟，社會福利；（給失業者和窮人的）福利救濟金"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"福利的；接受社會救濟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>welfare</b> of a person or group is their health, comfort, and happiness. 健康; 幸福; 福利","examples":["I do not think he is considering Emma's welfare. 我認為他沒有考慮到艾瑪的幸福。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Welfare</b> is money that is paid by the government to people who are unemployed, poor, or sick. 社會保障金","examples":["States such as Michigan are making deep cuts in welfare. 密西根等州正在大幅度削減社會保障金。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Welfare</b> services are provided to help with people's living conditions and financial problems. 福利的","examples":["Child welfare services are well established and comprehensive. 兒童福利機構發展成熟、體系完善。"]}]}]},"wit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（說話）風趣；說話風趣的人；機智；明智（the wit）；（不使用語言的）幽默機智"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>知道；即，就是"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wit</b> is the ability to use words or ideas in an amusing, clever, and imaginative way. 風趣; 機智","examples":["Boulding was known for his biting wit. 博爾丁以其嘲諷式的風趣而出名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>the wit</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they have the intelligence and understanding to make the right decision or take the right action in a particular situation. 才智","examples":["The information is there and waiting to be accessed by anyone with the wit to use it. 資訊是現成的，等著有頭腦的人去獲取和利用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to your ability to think quickly and effectively in a difficult situation as your <b>wits</b>. 機智","examples":["She has used her wits to progress to the position she holds today. 她用她的機智攀升到今天的這個位置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>wits</b> in expressions such as <b>frighten</b> someone <b>out of their wits</b> and <b>scare the wits out of</b> someone to emphasize that a person or thing worries or frightens someone very much. 神志","examples":["You scared us out of our wits. We heard you had an accident. 你把我們嚇壞了。我們聽說你出事了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"that is to say; namely (used to introduce statements, as in legal documents) 即; 也就是說","examples":[]}]}]},"wrinkle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（皮膚上的）皺紋；（布或紙上的）皺褶； <非正式>小困難，小難題；<非正式>令人吃驚的情節，出人意料的事情；<非正式>妙計，好主意"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使臉上）起皺紋，皺起；（布料等）起皺，起褶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wrinkles</b> are lines that form on someone's face as they grow old. 皺紋","examples":["His face was covered with wrinkles. 他的臉佈滿了皺紋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wrinkle</b> is a raised fold in a piece of cloth or paper that spoils its appearance. (布或紙上的) 皺褶","examples":["Ben brushed smooth a wrinkle in his trousers. 本把他褲子上的一個皺褶刷平了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a clever or useful trick, hint, or dodge 妙計; 竅門","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone's skin <b>wrinkles</b> or when something <b>wrinkles</b> it, lines start to form in it because the skin is getting old or damaged. 使起皺紋; 起皺紋","examples":["The skin on her cheeks and around her eyes was beginning to wrinkle. 她臉頰上和眼睛周圍的皮膚開始起皺紋了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If cloth <b>wrinkles</b>, or if someone or something <b>wrinkles</b> it, it gets folds or lines in it. 使起皺褶; 起皺褶","examples":["Her stockings wrinkled at the ankles. 她的長襪在腳踝處起皺褶了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>wrinkle</b> your nose or forehead, or when it <b>wrinkles</b>, you tighten the muscles in your face so that the skin folds. 皺起","examples":["Donna wrinkled her nose at her daughter. 多娜對她的女兒皺起鼻子。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有皺紋的","examples":["I did indeed look older and more wrinkled than ever. 我看起來確實比以前老了，皺紋也多了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"起皺褶的","examples":["His suit was wrinkled and he looked very tired. 他的外套皺皺巴巴的，他看上去非常疲憊。"]}]}]},"abrupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"突然的，意外的；粗魯的，唐突的，（言語）生硬的；險峻的，陡峭的；（講話或寫作風格）不流暢的，不連貫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>abrupt</b> change or action is very sudden, often in a way that is unpleasant. 驟然的","examples":["Rosie's idyllic world came to an abrupt end when her parents' marriage broke up. 當她的父母婚姻破裂後，羅茜的田園詩一般的世界驟然結束了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>abrupt</b> speaks in a rude, unfriendly way. 唐突的","examples":["He was abrupt to the point of rudeness. 他唐突到了無禮的地步。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"驟然地","examples":["He stopped abruptly and looked my way. 他突然停住，向我看了過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"唐突地","examples":["\"Good night, then,\" she said abruptly. “那麼，晚安”，她唐突地說道。"]}]}]},"wreck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破壞，斷送（計劃、關係等）；（嚴重）破壞，毀壞（車輛或建築物）；造成（船舶）失事，使遇難；<史>毀船打劫；<美>（為獲取有用的零件、碎料而）拆，拆除（破汽車、舊建築物等）；營救失事船隻；失事"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"沉船，遇難船；遭到嚴重破壞的東西（尤指建築物、車輛）；健康（或精神）嚴重受損的人；（船舶的）失事，遇難，交通事故；雜亂的地方；<法律>（船舶失事後被衝上岸的）殘貨，沉船漂浮物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>wreck</b> something means to completely destroy or ruin it. 摧毀","examples":["He wrecked the garden. 他毀掉了那個花園。","His life has been wrecked by the tragedy. 他的生活被這場悲劇毀了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wreck</b> is something such as a ship, car, plane, or building that has been destroyed, usually in an accident. (輪船、汽車、飛機或房屋失事後的) 殘骸","examples":["...the wreck of a sailing ship. …一艘帆船的殘骸。","The car was a total wreck. 這輛車完全報廢了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wreck</b> is an accident in which a moving vehicle hits something and is damaged or destroyed. 撞車事故","examples":["He was killed in a car wreck. 他在一場車禍中喪生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>wreck</b>, you mean that they are very exhausted or unhealthy. 疲憊不堪的人; 不健康的人","examples":["You look a wreck. 你看起來極度疲憊。"]}]}]},"wizard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巫師，術士；能手，奇才；嚮導程式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"卓越的，傑出的，極好的，奇妙的；男巫的，巫術的"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"練習巫術"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"召喚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In legends and fairy tales, a <b>wizard</b> is a man who has magic powers. 男巫","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you admire someone because they are very good at doing a particular thing, you can say that they are a <b>wizard</b>. 奇才","examples":["...a financial wizard. …一位金融奇才。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>wizard</b> is a computer program that guides you through the stages of a particular task. 嚮導程式","examples":["Wizards and templates can help you create brochures, calendars, and Web pages. 各向導程式和模板可以幫助你建立指南、日曆和網頁。"]}]}]},"abundant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大量的，豐富的，充足的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>abundant</b> is present in large quantities. 豐富的","examples":["There is an abundant supply of cheap labour. 有豐富的廉價勞動力供應。"]}]}]},"airtight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"密閉的，密封的，不透氣的；無懈可擊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a container is <b>airtight</b>, its lid fits so tightly that no air can get in or out. 密封的","examples":["Store the cookies in an airtight container. 把餅乾存放在一個密封的容器裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>airtight</b> alibi, case, argument, or agreement is one that has been so carefully put together that nobody will be able to find a fault in it. 無懈可擊的","examples":[]}]}]},"absurd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愚蠢的，荒謬的；滑稽可笑的；荒誕派的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"荒誕，荒誕的事物 （the absurd）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>absurd</b>, you are criticizing it because you think that it is ridiculous or that it does not make sense. 荒謬的","examples":["That's absurd. 那是荒謬的。","It's absurd to suggest that they knew what was going on but did nothing. 暗示說他們知道怎麼回事但卻袖手旁觀是荒謬的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The absurd</b> is something that is absurd. 荒謬之事","examples":["Connie had a sharp eye for the absurd. 康妮對荒謬之事有敏銳的眼光。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"荒謬地","examples":["Prices were still absurdly low, in his opinion. 在他看來，價格依然低得荒謬。"]}]}]},"apt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易於……的，有……傾向的；恰當的，適宜的；善學的，聰明的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apt</b> remark, description, or choice is especially suitable. 恰當的","examples":["The words of this report are as apt today as in 1929. 這份報告的措詞在當今如在1929年一樣恰當。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>apt</b> <b>to</b> do something, they often do it and so it is likely that they will do it again. 易於…的","examples":["She was apt to raise her voice and wave her hands about. 她常常提高嗓門並揮舞雙手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>apt</b> student is intelligent and able to understand things easily. 聰慧的","examples":["She had taught him French and he had been an apt student. 她教過他法語，他一直是個聰慧的學生。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"恰當地","examples":["...the beach in the aptly named town of Oceanside. …命名貼切的“海邊鎮”上的沙灘。"]}]}]},"allergic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"對……過敏的；過敏引起的，過敏性的；對……極其反感的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>allergic</b> <b>to</b> something, you become ill or get a rash when you eat it, smell it, or touch it. 過敏的","examples":["I'm allergic to cats. 我對貓過敏。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have an <b>allergic</b> reaction to something, you become ill or get a rash when you eat it, smell it, or touch it. (反應) 過敏的","examples":["Soy milk can cause allergic reactions in some children. 豆奶會導致有些兒童起過敏反應。"]}]}]},"ample":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"充足的，充裕的；豐滿的；寬敞的，巨大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>ample</b> amount of something, there is enough of it and usually some extra. 充足的","examples":["There'll be ample opportunity to relax, swim and soak up some sun. 將會有充足的機會來放鬆、游泳和接受一些陽光。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"充足地","examples":["This collection of his essays and journalism amply demonstrates his commitment to democracy. 他的這部散文和新聞報道集充分地證明了他對民主的奉獻。"]}]}]},"carefree":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無憂無慮的，無牽掛的；不負責任的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carefree</b> person or period of time doesn't have or involve any problems, worries, or responsibilities. 無憂無慮的","examples":["Chantal remembered carefree summers at the beach. 香岱兒想起了在海灘上的那些無憂無慮的夏日。"]}]}]},"agricultural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"農業的，與農業有關的；務農的，農用的；<英，非正式>笨拙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Agricultural</b> means involving or relating to agriculture. 農業的","examples":["Farmers struggling for survival strip the forests for agricultural land. 為生存而掙扎的農民們把森林伐光來作農業用地。"]}]}]},"barren":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"貧瘠的，不毛的；不結果實的；<舊>不育的；不出成績的，無效果的；沉悶無趣的，沒有吸引力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘠地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barren</b> landscape is dry and bare, and has very few plants and no trees. 荒蕪的","examples":["...the Tibetan landscape of high barren mountains. …西藏荒蕪的高山景觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Barren</b> land consists of soil that is so poor that plants cannot grow in it. 貧瘠的","examples":["He wants to use the water to irrigate barren desert land. 他想用該水來灌溉貧瘠的沙漠土地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as an activity or a period of your life as <b>barren</b>, you mean that you achieve no success during it or that it has no useful results. 無成就的; 不成功的","examples":["...an empty exercise barren of utility. …一項毫無效用的無聊訓練。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe a room or a place as <b>barren</b>, you do not like it because it has almost no furniture or other objects in it. 空蕩蕩的","examples":["The room was austere, nearly barren of furniture or decoration. 這個房間很簡樸，幾乎沒有什麼傢俱或裝飾。"]}]}]},"beneficial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有益的，有利的；<法律>（與）權益（有關）的，有財產使用權的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>beneficial</b> helps people or improves their lives. 有幫助的","examples":["...vitamins that are beneficial to our health. …有益我們健康的維生素。"]}]}]},"chubby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"圓胖的，豐滿的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chubby</b> person is somewhat fat. 圓胖的","examples":["Do you think I'm too chubby? 你覺得我太胖了嗎？"]}]}]},"witness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指犯罪或事故的）目擊者；（法庭等的）證人；（簽署正式檔案的）見證人，連署人；宗教信仰宣告，見證；見證人（宣告自己篤信基督教的人）；證據，證言；證明標誌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"目擊，目睹；見證，經歷（事件、變化等）；在（正式檔案）上簽名，連署；作見證（公開宣告自己對基督教的信仰）；證明，表明；為…...作證；作證，作證人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>witness</b> to an event such as an accident or crime is a person who saw it. 目擊者","examples":["Witnesses to the crash say they saw an explosion just before the disaster. 這起墜機事故的目擊者說, 在災難發生之前他們看到了爆炸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>witness</b> is someone who appears in a court of law to say what they know about a crime or other event. 證人","examples":["In the next three or four days, eleven witnesses will be called to testify. 在隨後的三四天裡，11名證人將傳喚來作證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>witness</b> is someone who writes their name on a document that you have signed, to confirm that it really is your signature. 連署人","examples":["The codicil must first be signed and dated by you in the presence of two witnesses. 該遺囑附件必須首先由你當著兩個連署人的面簽名並寫上日期。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>witness</b> something, you see it happen. 目擊","examples":["Anyone who witnessed the attack should call the police. 任何目睹了那場攻擊的人都應該報警。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>witnesses</b> your signature on a document, they write their name after it, to confirm that it really is your signature. 連署","examples":["Ask a friend, (not your spouse), to witness your signature. 請一位朋友（不可以是你的配偶），來連署你的簽名。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a place, period of time, or person <b>witnessed</b> a particular event or change, you mean that it happened in that place, during that period of time, or while that person was alive. 見證","examples":["India has witnessed many political changes in recent years. 印度近些年見證了許多政治變革。"]}]}]},"cautious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小心的，謹慎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cautious</b> acts very carefully in order to avoid possible danger. 謹慎的","examples":["The scientists are cautious about using enzyme therapy on humans. 科學家們對於人體使用酶療法持謹慎態度。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"謹慎地","examples":["David moved cautiously forward and looked over the edge. 大衛小心翼翼地向前移動，視線越過邊緣看過去。"]}]}]},"compassionate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有同情心的，憐憫的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"同情，憐憫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>compassionate</b>, you mean that they feel or show pity, sympathy, and understanding for people who are suffering. 有同情心的; 表示同情的","examples":["My father was a deeply compassionate man. 我的父親是個極富同情心的人。","She has a wise, compassionate face. 她有一張智慧和同情的臉。"]}]}]},"civic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"城鎮的，市政的；公民的，市民的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>civic</b> to describe people or things that have an official status in a town or city. 市政的","examples":["...the businessmen and civic leaders of Manchester. …曼徹斯特的商人們和市政領導。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>civic</b> to describe the duties or feelings that people have because they belong to a particular community. 市民的; 公民的","examples":["...a sense of civic pride. …市民自豪感。"]}]}]},"considerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"體貼的，考慮周到的；<舊>小心的，謹慎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>considerate</b> pays attention to the needs, wishes, or feelings of other people. 體貼的","examples":["I think he's the most charming, most considerate man I've ever known. 我覺得他是我所認識的最有魅力、最體貼的男士。"]}]}]},"cowardly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"怯懦的，膽小的；恃強凌弱的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<古>膽怯地，怯懦地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>cowardly</b>, you disapprove of them because they are easily frightened and avoid doing dangerous and difficult things. 膽小的; 怯懦的","examples":["I was too cowardly to complain. 我膽小得都不敢抱怨。"]}]}]},"contagious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（疾病）接觸性傳染的；（情感）具有感染力的；患接觸傳染病的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A disease that is <b>contagious</b> can be caught by touching people or things that are infected with it. Compare . 接觸傳染的","examples":["...a highly contagious disease of the lungs. …一種高度接觸傳染的肺病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A feeling or attitude that is <b>contagious</b> spreads quickly among a group of people. 有感染力的","examples":["Laughing is contagious. 笑是有感染力的。"]}]}]},"descriptive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"描寫的，說明的，敘述的；描述性的（學科）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Descriptive</b> language or writing indicates what someone or something is like. 描述的","examples":["The group adopted the simpler, more descriptive title of Angina Support Group. 該組織採用了更簡單、更具描述性的名稱——心絞痛支援組織。"]}]}]},"destructive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"破壞性的，毀滅性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>destructive</b> causes or is capable of causing great damage, harm, or injury. 毀壞性的","examples":["...the awesome destructive power of nuclear weapons. …核武器可怕的毀懷性力量。"]}]}]},"cozy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"舒適的，溫暖的，愜意的；友好的，親密無間的，溫馨的；（貶義）密切的，互相勾結的，串通的；安逸的，輕易得到的（但不一定是恰當的）；不提出（或不接受）挑戰的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（茶壺的）保溫罩，茶壺套（常作 tea cozy）；（舊式）（角落裡的）帶篷雙人座"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（非正式）使感到舒適，使得意；cozy up to：討好，奉承，巴結"}],"sections":[]},"continental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大洲的，大陸的；歐洲大陸的；具有歐洲特點的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（歐洲）大陸人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Continental</b> is used to refer to something that belongs to or relates to a continent. 大陸的","examples":["The most ancient parts of the continental crust are 4000 million years old. 該大陸地殼最古老的那些部分有40億年了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>continental</b> United States consists of all the states which are situated on the continent of North America, as opposed to Hawaii and territories such as the Virgin Islands. 內陸的 (美國)","examples":["Shipping is included on orders sent within the continental U.S. 運費含在美國內陸發出的訂單中。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Continental</b> means existing or happening in the American colonies during the American Revolution. 大陸的 (指在美國獨立戰爭期間的美國殖民地存在或發生的)","examples":["...George Washington, Commander of the Continental Army. …喬治·華盛頓，大陸軍總司令。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Continental</b> means situated on or belonging to the continent of Europe except for Britain. (除英國外的) 歐洲大陸的","examples":["He sees no signs of improvement in the U.K. and continental economy. 他看不出英國和歐洲大陸的經濟好轉的跡象。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Continentals</b> were soldiers who fought in the Continental Army against the British in the American Revolution. (美國獨立戰爭中的) 大陸軍士兵","examples":[]}]}]},"distinctive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨特的，與眾不同的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>distinctive</b> has a special quality or feature which makes it easily recognizable and different from other things of the same type. 與眾不同的; 有特色的","examples":["...the distinctive odour of chlorine. …氯氣的特殊氣味。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"特別地; 有特色地","examples":["...the distinctively fragrant taste of elderflowers. …接骨木花奇特的香味。"]}]}]},"eternal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"永恆的，永存的；似乎無休無止的，沒完沒了的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>eternal</b> lasts forever. 永恆的","examples":["...the quest for eternal youth. …對永遠年輕的追求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>eternal</b>, you mean that it seems to last forever, often because you think it is boring or annoying. 無休止的","examples":["In the background was that eternal hum. 背景裡是那沒完沒了的哼哼聲。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"永恆地","examples":["She is eternally grateful to her family for their support. 她因家人的支援對他們永存感激之心。"]}]}]},"dreadful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"糟糕透頂的，極其討厭的；極端的，極度的；非常疲憊的，非常沮喪的；可怕的，令人畏懼的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>dreadful</b>, you mean that it is very bad or unpleasant, or very poor in quality. 糟糕透頂的","examples":["They told us the dreadful news. 他們告訴了我們這個壞訊息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dreadful</b> is used to emphasize the degree or extent of something bad. 非常的; 極度的","examples":["We've made a dreadful mistake. 我們犯了一個很大的錯誤。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"糟糕透頂地","examples":["You behaved dreadfully. 你表現得糟透了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非常地; 極度地","examples":["He looks dreadfully ill. 他看上去病得非常嚴重。"]}]}]},"enthusiastic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱心的，熱情的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>enthusiastic</b> <b>about</b> something, you show how much you like or enjoy it by the way that you behave and talk. 熱衷的; 熱烈的","examples":["Tom was very enthusiastic about the place. 湯姆曾非常熱衷於那個地方。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"熱衷地; 熱烈地","examples":["The announcement was greeted enthusiastically. 這則通告受到了熱烈的歡迎。"]}]}]},"exceptional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"卓越的，傑出的；不尋常的，罕見的；（心理或身體上）有缺陷的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司賬目上的）異常專案"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>exceptional</b> to describe someone or something that has a particular quality, usually a good quality, to an unusually high degree. 非凡的","examples":["...children with exceptional ability. …能力非凡的孩子們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Exceptional</b> situations and incidents are unusual and only likely to happen infrequently. 例外的","examples":["A review panel concluded that there were no exceptional circumstances that would warrant a lesser penalty for him. 一個評估小組作出結論：沒有什麼例外情況可使他獲得從輕懲罰。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非凡地","examples":["He's an exceptionally talented dancer and needs to practise several hours every day. 他是位非凡有天賦的的舞蹈家，每天需要練幾小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"例外地","examples":["Exceptionally, in times of emergency, we may send a team of experts. 緊急情況下我們可以破例派遣一個專家隊。"]}]}]},"forgetful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"健忘的，記性差的；疏忽的，不經心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>forgetful</b> often forgets things. 健忘的","examples":["My mother has become very forgetful and confused. 我母親已變得很健忘很糊塗了。"]}]}]},"extinct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"滅絕的；消亡的；（火山）死的；（貴族稱號）無合法繼承人的；熄滅了的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A species of animal or plant that is <b>extinct</b> no longer has any living members, either in the world or in a particular place. 絕種的","examples":["At the current rate of decline, many of the rain forest animals could become extinct in less than 10 years. 按照目前的下降速度，許多雨林動物不到十年就會絕種。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a particular kind of worker, way of life, or type of activity is <b>extinct</b>, it no longer exists, because of changes in society. 不復存在的","examples":["Herbalism had become an all but extinct skill in the Western world. 草藥醫術在西方世界幾乎已成了一項絕跡的技術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>extinct</b> volcano is one that does not erupt or is not expected to erupt anymore. 死的 (火山)","examples":["Its tallest volcano, long extinct, is Olympus Mons. 它最高的火山是已死很久的奧林匹斯山。"]}]}]},"extensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"廣闊的；廣泛的；巨大的，大量的；（農業）粗放（經營）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>extensive</b> covers or includes a large physical area. 廣闊的","examples":["...an extensive tour of Latin America. …在拉丁美洲的一次大範圍的觀光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>extensive</b> covers a wide range of details, ideas, or items. 廣泛的","examples":["She recently completed an extensive study of elected officials who began their political careers before the age of 35. 她最近完成了一項對35歲前開始政治生涯的當選的官員的廣泛研究。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>extensive</b>, it is very great. 巨大的","examples":["The security forces have extensive powers of search and arrest. 安全部隊有很大的搜查和逮捕的權力。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"廣闊地","examples":["Mark, however, needs to travel extensively with his varied business interests. 然而，馬克因各種各樣的商業利益而需要四處旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"廣泛地","examples":["All these issues have been extensively researched in recent years. 所有這些問題近年來都得到廣泛地研究。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"巨大地","examples":["Hydrogen is used extensively in industry for the production of ammonia. 氫氣大量地在工業中被用於氨的生產。"]}]}]},"feeble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"衰弱的，虛弱的；（光線或聲音）微弱的；軟弱的；無效的，不佳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>feeble</b>, you mean that they are weak. 虛弱的","examples":["He told them he was old and feeble and was not able to walk so far. 他告訴他們自己年老體弱，不能走那麼遠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something that someone says as <b>feeble</b>, you mean that it is not very good or convincing. 不可信的","examples":["This is a particularly feeble argument. 這是個特別站不住腳的論點。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"虛弱地","examples":["His left hand moved feebly at his side. 他的左手在身邊無力地動了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"薄弱地","examples":["I said \"Sorry,\" very feebly, feeling rather embarrassed. 我很微弱地說了句“對不起”，感到特別尷尬。"]}]}]},"extraordinary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"異乎尋常的，令人驚奇的；非凡的，卓越的；特別的，臨時的；特大（或多）的；特派的，特命的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司正常業務活動之外的）非常賬目，特支款項"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>extraordinary</b>, you mean that they have some extremely good or special quality. 非凡的","examples":["We've made extraordinary progress as a society in that regard. 我們社會在那方面已經取得了巨大進步。","The task requires extraordinary patience and endurance. 這項工作需要非凡的耐心和毅力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>extraordinary</b>, you mean that it is very unusual or surprising. 非同尋常的","examples":["What an extraordinary thing to happen! 發生了多麼非同尋常的事啊！"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>extraordinary</b> meeting is arranged to deal with a particular situation or problem, rather than happening regularly. 特別的 (會議)","examples":["The U.S. has called for an extraordinary emergency meeting of the UN Human Rights Commission to examine the crisis. 美國已要求召開一次聯合國人權委員特別緊急會議來調查這次危機。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非凡地","examples":["She's extraordinarily disciplined. 她特別遵守紀律。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非同尋常地","examples":["Apart from the hair, he looked extraordinarily unchanged. 除了頭髮，他看上去真是一點也沒變。"]}]}]},"federal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聯邦（制）的；（與）聯邦政府（有關）的；中央集權式的；（美國內戰時期）北部聯邦政府的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯邦探員，聯邦政府官員；（美國南北戰爭時期）北部聯邦政府支持者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>federal</b> country or system of government is one in which the different states or provinces of the country have important powers to make their own laws and decisions. 聯邦制的","examples":["Five of the six provinces are to become autonomous regions in a new federal system of government. 在新的聯邦政府體制下，6個省中的5個將成為自治區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Federal</b> also means belonging or relating to the national government of a federal country rather than to one of the states within it. 聯邦政府的","examples":["The federal government controls just 6% of the education budget. 聯邦政府只掌控教育預算的6％。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聯邦政府地","examples":["...residents of public housing and federally subsidized apartments. …公共住房的住戶和享受聯邦政府補貼的公寓住戶。"]}]}]},"geographical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地理的，地理學的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Geographical</b> or <b>geographic</b> means concerned with or relating to geography. 地理的","examples":["Its geographical location stimulated overseas mercantile enterprise. 它的地理位置激發了海外商業企業的興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在地理上","examples":["It is geographically more diverse than any other continent. 它在地理上比其他任何大陸都更具多樣性。"]}]}]},"gorgeous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"美麗動人的；令人愉快的；絢麗的，華麗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>gorgeous</b>, you mean that it gives you a lot of pleasure or is very attractive. 十分宜人的; 很吸引人的","examples":["...gorgeous mountain scenery. …壯觀的山間景色。","It's a gorgeous day. 今天天氣真棒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>gorgeous</b>, you mean that you find them very sexually attractive. (人) 很性感的","examples":["The cosmetics industry uses gorgeous women to sell its skincare products. 化妝品行業用很性感的女人來推銷護膚品。"]}]}]},"frantic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"緊張忙亂的；（由於恐懼或擔心）無法控制感情的，發狂似的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>frantic</b>, you are behaving in a wild and uncontrolled way because you are frightened or worried. (因恐懼或憂慮而) 發狂似的","examples":["A bird had been locked in and was by now quite frantic. 一隻鳥被關了起來，到現在它都非常狂躁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an activity is <b>frantic</b>, things are done quickly and in an energetic but disorganized way, because there is very little time. 忙亂的","examples":["A busy night in the restaurant can be frantic in the kitchen. 晚上餐館生意繁忙，廚房可能就會忙作一團了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"發狂似地","examples":["She clutched frantically at Emily's arm. 她發狂似地緊緊抓著艾米莉的胳膊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"忙亂地","examples":["We have been frantically trying to save her life. 我們一直在手忙腳亂地設法挽救她的生命。"]}]}]},"hardy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"堅強的，吃苦耐勞的；（植物）耐寒的；堅定不移的，非常忠誠的；魯莽的，蠻橫的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"方柄鑿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Plants that are <b>hardy</b> are able to survive cold weather. (植物) 耐寒的","examples":["The silver-leaved varieties of cyclamen are not quite as hardy. 銀色仙客來品種不是十分耐寒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"having or demanding a tough constitution; robust 能吃苦耐勞的; 強健的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"any blacksmith's tool made with a square shank so that it can be lodged in a square hole in an anvil (鍛工用的)方柄鑿","examples":[]}]}]},"hoarse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（聲音）嘶啞的，沙啞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your voice is <b>hoarse</b> or if you are <b>hoarse</b>, your voice sounds rough and unclear, for example because your throat is sore. 嘶啞的","examples":["\"So what do you think?\" she said in a hoarse whisper. “那麼你怎麼認為？”她用嘶啞的嗓音悄聲說道。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嘶啞地","examples":["\"Thank you,\" Maria said hoarsely. “謝謝，”瑪麗亞嗓音嘶啞地說道。"]}]}]},"heavenly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天國的，神聖的；天空的，天上的（如 heavenly body 天體）；<非正式>極美好的，令人愉快的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>極其，無比"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heavenly</b> things are things that are connected with the religious idea of heaven. 天國的","examples":["...heavenly beings whose function it is to serve God. …職責為侍奉上帝的天使們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>heavenly</b> is very pleasant and enjoyable. 極美好的","examples":["The idea of spending two weeks with him may seem heavenly. 這個與他共度兩週的主意似乎妙不可言。"]}]}]},"immense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極大的，巨大的；非常好，極好；無邊無際的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>immense</b>, you mean that it is extremely large or great. 巨大的","examples":["...an immense cloud of smoke. …一大片煙雲。"]}]}]},"hostile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"敵對的，懷敵意的；強烈反對的；敵人的，敵方的；艱苦的，不利的；不受（被購公司）歡迎的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"敵對分子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>hostile</b> <b>to</b> another person or an idea, you disagree with them or disapprove of them, often showing this in your behaviour. 反對的; 敵對的","examples":["Many people felt he would be hostile to the idea of foreign intervention. 許多人覺得他會反對外來干預。","The West has gradually relaxed its hostile attitude to this influential state. 西方對這個有影響力的國家的敵對態度已趨緩和。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>hostile</b> is unfriendly and aggressive. 懷敵意的","examples":["Drinking may make a person feel relaxed and happy, or it may make her hostile, violent, or depressed. 喝酒可以使一個人感到放鬆和愉快，也可以讓人變得不友善、粗暴或沮喪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hostile</b> situations and conditions make it difficult for you to achieve something. (環境和條件等) 不利的","examples":["...some of the most hostile climatic conditions in the world. …世界上最不利的一些氣候條件。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>hostile</b> takeover bid is one that is opposed by the company that is being bid for. (收購投標) 惡意的","examples":["Soon after he arrived, Kingfisher launched a hostile bid for Dixons. 金費希爾到任之後不久就開始了對迪克森斯公司的惡意收購投標。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In a war, you use <b>hostile</b> to describe your enemy's forces, organizations, weapons, land, and activities. (戰爭中) 敵方的","examples":["The city is encircled by a hostile army. 該市被敵軍包圍。"]}]}]},"imperial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"帝國的，皇帝的；宏偉的，華麗的；專橫的，飛揚跋扈的；（度量衡）英制的；<史>（紙張尺寸）（英國）762×559毫米的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（在下唇下的）尖鬍鬚；紙張尺寸；特等品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Imperial</b> is used to refer to things or people that are or were connected with an empire. 帝國的","examples":["...the Imperial Palace in Tokyo. …東京的皇宮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>imperial</b> system of measurement uses inches, feet, yards and miles to measure length, ounces and pounds to measure weight, and pints, quarts and gallons to measure volume. (度量衡) 英制的","examples":[]}]}]},"hearty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱情友好的；精力充沛的，強健的；豐盛的；真摯的，強烈的；<英>假裝熱情友好的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>開朗活潑之人；好夥計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hearty</b> people or actions are loud, cheerful, and energetic. 喧鬧活潑的","examples":["Wade was a hearty, athletic sort of guy. 韋德是那種精力充沛、身體強壯的傢伙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hearty</b> feelings or opinions are strongly felt or strongly held. (感情或觀點等) 強烈的","examples":["With the last sentiment, Arnold was in hearty agreement. 對於最後一個觀點，阿諾德強烈贊同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hearty</b> meal is large and very satisfying. (飯菜) 豐盛的","examples":["The men ate a hearty breakfast. 男士們吃了一頓豐盛的早餐。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"喧鬧活潑地","examples":["He laughed heartily. 他開懷大笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"強烈地","examples":["Most Afghans are heartily sick of war. 大多數阿富汗人極其厭惡戰爭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"胃口很大地","examples":["He ate heartily but would drink only beer. 他吃飯的胃口很大，但只喝啤酒。"]}]}]},"indifferent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冷淡的，不關心的；中等的，平庸的；一般的，相當差的；中立的；不分化的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of being <b>indifferent</b> <b>to</b> something, you mean that they have a complete lack of interest in it. 漠不關心的","examples":["People have become indifferent to the suffering of others. 人們已經變得對別人的痛苦漠不關心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>indifferent</b>, you mean that their standard or quality is not very good, and often quite bad. 平庸的","examples":["She had starred in several very indifferent movies. 她領銜主演過好幾部非常平庸的電影。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"漠不關心地","examples":["\"Not that it matters,\" said Trujillo indifferently. “它倒不是那麼重要”，特魯希略漠然地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"平庸地","examples":["...a shoddy piece of work, poorly written, indifferently performed. …一部粗製濫造的作品，寫得差勁，演得也蹩腳。"]}]}]},"indispensable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不可或缺的，必需的；不能撇開的，責無旁貸的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不可缺少之物，必不可少的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>indispensable</b>, you mean that they are absolutely essential and other people or things cannot function without them. 必不可少的","examples":["She was becoming indispensable to him. 對他來說她正變得不可或缺。"]}]}]},"grim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嚴肅的，堅定的；令人不快的，令人沮喪的；陰森的，淒涼的；<非正式>生病的；<英，非正式>質量低劣，糟糕；（地方）簡陋的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A situation or piece of information that is <b>grim</b> is unpleasant, depressing, and difficult to accept. 嚴酷的; 令人沮喪的","examples":["They painted a grim picture of growing crime. 他們描繪了一個犯罪增長的嚴酷局面。","There was further grim economic news yesterday. 昨天有更令人沮喪的經濟新聞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A place that is <b>grim</b> is unattractive and depressing in appearance. (地方) 陰沉的","examples":["The city might be grim at first, but there is a vibrancy and excitement. 這個城市也許一開始沉悶，但它有一種活力和激情。"]}]}]},"indignant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"憤憤不平的，憤慨的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>indignant</b>, you are shocked and angry, because you think that something is unjust or unfair. 憤怒不平的","examples":["He is indignant at suggestions that they were secret agents. 他對關於他們是特務的暗示很憤慨。","He was indignant that his rival was offered the job. 他對他的對手得到了那份工作感到憤憤不平。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"憤怒地","examples":["\"That is not true,\" Erica said indignantly. “那不是真的，”埃麗卡氣憤地說。"]}]}]},"knowledgeable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有見識的，知識淵博的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>knowledgeable</b> has or shows a clear understanding of many different facts about the world or about a particular subject. 知識淵博的","examples":["Do you think you are more knowledgeable about life than your parents were at your age? 父母在你這個年齡時，你認為你比他們更瞭解生活嗎？"]}]}]},"lifelong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"終身的，畢生的，終生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lifelong</b> means existing or happening for the whole of a person's life. 終生的","examples":["...her lifelong friendship with Naomi. …她與娜奧米的終生友誼。"]}]}]},"lonesome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"寂寞的，孤寂的；人跡稀少的，荒僻的；唯一的，單獨的，孤零零的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>自己（僅用於 by one's lonesome、on one's lonesome 等固定短語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>lonesome</b> is unhappy because they do not have any friends or do not have anyone to talk to. 孤寂的","examples":["I've grown so lonesome, thinking of you. 我從小到大都很孤單，經常想起你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lonesome</b> place is one which very few people come to and which is a long way from places where people live. 荒僻的","examples":["He was finding the river lonesome. 他發現這條河很偏僻。"]}]}]},"innumerable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無數的，數不清的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Innumerable</b> means very many, or too many to be counted. 數不清的; 無數的","examples":["He has invented innumerable excuses, told endless lies. 他編造了數不清的藉口，說了無止盡的謊言。"]}]}]},"lofty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"巍峨的，高聳的；崇高的，高尚的；傲慢的，高傲的；（毛和其他紡織品）厚實而有彈性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lofty</b> ideal or ambition is noble, important, and admirable. 崇高的","examples":["It was a bank that started out with grand ideas and lofty ideals. 那是一家創辦時帶著宏大理念、崇高理想的銀行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lofty</b> building or room is very high. 高聳的","examples":["...a light, lofty apartment in the suburbs of Salzburg. …位於薩爾茨堡郊外的一幢光線充足、高高聳立的公寓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone behaves in a <b>lofty</b> way, you are critical of them for behaving in a proud and somewhat overbearing way, as if they think they are very important. 高傲的","examples":["...the lofty disdain he often expresses for his profession. …他經常表露出的對其職業的輕慢。"]}]}]},"majestic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雄偉的，壯麗的，威嚴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>majestic</b>, you think they are very beautiful, dignified, and impressive. 壯麗的; 雄偉的","examples":["...a majestic country home that once belonged to the Astor family. …一座曾經屬於阿斯特家族的漂亮的鄉村住所。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"壯麗地; 雄偉地","examples":["She rose majestically to her feet. 她端莊地站了起來。"]}]}]},"martial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<正式>軍事的，戰爭的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Martial</b> is used to describe things relating to soldiers or war. 軍人的; 軍事的","examples":["The paper was actually twice banned under the martial regime. 這份報紙在軍人統治時期確實曾兩次被禁。"]}]}]},"minimal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極小的，極少的；極簡抽象藝術的；簡樸的，樸實無華的；極簡的（指短小樂句不斷重複並逐漸變化）；最小差別的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>minimal</b> is very small in quantity, value, or degree. 儘可能少的; 最低限度的","examples":["The cooperation between the two is minimal. 兩者之間的合作是最低程度的。"]}]}]},"infinite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無限的，無窮盡的；（數量或程度上）極大的，無窮大的；非限定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（空間或數量的）無窮大（the infinite）；上帝（the infinite）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>infinite</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely great in amount or degree. 極大的; 極多的","examples":["...an infinite variety of landscapes. …極其多樣的地形地貌。","With infinite care, John shifted position. 約翰小心翼翼地換了位置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>infinite</b> has no limit, end, or edge. 無窮的; 無限的","examples":["...an infinite number of atoms. …無數個原子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極大地","examples":["His design was infinitely better than anything I could have done. 他的設計比我所能設計的不知要好上多少倍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"無窮無盡地","examples":["A centimetre can be infinitely divided into smaller units. 一釐米能被無窮盡地分為更小的單位。"]}]}]},"monstrous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不公正道德的，殘忍的；巨大的，龐大的；醜陋的，駭人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation or event as <b>monstrous</b>, you mean that it is extremely shocking or unfair. 駭人聽聞的; 極不公正的","examples":["She endured the monstrous behaviour for years. 她忍受這種駭人聽聞的行為多年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an unpleasant thing as <b>monstrous</b>, you mean that it is extremely large in size or extent. (令人不悅的事物) 巨大的","examples":["A group of men are erecting a monstrous copper edifice. 一群人正在建造一座巨大的銅色建築。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>monstrous</b>, you mean that it is extremely frightening because it appears unnatural or ugly. 恐怖的","examples":["...the film's monstrous fantasy figure. …電影中恐怖的魔幻形象。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"駭人聽聞地; 極不公正地","examples":["Your husband's family has behaved monstrously. 你婆家人做得太不公正了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"巨大地","examples":["It would be monstrously unfair. 那將太不公平了。"]}]}]},"marginal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小的，微不足道的；（活動、花費、稅項等）邊際的；非主流的，邊緣的；以相差無幾的票數獲勝（或失敗）的；寫在頁邊空白的；貧瘠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"岸邊水生植物；邊緣席位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>marginal</b>, you mean that it is small or not very important. 微小的","examples":["This is a marginal improvement on October. 這是對10月份的一個小小的改進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe people as <b>marginal</b>, you mean that they are not involved in the main events or developments in society because they are poor or have no power. 無足輕重的","examples":["The tribunals were established for the well-integrated members of society and not for marginal individuals. 這個特別法庭是為社會中的主流人群設立的，而不是為了無足輕重的小人物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Marginal</b> activities, costs, or taxes are not the main part of a business or an economic system, but often make the difference between its success or failure, and are therefore important to control. 邊際的","examples":["The analysts applaud the cuts in marginal businesses, but insist the company must make deeper sacrifices. 分析家們贊同對邊際業務的削減，但堅持認為公司必須作出更大犧牲。"]}]}]},"nonviolent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非暴力的"},{"pos":"","zh":"不使用暴力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nonviolent</b> methods of bringing about change do not involve hurting people or causing damage. 非暴力的","examples":["King was a worldwide symbol of nonviolent protest against racial injustice. 金是全世界以非暴力抗議種族不平等的象徵。","I would only belong to an environmental movement if it was explicitly nonviolent. 我只會投身一個明確宣稱只用非暴力手段的環護運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone or something such as a crime as <b>nonviolent</b> when that person or thing does not hurt or injure people. 不傷害他人的; 不使用暴力的","examples":["...nonviolent offenders. ...非暴力犯罪的罪犯。"]}]}]},"massive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大而重的，結實的；非常嚴重的；大量的，大規模的；<非正式>特別成功的，非常有影響的；（岩石或地層）均勻構造的，大塊的；（礦物）外觀非晶質的；<英，非正式>極好的，非常妙的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英，非正式>（某一地區的年輕人群體）嬉蹦音樂迷（或叢林爵士音樂迷）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>massive</b> is very large in size, quantity, or extent. (尺寸、數量、規模) 非常大的","examples":["There was evidence of massive fraud. 有證據表明是鉅額欺詐。","...massive air attacks. …大規模的空襲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a medical condition as <b>massive</b>, you mean that it is extremely serious. 嚴重的","examples":["He died six weeks later of a massive heart attack. 他6周後死於一次嚴重的心臟病發作。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非常大地","examples":["...a massively popular game. …一種非常受歡迎的遊戲。"]}]}]},"muscular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"肌肉的，影響肌肉的；肌肉發達的，強壯的；強勁有力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Muscular</b> means involving or affecting your muscles. (有關) 肌肉的","examples":["As a general rule, all muscular effort is enhanced by breathing in as the effort is made. 一般規律是，肌肉都透過用力吸氣而增強力量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or their body is <b>muscular</b>, they are very fit and strong, and have firm muscles which are not covered with a lot of fat. 強壯的","examples":["Like most female athletes, she was lean and muscular. 像大多數女運動員一樣，她精瘦而健壯。"]}]}]},"naive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天真的，幼稚的；（藝術風格）樸素的，原始的；缺乏閱歷的，輕信他人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>naive</b>, you think they lack experience and so expect things to be easy or people to be honest or kind. 幼稚的","examples":["It's naive to think that teachers are always tolerant. 認為老師總是很寬容是幼稚的。","Their view was that he had been politically naive. 他們的看法是，他在政治上曾是幼稚的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"幼稚地","examples":["...naively applying Western solutions to Eastern problems. …幼稚地用西方的辦法來解決東方的問題。"]}]}]},"obstinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"執拗的，固執的；棘手的，難以去除的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>obstinate</b>, you are being critical of them because they are very determined to do what they want, and refuse to change their mind or be persuaded to do something else. 固執的","examples":["He is obstinate and determined and will not give up. 他固執、堅決，不會放棄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe things as <b>obstinate</b> when they are difficult to move, change, or destroy. 難以消除的","examples":["...rusted farm equipment strewn among the obstinate weeds. …散落在叢生的雜草中生了鏽的農具。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"固執地","examples":["I stayed obstinately in my room, sitting by the telephone. 我執意呆在自己的房間裡，坐在電話旁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"頑固地","examples":["...the door of the shop which obstinately stayed closed when he tried to push it open. …那扇他盡力想推開可又推不開的店門。"]}]}]},"noticeable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"顯而易見的，明顯的；值得注意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>noticeable</b> is very obvious, so that it is easy to see, hear, or recognize. 顯而易見的","examples":["It is noticeable that women do not have the rivalry that men have. 顯而易見的是女性沒有像男性那樣的爭強好勝。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"顯而易見地","examples":["Standards of living were deteriorating rather noticeably. 生活水平相當明顯地下降了。"]}]}]},"permissible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"允許的，許可的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>permissible</b>, it is considered to be acceptable because it does not break any laws or rules. 可允許的","examples":["Religious practices are permissible under the Constitution. 根據憲法，宗教行為是可允許的。"]}]}]},"nasty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"惡毒的，兇相的；令人不快的，令人厭惡的；（傷口、疾病等）嚴重的，惡性的；汙穢的，下流的；（外表）醜陋的，（氣味等）難聞的；造成很大傷害的；令人擔憂的，難對付的；有威脅性的，嚇人的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>令人不快的人（或事），危害別人的人（或事）；<非正式>恐怖錄影（或影片）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>nasty</b> is very unpleasant to see, experience, or feel. 可惡的 (事物)","examples":["...an extremely nasty murder. …一起極其令人厭惡的謀殺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>nasty</b>, you mean that they behave in an unkind and unpleasant way. 可惡的 (人或行為)","examples":["What nasty little snobs you all are. 你們是多麼可惡的勢利小人！","The guards looked really nasty. 那些警衛看上去真可惡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>nasty</b>, you mean it is unattractive, undesirable, or in bad taste. 低俗可厭的 (事物)","examples":["They should put warning labels on those nasty little devices. 他們應該在那些討厭的小裝置上貼警示標籤。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>nasty</b> problem or situation is very worrisome and difficult to deal with. 難對付的 (問題、情況等)","examples":["A spokesman said this firm action had defused a very nasty situation. 一位發言人說，這次果斷的行動已經緩解了僵局。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you describe an injury or a disease as <b>nasty</b>, you mean that it is serious or looks unpleasant. (傷、疾病等) 嚴重的","examples":["My little granddaughter caught her heel in the spokes of her bicycle – it was a very nasty wound. 我的小孫女把她的後腳跟捲到她的腳踏車輻條裡了–傷得很嚴重。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可惡","examples":["...the nastiness of war. …戰爭的可惡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"厭惡地","examples":["She took the money and eyed me nastily. 她拿了錢，厭惡地盯著我。"]}]}]},"passionate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱誠的，狂熱的；熱戀的，情意綿綿的；易怒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>passionate</b> person has very strong feelings about something or a strong belief in something. 狂熱的; 熱誠的","examples":["...his passionate commitment to peace. …他對和平事業的狂熱信奉。","He is very passionate about the project. 他對這個專案非常熱誠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>passionate</b> person has strong romantic or sexual feelings and expresses them in their behaviour. 非常浪漫的; 性慾強的","examples":["...a beautiful, passionate woman of twenty-six. …一位美麗的、非常浪漫的26歲的婦女。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狂熱地; 熱誠地","examples":["I am passionately opposed to the death penalty. 我強烈地反對死刑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非常浪漫地; 性慾強地","examples":["He was passionately in love with her. 他熱戀著她。"]}]}]},"outgoing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛交際的，外向的；即將離職的；往外去的，離去的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>外出，離開物；<英>日常支出，開銷（outgoings）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"超過，優於（outgo 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outgoing</b> things such as planes, mail, and passengers are leaving or being sent somewhere. 往外去的","examples":["All outgoing flights were grounded. 所有的離港航班都停飛了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>outgoing</b> is very friendly and likes meeting and talking to people. 友好的; 喜歡交際的","examples":["She's very outgoing. 她非常友好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>outgoing</b> to describe a person in charge of something who is soon going to leave that position. 行將離職的","examples":["...the outgoing director of the International Folk Festival. …即將卸任的國際民俗節負責人。"]}]}]},"poetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"詩的，詩歌的；充滿詩情畫意的，富有想象力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>詩學，詩論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>poetic</b> is very beautiful and expresses emotions in a sensitive or moving way. 富有詩意的","examples":["Nikolai Demidenko gave an exciting yet poetic performance. 尼古拉·德米丹柯獻上了一場激動人心而又富有詩意的演出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Poetic</b> means relating to poetry. 詩歌的","examples":["...Keats' famous poetic lines. …濟慈的著名詩句。"]}]}]},"priceless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無價的；非常有用的；<非正式> 十分有趣的，極為可笑的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>priceless</b>, you are emphasizing that it is worth a very large amount of money, or that it is very important to you although it has little financial value. 無價的","examples":["They are priceless, unique and irreplaceable. 它們是無價的、獨一無二的，不可替代的。","Did Mom throw away your priceless Dungeons and Dragons magazine?. 媽媽扔掉了你那本寶貝雜誌《龍與地下城》嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>priceless</b>, you approve of it because it is extremely useful. 寶貴的","examples":["They are a priceless record of a brief period in Colorado history. 它們是科羅拉多歷史上一段短暫時期的寶貴記錄。"]}]}]},"prehistoric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"史前的，有文字記載以前的；<非正式>古老的，過時的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prehistoric</b> people and things existed at a time before information was written down. 史前的","examples":["...the famous prehistoric cave paintings of Lascaux. …拉斯科著名的史前洞穴繪畫。"]}]}]},"polar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極地的，來自極地的；截然不同的；磁極的；（天體）極性的，極地的；（細胞，器官，身體部分）極的；（液體，尤指溶劑）由偶極矩分子組成的；（固體）離子的；（幾何）（球體）軸極的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（幾何）極線；極光雙子星"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Polar</b> means near the North or South Poles. 極地的","examples":["...the rigours of life in the polar regions. …極地的艱苦生活。","There was a period of excessive warmth which melted some of the polar ice. 有段時期溫度過高，融化了極地的部分冰層。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Polar</b> is used to describe things that are completely opposite in character, quality, or type. (性格、質量或型別) 正好相反的","examples":["The nomads' lifestyle was the polar opposite of collectivization. 遊牧民的生活方式同集體化的生活方式剛好相反。"]}]}]},"reckless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"魯莽的，不計後果的；粗心大意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>reckless</b>, you mean that they act in a way which shows that they do not care about danger or the effect their behaviour will have on other people. 魯莽的; 不顧後果的","examples":["He is charged with reckless driving. 他被控莽撞駕駛。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"魯莽地; 不計後果地","examples":["He was leaning recklessly out of the open window. 他魯莽地從開著的窗戶探出身子。"]}]}]},"ridiculous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可笑的，荒謬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>ridiculous</b>, you mean that they are very foolish. 荒唐可笑的","examples":["It is ridiculous to suggest we are having a romance. 說我們之間有風流韻事真是荒唐可笑。"]}]}]},"ragged":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（衣服）破舊的；（人）衣衫襤褸的；高低不平的，參差不齊的；不流暢的，不規則的；精疲力竭的；不熟練的，蹩腳的；（尤指右邊距）未對齊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>ragged</b> looks messy and is wearing clothes that are old and torn. 衣衫襤褸的","examples":["The five survivors eventually reached safety, ragged, half-starved, and exhausted. 這5名倖存者最終到達了安全地帶，衣衫襤褸、餓得半死、筋疲力盡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ragged</b> clothes are old and torn. 破舊的","examples":["...an elderly, bearded man in ragged clothes. …一個上了年紀、留著鬍鬚、穿著破舊衣服的男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>ragged</b> when it is rough or uneven. 粗糙的; 參差不齊的","examples":["O'Brien formed the men into a ragged line. 奧布賴恩把這些男人排成了歪歪扭扭的一排。"]}]}]},"rugged":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（地面，地形）高低不平的，崎嶇的；（男人的外貌）粗獷而英俊的；強健而堅毅的；（機器或其他製造品）堅固耐用的；艱難的，嚴峻的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rugged</b> area of land is uneven and covered with rocks, with few trees or plants. 崎嶇多巖的","examples":["We left the rough track and bumped our way over a rugged mountainous terrain. 我們駛離坎坷的小道，又顛簸過了崎嶇多巖的山地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a man as <b>rugged</b>, you mean that he has strong, masculine features. (男子) 粗獷的","examples":["A look of pure disbelief crossed Shankly's rugged face. 尚克利粗獷的臉上掠過一副完全不信任的表情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's character as <b>rugged</b>, you mean that they are strong and determined, and have the ability to cope with difficult situations. 堅毅的","examples":["Rugged individualism forged America's frontier society. 堅定的個人主義鑄就了美國這個前沿社會。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>rugged</b> piece of equipment is strong and is designed to last a long time, even if it is treated roughly. 結實耐用的","examples":["The camera combines rugged reliability with unequalled optical performance and speed. 這款照相機集經久可靠性、無與倫比的光學效能和速度於一身。"]}]}]},"sacred":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"神的，神聖的；宗教的，宗教性的；受尊重的，受崇敬的；不可侵犯的，不容干涉的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>sacred</b> is believed to be holy and to have a special connection with God. 神聖的","examples":["The owl is sacred for many Californian Indian people. 貓頭鷹對於很多加利福利亞的印第安人來說是神聖的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something connected with religion or used in religious ceremonies is described as <b>sacred</b>. 宗教的","examples":["...sacred art. …宗教藝術。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe something as <b>sacred</b> when it is regarded as too important to be changed or interfered with. 不容更改的; 不容干涉的","examples":["My memories are sacred. 我的記憶不能泯滅。"]}]}]},"shabby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"破舊的，破爛的；（人）衣著破舊的，衣衫襤褸的；（行為）卑鄙的，不公正的；（質量）低劣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shabby</b> things or places look old and in bad condition. 破舊的; 破爛的","examples":["His clothes were old and shabby. 他的衣服又舊又破。"]}]}]},"rigid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（方法、體制等）嚴格死板的，僵化的；（人）頑固的，不通融的；剛硬的，不易彎曲的；（因強烈的感情而）僵硬的，僵直的；精確的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"未鉸接的貨車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Laws, rules, or systems that are <b>rigid</b> cannot be changed or varied, and are therefore considered to be rather severe. (法律、規章或制度) 僵死的; 過於嚴格的","examples":["Several colleges in our study have rigid rules about student conduct. 我們調查中的幾所學院對學生行為舉止都有過於嚴格的規定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you disapprove of someone because you think they are not willing to change their way of thinking or behaving, you can describe them as <b>rigid</b>. (人) 刻板的; 頭腦僵化的","examples":["She was a fairly rigid person who had strong religious views. 她是個相當刻板、有著很強宗教觀念的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rigid</b> substance or object is stiff and does not bend, stretch, or twist easily. 僵硬的","examples":["...rigid plastic containers. …堅硬的塑膠容器。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(法律、規章或制度的) 僵死; 過於嚴格","examples":["...the rigidity of government policy. …政府政策的僵化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"硬度","examples":["...the strength and rigidity of glass. …玻璃的強度與硬度。"]}]}]},"robust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"強健的，強壯的；（系統或組織）穩固的，健全的；（物體）結實的，堅固的；（觀點等）強烈的，堅定的；（食物或飲料）味濃的，醇厚的；特大的；粗野的，粗魯的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>robust</b> is very strong or healthy. 健壯的","examples":["He was always the robust one, physically strong and mentally sharp. 他一向是個健壯的人，身體強壯、頭腦敏銳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Robust</b> views or opinions are strongly held and forcefully expressed. 強有力的 (觀點、見解)","examples":["The Secretary of State has made a robust defence of the agreement. 國務卿對這項協議進行了強有力的辯護。"]}]}]},"sloppy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"馬虎的，草率的；（衣服）寬鬆的，肥大的；太稀的，不夠稠的；庸俗傷感的，過分動情的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's work or activities as <b>sloppy</b>, you mean they have been done in a careless and lazy way. 慵懶的; 馬虎的","examples":["He has little patience for sloppy work from colleagues. 他無法忍耐同事們馬虎的工作。"]}]}]},"sly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狡猾的，狡詐的；詭秘的，心知肚明的；（動作）躲躲閃閃的，偷偷摸摸的；淘氣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sly</b> look, expression, or remark shows that you know something that other people do not know or that was meant to be a secret. (眼神、表情或話語) 會意的","examples":["His lips were spread in a sly smile. 他的雙唇在會心的微笑中張開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>sly</b>, you disapprove of them because they keep their feelings or intentions hidden and are clever at deceiving people. 虛偽的; 狡詐的","examples":["She is devious and sly and manipulative. 她陰險、狡詐，而且愛操縱他人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"會意地","examples":["Anna grinned slyly. 安娜會意地咧嘴笑了。"]}]}]},"solemn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"表情嚴肅的，莊嚴的；（承諾、協定等）莊嚴的，鄭重的；（儀式）莊嚴的，隆重的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>solemn</b> is very serious rather than cheerful or humorous. (人) 嚴肅的; (物) 莊嚴的","examples":["His solemn little face broke into smiles. 他那嚴肅的小臉綻開了笑容。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>solemn</b> promise or agreement is one that you make in a very formal, sincere way. 正式的; 鄭重的","examples":["She made a solemn promise to him when they became engaged that she would give up cigarettes for good. 他們訂婚時，她向他許下鄭重的承諾，說她會永遠戒菸。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴肅; 莊嚴","examples":["The setting for this morning's signing ceremony matched the solemnity of the occasion. 今天早上簽字儀式的佈置符合這種場合的莊嚴氣氛。"]}]}]},"statistical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"統計的，統計學的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Statistical</b> means relating to the use of statistics. 統計的; 統計學的","examples":["The report contains a great deal of statistical information. 該報告包含大量統計資料。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"統計上地; 統計學上地","examples":["The results are not statistically significant. 這些結果在統計上沒有顯著意義。"]}]}]},"stout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）肥胖的，壯實的；厚而結實的；不屈不撓的，頑強的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"烈性黑啤酒；特大號衣服；胖子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stout</b> person is rather fat. 肥胖的","examples":["He was a tall, stout man with grey hair. 他是一個又高又胖、滿頭銀髮的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Stout</b> shoes, branches, or other objects are thick and strong. (鞋、枝條等物體) 結實的","examples":["I hope you've both got stout shoes. 我希望你們兩個都穿結實的鞋。"]}]}]},"straightforward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"簡單的，易懂的；（人）誠實的，坦率的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"直截了當地，坦率地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>straightforward</b>, you approve of it because it is easy to do or understand. 容易的; 易懂的","examples":["Disposable diapers are fairly straightforward to put on. 一次性尿布非常容易穿。","The question seemed straightforward enough. 這個問題看起來夠容易的了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>straightforward</b>, you approve of them because they are honest and direct, and do not try to hide their feelings. 坦率的","examples":["She is very blunt, very straightforward, and very honest. 她直言不諱，非常坦率，也非常誠實。"]}]}]},"stern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人或其態度）嚴厲的，認真的；（工作等）嚴峻的，棘手的；不屈從的，不動搖的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"船尾，艉部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stern</b> words or actions are very severe. (話語或行為) 嚴厲的","examples":["Mr. Monroe issued a stern warning to those who persist in violence. 門羅先生向那些頑守暴力之徒發出嚴厲警告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>stern</b> is very serious and strict. 苛刻的","examples":["Her father was stern and hard to please. 她父親苛刻，不易討好。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴厲地","examples":["\"We will take the necessary steps,\" she said sternly. “我們將採取必要措施，”她嚴厲地說道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the rear or after part of a vessel, opposite the bow or stem 船尾; 艉","examples":[]}]}]},"stylish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"時髦的，流行的，有格調的；瀟灑的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>stylish</b> is elegant and fashionable. 有格調的; 時髦的","examples":["...a very attractive and very stylish woman of 27. …一個非常迷人又非常時髦的27歲女子。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有格調地; 時髦地","examples":["...stylishly dressed middle-aged women. …衣著時髦的中年女人們。"]}]}]},"sturdy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"結實的，堅固的；（人或身體）強壯的，健壯的；堅決的，堅定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（絛蟲幼蟲在腦中形成包囊使綿羊產生的）暈倒病，蹣跚病"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>sturdy</b> looks strong and is unlikely to be easily injured or damaged. 結實的; 堅固的","examples":["She was a short, sturdy woman in her early sixties. 她是一位六十出頭、矮小結實的女人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"結實地; 堅固地","examples":["It was a good table too, sturdily constructed of elm. 它也是一張很好的桌子，榆木做的，很結實。"]}]}]},"structural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"建築結構的；建築用的；結構（或構造）上的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Structural</b> means relating to or affecting the structure of something. 結構上的","examples":["The explosion caused little structural damage to the office towers themselves. 這次爆炸對辦公大樓本身幾乎沒有造成結構上的破壞。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在結構上","examples":["When we bought the house, it was structurally sound, but I decided to redecorate throughout. 我們買下這個房子時，它在結構上很完好，但我決定全部重新裝修。"]}]}]},"substantial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大量的，價值巨大的；牢固的，結實的；基本的，實質性的；（飯菜）豐盛的；重要的，真實的；有地位的，富有的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要材料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Substantial</b> means large in amount or degree. 大量的; 很大程度的","examples":["A substantial number of mothers with young children are deterred from undertaking paid work because they lack access to childcare. 很多有小孩的母親找不到人照顧小孩，從而無法從事有薪工作。"]}]}]},"superficial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗淺的，粗略的；（思想）淺薄的，缺乏深度的；表面的，乍看起來的（尤指實際並非如此）；（傷勢或傷害）表皮的；（皮膚、土壤或岩石）表層的；不重要的，無關痛癢的；<英>（建築）面積的，平方的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>superficial</b>, you disapprove of them because they do not think deeply, and have little understanding of anything serious or important. (人) 膚淺的","examples":["This guy is a superficial yuppie with no intellect whatsoever. 這個傢伙是個膚淺的雅皮士，沒有任何智慧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something such as an action, feeling, or relationship as <b>superficial</b>, you mean that it includes only the simplest and most obvious aspects of that thing, and not those aspects which require more effort to deal with or understand. (行動、感情、關係等) 淺表的","examples":["Their arguments do not withstand the most superficial scrutiny. 他們的論點經不起最為淺表的細察。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Superficial</b> is used to describe the appearance of something or the impression that it gives, especially if its real nature is very different. 表面上的","examples":["Despite these superficial resemblances, this is a darker work than her earlier novels. 儘管有這些表面的相似，這相比她早期的小說是一部更悲觀的作品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Superficial</b> injuries are not very serious, and affect only the surface of the body. You can also describe damage to an object as <b>superficial</b>. 表皮的 (傷、損壞)","examples":["The 69-year-old clergyman escaped with superficial wounds. 這位69歲的牧師帶著些皮肉傷逃脫了。"]}]}]},"supreme":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最高的，至高無上的；（政府、司法或軍事機構）擁有最高權力的；極大的，極度的；（處罰，犧牲）涉及死的；傑出的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"奶油沙司"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用工具處理水果（尤指柑橘類）以達到最佳效果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supreme</b> is used in the title of a person or an official group to indicate that they are at the highest level in a particular organization or system. 最高的","examples":["MacArthur was Supreme Commander for the allied powers in the Pacific. 麥克阿瑟是太平洋盟軍的最高司令官。","...the Supreme Court. …最高法院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>supreme</b> to emphasize that a quality or thing is very great. 極其的","examples":["Her approval was of supreme importance. 她的認可是極其重要的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極其地","examples":["She does her job supremely well. 她工作得極其出色。"]}]}]},"understandable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可以理解的，可以瞭解的，易懂的；情有可原的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour or feelings as <b>understandable</b>, you think that they have reacted to a situation in a natural way or in the way you would expect. 可以理解的","examples":["His unhappiness was understandable. 他的不高興是可以理解的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a statement or theory is <b>understandable</b>, you mean that people can easily understand it. (陳述、理論等) 易懂的","examples":["Roger Neuberg writes in a simple and understandable way. 羅傑·紐伯格的作品簡單易懂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可以理解地","examples":["Officials are understandably nervous about the tense situation in the neighbourhood. 官員們對這個地區的緊張局勢很感不安，這是可以理解的。"]}]}]},"tentative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"試探性的，暫定的；躊躇的，猶豫不定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不確定的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tentative</b> agreements, plans, or arrangements are not definite or certain, but have been made as a first step. 初步的","examples":["Political leaders have reached a tentative agreement to hold a preparatory conference next month. 政治領導人已經就下個月召開準備會達成初步協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>tentative</b>, they are cautious and not very confident because they are uncertain or afraid. 猶豫的","examples":["My first attempts at complaining were kind of tentative. 我頭幾次的投訴嘗試都有點兒猶豫。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"初步地","examples":["The next round of talks is tentatively scheduled to begin October 21st in Washington. 下一輪談判初步定在10月21日於華盛頓進行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"猶豫地","examples":["Perhaps, he suggested tentatively, they should send for Dr. Esteves. 他猶猶豫豫地建議道，他們也許應該派人去請埃斯特維斯醫生。"]}]}]},"vigorous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精力充沛的，充滿活力的；強壯的，強健的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vigorous</b> physical activities involve using a lot of energy, usually to do short and repeated actions. 用力的","examples":["Very vigorous exercise can increase the risk of heart attacks. 耗費大量體力的運動會增加心臟病發作的風險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vigorous</b> person does things with great energy and enthusiasm. A <b>vigorous</b> campaign or activity is done with great energy and enthusiasm. 精力充沛的 (人); 強有力的 (運動、活動)","examples":["Theodore Roosevelt was a strong and vigorous politician. 西奧多·羅斯福是一位身體強壯、精力充沛的政治家。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"用力地","examples":["He shook his head vigorously. 他用力地搖了搖頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"強烈地","examples":["The police vigorously denied that excessive force had been used. 警方堅決否認曾過度使用武力。"]}]}]},"toxic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有毒的，引起中毒的；令人極不愉快的，極其有害的，惡毒的；中毒的，中毒性的；（財政）（債務）有毒的，風險高的；（證券）有毒的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有毒物質，毒藥（toxics）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toxic</b> substance is poisonous. 有毒的","examples":["...the cost of cleaning up toxic waste. …清除有毒廢棄物的成本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a financial asset is described as <b>toxic</b>, it is likely to cause significant loss to the holder 有毒的(資產)","examples":[]}]}]},"transparent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"透明的，清澈的；（過程、活動或組織）透明的，公開的；明顯的，一目瞭然的；（謊言或藉口）易識破的；（思想、情感、動機）易被人所知的；（計算機）（過程、介面）透明的；（物理）可穿透的，（熱、電磁波）可透過的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object or substance is <b>transparent</b>, you can see through it. 透明的","examples":["...a sheet of transparent coloured plastic. …一片透明的彩色塑膠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation, system, or activity is <b>transparent</b>, it is easily understood or recognized. 易懂的; 顯而易見的","examples":["The company has to make its accounts and operations as transparent as possible. 該公司不得不盡力使它的帳目和運作一目瞭然。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>transparent</b> to describe a statement or action that is obviously dishonest or wrong, and that you think will not deceive people. If a person is transparent, you can see their true bad motives. 易識破的","examples":["He thought he could fool people with transparent deceptions. 他以為他能用易識破的騙術愚弄人。","He's so transparent. 他很容易被識破。"]}]}]},"wary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小心翼翼的，謹慎的，警戒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>wary</b> <b>of</b> something or someone, you are cautious because you do not know much about them and you believe they may be dangerous or cause problems. 小心的; 提防的","examples":["People did not teach their children to be wary of strangers. 人們以前沒教過自己的孩子們要提防陌生人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"小心地; 謹慎地","examples":["She studied me warily, as if I might turn violent. 她警惕地盯著我，好像我會變得很粗暴似的。"]}]}]},"vague":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不明確的，不清楚的；（形狀）模糊的；（感情、記憶等）不完整的，不清晰的；含糊其詞的，閃爍其詞的；茫然的，心不在焉的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something written or spoken is <b>vague</b>, it does not explain or express things clearly. 含糊的","examples":["A lot of the talk was apparently vague and general. 這次會談的許多內容顯然是含糊而籠統的。","The description was pretty vague. 這項描述是相當含糊的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>vague</b> memory or idea of something, the memory or idea is not clear. 模糊的","examples":["They have only a vague idea of the amount of water available. 他們對於可用水量只有一點模糊的瞭解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>vague</b> about something, you deliberately do not tell people much about it. 含糊其辭的","examples":["He was vague, however, about just what U.S. forces might actually do. 然而，他對於美國軍隊真正可能做什麼卻含糊其辭。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as a feeling is <b>vague</b>, you experience it only slightly. (感覺等) 輕微的","examples":["He was conscious of that vague feeling of irritation again. 他又一次感到微微有些惱火。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>vague</b> shape or outline is not clear and is therefore not easy to see. 模糊不清的","examples":["The bus was a vague shape in the distance. 遠處的那輛公共汽車只是一個模糊不清的輪廓。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"含糊地","examples":["\"I'm not sure,\" Liz said vaguely. “我不能肯定，” 莉茲含糊地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"模糊地","examples":["Judith could vaguely remember her mother lying on the sofa. 朱迪斯能夠模糊地記得她母親當時正躺在沙發上。"]}]}]},"widespread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"普遍的，廣泛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>widespread</b> exists or happens over a large area, or to a great extent. 廣泛的","examples":["There is widespread support for the new proposals. 這些新提案得到廣泛的支援。"]}]}]},"wholesome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（食物）有益健康的；有益身心健康的，增進身心健康的；（顯得）健康的，朝氣蓬勃的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>wholesome</b>, you approve of it because you think it is likely to have a positive influence on people's behaviour or mental state, especially because it does not involve anything sexually immoral. 有益身心的 (尤指不涉及非道德的性內容)","examples":["The Dove Foundation aims to promote wholesome family entertainment. 達夫基金會旨在倡導有益身心的家庭娛樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe food as <b>wholesome</b>, you approve of it because you think it is good for your health. (食物) 有益健康的","examples":["...fresh, wholesome ingredients. …有益健康的新鮮配料。"]}]}]},"worthwhile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重要的，有益的，值得做的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>worthwhile</b>, it is enjoyable or useful, and worth the time, money, or effort that is spent on it. 值得的","examples":["The president's trip to Washington this week seems to have been worthwhile. 該總統本週的華盛頓之行似乎是值得的。"]}]}]},"weird":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇怪的，不尋常的；怪異的，超自然的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"命運；預言者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美，非正式>使心生疑惑，使感到疏遠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>weird</b>, you mean that they are strange. 奇怪的","examples":["That first day was weird. 第一天很奇怪。","Drugs can make you do all kinds of weird things. 毒品可以讓你做出各種各樣奇怪的事情來。"]}]}]},"worthy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"值得尊敬的，值得注意的，值得敬仰的；值得的，應得的，相配的；好（但乏味）的；有（某人或事物）的典型特徵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"知名人士，要人（常為玩笑或貶義）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing is <b>worthy</b> <b>of</b> something, they deserve it because they have the qualities or abilities required. 應得的","examples":["The bank might think you're worthy of a loan. 這家銀行可能認為你應該得到一筆貸款。"]}]}]},"abolish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"廢除，廢止，取消"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>abolishes</b> a system or practice, they formally put an end to it. 廢除","examples":["An Illinois House committee voted Thursday to abolish the death penalty. 伊利諾伊州議院的一個委員會在星期四投票廢除了死刑。"]}]}]},"abide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遵守（abide by）；容忍，忍受；<舊>居住，逗留；（感情，記憶）始終不渝，持續"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>can't abide</b> someone or something, you dislike them very much. 無法容忍","examples":["I can't abide people who can't make up their minds. 我無法容忍下定不了決心的人。"]}]}]},"adore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"非常喜歡，熱愛；愛慕，疼愛；崇拜，崇敬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>adore</b> someone, you feel great love and admiration for them. 愛慕 (某人)","examples":["She adored her parents and would do anything to please them. 她深愛她的父母，願做任何事來讓他們高興。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>adore</b> something, you like it very much. 很喜歡 (某物)","examples":["My mother adores bananas and eats two a day. 我媽媽很喜歡香蕉，一天吃兩根。"]}]}]},"accustom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使習慣於，使適應於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>accustom</b> <b>yourself</b> or another person <b>to</b> something, you make yourself or them become used to it. 使習慣","examples":["She tried to accustom herself to the tight bandages. 她嘗試著使自己習慣那些緊繃的繃帶。"]}]}]},"alter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"改變，改動；（使）變化；改（服裝）；改建（某建築）；<美>閹割"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>alters</b> or if you <b>alter</b> it, it changes. 更改","examples":["Nothing has altered and the deadline still stands. 什麼也沒有更改，最後期限依然有效。"]}]}]},"acknowledge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"承認；認可； 跟……打招呼，理會；告知收到；（公開）感謝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>acknowledge</b> a fact or a situation, you accept or admit that it is true or that it exists. 承認 (事實或情況)","examples":["Naylor acknowledged, in a letter to the judge, that he was a drug addict. 在一封寫給法官的信中，內勒承認他是一個吸毒者。","Belatedly, the government has acknowledged the problem. 政府過晚地承認了這個問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's achievements, status, or qualities <b>are acknowledged</b>, they are known about and recognized by a lot of people, or by a particular group of people. 認可 (某人的成就、地位或品質)","examples":["He is also acknowledged as an excellent goalkeeper. 他還被認可為一名優秀的守門員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>acknowledge</b> a message or letter, you write to the person who sent it in order to say that you have received it. 確認收到","examples":["The army sent me a postcard acknowledging my request. 軍方寄給我一張明信片以確認收到了我的請求。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>acknowledge</b> someone, for example, by moving your head or smiling, you show that you have seen and recognized them. (點頭或微笑) 向…致意","examples":["He saw her but refused to even acknowledge her. 他看到了她，但甚至都拒絕向她致意。"]}]}]},"beautify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使美麗，美化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>beautify</b> something, you make it look more beautiful. 美化","examples":["Claire worked to beautify the garden. 克萊爾為美化花園工作著。"]}]}]},"ascend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攀登，登上；上升，升高，通往高處；升職，晉升；追溯，溯源"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ascend</b> a hill or staircase, you go up it. 上 (山、樓梯)","examples":["Mrs. Clayton had to hold Lizzie's hand as they ascended the steps. 上臺階時克萊頓夫人不得不抓著莉齊的手。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a staircase or path <b>ascends</b>, it leads up to a higher position. (樓梯或路) 向上延伸","examples":["A number of staircases ascend from the cobbled streets onto the ramparts. 若干個階梯從鵝卵石街道向上延伸到城牆上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>ascends</b>, it moves up, usually vertically or into the air. (通常垂直地) 向上移動","examples":["Keep the drill centred in the borehole while it ascends and descends. 當鑽頭上下鑽時，要把鑽孔保持在中心。"]}]}]},"applaud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鼓掌；稱讚，讚許"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a group of people <b>applaud</b>, they clap their hands in order to show approval, for example, when they have enjoyed a play or concert. 鼓掌","examples":["The audience laughed and applauded. 觀眾歡笑並且鼓掌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an attitude or action <b>is applauded</b>, people praise it. 稱讚","examples":["He should be applauded for his courage. 他應該因其勇氣而受到稱讚。","This last move can only be applauded. 這最後的舉措不得不受到稱讚。"]}]}]},"astonish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使吃驚，使驚訝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>astonishes</b> you, they surprise you very much. 使十分驚訝","examples":["My news will astonish you. 我的訊息會令你十分驚訝。"]}]}]},"beware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"當心，提防"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone to <b>beware</b> <b>of</b> a person or thing, you are warning them that the person or thing may harm them or be dangerous. 當心; 提防","examples":["Beware of being too impatient with others. 謹防對別人過於急噪。","Motorists were warned to beware of slippery conditions. 汽車駕駛者被提醒小心路滑。"]}]}]},"broaden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"增長（經驗、知識等）；變寬，變闊；（使）擴大影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>broadens</b>, it becomes wider. 變寬","examples":["The trails broadened into roads. 小徑變寬成大路了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>broaden</b> something such as your experience or popularity, or when it <b>broadens</b>, the number of things or people that it includes becomes greater. 擴寬; 開闊","examples":["We must broaden our appeal. 我們必須擴大我們的吸引力。","I thought you wanted to broaden your horizons. 我以為你想拓寬自己的視野。"]}]}]},"compel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"強迫，迫使；使發生，促使；<文>驅趕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation, a rule, or a person <b>compels</b> you <b>to</b> do something, they force you to do it. 迫使","examples":["...the introduction of legislation to compel cyclists to wear a helmet. …強制騎車人戴頭盔的法律的引入。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>feel compelled</b> <b>to</b> do something, you feel that you must do it, because it is the right thing to do. 感到必須 (做某事)","examples":["Dickens felt compelled to return to the stage for a final goodbye. 狄更斯感到必須返回舞臺作最後的告別。"]}]}]},"computerize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"用計算機做，使計算機化；給（某物）安裝計算機，用電腦裝備（某物）；把……輸入計算機，用電腦儲存"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>computerize</b> a system, process, or type of work means to arrange for a lot of the work to be done by computer. 使計算機化","examples":["I'm trying to make a spreadsheet up to computerize everything that's done by hand at the moment. 我正在試圖作一個電子表格程式來使我們現在用手工做的一切工作計算機化。"]}]}]},"cling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抓住，抱緊；黏附，粘住；依戀，依附；堅持，堅信；緊抓不放，堅守"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"粘核桃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cling</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you hold onto them tightly. 緊緊抓住","examples":["Another man was rescued as he clung to the riverbank. 另一個男人因為緊緊抓住了河堤而被救了。","She had to cling onto the door handle until the pain passed. 她不得不緊緊抓住門的把手，直到疼痛消失為止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>clings</b> <b>to</b> a position or a possession they have, they do everything they can to keep it even though this may be very difficult. 固守","examples":["Instead, he appears determined to cling to power. 反而，他看來堅決要握緊權力不放。","Another congressman clung on with a majority of only 18. 另一位國會議員在獲得僅僅18張多數票的情況下保住了位子。"]}]}]},"cite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引用，援引；引證，引以為例；傳喚，傳訊；嘉獎，表彰"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>引用，引文"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cite</b> something, you quote it or mention it, especially as an example or proof of what you are saying. 引用","examples":["She cites a favourite poem by George Herbert. 她引用了一首她所喜愛的喬治·赫伯特的詩。","Domestic interest rates are often cited as a major factor affecting exchange rates. 國內利率常常被援引為影響匯率的一個主要因素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>cite</b> a person means to officially name them in a legal case. To <b>cite</b> a reason or cause means to state it as the official reason for your case. 引證","examples":["They cited Alex's refusal to return to the marital home. 他們援引了亞歷克斯拒絕重返婚後住所這一事實為證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is cited</b>, they are officially ordered to appear before a court. 傳訊","examples":["He is the owner of a restaurant chain that was cited for violations of child labour laws. 他是那個因違反童工法而被傳訊的餐飲連鎖店的業主。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a judge <b>cites</b> someone, he or she officially names them in a critical way in court. 指控","examples":["The judge ruled a mistrial and cited the prosecutors for outrageous misconduct. 法官裁定判決無效並且指控控方有極其不端的行為。"]}]}]},"comprehend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"理解，領悟；包括，包含"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cannot <b>comprehend</b> something, you cannot understand it. 理解","examples":["I just cannot comprehend your attitude. 我就是不能理解你的態度。"]}]}]},"compute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"估算，計算；<美，非正式>不合情理，講不通；用計算機計算"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"計算，估計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>compute</b> a quantity or number means to calculate it. 計算","examples":["To compute your scores, merely add or subtract your scores for each item. 要計算你的分數，只需加減一下你每項上的得分。"]}]}]},"commute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"通勤，上下班往返；減輕（刑罰）；代償；（兩個運算，兩個量）可交換"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"通勤，上下班交通路程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>commute</b>, you travel a long distance every day between your home and your place of work. 通勤","examples":["Mike commutes to Miami every day. 邁克每天通勤去邁阿密。","McLaren began commuting between Philadelphia and New York. 麥克拉倫開始在費城和紐約之間通勤。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"通勤者","examples":["There are significant numbers of commuters using our streets. 有相當多的通勤者使用我們的街道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commute</b> is the journey that you make when you commute. 通勤的路程","examples":["The average Los Angeles commute is over 60 miles a day. 洛杉磯平均通勤路程每天超過60英里。"]}]}]},"conceal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"隱匿，隱藏；隱瞞（真實感情或真相）；遮蓋，遮住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>conceal</b> something, you cover it or hide it carefully. 掩蓋; 隱藏","examples":["Frances decided to conceal the machine behind a hinged panel. 弗朗西絲決定把那臺機器藏到一塊可開合的鑲板後面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>conceal</b> a piece of information or a feeling, you do not let other people know about it. 隱瞞 (資訊); 掩飾 (情感)","examples":["Robert could not conceal his relief. 羅伯特掩飾不住自己如釋重負的心情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>conceals</b> something else, it covers it and prevents it from being seen. 遮蓋","examples":["...a pair of carved Indian doors which conceal a built-in cupboard. …一對遮擋嵌入壁櫥的印度式雕花門。"]}]}]},"conceive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"構思，設想；使受孕，懷孕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cannot <b>conceive</b> <b>of</b> something, you cannot imagine it or believe it. 想像; 相信","examples":["I just can't even conceive of that quantity of money. 我簡直無法想像那樣一筆數量的錢。","We could not conceive that he might soon be dead. 我們無法相信他可能很快就會死去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>conceive</b> something <b>as</b> a particular thing, you consider it to be that thing. 認為","examples":["The ancients conceived the earth as afloat in water. 古人認為地球漂浮在水裡。","We conceive of the family as being in a constant state of change. 我們認為家庭是處於不斷變化之中的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>conceive</b> a plan or idea, you think of it and work out how it can be done. 構想出","examples":["She had conceived the idea of a series of novels, each of which would reveal some aspect of Chinese life. 她已經想出了個關於一個系列小說的主意，每一部都將反映中國人生活的某一方面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a woman <b>conceives</b> a child or <b>conceives</b>, she becomes pregnant. 懷 (胎); 懷孕","examples":["Women, he says, should give up alcohol before they plan to conceive. 他說女人在計劃懷孕前應該戒酒。"]}]}]},"condemn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"譴責，嚴厲指責；宣判，判決；使陷入（不愉快的境地）；宣佈……不安全；證明（或表明）有罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>condemn</b> something, you say that it is very bad and unacceptable. 譴責; 責備","examples":["Political leaders united yesterday to condemn the latest wave of violence. 政治領袖們昨天聯合譴責最近發生的一波暴力事件。","Graham was right to condemn his players for lack of ability, attitude, and application. 格雷厄姆責備他的隊員缺乏能力、態度不端正以及不肯用功，這是對的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is condemned</b> <b>to</b> a punishment, they are given this punishment. 判 (某人某罪)","examples":["He was condemned to life imprisonment. 他被判終身監禁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If circumstances <b>condemn</b> you <b>to</b> an unpleasant situation, they make it certain that you will suffer in that way. 迫使 (陷於不幸的境地)","examples":["Their lack of qualifications condemned them to a lifetime of boring, usually poorly-paid work. 他們資歷的缺乏迫使他們要一輩子做單調乏味且通常報酬很低的工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If authorities <b>condemn</b> a building, they officially decide that it is not safe and must be pulled down or repaired. 確定 (某建築物) 為危房","examples":["The court's ruling clears the way to condemn buildings in the area. 法院的裁決為確定這一地區的建築物為危房掃清了障礙。"]}]}]},"contaminate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"汙染，弄髒；毒害，腐蝕（人的思想或品德）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is contaminated</b> <b>by</b> dirt, chemicals, or radiation, they make it dirty or harmful. 汙染","examples":["Have any fish been contaminated in the Arctic Ocean? 北冰洋裡有魚受到汙染了嗎?"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"汙染","examples":["The contamination of the ocean around Puget Sound may be just the beginning. 普吉特海灣周圍海域的汙染可能才開始。"]}]}]},"contend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"聲稱，主張；競爭，爭奪；處理，對付"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have to <b>contend with</b> a problem or difficulty, you have to deal with it or overcome it. 解決","examples":["It is time, once again, to contend with racism. 又是對付種族主義的時候了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contend</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you state or argue that it is true. 辯稱","examples":["The government contends that he is fundamentalist. 政府辯稱他是原教旨主義者。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contend</b> <b>with</b> someone <b>for</b> something such as power, you compete with them to try to get it. 爭奪 (權力等)","examples":["...the two main groups contending for power. …爭奪權力的兩大主要集團。","Small-market clubs such as the Kansas City Royals have had trouble contending with richer teams for championships. 像堪薩斯城皇家隊這樣市場規模較小的俱樂部一直難以同財力更雄厚的球隊爭奪冠軍。"]}]}]},"contemplate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"沉思，深思熟慮；盤算，打算；凝視，注視；考慮接受（發生某事的可能性）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contemplate</b> an action, you think about whether to do it or not. 考慮","examples":["For a time he contemplated a career as an army medical doctor. 他曾一度考慮做一名軍醫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>contemplate</b> an idea or subject, you think about it carefully for a long time. 對…考慮再三","examples":["As he lay in his hospital bed that night, he cried as he contemplated his future. 那天晚上他躺在醫院病床上，當他反覆考慮自己的未來時他哭了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>contemplate</b> something or someone, you look at them for a long time. 凝視","examples":["He contemplated his hands, still frowning. 他凝視著他的雙手，依然皺著眉頭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"考慮再三","examples":["It is a place of quiet contemplation. 這是一個適合靜靜深思的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"凝視","examples":["He was lost in the contemplation of the landscape for a while. 他沉湎在對風景的凝視中好一會兒。"]}]}]},"despise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鄙視，厭惡，看不起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>despise</b> something or someone, you dislike them and have a very low opinion of them. 鄙視","examples":["I can never, ever forgive him. I despise him. 我永遠，永遠都不會原諒他。我鄙視他。"]}]}]},"deceive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"欺騙，矇騙；使誤信，誤導；對（丈夫、妻子或伴侶）不忠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deceive</b> someone, you make them believe something that is not true, usually in order to get some advantage for yourself. 欺騙","examples":["He has deceived and disillusioned us all. 他欺騙了我們所有人, 令我們所有人失望至極。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>deceives</b> you, it gives you a wrong impression and makes you believe something that is not true. 誤導","examples":["Do not be deceived by claims on food labels like \"light\" or \"low fat.\" 不要被食品標籤上像“少脂”或“低脂”的字樣誤導。"]}]}]},"confront":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"面對，面臨；正視，處理；對峙，對抗；對質，當面對證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are confronted</b> <b>with</b> a problem, task, or difficulty, you have to deal with it. 面臨 (問題、任務、困難等)","examples":["She was confronted with severe money problems. 她面臨嚴重的資金問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>confront</b> a difficult situation or issue, you accept the fact that it exists and try to deal with it. 正視 (困難局面或問題)","examples":["We are learning how to confront death. 我們在學習如何正視死亡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are confronted</b> by something that you find threatening or difficult to deal with, it is there in front of you. 面對 (有威脅或難處理的事物)","examples":["I was confronted with an array of knobs, levers, and switches. 我面對著一排旋鈕、控制桿和開關。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>confront</b> someone, you stand or sit in front of them, especially when you are going to fight, argue, or compete with them. 與 (某人) 對峙 (尤指準備打鬥、爭論或競爭)","examples":["She pushed her way through the mob and confronted him face to face. 她從那群暴民中擠出來，與他當面對峙。","They don't hesitate to open fire when confronted by police. 他們一旦遭遇警察就毫不猶豫地開火。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>confront</b> someone <b>with</b> something, you present facts or evidence to them in order to accuse them of something or force them to deal with a situation. (以某事物) 與 (某人) 對質","examples":["She had decided to confront Kathryn with the truth. 她已決定用事實與凱瑟琳對質。","I could not bring myself to confront him about it. 我不能就此事讓自己與他對質。"]}]}]},"devour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"狼吞虎嚥地吃；如飢似渴地閱讀，熱切地看；吞噬，毀滅；充滿（感情）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>devours</b> something, they eat it quickly and eagerly. 狼吞虎嚥地吃","examples":["A medium-sized dog will devour at least one can of food plus biscuits per day. 一隻中等大小的狗每天至少要幹掉一罐食物外加餅乾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>devour</b> a book or magazine, for example, you read it quickly and with great enthusiasm. 急切地讀","examples":["She began buying and devouring newspapers when she was only 12. 她才12歲時，就開始買報紙並如飢似渴地閱讀。"]}]}]},"corrupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"腐敗的，貪汙的；不道德的，墮落的；有缺陷的，有錯誤的；<古>腐壞的，腐爛的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使腐化，使墮落；<古>腐蝕，汙染；損壞，破壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>corrupt</b> behaves in a way that is morally wrong, especially by doing dishonest or illegal things in return for money or power. 腐敗的","examples":["...to save the nation from corrupt politicians of both parties. …把國家從兩黨腐敗的政客們手中解救出來。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is corrupted</b> <b>by</b> something, it causes them to become dishonest and unjust and unable to be trusted. 使…腐化; 腐化","examples":["It is sad to see a man so corrupted by the desire for money and power. 看到一個人被金錢和權力慾望所腐蝕很可悲。","Power tends to corrupt. 權力容易造成腐化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>corrupt</b> someone means to cause them to stop caring about moral standards. 使…墮落","examples":["...warning that television will corrupt us all. …電視會使我們所有人墮落的警示。"]}]}]},"convert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）轉變，（使）轉換；（使）改變信仰，（使）皈依；（達陣後）得附加分；使……迷上，使……熱衷於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"皈依宗教者，改變信仰者；剛迷上……的人，最近開始熱衷於……的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>is converted</b> or <b>converts</b> <b>into</b> another, it is changed into a different form. 轉變","examples":["The signal will be converted into digital code. 訊號將被轉變成數字編碼。","...naturally occurring substances which the body can convert into vitamins. …可以在身體內轉化成維生素的天然物質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>converts</b> a room or building, they alter it in order to use it for a different purpose. 改建","examples":["By converting the attic, they were able to have two extra bedrooms. 透過改建閣樓，他們又多出了兩間臥室。","...the entrepreneur who wants to convert County Hall into a hotel. …想把縣政大廳改建成旅館的企業家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>convert</b> a vehicle or piece of equipment, you change it so that it can use a different fuel. 改裝","examples":["Save money by converting your car to run on used vegetable oil. 透過改裝你的汽車使其燃燒用過的植物油來省錢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>convert</b> a quantity <b>from</b> one system of measurement <b>to</b> another, you calculate what the quantity is in the second system. 換算","examples":["Converting metric measurements to U.S. equivalents is easy. 把公制度量衡換算成美製度量衡很容易。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone <b>converts</b> you, they persuade you to change your religious or political beliefs. You can also say that someone <b>converts</b> <b>to</b> a different religion. 改變信仰","examples":["If you try to convert him, you could find he just walks away. 如果你想讓他改變信仰，他會扭頭就走。","He was a major influence in converting Godwin to political radicalism. 戈德溫主要在他的影響下信仰了政治激進主義。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>convert</b> is someone who has changed their religious or political beliefs. 改變信仰的人","examples":["She, too, was a convert to Roman Catholicism. 她也改信羅馬天主教了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>convert</b> <b>to</b> something, you mean that they have recently become very enthusiastic about it. 熱衷…的人","examples":["As recent converts to vegetarianism and animal rights, they now live with a menagerie of stray animals. 作為最近開始熱衷素食主義和動物權利保護的人們，他們現在和一群流浪動物生活在一起。"]}]}]},"dispense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發放，分配；提供，施予；配（藥），發（藥）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>dispenses</b> something that they own or control, they give or provide it to a number of people. 分發","examples":["The union had already dispensed $60000 in grants. 工會已經分發了6萬美元的補助金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you obtain a product by getting it out of a machine, you can say that the machine <b>dispenses</b> the product. (機器) 售出 (商品)","examples":["For two weeks, the cash machine spewed out receipts apologizing for its inability to dispense money. 兩週了，自動取款機就輸出了一些因其無法提款而致歉的憑條。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a pharmacist <b>dispenses</b> medicine, he or she prepares it, and gives or sells it to the patient or customer. 配發; 配售 (藥)","examples":["Health officials hope to begin dispensing anti-retroviral drugs on a wide scale at the beginning of next year. 衛生官員們希望在明年年初開始大規模配發抗逆轉錄病毒藥物。"]}]}]},"dwell":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"居住，棲身；總是想著，嘮叨（dwell on）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dwell</b> <b>on</b> something, especially something unpleasant, you think, speak, or write about it a lot or for quite a long time. 細想; 詳述","examples":["\"I'd rather not dwell on the past,\" he told me. “我寧願不多想過去，”他告訴我。"]}]}]},"enroll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"登記；使加入；把……記入名冊；招收；錄取；（軍事）使入伍"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"登記；註冊；報名；參加；記入名冊"}],"sections":[]},"discriminate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"區分，辨別；歧視，區別對待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you can <b>discriminate</b> <b>between</b> two things, you can recognize that they are different. 區分","examples":["He is incapable of discriminating between a good idea and a terrible one. 他沒能力在一個好主意和一個壞主意之間進行區分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>discriminate</b> <b>against</b> a group of people or <b>in favour of</b> a group of people means to unfairly treat them worse or better than other groups. 不公平對待","examples":["They believe the law discriminates against women. 他們認為這項法律歧視婦女。","...legislation which would discriminate in favour of racial minorities. …會偏向少數民族的法規。"]}]}]},"dispose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"處理，放置，安排；使易於，使傾向於；丟掉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to deal with or settle 處理; 安排","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to give, sell, or transfer to another 給予; 賣給","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to throw out or away 扔掉","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"to consume, esp hurriedly 消耗; 尤指匆忙地","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"to kill 殺","examples":[]}]}]},"elevate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提拔，提升；抬起，提起；提高，增加；使情緒高昂，使興高采烈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something achieves a more important rank or status, you can say that they <b>are elevated</b> <b>to</b> it. 提拔","examples":["He was elevated to the post of president. 他被提拔到總裁的職位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>elevate</b> something <b>to</b> a higher status, you consider it to be better or more important than it really is. 抬高 (地位)","examples":["Don't elevate your superiors to superstar status. 不要把你的上級抬高到超級明星的地位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>elevate</b> something means to increase it in amount or intensity. 提高","examples":["Emotional stress can elevate blood pressure. 情緒緊張會使血壓升高。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>elevate</b> something, you raise it higher. 舉起; 抬高","examples":["A few times a day, elevate feet above heart level. 一天幾次把腳抬到高過心臟的位置。","I built a platform to elevate the bed. 我搭了一個臺子把床抬高了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"提拔","examples":["The elevation of the assistant coach to the head coaching position within only 9 months was a surprise. 這位助理教練僅僅在9個月內就被提拔到總教練的位置是件令人驚訝的事。"]}]}]},"elaborate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"複雜的，詳盡的；精心製作的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"詳細說明，詳盡闡述；精心製作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>elaborate</b> to describe something that is very complex because it has a lot of different parts. 複雜的","examples":["...an elaborate research project. …一項複雜的研究專案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Elaborate</b> plans, systems, and procedures are complicated because they have been planned in very great detail, sometimes too much detail. (有時過於) 周密的","examples":["...elaborate efforts at the highest level to conceal the problem. …最高層企圖掩飾這個問題的百般努力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Elaborate</b> clothing or material is made with a lot of detailed artistic designs. 設計繁麗的","examples":["He is known for his elaborate costumes. 他以其繁麗的服裝著稱。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"周密地","examples":["It was clearly an elaborately planned operation. 這顯然是一次經過周密策劃的行動。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>elaborate</b> a plan or theory, you develop it by making it more complicated and more effective. 周密制定; 周密發展","examples":["His task was to elaborate policies that would make a market economy compatible with a clean environment. 他的任務是周密地制定能夠讓市場經濟適合於無汙染的環境的政策。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"周密的制定; 周密的發展","examples":["...the elaboration of specific policies and mechanisms. …對具體政策和機制的周密制定。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>elaborate</b> <b>on</b> something that has been said, you say more about it, or give more details. 作詳細闡述","examples":["A spokesman declined to elaborate on a statement released late yesterday. 發言人拒絕對昨天晚些時候發表的一份宣告作出更多說明。"]}]}]},"entitle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給予（某人）權利，給（某人）資格；給......命名，給......題名"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are entitled</b> <b>to</b> something, you have the right to have it or do it. 使有權","examples":["If the warranty is limited, the terms may entitle you to a replacement or refund. 如果保修單有限制，這些條款可讓你有權換貨或退款。","They are entitled to first class travel. 他們有權享受頭等艙旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the title of something such as a book, film, or painting is, for example, \"Sunrise,\" you can say that it <b>is entitled</b> \"Sunrise.\" 給 (書、電影、畫作等) 命名","examples":["...a performance entitled \"United States.\" …一場名為“合眾國”的演出。"]}]}]},"ensure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"確保，保證；保護，使安全"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>ensure</b> something, or to <b>ensure</b> <b>that</b> something happens, means to make certain that it happens. 確保","examples":["We must ensure that all patients have access to high quality care. 我們必須確保所有的病人都能夠得到高質量的護理。"]}]}]},"exceed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"超過，超出；超越（限制）；優於，勝過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>exceeds</b> a particular amount or number, it is greater or larger than that amount or number. 超過 (某數量)","examples":["Its research budget exceeds $700 million a year. 其研究預算每年超過7億美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>exceed</b> a limit or rule, you go beyond it, even though you are not supposed to or it is against the law. 超越 (限制、規定)","examples":["He accepts that he was exceeding the speed limit. 他承認他當時超過了速限。"]}]}]},"equate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）等同；使（兩個或兩個以上事物）相等，使平衡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>equate</b> one thing <b>with</b> another, or if you say that one thing <b>equates</b> <b>with</b> another, you believe that they are strongly connected. 將…等同於; 等同於","examples":["I'm always wary of men wearing suits, as I equate this with power and authority. 我總是提防著穿制服的人，因為我將其等同於權力及權威。","The author doesn't equate liberalism and conservatism. 該作者沒有將自由主義等同於保守主義。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"等同","examples":["The equation of gangsterism with business in general in Coppola's film was intended to be subversive. 柯波拉電影中黑幫文化與普通事務的等同旨在具有顛覆性。"]}]}]},"excel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"精通，擅長；超過，勝過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>excels</b> <b>in</b> something or <b>excels</b> <b>at</b> it, they are very good at doing it. (在某方面) 擅長","examples":["Mary was a better rider than either of them and she excelled at outdoor sports. 瑪麗比他們倆騎得都好，她擅長戶外運動。","Academically he began to excel. 他開始在學術上脫穎而出。"]}]}]},"erect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搭建，建造；使豎立，豎起；創立，建立；安裝，裝配；（使）勃起"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"豎直的，直立的；豎起的；勃起的，堅挺的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>erect</b> something such as a building, bridge, or barrier, they build it or create it. 建造","examples":["Opposition demonstrators have erected barricades in roads leading to the parliament building. 反對派示威者在通往議會大廈的路上設定了路障。","The building was erected in 1900-1901. 該建築建於1900-1901年間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>erect</b> a system, a theory, or an institution, you create it. 建立","examples":["Japanese proprietors are erecting a complex infrastructure of political influence throughout America. 日本業主們正在全美國構建複雜的政治影響力網路。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People or things that are <b>erect</b> are straight and upright. 直立的; 豎直的","examples":["Stand reasonably erect, your arms hanging naturally. 儘可能站直，雙臂自然下垂。"]}]}]},"exclaim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"呼喊，驚叫，大聲說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Writers sometimes use <b>exclaim</b> to show that someone is speaking suddenly, loudly, or emphatically, often because they are excited, shocked, or angry. (因興奮、震驚、憤怒等) 突然呼喊; 驚叫","examples":["\"He went back to the lab,\" Inez exclaimed impatiently. “他回實驗室了，”伊內茲不耐煩地叫道。"]}]}]},"erupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"噴發；爆發，突然發生；（感情）迸發；（斑疹等）突然冒出；長牙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a volcano <b>erupts</b>, it throws out a lot of hot, melted rock called lava, as well as ash and steam. 噴發","examples":["The volcano erupted in 1980, devastating a large area of Washington state. 這座火山1980年噴發，摧毀了華盛頓州的大片地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If violence or fighting <b>erupts</b>, it suddenly begins or gets worse in an unexpected, violent way. 爆發","examples":["Heavy fighting erupted there today after a two-day cease-fire. 激烈的戰鬥在兩天的停火之後今天在那裡爆發了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people in a place suddenly become angry or violent, you can say that they <b>erupt</b> or that the place <b>erupts</b>. 爆發騷亂","examples":["In Los Angeles, the neighbourhood known as Watts erupted into riots. 在洛杉磯，一個叫做沃茨的街區爆發了騷亂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that someone <b>erupts</b> when they suddenly have a change in mood, usually becoming quite noisy. 爆發 (某種情緒)","examples":["Then, without warning, she erupts into laughter. 然後，突如其來地，她爆發出笑聲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"噴發","examples":["...the volcanic eruption of Tambora in 1815. …1815年坦布拉火山的噴發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"爆發","examples":["...this sudden eruption of violence. …這起暴力事件的突然爆發。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(某種情緒的) 爆發","examples":["...an eruption of despair. …一陣突然的絕望。"]}]}]},"exclude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（故意）不包括，把……排除在外；認為……不可能，排除……的可能；阻擋；開除（學生）；防止……的發生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>exclude</b> someone <b>from</b> a place or activity, you prevent them from entering it or taking part in it. 拒 (某人) 於 (某地、活動) 之外; 不包括","examples":["Many of the youngsters feel excluded. 很多年輕人感覺受排擠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>exclude</b> something that has some connection with what you are doing, you deliberately do not use it or consider it. 故意不用; 故意不考慮","examples":["In some schools, Christmas carols are being modified to exclude any reference to Christ. 在有些學校，聖誕頌歌正在被修改以去掉任何涉及基督的內容。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>exclude</b> a possibility means to decide or prove that it is wrong and not worth considering. 排除 (某種可能性)","examples":["I cannot entirely exclude the possibility that some form of pressure was applied to the neck. 我不能完全排除有些壓力作用到了頸部的可能性。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>exclude</b> something such as the sun's rays or harmful germs means to prevent them physically from reaching or entering a particular place. 阻擋","examples":["This was intended to exclude the direct rays of the sun. 這是用來阻擋太陽直射光線的。"]}]}]},"falter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"衰弱，衰退；結巴地說，支支吾吾地說；蹣跚，踉蹌；猶豫，躊躇；（目光）遊離，（微笑）僵住"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"躊躇；支吾；顫抖；（Falter）（美、德）法爾特（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>falters</b>, it loses power or strength in an uneven way, or no longer makes much progress. 衰退","examples":["Normal life is at a standstill, and the economy is faltering. 正常生活陷入停滯，經濟正在衰退。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>falter</b>, you lose your confidence and stop doing something or start making mistakes. 猶豫","examples":["I have not faltered in my quest for a new future. 我對嶄新未來的追求未曾猶豫過。"]}]}]},"execute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"執行，實施；處決；完成，表演（高難度動作）；製作（藝術作品）；（計算機）執行指令（或程式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>execute</b> someone means to kill them as a punishment for a serious crime. 處死","examples":["He said nobody had been executed as a direct result of the events. 他說沒有人作為這幾起事件的直接後果被處死。","One group claimed to have executed the hostage. 一個組織聲稱他們已處死了那名人質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>execute</b> a plan, you carry it out. 執行 (計劃等)","examples":["We are going to execute our campaign plan to the letter. 我們將嚴格執行我們的競選方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>execute</b> a difficult action or movement, you successfully perform it. 完成 (高難動作)","examples":["The landing was skilfully executed. 著陸熟練地完成了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"處死","examples":["Execution by lethal injection is scheduled for July 30th. 注射死刑定於7月30日執行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"執行","examples":["U.S. forces are fully prepared for the execution of any action once the order is given by the president. 美國軍隊做好了充分準備，一旦總統下令就採取行動。"]}]}]},"fascinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊>（尤指蛇）以眼神震懾（人，動物），使無法動彈；深深吸引，迷住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>fascinates</b> you, it interests and delights you so much that your thoughts tend to concentrate on it. 使著迷","examples":["Politics fascinated Franklin's father. 政治讓富蘭克林的父親著迷。"]}]}]},"heighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提高，增強"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>heightens</b> a feeling or if the feeling <b>heightens</b>, the feeling increases in degree or intensity. 加劇","examples":["The move has heightened tension in the state. 這一舉動加劇了該州的緊張局勢。","Cross's interest heightened. 克羅斯的興趣增強了。"]}]}]},"gobble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"狼吞虎嚥，大口吞食；吞併，攫取；（很快地）大量消耗；（雄火雞）咯咯叫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"公火雞快速的咯咯大叫聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gobble</b> food, you eat it quickly and greedily. 狼吞虎嚥地吃","examples":["Pete gobbled all the beef stew. 皮特狼吞虎嚥地吃完了所有的燉牛肉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gobble down</b> and <b>gobble up</b> mean the same as . 狼吞虎嚥地吃，同gobble","examples":["There were dangerous beasts in the river that might gobble you up. 那條河裡曾有危險的野獸，會把你吞吃掉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the loud rapid gurgling sound made by male turkeys 公火雞快速的咯咯大叫聲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a turkey) to make this sound 火雞叫","examples":[]}]}]},"gnaw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"反覆咬，啃，齧；（情緒、念頭等）折磨，使不安，困擾；侵蝕，腐蝕，逐漸消耗"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（常與 at、on、into 連用）反覆咬，啃，齧；（情緒、念頭等）折磨，使不安，困擾；侵蝕，腐蝕，逐漸消耗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or animals <b>gnaw</b> something or <b>gnaw</b> <b>at</b> it, they bite it repeatedly. 反覆齧咬","examples":["Woodlice attack living plants and gnaw at the stems. 木蝨會侵襲活體植物並不停地齧咬它們的莖。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a feeling or thought <b>gnaws at</b> you, it causes you to keep worrying. 困擾","examples":["...the nagging disquiet that had gnawed at him for days. …困擾了他數日、令他不得安寧的憂慮。"]}]}]},"graze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吃草；放牧；擦過；擦傷，擦破；<非正式>經常吃零食而不吃正餐，吃很多零食；<美，非正式>隨意地嘗試（或體驗、瀏覽）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擦傷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals <b>graze</b> or <b>are grazed</b>, they eat the grass or other plants that are growing in a particular place. You can also say that a field <b>is grazed</b> by animals. 放牧 (牛、羊等); (牛、羊等) 吃草","examples":["Five cows graze serenely around a massive oak. 5頭奶牛在一棵大橡樹附近安靜地吃草。","Several horses grazed the meadowland. 幾匹馬在牧場上吃草。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>graze</b> a part of your body, you injure your skin by scraping against something. 擦破皮","examples":["I had grazed my knees a little. 我的膝蓋擦破了一點皮。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>grazes</b> another thing, it touches that thing lightly as it passes by. 擦過","examples":["A bullet had grazed his arm. 一顆子彈擦過他的胳膊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>graze</b> is a small wound caused by scraping against something. 擦傷","examples":["Although cuts and grazes are not usually very serious, they can be quite painful. 儘管割傷和擦傷一般並無大礙，卻會很疼。"]}]}]},"induce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引誘，誘使；引起，導致；給（孕婦）引產，（用藥物）催生；歸納出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>induce</b> a state or condition means to cause it. 引起","examples":["Doctors said surgery could induce a heart attack. 醫生們說手術可能導致心臟病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>induce</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you persuade or influence them to do it. 引誘; 勸說","examples":["More than 4,000 teachers were induced to take early retirement. 四千多名教師被勸說提前退休。"]}]}]},"impose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"強制推行，強制實行；把（自己的觀點、信仰等）強加於；打擾，麻煩；把（活字頁）拼版；欺騙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>impose</b> something <b>on</b> people, you use your authority to force them to accept it. 強制實行","examples":["Fines are imposed on retailers who sell tobacco to minors. 向未成年人銷售菸草製品的零售商要被強制罰款。","A third of companies reviewing pay since last August have imposed a pay freeze of up to a year. 自去年8月以來，在審檢工資發放的公司中，有三分之一已經強行實施工資凍結長達1年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>impose</b> your opinions or beliefs <b>on</b> other people, you try and make people accept them as a rule or as a model to copy. 把 (觀點、信仰等) 強加於","examples":["Parents should beware of imposing their own tastes on their children. 父母應該提防把自己的興趣強加給孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>imposes</b> strain, pressure, or suffering <b>on</b> someone, it causes them to experience it. 使承受 (令人不快之事物)","examples":["The filming imposed an additional strain on her. 影片拍攝使她承受了額外的壓力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>imposes</b> <b>themselves on</b> you, they force you to accept their company although you may not want to. 使強迫接受","examples":["I didn't want to impose myself on my married friends. 我不想硬要我的已婚朋友們接受我。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"強制實行","examples":["...the imposition of sanctions against Pakistan. …對巴基斯坦制裁的強制實行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不合理的要求","examples":["I know this is an imposition. But please hear me out. 我知道這是個不合理的要求，但請聽我把話說完。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>imposes</b> <b>on</b> you, they unreasonably expect you to do something for them which you do not want to do. 不合理地要求","examples":["I was afraid you'd feel we were imposing on you. 我擔心你會覺得我們在不合理地要求你。"]}]}]},"inquire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"調查，查究；詢問，打聽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>inquire</b> about something, you ask for information about it. 查詢; 打聽","examples":["\"What are you doing there?\" she inquired. “你在那裡做什麼？”她問道。","He called them several times to inquire about job possibilities. 他給他們打了幾次電話打聽就業的可能性。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>inquire into</b> something, you investigate it carefully. 調查; 查究","examples":["Inspectors were appointed to inquire into the affairs of the company. 檢查員被派去調查該公司的事務。"]}]}]},"jaywalk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"亂穿馬路；不遵守交通規則橫穿馬路"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cross or walk in a street recklessly or illegally 亂穿馬路","examples":[]}]}]},"indulge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"沉湎，沉溺；縱容，遷就；滿足（情感、興趣、慾望等）；參加，參與（尤指違法活動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>indulge</b> <b>in</b> something or if you <b>indulge</b> <b>yourself</b>, you allow yourself to have or do something that you know you will enjoy. 使沉溺; 沉溺","examples":["Only rarely will she indulge in a glass of wine. 她只是偶爾才會喝上杯葡萄酒。","He returned to Ohio so that he could indulge his passion for football. 他重返俄亥俄以釋放自己對足球的激情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>indulge</b> someone, you let them have or do what they want, even if this is not good for them. 縱容","examples":["He did not agree with indulging children. 他不同意嬌慣孩子。"]}]}]},"inherit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繼承（遺產）；經遺傳獲得（品質、身體特徵等）；接手，承擔；接收（前所有者的事物）；<古>（尤作聖經翻譯和典故用語）得到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>inherit</b> money or property, you receive it from someone who has died. 繼承 (財產)","examples":["He has no son to inherit his land. 他沒有兒子來繼承他的土地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>inherit</b> something such as a task, problem, or attitude, you get it from the people who used to have it, for example, because you have taken over their job or been influenced by them. 接手; 接任","examples":["The Endara government inherited an impossibly difficult situation from its predecessors. 恩達拉政府從其前任手裡接過了一個極為困難的局面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>inherit</b> a characteristic or quality, you are born with it, because your parents or ancestors also had it. 經遺傳而得 (特徵、品質等)","examples":["We inherit from our parents many of our physical characteristics. 我們從父母的遺傳中得到許多體貌特徵。","Her children have inherited her love of sports. 她的孩子們從她那裡繼承了對體育運動的愛好。"]}]}]},"insure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……投保；為……提供保險；保證，確保；獲得（賠償數額的）支付"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>insure</b> yourself or your property, you pay money to an insurance company so that, if you become ill or if your property is damaged or stolen, the company will pay you a sum of money. 為…投保; 投保","examples":["For protection against unforeseen emergencies, you insure your house, your furnishings and your car. 為防止發生無法預料的緊急情況，人們給房屋、傢俱和汽車投保。","While many people insure against death, far fewer take precautions against long-term loss of income because of sickness. 雖然許多人買人壽險，但很少有人採取預防措施以避免因疾病而造成的長期收入損失。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>insure</b> <b>yourself against</b> something unpleasant that might happen in the future, you do something to protect yourself in case it happens, or to prevent it from happening. 使預防","examples":["All the electronics in the world cannot insure people against accidents, though. 不過，世界上所有的電子裝置並不能預防意外的發生。"]}]}]},"lessen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）縮小，（使）減少"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>lessens</b> or you <b>lessen</b> it, it becomes smaller in size, amount, degree, or importance. 減少; 降低; 減輕","examples":["He is used to a lot of attention from his wife, which will inevitably lessen when the baby is born. 他習慣了妻子無微不至的關心，這種關心在孩子出生以後將不可避免地減少。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"減輕","examples":["...increased trade and a lessening of tension on the border. …貿易的增加和邊境緊張局勢的減輕。"]}]}]},"kindle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"點燃，開始燃燒；激起，激發；（感情）激動起來；（兔）產仔；照亮，（使）發亮；著火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>kindles</b> a particular emotion in someone, it makes them start to feel it. 激發","examples":["The Second World War kindled his enthusiasm for politics. 第二次世界大戰激發了他的政治熱情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>kindle</b> a fire, you light paper or wood in order to start it. 點燃","examples":["I came in and kindled a fire in the stove. 我進來把爐子點著了。"]}]}]},"justify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是……的正當理由；對……作出解釋，為……辯解；使（文字）對齊；（在上帝的眼中）稱義，使有義；證明合法；整理版面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>justify</b> a decision, action, or idea means to show or prove that it is reasonable or necessary. 證明…有理","examples":["No argument can justify a war. 沒有任何理由能證明一個戰爭有理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>justify</b> printed text means to adjust the spaces between the words so that each line of type is exactly the same length. 使 (文字) 對齊","examples":["Click on this icon to align or justify text at both the left and right margins. 點選這個圖示調整文字，使其左右兩端對齊。"]}]}]},"lame":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瘸的，跛的，殘疾的；（尤指藉口或論據）站不住腳的，無說服力的；差勁的，拙劣的；<美，非正式>幼稚的，無能的（尤指社交方面）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（人或動物）跛（瘸），使殘廢"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"金銀錦緞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>lame</b>, they are unable to walk properly because of damage to one or both of their legs. 瘸的","examples":["He was aware that she was lame in one leg. 他知道她有一條腿是瘸的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an excuse, argument, or remark as <b>lame</b>, you mean that it is poor or weak. 站不住腳的","examples":["He mumbled some lame excuse about having gone to sleep. 他為剛才睡著咕噥了個站不住腳的理由。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The lame</b> are people who are lame. 瘸子","examples":["...the wounded and the lame of the last war. …在上次戰爭中受傷的和腿瘸的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"站不住腳地","examples":["\"Lovely house,\" I said lamely. “好漂亮的房子，”我勉強地說。"]}]}]},"magnify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放大，擴大；誇張，誇大；使（問題）加重，加劇；<古>讚美，頌揚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>magnify</b> an object means to make it appear larger than it really is, by means of a special lens or mirror. 放大","examples":["This version of the Digges telescope magnifies images 11 times. 這種型號的迪格斯望遠鏡能將影象放大11倍。","A lens would magnify the picture so it would be like looking at a large TV screen. 透鏡會把影象放大，這樣就會像看大電視螢幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>magnify</b> something means to increase its effect, size, loudness, or intensity. 增大","examples":["Poverty and human folly magnify natural disasters. 貧窮和人類的愚蠢加劇自然災難。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>magnify</b> something, you make it seem more important or serious than it really is. 誇大","examples":["They do not grasp the broad situation and spend their time magnifying ridiculous details. 他們沒有把握大局而把時間花費在誇大荒謬的細節上。"]}]}]},"linger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繼續存留，緩慢消失；流連，逗留；持續看（或思考）；苟延殘喘；消磨，緩慢度過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as an idea, feeling, or illness <b>lingers</b>, it continues to exist for a long time, often much longer than expected. (想法、感覺、疾病) 繼續存留","examples":["The scent of her perfume lingered on in the room. 她的香水味在房間裡久久不散。","He was ashamed. That feeling lingered, and he was never comfortable in church after that. 他很慚愧。這種感覺持續著，此後他在教堂裡就再沒有自在過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>linger</b> somewhere, you stay there for a longer time than is necessary, for example, because you are enjoying yourself. 繼續逗留","examples":["Customers are welcome to linger over coffee until around midnight. 顧客們可以慢慢品味咖啡到午夜。"]}]}]},"manifest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"顯示，表明；（鬼魂或神靈）顯靈，出現；（病症）顯現；把……列入貨單；顯化（指透過視覺化和積極思考來幫助夢想成真）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明顯的，顯而易見的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅客名單，載貨清單；貨運列車編組清單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>manifest</b>, you mean that it is clearly true and that nobody would disagree with it if they saw it or considered it. 明顯的","examples":["...the manifest failure of the policies. …這些政策明顯的失敗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Manifest</b> is also an adjective. 顯現出的","examples":["The same alarm is manifest everywhere. 同樣的恐慌在各地都已出現。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"明顯地","examples":["She manifestly failed to last the mile-and-a-half of the race. 她顯然沒有跑完1.5英里的比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>manifest</b> a particular quality, feeling, or illness, or if it <b>manifests</b> <b>itself</b>, it becomes visible or obvious. 顯現出","examples":["He manifested a pleasing personality on stage. 他在舞臺上表現出討人喜歡的個性。","The virus needs two weeks to manifest itself. 這種病毒需要兩週才能發作。"]}]}]},"mingle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在聚會中）應酬，交際；（使）混合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things such as sounds, smells, or feelings <b>mingle</b>, they become mixed together but are usually still recognizable. 混合","examples":["Now the cheers and applause mingled in a single sustained roar. 這時歡呼聲和掌聲匯聚成了一陣經久不息的轟響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"At a party, if you <b>mingle</b> <b>with</b> the other people there, you move around and talk to them. 交際","examples":["Go out of your way to mingle with others at the wedding. 在婚禮上你要主動地和別人交際。","Guests ate and mingled. 客人們邊吃邊交談。"]}]}]},"mediate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"調停，斡旋；影響……的發生，使……可能發生；促成（協議），找到……的解決辦法；引起，形成；傳遞，傳達；連線，溝通；處於中間地位"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"間接的；居間的，介於中間的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mediates</b> <b>between</b> two groups of people, or <b>mediates</b> an agreement <b>between</b> them, they try to settle an argument between them by talking to both groups and trying to find things that they can both agree to. 調解","examples":["My mom was the one who mediated between Zelda and her mom. 我媽媽是那個調解塞爾達和她媽媽的人。","United Nations officials have mediated a series of peace meetings between the two sides. 聯合國官員們已經調解了雙方的一系列和談。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"調解","examples":["The agreement provides for United Nations mediation between the two sides. 該協議為聯合國對雙方的調解奠定了基礎。"]}]}]},"mourn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"悼念，哀悼；對……感到痛心（遺憾）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mourn</b> someone who has died or <b>mourn</b> <b>for</b> them, you are very sad that they have died and show your sorrow in the way that you behave. 悼念","examples":["Joan still mourns her father. 瓊還在哀悼她的父親。","He mourned for his valiant men. 他為他的勇士們悼念。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mourn</b> something or <b>mourn</b> <b>for</b> it, you regret that you no longer have it and show your regret in the way that you behave. 為 (失去) …而痛惜","examples":["We mourned the loss of our cities. 我們為失去我們那些城市而痛惜。"]}]}]},"modernize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使現代化；變得現代化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>modernize</b> something such as a system or a factory means to change it by replacing old equipment or methods with new ones. 使現代化","examples":["...plans to modernize the refinery. …使精煉廠現代化的各項計劃。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"現代化","examples":["...a five-year modernization programme. …一個為期5年的現代化規劃。"]}]}]},"modify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修改，改進；修飾，限定；緩和，使溫和；使改形，使轉化；變（音）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>modify</b> something, you change it slightly, usually in order to improve it. 修改","examples":["The club members did agree to modify their recruitment policy. 俱樂部成員確已同意修改他們的入會政策。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"修改","examples":["Relatively minor modifications were required. 需要相對較小的修改。"]}]}]},"navigate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"導航，引路；航行於，橫渡；穿過，穿越；駕駛，操縱；瀏覽；（有效地）處理；(魚、動物或昆蟲)找到正確的行動方向；繞過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>navigates</b> a ship or an aircraft somewhere, they decide which course to follow and steer it there. 給 (船或飛機) 導航","examples":["Captain Cook was responsible for safely navigating his ship without accident for 100 voyages. 庫克船長負責了安全導航他的船，百次航行無事故。","The purpose of the visit was to navigate into an ice-filled fiord. 這次訪問的目的是為駛入一個冰雪覆蓋的峽灣導航。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a ship or boat <b>navigates</b> an area of water, it sails on or across it. 航行","examples":["...a lock system to allow sea-going craft to navigate the upper reaches of the river. 一個能使海輪航行至河流上游的船閘系統。","Such boats can navigate on the Hudson. 這樣的船能在哈得孫河上航行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>navigate</b> an obstacle, you move carefully in order to avoid hitting the obstacle or hurting yourself. 繞過","examples":["He's got to learn how to navigate his way around the residence. 他應該學會如何繞過這片住處。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"導航","examples":["The expedition was wrecked by bad planning and poor navigation. 這次探險因計劃不周和導航不利而失敗。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone in a car <b>navigates</b>, they decide what roads the car should be driven along in order to get somewhere. (為汽車) 導航","examples":["When travelling on fast roads at night it is impossible to drive and navigate at the same time. 夜晚在快速路上行駛時，不可能邊開車邊找路。","...the relief at successfully navigating across the Golden Gate Bridge to arrive here. …成功指引透過金門大橋抵達這裡的如釋重負。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When fish, animals, or insects <b>navigate</b> somewhere, they find the right direction to go and travel there. (魚、動物或昆蟲) 找到正確的行進方向","examples":["In tests, the bees navigate back home after being placed in a field a mile away. 在試驗中，蜜蜂們被放到一英里之外的田地中後，尋找到回家的路。"]}]}]},"nominate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提名，推薦；任命，指派；挑選，指定（事件的日期或地點）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（動植物）以種名命名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is nominated</b> for a job or position, their name is formally suggested as a candidate for it. (為工作、職位) 提名","examples":["This week one of them will be nominated by the Democratic Party for the presidency of the United States. 本週他們中的一人將被民主黨提名為美國總統職位的候選人。","The Security Council can nominate anyone for secretary-general. 安全理事會可以提名任何人為秘書長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>nominate</b> someone to a job or position, you formally choose them to hold that job or position. 任命","examples":["In 1967 Johnson nominated Thurgood Marshall to the Supreme Court. 1967年，約翰遜任命瑟古德·馬歇爾為最高法院法官。","She was nominated by the president as ambassador to Barbados. 她被總統任命為駐巴貝多大使。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something such as an actor or a film <b>is nominated</b> for an award, someone formally suggests that they should be given that award. (某人或某物) 被提名 (某獎項)","examples":["Practically every film he made was nominated for an Oscar. 他製作的每部電影幾乎都獲得了奧斯卡提名。"]}]}]},"outdo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"超過，勝過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>outdo</b> someone, you are a lot more successful than they are at a particular activity. 超過","examples":["It was important for me to outdo them, to feel better than they were. 對我來說重要的是超過他們，感覺比他們更好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>not to be outdone</b> to introduce an action which someone takes in response to a previous action. 不甘落後","examples":["She wore a lovely tiara but the groom, not to be outdone, had on a very smart embroidered waistcoat. 她戴著一個漂亮的冕狀頭飾，而新郎也不甘示弱，穿了一件很瀟灑的刺繡馬甲。"]}]}]},"notify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"通報，告知；申報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>notify</b> someone of something, you officially inform them about it. 通知","examples":["The skipper notified the coastguard of the tragedy. 船長通知了海岸警衛隊這一災難。","Earlier this year they were notified that their homes were to be cleared away. 今年早些時候他們被通知說他們的家將被拆除。"]}]}]},"overeat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"吃得過多，吃得過飽"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"過量食用（某種食物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>overeats</b>, you mean they eat more than they need to or more than is healthy. 吃得過多","examples":["If you tend to overeat because of depression, first take steps to recognize the source of your sadness. 如果你因為沮喪而打算暴食的話，首先要設法弄清你悲傷的來源。"]}]}]},"overdo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把……做得過分，誇張；使過於疲勞；對……表演過火；把（食物）烹調得過久"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"做得過分；表演過火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>overdoes</b> something, they behave in an exaggerated or extreme way. 把…做得過頭","examples":["The extent of the rise might indicate that it had been overdone. 上漲的程度可能顯示事情做得過頭了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>overdo</b> an activity, you try to do more than you can physically manage. 過度地做","examples":["It is important never to overdo new exercises. 重要的是，千萬不要過度進行一項新的鍛鍊。","It's important to study hard, but don't overdo it. 刻苦學習很重要，但不要超過極限。"]}]}]},"oversleep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"睡過頭，睡眠時間超過預定或應有的時間"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"睡過（某一時刻）；因睡過頭而錯過（鬧鐘、約定等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>oversleep</b>, you sleep longer than you should have. 睡過頭","examples":["I forgot to set my alarm and I overslept. 我忘了上鬧鐘，所以睡過了頭。"]}]}]},"overhear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"無意中聽到，偷聽到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>overhear</b> someone, you hear what they are saying when they are not talking to you and they do not know that you are listening. 無意中聽到","examples":["I overheard two doctors discussing my case. 我無意中聽到兩個醫生在討論我的病例。"]}]}]},"overwhelm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（感情上）使受不了，使不知所措；使大吃一驚；壓垮，使應接不暇；打敗，擊垮；<文> （水）漫過，淹沒；壓倒，制服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are overwhelmed</b> <b>by</b> a feeling or event, it affects you very strongly, and you do not know how to deal with it. (強烈地影響而) 使不知所措","examples":["He was overwhelmed by a longing for times past. 他陷入了一種對過去的渴望而不能自拔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a group of people <b>overwhelm</b> a place or another group, they gain complete control or victory over them. 徹底制服; 擊敗","examples":["It was clear that one massive Allied offensive would overwhelm the weakened enemy. 顯然同盟國一次大規模的進攻就會徹底擊敗已被削弱的敵軍。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(強烈地影響而使) 不知所措的","examples":["Sightseers may be a little overwhelmed by the crowds and noise. 觀光者可能被人群和噪聲搞得有點不知所措。"]}]}]},"perish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人或動物）慘死，猝死；湮滅，毀滅；（木頭、橡膠、食物等）腐爛，腐敗；<英，非正式> 經受酷寒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or animals <b>perish</b>, they die as a result of very harsh conditions or as the result of an accident. (因惡劣條件或事故) 死亡","examples":["Most of the butterflies perish in the first frosts of autumn. 大多數蝴蝶在秋季初霜來臨時死亡。"]}]}]},"perceive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"認為，理解；察覺，注意到；意識到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>perceive</b> something, you see, notice, or realize it, especially when it is not obvious. 感知到","examples":["Students must perceive for themselves the relationship between success and effort. 學生們必須自己去認識到成功與努力之間的關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>perceive</b> someone or something <b>as</b> doing or being a particular thing, it is your opinion that they do this thing or that they are that thing. 認為","examples":["Stress is widely perceived as contributing to coronary heart disease. 壓力普遍被認為能造成冠心病。"]}]}]},"persist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繼續存在，持續；堅持，執意；堅持說，反覆說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something undesirable <b>persists</b>, it continues to exist. (尤指不合意的事物) 繼續存在","examples":["Contact your doctor if the cough persists. 如果持續咳嗽，就與醫生聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>persist</b> <b>in</b> doing something, you continue to do it, even though it is difficult or other people are against it. 堅持; 執意","examples":["Why do people persist in begging for money in the street? 為什麼人們非要在街上討錢呢？","He urged the United States to persist with its efforts to bring about peace. 他敦促美國堅持努力實現和平。"]}]}]},"penetrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"刺入，穿透；打進（某地區或國家的市場）；滲入，打入（組織、團體等）；洞察，瞭解；被理解，被領悟；透過……看見，看穿；（以陰莖）插入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>penetrates</b> a physical object or an area, they succeed in getting into it or passing through it. 進入; 穿透","examples":["X-rays can penetrate many objects. X射線能穿透很多物體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>penetrates</b> an organization, a group, or a profession, they succeed in entering it although it is difficult to do so. (排除困難) 進入","examples":["...the continuing failure of women to penetrate the higher levels of engineering. …女性躋身工程業較高層級的連續失敗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>penetrates</b> an enemy group or a rival organization, they succeed in joining it in order to get information or cause trouble. 打入 (敵對組織)","examples":["The CIA had requested our help to penetrate a drug ring operating out of Munich. 中情局曾要求我們協助打入在慕尼黑外活動的一個販毒團伙。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a company or country <b>penetrates</b> a market or area, they succeed in selling their products there. 打入 (某市場或地區)","examples":["There have been around 15 attempts from outside Idaho to penetrate the market. 已有約十五次從愛達荷州以外打入該市場的企圖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"進入; 穿透","examples":["The thick walls prevented penetration by debris from the hurricane. 一堵堵厚牆阻擋了颶風帶來的碎片的穿透。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"打入","examples":["...the successful penetration by the KGB of the French intelligence service. …克格勃向法國情報機構的成功滲入。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"打入","examples":["...import penetration across a broad range of heavy industries. …橫跨廣泛重工業領域的進口滲入。"]}]}]},"prolong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拉長，拖長（感覺或活動）；<罕>延長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>prolong</b> something means to make it last longer. 延長","examples":["Mr. Chesler said foreign military aid was prolonging the war. 切斯勒先生說外國的軍事援助正在延長這場戰爭。"]}]}]},"plead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懇求，乞求；極力主張，極力為……辯護；（在法庭）申辯，認罪；（向法庭）陳述案情；以……為理由，提出……作藉口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plead with</b> someone to do something, you ask them in an intense, emotional way to do it. 懇求","examples":["The lady pleaded with her daughter to come back home. 那位女士懇求她的女兒回家。","He was kneeling on the floor pleading for mercy. 他正跪在地板上請求寬恕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone charged with a crime <b>pleads guilty</b> or <b>not guilty</b> in a court of law, they officially state that they are guilty or not guilty of the crime. 表示服罪/不服罪","examples":["Morris had pleaded guilty to robbery. 莫里斯已經承認犯有搶劫罪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plead the case</b> or <b>cause</b> of someone or something, you speak out in their support or defence. 為…辯護","examples":["He appeared before the committee to plead his case. 他出現在委員會上為他的案子辯護。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>plead</b> a particular thing as the reason for doing or not doing something, you give it as your excuse. 以…為藉口","examples":["Mr. Giles pleads ignorance as his excuse. 賈爾斯先生以不知情作為他的藉口。"]}]}]},"publicize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"宣傳，公佈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>publicize</b> a fact or event, you make it widely known to the public. 宣傳; 公佈","examples":["The author appeared on television to publicize her latest book. 作者出現在電視上宣傳她的新書。","He never publicized his plans. 他從未將他的計劃公之於眾。"]}]}]},"preach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"佈道，講道；宣揚，鼓吹；說教，訓誡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a member of the clergy <b>preaches</b> a sermon, he or she gives a talk on a religious or moral subject during a religious service. 布 (道); 佈道","examples":["At High Mass the priest preached a sermon on the devil. 在大彌撒儀式上，牧師布了一次有關魔鬼的道。","The bishop preached to a crowd of several hundred local people. 主教向一群幾百名當地人佈道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>preach</b> a belief or a course of action, they try to persuade other people to accept the belief or to take the course of action. 宣揚","examples":["He said he was trying to preach peace and tolerance to his people. 他說他正試圖向他的人民宣揚和平與寬容。","Health experts are now preaching that even a little exercise is far better than none at all. 如今，健康專家宣揚說，即使少量的運動也比一點不運動要好得多。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone gives you advice in a very serious, boring way, you can say that they <b>are preaching at</b> you. 說教","examples":["\"Don't preach at me,\" he shouted. “不要對我說教，”他喊道。"]}]}]},"prevail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"流行，盛行；（在比賽、競賽或爭辯中）擊敗，獲勝；佔優勢，佔上風；（繼續）使用；說服，勸服（prevail on/upon）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a proposal, principle, or opinion <b>prevails</b>, it gains influence or is accepted, often after a struggle or argument. 佔上風","examples":["We hoped that common sense would prevail. 我們希望常識能佔上風。","Rick still believes that justice will prevail. 裡克仍然相信正義會佔上風。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a situation, attitude, or custom <b>prevails</b> in a particular place at a particular time, it is normal or most common in that place at that time. 盛行; 普遍存在","examples":["A similar situation prevails in Canada. 同樣的情況在加拿大也普遍存在。","...the confusion which had prevailed at the time of the revolution. …在革命時期普遍存在的混亂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one side in a battle, contest, or dispute <b>prevails</b>, it wins. 獲勝","examples":["He appears to have the votes he needs to prevail. 他看來有他勝出所需要的選票。"]}]}]},"reap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得，收穫；收割（莊稼等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reap</b> the benefits or the rewards of something, you enjoy the good things that happen as a result of it. 獲得","examples":["You'll soon begin to reap the benefits of being fitter. 你很快就會獲得身體更健康帶來的好處。"]}]}]},"refute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 駁斥，批駁；<正式> 否認，辯駁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>refute</b> an argument, accusation, or theory, you prove that it is wrong or untrue. 駁倒","examples":["It was the kind of rumour that it is impossible to refute. 這是那種不可能推翻的謠言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>refute</b> an argument or accusation, you say that it is not true. 否認","examples":["Isabelle is quick to refute any suggestion of intellectual snobbery. 對於任何暗示她恃才傲物的話，伊莎貝爾都立即予以否認。"]}]}]},"rejoice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"非常高興，深感欣喜；<英>享有（用於吸引人注意奇特之處，尤指名字）（rejoice in）；<古>使感到高興，使喜悅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rejoice</b>, you are very pleased about something and you show it in your behaviour. 欣喜","examples":["Garbo plays the queen, rejoicing in the love she has found with Antonio. 嘉寶飾演沉浸在與安東尼奧愛情的欣喜中的王后。","Party activists in New Hampshire rejoiced that the presidential campaign had finally started. 新罕布什爾州的黨派積極分子們為總統競選活動終於開始而欣喜。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"欣喜","examples":["There was general rejoicing at the news. 這個訊息帶來一片欣喜。"]}]}]},"qualify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）有權去做；取得資格，達到標準；獲得參賽資格；使合格，勝任；符合，可算作；具體說明，使語氣緩和；修飾，限定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>qualify</b> in a competition, you are successful in one part of it and go on to the next stage. 透過預賽; 取得下一輪比賽資格","examples":["We qualified for the final by beating Stanford on Tuesday. 我們在星期二擊敗了斯坦福隊，取得了決賽資格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>qualifies</b>, they receive the certificate, licence, diploma, or degree that they need to be able to work in a particular profession. 取得資格; 獲得文憑","examples":["But when I'd qualified and started teaching it was a different story. 但是當我取得資格並開始從教時，情況就完全不同了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"透過預賽者","examples":["Kenya's Robert Kibe was the fastest qualifier for the 800 metres final. 肯亞的羅伯特·凱布是800米決賽入圍者中速度最快的選手。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>qualify</b> <b>as</b> something or to <b>be qualified</b> <b>as</b> something means to have all the features that are needed to be that thing. 使…符合 (某物的全部特徵); 符合","examples":["13 percent of American households qualify as poor, says Mr. Mishel. 13％的美國家庭稱得上是貧民，米歇爾先生說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>qualify</b> a statement, you make it less strong or less general by adding a detail or explanation to it. (透過增加細節、解釋) 使語氣緩和; 使…不太籠統","examples":["I would qualify that by putting it into context. 我會把它放入上下文中加以解釋。","Boyd qualified his opinion, noting that the evidence could be interpreted in other ways. 博伊德補充說明了他的觀點，指出證據可以用其他方式加以解釋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>qualify</b> for something or if something <b>qualifies</b> you for it, you have the right to do it or have it. (使) 有權做; (使) 有資格擁有","examples":["To qualify for maternity leave you must have worked for the same employer for two years. 你必須為同一僱主工作兩年才有資格休產假。","The basic course does not qualify you to practise as a therapist. 這門基礎課程並不能使你有資格當一名治療師。"]}]}]},"resent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"怨恨，憎惡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>resent</b> someone or something, you feel bitter and angry about them. 憎恨","examples":["She resents her mother for being so tough on her. 她恨她的媽媽對她如此苛刻。"]}]}]},"reside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>居住，定居；<正式>存在於；<正式>（權利、權力等）屬於；位（於）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>resides</b> somewhere, they live there or are staying there. 居住","examples":["Margaret resides with her invalid mother in a Seattle suburb. 瑪格麗特和她有病的媽媽住在西雅圖郊區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a quality <b>resides</b> <b>in</b> something, the thing has that quality. 存在","examples":["Happiness does not reside in strength or money. 幸福不存在於力量或金錢之中。"]}]}]},"reckon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"估算，計算；<非正式>料想，認為；把……看作；<英，非正式>期望，指望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reckon</b> that something is true, you think that it is true. 想","examples":["Toni reckoned that it must be about three o'clock. 託尼想一定是3點鐘左右了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is reckoned</b> to be a particular figure, it is calculated to be roughly that amount. 估算","examples":["The market is reckoned to be worth $1.4 bn in the U.S. alone. 這個市場僅在美國的價值估計就有14億美元。"]}]}]},"reproduce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"複製，翻印；模擬；再製造，再現；繁殖，生殖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you try to <b>reproduce</b> something, you try to copy it. 複製; 再造","examples":["The effect has proved hard to reproduce. 這種效果經證實很難再造。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reproduce</b> a picture, speech, or piece of writing, you make a photograph or printed copy of it. 複製; 影印","examples":["We are grateful to you for permission to reproduce this article. 我們很感激您允許我們影印這篇文章。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>reproduce</b> an action or an achievement, you repeat it. 重演","examples":["If we can reproduce the form we have shown in the last couple of months we will be successful. 如果我們能夠重演上兩個月表現出來的狀態，我們就會成功。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When people, animals, or plants <b>reproduce</b>, they produce young. 生育; 繁殖","examples":["...a society where women are defined by their ability to reproduce. …一個以生育能力來定位婦女角色的社會。","We are reproducing ourselves at such a rate that our numbers threaten the ecology of the planet. 我們繁衍得如此之快，以至於人口數量威脅到地球的生態系統。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"生育; 繁殖","examples":["Treatments using assisted reproduction techniques jumped 30 percent. 使用輔助技術的生育療法猛增了30％。"]}]}]},"repay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"付還，償還；報答，回報；值得付出（時間、努力等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>repay</b> a loan or a debt, you pay back the money that you owe to the person who you borrowed or took it from. 付還; 償還 (貸款、債務)","examples":["He advanced funds of his own to his company, which was unable to repay him. 他把自己的資金預付給公司，公司卻未能償還給他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>repay</b> a favour that someone did for you, you do something for them in return. 報答; 回報","examples":["It was very kind. I don't know how I can ever repay you. 太好了。我不知道怎樣才能報答你。"]}]}]},"recommend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"建議，勸告 ；推薦，介紹；使顯得吸引人，使受歡迎；<古> 把……交託給，把……託付給"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>recommends</b> a person or thing to you, they suggest that you would find that person or thing good or useful. 推薦","examples":["I just spent a holiday there and would recommend it to anyone. 我剛在那兒度過一個假期，願意向任何人推薦那裡。","\"You're a good worker,\" he told him. \"I'll recommend you for a promotion.\" “你是名好員工，”他說。“我要推薦你升職。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>recommend</b> that something is done, you suggest that it should be done. 建議","examples":["The judge recommended that he serve 20 years in prison. 法官建議判他入獄服刑20年。","We strongly recommend reporting the incident to the police. 我們強烈建議將此事報警。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something or someone has a particular quality to <b>recommend</b> them, that quality makes them attractive or gives them an advantage over similar things or people. 使受歡迎; 使有優勢","examples":["La Cucina restaurant has much to recommend it. 拉庫奇那餐館有許多值得稱道的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被推崇的","examples":["Though ten years old, this book is highly recommended. 儘管已出版10年了，這本書仍備受推崇。"]}]}]},"restrain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"制止，阻止；剋制，抑制；控制（某事物）；剝奪……的行動自由（或人身自由），管押；（安全帶）縛住（人或其身體部位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>restrain</b> someone, you stop them from doing what they intended or wanted to do, usually by using your physical strength. 制止","examples":["Wally gripped my arm, partly to restrain me and partly to reassure me. 沃利抓住了我的胳膊，部分是想制止我，部分是想安慰我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>restrain</b> an emotion or you <b>restrain</b> <b>yourself from</b> doing something, you prevent yourself from showing that emotion or doing what you wanted or intended to do. 抑制","examples":["She was unable to restrain her desperate anger. 她無法抑制她那不顧一切的憤怒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>restrain</b> something that is growing or increasing means to prevent it from getting too large. 限制","examples":["The radical 500-day plan was very clear on how it intended to try to restrain inflation. 這項激進的500天計劃在其想要如何試圖限制通貨膨脹上是非常清晰的。"]}]}]},"sharpen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變鋒利（尖銳，清晰）；（使）改善，提高；（使）加劇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your senses, understanding, or skills <b>sharpen</b> or <b>are sharpened</b>, you become better at noticing things, thinking, or doing something. 使敏銳; 增強","examples":["Her gaze sharpened, as if she had seen something unusual. 她眼睛一亮，好像看到了不尋常的東西。","He will need to sharpen his diplomatic skills in order to work with Congress. 他將需要增強外交技巧以與國會打交道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sharpen</b> an object, you make its edge very thin or you make its end pointed. 使變鋒利; 弄尖","examples":["He started to sharpen his knife. 他開始磨刀。"]}]}]},"slay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（以暴力）殺死；<美>（尤用於報章）謀殺；<非正式>給（某人）以極深印象，逗樂（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>slays</b> an animal, they kill it in a violent way. 屠殺","examples":["...the hill where St. George slew the dragon. …聖喬治屠龍之丘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>has been slain</b>, they have been murdered. 謀殺","examples":["Two Australian tourists were slain. 兩位澳大利亞遊客被謀殺了。"]}]}]},"shatter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）破碎，碎裂；破壞，摧毀（抽象物）；使極為驚愕難過，給予極大打擊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"碎片；受到極大打擊的狀態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>shatters</b> or <b>is shattered</b>, it breaks into a lot of small pieces. 粉碎","examples":["...safety glass that won't shatter if it's broken. …安全玻璃即使破了也不會粉碎。","The car shattered into a thousand burning pieces in a 200 mph crash. 這輛轎車在時速200英里的碰撞中裂成了數以千計燃燒著的碎片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>shatters</b> your dreams, hopes, or beliefs, it completely destroys them. 粉碎 (夢想、希望、信仰等)","examples":["A failure would shatter the hopes of many people. 一次失敗會粉碎很多人的希望。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is shattered</b> by an event, it shocks and upsets them very much. 嚴重打擊","examples":["He had been shattered by his son's death. 兒子的死使他很受打擊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粉碎","examples":["...the shattering of glass. …玻璃的粉碎。"]}]}]},"revive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）復原，（使）復甦；重新喚起，重新記起；重新使用，使復興；重新上演"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as the economy, a business, a trend, or a feeling <b>is revived</b> or when it <b>revives</b>, it becomes active, popular, or successful again. 恢復; 復興","examples":["...an attempt to revive the economy. …一次重振經濟的嘗試。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>revives</b> a play, opera, or ballet, they present a new production of it. 重新上演 (作品的新版)","examples":["His plays continue to be revived both here and abroad. 他的劇作在國內外繼續重新上演。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>revive</b> someone who has fainted or if they <b>revive</b>, they become conscious again. 使甦醒; 甦醒","examples":["She and a neighbour tried in vain to revive him. 她和一個鄰居試圖使他甦醒過來，卻沒有成功。"]}]}]},"sober":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"未喝醉的，清醒的；嚴肅的，冷靜的；素淡的，樸素的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變得持重，變得冷靜；（使）醒酒，（使）清醒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>sober</b>, you are not drunk. 清醒的","examples":["He'd been drunk when I arrived. Now he was sober. 我到的時候他已經喝醉了。現在他清醒了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sober</b> person is serious and thoughtful. 嚴肅的","examples":["We are now far more sober and realistic. 我們現在嚴肅多了，也現實多了。","It was a room filled with sad, sober faces. 這是一個滿是憂傷和嚴肅面孔的房間。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sober</b> colours and clothes are plain and rather dull. (顏色或衣服) 素淡的","examples":["He dresses in sober grey suits. 他穿著一套素淨的灰色衣服。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴肅地","examples":["\"There's a new development,\" he said soberly. “有新的進展，”他嚴肅地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"素淡地","examples":["She saw Ellis, soberly dressed in a well-cut dark suit. 她看見了埃利斯，素淡地穿著一套裁剪合體的黑西服。"]}]}]},"revolve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）旋轉；圍繞……旋轉（revolve around）；以……為最重要內容，以……為中心（revolve around）；反覆思考，反覆斟酌；迴圈出現"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"旋轉舞臺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>revolves</b> <b>around</b> another thing, you mean that the second thing is the main feature or focus of the first thing. 以…為中心","examples":["Since childhood, her life has revolved around tennis. 從孩提時代起，她的生活就一直以網球為中心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a discussion or conversation <b>revolves</b> <b>around</b> a particular topic, it is mainly about that topic. 圍繞 (某個主題)","examples":["The debate revolves around specific accounting techniques. 這場討論圍繞具體的會計技巧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one object <b>revolves</b> <b>around</b> another object, the first object turns in a circle around the second object. 圍繞…轉","examples":["The satellite revolves around the earth once every hundred minutes. 該人造衛星每100分鐘繞地球旋轉一圈。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>revolves</b> or when you <b>revolve</b> it, it moves or turns in a circle around a central point or line. 使旋轉; 旋轉","examples":["Overhead, the fan revolved slowly. 頭頂上，電扇緩慢地旋轉著。"]}]}]},"soften":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變軟，軟化；（使）態度緩和，變寬厚；減輕，削弱；（使）（表情或聲音）變輕柔；（使）柔和，和緩；（市場、貨幣或商品）貶值；軟化（水），從（水）中除去無機鹽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>soften</b> something or if it <b>softens</b>, it becomes less hard, stiff, or firm. 使變軟; 變軟","examples":["Soften the butter mixture in a small saucepan. 在小平底鍋裡將黃油混合物弄軟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>softens</b> the damaging effect of another thing, it makes the effect less severe. 使減弱","examples":["There were also pledges to soften the impact of the subsidy cuts on the poorer regions. 也有保證要減輕消減給較貧困地區補貼所造成的衝擊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>soften</b> your position, if your position <b>softens</b>, or if you <b>soften</b>, you become more sympathetic and less hostile or critical. 使變溫和; 變溫和","examples":["The letter shows no sign that the Germans have softened their position. 這封信沒有任何跡象表明德國人的態度已有所緩和。","His party's policy has softened a lot in recent years. 近年來他所在政黨的政策變得溫和了許多。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If your voice or expression <b>softens</b> or if you <b>soften</b> it, it becomes much more gentle and friendly. 使溫和; 變溫和","examples":["All at once, Mick's serious expression softened into a grin. 頃刻間，米克嚴肅的表情和藹起來，咧嘴笑了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>soften</b> something such as light, a colour, or a sound, you make it less bright or harsh. 使 (光、顏色或聲音) 變柔和","examples":["We wanted to soften the light without destroying the overall effect of space. 我們希望在不破壞整體空間效果的同時使光線柔和些。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"Something that <b>softens</b> your skin makes it very smooth and pleasant to touch. 使 (皮膚) 變得光滑柔軟","examples":["...products designed to moisturize and soften the skin. …為滋潤柔滑肌膚而設計的產品。"]}]}]},"sow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"播種，種；激起，散佈，煽動；埋（地雷），將（一地區）布上地雷；佈滿，覆蓋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"母豬；某些雌性哺乳動物（如豚鼠）；鐵錠"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sow</b> seeds or <b>sow</b> an area of land <b>with</b> seeds, you plant the seeds in the ground. 播 (種)","examples":["Sow the seed in a warm place in February/March. 2/3月裡把種子播在溫暖的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>sows</b> an undesirable feeling or situation, they cause it to begin and develop. 散佈","examples":["He cleverly sowed doubts into the minds of his rivals. 他巧妙地在他對手們的心裡佈下了疑雲。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>sows the seeds of</b> another, it starts the process which leads eventually to the other thing. 播下某事的種子","examples":["Rich industrialized countries have sown the seeds of global warming. 富裕的工業化國家已經播下了使全球變暖的種子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sow</b> is an adult female pig. 成年母豬","examples":[]}]}]},"startle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使嚇一跳，使驚奇"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚愕，驚恐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something sudden and unexpected <b>startles</b> you, it surprises and frightens you slightly. 使受驚","examples":["The telephone startled him. 電話聲嚇了他一跳。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受驚嚇了的","examples":["Martha gave her a startled look. 瑪莎受驚地看了她一眼。"]}]}]},"secure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"穩固的，可靠的；嚴密把守的，牢固的；安全的，穩妥的；（對自己和自己的能力）有自信的；感到有保障的，沒有顧慮的；固定住的，繫牢的；秘密的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指經過努力而）獲得，得到；使安全，保護；縛牢，將（某物）固定；確保，保證；為（債務或貸款）作抵押，作保；（外科）壓迫（血管）止血；停止工作；船拋錨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>secure</b> something that you want or need, you obtain it, often after a lot of effort. 爭取到","examples":["Federal leaders continued their efforts to secure a ceasefire. 聯邦政府的領導人們繼續他們爭取停火的努力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>secure</b> a place, you make it safe from harm or attack. 使 (某地) 免遭傷害或攻擊","examples":["Staff withdrew from the main part of the prison but secured the perimeter. 工作人員從監獄的主體區域撤了出來，但封鎖了監獄四周。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>secure</b> an object, you fasten it firmly to another object. 縛牢","examples":["He helped her close the cases up, and then he secured the canvas straps as tight as they would go. 他幫她關上箱子，然後他又把帆布帶儘可能縛緊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a loan <b>is secured</b>, the person who lends the money may take property such as a house from the person who borrows the money if they fail to repay it. 以…作抵押","examples":["The loan is secured against your home. 這筆貸款以你的房屋作抵押。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>secure</b> place is tightly locked or well protected, so that people cannot enter it or leave it. 鎖牢了的; 嚴密保護的","examples":["We'll make sure our home is as secure as possible from now on. 我們將從現在起確保我們的家儘可能安全。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object is <b>secure</b>, it is fixed firmly in position. 牢固的","examples":["Check that joints are secure and the wood is sound. 檢查接頭是否牢固，木頭是否完好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something such as a job as <b>secure</b>, it is certain not to change or end. (工作等) 穩定的","examples":["...demands for secure wages and employment. …對穩定的工資和就業的要求。","Senior citizens long for a more predictable and secure future. 老年人渴望一個更可預知、更穩定的未來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>secure</b> base or foundation is strong and reliable. 堅實的 (基礎)","examples":["He was determined to give his family a secure and solid base. 他決心為他的家庭打下一個堅實牢固的基礎。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you feel <b>secure</b>, you feel safe and happy and are not worried about life. (感覺) 安全的","examples":["She felt secure and protected when she was with him. 她和他在一起的時候感到很安全。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鎖牢了地; 嚴密保護地","examples":["He locked the heavy door securely and kept the key in his pocket. 他鎖牢了那扇重門把鑰匙放在了他的口袋裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"牢固地","examples":["Ensure that the frame is securely fixed to the ground with bolts. 確保框架用螺栓牢牢地固定在地面上。"]}]}]},"stun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使震驚，使驚訝；使昏迷，（尤指）打昏；給（某人）以深刻印象，使深深感動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"昏迷；打昏；驚倒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are stunned</b> by something, you are extremely shocked or surprised by it and are therefore unable to speak or do anything. 使震驚","examples":["He's stunned by today's resignation of his longtime ally. 他被自己的長期助手今天的辭職所震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a blow on the head <b>stuns</b> you, it makes you unconscious or confused and unsteady. 把…打昏","examples":["Sam stood his ground and got a blow that stunned him. 薩姆不讓步，遭到一擊，把他打昏了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"驚呆的","examples":["When they told me she was missing I was totally stunned. 當他們告訴我她不見了時，我完全驚呆了。"]}]}]},"straighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變直，（使）變正；挺直身子，直起身來；整理，清理；整頓，（使……）好轉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>straighten</b> something, you make it neat or put it in its proper position. 整理; 擺好","examples":["She sipped her coffee and straightened a picture on the wall. 她抿了口咖啡，然後把牆上的一幅畫扶正。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>straighten</b> something, or it <b>straightens</b>, it becomes straight. 使變直; 變直","examples":["Straighten both legs until they are fully extended. 使雙腿挺直，直到他們完全伸展開。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Straighten up</b> means the same as . 整理; 擺好","examples":["This is my job, to straighten up, to file things. 這就是我的工作，整理東西，把東西歸檔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Straighten up</b> means the same as . 挺直腰","examples":["He straightened up and slipped his hands in his pockets. 他挺直腰，把雙手插進衣兜裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Straighten out</b> means the same as . 使變直; 變直","examples":["No one would dream of straightening out the church's knobbly spire. 沒人會夢想使教堂的圓形尖頂變直。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are standing in a relaxed or slightly bent position and then you <b>straighten</b>, you make your back or body straight and upright. 挺直腰","examples":["The three men straightened and stood waiting. 那3個人挺直了腰站著等。"]}]}]},"submit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"呈遞，提交；屈服，不得已接受；建議，主張；使經受，使受到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>submit</b> <b>to</b> something, you unwillingly allow something to be done to you, or you do what someone wants, for example because you are not powerful enough to resist. 屈從","examples":["In desperation, Mrs. Jones submitted to an operation on her right knee to relieve the pain. 絕望中，瓊斯夫人不得已接受了一次她右膝的手術以減輕疼痛。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>submit</b> a proposal, report, or request <b>to</b> someone, you formally send it to them so that they can consider it or decide about it. 提交 (建議、報告或請求)","examples":["They submitted their reports to the chancellor yesterday. 他們昨天向財政大臣提交了他們的報告。"]}]}]},"supervise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"指導（某人）的工作；監督（任務，計劃，活動）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>supervise</b> an activity or a person, you make sure that the activity is done correctly or that the person is doing a task or behaving correctly. 監督","examples":["A team was sent to supervise the elections in Nicaragua. 一隊人馬被派去監督尼加拉瓜的選舉。"]}]}]},"summon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"召喚；召集（會議）；傳喚，傳訊（出庭）；迫切地要求（幫助）；鼓起（勇氣），振作（精神）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>summon</b> someone, you order them to come to you. 召喚","examples":["Howe summoned a doctor and hurried over. 豪叫了一位醫生，匆忙趕過去了。","Suddenly we were summoned to the interview room. 突然我們被召喚進了面試室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>summon</b> a quality, you make a great effort to have it. For example, if you <b>summon</b> the courage or strength to do something, you make a great effort to be brave or strong, so that you will be able to do it. 努力擁有 (某特質); 鼓起 (勇氣、力氣)","examples":["It took her a full month to summon the courage to tell her mother. 她用了整整一個月的時間才鼓起勇氣告訴了母親。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Summon up</b> means the same as . 努力擁有; 鼓起 (同)(summon)","examples":["Painfully shy, he finally summoned up courage to ask her to a game. 儘管他非常靦腆，最終還是鼓起了勇氣邀她去看一場比賽。"]}]}]},"suppress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指用武力）鎮壓，壓制；阻止（程序或活動）；封鎖，隱瞞（訊息）；抑制（生理過程）；剋制（感情或反應），忍住；部分（或完全）消除（電干擾）；（心理分析）自覺抑制（不愉快的想法，記憶）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>suppresses</b> an activity, they prevent it from continuing, by using force or making it illegal. 鎮壓; 壓制","examples":["...drug traffickers, who continue to flourish despite international attempts to suppress them. …儘管全世界努力鎮壓卻繼續猖獗的毒販子們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a natural function or reaction of your body <b>is suppressed</b>, it is stopped, for example by drugs or illness. 抑制 (身體功能或反應)","examples":["The reproduction and growth of the cancerous cells can be suppressed by bombarding them with radiation. 癌細胞的繁殖和生長可透過放射線輻射加以抑制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>suppress</b> your feelings or reactions, you do not express them, even though you might want to. 抑制 (情感或反應)","examples":["Liz thought of Barry and suppressed a smile. 利茲想到了巴里，強忍住一個微笑。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>suppresses</b> a piece of information, they prevent other people from learning it. 封鎖","examples":["At no time did they try to persuade me to suppress the information. 他們從未試圖勸我封鎖這個訊息。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If someone or something <b>suppresses</b> a process or activity, they stop it continuing or developing. 阻止 (活動); 抑制 (過程)","examples":["The government is suppressing inflation by increasing interest rates. 政府正透過提高利率來抑制通貨膨脹。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鎮壓; 壓制","examples":["...people who were imprisoned after the violent suppression of the pro-democracy movement protests. …贊成民主的抗議活動受暴力鎮壓後被囚禁的人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"抑制","examples":["Eye problems can indicate an unhealthy lifestyle with subsequent suppression of the immune system. 眼睛問題表明一種不健康的生活方式以及隨後免疫系統所受的抑制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"抑制","examples":["A mother's suppression of her own feelings can cause problems. 一位母親對她自己情感的壓抑可能會導致問題。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"封鎖","examples":["The inspectors found no evidence which supported any allegation of suppression of official documents. 這些檢察官們找不到證據證明對封鎖官方檔案的任何指控。"]}]}]},"sympathize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"同情，體諒；贊同，支援"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sympathize</b> with someone who is in a bad situation, you show that you are sorry for them. 同情","examples":["I must tell you how much I sympathize with you for your loss, Professor. 教授，我必須告訴您我對您所受的損失深表同情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sympathize</b> <b>with</b> someone's feelings, you understand them and are not critical of them. 理解","examples":["Some Europeans sympathize with the Americans over the issue. 一些歐洲人在這個問題上對美國人表示理解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>sympathize</b> <b>with</b> a proposal or action, you approve of it and are willing to support it. 支援","examples":["Most of the people living there sympathized with the guerrillas. 住在那兒的大部分人支援這些游擊隊員。"]}]}]},"suspend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"暫停，中止；使暫停使用（或生效）；使暫時停職（或停學等）；延緩，推遲；懸，掛；懸浮，漂浮；<法律> （法官或法庭作出的）暫緩執行（判決）；延留（和絃），延長（和音）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>suspend</b> something, you delay it or stop it from happening for a while or until a decision is made about it. 暫停","examples":["The union suspended strike action this week. 工會本週暫停了罷工行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is suspended</b>, they are prevented from holding a particular job or position for a fixed length of time or until a decision is made about them. 使停職","examples":["Julie was suspended from her job shortly after the incident. 該事件發生後不久，朱莉被停職了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is suspended</b> from a high place, it is hanging from that place. 懸掛","examples":["...instruments that are suspended on cables. …懸掛在電纜上的儀器。"]}]}]},"sustain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"維持，保持；維持……的生命；遭受，經受；（在體力或精神方面）支援，支撐；承受住……的重量；證實，證明；認可，贊成，確認；（演員）充分表演（角色，人物），扮演"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（樂）延音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sustain</b> something, you continue it or maintain it for a period of time. 保持","examples":["He has sustained his fierce social conscience from young adulthood through old age. 他從青年時代到晚年一直保持著強烈的社會良知。","Recovery can't be sustained unless more jobs are created. 除非有更多的工作機會被創造出來，否則復甦無法保持下去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sustain</b> something such as a defeat, loss, or injury, it happens to you. 遭受","examples":["Every aircraft in there has sustained some damage. 那裡的每架飛機都遭到了一些損壞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>sustains</b> you, it supports you by giving you help, strength, or encouragement. 支撐","examples":["The cash dividends they get from the cash crop would sustain them during the lean season. 他們從經濟作物中得到的那些現金紅利能支撐他們度過歉收季節。"]}]}]},"vibrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）震動，（使）顫動；搖擺，躊躇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>vibrates</b> or if you <b>vibrate</b> it, it shakes with repeated small, quick movements. 使顫動; 顫動","examples":["The ground shook and the cliffs seemed to vibrate. 大地搖晃，那些懸崖似乎在顫動。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"顫動","examples":["The vibrations of the vehicles rattled the shop windows. 那些車輛的顫動使得商店的窗戶咯咯作響。"]}]}]},"wither":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）枯萎，（使）乾枯；衰弱，逐漸消失；使感到愚蠢，使感到羞愧；（人的四肢、皮膚等）變枯槁，萎縮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"甲，馬肩隆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>withers</b>, they become very weak. 變虛弱","examples":["When he went into retirement, he visibly withered. 到了退休年齡時，他明顯變得虛弱了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a flower or plant <b>withers</b>, it dries up and dies. (花朵或植物) 枯萎","examples":["The flowers in Isabel's room had withered. 伊莎貝爾房間裡的花朵已經枯萎了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wither away</b> means the same as . 變虛弱","examples":["To see my body literally wither away before my eyes was exasperating. 看著我的身體在自己的眼前日漸虛弱真是讓人惱火。"]}]}]},"astray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"迷失，迷路；步入歧途，墮落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are led astray</b> by someone or something, you behave badly or foolishly because of them. 引某人偏離正道","examples":["The judge thought he'd been led astray by older children. 法官認為他是被更大的孩子們引入了歧途。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>leads</b> you <b>astray</b>, they make you believe something that is not true, causing you to make a wrong decision. 引某人偏離真相","examples":["The testimony would inflame the jurors, and lead them astray from the facts of the case. 這證詞會惹怒陪審員們，讓他們偏離案件事實。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>goes astray</b>, it gets lost while it is being taken or sent somewhere. 丟失","examples":["Many items of mail being sent to her have gone astray. 很多寄給她的郵件都丟失了。"]}]}]},"utter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全的，徹底的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"說，講；發出（聲音）；使用（偽鈔）；發射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>utters</b> sounds or words, they say them. 發出 (聲音); 說","examples":["He uttered a snorting laugh. 他撲哧一聲笑了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>utter</b> to emphasize that something is great in extent, degree, or amount. 完全的; 徹底的","examples":["This, of course, is utter nonsense. 這當然純屬胡言亂語。","...this utter lack of responsibility. …如此徹底地缺乏責任心。"]}]}]},"tempt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引誘，誘惑；慫恿，利誘；冒……的風險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>tempts</b> you attracts you and makes you want it, even though it may be wrong or harmful. 引誘; 吸引","examples":["Cars like that may tempt drivers to speed. 那樣的汽車可能會引誘司機超速行駛。","It is the fresh fruit that tempts me at this time of year. 只有新鮮的水果才會在每年的這個時候吸引我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tempt</b> someone, you offer them something they want in order to encourage them to do what you want them to do. 誘使","examples":["...a million dollar marketing campaign to tempt American tourists back to Britain. …旨在誘使美國遊客回到英國的、耗資一百萬美元的營銷活動。","Don't let credit tempt you to buy something you can't afford. 不要讓賒購誘使你去購買你支付不起的東西。"]}]}]},"tackle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"應付，解決（難題或局面）；與……交涉；（足球、曲棍球等比賽中）搶斷；（橄欖球等比賽中）擒抱並摔倒（對方球員）；擒獲；對付，打（尤指罪犯）；質問，責問；反對，反抗"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（足球等中的）搶斷球；（橄欖球或美式足球）擒抱摔倒；（美式足球中的）阻截隊員；體育器械，（尤指）漁具；（吊起重物用的）索具，滑輪；<英，俚>男性性器官"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tackle</b> a difficult problem or task, you deal with it in a very determined or efficient way. 處理","examples":["The first reason to tackle these problems is to save children's lives. 解決這些問題的首要原因是為了挽救孩子們的生命。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tackle</b> someone in a game such as American football or rugby, you knock them to the ground. If you <b>tackle</b> someone in soccer or hockey, you try to take the ball away from them. (美式或英式橄欖球比賽中) 擒抱摔倒; (足球運動或曲棍球運動中) 搶斷","examples":["Foley tackled the quarterback. 福利擒住並摔倒了四分衛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>tackle</b> someone about a particular matter, you speak to them honestly about it, usually in order to get it changed or done. 坦率地與某人交談","examples":["I tackled him about how anyone could live amidst so much poverty. 我坦率地與他談論哪有人能在如此的極度貧困中生活。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>tackle</b> someone, you attack them and fight them. 攻擊","examples":["Two security guards tackled and apprehended a man suspected of robbing 17 banks. 兩名保安與一名涉嫌搶劫17家銀行的男子搏鬥並逮捕了他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tackle</b> is also a noun. 擒抱撞倒; 搶斷","examples":["...a tackle by fullback Brian Burrows. …後衛布賴恩•伯羅斯的阻截。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tackle</b> is the equipment that you need for a sport or activity, especially fishing. (尤指釣魚等活動的) 器具","examples":["...fishing tackle. …漁具。"]}]}]},"awhile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一會兒，片刻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Awhile</b> means for a short time. 一會兒","examples":["He worked awhile as a pharmacist in Cincinnati. 他在辛辛那提做了一陣子的藥劑師。"]}]}]},"weary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"疲勞的，疲倦的；使人疲勞的，令人厭煩的；厭倦的，厭煩的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）疲倦，（使）厭煩；<蘇格蘭>憂傷，煩惱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>weary</b>, you are very tired. 疲憊的","examples":["Rachel looked pale and weary. 雷切爾看起來蒼白而疲憊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>weary of</b> something, you have become tired of it and have lost your enthusiasm for it. 對…感到厭倦","examples":["They're getting awfully weary of this silly war. 他們對這場愚蠢的戰爭感到極其厭倦。"]}]}]},"barefoot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"赤腳的，光著腳的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"赤著腳地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Barefoot）人名；（英）貝爾富特"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>barefoot</b> is not wearing anything on their feet. 赤足的","examples":["I wore a white dress and was barefoot. 我穿了件白色連衣裙，光著腳。"]}]}]},"beforehand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"事先，預先，提前"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"早做準備的；提前的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>beforehand</b>, you do it earlier than a particular event. 事先; 預先","examples":["How could she tell beforehand that I was going to go out? 她如何預先知道我將出門的？"]}]}]},"clockwise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"順時針方向的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"順時針方向地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something is moving <b>clockwise</b>, it is moving in a circle in the same direction as the hands on a clock. 順時針地","examples":["He told the children to start moving clockwise around the room. 他告訴孩子們在房間裡開始按順時針方向移動。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clockwise</b> is also an adjective. 順時針的","examples":["Gently swing your right arm in a clockwise direction. 按順時針方向輕輕擺動你的右臂。"]}]}]},"inwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向內，向中心；<喻>轉向內心，內省"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"towards the interior or middle of something 向內; 向中心","examples":[]}]}]},"downwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向下地，下降地"}],"sections":[]},"counterclockwise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"逆時針方向的，反時針方向的（同 anticlockwise）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"逆時針方向地，反時針方向地（同 anticlockwise）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is moving <b>counterclockwise</b>, it is moving in the opposite direction to the direction in which the hands of a clock move. 逆時針方向地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Counterclockwise</b> is also an adjective. 逆時針方向的","examples":["The dance moves in a counterclockwise direction. 這個舞是逆時針移動的。"]}]}]},"bodily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人體的，身體的，軀體的；（與精神相對的）物質的，實體的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"整個身體地，全身地；整個地，完全地；親自地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>bodily</b> needs and functions are the needs and functions of your body. 身體的","examples":["...descriptions of natural bodily functions. …對身體自然機能的描述。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>bodily</b> to indicate that an action involves the whole of someone's body. 整個身體地","examples":["I was hurled bodily to the deck. 我整個人被扔到了甲板上。"]}]}]},"downward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"向下的，下降的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向下地，下降地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>downward</b> movement or look is directed toward a lower place or a lower level. 向下的","examples":["...a firm downward movement of the hands. …一個堅定有力的雙手向下的動作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a <b>downward</b> trend, you mean that something is decreasing or that a situation is getting worse. 逐漸下降的; 日趨惡化的","examples":["The downward trend in home ownership is likely to continue. 住房擁有率的下降趨勢有可能還要延續。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you move or look <b>downward</b>, you move or look toward the ground or a lower level. 朝下地","examples":["Benedict pointed downward again with his stick. 貝內迪克特又用他的柺杖向下指了指。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or rate moves <b>downward</b>, it decreases. 下降地","examples":["Inflation is moving firmly downward. 通貨膨脹在穩步下降。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you want to emphasize that a statement applies to everyone in an organization, you can say that it applies from its leader <b>downward</b>. 往下地","examples":["...from the president downward. …自總經理而下。"]}]}]},"hence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"因此；之後"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>hence</b> to indicate that the statement you are about to make is a consequence of what you have just said. 因此","examples":["The trade imbalance is likely to rise again in 2007. Hence a new set of policy actions will be required soon. 貿易不平衡在2007年可能會再度上揚。因此需要很快採取一系列新的政策行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>hence</b> in expressions such as \"<b>several years hence</b>\" or \"<b>six months hence</b>\" to refer to a time in the future, especially a long time in the future. 此後","examples":["The gases that may be warming the planet will have their main effect many years hence. 這些可能正在使行星變暖的氣體，其重要影響將在許多年之後顯現。"]}]}]},"inward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內心的，精神的；向內的，向中心的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向內 (=inwards)；向自己，向內心 (=inwards)"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部；內臟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>inward</b> thoughts or feelings are the ones that you do not express or show to other people. 內心的","examples":["I sighed with inward relief. 我內心釋然地長出了一口氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>inward</b> movement is one toward the inside or centre of something. 向內的","examples":["...a sharp, inward breath like a gasp. …像倒抽氣一樣急速吸入的一口氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"內心地","examples":["Sara was inwardly furious. 薩拉內心異常憤怒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something moves or faces <b>inward</b>, it moves or faces toward the inside or centre of something. 向內地","examples":["He pushed open the front door, which swung inward with a groan. 他推開前門，門呀的一聲向裡開了。"]}]}]},"nonetheless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"然而，儘管如此"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nonetheless</b> means the same as . 然而","examples":["There was still a long way to go. Nonetheless, some progress had been made. 仍然有很長的路要走。不過還是取得了一些進步。"]}]}]},"undoubtedly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"無疑，肯定"}],"sections":[]},"outwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向外（地），朝外"}],"sections":[]},"upwards":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向上，朝上，向高處；（數量、水平等）趨於上升，上調"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"upwards of：多於，……以上，超過"}],"sections":[]},"outward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外表的，表面的；（特定方面）可見的，外部的；朝外的，向外的；（旅程）往外地的，外出的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向外，朝外；自身之外；明顯地，公然地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外表，外面；外部世界，物質世界"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>outward</b> feelings, qualities, or attitudes of someone or something are the ones they appear to have rather than the ones that they actually have. 表面看起來的","examples":["In spite of my outward calm I was very shaken. 儘管表面看似鎮靜，我內心卻非常慌亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>outward</b> features of something are the ones that you can see from the outside. 外在的","examples":["Mark was lying unconscious but with no outward sign of injury. 馬克躺著, 神志不清，但卻沒有外在的受傷跡象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>outward</b> flight or journey is one that you make away from a place that you are intending to return to later. 外出的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something moves or faces <b>outward</b>, it moves or faces away from the place you are in or the place you are talking about. 向外 (移動) 地; (面) 向外地","examples":["The top door opened outward. 最上面的門向外開著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a person or a group of people, such as a government, looks <b>outward</b>, you mean that they turn their attention to another group that they are interested in or would like greater involvement with. 向外 (看) 地","examples":["Other poor countries looked outward, strengthening their ties to the economic superpowers. 其他的窮國向外看，加強它們和經濟大國的聯絡。"]}]}]},"partly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"部分地，在某種程度上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>partly</b> to indicate that something happens or exists to some extent, but not completely. 在一定程度上","examples":["It's partly my fault. 在一定程度上是我的錯。","I have not worried so much this year, partly because I have had other things to think about. 今年我不那麼擔心了，在一定程度上是因為我還有其他的事情要考慮。"]}]}]},"upward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"升高的，上升的；向上的，朝上的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向上，向高處；改善，升高；（數量）上升地，上漲地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>upward</b> movement or look is directed towards a higher place or a higher level. 向上的","examples":["She started once again on the steep upward climb. 她再次沿著峭壁開始向上攀爬。","She gave him a quick, upward look, then lowered her eyes. 她飛速地抬眼看了看他，然後又垂下雙眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to an <b>upward</b> trend or an <b>upward</b> spiral, you mean that something is increasing in quantity or price. 上升的 (趨勢、螺旋)","examples":["...the Army's concern that the upward trend in the numbers avoiding military service may continue. …軍方對逃避服兵役者數量的上升趨勢可能繼續下去的擔憂。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone moves or looks <b>upward</b>, they move or look up towards a higher place. 向上","examples":["They climbed upward along the steep cliffs surrounding the village. 他們沿著環繞村莊的陡峭懸崖向上爬。","'There,' said Jack, pointing upwards. “那兒，”傑克往上指著說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or rate moves <b>upward</b>, it increases. (數量、比率) 向上 ; 增漲","examples":["...with prices soon heading upward in stores. …隨著商店裡價格迅速上漲。","Unemployment will continue upward for much of this year. 失業率今年大部分時間將繼續上升。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A quantity that is <b>upwards of</b> a particular number is more than that number. (某數字) 以上","examples":["It costs upwards of $40,000 a year to keep some prisoners in prison. 關押一些囚犯每年要花費4萬美元以上。"]}]}]},"lest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"以免，避免；唯恐，擔心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>lest</b> something unpleasant should happen, you do it to try to prevent the unpleasant thing from happening. 以防","examples":["I was afraid to open the door lest he should follow me. 我當時害怕開啟那個門惟恐他跟蹤我。","And, lest we forget, Einstein wrote his most influential papers while working as a clerk. 而且，為了不使我們忘記，愛因斯坦在做小職員的時候寫了他最有影響的論文。"]}]}]},"nowhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"無處，哪裡都不；不可能看見（或找到）的；沒有任何地方；無名的小地方；（在文字、演講或爭論中） 任何地方都沒有"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不存在的地方，荒蕪的地區"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>無望成功的；不知名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>nowhere</b> to emphasize that a place has more of a particular quality than any other place, or that it is the only place where something happens or exists. 任何其他地方都不","examples":["Nowhere is language a more serious issue than in Hawaii. 語言在任何地方都不像在夏威夷那樣是個嚴重的問題。","This kind of forest exists nowhere else in the world. 這種森林在世界任何其他地方都沒有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>nowhere</b> when making negative statements to say that a suitable place of the specified kind does not exist. 沒有任何地方","examples":["There was nowhere to hide and nowhere to run. 沒有任何地方可藏，也沒有任何地方可逃。","I have nowhere else to go, nowhere in the world. 我無別處可去，在這個世界沒有任何可去的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>nowhere</b> to indicate that something or someone cannot be seen or found. 任何地方都沒有","examples":["Michael glanced anxiously down the corridor, but Wilfred was nowhere to be seen. 邁克爾焦慮地順著走廊掃視，但任何地方都沒有威爾弗雷德的身影。","The escaped prisoner was nowhere in sight. 那個越獄的囚犯已無蹤影。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can use <b>nowhere</b> to refer in a general way to small, unimportant, or uninteresting places. 無名的小地方","examples":["...endless paths that led nowhere in particular. …不特別通往什麼名勝的無盡頭的小路。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something or someone appears <b>from nowhere</b> or <b>out of nowhere</b>, you mean that they appear suddenly and unexpectedly. 無故突然出現","examples":["A car came from nowhere, and I had to jump back into the hedge just in time. 一輛轎車不知從哪裡突然開了過來，我不得不趕緊向後跳進籬笆，險些來不及。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>nowhere</b> to mean not in any part of a text, speech, or argument. (在文字、演講或爭論中) 任何地方都沒有","examples":["He nowhere offers concrete historical background to support his arguments. 他在任何地方都沒有給出具體的歷史背景來支援他的論點。","Point taken, but nowhere did we suggest that this yacht's features were unique. 你說的是，但是我們在任何地方都沒有表示這艘遊艇的特點是獨一無二的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a place is <b>in the middle of nowhere</b>, you mean that it is a long way from other places. 在遙遠偏僻處","examples":["At dusk we pitched camp in the middle of nowhere. 黃昏時我們在遙遠偏僻的地方搭起了帳篷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you use <b>nowhere near</b> in front of a word or expression, you are emphasizing that the real situation is very different from, or has not yet reached, the state which that word or expression suggests. 遠非","examples":["He's nowhere near recovered yet from his experiences. 他遠未從他的經歷中恢復過來。"]}]}]},"versus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"（比賽或訴訟中）以……為對手，與……競爭；與……相對，與……相比"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>versus</b> to indicate that two figures, ideas, or choices are opposed. 與…相對","examples":["Only 18.8% of the class of 1982 had some kind of diploma four years after high school, versus 45% of the class of 1972. 相對於1972屆學生中有45%在中學畢業4年後獲得了某種文憑來說，1982屆學生的這一比例只有18.8%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Versus</b> is used to indicate that two teams or people are competing against each other in a sports event. (體育比賽中) …對…","examples":["Italy versus Japan is turning out to be a surprisingly well matched competition. 義大利對日本隊的比賽結果是一場出人意料地勢均力敵的比賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Versus</b> is used in a court of law to indicate that two people or organizations are involved in a law suit. The abbreviation <b>v</b> is also used. (在法庭上) …訴…","examples":["That case became known as Healey versus Jones. 那起訟案被稱作“希利訴瓊斯案”。"]}]}]},"via":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"經由，經過（某一地方）；透過，藉助於（某種手段或人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go somewhere <b>via</b> a particular place, you go through that place on the way to your destination. 經由","examples":["We drove via Lovech to the old Danube town of Ruse. 我們驅車經由洛維奇去了多瑙河畔的古城魯塞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>via</b> a particular means or person, you do it by making use of that means or person. 透過","examples":["The technology to allow relief workers to contact the outside world via satellite already exists. 允許救援人員透過衛星與外界取得聯絡的技術已經存在。"]}]}]},"whereas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（表示對比）但是，然而；鑑於（用於檔案的開頭）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"序言，開場白；條件語句"}],"sections":[{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whereas</b> to introduce a comment that contrasts with what is said in the main clause. 而 (引導與主句內容相對比的評論)","examples":["Benefits are linked to inflation, whereas they should be linked to the cost of living. 救濟金與通貨膨脹聯絡了起來，而它們應該與生活費用掛鉤。"]}]}]},"acne":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痤瘡，粉刺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>acne</b>, they have a skin condition which causes a lot of pimples on their face and neck. 粉刺","examples":["She wore no makeup, and her face was dotted with acne. 她沒有化妝，臉上長滿了粉刺。"]}]}]},"abortion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流產，墮胎；失敗；（生）（器官，尤其是種子或水果的）敗育，停止發育；流產的胎兒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a woman has an <b>abortion</b>, she ends her pregnancy deliberately so that the baby is not born alive. 流產","examples":["He and his girlfriend had been going out together for a year when she had an abortion. 他的女友流產時，他和她已經交往了一年時間。"]}]}]},"admiral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海軍上將，海軍將軍；艦隊司令；海軍上將蛺蝶；（Admiral）（美、俄、加）阿德米拉爾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>admiral</b> is a very senior officer who commands a navy. 海軍上將","examples":["...Admiral Hodges. …霍奇斯海軍上將。"]}]}]},"adolescence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青春期，青春"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Adolescence</b> is the period of your life in which you develop from being a child into being an adult. 青春期","examples":["Some young people suddenly become self-conscious and tongue-tied in early adolescence. 一些年青人在青春期早期突然變得害羞結舌。"]}]}]},"acknowledgement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"承認；感謝；（作者的）致謝；回執；（表示注意到了某人或某事的）示意"}],"sections":[]},"academy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專科院校；研究院，學會；（美國的）私立學校；（蘇格蘭的）中等學校"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Academy</b> is sometimes used in the names of schools and colleges, especially those specializing in particular subjects or skills, or private high schools in the United States. 有時用於 (尤為專科) 院校或美國私立中學名稱中","examples":["He is an English teacher at the Seattle Academy for Arts and Sciences. 他是西雅圖文理學院的一名英語老師。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Academy</b> appears in the names of some societies formed to improve or maintain standards in a particular field. 用於專業學術團體名稱中","examples":["...the American Academy of Psychotherapists. …美國心理治療師學會。"]}]}]},"adulthood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"成年，成人時期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Adulthood</b> is the state of being an adult. 成年","examples":["Few people nowadays are able to maintain friendships into adulthood. 現今很少有人能夠把友誼維持到成年。"]}]}]},"adolescent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青少年"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"青春期的；不成熟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Adolescent</b> is used to describe young people who are no longer children but who have not yet become adults. It also refers to their behaviour. 青春期的 (少年、行為)","examples":["It is important that an adolescent boy should have an adult in whom he can confide. 一個青春期男孩應該有一個他能傾吐心聲的成年人，這是很重要的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adolescent</b> is an adolescent boy or girl. 青春期少年","examples":["Young adolescents are happiest with small groups of close friends. 年輕的青春期少年們和一小圈親近的朋友在一起時最高興。"]}]}]},"ace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（撲克牌中的）A牌；擅長……的人，一流高手；（網球中的）發球得分，愛司球；（擊落多架敵機的）王牌飛行員；（高爾夫）一桿進洞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>一流的；<非正式>極好的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……中取得好成績；（網球或排球）發球得分；勝過；（在高爾夫球比賽中）一杆進穴，一杆得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ace</b> is a playing card with a single symbol on it. In most card games, the ace of a particular suit has either the highest or the lowest value of the cards in that suit. (紙牌)(A)","examples":["...the ace of hearts. …紅桃A。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone such as a sports player as an <b>ace</b>, you mean that they are very good at what they do. 一流選手","examples":["Despite the loss of their ace early in the game, Seattle beat the Brewers 6-5. 儘管在那場比賽開始不久就失去了一流隊員，西雅圖隊仍以6比5擊敗了釀酒人隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In tennis, an <b>ace</b> is a serve which is so fast that the other player cannot reach the ball. Ace球 (網球比賽中直接得分的發球)","examples":["Agassi believed he had served an ace at 5-3 (40-30) in the deciding set. 阿加西認為他在決勝盤中5-3(40-30)時曾發出過一記Ace球。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ace</b> is also an adjective. 一流的","examples":["...ace horror-film producer Lawrence Woolsey. …一流的恐怖片製片人勞倫斯·伍希。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is an <b>ace in the hole</b> is an advantage which you have over an opponent or rival, and which you can use if necessary. 手中的王牌","examples":["Our superior technology is our ace in the hole. 我們的優越技術是我們手中的王牌。"]}]}]},"advertiser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廣告客戶（即廣告主），廣告商，登廣告者；（用於報刊名）……廣告報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advertiser</b> is a person or company that pays for a product, event, or job to be advertised in a newspaper, on television, or on a poster. 廣告客戶","examples":["When will advertisers stop bombarding women with images of unattainable beauty? 什麼時候廣告客戶們才會停止用不可企及的美麗形象來持續轟炸女性？"]}]}]},"ai":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"三趾樹懶；安圭拉島；安圭拉的國家及地區頂級域名 .ai"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（AI）人工智慧（Artificial Intelligence）；人工授精（Artificial Insemination）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the three-toed sloth 三趾樹懶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Anguilla 安圭拉島","examples":[]}]}]},"airway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（醫學）氣道，呼吸道；（航空）空中航線，航路；（工程/礦業）通風道，導氣管，通風孔，風巷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>airways</b> are the passages from their nose and mouth down to their lungs, through which air enters and leaves their body. 呼吸道","examples":["...an inflammation of the airways. …一次呼吸道發炎"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>airways</b> are all the routes that planes can travel along. 飛機航線","examples":["How does a private pilot get access to the airways? 一個私人飛機的飛行員如何獲得航線使用權呢？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Airways</b> means the same as . 無線電波","examples":["The interview went out over the airways. 訪談透過無線電波傳了出去。"]}]}]},"agony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇痛，創痛；痛楚，苦難"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Agony</b> is great physical or mental pain. 極大痛苦","examples":["A new machine may save thousands of animals from the agony of drug tests. 一種新機器可能使成千上萬只動物免於藥物試驗的極大痛苦。"]}]}]},"affection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜愛，關愛；愛戀，愛慕之情；精神狀況，感情；疾患，病；影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you regard someone or something with <b>affection</b>, you like them and are fond of them. 喜愛","examples":["She thought of him with affection. 她懷著喜愛想起了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>affections</b> are your feelings of love or fondness for someone. 感情","examples":["Caroline is the object of his affections. 卡羅琳是他感情的歸屬。"]}]}]},"agenda":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"待議事項，議事日程；（政治）議題；秘密計劃，秘密目標"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the political issues that are important at a particular time as an <b>agenda</b>. (政治) 議題","examples":["Does television set the agenda on foreign policy? 電視安排了有關外交政策的議題了嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>agenda</b> is a list of the items that have to be discussed at a meeting. 議事日程","examples":["This is sure to be an item on the agenda next week. 這必將成為下週議事日程上的一項議題。"]}]}]},"algebra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代數；代數學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Algebra</b> is a type of mathematics in which letters are used to represent possible quantities. 代數","examples":[]}]}]},"alligator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短吻鱷；短吻鱷皮革，類鱷魚皮材料"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（靴子、提包等）鱷魚皮製的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alligator</b> is a large reptile with short legs, a long tail, and very powerful jaws. 短吻鱷","examples":["There are numerous signs warning people not to feed the alligators in the area. 有很多標識警告人們不要在這個區域喂這些短吻鱷。"]}]}]},"allergy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過敏反應，過敏症；厭惡，反感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a particular <b>allergy</b>, you become ill or get a rash when you eat, smell, or touch something that does not normally make people ill. 過敏","examples":["Food allergies can result in an enormous variety of different symptoms. 食物過敏會導致大量不同種類的症狀。"]}]}]},"aisle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"走廊，過道；（教堂）耳堂，側堂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>aisle</b> is a long narrow gap that people can walk along between rows of seats in a public building such as a church or between rows of shelves in a supermarket. (座位間或貨架間的) 通道","examples":["...the frozen food aisle. …冷凍食品的貨架通道。"]}]}]},"alien":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陌生的；外國的，異域的；與外星人有關的，與地球外有關的；（植物或動物種類）外來的；不相容的，格格不入的 （alien to）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外國人，僑民；外星人（或生物）；（植物或動物種類）外國引進品種"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"讓渡，轉讓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alien</b> means belonging to a different country, race, or group, usually one you do not like or are frightened of. 外國的","examples":["He said they were opposed to what he described as the presence of alien forces in the region. 他說他們反對他所描述的在該地區有外國軍隊的存在。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>alien</b> <b>to</b> you or <b>to</b> your normal feelings or behaviour, it is not the way you would normally feel or behave. 陌生的","examples":["Such an attitude is alien to most businessmen. 這種態度對大多數商人都很陌生。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alien</b> is someone who is not a legal citizen of the country in which they live. 外國人","examples":["Both women had hired illegal aliens for child care. 這兩個女人都僱傭了非法入境者來照看孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In science fiction, an <b>alien</b> is a creature from outer space. 外星人","examples":["...aliens from another planet. …從另一個行星來的外星人。"]}]}]},"ally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同盟國；盟友，支持者；輔助物，助手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與……結盟，與……聯合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A country's <b>ally</b> is another country that has an agreement to support it, especially in war. 同盟國","examples":["Washington would not take such a step without its allies' approval. 沒有其同盟國的贊同，華盛頓不會邁出這樣的一步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as your <b>ally</b>, you mean that they help and support you, especially when other people are opposing you. 盟友","examples":["He is a close ally of the president. 他是總統的一位親密盟友。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The Allies</b> were the armed forces that fought against Germany and Japan in World War II. (二戰時的) 同盟國","examples":["...Germany's surrender to the Allies. …德國向同盟國的投降。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ally</b> <b>yourself with</b> someone or something, you give your support to them. 使結盟","examples":["He will have no choice but to ally himself with the new movement. 他將別無選擇，只能與這個新運動結盟。"]}]}]},"anthem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國歌，（團體組織的）頌歌，讚歌；（尤指聖公會或新教教會的）聖歌；（對某一群體很重要的）歌曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>anthem</b> is a song that is used to represent a particular nation, society, or group and that is sung on special occasions. 國歌; 會歌","examples":["The band played the Czech anthem. 這支樂隊演奏了捷克國歌。"]}]}]},"applause":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"掌聲，喝彩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Applause</b> is the noise made by a group of people clapping their hands to show approval. 掌聲","examples":["They greeted him with thunderous applause. 他們以雷鳴般的掌聲歡迎了他。"]}]}]},"altitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海拔高度；高地；（天體在地平線上的）地平緯度；頂垂線；（等級和地位等的）高階"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is at a particular <b>altitude</b>, it is at that height above sea level. 海拔高度","examples":["The aircraft had reached its cruising altitude of about 39,000 feet. 那架飛機已經達到了大約三萬九千英尺的巡航高度。"]}]}]},"architect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建築師；設計師，締造者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>architect</b> is a person who designs buildings. 建築師","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>architect</b> <b>of</b> an idea, event, or institution is the person who invented it or made it happen. 設計師; 締造者","examples":["James Madison was the principal architect of the constitution. 詹姆斯·麥迪遜是該憲法的主設計師。"]}]}]},"alternate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輪流的，交替的；間隔的；供選擇的，備用的；（葉，芽）互生的；另類的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）交替，（使）輪流"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"替補者，候補者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>alternate</b> two things, you keep using one then the other. When one thing <b>alternates</b> <b>with</b> another, the first regularly occurs after the other. 交替","examples":["Her aggressive moods alternated with gentle or more cooperative states. 她的挑釁情緒與溫和或更為合作的情緒互相交替。","Now you just alternate layers of that mixture and eggplant. 現在你只用把那種混合物與茄子一層層交疊起來。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alternate</b> actions, events, or processes regularly occur after each other. 交替的","examples":["They were streaked with alternate bands of colour. 他們都帶有色彩交替相間的條紋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens on <b>alternate</b> days, it happens on one day, then happens on every second day after that. In the same way, something can happen in <b>alternate</b> weeks, years, or other periods of time. 間隔的","examples":["Lesley had agreed to Jim going skiing in alternate years. 萊斯麗已經同意了吉姆隔年去滑雪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>alternate</b> to describe a plan, idea, or system which is different from the one already in operation and can be used instead of it. 供替換的","examples":["His group was forced to turn back and take an alternate route. 他的小組被迫返回並採用了替代路線。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"交替地","examples":["He could alternately bully and charm people. 他能時而欺負人，時而吸引人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alternate</b> is a person or thing that replaces another, and can act or be used instead of them. 替補","examples":["In most jurisdictions, twelve jurors and two alternates are chosen. 在大多數審判中，12名陪審員和2名替補人員會被選出。"]}]}]},"antique":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"古老的，古董的；老式的，過時的；（木器表面罩漆工藝）仿古的，古式的；年久的，破舊的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"古物，古董；古式（尤指古希臘、古羅馬的雕刻、建築等）；西文粗體字型"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以仿古式樣製作；覓購古玩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>antique</b> is an old object such as a piece of china or furniture that is valuable because of its beauty or rarity. 古董","examples":["...a genuine antique. …一件真古董。"]}]}]},"architecture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"建築設計，建築風格；建築學；結構；計算機的體系結構，架構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Architecture</b> is the art of planning, designing, and constructing buildings. 建築藝術","examples":["He studied classical architecture and design in Rome. 他在羅馬學過古典建築藝術和設計。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>architecture</b> of a building is the style in which it is designed and constructed. 建築風格","examples":["...modern architecture. …現代建築風格。"]}]}]},"anchor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錨；支柱，靠山；商場；<美>新聞節目主持人；<英，非正式>（汽車的）剎車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拋錨，泊（船）；使穩固，使固定；成為支柱；<美>主持（新聞節目）；使紮根，使基於；支援，保護"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"末棒的，最後一棒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>anchor</b> is a heavy hooked object that is dropped from a boat into the water at the end of a chain in order to make the boat stay in one place. 錨","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>anchor</b> on a television or radio programme, especially a news programme, is the person who presents it. 節目主持人","examples":["He worked in the news division of ABC – he was the anchor of its 15-minute evening newscast. 他以前在美國廣播公司的新聞部工作–他是該公司15分鐘晚間新聞節目的主持人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>anchor</b> is the main shop in a mall or shopping centre. 主體商店","examples":["A clothing shop is to be a key anchor in a new development planned on the vacant lot. 一個服裝店將成為在這塊空地上計劃新開發專案中的一個關鍵主體商店。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a boat <b>anchors</b> or when you <b>anchor</b> it, its anchor is dropped into the water in order to make it stay in one place. 拋錨","examples":["We could anchor off the pier. 我們可以在碼頭拋錨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>is anchored</b> somewhere, it is fixed to something to prevent it moving from that place. 使固定","examples":["The roots anchor the plant in the earth. 根鬚把這植物固定在土裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The person who <b>anchors</b> a television or radio programme, especially a news programme, is the person who presents it and acts as a link between interviews and reports that come from other places or studios. 主持","examples":["Viewers saw him anchoring a five-minute summary of regional news. 觀眾們看到了他主持地區新聞的5分鐘綜述。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a boat is <b>at anchor</b>, it is floating in a particular place and is prevented from moving by its anchor. 停泊","examples":["Sailboats lay at anchor in the narrow waterway. 帆船停泊在狹窄的水道里。"]}]}]},"arena":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"競技場，圓形劇場；鬥爭場所，活動舞臺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>arena</b> is a place where sports, entertainments, and other public events take place. It has seats around it where people sit and watch. 競技場","examples":["...the largest indoor sports arena in the world. …世界上最大的室內體育競技場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a field of activity, especially one where there is a lot of conflict or action, as an <b>arena</b> of a particular kind. 鬥爭場所","examples":["He made it clear he had no intention of withdrawing from the political arena. 他明確表示他沒有退出政治舞臺的意圖。"]}]}]},"asset":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"有利條件，有價值的人或物；資產，財產"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is an <b>asset</b> is considered useful or helps a person or organization to be successful. 資本","examples":["Our creativity in the field of technology is our greatest asset. 我們在技術領域的創造力是我們最大的資本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>assets</b> of a company or a person are all the things that they own. 資產","examples":["By the end of 1989 the group had assets of $3.5 billion. 到1989年底該集團已有35億美元的資產。"]}]}]},"ass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傻瓜，笨蛋；屁股，臀部；<舊>驢；性感的人"},{"pos":"","zh":"null 【名】（Ass）（俄）阿斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ass</b> is your buttocks. 屁股","examples":["I jumped back and fell on my ass. 我往後一跳，摔了個屁股墩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as an <b>ass</b>, you think that they are silly or do silly things. 蠢貨","examples":["He was generally disliked and regarded as a pompous ass. 他普遍不受喜歡且被認為是個自命不凡的蠢貨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>ass</b> is an animal related to a horse but that is smaller and has long ears. 驢","examples":[]}]}]},"armor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盔甲，甲冑；裝甲，防彈鋼板；甲殼；裝甲部隊，裝甲車輛；（感情、社交或其他方面的）防禦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（感情、社交或其他方面的）防禦"}],"sections":[]},"astronomer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天文學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>astronomer</b> is a scientist who studies the stars, planets, and other natural objects in space. 天文學家","examples":[]}]}]},"astronaut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宇航員，太空人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>astronaut</b> is a person who is trained for travelling in a spacecraft. 宇航員","examples":[]}]}]},"assault":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（軍事）襲擊，攻擊；人身攻擊，侵犯人身（罪）；抨擊；闖關，衝擊（難關）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"襲擊，毆打；使（感官）難受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>assault</b> by an army is a strong attack made on an area held by the enemy. 猛攻","examples":["The rebels are poised for a new assault on the government garrisons. 叛亂分子作好了對政府衛戍部隊的新一輪猛攻的準備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>assault</b> <b>on</b> a person is a physical attack on them. 襲擊","examples":["The attack is one of a series of savage sexual assaults on women in the university area. 這次襲擊是一系列在大學區對女性的野蠻性侵犯之一。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Assault</b> weapons such as rifles are intended for soldiers to use in battle rather than for purposes such as hunting. 用於戰爭的 (武器)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>assault</b> someone means to physically attack them. 襲擊","examples":["The gang assaulted him with iron bars. 該團伙用鐵棒襲擊了他。"]}]}]},"astronomy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天文學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Astronomy</b> is the scientific study of the stars, planets, and other natural objects in space. 天文學","examples":[]}]}]},"auditorium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀眾席；禮堂，會堂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>auditorium</b> is the part of a theatre or concert hall where the audience sits. 觀眾席","examples":["Anderson was to sing at the Constitution Hall auditorium. 安德森將要在憲法廳的觀眾席演唱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>auditorium</b> is a large room, hall, or building that is used for events such as meetings and concerts. 禮堂","examples":["...a high school auditorium. …一所中學的禮堂。"]}]}]},"astonishment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"驚訝，驚愕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Astonishment</b> is a feeling of great surprise. 驚訝","examples":["I spotted a shooting star which, to my astonishment, was bright green in colour. 我看見了一顆劃過長空的流星，讓我驚訝的是，它是鮮綠色的。"]}]}]},"awe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敬畏，驚歎；<古>使人敬畏的力量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使敬畏，使驚歎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Awe</b> is the feeling of respect and amazement that you have when you are faced with something wonderful and often rather frightening. 敬畏","examples":["She gazed in awe at the great stones. 她敬畏地凝視著那些巨石。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are awed</b> <b>by</b> someone or something, they make you feel respectful and amazed, though often rather frightened. 對…感到敬畏","examples":["I am still awed by David's courage. 我依然對戴維的勇氣感到敬佩。"]}]}]},"bachelor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"未婚男子，單身漢；學士；尚未交配的雄鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bachelor</b> is a man who has never married. 單身漢","examples":["...America's most eligible bachelor. …美國最適合做夫婿的單身漢。"]}]}]},"badge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"徽章，獎章；標記，象徵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給予……徽章（或標記）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>badge</b> is a piece of metal, cloth or plastic which you wear or carry to show that you work for a particular organization, or that you have achieved something. (表明身份的) 徽章","examples":["...a police officer's badge. …警官的徽章。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>badge</b> is a small piece of metal or plastic which you wear in order to show that you support a particular movement, organization, or person. You fasten a badge to your clothes with a pin. (表明支援物件的) 徽章","examples":[]}]}]},"backbone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"脊骨，脊柱；支柱，骨幹；骨氣，毅力；<美>書脊；（聚合分子的）主鏈；（計算機）主幹網"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>backbone</b> is the column of small linked bones down the middle of your back. 脊骨","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has no <b>backbone</b>, you think that they do not have the courage to do things which need to be done. 骨氣","examples":["You might be taking drastic measures and you've got to have the backbone to do that. 你可能在採取極端措施，而且你得有骨氣做它。"]}]}]},"auxiliary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輔助的；備用的，後備的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"助手，輔助人員；外國援軍士兵，僱傭兵；附屬機構；志願隊；輔助艦船；助動詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Auxiliary</b> equipment is extra equipment that is available for use when necessary. 備用的","examples":["...an auxiliary motor. …一臺備用的發動機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Auxiliary</b> staff and troops assist other staff and troops. 後備的","examples":["The government's first concern was to augment the army and auxiliary forces. 政府首要關注的是擴充軍隊與後備軍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>auxiliary</b> is a person who is employed to assist other people in their work. Auxiliaries are often medical workers or members of the armed forces. 助手","examples":["Nursing auxiliaries provide basic care, but are not qualified nurses. 助理護士們提供基本護理，但沒有護士資格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, an <b>auxiliary</b> or <b>auxiliary verb</b> is a verb that is used with a main verb, for example, to form different tenses or to make the verb passive. In English, the basic auxiliary verbs are \"be,\" \"have,\" and \"do.\" Modal verbs such as \"can\" and \"will\" are also sometimes called auxiliaries. 助動詞","examples":[]}]}]},"bandit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"強盜，土匪；惡棍；敲詐者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Robbers are sometimes called <b>bandits</b>, especially if they are found in areas where the law has broken down. 土匪","examples":["This is real bandit country. 這是真正的強盜之地。"]}]}]},"attendance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出席人數；出席，出勤；考勤情況；提供幫助（in attendance）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>attendance</b> at an event or an institution is the fact that they are present at the event or go regularly to the institution. 出勤; 出席","examples":["Her attendance in school was sporadic. 她在學校的出勤率很低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>attendance</b> at an event is the number of people who are present at it. 出席人數","examples":["Rain played a big part in the air show's drop in attendance. 下雨是這次飛行表演觀眾數量下降的主要原因。"]}]}]},"ballot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（無記名）投票選舉，投票表決；選票；投票總數（the ballot）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"要求（某人）投票；（為……）投票；抽籤決定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ballot</b> is a secret vote in which people select a candidate in an election, or express their opinion about something. 無記名投票","examples":["The result of the ballot will not be known for two weeks. 本次無記名投票的結果將在兩週後才會揭曉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ballot</b> is a piece of paper on which you indicate your choice or opinion in a secret vote. 無記名選票","examples":["Election boards will count the ballots by hand. 選舉委員會將手工清點選票。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ballot</b> a group of people, you find out what they think about a subject by organizing a secret vote. 組織…進行秘密投票","examples":["The union said they will ballot members on whether to strike. 工會稱他們將組織會員們秘密投票表決是否罷工。"]}]}]},"barbarian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（歷史，常含貶義）野蠻人，未開化的人，蠻族；（貶義）無教養的人，粗野的人，殘暴的人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"野蠻的，未開化的；粗野的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In former times, <b>barbarians</b> were people from other countries who were thought to be uncivilized and violent. 蠻族人","examples":["The Roman Empire was overrun by Nordic barbarians. 羅馬帝國被北歐蠻族推翻了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>barbarian</b>, you disapprove of them because they behave in a way that is cruel or uncivilized. 野蠻人","examples":["Our maths teacher was a bully and a complete barbarian. 我們的數學老師是個惡霸，十足的野蠻人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Barbarian</b> is also an adjective. 野蠻的","examples":["We need to fight this barbarian attitude to science. 我們需要向這種對待科學的野蠻態度作鬥爭。"]}]}]},"banner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橫幅標語；（網頁上的）橫幅廣告；信仰，準則；旗幟"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，出色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（頭版的）通欄大字標題下刊登（新聞報道等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>banner</b> is a long strip of cloth with something written on it. Banners are usually attached to two poles and carried during a protest or rally. (遊行或集合用的) 橫幅","examples":["A large crowd of students followed the coffin, carrying banners and shouting slogans denouncing the government. 一大群學生跟在靈柩的後面，舉著橫幅，高喊口號譴責政府。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does something <b>under the banner of</b> a particular cause, idea, or belief, they do it saying that they support that cause, idea, or belief. 在…旗幟下; 在…名義下","examples":["Russia was the first country to forge a new economic system under the banner of Marxism. 蘇聯是第一個在馬克思主義的旗幟下建立新的經濟體制的國家。"]}]}]},"ban":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禁止，禁令；逐出令；<史>褫奪公民權的判決；<古>詛咒；巴尼（羅馬尼亞貨幣單位，複數bani）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"禁止，取締；（官方）把（某人）逐出某地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>ban</b> something means to state officially that it must not be done, shown, or used. (官方) 明令禁止","examples":["Canada will ban smoking in all offices later this year. 加拿大將於今年晚些時候禁止在所有辦公場所吸菸。","Last year arms sales were banned. 去年軍火交易被明令禁止了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are banned</b> <b>from</b> doing something, you are officially prevented from doing it. 禁止","examples":["He was banned from driving for three years. 他被禁止駕駛3年。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ban</b> is an official ruling that something must not be done, shown, or used. 官方禁令","examples":["The general lifted the ban on political parties. 將軍解除了對政黨的官方禁令。"]}]}]},"banquet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宴會，盛宴；筵席，宴席"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"宴請；參加宴會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>banquet</b> is a grand formal dinner. 正式宴會","examples":["...this week's Greater Cleveland Sports Commission awards banquet. …本週的大克利夫蘭體育委員會的頒獎宴會。","...a wedding banquet. …一場婚宴。"]}]}]},"barbershop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"理髮店（通常指男子理髮店）；男聲無伴奏和聲演唱風格"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"男聲無伴奏和聲演唱的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Barbershop</b> is a style of singing where a small group of people, usually men, sing in close harmony and without any musical instruments accompanying them. 男聲小合唱; 小型(男聲)無伴奏和聲演唱團","examples":["...a barbershop quartet. ...一個男聲四重唱組合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>barbershop</b> is a place where a barber works. (男性)理髮店","examples":[]}]}]},"batch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一批，一批生產量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分批處理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>batch</b> <b>of</b> things or people is a group of things or people of the same kind, especially a group that is dealt with at the same time or is sent to a particular place at the same time. (一) 批","examples":["...the current batch of trainee priests. …當前的這一批受訓牧師。","She brought a large batch of newspaper clippings. 她帶來一大批剪報。","I baked a batch of cookies. 我烤了一批小甜餅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the amount of a material needed for an operation 一次手術所需的材料數","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a tall loaf having a close texture and a thick crust on the top and bottom, baked as part of a batch: the sides of each loaf are greased so that they will pull apart after baking to have pale crumby sides; made esp in Scotland and Ireland 一大條麵包 (Also called batch loaf)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to group (items) for efficient processing (為提高處理效率而進行的)分組","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to handle by batch processing","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(of a man) to do his own cooking and housekeeping (一個男人)獨自做飯做家務","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"to live alone 獨自生活","examples":[]}]}]},"bazaar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指中東、印度等地的）集市，市場，巴扎；為慈善等目的舉辦的義賣會，義賣市場；<美>出售多種商品的商店"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In areas such as the Middle East and India, a <b>bazaar</b> is a place where there are many small stores and stalls. (中東、印度等地的) 集市","examples":["Kamal was a vendor in Cairo's open-air bazaar. 卡莫爾曾是開羅露天集市的攤販。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bazaar</b> is a sale to raise money for charity. 義賣會","examples":["...a church bazaar. …一場教會義賣會。"]}]}]},"batter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"接連猛打；毆打，毒打；肆虐，嚴重破壞；抨擊，責難；給……裹麵糊；（牆等的）向後傾斜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵糊（煎料），麵糰；擊球員；（牆等的）向後傾斜；（活字或鉛版的）字面磨損處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>batter</b> someone means to hit them many times, using fists or a heavy object. 連續猛擊 (某人)","examples":["The passengers were battered by flying luggage and cargo as the cabin lost pressure. 當機艙失去壓力時，乘客們受到飛落的行李和貨物連續猛擊。","A karate expert battered a man to death. 一位空手道高手將一名男子猛擊致死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is battered</b>, they are regularly hit and badly hurt by a member of their family or by their partner. 虐待","examples":["...evidence that the child was being battered. …這個孩子正遭虐待的證據。","...boys who witness fathers battering their mothers. …親眼目睹父親虐待他們母親的男孩們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place <b>is battered</b> <b>by</b> wind, rain, or storms, it is seriously damaged or affected by very bad weather. (風、雨或風暴等的) 襲擊","examples":["The country has been battered by winds of between fifty and seventy miles an hour. 這個國家一直受到時速50至70英里大風的襲擊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>batter</b> something, you hit it many times, using your fists or a heavy object. 連續猛擊","examples":["They were battering the door, they were trying to break in. 他們連續擊門，試圖破門而入。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遭毆打的","examples":["Her battered body was discovered in a field. 她被毆打過的屍體在一塊地裡被發現了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"虐待","examples":["Leaving the relationship does not mean that the battering will stop. 脫離了這種關係並不意味著虐待會停止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Batter</b> is a mixture of flour, eggs, and milk that is used in cooking. (麵粉、蛋和牛奶混合成的) 糊","examples":["...pancake batter. …做薄煎餅的麵糊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports such as baseball and softball, a <b>batter</b> is a person who hits the ball with a wooden bat. 擊球員","examples":["...batters and pitchers. …擊球員和投球手們。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the slope of the face of a wall that recedes gradually backwards and upwards (牆面的)斜坡","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a spree or debauch 狂歡或放蕩","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to have such a slope 形成坡度","examples":[]}]}]},"belongings":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"所有物，財物；親屬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>belongings</b> are the things that you own, especially things that are small enough to be carried. 所有物","examples":["I collected my belongings and left. 我收拾好行李就離開了。"]}]}]},"blacksmith":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鐵匠，鍛工（以加熱和錘打金屬製作或修理鐵器的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blacksmith</b> is a person whose job is making things by hand out of metal that has been heated to a high temperature. 鐵匠","examples":[]}]}]},"behalf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代表（on behalf of）；因為，為了……的利益（in/on behalf of）；就……而言，在……一方（on behalf of）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on</b> someone's <b>behalf</b>, you do it for that person as their representative. 代表","examples":["She made an emotional public appeal on her son's behalf. 她代表兒子作了感動人心的公開呼籲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel, for example, embarrassed or angry <b>on</b> someone's <b>behalf</b>, you feel embarrassed or angry for them. 替某人 (感到害羞、憤怒等)","examples":["\"What do you mean?\" I asked, offended on Liddie's behalf. “你什麼意思？”我問道，很為莉迪生氣。"]}]}]},"beloved":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鍾愛的，深受愛戴的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"心愛的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>beloved</b> person, thing, or place is one that you feel great affection for. 深愛的","examples":["He lost his beloved wife last year. 他去年痛失愛妻。"]}]}]},"bass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"男低音歌手；低音，低音部；低音吉他，低音提琴；鱸魚；椴樹"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"低音的，低聲調的"}],"sections":[]},"blizzard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴風雪；大批侵擾性的事物，大量的負擔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"下暴風雪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blizzard</b> is a very bad snowstorm with strong winds. 暴風雪","examples":[]}]}]},"blond":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（多指毛髮）亞麻色的，金黃色的；（尤指人種）白膚金髮的；淺色的；（多指毛髮）亞麻色的，金黃色的，淺茶褐色的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長著金髮的人；（毛髮）金黃色，淺茶褐色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of men's hair) of a light colour; fair (男性頭髮)淺色的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a person, esp a man, having light-coloured hair and skin 髮色和皮膚呈淺色的男性","examples":[]}]}]},"bleach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"漂白，使褪色，曬白；使失去活力，使失去實質內容；用漂白劑給……清洗，消毒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"漂白劑，消毒劑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bleach</b> something, you use a chemical to make it white or pale in colour. 漂白; 使脫色","examples":["These products don't bleach the hair. 這些產品不會使頭髮脫色。","...bleached pine tables. …褪色的松木桌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the sun <b>bleaches</b> something, or something <b>bleaches</b>, its colour gets paler until it is almost white. 曬白; 逐漸變白","examples":["The tree's roots are stripped and hung to season and bleach. 這些樹根被剝去皮並掛起來風乾曬白。","He has hair which is naturally black but which has been bleached by the sun. 他有著一頭天生的黑髮，但已經被太陽曬得變淡了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bleach</b> is a chemical that is used to make cloth white, or to clean things thoroughly and kill germs. 漂白劑","examples":[]}]}]},"blonde":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"金黃色的，淺棕色的；金髮的；淺色的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長著金髮的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A woman who has <b>blonde</b> hair has pale-coloured hair. Blonde hair can be very light brown or light yellow. The form <b>blond</b> is used when describing men. 淺色的; (頭髮) 金黃色的","examples":["...a little girl with blonde hair. …一頭金髮的小女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>blonde</b> has blonde hair. 金髮的","examples":["He was blonder than his brother. 他的頭髮比哥哥的還黃。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blonde</b> is a woman who has blonde hair. 金髮女子","examples":["...a stunning blonde in her early thirties. …一位美貌驚人的三十出頭的金髮女郎。"]}]}]},"bid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"出價；投標，競標；努力爭取；（紙牌戲中的）叫牌；命令，吩咐；打招呼，示意；邀請"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"出價，喊價；投標；努力，嘗試；（紙牌戲中的）叫牌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bid</b> <b>for</b> something or a <b>bid</b> <b>to</b> do something is an attempt to obtain it or do it. 努力嘗試","examples":["...Sydney's successful bid for the 2000 Olympic Games. …悉尼對2000年奧林匹克運動會成功的申辦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bid</b> is an offer to pay a particular amount of money for something that is being sold. 出價","examples":["Hanson made an agreed takeover bid of $351 million. 漢森按約定出價3.51億美元進行收購。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bid</b> <b>for</b> something or <b>bid</b> <b>to</b> do something, you try to obtain it or do it. 力求獲得; 努力爭取","examples":["Singapore Airlines is rumoured to be bidding for a management contract to run both airports. 據傳，新加坡航空公司正在努力爭取這兩個機場的管理合約。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bid</b> <b>for</b> something that is being sold, you offer to pay a particular amount of money for it. 出價","examples":["She wanted to bid for it. 她想出價買下它。","The bank announced its intention to bid. 銀行宣佈了其投標意向。"]}]}]},"blues":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憂鬱布魯斯歌曲，布魯斯，藍調音樂；the blues 憂鬱，沮喪；藍色物（blue 的複數）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……染成藍色（blue 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a feeling of depression or deep unhappiness 憂鬱 (習語the blues)","examples":[]}]}]},"blaze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"熊熊燃燒；閃耀，發亮光；<正式>怒視，（怒火）燃燒；醒目地刊登在報紙等上，大肆宣揚；（槍炮）連續射擊（或開火）；<非正式> 奪取，摘取；大力擊（球）；在樹皮上刻路標；<喻>帶頭，開拓；快速移動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大火，烈火；火焰；（光或色彩等的）展現，燦爛；（強烈感情的）迸發；（刻在樹上用於指示道路的）標記，記號；（尤指馬面部的一條）白斑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a fire <b>blazes</b>, it burns strongly and brightly. 熊熊燃燒","examples":["Three people died as wreckage blazed, and rescuers fought to release trapped drivers. 三個人喪生於熊熊燃燒的殘骸，營救人員奮力去解救被困的司機。","The log fire was blazing merrily. 篝火正在歡快地熊熊燃燒著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>blazes</b> <b>with</b> light or colour, it is extremely bright. 閃耀","examples":["The gardens blazed with colour. 公園裡色彩繽紛，豔麗奪目。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If guns <b>blaze</b>, or <b>blaze</b> <b>away</b>, they fire continuously, making a lot of noise. 連續射擊","examples":["Guns were blazing, flares going up and the sky was lit up all around. 槍聲響個不停，照明彈升起來，周圍的天空都被照亮了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blaze</b> is a large fire which is difficult to control and which destroys a lot of things. 大火","examples":["Some 4,000 firefighters are battling the blaze. 約有四千名消防人員正在與大火搏鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Blaze</b> is also a noun. 燦爛","examples":["I wanted the front garden to be a blaze of colour. 我想把前花園裝點得五彩繽紛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>A blaze of</b> publicity or attention is a great amount of it. 大量","examples":["He was arrested in a blaze of publicity. 他在鋪天蓋地的報道中被捕。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a light-coloured marking on the face of a domestic animal, esp a horse (家養動物尤其是馬臉上的)淺顏色的斑","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make widely known; proclaim 廣而告之; 宣告","examples":[]}]}]},"blot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用軟紙或布）吸乾，擦乾；玷汙……的品性（或名譽）；弄髒，塗汙；遮住，掩藏；從記憶中抹去，丟棄；把墨水濺到（紙上）；（用墨水）塗去（字跡），（用顏料）蓋去（圖畫）；（生化）印跡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙點，墨漬；破壞景緻的東西；（品性、名譽上的）汙點，恥辱；（生化）印跡法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is a <b>blot on</b> a person's or thing's reputation, it spoils their reputation. (名譽上的) 汙點","examples":["...a blot on the reputation of the architectural profession. …建築業名聲上的汙點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>blot</b> is a drop of liquid that has fallen on to a surface and has dried. 汙漬","examples":["...an ink blot. …一滴墨水漬。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blot</b> a surface, you remove liquid from it by pressing a piece of soft paper or cloth onto it. (用紙、布) 吸乾","examples":["Before applying makeup, blot the face with a tissue to remove any excess oils. 化妝之前，用紙巾吸乾臉上所有過多的油。"]}]}]},"blast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爆炸，爆破；衝擊波；爆炸聲，爆破聲；強勁的（氣或水）流，疾風；吹奏聲，轟鳴；嚴厲的批評；狂歡，有趣的事；（球隊或選手的）猛烈進攻；槍擊；<美>（公司、組織等發出的）群發電子郵件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"炸燬，爆破；轟開，炸開（通路）；向……射擊，槍擊；發出刺耳的高音；嚴厲批評，痛斥；由爆炸引起；用力踢，猛擊；噴射（水流、氣流等）；使枯萎；<美，非正式>輕易擊敗；損壞，摧毀；開，炸開（通路）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式>該死，討厭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blast</b> is a big explosion, especially one caused by a bomb. (尤指炸彈引起的) 大爆炸","examples":["250 people were killed in the blast. 250人在這次大爆炸中喪生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Blast</b> is also a noun. 槍擊","examples":["Anthony died from a shotgun blast to the face. 安東尼因被獵槍擊中面部而死。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Blast</b> is also a noun. 強勁的 (氣或水) 流","examples":["Blasts of cold air swept down from the mountains. 陣陣強冷氣流從山上席捲下來。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Blast</b> is also a noun. (喇叭或音樂等的) 大聲鳴響","examples":["The buzzer suddenly responded in a long blast of sound. 蜂鳴器突然以一聲長長的鳴響做出回應。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that something was a <b>blast</b>, you mean that you enjoyed it very much. 奇妙的感受","examples":["He went sledding with his daughter. \"It was a blast,\" he said later. 他和女兒去坐雪橇玩了。“那真是一次奇妙的感受，”他後來說。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is blasted</b> into a particular place or state, an explosion causes it to be in that place or state. If a hole <b>is blasted</b> in something, it is created by an explosion. 由爆炸生成; 由爆炸引起","examples":["There is a risk that toxic chemicals might be blasted into the atmosphere. 有毒化學品有爆炸後進入空氣的危險。","The explosion which followed blasted out the wall of her apartment. 隨後的爆炸炸開了她房間的那面牆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If workers <b>are blasting</b> rock, they are using explosives to make holes in it or destroy it, for example, so that a road or tunnel can be built. 用炸藥炸","examples":["Local workmen were blasting the rock face beside the track in order to make it wider. 當地工人正在用炸藥炸開小路旁邊的岩石面以便將其拓寬。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>blast</b> someone means to shoot them with a gun. 向…射擊","examples":["A son blasted his father to death after a lifetime of bullying, a court was told yesterday. 昨天有人告知法庭，一個兒子因長期受欺凌而開槍打死了其父親。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>blasts</b> their way somewhere, they get there by shooting at people or causing an explosion. 藉助射擊或爆炸開啟 (通道)","examples":["The police were reported to have blasted their way into the house using explosives. 據報道，警察已經藉助炸藥開道衝進了那所房子。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>blasts</b> water or air somewhere, it sends out a sudden, powerful stream of it. 強速噴射 (水流或氣流)","examples":["Blasting cold air over it makes the water evaporate. 向它上面快速噴冷氣可使水蒸發掉。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>blast</b> something such as a car horn, or if it <b>blasts</b>, it makes a sudden, loud sound. If something <b>blasts</b> music, or music <b>blasts</b>, the music is very loud. 突然大聲按響; 大聲放 (音樂); 突然發出巨響; (音樂) 大聲播放","examples":["...drivers who do not blast their horns. …那些沒有狂按喇叭的駕駛員。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a radio or a heater is on <b>full blast</b>, or on <b>at full blast</b>, it is producing as much sound or power as it is able to. 最大音量; 最大限量","examples":["In many of those homes the television is on full blast 24 hours a day. 許多家庭一天24小時都把電視開到最大音量。"]}]}]},"bodyguard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保鏢；保鏢隊，衛隊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bodyguard</b> is a person or a group of people employed to protect someone. 保鏢","examples":["Three of his bodyguards were injured in the attack. 他的三名保鏢在襲擊中受了傷。"]}]}]},"bog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沼澤，泥塘，泥炭沼；（英式非正式）廁所；（Bog，德語/挪威語人名或姓氏）博格"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（常作 bog down）使陷於泥沼；使動彈不得；使陷入困境"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（常作 bog down）陷於泥沼；動彈不得；陷入困境"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（英式非正式，bog off）走開，滾開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bog</b> is an area of land that is very wet and muddy. 沼澤","examples":[]}]}]},"blur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模糊不清的事物；模糊的記憶，記不清的事情；汙跡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）看不清楚，記不清；（使）難以區分；玷汙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blur</b> is a shape or area which you cannot see clearly because it has no distinct outline or because it is moving very fast. 模糊不清","examples":["Out of the corner of my eye I saw a blur of movement on the other side of the glass. 從眼角我看見了玻璃窗另一邊一個移動的模糊身影。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a thing <b>blurs</b> or when something <b>blurs</b> it, you cannot see it clearly because its edges are no longer distinct. 使變模糊; 變模糊","examples":["This creates a spectrum of colours at the edges of objects which blurs the image. 這在物體的邊緣產生了一系列顏色，使影象變得模糊不清。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>blurs</b> an idea or a distinction between things, that idea or distinction no longer seems clear. 使…變模糊","examples":["...her belief that scientists are trying to blur the distinction between \"how\" and \"why\" questions. …她認為科學家們正試圖模糊“如何”與“為什麼”問題之間的區別的想法。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your vision <b>blurs</b>, or if something <b>blurs</b> it, you cannot see things clearly. 使 (視力) 模糊; (視力) 變模糊","examples":["Her eyes, behind her glasses, began to blur. 她戴著眼鏡的眼睛開始看不清了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"模糊不清的","examples":["...blurred black and white photographs. …模糊的黑白照片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"使變模糊的","examples":["The line between fact and fiction is becoming blurred. 事實和虛構之間的界線正在變得模糊起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(視覺) 模糊的","examples":["...visual disturbances like eye-strain and blurred vision. …諸如眼睛疲勞和視力模糊的視覺紊亂。"]}]}]},"boredom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"厭煩，無聊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boredom</b> is the state of being bored. 厭煩","examples":["He had given up attending lectures out of sheer boredom. 他已經不再去聽講座了，純粹出於厭倦。"]}]}]},"booth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電話亭，投票間；售貨棚，攤位；崗亭；（隔開的）小間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>booth</b> is a small area separated from a larger public area by screens or thin walls where, for example, people can make a telephone call or vote in private. 小隔間 (如公用電話亭、投票間)","examples":["I called her from a public phone booth near the entrance to the bar. 我在酒吧入口附近的一個公用電話亭給她打了電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>booth</b> in a restaurant or café consists of a table with long fixed seats on two or sometimes three sides of it. 隔開的用餐區 (固定的長座圍繞著餐桌)","examples":["They sat in a corner booth, away from other diners. 他們坐在角落裡的分隔用餐區，遠離其他就餐者。"]}]}]},"bonus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎金，津貼，紅利；意外收穫，額外好處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bonus</b> is an extra amount of money that is added to someone's pay, usually because they have worked very hard. 獎金","examples":["Workers in big firms receive a substantial part of their pay in the form of bonuses and overtime. 大公司的工人，工資很大一部分是獎金和加班費。","...a $60 bonus. …一筆$60的獎金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bonus</b> is something good that you get in addition to something else, and which you would not usually expect. 額外收穫","examples":["We felt we might finish third. Any better would be a bonus. 我們覺得我們可能得第三名。任何更好的結果都是意外收穫。"]}]}]},"botany":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"植物學；（特定地區的）植物（生態）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Botany</b> is the scientific study of plants. 植物學","examples":[]}]}]},"boulevard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"林蔭大道，城市中的寬闊大街；<美>大馬路"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"娛樂性的（尤指輕鬆通俗的戲劇、娛樂）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"給…提供林蔭大道；把…建成林蔭大道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>boulevard</b> is a wide street in a city, usually with trees along each side. 林蔭大道","examples":["...Lenton Boulevard. …倫特林蔭大道。"]}]}]},"bosom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（女人的）胸，乳房；（女人的）胸衣；內心，胸懷；安全而舒適的地方，溫馨的氛圍；胸前，懷；衣服的胸部，胸襟"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（朋友）親密的，知心的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"懷抱；把……藏在心中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A woman's breasts are sometimes referred to as her <b>bosom</b> or her <b>bosoms</b>. 乳房","examples":["...a young mother with a baby resting against her ample bosom. …嬰兒依偎在其豐滿乳房上的一位年輕母親。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bosom</b> buddy is a friend who you know very well and like very much. 知心的","examples":["They were bosom buddies. 他們曾是知心的夥伴。"]}]}]},"bolt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃電，霹靂；（門或窗的）金屬插銷；螺栓；迅速逃跑，溜走；（布的）一匹；槍栓，槍機；弩箭；（紙等的）卷邊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"突然快速移動；<美>突然離開，脫離（政黨、團體等）；用螺栓固定；閂上（門或窗）；狼吞虎嚥；（蔬菜）生長過快，結實過早（而不宜食用）；脫口而出；（馬）脫韁，逃跑；篩選"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"筆直地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bolt</b> is a long metal object that screws into a nut and is used to fasten things together. 螺釘","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bolt</b> on a door or window is a metal bar that you can slide across in order to fasten the door or window. (門或窗的)閂","examples":["I heard the sound of a bolt being slowly and reluctantly slid open. 我聽到門閂被人緩慢而費勁地抽出來的聲音。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bolt of</b> lightning is a flash of lightning that is seen as a white line in the sky. (閃電) 道","examples":["Suddenly a bolt of lightning crackled through the sky. 突然，一道閃電劃破天空。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>bolt</b> one thing to another, you fasten them firmly together, using a bolt. 栓牢","examples":["The safety belt is easy to fit as there's no need to bolt it to seat belt anchorage points. 這種安全帶很容易安裝，因為不需要把它拴在安全帶固定點上。","Bolt the components together. 把所有的部件栓接起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>bolt</b> a door or window, you slide the bolt across to fasten it. 閂 (門或窗)","examples":["He reminded her that he would have to lock and bolt the kitchen door after her. 他提醒她，他得在她離開後鎖上廚房的門並插上門閂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>bolt</b> your food, you eat it so quickly that you hardly chew it or taste it. 吞吃","examples":["Being under stress can cause you to miss meals, eat on the move, or bolt your food. 壓力之下會造成錯過進餐、邊做事邊吃、或者吞吃食物。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>bolts</b>, they suddenly start to run very fast, often because something has frightened them. (因受驚嚇) 突然快跑","examples":["The pig rose squealing and bolted. 那頭豬尖叫著站起來，飛快地跑開了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to pass (flour, a powder, etc) through a sieve 篩(麵粉、粉末等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bolt down</b> means the same as . 吞吃","examples":["I like to think back to high school, when I could bolt down three or four burgers and a pile of French fries. 我喜歡回想高中時，那時我可以一氣吞下三四個漢堡和一大堆炸薯條。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is sitting or standing <b>bolt upright</b>, they are sitting or standing very straight. 筆直地","examples":["When I pushed his door open, Trevor was sitting bolt upright in bed. 我推開他的門時，發現特雷弗正筆直地坐在床上。"]}]}]},"boyhood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"童年，少年時代；男孩們（總稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boyhood</b> is the period of a male person's life during which he is a boy. 少年時代","examples":["They are rivals who have known each other since boyhood. 他們是少年時代就相識的對手。"]}]}]},"boom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繁榮；流行，風靡；隆隆聲；吊杆；帆桁；水柵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迅速發展，繁榮；轟鳴，轟響；用低沉的聲音說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>boom</b> in the economy, there is an increase in economic activity, for example, in the number of things that are being bought and sold. (經濟) 繁榮","examples":["An economic boom followed, especially in housing and construction. 接著是一個經濟的繁榮，尤其在住房和建築方面。","The 1980s were indeed boom years. 20世紀80年代確實是繁榮的時代。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>boom</b> <b>in</b> something is an increase in its amount, frequency, or success. 增長","examples":["The boom in the sport's popularity has meant more calls for stricter safety regulations. 該項運動普及程度的大幅提高帶來了更多要求更嚴格安全法規的呼聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Boom</b> is also a noun. 轟鳴聲","examples":["The stillness of the night was broken by the boom of a cannon. 夜晚的寂靜被大炮的轟鳴聲打破了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the economy or a business <b>is booming</b>, the number of things being bought or sold is increasing. 激增","examples":["By 1988 the economy was booming. 到1988年為止經濟一直很繁榮。","Sales are booming. 銷售量在激增。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as someone's voice, a cannon, or a big drum <b>booms</b>, it makes a loud, deep sound that lasts for several seconds. 發出低沉洪亮的聲音","examples":["\"Ladies,\" boomed Helena, without a microphone, \"we all know why we're here tonight.\" “女士們”，海倫娜沒用話筒朗聲說道，“我們都知道今晚我們為什麼在這兒。”","Thunder boomed over Crooked Mountain. 雷聲在克魯克德山上空轟鳴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boom out</b> means the same as . 發出低沉洪亮的聲音","examples":["Music boomed out from loudspeakers. 揚聲器傳出了低沉響亮的音樂。","A megaphone boomed out, \"This is the police.\" 擴音器傳出了低沉而響亮的聲音：“我們是警察。”"]}]}]},"boxer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拳師，拳擊手；拳師犬，拳獅犬；拳擊短褲，男式平角短褲（boxer shorts，常作 boxers）；（常大寫 Boxer）義和團成員，拳民；（Boxer Rebellion）義和團運動；（Boxer）人名（英、法：博克瑟）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>boxer</b> is someone who takes part in the sport of boxing. 拳擊手","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a medium-sized smooth-haired breed of dog with a short nose and a docked tail 拳師狗","examples":[]}]}]},"boundary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分界線，邊界；界限，範圍；（板球）擊球超過邊界線得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>boundary</b> <b>of</b> an area of land is an imaginary line that separates it from other areas. 邊界","examples":["The Bow Brook forms the western boundary of the wood. 鮑溪成了樹林的西邊界。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>boundaries</b> <b>of</b> something such as a subject or activity are the limits that people think that it has. 界限","examples":["The boundaries between history and storytelling are always being blurred and muddled. 歷史與故事的界限一直模糊不清。"]}]}]},"braid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（裝飾傢俱和軍裝的）彩色穗帶；<美>髮辮，辮子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……編成繩子（或穗帶）；把（頭髮）編成辮子；（用飾帶等）鑲邊，鑲綴；（河或小溪）迂迴流動，交叉往來"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Braid）（美）佈雷德（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Braid</b> is a narrow piece of decorated cloth or twisted threads, which is used to decorate clothes or curtains. 流穗","examples":["...a plum-coloured uniform with lots of gold braid. …一套帶很多金色流穗的梅色制服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>braid</b> is a length of hair that has been divided into three or more lengths and then braided. 髮辮","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>braid</b> hair or a group of threads, you twist three or more lengths of the hair or threads over and under each other to make one thick length. 把…編成辮子","examples":[]}]}]},"boxing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拳擊（運動）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……裝入盒中（box 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boxing</b> is a sport in which two people wearing large padded gloves fight according to special rules. 拳擊","examples":[]}]}]},"bowel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腸，腸道；內部，深處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>bowels</b> are the tubes in your body through which digested food passes from your stomach to your anus. 腸","examples":["Symptoms such as stomach pains and irritable bowels can be signs of bowel cancer. 胃痛和腸易激等症狀都可能是腸癌的徵兆。"]}]}]},"breadth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寬度，幅度；廣度，廣泛性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>breadth</b> <b>of</b> something is the distance between its two sides. 寬度","examples":["The breadth of the whole camp was 400 paces. 整個營地的寬度為400步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>breadth</b> <b>of</b> something is its quality of consisting of or involving many different things. 廣度","examples":["Older people have a tremendous breadth of experience. 年長的人們有極其廣泛的經驗。"]}]}]},"briefcase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公文包，公事包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>briefcase</b> is a case used for carrying documents in. 公文包","examples":[]}]}]},"bribe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賄賂；（尤指用來哄小孩做事的）好處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……行賄；誘哄（尤指小孩）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bribe</b> is a sum of money or something valuable that one person offers or gives to another in order to persuade him or her to do something. 賄賂","examples":["He was being investigated for receiving bribes. 他那時因為接收賄賂在受到調查。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person <b>bribes</b> another, they give them a bribe. 賄賂","examples":["He was accused of bribing a senior bank official. 他被控賄賂一位銀行高階職員。"]}]}]},"brace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）作好準備；支撐，加固；抵住，頂住；（身體或身體某部分）繃緊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"支撐物，支架；牙箍，牙齒矯正器；大括弧，大括號；一對（獵獲的鳥）；<英>吊褲帶，揹帶；手搖曲柄；（船上的）轉帆索"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>brace</b> <b>yourself for</b> something unpleasant or difficult, you prepare yourself for it. 準備 (面對不愉快或困難之事)","examples":["He braced himself for the icy plunge into the black water. 他準備跳入冰冷的黑水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>brace</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>against</b> something or <b>brace</b> part of your body <b>against</b> it, you press against something in order to steady your body or to avoid falling. 抵住","examples":["Elaine braced herself against the dresser and looked in the mirror. 伊萊恩身體抵住梳妝檯，照了照鏡子"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>brace</b> your shoulders or knees, you keep them stiffly in a particular position. 繃緊 (肩或膝蓋)","examples":["He braced his shoulders defiantly as another squall of wet snow slashed across his face. 當又一陣雨雪呼嘯著劃過他的臉龐時，他毫無畏懼地繃緊雙肩。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>brace</b> something means to strengthen or support it with something else. 支撐","examples":["Overhead, the lights showed the old timbers, used to brace the roof. 在頭頂上，光線照射出支撐屋頂的舊木頭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brace</b> is a device attached to a part of a person's body, for example, to a weak leg, in order to strengthen or support it. 支架","examples":["He wore leg braces after he had polio in childhood. 小時候患小兒麻痺症後，他使用了腿部支架。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Braces</b> are a metal device that can be fastened to a person's teeth in order to help them grow straight. 牙箍","examples":["I used to have to wear braces. 我以前不得不戴牙箍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Braces</b> are a pair of straps that pass over your shoulders and fasten to your trousers at the front and back in order to stop them from falling down. (褲子的) 揹帶","examples":[]}]}]},"bronze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青銅；青銅色，古銅色；青銅藝術品；銅牌"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"青銅製的；青銅色的，古銅色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使被太陽曬黑；鑲上青銅面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bronze</b> is a yellowish-brown metal which is a mixture of copper and tin. 青銅","examples":["...a bronze statue of Giorgi Dimitrov. …一座喬治·季米特洛夫銅像。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>bronze</b> is yellowish-brown in colour. 青銅色的","examples":["Her hair shone bronze and gold. 她的頭髮閃耀著青銅色和金黃色的光彩。"]}]}]},"brooch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（女用的）胸針，飾針，領針"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brooch</b> is a piece of jewellery that has a pin at the back so it can be fastened on a dress, blouse, or coat. (可以別在衣服上的) 飾針","examples":[]}]}]},"broth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肉湯，清湯，高湯；（微生物學）液體培養基"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Broth</b> is a kind of soup made by boiling meat or vegetables. 肉湯; 蔬菜清湯","examples":[]}]}]},"bound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"必然的，肯定的；受約束的，有義務的；被……所限制的，被……所束縛的；要到……去的，駛往……的；裝訂好的，有封面的；（與……）緊密相連的，關係密切；準備就緒的；（語法要素）黏附的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"跳躍，蹦跳著走；形成……的邊界，劃界；限制，約束；突然增長，急劇上升；（尤指圓形的物體）彈回，彈開"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"界限，限制；蹦跳，跳躍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捆綁；使團結；凝結（bind 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bound</b> is the past tense and past participle of . (bind)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is bound to</b> happen, you mean that you are sure it will happen, because it is a natural consequence of something that is already known or exists. 必然會","examples":["There are bound to be price increases next year. 明年價格必然會上漲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is bound to</b> happen or be true, you feel confident and certain of it, although you have no definite knowledge or evidence. 應該會","examples":["I'll show it to Benjamin. He's bound to know. 我要讓本傑明瞧瞧，他該知道。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place is <b>out of bounds</b>, people are not allowed to go there. 禁止進入","examples":["For the last few days the area has been out of bounds to foreign journalists. 過去幾天，這個地區禁止外國記者入內。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>out of bounds</b>, people are not allowed to do it, use it, see it, or know about it. 禁止的","examples":["American parents may soon be able to rule violent TV programmes out of bounds. 美國父母也許很快就能禁止暴力電視節目的播放。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(of a book) secured within a cover or binding (書)有封面的; (書)裝訂好的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person, thing, or situation is <b>bound to</b> another, they are closely associated with each other, and it is difficult for them to be separated or to escape from each other. 與…密切相關的","examples":["We are as tightly bound to the people we dislike as to the people we love. 我們與我們喜歡的以及不喜歡的人都一樣密切相關。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a vehicle or person is <b>bound for</b> a particular place, they are travelling toward it. 前往","examples":["The ship was bound for Italy. 這艘船是開往義大利的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Bound</b> is also a combining form. 開往","examples":["...a Texas-bound oil freighter. …一艘開往得克薩斯州的油輪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bounds</b> are limits which normally restrict what can happen or what people can do. 界限; 限制; 範圍","examples":["Changes in temperature occur slowly and are constrained within relatively tight bounds. 溫度變化得很慢，而且被控制在相對嚴格的範圍內。","...a forceful personality willing to go beyond the bounds of convention. …想要打破世俗束縛的堅強個性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bound</b> is a long or high jump. 跳躍","examples":["With one bound Jack was free. 縱身一躍，傑克自由了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a number which is greater than all the members of a set of numbers (an <b>upper bound</b>), or less than all its members (a <b>lower bound</b>) 界","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"more generally, an element of an ordered set that has the same ordering relation to all the members of a given subset 有序集的一個元素","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"whence, an estimate of the extent of some set (某集合的)大致範圍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an area of land <b>is bounded by</b> something, that thing is situated around its edge. 位於…的界線周圍","examples":["Kirgizia is bounded by Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan and Tajikistan. 吉爾吉斯與烏茲別克，哈薩克和塔吉克相毗鄰。","...the trees that bounded the parking lot. …停車場周圍的樹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's life or situation <b>is bounded</b> <b>by</b> certain things, those are its most important aspects and it is limited or restricted by them. 約束","examples":["Our lives are bounded by work, family and television. 我們的生活受到工作、家庭及電視的約束。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>bounds</b> in a particular direction, they move quickly with large steps or jumps. 跳躍著前行","examples":["He bounded up the steps and pushed the bell of the door. 他跳上了臺階，按了門鈴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the quantity or performance of something <b>bounds</b> ahead, it increases or improves quickly and suddenly. 驟升","examples":["Shares in the company bounded ahead by almost 3 percent. 公司的股份幾乎驟升了3%。"]}]}]},"brood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"孵蛋；沉思，擔憂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一窩幼雛；一大家孩子；幼蜂"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傳種的，為繁殖而飼養的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brood</b> is a group of baby birds that were born at the same time to the same mother. 一窩幼雛","examples":["...a hungry brood of fledglings. …一窩飢餓的雛鳥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's young children as their <b>brood</b> when you want to emphasize that there are a lot of them. 一家子","examples":["...a large brood of children. …一大家子小孩。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>broods</b> over something, they think about it a lot, seriously and often unhappily. 擔憂","examples":["She constantly broods about her family. 她一直在為她的家人擔憂。"]}]}]},"brotherhood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"兄弟關係，手足情誼；兄弟會，同業會，工會；四海之內皆兄弟的信念；同行，同業者；（Brotherhood）人名；<英>布拉澤胡德"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Brotherhood</b> is the affection and loyalty that you feel for people who you have something in common with. 兄弟情誼; 手足情誼","examples":["People threw flowers into the river between the two countries as a symbolic act of brotherhood. 人們把花扔進兩國之間的河裡，以此作為兄弟情誼的象徵性的行為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>brotherhood</b> is an organization whose members all have the same political aims and beliefs or the same job or profession. 兄弟會; 同業會","examples":["...the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers. …機車工程師同業會。"]}]}]},"bulge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鼓起，凸出；裝滿，充滿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼓起，凸出；驟增，暴漲；（身體的）肥胖部位；（尤用於軍事場合）突出部；腫塊，疙瘩；（尤指暫時的或幅度不大的）增大，增多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a person's stomach <b>bulges</b>, it sticks out. 鼓起","examples":["Jiro waddled closer, his belly bulging and distended. 吉羅大腹便便地蹣跚而來。","He bulges out of his black T-shirt. 他臃腫的身體在黑色Ｔ恤下面鼓了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's eyes or veins <b>are bulging</b>, they seem to stick out a lot, often because the person is making a strong physical effort or is experiencing a strong emotion. (眼睛或血管因用力或激動而) 凸出","examples":["He shouted at his brother, his neck veins bulging. 他衝著弟弟大喊大叫，脖子上的血管都凸起來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is bulging</b> <b>with</b> things, you are emphasizing that it is full of them. 塞滿","examples":["They returned home with the car bulging with boxes. 他們開著那輛塞滿了盒子的車回到了家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bulges</b> are lumps that stick out from a surface which is otherwise flat or smooth. (平面上) 凸起的一塊","examples":["Why won't those bulges on your hips and thighs go? 為什麼你臀部和大腿上的贅肉不能消失呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is a <b>bulge</b> <b>in</b> something, there is a sudden large increase in it. 驟增","examples":["...a bulge in aircraft sales. …飛機銷量的驟增。"]}]}]},"browse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"隨意翻閱；（動物）吃草；（在商店裡）隨便看看；瀏覽資訊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"隨意的看，瀏覽；（動物吃的）植物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>browse</b> in a shop, you look at things in a fairly casual way, in the hope that you might find something you like. 瀏覽; 逛","examples":["I stopped in several bookshops to browse. 我去了幾家書店，隨便瀏覽了一下。","She browsed in an upscale antiques shop. 她逛了一家上等的古玩店。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>browse</b> <b>through</b> a book or magazine, you look through it in a fairly casual way. 隨意翻閱","examples":["...sitting on the sofa browsing through the TV pages of the paper. …坐在沙發上隨意翻看報紙上的電視版面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>browse</b> on a computer, you search for information in computer files or on the Internet, especially on the World Wide Web. (在電腦或網路上) 搜尋","examples":["Try browsing around in the network bulletin boards. 在網路佈告欄裡搜尋一下試試。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Browse</b> is also a noun. 瀏覽; 逛","examples":["...a browse around the shops. …在商店的一番閒逛。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals <b>browse</b>, they feed on plants. (動物) 嚼食植物","examples":["...three red deer stags browsing on the fringes of the forest. …在森林邊上吃嫩枝嫩葉的3頭紅色雄鹿。"]}]}]},"bureau":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"局，處，科；辦事處，辦公室；五斗櫥，衣櫃；書桌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bureau</b> is an office, organization, or government department that collects and distributes information. 局","examples":["...the Federal Bureau of Investigation. …聯邦調查局。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bureau</b> is an office of a company or organization that has its main office in another city or country. 分公司","examples":["...the Wall Street Journal's Washington bureau. …《華爾街日報》的華盛頓分社。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bureau</b> is a chest of drawers. 五斗櫥","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>bureau</b> is a writing desk with shelves and drawers and a lid that opens to form the writing surface. 寫字檯","examples":[]}]}]},"cactus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"仙人掌科植物，仙人掌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cactus</b> is a thick, fleshy plant that grows in many hot, dry parts of the world. Cacti have no leaves and many of them are covered in prickles. 仙人掌屬植物","examples":[]}]}]},"bruise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"青瘀，傷痕；（水果或蔬菜的）碰傷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打擊，挫傷；壓碎，碾碎；使青腫，使出現傷痕；碰傷（水果）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bruise</b> is an injury that appears as a purple mark on your body, although the skin is not broken. 瘀傷","examples":["How did you get that bruise on your cheek? 你臉頰上怎麼有一塊瘀傷？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bruise</b> is also a noun. (水果、蔬菜等表皮上) 碰的傷痕","examples":["...bruises on the fruit's skin. …水果表皮上的碰的傷痕。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bruise</b> a part of your body, a bruise appears on it, for example, because something hits you. If you <b>bruise</b> easily, bruises appear when something hits you only slightly. 使受瘀傷; 受瘀傷","examples":["I had only bruised my knee. 我只是膝蓋受了瘀傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a fruit, vegetable, or plant <b>bruises</b> or <b>is bruised</b>, it is damaged by being handled roughly, making a mark on the skin. (水果、蔬菜等) 碰傷","examples":["Choose a warm, dry day to cut them off the plants, being careful not to bruise them. 選擇暖和乾燥的一天把它們從植物上剪下來，小心不要碰傷它們。","...bruised tomatoes and cucumbers. …碰傷了的西紅柿和黃瓜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are bruised</b> by an unpleasant experience, it makes you feel unhappy or upset. 受傷","examples":["The government will be severely bruised by yesterday's events. 政府將因昨天的事件而嚴重受挫。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受了瘀傷的","examples":["I escaped with severely bruised legs. 我拖著受了嚴重瘀傷的腿逃走了。"]}]}]},"calligraphy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"書法，書法藝術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Calligraphy</b> is the art of producing beautiful handwriting using a brush or a special pen. 書法","examples":[]}]}]},"bulk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主體，大部分；龐大的身軀，肥碩的體形；（巨大的）容積，體積"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大批的，大宗的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（產品）數量顯得很大；結合（待售的股票或商品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to something's <b>bulk</b> when you want to emphasize that it is very large. 大塊","examples":["The truck pulled out of the lot, its bulk unnerving against the dawn. 拂曉時分，卡車駛出了停車場，龐大的車身看起來有點兒可怕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a large person's body or to their weight or size as their <b>bulk</b>. 龐大肥碩的身軀","examples":["Bannol lowered his bulk carefully into the chair. 班諾爾那肥碩的身軀小心地坐落到了椅子上。"]}]},{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>bulk</b> <b>of</b> something is most of it. 大部分","examples":["The bulk of the text is essentially a review of these original documents. 正文的大部分基本上是對這些原始文獻的回顧。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bulk</b> is also a pronoun. 大部分","examples":["They come from all over the world, though the bulk is from the Indian subcontinent. 他們來自世界各地，但其中大部分人還是來自印度次大陸。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you buy or sell something <b>in</b> <b>bulk</b>, you buy or sell it in large quantities. 大批地 (買賣)","examples":["Buying in bulk is more economical than shopping for small quantities. 大批採購比少量購買更經濟實惠。"]}]}]},"bully":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恃強凌弱者，橫行霸道者；<非正式>醃牛肉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"威嚇，欺侮；威脅，脅迫"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<美，非正式>很棒，一流的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式>沒什麼了不起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bully</b> is someone who uses their strength or power to hurt or frighten other people. 恃強凌弱者","examples":["I fell victim to the office bully. 我成了這個辦公室霸王欺負的物件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"欺凌行為","examples":["...schoolchildren who were victims of bullying. …遭受欺凌的小學生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various small freshwater fishes of the genera <b>Gobiomorphus</b> and <b>Philynodon</b> of New Zealand (紐西蘭)塘鯉 (Also called (NZ) pakoko, titarakura, toitoi)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>bullies</b> you, they use their strength or power to hurt or frighten you. 欺負","examples":["I wasn't going to let him bully me. 我可不會讓他欺負我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>bullies</b> you <b>into</b> something, they make you do it by using force or threats. 威逼","examples":["We think an attempt to bully them into submission would be counterproductive. 我們認為威逼他們屈服的嘗試可能會適得其反。","She used to bully me into doing my schoolwork. 她過去總逼我做作業。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"well done! bravo! 真棒 (Also bully for you)","examples":[]}]}]},"butcher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"屠夫；肉店；劊子手；笨蛋，莽夫；（火車或劇院的）小販"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"屠宰；弄砸；殘殺，殺戮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>butcher</b> is a shopkeeper who cuts up and sells meat. Some butchers also kill animals for meat and make foods such as sausages and meat pies. 屠夫; 肉商","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>butcher</b> or a <b>butcher's</b> is a shop where meat is sold. 肉鋪","examples":["He worked in a butcher's. 他在肉鋪工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>butcher</b> an animal means to kill it and cut it up for meat. 宰殺","examples":["Pigs were butchered, hams were hung to dry from the ceiling. 豬被宰殺了，火腿吊在屋頂下風乾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>has butchered</b> people when they have killed a lot of people in a very cruel way, and you want to express your horror and disgust. 屠殺","examples":["...rebels who butchered eight tourists in Bwindi national park. …在布文迪國家公園屠殺了8名遊客的叛亂分子。"]}]}]},"calf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小牛，牛犢；腓腸，小腿肚；（象、鯨等的）崽，幼獸；浮冰，幼冰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calf</b> is a young cow. 牛犢","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some other young animals, including elephants and whales, are called <b>calves</b>. (大象、鯨魚等的) 幼獸","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>calf</b> is the thick part at the back of your leg, between your ankle and your knee. 腓; 小腿肚","examples":["...a calf injury. …一處小腿的傷。"]}]}]},"cardboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"硬紙板，紙板箱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不真實的，做作的；硬紙板制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cardboard</b> is thick, stiff paper that is used, for example, to make boxes and models. 硬紙板","examples":["...a cardboard box. …一個紙板箱。"]}]}]},"caretaker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"看管者，看門人，管理員；看護者，照料者；臨時負責人，看守者；守護者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"臨時代理的（政府、領導人、教練等暫時任職的）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>caretaker</b> is a person whose job it is to take care of a house or property when the owner is not there. (主人不在時看管房子或財產的) 看管人","examples":["Slater remained at the house, acting as its caretaker when the family was not in residence. 這家人不在的時候，斯萊特留在這幢房子裡看家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>caretaker</b> is someone who is responsible for looking after another person, for example, a person who is disabled, ill, or very young. 看護者","examples":["His caretakers labelled him severely disabled. 他的看護人說他嚴重殘疾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>caretaker</b> is a person whose job it is to take care of a large building such as a school or an apartment house, and deal with small repairs to it. 物業管理員","examples":["The caretaker, a bundle of keys hanging from his belt, was standing at the door. 這位管理員正站在門口，腰帶上掛著一串鑰匙。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>caretaker</b> government or leader is in charge temporarily until a new government or leader is appointed. 臨時的 (政府或領導人)","examples":["The military intends to hand over power to a caretaker government and hold elections within six months. 軍方打算將權力移交給臨時政府，並在6個月內進行選舉。"]}]}]},"carnation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香石竹，康乃馨；肉紅色，粉紅色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"肉紅色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carnation</b> is a plant with white, pink, or red flowers. 康乃馨","examples":[]}]}]},"cannon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加農炮，大炮；自動機關炮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛撞，碰撞；炮轟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cannon</b> is a large gun, usually on wheels, which used to be used in battles. 大炮","examples":["The cannons boom, the band plays. 炮聲隆隆，鼓樂齊鳴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cannon</b> is a heavy automatic gun, especially one that is fired from an aircraft. 機關炮","examples":["Others carried huge cannons plundered from Russian aircraft. 其他人扛著從俄國飛機上搶來的巨型機關炮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is a <b>loose cannon</b>, they do whatever they want and nobody can predict what they are going to do. 隨心所欲的人","examples":["Max is a loose cannon politically. 馬克斯是個在政治上隨心所欲的人。"]}]}]},"canal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運河，灌溉渠，水道；（體內的）管，道"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……開鑿運河"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>canal</b> is a long, narrow stretch of water that has been made for boats to travel along or to bring water to a particular area. 運河","examples":["...the Grand Union Canal. …大聯盟運河。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>canal</b> is a narrow tube inside your body for carrying food, air, or other substances. (體內的) 管道","examples":["...delaying its progress through the alimentary canal. …透過消化道延遲它的作用。"]}]}]},"carton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"硬紙盒，塑膠盒；（內裝小盒的）大包裝盒，紙板箱；靶心白點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用盒包裝；製作紙箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carton</b> is a plastic or cardboard container in which food or drink is sold. (盛裝賣品的) 盒","examples":["A quarter carton of milk is cheaper than two single pints. 一夸脫的盒裝牛奶比兩盒一品脫的要便宜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>carton</b> to refer to the carton and its contents, or to the contents only. 盒; 盒裝物","examples":["He went to the shop for a carton of milk. 他到店裡買了一盒牛奶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>carton</b> is a large, strong cardboard box in which goods are stored and transported. 硬紙箱","examples":["Those boxes contain the archives of The New Yorker for the years 1925 to 1980. 那些紙箱裡裝著1925年到1980年的《紐約客》雜誌存檔。"]}]}]},"carbon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碳；複寫紙；炭精棒；碳纖維"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"碳的，碳處理的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Carbon</b> is a chemical element that diamonds and coal are made up of. (化學元素) 碳","examples":[]}]}]},"carp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鯉魚；抱怨；鯉科屬魚"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吹毛求疵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Carp）（美）卡普（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carp</b> is a kind of fish that lives in lakes and rivers. 鯉魚","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is carping</b>, you mean that they keep criticizing or complaining about someone or something, especially in a way you think is unnecessary or annoying. 吹毛求疵","examples":["He cannot understand why she's constantly carping at him. 他不理解為什麼她對他總是百般的挑剔。"]}]}]},"carnival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狂歡節，嘉年華會；<美>遊樂會，遊藝場；激動人心的事物組合，五彩繽紛事物的組合；慶祝活動；（學校的）遊園會，嘉年華會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>carnival</b> is a public festival during which people play music and sometimes dance in the streets. 狂歡節","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>carnival</b> is a travelling show which is held in a park or field and at which there are machines to ride on, entertainments, and games. 嘉年華","examples":[]}]}]},"category":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"種類，範疇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things are divided into <b>categories</b>, they are divided into groups in such a way that the members of each group are similar to each other in some way. 種類; 範疇","examples":["This book clearly falls into the category of fictionalized autobiography. 這本書顯然類屬自傳體小說。"]}]}]},"celery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芹菜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Celery</b> is a vegetable with long, pale green stalks. It is eaten raw in salads. 芹菜","examples":["...a stick of celery. …一根芹菜。"]}]}]},"cellar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"地下室，地窖；窖藏酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將（酒）存於地窖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cellar</b> is a room underneath a building, which is often used for storing things in. 地窖; 地下室","examples":["The box of papers had been stored in a cellar at the family home. 那盒檔案已存放在家中的一個地窖裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person's or restaurant's <b>cellar</b> is the collection of different wines that they have. 酒窖","examples":["Choose a superb wine to complement your meal from our extensive wine cellar. 從我們的大酒窖裡挑一瓶上等好酒來配你這頓飯菜吧。"]}]}]},"cello":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大提琴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cello</b> is a musical instrument with four strings that looks like a large violin. You play the cello with a bow while sitting down and holding it upright between your legs. 大提琴","examples":[]}]}]},"cathedral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大教堂，（主教控制的）教區總教堂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cathedral</b> is a very large and important church which has a bishop in charge of it. 大教堂; 主教座堂","examples":["...St. Paul's Cathedral. …聖保羅大教堂。"]}]}]},"celebrity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名聲，名望；名人，明星"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>celebrity</b> is someone who is famous, especially in areas of entertainment such as movies, music, writing, or sports. (尤指娛樂界的) 名人","examples":["In 1944, at the age of 30, Hersey suddenly became a celebrity. 1944年，30歲的赫西突然成了一位名人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing achieves <b>celebrity</b>, they become famous, especially in areas of entertainment such as movies, music, writing, or sports. (尤指娛樂界的) 名望","examples":["He achieved celebrity as a sports commentator. 他作為一名體育評論員而享譽四方。"]}]}]},"cellular phone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國英語）行動電話，手機：一種透過無線電波與基站通訊的無線通訊裝置，可用於語音通話、簡訊和網際網路服務。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cellular phone</b> or <b>cellular telephone</b> is a type of telephone which does not need wires to connect it to a telephone system. 行動電話","examples":[]}]}]},"cell-phone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cellphone</b> is the same as a mobile phone and a . 行動電話","examples":[]}]}]},"cellphone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<北美>行動電話，手機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cellphone</b> is the same as a mobile phone and a . 行動電話","examples":[]}]}]},"centigrade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"攝氏溫度"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"攝氏度的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Centigrade</b> is a scale for measuring temperature, in which water freezes at 0 degrees and boils at 100 degrees. It is represented by the symbol °C. 攝氏的 (簡寫為C)","examples":["...daytime temperatures of up to forty degrees centigrade. …高達40攝氏度的日間氣溫。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Centigrade</b> is also a noun. 攝氏","examples":["The number at the bottom is the recommended water temperature in centigrade. 底部的數字為建議性攝氏度水溫。"]}]}]},"caution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小心，謹慎；提醒，告誡；（警察向犯輕罪的人發出的）警告"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"警告，提醒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Caution</b> is great care which you take in order to avoid possible danger. 謹慎","examples":["Extreme caution should be exercised when buying used tyres. 買二手輪胎時一定要極其謹慎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Caution</b> is also a noun. 警告; 告誡","examples":["There was a note of caution for the treasury in the figures. 這些資料向財政部亮出了一個警告。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>cautions</b> you, they warn you about problems or danger. 警告; 告誡","examples":["Tony cautioned against misrepresenting the situation. 託尼告誡說不要歪曲事實。","The statement clearly was intended to caution Seoul against attempting to block the council's action again. 很顯然，這份宣告用意在於警告首爾別再試圖阻止委員會的行動。"]}]}]},"chairperson":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主席；議長；主持人（會議、委員會或組織的負責人，性別中立用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>chairperson</b> of a meeting, committee, or organization is the person in charge of it. (會議) 主持人; (委員會、組織的) 主席","examples":["She's the chairperson of the safety committee. 她是安全委員會主席。"]}]}]},"checkbook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"支票簿，支票本"}],"sections":[]},"ceremony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"儀式，典禮；禮節，禮儀，客套"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ceremony</b> is a formal event such as a wedding. 儀式; 典禮","examples":["...his grandmother's funeral, a private ceremony attended only by the family. …他祖母的葬禮，一場只有家人參加的私人儀式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ceremony</b> consists of the special things that are said and done on very formal occasions. (全套) 儀式","examples":["The republic was proclaimed with great ceremony. 以隆重的儀式宣告共和國成立。"]}]}]},"chairman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指男性）主席，（委員會或組織的）負責人；（公司）總裁，（組織）主席；會議主持人，大會主席；<史>轎伕；（自1949年）中國共產黨主席（Chairman）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"主持，掌管"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>chairman</b> of a committee, organization, or company is the head of it. (委員會、組織機構、公司的) 主席","examples":["Glyn Ford is chairman of the committee which produced the report. 格林·福特是撰寫該報告的委員會的主席。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>chairman</b> of a meeting or debate is the person in charge, who decides when each person is allowed to speak. (會議、辯論的) 主持人","examples":["The chairman declared the meeting open. 主持人宣佈會議開始。"]}]}]},"chairwoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女主席，女議長，（會議、委員會或組織等的）女性負責人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>chairwoman</b> of a meeting, committee, or organization is the woman in charge of it. (會議) 女主持人; (委員會、組織的) 女主席","examples":["Primakov was in Japan meeting with the chairwoman of the Socialist Party there. 普里馬科夫正在日本和那裡的社會黨女主席會面。"]}]}]},"certificate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"證明，證書；文憑，成績合格證書；電影放映許可證"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發證書給……，用證書證明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>certificate</b> is an official document stating that particular facts are true. 證明書","examples":["...birth certificates. …出生證明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>certificate</b> is an official document that you receive when you have completed a course of study or training. The qualification that you receive is sometimes also called a <b>certificate</b>. 結業證書","examples":["To the right of the fireplace are various framed certificates. 火爐右側是各式各樣加框的證書。"]}]}]},"chant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"反覆唱，反覆呼喊；唱聖歌，誦經文"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"反覆喊的話，反覆唱的調子；聖歌，頌歌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chant</b> is a word or group of words that is repeated over and over again. 重複的話語","examples":["He was greeted by the chant of \"Judas! Judas!\" 他迎來的是不絕於耳的呼喊“叛徒！叛徒！”。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chant</b> is a religious song or prayer that is sung on only a few notes. 聖歌; 讚美詩","examples":["...a Gregorian chant. …一首格列高利聖歌。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"重複的呼聲","examples":["A lot of the chanting was in support of the deputy prime minister. 很多不絕於耳的呼聲都支援副總理。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"吟誦聲","examples":["The chanting inside the temple stopped. 寺廟裡面的誦經聲停止了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chant</b> something or if you <b>chant</b>, you repeat the same words over and over again. 反覆地說","examples":["Demonstrators chanted slogans. 示威者們反覆地喊著口號。","The crowd chanted \"We are with you.\" 民眾反覆喊著“我們支援你。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>chant</b> or if you <b>chant</b> something, you sing a religious song or prayer. 吟誦; 唱聖歌","examples":["Muslims chanted and prayed. 穆斯林唱了聖歌並祈禱了。"]}]}]},"checkup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"健康檢查，體檢；檢查，審查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>checkup</b> is a medical examination by your doctor or dentist to make sure that there is nothing wrong with your health. 體檢","examples":["The disease was detected during a routine checkup. 這種疾病是在一次例行體檢中查出來的。"]}]}]},"check-in":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（機場、酒店等處）辦理登機、入住等手續，報到，登記；登機手續辦理處，報到處，登記處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"At an airport, a <b>check-in</b> is the counter or desk where you check in. 登機手續辦理處","examples":["The line at the check-in was already dispersing. 在登機手續辦理處排的隊已在散開了。"]}]}]},"chatter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘮叨，喋喋不休；唧唧叫，吱吱叫；咯咯作響，打顫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閒聊，閒扯；吱吱聲，唧唧聲；咯咯聲，打顫聲；（網路聊天室的）網友"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chatter</b>, you talk quickly and continuously, usually about things which are not important. 喋喋不休地說 (不重要的事)","examples":["Everyone's chattering away in different languages. 大家用不同的語言喋喋不休地說著。","Erica was friendly and chattered about Andrew's children. 埃麗卡很友好並絮叨起安德魯的孩子們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your teeth <b>chatter</b>, they keep knocking together because you are very cold or very nervous. (牙齒) 格格作響","examples":["She was so cold her teeth chattered. 她凍得連牙齒都格格作響。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When birds or animals <b>chatter</b>, they make high-pitched noises. (鳥類、動物) 鳴叫","examples":["Birds were chattering somewhere, and occasionally he could hear a vehicle pass by. 鳥兒們在某處啁啾，偶爾他能聽到一輛汽車經過。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chatter</b> is also a noun. 喋喋不休","examples":["...idle chatter. …閒聊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chatter</b> is also a noun. (鳥類、動物的) 鳴叫","examples":["...almond trees vibrating with the chatter of crickets. …伴隨蟋蟀的鳴叫而顫動的杏樹。"]}]}]},"chair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"椅子；主席，委員長；電椅；大學教授的職位"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"主席，主持；用椅子把某人高高抬起；使……入座；使就任要職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chair</b> is a piece of furniture for one person to sit on, with a back and four legs. 椅子","examples":["He rose from his chair and walked to the window. 他從椅子上站起來走到窗戶旁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"At a university, a <b>chair</b> is the position or job of professor. 大學教授","examples":["He has been appointed to the chair of sociology. 他受命任職社會學教授。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The person who is the <b>chair</b> <b>of</b> a committee or meeting is the person in charge of it. 主席","examples":["She is the chair of the Defense Advisory Committee on Women in the Military. 她是軍隊女兵國防顧問委員會的主席。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The chair</b> is the same as the . 死刑電椅","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>chair</b> a meeting or a committee, you are the person in charge of it. 擔任 (會議、委員會) 主席","examples":["He was about to chair a meeting in Venice of E.U. foreign ministers. 他將擔任威尼斯歐盟外交部長會議的主席 。"]}]}]},"check-out":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（旅館）結賬退房；退房截止時間；（商店）付款處，收銀臺；檢查，檢驗，核查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>check out</b> <b>of</b> a hotel or clinic where you have been staying, or if someone <b>checks</b> you <b>out</b>, you pay the bill and leave. 退房","examples":["They packed and checked out of the hotel. 他們收拾好行李，退了旅館的房。","I was disappointed to miss Bryan, who had just checked out. 我很失望沒見到布萊恩，他剛剛退房走了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>check out</b> something or someone, you find out information about them to make sure that everything is correct or satisfactory. 調查","examples":["Maybe we ought to go down to the library and check it out. 也許我們該去圖書館調查一下。","We ought to check him out on the computer. 我們應該在計算機上調查他的資訊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>checks out</b>, it is correct or satisfactory. 成立","examples":["She was in San Diego the weekend Jensen got killed. Her alibi checked out. 詹森遇害的那個週末她在聖地亞哥。她不在現場的申辯成立。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>check out</b> a library book, you borrow it for a fixed period of time. 借出","examples":["No books can be checked out after 6 p.m. tomorrow. 明天下午6點以後圖書不可以借出。"]}]}]},"chef":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廚師，主廚"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>當廚師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chef</b> is a cook in a restaurant or hotel. 廚師","examples":["...some of Australia's leading chefs. …一些澳大利亞的頂尖廚師們。"]}]}]},"chimpanzee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黑猩猩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chimpanzee</b> is a kind of small African ape. 黑猩猩","examples":[]}]}]},"chestnut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"栗子；慄樹；栗色；栗色馬；慄木；切斯特納特（姓氏 Chestnut）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"栗色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chestnut</b> or <b>chestnut tree</b> is a tall tree with broad leaves. 栗子樹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Chestnuts</b> are the reddish brown nuts that grow on chestnut trees. You can eat chestnuts. 栗子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>chestnut</b> is dark reddish brown in colour. 栗色","examples":["...chestnut hair. …栗色的頭髮。"]}]}]},"chemist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"化學家；<英>藥劑師；<英>藥店，藥房"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chemist</b> is a person who does research connected with chemistry or who studies chemistry. 化學家","examples":["She worked as a research chemist. 她是一名化學研究員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>chemist</b> or a <b>chemist's</b> is the same as a. 藥房","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>chemist</b> is the same as a. 同pharmacist","examples":[]}]}]},"chili":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紅辣椒，辣椒（美式英語；英式拼寫 chilli，可指果實或植株）；辣椒燉肉（chili con carne 的簡稱，用牛肉末、辣椒或辣椒粉、番茄和菜豆等燉成的辣味菜餚）"}],"sections":[]},"clam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛤，蛤蜊；<非正式>可食用的雙殼軟體動物（如扇貝）；<美，非正式>美元；<非正式>嘴緊的人，沉默寡言的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>挖蛤，拾蛤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clams</b> are a kind of shellfish which can be eaten. 蛤蜊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"...to gather clams. ...抓蛤蜊。","examples":[]}]}]},"choir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"唱詩班，合唱團；唱詩席；（合唱團的）聲部；一組同類樂器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"合唱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>choir</b> is a group of people who sing together, for example in a church or school. 唱詩班; 合唱團","examples":["He has been singing in his church choir since he was six. 他從6歲起就開始在教堂的唱詩班詠唱了。"]}]}]},"clan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宗族，氏族；<非正式>大家庭，大家族；<非正式>集團，幫派"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clan</b> is a group which consists of families that are related to each other. 家族","examples":["...rival clans. …敵對家族。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people with the same interests as a <b>clan</b>. 幫派","examples":["...a powerful clan of industrialists from Monterrey. …有權勢的一幫來自於蒙特雷的實業家們。"]}]}]},"circuit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電路，迴路；巡迴活動，巡迴地；環道，環線；巡迴賽；賽車道；（英國）巡迴審判區，巡迴上訴法院；（一套）體操動作；統一經營的連鎖劇院（或影院）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（繞……）環行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An electrical <b>circuit</b> is a complete route which an electric current can flow around. 電路","examples":["Any attempts to cut through the cabling will break the electrical circuit. 任何切斷電纜的做法都會使電路中斷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>circuit</b> is a series of places that are visited regularly by a person or group, especially as a part of their job. 巡迴的場所","examples":["It's a common problem, the one I'm asked about most when I'm on the lecture circuit. 這是個常見問題，一個在我巡迴演講時人們最常問到的問題。"]}]}]},"clasp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"釦子，釦環；緊握，緊抱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"扣住，扣緊；握緊，抱緊；緊緊纏繞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>clasp</b> someone or something, you hold them tightly in your hands or arms. 握緊; 抱緊","examples":["She clasped the children to her. 她緊緊地摟住孩子們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clasp</b> is a small device that fastens something. (拴牢某物的) 釦子; 勾子","examples":["...the clasp of her handbag. …她的手包扣。"]}]}]},"clover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"三葉草，苜蓿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clover</b> is a small plant with pink or white ball-shaped flowers and usually three round leaves. 三葉草","examples":["...a four leaf clover. ...一株四葉的三葉草。"]}]}]},"clause":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"從句，分句；（法律檔案的）條款"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clause</b> is a section of a legal document. (法律檔案的) 條款","examples":["He has a clause in his contract which entitles him to a percentage of the profits. 他在他的合同裡有一項條款保證他享有一定比例的利潤。","...a compromise document sprinkled with escape clauses. …一份滿是免責條款的妥協性檔案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>clause</b> is a group of words containing a verb. Sentences contain one or more clauses. 分句","examples":[]}]}]},"chord":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"和絃，和音；弦；（解）腱，帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以和絃演奏（或歌唱、譜曲）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chord</b> is a number of musical notes played or sung at the same time with a pleasing effect. 和絃","examples":["I could play a few chords on the guitar and sing a song. 我能彈一些擊他和絃唱一首歌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a straight line connecting two points on a curve or curved surface 弦; 連線弧線或弧形面兩點的直線","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>strikes a chord</b> <b>with</b> you, it makes you feel sympathy or enthusiasm. 引起同情; 引起共鳴","examples":["Mr. Jenkins's arguments for stability struck a chord with Europe's two most powerful politicians. 詹金斯先生支援穩定的觀點引起了歐洲兩位最有權力的政治家的共鳴。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to provide (a melodic line) with chords 用弦演奏(旋律)","examples":[]}]}]},"coastline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海岸線，海岸的輪廓線；沿海地帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A country's <b>coastline</b> is the outline of its coast. 海岸線","examples":["This is some of the most exposed coastline in the world. 這是世界上最無遮蔽的海岸線。"]}]}]},"cluster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組，簇；星團；一連串同類事件；（聚集在同一地方的）一群人；（計算機磁碟上的）叢集，群集；子音群，子音連綴；基"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"群聚，聚集；（資料點）具近似數值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cluster</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a small group of them close together. (人或物的) 群","examples":["...clusters of men in formal clothes. …幾組身著正裝的男人。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>cluster</b> <b>together</b>, they gather together in a small group. (人) 結成群","examples":["The passengers clustered together in small groups. 乘客們聚整合小群體。"]}]}]},"colonel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（陸軍、空軍或海軍陸戰隊）上校"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>colonel</b> is a senior officer in an army, air force, or the marines. (陸軍、空軍或海軍的) 上校","examples":["This particular place was run by an ex-Army colonel. 這個特別的地方歸一位前陸軍上校掌管。"]}]}]},"cocoon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繭，卵袋；（尤指保護性或安慰性的）遮蓋（或包裹）物；安全寧靜的地方，避風港；（防止金屬裝置腐蝕的）防護膜"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"庇護，將……保護起來；把……蓋住，把……包住；隱退（指避開公眾生活的壓力享受天倫之樂）；給……噴上保護層"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cocoon</b> is a covering of silky threads that the larvae of moths and other insects make for themselves before they grow into adults. 繭","examples":["...like a butterfly emerging from a cocoon. …好似蝴蝶破繭而出。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are in a <b>cocoon</b> <b>of</b> something, you are wrapped up in it or surrounded by it. 包圍層","examples":["He stood there in a cocoon of golden light. 他站在那兒，被一圈金色光環籠罩著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are living in a <b>cocoon</b>, you are in an environment in which you feel protected and safe, and sometimes isolated from everyday life. 隔護層; 與世隔絕","examples":["...her innocent desire to envelop her beloved in a cocoon of love. …她用愛呵護心上人的純真願望。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>cocoons</b> you <b>from</b> something, it protects you or isolates you from it. 把…保護或隔離起來","examples":["There is nowhere to hide when things go wrong, no organization to cocoon you from blame. 出了差錯無處可躲，沒有組織會庇護你免於責難。"]}]}]},"clutch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"緊握，緊抓；（因害怕或痛苦）突然抓住"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"離合器踏板；一小群，一小簇；勢力範圍，控制；緊握，緊抓；一窩（蛋）；<美>女式無帶手提包"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"關鍵性的；（尤指體育比賽中）在關鍵時刻表現良好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>clutch</b> <b>at</b> something or <b>clutch</b> something, you hold it tightly, usually because you are afraid or anxious. (因為害怕或焦慮而) 抓牢","examples":["I staggered and had to clutch at a chair for support. 我踉蹌了幾步，不得不抓住一把椅子扶穩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is in another person's <b>clutches</b>, that person has captured them or has power over them. 掌控","examples":["Tony fell into the clutches of an attractive American who introduced him to drugs. 託尼落入一個有魅力的美國人的掌控，那人給他介紹毒品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a vehicle, the <b>clutch</b> is the pedal that you press before you change gear. 離合器踏板","examples":["Laura let out the clutch and pulled slowly away down the drive. 勞拉鬆開離合器踏板，慢慢沿著車道把車開走了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a hatch of eggs laid by a particular bird or laid in a single nest 一窩蛋","examples":[]}]}]},"colleague":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同事，同僚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>colleagues</b> are the people you work with, especially in a professional job. 同事","examples":["Without consulting his colleagues, he flew from Los Angeles to Chicago. 在沒有和同事商量的情況下，他從洛杉磯飛到了芝加哥。"]}]}]},"colonial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"殖民地的，殖民主義的；殖民地時期風格的；群體的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指來自宗主國的）殖民地居民；殖民地時期式樣的房屋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Colonial</b> means relating to countries that are colonies, or to colonialism. 殖民地的; 殖民主義的","examples":["...the 31st anniversary of Jamaica's independence from British colonial rule. …牙買加擺脫英國殖民統治並獲得獨立的第31週年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>colonial</b> building or piece of furniture was built or made in a style that was popular in America in the 17th and 18th centuries. (17和18世紀美洲) 殖民地時期風格的","examples":["...the white colonial houses on the north side of the campus. …校園北邊的殖民地時期風格的白房子。"]}]}]},"coil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（繩或線等的）卷，匝；（電路的）線圈；（汽車發動機的）盤管；子宮節育環；蚊香；成卷郵票；<古>混亂，騷動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"卷，盤繞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coil</b> <b>of</b> rope or wire is a length of it that has been wound into a series of loops. (繩子或金屬線的) 圈","examples":["Tod shook his head angrily and slung the coil of rope over his shoulder. 託德生氣地搖搖頭，把那圈繩索甩過肩頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>coil</b> is one loop in a series of loops. 一圈","examples":["Pythons kill by tightening their coils so that their victim cannot breathe. 蟒蛇捕殺時緊緊盤成圈，使獵物無法呼吸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>coil</b> is a thick spiral of wire through which an electrical current passes.  線圈","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to wind or gather (ropes, hair, etc) into loops or (of rope, hair, etc) to be formed in such loops 將(繩、頭髮等)盤成圈","examples":[]}]}]},"comedian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喜劇演員，滑稽演員；劇作家；有趣的人，滑稽的人；（有時指言行）沒意思的人，無聊的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comedian</b> is an entertainer whose job is to make people laugh, by telling jokes or funny stories. 喜劇演員","examples":["...a stand-up comedian. …一位單人喜劇表演演員。"]}]}]},"comet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"彗星"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>comet</b> is a bright object with a long tail that travels around the sun. 彗星","examples":["Halley's Comet is going to come back in 2061. 哈雷彗星將在2061年返回。"]}]}]},"commentator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現場解說員，實況播音員；評論員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>commentator</b> is a broadcaster who gives a radio or television commentary on an event. (電臺或電視的) 解說員","examples":["...a sports commentator. …一名體育解說員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commentator</b> is also someone who often writes or broadcasts about a particular subject. 評論員","examples":["...a political commentator. …一名政治評論員。"]}]}]},"combat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰鬥，搏鬥；爭論，反對"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與……作鬥爭；防止，減輕"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"戰鬥的；為……鬥爭的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Combat</b> is fighting that takes place in a war. 戰鬥","examples":["Over 16 million men had died in combat. 一千六百多萬人在戰鬥中陣亡。","Yesterday saw hand-to-hand combat in the city. 昨天那座城裡發生了肉搏戰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>combat</b> is a battle, or a fight between two people. 搏鬥","examples":["It was the end of a long combat. 那是一場長時間搏鬥的結束。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people in authority <b>combat</b> something, they try to stop it from happening. 防止","examples":["Congress has criticized new government measures to combat crime. 國會批評了新政府防止犯罪的措施。"]}]}]},"commodity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商品，貨物；有用的東西，必需品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>commodity</b> is something that is sold for money. 商品","examples":["Prices went up on several basic commodities like bread and meat. 麵包、肉等幾種基本商品的價格上漲了。"]}]}]},"communist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"共產主義者，共產黨黨員"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"共產主義的，共產黨黨員的；共產黨的（Communist）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>communist</b> is someone who believes in communism. 共產主義者","examples":["Without the communists in France, the resistance might not have succeeded in World War II. 如果沒有法國的共產主義者，二戰中的抵抗運動可能不會成功。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Communist</b> means relating to communism. 共產主義的","examples":["...the Communist Party. …共產黨。"]}]}]},"commonplace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平凡的，不足為奇的；平庸的，陳腐的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"司空見慣的事，常見的東西；老生常談，陳詞濫調"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>commonplace</b>, it happens often or is often found, and is therefore not surprising. 常見的","examples":["Inter-racial marriages have become commonplace. 不同種族間的通婚已經變得很常見。"]}]}]},"commuter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"上下班往返的人"}],"sections":[]},"compass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指南針，羅盤；圓規，兩腳規；界限，範圍"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"繞（某物）而行，圍繞；圖謀完成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>compass</b> is an instrument that you use for finding directions. It has a dial and a magnetic needle that always points to the north. 羅盤","examples":["We had to rely on a compass and a lot of luck to get here. 我們只得靠羅盤和很大的運氣到達這兒。"]}]}]},"communism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"共產主義，共產主義理論（或制度）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Communism</b> is the political belief that all people are equal, that there should be no private ownership and that workers should control the means of producing things. 共產主義","examples":["...the ultimate triumph of communism in the world. …共產主義在全世界的最終勝利。"]}]}]},"commission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"考察團，委員會；佣金，回扣；犯罪；委託，命令；（軍隊中的）官職，軍銜；（尤指藝術品）委託製作；<古>所授之權，代辦權"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"委託撰寫，委託製作；委任，任命……為軍官；（使軍艦）正式使用，服現役"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>commission</b> something or <b>commission</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you formally arrange for someone to do a piece of work for you. 委託","examples":["The Department of Agriculture commissioned a study into organic farming. 農業部委託了一項有機耕作的研究。","You can commission them to paint something especially for you. 你可以委託他們專門為你畫點什麼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Commission</b> is also a noun. 委託","examples":["Our china can be bought off the shelf or by commission. 我們的瓷器可以現貨購買或委託定做。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commission</b> is a piece of work that someone is asked to do and is paid for. 委託任務","examples":["Just a few days ago, I finished a commission. 就在幾天之前我完成了一項委託任務。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Commission</b> is a sum of money paid to a salesperson for every sale that he or she makes. If a salesperson is paid <b>on</b> <b>commission</b>, the amount they receive depends on the amount they sell. 銷售佣金","examples":["The salespeople work on commission only. 推銷員只拿銷售佣金。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a bank or other company charges <b>commission</b>, they charge a fee for providing a service, for example for exchanging money or issuing an insurance policy. 服務費","examples":["Travel agents charge 1 per cent commission on tickets. 旅行社收1%的購票服務費。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>commission</b> is a group of people who have been appointed to find out about something or to control something. 委員會","examples":["The government has set up a commission to look into those crimes. 政府已成立一個委員會調查那些罪行。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a member of the armed forces receives a <b>commission</b>, he or she becomes an officer. 任命","examples":["He accepted a commission as a naval officer. 他接受了海軍軍官的任命。"]}]}]},"compassion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同情，憐憫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Compassion</b> is a feeling of pity, sympathy, and understanding for someone who is suffering. 同情","examples":["Elderly people need time and compassion from their physicians. 老年人需要醫生的時間和同情心。"]}]}]},"compact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"小型的，袖珍的；緊湊的；緊密的，堅實的；矮小而健壯的；（演講，作品）簡潔的，簡練的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"帶鏡小粉盒；合約，協定；小型汽車；袖珍物；坯塊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓緊，壓實；縮短，精簡；訂立（或簽訂）（協定）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Compact</b> things are small or take up very little space. You use this word when you think this is a good quality. 小巧的","examples":["...my compact office in Washington. …我在華盛頓的小巧辦公室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>compact</b> person is small but looks strong. 矮小結實的","examples":["He was compact, probably no taller than me. 他矮小結實，大概沒我高。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>compact</b> or a <b>compact car</b> is a car that is smaller than the average car, and that is economical to run. 小型汽車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a small flat case containing a mirror, face powder, etc, designed to be carried in a woman's handbag 化妝盒","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an official contract or agreement 官方合同; 官方協議","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to pack or join closely together; compress; condense 緊密地裝、連在一起; 壓縮; 濃縮","examples":[]}]}]},"comprehension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"理解力，領悟力；（聽力或閱讀）理解測試；包括，包含"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Comprehension</b> is the ability to understand something. 理解力","examples":["This was utterly beyond her comprehension. 這完全超出了她的理解力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Comprehension</b> is full knowledge and understanding of the meaning of something. 理解","examples":["They turned to one another with the same expression of dawning comprehension, surprise, and relief. 他們帶著一樣恍然大悟、驚奇、鬆了一口氣的表情相互看了看。"]}]}]},"comrade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夥伴，戰友；同志（用於社會主義政黨的成員之間）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>comrades</b> are your friends, especially friends that you share a difficult or dangerous situation with. (尤指共患難的) 同伴","examples":["Unlike so many of his comrades, he survived the war. 不像他的許多戰友，他在戰爭中倖存了下來。"]}]}]},"compliment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"讚揚，稱讚；問候，祝賀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"讚美，恭維"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>compliment</b> is a polite remark that you make to someone to show that you like their appearance, appreciate their qualities, or approve of what they have done. 恭維話","examples":["You can do no harm by paying a woman compliments. 對女人講恭維話不會有什麼害處。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>compliment</b> someone, you give them a compliment. 恭維","examples":["They complimented me on the way I looked each time they saw me. 他們每次見到我都就我的外貌恭維我。"]}]}]},"compromise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"折中，妥協；妥協方案，折中辦法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"妥協，讓步；危及，損害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>compromise</b> is a situation in which people accept something slightly different from what they really want, because of circumstances or because they are considering the wishes of other people. 折衷","examples":["Encourage your child to reach a compromise between what he wants and what you want. 鼓勵你的孩子在他想要的和你想要的之間折衷。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>compromise</b> <b>with</b> someone, you reach an agreement with them in which you both give up something that you originally wanted. You can also say that two people or groups <b>compromise</b>. 妥協","examples":["The government has compromised with its critics over monetary policies. 政府已經在貨幣政策上與其批評者們有了妥協。","\"Nine,\" I said. \"Nine thirty,\" he replied. We compromised on 9:15. “9點，”我說。“9：30，”他回答道。我們各讓一步定在9:15。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>compromises</b> themselves or <b>compromises</b> their beliefs, they do something which damages their reputation for honesty, loyalty, or high moral principles. 使 (自己、自己的信念) 降格","examples":["...members of the government who have compromised themselves by accepting bribes. 收受賄賂而使其聲譽受損的政府成員們。"]}]}]},"confession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"供認，供狀；承認，坦白；懺悔，告解；宣告，告白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>confession</b> is a signed statement by someone in which they admit that they have committed a particular crime. 供狀","examples":["They forced him to sign a confession. 他們強迫他簽了供狀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Confession</b> is the act of admitting that you have done something that you are ashamed of or embarrassed about. 承認","examples":["I have a confession to make. 我要作個坦白。","The diaries are a mixture of confession and observation. 這些日記混合著自白和一些觀察。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you make a <b>confession</b> <b>of</b> your beliefs or feelings, you publicly tell people that this is what you believe or feel. (對信念、情感的) 表白","examples":["...Tatyana's confession of love. …塔蒂安娜的愛的表白。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In the Catholic church and in some other churches, if you go to <b>confession</b>, you privately tell a priest about your sins and ask for forgiveness. (私下對神父的) 懺悔","examples":["He never went to Father Porter for confession again. 他再也沒私下去向波特神父懺悔。"]}]}]},"compound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"混合物，化合物；複合詞；大院，有圍牆的場地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"複合的，混合的；以複利計算的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使加重，使惡化；合成，混合；以複利計算支付；和解，私了"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>compound</b> is an enclosed area of land that is used for a particular purpose. 作特定用途的圍地","examples":["They took refuge in the embassy compound. 他們在大使館圍區內避難。","...a military compound. …一個軍事管轄區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In chemistry, a <b>compound</b> is a substance that consists of two or more elements. 化合物","examples":["Organic compounds contain carbon in their molecules. 有機化合物的分子裡含碳。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is a <b>compound</b> <b>of</b> different things, it consists of those things. 混合物","examples":["Honey is basically a compound of water, two types of sugar, vitamins and enzymes. 蜂蜜主要是水、兩種糖、維生素和酶的混合物。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Compound</b> is used to indicate that something consists of two or more parts or things. 複合的","examples":["...the big compound eyes of dragonflies. …蜻蜓的大複眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, a <b>compound</b> noun, adjective, or verb is one that is made up of two or more words, for example \"fire engine,\" \"bottle-green,\" and \"firelight.\" 合成的 (詞)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to mix or combine so as to create a compound or other product 透過混合或化合製成","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>compound</b> a problem, difficulty, or mistake means to make it worse by adding to it. 加劇","examples":["Additional loss of life will only compound the tragedy. 生命力的進一步喪失只會加重這一悲劇。","The problem is compounded by the medical system here. 這個問題被這裡的醫療體制弄得更糟。"]}]}]},"consent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"許可，允許；同意，贊同；正式批准檔案，批文"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贊同，准許，同意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give your <b>consent</b> <b>to</b> something, you give someone permission to do it. 准許","examples":["At approximately 11:30 p.m., Pollard finally gave his consent to the search. 大約晚上11:30的時候，波拉德終於對搜查予以同意。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>consent</b> <b>to</b> something, you agree to do it or to allow it to be done. 同意","examples":["He finally consented to go. 他最終同意去。","He asked Ginny if she would consent to a small celebration after the christening. 他問金尼她是否同意在洗禮儀式後來個小慶祝。"]}]}]},"conserve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護，儲存；節省，節約；使（量，如能量、質量）守恆；將……製成蜜餞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜜餞，果脯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>conserve</b> a supply of something, you use it carefully so that it lasts for a long time. 節省","examples":["The factories have closed for the weekend to conserve energy. 這些工廠在那個週末關了廠以節省能源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>conserve</b> something means to protect it from harm, loss, or change. 保護","examples":["...a big increase in U.S. aid to help developing countries conserve their forests. …美國對幫助發展中國家保護森林的援助的大幅增加。"]}]}]},"conduct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"實施，進行；指揮；帶領，引導；舉止，表現；傳導"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為，舉止；經營方式，管理方法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>conduct</b> an activity or task, you organize it and do it. 組織並實施","examples":["I decided to conduct an experiment. 我決定做一項實驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>conduct</b> yourself in a particular way, you behave in that way. (以某種方式) 表現","examples":["The way he conducts himself reflects on the family. 他的行為方式折射出他的家庭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When someone <b>conducts</b> an orchestra or choir, they stand in front of it and direct its performance. 指揮 (交響樂、合唱等)","examples":["Dennis had recently begun a successful career conducting opera. 丹尼斯最近成功地開始了指揮歌劇的生涯。","Solti continued to conduct here and abroad. 佐爾蒂繼續在國內外指揮。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>conducts</b> heat or electricity, it allows heat or electricity to pass through it or along it. 傳導 (熱、電)","examples":["Water conducts heat faster than air. 水比空氣導熱快。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>conduct</b> <b>of</b> a task or activity is the way in which it is organized and carried out. 進行實施","examples":["Also up for discussion will be the conduct of free and fair elections. 還需討論的是公平自由的選舉如何進行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>conduct</b> is the way they behave in particular situations. (某人在某情形中的) 行為方式","examples":["For Europeans, the law is a statement of basic principles of civilized conduct. 對歐洲人來說，該法律是對基本文明行為原則的表述。"]}]}]},"console":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"安慰；慰藉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"控制檯，儀表盤；電視機（或收音機）櫃；風琴的操作部分；（帶裝飾的）支架，支託"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>console</b> someone who is unhappy about something, you try to make them feel more cheerful. 安慰","examples":["\"Never mind, Ned,\" he consoled me. “不要緊，內德”，他安慰我說。","I can console myself with the fact that I'm not alone. 我可以用不只我一個人的這種事實來安慰自己。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"安慰","examples":["The only consolation for the baseball team is that they look likely to get another chance. 對這支棒球隊的惟一安慰是他們看來可能會得到另一次機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>console</b> is a panel with a number of switches or knobs that is used to operate a machine. 控制檯","examples":["Several nurses sat before a console of flickering lights and bleeping monitors. 幾名護士坐在燈光閃爍、監聽器嘟嘟作響的控制檯前。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an ornamental bracket, esp one used to support a wall fixture, bust, etc. 裝飾性支架","examples":[]}]}]},"constitutional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"憲法的；憲法規定的，合乎憲法的；體質的，體格的；本性的，天性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>保健散步"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Constitutional</b> means relating to the constitution of a particular country or organization. 有關憲法的; 有關章程的","examples":["The issue is one of constitutional and civil rights. 這問題涉及憲法的和民事的權利。"]}]}]},"contemporary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"當代的，現代的；同時期的，同時代的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同時代的人；同齡人，同輩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Contemporary</b> things are modern and relate to the present time. 當代的","examples":["She writes a lot of contemporary music for people like Whitney Houston. 她為惠特尼·休斯敦等人創作大量當代音樂作品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Contemporary</b> people or things were alive or happened at the same time as something else you are talking about. 同時代的","examples":["...drawing upon official records and the reports of contemporary witnesses. …藉助官方記錄以及當時目擊者的證言。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>contemporary</b> is a person who is or was alive at the same time as them. 同時代的人","examples":["Like most of my contemporaries, I grew up in a vastly different world. 像我同時代的大多數人一樣，我在一個非常不同的世界裡長大。"]}]}]},"contempt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輕視，蔑視；忽視，不顧；藐視法庭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>contempt</b> <b>for</b> someone or something, you have no respect for them or think that they are unimportant. 蔑視","examples":["He has contempt for those beyond his immediate family circle. 他對自己直系親屬以外的人都心懷蔑視。"]}]}]},"continuity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"連續性，連貫性；（電影、電視的）場景串聯，銜接；（邏輯上的）連線，聯結"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Continuity</b> is the fact that something continues to happen or exist, with no great changes or interruptions. 連續性; 持續性","examples":["...a tank designed to ensure continuity of fuel supply during aerobatics. …為特技飛行中確保持續供油而設計的油箱。"]}]}]},"convict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"定罪，宣判……有罪"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"已決犯，服刑囚犯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is convicted</b> <b>of</b> a crime, they are found guilty of that crime in a court of law. 證明…有罪","examples":["In 1977 he was convicted of murder and sentenced to life imprisonment. 在1977年，他因謀殺被判處終生監禁。","There was insufficient evidence to convict him. 沒有足夠的證據證明他有罪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>convict</b> is someone who is in prison. 囚犯","examples":["...Neil Jordan's tale of two escaped convicts who get mistaken for priests. …尼爾·喬丹的兩個越獄囚犯被誤認為是牧師的故事。"]}]}]},"copyright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"版權，著作權"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"版權的，受版權保護的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得……的版權；保護……的版權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has the <b>copyright</b> on a piece of writing or music, it is illegal to reproduce or perform it without their permission. 版權","examples":["Who owns the copyright on this movie? 誰擁有這部電影的版權？"]}]}]},"coral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"珊瑚；（作珠寶的）珊瑚寶石；珊瑚色，橘紅色；珊瑚蟲；龍蝦卵，扇貝卵"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"珊瑚色的，淺橘紅色的；珊瑚的，珊瑚制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Coral</b> is a hard substance formed from the bones of very small sea animals. It is often used to make jewellery. 珊瑚","examples":["The women have elaborate necklaces of turquoise and pink coral. 女士們擁有綠寶石和粉色珊瑚製成的精美項鍊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Corals</b> are very small sea animals. 珊瑚蟲","examples":["The seas around Bermuda are full of colourful corals and fantastic fish. 百慕大周圍的海域中到處都是五彩的珊瑚蟲和奇異的魚類。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>coral</b> is dark orangey-pink in colour. 珊瑚色的","examples":["...coral lipstick. …珊瑚色的口紅。"]}]}]},"corporation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社團，公司，法人（團體）；市政當局"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>corporation</b> is a large business or company with special rights and powers. 大公司; 企業","examples":["...multinational corporations. …跨國公司。","Many voters resented the power of big corporations. 許多投票人憎恨大公司的權力。"]}]}]},"corridor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（建築物或火車內的）通道，過道；（一國領土透過他國境內的）走廊；狹長地帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>corridor</b> is a long passage in a building, with doors and rooms on one or both sides. 走廊","examples":["There were doors on both sides of the corridor. 走廊的兩側都有門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>corridor</b> is a strip of land that connects one country to another or gives it a route to the sea through another country. 走廊地帶 (與另一國家相連或穿越另一國取得出海通道的狹長地帶)","examples":["East Prussia and the rest of Germany were separated, in 1919, by the Polish Corridor. 1919年，波蘭走廊把東普魯士和德國其他地方分隔開了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>corridor</b> is an area of land between 2 large cities. (兩大城市之間的) 走廊地帶","examples":["...the Northeast corridor. …東北走廊地帶。"]}]}]},"counselor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧問，諮詢師；律師，法律顧問；（學校或夏令營的）輔導員（counsellor 的美式拼寫）；（使館的）參贊，參事"}],"sections":[]},"correspondence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信件，信函；通訊；相似，關聯；一致"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Correspondence</b> is the act of writing letters to someone. 通訊","examples":["The judges' decision is final and no correspondence will be entered into. 法官們的判決為終審判決，所以再寫信也不會付以審議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>correspondence</b> is the letters that they receive or send. 信件","examples":["He always replied to his correspondence. 他總是來函必復。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If there is a <b>correspondence</b> <b>between</b> two things, there is a close similarity or connection between them. 一致","examples":["In African languages there is a close correspondence between sounds and letters. 在非洲各語言中，語音和字母之間有著密切的對應關係。"]}]}]},"courtyard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"庭院，院子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>courtyard</b> is an open area of ground which is surrounded by buildings or walls. 庭院","examples":["They walked together through the arch and into the cobbled courtyard. 他們一起走過拱門，來到了鋪著鵝卵石的庭院。"]}]}]},"creek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小溪；小灣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>creek</b> is a small stream or river. 小溪; 小河","examples":["Follow Austin Creek for a few miles. 沿著奧斯汀河走上幾英里。"]}]}]},"coupon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"贈券，優惠券；（剪自報刊的）參賽表，訂貨單；（債券的）息票；（尤指戰時食品、衣服或其他商品的）配給券，票證；（固定利息證券的）票面利率；<英>（足球博彩或其他比賽的）彩票；<蘇格蘭，愛爾蘭>臉，面孔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coupon</b> is a piece of printed paper which allows you to pay less money than usual for a product, or to get it free. 優惠券","examples":["...a money-saving coupon. …一張省錢的優惠券。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>coupon</b> is a small form, for example, in a newspaper or magazine, which you send off to ask for information, to order something, or to enter a competition. (報紙、雜誌附的) 傳單","examples":["Mail this coupon with your cheque or postal order. 把這張表單和你的支票或匯款單一起郵寄。"]}]}]},"crater":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（撞擊或爆炸形成的）坑，彈坑；火山口；穴，洞；（古希臘用的）調酒碗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（地面或行星）上形成坑；<美，非正式>失敗，突然落下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crater</b> is a very large hole in the ground, which has been caused by something hitting it or by an explosion. (撞擊或爆炸形成的) 大坑","examples":["The explosion, believed to be a car bomb, left a ten-foot crater in the street. 這次爆炸，據說是一個汽車炸彈引起的，在街道上留下了一個10英尺的大坑。"]}]}]},"cracker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薄脆餅乾；彩色爆竹；<英，非正式>好東西，有趣的事物；駭客；精神崩潰的人，斷裂（或裂開）的東西；<英，非正式>迷人的女子；<美，非正式>車把式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cracker</b> is a thin, crisp piece of baked bread which is often eaten with cheese. 薄脆餅乾","examples":[]}]}]},"counsel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忠告，建議；辯護律師；<古>諮詢，磋商"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"建議，勸告（做……）；為……提供諮詢，給……提供建議；商討，提出忠告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Counsel</b> is advice. 勸告","examples":["He had always been able to count on her wise counsel. 他總是能夠指望她明智的忠告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>counsel</b> is the lawyer who gives them advice on a legal case and speaks on their behalf in court. 辯護律師","examples":["Singleton's counsel said after the trial that he would appeal. 庭審之後辛格爾頓的辯護律師說他會上訴。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>counsel</b> someone <b>to</b> take a course of action, or if you <b>counsel</b> a course of action, you advise that course of action. 建議; 提議","examples":["My advisers counselled me to do nothing. 我的顧問建議我不要做任何事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>counsel</b> people, you give them advice about their problems. 提供建議","examples":["...a psychologist who counsels people with eating disorders. …一名向飲食紊亂症患者提供諮詢的心理醫生。"]}]}]},"creak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（門、木地板等）嘎吱作響；（比喻）因過勞或緊張而顯得虛弱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘎吱聲；（Creak）（愛、英）克里克（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>creaks</b>, it makes a short, high-pitched sound when it moves. 嘎吱作響","examples":["The bed-springs creaked. 床的彈簧嘎吱作響。","The door creaked open. 門嘎吱一聲開了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Creak</b> is also a noun. 嘎吱聲","examples":["The door was pulled open with a creak. 門嘎吱一聲被拉開了。"]}]}]},"crib":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（有圍欄的）嬰兒床；飼料槽，秣槽；<英>聖誕馬槽（表現耶穌誕生的情景）；<英，非正式>（學生用於作弊的）夾帶；<非正式>（尤指學生偷偷摸摸地用的課文的）對照譯文；抄襲（或剽竊）來的東西；<美，非正式>住處，小窩；克里比奇紙牌戲（cribbage 的簡稱）；（克里比奇牌戲中的）配點牌張；（建築物的）木籠，（礦井的）井框（=cribwork）；<澳新>簡單飯菜，快餐"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>抄襲，剽竊；<古>束縛，限制；<英，舊>抱怨，發牢騷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crib</b> is a bed for a baby. 嬰兒床","examples":[]}]}]},"crocodile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鱷魚；鱷魚皮（皮革）；（短語 crocodile tears）鱷魚的眼淚，假慈悲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crocodile</b> is a large reptile with a long body and strong jaws. Crocodiles live in rivers and eat meat. 鱷魚","examples":[]}]}]},"crouch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"蹲下，蹲伏；俯身接近；（動物）蜷伏"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蹲（伏）的姿勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are crouching</b>, your legs are bent under you so that you are close to the ground and leaning forward slightly. 蹲伏","examples":["We were crouching in the bushes. 我們那時正蹲伏在灌木叢中。","I crouched on the ground. 我蹲伏在地上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crouch</b> is also a noun. 蹲伏","examples":["They walked in a crouch, each bent over close to the ground. 他們蹲伏著行走，一個個彎著腰快要貼著地面了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crouch down</b> means the same as . 蹲下","examples":["He crouched down and reached under the mattress. 他蹲下來，把手伸到了床墊下面。"]}]}]},"crossing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人行橫道，渡口；交叉口，十字路口；橫渡，橫越；（十字形教堂中）中殿和耳堂相交處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"穿越，橫渡；交叉；反對（cross 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crossing</b> is a journey by boat or ship to a place on the other side of an ocean, river, or lake. 橫渡","examples":["He made the crossing from Cape Town to Sydney in just over twenty-six days. 他從開普敦橫渡到悉尼只用了二十六天多時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crossing</b> is a place where two roads, paths, or lines cross. 交叉路口","examples":["She sighed and squatted down next to the crossing of the two trails. 她嘆了口氣，在兩條小路的交叉口旁蹲了下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>crossing</b> is the same as a  or a . 平交道口","examples":[]}]}]},"cuisine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烹飪，風味；飯菜，菜餚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>cuisine</b> of a country or district is the style of cooking that is characteristic of that place. 烹調風格","examples":["The cuisine of Japan is low in fat. 日式烹調脂肪含量低。"]}]}]},"crunch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘎吱嘎吱地嚼；（使）發出碎裂聲；嘎吱嘎吱地行進；（大量地）處理（數字）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"壓碎聲，碎裂聲；<非正式>危急關頭，艱難局面（the crunch）；不足，短缺；仰臥起坐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>crunch</b> something hard, such as a sweet, or if it <b>crunches</b>, you crush it noisily between your teeth. 嘎吱嘎吱地咬嚼 (某物); 發出嘎吱聲","examples":["She sucked an ice cube into her mouth, and crunched it loudly. 她把一冰塊兒含在嘴裡，並嘎吱嘎吱地大聲嚼起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>crunches</b> or if you <b>crunch</b> it, it makes a breaking or crushing noise, for example, when you step on it. 嘎吱嘎吱地碾或踩 (某物); 發出嘎吱聲","examples":["A piece of china crunched under my foot. 一塊瓷片在我的腳下發出嘎吱的響聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>crunch</b> numbers means to do a lot of calculations using a calculator or computer. (用計算器或電腦) 運算","examples":["I pored over the books with great enthusiasm, often crunching the numbers until 1:00 a.m. 我饒有興趣地細讀這些書，常常運算到凌晨1：00。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crunch</b> is also a noun. 嘎吱嘎吱的聲音","examples":["She heard the crunch of tyres on the gravel driveway. 她聽到車胎碾在碎石鋪成的私家車道上發出的嘎吱聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an important time or event, for example, when an important decision has to be made, as <b>the</b> <b>crunch</b>. 關鍵時刻","examples":["He can rely on my support when the crunch comes. 在關鍵時刻他會得到我的支援的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A situation in which a business or economy has very little money can be referred to as a <b>crunch</b>. 財政困難","examples":["The U.N. is facing a cash crunch. 聯合國正面臨著資金短缺。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>crunch</b> across a surface made of very small stones, you move across it causing it to make a crunching noise. 嘎吱嘎吱地踩","examples":["I crunched across the gravel. 我從石子上嘎吱嘎吱地踩過。"]}]}]},"curb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"控制，抑制；勒住（馬）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"控制，抑制；<美>路緣，馬路牙子；（馬的跗關節後部因扭傷韌帶引起的）硬瘤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>curb</b> something, you control it and keep it within limits. 抑制","examples":["...advertisements aimed at curbing the spread of AIDS. …旨在抑制愛滋病蔓延的廣告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>curb</b> an emotion or your behaviour, you keep it under control. 控制 (脾氣、行為等)","examples":["He curbed his temper. 他控制住了自己的脾氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curb</b> is also a noun. 控制; 限制","examples":["He called for much stricter curbs on immigration. 他呼籲對移民實行更為嚴格的限制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a swelling on the leg of a horse, below the point of the hock, usually caused by a sprain (馬腿上由扭傷導致的)腫脹","examples":[]}]}]},"curriculum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"課程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>curriculum</b> is all the different courses of study that are taught in a school, college, or university. 總課程","examples":["Teachers incorporated business skills into the regular school curriculum. 教師們將商業技能納入學校常規課程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>curriculum</b> is one particular course of study that is taught in a school, college, or university. 課程","examples":["...the history curriculum. …歷史課程。"]}]}]},"curry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"咖哩菜餚；咖哩粉"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以（肉或蔬菜）烹製咖哩燒菜，給……加咖哩（粉）；拍馬屁，奉承；（用馬梳）梳刷，梳洗（馬匹）；鞣製；鞭打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Curry</b> is a dish composed of meat and vegetables, or just vegetables, in a sauce containing hot spices. It is usually eaten with rice and is one of the main dishes of India. 咖哩","examples":["...vegetable curry. …蔬菜咖哩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to prepare (food) with curry powder or sauce 加咖哩粉(或醬)的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person tries to <b>curry favour</b> <b>with</b> another, they do things in order to try to gain their support or cooperation. 討好某人","examples":["Politicians are eager to promote their \"happy family\" image to curry favour with voters. 政客們積極推廣其“幸福家庭”的形象以討好選民。"]}]}]},"crystal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結晶，晶體；水晶；水晶玻璃；（鐘錶的）石英玻璃保護面，錶蒙子"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"晶瑩的，清澈透明的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crystal</b> is a small piece of a substance that has formed naturally into a regular symmetrical shape. 結晶體","examples":["...salt crystals. …鹽的結晶體。","...ice crystals. …冰晶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Crystal</b> is a transparent rock that is used to make jewellery and ornaments. 水晶","examples":["She was wearing a strand of crystal beads. 她戴著一串水晶珠子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Crystal</b> is a high quality glass, usually with patterns cut into its surface. 晶質玻璃","examples":["Some of the finest drinking glasses are made from lead crystal. 一些最精緻的酒杯是用鉛晶質玻璃製成的。"]}]}]},"customs":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海關；關稅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Customs</b> is the official organization responsible for collecting taxes on goods coming into a country and preventing illegal goods from being brought in. 海關部門","examples":["What right does Customs have to search my car? 海關有什麼權力搜查我的車？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Customs</b> is the place where people arriving from a foreign country have to declare goods that they bring with them. 海關","examples":["He walked through customs. 他步行透過了海關。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Customs</b> duties are taxes that people pay for importing and exporting goods. 海關的","examples":["Personal property which is to be re-exported at the end of your visit is not subject to customs duties. 停留結束時要再次帶出境的個人物品免收關稅。"]}]}]},"declaration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宣告，表白；申報（單）；（板球）對一賽局結束的宣佈；公告，宣告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>declaration</b> is an official announcement or statement. 官方宣告","examples":["The opening speeches sounded more like declarations of war than offerings of peace. 那些開幕辭聽起來更像宣戰書而不是和平倡議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>declaration</b> is a firm, emphatic statement which shows that you have no doubts about what you are saying. 宣言","examples":["...declarations of undying love. …永恆愛情的宣言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>declaration</b> is a written statement about something which you have signed and which can be used as evidence in a court of law. 書面宣告","examples":["On the customs declaration, the sender labelled the freight as agricultural machinery. 在報關單上，發貨方將貨物列為農業機械。"]}]}]},"dazzle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（強光）使目眩，使眼花；使驚歎，使眼花繚亂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（光的）炫目，耀眼；燦爛，令人讚歎的特質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>dazzles</b> you, you are extremely impressed by their skill, qualities, or beauty. 使傾倒","examples":["George dazzled her with his knowledge of the world. 喬治對世界的瞭解令她傾倒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a bright light <b>dazzles</b> you, it makes you unable to see properly for a short time. 使目眩","examples":["The sun, glinting from the pool, dazzled me. 池水折射的陽光使我目眩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>dazzle</b> <b>of</b> something is a quality it has, such as beauty or skill, which is impressive and attractive. 絢爛; 輝煌","examples":["The dazzle of stardom and status attracts them. 明星和身份的耀眼光環吸引著他們。"]}]}]},"democrat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國）民主黨黨員；民主主義者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>Democrat</b> is a member or supporter of a particular political party which has the word \"democrat\" or \"democratic\" in its title, for example, the Democratic Party in the United States. 民主黨人","examples":["Murray has joined other Senate Democrats in blocking the legislation. 默裡已經加入其他民主黨參議員反對這項立法了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>democrat</b> is a person who believes in the ideals of democracy, personal freedom, and equality. 民主主義者","examples":["This is the time for democrats and not dictators. 這是民主主義者而不是獨裁者的時代。"]}]}]},"delegation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代表團；授權，委派"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>delegation</b> is a group of people who have been sent somewhere to have talks with other people on behalf of a larger group of people. 代表團","examples":["...the Chinese delegation to the UN talks in New York. …在紐約參加聯合國談判的中國代表團。"]}]}]},"currency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"通貨，貨幣；通用，流行；現時性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The money used in a particular country is referred to as its <b>currency</b>. 貨幣","examples":["Tourism is the country's top earner of foreign currency. 旅遊業是該國外匯收入最高的行業。","More people favour a single European currency than oppose it. 支援歐洲單一貨幣的人比反對的多。"]}]}]},"denial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"否認；拒絕接受，拒不承認；剝奪，拒絕給予"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>denial</b> of something is a statement that it is not true, does not exist, or did not happen. 否認","examples":["It seems clear that despite official denials, differences of opinion lay behind the ambassador's decision to quit. 很清楚，儘管官方否認，人們對大使決定辭職還是有不同看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>denial</b> <b>of</b> something to someone is the act of refusing to let them have it. 拒絕給予","examples":["...the denial of visas to international relief workers. …對國際救濟工作人員拒發籤證。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In psychology, <b>denial</b> is when a person cannot or will not accept an unpleasant truth. (不愉快事實的) 拒絕接受","examples":["With major life traumas, like losing a loved one, for instance, the mind's first reaction is denial. 面對人生的重大創痛，例如失去深愛的人，心理的第一反應就是拒絕接受。"]}]}]},"decay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（建築、地方等）破敗，衰落；（觀念、影響力等）衰敗；（使）腐朽，腐爛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"腐爛；（觀念、機構、制度等）衰退"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as a dead body, a dead plant, or a tooth <b>decays</b>, it is gradually destroyed by a natural process. 腐壞","examples":["The bodies buried in the fine ash slowly decayed. 埋在細灰裡的屍體慢慢腐爛了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a society, system, or institution <b>decays</b>, it gradually becomes weaker or its condition gets worse. (社會、制度或機構) 衰敗","examples":["In practice, the agency system has decayed. Most \"agents\" now sell only to themselves or their immediate family. 實際上，這種代理制已經衰退。現在，大多數“代理人”都只把產品賣給自己或親近的家人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Decay</b> is also a noun. 腐壞","examples":["When not removed, plaque causes tooth decay and gum disease. 牙斑沒有清除就會導致蛀牙和牙齦疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Decay</b> is also a noun. 衰敗","examples":["There are problems of urban decay and gang violence. 存在都市衰敗和黑幫暴力問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"腐壞的","examples":["Even young children have teeth so decayed they need to be pulled. 連幼兒也有這麼嚴重的齲齒，需要拔掉。"]}]}]},"dart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"飛奔，猛衝；瞥，急掃（一眼）；（為施藥而）用飛鏢射（動物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"飛鏢；飛鏢遊戲；縫褶；猛衝，突進；（恐懼、憤怒等的）一陣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>darts</b> somewhere, they move there suddenly and quickly. 飛奔; 猛衝","examples":["Ingrid darted across the deserted street. 英格里德飛奔過空無一人的街道。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dart</b> a look <b>at</b> someone or something, or if your eyes <b>dart</b> <b>to</b> them, you look at them very quickly. 投射 (目光)","examples":["She darted a sly sideways glance at Bramwell. 她狡猾地斜瞟了布萊威爾一眼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dart</b> is a small, narrow object with a sharp point which can be thrown or shot. 飛鏢","examples":["Markov died after being struck by a poison dart. 馬爾科夫被毒鏢擊中後身亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Darts</b> is a game in which you throw darts at a round board which has numbers on it. 擲鏢遊戲","examples":["I started playing darts at 15. 我從15歲開始玩擲鏢遊戲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a tapered tuck made in dressmaking (衣服的)褶","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"any of various tropical and semitropical marine fish 熱帶和亞熱帶魚類","examples":[]}]}]},"detergent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洗滌劑，去汙劑"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"使清潔的，（與）清潔新增劑（有關）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Detergent</b> is a chemical substance, usually in the form of a powder or liquid, which is used for washing things such as clothes or dishes. 清潔劑","examples":["...a brand of detergent. …一種品牌的清潔劑。"]}]}]},"despair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"絕望；令人絕望的人或事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"絕望，喪失信心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Despair</b> is the feeling that everything is wrong and that nothing will improve. 絕望","examples":["I looked at my wife in despair. 我絕望地看著妻子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>despair</b>, you feel that everything is wrong and that nothing will improve. 絕望","examples":["\"Oh, I despair sometimes,\" he says in mock sorrow. “哦，我有時會絕望。”他假裝悲傷地說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>despair of</b> something, you feel that there is no hope that it will happen or improve. If you <b>despair of</b> someone, you feel that there is no hope that they will improve. 對…絕望","examples":["He wished to earn a living through writing but despaired of doing so. 他原想透過寫作謀生，但卻對此絕望了。"]}]}]},"destination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目的地，終點，目標"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"作為目的地的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>destination</b> of someone or something is the place to which they are going or being sent. 目的地","examples":["Ellis Island has become one of America's most popular tourist destinations. 埃利斯島已經成為美國最受歡迎的遊覽地之一。"]}]}]},"destiny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"命運，定數；天意，命運之神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>destiny</b> is everything that happens to them during their life, including what will happen in the future, especially when it is considered to be controlled by someone or something else. 命運","examples":["We are masters of our own destiny. 我們是自己命運的主人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Destiny</b> is the force which some people believe controls the things that happen to you in your life. 天數; 定數","examples":["Is it destiny that brings people together, or is it accident? 是定數，還是偶然，將人們帶到一起？"]}]}]},"disciple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耶穌的十二門徒之一（=the Disciples）；追隨者，門徒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are someone's <b>disciple</b>, you are influenced by their teachings and try to follow their example. 信徒","examples":["...a major intellectual figure with disciples throughout Europe. …一位信徒遍佈歐洲的重要知識分子。"]}]}]},"disbelief":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懷疑，不信；（宗教）無信仰，不信宗教"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disbelief</b> is not believing that something is true or real. 懷疑","examples":["She looked at him in disbelief. 她懷疑地看著他。"]}]}]},"devotion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"摯愛，忠誠；奉獻；（宗教的）虔誠；祈禱，禮拜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Devotion</b> is great love, affection, or admiration for someone. 熱愛","examples":["At first she was flattered by his devotion. 最初他的摯愛使她感到受寵若驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Devotion</b> is commitment to a particular activity. 獻身","examples":["...devotion to the cause of the people and to socialism. …對於人民的事業和社會主義的獻身。"]}]}]},"dialect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方言，土話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dialect</b> is a form of a language that is spoken in a particular area. 方言","examples":["It is often appropriate to use the local dialect to communicate your message. 用方言來交流資訊往往很合適。"]}]}]},"discard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扔掉，棄置；打出（無用的牌），墊（牌）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"被拋棄物；（紙牌遊戲中）墊出的牌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>discard</b> something, you get rid of it because you no longer want it or need it. 丟棄","examples":["Read the manufacturer's guidelines before discarding the box. 先閱讀製造商的說明書再把盒子丟掉。"]}]}]},"doorstep":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"門階"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doorstep</b> is a step in front of a door on the outside of a building. 門前臺階","examples":["...a youth who was sitting on a doorstep, drinking. …一個坐在門前臺階上喝酒的年輕人。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place is <b>on</b> your <b>doorstep</b>, it is very near to where you live. If something happens <b>on</b> your <b>doorstep</b>, it happens very close to where you live. 在住所附近","examples":["It is easy to lose sight of what is happening on our own doorstep. 家門口發生的事反而容易被我們忽視。"]}]}]},"doorway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"門道；門口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doorway</b> is a space in a wall where a door opens and closes. 門口","examples":["Hannah looked up to see David and another man standing in the doorway. 漢納抬起頭，看到戴維和另一個男人站在門口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>doorway</b> is a covered space just outside the door of a building. 門廊","examples":["...homeless people sleeping in doorways. …睡在門廊裡的無家可歸者。"]}]}]},"distress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憂慮，悲傷；貧困；危難，險情；（肉體的）劇痛"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使悲傷，使憂慮；使（傢俱，皮革）有仿磨損的痕跡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Distress</b> is a state of extreme sorrow, suffering, or pain. 悲痛; 疼痛","examples":["Jealousy causes distress and painful emotions. 嫉妒會引發悲傷和痛苦的情緒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Distress</b> is the state of being in extreme danger and needing urgent help. 危難; 危急","examples":["He expressed concern that the ship might be in distress. 他對船可能處在危急狀態表示憂慮。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>distresses</b> you, they cause you to be upset or worried. 使心煩; 使憂慮","examples":["The idea of Toni being in danger distresses him enormously. 想到託尼仍處在危險當中就使他憂心忡忡。"]}]}]},"dough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生麵糰；<舊>錢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dough</b> is a fairly firm mixture of flour, water, and sometimes also fat and sugar. It can be cooked to make bread or pastry. 麵糰","examples":["Roll out the dough into one large circle. 將麵糰擀成一個大圓形。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to money as <b>dough</b>. 錢","examples":["He worked hard for his dough. 他為了賺錢而努力工作。"]}]}]},"dormitory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"集體宿舍；<美>（學院或大學的）學生宿舍樓；<英>（為在附近城市裡工作的人提供的）住宅城，郊外居住區"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英>（供在另一個城市工作的人）住宅的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dormitory</b> is a building at a college or university where students live. 宿舍樓","examples":["She lived in a college dormitory. 她住在一幢大學宿舍樓裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dormitory</b> is a large bedroom where several people sleep, for example, in a boarding school. 宿舍","examples":["...the boys' dormitory. …男生宿舍。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to a place as a <b>dormitory</b> <b>community</b> or <b>suburb</b>, you mean that most of the people who live there travel to work in a city or another, larger town a short distance away. (指通勤者居住的) 臥室社群","examples":[]}]}]},"document":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"檔案，公文，文獻；證件，單據；（計算機）檔案，文件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"記錄，記載（詳情）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>document</b> is one or more official pieces of paper with writing on them. 檔案; 公文","examples":["She produces legal documents for a downtown Seattle law firm. 她為西雅圖市區的一家法律事務所撰寫法律檔案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>document</b> is a piece of text or graphics, for example, a letter, that is stored as a file on a computer and that you can access in order to read it or change it. 文件","examples":["When you are finished typing, remember to save your document. 輸入完畢後，要記著儲存文件。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>document</b> something, you make a detailed record of it in writing or on film or tape. 記錄","examples":["He wrote a book documenting his prison experiences. 他寫了一本書，記錄他的牢獄經歷。"]}]}]},"drape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用布簾等鬆散地披掛或覆蓋；使（布料、衣物）呈褶襉狀"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"成褶皺狀垂下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窗簾，尤指長而厚重的簾子（美式英語，常用複數）；布料垂墜或懸掛的方式、狀態；褶襉；手術洞巾；（德語、瑞典語人名）德拉佩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>drape</b> a piece of cloth somewhere, you place it there so that it hangs down in a casual and graceful way. 將…披掛於","examples":["Natasha took the coat and draped it over her shoulders. 娜塔莎拿起外套，披在肩上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is draped</b> <b>in</b> a piece of cloth, they are loosely covered by it. 覆蓋","examples":["...a casket draped in the Virginia flag. …一口覆蓋著弗吉尼亞州旗的棺材。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drapes</b> are long heavy curtains. (長且重的) 簾子","examples":["He pulled the drapes shut, locked the door behind him. 他拉上長簾,鎖上了身後的門。"]}]}]},"distinction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"差別，區分；傑出，卓越；特點；榮譽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>distinction</b> <b>between</b> similar things is a difference. 區別","examples":["There are obvious distinctions between the two wine-making areas. 這兩個釀酒區之間有明顯的不同。","The distinction between craft and fine art is more controversial. 工藝和美術之間的區別更有爭議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>distinction</b> is a special award or honour that is given to someone because of their very high level of achievement. 榮譽","examples":["The award was established in 1902 as a special distinction for eminent men and women. 該獎設立於1902年，作為特別榮譽頒給傑出的男士和女士。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Distinction</b> is the quality of being very good or better than other things of the same type. 卓越","examples":["Lewis emerges as a composer of distinction and sensitivity. 劉易斯脫穎而出，成為一位有卓越能力和敏銳度的作曲家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>the</b> <b>distinction</b> <b>of</b> being something, you are drawing attention to the fact that they have the special quality of being that thing. <b>Distinction</b> is normally used to refer to good qualities, but can sometimes also be used to refer to bad qualities. 特質","examples":["He has the distinction of being regarded as the Federal Republic's greatest living writer. 他有一種特質，因此被認為是聯邦共和國在世的最偉大的作家。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>draw a distinction</b> or <b>make a distinction</b>, you say that two things are different. 區分","examples":[]}]}]},"dresser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"梳妝檯，化妝臺；<北美>抽屜櫃，五斗櫃（常帶鏡子）；<英>碗櫃，餐具櫃；穿著…的人（如 a smart dresser 衣著講究的人）；（劇院/影視）服裝師；<舊>裹傷員；（Dresser）德雷瑟（英、德人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dresser</b> is a chest of drawers, sometimes with a mirror on the top. 梳妝檯","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>dresser</b> to refer to the kind of clothes that a person wears. For example, if you say that someone is a <b>casual dresser</b>, you mean that they wear casual clothes. 穿著…衣服的人","examples":["Mr. Jorgensen was an immaculate dresser. 喬根森先生是個衣著考究的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a person employed to assist actors in putting on and taking off their costumes 服裝師","examples":[]}]}]},"driveway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（從建築物、住宅、車庫等通往公共道路的）私人車道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>driveway</b> is a piece of hard ground that leads from the road to the front of a house, garage, or other building. 私人車道","examples":["I was running down the driveway to the car and I lost my balance. 我正沿著車道向車子跑去，然後我失去了平衡。"]}]}]},"dusk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃昏，傍晚；暮色；昏暗，幽暗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>變暗，變黑；使變微暗"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<文>幽暗的，昏暗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dusk</b> is the time just before night when the daylight has almost gone but when it is not completely dark. 黃昏","examples":["We arrived home at dusk. 我們於黃昏時分到家了。"]}]}]},"dwelling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"住宅，住所，公寓"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"居住（dwell 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dwelling</b> or a <b>dwelling place</b> is a place where someone lives. 住所; 居住地","examples":["Some 3,500 new dwellings are planned for the area. 大約三千五百套新住宅計劃在這個地區新建。"]}]}]},"dressing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（拌制色拉用的）調料；餡，填料；（保護傷口的）敷料；穿衣，打扮；肥料"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……穿衣服；打扮（dress 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A salad <b>dressing</b> is a mixture of oil, vinegar, and herbs or flavourings, which you pour over salad. 色拉調料","examples":["Mix the ingredients for the dressing in a bowl. 在碗裡把這些配料攪拌成調味品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dressing</b> is a covering that is put on a wound to protect it while it heals. 敷料","examples":["Miss Finkelstein will put a dressing on your thumb. 芬克爾斯坦小姐將在你的大拇指上包一層敷料。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Dressing</b> is a mixture of food that is cooked and then put inside a bird such as a turkey before it is eaten. (烹調時塞入火雞等中的) 填料","examples":["...cornbread dressing for the first Thanksgiving she cooked at home. …她在家為第一個感恩節烹製的玉米餅填料。"]}]}]},"eel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鱔魚，鰻魚；鰻魚肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>eel</b> is a long, thin fish that looks like a snake. 鰻魚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Eel</b> is the flesh of this fish eaten as food. 鰻肉","examples":["...smoked eel. …燻鰻。"]}]}]},"duration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"持續，持續時間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>duration</b> <b>of</b> an event or state is the time during which it happens or exists. 持續期間","examples":["He was given the task of protecting her for the duration of the trial. 他被委以在審判期間保護她的任務。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will happen <b>for the duration</b>, you mean that it will happen for as long as a particular situation continues. 在整個時間段","examples":["His wounds knocked him out of combat for the duration. 在整個戰鬥中，他的傷一直令他無法參戰。"]}]}]},"dwarf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（神話中有魔法的）小矮人；侏儒，矮子；矮星"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使顯得矮小，使相形見絀"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"矮小的，矮種的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person or thing <b>is dwarfed</b> by another, the second is so much bigger than the first that it makes them look very small. 使…顯得過於矮小","examples":["His figure is dwarfed by the huge red McDonald's sign. 他的個子被巨大的紅色麥當勞招牌襯得格外矮小。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dwarf</b> is used to describe varieties or species of plants and animals which are much smaller than the usual size for their kind. (植物或動物) 過於矮小的","examples":["...dwarf shrubs. …過於矮小的灌木叢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In children's stories, a <b>dwarf</b> is an imaginary creature that is like a small man. Dwarfs often have magical powers. (童話中的) 小矮人","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In former times, people who were much smaller than normal were called <b>dwarves</b>. 侏儒","examples":[]}]}]},"eclipse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"日食，月食；黯然失色；羽毛暗淡期；消失，喪失"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"遮住……的光，使黯然失色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>eclipse</b> <b>of</b> the sun is an occasion when the moon is between the earth and the sun, so that for a short time you cannot see part or all of the sun. An <b>eclipse</b> <b>of</b> the moon is an occasion when the earth is between the sun and the moon, so that for a short time you cannot see part or all of the moon. (日、月) 食","examples":["...an eclipse of the sun. …一次日食。","...the solar eclipse on May 21. …5月21日的日食。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>is eclipsed</b> <b>by</b> a second thing that is bigger, newer, or more important than it, the first thing is no longer noticed because the second thing gets all the attention. 使黯然失色","examples":["...the space programme has been eclipsed by other pressing needs. …這項太空計劃和其他的緊迫需要相比已經黯然失色了。"]}]}]},"ego":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自負，自尊，自我意識；（心理學）自我"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>ego</b> is their sense of their own worth. For example, if someone has a large <b>ego</b>, they think they are very important and valuable. 自我價值感","examples":["He had a massive ego, never would he admit he was wrong. 他有極強的自我價值感，從來不會承認他錯了。"]}]}]},"endeavor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"努力，盡力，嘗試；（尤指需要努力或勇氣的）活動，事業（英式拼作 endeavour）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"努力，盡力（通常後接不定式）（英式拼作 endeavour）"}],"sections":[]},"enrollment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"登記，註冊，入學，入伍；入學人數，註冊人數"}],"sections":[]},"embrace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擁抱；欣然接受，樂意採納；包括，涉及；圍繞，環繞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擁抱；接受，信奉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>embrace</b> someone, you put your arms around them and hold them tightly, usually in order to show your love or affection for them. You can also say that two people <b>embrace</b>. 擁抱","examples":["Penelope came forward and embraced her sister. 佩內洛普走上前來擁抱了她的妹妹。","At first people were sort of crying for joy and embracing each other. 開始時人們有點喜極而泣，互相擁抱。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Embrace</b> is also a noun. 擁抱","examples":["...a young couple locked in an embrace. …緊緊相擁的年輕一對。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Embrace</b> is also a noun. 欣然接受; 信奉","examples":["The marriage signalled James's embrace of the Catholic faith. 這場婚姻標誌著詹姆士對天主教的信奉。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>embrace</b> a change, political system, or idea, you accept it and start supporting it or believing in it. 欣然接受; 信奉","examples":["He embraces the new information age. 他歡迎新的資訊時代。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>embraces</b> a group of people, things, or ideas, it includes them in a larger group or category. 囊括","examples":["...a theory that would embrace the whole field of human endeavour. …一個囊括人類整個奮鬥領域的理論。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to commit or attempt to commit embracery against (a jury, etc) 籠絡(陪審員等)","examples":[]}]}]},"escort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"護送者，護衛隊，護航艦；（通常指異性的）社交聚會陪伴者，伴遊；陪護，護送"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"押送；護送，護衛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>escort</b> someone somewhere, you accompany them there, usually in order to make sure that they leave a place or get to their destination. 護送","examples":["I escorted him to the door. 我護送他到門口。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>escort</b> is a person who travels with someone in order to protect or guard them. 護送者","examples":["He arrived with a police escort shortly before half past nine. 快到9點半時，他由警察護送到達了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>escort</b> is a person who accompanies another person of the opposite sex to a social event. Sometimes people are paid to be escorts. (異性的) 社交陪同","examples":["My sister needed an escort for a company dinner. 我妹為了一個公司晚宴而需要一個社交陪同。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is taken somewhere <b>under escort</b>, they are accompanied by guards, either because they have been arrested or because they need to be protected. 在押送下; 在護送下","examples":[]}]}]},"estate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"財產，遺產；大片私有土地，莊園；<英>住宅區，工業區；<舊>社會階層；（生活）狀況，條件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>estate</b> is a large area of land in the country which is owned by a person, family, or organization. 莊園","examples":["He spent holidays at the 300-acre estate of his aunt and uncle. 他在叔叔和嬸嬸的300英畝莊園裡度過許多假日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>estate</b> is all the money and property that they leave behind when they die. 遺產","examples":["His estate was valued at $150,000. 他的遺產價值為15萬美元。"]}]}]},"evergreen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"常綠的；經久不衰的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常綠植物；經久不衰的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>evergreen</b> is a tree or bush that has green leaves all year long. 常青樹; 常綠植物","examples":["Holly, like ivy and mistletoe, is an evergreen. 冬青與常春藤和槲寄生一樣，也是一種常綠植物。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Evergreen</b> is also an adjective. 常綠的","examples":["Plant evergreen shrubs around the end of the month. 大約在月末種植常綠灌木。"]}]}]},"enterprise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"企業，事業單位；事業心，進取心；事業；創業，企業經營"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>enterprise</b> is a company or business. 公司; 企業","examples":["There are plenty of small industrial enterprises. 有很多小型的工業企業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>enterprise</b> is something new, difficult, or important that you do or try to do. 事業","examples":["Horse breeding is indeed a risky enterprise. 養馬的確是一項有風險的事業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Enterprise</b> is the activity of managing companies and businesses and starting new ones. 創業","examples":["He is still involved in voluntary work promoting local enterprise. 他仍從事志願工作推動當地創業。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Enterprise</b> is the ability to think of new and effective things to do, together with an eagerness to do them. 開創力; 開拓精神","examples":["...the spirit of enterprise worthy of a free and industrious people. …與一個自由勤勞的民族相稱的開拓精神。"]}]}]},"exaggeration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誇張，言過其實；（藝術等的）誇張手法"}],"sections":[]},"ethic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為準則，道德規範，倫理標準；信仰"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（與）道德規範（有關）的，（與）倫理（有關）的（=ethical）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ethics</b> are moral beliefs and rules about right and wrong. 道德","examples":["Refugee workers said such action was a violation of medical ethics. 難民工作者稱這種行為違背了醫學道德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>ethics</b> are the moral principles about right and wrong behaviour that they believe in. 行為準則","examples":["He told the police that he had thought honestly about the ethics of what he was doing. 他告訴警察他曾真誠地考慮過他所作所為依據的行為準則。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ethics</b> is the study of questions about what is morally right and wrong. 倫理學","examples":["...the teaching of ethics and moral philosophy. …倫理學和道德哲學的教學。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>ethic</b> of a particular kind is an idea or moral belief that influences the behaviour, attitudes, and philosophy of a group of people. 道德觀念","examples":["...the ethic of public service. …公共服務的道德觀念。"]}]}]},"esteem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尊重，敬重"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"尊重，敬重；認為，把……看作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Esteem</b> is the admiration and respect that you feel toward another person. 敬重","examples":["He is held in high esteem by colleagues in the construction industry. 他深受建築業的同事們的敬重。"]}]}]},"excess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"超過，過量；越軌行為，暴行；無節制，無度；（保險中的）免賠額"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過多的，超額的；額外的，附加的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>excess</b> <b>of</b> something is a larger amount than is needed, allowed, or usual. 過量","examples":["An excess of house plants in a small apartment can be oppressive. 在一套狹小公寓裡放過多的室內植物會給人壓抑感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>excess</b> is a sum of money which an insured person has to pay toward the cost of an insurance claim. The insurance company pays the rest. 免賠額; 該公司對於1800英鎊的保單要求21歲以下者負擔400英鎊的免賠額。","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Excess</b> is used to describe amounts that are greater than what is needed, allowed, or usual. 過量的","examples":["After cooking the fish, pour off any excess fat. 烹調完魚後，倒掉多餘的油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Excess</b> is used to refer to additional amounts of money that need to be paid for services and activities that were not originally planned or taken into account. 額外的","examples":["Make sure that you don't have to pay expensive excess charges. 確保你不需要支付昂貴的額外費用。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>In excess of</b> means more than a particular amount. 超過","examples":["The value of the company is well in excess of $2 billion. 該公司的價值遠超過20億美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>to excess</b>, you do it too much. 過度地; 過多地","examples":["I was reasonably fit, played a lot of tennis, and didn't smoke or drink to excess. 我那時很健康，常打網球，不過度抽菸或喝酒。"]}]}]},"exterior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外部的，外面的；外表的，表面的；（電影場景）外部拍攝的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外觀，外部；外貌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>exterior</b> of something is its outside surface. 外部","examples":["The exterior of the building was a masterpiece of architecture, elegant and graceful. 該建築物在外觀上是一項建築傑作，精美雅緻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone's usual appearance or behaviour as their <b>exterior</b>, especially when it is very different from their real character. 外表","examples":["According to Mandy, Pat's tough exterior hides a shy and sensitive soul. 據曼迪說，帕特堅強的外表下藏著一個害羞、敏感的靈魂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>exterior</b> to refer to the outside parts of something or things that are outside something. 外面的","examples":["The exterior walls were made of preformed concrete. 外牆是用預製混凝土建造的。"]}]}]},"eyelash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"睫毛，眼睫毛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>eyelashes</b> are the hairs that grow on the edges of your eyelids. 睫毛","examples":[]}]}]},"eyelid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（解剖）眼瞼，眼皮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>eyelids</b> are the two pieces of skin that cover your eyes when they are closed. 眼皮","examples":[]}]}]},"exile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流放；被流放者，流亡者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"流放；使離開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is living <b>in</b> <b>exile</b>, they are living in a foreign country because they cannot live in their own country, usually for political reasons. (通常出於政治原因的) 流亡他國","examples":["He is now living in exile in Egypt. 他現在流亡在埃及。","He returned from exile earlier this year. 今年年初他流亡歸國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>exile</b> is someone who has been exiled. 流亡者","examples":["He is also an exile, a native of Palestine who has long given up the idea of going home. 他也是個流亡者，一個早已放棄回家念頭的巴勒斯坦人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Exile</b> is also a noun. 逐出","examples":["...the Left's long exile from power from 1958 to 1981. …左派從1958至1981年的長期失權。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is exiled</b>, they are living in a foreign country because they cannot live in their own country, usually for political reasons. (通常出於政治原因而) 放逐他國","examples":["His second wife, Hilary, had been widowed, then exiled from South Africa. 他的第二任妻子希拉里曾一度孀居，之後被逐出南非。","They threatened to exile her in southern Spain. 他們威脅要把她放逐到西班牙南部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has been exiled</b> <b>from</b> a particular place or situation, you mean that they have been sent away from it or removed from it against their will. 逐出","examples":["He served less than a year of a five-year prison sentence, but was permanently exiled from the sport. 他5年刑期只服了1年不到，但被永遠逐出了體育界。"]}]}]},"delegate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代表；委員會成員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"授權，把……委託給；選派（某人做某事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>delegate</b> is a person who is chosen to vote or make decisions on behalf of a group of other people, especially at a conference or a meeting. 代表","examples":["The Canadian delegate offered no reply. 那位加拿大代表沒給答覆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"委託; 授權","examples":["A key factor in running a business is the delegation of responsibility. 經商的一個關鍵因素是責任委託。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>delegate</b> duties, responsibilities, or power <b>to</b> someone, you give them those duties, those responsibilities, or that power so that they can act on your behalf. 委託; 授權","examples":["He talks of travelling less, and delegating more authority to his deputies. 他說要減少旅行，還有要授予他的副手們更多的權力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are delegated</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are given the duty of acting on someone else's behalf by making decisions, voting, or doing some particular work. 委派","examples":["Officials have now been delegated to start work on a draft settlement. 官員們現已被委派開始準備一份擬定協議。"]}]}]},"executive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"行政的，有執行權的；高檔的，豪華的；供主管人員使用的；（有關）經營管理的，領導的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"主管，經理；行政部門，執行委員會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>executive</b> is someone who is employed by a business at a senior level. Executives decide what the business should do, and ensure that it is done. 執行總監","examples":["...an advertising executive. …一位廣告執行總監。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>executive</b> committee or board of an organization is a committee within that organization that has the authority to make decisions and ensures that these decisions are carried out. 執行委員會","examples":["They opted to put an executive committee in charge of the project rather than a single person. 他們選擇由一個執行委員會而非個人來負責這個專案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The executive</b> is the part of the government of a country that is concerned with carrying out decisions or orders, as opposed to the part that makes laws or the part that deals with criminals. (政府的) 行政部門","examples":["The government, the executive and the judiciary are supposed to be separate. 政府、行政和司法應該彼此分立。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>executive</b> sections and tasks of an organization are concerned with the making of decisions and with ensuring that decisions are carried out. 執行的","examples":["A successful job search needs to be as well organized as any other executive task. 一次成功的尋職要像任何其他執行任務一樣精心安排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Executive</b> goods are expensive products designed or intended for executives and other people at a similar social or economic level. 高階的","examples":["...an executive briefcase. …一個高階公文包。"]}]}]},"external":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外部的，外面的；對外的，與外國有關的；外來的，外聘的；（藥品等類似物質）外用的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外表，外部特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>External</b> is used to indicate that something is on the outside of a surface or body, or that it exists, happens, or comes from outside. 外部的; 外來的; 外在的","examples":["...a much reduced heat loss through external walls. …透過外牆的大大減少的熱量損失。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>External</b> means involving or intended for foreign countries. 涉外的; 對外的","examples":["...the commissioner for external affairs. …外事專員。","...Jamaica's external debt. …牙買加的外債。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>External</b> means happening or existing in the world in general and affecting you in some way. 外界的","examples":["Such events occur only when the external conditions are favourable. 此類事件只有當外界條件有利時才會發生。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"外部地; 外來地; 外在地","examples":["Vitamins can be applied externally to the skin. 維他命可以外用於皮膚上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"涉外地; 對外地","examples":["...protecting the value of the dollar both internally and externally. …保護美元在國內外的價值。"]}]}]},"fabric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"布料，織物；構造，結構；（汽車的）車身，（飛機的）機身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fabric</b> is cloth or other material produced by weaving together cotton, nylon, wool, silk, or other threads. Fabrics are used for making things such as clothes, curtains, and sheets. 織物","examples":["...small squares of red cotton fabric. …幾小塊方形紅棉布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>fabric</b> of a society or system is its basic structure, with all the customs and beliefs that make it work successfully. (社會或系統的) 結構","examples":["The fabric of society has been deeply damaged by the previous regime. 社會結構已被上屆執政者嚴重地破壞了。"]}]}]},"extension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"延伸，擴充套件；展期，延長期；擴建部分，延伸部分；（電話）分機；副檔名；（為非全日制學生開設的）進修部；牽伸（術）；外延；廣延（性）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>extension</b> is a new room or building that is added to an existing building or group of buildings. (已有建築或建築群的) 延伸建築","examples":["We are thinking of having an extension built, as we now require an extra bedroom. 我們正在考慮擴建房屋，因為我們現在需要多一間臥室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>extension</b> is a new section of a road or railway that is added to an existing road or railway. (已有公路、鐵路的) 延長路段","examples":["...a proposed extension to the No. 7 subway line. …提議的地鐵7號線的一段延長路段。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>extension</b> is an extra period of time for which something lasts or is valid, usually as a result of official permission. 延長的期限","examples":["He first entered the country on a six-month visa, and was given a further extension of six months. 他最初憑有效期為6個月的簽證進入這個國家，之後又得到了6個月的續簽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Something that is an <b>extension</b> <b>of</b> something else is a development of it that includes or affects more people, things, or activities. 延展","examples":["Many Filipinos see the bases as an extension of American colonial rule. 許多菲律賓人把這些基地看作是美國殖民統治的延展。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>extension</b> is a telephone line that is connected to the switchboard of a company or institution, and that has its own number. The written abbreviation  is also used. (電話的) 分機","examples":["She can get me on extension 308. 她可以透過分機308找到我。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"An <b>extension</b> is a part connected to a piece of equipment in order to make it reach something further away. (裝置的) 延伸部分","examples":["...a 30-foot extension cord. …一條30英尺的延長線。"]}]}]},"fahrenheit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Fahrenheit）華氏溫標（亦指華氏溫度）；法倫海特（德國物理學家，發明水銀溫度計並制定華氏溫標）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（Fahrenheit）華氏的，華氏溫度計的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fahrenheit</b> is a scale for measuring temperature, in which water freezes at 32 degrees and boils at 212 degrees. It is represented by the symbol °F. 華氏的","examples":["By mid-morning, the temperature was already above 100 degrees Fahrenheit. 到上午10點左右，氣溫已超過華氏100度了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fahrenheit</b> is also a noun. 華氏溫標","examples":["He was asked for the boiling point of water in Fahrenheit. 有人問他華氏溫標下水的沸點。"]}]}]},"fad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指短暫和無根據的）時尚，狂熱；一時的愛好；苛求，過分講究"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>fad</b> to refer to an activity or topic of interest that is very popular for a short time, but which people become bored with very quickly. 一時的狂熱","examples":["Hamnett does not believe environmental concern is a passing fad. 哈姆內特不相信對環境的關注是一時的狂熱。"]}]}]},"fertilizer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肥料，化肥；受精媒介物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fertilizer</b> is a substance such as solid animal waste or a chemical mixture that you spread on the ground in order to make plants grow more successfully. 肥料","examples":["...farming without any purchased chemical, fertilizer or pesticide. …不使用任何購買的化學品、肥料或殺蟲劑的耕作。"]}]}]},"fiance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"未婚夫"}],"sections":[]},"fiber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"纖維，纖維材料（等於 fibre）；膳食纖維，粗纖維（食物中不能消化的植物性物質）；品質，骨氣（常作 moral fiber）；光纖，光導纖維（optical fiber 的簡稱）；（Fiber）（匈）菲貝爾（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"fatigue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疲乏，厭倦；（金屬部件的）疲勞；（士兵穿的）工作服；士兵雜役（尤指作為懲罰,如做打掃、幫廚）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使疲勞，使勞累"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"疲勞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fatigue</b> is a feeling of extreme physical or mental tiredness. 疲憊","examples":["She continued to have severe stomach cramps, aches, fatigue, and depression. 她仍有嚴重的胃痙攣、疼痛、疲憊和抑鬱症狀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that people are suffering from a particular kind of <b>fatigue</b> when they have been doing something for a long time and feel they can no longer continue to do it. 疲乏","examples":["...compassion fatigue caused by endless TV and celebrity appeals. …電視和名人無休止的呼籲所引起的憐憫疲勞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fatigue</b> in metal or wood is a weakness in it that is caused by repeated stress. Fatigue can cause the metal or wood to break. (金屬、木材的) 疲勞","examples":["The problem turned out to be metal fatigue in the fuselage. 問題原來出在機身的金屬疲勞。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Fatigues</b> are clothes that soldiers wear when they are fighting or when they are doing routine jobs. 軍服","examples":["He never expected to return home wearing combat fatigues. 他從未想到會穿著作戰服回家。"]}]}]},"feminine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"女性特有的，女子氣的；女性的，婦女的；（語法）陰性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（語法）陰性詞，陰性形式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Feminine</b> qualities and things relate to or are considered typical of women, in contrast to men. 女性的","examples":["...male leaders worrying about their women abandoning traditional feminine roles. …擔心他們的女人會拋棄傳統女性角色的男性領導人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>feminine</b> has qualities that are considered typical of women, especially being pretty or gentle. 女人味的","examples":["I've always been attracted to very feminine women who are not overpowering. 我總是被那些不強悍的女人味十足的女人所吸引。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some languages, a <b>feminine</b> noun, pronoun, or adjective has a different form from a masculine or neuter one, or behaves in a different way. 陰性的","examples":[]}]}]},"fishery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漁業，水產業；漁場；養魚場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fisheries</b> are areas of the sea where fish are caught in large quantities for commercial purposes. 漁場","examples":["...the fisheries off Newfoundland. …紐芬蘭附近的那些漁場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fishery</b> is a place where fish are bred and reared. 養魚場","examples":[]}]}]},"fin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（魚的）鰭；鰭狀物，（飛機或汽車的）尾翅，尾翼；（潛水者的）腳蹼；散熱片"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（穿著腳蹼）在水下游泳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A fish's <b>fins</b> are the flat parts which stick out of its body and help it to swim and keep its balance. 鰭","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fin</b> on something such as an aeroplane, rocket, or bomb is a flat part which sticks out and which is intended to help control its movement. (飛機、火箭、炸彈等的) 翼","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a five-dollar bill 五美元鈔票","examples":[]}]}]},"fiddle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指厭煩或緊張地）不停擺弄；<非正式>篡改，偽造；拉小提琴；略微變動；調整"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>小提琴；<非正式>欺詐，騙局；<非正式>修理，調整；<非正式>難事；（防止餐具在惡劣天氣條件下滾落或滑落的）餐桌緣框"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fiddle with</b> an object, you keep moving it or touching it with your fingers. 不停擺弄","examples":["Harriet fiddled with a pen on the desk. 哈麗雅特不停地擺弄桌上的一支鋼筆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fiddle with</b> something, you change it in minor ways. 略微改動","examples":["She told Whistler that his portrait of her was finished and to stop fiddling with it. 她告訴惠斯勒他為她畫的肖像已經完成了，不要再改來改去了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fiddle with</b> a machine, you adjust it. 除錯","examples":["He turned on the radio and fiddled with the knob until he got a talk show. 他開啟收音機，調動旋鈕，直到他收到了一個談話節目。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people call violins <b>fiddles</b>, especially when they are used to play folk music. 小提琴","examples":["Hardy played the fiddle at local dances. 哈迪在當地的舞會上拉了小提琴。"]}]}]},"flake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小薄片，碎片；雪花；<非正式>古怪的人，不可靠的人；（考古）石片，堅硬石片；晾乾架，擱架；（航海）（卷繩或盤索的）一圈；（Flake）<美>弗拉克（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"剝落，將……剝落；使成薄片；（航海）把（繩子）鬆鬆挽好；<非正式>入睡，筋疲力盡（flake out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flake</b> is a small thin piece of something, especially one that has broken off a larger piece. 小薄片 (尤指碎片)","examples":["...flakes of paint. …顏料碎片。","Large flakes of snow began swiftly to fall. 大片大片的雪花開始飛快地落下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone as a <b>flake</b>, you mean that you think they are very unreliable. 不可靠的人","examples":["Sophie turned out to be such a flake. She said she'd meet me here and instead I'm just lying around this hotel room and I'm totally bored. 索菲原來是這麼不可靠。她說過要在這裡見我，可現在我只能躺在這間旅館的房間裡，感到百無聊賴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a rack or platform for drying fish or other produce (魚等的)晾乾架","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as paint <b>flakes</b>, small thin pieces of it come off. (油漆等) 剝落","examples":["They can see how its colours have faded and where paint has flaked. 他們可以看到其顏色褪去的情況和油漆剝落的地方。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flake off</b> means the same as . 剝落","examples":["The surface corrosion was worst where the paint had flaked off. 油漆已經剝落的地方，表面的腐蝕最嚴重。"]}]}]},"flaw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺點，缺陷；裂痕，瑕疵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"削弱，使失效"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flaw</b> <b>in</b> something such as a theory or argument is a mistake in it, which causes it to be less effective or valid. (理論或論點中的) 欠缺","examples":["There were, however, a number of crucial flaws in his monetary theory. 然而，他的貨幣理論中有很多關鍵性的欠缺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>flaw</b> <b>in</b> someone's character is an undesirable quality that they have. (性格中的) 缺點","examples":["The only flaw in his character seems to be a short temper. 他性格中唯一的缺點似乎就是脾氣急躁。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>flaw</b> <b>in</b> something such as a pattern or material is a fault in it that should not be there. 瑕疵","examples":["It's like having a flaw in a piece of material - the longer you leave it, the weaker it gets. 這就像一塊料子上有瑕疵一樣—你把它放得越久，它就變得越不結實。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a sudden short gust of wind; squall 一陣狂風","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a spell of bad, esp windy, weather 一陣壞天氣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make or become blemished, defective, or imperfect 使有缺陷","examples":[]}]}]},"filter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過濾器；濾光器，濾聲器，濾波器；過濾程式，過濾軟體；（指示車輛轉彎的）分流指示燈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"過濾；滲入，透過；（訊息、資訊等）慢慢傳開，走漏；緩慢進入，陸續步入；（車輛）看到分流指示燈的訊號後轉彎；（用程式）篩選"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>filter</b> a substance means to pass it through a device which is designed to remove certain particles contained in it. 過濾","examples":["The best prevention for cholera is to boil or filter water, and eat only well-cooked food. 預防霍亂最好的方法是把水煮沸或過濾，並且只吃煮熟的食物。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If light or sound <b>filters</b> <b>into</b> a place, it comes in weakly or slowly, either through a partly covered opening, or from a long distance away. (光、聲) 透入","examples":["Light filtered into my kitchen through the soft, green shade of the honey locust tree. 光線透過皂莢樹柔和的綠蔭照進了我的廚房。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When news or information <b>filters</b> through to people, it gradually reaches them. (新聞、資訊等) 逐漸傳開","examples":["It took months before the findings began to filter through to the politicians. 幾個月後調查結果才開始逐漸傳到政治家們那裡。","News of the attack quickly filtered through the college. 襲擊的訊息很快就在這所大學傳開了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>filter</b> is a device through which a substance is passed when it is being filtered. 過濾器","examples":["...a paper coffee filter. …一張咖啡濾紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>filter</b> is a device through which sound or light is passed and which blocks or reduces particular sound or light frequencies. 濾聲器; 濾光器","examples":["You might use a yellow filter to improve the clarity of a hazy horizon. 你可以用一個黃色濾光器來提高模糊的地平線的清晰度。"]}]}]},"flap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"片狀懸垂物；拍打，拍動；（飛機的）襟翼；<非正式>混亂，激動；<美>群眾憤怒，大眾批評"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>激動，緊張；擺動，拍打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a piece of cloth or paper <b>flaps</b> or if you <b>flap</b> it, it moves quickly up and down or from side to side. 使快速擺動; 快速擺動","examples":["Grey sheets flapped on the clothes line. 灰色的床單在晾衣繩上飄動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a bird or insect <b>flaps</b> its wings or if its wings <b>flap</b>, the wings move quickly up and down. 快速振動 (翅膀)","examples":["The bird flapped its wings furiously. 那隻鳥兒使勁地拍打著翅膀。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>flap</b> your arms, you move them quickly up and down as if they were the wings of a bird. (雙臂像小鳥般) 扇動","examples":["...a kid running and flapping her arms. …一個邊跑邊像小鳥一樣上下扇動著雙臂的小女孩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flap</b> of cloth or skin, for example, is a flat piece of it that can move freely up and down or from side to side because it is held or attached by only one edge. (一端固定、可自由掀動的布或皮的) 垂懸平片","examples":["He drew back the tent flap and strode out into the blizzard. 他拉開帳篷的門簾，大步走進了暴風雪中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>flap</b> on the wing of an aircraft is an area along the edge of the wing that can be raised or lowered to control the movement of the aircraft. (飛機的) 副翼","examples":["...the sudden slowing as the flaps were lowered. …副翼降下時的突然減速。"]}]}]},"foe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敵人，對頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>foe</b> is their enemy. 敵人","examples":["But he soon discovers that his old foe may be leading him into a trap. 但他不久發現他的老對頭也許正把他引入圈套。"]}]}]},"fluency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（說話）流利；（做事）流暢，嫻熟"}],"sections":[]},"flourish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繁榮，昌盛；揮動；（植物或動物）長勢好，茁壯成長"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"誇張動作；（講話或文章的）華麗辭藻，修飾；花彩號聲；（手寫花體字的）花飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>flourishes</b>, it is successful, active, or common, and developing quickly and strongly. 繁榮; 興旺","examples":["Business flourished and within six months they were earning 18,000 roubles a day. 生意興隆，6個月中他們每天掙18000盧布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a plant or animal <b>flourishes</b>, it grows well or is healthy because the conditions are right for it. (動植物因環境適宜而) 旺盛","examples":["The plant flourishes particularly well in slightly harsher climes. 這種植物在較為惡劣一點的氣候中長得特別茂盛。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"繁榮的; 興旺的","examples":["Boston quickly became a flourishing port. 波斯頓迅速成為一個繁榮的港口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"繁盛的","examples":["...a flourishing fox population. …不斷繁衍的狐狸群。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flourish</b> an object, you wave it about in a way that makes people notice it. 揮舞","examples":["He flourished the glass to emphasize the point. 他揮舞著杯子來強調這一點。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flourish</b> is also a noun. 揮動","examples":["He took his cap from under his arm with a flourish and pulled it low over his eyes. 他揮手從腋下取出帽子，拉低帽簷蓋住眼睛。"]}]}]},"folklore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"民間傳說，民俗；民俗學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Folklore</b> is the traditional stories, customs, and habits of a particular community or nation. 民間傳說; 民俗","examples":["In Chinese folklore the bat is a symbol of good fortune. 在中國民間傳說中，蝙蝠是好運的象徵。"]}]}]},"flick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指用手指或手快速地）輕擊，輕彈；（使）突然快速移動；用（毛巾、繩等）輕拂，輕快地甩打；向……笑了一下（或瞥了一眼等）；輕按開關（開啟或關上）；快速翻閱，不停地轉換（電影片道）（flick through）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（手指或拇指的）輕彈，彈開（尤指小物體）；輕拂，輕拍；（尤指鞭子的）輕快抽擊；快速瀏覽（a flick through sth.）；電影；電影院（the flicks）；輕打聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>flicks</b> in a particular direction, or if someone <b>flicks</b> it, it moves with a short, sudden movement. 迅速地移動","examples":["His tongue flicked across his lips. 他的舌頭在雙唇間快速移動。","He flicked his cigarette out of the window. 他倏地一下把香菸彈出了窗外。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>flick</b> something away, or off something else, you remove it with a quick movement of your hand or finger. (用手或手指) 彈掉","examples":["Shirley flicked a piece of lint from the sleeve of her black suit. 雪莉輕輕彈掉了黑色套裝袖子上的一塊棉絨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>flick</b> something such as a whip or a towel, or <b>flick</b> something with it, you hold one end of it and move your hand quickly up and then forward, so that the other end moves. 抽打","examples":["She sighed and flicked a dishcloth at the counter. 她嘆了口氣，用一塊洗碗布在櫃檯上抽打了一下。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>flick</b> a switch, or <b>flick</b> an electrical appliance on or off, you press the switch sharply so that it moves into a different position and works the equipment. 啪地開啟或關掉 (開關或電器)","examples":["Sam was flicking a flashlight on and off. 薩姆正啪啪不停地開關著手電筒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flick</b> is also a noun. 快速的移動","examples":["...a flick of a paintbrush. …畫筆的一次快速移動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flick</b> is also a noun. 抽打","examples":["...a flick of the whip. …鞭子的一下輕抽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Flick</b> is also a noun. 快速翻看","examples":["I thought I'd have a quick flick through some recent issues. 我想我要快速瀏覽一下最近的幾期雜誌了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a cinema film 一部影院放映的電影","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flick through</b> a book or magazine, you turn its pages quickly, for example, to get a general idea of its contents or to look for a particular item. If you <b>flick through</b> television channels, you continually change channels very quickly, usually using a remote control. 快速翻看","examples":["She was flicking through some magazines on a table. 她正在快速翻閱桌子上的一些雜誌。"]}]}]},"flip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）快速翻轉，迅速翻動；快速翻閱，瀏覽；<非正式>勃然大怒，心煩意亂；（快速地）調頻道，換臺；輕拋，輕擲；按（開關）；（話題、活動或意見）突然改變，突然轉換；改變，交換（位置）；突然變得熱情，突然極感興趣；為盈利而從速轉賣（股份，財產）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕率的，無禮的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輕拋，輕擲，輕擊；空翻；瀏覽，草草翻閱；<英，非正式>短暫旅行（或遊覽）；蛋奶酒"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<非正式>討厭（表示輕微厭惡）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flip</b> a device on or off, or if you <b>flip</b> a switch, you turn it on or off by pressing the switch quickly. 快速地按動 (裝置或開關)","examples":["He didn't flip on the headlights until he was two blocks away. 直到過了兩個街區後，他才開啟前燈。","Then he walked out, flipping the lights off. 接著他走了出去，隨手把燈關掉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>flips</b> over, or if you <b>flip</b> it over or into a different position, it moves or is moved into a different position. 翻動","examples":["The plane then flipped over and burst into flames. 這時飛機翻了個個兒，接著就燃燒了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>flip</b> something, especially a coin, you use your thumb to make it turn over and over, as it goes through the air. 投擲 (尤指硬幣)","examples":["I pulled a coin from my pocket and flipped it. 我從口袋裡掏出一枚硬幣，把它投擲出去。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>flip</b> through the pages of a book, for example, you quickly turn over the pages in order to find a particular one or to get an idea of the contents. 快速翻閱","examples":["He was flipping through a magazine in the living room. 他在起居室裡快速翻閱一本雜誌。"]}]}]},"foil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"箔；箔紙；陪襯者，陪襯物；花劍；獵物足跡（或嗅跡）；<古>挫折，失敗；水翼"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"挫敗，阻止；（獵物）搞亂，攪亂（嗅跡，足跡）；貼箔於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Foil</b> consists of sheets of metal as thin as paper. It is used to wrap food in. (用於包裹食物的) 箔紙","examples":["Pour cider around the meat and cover with foil. 在肉的四周倒上蘋果酒，然後蓋上箔紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any scent that obscures the trail left by a hunted animal (掩蓋獵物留下痕跡的)氣味","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a light slender flexible sword tipped by a button and usually having a bell-shaped guard 花劍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>foil</b> someone's plan or attempt to do something, for example, to commit a crime, you succeed in stopping them from doing what they want. 挫敗","examples":["A brave police chief foiled an armed robbery by grabbing the raider's shotgun. 一個勇敢的警長奪過歹徒的獵槍，挫敗了一起武裝搶劫。"]}]}]},"fowl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家禽，禽鳥（尤指雞、鴨、鵝、火雞等家養禽類）；禽肉；（文學、聖經或詩歌語體）鳥，飛禽"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"捕野禽，打鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fowl</b> is a bird, especially one that can be eaten as food, such as a duck or a chicken. 家禽","examples":["Carve the fowl into 8 pieces. 將這隻家禽切成8塊。"]}]}]},"format":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"總體安排，計劃，設計；（書或雜誌的）開本，版式；（錄影、鐳射唱片、磁帶等的）格式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……編排格式；格式化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>format</b> of something is the way or order in which it is arranged and presented. 程式","examples":["I had met with him to explain the format of the programme and what we had in mind. 我已經同他見過面，解釋了這個節目的程式和我們的想法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>format</b> of a piece of computer software, a film or a musical recording is the type of equipment on which it is designed to be used or played. For example, possible formats for a film are DVD and video cassette. (計算機軟體、電影、音樂錄製品等的) 格式","examples":["His latest album is available on all formats. 他的最新專輯有各種格式可以買到。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>format</b> a computer disk means to run a program so that the disk can be written on. 將 (電腦磁碟) 格式化","examples":["...a menu that includes the choice to format a disk. …一個包括格式化磁碟選項的選單。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>format</b> a piece of computer text or graphics means to arrange the way in which it appears when it is printed or is displayed on a screen. 設定 (電腦文字或圖形的) 版式","examples":["When text is saved from a Web page, it is often very badly formatted with many short lines. 文字從網頁上另存時版式通常會變亂，出現很多短行。"]}]}]},"fraction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分數，小數；小部分，微量；持不同意見的小集團；分離；（基督教用語）分切聖餐麵包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fraction</b> <b>of</b> something is a tiny amount or proportion of it. 少量","examples":["She hesitated for a fraction of a second before responding. 她猶豫了一下才回應。","Here's how to eat like the stars, at a fraction of the cost. 這就是如何花少量錢卻能像明星一樣吃喝的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fraction</b> is a number that can be expressed as a proportion of two whole numbers. For example, 1/2 and 1/3 are both fractions. 分數","examples":["The students had a grasp of decimals, percentages and fractions. 學生們掌握了小數、百分數和分數。"]}]}]},"freight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貨物；貨運；運費；<美>貨運列車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"運送（貨物）；使充滿，使負擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Freight</b> is the movement of goods by trucks, trains, ships, or aeroplanes. 貨運","examples":["France derives 16% of revenue from air freight. 法國國家稅收的16%來自於航空貨運。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Freight</b> is goods that are transported by trucks, trains, ships, or aeroplanes. 貨物","examples":["...26 tons of freight. …26噸貨物。"]}]}]},"framework":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"(建築物或物體的）構架，結構；參照標準，準則；(社會、法律、政治等）框架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>framework</b> is a particular set of rules, ideas, or beliefs which you use in order to deal with problems or to decide what to do. 體系","examples":["...within the framework of federal regulations. …在聯邦法規的體系內。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>framework</b> is a structure that forms a support or frame for something. 構架","examples":["...wooden shelves on a steel framework. …在鋼架上的木擱板。"]}]}]},"fume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發怒，生氣；冒氣（或煙、汽）；燻（尤指木材）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺鼻（或有害）的氣，煙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fumes</b> are the unpleasant and often unhealthy smoke and gases that are produced by fires or by things such as chemicals, fuel, or cooking. (難聞且常有害的) 煙氣","examples":["...car exhaust fumes. …汽車尾氣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fume</b> over something, you express annoyance and anger about it. 表達氣憤","examples":["\"It's monstrous!\" Jackie fumed. “這太不像話了！”傑基表達了氣憤。"]}]}]},"fury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴怒，狂怒；（暴風雨或洪水的）猛烈，劇烈；激怒者；復仇三女神 （The Furies）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fury</b> is violent or very strong anger. 狂怒","examples":["She screamed, her face distorted with fury and pain. 她尖叫著，她的臉因憤怒和痛苦而扭曲了。"]}]}]},"foul":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難聞的，令人噁心的；(脾氣）暴躁的，（心情）煩躁的；不正當的，不道德的；（語言）下流的，無禮的；犯規的；骯髒的，被汙染的；被阻塞的；（繩子、錨）纏結住的；（天氣）惡劣的；界外的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"犯規；（馬術、划船、賽跑）碰撞，纏結；界外球"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弄髒，汙染；犯規；（棒球中）擊出界外球；（船）碰撞，妨礙（另一艘船的）航行；（繩索、鏈條等）纏結（或堵塞）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"違反規則地，不正當地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>foul</b>, you mean it is dirty and smells or tastes unpleasant. 又髒又臭的; 味道不好的","examples":["...foul polluted water. …汙染了的、又髒又臭的水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Foul</b> language is offensive and contains swear words or rude words. 粗俗的 (語言)","examples":["The teachers had to deal with her foul language, disruptive behaviour, and low academic performance. 老師們不得不應付她粗俗的語言、搗亂的行為和不良的學業成績。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone has a <b>foul</b> temper or is in a <b>foul</b> mood, they become angry or violent very suddenly and easily. 暴躁的","examples":["Collins was in a foul mood even before the interviews began. 柯林斯甚至在面試開始之前就處於暴躁情緒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Foul</b> weather is unpleasant, windy, and stormy. 惡劣的 (天氣)","examples":["No amount of foul weather, whether hail, wind, rain or snow, seems to deter them. 不管天氣有多惡劣，哪怕是冰雹、大風、雨還是雪，似乎都阻止不了他們。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Foul</b> is also an adjective. 犯規的","examples":["...a foul tackle. …一次犯規的阻截。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an animal <b>fouls</b> a place, it drops faeces onto the ground. 在 (某地上) 拉屎","examples":["It is an offence to let your dog foul a footpath. 讓你的狗在人行道上拉屎是一種違法行為。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a game or sport, if a player <b>fouls</b> another player, they touch them or block them in a way which is not allowed according to the rules. 對 (某人) 犯規","examples":["Nowitzki fouled Mitchell early in the third quarter. 在第三節早些時候，諾維斯基就對米切爾犯了規。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>foul</b> is an act in a game or sport that is not allowed according to the rules. (體育比賽中的) 犯規","examples":["Harridge was charged with a flagrant foul and ejected from the game. 哈里基被指惡意犯規並被逐出了比賽。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>run foul of</b> someone or <b>fall foul of</b> them, you do something which gets you into trouble with them. 惹惱","examples":["He had fallen foul of the FBI. 他已惹惱了聯邦調查局。"]}]}]},"frontier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊境，國界；(常sing.) 西部邊疆，邊遠地區；（尤指知識的）前沿，新領域；西部邊疆，邊遠地區"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"邊境的，邊疆的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are talking about the western part of America before the twentieth century, you use <b>frontier</b> to refer to the area beyond the part settled by Europeans. (20世紀前美國) 西部邊疆","examples":["...a far-flung outpost on the frontier. …遠駐西部邊疆的一個哨所。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>frontiers</b> of something, especially knowledge, are the limits to which it extends. (尤指知識的) 前沿","examples":["...pushing back the frontiers of science. …推進科學前沿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>frontier</b> is a border between two countries. 國界","examples":["It wasn't difficult then to cross the frontier. 那時候穿越國界並不難。"]}]}]},"garment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（一件）衣服"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>garment</b> is a piece of clothing; used especially in contexts where you are talking about the manufacture or sale of clothes. 衣服 (尤用於衣服生產和銷售的領域)","examples":["Many of the garments have the customers' name tags sewn into the linings. 這些衣服中很多都把顧客的姓名牌縫進襯裡中。"]}]}]},"gallop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（馬）飛跑，飛奔；騎馬賓士，使（馬）疾馳；飛速移動，極快發展；急急忙忙地說；迅速運輸"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（馬的）飛跑，疾馳；騎馬賓士；極快的速度；<英>訓練馬的跑道，馳馬場"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a horse <b>gallops</b>, it runs very fast so that all four legs are off the ground at the same time. If you <b>gallop</b> a horse, you make it gallop. 使 (馬) 疾馳; (馬) 疾馳","examples":["The horses galloped away. 那些馬疾馳而去。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gallop</b>, you ride a horse that is galloping. 騎馬疾馳","examples":["Major Winston galloped into the distance. 溫斯頓少校騎馬疾馳遠去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a process <b>gallops</b>, it develops very quickly and is often difficult to control. 飛速發展","examples":["China's economy galloped ahead. 中國的經濟飛速向前發展。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gallop</b> is a ride on a horse that is galloping. 騎馬疾馳","examples":["I was forced to attempt a gallop. 我被迫嘗試一次騎馬疾馳。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>at a gallop</b>, you do it very quickly. 快速地","examples":["I read the book at a gallop. 我迅速讀完了那本書。"]}]}]},"gathering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聚集，聚會；蒐集，採集"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"聚集，召集；收集，採集；認為，推斷（gather 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gathering</b> is a group of people meeting together for a particular purpose. 聚會","examples":["...the twenty-second annual gathering of the South Pacific Forum. …第22屆南太平洋論壇年會。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>gathering</b> darkness, the light is gradually decreasing, usually because it is nearly night. 逐漸 (進入黑夜) 的","examples":["The lighthouse beam was quite distinct in the gathering dusk. 燈塔的光柱在漸暗的黃昏中相當清楚。"]}]}]},"fuss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大驚小怪，緊張不安；（為小事）大發牢騷；反對，抗議；繁瑣的手續，麻煩"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"大驚小怪，瞎忙活；過分體貼（fuss over）；使煩惱，煩擾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fuss</b> is anxious or excited behaviour which serves no useful purpose. 無謂的忙乎","examples":["I don't know what all the fuss is about. 我不知道這一切無謂的忙乎是怎麼回事。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fuss</b>, you worry or behave in a nervous, anxious way about unimportant matters or rush around doing unnecessary things. 瞎緊張; 瞎操心; 瞎忙乎","examples":["Carol fussed about getting me a drink. 卡蘿爾忙乎著給我弄杯飲料。","My wife was fussing over the food and clothing we were going to take. 我妻子在為我們要帶的食物和衣服瞎操心。","\"Stop fussing,\" he snapped. “別瞎忙了，”他怒斥道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fuss over</b> someone, you pay them a lot of attention and do things to make them happy or comfortable. 寵愛","examples":["Auntie Hilda and Uncle Jack couldn't fuss over them enough. 希爾達嬸嬸和傑克叔叔再寵愛他們不過了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make a fuss</b> or <b>kick up a fuss</b> about something, you become angry or excited about it and complain. 大發牢騷","examples":["I don't know why everybody makes such a fuss about a few mosquitoes. 我不知道為什麼所有人都為幾隻蚊子發這麼大的牢騷。"]}]}]},"fuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保險絲，熔絲；導火線，引信"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"熔合，結合；<英>（使保險絲熔斷而）停止工作；在（電路或電器）中安裝保險絲；裝引信（或導火索）於（炸彈，炮彈，地雷）；（使）熔化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fuse</b> is a safety device in an electric plug or circuit. It contains a piece of wire which melts when there is a fault so that the flow of electricity stops. 保險絲","examples":["The fuse blew as he pressed the button to start the motor. 保險絲在他按下按鈕發動車子時燒斷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fuse</b> is a device on a bomb or firework which delays the explosion so that people can move a safe distance away. 導火線","examples":["A bomb was deactivated at the last moment, after the fuse had been lit. 一枚炸彈在導火線已被點燃後的最後一刻被解除。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When things <b>fuse</b> or <b>are fused</b>, they join together physically or chemically, usually to become one thing. You can also say that one thing <b>fuses</b> with another. 結合; 融合; 熔合","examples":["The skull bones fuse between the ages of fifteen and twenty-five. 顱骨在15和25歲之間長合。","Manufactured glass is made by fusing various types of sand. 人造玻璃是透過熔合不同種類的沙子製造出來的。"]}]}]},"glacier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰河，冰川"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glacier</b> is an extremely large mass of ice which moves very slowly, often down a mountain valley. 冰川","examples":[]}]}]},"geometry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幾何，幾何學；幾何形狀，幾何構造；幾何體系"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Geometry</b> is the branch of mathematics concerned with the properties and relationships of lines, angles, curves, and shapes. 幾何學","examples":["...the very ordered way in which mathematics and geometry describe nature. …數學和幾何學描述自然的條理性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>geometry</b> of an object is its shape or the relationship of its parts to each other. 幾何圖形; 幾何結構","examples":["...the geometry of the curved roof. …幾何圖形的弧形房頂。"]}]}]},"gay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同性戀的；<舊>豔麗的；<舊>快樂的；<非正式>品質差的，沒有意義的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同性戀者（尤指男性）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gay</b> person is homosexual. 同性戀的","examples":["The quality of life for gay men has improved over the last two decades. 男同性戀者的生活質量過去20年有了改善。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gays</b> are homosexual people, especially homosexual men. (尤指男性) 同性戀者","examples":["More importantly, gays have proved themselves to be style leaders. 更重要的是，同性戀們證實了他們是時尚的引導者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"同性戀","examples":["...Mike's admission of his gayness. …邁克承認自己是同性戀。"]}]}]},"glee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不可數）快樂，歡欣（常含幸災樂禍意味）；（音樂，可數）重唱歌曲，多聲部合唱曲；（Glee）美國音樂喜劇類電視劇《歡樂合唱團》；（Glee）人名，法語譯作“格萊”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glee</b> is a feeling of happiness and excitement, often caused by someone else's misfortune. 高興 (常指幸災樂禍)","examples":["His victory was greeted with glee by his fellow American golfers. 他的勝利也使他的美國高爾夫球伴們為之高興。"]}]}]},"gasp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因驚訝或疼痛）喘氣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喘息，倒抽氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gasp</b> is a short, quick breath of air that you take in through your mouth, especially when you are surprised, shocked, or in pain. (尤指驚訝或疼痛時的) 倒吸氣","examples":["An audible gasp went around the court as the jury announced the verdict. 陪審團宣佈判決的時候，法庭上聽到倒抽了一口氣的聲音。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>gasp</b>, you take a short, quick breath through your mouth, especially when you are surprised, shocked, or in pain. 倒吸氣","examples":["She gasped for air and drew in a lungful of water. 她倒吸氣，吸了一大口水。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe something as <b>the last gasp</b> to emphasize that it is the final part of something or happens at the last possible moment. 最後時刻","examples":["...the last gasp of a dying system of censorship. …行將結束的審查制度的最後時刻。"]}]}]},"gender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"性別；（語法中的）性；（總稱）男性，女性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>gender</b> is the fact that they are male or female. 性別","examples":["Women are sometimes denied opportunities solely because of their gender. 女性有時僅僅因為她們的性別而被剝奪機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to all male people or all female people as a particular <b>gender</b>. 性","examples":["While her observations may be true about some men, they could hardly apply to the entire gender. 她的觀察對某些男人可能是對的，但並不適用於所有男性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In grammar, the <b>gender</b> of a noun, pronoun, or adjective is whether it is masculine, feminine, or neuter. A word's gender can affect its form and behaviour. In English, only personal pronouns such as \"she,\" reflexive pronouns such as \"itself,\" and possessive determiners such as \"his\" have gender. (語法上的) 性","examples":["In both Welsh and Irish the word for \"moon\" is of feminine gender. 在威爾士語和愛爾蘭語中，“月亮”這個單詞都是陰性。"]}]}]},"gloom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憂鬱，絕望；昏暗，幽暗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"外觀昏暗；顯得蕭條（或消沉）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The gloom</b> is a state of near darkness. 昏暗","examples":["...the gloom of a foggy November morning. …一個霧濛濛的11月早晨的昏暗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gloom</b> is a feeling of sadness and lack of hope. 憂鬱","examples":["...the deepening gloom over the economy. …對經濟日漸加深的憂慮。"]}]}]},"gorilla":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大猩猩；（非正式，常含貶義）高大強壯、兇悍的人，常指保鏢或打手，也指粗壯笨拙的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gorilla</b> is a very large ape. It has long arms, black fur, and a black face. 大猩猩","examples":[]}]}]},"gorge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"峽，峽谷；厭惡，氣憤；（獵鷹）鷹的嗉囊，胃；（堵塞狹道，尤指堵塞河道的）冰塊；<舊> 喉嚨"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"貪婪地吃，狼吞虎嚥；盡情享受，沉醉；使擴張"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非常漂亮的，極其吸引人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gorge</b> is a deep, narrow valley with very steep sides, usually where a river passes through mountains or an area of hard rock. 峽谷","examples":["...the deep gorge between these hills. …山間的那個深谷。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gorge on</b> something or <b>gorge</b> <b>yourself on</b> it, you eat lots of it in a very greedy way. 狼吞虎嚥","examples":["I could spend each day gorging on chocolate. 我可以將每一天都花在狂吃巧克力上。"]}]}]},"glitter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃光，閃爍；（某種強烈的感情）閃現，流露"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃耀；（某種感情的）閃現，流露；奢華，華麗；（裝飾用的）閃亮小物件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>glitters</b>, light comes from or is reflected off different parts of it. 閃閃發光","examples":["The bay glittered in the sunshine. 海灣在陽光下閃閃發光。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glitter</b> consists of tiny, shining pieces of metal. It is glued to things for decoration. 發光小飾物","examples":["Cut out a piece of sandpaper and sprinkle it with glitter. 剪下一塊砂紙，再在上面撒些發光小飾物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>glitter</b> to refer to superficial attractiveness or to the excitement connected with something. 表面光輝","examples":["She was blinded by the glitter and the glamour of her own life. 她被自己生活的表面光耀所矇蔽。"]}]}]},"gleam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發微光，閃爍；顯得光潔明亮；（眼睛）表露出，流露出；（因興奮而眼睛）發光，發亮"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"反光，閃光；微光，一絲光線；少量，一線；（情感等的）閃現；（指暫時還不能實現的）想法，願望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object or a surface <b>gleams</b>, it reflects light because it is shiny and clean. 閃光","examples":["His black hair gleamed in the sun. 他的黑頭髮在陽光下閃閃發光。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gleam of</b> something is a faint sign of it. 一絲","examples":["There was a gleam of hope for a peaceful settlement. 和平解決曾有一線希望。"]}]}]},"gospel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"福音書（《聖經》四福音書之一）；福音（耶穌的啟示和教義）；教義，信條；絕對真理（=gospel truth）；福音音樂（=gospel music）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傳播福音的；福音讚美詩的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the New Testament of the Bible, the <b>Gospels</b> are the four books which describe the life and teachings of Jesus Christ. 福音書 (《聖經·新約》中記述耶穌基督生平和教誨的頭四卷)","examples":["...the parable in St. Matthew's Gospel. …《馬太福音》裡的寓言故事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the Christian religion, <b>the gospel</b> refers to the message and teachings of Jesus Christ, as explained in the New Testament. 耶穌的福音和教義","examples":["I didn't shirk my duties. I visited the sick and I preached the gospel. 我沒有逃避責任。我探望了病人並傳佈了耶穌的福音和教義。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Gospel</b> or <b>gospel music</b> is a style of religious music that uses strong rhythms and vocal harmony. It is especially popular among black Christians in the southern United States. (尤指在美國南部黑人基督徒中間流行的) 福音音樂","examples":["I had to go to church, so I grew up singing gospel. 從前我必須上教堂，所以我是唱著福音聖歌長大的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you take something <b>as</b> <b>gospel</b>, or it is <b>the</b> <b>gospel truth</b>, you believe that it is completely true. 絕對真理","examples":["He wouldn't say this if it weren't the gospel truth. 如果這不是絕對真理，他就不會這麼說。"]}]}]},"glare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"怒視，瞪眼；發出刺眼的強光，閃耀"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺眼的強光；怒視；密切關注；<古>耀眼（或炫耀的）外表，俗豔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>glare</b> <b>at</b> someone, you look at them with an angry expression on your face. 怒目而視","examples":["The old woman glared at him. 那個老婦人怒視著他。","Jacob glared and muttered something. 雅各布怒目而視，嘴裡嘟噥著什麼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the sun or a light <b>glares</b>, it shines with a very bright light which is difficult to look at. 發出刺眼的光","examples":["The sunlight glared. 太陽光很刺眼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glare</b> is an angry, hard, and unfriendly look. 怒視","examples":["His glasses magnified his irritable glare. 他的眼鏡使他怒視的目光顯得更兇了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Glare</b> is very bright light that is difficult to look at. 刺眼的光","examples":["...the glare of a car's headlights. …汽車前燈刺眼的強光。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is in <b>the glare of</b> publicity or public attention, they are constantly being watched and talked about by a lot of people. 顯眼; 張揚","examples":["Norma is said to dislike the glare of publicity. 據說諾爾瑪不喜歡張揚。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"smooth and glassy 光滑的","examples":[]}]}]},"greed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貪婪，貪慾；貪食，貪吃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Greed</b> is the desire to have more of something, such as food or money, than is necessary or fair. 貪婪","examples":["...an insatiable greed for personal power. …對個人權力的貪得無厭。"]}]}]},"gravity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重力，地心引力；嚴重性；嚴肅，莊嚴；重（量）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gravity</b> is the force that causes things to drop to the ground. 地球引力; 重力","examples":["Arrows would continue to fly forward forever in a straight line were it not for gravity, which brings them down to earth. 要不是重力使箭掉落地上，它將會一直沿直線往前飛行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>gravity</b> <b>of</b> a situation or event is its extreme importance or seriousness. (事態、事件等的) 重要","examples":["The president said those who grab power through violence deserve punishment which matches the gravity of their crime. 總統說那些透過暴力攫取權力的人應當受到與其罪行嚴重性相一致的懲罰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>gravity</b> of someone's behaviour or speech is the extremely serious way in which they behave or speak. (行為、說話的) 嚴肅","examples":["There was an appealing gravity to everything she said. 她說的一切都帶有一種吸引人的嚴肅與莊重。"]}]}]},"grease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"油脂；潤滑油"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加潤滑油，為……塗（或抹）油"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grease</b> is a thick, oily substance which is put on the moving parts of cars and other machines in order to make them work smoothly. 潤滑油","examples":["...grease-stained hands. …沾滿了油漬的手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Grease</b> is an oily substance that is produced by your skin. (皮膚分泌的) 油脂","examples":["His hair is thick with grease. 他的頭髮油膩膩的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Grease</b> is animal fat that is produced by cooking meat. You can use <b>grease</b> for cooking. 動物油脂","examples":["He could smell the bacon grease. 他聞到了一股燻肉的油脂味兒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grease</b> a part of a car, machine, or device, you put grease on it in order to make it work smoothly. 給…加潤滑油","examples":["I greased front and rear hubs and adjusted the brakes. 我把前後輪軸都加了潤滑油並除錯了剎車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grease</b> a dish, you put a small amount of fat or oil around the inside of it in order to prevent food from sticking to it during cooking. 給…塗上油 (以避免粘鍋)","examples":["Grease two sturdy baking sheets and heat the oven to 400 degrees. 給兩個堅固耐用的烘烤盤塗上油，然後把烤箱加熱到400度。"]}]}]},"growl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（動物）低沉吼叫，咆哮；（人）低聲咆哮著說，惡狠狠地威脅；（事物）發轟隆聲；憤憤不平地抱怨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"怒吼聲，咆哮；（尤指狗發出的）低吠；（機器或引擎發出的）隆隆聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a dog or other animal <b>growls</b>, it makes a low noise in its throat, usually because it is angry. (狗或其它動物因憤怒而) 低沉地吼叫","examples":["The dog was biting, growling, and wagging its tail. 那條狗又咬又叫，搖著尾巴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Growl</b> is also a noun. 咆哮聲","examples":["Their noise modulated to a concerted menacing growl punctuated by sharp yaps. 它們的喧鬧聲逐漸變為整齊劃一的、帶有威脅性的吼叫，還夾雜著刺耳的狂吠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Growl</b> is also a noun. 低吼聲","examples":["...with an angry growl of contempt for her own weakness. …帶著一聲對她自己的懦弱發出的輕蔑的低吼。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>growls</b> something, they say something in a low, rough, and angry voice. 低吼","examples":["His fury was so great he could hardly speak. He growled some unintelligible words at Pete. 他的怒氣大到讓他幾乎說不出話來。他向皮特低吼了一些莫名其妙的話。"]}]}]},"groan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"呻吟，嘆息；咕噥；抱怨，發牢騷；（樹木等）發出嘎吱聲；堆滿（食物）；受……重壓"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"呻吟聲，嘆息聲；抱怨，牢騷；低沉的聲響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>groan</b>, you make a long, low sound because you are in pain, or because you are upset or unhappy about something. 呻吟","examples":["Slowly, he opened his eyes. As he did so, he began to groan with pain. 他慢慢地睜開眼睛，並開始痛苦地呻吟。","They glanced at the man on the floor, who began to groan. 他們掃了一眼地板上那個開始呻吟的男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>groan</b> <b>about</b> something, you complain about it. 抱怨","examples":["His parents were beginning to groan about the price of college tuition. 他的父母開始抱怨大學的學費。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If wood or something made of wood <b>groans</b>, it makes a loud sound when it moves. (木頭移動時) 發吱嘎聲","examples":["The timbers groan and creak and the floorboards shift. 木料吱嘎作響，地板也跟著動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that something such as a table <b>groans</b> <b>under</b> the weight of food, you are emphasizing that there is a lot of food on it. 堆滿","examples":["The bar counter groans under the weight of huge plates of the freshest fish. 酒吧櫃檯上堆滿了大盤大盤最新鮮的魚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>is groaning under</b> the weight of something, you think there is too much of that thing. 受重壓","examples":["Consumers were groaning under the weight of high interest rates. 消費者受著高利率的重壓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Groan</b> is also a noun. 呻吟","examples":["She heard him let out a pitiful, muffled groan. 她聽到他發出一聲可憐、壓抑的呻吟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Groan</b> is also a noun. 抱怨","examples":["Listen sympathetically to your child's moans and groans about what she can't do. 要充滿同情地去傾聽孩子對她不能做的事而發的牢騷和抱怨。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>groan</b> something, you say it in a low, unhappy voice. 呻吟著說","examples":["\"My leg – I think it's broken,\" Eric groaned. “我的腿–我想是斷了，”埃裡克呻吟著說。"]}]}]},"guideline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"指導方針，準則；參考"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an organization issues <b>guidelines</b> <b>on</b> something, it issues official advice about how to do it. 指導方針","examples":["The government should issue clear guidelines on the content of religious education. 政府應該頒佈明確的關於宗教教育內容的指導方針。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>guideline</b> is something that can be used to help you plan your actions or to form an opinion about something. 參考","examples":["A written IQ test is merely a guideline. 書面的智商測試只是個參考。"]}]}]},"grumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抱怨，嘟囔；咕隆，發轟隆聲；（內臟）間歇性地鬧病"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抱怨，牢騷；咕隆聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>grumbles</b>, they complain about something in a bad-tempered way. 抱怨","examples":["They grumble about how hard they have to work. 他們抱怨自己工作得很辛苦。","Taft grumbled that the law so favoured the criminal that trials seemed like a game of chance. 塔夫脫抱怨法律如此有利於罪犯，使得審判看來像是一場運氣的遊戲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Grumble</b> is also a noun. 抱怨","examples":["My only grumble is that there isn't a non-smoking section. 我惟一的抱怨是這兒沒有無煙區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Grumble</b> is also a noun. 隆隆響聲","examples":["One could often hear, far to the east, the grumble of guns. 人們經常可以聽到在遠遠的東邊有隆隆的槍炮聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>grumbles</b>, it makes a low continuous sound. 隆隆作響","examples":["It was quiet now, the thunder had grumbled away to the west. 現在安靜了，雷聲已經隆隆作響地傳到西邊了。"]}]}]},"grant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"授予，給予；承認"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"補助金，撥款；（政府給予的）土地；<正式>給予，授予；合法轉讓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grant</b> is an amount of money that a government or other institution gives to an individual or to an organization for a particular purpose such as education or home improvements. 補助金","examples":["They'd got a special grant to encourage research. 他們已得到了一筆用來支援研究的特別補助金。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>grants</b> you something, or if something <b>is granted</b> <b>to</b> you, you are allowed to have it. 准予","examples":["France has agreed to grant him political asylum. 法國已經同意給予他政治庇護。","Single parents tend to grant more independence to their children than other parents do. 單親父母往往比其他父母給予孩子們更多的自主性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grant</b> <b>that</b> something is true, you accept that it is true, even though your opinion about it does not change. 承認","examples":["The magistrates granted that the charity was justified in bringing the action. 這些地方法官承認該慈善機構提起訴訟是有正當理由的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>takes</b> you <b>for granted</b>, you are complaining that they benefit from your help, efforts, or presence without showing that they are grateful. 對某人無感激之心","examples":["What right has the family to take me for granted, Martin? 這一家子有什麼資格認為我所做的一切都是應該的，馬丁？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> something <b>for granted</b>, you believe that it is true or accept it as normal without thinking about it. 視某事為理所當然","examples":["I was amazed that virtually all the things I took for granted up north just didn't happen in Savannah. 令我感到驚訝的是，我在北方視為理所當然的一切事物，在南美大草原上幾乎都沒有發生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>take it for granted</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you believe that it is true or you accept it as normal without thinking about it. 理所當然地認為","examples":["He seemed to take it for granted that he should speak as a representative. 他似乎理所當然地認為他應當作為代表發言。"]}]}]},"gulp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"狼吞虎嚥，匆匆吞下；大口呼吸；（因害怕或驚訝而）倒吸氣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"大口吞食，大口啜飲；一大口（飲入物）；一大口（吸入的空氣）；吞嚥，吸入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>gulp</b> something, you eat or drink it very quickly by swallowing large quantities of it at once. 大口吞下","examples":["She quickly gulped her soda. 她很快地把汽水一飲而盡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>gulp</b>, you swallow air, often making a noise in your throat as you do so, because you are nervous or excited. (因擔憂或興奮) 倒吸氣","examples":["I gulped, and then proceeded to tell her the whole story. 我倒吸了口氣，接著把事情的原委都告訴了她。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>gulp</b> air, you breathe in a large amount of air quickly through your mouth. 大口地吸","examples":["She gulped air into her lungs. 她大口地把空氣吸入肺部。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gulp down</b> means the same as . 大口吞下 (同 )(gulp)","examples":["Paige gulped down more coffee and a chocolate bar from the machine. 佩奇大口飲下更多的咖啡，又一口吞下一個取自這臺機器的糖塊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gulp</b> <b>of</b> air, food, or drink, is a large amount of it that you swallow at once. 一大口","examples":["I took in a large gulp of air. 我吸了一大口氣。"]}]}]},"hairdo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式> 髮型，髮式（尤指女子頭髮經修剪、梳理後的樣式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hairdo</b> is the style in which your hair has been cut and arranged. 髮型","examples":[]}]}]},"gross":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總的，毛的；嚴重的，極端的；粗魯的；肥胖難看的，臃腫的；大範圍的，粗略的；（高爾夫球的得分）實際所得的；明顯的；讓人噁心的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"總共，全部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"總共賺得"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一羅（144個）；毛收入，總收入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>gross</b> to describe something unacceptable or unpleasant to a very great amount, degree, or intensity. 嚴重的","examples":["The company was guilty of gross negligence. 該公司犯了重大的失職罪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone's speech or behaviour is <b>gross</b>, you think it is very coarse, vulgar, or unacceptable. 粗俗的","examples":["He abused the Admiral in the grossest terms. 他用最粗俗的字眼辱罵那位海軍上將。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>gross</b>, you think it is very unpleasant. 不雅的","examples":["They had a commercial on the other night for Drug Free America that was so gross I thought Dad was going to faint. 前天晚上他們為“無毒美國”播出的一則廣告如此令人噁心，我想爸爸都快暈過去了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>gross</b>, you mean that they are extremely fat and unattractive. 肥胖臃腫的","examples":["I only resist things like chocolate if I feel really gross. 只有當我感到自己胖得很難看時，我才會拒吃巧克力這類東西。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Gross</b> means the total amount of something, especially money, before any has been taken away. (尤指錢) 總的; 毛的","examples":["...a fixed rate account guaranteeing 10.4% gross interest or 7.8% net until October. …一個能保證到10月份為止獲得10.4%毛利或7.8%淨利的固定利率賬戶。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Gross</b> means the total amount of something, after all the relevant amounts have been added together. 總共的","examples":["Gross sales reached nearly $2 million a year. 全年總銷售額達到近二百萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴重地","examples":["Funding of education had been grossly inadequate for years. 多年來教育資金嚴重不足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Gross</b> is also an adverb. 總地","examples":["Interest is paid gross, rather than having tax deducted. 利息按總額來付，沒有扣除稅收。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or a business <b>grosses</b> a particular amount of money, they earn that amount of money before tax has been taken away. 稅前收入賺得","examples":["The company grossed $16.8 million last year. 該公司去年稅前收入為1680萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"num.","pos_name":"數詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gross</b> is a group of 144 things. 一羅 (合144個)","examples":["In all honesty he could not have justified ordering more than twelve gross of the disks. 說實話他本來就不能為定購這些超過十二羅的光碟提供正當理由."]}]}]},"hairstyle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"髮型，髮式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>hairstyle</b> is the style in which your hair has been cut or arranged. 髮型","examples":["I think her new short hairstyle looks simply great. 我覺得她新剪的短髮看上去簡直棒極了。"]}]}]},"gypsy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"吉卜賽人，吉普賽人（即羅姆人；該詞常被認為有冒犯性；較中性說法為 Romani、Roma）；吉卜賽語，羅姆語（羅馬尼語）；像吉卜賽人一樣四處漂泊的人，流浪者；（歌舞劇中的）歌舞隊員；另見 gypsy moth（舞毒蛾）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（可能具冒犯性）吉卜賽人的，羅姆人的；像吉卜賽人的，流浪的，四處漂泊的；無照的，非正規的（如 gypsy cab）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"流浪，過漂泊生活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gypsy</b> is a member of a race of people who travel from place to place, usually in caravans, rather than living in one place. Some people find this word offensive. 吉卜賽人","examples":["I'm proud of being brought up by gypsies. 我為自己是吉卜賽人撫養長大的而感到自豪。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Gypsy</b> is also an adjective. 吉卜賽人的","examples":["...the largest gypsy community of any country. …所有國家中最大的吉卜賽人社群。"]}]}]},"gust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一陣強風，一陣狂風；（雨、聲音、感情等的）一陣突發，爆發"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"一陣陣地勁吹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gust</b> is a short, strong, sudden rush of wind. 一陣強風","examples":["A gust of wind drove down the valley. 一陣狂風掠過山谷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you feel a <b>gust of</b> emotion, you feel the emotion suddenly and intensely. (感情的) 迸發","examples":["...a small gust of pleasure. …一絲愉悅的迸發。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the wind <b>gusts</b>, it blows with short, strong, sudden rushes. 勁吹","examples":["The wind gusted again. 風又猛刮起來。"]}]}]},"handicraft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手工藝；手工藝品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Handicrafts</b> are activities such as embroidery and pottery which involve making things with your hands in a skilful way. 手工藝","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Handicrafts</b> are the objects that are produced by people doing handicrafts. 手工藝品","examples":["She sells handicrafts to the tourists. 她向遊客們出售手工藝品。"]}]}]},"handicap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（生理或智力上的）殘障，殘疾；障礙，不利因素；讓步賽；讓杆數"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"妨礙，使不利；<美>預測（可能的獲勝者）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handicap</b> is a physical or mental disability. 殘疾","examples":["He lost his leg when he was ten, but learned to overcome his handicap. 他10歲時失去了一條腿，但學會了戰勝自己的殘疾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>handicap</b> is an event or situation that places you at a disadvantage and makes it harder for you to do something. 不利條件","examples":["Being a foreigner was not a handicap. 作一名外國人並不是一個不利條件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In golf, a <b>handicap</b> is an advantage given to someone who is not a good player, in order to make the players more equal. As you improve, your handicap gets lower. 差點 (高爾夫運動中給弱者增加的杆數)","examples":["I see your handicap is down from 16 to 12. 我注意到你的差點從16降到了12。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In horse racing, a <b>handicap</b> is a race in which some competitors are given a disadvantage of extra weight in an attempt to give everyone an equal chance of winning. (賽馬中的) 讓步賽","examples":["...the Melbourne Cup, a two-mile handicap. …墨爾本杯，一場兩英里的讓步賽。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event or a situation <b>handicaps</b> someone or something, it places them at a disadvantage. 將...置於不利地位","examples":["Greater levels of stress may seriously handicap some students. 更高程度的壓力可能會將一些學生置於不利地位。"]}]}]},"gut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腸，腸道；內臟；<非正式>勇氣，魄力；（尤指大的）胃，肚子；直覺，本能；核心，實質；腸線；<非正式>（機器或裝置的）內部零件；狹道，狹海峽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"取出……的內臟（以便烹飪）；毀壞（建築物）的內部"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感情的，本能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's or animal's <b>guts</b> are all the organs inside them. 內臟","examples":["By the time they finish, the crewmen are standing ankle-deep in fish guts. 到他們結束時，船員們正站在齊腳踝深的魚內臟堆裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The gut</b> is the tube inside the body of a person or animal through which food passes while it is being digested. 腸","examples":["Toxins can leak from the gut into the bloodstream. 毒素能夠從腸道滲透到血液裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Guts</b> is the will and courage to do something that is difficult or unpleasant, or which might have unpleasant results. 膽量","examples":["The new governor has the guts to push through unpopular tax increases. 新任州長有膽量強制透過不得人心的增稅方案透過。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to someone's stomach as their <b>gut</b>, especially when it is very large and sticks out. 肚腩","examples":["His gut sagged out over his belt. 他的肚腩垂在腰帶上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Gut</b> is string made from part of the stomach of an animal. Traditionally, it is used to make the strings of sports rackets or musical instruments such as violins. (用於制網球拍、琴絃等的) 腸線","examples":["Gerald's violin strings are made of gut rather than steel. 傑拉爾德的小提琴絃是用腸線而不是鋼絲製成的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>guts</b> a dead animal or fish, they prepare it for cooking by removing all the organs from inside it. 取出…的內臟","examples":["It is not always necessary to gut the fish prior to freezing. 在冷凍魚之前沒有必要總是取出其內臟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>gut</b> a building means to destroy the inside of it so that only its outside walls remain. 損毀 (建築物) 的內部","examples":["Over the weekend, a firebomb gutted a building where 60 people lived. 週末，一顆燃燒彈焚燬了一座住著60人的建築內部。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gut</b> feeling is based on instinct or emotion rather than reason. 直覺的","examples":["Let's have your gut reaction to the facts as we know them. 請告訴我們你對這些我們瞭解的事實的直覺反應。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hate</b> someone's <b>guts</b>, you dislike them very much. 對某人恨之入骨","examples":["We hate each other's guts. 我們對彼此恨之入骨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>are working</b> your <b>guts out</b>, you are emphasizing that you are working as hard as you can. 拼命工作","examples":["Most have worked their guts out and made sacrifices. 大多數人都拼命工作並做出了犧牲。"]}]}]},"grip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"緊握；掌握，控制；理解；不打滑，走得穩；手柄；緊握（或抓牢）的方式；（拍攝電影時）攝影機和照明裝置管理人員；<英>髮夾；旅行袋"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"握緊，夾住；（尤指透過摩擦力）牢牢地附著，緊貼；使感興趣，吸引住（某人）的注意；對……產生強有力的影響"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grip</b> something, you take hold of it with your hand and continue to hold it firmly. 緊握","examples":["She gripped the rope. 她緊緊抓住繩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>grips</b> you, it affects you very strongly. 強烈地影響","examples":["The entire community has been gripped by fear. 整個社群已被恐懼籠罩著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>are gripped</b> <b>by</b> something such as a story or a series of events, your attention is concentrated on it and held by it. 吸引","examples":["The nation is gripped by the dramatic story. 整個國家都被這個戲劇性的故事所吸引。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grip</b> is a firm, strong hold on something. 緊握","examples":["His strong hand eased the bag from her grip. 他強有力的手使她把緊握的包鬆開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>grip</b> <b>on</b> something is the power and control they have over it. 掌控","examples":["The president maintains an iron grip on his country. 總統保持著對國家的鐵腕統治。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If things such as shoes or car tyres have <b>grip</b>, they do not slip. 抓力","examples":["...a new way of reinforcing rubber which gives car tyres a better grip. …一種增強橡膠使汽車輪胎抓力加強的新方法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a part by which an object is grasped; handle 抓住 (Also called handgrip)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"吸引人的","examples":["The film turned out to be a gripping thriller. 這部電影原來是一部扣人心絃的驚險片。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>come to grips with</b> a problem, you consider it seriously, and start taking action to deal with it. 認真著手處理","examples":["The administration's first task is to come to grips with the economy. 該政府首要的任務是認真著手處理經濟問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get a grip</b> on yourself, you make an effort to control or improve your behaviour or work. 控制 ; 完善","examples":["Part of me was very frightened and I consciously had to get a grip on myself. 我其實非常害怕，但又不得不有意識地控制住自己。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person, group, or place is <b>in the grip of</b> something, they are being severely affected by it. 在某事的強烈影響下","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>lose</b> your <b>grip</b>, you become less efficient and less confident, and less able to deal with things. 失去掌控","examples":["He wondered if perhaps he was getting old and losing his grip. 他懷疑自己或許在變老，對事情感到力不從心。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone has a <b>grip on reality</b>, you mean they recognize the true situation and do not have mistaken ideas about it. 面對現實","examples":["Shakur loses his fragile grip on reality and starts blasting away at friends and foes alike. 沙庫爾喪失了對現實脆弱的控制力，無論對朋友還是敵人都開始猛烈抨擊起來。"]}]}]},"harness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"控制並利用；（把動物）拴在一起（或拴到某物上）；給（馬）套上挽具；連線，串聯"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（馬的）挽具，馬具；繫帶，吊帶；日常工作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>harness</b> something such as an emotion or natural source of energy, you bring it under your control and use it. 利用","examples":["Turkey plans to harness the waters of the Tigris and Euphrates rivers for big hydro-electric power projects. 土耳其計劃利用底格里斯河與幼發拉底河的水來建造大型水力發電工程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a horse or other animal <b>is harnessed</b>, a harness is put on it, especially so that it can pull a carriage, cart, or plough. 給…套上挽具","examples":["On Sunday the horses were harnessed to a heavy wagon for a day-long ride over the border. 星期天這些馬被套在一輛沉重的貨車上，踏上長達一天的旅程越過邊境。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>harness</b> is a set of straps which fit under a person's arms and fasten around their body in order to keep a piece of equipment in place or to prevent the person moving from a place. 揹帶; 安全帶","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>harness</b> is a set of leather straps and metal links fastened around a horse's head or body so that the horse can have a carriage, cart, or plough fastened to it. 馬具; 挽具","examples":[]}]}]},"haunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鬼魂）出沒；縈繞在……心頭；（長期）困擾；常去（某地）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"常去的地方；棲息地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something unpleasant <b>haunts</b> you, you keep thinking or worrying about it over a long period of time. (令人不愉快的事) 縈繞在心頭","examples":["He would always be haunted by that scene in Well Park. 他將不斷回想起威爾公園的那一幕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>haunts</b> a person or organization regularly causes them problems over a long period of time. 長期不斷地糾纏","examples":["The stigma of being a bankrupt is likely to haunt him for the rest of his life. 作為一名破產者的恥辱很可能在他的餘生不斷來糾纏他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A ghost or spirit that <b>haunts</b> a place or a person regularly appears in the place, or is seen by the person and frightens them. (鬼魂等) 常出沒於","examples":["His ghost is said to haunt some of the rooms, banging a toy drum. 據說他的鬼魂常在其中一些屋子裡出現，還敲打著一個玩具鼓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A place that is the <b>haunt</b> of a particular person is one which they often visit because they enjoy going there. 常去之處","examples":["The islands are a favourite summer haunt for yachtsmen. 這片島嶼是遊艇駕駛者夏天最愛去的一個地方。"]}]}]},"heed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>注意，留心"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>注意，留心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>heed</b> someone's advice or warning, you pay attention to it and do what they suggest. 注意; 聽從","examples":["But few at the conference in London last week heeded his warning. 但幾乎沒有人在上週倫敦會議上注意他的警告。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take heed of</b> what someone says or if you <b>pay heed to</b> them, you pay attention to them and consider carefully what they say. 注意","examples":["But what if the government takes no heed? 但要是政府不理會該怎麼辦呢？"]}]}]},"heir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼承人，子嗣；接班人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"繼承"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>heir</b> is someone who has the right to inherit a person's money, property, or title when that person dies. 繼承人","examples":["...the heir to the throne. …王位繼承人。"]}]}]},"hedge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹籬；防範措施，防備手段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拐彎抹角，避免正面回答；用樹籬圍住；包圍，限制；採取保值措施以規避風險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hedge</b> is a row of bushes or small trees, usually along the edge of a lawn, garden, field, or road. 樹籬","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is a <b>hedge against</b> something unpleasant will protect you from its effects. 防備手段","examples":["Gold is traditionally a hedge against inflation. 黃金傳統上是一種防範通貨膨脹的手段。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hedge</b> <b>against</b> something unpleasant or unwanted that might affect you, especially losing money, you do something which will protect you from it. 防備 (尤指金錢損失)","examples":["You can hedge against illness with insurance. 你可以買保險以備治療患病之需。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hedge</b> your <b>bets</b>, you reduce the risk of losing a lot by supporting more than one person or thing in a situation where they are opposed to each other. 幾面下注","examples":["The company tried to hedge its bets by diversifying into other fields. 該公司試圖透過兼營其他領域幾面下注。"]}]}]},"herald":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預示……的來臨；宣佈，宣傳；熱烈歡迎；公開稱讚"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"預兆；使者，先驅；棘翅夜蛾；<古> 掌禮官，（負責比武大會的）紋章官；（英國）宗譜紋章院或蘇格蘭紋章院官員（位低於紋章官助理）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>heralds</b> a future event or situation is a sign that it is going to happen or appear. 預示…的來臨","examples":["...the sultry evening that heralded the end of the baking hot summer. …預示著炙熱的夏天即將結束的那個悶熱的夜晚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an important event or action <b>is heralded</b> <b>by</b> people, announcements are made about it so that it is publicly known and expected. 預告; 宣傳","examples":["Janet Jackson's new album has been heralded by a massive media campaign. 珍妮特·傑克遜的新唱片已在媒體上進行了大規模的宣傳。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is a <b>herald</b> <b>of</b> a future event or situation is a sign that it is going to happen or appear. 預兆","examples":["I welcome the report as a herald of more freedom. 我歡迎這份報告，認為它預示著更多的自由。"]}]}]},"hermit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指因宗教原因隱居的）隱士，隱居者；蜂鳥（尤指隱蜂鳥，多用於鳥名複合詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hermit</b> is a person who lives alone, away from people and society. 隱士","examples":["I've spent the past ten years living like a hermit. 我過去10年裡過著隱士般的生活。"]}]}]},"haul":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用力）拖，拉；強迫（某人）去某處；費力前進，艱難地走；<非正式>迫使（某人）出庭受審；（用運載工具）運送，運輸；<英>（費力地）升級；（尤指帆船）突然改變航道"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拖，拉；大批贓物，大量非法物品；賽季（或賽事）得分總數；旅行的距離；一網的捕魚量；託運的距離"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>haul</b> something which is heavy or difficult to move, you move it using a lot of effort. (用力地) 拉","examples":["A crane had to be used to haul the car out of the stream. 不得不用了一臺起重機把轎車從河裡拉出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is hauled</b> <b>before</b> a court or someone in authority, they are made to appear before them because they are accused of having done something wrong. 傳訊","examples":["He was hauled before the managing director and fired. 他被總裁叫去問話並被解僱了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Haul up</b> means the same as . 傳訊","examples":["He was hauled up before the board of trustees. 他被帶到了託管委員會面前問話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>haul</b> is a quantity of things that are stolen, or a quantity of stolen or illegal goods found by police or customs. 一次偷得之量; (警察或海關) 一次查獲之量","examples":["The size of the drug haul shows that the international trade in heroin is still flourishing. 這次的毒品繳獲量說明國際性海洛因交易依然猖獗。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a task or a journey is a <b>long haul</b>, you mean that it takes a long time and a lot of effort. 費時費力的工作","examples":["Revitalizing the Romanian economy will be a long haul. 復興羅馬尼亞經濟將是一項長期艱鉅的工作。"]}]}]},"herb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥草，香草；草本植物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>herb</b> is a plant whose leaves are used in cooking to add flavour to food, or as a medicine. (調味或藥用的) 香草","examples":["...beautiful, fragrant herbs such as basil and coriander. …羅勒和芫荽等美麗芬芳的香草。"]}]}]},"heterosexual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"異性的（異性間的）；異性戀的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"異性戀者，異性戀的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>heterosexual</b> relationship is a sexual relationship between a man and a woman. 異性間的","examples":["An increasing number of people are becoming infected with HIV through heterosexual sex. 越來越多的人正透過異性間的性行為感染上艾滋病病毒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>heterosexual</b> is sexually attracted to people of the opposite sex. 異性戀的","examples":["It doesn't matter whether people are heterosexual or homosexual. 一個人是異性戀還是同性戀無關緊要。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heterosexual</b> is also a noun. 異性戀者","examples":["In Denmark the age of consent is fifteen for both heterosexuals and homosexuals. 在丹麥異性戀者和同性戀者的合法性交年齡都是15歲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"異性戀","examples":["...a challenge to the assumption that heterosexuality was \"normal.\" …對異性戀“是正常的”說法的挑戰。"]}]}]},"hi-fi":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高保真度音響裝置；高保真（指失真很小、接近原聲的聲音重放）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高保真的，高保真度的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hi-fi</b> is a set of equipment on which you play CDs and tapes, and which produces stereo sound of very good quality. 高保真度音響裝置","examples":[]}]}]},"hockey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>曲棍球；<美>冰球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hockey</b> is an outdoor game played between two teams of 11 players who use long curved sticks to hit a small ball and try to score goals. 曲棍球","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hockey</b> is a game played on ice between two teams of 11 players who use long curved sticks to hit a small rubber disc, called a puck, and try to score goals. 冰球","examples":["...a new hockey arena. …一個新的冰球場。"]}]}]},"hijack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搶劫，劫持；強行控制，操縱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"劫持事件（或行為）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>hijacks</b> a plane or other vehicle, they illegally take control of it by force while it is travelling from one place to another. 劫持","examples":["Two men tried to hijack a plane on a flight from Riga to Murmansk. 兩名男子試圖劫持一架從里加飛往摩爾曼斯克的飛機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has hijacked</b> something, you disapprove of the way in which they have taken control of it when they had no right to do so. 強行控制","examples":["A peaceful demonstration had been hijacked by anarchists intent on causing trouble. 一場和平示威已被一心想製造事端的無政府主義分子強行控制了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hijack</b> is also a noun. 劫持","examples":["Every minute during the hijack seemed like a week. 劫持過程中，每一分鐘都像一個星期似的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"劫持","examples":["Car hijackings are running at a rate of nearly 50 a day. 平均每天發生50起劫車事件。"]}]}]},"honk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雁叫聲（或類似聲音）；汽車喇叭聲，鳴笛聲；（Honk）洪（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發雁鳴（或發出類似雁叫的聲音）；按汽車喇叭，鳴喇叭；<非正式>嘔吐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>honk</b> the horn of a vehicle or if the horn <b>honks</b>, you make the horn produce a short loud sound. 鳴 (車輛喇叭); (車輛喇叭) 鳴響","examples":["Drivers honked their horns in solidarity with the peace marchers. 司機們鳴笛，表示對和平示威者的堅決支援。","Horns honk. An angry motorist shouts. 喇叭鳴響。一位憤怒的司機大聲叫喊著。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Honk</b> is also a noun. 鳴笛; 鳴響","examples":["She pulled to the right with a honk. 她按了聲喇叭，把車開到了右邊。"]}]}]},"heroic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"英雄的，英勇的；矢志不渝的，艱苦卓絕的；巨大的；男主角的；（雕像）大於真人（或實物）但不及其兩倍大的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇敢果斷的行為；譁眾取寵的愚蠢行為；英雄詩體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or their actions as <b>heroic</b>, you admire them because they show extreme bravery. 英勇的","examples":["His heroic deeds were celebrated in every corner of India. 他的英勇事蹟在印度的每個角落被傳頌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an action or event as <b>heroic</b>, you admire it because it involves great effort or determination to succeed. 艱苦卓絕的","examples":["The company has made heroic efforts at cost reduction. 該公司在降低成本方面進行了艱苦卓絕的努力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Heroic</b> means being or relating to the hero or heroine of a story. 主人公的","examples":["...the book's central, heroic figure. …書中的中心主角人物。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"英勇地","examples":["He had acted heroically during the liner's evacuation. 他在疏散客輪乘客的過程中表現得很英勇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"艱苦卓絕地","examples":["Single parents cope heroically in doing the job of two people. 單身父母做著兩個人的工作，非常艱苦也非常有毅力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heroics</b> are actions involving bravery, courage, or determination. 英雄壯舉","examples":["...the man whose aerial heroics helped save the helicopter pilot. …那個以空中的英雄壯舉拯救直升機飛行員的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's actions or plans as <b>heroics</b>, you think that they are foolish or dangerous because they are too difficult or brave for the situation in which they occur. 逞能行為","examples":["He said his advice was: \"No heroics, stay within the law.\" 他說他的意見是：“不要有逞能行為，要依法辦事。”"]}]}]},"hiss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"發出噓聲；發噓聲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"噓聲；嘶嘶聲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Hiss）人名；（英、德）希斯；（法）伊斯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>hiss</b> means to make a sound like a long \"s.\" 發嘶嘶聲","examples":["The tyres of Lenny's bike hissed over the wet pavement as he slowed down. 蘭尼減速時，他腳踏車的兩個輪胎在潮溼的路面上發出嘶嘶聲。","My cat hissed when I stepped on its tail. 我踩在了貓的尾巴上，於是它嘶嘶地叫了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>hiss</b> <b>at</b> someone such as a performer or a person making a speech, they express their disapproval or dislike of that person by making long loud \"s\" sounds. 發噓聲; 喝倒彩","examples":["One had to listen hard to catch the words of the president's speech as the delegates booed and hissed. 由於代表們發噓聲、喝倒彩，得費勁兒地聽才能聽清總統的演講。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hiss</b> is also a noun. 嘶嘶聲","examples":["...the hiss of water running into the burned pan. …水流進燒紅的煎鍋時的嘶嘶聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嘶嘶聲","examples":["...a silence broken only by a steady hissing from above my head. …僅僅被我頭頂上傳來的持續的嘶嘶聲所打破的一片寂靜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Hiss</b> is also a noun. 噓聲","examples":["She was greeted with boos and hisses. 迎接她的是一片噓聲和反對聲。"]}]}]},"homosexual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同性戀者（通常指男性）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同性戀的，同性性慾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>homosexual</b> relationship is a sexual relationship between people of the same sex. 同性戀的","examples":["...partners in a homosexual relationship. …同性戀戀人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>homosexual</b> is sexually attracted to people of the same sex. 同性戀性向的","examples":["...a fraud trial involving two homosexual lawyers. …一起涉及兩名同性戀律師的欺詐案的審判。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Homosexual</b> is also a noun. 同性戀","examples":["The judge said that discrimination against homosexuals is deplorable. 法官說歧視同性戀的行為應該受到譴責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"同性戀","examples":["...a place where gays could openly discuss homosexuality. …一個同性戀者可以公開討論同性戀問題的場所。"]}]}]},"hoof":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（馬等動物的）蹄；人的腳"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"步行；猛踢（球）；跳舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>hooves</b> of an animal such as a horse are the hard lower parts of its feet. (馬等動物的) 蹄","examples":["The horses' hooves often could not get a proper grip. 這些馬的蹄子經常踩不穩。"]}]}]},"hood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（衣服上的）兜帽，風帽；頭巾，面罩；（裝置或機器的）防護罩，罩；汽車發動機罩；（爐灶上方的）排風罩，抽油煙罩；（汽車、嬰兒車等）可摺疊車篷；<美，非正式>惡棍，暴徒；<美，非正式>社群，街區；羽冠，垂兜，頸部皮褶；（野芝麻等植物的）盔狀花冠；學位連領帽（表示學位種類）；（獵鷹）（鷹的）皮頭罩"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加罩於，覆蓋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hood</b> is a part of a coat which you can pull up to cover your head. It is in the shape of a triangular bag attached to the neck of the coat at the back. (連在外套上的) 風帽","examples":["She threw back the hood of her cloak. 她把披風上的風帽向後甩去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>hood</b> of a car is the metal cover over the engine at the front. (汽車的) 引擎罩","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"hoodlum的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cover or provide with or as if with a hood 覆蓋","examples":[]}]}]},"hostage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hostage</b> is someone who has been captured by a person or organization and who may be killed or injured if people do not do what that person or organization demands. 人質","examples":["It is hopeful that two hostages will be freed in the next few days. 兩名人質有望在幾天後獲釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say you are <b>hostage to</b> something, you mean that your freedom to take action is restricted by things that you cannot control. 受到…的限制","examples":["Wine growers say they've been held hostage to the interests of cereal farmers. 葡萄酒製造商們說他們已被穀物種植者的利益所左右。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is taken hostage</b> or <b>is held hostage</b>, they are captured and kept as a hostage. 將某人扣作人質","examples":["He was taken hostage while on his first foreign assignment as a television journalist. 他第一次作為電視記者出國採訪時就被扣作人質。"]}]}]},"horizontal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"水平的；（公司）同一層次的；統一的，一致的；地平線的，在地平線上的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水平位置；水平線，水平面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>horizontal</b> is flat and level with the ground, rather than at an angle to it. 水平的; 橫的","examples":["The board consists of vertical and horizontal lines. 牌子是由縱向和橫向的線條構成的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Horizontal</b> is also a noun. 水平線; 水平面","examples":["Do not raise your left arm above the horizontal. 不要把你的左臂舉過水平位置。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"水平地","examples":["The wind was cold and drove the snow at him almost horizontally. 風很冷，裹著雪幾乎是橫著向他撲來。"]}]}]},"hymn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"讚美詩，聖歌，歡樂的歌（歌頌上帝、聖徒或國家的歌曲，尤指基督教禮拜中所唱）；頌歌，讚歌（新聞或文學；常作 hymn to something，指讚揚或頌揚某人或某事物的歌曲、詩歌、文章等）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"唱讚美歌，用讚美詩讚美或頌揚（某人或某事物）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"唱讚美詩，唱讚歌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hymn</b> is a religious song that Christians sing in church. (基督教的) 讚美詩","examples":["I like singing hymns. 我喜歡唱聖歌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a film, book, or speech as a <b>hymn to</b> something, you mean that it praises or celebrates that thing. 頌歌","examples":["...a hymn to freedom and rebellion. …自由與反叛的頌歌。"]}]}]},"hound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獵犬；<非正式>卑鄙的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"糾纏，煩擾；（用獵犬）追獵，追逐；激勵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hound</b> is a type of dog that is often used for hunting or racing. 獵犬; 賽犬","examples":["Rainey's chief interest in life is hunting with hounds. 雷尼一生中的主要嗜好是帶著獵犬去打獵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(<b>in combination</b>) 結合詞","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"either of a pair of horizontal bars that reinforce the running gear of a horse-drawn vehicle 馬車兩邊的固定橫杆","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>hounds</b> you, they constantly disturb or speak to you in an annoying or upsetting way. (不斷地) 煩擾","examples":["Newcomers are constantly hounding them for advice. 新來的人老是纏著他們問這問那的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is hounded</b> <b>out of</b> a job or place, they are forced to leave it, often because other people are constantly criticizing them. 迫使 (某人) 離開","examples":["There is a general view around that he has been hounded out of office by the press. 人們普遍認為是媒體迫使他離職的。"]}]}]},"hurl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛扔，猛摔；大聲說出（辱罵或斥責等）；嘔吐"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>乘車，搭便車；猛投，投擲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hurl</b> something, you throw it violently and with a lot of force. 用力擲","examples":["Groups of angry youths hurled stones at police. 一群群憤怒的年輕人朝著警察猛擲石塊。","Simon caught the grenade and hurled it back. 西蒙接住手榴彈，把它擲了回去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hurl</b> abuse or insults <b>at</b> someone, you shout insults at them aggressively. 大聲叫罵","examples":["How would you handle being locked in the back of a cab while the driver hurled abuse at you? 如果你被鎖在計程車後座又遭司機謾罵，你會怎麼辦？"]}]}]},"hover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懸停；徘徊，守候；處於不穩定狀態；上下波動，左右搖擺；伏窩孵化"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"翱翔，徘徊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>hover</b> means to stay in the same position in the air without moving forward or backward. Many birds and insects can hover by moving their wings very quickly. (鳥、昆蟲等透過快速扇動翅膀在原地) 盤旋","examples":["Beautiful butterflies hovered above the wild flowers. 美麗的蝴蝶在野花上方盤旋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hover</b>, you stay in one place and move slightly in a nervous way, for example because you cannot decide what to do. (人) 徘徊","examples":["Judith was hovering in the doorway. 朱迪絲在門口徘徊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>hover</b>, you are in an uncertain situation or state of mind. 處於不穩定狀態","examples":["She hovered on the brink of death for three months as doctors battled to save her. 3個月來在醫生們奮力挽救她的生命的過程中，她一直處在死亡的邊緣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something such as a price, value, or score <b>hovers</b> around a particular level, it stays at more or less that level and does not change much. (價格、價值或分數等) 徘徊 (在某個水平上下)","examples":["In September 1989 the exchange rate hovered around 140 yen to the dollar. 在1989年9月，匯率一直在140日元比1美元左右徘徊。"]}]}]},"housing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房屋，住宅；住房供給，住房建設；（機器的）外殼，外罩；（木塊上的）槽，榫眼；遮蓋物，遮蔽物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"覆蓋；給……房子住；把……儲藏在房內（house 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to the buildings in which people live as <b>housing</b> when you are talking about their standard, price, or availability. 住房","examples":["...a shortage of affordable housing. …廉價住房的短缺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a part designed to shelter, cover, contain, or support a component, such as a bearing, or a mechanism, such as a pump or wheel","examples":[]}]}]},"howl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（狗、狼等）嗥叫，長嚎；（因疼痛、憤怒、開心等）大聲叫喊；（風）怒號，呼嘯；怒吼，怒聲要求；嚎哭"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（狗、狼等）嗥叫，長嚎；（痛苦、憤怒、快樂的）嚎叫，咆哮；（狂風的）怒號，呼嘯；顫噪效應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an animal such as a wolf or a dog <b>howls</b>, it makes a long, loud, crying sound. (狼、狗等動物) 嗥叫","examples":["Somewhere a dog suddenly howled, baying at the moon. 某個地方的一隻狗突然嗥叫起來，對著月亮狂吠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person <b>howls</b>, they make a long, loud cry expressing pain, anger, or unhappiness. (人因痛苦、憤怒、不愉快等) 嚎叫","examples":["He howled like a wounded animal as blood spurted from the gash. 當鮮血從傷口噴射出來時，他像受傷的動物一樣嚎叫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When the wind <b>howls</b>, it blows hard and makes a loud noise. 呼嘯","examples":["The wind howled all night, but I slept a little. 風整夜呼嘯著，但我還是睡了一會兒。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>howl</b> <b>with</b> laughter, you laugh very loudly. 放聲大笑","examples":["Joe, Pink, and Booker howled with delight. 喬、平克和布克高興地放聲大笑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Howl</b> is also a noun. 嗥叫","examples":["The dog let out a savage howl and, wheeling round, flew at him. 狗發出兇猛的嗥叫聲，轉過身向他猛撲過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Howl</b> is also a noun. 嚎叫","examples":["With a howl of rage, he grabbed the neck of a broken bottle and advanced. 他一聲怒號，抓起一個破瓶子的瓶頸向前走去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Howl</b> is also a noun. 大笑","examples":["His stories caused howls of laughter. 他的故事引起陣陣大笑。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>howl</b> something, you say it in a very loud voice. 高聲嚷","examples":["\"Get away, get away, get away,\" he howled. “滾開，滾開，滾開，”他高聲嚷道。"]}]}]},"idiot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"白痴，笨蛋；<古>弱智者，低能兒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call someone an <b>idiot</b>, you are showing that you think they are very stupid or have done something very stupid. 笨蛋","examples":["I knew I'd been an idiot to stay there. 我知道我呆在那兒很傻。"]}]}]},"impulse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衝動；脈衝；推動力"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一時興起的，隨興的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"推動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>impulse</b> is a sudden desire to do something. 衝動","examples":["Unable to resist the impulse, he glanced at the sea again. 他抑制不住衝動，又看了一眼大海。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>impulse</b> is a short electrical signal that is sent along a wire or nerve or through the air, usually as one of a series. 脈衝","examples":["It works by sending a series of electrical impulses which are picked up by hi-tech sensors. 它透過傳輸由高技術感測器收集的電脈衝而起作用。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>impulse</b> buy or <b>impulse</b> purchase is something that you decide to buy when you see it, although you had not planned to buy it. 一時心血來潮的","examples":["The curtains were an impulse buy. 這窗簾是一時心血來潮買下的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on impulse</b>, you suddenly decide to do it, without planning it. 憑一時衝動","examples":["Sean's a fast thinker, and he acts on impulse. 肖恩是個思維敏捷、憑一時衝動行事的人。"]}]}]},"incense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香（樹脂、香料等燃燒可得香氣的物質）；焚香時的煙，香氣；奉承"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"薰香；激怒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Incense</b> is a substance that is burned for its sweet smell, often as part of a religious ceremony. (常指祭祀時用的) 香","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>incenses</b> you, you mean that it makes you extremely angry. 使大怒","examples":["This proposal will incense conservation campaigners. 這項提議將激怒自然保護的倡導者。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被激怒的","examples":["Mom was incensed at his lack of compassion. 媽媽對他缺乏同情心非常憤怒。"]}]}]},"inland":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在內地，向內陸"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內陸的，內地的；國內的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"內陸，內地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is situated <b>inland</b>, it is away from the coast, toward or near the middle of a country. If you go <b>inland</b>, you go away from the coast, toward the middle of a country. 在內地 (或內陸); 向內地 (或內陸)","examples":["The vast majority live further inland. 大多數人居住在更遠的內陸。","It's about 15 minutes' drive inland from Pensacola. 從彭薩科拉出發向內陸行駛，大約有15分鐘的車程。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inland</b> areas, lakes, and places are not on the coast, but in or near the middle of a country. 內地的; 內陸的","examples":["...a rather quiet inland town. …一個很安靜的內陸城鎮。"]}]}]},"indifference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不感興趣，漠不關心；不重要，無價值；平凡，普通"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of <b>indifference</b> <b>to</b> something, you mean that they have a complete lack of interest in it. 漠不關心","examples":["...his callous indifference to the plight of his son. …他對兒子困境的冷漠無情。"]}]}]},"initiate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始實施，發起；使瞭解，傳授；（尤指在秘密儀式上）使加入，接納"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"新加入某組織的人，新入會的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>initiate</b> something, you start it or cause it to happen. 使開始; 發起","examples":["They wanted to initiate a discussion on economics. 他們想發起一次關於經濟學的討論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>initiate</b> someone <b>into</b> something, you introduce them to a particular skill or type of knowledge and teach them about it. 使初步瞭解; 傳授","examples":["He initiated her into the study of other cultures. 他引導她進入對於其他文化的研究。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>is initiated</b> <b>into</b> something such as a religion, secret society, or social group, they become a member of it by taking part in special ceremonies. (常透過特殊儀式) 使加入","examples":["In many societies, young people are formally initiated into their adult roles. 在很多社會，年輕人要透過正式的儀式進入成年。"]}]}]},"institute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"研究所，學院，協會；（尤指與法律相關的）註釋，論述"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"制定（制度、規則等）；提出（訴訟）；任命，授予……職位（尤指聖職）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>institute</b> is an organization set up to do a particular type of work, especially research or teaching. You can also use <b>institute</b> to refer to the building the organization occupies. 協會; 研究所","examples":["...the National Cancer Institute. …國家癌症研究所。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>institute</b> a system, rule, or course of action, you start it. 制定 (規章、制度); 創立","examples":["We will institute a number of measures to better safeguard the public. 我們將制定許多措施更好地保護公眾。"]}]}]},"intent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"專注的，專心致志的；堅決的；急切的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"目的，意圖；故意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>intent</b> <b>on</b> doing something, you are eager and determined to do it. 堅決的","examples":["The rebels are obviously intent on keeping up the pressure. 反叛分子顯然決心繼續施加壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone does something in an <b>intent</b> way, they pay great attention to what they are doing. 專注的","examples":["She looked from one intent face to another. 她看著一張張專注的面孔。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"專注地","examples":["He listened intently, then slammed down the phone. 他專注地聽著，然後猛地把電話放下。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>intent</b> is their intention to do something. 意圖","examples":["The timing of this strong statement of intent on arms control is crucial. 發表這項意圖實施軍備控制的強硬宣告的時機至關重要。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say <b>to all intents and purposes</b> to suggest that a situation is not exactly as you describe it but the effect is the same as if it were. 實際上","examples":["To all intents and purposes he was my father. 他實際上可以稱得上是我的父親。"]}]}]},"index":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"索引；（物價和工資等）指數；指標，量度；冪，根指數；指標"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……編索引，將……編入索引；使指數化，將（工資）等與（物價水平等）掛鉤；（機器，部件）轉位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>index</b> is a system by which changes in the value of something and the rate at which it changes can be recorded, measured, or interpreted. 指數","examples":["...the consumer price index. …消費價格指數。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>index</b> is an alphabetical list that is printed at the back of a book and tells you on which pages important topics are referred to. 索引","examples":["There's even a special subject index. 甚至有一個特別的主題索引。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>index</b> a book or a collection of information, you make an alphabetical list of the items in it. 為…編索引","examples":["A quarter of this vast archive has been indexed and made accessible to researchers. 這批數量巨大的檔案的1/4都已編了索引，可供研究者查閱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a quantity or value <b>is indexed</b> <b>to</b> another, a system is arranged so that it increases or decreases whenever the other one increases or decreases. 使與…掛鉤","examples":["Minimum benefits and wages are to be indexed to inflation. 最低養老金和最低工資都要與通貨膨脹掛鉤。"]}]}]},"interference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"干涉，干預；（收音機或電視機受到的）干擾訊號；犯規阻擋；牴觸，衝突"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Interference</b> by a person or group is their unwanted or unnecessary involvement in something. 干涉","examples":["Airlines will be able to set cheap fares without further interference from the government. 如果不受政府更多的干預，各航空公司將能夠把票價定得很低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When there is <b>interference</b>, a radio signal is affected by other radio waves or electrical activity so that it cannot be received properly. 干擾","examples":["...electrical interference. …電子干擾。"]}]}]},"interior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內部的，裡面的；國內的，內政的；內心的，本質的；內陸的，腹地的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部，裡面；內陸，腹地；（本國的）內政，內務；（建築物或房間內的）內景；內心，本質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>interior</b> of something is the inside part of it. 內部","examples":["The interior of the house was furnished with heavy, old-fashioned pieces. 房內陳設著些笨重、老式的傢俱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>interior</b> of a country or continent is the central area of it. 內地","examples":["The Yangtze River would give access to much of China's interior. 長江使得人們能夠到達中國內陸許多地方。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>interior</b> to describe something that is inside a building or vehicle. (建築或者車輛) 內部的","examples":["The interior walls were painted green. 內牆被漆成了綠色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>interior</b> minister, ministry, or department in some countries deals with affairs within that country, such as law and order. 內政的","examples":["The French Interior Minister has intervened in a scandal over the role of a secret police force. 法國內務部長對一起有關秘密警察部隊職責的醜聞進行了干預。"]}]}]},"isle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（常用於詩歌和名稱中）島"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成島（狀）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>isle</b> is an island; often used as part of an island's name, or in literary English. 島 (用於島名或文學作品中)","examples":["...the Isle of Pines. …派恩斯島。"]}]}]},"interpreter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口譯者，譯員；演奏者，表演者；解釋程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interpreter</b> is a person whose job is to translate what someone is saying into another language. 口譯員","examples":["Speaking through an interpreter, Aristide said that Haitians had hoped coups were behind them. 透過口譯員，亞里斯蒂德說海地人希望政變再也不發生了。"]}]}]},"interpretation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解釋，理解；表演，演奏，藝術處理；口譯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interpretation</b> of something is an opinion about what it means. 解釋","examples":["Professor Wolfgang gives the data a very different interpretation. 沃爾夫岡教授對資料作出很不一樣的解釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A performer's <b>interpretation</b> of something such as a piece of music or a role in a play is the particular way in which they choose to perform it. 演奏; 表演","examples":["...a pianist celebrated for his interpretation of Chopin. …一位以演奏蕭邦作品而聞名的鋼琴家。"]}]}]},"intuition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"直覺力；直覺感知，直覺知識"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>intuition</b> or your <b>intuitions</b> are unexplained feelings that something is true even when you have no evidence or proof of it. 直覺","examples":["Her intuition was telling her that something was wrong. 她的直覺在告訴她事情有些不對頭。"]}]}]},"ivy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"常青藤；用於類似的攀緣植物的名稱中"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"常春藤聯盟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ivy</b> is an evergreen plant that grows up walls or along the ground. 常春藤","examples":[]}]}]},"janitor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（北美英語）清潔工，大樓管理員（負責打掃並維護建築物的人）；（舊義）看門人，守衛，門警"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>janitor</b> is a person whose job is to take care of a building. 看門人","examples":["Ed Roberts had been a school janitor for a long time. 埃德·羅伯茨做學校的看門人已很久了。"]}]}]},"jasmine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"茉莉，茉莉花；淡黃色；（Jasmine）人名；<英>賈絲明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jasmine</b> is a plant with small white or yellow flowers that have a pleasant smell. 茉莉","examples":[]}]}]},"jade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玉，翡翠；玉製品；翡翠色（=jade green）；潑婦，蕩婦；劣馬，衰老的馬"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"疲倦"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"玉製的；綠玉色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jade</b> is a hard stone, usually green in colour, that is used for making jewellery and ornaments. 玉","examples":["The Burmese jade choker in the catalogue was very beautiful. 該目錄中的緬甸玉貼頸項鍊非常漂亮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an old overworked horse; nag; hack 不堪重負的老馬","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>jade</b> or <b>jade green</b> is bright green in colour. 翠綠色","examples":["Amy had bought a soft, jade green cashmere jacket for Helen. 埃米給海倫買了一件柔軟的、翠綠色的山羊絨短上衣。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to exhaust or make exhausted from work or use 耗盡; 使···耗盡","examples":[]}]}]},"jingle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"叮噹聲，丁零聲；短小易記的歌曲或韻文（如節拍規則的簡單詩歌），尤指廣告短歌"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）發出叮噹聲，使丁零作響；（多指詩、韻文）具有簡單而又引人注意的韻律，押韻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>jingles</b> or when you <b>jingle</b> it, it makes a gentle ringing noise, like small bells. 使發出丁零聲; 發出丁零聲","examples":["Brian put his hands in his pockets and jingled some change. 布賴恩把雙手伸進口袋，碰得一些硬幣丁零作響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Jingle</b> is also a noun. 丁零聲","examples":["...the jingle of money in a man's pocket. …一個男人口袋裡硬幣的丁零聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>jingle</b> is a short, simple tune, often with words, that is used to advertise a product or programme on radio or television. (廣播、電視中用於廣告的) 短歌曲","examples":["...advertising jingles. …廣告短歌。"]}]}]},"journalist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞工作者，新聞記者；報人，報紙撰稿人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>journalist</b> is a person whose job is to collect news and write about it for newspapers, magazines, television, or radio. 新聞工作者","examples":[]}]}]},"journalism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞業，新聞工作；報刊雜誌，新聞報道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Journalism</b> is the job of collecting news and writing about it for newspapers, magazines, television, or radio. 新聞工作","examples":["He began a career in journalism, working for the Rocky Mountain News. 他開始從事新聞事業，供職於落基山新聞報。"]}]}]},"jolly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愉快的，高興的；令人愉快的，愜意的；明亮好看的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>鼓勵（某人），勸（某人）高興；開玩笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"聚會，慶祝活動"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於強調）很，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>jolly</b> is happy and cheerful in their appearance or behaviour. 快樂的","examples":["She was a jolly, kindhearted woman. 她是一個開朗、善良的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>jolly</b> event is lively and enjoyable. 令人愉快的","examples":["She had a very jolly time in Korea. 她在韓國過得很愉快。"]}]}]},"jack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"千斤頂，起重器；J 牌，傑克；插孔，插座；絲毫，根本；（滾木球戲中的）小白球；拋接子游戲；<非正式>男人，普通人（Jack）；<美，非正式>伐木工人；<非正式>偵探，警察；<古>高空作業工人；船首旗；<美，非正式>錢；烤肉炙叉旋轉器；琴鍵撥子；鰺；雄性動物（尤指公灰背隼或公驢）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用千斤頂托起；提高，增加；<美>浪費時間；<英，非正式>停止，放棄；登入，接入；<美，非正式>偷竊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<澳，非正式>厭倦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jack</b> is a device for lifting a heavy object, such as a car, off the ground. 千斤頂","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>jack</b> is a playing card whose value is between a ten and a queen. A jack is usually represented by a picture of a young man. (紙牌中的) J","examples":["...the jack of spades. …黑桃J。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a man or fellow 人","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a female socket with two or more terminals designed to receive a male plug (<b>jack plug</b>) that either makes or breaks the circuit or circuits 插座","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a short sleeveless coat of armour of the Middle Ages, consisting usually of a canvas base with metal plates 一種中世紀的無袖鎧甲","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"jackfruit或jakfruit的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to lift or push (an object) with a jack 用千斤頂去頂","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"tired or fed up with (something) 對(事物)厭倦的","examples":[]}]}]},"jug":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（有柄有嘴的）壺，罐；<美> （細口帶柄的）大罐；一壺，一罐（的量）；<非正式>監獄（the jug）；<俚>（女子的）乳房（jugs）；（登山時鑿入山岩中的）攀手（=jug handle）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用罐悶）煮，燉（兔肉）；<美，非正式>起訴並監禁；模仿夜鶯叫；放入壺中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>jug</b> is a cylindrical container with a handle and is used for holding and pouring liquids. 水罐","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>jug</b> to refer to the jug and its contents, or to the contents only. 一水罐的量","examples":["...a jug of water. …一罐水。"]}]}]},"jury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陪審團；（競賽的）裁判委員會"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（航海時）應急的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>鑑定，評審（藝術品、工藝品展覽會或展品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a court of law, the <b>jury</b> is the group of people who have been chosen from the general public to listen to the facts about a crime and to decide whether the person accused is guilty or not. 陪審團","examples":["The jury convicted Mr. Hampson of all offences. 該陪審團裁定漢普森先生的全部罪名成立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>jury</b> is a group of people who choose the winner of a competition. (競賽的) 評委會","examples":["I am not surprised that the jury chose to award this novel the prize. 我並不驚訝於評委選擇給這部小說頒獎。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"makeshift 應急的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that <b>the jury is out</b> or that <b>the jury is still out</b> on a particular subject, you mean that people in general have still not made a decision or formed an opinion about that subject. 尚無定論","examples":["The jury is out on whether or not this is true. 這是否屬實尚無定論。"]}]}]},"jeer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘲笑，戲弄，奚落（常與 at 連用）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘲笑，戲弄；奚落人的話，揶揄的言語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>jeer</b> <b>at</b> someone means to say or shout rude and insulting things to them to show that you do not like or respect them. 嘲弄","examples":["Marchers jeered at white passers-by, but there was no violence, nor any arrests. 遊行者們嘲弄路過的白人們，但並沒有發生暴力事件，也沒人被逮捕。","Demonstrators jeered the mayor as he arrived for a week-long visit. 示威者們在市長到達進行為期一週訪問的時候嘲弄了他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嘲弄","examples":["There was constant jeering and interruption from the floor. 議員席上不時有嘲笑和打岔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Jeers</b> are rude and insulting things that people shout to show they do not like or respect someone. 奚落人的話","examples":["...the heckling and jeers of his audience. …觀眾對他的那些詰問和奚落。"]}]}]},"kin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（統稱）家屬，親戚"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）有親戚關係的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>kin</b> are your relatives. 親戚","examples":[]}]}]},"juvenile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"青少年的，未成年的；少年犯的；幼稚的，孩子氣的；（鳥或動物）幼年的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"青少年，未成年人；扮演青少年角色的演員；幼鳥，幼獸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>juvenile</b> is a child or young person who is not yet old enough to be regarded as an adult. 青少年","examples":["The number of juveniles in the general population has fallen by a fifth in the past 10 years. 在過去的10年中，青少年在總人口中所佔的比重下降了1/5。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Juvenile</b> activity or behaviour involves young people who are not yet adults. 青少年的","examples":["Juvenile crime is increasing at a terrifying rate. 青少年犯罪在以驚人的速度增加。"]}]}]},"issue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"議題，爭論點；（報紙、雜誌等的）期，號；發放，分配；（新股票或郵票等的）發行；子女，後嗣；流出，發出；<舊>結果，後果"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"發表，頒佈；分發，分配；正式發行；流出，發出；由……產生，由……得出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>issue</b> is an important subject that people are arguing about or discussing. 議題","examples":["Agents will raise the issue of prize-money for next year's world championships. 代理商們會提出明年世界錦標賽的獎金問題。","A key issue for higher education in the 1990s is the need for greater diversity of courses. 20世紀90年代高等教育的一個關鍵問題是需要使課程更加多樣化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>the issue</b>, it is the thing you consider to be the most important part of a situation or discussion. 要點","examples":["I was earning a lot of money, but that was not the issue. 我是掙著很多錢，但那不是問題的關鍵。","Do not draw it on the chart, however, as this will confuse the issue. 但是不要把它畫在圖表上，因為這將使要點模糊不清。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>issue</b> of something such as a magazine or newspaper is the version of it that is published, for example, in a particular month or on a particular day. (雜誌或報刊的) 期","examples":["The growing problem is underlined in the latest issue of the Scientific American. 這一日益嚴重的問題在最新一期的《科學美國人》上得到強調。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Issue</b> is also a noun. 分發","examples":["...a standard army issue rifle. …一支標準的軍隊配發的步槍。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>issue</b> a statement or a warning, you make it known formally or publicly. 發表 (宣告); 發出 (警告)","examples":["Last night he issued a statement denying the allegations. 昨天晚上，他發表了一項宣告否認那些說法。","The government issued a warning that the strikers should end their action or face dismissal. 該政府發出了警告，罷工者們應停止他們的行動，否則將被免職。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are issued with</b> something, it is officially given to you. 分發","examples":["On your appointment you will be issued with a written statement of particulars of employment. 你上任時會收到一份聘用細則的書面材料。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The question or point <b>at issue</b> is the question or point that is being argued about or discussed. 爭論中的","examples":["The problems of immigration were not the question at issue. 移民問題不在爭論之列。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make an issue of</b> something, you try to make other people think about it or discuss it, because you are concerned or annoyed about it. 挑起對…的爭論","examples":["It seemed the Colonel had no desire to make an issue of the affair. 那位上校似乎不願挑起對此事的爭論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>take issue with</b> someone or something they said, you disagree with them, and start arguing about it. 對…持異議","examples":["I will not take issue with the fact that we have a recession. 我不會對我們經歷經濟衰退這一事實表示異議。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>has issues</b> <b>with</b> a particular aspect of their life, they have problems connected with it. 有…方面的問題","examples":["Once you have issues with food, you're going to have them for the rest of your life. 一旦你在食物方面有問題，你以後的生活中就一直會有這樣的問題。"]}]}]},"landlord":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房東，地主；<英>（客棧、酒吧或出租公寓的）店主，老闆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>landlord</b> is the man who allows them to live or work in a building which he owns, in return for rent. 房東","examples":["His landlord doubled the rent. 他的房東把房租提高了一倍。"]}]}]},"landlady":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女房東，女地主；（酒吧或招待所的）女老闆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>landlady</b> is the woman who allows them to live or work in a building which she owns, in return for rent. 女房東","examples":["There was a note under the door from my landlady. 門下有我女房東的一張便條。"]}]}]},"lad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"男孩，小夥子；<英，非正式>夥伴，哥們兒；<英，非正式>放蕩不羈的人；<英>馬廄工人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lad</b> is a young man or boy. 小夥子","examples":["When I was a lad his age I would laugh at the strangest things. 我是他那麼大的小夥子時，我常嘲笑一些最奇怪的事情。"]}]}]},"lawmaker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立法者，議員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lawmaker</b> is someone such as a politician who is responsible for proposing and passing new laws. 立法者","examples":[]}]}]},"laser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鐳射（器）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使用鐳射器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>laser</b> is a narrow beam of concentrated light produced by a special machine. It is used for cutting very hard materials, and in many technical fields such as surgery and telecommunications. 鐳射","examples":["...new laser technology. …新的鐳射技術。"]}]}]},"lash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛擊，狠打；鞭打，抽打；怒斥，抨擊；捆綁，捆紮；煽動，激勵；（動物）用力甩動（尾巴）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"睫毛；鞭打（尤作為懲罰）；突然（猛烈）的一甩；責罵，諷刺；鞭梢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>lashes</b> are the hairs that grow on the edge of your upper and lower eyelids. 睫毛","examples":["...sombre grey eyes, with unusually long lashes. …憂鬱的灰眼睛，長著特長的睫毛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lash</b> is a blow with a whip, especially a blow on someone's back as a punishment. 鞭打","examples":["The villagers sentenced one man to five lashes for stealing a ham from his neighbour. 村民們判一個男人5下鞭刑，因為他偷了一個鄰居的火腿。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lash</b> two or more things together, you tie one of them firmly to the other. 捆緊","examples":["Secure the anchor by lashing it to the rail. 把錨緊緊地捆在橫木上。","The shelter is built by lashing poles together to form a small dome. 該掩蔽處是把杆子捆到一起形成一個小圓頂而搭建成。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If wind, rain, or water <b>lashes</b> someone or something, it hits them violently. (風、雨、水等) 猛襲","examples":["The worst winter storms of the century lashed the east coast of North America. 本世紀最猛烈的暴風雪襲擊了北美的東海岸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>lashes</b> you or <b>lashes</b> <b>into</b> you, they speak very angrily to you, criticizing you or saying you have done something wrong. 怒斥","examples":["She went quiet for a moment while she summoned up the words to lash him. 她沉默了一會兒，想了些話來怒斥他。"]}]}]},"latitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"緯度；緯度地區；選擇的自由，迴旋餘地；（感光乳劑，相紙）曝光寬容度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>latitude</b> of a place is its distance from the equator. Compare . 緯度","examples":["In the middle to high latitudes rainfall has risen steadily over the last 20-30 years. 中高緯度地區的降雨量在過去的20到30年間穩步上升了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Latitude</b> is freedom to choose the way in which you do something. 自由度","examples":["He would be given every latitude in forming a new government. 他將被給予高度自由來建立一個新政府。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Latitude</b> is also an adjective. 緯度的","examples":["The army must cease military operations above 36° latitude north. 軍隊必須停止在北緯36度以北地區的軍事行動。"]}]}]},"legislation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"法規，法律；立法，制訂法律"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Legislation</b> consists of a law or laws passed by a government. 立法","examples":["...a letter calling for legislation to protect women's rights. …呼籲立法保護婦女權利的一封信。"]}]}]},"lieutenant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（陸軍、海軍、空軍）中尉；（美國消防、警察部門的）中尉；副職官員，代理官員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lieutenant</b> is a person who holds a junior officer's rank in the army, navy, marines, or air force, or in the U.S. police force. 陸軍中尉; 海軍上尉; (美國的) 警官","examples":["Lieutenant Campbell ordered the man at the wheel to steer for the gunboat. 坎貝爾上尉命令舵手向炮艇駛去。"]}]}]},"league":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯盟，同盟；（體育專案）聯合會，社團；聯賽；級別，水平；裡格（舊時長度單位，約等於5公里）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（與……）組成聯盟，加入聯盟"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>league</b> is a group of people, clubs, or countries that have joined together for a particular purpose, or because they share a common interest. 聯盟; 協會","examples":["...the League of Nations. …國際聯盟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>league</b> is a group of teams that play the same sport or activity against each other. (各種運動隊的) 聯盟","examples":["...the American League series between the Boston Red Sox and World Champion Oakland Athletics. …波士頓紅襪隊和世界冠軍奧克蘭運動家隊之間的美國職業棒球聯盟系列賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>league</b> to make comparisons between different people or things, especially in terms of their quality. 級別; 水平","examples":["Her success has taken her out of my league. 她的成功使她和我不再處於同一個等級上了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"an obsolete unit of distance of varying length. It is commonly equal to 3 miles 裡格; 長度單位，約為3英里","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>in league</b> <b>with</b> another person to do something bad, you mean that they are working together to do that thing. (與某人) 勾結","examples":["There is no evidence that the broker was in league with the fraudulent vendor. 沒有代理人和姦商相勾結的證據。"]}]}]},"layer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"層；層次，等級；擺放者，鋪設者，產卵者；壓條"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分層放置；把（頭髮）分層剪短；用壓條培育（植物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>layer</b> of a material or substance is a quantity or piece of it that covers a surface or that is between two other things. 層","examples":["...the depletion of the ozone layer. …臭氧層的損耗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a system or an idea has many <b>layers</b>, it has many different levels or parts. 層次","examples":["Critics and the public puzzle out the layers of meaning in his photos. 評論家和公眾苦思冥想出了他照片中的層層含意。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>layer</b> something, you arrange it in layers. 分層放置","examples":["Layer half the onion slices on top of the potatoes. 把一半洋蔥片一層層地放在土豆上。"]}]}]},"likelihood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能，可能性；可能的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>likelihood</b> <b>of</b> something happening is how likely it is to happen. 可能性","examples":["The likelihood of infection is minimal. 傳染的可能性微乎其微。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is a <b>likelihood</b>, it is likely to happen. 可能發生的事情","examples":["But the likelihood is that people would be willing to pay if they were certain that their money was going to a good cause. 但有可能的是，如果人們確信自己的錢將用於善事，他們會願意出錢的。"]}]}]},"livestock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牲畜，家畜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Animals such as cattle and sheep which are kept on a farm are referred to as <b>livestock</b>. 家畜","examples":["The heavy rains and flooding killed scores of livestock. 大雨和洪水淹死了許多家畜。"]}]}]},"lizard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蜥蜴；類蜥蜴爬行動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lizard</b> is a reptile with short legs and a long tail. 蜥蜴","examples":[]}]}]},"locomotive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機車，火車頭"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"移動的，運動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>locomotive</b> is a large vehicle that pulls a train. 火車頭","examples":[]}]}]},"lime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酸橙（樹）；酸橙飲料；酸橙綠色，淡黃綠色；石灰，生石灰；歐椴樹，菩提樹；<舊>粘鳥膠；（交談時較注重禮儀和規矩的）非正式社交聚會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"撒石灰於；坐著（或站著）閒聊；粉刷，用石灰塗白；<舊>用粘鳥膠捕鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lime</b> is a green fruit that tastes like a lemon. Limes grow on trees in tropical countries. 酸橙","examples":["...peeled slices of lime. …去皮橙片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any linden tree, such as <b>Tilia europaea,</b> planted in many varieties for ornament 歐椴樹","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Lime</b> is a substance containing calcium. It is found in soil and water. 石灰","examples":["If your soil is very acidic, add lime. 如果你的土壤酸性很強，就加點石灰。"]}]}]},"locust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蝗蟲，蚱蜢；洋槐，刺槐；槐木"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Locusts</b> are large insects, similar to grasshoppers, that live mainly in hot areas and often cause serious damage to crops. 蝗蟲","examples":["...a swarm of locusts. …一群蝗蟲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a North American leguminous tree, <b>Robinia pseudoacacia,</b> having prickly branches, hanging clusters of white fragrant flowers, and reddish-brown seed pods 洋槐樹 (Also called locust tree, false acacia)","examples":[]}]}]},"limp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"瘸著腳走，跛行；進展緩慢，艱難地行進"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"柔軟的，不直挺的；無力的，無精神的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跛行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>limps</b>, they walk with difficulty or in an uneven way because one of their legs or feet is hurt. 跛行","examples":["I wasn't badly hurt, but I injured my thigh and had to limp. 我傷得並不嚴重，但我傷到了大腿，不得不一瘸一拐地走路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as an organization, process, or vehicle <b>limps</b> <b>along</b>, you mean that it continues slowly or with difficulty, for example because it has been weakened or damaged. (交通工具等) 緩慢或艱難地前進; (組織、程序等) 進展緩慢","examples":["In recent years the newspaper had been limping along on limited resources. 近年來該報一直靠有限的資源艱難地發展。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Limp</b> is also a noun. 跛行","examples":["A stiff knee following surgery forced her to walk with a limp. 手術後僵直的膝蓋迫使她瘸著走路。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>limp</b>, you mean that it is soft or weak when it should be firm or strong. 無力的","examples":["She was told to reject applicants with limp handshakes. 有人告訴她透過無力的握手來拒絕申請者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>limp</b>, their body has no strength and is not moving, for example, because they are asleep or unconscious. 軟弱無力的","examples":["He carried her limp body into the room and laid her on the bed. 他抱起她軟綿綿的身體走進那房間，把她放到床上。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無力地","examples":["Flags and bunting hung limply in the still, warm air. 旗子和飄帶在靜止、溫暖的空中無力地垂著。"]}]}]},"logo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司或組織的）標識，徽標；（Logo）<美>洛戈（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>logo</b> of a company or organization is the special design or way of writing its name that it puts on all its products, stationery, or advertisements. 標誌","examples":["...the famous MGM logo of the roaring lion. …米高梅公司著名的怒吼狂獅標誌。"]}]}]},"longitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經度，經線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>longitude</b> of a place is its distance to the west or east of a line passing through Greenwich, England. Compare . 經度","examples":["He noted the latitude and longitude, then made a mark on the admiralty chart. 他記下經度和緯度，然後在海圖上作了標記。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Longitude</b> is also an adjective. 經度的","examples":["A similar feature is found at 13 degrees north between 230 degrees and 250 degrees longitude. 在北緯13度、經度230度到250度之間也發現了類似的特點。"]}]}]},"lottery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽彩給獎法，博彩；<美>抽籤法，隨機選擇；碰運氣的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lottery</b> is a type of gambling game in which people buy numbered tickets. Several numbers are then chosen, and the people who have those numbers on their tickets win a prize. 彩票抽獎","examples":["...the national lottery. …全國性的彩票抽獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>a lottery</b>, you mean that what happens depends entirely on luck or chance. 靠運氣的事","examples":["The stockmarket is a lottery. 股市靠的是運氣。"]}]}]},"lotus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蓮屬植物；蓮（花）飾（在亞洲藝術和宗教中帶有象徵意義）；落拓棗，忘憂果（食後感到夢幻般的快樂輕鬆）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lotus</b> or a <b>lotus flower</b> is a type of water lily that grows in Africa and Asia. 蓮花","examples":[]}]}]},"mainland":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大陸，本土"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the largest part of a country or continent as <b>the mainland</b> when contrasting it with the islands around it. 大陸","examples":["She was going to Nanaimo to catch the ferry to the mainland. 她打算到納奈莫乘渡船去大陸。"]}]}]},"lumber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"緩慢地移動，笨拙地行走；迫使擔負（工作或責任）；<美>伐木；逢場作戲地結識；亂堆"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"木材；<英>廢舊傢俱，廢舊大件雜物；被看作可能成為性伴侶的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lumber</b> consists of trees and large pieces of wood that have been roughly cut up. 木材","examples":["It was made of soft lumber, spruce by the look of it. 它是軟木做的，看樣子是雲杉。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>lumbers</b> from one place to another, they move there very slowly and clumsily. 緩慢笨拙地移動","examples":["He lumbered back to his chair. 他蹣跚地坐回到椅子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to burden with something unpleasant, tedious, etc 使煩惱; 煩擾","examples":[]}]}]},"maiden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>少女，未婚女子，處女；（板球）零得分投球輪；（賽跑中）未贏過的馬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"首次的，初次的；（女子）未婚的；（賽馬）從未跑贏過的；（樹木或其他果實植物）生長期第一年內的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>maiden</b> is a young girl or woman. 少女","examples":["...stories of noble princes and their brave deeds on behalf of beautiful maidens. …高貴的王子以及他們英雄救美的故事。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>maiden</b> voyage or flight of a ship or aircraft is the first official journey that it makes. (航行、飛行) 首次的","examples":["In 1912, the Titanic sank on her maiden voyage. 1912年，泰坦尼克號首次航行時沉沒。"]}]}]},"lodge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）固定，（使）卡住；（通常付住宿費地）借住，寄住，（為某人）提供住宿；存放，寄放（貴重物品）；正式提出（投訴、要求等）；銘記，留存"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公園或宅第的）門口小屋，門房；（大學、機構等的）門房，管理員室；（鄉村或山間供狩獵者等使用的）小屋，小舍；（地方分會會員的）集會地，活動地；（河狸或水獺的）穴，窩；印第安錐形棚屋；（劍橋的）學院院長住宅；用於名字中宅，舍，旅館"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lodge</b> is a house or hotel in the country or in the mountains where people stay on holiday, especially when they want to hunt or fish. (鄉野中的度假) 屋舍; 旅館","examples":["...a Victorian hunting lodge. …一間維多利亞式的小屋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lodge</b> is a small house at the entrance to the grounds of a large house. 門房","examples":["I drove out of the gates, past the keeper's lodge. 我開車出了大門，經過看門人的門房。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lodge</b> a complaint, protest, accusation, or claim, you officially make it. 正式提出 (投訴、抗議、指控、要求)","examples":["He has four weeks in which to lodge an appeal. 他有4周時間來正式提出上訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>lodge</b> somewhere, such as in someone else's house or if you <b>are lodged</b> there, you live there, usually paying rent. 借住; 租住","examples":["...the story of the farming family she lodged with as a young teacher. …關於她還是個年輕老師時所借住的那個農家的故事。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object <b>lodges</b> somewhere, it becomes stuck there. 卡住","examples":["The bullet lodged in the sergeant's leg, shattering his thigh bone. 子彈射入這個軍士的腿部，擊碎了他的大腿骨。"]}]}]},"majesty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雄偉，壯麗，威嚴；陛下（對國王或女王的稱呼）；君權，王權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use majesty in expressions such as <b>Your Majesty</b> or <b>Her Majesty</b> when you are addressing or referring to a king or queen. 陛下","examples":["His Majesty requests your presence in the royal chambers. 國王陛下要求你在皇室受召見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Majesty</b> is the quality of being beautiful, dignified, and impressive. 壯麗; 雄偉","examples":["...the majesty of the mainland mountains. …大陸山嶽的壯美。"]}]}]},"mainstream":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主流"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主流的；（學校，班級）為無特殊需求學生開設的，普通的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使主流化，使成為主流；（把有特殊教育需求的孩子）編入普通班級"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People, activities, or ideas that are part of the <b>mainstream</b> are regarded as the most typical, normal, and conventional because they belong to the same group or system as most others of their kind. 主流","examples":["...people outside the economic mainstream. …經濟主流之外的人們。"]}]}]},"lump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不定形的）塊；（單獨的）大量；腫塊；方糖；<非正式>笨重的人，傻大個；<非正式>個體勞動者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……歸併在一起；無奈地接受，勉強同意；結塊，起疙瘩；<英>揹負（重物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"成團的；總共的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lump</b> <b>of</b> something is a solid piece of it. 塊","examples":["The potter shaped and squeezed the lump of clay into a graceful shape. 製陶工人把一塊黏土塑形，壓成漂亮的形狀。","...a lump of wood. …一塊木頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lump</b> on or in someone's body is a small, hard swelling that has been caused by an injury or an illness. 腫塊","examples":["I've got a lump on my shoulder. 我的肩膀上有個腫塊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>lump</b> <b>of</b> sugar is a small cube of it. 一小方塊 (糖)","examples":["...a nugget of rough gold about the size of a lump of sugar. …未加工的天然金塊，約一塊方糖大小。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you have a <b>lump in</b> your <b>throat</b>, you mean that you have a tight feeling in your throat because of a strong emotion such as sorrow or gratitude. 喉嚨哽咽","examples":["I stood there with a lump in my throat and tried to fight back tears. 我站在那兒，喉嚨哽咽，拼命忍住眼淚。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to collect into a mass or group (積成)塊; 團","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to tolerate or put up with; endure (in the phrase <b>lump it</b>) 容忍; 忍耐","examples":[]}]}]},"mansion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大廈，宅邸；<英>公寓樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mansion</b> is a very large house. 大廈","examples":["...an eighteenth-century mansion in New Hampshire. …新罕布什爾州一座18世紀的大廈。"]}]}]},"maintenance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"維護，保養；保持，維持；（依法應負擔的）生活費，撫養費；包攬訴訟罪，非法資助訴訟罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>maintenance</b> of a building, vehicle, road, or machine is the process of keeping it in good condition by regularly checking it and repairing it when necessary. 檢修","examples":["...maintenance work on government buildings. …政府各大樓的檢修工作。","The window had been replaced last week during routine maintenance. 那窗在上星期的例行檢修中已被換掉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Maintenance</b> is money that someone gives regularly to another person to pay for the things that the person needs. 贍養費; 撫養費","examples":["...the government's plan to make absent fathers pay maintenance for their children. …讓那些不在孩子身邊的父親為孩子提供撫養費的政府計劃。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you ensure the <b>maintenance</b> <b>of</b> a state or process, you make sure that it continues. 維持","examples":["...the maintenance of peace and stability in Asia. …亞洲和平與穩定的維持。"]}]}]},"maple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（生長在加拿大等北方國家的）槭樹，楓樹（=maple tree）；槭木，楓木"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"淡棕色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>maple</b> or a <b>maple tree</b> is a tree with five-pointed leaves which turn bright red or gold in the fall. 楓樹","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Maple</b> is the wood of this tree. 楓木","examples":["...a solid maple worktop. …一張結實的楓木工作臺。"]}]}]},"mammal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"哺乳動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mammals</b> are animals such as humans, dogs, lions, and whales. In general, female mammals give birth to babies rather than laying eggs, and feed their young with milk. 哺乳動物","examples":[]}]}]},"marine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"海洋的，海產的；海運的，海事的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"水兵，海軍陸戰隊士兵；（一個國家的）船舶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>marine</b> is a member of an armed force, for example the U.S. Marine Corps or the Royal Marines, who is specially trained for military duties at sea as well as on land. 海軍陸戰隊士兵","examples":["A small number of Marines were wounded. 幾名海軍陸戰隊士兵受了傷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Marine</b> is used to describe things relating to the sea or to the animals and plants that live in the sea. 海洋的","examples":["...breeding grounds for marine life. …海洋生物的繁殖地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Marine</b> is used to describe things relating to ships and their movement at sea. 海事的","examples":["...a lawyer specializing in marine law. …一名專攻海事法的律師。"]}]}]},"marvel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"令人驚異的人（或事），奇蹟"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"感到驚奇，大為讚歎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>marvel</b> at something, you express your great surprise, wonder, or admiration. 大為讚歎","examples":["Her fellow members marvelled at her seemingly infinite energy. 她的同事們對她那似乎無盡的精力大為讚歎。","Sara and I read the story and marvelled. 我和薩拉讀了這個故事後驚歎不已。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe something or someone as a <b>marvel</b> to indicate that you think that they are wonderful. 奇蹟","examples":["The whale, like the dolphin, has become a symbol of the marvels of creation. 鯨，和海豚一樣，已經成為造物傑作的象徵。"]}]}]},"massage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"按摩，推拿"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"按摩，推拿；竄改；用………揉擦（皮膚、頭髮等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Massage</b> is the action of squeezing and rubbing someone's body, as a way of making them relax or reducing their pain. 按摩","examples":["Alex asked me if I wanted a massage. 亞歷克斯問我是否需要一次按摩。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>massage</b> someone or a part of their body, you squeeze and rub their body, in order to make them relax or reduce their pain. 按摩","examples":["She continued massaging her right foot, which was bruised and aching. 她繼續按摩她的右腳，那隻腳又腫又疼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>massages</b> statistics, figures, or evidence, you are criticizing them for changing or presenting the facts in a way that misleads people. 竄改","examples":["Their governments have no reason to \"massage\" the statistics. 他們的政府沒有理由“竄改”這些資料。"]}]}]},"marshal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（英國）陸軍元帥，空軍元帥；司儀，典禮官；（尤指體育賽事的）總指揮；（美國法院的）執行官；一些美國城市的）警察局長，消防局長；（英國）巡迴法官隨員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結集，安排；控制，組織；整理（思路、想法等）；（車輛）編組；引導（飛機在機場地面移動）；合併（盾徽）；成形，有序"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>marshal</b> people or things, you gather them together and arrange them for a particular purpose. 召集; 安排","examples":["The company turned its attention to marshalling its creditors' approval. 這家公司把注意力轉向了集結債權人的支援。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>marshal</b> is an official who helps to supervise a public event, especially a sports event. (尤指體育賽事的) 典禮官","examples":["The grand prix is controlled by well-trained marshals. 大賽由訓練有素的典禮官們掌控。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the United States and some other countries, a <b>marshal</b> is a police officer, often one who is responsible for a particular area. (美國等國家的) 警察局長","examples":["A federal marshal was killed in a shoot-out. 一名聯邦警察局長在槍戰中被打死了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>marshal</b> is an officer in a fire department. 消防隊長","examples":["She was ordered out of her home by a fire marshal because the house next door had an explosion from a leaking gas main. 她被消防隊長命令離開自己的家，因為隔壁房的煤氣主管道洩漏發生了爆炸。"]}]}]},"mash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"糊狀物，泥狀物；飼料；麥芽漿，醪液；（Mash，英）人名：馬什"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"搗碎，把…搗成糊狀；調情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mash</b> food that is solid but soft, you crush it so that it forms a soft mass. 把…搗成糊狀","examples":["Mash the bananas with a fork. 用叉子把這些香蕉搗成糊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a soft pulpy mass or consistency 糊狀物","examples":[]}]}]},"mayonnaise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蛋黃醬；<英>用蛋黃醬調製的食物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mayonnaise</b> is a thick, pale sauce made from egg yolks and oil. It is put on food such as salad and sandwiches. 蛋黃醬","examples":[]}]}]},"masculine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"男性的，男子的；陽剛的，男子氣概的；（某些語言中）陽性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"陽性詞，陽性詞形；男性，雄性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Masculine</b> qualities and things relate to or are considered typical of men, in contrast to women. 男性的","examples":["...masculine characteristics like a husky voice and facial hair. …沙啞的嗓音和麵部的鬍鬚之類的男性特徵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>masculine</b>, you mean that they have qualities such as strength or confidence which are considered typical of men. 男子氣概的","examples":["...her aggressive, masculine image. …她敢作敢為、男人般的形象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In some languages, a <b>masculine</b> noun, pronoun, or adjective has a different form from a feminine or neuter one, or behaves in a different way. (某些語言中的詞) 陽性的","examples":[]}]}]},"masterpiece":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代表作，傑作；極好的例證；手藝人為取得大師資格並進入行會而製作的作品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>masterpiece</b> is an extremely good painting, novel, film, or other work of art. 傑作","examples":["His book, I must add, is a masterpiece. 他的書，我必須補充一點，是一部傑作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An artist's, writer's, or composer's <b>masterpiece</b> is the best work that they have ever produced. 代表作","examples":["\"Man's Fate,\" translated into sixteen languages, is probably his masterpiece. 《人類的命運》，被翻譯成16種文字，可能是他的代表作。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>masterpiece</b> is an extremely clever or skilful example of something. 典範","examples":["The whole thing was a masterpiece of crowd management. 整件事情是大眾管理的典範。"]}]}]},"meantime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"同時，在此期間"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"其時，其間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>In the meantime</b> or <b>meantime</b> means in the period of time between two events. 在…期間","examples":["Eventually your child will leave home to lead her own life, but in the meantime she relies on your support. 最終你的孩子將會離開家去過她自己的生活，不過在此期間她依賴你的支援。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>For the meantime</b> means for a period of time from now until something else happens. 暫時","examples":["Some of her stuff is stored for the meantime with her children. 她的一些東西暫時儲存在她的孩子那裡。"]}]}]},"mechanics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機械學，力學；機制，運作方式；機械部件，運轉部件；結構，構成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mechanic</b> is someone whose job is to repair and maintain machines and engines, especially car engines. 機修工","examples":["If you smell something unusual (gas fumes or burning, for instance), take the car to your mechanic. 如果你聞到了異味（例如汽油味或燃燒味），就把車帶給你的修理工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mechanics</b> <b>of</b> a process, system, or activity are the way in which it works or the way in which it is done. 運作方式","examples":["What are the mechanics of this new process? 這一新工序的運作方式是什麼？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Mechanics</b> is the part of physics that deals with the natural forces that act on moving or stationary objects. 力學","examples":["He has not studied mechanics or engineering. 他沒有學習過力學或者工程學。"]}]}]},"mermaid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美人魚（傳說中的）；女子游泳健將"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In fairy tales and legends, a <b>mermaid</b> is a woman with a fish's tail instead of legs, who lives in the sea. 美人魚","examples":[]}]}]},"menace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"威脅，危險的人或物；煩人的人（或事物），引起麻煩的人（或事物）；危險氣氛，威脅；<英，法律>（以）威脅（或恐嚇）的手段（索要錢財）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>威脅，威嚇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is a <b>menace</b> to other people or things, you mean that person or thing is likely to cause serious harm. 威脅","examples":["In my view, you are a menace to the public. 在我看來，你對公眾是一個威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone or something as a <b>menace</b> when you want to say that they cause you trouble or annoyance. 煩人之人; 煩人之物","examples":["You're a menace to my privacy, Kenton. 你是個侵犯我隱私的討厭的人，肯頓。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Menace</b> is a quality or atmosphere that gives you the feeling that you are in danger or that someone wants to harm you. 危險性; 威脅性","examples":["There is a pervading sense of menace. 有一種在蔓延的危險感。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>menaces</b> another, you mean that the first thing is likely to cause the second thing serious harm. 威脅","examples":["They seem determined to menace the United States and its allies. 他們好像決心要威脅美國及其盟國。"]}]}]},"milestone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要事件，轉折點；里程碑，里程標"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>milestone</b> is an important event in the history or development of something or someone. 里程碑","examples":["He said the launch of the party represented a milestone in Zambian history. 他說該黨的成立代表著尚比亞歷史上的一個里程碑。"]}]}]},"midst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"中部，中間"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……中間，在……之中（=amidst）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>in the midst of</b> doing something, you are doing it at the moment. 正當…的時候","examples":["We are in the midst of one of the worst recessions for many, many years. 我們正處於許多年以來最嚴重的一次經濟衰退。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>in the midst of</b> an event, it happens during it. 正當…時","examples":["Eleanor arrived in the midst of a blizzard. 埃莉諾到達時正下著暴風雪。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>in the midst of</b> a group of people or things, they are among them or surrounded by them. 在…當中","examples":["Many were surprised to see him exposed like this in the midst of a large crowd. 很多人看到他這樣暴露在一大群人當中，都感到很意外。"]}]}]},"migrant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（為工作）移居者，移民；候鳥，遷徙動物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"移民的，有遷徙習性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>migrant</b> is a person who moves from one place to another, especially in order to find work. 移民","examples":["The government divides asylum seekers into economic migrants and genuine refugees. 政府將尋求政治庇護的人劃分為經濟移民和真正的難民。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Migrants</b> are birds, fish, or animals that migrate from one part of the world to another. 遷徙動物","examples":["Migrant birds shelter in the reeds. 候鳥隱蔽在蘆葦叢中。"]}]}]},"miser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（貶義）守財奴，吝嗇鬼；（工程技術）鑿井機，大型土螺鑽；（Miser，首字母大寫）人名（英：邁澤，德：米澤，西：米塞爾）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is a <b>miser</b>, you disapprove of them because they seem to hate spending money, and to spend as little as possible. 吝嗇鬼; 守財奴","examples":["I'm married to a miser. 我嫁了個守財奴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a large hand-operated auger used for loose soils (手動)大土螺鑽","examples":[]}]}]},"mileage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行駛里程；英里數；好處，益處；按英里支付的交通補貼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mileage</b> refers to the distance that you have travelled, measured in miles. 英里里程","examples":["While most of their mileage may be in and around town, they still want motorways for longer trips. 他們大多數的行程可能都在城裡或城周圍，可是他們仍然需要適合長距離旅行的高速公路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>mileage</b> of a vehicle is the number of miles that it can travel using one gallon or litre of fuel. (耗油1加侖或1升可行駛的) 英里里程","examples":["They are willing to pay up to $500 more for cars that get better mileage. 他們願意多付$500來買單位汽油里程數更高的汽車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>mileage</b> in a particular course of action is its usefulness in getting you what you want. 好處","examples":["It's obviously important to get as much mileage out of the convention as possible. 從契約中得到儘可能多的好處顯然很重要。"]}]}]},"mint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"薄荷；薄荷糖；鑄幣廠；鉅款"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鑄造（硬幣）；創造，製造"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（物品）嶄新的，無汙損的；<英> 非常好的，很棒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mint</b> is an herb with fresh-tasting leaves. 薄荷","examples":["Garnish with mint sprigs. 以薄荷枝裝飾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mint</b> is a sweet with a peppermint flavour. Some people suck mints in order to make their breath smell fresher. 薄荷糖","examples":["She popped a mint into her mouth. 她往嘴裡丟了塊兒薄荷糖。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>mint</b> is the place where the official coins of a country are made. 造幣廠","examples":["In 1965 the mint stopped putting silver in dimes. 1965年，造幣廠停止在10美分鑄幣中加入銀。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mint</b> coins or medals means to make them in a mint. 鑄造","examples":["...the right to mint coins. …鑄造硬幣權。"]}]}]},"moan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"呻吟，嗚咽；<非正式>抱怨，發牢騷；（風）發出蕭蕭聲； <文>悲嘆，哀悼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>（尤指風的）呼嘯聲，蕭蕭聲；呻吟聲，嗚咽聲；<非正式>不滿，牢騷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>moan</b>, you make a low sound, usually because you are unhappy or in pain. 呻吟","examples":["Tony moaned in his sleep and then turned over on his side. 託尼在睡夢中呻吟了一下，然後轉身側躺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Moan</b> is also a noun. 呻吟","examples":["Suddenly she gave a low, choking moan and began to tremble violently. 突然她發出了一聲低沉、令人窒息的呻吟，身體開始劇烈地抖動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>moan</b> is a complaint. 抱怨","examples":["They have been listening to people's moans and praise. 他們一直在傾聽人民的抱怨與稱讚。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>moan</b> means to complain or speak in a way which shows that you are very unhappy. 抱怨","examples":["I used to moan if I didn't get at least six hours' sleep at night. 我過去常常抱怨晚上睡不夠6小時。","...moaning about the weather. …抱怨天氣。"]}]}]},"mock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘲笑，（模仿）嘲弄；使顯得徒勞，使顯得可笑；（照原尺寸）模仿，仿製 （mock sth. up）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"假裝的，假的；模擬的；（考試、作戰等）模擬的，演習的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>模擬考試（mocks）；<舊>嘲笑物件，笑柄；嘲笑；模仿，仿造（品）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"虛假地，不誠實地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mocks</b> you, they show or pretend that they think you are foolish or inferior, for example by saying something funny about you, or by imitating your behaviour. 嘲笑; (為了取笑) 模仿","examples":["I thought you were mocking me. 我以為你在嘲笑我。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>mock</b> to describe something which is not real or genuine, but which is intended to be very similar to the real thing. 假裝的","examples":["\"It's tragic!\" swoons Jeffrey in mock horror. “太悲慘了！”傑弗裡假裝害怕得昏了過去。"]}]}]},"moss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"苔蘚，蘚類植物；苔蘚綠（moss green）；（蘇格蘭，北英格蘭）沼澤（尤指泥炭沼）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"長滿苔蘚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Moss</b> is a very small, soft, green plant which grows on damp soil, or on wood or stone. 青苔","examples":["...ground covered over with moss. …長滿青苔的地面。"]}]}]},"monarch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"君主，女王；黑脈金斑蝶；王鶲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>monarch</b> of a country is the king, queen, emperor, or empress. 君主","examples":[]}]}]},"motherhood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"母親身份，母性；母親們（總稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Motherhood</b> is the state of being a mother. 母親身份","examples":["...women who try to combine work and motherhood. …試圖兼顧工作又當好母親的女性們。"]}]}]},"mode":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"方式，做法；（機器、裝置的）執行方式，狀態；（衣著、藝術等的）形式，風格；<非正式>（思想、情感或行為的）狀態，狀況；（音樂的）調式；眾數（一組數字中出現次數最多的數）；（邏）（模態命題的）式，形式；（物理）模（式），波型；（模態命題的）式，形式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mode</b> of life or behaviour is a particular way of living or behaving. (生活或行為) 方式","examples":["...the capitalist mode of production. …資本主義的生產方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mode</b> is a particular style in art, literature, or dress. (文學、藝術或穿著等的) 風格","examples":["...a slightly more elegant and formal mode of dress. …略顯雅緻和正式的著裝風格。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On some cameras or electronic devices, the different <b>modes</b> available are the different programmes or settings that you can choose when you use them. 模式","examples":["...when the camera is in manual mode. …照相機處於手動模式時。"]}]}]},"molecule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分子，摩爾；少量，一點兒；微小顆粒，微粒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>molecule</b> is the smallest amount of a chemical substance which can exist by itself. 分子","examples":["...the hydrogen bonds between water molecules. …水分子之間的氫連線。"]}]}]},"mortal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"終有一死的，不能永生的；極其嚴重的，致命的；至死方休的，不共戴天的；極度的，極其強烈的；死的，臨死的；（因罪孽深重而）靈魂無法得救的，不能蒙神恩得寬恕的；<非正式>想像得出的，可能；世間的，凡人的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"凡人，普通人；地位（或能力）不如他人者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the fact that people are <b>mortal</b>, you mean that they have to die and cannot live forever. 終有一死的","examples":["A man is deliberately designed to be mortal. He grows, he ages, and he dies. 人是被故意設計成終歸一死的。成長，變老，然後死去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>mortal</b> to show that something is very serious or may cause death. 致命的","examples":["The police were defending themselves and others against mortal danger. 警察在保衛他們自己和其他人免受致命的危險。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>mortal</b> to emphasize that a feeling is extremely great or severe. 極度的","examples":["When self-esteem is high, we lose our mortal fear of jealousy. 當自尊心很強時，我們會失去對嫉妒的極度恐懼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"終有一死","examples":["She has suddenly come face to face with her own mortality. 突然，她已經與死神面對面了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone as a <b>mortal</b> when you want to say that they are an ordinary person. 凡人","examples":["Tickets seem unobtainable to the ordinary mortal. 票對於普通大眾來說似乎是得不到的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"致命地","examples":["He falls, mortally wounded. 他摔了，傷得很重。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"極度地","examples":["Candace admits to having been \"mortally embarrassed.\" 坎達絲承認曾經“極其尷尬”。"]}]}]},"mistress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>女教師；（奴僕的）女主人；（寵物的）女主人；絕對控制……的女人，主宰……的女人；（精通某項活動的）女能手，女行家；女士（用作女子姓氏或姓名前的稱呼）；<英>女院長 (Mistress)；情婦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A married man's <b>mistress</b> is a woman who is not his wife and with whom he is having a sexual relationship. 情婦","examples":["Tracy was his mistress for three years. 特蕾西給他做了3年情婦。"]}]}]},"mower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"割草機，剪草機；割草的人；（農業）刈草機；（Mower）人名，音譯莫厄爾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mower</b> is the same as a . 割草機","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mower</b> is a machine that has sharp blades for cutting something such as corn or wheat. 收割機","examples":[]}]}]},"mound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"土堆，石堆；（棒球場中的）投球區土墩；一大堆，大量；（有時指為防禦或埋葬而人為構築的）土堤，土墩；小山丘；小山崗"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把……攏成堆；<古>用土堤圍，用土堤加固"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mound</b> of something is a large, rounded pile of it. 堆","examples":["The bulldozers piled up huge mounds of dirt. 推土機推起一堆堆泥土。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In baseball, the <b>mound</b> is the raised area where the pitcher stands when he or she throws the ball. (棒球運動中的) 投球區土墩","examples":["He went to the mound to talk with a struggling pitcher who spoke only Spanish. 他走到投球區土墩和一名只講西班牙語、奮力拼搏的投手交談。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a small natural hill 小山岡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to gather into a mound; heap 成堆; 堆積","examples":[]}]}]},"motive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動機，目的，原因；（文藝作品、音樂的）藝術思想，主題"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"引起運動的，起推動作用的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使產生動機，激起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>motive</b> for doing something is your reason for doing it. 動機","examples":["Police have ruled out robbery as a motive for the killing. 警方已排除了搶劫是殺人的動機。"]}]}]},"mutter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘀咕，嘟囔；（私下）抱怨，發牢騷"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘀咕，嘟囔；私下抱怨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mutter</b>, you speak very quietly so that you cannot easily be heard, often because you are complaining about something. 輕聲說話; 小聲抱怨","examples":["\"God knows,\" she muttered, \"what's happening in that madman's mind.\" “天知道，”她低聲抱怨，“那個瘋子腦子裡正在想什麼。”","She can hear the old woman muttering about consideration. 她能聽見這老婦人低聲說要考慮考慮。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mutter</b> is also a noun. 輕聲低語; 小聲抱怨","examples":["They make no more than a mutter of protest. 他們不過是小聲抗議了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"喃喃細語","examples":["He heard muttering from the front of the crowd. 他聽到人群前面傳來喃喃低語。"]}]}]},"mumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"含糊地說，咕噥；（用無齒的牙床）費力嚼咬，咬磨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"喃喃自語，嘟噥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mumble</b>, you speak very quietly and not at all clearly with the result that the words are difficult to understand. 咕噥","examples":["Her grandmother mumbled in her sleep. 她祖母睡覺時咕噥了。","He mumbled a few words. 他咕噥了幾句。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mumble</b> is also a noun. 咕噥","examples":["He could hear the low mumble of Navarro's voice. 他能聽到納瓦羅的低聲咕噥。"]}]}]},"mutton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"羊肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mutton</b> is meat from an adult sheep that is eaten as food. 羊肉","examples":["...a leg of mutton. …一條羊腿。"]}]}]},"muse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靈感，激發創作靈感的人；繆斯（古希臘神話中掌管藝術或科學的九位女神之一）（Muse）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"沉思，冥想；沉思地說；若有所思地凝視（muse on）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>muse</b> on something, you think about it, usually saying or writing what you are thinking at the same time. 揣摩","examples":["Many of the papers muse on the fate of the president. 許多報紙在揣測總統的命運。","\"As a whole,\" she muses, \"the `organized church' turns me off.\" “總的來說，”她若有所思地說，“‘組織嚴密的教會’讓我厭煩。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沉思","examples":["His musings were interrupted by Montagu who came and sat down next to him. 蒙塔古來到他旁邊坐下時，他的思緒被打斷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a goddess that inspires a creative artist, esp a poet (尤指給詩人帶來靈感的)女神; 創作女神","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of nine sister goddesses, each of whom was regarded as the protectress of a different art or science. Daughters of Zeus and Mnemosyne, the nine are Calliope, Clio, Erato, Euterpe, Melpomene, Polyhymnia, Terpsichore, Thalia, and Urania 繆斯; 九位文藝和科學保護女神的通稱，宙斯和記憶女神摩涅莫辛涅的女兒","examples":[]}]}]},"mount":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"組織，開展；爬上，登上；騎上；增多，增加，上升；增強，加劇；鑲嵌，裱貼，安置；上演，展出；爬上（雌性動物的背）進行交配；設定（崗哨），擔任（警衛）；把（觀察物件）固定於顯微鏡的載玻片"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"山，山峰；坐騎，馬；登，騎；（相片）框，（藝術品）裝幀，襯托紙；底座，底架；（貼郵票用的）透明膠紙；（顯微鏡觀察的）封片；掌丘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mount</b> a campaign or event, you organize it and make it take place. 組織; 發動","examples":["The ANC announced it was mounting a major campaign of mass political protests. 非國大宣佈正在發動一場大型群眾性政治抗議運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mount</b> the stairs or a platform, you go up the stairs or go up onto the platform. 登上","examples":["Larry was mounting the stairs up into the attic. 拉里正在拾級而上到閣樓去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>mount</b> a horse or motorcycle, you climb on to it so that you can ride it. 騎上","examples":["A man in a crash helmet was mounting a motorcycle. 一個戴著防撞頭盔的男子正騎上一輛摩托車。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>mount</b> an object <b>on</b> something, you fix it there firmly. 安裝","examples":["Her husband mounts the work on velour paper and makes the frame. 她丈夫把作品裝裱到絲絨紙上，又做了框架。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>mount</b> an exhibition or display, you organize and present it. 舉辦","examples":["The gallery has mounted an exhibition of art by Irish women painters. 這家畫廊已經舉辦過一次愛爾蘭女畫家們的藝術作品展。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>mounts</b>, it increases in intensity. 增強","examples":["For several hours, tension mounted. 幾個小時中，緊張局勢加劇了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>mounts</b>, it increases in quantity. 增加","examples":["The uncollected rubbish mounts in city streets. 城市街道中未被收集的垃圾增多。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mount up</b> means the same as to . 增加","examples":["Her medical bills mounted up. 她的醫療賬單越來越多。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"安裝在…上的","examples":["She installed a wall-mounted electric fan. 她裝了一臺牆壁式電扇。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名稱內的名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mount</b> is used as part of the name of a mountain. (冠于山名之前) 山","examples":["...Mount Everest. …珠穆朗瑪峰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a backing, setting, or support onto which something is fixed (固定東西的)背板; 底座; 支架","examples":[]}]}]},"myth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯誤的觀點，荒誕的說法；神話，神話故事；虛構的人（或事），想象中的人（或事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>myth</b> is a well-known story which was made up in the past to explain natural events or to justify religious beliefs or social customs. 神話","examples":["There is a famous Greek myth in which Icarus flew too near to the Sun. 一個著名的希臘神話中說，伊卡洛斯飛得離太陽太近了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a belief or explanation as a <b>myth</b>, you mean that many people believe it but it is actually untrue. 謬見","examples":["Contrary to the popular myth, women are not reckless spendthrifts. 與盛行的謬見相反，女人們並非揮霍無度。"]}]}]},"newscast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞廣播，新聞節目"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>newscast</b> is a news programme that is broadcast on the radio or on television. 新聞廣播","examples":[]}]}]},"mustard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"芥末醬；芥末黃，深黃色；芥菜；強烈的興趣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mustard</b> is a yellow or brown paste usually eaten with meat. It tastes hot and spicy. 芥末醬","examples":["...a jar of mustard. …一罐芥末醬。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mustard</b> is used to describe things that are brownish yellow in colour. 褐黃色 (的)","examples":["I sat in my father's chair, a mustard-coloured recliner. 我坐在父親的椅子上，一把褐黃色的躺椅。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone does not <b>cut the mustard</b>, their work or their performance is not as good as it should be or as good as it is expected to be. 未能達到要求; 不如所期待地那麼好","examples":["He just wasn't a good student. He wasn't cutting the mustard and we let him go. 他不是什麼好學生。不合格，我們就讓他走了。"]}]}]},"nag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛嘮叨的人，挑剔的人；老馬，疲憊的馬；競賽馬；（Nag）人名：納吉（查德）、納（緬甸）、納格（印度）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不斷地嘮叨，嘮叨催促，不斷要求；（疑慮、擔憂等）煩擾，困擾，使煩惱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>nags</b> you, or if they <b>nag</b>, they keep asking you to do something you have not done yet or do not want to do. 嘮叨催促","examples":["The more Sarah nagged her, the more stubborn Cissie became. 薩拉越是對她嘮叨不休，茜茜就越是固執。","My girlfriend nagged me to cut my hair. 我女朋友嘮叨著催我去理髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a doubt or worry <b>nags</b> <b>at</b> you, or <b>nags</b> you, it keeps worrying you. 煩擾","examples":["He could be wrong about her. The feeling nagged at him. 他可能錯怪她了。這種感覺煩擾著他。","...the anxiety that had nagged Amy all through lunch. …煩擾了埃米整個午餐時間的焦慮情緒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nag</b> is someone who nags. 嘮叨催促的人","examples":["Aunt Molly is a nag about regular meals. 莫莉姨媽是個對一日三餐絮絮叨叨的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嘮叨催促","examples":["Her endless nagging drove him away from home. 她無休止的嘮叨催促迫使他離開了家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a horse 馬","examples":[]}]}]},"nightingale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夜鶯；奈廷格爾（英語姓氏 Nightingale 的音譯）；南丁格爾（常指英國護士、現代護理事業先驅弗洛倫斯·南丁格爾，1820—1910）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nightingale</b> is a small brown bird. The male, which can be heard at night, sings beautifully. 夜鶯","examples":[]}]}]},"nostril":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼻孔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>nostrils</b> are the two openings at the end of your nose. 鼻孔","examples":["Keeping your mouth closed, breathe in through your nostrils. 把嘴閉著，用鼻孔吸氣。"]}]}]},"nickel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（金屬）鎳；（美國或加拿大的）五分硬幣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鍍鎳於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nickel</b> is a silver-coloured metal that is used in making steel. 鎳","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In the United States and Canada, a <b>nickel</b> is a coin worth five cents. (美國和加拿大的) 五分鎳幣","examples":["...a large glass jar filled with pennies, nickels, dimes, and quarters. …一個裝滿1分、5分、10分和25分硬幣的大玻璃罐。"]}]}]},"nibble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啃，小口咬；反覆輕咬；（對提議或想法）略顯興趣；蠶食；（動物）小口地啃"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一小口；<非正式>（常為聚會上提供的）點心，小吃（nibbles）；<非正式>對商業機會感興趣的表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nibble</b> food, you eat it by biting very small pieces of it, for example because you are not very hungry. 小口地吃","examples":["Linda lay face down on a living room couch, nibbling popcorn. 琳達趴在客廳的一張沙發上，小口吃著爆米花。","She nibbled at a piece of dry toast. 她小口啃著一片乾麵包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>nibble</b> something, you bite it very gently. 輕咬","examples":["John found he was kissing and nibbling her ear. 約翰發覺他正輕輕吻咬她的耳朵。","Daniel nibbled on his pen. 丹尼爾輕輕咬著他的鋼筆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When an animal <b>nibbles</b> something, it takes small bites of it quickly and repeatedly. (動物) 啃啄","examples":["A herd of goats was nibbling the turf around the base of the tower. 一群山羊正在啃著塔基周圍的草皮。","The birds nibble at the brickwork. 鳥兒們啄著磚牆。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nibble</b> is also a noun. 一小口","examples":["We each took a nibble. 我們每人吃了一小口。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nibble away</b> means the same as . 啃啄","examples":["The rabbits nibbled away on the herbaceous plants. 野兔把那些草本植物慢慢啃光了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Nibble away</b> means the same as . 逐步的破壞影響","examples":["Several manufacturers are also nibbling away at Ford's traditional customer base. 幾家製造商也正在蠶食福特公司傳統的客戶基礎。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>nibbles</b> <b>at</b> another, it gradually affects, harms, or destroys it. 逐漸影響; 逐漸破壞","examples":["It was all going according to plan, yet small doubts kept nibbling at the edges of his mind. 一切都在按計劃進行，只是一些小小的疑慮一直在折磨著他。"]}]}]},"notable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"顯要的，值得注意的；非常成功的，令人尊敬的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"顯要人物，名流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>notable</b> is important or interesting. 值得注意的; 有趣的","examples":["The proposed new structure is notable not only for its height, but for its shape. 那座提議的新建築值得注意，不僅因其高度，還因其外形。","Mo did not want to be ruled by anyone and it is notable that she never allowed the men in her life to eclipse her. 莫不想被任何人管制，很顯然，她從不允許她生活中的男性使她黯然失色。"]}]}]},"novice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"初學者，新手；見習修士，見習修女；尚未贏過大賽的賽馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>novice</b> is someone who has been doing a job or other activity for only a short time and so is not experienced at it. 新手","examples":["I'm a novice at these things, Lieutenant. You're the professional. 在這些事情上我是一名新手，中尉。你是行家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a monastery or convent, a <b>novice</b> is a person who is preparing to become a monk or nun. 見習修士; 見習修女","examples":[]}]}]},"oar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"櫓，槳；槳手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>划槳，做划槳動作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oars</b> are long poles with a wide, flat blade at one end which are used for rowing a boat. 槳","examples":[]}]}]},"notion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"概念，想法；縫紉用品；一時的念頭，突發的奇想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>notion</b> is an idea or belief about something. 想法","examples":["We each have a notion of just what kind of person we'd like to be. 我們每個人都對自己要做個什麼樣的人有各自的想法。","I reject absolutely the notion that privatization of our industry is now inevitable. 我絕不接受我們的產業私有化在當今是不可避免的這種看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Notions</b> are small articles for sewing, such as buttons, zips, and thread. 縫紉用的雜物 (如釦子、拉鎖、線等)","examples":[]}]}]},"nucleus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"原子核；細胞核；核心，中心；神經核；（彗星的）核"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>nucleus</b> of an atom or cell is the central part of it. (原子或細胞) 核","examples":["Neutrons and protons are bound together in the nucleus of an atom. 在一個原子的核內，中子和質子聚合在一起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>nucleus</b> <b>of</b> a group of people or things is the small number of members which form the most important part of the group. 核心","examples":["Matt Cummings and Liko Soules-Ono form the nucleus of the team. 馬特·卡明斯和萊克·索爾斯-奧諾形成了這個團隊的核心。"]}]}]},"nude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"裸體的，赤裸的；肉色的；光禿的，無裝飾的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"裸體人像，人物裸體作品；肉色，裸色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nude</b> person is not wearing any clothes. 裸體的","examples":["The occasional nude bather comes here. 偶爾裸浴的那個人來到這裡 。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>in the nude</b>, you are not wearing any clothes. If you paint or draw someone <b>in the nude</b>, they are not wearing any clothes. 裸體中","examples":["Sleeping in the nude, if it suits you, is not a bad idea. 如果適合你的話，光著身子睡覺並不是一個壞主意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nude</b> is a picture or statue of a person who is not wearing any clothes. A <b>nude</b> is also a person in a picture who is not wearing any clothes. 裸體畫; 裸體雕像; 畫像中裸體的人","examples":["He was one of Australia's most distinguished artists, renowned for his portraits, landscapes, and nudes. 他是澳大利亞最傑出的藝術家之一，以肖像畫、風景畫和裸體畫而聞名。"]}]}]},"oblong":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"長方形的，矩形的；橢圓形的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"長方形（物體）；橢圓形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oblong</b> is a shape which has two long sides and two short sides and in which all the angles are right angles. 長方形","examples":["...an oblong table. ...一張長方形桌子。"]}]}]},"oatmeal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>燕麥粥，麥片粥，燕麥糊；燕麥片，燕麥粉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oatmeal</b> is a kind of flour made by crushing oats. 燕麥粉","examples":["...oatmeal cookies. …燕麥小甜餅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Oatmeal</b> is a thick sticky food made from oats cooked in water or milk and eaten hot, especially for breakfast. 燕麥糊","examples":[]}]}]},"oasis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（沙漠中的）綠洲；（困苦中）令人快慰的地方（或時刻），樂事；（商標）（插花時將花莖插牢於其中的）插花泥（Oasis）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oasis</b> is a small area in a desert where water and plants are found. (沙漠中的) 綠洲","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a pleasant place or situation as an <b>oasis</b> when it is surrounded by unpleasant ones. 綠洲般的地方","examples":["The immaculately tended gardens are an oasis in the midst of Cairo's urban sprawl. 那些打理得非常整潔的花園是雜亂擴張的開羅市區中的一片綠洲。"]}]}]},"oath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誓言，誓約；（在法庭上的）誓詞；詛咒，咒罵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oath</b> is a formal promise, especially a promise to be loyal to a person or country. (尤指忠於某人或國家的) 誓言; 宣誓","examples":["He took an oath of loyalty to the government. 他做了效忠於政府的宣誓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a court of law, when someone takes <b>the</b> <b>oath</b>, they make a formal promise to tell the truth. You can say that someone is <b>under oath</b> when they have made this promise. (在法庭上的) 宣誓","examples":["His girlfriend had gone into the witness box and taken the oath. 他的女朋友已進了證人席並宣了誓。","Under oath, Andy finally admitted that he had lied. 宣誓之後，安迪終於承認他曾撒了謊。"]}]}]},"octopus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"章魚；章魚肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>octopus</b> is a soft sea creature with eight long arms called tentacles which it uses to catch food. 章魚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Octopus</b> is this creature eaten as food. 章魚肉","examples":["...plates of octopus. …一盤盤章魚肉。"]}]}]},"occurrence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發生的事，事件；發生，出現（尤指意外且令人不快的事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>occurrence</b> is something that happens. 發生的事情","examples":["Complaints seemed to be an everyday occurrence. 投訴似乎成了天天發生的事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The occurrence of</b> something is the fact that it happens or is present. (某事物的) 發生; 存在","examples":["The greatest occurrence of coronary heart disease is in those over 65. 冠心病的最高發病率在65歲以上的人群中。"]}]}]},"odor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣味（美國英語，英國英語作 odour，尤指難聞的氣味）；名聲，聲望（常用於 in good/bad odor 等搭配）；（Odor）人名，尤指匈牙利姓氏歐多爾"}],"sections":[]},"observer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀察者，目擊者；觀察家，評論員；（會議等的）觀察員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to someone who sees or notices something as an <b>observer</b>. 目擊者","examples":["A casual observer would have taken them to be three men out for an evening stroll. 一位不經意的目擊者會認為他們是晚上出來閒逛的3個男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>observer</b> is someone who studies current events and situations, especially in order to comment on them and predict what will happen next. 觀察家","examples":["Observers say the events of the weekend seem to have increased support for the opposition. 觀察家們說週末事件似乎增加了對反對派的支援。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>observer</b> is a person who is sent to observe an important event or situation, especially in order to make sure it happens as it should, or to tell other people about it. 觀察員","examples":["The president suggested that a UN observer should attend the conference. 大會主席建議應該有一名聯合國觀察員參加該會議。"]}]}]},"organizer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組織者，主辦者，承辦單位；工會、政黨或社群等的組織者；個人記事簿，電子記事本（常作 personal organizer）；（生物學）組織導體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>organizer</b> of an event or activity is the person who makes sure that the necessary arrangements are made. 組織者","examples":["He became an organizer for the Democratic Party. 他成了民主黨的一名組織者。"]}]}]},"orchard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"果園；果樹林"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orchard</b> is an area of land on which fruit trees are grown. 果園","examples":[]}]}]},"olive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"橄欖；橄欖樹；橄欖色，黃綠色；燉牛肉卷；橄欖貝；（剖）橄欖體；（墊在螺母下擰緊以形成密封的）橄欖環"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"橄欖色的，茶青色的；（皮膚）橄欖色的，淺褐色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Olives</b> are small green or black fruits with a bitter taste. Olives are often pressed to make olive oil. 橄欖","examples":["...a pile of black olives. …一堆黑橄欖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>olive tree</b> or an <b>olive</b> is a tree on which olives grow. 橄欖樹","examples":["Olives look romantic on a hillside in Provence. 在普羅旺斯的一個山坡上橄欖樹看起來很浪漫。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>olive</b> is yellowish-green in colour. 橄欖色的","examples":["...glowing colours such as deep red, olive, saffron and ochre. …鮮豔顏色，如深紅色、橄欖色、橘黃色和赭石色。"]}]},{"pos":"comb in color.","pos_name":"與顏色結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Olive</b> is also a combining form. (用於構成表示顏色的複合詞) 橄欖色的","examples":["She wore an olive-green T-shirt. 她穿了一件橄欖綠的T恤衫。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has <b>olive</b> skin, the colour of their skin is yellowish brown. (皮膚) 黃褐色的","examples":["They are handsome with dark, shining hair, olive skin and fine brown eyes. 他們很帥，有著烏黑閃亮的頭髮，黃褐色的皮膚，迷人的棕色眼睛。"]}]}]},"opponent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對手，競爭者；反對者，阻止者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"對立的，敵對的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A politician's <b>opponents</b> are other politicians who belong to a different party or who have different aims or policies. (政) 敵","examples":["...Mr. Kennedy's opponent in the leadership contest. …肯尼迪先生在領導權競爭中的對手。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a sports contest, your <b>opponent</b> is the person who is playing against you. (體育比賽中的) 對手","examples":["Norris twice knocked down his opponent in the early rounds of the fight. 諾里斯在拳擊賽的頭幾個回合中，曾兩度擊倒他的對手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>opponents</b> <b>of</b> an idea or policy do not agree with it and do not want it to be carried out. 反對者","examples":["...opponents of the spread of nuclear weapons. …核武器擴散的反對者們。"]}]}]},"odds":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（事物發生的）可能性，機會；困難，不利條件；投注賠率；（力量、權力或資源上的）優勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You refer to how likely something is to happen as the <b>odds</b> that it will happen. 可能性","examples":["What are the odds of finding a parking space right outside the door? 就在門外找到一個停車位的可能性有多大？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In betting, <b>odds</b> are expressions with numbers such as \"10 to 1\" and \"7 to 2\" that show how likely something is thought to be, for example, how likely a particular horse is to lose or win a race. (賭博中的) 賠率","examples":["We are offering odds of 6-1 on the fight ending in a knockout. 我們以6比1的賠率賭該拳擊賽以擊倒告終。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>at odds</b> with someone else, or if two people are <b>at odds</b>, they are disagreeing or arguing with each other. (與某人) 不合","examples":["He was at odds with the boss. 他與老闆不合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that <b>the odds are against</b> something or someone, you mean that they are unlikely to succeed. (某人、某事物) 不大可能成功","examples":["He reckons the odds are against the plan going ahead. 他認為該計劃不太可能進行下去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something happens <b>against</b> all <b>odds</b>, it happens or succeeds although it seemed impossible or very unlikely. 貌似不可能 (卻發生或成功)","examples":["...families in terrible circumstances, who have stayed together against all odds. …狀況糟糕的家庭，似乎不可能維持下去，卻仍然住在一起。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that <b>the odds are in</b> someone's <b>favour</b>, you mean that they are likely to succeed in what they are doing. (某人) 可能會成功","examples":["The troops will only engage in a ground battle when all the odds are in their favour. 該部隊只會在完全可能取勝的情況下進行一場地面戰鬥。"]}]}]},"optimism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樂觀；樂觀主義"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Optimism</b> is the feeling of being hopeful about the future or about the success of something in particular. 樂觀主義","examples":["The Indian prime minister has expressed optimism about India's future relations with the U.S. 印度總理表達了對未來印美關係的樂觀態度。"]}]}]},"orphanage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"孤兒院；<古>孤兒身份，孤兒狀態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>orphanage</b> is a place where orphans live and are cared for. 孤兒院","examples":[]}]}]},"oriental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"東方（尤指中國和日本）的，東方人的；（動物學）（與）東方界（有關）的（Oriental）；（珍珠或其他珠寶）有光澤的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>東方人（=Oriental）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oriental</b> means coming from or associated with eastern Asia, especially China and Japan. 東方的 (尤指中國和日本的)","examples":["There were Oriental carpets on the floors. 地板上鋪著東方的地毯。"]}]}]},"orient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"朝向，面對，使適合；定向放置（某物）；確定方位，認識方向（orient oneself）；引導；使熟悉，幫助適應"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>東方，東亞諸國（the Orient）；（優質珍珠的）光澤；優質珍珠"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<文>東方的，東方國家的；（尤指寶石）光彩奪目的；（太陽等）冉冉上升的，（白晝的光亮等）漸漸變強的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>orient</b> <b>yourself to</b> a new situation or course of action, you learn about it and prepare to deal with it. 適應","examples":["You will need the time to orient yourself to your new way of eating. 你需要時間適應新的吃法。"]}]}]},"ostrich":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鴕鳥；逃避現實的人，不願正視現實者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ostrich</b> is a very large, long-necked African bird that cannot fly. 鴕鳥","examples":[]}]}]},"ornament":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"裝飾品，點綴品；<正式>裝飾，擺設；<正式>首飾，飾物； 為……增添光彩的人（或事物）（ornament to sth.）；（樂）裝飾音（ornaments） ；（基督教）（聖壇、聖餐杯和聖器等）禮拜用品，典禮用品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝飾，點綴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ornament</b> is an attractive object that you display in your home or in your garden. 裝飾品","examples":["...a shelf containing a few photographs and ornaments. …一個放有幾張照片和幾件裝飾品的架子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Decorations and patterns on a building or a piece of furniture can be referred to as <b>ornament</b>. (建築、傢俱上的) 裝飾","examples":["...walls of glass overlaid with ornament. …覆有裝飾的玻璃牆。"]}]}]},"outskirts":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"市郊，郊區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The outskirts</b> <b>of</b> a city or town are the parts of it that are farthest away from its centre. (市、鎮的) 外圍地帶","examples":["Hours later we reached the outskirts of New York. 數小時後我們到達了紐約市的外圍地帶。"]}]}]},"ounce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盎司（重量單位，1盎司約等於28克）；一點點，少量；雪豹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ounce</b> is a unit of weight used in the U.S. and Britain. There are sixteen ounces in a pound and one ounce is equal to 28.35 grams. 盎司","examples":["...four ounces of sugar. …4盎司的糖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a very small amount of something, such as a quality or characteristic, as an <b>ounce</b>. 一點點","examples":["If only my father had possessed an ounce of business sense. 要是我父親有一點點商業頭腦就好了。"]}]}]},"outsider":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"局外人， 外人；（組織、行業）外部的人，外來者；（比賽中）不大可能獲勝的人（或動物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outsider</b> is someone who does not belong to a particular group or organization. (不屬於某組織或團體的) 外部人士","examples":["The most likely outcome may be to subcontract much of the work to an outsider. 最有可能的結果是把大量工作分包給外部人員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>outsider</b> is someone who is not accepted by a particular group, or who feels that they do not belong in it. (未被某組織接受或自感不屬其內的) 外人","examples":["Malone, a cop, felt as much an outsider as any of them. 馬隆，一個警察，跟他們中任何人一樣感到自己是個外人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a competition, an <b>outsider</b> is a competitor who is unlikely to win. (在比賽中) 無望獲勝者","examples":["He was an outsider in the race to be the new UN Secretary-General. 他在本屆新聯合國秘書長的角逐中是無望獲勝者。"]}]}]},"overwork":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）工作過度，（使）過度勞累；對……使用過度，濫用"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"勞累過度，過勞；過量工作，過於繁重的工作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>overwork</b> or if someone <b>overworks</b> you, you work too hard, and are likely to become very tired or sick. 使工作過度; 工作過度","examples":["He's overworking and has a lot on his mind. 他在過度工作，有許多事要操心。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overwork</b> is also a noun. 過度工作","examples":["He died of a heart attack brought on by overwork. 他死於過度工作導致的一次心臟病發作。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"過度工作的","examples":["...an overworked doctor. …一位過度工作的醫生。"]}]}]},"output":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"產量，作品；產生，生產過程；輸出功率；（計算機的）輸出資訊；輸出端"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"輸出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Output</b> is used to refer to the amount of something that a person or thing produces. 產量","examples":["Government statistics show the largest drop in industrial output for ten years. 政府的統計數字顯示出10年來工業產量最大幅度的下降。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>output</b> of a computer or word processor is the information that it displays on a screen or prints on paper as a result of a particular program. (計算機或文書處理機的) 輸出資訊","examples":["You run the software, you look at the output, you make modifications. 執行這個軟體，看看輸出資訊，並做修改。"]}]}]},"oyster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牡蠣，蠔；牡蠣白；（雞脊骨兩邊的）蠔狀雞背肉；<非正式>沉默寡言的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"養殖（或採撈、採集）牡蠣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>oyster</b> is a large flat shellfish. Some oysters can be eaten and others produce valuable objects called pearls. 牡蠣","examples":["He had two dozen oysters and enjoyed every one of them. 他吃了兩打牡蠣，每一個都吃得津津有味。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that <b>the world is</b> someone's <b>oyster</b>, you mean that they can do anything or go anywhere that they want to. 某人可以隨心所欲","examples":["You're young, you've got a lot of opportunity. The world is your oyster. 你年輕，又得到了很多機會。你可以隨心所欲地施展自己。"]}]}]},"overall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"總的，全面的；所有的，包括一切的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"全部，總共； 總的說來，大體上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（工作時穿的）罩衣；<英>（上下連身的）工作服，防護服（overalls）；<美>揹帶工裝褲（overalls）；<英>騎馬褲，緊身制服褲（overalls）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>overall</b> to indicate that you are talking about a situation in general or about the whole of something. 總的","examples":["...the overall rise in unemployment. …失業人數的總體上升。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overall</b> is also an adverb. 總體上地","examples":["Overall I was disappointed. 總的來說，我感到失望。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overalls</b> are trousers that are attached to a piece of cloth which covers your chest and which has straps going over your shoulders. 工裝褲","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Overalls</b> consist of a single piece of clothing that combines trousers and a jacket. You wear overalls over your clothes in order to protect them while you are working. (連體的) 防護服","examples":["...a man in white overalls. ...一個穿白色防護服的男人。"]}]}]},"ozone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臭氧；（尤指海邊的）清新空氣；臭氧層（ozone layer 的簡寫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ozone</b> is a colourless gas which is a form of oxygen. There is a layer of ozone high above the Earth's surface, that protects us from harmful radiation from the sun. 臭氧","examples":["What they find could provide clues to what might happen worldwide if ozone depletion continues. 如果臭氧的損耗繼續下去，他們的發現能為全世界可能發生的情況提供線索。"]}]}]},"overflow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"漫出，氾濫 ；充滿，擠滿；裝滿，完全蓋住；擴充套件出界，過度延伸；洋溢著（情感）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"溢位，溢位的液體；容納不下的人（或物）；溢流管（=overflow pipe）；（計算機）資料過載"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid or a river <b>overflows</b>, it flows over the edges of the container or place it is in. 溢位; 漫出","examples":["Pour in some of the broth, but not all of it, because it will probably overflow. 倒入部分肉湯，不要全部，因為很可能會溢位來。","The rivers overflowed their banks. 那些河裡的水漫過了河岸。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or container <b>is overflowing</b> <b>with</b> people or things, it is too full of them. 擠滿","examples":["Schreiber addressed an auditorium overflowing with journalists. 施賴伯向擠滿了新聞記者的觀眾席致辭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>overflow</b> is the extra people or things that something cannot contain or deal with because it is not large enough. (因空間所限) 無法容納或安頓下的人或物","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or container is filled <b>to overflowing</b>, it is so full of people or things that no more can fit in. 滿滿地","examples":["The kitchen garden was full to overflowing with fresh vegetables. 菜園裡長滿了新鮮的蔬菜。"]}]}]},"pane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（窗戶或門上的）一塊玻璃；（計算機）窗片，子視窗；整張郵票；邊，面；嵌板；窗格"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用錘頭敲打使（金屬片）彎曲（同 peen）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pane</b> of glass is a flat sheet of glass in a window or door. (門、窗上的) 一塊 (玻璃)","examples":["I watch my reflection in a pane of glass. 我在一塊玻璃裡看著我的映像。"]}]}]},"pacific":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"太平洋（the Pacific）；車輪4-6-2排列的蒸汽機車，“太平洋”號機車"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"太平洋的（Pacific）；愛和平的，息事寧人的；平靜的，寧靜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pacific</b> person, country, or course of action is peaceful or has the aim of bringing about peace. 溫和的","examples":["Gorbachev was less pacific than people thought. 戈爾巴喬夫不像人們想得那樣溫和。"]}]}]},"packet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>包裝盒，包裝袋；<英>（扁平的）小包裹；<美>（通常內容物僅夠用一次的）小袋，小包（=sachet）；<美>檔案包；資訊包，資料包；<英，非正式>一筆鉅款；<英>男性的性器官"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把..……打包"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An information <b>packet</b> is a set of information about a particular subject that is given to people who are interested in that subject. (資訊) 包","examples":["Call us for a free information packet that tells you more. 打電話給我們索要為你提供更多資訊的免費資訊包。","...a 23-page packet of topics to be discussed. …一份23頁的需要討論的主題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>packet</b> is a small container in which a quantity of something is sold. Packets are either small boxes made of thin cardboard, or bags or envelopes made of paper or plastic. 小盒子; 包裝袋","examples":["...sugar packets. …糖盒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>packet</b> to refer to a packet and its contents, or to the contents only. 包裹","examples":[]}]}]},"paddle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（小船的）短槳，槳；槳狀工具，槳狀物；划槳；<美>（乒乓球的）球拍；<美，非正式>扁條刑杖；（明輪船驅動所用的）輪葉，明輪翼；<英>赤腳涉水，蹚水；（飛船上伸出的）太陽能電池板；（心臟起搏用的）電極棒；鰭狀前肢"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用槳劃（船）；在……上划船；<英>蹚水，赤足涉水；（游泳時快速）撥水；<美，非正式>用戒尺打（孩子）；攪拌，混合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>paddle</b> is a short pole with a wide flat part at one end or at both ends. You hold it in your hands and use it as an oar to move a small boat through water. 短槳","examples":["We might be able to push ourselves across with the paddle. 我們或許可以自己划槳過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the act of paddling in water 在水窪裡踩過","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>paddle</b> is a specially shaped piece of wood that is used for hitting the ball in table tennis. 乒乓球拍","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>paddle</b> a boat, you move it through water using a paddle. 用槳劃","examples":["...the skills you will use to paddle the canoe. …你將使用到的劃獨木舟的技巧。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to walk or play barefoot in shallow water, mud, etc 赤腳踩(水窪)","examples":[]}]}]},"participant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"參加者，參與者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"參與的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>participants</b> in an activity are the people who take part in it. 參加者","examples":["40 of the course participants are offered employment with the company. 參加課程學習的人中有40名得到了在該公司工作的機會。"]}]}]},"paradox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矛盾的人（或事物、情況）；似非而是的雋語，悖論；悖論修辭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe a situation as a <b>paradox</b> when it involves two or more facts or qualities that seem to contradict each other. 自相矛盾","examples":["The paradox is that the region's most dynamic economies have the most primitive financial systems. 矛盾的是，該地區最具活力的經濟體制有著最原始的金融體系。","The paradox of exercise is that while using a lot of energy it seems to generate more. 鍛鍊的矛盾之處在於消耗很多能量卻似乎又產生更多能量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>paradox</b> is a statement in which it seems that if one part of it is true, the other part of it cannot be true. 悖論","examples":["The story contains many levels of paradox. 這個故事包含很多層面的悖論。"]}]}]},"pastry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"油酥麵糰；酥皮糕點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pastry</b> is a food made from flour, fat, and water that is mixed together, rolled flat, and baked in the oven. It is used, for example, for making pies. 油酥麵糰","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pastry</b> is a small cake made with sweet pastry. 油酥糕點","examples":["...a wide range of cakes and pastries. …各種各樣的蛋糕和油酥糕點。"]}]}]},"pastime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"娛樂，消遣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pastime</b> is something that you do in your spare time because you enjoy it or are interested in it. 消遣","examples":["His favourite pastime is golf. 他最喜歡的消遣是打高爾夫。"]}]}]},"parlor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"客廳，會客室，起居室；業務室，店鋪，營業場所"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"客廳的，適於客廳使用的，室內的；只會空談的，紙上談兵的"}],"sections":[]},"particle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"微粒；極少量；粒子（原子的極微小成分，如電子、質子或中子）；（數）質點；（語法中的）小品詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>particle</b> <b>of</b> something is a very small piece or amount of it. 微粒; 極小量","examples":["...a particle of hot metal. …熱金屬微粒。","There is a particle of truth in his statement. 在他的宣告中只有極少的事實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In physics, a <b>particle</b> is a piece of matter smaller than an atom such as an electron or a proton. 粒子","examples":["...the sub-atomic particles that make up matter. …構成物質的次原子微粒。"]}]}]},"patriot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛國者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is a <b>patriot</b> loves their country and feels very loyal toward it. 愛國者","examples":["It has been suggested the founders were not true patriots but men out to protect their own interests. 有人指出建立者並非真正的愛國者，而是一些維護自己利益的人。"]}]}]},"parallel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平行的；相似的，同時發生的；（計算機）並行的；並聯的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或事物的）相似的手法，共同點；相似的人（或物）；（地球的）緯線，緯圈；（印刷）平行符號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與……相似；與……同時發生；與……並行；與……相當，比得上"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"與……平行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something has a <b>parallel</b>, it is similar to something else, but exists or happens in a different place or at a different time. If it has <b>no parallel</b> or is <b>without parallel</b>, it is not similar to anything else. (存在或發生在不同地點或不同時間的) 類似的事情","examples":["Readers familiar with military conflict will find a vague parallel to the Vietnam War. 熟悉軍事衝突的讀者們會發現一個和越南戰爭大致相似的事件。","It's an ecological disaster with no parallel anywhere else in the world. 這是一場世界其他任何地方均無等同的生態災難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there are <b>parallels</b> between two things, they are similar in some ways. 相似之處","examples":["Detailed study of folk music from a variety of countries reveals many close parallels. 對不同國家的民樂的詳細研究表明它們有很多相似之處。","There are significant parallels with the 1980s. 與20世紀80年代有顯著的相似之處。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>parallel</b> is an imaginary line round the earth that is parallel to the equator. Parallels are shown on maps. 緯線","examples":["...the area south of the 38th parallel. …38度緯線以南的地區。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>parallels</b> another, they happen at the same time or are similar, and often seem to be connected. 與…同時發生","examples":["Often there are emotional reasons paralleling the financial ones. 經濟原因的常常伴有情感原因。","His remarks paralleled those of the president. 他的評論與總統的評論相同。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Parallel</b> events or situations happen at the same time as one another, or are similar to one another. 同時發生的; 相似的","examples":["...parallel talks between the two countries' foreign ministers. …兩國外長之間相似的談話。","Their instincts do not always run parallel with ours. 他們的直覺並不總是與我們的同步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two lines, two objects, or two lines of movement are <b>parallel</b>, they are the same distance apart along their whole length. 平行的","examples":["...seventy-two ships, drawn up in two parallel lines. …72艘船，停靠成兩條平行線。","Remsen Street is parallel with Montague Street. 雷姆森大街與蒙塔古大街是平行的。"]}]}]},"peacock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（雄）孔雀；注重儀表和衣飾的男子，虛榮驕傲的男子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"炫耀，神氣活現地走"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>peacock</b> is a large bird. The male has a very large tail covered with blue and green spots, which it can spread out like a fan. 孔雀","examples":["...peacocks strutting slowly across the garden. ...孔雀在花園中趾高氣揚地走來走去。","...peacock feathers. ...孔雀翎。"]}]}]},"patron":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（藝術家的）贊助人，資助者；代言人，名義贊助人；（酒吧、旅館等的）主顧，顧客；（古羅馬）有權勢的保護人，庇護人；（古羅馬）已獲得自由的奴隸的原主人和保護人；<英>有聖職授予權的人（或機構）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>patron</b> is a person who supports and gives money to artists, writers, or musicians. (藝術家、作家、音樂家等的) 資助人","examples":["Catherine the Great was a patron of the arts and sciences. 凱瑟琳大帝是藝術和科學的贊助人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>patron</b> of a charity, group, or campaign is an important person who allows his or her name to be used for publicity. (慈善機構、團體、運動等的) 名譽贊助人","examples":["He has now become one of the patrons of the association. 他如今已成為該協會的名譽贊助人之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>patrons</b> of a place such as a bar or hotel are its customers. (酒吧、旅館等的) 顧客","examples":["Few patrons of a high-priced hotel can be led to expect anything other than luxury service. 高價旅館的顧客幾乎沒有人會被引導去期待奢侈服務以外的任何東西。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a man, who owns or manages a hotel, restaurant, or bar (旅店，餐館、酒吧等的)老闆","examples":[]}]}]},"patent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專利（權），專利證書；專利發明"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"受專利保護的，專利的；專利生產的，專利經銷的；顯而易見的，赤裸裸的；（寄生蟲感染）明顯的，顯著的；（脈管、導管或孔）開放的，不閉合的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得……的專利權；授予專利"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>patent</b> is an official right to be the only person or company allowed to make or sell a new product for a certain period of time. 專利","examples":["P&G applied for a patent on its cookies. 寶潔公司為其餅乾申請了專利。","He held a number of patents for his many innovations. 他為他的許多革新申請了幾項專利。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>patent</b> something, you obtain a patent for it. 得到…專利","examples":["He patented the idea that the atom could be split. 他得到了原子可以分裂的這個見解的專利。","The invention has been patented by the university. 那項發明已經由那所大學獲取了專利。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>patent</b> to describe something, especially something bad, in order to indicate in an emphatic way that you think its nature or existence is clear and obvious. 顯而易見的","examples":["This was patent nonsense. 這顯然是一派胡言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"open or available for inspection (esp in the phrase <b>letters patent</b>)  公開的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"顯而易見地","examples":["He made his displeasure patently obvious. 他清楚地表明瞭他的不悅。"]}]}]},"peddler":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小販，商販，沿街叫賣者；毒販；（思想、資訊等的）宣揚者，散佈者，傳播者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drug peddler</b> is a person who sells illegal drugs. 毒販","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>peddler</b> <b>of</b> information or ideas is someone who frequently expresses such ideas to other people. 宣揚者; 散佈者","examples":["...the peddlers of fear. ...恐懼的散佈者。"]}]}]},"patrol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巡邏，巡查；巡邏隊，巡邏車；童子軍小隊；<英>"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指士兵或員警）巡邏，巡查；（尤指威脅性）逛蕩，閒逛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When soldiers, police, or guards <b>patrol</b> an area or building, they move around it in order to make sure that there is no trouble there. 在…巡邏","examples":["Prison officers continued to patrol the grounds within the jail. 獄警們繼續在監獄內的場地裡巡邏。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Patrol</b> is also a noun. 巡邏","examples":["He failed to return from a patrol. 他沒能從一次巡邏中回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>patrol</b> is a group of soldiers or vehicles that are patrolling an area. 巡邏隊","examples":["Guerrillas attacked a patrol with hand grenades. 游擊隊用手榴彈襲擊了一支巡邏隊。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Soldiers, police, or guards who are <b>on patrol</b> are patrolling an area. 在巡邏","examples":["The army is now on patrol in Srinagar and a curfew has been imposed. 軍隊現在在斯利那加巡邏，宵禁也已實行。"]}]}]},"peasant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（舊時或貧窮國家的）農民，佃農；<非正式>沒教養的人，粗人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>peasant</b> is a poor person of low social status who works on the land; used to refer to people who live in countries where farming is still a common way of life. 農民","examples":["...the peasants in the Peruvian highlands. …秘魯高原地區的農民們。"]}]}]},"patch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"補丁，補片；（保護受傷眼睛的）眼罩；<美>（衣服上的）徽章，標識；藥膏，膠布；（與周圍部分不同的）斑，小塊；小片，碎片；（尤指園藝用的）一小塊地；熟悉的地方，家鄉；<非正式> 屬地，管轄地；一段時間；<史>（尤指17、18世紀婦女裝飾用的）飾顏片，美人斑；（軟體的）補丁程式；（電氣或電話的）臨時連線（線）；（電子樂器，尤指合成樂器中的）預設配置（或聲音）資料檔案，配音"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"修補，縫補；使出現斑塊；臨時連線，臨時接入（通訊系統）；（計算機）（用補丁對程式進行）修正，打補丁；解決；拼湊，匆匆製成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>patch</b> on a surface is a part of it that is different in appearance from the area around it. (與周圍不同的) 塊; 片","examples":["...the bald patch on the top of his head. …他頭頂上那塊禿斑。","There was a small patch of blue in the grey clouds. 烏雲中透著一小塊藍天。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>patch</b> <b>of</b> land is a small area of land where a particular plant or crop grows. 小塊田地","examples":["...a patch of land covered in forest. …一塊長著樹林的田地。","...the little vegetable patch in her backyard. …在她後院的小塊菜地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>patch</b> is a piece of material that you use to cover a hole in something. 補丁","examples":["...jackets with patches on the elbows. …肘部打著補丁的夾克。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>patch</b> is a small piece of material that you wear to cover an injured eye. (保護受傷眼睛的) 眼罩","examples":["She went to the hospital and found him lying down with a patch over his eye. 她去醫院看見他躺著，眼睛上蒙著眼罩。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>patch</b> is a piece of computer program code written as a temporary solution for dealing with a computer virus and distributed by the makers of the original program. (對付計算機病毒的) 補丁","examples":["Older machines will need a software patch to correct the date. 舊的機器需要軟體補丁來修正日期。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>patch</b> something that has a hole in it, you repair it by fastening a patch over the hole. 打補丁","examples":["He and Walker patched the barn roof. 他和沃克修補了那個穀倉的頂。","One of the mechanics took off the damaged tyre, and took it back to the station to be patched. 其中一個機械師取下受損輪胎，把它拿到站裡修補。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have or go through <b>a rough patch</b>, you have a lot of problems for a time. 一段艱難時期","examples":["His marriage was going through a rough patch. 他的婚姻正處於一段艱難時期。"]}]}]},"peek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偷看，窺視；微露出，探出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一瞥，偷偷地一看；（計算機）讀取資料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>peek at</b> something or someone, you take a quick look at them, often secretly. (常指偷偷地) 瞥一眼","examples":["On two occasions she had peeked at him through a crack in the wall. 有兩次她曾透過牆上的一個裂縫偷窺了他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Peek</b> is also a noun. 一瞥","examples":["Companies have been paying outrageous fees for a peek at the technical data. 各公司一直在為該技術資料的一窺支付驚人的費用。"]}]}]},"peck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啄，啄食；匆匆輕吻；緩慢而費力地用打字機打；<非正式>（馬）向前跌倒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"匆匆的輕吻；（鳥的）啄；配克（穀物、水果等的乾量單位，等於8夸脫）；啄痕"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a bird <b>pecks at</b> something or <b>pecks</b> something, it moves its beak forward quickly and bites at it. 啄; 啄食","examples":["It was winter and the sparrows were pecking at whatever they could find. 已是冬天了，麻雀們能找到什麼就啄食什麼。","Chickens pecked in the dust. 小雞們在塵土中啄食。","It pecked his leg. 它啄了他的腿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>peck</b> someone <b>on</b> the cheek, you give them a quick, light kiss. 快速輕吻","examples":["Elizabeth walked up to him and pecked him on the cheek. 伊麗莎白走近他，快速輕吻了他的臉頰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a quick light blow, esp from a bird's beak (快而輕的)一擊","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Peck</b> is also a noun. 快速輕吻","examples":["He gave me a little peck on the cheek. 他在我臉上輕輕一吻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a unit of dry measure equal to 8 quarts or one quarter of a bushel 配克; 計量單位，等於8夸脫或1／4蒲式耳","examples":[]}]}]},"performer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"表演者，演出者，演員；表現……的人（或事物），效能……的事物；（業績好或業績差的）公司，產品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>performer</b> is a person who acts, sings, or does other entertainment in front of audiences. 表演者","examples":["A performer plays classical selections on the violin. 一位表演者用小提琴演奏古典音樂選段。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>performer</b> when describing someone or something in a way that indicates how well they do a particular thing. 表現…者","examples":["Until 1987, Canada's industry had been the star performer. 直到1987年，加拿大的工業一直是明星產業。"]}]}]},"pessimism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"悲觀，悲觀情緒；（哲）悲觀主義"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pessimism</b> is the belief that bad things are going to happen. 悲觀主義","examples":["...universal pessimism about the economy. …對經濟形勢普遍的悲觀看法。"]}]}]},"peril":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巨大的危險，危難；（某活動或行為的）危險，問題"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>使有危險，使臨險境，危及"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Perils</b> are great dangers. 極大危險","examples":["...the perils of the sea. …海洋的嚴重危險。","In spite of great peril, I have survived. 儘管危險巨大，我還是活了下來。"]}]}]},"pilgrim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"朝聖者，香客；（Pilgrim）前輩清教徒移民；到某重要地點（或人物居所）參觀的人；<文>流浪者，旅客"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>漫遊，流浪；去朝聖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pilgrims</b> are people who journey to a holy place for a religious reason. 朝聖者","examples":["This is where pilgrims to the abbey would pay their first devotions. 這兒就是來此修道院的朝聖者做第一次祈禱的地方。"]}]}]},"personnel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司、組織或軍隊中的）全體人員，員工；人事部門"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人員的，有關人事的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>personnel</b> of an organization are the people who work for it. 人員","examples":["Since 1954 Japan has never dispatched military personnel abroad. 自1954年以來，日本再也沒有向海外派遣過軍事人員。","There has been very little renewal of personnel in higher education. 高等教育事業中人員更新很少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Personnel</b> is the department in a large company or organization that deals with employees, keeps their records, and helps with any problems they might have. 人事部門","examples":["Her first job was in personnel. 她的第一份工作是在人事部。"]}]}]},"perch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鳥）棲息，停留；（尤指人在高處或很窄的地方）稍坐，暫歇；（建築物）坐落於……的上方（或邊緣）；把……平穩置於，使坐落於"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鳥的）棲木，棲枝；高處，高位；河鱸，鱸魚；杆（尤指用來測量土地長度的單位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>perch on</b> something, you sit down lightly on the very edge or tip of it. 輕坐在; 輕落在 (邊上或頂上)","examples":["He lit a cigarette and perched on the corner of the desk. 他點了一支菸，輕輕地坐在書桌角上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>perch</b> somewhere means to be on the top or edge of something. 坐落於 (某物頂部或邊緣)","examples":["...the vast slums that perch precariously on top of the hills around which the city was built. …搖搖欲墜地坐落於城市中心群山之頂的大片貧民窟。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a bird <b>perches</b> <b>on</b> something such as a branch or a wall, it lands on it and stands there. (鳥) 棲息","examples":["A blackbird flew down and perched on the parapet outside his window. 一隻烏鶇飛下來，棲息在他家窗外的矮牆上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>perch</b> something <b>on</b> something else, you put or balance it on the top or edge of that thing. 把…穩置於 (某物頂部或邊緣)","examples":["The use of steel and concrete has allowed the builders to perch a light concrete dome on eight slender columns. 鋼筋混凝土的使用使建築者們能將一個輕巧的混凝土穹頂架在8根細柱上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>perch</b> is a short rod for a bird to stand on. (鳥的) 棲木","examples":["A small, yellow bird in a cage sat on its perch outside the house. 屋外，一隻小黃鳥站在鳥籠的棲木上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>perch</b> is an edible fish. There are several kinds of perch. 河鱸","examples":[]}]}]},"peg":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"掛鉤，掛釘；<英>晾衣夾子；（系帳篷用的）樁；（標明某物位置的）界樁；（價格、數量等的）限度，標定點；（進一步討論某事物的）依據，理由；（桶）孔塞；<非正式>（摩托車的）腳鐙；賽位（分配給參賽者釣魚或射擊的位置）；<非正式>（人的）腿；少量威士忌（白蘭地）；（烈酒的）計量，度量；弦鈕，琴栓；<美，非正式>全力投球，釘子球"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用釘（或樁）固定；使工資、價格等固定於某水平（或與……掛鈎）；用衣夾把（洗的衣服）夾在衣繩上；（釣魚或射擊比賽中）給（比賽者）分派賽位；<非正式>視為，看作；（棒球）投擲快速低球；（在克里比奇牌戲中）用得分枚計分；疾行，孜孜不倦地做某事"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"越往下端越細的"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（PEG）聚乙（烯）二醇（polyethylene glycol）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>peg</b> is a small piece of wood or metal that is used for fastening something to something else. 銷釘","examples":["He builds furniture using wooden pegs instead of nails. 他用木釘而不是鐵釘製作傢俱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>peg</b> is a small hook or knob that is attached to a wall or door and is used for hanging things on. 掛鉤; 掛環","examples":["His work jacket hung on the peg in the kitchen. 他的工作服掛在廚房裡的掛鉤上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>peg</b> is a small device that you use to fasten clothes to a clothes line. 衣夾","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>peg</b> something somewhere or <b>peg</b> it <b>down</b>, you fix it there with pegs. 用衣夾夾住; 用銷釘固定","examples":["Peg down netting over the top to keep out leaves. 把網子用銷釘固定在頂部以防止樹葉掉入。","...a tent pegged to the ground nearby for the kids. …用銷釘固定在附近的地上給孩子們用的一個帳篷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a price or amount of something <b>is pegged</b> <b>at</b> a particular level, it is fixed at that level. 固定 (價格、數量等)","examples":["Its currency is pegged to the dollar. 其貨幣與美元的匯率固定了。","The Bank wants to peg rates at 9%. 該銀行想要把利率固定在9%。"]}]}]},"pillar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"柱子，支柱；主心骨，棟樑；（組織、制度、信仰等的）核心，基礎；柱狀物；紀念柱；煤柱，礦柱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用柱支撐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pillar</b> is a tall solid structure that is usually used to support part of a building. 柱子","examples":["...the pillars supporting the roof. …支撐屋頂的柱子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is the <b>pillar</b> <b>of</b> a system or agreement, it is the most important part of it or what makes it strong and successful. (系統、協議的) 核心","examples":["The pillar of her economic policy was keeping tight control over money supply. 她的經濟政策的核心就是嚴格控制貨幣供應。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>pillar of</b> society or as a <b>pillar</b> <b>of</b> the community, you approve of them because they play an important and active part in society or in the community. 棟樑","examples":["My father is a pillar of the community. 我父親是社群的頂樑柱。"]}]}]},"pier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指海邊伸入海中，供散步和遊樂的）突堤，長堤；（用於供船上下客或裝卸貨物的）凸式碼頭；<英>旅客橋，上下機走廊；用以承受垂直壓力的固體支架；橋墩，支柱；窗間牆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pier</b> is a platform sticking out into water that people walk along or use when getting onto or off boats. 凸式碼頭","examples":["...Chicago's Navy Pier. …芝加哥的海軍碼頭。"]}]}]},"pimple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疙瘩，（醫）丘疹，面皰（痘痘）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pimples</b> are small raised spots, especially on the face. 丘疹; 膿皰; 粉刺","examples":[]}]}]},"pistol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手槍；<美，非正式>精力旺盛的人"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用手槍射擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pistol</b> is a small gun. 手槍","examples":[]}]}]},"playwright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇作家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>playwright</b> is a person who writes plays. 劇作家","examples":[]}]}]},"plantation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指熱帶的）種植地，農園；人工林場，苗木場；殖民地，新開墾地；普蘭泰申市（美國佛羅里達州城市名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plantation</b> is a large piece of land, especially in a tropical country, where crops such as rubber, coffee, tea, or sugar are grown. (尤指熱帶國家的橡膠、咖啡、茶、甘蔗) 種植園","examples":["...banana plantations in Costa Rica. …在哥斯大黎加的香蕉種植園。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>plantation</b> is a large number of trees that have been planted together. 人工林","examples":["...a plantation of almond trees. …一片人工杏樹林。"]}]}]},"piss":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<忌，俚>撒尿，小便；<英，忌，俚>下大雨；<忌，俚>大笑不止，笑破肚皮（piss yourself (laughing)）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<忌，俚>撒尿；<忌，俚>尿，小便；<澳，粗，俚>酒精飲料（尤指啤酒）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<英，不禮貌>用於強調所說的話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>piss</b> means to urinate. 撒尿","examples":["A man pissed against a wall. 一個男人對著牆撒尿。"]}]}]},"plea":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"懇求，請求；（法庭上所作的）有罪（無罪）陳述；藉口，託辭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>plea</b> is an appeal or request for something, made in an intense or emotional way. 懇求","examples":["Mr. Nicholas made his emotional plea for help in solving the killing. 尼古拉斯先生髮出了令人感動的呼籲，懇求幫助破解這樁殺人案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a court of law, a person's <b>plea</b> is the answer that they give when they have been charged with a crime, saying whether or not they are guilty of that crime. (法庭上表明是否認罪的) 抗辯","examples":["The judge questioned him about his guilty plea. 法官就他的認罪答辯對他提出質疑。","We will enter a plea of not guilty. 我們將進行無罪抗辯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>plea</b> is a reason given, to a court of law or to other people, as an excuse for doing something or for not doing something. (向法庭或其他人說明是否做某事的) 託辭","examples":["Phillips murdered his wife, but got off on a plea of insanity. 菲利普斯謀殺了自己的妻子，但以精神錯亂為由逃脫了罪責。"]}]}]},"plague":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘟疫，傳染病；鼠疫（尤指腺鼠疫）；（老鼠或昆蟲等肆虐造成的）災害，禍患； 普遍的禍害；煩惱事；<古>願上天降災難於……（a plague on）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"困擾，折磨；煩擾，糾纏；使得災禍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Plague</b> or <b>the plague</b> is a very infectious disease that usually results in death. The patient has a severe fever and swellings on his or her body. 瘟疫","examples":["...a fresh outbreak of plague. …瘟疫的新一輪爆發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>plague of</b> unpleasant things is a large number of them that arrive or happen at the same time. 氾濫","examples":["The city is under threat from a plague of rats. 這座城市面臨著鼠患的威脅。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are</b> <b>plagued</b> <b>by</b> unpleasant things, they continually cause you a lot of trouble or suffering. 使困擾","examples":["She was plagued by weakness, fatigue, and dizziness. 她被虛弱、疲勞和眩暈折磨。"]}]}]},"plow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犁；犁過的地；雪犁；犁式；北斗七星（the Plow）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"耕，犁；（用犁）挖出；（用或彷彿用犁）劃出（溝或線）；艱難地進行；奮力前進；（尤指車輛）猛撞；<美>（用剷雪機）剷雪；（輪船，木船）穿過（水域），破浪前進"}],"sections":[]},"pocketbook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錢包，皮夾；女式手提包，手袋；經濟來源，財力；袖珍書；小筆記本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>pocketbook</b> to refer to people's concerns about the money they have or hope to earn. 對錢袋的顧慮","examples":["People feel pinched in their pocketbooks and insecure about their futures. 人們感到錢袋緊縮，對未來缺少安全感。","...the voters' concerns over pocketbook issues. …選民們對錢袋問題的關心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pocketbook</b> is a small bag that a woman uses to carry things such as her money and keys in when she goes out. 女式手提包","examples":[]}]}]},"pinch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"捏，擰，掐；揑住，夾緊；掐掉；（穿的鞋等）夾痛，擠痛；<非正式>偷竊；<非正式>逮捕，拘捕；節約，節省；使經濟拮据；捏拉縮放；（由於擔心或緊張）抿（嘴唇）；（航海）使（帆船）緊搶風"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"捏，掐，擰；一撮；偷竊；（棒球）緊要時刻，緊要關頭"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"替代的，替補的；由替補擊球手完成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pinch</b> a part of someone's body, you take a piece of their skin between your thumb and first finger and give it a short squeeze. 掐; 擰","examples":["She pinched his arm as hard as she could. 她使出全力擰他的胳膊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>pinch</b> something, especially something of little value, means to steal it. 偷拿 (尤為不太值錢的東西)","examples":["Do you remember when I pinched your glasses? 你還記得我偷拿過你的眼鏡嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pinch</b> is also a noun. 掐; 擰","examples":["She gave him a little pinch. 她輕輕地擰了他一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pinch of</b> an ingredient such as salt is the amount of it that you can hold between your thumb and your first finger. 撮","examples":["Put all the ingredients, including a pinch of salt, into a food processor. 將所有的配料，連同一撮鹽，放進食品加工機裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or company <b>is feeling the pinch</b>, they do not have as much money as they used to, and so they cannot buy the things they would like to buy. 感到手頭拮据","examples":["Consumers are spending less and merchants are feeling the pinch. 消費者花錢少了，商家感到手頭拮据。"]}]}]},"pluck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"摘，掐；拉，扯；（用指甲或鑷子）夾，拔（毛髮）；拔去（雞或鳥的毛）；彈撥（絃樂器）；解救，搭救；挖掘，使一躍成名；鼓起勇氣（pluck up the courage）；挑選；（用手指）迅速揀起；（地質）（冰川冰）拔削，拔蝕"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"膽識，勇氣；（供食用的）動物內臟；猛拉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pluck</b> a fruit, flower, or leaf, you take it between your fingers and pull it in order to remove it from its stalk where it is growing. 採摘","examples":["I plucked a lemon from the tree. 我從樹上摘下一枚檸檬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pluck</b> something from somewhere, you take it between your fingers and pull it sharply from where it is. 拔; 扯","examples":["He plucked the cigarette from his mouth and tossed it out into the street. 他從嘴上扯下了香菸，扔在外面的街上。","He plucked the baby out of my arms. 他從我的懷中奪走了孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pluck</b> a guitar or other musical instrument, you pull the strings with your fingers and let them go, so that they make a sound. 彈; 撥 (樂器)","examples":["Nell was plucking a harp. 內爾那時在彈豎琴。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pluck</b> a chicken or other dead bird, you pull its feathers out to prepare it for cooking. 拔除 (禽類的羽毛)","examples":["She looked relaxed as she plucked a chicken. 她拔雞毛的時候看上去很輕鬆。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a woman <b>plucks</b> her <b>eyebrows</b>, she pulls out some of the hairs using tweezers. (用鑷子) 拔 (眉毛)","examples":["You've plucked your eyebrows at last! 你終於修了眉！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>pluck up the courage</b> <b>to</b> do something that you feel nervous about, you make an effort to be brave enough to do it. 鼓起勇氣","examples":["It took me about two hours to pluck up the courage to call. 大約兩小時後我才鼓起勇氣打了電話。"]}]}]},"pledge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誓言，保證，承諾；捐款承諾；戒酒誓言（the pledge）；信物；質押；（美國大學中）宣誓加入男生（女生）聯誼會的人；<古>為健康祝酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保證，發誓；使保證，使許諾；承諾給予，承諾提供；用……抵押，以……典押；<美>宣誓加入（大學男生聯誼會或女生聯誼會）；<古>為健康祝酒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone makes a <b>pledge</b>, they make a serious promise that they will do something. 誓言","examples":["The meeting ended with a pledge to step up cooperation between the six states of the region. 會議以加快該地區6個州之間合作的承諾結束。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pledge</b> is also a noun. 承諾撥款","examples":["...a pledge of forty two million dollars a month. …一個每月撥款4200萬美元的承諾。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>pledges</b> <b>to</b> do something, they promise in a serious way to do it. When they <b>pledge</b> something, they promise to give it. 保證 (做某事); 保證給予 (某物)","examples":["The Communists have pledged to support the opposition's motion. 共產黨員們已經承諾支援反對黨的動議。","Philip pledges support and offers to help in any way that he can. 菲利普承諾給予支援並提供力所能及的幫助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>pledge</b> a sum of money to an organization or activity, you promise to pay that amount of money to it at a particular time or over a particular period. 承諾支付 (一筆款)","examples":["The French president is pledging $150 million in French aid next year. 法國總統承諾來年將撥款1.5億美元用於法國援助。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>pledge</b> <b>yourself to</b> something, you commit yourself to following a particular course of action or to supporting a particular person, group, or idea. 保證","examples":["The president pledged himself to increase taxes for the rich but not the middle classes. 總統保證增加富人而不是中產階級的稅收。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>pledge</b> something such as a valuable possession or a sum of money, you leave it with someone as a guarantee that you will repay money that you have borrowed. 抵押","examples":["He asked her to pledge the house as security for a loan. 他要她抵押房子作為貸款擔保。"]}]}]},"poultry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"家禽；家禽肉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to chickens, ducks, and other birds that are kept for their eggs and meat as <b>poultry</b>. 家禽","examples":["...a poultry farm. …一個家禽飼養場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Meat from these birds is also referred to as <b>poultry</b>. 家禽肉","examples":["The menu features roast meats and poultry. 選單以各種烤肉和家禽肉為特色。"]}]}]},"porch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"門廊；<美>走廊，遊廊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>porch</b> is a sheltered area at the entrance to a building. It has a roof and sometimes has walls. 門廊","examples":["She huddled inside the porch as she rang the bell. 她一邊按門鈴一邊蜷縮排門廊裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>porch</b> is a raised platform built along the outside wall of a house and often covered with a roof. 走廊","examples":["He was standing on the porch, waving as we drove away. 我們開車離開的時候，他站在走廊上向我們揮手。"]}]}]},"prairie":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（北美的）大草原；蒸氣火車頭（Prairie）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prairie</b> is a large area of flat, grassy land in North America. Prairies have very few trees. 北美大草原","examples":[]}]}]},"plunge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）突然向前倒下（跌落）；猛推，猛插；投入（液體中以使淹沒）；（價值）猛跌；（劇烈）顛簸，震盪；（馬）猛地用後腿直立；陡然向下傾斜；驟然陷入；（魯莽地）開始；（使）投身，（使）突然開始從事；種下（植物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（突然的）墜落；跳水，快速游泳；（價值或數量的）驟然下跌；突然陷入"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（女式服裝）領口低的（plunging）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>plunges</b> in a particular direction, especially into water, they fall, rush, or throw themselves in that direction. 縱身跳向; 猛衝向","examples":["At least 50 people died when a bus plunged into a river. 一輛公共汽車衝進了河裡，至少有50人死亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or rate <b>plunges</b>, it decreases quickly and suddenly. 驟降","examples":["His weight began to plunge. 他的體重開始驟然下降。","The Peso plunged to a new low on the foreign exchange markets yesterday. 昨天，比索在外匯市場上暴跌到了歷史新低。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Plunge</b> is also a noun. 投入 (水中); 俯衝","examples":["...a plunge into cold water. …向著冰冷的水中的縱身一跳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Plunge</b> is also a noun. 突然陷入","examples":["That peace often looked like a brief truce before the next plunge into war. 那種和平看起來常常像是投入新一輪戰爭前的短暫停火期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Plunge</b> is also a noun. 突然開始","examples":["His sudden plunge into the field of international diplomacy is a major surprise. 他突然進入了國際外交領域，讓人十分意外。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Plunge</b> is also a noun. 驟降","examples":["Japan's banks are in trouble because of bad loans and the stock market plunge. 日本各家銀行處於困境，緣於不良貸款以及股市的暴跌。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>plunge</b> an object <b>into</b> something, you push it quickly or violently into it. (猛地) 將…推入","examples":["A soldier plunged a bayonet into his body. 一名士兵猛地將刺刀刺入了他的身體。","She plunged her face into a bowl of cold water. 她猛地把臉浸入一盆冷水中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>is plunged</b> <b>into</b> a particular state or situation, or if they <b>plunge</b> <b>into</b> it, they are suddenly in that state or situation. 使突然陷入; 突然陷入","examples":["The government's political and economic reforms threaten to plunge the country into chaos. 該政府的政治和經濟改革有可能使這個國家陷入混亂之中。","Eddy found himself plunged into a world of brutal violence. 埃迪發現自己突然陷入了一個殘酷暴力的世界。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>plunge into</b> an activity or <b>are plunged into</b> it, you suddenly get very involved in it. 使突然開始; 突然開始","examples":["The two men plunged into discussion. 這兩個男人突然投入了討論。","The prince should be plunged into work. 應該趕緊讓王子投入工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take the plunge</b>, you decide to do something that you consider difficult or risky. 決定冒險一試","examples":["If you have been thinking about buying mutual funds, now could be the time to take the plunge. 如果你一直在考慮購買共同基金，現在也許是冒險一試的時候了。"]}]}]},"precaution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預防措施，防備；避孕措施（precautions）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>precaution</b> is an action that is intended to prevent something dangerous or unpleasant from happening. 防範行動","examples":["Could he not, just as a precaution, move to a place of safety? 難道他不能就當是一種防範搬到一個安全的地方去嗎？"]}]}]},"potential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"潛在的，可能的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（事物的）潛力，可能性；（人的）潛能，潛力；電勢，電位，電壓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>potential</b> to say that someone or something is capable of developing into the particular kind of person or thing mentioned. 潛在的","examples":["The company has identified 60 potential customers. 該公司已確定了60位潛在的客戶。","We are aware of the potential problems and have taken every precaution. 我們意識到了潛在的問題，已經採取了一切防範措施。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"潛在地","examples":["Clearly this is a potentially dangerous situation. 顯然這是一種具有潛在危險的局勢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>potential</b>, you mean that they have the necessary abilities or qualities to become successful or useful in the future. 潛力; 潛質","examples":["The boy has great potential. 這個男孩有很大的潛力。","The school strives to treat students as individuals and to help each one to achieve their full potential. 學校力圖因材施教，並幫助每位學生髮揮他們的全部潛能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>potential</b> <b>for</b> doing a particular thing, you mean that it is possible they may do it. If there is <b>the potential for</b> something, it may happen. 潛在性","examples":["John seemed as horrified as I about his potential for violence. 和我一樣，約翰對他的暴力傾向感到恐懼。","The meeting has the potential to be a watershed event. 這次會議有可能成為一次分水嶺事件。"]}]}]},"poke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用手指或尖利物品）戳，刺；從……露出（或伸出、探出）；把……戳進，把……插入；戳（洞）；撥（火）；<俚>與（某人）性交；吸引（另一使用者）的注意"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"捅，戳；輕微的批評，奚落；<非正式>張望，尋覓；（汽車的）馬力，推進力；（尤指19世紀初的）寬前簷女帽（poke bonnet）；<蘇格蘭>袋，小包；<美，非正式>錢包；美國商陸；美國白藜蘆（Indian poke）；<俚>性交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>poke</b> someone or something, you quickly push them with your finger or with a sharp object. 戳; 捅","examples":["Lindy poked him in the ribs. 林迪戳了戳他的肋骨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>poke</b> one thing <b>into</b> another, you push the first thing into the second thing. 把…戳進","examples":["He poked his finger into the hole. 他把手指戳進洞裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>poke</b> your head through an opening or if it <b>pokes</b> through an opening, you push it through, often so that you can see something more easily. 探出 (頭); (頭) 探出","examples":["Julie tapped on my door and poked her head in. 朱莉敲了敲我的房門，接著將頭探了進來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Poke</b> is also a noun. 戳","examples":["John smiled at them and gave Richard a playful poke. 約翰衝他們笑了笑，還頑皮地捅了理查德一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a pocket or bag 衣袋; 袋子","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a woman's bonnet with a brim that projects at the front, popular in the 18th and 19th centuries (流行於18、19世紀的)寬前沿女帽 (Also called poke bonnet)","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"pokeweed的縮寫","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>pokes out of</b> or <b>through</b> another thing, you can see part of it appearing from behind or underneath the other thing. 伸出; 露出","examples":["He saw the dog's twitching nose poke out of the basket. 他看見那條狗顫搐的鼻子從籃子裡露出來。"]}]}]},"prey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獵物，捕獲物；受害者，受騙者；<古>掠奪品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捕食；欺凌，坑害（尤指弱者）；不斷困擾，折磨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A creature's <b>prey</b> are the creatures that it hunts and eats in order to live. 獵物","examples":["Electric rays stun their prey with huge electrical discharges. 電鰩釋放大量的電荷將他們的獵物擊昏。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the people who someone tries to harm or trick as their <b>prey</b>. (某人的) 坑害物件","examples":["Police officers lie in wait for the gangs who stalk their prey at night. 警官們埋伏起來等待捉拿那些夜間悄悄追蹤作案物件的黑幫成員。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A creature that <b>preys on</b> other creatures lives by catching and eating them. 捕食","examples":["The effect was to disrupt the food chain, starving many animals and those that preyed on them. 後果是打斷食物鏈，使許多動物和捕食它們的動物餓死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>preys on</b> other people, especially people who are unable to protect themselves, they take advantage of them or harm them in some way. 坑害","examples":["Pam had never learned that there were men who preyed on young runaways. 帕姆從未瞭解到有些人專門坑害那些年輕的離家出走者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>preys on</b> your mind, you cannot stop thinking and worrying about it. 困擾","examples":["It was a misunderstanding and it preyed on his conscience. 這是個誤會，讓他的良心很不安。"]}]}]},"prior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"先前的，事先的；<正式>優先的，更重要的；<正式>在前面的（prior to）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美，非正式>犯罪前科；小修道院院長；大修道院副院長；託缽會會長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>prior</b> to indicate that something has already happened, or must happen, before another event takes place. 事先的","examples":["He claimed he had no prior knowledge of the protest. 他聲稱他事先對那次抗議一無所知。","The Constitution requires the president to seek the prior approval of Congress for military action. 憲法要求總統尋求國會對軍事行動的事先批准。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>prior</b> claim or duty is more important than other claims or duties and needs to be dealt with first. 優先的","examples":["The firm I wanted to use had prior commitments. 我選擇的那家公司有優先承諾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a prior probability 先驗的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the superior of a house and community in certain religious orders (一些宗教教派中的社群)長老; 德高望重者","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>prior to</b> a particular time or event, it happens before that time or event. 在 (某時間或事件) 之前","examples":["A death prior to 65 is considered to be a premature death. 65歲以前的死亡被認為是過早死亡。"]}]}]},"procession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或車輛的）行列，隊伍；一連串的人（或物）；（神學）聖靈流出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>procession</b> is a group of people who are walking, riding, or driving in a line as part of a public event. (行走、騎行、開車等的) 隊伍","examples":["...a funeral procession. …一行送葬隊伍。"]}]}]},"preview":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預映，預演，預展；預告片；（預先看電影、戲劇、書等後所作的）預告性述評；預審，預視；預覽樣品；預兆；預測；（計算機）列印預覽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為（電影等）寫預評；預先播映（或展示），預告；預看，預聽；概述，扼要介紹；預審，預觀；預測"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>preview</b> is an opportunity to see something such as a movie, exhibition, or invention before it is open or available to the public. 預先觀看","examples":["He had gone to see the preview of a play. 他去看過一齣戲的預演。"]}]}]},"preference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偏愛，偏好；更喜歡的人（或物）；優待，優先（權）；<法律>（尤指債務償付）優先償還權"}],"sections":[]},"prick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扎，戳；使（身體某部位）刺痛；使……感到內疚（或尷尬）；驅使，驅策；（動物）豎起（耳朵）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"扎，穿刺；針刺感，刺痛（感）；蠢材，笨蛋，討厭的傢伙；一陣不快；陰莖；<古>趕牛棒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prick</b> something or <b>prick</b> holes in it, you make small holes in it with a sharp object such as a pin. 扎 (某物); 戳 (洞)","examples":["Prick the potatoes and rub the skins with salt. 在這些土豆扎些洞，然後用鹽擦它們的皮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something sharp <b>pricks</b> you or if you <b>prick</b> <b>yourself with</b> something sharp, it sticks into you or presses your skin and causes you pain. 扎 (人)","examples":["She had just pricked her finger with the needle. 她剛用針紮了她的手指。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prick</b> is a small, sharp pain that you get when something pricks you. 刺痛","examples":["At the same time she felt a prick on her neck. 同時她感到脖子上一陣刺痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>prick</b>, you are insulting them because you think they are mean and spiteful or stupid, or you do not like them. 小氣鬼; 可惡之人; 蠢貨","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A man's <b>prick</b> is his penis. 陰莖","examples":[]}]}]},"priority":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"優先事項，最重要的事；優先，優先權，重點；<英>優先通行權"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"優先的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is a <b>priority</b>, it is the most important thing you have to do or deal with, or must be done or dealt with before everything else you have to do. 優先處理的事","examples":["Being a parent is her first priority. 做母親是她的頭等大事。","The government's priority is to build more power plants. 政府的當務之急是建造更多的發電廠。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give priority</b> <b>to</b> something or someone, you treat them as more important than anything or anyone else. 優先考慮","examples":["Women are more likely to give priority to child care and education policies. 女性更可能給孩子的照料和教育方案以優先考慮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>takes priority</b> or <b>has priority</b> <b>over</b> other things, it is regarded as being more important than them and is dealt with first. 有優先性","examples":["The fight against inflation took priority over measures to combat the deepening recession. 對抗通貨膨脹的鬥爭比對抗日益加深的經濟衰退措施更具優先性。"]}]}]},"prop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"支柱，支撐物；（戲劇或電影中的）道具；<舊，非正式> 道具管理員（props）；支持者，後盾；<非正式> 螺旋槳，推進器；（英式橄欖球運動的）前排邊鋒；（本身沒有具體意義但能使句法完整的）結構詞；（馬快跑時的）驟停"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"支撐，倚靠；<澳>（尤指馬等挺直前腿）驟停；用……撐住（某物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prop</b> an object <b>on</b> or <b>against</b> something, you support it by putting something underneath it or by resting it somewhere. 架; 擱","examples":["He rocked back in the chair and propped his feet on the desk. 他往椅背上一靠，將雙腳擱在了桌子上。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prop up</b> means the same as . 支撐; 維持","examples":["Sam slouched back and propped his elbows up on the bench behind him. 薩姆懶懶地往後一靠，將他的兩胳膊肘撐在了他背後的長凳上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prop</b> is a stick or other object that you use to support something. 支撐物","examples":["Using the table as a prop, he dragged himself to his feet. 他用桌子作支撐，緩慢費力地站了起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To be a <b>prop</b> for a system, institution, or person means to be the main thing that keeps them strong or helps them survive. 支柱","examples":["The army is one of the main props of the government. 軍隊是政府的主要支柱之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>props</b> in a play or movie are all the objects or pieces of furniture that are used in it. (戲劇、電影中的) 道具","examples":["...the backdrop and props for a stage show. …一場舞臺劇的背景幕和道具。"]}]}]},"prophet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（基督教、猶太教、伊斯蘭教等的）先知；預言家；提倡者，擁護者；穆罕默德（the Prophet，伊斯蘭教創始人）；猶太教諸先知，《先知書》（the Prophets）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prophet</b> is a person who is believed to be chosen by God to say the things that God wants to tell people. 先知","examples":["...the sacred name of the Holy Prophet of Islam. …伊斯蘭教神聖先知之聖名。"]}]}]},"profile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人頭部的）側面（像），側影；（某物的）外形，輪廓；（人、團體或組織的）簡介，概況；（人或組織的）形象，姿態；縱斷面，剖面；（地球表面縱斷面的）輪廓（如河流走向）；（舞臺的）平面佈景；（以數量形式記錄事物特點的）曲線圖，資料圖表；（記載個人心理或行為特點、喜好等的）檔案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"概述，扼要介紹；給……畫側面像，顯出……側面輪廓；顯出……的輪廓（be profiled）；（尤指用模板）銑出輪廓，使……成形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>profile</b> is the outline of your face as it is seen when someone is looking at you from the side. (面部的) 側面輪廓","examples":["His handsome profile was turned away from us. 他英俊的側面輪廓轉離了我們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you see someone <b>in profile</b>, you see them from the side. 從側面","examples":["This picture shows the girl in profile. 這張照片從側面顯示該女孩。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>profile of</b> someone is a short article or programme in which their life and character are described. (有關某人的) 簡介","examples":["A Washington newspaper published comparative profiles of the candidates' wives. 一家華盛頓的報紙刊登了候選人妻子們的對比簡介。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If the police make a <b>profile</b> <b>of</b> someone they are looking for, they write a description of the sort of person they are looking for. (書面的) 描述","examples":["...the FBI profile of the anthrax killer. …聯邦調查局對那名炭疽殺人犯的描述。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"進行描畫","examples":["...a former FBI agent who pioneered psychological profiling in the 1970s. …在20世紀70年代開創了犯罪心理描畫的一名前聯邦調查局特工。","DNA profiling would now be added to the struggle against vandalism. DNA描畫如今也許會被加到對抗故意破壞公共財物的鬥爭中。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has a <b>high profile</b>, people notice them and what they do. If you <b>keep a</b> <b>low profile</b>, you avoid doing things that will make people notice you. 高關注度","examples":["...a move that would give Egypt a much higher profile in the upcoming peace talks. …會給埃及在即將到來的和平談判中高關注度的一個行動。"]}]}]},"quart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"夸脫（液體單位，英制中約為1.14升，美製中約為0.95升）；<美>夸脫（乾量單位，約等於1.10升）；（皮克牌用語）同花順（指四張連續的同花牌）；（劍）第四姿勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quart</b> is a unit of volume that is equal to two pints. There are four quarts in a gallon. The abbreviation  is also used. 夸脫 (容量單位，等於2品脫或1/4加侖)","examples":["Pick up a quart of milk and a loaf of bread. 買一夸脫牛奶和一條麵包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a sequence of four cards in the same suit 四張一串的同花色紙牌","examples":[]}]}]},"province":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（知識、興趣、責任的）範圍，領域；省；（由大主教負責管轄的）教省；外省，外地（the provinces）；<英> 北愛爾蘭（the Province）；（古羅馬總督統治的義大利境外的）行省"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>province</b> is a large section of a country that has its own administration. 省","examples":["...the Algarve, Portugal's southernmost province. …阿爾加維，葡萄牙最南端的一個省。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>provinces</b> are all the parts of a country except the part where the capital is situated. 外省","examples":["The government plans to transfer some 30,000 government jobs from Paris to the provinces. 政府計劃將30000個政府職位從巴黎下放到外省去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a subject or activity is a particular person's <b>province</b>, you mean that this person has a special interest in it, a special knowledge of it, or a special responsibility for it. (學識或活動的) 領域; (興趣或職責的) 範圍","examples":["Tattooing is not just the province of sailors. 紋身不只是水手們才感興趣的事。"]}]}]},"prune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修剪，修整；刪除，削減"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"李子幹，西梅乾；<非正式>討厭的人，乏味的人；（樹枝、灌木叢等的）修剪，修整"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prune</b> is a dried plum. 李子幹","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>prune</b>, or <b>prune</b> a tree or bush, you cut off some of the branches so that it will grow better the next year. 修剪 (樹木)","examples":["You have to prune a bush if you want fruit. 如果你想要果樹結果，你就得給它剪枝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>prune</b> something, you cut out all the parts that you do not need. 刪減","examples":["Companies are cutting investment and pruning their product ranges. 公司都在削減投資並減少產品種類。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prune back</b> means the same as . 修剪 (樹木)","examples":["Apples, pears, and cherries can be pruned back when they've lost their leaves. 蘋果樹、梨樹和櫻桃樹在落葉之後就可以被修剪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Prune back</b> means the same as . 刪減","examples":["The company has pruned back its workforce by 20,000 since 2003. 公司自2003年以來已經裁減了2萬名員工。"]}]}]},"prospect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能性，希望；預期，展望；（尤指事業的）成功機會，前景；有望成功的人，有前途的人；可能的顧客，潛在的主顧；<正式>（尤指從高處看到的）景象，景色；潛在礦藏或礦床"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"勘探，勘察；尋找（商業機會）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is some <b>prospect</b> <b>of</b> something happening, there is a possibility that it will happen. 可能性; 前景","examples":["Unfortunately, there is little prospect of seeing these big questions answered. 遺憾的是，幾乎沒有可能看到這些重大問題得到解答。","The prospects for peace in the country's eight-year civil war are becoming brighter. 在該國的8年內戰中，和平的前景正變得越來越光明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>prospect</b> is something that you expect or know is going to happen. 將要發生的事","examples":["There was a mixed reaction to the prospect of having new neighbours. 對於將要有新鄰居這件事有多種反應。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>prospects</b> are their chances of being successful, especially in their career. 成功的機會; 前途","examples":["I chose to work abroad to improve my career prospects. 我選擇到國外工作，以增進我的事業成功的機會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>prospect for</b> oil, gold, or some other valuable substance, they look for it in the ground or under the sea. 勘探","examples":["He had prospected for minerals everywhere from the Gobi Desert to the Transvaal. 他在世界各地探過礦，從戈壁沙漠到德蘭士瓦。"]}]}]},"quack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（鴨子的）呱呱聲，嘎嘎聲；庸醫，江湖郎中；<非正式>醫生"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鴨子）呱呱叫，嘎嘎叫；<非正式>大聲說蠢話，咭咭呱呱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"江湖醫生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a duck <b>quacks</b>, it makes the noise that ducks typically make. (鴨子)發出嘎嘎聲","examples":["There were ducks quacking on the lawn. 有鴨子在草坪上發出嘎嘎的叫著。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quack</b> is also a noun. 嘎嘎聲","examples":["Suddenly he heard a quack. 突然，他聽到嘎的一聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>quack</b> or a <b>quack doctor</b>, you mean that they claim to be skilled in medicine but are not. 庸醫; 江湖醫生","examples":["I went everywhere for treatment, tried all sorts of quacks. 我為求醫走遍了每一寸土地，嘗試了所有江湖醫生的療法。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quack remedies</b> or <b>quack cures</b> are medical treatments that you think are unlikely to work because they are not scientific. 江湖療法的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to act in the manner of a quack 以庸醫之道行醫","examples":[]}]}]},"pulse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"脈搏，脈率； 強勁的音樂節拍，律動；（聲波、光波或電流的）脈衝；（生化）（供細胞培養的）衝量；<文> 衝動；共有立場，心態；（喻）（活力或組織的）核心；（可食用的）豆子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（有節奏地）搏動，跳動；產生節奏；洋溢著，充滿（激情等）；用脈衝調製（波，光束）；應用脈衝訊號於（裝置）；（生化）用同位素脈衝標記（培養中的細胞）（pulse-label 的簡稱）；有節奏地驅動（食物攪拌機）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>pulse</b> is the regular beating of blood through your body, which you can feel when you touch particular parts of your body, especially your wrist. 脈搏","examples":["Mahoney's pulse was racing, and he felt confused. 馬奧尼的脈搏跳得很快，他感到很慌亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In music, a <b>pulse</b> is a regular beat, often produced by a drum. 節拍","examples":["...the repetitive pulse of the music. …樂曲的重複節拍。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>pulse</b> <b>of</b> electrical current, light, or sound is a temporary increase in its level. 脈衝","examples":["The switch works by passing a pulse of current between the tip and the surface. 電源開關的工作原理是讓電流脈衝穿過觸點和觸面之間。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to <b>the pulse of</b> a group in society, you mean the ideas, opinions, or feelings they have at a particular time. 意向","examples":["The White House insists that the president is in touch with the pulse of the black community. 白宮堅持說總統瞭解黑人社群的民意。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Some seeds that can be cooked and eaten are called <b>pulses</b>, for example, peas, beans, and lentils. 可食用的豆子","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>pulses</b>, it moves, appears, or makes a sound with a strong regular rhythm. 有節奏地跳動","examples":["His temples pulsed a little, threatening a headache. 他的太陽穴跳動得有點厲害，預示著要頭痛了。"]}]}]},"pyramid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金字塔；金字塔形的物體（或一堆東西）；角錐體，稜錐體；（解剖）錐體；金字塔式組織（體系）；金字塔式檯球（pyramids）；金字塔式控股；金字塔式騙局（pyramid scheme）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……堆成尖塔（或角錐）形；在（小投資）上獲得豐厚的收益；漸增，上漲；（使）漸增，（使）上漲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pyramids</b> are ancient stone buildings with four triangular sloping sides. The most famous pyramids are those built in ancient Egypt to contain the bodies of their kings and queens. 金字塔","examples":["We set off to see the Pyramids and Sphinx. 我們出發去看金字塔和獅身人面像。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>pyramid</b> is a shape, object, or pile of things with a flat base and sloping triangular sides that meet at a point. 角錐形; 角錐體","examples":["On a plate in front of him was piled a pyramid of flat white crackers. 他面前盤子裡的白色薄餅乾堆成了金字塔形。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can describe something as a <b>pyramid</b> when it is organized so that there are fewer people at each level as you go toward the top. 金字塔形結構","examples":["Traditionally, the Brahmins, or the priestly class, are set at the top of the social pyramid. 傳統上，婆羅門或僧侶階層位於社會金字塔的頂層。"]}]}]},"proportion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"部分，份額；比例；正確的比例，均衡；大小，程度（proportions）；（事情的）重要性，嚴重性；等比關係"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 使（某物）成比例，使相稱；分攤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>proportion of</b> a group or an amount is a part of it. 部分","examples":["A large proportion of the dolphins in that area will eventually die. 那個地區的很大一部分海豚最終都會死去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>proportion of</b> one kind of person or thing in a group is the number of people or things of that kind compared to the total number of people or things in the group. (某部分在總體中所佔的) 比例","examples":["The proportion of women in the profession had risen to 17.3%. 從事那個職業的女性比例已經增長到17.3%。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>proportion of</b> one amount <b>to</b> another is the relationship between the size of the two amounts. (一個量與另一個量的) 比值","examples":["Women's bodies tend to have a higher proportion of fat to water. 女性體內往往有更高的脂肪與水的比值。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>proportions</b> of something, you are referring to its size, usually when this is extremely large. (某物的) 大小","examples":["In the tropics plants grow to huge proportions. 在熱帶，植物長得很高大。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing increases or decreases <b>in proportion to</b> another thing, it increases or decreases to the same degree as that thing. (與…) 成比例地","examples":["The pressure in the cylinders would go up in proportion to the boiler pressure. 汽缸內的壓力會與鍋爐的壓力成比例上升。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is small or large <b>in proportion to</b> something else, it is small or large when compared with that thing. (與…) 比","examples":["Children tend to have relatively larger heads than adults in proportion to the rest of their body. 與身體其餘部位相比，孩子頭部所佔比例往往比成人大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>out of all proportion to</b> something else, you think that it is far greater or more serious than it should be. (與…) 完全不成比例","examples":["The punishment was out of all proportion to the crime. 懲罰和罪行完全不成比例。"]}]}]},"purchase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>購買，採購；<正式>購買的東西；<法律>（非繼承性的）財產置得；<正式>緊握，牢牢抓住；（移動重物的）滑輪（或類似裝置）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式> 購買，採購；<古>（努力或艱難地）獲得，得到；（航海）（用滑輪或槓桿）升起，舉起（繩，索，錨）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>purchase</b> something, you buy it. 購買","examples":["He purchased a ticket and went up on the top deck. 他買了張票，上了頂層。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"購買者","examples":["The broker will get 5% if he finds a purchaser. 這個中間人如果找到一個買主就將提成5%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>purchase of</b> something is the act of buying it. 購買","examples":["This week he is to visit China to discuss the purchase of military supplies. 本週他將訪問中國，討論軍用物資的採購。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>purchase</b> is something that you buy. 購買的東西","examples":["She opened the tie box and looked at her purchase. It was silk, with maroon stripes. 她開啟領帶盒子，看著自己買的東西。那是真絲的，有栗色的條紋。"]}]}]},"puff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸，抽（煙、菸斗等）；吹，噴出；（尤指跑步、攀登之後）氣喘吁吁，喘息；噴著汽（或煙）移動；（尤指顯得很愚蠢地）咆哮，怒吼；膨脹；吹捧"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"吸菸；（煙、氣等的）一縷；（空氣或蒸汽突然噴射發出的）噗的一聲；（蒸汽，煙霧的）一噴；吐氣，喘氣；（充足的）氣息，氣力；泡芙；吹捧文字；<英>（尤指誇大產品價值的）廣告；（裙子等的）泡泡襉；蓬鬆隆起的卷繞髮型；<北美>鴨絨被；粉撲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>puffs</b> <b>on</b> or <b>at</b> a cigarette, cigar, or pipe, they smoke it. 抽 (香菸、雪茄、菸斗等)","examples":["He lit a cigar and puffed on it twice. 他點上一支雪茄，抽了兩口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are puffing</b>, you are breathing loudly and quickly with your mouth open because you are out of breath after a lot of physical effort. 喘粗氣","examples":["I know nothing about boxing, but I could see he was unfit, because he was puffing. 我對拳擊一無所知，但我看得出他身體不行，因為他直喘粗氣。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Puff</b> is also a noun. 一口煙","examples":["I took a puff on the cigarette and started coughing. 我抽了一口煙就開始咳嗽起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>puff of</b> something such as air or smoke is a small amount of it that is blown out from somewhere. 一股","examples":["Wind caught the sudden puff of dust and blew it inland. 風夾裹著那股突然揚起的塵土，把它吹向內陸。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>puff</b> smoke or moisture from your mouth or if it <b>puffs</b> from your mouth, you breathe it out. (從口中) 噴出","examples":["Richard lit another cigarette and puffed smoke toward the ceiling. 理查德點上另一支菸，將煙霧噴向天花板。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an engine, chimney, or stove <b>puffs</b> smoke or steam, clouds of smoke or steam come out of it. (發動機、煙囪或爐子等) 噴","examples":["As I completed my 26th lap the Porsche puffed blue smoke. 我跑完第26圈時，保時捷車噴起了藍色的煙霧。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Puff out</b> means the same as . (從口中) 噴出","examples":["He drew heavily on his cigarette and puffed out a cloud of smoke. 他深深地吸了一口煙，噴出了一團煙霧。"]}]}]},"quest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>（長久或辛勤的）尋求，探求；（中世紀傳奇故事中騎士的）探險"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>探尋，尋求"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quest</b> is a long and difficult search for something. (長久而艱難的) 搜尋; 探求","examples":["My quest for a better bank continues. 我繼續在搜尋一家更好的銀行。","...the quest for the Holy Grail. …對聖盃的探求"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you go <b>in quest of</b> something, you try to find or obtain it. 尋找; 尋求","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are questing</b> <b>for</b> something, you are searching for it. 搜尋; 探求","examples":["He had been questing for religious belief from an early age. 他從早年開始就一直在尋求宗教信仰。","...his questing mind and boundless enthusiasm. …他的探索型頭腦和無限的熱情"]}]}]},"quiver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指突然的強烈情感所致的）顫抖，顫音；箭囊，箭袋；一組（長度、形狀各異的）衝浪板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"顫抖，抖動；使顫抖，使抖動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>quivers</b>, it shakes with very small movements. 顫抖","examples":["Her bottom lip quivered and big tears rolled down her cheeks. 她的下唇顫動著，大滴大滴的淚珠順著臉頰滾了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or their voice <b>is quivering</b> <b>with</b> an emotion such as rage or excitement, you mean that they are strongly affected by this emotion and show it in their appearance or voice. (聲音因憤怒或激動而) 顫抖","examples":["Cooper arrived, quivering with rage. 庫珀到了，氣得渾身發抖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quiver</b> is also a noun. 顫抖","examples":["I recognized it instantly and felt a quiver of panic. 我立刻認出它了，感到一陣驚恐的顫抖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a case for arrows 弓箭箱","examples":[]}]}]},"radius":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"半徑；半徑範圍，周圍；（剖）橈骨；（昆）徑脈；（棘皮動物或腔腸動物的）輻射對稱軸"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（角，邊緣）成弧形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>radius</b> around a particular point is the distance from it in any direction. 範圍","examples":["Nick has searched for work in a ten-mile radius around his home. 尼克已經在以家為中心10英里的範圍內尋找工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>radius</b> of a circle is the distance from its centre to its outside edge. 半徑","examples":["He indicated a semicircle with a radius of about thirty miles. 他標示出一個半徑大約三十英里的半圓。"]}]}]},"rascal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流氓，無賴，不誠實的人；淘氣鬼，小壞蛋"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（古舊/書面）下賤的，卑鄙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call a man a <b>rascal</b>, you mean that he behaves badly and is rude or dishonest. 壞蛋; 淘氣鬼; 無賴","examples":["What's that old rascal been telling you? 那個老傢伙對你都一直說些什麼？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call a child a <b>rascal</b>, you mean that they behave badly. 淘氣鬼","examples":["He's a little rascal - but he's still great fun. 他有點淘氣 - 但他還是很有趣的。"]}]}]},"ranch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指飼養牛、馬、羊等的）大農場，大牧場；<美>牧場式住宅（=ranch house）；<美>酸奶油沙拉醬（=ranch dressing）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"經營牧場（或農場）；在農場飼養（牲畜）；把（土地）用作牧場（或農場）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ranch</b> is a large farm used for raising animals, especially cattle, horses, or sheep. (尤指飼養牛、馬或羊的) 大牧場","examples":["He lives on a cattle ranch in Texas. 他住在德克薩斯州的一個養牛的大牧場裡。"]}]}]},"radish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小蘿蔔（可在色拉中生食）；蘿蔔植物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Radishes</b> are small red or white vegetables that are the roots of a plant. They are eaten raw in salads. 水蘿蔔","examples":[]}]}]},"ratio":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"比率，比例"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ratio</b> is a relationship between two things when it is expressed in numbers or amounts. For example, if there are ten boys and thirty girls in a room, the ratio of boys to girls is 1:3, or one to three. 比率","examples":["The adult to child ratio is one to six. 成人與兒童之比是1比6。"]}]}]},"rack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"架子，支架；（固定檯球球位的）三角框；一局檯球比賽；（舊時的）拉肢刑具（the rack）；（機器的）齒條，齒軌；（羊、豬等帶前肋的）頸脊肉；一對鹿角；<美，非正式>床；毀滅，毀壞；（吉他等樂器的）數字音響效果裝置；伸長快步（指馬側蹄幾乎同時依次抬起、四蹄偶爾同時離地的步態）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"折磨，使痛苦；<史>對……施以肢刑；把……放在架子裡（或架子上）；<美>（檯球比賽開局前）將球擺成三角形；用齒條及小齒輪傳動；（從酒桶渣滓中）抽取（葡萄酒，啤酒等）；<澳，非正式>走開，離去（rack off）；（馬）伸長快步跑，輕快小跑；<古>不合理地提高（租金）；<古>（雲）隨風飄動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rack</b> is a frame or shelf, usually with bars or hooks, that is used for holding things or for hanging things on. 擱物架; 掛物架","examples":["A luggage rack is a sensible option. 行李架是個明智的選擇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an instrument of torture that stretched the body of the victim 拉肢刑架","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"destruction; wreck (obsolete except in the phrase <b>go to rack and ruin</b>) 毀滅","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the neck or rib section of mutton, pork, or veal (羊、豬或小牛的)頸脊","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"another word for single-foot, a gait of the horse (馬)小步跑","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a group of broken clouds moving in the wind 碎積雲","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is racked</b> <b>by</b> something such as illness or anxiety, it causes them great suffering or pain. 使痛苦","examples":["His already infirm body was racked by high fever. 他已經很孱弱的身體受到高燒的折磨。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to torture on the rack 施拉肢酷刑","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(of clouds) to be blown along by the wind (雲)隨風飄過","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to clear (wine, beer, etc) as by siphoning it off from the dregs 吸乾(酒等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rack</b> your <b>brains</b>, you try very hard to think of something. 絞盡腦汁","examples":["She began to rack her brains to remember what had happened at the nursing home. 她開始絞盡腦汁地回憶在療養院發生的事。"]}]}]},"rail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鐵路系統；鐵軌，軌道；欄杆，扶手；（掛物用的）橫杆；（賽馬或賽狗場的）圍欄；（鑲板門或上下推拉窗的）橫檔，冒頭；衝浪板（或帆板的）邊緣；（電子）定電位導體軌；秧雞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用欄杆把……圍起，把……隔開；<正式>譴責，抱怨；由鐵路運送（貨物）；（風帆衝浪用語）斜板滑行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rail</b> is a horizontal bar attached to posts or around the edge of something as a fence or support. 欄杆","examples":["They had to walk across an emergency footbridge, holding onto a rope that served as a rail. 他們不得不抓著當作欄杆用的繩子，走過一架應急人行橋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rail</b> is a horizontal bar that you hang things on. (掛物用的) 橫杆","examples":["This pair of curtains will fit a rail up to 7 ft 6 in wide. 這副窗簾適合安裝在寬度為7英尺6英寸的橫杆上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Rails</b> are the steel bars which trains run on. 鐵軌","examples":["The train left the rails but somehow forced its way back onto the line. 火車偏離了鐵軌，但又設法回到了原來的軌道上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you travel or send something <b>by</b> <b>rail</b>, you travel or send it on a train. 乘火車; 用火車 (運送)","examples":["The president travelled by rail to his home town. 總統乘火車回到了家鄉。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"any of various small wading birds of the genus <b>Rallus</b> and related genera: family <b>Rallidae</b>, order <b>Gruiformes</b> (cranes, etc). They have short wings, long legs, and dark plumage 普通秧雞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to provide with a rail or railings 提供護欄","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to complain bitterly or vehemently 強烈抗議","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>back on the rails</b>, it is beginning to be successful again after a period when it almost failed. 東山再起","examples":["It may take some time to get the economy back on the rails. 可能要花一些時間使經濟重回正軌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>goes off the rails</b>, they start to behave in a way that other people think is unacceptable or very strange, for example, they start taking drugs or breaking the law. 行為出軌","examples":["They've got to do something about these children because clearly they've gone off the rails. 他們必須對這些孩子採取點行動，因為很明顯他們的行為已經出軌了。"]}]}]},"rally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"召集，集合；公開支援（或反對）；重新集合，重整（軍隊）；恢復，重新振作；動員（全體人員）發憤圖強；（價格）回升，升值；參加汽車拉力賽；<古>對……善意打趣，嘲笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"集會，大會；賽車，汽車拉力賽；（網球等比賽中的）相持，拉鋸；（球隊技藝的）改進，提高；恢復健康，康復；（尤指股價）止跌回升"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rally</b> is a large public meeting that is held in order to show support for something such as a political party. 集會","examples":["About three thousand people held a rally to mark international human rights day. 大約三千人舉行集會以紀念國際人權日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rally</b> is also a noun. 恢復健康; 好轉","examples":["After a brief rally the shares returned to $2.15. 短暫的反彈之後，股票回到了$2.15。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>rally</b> in tennis, badminton, or squash is a continuous series of shots that the players exchange without stopping. (網球、羽毛球、壁球中的) 連續對打","examples":["...a long rally. …一陣長時間的連續對打。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>rally</b> is a competition in which vehicles are driven over public roads. 公路車賽","examples":["Carlos Sainz of Spain has won the New Zealand Motor Rally. 西班牙的卡洛斯·賽恩斯在紐西蘭摩托車公路賽中獲勝。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>rally</b> <b>to</b> something or when something <b>rallies</b> them, they unite to support it. 一致支援; 團結起來","examples":["Her cabinet colleagues have continued to rally to her support. 她的內閣同僚們繼續團結一致地支援她。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to bring (a group, unit, etc) into order, as after dispersal, or (of such a group) to reform and come to order 重整; 整編","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to mock or ridicule (someone) in a good-natured way; chaff; tease (善意地)取笑; 打趣","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>rallies</b>, they begin to recover or improve after having been weak. 恢復健康; 好轉","examples":["He rallied enough to thank his doctors. 他身體恢復得能向醫生們道謝了。"]}]}]},"reef":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"礁，暗礁，礁脈；（尤指含金的）礦脈；縮帆部，帆的可收縮部"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"收帆，捲起縮帆部；縮短，收進（中桅，船首斜桁）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reef</b> is a long line of rocks or sand, the top of which is just above or just below the surface of the sea. 礁","examples":["An unspoiled coral reef encloses the bay. 一道完好的珊瑚礁圍繞著海灣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the part gathered in when sail area is reduced, as in a high wind 帆的可收縮部","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to reduce the area of (sail) by taking in a reef 收帆","examples":[]}]}]},"rattle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）咯咯作響；（車輛） 嘎拉嘎拉地響，（移動時）隆隆作響；使慌張，使緊張；呆在......裡，佔用（大得不必要的房間或建築）；喋喋不休地講話（rattle on）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"咯咯聲，咔嗒聲；發連續短促尖利聲的器具；撥浪鼓；<英>（在觀看足球比賽或舉行部落儀式中使用的）急響器，響板；（響尾蛇尾部的）角質環，響環；（人垂死時喉間發出的）呼嚕聲，臨終喉鳴；<古> 喋喋不休的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>rattles</b> or when you <b>rattle</b> it, it makes short, sharp, knocking sounds because it is being shaken or it keeps hitting against something hard. 使發出嘎嘎聲; 發出嘎嘎聲","examples":["She slams the kitchen door so hard I hear dishes rattle. 她砰地一下使勁關上廚房門，我聽到盤子都震得嘎嘎響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>rattles</b> you, they make you nervous. 使緊張","examples":["Officials are not normally rattled by any reporter's question. 官員們一般不會因為任何記者的提問而緊張不安。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rattle</b> is also a noun. 嘎嘎聲","examples":["There was a rattle of rifle fire. 有步槍射擊發出的嘎嘎聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rattle</b> is a baby's toy with small, loose objects inside which make a noise when the baby shakes it. 撥浪鼓","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"緊張的","examples":["He swore in Spanish, an indication that he was rattled. 他用西班牙語宣誓，這表明他很緊張。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to fit (a vessel or its rigging) with ratlines 給(船或其桅索)扎梯繩","examples":[]}]}]},"relic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遺物，遺蹟，遺風；聖物，聖骨；（事物存在或發生的）證據，痕記；殘留物，廢墟（relics）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to something or someone as a <b>relic</b> <b>of</b> an earlier period, you mean that they belonged to that period but have survived into the present. 遺物; 遺蹟","examples":["Germany's asylum law is a relic of an era in European history that has passed. 德國的避難法是歐洲歷史上一個逝去時代的遺留物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>relic</b> is something which was made or used a long time ago and which is kept for its historical significance. 紀念物","examples":["...a museum of war relics. …一個戰爭紀念物博物館。"]}]}]},"refuge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"庇護，避難；（行為和想法的）逃避，躲避；避難所，庇護處；<英>（街道中央的）避車島，安全島"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<古>給予庇護，接納避難；<古>避難，逃避"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you take <b>refuge</b> somewhere, you try to protect yourself from physical harm by going there. 避難","examples":["They took refuge in a bomb shelter. 他們在一個防空洞裡避難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>refuge</b> is a place where you go for safety and protection, for example from violence or from bad weather. 避難所; 收容所","examples":["Eventually Suzanne fled to a refuge for battered women. 最後蘇珊娜逃到了一家受虐婦女收容所。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you take <b>refuge</b> <b>in</b> a particular way of behaving or thinking, you try to protect yourself from unhappiness or unpleasantness by behaving or thinking in that way. 庇護","examples":["All too often, they get bored and seek refuge in drink and drugs. 多數時間，他們感覺厭倦便借酒和毒品得以逃避。"]}]}]},"reel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"卷軸，線軸；（釣竿上的）卷線輪；一卷，一盤；（影片的）一本；里爾舞（一種輕快的蘇格蘭或愛爾蘭舞蹈），里爾舞曲；蹣跚（或搖晃）的動作"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"震驚，困惑；（尤指被打或震驚而）踉蹌著後退；蹣跚，踉蹌；（感覺）暈眩，天旋地轉；卷，繞（reel sth. in）；跳里爾舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reel</b> is a cylindrical object around which you wrap something such as movie film, magnetic tape, or fishing line. 卷軸","examples":["...a 30-metre reel of cable. …一卷30米長的電纜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a staggering or swaying motion or sensation 蹣跚的動作; 搖晃的動作","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various lively Scottish dances, such as the <b>eightsome reel</b> and <b>foursome reel</b> for a fixed number of couples who combine in square and circular formations (蘇格蘭)里爾舞; 由數量固定的一對對人編成方隊和圓隊表演","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to wind (cotton, thread, etc) onto a reel 繞上卷軸","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>reels</b>, they move about in an unsteady way as if they are going to fall. 踉蹌","examples":["He was reeling a little. He must be very drunk. 他有點踉蹌。他一定醉得很厲害。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are</b> <b>reeling</b> from a shock, you are feeling extremely surprised or upset because of it. 感到震驚; 心煩意亂","examples":["I'm still reeling from the shock of hearing about it. 我現在仍然因為聽到這個訊息而震驚不已。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that your brain or your mind <b>is reeling</b>, you mean that you are very confused because you have too many things to think about. 混亂","examples":["His mind reeled at the question. 他的腦子被這個問題攪混了。"]}]}]},"rear":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指建築物或車輛等的）後部，背部（the rear）；（佇列的）後方，後尾部隊（或艦隊）；<非正式>臀部，屁股（=rear end）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"後方的，背部的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"養育，飼養；栽種，培植；（動物）用後腿直立；（建築、山等）高聳；（人）發火，暴跳（rear up）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"向後，在後面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>rear</b> of something such as a building or vehicle is the back part of it. (建築物或機動車等的) 後部","examples":["He settled back in the rear of the taxi. 他在計程車後座，往後靠著坐好了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are at the <b>rear</b> of a moving line of people, you are the last person in it. (佇列的) 尾部","examples":["Musicians played at the front and rear of the procession. 樂師們在遊行隊伍的前面和後面演奏。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Your <b>rear</b> is the part of your body that you sit on. 臀部","examples":["I saw him pat a waitress on her rear. 我看見他拍一個女服務生的屁股。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rear</b> is also an adjective. 後部的","examples":["Manufacturers have been obliged to fit rear seat belts in all new cars. 生產商不得不在所有的新車上安裝後部座椅安全帶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rear</b> children, you take care of them until they are old enough to take care of themselves. 撫養","examples":["She reared sixteen children, six her own and ten her husband's. 她撫養大了16個孩子，6個她自己的，10個她丈夫的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rear</b> a young animal, you keep and take care of it until it is old enough to be used for work or food, or until it can look after itself. 飼養","examples":["She spends a lot of time rearing animals. 她花很多時間飼養動物。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a horse <b>rears</b>, it moves the front part of its body upward, so that its front legs are high in the air and it is standing on its back legs. (指馬) 後腿直立","examples":["The horse reared and threw off its rider. 那匹馬後腿直立，把騎手摔了下去。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or vehicle <b>is</b> <b>bringing up the rear</b>, they are the last person or vehicle in a moving line of them. 殿後","examples":["...police motorcyclists bringing up the rear of the procession. …警用摩托車為遊行隊伍殿後。"]}]}]},"referee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（比賽的）裁判員；仲裁員，調解人；<英>（求職等時的）證明人，介紹人；（刊登前鑑定文章的）審閱人，（撥款前鑑定研究計劃的）鑑定專家"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（給……）當裁判；（給……）做仲裁員，（給……）做調解人；審閱，鑑定（專業性強的文章）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>referee</b> is the official who controls a sports event such as a football game or a boxing match. 裁判員","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>referee</b> is a person who gives you a reference, for example when you are applying for a job. 介紹人; 推薦人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>referees</b> a sports event or contest, they act as referee. 擔任裁判","examples":["Vautrot has refereed in two World Cups. 沃特羅特已經在兩屆世界盃比賽中擔任過裁判。"]}]}]},"reign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（君主）在位時期，統治時期；領導期，任期；支配期，極盛期；（運動員或運動隊）持有指明榮譽頭銜的時期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為王，統治；支配，盛行；成為最佳，成為最重要的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say, for example, that silence <b>reigns</b> in a place or confusion <b>reigns</b> in a situation, you mean that the place is silent or the situation is confused. 主宰","examples":["Last night confusion reigned about how the debate, which continues today, would end. 昨晚，這場在今天繼續進行的辯論將如何結束的問題令人困惑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a king or queen <b>reigns</b>, he or she rules a country. 在位統治","examples":["...Henry II, who reigned from 1154 to 1189. …1154年至1189年在位統治的亨利二世。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reign</b> is also a noun. 統治時期","examples":["...Queen Victoria's reign. …維多利亞女王的統治時期。"]}]}]},"realm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（知識、活動、思想的）領域，範圍；<正式>王國；（動物學）界（對地球表面所作的最主要的生物地理劃分）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>realm</b> to refer to any area of activity, interest, or thought. (活動、興趣、思想的) 領域","examples":["...the realm of politics. …政治領域。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>realm</b> is a country that has a king or queen. 王國","examples":["Defence of the realm is crucial. 王國的防禦是至關重要的。"]}]}]},"reminder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"提醒物，引起回憶的事物；（提醒做某事的）提示信，通知單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that serves as a <b>reminder</b> <b>of</b> another thing makes you think about the other thing. 提醒人記憶之物","examples":["The last thing you'd want is a constant reminder of a bad experience. 你最不想要的就是不斷讓你想起一段糟糕經歷的東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reminder</b> is a letter or note that is sent to tell you that you have not done something such as pay a bill or return library books. 催繳單; 催費單","examples":["...the final reminder for the gas bill. …煤氣費的最後催繳單。"]}]}]},"republican":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"共和政體的，共和國的；擁護共和政體的，共和主義的；（美國）共和黨的，支援共和黨的（Republican）；北愛爾蘭共和主義者的，支援北愛爾蘭共和主義者的（Republican）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"共和主義者，擁護共和政體者；（美國）共和黨人，共和黨支持者（Republican）；（主張北愛爾蘭應脫離英國成為愛爾蘭共和國一部分的）北愛爾蘭共和主義者（Republican）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Republican</b> means relating to a republic. In <b>republican</b> systems of government, power is held by the people or the representatives that they elect. 共和的","examples":["...the nations that had adopted the republican form of government. …採用了共和制政體的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>Republican</b>, they belong to or support the Republican Party. 共和黨的","examples":["Lower taxes made Republican voters happier with their party. 更低的稅率使共和黨選民對該黨更加滿意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>Republican</b> is someone who supports or belongs to the Republican Party. 共和黨人","examples":["What made you decide to become a Republican, as opposed to a Democrat? 是什麼使你決定成為共和黨人，而不是民主黨人呢？"]}]}]},"resentment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憤恨，怨恨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Resentment</b> is bitterness and anger that someone feels about something. 怨恨","examples":["She expressed resentment at being interviewed by a social worker. 她對於被一個社會工作者面試表示了怨恨。"]}]}]},"residence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"住宅，住所；居住，定居；（在某國的）居住權，居留許可；（大學的）學生宿舍樓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>residence</b> is a house where people live. 住宅","examples":["The house is currently run as a country inn, but could easily convert back into a private residence. 這棟房子目前被當作一家鄉村客棧用，但可以容易地改回成一所私用住宅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your place of <b>residence</b> is the place where you live. 住所","examples":["There were significant differences among women based on age, place of residence, and educational levels. 基於年齡、住處和教育水平，婦女們之間存在顯著的差異。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone's <b>residence</b> in a particular place is the fact that they live there or that they are officially allowed to live there. 居住","examples":["They had entered the country and had applied for permanent residence. 他們已進入了那個國家，並已經申請了永久居住權。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>in residence</b> in a particular place, they are living there. 住在 (某處)","examples":["The king and queen of Jordan are in residence. 約旦的國王和王后住在宮邸。"]}]}]},"retort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（憤怒或風趣地）反駁，回嘴；<古>對（侮辱，傷害）進行報復；利用（對方的論據）反駁對方；蒸餾，乾餾"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"反駁，回嘴；曲頸瓶，蒸餾器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>retort</b> means to reply angrily to someone. 反駁","examples":["\"You can't smoke in here,\" Shaw said.—\"Don't worry, it's not tobacco,\" he retorted. “你不能在這兒吸菸，”肖說道。—“別擔心，這不是菸葉，”他反駁道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Retort</b> is also a noun. 反駁","examples":["His sharp retort clearly made an impact. 他的尖銳反駁顯然起了作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a glass vessel with a round bulb and long tapering neck that is bent down, used esp in a laboratory for distillation 曲頸瓶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to heat in a retort 在曲頸瓶里加熱","examples":[]}]}]},"resident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"居民，住戶；（旅館的）住宿者；<美>住院醫生；<美> 寄宿制學校學生；<史>（英國政府派駐半獨立國家的） 特派代表；駐外特工；留鳥，無遷徙習性的蝴蝶（或其他動物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（在某地）居住的，居留的；常駐的；屬於（某個群體）的；（鳥、蝴蝶等）非遷徙性的；（計算機程式、檔案等在儲存器中）駐留的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>residents</b> of a house or area are the people who live there. 居民","examples":["The archbishop called on the government to build more low cost homes for local residents. 這位大主教呼籲該政府為當地居民建更多的廉價住宅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>resident</b> or a <b>resident</b> doctor is a doctor who is receiving a period of specialized training in a hospital after completing his or her internship. 住院醫師","examples":["Many resident doctors complain that they are assigned too many duties that are usually not performed by physicians. 很多住院醫師抱怨他們被指派了太多通常不由內科醫生完成的職責。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>resident</b> <b>in</b> a country or a town lives there. 居住的","examples":["He moved to the United States in 1990 to live with his son, who had been resident in Baltimore since 1967. 他1990年移居美國去和從1967年就住在巴爾的摩的兒子一起住。"]}]}]},"resume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"恢復（職位），回到（座位）；繼續說，接著說；概述；（中斷後）重新開始，繼續"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"梗概，摘要（résumé或resumé）；<美>簡歷，履歷（résumé或resumé）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>resume</b> an activity or if it <b>resumes</b>, it begins again. 重新開始","examples":["After the war he resumed his duties at Wellesley College. 那場戰爭之後，他恢復了在韋爾斯利學院的任職。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>resume</b> your seat or position, you return to the seat or position you were in before you moved. 重返","examples":["\"I changed my mind,\" Blanche said, resuming her seat. “我改主意了，”布蘭奇說，返回到她的座位上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"重新開始","examples":["It is premature to speculate about the resumption of negotiations. 考慮談判的恢復還太早。"]}]}]},"resort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅遊勝地，度假勝地；求助的方法，採用的手段；採用，訴諸，求助"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"訴諸，求助於；<正式>常去，（成群結隊地）去"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>resort</b> <b>to</b> a course of action that you do not really approve of, you adopt it because you cannot see any other way of achieving what you want. 不得不求助","examples":["His punishing work schedule had made him resort to drugs. 他那累人的工作日程已經使他不得不求助於毒品了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you achieve something without <b>resort</b> <b>to</b> a particular course of action, you succeed without carrying out that action. To have <b>resort</b> <b>to</b> a particular course of action means to have to do that action in order to achieve something. 訴諸","examples":["Congress has a responsibility to ensure that all peaceful options are exhausted before resort to war. 國會有責任確保在所有和平的手段用盡之後再訴諸武力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>resort</b> is a place where a lot of people spend their holiday. (度假) 勝地","examples":["The ski resorts are expanding to meet the growing number of skiers that come here. 該滑雪勝地正在擴建以應付來這裡滑雪的不斷增長的人數。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>as a last resort</b>, you do it because you can find no other way of getting out of a difficult situation or of solving a problem. 作為最後手段","examples":["Nuclear weapons should be used only as a last resort. 核武器應該只被用作最後手段。"]}]}]},"reptile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爬行動物；（非正式）卑鄙的人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"爬行動物的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reptiles</b> are a group of cold-blooded animals which lay eggs and have skins covered with small, hard plates called scales. Snakes, lizards, and crocodiles are reptiles. 爬行動物","examples":[]}]}]},"rhino":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犀牛（同 rhinoceros）；錢，現金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rhino</b> is the same as a . 犀牛","examples":[]}]}]},"rhinoceros":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犀，犀牛（棲於非洲和亞洲）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rhinoceros</b> is a large Asian or African animal with thick, grey skin and a horn, or two horns, on its nose. 犀牛","examples":[]}]}]},"revolt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對權威、規定、法律的）反抗，違抗；叛亂，造反"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"叛亂，造反；反抗，拒絕服從（權威、規定或法律）；使反感，使震驚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>revolt</b> is an illegal and often violent attempt by a group of people to change their country's political system. 造反; 叛亂","examples":["It was undeniably a revolt by ordinary people against their leaders. 不可否認，這是一場普通百姓反抗領導人的起義。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>revolt</b> by a person or group against someone or something is a refusal to accept the authority of that person or thing. 反抗; 抵制","examples":["Conservative Republicans had led the revolt against the budget package. 保守共和黨帶領了對這一預算計劃的抵制。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>revolt</b>, they make an illegal and often violent attempt to change their country's political system. 造反; 叛亂","examples":["In 1375 the townspeople revolted. 1375年，市民造反了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>revolt</b> <b>against</b> someone or something, they reject the authority of that person or reject that thing. 反抗; 抵制","examples":["In 1978 California taxpayers revolted against higher taxes. 1978年加利福尼亞的納稅人抵制了高稅費。"]}]}]},"rib":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肋骨；排骨（肉），肋條（肉）；肋骨狀物（構成船、房頂等骨架的金屬或木質等）；（編織）羅紋，羅紋花樣；葉的脈紋（尤指葉的主脈），（昆蟲的）翅脈；（岩石的）脈紋，（田地上的）壟"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊，非正式>（友善地）開……的玩笑，取笑；形成攏起的條紋（或脊坡）；裝肋於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>ribs</b> are the 12 pairs of curved bones that surround your chest. 肋骨","examples":["Her heart was thumping against her ribs. 當時她的心挨著她的肋骨砰砰直跳。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rib</b> <b>of</b> meat such as beef or pork is a piece that has been cut to include one of the animal's ribs. 排骨","examples":["...a rib of beef. …一塊牛小排。","...pork ribs. …豬排骨。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a part or element similar in function or appearance to a rib, esp a structural or supporting member or a raised strip or ridge","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a joke or hoax 玩笑; 惡作劇","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to furnish or support with a rib or ribs 裝肋狀物於; 用肋狀物支撐","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to tease or ridicule 戲弄; 嘲笑","examples":[]}]}]},"ridge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"山脊，山脈；屋脊；隆起部分，脊狀突起；（大氣層的）高壓脊，高壓帶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使隆起，使形成脊狀；（表面）成脊狀，起皺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ridge</b> is a long, narrow piece of raised land. 脊; 山脈","examples":["...a high road along a mountain ridge. …一條沿山脊而建的公路。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ridge</b> is a raised line on a flat surface. (平面上的) 隆起線","examples":["...the bony ridge of the eye socket. …眼窩的骨質隆起線。"]}]}]},"rifle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"步槍，來復槍；步槍隊（rifles）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"快速搜尋，匆忙翻找；偷竊，盜取；用力擲，猛踢（球）；為（槍、槍管或內膛）鑿制來復線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rifle</b> is a gun with a long barrel. 來復槍; 步槍","examples":["They shot him at point blank range with an automatic rifle. 他們用一支自動步槍在近距離射程內射中了他。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rifle</b> <b>through</b> things or <b>rifle</b> them, you make a quick search among them in order to find something or steal something. 匆忙搜尋","examples":["I discovered my husband rifling through the filing cabinet. 我發現我丈夫在檔案櫃裡匆忙地翻找。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cut or mould spiral grooves inside the barrel of (a gun) 在(槍的螺旋槽)內製來復線","examples":[]}]}]},"rim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（圓形物體的）邊沿；（汙垢等）一週，一圈；輪輞，輪圈；眼鏡框；（籃球的）籃筐，籃圈 ；界，邊界"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"形成......的邊沿，給......鑲邊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>rim</b> of a container such as a cup or glass is the edge that goes all the way around the top. (容器的) 上緣","examples":["She looked at him over the rim of her glass. 她沿玻璃杯口看著他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>rim</b> of a circular object is its outside edge. (圓形物體的) 外緣; 外框","examples":["...a round mirror with white metal rim. …一面有白色金屬邊框的圓鏡子。"]}]}]},"reverse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逆轉，徹底改變（決定、政策、趨勢等）；撤銷，推翻（法庭判決）；顛倒，反轉；交換，互換（位置、功能）；<美>承認錯誤，放棄（立場）；倒（車）；（發動機）反向運轉；<英>打對方付費的電話；使（鉛字，圖案）印成白或淺色"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"相對，相反（the reverse）；逆向，逆轉；倒車擋；<正式>失敗，挫折；反面，背面；（翻開的書）左手頁，（活頁檔案的）背面；（硬幣或獎牌）反面圖案（或刻字）；（美式橄欖球）反向傳球，變位傳球"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相反的，反向的；背面的，反面的；（半導體結的外加電壓）反向的；（地層）逆斷的，沖斷的；反身的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone or something <b>reverses</b> a decision, policy, or trend, they change it to the opposite decision, policy, or trend. 使 (決定、政策、趨勢) 轉向; 逆轉","examples":["They have made it clear they will not reverse the decision to increase prices. 他們已經明確表示不會為了提高價格而轉變這一決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reverse</b> the order of a set of things, you arrange them in the opposite order, so that the first thing comes last. 顛倒 (順序)","examples":["Because the normal word order is reversed in passive sentences, they are sometimes hard to follow. 由於正常語序在被動句中被顛倒過來了，所以有時很難理解。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>reverse</b> the positions or functions of two things, you change them so that each thing has the position or function that the other one had. 調換 (位置、功能)","examples":["He reversed the position of the two stamps. 他調換了兩張郵票的位置。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a car <b>reverses</b> or when you <b>reverse</b> it, the car is driven backward. 倒 (車); (車) 倒過來","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your car is <b>in</b> <b>reverse</b>, you have changed gears so that you can drive it backward. (汽車的) 倒檔","examples":["He lurched the car in reverse along the ruts to the access road. 他沿著車轍顛簸著倒行到通行道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that one thing is <b>the reverse</b> of another, you are emphasizing that the first thing is the complete opposite of the second thing. 相反物; 相反面","examples":["He was not at all jolly. Quite the reverse. 他一點兒也不高興。恰恰相反。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>reverse</b> or <b>the</b> <b>reverse</b> <b>side</b> of a flat object which has two sides is the less important or the other side. 背面; 反面","examples":["A chart on the reverse of this letter highlights your savings. 這封信背面的圖表著重寫明瞭你的存款情況。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reverse</b> means opposite from what you expect or to what has just been described. 相反的","examples":["The wrong attitude will have exactly the reverse effect. 這種錯誤的態度會得到恰好相反的結果。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>in reverse</b> or goes <b>into reverse</b>, things happen in the opposite way from what usually happens or from what has been happening. 朝相反方向; 反向地 (發展)","examples":["Amis tells the story in reverse, from the moment the man dies. 埃米斯以倒敘方式講這個故事，從那個男人死去的那一刻開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reverse the charges</b> when you make a telephone call, the person who you are phoning pays the cost of the call and not you. 對方付費電話; 受話人付費","examples":[]}]}]},"roam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"漫步，閒逛；（眼睛）掃視，（手）掃過；（思緒，想象力）遨遊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"漫步"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>roam</b> an area or <b>roam around</b> it, you wander or travel around it without having a particular purpose. 閒逛; 漫遊","examples":["Barefoot children roamed the streets. 光著腳的孩子們在街上閒逛。","I spent a couple of years roaming around the countryside. 我花了幾年時間在鄉村漫遊。"]}]}]},"ripple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"漣漪；（外觀或運動）如波紋的東西；（聲音的）傳播起伏，（感情的）逐漸擴散；連鎖反應；彩條冰淇淋；表面張力波；脈動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）如波浪般起伏；（情緒）波動，（聲音）盪漾；發出潺潺聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ripples</b> are little waves on the surface of water caused by the wind or by something moving in or on the water. 漣漪","examples":["Gleaming ripples cut the lake's surface. 閃著微光的漣漪打破了湖面的平靜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event causes <b>ripples</b>, its effects gradually spread, causing several other events to happen one after the other. 連鎖反應","examples":["If Brazil defaults on its foreign debt, it will cause ripples throughout the world. 如果巴西不還外債的話，這將在全世界引起連鎖反應。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a special kind of comb designed to separate the seed from the stalks in flax, hemp, or broomcorn 麻梳(用來梳除亞麻莖、棕櫚或高粱上籽的粗鋼梳)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the surface of an area of water <b>ripples</b> or when something <b>ripples</b> it, a number of little waves appear on it. 使泛起漣漪; 泛起漣漪","examples":["You throw a pebble in a pool and it ripples. 你把卵石扔進水池裡，水面就泛起漣漪。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a feeling <b>ripples</b> over someone's body, it moves across it or through it. (感覺等) 擴散全身","examples":["A chill shiver rippled over his skin. 一陣寒顫傳遍了他全身。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to comb with this tool (用麻梳)梳理","examples":[]}]}]},"rival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"競爭對手，敵手；可與之匹敵者，可與之相比的人（或物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"與......相匹敵，比得上"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"競爭的，對抗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>rival</b> is a person, business, or organization who you are competing or fighting against in the same area or for the same things. 對手","examples":["The world champion finished more than two seconds ahead of his nearest rival. 這位世界冠軍領先離他最近的對手兩秒多鍾衝過終點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>no</b> <b>rivals</b> or is <b>without</b> <b>rival</b>, you mean that it is best of its type. 可匹敵者","examples":["The area is famous for its wonderfully fragrant wine which has no rivals in the Rhone. 這一地區以其極為醇香的葡萄酒而聞名，這種酒在羅納河流域沒有可匹敵者。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing <b>rivals</b> another, you mean that they are both of the same standard or quality. 與…相匹敵","examples":["Cassette recorders cannot rival the sound quality of CDs. 盒式磁帶錄音機在音質上無法與CD相媲美。"]}]}]},"rip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）撕裂，（使）劃破；迅速扯開，猛力去除；（迅速）貫穿，穿過；劃出（孔洞），擊穿；搶掠，剝奪；嚴厲批評，訓斥；利用程式將（光碟上的音序）複製到硬碟驅動器上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"裂口，裂縫；撕，撕破；<美，非正式>欺詐，剽竊；（在電腦上製作的光碟）複製本；（由海、河中不同水流相遇造成的）裂流（激浪）水域，離岸流；<非正式，舊>生活放蕩的人（尤指男人），浪子；<非正式，舊>調皮的人，淘氣鬼（尤指小孩）；<非正式，舊>劣馬，無用的馬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>rips</b> or when you <b>rip</b> it, you tear it forcefully with your hands or with a tool such as a knife. 撕; 撕裂","examples":["I felt the banner rip as we were pushed in opposite directions. 當我們被擠向相反的方向的時候，我感到橫幅撕裂了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rip</b> something away, you remove it quickly and forcefully. 撕; 扯 (掉)","examples":["He ripped away a wire that led to the alarm button. 他把連線報警按鈕的電線扯掉了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rip</b> is a long cut or split in something made of cloth or paper. (布或紙上的) 裂口","examples":["Looking at the rip in her new dress, she flew into a rage. 看著新連衣裙上的裂口，她勃然大怒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"riptide的縮寫","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"something or someone of little or no value 沒有價值的東西; 沒用的人","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>rips</b> into someone or something or <b>rips</b> through them, it enters that person or thing so quickly and forcefully that it often goes completely through them. 穿 (過); 穿 (透)","examples":["A volley of bullets ripped into the facing wall. 一排子彈穿透了對面的牆。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>let it rip</b>, you do something forcefully and without trying to control yourself. 盡情地幹","examples":["Turn the guitars up full and let it rip. 把吉他的音量調到最大，盡情地玩。"]}]}]},"robin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歐亞鴝，歐洲知更鳥；旅鶇，美洲知更鳥（毛灰色，胸部紅色，比歐亞鴝大）"}],"sections":[]},"rod":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棒，杆；釣竿，魚竿；釣魚者；權力，權杖；枝條，柳條；（責打人用的）棍棒；杖責，懲罰（the rod）；<美，非正式>（左輪）手槍；視網膜杆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rod</b> is a long, thin, metal or wooden bar. 長杆; 長棒","examples":["...a 15-foot thick roof that was reinforced with steel rods. …用鋼條加固了的15英尺厚的屋頂。"]}]}]},"rustle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）沙沙作響；偷竊（牲口）；<美，非正式>急速行進，趕緊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"沙沙聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something thin and dry <b>rustles</b> or when you <b>rustle</b> it, it makes soft sounds as it moves. 使沙沙作響; 沙沙作響","examples":["The leaves rustled in the wind. 那些樹葉在風中沙沙作響。","She rustled her papers impatiently. 她不耐煩地把檔案翻得沙沙響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rustle</b> is also a noun. 沙沙聲","examples":["She sat perfectly still, without even a rustle of her frilled petticoats. 她一動不動地坐著，就連她那褶邊長裙也無一絲窸窣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"沙沙聲","examples":["We were all terrified by a rustling sound coming from beneath one of the seats. 我們都被從一個座位下發出的沙沙聲嚇著了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to steal (cattle, horses, etc) 偷(牛馬等)","examples":[]}]}]},"rumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發出隆隆聲；轟鳴著緩慢行進；（肚子因飢餓而）咕嚕作響；低沉地說；（爭論）有節制地持續，低調地持續（rumble on）；<英，非正式>看穿（違法活動或進行違法活動者）；<美，非正式>打群架"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"持續而低沉的聲音，隆隆聲；<美，非正式>打群架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rumble</b> is a low, continuous noise. 隆隆聲","examples":["The silence of the night was punctuated by the distant rumble of traffic. 夜晚的寧靜被遠處車輛的隆隆聲所打破。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>rumbles</b> somewhere, it moves slowly forward while making a low, continuous noise. 轟隆著緩慢行進","examples":["A bus rumbled along the road. 一輛公共汽車轟隆著緩慢行駛在路上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>rumbles</b>, it makes a low, continuous noise. 隆隆作響","examples":["The sky, swollen like a black bladder, rumbled and crackled. 天空脹得像個黑色的氣囊，發出隆隆聲和劈啪聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your stomach <b>rumbles</b>, it makes a vibrating noise, usually because you are hungry. (肚子因飢餓) 發咕咕聲","examples":["Her stomach rumbled. She hadn't eaten any breakfast. 她的肚子咕咕直叫。她早上什麼也沒吃。"]}]}]},"salmon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鮭魚，三文魚，大麻哈魚；鮭魚肉，三文魚肉；鮭肉粉紅色，淺橙色；類似鮭的魚，尤指澳鮭，石首魚"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淺橙色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>salmon</b> is a large silver-coloured fish. 三文魚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Salmon</b> is the orangey-pink flesh of this fish which is eaten as food. It is often smoked and eaten raw. 鮭魚肉","examples":["He gave them a splendid lunch of smoked salmon. 他款待了他們一頓極好的燻三文魚午餐。"]}]}]},"rubbish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"垃圾，廢棄物；毫無價值的東西，劣質產品；廢話，瞎說"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>嚴厲批評，把……說得一無是處"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英，非正式>很差勁的，無用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rubbish</b> consists of unwanted things or waste material such as used paper, empty cans and bottles, and waste food. 垃圾","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you think that something is of very poor quality, you can say that it is <b>rubbish</b>. 垃圾 (強調質量極差)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rubbish</b> a person, their ideas or their work, you say they are of little value. 把…說得一文不值","examples":[]}]}]},"saddle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鞍，馬鞍；（腳踏車或摩托車的）車座；（羊、兔或鹿的）脊肉；（哺乳動物或家禽的）後背部，脊；（電纜、電線或管的）托架；（窯裡用於支撐陶瓷器的）耐火黏土托架；（役馬的）鞍部；（山的）鞍部；鞍點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（馬）裝鞍；（馴馬師）使（馬）參加比賽；使承擔（責任、任務），使負重擔；跨上馬鞍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saddle</b> is a leather seat that you put on the back of an animal so that you can ride the animal. 鞍","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>saddle</b> is a seat on a bicycle or motorcycle. (腳踏車或摩托車的) 車座","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>saddle</b> a horse, you put a saddle on it so that you can ride it. 給 (馬) 配鞍","examples":["Why don't we saddle a couple of horses and go for a ride? 為什麼我們不給幾匹馬配上鞍騎著轉轉？"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Saddle up</b> means the same as . 同(saddle)","examples":["I want to be gone from here as soon as we can saddle up. 我想一配好鞍就離開這兒。"]}]}]},"saint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（基督教追封的）聖者，聖徒；聖人，道德高尚的人；聖（用於宗教聖徒的頭銜中）（Saint，縮寫為St或S）；摩門教信徒（Saint）；（《聖經》中使用或典出《聖經》的）基督信徒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……正式封為聖者（或聖人），封聖"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高尚的，聖賢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saint</b> is someone who has died and been officially recognized and honoured by the Christian church because his or her life was a perfect example of the way Christians should live. (基督教教會正式追封的) 聖人","examples":["Every parish was named after a saint. 每個教區都以一個聖徒的名字命名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a living person as a <b>saint</b>, you mean that they are extremely kind, patient, and unselfish. 聖人","examples":["My girlfriend Geraldine is a saint to put up with me. 我的女友傑拉爾丁是個能包容我的聖人。"]}]}]},"sandal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"涼鞋；檀香，檀香木（sandalwood 的簡稱）；便鞋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sandals</b> are light shoes that you wear in warm weather, which have straps instead of a solid part over the top of your foot. 涼鞋","examples":["...a pair of old sandals. …一雙舊涼鞋。"]}]}]},"salute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（向……）行軍禮，（向……）致敬；（尤指公開地）讚揚，頌揚；（尤指用手或身體動作）向……打招呼，向……致意"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"敬禮，舉手禮；致敬，致意； 鳴禮炮，鳴炮致敬；舉劍致敬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>salute</b> someone, you greet them or show your respect with a formal sign. Soldiers usually salute officers by raising their right hand so that their fingers touch their forehead. 向…打招呼; 向…行軍禮","examples":["One of the company stepped out and saluted the General. 隊中的一人站出來，向那位將軍行軍禮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>salute</b> a person or their achievements means to publicly show or state your admiration for them. 對…表示敬意","examples":["I salute the governor for the leadership role that he is taking. 我對州長的領導風範表示敬意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Salute</b> is also a noun. 招呼; 軍禮","examples":["He gave his salute and left. 他打了招呼然後離開了。"]}]}]},"savage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兇猛的，殘暴的；猛烈的，惡狠狠的；極嚴重的，大幅度的；<舊>未開化的，野蠻的；（土地）荒涼的，無人煙的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>未開化的人，野蠻人； 兇狠殘暴的人；（紋章）長鬚半裸帶葉環男人形"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（動物）兇猛攻擊，撕咬； 激烈抨擊，猛烈批評"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>savage</b> is extremely cruel, violent, and uncontrolled. 野蠻的; 殘暴的","examples":["This was a savage attack on a defenceless young girl. 這是對一個無力自衛的小姑娘的野蠻襲擊。","...the savage wave of violence that swept the country in November 1987. …1987年11月席捲了該國的野蠻暴力浪潮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"野蠻地; 殘暴地","examples":["He was savagely beaten. 他被毒打了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to people as <b>savages</b>, you dislike them because you think that they do not have an advanced society and are violent. 野蠻人; 殘暴的人","examples":["...their conviction that the area was a frozen desert peopled with uncouth savages. …他們深信該地區是一片冰冷的沙漠，住著一些沒有教養的野蠻人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is savaged</b> by a dog or other animal, the animal attacks them violently. (動物) 兇猛地攻擊","examples":["The animal then turned on him and he was savaged to death. 那隻獸接而撲向他，把他攻擊至死。"]}]}]},"scandal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醜行，醜聞；流言蜚語，謠言；（由醜聞引起的）反感，公憤；令人震驚（或反感）的事情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scandal</b> is a situation or event that is thought to be shocking and immoral and that everyone knows about. 醜聞","examples":["...a financial scandal. …一樁金融醜聞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Scandal</b> is talk about the shocking and immoral aspects of someone's behaviour or something that has happened. 流言蜚語","examples":["He loved gossip and scandal. 他喜歡閒話和流言蜚語。"]}]}]},"scorn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蔑視，輕視；嗤之以鼻的態度；<古> 被鄙視的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鄙視，嘲笑；拒絕，不屑於做；批評，抨擊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you treat someone or something <b>with</b> <b>scorn</b>, you show contempt for them. 輕蔑; 鄙視","examples":["Researchers greeted the proposal with scorn. 研究者們對這個提議報以輕蔑的態度。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scorn</b> someone or something, you feel or show contempt for them. 鄙視; 看不起","examples":["Several leading officers have quite openly scorned the peace talks. 幾名高階官員曾相當公開地鄙視和平談判。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>scorn</b> something, you refuse to have it or accept it because you think it is not good enough or suitable for you. 擯棄","examples":["...people who scorned traditional methods. …擯棄傳統做法的人們。"]}]}]},"scar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傷疤，疤痕；（精神上的）創傷；損傷痕跡，汙點；（植物的）葉柄疤；（尤指石灰岩的）峭壁，露出地表的岩層"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結疤，留下傷疤；給……留下精神創傷；損害……的外觀，破壞……的景緻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scar</b> is a mark on the skin which is left after a wound has healed. 傷疤","examples":["He had a scar on his forehead. 他前額上有個傷疤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an irregular enlongated trench-like feature on a land surface that often exposes bedrock 斷崖","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an unpleasant physical or emotional experience leaves a <b>scar</b> on someone, it has a permanent effect on their mind. (肉體或情感上的) 創傷","examples":["The early years of fear and the hostility left a deep scar on the young boy. 早年的恐懼和這種敵意在這個小男孩的心靈上留下了深深的創傷。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your skin <b>is scarred</b>, it is badly marked as a result of a wound. 在…留下傷疤","examples":["He was scarred for life during a fight. 他在一次打架中留下了一輩子的疤痕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a surface <b>is scarred</b>, it is damaged and there are ugly marks on it. 留下損傷痕跡","examples":["The arena was scarred by deep muddy ruts. 競技場上留下了深深的車轍泥痕。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an unpleasant physical or emotional experience <b>scars</b> you, it has a permanent effect on your mind. 給…留下精神創傷","examples":["This is something that's going to scar him forever. 這將會是永遠給他留下心靈創傷的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to heal leaving a scar 結疤","examples":[]}]}]},"scan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"細看，審視；粗略看，瀏覽；掃描檢查（物體或身體部位等）；（機器或計算機程式）掃描，察看；將（檔案、照片等）掃描進計算機；（用聲吶或雷達）掃描，掃掠；（詩）符合格律，韻節合拍；用（光束）掃描；電視掃描"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"快速查閱，瀏覽；（醫療）掃描檢查；掃描圖；胎兒掃描檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>scan</b> written material, you look through it quickly in order to find important or interesting information. 瀏覽","examples":["She scanned the advertisement pages of the newspapers. 她瀏覽了報紙的廣告頁。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>scan</b> a place or group of people, you look at it carefully, usually because you are looking for something or someone. 仔細察看","examples":["The officer scanned the room. 警察仔細察看了那個房間。","She was nervous and kept scanning the crowd for Paul. 她很緊張，一直在人群中尋找保羅。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people <b>scan</b> something such as luggage, they examine it using a machine that can show or find things inside it that cannot be seen from the outside. (用機器) 掃描 (行李等)","examples":["Their approach is to scan every checked-in bag with a bomb detector. 他們的做法是用炸彈探測器掃描每一個辦理了登機手續的箱包。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a computer disk <b>is scanned</b>, a program on the computer checks the disk to make sure that it does not contain a virus. 掃描 (計算機磁碟以查病毒)","examples":["Not all ISPs are equipped to scan for viruses. 並非所有的因特網服務供應商都有裝備來掃描病毒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a picture or document <b>is scanned</b> into a computer, a machine passes a beam of light over it to make a copy of it in the computer. 掃描 (圖片或檔案)","examples":["The entire paper contents of all libraries will eventually be scanned into computers. 所有圖書館的全部紙質內容最終都會被掃描進電腦。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a radar or sonar machine <b>scans</b> an area, it examines or searches it by sending radar or sonar beams over it. (用雷達或聲納波束) 掃描","examples":["The ship's radar scanned the sea ahead. 船上的雷達掃描了前方海域。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scan</b> is also a noun. 瀏覽","examples":["I just had a quick scan through your book again. 我剛剛把你的書又作了一次瀏覽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scan</b> is a medical test in which a machine sends a beam of X-rays over a part of your body in order to check that it is healthy. (身體) 掃描檢查","examples":["A brain scan revealed the blood clot. 腦部掃描檢查發現了那個血塊。"]}]}]},"scroll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（供書寫的）長卷紙，卷軸；一卷古書（或公文、檔案）；（繪製或雕刻的）渦卷形裝飾；印上格言（或題字）的絲帶的描繪；（影片顯示器螢幕上為檢視新資料而設的）顯示滾動裝置"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"滾屏，滾動；使像紙卷合（或開啟）那樣移動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scroll</b> is a long roll of paper or a similar material with writing on it. (寫有文字的) 卷軸","examples":["Ancient scrolls were found in caves by the Dead Sea. 在死海邊的洞穴裡發現了古代的卷軸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scroll</b> is a painted or carved decoration made to look like a scroll. 卷軸形裝飾","examples":["...a handsome suite of chairs incised with Grecian scrolls. …一套漂亮的刻有古希臘式卷軸形裝飾的椅子。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scroll</b> through text on a computer screen, you move the text up or down to find the information that you need. (在計算機螢幕上的文字中) 滾動","examples":["I scrolled down to find \"United States of America.\" 我向下滾動以尋找。"]}]}]},"scent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香味，芳香；（動物或人的）氣味，臭跡；香水；察覺，預示；線索，蹤跡；<古>嗅覺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……帶有某種香味；（動物）嗅出，聞到；預感，覺察"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>scent</b> of something is the pleasant smell that it has. 香味","examples":["Flowers are chosen for their scent as well as their look. 花兒不僅憑外觀也憑香味而被選中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Scent</b> is a liquid which women put on their necks and wrists to make themselves smell nice. 香水","examples":["She dabbed herself with scent. 她在自己身上擦了點香水。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>scent</b> of a person or animal is the smell that they leave and that other people sometimes follow when looking for them. (人的) 氣味; (動物留下的) 臭跡","examples":["A police dog picked up the murderer's scent. 一條警犬嗅出了兇手的氣味。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>scents</b> a place or thing, it makes it smell pleasant. 使充滿香味","examples":["Jasmine flowers scent the air. 茉莉花使空氣充滿芳香。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an animal <b>scents</b> something, it becomes aware of it by smelling it. 嗅到","examples":["...dogs which scent the hidden birds. …嗅到隱藏的鳥的狗。"]}]}]},"sculptor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雕刻家，雕塑家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sculptor</b> is someone who creates sculptures. 雕塑家","examples":[]}]}]},"scrap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（紙、布等的）碎片，小塊；絲毫，一丁點；廢品，廢棄材料（=scrap metal）；吃剩的東西，殘羹剩飯（scraps）；<非正式>小摩擦，小口角；<英，非正式>極瘦小的人（常指小孩）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因不切實際而）放棄，拋棄（計劃、體系）；把（舊機器、舊汽車等當）作廢料處理，報廢；<非正式>打架，吵架；激烈競爭"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（金屬、紙張）廢棄的，報廢的；零碎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scrap</b> <b>of</b> something is a very small piece or amount of it. 小塊; 碎片","examples":["A crumpled scrap of paper was found in her handbag. 在她的手提包裡找到了一張弄皺的小紙片。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Scraps</b> are pieces of unwanted food which are thrown away or given to animals. 殘羹剩飯","examples":["...the scraps from the Sunday dinner table. …週日餐桌上的殘羹剩飯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Scrap</b> is metal from old or damaged machinery or cars. 廢金屬","examples":["Thousands of tanks, artillery pieces and armoured vehicles will be cut up for scrap. 成千上萬的坦克、大炮和裝甲車將被切割成廢金屬。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a fight or a quarrel as a <b>scrap</b>, especially if it is not very serious. 打架; 鬥嘴","examples":["He had suffered a mild concussion in a scrap for a loose ball. 在一次爭球引起的打架中他被打成輕度腦震盪。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scrap</b> something, you get rid of it or cancel it. 取消; 放棄","examples":["President Hussein called on all countries in the Middle East to scrap nuclear or chemical weapons. 侯賽因總統呼籲中東各國放棄核武器或化學武器。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scrap</b> metal or paper is no longer wanted for its original purpose, but may have some other use. 廢棄的; 剩餘的","examples":["There's always tons of scrap paper in Dad's office. 爸爸的辦公室裡總有大量的廢紙。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scrap</b> is also a verb. 打架; 鬥嘴","examples":["Our guys scrapped and competed and went right to the wire. 我們的小夥子們一邊吵著，一邊比賽，一直到比賽結束。"]}]}]},"scheme":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（政府或其他組織的）計劃，方案；（用於組織或整理資訊的）系統，體系；組合，佈局；陰謀，詭計；<蘇格蘭，非正式>社會住宅區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"密謀，策劃；<南非，非正式>認為，猜想；按色調佈置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scheme</b> is someone's plan for achieving something, especially something that will bring them some benefit. 計劃","examples":["...a quick money-making scheme to get us through the summer. …一個能讓我們迅速賺到錢以順利度過這個夏季的計劃。","They would first have to work out some scheme for getting the treasure out. 他們首先得想出某種計劃把珍寶取出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scheme</b> is a plan or arrangement involving many people which is made by a government or other organization. (政府或其他機構的) 大規模計劃","examples":["...a private pension scheme. …一個私人養老金計劃。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that people <b>are scheming</b>, you mean that they are making secret plans in order to gain something for themselves. 密謀","examples":["Everyone's always scheming and plotting. 每個人時刻都在算計和謀劃。","The bride's family were scheming to prevent a wedding. 新娘的家人在密謀阻止婚禮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people talk about <b>the scheme of things</b> or <b>the grand scheme of things</b>, they are referring to the way that everything in the world seems to be organized. 天地萬物的格局","examples":["We realize that we are infinitely small within the scheme of things. 我們認識到在大千世界中我們是極其渺小的。"]}]}]},"scramble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（迅速而吃力地）爬，攀登；不規則地生長；匆忙地移動；倉促完成（困難的事）；匆忙穿（衣）（scramble into）；爭奪，搶奪；變換……的無線電訊號，倒換……的頻率；擾亂（思維）；炒蛋；命令（飛機）緊急起飛，緊急起飛；（四分衛）持球跑進；打亂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"攀爬，爬行；（互相推撞的）爭奪，爭搶；（因趕任務出現的）忙亂，亂作一團；<英> 摩托車越野賽；（四分衛的）持球跑進；戰鬥機緊急起飛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scramble</b> over rocks or up a hill, you move quickly over them or up it using your hands to help you. 攀爬","examples":["Tourists were scrambling over the rocks looking for the perfect camera angle. 旅行者們爬上岩石，尋找最完美的拍攝角度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>scramble</b> to a different place or position, you move there in a hurried, awkward way. 倉促行動","examples":["Ann threw back the covers and scrambled out of bed. 安掀開被子，急忙下了床。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a number of people <b>scramble</b> <b>for</b> something, they compete energetically with each other for it. 爭奪","examples":["More than three million fans are expected to scramble for tickets. 預計會有三百萬以上的歌迷搶購門票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>scramble</b> eggs, you break them, mix them together and then cook them in butter. 炒 (蛋)","examples":["Make the toast and scramble the eggs. 烤麵包，炒雞蛋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a device <b>scrambles</b> a radio or telephone message, it interferes with the sound so that the message can only be understood by someone with special equipment. 對 (無線電或電話訊號) 作擾頻處理","examples":["The system lets you encrypt or scramble the data that's sent between machines. 這個系統可以讓你對機器間互發的資料作加密或擾頻處理。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Scramble</b> is also a noun. 爭奪","examples":["...the scramble for jobs. …工作的競爭。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"炒的","examples":["...scrambled eggs and bacon. …炒蛋和燻鹹肉。"]}]}]},"scrape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用小刀等）刮除；（使）刮擦；擦傷，刮壞；（使）發出刺耳的刮擦聲；勉強維持，艱難地完成；勉強維持生活（scrape by/along）；勉強透過；（艱難地）湊集，積累（scrape sth. together/up）；節儉；挖坑，挖洞； 把頭髮攏在後面（scrape sth. back）；（幽默）不入調地演奏小提琴；<英>在麵包上塗一層薄薄的（黃油，人造黃油）；用程式從網上下載（資料）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擦傷，擦痕；刮擦，刮擦聲；<非正式>困境，窘境；地面空洞處，（尤指鳥求愛、築巢時）在地面挖的洞；<英>塗在麵包上的一層黃油（或麥琪淋）；<非正式>（醫）刮宮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scrape</b> something from a surface, you remove it, especially by pulling a sharp object over the surface. 刮掉","examples":["She went around the car scraping the frost off the windows. 她繞著車刮掉車窗上的霜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>scrapes</b> against something else, it rubs against it, making a noise or causing slight damage. 刮擦","examples":["The only sound is that of knives and forks scraping against china. 惟一的聲音是刀叉刮擦瓷器的聲音。","The car hurtled past us, scraping the wall and screeching to a halt. 那輛汽車從我們身旁疾馳而過，刮擦著牆嘎然停下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>scrape</b> a part of your body, you accidentally rub it against something hard and rough, and damage it slightly. 擦傷","examples":["She stumbled and fell, scraping her palms and knees. 她絆了一跤摔倒了，擦傷了雙掌和雙膝。"]}]}]},"sergeant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（陸軍、海軍陸戰隊或空軍的）中士；（英國的）巡佐，（美國的）警佐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sergeant</b> is a non-commissioned officer of middle rank in the army, marines, or air force. 中士","examples":["A sergeant with a detail of four men came into view. 1名中士率領由4名士兵組成的小分隊進入了視野。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sergeant</b> is an officer with the rank immediately below a captain. 警官","examples":["A police sergeant patrolling the area spotted flames at the shop. 在該地區巡邏的一名警官發現那家商店失火了。"]}]}]},"sensation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感覺，知覺；感覺能力，知覺能力；（某種經歷所產生的）整體感覺，總體印象；轟動，引起轟動的人（或事）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sensation</b> is a physical feeling. 感覺","examples":["Floating can be a very pleasant sensation. 漂浮會給人一種非常愉快的感覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sensation</b> is your ability to feel things physically, especially through your sense of touch. 感覺能力","examples":["The pain was so bad that she lost all sensation. 疼得太厲害了，她完全失去了感覺能力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>sensation</b> to refer to the general feeling or impression caused by a particular experience. (某種經歷所產生的) 整體感覺","examples":["It's a funny sensation to know someone's talking about you in a language you don't understand. 知道有人正用一種你不懂的語言談論你，這種感覺真奇怪。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a person, event, or situation is a <b>sensation</b>, it causes great excitement or interest. 引起轟動的人或事物","examples":["...the film that turned her into an overnight sensation. …讓她一夜成名的影片。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a person, event, or situation causes <b>a sensation</b>, they cause great interest or excitement. 轟動","examples":["She was just 14 when she caused a sensation at the Montreal Olympics. 她在蒙特利爾奧運會上引起轟動時，年僅14歲。"]}]}]},"segment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"部分，片段；（市場）細分的部分；（水果或花自然形成的）瓣，（昆蟲的）節； 球缺，弓形；（直線或弧線上兩點間的）段；（特定廣播或電視節目的）時間段；某一時段單獨播放的節目；音段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分割，劃分；（細胞）分裂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>segment of</b> something is one part of it, considered separately from the rest. 部分","examples":["...the poorer segments of society. …社會中的較貧困階層。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>segment</b> of fruit such as an orange or grapefruit is one of the sections into which it is easily divided. (水果的) 瓣","examples":["Peel all the fruit except the lime and separate into segments. 除了酸橙之外，把所有的水果剝皮並分成瓣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>segment</b> of a circle is one of the two parts into which it is divided when you draw a straight line through it. 圓缺","examples":["The other children stood around the circle, one in each segment. 其他孩子圍著圓圈而站,每一半圈裡站著一個孩子。"]}]}]},"sentiment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀點，看法，情緒；多愁善感，傷感情緒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sentiment</b> that people have is an attitude which is based on their thoughts and feelings. 情緒","examples":["Public sentiment rapidly turned anti-American. 公眾的情緒迅速轉向反美。","He's found growing sentiment for military action. 他已經發現支援軍事行動的情緒在日益增長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sentiment</b> is an idea or feeling that someone expresses in words. 觀點; 感想","examples":["I must agree with the sentiments expressed by John Prescott. 我必須同意約翰·普雷斯科特表達的觀點。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sentiment</b> is feelings such as pity or love, especially for things in the past, and may be considered exaggerated and foolish. 傷感; 感情","examples":["Laura kept that letter out of sentiment. 勞拉出於傷感保留了那封信。"]}]}]},"sensitivity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對細節或質量的）感知，覺察；（對新情況的）靈敏度；敏感，易生氣；多愁善感；體貼，有分寸；小心謹慎；過敏；敏感性，易惹惱人的傾向；（天生的）悟性，敏銳性；表現力；機密性"}],"sections":[]},"sermon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"佈道，講道；<非正式>冗長的說教，訓誡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sermon</b> is a talk on a religious or moral subject that is given by a member of the clergy as part of a church service. 佈道; 講道","examples":["Cardinal Murphy will deliver the sermon on Sunday. 墨菲紅衣主教將在週日佈道。"]}]}]},"series":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"連續，一系列（事件）；（電視、廣播等的）系列片，系列節目；叢書，系列出版物；（兩隊之間的）系列比賽；（電路的）串聯；（同時發行的）一套郵票（或貨幣、硬幣）；（由某一公司推出的）系列產品，（尤指）汽車系列；（年代地層學用語）統；（元素的）系；級數，序列項的總和；有共同特徵的一組語音，系列（音）；音列"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>series</b> <b>of</b> things or events is a number of them that come one after the other. 一連串; 一系列","examples":["...a series of meetings with students and political leaders. …與學生和政治領袖們的一連串會晤。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A radio or television <b>series</b> is a set of programs of a particular kind which have the same title. (廣播或電視的) 系列節目","examples":["...Captain Kirk's chair from the TV series \"Star Trek.\" …電視系列片《星際迷航》中柯克船長的椅子。"]}]}]},"server":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"伺服器；<美>服務生，服務員；上餐用具；發球者；（基督教牧師做禮拜時的）助祭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In computing, a <b>server</b> is part of a computer network which does a particular task, such as storing or processing information, for all or part of the network. 伺服器","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>server</b> is a person who works in a restaurant, serving people with food and drink. 侍者","examples":["A server came by balancing a tray of wineglasses. 一名侍者平穩地託著一托盤葡萄酒杯走了過來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In tennis and badminton, the <b>server</b> is the player whose turn it is to hit the ball or shuttlecock to start play. (網球、羽毛球等的) 發球員","examples":["...the fastest server in tennis. …最快的網球發球手。"]}]}]},"sheriff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國）縣治安官，郡治安官（亦譯警長）；（英格蘭和威爾士）高階郡官（High Sheriff）；（蘇格蘭）郡法院法官；（歷史）郡長（亦作執行吏）；（Sheriff）人名，謝里夫（英、葡、阿拉伯人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the United States, a <b>sheriff</b> is a person who is elected to make sure that the law is obeyed in a particular county. (美國的) 縣治安官","examples":["...the local sheriff. …當地的縣治安官。"]}]}]},"shortcoming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺點，短處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>shortcomings</b> are the faults or weaknesses which they have. 缺點","examples":["Marriages usually break down as a result of the shortcomings of both partners. 婚姻常常因雙方的缺點而破裂。"]}]}]},"setting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某事發生的）環境，場合；（戲劇、小說或電影的）場景，背景；<美>舞臺佈景；（裝置的）檔位；（寶石的）鑲嵌底座；（為詩、禱文等譜寫的）樂曲；（供一人用的）一副餐具"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（小心地）放置；嵌入（表面）；（電影、戲劇、故事等）以……為背景（set 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>setting</b> is a particular place or type of surroundings where something is or takes place. (事件發生的) 背景; 地點","examples":["Rome is the perfect setting for romance. 羅馬是尋求浪漫的最佳地點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>setting</b> is one of the positions to which the controls of a device such as a stove or heater can be adjusted. 擋位","examples":["You can boil the fish fillets on a high setting. 你可以設定在高擋位上煮魚片。"]}]}]},"shrine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"神殿，聖祠，神龕，聖地，神社；紀念地（與逝者或重大事件相關、供人瞻仰的地方，常與 to 連用）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"將……置於神龕內；把……奉為神聖（古舊/文學用法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shrine</b> is a place of worship which is associated with a particular holy person or object. 聖殿","examples":["...the holy shrine of Mecca. …麥加的聖殿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shrine</b> is a place that people visit and treat with respect because it is connected with a dead person or with dead people that they want to remember. 聖地","examples":["The monument has been turned into a shrine to the dead and the missing. 這座紀念碑已經變成了紀念那些過世或失蹤的人的聖地。"]}]}]},"shiver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因寒冷或害怕而）顫抖，哆嗦，發抖"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"顫抖,哆嗦（因寒冷、恐懼、激動等）；寒戰，寒噤（因恐懼或發高燒）（the shivers）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>shiver</b>, your body shakes slightly because you are cold or frightened. (因寒冷或害怕而) 顫抖","examples":["He shivered in the cold. 他在寒冷中發抖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shiver</b> is also a noun. 顫抖","examples":["The emptiness here sent shivers down my spine. 這裡的空寂讓我感到脊背一陣顫慄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a splintered piece 碎片","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to break or cause to break into fragments 打碎","examples":[]}]}]},"shriek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"尖叫；尖叫著說，尖聲說；明顯地不協調；（無生命的東西）發出尖銳刺耳聲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"尖叫，尖聲；<非正式>感嘆號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>shrieks</b>, they make a short, very loud cry, for example, because they are suddenly surprised, are in pain, or are laughing. 尖叫","examples":["She shrieked and leapt from the bed. 她尖叫著從那張床上跳了起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shriek</b> is also a noun. 尖叫","examples":["Sue let out a terrific shriek and leapt out of the way. 蘇發出一聲恐怖的尖叫，跳了出來。"]}]}]},"shrub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"灌木；（尤指摻朗姆酒或白蘭地的）果汁甜酒；<美>果汁露酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"因肯亞英語的影響而發錯音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shrubs</b> are plants that have several woody stems. 灌木","examples":["...flowering shrubs. …開花的灌木。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a mixed drink of rum, fruit juice, sugar, and spice 果汁甜酒","examples":[]}]}]},"shred":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（撕或切的）細條，碎片；極少量，些許；完全毀壞（shreds）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"切碎，撕碎；粉碎銷燬（檔案）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shred</b> something such as food or paper, you cut it or tear it into very small, narrow pieces. 切碎; 撕碎","examples":["They may be shredding documents. 他們也許正在粉碎那些檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you cut or tear food or paper <b>into</b> <b>shreds</b>, you cut or tear it into small, narrow pieces. 碎片; 細條","examples":["Cut the cabbage into fine long shreds. 把這棵捲心菜切成細長條。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there is not a <b>shred</b> <b>of</b> something, there is not even a small amount of it. 一丁點兒","examples":["He said there was not a shred of evidence to support such remarks. 他說沒有一丁點兒支援這些說法的證據。","There is not a shred of truth in the story. 這個故事沒有一點真實性。"]}]}]},"shove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛推，亂擠；連推帶擠地走；<非正式> 隨便放置，亂放（某物）；<非正式>移動身體，挪動身體（以騰出地方）；<非正式>去他的，讓……見鬼"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"猛推"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shove</b> someone or something, you push them with a quick, violent movement. 猛推","examples":["He shoved her out of the way. 他把她推開。","He's the one who shoved me. 他是推我的那個人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shove</b> something somewhere, you push it there quickly and carelessly. 亂塞","examples":["We shoved a copy of the newsletter beneath their door. 我們在他們的門下塞了一份時事通訊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shove</b> is also a noun. 猛推","examples":["She gave Gracie a shove toward the house. 她把格雷西向那所房子猛地一推。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about what you think will happen <b>if</b> <b>push comes to shove</b>, you are talking about what you think will happen if a situation becomes very bad or difficult. 情況不妙時","examples":["If push comes to shove, if you should lose your case in the court, what will you do? 如果情況不妙，你在法庭上輸了官司，你會怎麼辦？"]}]}]},"shield":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盾（牌）；防護物，保護人；盾形紋（徽）章；<美>警徽；盾形獎牌；（頒發盾形獎牌的）比賽；背甲，頭胸甲，龜甲板；（地質）地盾"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護，保衛；遮擋；給……加防護罩；防止（或減少）輻射；（體育運動中）護住（球）；防禦，起保護作用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone which is a <b>shield</b> against a particular danger or risk provides protection from it. 防護物; 保護人","examples":["He used his left hand as a shield against the reflecting sunlight. 他用左手遮擋反射過來的陽光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shield</b> is a large piece of metal or leather which soldiers used to carry to protect their bodies while they were fighting. 盾","examples":["He clanged his sword three times on his shield. 他用他的劍噹噹噹地敲了3下盾。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>shield</b> is a sports prize or badge that is shaped like a shield. 盾形獎章; 盾形徽章","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>shields</b> you <b>from</b> a danger or risk, they protect you from it. 保護","examples":["He shielded his head from the sun with an old sack. 他用一箇舊袋子遮住頭來防曬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>shield</b> your eyes, you put your hand above your eyes to protect them from direct sunlight. 遮擋","examples":["He squinted and shielded his eyes. 他眯著眼並遮住眼睛。"]}]}]},"shudder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因恐懼、寒冷等）發抖，打戰；強烈震動，劇烈抖動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰慄，發抖；強烈的震動，劇烈的抖動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shudder</b>, you shake with fear, horror, or disgust, or because you are cold. (因害怕、恐懼、厭惡或寒冷) 發抖","examples":["Lloyd had urged her to eat caviar. She had shuddered at the thought. 勞埃德已鼓動她吃魚子醬。可她一想到這個就打哆嗦了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a machine or vehicle <b>shudders</b>, it shakes suddenly and violently. (機器或車輛) 劇烈震動","examples":["The train began to pull out of the station – then suddenly shuddered to a halt. 火車開始駛出車站–然後就突然劇烈震動停了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shudder</b> is also a noun. (因害怕、恐懼、厭惡或寒冷而產生的) 發抖","examples":["She gave a violent shudder. 她猛地抖了一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something sends <b>a shudder</b> or <b>shudders</b> through a group of people, it makes them worried or afraid. 擔憂; 害怕","examples":["The next crisis sent a shudder of fear through the UN community. 下一次危機引起了聯合國組織的擔憂。"]}]}]},"shortage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短缺，不足"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>shortage</b> <b>of</b> something, there is not enough of it. 短缺","examples":["A shortage of funds is preventing the UN from monitoring relief. 資金短缺使得聯合國無法監督救濟工作。","Vietnam is suffering from food shortage. 越南正遭受食品短缺之苦。"]}]}]},"shutter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"百葉窗，活動護窗；（照相機的）快門；（風琴的）開閉器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>使停業，使倒閉；關上（窗戶）的百葉窗，合上（建築）的遮光板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shutters</b> are wooden or metal covers fitted on the outside of a window. They can be opened to let in the light, or closed to keep out the sun or the cold. 百葉窗","examples":["She opened the shutters and gazed out over village roofs. 她開啟了百葉窗，朝村裡的房頂望去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>shutter</b> in a camera is the part which opens to allow light through the lens when a photograph is taken. (照相機的) 快門","examples":["There are a few things you should check before pressing the shutter release. 在按快門之前，有幾件事情你應該檢查。"]}]}]},"silkworm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蠶，桑蠶；泛指能吐絲結繭的蛾類幼蟲（如野蠶、柞蠶等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>silkworm</b> is the young form of a Chinese moth and it produces silk. 蠶","examples":[]}]}]},"simmer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"燉，煨；充滿（難以控制的感情，尤指憤怒）；即將爆發，醞釀；息怒，平靜（simmer down）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"小沸，即將沸騰狀態"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>simmer</b> food or when it <b>simmers</b>, you cook it by keeping it at boiling point or just below boiling point. 用文火燉; 煨","examples":["Make an infusion by boiling and simmering the rhubarb and camomile together. 煮燉大黃和黃春菊來熬成濃汁。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Simmer</b> is also a noun. 燉; 煨","examples":["Combine the stock, whole onion and peppercorns in a pan and bring to a simmer. 把高湯料、整個洋蔥和胡椒粒拌入平底鍋內，然後用文火燉。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a conflict or a quarrel <b>simmers</b>, it does not actually happen for a period of time, but eventually builds up to the point where it does. (衝突或爭吵) 醞釀; 趨於激化","examples":["...bitter divisions that have simmered for more than half a century. …醞釀了半個多世紀的嚴重分歧。"]}]}]},"skull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顱骨，頭骨；<非正式>腦袋，頭腦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>擊中（某人的）頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>skull</b> is the bony part of your head which encloses your brain. 顱骨; 頭顱","examples":["Her husband was later treated for a fractured skull. 她丈夫後來因顱骨碎裂而接受治療。"]}]}]},"skeleton":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"骨骼，骨架；梗概，提綱；骨瘦如柴的人（或動物）；（建築物、橋樑等的）框架，骨架；（維持運轉所需的）最少人員，基幹人員；鋼架雪車"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（員工）最基本的，基幹的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>skeleton</b> is the framework of bones in your body. 骨骼","examples":["...a human skeleton. …人體骨骼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>skeleton</b> of something such as a building or a plan is its basic framework. (樓房或計劃的) 構架; 框架","examples":["The town of Rudbar had ceased to exist, with only skeletons of buildings remaining. 魯德巴爾城已不存在，只剩一些建築骨架。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>skeleton</b> staff is the smallest number of staff necessary in order to run an organization or service. 最起碼的 (員工)","examples":["Only a skeleton staff remains to show anyone interested around the site. 只有極少數的員工留下來帶領感興趣的人參觀場地。"]}]}]},"slaughter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對動物的）屠宰；（對人的）屠殺；<非正式>徹底擊敗，一邊倒的比賽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"宰殺（動物）；屠殺，殺戮；<非正式>（在體育比賽中）使慘敗；<非正式>嚴厲批評"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If large numbers of people or animals <b>are slaughtered</b>, they are killed in a way that is cruel or unnecessary. 屠殺","examples":["Thirty four people were slaughtered while lining up to cast their votes. 有34人在排隊投票時遭屠殺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>slaughter</b> animals such as cows and sheep means to kill them for their meat. 屠宰","examples":["Lack of chicken feed means that chicken farms are having to slaughter their stock. 飼料不足意味著養雞場將不得不宰殺雞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slaughter</b> is also a noun. 屠殺","examples":["This was only a small part of a war where the slaughter of civilians was commonplace. 這只是戰爭的一小部分，在戰爭中對平民的屠殺已司空見慣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Slaughter</b> is also a noun. 屠宰","examples":["More than 491,000 sheep were exported for slaughter last year. 去年，超過四十九萬一千隻羊被出口供屠宰。"]}]}]},"slam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）砰地關上；用力一放，使勁一推；猛烈撞擊；猛烈抨擊；突然（或猛然）採取行動；闖，衝；<非正式，美> 輕鬆得分或戰勝（某人）；<美> （電話公司）未經允許接管（電話顧客）的賬單（slamming）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"猛關（或推、摔、撞等），猛摔（或撞等）的聲音；<美> 詩歌朗誦比賽；（橋牌）滿貫；<非正式，美> 監獄（the slam）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slam</b> a door or window or if it <b>slams</b>, it shuts noisily and with great force. 砰地關上; 使勁關上","examples":["She slammed the door and locked it behind her. 她砰地關上門，身後的門鎖上了。","I was relieved to hear the front door slam. 聽到前門砰地一聲關上，我才放下了心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>slam</b> something <b>down</b>, you put it there quickly and with great force. 摔; 使勁扔","examples":["She listened in a mixture of shock and anger before slamming the phone down. 她震驚而氣憤地聽著，隨後啪地掛上電話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>slam</b> someone or something means to criticize them very severely. 嚴厲批評; 猛烈抨擊","examples":["The famed filmmaker slammed the claims as \"an outrageous lie.\" 該享有盛名的電影製片人猛烈抨擊這些說法，稱其為“無恥讕言。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If one thing <b>slams</b> into or against another, it crashes into it with great force. 猛烈撞擊","examples":["The plane slammed into the building after losing an engine shortly after take-off. 飛機起飛後不久便失去一個引擎，猛地撞到那棟建築物上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act or noise of slamming 猛擊; 撞擊的聲音","examples":[]}]}]},"snarl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"齜牙狂吠；咆哮著說；（使）纏結；妨礙，使（交通等）堵塞；（敲打金屬製品底部）打出凸起花紋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動物的）呲牙低吼；憤怒叫嚷（聲），咆哮（聲）；纏結物；混亂，堵塞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an animal <b>snarls</b>, it makes a fierce, rough sound in its throat while showing its teeth. (動物) 露齒嗥叫","examples":["He raced ahead up into the bush, barking and snarling. 它向前衝進了樹叢，又吠又嗥叫的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Snarl</b> is also a noun. 露齒嗥叫","examples":["With a snarl, the second dog made a dive for his heel. 伴著一聲嗥叫，第二條狗撲向了他的腳後跟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a vicious growl, utterance, or facial expression 咆哮; 嗥叫; 作嗥叫狀","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to speak or express (something) viciously or angrily 咆哮地","examples":[]}]}]},"slap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用手掌）打，拍；拍打，拍擊；（尤指生氣地）啪的一聲放下，隨意扔放；（快速地、隨意地或用力地）塗抹（某物）；甩擊；侮辱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"拍，掌擊；掌擊聲，拍打聲；<英，非正式>（厚厚地或隨意塗抹的）化妝品；侮辱"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式> 直接地，猛然；<非正式> 恰好，正好"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精力不足的，效率不高的；（食物）鬆軟的，過於柔軟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slap</b> someone, you hit them with the palm of your hand. 摑; (用手掌) 拍打","examples":["He would push or slap her once in a while. 他時不時地推搡她，或是打她耳光。","I slapped him hard across the face. 我重重地打了他一記耳光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>slap</b> something <b>onto</b> a surface, you put it there quickly, roughly, or carelessly. 重重放下; 摔; 摜","examples":["He emptied his drink and slapped the money on the bar. 他喝光了飲料，然後把錢摔在吧檯上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If journalists say that the authorities <b>slap</b> something such as a tax or a ban <b>on</b> something, they think it is unreasonable or put on without careful thought. (無理地或者盲目地) 強加","examples":["The government slapped a ban on the export of unprocessed logs. 政府強制禁止出口未加工過的木料。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slap</b> is also a noun. 摑; 拍打","examples":["He reached forward and gave her a slap. 他走上前去，給了她一個耳光。"]}]}]},"sneaker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>球鞋，運動鞋；卑鄙者；鬼鬼祟祟做事的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sneakers</b> are casual shoes with rubber soles that people wear often for running or other sports. 運動鞋","examples":[]}]}]},"slump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（價格、價值、數量等）驟降，猛跌；慘敗，猛跌；（因無力站立而）倒下，倚，靠；（肩或腦袋）耷拉著"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（價格、銷售額、利潤等的）突然下跌；（經濟的）不景氣，蕭條；（運動員或運動隊的）低迷期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as the value of something <b>slumps</b>, it falls suddenly and by a large amount. (價值等) 暴跌","examples":["Net profits slumped by 41%. 淨利潤暴跌了41%。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slump</b> is also a noun. (價值等的) 暴跌","examples":["The council's land is now worth much less than originally hoped because of a slump in property prices. 由於地產價格的暴跌，委員會的土地目前大不如原來所希望的那麼值錢了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slump</b> is a time when many people in a country are unemployed and poor. 經濟蕭條時期","examples":["...the slump of the early 1980s. …20世紀80年代初期的經濟蕭條時期。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slump</b> somewhere, you fall or sit down there heavily, for example, because you are very tired or you feel ill. 癱倒; (因勞累或生病等) 跌坐","examples":["She slumped into a chair. 她癱倒在一張椅子上。"]}]}]},"snatch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"一把抓住，立馬奪下；奪去，搶走；抓住機會做（某事）；僥倖獲得（勝利），險勝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"搶奪，偷竊；（歌曲或談話的）片段；片刻，一會兒；（舉重）抓舉；<非正式>（女性的）陰部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>snatch</b> something or <b>snatch</b> <b>at</b> something, you take it or pull it away quickly. 迅速拿走; 奪取","examples":["Mick snatched the cards from Archie's hand. 米克一把奪過阿徹手裡的牌。","He snatched up the telephone. 他一把抓起了電話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is snatched</b> from you, it is stolen, usually using force. If a person <b>is snatched</b>, they are taken away by force. 強搶","examples":["If your bag is snatched, let it go. 如果你的包被搶走，就隨它去吧。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>snatch</b> an opportunity, you take it quickly. If you <b>snatch</b> something to eat or a rest, you have it quickly in between doing other things. 抓緊 (時機或時間)","examples":["I snatched a glance at the mirror. 我乘機瞥了一眼鏡子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>snatch</b> victory in a competition, you defeat your opponent by a small amount or just before the end of the contest. 僥倖獲得","examples":["The American came from behind to snatch victory by a mere eight seconds. 美國隊後來居上，僅以8秒鐘的優勢贏得了勝利。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snatch</b> <b>of</b> a conversation or a song is a very small piece of it. (談話或歌曲的) 片斷","examples":["I heard snatches of the conversation. 我聽到幾段零星的談話。"]}]}]},"sneak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偷偷地走，潛行；偷帶，私運；<非正式>偷走（不重要的或小的東西）；偷偷地做（或獲得）；<英>（尤作兒童用語）打小報告，告密"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>打小報告的人，告狀者（尤指兒童）；<非正式>鬼鬼祟祟的人；四分衛快速帶球切入；<美，非正式>旅遊鞋，軟幫運動鞋；偷偷摸摸的行為"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"出其不意的，偷偷摸摸的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sneak</b> somewhere, you go there very quietly on foot, trying to avoid being seen or heard. 偷偷地走","examples":["Sometimes he would sneak out of his house late at night to be with me. 有時候他會在深夜偷偷溜出他的家來陪伴我。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sneak</b> something somewhere, you take it there secretly. 偷偷地拿","examples":["He smuggled papers out each day, photocopied them, and snuck them back. 他每天都把檔案偷帶出來，影印後又偷偷送回去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sneak</b> a look at someone or something, you secretly have a quick look at them. 偷偷地看","examples":["You sneak a look at your watch to see how long you've got to wait. 你偷偷看一眼手錶，看還要等多久。"]}]}]},"smash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打碎，（使）粉碎；（使）猛擊，（使）猛撞；（用力）撞開，闖過；擊潰，使結束；撞毀，撞壞（交通工具）；（網球等比賽中）扣球，打高壓球；（輕鬆）打破（記錄）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"猛烈撞擊聲，破碎時的嘩啦聲；猛擊；<英，非正式>撞車，車禍；（網球運動中的）高壓球，扣球；<非正式>大獲成功的歌曲（或戲劇、電影）（=smash hit）；（由白蘭地、果味水和冰混合調製的）斯馬喜（混合烈酒）飲料；<非正式，舊>破產，投資失敗"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"嘩啦一聲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非常轟動的，出色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smash</b> something or if it <b>smashes</b>, it breaks into many pieces, for example, when it is hit or dropped. 打碎; 破碎","examples":["Someone smashed a bottle. 有人打碎了一個瓶子。","A crowd of youths started smashing windows. 一群年輕人開始打碎窗戶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>smash</b> through a wall, gate, or door, you get through it by hitting and breaking it. 撞破 (牆或門) 而入","examples":["The demonstrators used trucks to smash through embassy gates. 示威者們用卡車撞破大門闖進大使館。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>smashes</b> or <b>is smashed</b> against something solid, it moves very fast and with great force against it. 使猛撞; 撞擊","examples":["The bottle smashed against a wall. 那瓶子撞到了一面牆上。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>smash</b> a political group or system means to deliberately destroy it. 搞垮 (政治集團或體制)","examples":["Their attempts to clean up politics and smash the power of party machines failed. 他們整治政治和搞垮黨派組織權力的企圖失敗了。"]}]}]},"snore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打鼾"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鼾聲，呼嚕聲；<非正式>乏味的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone who is asleep <b>snores</b>, they make a loud noise each time they breathe. 打鼾","examples":["His mouth was open, and he was snoring. 他張著嘴巴，打著鼾。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Snore</b> is also a noun. 打鼾","examples":["Uncle Arthur, after a loud snore, woke suddenly. 阿瑟大叔響亮地打了個鼾後，突然醒了過來。"]}]}]},"snort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"噴鼻息，發哼聲（常表示輕蔑、憤怒或好笑）；噴出蒸汽聲"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"發哼聲表示，以哼聲說出；噴出（蒸汽、煙氣等）；用鼻子吸食（毒品）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"噴鼻息，哼聲，嗤笑；<非正式>一小杯酒（尤指烈酒）；（電腦保安） Snort（開源網路入侵檢測與防禦系統）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people or animals <b>snort</b>, they breathe air noisily out through their noses. People sometimes snort in order to express disapproval or amusement. 噴鼻息 (有時表示不贊同或可笑)","examples":["Harrell snorted with laughter. 哈雷爾撲哧一聲笑了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Snort</b> is also a noun. 噴鼻息","examples":["...snorts of laughter. …陣陣嗤笑聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>snort</b> a drug such as cocaine means to breathe it in quickly through your nose. 用鼻子吸食 (毒品)","examples":["He died of cardiac arrest after snorting cocaine at a party. 在一次聚會上鼻吸了可卡因之後，他死於心臟停搏。"]}]}]},"sniff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（出聲地）以鼻吸氣，抽鼻子（如因哭泣或感冒）；嗅，聞；嗤之以鼻地說，輕蔑地說；吸入（氣體或毒品）；嗅到，察覺出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽鼻子，哼；吸入的空氣（或其他物質）；氣味；線索，跡象；輕蔑，厭惡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>sniff</b>, you breathe in air through your nose hard enough to make a sound, for example, when you are trying not to cry, or in order to show disapproval. 抽鼻子 (用來忍住哭聲或表示不贊同)","examples":["She wiped her face and sniffed loudly. 她擦擦臉，大聲地抽著鼻子。","Then he sniffed. There was a smell of burning. 然後他抽了抽鼻子。空氣裡有一股燒焦的味道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sniff</b> is also a noun. 抽鼻子聲","examples":["At last the sobs ceased, to be replaced by sniffs. 最後嗚咽聲終於停止了，取而代之的是抽鼻子的聲音。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sniff</b> something or <b>sniff at</b> it, you smell it by sniffing. (吸著氣) 聞","examples":["Suddenly, he stopped and sniffed the air. 突然他停下來，嗅了嗅空氣中的味道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>sniff</b> to indicate that someone says something in a way that shows their disapproval or contempt. 嗤之以鼻地說","examples":["\"Tourists!\" she sniffed. “觀光客！”她鄙夷地說。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>not to be sniffed at</b>, you think it is very good or worth having. If someone <b>sniffs at</b> something, they do not think it is good enough, or they express their contempt for it. 輕視","examples":["The salary was not to be sniffed at either. 當時的工資也是不容輕視的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>sniffs</b> a substance such as glue, they deliberately breathe in the substance or the gases from it as a drug. 用鼻子吸","examples":["He felt light-headed, as if he'd sniffed glue. 他覺得頭暈，好像吸了膠毒一樣。"]}]}]},"solo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單獨的，獨自的；獨奏的，單人表演的；（擊球時）壘上無跑壘員的；（摩托車）沒有跨斗的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"單人表演，單飛，獨自完成的事情；單人紙牌戲，惠斯特紙牌戲；惠斯特紙牌戲中為贏五圈牌的叫牌；沒有跨斗的摩托車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"獨奏，獨唱；單獨飛行；單人攀登"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"單獨地，獨自地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>solo</b> to indicate that someone does something alone rather than with other people. 單獨的","examples":["He had just completed his final solo album. 他剛剛完成他最後一張個人專輯。","...Daniel Amokachi's spectacular solo goal. …丹尼爾•阿莫卡奇精彩的個人進球得分。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Solo</b> is also an adverb. 單獨地","examples":["Charles Lindbergh became the very first person to fly solo across the Atlantic. 查爾斯•林白成為第一個單獨飛越大西洋的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>solo</b> is a piece of music or a dance performed by one person. 獨奏曲; 獨舞","examples":["The original version featured a guitar solo. 原版以吉他獨奏為特色。"]}]}]},"solitary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨自的，單獨的；偏僻的，孤立的；獨自完成的；（人或動物）獨處的，獨居的；（花或其他部分）單生的；唯一的，僅有的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"單獨監禁；獨居者，隱士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or animal that is <b>solitary</b> spends a lot of time alone. 獨處的","examples":["Paul was a shy, pleasant, solitary man. 保羅是個靦腆的、討人喜歡的、慣於獨處的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>solitary</b> activity is one that you do alone. 獨自的","examples":["His evenings were spent in solitary drinking. 他的每個夜晚都在獨自飲酒中度過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>solitary</b> person or object is alone, with no others near them. 孤獨的","examples":["You could see the occasional solitary figure making a study of wildflowers or grasses. 你偶爾可以看見那個研究野生花草的孤獨身影。"]}]}]},"spaceship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宇宙飛船"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spaceship</b> is a spacecraft that carries people through space. 載人宇宙飛船","examples":["...an alien spaceship. …一艘外星人的宇宙飛船。"]}]}]},"spacecraft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宇宙飛船，航天器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spacecraft</b> is a rocket or other vehicle that can travel in space. 航天器","examples":["...the world's largest and most expensive unmanned spacecraft. …世界上最大、最貴的無人航天器。"]}]}]},"soak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"浸泡；使溼透，浸溼；（液體）滲入，滲透；（在浴缸裡）長時間泡浴；<非正式>向……敲竹槓（徵重稅）；吸收，吸入；沉浸在（學習中）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"浸泡，浸透；（長時間的）泡浴，洗澡；<非正式>酒鬼；<澳新>積水窪地，水窪；<英，非正式>大雨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>soak</b> something or leave it <b>to</b> <b>soak</b>, you put it into a liquid and leave it there. 浸泡","examples":["Soak the beans for 2 hours. 把豆子泡上兩個小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a liquid <b>soaks</b> something or if you <b>soak</b> something <b>with</b> a liquid, the liquid makes the thing very wet. 使浸溼","examples":["The water had soaked his jacket and shirt. 水浸溼了他的夾克和襯衣。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid <b>soaks</b> <b>through</b> something, it passes through it. 滲透","examples":["There was so much blood it had soaked through my boxer shorts. 血出得太多，都滲透了我的平腳短褲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>soaks</b>, they spend a long time in a hot bath, because they enjoy it. 長時間泡浴","examples":["What I need is to soak in a hot tub. 我需要的是在浴盆裡泡個熱水澡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Soak</b> is also a noun. 泡浴","examples":["I was having a long soak in the bath. 我當時正在浴室裡長時間地泡浴。"]}]}]},"sovereign":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"君主，元首；金鎊（舊時英國金幣，面值一英鎊）；獨立國"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（國家）有主權的，完全獨立的；掌握全部權力的，有至高無上的權力的；首要的；非常好的，非常有效的；不折不扣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sovereign</b> state or country is independent and not under the authority of any other country. 具有獨立主權的","examples":["Lithuania and Armenia signed a treaty in Vilnius recognizing each other as independent sovereign states. 立陶宛和亞美尼亞在維爾紐斯簽訂了一份互相承認各自為獨立主權國家的協定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sovereign</b> is used to describe the person or institution that has the highest power in a country. (人或機構的權力) 至高無上的","examples":["Sovereign power will continue to lie with the Supreme People's Assembly. 至高無上的權力將繼續掌控在最高人民議會。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sovereign</b> is a king, queen, or other royal ruler of a country. 君主","examples":["In March 1889, she became the first British sovereign to set foot on Spanish soil. 1889年3月，她成為首位踏上西班牙國土的英國君主。"]}]}]},"specimen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樣品，標本；（尤指動植物的）例項；（化驗的）抽樣，血樣，尿樣；具有……特性的人（幽默用法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>specimen</b> is a single plant or animal which is an example of a particular species or type and is examined by scientists. (動植物的) 標本","examples":["200,000 specimens of fungus are kept at the Komarov Botanical Institute. 20萬個真菌標本被儲存在科馬羅夫植物研究所。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>specimen</b> <b>of</b> something is an example of it which gives an idea of what the whole of it is like. 樣本","examples":["Job applicants have to submit a specimen of handwriting. 求職者必須提交一份筆跡樣本。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>specimen</b> is a small quantity of someone's urine, blood, or other body fluid which is examined in a medical laboratory, in order to find out if they are ill or if they have been drinking alcohol or taking drugs. (供檢驗用的尿液、血液等的) 抽樣","examples":["He refused to provide a specimen. 他拒絕提供抽樣。"]}]}]},"splendor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壯麗，壯觀；美景，讓人印象深刻的事物（splendors）"}],"sections":[]},"specialist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專家；專科醫生；美國陸軍專業人員（高於一等兵低於下士的軍銜）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"專業的；專門的；專家的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>specialist</b> is a person who has a particular skill or knows a lot about a particular subject. 專家","examples":["Peckham, himself a cancer specialist, is well aware of the wide variations in medical practice. 佩卡姆本人就是個癌症專家，非常清楚醫療實踐中的廣泛差異。"]}]}]},"spectator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指體育比賽的）觀看者，觀眾；旁觀者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spectator</b> is someone who watches something, especially a sports event. (尤指體育賽事的) 觀眾","examples":["Thirty thousand spectators watched the final game. 3萬觀眾觀看了那場決賽。"]}]}]},"spectacle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精彩的表演，壯觀的場面；壯觀的景象；不尋常的事，出人意料的情況；<正式>眼鏡（spectacles）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spectacle</b> is a strange or interesting sight. 奇觀","examples":["It was a spectacle not to be missed. 它是不可錯過的奇觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spectacle</b> is a grand and impressive event or performance. 盛大的活動; 盛大的演出","examples":["Ninety-four thousand people turned up for the spectacle. 9.4萬人參加了這個盛大的活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Glasses are sometimes referred to as <b>spectacles</b>. 眼鏡","examples":["He looked at me over the tops of his spectacles. 他從眼鏡的上方看了看我。"]}]}]},"sole":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"唯一的，僅有的；專用的，獨享的；<古>（尤指女性）未婚的；<古>單獨的，沒人陪伴的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳底；鞋底（不包括後跟）；腳趾和腳弓之間的部分；（刨子等工具的）底部，（高爾夫球棒頭的）底端；（船艙或駕駛室的）地面，地板；鰨（魚）； 腳底"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（鞋）換底"}],"sections":[]},"spine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"脊髓，脊柱；書脊；（動植物的）刺，刺毛；中心力量，中流砥柱；骨氣，勇氣；直線型薪酬級別制；（地質）火山栓，熔岩塔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>spine</b> is the row of bones down your back. 脊柱","examples":["...injuries to his spine. …對他的脊柱的創傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>spine</b> of a book is the narrow stiff part which the pages and covers are attached to. (書) 脊","examples":["...a book with \"Lifestyle\" on the spine. …一本脊上印有“生活方式”的書。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Spines</b> are also long, sharp points on an animal's body or on a plant. (動物的) 刺毛; (植物的) 刺","examples":["An adult hedgehog can boast 7,500 spines. 一隻成年刺蝟能有多達7500根刺。"]}]}]},"spotlight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聚光燈，反光燈；媒體和公眾的注意；聚光燈照明圈"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"聚光照明；使公眾注意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spotlight</b> is a powerful light, for example in a theatre, which can be directed so that it lights up a small area. (劇院等的) 聚光燈","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>spotlights</b> a particular problem or situation, it makes people notice it and think about it. 使備受關注","examples":["The budget crisis also spotlighted a weakening economy. 預算危機也使日益衰弱的經濟備受關注。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>in the spotlight</b> is getting a great deal of public attention. 矚目中","examples":["Webb is back in the spotlight. 韋布又重新受到矚目。"]}]}]},"sprint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"衝刺，短跑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"衝刺，快跑；短跑比賽，短距離速度競賽；（速度、能量或活動的）突然爆發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The sprint</b> is a short, fast running race. 短跑賽","examples":["Rob Harmeling won the sprint in Bordeaux. 羅布•哈梅林贏得了波爾多短跑賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sprint</b> is a short race in which the competitors run, drive, ride, or swim very fast. (跑、駕車、騎馬、游泳等) 短程賽","examples":["Lewis will compete in both sprints in Stuttgart. 劉易斯將參加在斯圖加特舉行的兩項短程賽。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>A sprint</b> is a fast run that someone does, either at the end of a race or because they are in a hurry. 衝刺; 快跑","examples":["Gilles Delion, of France, won the Tour of Lombardy in a sprint finish at Monza yesterday. 法國選手吉勒斯·德利翁昨天在蒙扎最後衝刺時贏得了倫巴第巡迴賽冠軍。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sprint</b>, you run or ride as fast as you can over a short distance. 快速奔跑; 衝刺","examples":["Sergeant Horne sprinted to the car. 霍恩中士衝向那輛汽車。"]}]}]},"sponge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（擦洗用的天然或人造的）海綿塊；（用海綿或布）擦拭，擦洗；海綿蛋糕，鬆軟布丁；依賴他人生活的寄生蟲，揩油者；海綿（一種海洋軟體動物）；（女用）避孕海綿；海綿填料；金屬綿"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用海綿擦洗；用溼布（或海綿）擦掉，揩去；白吃，揩油；用海綿抹（漆）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sponge</b> is a very light soft substance with lots of little holes in it, which can be either artificial or natural. It is used to clean things or as a soft layer. 海綿","examples":["...a sponge mattress. …一張海綿床墊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sponge</b> is a piece of sponge that you use for washing yourself or for cleaning things. (洗澡或清潔用的) 海綿塊","examples":["He wiped off the table with a sponge. 他用一塊海綿擦了桌子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sponge</b> is a light cake or pudding made from flour, eggs, sugar, and sometimes shortening. 鬆軟蛋糕; 鬆軟布丁","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sponge</b> something, you clean it by wiping it with a wet sponge. 用溼海綿擦拭","examples":["Fill a bowl with water and gently sponge your face and body. 裝滿一碗水，然後用溼海綿輕輕擦洗你的臉和身子。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sponge down</b> means the same as . 用溼海綿擦洗","examples":["If your child's temperature rises, sponge her down gently with tepid water. 如果你孩子的體溫升高，用溼海綿沾溫水輕輕地擦洗她。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>sponges off</b> other people or <b>sponges on</b> them, you mean that they regularly get money from other people when they should be trying to support themselves. 揩油","examples":["He should just get an honest job and stop sponging off the rest of us! 他就應該找一份踏實的工作，不要再揩我們其他人的油了！"]}]}]},"squat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"蹲坐；擅自佔用（建築物或土地）；<澳新，史>佔用王室土地來放牧牛羊；（舉重）蹲舉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蹲坐；被非法佔用的建築物；非法佔用空屋；<美，非正式>幾乎沒有（常用於否定句中作強調）；（舉重）蹲舉訓練；（體操）下蹲動作；俯撐腿屈伸（雙手撐地下蹲後雙腿同時前後跳動）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"矮胖的，粗矮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>squat</b>, you lower yourself toward the ground, balancing on your feet with your legs bent. 蹲下","examples":["We squatted beside the pool and watched the diver sink slowly down. 我們蹲在池邊，看潛水員慢慢沉下水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People who <b>squat</b> occupy an unused building or unused land without having a legal right to do so. (對某空建築、空地) 非法佔據","examples":["You can't simply wander around squatting on other people's property. 你不能只是四處遊蕩，非法佔據他人房產。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Squat down</b> means the same as . 蹲下","examples":["Albert squatted down and examined it. 阿爾伯特蹲下仔細檢視它。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Squat</b> is also a noun. 蹲下","examples":["He bent to a squat and gathered the puppies on his lap. 他彎腰蹲下，把小狗們聚攬到他的大腿上。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>squat</b>, you mean they are short and thick, usually in an unattractive way. 矮胖的","examples":["Eddie was a short squat fellow in his forties with thinning hair. 埃迪是個矮胖的人，四十來歲，頭髮稀疏。"]}]}]},"stagger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"搖搖晃晃地走，蹣跚；使震驚，使大吃一驚；使交錯，使錯開"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"踉蹌，蹣跚；使（物體，物體的組成部分）交錯排列；賽跑選手起跑時的梯形排列"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"交錯的，錯開的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stagger</b>, you walk very unsteadily, for example because you are ill or drunk. (因生病、醉酒等) 搖晃地走; 蹣跚","examples":["He lost his balance, staggered back against the rail and toppled over. 他失去了平衡，向後趔趄撞在了欄杆上摔倒了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>staggers</b> you, it surprises you very much. 使震驚","examples":["The whole thing staggers me. 整件事讓我震驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>stagger</b> things such as people's holiday or hours of work means to arrange them so that they do not all happen at the same time. 錯開 (假期或工作時間)","examples":["During the past few years the university has staggered the summer holiday periods for students. 在過去幾年裡該大學已經把學生的暑假時間錯開了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"震驚的","examples":["I was simply staggered by the heat of the Argentinian high-summer. 我只是震驚於阿根廷盛夏的高溫。"]}]}]},"stanza":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩的一節，詩節"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stanza</b> is one of the parts into which a poem is divided. 詩節","examples":[]}]}]},"spur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一時衝動之下，心血來潮；刺激，激勵；山嘴，尖坡；（公路或鐵路的）支線，岔線；馬刺，靴刺"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"激勵，鼓勵；促進，加速，刺激（某事發生）；用馬刺策（馬）前進；緊貼主幹剪短（副梢）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>spurs</b> you <b>to</b> do another, it encourages you to do it. 鼓動; 激勵","examples":["It's the money that spurs these fishermen to risk a long ocean journey in their flimsy boats. 是金錢驅使這些漁民駕駛單薄的小船冒險出海遠航。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>spurs</b> a change or event, it makes it happen faster or sooner. 使更快發生; 加速","examples":["The administration may put more emphasis on spurring economic growth. 政府可能會更加重視經濟的加快增長。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spur on</b> means the same as . 鼓動; 激勵 (同)(spur)","examples":["Their attitude, rather than reining him back, only seemed to spur Philip on. 他們的態度非但沒令菲利普回頭，似乎只是激勵他繼續下去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that acts as a <b>spur</b> <b>to</b> something else encourages a person or organization to do that thing or makes it happen more quickly. 促進因素; 推動","examples":["...a belief in competition as a spur to efficiency. …一種認為競爭能促進效率提高的觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on the spur of the moment</b>, you do it suddenly, without planning it beforehand. 一時衝動之下","examples":["They admitted they had taken a vehicle on the spur of the moment. 他們承認一時衝動之下偷了一輛車。"]}]}]},"statesman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"政治家，國務活動家，治國之才"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>statesman</b> is an important and experienced politician, especially one who is widely known and respected. 政治家","examples":["Hamilton is a great statesman and political thinker. 漢密爾頓是個偉大的政治家和政治思想家。"]}]}]},"stack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（整齊的）一堆；<英> 垛，堆；大量，許多；（尤指工廠的）大煙囪；（圖書館的）藏書架，雙面書架（the stacks）；定高分層盤旋（等待降落）的機群；（計算機）（儲存）棧；豎著置放的高保真音響（或吉他擴音）裝置；（數支步槍支起的錐形）槍架；<英>（浪蝕）巖柱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成整齊的一堆；使成疊（或成摞、成堆）地放在…...；指令（待著陸飛機）作定高分層盤旋；洗牌時作弊；在（某組織機構中）安插（對自己有利的人員）；（滑雪板運動用語）跌倒，倒下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stack</b> <b>of</b> things is a pile of them. 摞; 堆","examples":["There were stacks of books on the bedside table and floor. 床頭桌上和地板上有一摞摞的書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>stacks of</b> something, you mean that they have a lot of it. 堆","examples":["If the job's that good, you'll have stacks of money. 如果那份工作真那麼好，你就會有成堆的錢。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stack</b> a number of things, you arrange them in neat piles. 堆放; 摞起","examples":["Mrs. Cathiard was stacking the clean bottles in crates. 卡提亞夫人當時正在把乾淨的瓶子堆放到板條箱裡。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stack up</b> means the same as . 堆放; 摞起","examples":["He ordered them to stack up pillows behind his back. 他命令他們在他背後堆放一些枕頭。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that <b>the odds are stacked against</b> someone, or that particular factors <b>are stacked against</b> them, you mean that they are unlikely to succeed in what they want to do because the conditions are not favourable. 形勢對某人不利","examples":["The odds are stacked against civilians getting a fair trial. 形勢對想得到公正判決的平民不利。"]}]}]},"stain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（被）玷汙，留下汙漬；給……染色（或著色）；玷汙，敗壞（名聲等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙點，汙漬；染色劑，著色劑；（名聲上的）汙點；（紋章）（紋章和徽章的）輔助色，次要顏色（尤指棕褐色和血紅色）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stain</b> is a mark on something that is difficult to remove. 汙漬","examples":["Remove stains by soaking in a mild solution of bleach. 用溫和的漂白溶液浸泡以去除汙漬。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a liquid <b>stains</b> something, the thing becomes coloured or marked by the liquid. (在某物上) 留下汙漬","examples":["Some foods can stain the teeth, as of course can smoking. 某些食物會使牙齒著色，吸菸當然也會。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沾了汙漬的","examples":["His clothing was stained with mud. 他的衣服沾了泥。"]}]}]},"stall":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貨攤，販賣處，諮詢臺；牲畜棚，馬廄，牛棚；（房間內的）小隔間，淋浴室，洗手間；（教堂內）唱詩班和牧師的座位；<英>（劇場的）正廳前排座位（stalls）；（發動機的）熄火，（車輛的）拋錨，（飛機的）失速，（輪船的）停泊；<美>（機動車停車場的）車位；（賽馬開始前各馬站位的）單間馬房"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）熄火，拋錨；故意拖延（以贏得時間）；拖住（某人）；暫緩，擱置，停頓；（飛機）失速；（航海）（由於風力不夠而）航行失控；把（牲畜）關在廄內（養肥）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a process <b>stalls</b>, or if someone or something <b>stalls</b> it, the process stops but may continue at a later time. 使暫停; 暫停","examples":["The Social Democratic Party has vowed to try to stall the bill until the current session ends. 該社會民主黨已立誓設法暫停該議案直至當前會議結束。","...but the peace process stalled. …但是和平程序暫停了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stall</b> someone, you prevent them from doing something until a later time. 拖住 (某人)","examples":["The shop manager stalled the man until the police arrived. 那個商場經理把那人拖住直到警察趕到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a vehicle <b>stalls</b> or if you accidentally <b>stall</b> it, the engine stops suddenly. 使 (發動機) 突然熄火; (發動機) 突然熄火","examples":["The engine stalled. 發動機突然熄火了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stall</b>, you try to avoid doing something until later. 拖延","examples":["Thomas had spent all week stalling over his decision. 托馬斯花了整週的時間遲遲不做決定。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stall</b> is a large table on which you put goods that you want to sell, or information that you want to give people. 貨攤; 諮詢臺","examples":["...market stalls selling local fruits. …出售當地水果的市場攤位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The stalls</b> in a theatre or concert hall are the seats on the ground floor directly in front of the stage.  舞臺前排座位","examples":["With the balcony blocked off, patrons filled most of the stalls. 樓廳包廂被封閉了，贊助人幾乎坐滿了舞臺前方的座位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>stall</b> is a small enclosed area in a room which is used for a particular purpose, for example a shower.  小隔間","examples":["She went into the shower stall, turned on the water, and grabbed the soap. 她走進淋浴間，開啟水，抓起香皂。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a compartment in a stable or shed for confining or feeding a single animal (馬廄或牛棚裡圈養一個動物的)小隔間","examples":[]}]}]},"statistic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"統計數字，統計資料；統計學（statistics）；（一項）統計資料"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"統計的，統計學的（同 statistical）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Statistics</b> are facts which are obtained from analysing information expressed in numbers, for example information about the number of times that something happens. 統計資料","examples":["Official statistics show real wages declining by 24%. 官方統計資料表明實際工資水平下降了24％。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Statistics</b> is a branch of mathematics concerned with the study of information that is expressed in numbers. 統計學","examples":["...a professor of mathematical statistics. …一位數理統計學教授。"]}]}]},"stake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"股本，股份；樁，標樁，籬笆樁；賭注；賽馬獎金（stakes）；比賽，競賽（stakes）；利害關係；火刑柱；（製作籃子的）縱向基杆，經條；（鐵匠用的）小鐵砧；摩門主教管轄區"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拿…...冒險，以…...打賭；用樁支撐；<美，非正式>資助，幫助"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>at stake</b>, it is being risked and might be lost or damaged if you are not successful. 得失難料","examples":["The tension was naturally high for a game with so much at stake. 一場成敗如此難料的比賽緊張度自然很高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stake a claim</b>, you say that something is yours or that you have a right to it. 提出所有權要求","examples":["Jane is determined to stake her claim as an actress. 簡決心提出她作為一名女演員的應有權利。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>stakes</b> involved in a contest or a risky action are the things that can be gained or lost. (競賽、冒險行為中的) 賭注","examples":["The game was usually played for high stakes between two large groups. 這種遊戲通常是兩大組人為贏得大的賭注而進行的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>stake in</b> something such as a business, it matters to you, for example because you own part of it or because its success or failure will affect you. (商業等中的) 利害關係","examples":["He was eager to return to a more entrepreneurial role in which he had a big financial stake in his own efforts. 他渴望回到更具企業家性質的角色，這樣他的努力就跟自己有大的金融利害關係。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>stakes</b> to refer to something that is like a contest. For example, you can refer to the choosing of a leader as <b>the</b> leadership <b>stakes</b>. 爭奪賽","examples":["We are lagging behind in the childcare stakes. 我們在兒童保育競賽中正落在後面。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>stake</b> is a pointed wooden post which is pushed into the ground, for example in order to support a young tree. 樁","examples":["His arms were tied to wooden stakes to hold him flat. 他的雙臂被綁在木樁上以便使他平躺著。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stake</b> something such as your money or your reputation <b>on</b> the result of something, you risk your money or reputation on it. 以 (金錢、名譽等) 下賭注","examples":["He has staked his political future on an election victory. 他已把他的政治前途賭在了一次選舉獲勝上。"]}]}]},"stewardess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（船舶、飛機或火車上的）女服務員，女乘務員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stewardess</b> is a woman who works on a ship, plane, or train, taking care of passengers and serving meals to them. 女乘務員","examples":[]}]}]},"steward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（飛機、火車或船上的）男服務員，男乘務員；（賽馬、聚會或其他公共活動的）負責人，管事；（金錢、財產等的）管理人，主管；（私人家中的）管家；（大學、俱樂部等機構的）伙食管理員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（官員）管理（大型公共事件）；當……的管家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>steward</b> is a man who works on a ship, plane, or train, taking care of passengers and serving meals to them. 男乘務員","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>steward</b> is a man or woman who helps to organize a race, march, or other public event. (比賽、遊行等公共活動的) 組織者","examples":["The steward at the march stood his ground while the rest of the marchers decided to run. 當其餘的遊行者決定跑掉時，遊行的組織者堅守了他的位置。"]}]}]},"stereotype":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模式化的思想，老一套；公式化人物；鉛版，鉛版澆鑄，鉛版印刷"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……形成刻板的看法，（尤指）對……有成見；使用鉛版"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stereotype</b> is a fixed general image or set of characteristics that a lot of people believe represent a particular type of person or thing. 模式化形象; 成見","examples":["There's always been a stereotype about successful businessmen. 對成功的商人們總有一種成見。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is stereotyped</b> as something, people form a fixed general idea or image of them, so that it is assumed that they will behave in a particular way. 把…模式化; 對…產生成見","examples":["He was stereotyped by some as a renegade. 他被一些人帶著成見視為一名叛逆者。"]}]}]},"stew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"燉煮的菜餚；<非正式>困惑的，焦慮的（in a stew）；<英>魚塘，大魚桶；<美，非正式>（客機的）乘務員；人工牡蠣養殖場；妓院；悶熱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"燉，煨；<非正式>自作自受（stew in one's own juice）；思考，擔憂；<非正式>生氣，發火；<英>消磨時間，無所事事；<英>（茶）（因久泡）變濃變苦；<非正式>處於炎熱（或沉悶）的空氣中；<喻>沉浸於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stew</b> is a meal which you make by cooking meat and vegetables in liquid at a low temperature. 燉煮的菜餚","examples":["She served him a bowl of beef stew. 她給他端了一碗燉牛肉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a fishpond or fishtank 魚塘; 魚缸","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>stew</b> meat, vegetables, or fruit, you cook them slowly in liquid in a covered pot. 燉","examples":["Stew the apple and blackberries to make a thick pulp. 把蘋果和黑莓燉成濃稠的果漿。"]}]}]},"steer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"駕駛（交通工具），掌方向盤；引導，指導（某人的行為）；引導，帶領（某人去某地）；（交通工具）行駛，沿（特定路線或方向）行進；選擇某種做法，採取某種方式；（機動車）容易（或難以）駕駛"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（車輛的）驅動方式；<非正式> 建議，忠告；閹公牛，食用公牛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>steer</b> a car, boat, or plane, you control it so that it goes in the direction that you want. 駕駛","examples":["What is it like to steer a ship this size? 駕駛這樣大小的船會怎麼樣呢？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>steer</b> people toward a particular course of action or attitude, you try to lead them gently in that direction. 引導","examples":["The new government is seen as one that will steer the country in the right direction. 新政府被認為能將這個國家引向正確的方向。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>steer</b> someone in a particular direction, you guide them there. 引領","examples":["Nick steered them into the nearest seats. 尼克領著他們到最近的座位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>steer clear</b> <b>of</b> someone or something, you deliberately avoid them. 有意避開某人/某物","examples":["I think a lot of people, women in particular, steer clear of these sensitive issues. 我認為很多人，尤其是女性，有意避開這些敏感問題。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a castrated male ox or bull; bullock 犍牛; 小公牛","examples":[]}]}]},"stink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發惡臭，有異味；<非正式>極糟糕，令人厭惡；極具（可鄙之事）的味道（stink of）；（令人反感地）大量擁有（某物，尤指金錢），……多得發臭（stink of）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"惡臭，難聞的氣味；<非正式>大吵大鬧，強烈抱怨；<舊>賣力地工作/奔跑/行走"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<西印度>有惡臭的，臭氣熏天的；<西印度>討厭的，腐敗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>stink</b> means to smell very bad. 發臭","examples":["We all stank and nobody minded. 我們大家都很臭，所以也就沒人在乎。","The place stinks of fried onions. 這地方有股難聞的炒洋蔥味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>stinks</b>, you mean that you disapprove of it because it involves ideas, feelings, or practices that you do not like. 令人討厭","examples":["I think their methods stink. 我覺得他們的方法令人討厭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stink</b> is also a noun. 臭味","examples":["He was aware of the stink of stale beer on his breath. 他注意到自己有變味啤酒般的口臭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone makes <b>a stink</b> about something they are angry about, they show their anger in order to make people take notice. 公然表示的憤怒","examples":["The family's making a hell of a stink. 這家人正在大吵大鬧。"]}]}]},"strait":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海峽，狹窄水道；（尤指財務問題導致的）窘境，困境（straits）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古>嚴格的，精確的；<古>（地方）空間有限的，狹窄的；苦惱的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"嚴格地，精確地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a narrow strip of sea which joins two large areas of sea as a <b>strait</b> or <b>the</b> <b>straits</b>. 海峽","examples":["An estimated 1,600 vessels pass through the strait annually. 估計每年有1600艘船經過這個海峽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>in</b> dire or desperate <b>straits</b>, they are in a very difficult situation, usually because they do not have much money. (常指缺錢造成的) 困境","examples":["The company's closure has left many small businessmen in desperate financial straits. 該公司的關閉使得許多小商人陷入經濟困境。"]}]}]},"stoop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"俯身，彎腰；（站立或行走時）弓背，駝背；卑鄙，墮落；（猛禽）下撲，猛撲"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"駝背，彎腰曲背；<美>門廊，門階；（猛禽的）下撲，猛撲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stoop</b>, you stand or walk with your shoulders bent forward. 駝背","examples":["She was taller than he was and stooped slightly. 她比他高，但有點兒駝背。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stoop</b>, you bend your body forward and downward. 彎腰","examples":["He stooped to pick up the carrier bag of groceries. 他彎腰提起裝滿食品雜貨的購物袋。","Two men in shirt sleeves stooped over the car. 兩個穿襯衫的男人趴在那輛汽車上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a person <b>stoops</b> <b>to</b> doing something, you are criticizing them because they do something wrong or immoral that they would not normally do. 卑鄙到…","examples":["He had not, until recently, stooped to personal abuse. 他最近才卑鄙到進行人身攻擊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stoop</b> is also a noun. 駝背","examples":["He was a tall, thin fellow with a slight stoop. 他是一個有點兒駝背的瘦高個男子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a small platform with steps up to it at the entrance to a building 小門廊","examples":[]}]}]},"storage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"儲存，貯藏；（資訊的）儲存，儲存空間；（傢俱等的）存放，保管；儲存空間，儲藏場所；倉庫費，倉租"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"儲存的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>storage</b> of something, you mean that it is kept in a special place until it is needed. 貯藏","examples":["...the storage of toxic waste. …有毒廢棄物的貯藏。","Some of the space will at first be used for storage. 一些空間將首先用於貯藏。"]}]}]},"strand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（繩、線、毛髮等的）股，縷；串；（故事、觀點、計劃等的）部分；（海洋、湖或河的）岸，濱"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使滯留，使困在（某處）；使（船，船員，海洋生物）擱淺；使（跑壘員）殘留壘上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strand</b> <b>of</b> something such as hair, wire, or thread is a single thin piece of it. (頭髮、電線或紗線的) 縷","examples":["She tried to blow a grey strand of hair from her eyes. 她試圖吹開眼前的一縷白髮。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are stranded</b>, you are prevented from leaving a place, for example because of bad weather. 使滯留","examples":["The climbers had been stranded by a storm. 這些登山者被暴風雨困住了。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to form (a rope, cable, etc) by winding strands together 搓; 絞(繩索等)","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to leave or drive (ships, fish, etc) aground or ashore or (of ships, fish, etc) to be left or driven ashore 使(船、魚等)擱淺","examples":[]}]}]},"strap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帶子，皮帶；鐵皮條，金屬帶，鉸鏈片；鞭打（the strap）；拉手吊帶，拉手吊環"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用帶子）束住，捆綁；用繃帶包紮（傷口）；用皮鞭抽打，鞭打"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>strap</b> is a narrow piece of leather, cloth, or other material. Straps are used to carry things, fasten things together, or to hold a piece of clothing in place. 帶子","examples":["Nancy gripped the strap of her beach bag. 南希抓住自己海灘休閒包的帶子。","She pulled the strap of her nightgown onto her shoulder. 她把睡衣的帶子拉到她的肩上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>strap</b> something somewhere, you fasten it there with a strap. 用帶子綁","examples":["She strapped the baby seat into the car. 她把嬰兒座椅用帶子綁在那輛汽車上。"]}]}]},"stray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"走失，迷路；走神，離題；（眼睛，手）悠閒 （或漫不經心）地移動；入歧途，犯錯誤；有外遇，在別處拈花惹草；<文>遊蕩，徘徊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（動物）走失的，流浪的；離散的，零落的；（物理量）雜散的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"走失（流浪）的動物；離群者，走散者；天電干擾"},{"pos":"","zh":"null （Stray）（挪、美、英、俄）斯特雷（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>strays</b> somewhere, they wander away from where they are supposed to be. 走失","examples":["Tourists often get lost and stray into dangerous areas. 旅遊者們經常迷路走進一些危險區域。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your mind or your eyes <b>stray</b>, you do not concentrate on or look at one particular subject, but start thinking about or looking at other things. (思想或視線) 不集中","examples":["Even with the simplest cases I find my mind straying. 即使對最簡單的案例我發現自己的思想也無法集中。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stray</b> dog or cat has wandered away from its owner's home. 走失的 (狗或貓)","examples":["A stray dog came up to him. 一隻走失的狗來到他跟前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>stray</b> to describe something that exists separated from other similar things. 離群的","examples":["An 8-year-old boy was killed by a stray bullet. 一個8歲的男孩被一顆流彈打死。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stray</b> is also a noun. 走失的寵物","examples":["The dog was a stray which had been adopted. 這隻狗是被收養的流浪狗。"]}]}]},"stride":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大步，闊步；步態，步伐；步距，步幅；步速；進展，進步；<非正式>褲子（strides）；鋼琴跨越彈奏法"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"大步走，闊步走；跨越，跨過；<文>跨坐在……上，跨立在……上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stride</b> somewhere, you walk there with quick, long steps. 大步走","examples":["They were joined by a newcomer who came striding across a field. 他們中又來了個新人，那人穿過一塊田地大步走過來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stride</b> is a long step which you take when you are walking or running. 大步","examples":["With every stride, runners hit the ground with up to five times their body-weight. 賽跑者的每一步都以5倍於他們體重的力量撞擊地面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> <b>strides</b> in something that you are doing, you make rapid progress in it. 進步","examples":["The country has made enormous strides politically but not economically. 這個國家在政治上取得了巨大進步，但在經濟上卻沒有。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>get into</b> your <b>stride</b> or <b>hit</b> your <b>stride</b>, you start to do something easily and confidently, after being slow and uncertain. 進入狀態","examples":["The campaign is just getting into its stride. 這場運動剛剛進入狀態。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> a problem or difficulty <b>in stride</b>, you deal with it calmly and easily. 從容處理某事","examples":["He took the ridiculous accusation in stride. 他從容應對那荒謬的指控。"]}]}]},"streak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"條紋，條痕；（尤指不好的）性格特徵；（成功或幸運的）一段時間，一陣子；<非正式>公共場合裸跑；（細菌在固體培養基上的）畫線；一縷縷（淺色頭髮）；一道（亮光）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"飛快地移動，疾行；在（表面）佈滿條紋；（在公共場所）裸奔；使（頭髮）染上不同的顏色，挑染；（用針或藥籤在固體培養基表面）畫線（接種細菌）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>streak</b> is a long stripe or mark on a surface which contrasts with the surface because it is a different colour. 條紋","examples":["There are these dark streaks on the surface of the moon. 月亮表面有這些黑色的條紋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has a <b>streak</b> of a particular type of behaviour, they sometimes behave in that way. 性格特徵","examples":["We're both alike – there is a streak of madness in us both. 我們兩個很像–我們兩人都有一種瘋狂的性格特徵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A winning <b>streak</b> or a lucky <b>streak</b> is a continuous series of successes, for example in gambling or sports. A losing <b>streak</b> or an unlucky <b>streak</b> is a series of failures or losses. (賭博或體育比賽中的) 運氣","examples":["The casinos had better watch out since I'm obviously on a lucky streak! 我的手氣顯然很好，那些賭場最好當心！"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>streaks</b> a surface, it makes long stripes or marks on the surface. 在…上留下條痕","examples":["Rain had begun to streak the windowpanes. 雨已開始在窗玻璃上留下條痕。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>streaks</b> somewhere, they move there very quickly. 疾馳","examples":["A meteorite streaked across the sky. 一顆流星劃過天空。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to run naked through a crowd of people in a public place in order to shock or amuse them 裸奔","examples":[]}]}]},"stroll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"散步，閒逛；（體育比賽）輕而易舉地獲勝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"散步，溜達；（競賽中）輕易的勝利"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stroll</b> somewhere, you walk there in a slow, relaxed way. 溜達","examples":["He collected some orange juice from the refrigerator and, glass in hand, strolled to the kitchen window. 他從冰箱裡取了些橙汁，然後手拿玻璃杯，溜達到廚房的窗邊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stroll</b> is also a noun. 溜達","examples":["After dinner, I took a stroll round the city. 晚飯後，我繞著城溜達了一圈。"]}]}]},"stripe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"條紋，線條；（軍裝上表示等級的）臂章，軍階條；型別，特點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加條紋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stripe</b> is a long line which is a different colour from the areas next to it. 條紋","examples":["She wore a bright green jogging suit with a white stripe down the sides. 她穿了一套側邊有一條白色條紋的豔綠色慢跑服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a stroke from a whip, rod, cane, etc 鞭打; 抽打","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to mark with a stripe or stripes 加條紋於","examples":[]}]}]},"stumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"絆腳，絆跌；跌跌撞撞地走，蹣跚而行；結結巴巴地說；偶然發現；（努力要獲得某物時）出岔子，出差錯；失足；使……困惑；使……絆倒"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"絆倒；跌跌撞撞地走，蹣跚而行；錯誤，差錯"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stumble</b>, you put your foot down awkwardly while you are walking or running and nearly fall over. 踉蹌; 絆腳","examples":["He stumbled and almost fell. 他絆了一下，差點兒摔倒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stumble</b> is also a noun. 踉蹌; 絆腳","examples":["I make it into the darkness with only one stumble. 我只踉蹌了一下就把它弄進了黑暗中。"]}]}]},"strain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"焦慮，緊張；負擔，緊張；張力，壓力；損傷，扭傷；品種，型別；氣質，個性特點；旋律，曲調；口吻，語氣；（物理）應變，脅變；血緣；困難，負擔"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拉傷，扭傷；繃緊，用力拉；竭力，使勁；過濾；使不堪忍受，使緊張；用力推（或拉），拉緊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If <b>strain</b> is put <b>on</b> an organization or system, it has to do more than it is able to do. 壓力","examples":["The prison service is already under considerable strain. 監獄系統已受到很大的壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Strain</b> is a state of worry and tension caused by a difficult situation. 壓力","examples":["She was tired and under great strain. 她疲倦且處於巨大的壓力之下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that a situation is <b>a strain</b>, you mean that it makes you worried and tense. 負擔","examples":["I sometimes find it a strain to be responsible for the mortgage. 我有時發現償還抵押借款是個負擔。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Strain</b> is a force that pushes, pulls, or stretches something in a way that may damage it. 壓力","examples":["Place your hands under your buttocks to take some of the strain off your back. 把雙手放在臀部下面，以減輕一些背部壓力。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Strain</b> is an injury to a muscle in your body, caused by using the muscle too much or twisting it. 損傷; 扭傷","examples":["Avoid muscle strain by warming up with slow jogging. 透過慢跑熱身避免肌肉損傷。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A <b>strain</b> <b>of</b> a germ, plant, or other organism is a particular type of it. 型別; 品種","examples":["Every year new strains of influenza develop. 每年都有新的流感型別出現。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>strain</b> something means to make it do more than it is able to do. 使受到壓力","examples":["The volume of scheduled flights is straining the air traffic control system. 定期航班的數量使空中交通控制系統受到壓力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>strain</b> a muscle, you injure it by using it too much or twisting it. 損傷; 扭傷","examples":["He strained his back during a practice session. 他在一次練習課上扭傷了背部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>strain</b> <b>to</b> do something, you make a great effort to do it when it is difficult to do. 努力做","examples":["I had to strain to hear. 我不得不努力地聽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>strain</b> food, you separate the liquid part of it from the solid parts. 過濾","examples":["Strain the stock and put it back into the pan. 濾出原湯，然後把它放回平底鍋。"]}]}]},"suitcase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（旅行用的）手提箱，衣箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>suitcase</b> is a box or bag with a handle and a hard frame in which you carry your clothes when you are travelling. 手提箱","examples":["It did not take Andrew long to pack a suitcase. 安德魯沒有用多長時間就整理好了手提箱。"]}]}]},"stutter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"口吃，結結巴巴地說；（機器，槍）突突地響"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"口吃，結巴；（機器或槍的）突突響聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone has a <b>stutter</b>, they find it difficult to say the first sound of a word, and so they often hesitate or repeat it two or three times. 口吃","examples":["He spoke with a pronounced stutter. 他說話帶有明顯的口吃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"口吃","examples":["He had to stop talking because if he'd kept on, the stuttering would have started. 他不得不停止講話，因為如果他繼續下去，口吃就會發作。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>stutters</b>, they have difficulty speaking because they find it hard to say the first sound of a word. 結結巴巴地說話","examples":["I was trembling so hard, I thought I would stutter when I spoke. 我那時抖得很厲害，我覺得說話時都會結結巴巴。"]}]}]},"stump":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樹樁；（主體被砍斷、折斷或磨損後的）殘餘部分；殘肢；（政治家在選舉前的）巡迴演說；（板球三柱門的）柱；（板球比賽的）結束；（將紙或其他軟材料卷尖，用來淡化或調和彩色粉筆、蠟筆或鉛筆畫痕的）擦筆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"砍伐；使為難，使困惑；邁著沉重的步子走；（政治競選期間）巡迴演說；（以球觸三柱門）使（擊球手）出局；用擦筆擦（畫、線條等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stump</b> is a small part of something that remains when the rest of it has been removed or broken off. 殘餘部分","examples":["If you have a tree stump, check it for fungus. 如果你有一個樹樁，就在上面找找菌類。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are stumped</b> by a question or problem, you cannot think of any solution or answer to it. 把…難住","examples":["John Diamond is stumped by an unexpected question. 約翰·戴蒙德被一個意想不到的問題難住了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If politicians <b>stump</b> <b>for</b> a candidate, they travel around making campaign speeches before an election. (選舉前為候選人) 作巡迴政治演說","examples":["Since September, the president has stumped for Republicans in 23 states. 自9月以來，這位總統已在23個州為共和黨人作了巡迴政治演說。"]}]}]},"sulfur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"硫，硫磺；硫磺色；美洲粉蝶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用硫磺處理（如用硫消毒或熏製）"}],"sections":[]},"superstition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"迷信"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Superstition</b> is belief in things that are not real or possible, for example magic. 迷信","examples":["Fortune-telling is a very much debased art surrounded by superstition. 算命是一種透著迷信色彩的十分低階的把戲。"]}]}]},"supervisor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監督者，管理者；（英國大學裡負責學生研究工作的）指導教師；<美>鎮長，縣長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>supervisor</b> is a person who supervises activities or people, especially workers or students. 監督員; 指導者","examples":["...a full-time job as a supervisor at a factory. …在一家工廠擔任監督員的一項全職工作。"]}]}]},"substitute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"替代品，代替物；（體育比賽中的）替補隊員；令人滿意的替代物，與之媲美的事物；<蘇格蘭，法律>副職"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用……代替；（比賽中）替換（運動員）；代替（某人的工作）；（化）取代（分子中的一個或一組原子，尤指氫原子）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"替代性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>substitute</b> one thing <b>for</b> another, or if one thing <b>substitutes</b> <b>for</b> another, it takes the place or performs the function of the other thing. 以…代替; 代替","examples":["They were substituting violence for dialogue. 他們那時在以暴力代替對話。","He was substituting for the injured William Wales. 他那時在代替受傷的威廉·威爾士。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"代替","examples":["In my experience a straight substitution of carob for chocolate doesn't work. 以我的經驗，角豆直接代替巧克力不會奏效。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>substitute</b> is something that you have or use instead of something else. 替代者","examples":["She is seeking a substitute for the very man whose departure made her cry. 他在尋找一個男人的替代者，這個男人的離去曾使她傷心落淚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that one thing is no <b>substitute</b> <b>for</b> another, you mean that it does not have certain desirable features that the other thing has, and is therefore unsatisfactory. If you say that there is no <b>substitute</b> <b>for</b> something, you mean that it is the only thing which is really satisfactory. 可替代者","examples":["The printed word is no substitute for personal discussion with a great thinker. 印刷字無法替代與偉大思想家的當面交流。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In team games such as football, a <b>substitute</b> is a player who is brought into a game to replace another player. 替補隊員","examples":["Jefferson entered as a substitute in the 60th minute. 傑斐遜在第60分鐘時作為替補隊員上了場。"]}]}]},"swamp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溼地，沼澤地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"浸沒，吞沒；（喻）壓倒，淹沒；使疲於應對，使應接不暇；（大批人等）湧入（某處），包圍（某人）；極大地影響（某人），使崩潰；<非正式>（衣服）太大而不適合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>swamp</b> is an area of very wet land with wild plants growing in it. 沼澤地","examples":["I spent one whole night by a swamp behind the road listening to frogs. 我整個晚上都在這條路後面的一個沼澤地旁聽蛙鳴。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>swamps</b> a place or object, it fills it with water. 淹沒","examples":["Their electronic navigation failed and a rogue wave swamped the boat. 他們的電子導航裝置失靈了，一個巨浪吞沒了那隻船。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are swamped</b> by things or people, you have more of them than you can deal with. 使應接不暇","examples":["He is swamped with work. 他工作正忙得不可開交。"]}]}]},"surge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"激增，猛增；（風、水等的）奔湧，洶湧；（情感的）湧起，翻湧；（人群的）蜂擁；電流急衝，電湧；增兵，增援"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"急劇上升，激增；（人群，自然力）洶湧，奔騰；（感情）湧起，湧現；（電壓，電流）猛增，浪湧；（繩子，纜索，絞盤）突然鬆開，突然滑脫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>surge</b> is a sudden large increase in something that has previously been steady, or has only increased or developed slowly. 劇增","examples":["Specialists see various reasons for the recent surge in inflation. 專家認為最近通貨膨脹加劇有各種原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>surge</b> is a sudden powerful movement of a physical force such as wind or water. (風、水等) 突然的湧動","examples":["The whole car shuddered with an almost frightening surge of power. 整輛車因受到一股幾乎令人驚駭的衝力而顫動。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>surges</b>, it increases suddenly and greatly, after being steady or developing only slowly. 劇增","examples":["The Freedom Party's electoral support surged from just under 10 percent to nearly 17 percent. 自由黨的選舉支援率從只有不到10%劇增到近17%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a crowd of people <b>surge</b> forward, they suddenly move forward together. 湧動","examples":["The photographers and cameramen surged forward. 那些攝影和攝像師們湧向前去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a physical force such as water or electricity <b>surges</b> through something, it moves through it suddenly and powerfully. (水、電流等) 湧","examples":["Thousands of volts surged through his car after he careered into a lamp post, ripping out live wires. 當他急速撞向一個燈柱、扯斷了通電的電線之後，幾千伏的電流湧過他的汽車。"]}]}]},"taunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"奚落，嘲諷，嘲弄；逗弄"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘲弄的話，譏諷的話"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（古/航海）很高的，高聳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>taunts</b> you, they say unkind or insulting things to you, especially about your weaknesses or failures. 嘲笑; 羞辱","examples":["A gang taunted a disabled man. 一幫混混兒羞辱了一個殘疾人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Taunt</b> is also a noun. 嘲笑; 羞辱","examples":["For years they suffered racist taunts. 多年來他們遭到了種族主義者的羞辱。"]}]}]},"tangle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）糾結，（使）纏結；<非正式> 和……發生衝突，和……發生糾紛；（思想、局勢變得）紛亂，混亂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（線、毛髮等的）纏結的一團，亂團；混亂，紛亂；<非正式>爭吵，打架；大型棕色海藻（尤指昆布）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tangle</b> <b>of</b> something is a mass of it twisted together in a messy way. 亂糟糟的一團","examples":["A tangle of wires is all that remains of the computer and phone systems. 亂糟糟的一團電線是電腦和電話系統留下來的全部。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is tangled</b> or <b>tangles</b>, it becomes twisted together in a messy way. 使纏結; 纏結","examples":["Animals get tangled in fishing nets and drown. 動物被纏在漁網裡淹死了。","Her hair tends to tangle. 她的頭髮易打結。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to come into conflict; contend 與...打架; 爭執","examples":[]}]}]},"tar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"焦油，柏油，瀝青（黑色粘稠物質）；（菸草中的）焦油；水手（舊稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"塗以焦油（或柏油、瀝青）；玷汙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tar</b> is a thick black sticky substance that is used especially for making roads. 瀝青","examples":["The oil has hardened to tar. 油已硬化成瀝青了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tar</b> is one of the poisonous substances contained in tobacco. (菸草中的) 焦油","examples":["...strict guidelines as to the amount of tar contained in cigarettes. …關於香菸中焦油含量的嚴格的指導原則。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to coat with tar 用焦油或瀝青塗抹","examples":[]}]}]},"swarm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一大群（移動中的昆蟲）；（移動著的）一大群人；（多指發生在火山附近的）地震群；（天文）一大群小型天體同時在空中出現"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（昆蟲）成群飛行；（人）蜂湧，湧動；擠滿，雲集；成群地包圍；爬（梯子等），攀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>swarm</b> <b>of</b> bees or other insects is a large group of them flying together. 大群 (蜜蜂等昆蟲)","examples":["...a swarm of locusts. …一大群蝗蟲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>swarm</b> <b>of</b> people is a large group of them moving about quickly. (快速移動的) 一大群","examples":["A swarm of people encircled the hotel. 一大群人包圍了這家酒店。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When bees or other insects <b>swarm</b>, they move or fly in a large group. (蜜蜂或其他昆蟲) 大群移動","examples":["A dark cloud of bees comes swarming out of the hive. 黑壓壓的一大群蜜蜂從那座蜂巢湧過來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>swarm</b> somewhere, they move there quickly in a large group. (人群) 湧往","examples":["People swarmed to the stores, buying up everything in sight. 人們成群地湧到商場，看到什麼就買什麼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a place <b>is swarming</b> <b>with</b> people, it is full of people moving about in a busy way. 擠滿","examples":["Within minutes the area was swarming with officers who began searching a nearby wood. 幾分鐘之內這個地方擠滿了警官，他們開始搜查附近的一片樹林。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to climb (a ladder, etc) by gripping with the hands and feet 爬(梯子等); 攀","examples":[]}]}]},"tan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棕褐色，棕黃色；（日曬後變成的）棕褐色皮膚；鞣料樹皮；（鋪路和園藝中使用的）鞣酸皮渣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）曬成褐色，曬黑；鞣（革），硝（皮）；<非正式，舊> 痛打（某人），鞭打（尤指作為懲罰）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"棕黃色的，棕褐色的；曬黑的"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"正切（tangent）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>tan</b>, your skin has become darker than usual because you have been in the sun. 曬黑的皮膚","examples":["She is tall and blonde, with a permanent tan. 她個子高，一頭金髮，皮膚黝黑。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a part of your body <b>tans</b> or if you <b>tan</b> it, your skin becomes darker than usual because you spend a lot of time in the sun. 使曬黑; 曬黑","examples":["I have very pale skin that never tans. 我膚色很白，永遠曬不黑。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"曬黑的","examples":["Their skin was tanned and glowing from their weeks at the sea. 他們在海上呆了幾個星期，皮膚曬得黑裡泛紅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"of the colour tan 棕褐色","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to convert (a skin or hide) into leather by treating it with a tanning agent, such as vegetable tannins, chromium salts, fish oils, or formaldehyde 鞣革","examples":[]}]}]},"tavern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酒館；<舊式>客棧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tavern</b> is a bar. 酒吧","examples":["Drinkers line the bar at Byrnes Tavern. 酒客沿伯恩斯酒吧的吧檯排成一行。"]}]}]},"tart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（頂部不用麵皮密封的）甜餡餅；妓女"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（味道）酸的；（答覆或評論）尖酸的，刻薄的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>打扮以引人注目"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tart</b> is a shallow pastry case with a filling of food, especially sweet food. (尤指甜心) 餡餅","examples":["...apple tarts. …蘋果餡餅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone refers to a woman or girl as a <b>tart</b>, they are criticizing her because they think she is sexually immoral or dresses in a way that makes her look sexually immoral. 輕佻放蕩的女人","examples":["She was very upset when he accused her of looking like a tart. 當他指責她看起來像個輕佻女人的時候，她非常沮喪。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as fruit is <b>tart</b>, it has a sharp taste. (水果等) 味道濃烈的","examples":["The blackberries were too tart on their own, so we stewed them gently with some apples. 黑莓本身的味道太濃烈，所以我們加些蘋果將其稍稍燉一下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tart</b> remark or way of speaking is sharp and unpleasant, often in a way that is a little cruel. (言辭) 尖刻的","examples":["The words were more tart than she had intended. 這些話比她原本意欲表達的要尖刻。"]}]}]},"teller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（銀行）出納員；（尤指議會的）計票人；講述者，講故事的人；出納機，提款機；<英，史>（稅務署四位收、付款）稅官（之一）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>teller</b> is a someone who works in a bank and who customers pay money to or get money from. (銀行) 出納員","examples":["Every bank pays close attention to the speed and accuracy of its tellers. 每家銀行都密切關注其出納員的速度和準確性。","...a bank teller. …一位銀行出納員。"]}]}]},"tempo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（運動或活動的）速度，節奏；（音樂的）節奏，拍子；（印度次大陸）輕型三輪貨車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tempo</b> of an event is the speed at which it happens. (事件發展的) 速度","examples":["...owing to the slow tempo of change in an overwhelmingly rural country. …由於一個高度農業化國家變革的緩慢速度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>tempo</b> of a piece of music is the speed at which it is played. (音樂的) 節奏","examples":["In a new recording, the Boston Philharmonic tried the original tempo. 在一張新唱片中，波士頓愛樂樂團嘗試了音樂原本的節奏。"]}]}]},"thigh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大腿，股；（禽類的）腿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>thighs</b> are the top parts of your legs, between your knees and your hips. 大腿","examples":["The shorts are so small I can't fit my thighs into any of them. 短褲太小了，我的大腿塞不進去。"]}]}]},"temptation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"引誘，誘惑；誘惑人的東西；（魔鬼對耶穌的）引誘（the Temptation）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel you want to do something or have something, even though you know you really should avoid it, you can refer to this feeling as <b>temptation</b>. You can also refer to the thing you want to do or have as a <b>temptation</b>. 誘惑","examples":["Will they be able to resist the temptation to buy? 他們能抵抗得住購買的誘惑嗎？"]}]}]},"thriller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指關於罪案或間諜的）驚險小說（或戲劇、電影）；令人激動的比賽（或經歷）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>thriller</b> is a book, movie, or play that tells an exciting fictional story about something such as criminal activities or spying. 驚悚小說; 驚悚電影; 驚悚戲劇","examples":["...a tense psychological thriller. …一部緊張刺激的心理驚悚小說。"]}]}]},"tenant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"房客，租戶；<法律>業主"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（作為租賃者）居住，工作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tenant</b> is someone who pays rent for the place they live in, or for land or buildings that they use. 租戶; 佃戶","examples":["Regulations placed clear obligations on the landlord for the benefit of the tenant. 為了租戶的利益，條列給房東規定了明確的義務。"]}]}]},"terrace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（風格相同、互相連線的）排屋；（尤指房屋或餐館外的）露天平臺，陽臺；<英>（足球場的）階梯看臺；梯田，階地；<英>排屋中的一棟房屋；（地質）沿岸階地，階面"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成階地（或梯田）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>terrace</b> is a flat area of stone or grass next to a building where people can sit. (房屋旁的) 露臺; 草坪","examples":["Some guests recline in deck chairs on the sea-facing terrace. 有些客人斜躺在朝海露臺的躺椅上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Terraces</b> are a series of flat areas built like steps on the side of a hill so that crops can be grown there. 梯田","examples":["...massive terraces of corn and millet carved into the mountainside like giant steps. …山坡上開墾出來種玉米和小米的巨型臺階般的大塊大塊梯田。"]}]}]},"thorn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（植物莖上的）刺；帶刺的灌木，荊棘；刺形符，字母 ð； <喻>使人苦惱（或生氣）的事（或人），棘手的東西；霜尺蛾；（Thorn）託倫（波蘭城市，Toruń 的德語名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thorns</b> are the sharp points on some plants and trees, for example, on a rose bush. 刺","examples":["Roses will always have thorns but with care they can be avoided. 玫瑰總有刺，但是隻要小心，還是可以避開刺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>thorn</b> or a <b>thorn bush</b> or a <b>thorn tree</b> is a bush or tree which has a lot of thorns on it. 帶刺灌木叢; 帶刺的樹","examples":["...the shade of a thorn bush. …一棵帶刺灌木的樹陰。"]}]}]},"thrill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"興奮，激動；使人興奮的事物，令人激動的事；一陣強烈的感覺；（醫）震顫；追求的快感；性快感"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（某人）非常興奮，非常激動；（情感，感覺）顫抖，振動；<文>顫動，跳動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something gives you a <b>thrill</b>, it gives you a sudden feeling of great excitement, pleasure, or fear. (突然的) 激動; 狂喜; 恐懼","examples":["I can remember the thrill of not knowing what I would get on Christmas morning. 我記得，在不知道聖誕節早上會收到何種禮物時自己的激動心情。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>thrills</b> you, or if you <b>thrill</b> <b>at</b> it, it gives you a feeling of great pleasure and excitement. 使激動; 感到激動","examples":["The electric atmosphere both terrified and thrilled him. 這種緊張的氣氛使他既害怕又激動。"]}]}]},"terminal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（火車、公共汽車或船的）終點站；航空終點站，航站樓；電腦終端；（電路的）端子，線接頭；<英>晚期病人；（石油，天然氣的）集散站；（建築）界標，端飾，胸像柱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（疾病） 致命的，不治的，晚期的；（病狀）已達晚期的；逐步衰亡的，越來越糟的；終端的，末端的；極度的，極其的；學期的，期末的，按期的；（運輸）終點（站）的；（動）末端的，遠端的；（植）（花朵等）頂生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>terminal</b> illness or disease causes death, often slowly, and cannot be cured. (疾病) 晚期的; 致命的","examples":["...terminal cancer. …晚期癌症。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"致命地","examples":["The patient is terminally ill. 這個病人病入膏肓。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>terminal</b> is a place where vehicles, passengers, or goods begin or end a journey. 起點站; 終點站","examples":["Plans are underway for a new terminal at Dulles airport. 正計劃在杜勒斯機場修建新的航站大樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A computer <b>terminal</b> is a piece of equipment consisting of a keyboard and a screen that is used for putting information into a computer or getting information from it. (計算機) 終端","examples":["Carl sits at a computer terminal 40 hours a week. 卡爾每週要在電腦前坐40小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On a piece of electrical equipment, a <b>terminal</b> is one of the points where electricity enters or leaves it. (電路的) 端頭","examples":["...the positive terminal of the battery. …電池的正極。"]}]}]},"throng":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一大群，眾多"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"蜂擁，群集"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<蘇格蘭，北英格蘭>擁擠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>throng</b> is a large crowd of people. 一大群人","examples":["An official pushed through the throng. 一位官員從人群中擠過。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>throng</b> somewhere, they go there in great numbers. (人群) 湧向","examples":["The crowds thronged into the stadium. 人群湧進了體育館。"]}]}]},"tile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（貼牆或鋪地用的）瓷磚，地磚；（鋪屋頂的）瓦，瓦片；（拼字遊戲、麻將等牌戲中的）（一張）牌；（棋盤遊戲的）棋子；（數）平鋪"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鋪瓦，鋪磚；（計算機）平鋪（視窗）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tiles</b> are flat, square pieces of baked clay, carpet, cork, or other substance, which are fixed as a covering onto a floor or wall. (貼牆或鋪地用的) 瓷磚; 地毯; 地板","examples":["Amy's shoes squeaked on the tiles as she walked down the corridor. 埃米走過走廊時，鞋子在地磚上吱吱作響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tiles</b> are flat pieces of baked clay which are used for covering roofs. (覆蓋屋頂的) 瓦片","examples":["...a fine building, with a neat little porch and ornamental tiles on the roof. …一幢精緻建築，有個整潔的小門廊，屋頂上蓋著裝飾瓦。"]}]}]},"toad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蟾蜍，癩蛤蟆；（侮辱性用語）討厭鬼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toad</b> is a creature which is similar to a frog but which has a drier skin and spends less time in water. 蟾蜍","examples":[]}]}]},"throne":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（君王的）寶座，御座；王位，王權，帝位（the throne）；（幽默）廁所；座天使（thrones）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"<文>使登上王位（或寶座、御座），使掌握王權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>throne</b> is a decorative chair used by a king, queen, or emperor on important official occasions. (君王的) 寶座","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can talk about <b>the throne</b> as a way of referring to the position of being king, queen, or emperor. 王位; 皇位","examples":["...the queen's 40th anniversary on the throne. ...女王登位40週年紀念日。"]}]}]},"tiptoe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腳尖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"踮著腳走，躡手躡腳地走；迴避（難應付的話題、問題或人）（tiptoe round/around）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"踮著腳尖地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"踮著腳走的；偷偷摸摸的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tiptoe</b> somewhere, you walk there very quietly without putting your heels on the floor when you walk. 踮著腳尖走","examples":["She slipped out of bed and tiptoed to the window. 她溜下床，踮起腳尖走向窗戶。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>on tiptoe</b> or <b>on tiptoes</b>, you do it standing or walking on the front part of your foot, without putting your heels on the ground. 踮著腳","examples":["She leaned her bike against the stone wall and stood on tiptoe to peer over it. 她把腳踏車靠在石牆上，然後踮起腳從牆頭望過去。"]}]}]},"thrust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛推，猛塞；刺，扎；（人）推進，擠過；上伸，伸出；強使接受"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"要點，要旨；猛推，刺；（飛機、火箭等的）驅動力，推力；強攻，挺進；（拱、椽的）側向壓力；（地質）衝斷層，逆斷層；苛評"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>thrust</b> something or someone somewhere, you push or move them there quickly with a lot of force. 猛推; 猛塞; 猛刺","examples":["They thrust him into the back of a jeep. 他們把他猛推入吉普車的後部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>thrust</b> your <b>way</b> somewhere, you move there, pushing between people or things which are in your way. 擠; 推","examples":["She thrust her way into the crowd. 她擠進了人群。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thrust</b> is also a noun. 猛推; 猛塞; 猛刺","examples":["Two of the knife thrusts were fatal. 猛刺的其中兩刀是致命的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Thrust</b> is the power or force that is required to make a vehicle move in a particular direction. (車輛等的) 推力","examples":["It provides the thrust that makes the craft move forward. 它提供了使飛機前進的推力。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>thrusts</b> up or out of something else, it sticks up or sticks out in a noticeable way. 豎起; 挺出","examples":["...a seedling ready to thrust up into any available light. …一株正要挺出來迎接光線的幼苗。"]}]}]},"toil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（長時間地）苦幹，辛勤勞作；艱難緩慢地移動，跋涉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指體力上的）苦工，苦活；網，捕捉野獸的陷阱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>toil</b>, they work very hard doing unpleasant or tiring tasks. 辛苦工作","examples":["People who toiled in dim, dank factories were too exhausted to enjoy their family life. 在陰暗潮溼的工廠裡苦作的人們精疲力竭了，無法享受家庭生活。","Workers toiled long hours. 工人們長時間辛苦工作。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Toil away</b> means the same as . 辛苦工作","examples":["He doesn't spend every minute toiling away at his desk. 他並非每分鐘都在伏案辛苦地工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"hard or exhausting work 辛苦的工作","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a net or snare 網","examples":[]}]}]},"tin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錫（一種化學元素，符號為 Sn）；<英>罐，罐頭盒；（用於儲存糕點或餅乾的）有蓋金屬盒，金屬食品盒；<英>（盛塗料、膠水等的）馬口鐵罐，白鐵桶；<英>烤模，烤盤；鍍錫鐵皮，馬口鐵（tinplate 的簡稱）；<英>長方形麵包"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"錫制的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……上鍍錫（或包錫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tin</b> is a soft silvery-white metal. 錫","examples":["...a factory that turns scrap metal into tin cans. …一個將廢金屬製成馬口鐵罐的工廠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>tin</b> is a metal container with a lid in which things such as biscuits, cakes, or tobacco can be kept. 金屬罐","examples":["Store the biscuits in an airtight tin. 把這些餅乾存放在一個密封的金屬罐裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>tin</b> to refer to a tin and its contents, or to the contents only. 罐; 罐中之物","examples":["...a tin of paint. …一罐油漆。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>tin</b> is a metal container which is filled with food and sealed in order to preserve the food for long periods of time. 罐頭","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You can use <b>tin</b> to refer to a tin and its contents, or to the contents only. 罐頭; 罐中之物","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"A baking <b>tin</b> is a metal container used for baking things such as cakes and bread in an oven. (蛋糕、麵包等的) 烤模","examples":[]}]}]},"tilt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）傾斜，（使）傾側；（使）傾向於，（使）偏向於；俯仰（攝影機）；<史>（格鬥中）持矛衝刺（或比武）；以言詞或文字抨擊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"傾斜，傾側，傾斜度；（對某人、某信仰或某行為的）傾向，偏向；（意欲贏得某物或戰勝某人的）企圖，嘗試；（口頭或文字的）抨擊，攻擊；（攝影機的）俯仰轉動，上下搖攝；<美，非正式>（雙人或兩隊間的）比賽，競賽；<加>林中小屋；<史>騎馬持矛衝刺，馬上比槍，比武"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tilt</b> an object or if it <b>tilts</b>, it moves into a sloping position with one end or side higher than the other. 使傾斜; 傾斜","examples":["She tilted the mirror and began to comb her hair. 她把鏡子斜放，開始梳頭。","Leonard tilted his chair back on two legs and stretched his long body. 倫納德把他的椅子向後斜著撐在兩條腳上，然後舒展他修長的身軀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tilt</b> part of your body, usually your head, you move it slightly upward or to one side. 使 (常指頭部) 側傾; 使微仰","examples":["Mari tilted her head back so that she could look at him. 瑪麗把頭向後仰了仰，以便能看著他。","His wife tilted his head to the side and inspected the wound. 他的妻子把他的頭側向一邊，然後檢查傷口。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tilt</b> is also a noun. 傾斜","examples":["He opened the rear door for me with an apologetic tilt of his head. 他歉疚地歪著頭為我開啟了後門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>tilt</b> of something is the fact that it tilts or slopes, or the angle at which it tilts or slopes. 傾斜; 傾斜度","examples":["...calculations based on our understanding of the tilt of the Earth's axis. …基於我們對地球軸線傾斜度的理解的計算。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"an awning or canopy, usually of canvas, for a boat, booth, etc 罩棚","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to cover or provide with a tilt 罩上","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or thing <b>tilts</b> <b>toward</b> a particular opinion or if something <b>tilts</b> them <b>toward</b> it, they change slightly so that they become more in agreement with that opinion or position. 傾向","examples":["Political will might finally tilt toward some sort of national health plan. 政治意願可能最終會傾向於某種全民醫療方案。"]}]}]},"torch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>手電筒；火把；（象徵具有重大積極影響的政治運動或思想的）火炬；噴燈；（美，非正式）縱火犯"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"縱火焚燒，放火燒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>torch</b> is a long stick with burning material at one end, used to provide light or to set things on fire. 火把","examples":["The shepherd followed, carrying a torch to light his way. 牧羊人跟在後面，舉著火把把路照亮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>torch</b> is a device that produces a hot flame and is used for tasks such as cutting or joining pieces of metal. 吹管","examples":["The gang worked for up to ten hours with acetylene torches to open the vault. 這幫強盜為了開啟金庫，用乙炔吹管幹了長達10個小時。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>torch</b> is a small electric light which is powered by batteries and which you can carry in your hand. 手電筒","examples":["Len studied it a moment in the beam of his torch. 萊恩藉著手電筒的光把它仔細察看了一會兒。"]}]}]},"torment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（肉體、精神上的）折磨，痛苦；使人痛苦的人（物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使痛苦，折磨；騷擾，捉弄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Torment</b> is extreme suffering, usually mental suffering. (常指精神上的) 極度痛苦","examples":["After years of turmoil and torment, she is finally at peace. 經歷多年的動盪與痛苦後，她終於安心下來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>torment</b> is something that causes extreme suffering, usually mental suffering. 煩惱事","examples":["Sooner or later most writers end up making books about the torments of being a writer. 遲早大多數作家最終都會寫書訴說當一名作家的苦惱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>torments</b> you, it causes you extreme mental suffering. (精神上) 折磨","examples":["At times the memories returned to torment her. 有時這些記憶會又來折磨她。"]}]}]},"torrent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指似乎無法控制的）狂潮，迸發；洪流，激流；（Torrent）（西、法、美）託倫特（人名）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在急流中移動；透過位元流下載或上傳檔案"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"像急流的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>torrent</b> is a lot of water falling or flowing rapidly or violently. 急流","examples":["Torrents of water gushed into the reservoir. 急流湧進了水庫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>torrent</b> <b>of</b> abuse or questions is a lot of abuse or questions directed continuously at someone. (漫罵或問題的) 迸發","examples":["He turned around and directed a torrent of abuse at me. 他轉過身對我破口大罵了一通。"]}]}]},"token":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人工智慧和大語言模型）詞元；（某些機器中用以代替紙幣的）代幣，專用輔幣；象徵，標誌；禮券，代金券；（語言學）符號；（計算機）令牌，記號；（火車通行的）路籤"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"裝點門面的，裝樣子的；象徵性的，作為標誌的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>token</b> to describe things or actions which are small or unimportant but are meant to show particular intentions or feelings which may not be sincere. 裝樣子的","examples":["The announcement was welcomed as a step in the right direction, but was widely seen as a token gesture. 這個通告受到歡迎，被認為是向正確方向邁進了一步，但也被普遍看作是裝裝樣子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>token</b> is a round flat piece of metal or plastic that is sometimes used instead of money. 代用幣","examples":["...slot-machine tokens. …自動販賣機使用的代用幣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>token</b> is a piece of paper or card that can be exchanged for goods, either in a particular shop or as part of a special offer. 代金券; 購物卡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>by the same token</b> to introduce a statement that you think is true for the same reasons that were given for a previous statement. 同樣地","examples":["If you give up exercise, your muscles shrink and fat increases. By the same token, if you expend more energy you will lose fat. 如果你放棄鍛鍊，肌肉就會萎縮，脂肪會增多。同樣地，如果你消耗較多的體能，你就會減掉脂肪。"]}]}]},"torture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拷打，拷問，酷刑逼供；折磨，煎熬；變形"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拷打，拷問，嚴刑逼供；造成精神上的巨大痛苦，使憂慮；扭曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is tortured</b>, another person deliberately causes them terrible pain over a period of time, in order to punish them or to make them reveal information. 拷打; 拷問","examples":["Despite being tortured she proclaimed her innocence. 儘管受到拷打，她仍聲稱自己是清白的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>torture</b> someone means to cause them to suffer mental pain or anxiety. (精神上) 折磨","examples":["He would not torture her further by trying to argue with her. 他不會透過和她爭吵而進一步折磨她。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Torture</b> is also a noun. 拷打; 拷問","examples":["...alleged cases of torture and murder by the security forces. …安全部隊涉嫌嚴刑拷打與謀殺的案子。"]}]}]},"tournament":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錦標賽，聯賽；（中世紀的）騎士比武大會；閱兵式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tournament</b> is a sports competition in which players who win a match continue to play further matches in the competition until just one person or team is left. 錦標賽","examples":["...the biggest golf tournament to be held in Australia. …即將在澳大利亞舉行的最大規模的高爾夫球錦標賽。"]}]}]},"traitor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"叛徒，賣國賊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call someone a <b>traitor</b>, you mean that they have betrayed beliefs that they used to hold, or that their friends hold, by their words or actions. 背叛者","examples":["Some say he's a traitor to the peace movement. 一些人說他是和平運動的背叛者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is a <b>traitor</b>, they betray their country, friends, or a group of which they are a member by helping its enemies, especially during time of war. (尤指戰爭期間的) 賣國賊; 叛徒","examples":["...rumours that there were traitors among us who were sending messages to the enemy. …謠言說我們中有正給敵人送信的叛徒。"]}]}]},"trademark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商標；標誌，特點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……標上商標；認出（某種習慣、品質或生活方式）為某人的典型特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trademark</b> is a name or symbol that a company uses on its products and that cannot legally be used by another company. 商標","examples":["She has registered a trademark for a new range of perfumes. 她已為一個新系列的香水注冊了商標。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is the <b>trademark</b> of a particular person or place, you mean that it is characteristic of them or typically associated with them. 標誌","examples":["...the spiky punk hairdo that became his trademark. …刺蝟式的朋克髮型成了他的標誌。"]}]}]},"tick":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>鉤號；<英>一瞬間；（鐘錶等的）嘀嗒聲；壁蝨；<英>賒購；（股票）點；<英，非正式>一文不值的人，可鄙的人；褥套；（做墊套用的）堅質（條紋）布料（ticking 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鍾或其他機械裝置）發出滴答聲；<英>打鉤，做記號；進展，進步；正常運轉；輕觸，輕擊；<非正式> （某人的思想、願望或情感使其）做出……舉動，有……的行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a clock or watch <b>ticks</b>, it makes a regular series of short sounds as it works. (鐘錶) 嘀嗒作響","examples":["A wind-up clock ticked busily from the kitchen counter. 一個上了發條的時鐘在廚房案臺上不停地嘀嗒作響。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tick away</b> means the same as . 嘀嗒作響","examples":["A grandfather clock ticked away in a corner. 一個落地式大鐘在牆角嘀嗒作響。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嘀嗒聲","examples":["...the endless ticking of clocks. …時鐘沒完沒了的嘀嗒聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>tick</b> of a clock or watch is the series of short sounds it makes when it is working, or one of those sounds. (鐘錶的) 嘀嗒聲","examples":["He sat listening to the tick of the grandfather clock. 他坐著傾聽那個落地式大鐘的嘀嗒聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tick</b> is a written mark like a V. It is used to show that something is correct or has been selected or dealt with. 對勾","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>tick</b> is a small creature which lives on the bodies of people or animals and uses their blood as food. 壁蝨","examples":["The company produces chemicals that destroy ticks and mites. 該公司生產消滅壁蝨和蟎蟲的化學品。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tick</b> something that is written on a piece of paper, you put a tick next to it. 在…旁打勾","examples":["To request your free gift, please tick the appropriate box below. 需要免費禮品的，請在下面相關的框中打勾。"]}]}]},"trample":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"踩，踐踏；傷害，侵犯；腳步沉重地走"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>踐踏，踩踏聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>trample</b> <b>on</b> someone's rights or values or to <b>trample</b> them means to deliberately ignore them. 無視","examples":["They say loggers are destroying rain forests and trampling on the rights of natives. 他們說伐木工正在破壞雨林，無視當地人的權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is trampled</b>, they are injured or killed by being stepped on by animals or by other people. 踩傷; 踩死","examples":["Many people were trampled in the panic that followed. 很多人在隨後的恐慌中被踩傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>tramples</b> something or <b>tramples</b> <b>on</b> it, they step heavily and carelessly on it and damage it. 踐踏; 踩壞","examples":["They don't want people trampling the grass, pitching tents or building fires. 他們不想讓人們踐踏草地、搭帳篷或生火。"]}]}]},"treasury":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"財政部；大量珍品，寶藏；（城堡、教堂等的）寶庫，珍藏室；國庫，金庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集體可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the United States and some other countries, <b>the</b> <b>Treasury</b> is the government department that deals with the country's finances. 財政部","examples":["...a senior official at the Treasury. …財政部的一位高階官員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Treasuries</b> are financial bonds that are issued by the United States government in order to raise money. (美國政府發行的) 國庫券","examples":["...people who invest in 10- and 20- and 30-year Treasuries. …10年、20年和30年期國庫券的投資者。"]}]}]},"treaty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（國家之間的）條約，協定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>treaty</b> is a written agreement between countries in which they agree to do a particular thing or to help each other. 條約","examples":["...negotiations over a treaty on global warming. …關於全球變暖條約的談判。"]}]}]},"tramp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拖著沉重的腳步走，踩，踏；長途跋涉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"流浪漢，流浪乞丐；沉重的腳步聲；長途步行，徒步旅行；（航線不定的）貨船；（為挖地而穿的長統靴底）金屬片；鏟尖；<貶>不正經的女人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tramp</b> is a person who has no home or job, and very little money. Tramps go from place to place, and get food or money by asking people or by doing casual work. 流浪漢","examples":["Hypothermia is common among tramps sleeping outdoors. 體溫過低症在那些露宿戶外的流浪漢中很普遍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>tramp</b> of people is the sound of their heavy, regular walking. 沉重的腳步聲","examples":["He heard the slow, heavy tramp of feet on the stairs. 他聽見樓梯上緩慢而沉重的腳步聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone refers to a woman as a <b>tramp</b>, they are insulting her, because they think that she is immoral in her sexual behaviour. 蕩婦","examples":["He'd think I was a tramp, a cheap slut, and he'd lose all respect for me. 他會認為我是個蕩婦，一個低賤的妓女，不會對我有絲毫尊重。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tramp</b> somewhere, you walk there slowly and with regular, heavy steps, for a long time. 腳步沉重地緩緩行走; 踏","examples":["They put on their coats and tramped through the falling snow. 他們穿上大衣，在落雪中腳步沉重地緩緩走著。"]}]}]},"trench":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壕溝，溝渠；海溝，海底溝；戰壕，塹壕；塹壕陣地；一戰時期法國北部和比利時的塹壕戰（the trenches）；戰壕雨衣"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（地）上開溝，在……上挖戰壕；翻（田地，花園）的地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trench</b> is a long narrow channel that is cut into the ground, for example, in order to lay pipes or get rid of water. 溝渠","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trench</b> is a long narrow channel in the ground used by soldiers in order to protect themselves from the enemy. People often refer to the battlegrounds of the First World War in Northern France and Belgium as <b>the trenches</b>. 戰壕","examples":["We fought with them in the trenches. 我們在戰壕裡與他們作戰。"]}]}]},"tribute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（表示敬意的）禮物，頌辭，行為；（良好效果或影響的）體現，顯示；（尤指舊時一國向他國交納的）貢品，貢金；<史>（用於支付礦工工資，或給礦廠主、出租人的）礦石份子"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尤指團體或音樂家）（透過模仿）表演著名樂曲的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tribute</b> is something that you say, do, or make to show your admiration and respect for someone. 稱讚; 敬意","examples":["The song is a tribute to Roy Orbison. 這首歌是敬獻給羅伊·奧比森的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing is <b>a</b> <b>tribute</b> <b>to</b> another, the first thing is the result of the second and shows how good it is. 有成效的結果","examples":["His success has been a tribute to hard work, to professionalism. 他的成功是辛勤工作和兢兢業業的結果。"]}]}]},"trifle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瑣事，無價值的東西；屈萊弗甜食，乳脂鬆糕；稍微，有點兒（a trifle）；少量，少許"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"怠慢，小看；<古>輕浮地說（或做）；浪費（物品，尤指時間），虛度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>a trifle</b> to mean slightly or to a small extent, especially in order to make something you say seem less extreme. 有點兒","examples":["As a photographer, he'd found both locations just a trifle disappointing. 作為一名攝影師，他發現這兩個地方都有點兒令人失望。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trifle</b> is something that is considered to have little importance, value, or significance. 瑣事; 微不足道的東西","examples":["He had no money to spare on trifles. 他沒錢花在瑣碎的東西上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Trifle</b> is a cold dessert made of layers of sponge cake, fruit gelatin, fruit, and custard, and usually covered with cream. 屈萊弗甜食 (由蛋糕、果凍、水果、蛋奶沙司做成，上澆鮮奶油。)","examples":["...a bowl of trifle. …一碗屈萊弗甜食。"]}]}]},"trout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鱒魚，鮭魚（複數通常作 trout，也可作 trouts）；鱒魚肉；〈英，非正式，貶義〉不討人喜歡的老人；暴躁的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trout</b> is a fairly large fish that lives in rivers and streams. 鱒魚; 鮭魚","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Trout</b> is this fish eaten as food. 鱒魚肉; 鮭魚肉","examples":["Grilled trout needs only a squeeze of lemon. 烤鱒魚只需要一點檸檬榨汁。"]}]}]},"triple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"三倍的，三重的；三部分的，三人的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）成為三倍，（使）增加兩倍；三壘打，擊出三壘打"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（棒球中的）三壘打；三倍大的事物，由三部分組成的事物；三人賽（每邊三人的體育比賽）（triples）；三個同類事物組成的一組，三個一組（如體育賽事中的三連勝）；（滑冰、體操中的）轉體三週，連翻三圈；（鳴鐘術）三響（triples）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Triple</b> means consisting of three things or parts. 三個的; 三部分的","examples":["...a triple somersault. …連續三個筋斗。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>triples</b> or if you <b>triple</b> it, it becomes three times as large in size or number. 使成為三倍; 變成三倍","examples":["I got a fantastic new job and my salary tripled. 我得到了一份極好的新工作，我的薪水是原來的三倍。","The exhibition has tripled in size from last year. 這個展覽會面積是去年的三倍。"]}]},{"pos":"predet.","pos_name":"前置限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>triple the</b> amount or size of another thing, it is three times as large. 3倍的","examples":[]}]}]},"tuna":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"金槍魚；金槍魚肉；<美>金武仙人掌；<美>（可食用的）金武扇仙人掌果實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tuna</b> or <b>tuna fish</b> are large fish that live in warm seas and are caught for food. 金槍魚","examples":["...a shoal of tuna. …一群金槍魚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tuna</b> or <b>tuna fish</b> is this fish eaten as food. 金槍魚肉","examples":["She began opening a can of tuna. 她開始開啟一罐金槍魚。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any of various tropical American prickly pear cacti, esp <b>Opuntia tuna</b>, that are cultivated for their sweet edible fruits 刺梨仙人掌(尤指金槍仙人掌)","examples":[]}]}]},"tuition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指對個人或小組的）教學，指導；（尤指學院、大學或私立學校的）學費"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>tuition</b> to refer to the amount of money that you have to pay for being taught in a university, college, or private school. 學費","examples":["Angela's $7,000 tuition at university this year will be paid for with scholarships. 安吉拉今年$7000的大學學費將用獎學金來支付。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are given <b>tuition</b> in a particular subject, you are taught about that subject. 指導","examples":[]}]}]},"tyrant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴君"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>tyrant</b> to refer to someone who treats the people they have authority over in a cruel and unfair way. 暴君","examples":["...households where the father was a tyrant. …有暴君之父的家庭。"]}]}]},"trim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修剪，修整；削減，減少；修飾，點綴（尤指某物的邊緣）；切除，剪掉（不規則或不需要的部分）；調整（船帆）利用風力；使（飛機）配平；調整負載以保持（船，飛機）的平衡；使（身體某一部分）變結實，變瘦；（為個人升遷而在政治上）隨大流，見風使舵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指毛髮的）修剪；額外裝飾，邊飾，點綴物；汽車裝飾（尤指車內座椅鋪面或內墊襯料）；（電影剪輯後的）廢片；（船在水中的）水平位勢；（飛機）配平；良好的狀態（或情況）；機翼的位置"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"整齊的，整潔美觀的；修長的，苗條而健康的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>trim</b> is neat, and attractive. 整潔美觀的","examples":["The neighbors' gardens were trim and neat. 鄰居們的花園既整潔又美觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's figure as <b>trim</b>, you mean that it is attractive because there is no extra fat on their body. 苗條的","examples":["The driver was a trim young woman of perhaps thirty. 駕車者是一位大約三十來歲的苗條年輕女子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trim</b> something, for example, someone's hair, you cut off small amounts of it in order to make it look neater. 修剪","examples":["My friend trims my hair every eight weeks. 我朋友每隔8周就為我修剪一次頭髮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a government or other organization <b>trims</b> something such as a plan, policy, or amount, they reduce it slightly in extent or size. 削減","examples":["American companies looked at ways they could trim these costs. 美國公司研究了他們可能削減成本的方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as a piece of clothing <b>is trimmed</b> <b>with</b> a type of material or design, it is decorated with it, usually along its edges. 鑲邊於","examples":["...jackets, which are then trimmed with crocheted flowers. …鑲著鉤針編織花邊的夾克。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trim</b> is also a noun. 修剪","examples":["His hair needed a trim. 他的頭髮需要修剪了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>trim</b> on something such as a piece of clothing is a decoration, for example, along its edges, that is in a different colour or material. 鑲邊","examples":["...a white satin scarf with black trim. …一條鑲著黑邊的白色綢緞圍巾。"]}]}]},"umpire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（體育比賽中的）裁判；仲裁人，公斷人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……中擔任裁判"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>umpire</b> is a person whose job is to make sure that a sports contest or game is played fairly and that the rules are not broken. (體育比賽或競賽的) 裁判","examples":["The umpire's decision is final. 裁判的判決是不可更改的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>umpire</b> means to be the umpire in a sports contest or game. (在體育比賽或競賽中) 擔任裁判","examples":["He umpired baseball games. 他過去擔任棒球比賽的裁判。"]}]}]},"undergraduate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大學本科生，大學肄業生"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大學本科生的，大學肄業生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>undergraduate</b> is a student at a university or college who is studying for a bachelor's or associate's degree. 大學本科生","examples":["Economics undergraduates are probably the brightest in the university. 經濟學本科生很可能是該大學裡最聰明的學生。"]}]}]},"trot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（馬等動物的）小跑，慢跑；騎馬小跑；人的小步跑；<非正式>腹瀉，拉稀（the trots）；<澳，非正式>走運時期，倒黴時期；<澳，非正式>快步馬駕車賽（the trots）；（學生用來作弊的）筆記，答案；<英，非正式>（侮辱性用語）左傾分子，託派分子；剛學步的小孩；老太婆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（馬等四足動物）快步，疾走；步行，走；<非正式>小步快跑，疾行；騎馬小跑；<非正式>連珠炮似地說，急匆匆地做"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trot</b> somewhere, you move fairly fast at a speed between walking and running, taking small quick steps. 小跑","examples":["I trotted down the steps and out to the shed. 我小步跑下臺階去棚屋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an animal such as a horse <b>trots</b>, it moves fairly fast, taking quick small steps. You can also say that the rider of the animal <b>is trotting</b>. (馬等) 小跑","examples":["Alan took the reins and the small horse started trotting. 艾倫抓住韁繩，小馬開始小跑起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trot</b> is also a noun. 小跑","examples":["He walked briskly, but without breaking into a trot. 他輕快地走著，但沒有小跑起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Trot</b> is also a noun. (馬等的) 小跑","examples":["As they started up again, the horse broke into a brisk trot. 當他們又出發時，那匹馬便輕快地小跑起來。"]}]}]},"tuck":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把（布或紙張的邊緣）塞入；把…...塞入，把…...藏入；用…...蓋住，用…...圍緊；使蜷縮，使收縮；在…...上做拉皮手術；大吃；在（衣服上）縫褶子，給…...打"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（衣服或織物的）褶，打褶；（臉部或腹部的）整容小手術；食物,零食（尤指兒童在學校吃的糖果等）；（跳水、體操、下坡滑雪中的）抱膝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tuck</b> something somewhere, you put it there so that it is safe, comfortable, or neat. (為舒服或整齊) 把…塞入; 把…夾入","examples":["He tried to tuck his flapping shirt inside his trousers. 他試圖把飄動的襯衫塞進他的褲子裡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>tuck</b> to refer to a form of plastic surgery which involves reducing the size of a part of someone's body. 減脂手術","examples":["She'd undergone 13 operations, including a tummy tuck. 她做過13次手術，包括1次腹部減脂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a pleat or fold in a part of a garment, usually stitched down so as to make it a better fit or as decoration 縫摺","examples":[]}]}]},"underline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……下面畫線；強調，突出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指為強調）下劃線；（動物）下體輪廓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing, for example an action or an event, <b>underlines</b> another, it draws attention to it and emphasizes its importance. 突出顯示; 強調","examples":["The report underlined his concern that standards were at risk. 該報告強調了他對於標準被降低的擔憂。","This incident underlines the danger of travelling in the border area. 這一事件突出顯示了在邊界地區旅行的危險。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>underline</b> something such as a word or a sentence, you draw a line underneath it in order to make people notice it or to give it extra importance. 在…下面劃線","examples":["Underline the following that apply to you. 在以下適用於你的部分下面劃線。"]}]}]},"underneath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……下面，在……底下；在……底面，在……底部；在……表面之下"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在……下面，在……底下；在……底面，在……底部；在……表面之下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"物體的下表面，底面，底部（the underneath）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"下面的，底層的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>underneath</b> another, it is directly under it, and may be covered or hidden by it. 在…下面; 在…底下","examples":["The device exploded underneath a van. 那個裝置在一輛麵包車底下爆炸了。","...using dogs to locate people trapped underneath collapsed buildings. …利用狗來尋找困在倒塌樓房下面的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Underneath</b> is also a preposition. 在…內","examples":["Underneath his outgoing behaviour Luke was shy. 盧克表面外向、內心羞怯。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Underneath</b> is also an adverb. 在下面; 在底下","examples":["He has on his jeans and a long-sleeved blue denim shirt with a white T-shirt underneath. 他身穿牛仔褲和一件藍色長袖粗斜紋棉布襯衫，裡面還有件白色T恤衫。","The shooting-range is lit from underneath by rows of ruby-red light fixtures. 射擊場被一排排寶石紅照明裝置從下面照亮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The part of something which is <b>underneath</b> is the part which normally touches the ground or faces toward the ground. 在下面; 在底部","examples":["Check the actual construction of the chair by looking underneath. 看一下椅子的底部來檢查它的實際結構。","The sand martin is a brown bird with white underneath. 崖沙燕是一種腹部為白色的褐色的鳥。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>underneath</b> when talking about feelings and emotions that people do not show in their behaviour. 在內心","examples":["He was as violent as Nick underneath. 他在內心和尼克一樣暴烈。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Underneath</b> is also a noun. 下面; 底部","examples":["Now I know what the underneath of a car looks like. 現在我知道汽車的底部是什麼樣子了。"]}]}]},"vacancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"空缺，空職；（旅館等的）空房，空間；無知，空虛；空隙，空處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vacancy</b> is a job or position that has not been filled. 職位空缺","examples":["Most vacancies are at the senior level, requiring appropriate qualifications. 大多數空缺在高層，要求適當的資歷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If there are <b>vacancies</b> at a building such as a hotel, some of the rooms are available to rent. (酒店等的) 空房間","examples":["This year hotels that usually are jammed had vacancies all summer. 今年那些通常爆滿的旅館整個夏天都有空房。"]}]}]},"vapor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"蒸氣，水蒸氣（等於 vapour）；霧氣，煙霧"}],"sections":[]},"update":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……增加最新資訊，更新；使現代化；向……提供最新資訊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最新報道，最新訊息；（計算機軟體的）更新；新型，新版"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>update</b> something, you make it more modern, usually by adding new parts to it or giving new information. 更新","examples":["He was back in the office, updating the work schedule on the computer. 他回到辦公室，在計算機上更新了工作日程。","Airlines would prefer to update rather than retrain crews. 航空公司寧願增添新機組人員而不願對老的機組人員進行再培訓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>update</b> someone <b>on</b> a situation, you tell them the latest developments in that situation. 給…提供最新資訊","examples":["We'll update you on the day's top news stories. 我們將向你提供當天的頭條新聞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>update</b> is a news item containing the latest information about a particular situation. 最新訊息; 快訊","examples":["She had heard the newsflash on a TV channel's news update. 她在電影片道的新聞快訊裡聽到了這條簡短報道。","...a weather update. …最新天氣預報。"]}]}]},"upright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）直立的，挺直的；直立的，垂直的，立式的；正直的，誠實的；（椅子）直靠背的，沒有扶手的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"筆直地，直立地，垂直地；平穩地"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（起支撐作用的）直柱，立柱，直立部分；球門柱；立式鋼琴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are sitting or standing <b>upright</b>, you are sitting or standing with your back straight, rather than bending or lying down. 筆直的","examples":["Helen sat upright in her chair. 海倫筆直地坐在椅子上。","He moved into an upright position. 他換成了一個挺直的姿勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>upright</b> vacuum cleaner or freezer is tall rather than wide. 立式的 (吸塵器或冰箱)","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>upright</b> chair has a straight back and no arms. 有靠背無扶手的 (椅子)","examples":["He was sitting on an upright chair beside his bed, reading. 他正坐在床邊一把有靠背無扶手的椅子上閱讀。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can describe people as <b>upright</b> when they are careful to follow acceptable rules of behaviour and behave in a moral way. 正直的","examples":["...a very upright, trustworthy man. …一個非常正直、值得信任的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to vertical posts or the vertical parts of an object as <b>uprights</b>. 立柱","examples":["...the uprights of a canopy bed. …一張頂篷床的立柱。"]}]}]},"vanity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"虛榮（心），自負；（相對於非常嚴肅的事而言）無意義，微不足道；梳妝檯，盥洗櫃；自負的行為，虛榮的態度；自費出版"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>vanity</b>, you are critical of them because they take great pride in their appearance or abilities. 虛榮","examples":["Men who use steroids are motivated by sheer vanity. 服用類固醇的男人們純粹是受了虛榮心的驅使。"]}]}]},"vegetation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（總稱）植物，植被；（植物的）生長；呆板單調的生活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Plants, trees, and flowers can be referred to as <b>vegetation</b>. 植物","examples":["The inn has a garden of semi-tropical vegetation. 這家小旅館擁有一個亞熱帶植物園。"]}]}]},"vacuum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"真空，真空容器；真空吸塵器；空白，空虛；（用真空吸塵器所做的）清潔，清掃"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用真空吸塵器打掃"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"利用真空的；真空的；產生真空的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something creates a <b>vacuum</b>, they leave a place or position that then needs to be filled by another person or thing. 空缺","examples":["His presence should fill the power vacuum that has been developing over the past few days. 他的出現應該能填補過去幾天中形成的權力空缺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vacuum</b> is a space that contains no air or other gas. 真空","examples":["Wind is a current of air caused by a vacuum caused by hot air rising. 風是由熱空氣上升產生真空而引起的空氣流動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>vacuum</b> is the same as a . 真空吸塵器","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>in a vacuum</b>, it is not affected by any outside influences or information. 在與世隔絕的狀態中","examples":["Moral values cannot be taught in a vacuum. 道德價值觀不能在與世隔絕的狀態中進行傳授。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>vacuum</b> something, you clean it using a vacuum cleaner. 用真空吸塵器清潔","examples":["I vacuumed the carpets today. 我今天用吸塵器清潔地毯了。","It's important to vacuum regularly. 定期用吸塵器清潔是很重要的。"]}]}]},"veil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"面紗，面罩；（修女的）頭巾；遮蓋物，掩飾，藉口；避而不談（難堪或不愉快的）某事；（古猶太教）聖布；（植）菌幕；（穆斯林國家婦女）帶面紗的習俗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以面紗掩蓋；遮蓋，掩飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>veil</b> is a piece of thin soft cloth that women sometimes wear over their heads and that can also cover their face. 面紗","examples":["She's got long fair hair but she's got a veil over it. 她有長長的金髮，卻把面紗罩於其上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to something that hides or partly hides a situation or activity as a <b>veil</b>. 掩飾物","examples":["The country is ridding itself of its disgraced prime minister in a veil of secrecy. 該國正在暗地裡將其名譽掃地的首相趕下臺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to something that you can partly see through, such as a mist, as a <b>veil</b>. (薄霧等) 半透明物","examples":["The eruption has left a thin veil of dust in the upper atmosphere. 這次火山噴發在上層大氣中留下了一個薄薄的塵土層。"]}]}]},"vein":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靜脈；（植物的）葉脈，（昆蟲的）翅脈；（乾酪、石頭等的）紋理，紋路；礦脈，礦層，岩脈；（某種特定的）情緒，風格，主題；幾分；（普通用語或比喻用法）血管"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成脈絡；像脈絡般分佈於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>veins</b> are the thin tubes in your body through which your blood flows toward your heart. Compare . 靜脈","examples":["Many veins are found just under the skin. 許多靜脈就在皮膚下面。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is written or spoken <b>in</b> a particular <b>vein</b> is written or spoken in that style or mood. 風格; 語氣","examples":["It is one of his finest works in a lighter vein. 這是他使用了較為輕盈的風格的最佳作品之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>vein</b> <b>of</b> a particular quality is evidence of that quality that someone often shows in their behaviour or work. 跡象","examples":["A rich vein of humour runs through the book. 幽默的痕跡遍佈全書。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>veins</b> on a leaf are the thin lines on it. 葉脈","examples":["...the serrated edges and veins of the feathery leaves. …這些羽狀樹葉的鋸齒形邊緣和葉脈。"]}]}]},"velvet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天鵝絨，絲絨；（鹿角成長期中帶茸毛的）鹿角嫩皮，鹿茸；天鵝絨似的東西"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"天鵝絨制的，天鵝絨的；柔軟光滑的，天鵝絨般的（通常為暗色的）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Velvet</b> is soft material made from cotton, silk, or nylon, that has a thick layer of short cut threads on one side. 天鵝絨","examples":["...a charcoal-grey overcoat with a velvet collar. …一件帶天鵝絨衣領的深灰色大衣。"]}]}]},"videotape":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不可數）錄影帶；（可數）盒式錄影帶，錄影"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"將……錄到錄影帶上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Videotape</b> is magnetic tape that is used to record moving pictures and sounds to be shown on television. 錄影帶","examples":["...the use of videotape in criminal court rooms. …錄影帶在刑事法庭上的使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>videotape</b> is the same as a . 盒式錄影帶","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>videotape</b> a television programme or event, you record it on tape using a video recorder or video camera, so that you can watch it later. 錄製","examples":["She videotaped the entire trip. 她錄下了整個旅程。"]}]}]},"veto":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"否決權；拒絕認可，禁止"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"否決，禁止；拒不接受，反對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>vetoes</b> something, they forbid it, or stop it from being put into action. 否決","examples":["The president vetoed the economic package passed by Congress. 總統否決了國會透過的一攬子經濟計劃。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Veto</b> is also a noun. 否決","examples":["They need 12 votes to override his veto. 他們需要12票來推翻他的否決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Veto</b> is the right that someone in authority has to forbid something. 否決權","examples":["...the president's power of veto. …總統的否決權。"]}]}]},"vigor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"活力，精力（美式拼法；英式常作 vigour）；（文風、表達等的）氣勢，力度；（人名；英、法） Vigor，維戈爾"}],"sections":[]},"viewer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電視觀眾，觀眾；觀看者，觀賞者，觀察者；（計算機）檢視器，檢視程式；（光學）觀片器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Viewers</b> are people who watch television, or who are watching a particular programme on television. 電視觀眾","examples":["These programmes are each watched by around 19 million viewers every week. 這些電視節目中，每個每週都有約一千九百萬觀眾收看。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>viewer</b> is someone who is looking carefully at a picture or other interesting object. 觀賞者","examples":["...the relationship between the art object and the viewer. …藝術品和觀賞者之間的關係。"]}]}]},"vertical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"垂直的，直立的；縱向的；不同層次（或等級）的；（某類產品從生產到銷售各個階段）縱向結構的；（尤指疾病或遺傳特性傳遞）代代相傳的；（解剖）顱頂的，頭頂的；<古>頂點的，最高點的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"垂直線，垂直面，豎直位置；豎杆；垂直高度差"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>vertical</b> stands or points straight up. 垂直的","examples":["The climber inched up a vertical wall of rock. 那名登山者一點點爬上了一處垂直的岩石峭壁。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"垂直地","examples":["Cut each bulb in half vertically. 將每一個球莖垂直切成兩半。"]}]}]},"venture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"風險專案，冒險事業；冒險旅行，冒險行動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"敢於去（未知或危險等地方）；冒險；小心地說，謹慎地做；敢說，大膽表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>venture</b> is a project or activity that is new, exciting, and difficult because it involves the risk of failure. 風險專案; 冒險活動","examples":["...a Russian-American joint venture. …一個俄美合資的風險專案。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>venture</b> somewhere, you go somewhere that might be dangerous. 冒險去 (某處)","examples":["People are afraid to venture out for fear of sniper attacks. 人們不敢冒險外出，害怕狙擊手的襲擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>venture into</b> an activity, you do something that involves the risk of failure because it is new and different. 冒險 (從事活動)","examples":["He enjoyed little success when he ventured into business. 他在冒險涉足生意時很少成功。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>venture</b> a question or statement, you say it in an uncertain way because you are afraid it might be stupid or wrong. 試探地提出 (問題或觀點)","examples":["\"So you're Leo's girlfriend?\" he ventured. “那麼你就是利奧的女朋友了？”他小心地問道。","He ventured that plants draw part of their nourishment from the air. 他試探著提出了植物從空氣中吸取它們的部分養分的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>venture</b> <b>to</b> do something that requires courage or is risky, you do it. 冒險 (做某事)","examples":["\"Don't ask,\" he said, whenever Ginny ventured to raise the subject. 每當金尼冒險提起這個話題時，他總是說∶“你不要問了。”"]}]}]},"violinist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小提琴演奏者，小提琴家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>violinist</b> is someone who plays the violin. 小提琴手","examples":["Rose's father was a talented violinist. 羅斯的父親是一位天才的小提琴手。"]}]}]},"villain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反派角色，反面人物；<非正式>罪犯；禍首，元兇；壞人，惡棍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>villain</b> is someone who deliberately harms other people or breaks the law in order to get what he or she wants. 惡棍","examples":["I left the room, feeling like a villain and a murderer. 我離開了那個房間，感覺自己就像一個惡棍，一個殺人犯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>villain</b> in a novel, movie, or play is the main bad character. (小說、電影、戲劇中的) 反面主角","examples":["He also played a villain opposite Sylvester Stallone in Demolition Man (1992). 他在1992年的影片《超級戰警》中扮演了一個與西爾維斯特·史泰龍敵對的反面主角。"]}]}]},"visa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"簽證"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"簽發簽證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>visa</b> is an official document, or a stamp put in your passport, that allows you to enter or leave a particular country. 簽證","examples":["His visitor's visa expired. 他的訪問簽證過期了。","...an exit visa. …一張出境簽證。"]}]}]},"vine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葡萄屬植物，葡萄藤；藤本植物，攀緣植物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"長成藤蔓，爬藤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vine</b> is a plant that grows up or over things, especially one that produces grapes. (尤指葡萄的) 藤","examples":["Every square metre of soil was used, mainly for olives, vines, and almonds. 每一平方米的土壤都用上了，主要是種植橄欖、葡萄藤和杏樹。"]}]}]},"verbal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"口頭的，非書面的；用言辭的，文字的；動詞的；多話的，愛說話的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（語法）動詞性單詞（或短語、從句）；辱罵，侮辱；<非正式>話，（尤指）氣話；<非正式>歌詞，電影對話（verbals）；<英，非正式>（不利的）口頭供認"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>（尤指不正當地）誘使（嫌疑犯）招供"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>verbal</b> to indicate that something is expressed in speech rather than in writing or action. 口頭的","examples":["They were jostled and subjected to a torrent of verbal abuse. 他們被推來搡去，並受到了潮水般的辱罵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>verbal</b> to indicate that something is connected with words and the use of words. 詞語的; 文字的","examples":["The test has scores for verbal skills, mathematical skills, and abstract reasoning skills. 該項測試對文字表達技能、數學技能和抽象推理技能進行記分。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In grammar, <b>verbal</b> means relating to a verb. 動詞的","examples":["...a verbal noun. …一個動名詞。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"口頭地","examples":["Dave drank heavily and became verbally abusive. 戴夫喝多了，嘴裡髒話連篇。"]}]}]},"vow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誓約，諾言；（婚禮等上的）誓言"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"立誓，發誓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>vow</b> to do something, you make a serious promise or decision that you will do it. 發誓","examples":["While many models vow to go back to college, few do. 很多模特兒發誓要重返大學，但幾乎無人做到。","I solemnly vowed that someday I would return to live in Europe. 我鄭重起誓總有一天我要重回歐洲生活。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vow</b> is a serious promise or decision to do a particular thing. 誓言","examples":["I made a silent vow to be more careful in the future. 我默默發誓今後要更加小心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Vows</b> are a particular set of serious promises, such as the promises two people make when they are getting married. 誓約","examples":["I took my marriage vows and kept them. 我結婚時立下了誓言而且一直信守諾言。"]}]}]},"wade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"涉水，趟水，艱難地行進；強行介入，干預，插手；艱難地處理，費力地閱讀"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"跋涉，涉水，艱難行走"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wade</b> through something that makes it difficult to walk, usually water or mud, you walk through it. 蹚 (過水、泥等)","examples":["Her mother came to find them, wading across a river to reach them. 她的母親蹚過河來找他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>wade through</b> a lot of documents or pieces of information means to spend a lot of time and effort reading them or dealing with them. 費時費力地啃讀","examples":["It has taken a long time to wade through the \"incredible volume\" of evidence. 已經花費了很長時間來研讀這宗“卷帙浩瀚”的證據。"]}]}]},"wail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（因悲傷或疼痛）慟哭，號啕；哀號，高聲抱怨；發出長而高的聲音，呼嘯"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"慟哭，號啕大哭；呼嘯聲，尖嘯聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>wails</b>, they make long, loud, high-pitched cries which express sorrow or pain. 哀號","examples":["The women began to wail in mourning. 女人們開始大放悲聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a siren or an alarm <b>wails</b>, it makes a long, loud, high-pitched sound. (汽笛、警報等) 長鳴","examples":["Police cars, their sirens wailing, accompanied the trucks. 警車警笛長鳴，與卡車相隨。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wail</b> is also a noun. 悲鳴聲","examples":["Wails of grief were heard as visitors filed past the site of the disaster. 當來訪者們列隊走過災難現場時聽見陣陣悲痛的哀號聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wail</b> is also a noun. 長鳴聲","examples":["The wail of the bagpipe could be heard in the distance. 老遠就可聽到風笛悠長的奏鳴聲。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wail</b> something, you say it in a loud, high-pitched voice that shows that you are unhappy or in pain. 高聲數落","examples":["\"Now look what you've done!\" Shirley wailed. “現在，看看你幹了什麼！”雪莉高聲數落道。"]}]}]},"ware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陶器，器皿；（某種）物品，器皿；（尤指在市場或街上出售的）商品，貨物"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"當心，注意（狩獵時的警告叫喊聲）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"留意，小心"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to spend or squander 花費; 浪費","examples":[]}]}]},"wheelchair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輪椅，一種裝有輪子的可移動座椅，供因殘疾、患病或行走不便的人使用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wheelchair</b> is a chair with wheels that you use in order to move around in if you cannot walk properly, for example, because you are disabled or sick. 輪椅","examples":[]}]}]},"wharf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碼頭，停泊處"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"靠碼頭；把貨卸在碼頭上；為……建碼頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wharf</b> is a platform by a river or the sea where ships can be tied up. 碼頭","examples":[]}]}]},"warrior":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指舊時的）武士，勇士；（瑜伽體式）戰士"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>warrior</b> is a fighter or soldier, especially one in former times who was very brave and experienced in fighting. 武士; 勇士","examples":["...the tale of Bima, the great warrior of Indonesian folklore. …印度尼西亞民間傳說中大勇士畢馬的故事。"]}]}]},"warehouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"倉庫，貨棧，貨倉；倉儲式批發商店，倉儲式零售商店"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將（商品）存庫，使入庫；<美，非正式>將（某人，尤其是犯人或精神病患者）安置在條件差的倉庫式的收容所中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>warehouse</b> is a large building where raw materials or manufactured goods are stored until they are exported to other countries or distributed to stores to be sold. 倉庫; 貨棧","examples":[]}]}]},"ward":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"病房，病室；（城鎮或村莊的）區，選區；被監護人（尤指兒童）；<美>牢房；<古>監視，看守；（鎖內）齒凸（wards）；<史>城堡內空地，堡場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"接受（病人）入病房；<古>看守，保護"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ward</b> is a room in a hospital which has beds for many people, often people who need similar treatment. 病房","examples":["They transferred her to the psychiatric ward. 他們把她轉移到了精神病病房。"]}]}]},"whiskey":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"威士忌酒（通常作不可數名詞，由穀物發酵、蒸餾製成的烈性酒，美國、愛爾蘭等地常拼作 whiskey，蘇格蘭、加拿大等地常拼作 whisky）；（一）杯威士忌（酒）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"威士忌酒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whiskey</b> is a strong alcoholic drink made, especially in the United States and Ireland, from grain such as barley or rye. 威士忌酒 (尤指產於美國和愛爾蘭，由大麥或黑麥等釀成的烈性酒)","examples":["...a tumbler with about an inch of whiskey in it. …一個裝了大約一英寸高的威士忌酒的大玻璃杯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>whiskey</b> is a glass of whiskey. (一) 杯威士忌酒","examples":["Stark took two whiskeys from a tray. 斯塔克從托盤裡拿了兩杯威士忌。"]}]}]},"whine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘀咕，抱怨；發出哀鳴；（機器）嘎嘎響，嗖嗖響"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘎吱聲，吱吱聲；抱怨，嘀咕；哀鳴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>whines</b>, they make a long, high-pitched noise, especially one that sounds sad or unpleasant. 哀鳴","examples":["He could hear her dog barking and whining in the background. 他能聽到她的狗在遠處吠叫哀鳴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whine</b> is also a noun. 哀鳴","examples":["...the whine of air-raid sirens. …空襲警報的尖叫。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>whines</b>, they complain in an annoying way about something unimportant. (為小事) 令人厭煩地抱怨","examples":["They come to me to whine about their troubles. 他們到我這裡來絮絮叨叨地抱怨他們的煩惱。","...children who whine that they are bored. …哼哼唧唧地抱怨無聊的孩子們。"]}]}]},"whisk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攪打，攪拌，攪動（蛋、奶油等）；迅速帶走，急送；拂，撣（灰塵、碎屑等）；揮動（手、尾巴、布等）；飛快移動，飛奔"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"攪拌器，打蛋器；小笤帚，小掃帚；毛撣子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>whisk</b> someone or something somewhere, you take them or move them there quickly. 迅速帶走","examples":["He whisked her across the dance floor. 他帶她迅速穿過舞池。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>whisk</b> something such as eggs or cream, you stir it very fast, often with an electric device, so that it becomes full of small bubbles. (常指用攪打器) 快速攪打 (雞蛋、奶油等)","examples":["Just before serving, whisk the cream. 在端上桌之前，要攪打一下奶油。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>whisk</b> is a kitchen tool used for whisking eggs or cream. 攪拌器","examples":["Using a whisk, mix the yolks and sugar to a smooth paste. 用攪拌器將蛋黃和糖攪打成均勻的糊狀。"]}]}]},"widower":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鰥夫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>widower</b> is a man whose wife has died and who has not married again. 鰥夫","examples":["He is a widower and lives in Durango. 他是一個鰥夫，住在杜蘭戈。"]}]}]},"wig":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"假髮；<美，俚>頭腦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式，舊>嚴斥，斥責；使戴假髮；激動，發狂（wig out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wig</b> is a covering of false hair that you wear on your head, for example, because you have little hair of your own or because you want to cover up your own hair. 假髮","examples":["Jo wore a long wig that made her look very sexy. 喬帶著一頭長長的假髮，使她看起來很性感。"]}]}]},"whisky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"威士忌酒，威士忌（亦作 whiskey）；一杯威士忌（酒）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"威士忌的，威士忌酒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whisky</b> is whisky that is made especially in Scotland and Canada. (尤指產於蘇格蘭和加拿大的) 威士忌酒","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>whisky</b> is a glass of whisky. (一) 杯威士忌酒","examples":[]}]}]},"whirl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）飛旋，（使）旋轉；猛地轉動；暈眩，（思緒）混亂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"旋轉，迴旋； 紛繁，忙亂；暈眩；螺旋狀的糖果（或餅乾）；短暫的旅行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>whirls</b> around or if you <b>whirl</b> them around, they move around or turn around very quickly. 使快速旋轉; 快速旋轉","examples":["Not receiving an answer, she whirled around. 沒有得到答覆，她猛地轉過身來。","He was whirling Anne around the floor. 他正與安妮旋轉起舞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whirl</b> is also a noun. 快速旋轉","examples":["...the barely audible whirl of wheels. …幾乎聽不見的輪子轉動聲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a lot of intense activity as a <b>whirl</b> of activity. 緊張激烈的一連串","examples":["In half an hour's whirl of activity she does it all. 在半個小時馬不停蹄的忙碌中，她做完了這一切。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you decide to <b>give</b> an activity <b>a whirl</b>, you do it even though it is something that you have never tried before. 試一試","examples":["Why not give acupuncture a whirl? 為什麼不試試針灸？"]}]}]},"widow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"寡婦，遺孀；活寡婦（指丈夫經常外出參加某項運動或活動的女人）；寡婦鳥；（印刷）未排足的行"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使喪偶，使成為寡婦（或鰥夫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>widow</b> is a woman whose husband has died and who has not married again. 寡婦","examples":["She became a widow a year ago. 她一年前成了寡婦。"]}]}]},"wholesale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"批發，躉售"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"批發的，躉售的；大規模的，大批的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"批發地，成批賣地；完全地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"批發銷售；以……價格批發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wholesale</b> is the activity of buying and selling goods in large quantities and therefore at cheaper prices, usually to stores who then sell them to the public. Compare . 批發","examples":["Warehouse clubs allow members to buy goods at wholesale prices. 倉儲式會所允許會員以批發價購買商品。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is sold <b>wholesale</b>, it is sold in large quantities and at cheaper prices, usually to stores. 批發地","examples":["The fabrics are sold wholesale to retailers, fashion houses, and other manufacturers. 這些紡織品批發給零售商、時裝店和其他廠家。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>wholesale</b> to describe the destruction, removal, or changing of something when it affects a very large number of things or people. (破壞、遷移或變動) 大規模的","examples":["They are only doing what is necessary to prevent wholesale destruction of vegetation. 他們只是在做為防止植被遭大規模破壞而必須做的事情。"]}]}]},"whereabouts":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"下落，去向，所在之處"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在何處，靠近什麼地方"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"（尤用於某些動詞和形容詞後，引導表示具體處所的從句）具體在哪裡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>whereabouts</b> of a particular person or thing, you mean the place where that person or thing may be found. 下落","examples":["The police are anxious to hear from anyone who may know the whereabouts of the firearms. 警察急於從任何可能知道那些槍支下落的人那裡得到訊息。"]}]},{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whereabouts</b> in questions when you are asking precisely where something is. (用在疑問句中) 確切在哪裡","examples":["\"Whereabouts in France?\"—\"Normandy,\" I said. “在法國的確切位置？”—“諾曼底，”我說。","Whereabouts are you living? 你居住的確切地點是哪裡？"]}]}]},"wilderness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"未開發的地區，荒野；荒蕪的地方，雜草叢生處；低潮時期，在野；大量，茫茫一片"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wilderness</b> is a desert or other area of natural land which is not used by people. 荒野","examples":["...the icy Canadian wilderness. …冰封的加拿大荒野。"]}]}]},"wildlife":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"野生動植物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"野生動植物的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>wildlife</b> to refer to the animals and other living things that live in the wild. 野生生物","examples":["People were concerned that pets or wildlife could be affected by the pesticides. 人們擔心寵物或野生生物會受到殺蟲劑的影響。"]}]}]},"woodpecker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"啄木鳥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>woodpecker</b> is a type of bird with a long sharp beak. Woodpeckers use their beaks to make holes in tree trunks. 啄木鳥","examples":[]}]}]},"yacht":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帆船，快艇，遊艇"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"駕帆船比賽，駕駛帆船，乘遊艇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yacht</b> is a large boat with sails or a motor, used for racing or pleasure trips. 賽艇; 遊艇","examples":["His 36 ft yacht sank suddenly last summer. 他的36英尺遊艇去年夏天突然沉沒了。"]}]}]},"woe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痛苦，悲傷；麻煩，問題"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"唉（表示痛苦、悲傷或悔恨）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Woe</b> is great sadness. 悲傷","examples":["He listened to my tale of woe. 他聽了我悲傷的故事。"]}]}]},"workshop":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"車間，工場，作坊；研討會，講習班"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在正式上演前）研討性演出（戲劇）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>workshop</b> is a period of discussion or practical work on a particular subject in which a group of people share their knowledge or experience. 討論會","examples":["Trumpeter Marcus Belgrave ran a jazz workshop for young artists. 鼓手馬庫斯馬貝爾格瑞夫為年輕藝術家們舉辦了一場爵士樂研討會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>workshop</b> is a building that contains tools or machinery for making or repairing things, especially using wood or metal. 車間","examples":["...a modestly equipped workshop. …一個裝備普通的車間。"]}]}]},"wreath":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花環，花冠，花圈；環狀物，圈狀物；（煙、雲等的）環，圈；（紋章）飾環"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wreath</b> is an arrangement of flowers and leaves in the shape of a circle, which you put on a grave or by a statue to show that you remember a person who has died or people who have died. 花圈","examples":["The coffin lying before the altar was bare, except for a single wreath of white roses. 擺在聖壇前的棺材上光禿禿的，只有一個白玫瑰花圈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wreath</b> is a circle of leaves that some people hang somewhere in their house or on the front door as decoration. (裝飾用的) 花環","examples":["A Christmas wreath exclaiming PEACE ON EARTH hangs on the restaurant door. 一個寫著“世界和平”的聖誕花環懸掛在飯店的門上。"]}]}]},"wring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"擰，絞（用力扭轉擠壓以擠出水分）；設法獲取，榨取，強行索取；扭斷，猛扭（尤指脖頸）；搓手，絞手；緊握（手）；使痛苦，折磨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一擰，一絞，一擠；扭動"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<舊，文學>扭動，蠕動；感到痛苦，感到苦惱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<習語> wringing wet 渾身溼透，溼得擰得出水來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wring</b> something <b>out of</b> someone, you manage to make them give it to you even though they do not want to. 設法獲取","examples":["Buyers use different ruses to wring free credit out of their suppliers. 買主們想方設法從他們那些供應商那裡獲取無息賒購。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>wrings</b> their <b>hands</b>, they hold them together and twist and turn them, usually because they are very worried or upset about something. You can also say that someone is <b>wringing</b> their <b>hands</b> when they are expressing sorrow that a situation is so bad but are saying that they are unable to change it. (因焦慮、悲傷或無計可施) 紐絞雙手","examples":["We can't simply stand by wringing our hands. We have to do something. 我們不能只站著搓手，我們得做點什麼。"]}]}]},"worship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"敬奉（神）；愛慕，崇拜"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"敬神，拜神；崇拜，愛慕；<英> 閣下（對地位高的人的尊稱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>worship</b> a god, you show your respect to the god, for example, by saying prayers. 敬奉","examples":["..disputes over ways of life and ways of worshipping God. …一些在生活方式和敬奉上帝方式上的爭論。","He prefers to worship in his own home. 他更喜歡在自己的家裡敬奉神明。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>worship</b> someone or something, you love them or admire them very much. 愛慕","examples":["She had worshipped him for years. 她愛慕他已有好多年了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worship</b> is also a noun. 敬奉","examples":["...the worship of the ancient Roman gods. …對古羅馬眾神的敬奉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"敬神者","examples":["She burst into tears and loud sobs that disturbed the other worshippers. 她突然哭起來，大聲抽噎，干擾了其他拜神者。"]}]}]},"yarn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（棉、毛等的）紗，紗線，紡線；（尤指難以置信的）故事，奇談；<澳，紐西蘭>閒聊，閒談"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>講（長而不可信的）故事，信口開河；<澳，紐西蘭>閒聊，談話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yarn</b> is thread used for knitting or making cloth. 紗線","examples":["She still spins the yarn and knits sweaters for her family. 她仍在為她的家人紡線織毛衣。"]}]}]},"yeast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酵母菌；酵母（含酵母菌的發酵劑，用於發麵和釀酒）；酵母片；（比喻）引起騷動或變化的因素；（舊用或文學）泡沫，浮沫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（罕）發酵；起泡沫；加入酵母使發酵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yeast</b> is a kind of fungus which is used to make bread rise, and in making alcoholic drinks such as beer. 酵母","examples":[]}]}]},"yoga":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瑜伽，瑜伽術； 瑜伽派（印度哲學派別）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Yoga</b> is a type of exercise in which you move your body into various positions in order to become more fit or flexible, to improve your breathing, and to relax your mind. 瑜伽","examples":["I do yoga twice a week. 我一週做兩次瑜伽。"]}]}]},"absentminded":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"心不在焉的，茫然的，神情恍惚的"}],"sections":[]},"zinc":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鋅；（非洲某些地方用於搭建屋頂、棚子等的）波紋鐵板，瓦楞鐵板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（為防鏽而）鍍鋅於（鐵）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Zinc</b> is a bluish-white metal which is used to make other metals such as brass, or to cover other metals such as iron to stop rust from forming. 鋅","examples":[]}]}]},"abnormal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反常的，異常的，變態的；不規則的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>abnormal</b> is unusual, especially in a way that is troublesome. 異常的","examples":["...abnormal heart rhythms and high anxiety levels. …異常的心律和高度焦慮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"異常地","examples":["...abnormally high levels of glucose. …異常高的葡萄糖指標。"]}]}]},"accountable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"負有責任的，應作解釋的；可理解的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>accountable</b> <b>to</b> someone <b>for</b> something that you do, you are responsible for it and must be prepared to justify your actions to that person. 負有責任的","examples":["Public officials can finally be held accountable for their actions. 政府官員最終是要對他們的行為負責任的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"責任心","examples":["...a drive toward democracy and greater accountability. …一場促進民主和增強責任心的運動。"]}]}]},"zoom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"快速移動，迅速前往；（價格、數量、大小等）陡升，激增；（使鏡頭或攝影機）推近（或拉遠）；留意到，特別關注；使用視訊會議軟體 Zoom 與人交流"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（車輛等）疾馳的聲音；變焦鏡頭；進行變焦攝影"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"用於表示突然的快速移動嗖，嗖地，霍地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>zoom</b> somewhere, you go there very quickly. 趕往","examples":["We zoomed through the gallery. 我們快速穿過了畫廊。"]}]}]},"accessible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可到達的，可進入的；易得到的，可使用的；可以理解的，易懂的；平易近人的，隨和的；易受影響的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or building is <b>accessible</b> <b>to</b> people, it is easy for them to reach it or get into it. If an object is <b>accessible</b>, it is easy to reach. (地方) 易於進入的; (物品) 易於接近的","examples":["The centre is easily accessible to the general public. 該中心對於廣大公眾來講很便利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>accessible</b> <b>to</b> people, they can easily use it or obtain it. 易使用的; 易得到的","examples":["The aim of any reform of legal aid should be to make the system accessible to more people. 任何法律援助改革的目標都應該是讓該體系服務於更多的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a book, painting, or other work of art as <b>accessible</b>, you think it is good because it is simple enough for people to understand and appreciate easily. 淺顯易懂的","examples":["Both say they want to write literary books that are accessible to a general audience. 兩個人都說他們要寫對於普通讀者淺顯易懂的文學書籍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(地方) 易於進入性; (物品) 易於接近性","examples":["...the easy accessibility of the area. …該地區的交通便利性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"易使用性; 可及性","examples":["...growing public concern about the cost, quality and accessibility of health care. …公眾對醫療保健的費用、質量與可及性的日益關注。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"易懂性","examples":["Seminar topics are chosen for their accessibility to a general audience. 專題討論會的話題是根據普通聽眾的理解力來選定的。"]}]}]},"administrative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"管理的，行政的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Administrative</b> work involves organizing and supervising an organization or institution. 行政的; 管理的","examples":["Other industries have had to sack managers to reduce administrative costs. 其他行業已不得不解僱管理人員來減少管理成本。"]}]}]},"zip":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>拉鍊，拉鎖；<非正式>速度，活力；<美，非正式>零，沒有；郵政編碼；移動速度"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用拉鍊扣上，拉開拉鍊；（使）迅速移動；壓縮（電腦檔案）；伴隨嘶嘶聲移動；給……以力量或速度；增添活力或興趣"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（袋，包等）用拉鍊扣住的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>zip</b> something, you fasten it using a zipper. 用拉鎖繫上","examples":["She zipped her jeans. 她拉上了她的牛仔褲拉鎖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>zip</b> a computer file means to compress it so that it needs less space for storage on disk and can be transmitted more quickly. 壓縮 (電腦檔案)","examples":["If you zipped the files first, they did not become read-only when written to the CD. 如果你先壓縮了這些檔案，寫入光碟時它們就不變成只讀檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>zip</b> is a device used to open and close parts of clothes and bags. It consists of two rows of metal or plastic teeth which separate or fasten together as you pull a small handle along them. 拉鎖","examples":["He pulled the zip of his leather jacket down slightly. 他稍稍拉下了他皮夾克的拉鎖。"]}]}]},"affectionate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"表達愛意的，深情的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>affectionate</b>, you show your love or fondness for another person in the way that you behave toward them. 顯露感情的","examples":["They seemed devoted to each other and were openly affectionate. 他們似乎很相愛，公然含情脈脈。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"顯露感情地","examples":["He looked affectionately at his niece. 他慈愛地看著他的侄女。"]}]}]},"yield":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"產生（收益、效益等），產生（結果）；出產（天然產品，農產品，工業產品）；屈服，讓步；放棄，讓出；給（大路上的車輛）讓路；（受壓）活動，彎曲，折斷；<正式>被……替代；請（某人）講話；停止爭論"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"產量；收益，利潤，紅利（或股息）率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>yield</b> <b>to</b> someone or something, you stop resisting them. 屈服","examples":["Carmen yielded to general pressure and grudgingly took the child to a specialist. 卡門屈服於普遍的壓力，不得已帶孩子去看了位專科大夫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a moving person or a vehicle <b>yields</b>, they slow down in order to allow other people or vehicles to pass in front of them. 讓行","examples":["When entering a trail or starting a descent, yield to other skiers. 進入滑道或開始下滑時，給其他滑雪者們讓行。","...examples of common signs like No Smoking and Yield. …像“禁止吸菸”和“讓行”這樣的常見標誌例子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>yields</b>, it breaks or moves position because force or pressure has been put on it. (因受力或受壓而) 破碎; 斷裂; 移位","examples":["He reached the massive door of the barn and pushed. It yielded. 他夠著了畜棚厚重的大門推了推。門開了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>yield</b> something that you have control of or responsibility for, you allow someone else to have control or responsibility for it. 放棄","examples":["He may yield control. 他可能放棄控制權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an area of land <b>yields</b> a particular amount of a crop, this is the amount that is produced. You can also say that a number of animals <b>yield</b> a particular amount of meat. 產","examples":["Last year 400,000 acres of land yielded a crop worth $1.75 billion. 去年40萬英畝的土地出產了價值17.5億美元的糧食。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a tax or investment <b>yields</b> an amount of money or profit, this money or profit is obtained from it. 產生 (收益)","examples":["It yielded a profit of at least $36 million. 它帶來了至少三千六百萬美元的利潤。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>yields</b> a result or piece of information, it produces it. 產生 (結果); 製造 (訊息)","examples":["This research has been in progress since 1961 and has yielded a great number of positive results. 這項研究自1961年以來一直在開展，已經取得了大量的積極成果。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>yield</b> is the amount of food produced on an area of land or by a number of animals. 產量","examples":["...improving the yield of the crop. …增加農作物的產量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>yield</b> is the amount of money or profit produced by an investment. (投資的) 利潤; 收益","examples":["...a yield of 4%. …4%的收益。","The high yields available on the dividend shares made them attractive to private investors. 股息股能獲得的高收益使它們對私人投資者們很有吸引力。"]}]}]},"acute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嚴重的，危險的；急性的，劇烈的；靈敏的；敏銳的，有洞察力的；銳角的；帶尖音符的；（聲音）高的，尖的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>acute</b> to indicate that an undesirable situation or feeling is very severe or intense. 嚴峻的","examples":["The war has aggravated an acute economic crisis. 這場戰爭加劇了一場嚴峻的經濟危機。","The report has caused acute embarrassment to the government. 這份報告使政府極其尷尬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>acute</b> illness is one that becomes severe very quickly but does not last very long. Compare . 急性的","examples":["...a patient with acute rheumatoid arthritis. …一位患急性風溼性關節炎的病人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a person's or animal's sight, hearing, or sense of smell is <b>acute</b>, it is sensitive and powerful. 敏銳的","examples":["When she lost her sight, her other senses grew more acute. 失明以後，她的其他感官變得更加敏銳了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>acute</b> angle is less than 90°. Compare  angle. 銳 (角)","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"An <b>acute</b> accent is a symbol that is placed over vowels in some languages in order to indicate how that vowel is pronounced or over one letter in a word to indicate where it is stressed. You refer to a letter with this accent as, for example, e <b>acute</b>. For example, there is an acute accent over the letter \"e\" in the French word \"café.\" 尖音符的 (E)(上的符號)","examples":[]}]}]},"amiable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"和藹可親的，友好的；令人愉快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>amiable</b> is friendly and pleasant to be with. 和藹可親的","examples":["She had been surprised at how amiable and polite he had been. 她對他如此和藹可親、彬彬有禮感到了驚訝。"]}]}]},"ambiguous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"模稜兩可的，有歧義的；不明朗的，不確定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>ambiguous</b>, you mean that it is unclear or confusing because it can be understood in more than one way. 模稜兩可的","examples":["This agreement is very ambiguous and open to various interpretations. 這個協議非常模稜兩可，可以有多種解釋。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"模稜兩可地","examples":["The national conference on democracy ended ambiguously. 這次全國民主大會含糊其詞地結束了。"]}]}]},"analytical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"具備分析能力的，善於分析的；分析的，分析性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>analytical</b> way of doing something involves the use of logical reasoning. 分析的","examples":["I have an analytical approach to every survey. 我對每項調查都採用一種分析的方法。"]}]}]},"anonymous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"匿名的，不知名的；不記名的，不具名的；無特色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you remain <b>anonymous</b> when you do something, you do not let people know that you were the person who did it. 匿名的","examples":["You can remain anonymous if you wish. 如果你願意你可以保持匿名。","An anonymous benefactor stepped in to provide the prize money. 一位匿名捐助人參與進來提供了獎金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>anonymous</b> does not reveal who you are. 不記名的","examples":["Of course, that would have to be by anonymous vote. 當然，那得是透過不記名投票。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"匿名","examples":["Both mother and daughter, who have requested anonymity, are doing fine. 要求匿名的母女情況都好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不記名","examples":["He claims many more people would support him in the anonymity of a voting booth. 他聲稱在投票站不記名的情況下更多的人會支援他。"]}]}]},"applicable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"適用的，適當的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>applicable</b> <b>to</b> a particular situation is relevant to it or can be applied to it. 適用的","examples":["What is a reasonable standard for one family is not applicable for another. 對一個家庭合理的標準對於另一個家庭並不適用。"]}]}]},"arrogant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傲慢的，自大的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>arrogant</b> behaves in a proud, unpleasant way toward other people because they believe that they are more important than others. 傲慢的","examples":["He was so arrogant. 他是如此傲慢。","That sounds arrogant, doesn't it? 那聽起來很傲慢，不是嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傲慢","examples":["At times the arrogance of those in power is quite blatant. 有時那些當權者的傲慢很露骨。"]}]}]},"bizarre":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇異的，古怪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>bizarre</b> is very odd and strange. 怪異的","examples":["The game was also notable for the bizarre behaviour of the team's manager. 這場比賽另一值得注意的地方是該隊經理人異乎尋常的表現。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"怪異地","examples":["She dressed bizarrely. 她穿著怪異。"]}]}]},"awesome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"讓人驚歎的，令人敬畏的；非常棒的，極佳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>awesome</b> person or thing is very impressive and often frightening. 令人畏懼的","examples":["...the awesome responsibility of sending men into combat. …派士兵去打仗的令人畏懼的責任。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>awesome</b>, you are emphasizing that you think that they are very impressive or extraordinary. 棒極了的","examples":["Melvill called the flight \"mind-blowing\" and \"awesome.\" 梅爾維爾說這次飛行令人“無比興奮”、“棒極了”。"]}]}]},"authentic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原作的，真跡的；傳統的，正宗的；逼真的，模擬的；真實的，可靠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>authentic</b> person, object, or emotion is genuine. 真實的","examples":["...authentic Italian food. …正宗的義大利食品。","She has authentic charm whereas most people simply have nice manners. 她有真正的魅力，而大多數人只是有禮貌而已。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>authentic</b>, you mean that it is such a good imitation that it is almost the same as or as good as the original. 逼真的","examples":["...patterns for making authentic frontier-style clothing. …製作地道的邊疆風格服裝的圖樣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>authentic</b> piece of information or account of something is reliable and accurate. 可靠的","examples":["I had obtained the authentic details about the birth of the organization. 我已經弄到了有關該組織成立的可靠的詳細資料。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"真實性","examples":["There are factors, however, that have cast doubt on the statue's authenticity. 然而，有些因素已經讓人們對這座雕像的真實性產生了懷疑。"]}]}]},"bleak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不樂觀的，無望的；無遮掩的，荒涼的；陰冷的，寒冷的；沮喪的，陰鬱的；（人或其表情）冷漠的，冷峻的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"歐鮊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation is <b>bleak</b>, it is bad, and seems unlikely to improve. 黯淡的","examples":["The immediate outlook remains bleak. 最近的前景依然很黯淡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place as <b>bleak</b>, you mean that it looks cold, empty, and unattractive. 荒涼的","examples":["The island's pretty bleak. 這個島很荒涼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When the weather is <b>bleak</b>, it is cold, dull, and unpleasant. 陰冷的","examples":["The weather can be quite bleak on the coast. 沿海一帶的天氣可能會十分陰冷。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone looks or sounds <b>bleak</b>, they look or sound depressed, as if they have no hope or energy. 沮喪的","examples":["His face was bleak. 他面容沮喪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"黯淡","examples":["The continued bleakness of the American job market was blamed. 美國就業市場的持續低迷被認為是其根源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any slender silvery European cyprinid fish of the genus <b>Alburnus</b>, esp <b>A. lucidus</b>, occurring in slow-flowing rivers 歐鮊魚; 銀鯉","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"沮喪地","examples":["\"There is nothing left,\" she says bleakly. “一點也不剩了，”她沮喪地說。"]}]}]},"bulky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"笨重的，龐大的；大塊頭的，高大肥胖的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>bulky</b> is large and heavy. Bulky things are often difficult to move or deal with. 大而笨重的","examples":["...bulky items like lawn mowers. …割草機這樣笨重的東西。"]}]}]},"biological":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生物的，生物學的，生命的；親生的；含酶的；生化武器的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Biological</b> is used to describe processes and states that occur in the bodies and cells of living things. 與生命過程和狀態有關的","examples":["The living organisms somehow concentrated the minerals by biological processes. 活的有機物以某種方式隨其生命過程聚集了礦物質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Biological</b> is used to describe activities concerned with the study of living things. 生物學的","examples":["...all aspects of biological research associated with leprosy. …與麻風病有關的生物學研究的方方面面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Biological</b> weapons and <b>biological</b> warfare involve the use of bacteria or other living organisms in order to attack human beings, animals, or plants. 生物性的 (武器、戰爭)","examples":["Such a war could result in the use of chemical and biological weapons. 這樣一場戰爭可能導致生化武器的使用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Biological</b> pest control is the use of bacteria or other living organisms in order to destroy other organisms which are harmful to plants or crops. (利用細菌或其他生物對有害生物進行) 生物控制的","examples":["...a consultant on biological control of agricultural pests. …一位農作物害蟲生物防治顧問。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A child's <b>biological</b> parents are the man and woman who caused him or her to be born, rather than other adults who raise him or her. (指父母親) 生身的","examples":["...foster parents for young teenagers whose biological parents have rejected them. …被親生父母拋棄的十幾歲青少年的養父母們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"與生命過程和狀態有關地","examples":["Much of our behaviour is biologically determined. 我們的許多行為是由生命過程和狀態所決定的。"]}]}]},"brisk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕快的，生氣勃勃的；興隆的，紅火的；涼爽的，清新的；精幹利落的，麻利的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"加快；使……活潑，使……興旺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brisk</b> activity or action is done quickly and in an energetic way. 輕快的","examples":["Taking a brisk walk can often induce a feeling of well-being. 輕快的散步經常能使人心曠神怡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If trade or business is <b>brisk</b>, things are being sold very quickly and a lot of money is being made. (買賣、生意) 興隆的","examples":["Vendors were doing a brisk trade in souvenirs. 小販們的紀念品生意很興隆。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the weather is <b>brisk</b>, it is cold and fresh. 寒冷而清新的","examples":["...a typically brisk winter's day on the south coast. …南海岸典型的寒冷而清新的冬日。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Someone who is <b>brisk</b> behaves in a busy, confident way which shows that they want to get things done quickly. 乾脆利索的","examples":["The Chief summoned me downstairs. He was brisk and businesslike. 上司召我到樓下。他做事幹脆利索而有效率。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕快地","examples":["Eve walked briskly down the corridor to her son's room. 伊芙輕快地沿著走廊走到她兒子的房間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"興隆地","examples":["A trader said gold sold briskly on the local market. 一位貿易商說黃金在當地市場的銷售很興旺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"脆利索地","examples":["\"Anyhow,\" she added briskly, \"it's none of my business.\" “無論如何”，她乾脆利索地加了一句：“這不關我的事。”"]}]}]},"colloquial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"口語的，非正式的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Colloquial</b> words and phrases are informal and are used mainly in conversation. 口語的","examples":["...a colloquial expression. …一個口語表達法。"]}]}]},"coherent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有條理的，連貫的；說話條理清晰的，易於理解的；團結一致的，凝聚的；（波）相干的，相參的；黏著的，黏連的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>coherent</b>, it is well planned, so that it is clear and sensible and all its parts go well with each other. 連貫的","examples":["He has failed to work out a coherent strategy for modernizing the service. 他無法想出一個連貫的策略來使該服務現代化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>coherent</b>, they express their thoughts in a clear and calm way, so that other people can understand what they are saying. 條理清楚的","examples":["He's so calm when he answers questions in interviews. I wish I could be that coherent. 他如此鎮定地回答了訪談中的問題。我希望我也能那樣有條不紊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"連貫性","examples":["The campaign was widely criticized for making tactical mistakes and for a lack of coherence. 該運動遭到廣泛批評，因其有策略錯誤且缺乏連貫性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"條理性","examples":["This was debated eagerly at first, but with diminishing coherence as the champagne took hold. 辯論一開始滿熱烈的，可是上了香檳後，條理性就降低了。"]}]}]},"clinical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"診所的，醫務室的；臨床的，臨床診斷的；冷靜的，無感情的；簡陋的，無裝飾的；精確的，嫻熟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clinical</b> means involving or relating to the direct medical treatment or testing of patients. 臨床的","examples":["The first clinical trials were expected to begin next year. 第一批臨床試驗預計明年開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>clinical</b> to describe thought or behaviour that is very logical and does not involve any emotion. 無人情味的","examples":["All this questioning is so clinical – it kills romance. 所有這些發問是如此如此無人情味–使浪漫蕩然無存。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"臨床地","examples":["She was diagnosed as being clinically depressed. 她被診斷為患臨床抑鬱症。"]}]}]},"charitable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"慈善的；仁慈的，寬容的；慷慨的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>charitable</b> organization or activity helps and supports people who are ill, disabled, or very poor. 慈善的","examples":["...charitable work for the handicapped. …為殘疾人做的慈善工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>charitable</b> to people is kind or understanding toward them. 仁慈的","examples":["They were less than charitable toward the referee. 他們對裁判員毫不仁慈。"]}]}]},"communicative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛說話的，健談的；交際的，溝通的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>communicative</b> talks to people, for example about their feelings, and tells people things. 愛說話的; 健談的","examples":["She has become a lot more tolerant and communicative. 她變成了一個更寬容，更健談的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Communicative</b> means relating to the ability to communicate. 交際能力的","examples":["We have a very communicative approach to teaching languages. 我們有一個交際能力很強的方法來教授語言。"]}]}]},"chronic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（疾病）慢性的，長期的；（問題）一直有的，反覆出現的；難以根除的，積習難改的；<英，非正式>糟透的，拙劣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>chronic</b> illness or disability lasts for a very long time. Compare . 慢性的; 長期的","examples":["...chronic back pain. …長期背痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe someone's bad habits or behaviour as <b>chronic</b> when they have behaved like that for a long time and do not seem to be able to stop themselves. 積習難改的","examples":["...a chronic worrier. …一個老是發愁的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>chronic</b> situation or problem is very severe and unpleasant. 嚴重的","examples":["One cause of the artist's suicide seems to have been chronic poverty. 那位藝術家自殺的原因之一好像是極度貧困。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"慢性地; 長期地","examples":["Most of them were chronically ill. 他們中大部分人都有慢性病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"嚴重地","examples":["Research and technology are said to be chronically underfunded. 據說研究和技術資金嚴重不足。"]}]}]},"comparable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可比的，可比較的；類似的，同類的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>comparable</b> to something else is roughly similar, for example in amount or importance. (數量、重要性等) 相當的","examples":["...paying the same wages to men and women for work of comparable value. …對同等工作的男女支付同樣的工薪。","Farmers were supposed to get an income comparable to that of townspeople. 農民應該獲得與城鎮人相當的收入。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If two or more things are <b>comparable</b>, they are of the same kind or are in the same situation, and so they can reasonably be compared. 可比的","examples":["In other comparable countries, real wages increased much more rapidly. 在其他可比的國家裡實際工資增長快得多。","By contrast, the comparable figure for Canada is 16 percent. 對比之下，加拿大的可比數字是16%。"]}]}]},"comparative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（形容詞或副詞的）比較級；對手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"比較的，相比的；相對的，比較而言的；（形容詞或副詞）比較級的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>comparative</b> to show that you are judging something against a previous or different situation. For example, <b>comparative</b> calm is a situation which is calmer than before or calmer than the situation in other places. 比較的 (平靜等)","examples":["The task was accomplished with comparative ease. 這項任務完成得比較容易。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>comparative</b> study is a study that involves the comparison of two or more things of the same kind. 比較的 (研究)","examples":["...a comparative study of the dietary practices of people from various regions of India. …對印度不同地區人們飲食習慣的比較研究。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In grammar, the <b>comparative</b> form of an adjective or adverb shows that something has more of a quality than something else has. For example, \"bigger\" is the comparative form of \"big,\" and \"more quickly\" is the comparative form of \"quickly.\" Compare . 比較級的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"比較地","examples":["...a comparatively small nation. …一個比較小的國家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Comparative</b> is also a noun. 比較級","examples":["The comparative of \"pretty\" is \"prettier.\" 的比較級是。"]}]}]},"compatible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相容的；可共存的；可和睦相處的；與……一致的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"相容性計算機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things, for example systems, ideas, and beliefs, are <b>compatible</b>, they work well together or can exist together successfully. (系統、觀點、信念等) 相容的","examples":["Free enterprise, he argued, was compatible with Russian values and traditions. 他辯稱自由企業與俄羅斯的價值觀和傳統是相容的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you are <b>compatible</b> with someone, you mean that you have a good relationship with them because you have similar opinions and interests. 意趣相投的","examples":["Mildred and I are very compatible. She's interested in the things that interest me. 米爾德麗德和我非常意趣相投。我感興趣的東西她也感興趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one brand of computer or computer equipment is <b>compatible</b> <b>with</b> another brand, they can be used together and can use the same software. (電腦品牌) 相容的","examples":["Fujitsu took over another American firm, Amdal, to help it to make and sell machines compatible with IBM in the United States. 富士通接管了另一家美國公司安島，以幫助其在美國生產並銷售與IBM相容的機器。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"相容性","examples":["...the issue of Islam and its compatibility with democracy. …伊斯蘭教及其與民主體制的相容性問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"意趣相投","examples":["As a result of their compatibility, Haig and Fraser were able to bring about wide-ranging reforms. 由於意趣相投，黑格和弗雷澤能帶來廣泛的改革。"]}]}]},"conscientious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"認真的，勤勤懇懇的；憑良心的，與良心有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>conscientious</b> is very careful to do their work properly. 認真的","examples":["We are generally very conscientious about our work. 我們一般對工作都是很認真的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"認真地","examples":["He studied conscientiously and enthusiastically. 他認真積極地學習。"]}]}]},"competent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"能幹的，能勝任的；合格的，過得去的；精神正常的，智力無缺陷的；有決定權的；有法定資格的；活性的，（處於）感受態的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>competent</b> is efficient and effective. 有能力的","examples":["He was a loyal, distinguished and very competent civil servant. 他是一個忠誠、出色、很有能力的公務員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>competent</b> <b>to</b> do something, you have the skills, abilities, or experience necessary to do it well. 能勝任的","examples":["Most adults do not feel competent to deal with a medical emergency involving a child. 多數成年人感到難以應付小孩醫療突發事件。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有能力地","examples":["The government performed competently in the face of multiple challenges. 政府在面臨多重挑戰時表現得很出色。"]}]}]},"concise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"簡明的，簡潔的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>concise</b> says everything that is necessary without using any unnecessary words. 簡潔的","examples":["Burton's text is concise and informative. 伯頓的文章文字簡潔、內容豐富。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>concise</b> edition of a book, especially a dictionary, is shorter than the original edition. 簡明的 (版本)","examples":["...Sotheby's Concise Encyclopedia of Porcelain. …索思比的《簡明瓷器百科全書》。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"簡潔地","examples":["He'd delivered his report clearly and concisely. 他簡潔明瞭地陳述了他的報告。"]}]}]},"confidential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"機密的，保密的；（言談舉止）神秘的，隱秘的；受信任的，委以機密的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Information that is <b>confidential</b> is meant to be kept secret or private. 保密的","examples":["She accused them of leaking confidential information about her private life. 她指責他們洩露了有關她的私生活的保密資訊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk to someone in a <b>confidential</b> way, you talk to them quietly because what you are saying is secret or private. 悄悄的","examples":["\"Look,\" he said in a confidential tone, \"I want you to know that me and Joey are cops.\" “喂，”他悄聲說，“我想要你知道我和喬伊都是警察。”"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"保密地","examples":["People can phone in, knowing that any information they give will be treated confidentially. 人們可以打電話進來，他們知道他們所提供的一切資訊都會被保密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"悄悄地","examples":["Nash hadn't raised his voice, still spoke rather softly, confidentially. 納什沒有提高嗓門，仍然很輕地、悄悄地說。"]}]}]},"controversial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有爭議的，引發爭論的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>controversial</b>, you mean that they are the subject of intense public argument, disagreement, or disapproval. 有爭議的","examples":["Immigration is a controversial issue in many countries. 移民在很多國家都是一個有爭議的問題。"]}]}]},"comprehensive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"綜合性的，全面的；有理解力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"綜合中學；專業綜合測驗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>comprehensive</b> includes everything that is needed or relevant. 全面的","examples":["The Rough Guide to Nepal is a comprehensive guide to the region. 《尼泊爾概覽》是介紹該地區的一本全面指南。"]}]}]},"cordial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱情友好的；感覺強烈的，由衷的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>甜果汁飲料；<美>烈性甜酒；鎮定藥，不太難吃的藥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cordial</b> means friendly. 友善的","examples":["He had never known him to be so chatty and cordial. 他以前從來不知道他是這樣一個健談而友善的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"友善地","examples":["They all greeted me very cordially and were eager to talk about the new project. 他們非常友善地和我打招呼，很想談談新專案。"]}]}]},"crooked":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"彎曲的，不直的；歪的；不誠實的，狡詐的；<澳新，非正式>生氣的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（手指或手臂）彎曲；詐騙，偷竊；彎曲，成鉤形（crook 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>crooked</b>, especially something that is usually straight, you mean that it is bent or twisted. 扭曲的","examples":["...the crooked line of his broken nose. …他折了的鼻樑的曲線。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>crooked</b> smile is uneven and bigger on one side than the other. 歪斜著嘴的","examples":["Polly gave her a crooked grin. 波莉給了她歪斜著嘴的一笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person or an activity as <b>crooked</b>, you mean that they are dishonest or criminal. 腐敗的; 惡棍般的","examples":["...a crooked cop. …一名壞警察。"]}]}]},"credible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可信的，可靠的；足夠好的，有明顯效果的；（因看似可能成功而）可接受的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Credible</b> means able to be trusted or believed. 可信的","examples":["Her claims seem credible to many. 她的說法似乎在許多人看來是可信的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>credible</b> candidate, policy, or system, for example, is one that appears to have a chance of being successful. 有可能成功","examples":["Mr. Robertson would be a credible candidate. 羅伯遜先生將是一名有希望成功的候選人。"]}]}]},"cosmetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"裝門面的，表面的；化妝用的，美容的；整容的；不重要的，沒意義的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"化妝品，美容品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cosmetics</b> are substances such as lipstick or powder, which people put on their face to make themselves look more attractive. 化妝品","examples":["...the cosmetics counter of a department store. …一個百貨商店的化妝品專櫃。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe measures or changes as <b>cosmetic</b>, you mean they improve the appearance of a situation or thing but do not change its basic nature, and you are usually implying that they are inadequate. 裝門面的","examples":["It is a cosmetic measure which will do nothing to help the situation long term. 這是裝點門面的措施，無益於局勢的長期發展。"]}]}]},"crucial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"至關重要的，決定性的；<非正式>極好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>crucial</b>, you mean it is extremely important. 至關重要的","examples":["He had administrators under him but made the crucial decisions himself. 儘管他手下有許多官員，但重要的決定還是他自己做。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"至關重要地","examples":["Chewing properly is crucially important. 正確地咀嚼是至關重要的。"]}]}]},"cumulative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"積累的，漸增的；累計的，累積的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a series of events have a <b>cumulative</b> effect, each event makes the effect greater. 累積的","examples":["It is simple pleasures, such as a walk on a sunny day, which have a cumulative effect on our mood. 諸如在晴朗的日子散步這樣簡樸的樂趣對我們的情緒有累積性益處。"]}]}]},"customary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"習俗的，習慣的；特有的，典型的；<法律>按習慣法的，依慣例的；與非洲黑人傳統（或法律）有關的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<史>習慣法彙編"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Customary</b> is used to describe things that people usually do in a particular society or in particular circumstances. 通常的","examples":["It is customary to offer a drink or a snack to guests. 通常用飲料或小吃招待客人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Customary</b> is used to describe something that a particular person usually does or has. 習慣上的","examples":["Yvonne took her customary seat behind her desk. 伊馮娜坐在了她的書桌後面慣坐的位子上。"]}]}]},"decisive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"果斷的，決斷的；決定性的，關鍵的；確定的，明確的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a fact, action, or event is <b>decisive</b>, it makes certain a particular result. 決定性的","examples":["...his decisive victory in the presidential elections. …他在這次總統選舉中的決定性勝利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>decisive</b>, they have or show an ability to make quick decisions in a difficult or complicated situation. 果斷的","examples":["He should give way to a younger, more decisive leader. 他應該讓位給一位更年輕、更果斷的領導者。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"決定性地","examples":["The plan was decisively rejected by Congress three weeks ago. 這個計劃三週前被國會關鍵性地否決了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"果斷地","examples":["\"I'll call for you at ten,\" she said decisively. “我10點來接你，”她果斷地說。"]}]}]},"crude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗略的，大概的；粗糙的，粗製的；冒犯的，粗俗的；天然的，自然的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"原油；天然的物質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crude</b> method or measurement is not exact or detailed, but may be useful or correct in a rough, general way. 粗略的","examples":["Standard measurements of blood pressure are an important but crude way of assessing the risk of heart disease or strokes. 標準的血壓測量是評估心臟病或中風風險的一種重要卻粗略的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe an object that someone has made as <b>crude</b>, you mean that it has been made in a very simple way or from very simple parts. 粗製的","examples":["...crude wooden boxes. …粗製的木盒子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>crude</b>, you disapprove of them because they speak or behave in a rude, offensive, or unsophisticated way. 粗魯的","examples":["Must you be quite so crude? 你一定要這樣粗魯嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Crude</b> substances are in a natural or unrefined state, and have not yet been used in manufacturing processes. 未加工的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗略地","examples":["The donors can be split – a little crudely – into two groups. 捐獻者們可以分成–大致地–兩個組。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"粗糙地","examples":["...a crudely carved wooden form. …一件粗糙的木頭雕刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"粗魯地","examples":["He hated it when she spoke so crudely. 他討厭她說話那麼粗魯。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crude</b> is the same as . 原油","examples":[]}]}]},"decent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"像樣的，尚好的；得體的，合宜的；<非正式>穿好衣服的；正派的，規矩的；待人寬厚的，和善的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Decent</b> is used to describe something which is considered to be of an acceptable standard or quality. 像樣的","examples":["He didn't get a decent explanation. 他沒有得到一個合理的解釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Decent</b> is used to describe something which is morally correct or acceptable. 合宜的","examples":["But, after a decent interval, trade relations began to return to normal. 但是在一段適當的間斷之後，貿易關係開始恢復正常。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Decent</b> people are honest and behave in a way that most people approve of. 正直的","examples":["The majority of people around here are decent people. 這兒的大多數人都是正派人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"像樣地","examples":["The allies say they will treat their prisoners decently. 同盟國家稱他們將有分寸地對待戰俘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"合宜地","examples":["And can't you dress more decently – people will think you're a tramp. 而且你不能穿得再體面些嗎？人們會以為你是個流浪漢。"]}]}]},"corporate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公司的；法人的；共同的，全體的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"公司，集團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Corporate</b> means relating to business corporations or to a particular business corporation. 公司的","examples":["...top U.S. corporate executives. …美國公司的高層管理人員。","...a corporate lawyer. …一名公司律師。"]}]}]},"destined":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"指定的，預定的；前往的，被送往的；（命中）註定的，肯定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>destined</b> <b>to</b> happen or if someone is <b>destined</b> <b>to</b> behave in a particular way, that thing seems certain to happen or be done. 註定的","examples":["Any economic strategy based on a weak dollar is destined to fail. 任何基於疲軟的美元之上的經濟策略都註定會失敗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>destined for</b> a particular place, or if goods are <b>destined for</b> a particular place, they are travelling toward that place or will be sent to that place. 去往某地的","examples":["...products destined for Saudi Arabia. …運往沙烏地阿拉伯的產品。"]}]}]},"disciplinary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有關紀律的，懲戒性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disciplinary</b> bodies or actions are concerned with making sure that people obey rules or regulations and that they are punished if they do not. 紀律性的","examples":["He will now face a disciplinary hearing for having an affair. 他將因一起風流韻事而面對一場紀律聽證會。"]}]}]},"diplomatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外交的，從事外交的；有手腕的，靈活變通的；（版本，副本）模擬的，和原件完全一致的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Diplomatic</b> means relating to diplomacy and diplomats. 外交的","examples":["...before the two countries resume full diplomatic relations. …在兩國全面恢復外交關係之前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>diplomatic</b> is careful to say or do things without offending people. 圓通得體的","examples":["She is very direct. I tend to be more diplomatic, I suppose. 她很直率。我覺得我更圓通些。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"外交地","examples":["...a growing sense of doubt that the conflict can be resolved diplomatically. …對該衝突能用外交手段得以解決的不斷增加的懷疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"圓通得體地","examples":["\"I really like their sound, although I'm not crazy about their lyrics,\" he says, diplomatically. “我非常喜歡他們的聲音，但不太喜歡他們的歌詞，”他很圓滑地說。"]}]}]},"dental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"牙齒的，牙科的；齒音的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"齒音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dental</b> is used to describe things that relate to teeth or to the care and treatment of teeth. 牙齒的; 牙科的","examples":["Good oral hygiene and regular dental care are important, whatever your age. 無論年齡大小，良好的口腔衛生和定期的牙齒保健都非常重要。"]}]}]},"disastrous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"災難性的，使損失慘重的；極失敗的，很糟的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disastrous</b> event has extremely bad consequences and effects. 災難性的","examples":["...the recent, disastrous earthquake. …那場最近發生的、災難性的地震。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>disastrous</b>, you mean that it was very unsuccessful. 非常失敗的","examples":["...after their disastrous performance in the election. …繼他們在競選中非常失敗的表現之後。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"災難性地","examples":["The vegetable harvest is disastrously behind schedule. 蔬菜收割災難性地滯後於計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"非常失敗地","examples":["...debts resulting from the company's disastrously timed venture into property development. …該公司不合時宜地冒險投資房地產開發而導致的債務。"]}]}]},"disgraceful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不名譽的，可恥的，丟臉的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something such as behaviour or a situation is <b>disgraceful</b>, you disapprove of it strongly, and feel that the person or people responsible should be ashamed of it. 可恥的; 丟臉的","examples":["It's disgraceful that they have detained him for so long. 真是可恥，他們扣押了他這麼久。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可恥地","examples":["He felt that his brother had behaved disgracefully. 他覺得他兄弟表現得丟人現眼。"]}]}]},"discreet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"謹慎的，周到的；小巧的，不引人注意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>discreet</b>, you are polite and careful in what you do or say, because you want to avoid embarrassing or offending someone. (言行) 謹慎的","examples":["They were gossipy and not always discreet. 他們愛說閒話，而且不總是言語謹慎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>discreet</b> <b>about</b> something you are doing, you do not tell other people about it, in order to avoid being embarrassed or to gain an advantage. 謹慎保密的","examples":["We were very discreet about the romance. 我們對這一段羅曼史守口如瓶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>discreet</b>, you approve of it because it is small in size or degree, or not easily noticed. 小巧的; 不顯眼的","examples":["She is wearing a noticeably stylish, feminine dress, plus discreet jewellery. 她穿著一條非常時髦、有女人味的連衣裙，配以小巧的首飾。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"謹慎地","examples":["I took the phone, and she went discreetly into the living room. 我拿了電話，她就謹慎地到客廳去了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"謹慎保密地","examples":["Everyone worked to make him welcome, and, more discreetly, to find out about him. 大家都盡力使他受歡迎，且更為小心地去了解他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"小巧地; 不顯眼地","examples":["...stately houses, discreetly hidden behind great avenues of sturdy trees. …那些豪宅，隱隱約約掩藏在茂密的林蔭大道後面。"]}]}]},"dispensable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不必要的，可有可無的；（法律或其他規則）在特定情況下可放寬的，可通融的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>dispensable</b> they are not really needed. 可有可無的","examples":["All those people in the middle are dispensable. 那些在中間的人都是可有可無的。"]}]}]},"diverse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不同的，各式各樣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of things is <b>diverse</b>, it is made up of a wide variety of things. 各種各樣的","examples":["The building houses a wide and diverse variety of antiques. 這棟樓裡擺放著大量各式各樣的古董。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Diverse</b> people or things are very different from each other. 不同的","examples":["Albert Jones' new style will inevitably put him in touch with a much more diverse and perhaps younger audience. 艾伯特·瓊斯的新風格無疑將使他接觸更多形形色色的、或許更年輕的觀眾。"]}]}]},"dreary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"沉悶的，令人沮喪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>dreary</b>, you mean that it is dull and depressing. 沉悶的; 枯燥無味的","examples":["...a dreary little town in the Midwest. …中西部一個沉悶的小鎮。"]}]}]},"drastic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極端的，激烈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have to take <b>drastic</b> action in order to solve a problem, you have to do something extreme to solve it. 極端的","examples":["Drastic measures are needed to clean up the profession. 需要採取極端的措施來整頓這個行業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>drastic</b> change is a very great change. 劇烈的","examples":["Foreign food aid has led to a drastic reduction in the numbers of people dying of starvation. 外國的食品援助使得因飢餓而死亡的人數大幅下降。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"劇烈地","examples":["As a result, services have been drastically reduced. 結果，服務被大大減少了。"]}]}]},"dual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雙的，雙重的；雙數的；（飛機）雙重控制的，複式操縱的；（定理、表示式等）對偶的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雙數詞；對偶定理（或表示式等）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>把（道路）改為複式車行道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dual</b> means having two parts, functions, or aspects. 雙重的","examples":["...his dual role as head of the party and head of state. …他作為政黨領袖和國家首腦的雙重角色。"]}]}]},"dubious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可疑的，靠不住的；有疑慮的；（榮譽、名聲等）不好的，不光彩的；質量不佳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>dubious</b>, you mean that you do not consider it to be completely honest, safe, or reliable. 可疑的; 不太可靠的","examples":["This claim seems to us to be rather dubious. 這項宣告在我們看來相當不可信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>dubious</b> <b>about</b> something, you are not completely sure about it and have not yet made up your mind about it. 有疑慮的","examples":["My parents were a bit dubious about it all at first but we soon convinced them. 起初我父母親對此尚心存疑慮，但很快我們便說服了他們。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可疑地; 不太可靠地","examples":["Carter was dubiously convicted of shooting three white men in a bar. 卡特很有嫌疑地被宣叛在一家酒吧射殺了3名白人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"遲疑地","examples":["He eyed Coyne dubiously. 他懷疑地注視著科因。"]}]}]},"edible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可食用的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"食物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>edible</b>, it is safe to eat and not poisonous. 可食用的","examples":["...edible fungi. …食用菌。"]}]}]},"eloquent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"雄辯的，口才流利的；傳神的，明確表示的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Speech or writing that is <b>eloquent</b> is well expressed and effective in persuading people. 雄辯的; 有說服力的","examples":["I heard him make a very eloquent speech at that dinner. 我聽他在那次晚餐上做了一次很有說服力的演說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A person who is <b>eloquent</b> is good at speaking and able to persuade people. 能言善辯的","examples":["He was eloquent about his love of books. 他善於談論他對書籍的熱愛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"雄辯力; 說服力","examples":["...the eloquence of his prose. …他散文的說服力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"能言善辯","examples":["She can speak with an eloquence that is almost inspirational. 她能用一種近乎激發靈感的口才發言。"]}]}]},"ethical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"道德的，倫理的；合乎道德的；有益於人（類）的，環保的；（藥品）憑處方出售的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ethical</b> means relating to beliefs about right and wrong. 道德上的","examples":["...the medical, nursing and ethical issues surrounding terminally-ill people. …關於患絕症病人們的醫學、護理和道德問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>ethical</b>, you mean that it is morally right or morally acceptable. 合乎道德的","examples":["The trade association promotes ethical business practices. 這個貿易協會提倡合乎道德標準的商業行為。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"道德上地","examples":["Attorneys are ethically and legally bound to absolute confidentiality. 律師在道德上和法律上都得絕對保守機密。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"合乎道德地","examples":["Mayors want local companies to behave ethically. 市長們希望當地公司按道德行事。"]}]}]},"eligible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"符合條件的，合格的；（婚姻）合適的，合意的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"合格者，適任者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>eligible</b> <b>to</b> do something is qualified or able to do it, for example, because they are old enough. 有資格的","examples":["Almost half the population are eligible to vote in today's election. 將近一半的居民有資格在今天的選舉中投票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>eligible</b> man or woman is not yet married and is thought by many people to be a suitable partner. (指結婚物件) 令人中意的","examples":["He's the most eligible bachelor in Japan. 他是日本最令人中意的單身漢。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"資格; 合格","examples":["The rules covering eligibility for benefits changed in the 1980s. 關於社會救濟金合格條件的規定在20世紀80年代發生了變化。"]}]}]},"emphatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"強調的，堅決的；明顯的；帶重音的，重讀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emphatic</b> response or statement is one made in a forceful way, because the speaker feels very strongly about what they are saying. 斷然的","examples":["His response was immediate and emphatic. 他的回答迅速且斷然。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>emphatic</b> <b>about</b> something, you use forceful language that shows you feel very strongly about what you are saying. 堅決強調的","examples":["The rebels are emphatic that this is not a surrender. 叛亂者堅稱這不是投降。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>emphatic</b> win or victory is one in which the winner has won by a large amount or distance. 大比分的","examples":["Yesterday's emphatic victory was their fifth in succession. 昨天的大比分勝利是他們第5次的接連勝利。"]}]}]},"excessive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過度的，過多的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe the amount or level of something as <b>excessive</b>, you disapprove of it because it is more or higher than is necessary or reasonable. 過多的; 過度的","examples":["Their spending on research is excessive and is slowing developments of new treatments. 他們在研究上的花銷過多，正在減慢新療法的開發。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"過多地; 過度地","examples":["Managers are also accused of paying themselves excessively high salaries. 經理們還被指責給自己發過高的工資。"]}]}]},"fabulous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極好的，絕妙的；非凡的，巨大的，驚人的；虛構的，傳說的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>fabulous</b>, you are emphasizing that you like it a lot or think that it is very good. 極好的","examples":["This is a fabulous album. It's fresh, varied, fun. 這是個極好的專輯。它是新穎的、多樣的、有趣的。"]}]}]},"fireproof":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"防火的，耐火的"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使耐火，使防火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>fireproof</b> cannot be damaged by fire. 防火的","examples":["...fireproof clothing. ...防火服。"]}]}]},"explicit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"清楚明白的，明確的，詳述的；直截了當的，坦率的；赤裸裸表現性愛（或暴力）的，露骨的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（手稿、早期印刷品或禮拜儀式上唱詩的）結束語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>explicit</b> is expressed or shown clearly and openly, without any attempt to hide anything. 明確表達的; 公開顯露的","examples":["Sexually explicit scenes in movies and books were taboo under the old regime. 電影和書籍中露骨的性愛場景在舊體制下是禁忌的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>explicit</b> <b>about</b> something, you speak about it very openly and clearly. 直言不諱的","examples":["He was explicit about his intention to overhaul the party's internal voting system. 他對自己徹底革新該黨內投票體制的意圖直言不諱。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"明確表達地; 公開顯露地","examples":["The play was the first commercially successful work dealing explicitly with homosexuality. 該劇是首部在商業上獲得成功的公然描寫同性戀的作品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"直言不諱地","examples":["She has been talking very explicitly about AIDS to these groups. 她一直在毫不避諱地與這些群體談論艾滋病。"]}]}]},"exclusive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獨有的，專用的；高檔的，昂貴的；不含……的；排外的；排斥的；全部的；唯一關心的；（新聞或報道）獨家的；（條款）除外責任的；高階的，昂貴的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨家新聞，獨家報道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>exclusive</b>, you mean that it is limited to people who have a lot of money or who are privileged, and is therefore not available to everyone. 僅限富貴人士的","examples":["It used to be a private, exclusive club, and now it's open to all New Yorkers. 它曾是一家高檔的私人俱樂部，而現在它對所有紐約人開放。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>exclusive</b> is used or owned by only one person or group, and not shared with anyone else. 專用的; 獨有的","examples":["Our group will have exclusive use of a 60-foot boat. 我們組將有一條專用的60英尺的船。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a newspaper, magazine, or broadcasting organization describes one of its reports as <b>exclusive</b>, they mean it is a special report that does not appear in any other publication or on any other channel. 獨家的 (新聞報道)","examples":["He told the magazine in an exclusive interview: \"All my problems stem from drinking.\" 他在一次獨家採訪中告知那家雜誌：“我所有的問題源於飲酒。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a company states that its prices, goods, or services are <b>exclusive</b> <b>of</b> something, that thing is not included in the stated price, although it usually still has to be paid for. 不包括…的","examples":["...the average cost of a three-course dinner exclusive of tax, tip and beverage. …不含稅、小費和酒水費用的3道菜晚餐的平均花費。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>exclusive</b> is an exclusive article or report. 獨家文章; 獨家報道","examples":["Some papers thought they had an exclusive. 一些報社以為他們有一條獨家報道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two things are <b>mutually exclusive</b>, they are separate and very different from each other, so that it is impossible for them to exist or happen together. 互相排斥的; 不相容的","examples":["They both have learned that ambition and successful fatherhood can be mutually exclusive. 他們都明白了事業心與做個成功的父親是互相排斥的。"]}]}]},"extracurricular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"課外的；工作之外的，婚姻之外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Extracurricular</b> activities are activities for students that are not part of their course. 課外的","examples":["Each child had participated in extracurricular activities at school. 每個孩子都參加了學校的課外活動。","...extracurricular sports. ...課外體育活動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Extracurricular</b> activities are activities that someone does outside of their normal work. 工餘的","examples":["The money he made from these extracurricular activities enabled him to pursue other ventures. 他在工作之外賺取的外塊使他可以嘗試新事物。"]}]}]},"feasible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可行的，辦得到的；很可能會發生的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>feasible</b>, it can be done, made, or achieved. 可行的","examples":["She questioned whether it was feasible to stimulate investment in these regions. 她質問在這些地區刺激投資是否可行。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可行性","examples":["The committee will study the feasibility of setting up a national computer network. 委員會將研究建立一個國家計算機網路的可行性。"]}]}]},"exquisite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精緻的，精美的；劇烈的；細緻的，有鑑賞力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"花花公子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>exquisite</b> is extremely beautiful or pleasant, especially in a delicate way. 精美的","examples":["The Indians brought in exquisite beadwork to sell. 印地安人帶了精美的珠飾來銷售。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"精美地","examples":["...exquisitely crafted dollshouses. …製作精美的玩具小屋。"]}]}]},"formidable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可怕的，令人敬畏的；（形狀、數量）巨大的；難對付的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>formidable</b>, you mean that you feel slightly frightened by them because they are very great or impressive. 可怕的; 令人敬畏的","examples":["We have a formidable task ahead of us. 我們面前有一項艱鉅的任務。"]}]}]},"finite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有限的，有限制的；限定的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有限之物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>finite</b> has a definite fixed size or extent. 有限的","examples":["...a finite set of elements. …有限的一組元素。","Only a finite number of situations can arise. 只有有限的幾種情況可能會出現。"]}]}]},"forthcoming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"即將發生的；樂於提供資訊的，願意提供幫助的；現成的，可得到的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"來臨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>forthcoming</b> event is planned to happen soon. 即將到來的","examples":["...his opponents in the forthcoming elections. …他在即將到來的選舉中的對手們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something that you want, need, or expect is <b>forthcoming</b>, it is given to you or it happens. 實現的","examples":["They promised that the money would be forthcoming. 他們承諾說錢會到位的。","One source predicts no major shift in policy will be forthcoming at the committee hearings. 有一訊息預言在委員會聽證會上不會有政策上的重大變動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>forthcoming</b>, you mean that they willingly give information when you ask them. 願意提供資訊的","examples":["William, sadly, was not very forthcoming about any other names he might have, where he lived or what his phone number was. 很遺憾，威廉在有關他可能有的其它名字、他的住處或者電話號碼等方面不太願意提供資訊。"]}]}]},"honorary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"榮譽的；（職位）無報酬的，義務的；（成員）名譽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>honorary</b> title or membership of a group is given to someone without their needing to have the necessary qualifications, usually because of their public achievements. (稱號或成員資格) 作為榮譽的","examples":["Harvard awarded him an honorary degree. 哈佛大學授予他榮譽學位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Honorary</b> is used to describe an official job that is done without payment. 名譽的但無報酬的 (職位)","examples":["...the honorary secretary of the Beekeepers' Association. …養蜂人協會的名譽秘書。"]}]}]},"frail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）脆弱的，虛弱的；易碎的，易壞的；（性格、道德方面）脆弱的，意志薄弱的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（裝無花果或葡萄乾的）燈心草籃；<美，非正式，舊>女人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>frail</b> is not very strong or healthy. 虛弱的","examples":["She lay in bed looking frail. 她躺在床上，看上去很虛弱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>frail</b> is easily broken or damaged. 易碎的; 易壞的","examples":["The frail boat rocked as he clambered in. 他爬進去的時候，那條破船搖晃起來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a rush basket for figs or raisins (裝無花果或葡萄乾的)燈心草籃","examples":[]}]}]},"genetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"基因的，遺傳學的；有共同起源的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>genetic</b> to describe something that is concerned with genetics or with genes. 遺傳的","examples":["Cystic fibrosis is the most common fatal genetic disease in the United States. 囊腫性纖維化在美國是最常見的致命性遺傳疾病。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遺傳地","examples":["Some people are genetically predisposed to diabetes. 有些人因遺傳因素而易患糖尿病。"]}]}]},"hospitable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好客的，熱情友好的；環境適宜的；樂於接受的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hospitable</b> person is friendly, generous, and welcoming to guests or people they have just met. 好客的; 殷勤周到的","examples":["The locals are hospitable and welcoming. 當地人熱情好客。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hospitable</b> climate or environment is one that encourages the existence or development of particular people or things. (氣候、環境等) 適宜的","examples":["Even in summer this place did not look exactly hospitable: in winter, conditions must have been exceedingly harsh. 即使在夏天，這個地方看上去也並不太宜人：在冬天，條件一定非常惡劣。"]}]}]},"imposing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"壯觀的，儀表堂堂的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強制推行，強制實行；把（自己的觀點、信仰等）強加於；打擾，麻煩（impose 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>imposing</b>, you mean that they have an impressive appearance or manner. 儀態使人印象深刻的","examples":["He was an imposing man. 他是個儀表堂堂的男子漢。"]}]}]},"fragile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易碎的，易損的；不牢固的，易被摧毀的；纖巧美麗的；虛弱的，體弱的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>fragile</b>, you mean that it is weak or uncertain, and unlikely to be able to resist strong pressure or attack. 脆弱的","examples":["The fragile economies of several southern African nations could be irreparably damaged. 幾個南部非洲國家脆弱的經濟可能會無可挽救地被摧垮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>fragile</b> is easily broken or damaged. 易碎的","examples":["He leaned back in his fragile chair. 他向後靠在他那把不結實的椅子上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"脆弱","examples":["By mid-1988 there were clear indications of the extreme fragility of the Right-wing coalition. 到1988年年中有明顯的跡象表明右翼聯盟極度脆弱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"易碎性","examples":["Older drivers are more likely to be seriously injured because of the fragility of their bones. 年紀較大的司機因骨骼易碎而更可能會受重傷。"]}]}]},"hysterical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"歇斯底里的，異常興奮的；<非正式>極為有趣的，極滑稽的；患癔病的；（笑聲）瘋狂失控的，不可抑制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>hysterical</b> is in a state of uncontrolled excitement, anger, or panic. 歇斯底里的","examples":["Police and bodyguards had to form a human shield around him as the almost hysterical crowds struggled to approach him. 當近乎歇斯底里的人群奮力接近他時，警察和保鏢們不得不在他周圍形成一堵人牆。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hysterical</b> laughter is loud and uncontrolled. (笑) 瘋狂失控的","examples":["The young woman burst into hysterical laughter. 那個少婦突然狂笑起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>hysterical</b>, you think that they are very funny and they make you laugh a lot. 非常滑稽的","examples":["Paul Mazursky was Master of Ceremonies, and he was pretty hysterical. 保羅·馬祖爾斯基擔任司儀，他相當詼諧風趣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"歇斯底里地","examples":["I don't think we can go around screaming hysterically: \"Ban these dogs. Muzzle all dogs.\" 我認為我們不能歇斯底里地四處高喊：“禁止養這些狗。給所有的狗戴上口套。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"瘋狂失控地","examples":["She says she hasn't laughed as hysterically since she was 13. 她說自己從13歲起就沒有像這樣狂笑過。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"滑稽地","examples":["It wasn't supposed to be a comedy but I found it hysterically funny. 它本不是個喜劇，可我覺得它非常滑稽。"]}]}]},"gloomy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"陰暗的，幽暗的；沮喪的，悲傷的；前景黯淡的，悲觀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place is <b>gloomy</b>, it is almost dark so that you cannot see very well. 昏暗的","examples":["Inside it's gloomy after all that sunshine. 明媚的陽光過後，裡面一片昏暗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people are <b>gloomy</b>, they are unhappy and have no hope. 憂傷的","examples":["Miller is gloomy about the fate of the serious playwright in America. 米勒對這位嚴肅的美國劇作家的命運感到憂傷。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a situation is <b>gloomy</b>, it does not give you much hope of success or happiness. 前景暗淡的","examples":["...a gloomy picture of an economy sliding into recession. …經濟陷入衰退的一幅暗淡景象。","Officials say the outlook for next year is gloomy. 官員們稱來年前景暗淡。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"憂傷地","examples":["He tells me gloomily that he has been called up for army service. 他沮喪地告訴我他已經被徵召入伍了。"]}]}]},"implicit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"含蓄的，未言明的；內含的，固有的；無疑問的，無保留的；（函式）隱式的，隱的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>implicit</b> is expressed in an indirect way. 含蓄的","examples":["...an implicit warning to the Moroccans not to continue or repeat the military actions they began a week ago. …叫摩洛哥人不要繼續或重複一週前開始的軍事行動的含蓄警告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a quality or element is <b>implicit in</b> something, it is involved in it or is shown by it. 內含的","examples":["Trust is implicit in the system. 信任是這種體制裡內含的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has an <b>implicit</b> belief or faith in something, you mean that they have complete faith in it and no doubts at all. 絕對的 (信任)","examples":["He had implicit faith in the noble intentions of the Emperor. 他對皇帝的崇高旨意篤信不疑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"含蓄地","examples":["The jury implicitly criticized the government by their verdict. 陪審團透過他們的裁決含蓄地批評了政府。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"絕對地","examples":["I trust him implicitly. 我絕對信任他。"]}]}]},"incidental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"附帶的，次要的；伴隨而來的，免不了的；偶然發生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"雜費，附帶事件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>incidental</b> to another, it is less important than the other thing or is not a major part of it. 附帶的; 次要的","examples":["The playing of music proved to be incidental to the main business of the evening. 音樂演奏結果只是當晚主要活動的陪襯。"]}]}]},"infectious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傳染的，傳染性的；有感染力的，有影響力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A disease that is <b>infectious</b> can be caught by being near a person who has it. Compare . 傳染的","examples":["...infectious diseases such as measles. …像麻疹這樣的傳染病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a feeling is <b>infectious</b>, it spreads to other people. 有感染力的","examples":["She radiates an infectious enthusiasm for everything she does. 她做的每件事都散發出一種有感染力的熱情。"]}]}]},"inclusive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"包容廣闊的；包括一切費用在內的；包括的，包含的；無性別歧視的；對外開放的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a group or organization as <b>inclusive</b>, you mean that it allows all kinds of people to belong to it, rather than just one kind of person. 兼收幷蓄的","examples":["The academy is far more inclusive now than it used to be. 該學院如今比過去更為兼收幷蓄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"After stating the first and last item in a set of things, you can add <b>inclusive</b> to make it clear that the items stated are included in the set. 首末項包括在內的","examples":["You are also invited to join us on our prayer days (this year, June 6 to June 14 inclusive). 你也受邀加入我們的禱告日（今年從6月6日（含）至6月14日（含））。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a price is <b>inclusive</b>, it includes all the charges connected with the goods or services offered. If a price is <b>inclusive</b> <b>of</b> shipping and handling, it includes the charge for this. 包括一切費用在內的","examples":["...all prices are inclusive of delivery. …所有價格包括運費。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Inclusive</b> is also an adverb. 包括一切費用在內地","examples":["The outpatient programme costs $105 per day, all inclusive. 門診病人方案收費每人每天105美元，一切費用包括在內。"]}]}]},"intact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完好無損的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>intact</b> is complete and has not been damaged or changed. 完整無缺的","examples":["Customs men put dynamite in the water to destroy the cargo, but most of it was left intact. 海關人員把炸藥放入水中以摧毀貨物，但大部分貨物卻完好無損。"]}]}]},"ingenious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"靈巧的，有獨創性的；精巧的，巧妙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>ingenious</b> is very clever and involves new ideas, methods, or equipment. 靈巧的; 新穎的","examples":["...a truly ingenious invention. …一項的確新穎的發明。"]}]}]},"innovative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"革新的，新穎的；富有革新精神的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>innovative</b> is new and original. 創新的; 革新的","examples":["...products which are cheaper, more innovative and more reliable than those of their competitors. …比其競爭對手更便宜、更新穎、更可靠的產品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>innovative</b> person introduces changes and new ideas. 富有創新精神的; 採用新觀念的","examples":["He was one of the most creative and innovative engineers of his generation. 他是同代人中最富有創造力和革新精神的工程師之一。"]}]}]},"immune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"免疫的；不受影響的；免除的，豁免的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"免疫者，免除者"}],"sections":[]},"inherent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"內在的，固有的；<法律>（權利，特權）固定屬於（某人）的；（形容詞）作定語和表語時意義相同的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>inherent</b> qualities of something are the necessary and natural parts of it. 內在的","examples":["Stress is an inherent part of dieting. 要節食必定會經受壓力。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"內在地","examples":["Man is not inherently violent. 人類並非生來就暴力。"]}]}]},"invaluable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極有用的，極寶貴的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>invaluable</b>, you mean that it is extremely useful. 非常寶貴的","examples":["I was able to gain invaluable experience over that year. 在那一年裡我獲得了十分寶貴的經驗。"]}]}]},"joyous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高興的，令人愉快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Joyous</b> means extremely happy. 非常快樂的","examples":["She had made their childhood so joyous and carefree. 她使他們的童年生活非常快樂、無憂無慮。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非常快樂地","examples":["Sarah accepted joyously. 薩拉非常快樂地接受了。"]}]}]},"legislative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"立法的；（與）立法機關（有關）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Legislative</b> means involving or relating to the process of making and passing laws. 立法的","examples":["Today's hearing was just the first step in the legislative process. 今天的聽證會僅僅是立法程式的第一步。"]}]}]},"lengthy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"漫長的，長時間的；（講話、文章等）冗長的，過於詳盡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>lengthy</b> to describe an event or process which lasts for a long time. 漫長的","examples":["The board members held a lengthy meeting to decide future policy. 董事會成員開了一次漫長的會議來決定未來的政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lengthy</b> report, article, book, or document contains a lot of speech, writing, or other material. 冗長的","examples":["Friedman's lengthy report quoted an unnamed source. 弗裡德曼冗長的報告引用了一個未指明出處的資料。"]}]}]},"irritable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易怒的，急躁的；（身體部位或器官）過敏的；（生物機體）應激性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>irritable</b>, you are easily annoyed. 易怒的","examples":["He had been waiting for over an hour and was beginning to feel irritable. 他已經等了一個多小時，開始覺得有些煩躁了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"易怒地","examples":["\"Why are you whispering?\" he asked irritably. “你們為什麼竊竊私語？”他生氣地問。"]}]}]},"legendary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非常有名的，大名鼎鼎的；傳說（中）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>legendary</b>, you mean that they are very famous and that many stories are told about them. 大名鼎鼎的","examples":["...the legendary Jazz singer Adelaide Hall. …大名鼎鼎的爵士樂歌手阿德萊德·霍爾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>legendary</b> person, place, or event is mentioned or described in an old legend. 傳說中的","examples":["The hill is supposed to be the resting place of the legendary King Lud. 這座山據說是傳說中的路德國王休息的地方。"]}]}]},"liable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（在法律上）有責任的，有義務的；負有償付責任的；很可能會發生的；有……傾向的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>is liable to</b> happen, it is very likely to happen. 很有可能的","examples":["Only a small minority of the mentally ill are liable to harm themselves or others. 只有極少數的精神病人很有可能傷害到自己或他人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things are <b>liable to</b> something unpleasant, they are likely to experience it or do it. 易於…的","examples":["She will grow into a woman particularly liable to depression. 她將變成一個特別易於消沉的女人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>liable</b> <b>for</b> something such as a debt, you are legally responsible for it. 負法律責任的","examples":["The airline's insurer is liable for damages to the victims' families. 航空公司投保的保險公司為遇難者家庭的損失負法律責任。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"責","examples":["The company does not accept liability for fragile, valuable or perishable articles. 公司對於易碎、貴重或易腐爛的物品不負責任。"]}]}]},"lush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"茂盛的，鬱鬱蔥蔥的；豪華的，奢侈的；性感的，迷人的；（色彩，音樂）非常華麗的，賞心悅目的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>酒鬼；酒"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"喝（酒等液體）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lush</b> fields or gardens have a lot of very healthy grass or plants. 茂盛的","examples":["...the lush green meadows bordering the river. …河邊青蔥翠綠的草地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a place or thing as <b>lush</b>, you mean that it is very luxurious. 豪華的","examples":["The Carlton-intercontinental hotel is lush, plush, and very non- backpacker. 卡爾頓洲際酒店豪華舒適，揹包徒步旅行者是絕對住不起的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>lush</b>, you mean that they drink too much alcohol. 酒鬼","examples":[]}]}]},"literal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"字面上的；逐字的；缺乏想象力的，刻板的；確切的，不誇張的；（影象）寫實的；（用）字母（表示）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>誤印"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>literal</b> sense of a word or phrase is its most basic sense. 字面上的","examples":["In many cases, the people there are fighting, in a literal sense, for their homes. 多數情況下，那裡的人們實際上都是在為他們的家園而戰鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>literal</b> translation is one in which you translate each word of the original work rather than giving the meaning of each expression or sentence using words that sound natural. 按字面意思的","examples":["A literal translation of the name Tapies is \"walls.\" 名字的字面翻譯是“牆”。"]}]}]},"ironic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反語的，諷刺的；（因出乎意料而）奇怪的，好笑的"}],"sections":[]},"monotonous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"單調乏味的，毫無變化的；無抑揚頓挫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>monotonous</b> is very boring because it has a regular, repeated pattern which never changes. 單調的","examples":["It's monotonous work, like most factory jobs. 這是個單調的工作，和大多數工廠工作一樣。"]}]}]},"mournful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲哀的，悲傷的，憂傷的；（聲音）悲切的，哀怨的；令人悲傷的，令人惋惜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>mournful</b>, you are very sad. 悲傷的","examples":["He looked mournful, even near to tears. 他看上去很悲傷，幾乎要掉淚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mournful</b> sound seems very sad. (聲音) 悲切的","examples":["...the mournful wail of bagpipes. …風笛的悲鳴聲。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悲傷地","examples":["He stood mournfully at the gate waving bye bye. 他悲傷地站在門口，揮手說再見。"]}]}]},"medieval":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中世紀的；<非正式>非常老派的，極其過時的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>medieval</b> relates to or was made in the period of European history between the end of the Roman Empire in AD 476 and about AD 1500. 中世紀的","examples":["...a medieval castle. …一座中世紀的城堡。"]}]}]},"miraculous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇蹟般的，不可思議的；超自然的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a good event as <b>miraculous</b>, you mean that it is very surprising and unexpected. 奇蹟般的","examples":["The horse made a miraculous recovery to finish a close third. 這匹馬奇蹟般地緩過勁來，最終以微弱的差距獲得了第三名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone describes a wonderful event as <b>miraculous</b>, they believe that the event was caused by God. 超自然的","examples":["...miraculous healing. …奇蹟般的治癒。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"神奇地","examples":["Miraculously, the guards escaped death or serious injury. 警衛們奇蹟般地逃脫了傷亡。"]}]}]},"mischievous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淘氣的，惡作劇的；（行為，事情）有害的，惡意中傷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mischievous</b> person likes to have fun by playing harmless tricks on people or doing things they are not supposed to do. 調皮的","examples":["She rocks back and forth on her chair like a mischievous child. 她在椅子上前後晃動，像個調皮的孩子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mischievous</b> act or suggestion is intended to cause trouble. 惡意的","examples":["\"I have a few mischievous plans,\" says Zevon. “我有幾個鬼點子。”澤馮說。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"調皮地","examples":["Kathryn winked mischievously. 凱瑟琳調皮地眨了眨眼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"惡意地","examples":["That does not require \"massive\" military intervention, as some have mischievously claimed. 那不需要“大規模”的軍事幹涉，一些人惡意地如此宣稱。"]}]}]},"municipal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"城市的，市政的；自治城市的，地方自治的；內政的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Municipal</b> means associated with or belonging to a city or town that has its own local government. 市政的","examples":["The municipal authorities gave the go-ahead for the march. 市政當局批准了此次遊行。","...next month's municipal elections. …下個月的市政選舉。"]}]}]},"naval":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"海軍的，軍艦的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Naval</b> means belonging to, relating to, or involving a country's navy. 海軍的","examples":["He was the senior serving naval officer. 他曾是高階現役海軍軍官。"]}]}]},"notorious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聲名狼藉的，臭名昭著的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>notorious</b> means to be well known for something bad. 聲名狼藉的","examples":["...an area notorious for drugs, crime and violence. …一個因毒品、犯罪和暴力而聲名狼藉的地區。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聲名狼藉地","examples":["The train company is overstaffed and notoriously inefficient. 這家鐵路公司人員超編，且出了名地沒有效率。","He worked mainly in New York City where living space is notoriously at a premium. 他主要在紐約市工作，那裡的生存空間出了名地昂貴。"]}]}]},"optional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可選擇的，選修的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>optional</b>, you can choose whether or not you do it or have it. 可選擇的","examples":["Sex education is a sensitive area for some parents, and thus it should remain optional. 性教育對一些家長來說是個敏感的話題，因此應該還是非強制性的。"]}]}]},"patriotic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛國的，有愛國心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>patriotic</b> loves their country and feels very loyal toward it. 愛國的","examples":["Winona is fiercely patriotic. 威諾娜極度愛國。"]}]}]},"outrageous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"駭人的，無法容忍的；反常的，令人驚訝的；極其誇張的，不可能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>outrageous</b>, you are emphasizing that it is unacceptable or very shocking. 不可接受的; 令人震驚的","examples":["By diplomatic standards, this was outrageous behaviour. 按外交標準，這是不可接受的行為。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不可接受地; 令人震驚地","examples":["...outrageously expensive skin care items. …貴得不可接受的護膚品。"]}]}]},"pathetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人憐憫的，可憐的；無用的，差勁的；感傷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or animal as <b>pathetic</b>, you mean that they are sad and weak or helpless, and they make you feel very sorry for them. 可憐的","examples":["...a pathetic little dog with a curly tail. …一隻可憐的卷尾小狗。","The small group of onlookers presented a pathetic sight. 那一小群旁觀者顯出一幅可憐的樣子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>pathetic</b>, you mean that they make you feel impatient or angry, often because they are weak or not very good. 差勁的; 無力的","examples":["What pathetic excuses. 多麼無力的藉口！","Don't be so pathetic. 別那麼差勁。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可憐地","examples":["She was pathetically thin. 她那時瘦弱得可憐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"差勁地; 無力地","examples":["Five women in a group of 18 people is a pathetically small number. 18個人中5位女性是個小得可憐的數目。"]}]}]},"nutritious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有營養的，營養豐富的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nutritious</b> food contains substances which help your body to be healthy. 有營養的","examples":["It is always important to choose enjoyable, nutritious foods. 選擇好吃的、有營養的食品總是很重要的。"]}]}]},"inevitable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"必然發生的，不可避免的；總會發生的，慣常的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"必然發生的事，不可避免的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>inevitable</b>, it is certain to happen and cannot be prevented or avoided. 必然發生的","examples":["If the case succeeds, it is inevitable that other trials will follow. 如果這場官司獲勝，其他審判必將效法。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The inevitable</b> is something that is inevitable. 必然發生的事","examples":["\"It's just delaying the inevitable,\" he said. “那只是拖延該發生的事罷了，”他說。"]}]}]},"photographic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"攝影的，照片的；（記憶）精確的，能詳細記錄的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Photographic</b> means connected with photographs or photography. 攝影的; 照片的","examples":["...photographic equipment. …攝影器材。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>photographic</b> <b>memory</b>, you are able to remember things in great detail after you have seen them. 攝影般精確的記憶力","examples":["He had a photographic memory for maps. 他對地圖具有攝影般精確的記憶力。"]}]}]},"petty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不重要的，瑣碎的，小的；小氣的，小心眼的；次要的，職位低的；（罪行）輕微的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>petty</b> to describe things such as problems, rules, or arguments that you think are unimportant or relate to unimportant things. 不重要的","examples":["He was miserable all the time and fights would start over petty things. 他一直都很悶悶不樂，常為一些雞毛蒜皮的事吵架。","...endless rules and petty regulations. …沒完沒了的規則和無足輕重的規定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour as <b>petty</b>, you mean that they care too much about small, unimportant things and perhaps that they are unnecessarily unkind. 過分在乎瑣事的","examples":["He was petty-minded and obsessed with detail. 他謹小慎微，過於在意細節。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Petty</b> is used of people or actions that are less important, serious, or great than others. (人或行動) 次要的","examples":["...petty crime, such as purse-snatching and minor break-ins. …諸如搶錢包、不嚴重的入室盜竊之類的輕罪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"狹隘","examples":["Never had she met such spite and pettiness. 她以前從來沒有碰到過這樣的惡意和狹隘。"]}]}]},"persistent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"執意的，堅持不懈的；持續的，反覆出現的；（化學品，放射性）作用持久的，揮發慢的；（動植物某部位，如角、葉等）宿存的，不落的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>persistent</b> continues to exist or happen for a long time; used especially about bad or undesirable states or situations. (壞的或令人不悅的狀態或情形) 持續存在的","examples":["Her position as national leader has been weakened by persistent fears of another coup attempt. 她國家領導人的地位因為人們一直擔心再次的政變企圖而被削弱了。","His cough grew more persistent until it never stopped. 他的咳嗽愈來愈頻繁，直到咳個不停。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>persistent</b> continues trying to do something, even though it is difficult or other people are against it. 堅持不懈的; 執著的","examples":["...a persistent critic of the president. …一個執著的批評總統的人。"]}]}]},"pious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"虔誠的，敬神的；（常含貶義）偽善的，道貌岸然的；（多用於 pious hope/wish）一廂情願的，難以兌現的；（舊用或書面）盡責的，孝順的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>pious</b> is very religious and moral. 虔誠的","examples":["He was brought up by pious female relatives. 他是由虔誠的女性親屬撫養大的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"虔誠地","examples":["Conti kneeled and crossed himself piously. 康蒂跪下，虔誠地在身上劃十字。"]}]}]},"presidential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"與總統有關的；總統似的，像總統的（尤指貌似自信大方、經驗老到的）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Presidential</b> activities or things relate or belong to a president. 最高權力人的","examples":["...campaigning for Peru's presidential election. …秘魯總統選舉競選活動。"]}]}]},"picturesque":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（地方）古雅的，風景如畫的；（語言）生動的，獨特的；（服飾和外貌）引人注意的，奇特的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>picturesque</b> place is attractive and interesting, and has no ugly modern buildings. 古雅的","examples":["...a picturesque mountain village. …一個古雅的山村。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to picturesque things as <b>the picturesque</b>. 古雅的事物","examples":["...lovers of the picturesque. …古雅物品的愛好者。"]}]}]},"premature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過早的，提早的；早產的；草率的，倉促的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>premature</b> happens earlier than usual or earlier than people expect. 提早的","examples":["Accidents are still the number one cause of premature death for Americans. 事故仍然是美國人非自然死亡的首要原因。","His career was brought to a premature end by a succession of knee injuries. 他的職業生涯因連續的膝傷過早地結束了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that something is <b>premature</b> when it happens too early and is therefore inappropriate. 過早的","examples":["It now seems their optimism was premature. 目前，他們的樂觀好像還為時過早。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>premature</b> baby is one that was born before the date when it was expected to be born. 早產的","examples":["Even very young premature babies respond to their mother's presence. 即使很小的早產兒也會對母親的在場有所反應。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"提早地","examples":["The war and the years in the harsh mountains had prematurely aged him. 戰爭和深山老林的歲月使他提早衰老了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"過早地","examples":["He was careful not to celebrate prematurely. 他很謹慎，沒有過早地舉行慶祝活動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"早產地","examples":["Danny was born prematurely, weighing only 3lb 3oz. 丹尼是早產的，體重只有3磅3盎司。"]}]}]},"prone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有做……傾向的，易於……的；俯臥的，趴著的；（前臂姿勢）手心向下的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指面部向下）使俯臥，趴著"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Prone）（意、阿根、法、美、巴西）普羅內（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To be <b>prone to</b> something, usually something bad, means to have a tendency to be affected by it or to do it. 易於 (受某事物影響或做某事) 的","examples":["For all her experience as a television reporter, she was still prone to camera nerves. 儘管有豐富的做電視記者的經驗，她仍然傾向於在鏡頭前緊張。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>-prone</b> combines with nouns to make adjectives that describe people who are frequently affected by something bad. 易受…影響的 (與名詞結合構成形容詞)","examples":["...the most injury-prone rider on the circuit. …賽車道上最容易受傷的車手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are lying <b>prone</b>, you are lying on your front. 面朝下的","examples":["Bob slid from his chair and lay prone on the floor. 鮑勃從椅子上滑下來，面朝下躺在了地板上。"]}]}]},"prospective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有希望的，潛在的； 可能發生的，預期的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>prospective</b> to describe someone who wants to be the thing mentioned or who is likely to be the thing mentioned. 預期的","examples":["The story should act as a warning to other prospective buyers. 這篇報道應該可以對其他可能的購買者起到警告作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>prospective</b> to describe something that is likely to happen soon. 可能很快發生的","examples":["The terms of the prospective deal are most clearly spelled out in Business Week. 這筆即將達成的交易條款在《商業週刊》上清楚地闡述了。"]}]}]},"quarrelsome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"愛爭吵的，好口角的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarrelsome</b> person often gets involved in arguments. 好爭吵的","examples":["Benedict had been a wild boy and a quarrelsome young man. 本尼迪克特曾是個狂野的男孩，一個好爭吵的年輕男子。"]}]}]},"punctual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"準時的，守時的；<舊>精確的；（語法）（動作）瞬息性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>punctual</b>, you do something or arrive somewhere at the right time and are not late. 準時的","examples":["He's always very punctual. I'll see if he's here yet. 他一向很準時。我要看看他是不是已經來了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"準時地","examples":["My guest arrived punctually. 我的客人準時到了。"]}]}]},"profound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（影響）深刻的，極大的；（感情）強烈的，深切的；（思想）深邃的，（見解）深刻的；<文>深的，深處的；完全的；艱深的，玄奧的；（疾病，殘疾）嚴重的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>profound</b> to emphasize that something is very great or intense. 深刻的; 極大的","examples":["...discoveries which had a profound effect on many areas of medicine. …對醫學的許多領域都有深刻影響的一些發現。","...profound disagreement. …極大的分歧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>profound</b> idea, work, or person shows great intellectual depth and understanding. 高深的","examples":["This is a book full of profound, original, and challenging insights. 這是一本充滿高深、新穎且富有挑戰性見解的書。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"深刻地; 極大地","examples":["This has profoundly affected my life. 這已極大地影響了我的生活。"]}]}]},"recreational":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"娛樂的，消遣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Recreational</b> means relating to things people do in their spare time to relax. 娛樂的","examples":["...parks and other recreational facilities. …公園及其它娛樂設施。"]}]}]},"redundant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<英> 被解僱的，被裁員的；多餘的，累贅的；（為預防機器或系統中主要元件故障而設的）復置裝置的，備用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>redundant</b> is unnecessary, for example, because it is no longer needed or because its job is being done by something else. 多餘的","examples":["Changes in technology may mean that once-valued skills are now redundant. 技術的變化可能意味著從前受重視的技巧現在變得多餘了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are made <b>redundant</b>, your employer tells you to leave because your job is no longer necessary or because your employer cannot afford to keep paying you. 被裁減的","examples":[]}]}]},"random":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"任意的，隨機的，胡亂的；（磚石建築）石頭大小不一的；<非正式>奇怪的，不同尋常的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"隨意，隨機；<非正式>不認識的人，陌生人"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"隨機地，胡亂地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>random</b> sample or method is one in which all the people or things involved have an equal chance of being chosen. 隨機的","examples":["The survey used a random sample of two thousand people across the Midwest. 這項調查使用的是對中西部地區2000人的隨機取樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe events as <b>random</b>, you mean that they do not seem to follow a definite plan or pattern. 隨意的","examples":["...random violence against innocent victims. …對無辜受害者的隨意攻擊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"隨機地","examples":["...interviews with a randomly selected sample of 30 girls aged between 13 and 18. …對隨機抽取的30名年齡在13至18歲之間的女孩的訪談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"隨意地","examples":["...drinks and magazines left scattered randomly around. …隨意四處散落的飲料和雜誌。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you choose people or things <b>at random</b>, you do not use any particular method, so they all have an equal chance of being chosen. 隨機地","examples":["We received several answers, and we picked one at random. 我們收到了好幾個答案，就隨機地揀選了一個。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something happens <b>at random</b>, it happens without a definite plan or pattern. 隨意地","examples":["Three African-Americans were killed by shots fired at random from a minibus. 3名非洲裔美國人被從一輛小型公共汽車中胡亂射出的子彈打死了。"]}]}]},"renowned":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有名望的，著名的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使有聲譽（renown 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person or place that is <b>renowned</b> <b>for</b> something, usually something good, is well known because of it. 有名望的; 有聲譽的","examples":["The area is renowned for its Romanesque churches. 這個地區以其羅馬式教堂聞名。"]}]}]},"rational":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（想法、決定等）合理的，基於理性的；（人）理性的，理智的；富有理性的；（數）有理的，有理數的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有理數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rational</b> decisions and thoughts are based on reason rather than on emotion. 理性的","examples":["He's asking you to look at both sides of the case and come to a rational decision. 他是在要求你看到問題的兩面，然後做出理性的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>rational</b> person is someone who is sensible and is able to make decisions based on intelligent thinking rather than on emotion. 理智的","examples":["Did he come across as a sane, rational person? 他看上去是不是一個頭腦清醒而理智的人？"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"理性地","examples":["It can be very hard to think rationally when you're feeling so vulnerable and alone. 在你感到如此脆弱和孤單的時候很難理性地思考問題。"]}]}]},"reflective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反射的，反光的 ；沉思的，深思的；體現……的，反映……的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>reflective</b>, you are thinking deeply about something. 沉思的","examples":["I walked on in a reflective mood to the car, thinking about the poor honeymooners. 我若有所思地朝那輛汽車走去，心裡想著那些可憐的度蜜月的人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>reflective</b> <b>of</b> a particular situation or attitude, it is typical of that situation or attitude, or is a consequence of it. 反映的","examples":["The German government's support of the U.S. is not entirely reflective of German public opinion. 德國政府對美國的支援並沒有完全反映出德國的民意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>reflective</b> surface or material sends back light or heat. 反射的","examples":["Avoid using pans with a shiny, reflective base as the heat will be reflected back. 避免使用底部閃亮、能反射的鍋，因為熱量會被反射回去。"]}]}]},"residential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"住宅區的，居民區的 ；家庭的，住宅的；（為工作、學習或受人照料而）住宿（在某地）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>residential</b> area contains houses rather than offices or factories. 住宅的","examples":["...a posh residential area 20 minutes from the White House. …距離白宮20分鐘路程的一個豪華住宅區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>residential</b> institution is one where people live while they are studying there or being cared for there. 寄宿制的","examples":["Training involves a two-year residential course. 培訓包括兩年的住校課程。"]}]}]},"relevant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有關的，切題的；正確的，適宜的；有價值的，有意義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>relevant</b> <b>to</b> a situation or person is important or significant in that situation or to that person. 相關的","examples":["Is religion still relevant to most people's lives? 宗教和大多數人的生活還有關係嗎？"]}]}]},"resolute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"堅決的，果斷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>resolute</b>, you approve of them because they are very determined not to change their mind or not to give up a course of action. 堅定的","examples":["Voters perceive him as a decisive and resolute international leader. 選民認識到他是一位果斷、堅定的國際領袖。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"堅定地","examples":["He resolutely refused to speak English unless forced to. 除非被逼迫，他堅決拒絕說英語。"]}]}]},"resistant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"抵制的，反抗的；有抵抗力的，不受……損害的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抵抗者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>resistant</b> <b>to</b> something is opposed to it and wants to prevent it. 抵制的","examples":["Some people are very resistant to the idea of exercise. 一些人對鍛鍊的主意非常抵制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>resistant</b> <b>to</b> a particular thing, it is not harmed by it. 有抵抗力的","examples":["...how to improve plants to make them more resistant to disease. …如何改良植物來使它們對疾病更有抵抗力。"]}]}]},"operational":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（機器、裝置等）正常運轉的，可使用的；操作的，運營的，業務的；軍事行動的；操作論的，操作主義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A machine or piece of equipment that is <b>operational</b> is in use or is ready for use. (機器、裝置) 使用中的; 可以使用的","examples":["The whole system will be fully operational by December. 整個系統將於12月全面投入使用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Operational</b> factors or problems relate to the working of a system, device, or plan. 操作上的","examples":["The nuclear industry was required to prove that every operational and safety aspect had been fully researched. 核工業需要證明每一個操作和安全專案都已全面調查過。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"操作上地","examples":["...goods which are economically or operationally impractical to transport. …那些從經濟角度和可操作角度來說都不適合運輸的商品。"]}]}]},"rhythmic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有節奏的，有韻律的；規律性發生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"韻律學（=rhythmics）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rhythmic</b> movement or sound is repeated at regular intervals, forming a regular pattern or beat. 有節奏的","examples":["Good breathing is slow, rhythmic and deep. 良好的呼吸緩慢、有節奏並且深沉。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有節奏地","examples":["She stood, swaying her hips, moving rhythmically. 她站著，搖擺著臀部，有節奏地動著。"]}]}]},"sane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"心智健全的，頭腦清醒的；明智的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>sane</b> is able to think and behave normally and reasonably, and is not mentally ill. 心智健全的; 神志正常的","examples":["He seemed perfectly sane. 他看來心智非常健全。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a <b>sane</b> person, action, or system, you mean one that you think is reasonable and sensible. 理智的; 合乎情理的","examples":["No sane person wishes to see conflict or casualties. 理智的人都不希望看到衝突或傷亡。"]}]}]},"respective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"分別的，各自的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Respective</b> means relating or belonging separately to the individual people you have just mentioned. 各自的","examples":["Steve and I were at very different stages in our respective careers. 史蒂夫和我處在各自事業的迥然不同的階段。"]}]}]},"rigorous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（測試、系統或程式）嚴密的，縝密的；（規則，制度等）嚴格的，苛刻的；一絲不苟的；嚴酷的，惡劣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A test, system, or procedure that is <b>rigorous</b> is very thorough and strict. (測試、制度、程式) 嚴格縝密的","examples":["The selection process is based on rigorous tests of competence and experience. 挑選過程是建立在對能力和經驗嚴格縝密的考核的基礎之上的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>rigorous</b> in the way that they do something, they are very careful and thorough. 一絲不苟的; 縝密的","examples":["He is rigorous in his control of expenditure. 他在控制開支方面一絲不苟。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"嚴格縝密地","examples":["...rigorously conducted research. …嚴格進行的研究。"]}]}]},"scenic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"風景優美的；觀光的；舞臺佈景的；（畫）描繪事件的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scenic</b> place has attractive scenery. 風景優美的","examples":["This is an extremely scenic part of America. 這是美國風景極其優美的一個地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scenic</b> route goes through attractive scenery and has nice views. 觀光的 (路線)","examples":["It was even marked on the map as a scenic route. 它在地圖上甚至被標明為一條觀光路線。"]}]}]},"serene":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平靜的，安詳的；清澈的，晴朗的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>晴空，平靜的大海；平靜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>serene</b> is calm and quiet. 安詳的; 寧靜的","examples":["She looked as calm and serene as she always did. 她看上去如往常一樣安詳寧靜。","He didn't speak much, he just smiled with that serene smile of his. 他沒有多說，僅是面含他特有的安詳微笑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"安詳地; 寧靜地","examples":["We sailed serenely down the river. 我們乘船平靜地沿江而下。","She carried on serenely sipping her gin and tonic. 她繼續平靜地呷著加奎寧水的杜松子酒。"]}]}]},"selective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"認真挑選的，嚴格篩選的；選擇性的，有選擇的；（記憶）只記一部分的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>selective</b> process applies only to a few things or people. 選擇性的","examples":["Selective breeding may result in a greyhound running faster and seeing better than a wolf. 選擇育種可能會培育出一種比狼跑得更快、視力更好的靈緹。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone is <b>selective</b>, they choose things carefully, for example, the things that they buy or do. 仔細挑選的; 講究的","examples":["Sales still happen, but buyers are more selective. 銷售仍在進行,但買家更挑剔了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone has a <b>selective</b> memory, you disapprove of the fact that they remember certain facts about something and deliberately forget others, often because it is convenient for them to do so. 選擇性的 (記憶)","examples":["We seem to have a selective memory for the best bits of the past. 我們似乎對過去最美好的時光有選擇性的記憶。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有選擇地","examples":["Within the project, trees are selectively cut on a 25-year rotation. 在這一計劃中，會以25年為週期有選擇地砍伐樹木。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"仔細挑選地","examples":["...people on small incomes who wanted to shop selectively. …購物時需要仔細挑選的低收入人群。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"有選擇性地","examples":["...a tendency to remember only the pleasurable effects of the drug and selectively forget all the adverse effects. …一種只記住毒品帶來的快感而有選擇性地忘掉其所有負面作用的傾向。"]}]}]},"shrewd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）精明的，機敏的；（決定和判斷）精明的，準確的；（打擊）沉重的，尖銳的；邪惡的，惡意的；<古>（尤指天氣）寒冷刺骨的，凜冽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shrewd</b> person is able to understand and judge a situation quickly and to use this understanding to their own advantage. 精明的","examples":["She's a shrewd businesswoman. 她是一個精明的商人。"]}]}]},"sentimental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"情感的（而非理性的）；多愁善感的，柔情的；（故事、電影、書等）感傷的，故作傷感的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>sentimental</b> feels or shows pity or love, sometimes to an extent that is considered exaggerated and foolish. 傷感的; 多愁善感的","examples":["I'm trying not to be sentimental about the past. 我盡力不為過去的事情而多愁善感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sentimental</b> means relating to or involving feelings such as pity or love, especially for things in the past. 情感的","examples":["Our paintings and photographs are of sentimental value only. 我們的畫和照片只有情感價值。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"傷感地; 多愁善感地","examples":["Childhood had less freedom and joy than we sentimentally attribute to it. 童年的自由和歡樂沒有我們多愁善感地賦予它的那麼多。"]}]}]},"sneaky":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鬼鬼祟祟的；暗中的，卑鄙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>sneaky</b>, you disapprove of them because they do things secretly rather than openly. 鬼祟的; 偷偷摸摸的","examples":["It is a sneaky and underhand way of doing business. 這是一種偷偷摸摸、見不得人的生意經。"]}]}]},"simultaneous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"同時發生的，同步的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Things which are <b>simultaneous</b> happen or exist at the same time. 同時的","examples":["...the simultaneous release of the book and the CD. …書與鐳射唱片的同時發行。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"同時地","examples":["The two guns fired almost simultaneously. 兩支槍幾乎同時開火。"]}]}]},"sociable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好交際的，合群的，友善的；（地方，場合，活動）氣氛友好的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美，舊>（非正式的）社交聚會，交誼會；<史>座位面對面的敞篷馬車；<史>並肩雙座的三輪車；<英>S 形的雙人坐椅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sociable</b> people are friendly and enjoy talking to other people. 友善的; 好交際的","examples":["She was, and remained, extremely sociable, enjoying dancing, golf, tennis, skating, and bicycling. 她以前是，現在依然是極其好交際，喜歡跳舞、打高爾夫、打網球、滑冰和騎腳踏車。"]}]}]},"skeptical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不相信的，持懷疑態度的；（哲）懷疑論的，不可知論的"}],"sections":[]},"spacious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（房間或建築物）寬敞的；無邊無際的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spacious</b> room or other place is large in size or area, so that you can move around freely in it. 寬敞的","examples":["The house has a spacious kitchen and dining area. 這座住宅有一個寬敞的廚房和用餐區。"]}]}]},"sophisticated":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"見多識廣的，老練的，見過世面的；複雜巧妙的，先進的，精密的；水平高的，在行的；時尚的，精緻的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使老於世故；使（裝置、技術等）更復雜先進；<古>（老練地）講話（或推理）（sophisticate 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sophisticated</b> machine, device, or method is more advanced or complex than others. 高階的; 複雜的","examples":["Honeybees use one of the most sophisticated communication systems of any insect. 蜜蜂所使用的交流系統是昆蟲中最複雜的之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>sophisticated</b> is comfortable in social situations and knows about culture, fashion, and other matters that are considered socially important. 老練的; 久經世故的","examples":["Claude was a charming, sophisticated companion. 克勞德是個有魅力、見多識廣的夥伴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sophisticated</b> person is intelligent and knows a lot, so that they are able to understand complicated situations. 幹練的","examples":["These people are very sophisticated observers of the foreign policy scene. 這些人是外交政策領域幹練的觀察家。"]}]}]},"stationary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不動的，靜止的；不變的，穩定的；（行星）經度無明顯移動的；定居的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不動的人或物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>stationary</b> is not moving. 靜止不動的","examples":["Stationary cars in traffic jams cause a great deal of pollution. 交通堵塞中停止不前的車輛造成大量汙染。"]}]}]},"subjective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"出自（或涉及）個人感情的，個人的；主觀的（非現實世界的）；（語法中）主語的；自覺的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（語法）主格（the subjective）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>subjective</b> is based on personal opinions and feelings rather than on facts. 主觀的","examples":["We know that taste in art is a subjective matter. 我們知道藝術品味是個主觀問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"主觀地","examples":["Our preliminary results suggest that people do subjectively find the speech clearer. 我們的初步結果表明人們的確主觀地覺得這個演講更清楚。"]}]}]},"spontaneous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自發的，非籌劃安排的；（程式，事件）自發的，自然的；（人）天真率直的；（生物）（機體活動）本能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spontaneous</b> acts are not planned or arranged, but are done because someone suddenly wants to do them. 自然的; 自發的 (行為)","examples":["Diana's house was crowded with happy people whose spontaneous outbursts of song were accompanied by lively music. 戴安娜的房子擠滿了幸福的人們，他們在歡快音樂的伴奏下不由自主地唱起歌來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spontaneous</b> event happens because of processes within something rather than being caused by things outside it. 自然的 (事件)","examples":["I had another spontaneous miscarriage at around the 16th to 18th week. 在大約第16至18周時我又一次自然流產了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"自然地; 自發地","examples":["Many people spontaneously stood up and cheered. 許多人自發地站起來歡呼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"自然地","examples":["Usually a woman's breasts produce milk spontaneously after the birth. 通常女性在生孩子後乳房會自然泌乳。"]}]}]},"strategic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"戰略（性）的， 策略（上）的；（計劃或戰略上）有用的，重要的；（武器、戰爭或地方）戰略性的，有戰略優勢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Strategic</b> means relating to the most important, general aspects of something such as a military operation or political policy, especially when these are decided in advance. 戰略上的","examples":["...the new strategic thinking which NATO leaders produced at the recent London summit. …北大西洋公約組織領導人在最近倫敦峰會上提出的新的戰略思維。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Strategic</b> weapons are very powerful missiles that can be fired only after a decision to use them has been made by a political leader. 戰略性的","examples":["...strategic nuclear weapons. …戰略性核武器。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you put something in a <b>strategic</b> position, you place it cleverly in a position where it will be most useful or have the most effect. 巧妙的","examples":["...the marble benches Eve had placed at strategic points throughout the gardens, where the views were spectacular. …伊夫在花園各個景色優美的巧妙位置安放的大理石長凳。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"戰略上地","examples":["...strategically important roads, bridges and buildings. …戰略上具有重要意義的公路、橋樑和建築物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"巧妙地","examples":["We had kept its presence hidden with a strategically placed chair. 我們用一把巧妙放置的椅子把它隱藏起來。"]}]}]},"subsequent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"隨後的，接著的；（河，谷）後成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>subsequent</b> to describe something that happened or existed after the time or event that has just been referred to. 隨後的","examples":["...the increase of population in subsequent years. …隨後幾年中的人口增長。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"後來","examples":["He subsequently worked on Boeing's 747, 767 and 737 jetliner programmes. 他後來從事了波音747、767 和 737噴氣式飛機的專案。"]}]}]},"suburban":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"郊區的，城郊的；平淡乏味的，鄉氣的，平庸的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"郊區居民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Suburban</b> means relating to a suburb. 郊區的","examples":["...a comfortable suburban home. …一個舒適的位於郊區的家。"]}]}]},"supersonic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"超音速的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"超音速，超聲波；超音速飛機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supersonic</b> aircraft travel faster than the speed of sound. 超音速的","examples":["There was a huge bang; it sounded like a supersonic jet. 發出一聲巨響；聽起來像一架超音速噴氣式飛機。"]}]}]},"successive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"連續的，依次的；接替的，繼承的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Successive</b> means happening or existing one after another without a break. 連續的","examples":["Jackson was the winner for a second successive year. 傑克遜是連續第二年的獲勝者。"]}]}]},"subtle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不易察覺的，微妙的；敏銳的，有洞察力的；靈活的，巧妙的；含蓄的，隱晦的；<古>狡猾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>subtle</b> is not immediately obvious or noticeable. 不易察覺的","examples":["...the slow and subtle changes that take place in all living things. …所有生物中發生的緩慢而不易察覺的變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>subtle</b> person cleverly uses indirect methods to achieve something. 不露聲色的","examples":["I even began to exploit him in subtle ways. 我甚至開始不露聲色地利用他。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Subtle</b> smells, tastes, sounds, or colours are pleasantly complex and delicate. 淡的; 精妙的","examples":["...subtle shades of brown. …各種淡棕色。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不易察覺地","examples":["The truth is subtly different. 事實略有不同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不露聲色地","examples":["Nathan is subtly trying to turn her against Barry. 內森在盡力不露聲色地使她轉而反對巴里。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"淡地; 精妙地","examples":["...a white sofa teamed with subtly coloured rugs. …一張鋪著色彩淡雅的小墊的白色沙發。"]}]}]},"superb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極佳的，質量極高的；（信心、控制力、技巧）非同一般的，超凡的；壯麗的，輝煌的；羽毛鮮豔奪目的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>superb</b>, its quality is very good indeed. 極好的","examples":["There is a superb 18-hole golf course 6 miles away. 6英里外有個極好的18洞高爾夫球場。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone has <b>superb</b> confidence, control, or skill, you mean that they have very great confidence, control, or skill. (信心、控制力或技巧) 超凡的","examples":["With superb skill he managed to make a perfect landing. 他以超凡的技巧設法完成了一次完美的著陸。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極好地","examples":["The orchestra played superbly. 這支管絃樂隊演奏得好極了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"超凡地","examples":["...his superbly disciplined opponent. …他的那個受過超凡訓練的對手。"]}]}]},"superstitious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"迷信的；迷信引起的，沒有充分根據的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who are <b>superstitious</b> believe in things that are not real or possible, for example magic. (人) 迷信的","examples":["Jean was extremely superstitious and believed the colour green brought bad luck. 瓊極端迷信，認為綠色會帶來厄運。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Superstitious</b> fears or beliefs are irrational and not based on fact. (恐懼或信念) 迷信的","examples":["A wave of superstitious fear spread among the townspeople. 一股迷信的恐懼浪潮在城裡人中蔓延。"]}]}]},"tedious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冗長的，單調乏味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something such as a job, task, or situation as <b>tedious</b>, you mean it is boring and frustrating. 乏味煩人的","examples":["Such lists are long and tedious to read. 這種清單讀起來既冗長又乏味煩人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"乏味煩人地","examples":["...the most tediously boring aspects of international relations. …國際關係中最乏味煩人的某些方面。"]}]}]},"thrifty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"節儉的，節約的；<古>（牲畜，植物）茁壯的，健康的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>thrifty</b>, you are praising them for saving money, not buying unnecessary things, and not wasting things. 節儉的; 節省的; 節約的","examples":["My mother taught me to be thrifty. 我母親教會我生活要節儉。","...thrifty shoppers. ...花錢精打細算的購物者。"]}]}]},"symbolic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"用作象徵的，被認為是象徵的；有象徵意義的；（行為舉動）象徵性的，沒有甚麼實際影響的；符號的，使用象徵的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an event, action, or procedure as <b>symbolic</b>, you mean that it represents an important change, although it has little practical effect. 有象徵意義的","examples":["A lot of Latin-American officials are stressing the symbolic importance of the trip. 許多拉丁美洲官員正在強調這次旅行在象徵意義上的重要性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>symbolic of</b> a person or thing is regarded or used as a symbol of them. 用作象徵的","examples":["Yellow clothes are worn as symbolic of spring. 黃色衣服被穿著來象徵春天。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Symbolic</b> is used to describe things involving or relating to symbols. 符號的","examples":["...symbolic representations of landscape. …地形的符號表徵。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有象徵意義地","examples":["It was a simple enough gesture, but symbolically important. 這雖是個再簡單不過的手勢，但卻有著重要的象徵意義。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"象徵性地","examples":["Each circle symbolically represents the whole of humanity. 每個圓圈都象徵性地代表全人類。"]}]}]},"theatrical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"戲劇的，演劇的；戲劇性的，誇張的；盛大的，壯觀的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指業餘的）戲劇表演，娛樂表演；誇張的行為； 職業演員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Theatrical</b> means relating to the theatre. 戲劇的","examples":["...the most outstanding theatrical performances of the year. …年度最傑出的戲劇表演。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Theatrical</b> behaviour is exaggerated and unnatural, and intended to create an effect. (行為) 誇張的","examples":["In a theatrical gesture Jim clamped his hand over his eyes. 以一個誇張的手勢，吉姆用一隻手緊緊捂住雙眼。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在戲劇上","examples":["Shaffer's great gift lies in his ability to animate ideas theatrically. 謝弗的天賦在於他能把想法在戲劇上表現出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"誇張地","examples":["He looked theatrically at his watch. 他誇張地看了看錶。"]}]}]},"theoretical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"理論的；理論上存在的，假設的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>theoretical</b> study or explanation is based on or uses the ideas and abstract principles that relate to a particular subject, rather than the practical aspects or uses of it. 理論的","examples":["...theoretical physics. …理論物理。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as a <b>theoretical</b> one, you mean that although it is supposed to be true or to exist in the way stated, it may not in fact be true or exist in that way. 理論上的","examples":["This is certainly a theoretical risk but in practice there is seldom a problem. 這在理論上肯定有風險，但在實踐中卻很少出問題。"]}]}]},"triumphant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（因勝利或成功而）洋洋得意的，耀武揚威的；勝利的，成功的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>triumphant</b> has gained a victory or succeeded in something and feels very happy about it. (因勝利或成功而) 得意洋洋的","examples":["The captain's voice was triumphant. 船長的聲音聽起來得意洋洋的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"得意洋洋地","examples":["They marched triumphantly into the capital. 他們得意洋洋地列隊進入首都。"]}]}]},"tranquil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平靜的，寧靜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>tranquil</b> is calm and peaceful. 寧靜的","examples":["The tranquil atmosphere of the inn allows guests to feel totally at home. 這家客棧的寧靜氛圍讓客人們感到賓至如歸。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"寧靜","examples":["The hotel is a haven of peace and tranquillity. 這個旅館是一個寧靜的好去處。"]}]}]},"valiant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"英勇的，勇敢的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇士，勇敢的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>valiant</b> action is very brave and determined, though it may lead to failure or defeat. 頑強的","examples":["Despite valiant efforts by the finance minister, inflation rose to 36%. 儘管這位財政部長作了頑強的努力，通貨膨脹率還是升到了36%。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"頑強地","examples":["He suffered further heart attacks and strokes, all of which he fought valiantly. 他又發作過幾次心臟病並中過幾次風，他與這一切都作了頑強的鬥爭。"]}]}]},"unanimous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（投票、決定、協議等）全體同意的，無異議的；（所有人）一致同意的，意見一致的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a group of people are <b>unanimous</b>, they all agree about something or all vote for the same thing. 一致同意的","examples":["Editors were unanimous in their condemnation of the proposals. 編輯們一致譴責這些提議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>unanimous</b> vote, decision, or agreement is one in which all the people involved agree. 全體同意的 (投票、決定、協議等)","examples":["Their decision was unanimous. 他們的決定是全體同意的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"一致同意地","examples":["The board unanimously approved the project last week. 董事會上週一致同意批准了這個專案。"]}]}]},"trivial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瑣碎的，不重要的；容易解決的，不費吹灰之力的；（人）務小的，淺薄的；（數學）平凡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>trivial</b>, you think that it is unimportant and not serious. 無關緊要的","examples":["The director tried to wave aside these issues as trivial details that could be settled later. 那位主任對這些問題置之不理，視它們為可以後解決的無關緊要的細節。"]}]}]},"versatile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"多才多藝的，有多種技能的；多用途的，多功能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a person is <b>versatile</b>, you approve of them because they have many different skills. 多才多藝的","examples":["He had been one of the game's most versatile athletes. 他是這次運動會中最有才能的運動員之一。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A tool, machine, or material that is <b>versatile</b> can be used for many different purposes. 用途廣泛的","examples":["Never before has computing been so versatile. 計算機技術從未像現在這樣用途廣泛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"多才多藝","examples":["Aileen stands out for her incredible versatility as an actress. 作為一名女演員，艾琳以其難以置信的多才多藝而出類拔萃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"用途廣泛","examples":["Velvet as a fabric is not known for its versatility. 天鵝絨作為一種織物並非以其用途廣泛而聞名。"]}]}]},"victorious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勝利的，獲勝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>victorious</b> to describe someone who has won a victory in a struggle, war, or competition. 勝利的","examples":["In 1978 he played for the victorious Argentinian side in the World Cup. 1978年，他為世界盃上獲勝的阿根廷隊踢球。"]}]}]},"vocational":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"職業的，職業技術的，業務知識的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vocational</b> training and skills are the training and skills needed for a particular job or profession. 職業的","examples":["...a course designed to provide vocational training in engineering. …為提供工程學職業培訓而設計的一門課程。"]}]}]},"valid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（檔案或票證）有效的；正當的，合理的；合法有效的；計算機系統接受的，被計算機系統認為有效的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>valid</b> argument, comment, or idea is based on sensible reasoning. 有根據的","examples":["They put forward many valid reasons for not exporting. 他們提出了許多有根據的理由來反對出口。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>valid</b> is important or serious enough to make it worth saying or doing. 重要的","examples":["Most designers share the unspoken belief that fashion is a valid form of visual art. 大多數設計師都有一種心照不宣的信念，即時尚是視覺藝術的一種重要形式。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a ticket or other document is <b>valid</b>, it can be used and will be accepted by people in authority. 有效的","examples":["All tickets are valid for two months. 所有的票在兩個月內有效。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合理性","examples":["The editorial says this argument has lost much of its validity. 這篇社論說該論點已失去了其許多合理性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"重要性","examples":["...the validity of making children wear bicycle helmets. …讓孩子們戴腳踏車頭盔的重要性。"]}]}]},"vicious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兇險的，會造成傷害的；嚴厲的，惡毒的，惡意的；劇烈的，惡劣的；<文>不道德的，罪惡的；<古>（語言，推理）不完善的，謬誤的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vicious</b> person or a <b>vicious</b> blow is violent and cruel. 兇殘的","examples":["He was a cruel and vicious man. 他是一個殘忍而兇惡的人。","He suffered a vicious attack by a gang of white youths. 他遭到了一幫白人青年兇殘的攻擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vicious</b> remark is cruel and intended to upset someone. 惡毒的","examples":["It is a deliberate, nasty and vicious attack on a young man's character. 這是對一位青年的人格蓄意的、下流的和惡毒的攻擊。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"兇殘地","examples":["She had been viciously attacked with a hammer. 她曾被人用錘子兇殘地襲擊過。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"惡毒地","examples":["\"He deserved to die,\" said Penelope viciously. “他該死，” 佩內洛普惡毒地說道。"]}]}]},"whatsoever":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"任何，無論什麼"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"絲毫（用於強調否定句）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何事物，無論什麼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whatsoever</b> after a noun group in order to emphasize a negative statement. 任何 (用於名詞片語之後，強調否定陳述)","examples":["My school did nothing whatsoever in the way of athletics. 我的學校就體育運動而言沒有任何作為。"]}]}]},"watertight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（容器或房間）防漏水的，水密的；（理論、計劃或協議）嚴密的，無懈可擊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>watertight</b> does not allow water to pass through it, for example, because it is tightly sealed. 不透水的","examples":["The flask is completely watertight, even when laid on its side. 這水瓶即使平放也不漏一滴水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>watertight</b> case, argument, or agreement is one that has been so carefully put together that nobody will be able to find a fault in it. (事實、論點、協議等) 嚴密的; 無懈可擊的","examples":["If she could just establish the time the picture had been taken, Mick would have a watertight alibi. 只要她能確定拍這張照片的時間，米克就可以有一個無懈可擊的不在現場的證據。"]}]}]},"vulgar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗俗的，庸俗的，不雅的；（笑話、評論、動作等）下流的；（人）粗魯的，無禮的；平民的，通俗語言的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>平民，百姓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>vulgar</b>, you think it is in bad taste or of poor artistic quality. 粗俗的","examples":["I think it's a very vulgar house. 我認為這是一棟很俗氣的房子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe pictures, gestures, or remarks as <b>vulgar</b>, you dislike them because they refer to sex or parts of the body in an offensive way that you find unpleasant. 下流的","examples":["The women laughed coarsely at the comedian's vulgar jokes. 那些女人們聽到滑稽演員的下流笑話後都放蕩地大笑起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>vulgar</b>, you mean that they lack taste or behave offensively. 粗魯的","examples":["He was a vulgar old man, but he never swore in front of a woman. 他是個粗魯的老頭，但他從來沒有在女人面前說過髒話。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗俗","examples":["I hate the vulgarity of the bright colours in this room. 我不喜歡這個房間裡豔麗而俗氣的色調。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"下流","examples":["Charles was a complete gentleman, incapable of rudeness or vulgarity. 查爾斯完完全全是個紳士，無粗魯下流之舉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"粗魯","examples":["It's his vulgarity that I can't take. 我不能忍受的正是他的粗魯。"]}]}]},"virtual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"幾乎……的，實質上的；（在計算機或網際網路上存在或出現的）虛擬的，模擬的；（光學）虛的，虛擬的；（機械學）虛的；（物理）虛的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>virtual</b> to indicate that something is so nearly true that for most purposes it can be regarded as true. 事實上的","examples":["Argentina came to a virtual standstill while the game was being played. 阿根廷在比賽進行期間全國上下事實上進入了停頓狀態。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Virtual</b> objects and activities are generated by a computer to simulate real objects and activities. (計算機模擬) 虛擬的","examples":["Up to four players can compete in a virtual world of role playing. 最多能有4個人可以在虛擬世界中扮演角色進行角逐。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"虛擬性","examples":["People speculate about virtuality systems, but we're already working on it. 人們對虛擬系統尚存疑慮，而我們已經在開發了。"]}]}]},"witty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"風趣的，詼諧的，機智的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>witty</b> is amusing in a clever way. 詼諧的","examples":["His plays were very good, very witty. 他的那些劇作非常好，非常詼諧。"]}]}]},"vulnerable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（身體或精神）脆弱的，易受傷的；（事物、人或地方）易受攻擊的，易受傷害的；易患病的；（橋牌）有局方的，有身價的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>vulnerable</b> is weak and without protection, with the result that they are easily hurt physically or emotionally. 易受傷害的","examples":["Old people are particularly vulnerable members of our society. 老人是我們社會中特別容易受到傷害的成員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person, animal, or plant is <b>vulnerable</b> <b>to</b> a disease, they are more likely to get it than other people, animals, or plants. 容易患…病的","examples":["People with high blood pressure are especially vulnerable to diabetes. 血壓高的人尤其容易患糖尿病。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Something that is <b>vulnerable</b> can be easily harmed or affected by something bad. 易受損害的","examples":["Their tanks would be vulnerable to attack from the air. 他們的坦克將易受空襲。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"脆弱","examples":["David accepts his own vulnerability. 戴維承認自己的脆弱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"患病的可能性","examples":["Taking long-term courses of certain medicines may increase vulnerability to infection. 長期服用某些藥物可能會增加受感染的機率。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"易受攻擊性","examples":["...anxieties about the country's vulnerability to invasion. …對國家易受侵略的憂慮。"]}]}]},"abound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"大量存在，有許多；富於，盛產（abound with/in sth.）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things <b>abound</b>, or if a place <b>abounds</b> <b>with</b> things, there are very large numbers of them. 充滿","examples":["Stories abound about when he was in charge. 他負責時傳聞很多。"]}]}]},"abbreviate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"縮寫，縮短，使簡短"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"使用縮寫詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>abbreviate</b> something, especially a word or a piece of writing, you make it shorter. 縮寫","examples":["The creators of the original X-Men abbreviated the title of its sequel to simply X2. 第1部《X戰警》的創作者們把其續集的片名縮寫成簡單的《X2》。"]}]}]},"administrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"管理，經營"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>administrate</b> an organization's business activities means to manage or direct them. 管理 (商業活動)","examples":["The Internet opens up new ways of administrating the tax system. 網際網路開拓了管理稅收系統的一些新途徑。"]}]}]},"accelerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）加快，促進；（車輛或駕駛者）加速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the process or rate of something <b>accelerates</b> or if something <b>accelerates</b> it, it gets faster and faster. 使加速; 加速","examples":["Growth will accelerate to 2.9 percent next year. 增長明年將加快到2.9%。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a moving vehicle <b>accelerates</b>, it goes faster and faster. 加速","examples":["Suddenly the car accelerated. 突然車加速了。"]}]}]},"affirm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"斷言，證實； 宣稱擁護，支援；認可（判決，協議），批准；不宣誓而提供正式證詞；給予（某人）情感支援（或鼓勵）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>affirm</b> that something is true or that something exists, you state firmly and publicly that it is true or exists. 公開肯定","examples":["The court affirmed that the information can be made public under the Freedom of Information Act. 法院公開肯定了此資訊能依據《自由資訊法案》公之於眾。","...a speech in which he affirmed a commitment to lower taxes. …在其中他公開肯定了減稅承諾的一次演講。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event <b>affirms</b> something, it shows that it is true or exists. 證實","examples":["Everything I had accomplished seemed to affirm that opinion. 我所做成的每件事似乎都證實了那個觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"公開肯定","examples":["The North Atlantic Treaty begins with the affirmation that its parties \"reaffirm their faith in the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations.\" 《北大西洋公約》以公開肯定其成員“重申其對《聯合國憲章》的目的以及原則的信念”開頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"證實","examples":["The ruling was a welcome affirmation of the constitutional right to free speech. 此裁決是對言論自由這一憲法權利的受人歡迎的肯定。"]}]}]},"accumulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"積累，積攢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>accumulate</b> things or when they <b>accumulate</b>, they collect or are gathered over a period of time. 積聚","examples":["Lead can accumulate in the body until toxic levels are reached. 鉛可以在體內積聚直至到達有毒的程度。"]}]}]},"administer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"管理，治理；執行，實施；給予（藥物或治療）；給予幫助，關心照顧（某人）；主持（儀式等）；<正式>踢，打；執行遺產管理人的職責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>administers</b> something such as a country, the law, or a test, they take responsibility for organizing and supervising it. 監管 (國家、法律、考試等)","examples":["The plan calls for the UN to administer the country until elections can be held. 該計劃呼籲聯合國監管該國直至選舉可以舉行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a doctor or a nurse <b>administers</b> a drug, they give it to a patient. (醫生、護士) 派發 (藥物)","examples":["The physician may prescribe but not administer the drug. 內科醫師可以開處方但不可發藥。"]}]}]},"accommodate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……提供住宿；容納，提供空間；考慮到，顧及；順應，適應；幫助（某人），向……施以援手；迎合，遷就；調解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a building or space can <b>accommodate</b> someone or something, it has enough room for them. 容納","examples":["The school was not big enough to accommodate all the children. 學校沒有足夠的地方容納所有的學生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>accommodate</b> someone means to provide them with a place to live or stay. 為…提供住宿","examples":["...a hotel built to accommodate guests for the wedding of King Alfonso. …一個為來參加阿方索國王婚禮的客人提供住宿而建造的賓館。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is planned or changed to <b>accommodate</b> a particular situation, it is planned or changed so that it takes this situation into account. 使…適應","examples":["The roads are built to accommodate gradual temperature changes. 這些道路是為適應氣溫的逐漸變化而建的。"]}]}]},"alienate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使疏遠，使敵對；使格格不入；轉讓，讓渡（財產或權利）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>alienate</b> someone, you make them become unfriendly or unsympathetic toward you. 冷落","examples":["The government cannot afford to alienate either group. 該政府承擔不起冷落兩個組織中的任何一個。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>alienate</b> a person <b>from</b> someone or something that they are normally linked with means to cause them to be emotionally or intellectually separated from them. 使疏遠","examples":["His second wife, Alice, was determined to alienate him from his two boys. 他的第2個妻子阿麗絲決心讓他疏遠他的兩個兒子。"]}]}]},"amplify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放大，擴大（聲音）；增強，加強；詳述，進一步闡明；擴增（基因，DNA序列）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>amplify</b> a sound, you make it louder, usually by using electronic equipment. 擴大 (聲音)","examples":["This landscape seemed to trap and amplify sounds. 這種地形好像能聚攏和擴大聲音。","The music was amplified with microphones. 那音樂被麥克風擴大了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>amplify</b> something means to increase its strength or intensity. 增強","examples":["The mist had been replaced by a kind of haze that seemed to amplify the heat. 這薄霧已經被一種熱汽代替了，這似乎加重了炎熱的程度。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"擴音","examples":["...a voice that needed no amplification. …一個不需要擴音的嗓門。"]}]}]},"animate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有生命的，有活力的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使生動，使興奮；把……製作成動畫；鼓動，激勵；使有生命"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>animate</b> has life, in contrast to things like stones and machines which do not. 有生命的","examples":["Natural philosophy involved the study of all aspects of the material world, animate and inanimate. 自然哲學涉及到了對包括有生命體與無生命體的物質世界的全面研究。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>animate</b> something means to make it lively or more cheerful. 使有生氣","examples":["There was precious little about the cricket to animate the crowd. 這場板球比賽極少有讓觀眾興奮的地方。"]}]}]},"allocate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"分配，分派，劃撥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one item or share of something <b>is allocated</b> <b>to</b> a particular person or <b>for</b> a particular purpose, it is given to that person or used for that purpose. 分配","examples":["Tickets are limited and will be allocated to those who apply first. 票數有限，將分配給那些先申請的人。","The 1985 federal budget allocated $7.3 billion for development programmes. 1985年聯邦預算撥了73億美元用於開發專案。"]}]}]},"approximate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大概的，近似的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"類似，接近；模仿，模擬；粗略估計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>approximate</b> number, time, or position is close to the correct number, time, or position, but is not exact. 大概的 (數字、時間或方位等)","examples":["The approximate cost varies from around $150 to $250. 大致的費用在$150至$250之間不等。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An idea or description that is <b>approximate</b> is not intended to be precise or accurate, but to give some indication of what something is like. 大概的 (觀點或描述等)","examples":["They did not have even an approximate idea what the Germans really wanted. 他們對於德國人真正想要什麼甚至沒有一個大致概念。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"大概地","examples":["Approximately $150 million is to be spent on improvements. 大概1.5億美元將花在改進上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>approximates</b> something else, it is similar to it but is not exactly the same. 近似於","examples":["The mixture described below will approximate it, but is not exactly the same. 下面所描述的混合物會與之近似，但不完全一樣。"]}]}]},"anticipate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預期，預料；預見（並做準備）；期望，盼望；先於……做，早於……行動；提前使用；在期限內履行（義務），償還（債務）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>anticipate</b> an event, you realize in advance that it may happen and you are prepared for it. 預期","examples":["At the time we couldn't have anticipated the result of our campaigning. 當時我們不可能預期到我們活動的結果。","It is anticipated that the equivalent of 192 full-time jobs will be lost. 據預測相當於192個全職的工作將會喪失。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>anticipate</b> a question, request, or need, you do what is necessary or required before the question, request, or need occurs. 預先準備","examples":["What Jeff did was to anticipate my next question. 傑夫所做的是預先準備我的下一個問題。"]}]}]},"attain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得，實現；達到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>attain</b> something, you gain it or achieve it, often after a lot of effort. (常指經過努力) 獲得","examples":["Jim is halfway to attaining his pilot's licence. 吉姆快要拿到他的飛行員執照了。"]}]}]},"articulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"明確表達，清楚說明；口齒清楚地說，清晰地發音；用關節連線，連結"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"善於表達的；口齒清楚的，發音清晰的；有關節的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>articulate</b>, you mean that they are able to express their thoughts and ideas easily and well. 善表達的","examples":["She is an articulate young woman. 她是個善表達的年輕女子。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>articulate</b> your ideas or feelings, you express them clearly in words. 清楚地表述","examples":["The president has been accused of failing to articulate an overall vision in foreign affairs. 總統被指責沒能清楚地表述對外交事務的總體設想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>articulate</b> something, you say it very clearly, so that each word or syllable can be heard. 清楚地說出","examples":["He articulated each syllable. 他清楚地說出了每個音節。"]}]}]},"beckon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（招手）示意，召喚；吸引，引誘；可能發生"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"召喚的表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>beckon</b> <b>to</b> someone, you signal to them to come to you. 向…招手","examples":["He beckoned to the waiter. 他朝服務員招了招手。","I beckoned her over. 我招手叫她過來。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>beckons</b>, it is so attractive to someone that they feel they must become involved in it. 召喚","examples":["All the attractions of the peninsula beckon. 那半島上所有勝地都引人入勝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>beckons</b> <b>for</b> someone, it is very likely to happen to them. 向…召喚","examples":["The big time beckons for Billy Dodds. 偉大的時刻在向比利•多茲召喚。"]}]}]},"authorize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"批准，許可；授權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in a position of authority <b>authorizes</b> something, they give their official permission for it to happen. 批准","examples":["It would certainly be within his power to authorize a police raid like that. 他肯定有權批准那種警方突襲行動。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"批准","examples":["The United Nations will approve his request for authorization to use military force to deliver aid. 聯合國將同意他的請求，批准他動用軍隊來運送救援物資。"]}]}]},"assert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"堅稱，斷言；維護，堅持（權利或權威）；堅持自己的主張，表現堅定；生效，起作用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>asserts</b> a fact or belief, they state it firmly. 堅定地陳述","examples":["Mr. Helm plans to assert that the bill violates the First Amendment. 赫爾姆先生計劃堅定地陳述該法案有違《第一修正案》。","The defendants, who continue to assert their innocence, are expected to appeal. 那些繼續宣稱其清白的被告預計會上訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>assert</b> your authority, you make it clear by your behaviour that you have authority. 顯示 (權威)","examples":["After the war, the army made an attempt to assert its authority in the south of the country. 戰後，軍隊試圖在該國南部顯示其權威。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>assert</b> your right or claim to something, you insist that you have the right to it. 堅持 (權利或要求)","examples":["The republics began asserting their right to govern themselves. 各共和國開始堅持他們自治的權利。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>assert</b> <b>yourself</b>, you speak and act in a forceful way, so that people take notice of you. 彰顯 (自己)","examples":["He's speaking up and asserting himself and doing things he enjoys. 他現在直言不諱、彰顯自我，做著他喜歡做的事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"斷言","examples":["There is no concrete evidence to support assertions that the recession is truly over. 沒有任何確鑿的證據支援經濟衰退已真正結束的斷言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(權威的) 顯示","examples":["The decision is seen as an assertion of his authority within the company. 這一決定被看作是公司內他的權威的顯示。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"堅持","examples":["These institutions have made the assertion of ethnic identity possible. 這些機構已使種族身份的堅持成為可能。"]}]}]},"besiege":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包圍，圍困；打擾，糾纏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are besieged</b> <b>by</b> people, many people want something from you and continually bother you. 不斷打擾","examples":["She was besieged by the press and the public. 她不斷被媒體和公眾打擾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If soldiers <b>besiege</b> a place, they surround it and wait for the people in it to stop fighting or resisting. 圍攻","examples":["The main part of the army moved to Sevastopol to besiege the town. 這支部隊的主力前往塞瓦斯托波爾去圍攻那個小鎮。"]}]}]},"assassinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"暗殺，行刺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone important <b>is assassinated</b>, they are murdered as a political act. (因政治原因而) 刺殺","examples":["Would the U.S. be radically different today if Kennedy had not been assassinated? 如果肯尼迪沒有被刺殺，今天的美國會大不相同嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"刺殺","examples":["She would like an investigation into the assassination of her husband. 她想要對其丈夫的遇刺進行調查。","He lives in constant fear of assassination. 他一直生活在對刺殺的恐懼之中。"]}]}]},"assess":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"評價，評定；估價，估計；徵稅，處以罰金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>assess</b> a person, thing, or situation, you consider them in order to make a judgment about them. 評估","examples":["The test was to assess aptitude rather than academic achievement. 該測試將評估能力而不是學業成績。","It would be a matter of assessing whether she was well enough to travel. 這將是個評估她是否身體好到可以旅行的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>assess</b> the amount of money that something is worth or should be paid, you calculate or estimate it. 計算; 估算","examples":["Ask them to send you information on how to assess the value of your belongings. 叫他們把如何估算你的財產價值的資料寄給你。"]}]}]},"civilize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"教化，薰陶；改善，改進；使文明，使開化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>civilize</b> a person or society means to educate them and improve their way of life. 使文明; 教化","examples":["...a comedy about a man who tries to civilize a woman – but she ends up civilizing him. …一部關於一個男人試圖去教化一個女人–結果卻是那個女人教化了他的喜劇。"]}]}]},"bombard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"轟炸，連環炮擊；攻擊，轟擊；連珠炮似地質問，大肆提問；（物）以高速粒子轟擊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>射石炮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bombard</b> someone <b>with</b> something, you make them face a great deal of it. For example, if you <b>bombard</b> them <b>with</b> questions or criticism, you keep asking them a lot of questions or you keep criticizing them. 連珠炮似地提問; 不斷批評","examples":["He bombarded Catherine with questions to which he should have known the answers. 他不停地追問凱瑟琳他本該知道答案的問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When soldiers <b>bombard</b> a place, they attack it with continuous heavy gunfire or bombs. 連續轟炸","examples":["Rebel artillery units have regularly bombarded the airport. 叛軍的炮兵部隊經常炮轟機場。"]}]}]},"characterize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"描述，刻畫；成為……的特徵，是……的典型"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is characterized</b> <b>by</b> a particular feature or quality, that feature or quality is an obvious part of it. 以…為特徵","examples":["This election campaign has been characterized by violence. 這次競選運動以暴力為特徵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>characterize</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a particular thing, you describe them as that thing. 描述為","examples":["Both companies have characterized the relationship as friendly. 兩家公司都認為彼此的關係是友好的。"]}]}]},"betray":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"背叛，出賣；食言，辜負；違背（信仰、原則等）；洩露（機密，資訊）；流露，顯露出（情感或特性）；暴露（不易發覺的東西）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>betray</b> someone who loves or trusts you, your actions hurt and disappoint them. 辜負","examples":["When I tell someone I will not betray his confidence I keep my word. 當我對人說我不會辜負他的信任時，我會說到做到。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>betrays</b> their country or their friends, they give information to an enemy, putting their country's security or their friends' safety at risk. 出賣; 背叛","examples":["They offered me money if I would betray my associates. 如果我出賣自己的同伴，他們就會給我錢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>betray</b> an ideal or your principles, you say or do something which goes against those beliefs. 違背","examples":["We betray the ideals of our country when we support capital punishment. 我們贊同死刑就會違揹我們國家的理想。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>betray</b> a feeling or quality, you show it without intending to. (無意中) 流露","examples":["She studied his face, but it betrayed nothing. 她審視著他的臉，但他卻絲毫不露聲色。"]}]}]},"blunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鈍的，不鋒利的；直言不諱的，說話生硬的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"減弱；使不鋒利，使變鈍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>blunt</b>, you say exactly what you think without trying to be polite. 直言不諱的","examples":["She is blunt about her personal life. 她對自己的私生活直言不諱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>blunt</b> object has a rounded or flat end rather than a sharp one. 鈍的","examples":["One of them had been struck 13 times over the head with a blunt object. 他們其中一人的頭部被鈍器砸了13下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>blunt</b> knife or blade is no longer sharp and does not cut well. 不鋒利的","examples":["The edge is as blunt as an old butter knife. 刃鈍得跟一把老黃油刀一樣。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"直言不諱地","examples":["\"I don't believe you!\" Jeanne said bluntly. “我不信你！” 珍妮直言不諱地說。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>blunts</b> an emotion, a feeling or a need, it weakens it. 使減弱","examples":["The constant repetition of violence has blunted the human response to it. 持續不斷的暴力事件使人們對它的反應減弱了。"]}]}]},"cleanse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使清潔，清洗；清理，整頓（壞人或不良的情形等）；免除（某人）的罪過；<古>（聖經譯文）治癒（麻風病患者）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"對某物（尤指皮膚）的清潔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>cleanse</b> a place, person, or organization <b>of</b> something dirty, unpleasant, or evil means to make them free from it. 使清潔; 使淨化","examples":["Right after your last cigarette, your body will begin to cleanse itself of tobacco toxins. 在最後一根香菸後，你的身體將馬上開始清除菸草毒素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cleanse</b> your skin or a wound, you clean it. 清潔 (皮膚、傷口)","examples":["Catherine demonstrated the proper way to cleanse the face. 凱瑟琳演示了潔面的正確方法。"]}]}]},"collide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"衝突，牴觸；（迥異的事物）碰在一起；碰撞，相撞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more moving people or objects <b>collide</b>, they crash into one another. If a moving person or object <b>collides</b> <b>with</b> a person or object that is not moving, they crash into them. 碰撞","examples":["Two trains collided head-on in Ohio early this morning. 兩輛列車今天早晨在俄亥俄州迎頭相撞。","Racing up the stairs, he almost collided with Daisy. 他衝上樓梯，幾乎與戴西相撞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the aims, opinions, or interests of one person or group <b>collide</b> <b>with</b> those of another person or group, they are very different from each other and are therefore opposed. (目標、觀點或利益等) 相牴觸; 相沖突","examples":["The aims of the negotiators in New York again seem likely to collide with the aims of the warriors in the field. 紐約談判者的目標看起來可能再次與戰場上勇士們的目標相沖突。"]}]}]},"cater":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供餐飲服務，承辦酒席；滿足，迎合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>cater to</b> a group of people means to provide all the things that they need or want. 滿足…需要; 迎合","examples":["We cater to an exclusive clientele. 我們滿足一個特殊客戶群的需求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>cater to</b> something means to take it into account. 考慮","examples":["Exercise classes cater to all levels of fitness. 訓練課照顧到各種健康狀況。","...shops that cater to the needs of men. … 經營男士用品的商店。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or company <b>caters</b> an occasion such as a wedding or a party, they provide food and drink for all the people there. (在婚禮、派對等場合) 提供餐飲服務; 承辦酒席","examples":["...a full-service restaurant equipped to cater large events. …一家承辦大型活動及提供全方位服務的飯店。"]}]}]},"coincide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"巧合，同時發生；一致，相符；相交，重疊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one event <b>coincides</b> <b>with</b> another, they happen at the same time. 同時發生","examples":["The exhibition coincides with the 50th anniversary of his death. 展會與他50週年忌辰同日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the ideas or interests of two or more people <b>coincide</b>, they are the same. (觀點或興趣) 一致","examples":["The kids' views on life don't always coincide, but they're not afraid of voicing their opinions. 孩子們的生活觀未必總是一致，但是他們不怕表達自己的觀點。"]}]}]},"commemorate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"紀念，用以紀念"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>commemorate</b> an important event or person means to remember them by means of a special action, ceremony, or specially created object. 紀念","examples":["One room contained a gallery of paintings commemorating great moments in baseball history. 有一間房間裡有一個畫廊，陳列著紀念棒球史上偉大時刻的繪畫作品。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"紀念","examples":["...a march in commemoration of Malcolm X. …一次為紀念馬爾科姆·艾克斯而舉行的遊行。"]}]}]},"certify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"證明，證實；給……頒發合格證書；證明（某人）患有精神病；保證"}],"sections":[]},"commence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始，著手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>commences</b> or you <b>commence</b> it, it begins. 使…開始; 開始","examples":["The academic year commences at the beginning of October. 該學年於10月初開始。","They commenced a systematic search. 他們開始了系統的搜查。"]}]}]},"compile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"彙編，編纂；編譯（電腦程式）；收集，蒐集（資訊，資料）；累積（得分）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>compile</b> something such as a report, book, or programme, you produce it by collecting and putting together many pieces of information. 彙編; 彙集","examples":["The book took 10 years to compile. 這本書花了10年編寫。"]}]}]},"confer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"授予，賦予；商討，交換意見"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>confer</b> <b>with</b> someone, you discuss something with them in order to make a decision. You can also say that two people <b>confer</b>. 商議","examples":["He conferred with Hill and the others in his office. 他和希爾以及他辦公室裡的其他人進行了商議。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>confer</b> something such as power or an honour <b>on</b> someone means to give it to them. 授予","examples":["The constitution also confers large powers on Brazil's 25 constituent states. 憲法還授予巴西25個成員州極大的權力。"]}]}]},"compensate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"賠償，償付；彌補，補償；抵消；酬報（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>compensate</b> someone <b>for</b> money or things that they have lost, means to pay them money or give them something to replace those things. 補償 (損失)","examples":["The damages are designed to compensate victims for their direct losses. 該賠償金是用來補償受害人的直接損失的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>compensate</b> <b>for</b> a lack of something or <b>for</b> something you have done wrong, you do something to make the situation better. 彌補 (過失)","examples":["The company agreed to keep up high levels of output in order to compensate for supplies lost. 該公司同意保持高產出水平以補償損失掉的供應品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>compensates for</b> something else balances it or reduces its effects. 抵消","examples":["Senators say it is crucial that a mechanism is found to compensate for inflation. 參議員們說找到抵消通貨膨脹的機制是至關重要的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you try to <b>compensate</b> <b>for</b> something that is wrong or missing in your life, you try to do something that removes or reduces the harmful effects. 彌補","examples":["Their sense of humour and ability to get along with people are two characteristics that compensate for their lack of experience. 他們的幽默感和與人相處的能力是彌補他們經驗不足的兩個特質。"]}]}]},"condense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"冷凝，凝結；壓縮，簡縮；濃縮，變濃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>condense</b> something, especially a piece of writing or a speech, you make it shorter, usually by including only the most important parts. 簡縮 (尤指文章、演講稿)","examples":["When you summarize, you condense an extended idea or argument into a sentence or more in your own words. 總結的時候，用自己的話把拓展了的觀念或論據簡縮成一句或幾句話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a gas or vapour <b>condenses</b>, or <b>is condensed</b>, it changes into a liquid. (氣體、蒸汽) 冷凝","examples":["Water vapour condenses to form clouds. 水蒸汽冷凝形成雲。"]}]}]},"concede":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（通常指不情願地）承認；認（輸），承認（失敗）；授予，讓與；讓對手得分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>concede</b> something, you admit, often unwillingly, that it is true or correct. (常指不情願地) 承認","examples":["Bess finally conceded that Nancy was right. 貝絲最終承認南希是對的。","\"Well,\" he conceded, \"I do sometimes mumble a bit.\" “嗯，”他承認道，“我有時說話確實有點兒含糊。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>concede</b> something <b>to</b> someone, you allow them to have it as a right or privilege. 給予 (權利或特權)","examples":["Poland's Communist government conceded the right to establish independent trade unions. 波蘭共產黨政府給予了建立獨立工會的權力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>concede</b> something, you give it to the person who has been trying to get it from you. 讓與","examples":["The strike by bank employees ended after employers conceded some of their demands. 銀行僱員的罷工在僱主們答應了他們的一些要求之後停止了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>concede</b> a game, contest, or argument, you end it by admitting that you can no longer win. (透過認輸而) 使 (比賽、競賽、爭論等) 結束","examples":["Reiner, 56, has all but conceded the race to his rival. 56歲的賴納差一點就向他的對手認輸而使比賽結束。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>concede</b> defeat, you accept that you have lost a struggle. 承認 (失敗)","examples":["She has conceded defeat in her bid for the Democratic Party's nomination for governor. 她已經承認自己在民主黨州長提名競選中失敗。"]}]}]},"conform":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遵守，符合；順從，隨潮流；一致，相吻合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>conforms</b> <b>to</b> something such as a law or someone's wishes, it is of the required type or quality. (與法律、願望等) 相符合","examples":["The lamp has been designed to conform to new safety standards. 該燈設計得符合新的安全標準。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>conform</b>, you behave in the way that you are expected or supposed to behave. 守規矩","examples":["Many children who can't or don't conform are bullied. 許多無法或不願迎合常規的孩子，往往會受到欺負。"]}]}]},"covet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"貪求，覬覦；<正式>貪求，覬覦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>covet</b> something, you strongly want to have it for yourself. 對…垂涎三尺","examples":["She coveted his job so openly that their conversations were tense. 她如此公開地對他的工作垂涎三尺，以至兩人之間的談話很緊張。"]}]}]},"comprise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包括，包含；構成，組成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>comprises</b> or <b>is comprised of</b> a number of things or people, you mean it has them as its parts or members. 包含; 由…組成","examples":["The special cabinet committee comprises Mr. Brown, Mr. Mandelson, and Mr. Straw. 這一特殊內閣委員會包括布朗先生、曼德爾森先生和斯特勞先生。","The task force is comprised of congressional leaders, cabinet heads and administration officials. 該任務隊由國會領導人、內閣首腦和行政官員構成。"]}]}]},"contradict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"反駁，否認；相牴觸，相矛盾；發生矛盾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>contradict</b> someone, you tell them that what they have just said is wrong, or suggest that it is wrong by saying something different. 反駁","examples":["She dared not contradict him. 她不敢反駁他。","His comments appeared to contradict remarks made earlier in the day by the chairman. 他的評論好像在反駁主席當天早些時候的言論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one statement or piece of evidence <b>contradicts</b> another, the first one makes the second one appear to be wrong. 與…矛盾","examples":["Her version contradicted her daughter's. 她的說法與她女兒的說法相矛盾。"]}]}]},"deem":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"認為，相信"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is deemed</b> <b>to</b> have a particular quality or <b>to</b> do a particular thing, it is considered to have that quality or do that thing. 認為; 相信","examples":["French and German were deemed essential. 法語和德語被認為是必需的。","He says he would support the use of force if the UN deemed it necessary. 他說如果聯合國認為有必要，他就支援動用武力。"]}]}]},"cultivate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開墾，耕作；栽培，培育；陶冶，培養；建立（友誼），結交"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cultivate</b> land or crops, you prepare land and grow crops on it. 開墾; 種植","examples":["She also cultivated a small garden of her own. 她還開墾了一個自己的小花園。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>cultivate</b> an attitude, image, or skill, you try hard to develop it and make it stronger or better. 培養 (態度、技巧等); 樹立 (形象、觀念等)","examples":["He has written eight books and has cultivated the image of an elder statesman. 他已寫了8本書，並樹立了一個政界元老的形象。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>cultivate</b> someone or <b>cultivate</b> a friendship with them, you try hard to develop a friendship with them. 建立 (友誼)","examples":["Howe carefully cultivated Daniel C. Roper, the Assistant Postmaster General. 豪精心與郵政助理部長丹尼爾·C·羅珀拉關係。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"開墾; 種植","examples":["...the cultivation of fruits and vegetables. …水果蔬菜的種植。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"培養; 樹立","examples":["...the cultivation of a positive approach to life and health. …積極的生活和健康觀的樹立。"]}]}]},"dedicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"致力於，獻身於；把（書、戲劇、音樂作品等）獻給；為（建築物或教堂）舉行奉獻（或落成）典禮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has dedicated</b> themselves <b>to</b> something, you approve of the fact that they have decided to give a lot of time and effort to it because they think that it is important. 投身","examples":["For the next few years, she dedicated herself to her work. 隨後的幾年裡，她全身心地投入工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>dedicates</b> something such as a book, play, or piece of music <b>to</b> you, they mention your name, for example, in the front of a book or when a piece of music is performed, as a way of showing affection or respect for you. (把創作品) 獻給","examples":["She dedicated her first album to Woody Allen, who she says understands her obsession. 她把她的第一張唱片獻給伍迪·艾倫，她說艾倫理解她的痴迷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"投身於…的","examples":["He's quite dedicated to his students. 他奉獻很多給他的學生們。"]}]}]},"degrade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"侮辱，貶低；降低，削弱（尤指質量）；降解，分解；使降級，貶黜；使（岩石）陵削；使（能量）衰變"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that <b>degrades</b> someone causes people to have less respect for them. 使貶低身份; 使有辱人格","examples":["...the notion that pornography degrades women. …色情作品貶低婦女的這種看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>degrade</b> something means to cause it to get worse. 使惡化","examples":["...the ability to meet human needs indefinitely without degrading the environment. …滿足人類無限需求但又不會使環境惡化的能力。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"貶低身份的; 有辱人格的","examples":["Mr. Porter was subjected to a degrading strip search. 波特先生受到了有辱人格的脫衣搜身。"]}]}]},"denounce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"譴責，痛斥；檢舉，告發"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>denounce</b> a person or an action, you criticize them severely and publicly because you feel strongly that they are wrong or evil. 譴責","examples":["German leaders all took the opportunity to denounce the attacks and plead for tolerance. 德國領導人們都藉此機會譴責這些攻擊，並且懇請寬容。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>denounce</b> someone who has broken a rule or law, you report them to the authorities. 告發","examples":["They were at the mercy of informers who might at any moment denounce them. 他們完全受那些隨時可能告發他們的告密者的支配。"]}]}]},"deliberate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"故意的，蓄意的；從容的，小心翼翼的；深思熟慮的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細考慮，認真商討"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something that is <b>deliberate</b>, you planned or decided to do it beforehand, and so it happens on purpose rather than by chance. 故意的","examples":["Witnesses say the firing was deliberate and sustained. 目擊者說這次射擊是蓄意的，而且還持續了一段時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a movement or action is <b>deliberate</b>, it is done slowly and carefully. 從容謹慎的","examples":["...stepping with deliberate slowness up the steep paths. …小心翼翼地緩步走上陡峭的小徑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"故意地","examples":["It looks as if the blaze was started deliberately. 看來那場火是有人故意放的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"從容謹慎地","examples":["The Japanese have acted calmly and deliberately. 那些日本人表現得鎮定且從容。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deliberate</b>, you think about something carefully, especially before making a very important decision. 仔細考慮","examples":["She deliberated over the decision for a good few years before she finally made up her mind. 在她最終下定決心之前，她仔細考慮了這個決定多年。"]}]}]},"deprive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"剝奪，使喪失；免去……的職務（尤指聖職）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deprive</b> someone <b>of</b> something that they want or need, you take it away from them, or you prevent them from having it. 剝奪; 使不能有","examples":["They've been deprived of the fuel necessary to heat their homes. 他們無法得到住房取暖必需的燃料。"]}]}]},"depict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"描述，描繪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>depict</b> someone or something means to show or represent them in a work of art such as a drawing or painting. 描繪","examples":["...a gallery of pictures depicting Lee's most famous battles. …一批描繪李的最著名戰役的圖畫。"]}]}]},"derive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"獲得，取得；起源於，來自；提取，衍生（化學物質）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>derive</b> something such as pleasure or benefit <b>from</b> a person or from something, you get it from them. 獲得","examples":["Mr. Ying is one of those happy people who derive pleasure from helping others. 英先生是那種助人為樂的快活人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a word or feeling <b>derives</b> or <b>is derived from</b> something else, you mean that it comes from that thing. 衍生","examples":["The name Anastasia is derived from a Greek word meaning \"of the resurrection.\" 阿納斯塔西婭這個名字是從一個意為“復活”的希臘詞語衍生而來的。"]}]}]},"detach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拆下，使分離；脫離，擺脫；派遣，分派"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>detach</b> one thing <b>from</b> another that it is attached to, you remove it. If one thing <b>detaches</b> <b>from</b> another, it becomes separated from it. 拆卸; 分離","examples":["Detach the white part of the application form and keep it for reference only. 取下申請表的白色部分，僅備參考。","They clambered back under the falls to detach the raft from a jagged rock. 他們爬回到瀑布下面以便將卡在鋸齒狀岩石間的小艇拉出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>detach</b> <b>yourself from</b> something, you become less involved in it or less concerned about it than you used to be. 超脫","examples":["It helps them detach themselves from their problems and become more objective. 這幫助他們從自己的問題中超脫出來，變得更加客觀。"]}]}]},"designate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……定名為，把……描述為；任命，指定；標明，標示"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"已當選而尚未上任的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>designate</b> someone or something <b>as</b> a particular thing, you formally give them that description or name. 命名","examples":["...a man interviewed in one of our studies whom we shall designate as E. …一個我們在一項研究中採訪過並會將其命名為E的男人。","There are efforts under way to designate the bridge a historic landmark. 在努力把這座橋定為歷史地標。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>is designated</b> <b>for</b> a particular purpose, it is set aside for that purpose. 指定","examples":["Some of the rooms were designated as offices. 其中一些房間是被指定用作辦公室的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you <b>designate</b> someone <b>as</b> something, you formally choose them to do that particular job. 指派","examples":["Designate someone as the spokesperson. 指派某人為發言人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Designate</b> is used to describe someone who has been formally chosen to do a particular job, but has not yet started doing it. 已任命但未就職的","examples":["Japan's prime minister-designate is completing his cabinet today. 日本即將上任的首相今天將完成他的內閣組建。"]}]}]},"detain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拘留，扣押；耽擱，阻留"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people such as the police <b>detain</b> someone, they keep them in a place under their control. 拘留","examples":["Police have detained two suspects in connection with the attack. 警方拘留了2名與該襲擊事件有關的嫌疑人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>detain</b> someone means to delay them, for example, by talking to them. 耽擱","examples":["Millson stood up. \"Thank you. We won't detain you any further, Mrs. Stebbing.\" 米爾森站起來。“謝謝您。我們不再耽擱您了，斯特賓太太。”"]}]}]},"deter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使打消念頭，防止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>deter</b> someone <b>from</b> doing something means to make them not want to do it or continue doing it. 阻止","examples":["Supporters of the death penalty argue that it would deter criminals from carrying guns. 死刑的支持者辯稱，死刑可以阻止罪犯攜帶槍支。"]}]}]},"descend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"下來，下降；下傾，下斜；降臨，來臨；（情緒、氣氛等）籠罩；突然到來，突然造訪；降低身份，墮落；衰落，陷入；遺傳"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>descend</b> or if you <b>descend</b> a staircase, you move downward from a higher to a lower level. 下 (樓梯等); 下來","examples":["Things are cooler and more damp as we descend to the cellar. 我們往地窖中下得越深，裡面就越冷、越潮溼。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a large group of people arrive to see you, especially if their visit is unexpected or causes you a lot of work, you can say that they <b>have descended</b> <b>on</b> you. 突然到訪","examples":["Some 3,000 city officials will descend on Capitol Hill on Tuesday to lobby for more money. 大約三千名市政官員將於週二突訪美國國會山，為爭取更多經費遊說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you want to emphasize that the situation that someone is entering is very bad, you can say that they <b>are descending into</b> that situation. 陷入","examples":["He was ultimately overthrown and the country descended into chaos. 他最終被推翻，國家陷入了混亂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>descends to</b> behaviour which you consider unacceptable, you are expressing your disapproval of the fact that they do it. 墮落","examples":["We're not going to descend to such methods. 我們不會墮落到使用這些方式的份上。"]}]}]},"devalue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使貶值，降低……的價值；貶低，降低……的重要性"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（貨幣、資產等）貶值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>devalue</b> something means to cause it to be thought less impressive or less deserving of respect. 貶低","examples":["They spread tales about her in an attempt to devalue her work. 他們散佈關於她的傳聞，企圖貶低她的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>devalue</b> the currency of a country means to reduce its value in relation to other currencies. 使貶值","examples":["India has devalued the rupee by about eleven percent. 印度已經使盧比貶值約11%。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"貶值","examples":["It will lead to devaluation of a number of currencies. 這將導致多種貨幣的貶值。"]}]}]},"deteriorate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"惡化，變壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>deteriorates</b>, it becomes worse in some way. 惡化","examples":["There are fears that the situation might deteriorate into full-scale war. 人們擔心局勢會惡化為全面戰爭。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"惡化","examples":["...concern about the rapid deterioration in relations between the two countries. …對兩國關係迅速惡化的擔憂。"]}]}]},"diagnose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"診斷（病症）；找出原因"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is diagnosed</b> <b>as</b> having a particular illness or problem, their illness or problem is identified. If an illness or problem <b>is diagnosed</b>, it is identified. 診斷","examples":["The soldiers were diagnosed as having flu. 這些士兵被診斷為患了流感。","Susan had a mental breakdown and was diagnosed with schizophrenia. 蘇珊精神崩潰，被診斷為精神分裂。"]}]}]},"dictate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"命令，規定；影響，支配；口述，使聽寫"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"命令，規定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dictate</b> something, you say or read it aloud for someone else to write down. 口授; 使聽寫","examples":["Sheldon writes every day of the week, dictating his novels in the morning. 謝爾登每天都進行創作，在上午口述他的小說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>dictates</b> <b>to</b> someone else, they tell them what they should do or can do. 指示; 命令","examples":["What right has one country to dictate the environmental standards of another? 一個國家有什麼權利規定另一個國家的環境標準？","What gives them the right to dictate to us what we should eat? 是什麼給他們權利來規定我們該吃什麼？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If one thing <b>dictates</b> another, the first thing causes or influences the second thing. 導致; 影響","examples":["The film's budget dictated a tough schedule. 該影片的預算決定了緊張的拍攝進度。","Of course, a number of factors will dictate how long an apple tree can survive. 當然，一棵蘋果樹能存活多久是由許多因素決定的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You say that logic or common sense <b>dictates</b> <b>that</b> a particular thing is the case when you believe strongly that it is the case and that logic or common sense will cause other people to agree. (邏輯或常識) 使人相信","examples":["Logic dictates that our ancestors could not have held a yearly festival until they figured what a year was. 依照邏輯推論，我們的祖先在弄清1年是什麼意思之前，不可能舉行過每年一度的節慶。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dictates</b> are principles or rules which you consider to be extremely important. 原則; 規定","examples":["We have followed the dictates of our consciences and have done our duty. 我們憑良心做事，盡了我們的職責。"]}]}]},"differentiate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使不同；求……的微分；區別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>differentiate</b> <b>between</b> things or if you <b>differentiate</b> one thing <b>from</b> another, you recognize or show the difference between them. 區分","examples":["A child may not differentiate between his imagination and the real world. 孩子也許無法區分想像與真實世界的差別。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A quality or feature that <b>differentiates</b> one thing <b>from</b> another makes the two things different. 使有差別","examples":["...distinctive policies that differentiate them from the other parties. …使他們與其他政黨區別開來的獨特政策。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"差別","examples":["For about six or seven weeks after conception, there is no differentiation between male and female. 在受精後大約六七個星期時，男性和女性胚胎之間沒有什麼差別。"]}]}]},"disperse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"分散，散佈；疏散，驅散；使（光）色散"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"分散的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>disperses</b> or when you <b>disperse</b> it, it spreads over a wide area. 使分散; 擴散","examples":["The oil appeared to be dispersing. 油看上去正在擴散。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a group of people <b>disperses</b> or when someone <b>disperses</b> them, the group splits up and the people leave in different directions. 驅散; 散開","examples":["Police fired shots and used tear gas to disperse the demonstrators. 警察開槍並使用了催淚瓦斯來驅散示威人群。"]}]}]},"disclose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"透露，公開；揭開，使顯露"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disclose</b> new or secret information, you tell people about it. 透露","examples":["Neither side would disclose details of the transaction. 雙方都不會透露交易的細節。"]}]}]},"disapprove":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"不贊成，反對；不批准，否決"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disapprove</b> <b>of</b> something or someone, you feel or show that you do not like them or do not approve of them. 不贊同; 不喜歡","examples":["Most people disapprove of such violent tactics. 多數人不贊同這類暴力手段。"]}]}]},"dismantle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拆開，拆卸；廢除，取消；去掉……的覆蓋物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dismantle</b> a machine or structure, you carefully separate it into its different parts. 拆除","examples":["He asked for immediate help from the United States to dismantle the warheads. 他向美國請求即時援助，拆除彈頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>dismantle</b> an organization or system means to cause it to stop functioning by gradually reducing its power or purpose. 逐步廢除","examples":["Public services of all kinds are being dismantled. 各種公共服務正被逐步廢除。"]}]}]},"disable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使喪失能力，使傷殘；使無效，使不能運轉；使無資格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an injury or illness <b>disables</b> someone, it affects them so badly that it restricts the way that they can live their life. 使傷殘","examples":["She did all this tendon damage and it really disabled her. 她肌腱受了這麼多損傷，這真地使她致殘了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>disables</b> a system or mechanism, they stop it from working, usually temporarily. 使 (系統、機制等) 癱瘓","examples":["...if you need to disable a car alarm. …如果你要使汽車警報器失靈。"]}]}]},"diminish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"減弱，降低，減少；貶低，輕視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>diminishes</b>, or when something <b>diminishes</b> it, it becomes reduced in size, importance, or intensity. 使減少; 變少","examples":["The threat of nuclear war has diminished. 核戰的威脅變小了。","Federalism is intended to diminish the power of the central state. 聯邦制度旨在削弱中央政府的權力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>diminish</b> someone or something, you talk about them or treat them in a way that makes them appear less important than they really are. 貶低","examples":["He never put her down or diminished her. 他從未輕視過她或貶低過她。"]}]}]},"displease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使生氣，觸怒"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"使生氣，使不快"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>displeases</b> you, they make you annoyed or rather angry. 冒犯","examples":["Not wishing to displease her, he avoided answering the question. 由於不想對她有所冒犯，他迴避了這個問題。"]}]}]},"displace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"取代，代替；使（人或動物群體）離開家園；移動，轉移"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>displaces</b> another, it forces the other thing out of its place, position, or role, and then occupies that place, position, or role itself. 取代","examples":["These factories have displaced tourism as the country's largest source of foreign exchange. 這些工廠已經取代了旅遊業而成為該國最大的外匯來源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or group of people <b>is displaced</b>, they are forced to move away from the area where they live. 使背井離鄉","examples":["More than 600,000 people were displaced by the tsunami. 超過60萬人被海嘯搞得背井離鄉。"]}]}]},"dissuade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"勸阻，勸止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dissuade</b> someone <b>from</b> doing or believing something, you persuade them not to do or believe it. 勸阻","examples":["Doctors had tried to dissuade patients from smoking. 醫生曾試圖說服病人不要抽菸。","She steadfastly maintained that her grandsons were innocent, and nothing could dissuade her from that belief. 她始終堅持她的孫子們是無辜的，沒有什麼能改變她的這一信念。"]}]}]},"diversify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）多樣化，（使）不同；擴大經營範圍，增加……的品種；（投資）多元化；null"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an organization or person <b>diversifies</b> into other things, or <b>diversifies</b> their product line, they increase the variety of things that they do or make. 使多樣化","examples":["The company's troubles started only when it diversified into new products. 該公司的麻煩從實現產品多樣化時才開始。","As demand has increased, so manufacturers have been encouraged to diversify and improve quality. 製造商們受需求增加的刺激而擴大生產品種，提高產品質量。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"多樣化","examples":["The seminar was to discuss diversification of agriculture. 該研討會討論的是農業多種經營。"]}]}]},"distort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扭曲，使失真；歪曲，曲解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>distort</b> a statement, fact, or idea, you report or represent it in an untrue way. 歪曲; 曲解","examples":["The media distorts reality; it categorizes people as all good or all bad. 媒體歪曲事實，將人分為十足的好人和壞蛋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something you can see or hear <b>is distorted</b> or <b>distorts</b>, its appearance or sound is changed so that it seems unclear. 扭曲; 失真","examples":["A painter may exaggerate or distort shapes and forms. 畫家可能會誇大或扭曲形狀與形式。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"扭曲的","examples":["These figures give a distorted view of the significance for the local economy. 這些資料對當地經濟的重要性給出了歪曲的看法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"扭曲的; 失真的","examples":["Sound was becoming more and more distorted through the use of hearing aids. 由於使用助聽器，聲音變得越來越失真。"]}]}]},"distract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使分心，使轉移注意力；<古>使困惑，使迷惑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>distracts</b> you or your attention <b>from</b> something, it takes your attention away from it. 分散 (注意力); 使分心","examples":["Tom admits that playing video games sometimes distracts him from his homework. 湯姆承認玩電子遊戲有時讓他做家庭作業時分心。","Don't let yourself be distracted by fashionable theories. 別讓自己被新潮的理論給分心了。"]}]}]},"donate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"捐贈，贈送；獻（血），捐獻（器官）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>donate</b> something <b>to</b> a charity or other organization, you give it to them. 捐贈","examples":["He frequently donates large sums to charity. 他經常向慈善機構大筆捐款。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>donate</b> your blood or a part of your body, you allow doctors to use it to help someone who is ill. 捐獻","examples":["...people who are willing to donate their organs for use after death. …願意在死後捐獻器官的人。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"捐贈","examples":["...the donation of his collection to the art gallery. …他向藝術館所做的收藏品捐贈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"捐獻","examples":["...measures aimed at encouraging organ donation. …旨在鼓勵器官捐獻的措施。"]}]}]},"dissolve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解散，解除；消失；（以化學手段）除去，分散；（使）溶解"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電影中）（畫面的）疊化，淡入淡出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a substance <b>dissolves</b> in liquid or if you <b>dissolve</b> it, it becomes mixed with the liquid and disappears. 使溶解; 溶解","examples":["Heat gently until the sugar dissolves. 微微加熱直到糖溶解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When an organization or institution <b>is dissolved</b>, it is officially ended or broken up. 解散 (組織或機構)","examples":["The committee has been dissolved. 委員會被解散了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a parliament <b>is dissolved</b>, it is formally ended, so that elections for a new parliament can be held. 解散 (議會)","examples":["The present assembly will be dissolved on April 30th. 本屆議會將於4月30日解散。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a marriage or business arrangement <b>is dissolved</b>, it is officially ended. 解除 (婚姻關係或業務協議)","examples":["The marriage was dissolved in 1976. 那樁婚姻在1976年被解除了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something such as a problem or feeling <b>dissolves</b> or <b>is dissolved</b>, it becomes weaker and disappears. 使消失; 消失","examples":["His new-found optimism dissolved. 他剛剛建立的樂觀情緒消失了。"]}]}]},"emigrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"移居外國，移民；迫使（或幫助）……移居外國"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>emigrate</b>, you leave your own country to live in another country. 移居外國","examples":["He emigrated to Belgium. 他移民去了比利時。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"移居外國","examples":["...the huge emigration of workers to the West. …工人們的大規模向西方移居。"]}]}]},"embark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"上船，上飛機；著手，開始（新的或艱難的事情）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>embark</b> <b>on</b> something new, difficult, or exciting, you start doing it. 開始從事","examples":["He's embarking on a new career as a writer. 他正開始一個當作家的新生涯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>embarks</b> <b>on</b> a ship, they go on board before the start of a journey. 登上 (船)","examples":["They embarked on a ship bound for Europe. 他們登上了一艘去歐洲的船。"]}]}]},"divert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使轉向，使繞道；分散，轉移；娛樂，供消遣；轉接（電話）；改變（資金、材料等）的用途"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>divert</b> vehicles or travellers means to make them follow a different route or go to a different destination than they originally intended. You can also say that someone or something <b>diverts</b> <b>from</b> a particular route or <b>to</b> a particular place. 使改道; 改道","examples":["We diverted a plane to rescue 100 passengers. 我們改變飛機航線以拯救100名乘客。","Abington Memorial Hospital has been diverting trauma patients to other hospitals because it does not have enough surgeons. 由於缺乏足夠的外科醫生，阿賓頓紀念醫院一直在將外傷病人轉到其他醫院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>divert</b> money or resources means to cause them to be used for a different purpose. 轉移","examples":["A wave of deadly bombings has forced the United States to divert funds from reconstruction to security. 一系列致命的炸彈襲擊迫使美國將資金從重建轉向安全防禦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>divert</b> a phone call means to send it to a different number or place from the one that was dialled by the person making the call. 轉接 (電話)","examples":["He instructed the switchboard staff to divert all Laura's calls to him. 他通知接線員把勞拉打來的所有電話都轉給他。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>diverts</b> your attention from something important or serious, you disapprove of them behaving or talking in a way that stops you thinking about it. 轉移…的注意力","examples":["They want to divert the attention of the people from the real issues. 他們想把人民的注意力從真正的問題上轉移開。"]}]}]},"enact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"制定，透過，頒佈（法令）；扮演，表演；使發生，付諸實際"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a government or authority <b>enacts</b> a proposal, they make it into a law. 透過","examples":["The authorities have failed so far to enact a law allowing unrestricted emigration. 當局到目前為止還未能透過一項允許自由移民出境的法律。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>enact</b> a story or play, they perform it by acting. 表演.","examples":["She often enacted the stories told to her by her father. 她經常把父親講給她的故事表演出來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a particular event or situation <b>is enacted</b>, it happens; used especially to talk about something that has happened before. 發生 (尤指過去已發生的事件或情況)","examples":["It was a scene enacted month after month for eight years. 這是8年來月復一月出現的場景。"]}]}]},"enhance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"增強，提高，改善"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>enhance</b> something means to improve its value, quality, or attractiveness. 提高","examples":["The White House is eager to protect and enhance that reputation. 白宮急於保護並提高那聲望。"]}]}]},"enlighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"闡明，指導；教導，啟迪；<古>照耀，照亮（物體）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>enlighten</b> someone means to give them more knowledge and greater understanding about something. 啟迪","examples":["A few dedicated doctors have fought for years to enlighten the profession. 少數富有獻身精神的醫生為啟蒙這一行業而奮鬥多年。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"具有啟發性的","examples":["...an enlightening talk on the work done at the zoo. …一段關於動物園工作的具有啟發性的講話。"]}]}]},"exert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"運用，施加（影響）；努力，盡力（exert oneself）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>exerts</b> influence, authority, or pressure, they use it in a strong or determined way, especially in order to produce a particular effect. 施加 (影響、壓力); 運用 (權威)","examples":["He exerted considerable influence on the thinking of the scientific community on these issues. 他對科學界在這些問題上的思考施加了相當大的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>exert</b> <b>yourself</b>, you make a great physical or mental effort, or work hard to do something. 耗費 (自己的精力)","examples":["Do not exert yourself unnecessarily. 不要無謂地耗費自己的精力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"耗費","examples":["He clearly found the physical exertion exhilarating. 他明顯發現體力消耗令人愉悅。"]}]}]},"enrich":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使充實，使豐富；使富裕，使富有；使（土壤）肥沃；濃縮（核燃料中的原子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>enrich</b> something means to improve its quality, usually by adding something to it. 充實; 豐富","examples":["It is important to enrich the soil prior to planting. 栽種之前給土壤施肥很重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>enrich</b> someone means to increase the amount of money that they have. 使富裕","examples":["He will drain, rather than enrich, the country. 他將耗盡而不是增加國家的財富。"]}]}]},"escalate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變得嚴重，（使）升級；迅速增加，迅速增長；逐步增強，逐步升高"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a bad situation <b>escalates</b> or if someone or something <b>escalates</b> it, it becomes greater in size, seriousness, or intensity. 使…加劇; 加劇","examples":["Both unions and management fear the dispute could escalate. 各工會與資方都害怕爭端會加劇。","The protests escalated into five days of rioting. 抗議逐漸升級為5天的暴亂。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"加劇","examples":["The threat of nuclear escalation remains. 核升級的威脅依然存在。"]}]}]},"evacuate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（把人從危險的地方）疏散，撤離；（從危險的地方）搬出，撤空；（用泵等）抽出，抽空；排洩（糞便等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>evacuate</b> someone means to send them to a place of safety, away from a dangerous building, town, or area. 疏散; 使…撤離","examples":["They were planning to evacuate the seventy American officials still in the country. 他們當時在計劃將仍在那個國家的70位美國官員撤離。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>evacuate</b> a place, they move out of it for a period of time, especially because it is dangerous. (尤指因為危險而) 撤離","examples":["The fire is threatening about sixty homes, and residents have evacuated the area. 這場大火威脅著約六十個家庭，居民已經撤離了該地區。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"疏散; 撤離","examples":["...the evacuation of the sick and wounded. …傷病員的撤離。","An evacuation of the city's four-million inhabitants is planned for later this week. 該市400萬居民的撤離計劃本週晚些時候進行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"撤離","examples":["...the mass evacuation of the Bosnian town of Srebrenica. …波斯尼亞的斯雷布雷尼察鎮大撤離。"]}]}]},"expel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……開除（或除名）；驅逐；排出（空氣、水、氣體等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is expelled</b> <b>from</b> a school or organization, they are officially told to leave because they have behaved badly. 開除","examples":["More than five-thousand high school students have been expelled for cheating. 五千多名中學生因考試作弊而被開除。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>are expelled</b> <b>from</b> a place, they are made to leave it, often by force. 逐出","examples":["An American academic was expelled from the country yesterday. 一名美國學者昨天被逐出該國。","They were told that they should expel the refugees. 他們被告知應該逐出那些難民。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>expel</b> something means to force it out from a container or from your body. 排出","examples":["As the lungs exhale this waste, gas is expelled into the atmosphere. 當肺撥出這股廢氣，氣體就被排到空氣中。"]}]}]},"evolve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"進化，演化；逐步發展，逐漸演變"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When animals or plants <b>evolve</b>, they gradually change and develop into different forms. 進化","examples":["The bright plumage of many male birds was thought to have evolved to attract females. 許多雄鳥的鮮豔羽毛被認為是為吸引雌鳥而進化來的。","Birds are widely believed to have evolved from dinosaurs. 鳥類普遍被認為是從恐龍進化而來的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>evolves</b> or you <b>evolve</b> it, it gradually develops over a period of time into something different and usually more advanced. 使…逐步發展; 逐步發展","examples":["...a tiny airline which eventually evolved into Pakistan International Airlines. …最終發展成為巴基斯坦國際航空公司的一家小型航空公司。","Popular music evolved from folk songs. 流行音樂由民歌演變而來。"]}]}]},"expire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"到期，失效；死亡；呼氣，吐氣；（任期）屆滿"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as a contract, deadline, or visa <b>expires</b>, it comes to an end or is no longer valid. 到期; 失效","examples":["He had lived illegally in the United States for five years after his visitor's visa expired. 訪問簽證到期後他在美國非法居住了5年。"]}]}]},"facilitate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使更容易，使便利；促進，推動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>facilitate</b> an action or process, especially one that you would like to happen, means to make it easier or more likely to happen. 促進","examples":["The new airport will facilitate the development of tourism. 新機場將促進旅遊業的發展。"]}]}]},"forsake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"拋棄，離開（尤指不履行責任)；摒棄，離開（尤指喜愛的事物）；離開，告別（某地）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>forsake</b> someone, you leave them when you should have stayed, or you stop helping them or looking after them. 離棄","examples":["I still love him and I would never forsake him. 我仍然愛他，我永遠不會離棄他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>forsake</b> something, you stop doing it, using it, or having it. 放棄","examples":["He doubted their claim to have forsaken military solutions to the civil war. 他對他們聲稱已經放棄以軍事手段解決內戰的說法有懷疑。"]}]}]},"foresee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"預見，預知"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>foresee</b> something, you expect and believe that it will happen. 預見","examples":["He did not foresee any problems. 他沒有預見到任何問題。"]}]}]},"erode":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"侵蝕，腐蝕；削弱，降低"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If rock or soil <b>erodes</b> or <b>is eroded</b> by the weather, sea, or wind, it cracks and breaks so that it is gradually destroyed. 侵蝕","examples":["The storm washed away buildings and roads and eroded beaches. 暴風雨沖走了建築物和道路，侵蝕了沙灘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's authority, right, or confidence <b>erodes</b> or <b>is eroded</b>, it is gradually destroyed or removed. 削弱","examples":["His critics say his fumbling on the issue of reform has eroded his authority. 他的批評者們說他在改革問題上的拙劣做法已削弱了他的權威。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the value of something <b>erodes</b> or <b>is eroded</b> by something such as inflation or age, its value decreases. 降低","examples":["Competition in the financial marketplace has eroded profits. 金融市場的競爭降低了利潤。"]}]}]},"fortify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"築防於，設要塞於；提高（食品）營養價值；使增強體質，使振奮精神；增強（感覺或態度）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>fortify</b> a place means to make it stronger and more difficult to attack, often by building a wall or ditch round it. (常透過築牆、挖溝等) 鞏固 (某地)","examples":["...soldiers working to fortify an airbase in Bahrain. …在鞏固一個在巴林的空軍基地計程車兵們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If food or drink <b>is fortified</b>, another substance is added to it to make it healthier or stronger. (透過新增另一種物質而) 強化 (食品或飲料)","examples":["Choose margarine or butter fortified with vitamin D. 選擇人造黃油或用維生素D強化了的黃油。","All sherry is made from wine fortified with brandy. 所有雪利酒都是由用白蘭地強化了的葡萄酒製成的。"]}]}]},"formulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"制定，規劃；確切表達，認真闡述；用公式表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>formulate</b> something such as a plan or proposal, you invent it, thinking about the details carefully. 構想出 (計劃或提案)","examples":["Little by little, he formulated his plan for escape. 他一點一點地構想出了他的逃跑計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>formulate</b> a thought, opinion, or idea, you express it or describe it using particular words. 用獨特的詞語表述","examples":["I was impressed by the way he could formulate his ideas. 我對他表述自己想法的獨特用詞印象深刻。"]}]}]},"generalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"概括，歸納；推廣，普及；籠統地表達"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>generalize</b>, you say something that seems to be true in most situations or for most people, but that may not be completely true in all cases. 概括","examples":["Critics love to generalize, to formulate trends into which all new work must be fitted, however contradictory. 評論家喜歡概括，歸納出所有新作品都必須符合的趨勢，不管它們是如何地不符。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>generalize</b> something such as an idea, you apply it more widely than its original context, as if it was true in many other situations. 普及","examples":["A child first labels the household pet cat as a \"cat\" and then generalizes this label to other animals that look like it. 孩子先把家養的寵物貓稱為“貓”，然後把這個稱呼擴大到其他看起來像貓的動物。"]}]}]},"foster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"促進，培養；領養，收養"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"代養的，寄養的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Foster</b> parents are people who officially take a child into their family for a period of time, without becoming the child's legal parents. The child is referred to as their <b>foster</b> child. 收養的","examples":["Little Jack was placed with foster parents. 小杰克被安置在養父母家。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>foster</b> a child, you take it into your family for a period of time, without becoming its legal parent. 收養","examples":["She has since gone on to find happiness by fostering more than 100 children. 她此後又透過收養一百多個孩子找到了快樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>foster</b> something such as an activity or idea means to help it to develop. 促進","examples":["He said that developed countries had a responsibility to foster global economic growth to help new democracies. 他說發達國家有一種促進全球經濟增長以幫助新興民主國家的責任。"]}]}]},"generate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"產生，引起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>generate</b> something means to cause it to begin and develop. 造成","examples":["The labour secretary said the reforms would generate new jobs. 勞動部長說這些改革將帶來新的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>generate</b> a form of energy or power means to produce it. 產生 (電等能量)","examples":["The company, New England Electric, burns coal to generate power. 新英格蘭電力公司燃燒煤來發電。"]}]}]},"hospitalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"送入醫院療養（或治療）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is hospitalized</b>, they are sent or admitted to a hospital. 送…住院治療","examples":["Most people do not have to be hospitalized for asthma or pneumonia. 多數人不必因哮喘或肺炎住院。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"住院治療","examples":["Occasionally hospitalization is required to combat dehydration. 治療脫水有時需要住院。"]}]}]},"harass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"騷擾；不斷攻擊（敵人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>harasses</b> you, they trouble or annoy you, for example by attacking you repeatedly or by causing you as many problems as they can. 騷擾","examples":["A woman reporter complained one of them sexually harassed her in the locker room. 一名女記者抱怨說，他們當中的一個在更衣室裡對她進行了性騷擾。"]}]}]},"humiliate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"羞辱，使蒙羞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>humiliate</b> someone means to say or do something which makes them feel ashamed or stupid. 使蒙羞","examples":["She had been beaten and humiliated by her husband. 她曾被丈夫毆打和羞辱。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"感到丟臉的","examples":["I have never felt so humiliated in my life. 我一生中從未感到這麼丟臉過。"]}]}]},"fret":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"煩惱，發愁；（透過摩擦或齧咬）使磨損，使銷蝕；（經侵蝕而）形成（溝，通道）；打著漣漪流動（或移動）；給（絃樂器）裝品；把琴絃壓在音品上演奏（某音）；用回紋裝飾"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（吉他等指板上定音的）品；（從海上飄來的）霧，海霧；煩躁，苦惱，焦急；（藝術，建築）回紋飾；（紋章）鑽石上的回紋飾圖案"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fret</b> about something, you worry about it. 擔心","examples":["I was working all hours and constantly fretting about everyone else's problems. 我一刻不停地工作著，還一直擔心著其他人的問題。","But congressional staffers fret that the project will eventually cost billions more. 但國會的工作人員們擔心這個方案最終會多花幾十億。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>frets</b> on a musical instrument such as a guitar are the raised lines across its neck. (吉他等絃樂器指板上定音的) 音品","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a repetitive geometrical figure, esp one used as an ornamental border 回紋飾","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"sea fret的縮寫","examples":[]}]}]},"hack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"砍，劈；非法侵入（他人計算機系統）；大幅刪改（文章）；<非正式>對付，處理；劈出，開闢（道路）；大聲咳嗽；猛踢；<英>騎馬消遣；在飼草架上放（飼草）；<美，非正式>開計程車"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"僱傭文人，寫手；二流政客，政治僕從；（對他人計算機）侵入；<美，非正式>計程車，計程車司機；砍，劈；可出租的馬；老馬；（大聲的）乾咳；（冰壺運動中溜擲冰壺時作為足部支撐點的）冰槽，起蹬器；劈（或砍、擊）的工具；<古>傷口；（獵鷹）飼鷹板；（曬乳酪等的）曬架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hack</b> something or <b>hack</b> at it, you cut it with strong, rough strokes using a sharp tool such as an axe or a knife. 劈; 砍","examples":["An armed gang barged onto the train and began hacking and shooting anyone in sight. 一夥武裝匪徒衝上火車，開始見人就刀砍槍擊。","Matthew desperately hacked through the leather. 馬修絕望地刺穿了那塊皮革。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>hacks into</b> a computer system, they break into the system, especially in order to get secret information. 侵入 (計算機系統)","examples":["The saboteurs had demanded money in return for revealing how they hacked into the systems. 這些破壞分子要求以錢作交換，才會透露他們是如何侵入該系統的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to ride (a horse) cross-country for pleasure 騎(馬)越野","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to place (fodder) in a hack 在飼草架上放(飼草)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"(計算機系統的) 侵入","examples":["...the common and often illegal art of computer hacking. …那種常見且常為非法的電腦入侵行徑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a politician as a <b>hack</b>, you disapprove of them because they are too loyal to their party and perhaps do not deserve the position they have. 唯命是從的政客","examples":["Far too many party hacks from the old days still hold influential jobs. 太多的老一輩黨僕仍然佔據著有影響力的職位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you refer to a professional writer, such as a journalist, as a <b>hack</b>, you disapprove of them because they write for money without worrying very much about the quality of their writing. (粗製濫造的)職業寫手","examples":["...tabloid hacks, always eager to find victims in order to sell newspapers. …小報寫手，總是為了賣掉報紙而急於找到犧牲品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>hack</b> is the same as a . 同taxi","examples":["I will pay for a hack. There is no need for you to return home on foot. 我會花錢打輛計程車。你沒有必要步行回家。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a horse kept for riding or (more rarely) for driving 乘騎馬","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"a rack used for fodder for livestock 飼料架","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"banal, mediocre, or unoriginal 陳腐的; 平庸的; 無新意的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>can't hack it</b> or <b>couldn't hack it</b>, you mean that they do not or did not have the qualities needed to do a task or cope with a situation. 應付不了它","examples":["You have to be strong and confident, and never give the slightest impression that you can't hack it. 你必須堅強和自信，決不要給人留下絲毫應付不了此事的印象。"]}]}]},"imprison":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"關押，監禁；束縛，限制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is imprisoned</b>, they are locked up or kept somewhere, usually in prison, as a punishment for a crime or for political opposition. 監禁","examples":["He was imprisoned for 18 months on charges of theft. 他因盜竊指控而被監禁了18個月。"]}]}]},"illuminate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"照射，照亮；闡明，解釋；使容光煥發；用彩燈裝飾；用金、銀等彩色圖案裝飾（書稿的書頁或首詞第一個字母）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>illuminate</b> something means to shine light on it and to make it brighter and more visible. 照亮","examples":["No streetlights illuminated the street. 一盞照亮街道的路燈也沒有。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>illuminate</b> something that is unclear or difficult to understand, you make it clearer by explaining it carefully or giving information about it. 闡明","examples":["Instead of formulas and charts, the two instructors use games and drawings to illuminate their subject. 這兩位教師用遊戲和圖畫而不是公式和圖表來闡明他們的題旨。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"富有啟發性的","examples":["It would be illuminating to hear the views of the club vice-chairman. 聽聽俱樂部副主席的觀點或許會有啟發。"]}]}]},"inhabit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"居住於，棲居在；存在於，佔據"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place or region <b>is inhabited</b> by a group of people or a species of animal, those people or animals live there. 居住於","examples":["The valley is inhabited by the Dani tribe. 這個山谷里居住著丹尼部落。","...the people who inhabit these islands. …居住於這些島嶼的人們。"]}]}]},"infer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推斷，推論；暗示，暗指"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>infer</b> that something is the case, you decide that it is true on the basis of information that you already have. 推斷","examples":["I inferred from what she said that you have not been well. 我從她的話裡推斷出你身體一直不大好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some people use <b>infer</b> to mean \"imply,\" but this use is incorrect. 暗指 (一些人用)(infer)(表示)(imply)(的意思，但這種用法是錯誤的)","examples":["The police inferred, though they didn't exactly say it, that they found her behaviour rather suspicious. 警方雖未明說卻暗示他們發現她的行跡相當可疑。"]}]}]},"intimidate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"恫嚇，威脅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>intimidate</b> someone, you deliberately make them frightened enough to do what you want them to do. 恐嚇; 威脅","examples":["Jones had set out to intimidate and dominate Paul. 瓊斯曾試圖威脅並控制保羅。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"威脅","examples":["...an inquiry into allegations of intimidation during last week's vote. …一項對上週選舉期間恐嚇指控的調查。"]}]}]},"intrude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"闖入；打擾，侵擾；（火成岩）侵入（已生成構造）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is intruding</b> <b>into</b> a particular place or situation, you mean that they are not wanted or welcome there. 侵擾","examples":["The press has been blamed for intruding into people's personal lives in an unacceptable way. 新聞媒體因以一種令人無法接受的方式侵入人們的私生活而受到譴責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>intrudes</b> <b>on</b> your mood or your life, it disturbs it or has an unwanted effect on it. 擾亂","examples":["Do you feel anxious when unforeseen incidents intrude on your day? 當無可預料的事件侵擾到你的生活時，你會感到焦慮嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>intrudes</b> <b>into</b> a place, they go there even though they are not allowed to be there. 侵入","examples":["An American officer on the scene said no one had intruded into the space he was defending. 現場的一名美國軍官說還沒有人闖入過他所防衛的區域。"]}]}]},"inject":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"注射；（給……）新增，增加（某品質）；投入（金錢或資源）；（往物質、裝置中）注入或射入（電流、粒子束等）；將（宇宙飛船等）射入軌道（或彈道）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>inject</b> a substance such as a medicine into someone means to put it into their body using a device with a needle called a syringe. 給…注射","examples":["His son was injected with strong drugs. 他的兒子被注射了強效的藥。","The technique consists of injecting healthy cells into the weakened muscles. 這項技術包括把健康細胞注射進衰弱的肌肉裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>inject</b> a new, exciting, or interesting quality <b>into</b> a situation, you add it. 注入; 增添","examples":["She kept trying to inject a little fun into their relationship. 她一直設法給他們的關係增添一點情趣。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>inject</b> money or resources <b>into</b> a business or organization, you provide more money or resources for it. 注入 (資金或資源)","examples":["The insurance fund would inject $750 into the banks. 該保險基金將向銀行投入750美元。"]}]}]},"integrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）合併，成為一體；（使）加入，融入群體；（使）取消種族隔離；求……的積分；表示（面積、溫度等）的總和，表示……的平均值"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"整合的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>integrates</b> into a social group, or <b>is integrated</b> into it, they behave in such a way that they become part of the group or are accepted into it. 使融入; 結合在一起","examples":["He didn't integrate successfully into the Italian way of life. 他沒有成功融入到義大利的生活方式中去。","Integrating the kids with the community is essential. 使孩子們融入這個社群是非常必要的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When races <b>integrate</b> or when schools and organizations <b>are integrated</b>, people who belong to ethnic minorities can join others in their schools and organizations. 使合併; 成為一體","examples":["The Marine Corps was the last service to integrate. 美國海軍陸戰隊是最後合併的部隊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"融合的","examples":["He thinks we are living in a fully integrated, supportive society. 他認為我們生活在一個完全融合、互相幫助的社會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(種族) 融合的","examples":["...a black honour student in Chicago's integrated Lincoln Park High School. …在芝加哥混合種族的林肯公園高中上學的一位黑人優等學生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"整體的","examples":["There is, he said, a lack of an integrated national transportation policy. 他說目前缺乏一個整體的全國運輸政策。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>integrate</b> one thing <b>with</b> another, or one thing <b>integrates</b> <b>with</b> another, the two things become closely linked or form part of a whole idea or system. You can also say that two things <b>integrate</b>. 結合","examples":["Writing about a topic helps you integrate new knowledge with what you already know. 圍繞某一題目寫作有助於你將新知識和已有知識結合起來。","...historic landmarks that integrate with the community. …與社群融為一體的歷史性里程碑。"]}]}]},"kidnap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"綁架，劫持"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"綁架，誘拐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>kidnap</b> someone is to take them away illegally and by force, and usually to hold them prisoner in order to demand something from their family, employer, or government. 綁架","examples":["Police in Brazil uncovered a plot to kidnap him. 巴西警方偵破了一起要綁架他的陰謀。","They were middle-class university students, intelligent and educated, yet they chose to kidnap and kill. 他們是中產階級大學生，聰明而且受過教育，卻選擇了綁架和謀殺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"綁架者","examples":["His kidnappers have threatened that they will kill him unless three militants are released from prison. 綁架者威脅說，如果不釋放3個武裝分子出獄，他們就會殺了他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Kidnap</b> or a <b>kidnap</b> is the crime of taking someone away by force. 綁架","examples":["Stewart denies attempted murder and kidnap. 斯圖爾特否認有謀殺和綁架的企圖。"]}]}]},"intervene":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"干預，干涉；插話，打岔；干擾，阻撓；發生於其間，介於中間；調停，斡旋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>intervene</b> <b>in</b> a situation, you become involved in it and try to change it. 干預","examples":["The situation calmed down when police intervened. 警察干預後，局勢平靜了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>intervene</b>, you interrupt a conversation in order to add something to it. 插話","examples":["Hernandez intervened and told me to stop it. 賀爾南德茲插話，不讓我再說下去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an event <b>intervenes</b>, it happens suddenly in a way that stops, delays, or prevents something from happening. 干擾","examples":["The mailboat arrived on Friday mornings unless bad weather intervened. 除非受到惡劣天氣的干擾，郵船於星期五上午到達。"]}]}]},"irritate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使不耐煩，激怒；刺激（身體某部位），使疼痛；使（生物體、細胞或器官）興奮；引起不愉快"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>irritates</b> you, it keeps annoying you. 激怒","examples":["Their attitude irritates me. 他們的態度激怒了我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>irritates</b> a part of your body, it causes it to itch or become sore. 刺激","examples":["Wear rubber gloves while chopping chillies as they can irritate the skin. 剁辣椒時戴上橡皮手套，因為它們會刺激皮膚。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被激怒的","examples":["Not surprisingly, her teacher is getting irritated with her. 不出所料，她的老師快被她激怒了。"]}]}]},"liberate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解放，解救；使自由，使擺脫約束；偷竊；釋放（氣體、能量等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>liberate</b> a place or the people in it means to free them from the political or military control of another country, area, or group of people. 解放","examples":["They planned to march on and liberate the city. 他們打算繼續前進解放這座城市。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>liberate</b> someone <b>from</b> something means to help them escape from it or overcome it, and lead a better way of life. 使解脫","examples":["He asked how committed the leadership was to liberating its people from poverty. 他問領導層讓人民脫貧的態度有多麼堅決。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"解放","examples":["...a mass liberation movement. …一場大眾解放運動。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"解脫的","examples":["If you have the chance to spill your problems out to a therapist it can be a very liberating experience. 如果有機會向治療專家傾訴問題，那會是一種讓人非常解脫的體驗。"]}]}]},"mar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破壞，損壞"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙點，瑕疵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mar</b> something means to spoil or damage it. 破壞","examples":["A number of problems marred the smooth running of this event. 許多問題破壞了該事件的順利進行。"]}]}]},"legitimate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"正當的，合理的；合法的，依法的；合法婚姻所生的；（君主）有合法王位繼承權的；（與音樂喜劇、滑稽劇相對）正劇的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<美>使合法化，使正當化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>legitimate</b> is acceptable according to the law. 合法的","examples":["The French government has condemned the coup in Haiti and has demanded the restoration of the legitimate government. 法國政府已經譴責了海地的政變，並要求恢復合法政府。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a feeling or claim is <b>legitimate</b>, you think that it is reasonable and justified. 合理的","examples":["That's a perfectly legitimate fear. 那是種完全合乎邏輯的恐懼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合法性","examples":["The opposition parties do not recognize the political legitimacy of his government. 反對黨不承認他的政府的政治合法性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"合理性","examples":["Sampras beat Carl-Uwe Steeb by 6-1, 6-2, 6-1 to underline the legitimacy of his challenge for the title. 桑普拉斯以6比1、6比2和6比1戰勝了卡爾-尤韋·斯蒂布，證明了他挑戰冠軍頭銜的合理性。"]}]}]},"manipulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"操縱，擺佈；操作，使用；正骨，推拿；篡改；巧妙地移動（某物），巧妙地處理（某事）；校正，轉移（儲存在計算機上的資訊）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>manipulates</b> people, you disapprove of them because they skilfully force or persuade people to do what they want. 控制","examples":["She's always borrowing my clothes and manipulating me to give her vast sums of money. 她總是向我借衣服，並控制我，讓我給她大筆的錢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>manipulates</b> an event or situation, you disapprove of them because they use or control it for their own benefit, or cause it to develop in the way they want. 操縱","examples":["She was unable, for once, to control and manipulate events. 她曾一度無法控制和操縱事件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>manipulate</b> something that requires skill, such as a complicated piece of equipment or a difficult idea, you operate it or process it. 操作","examples":["The technology uses a pen to manipulate a computer. 這項技術使用筆來操作計算機。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone <b>manipulates</b> your bones or muscles, they skilfully move and press them with their hands in order to push the bones into their correct position or make the muscles less stiff. 使脫臼復位; 用推拿術治療","examples":["The way he can manipulate my leg has helped my arthritis so much. 他針對我的腿部做的推拿治療對我的關節炎大有幫助。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"控制","examples":["...repeated criticism or manipulation of our minds. …對我們思想的反覆批評或一再控制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"操縱","examples":["...accusations of political manipulation. …對政治操縱的指控。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"操作","examples":["...science that requires only the simplest of mathematical manipulations. …只要求進行最簡單數學運算的科學。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"推拿術","examples":["A permanent cure will only be effected by acupuncture, chiropractic, or manipulation. 只有針灸、按摩或推拿術才能實現永久的治癒。"]}]}]},"meditate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（宗教中）默想，冥想；思考，沉思（meditate on/upon）；暗自策劃，謀劃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>meditate on</b> something, you think about it very carefully and deeply for a long time. 深思","examples":["On the day her son began school, she meditated on the uncertainties of his future. 在她兒子入學那天，她深思了有關他未來的種種不確定因素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>meditate</b> you remain in a silent and calm state for a period of time, as part of a religious training or so that you are more able to deal with the problems and difficulties of everyday life. 冥想","examples":["I was meditating, and reached a higher state of consciousness. 我正在冥想，並進入了一種更高的意識境界。"]}]}]},"mellow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（顏色或光線）柔和的，溫暖的；（聲音）悅耳的，圓潤的；（酒）芳醇的，（水果）成熟香甜的；（性格）穩健的，老練的；悠閒的，怡然自得的；<非正式>（喝酒或吸毒後）輕鬆自在的，飄飄然的；（土壤）肥沃的，富饒的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）變成熟老練，（使）變平易近人；（使）變柔和；（使）（酒）變得芳醇；<美，非正式>（使）變得輕鬆平靜（mellow out）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mellow</b> is used to describe things that have a pleasant, soft, rich colour, usually red, orange, yellow, or brown. 柔和的","examples":["...the softer, mellower light of evening. …傍晚較柔和的燈光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mellow</b> sound or flavour is pleasant, smooth, and rich. (聲音) 柔美的; (味道) 香醇的","examples":["His voice was deep and mellow and his speech had a soothing and comforting quality. 他的嗓音深沉柔美，他的演講令人舒心寬慰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Mellow</b> is also an adjective. 平和的","examples":["Is she more mellow and tolerant? 她更平和、更寬容了嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mellows</b> or if something <b>mellows</b> them, they become kinder or less extreme in their behaviour, especially as a result of growing older. 使變平和; 變平和","examples":["He became a taciturn man, a man not easy to live with. Later, when the older children married and had children of their own, he mellowed a little. 他變成了一個沉默寡言的人、一個不容易相處的人。後來，等大點的孩子們結了婚，也有了他們自己的孩子，他變得平和了些。"]}]}]},"minimize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使減少到最低限度；貶低，使顯得不重要；（尤指在計算機螢幕上）使最小化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>minimize</b> a risk, problem, or unpleasant situation, you reduce it to the lowest possible level, or prevent it from increasing beyond that level. 減到最低數量; 降到最低程度","examples":["Concerned people want to minimize the risk of developing cancer. 憂心忡忡的人們想把患上癌症的風險降到最低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>minimize</b> something, you make it seem smaller or less significant than it really is. 貶低…的重要性","examples":["Some have minimized the importance of ideological factors. 一些人已經貶低了意識形態因素的重要性。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>minimize</b> a window on a computer screen, you make it very small, because you do not want to use it. 使最小化","examples":["Click the square icon again to minimize the window. 再次點選正方形圖示使那個視窗最小化。"]}]}]},"merge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）合併，（使）融合；漸漸消失於，融入；兼併（產權，產業）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>merges</b> <b>with</b> another, or <b>is merged</b> <b>with</b> another, they combine or come together to make one whole thing. You can also say that two things <b>merge</b>, or <b>are merged</b>. 使合併; 合併","examples":["Bank of America merged with a rival bank. 美國銀行和一家競爭銀行合併了。","The rivers merge just north of a vital irrigation system. 這些河流在一個重要的灌溉系統的北部匯合了。","The two countries merged into one. 這兩個國家合二為一了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one sound, colour, or object <b>merges</b> into another, the first changes so gradually into the second that you do not notice the change. 融入","examples":["Like a chameleon, he could merge unobtrusively into the background. 他像變色龍一樣，可以不引人注意地融入背景之中。","His features merged with the darkness. 他的面容融入了黑暗中。"]}]}]},"migrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（候鳥或動物）遷徙；（尤指為找工作）移居，遷移；轉移（從一個部位移到另一部位）；把（程式，硬體）從一系統轉移到另一系統；改用作業系統"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>migrate</b>, they move from one place to another, especially in order to find work or to live somewhere for a short time. 遷移","examples":["People migrate to cities like Jakarta in search of work. 人們移居到雅加達這樣的城市找工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When birds, fish, or animals <b>migrate</b>, they move at a particular season from one part of the world or from one part of a country to another, usually in order to breed or to find new feeding grounds. 遷徙","examples":["Most birds have to fly long distances to migrate. 大多數的鳥類不得不飛行很長的距離進行遷徙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遷移","examples":["...the migration of Soviet Jews to Israel. …蘇聯猶太人向以色列的遷移。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"遷徙","examples":["...the migration of animals in the Serengeti. …塞倫蓋蒂的動物遷徙。"]}]}]},"mobilize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"動員，組織；調動，呼叫；動員（士兵、軍隊等）參戰；幫助（某物更輕鬆地）移動；使流動；使鬆動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mobilize</b> support or <b>mobilize</b> people to do something, you succeed in encouraging people to take action, especially political action. If people <b>mobilize</b>, they prepare to take action. 動員; 動員起來","examples":["The best hope is that we will mobilize international support and get down to action. 最大的希望就是我們將動員國際社會的支援，開始行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mobilize</b> resources, you start to use them or make them available for use. 調動","examples":["If you could mobilize the resources, you could get it done. 如果你能調動資源，你就能完成它。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a country <b>mobilizes</b>, or <b>mobilizes</b> its armed forces, or if its armed forces <b>mobilize</b>, they are given orders to prepare for a conflict. 動員 (軍隊); (國家軍事力量) 動員起來","examples":["Sudan even threatened to mobilize in response to the ultimatums. 蘇丹甚至威脅說要動用軍事力量來回應最後通牒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"動員","examples":["...the rapid mobilization of international opinion in support of the revolution. …對支援革命的國際輿論的迅速動員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"調動","examples":["...the mobilization of resources for education. …調動教育資源。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(軍事) 動員","examples":["...a demand for full-scale mobilization to defend the republic. …全面動員來保衛共和國的命令。"]}]}]},"nourish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"養育，滋養；培養，懷有（感情、信念等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>nourish</b> a person, animal, or plant means to provide them with the food that is necessary for life, growth, and good health. 為…提供營養","examples":["The food she eats nourishes both her and the baby. 她吃的食物為她和嬰兒提供營養。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有營養的","examples":["Most of these nourishing substances are in the yolk of the egg. 這些營養物質大部分在蛋黃裡。"]}]}]},"oblige":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"迫使，責成；施恩惠於，幫……的忙；<古>使（某人）遵守誓約（或承諾、約定）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are obliged</b> <b>to</b> do something, a situation, rule, or law makes it necessary for you to do that thing. 迫使","examples":["The storm got worse and worse. Finally, I was obliged to abandon the car and continue on foot. 暴風雨越來越猛烈。最終，我被迫棄車徒步前行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>oblige</b> someone means to be helpful to them by doing what they have asked you to do. (透過滿足要求而) 幫助","examples":["Mr. Oakley has always been ready to oblige journalists with information. 奧克利先生一直樂於提供資訊幫助記者們。","We called up three economists to ask how to eliminate the deficit and they obliged with very straightforward answers. 我們致電3位經濟學家諮詢消除赤字的方法，他們滿足了我們的要求，給出了非常直接的答覆。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone that you <b>would be obliged</b> or <b>should be obliged</b> if they would do something, you are telling them in a polite but firm way that you want them to do it. (如蒙…) 將不勝感激","examples":["I would be obliged if you could read it to us. 如果你能把它讀給我們聽，我將不勝感激。"]}]}]},"oppress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓迫，欺壓；使壓抑，使煩惱；（紋章）使（圖記）部分模糊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>oppress</b> people means to treat them cruelly, or to prevent them from having the same opportunities, freedom, and benefits as others. 壓迫","examples":["These people often are oppressed by the governments of the countries they find themselves in. 這些人經常受到他們所在國家政府的壓迫。"]}]}]},"outnumber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"數目超過，比……多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one group of people or things <b>outnumbers</b> another, the first group has more people or things in it than the second group. 在數量上超過","examples":["...a town where men outnumber women four to one. …一個男女比例為4比1的城鎮。"]}]}]},"paralyze":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（醫學）使麻痺，使癱瘓；使（組織、系統、活動等）陷於停頓或無法正常運作，或使（人）因恐懼、震驚等而無法行動或思考"}],"sections":[]},"obscure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難以說清楚的，模糊的；鮮為人知的，默默無聞的；未被查實的，不確定的；費解的，晦澀的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"遮掩，遮蔽；使費解"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"某種模糊的或不清楚的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone is <b>obscure</b>, they are unknown, or are known by only a few people. 鮮為人知的","examples":["The origin of the custom is obscure. 該習俗的起源鮮為人知。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>obscure</b> is difficult to understand or deal with, usually because it involves so many parts or details. 複雜難懂的; 難處理的","examples":["The contracts are written in obscure language. 那些合同是用複雜難懂的語言寫的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>obscures</b> another, it prevents it from being seen or heard properly. 遮掩","examples":["Trees obscured his vision; he couldn't see much of the square's southern half. 樹木遮住了他的視線，他不怎麼看得見廣場南半部。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>obscure</b> something means to make it difficult to understand. 使…難懂","examples":["...the jargon that frequently obscures educational writing. …常使教學行文變得複雜難懂的術語。"]}]}]},"originate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"起源，產生；創始，開創"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>originates</b> or when someone <b>originates</b> it, it begins to happen or exist. 始創; 起源","examples":["The disease originated in Africa. 這種疾病起源於非洲。","All carbohydrates originate from plants. 所有的碳水化合物均來源於植物。"]}]}]},"narrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"講（故事），敘述；給（電影、廣播或音樂等）配解說詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>narrate</b> a story, you tell it from your own point of view. 敘述","examples":["The three of them narrate the same events from three perspectives. 他們3個人從3個角度敘述同樣那些事件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The person who <b>narrates</b> a film or programme speaks the words which accompany the pictures, but does not appear in it. 給 (電影或節目) 作解說","examples":["She also narrated a documentary about the Kirov Ballet School. 她還為一部關於基洛夫芭蕾舞學院的記錄片作過解說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"敘述","examples":["Its story-within-a-story method of narration is confusing. 它那故事裡套故事的敘述方法令人迷惑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(電影或節目的) 解說","examples":["As soon as the crew gets back from lunch, we can put your narration on it right away. 工作人員吃過午飯一回來，我們就能馬上把你的解說加在上面。"]}]}]},"peddle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"挨戶銷售，巡迴銷售；販賣（非法毒品，偷竊的贓物）；宣傳，散佈（思想或訊息）；忙於瑣事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who <b>peddles</b> things goes from place to place trying to sell them. 兜售","examples":["His attempts to peddle his paintings around Laramie's tiny gallery scene proved unsuccessful. 他在拉勒米的小畫廊現場周圍兜售其畫作的企圖證明不成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>peddles</b> drugs sells illegal drugs. 販賣 (非法藥品)","examples":["When a drug pusher offered the Los Angeles youngster $100 to peddle drugs, Jack refused. 當一名毒販子給這位洛杉磯小夥子傑克$100讓他販賣毒品時，他拒絕了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>peddles</b> an idea or a piece of information, they try to get people to accept it. 散佈 (某觀點或資訊)","examples":["They even set up their own news agency to peddle anti-isolationist propaganda. 他們甚至建立了自己的新聞機構以散佈反孤立主義思想。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"販賣","examples":["The war against drug peddling is all about cash. 反對毒品販賣的鬥爭完全是個錢的問題。"]}]}]},"persevere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"鍥而不捨，堅持不懈；固執己見（在辯論中）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>persevere</b> <b>with</b> something, you keep trying to do it and do not give up, even though it is difficult. 堅持不懈","examples":["This ability to persevere despite obstacles and setbacks is the quality people most admire in others. 這種不管障礙和挫折的鍥而不捨的能力是人們最為欽佩的品質。","...a school with a reputation for persevering with difficult and disruptive children. …一所因堅持不懈地教誨難管搗蛋的學生而聞名的學校。"]}]}]},"poach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"水煮，燉，煨（尤指魚）；煮（荷包蛋）；（侵入他人地界）偷獵；挖走（人員）；竊取，盜用（他人的想法）；（球類運動用語）搶打（同伴的球）；（動物用蹄）踐踏（或踩爛）（草皮）；（土地因被踐踏而）變得泥濘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>poaches</b> fish, animals, or birds, they illegally catch them on someone else's property. 偷獵","examples":["Many national parks set up to provide a refuge for wildlife are regularly invaded by people poaching game. 很多旨在為野生動物提供庇護的國家公園經常受到偷獵者的入侵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an organization <b>poaches</b> members or customers <b>from</b> another organization, they secretly or dishonestly persuade them to join them or become their customers. (透過不正當的手段或秘密) 挖走 (其他組織的成員或顧客)","examples":["Companies sometimes poach employees from one another. 一些公司有時會相互挖走對方的僱員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone <b>poaches</b> an idea, they dishonestly or illegally use the idea. 竊取 (別人的想法)","examples":["They've poached all our best ideas. 他們已經竊取了我們所有最好的想法。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>poach</b> food such as fish, you cook it gently in boiling water, milk, or other liquid. 小火煮","examples":["Poach the chicken until just cooked. 把雞用小火煮到剛剛熟。","...a pear poached in red wine. …用紅酒煮過的梨。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"偷獵者","examples":["Security cameras have been installed to guard against poachers. 已經安裝了安防攝像機來防範偷獵者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"挖人","examples":["The union was accused of poaching. 該工會被指控有挖人行徑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"烹煮","examples":["You will need a pot of broth for poaching. 你需要用一鍋湯來煮食物。"]}]}]},"ponder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細考慮，琢磨，沉思"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ponder</b> something, you think about it carefully. 仔細思考","examples":["I found myself constantly pondering the question: \"How could anyone do these things?\" 我發現自己不停地思索著這個問題：“怎麼會有人做出這些事情？”","He pondered over the difficulties involved. 他仔細思考了有關的種種困難。"]}]}]},"populate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（大批人或動物）居住於，生活於；充滿，出現於（某地方，領域）；遷移，殖民於；（給檔案）增添資料，輸入資料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an area <b>is populated</b> <b>by</b> certain people or animals, those people or animals live there, often in large numbers. 聚居; 棲息","examples":["Before all this the island was populated by native American Arawaks. 在所有這一切之前，該島聚居著土著美洲阿拉瓦克人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>populate</b> an area means to cause people to live there. 使聚居","examples":["Successive regimes annexed the region and populated it with lowland people. 後繼政權吞併了這個地區並讓低地居民聚居於此。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"聚居了的; 棲息了的","examples":["The southeast is the most densely populated area. 東南部是最稠密的居住區。"]}]}]},"pierce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（鋒利尖銳物體）刺入，刺穿；（在身體某部位）扎眼，穿孔（以佩戴珠寶）；（聲或光）穿過，透入；衝過，突破；讓某人心如刀割，深深地打動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a sharp object <b>pierces</b> something, or if you <b>pierce</b> something <b>with</b> a sharp object, the object goes into it and makes a hole in it. 刺穿","examples":["One bullet pierced the left side of his chest. 一顆子彈射入了他的左胸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have your ears or some other part of your body <b>pierced</b>, you have a small hole made through them so that you can wear a piece of jewellery in them. 穿孔","examples":["I'm having my ears pierced on Saturday. 我星期六要去扎耳洞。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"穿孔","examples":["...health risks from needles used in piercing and tattooing. …穿孔和紋身中使用針而帶來的健康風險。","...barefoot girls with braids and piercings. …梳著辮子、扎有耳洞的赤腳姑娘們。"]}]}]},"precede":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"處在……之前，先於；在……之前做（或說）；比……更重要，比……（級別）更高"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one event or period of time <b>precedes</b> another, it happens before it. (某事件) 先於 (另一事件) 而發生; (某時段) 先於 (另一時段) 而存在","examples":["Intensive negotiations between the main parties preceded the vote. 投票之前，主要政黨間進行了深入細緻的磋商。","The earthquake was preceded by a loud roar and lasted 20 seconds. 地震之前有一聲巨響，持續了20秒鐘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>precede</b> someone somewhere, you go in front of them. 走在…的前面","examples":["He gestured to Alice to precede them from the room. 他示意艾麗斯從房間裡出來走在他們前面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A sentence, paragraph, or chapter that <b>precedes</b> another one comes just before it. (句、段、章) 處於 (另一句、段、章) 之前","examples":["Look at the information that precedes the paragraph in question. 請看所談這一段之前的資訊。"]}]}]},"preside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"主持，擔任主持；主管某地，掌管（局勢）（preside over）；（尤指鍵盤樂器）領奏，主奏（preside at）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>preside over</b> a meeting or an event, you are in charge. 做主持","examples":["The PM returned to Downing Street to preside over a meeting of his inner cabinet. 首相回到唐寧街去主持一場核心內閣會議。"]}]}]},"prescribe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……開（藥），讓……採用（療法）；開處方；規定，命令；制定規定；推薦，推舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a doctor <b>prescribes</b> medicine or treatment for you, he or she tells you what medicine or treatment to have. 開 (藥、處方)","examples":["The physician examines the patient then diagnoses the disease and prescribes medication. 內科醫生檢查了病人，然後對疾病作出診斷，並開出藥方。","She took twice the prescribed dose of sleeping tablets. 她服用了所開劑量兩倍的安眠藥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or set of laws or rules <b>prescribes</b> an action or duty, they state that it must be carried out. 規定","examples":["...article II of the constitution, which prescribes the method of electing a president. …規定總統選舉辦法的憲法第二條。"]}]}]},"prohibit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（透過法律、條例等）禁止；阻止，使不可能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a law or someone in authority <b>prohibits</b> something, they forbid it or make it illegal. 禁止","examples":["...a law that prohibits tobacco advertising in newspapers and magazines. …一項禁止在報紙和雜誌上刊登菸草廣告的法律。","Fishing is prohibited. 捕魚是受禁止的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"禁止","examples":["The air force and the navy retain their prohibition of women on air combat missions. 空軍和海軍都保留了對女性空中作戰任務的禁止。"]}]}]},"presume":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"料想，（不肯定地）認為；假設，設想；（法律上或官方）假定，推定；擅自，冒昧；意味著；<正式>擅作主張，冒昧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>presume</b> <b>that</b> something is the case, you think that it is the case, although you are not certain. 推測","examples":["I presume you're here on business. 我想你是來這兒出差的吧。","\"Had he been home all week?\"—\"I presume so.\" “他整個星期都在家嗎？”—“我想是。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>presumes</b> <b>to</b> do something, you mean that they do it even though they have no right to do it. 擅自 (做某事)","examples":["They're resentful that outsiders presume to meddle in their affairs. 他們對外人擅自干預他們的事務怨恨不已。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an idea, theory, or plan <b>presumes</b> certain facts, it regards them as true so that they can be used as a basis for further ideas and theories. 假定 (某事實) 為真","examples":["The legal definition of \"know\" often presumes mental control. “知情”的法律界定通常以思維控制力為前提。"]}]}]},"propel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推進，驅動；推搡（某人走向特定方向）； 驅使，促使"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>propel</b> something in a particular direction means to cause it to move in that direction. 推進","examples":["The tiny rocket is attached to the spacecraft and is designed to propel it toward Mars. 微型火箭附在宇宙飛船上，用來推進飛船飛向火星。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"與形容詞結合的複合詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>-propelled</b> combines with nouns to form adjectives that indicate how something, especially a weapon, is propelled. (與名詞結合構成形容詞) …推進的","examples":["...rocket-propelled grenades. …火箭推進的榴彈。"]}]}]},"prosecute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"起訴，控告，檢舉；（律師在法庭上）指控，公訴；<正式>繼續（尤指戰爭）；<古>繼續從事（某職業），追求"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the authorities <b>prosecute</b> someone, they charge them with a crime and put them on trial. 對…提起公訴; 提起公訴","examples":["The police have decided not to prosecute because the evidence is not strong enough. 警方已決定不起訴，因為證據不夠充分。","Photographs taken by roadside cameras will soon be enough to prosecute drivers for speeding. 路邊攝像機所拍到的照片不久將足以用來起訴超速的司機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a lawyer <b>prosecutes</b> a case, he or she tries to prove that the person who is on trial is guilty. (原告律師) 起訴","examples":["The attorney who will prosecute the case says he cannot reveal how much money is involved. 即將起訴這件案子的原告律師說他不能透漏涉案金額。"]}]}]},"provoke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"激起，引起；激勵，刺激；挑釁，激怒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>provoke</b> someone, you deliberately annoy them and try to make them behave aggressively. 對…挑釁","examples":["He started beating me when I was about fifteen but I didn't do anything to provoke him. 我大約十五歲時，他開始打我，但我並沒有做什麼招惹他的事情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>provokes</b> a reaction, it causes it. 引起","examples":["His election success has provoked a shocked reaction. 他的競選勝利已經引起了震驚的反應。"]}]}]},"purify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（某物）潔淨，淨化；變純淨；洗滌（思想），淨化（心靈）；提純，精煉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>purify</b> a substance, you make it pure by removing any harmful, dirty, or inferior substances from it. 淨化","examples":["I take wheat and yeast tablets daily to purify the blood. 我每天服用小麥酵母片來淨化血液。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"淨化","examples":["...a water purification plant. …一家淨化水工廠。"]}]}]},"quench":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（喝水）止（渴）；滿足（慾望）；撲滅，熄滅（火）；抑制，壓制（感情）；（尤指用冷水或油）將……淬火，使冷卻；控制（發光、震動或放電等效果）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"淬火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who is thirsty <b>quenches</b> their <b>thirst</b>, they lose their thirst by having a drink. (透過喝水) 解 (渴)","examples":["He stopped to quench his thirst at a stream. 他停在一條小溪邊喝水解渴。"]}]}]},"radiate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使品質或情感）顯出，流露；輻射，發射；自中心輻射出，向周圍伸展；（動物或植物群）輻射形進化"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<罕>輻射（狀）的，光芒四射的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If things <b>radiate</b> out <b>from</b> a place, they form a pattern that is like lines drawn from the centre of a circle to various points on its edge. 輻射","examples":["Many kinds of woodland can be seen on the various walks which radiate from the Heritage Centre. 從遺產中心向外伸展的各條走道上可以看到多種林地。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>radiate</b> an emotion or quality or if it <b>radiates</b> <b>from</b> you, people can see it very clearly in your face and in your behaviour. 顯現 (特質); 流露 (情感)","examples":["She radiates happiness and health. 她渾身洋溢著快樂與健康。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>radiates</b> heat or light, heat or light comes from it. 散發出 (光或熱)","examples":["The metal plate behind my head radiated heat. 我腦後的金屬盤散發出熱量。"]}]}]},"recur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"再發生，反覆出現；（思考或講話時）重新回到，反覆提及（recur to）；（小數）迴圈"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>recurs</b>, it happens more than once. 再現; 屢次發生","examples":["...a theme that was to recur frequently in his work. …一個將在他的作品中多次出現的主題。"]}]}]},"reconcile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"調和，使協調一致；（使）和解，（使）恢復友好關係；調停，調解（爭吵）；使順從於，使接受；核對，查核（賬目）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reconcile</b> two beliefs, facts, or demands that seem to be opposed or completely different, you find a way in which they can both be true or both be successful. 使和諧一致; 調和","examples":["It's difficult to reconcile the demands of my job and the desire to be a good father. 協調我工作的要求與我當個好父親的願望很難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reconcile</b> two people, you make them become friends again after a quarrel or disagreement. 使和解","examples":["...my attempt to reconcile him with Toby. …我使他與託比和解的努力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>reconcile</b> <b>yourself</b> <b>to</b> an unpleasant situation, you accept it, although it does not make you happy to do so. 妥協; 將就","examples":["She had reconciled herself to never seeing him again. 她不情願地接受了再也不和他見面的事實。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip-passive.","pos_name":"被動相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are reconciled</b> <b>with</b> someone, you become friendly with them again after a quarrel or disagreement. 與…和好","examples":["He never believed he and Susan would be reconciled. 他不認為他和蘇珊會和好。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"妥協的; 將就的","examples":["She felt, if not grateful for her own situation, at least a little more reconciled to it. 她覺得，即便對自己的處境不心存感激，至少能將就一些了。"]}]}]},"refine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"精煉，提純；改進，改善；使……文雅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a substance <b>is refined</b>, it is made pure by having all other substances removed from it. 提煉","examples":["Oil is refined to remove naturally occurring impurities. 油經過提煉去除天然生成的雜質。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a process, theory, or machine <b>is refined</b>, it is improved by having small changes made to it. 完善","examples":["Surgical techniques are constantly being refined. 外科手術技術正在不斷得到完善。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"提煉","examples":["...oil refining. …煉油。"]}]}]},"rehearse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"排練，排演；監督（表演者或團體）排演；默誦，默默地練習；<正式>詳述，重複"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>rehearse</b> a play, dance, or piece of music, they practise it in order to prepare for a performance. 排練","examples":["In his version, a group of actors are rehearsing a play about Joan of Arc. 按他說，一群演員正在排練一出關於聖女貞德的戲。","Tens of thousands of people have been rehearsing for the opening ceremony in the new stadium. 數萬人一直在新體育場裡為開幕式進行排練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>rehearse</b> something that you are going to say or do, you silently practise it by imagining that you are saying or doing it. 在心裡預演","examples":["Anticipate any tough questions and rehearse your answers. 事先預想會有任何難的問題，然後在心裡預演你的答覆。"]}]}]},"reinforce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"加強，強化（觀點、思想或感覺）；加固，使更結實；給……加強力量（或裝備），增援；尋求（或得到）增援"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"加固物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>reinforces</b> a feeling, situation, or process, it makes it stronger or more intense. 加強","examples":["I hope this will reinforce Indonesian determination to deal with this kind of threat. 我希望這會加強印度尼西亞對付這類威脅的決心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>reinforces</b> an idea or point of view, it provides more evidence or support for it. 鞏固","examples":["The delegation hopes to reinforce the idea that human rights are not purely internal matters. 代表團希望鞏固人權不完全是國家內政的觀念。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>reinforce</b> an object means to make it stronger or harder. 加固","examples":["Eventually, they had to reinforce the walls with exterior beams. 最後，他們不得不用外梁來加固那些牆壁。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>reinforce</b> an army or a police force means to make it stronger by increasing its size or providing it with more weapons. To <b>reinforce</b> a position or place means to make it stronger by sending more soldiers or weapons. 增援","examples":["Both sides have been reinforcing their positions after yesterday's fierce fighting. 在昨天的激戰後，雙方一直在增援各自的陣地。"]}]}]},"repress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓抑（痛苦的情感、回憶等）；抑制，剋制（行為）；（尤指用武力）鎮壓，壓制；實施鎮壓；使（基因）轉錄受阻遏"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>repress</b> a feeling, you make a deliberate effort not to show or have this feeling. 抑制 (感情)","examples":["It is anger that is repressed that leads to violence and loss of control. 正是被抑制的憤怒導致暴力和失控。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>repress</b> a smile, sigh, or moan, you try hard not to smile, sigh, or moan. 忍住 (笑、嘆氣或呻吟)","examples":["He repressed a smile. 他忍住沒有笑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a section of society <b>is repressed</b>, their freedom is restricted by the people who have authority over them. 鎮壓; 壓制","examples":["...a UN resolution banning him from repressing his people. …聯合國的一項禁止他鎮壓人民的決議。"]}]}]},"retaliate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"報復，反擊；<古>就（傷害，侮辱）進行報復"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>retaliate</b> when someone harms or annoys you, you do something which harms or annoys them in return. 報復","examples":["I was sorely tempted to retaliate. 我非常想報復。","The company would retaliate against employees who joined a union. 該公司將對加入工會的員工們進行報復。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"報復","examples":["Police said they believed the attack was in retaliation for the death of the drug trafficker. 警方說他們認為這起襲擊是為那個毒販的死而實施的報復。"]}]}]},"seduce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"誘姦，勾引；引誘，吸引"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>seduces</b> you, it is so attractive that it makes you do something that you would not otherwise do. 誘惑","examples":["The view of lake and plunging cliffs seduces visitors. 湖水和陡峭的懸崖景觀吸引著遊客。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>seduces</b> another person, they use their charm to persuade that person to have sex with them. 勾引; 誘姦","examples":["She has set out to seduce Stephen. 她已開始勾引斯蒂芬。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"誘惑","examples":["...the seduction of words. …言語的誘惑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"勾引","examples":["Her methods of seduction are subtle. 她勾引人的手法很巧妙。"]}]}]},"retrieve":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"找回，收回；檢索（儲存於計算機的資訊）；（狗等）銜回（物品、獵物）；挽救，挽回；回憶，追憶；收繞釣魚線"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指中槍獵物的）找回；收繞釣魚線；<古> 恢復的可能性；檢索"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>retrieve</b> something, you get it back from the place where you left it. 找回; 取回","examples":["The men were trying to retrieve weapons left when the army abandoned the island. 那些人正試圖找回該軍隊撤離這個島時留下的武器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you manage to <b>retrieve</b> a situation, you succeed in bringing it back into a more acceptable state. 挽回","examples":["He, the one man who could retrieve that situation, might receive the call. 他這個惟一能挽回那個局面的人可能會接到這個電話。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>retrieve</b> information from a computer or from your memory means to get it back. (從電腦中) 讀取 (資訊)","examples":["Computers can instantly retrieve millions of information bits. 計算機能立刻讀取數百萬條資訊。"]}]}]},"render":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使成為，使處於某種狀態；給予，提供；（以某種方式）表達，表現；粉刷，往（牆上）抹灰；將（脂肪）熬成油，使熔化；正式宣佈（判決或決定）；（供審查，考慮）提交，呈報；<文>放棄，獻出；演奏，演唱；翻譯；繪製（指用色彩和明暗使輪廓影象具立體感）；秘密引渡（外國罪犯、恐怖嫌疑犯）；從（動物身體）提取（蛋白質、脂肪及其他可用部分）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"底灰，底泥；<史>交納"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>render</b> with an adjective that describes a particular state to say that someone or something is changed into that state. For example, if someone or something makes a thing harmless, you can say that they <b>render</b> it harmless. 使成為; 使變得","examples":["It contained so many errors as to render it worthless. 太多的錯誤使之變得毫無價值。"]}]}]},"shoplift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"在商店中偷竊，入店行竊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>shoplifts</b>, they steal goods from a shop by hiding them in a bag or in their clothes. 在商店偷竊","examples":["He openly shoplifted from a supermarket. 他在一家超市公然行竊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"在商店行竊的人","examples":["A persistent shoplifter has been banned from every shop in town. 一個商店行竊慣犯已被禁止進入鎮上任何一家商店。"]}]}]},"shun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（故意）避開，躲開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>shun</b> someone or something, you deliberately avoid them or keep away from them. 有意迴避","examples":["From that time forward everybody shunned him. 從那時起，人人都有意迴避他。"]}]}]},"rotate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）旋轉，（使）轉動；（人員）輪換，輪值；輪種，輪作；定期調換地點（或位置）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（植） 輻狀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>rotates</b> or when you <b>rotate</b> it, it turns with a circular movement. 旋轉","examples":["The earth rotates around the sun. 地球圍繞太陽旋轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people or things <b>rotate</b>, or if someone <b>rotates</b> them, they take turns to do a particular job or serve a particular purpose. 使輪流; 輪流","examples":["The members of the club can rotate and one person can do all the preparation for the evening. 該俱樂部的成員可輪流工作，一個人可做晚會所有的準備工作。"]}]}]},"signify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"意味著，象徵；<正式> 表達，顯示（感情、意願等）；<正式> 要緊，有重要性；<美，非正式>（作為一種遊戲或習俗，美國黑人之間）相互吹牛，相互辱罵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an event, a sign, or a symbol <b>signifies</b> something, it is a sign of that thing or represents that thing. 表示; 意味著","examples":["These were not the only changes that signified the end of boyhood. 這些不是表示男孩時代已結束的惟一變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>signify</b> something, you make a sign or gesture in order to communicate a particular meaning. (用符號或手勢) 表達","examples":["Two jurors signified their dissent. 兩個陪審員表達了他們的異議。"]}]}]},"smuggle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"走私，偷運；偷偷攜帶，夾帶"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>smuggles</b> things or people into a place or out of it, they take them there illegally or secretly. 走私; 偷運","examples":["My message is \"If you try to smuggle drugs you are stupid.\" 我的訊息是，“你若企圖走私毒品，那是犯傻。”","Police have foiled an attempt to smuggle a bomb into Belfast airport. 警方挫敗了一個將炸彈偷帶進貝爾法斯特機場的企圖。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"走私","examples":["An air hostess was arrested and charged with drug smuggling. 一位空姐被抓了起來，並被指控走私毒品。"]}]}]},"simplify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使簡易，簡化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>simplify</b> something, you make it easier to understand or you remove the things which make it complex. 簡化","examples":["Our aim is to simplify the complex social security system. 我們的目的是要簡化複雜的社會保險體系。"]}]}]},"soar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（數量、價值、水平、規模等）急升，猛漲；高飛，翱翔；升空，升騰；（精神或希望）高漲；(樹木、建築等）高聳，屹立；升至（很高的高度），高達；（音樂）升高，增強"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"高飛；高漲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the amount, value, level, or volume of something <b>soars</b>, it quickly increases by a great deal. 急劇增加","examples":["Insurance claims are expected to soar. 預計保險索賠會急劇增加。","Shares soared on the New York stock exchange. 紐約證券交易所股票暴漲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a bird <b>soars</b> into the air, it goes quickly up into the air. 高飛","examples":["If you're lucky, a splendid golden eagle may soar into view. 幸運的話，一隻金色雄鷹會躍入視線。"]}]}]},"socialize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"交往，交際；使合群，使適應社會生活；使社會主義化，按社會主義原則行事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>socialize</b>, you meet other people socially, for example at parties. 社交","examples":["...an open meeting, where members socialized and welcomed any new members. …讓會員們相互交流、歡迎所有新成員的一次公開集會。"]}]}]},"soothe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使平靜，安撫；減輕，緩和（疼痛）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>soothe</b> someone who is angry or upset, you make them feel calmer. 使鎮定","examples":["He would take her in his arms and soothe her. 他就會把她摟在懷裡，使她鎮定下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that <b>soothes</b> a part of your body where there is pain or discomfort makes the pain or discomfort less severe. 緩和 (疼痛或不適)","examples":["...body lotion to soothe dry skin. …減輕皮膚乾燥的潤膚露。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"撫慰的","examples":["Put on some nice soothing music. 放些柔和舒緩的音樂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"緩和的","examples":["Cold tea is very soothing for burns. 冷茶對灼傷有鎮痛作用。"]}]}]},"specify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"明確指出；具體說明；把……列入說明書"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>specify</b> something, you give information about what is required or should happen in a certain situation. 明確要求","examples":["They specified a spacious entrance hall. 他們明確要求門廳要寬敞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>specify</b> what should happen or be done, you explain it in an exact and detailed way. 具體說明","examples":["Each recipe specifies the size of egg to be used. 每種食譜都具體說明了所用雞蛋的大小。","A new law specified that houses must be a certain distance back from the water. 一項新法律詳細規定了房子必須與水域相隔一定的距離。"]}]}]},"specialize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"專門研究（或從事），專攻；專營；（生）使（器官）專化，使特化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>specialize in</b> a thing, you know a lot about it and concentrate a great deal of your time and energy on it, especially in your work or when you are studying or training. You also use <b>specialize</b> to talk about a restaurant which concentrates on a particular type of food. (在某事物上) 有專長","examples":["...a University professor who specializes in the history of the Russian empire. …一位專門研究沙俄歷史的大學教授。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"專門研究","examples":["This degree offers a major specialization in social policy alongside a course in sociology. 該學位提供一門社會政策主專業課和一門社會學課程。"]}]}]},"stabilize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）穩定，穩固；使不易移動；使穩定，使不易分解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>stabilizes</b>, or <b>is stabilized</b>, it becomes stable. 穩定","examples":["Although her illness is serious, her condition is beginning to stabilize. 雖然她的病情很嚴重，但她的情況正開始穩定下來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"穩定","examples":["...the stabilization of property prices. …房地產價格的穩定。"]}]}]},"strangle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扼死，勒死，絞死；抑制，扼殺；抑制，壓制（衝動，行動，聲音）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>strangle</b> someone means to kill them by squeezing their throat tightly so that they cannot breathe. 扼死","examples":["He tried to strangle a border policeman and steal his gun. 他試圖扼死一位邊防警察並偷走他的槍。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>strangle</b> something means to prevent it from succeeding or developing. 抑制","examples":["The country's economic plight is strangling its scientific institutions. 這個國家的經濟困境正在抑制其科研機構的發展。"]}]}]},"stimulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"促進，激發（某事物）；激發，鼓勵；使（身體，生物系統）興奮，刺激；起刺激作用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>stimulate</b> something means to encourage it to begin or develop further. 鼓勵; 刺激","examples":["America's priority is rightly to stimulate its economy. 美國的首要任務自然是刺激經濟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are</b> <b>stimulated</b> <b>by</b> something, it makes you feel full of ideas and enthusiasm. 激勵","examples":["Bill was stimulated by the challenge. 比爾受到該挑戰的激勵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>stimulates</b> a part of a person's body, it causes it to move or start working. 刺激 (身體器官)","examples":["Exercise stimulates the digestive and excretory systems. 運動刺激消化和排洩系統。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"鼓勵; 刺激","examples":["...an economy in need of stimulation. …一個需要刺激的經濟。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"激勵的","examples":["It is a complex yet stimulating book. 這是一本複雜卻能引發興趣的書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"刺激的","examples":["...the stimulating effect of adrenaline. …腎上腺素的刺激作用。"]}]}]},"speculate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猜測，推測；投機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>speculate</b> about something, you make guesses about its nature or identity, or about what might happen. 猜測","examples":["Critics of the project speculate about how many hospitals could be built instead. 該專案的批評者們則猜想這相當於可以建多少家醫院。","The doctors speculate that he died of a cerebral haemorrhage caused by a blow on the head. 醫生們猜測他死於頭部撞擊引起的腦溢血。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"猜測","examples":["The president has gone out of his way to dismiss speculation over the future of the economy. 總統努力消除對未來經濟的悲觀估測。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>speculates</b> financially, they buy property, stocks, or shares, in the hope of being able to sell them again at a higher price and make a profit. 做投機買賣","examples":["The banks made too many risky loans which now can't be repaid, and they speculated in property whose value has now dropped. 銀行貸出了太多現在無法償還的風險貸款，而且他們在房地產業做了投機買賣，其價值目前也已經下跌。"]}]}]},"suffocate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）窒息而死，（使）悶死；（使）呼吸困難，（使）憋悶；（受）束縛，（受）扼制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>suffocates</b> or <b>is suffocated</b>, they die because there is no air for them to breathe. 使窒息而死; 窒息而死","examples":["He either suffocated, or froze to death. 他要麼窒息而死，要麼凍死了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that you <b>are suffocating</b> or that something <b>is suffocating</b> you, you mean that you feel very uncomfortable because there is not enough fresh air and it is difficult to breathe. 使感到窒息; 感到窒息","examples":["That's better. I was suffocating in that cell of a room. 那樣好多了。我剛才在那個小房間裡感到窒息。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"窒息","examples":["Many of the victims died of suffocation. 受害者中許多死於窒息。"]}]}]},"subscribe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"訂閱，訂購；定期繳納會員費; 定期捐款贊助；認購（股票）；贊成，同意；〈正式〉簽署（遺囑、合同或其他檔案）；申請，註冊，報名；購買（一系列演出的）聯票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>subscribe to</b> an opinion or belief, you are one of a number of people who have this opinion or belief. 持有 (意見或信仰)","examples":["I've personally never subscribed to the view that either sex is superior to the other. 我個人從未持有過一種性別比另一種性別優越的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>subscribe to</b> a magazine or a newspaper, you pay to receive copies of it regularly. 訂閱","examples":["My main reason for subscribing to New Scientist is to keep abreast of advances in science. 我訂閱《新科學家》的主要原因是要跟上科學的進步。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>subscribe to</b> an online newsgroup or service, you send a message saying that you wish to receive it or belong to it. 申請加入 (線上新聞組); 申請 (線上服務)","examples":["Usenet is a collection of discussion groups, known as newsgroups, to which anybody can subscribe. 新聞組網路是由稱為新聞組的討論組組成，任何人都能申請加入。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>subscribe</b> <b>for</b> shares in a company, you apply to buy shares in that company. 申購 (股份)","examples":["Employees subscribed for far more shares than were available. 僱員們申購了遠比實際數額還多的股份。"]}]}]},"surpass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"超過，勝過，優於；比（預期的或希望的）更好；超越自我；超出（理解範圍）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person or thing <b>surpasses</b> another, the first is better than, or has more of a particular quality than, the second. 優於; 超過","examples":["He was determined to surpass the achievements of his older brothers. 他決心超過他的幾位哥哥的成就。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>surpasses</b> expectations, it is much better than it was expected to be. 遠遠超出 (預期)","examples":["Conrad Black gave an excellent party that surpassed expectations. 康拉德·布萊克辦了一次遠遠超出預期的精彩聚會。"]}]}]},"symbolize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"象徵，用符號代表；採用象徵，使用符號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>symbolizes</b> another, it is used or regarded as a symbol of it. 象徵","examples":["The fall of the Berlin Wall symbolized the end of the Cold War between East and West. 柏林牆的倒塌象徵著東西方冷戰的結束。"]}]}]},"thrive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"茁壯成長，興旺，繁榮；（尤指在別人覺得困難的時候）以……為樂，可以出色應對"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>thrives</b>, they do well and are successful, healthy, or strong. 興旺發達; 茁壯成長","examples":["He appears to be thriving. 他看起來興旺發達蒸蒸日上。","Today her company continues to thrive. 如今，她的公司繼續蓬勃發展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>thrives on</b> a particular situation, you mean that they enjoy it or that they can deal with it very well, especially when other people find it unpleasant or difficult. 喜歡; 從容應對 (尤指別人不喜歡或認為困難的事)","examples":["Many people thrive on a stressful lifestyle. 許多人喜歡有壓力的生活方式。"]}]}]},"terminate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）結束，（使）終止；到達終點站；終止妊娠，人工流產；<美>解僱；<美>謀殺（某人）；在……結尾，以……收尾"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"結束的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>terminate</b> something or when it <b>terminates</b>, it ends completely. 終止","examples":["Her next remark abruptly terminated the conversation. 她接下來的言論使得談話突然終止。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>terminate</b> a pregnancy means to end it. 終止 (妊娠)","examples":["After a lot of agonizing she decided to terminate the pregnancy. 在多次痛苦的考慮後，她決定終止妊娠。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"終止","examples":["...a dispute which led to the abrupt termination of trade. …一個導致貿易突然終止的爭端。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"終止妊娠","examples":["You should also have a medical check-up after the termination of a pregnancy. 你在終止妊娠後也應該做個體檢。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a train or bus <b>terminates</b> somewhere, it ends its journey there. (火車或公共汽車) 到達終點","examples":["This train will terminate at Lamy. 這列火車的終點站是拉米。"]}]}]},"topple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）不穩而倒下，（使）倒塌；推翻（首領），顛覆（政權）；<美>戰勝，打敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>topples</b> somewhere or if you <b>topple</b> them, they become unsteady or unstable and fall over. 倒下","examples":["He just released his hold and toppled slowly backwards. 他就鬆手，慢慢地向後倒下了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>topple</b> a government or leader, especially one that is not elected by the people, means to cause them to lose power. 推翻","examples":["...the revolution which toppled the regime. …推翻了該政權的革命。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Topple over</b> means the same as . 同(topple)","examples":["The tree is so badly damaged they are worried it might topple over. 這棵樹損傷非常嚴重以至於他們擔心它會倒下。"]}]}]},"undergo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"經歷，經受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>undergo</b> something necessary or unpleasant, it happens to you. 經歷; 經受","examples":["New recruits have been undergoing training in recent weeks. 新兵們最近幾週一直在接受訓練。"]}]}]},"uncover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"揭露，發現；揭開蓋子，移開覆蓋物；發掘，挖出；脫帽（尤指表示敬意）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>uncover</b> something, especially something that has been kept secret, you discover or find out about it. 找出","examples":["Auditors said they had uncovered evidence of fraud. 審計員們說他們已找到了詐騙的證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>uncover</b> something means to remove something that is covering it. 移去 (某物的) 遮蓋物","examples":["When the seedlings sprout, uncover the tray. 幼苗發芽後，揭開盤上的遮蓋物。"]}]}]},"undo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"解開，鬆開；消除……影響或結果，使恢復原狀；撤銷（先前的計算機指令）；破壞，毀掉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）撤消還原"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>undo</b> something that is closed, tied, or held together, or if you <b>undo</b> the thing holding it, you loosen or remove the thing holding it. 開啟; 解開; 鬆開","examples":["I managed secretly to undo a corner of the parcel. 我設法偷偷地開啟包裹的一角。","I undid the bottom two buttons of my yellow and grey shirt. 我解開了我黃灰色相間襯衫最下面的兩個鈕釦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>undo</b> something that has been done means to reverse its effect. 使無效","examples":["A heavy-handed approach from the police could undo that good impression. 警察的專制手段能使那個好印象化為烏有。","She knew it would be difficult to undo the damage that had been done. 她知道難以挽回已造成的損失。"]}]}]},"unpack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開啟（行李、箱子、包裹等）取出或卸下物品；分析，剖析（論點、問題等）；解壓，解包（檔案、資料等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>unpack</b> a suitcase, box, or similar container, or you <b>unpack</b> the things inside it, you take the things out of the container. 開啟(箱子或盒子) 取出","examples":["He unpacked his bag. 他開啟了他的包。"]}]}]},"unify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）聯合，（使）統一；使協調"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>unifies</b> different things or parts, or if the things or parts <b>unify</b>, they are brought together to form one thing. 使成一體; 成為一體","examples":["He pledged to unify the city's political factions. 他保證要統一全市的政治小集團。","...constitutional reforms designed to unify the country. …旨在統一國家的憲法改革。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"統一的","examples":["...a unified system of taxation. …統一的稅制。"]}]}]},"undertake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"承擔，從事；承諾，答應；<英>在內側行駛時趕上並超越（另一輛車）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>undertake</b> a task or job, you start doing it and accept responsibility for it. 從事; 承擔","examples":["She undertook the task of monitoring the elections. 她承擔了監督選舉的任務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>undertake</b> <b>to</b> do something, you promise that you will do it. 承諾","examples":["He undertook to edit the text himself. 他承諾親自編輯正文。"]}]}]},"unlock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開……的鎖；釋放（潛能），揭開（秘密）；開啟，提供；解開，解除鎖定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>unlock</b> something such as a door, a room, or a container that has a lock, you open it using a key. 用鑰匙開啟","examples":["He unlocked the car and threw the coat on to the back seat. 他啟動汽車，將外套扔到了後座。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>unlock</b> the potential or the secrets of something or someone, you release them. 發掘 (潛力); 揭開 (秘密)","examples":["The point of the competition is to encourage all people to unlock their hidden potential. 競賽的目的是鼓勵所有人發掘其隱藏的潛力。"]}]}]},"undermine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逐漸削弱（損害）；故意破壞（某人）的形象（或威信）；在……下面挖，（尤指）從根基處損壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>undermine</b> something such as a feeling or a system, you make it less strong or less secure than it was before, often by a gradual process or by repeated efforts. 逐漸削弱; 逐漸動搖","examples":["Offering advice on each and every problem will undermine her feeling of being adult. 每個問題都為她提出忠告會逐漸削弱她的成年意識。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>undermine</b> someone or <b>undermine</b> their position or authority, you make their authority or position less secure, often by indirect methods. (通常以間接方式) 動搖 (某人的地位或權威)","examples":["She undermined him and destroyed his confidence in his own talent. 她動搖了他的地位，摧毀了他對自己才能的信心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>undermine</b> someone's efforts or <b>undermine</b> their chances of achieving something, you behave in a way that makes them less likely to succeed. 破壞; 損害 (某人的努力或成功的機會)","examples":["The continued fighting threatens to undermine efforts to negotiate an agreement. 持續的戰鬥有可能破壞透過談判達成協議的努力。"]}]}]},"uphold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"支援，維護（法規、制度或原則）；認可，維持（法院原判）；鼓勵；舉起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>uphold</b> something such as a law, a principle, or a decision, you support and maintain it. 維護","examples":["Our policy has been to uphold the law. 我們的政策一直是維護法律。","It is the responsibility of every government to uphold certain basic principles. 每個政府都有責任維護某些基本原則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a court of law <b>upholds</b> a legal decision that has already been made, it decides that it was the correct decision. 維持 (原判)","examples":["The State Supreme Court upheld the Superior Court judge's decision. 國家最高法院維持了高階法院法官的判決。"]}]}]},"vend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（及物和不及物）出售，銷售；<正式>公開發表，表達（觀點、意見等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to sell or be sold 出售","examples":[]}]}]},"victimize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使受害，迫害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is victimized</b>, they are deliberately treated unfairly. 受迫害","examples":["He felt the students had been victimized because they'd voiced opposition to the government. 他認為學生們因發表反對政府的言論而受到了迫害。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"迫害","examples":["...society's cruel victimization of women. …社會對婦女的殘酷迫害。"]}]}]},"utilize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"利用，使用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>utilize</b> something, you use it. 利用","examples":["Sound engineers utilize a range of techniques to enhance the quality of the recordings. 音響工程師利用一系列的技術來提高錄音質量。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"利用","examples":["...the utilization of human resources. …人力資源的利用。"]}]}]},"unfold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"開啟，展開；呈現，逐漸明朗；發生，發展"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a situation <b>unfolds</b>, it develops and becomes known or understood. 逐漸明朗","examples":["The outcome depends on conditions as well as how events unfold. 結果取決於條件以及事件如何發展。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a story <b>unfolds</b> or if someone <b>unfolds</b> it, it is told to someone else. 使 (事情等) 傳開; 傳開","examples":["Don's story unfolded as the cruise got under way. 唐的故事隨著航遊的開始而漫漫展開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>unfolds</b> something which has been folded or if it <b>unfolds</b>, it is opened out and becomes flat. 展開","examples":["He quickly unfolded the blankets and spread them on the mattress. 他迅速攤開毯子，鋪在褥墊上。"]}]}]},"transmit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"播送，傳輸，發射；傳遞，傳達（思想、情感）；傳播，傳染（病毒、疾病等）；傳導（聲、電等），透（光等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When radio and television programmes, computer data, or other electronic messages <b>are transmitted</b>, they are sent from one place to another, using wires, radio waves, or satellites. 傳播 (廣播電視節目、計算機資訊等)","examples":["The game was transmitted live. 這場比賽被現場直播。","This is currently the most efficient way to transmit certain types of data like electronic mail. 這是目前傳輸電子郵件等某類資料最有效的方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one person or animal <b>transmits</b> a disease to another, they have the disease and cause the other person or animal to have it. 傳播 (疾病)","examples":["...mosquitoes that transmit disease to humans. …向人類傳播疾病的蚊子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If an object or substance <b>transmits</b> something such as sound or electrical signals, the sound or signals are able to pass through it. 傳導 (聲音、電子訊號等)","examples":["These thin crystals transmit much of the power. 這些薄薄的晶體能傳導大部分的能量。"]}]}]},"visualize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"想象，使形象化；使可見，使顯現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>visualize</b> something, you imagine what it is like by forming a mental picture of it. 想像","examples":["Susan visualized her wedding day and saw herself walking down the aisle on her father's arm. 蘇珊想像著自己婚禮那天，挽著父親的手臂沿著教堂過道走過來。","He could not visualize her as old. 他無法想像她年老的樣子。"]}]}]},"withstand":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"頂住，抵住；經受住，承受住（攻擊、批評等）；反抗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>withstands</b> a force or action, they survive it or do not give in to it. 抵禦","examples":["...armoured vehicles designed to withstand chemical attack. …設計來抵禦化學攻擊的裝甲車。"]}]}]},"waterproof":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"防水的，不透水的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……不透水，對……作防水處理"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"防水衣物，雨衣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>waterproof</b> does not let water pass through it. 防水的","examples":["Take waterproof clothing – Oregon weather is unpredictable. 帶上防水的衣物吧–俄勒岡州的天氣總是難以預測。"]}]}]},"yearn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"懷念，渴望"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>yearns</b> <b>for</b> something that they are unlikely to get, they want it very much. 渴望","examples":["He yearned for freedom. 他曾渴望自由。","I yearned to be an actor. 我曾渴望成為一名演員。"]}]}]},"woo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"追求；招致；向……求愛；懇求"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"求愛；懇求"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>woo</b> people, you try to encourage them to help you, support you, or vote for you, for example, by promising them things which they would like. 爭取","examples":["They wooed customers by offering low interest rates. 他們透過提供低利率來爭取顧客。"]}]}]},"accordingly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相應地，照著；因此，所以"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>accordingly</b> to introduce a fact or situation that is a result or consequence of something that you have just referred to. 因此","examples":["We have a different background, a different history. Accordingly, we have the right to different futures. 我們擁有不同的背景、不同的歷史。因此，我們有權獲得不一樣的前途。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you consider a situation and then act <b>accordingly</b>, the way you act depends on the nature of the situation. 相應地","examples":["It is a difficult job and they should be paid accordingly. 它是一項艱鉅的工作，他們應該相應地獲得報酬。"]}]}]},"likewise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"同樣地，類似地；（表示感覺相同）我也是，我有同感；也，還"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>likewise</b> when you are comparing two methods, states, or situations and saying that they are similar. 同樣地","examples":["What is fair for homeowners likewise should be fair to businesses. 對私房業主公平的，同樣也該對商家公平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something and someone else does <b>likewise</b>, they do the same or a similar thing. 照樣地","examples":["He lent money, made donations and encouraged others to do likewise. 他把錢借出、捐出，並鼓勵其他人這麼做。"]}]}]},"thereafter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<正式>其後，此後"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thereafter</b> means after the event or date mentioned. 其後","examples":["The plan will help you lose 3-4 pounds the first week, and 1-2 pounds the weeks thereafter. 該計劃將幫助你在第1周減3到4磅，其後每週減1到2磅。"]}]}]},"thereby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"因此，從而"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>thereby</b> to introduce an important result or consequence of the event or action you have just mentioned. 由此","examples":["Our bodies can sweat, thereby losing heat by evaporation. 我們的身體會流汗，由此能透過蒸發散熱。"]}]}]},"outright":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全的，徹底的；公開的，直率的；絕對的，全面的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"公開地，直率地；完全地，徹底地；立刻，立即；一次付清地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>outright</b> to describe behaviour and actions that are open and direct, rather than indirect. 直率的","examples":["Kawaguchi finally resorted to an outright lie. 川口最後乾脆公開撒謊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Outright</b> means complete and total. 完全徹底的","examples":["She had failed to win an outright victory. 她沒能大獲全勝。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outright</b> is also an adverb. 直率地","examples":["Why are you so mysterious? Why don't you tell me outright? 你為什麼這麼神神秘秘？為什麼不直截了當地告訴我？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Outright</b> is also an adverb. 完全徹底地","examples":["The peace plan wasn't rejected outright. 該和平計劃沒有被全盤否定。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is killed outright</b>, they die immediately, for example, in an accident. 當即死亡","examples":[]}]}]},"regardless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不顧，不加理會；不管怎樣，無論如何"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不管的，不注意的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>regardless of</b> something else, it is not affected or influenced at all by that other thing. 不管; 無論","examples":["It takes in anybody regardless of religion, colour, or creed. 這個組織接納任何人，不管其宗教、膚色或信仰。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone did something <b>regardless</b>, you mean that they did it even though there were problems or factors that could have stopped them, or perhaps should have stopped them. 不顧一切地","examples":["Despite her recent surgery she has been carrying on regardless. 儘管她最近動了手術，她卻一直在不顧一切地繼續工作。"]}]}]},"alongside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"在……旁邊；沿著……的邊；與……一起，與……並肩（工作）；與……相比；與……同等重要的；同時，共存"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在旁邊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>alongside</b> another thing, the first thing is next to the second. 在…旁邊","examples":["He crossed the street and walked alongside Central Park. 他過了馬路，然後在中央公園旁邊走著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you work <b>alongside</b> other people, you all work together in the same place. 與…並肩 (工作)","examples":["He had worked alongside Frank and Mark and they had become friends. 他曾與弗蘭克和馬克並肩工作過，他們已經成為朋友了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alongside</b> is also an adverb. 在旁邊","examples":["He waited several minutes for a car to pull up alongside. 他等了幾分鐘等一輛車停靠在旁邊。"]}]}]},"aborigine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"土著，土著居民，原住民；澳大利亞原住民（常大寫為 Aborigine）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an original inhabitant of a country or region who has been there from the earliest known times 土著居民","examples":[]}]}]},"aboriginal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"原始的，土著的；（與）澳大利亞土著人（有關）的，（與）澳大利亞土著語（有關）的（Aboriginal）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"土著居民，土生生物；澳大利亞土著居民（Aboriginal）；（任何一種）澳大利亞土著語（Aboriginal）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>Aboriginal</b> is an Australian Aborigine. 澳大利亞的土著人","examples":["He remained fascinated by the Aboriginals' tales. 他一直對澳大利亞土著人的故事很著迷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aboriginal</b> means belonging or relating to the Australian Aborigines. 澳大利亞土著的","examples":["...Aboriginal art. …土著藝術。"]}]}]},"sheer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（用於強調）純粹的，完全的；程度深的，數量大的；陡峭的，垂直的；（織物等）極薄的，透明的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"垂直地，陡峭地；<古>徹底地，完全地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"急轉彎，突然轉向；避開（不愉快的話題）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"精紡（或透明）織物（或物品）；（尤指船）突然偏航，突然轉向；（船首及船尾處的）舷弧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>sheer</b> to emphasize that a state or situation is complete and does not involve or is not mixed with anything else. 純粹的","examples":["His music is sheer delight. 他的音樂是純粹的快樂。","Sheer chance quite often plays an important part in sparking off an idea. 純粹的運氣常常在激發思想方面起著重要的作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sheer</b> cliff or drop is extremely steep or completely vertical. 陡峭的; 完全垂直的","examples":["There was a sheer drop just outside my window. 就在我的窗外有一個陡坡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Sheer</b> material is very thin, light, and delicate. 極輕薄的","examples":["...sheer black tights. …極薄的黑色緊身衣。"]}]}]},"abbreviation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"縮略詞，縮寫形式；縮略，縮寫"}],"sections":[]},"deadly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"致命的；極度的；乏味枯燥的；死一般的；陰險毒辣的，冷酷無情的；極有害的，破壞性的；（運動員或其動作）極富技巧性的，極難防禦的；極好的，卓越的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"極其；死一般"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>deadly</b>, it is likely or able to cause someone's death, or has already caused someone's death. 致命的; 致死的","examples":["He was acquitted on charges of assault with a deadly weapon. 他用兇器傷人的罪名不成立。","...a deadly disease currently affecting dolphins. …目前影響海豚的一種致命疾病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or their behaviour as <b>deadly</b>, you mean that they will do or say anything to get what they want, without caring about other people. 不擇手段的; 肆無忌憚的","examples":["The Duchess levelled a deadly look at Nikko. 公爵夫人無所顧忌地瞪了尼克一眼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>deadly</b> situation has unpleasant or dangerous consequences. 極有害的","examples":["...the deadly combination of low expectations and low achievement. …低期望值和低成就的不良結合。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>deadly</b> to emphasize that something has a particular quality, especially an unpleasant or undesirable quality. 極度地","examples":["Broadcast news was accurate and reliable but deadly dull. 新聞廣播準確、可靠，但極其枯燥。"]}]}]},"abundance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大量，豐富；繁榮，富裕；數量，丰度；（紙牌惠斯特用語）獨得九墩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>abundance</b> <b>of</b> something is a large quantity of it. 豐富","examples":["This area of Mexico has an abundance of safe beaches and a pleasing climate. 墨西哥的這個地區有大量的安全沙灘與宜人的氣候。"]}]}]},"abstraction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抽象，抽象化；<正式>抽象概念；（電腦科學）抽象化；（藝術）抽象藝術；抽象作品；（技術、化學）提取，抽取；心不在焉，出神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>abstraction</b> is a general idea rather than one relating to a particular object, person, or situation. 抽象概念","examples":["Is it worth fighting a big war, in the name of an abstraction like sovereignty? 以象主權這樣一個抽象概念的名義，值得打一場大戰嗎？"]}]}]},"acceleration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加速，加快；（車輛）加速能力，加速幅度；加速度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>acceleration</b> <b>of</b> a process or change is the fact that it is getting faster and faster. 增速","examples":["He has also called for an acceleration of political reforms. 他也已呼籲加速政治改革。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Acceleration</b> is the rate at which a car or other vehicle can increase its speed, often seen in terms of the time that it takes to reach a particular speed. 加速幅度","examples":["Acceleration to 60 mph takes a mere 5.7 seconds. 加速到每小時60英里僅用5.7秒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Acceleration</b> is the rate at which the speed of an object increases. 加速度","examples":[]}]}]},"accessory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"附件，配件；裝飾品，配飾；同謀，從犯"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輔助的，副的；附屬的；同謀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Accessories</b> are items of equipment that are not usually essential, but can be used with or added to something else in order to make it more efficient, useful, or decorative. 附件","examples":["...an exclusive range of hand-made bedroom and bathroom accessories. …一個高檔系列的手工製作的臥室及衛生間裝置附件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Accessories</b> are articles such as belts and scarves which you wear or carry but which are not part of your main clothing. 配飾","examples":["It also has a good range of accessories, including sunglasses, handbags and belts. 它還有多種配飾，包括墨鏡、手包和皮帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is guilty of being an <b>accessory</b> <b>to</b> a crime, they helped the person who committed it, or knew it was being committed but did not tell the police. 從犯","examples":["She had been charged with being an accessory to the embezzlement of funds from a cooperative farm. 她已被指控為挪用一個合作農場資金的一個從犯。"]}]}]},"accordance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"按照，依據，與……一致（in accordance with）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>in accordance with</b> a particular rule or system, it is done in the way that the rule or system says that it should be done. 按照","examples":["Entries which are illegible or otherwise not in accordance with the rules will be disqualified. 難以辨認的或不符合這些規定的參賽作品將被取消資格。"]}]}]},"accord":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"協議，條約；符合，一致"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使受到，給予（某種待遇）；（與……）一致，符合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accord</b> between countries or groups of people is a formal agreement; for example, to end a war. 協議","examples":["UNITA was legalized as a political party under the 1991 peace accords. 根據1991年和平協議，安盟作為一個政黨被合法化了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are accorded</b> a particular kind of treatment, people act toward you or treat you in that way. 給予 (某種待遇)","examples":["His predecessor was accorded an equally tumultuous welcome. 他的前任受到了同樣熱烈的歡迎。","On his return home, the government accorded him the rank of Colonel. 在他回國時，該國政府授予他上校軍銜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>of its own accord</b>, it seems to happen by itself, without anyone making it happen. 自動地","examples":["In many cases the disease will clear up of its own accord. 在很多情況下這種疾病會自動地痊癒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>of</b> your <b>own accord</b>, you do it because you want to, without being asked or forced. 自願地","examples":["He did not quit as France's prime minister of his own accord. 他不是自願地辭去法國總理一職的。"]}]}]},"accommodation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>住宿，膳宿；<英>住處，辦公處，停留處；（樓房或交通工具內的）空間，座位；和解，調和；（透過改變眼球晶狀體形狀）自動調焦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Accommodation</b> is buildings or rooms where people live or stay. 住所","examples":["The government will provide temporary accommodation for up to three thousand homeless people. 政府將為多達三千無家可歸的人提供臨時住所。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Accommodation</b> is space in buildings or vehicles that is available for certain things, people, or activities. (樓內或車內等) 專用空間","examples":["Their offices are housed in rented accommodation in a modernized wing of the Mathematics Institute. 他們的辦公室坐落在數學研究所的現代化側樓的租賃樓層中。"]}]}]},"accumulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"積累，堆積；堆積物，堆積量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accumulation</b> <b>of</b> something is a large number of things that have been collected together or acquired over a period of time. 積累","examples":["...an accumulation of experience and knowledge. …經驗和知識的一種積累。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Accumulation</b> is the collecting together of things over a period of time. 積累","examples":["...the accumulation of capital and the distribution of income. …資金的積累和收入的分配。"]}]}]},"accounting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"會計，會計學；會計工作，會計職業（=accountancy）；賬單"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"解釋，說明；佔（一定數量或比例）（account 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Accounting</b> is the activity of keeping detailed records of the amounts of money a business or person receives and spends. 會計","examples":["...the accounting firm of Leventhal & Horwath. …利文撒爾與霍瓦特會計事務所。"]}]}]},"abuse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"虐待；濫用，辜負；辱罵；糟蹋（某物）；性侵犯"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"虐待，凌辱；濫用，妄用；辱罵；舞弊，腐敗；糟蹋；性侵犯；惡習，陋習"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Abuse</b> of someone is cruel and violent treatment of them. 虐待","examples":["...investigation of alleged child abuse. …對涉嫌虐待兒童的調查。","...victims of sexual and physical abuse. …性虐待和肉體摧殘的受害者們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Abuse</b> is extremely rude and insulting things that people say when they are angry. 辱罵","examples":["I was left shouting abuse as the car sped off. 當車加速離去時，我在那裡破口大罵。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Abuse</b> of something is the use of it in a wrong way or for a bad purpose. 濫用","examples":["What went on here was an abuse of power. 這裡發生的情況是職權的濫用。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is abused</b>, they are treated cruelly and violently. 虐待","examples":["Janet had been abused by her father since she was eleven. 詹妮特自從11歲起就被她的父親虐待。","...parents who feel they cannot cope or might abuse their children. …感到自己不能應付或可能虐待孩子的家長們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>is abused</b> if extremely rude and insulting things are said to them. 侮辱","examples":["He alleged that he was verbally abused by other soldiers. 他聲稱他被其他士兵們口頭侮辱了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>abuse</b> something, you use it in a wrong way or for a bad purpose. 濫用","examples":["He showed how the rich and powerful can abuse their position. 他揭露了有錢有勢的人會如何濫用他們的地位。"]}]}]},"accusation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"控告，指責，譴責；（尚未證實的被控告的）罪名，罪狀"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make an <b>accusation</b> against someone, you criticize them or express the belief that they have done something wrong. 指責","examples":["Kim rejects accusations that country music is over-sentimental. 金姆反駁了那些說鄉村音樂過於傷感的指責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>accusation</b> is a statement or claim by a witness or someone in authority that a particular person has committed a crime, although this has not yet been proved. 指控","examples":["...people who have made public accusations of rape. …對強姦進行了公開指控的人們。"]}]}]},"acquisition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學得，習得；（金錢、財物等的）獲取；購買，添置，增添物；收購，購置的產業"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company or business person makes an <b>acquisition</b>, they buy another company or part of a company. 收購","examples":["...the acquisition of a profitable paper recycling company. 對一家有利潤的廢紙回收公司的收購。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you make an <b>acquisition</b>, you buy or obtain something, often to add to things that you already have. 獲得","examples":["How did you go about making this marvellous acquisition then? 那麼你是怎麼著手進行這宗不可思議的購置的？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>acquisition</b> of a skill or a particular type of knowledge is the process of learning it or developing it. 習得","examples":["...language acquisition. …語言習得。"]}]}]},"activist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"積極分子，活動家"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"積極分子的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>activist</b> is a person who works to bring about political or social changes by campaigning in public or working for an organization. 激進分子","examples":["The police say they suspect the attack was carried out by animal rights activists. 警方說他們懷疑這次襲擊是由保護動物權利的激進分子實施的。","Dobson blames activist judges for undermining families with favourable gay-marriage rulings. 多布森責備激進派法官們透過贊成同性婚姻的裁決破壞家庭。"]}]}]},"addict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指毒品）上癮者，癮君子；<非正式>對……入迷的人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使上癮，使沉迷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>addict</b> is someone who takes harmful drugs and cannot stop taking them. (吸毒) 上癮者","examples":["He's only 24 years old and a drug addict. 他只有24歲，可已經是一個癮君子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is an <b>addict</b>, you mean that they like a particular activity very much and spend as much time doing it as they can. 對…入迷的人","examples":["She is a TV addict and watches as much as she can. 她是一個電視迷，看儘可能多的電視。"]}]}]},"administrator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司、學校等的）管理者，行政人員；（死者）遺產管理人，（債務人、其他個人或破產公司）資產管理人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>administrator</b> is a person whose job involves helping to organize and supervise the way that an organization or institution functions. 行政人員; 管理人員","examples":["On Friday the company's administrators sought permission from a Melbourne court to keep operating. 在星期五，該公司的管理人員們從一家墨爾本法院取得了繼續經營的許可。"]}]}]},"addiction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"癮；入迷，嗜好"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Addiction</b> is the condition of taking harmful drugs and being unable to stop taking them. (毒品) 癮","examples":["She helped him fight his drug addiction. 她幫助了他對抗自己的毒癮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>addiction</b> <b>to</b> something is a very strong desire or need for it. 癮","examples":["He needed money to feed his addiction to gambling. 他需要錢來滿足他的賭癮。"]}]}]},"aggression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"好鬥性，攻擊性；侵略，侵犯，挑釁"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aggression</b> is a quality of anger and determination that makes you ready to attack other people. 攻擊性","examples":["Aggression is by no means a male-only trait. 攻擊性決不是男性獨有的特徵。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Aggression</b> is violent and attacking behaviour. 攻擊","examples":["...the threat of massive military aggression. …大規模軍事攻擊的威脅。"]}]}]},"adaptation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"改編本，改寫本；適應，改變；適應（性），適應力；適應性變化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>adaptation</b> of a book or play is a film or a television programme that is based on it. 改編","examples":["Branagh won two awards for his screen adaptation of Shakespeare's Henry the Fifth. 布拉納因他對莎士比亞的《亨利五世》的熒幕改編而獲了兩次獎。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Adaptation</b> is the act of changing something or changing your behaviour to make it suitable for a new purpose or situation. 適應","examples":["Most living creatures are capable of adaptation when compelled to do so. 大多數生物在為情勢所迫時都能適應。"]}]}]},"alcoholic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"酒精的，含酒精的；酒精中毒的，酗酒的；喝酒引起的，由酒精引起的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"酗酒者，酒鬼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alcoholic</b> is someone who cannot stop drinking large amounts of alcohol, even when this is making them ill. 酗酒者","examples":["He showed great courage by admitting on television that he is an alcoholic. 他在電視上承認他是個酒鬼，表現出了極大的勇氣。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Alcoholic</b> drinks are drinks that contain alcohol. 含酒精的","examples":["The serving of alcoholic drinks was forbidden after six o'clock. 在6點以後供應酒精飲料是被禁止的。"]}]}]},"alliance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯盟，結盟；結盟團體，結盟國家；（人們間的）親密關係，（尤指）聯姻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alliance</b> is a group of countries or political parties that are formally united and working together because they have similar aims. 聯盟","examples":["The two parties were still too much apart to form an alliance. 這兩個黨派分歧大得還不能形成聯盟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>alliance</b> is a relationship in which two countries, political parties, or organizations work together for some purpose. 結盟","examples":["The Socialists' electoral strategy has been based on a tactical alliance with the Communists. 社會黨人的參選策略一直以和共產黨人的戰略性結盟為基礎。"]}]}]},"administration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"管理，行政；管理部門，行政部門；（某一任期的）政府；執行，監管；（藥的）服用，配給；遺產管理，（債務人、其他個人或破產公司的）資產管理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Administration</b> is the range of activities connected with organizing and supervising the way that an organization or institution functions. 行政工作; 管理工作","examples":["Too much time is spent on administration. 太多的時間花在了管理工作上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>administration</b> of something is the process of organizing and supervising it. 監管","examples":["Standards in the administration of justice have degenerated. 司法監管的標準已退化了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The administration</b> of a company or institution is the group of people who organize and supervise it. 管理層; 行政部門","examples":["They would like the college administration to exert more control over the fraternity. 他們希望該學院行政部門加大對該兄弟會的控制力度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can refer to a country's government as <b>the</b> <b>administration</b>; used especially in the United States. 政府 (尤用於美國)","examples":["O'Leary served in federal energy posts in both the Ford and Carter administrations. 奧利裡在福特政府和卡特政府期間都任過聯邦政府能源部門的職位。"]}]}]},"advocate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擁護，提倡"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擁護者，提倡者；辯護律師；（為某一類人）謀利益者；（一項事業或個組織的）工作者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>advocate</b> a particular action or plan, you recommend it publicly. 提倡","examples":["Mr. Williams is a conservative who advocates fewer government controls on business. 威廉斯先生是一位提倡減少政府對商業的控制的保守人士。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>advocate</b> <b>of</b> a particular action or plan is someone who recommends it publicly. 倡導者","examples":["He was a strong advocate of free market policies and a multi-party system. 他是自由市場政策以及多黨制的堅定倡導者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>advocate</b> for a particular group is a person who works for the interests of that group. 為 (某團體) 謀利益者","examples":["...advocates for the homeless. …為無家可歸者謀利益的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>advocate</b> is a lawyer who speaks in favour of someone or defends them in a court of law. 辯護律師","examples":[]}]}]},"ambiguity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模稜兩可，不明確；含混不清的語句；一語多義；曖昧，難以理解的感情（或想法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>ambiguity</b> in something, you mean that it is unclear or confusing, or it can be understood in more than one way. 模稜兩可","examples":["There is considerable ambiguity about what this part of the agreement actually means. 關於協議這一部分到底是什麼意思存在著相當大的含混不清。"]}]}]},"ambulance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"急救車，救護車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用救護車送（人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ambulance</b> is a vehicle for taking people to and from a hospital. 救護車","examples":[]}]}]},"alternative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可供選擇的事物，替代物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可替代的，備選的；非傳統的，另類的；（兩者）互不相容的，非此即彼的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is an <b>alternative</b> <b>to</b> another, the first can be found, used, or done instead of the second. 替代品","examples":["New ways to treat arthritis may provide an alternative to painkillers. 治療關節炎的新方法可能會提供一種止痛藥的替代品。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>alternative</b> plan or offer is different from the one that you already have, and can be done or used instead. 另外的","examples":["There were alternative methods of travel available. 有另外的旅行方式可採用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Alternative</b> is used to describe something that is different from the usual things of its kind, or the usual ways of doing something, in modern Western society. For example, an <b>alternative</b> lifestyle does not follow conventional ways of living and working. 另類的","examples":["...unconventional parents who embraced the alternative lifestyle of the Sixties. …信奉60年代另類生活方式的與眾不同的家長們。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Alternative</b> medicine uses traditional ways of curing people, such as medicines made from plants, massage, and acupuncture. 替代性的 (療法)","examples":["...alternative health care. …替代性保健。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Alternative</b> energy uses natural sources of energy such as the sun, wind, or water for power and fuel, rather than oil, coal, or nuclear power. 可再生的 (能源)","examples":[]}]}]},"analects":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短論選，短文選"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"selected literary passages from one or more works 文選","examples":[]}]}]},"ambush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n. n.","zh":"伏擊，埋伏"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"伏擊，埋伏突襲；突然向（某人）提出尷尬的問題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people <b>ambush</b> their enemies, they attack them after hiding and waiting for them. 伏擊","examples":["The Guatemalan army says rebels ambushed and killed 10 patrolmen. 瓜地馬拉軍方稱叛軍伏擊並殺死了10名巡邏兵。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ambush</b> is an attack on someone by people who have been hiding and waiting for them. 伏擊","examples":["Three civilians were killed in guerrilla ambushes. 3名平民在游擊隊的伏擊中喪生。"]}]}]},"analogy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"類比，比擬；用類比方法，進行比照；同功"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make or draw an <b>analogy</b> <b>between</b> two things, you show that they are similar in some way. 類比","examples":["The analogy between music and fragrance has stuck. 音樂與香味的類比已經深入人心了。"]}]}]},"analyst":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分析者，化驗員；心理分析師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>analyst</b> is a person whose job is to analyse a subject and give opinions about it. 分析師","examples":["...a political analyst. …一位政治分析家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>analyst</b> is someone, usually a doctor, who examines and treats people who have emotional problems. 心理分析師","examples":["My analyst warned me that I liked married men too much. 我的心理分析師警告過我太喜歡已婚男人。"]}]}]},"anchorman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞節目主持人，新聞主播；（討論）主持人；（接力賽等的）末棒運動員或（拔河等的）壓陣隊員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>anchorman</b> on a television or radio programme, especially a news programme, is the person who presents it. 電視或廣播中(尤指新聞節目的)男主持人","examples":[]}]}]},"anchorwoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廣播新聞的女主持人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>anchorwoman</b> on a television or radio programme, especially a news programme, is the woman who presents it. 電視或廣播中(尤指新聞節目的)女主持人","examples":[]}]}]},"anecdote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"軼事，趣聞；傳聞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>anecdote</b> is a short, amusing account of something that has happened. 趣聞軼事","examples":["Pete was telling them an anecdote about their mother. 皮特正告訴他們一個關於他們母親的趣聞軼事。"]}]}]},"annoyance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"煩惱，氣惱；令人惱火的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Annoyance</b> is the feeling that you get when someone makes you feel fairly angry or impatient. 厭煩","examples":["To her annoyance the stranger did not go away. 讓她厭煩的是這個陌生人沒有離開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>annoyance</b> is something that makes you feel angry or impatient. 煩人的事物","examples":["Snoring can be more than an annoyance. 打呼嚕不只是一樁煩人的事。"]}]}]},"antarctic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"(the Antarctic) 南極洲，南極地區"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"南極的，南極地帶的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>Antarctic</b> is the area around the South Pole. 南極洲","examples":[]}]}]},"antenna":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觸鬚，觸角；<美>天線；感覺，直覺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>antennae</b> of something such as an insect or crustacean are the two long, thin parts attached to its head that it uses to feel things with. 觸角","examples":[]}]}]},"antibody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（免疫）抗體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Antibodies</b> are substances that a person's or an animal's body produces in their blood in order to destroy substances that carry disease. 抗體","examples":["Such women carry antibodies which make their blood more likely to clot during pregnancy. 這樣的女性攜帶在孕期使她們的血液更可能凝結的抗體。"]}]}]},"antibiotic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抗生素，抗菌素"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（與）抗生素（有關）的，（與）抗菌素（有關）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Antibiotics</b> are medical drugs used to kill bacteria and treat infections. 抗生素","examples":["Your doctor may prescribe antibiotics. 你的大夫可能會開抗生素。"]}]}]},"anticipation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預期，預料；期盼，期望；先現音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anticipation</b> is a feeling of excitement about something pleasant or exciting that you know is going to happen. 期待","examples":["There's been an atmosphere of anticipation around here for a few days now. 一種期待的氛圍在這兒已存在幾天了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done <b>in anticipation of</b> an event, it is done because people believe that event is going to happen. 預期某事的發生","examples":["Troops in the Philippines have been put on full alert in anticipation of trouble during a planned general strike. 預期在計劃的總罷工期間會有麻煩，在菲律賓的軍隊已處於完全戒備狀態。"]}]}]},"antonym":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反義詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>antonym</b> of a word is a word that means the opposite. 反義詞","examples":[]}]}]},"apprentice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"學徒，徒弟；生手，新手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"收……為學徒；當學徒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>apprentice</b> is a young person who works for someone in order to learn their skill. 學徒","examples":["I started off as an apprentice and worked my way up. 我從學徒做起，然後一步一步做上來的。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a young person <b>is apprenticed</b> <b>to</b> someone, they go to work for them in order to learn their skill. 使做學徒","examples":["I was apprenticed to a plumber when I was fourteen. 我14歲時給一個管子工做學徒。"]}]}]},"aptitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"天資，天賦；自然的傾向，習性；適宜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>aptitude</b> <b>for</b> a particular kind of work or activity is their ability to learn it quickly and to do it well. 天資","examples":["He drifted into publishing and discovered an aptitude for working with accounts. 他偶入出版界，發現自己具有管賬的天資。"]}]}]},"arctic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"北極的；嚴寒的，極冷的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"北極，北極地區；防水套鞋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The Arctic</b> is the area of the world around the North Pole. It is extremely cold and there is very little light in winter and very little darkness in summer. 北極","examples":["...winter in the Arctic. …北極的冬天。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a place or the weather as <b>arctic</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely cold. 極冷的","examples":["The bathroom, with its spartan pre-war facilities, is positively arctic. 這個有簡陋戰前設施的浴室實在冷極了。"]}]}]},"artery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"動脈；幹線，幹道，幹流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Arteries</b> are the tubes in your body that carry blood from your heart to the rest of your body. Compare . 動脈","examples":["...patients suffering from blocked arteries. …患動脈堵塞的病人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an important main route within a complex road, railway, or river system as an <b>artery</b>. 幹線","examples":["...Connecticut Ave., one of the main arteries of Washington. …康涅狄格大道，華盛頓的主幹道之一。"]}]}]},"artifact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指有文化價值或歷史價值的）人工製品，歷史文物；非自然存在物體，假象（=artefact）"}],"sections":[]},"assessment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"評估，評價；估價，估計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>assessment</b> is a consideration of someone or something and a judgment about them. 評估","examples":["There is little assessment of the damage to the natural environment. 幾乎沒有有關自然環境破壞的評估。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>assessment</b> of the amount of money that something is worth or that should be paid is a calculation or estimate of the amount. 估算","examples":["Tax assessment is all about comparing values of similar properties. 稅金估算就是比較類似房產的價值。"]}]}]},"assumption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"假定，假設；取得，承擔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make an <b>assumption</b> <b>that</b> something is true or will happen, you accept that it is true or will happen, often without any real proof. 假設","examples":["You would be making an assumption that's not based on any fact that you could report. 你會做出不以你能報道的任何事實為依據的一種假設。"]}]}]},"asthma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"哮喘，氣喘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Asthma</b> is a lung condition that causes difficulty in breathing. 哮喘","examples":[]}]}]},"attainment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"達到，獲得；成就，造詣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>attainment</b> <b>of</b> an aim is the achieving of it. 獲得","examples":["...the attainment of independence. …獲得獨立。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>attainment</b> is a skill you have learned or something you have achieved. 技能; 成就","examples":["...their educational attainments. …他們的教育成就。"]}]}]},"asylum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"政治避難，政治庇護；<舊>精神病院"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a government gives a person from another country <b>asylum</b>, they allow them to stay, usually because they are unable to return home safely for political reasons. (給予通常因政治原因不能回國的人的) 避難許可","examples":["He applied for asylum in 1987 after fleeing the police back home. 他於1987年逃脫本國的警察之後申請了避難許可。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>asylum</b> is a psychiatric hospital. 精神病院","examples":[]}]}]},"attendant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"服務人員；侍從，隨從；護理者；隨員，助手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"伴隨的，隨之產生的；伺候的；陪伴的；到場的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>attendant</b> is someone whose job is to serve or help people in a place such as a petrol station or a car park. (加油站或停車場的) 服務員","examples":["Tony Williams was working as a car park attendant in Los Angeles. 託尼·威廉斯當時在洛杉磯的一個停車場做服務生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>attendants</b> at a wedding are people such as the bridesmaids and the ushers, who accompany or help the bride and groom. 婚禮隨員 (如迎賓招待員、儐相)","examples":["If the bride pays, she has the right to decide on the style of dress worn by her attendants. 如果新娘付費，她有權決定她的婚禮隨員穿什麼款式。"]}]}]},"attic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"閣樓，頂樓；<建>（簷部上方的）矮牆，樓層；<解剖>鼓室上隱窩；（古希臘）阿提卡方言，雅典方言（Attic）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（古希臘）阿提卡（語）的，雅典（語）的（Attic）；文雅的，簡潔典雅的（Attic）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>attic</b> is a room at the top of a house just below the roof. 閣樓","examples":[]}]}]},"auction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拍賣；（橋牌）叫牌階段"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"拍賣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>auction</b> is a public sale where items are sold to the person who offers the highest price. 拍賣","examples":["The painting is expected to fetch up to $400,000 at auction. 這幅畫預計在拍賣會上能賣到40萬美元。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is auctioned</b>, it is sold in an auction. 被拍賣","examples":["Eight drawings by French artist Jean Cocteau will be auctioned next week. 法國藝術家讓·科克託的8幅畫作將在下週拍賣。"]}]}]},"autograph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（名人的）親筆簽名；（作家或音樂家的）手稿，真跡；筆跡，字跡"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（名人）在……上簽名"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"親筆的；（畫，雕塑）真跡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>autograph</b> is the signature of someone famous that is specially written for a fan to keep. (名人的) 簽名","examples":["He went backstage and asked for her autograph. 他到後臺去要她的簽名。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone famous <b>autographs</b> something, they put their signature on it. 在…簽名","examples":["I autographed a copy of one of my books. 我在我的一本書上籤了名。"]}]}]},"aviation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"航空，飛行（術）；航空工業，飛機工業"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Aviation</b> is the operation and production of aircraft. 航空; 飛機製造業","examples":["...the aviation industry. …航空工業。"]}]}]},"beverage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飲料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beverages</b> are drinks. 飲料","examples":["Alcoholic beverages are served in the hotel lounge. 賓館的休息室供應酒類飲料。","...artificially sweetened beverages. …人工甜味飲料。"]}]}]},"barometer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣壓計，晴雨表；變化的標誌，指標"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>barometer</b> is an instrument that measures air pressure and shows when the weather is changing. 氣壓計","examples":["A man in camp took a barometer reading at half-hour intervals. 營地裡的一個人每半小時看一次氣壓計。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is a <b>barometer</b> <b>of</b> a particular situation, it indicates how things are changing or how things are likely to develop. 發展變化的指示計","examples":["In past presidential elections, Missouri has been a barometer of the rest of the country. 在過去的總統大選中，密蘇里州一直是該國其餘各州的晴雨表。"]}]}]},"autonomy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自治，自治權；獨立自主，自主權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Autonomy</b> is the control or government of a country, organization, or group by itself rather than by others. 自治","examples":["Activists stepped up their demands for local autonomy last month. 活動的積極分子上個月提高了其對地方自治的要求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Autonomy</b> is the ability to make your own decisions about what to do rather than being influenced by someone else or told what to do. 獨立自主","examples":["Each of the area managers enjoys considerable autonomy in the running of his own area. 每一位地區經理在各自主管的區域都享有相當大的自主權。"]}]}]},"binoculars":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"雙筒望遠鏡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Binoculars</b> consist of two small telescopes joined together side by side, which you look through in order to look at things that are a long distance away. 雙筒望遠鏡","examples":[]}]}]},"biochemistry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物化學；生物化學過程；生物的化學結構和特性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Biochemistry</b> is the study of the chemical processes that occur in living things. 生物化學","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>biochemistry</b> of a living thing is the chemical processes that occur in it or are involved in it. 生物化學過程","examples":["...the effects of air pollutants on the biochemistry of plants or animals. …大氣汙染物對植物或動物生化過程的影響。"]}]}]},"blunder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"跌跌撞撞地走，摸索；犯愚蠢的錯誤，出漏子；誤入，不小心陷入（困境）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"愚蠢的錯誤，疏忽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blunder</b> is a stupid or careless mistake. 愚蠢錯誤","examples":["I think he made a tactical blunder by announcing it so far ahead of time. 我認為他如此提早宣佈訊息是犯了戰術上的錯誤。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>blunder</b>, you make a stupid or careless mistake. 犯愚蠢錯誤","examples":["No doubt I had blundered again. 不用說我又犯了個蠢錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>blunder</b> <b>into</b> a dangerous or difficult situation, you get involved in it by mistake. 誤入 (危險境地或困境)","examples":["People wanted to know how they had blundered into war, and how to avoid it in the future. 人們想弄清他們怎麼會錯誤地捲入戰爭，將來如何才能避免這樣的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>blunder</b> somewhere, you move there in a clumsy and careless way. 跌跌撞撞地走","examples":["He had blundered into the table, upsetting the flowers. 他撞上了桌子，打翻了花。"]}]}]},"bias":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偏見，成見；偏好，天賦；傾向，趨勢；斜紋；（統計）偏差，偏倚；偏重心球形；偏壓，偏統"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使有偏見，使偏心；加偏壓（或偏流）於"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"偏斜的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"偏斜地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bias</b> is a tendency to prefer one person or thing to another, and to favour that person or thing. 偏見","examples":["...his desire to avoid the appearance of bias in favour of one candidate or another. …他想避免表現出對這個或那個候選人有偏好。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>bias</b> someone means to influence them in favour of a particular choice. (影響某人) 使偏心; 使產生偏見","examples":["We mustn't allow it to bias our teaching. 我們不允許它使我們的教學產生偏見。"]}]}]},"bondage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奴役，束縛；施虐性行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bondage</b> is the condition of being someone's property and having to work for them. 奴役","examples":["Masters sometimes allowed their slaves to buy their way out of bondage. 主人們有時候允許奴隸贖身。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bondage</b> is the condition of not being free because you are strongly influenced by something or someone. 束縛","examples":["All people, she said, lived their lives in bondage to hunger, pain and lust. 她說所有人都生活在飢餓、痛苦和慾望的束縛之中。"]}]}]},"breakup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（婚姻、戀愛、合夥關係等的）分手，破裂，散夥；（組織、公司、國家等的）解體，分裂，拆分；（物體等的）碎裂，瓦解"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>breakup</b> <b>of</b> a marriage, relationship, or association is the act of it finishing or coming to an end because the people involved decide that it is not working successfully. (婚姻、關係、聯絡等的) 破裂","examples":["...the acrimonious breakup of the meeting's first session. …惡言相向後該會議第一輪的破裂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>breakup</b> <b>of</b> an organization or a country is the act of it separating or dividing into several parts. (組織、國家的) 解體","examples":["The Justice Department advocated a breakup of Microsoft. 司法部主張微軟公司解體。"]}]}]},"boycott":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"抵制，拒絕參加"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抵制行動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country, group, or person <b>boycotts</b> a country, organization, or activity, they refuse to be involved with it in any way because they disapprove of it. 聯合抵制","examples":["The main opposition parties are boycotting the elections. 主要的反對黨派正在聯合抵制選舉。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boycott</b> is also a noun. 聯合抵制","examples":["Opposition leaders had called for a boycott of the vote. 反對派領導者號召聯合抵制投票。"]}]}]},"bout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發作，發病期；一陣，一次，一場；拳擊賽，摔跤比賽；（小提琴、吉他或其他樂器邊緣的）曲線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>bout</b> <b>of</b> an illness or of an unpleasant feeling, you have it for a short period. (疾病或不愉快情緒) 發作","examples":["He was recovering from a severe bout of flu. 他當時正從一次嚴重的流感中康復。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bout</b> <b>of</b> something that is unpleasant is a short time during which it occurs a great deal. 爆發","examples":["The latest bout of violence has claimed twenty four lives. 最近的一次暴力事件造成了24人死亡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>bout</b> is a boxing or wrestling match. 拳擊 (或摔跤) 比賽","examples":["This will be his eighth title bout in 19 months. 這將是他19個月中的第八次比賽奪冠。"]}]}]},"boost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使增長，推動；<美，非正式>偷竊；宣揚，推廣"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"推動，促進；廣告，宣揚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>boosts</b> another, it causes it to increase, improve, or be more successful. 促進","examples":["Lower interest rates can boost the economy by reducing borrowing costs for consumers and businesses. 低利率可以透過為消費者和商家降低借貸成本來促進經濟發展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>boosts</b> your confidence or morale, it improves it. 增強 (信心、士氣)","examples":["We need a big win to boost our confidence. 我們需要一個大的勝利來增強我們的自信心。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Boost</b> is also a noun. 推動力","examples":["It would get the economy going and give us the boost that we need. 這會推動經濟發展並帶給我們所需要的推動力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Boost</b> is also a noun. (信心、士氣的) 增強","examples":["It did give me a boost to win such a big event. 贏了這麼一場大型比賽，的確使我士氣大振。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>boost</b>, you push or lift them from behind so that they can reach something. 推; 託","examples":["He cupped his hands and gave her a boost up to the ledge. 他雙手攏作杯狀把她託上了窗臺。"]}]}]},"breakthrough":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"突破，重大進展"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>breakthrough</b> is an important development or achievement. 突破","examples":["The company looks poised to make a significant breakthrough in China. 該公司看上去穩將在中國實現一次重大突破。"]}]}]},"breakdown":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（汽車或機器的）故障，損壞；（關係的）破裂，（系統的）癱瘓；精神崩潰，（健康、體力等的）衰竭；細目，分類；分解；跺腳曳步舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>breakdown</b> <b>of</b> something such as a relationship, plan, or discussion is its failure or ending. (關係、計劃、討論等的) 失敗; 結束","examples":["...the breakdown of talks between the U.S. and E.U. officials. …美國與歐盟官員會談的失敗。","...the irretrievable breakdown of a marriage. …無法挽回的一場婚姻的破裂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>breakdown</b>, you become very depressed, so that you are unable to cope with your life. 精神崩潰","examples":["My personal life was terrible. My mother had died, and a couple of years later I had a breakdown. 我的個人生活糟透了。母親去世了,幾年後我精神崩潰了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a car or a piece of machinery has a <b>breakdown</b>, it stops working. 故障","examples":["Her old car was unreliable, so the trip was plagued by breakdowns. 她的舊車效能不可靠,所以旅途被故障所困擾。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>breakdown</b> <b>of</b> something is a list of its separate parts. 細目列表","examples":["The organizers were given a breakdown of the costs. 組織者們被給了一份花銷細目。"]}]}]},"brink":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊緣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the</b> <b>brink</b> <b>of</b> something, usually something important, terrible, or exciting, you are just about to do it or experience it. 邊緣","examples":["Their economy is teetering on the brink of collapse. 他們的經濟正搖擺於崩潰的邊緣。"]}]}]},"brew":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"沏（茶），衝（咖啡）；釀（啤酒）；醞釀，即將來臨"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"啤酒；茶，咖啡；交融，混合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>brew</b> tea or coffee, you make it by pouring hot water over tea leaves or ground coffee. 沖泡 (茶、咖啡等)","examples":["He brewed a pot of coffee. 他衝了一壺咖啡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person or company <b>brews</b> beer, they make it. 釀造 (啤酒)","examples":["I brew my own beer. 我釀造自己的啤酒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brew</b> is a particular kind of tea or coffee. It can also be a particular pot of tea or coffee. (茶或咖啡的) 種類","examples":["She swallowed a mouthful of the hot strong brew, and wiped her eyes. 她嚥下一大口熱濃茶,然後擦了擦眼睛。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a storm <b>is brewing</b>, large clouds are beginning to form and the sky is becoming dark because there is going to be a storm. (暴風雨) 醞釀","examples":["We'd seen the storm brewing when we were out in the boat. 我們乘船外出時看到了暴風雨正在醞釀之中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an unpleasant or difficult situation <b>is brewing</b>, it is starting to develop. (危機、困境等) 醞釀","examples":["At home a crisis was brewing. 家裡一場危機正在醞釀著。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to devise or plan 籌劃","examples":[]}]}]},"brochure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小冊子，資料（或廣告）手冊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brochure</b> is a thin magazine with pictures that gives you information about a product or service. 小冊子","examples":["...travel brochures. …旅遊小冊子。"]}]}]},"brute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"粗野的人，殘忍的人；強壯的男子；大野獸，牲畜；笨重難看的東西，麻煩事"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不理智的，野獸似的；蠻幹不動腦筋的；根本而令人不快的，赤裸裸的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you call someone, usually a man, a <b>brute</b>, you mean that they are rough, violent, and insensitive. 粗暴的人 (通常指男性)","examples":["Custer was an idiot and a brute and he deserved his fate. 卡斯特是個愚蠢而粗暴的人，他應該有這樣的下場。"]}]}]},"bureaucracy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"官僚制度，官僚機構，官僚作風；官僚，政府官員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bureaucracy</b> is an administrative system operated by a large number of officials. 官僚體制","examples":["State bureaucracies can tend to stifle enterprise and initiative. 國家官僚體制會壓抑人的進取心和積極性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bureaucracy</b> refers to all the rules and procedures followed by government departments and similar organizations, especially when you think that these are complicated and cause long delays. 官僚作風","examples":["People usually complain about too much bureaucracy. 人們通常會抱怨過多的官僚作風。"]}]}]},"burial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"埋葬，葬禮；葬地，墳墓"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"埋葬的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>burial</b> is the act or ceremony of putting a dead body into a grave in the ground. 埋葬; 葬禮","examples":["The priest prepared the body for burial. 牧師為屍體做好了下葬的準備。"]}]}]},"buckle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"發軟；屈服，讓步；（人）精神崩潰；（使）彎曲，（使）變形；扣住，扣緊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（皮帶等的）搭扣，搭鉤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>buckle</b> is a piece of metal or plastic attached to one end of a belt or strap, which is used to fasten it. (皮帶等的) 帶扣","examples":["He wore a belt with a large brass buckle. 他繫了一根有很大黃銅釦的皮帶。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>buckle</b> a belt or strap, you fasten it. 扣緊","examples":["A door slammed in the house and a man came out buckling his belt. 屋子裡門砰地關上了，一名男子一邊扣著皮帶一邊走了出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an object <b>buckles</b> or if something <b>buckles</b> it, it becomes bent as a result of very great heat or force. 使彎曲; (因受熱或受壓而) 變彎","examples":["The door was beginning to buckle from the intense heat. 由於高溫，門正開始變彎。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If your legs or knees <b>buckle</b>, they bend because they have become very weak or tired. (腿、膝) 發軟彎曲","examples":["Mcanally's knees buckled and he crumpled down onto the floor. 麥卡納利雙膝發軟彎了下去，癱倒在地板上。"]}]}]},"byte":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"位元組，8 位元組（計算機中由 8 個二進位制位組成的資料單位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In computing, a <b>byte</b> is a unit of storage approximately equivalent to one printed character. 位元組","examples":["...two million bytes of data. …200萬位元組的資料。"]}]}]},"caffeine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"[有化][藥] 咖啡因；茶精（興奮劑）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Caffeine</b> is a chemical substance found in coffee, tea, and cocoa, which affects your brain and body and makes you more active. 咖啡因","examples":[]}]}]},"calcium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（化學元素）鈣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Calcium</b> is a soft white chemical element which is found in bones and teeth, and also in limestone, chalk, and marble. 鈣","examples":[]}]}]},"canvas":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"帆布；畫布，油畫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用帆布覆蓋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Canvas</b> is a strong, heavy cloth that is used for making things such as tents, sails, and bags. 帆布","examples":["...a canvas bag. …一個帆布包。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>canvas</b> is a piece of canvas or similar material on which an oil painting can be done. 油畫布","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>canvas</b> is a painting that has been done on canvas. 帆布油畫","examples":["The show includes canvases by masters like Carpaccio, Canaletto and Guardi. 展覽包括卡巴秋、卡納列託和瓜第等大師的帆布油畫。"]}]}]},"capability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能力，才能；（國家的）軍事力量；計算機效能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have the <b>capability</b> or the <b>capabilities</b> to do something, you have the ability or the qualities that are necessary to do it. 能力; 才能","examples":["People experience differences in physical and mental capability depending on the time of day. 視一天中的不同時候而定，人們會經歷體能和智慧上的差異。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A country's military <b>capability</b> is its ability to fight in a war. 軍事力量","examples":["Their military capability has gone down because their air force has proved not to be an effective force. 他們的軍事力量已經削弱了，因為其空軍被證明不是一隻有戰鬥力的隊伍。"]}]}]},"caption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（圖片的）說明文字；（電影或電視的）字幕；（法律檔案的）開端部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……加文字說明"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>caption</b> is the words printed underneath a picture or cartoon which explain what it is about. (圖片或卡通的) 說明文字","examples":["The local paper featured me standing on a stepladder with a caption, \"Wendy climbs the ladder to success.\" 當地的報紙刊登了一幅我站在活梯上的特寫，下面寫著：“溫迪登上了成功之梯。”"]}]}]},"capsule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膠囊；小容器；太空艙，航天艙；蒴果，莢膜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"簡短的；壓縮的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓縮；簡述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>capsule</b> is a very small tube containing powdered or liquid medicine, which you swallow. (裝藥的) 膠囊","examples":["...cod liver oil capsules. …鱈魚魚肝油膠囊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>capsule</b> is a small container with a drug or other substance inside it, which is used for medical or scientific purposes. (用於醫學或科學目的的) 小容器","examples":["They first implanted capsules into the animals' brains. 他們先將膠囊植入那些動物的大腦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A space <b>capsule</b> is the part of a spacecraft in which people travel, and which often separates from the main rocket. 太空艙","examples":["A Russian space capsule is currently orbiting the Earth. 一個俄羅斯太空艙目前正環繞地球飛行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A time <b>capsule</b> is a container into which people put typical everyday objects from their lives. The container is buried so that people in the future can dig it up, and find out about what life was like in the past. 時光寶盒 (指裝入日常用品後埋於地下，有待後來人挖掘以便了解過去的盒子)","examples":["Twenty-five years ago they filled a time capsule and buried it. 25年前，他們裝滿一個時光寶盒並把它埋了起來。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a dry fruit that liberates its seeds by splitting, as in the violet, or through pores, as in the poppy 蒴果","examples":[]}]}]},"captive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"被俘虜的，被圈養的；受限制的，受控制的；（裝置，服務）受壟斷的；被迷住的，被吸引的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"俘虜，獵獲物；被迷住的人，被吸引的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>captive</b> person or animal is being kept imprisoned or enclosed. 被囚禁的; 被圈養的","examples":["Her heart had begun to pound inside her chest like a captive animal. 她心如鹿撞，怦怦跳個不停。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>captive</b> audience is a group of people who are not free to leave a certain place and so have to watch or listen. A <b>captive</b> market is a group of people who cannot choose whether or where to buy things. (觀眾) 不能隨意離開的; (市場) 被壟斷的","examples":["We all performed action songs, sketches, and dances before a captive audience of parents and patrons. 我們都表演了帶動作的歌曲、短劇和舞蹈給父母和贊助人這類被動觀眾看。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>captive</b> is someone who is captive. 被囚禁者","examples":["He described the difficulties of surviving for four months as a captive. 他講述了淪為階下囚的4個月中生存的種種不易。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take</b> someone <b>captive</b> or <b>hold</b> someone <b>captive</b>, you take or keep them as a prisoner. 囚禁某人","examples":["Richard was finally released on February 4, one year and six weeks after he'd been taken captive. 理查德經歷了1年零6周的囚禁之後，終於在2月4日被釋放。"]}]}]},"carbohydrate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碳水化合物，糖類；含碳水化合物的食物，糖類食物；含碳水化合物的食物，糖類食物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Carbohydrates</b> are substances, found in certain kinds of food, that provide you with energy. Foods such as sugar and bread that contain these substances can also be referred to as <b>carbohydrates</b>. (為身體提供熱量的) 碳水化合物; 含碳水化合物的食物","examples":["...carbohydrates such as bread, pasta, or potatoes. …含碳水化合物的食物，如麵包、義大利麵或馬鈴薯。"]}]}]},"captivity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"囚禁，被關，監禁；（動物的）圈養，關養"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Captivity</b> is the state of being kept imprisoned or enclosed. 囚禁; 圈養","examples":["The great majority of barn owls are reared in captivity. 絕大多數倉鴞是圈養的。"]}]}]},"cashier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收銀員，出納員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開除，革除（軍職）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cashier</b> is a person who customers pay money to or get money from in places such as stores or banks. 出納員; 收銀員","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to dismiss with dishonour, esp from the armed forces (因不誠實而被)開除","examples":[]}]}]},"casualty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傷亡人員；受害者，毀壞物；急診室，急救室；事故，災難（主要用於保險中）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>casualty</b> is a person who is injured or killed in a war or in an accident. 死傷者","examples":["Troops fired on the demonstrators causing many casualties. 軍隊向示威的人群開火，造成不少傷亡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>casualty</b> <b>of</b> a particular event or situation is a person or a thing that has suffered badly as a result of that event or situation. 受害者","examples":["The car industry has been one of the greatest casualties of the recession. 汽車工業是經濟不景氣最大的受害者之一。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Casualty</b> is the part of a hospital where people who have severe injuries or sudden illnesses are taken for emergency treatment. 急救室","examples":[]}]}]},"caress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"愛撫，親吻；輕觸，輕拍"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"愛撫，親吻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>caress</b> someone or something, you stroke them gently and affectionately. 撫摸","examples":["He was gently caressing her golden hair. 他正溫柔地撫摸著她的金髮。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Caress</b> is also a noun. 撫摸","examples":["Margaret took me to one side, holding my arm in a gentle caress. 瑪格麗特把我拉到一旁，輕輕地撫弄著我的手臂。"]}]}]},"carol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（聖誕）頌歌（=Christmas carol）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（歡快地）唱（歌），說（話）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Carols</b> are Christian religious songs that are sung at Christmas. 聖誕頌歌","examples":["The singing of Christmas carols is a custom derived from early dance routines of pagan origin. 唱聖誕歌這一傳統源自異教早期的舞蹈儀式。"]}]}]},"catastrophe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"災難，災禍；麻煩，困境；慘敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>catastrophe</b> is an unexpected event that causes great suffering or damage. 災難","examples":["From all points of view, war would be a catastrophe. 從各個方面來看，戰爭都會是一場災難。"]}]}]},"cemetery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公墓，墓地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cemetery</b> is a place where dead people's bodies or their ashes are buried. 墓地","examples":[]}]}]},"cavity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洞，腔；(牙齒的) 齲洞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cavity</b> is a space or hole in something such as a solid object or a person's body. 洞; 腔","examples":["...a cavity in the roof. …屋頂的一個洞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In dentistry, a <b>cavity</b> is a hole in a tooth, caused by decay. (牙齒的) 齲洞","examples":[]}]}]},"certainty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"確實，確定性；確實的事，必然的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Certainty</b> is the state of being definite or of having no doubts at all about something. 確定","examples":["I have told them with absolute certainty there'll be no change of policy. 我十分確定地告訴他們政策不會有變。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Certainty</b> is the fact that something is certain to happen. 必然的事","examples":["A general election became a certainty last week. 普選上週已成必然。","...the certainty of more violence and bloodshed. …必然會有的更多的暴力和流血事件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Certainties</b> are things that nobody has any doubts about. 確定的事","examples":["There are no certainties in modern Europe. 現代歐洲無定事。"]}]}]},"champagne":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香檳酒；香檳色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Champagne</b> is an expensive French white wine with bubbles in. It is often drunk to celebrate something. 香檳酒","examples":[]}]}]},"chaos":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"混亂，無秩序狀態；混沌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chaos</b> is a state of complete disorder and confusion. 混亂","examples":["The world's first transatlantic balloon race ended in chaos last night. 世界首次橫渡大西洋的氣球比賽昨晚在混亂中結束了。"]}]}]},"charcoal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木炭；（繪畫用的）炭筆，木炭條；木炭畫；深灰色"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"炭黑色的，灰黑色的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用木炭條繪畫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Charcoal</b> is a black substance obtained by burning wood without much air. It can be burned as a fuel, and small sticks of it are used for drawing. 木炭","examples":[]}]}]},"chariot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"古代由馬牽引的雙輪戰車，用於戰爭、競賽或儀式；（舊時用語）輕便四輪禮賓馬車；大寫 Chariot（人名，法語姓氏，常譯作“沙里奧”）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（罕）駕馭（戰車）；用戰車運送"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（罕）乘戰車；駕馭戰車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In ancient times, <b>chariots</b> were fast-moving vehicles with two wheels that were pulled by horses. 雙輪馬車","examples":[]}]}]},"cholesterol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膽固醇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cholesterol</b> is a substance that exists in the fat, tissues, and blood of all animals. Too much cholesterol in a person's blood can cause heart disease. 膽固醇","examples":["...a dangerously high cholesterol level. …一個危險的高膽固醇水平。"]}]}]},"chuckle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"輕聲笑，暗自笑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輕笑，暗笑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>chuckle</b>, you laugh quietly. 輕聲地笑","examples":["The banker chuckled and said, \"Of course not.\" 銀行家輕聲笑了，說道，“當然不。”"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Chuckle</b> is also a noun. 輕聲笑","examples":["He gave a little chuckle. 他輕聲一笑。"]}]}]},"cavalry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"騎兵，騎兵部隊；裝甲兵，裝甲部隊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>cavalry</b> is the part of an army that uses armoured vehicles for fighting. 裝甲部隊","examples":["The 3rd Cavalry went on the offensive. 第3裝甲兵團繼續發動進攻。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>cavalry</b> is the group of soldiers in an army who ride horses. 騎兵團","examples":["...a young cavalry officer. …一位年輕的騎兵軍官。"]}]}]},"clarity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"清晰易懂；思路清晰；（畫面或聲音的）清晰，清楚；清澈，明淨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>clarity</b> of something such as a book or argument is its quality of being well explained and easy to understand. 明晰; 清楚","examples":["...the ease and clarity with which the author explains difficult technical and scientific subjects. …該作者用於解釋難懂的科技主題的輕鬆與明晰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Clarity</b> is the ability to think clearly. (思路的) 清晰","examples":["In business circles he is noted for his flair and clarity of vision. 在商界，他以其風度與犀利的眼光而聞名。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Clarity</b> is the quality of being clear in outline or sound. (指輪廓、聲音等) 清晰","examples":["This remarkable technology provides far greater clarity than conventional x-rays. 這一非凡技術提供了比傳統的X光要高得多的清晰度。"]}]}]},"closure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（永久的）關閉，倒閉；（尤指通路、邊境的）封鎖；（討論、寫作、活動或事件的）結尾；（事件或一段時間的）了結，解脫感；（立法院）辯論終止提付表決；認栽；閉鎖物（如帽子、領帶）；（夾克等）閉合方式"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（在立法會議上）終止（辯論，發言）；使終止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>closure</b> of a place such as a business or factory is the permanent ending of the work or activity there. 倒閉; 關閉","examples":["...the closure of the steel mill. …這家鋼廠的關閉。","...protests against the proposed pit closures. …針對關閉礦井計劃的抗議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>closure</b> of a road or border is the blocking of it in order to prevent people from using it. (道路、邊界等的) 封閉","examples":["Overnight storms left many streets underwater and forced the closure of road tunnels in the city. 一夜的暴風雨使城市裡的許多街道都淹沒在水中，公路隧道被迫封閉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone achieves <b>closure</b>, they succeed in accepting something bad that has happened to them. 認栽","examples":["I asked McKean if the reunion was meant to achieve closure. 我問邁可基恩再度聯合是否意味著認栽。"]}]}]},"coffin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"棺材"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把（屍體）裝入棺材；收殮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coffin</b> is a box in which a dead body is buried or cremated. 棺材","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that one thing is <b>a nail in</b> <b>the</b> <b>coffin</b> <b>of</b> another thing, you mean that it will help bring about its end or failure. 斷送","examples":["A fine would be the final nail in the coffin of the airline. 一筆罰款將最終斷送該航線。"]}]}]},"clamp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用夾具）夾緊，夾住；緊緊抓住，牢牢固定住；<英>給（車輛）上夾鉗；保持（電訊號）電壓極限在規定水平"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"夾具，夾鉗；車輪固定夾；鉗位電路；（窯內的）磚垛；（保護塊根作物越冬的）草皮堆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>clamp</b> is a device that holds two things firmly together. 夾具","examples":["Many openers have a magnet or set of clamps to grip the open lid. 許多開啟器是用磁鐵或夾具來夾緊要開啟的蓋子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clamp</b> is a large metal device which is attached to the wheel of an illegally parked car or other vehicle in order to prevent it from being driven away. The driver has to pay to have the device removed. 丹佛鎖釦 (用來鉗鎖違章停車的汽車輪子)","examples":["I watched a couple of cops put a clamp on a green Mercedes. 我看到幾個警察給一輛綠色賓士車加上丹佛鎖釦。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>clamp</b> one thing <b>to</b> another, you fasten the two things together with a clamp. 用 (夾具) 夾緊","examples":["Somebody forgot to bring along the U-bolts to clamp the microphones to the pole. 有人忘記帶來把麥克風夾在支桿上的U型螺栓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>clamp</b> something in a particular place means to put it or hold it there firmly and tightly. 把…夾緊; 固定","examples":["Simon finished dialling and clamped the phone to his ear. 西蒙撥完號碼，把話筒緊夾在耳朵上。","He clamped his lips together. 他緊閉雙唇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"To <b>clamp</b> an illegally parked car means to fit a device to one of its wheels so that it cannot be driven away. 鎖釦 (違章停放的車輛)","examples":["Though the city will no longer clamp cars, illegally parked vehicles will be towed. 儘管該城將不再鎖釦車輛，違規停放的車輛將被拖走。"]}]}]},"clench":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"攥緊（拳頭等），咬緊（牙齒等）；緊握，緊咬"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（身體部位的）緊縮，緊繃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>clench</b> your fist or your fist <b>clenches</b>, you curl your fingers up tightly, usually because you are very angry. (常指因生氣而) 握緊 (拳頭)","examples":["Alex clenched her fists and gritted her teeth. 亞麗克斯握緊拳頭，咬緊牙。","She pulled at his sleeve and he turned on her, fists clenching again before he saw who it was. 她扯了扯他的袖子，他惡洶洶地轉過身，在看見她是誰之前又再次握緊了拳頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>clench</b> your teeth or they <b>clench</b>, you squeeze your teeth together firmly, usually because you are angry or upset. (常指因生氣或不安而) 咬緊 (牙)","examples":["Patsy had to clench her jaw to suppress her anger. 帕茜不得不咬緊牙關來壓下怒火。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>clench</b> something in your hand or in your teeth, you hold it tightly with your hand or your teeth. 握緊; 咬緊","examples":["I clenched the arms of my chair. 我緊緊握住我的椅子扶手。"]}]}]},"clearance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"稽核批准；（飛機起降的）許可，准許；間距，間隙；清理，清除；（足球等中使對方不能破門的）解圍；（銀行支票的）結算，兌現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Clearance</b> is the removal of old buildings, trees, or other things that are not wanted from an area. 拆除; 清除","examples":["The U.N. pledged to help supervise the clearance of mines. 聯合國承諾幫助監督掃雷工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you get <b>clearance</b> <b>to</b> do or have something, you get official approval or permission to do or have it. 官方許可","examples":["Thai Airways said the plane had been given clearance to land. 泰國航空公司說該飛機已經被授予了著陸的官方許可。"]}]}]},"clone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動植物的）無性繁殖，克隆；極為相似的人（或事物），複製品；仿製品，山寨貨；複製器，仿製機；<非正式>外表或著裝誇大男性氣概的男同性戀者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"克隆，使無性繁殖；盜用（他人的手機號碼），非法複製"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is a <b>clone</b> of another person or thing, they are so similar to this person or thing that they seem to be exactly the same as them. 翻版","examples":["Tom was in some ways a younger clone of his handsome father. 湯姆在某些方面是他英俊父親年輕時的翻版。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>clone</b> is an animal or plant that has been produced artificially, for example in a laboratory, from the cells of another animal or plant. A clone is exactly the same as the original animal or plant. 克隆","examples":["...the world's first human clone. …世界上第一個克隆人。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>clone</b> an animal or plant means to produce it as a clone. 對…進行克隆","examples":["The idea of cloning extinct life forms still belongs to science fiction. 對絕種的生命形式進行克隆的想法仍然屬於科學幻想。"]}]}]},"coincidence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巧合，同時發生；相符，一致；符合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>coincidence</b> is when two or more similar or related events occur at the same time by chance and without any planning. 巧合","examples":["Mr. Berry said the timing was a coincidence and that his decision was unrelated to Mr. Roman's departure. 貝里先生說時間的安排是個巧合，而且他的決策與羅曼先生的離去毫無關係。"]}]}]},"chunk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大塊，厚塊；大量，大部分；話語組成部分，組塊；矮胖的（男）人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……分成數份；將……組合（或歸類）；扔，拋；發出“砰啷”聲；切分，切割（資料）"}],"sections":[]},"collector":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收藏家，收集者；收稅員，徵收者，收取人（如收票員、清潔工）；（電子）集電極；收集器，如太陽能集熱器、集塵器、集電器等裝置；（計算機）垃圾回收器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>collector</b> is a person who collects things of a particular type as a hobby. 收藏家","examples":["...a stamp collector. …一位集郵者。","...a respected collector of Indian art. …一位受人尊敬的印第安藝術品收藏家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>collector</b> to refer to someone whose job is to take something such as money, tickets, or rubbish from people. For example, a rent <b>collector</b> collects rent from people. (錢款、票據或垃圾的) 收取人","examples":["He earned his living as a tax collector. 他做收稅員謀生。"]}]}]},"collective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"集體的，共同的；總的，集合的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"集體農莊，集體企業；集合名詞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Collective</b> actions, situations, or feelings involve or are shared by every member of a group of people. 集體的","examples":["It was a collective decision. 這是集體的決定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>collective</b> amount of something is the total obtained by adding together the amounts that each person or thing in a group has. 總體的","examples":["Their collective volume wasn't very large. 他們總體的數量不太大。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>collective</b> term for two or more types of thing is a general word or expression which refers to all of them. 總的","examples":["Social science is a collective name, covering a series of individual sciences. 社會科學是一個總稱，涵蓋一系列獨立學科。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"集體地","examples":["They collectively decided to recognize the changed situation. 他們集體決定承認局勢的變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"總體地","examples":["In 1968 the states collectively spent $2 billion on it. 1968年各州總體為此花了20億美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"總地","examples":["...other sorts of cells (known collectively as white corpuscles). …其他幾種細胞（總稱白血球）。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>collective</b> is a business or farm which is run, and often owned, by a group of people. 集體企業; 集體農莊","examples":["He will see that he is participating in all the decisions of the collective. 他要確保他在參與集體企業的所有決策。"]}]}]},"columnist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專欄作家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>columnist</b> is a journalist who regularly writes a particular kind of article in a newspaper or magazine. 專欄記者","examples":["Clarence Page is a columnist for the Chicago Tribune. 克拉倫斯·佩奇是《芝加哥論壇報》的專欄記者。"]}]}]},"commentary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現場解說，實況報道；評註性著作，評論文；討論，評論；說明，寫照"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>commentary</b> is a description of an event that is broadcast on radio or television while the event is taking place. 實況報道","examples":["He gave the listening crowd a running commentary. 他為聽眾進行了實況報道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commentary</b> is an article or book which explains or discusses something. 評論性文章 (或書籍)","examples":["Ms. Rich will be writing a twice-weekly commentary on American society and culture. 裡奇女士將就美國社會和文化每週寫兩篇評論文章。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Commentary</b> is discussion or criticism of something. 評論","examples":["The show mixed comedy with social commentary. 這個節目把喜劇和社會評論結合了起來。"]}]}]},"companionship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"情誼，友誼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Companionship</b> is having someone you know and like with you, instead of being on your own. 陪伴","examples":["I depended on his companionship and on his judgment. 我依賴他的陪伴和他的判斷。"]}]}]},"collision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碰撞，相撞；衝突，牴觸；爭用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>collision</b> occurs when a moving object crashes into something. 碰撞","examples":["They were on their way to the airport when their van was involved in a collision with a car. 他們正往機場趕路的時候，其貨車和一輛小汽車相撞了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>collision</b> <b>of</b> cultures or ideas occurs when two very different cultures or people meet and conflict. (文化或觀點的) 衝突","examples":["The play represents the collision of three generations. 該劇表現了3代人之間的衝突。"]}]}]},"commitment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"忠誠，獻身；承諾，保證；奉獻，投入；熱情，決心；義務，責任；花費，使用（資金、時間、人力）；需要定期支付的款項"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Commitment</b> is a strong belief in an idea or system. 信奉","examples":["...commitment to the ideals of democracy. …對民主理想的信奉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>commitment</b> is something which regularly takes up some of your time because of an agreement you have made or because of responsibilities that you have. 投身的事","examples":["I've got a lot of commitments. 我有很多要做的事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you make a <b>commitment</b> <b>to</b> do something, you promise that you will do it. 承諾","examples":["We made a commitment to keep working together. 我們作了承諾要繼續在一起工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Commitment</b> is the process of officially sending someone to a prison or a hospital. 送交 (監獄、醫院)","examples":[]}]}]},"compensation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賠償金，補償金；彌補，抵消；報酬，薪水"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Compensation</b> is money that someone who has experienced loss or suffering claims from the person or organization responsible, or from the state. 補償金","examples":["He received one year's salary as compensation for loss of office. 他得到一年的薪水作為失去職位的補償金。","They want $20,000 in compensation for each of about 500 claimants. 他們想要給約500個投訴者每人2萬美元作為補償金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is some <b>compensation</b> <b>for</b> something bad that has happened, it makes you feel better. 補償","examples":["Helen gained some compensation for her earlier defeat by winning the final open class. 海倫透過贏得公開賽的決賽獲得了對先前失利的一些補償。"]}]}]},"complexion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"膚色，氣色；概貌，局勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you refer to someone's <b>complexion</b>, you are referring to the natural colour or condition of the skin on their face. 面色","examples":["She had short brown hair and a pale complexion. 她留棕色短髮，面色蒼白。"]}]}]},"competence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能力，勝任；許可權，管轄權；技能；感受態，反應能力；<舊>足以謀生的收入（尤指非勞動所得）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Competence</b> is the ability to do something well or effectively. 能力","examples":["Many people have testified to his competence. 很多人已證實了他的能力。"]}]}]},"conceit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"自負，驕傲自大；藝術效果，幻想，奇想"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英> 幻想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conceit</b> is too much pride in your abilities or achievements. 自滿的; 自負的","examples":["Reyes emits confidence without conceit. 羅伊斯表現出自信但不自負。"]}]}]},"complement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"補充，補足"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"補足物，襯托物；足數，足額；補語；餘角；補體，防禦素"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>complements</b> another, it goes well with the other thing and makes its good qualities more noticeable. 襯托","examples":["Nutmeg, parsley and cider all complement the flavour of these beans well. 肉豆蔻、歐芹和蘋果酒都凸顯這些菜豆的味道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people or things <b>complement</b> each other, they are different or do something different, which makes them a good combination. 補充","examples":["There will be a written examination to complement the practical test. 會有一次書面考試來補充實踐測試。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is a <b>complement</b> <b>to</b> something else complements it. 襯托物; 補充物","examples":["The green wallpaper is the perfect complement to the old pine of the dresser. 綠色牆紙是舊松木梳妝檯的完美襯托。"]}]}]},"complication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"使複雜化的難題（或困難）；併發症"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>complication</b> is a problem or difficulty that makes a situation harder to deal with. 使情況複雜化的因素","examples":["The age difference was a complication to the relationship. 年齡差異是使該關係複雜化的一個因素。","There are too many complications to explain now. 現在有太多使情況複雜化的因素要解釋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>complication</b> is a medical problem that occurs as a result of another illness or disease. 併發症","examples":["Blindness is a common complication of diabetes. 失明是糖尿病常有的一種併發症。"]}]}]},"conception":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"概念，觀念；想出，構想；受孕，懷孕；創始"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>conception</b> <b>of</b> something is an idea that you have of it in your mind. (對某事物的) 概念","examples":["My conception of a garden was based on gardens I had visited in England. 我對花園的概念是基於我在英格蘭參觀過的一些花園的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Conception</b> is the process in which the egg in a woman is fertilized and she becomes pregnant. 受孕","examples":["Six weeks after conception, your baby is the size of your little fingernail. 受孕六週後你的孩子有你小手指甲那麼大。"]}]}]},"component":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"組成部分，成分，部件"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"組成的，構成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>components</b> of something are the parts that it is made of. 組成部分","examples":["Enriched uranium is a key component of a nuclear weapon. 濃縮鈾是核武器的一個關鍵組成部分。","The management plan has four main components. 該管理計劃有4個主要組成部分。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>component</b> parts of something are the parts that make it up. 組成的","examples":["Gorbachev failed to keep the component parts of the Soviet Union together. 戈爾巴喬夫沒能使蘇聯各組成部分保持在一起。"]}]}]},"complexity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"複雜性，錯綜複雜；複雜之處，費解之處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Complexity</b> is the state of having many different parts connected or related to each other in a complicated way. 複雜性","examples":["...a diplomatic tangle of great complexity. …一場非常複雜的外交糾紛。"]}]}]},"confrontation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對抗，衝突；戰鬥，戰役"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>confrontation</b> is a dispute, fight, or battle between two groups of people. 爭執; 對抗","examples":["The commission remains so weak that it will continue to avoid confrontation with governments. 該委員會依然如此弱小以致它將繼續避免和各政府的衝突。"]}]}]},"congressman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國會議員；眾議院議員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>congressman</b> is a male member of the U.S. Congress, especially of the House of Representatives. (尤指眾議院的) 美國國會男議員","examples":[]}]}]},"congresswoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美）國會女議員；眾議院女議員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>congresswoman</b> is a female member of the U.S. Congress, especially of the House of Representatives. 美國國會女議員 (尤指眾議院的)","examples":[]}]}]},"concession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"讓步，妥協；特許權；<英>優惠價，減價；商鋪；小攤賣的東西；認輸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>concession</b> <b>to</b> someone, you agree to let them do or have something, especially in order to end an argument or conflict. 讓步","examples":["We made too many concessions and we got too little in return. 我們作出了太多讓步，而得到了太少回報。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>concession</b> is a special right or privilege that is given to someone. 特許權","examples":["Farmers were granted concessions from the government to develop the farms. 農民已獲得政府授權開發這些農場。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>concession</b> is an arrangement where someone is given the right to sell a product or to run a business, especially in a building belonging to another business. (尤指在另一公司的建築物內) 特許經營","examples":["...the man who ran the catering concession at the Rob Roy Links in Palominas. …在帕羅米那斯的羅布羅依高爾夫球場特許經營飲食特許業務的人。"]}]}]},"conquest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"征服，佔領；佔領地，征服的土地；克服，攻克；愛情的俘虜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conquest</b> is the act of conquering a country or group of people. 征服","examples":["He had led the conquest of southern Poland in 1939. 他曾於1939年統領對波蘭南部的征服。","...the Spanish conquest of Mexico. …西班牙人對墨西哥的征服。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>conquest</b> <b>of</b> something such as a problem is success in ending it or dealing with it. 克服","examples":["The conquest of inflation has been the Government's overriding economic priority for nearly 15 years. 對通貨膨脹的克服一直是近15年以來政府的頭等經濟工作重點。"]}]}]},"consolation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"安慰，起安慰作用的人（物）"}],"sections":[]},"conspiracy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"陰謀，密謀；陰謀集團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conspiracy</b> is secret planning by a group of people to do something illegal. 合謀","examples":["Seven men, all from North Carolina, admitted conspiracy to commit arson. 全都來自於北卡羅來納州的七名男子承認了合謀縱火。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>conspiracy</b> is an agreement between a group of people which other people think is wrong or is likely to be harmful. 陰謀","examples":["It's all part of a conspiracy to dispense with the town centre all together and move everything out to the suburbs. 這全都屬於一個陰謀，以徹底放棄市中心而把一切搬到郊區。"]}]}]},"consensus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一致看法，共識"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consensus</b> is general agreement among a group of people. 共識","examples":["The consensus among the world's scientists is that the world is likely to warm up over the next few decades. 全世界科學家的共識是地球可能在未來幾十年中變暖。"]}]}]},"conservation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保護，儲存；節約，防止浪費；守恆定律"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Conservation</b> is saving and protecting the environment. (對環境的) 保護","examples":["...a four-nation regional meeting on elephant conservation. …一次有關大象保護的4國區域性會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Conservation</b> is saving and protecting historical objects or works of art such as paintings, sculptures, or buildings. (對歷史文物、藝術品等的) 保護","examples":["Then he began his most famous work, the conservation and rebinding of the Book of Kells. 接著，他就開始了他最著名的工作，即對《凱爾經》的維護和重新裝訂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>conservation</b> of a supply of something is the careful use of it so that it lasts for a long time. 節約","examples":["...projects aimed at promoting energy conservation. …旨在促進能源節約的專案。"]}]}]},"consultation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商討，磋商，磋商會議；諮詢，就診；查詢，查閱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consultation</b> is a meeting to discuss something. <b>Consultation</b> is discussion about something. 磋商會議; 磋商","examples":["Next week he'll be in Florida for consultations with President Vicente Fox. 下星期他將在佛羅里達同維森特·福克斯總統作磋商。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>consultation</b> <b>with</b> a doctor or other expert is a meeting with them to discuss a particular problem and get their advice. <b>Consultation</b> is the process of getting advice from a doctor or other expert. 諮詢會; 諮詢","examples":["A personal diet plan is devised after a consultation with a nutritionist. 經向營養師作諮詢後，一份個人飲食方案設計出來了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>consultation</b> is a meeting where several doctors discuss a patient and his or her condition and treatment. 會診","examples":[]}]}]},"constituent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選民；成分，構成要素；委託人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"組成的，構成的；選舉的，有任命（或選舉）權的；立憲的，有憲法制定（或修改）權的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>constituent</b> is someone who lives in a particular constituency, especially someone who is able to vote in an election. 選民","examples":["He told his constituents that he would continue to represent them to the best of his ability. 他告訴他的選民們他會繼續竭盡所能代表他們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>constituent</b> <b>of</b> a mixture, substance, or system is one of the things from which it is formed. 成分","examples":["Caffeine is the active constituent of drinks such as tea and coffee. 咖啡因是茶和咖啡這類飲品的活性成分。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>constituent</b> parts of something are the things from which it is formed. 構成的","examples":["...a plan to split the company into its constituent parts and sell them separately. …一項把公司拆分為各構成部分然後分別出售的計劃。"]}]}]},"contemplation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"沉思，冥想；打算，意圖；凝視，默默注視"}],"sections":[]},"contestant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"參賽者，競爭者；爭辯者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>contestant</b> in a competition or game show is a person who takes part in it. 參賽者","examples":["Later he applied to be a contestant on the television show. 之後他報了名做該電視秀的參賽者。"]}]}]},"consumption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消費，消耗；食用，引用，吸入；專用；<舊>肺癆，肺結核"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>consumption</b> of fuel or natural resources is the act of using them or the amount used. 消耗","examples":["The laws have led to a reduction in fuel consumption in the U.S. 這些法律已導致美國燃料消耗的降低。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>consumption</b> of food or drink is the act of eating or drinking something, or the amount eaten or drunk. 食用; 飲用","examples":["Most of the wine was unfit for human consumption. 大多數酒都是不適合人類飲用的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Consumption</b> is the act of buying and using things. 消費","examples":["They were prepared to put people out of work and reduce consumption by strangling the whole economy. 他們準備讓人們失業、降低消費，由此來遏制整個經濟。"]}]}]},"contractor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"承包商，立約人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>contractor</b> is a person or company that does work for other people or organizations. 承包人; 承包商","examples":["We told the building contractor that we wanted a garage big enough for two cars. 我們告訴建築承包商，我們想要一個可以停放兩輛汽車的車庫。"]}]}]},"controversy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"爭論，爭議"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Controversy</b> is a lot of discussion and argument about something, often involving strong feelings of anger or disapproval. 論戰","examples":["The proposed cuts have caused considerable controversy. 削減的提議引起了巨大的爭議。"]}]}]},"contradiction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矛盾，不一致；反駁，駁斥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an aspect of a situation as a <b>contradiction</b>, you mean that it is completely different from other aspects, and so makes the situation confused or difficult to understand. 矛盾","examples":["The militants see no contradiction in using violence to bring about a religious state. 好戰分子認為使用暴力與建立宗教國家不矛盾。"]}]}]},"corps":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特種部隊；（從事某工作或活動的）一群人；（美國）海軍陸戰隊；（由兩個或兩個以上師組成的）軍，兵團"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>corps</b> is a part of the army which has special duties. 特殊兵種","examples":["...the Army Medical Corps. …陸軍醫療部隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The Corps</b> is the United States Marine Corps. 美國海軍陸戰隊","examples":["...seventy-five men, all combat veterans, all members of The Corps' most exclusive unit. …75名士兵，全都是作戰老手、海軍陸戰隊最精銳部隊的成員。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>corps</b> is a small group of people who do a special job. 特別小組","examples":["...the diplomatic corps. …外交使團。"]}]}]},"corpse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"屍體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英，非正式>使戲劇演員的演出僵住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>corpse</b> is a dead body, especially the body of a human being. 屍體","examples":["Detectives placed the corpse in a body bag. 刑警們把屍體裝進了一個運屍袋。"]}]}]},"conviction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"定罪，判罪；堅定的信仰，深信的觀點；確信，深信"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>conviction</b> is a strong belief or opinion. 堅定的信念","examples":["It is our firm conviction that a step forward has been taken. 我們堅信已經向前邁進了一步。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has a <b>conviction</b>, they have been found guilty of a crime in a court of law. 判罪","examples":["He will appeal against his conviction. 他將對判決進行上訴。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>conviction</b>, you have great confidence in your beliefs or opinions. 堅信","examples":["\"We shall, sir,\" said Thorne, with conviction. 索恩堅定地說：“先生，我們會的”。"]}]}]},"core":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"果核；中心部分；核心，要點；骨幹，核心成員；地核，天體的核心；核反應堆堆芯；芯體"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……去核"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"核心的，最重要的；基礎的，必修的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>core</b> of a fruit is the central part of it that contains seeds. 核","examples":["Someone threw an apple core. 有人扔了一個蘋果核。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>core</b> of an object, building, or city is the central part of it. 中心","examples":["...the Earth's core. …地核。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The core</b> <b>of</b> something such as a problem or an issue is the part of it that has to be understood or accepted before the whole thing can be understood or dealt with. (問題的) 核心","examples":["...the ability to get straight to the core of a problem. …直擊問題核心的能力。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>core</b> businesses or the <b>core</b> activities of a company or organization are their most important ones. 核心 (工作或活動)","examples":["The core activities of social workers were reorganized. 社工的核心工作被重新安排了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>core</b> a fruit, you remove its core. 去核","examples":["...machines for peeling and coring apples. …蘋果削皮去核機。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>core</b> team or a <b>core</b> group is a group of people who do the main part of a job or piece of work. Other people may also help, but only for limited periods of time. 核心 (團體)","examples":["We already have our core team in place. 我們的核心隊伍已經就位。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a school or college, <b>core</b> subjects are a group of subjects that have to be studied. 必修的 (課程)","examples":["The core subjects are English, mathematics and science. 必修課程為英語、數學和科學。","I'm not opposed to a core curriculum in principle, but I think requiring a foreign language is unrealistic. 原則上我不反對必修課程，但是我認為把外語列為必修課是不現實的。"]}]}]},"coordinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"協調，配合；使身體協調；（使顏色、款式、風格等）搭配，配套；給 （原子或分子）配位，與……形成共價鍵"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"座標；配套服裝；同等級（或類別）的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地位相當的，同等重要的；（語法）並列的；（化學）配位的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>coordinate</b> an activity, you organize the various people and things involved in it. 協調","examples":["Government officials visited the earthquake zone on Thursday morning to coordinate the relief effort. 政府官員星期四上午視察了地震災區以協調救災工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>coordinate</b> the different parts of your body, you make them work together efficiently to perform particular movements. 使 (身體各部位) 協調","examples":["You need to coordinate legs, arms, and breathing for the front crawl. 匍匐前進時，你要協調雙腿、胳膊和呼吸。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"協調的","examples":["Coalition forces were planning a coordinated effort to attack the drug trade. 聯合部隊正在計劃共同打擊毒品買賣。","...a well-coordinated surprise attack. …一次完美配合的突襲。"]}]},{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>coordinate</b> clothes or furnishings that are used together, or if they <b>coordinate</b>, they are similar in some way and look nice together. 搭配 (衣服、飾品)","examples":["She'll show you how to coordinate pattern and colours. 她會向你展示如何搭配款式和顏色。","Tie it with fabric bows that coordinate with other furnishings. 紮上和其他的飾品相配的布制蝴蝶結。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>coordinates</b> of a point on a map or graph are the two sets of numbers or letters that you need in order to find that point. 座標","examples":["Can you give me your coordinates? 能給我你的座標嗎？"]}]}]},"cosmetics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"化妝品，美容用品（cosmetic 的複數）；化妝品行業"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用化妝品打扮（cosmetic 的第三人稱單數形式；罕見）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cosmetics</b> are substances such as lipstick or powder, which people put on their face to make themselves look more attractive. 化妝品","examples":["...the cosmetics counter of a department store. …一個百貨商店的化妝品專櫃。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe measures or changes as <b>cosmetic</b>, you mean they improve the appearance of a situation or thing but do not change its basic nature, and you are usually implying that they are inadequate. 裝門面的","examples":["It is a cosmetic measure which will do nothing to help the situation long term. 這是裝點門面的措施，無益於局勢的長期發展。"]}]}]},"corruption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貪汙，腐敗；墮落，腐蝕；（電腦上資訊的）破壞，損壞；（語言）變體；<古>腐壞，腐爛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Corruption</b> is dishonesty and illegal behaviour by people in positions of authority or power. 腐敗","examples":["The president faces 54 charges of corruption and tax evasion. 總統面臨著54項腐敗和逃稅的指控。"]}]}]},"cosmopolitan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"世界主義的，四海為家的；國際性的，國際化的；見過世面的，見識廣的；廣佈的，遍生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"四海為家的人，周遊世界的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cosmopolitan</b> place or society is full of people from many different countries and cultures. 世界性的","examples":["...a cosmopolitan city. …一個國際化都市。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>cosmopolitan</b> has had a lot of contact with people and things from many different countries and as a result is very open to different ideas and ways of doing things. 見多識廣的","examples":["The family is rich, and extremely sophisticated and cosmopolitan. 這個家庭殷實富足，深諳世故，又見多識廣。"]}]}]},"counterpart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對應的人（或事物）；（法律檔案的）副本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's or something's <b>counterpart</b> is another person or thing that has a similar function or position in a different place. 對應的人或物","examples":["As soon as he heard what was afoot, he telephoned his German and Italian counterparts to protest. 他一聽到在進行中的事，馬上就給德國和義大利相應人員打電話抗議。"]}]}]},"credibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可靠性，可信度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something has <b>credibility</b>, people believe in them and trust them. 可信性","examples":["The police have lost their credibility. 警察已經失去了他們的可信性。"]}]}]},"correspondent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指從某一國家發回專題報道的）記者，通訊員；通訊者，寫信人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>correspondent</b> is a newspaper or television journalist, especially one who specializes in a particular type of news. (尤指對某一專題進行報道的) 記者","examples":["As our Diplomatic Correspondent Mark Brayne reports, the president was given a sympathetic hearing. 據我臺外事記者馬克·布雷恩報道，該總統獲得了一個同情的申訴機會。"]}]}]},"coverage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"覆蓋範圍；新聞報道；保險範圍；課程內容；防守，盯守"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>coverage</b> of something in the news is the reporting of it. 報道","examples":["Now a special TV network gives live coverage of most races. 現在一個專門的電視網對大多數比賽進行現場報道。"]}]}]},"cramp":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痛性痙攣，抽筋；<美>（女性經期）腹部絞痛；鐵夾鉗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"束縛，限制；束縛（行為或表達）；引起抽筋，導致痙攣；抽筋，痙攣；用鐵夾鉗固定；束縛，限制"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"狹窄的；難以理解的，難以辨認的；受限制的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cramp</b> is a sudden strong pain caused by a muscle suddenly contracting. You sometimes get cramps in a muscle after you have been making a physical effort over a long period of time. 抽筋","examples":["Hillsden was complaining of a cramp in his calf muscles. 希爾斯登一直在抱怨他小腿肌肉抽筋。","...muscle cramps. …肌肉痙攣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a strip of metal with its ends bent at right angles, used to bind masonry 鉗子; 夾子 (Also called cramp iron)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>cramps</b> your <b>style</b>, their presence or existence restricts your behaviour in some way. 束縛某人行為","examples":["Like more and more women, she believes wedlock would cramp her style. 和越來越多的女性一樣，她認為婚姻會束縛她的行為方式。"]}]}]},"criterion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尺度，標準，準則"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>criterion</b> is a factor on which you judge or decide something. (判斷的) 標準","examples":["The most important criterion for entry is that applicants must design and make their own work. 參加的最重要標準就是申請人必須設計並製作自己的作品。"]}]}]},"crook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>騙子，罪犯；彎曲部分（尤指胳膊肘處的彎曲處）；（某物的）彎曲部分；（主教或牧羊人用的）曲柄杖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"(手指或手臂)彎曲；詐騙，偷竊；彎曲，成鉤形；（手指或手臂）彎曲"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>有病的；不誠實的，非法的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>crook</b> is a dishonest person or a criminal. 無賴; 惡棍","examples":["The man is a crook and a liar. 這名男子是個惡棍和騙子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The crook of</b> your arm or leg is the soft inside part where you bend your elbow or knee. 臂彎; 腿彎","examples":["She hid her face in the crook of her arm. 她把臉埋進了臂彎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>crook</b> is a long pole with a large hook at the end. A crook is carried by a bishop in religious ceremonies, or by a shepherd. (主教在宗教儀式上所用的或牧羊人使用的) 曲柄手杖","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>crook</b> your arm or finger, you bend it. 彎曲","examples":["He crooked his finger: \"Come forward,\" he said. 他彎了彎手指，說：“過來。”"]}]}]},"cruiser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"艙式遊艇；巡洋艦；<美>巡邏警車"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cruiser</b> is a motorboat which has an area for people to live or sleep. 遊艇","examples":["...a three-hour journey in a small cruiser with indoor and outdoor seating. …一次乘坐裡外皆設有座椅的小遊艇的3小時旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>cruiser</b> is a large fast warship. 巡洋艦","examples":["Italy had lost three cruisers and two destroyers. 義大利損失了3艘巡洋艦和2艘驅逐艦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>cruiser</b> is a police car. 警車","examples":["Police cruisers surrounded the bank throughout the day. 警車把這家銀行包圍了一整天。"]}]}]},"crumb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"食物碎屑，麵包（蛋糕）屑；點滴，少許；麵包心；<北美，非正式>討厭的人；（常指用回收利用的汽車輪胎製成的）粒化橡膠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在（食品）上塗麵包屑；弄碎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crumbs</b> are tiny pieces that fall from bread, biscuits, or cake when you cut it or eat it. (麵包、餅乾、蛋糕等的) 碎屑","examples":["I stood up, brushing crumbs from my trousers. 我站起來，撣去褲子上的食物碎屑。"]}]}]},"cruise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巡遊，乘船遊覽"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘船遊覽；以平穩的速度行駛；緩慢巡行，兜風；輕而易舉贏得，輕取；<非正式>獵豔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cruise</b> is a holiday during which you travel on a ship or boat and visit a number of places. 海上航遊","examples":["He and his wife were planning to go on a world cruise. 他和妻子那時正計劃進行一次環球海上航遊。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>cruise</b> an ocean, river, or canal, you travel around it or along it on a cruise. 巡航; 巡航於","examples":["She wants to cruise the canals of France in a barge. 她想坐駁船遊覽法國的運河。","...a holiday cruising around the Caribbean. …環遊加勒比海的度假航行。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a car, ship, or aircraft <b>cruises</b> somewhere, it moves there at a steady comfortable speed. (車輛、船隻、飛機等) 漫遊","examples":["A black and white police car cruised past. 一輛黑白相間的警車平穩駛過。"]}]}]},"daybreak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黎明，破曉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Daybreak</b> is the time in the morning when light first appears. 黎明","examples":["Pedro got up every morning before daybreak. 佩德羅每天早上天不亮就起床。"]}]}]},"crumble":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"崩裂，坍塌；（使）粉碎，（使）成碎屑；瓦解，崩潰；不再抵抗，無力應付"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>酥皮水果甜點心； <美>碎屑；<英>（經烹呼叫作水果澆頭的）脂質麵包屑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>crumbles</b>, or if you <b>crumble</b> it, it breaks into a lot of small pieces. 碎裂; 弄碎","examples":["Under the pressure, the flint crumbled into fragments. 在壓力作用下，燧石裂成了碎片。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an old building or piece of land <b>is crumbling</b>, parts of it keep breaking off. 崩塌","examples":["The high- and low-rise apartment blocks built in the 1960s are crumbling. 建於20世紀60年代的高、低層公寓樓正搖搖欲墜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as a system, relationship, or hope <b>crumbles</b>, it comes to an end. (制度、關係或希望) 崩潰","examples":["Their economy crumbled under the weight of United Nations sanctions. 在聯合國制裁的重壓之下，他們的經濟崩潰了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Crumble away</b> means the same as . 崩塌","examples":["Much of the coastline is crumbling away. 多處海岸線正在垮塌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Crumble away</b> means the same as . (制度、關係或希望) 崩潰","examples":["Opposition more or less crumbled away. 反對黨差不多崩潰了。"]}]}]},"daffodil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水仙花"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"水仙花色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>daffodil</b> is a yellow spring flower with a central part shaped like a tube and a long stem. 水仙花","examples":[]}]}]},"dedication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獻身，奉獻；獻辭；落成典禮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dedication</b> is a message which is written at the beginning of a book, or a short announcement which is sometimes made before a play or piece of music is performed, as a sign of affection or respect for someone. 獻辭","examples":[]}]}]},"crust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵包皮；（餡餅或比薩餅等的）酥皮；硬外皮，硬外殼；地殼；<非正式>生活，生計"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"形成（或結成）硬皮（或硬殼）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>crust</b> on a loaf of bread is the outside part. 麵包皮","examples":["Cut the crusts off the bread and soak the bread in the milk. 切掉麵包皮，將麵包浸在牛奶中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A pie's <b>crust</b> is its cooked pastry. 餡餅皮","examples":["The Key lime pie was bursting with flavour. Good crust, too. “基”牌酸橙派味道很濃，外皮也很好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>crust</b> is a hard layer of something, especially on top of a softer or wetter substance. 硬外殼","examples":["As the water evaporates, a crust of salt is left on the surface of the soil. 水蒸發後，土壤表面留下一層鹽。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The Earth's <b>crust</b> is its outer layer. 地殼","examples":["Earthquakes leave scars in the Earth's crust. 地震會在地殼上留下痕跡。"]}]}]},"decline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"下降，衰退；拒絕，謝絕；變格，詞形變化"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"減少，衰退"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>declines</b>, it becomes less in quantity, importance, or strength. 下降","examples":["The number of staff has declined from 217,000 to 114,000. 員工人數已從217000人減少到114000人。","Hourly output by workers declined 1.3% in the first quarter. 工人每小時的產量在第1季度下降了1.3%。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>decline</b> something or <b>decline</b> <b>to</b> do something, you politely refuse to accept it or do it. 謝絕","examples":["He declined their invitation. 他謝絕了他們的邀請。","He offered the boys some coffee. They declined politely. 他要給男孩們來些咖啡。他們禮貌地拒絕了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>decline</b> <b>in</b> something, it becomes less in quantity, importance, or quality. 下降","examples":["Official figures show a sharp decline in the number of foreign tourists. 官方數字顯示外國遊客數量驟降。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in decline</b> or <b>on the decline</b>, it is gradually decreasing in importance, quality, or power. 在下降","examples":["Thankfully the smoking of cigarettes is on the decline. 感謝的是吸菸正在減少。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>goes</b> or <b>falls</b> <b>into decline</b>, it begins to gradually decrease in importance, quality, or power. 開始下降","examples":["Libraries are an investment for the future and they should not be allowed to fall into decline. 圖書館是對未來的一種投資，不應該讓圖書館衰落。"]}]}]},"delinquent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"拖欠債務的，逾期的，到期未付的；有過失的，有不良行為的，有輕微違法行為的；失職的，怠忽的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"少年犯，行為不良的人，流氓；失職者，翫忽職守的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone, usually a young person, who is <b>delinquent</b> repeatedly commits minor crimes. (尤指青少年) 累犯的","examples":["...homes for delinquent children. …少管所。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>delinquent</b> borrower or taxpayer is someone who has failed to pay their debts or taxes. (債款、稅款等) 拖欠的","examples":["...a legal shortcut to take homes from delinquent borrowers. …一個取得拖欠貸款者房產的法律捷徑。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Delinquent</b> is also a noun. 少年犯","examples":["...a nine-year-old delinquent. …一名9歲的少年犯。"]}]}]},"defect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺點，缺陷，毛病"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"背叛，叛變"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>defect</b> is a fault or imperfection in a person or thing. 缺陷","examples":["He was born with a hearing defect. 他天生聽力就有缺陷。","A report has pointed out the defects of the present system. 一份報告指出了現有體制的缺陷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"背叛","examples":["...the defection of at least sixteen parliamentary deputies. …至少16位國會議員的背叛。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>defect</b>, you leave your country, political party, or other group, and join an opposing country, party, or group. 背叛","examples":["...a KGB officer who defected in 1963. …一個1963年叛變的克格勃官員。"]}]}]},"density":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"稠密，密集；密度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Density</b> is the extent to which something is filled or covered with people or things. 密度","examples":["The region has a very high population density. 這一地區人口密度很高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In science, the <b>density</b> of a substance or object is the relation of its mass or weight to its volume. 密度","examples":["Jupiter's moon Io, whose density is 3.5 grams per cubic centimetre, is all rock. 木星的衛星木衛一全是岩石，其密度為每立方厘米3.5克。"]}]}]},"dandruff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頭皮屑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dandruff</b> is small white pieces of dead skin in someone's hair, or fallen from someone's hair. 頭皮屑","examples":["He has very bad dandruff. 他的頭皮屑很多。"]}]}]},"descendant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"後裔，子孫；派生物，衍生物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"下降的；祖傳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>descendants</b> are the people in later generations who are related to them. 後代","examples":["They are descendants of the original English and Scottish settlers. 他們是最初的英格蘭和蘇格蘭移民的後裔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something modern which developed from an older thing can be called a <b>descendant</b> <b>of</b> it. 衍生物","examples":["His design was a descendant of a 1956 device. 他的設計是1956年一個裝置的衍生物。"]}]}]},"deputy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代理人，副手，副職；代表，議員；（美國協助地方治安官辦案的）警官"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"副的；代理的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deputy</b> is the second most important person in an organization such as a business or government department. Someone's deputy often acts on their behalf when they are not there. 副手","examples":["...Jack Lang, France's minister for culture, and his deputy, Catherine Tasca. …法國文化部長傑克·朗和他的副手凱瑟琳·塔斯卡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In some legislatures, the elected members are called <b>deputies</b>. 議員","examples":["The president appealed to deputies to approve the plan quickly. 總統呼籲議員們迅速透過該方案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>deputy</b> is a police officer. 警官","examples":["Robyn asked the deputy on duty if she could speak with Sheriff Adkins. 蘿賓問值班警官她能否跟縣治安官阿德金斯談話。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>deputy</b> is a person appointed to act on another person's behalf. 代理人","examples":["His brother was acting as his deputy in America. 他的兄弟充當他在美洲的代理人。"]}]}]},"diabetes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"糖尿病，多尿症"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Diabetes</b> is a medical condition in which someone has too much sugar in their blood. 糖尿病","examples":[]}]}]},"descent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"下降，降落；斜坡，斜面；出身，血統；墮落，淪落；突然到訪，突襲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>descent</b> is a movement from a higher to a lower level or position. 下降","examples":["Sixteen of the youngsters set off for help, but during the descent three collapsed in the cold and rain. 那些年輕人中有16人出發尋求幫助，但在下山過程中有3人在寒冷和陰雨中倒下了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>descent</b> is a surface that slopes downward, for example, the side of a steep hill. 下坡","examples":["On the descents, cyclists spin past cars, freewheeling downhill at tremendous speed. 在下坡道上，腳踏車手們飛快地掠過汽車，靠慣性極速衝下山去。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When you want to emphasize that a situation becomes very bad, you can talk about someone's or something's <b>descent</b> into that situation. 沉淪; 沒落","examples":["...his swift descent from respected academic to struggling small businessman. …他從受人尊敬的學者到掙扎求存的小商人的迅速淪落。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>descent</b> to talk about a person's family background, for example, their nationality or social status. 出身","examples":["All the contributors were of African descent. 所有捐助者都是非洲血統。"]}]}]},"diagnosis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"診斷，判斷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Diagnosis</b> is the discovery and naming of what is wrong with someone who is ill or with something that is not working properly. 診斷","examples":["I need to have a second test to confirm the diagnosis. 我需要複查來確診。"]}]}]},"deficiency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺乏，不足；缺陷，瑕疵；赤字"}],"sections":[]},"diameter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"直徑；放大倍數"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>diameter</b> of a round object is the length of a straight line that can be drawn across it, passing through the middle of it. 直徑","examples":["...a tube less than a fifth of the diameter of a human hair. …一根直徑不到頭髮五分之一的微管。"]}]}]},"dictation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口述，聽寫；命令，發號施令"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dictation</b> is the speaking or reading aloud of words for someone else to write down. 口授; 聽寫","examples":["...taking dictation from the dean of the graduate school. …記錄研究生院院長的口述。"]}]}]},"diagram":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖表，圖解；幾何圖形"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以圖表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diagram</b> is a simple drawing which consists mainly of lines and is used, for example, to explain how a machine works. 示意圖","examples":["...a circuit diagram. …電路圖。"]}]}]},"dilemma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（進退兩難的）窘境，困境；二難推理，兩刀論法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dilemma</b> is a difficult situation in which you have to choose between two or more alternatives. 進退兩難的局面","examples":["He was faced with the dilemma of whether or not to return to his country. 他面臨著是否回國的艱難選擇。"]}]}]},"dictator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨裁者；專橫的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dictator</b> is a ruler who has complete power in a country, especially power which was obtained by force and is used unfairly or cruelly. 獨裁者","examples":["...foreign dictators who contravene humanitarian conventions. …違反人道主義公約的外國獨裁者們。"]}]}]},"directory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名址錄，電話號碼簿；（計算機的）目錄，資料夾；<史>（尤指長老會和羅馬天主教會的）禮拜規則書"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"指導的，諮詢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>directory</b> is a book which gives lists of facts, for example, people's names, addresses, and telephone numbers, or the names and addresses of business companies, usually arranged in alphabetical order. (通常按字母順序記錄姓名、地址、電話、公司通訊錄等的) 簿","examples":["...a telephone directory. …電話簿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>directory</b> is an area of a computer disk which contains one or more files or other directories. (計算機磁碟中包含一個或多個檔案的) 目錄","examples":["This option lets you search your current directory for files by date, contents, and document summary. 這一選項讓你按日期、內容和檔案摘要在當前目錄中查詢檔案。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"On the World Wide Web, a <b>directory</b> is a list of the subjects that you can find information on. (全球資訊網上的) 主題目錄","examples":["Yahoo is the oldest and best-known Web directory service. 雅虎是提供網上目錄檢索服務最早、最知名的網站。"]}]}]},"diplomacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外交，外交技巧；（處理人際關係的）手腕，策略"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Diplomacy</b> is the activity or profession of managing relations between the governments of different countries. 外交","examples":["Today's Security Council resolution will be a significant success for American diplomacy. 今天的安理會決議將成為美國外交的一次重大勝利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Diplomacy</b> is the skill of being careful to say or do things which will not offend people. 交際手腕","examples":["He stormed off in a fury, and it took all Minnelli's powers of diplomacy to get him to return. 他憤然離去，明內利使盡一切交際手腕才讓他回來。"]}]}]},"dimension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"大小，尺寸；（空間的）維度；範圍，規模；方面，部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"切削（或製作）成特定尺寸；標出尺寸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>dimension</b> of something is a particular aspect of it. 方面","examples":["There is a political dimension to the accusations. 這些指控含有政治因素。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dimension</b> is a measurement such as length, width, or height. If you talk about the <b>dimensions</b> of an object or place, you are referring to its size and proportions. (單數) 尺寸; (複數) 比例大小","examples":["Drilling will continue on the site to assess the dimensions of the new oilfield. 鑽探還將繼續在現場進行以估測新油田的大小。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>dimensions</b> of a situation or problem, you are talking about its extent and size. 規模","examples":["The dimensions of the market collapse, in terms of turnover and price, were certainly not anticipated. 股市崩盤的規模，無論從成交量還是價格來看，都是出乎意料的。"]}]}]},"disability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"殘疾，缺陷；無能力，障礙；殘疾補貼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disability</b> is a permanent injury, illness, or physical or mental condition that tends to restrict the way that someone can live their life. (身體或精神方面的) 殘疾","examples":["Facilities for people with disabilities are still insufficient. 供殘疾人使用的設施仍然不足。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Disability</b> is the state of being disabled. 殘疾狀態","examples":["Disability can make extra demands on financial resources because the disabled need extra care. 殘疾會增加額外經濟需求，因為殘疾人需要特別護理。"]}]}]},"disclosure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"披露，洩密；透露的秘聞，公開的事情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disclosure</b> is the act of giving people new or secret information. 公開","examples":["...insufficient disclosure of negative information about the company. …有關該公司負面資訊的不充分公開。"]}]}]},"discomfort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不適，不舒服；不安，不自在；不便之處"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使……不舒服；使……不安"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Discomfort</b> is a painful feeling in part of your body when you have been hurt slightly or when you have been uncomfortable for a long time. 不舒服","examples":["Steve had some discomfort, but no real pain. 史蒂夫有些不舒服，但不真疼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Discomfort</b> is a feeling of worry caused by shame or embarrassment. 不安","examples":["She hears the discomfort in his voice. 她聽出他聲音裡的不安。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Discomforts</b> are conditions which cause you to feel physically uncomfortable. 不舒適的情況","examples":["...the discomforts of camping. …野營不舒適的種種情況。"]}]}]},"dismay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"擔憂；失望，沮喪；驚愕"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使擔憂；使失望，使沮喪；使驚恐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dismay</b> is a strong feeling of fear, worry, or sadness that is caused by something unpleasant and unexpected. 恐慌; 悲傷","examples":["Local politicians have reacted with dismay and indignation. 當地政客們作出了恐慌和憤慨的反應。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are dismayed</b> by something, it makes you feel afraid, worried, or sad. 使恐慌; 使悲傷","examples":["The committee was dismayed by what it had been told. 該委員會被所告知的情況搞得焦慮不安。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"恐慌的; 悲傷的","examples":["He was dismayed at the cynicism of the youngsters. 他對年輕人們的憤世嫉俗感到傷心焦慮。"]}]}]},"discrimination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歧視，區別對待；區分，辨別；辨別力，鑑賞力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Discrimination</b> is the practice of treating one person or group of people less fairly or less well than other people or groups. 歧視","examples":["She is exempt from sex discrimination laws. 她不用遵守性別歧視法規。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Discrimination</b> is knowing what is good or of high quality. 鑑賞力","examples":["They cooked without skill and ate without discrimination. 他們做飯沒廚藝，吃飯沒品味。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Discrimination</b> is the ability to recognize and understand the differences between two things. 辨別力","examples":["We will then have an objective measure of how colour discrimination and visual acuity develop at the level of the brain. 我們隨後將進行一項客觀的測量，看色彩辨別力和視覺敏銳度如何在大腦的層面形成。"]}]}]},"discharge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"釋放，允許……離開；解僱；使退伍；（使）流出，（使）排出；開火，發射；放（電）；履行（職責），清償（債務）；（法官，法庭）撤銷（法院命令）；卸（貨），讓……下車"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"允許出院，釋放；任務的執行，債務的償還；解僱；退伍；（法庭命令的）撤銷；放電；排出物，分泌物；（物質的）放出，排出；射擊，開火；（儀器、雷暴等釋放出來的）電"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>is discharged</b> <b>from</b> a hospital, prison, or one of the armed services, they are officially allowed to leave, or told that they must leave. 批准離開; 命令離開","examples":["He has a broken nose but may be discharged today. 他鼻樑斷了，但今天可能獲准出院。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>discharges</b> their duties or responsibilities, they do everything that needs to be done in order to complete them. 履行 (職責或義務)","examples":["...the quiet competence with which he discharged his many duties. …他履行他的諸多職責所用的平靜的辦事能力。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>is discharged</b> from inside a place, it comes out. 排出","examples":["The resulting salty water will be discharged at sea. 產生的鹹水將被排放到海里。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Discharge</b> is also a noun. 釋放","examples":["He was given a conditional discharge and ordered to pay Miss Smith $500 compensation. 他被判有條件釋放，並被命令向史密斯小姐支付$500的賠償金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When there is a <b>discharge</b> of a substance, the substance comes out from inside somewhere. 排出","examples":["They develop a fever and a watery discharge from their eyes. 他們開始發燒，且有一種水狀分泌物從他們的眼睛裡流出。"]}]}]},"disposable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一次性的，用完即丟棄的；可支配的，可自由使用的；（人，觀點）可有可無的，可輕易放棄的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"一次性用品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disposable</b> product is designed to be thrown away after it has been used. 一次性的","examples":["...disposable diapers suitable for babies up to 8lbs. …適合重至8磅的嬰兒使用的一次性尿布。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>disposable</b> income is the amount of income you have left after you have paid bills and taxes. 可自由支配的 (收入)","examples":["Gerald had little disposable income. 傑拉爾德沒有多少可自由支配的收入。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Disposable products can be referred to as <b>disposables</b>. 一次性物品","examples":["Currently, disposables account for about 80% to 85% of the $3 billion-plus annual diaper market. 目前，一次性尿布佔年銷售額30多億美元的尿布市場的80%至85%左右。"]}]}]},"disgrace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恥辱，不光彩； 令人感到羞恥的人（或事），不名譽的事；失寵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使丟臉，使蒙受恥辱；使名譽掃地，使失勢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>in</b> <b>disgrace</b>, you are emphasizing that other people disapprove of them and do not respect them because of something that they have done. 恥辱","examples":["His vice president also had to resign in disgrace. 他的副總統也只得不光彩地辭職。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>a disgrace</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very bad or wrong, and that you find it completely unacceptable. 丟臉的事","examples":["The way the sales were handled was a complete disgrace. 所採取的銷售方式丟盡了人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say that someone is <b>a disgrace</b> <b>to</b> someone else when you want to emphasize that their behaviour causes the other person to feel ashamed. (給某人) 帶來恥辱的人","examples":["Republican leaders called him a disgrace to the party. 共和黨領導人們稱他為該黨的恥辱。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>disgraces</b> someone else, you are emphasizing that their behaviour causes the other person to feel ashamed. 使 (某人) 丟臉","examples":["I have disgraced my family's name. 我玷汙了家族的名聲。"]}]}]},"disregard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"忽視，輕視，不尊重"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"漠視，輕視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>disregard</b> something, you ignore it or do not take account of it. 對…置之不理","examples":["He disregarded the advice of his executives. 他對主管們的建議置之不理。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disregard</b> is also a noun. 忽視","examples":["Whoever planted the bomb showed a total disregard for the safety of the public. 不論誰安置了炸彈都顯示出對公眾安全的全然漠視。"]}]}]},"dispatch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"派遣；傳送；迅速處理，迅速辦妥；殺死，處決"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"派遣，傳送；公文，急件；報道，電訊；殺死，除掉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>dispatch</b> someone to a place, you send them there for a particular reason. 派遣","examples":["He had been continually dispatching scouts ahead. 他一直不斷地派遣偵察員到前面去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>dispatch</b> a message, letter, or parcel, you send it to a particular person or destination. 傳送","examples":["The victory inspired him to dispatch a gleeful telegram to Roosevelt. 勝利鼓舞了他發喜電給羅斯福。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dispatch</b> is also a noun. 派遣","examples":["The dispatch of the task force is purely a contingency measure. 派遣特遣隊純粹是應急措施。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Dispatch</b> is also a noun. 傳送","examples":["We have 125 cases ready for dispatch. 我們有125個待發的箱子。"]}]}]},"dissident":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"持不同政見者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有不同意見的，持不同政見的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dissidents</b> are people who disagree with and criticize their government, especially because it is undemocratic. 異議分子","examples":["...political dissidents. …政治異議分子。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dissident</b> people disagree with or criticize their government or a powerful organization they belong to. 持不同政見的","examples":["...a dissident Russian novelist. …一位與政府意見相左的俄羅斯小說家。"]}]}]},"distraction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"使人分心的事物，干擾；分心的事物，干擾；消遣，娛樂；心煩意亂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>distraction</b> is something that turns your attention away from something you want to concentrate on. 分心的事物","examples":["Total concentration is required with no distractions. 需要全神貫注，不可有分心之事。"]}]}]},"disposal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"處理，清除；（土地、財產等的）變賣，轉讓；<文>安排，安置；<美>汙物碾碎器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have something <b>at</b> your <b>disposal</b>, you are able to use it whenever you want, and for whatever purpose you want. If you say that you are <b>at</b> someone's <b>disposal</b>, you mean that you are willing to help them in any way you can. 任某人支配; 盡力為某人提供幫助","examples":["Do you have this information at your disposal? 這個資料你能隨意使用嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Disposal</b> is the act of getting rid of something that is no longer wanted or needed. 清除","examples":["...methods for the permanent disposal of radioactive wastes. …放射性廢料的永久清除方法。"]}]}]},"distrust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不信任，懷疑"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"不信任，懷疑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>distrust</b> someone or something, you think they are not honest, reliable, or safe. 不信任","examples":["I don't have any particular reason to distrust them. 我沒有任何特殊的理由不信任他們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Distrust</b> is the feeling of doubt that you have toward someone or something you distrust. 懷疑","examples":["What he saw there left him with a profound distrust of all political authority. 他在那個地方之所見讓他對所有政治權威產生了極度懷疑。"]}]}]},"disturbance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"干擾，擾亂；騷亂，動亂；失調，紊亂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disturbance</b> is an incident in which people behave violently in public. 騷亂","examples":["During the disturbance which followed, three Englishmen were hurt. 在隨後的騷亂中，3個英國人受傷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Disturbance</b> means upsetting or disorganizing something which was previously in a calm and well-ordered state. 煩亂; 擾亂","examples":["Successful breeding requires quiet, peaceful conditions with as little disturbance as possible. 成功繁殖需要安寧的環境，干擾越少越好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>disturbance</b> to refer to a medical or psychological problem, when someone's body or mind is not working in the normal way. (身體) 不適; 心神不安","examples":["Poor educational performance is related to emotional disturbance. 學習表現不好與情緒不穩定有關。"]}]}]},"diversity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"多樣性，多樣化；不同，差異"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>diversity</b> of something is the fact that it contains many very different elements. 多樣性","examples":["...the cultural diversity of Latin America. …拉丁美洲文化的多樣性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>diversity of</b> things is a range of things which are very different from each other. 各種各樣","examples":["Forslan's object is to gather as great a diversity of genetic material as possible. 福斯蘭的目標是儘可能收集各種不同的基因物質。"]}]}]},"doctrine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教義，主義，信條；（政府政策的）正式宣告"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>doctrine</b> is a set of principles or beliefs, especially religious ones. (尤指宗教的) 信條; 學說","examples":["...the Marxist doctrine of perpetual revolution. …馬克思主義不斷革命的學說。"]}]}]},"dome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"穹頂，圓屋頂；半球形物，圓頂狀物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"變圓，膨脹；加穹頂（狀物）於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dome</b> is a round roof. 穹頂","examples":["...the dome of the Capitol. …國會大廈的穹頂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dome</b> is any object that has a similar shape to a dome. 圓頂狀物","examples":["...the dome of the hill. …山包。"]}]}]},"documentary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紀實節目，紀錄片"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"書面的，檔案的，文獻的；記錄的，紀實的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>documentary</b> is a television or radio programme, or a film, which shows real events or provides information about a particular subject. 記錄片","examples":["...a TV documentary on homelessness. …一部關於無家可歸現象的電視記錄片。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Documentary</b> evidence consists of things that are written down. 書面的 (證據)","examples":["The government says it has documentary evidence that the two countries were planning military action. 該政府宣稱，它擁有這兩個國家正在策劃軍事行動的書面證據。"]}]}]},"donor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"捐獻者，捐贈者；（化學）供體；（物理）施主"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"捐獻的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>donor</b> is someone who gives a part of their body or some of their blood to be used by doctors to help a person who is ill. 器官捐獻者; 獻血者","examples":["Doctors removed the healthy kidney from the donor. 醫生從捐獻者體內取出了健康的腎臟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>donor</b> is a person or organization who gives something, especially money, to a charity, organization, or country that needs it. 捐贈者","examples":["Donor countries are becoming more choosy about which countries they are prepared to help. 捐贈國對受贈國的選擇變得更加慎重了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Donor</b> organs or parts are organs or parts of the body which people allow doctors to use to help people who are ill. 捐獻的","examples":["...the severe shortage of donor organs. …捐獻器官的嚴重匱乏。"]}]}]},"donation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"捐贈物，捐贈，贈送"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>donation</b> is something which someone gives to a charity or other organization. 捐贈物","examples":["Employees make regular donations to charity. 員工們定期向慈善機構捐贈物品。"]}]}]},"dosage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劑量，用量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dosage</b> is the amount of a medicine or drug that someone takes or should take. 劑量","examples":["He was put on a high dosage of vitamin C. 他在大劑量服用維生素C。"]}]}]},"doom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"厄運，劫數；悲觀，沮喪"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"註定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Doom</b> is a terrible future state or event which you cannot prevent. 厄運","examples":["...his warnings of impending doom. …他對即將到來的厄運發出的警告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a sense or feeling of <b>doom</b>, you feel that things are going very badly and are likely to get even worse. 悲觀","examples":["Why are people so full of gloom and doom? 人們的心裡為什麼滿是悲觀失望？"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a fact or event <b>dooms</b> someone or something <b>to</b> a particular fate, it makes certain that they are going to suffer in some way. 註定","examples":["That argument was the turning point for their marriage, and the one which doomed it to failure. 那次爭吵是他們婚姻的一個轉折點，它註定了他們婚姻的失敗。"]}]}]},"drawback":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"缺點，不利條件；出口退稅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drawback</b> is an aspect of something or someone that makes them less acceptable than they would otherwise be. 缺點; 障礙","examples":["He felt the apartment's only drawback was that it was too small. 他感覺這個公寓惟一的缺點就是太小。"]}]}]},"drizzle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"下毛毛雨，下濛濛細雨； （毛毛雨似的）灑落；（毛毛雨似的）灑落"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"毛毛細雨，濛濛細雨；（烹）（澆在食品上的）液態調料細流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Drizzle</b> is light rain falling in fine drops. 毛毛雨","examples":["The drizzle had now stopped and the sun was breaking through. 細雨已經停了，太陽露出了臉。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it <b>is drizzling</b>, it is raining very lightly. 下毛毛雨","examples":["Clouds had come down and it was starting to drizzle. 雲壓了下來，開始下起了毛毛雨。"]}]}]},"diversion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"轉向，轉移；繞行路，支路；轉移注意力的事物，分心的事物；消遣，娛樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>diversion</b> is an action or event that attracts your attention away from what you are doing or concentrating on. 令人分心的事物","examples":["...armed robbers who escaped after throwing smoke bombs to create a diversion. …在扔出煙霧彈造成注意力分散之後逃跑的武裝搶劫犯們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>diversion</b> is a special route arranged for traffic to follow when the normal route cannot be used. 改道路線","examples":["A slight diversion in the road is causing major headaches for businesses along El Camino Real. 馬路上的一小段繞行道讓國王大道沿街的商家十分頭疼。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The diversion of</b> something involves changing its course or destination. 轉移; 轉向","examples":["...the illegal diversion of profits from secret arms sales. …銷售秘密武器所得收益的非法轉移。"]}]}]},"drought":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"長期缺乏，嚴重短缺；<古>口渴；乾旱，旱災"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>drought</b> is a long period of time during which no rain falls. 乾旱","examples":["...a country where drought and famines have killed up to two million people during the last eighteen years. …過去18年來乾旱和饑荒致死達兩百萬人的一個國家。"]}]}]},"ebb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衰退；退潮"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"衰退，衰落；（潮水或海水）退，落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When the tide or the sea <b>ebbs</b>, its level gradually falls. 退潮","examples":["When the tide ebbs, you can paddle out for a mile and barely get your ankles wet. 退潮時，你可以蹚水走出1英里遠而幾乎溼不到腳踝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone's life, support, or feeling <b>ebbs</b>, it becomes weaker and gradually disappears. 衰退","examples":["Were there occasions when enthusiasm ebbed? 熱情會有衰退的時候嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>ebb</b> or the <b>ebb</b> tide is one of the regular periods, usually two per day, when the sea gradually falls to a lower level as the tide moves away from the land. 退潮","examples":["...the spring ebb tide. …春季的退潮。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ebb away</b> means the same as . 衰退","examples":["His little girl's life ebbed away. 他小女兒的生命衰竭了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>at a low ebb</b> or <b>at</b> their <b>lowest ebb</b>, they are not very successful or profitable. 處於低潮","examples":["...a time when everyone is tired and at a low ebb. …一個每人都處於疲憊狀態和低潮的時刻"]}]}]},"dynamite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"炸藥；具有爆炸性的事物，具有隱患的事物；<非正式>轟動一時的人（或事物），極其令人興奮的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"炸燬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人印象深刻的，激動人心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Dynamite</b> is a type of explosive that contains nitroglycerin. 炸藥","examples":["Fifty yards of track was blown up with dynamite. 50碼長的軌道被炸藥炸燬了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a piece of information as <b>dynamite</b>, you think that people will react strongly to it. 引發爆炸效應事物","examples":["The book is dynamite, and if she publishes it, there will be no hiding place for her. 這本書是顆“炸彈”，如果她將其出版，必無藏身之所。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>dynamite</b>, you think that they are exciting. 引發轟動效應的人或物","examples":["The first kiss is dynamite. 初吻是激動人心的。"]}]}]},"eccentric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"古怪的，異乎尋常的；不同圓心的，不正圓的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"古怪的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>eccentric</b>, you mean that they behave in a strange way, and have habits or opinions that are different from those of most people. 古怪的; 異乎尋常的","examples":["He is an eccentric character who likes wearing a beret and dark glasses. 他是個怪人，喜歡戴貝雷帽和墨鏡。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>eccentric</b> is an eccentric person. 古怪的人","examples":["Askew used several names, and had a reputation as an eccentric. 艾斯丘用過幾個名字，並以“怪人”著稱。"]}]}]},"ecology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生態學；生態；生態保護運動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ecology</b> is the study of the relationships between plants, animals, people, and their environment, and the balances between these relationships. 生態學","examples":["...a professor in ecology. …一位生態學教授。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you talk about the <b>ecology</b> of a place, you are referring to the pattern and balance of relationships between plants, animals, people, and the environment in that place. 生態","examples":["...the ecology of the rocky Negev desert in Israel. …以色列內蓋夫的多岩石沙漠生態。"]}]}]},"ecstasy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"狂喜，陶醉；搖頭丸（Ecstasy）；（情緒或宗教原因引起的）瘋狂，出神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ecstasy</b> is a feeling of very great happiness. 狂喜","examples":["...a state of almost religious ecstasy. …一種近乎宗教極樂的狀態。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Ecstasy</b> is an illegal drug that makes people feel happy and energetic. 搖頭丸","examples":["The teenager died after taking ecstasy on her birthday. 那個少女在她生日當天服用搖頭丸後喪生。"]}]}]},"editorial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"編輯的，主編的；社論的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"社論，社評；（報刊的）由編輯撰寫的部分，非廣告部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Editorial</b> means involved in preparing a newspaper, magazine, or book for publication. 編輯的","examples":["I went to the editorial board meetings when I had the time. 我當時有空兒就去參加編輯委員會的會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Editorial</b> means involving the attitudes, opinions, and contents of something such as a newspaper, magazine, or television programme. 社論的","examples":["We are not about to change our editorial policy. 我們不打算改變我們的社論方針。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>editorial</b> is an article in a newspaper that gives the opinion of the editor or owner on a topic or item of news. 社論","examples":["In an editorial, The New York Times suggests the victory could turn nasty. 在一篇社論中，《紐約時報》認為該勝利會轉成惡夢。"]}]}]},"electron":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>electron</b> is a tiny particle of matter that is smaller than an atom and has a negative electrical charge. 電子","examples":["Most things are balanced - with equal numbers of electrons and protons. 大部分物體都是電荷平衡的——含等量的電子和質子。"]}]}]},"eloquence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流利的口才，流暢的文筆；雄辯術，修辭"}],"sections":[]},"elite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"權力集團，上層人士；尖子，精英"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"出類拔萃的，精銳的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the most powerful, rich, or talented people within a particular group, place, or society as the <b>elite</b>. 精英","examples":["...a government comprised mainly of the elite. …主要由精英組成的政府。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elite</b> people or organizations are considered to be the best of their kind. 精英的","examples":["...the elite troops of the president's bodyguard. …總統衛隊中的精英部隊。"]}]}]},"emigration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移居外國，遷移出境；移民"}],"sections":[]},"emigrant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移居外國的人，移民"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"移民的，移居的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>emigrant</b> is a person who has left their own country to live in another country. Compare . 移居國外者","examples":["...Irish emigrants to America. …移居美國的愛爾蘭移民。"]}]}]},"enclosure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圍場，圍牆，圈佔地；附件；圍住，圈起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>enclosure</b> is an area of land that is surrounded by a wall or fence and that is used for a particular purpose. 圍場","examples":["This enclosure was so vast that the outermost wall could hardly be seen. 這塊圈地大得幾乎看不見它最外面的圍牆。"]}]}]},"enactment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（法律的）制定，透過；表演，上演；法令，透過的法律；展現，付諸行動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>enactment</b> <b>of</b> a law is the process in a legislature by which the law is agreed upon and made official. 法律制定","examples":["We support the call for the enactment of a Bill of Rights. 我們支援《權利法案》制定的呼籲。"]}]}]},"encyclopedia":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"百科全書，（某一學科的）專科全書（=encyclopaedia）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>encyclopedia</b> is a book or set of books in which facts about many different subjects or about one particular subject are arranged for reference, usually in alphabetical order. 百科全書","examples":[]}]}]},"endurance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"持久力，忍耐力；耐久性，耐用度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Endurance</b> is the ability to continue with an unpleasant or difficult situation, experience, or activity over a long period of time. 耐力","examples":["The exercise obviously will improve strength and endurance. 這項練習將明顯增強力量和耐力。"]}]}]},"enlightenment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"啟迪，指導，教導；啟蒙運動（the Enlightenment）；（佛教）般若，智慧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enlightenment</b> means the act of enlightening or the state of being enlightened. 啟發; 教化","examples":["Stella had a moment of enlightenment. 斯特拉恍然大悟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In Buddhism, <b>enlightenment</b> is a final spiritual state in which everything is understood and there is no more suffering or desire. (佛教中的)覺悟; 超脫; 包括菩提、般若等佛家智慧境界","examples":["...a sense of deep peace and spiritual enlightenment. ...一種深深的平和感和精神超脫。"]}]}]},"enhancement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"增加，增強，改善"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>enhancement</b> <b>of</b> something is the improvement of it in relation to its value, quality, or attractiveness. 提高","examples":["Music is merely an enhancement to the power of her words. 音樂只不過是對她文字力量的一個提升。"]}]}]},"enrichment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"充實，豐富，改進；（土壤）肥沃化；發財致富，獲利；（法律）不當得利；（化學、核能等）富集，濃縮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Enrichment</b> is the act of enriching someone or something or the state of being enriched. 充實; 豐富","examples":["...the enrichment of society. …社會的富足。"]}]}]},"episode":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一段經歷，一段時期；（電視劇或廣播劇的）集，一集；疾病的發作，發病；插句，插段；（希臘悲劇中）兩段合唱之間的部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to an event or a short period of time as an <b>episode</b> if you want to suggest that it is important or unusual, or has some particular quality. 事件; 經歷","examples":["This episode is bound to be a deep embarrassment for Washington. 這一事件必然使華盛頓大為尷尬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>episode</b> of something such as a series on television or a story in a magazine is one of the separate parts in which it is broadcast or published. (電視連續劇的) 集; (連載小說的) 節","examples":["The final episode will be shown next Sunday. 最後一集將於下週日播放。"]}]}]},"epidemic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流行病，傳染病；（迅速的）盛行，蔓延"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"盛行的，氾濫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>epidemic</b> <b>of</b> a particular disease somewhere, it affects a very large number of people there and spreads quickly to other areas. (疾病的) 流行","examples":["A flu epidemic is sweeping through Moscow. 一場流感正席捲莫斯科。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an activity that you disapprove of is increasing or spreading rapidly, you can refer to this as an <b>epidemic</b> <b>of</b> that activity. (壞事的) 盛行","examples":["...an epidemic of serial killings. …連環謀殺的盛行。"]}]}]},"eruption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"噴發；（戰爭、怒氣等的）爆發；發疹"}],"sections":[]},"equation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"等式，方程（式）；等同（看待）；（必須考慮多種因素的）複雜局面（或問題）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>equation</b> is a mathematical statement saying that two amounts or values are the same, for example 6x4=12x2. 等式","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>equation</b> is a situation in which two or more parts have to be considered together so that the whole situation can be understood or explained. 制衡局面","examples":["The equation is simple: research breeds new products. 這個情況是簡單的：研究孕育新產品。","The party fears the equation between higher spending and higher taxes. 該黨害怕增加開支和增高稅收之間的相互制衡。"]}]}]},"eternity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"無窮無盡的時間；永恆，永久；永生；未來，來世；死"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eternity</b> is time without an end or a state of existence outside time, especially the state that some people believe they will pass into after they have died. 永恆; 永存","examples":["I have always found the thought of eternity terrifying. 我總覺得永生的想法很可怕。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a situation lasted for <b>an eternity</b>, you mean that it seemed to last an extremely long time, usually because it was boring or unpleasant. 極長的時間","examples":["The war continued for an eternity. 那場戰爭持續了極長的時間。"]}]}]},"equivalent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"等同的，等效的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"對等的人（或事物），對應的人（或事物）；當量（equivalent weight）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one amount or value is <b>the</b> <b>equivalent</b> <b>of</b> another, they are the same. 等量物; 等價物","examples":["Mr. Li's pay is the equivalent of about $80 a month. 李先生的報酬大約等於每月80美元。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>equivalent</b> of someone or something is a person or thing that has the same function in a different place, time, or system. 等效物件","examples":["...the Red Cross emblem, and its equivalent in Muslim countries, the Red Crescent. …紅十字徽章、及其在穆斯林國家對應物的紅新月。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>equivalent</b> to emphasize the great or severe effect of something. 等效物件","examples":["His party has just suffered the equivalent of a near-fatal heart attack. 他的政黨剛經受了相當於一次幾乎致命的心臟病發作的打擊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Equivalent</b> is also an adjective. 等量的; 等值的","examples":["If they want to change an item in the budget, they will have to propose equivalent cuts elsewhere. 如果他們想要改變預算中的一個款項，必須得提出其他等值的削減。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Equivalent</b> is also an adjective. 等效的","examples":["...a decrease of 10% in property investment compared with the equivalent period in 1991. …房產投資相比1991年同期10％的降幅。"]}]}]},"essence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"本質，要素；香精，香料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>essence</b> <b>of</b> something is its basic and most important characteristic that gives it its individual identity. 本質","examples":["The essence of consultation is to listen to, and take account of, the views of those consulted. 諮詢的本質是傾聽並把那些被諮詢者的觀點考慮進來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Essence</b> is a very concentrated liquid that is used for flavouring food or for its smell. 精油","examples":["...a few drops of vanilla essence. …幾滴香草精油。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>is of the essence</b>, you mean that it is absolutely necessary in order for a particular action to be successful. 至關重要","examples":["Speed was of the essence in a project of this type. 速度在一個這種型別的專案中至關重要。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>in essence</b> to emphasize that you are talking about the most important or central aspect of an idea, situation, or event. 本質上","examples":["Though complicated in detail, local taxes are in essence simple. 雖然細節複雜，地方稅本質上是簡單的。"]}]}]},"ethnic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（有關）種族的，民族的；少數民族的；具有民族特色的，異國風味的；既非基督教亦非猶太教的，異教徒的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"少數民族成員，某民族群體的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ethnic</b> means connected with or relating to different racial or cultural groups of people. 種族的","examples":["...a survey of Britain's ethnic minorities. …對英國少數民族的一項調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>ethnic</b> to describe people who belong to a particular racial or cultural group but who, usually, do not live in the country where most members of that group live. 少數民族的","examples":["There are still several million ethnic Germans in Russia. 在俄羅斯仍有幾百萬德國族裔。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ethnic</b> clothing, music, or food is characteristic of the traditions of a particular ethnic group, and different from what is usually found in modern Western culture. 具有民族特色的","examples":["...a magnificent range of ethnic fabrics. …各色各樣具有民族特色的織物。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"種族上地","examples":["...a predominantly young, ethnically mixed audience. …一群大部分為年輕的、包含不同種族的觀眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"少數民族地","examples":["...a large ethnically Albanian population. …大量阿爾巴尼亞族人口。"]}]}]},"excerpt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"摘錄，節選"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"摘錄，節選"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>excerpt</b> is a short piece of writing or music taken from a larger piece. 摘錄; 節選","examples":["...an excerpt from Tchaikovsky's Nutcracker. …柴可夫斯基的《胡桃夾子》選段。"]}]}]},"evolution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"進化（論）；演變，發展；（氣體的）釋放，（熱量的）散發；隊形變換，位置變換；<舊>開方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Evolution</b> is a process of gradual change that takes place over many generations, during which species of animals, plants, or insects slowly change some of their physical characteristics. 進化","examples":["...the evolution of plants and animals. …動植物的進化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Evolution</b> is a process of gradual development in a particular situation or thing over a period of time. 演化; 發展","examples":["...a crucial period in the evolution of modern physics. …現代物理學發展過程中的一個關鍵時期。"]}]}]},"execution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"執行，實施，完成；處決，死刑；表演，製作；政治謀殺；沒收債務人財產，扣押債務人；（法律文書或命令的）執行"}],"sections":[]},"exotic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"奇異的，異國風情的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"外來植物，外來動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>exotic</b> is unusual and interesting, usually because it comes from or is related to a distant country. (常因來自遙遠的他國而顯得) 奇異的","examples":["...brilliantly coloured, exotic flowers. …色彩絢麗的奇異花卉。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"奇異地","examples":["...exotically beautiful scenery. …奇異美景。"]}]}]},"expedition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遠征，考察；探險隊，考察隊；動作敏捷，迅速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>expedition</b> is an organized trip made for a particular purpose such as exploration. (以探險等為目的的) 有組織的旅行","examples":["...Byrd's 1928 expedition to Antarctica. …伯德1982年到南極洲的探險之旅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a group of people who are going on an expedition as an <b>expedition</b>. (以探險等為目的的) 旅行隊","examples":["Forty-three members of the expedition were killed. 探險隊中43名成員喪生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>expedition</b> is a short trip that you make for pleasure. 短程旅行","examples":["...Officer Goss was on a fishing expedition. …戈斯軍官正在進行一次垂釣之旅。"]}]}]},"expertise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專長，專門技能（知識）；專家的意見"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Expertise</b> is special skill or knowledge that is acquired by training, study, or practice. 專業技能; 專業知識","examples":["She was not an accountant and didn't have the expertise to verify all of the financial details. 她不是會計，不具有核查所有這些財政細目的專業知識。"]}]}]},"expiration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"到期，（一段時間的）結束；呼氣，吐氣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>expiration</b> <b>of</b> a fixed period of time is its ending. 結束","examples":["...about ten days before the expiration of my leave of absence. ...大約在我休假結束的十天前。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>expiration</b> of something such as a contract, deadline, or visa is the time when it comes to an end or stops being valid. 期滿","examples":[]}]}]},"exploration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勘探，勘察；研究，探究"}],"sections":[]},"exploit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"剝削，壓榨；利用（……為自己謀利）；運用，發揮；開發，開拓"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"英勇事蹟，壯舉；大膽的表演，不凡的身手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is exploiting</b> you, you think that they are treating you unfairly by using your work or ideas and giving you very little in return. 利用; 剝削","examples":["Critics claim he exploited black musicians for personal gain. 批評家們聲稱他為私利利用了黑人音樂家們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is exploiting</b> a situation, you disapprove of them because they are using it to gain an advantage for themselves, rather than trying to help other people or do what is right. 利用 (某種情勢)","examples":["The government and its opponents compete to exploit the troubles to their advantage. 政府及其反對者們競相利用這些動亂來取得利益。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>exploit</b> something, you use it well, and achieve something or gain an advantage from it. 充分利用","examples":["You'll need a good antenna to exploit the radio's performance. 你需要一根好的天線來充分利用該電臺的節目。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>exploit</b> resources or raw materials means to develop them and use them for industry or commercial activities. 開發利用 (資源、原材料)","examples":["I think we're being very short-sighted in not exploiting our own coal. 我想我們不開採利用自己的煤礦實在是目光短淺。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"利用; 剝削","examples":["Extra payments should be made to protect the interests of the staff and prevent exploitation. 額外報酬應被支付以維護員工的利益和防止剝削。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(對某種情勢的) 利用","examples":["...the exploitation of the famine by local politicians. …當地政客對饑荒的利用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"(對資源、原材料的) 開發利用","examples":["...the planned exploitation of its potential oil and natural gas reserves. …對其潛在石油和天然氣儲備的有計劃的開採利用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>exploits</b>, you mean the brave, interesting, or amusing things that they have done. 英勇事蹟","examples":["His wartime exploits were later made into a film and a television series. 他戰時的英勇事蹟後來被改編成了電影和電視劇。"]}]}]},"eyesight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"目力，視力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>eyesight</b> is your ability to see. 視力","examples":["He suffered from poor eyesight and could no longer read properly. 他視力不好了，再也不能正常地閱讀。"]}]}]},"faction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"派系，宗派；派系之爭，內訌；紀實與虛構相結合的電影（或書等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>faction</b> is an organized group of people within a larger group, which opposes some of the ideas of the larger group and fights for its own ideas. 派系","examples":["A peace agreement will be signed by the leaders of the country's warring factions. 一項和平協議將由該國交戰各派領導們簽署。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a television programme, film, or literary work comprising a dramatized presentation of actual events (電視、電影、文學等的)紀實","examples":[]}]}]},"extract":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"選段，引文；提取物，汁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提取，提煉；取出，拔出；摘錄；索取，設法得到；開（方），求（根）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>extract</b> a substance means to obtain it from something else, for example, by using industrial or chemical processes. 提煉; 提取","examples":["...the traditional method of pick and shovel to extract coal. …用鋤和鏟採煤的傳統方法。","Citric acid can be extracted from the juice of oranges, lemons, limes or grapefruit. 檸檬酸可以從橙汁、檸檬汁、酸橙汁或柚子汁中提取。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>extract</b> something <b>from</b> a place, you take it out or pull it out. 取出","examples":["He extracted a small notebook from his hip pocket. 他從臀後口袋拿出了一本小筆記簿。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a dentist <b>extracts</b> a tooth, they remove it from the patient's mouth. 拔 (牙)","examples":["A dentist may decide to extract the tooth to prevent recurrent trouble. 牙醫可能會決定拔掉這顆牙，以防復發。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>extracts</b> something, you disapprove of them because they take it for themselves to gain an advantage. 謀取","examples":["He sought to extract the maximum political advantage from the cut in interest rates. 他力圖從利息削減中謀取最大的政治利益。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>extract</b> information or a response <b>from</b> someone, you get it from them with difficulty, because they are unwilling to say or do what you want. 探取 (訊息、反映)","examples":["He made the mistake of trying to extract further information from our director. 他犯了想從我們主任那裡探取進一步資訊的錯誤。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>extract</b> a particular piece of information, you obtain it from a larger amount or source of information. 摘取 (資訊)","examples":["I've simply extracted a few figures. 我只是摘取了一些資料。","Britain's trade figures can no longer be extracted from export-and-import documentation at ports. 英國的貿易數字再也不能從各港口的進出口檔案中摘取了。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If part of a book or text <b>is extracted</b> <b>from</b> a particular book, it is printed or published. (從書中) 摘錄","examples":["This material has been extracted from \"Collins Good Wood Handbook.\" 該資料摘自《柯林斯良木手冊》。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"提煉; 提取","examples":["Petroleum engineers plan and manage the extraction of oil. 石油工程師們規劃並管理石油的提煉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"拔牙","examples":["In those days, dentistry was basic. Extractions were carried out without anaesthetic. 那時牙科學剛起步，拔牙是在沒有麻藥的情況下進行的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>extract</b> <b>from</b> a book or piece of writing is a small part of it that is printed or published separately. 摘錄; 選段","examples":["Read this extract from an information booklet about the work of an airline cabin crew. 閱讀這個航空公司機務員工作資訊手冊的選段。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Extract</b> is a very concentrated liquid that is used for flavouring food or for its smell. 高濃縮汁液","examples":["Blend in the vanilla extract, lemon peel, and walnuts. 調和香草精、檸檬皮和核桃。"]}]}]},"famine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"饑荒，饑饉；匱乏，短缺；<古>飢餓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Famine</b> is a situation in which large numbers of people have little or no food, and many of them die. 饑荒","examples":["Thousands of refugees are trapped by war, drought and famine. 成千上萬的難民陷於戰爭、乾旱和饑荒的困境。"]}]}]},"faculty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機能；天賦，才能；（高等院校的）系，院；<美> 全體教員；<舊>（某行業，尤指醫學行業的）全體從業人員；（尤指來自教會當權者的）特許證，許可證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>faculties</b> are your physical and mental abilities. 機能","examples":["He was drunk and not in control of his faculties. 他喝醉了，控制不了他的各項機能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>faculty</b> is all the teaching staff of a university or college, or of one department. 全體教員","examples":["The faculty agreed on a change in the requirements. 全體教員同意改變要求。","How can faculty improve their teaching so as to encourage creativity? 全體教員怎樣才能改進教學以便激發創造力？"]}]}]},"federation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聯邦政府，聯邦；聯合會；結成聯邦（或聯盟）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>federation</b> is a federal country. 聯邦制國家","examples":["...the Russian Federation. …俄羅斯聯邦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>federation</b> is a group of societies or other organizations which have joined together, usually because they share a common interest. 聯合會","examples":["...the American Federation of Government Employees. …美國政府僱員聯合會。"]}]}]},"fascination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"入迷，著迷；魅力，令人著迷的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fascination</b> is the state of being greatly interested in or delighted by something. 著迷","examples":["I've had a lifelong fascination with the sea and with small boats. 我畢生都對海和小船有一份沉迷。"]}]}]},"feedback":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"反饋意見；（訊號返回電子音響系統所致的）噪聲；（返回機器、系統或者程式的）返回資訊，返回電流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get <b>feedback</b> <b>on</b> your work or progress, someone tells you how well or badly you are doing, and how you could improve. If you get good feedback you have worked or performed well. 反饋","examples":["Continue to ask for feedback on your work. 繼續徵求對你工作的反饋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Feedback</b> is the unpleasant high-pitched sound produced by a piece of electrical equipment when part of the signal that comes out goes back into it. (電子訊號產生的) 尖厲噪聲","examples":["The microphone screeched with feedback. 麥克風發出了尖厲的噪聲。"]}]}]},"fidelity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對配偶或伴侶的）忠貞；(對人、組織或信仰的）忠誠；精確性；（CD播放器、收音機、電視機等裝置的）保真度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fidelity</b> is loyalty to a person, organization, or set of beliefs. 忠誠","examples":["People have failed to act in fidelity to their vows. 人們沒能忠誠地履行自己的誓言。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Fidelity</b> is being loyal to your husband, wife, or partner by not having a sexual relationship with anyone else. 忠貞","examples":["Women expect fidelity from their men. 女人期望來自她們男人的忠貞。"]}]}]},"fertility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肥沃，富饒；可繁殖性，生育能力；（思想的）豐富，多產"}],"sections":[]},"flare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"突然燒旺，閃耀；突發，加劇；突然發怒，突然爆發；張開，展開"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"閃耀的光；閃光裝置，訊號彈；突然發怒，發脾氣；喇叭褲；（發炎等症狀的）突然復發；（太陽等恆星的）耀斑；（底片上的）翳霧斑；船舷的翻邊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>flare</b> is a small device that produces a bright flame. Flares are used as signals, for example, on ships. 訊號彈","examples":["...a ship which had fired a distress flare. …一艘發出了遇險訊號彈的船。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a fire <b>flares</b>, the flames suddenly become larger. (火) 突然燒旺","examples":["Camp fires flared like beacons in the dark. 篝火突然熊熊燃燒起來，像黑暗中的燈塔。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as trouble, violence, or conflict <b>flares</b>, it starts or becomes more violent. 爆發; 激化","examples":["Even as the president appealed for calm, trouble flared in several American cities. 即使在總統呼籲大家保持冷靜時，美國幾座城市裡仍在爆發騷亂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If people's tempers <b>flare</b>, they get angry. 發怒","examples":["Tempers flared and harsh words were exchanged. 人們大動肝火，對罵起來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flare up</b> means the same as . 突然燒旺","examples":["Don't spill too much fat on the barbecue as it could flare up. 不要在烤肉上澆太多的油，因為它可能會突然燒起來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Flare up</b> means the same as . 爆發; 激化","examples":["Dozens of people were injured as fighting flared up. 數十人由於戰鬥激化而負傷。"]}]}]},"familiarity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精通，通曉；熟悉，親切感；隨便，冒昧"}],"sections":[]},"fleet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"船隊，艦隊；（某家公司控制的）車隊；小灣，水道"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<文>快速的；快速的；（水）淺的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"淺，不深地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<文>疾馳，飛逝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fleet</b> is a group of ships organized to do something together, for example, to fight battles or to catch fish. 艦隊; 船隊","examples":["A fleet sailed for New South Wales to establish the first European settlement in Australia. 一支艦隊駛向新南威爾士去建立歐洲在澳大利亞的第一個移民地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fleet</b> of vehicles is a group of them, especially when they all belong to a particular organization or business, or when they are all going somewhere together. 車隊","examples":["With its own fleet of trucks, the company delivers most orders overnight. 因為有自己的運輸車隊，該公司的大部分訂貨可以第二天就送到。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"rapid in movement; swift 疾馳的","examples":[]}]}]},"flicker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"閃爍，搖曳；閃現，一閃而過；（表情）掠過；（眼睛）瞟過；顫動，快速抖動；撲動翅膀；使……突然動一下"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（火焰，光的）閃爍，搖曳；（感覺或情緒的）閃現，一閃而過；（身體部位的）小而快的動作；（電影或電視每秒幀數過少時的）影象閃爍；（鳥）撲翅鴷屬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a light or flame <b>flickers</b>, it shines unsteadily. 閃爍不定","examples":["Fluorescent lights flickered, and then the room was blindingly bright. 熒光燈閃了閃，接著房間裡就亮得令人目眩了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flicker</b> is also a noun. 閃爍","examples":["Looking through the window I saw the flicker of flames. 透過窗子望出去，我看到了閃爍的火光。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a visual sensation, often seen in a television image, produced by periodic fluctuations in the brightness of light at a frequency below that covered by the persistence of vision (在光柵掃描顯示中的)閃爍","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"any North American woodpecker of the genus <b>Colaptes</b>, esp <b>C. auratus</b> (<b>yellow-shafted flicker</b>), which has a yellow undersurface to the wings and tail 北美啄木鳥統稱","examples":[]}]}]},"fling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"扔，擲；猛動（身體部位）；粗暴地（向某人）說"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"短暫的風流韻事；一陣盡情的歡樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> something somewhere, you throw it there using a lot of force. 猛擲","examples":["The woman flung the cup at him. 那女人使勁把杯子朝他扔過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> <b>yourself</b> somewhere, you move or jump there suddenly and with a lot of force. 突然移向; 突然跳到","examples":["He flung himself to the floor. 他突然跳到了地板上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> a part of your body in a particular direction, especially your arms or head, you move it there suddenly. 猛然移動 (臂、頭等身體部位)","examples":["She flung her arms around my neck and kissed me. 她猛地摟住我的脖子吻了我。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> someone to the ground, you push them very roughly so that they fall over. 推倒","examples":["The youth got him by the front of his shirt and flung him to the ground. 那個年輕人抓住他的襯衫前襟把他推倒在地。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> something into a particular place or position, you put it there in a quick or angry way. 扔","examples":["Peter flung his shoes into the corner. 彼得把他的鞋扔到了角落裡。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If you <b>fling</b> <b>yourself into</b> a particular activity, you do it with a lot of enthusiasm and energy. 投身於","examples":["She flung herself into her career. 她投身於自己的事業中。"]}]},{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fling</b> can be used instead of \"throw\" in many expressions that usually contain \"throw.\" 在許多短語中可以替代(throw)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two people have <b>a</b> <b>fling</b>, they have a brief sexual relationship. 短暫的風流韻事","examples":["She claims she had a brief fling with him 30 years ago. 她聲稱30年前曾跟他有過一段短暫的風流韻事。"]}]}]},"fluid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流體，液體"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"液體的，流體的；易變的，不穩定的；流暢優美的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fluid</b> is a liquid. 液體","examples":["The blood vessels may leak fluid, which distorts vision. 血管可能滲漏出液體，擾亂視覺。","Make sure that you drink plenty of fluids. 一定要飲用大量流質。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fluid</b> movements or lines or designs are smooth and graceful. 優雅流暢的","examples":["His painting became less illustrational and more fluid. 他的畫變得更為流暢，沒那麼生硬了。"]}]}]},"flutter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"飄動，顫動；振（翼），拍打（翅膀）；翩翩飛舞；（心臟等）砰砰亂跳；急趕，奔走；（心臟等）怦怦亂跳"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"飄動，顫動；<英，非正式> 小賭注；激動，不安；（心臟因激動或緊張而）快速跳動；（錄音中的）顫振"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something thin or light <b>flutters</b>, or if you <b>flutter</b> it, it moves up and down or from side to side with a lot of quick, light movements. 拍動; 飄動","examples":["Her chiffon skirt was fluttering in the night breeze. 她的薄綢裙在晚風中飄動。","...a butterfly fluttering its wings. …一隻拍動著翅膀的蝴蝶。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Flutter</b> is also a noun. 飄動; 拍動","examples":["...a flutter of white cloth. …白布的飄動。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something light such as a small bird or a piece of paper <b>flutters</b> somewhere, it moves through the air with small quick movements. 飄舞; 振翅","examples":["The paper fluttered to the floor. 紙飄落到地板上。"]}]}]},"fraud":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"欺詐，騙局，詭計；騙子；偽劣品，冒牌貨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fraud</b> is the crime of gaining money or financial benefits by a trick or by lying. 詐騙罪","examples":["He was jailed for two years for fraud and deception. 他因詐騙與欺詐被監禁了兩年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fraud</b> is something or someone that deceives people in a way that is illegal or dishonest. 騙人的東西; 騙子","examples":["He's a fraud and a cheat. 他是一個騙子。"]}]}]},"fracture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"破裂，斷裂；骨折；（尤指岩層的）裂縫，裂痕；（語音）母音割裂；由單母音割裂成的複合母音"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"破裂，折斷；瓦解，分裂；毀壞，破壞；違反，越出……範圍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fracture</b> is a crack or break in something, especially a bone. (尤指骨頭) 斷裂","examples":["At least one-third of all women over ninety have sustained a hip fracture. 90歲以上的婦女中至少有1/3遭受過髖骨骨折。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a bone <b>is fractured</b> or <b>fractures</b>, it gets a crack or break in it. 折斷","examples":["You've fractured a rib, maybe more than one. 你斷了一根肋骨，也許不止一根。","One strut had fractured and been crudely repaired in several places. 一根支柱斷裂了，好幾處已做了粗略修補。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something such as an organization or society <b>is fractured</b> or <b>fractures</b>, it splits into several parts or stops existing. 分裂","examples":["His policy risks fracturing the coalition. 他的政策有分裂聯盟的危險。"]}]}]},"fragment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碎片；片段；殘存部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）破碎，分裂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fragment</b> <b>of</b> something is a small piece or part of it. 碎片; 片段","examples":["The only reminder of the shooting is a few fragments of metal in my shoulder. 惟一使我記起那次槍擊的，是我肩膀裡的一些金屬碎片。","She read everything, digesting every fragment of news. 她什麼都讀，對新聞的每一個片段都細細品味。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"分裂","examples":["...the extraordinary fragmentation of styles on the music scene. …音樂界各種風格的不尋常分化。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>fragments</b> or <b>is fragmented</b>, it breaks or separates into small pieces or parts. 碎裂","examples":["The clouds fragmented and out came the sun. 雲開日出。"]}]}]},"friction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不和，分歧；摩擦；摩擦力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>friction</b> between people, there is disagreement and argument between them. (人與人之間的) 摩擦","examples":["Sara sensed that there had been friction between her children. 薩拉感覺到她的孩子們中間出現了摩擦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Friction</b> is the force that makes it difficult for things to move freely when they are touching each other. 摩擦力","examples":["The pistons are graphite-coated to reduce friction. 活塞表面塗有石墨以減少摩擦。"]}]}]},"glassware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"玻璃器皿，玻璃器具類；實驗室玻璃器皿（玻璃儀器）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glassware</b> consists of objects made of glass, such as bowls, drinking containers, and ornaments. 玻璃製品","examples":[]}]}]},"galaxy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"星系；銀河，銀河系（the Galaxy）；群英，人才薈萃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>galaxy</b> is an extremely large group of stars and planets that extends over many billions of light years. 星系","examples":["Astronomers have discovered a distant galaxy. 天文學家們發現了一個遙遠的星系。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The Galaxy</b> is the extremely large group of stars and planets to which the Earth and the solar system belong. 銀河系","examples":["The Galaxy consists of 100 billion stars. 銀河系由1千億顆恆星組成。"]}]}]},"generator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發電機；產生者；電力公司；母點，母線，母面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>generator</b> is a machine which produces electricity. 發電機","examples":["The house is far from water mains and electricity and relies on its own generators. 這座房子遠離自來水總管和供電網，依靠自備的發電機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>generator</b> <b>of</b> something is a person, organization, product, or situation which produces it or causes it to happen. 促使…發生的人或事物","examples":["The company has been a very good cash generator. 這家公司是臺非常出色的賺錢機器。"]}]}]},"genetics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遺傳學；（有機體、特徵等的）遺傳性，遺傳特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Genetics</b> is the study of heredity and how qualities and characteristics are passed on from one generation to another by means of genes. 遺傳學","examples":["Genetics is also bringing about dramatic changes in our understanding of cancer. 遺傳學也正使我們對癌症的理解發生巨大的變化。"]}]}]},"freak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"怪人，怪胎；<非正式>狂熱愛好者；畸形人（或物）；怪異的事；<古>主意突變"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>（使）吃驚，不安，惱怒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反常的，怪異的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>freak</b> event or action is one that is a very unusual or extreme example of its type. 不尋常的","examples":["Weir broke his leg in a freak accident playing golf. 韋爾打高爾夫球時因一次不尋常的事故而摔斷了腿。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as a particular kind of <b>freak</b>, you are emphasizing that they are very enthusiastic about a thing or activity, and often seem to think about nothing else. 狂熱愛好者","examples":["Diaz is a fitness freak who's trained in martial arts. 迪亞斯是個受過武術訓練的健身迷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person, animal, or plant that is abnormal or deformed; monstrosity 畸形; 怪物","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a fleck or streak of colour 彩色斑點; 彩色條紋","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to streak with colour; variegate 使成色彩斑斕","examples":[]}]}]},"glamour":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"吸引力，誘惑力，魅力；迷人的美，奢華；<古>魔法，巫術"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"迷住，迷惑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Glamour</b> is the quality of being more attractive, exciting, or interesting than ordinary people or things. 魅力","examples":["...the glamour of show biz. …演藝業的誘惑力。"]}]}]},"glisten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（尤指因溼潤、油滑或光滑而）閃光，閃亮，閃閃發光"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（溼潤或光滑表面反射的）閃光，閃耀，光澤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>glistens</b>, it shines, usually because it is wet or oily. (因有水或有油而) 發光","examples":["The calm sea glistened in the sunlight. 平靜的海面在陽光下閃閃發光。","Deborah's face was white and glistening with sweat. 德博拉面色蒼白，閃著汗光。"]}]}]},"graph":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖表，曲線圖；座標圖；代表聲音單位（或其他言語特徵）的書寫符號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用圖表表示"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>graph</b> is a mathematical diagram which shows the relationship between two or more sets of numbers or measurements. 圖表","examples":["...a graph showing that breast cancer deaths rose about 20 percent from 1960 to 1985. …一張顯示1960至1985年間乳腺癌死亡人數上升了大約20%的圖表。"]}]}]},"grocer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"食品雜貨商；食品雜貨店"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grocer</b> is a shopkeeper who sells foods such as flour, sugar, and canned foods. 食品雜貨商","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>grocer</b> or a <b>grocer's</b> is the same as a . 食品雜貨店","examples":[]}]}]},"graphic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"詳細的，生動的；繪畫的；圖形的，圖示的；（岩石表面紋理）文象的；（與）可檢視像（有關）的；（與）視覺藝術（有關）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖表，圖形；繪畫，圖形設計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a description or account of something unpleasant is <b>graphic</b>, you are emphasizing that it is clear and detailed. 清楚而具體的","examples":["The descriptions of sexual abuse are graphic. 這些對於性虐待的描述清楚而具體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Graphic</b> means concerned with drawing or pictures, especially in publishing, industry, or computing. 繪圖的; 圖畫的","examples":["...fine and graphic arts. …美術與製圖藝術。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"清楚而具體地","examples":["Here, graphically displayed, was confirmation of the entire story. 這裡，清清楚楚地展示的，是對整件事情的證實。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Graphics</b> is the activity of drawing or making pictures, especially in publishing, industry, or computing. 繪畫; 製圖","examples":["...a computer manufacturer that specializes in graphics. …一家以製圖為專長的電腦製造商。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Graphics</b> are drawings and pictures that are composed using simple lines and sometimes strong colours. 圖形","examples":["The Agriculture Department today released a new graphic to replace the old symbol. 農業部今天釋出了一個新的圖案以取代舊的標誌。"]}]}]},"grope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"摸索；摸索著走；探索，努力尋求；猥褻，亂摸"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"摸，猥褻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grope</b> <b>for</b> something that you cannot see, you try to find it by moving your hands around in order to feel it. 摸索","examples":["With his left hand he groped for the knob, turned it, and pulled the door open. 他用左手摸索到門把手，轉動把手，把門拉開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>grope</b> <b>for</b> something, for example the solution to a problem, you try to think of it, when you have no real idea what it could be. 尋找","examples":["He groped for solutions to his problems. 他尋找問題的解決辦法。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>grope</b> your <b>way</b> to a place, you move there, holding your hands in front of you and feeling the way because you cannot see anything. 摸索而行","examples":["I didn't turn on the light, but groped my way across the room. 我沒有開燈，而是摸索著穿過房間。"]}]}]},"habitat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動植物的）生活環境，棲息地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>habitat</b> of an animal or plant is the natural environment in which it normally lives or grows. 生長環境","examples":["In its natural habitat, the hibiscus will grow up to 25 ft. 在其野生環境中，木槿能長25英尺。"]}]}]},"grill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"烤架；帶烤架的炊具；電焙盤；一盤燒烤食物（尤指烤肉）；烤肉店；門窗護欄（同 grille）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"燒烤，烤制；盤問，追問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>grill</b> is a flat frame of metal bars on which food can be cooked over a fire. (置於火上的) 烤架","examples":["Jerry forced scrap wood through the vents in the grill to stoke the fire. 傑裡從烤架的通風孔塞一些小木片來使火更旺一些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>grill</b> is a part of a stove which produces strong direct heat to cook food that has been placed underneath it. (烤爐內的) 烤架","examples":["Remove from heat and finish off under the grill until cheese melts. 把它從火上拿開，放在烘烤器下面烤到乳酪熔化為止。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"烤","examples":["The breast can be cut into portions for grilling. 胸脯肉可以切成小塊來烤。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"盤問","examples":["He faced a hostile grilling from the committee's Republicans. 他面臨來自委員會中共和黨人不懷好意的盤問。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>grill</b> is a restaurant that serves grilled food. 烤肉餐館","examples":["...patrons of the Savoy Grill. …薩沃伊烤肉店的常客。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>grill</b> food, or when it <b>grills</b>, you cook it on metal bars above a fire or barbecue. 燒烤","examples":["Grill the steaks over a wood or charcoal fire that is quite hot. 在相當熱的柴火或木炭火上烤牛排。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>grill</b> food, or when it <b>grills</b>, you cook it in a stove using very strong heat directly above it. 烘烤","examples":["Grill the meat for 20 minutes on each side. 把肉的兩面分別烤20分鐘。","Apart from peppers and eggplant, many other vegetables grill well. 除了甜椒和茄子，許多別的蔬菜烤起來也不錯。","I'll grill the lobster. 我來烤龍蝦。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>grill</b> someone <b>about</b> something, you ask them a lot of questions for a long period of time. 盤問","examples":["Grill your travel agent about the facilities for families with children. 向旅行社多問問為有孩子隨行的家庭提供的設施。"]}]}]},"hacker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"駭客，駭客；<美，非正式>不擅長某項運動的人；計算機迷；砍（或劈）的人，用於砍（或劈）的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A computer <b>hacker</b> is someone who tries to break into computer systems, especially in order to get secret information. (電腦) 駭客","examples":["...a hacker who steals credit card numbers. …一個竊取信用卡號碼的駭客。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A computer <b>hacker</b> is someone who uses a computer a lot, especially so much that they have no time to do anything else. 計算機迷","examples":[]}]}]},"hail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"讚揚，歡呼；呼喊，招呼；下冰雹；（大量物體）像雹子般落下（或擊打）；<古>表示問候或歡呼歡迎"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"冰雹；雹子般的一陣；招呼（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, event, or achievement <b>is hailed</b> <b>as</b> important or successful, they are praised publicly. 稱讚","examples":["Faulkner has been hailed as the greatest American novelist of his generation. 福克納被讚頌為他那一代人中最偉大的美國小說家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>hail</b> a taxi, you wave at it in order to stop it because you want the driver to take you somewhere. 揮手呼叫","examples":["I hurried away to hail a taxi. 我匆忙離開去揮手招了一輛計程車。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"to greet, esp enthusiastically (熱烈)歡迎","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hail</b> consists of small balls of ice that fall like rain from the sky. 冰雹","examples":["...a sharp short-lived storm with heavy hail. …一場來去匆匆的帶著大冰雹的暴風雨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hail of</b> things, usually small objects, is a large number of them that hit you at the same time and with great force. (雹子般的) 一陣","examples":["The victim was hit by a hail of bullets. 那名受害者被一陣彈雨擊中了。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When <b>it hails</b>, hail falls like rain from the sky. 下冰雹","examples":["It started to hail, huge great stones. 天空開始下冰雹，巨大的雹子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who <b>hails from</b> a particular place was born there or lives there. 出生於","examples":["He hails from Memphis. 他出生於孟菲斯。"]}]},{"pos":"sentence substitute.","pos_name":"sentence substitute.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an exclamation of greeting 歡迎的喊叫聲","examples":[]}]}]},"harassment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"騷擾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Harassment</b> is behaviour which is intended to trouble or annoy someone, for example repeated attacks on them or attempts to cause them problems. 騷擾","examples":["Another survey found that 51 percent of women had experienced some form of sexual harassment in their working lives. 另一份調查顯示有51%的女性在其職業生涯中曾遭遇過某種形式的性騷擾。"]}]}]},"hereafter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（正式/書面語）今後，此後；（法律檔案等）以下；死後"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常用 the）來世，死後生活，死後的靈魂存在；將來"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"今後的，此後的；死後的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hereafter</b> means from this time onward. 今後; 此後","examples":["I realized how hard life was going to be for me hereafter. 我意識到我的生活今後將會多麼艱難。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In legal documents and in written English, <b>hereafter</b> is used to introduce information about an abbreviation that will be used in the rest of the text to refer to the person or thing just mentioned. (法律文書和書面語)以下","examples":["Michel Foucault (1972), The Archaeology of Knowledge; hereafter this text will be abbreviated as AK. 米歇爾•福柯（1972），《知識考古學》，下文簡稱AK。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>hereafter</b> is sometimes used to refer to the time after you have died, or to the life which some people believe you have after you have died. 死後; 死後的靈魂存在","examples":["...belief in the hereafter. ...死後靈魂存在的信仰。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hereafter</b> is also an adjective. 死後的","examples":["...the life hereafter. ...死後靈魂的存在。"]}]}]},"hemisphere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（地球的）半球；腦半球；（球體的）一半"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hemisphere</b> is one half of the earth. 半球","examples":["...the depletion of the ozone layer in the northern hemisphere. …北半球臭氧層的消耗。"]}]}]},"guerrilla":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"游擊隊員；游擊隊；游擊戰（亦作 guerilla）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遊擊的，遊擊式的（多作定語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guerrilla</b> is someone who fights as part of an unofficial army, usually against an official army or police force. 游擊隊員","examples":["The guerrillas threatened to kill their hostages. 游擊隊員們威脅要殺死人質。"]}]}]},"heritage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"遺產，傳統，世襲財產；<美>（植物種類）純種的，老品種的；<古>特殊（或個人）的所有物，（該有的）一份；<古>上帝選擇的人（以色列人或基督教教會）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A country's <b>heritage</b> is all the qualities, traditions, or features of life there that have continued over many years and have been passed on from one generation to another. 遺產; 傳統","examples":["The historic building is as much part of our heritage as the paintings. 這座歷史建築和這些繪畫作品一樣也是留給我們的遺產的組成部分。"]}]}]},"hazard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"危險，危害；（不可避免的）風險；（高爾夫球道）障礙物（如池塘或沙地）；<文>機會，機遇；雙骰子游戲；（網球）可得分割槽域；（檯球）使球觸他球后落入袋中的一擊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"冒失地提出，冒險猜測；使遭危險，使處於危險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hazard</b> is something which could be dangerous to you, your health or safety, or your plans or reputation. 危險","examples":["A new report suggests that chewing gum may be a health hazard. 一份新的報告指出，嚼口香糖可能給健康帶來危害。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hazard</b> or if you <b>hazard</b> a <b>guess</b>, you make a suggestion about something which is only a guess and which you know might be wrong. 大膽猜測","examples":["I would hazard a guess that they'll do fairly well in the next election. 我大膽猜測，他們在下次選舉中將會有不俗的表現。"]}]}]},"heroin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海洛因"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Heroin</b> is a powerful drug which some people take for pleasure, but which they can become addicted to. 海洛因","examples":[]}]}]},"hormone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"激素，荷爾蒙；人造激素；性激素（hormones）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hormone</b> is a chemical, usually occurring naturally in your body, that makes an organ of your body do something. 荷爾蒙","examples":["...the male sex hormone testosterone. …男性性激素睪酮。"]}]}]},"hostility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敵意，對抗；強烈的反對，憤怒反抗；戰鬥，戰爭行動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hostility</b> is unfriendly or aggressive behaviour toward people or ideas. 敵意; 敵對","examples":["The last decade has witnessed a serious rise in the levels of racism and hostility to black and ethnic groups. 過去的10年裡，種族主義及對黑人和少數民族的敵意變得更加嚴重了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>hostility</b> <b>to</b> something you do not approve of is your opposition to it. 反對","examples":["There is hostility among traditionalists to this method of teaching history. 傳統主義者中有人反對這種教授歷史的方法。"]}]}]},"hospitality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"殷勤款待，好客；（公司或機構提供給顧客的）食宿娛樂招待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hospitality</b> is friendly, welcoming behaviour toward guests or people you have just met. 殷勤好客","examples":["Every visitor to Georgia is overwhelmed by the kindness, charm, and hospitality of the people. 來到佐治亞州的每一個人都為當地人的善良、魅力和好客感動不已。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hospitality</b> is the food, drink, and other privileges which some companies provide for their visitors or clients at major sports events or other public events. (在重大體育賽事或其他公共活動中，一些公司為客人提供的) 食物、飲料和其它優待","examples":["...corporate hospitality tents. …公司為客人提供飲料食品等招待服務的帳篷。"]}]}]},"highlight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"突出，強調；用亮色突出；挑染"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最好（或最精彩、最激動人心）的部分；挑染的頭髮；強光部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>highlights</b> a point or problem, they emphasize it or make you think about it. 強調; 使注意","examples":["Last year Collins wrote a moving ballad which highlighted the plight of the homeless. 去年柯林斯寫了一首感人的敘事詩，突出描寫了無家可歸者的苦境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>highlight</b> a piece of text means to mark it in a different colour, either with a special type of pen or on a computer screen. (用不同顏色) 標出; (在電腦螢幕上) 突出顯示","examples":["Highlight the chosen area by clicking and holding down the left mouse button. 透過點選滑鼠左鍵並摁住以突出顯示所選區域。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>highlights</b> <b>of</b> an event, activity, or period of time are the most interesting or exciting parts of it. 最精彩的部分","examples":["...a match that is likely to prove one of the highlights of the tournament. …可能是本屆錦標賽最精彩的賽事之一。"]}]}]},"humanitarian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人道主義的，博愛的；基督凡人論的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"人道主義者，博愛者；慈善家；基督凡人論者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or society has <b>humanitarian</b> ideas or behaviour, they try to avoid making people suffer or they help people who are suffering. 人道主義的","examples":["Air bombardment raised criticism on the humanitarian grounds that innocent civilians might suffer. 空襲遭到了非難，因為從人道主義的角度來看，無辜的平民可能會遭受傷害。"]}]}]},"hunch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"直覺，預感；肉峰；厚片，大塊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"弓身，弓背"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>hunch</b> about something, you are sure that it is correct or true, even though you do not have any proof. 直覺; 預感","examples":["I had a hunch that Susan and I would work well together. 我憑直覺感到我和蘇珊共事會很融洽。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hunch</b> forward, you raise your shoulders, put your head down, and lean forward, often because you are cold, ill, or unhappy. (人) 聳肩弓身","examples":["He got out his map and hunched over it to read the small print. 他掏出地圖並俯身去看上面的小字。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hunch</b> your shoulders, you raise them and lean forward slightly. 聳起 (雙肩) 並微微前傾","examples":["Wes hunched his shoulders and leaned forward on the edge of the counter. 韋斯聳起雙肩，身子向前靠在櫃檯邊。"]}]}]},"hypocrisy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"虛偽，偽善"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of <b>hypocrisy</b>, you mean that they pretend to have qualities, beliefs, or feelings that they do not really have. 虛偽","examples":["He accused newspapers of hypocrisy in their treatment of the story. 他指責報紙在處理這篇報道時所表現出的虛偽。"]}]}]},"hurdle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"障礙，難關；（供人或馬在賽跑中跨越的）欄架，跨欄；跨欄賽跑，障礙賽跑；（把背叛者送往刑場的）囚籠"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（奔跑中）跳越（某物）；參加跨欄賽跑；克服（障礙或困難），渡過難關；用臨時圍欄隔開（或圍住）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hurdle</b> is a problem, difficulty, or part of a process that may prevent you from achieving something. 障礙; 困難","examples":["Two-thirds of candidates fail at this first hurdle and are sent home. 2/3的候選人未能透過這第一關，被打發回家了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Hurdles</b> is a race in which people have to jump over a number of obstacles that are also called hurdles. You can use <b>hurdles</b> to refer to one or more races. 跨欄賽跑","examples":["Davis won the 400 metre hurdles in a new Olympic time of 49.3 sec. 戴維斯以49.3秒這一新的奧運會記錄在400米跨欄賽跑中奪冠。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>hurdle</b>, you jump over something while you are running. (奔跑中) 跨越","examples":["He crossed the lawn and hurdled the short fence. 他穿過草坪，越過低矮的柵欄。"]}]}]},"hypocrite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偽君子，偽善者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of being a <b>hypocrite</b>, you mean that they pretend to have qualities, beliefs, or feelings that they do not really have. 偽君子","examples":["The magazine wrongly suggested he was a liar and a hypocrite. 該雜誌錯誤地暗示他是個騙子和偽君子。"]}]}]},"hygiene":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衛生；衛生學，保健學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hygiene</b> is the practice of keeping yourself and your surroundings clean, especially in order to prevent illness or the spread of diseases. 衛生","examples":["Be extra careful about personal hygiene. 要特別注意個人衛生。"]}]}]},"illusion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯覺，幻覺；幻想，錯誤的觀念"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>illusion</b> is a false idea or belief. 幻想","examples":["No one really has any illusions about winning the war. 事實上沒有人對打贏這場戰爭抱任何幻想。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>illusion</b> is something that appears to exist or be a particular thing but does not actually exist or is in reality something else. 假象","examples":["Floor-to-ceiling windows can look stunning, giving the illusion of extra height. 從地板直抵天花板的窗戶看上去非常漂亮，有增加高度的假象。"]}]}]},"imperative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極重要的，必要的；命令的，強制的；祈使的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要緊急的事，必要的事；祈使語氣，祈使語氣動詞；命令"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If it is <b>imperative</b> that something be done, that thing is extremely important and must be done. 至關重要的","examples":["It was imperative that he act as naturally as possible. 至關重要的是他要儘可能地自然行事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>imperative</b> is something that is extremely important and must be done. 緊迫之事","examples":["The most important political imperative is to limit the number of U.S. casualties. 政治上的當務之急是控制美國的傷亡人數。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, a clause that is in <b>the imperative</b>, or in <b>the imperative</b> mood, contains the base form of a verb and usually has no subject. Examples are \"Go away\" and \"Please be careful.\" Clauses of this kind are typically used to tell someone to do something. 祈使語氣","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>imperative</b> is a verb in the base form that is used, usually without a subject, in an imperative clause. 祈使語氣動詞","examples":[]}]}]},"implement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"執行，貫徹；為……提供工具"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"工具，器具；<蘇格蘭>履行；手段"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>implement</b> something such as a plan, you ensure that what has been planned is done. 實施; 執行","examples":["The government promised to implement a new system to control financial loan institutions. 政府許諾要實施新的制度來控制金融貸款機構。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"實施; 執行","examples":["Very little has been achieved in the implementation of the peace agreement signed last January. 去年1月份簽署的和平協議的執行幾乎沒有什麼進展。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>implement</b> is a tool or other piece of equipment. 器具","examples":["...writing implements. …書寫用具。"]}]}]},"imprisonment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監禁，關押"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Imprisonment</b> is the state of being imprisoned. 監禁","examples":["She was sentenced to seven years' imprisonment. 她被判處7年監禁。"]}]}]},"incentive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"激勵，刺激"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is an <b>incentive</b> <b>to</b> do something, it encourages you to do it. 鼓勵","examples":["There is little or no incentive to adopt such measures. 幾乎或根本沒有鼓勵來採取這樣的措施。"]}]}]},"indignation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憤憤不平，義憤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Indignation</b> is a feeling of shock and anger when you think that something is unjust or unfair. 憤怒不平","examples":["She was filled with indignation at the conditions under which miners were forced to work. 她為礦工們被迫工作的條件滿心憤慨。"]}]}]},"inference":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"推斷，推理；推斷結果，結論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inference</b> is a conclusion that you draw about something by using information that you already have about it. 推論","examples":["There were two inferences to be drawn from her letter. 從她的來信可以得到兩種推論。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Inference</b> is the act of drawing conclusions about something on the basis of information that you already have. 推斷","examples":["It had an extremely tiny head and, by inference, a tiny brain. 它的頭極小，可以根據推斷得出，大腦也小。"]}]}]},"ingenuity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心靈手巧，聰明才智，獨創力；精巧的裝置；靈活的方法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ingenuity</b> is skill at working out how to achieve things or skill at inventing new things. 善於創新; 足智多謀","examples":["Inspecting the nest can be difficult and may require some ingenuity. 仔細檢查鳥巢可能有困難，也許需要一些巧妙的心思。"]}]}]},"incline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）傾向於；點頭；（使）傾斜；贊同（某人，某事）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"斜坡，傾斜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>incline</b> is land that slopes at an angle. 斜坡","examples":["He came to a halt at the edge of a steep incline. 他停步在一個陡坡的邊上。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>incline</b> your head, you bend your neck so that your head is leaning forward. 點 (頭)","examples":["Jack inclined his head very slightly. 傑克微微點了點頭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>incline</b> <b>to</b> think or act in a particular way, or if something <b>inclines</b> you <b>to</b> it, you are likely to think or act in that way. 使傾向於; 使有意於","examples":["...the factors that incline us toward particular beliefs. …使我們傾向於特定信念的種種因素。","Those who fail incline to blame the world for their failure. 那些失敗者往往會將其失敗歸咎於社會。"]}]}]},"inhabitant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某地的）居民，棲息動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>inhabitants</b> of a place are the people who live there. 居民","examples":["...the inhabitants of Boise. …博伊斯的居民。"]}]}]},"injection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"注射；大量資金的投入；（液體）注入，噴入；（宇宙飛船等的）射入軌道，入軌；內射，單射"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>injection</b>, a doctor or nurse puts a medicine into your body using a device with a needle called a syringe. 注射","examples":["They gave me an injection to help me sleep. 他們給我打了一針以助我入眠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>injection</b> <b>of</b> money or resources into an organization is the act of providing it with more money or resources, to help it become more efficient or profitable. (資金或資源的) 注入","examples":["An injection of cash is needed to fund some of these projects. 其中的一些專案需要投入現金資助。"]}]}]},"initiative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"措施，倡議；主動性，積極性；主動權；（美國某些州的）公民立法提案程式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>initiative</b> is an important act or statement that is intended to solve a problem. (重要的) 法案; 倡議","examples":["Local initiatives to help young people have been inadequate. 當地對年輕人的扶助法案一直不夠完善。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a fight or contest, if you have <b>the initiative</b>, you are in a better position than your opponents to decide what to do next. 主動權","examples":["We have the initiative; we intend to keep it. 我們擁有主動權；我們想要保持主動權。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>initiative</b>, you have the ability to decide what to do next and to do it, without needing other people to tell you what to do. 主動性","examples":["She was disappointed by his lack of initiative. 她對他缺乏主動性感到失望。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>initiative</b> is a political procedure in which a group of citizens propose a new law or a change to the law, which all voters can then vote on. 公民立法提案程式","examples":["If they reject or ignore the initiative, the public will vote on it in November. 如果他們拒絕或無視公民立法提案程式，公眾將於11月對它進行投票表決。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take the initiative</b> in a situation, you are the first person to act, and are therefore able to control the situation. 採取主動","examples":["We are the only power willing to take the initiative in the long struggle to end the war. 在旨在結束戰爭的長期鬥爭中，我們是惟一願意首先採取行動的國家。"]}]}]},"injustice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不公正，無道義；非正義行為，不公正事件"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Injustice</b> is a lack of fairness in a situation. 不公正","examples":["They'll continue to fight injustice. 他們將繼續與不公正的現象抗爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An injustice is an action or statement in which someone judges you or treats you unfairly. 不公正的行為; 不公平的評論","examples":["Calling them a bunch of capricious kids with half-formed ideas does them an injustice. 把他們稱作一群懵懂無知、喜怒無常的孩子是冤枉了他們。"]}]}]},"innovation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新事物，新方法；革新，創新"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>innovation</b> is a new thing or a new method of doing something. 新事物; 新方法","examples":["They produced the first vegetarian beanburger – an innovation which was rapidly exported. 他們製造出第一個素式豆堡包–一種被迅速銷往國外的新食品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Innovation</b> is the introduction of new ideas, methods, or things. 創新; 革新","examples":["We must promote originality, inspire creativity and encourage innovation. 我們必須提倡獨創性，激發創造力，鼓勵創新。"]}]}]},"inquiry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詢問，疑問；調查，審查； 探查，探詢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inquiry</b> is a question you ask in order to get some information. 詢問","examples":["He made some inquiries and discovered she had gone to Connecticut. 他詢問了一番，發現她已去了康涅狄格州。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>inquiry</b> is an official investigation. (官方的) 調查","examples":["...a shocking murder inquiry. …一例令人震驚的謀殺案調查。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Inquiry</b> is the process of asking about or investigating something in order to find out more about it. 調查","examples":["The investigation has suddenly switched to a new line of inquiry. 調查突然改用一種新的探詢方法。"]}]}]},"insight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"洞悉，瞭解；洞察力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you gain <b>insight</b> or an <b>insight</b> <b>into</b> a complex situation or problem, you gain an accurate and deep understanding of it. 深入瞭解; 深刻見解","examples":["The project would give scientists new insights into what is happening to the Earth's atmosphere. 該專案將使科學家們對地球大氣層正在發生的情況有更新的瞭解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has <b>insight</b>, they are able to understand complex situations. 洞察力","examples":["He was a man of forceful character, with considerable insight and diplomatic skills. 他是個性格堅強的人，有著非凡的洞察力和交際手腕。"]}]}]},"insistence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"堅決要求，堅持主張"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>insistence</b> on something is the fact that they insist that it should be done or insist that it is the case. 堅持; 堅決要求","examples":["...her insistence on personal privacy. …她對個人隱私權的堅持。"]}]}]},"installation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"安裝，設定；裝置，裝置；（工業或軍事）設施；就職，就職儀式；現代雕塑裝置（除物體外用聲、光等元素）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>installation</b> is a place that contains equipment and machinery that are being used for a particular purpose. 裝置處","examples":["The building was turned into a secret military installation. 該樓被改建成一個秘密軍事設施處。"]}]}]},"installment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分期付款；每期應付款項；（連載或系列作品的）一期，一集；部分；安裝；就職"}],"sections":[]},"implication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可能的影響（或作用、結果）；含意，暗指；牽連，涉及"}],"sections":[]},"integration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結合，融合；取消種族隔離；（數）積分法，求積分；（心理分析）整合"}],"sections":[]},"intellect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"智力，思維能力；才智出眾者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intellect</b> is the ability to understand or deal with ideas and information. 智力","examples":["Do the emotions develop in parallel with the intellect? 情感與智力同步發展嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Intellect</b> is the quality of being intelligent. 才智","examples":["She is famed for her intellect. 她因才智而出名。"]}]}]},"intersection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交接（點或線），相交；交匯點（尤指道路）；（動作）交接，交叉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intersection</b> is a place where roads or other lines meet or cross. 道路交叉口; 交點","examples":["We crossed at a busy intersection. 我們穿過了一個繁忙的道路交叉口。"]}]}]},"integrity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正直，誠實；完整，完全；職業操守；（電子資料的）整合度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>integrity</b>, you are honest and firm in your moral principles. 正直; 誠實","examples":["I have always regarded him as a man of integrity. 我一直把他當作一個正直誠實的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>integrity</b> of something such as a group of people or a text is its state of being a united whole. 完整","examples":["Separatist movements are a threat to the integrity of the nation. 分裂活動是對國家領土完整的威脅。"]}]}]},"institution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機構，團體；社會收容機構；制度，習俗；建立，制定；知名的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>institution</b> is a large important organization such as a university, church, or bank. 機構","examples":["...financial institutions. …金融機構。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>institution</b> is a building where certain people are cared for, such as people who are mentally ill or children who have no parents. 社會福利機構","examples":["Larry has been in an institution since he was four. 拉里從4歲起就在孤兒院生活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>institution</b> is a custom or system that is considered an important or typical feature of a particular society or group, usually because it has existed for a long time. 習俗; 制度","examples":["I believe in the institution of marriage. 我相信婚姻制度。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>institution</b> of a new system is the act of starting it or bringing it in. 建立","examples":["There was never an official institution of censorship in Albania. 阿爾巴尼亞從來就沒有正式建立過審查制度。"]}]}]},"intervention":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"干預，介入；調停，斡旋；（為改善情況尤指病痛採取的）措施，做法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intervention</b> is the act of intervening in a situation. 干涉","examples":["...the role of the United States and its intervention in the internal affairs of many countries. …美國所扮演的角色及其對許多國家內政的干涉。"]}]}]},"intimacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"親密；性，性關係；親暱的言語（或行為）；熟知，精通；親切宜人，幽靜；私事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Intimacy</b> between two people is a very close personal relationship between them. 親密","examples":["...a means of achieving intimacy with another person. …和另一個人建立親密關係的一種方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You sometimes use <b>intimacy</b> to refer to sex or a sexual relationship. 性關係","examples":["He did not feel like intimacy with any woman. 他不想和任何女人發生性關係。"]}]}]},"intruder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"闖入者，侵入者；不速之客"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>intruder</b> is a person who goes into a place where they are not supposed to be. 侵入者","examples":["He owned a gun for scaring off intruders. 他有一支槍，用來嚇走入侵者。"]}]}]},"interval":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"間隔，間隙；幕間休息，中場休息；音程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interval</b> between two events or dates is the period of time between them. (時間上的) 間隔","examples":["The process is repeated after a short interval of time. 該程式間隔很短時間就重複一次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>interval</b> during a concert, show, film, or game is a short break between two of the parts. 幕間休息; 中場休息","examples":["...during the interval of the musical \"Steppin' Out.\" …在音樂劇《影舞追夢》的幕間休息期間。","Fraser did not perform until after the interval. 弗雷澤直到中場休息之後才出場。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>at intervals</b>, it happens several times with gaps or pauses in between. 不時","examples":["She woke him for his medicines at intervals throughout the night. 整個晚上她不時叫醒他，讓他吃藥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If things are placed <b>at</b> particular <b>intervals</b>, there are spaces of a particular size between them. 每隔","examples":["Several red and white barriers marked the road at intervals of about a mile. 每隔1英里左右就有一些紅白相間的路障來標示道路。"]}]}]},"inventory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詳細目錄，清單；存貨，庫存；盤貨，存貨盤點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開列清單"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inventory</b> is a supply or stock of something. 存貨","examples":["...one inventory of twelve sails for each yacht. …為每艘遊艇配備12張帆的存貨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>inventory</b> is a written list of all the objects in a particular place such as all the merchandise in a shop. 清單","examples":["Before starting, he made an inventory of everything that was to stay. 出發前，他把要留下的所有東西列了一份詳細清單。"]}]}]},"investigator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"調查者，偵察員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>investigator</b> is someone who carries out investigations, especially as part of their job. 調查者","examples":["...an undercover investigator. …一位秘密偵探。"]}]}]},"irony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（出乎意料的）奇異可笑之處，具有諷刺意味的情況；反語，諷刺"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鐵的；含鐵的；似鐵的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Irony</b> is a subtle form of humour that involves saying things that are the opposite of what you really mean. 諷刺","examples":["His tone was tinged with irony. 他的語氣中微含諷刺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>irony</b> of a situation, you mean that it is odd or amusing because it involves a contrast. 具有諷刺意味的事","examples":["The irony is that many officials in Washington agree in private that their policy is inconsistent. 具有諷刺意味的是，華盛頓的許多官員私下裡承認他們的政策是前後矛盾的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"of, resembling, or containing iron 鐵的; 似鐵的; 含鐵的","examples":[]}]}]},"irritation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"惱怒，生氣；（尤指一段時間的）惱人事，煩惱；（身體某部位的）疼痛；刺激（作用），興奮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Irritation</b> is a feeling of annoyance, especially when something is happening that you cannot easily stop or control. 惱怒","examples":["He tried not to let his irritation show as he blinked in the glare of the television lights. 在對著耀眼的電視光線眨眼時，他竭力不把自己的惱怒表現出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>irritation</b> is something that keeps annoying you. 惱人的事","examples":["Don't allow a minor irritation in the workplace to mar your ambitions. 不要讓工作場所中一件煩人的小事把你遠大的抱負破壞了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Irritation</b> in a part of your body is a feeling of slight pain and discomfort there. 刺激","examples":["These oils may cause irritation to sensitive skins. 這幾種油可能會對敏感皮膚有刺激。"]}]}]},"lament":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輓歌，悼文；表達哀傷（或痛惜）之情的言辭；抱怨"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"對……感到悲痛，對……表示失望；抱怨"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lament</b> something, you express your sadness, regret, or disappointment about it. 感到悲痛; 感到遺憾; 感到失望","examples":["Ken began to lament the death of his only son. 肯為他獨生子的去世開始感到悲痛。","He laments that people in Villa El Salvador are suspicious of the police. 他感到遺憾的是埃爾薩爾瓦多城的人們不信任警察。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>lament</b> is an expression of their sadness, regret, or disappointment about something. 哀嘆","examples":["She spoke of the professional woman's lament that a woman's judgment is questioned more than a man's. 她談到職業女性的悲哀，即女性的判斷會比男性的遭到更多的置疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lament</b> is a poem, song, or piece of music which expresses sorrow that someone has died. 悼詩; 悼歌; 哀樂","examples":["...Shelley's lament for the death of Keats. …雪萊為濟慈之死寫的悼詩。"]}]}]},"lava":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（火山）熔岩，岩漿；火山岩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Lava）（西、意）拉瓦（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lava</b> is the very hot liquid rock that comes out of a volcano. 熔岩","examples":["Mexico's Mount Colima began spewing lava and ash last night. 墨西哥科利馬山昨晚開始噴發熔岩和火山灰。"]}]}]},"layman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外行，門外漢；（基督教中的）平信徒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>layman</b> is a person who is not trained, qualified, or experienced in a particular subject or activity. 外行人","examples":["The mere mention of the words \"heart failure\" can conjure up, to the layman, the prospect of imminent death. 一提到“心力衰竭”幾個字，外行人就會想到立即死亡。"]}]}]},"layout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"佈局，設計；版面編排，版面設計；佈置的東西，陳列品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>layout</b> of a park, building, or piece of writing is the way in which the parts of it are arranged. (建築或文章的) 佈局","examples":["He tried to recall the layout of the farmhouse. 他想回憶那農舍的佈局。"]}]}]},"legislator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立法者，立法委員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>legislator</b> is a person who is involved in making or passing laws. 立法者","examples":["...an attempt to get U.S. legislators to change the system. …讓美國立法者改變體制的一次努力。"]}]}]},"legislature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立法機關，立法機構，議會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>legislature</b> of a particular state or country is the group of people in it who have the power to make and pass laws. 立法機構; 議會","examples":["The proposals before the legislature include the creation of two special courts to deal exclusively with violent crimes. 擺在議會面前的提案包括建立兩個特殊法庭專門審理暴力犯罪案件。"]}]}]},"limo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>豪華轎車（limousine 的縮略形式，通常指由專職司機駕駛的大型豪華轎車，也可指加長禮賓車）；（Limo）人名（塞爾維亞、芬蘭等地譯作利莫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>limo</b> is a . 豪華轎車","examples":[]}]}]},"liberation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解放，解放運動；解脫；釋出，放出；<非正式>劫掠，偷盜"}],"sections":[]},"limousine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"豪華轎車，大型豪華轎車（通常由專職司機駕駛，多用於商務或重要場合）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>limousine</b> is a large and very comfortable car. Limousines are usually driven by a chauffeur and often hired for important occasions. 豪華轎車","examples":[]}]}]},"kernel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（堅果可食用的）仁，核；玉米粒；（陳述、觀點、計劃等的）核心，要點；（某物的）極小一部分，微量；（計算機作業系統的）核心程式；（語言學）核心句"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>kernel</b> of a nut is the part that is inside the shell. (果)仁","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>kernel</b> of a cereal crop such as wheat is the seed that is inside the hard husk. (小麥等穀類作物麩殼裡的)穀粒","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>kernel</b> <b>of</b> something is the central and most important part of it. 核心","examples":["The kernel of that message was that peace must not be a source of advantage or disadvantage for anyone. 那一資訊的核心是和平絕不應該成為對任何人有利或不利的根源。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>kernel</b> <b>of</b> something is a small element of it. 一小部分","examples":["For all I know, there may be a kernel of truth in what he says. 據我所知，他的話可能有一點兒道理。"]}]}]},"liner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵輪；襯裡，內襯；細畫筆，細漆刷；（不用漁網的海上）釣魚船；覓蹤雪貂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>liner</b> is a large ship in which people travel long distances, especially on holiday. 客輪","examples":["...luxury ocean liners. …豪華遠洋客輪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a material used as a lining 襯裡","examples":[]}]}]},"linguist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精通外國語言的人；語言學家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>linguist</b> is someone who is good at speaking or learning foreign languages. 通曉數國外語的人; 學多種外語的人","examples":["He had a scholarly air and was an accomplished linguist. 他有一種學者的風度，而且是個熟練掌握多國語言的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>linguist</b> is someone who studies or teaches linguistics. 語言學家","examples":["Many linguists have looked at language in this way. 許多語言學家就是這樣看待語言的。"]}]}]},"liter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計量）公升，升（容量單位；美國英語拼寫，英國英語拼寫作 litre）；（Liter）人名；（英）利特"}],"sections":[]},"liquid crystal display":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"液晶顯示器：一種使用液晶技術來顯示影象的裝置，廣泛應用於電子裝置中，如計算機顯示器、電視、手機等。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>liquid crystal display</b> is a display of information on a screen, which uses liquid crystals that become visible when electricity is passed through them. 液晶顯示器","examples":[]}]}]},"literacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"識字，讀寫能力；專業知識；精通文學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Literacy</b> is the ability to read and write. 讀寫能力","examples":["Many adults have problems with literacy and numeracy. 很多成年人有讀寫和計算的困難。"]}]}]},"literate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有讀寫能力的，受過良好教育的；熟練的，通曉的；精通文學的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"有文化的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>literate</b> is able to read and write. 能讀會寫的","examples":["Over one-quarter of the adult population are not fully literate. 四分之一以上的成年人是半文盲。"]}]}]},"longevity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壽命；長壽，持久；持續時間，耐用期限；長期存在，長期供職"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Longevity</b> is long life. 長壽","examples":["Human longevity runs in families. 人類長壽是有遺傳的。","The main characteristic of the strike has been its longevity. 這次罷工的主要特點是持續時間長。"]}]}]},"lounge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（機場等的）等候室；（旅館、俱樂部等的）休息室；（私宅中的）起居室，客廳；<英>休閒，遊蕩；<美>躺椅，沙發；<英>雅座酒吧；<美>雞尾酒酒吧"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"懶洋洋地站（或坐、躺）著；<英>百無聊賴地消磨（打發）時間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a hotel, club, or other public place, a <b>lounge</b> is a room where people can sit and relax. 休息廳","examples":["I spoke to her in the lounge of a big Johannesburg hotel where she was attending a union meeting. 我在約翰內斯堡一家大酒店的休息室和她說過話，當時她在那兒參加一個工會會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In an airport, a <b>lounge</b> is a very large room where people can sit and wait for aircraft to arrive or leave. 等候大廳","examples":["Instead of taking me to the departure lounge they took me right to my seat on the plane. 他們沒有帶我去候機廳，而是直接把我帶到了飛機的座位上。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In a house, a <b>lounge</b> is a room where people sit and relax. 起居室","examples":["The present owners added a new kitchen, a front porch and a lounge. 目前的主人增添了一個新的廚房，一個前沿和一個會客廳。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lounge</b> somewhere, you sit or lie there in a relaxed or lazy way. 懶洋洋地坐著; 懶散地躺著","examples":["They ate and drank and lounged in the shade. 他們在陰涼處懶洋洋地坐著，又吃又喝。"]}]}]},"lyric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"歌詞；抒情詩"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"抒情的，寫抒情詩的；（歌聲）柔美的；適於演奏的；（感情、風格等）奔放的，不拘束的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lyric</b> poetry is written in a simple and direct style, and usually expresses personal emotions such as love. 抒情的 (詩歌)","examples":["...Lawrence's splendid short stories and lyric poetry. …勞倫斯出色的短篇小說和抒情詩。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>lyrics</b> of a song are its words. 歌詞","examples":["...Kurt Weill's Broadway opera with lyrics by Langston Hughes. …由蘭斯頓·休斯作詞的庫爾特·韋爾的百老匯歌劇。"]}]}]},"lunatic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瘋狂的，極其愚蠢的；混亂的，失控的；為精神錯亂者而設的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘋狂的人， 愚笨的人；精神病患者，瘋子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as a <b>lunatic</b>, you think they behave in a dangerous, stupid, or annoying way. 瘋子","examples":["Her son thinks she's an absolute raving lunatic. 她的兒子認為她是個十足的滿口胡言的瘋子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"People who were mentally ill used to be called <b>lunatics</b>. 精神病患者","examples":["...the lunatics in the Bedlam asylum. …貝德蘭瘋人院的精神病人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour or ideas as <b>lunatic</b>, you think they are very foolish and possibly dangerous. 極端愚蠢的; 瘋狂的","examples":["...the operation of the market taken to lunatic extremes. …瘋狂到極點的市場運作。"]}]}]},"magnitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"巨大，重要性；震級；規模，大小；數量，數值；（恆星的）亮度，星等"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>magnitude</b> of something, you are talking about its great size, scale, or importance. (尺寸、規模、重要性等) 大的程度","examples":["An operation of this magnitude is going to be difficult. 一個這麼大的手術會很難的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>order of magnitude</b> when you are giving an approximate idea of the amount or importance of something. 重要級; 數量級","examples":["America and Russia do not face a problem of the same order of magnitude as Japan. 美俄兩國沒有面臨與日本同樣的重要級別的問題。"]}]}]},"malaria":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘧疾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Malaria</b> is a serious disease carried by mosquitoes, which causes periods of fever. 瘧疾","examples":[]}]}]},"manuscript":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手稿，原稿；手抄本，手寫本"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"手寫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>manuscript</b> is a handwritten or typed document, especially a writer's first version of a book before it is published. 手稿","examples":["He had seen a manuscript of the book. 他見過這本書的一份手稿。"]}]}]},"massacre":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"屠殺，殘殺；<非正式>（運動或比賽中的）慘敗"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（大規模地）屠殺，殺戮；<非正式>（比賽或競爭等中）使慘敗，徹底擊敗；<非正式>笨拙地演奏（演唱）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>massacre</b> is the killing of a large number of people at the same time in a violent and cruel way. 大屠殺","examples":["Maria lost her 62-year-old mother in the massacre. 瑪麗亞在大屠殺中失去了她62歲的母親。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>are massacred</b>, a large number of them are attacked and killed in a violent and cruel way. 大規模屠殺","examples":["300 civilians are believed to have been massacred by the rebels. 據信300名平民被叛亂分子屠殺了。"]}]}]},"mastery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精通，熟練掌握；控制，駕馭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you show <b>mastery</b> <b>of</b> a particular skill or language, you show that you have learned or understood it completely and have no difficulty using it. 掌握","examples":["He doesn't have mastery of the basic rules of grammar. 他沒有掌握基本的語法規則。"]}]}]},"materialism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"唯物主義，唯物論；物質主義"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Materialism</b> is the attitude of someone who attaches a lot of importance to money and wants to possess a lot of material things. 物質主義","examples":["...the rising consumer materialism in society at large. …全社會範圍內日益高漲的消費者物質主義。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Materialism</b> is the belief that only physical matter exists, and that there is no spiritual world. 唯物主義","examples":["Scientific materialism thus triumphed over ignorance and superstition. 科學唯物主義就這樣戰勝了無知和迷信。"]}]}]},"material":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣料，布料；材料，原料；素材；節目，劇目；（有指明特徵的）人才；（某一活動所需的）材料"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"物質的，非精神上的；重要的，需予以考慮的；和推理內容有關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>material</b> is a solid substance. 固態物質","examples":["...electrons in a conducting material such as a metal. …金屬等導電物質中的電子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Material</b> is cloth. 布料","examples":["...the thick material of her skirt. …她裙子的厚布料。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Materials</b> are the things that you need for a particular activity. 材料","examples":["The builders ran out of materials. 建築商用完了材料。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Ideas or information that are used as a basis for a book, play, or film can be referred to as <b>material</b>. 素材","examples":["In my version of the story, I added some new material. 在我這個版本的故事中，我新增了一些新素材。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Material</b> things are related to possessions or money, rather than to more abstract things such as ideas or values. 物質的","examples":["Every room must have been stuffed with material things. 每個房間肯定已經堆滿了東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Material</b> evidence or information is directly relevant and important in a legal or academic argument. (法律或學術辯論中) 實質性的 (證據或資訊)","examples":["The nature and availability of material evidence was not to be discussed. 關鍵證據的性質和有效性將不予以討論。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"物質上地","examples":["He has tried to help this child materially and spiritually. 他已經盡力在物質和精神上幫助這個孩子了。"]}]}]},"mattress":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"床墊，褥墊；（工程）墊層，沉排，鋼筋網"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mattress</b> is the large, flat object which is put on a bed to make it comfortable to sleep on. 床墊","examples":[]}]}]},"mechanism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"機械裝置，機件；途徑，方法；（生物體內的）機制，構造；機械論；（產生自然現象等的）物理過程"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a machine or piece of equipment, a <b>mechanism</b> is a part, often consisting of a set of smaller parts, which performs a particular function. 機械裝置","examples":["...the locking mechanism. …鎖定裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mechanism</b> is a special way of getting something done within a particular system. 機制","examples":["There's no mechanism for punishing arms exporters who break the rules. 對於違反規定的軍火出口商還沒有懲罰機制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>mechanism</b> is a part of your behaviour that is automatic and that helps you to survive or to cope with a difficult situation. (行為的) 機制","examples":["...a survival mechanism, a means of coping with intolerable stress. …一種生存機制，一種應對無法承受的壓力的方法。"]}]}]},"lure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引誘，誘惑"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"誘惑（物），誘惑力；魚餌，誘餌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>lure</b> someone means to trick them into a particular place or to trick them into doing something that they should not do. 引誘","examples":["He lured her to his home and shot her with his father's gun. 他把她誘騙到家裡，然後用父親的槍把她打死。","They did not realize that they were being lured into a trap. 他們沒有意識到正被人騙入圈套。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lure</b> is an object which is used to attract animals, especially fish, so that they can be caught. 誘餌","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lure</b> is an attractive quality that something has, or something that you find attractive. 誘惑力; 魅力","examples":["The excitement of hunting big game in Africa has been a lure to Europeans for 200 years. 在非洲捕捉大型獵物所帶來的刺激，200年來一直吸引著歐洲人。"]}]}]},"medication":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥物，藥品；藥物治療"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Medication</b> is medicine that is used to treat and cure illness. 藥物","examples":["When somebody comes for treatment I always ask them if they are on any medication. 有人來治療時，我總是會問他們是否在服藥。"]}]}]},"meditation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"冥想，打坐；沉思，深思；（關於某主題的）感想，沉思錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Meditation</b> is the act of remaining in a silent and calm state for a period of time, as part of a religious training, or so that you are more able to deal with the problems of everyday life. 沉思","examples":["Many busy executives have begun to practise yoga and meditation. 許多工作繁忙的主管已開始練習瑜伽和冥想。"]}]}]},"melancholy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抑鬱，憂鬱；精神病（=melancholia）；<史>黑膽汁（=black bile）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（令人）悲哀的，（令人）沮喪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You describe something that you see or hear as <b>melancholy</b> when it gives you an intense feeling of sadness. 憂鬱的","examples":["The only sounds were the distant, melancholy cries of the sheep. 惟一的聲音是遠處的羊群的哀叫。"]}]}]},"mentality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"心態，思維方式；智力，智慧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>mentality</b> is your attitudes and your way of thinking. 心態","examples":["...a criminal mentality. …一種犯罪心態。"]}]}]},"merchandise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"商品，貨品；相關商品，指定商品"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用廣告等方式）推銷（商品或服務）；推介，宣傳（思想，人）；<古>從商"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Merchandise</b> is products that are bought, sold, or traded. 商品","examples":["...a mail-order company that provides merchandise for people suffering from allergies. …一家為患過敏症的人提供商品的郵購公司。"]}]}]},"metaphor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"隱喻，暗喻；象徵，標誌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>metaphor</b> is an imaginative way of describing something by referring to something else which is the same in a particular way. For example, if you want to say that someone is very shy and frightened of things, you might say that they are a mouse. 隱喻","examples":["...the avoidance of violent expressions and metaphors like \"kill two birds with one stone.\" …避免使用有暴力意味的表達和隱喻，如“一石二鳥。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing is a <b>metaphor</b> <b>for</b> another, it is intended or regarded as a symbol of it. 象徵","examples":["The divided family remains a powerful metaphor for a society that continued to tear itself apart. 破裂的家庭仍然是一個持續分裂的社會的有力象徵。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mix</b> your <b>metaphors</b>, you use two conflicting metaphors. People do this accidentally, or sometimes deliberately as a joke. 把兩個矛盾的隱喻混用在一起","examples":["To mix yet more metaphors, you were trying to run before you could walk, and I've clipped your wings. 再混用一些隱喻，你還不會走就想跑，而我又修短了你的翅膀。"]}]}]},"metropolitan":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大都市的；本土的；（與）宗主國（有關）的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（東正教和天主教的）大主教；大城市人，都會居民"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Metropolitan</b> means belonging to or typical of a large, busy city. 大都會的","examples":["...the metropolitan district of Miami. …邁阿密的大都會區。","...a dozen major metropolitan hospitals. …12家主要的大都會醫院。"]}]}]},"migration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移民，遷徙；（計算機系統的）改變，（程式或硬體的）遷移，轉移"}],"sections":[]},"miller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經營或操作磨坊（尤指磨穀物磨坊）的人：磨坊主，碾磨工，磨粉工；蛾（尤指翅上有粉狀鱗片的蛾）；（機械）銑床；（Miller）姓氏（英語、德語、法語、愛沙尼亞語、芬蘭語、羅馬尼亞語、瑞典語、波蘭語譯作“米勒”；西班牙語、葡萄牙語譯作“米列爾”）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>miller</b> is a person who owns or operates a mill in which grain is crushed to make flour. 磨坊主; 磨粉工","examples":[]}]}]},"militant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"好鬥的，激進的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"激進分子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>militant</b> to describe people who believe in something very strongly and are active in trying to bring about political or social change, often in extreme ways that other people find unacceptable. 激進的","examples":["Militant mine workers in the Ukraine have voted for a one-day stoppage next month. 在烏克蘭，激進的煤礦工人們已經投票決定在下個月進行一天的罷工。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Militant</b> is also a noun. 激進分子","examples":["Even now we could not be sure that the militants would not find some new excuse to call a strike the following winter. 即使到現在，我們也不能確定這些激進分子不會找到某個新的藉口在下一年冬天號召一場罷工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"好戰性","examples":["...the rise of trade union militancy. …工會好戰情緒的高漲。"]}]}]},"mimic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"模仿（人的言行舉止）；模擬（外觀或效果）；模擬（另一種植物或動物）；（藥）模擬（另一物質）的生理作用；（疾病）表現出（另一疾病）的症狀"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"善於模仿的人；會模擬的動物（或植物）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"模擬的，演習的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mimic</b> the actions or voice of a person or animal, you imitate them, usually in a way that is meant to be amusing or entertaining. 模仿","examples":["He could mimic anybody, and he often reduced Isabel to helpless laughter. 他可以模仿任何人，而且經常逗得伊莎貝爾情不自禁地大笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>mimics</b> another person or thing, they try to be like them. 模仿","examples":["The computer doesn't mimic human thought; it reaches the same ends by different means. 計算機模仿不了人類的思維；它透過不同的方式達到相同的目的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mimic</b> is a person who is able to mimic people or animals. 善於模仿的人","examples":["At school I was a good mimic. 上學時我是一個善於模仿的人。"]}]}]},"missionary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（派往國外的）傳教士"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"傳教的；（熱情）傳教士般的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>missionary</b> is a Christian who has been sent to a foreign country to teach people about Christianity. 傳教士","examples":["My mother would still like me to be a missionary in Africa. 我母親還是想讓我在非洲做一名傳教士。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Missionary</b> is used to describe the activities of missionaries. 傳教的","examples":["You should be in missionary work. 你該參加傳教工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to someone's enthusiasm for an activity or belief as <b>missionary</b> zeal, you are emphasizing that they are very enthusiastic about it. 傳教士般的","examples":["She had a kind of missionary zeal about bringing culture to the masses. 她對把文化帶給大眾具有一種傳教士般的熱情。"]}]}]},"modernization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現代化"}],"sections":[]},"miniature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"微型的，小型的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"縮微模型，微型複製品；微型畫，小畫像；小瓶裝酒；小種植物（或動物）；（華美裝飾手稿上的）畫飾，花字"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Miniature</b> is used to describe something that is very small, especially a smaller version of something which is normally much bigger. 微型的","examples":["Rosehill Farm has been selling miniature roses since 1979. 自1979年起，玫瑰山農場就一直出售袖珍玫瑰。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe one thing as another thing <b>in miniature</b>, you mean that it is much smaller in size or scale than the other thing, but is otherwise exactly the same. 縮影","examples":["Ecuador provides a perfect introduction to South America; it's a continent in miniature. 厄瓜多是南美的一個絕佳概覽；它是整個大陸的縮影。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>miniature</b> is a very small, detailed painting, often of a person. 袖珍畫像","examples":[]}]}]},"mold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模具，鑄模，模子；模製品；框架；型別，個性，風格；體型，模樣；黴，黴菌；鬆軟沃土，耕作土壤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"澆鑄，塑造，用模子製作；影響（性格、觀點等），對……影響重大，將……塑造成；（使）緊貼於，吻合，輪廓相符；（使）發黴"}],"sections":[]},"momentum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衝力，推力；動力，勢頭；動量，衝量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a process or movement gains <b>momentum</b>, it keeps developing or happening more quickly and keeps becoming less likely to stop. 勢頭","examples":["This campaign is really gaining momentum. 這場運動確實勢頭正猛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In physics, <b>momentum</b> is the mass of a moving object multiplied by its speed in a particular direction. 動量","examples":[]}]}]},"morality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"道德，品行；正當性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Morality</b> is the belief that some behaviour is right and acceptable and that other behaviour is wrong. 道德觀念","examples":["...standards of morality and justice in society. …社會中道德和正義的標準。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>morality</b> is a system of principles and values concerning people's behaviour, which is generally accepted by a society or by a particular group of people. 道德規範","examples":["...a morality that is sexist. …性別歧視的道德規範。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>morality</b> <b>of</b> something is how right or acceptable it is. 道德性","examples":["...the arguments about the morality of blood sports. …關於流血運動的道德性的爭論。"]}]}]},"monotony":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"單調乏味，千篇一律；（聲音或話語的）單調"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>monotony</b> of something is the fact that it never changes and is boring. 單調乏味; 一成不變","examples":["A night on the town may help to break the monotony of the week. 去城裡待一晚也許有助改變一週工作生活的單調。"]}]}]},"motto":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"座右銘，格言，警句；格言主題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>motto</b> is a short sentence or phrase that expresses a rule for sensible behaviour, especially a way of behaving in a particular situation. 格言","examples":["\"Stay true to yourself\" has always been his motto. “忠於自己”一直是他的座右銘。"]}]}]},"monopoly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壟斷，壟斷權；壟斷企業，專賣者；獨佔，專利品；大富翁（棋類遊戲,遊戲者以玩具鈔票買賣房地產）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company, person, or state has a <b>monopoly</b> <b>on</b> something such as an industry, they have complete control over it, so that it is impossible for others to become involved in it. 壟斷","examples":["...Russian moves to end a state monopoly on land ownership. …俄羅斯人提議結束國家對土地所有權的壟斷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>monopoly</b> is a company which is the only one providing a particular product or service. 壟斷企業","examples":["...a state-owned monopoly. …一個國有壟斷企業。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone does not have a <b>monopoly</b> <b>on</b> something, you mean that they are not the only person who has that thing. 獨有","examples":["Women do not have a monopoly on feelings of betrayal. 背叛感並非是女人獨有的。"]}]}]},"morale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"士氣，精神面貌"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Morale</b> is the amount of confidence and cheerfulness that a group of people have. 士氣","examples":["Many pilots are suffering from low morale. 很多飛行員現在士氣低落。"]}]}]},"mouthpiece":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喉舌；代言人；送話口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>mouthpiece</b> of a telephone is the part that you speak into. (電話的) 話筒","examples":["He shouted into the mouthpiece. 他衝著電話話筒大叫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>mouthpiece</b> of a musical instrument or other device is the part that you put into your mouth. (樂器的) 吹口; (器具的) 銜口","examples":["He showed him how to blow into the ivory mouthpiece. 他給他演示瞭如何把氣吹進象牙吹口。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>mouthpiece</b> of an organization or person is someone who informs other people of the opinions and policies of that organization or person. 代言人","examples":["Their mouthpiece is the vice president. 他們的代言人是副總裁。"]}]}]},"mythology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"神話，神話故事；錯誤的信念，謬誤；神話學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mythology</b> is a group of myths, especially all the myths from a particular country, religion, or culture. 神話 (集體名詞)","examples":["In Greek mythology, the god Zeus took the form of a swan to seduce Leda. 在希臘神話中，主神宙斯用天鵝之形引誘勒達。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>mythology</b> to refer to the beliefs or opinions that people have about something, when you think that they are false or untrue. 神話","examples":["Altman strips away the pretense and mythology to expose the film industry as a business like any other, dedicated to the pursuit of profit. 奧爾特曼揭去電影業的偽裝和神話，揭示了其與任何行業一樣追逐利潤的本質。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"神話中的","examples":["...the mythological beast that was part lion and part goat. …神話中半獅半羊的怪獸。"]}]}]},"narrative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"記敘文，敘述；敘事技巧"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"敘述的；敘事體的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>narrative</b> is a story or an account of a series of events. 故事; 敘事","examples":["...a fast-moving narrative. …一個快節奏的敘事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Narrative</b> is the description of a series of events, usually in a novel. (尤指小說中的) 記敘","examples":["Neither author was very strong on narrative. 兩位作者在記敘方面都不強。"]}]}]},"narrator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（小說或電影的）敘述者，敘事人；（電影或電視節目中的）解說員，旁白員"}],"sections":[]},"mute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"緘默的，沉默的；啞的，不會說話的；無聲的，寧靜的；（獵犬）追獵時不吠叫的；（字母）啞音的，無音的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"弱音器；啞巴；<舊>一群獵狗；<史>（一些亞洲國家的）啞奴，啞僕；<史>啞劇演員；受僱的送葬人，以送葬為業者；閉鎖音"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"消音，減音；減弱，緩和；關閉聲音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>mute</b> is silent for a particular reason and does not speak. 緘默的","examples":["He was mute, distant, and indifferent. 他緘默無言，對人疏遠而且冷漠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>mute</b> is unable to speak. 啞的","examples":["Marianna, the duke's daughter, became mute after a shock. 公爵的女兒瑪麗安娜在一場驚嚇之後失語了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"溫和的","examples":["The threat contrasted starkly with his administration's previous muted criticism. 這恐嚇與他執政當局先前溫和的批評形成了鮮明的對比。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(聲音) 降低的","examples":["\"Yes,\" he muttered, his voice so muted I hardly heard his reply. “是啊，”他輕聲說道，聲音輕得我幾乎聽不到他的回答。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mute</b> is also an adverb. 緘默地","examples":["He could watch her standing mute by the phone. 他能看到她緘默地站在電話旁。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mutes</b> something such as their feelings or their activities, they reduce the strength or intensity of them. 抑制 (感情等); 減弱 (行動的力度等)","examples":["The corruption does not seem to have muted the country's prolonged economic boom. 腐敗看來沒有減緩該國持續的經濟繁榮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>mute</b> a noise or sound, you lower its volume or make it less distinct. 降低 (聲音)","examples":["They begin to mute their voices, not be as assertive. 他們開始放低嗓門，不再那麼肯定了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"any of various devices used to soften the tone of stringed or brass instruments (樂器的)弱音器; 削音器","examples":[]}]}]},"naturalist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"博物學家，博物學者；自然主義者（哲學、文學、藝術等領域信奉或實踐自然主義的人）；<英>動物標本剝製者；買賣玩賞動物的商人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自然主義的，自然的（等於 naturalistic）；博物學的，與博物學相關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>naturalist</b> is a person who studies plants, animals, insects, and other living things. 博物學家","examples":[]}]}]},"nationalism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"國家主義，民族主義；民族自豪感，民族優越感；民族自決主義；民族特徵（或習慣，慣用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a person's great love for their nation as <b>nationalism</b>. It is often associated with the belief that a particular nation is better than any other nation, and in this case is often used showing disapproval. 民族主義","examples":["This kind of fierce nationalism is a powerful and potentially volatile force. 這種強勁的民族主義勢力是一股強大和潛在的不穩定的力量。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Nationalism</b> is the desire for political independence of people who feel they are historically or culturally a separate group within a country. 民族獨立主義","examples":["The rising tide of Slovak nationalism may also help the party to win representation in parliament. 斯洛伐克民族獨立主義浪潮的高漲也有可能幫助該黨在議會中贏得席位。"]}]}]},"navel":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"[解剖] 肚臍；中央；中心點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>navel</b> is the small hollow near your waist at the front of your body. 肚臍","examples":["...a girl with a ring in her navel. …一個肚臍上掛環的姑娘。"]}]}]},"navigation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導航；航行，航海；航運，水上運輸；瀏覽，訪問；領航術，航海術；內河水道（尤指運河）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to the movement of ships as <b>navigation</b>. 航行","examples":["Pack ice around Iceland was becoming a threat to navigation. 冰島周圍的浮冰一度成為船舶航行的威脅。"]}]}]},"newlywed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"新婚的，剛結婚的（常作定語）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"新婚者，新婚夫婦（複數形式為 newlyweds）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Newlyweds</b> are a man and woman who have very recently got married to each other. 新婚夫婦","examples":["Lavalais raised his glass to propose a toast to the newlyweds. 拉瓦萊斯舉起了他的酒杯，向這對新婚夫婦敬酒。"]}]}]},"neon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"霓虹燈；霓虹燈招牌；氖（10 號元素，符號 Ne）；（Neon）人名；（德）內翁；（俄）涅翁"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"霓虹（燈）的，用霓虹燈製作的；霓虹色的，熒光般鮮豔的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neon</b> lights or signs are made from glass tubes filled with neon gas which produce a bright electric light. 霓虹的","examples":["In the city squares the neon lights flashed in turn. 在城市的各個廣場上，霓虹燈交替閃爍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neon</b> is a gas which occurs in very small amounts in the atmosphere. 氖","examples":["Inert gases like neon and argon have eight electrons in their outer shell. 像氖和氬這樣的惰性氣體，在它們的外電子層有8個電子。"]}]}]},"negotiation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"談判，協商；轉讓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Negotiations</b> are formal discussions between people who have different aims or intentions, especially in business or politics, during which they try to reach an agreement. (尤指商業或政治上的) 談判","examples":["Warren said, \"We have had meaningful negotiations and I believe we are very close to a deal.\" 沃倫說：“我們已經進行了富有意義的談判，我相信我們很快就能達成協議。”"]}]}]},"nomination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"推薦；任命，指定；被提名的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nomination</b> is an official suggestion of someone as a candidate in an election or for a job. (選舉、工作的) 提名","examples":["...his candidacy for the Republican presidential nomination. …他共和黨總統提名的候選資格。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>nomination</b> <b>for</b> an award is an official suggestion that someone or something should be given that award. (獎項的) 提名","examples":["They say he's certain to get a nomination for best supporting actor. 他們說他肯定會獲得最佳男配角獎的提名。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>nomination</b> of someone to a particular job or position is their appointment to that job or position. 任命","examples":["...the nomination of Texas Senator Lloyd Bentsen to be treasury secretary. …德克薩斯州議員勞埃德·本特森作財政部長的任命。"]}]}]},"neutral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中立的，不偏不倚的；中性的，不帶感情色彩的；暗淡的，素淨的；（化學中）中性的，非酸非鹼的；不帶電的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（車輛排擋的）空擋；中立者，中立國；素淨色，中和色；不活動，停滯；不帶電的接觸點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or country adopts a <b>neutral</b> position or remains <b>neutral</b>, they do not support anyone in a disagreement, war, or contest. 中立的","examples":["Let's meet on neutral territory. 我們在中立地區會面吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone speaks in a <b>neutral</b> voice or if the expression on their face is <b>neutral</b>, they do not show what they are thinking or feeling. 不動聲色的","examples":["Isabel put her magazine down and said in a neutral voice, \"You're very late, darling.\" 伊莎貝爾放下她的雜誌,以不動聲色的口吻說，“親愛的，你太晚了”。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>neutral</b>, you mean that it does not have any effect on other things because it lacks any significant qualities of its own, or it is an equal balance of two or more different qualities, amounts, or ideas. 不引起變化的; 中和的","examples":["Three in every five interviewed felt that the budget was neutral and they would be no better off. 每5個受訪者中有3個認為該預算不會帶來什麼變化，他們的境況也不會改善。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In an electrical device or system, the <b>neutral</b> wire is one of the three wires needed to complete the circuit so that the current can flow. The other two wires are called the ground wire and the live or positive wire. (電線) 不帶電的 (三股中的一股，其它兩股分別叫做地線和火線)","examples":["The ground wire in the house is connected to the neutral wire. 這所房子裡的地線接在了零線上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In chemistry, <b>neutral</b> is used to describe things that are neither acid nor alkaline. (化學上) 中性的","examples":["Pure water is neutral with a pH of 7. 純淨水是中性的，PH值為7。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>neutral</b> is someone who is neutral. 中立者","examples":["It was a good game to watch for the neutrals. 對於中立觀眾來說，這是一場精彩的比賽。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"中立","examples":["...a reputation for political neutrality and impartiality. …政治上中立和公正的名聲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"不動聲色","examples":["I noticed, behind the neutrality of his gaze, a deep weariness. 我覺察到，在他那不動聲色的凝視背後有一種深深的厭倦。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Neutral</b> is the position between the gears of a vehicle such as a car, in which the gears are not connected to the engine. 空檔","examples":["Graham put the van in neutral and jumped out into the road. 格雷厄姆把貨車掛到空擋，然後跳到路上。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Neutral</b> is used to describe things that have a pale colour such as cream or grey, or that have no colour at all. 淺灰色的; 無色的","examples":["At the horizon the land mass becomes a continuous pale neutral grey, almost blending with the sky. 在地平線上，大片陸地變成一片連綿而暗淡的淺灰色，幾乎與天空交融在一起。"]}]}]},"newscaster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新聞播音員，新聞播報員，新聞廣播員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>newscaster</b> is a person who reads the news on the radio or on television. 新聞廣播員","examples":["...TV newscaster Barbara Walters. …電視新聞廣播員芭芭拉·沃爾特斯。"]}]}]},"nominee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"被提名者，被任命者；（投資等的）名義持有人，註冊人；代名人，代名組織"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nominee</b> is someone who is nominated for a job, position, or award. 候選人","examples":["His nominee for vice president was elected only after a second ballot. 他的副總統候選人僅在第二輪投票後就被選中。"]}]}]},"nuisance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麻煩事，討厭的人（或事物、情況）；損害，妨害；騷擾行為，妨害行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is a <b>nuisance</b>, you mean that they annoy you or cause you a lot of problems. 令人討厭的人或事物; 麻煩的人或事情","examples":["He could be a bit of a nuisance when he was drunk. 他喝醉時會是一個有點令人討厭的人。","Sorry to be a nuisance. 對不起，麻煩一下。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>makes a nuisance of</b> themselves, they behave in a way that annoys other people. 惹人討厭。","examples":[]}]}]},"nourishment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"滋養品，營養；營養狀況，提供營養"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something provides a person, animal, or plant with <b>nourishment</b>, it provides them with the food that is necessary for life, growth, and good health. 營養","examples":["The mother provides the embryo with nourishment and a place to grow. 母親為胎兒提供營養和一個生長的地方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The action of nourishing someone or something, or the experience of being nourished, can be referred to as <b>nourishment</b>. 營養的供給; 營養的吸收","examples":["Sugar gives quick relief to hunger but provides no lasting nourishment. 糖能快速緩解飢餓感，但不提供持久的營養。"]}]}]},"norm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社會準則，行為規範；標準，平均水平；常態，平常事物；模方；<澳，非正式>諾姆（指整日呆在家中看電視的懶人，尤指看體育節目）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Norms</b> are ways of behaving that are considered normal in a particular society. 準則","examples":["The actions taken depart from what she called the commonly accepted norms of democracy. 所採取的這些行動背離了她所謂的那些普遍接受的民主準則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a situation is <b>the norm</b>, you mean that it is usual and expected. 慣例; 常規","examples":["Families of six or seven are the norm in Borough Park. 六七口人的家庭在菠蘿園是常事兒。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>norm</b> is an official standard or level that organizations are expected to reach. 標準","examples":["About 32 percent of students meet national norms in reading. 大約32%的學生達到國家閱讀標準。"]}]}]},"nutrient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"養分，營養物"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"營養的，滋養的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nutrients</b> are substances that help plants and animals to grow. 營養物","examples":["In her first book she explained the role of vegetable fibres, vitamins, minerals, and other essential nutrients. 在她第一本書中，她解釋了植物纖維、維生素、礦物質和其他重要營養物質的作用。"]}]}]},"nutrition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"營養，滋養；營養學；食物，營養物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nutrition</b> is the process of taking food into the body and absorbing the nutrients in those foods. 吸收營養","examples":["There are alternative sources of nutrition to animal meat. 有能替代動物肉類的其他營養來源。"]}]}]},"nurture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"培養，促進；養育，培育；抱有，懷有；扶持，幫助；滋養，滋生"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"養育，培育；教養；（總稱）環境因素"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>nurture</b> something such as a young child or a young plant, you care for it while it is growing and developing. 養育","examples":["Parents want to know the best way to nurture and raise their child to adulthood. 父母們想了解把他們的孩子養育成人的最好方法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>nurture</b> plans, ideas, or people, you encourage them or help them to develop. 培養","examples":["She had always nurtured great ambitions for her son. 她一直在培養她兒子的雄心大志。","...parents whose political views were nurtured in the sixties. …政治觀點形成於60年代的父母們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nurture</b> is care and encouragement that is given to someone while they are growing and developing. 培育","examples":["The human organism learns partly by nature, partly by nurture. 人的學習能力部分是先天的，部分是後天培育的。"]}]}]},"offering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（供娛樂或出售的）產品；新近完成的藝術作品；禮品，禮物；供品，祭品；供奉，奉獻；（給教會的）捐助，捐贈物（尤指捐款）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供，給予；提議，表示願意（做某事）；出（價），開（價）（offer 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>offering</b> is something that is being sold. 出售物","examples":["It was very, very good, far better than vegetarian offerings in many an expensive restaurant. 那道菜非常非常好，遠遠好過許多豪華飯店的素菜。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>offering</b> is a gift that people offer to their God or gods as a form of worship. 祭品","examples":["...the holiest of the Shinto rituals, where offerings are made at night to the great Sun. …神道教儀式中最神聖的部分，祭品在夜間獻給偉大的太陽神。"]}]}]},"offspring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人的）後代，子女；（動物的）幼崽，崽獸；結果，產物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a person's children or to an animal's young as their <b>offspring</b>. 子女; 幼崽","examples":["Eleanor was now less anxious about her offspring than she had once been. 這時，埃莉諾已不像以前那樣為子女擔憂了。"]}]}]},"obligation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（法律上或道義上的）義務，責任；恩惠，人情債；（承諾付款等的）合同，契約；必須要做的事情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have an <b>obligation</b> <b>to</b> do something, it is your duty to do that thing. 義務","examples":["When teachers assign homework, students usually feel an obligation to do it. 老師佈置家庭作業時，學生們通常感覺做作業是一種義務。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have an <b>obligation</b> <b>to</b> a person, it is your duty to take care of them or protect their interests. 義務; 責任","examples":["The United States will do that which is necessary to meet its obligations to its own citizens. 美國會盡其對國民應盡的義務。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In advertisements, if a product or a service is available <b>without obligation</b>, you do not have to pay for that product or service until you have tried it and are satisfied with it. 無義務地","examples":["If you are selling your property, why not call us for a free valuation without obligation. 如果你打算出售房產，為什麼不打電話讓我們做個免費的評估呢。"]}]}]},"oppression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"壓迫，壓制；壓迫手段；鬱悶，壓抑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Oppression</b> is the cruel or unfair treatment of a group of people. 壓迫","examples":["...an attempt to escape political oppression. …逃避政治壓迫的一次嘗試。"]}]}]},"opposition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（強烈的） 反對，反抗；對手，競爭者（the opposition）；反對黨，在野黨（ the Opposition）；對立，對立的事物；（天文，占星）衝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Opposition</b> is strong, angry, or violent disagreement and disapproval. 強烈的反對","examples":["There is bitter opposition from local business to the plan. 有來自當地企業對此計劃的強烈反對。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>opposition</b> is the political parties or groups that are opposed to a government. 反對黨","examples":["The main opposition parties boycotted the election, saying it would not be conducted fairly. 主要的反對黨抵制了選舉，聲稱選舉不會公平進行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In countries with a parliament, such as Britain, <b>the</b> <b>opposition</b> refers to the politicians or political parties that form part of the parliament, but are not the government. 在野黨","examples":["...the Leader of the Opposition. …在野黨領袖。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>opposition</b> is the person or team you are competing against in a sports event. 對手","examples":["The coach says his team is not underestimating the opposition. 教練說他的隊沒在低估對手。"]}]}]},"organism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物，有機體，（尤指）微生物；有機組織，有機體系"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>organism</b> is an animal or plant, especially one that is so small that you cannot see it without using a microscope. 生物; 微生物","examples":["Not all chemicals normally present in living organisms are harmless. 並非所有正常存在於活的有機體中的化學物質都是無害的。"]}]}]},"orderly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有條理的，整齊的；守秩序的；傳達命令的，值班的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（醫院）護理員，勤雜工；傳令兵，勤務兵"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有秩序地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is done in an <b>orderly</b> fashion or manner, it is done in a well-organized and controlled way. 有秩序的","examples":["The organizers guided them in an orderly fashion out of the building. 組織者們帶領他們井然有序地走出了大樓。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>orderly</b> is neat or arranged in a neat way. 整齊的","examples":["It's a beautiful, clean and orderly city. 這是一座美麗、乾淨、整齊的城市。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"整齊","examples":["A balance is achieved in the painting between orderliness and unpredictability. 這幅畫在整齊和變幻間取得了平衡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>orderly</b> is a person who works in a hospital and does jobs that do not require special medical training. 護理員","examples":["For most of his life, he was a hospital orderly. 他做了大半輩子的醫院護理員。"]}]}]},"option":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可選擇的事物；選擇，選擇權；（將來的）買賣選擇權利，期權；（計算機程式中的）選項；<英>選修課；（購買新裝置，尤其是汽車時提供的）附件，配件"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"買賣（某物的）期權"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>option</b> is something that you can choose to do in preference to one or more alternatives. 供選擇的東西","examples":["He's argued from the start that the US and its allies are putting too much emphasis on the military option. 他從一開始就爭論說美國及其盟國過於看重軍事這個選項。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have the <b>option</b> of doing something, you can choose whether to do it or not. 選擇權","examples":["Criminals are given the option of going to jail or facing public humiliation. 罪犯們被給予進監獄或面對公眾羞辱的選擇權。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In business, an <b>option</b> is an agreement or contract that gives someone the right to buy or sell something such as property or shares at a future date. 購買權; 出售權; 期權","examples":["Each bank has granted the other an option on 19.9% of its shares. 每家銀行都已把自己股份的19.9%的期權給予另一家銀行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>option</b> is one of a number of subjects which a student can choose to study as a part of his or her course. 選修課","examples":["Several options are offered for the student's senior year. 好幾門選修課開給畢業班的學生。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> your <b>options open</b> or <b>leave</b> your <b>options open</b>, you delay making a decision about something. 暫不做決定","examples":["I am keeping my options open; I can decide in a few months. 我保留選擇的權利；我可以幾個月後再作出決定。"]}]}]},"originality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨創性，創意；獨創能力，創造力"}],"sections":[]},"outbreak":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（戰爭、疾病、暴力等的）爆發，突然發生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>outbreak</b> <b>of</b> something unpleasant, such as violence or a disease, it suddenly starts to happen. (暴動、疾病等的) 爆發","examples":["The four-day festival ended a day early after an outbreak of violence involving hundreds of youths. 由於一起數百名年輕人參與的暴力事件的爆發，為期4天的慶祝活動提前1天結束。","...an outbreak of chickenpox. …水痘的暴發。"]}]}]},"outing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"短途旅遊，遠足；出門，外出；<非正式>（尤指在體育專案或電影中的）出場；對同性戀者（尤指名人）的曝光"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擊倒，擊昏；<非正式>公開（知名人士）的同性戀身份；熄滅（out 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outing</b> is a short trip, usually with a group of people, away from your home, school, or place of work. (常指集體的) 短途旅行; 外出","examples":["One evening, she made a rare outing to the local night club. 一天晚上，她難得地去了一趟當地的夜總會。"]}]}]},"outlaw":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不法之徒，逃犯；<史>被剝奪法律權益和保護者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使非法，禁止，取締；（舊時）剝奪（某人的）法律權益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>is outlawed</b>, it is made illegal. 宣佈…為非法","examples":["In some states gambling was outlawed. 在一些州賭博被宣佈為非法。","The German government has outlawed some fascist groups. 德國政府已宣佈一些法西斯團體為非法。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outlaw</b> is a criminal who is hiding from the authorities. 逃犯","examples":["Jesse was an outlaw, a bandit, a criminal. 傑西曾是個逃犯、土匪、罪犯。"]}]}]},"outfit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指在某一場合穿的）全套服裝；全套工具，全套裝置；<非正式>（協同工作的）一組人，一隊人（尤指樂隊、運動隊、公司）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"配備，向……提供裝備（或服裝）；得到裝備"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outfit</b> is a set of clothes. 全套服裝","examples":["She was wearing an outfit she'd bought the previous day. 她穿著前一天買的一套服裝。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an organization as an <b>outfit</b>. 機構","examples":["He works for a private security outfit. 他在一傢俬人保安公司工作。"]}]}]},"outlet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（情緒或精力的）發洩方式，發洩途徑；排出口；商店，分銷點；廉價經銷店；從事大眾媒體行業的公司；<美>電源插座"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outlet</b> is a shop or organization which sells the goods made by a particular manufacturer or at a discount price, often direct from the manufacturer. 專賣店; 直銷店","examples":["...the largest retail outlet in the city. …該市最大的零售專賣店。","At the factory outlet you'll find discounted items at up to 75% off regular prices. 在工廠的直銷店裡，你會找到比常規價低75%的打折商品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has an <b>outlet</b> <b>for</b> their feelings or ideas, they have a means of expressing and releasing them. (感情的) 發洩途徑; (思想的) 表達途徑","examples":["Her father had found an outlet for his ambition in his work. 她父親在工作中找到了施展抱負的途徑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>outlet</b> is a hole or pipe through which liquid or air can flow away. 出水口; 排氣口","examples":["...a warm air outlet. …一個熱氣排氣口。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>outlet</b> is a place, usually in a wall, where you can connect electrical devices to the electricity supply. 電源插座","examples":[]}]}]},"outlook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"看法，態度；前景，展望；景色，風光；瞭望處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>outlook</b> is your general attitude toward life. 人生觀","examples":["I adopted a positive outlook on life. 我選擇了一種積極的人生觀。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>outlook</b> for something is what people think will happen in relation to it. 前景","examples":["The economic outlook is one of rising unemployment. 經濟前景惡化，失業率不斷增長。"]}]}]},"outrage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"憤慨，憤怒；駭人聽聞的事，暴行"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使憤怒，激怒；踐踏（準則、法律等）；凌辱，強姦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are outraged</b> by something, it makes you extremely angry and shocked. 使震怒","examples":["Many people have been outraged by some of the things that have been said. 許多人曾為其所聽說的一些事情所震怒。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"震怒的","examples":["He is truly outraged about what's happened to him. 他確實為發生在他身上的事情而震怒。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Outrage</b> is an intense feeling of anger and shock. 震怒","examples":["The decision provoked outrage from women and human rights groups. 該決定激起了婦女和各人權組織的震怒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to an act or event that angers and shocks you as an <b>outrage</b>. 令人震怒之舉; 令人震怒之事","examples":["The latest outrage was to have been a coordinated gun and bomb attack on the station. 最近令人震怒的事件是一次對該車站槍彈並用的襲擊。"]}]}]},"ordeal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"磨難，嚴峻考驗；<史>神明裁判（把被告是否經得起劇痛的考驗作為被告是否無辜的神諭）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an experience or situation as an <b>ordeal</b>, you think it is difficult and stressful. 煎熬","examples":["...the painful ordeal of the last eight months. …過去8個月裡令人痛苦的煎熬。"]}]}]},"outset":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"開始，開端"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>at the outset</b> of an event, process, or period of time, it happens at the beginning of it. If something happens <b>from the outset</b> it happens from the beginning and continues to happen. 在開始時; 從一開始","examples":["Decide at the outset what kind of learning programme you want to follow. 一開始就要定下你的學習計劃。"]}]}]},"overhead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在頭頂上方，在空中"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"頭頂上的，在空中的，高架的；（驅動裝置）頂置式的；經費的，管理費用的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>經常開支，營運費用（=<英>overheads）；（用於投影儀顯示文字、圖片等的）透明幻燈片；（尤指飛機的）頂艙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>overhead</b> to indicate that something is above you or above the place that you are talking about. 頭頂上的","examples":["She turned on the overhead light and looked around the little room. 她開啟頂燈，環視這間小屋。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overhead</b> is also an adverb. 在頭頂","examples":["...planes passing overhead. …飛過頭頂的飛機。"]}]}]},"overlap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（與……）互搭，（與……）復疊；（在關注的問題、承擔的責任等方面）部分地重疊，部分相同；（與……）同時發生"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（物體的）重疊部分，重疊量；（範圍方面的）重疊部分；（兩事發生的）重疊時間，交接時期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>overlaps</b> another, or if you <b>overlap</b> them, a part of the first thing occupies the same area as a part of the other thing. You can also say that two things <b>overlap</b>. 重疊","examples":["When the bag is folded, the bottom overlaps one side. 把包摺疊起來時，其底部與一邊就重合了。","Overlap the slices carefully so there are no gaps. 把薄片小心地疊放在一起，那樣就沒有間隙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one idea or activity <b>overlaps</b> another, or <b>overlaps</b> with another, they involve some of the same subjects, people, or periods of time. 與…重合","examples":["Christian Holy Week overlaps with the beginning of the Jewish holiday of Passover. 基督教的聖周與猶太教逾越節的開始時間是重合的。","The needs of patients invariably overlap. 患者們的各種需求總是相互重合的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overlap</b> is also a noun. 重合","examples":["...the overlap between civil and military technology. …民用技術與軍用技術之間的重合。"]}]}]},"overturn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）翻倒，（使）傾覆；推翻，撤銷（判決等）；顛覆，破壞（政府或體系）；<英>在英國大選中因獲得多數席位而獲勝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<罕>顛覆，革命；（尤指水溫分層的湖水每年兩次的）湖水對流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>overturns</b> or if you <b>overturn</b> it, it turns upside down or on its side. 打翻; 翻倒","examples":["The motorcycle veered out of control, overturned and smashed into a wall. 摩托車轉向失去了控制，翻倒在地，然後猛地撞到一面牆上。","Alex jumped up so violently that he overturned his glass of wine. 亞歷克斯躍起得太猛，以至於打翻了他的那杯葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>overturns</b> a legal decision, they officially decide that that decision is incorrect or not valid. 推翻","examples":["When the courts overturned his decision, he backed down. 當法院推翻了他的決定時，他讓步了。"]}]}]},"pamphlet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小冊子，活頁"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"向……散發小冊子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pamphlet</b> is a very thin book with a paper cover that gives information about something. 小冊子","examples":["...a pamphlet about smoking. …一本關於吸菸的小冊子。"]}]}]},"pact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"條約，協議，公約"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pact</b> is a formal agreement between two or more people, organizations, or governments to do a particular thing or to help each other. 條約; 協議","examples":["Last month he signed a new non-aggression pact with Germany. 上個月他與德國簽署了一份新的互不侵犯條約。"]}]}]},"parliament":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"議會，國會；英國議會（包括下議院和上議院）（Parliament）；一屆議會（會期）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>parliament</b> of some countries is the group of people who make or change its laws, and decide what policies the country should follow. 議會","examples":["The Bangladesh Parliament today approved the policy, but it has not yet become law. 孟加拉共和國議會今天批准了這項政策，但它還沒有成為法律。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>parliament</b> is a particular period of time in which a parliament is doing its work, between two elections or between two periods of holiday. 一屆議會的任期; (兩次大選之間的) 一屆議會","examples":["The legislation is expected to be passed in the next parliament. 這項法規有望在下屆議會中透過。"]}]}]},"pedestrian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"步行者，行人"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平淡無奇的，乏味的；行人的，行人使用的；徒步的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pedestrian</b> is a person who is walking, especially in a town or city, rather than travelling in a vehicle. 行人","examples":["Ingrid was a walker, even in Los Angeles, where a pedestrian is a rare sight. 英格麗德是個步行者，即使在行人少見的洛杉磯也是如此。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>pedestrian</b>, you mean that it is ordinary and not at all interesting. 平庸乏味的","examples":["His style is so pedestrian that the book becomes a real bore. 他的文風很平庸，以致那本書成了一本真正乏味的書。"]}]}]},"peninsula":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"半島"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>peninsula</b> is a long narrow piece of land that sticks out from a larger piece of land and is almost completely surrounded by water. 半島","examples":["...the political situation in the Korean peninsula. …朝鮮半島的政治局勢。"]}]}]},"pension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"養老金，退休金；（法國和其他一些歐洲國家的）廉價小旅店；<史>（給皇室寵臣、藝術家或學者以便他們能從事公益工作的）津貼，補助金"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指因年齡或疾病而）向（某人）支付養老金使其退休；（因陳舊或不再有用而）丟棄（某物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>pension</b> receives a regular sum of money from a former employer because they have retired or because they are widowed or disabled. 養老金; 撫卹金","examples":["...struggling by on a pension. …靠養老金艱難度日。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"in France and some other countries a relatively cheap boarding house 廉租屋","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to grant a pension to 給予…養老金","examples":[]}]}]},"perception":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"看法，認識；感覺，感知；洞察力；<法律>（租金、農作物等的）收取，佔有"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>perception</b> <b>of</b> something is the way that you think about it or the impression you have of it. 理解; 看法","examples":["He is interested in how our perceptions of death affect the way we live. 他對我們的死亡觀如何影響我們的生活方式感興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who has <b>perception</b> realizes or notices things that are not obvious. 洞察力","examples":["It did not require a lot of perception to realize the interview was over. 不需要很強的洞察力就可以意識到面試結束了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Perception</b> is the recognition of things using your senses, especially the sense of sight. (尤指透過視覺的) 感知","examples":[]}]}]},"persistence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼續存在，維持；堅持不懈，執意"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>persistence</b>, you continue to do something even though it is difficult or other people are against it. 堅持不懈; 執著","examples":["Skill comes only with practice, patience, and persistence. 只有透過練習、耐心和堅持不懈才能獲得技能。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>persistence</b> <b>of</b> something, especially something bad, is the fact of its continuing to exist for a long time. (尤指壞事物的) 持續存在","examples":["...an expression of concern at the persistence of inflation and high interest rates. …對持續通貨膨脹和高利率所表示的關注。"]}]}]},"pesticide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"殺蟲劑，農藥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pesticides</b> are chemicals that farmers put on their crops to kill harmful insects. 殺蟲劑","examples":[]}]}]},"petroleum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"石油，原油"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Petroleum</b> is oil that is found under the surface of the earth or under the sea bed. Petrol and kerosene are obtained from petroleum. 石油","examples":[]}]}]},"pharmacist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥劑師，藥師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pharmacist</b> is a person who is qualified to prepare and sell medicines. 藥劑師","examples":["Ask your pharmacist for advice. 向你的藥劑師徵詢意見吧。"]}]}]},"pharmacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"藥店；（醫院的）藥房，配藥室；藥劑學，配藥學；一批備用藥品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pharmacy</b> is a shop or a department in a shop where medicines are sold or given out. 藥店; 藥房","examples":["Pick up the medicine from the pharmacy. 從藥房取藥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Pharmacy</b> is the job or the science of preparing medicines. 製藥業; 藥劑學","examples":["He spent four years studying pharmacy. 他花了4年時間學習藥劑學。"]}]}]},"perspective":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（觀察問題的）視角，觀點；透視（畫）法；（幾何）透視關係，投影比例；洞察力，判斷力；景觀，遠景；角度；（聲音）立體效果"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"透視的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>perspective</b> is a particular way of thinking about something, especially one that is influenced by your beliefs or experiences. 思維方式; 看法","examples":["He says the death of his father 18 months ago has given him a new perspective on life. 他說１８個月前他父親的去世使他對人生產生了新的看法。","...two different perspectives on the nature of adolescent development. …關於青春期發育特點的兩種不同觀點。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you get something <b>in perspective</b> or <b>into perspective</b>, you judge its real importance by considering it in relation to everything else. If you get something <b>out of perspective</b>, you fail to judge its real importance in relation to everything else. (看待事物) 正確/不正確地","examples":["Remember to keep things in perspective. 記住要正確地看待事物。","I let things get out of perspective. 我沒能正確地看待事物。"]}]}]},"phase":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（發展或變化的）階段，時期；做出某種行為的短時期；（動物生活週期或年週期的）階段，期；（月亮的）位相，盈虧；同步，協調；（化）相；（動）（由遺傳或季節引起的）動物顏色變化（期）；（物理）相位，相角；（線圈的）匝，（多相電機或電路的）連線；（語言學）（系統語法用語）相（指連結動詞與後續動詞的關係）；相結構（含有連結動詞和後續動詞的結構）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"分階段進行；（物理）使相位同步，使定相"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>phase</b> is a particular stage in a process or in the gradual development of something. 階段","examples":["This autumn, 6000 residents will participate in the first phase of the project. 今年秋季，6000名居民將參與這項計劃的第一階段。","The crisis is entering a crucial, critical phase. 危機正進入一個至關重要的決定性階段。"]}]}]},"piety":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"虔誠，虔敬；虔誠信念，虔誠觀點；偽善的言語（pieties）；偽善的言語（pieties）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Piety</b> is strong religious belief, or behaviour that is religious or morally correct. 虔誠","examples":["Known for her piety, she would walk miles to attend communion services in the neighbouring villages. 她的虔誠是出了名的，她會步行幾英里去參加鄰村的聖餐儀式。"]}]}]},"perseverance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毅力，不屈不撓的精神"}],"sections":[]},"pitcher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（棒球）投手；投手位置；（主美）大水罐，水壺；一罐之量；（Pitcher）人名；（英）皮徹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pitcher</b> is a cylindrical container with a handle and is used for holding and pouring liquids. 壺","examples":["My sister fetched a pitcher of iced water. 我妹妹取來一壺冰水。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In baseball, the <b>pitcher</b> is the person who throws the ball to the batter, who tries to hit it. (棒球) 投手","examples":[]}]}]},"pipeline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（常指地下的）輸送管道；（供應貨物、資訊等的）渠道，途徑；研發生產系統（the pipeline）；（計算機）流水線；（衝浪用語）大浪的空心部分"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用管道輸送；（計算機）運用流水線技術設計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>pipeline</b> is a large pipe that is used for carrying oil or gas over a long distance, often underground. (長距離輸送石油、天然氣等的地下) 管道","examples":["A consortium plans to build a natural-gas pipeline from Russia to supply eastern Germany. 一家財團計劃修建一條從俄羅斯向德國東部供應天然氣的管道。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in the pipeline</b>, it has already been planned or begun. 已籌劃的; 已實施的","examples":["Already in the pipeline is a 2.9 percent pay increase for teachers. 已在籌劃之中的是教師收入將增長2.9%。"]}]}]},"pneumonia":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"肺炎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pneumonia</b> is a serious disease that affects your lungs and makes it difficult for you to breathe. 肺炎","examples":["She nearly died of pneumonia. 她差點死於肺炎。"]}]}]},"poacher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偷獵者，盜獵者；侵入者，越界者；（烹飪）煮蛋鍋，水煮鍋，燉蛋鍋（用於文火烹製荷包蛋或魚等）；（足球等運動）門前搶點射手，機會型球員；（動物學）小型海魚（Agonidae 科，體覆骨板，主要分佈於北太平洋較深水域，亦稱 sea poacher）"}],"sections":[]},"plight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"困境，窘境；誓約"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<舊> 宣誓，保證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>plight</b>, you mean that they are in a difficult or distressing situation that is full of problems. 困境","examples":["The nation saw the plight of the farmers, whose crops had died. 該國看到了農民因莊稼死亡而陷入困境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a solemn promise, esp of engagement; pledge 誓約; 婚約","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to give or pledge (one's word) 保證; 宣誓","examples":[]}]}]},"posture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（坐或立的）姿勢；態度，立場；（鳥或其他動物的）體態；情形"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"故作（姿態），裝腔作勢；<古>使處於……態度（或姿態）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>posture</b> is the position in which you stand or sit. (站或坐的) 姿勢","examples":["You can make your stomach look flatter instantly by improving your posture. 你可以改善坐姿，腹部就會馬上顯得平些。","Exercise, fresh air, and good posture are all helpful. 體育運動、新鮮空氣和良好姿勢都很有效果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>posture</b> is an attitude that you have toward something. 態度","examples":["The military machine is ready to change its defensive posture to one prepared for action. 軍事當局已準備從防禦態勢變為備戰態勢。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say that someone <b>is posturing</b> when you disapprove of their behaviour because you think they are trying to give a particular impression in order to deceive people. 作態","examples":["She says the president may just be posturing. 她說總統也許只是在作態。"]}]}]},"precedent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"先例，前例；判例，例項；常規，慣例"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在先的，前面的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>precedent</b> <b>for</b> an action or event, it has happened before, and this can be regarded as an argument for doing it again. 先例","examples":["The trial could set an important precedent for dealing with similar cases. 這次審判能為處理類似案件開創一個重要先例。"]}]}]},"predecessor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"前任，前輩；（被取代的）原有事物，前身"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>predecessor</b> is the person who had your job before you. 前任","examples":["He maintained that he learned everything he knew from his predecessor. 他堅稱他所知道的一切都是從他的前任那兒學到的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>predecessor</b> of an object or machine is the object or machine that came before it in a sequence or process of development. 前一代","examples":["Although the car is some 2 inches shorter than its predecessor, its boot is 20 percent larger. 儘管這款汽車比其上一代產品短2英寸，但它的行李箱大了20%。"]}]}]},"precision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精確（性），準確（性）；嚴謹，細緻；（測量、計算或說明的）精確化（尤以數字表現）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（設計）精密的，精確的；要求技術精確的，（行動）精確的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do something <b>with</b> <b>precision</b>, you do it exactly as it should be done. 準確性","examples":["The choir sang with precision. 合唱團的演唱準確無誤。"]}]}]},"prediction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預言之事，預報之事；預測（行為）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make a <b>prediction</b> about something, you say what you think will happen. 預言","examples":["He was unwilling to make a prediction for the coming year. 他不願對來年作出預言。","Weather prediction has never been a perfect science. 天氣預報從來都不是一門準確無誤的科學。"]}]}]},"preface":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書的）前言，（演講的）開場白；開端，序幕；（基督教）序禱，序誦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為（書）作序；以……為開端，以……作為開場白"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>preface</b> is an introduction at the beginning of a book that explains what the book is about or why it was written. 前言","examples":["...the preface to Kelman's novel. …凱爾曼小說的前言。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>preface</b> an action or speech <b>with</b> something else, you do or say this other thing first. 說…作為開場白; 做…作為開始","examples":["I will preface what I am going to say with a few lines from Shakespeare. 我將引用莎士比亞的幾行詩作為我講話的開場白。"]}]}]},"premier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"首要的，最好的；最早的，最初的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"總理，首相；（加拿大的）省總理，地方總理；（澳大利亞州或地區的）省長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The leader of the government of a country is sometimes referred to as the country's <b>premier</b>. 總理","examples":["...Australian premier Paul Keating. …澳大利亞總理保羅·基廷。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Premier</b> is used to describe something that is considered to be the best or most important thing of a particular type. 最好的; 首要的","examples":["...the country's premier opera company. …這個國家最好的歌劇團。"]}]}]},"presidency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"總統（主席，校長）的職位（任期）；（基督教）（牧師或司鐸）聖餐主持；監督，主管"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>presidency</b> of a country or organization is the position of being the president or the period of time during which someone is president. (某國、某組織的) 最高職位; 最高職位任期","examples":["He is a candidate for the presidency of the organization. 他是該組織最高職位候選人。"]}]}]},"prejudice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偏見，成見，歧視；<法律>損害，侵害"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使有偏見，使有成見； 損害，不利於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prejudice</b> is an unreasonable dislike of a particular group of people or things, or a preference for one group of people or things over another. 偏見","examples":["There was a deep-rooted racial prejudice long before the two countries went to war. 早在兩國交戰之前就有了根深蒂固的種族偏見。","There is widespread prejudice against workers over 45. 對年齡超過45歲的工人有普遍的偏見。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prejudice</b> someone or something, you influence them so that they are unfair in some way. 使…有偏見","examples":["I think your upbringing has prejudiced you. 我認為你的教養使你抱有偏見。","The report was held back for fear of prejudicing his trial. 因為擔心會使他的審判帶有偏見，該報告沒有公開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>prejudices</b> another person's situation, they do something that makes it worse than it should be. 損害","examples":["Her study was not in any way intended to prejudice the future development of the college. 她的研究絕對無意損害該學院的未來發展。"]}]}]},"prestige":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"聲望，威信"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"受尊重的，令人敬仰的；貴重的，氣派的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, a country, or an organization has <b>prestige</b>, they are admired and respected because of the position they hold or the things they have achieved. 威望","examples":["...efforts to build up the prestige of the United Nations. …為樹立聯合國威望而做的努力。","It was his responsibility for foreign affairs that gained him international prestige. 是他在外交事務中的盡職盡責為他贏得了國際聲望。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prestige</b> is used to describe products, places, or activities that people admire because they are associated with being rich or having a high social position. 名貴的","examples":["...such prestige cars as Cadillac, Mercedes, Porsche, and Jaguar. …像凱迪拉克、梅賽德斯、保時捷和捷豹這樣的名貴轎車。"]}]}]},"preventive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"預防（性）的，防備的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"預防藥，預防療法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Preventive</b> actions are intended to help prevent things such as disease or crime. 預防性的","examples":["Too much is spent on curative medicine and too little on preventive medicine. 在治療醫學上花費太多，而在預防醫學上花費太少。"]}]}]},"productivity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生產率，生產力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Productivity</b> is the rate at which goods are produced. 生產率","examples":["The third-quarter results reflect continued improvements in productivity. 第三季度的結果反映了生產率的持續提高。"]}]}]},"proficiency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熟練，精通"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you show <b>proficiency</b> <b>in</b> something, you show ability or skill at it. 水平","examples":["Evidence of basic proficiency in English is part of the admissions requirement. 基本英語水平的證明是錄取條件的一部分。"]}]}]},"prescription":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"處方，藥方；處方藥；開處方，開藥方；<正式>解決方法，訣竅；<法律>取得的時效（根據長期或不確定時期持續使用或以長期習慣為基礎確立的要求權）（=positive prescription)）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"憑處方方可購買的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prescription</b> is the piece of paper on which your doctor writes an order for medicine and which you give to a pharmacist to get the medicine. 處方","examples":["The new drug will not require a physician's prescription. 這種新藥不需要醫生的處方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>prescription</b> is a medicine that a doctor has told you to take. 處方藥","examples":["I'm not sleeping even with the prescription Ackerman gave me. 我服用了阿克曼開給我的處方藥還是睡不著。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>prescription</b> is a proposal or a plan that gives ideas about how to solve a problem or improve a situation. 方案","examples":["There's not much difference in the economic prescriptions of Ireland's two main political parties. 愛爾蘭兩大政黨的經濟方案沒有多大差異。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a medicine is available <b>by</b> or <b>on prescription</b>, you can only get it from a pharmacist if a doctor gives you a prescription for it. 憑處方","examples":[]}]}]},"pollutant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汙染物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Pollutants</b> are substances that pollute the environment, especially gases from vehicles and poisonous chemicals produced as waste by industrial processes. 汙染物 (尤指車輛尾氣和化學工業廢料)","examples":["Industrial pollutants are responsible for a sizable proportion of all cancers. 工業汙染物會引發多種癌症。"]}]}]},"progressive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"進步的，先進的；逐步發生的，逐步發展的；向前移動的；（音樂）現代的，新潮的；（稅制，稅種）累進的；（動詞）進行式的；（紙牌遊戲，舞蹈）搭檔輪換的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"進步分子，改革派人士；進行時（或體）；（印刷）分色打樣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>progressive</b> or has <b>progressive</b> ideas has modern ideas about how things should be done, rather than traditional ones. 進步的","examples":["...a progressive businessman who had voted for Roosevelt in 1932 and 1936. …在1932年和1936年投票支援羅斯福的一位進步商人。","Willan was able to point to the progressive changes he had already introduced. 威蘭能夠指出他已經帶來的有進步意義的變化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>progressive</b> change happens gradually over a period of time. 逐步的","examples":["One prominent symptom of the disease is progressive loss of memory. 這種病的一個突出症狀是記憶的逐步喪失。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>progressive</b> is someone who is progressive. 進步人士","examples":["The Republicans were deeply split between progressives and conservatives. 共和黨進步派和保守派之間分歧很大。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"逐步地","examples":["Her symptoms became progressively worse. 她的症狀逐步惡化。"]}]}]},"prohibition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"禁令，禁律；禁止；<英>（上級法院禁止下級法院對無權受理案件審理的）訴訟中止令；（1920至1933年美國的）禁酒時期（Prohibition）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prohibition</b> is a law or rule forbidding something. 禁令","examples":["...a prohibition on discrimination. …一項對歧視的禁令。"]}]}]},"propeller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（飛機或輪船的）螺旋槳，推進器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>propeller</b> is a device with blades attached to a boat or aircraft. The engine makes the propeller spin around and causes the boat or aircraft to move. 螺旋槳","examples":["...a fixed three-bladed propeller. …一個固定的三葉螺旋槳。"]}]}]},"propaganda":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"宣傳，鼓吹；（羅馬天主教的）傳信部（Propaganda）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Propaganda</b> is information, often inaccurate information, that a political organization publishes or broadcasts in order to influence people. (政治組織的) 宣傳","examples":["The party adopted an aggressive propaganda campaign against its rivals. 該黨採用了一場對抗其對手的咄咄逼人的宣傳運動。"]}]}]},"projection":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"估算，預測；投射，投影；（聲音的）傳送，放開；（思想感情的）體現，形象化；投射（不自覺地把自己的慾念等加諸他人）；凸出物，隆起物；（地球或天體在平面上的）投射；投影圖；規劃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>projection</b> is an estimate of a future amount. 預計","examples":["...the company's projection of 11 million visitors for the first year. …公司對第一年1100萬遊客的預計。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>projection</b> of a film or picture is the act of projecting it onto a screen or wall. 投映","examples":["They took me into a projection room to see a picture. 他們將我帶進了一個投映室去看一張圖片。"]}]}]},"prosecution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"起訴，訴訟；原告，控方；從事，進行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prosecution</b> is the action of charging someone with a crime and putting them on trial. 起訴","examples":["Yesterday the head of government called for the prosecution of those responsible for the deaths. 政府首腦昨日要求對那些造成死亡的責任人進行起訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The lawyers who try to prove that a person on trial is guilty are called <b>the prosecution</b>. 原告律師","examples":["The star witness for the prosecution took the stand. 原告律師傳訊的主要證人站到了證人席上。"]}]}]},"provincial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"省的；外省的，地方的；守舊的，偏狹的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鄉下人，外省人（常用作貶義，表示某人興趣狹隘或偏狹守舊）；（國家、帝國的）省內居民；<英>（相對於全國性報紙而言的）地方報紙（provincials）；（管轄教省的）大主教（或都主教）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Provincial</b> means connected with the parts of a country away from the capital city. 省的","examples":["...the Quebec and Ontario provincial police. …魁北克和安大略省的警察。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>provincial</b>, you disapprove of them because you think that they are old-fashioned and boring. 守舊的","examples":["He decided to revamp the company's provincial image. 他決定改變公司守舊的形象。"]}]}]},"prose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"散文，白話文；（尤指待翻譯的）一段散文；平淡乏味的文章（或話語，表達法）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"冗長乏味地說；<舊> 把……寫成散文，把……改寫成散文；寫散文"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"散文的，散文式的；平凡的，乏味的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prose</b> is ordinary written language, in contrast to poetry. 散文","examples":["Shute's prose is stark and chillingly unsentimental. 舒特的散文刻板而冷峻。"]}]}]},"prowl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"潛行；徘徊；搜尋"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"徘徊，潛行，悄悄踱步；on the prowl：正在潛行/徘徊，可指（動物）出動捕獵或（人）四處搜尋（幹某事的機會）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an animal or a person <b>prowls</b> <b>around</b>, they move around quietly, for example, when they are hunting. 悄悄巡行","examples":["He prowled around the room, not sure what he was looking for or even why he was there. 他在房間裡悄悄地走來走去，不知道自己在找什麼，甚至不知道自己為什麼在那裡。"]}]}]},"preliminary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"初步的，預備的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"初步行動，準備工作；預賽，預試"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Preliminary</b> activities or discussions take place at the beginning of an event, often as a form of preparation. 初步的","examples":["Preliminary results show the Republican Party with 11 percent of the vote. 初步結果顯示共和黨得到11%的選票。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>preliminary</b> is something that you do at the beginning of an activity, often as a form of preparation. (程式性或禮節性的) 預備事務","examples":["You all know why I am here. So I won't waste time on preliminaries. 你們都知道我為什麼在這裡。所以我就不浪費時間講客套話了。"]}]}]},"purity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"潔淨，純淨；純潔，清白 ；（聲音、文章、音樂等的）清晰；純度"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Purity）（肯）普麗蒂（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"questionnaire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"問卷，調查表"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>questionnaire</b> is a written list of questions which are answered by a lot of people in order to provide information for a report or a survey. 調查問卷","examples":["Teachers will be asked to fill in a questionnaire. 教師們將被要求填寫一份調查問卷。"]}]}]},"racism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"種族主義，種族偏見；種族歧視，種族迫害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Racism</b> is the belief that people of some races are inferior to others, and the behaviour which is the result of this belief. 種族主義; 種族歧視","examples":["There is a feeling among some black people that the level of racism is declining. 有些黑人感覺到種族歧視的程度正在減輕。"]}]}]},"radiant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"容光煥發的，喜悅的；明亮的，燦爛的；（熱、能量）輻射的；（情感、品質）強烈的，顯著的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"輻射源（尤指電熱器或氣熱器的產熱部分）；（天文）輻射點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>radiant</b> is so happy that their happiness shows in their face. 容光煥發的","examples":["On her wedding day the bride looked truly radiant. 在她婚禮那天，新娘看起來真的是容光煥發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>radiant</b> glows brightly. 光芒四射的","examples":["The evening sun warms the old red brick wall to a radiant glow. 傍晚的陽光照暖了那道舊紅磚牆，使它熠熠生輝。"]}]}]},"qualification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（透過考試或學習課程取得的）資格，學歷；（勝任某一工作或職位所需的）資歷，技能條件；獲得資格，達到標準；先決條件，正式要求；限制，限定性條件；（語法）（尤指對名詞等的）限定，修飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>qualifications</b> are the official documents or titles you have that show your level of education and training. 資格; 學歷","examples":["\"Do you have any qualifications?\"—\"Yes, I'm certified to teach high school.\" “你有資格嗎？”—“有，我有資格教高中。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Qualification</b> is the act of passing the examinations you need to work in a particular profession. 資格取得","examples":["She has met the minimum educational requirements for qualification. 她已達到了資格取得所需的最低教育水準。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>qualifications</b> you need for an activity or task are the qualities and skills that you need to be able to do it. 素質; 技能","examples":["Responsibility and reliability are necessary qualifications, as well as a friendly and outgoing personality. 責任感和可靠性是必需的素質，友善和外向的性格也必不可少。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>qualification</b> is a detail or explanation that you add to a statement to make it less strong or less general. 限制條件","examples":["The empirical evidence considered here is subject to many qualifications. 這裡所考慮的經驗證據有許多限制條件。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"Your <b>qualifications</b> are the examinations that you have passed. (已透過的) 資格考試","examples":["Lucy Thomson, 16, wants to study theatre but needs more qualifications. 露西·湯姆森16歲，想學戲劇，但還需要透過更多的資格考試。"]}]}]},"query":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疑問，詢問；問號"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"質疑，對……表示疑問；詢問，提問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>query</b> is a question, especially one that you ask an organization, publication, or expert. 疑問","examples":["If you have any queries about this insurance, please contact our call centre. 如果你對此項保險有任何疑問，請聯絡我們的呼叫中心。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>query</b> something, you check it by asking about it because you are not sure if it is correct. 對…提出疑問","examples":["It's got a number you can call to query your bill. 你可以撥打一個號碼，對賬單提出質疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>query</b> means to ask a question. 詢問","examples":["\"Is there something else?\" Ray queried as Helen stopped speaking. 海倫話音剛落，雷便問道：“還有別的什麼嗎？”"]}]}]},"radiator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暖氣片，散熱器；（暖氣片型）燃油爐，電熱器；（車輛或飛機發動機的）冷卻器，水箱；輻射體，輻射源"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>radiator</b> is a hollow metal device, usually connected by pipes to a central heating system, that is used to heat a room. 暖氣片","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>radiator</b> in a car is the part of the engine that is filled with water in order to cool the engine. (汽車引擎的) 水箱","examples":[]}]}]},"raft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"木排，木筏； 橡皮艇，充氣船；（游泳、跳水的）浮臺；大量，許多；（樹木、草木或冰塊等一堆）漂浮物；大群遊動的水鳥（或哺乳動物）；浮筏基礎，格床基礎"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"乘坐筏子（度河），用筏子運送；（浮冰）隨浮冰流淌；將（船或其他物體）並排連為一體"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>raft</b> is a floating platform made from large pieces of wood or other materials tied together. 木排; 筏","examples":["...a river trip on bamboo rafts through dense rainforest. …一次乘著竹筏穿過茂密雨林的河上旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>raft</b> is a small rubber or plastic boat that you blow air into to make it float. (橡皮或塑膠的) 小型充氣船","examples":["The crew spent two days and nights in their raft. 船員們在他們的小充氣船上度過了兩天兩夜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a large collection or amount 大量","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to convey on or travel by raft, or make a raft from 筏運; 筏行; 製成筏","examples":[]}]}]},"radiation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"輻射，放射線；輻射的熱（或能量等）；放射療法；輻射形進化，發散狀分化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Radiation</b> consists of very small particles of a radioactive substance. Large amounts of radiation can cause illness and death. 輻射物","examples":["They suffer from health problems and fear the long term effects of radiation. 他們受健康問題的困擾，還擔心遭受輻射造成的長期影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Radiation</b> is energy, especially heat, that comes from a particular source. 輻射能 (尤指熱能)","examples":["The $617 million satellite will study energy radiation from the most violent stars in the universe. 這個價值6.17億美元的人造衛星將研究宇宙中活動最劇烈的恆星所發出的輻射能。"]}]}]},"radical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"根本的，徹底的；激進的，極端的；全新的，不同凡響的；（增減）急劇的，大幅度的；（人，物）原本的，與生俱來的；<美，非正式>頂呱呱的；（外科，醫療）根治的；<英，史>（19世紀）自由黨激進派的；（數）根式的，根號的；詞根的；（植）根生的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"激進分子； 遊離基，自由基；詞根；（漢字）偏旁，部首；（數）根式；根號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Radical</b> changes and differences are very important and great in degree. 重大的; 徹底的","examples":["The country needs a period of calm without more surges of radical change. 這個國家需要一段平靜的時期，不再有重大變化所引發的動盪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Radical</b> people believe that there should be great changes in society and try to bring about these changes. 激進的","examples":["...threats by left-wing radical groups to disrupt the proceedings. …左翼激進團體要擾亂這些活動的威脅。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"重大地; 徹底地","examples":["...two large groups of people with radically different beliefs and cultures. …信仰與文化徹底不同的兩大群體。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>radical</b> is someone who has radical views. 激進分子","examples":["Vanessa and I had been student radicals together at Berkeley from 1965 to 1967. 瓦妮莎和我在1965年至1967年期間都是伯克利大學的學生激進分子。"]}]}]},"raid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"突襲，襲擊；突擊檢查，突然搜查；搶劫，打劫；（股票）惡意大量買進"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"突襲，偷襲；突擊搜捕，突然搜查；搶劫，劫掠；掃蕩（某處的食物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When soldiers <b>raid</b> a place, they make a sudden armed attack against it, with the aim of causing damage rather than occupying any of the enemy's land. 突襲","examples":["The guerrillas raided banks and destroyed a police barracks and an electricity substation. 游擊隊員們突襲了多家銀行，摧毀了一個警察營房和一座變電站。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the police <b>raid</b> a building, they enter it suddenly and by force in order to look for dangerous criminals or for evidence of something illegal, such as drugs or weapons. 突擊搜查","examples":["Police raided their headquarters and other offices. 警察突擊搜查了他們的總部和其他辦公場所。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Raid</b> is also a noun. 突襲","examples":["The rebels attempted a surprise raid on a military camp. 反叛者們曾經試圖對兵營發動一場突然襲擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Raid</b> is also a noun. 突擊搜查","examples":["They were arrested early this morning after a raid on a house by thirty armed police. 他們於今天凌晨，在30名武裝警察突擊搜查了一所住宅後被捕。"]}]}]},"ransom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"贖金；釋放"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贖出，贖回；把持（俘虜，監禁者）索要贖金，擄（人）索贖；得贖金後釋放（俘虜，監禁者）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ransom</b> is the money that has to be paid to someone so that they will set free a person they have kidnapped. 贖金","examples":["Her kidnapper successfully extorted a $250,000 ransom for her release. 綁架者們成功地勒索了25萬美元的贖金才釋放她。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ransom</b> someone who has been kidnapped, you pay the money to set them free. 贖出","examples":["The same system was used for ransoming or exchanging captives. 同一系統也被用來贖回或交換俘虜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a kidnapper <b>is</b> <b>holding</b> a person <b>for ransom</b>, they keep that person prisoner until they are given what they want. 劫持某人以勒取贖金","examples":["He is charged with kidnapping a businessman last year and holding him for ransom. 他被指控去年綁架了一名商人並挾持他以勒索贖金。"]}]}]},"ravage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"毀壞，破壞，劫掠"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"蹂躪，大破壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A town, country, or economy that <b>has been ravaged</b> is one that has been damaged so much that it is almost completely destroyed. 摧毀","examples":["The country has been ravaged by civil war. 這個國家被內戰摧毀了。"]}]}]},"realization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"認識，領悟；（目標等的）實現；變現，變賣；兌譜，改編；（語言特徵的）體現；貨物銷售；發聲，(戲劇)演出，設計成果"}],"sections":[]},"realism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"務實作風，實事求是；現實性，逼真；（藝術、文學中的）現實主義；（科學或哲學的）實在主義，唯實論；權力實用主義；現實主義法學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people show <b>realism</b> in their behaviour, they recognize and accept the true nature of a situation and try to deal with it in a practical way. 現實態度; 務實精神","examples":["It was time now to show more political realism. 是表現出更多的政治務實精神的時候了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If things and people are presented with <b>realism</b> in paintings, stories, or movies, they are presented in a way that is like real life. (繪畫、小說或電影中的) 現實主義","examples":["Greene's stories had an edge of realism that made it easy to forget they were fiction. 格林的故事帶有現實主義的色彩，使人容易忘記它們是虛構的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the philosophical theory that general terms such as common nouns refer to entities that have a real existence separate from the individuals which fall under them 唯實論; 實在論","examples":[]}]}]},"recession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（經濟的）衰退（期）；<正式>退後，撤回；（天文）退行；凹處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>recession</b> is a period when the economy of a country is doing badly, for example because industry is producing less and more people are becoming unemployed. 經濟衰退; 蕭條","examples":["The oil price increases sent Europe into deep recession. 石油價格的上漲使歐洲陷入嚴重的經濟衰退。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the act of restoring possession to a former owner 物歸原主","examples":[]}]}]},"rebellion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"叛亂，反抗； （對權威的）反抗，不服從；叛逆，不順從"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rebellion</b> is a violent organized action by a large group of people who are trying to change their country's political system. 叛亂","examples":["The government soon put down the rebellion. 政府很快鎮壓了這次叛亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A situation in which people show their opposition to the way things have been done in the past can be referred to as a <b>rebellion</b>. 反抗","examples":["Women are waging a quiet rebellion against the traditional roles their mothers have played. 婦女們正悄悄地發動一場反抗她們的母親們所扮演的傳統角色的運動。"]}]}]},"rash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"皮疹，疹子；一連串（不愉快的事）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕率的，魯莽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>rash</b> or does <b>rash</b> things, they act without thinking carefully first, and therefore make mistakes or behave foolishly. 輕率的","examples":["It would be rash to rely on such evidence. 依靠這樣的證據太輕率了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕率地","examples":["I made a lot of money, but I rashly gave most of it away. 我賺了很多錢，但我輕率地揮霍了其中的大部分。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rash</b> is an area of red spots that appears on your skin when you are ill or have a bad reaction to something that you have eaten or touched. 疹子","examples":["He may break out in a rash when he eats these nuts. 他吃了這些堅果以後可能會長出疹子。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about a <b>rash of</b> events or things, you mean a large number of unpleasant events or undesirable things, which have happened or appeared within a short period of time. (短期內出現的) 一連串 (不悅之事)","examples":["...one of the few major airlines left untouched by the industry's rash of takeovers. …在這一連串的行業兼併中剩下的少數幾個未被波及的大航空公司之一。"]}]}]},"recipient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>接受者，領受者；接收器，容器"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"接受的，容納的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>recipient</b> of something is the person who receives it. 接受者","examples":["...the largest recipient of U.S. foreign aid. …最大的美國對外援助接受方。"]}]}]},"recommendation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"正式建議，提議；推薦，介紹；<美>推薦信"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>recommendations</b> of a person or a committee are their suggestions or advice on what is the best thing to do. 建議; 勸告","examples":["The committee's recommendations are unlikely to be made public. 委員會的建議很可能不會公之於眾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>recommendation</b> of something is the suggestion that someone should have or use it because it is good. 推薦","examples":["The best way of finding a lawyer is through personal recommendation. 找律師的最好方法是透過個人推薦。"]}]}]},"refinement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精煉，精製；（精細的）改進，改善；舉止文雅；高雅情趣；改良品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Refinements</b> are small changes or additions that you make to something in order to improve it. <b>Refinement</b> is the process of making refinements. 改進; 完善","examples":["Older cars inevitably lack the latest safety refinements. 較老式的汽車難免缺乏最新的安全改進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Refinement</b> is politeness and good manners. 彬彬有禮; 舉止文雅","examples":[]}]}]},"recruit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"招聘，招收（新成員）；招募（新兵）；說服，動員；（透過招募）組成，組建；<舊> 恢復（數量、力氣等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"新兵；新成員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recruit</b> people for an organization, you select them and persuade them to join it or work for it. 招收; 招募","examples":["The police are trying to recruit more black and Hispanic officers. 警方正試圖招收更多的黑人和西班牙裔的警官。","She set up her stand to recruit students to the Anarchist Association. 她搭了一個攤位招募學生加入無政府主義者協會。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"招收; 招募","examples":["A bomb exploded at an army recruiting office. 一枚炸彈在一個徵兵辦公室爆炸了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>recruit</b> is a person who has recently joined an organization or an army. 新成員; 新兵","examples":["...a new recruit to the LA Police Department. …洛杉磯警察局的一名新警員。"]}]}]},"refreshment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"茶點，點心（refreshments）；食物和飲料；恢復活力，煥發精神"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Refreshments</b> are drinks and small amounts of food that are provided, for example, during a meeting or a trip. 茶點","examples":["Lunch and refreshments will be provided. 將提供午餐和茶點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to food and drink as <b>refreshment</b>. 食物和飲料","examples":["May I offer you some refreshment? 可以請您吃點喝點什麼嗎？"]}]}]},"regime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指獨裁的）政府，政權；（機構、公司、經濟等的）管理制度，組織方法；飲食起居制度，養生法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to a government or system of running a country as a <b>regime</b>, you are critical of it because you think it is not democratic and uses unacceptable methods. 統治","examples":["...the collapse of the Fascist regime at the end of the war. …戰爭結束時法西斯統治的崩潰。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>regime</b> is the way that something such as an institution, company, or economy is run, especially when it involves tough or severe action. (機構、公司或經濟等的) 管理方式","examples":["The authorities moved him to the less rigid regime of an open prison. 當局把他移送到管理相對寬鬆的不設防監獄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>regime</b> is a set of rules about food, exercise, or beauty that some people follow in order to stay healthy or attractive. 養生法","examples":["He has a new fitness regime to strengthen his back. 他有一套新的健康養生法來加強他的背部力量。"]}]}]},"rehearsal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"排練，排演；預演，演習；複述，重複"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rehearsal</b> of a play, dance, or piece of music is a practice of it in preparation for a performance. 排練","examples":["The band was scheduled to begin rehearsals for a concert tour. 樂隊按計劃開始了為巡迴音樂會進行的排練。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe an event or object that is a preparation for a more important event or object as a <b>rehearsal for</b> it. (重大事件的) 預演","examples":["Daydreams may seem to be rehearsals for real-life situations, but we know they are not. 白日夢可能看上去像是真實生活境遇的預演，但我們知道它們不是。"]}]}]},"refund":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"退款，償還金額"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"退還（錢款）；退款給，還錢給（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>refund</b> is a sum of money that is returned to you, for example because you have paid too much or because you have returned goods to a shop. 退款","examples":["Face it – you'll just have to take those cowboy boots back and ask for a refund. 面對現實吧–你不過是要把那些牛仔靴拿回去，要求退款。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>refunds</b> your money, they return it to you, for example because you have paid too much or because you have returned goods to a shop. 退還","examples":["We guarantee to refund your money if you're not delighted with your purchase. 如果你對購買的商品不滿意，我們保證退款。"]}]}]},"reliance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"依靠，信任；<古>被依賴的人（或物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's or thing's <b>reliance</b> <b>on</b> something is the fact that they need it and often cannot live or work without it. 依賴; 依靠","examples":["...the country's increasing reliance on foreign aid. …這個國家日益依賴外來援助。"]}]}]},"rein":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"韁繩；（成人牽引幼兒用的）安全繩套；控制，主宰"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用韁繩勒（馬）使停步或放慢步子，勒（馬）；控制住，約束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reins</b> are the thin leather straps attached around a horse's neck which are used to control the horse. 韁繩","examples":["Cord held the reins while the stallion tugged and snorted. 當那匹牡馬使勁掙扎，打著響鼻的時候，科德勒緊了韁繩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Journalists sometimes use the expression <b>the reins</b> or <b>the reins of power</b> to refer to the control of a country or organization. 執政; 掌權","examples":["He was determined to see the party keep a hold on the reins of power. 他決心要確保該黨繼續執掌政權。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>give free rein to</b> someone, you give them a lot of freedom to do what they want. 給 (某人) 充分的自由","examples":["The government continued to believe it should give free rein to the private sector in transportation. 政府繼續認為應該給私營運輸部門充分的自由。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>keep a tight rein on</b> someone, you control them firmly. 嚴格控制","examples":["Her parents kept her on a tight rein with their narrow and inflexible views. 她的父母目光短淺而又固執地嚴格控制著她。"]}]}]},"relay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"傳遞，傳達（資訊、新聞等）；中繼轉發，轉播（廣播或電視訊號）；重鋪，重新鋪設（過去式和過去分詞形式 relaid）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"接力賽；接班的人（或動物），輪換者；傳遞，傳送；中繼裝置；繼電器；中繼轉播的資訊（或節目）；傳輸系統，傳送系統"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>relay</b> or a <b>relay race</b> is a race between two or more teams, for example teams of runners or swimmers. Each member of the team runs or swims one section of the race. 接力賽","examples":["Britain's prospects of beating the United States in the relay looked poor. 英國隊在接力賽中戰勝美國隊的希望看上去不大。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>relay</b> television or radio signals means to send them or broadcast them. 轉播","examples":["The satellite will be used mainly to relay television programmes. 這顆衛星將主要用來轉播電視節目。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>relay</b> something that has been said to you, you repeat it to another person. 轉告","examples":["She relayed the message, then frowned. 她轉告了那個訊息，然後皺了皺眉。"]}]}]},"relish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"享受，樂趣；喜歡，喜愛；開胃小菜，調味品；滋味，風味；<古> 引起食慾的香味"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"享受，喜歡；憧憬，期盼；品味；味道可口；有……的味道；<古> 使有滋味，加佐料於"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>relish</b> something, you get a lot of enjoyment from it. 喜愛; 樂於; 玩賞","examples":["I relish the challenge of doing jobs that others turn down. 我喜歡接受挑戰做別人拒絕做的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Relish</b> is also a noun. 喜愛; 愛好","examples":["The three men ate with relish. 那3個人吃得津津有味。"]}]}]},"rental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"租費，租金；出租，租賃；<美>租用物（尤指房屋或車輛）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（與）租借（有關）的，可供租用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>rental</b> of something such as a car or piece of equipment is the activity or process of renting it. 出租; 租借","examples":["We can arrange car rental from Chicago's O'Hare Airport. 我們可以安排從芝加哥奧黑爾機場租車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>rental</b> is the amount of money that you pay when you rent something such as a car, property, or piece of equipment. 租金","examples":["It has been let at an annual rental of $393,000. 它已經以每年$393000的租金租出去了。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>rental</b> to describe things that are connected with the renting out of goods, properties, and services. 出租的; 租賃業的","examples":["A friend drove her to Atlanta, where she picked up a rental car. 一個朋友開車送她去了亞特蘭大，在那裡她租到了一輛車。"]}]}]},"removal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"移走，去掉；消除，清除；免職，開除；<英>搬運，搬遷；<南非，史>種族迫遷；<愛爾蘭>（從家裡運至教堂舉行葬禮的）屍體搬運儀式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>removal</b> of something is the act of removing it. 移動; 搬動; 去除","examples":["What they expected to be the removal of a small lump turned out to be major surgery. 他們本以為只是切除一個小腫塊，結果卻成了個大手術。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Removal</b> is the process of transporting furniture or equipment from one building to another. (傢俱、裝置的) 搬運","examples":[]}]}]},"renaissance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"復興，再生；文藝復興（時期）（the Renaissance）；文藝復興文化，文藝復興風格（Renaissance）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The Renaissance</b> was the period in Europe, especially Italy, in the 14th, 15th, and 16th centuries, when there was a new interest in art, literature, science, and learning. 文藝復興時期","examples":["...the Renaissance masterpieces in London's galleries. …倫敦美術館裡文藝復興時期的傑作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something experiences a <b>renaissance</b>, it becomes popular or successful again after a time when people were not interested in it. 復興","examples":["Popular art is experiencing a renaissance. 通俗藝術正在復興。"]}]}]},"remainder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剩餘部分，其餘；廉價出售的書，滯銷圖書；差數，餘數；<法律>有待繼承產權，指定繼承產權"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"削價出售（剩書）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<罕>剩餘的，殘餘的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The remainder</b> <b>of</b> a group are the things or people that still remain after the other things or people have gone or have been dealt with. 剩餘部分","examples":["He gulped down the remainder of his coffee. 他一口喝完了剩下的咖啡。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Remainder</b> is also a pronoun. 剩餘部分","examples":["Only 5.9 percent of the area is now covered in trees. Most of the remainder is farmland. 該地區現在的樹木覆蓋率僅為5.9％。剩餘部分大多是農田。"]}]}]},"reservoir":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"水庫，蓄水池；儲藏，蓄積 ；（機器等的）貯液器，貯液槽；（病原體的）儲存宿主"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>reservoir</b> is a lake that is used for storing water before it is supplied to people. 水庫","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reservoir</b> <b>of</b> something is a large quantity of it that is available for use when needed. 大量儲備","examples":["...the huge oil reservoir beneath the Kuwaiti desert. …科威特沙漠下面大量的石油儲備。"]}]}]},"restoration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（對藝術品、建築等的）修復；（做法、權利、慣例或情況的）恢復，重新實施；歸還，返還；（軟體程式的）恢復，還原；（牙科）修補；（模擬已滅絕動物或被毀建築等原型的）修復物（或圖），重建物（或圖）；（君主、元首、政權等的）原有地位的恢復，復位；王政復辟時期（1660 年英王查理二世復辟及其後的一段時期）（the Restoration）；法國波旁王朝王政復辟（the Restoration）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"專有名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The Restoration</b> was the event in 1660 when Charles the Second became king of England, Scotland, and Ireland after a period when there had been no king or queen. (1660年英王查理二世的)王政復辟","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Restoration</b> is used to refer to the style of drama and architecture that was popular during and just after the rule of Charles the Second in England. (戲劇、建築)王政復辟時期的","examples":["...a Restoration comedy. ...一部王政復辟時期的喜劇。"]}]}]},"revelation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"被揭示的真相，被揭露的內情；揭露，披露；出乎意料的事物，令人驚喜的發現；（上帝的）啟示，默示；《啟示錄》（《聖經·新約》末卷，講述上帝對聖約翰有關未來的啟示）（Revelation）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>revelation</b> is a surprising or interesting fact that is made known to people. 被透露的事實; 被洩露的秘密","examples":["...the seemingly everlasting revelations about his private life. …有關他私生活的似乎永無休止的披露。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>revelation</b> <b>of</b> something is the act of making it known. 揭露; 透露","examples":["...following the revelation of his affair with a former secretary. …在他和前任秘書的風流韻事被揭露之後。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something you experienced was <b>a</b> <b>revelation</b>, you are saying that it was very surprising or very good. (驚人的、極好的) 發現","examples":["Degas's work had been a revelation to her. 德各斯的工作曾是她的一大發現。"]}]}]},"retail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"零售"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"零售；以……價格銷售；詳說，述說（尤指別人的事情）"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以零售方式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"零售的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Retail</b> is the activity of selling products direct to the public, usually in small quantities. Compare . 零售","examples":["Retail stores usually count on the Christmas season to make up to half of their annual profits. 零售商店通常指望聖誕節期間來賺取一半的年利潤。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is sold <b>retail</b>, it is sold in ordinary shops direct to the public. 以零售方式地","examples":["We sell wholesale to several chains that sell retail to the public. 我們批發給幾家向公眾零售的連鎖店。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an item in a shop <b>retails</b> <b>at</b> or <b>for</b> a particular price, it is for sale at that price. (按某種價格) 零售","examples":["It originally retailed at $23.50. 它起初按$23.50的價格零售。"]}]}]},"restraint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剋制，抑制；控制，限制；管制措施，制約因素；<正式>（武力）阻止，制止；座椅安全帶，安全裝置；（尤指藝術表達中的）低調處理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Restraints</b> are rules or conditions that limit or restrict someone or something. 限制","examples":["The president is calling for spending restraints in some areas. 該總統要求在一些領域限制開支。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Restraint</b> is calm, controlled, and unemotional behaviour. 剋制","examples":["They behaved with more restraint than I'd expected. 他們表現了比我預想還多的剋制。"]}]}]},"resemblance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"相似，相像；相似點，相似之處；相似物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>resemblance</b> between two people or things, they are similar to each other. 相似之處","examples":["There was a remarkable resemblance between him and Pete. 他和皮特有一個驚人的相似之處。"]}]}]},"revival":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"復興，復甦；再流行；（舊劇的）重新上演；（復興基督教信仰的）奮興佈道會；（體力或活力的）重振"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is a <b>revival</b> <b>of</b> something, it becomes active or popular again. 再流行; 復興","examples":["This return to realism has produced a revival of interest in a number of artists. 這次向現實主義的迴歸引起了對許多藝術家興趣的復甦。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>revival</b> is a new production of a play, an opera, or a ballet. 新版演出","examples":["...John Clement's revival of Chekhov's \"The Seagull.\" …約翰•克萊門的新版特契訶夫的《海鷗》。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>revival</b> meeting is a public religious event that is intended to make people more interested in Christianity. 奮興 (佈道會)","examples":["He toured the country organizing revival meetings. 他巡遊全國，組織奮興佈道會。"]}]}]},"rhetoric":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"花言巧語，浮誇之詞；修辭，修辭學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to speech or writing as <b>rhetoric</b>, you disapprove of it because it is intended to convince and impress people but may not be sincere or honest. 虛華詞藻","examples":["The change is largely cosmetic, a matter of acceptable political rhetoric rather than social reality. 這一變化主要是表面文章，不過是受歡迎的政治性虛華詞藻而非社會現實。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Rhetoric</b> is the skill or art of using language effectively. 修辭藝術","examples":["...the noble institutions of political life, such as political rhetoric, public office, and public service. …政治生活中令人尊崇的機制，諸如政治修辭藝術、政府機構以及公益服務。"]}]}]},"ridicule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘲笑，奚落"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘲笑，奚落"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>ridicule</b> someone or <b>ridicule</b> their ideas or beliefs, you make fun of them in an unkind way. 嘲笑","examples":["I admired her all the more for allowing them to ridicule her and never striking back. 我更加欽佩她了，因為她能夠容許讓他們嘲笑她而從不回擊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is an object of <b>ridicule</b> or is held up to <b>ridicule</b>, someone makes fun of them in an unkind way. 嘲笑","examples":["As a heavy child, she became the object of ridicule from classmates. 作為一個胖孩子，她成了同學們的笑柄。"]}]}]},"rite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（宗教等的）儀式；禮節，慣例"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>rite</b> is a traditional ceremony that is carried out by a particular group or within a particular society. 傳統儀式","examples":["Most traditional societies have transition rites at puberty. 大多數傳統社會在青春期舉行過渡儀式。"]}]}]},"ritual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（宗教等的）儀式，典禮；習慣，例行公事；（尤指某一宗教或教派特定的）程式，儀式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"儀式上的，慶典上的；（行動）常規的，例行的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ritual</b> is a religious service or other ceremony which involves a series of actions performed in a fixed order. 宗教儀式; 典禮","examples":["This is the most ancient, and holiest of the Shinto rituals. 這是最古老、最神聖的神道教儀式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>ritual</b> is a way of behaving or a series of actions that people regularly carry out in a particular situation, because it is their custom to do so. 習俗","examples":["The whole Italian culture revolves around the ritual of eating. 整個義大利文化是圍繞著飲食習俗的。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ritual</b> activities happen as part of a ritual or tradition. 儀式性的; 傳統的","examples":["...fasting and ritual dancing. …齋戒和儀式性舞蹈。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe something as a <b>ritual</b> action when it is done in exactly the same way whenever a particular situation occurs. 例行公事般的; 習慣性的","examples":["I realized that here the conventions required me to make the ritual noises. 我意識到這裡的習俗要求我得說套話。"]}]}]},"revenue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（企業、組織的）收入，收益；（政府的）稅收；稅務局，稅務署（the revenue）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Revenue</b> is money that a company, organization, or government receives from people. (公司、組織或政府的) 收入","examples":["...a boom year at the movies, with record advertising revenue and the highest ticket sales since 1980. …電影業欣欣向榮的一年，廣告及票房收入都創下1980年以來的最高紀錄。"]}]}]},"safeguard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保障條款， 保護措施"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保護，護衛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>safeguard</b> something or someone means to protect them from being harmed, lost, or badly treated. 保護; 保衛","examples":["They will press for international action to safeguard the ozone layer. 他們將竭力要求國際行動來保護臭氧層。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>safeguard</b> is a law, rule, or measure intended to prevent someone or something from being harmed. 安全條例; 防護措施","examples":["As an additional safeguard against weeds you can always use an underlay of heavy duty polyethylene. 作為另外一種預防雜草的防護措施，你可以一直使用一層厚重耐磨的聚乙烯底墊。"]}]}]},"rivalry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"競爭，較量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rivalry</b> is competition or fighting between people, businesses, or organizations who are in the same area or want the same things. 競爭; 鬥爭","examples":["The rivalry between the Inkatha and the ANC has resulted in violence in the black townships. 英卡塔自由黨與非洲國民大會之間的鬥爭導致了黑人城鎮之間的暴力衝突。"]}]}]},"saloon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"酒吧，酒館（美式，常指舊時美國西部）；大廳（公共大廳、大會客室、展覽場）；轎車，三廂轎車（英國用法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>saloon</b> is a car with seats for four or more people, a fixed roof, and a boot that is separate from the part of the car that you sit in. 箱式小貨車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>saloon</b> is a place where alcoholic drinks are sold and drunk. 酒館","examples":["In the saloon, he drank whisky and let his eyes become accustomed to the dimness. 在酒館裡，他喝了威士忌，雙眼也變得適應昏暗。"]}]}]},"rotation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旋轉，轉動；旋轉一週（一圈）；輪流，交替；輪班，換班；<美>值輪班的人；<美>（尤指實習醫生的）輪流實習；輪作，輪耕；（林業）輪伐期；（數學）座標軸的旋轉；（數學）旋度，旋量（=curl）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Rotation</b> is circular movement. A <b>rotation</b> is the movement of something through one complete circle. 旋轉; 轉動","examples":["...the daily rotation of the earth upon its axis. …地球圍繞地軸的每日自轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>rotation</b> of a group of things or people is the fact of them taking turns to do a particular job or serve a particular purpose. If people do something <b>in rotation</b>, they take turns to do it. 輪流","examples":["He grew a different crop on the same field five years in a row, what researchers call crop rotation. 他連續5年在同一塊地上輪流種植不同作物，研究人員稱之為輪作。"]}]}]},"sanctuary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"避難權，庇護；避難所，庇護所；動物保護區，禁獵區；（某種受傷或遭遺棄動物的）收養所；宗教聖所，聖殿；（教堂內的）聖壇"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sanctuary</b> is a place where people who are in danger from other people can go to be safe. 避難所","examples":["His church became a sanctuary for thousands of people who fled the civil war. 他的教堂成了數千逃避內戰的人們的一個避難所。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sanctuary</b> is the safety provided in a sanctuary. 庇護","examples":["Some of them have sought sanctuary in the church. 他們中的一些人已在教堂裡尋求庇護。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sanctuary</b> is a place where birds or animals are protected and allowed to live freely. 鳥獸禁獵區","examples":["...a bird sanctuary. …一個鳥類禁獵區。"]}]}]},"salvation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解救物，救星；解救，拯救；（基督教中）對靈魂的拯救，救贖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In Christianity, <b>salvation</b> is the fact that Christ has saved a person from evil. (基督教中) 靈魂的拯救","examples":["The church's message of salvation has changed the lives of many. 這個教會的靈魂得救的訓誡已經改變了很多人的一生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>salvation</b> of someone or something is the act of saving them from harm, destruction, or an unpleasant situation. 解救; 拯救","examples":["...those whose marriages are beyond salvation. …那些婚姻無法拯救的人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone or something is your <b>salvation</b>, they are responsible for saving you from harm, destruction, or an unpleasant situation. 救星; 解救物","examples":["The country's salvation lies in forcing through democratic reforms. 拯救該國在於強制推行民主改革。"]}]}]},"sanitation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公共衛生，環境衛生；下水道設施，衛生裝置"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sanitation</b> is the process of keeping places clean and healthy, especially by providing a sewage system and a clean water supply. (尤指透過提供排汙系統和潔淨水源的) 公共衛生","examples":["...the hazards of contaminated water and poor sanitation. …汙水和不良公共衛生的危害。"]}]}]},"sanction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"制裁；處罰，懲罰；（正式）許可，批准；<史>（尤指基督教會的）法令，法律；（倫理學）約束力；支援，鼓勵"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"認可，准許；對……實施制裁，處罰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>sanctions</b> an action or practice, they officially approve of it and allow it to be done. 批准; 認可","examples":["He may now be ready to sanction the use of force. 他或許現在正準備批准使用武力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sanction</b> is also a noun. 批准; 認可","examples":["...a newspaper run by citizens without the sanction of the government. …未經政府許可的一家民辦報紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Sanctions</b> are measures taken by countries to restrict trade and official contact with a country that has broken international law. 國際制裁","examples":["The continued abuse of human rights has now led the United States to impose sanctions against the regime. 對人權的不斷踐踏現已導致美國對該政權實施國際制裁。"]}]}]},"scope":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"範圍，領域；（發揮能力的）機會，施展餘地；視野，眼界；觀測儀器（如望遠鏡、顯微鏡等）；（船拋錨時的）纜繩長度；特定論點的數量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"評估，調查（scope sth. out）；確定（規劃專案）的範圍；<非正式>仔細看，徹底檢查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is <b>scope</b> <b>for</b> a particular kind of behaviour or activity, people have the opportunity to behave in this way or do that activity. 機會","examples":["He believed in giving his staff scope for initiative. 他贊成給他的員工主動的機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>scope</b> <b>of</b> an activity, topic, or piece of work is the whole area which it deals with or includes. 範圍","examples":["Mr. Dobson promised to widen the organization's scope of activity. 多布森先生答應擴大該組織的活動範圍。"]}]}]},"sector":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"區域，部分；（尤指商業、貿易等的）部門，行業；小群體；（尤指軍隊控制的）分割槽，防區；（磁碟上的）扇區； 扇形，扇形面；函式尺，象限儀"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……分成扇形"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>sector</b> of a country's economy is the part connected with that specified type of industry. (經濟的) 部門","examples":["...the nation's manufacturing sector. …該國的製造部門。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sector</b> of a large group is a smaller group which is part of it. 部分","examples":["Workers who went to the Gulf came from the poorest sectors of Pakistani society. 去海灣的工人們來自巴基斯坦社會最貧窮的階層。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>sector</b> is an area of a city or country which is controlled by a military force. 軍事管制區","examples":["Officers were going to retake sectors of the city. 軍官們打算收回該市的一些軍事管制區。"]}]}]},"royalty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"王族，王室；王權，王威；版稅；(發明、創意、財產等的）使用費；（礦山、石油或天然氣的）開採權使用費；（國王授予個人或公司的）權利（尤指礦山開採權）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The members of royal families are sometimes referred to as <b>royalty</b>. 王室","examples":["Royalty and government leaders from all around the world are gathering in Japan. 來自世界各國的王室和政府首腦們正聚集日本。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Royalties</b> are payments made to authors and musicians when their work is sold or performed. They usually receive a fixed percentage of the profits from these sales or performances. 版稅","examples":["I lived on about $5,000 a year from the royalties on my book. 我靠的大約五千美元的出書版稅生活。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Payments made to someone whose invention, idea, or property is used by a commercial company can be referred to as <b>royalties</b>. (發明、創意、財產等的) 使用費","examples":["The royalties enabled the inventor to re-establish himself in business. 這些使用費使這名發明者能再次立足商界。"]}]}]},"seminar":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"研討會，培訓會；（大學的）專題討論課，研討班"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seminar</b> is a meeting where a group of people discuss a problem or topic. 研討會; 專題討論會","examples":["...a series of half-day seminars to help businessmen get the best value from investing in information technology. …一系列幫助商界人士從投資資訊科技中獲得最大價值的每次為期半天的專題討論會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>seminar</b> is a class at a college or university in which the teacher and a small group of students discuss a topic. (大學裡由教師指導小組學生參加的) 研討班","examples":["Students are asked to prepare material in advance of each weekly seminar. 要求學生為每星期一次的研討班預先準備好材料。"]}]}]},"senator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"參議員，（古羅馬的）元老院議員，（大學理事會的）理事；<蘇格蘭>庭長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>senator</b> is a member of a political Senate, for example, in the United States or Australia. 參議員","examples":["...Texas' first black senator. …得克薩斯州的第一位黑人參議員。"]}]}]},"script":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"劇本，講稿；筆跡，手寫體；連寫體，草體；字型；（一種語言的）字母系統，字母表；<英>（考生的）筆試答卷； 指令碼（程式）（計算機的一系列指令）；<非正式>（醫生的）處方；期待，計劃"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"寫劇本，寫講稿；事先準備，計劃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>script</b> of a play, movie, or television programme is the written version of it. 指令碼","examples":["Jenny's writing a film script. 珍妮在寫一個電影指令碼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a particular system of writing as a particular <b>script</b>. 文字系統","examples":["...a text in the Malay language but written in Arabic script. …一段用阿拉伯文書寫的馬來語文字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Script</b> is handwriting in which the letters are joined together. 連寫體","examples":["When you're writing in script, there are four letters of the alphabet that you can't complete in one stroke. 當你用連寫體書寫時，字母表裡有4個字母你不能一筆寫完。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The person who <b>scripts</b> a movie or a radio or television play writes it. 為 (電影、廣播、電視等) 寫指令碼","examples":["...James Cameron, who scripted and directed both films. …為這兩部電影寫指令碼並執導的詹姆斯·卡梅倫。"]}]}]},"serenity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"平靜，寧靜"}],"sections":[]},"sequence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"順序，次序；連續事件（或動作、事物）；（電影中表現同一主題或場面的）一組鏡頭；（生物學中分子或基因的排列）順序；模進；（紙牌的）同花順；序列；（天主教彌撒中聖歌與福音之間的）繼續經"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"按順序排列；測定（整套基因或分子成分的）序列；用音序器播放（或錄製）音樂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sequence</b> <b>of</b> events or things is a number of events or things that come one after another in a particular order. 一系列; 一連串","examples":["...the sequence of events which led to the murder. …導致這起謀殺的一連串事件。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A particular <b>sequence</b> is a particular order in which things happen or are arranged. 次序; 順序","examples":["...the colour sequence yellow, orange, purple, blue, green and white. …黃、橙、紫、藍、綠和白的顏色順序。"]}]}]},"serving":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（食物或飲料的）一人份"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"上菜用的，分菜餚用的；目前任職的，（尤指）現役的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……服務；供應，上（飲料、食物）；服役，供職於（serve 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>serving</b> is an amount of food that is given to one person at a meal. (食物的) 一份","examples":["Quantities will vary according to how many servings of soup you want to prepare. 數量取決於你要準備多少份湯。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>serving</b> spoon or dish is used for giving out food at a meal. 上菜用的","examples":["Pile the potatoes into a warm serving dish. 把土豆堆在一隻上菜的熱盤子裡。"]}]}]},"riot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴亂，騷亂；紛呈，豐富多彩；<非正式>非常有趣的人（或事物）；縱情歡鬧，狂歡；<喻>騷動；<喻>（感情的）爆發，宣洩"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（人群）發生騷亂，聚眾鬧事；<喻>放縱，恣意；<罕>浪費，揮霍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is a <b>riot</b>, a crowd of people behave violently in a public place, for example they fight, throw stones, or damage buildings and vehicles. 暴亂","examples":["Twelve inmates have been killed during a riot at the prison. 十二名囚犯在該監獄裡的一次暴亂中喪生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"鬧事者","examples":["The militia dispersed the rioters. 民兵驅散了鬧事者。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that there is <b>a riot of</b> something pleasant such as colour, you mean that there is a large amount of various types of it. (顏色等) 豐富多樣","examples":["It would be a riot of colour, of poppies and irises and flowers of every kind. 那將會是五彩斑斕的顏色，由罌粟花、鳶尾花以及各種花卉組成。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people <b>riot</b>, they behave violently in a public place. 鬧事","examples":["Last year 600 inmates rioted, starting fires and building barricades. 去年600名囚犯鬧事，放火併製造路障。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>reads</b> you <b>the riot act</b>, they tell you that you will be punished unless you start behaving properly. 向某人提出不良行為警告","examples":["I'm glad you read the riot act to Billy. He's still a kid and still needs to be told what to do. 我很高興你向比利提出了不良行為警告。他還是個孩子，還是需要有人指導。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If people <b>run riot</b>, they behave in a wild and uncontrolled manner. 肆意撒野","examples":["Rampaging prisoners ran riot through the jail. 鬧事的囚犯在監獄裡肆意撒野。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something such as your imagination <b>runs riot</b>, it is not limited or controlled, and produces ideas that are new or exciting, rather than sensible. (想像力等) 肆意馳騁","examples":["She dressed strictly for comfort and economy, but let her imagination run riot with costume jewellery. 她穿衣服嚴格地追求舒適和經濟，但是在佩戴時裝首飾方面則讓其想像力肆意發揮。"]}]}]},"setback":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"挫折，阻礙；（建築）壁階；<美>（建築物的）縮排距離"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>setback</b> is an event that delays your progress or reverses some of the progress that you have made. 挫折; 倒退","examples":["The move represents a setback for the Middle East peace process. 此舉意味著中東和平程序的倒退。"]}]}]},"sewer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"下水道，陰溝；縫紉工，縫紉機；（中世紀貴族宅邸中的）司膳管家"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"為……鋪設汙水管道，用下水道排除……的汙水；清洗汙水管"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sewer</b> is a large underground channel that carries waste matter and rain water away, usually to a place where it is treated and made harmless. 下水道","examples":["...the city's sewer system. …該城市的下水道系統。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a person or thing that sews 縫紉工或縫紉機","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to provide with sewers 為...鋪設汙水管道","examples":[]}]}]},"shilling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"先令（肯亞、坦尚尼亞、烏干達、索馬利亞等國的貨幣單位）；先令（舊時英國及澳大利亞使用的貨幣單位，等於 1/20 英鎊，縮寫為 s 或 sh）；Shilling（英語姓氏，常譯作希林）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a former British and Australian silver or cupronickel coin worth one twentieth of a pound: not minted in Britain since 1970 先令; 英國和澳大利亞曾使用的銀幣或銅鎳合金硬幣，價值二十分之一磅，自1970年起不再鑄造 (Abbreviation s, sh)","examples":[]}]}]},"siege":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（軍隊或警察對某地的）圍困，包圍；不斷的攻擊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"圍攻，包圍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>siege</b> is a military or police operation in which soldiers or police surround a place in order to force the people there to come out or give up control of the place. 包圍","examples":["We must do everything possible to lift the siege. 我們必須盡一切可能解除包圍。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If police, soldiers, or journalists <b>lay siege</b> <b>to</b> a place, they surround it in order to force the people there to come out or give up control of the place. 包圍","examples":["The rebels laid siege to the governor's residence. 叛亂者們包圍了那座總督官邸。"]}]}]},"shed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"去除，擺脫；（植物）落（葉），（動物）蛻（皮），脫（毛）；脫掉（所穿衣物）；掉落（貨物）；擋水，防水；射出，發出（光）；流，灑，落（淚）；<正式>（尤指在戰爭中）造成傷亡，使流（血）；把（車）停在庫棚內；（分割槽）切斷（電力載荷）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"棚屋，小屋；（工業上用於生產或存放裝置的）廠房，工棚；<澳新>剪羊棚，擠奶棚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shed</b> is a small building that is used for storing things such as garden tools. (用於存放園藝工具等的) 棚屋","examples":["...a garden shed. …一個園藝工具棚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>shed</b> is a large shelter or building, for example, at a train station, port, or factory. (車站、港口、工廠等的) 棚式建築","examples":["...a vast factory shed. …一座巨大的廠房。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a tree <b>sheds</b> its leaves, its leaves fall off in the autumn. When an animal <b>sheds</b> hair or skin, some of its hair or skin drops off. 落 (葉); 脫 (發); 蛻 (皮)","examples":["Some of the trees were already beginning to shed their leaves. 有些樹已經開始落葉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>shed</b> something means to get rid of it. 去除; 擺脫","examples":["The firm is to shed 700 jobs. 這個公司將裁掉700個工作崗位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>shed</b> tears, you cry. 落 (淚)","examples":["They will shed a few tears at their daughter's wedding. 他們在女兒的婚禮上會落些淚。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"To <b>shed</b> blood means to kill people in a violent way. If someone <b>sheds</b> their blood, they are killed in a violent way, usually when they are fighting in a war. 灑 (熱血)","examples":["...young warriors, eager to shed blood. …渴望灑熱血的年輕武士們。"]}]}]},"session":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某項活動的）一段時間，一場；（議會等的）會議，（法庭的）開庭；學年，上課時間；（酒吧中）演奏會（尤指演奏愛爾蘭音樂）；（計算機領域中的）會話；（尤指錄音師的）灌錄音樂時間；<非正式>酗酒期；基督教長老會的管理機構"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（音樂家）伴奏的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>session</b> is a meeting of a court, legislature, or other official group. 開庭; 會議","examples":["After two late night sessions, the Security Council has failed to reach agreement. 開過兩次深夜會議之後，安理會仍未能達成協議。","The Arab League is meeting in emergency session today. 阿拉伯國家聯盟今天正在舉行緊急會議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>session</b> is a period during which the meetings of a court, legislature, or other official group are regularly held. 開庭期; 會期","examples":["From September until December, Congress remained in session. 9月到12月國會一直處在開會期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>session</b> of a particular activity is a period of that activity. 一場 (活動)","examples":["The two leaders emerged for a photo session. 兩位領導人出場參加了合影。"]}]}]},"silicon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"矽（一種化學元素，符號為 Si）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Silicon</b> is an element that is found in sand and in minerals such as quartz and granite. Silicon is used to make parts of computers and other electronic equipment. 矽","examples":["The new chip will be made from a piece of silicon about the size of a postage stamp. 這種新的晶片將由大約郵票大小的一塊矽片製成。"]}]}]},"signature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"簽名，署名；簽字，簽署；鮮明特色，明顯特徵；（印刷）折標；書貼；<美>標記，用法籤（處方上說明藥的用法的部分）；（音樂的）拍號；（音樂的）調號"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"標誌性的，慣有的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>signature</b> is your name, written in your own characteristic way, often at the end of a document to indicate that you wrote the document or that you agree with what it says. 簽名","examples":["I was writing my signature at the bottom of the page. 我當時正把我的簽名寫在本頁的底部。"]}]}]},"simplicity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"簡單（性)，容易（性）；簡樸，樸素；簡單（或質樸、樸素）之處；愚蠢，無知"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>simplicity</b> of something is the fact that it is not complicated and can be understood or done easily. 簡單; 簡明","examples":["The apparent simplicity of his plot is deceptive. 他的陰謀貌似簡單，卻具有欺騙性。"]}]}]},"slang":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"俚語"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>謾罵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slang</b> consists of words, expressions, and meanings that are informal and are used by people who know each other very well or who have the same interests. 俚語; 行話","examples":["Archie liked to think he kept up with current slang. 阿奇樂於自認為能跟得上時新俚語。"]}]}]},"slavery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"奴隸制，蓄奴；奴隸身份，奴役；過分依賴，過分投入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slavery</b> is the system by which people are owned by other people as slaves. 奴隸制","examples":["My people have survived 400 years of slavery. 我的民族歷經400年的奴隸制度後倖存了下來。"]}]}]},"skim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（從液體表面）撇去（浮物）；掠過，擦過（表面）；<英>用（扁石）打水漂；略讀，瀏覽；略微討論（或處理）（skim over）；<非正式>（尤指一段時間內）挪用（小數額錢）；盜用（信用卡電子資訊）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"液麵上的表層物；瀏覽；脫脂品（尤指脫脂奶）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"脫脂的；撇去浮沫的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>skim</b> something <b>from</b> the surface of a liquid, you remove it. 撇去 (液體表面的浮物)","examples":["Rough seas today prevented specially equipped ships from skimming oil off the water's surface. 今天洶湧的海浪使特別裝備的船隻無法撇去浮在水面上的石油。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>skims</b> a surface, it moves quickly along just above it. 掠過","examples":["...seagulls skimming the waves. …掠過海浪的海鷗。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>skim</b> a piece of writing, you read through it quickly. 略讀; 瀏覽","examples":["He skimmed the pages quickly, then read them again more carefully. 他很快瀏覽了幾頁，然後又仔細地讀了一遍。"]}]}]},"smallpox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（醫學）天花"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Smallpox</b> is a serious infectious disease that causes spots which leave deep marks on the skin. 天花","examples":[]}]}]},"slash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用利器）砍，劈；大幅度削減，大大降低；嚴厲批評，抨擊；猛力移動，襲擊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（用刀等）砍，劈；（長而窄的）傷口，砍痕；斜槓，斜線號；<英，非正式> 撒尿，小便；裝飾性開叉；（喻）明亮的條紋（或色線）；<美> 殘留枝椏；沼澤低地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slash</b> something, you make a long, deep cut in it. 砍; 劈","examples":["He came within two minutes of bleeding to death after slashing his wrists. 他割腕後不到兩分鐘就失血而死。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>slash</b> something such as costs or jobs means to reduce them by a large amount. 大幅度削減","examples":["Car makers could be forced to slash prices. 汽車製造商可能會被迫大幅度降價。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slash</b> is also a noun. 劈砍; 砍擊","examples":["Make deep slashes in the meat and push in the spice paste. 把肉剁透，然後擠入調料醬。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slash</b> is a sloping line that separates letters, words, or numbers, for example, in 340/2/K. 斜線號","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slash</b> <b>at</b> a person or thing, you quickly hit at them with something such as a knife. 揮舞 (刀等) 擊打","examples":["He slashed at her, aiming carefully. 他瞄得準準的，朝她揮砍過去。"]}]}]},"ruby":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紅寶石；深紅色；（印刷）5點鉛字"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"深紅色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ruby</b> is a dark red jewel. 紅寶石","examples":["...a ruby and diamond ring. …一枚紅寶石鑽戒。"]}]},{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>ruby</b> is dark red in colour. 深紅色 (的)","examples":["...a glass of ruby-red Cabernet Sauvignon. …一杯深紅色的赤霞珠紅葡萄酒。"]}]}]},"slum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"貧民窟，棚屋區；<非正式>髒亂的房子（或房間）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>（短期）去貧窮地方，過簡樸生活"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slum</b> is an area of a city where living conditions are very bad and where the houses are in bad condition. 貧民區","examples":["...a slum area of St. Louis. …聖路易斯的一個貧民區。"]}]}]},"smack":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"用巴掌打，摑；猛擊，重撞；用拳猛擊，強力打進（或推進、放入）；類似於，含有……的意味（smack of）；咂嘴；<美，非正式>聲音響亮地吻；<古>甩（鞭子）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"掌摑，拍擊；猛擊一拳；砰的一聲，撞擊聲；響吻；海洛因；一絲，一點兒；小漁船"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"正好地，不偏不倚地；猛地，猛然作聲地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smack</b> someone, you hit them with your hand. (用手) 擊打","examples":["She smacked me on the side of the head. 她打到了我一邊腦袋上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>smack</b> something somewhere, you put it or throw it there so that it makes a loud, sharp noise. 啪地扔下; 啪地放下","examples":["He smacked his hands down on his knees. 他把雙手啪地放到了雙膝上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Smack</b> is also a noun. (用手) 擊打","examples":["Sometimes he just doesn't listen and I end up shouting at him or giving him a smack. 有時他就是不聽，最後我朝他大喊大叫，或者給他一巴掌。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a smell or flavour that is distinctive though faint 微有某味; 帶有某種風味","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Smack</b> is heroin. 海洛因","examples":["...a smack addict. …一個吸海洛因成癮的人。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to have the characteristic smell or flavour (of something) 風味","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>smacks of</b> another thing that you consider bad, it reminds you of it or is like it. 帶有…跡象; 含有…意味","examples":["The engineers' union was unhappy with the motion, saying it smacked of racism. 工程師聯合會不滿意這個提議，說它有種族主義的味道。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>smack</b> in a particular place is exactly in that place. 恰好","examples":["In part that's because industry is smack in the middle of the city. 部分是因為工業恰恰就在該市的中心地帶。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smack</b> your <b>lips</b>, you open and close your mouth noisily, especially before or after eating, to show that you are eager to eat or enjoyed eating. (尤指嘴饞或回味而) 咂嘴","examples":["\"I really want some dessert,\" Keaton says, smacking his lips. “我真的想要些餐後甜點，”基頓咂著嘴唇說。"]}]}]},"slot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（可投入東西的）狹長孔，狹槽；（在一系列事件中為某事安排的）時間，空檔；（組織、團體等中的）位置，職位"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……投入窄孔中，把……放到指定位置；為……安排時間，安置； 與……融洽相處，適應（生活方式）；<非正式>（足球運動員）準確射門進球；鹿的足跡（slots）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>slot</b> is a narrow opening in a machine or container, for example, a hole that you put coins in to make a machine work. (機器或容器上的) 狹槽; 投幣口","examples":["He dropped a coin into the slot and dialled. 他把一枚硬幣投進了那個投幣口，然後撥了號。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>slot</b> in a schedule or programme is a place in it where an activity can take place. 時段","examples":["Visitors can book a time slot a week or more in advance. 來訪者們可以提前一週或一週以上預約一個時段。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"the trail of an animal, esp a deer (尤指鹿的)足跡","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>slot</b> something into something else, or if it <b>slots</b> into it, you put it into a space where it fits. 把…放入狹縫; 放入狹縫","examples":["He was slotting a CD into a CD player. 他正把一張光碟放入光碟播放器中。","The car seat belt slotted into place easily. 那個汽車安全帶很容易就扣好了。"]}]}]},"snare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（捕鳥、獸的）陷阱，羅網；圈套，騙局；（音樂）小軍鼓（snare drum 的簡稱）；（音樂）響絃（繃在小軍鼓下鼓皮上）；（醫學）勒除器，圈套器（用於勒除息肉和增生）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"設陷阱（或羅網、套子）捕捉；誘捕（某人），使……上當；設法獲得（機會、顧客等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>snare</b> is a trap for catching birds or small animals. It consists of a loop of wire or rope which pulls tight around the animal. (捕捉鳥或小動物的) 羅網","examples":["I felt like an animal caught in a snare. 我感到自己像是一頭陷入網羅的野獸。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as a <b>snare</b>, you mean that it is a trap from which it is difficult to escape. 陷阱","examples":["Given data which are free from bias there are further snares to avoid in statistical work. 就算這些資料不帶任何偏見，但是統計工作中還有許多需要避免的陷阱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a set of gut strings wound with wire fitted against the lower drumhead of a snare drum. They produce a rattling sound when the drum is beaten (繃在小軍鼓下面的)響絃","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>snares</b> an animal, they catch it using a snare. 用羅網捕捉","examples":["He'd snared a rabbit earlier in the day. 那天早些時候，他用羅網捕了一隻野兔。"]}]}]},"sneer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"嘲笑，譏諷；鄙視"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘲笑，譏諷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sneer</b> <b>at</b> someone or something, you express your contempt for them by the expression on your face or by what you say. 嘲笑","examples":["Most critics have sneered at the movie, calling it dull and cheaply made. 大多數批評家都嘲笑這部電影，稱其無聊、製作低劣。","\"I don't need any help from you,\" he sneered. “我不需要你的任何幫助，”他嘲笑道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sneer</b> is also a noun. 嘲笑; 譏諷","examples":["Canete's mouth twisted in a contemptuous sneer. 卡內特撇了下嘴，一副蔑視嘲諷的樣子。"]}]}]},"socialist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"支援社會主義的，與社會主義有關的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"社會主義者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Socialist</b> means based on socialism or relating to socialism. 社會主義的","examples":["...members of the ruling Socialist Party. …執政的社會主義黨成員。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>socialist</b> is a person who believes in socialism or who is a member of a socialist party. 社會主義者; 社會主義黨成員","examples":["Esperanto has always been popular among socialists. 世界語在社會主義者中一直很受歡迎。"]}]}]},"sodium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鈉（一種化學元素，符號為 Na）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（發出橙色強光的）鈉光的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sodium</b> is a silvery white chemical element which combines with other chemicals. Salt is a sodium compound. 鈉","examples":["The fish or seafood is heavily salted with pure sodium chloride. 魚或海產品以厚厚的純氯化鈉鹽醃製。"]}]}]},"solidarity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"團結一致；（波蘭的）團結工會（Solidarity）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people show <b>solidarity</b>, they show support for each other or for another group, especially in political or international affairs. 團結一致; 相互支援","examples":["Supporters want to march tomorrow to show solidarity with their leaders. 支持者有意在明天遊行以表現對他們領導的支援。"]}]}]},"socialism":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社會主義，社會主義制度；（馬克思主義理論）社會主義社會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Socialism</b> is a set of political principles whose general aim is to create a system in which everyone has an equal opportunity to benefit from a country's wealth. Under socialism, the country's main industries are usually owned by the state. 社會主義","examples":[]}]}]},"smother":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使窒息，悶死；（用灰等）悶熄，撲滅；抑制，壓抑，忍住；掩蓋；完全覆蓋，厚厚地裹滿；溺愛，過分保護（使人透不過氣）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"窒息，悶死；被抑制"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"窒息狀態；令人窒息的濃煙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>smother</b> a fire, you cover it with something in order to put it out. 把 (火) 悶熄","examples":["The girl's parents were also burned as they tried to smother the flames. 女孩的父母在試圖悶熄火苗時也被燒傷了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>smother</b> someone means to kill them by covering their face with something so that they cannot breathe. 使窒息","examples":["He tried to smother me with a pillow. 他企圖用枕頭悶死我。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Things that <b>smother</b> something cover it completely. 完全覆蓋","examples":["Once the shrubs begin to smother the little plants, we have to move them. 一旦灌木開始把小植物完全覆蓋，我們不得不將它們移走。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>smother</b> someone, you show your love for them too much and protect them too much. 溺愛","examples":["She loved her own children, almost smothering them with love. 她愛自己的孩子，幾乎愛得讓他們透不過氣。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>smother</b> an emotion or a reaction, you control it so that people do not notice it. 壓抑; 抑制","examples":["She tried to smother her anger and help them resolve their conflicts. 她試圖抑制住怒氣，幫助他們解決糾紛。"]}]}]},"sociology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"社會學，社會關係研究"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sociology</b> is the study of society or of the way society is organized. 社會學","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"社會學的","examples":["Psychological and sociological studies were emphasizing the importance of the family. 心理學和社會學研究都在強調家庭的重要性。"]}]}]},"sovereignty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"主權，最高統治權，最高權威；獨立自主；主權國家，自治州"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sovereignty</b> is the power that a country has to govern itself or another country or state. 統治權","examples":["Concern to protect national sovereignty is far from new. 對捍衛國家主權的關注絕不是新話題。"]}]}]},"solitude":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨居，獨處，孤獨；偏僻的地方，無人居住的地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Solitude</b> is the state of being alone, especially when this is peaceful and pleasant. 獨處","examples":["He enjoyed his moments of solitude before the pressures of the day began in earnest. 他很喜歡一天的壓力真正開始前的獨處時刻。"]}]}]},"specialty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專業，專長；特色食品，特產；特產， 專賣店；（律）蓋印的書面合同"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>specialty</b> is the same as a . 專業; 專長","examples":[]}]}]},"span":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"時間跨度，一段時間；（橋或拱的）墩距，跨距；寬度，翼展；範圍，包括的種類；（航海）跨繩；一隊人（或動物）；數值範圍；一掌的長度"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"持續，貫穿；包括（廣大地區），涵蓋（多項內容）；橫跨，跨越；張開手覆蓋（或環繞）；<南非>給（動物）套上軛"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"整潔乾淨的，照管得很好的（spick and span）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>span</b> is the period of time between two dates or events during which something exists, functions, or happens. (兩時間點之間的) 時間段","examples":["The batteries had a life span of six hours. 電池的使用壽命是6小時。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your concentration <b>span</b> or your attention <b>span</b> is the length of time you are able to concentrate on something or be interested in it. (注意力的) 持續時間","examples":["His ability to absorb information was astonishing, but his concentration span was short. 他吸收資訊的能力讓人驚訝，但他的注意力持續時間很短。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>span</b> of something that extends or is spread out sideways is the total width of it from one end to the other. 寬距","examples":["It is a very pretty butterfly, with a 2 inch wing span. 它是一隻非常漂亮的蝴蝶，翅膀張開有2英寸寬。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a team of horses or oxen, esp two matched animals 馬隊或牛隊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>spans</b> a long period of time, it lasts throughout that period of time or relates to that whole period of time. 持續","examples":["His professional career spanned 16 years. 他的職業生涯持續了16年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>spans</b> a range of things, all those things are included in it. 包括","examples":["Bernstein's compositions spanned all aspects of music, from symphonies to musicals. 伯恩斯坦創作的樂曲包括了音樂的所有方面，從交響樂到音樂劇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A bridge or other structure that <b>spans</b> something such as a river or a valley stretches right across it. 橫跨","examples":["Travellers get from one side to the other by walking across a footbridge that spans a little stream. 旅遊者透過一座橫跨小溪的人行橋從一邊走到另一邊。"]}]}]},"spectacular":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"壯觀的，令人驚歎的；驚人的，突如其來的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"壯觀場面，盛大演出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>spectacular</b> is very impressive or dramatic. 壯觀的","examples":["...spectacular views of the Sugar Loaf Mountain. …甜麵包山壯觀的景色。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可觀地","examples":["My turnover increased spectacularly. 我的營業額大幅上升。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spectacular</b> is a show or performance which is very grand and impressive. 盛大的演出","examples":["...a television spectacular. …一場盛大的電視演出。"]}]}]},"spectrum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"範圍，幅度；光譜；波譜，頻譜；餘象"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The spectrum</b> is the range of different colours which is produced when light passes through a glass prism or through a drop of water. A rainbow shows the colours in the spectrum. 光譜","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>spectrum</b> is a range of a particular type of thing. 範圍","examples":["She'd seen his moods range across the emotional spectrum. 她見過他在各種情感間的情緒變化。","Politicians across the political spectrum have denounced the act. 政界圈各派政客都譴責了這種行為。"]}]}]},"spokesman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指男性）發言人，代言人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spokesman</b> is a male spokesperson. 男發言人","examples":["A UN spokesman said that the mission will carry 20 tons of relief supplies. 一位聯合國男發言人說該行動將運送20噸救濟物資。"]}]}]},"spire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（建築）尖塔，尖頂（尤指教堂等建築物頂部向上收尖的結構）；<罕>螺旋，螺旋形結構的一圈；（Spire）人名，德語作施皮雷，法語作斯皮爾"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"像尖頂般向上聳立，向上漸尖"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"給……加塔尖，給……裝尖頂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>spire</b> of a building such as a church is the tall pointed structure on the top. (教堂等建築物的) 尖頂","examples":["...a church spire poking above the trees. …伸出樹梢的教堂尖頂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"any of the coils or turns in a spiral structure (螺旋形結構的)盤管或拐角","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to assume the shape of a spire; point up 猜想(塔尖的形狀); 指向上","examples":[]}]}]},"sphere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（活動、興趣、專業知識的）範圍，領域；球體，球，球形；社會階層；勢力範圍；<文>蒼穹，天，天空；<文>天體；天體外殼；地球儀"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使……成球形；包圍；放入球內"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sphere</b> is an object that is completely round in shape like a ball. 球體","examples":["Because the earth spins, it is not a perfect sphere. 因為地球旋轉，所以它不是個完完全全的球體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>sphere</b> <b>of</b> activity or interest is a particular area of activity or interest. (活動、興趣的) 領域","examples":["...the sphere of international politics. …國際政治領域。"]}]}]},"spike":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"猛增，急升；尖狀物，金屬釘，尖木；（運動鞋上的）鞋釘；釘鞋（spikes）；細高跟鞋（spikes）；（尤指鐵軌上的）道釘，大釘；穗，穗狀花序；（電子）脈衝尖峰；<英，非正式>臨時簡易床位；（排球中的）扣球；<英>票插，紙插；<非正式>皮下注射用的針頭"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"在……中偷偷摻入（烈酒、毒藥或毒品）；給……新增風味，給……增加趣味；迅速提升，急劇增加；（用尖物）刺入，扎入；形成尖狀物，以尖狀物覆蓋；（排球中的）大力扣殺；<美>摔球觸地；棄置（新聞稿）不用，拒絕發表；停止（計劃，任務），制止，毀掉；<史>用大釘堵住火門使槍無用；<非正式>在……中加某種放射性同位素"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spike</b> is a long piece of metal with a sharp point. 長金屬錐","examples":["...a 15-foot wall topped with iron spikes. …頂上裝有長鐵錐的15英尺高的牆。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to add alcohol to (a drink) (向飲料中)加酒","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to hit (a ball) sharply downwards with an overarm motion from the front of one's own court into the opposing court (排球中的)大力扣殺","examples":[]}]}]},"spiral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"螺旋形，螺旋形之物；持續加劇的上升（或下降、惡化）；旋球"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"螺旋式上升（或下降），盤旋上升（或下降）；持續下降，持續惡化；急劇上升"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"螺旋形的；（醫）扭折（骨折的一種）；spiral-bound的簡稱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spiral</b> is a shape which winds around and around, with each curve above or outside the previous one. 螺旋形","examples":["The maze is actually two interlocking spirals. 這個迷宮實際上是兩個連鎖的螺旋體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Spiral</b> is also a noun. 螺旋式運動","examples":["Larks were rising in spirals from the ridge. 雲雀在從山脊上盤旋飛昇。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Spiral</b> is also a noun. 加速上升","examples":["...an inflationary spiral. …一次通脹性的激增。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Spiral</b> is also a noun. 加速下降","examples":["...a spiral of debt. …債務的加劇減少。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Spiral</b> is also an adjective. 螺旋形的","examples":["...a spiral staircase. …一段旋梯。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>spirals</b> or <b>is spiralled</b> somewhere, it grows or moves in a spiral curve. 使…螺旋式生長或移動; 螺旋式生長或移動","examples":["Vines spiralled upward toward the roof. 藤蔓螺旋式向上朝屋頂生長。","The aircraft began spiralling out of control. 那架飛機開始做螺旋式飛行，失去了控制。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an amount or level <b>spirals</b>, it rises quickly and at an increasing rate. 加速上升","examples":["Production costs began to spiral. 生產成本開始加速上漲。","...spiralling health care costs. …加速上漲的各種保健費用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an amount or level <b>spirals</b> downward, it falls quickly and at an increasing rate. 加速下降","examples":["House prices will continue to spiral downwards. 房價將繼續加速下跌。"]}]}]},"spokeswoman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"女發言人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>spokeswoman</b> is a female spokesperson. 女發言人","examples":["A United Nations spokeswoman in New York said the request would be considered. 一位在紐約的聯合國女發言人稱該請求會被予以考慮。"]}]}]},"spouse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"配偶"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"和……結婚"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>spouse</b> is the person they are married to. 配偶","examples":["You, or your spouse, must be at least 60 to participate. 你或你的配偶至少要有60歲才能加入。"]}]}]},"sprawl":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"伸開四肢坐（或躺）；蔓延"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（城市）雜亂無序拓展的地區；四肢攤開的姿勢；隨意擴充套件，蔓延物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sprawl</b> somewhere, you sit or lie down with your legs and arms spread out in a careless way. 伸開四肢坐著; 攤開四肢躺著","examples":["She sprawled on the bed as he had left her, not even moving to cover herself up. 他離開她後，她攤開四肢躺在床上，甚至懶得動動把自己蓋上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a place <b>sprawls</b>, you mean that it covers a large area of land. 延伸","examples":["The State Recreation Area sprawls over 900 acres on the southern tip of Key Biscayne. 州立休閒區佔地九百多英畝，地處基·比斯坎南端。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sprawl out</b> means the same as . 伸開四肢坐著; 攤開四肢躺著","examples":["He would take two aspirin and sprawl out on his bed. 他會吃兩片阿斯匹林，然後攤開四肢躺在床上。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>sprawl</b> to refer to an area where a city has grown outward in an uncontrolled way. (城市的) 無計劃擴張區域","examples":["The whole urban sprawl of Ankara contains over 2.6 million people. 整個安卡拉城區總共容納了260萬以上的人口。"]}]}]},"squad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（專門處理某類犯罪的）警察分隊；運動（代表）隊；（軍隊裡的）班，組；（進行某活動的）小組，隊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……編成班，把……編入班"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>squad</b> is a section of a police force that is responsible for dealing with a particular type of crime. (專門處理某類犯罪的) 警察分隊","examples":["The building was evacuated and the bomb squad called. 那座大樓進行了人員疏散，並通知了拆彈小組。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>squad</b> is a group of players from which a sports team will be chosen. (將從中挑選運動員組隊參賽的) 運動代表隊","examples":["The American squad has pulled out of the four-day basketball tournament. 美國運動代表隊已經退出了為期4天的籃球錦標賽。"]}]}]},"spokesperson":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發言人；代言人"}],"sections":[]},"sponsor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"贊助者，贊助商；（培訓或教育的）資助者；（慈善活動的）捐款者，捐資機構；法案的倡議者；擔保人，保證人；（宗教事宜中的）引領人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"贊助（活動、節目等）； 為慈善活動捐資，為義賽捐款；倡議，提交（法案等）；主辦，促成；縱容；為……擔保"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an organization or an individual <b>sponsors</b> something such as an event or someone's training, they pay some or all of the expenses connected with it, often in order to get publicity for themselves. 贊助 (某事、某人的培訓等)","examples":["Dozens of companies, including Hewlett-Packard, are sponsoring the event. 包括惠普在內的許多公司都在贊助這項賽事。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>sponsor</b> someone who is doing something to raise money for charity, for example trying to walk a certain distance, you agree to give them a sum of money for the charity if they succeed in doing it. 贊助 (為慈善事業募集資金者)","examples":["Please could you sponsor me for my school's campaign for Help the Aged? 請問你們能贊助我開展我校的“幫助老年人”活動嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>sponsor</b> a proposal or suggestion, you officially put it forward and support it. 倡議","examples":["Eight senators sponsored legislation to stop the military funding. 八位參議員倡議立法停撥軍費。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When a country or an organization such as the United Nations <b>sponsors</b> negotiations between countries, it suggests holding the negotiations and organizes them. 提議並組織 (商談)","examples":["Given the strength of pressure on both sides, the superpowers may well have difficulties sponsoring negotiations. 鑑於雙方的強大壓力，超級大國可能很難組織談判。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If one country accuses another of <b>sponsoring</b> attacks on it, they mean that the other country does not do anything to prevent the attacks, and may even encourage them. 縱容","examples":["We have to make the states that sponsor terrorism pay a price. 我們得讓那些縱容恐怖主義的國家付出代價。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If a company or organization <b>sponsors</b> a television programme, they pay to have a special advertisement shown at the beginning and end of the programme, and at each commercial break. 贊助 (電視節目)","examples":["The company plans to sponsor television programmes as part of its marketing strategy. 公司計劃贊助電視節目，以此作為營銷策略之一。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>sponsor</b> is a person or organization that sponsors something or someone. 贊助人; 贊助機構; 倡議人","examples":["Race officials announced a handful of new sponsors on Tuesday. 比賽官員們星期二公佈了幾位新贊助人。"]}]}]},"squash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"壓扁，壓碎；（使）擠進，（把……）塞進；打斷，制止，去除；控制，抑制（情緒）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（軟式）牆網球，壁球；<英>果汁飲料；南瓜屬植物（如南瓜）；擁擠的環境（或處所）；（生）（供顯微鏡觀察用的）軟化組織薄片，壓片；咯吱聲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is squashed</b>, they are pressed or crushed with such force that they become injured or lose their shape. 壓扁; 壓碎","examples":["Robert was lucky to escape with just a broken foot after being squashed against a fence by a car. 羅伯特很幸運，被一輛轎車擠壓到一排柵欄上只折了一隻腳而脫了險。","Whole neighbourhoods have been squashed flat by shelling. 整個的居住區已經被炮火夷為平地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>squash</b> something that is causing you trouble, you put a stop to it, often by force. 鎮壓","examples":["The troops would stay in position to squash the first murmur of trouble. 該部隊將嚴陣以待，一有騷亂聲音即進行鎮壓。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things are <b>squashed into</b> a place, they are put or pushed into a place where there is not enough room for them to be. 擠進去了的","examples":["There were 2,000 people squashed into her recent show. 有2千人擠進了她最近的演出現場。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>squash</b> is one of a family of vegetables that have thick skin and soft or firm flesh inside. 瓜類蔬菜","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Squash</b> is a game in which two players hit a small rubber ball against the walls of a court using rackets. 壁球","examples":["I also play squash. 我也玩壁球。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a still drink made from fruit juice or fruit syrup diluted with water 果汁飲料","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that getting a number of people into a small space is <b>a squash</b>, you mean that it is only just possible for them all to get into it. 塞滿","examples":["It was a squash in the car with five of them. 他們五個人把這小車全部塞滿。"]}]}]},"stability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"穩定（性），穩固（性）；堅定，恆心"}],"sections":[]},"stammer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"口吃，結結巴巴地說"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"結巴，口吃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stammer</b>, you speak with difficulty, hesitating and repeating words or sounds. 結結巴巴地說; 口吃","examples":["Five percent of children stammer at some point. 5%的兒童在某個時候都會口吃。","\"Forgive me,\" I stammered. “原諒我吧，”我結結巴巴地說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"口吃","examples":["Of all speech impediments stammering is probably the most embarrassing. 在所有語言障礙中，口吃可能是最讓人尷尬的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who has a <b>stammer</b> tends to stammer when they speak. 口吃","examples":["A speech therapist cured his stammer. 一位語言矯治專家治好了他的口吃。"]}]}]},"stapler":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訂書機；主要商品批發商；把羊毛分級的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stapler</b> is a device used for putting staples into sheets of paper. 訂書機","examples":[]}]}]},"starch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"澱粉，含澱粉的食物；（漿衣服的）漿粉，澱粉漿；（喻）（風格、性格上的）古板，刻板，拘謹"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……上漿；<美，非正式>（拳擊手）擊倒對手"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Starch</b> is a substance that is found in foods such as bread, potatoes, pasta, and rice and gives you energy. 澱粉","examples":["She reorganized her eating so that she was taking more fruit and vegetables and less starch, salt, and fat. 她重新調整了自己的飲食，在多吃水果蔬菜，少食用澱粉、鹽和脂肪。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Starch</b> is a substance that is used for making cloth stiffer, especially cotton and linen. (用於使布料挺直的) 漿粉","examples":["He never puts enough starch in my shirts. 他從不給我的襯衫上足夠的漿粉。"]}]}]},"staple":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某國的）主要產品，支柱產品；主食；主要部份，重要內容；<史>（特定商品的）貿易中心；訂書釘；U 形釘；（棉花、羊毛的）纖維（就其長度和細度而言）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要生產的，大量生產的；主要的，常用的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用訂書釘訂住；把……分級"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>staple</b> food, product, or activity is one that is basic and important in people's everyday lives. 基本的; 主要的 (食物、產品、活動)","examples":["Rice is the staple food of more than half the world's population. 大米是世界上半數以上人口的主食。","The Chinese also eat a type of pasta as part of their staple diet. 中國人也以一種麵食作為他們的部分主食。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Staple</b> is also a noun. 主食; 主要產品; 主要活動","examples":["Fish is a staple in the diet of many Africans. 魚是許多非洲人飲食中的主食。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>staple</b> is something that forms an important part of something else. 重要部分","examples":["Political reporting has become a staple of American journalism. 政治報道已經成為美國新聞業的一個重要內容。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Staples</b> are small pieces of bent wire that are used mainly for holding sheets of paper together firmly. You put the staples into the paper using a device called a stapler. 訂書釘","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>staple</b> something, you fasten it to something else or fix it in place using staples. 用訂書釘訂住","examples":["Staple some sheets of paper together into a book. 用訂書釘把一些紙張訂成一本。"]}]}]},"stationery":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（通常有配套信封的）信紙，信箋；文具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stationery</b> is paper, envelopes, and other materials or equipment used for writing. 文具","examples":["...envelopes and other office stationery. …信封及其他辦公文具。"]}]}]},"starvation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"飢餓，捱餓，餓死"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Starvation</b> is extreme suffering or death, caused by lack of food. 飢餓; 餓死","examples":["Over three hundred people have died of starvation since the beginning of the year. 自那年年初開始，已有三百多人餓死了。"]}]}]},"stature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"名望，聲望；身高"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>stature</b> is their height. 身高","examples":["It's more than his physical stature that makes him remarkable. 不單單是他的身高使他氣宇非凡。","Mother was of very small stature, barely five feet tall. 母親身材嬌小，僅有5英尺高。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>stature</b> of a person is the importance and reputation that they have. 名望","examples":["Who can deny his stature as the world's greatest cellist? 誰能否認他是世界上最偉大的大提琴演奏家？"]}]}]},"stimulus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺激（物）, 促進因素；（使生物產生反應的）刺激，刺激物；刺激性，趣味性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stimulus</b> is something that encourages activity in people or things. 刺激物","examples":["Interest rates could fall soon and be a stimulus to the U.S. economy. 利率可能很快會下降，從而刺激美國經濟。"]}]}]},"stimulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"刺激，激勵，興奮作用"}],"sections":[]},"stalk":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（植物的）莖，稈；（動物的）肉柄，肉莖；柄；（車輛）（轉向柱上控制指示儀、燈光等的）手柄；悄悄追蹤；高視闊步"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"偷偷接近，潛近；跟蹤，盯梢；怒衝衝地走，趾高氣揚地走；令人厭惡地穿過，威脅地透過；<文>（不好的氣氛）籠罩，蔓延"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>stalk</b> of a flower, leaf, or fruit is the thin part that joins it to the plant or tree. (花、葉、果實與植株相連的) 柄; 梗","examples":["A single pale blue flower grows up from each joint on a long stalk. 一根長梗的每個節上都長出了一朵淡藍色的花。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>stalk</b> a person or a wild animal, you follow them quietly in order to kill them, catch them, or observe them carefully. 悄悄跟蹤","examples":["He stalks his victims like a hunter after a deer. 他像獵人跟蹤鹿一樣悄悄跟蹤他的受害者們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>stalks</b> someone else, especially a famous person or a person they used to have a relationship with, they keep following them or contacting them in an annoying and frightening way. 騷擾; 糾纏","examples":["Even after their divorce he continued to stalk and threaten her. 甚至在他們離婚後，他繼續糾纏並恐嚇她。"]}]}]},"substitution":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代替，替換；代替物；（數） 置換"}],"sections":[]},"subscription":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（雜誌等的）訂閱費，（服務的）使用者費；訂閱，訂購； <英>（組織或俱樂部的）會費，捐贈款；集體資助，集體捐助；（對組織或專案的）捐贈協議，認捐書；<正式>（檔案末尾的）簽名，附註；季票（文化活動的季票）；（股票的）認購（協議）；透過預訂來全部或部分支付出版費用的方法"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（電視或電影片道）付費的，收費的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>subscription</b> is an amount of money that you pay regularly in order to belong to an organization, to help a charity or campaign, or to receive copies of a magazine or newspaper. 會員費; 捐贈款; 徵訂費","examples":["You can become a member by paying the yearly subscription. 你透過支付年度會員費可以成為一名會員。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Subscription</b> television is television that you can watch only if you pay a subscription. A <b>subscription</b> channel is a channel that you can watch only if you pay a subscription. (電視或頻道) 付費的","examples":["Premiere, a subscription channel which began in 1991, shows live football covering the top two divisions. 始於1991年的一個付費頻道實況轉播兩大頂級足球賽。"]}]}]},"subordinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"從屬的，下級的；次要的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"部屬，下級；從屬，次要"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使從屬於，使處於次要地位；使隸屬，使服從"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is your <b>subordinate</b>, they have a less important position than you in the organization that you both work for. 下級","examples":["Haig tended not to seek guidance from subordinates. 黑格不想向下屬們尋求指導。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"從屬; 次要","examples":["...the social subordination of women. …婦女們的社會從屬地位。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>subordinate</b> <b>to</b> you has a less important position than you and has to obey you. 下級的","examples":["Sixty of his subordinate officers followed his example. 他的60個下級官員都以他為榜樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>subordinate</b> <b>to</b> something else is less important than the other thing. 次要的; 從屬的","examples":["It was an art in which words were subordinate to images. 它是一種語言比影象次要的藝術。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>subordinate</b> something <b>to</b> another thing, you regard it or treat it as less important than the other thing. 使從屬於; 把…列於次要地位","examples":["He was both willing and able to subordinate all else to this aim. 他既願意也能夠讓別的一切從屬於這個目標。"]}]}]},"steamer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"汽船，大輪船；汽鍋，蒸鍋；<非正式>溼式潛水服；結幫搶劫者，團伙搶劫者；<美> 沙海螂；蒸汽熨斗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>steamer</b> is a ship that has an engine powered by steam. 汽輪","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>steamer</b> is a special container used for steaming food such as vegetables and fish. 蒸鍋","examples":[]}]}]},"succession":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"連續不斷的人（物）；繼任，繼承，繼承權；交替，更迭；（地質）（地層的）次序，生長順序"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>succession</b> <b>of</b> things of the same kind is a number of them that exist or happen one after the other. 一連串","examples":["Adams took a succession of jobs which have stood him in good stead. 亞當斯做了一連串對他很有利的工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Succession</b> is the act or right of being the next person to have an important job or position. 繼任; 繼任權","examples":["She is now seventh in line of succession to the throne. 她目前排在王位繼任順序的第7位。"]}]}]},"stock":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"現貨，存貨；儲備物，備用物；股本，資本；股份，股票；<英>公債，公債券；家畜，牲畜；種族，家系；高湯，原湯；手足枷（stocks）；柄，槍托；名聲，聲望；紫羅蘭；接穗，砧木；根莖，根狀莖；<美>保留劇目輪演劇團；信任，相信；鐵路上使用的所有車輛；（膠捲）原片；發剩下的牌；（商品的）原材料；錨杆；主軸臺，主軸箱（headstock 的簡寫）；尾架，尾座（tailstock 的簡寫）；白色領結，白色領帶；（牧師衣領下系的）黑色領帶；船臺（stocks）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"備有，存有；擺滿，供應；為（槍等火器）裝槍托；出新芽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"老一套的，陳腐的；（商店）庫存的，常備的；（有關）電影資料鏡頭的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stocks</b> are shares in the ownership of a company, or investments on which a fixed amount of interest will be paid. 股票; 證券","examples":["...the buying and selling of stocks and shares. …證券和股票的買賣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A company's <b>stock</b> is the amount of money which the company has through selling shares. (公司的) 股票價值","examples":["Two years later, when Compaq went public, their stock was valued at $38 million. 兩年後康柏公司上市時，他們的股票價值為3800萬美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A shop's <b>stock</b> is the total amount of goods which it has available to sell. 存貨","examples":["When a nearby shop burned down, our stock was ruined by smoke. 附近一家商店被燒成灰燼，我們的存貨也被濃煙燻壞了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you have a <b>stock</b> <b>of</b> things, you have a supply of them stored in a place ready to be used. 儲備","examples":["I keep a stock of cassette tapes describing various relaxation techniques. 我儲藏著一些講述各種放鬆技巧的盒式磁帶。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"<b>Stock</b> is a liquid, usually made by boiling meat, bones, or vegetables in water, that is used to give flavour to soups and sauces. (以肉、骨頭或蔬菜煮成的) 高湯","examples":["Finally, add the beef stock. 最後，加入牛肉高湯。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a shop <b>stocks</b> particular products, it keeps a supply of them to sell. 有…存貨","examples":["The shop stocks everything from cigarettes to recycled paper. 該商店的存貨包括香菸和再生紙等各種商品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>stock</b> something such as a cupboard, shelf, or room, you fill it with food or other things. 給…裝滿","examples":["I worked stocking shelves in a grocery shop. 我在一家雜貨店工作，給貨架上貨。","Some families stocked their cellars with food and water. 有些家庭在地窖裡裝滿食物和水。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Stock up</b> means the same as . 給…裝滿","examples":["I had to stock the boat up with food. 我不得不給小船裝滿食品。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stock</b> answer, expression, or way of doing something is one that is very commonly used, especially because people cannot be bothered to think of something new. (回答、表達或做事方式) 老一套的","examples":["My boss had a stock response – \"If it ain't broke, don't fix it!\" 我的老闆是老一套的回答–“沒壞的話就別修了！”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If goods are <b>in stock</b>, a shop has them available to sell. If they are <b>out of stock</b>, it does not. 有貨/缺貨","examples":["Check that your size is in stock. 查查你的尺碼是不是有貨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>take stock</b>, you pause to think about all the aspects of a situation or event before deciding what to do next. 估量","examples":["It was time to take stock of the situation. 是估量形勢的時候了。"]}]}]},"superiority":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"優越，優勢；優越感，驕傲自大"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one side in a war or conflict has <b>superiority</b>, it has an advantage over its enemy, for example because it has more soldiers or better equipment. 優勢","examples":["We have air superiority. 我們有空中優勢。"]}]}]},"successor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"繼承者，接替的事物；（組織、機器等的）接替物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>successor</b> is the person who takes their job after they have left. 繼任者","examples":["He set out several principles that he hopes will guide his successors. 他制定出了幾條原則,希望能指導其繼任者。"]}]}]},"suite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"套房，套間；一套傢俱；組曲；（程式）組，套；一套產品；（君主或高官的）（一批）隨員；（地質）系列礦石（或岩石、化石）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>suite</b> is a set of rooms in a hotel or other building. 套房","examples":["They had a fabulous time during their week in a suite at the Paris Hilton. 他們在巴黎希爾頓酒店的套房裡度過了非常愉快的一週。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>suite</b> is a set of matching furniture. 一套傢俱","examples":["...a three-piece suite. …一組三件套傢俱。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A bathroom <b>suite</b> is a matching bathtub, sink, and toilet. (浴室) 套件","examples":["...the horrible pink suite in the bathroom. …浴室裡那組難看的粉紅色套件。"]}]}]},"stunt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指電影中的）特技表演；噱頭，作秀；逞英雄，做愚蠢（有點危險）的事"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻礙……的成長（發育），妨礙發展；表演絕技"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>stunt</b> is something interesting that is done in order to attract attention and get publicity for the person or company responsible for it. 引人注目的噱頭","examples":["In a bold promotional stunt for the movie, he smashed his car into a passing truck. 在那部影片大膽的宣傳噱頭中，他把自己的汽車撞向一輛過路的卡車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>stunt</b> is a dangerous and exciting piece of action in a movie. (電影中的) 特技動作","examples":["Sean Connery insisted on living dangerously for his new film by performing his own stunts. 肖恩·康納利堅持透過為他的新影片表演他自己的特技動作而冒險。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>stunts</b> the growth or development of a person or thing, it prevents it from growing or developing as much as it should. 阻礙","examples":["The heart condition had stunted his growth a bit. 心臟病已經有點兒阻礙他的發育。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受阻礙的","examples":["Damage may result in stunted growth and sometimes death of the plant. 損害會導致植物生長受阻，有時還會導致死亡。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to perform a stunt or stunts 表演雜技","examples":[]}]}]},"supervision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"監督，管理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supervision</b> is the supervising of people, activities, or places. 監督","examples":["A toddler requires close supervision and firm control at all times. 剛學走路的孩子需要時刻認真照看，牢牢管住。"]}]}]},"supplement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"補充物，增補物；營養片劑，補品；補助，補貼；額外服務費用；（報紙或雜誌的）副刊，增刊；（書籍的）補編，附錄；（幾何）補角"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"增加，增補"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>supplement</b> something, you add something to it in order to improve it. 補充","examples":["...people doing extra jobs outside their regular jobs to supplement their incomes. …在固定工作之餘做兼職以增加收入的人們。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supplement</b> is also a noun. 補充","examples":["Business sponsorship must be a supplement to, not a substitute for, public funding. 商業贊助必須是公共資助的補充而非替代物。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>supplement</b> is a pill that you take or a special kind of food that you eat in order to improve your health. 養生片劑","examples":["...a multiple vitamin and mineral supplement. …一種複合維生素和礦物質養生片劑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>supplement</b> is a separate part of a magazine or newspaper, often dealing with a particular topic. (報紙或雜誌的) 增刊","examples":["...a special supplement to a monthly financial magazine. …一份金融月刊的特別增刊。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>supplement</b> <b>to</b> a book is an additional section, written some time after the main text and published either at the end of the book or separately. (書籍的) 附錄; 補編","examples":["...the supplement to the Encyclopedia Britannica. …《大不列顛百科全書》補編。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>supplement</b> is an extra amount of money that you pay in order to obtain special facilities or services, for example when you are travelling or staying at a hotel. (旅行或住賓館等所付的) 額外費用","examples":["If you are travelling alone, the single room supplement is $25 a night. 如果你獨自一人旅行，單人間的額外費用是每晚$25。"]}]}]},"suspense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"焦慮，懸念，興奮；<法律> 暫停，權利中止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Suspense</b> is a state of excitement or anxiety about something that is going to happen very soon, for example about some news that you are waiting to hear. 懸念","examples":["The suspense over the two remaining hostages ended last night when the police discovered the bullet ridden bodies. 有關剩下兩名人質的懸念在昨晚警方發現佈滿彈孔的屍體後結束了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>keep</b> or <b>leave</b> someone <b>in suspense</b>, you deliberately delay telling them something that they are very eager to know about. 讓某人心懸著","examples":["Keppler kept all his men in suspense until that morning before announcing which two would be going. 科普勒直到那天早上宣佈哪兩個人要走之前讓他所有的手下心懸在空中。"]}]}]},"surplus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過剩，剩餘，過剩量；盈餘，順差；超淨資產"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過剩的，剩餘的，多餘的；（商店）出售剩餘（或過時的）軍用品的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"甩賣，變賣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>surplus</b> <b>of</b> something, there is more than is needed. 過剩","examples":["...countries where there is a surplus of labour. …勞動力過剩的國家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a country has a trade <b>surplus</b>, it exports more than it imports. 順差","examples":["Japan's annual trade surplus is in the region of 100 billion dollars. 日本每年的貿易順差約有一千億美元。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a government has a budget <b>surplus</b>, it has spent less than it received in taxes. 盈餘","examples":["Norway's budget surplus has fallen from 5.9% in 1986 to an expected 0.1% this year. 挪威的預算盈餘已從1986年的5.9%下降到今年預計的0.1%。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Surplus</b> is used to describe something that is extra or that is more than is needed. 過剩的; 多餘的","examples":["Few people have large sums of surplus cash. 幾乎沒人有大筆的閒錢。","I sell my surplus birds to a local pet shop. 我把我多餘的鳥賣給一家當地的寵物店。"]}]}]},"suspension":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暫停，中止；暫令停職（或停學、停賽等）；（車輛的）懸架，減震裝置；懸浮液，懸膠體；（樂）延留音"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>suspension</b> of something is the act of delaying or stopping it for a while or until a decision is made about it. 延緩; 暫停","examples":["There's been a temporary suspension of flights out of LA. 從洛杉磯起飛的飛機已經暫停。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>suspension</b> is their removal from a job or position for a period of time or until a decision is made about them. 停職","examples":["The minister warned that any civil servant not at his desk faced immediate suspension. 那位部長警告說任何擅自離崗的公務員面臨著立即停職。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A vehicle's <b>suspension</b> consists of the springs and other devices attached to the wheels, which give a smooth ride over uneven ground. (車輛減震的) 懸架","examples":["...the only small car with independent front suspension. …惟一的一輛帶有獨立前懸架的小汽車。"]}]}]},"symmetry":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"對稱（性）；相似，相等；（物理，數） 對稱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that has <b>symmetry</b> is symmetrical in shape, design, or structure. 對稱","examples":["...the incredible beauty and symmetry of a snowflake. …雪花令人難以置信的美麗和對稱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Symmetry</b> in a relationship or agreement is the fact of both sides giving and receiving an equal amount. (關係或協議中雙方) 平衡; 均等","examples":["The superpowers pledged to maintain symmetry in their arms shipments. 這些超級大國承諾要在其武器運載上保持數量相等。"]}]}]},"synonym":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同義詞；代名詞，換喻詞；（分類學中的）同物異名"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>synonym</b> is a word or expression which means the same as another word or expression. 同義詞","examples":["The term \"industrial democracy\" is often used as a synonym for worker participation. “工業民主”這一詞語常被用作“工人參與”的同義詞。"]}]}]},"swap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"交換，交易； 用……替換，把……換成；交換（工作或崗位）； 交流（各自的經歷、想法等）；停下（手頭的事）改做"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"交易，交換；交易物，交換物；交換工作；（財政）換期，互惠信貸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>swap</b> something with someone, you give it to them and receive a different thing in exchange. 交換","examples":["Next week they will swap places and will repeat the switch weekly. 下週他們將互換位置，以後將每週換一次。","I know a sculptor who swaps her pieces for drawings by a well-known artist. 我知道有個雕塑家用她自己的作品去換一位著名畫家的畫作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Swap</b> is also a noun. 交換","examples":["Over the long term, a swap of some kind is clearly in the public interest. 從長遠看，有點交換顯然是為了公共利益。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>swap</b> one thing <b>for</b> another, you remove the first thing and replace it with the second, or you stop doing the first thing and start doing the second. 調換","examples":["Despite the heat, he'd swapped his overalls for a suit and tie. 儘管天氣炎熱，他還是把他的工裝褲換成了西裝和領帶。","He has swapped his hectic rock star's lifestyle for that of a country gentleman. 他已放棄緊張忙碌的搖滾明星的生活，改做鄉村紳士。"]}]}]},"symptom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（醫） 症狀；（大問題的）跡象，徵兆，徵候"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>symptom</b> of an illness is something wrong with your body or mind that is a sign of the illness. 症狀","examples":["One of the most common symptoms of schizophrenia is hearing imaginary voices. 精神分裂症最常見的症狀之一是幻聽。","...patients with flu symptoms. …有流感症狀的病人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>symptom</b> <b>of</b> a bad situation is something that happens which is considered to be a sign of this situation. 徵兆","examples":["Your problem with keeping boyfriends is just a symptom of a larger problem: making and keeping friends. 你無法留住男友的問題只是一個更大的問題的徵兆：結交朋友並與其維持關係。"]}]}]},"tact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"得體，乖巧，機敏；鑑賞力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tact</b> is the ability to avoid upsetting or offending people by being careful not to say or do things that would hurt their feelings. 得體","examples":["Her tact and intuition never failed. 她的得體和直覺從不出錯。"]}]}]},"synthetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合成的，人造的；（感情，行動）不誠懇的，虛假的；（語言）綜合型的；（命題）綜合的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"合成物，合成纖維（織物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Synthetic</b> products are made from chemicals or artificial substances rather than from natural ones. 合成的","examples":["Boots made from synthetic materials can usually be washed in a machine. 用合成材料做成的靴子通常可以在機器裡洗。"]}]}]},"tariff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（政府對進出口貨物徵收的）關稅，關稅表；（旅館、飯店或服務公司的）價目表，收費表；<英，法律>量刑標準"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"按稅率定……的價格；徵收關稅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tariff</b> is a tax that a government collects on goods coming into a country. (政府對進口貨物徵收的) 關稅","examples":["America wants to eliminate tariffs on items such as electronics. 美國想要取消電子類產品的關稅。"]}]}]},"tactic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"策略，手法；戰術，兵法（tactics）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"按順序的，依次排列的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tactics</b> are the methods that you choose to use in order to achieve what you want in a particular situation. 戰術","examples":["The rebels would still be able to use guerrilla tactics to make the country ungovernable. 反叛者仍然可以用游擊戰術使國家難以統治。"]}]}]},"temperament":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氣質，性格；（性情）暴躁，喜怒無常；調（音）律（在平均律中，8度音階包含有12個均等的半音程）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>temperament</b> is your basic nature, especially as it is shown in the way that you react to situations or to other people. 性格","examples":["His impulsive temperament regularly got him into difficulties. 他容易衝動的性格經常使他陷入困境。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Temperament</b> is the tendency to behave in an uncontrolled, bad-tempered, or unreasonable way. 喜怒無常的性情","examples":["Some of the models were given to fits of temperament. 模特中有些人喜怒無常。"]}]}]},"tempest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴風雨；騷動；動亂"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使狂怒；擾亂，使激動"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"小題大作；起大風暴"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Tempest）人名；（英）坦皮斯特"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tempest</b> is a very violent storm. 暴風雨","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a situation in which people are very angry or excited as a <b>tempest</b>. 風波; 暴動","examples":["I hadn't foreseen the tempest my request would cause. 我沒有想到我的請求會帶來這麼大一場風波。"]}]}]},"textile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"紡織物，織物；紡織業（textiles）；<非正式>著衣者，非自然主義者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"紡織的；<非正式>非自然主義者的，限於著衣者的（裸體主義者用語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Textiles</b> are types of cloth or fabric, especially ones that have been woven. 紡織品","examples":["...decorative textiles for the home. …家用的裝飾性紡織品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Textiles</b> are the industries concerned with the manufacture of cloth. 紡織業","examples":["Another 75,000 jobs will be lost in textiles and clothing. 紡織業和製衣業又將失去7.5萬個就業機會。"]}]}]},"theft":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"偷竊，盜竊；盜竊罪"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Theft</b> is the crime of stealing. 盜竊","examples":["Over the last decade, auto theft has increased by over 56 percent. 過去的10年來汽車盜竊案上升了56％以上。"]}]}]},"texture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"質地，紋理；口感；（音樂或文學的）諧和統一感，神韻"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（織物、牆面等）具浮凸結構（或特徵）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>texture</b> of something is the way that it feels when you touch it, for example, how smooth or rough it is. 手感","examples":["It is used in moisturizers to give them a wonderfully silky texture. 它被用於各種保溼霜中，使之產生絲般的美妙手感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>texture</b> of something, especially food or soil, is its structure, for example, whether it is light with lots of holes, or very heavy and solid. (尤指食品、土壤等的) 結構","examples":["Matured over 18 months, this cheese has an open, crumbly texture with a strong flavour. 這種乳酪18個月後發酵成熟，氣孔多，組織鬆脆，味道濃郁。"]}]}]},"therapist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"治療專家；心理治療師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>therapist</b> is a person who is skilled in a particular type of therapy, especially psychotherapy. (尤指心理療法的) 治療師","examples":["My therapist helped me to deal with my anger. 我的治療師幫我消除怒氣。"]}]}]},"therapy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"治療，療法；心理治療；（對身心健康）有裨益的活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Therapy</b> is the process or talking to a trained counsellor about your emotional and mental problems and your relationships in order to understand and improve the way you feel and behave. 心理治療","examples":["Children may need therapy to help them deal with grief and death. 孩子可能需要心理治療來幫助他們應對悲傷和死亡。","Since I've been in therapy, I've grown to be a better husband and father. 自從我接受心理治療後，我成了個更稱職的丈夫和父親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Therapy</b> or a <b>therapy</b> is a treatment for a particular illness or condition. (針對某種病情的) 治療","examples":["...hormonal therapies. …激素療法。"]}]}]},"thermometer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"溫度計，寒暑表，體溫計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>thermometer</b> is an instrument for measuring temperature. It usually consists of a narrow glass tube containing a thin column of a liquid which rises and falls as the temperature rises and falls. 溫度計","examples":[]}]}]},"thrift":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"節約，節儉；海石竹；<美>儲蓄機構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thrift</b> is the quality and practice of being careful with money and not wasting things. 節儉","examples":["They were rightly praised for their thrift and enterprise. 他們因勤儉節約和開創精神而受到了應得的表揚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>thrift</b> or a <b>thrift institution</b> is a kind of savings bank. 某種儲蓄銀行","examples":[]}]}]},"throb":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（身體部位）抽痛，抽搐，陣痛；（有規律地）抽動；（心臟、脈搏或機器等）有節奏地跳動，搏動，震動；（場所等）充滿活力，熱鬧"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（強烈有規律的）跳動，悸動，搏動；抽痛，抽搐，陣痛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If part of your body <b>throbs</b>, you feel a series of strong and usually painful beats there. 陣痛","examples":["His head throbbed. 他的頭一陣陣地痛。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>throbs</b>, it vibrates and makes a steady noise. (有規律地) 震動作響","examples":["The engines throbbed. 發動機轟隆隆地震動。"]}]}]},"tornado":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"龍捲風，大旋風；極具破壞力的人（或物），情感火爆的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tornado</b> is a violent wind storm consisting of a tall column of air which spins around very fast and causes a lot of damage. 龍捲風","examples":[]}]}]},"threshold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"門檻，門口；閾，界，起始點；開端，起點，入門；機場跑道入口，跑道頭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>threshold</b> of a building or room is the floor in the doorway, or the doorway itself. 門口","examples":["He stopped at the threshold of the bedroom. 他在臥室門口停了下來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>threshold</b> is an amount, level, or limit on a scale. When the <b>threshold</b> is reached, something else happens or changes. 界限; 臨界點","examples":["Moss has a high threshold for pain and a history of fast healing. 莫斯的忍痛力很強，而且有迅速癒合的經歷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the threshold of</b> something exciting or new, you are about to experience it. 即將經歷","examples":["We are on the threshold of a new era in astronomy. 我們將邁入天文學的新時代。"]}]}]},"toll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（道路、橋樑等的）通行費；<美>長途電話費；（事故、災難、戰爭等的）傷亡人數；嚴重的不良影響；（緩慢的）鐘聲"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（緩慢地）敲（鍾），鳴（鍾）；鳴鐘告知；收取（橋樑或道路的）通行費"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a bell <b>tolls</b> or when someone <b>tolls</b> it, it rings slowly and repeatedly, often as a sign that someone has died. 敲 (常指喪鐘); (常指喪鐘) 鳴響","examples":["Church bells tolled and black flags fluttered. 教堂喪鐘敲響了，黑旗飄動著。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toll</b> is a sum of money that you have to pay in order to use a particular bridge or road. (橋樑或道路的) 通行費","examples":["You can pay a toll to drive on Pike's Peak Highway or relax and take the Pike's Peak Cog Railway. 你可以付通行費開車上派克斯峰公路，或者放鬆一下，乘坐派克斯峰齒軌式火車。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>toll</b> road or <b>toll</b> bridge is a road or bridge that you have to pay to use. (道路或橋樑) 收費","examples":["Most people who drive the toll roads don't use them every day. 大部分開車上收費公路的人不是每天都走公路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>toll</b> is a total number of deaths, accidents, or disasters that occur in a particular period of time. (死亡、事故或災難的) 總數","examples":["There are fears that the casualty toll may be higher. 人們擔心傷亡人數可能會更多。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something <b>takes</b> its <b>toll</b> or <b>takes a heavy toll</b>, you mean that it has a bad effect or causes a lot of suffering. 造成壞影響 (或痛苦)","examples":["Winter takes its toll on your health. 冬季影響你的健康。"]}]}]},"trait":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人的個性的）特徵，特點；遺傳特徵；一點，少許"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trait</b> is a particular characteristic, quality, or tendency that someone or something has. 特徵","examples":["The study found that some alcoholics had clear personality traits showing up early in childhood. 這項研究發現一些酗酒者早在孩童時就表現出明顯的個性特徵。"]}]}]},"transaction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交易，買賣，業務；（學術團體會議的）議事錄，公報；（人與人之間的）交流，相互影響；事務（元），事項"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>transaction</b> is a piece of business, for example, an act of buying or selling something. 交易","examples":["The transaction is completed by payment of the fee. 交易在支付費用之後就完成了。"]}]}]},"transcript":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文字記錄，抄本，文字本；<美>成績單；（生化）轉錄本，轉錄物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>transcript</b> <b>of</b> a conversation or speech is a written text of it, based on a recording or notes. (根據錄音或筆記整理的) 文字本","examples":["A transcript of this PBS programme is available through our website, pbs.com. 這個公共廣播公司節目的文字本可透過我們的網址查閱。"]}]}]},"tranquilizer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鎮定劑，鎮靜劑，安定藥；使鎮定的人或物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tranquilizer</b> is a drug that makes people feel calmer or less anxious. Tranquilizers are sometimes used to make people or animals become sleepy or unconscious. 鎮靜劑","examples":["If a tranquilizer is prescribed, be sure your physician informs you of its possible side effects, such as addiction. 如果開了鎮靜劑，一定要讓醫生告訴你它可能帶來的副作用，例如上癮。"]}]}]},"transistor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"電晶體；電晶體收音機（transistor radio）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>transistor</b> is a small electronic part in something such as a television or radio, which controls the flow of electricity. 電晶體","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>transistor</b> or a <b>transistor radio</b> is a small portable radio. 電晶體收音機","examples":[]}]}]},"transformation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（徹底或重大的）改觀，變化，轉變；（用於南非）民主改革；舞臺場景的突變；（動物生命週期中的）變態；（物理）嬗變，核的轉換；（數，邏）變換；（語言學）轉換；（生）遺傳轉化；（生）細胞轉化"}],"sections":[]},"transit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運輸，運送；<美>交通運輸系統；透過，經過；（天文）凌日；（天文）中天；（占星）凌；（商標）（尤指用於運貨的）“全順”汽車（Transit）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"經過，穿過；（天文）（行星等天體）經過（另一天體、子午線）；（占星）（行星等天體）經過（黃道十二宮之一、住宅或星圖區域）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Transit</b> is the carrying of goods or people by vehicle from one place to another. 運輸","examples":["During their talks, the two presidents discussed the transit of goods between the two countries. 在會談中，兩位總統討論了兩國之間貨物的運輸。","...a transit time of about 42 minutes. …大約42分鐘的運輸時間。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or things are <b>in transit</b>, they are travelling or being taken from one place to another. 在途中; 在被運送中","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>transit</b> area is an area where people wait or where goods are kept between different stages of a journey. 中轉的 (地方)","examples":["...refugees arriving at the two transit camps. …到達兩個中轉難民營的難民。"]}]}]},"trauma":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"痛苦經歷，挫折；精神創傷，心理創傷；損傷，外傷；不安，震驚，痛苦"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trauma</b> is a very severe shock or very upsetting experience, which may cause psychological damage. (精神上的) 創傷; 痛苦經歷","examples":["I'd been through the trauma of losing a house. 我已經歷過失去房子的痛苦。"]}]}]},"transition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過渡，轉變；（分子生物）轉換；（樂）臨時轉調；（物理）躍遷，轉變"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"轉變，過渡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Transition</b> is the process in which something changes from one state to another. 轉型","examples":["The transition from a dictatorship to a multi-party democracy is proving to be difficult. 從專政國家到多黨民主國家的轉型證明是很艱難的。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>transitions</b> <b>from</b> one state or activity to another, they move gradually from one to the other. (逐漸地) 轉向","examples":["Most of the discussion was on what needed to be done now as we transitioned from the security issues to the challenging economic issues. 大多數討論都集中在目前需要做什麼，因為我們已從安全問題逐漸轉到具有挑戰性的經濟問題上。"]}]}]},"transplant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"移植（器官、皮膚等）；（使）遷移，（使）移居；移栽，移植（植物）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（器官、皮膚等的）移植（手術）；移植的器官，移植物；移居者，遷居者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>transplant</b> is a medical operation in which a part of a person's body is replaced because it is diseased. (器官) 移植","examples":["He was recovering from a heart transplant operation. 他正從心臟移植手術中康復。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If doctors <b>transplant</b> an organ such as a heart or a kidney, they use it to replace a patient's diseased organ. 移植","examples":["The operation to transplant a kidney is now fairly routine. 移植腎臟的手術如今相當常見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>transplant</b> a plant, person, or thing means to move them to a different place. 移種; 轉移","examples":["I have to transplant the begonias. 我得移種那些秋海棠。"]}]}]},"transmission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（無線電、電視等訊號的）播送，傳送；（電臺或電視等的）資訊，廣播；傳遞，傳播，傳染；（車輛的）傳動裝置，變速器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>transmission</b> of something is the passing or sending of it to a different person or place. 傳送; 傳播","examples":["Heterosexual contact is responsible for the bulk of HIV transmission. 異性間的性接觸是造成大多數艾滋病病毒傳播的原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>transmission</b> of television or radio programmes is the broadcasting of them. (電視或廣播節目的) 播送","examples":["The transmission of the programme was brought forward due to its unexpected topicality. 該節目提前播送是因有出人意料的熱門話題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>transmission</b> is a broadcast. 廣播節目; 電視節目","examples":["...foreign television transmissions. …外國的電視節目。"]}]}]},"treason":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"叛國罪，通敵罪；背叛，不忠，背信；（史）輕叛逆罪（殺害原被效忠者，如僕殺主、妻殺夫等的行為）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Treason</b> is the crime of betraying your country, for example, by helping its enemies or by trying to remove its government using violence. 叛國罪","examples":["They were tried and found guilty of treason. 他們受到了審判並被處以叛國罪。"]}]}]},"tread":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"踩，踏，踐踏；踩碎，踩爛；行走，步行；言行謹慎，小心處理；採取一系列行動"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"步態，腳步聲；（臺階或樓梯的）梯面，踏步板；（輪胎的）胎面，外胎花紋；鞋底，鞋底花紋；輪胎印；（鋼軌與車輪接觸的）鋼軌踏面"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>tread</b> of a tyre or shoe is the pattern of thin lines cut into its surface that stops it from slipping. (鞋底或輪胎上的) 花紋","examples":["The fat, broad tyres had a good depth of tread. 鼓鼓的寬輪胎上有一道很深的花紋。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tread</b> in a particular way, you walk that way. 行走","examples":["She trod casually, enjoying the touch of the damp grass on her feet. 她隨意行走，享受著腳底接觸著溼草的感覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>tread</b> carefully, you behave in a careful or cautious way. (小心) 行事","examples":["If you are hoping to form a new relationship tread carefully and slowly to begin with. 如果你希望建立一種新的關係，開始時就要小心緩慢行事。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>tread on</b> something, you put your foot on it when you are walking or standing. 踩","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>tread</b> a particular <b>path</b>, you take a particular course of action or do something in a particular way. 以…方式行事","examples":["He continues to tread an unconventional path. 他繼續以一種不合常規的方式行事。"]}]}]},"tremor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（身體或聲音的）顫抖，戰慄；興奮，害怕；輕微地震，小地震；波動，風波"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"震顫，顫抖，戰慄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tremor</b> is a small earthquake. 小地震","examples":["The earthquake sent tremors through the region. 這次地震的震感傳遍了整個地區。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an event causes a <b>tremor</b> in a group or organization, it threatens to make the group or organization less strong or stable. (團體或組織內的) 波動","examples":["News of 160 lay-offs had sent tremors through the community. 裁員160人的訊息在社群中引起了波動。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>tremor</b> is a shaking of your body or voice that you cannot control. (身體或聲音的) 顫抖","examples":["The old man has a tremor in his hands. 那位老人的雙手顫抖著。"]}]}]},"trespass":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"擅自進入，侵入（他人土地或建築物）；<古>傷害，冒犯；不公正地對待；干涉，插手"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擅闖私地，非法進入；<舊>罪過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>trespasses</b>, they go onto someone else's land without their permission. 擅自進入","examples":["They were trespassing on private property. 他們正在擅自闖入私人領地。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trespass</b> is the act of trespassing. 擅自進入","examples":["You could be prosecuted for trespass. 你可能會因擅自闖入而被起訴。"]}]}]},"trek":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指徒步）長途跋涉；（尤指在山中）遠足，徒步旅行；緩慢行走，沒精打采地走；<南非>不斷旅行，過流浪生活；<南非>（牛）拉車，馱運；<南非>用圍網捕魚；<南非，史>（隨裝載自己財物的牛車）遷移，旅行"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（顯得很漫長的）一段路程；（尤指徒步的）長途艱苦旅行；<南非>大遷徙（the Trek）；<南非>一網魚；<南非，非正式>財產，所有物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>trek</b> somewhere, you go on a journey across difficult country, usually on foot. (艱難地) 徒步旅行","examples":["...trekking through the jungles. …徒步穿越叢林。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>trek</b> somewhere, you go there heavily and unwillingly, usually because you are tired. 疲憊地行走","examples":["They trekked from shop to shop in search of white knee-high socks. 他們疲憊地奔波於一家又一家商店，尋找高到膝蓋的白色長筒襪。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trek</b> is also a noun. 徒步旅行","examples":["He is on a trek through the South Gobi desert. 他正徒步穿越南戈壁沙漠。"]}]}]},"tropic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熱帶，熱帶地區（the tropics）；迴歸線；（天文）天球的迴歸線"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熱帶的（同 tropical）；向性的，親……的；（激素或其作用）向性的，刺激另一內分泌腺活動的（同 trophic）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"either of the parallel lines of latitude at about 23<b></b>°N (<b>tropic of Cancer</b>) and 23<b></b>°S (<b>tropic of Capricorn</b>) of the equator 迴歸線","examples":[]}]}]},"trophy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獎盃，獎品；（用於比賽或賽跑名稱）獎，獎盃（Trophy）；戰利品，獵獲物；（古希臘或古羅馬用繳獲的武器搭成的）勝利紀念柱"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"向他人炫耀的，抬高自己身價的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trophy</b> is a prize, for example, a silver cup, that is given to the winner of a competition or race. 獎品","examples":["The special trophy for the best rider went to Chris Read. 最佳騎手的特別獎給了克里斯·裡德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>trophy</b> is something that you keep in order to show that you have done something very difficult. 戰利品","examples":["His office was lined with animal heads, trophies of his hunting hobby. 他的辦公室排列著動物的頭顱，都是他業餘狩獵的戰利品。"]}]}]},"truant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"曠課者，逃學者；逃避責任者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"曠課的，逃學的；懶惰的，閒散的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"曠課，逃學；偷懶，逃避責任"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>truant</b> is a student who stays away from school without permission. 逃學者","examples":["The parents of persistent truants can be put in jail. 那些長期逃學學生的家長會被監禁。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a student <b>plays truant</b>, he or she stays away from school without permission. 逃學","examples":["She was getting into trouble over playing truant from school. 她由於逃學而遇到了麻煩。"]}]}]},"truce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"停戰協定，休戰，停戰期"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"停戰；以休戰結束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>truce</b> is an agreement between two people or groups of people to stop fighting or arguing for a short time. 停戰協議","examples":["The fighting of recent days has given way to an uneasy truce between the two sides. 最近幾天的交戰已結束，雙方好不容易達成了休戰協議。"]}]}]},"trigger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（槍械等的）扳機；（尤指引發不良反應或發展的）起因，誘因；（炸彈的）引爆器，觸發器"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"引發，激發；起動，觸發；引爆（炸彈）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>trigger</b> of a gun is a small lever which you pull to fire it. 扳機","examples":["A man pointed a gun at them and pulled the trigger. 一個男人用槍指著他們，扣動了扳機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>trigger</b> of a bomb is the device which causes it to explode. (炸彈的) 引爆裝置","examples":["...trigger devices for nuclear weapons. …核武器的引爆裝置。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something acts as a <b>trigger</b> <b>for</b> another thing such as an illness, event, or situation, the first thing causes the second thing to begin to happen or exist. 引發…的原因","examples":["Stress may act as a trigger for these illnesses. 壓力也許是引發這些疾病的一個原因。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>trigger</b> a bomb or system means to cause it to work. 引爆; 觸發","examples":["The thieves must have deliberately triggered the alarm and hidden inside the house. 那些小偷一定是故意觸發了報警器，然後藏在屋子裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>triggers</b> an event or situation, it causes it to begin to happen or exist. 引起","examples":["...the incident which triggered the outbreak of the First World War. …引起第一次世界大戰爆發的事件。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Trigger off</b> means the same as . 引起","examples":["It is still not clear what events triggered off the demonstrations. 還不清楚是什麼事件引發了示威。"]}]}]},"tuberculosis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"結核病（尤指肺結核）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tuberculosis</b> is a serious infectious disease that affects someone's lungs and other parts of their body. The abbreviation  is also used. 肺結核","examples":[]}]}]},"tumor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"腫瘤，腫塊，贅生物"}],"sections":[]},"turmoil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"混亂，騷動"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擾亂，使不安"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Turmoil</b> is a state of confusion, disorder, uncertainty, or great anxiety. 混亂; 騷亂","examples":["She lived through the turmoil of the French Revolution. 她經歷過法國大革命的混亂之後仍舊活著。"]}]}]},"twilight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"黃昏，薄暮時分；暮光，暮色；衰退期，朦朧狀態"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"朦朧的，模糊的，虛幻的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Twilight</b> is the time just before night when the daylight has almost gone but when it is not completely dark. 黃昏","examples":["They returned at twilight. 他們在黃昏時返回。"]}]}]},"tyranny":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"暴虐，專橫；暴君統治，暴君統治的國家；嚴酷的事物；（對人們生活和行為方式的）控制，左右； （不中意或令人不快的）必需品；（尤指古希臘）僭主統治，僭王統治"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>tyranny</b> is a cruel, harsh, and unfair government in which a person or small group of people have power over everyone else. 專制暴政","examples":["Self-expression and individuality are the greatest weapons against tyranny. 自我表達和個性是對抗專制暴政的最強武器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour and treatment of others that they have authority over as <b>tyranny</b>, you mean that they are severe with them or unfair to them. 專橫暴虐","examples":["I'm the sole victim of Mother's tyranny. 我是母親專橫暴虐的惟一受害者。"]}]}]},"ulcer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（病理）潰瘍；（比喻）腐蝕或敗壞的事物或現象，如腐爛物、道德敗壞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ulcer</b> is a sore area on the outside or inside of your body which is very painful and may bleed or produce a poisonous substance. 潰瘍","examples":["In addition to headaches, you may develop stomach ulcers as well. 除了頭痛，你還可能患上胃潰瘍。"]}]}]},"unemployment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"失業人數，失業率；失業，失業狀態；<美>失業救濟金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Unemployment</b> is the fact that people who want jobs cannot get them. 失業","examples":["The state's unemployment rate rose slightly to 7.1 percent last month. 該國的失業率上個月略微上升到7.1%。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Unemployment</b> is the same as . 失業救濟金","examples":["He worked most of the year. Now he's getting unemployment. 他一年的大部分時間都在工作。現在他將得到失業救濟金。"]}]}]},"upbringing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教養，養育"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>upbringing</b> is the way that your parents treat you and the things that they teach you when you are growing up. 教養","examples":["Martin's upbringing shaped his whole life. 馬丁的教養影響了他的一生。"]}]}]},"underestimate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"低估，對……估計不足；輕視，小看（某人）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"低估，對……估計不足"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>underestimate</b> something, you do not realize how large or great it is or will be. 低估 (某事)","examples":["None of us should ever underestimate the degree of difficulty women face in career advancement. 我們誰都不應低估婦女在職業發展中所面臨的困難程度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>underestimate</b> someone, you do not realize what they are capable of doing. 低估 (某人)","examples":["I think a lot of people still underestimate him. 我認為許多人仍然低估了他。"]}]}]},"ultimate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最終的，最後的；最根本的，最基礎的；極限的，終極的；首要的，決定性的；（太空或時空中）最遙遠的；（物理）極限的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"最好的事物，最終的事物；最終（或最根本）的事實（或原則）；<美>極限飛盤（Ultimate Frisbee 的簡稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>ultimate</b> to describe the final result or aim of a long series of events. 最終的","examples":["He said it is still not possible to predict the ultimate outcome. 他說現在還不可能預測最終的結果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>ultimate</b> to describe the original source or cause of something. 最終的; 根本的","examples":["Plants are the ultimate source of all foodstuffs. 植物是所有食物的最終來源。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>ultimate</b> to describe the most important or powerful thing of a particular kind. 終極的 (指最重要或最強大的)","examples":["My experience as player, coach and manager has prepared me for this ultimate challenge. 我做球員、教練和經理人的經歷已經使我為這終極挑戰作好了準備。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>ultimate</b> to describe the most extreme and unpleasant example of a particular thing. 終極的 (指最極端、最惡劣的)","examples":["Bringing back the death penalty would be the ultimate abuse of human rights. 恢復死刑將是對人權最極端惡劣的踐踏。","Treachery was the ultimate sin. 背叛曾是彌天大罪。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>ultimate</b> to describe the best possible example of a particular thing. 終極的 (指最好的)","examples":["Experience the ultimate adventure! 去體驗最有刺激的冒險吧！"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The ultimate in</b> something is the best or most advanced example of it. 極致; 最佳典範","examples":["Ballet is the ultimate in human movement. 芭蕾舞是人類動作的至美。","This hotel is the ultimate in luxury. 這家酒店為豪華之典範。"]}]}]},"uranium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（化學元素）鈾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Uranium</b> is a naturally occurring radioactive metal that is used to produce nuclear energy and weapons. 鈾","examples":[]}]}]},"upgrade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）（計算機、機器或軟體）升級；提高（設施、服務等的）檔次，改善；（使）升級到更高待遇，（使）升艙；使（僱員）升職；使（某事物）升格"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"改善，提高檔次；（計算機的）升級；上坡"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"往上的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"往上"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If equipment or services <b>are upgraded</b>, they are improved or made more efficient. 使升級","examples":["Helicopters have been upgraded and modernized. 直升機已經升級並且裝上現代化裝置。","Medical facilities are being reorganized and upgraded. 醫療設施正在進行重組和升級。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>is upgraded</b>, their job or status is changed so that they become more important or receive more money. 提升","examples":["He was upgraded to security guard. 他被提升為保安。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>upgrade</b> or <b>are upgraded</b>, you change something such as your plane ticket or your hotel room to one that is more expensive. 使升艙; 使 (旅館房間等) 升級; 升艙; 升級","examples":["His family was upgraded from economy to business class. 他的家人從經濟艙升到了商務艙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Upgrade</b> is also a noun. 升級","examples":["...equipment which needs expensive upgrades. …需要進行昂貴升級的裝置。"]}]}]},"urine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"尿液，小便"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Urine</b> is the liquid that you get rid of from your body when you go to the toilet. 尿","examples":["The doctor took a urine sample and a blood sample. 醫生取了尿樣和血樣。"]}]}]},"urgency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"緊急，迫切；迫切需要；緊急的事"}],"sections":[]},"usher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電影院、戲院、婚禮等的）引座員，迎賓員；法庭庭警，法警；男儐相"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"引導，引領；（喻）使開始，開創（usher sth. in）；作招待員，當引座員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>usher</b> someone somewhere, you show them where they should go by going with them. 引領","examples":["I ushered him into the office. 我領他進了辦公室。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>usher</b> is a person who shows people where to sit, for example at a wedding or at a concert. (婚禮、音樂會等的) 引座員","examples":["He did part-time work as an usher in a theatre. 他曾在一家劇院做兼職引座員。"]}]}]},"utensil":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指廚房或家用的）器具，用具"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Utensils</b> are tools or objects that you use in order to help you to cook, serve food, or eat. 器皿; 用具","examples":["...utensils such as bowls, steamers and frying pans. …碗、蒸鍋、平底鍋等用具。"]}]}]},"utility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（煤氣、水、電等的）公共服務，公用事業；（供電、供水等的）公用事業單位；應用程式，實用程式；實用，有用；<澳>小卡車，輕型貨車；（博弈論，經濟學）效用"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有用的，多功能的；（體育運動）多面手的；實用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>utility</b> is an important service such as water, electricity, or gas that is provided for everyone, and that everyone pays for. 公用事業","examples":["...public utilities such as gas, electricity and phones. …煤氣、電和電話等公用事業。"]}]}]},"utmost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極度的，最大的；<正式>最遠的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"極度，極限"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>utmost</b> to emphasize the importance or seriousness of something or to emphasize the way that it is done. 最大的; 極度的","examples":["It is a matter of the utmost urgency to find out what has happened to these people. 當務之急是弄清楚這些人出了什麼事。","Security matters are treated with the utmost seriousness. 安全問題受到極為嚴肅的對待。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you are doing your <b>utmost</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are emphasizing that you are trying as hard as you can to do it. 最大努力","examples":["He would have done his utmost to help her. 他本來會盡最大努力幫助她。"]}]}]},"vanilla":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"香草精，香子蘭精；香草冰淇淋；香草冰淇淋色，淺奶黃色；香子蘭，香果蘭，香夾蘭"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"香草味的；無特色的，普通的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vanilla</b> is a flavoring used in ice cream and other sweet food. 香草","examples":["I added a dollop of vanilla ice cream to the pie. 我在餡餅中加了一塊香草冰淇淋。"]}]}]},"validity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（法律上的）有效，合法，認可；真實性，正確性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>validity</b> <b>of</b> something such as a result or a piece of information is whether it can be trusted or believed. 可信性","examples":["Shocked by the results of the elections, they now want to challenge the validity of the vote. 震驚於這些選舉的結果，他們現在想質疑投票的可信性。","Some people, of course, denied the validity of any such claim. 當然，一些人否認任何此類說法的可信性。"]}]}]},"vaccine":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疫苗；（計算機）防毒軟體"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"疫苗的，菌苗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vaccine</b> is a substance containing a harmless form of the germs that cause a particular disease. It is given to people, usually by injection, to prevent them from getting that disease. 疫苗","examples":["Anti-malarial vaccines are now undergoing trials. 抗瘧疾疫苗現在正處於試驗階段。"]}]}]},"verge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊緣；<英>（道路旁的）植草路肩，綠地；極限，臨界點；山牆突瓦；權杖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"趨向，接近，瀕臨；處在邊緣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>on the verge of</b> something, you are going to do it very soon or it is likely to happen or begin very soon. 即將","examples":["The country was on the verge of becoming prosperous and successful. 這個國家即將變得繁榮昌盛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an edge or rim; margin 邊緣","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>verge</b> of a road is a narrow piece of ground by the side of a road, which is usually covered with grass or flowers. (通常種有花草的) 路邊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to be near (to) 接近; 瀕臨","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to move or incline in a certain direction 趨向; 傾向","examples":[]}]}]},"vendor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小販，攤販；<法律>賣主，賣方；（出售某類商品的）銷售商，供應商；（貿易） 自動售貨機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vendor</b> is someone who sells things such as newspapers, cigarettes, or food from a small stall or cart. 小販","examples":["...ice cream vendors. …賣冰淇淋的小販們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vendor</b> is a company or person that sells a product or service, especially one who sells to other companies that sell to the public. 賣主","examples":["Tour America acts as an agent for other vendors and cannot be held responsible for any delays. “巡遊美國”充當其他賣主的代理商，它對任何延誤不承擔責任。"]}]}]},"variable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易變的，多變的；時好時壞的；可變的，可調節的；（數）（數字）變數的；（植，動）變異的，變型的；（齒輪）變速的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可變性，可變因素；（數學中的）變數，變元；（計算機）變數（元）；（天文）變星的簡稱；（東北信風帶以北或南半球的東南信風帶與西風帶之間的）變風區"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>variable</b> changes quite often, and there usually seems to be no fixed pattern to these changes. 多變的","examples":["The potassium content of foodstuffs is very variable. 食品中鉀的含量是多變的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可變性","examples":["There's a great deal of variability between individuals. 個體之間存在著很大的可變性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>variable</b> is a factor that can change in quality, quantity, or size, that you have to take into account in a situation. 可變因素","examples":["Decisions could be made on the basis of price, delivery dates, after-sales service or any other variable. 決定可以基於價格、送貨日期、售後服務或是任何其他可變因素而做出。"]}]}]},"variation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"變化，變動；變奏曲；變化，變異；（天文）二均差；（數）變分，變差；磁偏角；（芭蕾）單人舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>variation on</b> something is the same thing presented in a slightly different form. (某一事物) 略有變化的形式","examples":["This delicious variation on an omelette is quick and easy to prepare. 這種略有變化的美味煎蛋餅做起來又快又容易。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>variation</b> is a change or slight difference in a level, amount, or quantity. 變化; 差別","examples":["The survey found a wide variation in the prices charged for canteen food. 這項調查發現不同的餐廳出售食物的價格存在很大的差別。"]}]}]},"vet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獸醫；<美，非正式>老兵；獸醫診所（vet's）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細檢查；徹底審查（某人）；診療；作獸醫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vet</b> is someone who is qualified to treat sick or injured animals. <b>Vet</b> is an abbreviation for . 獸醫","examples":["She's at the vet, with her dog, right now. 她此刻正帶著自己的狗在獸醫那裡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>vet</b> is someone who has served in the armed forces of their country, especially during a war. <b>Vet</b> is an abbreviation for . (尤指曾在戰爭中服役的) 退伍軍人","examples":["The New England Shelter in Boston will serve Christmas dinner for 200 vets. 位於波士頓的新英格蘭收容所將為200名老兵提供聖誕晚餐。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"審查","examples":["The government is to make major changes to the procedure for carrying out security vetting. 該政府將對執行安全審查的程式作出重大調整。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is vetted</b>, they are investigated fully before being given a particular job, role, or position, especially one that involves military or political secrets. (尤指將要從事軍事或政治機密的工作人員) 受審查","examples":["She was secretly vetted before she ever undertook any work for me. 她在為我承擔任何工作之前受到了秘密審查。"]}]}]},"veteran":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"老兵，退伍軍人；經驗豐富的人，老手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經驗豐富的，老練的；<英>古老的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>veteran</b> is someone who has served in the armed forces of their country, especially during a war. 退伍軍人","examples":["They approved a $1.1 billion package of pay increases for the veterans of the Persian Gulf War. 他們批准了為參加過波斯灣戰爭的退伍軍人增付11億美元的一攬子計劃。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>veteran</b> to refer to someone who has been involved in a particular activity for a long time. 經驗豐富的人","examples":["...Annette Michelson, the veteran critic and professor of cinema studies at New York University. …安妮特·米切爾森，這位紐約大學電影研究的教授和資深影評人。"]}]}]},"veterinarian":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獸醫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>veterinarian</b> is a person who is qualified to treat sick or injured animals. 獸醫","examples":[]}]}]},"version":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（同一種物件稍有不同的）樣式，型號；（從不同角度的）說法，描述；（電影、劇本、樂曲等的）版本，改編形式；《聖經》譯本；胎位倒轉術"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"創制……的新版本，更新……的版本"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>version</b> <b>of</b> something is a particular form of it in which some details are different from earlier or later forms. 版本; 變體","examples":["...an updated version of his bestselling book. …他這本暢銷書的一個最新版本。","Ludo is a version of an ancient Indian racing game. “魯多遊戲”是一種古代印度競賽遊戲的變體。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>version</b> <b>of</b> an event is their own description of it, especially when it is different from other people's. (某人對某事有別於他人的) 說法","examples":["Some former hostages contradicted the official version of events. 一些以前的人質反駁了官方對這些事件的說法。"]}]}]},"vibration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"震動，顫動，抖動；<非正式>（情感）感應，共鳴"}],"sections":[]},"villa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"度假別墅；（城內的）豪宅；（附有土地的）鄉間宅第，莊園"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>villa</b> is a fairly large house, especially one in a hot country or a resort. (尤指熱帶國家或風景區的) 別墅","examples":["He lives in a secluded five-bedroom luxury villa. 他住在一幢僻靜的、有5間臥室的豪華別墅裡。"]}]}]},"victor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"勝利者"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Victor）人名；（俄、羅、保、匈）維克托"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>victor</b> in a battle or contest is the person who wins. 勝利者","examples":["Oliver Townsend and co-driver Kirk Lee eventually emerged as victors after five different cars had led the event. 5輛車相繼領先，最終奧利佛·湯森和副駕駛員柯克·李成為勝利者。"]}]}]},"vice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"墮落，邪惡；小毛病，壞習慣；（與性或毒品有關的）罪行，道德敗壞行為；老虎鉗（同 vise）；<非正式>代理人，任副職者；（尤指馬廄裡馬因厭倦而出現的）劣性，惡癖"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"握住，鉗緊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"副的；代替的，代理的"},{"pos":"prep.","zh":"代替"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vice</b> is a habit that is regarded as a weakness in someone's character, but not usually as a serious fault. 不良習慣","examples":["His only vice is to get drunk on champagne after concluding a successful piece of business. 他惟一的不良習慣就是在成功做成一筆生意之後喝香檳酒至大醉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Vice</b> refers to criminal activities, especially those connected with pornography or prostitution. (尤指與色情、賣淫等有關的) 犯罪活動","examples":["He said those responsible for offences connected with vice, gaming and drugs should be deported on conviction. 他說那些跟賣淫、賭博、販毒有關的罪犯應在判罪後被驅逐出境。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>vice</b> is a tool with a pair of parts that hold an object tightly while you do work on it. 虎鉗","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a person who serves as a deputy to another 代理人; 任副職者","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to grip (something) with or as if with a vice 握住; 鉗緊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"serving in the place of or as a deputy for 代替的; 代理的","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(<b>in combination</b>) 副的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"instead of; as a substitute for 代替; 取代","examples":[]}]}]},"vineyard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"葡萄園，葡萄酒廠；藤本植物園"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>vineyard</b> is an area of land where grape vines are grown in order to produce wine. You can also use <b>vineyard</b> to refer to the set of buildings in which the wine is produced. 葡萄園; 葡萄酒廠","examples":[]}]}]},"vocal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嗓音的，發聲的，歌唱的；直言不諱的，大聲表達的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（樂曲中的）歌唱部分，聲樂部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say that people are <b>vocal</b> when they speak forcefully about something that they feel strongly about. 直言不諱的","examples":["He has been very vocal in his displeasure over the results. 他直言不諱地說出了對結果的不滿。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Vocal</b> means involving the use of the human voice, especially in singing. 嗓音的","examples":["...a wider range of vocal styles. …更多樣的嗓音風格。"]}]}]},"vitality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"活力，熱情；生機，生命力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>vitality</b>, you mean that they have great energy and liveliness. 活力","examples":["Without continued learning, graduates will lose their intellectual vitality. 如果不繼續學習，畢業生們就會失去他們的思維活力。"]}]}]},"vocation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（認為某種職業適合自己的）使命感；（認為特別適合自己的）工作，職業，生活方式；神召，天命，（宗教）使命感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>vocation</b>, you have a strong feeling that you are especially suited to do a particular job or to fulfill a particular role in life, especially one that involves helping other people. 使命感","examples":["It could well be that he has a real vocation. 他很可能有種真正的使命感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to your job or profession as your <b>vocation</b>, you feel that you are particularly suited to it. 適合的職業","examples":["Her vocation is her work as an actress. 她適合的職業就是當演員。"]}]}]},"vogue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"流行，時髦"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"時髦的，流行的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（模仿模特在 T 形臺上的姿態）隨音樂跳舞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>vogue</b> <b>for</b> something, it is very popular and fashionable. 時尚","examples":["Despite the vogue for so-called health teas, there is no evidence that they are any healthier. 儘管所謂的保健茶成了時尚，但並沒有證據表明這種茶更有益於健康。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>in vogue</b>, it is very popular and fashionable. If it comes <b>into vogue</b>, it becomes very popular and fashionable. 正在流行; 變得流行","examples":["Pale colours are much more in vogue than autumnal bronzes and coppers. 淺色比秋季的古銅色和紫銅色更為流行。"]}]}]},"vomit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"吐，嘔吐；噴出，吐出"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"嘔吐物；嘔吐；<古>催吐劑"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>vomit</b>, food and drink comes back up from your stomach and out through your mouth. 嘔吐","examples":["Any product made from cow's milk made him vomit. 任何牛奶製品都會讓他嘔吐。","She began to vomit blood a few days before she died. 她在去世前幾天開始吐血。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vomit</b> is partly digested food and drink that has come back up from someone's stomach and out through their mouth. 嘔吐物","examples":["Zimmer slipped and nearly fell on a pool of vomit. 齊默滑了一跤，差點兒摔倒在一灘嘔吐物上。"]}]}]},"wardrobe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"衣櫃，衣櫥；（某人的）全部服裝；（劇院、電視臺等的）服裝部，戲裝管理部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>wardrobe</b> is the total collection of clothes that they have. (某人的) 全部服裝","examples":["Her wardrobe consists primarily of huge cashmere sweaters and tiny Italian sandals. 她的衣服主要是寬大的開司米毛衣和纖小的義大利涼鞋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>wardrobe</b> is a tall closet or cabinet in which you can hang your clothes. 衣櫃","examples":[]}]}]},"warfare":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"戰爭，作戰；（團體、公司等之間的）鬥爭，競爭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Warfare</b> is the activity of fighting a war. 作戰; 戰爭","examples":["...the threat of chemical warfare. …化學戰的威脅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Warfare</b> is sometimes used to refer to any violent struggle or conflict. 打鬥; 衝突","examples":["Much of the violence is related to drugs and gang warfare. 很多暴力行為都與毒品和幫派衝突有關。"]}]}]},"windshield":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美式英語）擋風玻璃，風擋"}],"sections":[]},"warranty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（商品的）保修單，保用卡；（保險合同用語）（被保險人對某些陳述所作的）保證，擔保；<古>正當理由，依據"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>warranty</b> is a written promise by a company that, if you find a fault in something they have sold you within a certain time, they will repair it or replace it free of charge. 保修單","examples":["...a twelve-month warranty. …為期12個月的保修單。"]}]}]},"zeal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"熱情，熱忱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Zeal</b> is great enthusiasm, especially in connection with work, religion, or politics. (尤指對工作、宗教或政治的) 熱衷","examples":["...his zeal for teaching. …他對教學的熱衷。"]}]}]},"xerox":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"施樂（商標名，美國辦公裝置製造公司）；靜電影印機，影印機；影印件，靜電印刷品"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用靜電覆印法影印"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>Xerox</b> is a machine that can make copies of pieces of paper which have writing or other marks on them. 施樂影印機","examples":["The rooms are crammed with humming Xerox machines. 那些房間裡擺滿了嗡嗡作響的施樂影印機。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>Xerox</b> is a copy of something written or printed on a piece of paper, which has been made using a Xerox machine. 施樂影印件","examples":["I got a Xerox of the lyrics, handed them out, and then we had the rehearsals. 我得到了那些歌詞的施樂影印件，發給了大家，而後我們進行了排練。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>Xerox</b> a document, you make a copy of it using a Xerox machine. 用施樂影印機影印","examples":["I should have simply Xeroxed this sheet for you. 我本應該只為你影印這張。"]}]}]},"wrench":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"猛拉，猛扭，掙脫；扭傷；奪走（某人），拆散；使痛苦，使十分難過（尤指以致哭喊出聲）；用扳鉗擰"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"扳手，扳鉗；（離別的）痛苦，難受；猛扭，猛拉；（機械）偶單力組；扭傷；歪曲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wrench</b> something that is fixed in a particular position, you pull or twist it violently, in order to move or remove it. 猛拽; 猛扭","examples":["He felt two men wrench the suitcase from his hand. 他感覺有兩個人在猛拽他手裡的手提箱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wrench</b> yourself free from someone who is holding you, you get away from them by suddenly twisting the part of your body that is being held. 掙脫","examples":["She wrenched herself from his grasp. 她掙脫了他的把持。","He wrenched his arm free. 他把手臂掙脫開來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>wrench</b> your neck, you hurt it by pulling or twisting it in an unusual way. 扭傷","examples":["She was involved in a car accident and she wrenched her neck. 她被捲入一場車禍，扭傷了脖子。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>wrench</b> is the same as a . 扳手","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>throws a wrench</b> or <b>throws a monkey wrench</b> into a process, they prevent something happening smoothly by deliberately causing a problem. 阻撓","examples":["The decision will throw a monkey wrench into our efforts to develop a national broadband policy. 這一決定將妨礙我們制定一個全國性寬頻政策的努力。"]}]}]},"my":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"哎呀（表示驚奇等）；喔唷"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（My）人名；（越）美；（老、柬）米"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>my</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to himself or herself. 我的","examples":["I invited him back to my apartment for coffee. 我請他回我的公寓喝咖啡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In conversations or in letters, <b>my</b> is used in front of a word like \"dear\" or \"darling\" to show affection. 我的 (用在對話或信件中表示親密)","examples":["My sweet Freda. 我可愛的弗雷達。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>My</b> is used in phrases such as \"<b>My God</b>\" and \"<b>My goodness</b>\" to express surprise or shock. 用於口語中表示驚訝或震驚","examples":["My God, I've never seen you so nervous. 我的天呀！我從沒見你這麼緊張過。"]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an exclamation of surprise, awe, etc 哎呀; 表示驚訝、敬畏等的嘆詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Malaysia 馬來西亞","examples":[]}]}]},"me":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我（賓格）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"自我；極端自私的人；自我的一部分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>me</b> to refer to himself or herself. <b>Me</b> is a first person singular pronoun. <b>Me</b> is used as the object of a verb or a preposition. 我 (第一人稱單數賓格代詞)","examples":["I had to make important decisions that would affect me for the rest of my life. 我不得不做出一些會影響我後半生的重要決定。","He asked me to go to California with him. 他邀我和他一起去加利福尼亞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the personality of the speaker or writer or something that expresses it (演講人或作家說的)自我","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Montenegro 黑山","examples":[]}]}]},"wrestle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（與某人）摔跤，扭打；使勁搬動，用力操作；努力解決，艱難對付"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"摔跤，角力；艱苦的鬥爭，搏鬥"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>wrestle</b> <b>with</b> a difficult problem, you try to deal with it. 試圖解決","examples":["Delegates wrestled with the problems of violence and sanctions. 代表們試圖解決暴力和制裁問題。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>wrestle</b> with someone, you fight them by forcing them into painful positions or throwing them to the ground, rather than by hitting them. Some people wrestle as a sport. 摔跤","examples":["They taught me to wrestle. 他們教我去摔跤。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>wrestle</b> a person or thing somewhere, you move them there using a lot of force, for example, by twisting a part of someone's body into a painful position. 費力地拉","examples":["We had to physically wrestle the child from the man's arms. 我們只得用力地從那個男子懷裡把孩子奪過來。"]}]}]},"i":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"英語字母 i（大寫 I）；數學虛數單位（滿足 i² = −1）；羅馬數字 1；美國州際公路編號字首（如 I-95）；碘（化學元素符號 I）；（哲學）自我，自我意識"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我（第一人稱單數主格代詞，通常大寫為 I）"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"義大利（國際車牌註冊程式碼 I）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>I</b> to refer to himself or herself. <b>I</b> is a first person singular pronoun. <b>I</b> is used as the subject of a verb. 我 (用作主格)","examples":["Jim and I are getting married. 吉姆和我要結婚了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>I</b> is the ninth letter of the English alphabet. 英文字母表中的第9個字母","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"symbol for.","pos_name":"symbol for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"iodine 碘","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Italy (international car registration) 義大利(國際汽車牌號標誌)","examples":[]}]}]},"yours":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"你（們）的東西；你的責任[義務]；你的家屬；來信，尊函"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"你（們）的（東西）；信末署名前用語"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>yours</b> to refer to something that belongs or relates to the person or people that they are talking or writing to. 你的; 你們的 (東西)","examples":["I'll take my coat upstairs. Shall I take yours, Roberta? 我將把我的外套拿到樓上去。要我把你的拿上去嗎，羅伯塔？","I believe Paul was a friend of yours. 我相信保羅曾是你的一個朋友。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People write <b>yours</b>, <b>yours sincerely</b>, <b>sincerely yours</b>, or <b>yours truly</b> at the end of a letter before they sign their name. 你…的 (常與)(truly)(或)(sincerely)(等詞連用寫於信末簽名前)","examples":["With best regards, Yours, George. 謹致問候。你真誠的：喬治。"]}]}]},"you":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"你；你們；（口語或非正式書面語）泛指任何人"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（You）人名；（柬）尤；（東南亞國家華語）猷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>you</b> to refer to the person or people that they are talking or writing to. It is possible to use <b>you</b> before a noun to make it clear which group of people you are talking to. 你; 你們","examples":["When I saw you across the room I knew I'd met you before. 當看見房間對面的你時，我知道我以前曾見過你。","You two seem very different to me. 你們倆在我看來似乎很不同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In spoken English and informal written English, <b>you</b> is sometimes used to refer to people in general. 你 (在口語及非正式書面語中用以泛指人)","examples":["Getting good results gives you confidence. 得到好的結果給你信心。","In those days you did what you were told. 在那些日子裡你做別人讓你做的事。"]}]}]},"your":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"你的，你們的；<口語>泛指任何人的；<口語>（用於 typical、normal 等形容詞前）通常所說的，典型的；<正式>（用於尊稱頭銜前）您的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>your</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to the person or people that they are talking or writing to. 你的; 你們的","examples":["Emma, I trust your opinion a great deal. 埃瑪，我非常相信你的觀點。","I left all of your messages on your desk. 我把你的所有便條都放到你的書桌上了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In spoken English and informal written English, <b>your</b> is sometimes used to indicate that something belongs to or relates to people in general. 你的 (口語中用於泛指屬於或有關任何人的)","examples":["Painkillers are very useful in small amounts to bring your temperature down. 小劑量的止痛藥對於降低體溫非常有用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In spoken English, a speaker sometimes uses <b>your</b> before an adjective such as \"typical\" or \"normal\" to indicate that the thing referred to is a typical example of its type. 人們所認為的 (口語中用於形容詞前，表示所指事物為某類事物的典型)","examples":["This isn't your typical economics class. 這不是人們所認為的典型的經濟學課。"]}]}]},"him":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"他（賓格）；它（指雄性動物）；（書面英語）用於泛指不限定性別的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>him</b> to refer to a man, boy, or male animal. 他; 它 (指雄性動物)","examples":["John's aunt died suddenly and left him a surprisingly large sum. 約翰的姑媽突然去世,給他留下一筆令人意想不到的鉅款。","Is Sam there? Let me talk to him. 薩姆在嗎？讓我和他談談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In written English, <b>him</b> is sometimes used to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people dislike this use and prefer to use \"him or her\" or \"them.\" 他 (書面英語中泛指人)","examples":["If the child encounters \"hear,\" we should show him that this is the base word in \"hearing\" and \"hears.\" 如果孩子遇到這個單詞，我們應該向他說明這個詞是和的詞根。"]}]}]},"his":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"他的，它的（指雄性動物）"},{"pos":"pron.","zh":"他的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>his</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to a man, boy, or male animal. 他的; 它的 (指雄性動物)","examples":["Brian splashed water on his face, then brushed his teeth. 布賴恩用水拍洗了臉，然後刷了牙。","He spent a large part of his career in Hollywood. 他職業生涯中的大部分時間是在好萊塢度過的。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>His</b> is also a possessive pronoun. 他的 (也作物主代詞)","examples":["Staff say the decision was his. 員工們說那個決定是他做出的。"]}]}]},"he":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"他；（泛指的）人；上帝"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"男性，男子；雄性動物"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（He）（中、美、丹）赫（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>he</b> to refer to a man, boy, or male animal. 他","examples":["He could never quite remember all our names. 他絕不可能完全記住我們所有人的名字。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In written English, <b>he</b> is sometimes used to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people dislike this use and prefer to use \"he or she\" or \"they.\" 一個人 (they)(”)","examples":["The teacher should encourage the child to proceed as far as he can, and when he is stuck, ask for help. 老師應當鼓勵孩子儘可能獨立思考，自己想不出來了，再尋求幫助。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a male person or animal 男人; 雄性動物","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(<b>in combination</b>) 表示“男···”或“雄···”","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"the fifth letter of the Hebrew alphabet (ה), transliterated as <b>h</b> 希伯來字母表中第5個字母，譯為英文字母中的h","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an expression of amusement or derision 嘻(表示感興趣或嘲笑等) (Also he-he!, hee-hee!)","examples":[]}]}]},"hers":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"（上文提過的女性）她的，屬於她的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Hers）（法、美、英）埃爾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>hers</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to a woman, girl, or female animal. 她的 (東西)","examples":["His hand as it shook hers was warm and firm. 當他握住她的手時，他的手溫暖而有力。","Professor Camm was a great friend of hers. 卡姆教授是她的一位摯友。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In written English, <b>hers</b> is sometimes used to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people dislike this use and prefer to use \"his or hers\" or \"theirs.\" (書面英語中泛指人) 她的; 他的","examples":["The author can report other people's results which more or less agree with hers. 作者可以報道與自己的觀點或多或少一致的別人的成果。"]}]}]},"she":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"她（主格，指女性或女孩；亦泛指未標明性別的人）；它（用於指雌性動物，或國家、船舶、汽車、機器、地球、月亮等擬人化事物，也可譯“她”）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"女人；雌性動物（複數 shes）；（She）人名，尤指中文姓氏“佘”的拉丁字母拼寫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>she</b> to refer to a woman, girl, or female animal who has already been mentioned or whose identity is clear. 她 (代指女性或雌性動物)","examples":["When Ann arrived home that night, she found Brian in the house watching TV. 當安那天晚上到家時，她發現布賴恩正在屋裡看電視。","She was seventeen and she had no education or employment. 她17歲了，既沒有受過教育也沒有工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some writers may use <b>she</b> to refer to a person who is not identified as either male or female. They do this because they wish to avoid using the pronoun \"he\" all the time. Some people dislike this use and prefer to use \"he or she\" or \"they.\" 她 (代指不分性別的所有人)","examples":["The student may show signs of feeling the strain of responsibility and she may give up. 學生可能表現出責任帶來的壓力感的種種跡象，她也許會放棄。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>She</b> is sometimes used to refer to a country or nation. 她 (代指國家或民族)","examples":["The country needs new leadership if she is to play a role in future development. 該國要在未來的發展中發揮作用的話，她就需要新的領導班子。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"Some people use <b>she</b> to refer to a car or machine. People who sail often use <b>she</b> to refer to a ship or boat. 她 (代指汽車、機器或船隻)","examples":["The Seaflower was being repaired, but soon she was fit to sail again. “海花號”當時正在修理，但很快她就又可以航行了。"]}]}]},"its":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"它的，其（it 的所有格形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>its</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to a thing, place, or animal that has just been mentioned or whose identity is known. You can use <b>its</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to a child or baby. 它的","examples":["He held the knife by its blade. 他握住了刀刃。"]}]}]},"her":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"她（she的賓格）；她的（she的所有格）；她（指某個國家；一艘船）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（法）埃爾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>her</b> to refer to a woman, girl, or female animal. 她","examples":["I went in the room and told her I had something to say to her. 我走進房間，告訴她我有話要對她說。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In written English, <b>her</b> is sometimes used to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people dislike this use and prefer to use \"him or her\" or \"them.\" 她 (有時在無需說明性別的情況下指人)","examples":["Talk to your baby, play games, and show her how much you enjoy her company. 跟你的嬰兒談話，玩遊戲，向她表明你是多麼喜歡與她在一起。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Her</b> is sometimes used to refer to a country or nation. 她 (有時用以指國家或民族)","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>her</b> to refer to a car, machine, or ship. 她 (有時用以指小汽車、機器或船)","examples":["Kemp got out of his truck. \"Just fill her up, thanks.\" 肯普下了卡車。“請給她加滿油，謝謝。”"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Her</b> is also a possessive determiner. 她的","examples":["Liz travelled around the world for a year with her boyfriend James. 莉茲跟她的男友詹姆斯到世界各地旅行了一年。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Her</b> is also a possessive determiner. 她的","examples":["The non-drinking, non-smoking model should do nothing to risk her reputation. 這名煙酒不沾的女模特兒不應該做任何對她的名譽不利的事情。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Her</b> is also a possessive determiner. 她的","examples":["America and her partners are helping to rebuild roads and bridges and buildings. 美國及其夥伴正幫助重建道路、橋樑和樓房。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Her</b> is also a possessive determiner. 她的","examples":["This dramatic photograph was taken from Carpathia's deck by one of her passengers. 這張戲劇化的照片是由卡帕西亞號的一名乘客在甲板上拍下的。"]}]}]},"we":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我們（主格）；筆者，本人（作者或演講人使用）；朕，寡人"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（We）人名；（緬）韋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>we</b> to refer both to himself or herself and to one or more other people as a group. You can use <b>we</b> before a noun to make it clear which group of people you are referring to. 我們","examples":["We both swore we'd be friends ever after. 我們倆人都發誓從此以後永為朋友。","We ordered another bottle of champagne. 我們又點了一瓶香檳酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>We</b> is sometimes used to refer to people in general. 我們 (泛指人們)","examples":["We need to take care of our bodies. 我們需要照顧好自己的身體。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A speaker or writer may use <b>we</b> instead of \"I\" in order to include the audience or reader in what they are saying, especially when discussing how a talk or book is organized. 我們 (作者或說話者使用，指讀者或聽眾以及自己，尤其用於報告中或書中)","examples":["We will now consider the raw materials from which the body derives energy. 我們現在來細想一下為身體提供能量的原料。"]}]}]},"us":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我們"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>us</b> to refer both to himself or herself and to one or more other people. You can use <b>us</b> before a noun to make it clear which group of people you are referring to. 我們","examples":["Neither of us forgot about it. 我倆都沒忘記它。","Heather went to the kitchen to get drinks for us. 希瑟去廚房給我們拿飲料。","They don't like us much. 他們不大喜歡我們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Us</b> is sometimes used to refer to people in general. 我們 (泛指人們)","examples":["All of us will struggle fairly hard to survive if we are in danger. 我們所有人如果遇到危險都會竭力掙扎著活下來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A speaker or writer may use <b>us</b> instead of \"me\" in order to include the audience or reader in what they are saying. 我們 (指演講者及其聽眾或作者及其讀者)","examples":["This brings us to the second question I asked. 這就將我們引入了我提出的第2個問題。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"United States 美國","examples":[]}]}]},"our":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"我們的，我方的；（泛指）我們（人類、一般人）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>our</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates both to yourself and to one or more other people. 我們的","examples":["We're expecting our first baby. 我們要生第一個孩子了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A speaker or writer sometimes uses <b>our</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to people in general. (用於泛指) 我們的","examples":["We are all entirely responsible for our actions, and for our reactions. 我們都對自己的行為、自己的反應完全負責。"]}]}]},"it":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"它，這，那（指已提到或將提及的事物、無生命的東西、動物、植物、活動、經驗、抽象觀念等）；用於指某人，尤指性別不詳或情況不詳時（如嬰兒、小孩、電話中的對方）；作無人稱動詞的主語，表示天氣、時間、日期、距離、光線、溫度、狀態等；作形式主語或形式賓語，替代通常出現在其後面的名詞、短語、從句或不定式；與 be 動詞構成強調結構，用於強調其後的句子成分；用作直接賓語，幾乎不具有或完全不具有任何含義（如 have it、call it a day）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（捉迷藏等兒童遊戲中的）捉人者，找人者；義大利苦艾酒，味美思酒"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"（IT）資訊科技（information technology）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> to refer to an object, animal, or other thing that has already been mentioned. 它 (指上文提及的某一物體、動物或其他事物)","examples":["It's a wonderful city, really. I'll show it to you if you want. 這確實是個很棒的城市。如果你願意的話，我帶你看一下。","My wife has become crippled by arthritis. She is embarrassed to ask the doctor about it. 我妻子因患關節炎腿瘸了。她不好意思去向醫生詢問相關病情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> to refer to a child or baby whose sex you do not know or whose sex is not relevant to what you are saying. 它 (指小孩或嬰兒)","examples":["She could compel him to support the child after it was born. 她可以迫使他在孩子出生後撫養孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> to refer in a general way to a situation that you have just described. 它 (指剛剛說過的情況)","examples":["He was through with sports, not because he had to be but because he wanted it that way. 他放棄體育運動了，不是因為他非放棄不可，而是因為他想要那樣。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> before certain nouns, adjectives, and verbs to introduce your feelings or point of view about a situation. 用於某些名詞、形容詞或動詞前表達對某種情況的看法或觀點","examples":["It was nice to see Steve again. 很高興又見到了史蒂夫。","It's a pity you never got married, Sarah. 薩拉，很遺憾你從來沒有結過婚。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> in passive clauses that report a situation or event. 用於被動句表示對某一情況或事件的報道","examples":["It has been said that stress causes cancer. 據說壓力會誘發癌症。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> with some verbs that need a subject or object, although there is no noun that \"it\" refers to. 用作某些動詞的形式主語或賓語","examples":["Of course, as it turned out, three-fourths of the people in the group were psychiatrists. 當然，結果證明這些人中3/4是精神病醫生。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> as the subject of \"be\" to say what the time, day, or date is. 用作動詞(be)的主語，指時間、日期等","examples":["It's three o'clock in the morning. 現在是凌晨3點。","It was a Monday, so she was at home. 那是個星期一，所以她在家。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> as the subject of a linking verb to describe the weather, the light, or the temperature. 用作系動詞的主語，指天氣、光、溫度等","examples":["It was very wet and windy the day I drove over the hill to Del Norte. 我開車越過小山去德爾諾特的那天下大雨又颳大風。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> when you are telling someone who you are, or asking them who they are, especially at the beginning of a phone call. You also use <b>it</b> in statements and questions about the identity of other people. 通電話時用作開首語，報出身份或名字","examples":["\"Who is it?\" he called.—\"It's your neighbour.\" “誰呀？”他喊道。—“你的鄰居。”"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are emphasizing or drawing attention to something, you can put that thing immediately after <b>it</b> and a form of the verb \"be.\" 與(be)動詞配合起強調作用，引起對某事物的注意","examples":["It's really the poor countries that don't have an economic base that have the worst environmental records. 確實是那些沒有經濟基礎的貧窮國家的環保記錄最糟糕。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>it</b> in expressions such as <b>it's not that</b> or <b>it's not just that</b> when you are giving a reason for something and are suggesting that there are several other reasons. 用於(it's not that)、(it's not just that)等表達法中，表示提出一個理由並同時暗示還有其它一些理由","examples":["It's not that I didn't want to be with my family. 並不是因為我不願意和我的家人在一起。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Italy 義大利","examples":[]}]}]},"ours":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"我們的，屬於我們的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Ours）（美）烏爾斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>ours</b> to refer to something that belongs or relates both to yourself and to one or more other people. 屬於我們的東西","examples":["That car is ours. 那輛車是我們的。","There are few strangers in a town like ours. 像我們這樣的鎮上，沒什麼陌生人的。"]}]}]},"their":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"他們的；她們的；它們的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Their）（英）蒂爾；（芬、瑞典）泰爾（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>their</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to the group of people, animals, or things that you are talking about. 他們的; 她們的; 它們的","examples":["Janis and Kurt have announced their engagement. 賈尼斯和庫爾特已宣佈訂婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>their</b> instead of \"his or her\" to indicate that something belongs or relates to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people think this use is incorrect. 用於代替“他的”或 “她的”，不指明是男是女","examples":["Each student determines their own pace in the yoga class. 每個學生決定他們自己在這個瑜珈班的學習速度。"]}]}]},"theirs":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"他們的，她們的，它們的（名詞性物主代詞）；他的，她的（不指明性別時，代替 his or hers）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"所有格代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>theirs</b> to indicate that something belongs or relates to the group of people, animals, or things that you are talking about. 他們的; 她們的; 它們的 (東西)","examples":["There was a big group of a dozen people at the table next to theirs. 他們旁邊的那張桌坐了一大群人，有十幾個。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>theirs</b> instead of \"his or hers\" to indicate that something belongs or relates to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people think this use is incorrect. 用於代替“他的”或“她的”，不指明是男是女，有些人認為這種用法不正確","examples":["He would leave the trailer unlocked. If there was something inside that someone wanted, it would be theirs for the taking. 他不會鎖活動房屋。如果屋裡有別人想要的東西，他們就可以拿走。"]}]}]},"they":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"第三人稱複數主格代詞：他們（男性或男女混合群體），她們（全女性群體），它們（動物、事物等）；也用作單數第三人稱主格代詞，指代性別未知、不願指明性別或認同非二元性別的人，相當於 he or she；泛指人們（如 they say、they call it 等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>they</b> to refer to a group of people, animals, or things. 他們; 她們; 它們","examples":["Feed the dogs because they haven't eaten. 喂喂這幾條狗，因為它們還沒吃呢。","The two men were far more alike than they would ever admit. 這兩個男子非常相像，儘管他們可能不願意承認。","People matter because of what they are, not what they have. 人重要的不在於他們擁有什麼，而在於他們是什麼樣的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>they</b> instead of \"he or she\" to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people think this use is incorrect. 代替(he)或(she)，而不指明是男是女，有些人認為這種用法不正確","examples":["The teacher is not responsible for the student's success or failure. They are only there to help the student learn. 教師不為學生的成敗負責。他們只是幫助學生學習而已。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>they</b> in expressions such as \"they say\" or \"they call it\" to refer to people in general when you are making general statements about what people say, think, or do. 人們","examples":["They say there's plenty of opportunities out there, you just have to look carefully and you'll find them. 人們說那裡有很多機會，你只要仔細尋找就能發現機會。"]}]}]},"them":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"他們，她們，它們；他/她（代替 him 或 her，指性別不明或無需指明性別的單數人；有人認為此用法不規範）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>them</b> to refer to a group of people, animals, or things. 他們; 她們; 它們","examples":["The Beatles – I never get tired of listening to them. 甲殼蟲樂隊–我百聽不厭。","Kids these days have no one to tell them what's right and wrong. 現在的孩子們沒人告訴他們什麼是對什麼是錯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>them</b> instead of \"him or her\" to refer to a person without saying whether that person is a man or a woman. Some people think this use is incorrect. 用於代替賓格“他”或“她”，不指明是男是女，有些人認為這種用法不正確","examples":["It takes great courage to face your child and tell them the truth. 需要很大的勇氣來面對你的孩子並告訴他們真相。"]}]}]},"a":{"summaries":[{"pos":"art.","zh":"一；任一；每一"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> when you are referring to someone or something for the first time or when people may not know which particular person or thing you are talking about. (用於首次提及或泛指某人或某物) 一 (個)","examples":["A waiter entered with a tray bearing a glass and a bottle of whisky. 一名服務員端著一個放有一隻玻璃杯和一瓶威士忌酒的托盤進來了。","He started eating an apple. 他開始吃蘋果。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> when you are referring to any person or thing of a particular type and do not want to be specific. 用於指一類人或物，不需要特指","examples":["I suggest you leave it to an expert. 我建議你把它留給專家來處理。","Bring a sleeping bag. 帶個睡袋來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> in front of an uncount noun when that noun follows an adjective, or when the noun is followed by words that describe it more fully. 一種 (用於前有形容詞或後有修飾語的不可數名詞前)","examples":["The islanders exhibit a constant happiness with life. 這些島民表現出一種對生活的持久的幸福感。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> in front of a mass noun when you want to refer to a single type or make of something. 一種 (用於物質名詞前，特指某物的種類或成分)","examples":["Bollinger \"RD\" is a rare, highly prized wine. 是一種罕見的、非常名貴的葡萄酒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> in quantifiers such as <b>a lot</b>, <b>a little</b>, and <b>a bit</b>. 用在量化片語中，如(a lot), (a little), (a bit##bit)等","examples":["I spend a lot on expensive jewellery and clothing. 我在昂貴的首飾和衣服上開銷很大。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> to refer to someone or something as a typical member of a group, class, or type. 指某人或某物是一個團隊、階層或型別中典型的一員或一部分","examples":["Some parents believe a boy must learn to stand up and fight like a man. 一些家長認為一個男孩必須學會像男子漢一樣奮起戰鬥。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> in front of the names of days, months, or festivals when you are referring to one particular instance of that day, month, or festival. 用於某一天、某一月份或某節日前，特指在該天、該月或該節日發生的事件","examples":["The interview took place on a Friday afternoon. 該面談是在一個星期五下午進行的。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> when you are saying what someone is or what job they have. 用於說明某人的職業","examples":["I explained that I was an artist. 我解釋說我是一位藝術家。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> instead of the number \"one,\" especially with words of measurement such as \"hundred,\" \"hour,\" and \"metre,\" and with fractions such as \"half,\" \"quarter,\" and \"third.\" 一 (代替)(one)","examples":["...more than a thousand acres of land. …一千多英畝的土地。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>a</b> or <b>an</b> in expressions such as <b>eight hours a day</b> to express a rate or ratio. 每一 (用於速率或比率的表達中)","examples":["Prices start at $13.95 a yard for printed cotton. 印花棉布開價為$13.95一碼。"]}]},{"pos":"symbol for.","pos_name":"symbol for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"acceleration 加速度","examples":[]}]}]},"was":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"是；在（am、is 的過去式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Was</b> is the first and third person singular of the past tense of . 動詞(be)的第一、第三人稱單數過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"been":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是，有（be 的過去分詞）；用於 have been to 結構，去過，到過"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Been）<美>貝恩（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Been</b> is the past participle of . (be)的過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>been</b> to a place, you have gone to it or visited it. 去過","examples":["He's already been to Tunisia, and is to go on to Morocco and Mauritania. 他已經去過了突尼西亞，還將接著去摩洛哥和茅利塔尼亞。"]}]}]},"did":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"做（do 的過去式）；用作助動詞，構成一般過去時的疑問句、否定句和強調結構（後接動詞原形）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Did</b> is the past tense of . (do)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"the":{"summaries":[{"pos":"art.","zh":"這；那"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"更加（用於比較級，最高階前）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> at the beginning of noun groups to refer to someone or something that you have already mentioned or identified. 用於名詞片語前，指前面已經提及的人或物","examples":["Six of the 38 people were U.S. citizens. 那38人中有6個是美國公民。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> at the beginning of a noun group when the first noun is followed by an \"of\" phrase or a clause which identifies the person or thing. 當名詞後接(of)片語或表明身份的從句時，該名詞前用(the)","examples":["There has been a slight increase in the consumption of meat. 肉類消費略微增加。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of some nouns that refer to something in our general experience of the world. 用於某些表示人們共同經歷的名詞前","examples":["It's always hard to speculate about the future. 推測未來總是很難的。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of nouns that refer to people, things, services, or institutions that are associated with everyday life. 用於表示與日常生活有關的人、事物、服務或機構的名詞前","examples":["The doctor's on his way. 醫生正在路上。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> instead of a possessive determiner, especially when you are talking about a part of someone's body or a member of their family. 用於代替所有格限定詞，尤其用於談論身體部位或家庭成員","examples":["\"How's the family?\"—\"Just fine, thank you.\" “家裡人好嗎？”—“很好，謝謝。”"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of a singular noun when you want to make a general statement about things or people of that type. 用於單數名詞前，指某一類人或事物","examples":["An area in which the computer has made considerable strides in recent years is in playing chess. 近年來計算機取得重大進展的一個領域是國際象棋。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> with the name of a musical instrument when you are talking about someone's ability to play the instrument. 用於樂器名稱前，談論某人是否會演奏該樂器","examples":["Did you play the piano as a child? 你小時候彈鋼琴嗎？"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> with nationality adjectives and nouns to talk about the people who live in a country. 與表示國籍的形容詞和名詞連用，指該國國民","examples":["The Japanese, Americans, and even the French and Germans, judge economic policies by results. 日本人、美國人，甚至法國人和德國人，都是根據結果來評判經濟政策的好壞。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> with words such as \"rich,\" \"poor,\" \"old,\" or \"unemployed\" to refer to all people of a particular type. 表示一類人","examples":["Conditions for the poor in Los Angeles have not improved. 洛杉磯窮人的生活條件還未改善。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"If you want to refer to a whole family or to a married couple, you can make their surname into a plural and use <b>the</b> in front of it. 用於姓氏的複數形式前，表示一家人或一對夫婦","examples":["The Taylors decided that they would employ an architect to do the work. 泰勒夫婦決定僱個建築師來做這個工作。"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of an adjective when you are referring to a particular thing that is described by that adjective. 用於形容詞前表示該形容詞描繪的事物","examples":["He knows he's wishing for the impossible. 他知道自己在企盼不可能的事。"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> to indicate whether or not you have enough of the thing mentioned for a particular purpose. 表示所提及的東西是否有足夠的量","examples":["She may not have the money to maintain or restore her property. 她也許沒有足夠的錢來保留或維修自己的房產。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> with some titles, place names, and other names. 和稱呼、地名等名稱連用","examples":["...the Seattle Times. …《西雅圖時報》。","...the White House. …白宮。","...The Great Gatsby. …《了不起的蓋茨比》。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of numbers such as first, second, and third. 用於序數詞前","examples":["The meeting should take place on the fifth of May. 會議應於5月5日舉行。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of numbers when they refer to decades. 用於表示年代的數字前","examples":["It's sometimes hard to imagine how bad things were in the thirties. 有的時候很難想像三十年代的情況有多糟。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of superlative adjectives and adverbs. 用於形容詞或副詞最高階前","examples":["Brisk daily walks are still the best exercise for young and old alike. 每天快步走對老老少少來說仍然是最好的鍛鍊方式。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> in front of each of two comparative adjectives or adverbs when you are describing how one amount or quality changes in relation to another. 用於兩個形容詞或副詞的比較級前，表示其中一個隨另一個發生數量或性質的變化","examples":["The longer the therapy goes on, the more successful it will be. 治療的時間越長，療效就越好。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"When you express rates, prices, and measurements, you can use <b>the</b> to say how many units apply to each of the items being measured. (表示速度、價格或計量) 每","examples":["...cars that get more miles to the gallon. …每加侖汽油能多行駛幾英里的汽車。"]},{"num":"19.","zh":"You use <b>the</b> to indicate that something or someone is the most famous, important, or best thing of its kind. In spoken English, you put more stress on it, and in written English, you often underline it or write it in capitals or italics. 表示某人或某物是最有名的、最重要的或最好的；口語中需要重讀，書面語中常加下劃線或用大寫或斜體","examples":["The circus is the place to be this Saturday or Sunday. 馬戲團是這週六或週日的最佳去處。"]}]}]},"has":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"有，吃，得到，從事，允許，僱用，享有（have的第三人稱單數）；（親屬關係中）接受；拿；買到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Has</b> is the third person singular of the present tense of <b>have</b>. (have)的第三人稱單數現在式","examples":[]}]}]},"does":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"做；工作；有用（do 的第三人稱單數）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Does）（荷）杜斯（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Does</b> is the third person singular in the present tense of . (do)的第三人稱單數現在式","examples":[]}]}]},"had":{"summaries":[{"pos":"aux.","zh":"已經（用於過去完成時態）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"擁有；有（想法、主意、觀點等）；吃，喝（have 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Had</b> is the past tense and past participle of . (have)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"aux.","pos_name":"助動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Had</b> is sometimes used instead of \"if\" to begin a clause which refers to a situation that might have happened but did not. For example, the clause \"had he been elected\" means the same as \"if he had been elected.\" 代替(if)，引導一個表示虛擬假設條件的分句","examples":["Had he succeeded, he would have acquired a monopoly. 如果他那時成功了，他就會獲得壟斷地位。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>have been had</b>, someone has tricked you, for example by selling you something at too high a price. 受騙上當","examples":["If your customer thinks he's been had, you have to make him happy. 要是顧客覺得他受騙了，你得想法取悅他。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>has had it</b>, you mean they are in very serious trouble or have no hope of succeeding. 完蛋了","examples":["Unless she loses some weight, she's had it. 除非她減掉一些體重，否則她就完蛋了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you <b>have had it</b>, you mean that you are very tired of something or very annoyed about it, and do not want to continue doing it or it to continue happening. 受夠了","examples":["I've had it. Let's call it a day. 我受夠了。我們今天就到這裡吧。"]}]}]},"done":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完成的；煮熟的；不再發生的；為社會所接受的，得體的；上當受騙的；筋疲力盡的"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"行，好"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"做（do 的過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Done</b> is the past participle of . (do)的過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A task or activity that is <b>done</b> has been completed successfully. 完成的","examples":["When her deal is done, the client emerges with her purchase. 交易完成後，顧客拿著購買的東西出來了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When something that you are cooking is <b>done</b>, it has been cooked long enough and is ready. (飯菜) 做好了的","examples":["As soon as the cake is done, remove it from the oven. 蛋糕一烤好，就把它從烤箱裡拿出來。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You say \"<b>Done</b>\" when you are accepting a deal, arrangement, or bet that someone has offered to make with you. 行; 好 (表示接受建議或條件)","examples":["\"You lead and we'll look for it.\"—\"Done.\" “你帶路，我們來找!”—“好的！”"]}]}]},"were":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"是，在（are 的過去式）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Were）人名；（英、肯）沃爾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Were</b> is the plural and the second person singular of the past tense of . (be)的複數形式和第二人稱單數過去式","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Were</b> is sometimes used instead of \"was\" in certain structures, for example, in conditional clauses or after the verb \"wish.\" 有時代替(was)，如在條件從句中或動詞(wish)之後","examples":["He told a diplomat that he might withdraw if he were allowed to keep part of a disputed oil field. 他對一名外交官說，如果允許他保留一個有爭議的油田的一部分，他可能會撤出。"]}]}]},"an":{"summaries":[{"pos":"det.","zh":"一個（用於母音前）"},{"pos":"art.","zh":"一（在母音音素前）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>An</b> is used instead of \"a,\" the indefinite article, in front of words that begin with vowel sounds. 代替不定冠詞(a)，用在母音字母開頭的詞之前","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Netherlands Antilles 荷屬安的列斯群島","examples":[]}]}]},"who":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"誰，什麼人（用於疑問句）；……的人（引導定語從句）；誰（用於某些動詞或形容詞後引導從句）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>who</b> in questions when you ask about the name or identity of a person or group of people. 誰 (用於疑問句，詢問姓名和身份)","examples":["Who's there? 那是誰？","Who is the least popular man around here? 誰是這裡最不受歡迎的人？","\"You reminded me of somebody.\"—\"Who?\" “你讓我想起了一個人。”—“誰？”"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>who</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause where you talk about the identity of a person or a group of people. 誰 (用於特別是動詞和形容詞之後，引導從句，說明人的身份)","examples":["Police have not been able to find out who was responsible for the forgeries. 警察還未能發現誰是那些偽造案的元兇。","I went over to start up a conversation, asking her who she knew at the party. 我走過去攀談起來，問她在聚會上都認識誰。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>who</b> at the beginning of a relative clause when specifying the person or group of people you are talking about or when giving more information about them. …的人 (用於關係從句句首，具體說明所談論的人或給出更多相關資訊)","examples":["There are those who eat out for a special occasion, or treat themselves. 有那麼一些在特殊日子到飯館吃飯或犒勞自己的食客。"]}]}]},"whom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"誰（who 的賓格）；（用作關係代詞）……的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whom</b> in questions when you ask about the name or identity of a person or group of people. 誰 (用於詢問姓名或身份)","examples":["\"I want to send a telegram.\"—\"Fine, to whom?\" “我想發個電報。” — “好的，給誰？”","Whom did he expect to answer his phone? 他原來以為誰會接他的電話？"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whom</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause where you talk about the name or identity of a person or a group of people. 尤用在動詞和形容詞後，引導用來談論人的姓名或身份的從句","examples":["He asked whom I'd told about his having been away. 他問我對誰說過他不在的事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whom</b> at the beginning of a relative clause when specifying the person or group of people you are talking about or when giving more information about them. 用在關係從句的句首，具體指明被談論者或給出更多相關資訊等","examples":["One writer in whom I had taken an interest was Immanuel Velikovsky. 一位令我產生興趣的作家是伊曼紐爾·韋利科夫斯基。"]}]}]},"analyse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"分析，細察；分解，化驗；對……進行心理分析"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>analyse</b> something, you consider it carefully or use statistical methods in order to fully understand it. 分析","examples":["McCarthy was asked to analyse the data from the first phase of trials of the vaccine. 麥卡西被要求分析從這種疫苗試驗的第一階段取得的資料。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>analyse</b> something, you examine it using scientific methods in order to find out what it consists of. 化驗分析","examples":["We haven't had time to analyse those samples yet. 我們還沒有時間化驗分析那些樣本。"]}]}]},"whose":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"誰的（疑問代詞）；其，……的（關係代詞）"},{"pos":"det.","zh":"誰的（限定詞）；其，……的（關係限定詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"關係代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whose</b> at the beginning of a relative clause where you mention something that belongs to or is associated with the person or thing mentioned in the previous clause. 用在關係從句的句首，表示某事與前面分句中提到人或事有所屬關係或相關聯","examples":["I saw a man shouting at a driver whose car was blocking the street. 我看見一個人正衝著一個司機大喊，那個司機的車擋住了街道。","...a speedboat, whose fifteen-strong crew claimed to belong to China's navy. ... 一艘快艇，其船員超過15人，聲稱自己屬於中國海軍。"]}]},{"pos":"quest.","pos_name":"疑問詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whose</b> in questions to ask about the person or thing that something belongs to or is associated with. 用在疑問句中，詢問某物所屬或與之有關聯的人或事","examples":["\"Whose is this?\"—\"It's mine.\" “這是誰的？”—“是我的。”","\"It wasn't your fault, John.\"—\"Whose, then?\" “這並非你的錯，約翰。”—“那麼，是誰的呢？”","Whose car were they in? 他們坐在誰的車裡？","Whose daughter is she? 她是誰的女兒？"]}]},{"pos":"det.","pos_name":"限定詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>whose</b> after certain words, especially verbs and adjectives, to introduce a clause where you talk about the person or thing that something belongs to or is associated with. 尤用在動詞和形容詞後，引導談論某物所屬或與何人何事有關的從句","examples":["I'm wondering whose mother she is then. 我想知道她又會是誰的母親呢。","I can't remember whose idea it was. 我記不得這是誰的主意了。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Whose</b> is also a conjunction. 誰的","examples":["I wondered whose the coat was. 我思忖著那件大衣是誰的。"]}]}]},"anybody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何人，隨便哪一個人；（用於疑問句或條件句）有人；別人"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"重要人物（常用於否定或疑問）；平常人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Anybody</b> means the same as . 任何人","examples":[]}]}]},"anyone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何人，無論誰，任何一個人（泛指）；某個人，有人（用於疑問句、條件句等）；任何……的人（後接定語）；沒有一個人（用於否定句，與否定詞連用）；重要人物（用於 anyone who is anyone）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anyone</b> or <b>anybody</b> in statements with negative meaning to indicate in a general way that nobody is present or involved in an action. 任何人 (用於含否定意義的陳述句中)","examples":["I won't tell anyone I saw you here. 我不會告訴任何人我在這兒看見了你。","You needn't talk to anyone if you don't want to. 如果你不想你就不需要和任何人說話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>anyone</b> or <b>anybody</b> in questions and conditional clauses to ask or talk about whether someone is present or doing something. 某個人 (用於疑問句和條件分句中)","examples":["Why would anyone want that job? 為什麼會有人想要那份工作？","How can anyone look sad at an occasion like this? 在像這樣的一個場合怎麼會有人看上去悲傷呢？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>anyone</b> or <b>anybody</b> before words that indicate the kind of person you are talking about. 任何…的人 (接後置修飾語)","examples":["I always had been the person who achieved things before anyone else at my age. 我過去一直是那種在任何同齡人之前達成目標的人。","It's not a job for anyone who is slow with numbers. 這不是一種適合任何對數字反應慢的人的工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>anyone</b> or <b>anybody</b> to refer to a person when you are emphasizing that it could be any person out of a very large number of people. 任何一個人","examples":["Anyone could be doing what I'm doing. 任何一個人都可以做我在做的事。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anyone who is anyone</b> and <b>anybody who is anybody</b> to refer to people who are important or influential. 任何要人","examples":["It seems anyone who's anyone in business is going to the conference. 似乎商界的任何要人都要來參加這次會議。"]}]}]},"approximately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大約，大概"}],"sections":[]},"anything":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"任何事物 （用於含有否定意義的陳述句中）；某事物（用於疑問句和條件分句中）；任一事物（強調）；任何……的事物（接後置修飾語）；任何（接近、像……的）事物；（某範圍的）任何事物；重要東西，重要事物；某一限定範圍之內的任何一個數量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anything</b> in statements with negative meaning to indicate in a general way that nothing is present or that an action or event does not or cannot happen. 任何事物 (用於含有否定意義的陳述句中)","examples":["We can't do anything. 我們什麼也做不了。","She couldn't see or hear anything at all. 她根本什麼也看不見、聽不見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>anything</b> in questions and conditional clauses to ask or talk about whether something is present or happening. 某事物 (用於疑問句和條件分句中)","examples":["What happened, is anything wrong? 發生什麼了，有什麼問題嗎？","Did you find anything? 你發現什麼了嗎？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>anything</b> before words that indicate the kind of thing you are talking about. 任何…的事物 (接後置修飾語)","examples":["More than anything else, he wanted to become a teacher. 比起任何別的職業，他更想當老師。","Anything that's cheap this year will be even cheaper next year. 今年任何便宜的東西明年甚至會更便宜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>anything</b> to emphasize a possible thing, event, or situation, when you are saying that it could be any one of a very large number of things. 任一事物","examples":["He is young, fresh, and ready for anything. 他年輕、未經世故，任何事都願意嘗試。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>anything</b> in expressions such as <b>anything near</b>, <b>anything close to</b> and <b>anything like</b> to emphasize a statement that you are making. 任何 (接近、像…的) 事物","examples":["Doctors have decided the only way he can live anything near a normal life is to give him an operation. 醫生們已經確定了他能過任何接近正常生活的惟一方法是給他做個手術。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you do not want to be exact, you use <b>anything</b> to talk about a particular range of things or quantities. (某範圍的) 任何事物","examples":["...Chinese herbs that have cured anything from colds to broken bones. …治癒了從感冒到骨折的任何病的中草藥。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>anything but</b> in expressions such as <b>anything but quiet</b> and <b>anything but attractive</b> to emphasize that something is not the case. 絕對不","examples":["There's no evidence that Christopher told anyone to say anything but the truth. 沒有證據證明克里斯托弗叫任何人絕對不說真相。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can say that you <b>would not</b> do something <b>for anything</b> to emphasize that you definitely would not want to do or be a particular thing. 決不會做某事/決不會是某事","examples":["I wouldn't want to move for anything in the world. 說什麼我也不會搬走。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>if anything</b>, especially after a negative statement, to introduce a statement that adds to what you have just said. 如果有什麼的話","examples":["I never had to clean up after the lodgers. If anything, they did most of the cleaning. 我從來不必在房客們走後做打掃。要做的話，他們做大部分的清掃。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You can add <b>or anything</b> to the end of a clause or sentence in order to refer vaguely to other things that are or may be similar to what you just mentioned. 或什麼的","examples":["Listen, if you talk to Elizabeth or anything make sure you let everyone know, will you. 聽著，如果你和伊麗莎白講話或什麼的，一定要讓每個人都知道，你能做到吧。"]}]}]},"classroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"教室，課堂（教學環境）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>classroom</b> is a room in a school where lessons take place. 教室","examples":[]}]}]},"beginning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"開始，開端；序曲，開始部分；早期，初期；發端，起源"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"初級的，基本的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始，著手（begin 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>beginning</b> <b>of</b> an event or process is the first part of it. (事情、過程的) 開始","examples":["This was also the beginning of her recording career. 這也是她灌片生涯的開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>beginnings</b> <b>of</b> something are the signs or events which form the first part of it. 序曲","examples":["The discussions were the beginnings of a dialogue with Moscow. 這些會談是與莫斯科對話的序曲。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>beginning</b> <b>of</b> a period of time is the time at which it starts. (某時段的) 初期","examples":["The wedding will be at the beginning of March. 婚禮將於3月初舉行。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"The <b>beginning</b> <b>of</b> a piece of written material is the first words or sentences of it. (文章的) 開頭","examples":["...the question that was raised at the beginning of this chapter. …本章開頭提出的問題。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you talk about the <b>beginnings</b> of a person, company, or group, you are referring to their backgrounds or origins. 背景; 出身","examples":["His views come from his own humble beginnings. 他的觀點源自於他卑微的出身。"]}]}]},"certainly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"無疑，確定；當然，行（用於回答）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>certainly</b> to emphasize what you are saying when you are making a statement. 的確; 無疑地","examples":["The public is certainly getting tired of hearing about it. 公眾無疑厭倦了聽這方面的事。","The bombs are almost certainly part of a much bigger conspiracy. 幾乎可以確定這些炸彈是一個更大陰謀的一部分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>certainly</b> when you are agreeing with what someone has said. 當然","examples":["\"In any case you remained friends.\"—\"Certainly.\" “不管怎樣，你們還是朋友。”—“那當然。”"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You say <b>certainly not</b> to say \"no\" in a strong way. 當然不","examples":["\"Perhaps it would be better if I withdrew altogether.\"—\"Certainly not!\" “我完全退出的話情況或許會好些。” — “當然不是。”"]}]}]},"everybody":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"每個人，人人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Everybody</b> means the same as . 每人","examples":[]}]}]},"everyone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"每個人，人人，大家"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>everyone</b> or <b>everybody</b> to refer to all the people in a particular group. (某群體中的) 所有人","examples":["Everyone on the street was shocked when they heard the news. 聽到這個訊息，街上所有人都感到震驚。","Not everyone thinks that the government is being particularly generous. 並不是所有人都認為政府是在特別慷慨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>everyone</b> or <b>everybody</b> to refer to all people. 人人","examples":["Everyone wrestles with self-doubt and feels like a failure at times. 人人都會有與不自信作鬥爭、感覺自己是個失敗者的時候。","Everyone needs some free time for rest and relaxation. 人人都需要一些休息和放鬆的空閒時間。"]}]}]},"everywhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"到處，處處"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"每個地方，所有地方"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>everywhere</b> to refer to a whole area or to all the places in a particular area. (某區域內的) 所有地方; 各地","examples":["Working people everywhere object to paying taxes. 各地勞動人民都反對納稅。","We went everywhere together. 我們到哪裡都一起去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>everywhere</b> to refer to all the places that someone goes to. 所到之處","examples":["Mary Jo is still accustomed to travelling everywhere in style. 瑪麗·喬仍然習慣於很有氣派地到處旅行。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>everywhere</b> to emphasize that you are talking about a large number of places, or all possible places. 到處 (強調地方之多或所有可能的地方)","examples":["I saw her picture everywhere. 我到處看到她的照片。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>everywhere</b>, you mean that they are present in a place in very large numbers. 遍地 (強調在某地數量之多); 到處","examples":["There were cartons of cigarettes everywhere. 到處都是香菸盒。"]}]}]},"everything":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"每件事物，（有關的）一切，萬事；形勢，情況；最重要的東西"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Everything）（印、美、澳）艾維辛（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不定代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>everything</b> to refer to all the objects, actions, activities, or facts in a particular situation. (某種情形中的) 每件事物","examples":["He'd gone to Seattle long after everything else in his life had changed. 他生活中其他方面都改變了很久之後他去了西雅圖。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>everything</b> to refer to all possible or likely actions, activities, or situations. 所有事物","examples":["\"This should have been decided long before now.\"—\"We can't think of everything.\" “這在此前早該定下了。”—“我們不可能事事都考慮。”","Najib and I do everything together. 納吉布和我什麼事情都一起做。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>everything</b> to refer to a whole situation or to life in general. 一切情況; 整體生活","examples":["She says everything is going smoothly. 她說一切進展順利。","Is everything all right? 一切都好嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>everything</b>, you mean you consider them to be the most important thing in your life, or the most important thing that there is. 至關重要的事物","examples":["I love him. He is everything to me. 我愛他。他對我來說比什麼都重要。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you say that someone or something has <b>everything</b>, you mean they have all the things or qualities that most people consider to be desirable. 一切 (值得要的東西)","examples":["This man had everything. He had the house, the sailboat and a full life with friends and family. 這個男人擁有一切。他有房子、帆船以及親朋相伴的圓滿生活。"]}]}]},"frequently":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"經常地，頻繁地"}],"sections":[]},"birthday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生日，誕辰；出生日期，誕生的日子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>birthday</b> is the anniversary of the date on which you were born. 生日","examples":["On his birthday she sent him presents. 他生日那天，她送了他禮物。"]}]}]},"exciting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人興奮的，令人激動的；驚險刺激的（尤指無法預知下一步將發生什麼）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使興奮，使激動；激發，引起（excite 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>exciting</b>, it makes you feel very happy or enthusiastic. 令人興奮的","examples":["The race itself is very exciting. 比賽本身就令人非常興奮。"]}]}]},"european":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"歐洲的；歐洲人的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"歐洲人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>European</b> means belonging or relating to, or coming from Europe. 歐洲的","examples":["...in some other European countries. …在其他一些歐洲國家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>European</b> is a person who comes from Europe. 歐洲人","examples":["Three-quarters of working-age Americans work, compared with roughly 60% of Europeans. 3/4處於工作年齡的美國人在工作，相比之下歐洲約為60%。"]}]}]},"finally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"終於；總之，最後；決定性地，不可變更地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>finally</b> to suggest that something happens after a long period of time, usually later than you wanted or expected it to happen. 終於","examples":["The food finally arrived at the end of last week and distribution began. 食物終於在上週末抵達並開始分發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>finally</b> to indicate that something is last in a series of actions or events. 最後","examples":["The action slips from comedy to melodrama and finally to tragedy. 劇情由喜劇慢慢發展成鬧劇，最後又演變為悲劇。"]}]}]},"probably":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"大概，或許"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>probably</b> the case, you think that it is likely to be the case, although you are not sure. 可能 (為事實) 地","examples":["The White House probably won't make this plan public until July. 白宮可能要到7月份才會公佈這項計劃。","Van Gogh is probably the best-known painter in the world. 梵高可能是世界上最知名的畫家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>probably</b> when you want to make your opinion sound less forceful or definite, so that you do not offend people. 可能 (用以緩和語氣)","examples":["What would he think of their story? He'd probably think she and Lenny were both crazy! 他會怎麼看他們的故事呢。他可能會想她和倫尼都瘋了！"]}]}]},"suddenly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"突然地，出乎意料地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>suddenly</b>, it happens quickly and unexpectedly. 突然地","examples":["Suddenly, she looked ten years older. 突然間，她看上去老了10歲。","Her expression suddenly altered. 她的表情突然變了。"]}]}]},"usually":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"通常地，經常地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>usually</b> happens, it is the thing that most often happens in a particular situation. 通常","examples":["The best information about hotels usually comes from friends and acquaintances who have been there. 有關旅館的最佳資訊通常來自曾經去過那兒的朋友和熟人。","Usually, the work is boring. 通常這種工作很乏味。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>more than usually</b> to show that something shows even more of a particular quality than it normally does. 比平常更甚地","examples":["She felt more than usually hungry after her excursion. 遠足後她感到非同尋常地飢餓。"]}]}]},"cheeseburger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"乳酪漢堡"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cheeseburger</b> is a hamburger with a slice of cheese on top, served on a bun. 乳酪漢堡","examples":[]}]}]},"becomes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"變得，變成，成為（become 的第三人稱單數現在時）；適合，與……相稱（become 的第三人稱單數現在時，及物用法）；用於 what becomes of... 結構，表示……怎麼樣了，……遭遇了什麼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-link.","pos_name":"連繫動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>becomes</b> a particular thing, they start to change and develop into that thing, or start to develop the characteristics mentioned. 變成","examples":["I first became interested in Islam while I was doing my nursing training. 我在進行護理訓練的時候，我初次對伊斯蘭教產生了興趣。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>becomes</b> someone, it makes them look attractive or it seems right for them. 適合; 與…相稱","examples":["Does khaki become you? 卡其布適合你嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you wonder <b>what</b> has <b>become of</b> someone or something, you wonder where they are and what has happened to them. (某人、某事物) 怎麼樣了","examples":["She thought constantly about her family; she might never know what had become of them. 她經常想著她的家人；她也許永遠都不知道他們怎麼樣了。"]}]}]},"wrote":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"寫（write 的過去式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wrote</b> is the past tense of . (write)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"yourself":{"summaries":[{"pos":"pron.","zh":"你自己"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"反身代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A speaker or writer uses <b>yourself</b> to refer to the person that they are talking or writing to. <b>Yourself</b> is used when the object of a verb or preposition refers to the same person as the subject of the verb. 你自己; 你們自己 (用於某動作的賓語和主語是同一人時)","examples":["Have the courage to be honest with yourself and about yourself. 有勇氣對自己誠實並對別人誠實。","Your baby depends on you to look after yourself properly while you are pregnant. 你的寶寶靠你懷孕時好好照顧你自己。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>yourself</b> to emphasize the person that you are referring to. 你自己 (用以強調所指之人)","examples":["You can't convince others if you yourself aren't convinced. 如果你沒有使你自己信服你就不能使別人信服。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>yourself</b> instead of \"you\" for emphasis or in order to be more polite when \"you\" is the object of a verb or preposition. 你自己 (代替)(you)(作動詞或介詞的賓語以表示強調或更禮貌)","examples":["A wealthy man like yourself is bound to make an enemy or two along the way. 像你自己這樣的一個有錢人註定會在前進的路上樹一兩個敵人。"]}]}]},"orderings":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"n．排序：將一組物件按照某種規則或順序排列的過程。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"any of a number of categories of relations that permit at least some members of their domain to be placed in order. A <b>linear</b> or <b>simple ordering</b> is reflexive, antisymmetric, transitive, and connected, as <b>less than or equal to</b> on the integers. A <b>partial ordering</b> is reflexive, antisymmetric, and transitive, as set inclusion. Either of these orderings is called <b>strict</b> if it is asymmetric instead of reflexive and antisymmetric. It is a <b>well-ordering</b> if every nonempty subset has a least member under the relation 排序","examples":[]}]}]},"boston":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"波士頓（美國城市）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a card game for four, played with two packs (四人玩兩套牌的)波士頓牌戲","examples":[]}]}]},"neighbours":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鄰居；同胞；仁慈的人（neighbour 的複數）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"鄰近；親近（neighbour 的三單形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>neighbour</b> is someone who lives near you. 鄰居","examples":["My neighbour spies on me through a crack in the fence. 我的鄰居透過籬笆牆的縫隙窺探我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the person who is standing or sitting next to you as your <b>neighbour</b>. 鄰近的人","examples":["The woman prodded her neighbour and whispered urgently in his ear. 那個女人戳了一下她旁邊的人，急切地對他耳語起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to something which stands next to something else of the same kind as its <b>neighbour</b>. 鄰近的同類物","examples":["...its big oil-rich neighbour. …它那幅員遼闊、石油資源豐富的鄰國。"]}]}]},"poems":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詩歌，詩作，詩集（poem 的複數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>poem</b> is a piece of writing in which the words are chosen for their beauty and sound and are carefully arranged, often in short lines that rhyme. 詩","examples":["...a book of love poems. …一本愛情詩集。"]}]}]},"wireless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無線的，使用無線電訊號的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"無線電發射和接收系統；<舊>無線電收音機"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"用無線電報與…聯絡，打無線電話"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wireless</b> technology uses radio waves rather than electricity and therefore does not require any wires. 無線電的","examples":["...the fast-growing wireless communication market. …快速增長的無線通訊市場。"]}]}]},"inflammatory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（醫學）炎症性的，炎性的；煽動性的，使人激憤的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse someone of saying or doing <b>inflammatory</b> things, you mean that what they say or do is likely to make people react very angrily. 使人激憤的","examples":["...nationalist policies that are too drastic and inflammatory. …過於激烈、煽動性強的民族主義政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>inflammatory</b> condition or disease is one in which the patient suffers from inflammation. 炎症的","examples":["...the inflammatory reactions that occur in asthma. …出現於哮喘的炎症反應。"]}]}]},"continues":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"繼續，持續，連續；中斷後繼續，接著說；保持，繼續處於原有狀態或職位；繼續行進；延伸，擴充套件（continue 的第三人稱單數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>continues</b> <b>to</b> do something, they keep doing it and do not stop. 繼續","examples":["I hope they continue to fight for equal justice after I'm gone. 我希望我走後他們繼續為司法公正而奮鬥。","Diana and Roy Jarvis are determined to continue working when they reach retirement age. 戴安娜·賈維斯和羅伊·賈維斯決心到退休年齡後還繼續工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>continues</b> or if you <b>continue</b> it, it does not stop. 使繼續; 繼續","examples":["He insisted that the conflict would continue until conditions were met for a ceasefire. 他堅持認為衝突會持續下去，直至停火條件得到滿足為止。","Outside the building people continue their vigil, huddling around bonfires. 在樓外，人們圍聚在篝火旁繼續守夜。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> something or <b>continue</b> with something, you start doing it again after a break or interruption. (某人在歇息或被打斷後) 繼續 (做某事或某事)","examples":["I went up to my room to continue with my packing. 我上我房間去繼續收拾行李。","She looked up for a minute and then continued drawing. 她抬頭看了一會兒，然後繼續畫。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something <b>continues</b> or if you <b>continue</b> it, it starts again after a break or interruption. (某事在停頓或被打斷後) 繼續","examples":["He denies 18 charges. The trial continues today. 他否認18項指控。審判今天繼續。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b>, you begin speaking again after a pause or interruption. (在停頓或被打斷後) 繼續說","examples":["\"You have no right to intimidate this man,\" Alison continued. “你無權威脅這個男人，”愛麗森繼續說。","Tony drank some coffee before he continued. 託尼喝了些咖啡繼續講。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> <b>as</b> something or <b>continue</b> in a particular state, you remain in a particular job or state. 繼續 (原有工作或狀態)","examples":["He had hoped to continue as a full-time career officer. 他原本希望繼續當全職警官。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>continue</b> in a particular direction, you keep walking or travelling in that direction. 繼續走","examples":["He continued rapidly up the path, not pausing until he neared the Chapter House. 他繼續快速地沿著那小徑走，直到走近牧師會禮堂才停下腳步。"]}]}]},"ambiance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"氛圍，周圍環境，格調；背景音（同 ambience）；（Ambiance）（法、美、巴西）安比昂斯（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"devastation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"毀壞，破壞；荒廢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Devastation</b> is severe and widespread destruction or damage. 毀壞","examples":["The war brought massive devastation and loss of life to the region. 戰爭給該地區造成巨大的破壞以及生命的喪失。"]}]}]},"biomechanics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生物力學，也譯“生物機械學”；又指生物體、器官或動作的力學特徵與運動機制"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the study of the mechanics of the movement of living organisms 生物力學","examples":[]}]}]},"relatively":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"相當地，相對地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Relatively</b> means to a certain degree, especially when compared with other things of the same kind. 相對地","examples":["The sums needed are relatively small. 所需金額相對較小。"]}]}]},"hurried":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"匆忙的，倉促的；草率的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"hurry 的過去式和過去分詞：催促；匆忙進行；急派"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>hurried</b> action is done quickly, because you do not have much time to do it in. 倉促完成的","examples":["...a hurried breakfast. …倉促吃的一頓早餐。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hurried</b> action is done suddenly, in reaction to something that has just happened. (行動) 突然應急採取的","examples":["There had been a hurried overnight redrafting of the text. 該文字被連夜做了改寫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"Someone who is <b>hurried</b> does things more quickly than they should because they do not have much time to do them. 倉促的","examples":["Parisians on the street often looked worried, hurried, and unfriendly. 街上的巴黎人常常看上去憂心忡忡，匆匆忙忙，還不太友好。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"匆忙地","examples":["...students hurriedly taking notes. …匆忙做著筆記的學生們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"匆忙地","examples":["The moment she saw it, she blushed and hurriedly left the room. 她一看見它臉就紅了，並慌忙地走出了房間。"]}]}]},"expecting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"期待，預期，企盼（expect 的現在分詞/動名詞）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>懷孕的，懷有身孕的（常用於 be expecting）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"pregnant 懷孕的","examples":[]}]}]},"charles":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"查爾斯（男子名，也用作姓氏）"}],"sections":[]},"draughts":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（英國英語）國際跳棋，西洋跳棋（美式英語作 checkers）；穿堂風，冷氣流（draught 的複數，美式拼寫為 drafts）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Draughts</b> is a game for two people, played with 24 round pieces on a board. 西洋跳棋","examples":["...a game of draughts. …一盤西洋跳棋遊戲。"]}]}]},"arrived":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"到達，抵達（arrive 的過去式和過去分詞）；（船舶等）抵港；arrived at：到達；得出（結論），達成（決定）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"已到達的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a person or vehicle <b>arrives</b> at a place, they come to it from somewhere else. 到達","examples":["Fresh groups of guests arrived. 新客成批到達了。","...a small group of commuters waiting for their train, which arrived on time. …幾個等候火車準點到達的通勤者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When you <b>arrive</b> at a place, you come to it for the first time in order to stay, live, or work there. 初次抵達","examples":["...in the old days before the European settlers arrived in the country. …在歐洲定居者們初次到這個國家之前的古老歲月。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something such as letter or meal <b>arrives</b>, it is brought or delivered to you. 送達","examples":["Breakfast arrived while he was in the bathroom. 早餐在他在浴室裡時送到了。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When something such as a new product or invention <b>arrives</b>, it becomes available. (產品、發明) 問世","examples":["Several long-awaited movies will finally arrive in the stores this month. 幾部期盼已久的影片最終將於本月在各家商店露面。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"When a particular moment or event <b>arrives</b>, it happens, especially after you have been waiting for it or expecting it. 到來","examples":["The time has arrived when I need to give up smoking. 我需要戒菸的時候到了。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"When you <b>arrive at</b> something such as a decision, you decide something after thinking about it or discussing it. 達成","examples":["...if the jury cannot arrive at a unanimous decision. …如果陪審團不能達成一致判決。"]}]}]},"architectural":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"建築學的，建築方面的；與建築物相似的；"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Architectural</b> means relating to the design and construction of buildings. 有關建築的","examples":["...Tibet's architectural heritage. …西藏的建築遺產。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"建築上","examples":["The old city centre is architecturally rich. 這座古老的市中心在建築上多姿多彩。"]}]}]},"sank":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"sink 的過去式（及物）：使下沉；使沉沒；擊沉；使陷入"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"sink 的過去式（不及物）：下沉；沉沒；墜落；陷入；下降"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Sank）德語人名“贊克”"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sank</b> is the past tense of . (sink)的過去式","examples":[]}]}]},"borrowed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"借來的，借入的；借用的，非原創的，外來的（多指詞語、思想、風格等從他人或他處採用）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"borrow 的過去式和過去分詞：借，借入；借用，採用；模仿"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"borrowed time：本應結束卻仍在延續的時間，苟延殘喘的時光（常用於 live on borrowed time）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> something that belongs to someone else, you take it or use it for a period of time, usually with their permission. 借","examples":["Can I borrow a pen please? 我可以借支筆嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> money <b>from</b> someone or <b>from</b> a bank, they give it to you and you agree to pay it back at some time in the future. 借 (錢)","examples":["Morgan borrowed $5,000 from his father to form the company 20 years ago. 摩根20年前向他父親借了$5000來建立這家公司。","It's so expensive to borrow from finance companies. 向金融公司借款費用真夠高的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> a book <b>from</b> a library, you take it away for a fixed period of time. 借 (書)","examples":["I couldn't afford to buy any, so I borrowed them from the library. 我一本也買不起，所以從圖書館借了這些。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>borrow</b> something such as a word or an idea from another language or from another person's work, you use it in your own language or work. 借用 (思想、詞等)","examples":["I borrowed his words for my book's title. 我借用他的話作為我的書名。"]}]}]},"disappeared":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"消失的，消失了的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"消失，不見；失蹤，丟失；不復存在，滅絕（disappear 的過去式和過去分詞）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"被秘密逮捕（或處決）的人（常作 the disappeared）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something <b>disappears</b>, you mean that you can no longer see them, usually because you or they have changed position. 消失","examples":["The black car drove away from them and disappeared. 黑色的小汽車駛離了他們便消失了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>disappears</b>, they go away or are taken away somewhere where nobody can find them. 失蹤","examples":["...a Japanese woman who disappeared thirteen years ago. …一位13年前失蹤的日本婦女。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>disappears</b>, it stops existing or happening. 滅絕","examples":["The immediate threat of the past has disappeared and the security situation in Europe has significantly improved. 過去的直接威脅不復存在了，歐洲的安全狀況有重大改善。"]}]}]},"discounts":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"discount 的複數形式：折扣，優惠，折價；扣減額；（金融）貼現，貼現金額"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"discount 的第三人稱單數形式：打折扣，降價出售；低估；不理會，漠視；（金融）貼現"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>discount</b> is a reduction in the usual price of something. 折扣","examples":["They are often available at a discount. 它們經常可以以折扣價買到。","All full-time staff get a 20 percent discount. 所有全職員工都可以享受8折優惠。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a shop or company <b>discounts</b> an amount or percentage from something that they are selling, they take the amount or percentage off the usual price. 對…打折","examples":["This has forced airlines to discount fares heavily in order to spur demand. 這已經迫使多家航空公司對機票大幅打折以刺激需求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>discount</b> an idea, fact, or theory, you consider that it is not true, not important, or not relevant. 不理會","examples":["However, traders tended to discount the rumour. 但是，商人們傾向於不理會這個傳聞。"]}]}]},"above-average":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"超出平均水平的；異於尋常的"}],"sections":[]},"abort":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）流產，墮（胎）；（由於問題或故障）中止，使夭折；（胚胎器官，有機體）發育不全，敗育"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>（飛行、航天任務或其他事業的）中斷，取消；夭折的計劃（或事業）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an unborn baby <b>is aborted</b>, the pregnancy is ended deliberately and the baby is not born alive. 使流產","examples":["Her lover walked out on her after she had aborted their child. 在她打掉了他們的孩子之後，她的情人離開了她。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>aborts</b> a process, plan, or activity, they stop it before it has been completed. 中途放棄","examples":["When the decision was made to abort the mission, there was great confusion. 中途放棄這次任務的決定引起了嚴重混亂。"]}]}]},"abruptly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"突然地；唐突地；陡然"}],"sections":[]},"should":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用於糾正別人）應該；（用於建議）該，可以；（表示預期）應該會；（表示與預期相反）本應；（與 I 或 we 連用代替 would，表示虛擬結果）就將；（用於 that 從句，表示建議或安排）可以；（用於 that 從句，表示感情）竟然會；（表示拒絕、惱怒或驚奇）竟會；（表示可能）假如，萬一；將（用作 shall 的過去式）；（與 I 和 we 連用，表示客氣地請求）想；當然，真的（用於強調自己所相信或所期待的）；（表示強調有趣、驚訝或印象深刻）真該"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> when you are saying what would be the right thing to do or the right state for something to be in. 應該","examples":["I should exercise more. 我應該多鍛鍊。","He's never going to be able to forget it. And I don't think he should. 他將永遠都不會忘記它。而且我認為他也不應該忘記。","Should our children be taught to swim at school? 我們的孩子應該在學校學游泳嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> to give someone an order to do something, or to report an official order. 必須; 應該","examples":["18-year-olds are sent reminders that they should register to vote. 給18歲的人派送了通知單，提醒他們應該登記投票。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something <b>should have</b> happened, you mean that it did not happen, but that you wish it had. If you say that something <b>should not have</b> happened, you mean that it did happen, but that you wish it had not. (本來) 應該","examples":["I should have gone this morning but I was feeling a bit ill. 今早我本應該去的，可是我感到有點不舒服。","You should have written to the area manager again. 你本應該再寫信給區域經理。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> when you are saying that something is probably the case or will probably happen in the way you are describing. If you say that something <b>should have</b> happened by a particular time, you mean that it will probably have happened by that time. 應該會","examples":["You should have no problem with reading this language. 你讀這種語言應該不會有問題。","The doctor said it will take six weeks and I should be fine by then. 醫生說這將需要6周時間而我到時應該會康復。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> in questions when you are asking someone for advice, permission, or information. (用於徵求意見、同意、資訊等) 該; 可以","examples":["Should I take out a loan? 我該去貸款嗎？","What should I do? 我該怎麼辦？"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You say \"<b>I should</b>,\" usually with the expression \"if I were you,\" when you are giving someone advice by telling them what you would do if you were in their position. (透過假設來提建議) 會","examples":["I should look out if I were you! 如果我是你，我就會小心的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> in conditional clauses when you are talking about things that might happen. 用於條件句，表示事情發生的可能性","examples":["If you should be fired, your health and pension benefits will not be automatically cut off. 如果你失業了，你的健康津貼和養老金將不會自動中斷。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> in \"that\" clauses after certain verbs, nouns, and adjectives when you are talking about a future event or situation. (用於某些動詞、名詞和形容詞後的that從句中，表示將來的事件或情形) 應該","examples":["He raised his glass and indicated that I should do the same. 他舉起了他的玻璃杯，暗示我應該照著做。","I insisted that we should have a look at every car. 我堅持我們應該把每輛車都看一看。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> in expressions such as <b>I should think</b> and <b>I should imagine</b> to indicate that you think something is true but you are not sure. 用於(I should think)和(I should imagine)中表示不確定的想法","examples":["I should think it's going to rain soon. 我覺得很快就會下雨了。"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>should</b> in expressions such as <b>You should have seen us</b> and <b>You should have heard him</b> to emphasize how funny, shocking, or impressive something that you experienced was. (表示強調有趣、驚訝或印象深刻) 真該","examples":["You should have heard him last night! 你真該聽到他昨晚說的話！"]}]}]},"abusive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"辱罵的，侮辱的；凌辱的，虐待的；受虐待的；舞弊的，不法的；濫用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>abusive</b> behaves in a cruel and violent way toward other people. 惡毒殘暴的","examples":["He became violent and abusive toward Ben's mother. 他對待本的媽媽變得粗暴而又殘酷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Abusive</b> language is extremely rude and insulting. 侮辱的","examples":["I did not use any foul or abusive language. 我沒有使用過任何粗話或侮辱性的語言。"]}]}]},"accessibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（地方）易於進入性，（物品）易於接近性；易使用性，可及性；易懂性"}],"sections":[]},"absolutely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"絕對地，完全地；確實地，極其；（強調同意或允許）當然，對極了；專制地，獨裁地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Absolutely</b> means totally and completely. 絕對地","examples":["Joan is absolutely right. 瓊絕對正確。","I absolutely refuse to get married. 我絕對拒絕結婚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Some people say <b>absolutely</b> as an emphatic way of saying yes or of agreeing with someone. They say <b>absolutely not</b> as an emphatic way of saying no or of disagreeing with someone. 絕對地","examples":["\"It's worrying that they're doing things without training though, isn't it?\"—\"Absolutely.\" “可是他們未經培訓就幹，這真讓人擔憂，是不是？”—“絕對是。”"]}]}]},"accident-prone":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易出事故的；易惹事故的；事故率超出一般的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>accident prone</b>, you mean that a lot of accidents or other unpleasant things happen to them. 易出事故的","examples":[]}]}]},"acclaim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"讚揚，稱讚，為……喝彩"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"讚揚，稱譽，高度評價"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is acclaimed</b>, they are praised enthusiastically. 熱烈稱讚","examples":["The restaurant has been widely acclaimed for its excellent French cuisine. 這個餐館因出眾的法式烹調而受到廣泛讚揚。","He was acclaimed as America's greatest filmmaker. 他被讚譽為美國最偉大的電影製片人。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受到高度讚揚的","examples":["She has published six highly acclaimed novels. 她已經出版了6本受到高度讚揚的小說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Acclaim</b> is public praise for someone or something. 讚揚","examples":["Angela Bassett has won critical acclaim for her excellent performance. 安傑拉·巴西特因她出色的表演而贏得了評論界的讚揚。"]}]}]},"acclimatize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使適應新環境，使服水土"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"適應新環境，服水土"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>acclimatize</b> or <b>are acclimatized</b> <b>to</b> a new situation, place, or climate, you become used to it. 使適應; 適應","examples":["I help them acclimatize to living in the U.S. 我幫助他們適應在美國的生活。","I hadn't had any time to acclimatize myself. 我那時沒有時間來適應環境。","It does take time to acclimatize, especially for guys who haven't grown up in an urban environment. 這確實需要時間適應，特別是對於那些不在城市長大的人。","Some ethnic groups can't become acclimatized to the mainstream. 一些種族群體不能適應主流。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"適應","examples":["...gradual acclimatization to strenuous exercise. …對高強度訓練的逐漸適應。"]}]}]},"according":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"按照，根據，依照（according to，後接名詞或名詞短語）；據……所說（according to，引出訊息來源）"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"根據，取決於（according as，後接從句）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"相符的，相應的，一致的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"accord 的現在分詞（給予；符合，一致）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>accord</b> between countries or groups of people is a formal agreement; for example, to end a war. 協議","examples":["UNITA was legalized as a political party under the 1991 peace accords. 根據1991年和平協議，安盟作為一個政黨被合法化了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are accorded</b> a particular kind of treatment, people act toward you or treat you in that way. 給予 (某種待遇)","examples":["His predecessor was accorded an equally tumultuous welcome. 他的前任受到了同樣熱烈的歡迎。","On his return home, the government accorded him the rank of Colonel. 在他回國時，該國政府授予他上校軍銜。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>of its own accord</b>, it seems to happen by itself, without anyone making it happen. 自動地","examples":["In many cases the disease will clear up of its own accord. 在很多情況下這種疾病會自動地痊癒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>of</b> your <b>own accord</b>, you do it because you want to, without being asked or forced. 自願地","examples":["He did not quit as France's prime minister of his own accord. 他不是自願地辭去法國總理一職的。"]}]}]},"accrue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（利益、好處等）產生，形成；（錢不斷地）積累，增加；準備累算償付"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If money or interest <b>accrues</b>, it gradually increases in amount over a period of time. 累積 (過程)","examples":["I owed $5,000 – part of this was accrued interest. 我欠$5000–這其中的一部分是累積的利息。","While they may use a credit card for convenience, affluent people never let interest charges accrue. 雖然有錢人可能為了方便而使用信用卡，他們從來不讓利息費累積。"]}]}]},"acquisitive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"渴望得到的，貪婪的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or an organization as <b>acquisitive</b>, you do not approve of them because you think they are too concerned with getting new possessions. 貪得無厭的","examples":["We live in an acquisitive society. 我們活在一個貪婪的社會里。"]}]}]},"activate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"啟用，使活化；使參戰；（尤指透過加熱）加速……的反應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a device or process <b>is</b> <b>activated</b>, something causes it to start working. 啟用","examples":["Video cameras with night vision can be activated by movement. 有夜視功能的攝像機能被物體的活動啟用。"]}]}]},"addictive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"使人成癮的；使欲罷不能的，使人入迷的；（人）容易沉迷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a drug is <b>addictive</b>, people who take it cannot stop taking it. 使人上癮的","examples":["Cigarettes are highly addictive. 香菸非常容易使人上癮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>addictive</b> is so enjoyable that it makes you want to do it or have it a lot. 使人著迷的","examples":["Video film-making can quickly become addictive. 影片電影製作能迅速讓人著迷。"]}]}]},"adapter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"介面卡，轉接器，接合器；改編者；（較少見）適應者"}],"sections":[]},"additionally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"另外，此外；分外地，更加"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>additionally</b> to introduce something extra such as an extra fact or reason. 另外","examples":["All teachers are qualified to teach their native language. Additionally, we select our teachers for their engaging personalities. 所有教師都具備教授其母語的資格。另外，我們還根據富有魅力的個性來選擇我們的教師。"]}]}]},"adept":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"熟練的，擅長的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"能手，內行"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>adept</b> <b>at</b> something can do it skilfully. 嫻熟的","examples":["He's usually very adept at keeping his private life out of the media. 他通常十分擅長於使他的私生活遠離媒體。"]}]}]},"really":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"真正地，事實上；確實的，的確（用於加強語氣）；很，十分；（用於帶有隱含的否定回答的疑問句和感嘆句）真的，是嗎；用於緩和否定語氣"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"真的（用來表示興趣、驚奇或疑惑）；真是的！（用於表示生氣或不贊成）；是啊！（用於表示同意某人的意見）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>really</b> to emphasize a statement. 的確 (用於強調)","examples":["I'm very sorry. I really am. 我很抱歉。真的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>really</b> to emphasize an adjective or adverb. (用於強調形容詞或副詞) 非常","examples":["It was really good. 這非常好。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>really</b> when you are discussing the real facts about something, in contrast to the ones someone wants you to believe. 實際上","examples":["My father didn't really love her. 我父親實際上並不愛她。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"People use <b>really</b> in questions and negative statements when they want you to answer \"no.\" 果真 (用在疑問句和否定句中，引出否定回答)","examples":["Do you really think he would be that stupid? 你果真認為他那麼蠢嗎？"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you refer to a time when something <b>really</b> begins to happen, you are emphasizing that it starts to happen at that time to a much greater extent and much more seriously than before. 真正地 (用於強調事情的發生較以前有所擴大且變得更嚴重)","examples":["That's when the pressure really started. 那是壓力真正開始的時候。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"People sometimes use <b>really</b> to slightly reduce the force of a negative statement. 真地 (用在否定句中，減輕語氣)","examples":["I'm not really surprised. 我並不真地驚訝。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say <b>really</b> to express surprise or disbelief at what someone has said. 真的 (表示驚訝或對別人的話不相信)","examples":["\"We discovered it was totally the wrong decision.\"—\"Really?\" “我們發現那完全是個錯誤的決定。”—“真的嗎？”"]}]}]},"actually":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"實際上，事實上；（用於開始新話題）其實；竟然，居然"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>actually</b> to indicate that a situation exists or happened, or to emphasize that it is true. 實際上 (指某種情形真實存在)","examples":["One afternoon, I got bored and actually fell asleep for a few minutes. 一天下午，我感到很無聊，實際上有幾分鐘還睡著了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>actually</b> when you are correcting or contradicting someone. 事實上 (用於糾正或反駁他人)","examples":["No, I'm not a student. I'm a doctor, actually. 不，我不是一名學生。事實上，我是一名醫生。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>actually</b> when you are politely expressing an opinion that other people might not have expected from you. (用於禮貌地表達觀點) 說實話","examples":["\"Do you think it's a good idea to socialize with one's patients?\"—\"Actually, I do, I think it's a great idea.\" “你覺得和病人交往是個好主意嗎？”——“說實話，我覺得是，我覺得這是一個非常好的主意。”"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>actually</b> to introduce a new topic into a conversation. (用於開始新話題) 其實","examples":["Well actually, John, I called you for some advice. 嗯，約翰，其實我打電話給你是尋求一些建議。"]}]}]},"adhere":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"黏附，附著；遵守，遵循（規定或協議）；擁護，持有（觀點或信仰）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>adhere</b> <b>to</b> a rule or agreement, you act in the way that it says you should. 遵守","examples":["All members of the association adhere to a strict code of practice. 所有該協會的成員都遵守嚴格的業務守則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>adheres</b> <b>to</b> something else, it sticks firmly to it. 緊貼","examples":["Small particles adhere to the seed. 微小的粒子緊貼著種子。"]}]}]},"admittance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"進入許可，加入許可；（物理）導納；通道"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Admittance</b> is the act of entering a place or institution or the right to enter it. 進入; 進入權","examples":["We had not been able to gain admittance to the flat. 我們還未能獲得進入那所公寓的權利。"]}]}]},"adoption":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"採用，接受；<英>推選；正式透過；選擇；收養，領養"}],"sections":[]},"adorn":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"裝飾；使生色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>adorns</b> a place or an object, it makes it look more beautiful. 裝飾","examples":["His watercolour designs adorn a wide range of books. 他的水彩設計裝飾著各種各樣的書籍。"]}]}]},"adversary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敵手，對手"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"對立的，敵對的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>adversary</b> is someone you are competing with, or arguing or fighting against. 對手","examples":["His political adversaries would like to discredit him. 他的政敵想破壞他的聲譽。"]}]}]},"adverse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不利的，有害的；相反的；敵對的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Adverse</b> decisions, conditions, or effects are unfavourable to you. 不利的","examples":["The police said Mr. Hadfield's decision would have no adverse effect on the progress of the investigation. 警方說哈德菲爾德先生的決定對於調查進展不會有任何不利的影響。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不利地","examples":["Price changes must not adversely affect the living standards of the people. 價格變化一定不能負面地影響人們的生活水平。"]}]}]},"after-tax":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"稅後；納稅後的"}],"sections":[]},"affirmative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"肯定的，同意的；（法律提案）須議會投票贊成生效的；積極的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"同意，贊成；陳述詞，肯定詞；贊成的一方"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"<美>同意的，贊成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>affirmative</b> word or gesture indicates that you agree with what someone has said or that the answer to a question is \"yes.\" 肯定的 (言辭、手勢)","examples":["Haig was desperately eager for an affirmative answer. 黑格極渴望得到一個肯定的回答。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In grammar, an <b>affirmative</b> clause is positive and does not contain a negative word. (語法中) 肯定的 (分句)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you reply to a question <b>in the affirmative</b>, you say \"yes\" or make a gesture that means \"yes.\" (回答問題) 肯定地","examples":["He asked me if I was ready. I answered in the affirmative. 他問我是否準備好了。我肯定地回答了。"]}]}]},"advisable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明智的，可取的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you tell someone that <b>it</b> is <b>advisable</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are suggesting that they should do it, because it is sensible or is likely to achieve the result they want. 可取的","examples":["Because of the popularity of the region, it is advisable to book hotels or camp sites in advance. 鑑於該地區的受歡迎度，事先預訂旅館或露營地是可取的。"]}]}]},"air-conditioner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"空調，空調機（可數名詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>air conditioner</b> is a machine that keeps the air in a building cool and dry. 空調機","examples":[]}]}]},"affix":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使固定，粘上；可固定"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"詞綴；附加物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>affix</b> is a letter or group of letters, for example, \"un-\" or \"-y,\" which is added to either the beginning or the end of a word to form a different word with a different meaning. For example, \"un-\" is added to \"kind\" to form \"unkind.\" Compare  and . 詞綴","examples":[]}]}]},"agility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（動作）敏捷，靈活；（思維）機敏"}],"sections":[]},"align":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"公開支援，與……結盟；（使）排成一條直線，使平行；調整，使一致；（使）參加，加入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>align</b> <b>yourself with</b> a particular group, you support them because you have the same political aim. 與…結盟","examples":["When war broke out, they aligned themselves with the rebel forces. 戰爭爆發以後，他們與叛軍結了盟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>align</b> something, you place it in a certain position in relation to something else, usually parallel to it. 使對齊","examples":["A tripod will be useful to align and steady the camera. 三腳架會有助於對齊穩住照相機。"]}]}]},"allegedly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"據說，據宣稱"}],"sections":[]},"allege":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"(未經證實地）宣稱，指控"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>allege</b> <b>that</b> something bad is true, you say it but do not prove it. 指稱 (但還未被證實)","examples":["She alleged that there was rampant drug use among the male members of the group. 她指稱該組織中有大量的男性成員吸毒。","The accused is alleged to have killed a man. 該被告據稱殺了一個男子。"]}]}]},"allure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"吸引力，魅力"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"吸引，引誘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>allure</b> of something or someone is the pleasing or exciting quality that they have. 魅力","examples":["It's a game that has really lost its allure. 這是一場已經真正失去其魅力的比賽。"]}]}]},"annually":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"每年，一年一次地"}],"sections":[]},"amendment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"修正，修訂之處；美國憲法修正案（Amendment）；（土壤結構或肥力的）改善；（對檔案或計劃的）修改"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>amendment</b> is a section that is added to a law or rule in order to change it. 修正案","examples":["...an amendment to the defence bill. …對辯護法案的一條修正案。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>amendment</b> is a change that is made to a piece of writing. 修改","examples":[]}]}]},"amend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"修改，修訂；糾正，改正；改善（土壤）的結構（或肥力）；<古>修復；改過自新"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>amend</b> something that has been written such as a law, or something that is said, you change it in order to improve it or make it more accurate. 修正","examples":["The president agreed to amend the constitution and allow multi-party elections. 總統同意了修正憲法並且允許多黨選舉。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make amends</b> when you have harmed someone, you show that you are sorry by doing something to please them. 做補償","examples":["He wanted to make amends for causing their marriage to fail. 他想為一手造成他們婚姻的破裂做出補償。"]}]}]},"apparently":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"據說，顯然；似乎，好像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>apparently</b> to indicate that the information you are giving is something that you have heard, but you are not certain that it is true. 據說","examples":["Apparently the girls are not at all amused by the whole business. 據說這些女孩們完全不覺得這整件事好笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>apparently</b> to refer to something that seems to be true, although you are not sure whether it is or not. 貌似地","examples":["The recent deterioration has been caused by an apparently endless recession. 最近的惡化是由貌似沒完沒了的蕭條造成的。"]}]}]},"apologetic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"道歉的，愧疚的；（為理論或宗教教義）辯護的，辯解的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>apologetic</b>, you show or say that you are sorry for causing trouble for someone, for hurting them, or for disappointing them. 表達歉意的","examples":["The hospital staff were very apologetic but that couldn't really compensate. 醫院員工都深表歉意，但那不能真正補償。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"表達歉意地","examples":["\"It's of no great literary merit,\" he said, almost apologetically. “它不具有重要的文學價值，”他幾乎抱歉地說道。"]}]}]},"appraise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"評價，估量；估價"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>appraise</b> something or someone, you consider them carefully and form an opinion about them. 評價","examples":["This prompted many employers to appraise their selection and recruitment policies. 這促使很多僱主評價其人才選聘政策。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When experts <b>appraise</b> something, they decide how much money it is worth. 估價","examples":["His estate is now appraised at a figure near $1,000,000. 他的財產現在被估價的數額接近$1000000。"]}]}]},"apprehend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逮捕，拘押； 理解，領會；<古>忐忑不安（或心懷恐懼）地期待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If the police <b>apprehend</b> someone, they catch them and arrest them. 逮捕","examples":["Police have not apprehended her killer. 警方尚未逮捕殺害她的兇手。"]}]}]},"archive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"存檔材料，檔案；檔案室"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……存檔，把……歸檔"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Archives</b> are a collection of documents and records that contain historical information. You can also use <b>archives</b> to refer to the place where archives are stored. 檔案; 檔案館","examples":["...the State Library's archives. …國立圖書館的檔案。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Archive</b> material is information that comes from archives. 記入檔案的","examples":["...archive material. …檔案資料。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>archive</b> material such as documents or data, you store it in an archive. 把…存檔","examples":["The system will archive the information so agencies can review it in detail. 該系統會將該資訊存檔，以便各代理機構能對其詳細審閱。"]}]}]},"atm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"自動取款機（Automatic Teller Machine）；非同步傳輸模式（Asynchronous Transfer Mode）；空中交通管理（Air Traffic Management）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"標準大氣壓（standard atmosphere）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>ATM</b> is a machine that allows people to take out money from their bank account by using a special card. <b>ATM</b> is an abbreviation for \"automated teller machine.\" 自動取款機","examples":["Keep your ATM card in a safe place. 把你的自動取款卡放在一個安全的地方。"]}]}]},"attest":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>證明，表明；<正式>（尤指在法庭上）證實；<史，英>宣誓服兵役"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>attest</b> something or <b>attest</b> <b>to</b> something means to say, show, or prove that it is true. 證明","examples":["Police records attest to his long history of violence. 警方記錄證明他有長期的暴力史。"]}]}]},"attorney":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"律師；代理人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In the United States, an <b>attorney</b> or <b>attorney-at-law</b> is a lawyer. 律師","examples":["...a prosecuting attorney. …一位公訴律師。","At the hearing, her attorney did not enter a plea. 在聽證會上，她的律師沒有提出申訴。"]}]}]},"commend":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"讚揚，讚許；推薦，舉薦；被接受，得到認可；把……託付給（或委託於）"}],"sections":[]},"audit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"審計，查……的賬目；審查，稽核；審計報告"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"審計，查賬；<美>旁聽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an accountant <b>audits</b> an organization's accounts, he or she examines the accounts officially in order to make sure that they have been done correctly. 審計","examples":["Each year they audit our accounts and certify them as being true and fair. 每年他們都會稽核我們的賬目，以證明其準確合理。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Audit</b> is also a noun. 審計","examples":["The bank first learned of the problem when it carried out an internal audit. 銀行是在進行內部審計時最先得知這個問題的。"]}]}]},"assimilate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"融入，（使）同化；吸收，理解；使相似，成為相似"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people such as immigrants <b>assimilate</b> <b>into</b> a community or when that community <b>assimilates</b> them, they become an accepted part of it. 同化; 被同化","examples":["There is every sign that new Asian-Americans are just as willing to assimilate. 各種跡象表明新的亞裔美籍人簡直一樣願意被同化。","His family tried to assimilate into the white and Hispanic communities. 他的家人努力融入到白人和拉美人社群。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>assimilate</b> new ideas, customs, or techniques, you learn them or adopt them. 吸納","examples":["My mind could only assimilate one impossibility at a time. 我的頭腦一次只能吸納一件不可能的事情。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"同化","examples":["They promote social integration and assimilation of minority ethnic groups into the culture. 他們提倡少數民族團體與該文化的社會融合及同化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"吸納","examples":["This technique brings life to instruction and eases assimilation of knowledge. 這種技術給教學帶來活力，並使知識的吸收更加容易。"]}]}]},"auditory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聽覺的，聽力的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<古>聽眾；<古>禮堂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Auditory</b> means related to hearing. 聽覺的","examples":["...the limits of the human auditory range. …人類聽覺範圍的侷限。"]}]}]},"avert":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"防止，避免；轉移"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>avert</b> something unpleasant, you prevent it from happening. 防止","examples":["Talks with the teachers' union over the weekend have averted a strike. 週末與教師工會的會談避免了一次罷工。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>avert</b> your eyes or gaze <b>from</b> someone or something, you look away from them. 轉移 (視線)","examples":["He avoids any eye contact, quickly averting his gaze when anyone approaches. 他避免任何目光接觸，任何人接近他時，他都會迅速轉移視線。"]}]}]},"avoidance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"避免，避開；廢止"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Avoidance</b> <b>of</b> someone or something is the act of avoiding them. 避免","examples":["...the avoidance of stress. …對壓力的避免。"]}]}]},"backbreaking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非常辛勞的，費力的"}],"sections":[]},"backache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背痛，腰痛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Backache</b> is a dull pain in your back. 背痛","examples":[]}]}]},"awareness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"認識，意識；感悟能力"}],"sections":[]},"backfire":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"產生事與願違的不良（或危險）後果，適得其反；（發動機或車輛）回火，逆火"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（車輛或發動機的）回火；<北美>（為形成防火隔離帶而有意點燃的）迎面火"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a plan or project <b>backfires</b>, it has the opposite result to the one that was intended. 事與願違","examples":["The president's tactics could backfire. 總統的策略可能會事與願違。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a motor vehicle or its engine <b>backfires</b>, it produces an explosion in the exhaust pipe. (機動車或引擎) 回火","examples":["The car backfired. 這輛車回火了。"]}]}]},"backlash":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指對政治或社會事件的）強烈反應，反對；（機械的）反衝，反作用；（機械部件間的）間隙，輪齒隙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>backlash</b> <b>against</b> a tendency or recent development in society or politics is a sudden, strong reaction against it. (對政治或社會變化的) 強烈反應","examples":["...the male backlash against feminism. …男性對女權主義的強烈反應。"]}]}]},"backlog":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"積壓的工作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>backlog</b> is a number of things which have not yet been done but which need to be done. 積壓待辦的事務","examples":["There is a backlog of repairs and maintenance in schools. 學校裡有積壓下來等待處理的維修和養護工作。"]}]}]},"back-to-back":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"背靠背的，背對背的；緊接的，連續的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Back-to-back</b> wins or victories are victories that are gained one after another without any defeats between them. 一個接著一個的","examples":["...their first back-to-back victories of the season. ...他們本季的第一場連勝。"]}]}]},"attribute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……歸因於；認為是……所作；認為……具有某種特質"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"屬性，特質；標誌，象徵；定語"}],"sections":[]},"backup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"支援，增援；備用品，後備；備份；伴唱，伴奏；堵塞"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"候補的，替代的；支援性的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Backup</b> consists of extra equipment, resources, or people that you can get help or support from if necessary. 後備 (裝置、物資或人力)","examples":["There is no emergency back-up immediately available. 沒有立即就能獲得的後備。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have something such as a second piece of equipment or set of plans as <b>backup</b>, you have arranged for them to be available for use in case the first one does not work. 備用物 (如裝置、計劃)","examples":["Every part of the system has a backup. 這套系統的每個部分都有備件。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>backup</b> of a song is the music that is sung or played to accompany the main tune. 伴奏; 伴唱","examples":["Sharon also sang backup for Barry Manilow. 莎倫還為巴里·馬尼洛唱了伴唱。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>backup</b> is the same as a . 後援","examples":[]}]}]},"backyard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"後院；後庭"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>backyard</b> is an area of land at the back of a house. 後院","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to a country's own <b>backyard</b>, you are referring to its own territory or to somewhere that is very close and where that country wants to influence events. (國家的) 後院","examples":["They seem to think that if it isn't happening in their own backyard, it isn't worth worrying about. 他們似乎認為，如果事情不是發生在他們本國的後院，就不值得擔心。"]}]}]},"baffle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使困惑，難住；抑制，控制"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"擋板，隔板，反射板"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>baffles</b> you, you cannot understand it or explain it. 使困惑","examples":["An apple tree producing square fruit is baffling experts. 一棵結方形果實的蘋果樹正令專家們感到困惑。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人困惑的","examples":["I was constantly ill, with a baffling array of symptoms. 我不斷地生病，還伴有一大堆莫名其妙的症狀。"]}]}]},"bailout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"緊急救助，紓困，緊急財政援助；跳傘，棄機跳傘"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bailout</b> of an organization or individual that has financial problems is the act of helping them by giving them money. 緊急財政援助","examples":["...one of the biggest government bailouts of a private company in years. ...政府近年來對私人公司最大的緊急財政援助之一。"]}]}]},"baker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"麵包師，糕點師；專用輕便烤箱；麵包店（=baker's）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>baker</b> is a person whose job is to bake and sell bread, pastries, and cakes. 麵包師","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>baker</b> or a <b>baker's</b> is a shop where bread and cakes are sold. 麵包店","examples":[]}]}]},"bankbook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行存摺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a book held by depositors at certain banks, in which the bank enters a record of deposits, withdrawals, and earned interest 銀行存摺 (Also called passbook)","examples":[]}]}]},"bankcard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行卡"}],"sections":[]},"bail":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保釋；保釋金；（板球）三柱門上的橫木；壓紙杆"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"保釋；（往外）舀水；從……中擺脫出來；離開"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bail</b> is a sum of money that an arrested person or someone else puts forward as a guarantee that the arrested person will attend their trial in a law court. If the arrested person does not attend it, the money will be lost. 保釋金","examples":["He was freed on bail pending an appeal. 他被保釋，等候上訴。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Bail</b> is permission for an arrested person to be released after bail has been paid. 保釋許可","examples":["Bilal was held without bail after a court appearance in Detroit. 比拉爾在底特律的一次出庭後，被扣押不予保釋。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"either of two small wooden bars placed across the tops of the stumps to form the wicket 橫木","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"the semicircular handle of a kettle, bucket, etc 半圓形把手","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"a framework in a cowshed used to secure the head of a cow during milking (擠奶時固定牛頭的)牛頭固定架","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is bailed</b>, they are released while they are waiting for their trial, after paying an amount of money to the court. 保釋","examples":["He was bailed to appear on 26 August. 他被保釋，於8月26日出庭。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>bail</b>, you use a container to remove water from a boat or from a place which is flooded. (從船裡或某處) 往外舀水","examples":["We kept her afloat for a couple of hours by bailing frantically. 我們拼命往外舀水讓船漂浮了幾個小時。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bail out</b> means the same as . (從船裡或某處) 往外舀水","examples":["A crew was sent down the shaft to close it off and bail out all the water. 一隊工作人員被派下去關閉豎井，並把所有積水舀出來。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone who has been arrested <b>makes bail</b>, or if another person <b>makes bail</b> for them, the arrested person is released on bail. 保釋","examples":["Guerrero was ultimately arrested, but he made bail and fled to Colombia. 格雷羅最終被捕了，可他保釋後，逃到了哥倫比亞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a prisoner <b>jumps bail</b>, he or she does not come back for his or her trial after being released on bail. 棄保潛逃","examples":["He had jumped bail last year while being tried on drug charges. 他去年在因毒品罪受審時棄保潛逃了。"]}]}]},"ballroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"舞廳，跳舞場；（酒店等的）宴會廳；（作定語）交際舞的，舞廳舞的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>ballroom</b> is a very large room that is used for dancing. 舞廳","examples":[]}]}]},"bad-tempered":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"脾氣不好的，易怒的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bad-tempered</b> is not very cheerful and gets angry easily. 脾氣壞的","examples":["When his headaches developed, Nick became bad-tempered and even violent. 尼克的頭疼起來時，他變得焦躁易怒，甚至暴躁。"]}]}]},"banish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"驅逐，趕走；將……驅逐出境，流放；清除，消除；打消……的念頭，驅除（想法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is banished</b> <b>from</b> a place or area of activity, they are sent away from it and prevented from entering it. 驅逐","examples":["John was banished from England. 約翰被逐出英國。","I was banished to the small bedroom upstairs. 我被趕到樓上的小臥室。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>banish</b> something unpleasant, you get rid of it. 消除","examples":["...a public investment programme intended to banish the recession. …一項旨在消除經濟衰退的公共投資計劃。"]}]}]},"baffling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人困惑的；阻礙的；令人喪氣的；變幻的（指風等方向不定）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"baffle 的現在分詞：使困惑；挫敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>baffles</b> you, you cannot understand it or explain it. 使困惑","examples":["An apple tree producing square fruit is baffling experts. 一棵結方形果實的蘋果樹正令專家們感到困惑。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人困惑的","examples":["I was constantly ill, with a baffling array of symptoms. 我不斷地生病，還伴有一大堆莫名其妙的症狀。"]}]}]},"bareness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"裸露；赤裸"}],"sections":[]},"banking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"銀行業；銀行業務；銀行家的職業；築堤"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"bank 的現在分詞：把錢存入銀行；做銀行家；在……邊築堤；傾斜轉彎"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Banking</b> is the business activity of banks and similar institutions. 銀行業務","examples":["...the online banking revolution. …線上銀行業務改革。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"an embankment of a river 河堤","examples":[]}]}]},"bar code":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"條形碼，條碼，電腦條碼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bar code</b> is an arrangement of numbers and parallel lines that is printed on products to be sold in stores. The bar code can be read by computers. 條形碼","examples":[]}]}]},"bankruptcy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"道德的淪喪；破產，倒閉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bankruptcy</b> is the state of being bankrupt. 破產 (狀態)","examples":["Pan Am is the second airline in two months to file for bankruptcy. 泛美航空公司是兩個月內第二家申請破產的航空公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bankruptcy</b> is an instance of an organization or person going bankrupt. 破產 (事件)","examples":["The number of corporate bankruptcies climbed in August. 企業破產的數量在8月份增加了。"]}]}]},"baseline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基線，基準；（網球場、排球場等場地的）底線；（棒球場的）壘線；（印刷）基線；（籃球、網球等場地的）底線"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>baseline</b> of a tennis, badminton, or basketball court is one of the lines at each end of the court that mark the limits of play. (網球場、羽毛球場或籃球場的)底線","examples":["Martinez, when she served, usually stayed on the baseline. 馬第尼斯發球的時候，經常踩在底線上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In baseball, the <b>baseline</b> is the line that a player must not cross when running between bases. (棒球場的)壘線","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>baseline</b> is a value or starting point on a scale with which other values can be compared. (價值的)基準","examples":["You'll need such information to use as a baseline for measuring progress. 你需要利用這些資訊作為基準來衡量進展情況。"]}]}]},"basically":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"基本上，大體上；從根本上說，總的說來"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>basically</b> for emphasis when you are stating an opinion, or when you are making an important statement about something. 基本上; 主要地","examples":["This gun is designed for one purpose – it's basically to kill people. 設計這把槍只有一個目的–主要用於殺人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>basically</b> to show that you are describing a situation in a simple, general way, and that you are not concerned with less important details. 簡單來說; 大致說來","examples":["Basically you've got two choices. 大致說來，你有兩個選擇。"]}]}]},"bearer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"攜帶者；送信人；搬運工人；持票人；不記名（債券、股票等）；<正式>持有者，擁有者；（建築）承木；（機械）托架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>bearer</b> <b>of</b> something such as a message is the person who brings it to you. 捎信人; 運送者","examples":["I hate to be the bearer of bad news. 我討厭當壞訊息的捎信人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bearer</b> of a particular thing is a person who carries it, especially in a ceremony. (尤指典禮中的) 搬運者","examples":["He was the U.S. flag bearer at the 1976 Montreal Games. 他是1976年蒙特利爾奧運會上美國的舉旗手。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>bearer</b> <b>of</b> something such as a document, a right, or an official position is the person who possesses it or holds it. 持有者; 擁有者","examples":["...the traditional bourgeois notion of the citizen as a bearer of rights. …傳統的中產階級觀念，認為公民是權利的所有者。"]}]}]},"bearable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可忍受的，可承受的，支援得住的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>bearable</b>, you feel that you can accept it or deal with it. 可忍受的","examples":["A cool breeze made the heat bearable. 一陣涼爽的微風使得炎熱可以忍受。"]}]}]},"bearing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"舉止，儀態；與……有關，對……有影響；（對壞事的）寬容，容忍；軸承，支軸；方位，方向角；（用羅盤）定向，測位；（盾形紋章面上的）圖案"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"寫有，刻有；手持，攜帶；承擔（bear 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>has a bearing on</b> a situation or event, it is relevant to it. 與…有關係","examples":["Experts generally agree that diet has an important bearing on your general health. 專家們普遍認可飲食與你的總體健康有著重要關係。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>get</b> your <b>bearings</b> or <b>find</b> your <b>bearings</b>, you find out where you are or what you should do next. If you <b>lose</b> your <b>bearings</b>, you do not know where you are or what you should do next. 方位","examples":["A sightseeing tour of the city is included to help you get your bearings. 城市觀光遊包括在內，以幫助你們弄清方向。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>bearing</b> is the way in which they move or stand. 舉止","examples":["She later wrote warmly of his bearing and behaviour. 稍後她熱情地寫到了他的風度與舉止。"]}]}]},"beaten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"打敗（beat 的過去分詞）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"被毆打的；被打敗的；筋疲力竭的；錘薄的；踏平的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"比滕（Beaten 的英譯人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Beaten</b> is the past participle of . (beat)的過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A place that is <b>off the beaten track</b> is in an area where not many people live or go. 人跡罕至","examples":["Tiny secluded beaches can be found off the beaten track. 極小的與世隔絕的海灘能在鮮有人至之處找到。"]}]}]},"beholder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旁觀者；觀看者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something such as beauty or art is <b>in the eye of the beholder</b>, you mean that it is a matter of personal opinion. 個人觀點","examples":["Beauty is in the eye of the beholder. 美是個人的主觀感受。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>beholder</b> of something is the person who is looking at it. 觀察者","examples":[]}]}]},"becoming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（衣服、顏色、髮型等）好看的，相配的；合適的，得體的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（變化過程的）形成，發生；生成變化（哲學上常與“存在”相對）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開始變得，成為，成長為；適合（某人），與…相稱，使（人）顯得漂亮（become 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A piece of clothing, a colour, or a hairstyle that is <b>becoming</b> makes the person who is wearing it look attractive. (衣服、顏色或髮式等)好看的","examples":["Softer fabrics are much more becoming than stiffer ones. 較軟布料比較硬的布料更好看。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Behaviour that is <b>becoming</b> is appropriate and proper in the circumstances. 得體的","examples":["This behaviour is not any more becoming among our politicians than it is among our voters. 這種行為在政客們與投票者們之間一樣不再是十分得體的行為。"]}]}]},"bedside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"床邊，床旁（尤指病床邊）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"床旁的，枕邊的；（醫學）床旁的，臨床床邊的；bedside manner 指醫生對待病人的態度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>bedside</b> is the area beside your bed. 床邊","examples":["She put a cup of tea down on the bedside table. 她把一杯茶放在了床邊的桌子上。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about being at someone's <b>bedside</b>, you are talking about being near them when they are ill in bed. 病床邊","examples":["She kept vigil at the bedside of her critically ill son. 她徹夜守護在病重兒子的病榻旁。"]}]}]},"bed and breakfast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"住宿加早餐：指提供一晚住宿和早餐的房間，或者指提供這種服務的私人住宅或小型酒店。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bed and breakfast</b> is a system of accommodations in a hotel or guest house, in which you pay for a room for the night and for breakfast the following morning. The abbreviation <b>B&B</b> is also used. 住宿加早餐","examples":["Bed and breakfast costs from $50 per person per night. 住宿加早餐每人每晚$50起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bed and breakfast</b> is a guest house that provides bed and breakfast accommodations. The abbreviation <b>B&B</b> is also used. 住宿加早餐客棧","examples":["The restored home is now a bed-and-breakfast. 這座重建後的房子現在是一家住宿加早餐客棧。"]}]}]},"bedtime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"就寢時間，睡覺時間"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（用於名詞前）睡前的，適於睡前的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>bedtime</b> is the time when you usually go to bed. 就寢時間","examples":["It was eight-thirty, Trevor's bedtime. 八點三十分是特雷弗的就寢時間。","...bedtime stories. ...睡前故事。"]}]}]},"behavioral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"行為的，與行為有關的"}],"sections":[]},"beige":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"米色，淡棕色；薄斜紋呢"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淺褐色的，米黃色的；無特色的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"color.","pos_name":"色彩詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>beige</b> is pale brown in colour. 淡棕色的","examples":["The walls are beige. 牆是淡棕色的。"]}]}]},"belated":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"遲來的，誤期的，遲到的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>belated</b> action happens later than it should have. 遲來的","examples":["...the government's belated attempts to alleviate the plight of the poor. …政府想減輕窮人的困苦的、為時已晚的嘗試。"]}]}]},"believer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信徒；相信……者（尤指相信或支援某觀念、做法或事業的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are a great <b>believer in</b> something, you think that it is good, right, or useful. 相信…的人","examples":["Mom was a great believer in herbal medicines. 媽媽是個深信草藥的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>believer</b> is someone who is sure that God exists or that their religion is true. 宗教信徒","examples":["I made no secret of the fact that I was not a believer. 我對自己不是一個宗教信徒的事實並不隱瞞。"]}]}]},"benchmark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"基準；（監測計算機效能的）基準（問題）標準檢查程式；（測量高度的）水準點，基準點"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（根據某種標準）評估，衡量；基準問題檢測結果為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>benchmark</b> is something whose quality or quantity is known and which can therefore be used as a standard with which other things can be compared. 衡量基準","examples":["The truck industry is a benchmark for the economy. 卡車產業是衡量經濟發展的基準。"]}]}]},"benignly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"親切地，仁慈地，和善地；無害地，無危險地（醫學上指非惡性地）"}],"sections":[]},"benefactor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"捐助人，贊助人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>benefactor</b> is someone who helps a person or organization by giving them money. 捐助人","examples":["In his old age he became a benefactor of the arts. 他晚年成了一位藝術贊助人。"]}]}]},"betrayal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背叛，出賣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>betrayal</b> is an action which betrays someone or something, or the fact of being betrayed. 背叛行為","examples":["She felt that what she had done was a betrayal of Patrick. 她覺得自己的所作所為是對帕特里克的背叛。"]}]}]},"bidder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"投標人、投標者；出價人、競買人；努力爭取…的人；（公司併購）收購方；（舊）命令者；Bidder（人名）：（英）比德、（俄）比德爾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bidder</b> is someone who offers to pay a certain amount of money for something that is being sold. If you sell something to the highest <b>bidder</b>, you sell it to the person who offers the most money for it. 出價者","examples":["The sale will be made to the highest bidder subject to a reserve price being attained. 在保證底價的條件下，出售給出價最高者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bidder</b> <b>for</b> something is someone who is trying to obtain it or do it. 努力爭取的人","examples":["Vodafone is among successful bidders for two licences to develop mobile phone systems in Greece. 沃達豐是成功獲得了兩個經營許可證來在希臘發展手機系統的的公司之一。"]}]}]},"bilingual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（人）熟悉兩種語言的，能說兩種語言的；涉及兩種語言的，使用兩種語言的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"熟諳兩種語言的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bilingual</b> means involving or using two languages. 雙語的","examples":["...bilingual education. …雙語教育。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone who is <b>bilingual</b> can speak two languages equally well, usually because they learned both languages as a child. 使用雙語的","examples":["He is bilingual in an Asian language and English. 他是通曉一種亞洲語言和英語的雙語使用者。"]}]}]},"billboard":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"廣告牌，佈告板；《公告牌》（美國音樂娛樂雜誌，亦指其音樂排行榜）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"宣傳，介紹"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>billboard</b> is a very large board on which advertising is displayed. 廣告牌","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"a fitting at the bow of a vessel for securing an anchor 錨座","examples":[]}]}]},"bent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"彎曲的，變形的；駝背的；(有權者）不誠實的，不正派的；下定決心的；同性戀的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"天賦，愛好；信仰；翦股穎；草莖，草梗；<英>莎草；<英，古>石南叢生的荒野，荒草牧場"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"彎腰；使彎曲；屈從（bend 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Bent</b> is the past tense and past participle of . (bend)的過去式和過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an object is <b>bent</b>, it is damaged and no longer has its correct shape. 弄彎的","examples":["The trees were all bent and twisted from the wind. 那些樹全都被風吹得東倒西歪的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a person is <b>bent</b>, their body has become curved because of old age or disease. 駝背的","examples":["...a bent, frail, old man. ...一個駝背體弱的老人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>bent on</b> doing something, especially something harmful, they are determined to do it. 執意的","examples":["He's bent on suicide. 他一心想自殺。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"(of goods) stolen (物品)被偷的","examples":[]},{"num":"5.","zh":"crazy; mad 瘋狂的，著迷的","examples":[]},{"num":"6.","zh":"homosexual 同性戀的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>bent</b> <b>for</b> something, you have a natural ability to do it or a natural interest in it. 天賦; 天生的喜好","examples":["His bent for natural history directed him towards his first job. 他在自然歷史上的天賦幫他找到了他的第一份工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>of</b> a particular <b>bent</b>, they hold a particular set of beliefs. 傾向","examples":["...economists of a socialist bent. ...有社會主義思想傾向的經濟學家。"]}]}]},"bin":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"垃圾桶；儲物箱；瓶酒擱架；統計堆疊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……扔進垃圾箱；摒棄，拒絕；把……放（或貯藏）在箱（或倉）中；把（酒等）放進擱架；把（資料）歸入統計堆"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bin</b> is a container that you keep or store things in. 貯物容器","examples":["...big steel storage bins. …鋼製大貯藏箱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>bin</b> is a container that you put waste or rubbish in. 垃圾箱","examples":[]}]}]},"bland":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平淡的，枯燥乏味的；（食品，飲料）未加調料的，清淡的；沉穩的，無動於衷的；（評論或話語）溫和的，無關痛癢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>bland</b>, you mean that they are rather dull and unexciting. 沒精打采的; 平淡乏味的","examples":["Serle has a blander personality than Howard. 塞爾在個性上比霍華德更沉悶。","It sounds like a commercial: easy on the ear but bland and forgettable. 它聽起來像句廣告語：順耳卻平淡易忘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Food that is <b>bland</b> has very little flavour. (食物) 淡而無味的","examples":["It tasted bland and insipid, like warmed cardboard. 它吃起來淡而無味，像加熱過的卡紙板。"]}]}]},"binding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"(協議，承諾）有約束力的，必須遵守的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書籍的）封面；鑲邊，滾邊；捆綁物，包紮物；（滑雪板的）皮靴固定裝置；黏合，稠合；（喬姆斯基語言學）（反身詞與原詞之間的）黏連關係"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"捆綁；（使）聯合在一起；約束，迫使（bind 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>binding</b> promise, agreement, or decision must be obeyed or carried out. 有約束力的","examples":["...proposals for a legally binding commitment on nations to stabilize emissions of carbon dioxide. …關於就穩定二氧化碳排放各國做出有法律約束力的承諾的建議。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>binding</b> of a book is its cover. (書的) 封面","examples":["Its books are noted for the quality of their paper and bindings. 其書籍以紙張和封面的品質而著稱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Binding</b> is a strip of material that you put around the edge of a piece of cloth or other object in order to protect or decorate it. 滾條; 鑲邊","examples":["...the Regency mahogany dining table with satinwood binding. …攝政時期有椴木鑲邊的桃花心木餐桌"]}]}]},"blockage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"造成阻塞的東西，阻塞物；堵塞，阻塞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blockage</b> <b>in</b> a pipe, tube, or tunnel is an object which blocks it, or the state of being blocked. 堵塞物; 堵塞","examples":["The logical treatment is to remove this blockage. 合理的處理方法是清除這種堵塞物。"]}]}]},"blender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"攪拌機，果汁機；摻和者，混合者，混合裝置；Blender（三維圖形軟體）；布倫德（姓氏）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>blender</b> is an electrical kitchen appliance used for mixing liquids and soft foods together or turning fruit or vegetables into liquid. (食物)攪拌機","examples":[]}]}]},"bookstore":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"書店（等於 bookshop，主要用於美國英語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bookstore</b> is a shop where books are sold. 書店","examples":[]}]}]},"boardroom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"董事會會議室，董事會議室，會議室；董事會，高層決策層（轉喻，常作定語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>boardroom</b> is a room where the board of a company meets. 董事會議室","examples":["Everyone had already assembled in the boardroom for the 9:00 a.m. session. 每個人都到了董事會議室參加上午9:00的會議。"]}]}]},"bookshelf":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"書架"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>bookshelf</b> is a shelf on which you keep books. 書架","examples":[]}]}]},"booklet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小冊子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>booklet</b> is a very thin book that has a paper cover and that gives you information about something. 小冊子","examples":["...a 48-page booklet of notes for the completion of the form. …一本48頁的表格填寫說明小冊子。"]}]}]},"bothersome":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"麻煩的，令人討厭的，煩人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>bothersome</b> is annoying or irritating. 煩人的","examples":[]}]}]},"borderline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"臨界的，邊緣的，勉強合格的；所屬不清的，曖昧的；邊界的，位於邊界上的；（醫學）交界性的，邊緣型的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"邊界線，邊界，分界線；臨界點；中間地帶，臨界狀態，曖昧狀態"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"幾乎，差不多"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>borderline</b> <b>between</b> two different or opposite things is the division between them. 分界線","examples":["...a task which involves exploring the borderline between painting and photography. …一項涉及探索繪畫與攝影之間界線的任務。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>borderline</b> is only just acceptable as a member of a class or group. 勉強合格的","examples":["Some were obviously unsuitable and could be ruled out at once. Others were borderline cases. 一些顯然不合適，可以馬上被排除。另一些勉強合格。"]}]}]},"bravely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"勇敢地，無畏地；<舊，文>華麗地（多指外觀、服飾、裝飾等）"}],"sections":[]},"box office":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（劇場、電影院等的）售票處；票房（收入或賣座情況，常作 the box office）；票房吸引力（即吸引觀眾購票的能力，常作定語，亦作 box-office）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>box office</b> in a theatre or concert hall is the place where the tickets are sold. 售票處","examples":["...the long line of people outside the box-office. …售票處外的長隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people talk about <b>the</b> <b>box office</b>, they are referring to the degree of success of a film or play in terms of the number of people who go to watch it or the amount of money it makes. 票房","examples":["The film has taken $180 million at the box office. 這部電影的票房收入已達到1.8億美元。"]}]}]},"boring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"令人厭煩的；乏味的，無趣的，無聊的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"鑽孔，擴洞；鑽成的孔，擴大的洞"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使厭煩；鑽；盯著看（bore 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something <b>boring</b> is so dull and uninteresting that they make people tired and impatient. 乏味的","examples":["Not only are mothers not paid but also most of their boring or difficult work is unnoticed. 母親們不僅得不到報酬，而且所幹的乏味艱辛的活兒也很少被留意。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act or process of making or enlarging a hole 鑽孔; 擴洞","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the hole made in this way 鑽成的孔; 擴大的洞","examples":[]}]}]},"brand-new":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"嶄新的，未用過的；最近獲得的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>brand-new</b> object is completely new. 全新的","examples":["Yesterday he went off to buy himself a brand-new car. 昨天他去給自己買了一輛嶄新的車。"]}]}]},"bravo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"喝彩聲；（無線電通訊中）字母B的程式碼；暴徒，（被人僱用的）殺手"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"喝彩"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"好哇，好（用於喝彩）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Bravo）（英、法、西、意、葡、塞）布拉沃（人名）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>bravo</b>\" to express appreciation when someone has done something well. 好樣的","examples":["\"Bravo, Rena! You're right,\" the students said. “好樣的，雷娜！你是對的，”學生們說道。"]}]}]},"brainstorm":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>靈感，突然想到的妙計；<英>一時糊塗；獻計獻策會，自由討論會"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"集體討論，集思廣益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>brainstorm</b>, you suddenly have a clever idea. 突發的靈感","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"頭腦風暴法討論","examples":["Hundreds of other ideas had been tried and discarded during two years of brainstorming. 數百個其它點子在兩年的頭腦風暴集體討論中被嘗試過但又被摒棄了。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a group of people <b>brainstorm</b>, they have a meeting in which they all put forward as many ideas and suggestions as they can think of. 開頭腦風暴法討論會","examples":["The women meet twice a month to brainstorm and set business goals for each other. 這些婦女們一個月聚頭兩次來開頭腦風暴會議,為彼此設定商業目標。","She brainstormed the possible approaches she might take. 她用頭腦風暴法想出了她可以採取的可能方法。"]}]}]},"bracket":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（固定在牆上的）托架，支架；（收入、年齡等的）等級段，組級；括號；夾叉射擊"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……置於括弧內，用括弧括；置於……兩側 ；把……歸為一類，把……相提並論"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is in a particular <b>bracket</b>, you mean that they come within a particular range, for example, a range of incomes, ages, or prices. (收入、年齡、價格等的) 範圍","examples":["...a 33% top tax rate on everyone in these high-income brackets. …這些高收入範圍內每個人的33%的最高稅率。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Brackets</b> are pieces of metal, wood, or plastic that are fastened to a wall in order to support something such as a shelf. (固定在牆上的) 支架","examples":["Fix the beam with the brackets and screws. 用支架和螺絲固定橫樑。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Brackets</b> are pair of marks ( ) that are placed around a series of symbols in a mathematical expression to indicate that those symbols function as one item within the expression. (數學中用以表示整體的) 括號","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Brackets</b> are a pair of written marks ( ) that you place around a word, expression, or sentence in order to indicate that you are giving extra information. (用以給出額外資訊的) 括號","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If two or more people or things <b>are bracketed</b> <b>together</b>, they are considered to be similar or related in some way. 歸為一類","examples":["The Magi, Brahmins, and Druids were bracketed together as men of wisdom. 三賢人、婆羅門、德魯伊特教僧侶一起被歸為智者。"]}]}]},"breakable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易碎的，易破裂的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"易碎品，易碎的東西（常用複數 breakables）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Breakable</b> objects are easy to break by accident. 易碎的","examples":["Put away any valuable or breakable objects. 將所有貴重及易碎的物品移走。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Breakables</b> are breakable objects. 易碎品","examples":["Keep breakables out of reach of very young children. 將易碎品放在嬰幼兒夠不到的地方。"]}]}]},"breach":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"違反，破壞；（關係）中斷，終止；缺口"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"違反，破壞；在……上開啟缺口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>breach</b> an agreement, a law, or a promise, you break it. 違反","examples":["The newspaper breached the code of conduct on privacy. 這家報紙違反了隱私保護行為準則。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>breaches</b> a barrier, they make an opening in it, usually leaving it weakened or destroyed. 使破開","examples":["The limestone is sufficiently fissured for tree roots to have breached the roof of the cave. 石灰岩裂開了足以讓樹根突破洞頂。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>breach</b> someone's security or their defences, you manage to get through and attack an area that is heavily guarded and protected. 攻破 (某人的防範)","examples":["The bomber had breached security by hurling his dynamite from a roof overlooking the building. 爆破手從一個俯瞰這幢樓房的屋頂上投擲了炸藥,攻破了安全防衛。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>breach</b> <b>of</b> an agreement, a law, or a promise is an act of breaking it. 違反","examples":["The congressman was accused of a breach of secrecy rules. 這個國會議員被指控違反保密條例。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>breach</b> <b>in</b> a relationship is a serious disagreement which often results in the relationship ending. (關係中的) 裂痕","examples":["Their actions threatened a serious breach in relations between the two countries. 他們的行動有威脅兩國關係分裂的危險。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Breach</b> is also a noun. 攻破","examples":["...serious breaches of security at Camp Delta. …三角洲軍營安全防禦的嚴重破壞。"]}]}]},"breakout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"越獄，脫逃；突圍，擺脫困境；爆發，突然發生（如疾病、戰爭，也指皮膚突然長痘或出疹）；分組討論（小組活動或房間）；突破（行情）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"突然走紅的，一炮而紅的（指明星、作品等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there has been a <b>breakout</b>, someone has escaped from prison. 越獄","examples":["He is thought to have planned a prison breakout of militants suspected of the July bombing. 他被認為曾經策劃了7月轟炸事件的嫌疑武力份子的越獄。"]}]}]},"breathtaking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"激動人心的，令人驚歎的；非常糟糕的，令人震驚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>breathtaking</b>, you are emphasizing that it is extremely beautiful or amazing. 令人驚歎的","examples":["The house has breathtaking views from every room. 這房子從各個房間都能看到令人驚歎的風景。","Some of their football was breathtaking, a delight to watch. 他們踢的足球賽有些場次令人驚歎,看起來賞心悅目。"]}]}]},"breathless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"喘不過氣來的，氣喘吁吁的，上氣不接下氣的；停止呼吸的，沒有呼吸的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>breathless</b>, you have difficulty in breathing properly, for example, because you have been running or because you are afraid or excited. 上氣不接下氣的","examples":["I was a little breathless and my heartbeat was bumpy and fast. 我有點上氣不接下氣,我的心跳不穩並且很快。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"上氣不接下氣地","examples":["\"I'll go in,\" he said breathlessly. “我要進去,”他上氣不接下氣地說。"]}]}]},"briefly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"簡短地，簡要地；短暫地，暫時地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that happens or is done <b>briefly</b> happens or is done for a very short period of time. 短暫地","examples":["He smiled briefly. 他短促地微微一笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say or write something <b>briefly</b>, you use very few words or give very few details. 簡潔地","examples":["There are four basic alternatives; they are described briefly below. 有4種基本選擇,簡略描述如下。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say <b>briefly</b> to indicate that you are about to say something in as few words as possible. 簡言之","examples":["Briefly, no less than nine of our agents have passed information to us. 簡言之,至少已經有9位我們的代理商將資訊傳遞給了我們。"]}]}]},"brittle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易碎的，脆的；（關係或局勢）不牢固的，易變的；脆弱的；冷淡的；尖利的，刺耳的；（聲音）像要哭的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"果仁薄脆糖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An object or substance that is <b>brittle</b> is hard but easily broken. 硬脆易碎的","examples":["Pine is brittle and breaks. 松木硬脆易折。"]}]}]},"brokered":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"broker 的過去式和過去分詞：促成，斡旋，安排（協議、交易、停火、談判等）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"broker 的過去分詞作定語：由中間人或某方促成、撮合或安排的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>broker</b> is a person whose job is to buy and sell securities, foreign money, real estate, or goods for other people. 經紀人; 掮客","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country or government <b>brokers</b> an agreement, a ceasefire, or a round of talks, they try to negotiate or arrange it. 斡旋","examples":["The United Nations brokered a peace in Mogadishu at the end of March. 聯合國於3月底在摩加迪沙促成了一場和平談判。"]}]}]},"brighten":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使明亮，使鮮豔；開顏，高興；（使）好轉，（使）變得樂觀；使生色，為……增輝添彩；放晴"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>brightens</b> or their face <b>brightens</b>, they suddenly look happier. 變得開心; 面露喜色","examples":["Seeing him, she seemed to brighten a little. 看見他她似乎高興點了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If your eyes <b>brighten</b>, you suddenly look interested or excited. (眼睛) 變亮","examples":["His eyes brightened and he laughed. 他眼睛一亮,笑了起來。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the weather <b>brightens</b>, it becomes less cloudy or rainy, and the sun starts to shine. (天氣) 放晴","examples":["By early afternoon the weather had brightened. 午後不久,天氣已經放晴了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Brighten up</b> means the same as . 變得開心; 面露喜色","examples":["He brightened up a bit. 他微露喜色。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Brighten up</b> means the same as . 使增輝","examples":["David spotted the pink silk lampshade in a shop and thought it would brighten up the room. 大衛在一家商店發現了這個粉色的絲綢燈罩,他想它會使房間生輝。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>brightens</b> a place, they make it more colourful and attractive. 使增輝","examples":["Tubs planted with flowers brightened the area outside the door. 盆裡種上了花給門外的那塊地增輝了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>brightens</b> a situation or the situation <b>brightens</b>, it becomes more pleasant, enjoyable, or favourable. 改善; 轉好","examples":["That does not do much to brighten the prospects of kids in the city. 那並沒怎麼改善城裡孩子們的前途。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a light <b>brightens</b> a place or when a place <b>brightens</b>, it becomes brighter or lighter. 照亮; 變亮","examples":["The sky above the ridge of mountains brightened. 山脊上方的天空變亮了。"]}]}]},"broker":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經紀人，中間人"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"協調，安排"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>broker</b> is a person whose job is to buy and sell securities, foreign money, real estate, or goods for other people. 經紀人; 掮客","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a country or government <b>brokers</b> an agreement, a ceasefire, or a round of talks, they try to negotiate or arrange it. 斡旋","examples":["The United Nations brokered a peace in Mogadishu at the end of March. 聯合國於3月底在摩加迪沙促成了一場和平談判。"]}]}]},"brutally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"殘忍地，野蠻地，殘酷地（亦作獸性地）；毫不留情地，不留情面地（常修飾 frank、honest 等形容詞）"}],"sections":[]},"browser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瀏覽器；逛商店的人，瀏覽書報者；吃高處草木的動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>browser</b> is a piece of computer software that you use to search for information on the Internet, especially on the World Wide Web. 瀏覽器","examples":["You need an up-to-date Web browser. 你需要一個最新的網路瀏覽器。"]}]}]},"brush-off":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>不理睬，不理會，漠視"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone gives you <b>the</b> <b>brush-off</b> when you speak to them, they refuse to talk to you or be nice to you. 不理睬; 冷落","examples":["I wanted to keep in touch, but when I called him he gave me the brush-off. 我想和他保持聯絡，可是當我打電話時，他卻不理我。"]}]}]},"businessman":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（男性）商人，生意人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>businessman</b> is a man who works in business. 商人","examples":["...a wealthy businessman who owns a printing business in Orlando. …一個在奧蘭多擁有印刷企業的富有商人。"]}]}]},"budge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）稍微移動；<美，非正式> 給別人挪開一塊地方；（使）改變主意，（使）讓步"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"羔羊皮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone will not <b>budge</b> on a matter, or if nothing <b>budges</b> them, they refuse to change their mind or to come to an agreement. 使讓步; 做讓步","examples":["The Americans will not budge on this point. 這些美國人在這一點上不會讓步的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something will not <b>budge</b>, they will not move. If you cannot <b>budge</b> them, you cannot make them move. 使移動; 移動","examples":["Her mother refused to budge from Omaha. 她母親拒絕離開奧馬哈。","The window refused to budge. 窗子怎麼也動不了。"]}]}]},"buyer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"買主，買方，買家；採購員；（法律）買受人；（Buyer）人名（英：拜爾、法：比耶、德：布耶爾）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>buyer</b> is a person who is buying something or who intends to buy it. 買主","examples":["Car buyers are more interested in safety and reliability than speed. 比起速度，汽車買主更關注安全性和可靠性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>buyer</b> is a person who works for a large shop deciding what goods will be bought from manufacturers to be sold in the shop. 採購員","examples":["Diana is a buyer for a chain of furniture shops. 戴安娜是一家連鎖傢俱商店的採購員。"]}]}]},"cafe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"咖啡館，小餐館"}],"sections":[]},"caliber":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"口徑、內徑、管徑；才幹、水準、素質；器量（同 calibre）"}],"sections":[]},"calling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"強烈願望，使命感；行業，職業；（動物或人的）喊叫"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打電話；叫作；呼喚（call 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>calling</b> is a profession or career which someone is strongly attracted to, especially one which involves helping other people. 使命","examples":["He was a consultant physician, a serious man dedicated to his calling. 他是一名顧問醫生，一個專注於其使命的嚴肅認真的人。"]}]}]},"candid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"坦率的，直言不諱的；抓拍的，偷拍的；公正的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are <b>candid</b> about something or with someone, you speak honestly. 直言不諱的; 坦率的","examples":["Natalie is candid about the problems she is having with Steve. 納塔莉對她與史蒂夫的問題直言不諱。","I haven't been completely candid with him. 我沒有完全對他說實話。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>candid</b> photograph of someone is one that was taken when the person did not know they were being photographed. 偷拍的","examples":["...candid snaps of off-duty film stars. …偷拍的熒幕下影星們的照片。"]}]}]},"capitalization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"用大寫字母；資本總額；（股票等的）市值；資本化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the act of capitalizing 資本化","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"the sum so derived 資本額","examples":[]}]}]},"capitalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"用大寫字母書寫（或印刷），把……首字母大寫；為（開辦或發展企業）提供資金；（將資產或股票）變現，使資本化；（根據公司的股票價值或其收益）核定（公司的）資本；利用（capitalize on）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>capitalize</b> <b>on</b> a situation, you use it to gain some advantage for yourself. 利用","examples":["The rebels seem to be trying to capitalize on the public's discontent with the government. 反叛者們似乎正試圖利用公眾對政府的不滿情緒。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In business, if you <b>capitalize</b> something that belongs to you, you sell it in order to make money. 使資本化","examples":["Our intention is to capitalize the company by any means we can. 我們的目的是盡一切可能把該公司資本化。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>capitalize</b> a letter, you write it as a capital letter. If you <b>capitalize</b> a word, you spell it in capital letters, or with the first letter as a capital letter. 把…大寫","examples":["Capitalize all proper nouns but not the articles (a, an) that precede them. 把所有的專有名詞大寫，它們之前的冠詞(a, an)則不用。"]}]}]},"carry out":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"執行，實施，進行（計劃、任務、命令、調查等）；完成，實現（任務、工作等）；履行（諾言、承諾等）；實施（威脅等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>carry out</b> a threat, task, or instruction, you do it or act according to it. 實行","examples":["The Social Democrats could still carry out their threat to leave the government. 社會民主黨人仍然可能實現其脫離政府的威脅。","Police say they believe the attacks were carried out by nationalists. 警方稱他們認為這些襲擊行為是民族主義分子發動的。"]}]}]},"categorize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"將……分類，把……列作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>categorize</b> people or things, you divide them into sets or you say which set they belong to. 把…分類","examples":["Lindsay, like his films, is hard to categorize. 就像他演的電影難於歸類一樣，很難說林賽屬於哪一類演員。","Make a list of your child's toys and then categorize them as sociable or antisocial. 把你孩子的玩具列個清單，然後將之分為交際型和非交際型。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"分類","examples":["Her first novel defies easy categorization. 她的處女作小說不容易歸類。"]}]}]},"carefully":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"小心地，仔細地"}],"sections":[]},"catering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（會議或社交活動的）飲食服務，酒席承辦"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提供餐飲服務，承辦酒席；滿足，迎合（cater 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Catering</b> is the activity of providing food and drink for a large number of people, for example, at weddings and parties. (婚禮、派對等的) 餐飲供應; 酒席承辦","examples":["His catering business made him a millionaire at 41. 他的酒宴承辦生意使他在41歲時成為了百萬富翁。"]}]}]},"cheque":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"支票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cheque</b> is a printed form on which you write an amount of money and who it is to be paid to. Your bank then pays the money to that person from your account. 支票","examples":["He handed me an envelope with a cheque for $1,500. 他遞給我一個信封，裡面有一張$1500的支票。"]}]}]},"cancellation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"取消，撤銷；作廢，廢除"}],"sections":[]},"caller":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"打電話的人，呼叫者，主叫方；訪客，來客；（計算機）呼叫者，呼叫方；召集人，召集員"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（蘇格蘭英語）新鮮的，清涼的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>caller</b> is a person who is making a telephone call. 打電話者","examples":["An anonymous caller told police what had happened. 一個打匿名電話的人告知了警方所發生的一切。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>caller</b> is a person who comes to see you for a short visit. 來訪者; 來客","examples":["She ushered her callers into a cluttered living room. 她把來客們帶到一間雜亂的客廳。"]}]}]},"circumvent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>規避，迴避；（為避免某物而）改道，繞過；克服（問題，困難）（尤指暗中智取）；<古>欺騙，智勝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>circumvents</b> a rule or restriction, they avoid having to obey the rule or restriction, in a clever and perhaps dishonest way. (利用小聰明)迴避","examples":["Military planners tried to circumvent the treaty. 軍事計劃員們試圖避開此條約。"]}]}]},"citizenship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公民資格，公民身份；公民義務，公民責任感"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have <b>citizenship</b> of a country, you are legally accepted as belonging to it. 公民身份","examples":["After 15 years in the U.S., he has finally decided to apply for American citizenship. 在美國住了15年後，他最終決定申請美國的公民身份。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Citizenship</b> is the fact of belonging to a community because you live in it, and the duties and responsibilities that this brings. 公民義務和責任","examples":["Their German peers had a more developed sense of citizenship. 他們的德國同齡人對於公民的義務和責任有更成熟的認識。"]}]}]},"citation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"引文，引語；傳喚，傳票；表彰，嘉獎狀；引用，引證"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>citation</b> is an official document or speech which praises a person for something brave or special that they have done. 嘉獎; 獎狀","examples":["His citation says he showed outstanding and exemplary courage. 他的嘉獎令中寫道他表現出了與眾不同和堪為楷模的英勇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>citation</b> from a book or other piece of writing is a passage or phrase from it. 引文","examples":["...a 50-minute manifesto with citations from the Koran. …一段長達50分鐘、帶有《古蘭經》引文的宣言。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>citation</b> is the same as a . 傳票","examples":["The court could issue a citation and fine Ms. Robbins. 法庭可以發出傳票並且罰羅賓斯女士的款。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>citation</b> is an official piece of paper which orders you to pay a fine or to appear in court because you have committed a traffic offence. 交通違規傳票; 交通罰單","examples":["The Highway Patrol this year issued 1,018 speeding citations. 高速公路巡警今年開出了1018張超速罰單。"]}]}]},"clearly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"清楚地，清晰地；毫無疑問，顯然；明智地，清醒地"}],"sections":[]},"cognition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"認識，認知；認識（或認知）的結果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Cognition</b> is the mental process involved in knowing, learning, and understanding things. 認知","examples":["...processes of perception and cognition. ...感受和認知的過程。"]}]}]},"cohesive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"團結的，有凝聚力的；使團結的，使凝聚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>cohesive</b> consists of parts that fit together well and form a united whole. 有聚合力的","examples":["\"Daring Adventures\" from '86 is a far more cohesive and successful album. 1986年出的《勇敢的冒險》是一張極富凝聚力、極成功的唱片集。"]}]}]},"circumspect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<正式>小心謹慎的，考慮周到的，慎重的，指說話做事留意潛在後果、不輕率冒險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>circumspect</b>, you are cautious in what you do and say and do not take risks. (指說話做事)謹慎小心的","examples":["The banks should have been more circumspect in their dealings. 銀行在交易時應更加謹慎。"]}]}]},"collaboration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"合作，協作；勾結，通敵；合作成果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Collaboration</b> is the act of working together to produce a piece of work, especially a book or some research. (尤指著書或進行研究時的) 合作","examples":["There is substantial collaboration with neighbouring departments. 相鄰的幾個院系進行了通力合作。","...scientific collaborations. …科學協作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>collaboration</b> is a piece of work that has been produced as the result of people or groups working together. 合作成果","examples":["He was also a writer of beautiful stories, some of which are collaborations with his fiancée. 他也撰寫優美的故事，有些是和他的未婚妻合作的成果。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Collaboration</b> is the act of helping an enemy who is occupying your country during a war. 通敵行為","examples":["...rumours of his collaboration with the occupying forces during the war. …關於他在戰爭期間與佔領軍勾結的謠傳。"]}]}]},"collateral":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"抵押物，擔保品；旁系親屬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"附屬的，次要的；（親戚）旁系的，非直系的；並列的，並行的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Collateral</b> is money or property which is used as a guarantee that someone will repay a loan. 擔保金; 抵押品","examples":["Many people use personal assets as collateral for small business loans. 許多人用個人資產作抵押，辦理小額商業貸款。"]}]}]},"collectible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有收藏價值的，值得收藏的（亦作 collectable）；可收集的，可收取或收回的（款項、債務等）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"收藏品，值得收藏的物品（常用複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>collectible</b> object is one which is valued very highly by collectors because it is rare or beautiful. 有收藏價值的","examples":["Many of these cushions have survived and are very collectible. 這些墊子中的許多儲存了下來並極具收藏價值。"]}]}]},"comforting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"安慰的，令人欣慰的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"安慰（comfort 的 ing 形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>comforting</b>, you mean it makes you feel less worried or unhappy. 令人安慰的","examples":["My mother had just died and I found the book very comforting. 我母親剛去世，我發現這本書能使我感到安慰。"]}]}]},"come across":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"偶然遇見，無意中發現（某人或某物）；遭遇，經歷（困難、情況或事件等）；給人留下（某種）印象，顯得（常作 come across as）；意思被理解，表達清楚；<非正式，尤英>提供，交付（所需資訊、錢款等，常作 come across with）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>come across</b> something or someone, you find them or meet them by chance. 偶然發現; 偶然遇見","examples":["He came across the jawbone of a 4.5 million-year-old marsupial. 他偶然發現了一個450萬年前的有袋動物的頜骨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or what they are saying <b>comes across</b> in a particular way, they make that impression on people who meet them or are listening to them. 留下印象","examples":["When sober, he can come across as an extremely pleasant and charming young man. 在他不醉酒的時候，他給人的印象可能會是一位極其可愛迷人的年輕人。"]}]}]},"comparatively":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"比較地，相對地"}],"sections":[]},"committed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"盡心盡力的，忠誠的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"承諾；委託；幹壞事（commit 的過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>commits</b> a crime or a sin, they do something illegal or bad. 犯 (罪); 做 (壞事)","examples":["I have never committed any crime. 我從沒有犯過任何罪。","This is a man who has committed murder. 這是個犯了謀殺罪的男人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>commits</b> <b>suicide</b>, they deliberately kill themselves. 進行 (自殺)","examples":["There are unconfirmed reports he tried to commit suicide. 有未經證實的報道說他曾企圖自殺。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> money or resources <b>to</b> something, you decide to use them for a particular purpose. 調撥 (錢、資源)","examples":["They called on Western nations to commit more money to the poorest nations. 他們號召西方國家為最貧困國家撥更多的款。","The company had committed thousands of dollars for a plan to reduce mercury emissions. 該公司已經為了一項減少汞排放的計劃調撥了數千美元。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> <b>yourself to</b> something, you say that you will definitely do it. If you <b>commit</b> <b>yourself to</b> someone, you decide that you want to have a long-term relationship with them. 使 (自己) 致力於; 使 (自己) 承諾 (與某人的長期關係)","examples":["I would advise people to think very carefully about committing themselves to working Sundays. 我會建議人們認真考慮答應週日工作。","I'd like a friendship that might lead to something deeper, but I wouldn't want to commit myself too soon. 我想要可能發展到更深層關係的友誼，但我不想太快做出承諾。","He won't commit. 他不會承諾。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If you do not want to <b>commit</b> <b>yourself on</b> something, you do not want to say what you really think about it or what you are going to do. (就某事) 表態","examples":["It isn't their diplomatic style to commit themselves on such a delicate issue. 就如此微妙的問題表態不是他們的外交風格。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If someone <b>is committed</b> <b>to</b> a mental hospital, prison, or other institution, they are officially sent there for a period of time. 送交 (到精神病院、監獄等)","examples":["Arthur's drinking caused him to be committed to a psychiatric hospital. 阿瑟酗酒導致他被關進了一家精神病院。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If you <b>commit</b> something <b>to</b> paper or <b>to</b> writing, you record it by writing it down. If you <b>commit</b> something <b>to</b> memory, you learn it so that you will remember it. 記 (在紙上、記憶中)","examples":["She had not committed anything to paper about it. 她還沒有把關於它的任何東西記在紙上。"]}]}]},"compliant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"服從的，順從的；（與規定或標準）符合的，一致的；（物理，醫）有可塑性的，柔量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>compliant</b>, you mean they willingly do what they are asked to do. 順從的","examples":["...a docile and compliant workforce. ...一個馴服而順從的勞動力。"]}]}]},"comply":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"遵從，服從；（商品）符合特定標準"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>complies</b> <b>with</b> an order or set of rules, they do what is required or expected. 遵從","examples":["The commander said that the army would comply with the ceasefire. 指揮官說過部隊會遵從停火協議。","Some beaches had failed to comply with environmental regulations. 一些海灘沒能遵守環保規定。"]}]}]},"complicated":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"複雜的，難處理的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使複雜化，使難以理解；引起併發症（complicate 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>complicated</b>, you mean it has so many parts or aspects that it is difficult to understand or deal with. 複雜的","examples":["The situation in Lebanon is very complicated. 黎巴嫩的形勢非常複雜。"]}]}]},"composure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（不可數名詞）鎮靜，沉著，鎮定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Composure</b> is the appearance or feeling of calm and the ability to control your feelings. 鎮定; 定力","examples":["She was a little nervous at first but she soon regained her composure. 她起初有點緊張但很快就恢復了鎮定。"]}]}]},"consciously":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有意識地，清楚地；有意地，故意地"}],"sections":[]},"concur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"同意，贊同；（事件）同時發生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v-recip.","pos_name":"相互動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one person <b>concurs</b> <b>with</b> another person, the two people agree. You can also say that two people <b>concur</b>. 意見一致","examples":["Local feeling does not necessarily concur with the press. 當地人的看法不一定和媒體一致。","Daniels and Franklin concurred in an investigator's suggestion that the police be commended. 丹尼爾斯和富蘭克林對一位調查員提出的警方應受到表揚的提議意見一致。"]}]}]},"confirmation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"確認，確定；證實，證明；批准，許可；堅信禮，堅振禮"}],"sections":[]},"consecutive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"連續的，不間斷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Consecutive</b> periods of time or events happen one after the other without interruption. 連續的","examples":["The Cup was won for the third consecutive year by the Toronto Maple Leafs. 這個獎盃連續第三年由多倫多楓葉隊贏去了。"]}]}]},"consequently":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"因此，結果"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Consequently</b> means as a result. 結果","examples":["Grandfather had sustained a broken back while working in the mines. Consequently, he spent the rest of his life in a wheelchair. 爺爺在礦上做工時受了背傷，結果，他在輪椅上度過了他的餘生。"]}]}]},"consciousness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"知覺，清醒；思想，意識；（群體的）觀念體系；感知，察覺"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>consciousness</b> is your mind and your thoughts. 思想頭腦","examples":["That idea has been creeping into our consciousness for some time. 那個念頭在我們腦子裡漸漸產生已有一段時間了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>consciousness</b> of a group of people is their set of ideas, attitudes, and beliefs. (群體的) 觀念體系","examples":["The Green Party is attempting to shift the American consciousness. 綠黨在試圖改變美國人的觀念體系。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>consciousness</b> to refer to an interest in and knowledge of a particular subject or idea. (對某話題或思想的) 意識","examples":["Her political consciousness sprang from her upbringing when her father's illness left the family short of money. 她的政治覺悟源於她的成長背景，當時她父親的病讓家裡缺錢。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Consciousness</b> is the state of being awake rather than being asleep or unconscious. If someone <b>loses consciousness</b>, they become unconscious, and if they <b>regain consciousness</b>, they become conscious after being unconscious. 知覺","examples":["She banged her head and lost consciousness. 她撞了頭，失去了知覺。"]}]}]},"considering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"prep.","zh":"考慮到，鑑於"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"考慮到，鑑於"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"<非正式>從各方面考慮，通盤考慮"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"考慮，斟酌；認為，視為；體貼，顧及（consider 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"prep.","pos_name":"介詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>considering</b> to indicate that you are thinking about a particular fact when making a judgment or giving an opinion. 鑑於 (某情況)","examples":["He must be hoping, but considering the situation in June he may be hoping for too much too soon. 他肯定正在期待著，但鑑於6月的情況，他可能期望得過多過早。"]}]},{"pos":"conj.","pos_name":"連詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>considering that</b> to indicate that you are thinking about a particular fact when making a judgment or giving an opinion. 考慮到 (某事實)","examples":["Considering that you are no longer involved with this man, your response is a little extreme. 考慮到你和這個男人不再有干係，你的反應有點過分。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you are giving an opinion or making a judgment, you can use <b>considering</b> to suggest that you have thought about all the circumstances, and often that something has succeeded in spite of these circumstances. 總的來看","examples":["I think you're pretty safe, considering. 總的來看，我認為你很安全。"]}]}]},"consistency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一致性，連貫性；黏稠度，平滑度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Consistency</b> is the quality or condition of being consistent. 連貫性; 一致性","examples":["She scores goals with remarkable consistency. 她以非凡的連貫性進球得分。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>consistency</b> of a substance is how thick or smooth it is. 黏稠度","examples":["Dilute the paint with water until it is the consistency of milk. 用水把顏料稀釋到牛奶的黏稠度。"]}]}]},"consistently":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一貫地，始終；一致地"}],"sections":[]},"constrain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"限制，約束；強迫，迫使"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>constrain</b> someone or something means to limit their development or force them to behave in a particular way. 限制; 迫使","examples":["Women are too often constrained by family commitments and by low expectations. 女性往往受家庭職責及低期望值約束。"]}]}]},"constraint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"限制，束縛；剋制，拘束"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>constraint</b> is something that limits or controls what you can do. 限制","examples":["Their decision to abandon the trip was made because of financial constraints. 他們放棄這次旅行的決定是因財務限制而作出的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Constraint</b> is control over the way you behave which prevents you from doing what you want to do. 約束","examples":["Journalists were given the freedom to visit, investigate, and report without constraint. 新聞記者被賦予在沒有約束下參觀、調查和報道的自由。"]}]}]},"consultancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"諮詢公司；諮詢意見，顧問工作"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>consultancy</b> is a company that gives expert advice on a particular subject. 諮詢公司","examples":["A survey of 57 hospitals by Newchurch, a consultancy, reveals striking improvements. 紐徹奇諮詢公司對57家醫院的調查顯示明顯的改善。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Consultancy</b> is expert advice on a particular subject which a person or group is paid to provide to a company or organization. 諮詢","examples":[]}]}]},"courteously":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有禮貌地，彬彬有禮地，親切地"}],"sections":[]},"cordially":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"誠摯地，誠懇地，熱誠地；友善地；書信或郵件署名前的客套語，謹上"}],"sections":[]},"controlling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（常含貶義，多作定語）控制慾強的，愛支配人的；（財經、法律）控股的，有控制權的（用於 controlling interest、controlling stake、controlling shareholder 等搭配）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"控制；管理（control 的現在分詞或動名詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Control</b> <b>of</b> an organization, place, or system is the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. (對某組織機構的) 控制","examples":["The restructuring involves Mr. Ronson giving up control of the company. 公司重組需要羅森先生放棄對公司的控制。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>control</b> of something or someone, you are able to make them do what you want them to do. (對某物或某人的) 控制","examples":["He lost control of his car. 他失去了對他的車的控制。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you show <b>control</b>, you prevent yourself behaving in an angry or emotional way. (對憤怒情緒等的) 剋制","examples":["He had a terrible temper, and sometimes he would completely lose control. 他脾氣暴躁，有時會完全失控。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Control</b> is also a noun. 管制","examples":["Control of inflation remains the government's absolute priority. 控制通貨膨脹仍然是政府的第一要務。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"A <b>control</b> is a device such as a switch or lever which you use in order to operate a machine or other piece of equipment. 控制裝置","examples":["I practised operating the controls. 我練習過操作這些控制裝置。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"<b>Controls</b> are the methods that a government uses to restrict increases, for example in prices, wages, or weapons. (政府的) 調控","examples":["Critics question whether price controls would do any good. 批評家們懷疑物價調控的作用。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"<b>Control</b> is used to refer to a place where your documents or luggage are officially checked when you enter a foreign country. 海關檢查處","examples":["He went straight through Passport Control without incident. 他順利透過了護照檢查。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>under</b> your <b>control</b>, you have the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. 處於…控制之下","examples":["All the newspapers are under government control. 所有的報紙都處在政府控制之下。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>in control</b> <b>of</b> something, you have the power to make all the important decisions about the way it is run. 掌管","examples":["Nobody knows who is in control of the club. 沒有人知道誰掌管這個俱樂部。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>out of control</b>, no one has any power over it. 失控","examples":["The fire is burning out of control. 火勢失控。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something harmful is <b>under control</b>, it is being dealt with successfully and is unlikely to cause any more harm. 處在控制之下","examples":["The situation is under control. 局面得到了控制。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受控制的","examples":["...a controlled experiment. …一個受控制的試驗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"剋制的","examples":["Her manner was quiet and very controlled. 她舉止恬靜很有涵養。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The people who <b>control</b> an organization or place have the power to make all the important decisions about the way that it is run. 管理","examples":["He now controls the largest retail development empire in southern California. 他現在管理著加利福尼亞南部最大的零售業帝國。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>control</b> a piece of equipment, process, or system means to make it work in the way that you want it to work. 控制 (裝置系統等)","examples":["...a computerized system to control the gates. …一個控制大門的計算機系統。","Scientists would soon be able to manipulate human genes to control the aging process. 科學家將很快能夠透過操控人類基因來控制衰老的過程。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a government <b>controls</b> prices, wages, or the activity of a particular group, it uses its power to restrict them. (政府) 管制 (價格、工資、團體活動等)","examples":["The federal government tried to control rising health-care costs. 聯邦政府努力控制不斷上漲的衛生保健費用。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>control</b> <b>yourself</b>, or if you <b>control</b> your feelings, voice, or expression, you make yourself behave calmly even though you are feeling angry, excited, or upset. 抑制 (感情、聲音、表情)","examples":["Jo was advised to learn to control herself. 人們建議喬要學會控制自己的情緒。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"To <b>control</b> something dangerous means to prevent it from becoming worse or from spreading. 抑制 (危險物)","examples":["...the need to control environmental pollution. …控制環境汙染的需要。"]}]}]},"courier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導遊，旅遊服務員；快遞員，快遞公司；（地下或間諜組織的）情報員"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"專遞投送，透過信使或遞送員遞送（貨物或檔案）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>courier</b> is a person who is paid to take letters and packages direct from one place to another. 信使","examples":["...a motorcycle courier. …一名騎摩托車的信使。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>courier</b> something somewhere, you send it there by courier. 讓信使送","examples":["I couriered it to Darren in New York. 我讓信使把它送給在紐約的達倫。"]}]}]},"crafted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"精心製作的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"精巧地製作（craft 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a boat, a spacecraft, or an aircraft as a <b>craft</b>. 船; 航天器; 航空器","examples":["With great difficulty, the fisherman manoeuvred his small craft close to the reef. 漁夫艱難地駕著小船靠近了礁石。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>craft</b> is an activity such as weaving, carving, or pottery that involves making things skilfully with your hands. 工藝","examples":["...the arts and crafts of the North American Indians. …北美印第安人的美術工藝。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>craft</b> to refer to any activity or job that involves doing something skilfully. 職業","examples":["...the craft of writing. …寫作工作。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is crafted</b>, it is made skilfully. 精心製作","examples":["The windows would probably have been crafted in the latter part of the Middle Ages. 這些窗戶可能是中世紀後期精製而成。","...original, hand-crafted bags at affordable prices. …價格適中的獨創手工包。"]}]}]},"credential":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"資格，證明；文憑，資格證書；（政府為新任大使提供的）國書"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……提供證書"}],"sections":[]},"creditor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"債權人，貸方，債主"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>creditors</b> are the people who you owe money to. 債權人","examples":["The company said it would pay in full all its creditors except Credit Suisse. 該公司說將全額付款給除瑞士信貸以外的所有債權人。"]}]}]},"crowded":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"擁擠的，塞滿的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"聚集，群集；擠滿，塞滿；靠近，盯著（crowd 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a place is <b>crowded</b>, it is full of people. 擁擠的","examples":["He peered slowly around the small crowded room. 他慢慢地仔細打量著那間擁擠的小房間的每個角落。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place is <b>crowded</b>, a lot of people live there. 人口密集的","examples":["...a crowded city of 2 million. …一個有200萬人口的擁擠的城市。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If your schedule, your life, or your mind is <b>crowded</b>, it is full of events, activities, or thoughts. 排滿的","examples":["Never before has a summit had such a crowded agenda. 從來沒有一個高峰會議把議程安排得這樣滿。"]}]}]},"customize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"訂製，改制（以滿足顧主的需要）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>customize</b> something, you change its appearance or features to suit your tastes or needs. 個性化設定","examples":["...a control that allows photographers to customize the camera's basic settings. …一種允許攝影師個性化設定相機基本設定的控制裝置。"]}]}]},"daring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"勇於冒險的，勇於創新的；大膽的，無畏的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"勇氣，膽量"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"敢於，膽敢；激，激將（dare 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People who are <b>daring</b> are willing to do or say things which are new or which might shock or anger other people. 大膽的","examples":["Bergit was probably more daring than I was. 伯傑特可能比我膽子還大。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>daring</b> person is willing to do things that might be dangerous. 勇敢的","examples":["His daring rescue saved the lives of the youngsters. 他英勇的救援行動挽救了那些少年的生命。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Daring</b> is the courage to do things which might be dangerous or which might shock or anger other people. 膽量; 魯莽","examples":["His daring may have cost him his life. 他的魯莽差點要了他的命。"]}]}]},"cutback":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"減少，削減；（影視、小說中的）情節倒敘，回切；（體育，尤指美式橄欖球）變向回切"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>cutback</b> is a reduction that is made in something. 削減","examples":["The region has also been hit hard by cutbacks in defence spending, which has left thousands out of work. 該地區也深受造成數千人失業的國防開支縮減的打擊。"]}]}]},"database":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）資料庫，資料庫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>database</b> is a collection of data that is stored in a computer and that can easily be used and added to. 資料庫","examples":["The state maintains a database of names of people allowed to vote. 該州有一個可以投票的人的姓名資料庫。"]}]}]},"daylight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"白天，日光；黎明，拂曉；差距，差別"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Daylight</b> is the natural light that there is during the day, before it gets dark. 日光","examples":["Lack of daylight can make people feel depressed. 缺乏日光的照射會讓人情緒低落。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Daylight</b> is the time of day when it begins to get light. 拂曉","examples":["Quinn returned shortly after daylight yesterday morning. 奎因昨天天剛亮就回來了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a crime is committed <b>in broad daylight</b>, you are expressing your surprise that it is done during the day when people can see it, rather than at night. 光天化日之下","examples":["A girl was attacked on a train in broad daylight. 光天化日之下，一個女孩在火車上遭襲。"]}]}]},"daytime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"白天，日間"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"日間的，白天的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>daytime</b> is the part of a day between the time when it gets light and the time when it gets dark. 白天","examples":["In the daytime he stayed up in his room, sleeping, or listening to music. 白天，他呆在自己的屋子裡睡覺或者聽音樂。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Daytime</b> television and radio is broadcast during the morning and afternoon on weekdays. 日間的","examples":["She took on the role as host of a daytime TV show. 她主持一個日間電視節目。"]}]}]},"debatable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（常作表語）有爭議的，有待商榷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>debatable</b>, you mean that it is not certain. 有爭議的","examples":["It is debatable whether or not the shareholders were ever properly compensated. 股東們是否曾被合理補償還存在爭議。"]}]}]},"debit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"借記，借方；借項，借款"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"記入（賬戶）的借方，借記；（從銀行賬戶中）取款"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When your bank <b>debits</b> your account, money is taken from it and paid to someone else. 記入…的借方賬戶","examples":["We will always confirm the revised amount to you in writing before debiting your account. 在記入你的借方賬戶前，我們每次都會以書面形式向你確認修改過的數額。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>debit</b> is a record of the money taken from your bank account, for example, when you write a cheque. 借方","examples":["The total of debits must balance the total of credits. 借方總額必須和貸款總方相抵。"]}]}]},"dean":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"院長，教務長；主任牧師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dean</b> is an important official at a university or college. (大學的) 學院院長; 系主任","examples":["She was dean of the University of Washington's Graduate School. 她曾任華盛頓大學研究生院的院長。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>dean</b> is a priest who is the main administrator of a large church. 教長","examples":["...Bob Gregg, dean of the Chapel, Stanford Memorial Church. 斯坦福紀念教堂小教堂教長，鮑勃·格雷格。"]}]}]},"dealing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交往，交易；經營方式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that you need or have <b>a great deal of</b> or <b>a good deal of</b> a particular thing, you are emphasizing that you need or have a lot of it. 數量","examples":["...a great deal of money. …許多錢。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal</b> is also an adverb. 非常","examples":["As a relationship becomes more established, it also becomes a good deal more complex. 當一段關係固定下來以後，它也會變得複雜得多。"]}]},{"pos":"pron.","pos_name":"代詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal</b> is also a pronoun. 量","examples":["Although he had never met Geoffrey Hardcastle, he knew a good deal about him. 儘管他從未見過傑弗裡·哈德卡斯爾，他還是十分了解他。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>make</b> a <b>deal</b>, <b>do</b> a <b>deal</b>, or <b>cut</b> a <b>deal</b>, you complete an agreement or an arrangement with someone, especially in business. 達成協議; 達成交易","examples":["He made a deal to testify against the others and wasn't charged. 他達成了協議出庭指證別人，因而未獲指控。","Japan will have to do a deal with the U.S. on rice imports. 日本將不得不就水稻進口問題和美國達成協議。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone has had a <b>bad deal</b>, they have been unfortunate or have been treated unfairly. 不公的待遇","examples":["The people of Hartford have had a bad deal for many, many years. 許多年來，哈特福德地區的人們遭受著不幸。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"a plank of softwood timber, such as fir or pine, or such planks collectively 軟木板","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, company, or shop <b>deals in</b> a particular type of goods, their business involves buying or selling those goods. 經營","examples":["They deal in antiques. 他們經營古董生意。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>deals</b> illegal drugs, they sell them. 販賣 (毒品)","examples":["I certainly don't deal drugs. 我當然不做毒品生意。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>deal</b> playing cards, you give them out to the players in a game of cards. (紙牌遊戲中) 發 (牌)","examples":["The croupier dealt each player a card, face down. 賭局主持人給每個玩牌者發了一張牌，牌面向下。"]}]},{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to give (a blow) to (someone); inflict 給(某人)以打擊","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deal out</b> means the same as . (紙牌遊戲中) 發 (牌)","examples":["Dalton dealt out five cards to each player. 多爾頓給每個玩牌的人發了5張牌。"]}]}]},"decease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"死亡；亡故（正式用語）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（正式用語）死亡；去世"}],"sections":[]},"deceit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"欺騙，詭計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Deceit</b> is behaviour that is deliberately intended to make people believe something which is not true. 欺騙","examples":["He was living a secret life of deceit and unfaithfulness. 他過著欺騙和不忠的隱瞞生活。"]}]}]},"deceitful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"欺騙的，撒謊的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>deceitful</b>, you mean that they behave in a dishonest way by making other people believe something that is not true. 欺騙的","examples":["The ambassador called the report deceitful and misleading. 大使稱該報導是不實的和誤導的。"]}]}]},"deceleration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"減速，減速過程，降低速度；（物理）減速度，負加速度；（經濟）<喻>增長減緩，增速回落"}],"sections":[]},"decelerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"減速，降低速度；（經濟增長、通貨膨脹等）減緩"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使減速"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a vehicle or machine <b>decelerates</b> or when someone in a vehicle <b>decelerates</b>, the speed of the vehicle or machine is reduced. 減速","examples":["...the sensation of the train decelerating. ... 火車減速的感覺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When the rate of something such as inflation or economic growth <b>decelerates</b>, it slows down. 減緩","examples":["Inflation has decelerated remarkably over the past two years. 過去兩年裡通貨膨脹已經顯著地減緩了。"]}]}]},"collaborate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"合作，協作；勾結，通敵"}],"sections":[]},"decode":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"破譯，譯解（密碼資訊）；譯解（電子訊號），破解轉換（電視廣播訊號）；理解（外文）；解讀，揣摩（戲劇、藝術作品、行為等）；（計算機）解（碼）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>密碼譯文"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>decode</b> a message that has been written or spoken in a code, you change it into ordinary language. 解碼","examples":["All he had to do was decode it and pass it over. 他所要做的就是解譯它，然後把它發過去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A device that <b>decodes</b> a broadcast signal changes it into a form that can be displayed on a television screen. 轉換 (訊號)","examples":["About 60,000 subscribers have special adapters to receive and decode the signals. 大約60000使用者有專用介面卡來接收和轉換訊號。"]}]}]},"deduce":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"推斷，演繹；<古>對……追本溯源"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deduce</b> something or <b>deduce</b> that something is true, you reach that conclusion because of other things that you know to be true. 演繹; 推斷","examples":["Alison cleverly deduced that I was the author of the letter. 艾莉森聰明地推斷出我是這封信的作者。","The date of the document can be deduced from references to the Civil War. 該檔案的日期可以從其對內戰的提及處推算出來。"]}]}]},"deduct":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"減去，扣除"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>deduct</b> an amount from a total, you subtract it from the total. 扣除","examples":["The company deducted this payment from his compensation. 公司從他的補償金中扣除了這筆款項。"]}]}]},"debut":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"首次登臺，（新事物的）問世"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"初次登臺，首次亮相；首次推出（某產品）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>debut</b> of a performer or sports player is their first public performance, appearance, or recording. 首次登臺","examples":["She made her debut in a 1937 production of \"Hamlet.\" 她在1937年《哈姆雷特》的演出中首次登臺。"]}]}]},"deduction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"演繹，推論；扣除，扣除額"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>deduction</b> is an amount that has been subtracted from a total. 扣除額","examples":["Most homeowners can get a federal income tax deduction on interest payments to a home equity loan. 在支付房屋淨值貸款利息方面，大多數房主可以享受聯邦所得稅減免待遇。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>deduction</b> is a conclusion that you have reached about something because of other things that you know to be true. 推演出來的結論","examples":["It was a pretty astute deduction. 那是個非常精明的結論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Deduction</b> is the process of reaching a conclusion about something because of other things that you know to be true. 演繹; 推論","examples":["Miss Allan beamed at him. \"You are clever to guess. I'm sure I don't know how you did it.\"—\"Deduction,\" James said. 阿倫小姐對他笑道：“你很會猜， 我確實不知道你怎麼辦到的。”——傑姆斯說：“推論。”"]}]}]},"deflate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"放氣，使（輪胎、氣球等）癟下去或縮小；使洩氣，打擊（信心、自尊）；（經濟）緊縮通貨，壓低（價格）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"（輪胎、氣球等）漏氣，癟下去或縮小；（經濟）緊縮，物價下降"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deflate</b> someone or something, you take away their confidence or make them seem less important. 使洩氣","examples":["I hate to deflate your ego, but you seem to have an exaggerated idea of your importance to me. 我不願傷你的自尊，但是你好像高估了你對我的重要性。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"洩氣的","examples":["When she refused I felt deflated. 她拒絕時，我感到很沮喪。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something such as a tyre or balloon <b>deflates</b>, or when you <b>deflate</b> it, all the air comes out of it. 放氣; 漏氣","examples":["We drove a few miles until the tyre deflated and we had to stop the car. 我們開了幾英里直到輪胎漏氣了，然後我們不得不停下車。"]}]}]},"deflect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使轉向，使偏斜，使彎曲；轉移（批評、注意力等）；使改變（主意、計劃等），常與 from 連用"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"轉向，偏斜"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>deflect</b> something such as criticism or attention, you act in a way that prevents it from being directed toward you or affecting you. 轉移","examples":["Cage changed his name to deflect accusations of nepotism. 凱奇改了名字以轉移裙帶關係的指責。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>deflect</b> someone <b>from</b> a course of action means to make them decide not to continue with it by putting pressure on them or by offering them something desirable. (透過施壓或給予好處) 使改變","examples":["The war did not deflect him from the path he had long ago taken. 戰爭沒有使他改變很久之前就選擇的道路。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>deflect</b> something that is moving, you make it go in a slightly different direction, for example, by hitting or blocking it. 使 (動作) 偏斜","examples":["My forearm deflected the first punch. 我的前臂擋開了第一拳。"]}]}]},"default":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不履行，違約；預設，系統設定值；缺席，棄權"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"違約，不履行義務；預設，預設；棄權，未到場"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"預設的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person, company, or country <b>defaults on</b> something that they have legally agreed to do, such as paying some money or doing a piece of work before a particular time, they fail to do it. 不履行 (義務); 違約","examples":["The credit card business is down, and more borrowers are defaulting on loans. 信用卡生意正在走下坡路，更多的借貸人不履行還貸責任。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Default</b> is also a noun. 不履行; 違約","examples":["The corporation may be charged with default on its contract with the government. 該公司可能會被指控違反了與政府簽訂的合同。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In computing, the <b>default</b> is a particular set of instructions which the computer always uses unless the person using the computer gives other instructions. 預設值","examples":["The default setting on Windows Explorer will not show these files. 視窗瀏覽器上的預設系統設定不顯示這些文件。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>default</b> situation is what exists or happens unless someone or something changes it. 原樣的","examples":["He appeared unimpressed; but then, unimpressed was his default state. 他看似不為所動，但是，不為所動就是他的原樣。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>by default</b>, it happens only because something else which might have prevented it or changed it has not happened. 在另外的可能性沒有發生的情況下","examples":["I would rather pay the individuals than let the money go to the State by default. 我寧可把錢付給個人，也不會毫無選擇就把錢交給國家。"]}]}]},"decipher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"破譯，辨認（難認、難解的東西）；理解（神秘或難懂的事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>decipher</b> a piece of writing or a message, you work out what it says, even though it is very difficult to read or understand. 破譯","examples":["I'm still no closer to deciphering the code. 破譯這個密碼我還是沒有進展。"]}]}]},"defy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"違抗，不服從；挑戰，激；無法，難以（描述或理解）；經受住，頂住"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>defy</b> someone or something that is trying to make you behave in a particular way, you refuse to obey them and behave in that way. 違抗","examples":["This was the first (and last) time that I dared to defy my mother. 這是我第一次（也是最後一次）膽敢違抗我母親。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>defy</b> someone <b>to</b> do something, you challenge them to do it when you think that they will be unable to do it or too frightened to do it. 向…挑戰; 惹","examples":["I defy you to come up with one major accomplishment of the current president. 我倒要看看你能否舉出現任董事長的一件主要成績。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something <b>defies</b> description or understanding, it is so strange, extreme, or surprising that it is almost impossible to understand or explain. 使不可能 (理解或解釋)","examples":["It's a devastating and barbaric act that defies all comprehension. 這是毀滅性的野蠻行徑，完全沒有方法可理解。"]}]}]},"deliberately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"故意地；從容不迫地，小心翼翼地"}],"sections":[]},"demographics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人口統計資料，人口統計資料；人口統計特徵（年齡、性別、收入、職業等）"}],"sections":[]},"delicacy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"美味，佳餚；脆弱，嬌嫩；微妙，棘手；審慎，體貼；（結構的）精巧，精緻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Delicacy</b> is the quality of being easy to break or harm, and refers especially to people or things that are attractive or graceful. 嬌弱; 精緻","examples":["...the delicacy of a rose. …玫瑰花的嬌嫩。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a situation or problem is <b>of</b> some <b>delicacy</b>, you mean that it is difficult to handle and needs careful and sensitive treatment. 微妙; 棘手","examples":["There was a matter of some delicacy on which he would be grateful for her advice. 有一件棘手的事，若能得到她的指點，他會感激不盡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone handles a difficult situation <b>with</b> <b>delicacy</b>, they handle it very carefully, making sure that nobody is offended. 考慮周到; 體諒","examples":["Both countries are behaving with rare delicacy. 兩個國家都表現出難得的體諒周到。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>delicacy</b> is a rare or expensive food that is considered especially nice to eat. 美味佳餚","examples":["Smoked salmon was considered an expensive delicacy. 燻三文魚被認為是一道昂貴的佳餚。"]}]}]},"delusion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"錯覺；妄想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>delusion</b> is a false idea. 錯覺","examples":["I was under the delusion that he intended to marry me. 我有一種錯覺，他要娶我。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Delusion</b> is the state of believing things that are not true. 妄想","examples":["Insinuations about her mental state, about her capacity for delusion, were being made. 當時有對她的精神狀態的影射——說她有妄想症的影射。"]}]}]},"demise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"倒閉，敗落；死亡，逝世；（律）（財產或所有權的）轉讓，遺贈"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（律）遺贈，轉讓（產業）；正式放棄，禪讓（最高統治者的頭銜）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>demise</b> of something or someone is their end or death. 終止; 死亡","examples":["...the demise of the reform movement. …改良運動的告終。"]}]}]},"demolish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"拆毀，拆除（建築物）；（意外）毀壞，破壞；推翻，駁倒（觀點或理論）；<非正式>輕易擊敗，完勝；<非正式>狼吞虎嚥地吃，很快吃光；傷害（感情），破壞（計劃）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>demolish</b> something such as a building means to destroy it completely. 徹底摧毀","examples":["A storm moved directly over the island, demolishing buildings and flooding streets. 一場暴風雨直掃這個島嶼，徹底摧毀了房屋，淹沒了街道。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>demolish</b> someone's ideas or arguments, you prove that they are completely wrong or unreasonable. 駁倒","examples":["Our intention was quite the opposite – to demolish rumours that have surrounded him since he took office. 我們的意圖恰恰相反–要粉碎自他就職以來就纏著他的謠言。"]}]}]},"departmental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"部門的；分科的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Departmental</b> is used to describe the activities, responsibilities, or possessions of a department in a government, company, or other organization. 部門的","examples":["The Secretary of Education is right to seek a bigger departmental budget. 教育部長尋求更多的部門預算是對的。"]}]}]},"dependency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"依賴，依靠，從屬；屬國，附屬國，屬地；從屬物；（多用於美式英語）（對藥物、酒精等的）成癮，依賴；（計算機軟體）依賴項或依賴關係"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dependency</b> is a country which is controlled by another country. 附屬國","examples":["...the tiny British dependency of Montserrat in the eastern Caribbean. …東加勒比地區英國的小附屬國蒙特塞拉特島。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You talk about someone's <b>dependency</b> when they have a deep emotional, physical, or financial need for a particular person or thing, especially one that you consider excessive or undesirable. 依賴","examples":["We saw his dependency on his mother and worried that he might not survive long if anything happened to her. 我們看到他對母親的依賴，擔心萬一她有個閃失，他也會活不長。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you talk about alcohol <b>dependency</b> or chemical <b>dependency</b>, you are referring to a situation where someone is an alcoholic or is addicted to drugs. (毒、酒) 癮","examples":["In 1985, he began to show signs of alcohol and drug dependency. 1985年，他開始表現出酗酒和吸毒成癮的跡象。"]}]}]},"dietician":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"營養師（專業人員，須獲得證書），膳食學家，營養學家（dietitian 的異體拼寫）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dietician</b> is a person whose job is to give people advice about the kind of food they should eat. 膳食學家","examples":[]}]}]},"detailed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"詳盡的，詳細的；（裝飾）精細的，細緻的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"詳細說明，詳述；徹底清洗（汽車）；（尤指軍隊中）派遣，選派（detail 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>detailed</b> report or plan contains a lot of details. 詳細的","examples":["Yesterday's letter contains a detailed account of the decisions. 昨天的信裡有對那些決定的詳細說明。"]}]}]},"developer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"開發商，開發公司；開發者，研製者；顯影劑，顯色劑；（在特定時間或以特定速度）成長（或發育成熟）的人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>developer</b> is a person or a company that buys land and builds houses, offices, stores, or factories on it, or buys existing buildings and makes them more modern. (房地產) 開發商","examples":["...common land which would have a high commercial value if sold to developers. …賣給開發商便有很高商業價值的普通地皮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>developer</b> is someone who develops something such as an idea, a design, or a product. 開發者","examples":["John Bardeen was also co-developer of the theory of superconductivity. 約翰·巴丁也是超導理論的共同發展人。"]}]}]},"disclaimer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"免責宣告，否認宣告；（法律）放棄權利、利益或主張"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>disclaimer</b> is a statement in which a person says that they did not know about something or that they are not responsible for something. 免責宣告","examples":["The company asserts in a disclaimer that it won't be held responsible for the accuracy of information. 該公司在一項免責宣告裡宣稱它不會對資訊的準確性負責。"]}]}]},"discouraged":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"洩氣的，心灰意冷的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使洩氣，使灰心；阻礙，制止（discourage 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>discourages</b> you, they cause you to lose your enthusiasm about your actions. 使氣餒","examples":["It may be difficult to do at first. Don't let this discourage you. 開始時做起來也許比較困難。不要讓這個洩你的氣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>discourage</b> an action or to <b>discourage</b> someone <b>from</b> doing it means to make them not want to do it. 阻攔","examples":["...typhoons that discouraged shopping and leisure activities. …打消購物和休閒活動的念頭的數起颱風。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"氣餒的","examples":["She was determined not to be too discouraged. 她下了決心不要太氣餒。"]}]}]},"discern":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（艱難地或努力地）看出，覺察出；瞭解，認識"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you can <b>discern</b> something, you are aware of it and know what it is. 認識; 瞭解","examples":["You need a long series of data to be able to discern such a trend. 你需要一大串資料才能認清這一趨勢。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you can <b>discern</b> something, you can just see it, but not clearly. 隱約看見","examples":["Below the bridge we could just discern a narrow, weedy ditch. 在橋下我們僅可隱約看見一條狹窄的、雜草叢生的溝壑。"]}]}]},"directly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"直接地，徑直地；坦率地；恰好，正好；立即，很快地"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"一……就……"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>directly</b> above, below, or in front of something, it is in exactly that position. 正好地","examples":["The second rainbow will be bigger than the first, and directly above it. 第二道彩虹將比第一道更大，並位於第一道的正上方。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do one action <b>directly</b> <b>after</b> another, you do the second action as soon as the first one is finished. 立即","examples":["Most guests left directly after the wake. 守靈儀式一結束，大部分客人就立刻走了。"]}]}]},"disembark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<正式>（乘客等）離開所乘的船、飛機、火車或巴士，上岸，登陸，下車"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"<正式>使（乘客等）登陸，上岸，下車；卸下（貨物）送上岸"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When passengers <b>disembark</b> <b>from</b> a ship, aeroplane, or bus, they leave it at the end of their trip. 著陸; 上岸; 下車","examples":["I looked toward the plane. Six passengers had already disembarked. 我向飛機看去。6名乘客已下機。"]}]}]},"distributor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經銷商，批發商；（汽油發動機中的）配電器，配電盤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>distributor</b> is a company that supplies goods to stores or other businesses. 配銷商; 批發商","examples":["...Spain's largest distributor of petroleum products. …西班牙最大的石油產品經銷商。"]}]}]},"dissipate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使某事物）消散，消失；揮霍，耗費；放蕩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When something <b>dissipates</b> or when you <b>dissipate</b> it, it becomes less or becomes less strong until it disappears or goes away completely. 驅散; 消散","examples":["The tension in the room had dissipated. 房間裡的緊張氣氛已經消散了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When someone <b>dissipates</b> money, time, or effort, they waste it in a foolish way. 浪費 (金錢、時間、努力等)","examples":["He needs someone who can keep him from dissipating his time and energy on too many different things. 他需要有人來阻止他浪費時間和精力做太多不同的事情。"]}]}]},"dismal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"憂鬱的，陰沉的；<非正式>差勁的，糟糕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>dismal</b> is bad in a sad or depressing way. 慘淡不良的","examples":["...Israel's dismal record in the Olympics. …以色列在奧運會上的慘淡紀錄。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>dismal</b> is sad and depressing, especially in appearance. (尤指外表) 沉悶的","examples":["The main part of the hospital is pretty dismal but the children's ward is really lively. 這家醫院的主要地方頗為沉悶，但是兒科病房卻很有生氣。"]}]}]},"disrupt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"中斷，擾亂；徹底改變（某物）的結構，使（某物）的結構破裂；使瓦解，使分裂"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something <b>disrupts</b> an event, system, or process, they cause difficulties that prevent it from continuing or operating in a normal way. 妨礙; 擾亂","examples":["Anti-war protesters disrupted the debate. 反戰示威者們擾亂了辯論。"]}]}]},"diversification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新產品的開發，多樣化經營"}],"sections":[]},"dotted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有斑點的，有點的，點狀的；（常用於 be dotted with / dotted around）星羅棋佈的，散佈的；（音樂）加附點的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"dot 的過去式和過去分詞：打點於，加小點於；星羅棋佈於，遍佈，點綴；（音樂）給（音符、休止符）加附點；（非正式）擊打（某人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>dotted</b> line is a line which is made of a row of dots. 由點構成的","examples":["Cut along the dotted line. 沿虛線剪開。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place or object is <b>dotted with</b> things, it has many of those things scattered over its surface. 佈滿的","examples":["The maps were dotted with the names of small towns. 地圖上標滿了各個小鎮的名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If things are <b>dotted</b> <b>around</b> a place, they can be found in many different parts of that place. 分散的","examples":["Many pieces of sculpture are dotted around the house. 雕塑作品在房子裡四處可見。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>sign on the dotted line</b>, you formally agree to something by signing an official document. 正式簽約接受","examples":[]}]}]},"documentation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"證明檔案，憑證；（書面、電影等形式的）記載，記錄；（電腦裝置或程式的）說明書；（對文字、照片等的）分類，評註"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Documentation</b> consists of documents which provide proof or evidence of something, or are a record of something. 檔案證據","examples":["Passengers must carry proper documentation. 旅客必須攜帶適當的證明材料。"]}]}]},"downsizing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精簡，裁員；縮小規模"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>downsize</b> something such as a business or industry means to make it smaller. 使縮小規模","examples":["American manufacturing organizations have been downsizing their factories. 美國製造商們一直在縮小他們工廠的規模。","...today's downsized economy. … 今天萎縮了的經濟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"縮小規模","examples":["...a trend toward downsizing in the personal computer market. …個人電腦市場規模縮小的趨勢。"]}]}]},"drastically":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（動作或變化）猛烈地，力度大地 ；極其，非常"}],"sections":[]},"dress code":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"著裝規範，著裝要求，著裝規定"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>dress code</b> of a place is the rules about what kind of clothes people are allowed to wear there. 著裝標準; 著裝規定","examples":["There was a brutally enforced dress code, which required women to be covered from head to toe. 曾有著嚴格的著裝規定，要求女士從頭到腳都要裹緊。"]}]}]},"eco-friendly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"環保的，對生態環境友好的，不損壞生態環境的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Eco-friendly</b> products or services are less harmful to the environment than other similar products or services. 環保的","examples":["...eco-friendly laundry detergent. …環保洗衣劑。"]}]}]},"economize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"節約，有效利用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>economize</b>, you save money by spending it very carefully. 節省開支","examples":["We're going to have to economize from now on. 我們得從現在起節省開支。"]}]}]},"eject":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"驅逐，趕出；噴射，排出；（飛行員從即將墜毀的飛機中）彈出；（磁帶或光碟）彈出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>eject</b> someone <b>from</b> a place, you force them to leave. 逐出","examples":["Officials used guard dogs to eject the protesters. 官員們用護衛犬驅走抗議者。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>eject</b> something means to remove it or push it out forcefully. 用力排出; 用力推出","examples":["He aimed his rifle, fired a single shot, then ejected the spent cartridge. 他用步槍瞄準，開了一槍，接著排出了空彈殼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"逐出","examples":["...the ejection and manhandling of hecklers at the meeting. …對會上起鬨者的驅逐和推搡。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When a pilot <b>ejects</b> <b>from</b> an aircraft, he or she leaves the aircraft quickly using an ejector seat, usually because the plane is about to crash. (從飛機裡) 彈射出來","examples":["The pilot ejected from the plane and escaped injury. 飛行員從飛機裡彈出，沒有受傷。"]}]}]},"duplicate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"複製，影印；（無必要地）重複（某事）；使成倍增加"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完全一樣的，複製的；二重的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"完全一樣的東西，複製品"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>duplicate</b> something that has already been done, you repeat or copy it. 複製","examples":["His task will be to duplicate his success overseas here at home. 他的任務將是在國內複製他在海外的成功。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>duplicate</b> something which has been written, drawn, or recorded onto tape means to make exact copies of it. 影印; 複製","examples":["...a business which duplicates video tapes for the film makers. …一家為電影製片人複製錄影帶的企業。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Duplicate</b> is also a noun. 複製; 複製品","examples":["The tight race is almost a duplicate of the elections in Georgia and South Dakota last month that pitted a Republican challenger against a Democratic incumbent. 這次緊張的競選幾乎是上個月在佐治亞州和南達科他州選舉的翻版，由一個共和黨的挑戰者競爭一個現任的民主黨人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Duplicate</b> is also a noun. 複本","examples":["I'm on my way to Switzerland, but I've lost my card. I've got to get a duplicate. 我在去瑞士的路上，但是我的卡丟了。我得弄張補發卡。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Duplicate</b> is used to describe things that have been made as an exact copy of other things, usually in order to serve the same purpose. 複製的","examples":["He let himself in with a duplicate key. 他用一把另配的鑰匙開啟門進去了。"]}]}]},"downsize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"裁減人員，裁員；縮小尺寸，縮減規模，減小規模；以較小尺寸設計"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>downsize</b> something such as a business or industry means to make it smaller. 使縮小規模","examples":["American manufacturing organizations have been downsizing their factories. 美國製造商們一直在縮小他們工廠的規模。","...today's downsized economy. … 今天萎縮了的經濟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"縮小規模","examples":["...a trend toward downsizing in the personal computer market. …個人電腦市場規模縮小的趨勢。"]}]}]},"elegance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"優雅，雅緻；簡練"}],"sections":[]},"elemental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"基本的，根本的，主要的；（化學）元素的，單質的；自然力的；（歷史、哲學）四大要素的（土、水、氣、火）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（古希臘神話、奇幻遊戲中的）四元素精靈，元素生物；基本原理"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elemental</b> feelings and types of behaviour are simple, basic, and forceful. (感情和行為等)質樸的; 內在的","examples":["...the elemental life they would be living in this new colony. ...他們在這塊新殖民地上將要過的簡樸生活。"]}]}]},"emit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"排放，散發（尤指氣體、輻射物）；發出（聲音或噪音）；發行，發表"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>emits</b> heat, light, gas, or a smell, it produces it and sends it out by means of a physical or chemical process. 發出; 散發 (熱、光、氣體或氣味)","examples":["The new device emits a powerful circular column of light. 這個新裝置發出一束強烈的環形光柱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>emit</b> a sound or noise means to produce it. 發出 (聲音或噪音)","examples":["Whitney blinked and emitted a long, low whistle. 惠特尼眨了眨眼，吹出了一聲長而低沉的口哨。"]}]}]},"elevation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"高度，海拔；立面，立檢視；提拔，提升；增加，升高；高地，高處；（槍炮的）射角，仰角；空中動作技巧"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>elevation</b> of a place is its height above sea level. 海拔","examples":["We're probably at an elevation of about 13,000 feet above sea level. 我們很可能在海拔13000英尺的高度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>elevation</b> is a piece of ground that is higher than the area around it. 高地","examples":["...the monument was on an elevation, which could be seen from the church. …這座紀念碑在一塊高地上，從教堂能看到。"]}]}]},"emulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"仿效，模仿；模擬；努力趕上"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古>爭強好勝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>emulate</b> something or someone, you imitate them because you admire them a great deal. 效仿","examples":["Sons are traditionally expected to emulate their fathers. 傳統上認為兒子應該效仿他們的父親。"]}]}]},"elimination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消除，排除；淘汰；消滅，剷除；排洩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Elimination</b> is the process of getting rid of waste products from your body by going to the bathroom. 排洩","examples":["Breast-feeding is as natural as sex or elimination or any other bodily function. 母乳哺養是天生的，就像性交、排洩或者其他任何身體功能一樣。"]}]}]},"empathy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"共鳴，同情；感同身受，產生共鳴（的能力）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Empathy</b> is the ability to share another person's feelings and emotions as if they were your own. 同感能力","examples":["Having begun my life in a children's home, I have great empathy with the little ones. 在一家兒童福利院長大使我對這些小孩子們懷有深深的同感。"]}]}]},"endorsement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"背書，票據簽字；（駕駛執照上的）違章記錄；（說明不予理賠或變更細節的）保險單附加條款；贊同，支援；（為某產品或服務所做的）宣傳，代言"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>endorsement</b> is a statement or action that shows you support or approve of something or someone. 認可","examples":["This is a powerful endorsement for his softer style of government. 這是對他的更溫和的執政風格的強有力認可。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>endorsement</b> <b>for</b> a product or company involves appearing in advertisements for it or showing support for it. 代言","examples":["His commercial endorsements for everything from running shoes to breakfast cereals will take his earnings to more than ten million dollars a year. 他的商業代言從跑鞋到早餐麥片一應俱全，令其年收入達到一千多萬美元。"]}]}]},"entertainer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"演藝人員，表演者（以表演、歌唱、講笑話等娛樂觀眾的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>entertainer</b> is a person whose job is to entertain audiences, for example, by telling jokes, singing, or dancing. 表演藝人","examples":["Some have called him the greatest entertainer of the twentieth century. 有人稱他為20世紀最偉大的表演藝術家。"]}]}]},"entirely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地，完整地；僅僅，只"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Entirely</b> means completely and not just partly. 完全地","examples":["...an entirely new approach. …一種全新的方法。","Their price depended almost entirely on their scarcity. 他們的價格幾乎完全靠他們的供不應求。","This administration is not entirely free of suspicion. 這屆政府並不是完全沒有疑點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Entirely</b> is also used to emphasize what you are saying. 完全地","examples":["I agree entirely. 我完全贊同。"]}]}]},"entitled":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有資格的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使享有權利；給……命名（或題名）（entitle 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>are entitled</b> <b>to</b> something, you have the right to have it or do it. 使有權","examples":["If the warranty is limited, the terms may entitle you to a replacement or refund. 如果保修單有限制，這些條款可讓你有權換貨或退款。","They are entitled to first class travel. 他們有權享受頭等艙旅行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If the title of something such as a book, film, or painting is, for example, \"Sunrise,\" you can say that it <b>is entitled</b> \"Sunrise.\" 給 (書、電影、畫作等) 命名","examples":["...a performance entitled \"United States.\" …一場名為“合眾國”的演出。"]}]}]},"entrust":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"委託，交託"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>entrust</b> something important <b>to</b> someone or <b>entrust</b> them <b>with</b> it, you make them responsible for looking after it or dealing with it. 委託","examples":["He entrusted his cash to a business partner for investment in a series of projects. 他把現款委託給一個生意合夥人投資一系列專案。","They can be entrusted to solve major national problems. 他們能受託解決重大國家問題。"]}]}]},"envision":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"想象，預想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>envision</b> something, you envisage it. 設想","examples":["In the future we envision a federation of companies. 我們設想將來會有公司聯盟。","Alana never envisioned her college career ending like this. 阿蘭娜從未想到她的大學生涯會如此結束。"]}]}]},"equity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公平，公正；資產淨值；普通股；衡平法"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In finance, your <b>equity</b> is the sum of your assets, for example the value of your house, once your debts have been subtracted from it. 資產淨值","examples":["To capture his equity, Murphy must either sell or refinance. 要獲取他的資產淨值，墨菲必須出售或重新融資。"]}]}]},"ethics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行為準則，道德原則；倫理學，道德學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ethics</b> are moral beliefs and rules about right and wrong. 道德","examples":["Refugee workers said such action was a violation of medical ethics. 難民工作者稱這種行為違背了醫學道德。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>ethics</b> are the moral principles about right and wrong behaviour that they believe in. 行為準則","examples":["He told the police that he had thought honestly about the ethics of what he was doing. 他告訴警察他曾真誠地考慮過他所作所為依據的行為準則。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ethics</b> is the study of questions about what is morally right and wrong. 倫理學","examples":["...the teaching of ethics and moral philosophy. …倫理學和道德哲學的教學。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"An <b>ethic</b> of a particular kind is an idea or moral belief that influences the behaviour, attitudes, and philosophy of a group of people. 道德觀念","examples":["...the ethic of public service. …公共服務的道德觀念。"]}]}]},"evade":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"規避，逃避；難倒，使困惑；未能（被某人）獲得；（尤指違法犯罪後）逃脫，躲開（追捕）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>evade</b> something, you find a way of not doing something that you really ought to do. 逃避","examples":["By his own admission, he evaded paying taxes as a Florida real-estate speculator. 據他自己承認，他作為佛羅里達房地產投機商時逃過稅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>evade</b> a question or a topic, you avoid talking about it or dealing with it. 迴避 (問題、話題)","examples":["Too many companies, she says, are evading the issue. 她說太多公司都在迴避這個問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>evade</b> someone or something, you move so that you can avoid meeting them or avoid being touched or hit. 避開","examples":["She turned and gazed at the river, evading his eyes. 她轉身注視著那條河，避開了他的目光。"]}]}]},"evasive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不坦率的，模稜兩可的；逃避的，規避的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>evasive</b>, you mean that they deliberately avoid giving clear direct answers to questions. 避而不談的","examples":["He was evasive about the circumstances of his first meeting with Stanley Dean. 他對與斯坦利·迪安第一次見面的情形避而不談。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"避而不談地","examples":["\"Until I can speak to your husband I can't come to any conclusion about that,\" Manuel said evasively. “關於那件事情我要跟你丈夫談了之後才能作出結論，”曼紐爾託辭說。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>take evasive action</b>, you deliberately move away from someone or something in order to avoid meeting them or being hit by them. 採取退避行動","examples":["At least four high-flying warplanes had to take evasive action. 至少有4架高空飛行戰機不得不採取退避行動。"]}]}]},"evoke":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"引起，喚起（感情、記憶或形象）；召（魂），喚（神）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>evoke</b> a particular memory, idea, emotion, or response means to cause it to occur. 喚起 (記憶); 引起 (想法、情感、反應)","examples":["...the scene evoking memories of those old movies. …喚起對那些老電影的記憶的場景。"]}]}]},"exclusion":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"排斥，排除在外；被排除在外的人（或事物）；認為不可能；（合約中的）除外事項；<英>開除學籍"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>exclusion</b> <b>of</b> something is the act of deliberately not using, allowing, or considering it. 故意不用; 故意不考慮","examples":["It calls for the exclusion of all commercial lending institutions from the college loan programme. 這要求大學貸款專案不考慮所有商業貸款機構。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Exclusion</b> is the act of preventing someone from entering a place or taking part in an activity. 排斥","examples":["...women's exclusion from political power. …政治權力對婦女的排斥。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you do one thing <b>to the exclusion of</b> something else, you only do the first thing and do not do the second thing at all. 拋開…","examples":["Diane had dedicated her life to caring for him to the exclusion of all else. 黛安娜曾拋開其他一切，來一心一意地照顧他。"]}]}]},"enlist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）參軍，（使）入伍；爭取，謀取；贊助，支援"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>enlists</b> or <b>is enlisted</b>, they join the army, navy, marines, or air force. 使入伍; 入伍","examples":["He enlisted in the 82nd Airborne 20 years ago. 他20年前加入了第82空降師。","He enlisted as a private in the Mexican War. 他以列兵身份參加了墨西哥戰爭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>enlist</b> the help of someone, you persuade them to help or support you in doing something. 贏得","examples":["I had to cut down a tree and enlist the help of seven neighbours to get it out of the garden! 我不得不砍了一棵樹，然後找了7位鄰居幫忙把它從院子裡弄出去。"]}]}]},"exclusively":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"僅僅，單獨地，專門地；作為唯一的（訊息）來源"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Exclusively</b> is used to refer to situations or activities that involve only the thing or things mentioned, and nothing else. 排他地; 獨佔地","examples":["...an exclusively male domain. …一個由男性獨佔的領域。"]}]}]},"facto":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（拉丁藉詞固定短語成分，主要見於 de facto 等）事實上，實際上"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（拉丁藉詞固定短語成分，主要見於 de facto 等）事實上的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（Facto）<美>法克特（人名）"}],"sections":[]},"expedite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"加速，促進（行為，過程）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>expedite</b> something, you cause it to be done more quickly. 加快","examples":["We tried to help you expedite your plans. 我們試圖幫你加快你的計劃。"]}]}]},"expenditure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"經費，支出額；（時間、金錢、精力等的）消耗，花費"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Expenditure</b> is the spending of money on something, or the money that is spent on something. 花銷; 支出","examples":["Policies of tax reduction must lead to reduced public expenditure. 減稅政策必然導致公共開支減少。"]}]}]},"fabricate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"製造，生產；捏造，編造；組裝，裝配"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>fabricates</b> information, they invent it in order to deceive people. 偽造","examples":["All four claim that officers fabricated evidence against them. 4人全部聲稱官員們偽造了不利於他們的證據。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"偽造","examples":["She described the interview as a \"complete fabrication.\" 她把這次採訪描述為“純屬虛構”。"]}]}]},"explorer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"探險者，勘探者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>explorer</b> is someone who travels to places about which very little is known, in order to discover what is there. 探險者","examples":["...the travels of Columbus, Magellan, and many other explorers. …哥倫布、麥哲倫和許多其他探險家的旅行。"]}]}]},"familiarize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使瞭解，使熟悉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>familiarize</b> yourself <b>with</b> something, or if someone <b>familiarizes</b> you <b>with</b> it, you learn about it and start to understand it. 使熟悉","examples":["The goal of the experiment was to familiarize the people with the new laws. 該實驗的目的是使人們熟悉新的規則。"]}]}]},"facilitator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"促進者、推動者（指幫助個人或組織達成目標或使事情更容易進行的人、組織或因素，亦譯“服務商”）；引導者、協調員、主持人（指在會議、培訓等群體活動中引導討論、協調程序的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>facilitator</b> is a person or organization that helps another person or organization to do or to achieve a particular thing. 協調者","examples":["The conference is chaired by a highly skilled facilitator who has been fully trained. 會議由一位受過充分訓練、技巧嫻熟的協調人主持。"]}]}]},"faulty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有故障的，有缺陷的；（思維方法）有錯誤的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>faulty</b> piece of equipment has something wrong with it and is not working properly. 出故障的","examples":["The money will be used to repair faulty equipment. 這筆錢將被用來修理出故障的裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's argument or reasoning as <b>faulty</b>, you mean that it is wrong or contains mistakes, usually because they have not been thinking in a logical way. (常指未按邏輯思考而) 錯誤的","examples":["Their interpretation was faulty – they had misinterpreted things. 他們的解釋是錯誤的–他們曲解了事物。"]}]}]},"father-in-law":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"岳父，公公（配偶的父親）；繼父"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>father-in-law</b> is the father of their husband or wife. 公公; 岳父","examples":[]}]}]},"feasibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可行性，可能性"}],"sections":[]},"feat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"功績，壯舉；武藝，技藝"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合適的，靈巧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to an action, or the result of an action, as a <b>feat</b>, you admire it because it is an impressive and difficult achievement. 功績","examples":["A racing car is an extraordinary feat of engineering. 賽車是工程學的一項非凡業績。"]}]}]},"fellowship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"交情，友誼；（有相似愛好的）團體，協會，聯誼會；（高等院校的）研究員； <美>（研究生）獎學金；董事職位，會員資格；（決定獎學金人選的）獎學金評選組；特邀研究員（職位或專案）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fellowship</b> is a group of people that join together for a common purpose or interest. 團體","examples":["...the National Schizophrenia Fellowship. …全國精神分裂協會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fellowship</b> at a university is a post which involves research work. 研究員職位","examples":["He was offered a research fellowship at Yale. 他得到了一個耶魯大學的研究員職位。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Fellowship</b> is a feeling of friendship that people have when they are talking or doing something together and sharing their experiences. 交情","examples":["...a sense of community and fellowship. …一種社群歸屬感和友誼感。"]}]}]},"fertilize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（生物）使受精；（農業）給土地或作物施肥，使肥沃"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When an egg from the ovary of a woman or female animal <b>is fertilized</b>, a sperm from the male joins with the egg, causing a baby or young animal to begin forming. A female plant <b>is fertilized</b> when its reproductive parts come into contact with pollen from the male plant. 使受精; 使授粉","examples":["Certain varieties cannot be fertilized with their own pollen. 某些品種不能自花授粉。","...the normal sperm levels needed to fertilize the egg. …使卵子受精所需的正常精子水平。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>fertilize</b> land means to improve its quality in order to make plants grow well on it, by spreading solid animal waste or a chemical mixture on it. 使肥沃","examples":["The faeces contain nitrogen which fertilizes the soil. 排洩物含有肥沃土壤的氮。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受精; 授粉","examples":["From fertilization until birth is about 266 days. 從受精到出生大約是266天。"]}]}]},"fire drill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"消防演習，火災演習：模擬火災發生時，組織人員按疏散程式撤離的實踐演習。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there is a <b>fire drill</b> in a particular building, the people who spend time there practise what to do if there is a fire. 消防演習","examples":[]}]}]},"finalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"最後決定，敲定；結束談判，完成協議（或安排）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>finalize</b> something such as a plan or an agreement, you complete the arrangements for it, especially by discussing it with other people. 最終確定 (計劃、協議等)","examples":["Negotiators from the three countries finalized the agreement in August. 3個國家的談判代表在8月最終確定了協議。","We are saying nothing until all the details have been finalized. 在所有細節最終確定之前我們無可奉告。"]}]}]},"fiscal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（政府）財政的；<美>財政年度的；<美>金融的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<舊>（某些國家的）檢察官，財政官員；領伯勞"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fiscal</b> is used to describe something that relates to government money or public money, especially taxes. 財政的","examples":["...in 1987, when the government tightened fiscal policy. …1987年，當該政府緊縮財政政策時。"]}]}]},"fixture":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"固定裝置，固定傢俱；既定人選（或事物）；（預定的）體育賽事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fixtures</b> are fittings or furniture which belong to a building and are legally part of it, for example, a bathtub or a toilet. (房屋內如浴缸、馬桶等的) 固定裝置","examples":["...a detailed list of what fixtures and fittings are included in the purchase price. …詳細列出的室內設施與裝備包括在購買價格中。"]}]}]},"flawed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有瑕疵的，有缺陷的；（人）性格有缺陷的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（缺陷）損害；削弱；使有瑕疵（flaw 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>flawed</b> has a mark, fault, or mistake in it. 有缺陷的","examples":["These tests were so seriously flawed as to render the results meaningless. 這些測試存在著如此嚴重的缺陷，以至於使得結果毫無意義。"]}]}]},"fitness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"健康；（生物體的）環境適度；適合，勝任"}],"sections":[]},"flawless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"完美的，無瑕的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something or someone is <b>flawless</b>, you mean that they are extremely good and that there are no faults or problems with them. 完美的","examples":["Discovery's takeoff this morning from Cape Canaveral was flawless. “發現號”今晨從卡納維拉爾角的發射是完美的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"完美地","examples":["Each stage of the battle was carried off flawlessly. 戰鬥的每個階段都都進行得很完美。"]}]}]},"fluctuate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"波動，起伏不定；使波動，使動搖"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>fluctuates</b>, it changes a lot in an irregular way. 波動","examples":["Body temperature can fluctuate if you are ill. 如果你病了，體溫會波動。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"波動","examples":["Don't worry about tiny fluctuations in your weight. 不用擔心你體重的輕微波動。"]}]}]},"formatted":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有格式的，格式化的，按格式編排的；已格式化的（尤指磁碟、光碟等儲存介質）"}],"sections":[]},"folder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指硬紙或紙板制的）資料夾，紙夾；（計算機系統中的）資料夾；<美>摺疊式傳單（或小冊子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>folder</b> is a thin piece of cardboard in which you can keep loose papers. 活頁夾","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>folder</b> is a group of files that are stored together on a computer. (電腦上儲存檔案的) 資料夾","examples":[]}]}]},"fluctuation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"波動，起伏"}],"sections":[]},"foremost":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最前的，最重要的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"首先，第一；最基礎地，最重要地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>foremost</b> thing or person in a group is the most important or best. 最重要的; 最好的","examples":["He was one of the world's foremost scholars of ancient Indian culture. 他是世界上最優秀的古印度文化學者之一。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>first and foremost</b> to emphasize the most important quality of something or someone. 首先","examples":["It is first and foremost a trade agreement. 它首先是一項貿易協定。"]}]}]},"fixation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專注，迷戀；（心理分析）固戀，固著；固化，加固；定影，定像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you accuse a person of having <b>a</b> <b>fixation</b> <b>on</b> something or someone, you mean they think about a particular subject or person to an extreme and excessive degree. 痴迷","examples":["The country's fixation on the war may delay a serious examination of domestic needs. 該國對這場戰爭的執迷不悟可能會令其推遲認真地審視國內需求。"]}]}]},"forum":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"討論會；（因特網上的）論壇，討論區；法院，法庭；（古羅馬）公共集會場所"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>forum</b> is a place, situation, or group in which people exchange ideas and discuss issues, especially important public issues. 論壇","examples":["Members of the council agreed that was an important forum for discussion. 理事會成員們一致認為那是一個用於討論的重要論壇。"]}]}]},"fortunately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"幸運地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fortunately</b> is used to introduce or indicate a statement about an event or situation that is good. 幸好","examples":["Fortunately, the weather that winter was reasonably mild. 幸好那個冬季的天氣頗暖和。"]}]}]},"franchisor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特許人，授予特許者，特許專營授權公司"}],"sections":[]},"franchise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特許經營權；獲特許經營權的企業（商店）；公民權，選舉權；<美，非正式>職業運動隊；<美>（由運動聯合會授予的）會員運動隊擁有權；特許經營品牌（或創意）；在相關故事中出現相同角色的一組電影"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給予特許經銷權；給予……公民權（或選舉權）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>franchise</b> is an authority that is given by an organization to someone, allowing them to sell its goods or services or to take part in an activity which the organization controls. (公司授予某人的) 特許經營權","examples":["...fast-food franchises. …快餐特許經營權。","...the franchise to build and operate the tunnel. …建造、運營隧道的特許權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Franchise</b> is the right to vote in an election. 選舉權","examples":["...the introduction of universal franchise. …普選權的採用。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company <b>franchises</b> its business, it sells franchises to other companies, allowing them to sell its goods or services. 出售…的特許經營權","examples":["She has recently franchised her business. 她最近已出售了其公司的特許經營權。"]}]}]},"fueled":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"加燃料，給（車輛、機器等）加註燃料（fuel 的過去式/過去分詞，英式常作 fuelled）；推動，激起，加劇（常作 be fueled by）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"由燃燒燃料驅動、加熱或產生的；使用某種燃料的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Fuel</b> is a substance such as coal, oil, or petrol that is burned to provide heat or power. 燃料","examples":["They ran out of fuel. 他們用完了燃料。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>fuel</b> a situation means to make it become worse or more intense. 加劇","examples":["The result will inevitably fuel speculation about the prime minister's future. 該結果將不可避免地加劇人們對首相前途的猜測。"]}]}]},"fraudulent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"欺詐的，詐騙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fraudulent</b> activity is deliberately deceitful, dishonest, or untrue. 欺騙性的","examples":["...fraudulent claims about being a nurse. …謊稱自己是護士。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"欺騙性地","examples":["All 5,000 of the homes were fraudulently obtained. 5000所房子全都是騙取的。"]}]}]},"frankly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"坦率地，直率地；（表示直言）老實說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>frankly</b> when you are expressing an opinion or feeling to emphasize that you mean what you are saying, especially when the person you are speaking to may not like it. 坦率地說","examples":["\"You don't give a damn about my feelings, do you.\"—\"Quite frankly, I don't.\" “你一點也不在乎我的感情，是吧。” —“坦率地說，是的。”","Frankly, Thomas, this question of your loan is beginning to worry me. 坦率地說，托馬斯，你貸款的問題開始讓我擔憂。"]}]}]},"functioning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"執行，運作；功能，機能"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"能正常工作的，功能正常的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"function 的現在分詞/動名詞；執行，起作用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>function</b> of something or someone is the useful thing that they do or are intended to do. 作用","examples":["The main function of the investment banks is to raise capital for industry. 各投資銀行的主要作用是為產業籌集資金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>function</b> is a large formal dinner or party. 宴會; 社交聚會","examples":["...a private function hosted by one of his students. …由他的一個學生做東的一場私人宴會。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a machine or system <b>is functioning</b>, it is working or operating. 運轉","examples":["The authorities say the prison is now functioning normally. 當局稱該監獄現在在正常運轉。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>functions</b> <b>as</b> a particular thing, they do the work or fulfil the purpose of that thing. (作為某物) 起作用","examples":["On weekdays, one third of the room functions as workspace. 在工作日，這個房間的三分之一充當工作場所。"]}]}]},"flexibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"靈活性；彈性，柔性"}],"sections":[]},"funding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專款，撥款"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"資助，為……提供資金（fund 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Funding</b> is money which a government or organization provides for a particular purpose. (政府或組織為某目的而提供的) 資金","examples":["They hope for government funding for the programme. 他們希望得到政府為這一計劃提供的資金。"]}]}]},"gatekeeper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"看門人，守門人；（引申）把關者，把關人（控制他人接觸資訊、資源或機會的人、機構或機制）；（電信）網守（H.323 網路中提供呼叫准入控制和地址翻譯等功能的裝置或軟體）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gatekeeper</b> is a person who is in charge of a gate and who allows people through it. 看門人","examples":[]}]}]},"glamor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"魅力，迷人的美（等於 glamour）；（文學或歷史用法）魔法，魔力"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（罕用）迷惑；使有魅力（等於 glamour）"}],"sections":[]},"getaway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"逃走，逃跑（尤指犯罪後或被人追趕時）；<非正式>短假，短期休假；度假地，適合旅行的地方；（車輛）起步加速能力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone makes a <b>getaway</b>, they leave a place quickly, especially after committing a crime or when trying to avoid someone. (尤指犯罪後或逃避某人的) 逃跑","examples":["They made their getaway on a stolen motorcycle. 他們騎上一輛偷來的摩托車逃掉了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>getaway</b> is a short holiday somewhere. 短期休假","examples":["Weekend tours are ideal for families who want a short getaway. 週末旅行對於想要短期休假的家庭來說非常理想。"]}]}]},"geographic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"地理的，地理學的"}],"sections":[]},"generally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"籠統地，大概；通常，普遍地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>generally</b> to give a summary of a situation, activity, or idea without referring to the particular details of it. 籠統地","examples":["University teachers generally have admitted a lack of enthusiasm about their subjects. 大學教師們已大致承認對他們的學科缺乏熱情。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>generally</b> to say that something happens or is used on most occasions but not on every occasion. 通常地","examples":["As women we generally say and feel too much about these things. 作為女人，我們通常對這些事說得、感受得太多了。","In the diet, it is generally true that the darker the fruit the higher its iron content. 在飲食中，水果顏色越深，其鐵含量就越高，這通常是正確的。"]}]}]},"gift-wrap":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"用包裝紙包裝；將……包裝成禮品"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"包裝紙"}],"sections":[]},"glitch":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>小故障，失靈；（電子）短時脈衝波干擾，毛刺；（Glitch）人名；<英>格利奇"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<非正式>發生故障，出毛病"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glitch</b> is a problem that stops something from working properly or being successful. 故障","examples":["Manufacturing glitches have limited the factory's output. 製造過程中的故障影響了工廠的產量。"]}]}]},"glorify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"讚美，稱頌；（常含貶義）美化，吹捧；（宗教）頌揚（神），崇拜（神）；使更壯麗，使增輝"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>glorify</b> something means to praise it or make it seem good or special, usually when it is not. 美化","examples":["This magazine in no way glorifies gangs. 本雜誌決不美化各種犯罪團伙。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"美化","examples":["...the glorification of violence. …對暴力的美化。"]}]}]},"glossary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"詞彙表，術語表；專門詞典"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>glossary</b> of special, unusual, or technical words or expressions is an alphabetical list of them giving their meanings, for example at the end of a book on a particular subject. 詞彙表","examples":["A glossary of terms is included for the reader's convenience. 為了方便讀者，還收錄了術語彙編。"]}]}]},"goodwill":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"友善，善意；（公司的）信譽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Goodwill</b> is a friendly or helpful attitude toward other people, countries, or organizations. 友好","examples":["I invited them to dinner, a gesture of goodwill. 我邀請他們來吃飯以示友好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>goodwill</b> of a business is something such as its good reputation, which increases the value of the business. 商業信譽","examples":["We do not want to lose the goodwill built up over 175 years. 我們不想失去用175年建立起來的商業信譽。"]}]}]},"fundraiser":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"籌款人，資金籌集人；籌款活動，資金籌集活動"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>fundraiser</b> is an event which is intended to raise money for a particular purpose, for example, for a charity. 募集資金的活動","examples":["Organize a fundraiser for your church. 為你們的教堂組織一次募集資金的活動吧。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>fundraiser</b> is someone who works to raise money for a particular purpose, for example, for a charity. 募集資金者","examples":["...a fundraiser for the Democrats. …一位民主黨的募集資金者。"]}]}]},"gratuity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"小費，賞錢；贈物，贈金；（勞經）退職金，退休酬金"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>gratuity</b> is a gift of money to someone who has done something for you. 小費","examples":["The porter expects a gratuity. 那個搬運工想要小費。"]}]}]},"guidebook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"旅行指南；指南，手冊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>guidebook</b> is a book that gives tourists information about a town, area, or country. 旅行指南","examples":[]}]}]},"groundbreaking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"開創性的，突破性的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"動工，破土動工；開工奠基儀式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>groundbreaking</b> to describe things which you think are significant because they provide new and positive ideas, and influence the way people think about things. 開拓性的","examples":["...his groundbreaking novel on homosexuality. ...他在同性戀方面開拓性的小說。","...groundbreaking research. ...開拓性的研究。"]}]}]},"gradually":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"逐漸地，逐步地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something changes or is done <b>gradually</b>, it changes or is done in small stages over a long period of time, rather than suddenly. 逐漸地","examples":["Electricity lines to 30,000 homes were gradually being restored yesterday. 通向3萬戶人家的電線昨日被逐步修復。"]}]}]},"halfway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在中間，在中途；還可以，過得去"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在中間的，在中途的；不完全的，不徹底的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Halfway</b> means in the middle of a place or between two points, at an equal distance from each of them. 在中途地","examples":["He was halfway up the ladder. 他梯子上到了一半。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Halfway</b> means in the middle of a period of time or of an event. 在中間地","examples":["By then, it was October and we were more than halfway through our tour. 那時是10月，我們的行程已經過半。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Halfway</b> means fairly or reasonably. 相當地","examples":["You need hard currency to get anything halfway decent. 你得有硬通貨才能買到像樣點兒的東西。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Halfway</b> is also an adjective. 在中間的","examples":["Cleveland held a 12-point advantage at the halfway point. 克利夫蘭在半程時擁有12分的優勢。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>meet</b> someone <b>halfway</b>, you accept some of the points they are making so that you can come to an agreement with them. 對某人讓步","examples":["The Democrats are willing to meet the president halfway. 民主黨人願意對總統作出讓步。"]}]}]},"hallmark":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"特點，特徵；（金銀製品上標明純度及製作時間、地點的）印記"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……打金銀純度印記；使具有……特徵"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>hallmark</b> of something or someone is their most typical quality or feature. 標誌; 特徵","examples":["It's a technique that has become the hallmark of Amber Films. 這是一項已成為安伯電影公司標誌的技術。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hallmark</b> is an official mark put on things made of gold, silver, or platinum that indicates the quality of the metal, where the object was made, and who made it. (金銀等製品上的) 標記","examples":["Early pieces of Scottish silver carry the hallmarks of individual silversmiths. 早期的蘇格蘭銀器上都有各個銀匠的標記。"]}]}]},"handbag":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手提包；手袋（通常指女式）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（英式，非正式）抨擊；嚴厲批評"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handbag</b> is a small bag which a woman uses to carry things such as her money and keys in when she goes out. 女用手提包","examples":[]}]}]},"handbook":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"手冊，指南"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handbook</b> is a book that gives you advice and instructions about a particular subject, tool, or machine. 手冊; 使用說明書","examples":["...a handbook on pool maintenance. …一本泳池保養手冊"]}]}]},"handout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指發給學生或聽報告的人的）講義；施捨物，救濟品；傳單，宣傳材料；政府撥款（為促進商業活動）；不勞而獲的錢"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handout</b> is a gift of money, clothing, or food, which is given free to poor people. 施捨物; 救濟品; 救濟金","examples":["Each family is being given a cash handout of six thousand rupees. 每個家庭都被給予6000盧比的救濟金。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you call money that is given to someone a <b>handout</b>, you disapprove of it because you believe that the person who receives it has done nothing to earn or deserve it. 不勞而獲的錢","examples":["...the tendency of politicians to use money on vote-buying handouts rather than on investment in the future. …政客們用錢送人拉選票而不是用於未來投資的趨勢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>handout</b> is a document which contains news or information about something and which is given, for example, to journalists or members of the public. 傳單; 宣傳品","examples":["Official handouts describe the Emperor as \"particularly noted as a scholar.\" 官方宣傳品把這位皇帝描述成“尤以飽學著稱”。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>handout</b> is a paper given out to students by a teacher, that contains a summary of the information or topics that will be dealt with in a lesson. (教師給學生的) 講義","examples":["Many teachers are opting for group discussions instead of handouts. 許多教師選擇組織小組討論，而不是發講義。"]}]}]},"handling":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"處理，應對，對待；（貨物、物料等的）搬運，裝卸，操作；（車輛、機械等的）操縱效能，操控性"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"handle 的現在分詞；拿；處理；應付；操縱；操作；負責"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>handle</b> is a small round object or a lever that is attached to a door and is used for opening and closing it. 門把手","examples":["I turned the handle and found the door was open. 我轉動把手，發現門是開著的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>handle</b> is the part of an object such as a tool, bag, or cup that you hold in order to be able to pick up and use the object. 柄; 把","examples":["...a broom handle. …一個掃帚柄"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"應付","examples":["The family has criticized the military's handling of Robert's death. 羅伯特的家人批評軍方沒有處理好羅伯特的死亡。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone can <b>handle</b> a problem or situation, you mean that they have the ability to deal with it successfully. (成功地) 處理","examples":["To tell the truth, I don't know if I can handle the job. 說實話，我不知道我能否做好這份工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you talk about the way that someone <b>handles</b> a problem or situation, you mention whether or not they are successful in achieving the result they want. 應付","examples":["I think I would handle a meeting with Mr. Siegel very badly. 我覺得我可能應付不了與西格爾先生的會談。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>handle</b> a particular area of work, you have responsibility for it. 負責","examples":["She handled travel arrangements for the press corps during the presidential campaign. 她負責安排新聞報道團在總統競選期間的出行事宜。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you <b>handle</b> something, you hold it or move it with your hands. 拿; 用手移動","examples":["Wear rubber gloves when handling cat litter. 撿拾貓糞時要帶橡皮手套。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>fly off the handle</b>, you suddenly and completely lose your temper. 突然大發脾氣","examples":["He flew off the handle at the slightest thing. 他為一點小事就突然大發雷霆。"]}]}]},"headquarter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（非正式，主要用於美國英語）將（組織的）總部設在某地；設立總部"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to place in or establish as headquarters 設立總部","examples":[]}]}]},"handshake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"握手；（計算機/通訊/電子）訊號交換，交握"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you give someone a <b>handshake</b>, you take their right hand with your own right hand and hold it firmly or move it up and down, as a sign of greeting or to show that you have agreed about something such as a business deal. 握手","examples":["He has a strong handshake. 他有力地握了一下手。"]}]}]},"hazardous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"危險的，有害的；碰運氣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>hazardous</b> is dangerous, especially to people's health or safety. 有危害的","examples":["They have no way to dispose of the hazardous waste they produce. 他們沒法處理那些由他們製造出來的危害性廢棄物。"]}]}]},"hidden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"隱形的，隱秘的；不易察覺的，潛在的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"隱藏；躲避；遮擋（hide 的過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hidden</b> is the past participle of . (hide)的過去分詞","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Hidden</b> facts, feelings, activities, or problems are not easy to notice or discover. 隱藏的","examples":["Under all the innocent fun, there are hidden dangers, especially for children. 在所有無害的娛樂節目背後都有隱患，對兒童來說尤其如此。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>hidden</b> place is difficult to find. 隱秘的","examples":["As you descend, suddenly you see at last the hidden waterfall. 你往下走，最終會突然發現那個隱秘的瀑布。"]}]}]},"hilarious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"很可笑的，很滑稽的；<古>歡鬧的，興高采烈的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>hilarious</b>, it is extremely funny and makes you laugh a lot. 令人捧腹大笑的","examples":["We thought it was hilarious when we first heard about it. 我們第一次聽說這件事的時候覺得它很可笑。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"令人大笑地","examples":["She found it hilariously funny. 她覺得這事兒滑稽極了。"]}]}]},"hinder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"阻礙，妨礙"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（尤指身體部位）後面的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>hinders</b> you, it makes it more difficult for you to do something or make progress. 阻礙","examples":["Further investigation was hindered by the loss of all documentation on the case. 由於有關此案的材料全部丟失，進一步的調查受到了阻礙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>hinders</b> your movement, it makes it difficult for you to move forward or move around. 牽制","examples":["A thigh injury increasingly hindered her mobility. 大腿上的傷愈發束縛了她的活動自由。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"situated at or further towards the back or rear; posterior 後面的; 後方的","examples":[]}]}]},"human resource":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"人力資源，勞動力（常作複數 human resources）：被視為一種可被僱用並對公司、組織等有用的資產；人力資源部門，人事部。"}],"sections":[]},"hub":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（活動的）中心；樞紐機場，樞紐城市；（輪）轂，（推進器、風扇等的）旋翼葉轂；（網路）集線器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can describe a place as a <b>hub</b> <b>of</b> an activity when it is a very important centre for that activity. 活動中心","examples":["The island's social hub is the Cafe Sport. 該島的社交中心是“運動咖啡館”。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>hub</b> of a wheel is the part at the centre. 輪轂","examples":[]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>hub</b> or a <b>hub airport</b> is a large airport from which you can travel to many other airports. 樞紐機場","examples":["...a campaign to secure Heathrow's place as Europe's main international hub. …一場確保希思羅機場成為歐洲主要國際樞紐機場的運動。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>hub</b> is a device for connecting computers in a network. 集線器","examples":[]}]}]},"humane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"人道的，仁慈的；（學科分支）人文的，高尚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Humane</b> people act in a kind, sympathetic way toward other people and animals, and try to do them as little harm as possible. 人道的","examples":["In the mid-nineteenth century, Dorothea Dix began to campaign for humane treatment of the mentally ill. 在19世紀中葉，多羅西婭·迪克斯發起了為精神病患者爭取人道待遇的運動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Humane</b> values and societies encourage people to act in a kind and sympathetic way toward others, even toward people they do not agree with or like. 仁愛的","examples":["...the humane values of socialism. … 社會主義的博愛價值觀。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"人道地","examples":["Suffering animals should be humanely euthanized on the farm. 農場上的病畜應該被人道地施與安樂死。"]}]}]},"hopeless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無望的；（感到）絕望的；極差的，糟糕透頂的；徹頭徹尾的；無能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you feel <b>hopeless</b>, you feel very unhappy because there seems to be no possibility of a better situation or success. 絕望的","examples":["He had not heard her cry before in this uncontrolled, hopeless way. 之前他從沒有聽過她這樣失態、絕望地哭泣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>hopeless</b> is certain to fail or be unsuccessful. 註定失敗的","examples":["I don't believe your situation is as hopeless as you think. If you love each other, you'll work it out. 我不相信你的情形像你想的那樣無望。如果你們相愛，你們會找到解決辦法的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone is <b>hopeless</b> <b>at</b> something, they are very bad at it. 不能勝任的","examples":["I'd be hopeless at working for somebody else. 我無法勝任為別人工作。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>hopeless</b> to emphasize how bad or inadequate something or someone is. 糟糕透頂的","examples":["Argentina's economic policies were a hopeless mess. 阿根廷的經濟政策混亂得一塌糊塗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"絕望地","examples":["I looked around hopelessly. 我絕望地四下看著。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"糟糕透頂地","examples":["Harry was hopelessly lost. 哈里徹底迷路了。"]}]}]},"ice-cold":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"冰冷的；冷漠的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>ice-cold</b>, you are emphasizing that it is very cold. 冰冷的; 凜冽的","examples":["...delicious ice-cold beer. ...冰冷可口的啤酒。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>ice-cold</b>, you are emphasizing that they do not allow their emotions to affect them or that they lack feeling and friendliness. (人)冷酷無情的; 冷若冰霜的","examples":["...the gunman's ice-cold stare. ...該槍手冷酷無情的注視。"]}]}]},"idealize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把…理想化，使理想化，理想化地描述（視為或表現得比實際更完美）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"理想化，形成理想"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>idealize</b> something or someone, you think of them, or represent them to other people, as being perfect or much better than they really are. 把…理想化","examples":["People idealize the past. 人們總是把過去理想化。"]}]}]},"icon":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"圖示；偶像，代表；畫像，雕像；聖像（如基督、聖母瑪利亞等）；類象符號"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as an <b>icon</b>, you mean that they are important as a symbol of a particular thing. 象徵物; 偶像","examples":["...only Marilyn has proved as enduring a fashion icon. …只有瑪麗蓮被證明是經久不衰的時尚偶像。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>icon</b> is a picture of Christ, his mother, or a saint painted on a wooden panel. (耶穌基督、聖母瑪利亞等聖人的) 木製聖像","examples":["...a painter of religious icons. …一位宗教聖像畫家。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>icon</b> is a picture on a computer screen representing a particular computer function. If you want to use it, you move the cursor onto the icon using a mouse. (電腦螢幕上可用滑鼠點選的) 圖示","examples":["Kate clicked on the mail icon on her computer screen. 凱特點選了她電腦螢幕上的郵件圖示。"]}]}]},"idolize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"把……當偶像崇拜，極端崇拜"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"崇拜偶像"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>idolize</b> someone, you admire them very much. 崇拜","examples":["Naomi idolized her father as she was growing up. 在成長過程中，娜奧米很崇拜她父親。"]}]}]},"ignite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"點燃，燃燒；引發，激起"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you <b>ignite</b> something or when it <b>ignites</b>, it starts burning or explodes. 點燃; 著火","examples":["The bombs ignited a fire which destroyed some 60 houses. 炸彈引起了一場火災，燒燬了大約六十間房屋。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something or someone <b>ignites</b> your feelings, they cause you to have very strong feelings about something. 激起","examples":["There was one teacher who really ignited my interest in words. 曾經有一位老師真正激起了我對文字的興趣。"]}]}]},"ill-advised":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不明智的，失策的，欠考慮的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something that someone does as <b>ill-advised</b>, you mean that it is not sensible or wise. 不明智的; 考慮不周的","examples":["They would be ill-advised to do this. 他們這麼做是不明智的。"]}]}]},"ignition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"著火，點燃；點火裝置，點火開關"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a car engine, the <b>ignition</b> is the part where the fuel is ignited. (汽車發動機中的) 點火裝置","examples":["The device automatically disconnects the ignition. 那個裝置自動斷開了點火器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Inside a car, <b>the ignition</b> is the part where you turn the key so that the engine starts. (汽車裡的) 點火開關","examples":["Abruptly he turned the ignition key and started the engine. 他突然轉動了點火開關的鑰匙，發動了引擎。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Ignition</b> is the process of something starting to burn. 起火","examples":["The ignition of methane gas killed eight men. 甲烷起火造成8人死亡。"]}]}]},"illegal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非法的，違法的；違規的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"非法移民，非法勞工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>illegal</b>, the law says that it is not allowed. 非法的","examples":["It is illegal to intercept radio messages. 竊聽無線電資訊是違法的。","...illegal drugs. …非法毒品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Illegal</b> immigrants or workers have travelled into a country or are working without official permission. (移民) 非法入境的; (工人) 非法務工的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非法地","examples":["He was convicted of illegally using a handgun. 他被判非法使用手槍。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Illegal immigrants or workers are sometimes referred to as <b>illegals</b>. 非法移民; 非法勞工","examples":["...a clothing factory where many other illegals also worked. …一家允許很多其他非法勞工工作的服裝廠。"]}]}]},"illicit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非法的，社會不容許的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>illicit</b> activity or substance is not allowed by law or the social customs of a country. 違法的; 不正當的","examples":["Dante clearly condemns illicit love. 但丁明確地譴責不正當的戀情。"]}]}]},"immature":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"發育未全的；（人）幼稚的，不成熟的；粗糙的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>immature</b> is not yet completely grown or fully developed. 未發育完全的; 不成熟的","examples":["She is emotionally immature. 她在情感上不成熟。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>immature</b>, you are being critical of them because they do not behave in a sensible or responsible way. 冒失的","examples":["She's just being childish and immature. 她真是小孩子氣，太冒失了。"]}]}]},"illogical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不合邏輯的；不合常理的，不合理的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an action, feeling, or belief as <b>illogical</b>, you are critical of it because you think that it does not result from a logical and ordered way of thinking. 沒有道理的; 不合邏輯的","examples":["It was absurd and illogical to go out into such a storm. 在這樣的暴風雨中外出簡直是荒唐和莫名其妙。"]}]}]},"illness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疾病；（某種）病，患病期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Illness</b> is the fact or experience of being ill. 生病","examples":["If your child shows any signs of illness, take her to the doctor. 如果您的孩子出現任何生病的症兆，帶她去看醫生。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>illness</b> is a particular disease such as measles or pneumonia. 疾病","examples":["She returned to her family home to recover from an illness. 她回到自己家裡養病。"]}]}]},"immobile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不動的，靜止的；固定的，不能移動的，無法活動的；穩定的，不變的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>immobile</b> is completely still. 固定的; 一動不動的","examples":["Joe remained immobile, as if he had been carved out of stone. 喬一動不動，彷彿一座石頭雕像一樣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>immobile</b> is unable to move or unable to be moved. 癱瘓的; 無法移動的","examples":["A riding accident left him immobile. 一次騎術事故使他癱瘓。"]}]}]},"illiteracy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"文盲；無知；表達錯誤"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Illiteracy</b> is the state of not knowing how to read or write. 文盲","examples":[]}]}]},"immediately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"立即，馬上；緊接地，緊靠地；直接地"},{"pos":"conj.","zh":"<英>一……就"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens <b>immediately</b>, it happens without any delay. 立即地","examples":["He immediately flung himself to the floor. 他立即撲倒在地。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>immediately</b> obvious, it can be seen or understood without any delay. 即刻地","examples":["The cause of the accident was not immediately apparent. 這次事故的起因並非即刻可明。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Immediately</b> is used to indicate that someone or something is closely and directly involved in a situation. 直接地","examples":["The man immediately responsible for this misery is the province's governor. 對這次慘劇負直接責任的人是該省省長。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Immediately</b> is used to emphasize that something comes next, or is next to something else. 緊接地","examples":["They wish to begin immediately after dinner. 他們希望晚飯後緊接著開始。"]}]}]},"impair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"損害，削弱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>impairs</b> something such as an ability or the way something works, it damages it or makes it worse. 損害","examples":["Consumption of alcohol impairs your ability to drive a car or operate machinery. 飲酒會削弱你駕駛汽車或操縱機器的能力。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"受損的","examples":["The blast left him with permanently impaired hearing. 爆炸造成了他永久性聽力損傷。"]}]}]},"impartial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公正的，不偏不倚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>impartial</b> is not directly involved in a particular situation, and is therefore able to give a fair opinion or decision about it. 公正的","examples":["Career counsellors offer impartial advice, guidance and information to all pupils. 就業指導員們向所有的學生提供無偏見的建議、指導和資訊。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"公正","examples":["...a justice system lacking impartiality by democratic standards. …以民主標準而言缺乏公正性的司法體系。"]}]}]},"impeccable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無瑕疵的，沒有缺點的；<罕>（神學）不會犯罪過的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something such as someone's behaviour or appearance as <b>impeccable</b>, you are emphasizing that it is perfect and has no faults. 無可挑剔的","examples":["She had impeccable taste in clothes. 她對服裝有著無可挑剔的品味。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"無可挑剔地","examples":["He was charming, considerate and impeccably mannered. 他富有魅力，待人體貼，舉止無可挑剔。"]}]}]},"impatient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不耐煩的，沒有耐心的；迫不及待的，急切的；（對不愉快的事）不能容忍，不願接受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>impatient</b>, you are annoyed because you have to wait too long for something. 不耐煩的","examples":["Investors are growing impatient with promises of improved earnings. 投資者們對提高收益的承諾越來越不耐煩了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>impatient</b>, you are easily irritated by things. 無耐心的","examples":["Beware of being too impatient with others. 注意不要對別人太沒有耐心。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>impatient</b> <b>to</b> do something or <b>impatient for</b> something to happen, you are eager to do it or for it to happen and do not want to wait. 焦急的","examples":["He didn't want to tell Mr. Morrisson why he was impatient to get home. 他不想告訴莫里森先生他為什麼要著急回家。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不耐煩地","examples":["People have been waiting impatiently for a chance to improve the situation. 人們一直在不耐地等待著改善這一狀況的機會。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"無耐心地","examples":["\"Come on, David,\" Harry said impatiently. “戴維，快點兒！” 哈里不耐煩地說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"焦急","examples":["She showed impatience to continue the climb. 她表現出要繼續往上爬的急切。"]}]}]},"impede":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"妨礙，阻礙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>impede</b> someone or something, you make their movement, development, or progress difficult. 阻礙","examples":["Debris and fallen rock are impeding the progress of the rescue workers. 瓦礫和落下的岩石正阻礙著救援人員的程序。"]}]}]},"implementation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"實施，執行"}],"sections":[]},"impolite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不禮貌的，粗魯的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>impolite</b>, you mean that they are rather rude and do not have good manners. 不禮貌的","examples":["The Count acknowledged the two newcomers as briefly as was possible without being impolite. 伯爵儘可能簡短而又不失禮節地向兩位新來者打招呼。"]}]}]},"improper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不正確的，錯誤的；不適當的；不合禮儀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Improper</b> activities are illegal or dishonest. 不合法的; 不誠實的","examples":["25 officers were investigated following allegations of improper conduct. 25名警官被指控行為不當而受到調查。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Improper</b> conditions or methods of treatment are not suitable or good enough for a particular purpose. 不適當的","examples":["The improper use of medicine could lead to severe adverse reactions. 用藥不當會引起嚴重的不良反應。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour as <b>improper</b>, you mean it is rude or shocking or in some way socially unacceptable. 不得體的","examples":["Such improper behaviour and language from a young lady left me momentarily incapable of speech. 如此不得體的言行竟來自一位年輕女士，這讓我驚愕得一時無語。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不合法地; 不誠實地","examples":["I acted neither fraudulently nor improperly. 我既未欺詐又未犯法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不適當地","examples":["The study confirmed many reports that doctors were improperly trained. 該研究證實了許多關於醫生培訓不足的報導。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"不得體地","examples":["The company turns down people who show up at job interviews improperly dressed. 該公司拒絕那些在面試時衣著不得體的人。"]}]}]},"impossible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不可能的，辦不到的；（境況）極其艱難的；（人）難以對付的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"不可能的事（the impossible）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>impossible</b> cannot be done or cannot happen. 不可能的","examples":["It was impossible for anyone to get in because no one knew the password. 任何人都不可能進得去，因為沒人知道口令。","He thinks the tax is impossible to administer. 他認為治稅是不可能的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>impossible</b> situation or an <b>impossible</b> position is one that is very difficult to deal with. 極難應付的","examples":["I think he was in an impossible position. 我想他當時處於一個極難應付的境地。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>impossible</b>, you are annoyed that their bad behaviour or strong views make them difficult to deal with. 難以忍受的","examples":["The woman is impossible, thought Francesca. 弗朗西絲卡暗自思忖，這個女人真讓人受不了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The impossible</b> is something that is impossible. 不可能的事","examples":["They were expected to do the impossible. 他們被要求去做不可能的事。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不可能地","examples":["Mathematical physics is an almost impossibly difficult subject. 數學物理學是一門難得難以想像的學科。"]}]}]},"inability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"無能，無力，不能"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to someone's <b>inability</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are referring to the fact that they are unable to do it. 無力","examples":["Her inability to concentrate could cause an accident. 她無法集中注意力可能會導致意外。"]}]}]},"inaccurate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不精確的，不準確的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a statement or measurement is <b>inaccurate</b>, it is not accurate or correct. 不準確的","examples":["The book is both inaccurate and exaggerated. 那本書既不準確又誇大事實。"]}]}]},"inactive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不活動的，不活躍的；未使用的，不運轉的；不參加的；無化學活性的，惰性的；（疾病）不顯症狀的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>inactive</b> is not doing anything or is not working. 不作為的; 不起作用的","examples":["He certainly was not politically inactive. 他在政治上當然不是無所作為。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不作為; 不起作用","examples":["The players have comparatively long periods of inactivity. 這些運動員有相當長的一段時間會無所事事。"]}]}]},"inadequate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不充分的，不足的，不夠好的；不能勝任的，信心不足的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>inadequate</b>, there is not enough of it or it is not good enough. 不足的; 不夠好的","examples":["Supplies of food and medicines are inadequate. 食品和藥物的供應是不足的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone feels <b>inadequate</b>, they feel that they do not have the qualities and abilities necessary to do something or to cope with life in general. 能力不足的","examples":["I still feel inadequate, useless and mixed up. 我仍舊感到能力不足，毫無用處，混淆不清。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不足地; 不夠好地","examples":["The projects were inadequately funded. 這些專案資助不足。"]}]}]},"inc":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"股份有限公司（incorporated 的縮寫）；包括，含（including 的縮寫）"}],"sections":[]},"impractical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不明智的，不切實際的；（人）無動手能力的，手不靈巧的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe an object, idea, or course of action as <b>impractical</b>, you mean that it is not sensible or realistic, and does not work well in practice. 不切實際的","examples":["Once there were regularly scheduled airlines, it became impractical to make a business trip by ocean liner. 一旦有了定期的飛機航班，乘坐遠洋客輪出差就變得不切實際了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>impractical</b>, you mean that they do not have the abilities or skills to do practical work such as making, repairing, or organizing things. 缺乏實際能力的","examples":["Geniuses are supposed to be difficult, eccentric and hopelessly impractical. 天才被認為很難相處、行為怪僻且毫無實際能力。"]}]}]},"inbound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（多作定語）入境的；到達的；入站的；歸本國的；回內地的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（多用於通訊、資訊科技、物流等）入站；呼入；流入"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inbound</b> flight is one that is arriving from another place. 歸航的; 到達的; 入站的","examples":["...a special inbound flight from Honduras. ...一架從宏都拉斯歸航的專機。"]}]}]},"incinerate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……燒成灰燼，焚燬"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When authorities <b>incinerate</b> rubbish or waste material, they burn it completely in a special container. 把…燒成灰燼","examples":["They were incinerating hazardous waste without a licence. 他們沒有許可就把危險廢棄物燒成灰燼。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"焚燒","examples":["South Pacific nations have protested against the incineration of the weapons. 南太平洋各國抗議武器的焚燒。"]}]}]},"incinerator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"焚化爐，焚燒爐，焚燒裝置（尤指焚燒垃圾、廢物等的高溫裝置）；焚屍爐，火葬爐"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>incinerator</b> is a special large container for burning waste at a very high temperature. 垃圾焚化爐","examples":[]}]}]},"incoherent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"語無倫次的，不連貫的，不合邏輯的；（物理學）非相干的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>incoherent</b>, they are talking in a confused and unclear way. 語無倫次的","examples":["The man was almost incoherent with fear. 那人幾乎害怕得說話語無倫次。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something such as a policy is <b>incoherent</b>, you are criticizing it because the different parts of it do not fit together properly. 不連貫的","examples":["...an incoherent set of objectives. …一組前後不連貫的的目標。"]}]}]},"incoming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"進來的，到來的，收到的；即將就任的，新任的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"進入；到來；常作 incomings 收入，收益"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>incoming</b> message or phone call is one that you receive. (簡訊、郵件等) 進來的","examples":["We keep a tape of incoming calls. 我們保留打進電話的錄音磁帶。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>incoming</b> plane or passenger is one that is arriving at a place. (飛機、旅客等) 正到達的","examples":["The airport was closed for incoming flights. 機場為正到達的飛機而關閉。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>incoming</b> official or government is one that has just been appointed or elected. 新任的","examples":["...the problems confronting the incoming government. …新一屆政府面臨的難題。"]}]}]},"inclination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傾向，意願；趨向，趨勢；斜坡，斜度；輕微向下的動作；軌道交角"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inclination</b> is a feeling that makes you want to act in a particular way. 意向","examples":["He had neither the time nor the inclination to think of other things. 他既沒時間也無意考慮其他事宜。","She showed no inclination to go. 她沒有表現出要走的意向。"]}]}]},"inconsistent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不一致的，不協調的，前後矛盾的；不符合（某套標準、思想等）；（行為、工作等）時好時壞的，變化無常的；（人）反覆無常的，易變的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>inconsistent</b>, you are criticizing them for not behaving in the same way every time a similar situation occurs. 反覆無常的","examples":["You are inconsistent and unpredictable. 你反覆無常，讓人捉摸不透。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>inconsistent</b> does not stay the same, being sometimes good and sometimes bad. 不穩定的; 時好時壞的","examples":["We had a terrific start to the season, but recently we've been inconsistent. 我們在本賽季的開頭極好，但最近時好時壞。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If two statements are <b>inconsistent</b>, one cannot possibly be true if the other is true. 不一致的","examples":["The evidence given in court was inconsistent with what he had previously told them. 他在法庭上的證詞與他當初告訴他們的不一致。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If something is <b>inconsistent with</b> a set of ideas or values, it does not fit in well with them or match them. 與…不相合的","examples":["This legislation is inconsistent with what they call Free Trade. 這項法規與他們所稱的自由貿易是相矛盾的。"]}]}]},"incomplete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不完整的，不完全的；不完善的，未完成的；（向前）傳球不成功的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<美>（學業成績評分）未修畢，未完成"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>incomplete</b> is not yet finished, or does not have all the parts or details that it needs. 沒完成的; 不完全的","examples":["The clearing of rubbish and drains is still incomplete. 垃圾和汙水的清理工作還沒有完成。"]}]}]},"incompetent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無能力的，不稱職的；<法律>無資格的；（醫）（尤指瓣膜或括約肌）無機能的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"無能力者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>incompetent</b>, you are criticizing them because they are unable to do their job or a task properly. 無能的; 不稱職的","examples":["He wants the power to fire incompetent employees. 他希望有權解僱不稱職的僱員。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>incompetent</b> is someone who is incompetent. 無能的人; 不稱職者","examples":["The president turned furiously on his staff. \"I'm surrounded by incompetents!\" 董事長憤怒地指責其職員，“我身邊全是些沒用的人！”"]}]}]},"inconvenient":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不便的，不方便的，打擾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>inconvenient</b> causes problems or difficulties for someone. 不方便的","examples":["Can you come at 10:30? I know it's inconvenient, but I have to see you. 你能10:30來嗎？我知道這不方便，但是我必須要見你。"]}]}]},"inconvenience":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不便，麻煩；帶來不便者，麻煩的人（或事物）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"麻煩，打擾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something causes <b>inconvenience</b>, they cause problems or difficulties. 不方便","examples":["We apologize for any inconvenience caused during the repairs. 我們對在修理過程中所造成的任何不便表示歉意。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>inconveniences</b> you, they cause problems or difficulties for you. 給…帶來不便","examples":["He promised to be quick so as not to inconvenience them any further. 他答應快一些，以免給他們帶來更多不便。"]}]}]},"incredibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不可信性，不能相信，難以置信；不可信的事物"}],"sections":[]},"incorporation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"合併；公司，團體組織"}],"sections":[]},"incorrect":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"錯誤的，不真實的；不適當的，不合禮節的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>incorrect</b> is wrong and untrue. 不正確的; 不真實的","examples":["He denied that his evidence about the telephone call was incorrect. 他否認他關於電話的證詞是不真實的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>incorrect</b> is not the thing that is required or is most suitable in a particular situation. 不適當的","examples":["...injuries caused by incorrect posture. …由不當姿勢造成的傷害。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不正確地","examples":["The magazine suggested, incorrectly, that he was planning to announce his retirement. 該雜誌錯誤地暗示說他正打算宣佈退休。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不適當地","examples":["He was told that the doors had been installed incorrectly. 他被告知房門安裝不當。"]}]}]},"incorporate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"包含，合併；組成公司；摻和，混合（成分）；使具體化，體現"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"合成一體的，合併的；具體化的；組成公司（或社團）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>incorporates</b> another thing, it includes the other thing. 包含","examples":["The new cars will incorporate a number of major improvements. 這種新型汽車將包含許多重大的改進。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something <b>is incorporated</b> <b>into</b> a large group, system, or area, they become a part of it. 使併入","examples":["The agreement would allow the rebels to be incorporated into a new national police force. 該協議將允許叛軍併入一支新的國家警察部隊。"]}]}]},"indecisive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（指人）猶豫不決的，優柔寡斷的；（指結果、比賽等）非決定性的，未分出勝負的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>indecisive</b>, you mean that they find it very difficult to make decisions. 優柔寡斷的","examples":["He was criticized as a weak and indecisive leader. 他被批評是位既懦弱又優柔寡斷的領導人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>indecisive</b> result in a contest or election is one that is not clear or definite. 非決定性的","examples":["The outcome of the battle was indecisive. 此役的結局是勝負不明的。"]}]}]},"in-depth":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"深入的，徹底的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>in-depth</b> analysis or study of something is a very detailed and complete study of it. 深入徹底的","examples":["...an in-depth look at censorship in the music business. ...對音樂產業中審查制度的一種深度觀察。"]}]}]},"incur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"帶來（成本、花費等）；招致，遭受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>incur</b> something unpleasant, it happens to you because of something you have done. 招致; 蒙受","examples":["The government had also incurred huge debts. 政府也已承受了大筆債務。"]}]}]},"incredible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不可思議的，難以置信的；驚人的，極大的，極多的；了不起的，極好的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something or someone as <b>incredible</b>, you like them very much or are impressed by them, because they are extremely or unusually good. 極好的","examples":["The wildflowers will be incredible after this rain. 這場雨過後，野花將開得非常好。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>incredible</b>, you mean that it is very unusual or surprising, and you cannot believe it is really true, although it may be. 難以置信的","examples":["It seemed incredible that people would still want to play football during a war. 在戰爭期間人們仍然想踢足球，這似乎不可思議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>incredible</b> to emphasize the degree, amount, or intensity of something. 非常的","examples":["I work an incredible amount of hours. 我工作的時間極長。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"極好地","examples":["Their father was incredibly good-looking. 他們的父親十分英俊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"難以置信地","examples":["Incredibly, some people don't like the name. 令人難以置信的是，有些人不喜歡這個名字。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"非常地","examples":["It was incredibly hard work. 那是個非常艱辛的工作。"]}]}]},"indefinite":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無限期的，期限不定的；模糊不清的，不明確的；（詞，屈折變化，短語）不定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation or period as <b>indefinite</b>, you mean that people have not decided when it will end. 不確定的","examples":["The trial was adjourned for an indefinite period. 審判被無限期推遲。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>indefinite</b> is not exact or clear. 不明確的","examples":["...at some indefinite time in the future. …在未來不確定的某個時間。"]}]}]},"indebt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使負債；使受恩惠，使感激"}],"sections":[]},"inevitably":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不可避免地，必然地；意料之中"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something will <b>inevitably</b> happen, it is certain to happen and cannot be prevented or avoided. 必然發生地","examples":["Technological changes will inevitably lead to unemployment. 技術變革將必然導致失業。"]}]}]},"infancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"幼年，嬰兒期；初期，搖籃期；<法律>未成年"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Infancy</b> is the period of your life when you are a very young child. 嬰兒期","examples":["...the development of the mind from infancy onwards. …從嬰兒期開始的智力開發。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>in its</b> <b>infancy</b>, it is new and has not developed very much. 初期","examples":["Computing science was still in its infancy. 電腦科學仍然處於初期階段。"]}]}]},"infamous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"聲名狼藉的，臭名昭著的；邪惡的，無恥的，不名譽的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Infamous</b> people or things are well-known because of something bad. 聲名狼藉的","examples":["He was infamous for his anti-feminist attitudes. 他因為他的反女權主義姿態而臭名昭著。"]}]}]},"indicator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"標誌，跡象；方向燈，轉向指示燈；指示器，顯示器；指示劑；指示（物）種"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>indicator</b> is a measurement or value that gives you an idea of what something is like. 指示物","examples":["...vital economic indicators, such as inflation, growth and the trade gap. …重要的經濟指標，如通貨膨脹，經濟增長以及貿易差額。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A car's <b>indicators</b> are the flashing lights that tell you when it is going to turn left or right. (車輛上的) 轉向指示燈","examples":["He flipped his indicator, and took a left. 他開啟汽車方向燈，向左轉了彎。"]}]}]},"infinity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（時、空、距離）無限，無窮；大量，大宗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Infinity</b> is a number that is larger than any other number and can never be given an exact value. 無窮大","examples":["These permutations multiply toward infinity. 這些排列向無窮大增加。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Infinity</b> is a point that is further away than any other point and can never be reached. 無限遠的點","examples":["...the darkness of a starless night stretching to infinity. …沒有星星的黑夜，向無垠延伸。"]}]}]},"influx":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人或物的）大量湧入，大量流入；（水）流入，注入（河，湖，海）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>influx</b> <b>of</b> people or things into a place is their arrival there in large numbers. (人或物的) 大量湧入","examples":["...problems caused by the influx of refugees. …難民大量湧入所造成的問題。"]}]}]},"info":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>資訊，情報，資料"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Info</b> is information. 資訊","examples":["For more info call 414-3935. 欲知詳情，請撥打電話414-3935。"]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an information provider 情報提供者","examples":[]}]}]},"infrastructure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"下面結構；永久性軍事設施；基礎設施，基礎建設"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>infrastructure</b> of a country, society, or organization consists of the basic facilities such as transportation, communications, power supplies, and buildings, which enable it to function. (國家、社會、組織賴以行使職能的) 基礎設施","examples":["...improvements in the country's infrastructure. …國家基礎設施的改善。"]}]}]},"informal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"輕鬆友好的，不拘禮節的；（文字或言談）非正式的，口語體的；（服裝）休閒的，家居的；（組織、團體和安排）非官方的，非正規的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Informal</b> speech or behaviour is relaxed and friendly rather than serious, very correct, or official. 非正式的 (言行)","examples":["She is refreshingly informal. 她隨和得令人耳目一新。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>informal</b> situation is one that is relaxed and friendly and not very serious or official. 輕鬆隨意的","examples":["The house has an informal atmosphere. 這屋子裡有一種輕鬆隨意的氣氛。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Informal</b> clothes are casual and suitable for wearing when you are relaxing, but not on formal occasions. (衣服) 休閒的","examples":["For lunch, dress is informal. 吃午餐可以穿著休閒裝。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>informal</b> to describe something that is done unofficially or casually without planning. 非正式的; 非正規的","examples":["The two leaders will retire to Camp David for informal discussions. 這兩位領導人將去戴維營進行非正式會談。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"非正式地 (言行)","examples":["She was always there at half past eight, chatting informally to the children. 她總是八點半鐘到那兒，與孩子們隨意交談。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"(穿著) 休閒地","examples":["Everyone dressed informally in shorts or faded jeans, and baggy sweatshirts. 大家都穿休閒裝，或短褲、或褪色牛仔褲、或寬鬆的運動衫。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"非正式地","examples":["He began informally to handle Ted's tax affairs for him. 他開始非正式地為特德管理他的稅務。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"輕鬆隨意","examples":["She enjoyed the relative informality of island life. 她喜歡相對輕鬆隨意的島嶼生活。"]}]}]},"initially":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"開始，最初"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Initially</b> means soon after the beginning of a process or situation, rather than in the middle or at the end of it. 最初","examples":["Forecasters say the storms may not be as bad as they initially predicted. 預報員們說暴風雨不像他們最初預報的那樣糟。"]}]}]},"injured":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"受傷的，有傷的；委屈的，受到傷害的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"傷者，傷員（the injured）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>injured</b> person or animal has physical damage to part of their body, usually as a result of an accident or fighting. 受傷的","examples":["The other injured man had a superficial stomach wound. 另一名受傷男子是腹部表層受傷。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have <b>injured</b> feelings, you feel upset because you believe someone has been unfair or unkind to you. (感情) 受傷害的","examples":["...a look of injured pride. …自尊心受傷的表情。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The injured</b> are people who are injured. 受傷者","examples":["Army helicopters tried to evacuate the injured. 軍用直升機設法撤出傷員。"]}]}]},"innovator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"創新者，革新者，改革者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>innovator</b> is someone who introduces changes and new ideas. 創新者; 革新者","examples":["He is an innovator in this field. 他是這個領域的革新者。"]}]}]},"innovate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"革新，創新"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>innovate</b> means to introduce changes and new ideas in the way something is done or made. 創新; 革新","examples":["What sets Rice apart from most engineers is his constant desire to innovate and experiment. 賴斯與大多數工程師不同之處在於他不斷地渴望創新和實驗。"]}]}]},"initiation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"入會，入會儀式；開始，創始；（某項活動或技能的）入門，初學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>initiation</b> of something is the starting of it. 開始; 發起","examples":["...the initiation of a rural development programme. …一項農村發展規劃的啟動"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>initiation</b> <b>into</b> a particular group is the act or process by which they officially become a member, often involving special ceremonies. 入會; 入會儀式","examples":["This was my initiation into the peace movement. 那是我加入和平運動的開始。"]}]}]},"inflict":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使遭受，使承受"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>inflict</b> harm or damage <b>on</b> someone or something means to make them suffer it. 使遭受 (傷害或破壞等)","examples":["...the damage being inflicted on industries by the recession. …經濟衰退給工業造成的損失。"]}]}]},"insane":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"瘋癲的，精神失常的；蠢極的，荒唐的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>insane</b> is severely mentally ill. 精神病的; 精神失常的","examples":["Some people simply can't take it and they just go insane. 一些人就是接受不了，於是便變得精神錯亂。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a decision or action as <b>insane</b>, you think it is very foolish or excessive. 瘋狂的; 愚蠢的","examples":["He asked me what I thought and I said, \"Listen, this is completely insane.\" 他問我是怎麼想的，我說，“聽著，這十分愚蠢。”"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"瘋狂地","examples":["I would be insanely jealous if Bill left me for another woman. 如果比爾為了另一個女人而離開我，我會妒忌得發瘋的。"]}]}]},"insanity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"精神錯亂，精神失常；愚蠢（或不理智）的事"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Insanity</b> is the state of being insane. 精神錯亂","examples":["...a psychiatrist who specialized in diagnosing insanity. …一位專門診斷精神錯亂的精神病學家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a decision or an action as <b>insanity</b>, you think it is very foolish. 荒唐的決定; 極端愚蠢的行為","examples":["...the final financial insanity of the 1980s. …20世紀80年代財政上最後的荒唐舉措。"]}]}]},"insecure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"缺乏信心的，無把握的；沒上鎖的，不牢靠的；（工作、投資等）無保障的，不安全的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>insecure</b>, you lack confidence because you think that you are not good enough or are not loved. 不自信的; 缺乏安全感的","examples":["Most mothers are insecure about their performance as mothers. 大多數母親對自己作為母親的表現缺乏自信。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Something that is <b>insecure</b> is not safe or protected. 不安全的; 無保障的","examples":["...low-paid, insecure jobs. …工資低、無保障的工作。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不自信; 缺乏安全感","examples":["She is always assailed by self-doubt and emotional insecurity. 她總是被自我懷疑和情感上的不安全感所困擾。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"不安全","examples":["...the increase in crime, which has created feelings of insecurity in the population. …犯罪的增加讓民眾感到不安全。"]}]}]},"instantaneously":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"立即，瞬間，即刻"}],"sections":[]},"insecurity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不安全，無把握"}],"sections":[]},"insider":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"內部的人，知情人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>insider</b> is someone who is involved in a situation and who knows more about it than other people. 知情者; 圈內人","examples":["An insider said, \"Katharine has told friends it is time to end her career.\" 一名知情者說，“凱瑟琳告訴朋友們她該結束自己的職業生涯了。”"]}]}]},"insignificant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"微不足道的，無足輕重的；（人）無權無勢的；無意義的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>insignificant</b> is unimportant, especially because it is very small. 不重要的; 無足輕重的","examples":["In 1949 Bonn was a small, insignificant city. 1949年，波恩還是個不足稱道的小城市。"]}]}]},"inspiring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鼓舞人心的，有激勵作用的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"激勵，鼓舞；賦予靈感，激發（想法）；使產生（感覺或情感）（inspire 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something or someone that is <b>inspiring</b> is exciting and makes you feel strongly interested and enthusiastic. 鼓舞人心的; 啟發靈感的","examples":["She was a very strong, impressive character and one of the most inspiring people I've ever met. 她性格堅強，令人欽佩，是我見過的最能鼓舞人心的人物之一。"]}]}]},"instrumental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有幫助的，起作用的；用樂器演奏的；與樂器有關的；與（事物）的工具效用有關的；與儀器或測量器具有關的；（語法）工具格的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"器樂曲（通常指非古典音樂）；工具格名詞，工具格"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone or something that is <b>instrumental</b> <b>in</b> a process or event helps to make it happen. 起作用的","examples":["In his first years as chairman he was instrumental in raising the company's wider profile. 在剛擔任董事長的頭幾年，他在提升公司形象方面發揮了作用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Instrumental</b> music is performed by instruments and not by voices. 用樂器演奏的","examples":["...a CD of vocal and instrumental music. …一張聲樂和器樂光碟。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Instrumentals</b> are pieces of instrumental music. 器樂曲","examples":["After a couple of brief instrumentals, he puts his guitar down. 演奏了幾首簡短的器樂曲之後，他放下了吉他。"]}]}]},"interchangeable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可互換的，可交換的，可交替的；（數學、邏輯）指論元或角色可以互換而不影響真值或有效性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Things that are <b>interchangeable</b> can be exchanged with each other without it making any difference. 可互換的","examples":["His greatest innovation was the use of interchangeable parts. 他最偉大的創新是使用了可互換部件。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可互換地","examples":["These expressions are often used interchangeably, but they do have different meanings. 這些表達法經常可以互換使用，但它們的確有不同的含義。"]}]}]},"intermittent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"間歇的，斷斷續續的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>intermittent</b> happens occasionally rather than continuously. 斷斷續續的","examples":["After three hours of intermittent rain, the game was abandoned. 雨斷斷續續地下了3個小時之後，比賽被取消了。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"斷斷續續地","examples":["The talks went on intermittently for three years. 會談斷斷續續地進行了3年。"]}]}]},"internationalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使國際化；置於國際管理下"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an issue or a crisis is <b>internationalized</b>, it becomes the concern of many nations throughout the world. 使···國際化","examples":["A danger exists of the conflict becoming internationalized. 存在著衝突變得國際化的危險。","They have been trying to internationalize the Kashmir problem. 他們已經試圖讓克什米爾問題國際化。"]}]}]},"interviewee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接受面試者，受接見者，被採訪者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interviewee</b> is a person who is being interviewed. 被面試者; 被採訪者; 被詢問者","examples":["Is there any interviewee who stands out as memorable? 參加面試的人中有沒有特別值得注意的？"]}]}]},"interviewer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"採訪者，面試官，接見者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>interviewer</b> is a person who is asking someone questions at an interview. 進行面試者; 採訪者; 詢問者","examples":["Being a good interviewer, however, requires much preparation and skill. 不過，好的採訪者需要許多準備和技巧。"]}]}]},"intricate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"錯綜複雜的；難理解的，難學會的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>intricate</b> to describe something that has many small parts or details. 複雜精細的","examples":["...the production of carpets with highly intricate patterns. …圖案複雜精細的地毯的製作。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"複雜精細地","examples":["...intricately carved sculptures. …一些精雕細刻的雕塑。"]}]}]},"introductory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"引導的，介紹的；入門的，初步的；（新產品）試銷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>introductory</b> remark, talk, or part of a book gives a small amount of general information about a particular subject, often before a more detailed explanation. 引言的","examples":["...an introductory course in religion and theology. …一門宗教和神學的入門課程。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>introductory</b> offer or price on a new product is something such as a free gift or a low price that is meant to attract new customers. 試銷的","examples":["...a special introductory offer. …一次特價試銷。"]}]}]},"inventive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有創造力的，善於創新的；發明的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>inventive</b> person is good at inventing things or has clever and original ideas. 有創造才能的","examples":["It inspired me to be more inventive with my own cooking. 它激勵我在自己烹飪時更具創造力。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"創造才能","examples":["He has surprised us before with his inventiveness. 他以前曾以創造才能令我們吃驚。"]}]}]},"investor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"投資者，投資機構"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>investor</b> is a person or organization that buys securities or property in order to receive a profit. 投資者","examples":["The main investor in the project is the French bank Credit National. 該專案的主要投資方是法國國民信貸銀行。"]}]}]},"invoice":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發票，賬單；貨物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"開發票給（某人）；（為提供的貨物或服務）開清單，開發票"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>invoice</b> is a document that lists goods that have been supplied or services that have been done, and says how much money you owe for them. 費用清單; 發票","examples":["We will then send you an invoice for the total course fees. 然後我們將寄給你一張全部課程費用的發票。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>invoice</b> someone, you send them a bill for goods or services you have provided them with. 給…開具發票","examples":["The agency invoices the client who then pays the full amount to the agency. 那個代銷處給客戶開具發票，然後客戶向代銷處支付全部的款項。"]}]}]},"invisible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"看不見的，隱形的；無形的，非貿易的；被忽視的，不為人注意的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"無形進出口"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>invisible</b>, you mean that it cannot be seen, for example, because it is transparent, hidden, or very small. 看不見的","examples":["The lines were so finely etched as to be invisible from a distance. 這些線條蝕刻得如此精細，離遠點都看不出來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>invisible</b> when you are talking about something that cannot be seen but has a definite effect. In this sense, <b>invisible</b> is often used before a noun that refers to something visible. 無形的","examples":["All the time you are in doubt about the cause of your illness, you are fighting against an invisible enemy. 一直以來你都在懷疑自己的病因，你是在和一個無形的敵人鬥爭。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that you feel <b>invisible</b>, you are complaining that you are being ignored by other people. If you say that a particular problem or situation is <b>invisible</b>, you are complaining that it is not being considered or dealt with. 被忽視的","examples":["It was strange, how invisible a clerk could feel. 很奇怪一名職員會感到如此地受人忽視。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"In stories, <b>invisible</b> people or things have a magic quality that makes people unable to see them. 隱身的","examples":["...The Invisible Man. …《隱身人》。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In economics, <b>invisible</b> earnings are the money that a country makes as a result of services such as banking and tourism, rather than by producing goods. 非貿易性的","examples":["The revenue from tourism is the biggest single item in the country's invisible earnings. 旅遊收入是該國非貿易性收益中最大的單項收入。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"看不見地","examples":["A thin coil of smoke rose almost invisibly into the sharp, bright sky. 一縷輕煙幾乎不見蹤跡地升上了耀眼的晴空。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"無形地","examples":["...the tradition that invisibly shapes things in the present. …這種無形地影響著現有事物的傳統。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被忽視","examples":["She takes up the issue of the invisibility of women and women's concerns in society. 她著手處理社會上對婦女及其所關注的事物的忽視問題。"]}]}]},"itemize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"逐條列記，逐項列出；（美國稅務）逐項申報扣除額（英式拼寫亦作 itemise）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>itemize</b> a number of things, you make a list of them. 逐條列記","examples":["The report will itemize the cost of various improvements. 報告將逐條列記各種改進工作所需的費用。"]}]}]},"irrelevant":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不相關的，不相干的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something such as a fact or remark as <b>irrelevant</b>, you mean that it is not connected with what you are discussing or dealing with. 不相關的","examples":["...irrelevant details. …一些不相關的細節。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>irrelevant</b>, you mean that it is not important in a situation. 不重要的","examples":["The choice of subject matter is irrelevant. 主題的選擇不重要。"]}]}]},"kickoff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（足球、美式橄欖球等）開球；開始，啟動，開場"}],"sections":[]},"judgmental":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（含貶義）好對人或事評頭論足的，動輒妄加評判的，吹毛求疵的；（較正式或專業）判斷的，基於判斷的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>judgmental</b>, you are critical of them because they form opinions of people and situations very quickly, when it would be better for them to wait until they know more about the person or situation. 妄下結論的","examples":["We tried not to seem critical or judgmental while giving advice that would protect him from ridicule. 在提出使他免受奚落的建議時，我們儘量不表現得挑剔或妄下結論。"]}]}]},"jobless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"失業的，無業的；（關於）失業者的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"失業者（常與 the 連用，總稱失業的人）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone who is <b>jobless</b> does not have a job, although they would like one. 失業的","examples":["He has turned his back on millions of jobless Americans. 他已經不管上百萬失業的美國人了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The jobless</b> are people who are jobless. 失業者","examples":["They joined the ranks of the jobless. 他們加入了失業大軍。"]}]}]},"junction":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公路或鐵路的）交叉口，岔道口；匯合處，交叉點；（電子）介面；連線，結合；（高速公路的）出入口；（鐵路的）樞紐站，聯軌站"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"n.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>junction</b> is a place where roads or railway lines join. (鐵路、公路的) 匯合點","examples":[]}]}]},"kidnapper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"綁匪，誘拐者，綁架者"}],"sections":[]},"keenly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"敏銳地；強烈地，深切地，熱切地；銳利地"}],"sections":[]},"itinerary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"行程，旅行路線；遊記，旅行日記"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"旅程的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>itinerary</b> is a plan of a trip, including the route and the places that you will visit. 旅行計劃","examples":["The next place on our itinerary was Sedona. 我們旅行計劃的下一站是塞多納。"]}]}]},"kindly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"親切地；溫和地；仁慈地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"親切的；和藹的；體貼的；爽快的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>kindly</b> person is kind, caring, and sympathetic. 仁慈的; 體貼的; 富於同情心的","examples":["He was a stern critic but an extremely kindly man. 他是一位嚴厲的批評家，卻是一個非常仁慈的人。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>kindly</b> does something for you, they act in a thoughtful and helpful way. 體貼地; 好意地","examples":["She kindly offered to go and fetch him some beer. 她體貼地主動去給他拿了些啤酒來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone asks you to <b>kindly</b> do something, they are asking you in a way which shows that they have authority over you, or that they are angry with you. (表命令或生氣的口氣) 煩請","examples":["Will you kindly obey the instructions I am about to give? 煩請您依照我要發出的指令去做好嗎？"]}]}]},"landscaper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"庭園設計家，園林設計師，景觀設計師"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a landscape gardener 庭園設計家","examples":[]}]}]},"kindness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"友好，仁慈，善良；善行，善舉"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Kindness</b> is the quality of being gentle, caring, and helpful. 和藹; 親切; 好意","examples":["We have been treated with such kindness by everybody. 我們受到了大家如此親切的對待。"]}]}]},"knowingly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"故意地；機警地，狡黠地，會意地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>knowingly</b> do something wrong, you do it even though you know it is wrong. 故意地","examples":["He repeated that he had never knowingly taken illegal drugs. 他反覆說自己從未故意吸毒。"]}]}]},"lacking":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"缺乏的，不足的（常與 in 連用）；缺失的，不存在的；有缺陷的，不充分的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"缺少，沒有，不足（lack 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something or someone <b>is lacking in</b> a particular quality, they do not have any of it or enough of it. 缺乏的; 沒有的","examples":["...if your hair is lacking in lustre and feeling dry. …如果你的頭髮缺乏光澤並且感覺乾燥。","She felt nervous, increasingly lacking in confidence about herself. 她感到緊張，對自己越來越缺乏信心。"]}]}]},"laid-back":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>悠閒的，隨和的，放鬆的（又作“懶散的”“閒散的”，但不指懶惰）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>laid-back</b>, you mean that they behave in a calm relaxed way as if nothing will ever worry them. 遇事泰然的","examples":["Everyone here has a really laid-back attitude. 這裡的每個人都很放鬆。"]}]}]},"landing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樓梯平臺；著陸，降落；（軍隊的）登陸；碼頭，卸貨處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a house or other building, the <b>landing</b> is the area at the top of the staircase which has rooms leading off it. 樓梯平臺","examples":["I ran out onto the landing. 我跑出去上了樓梯平臺。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>landing</b> is an act of bringing an aircraft or spacecraft down to the ground. 著陸","examples":["I had to make a controlled landing into the sea. 我不得不在海里進行有控制的降落。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When a <b>landing</b> takes place, troops are unloaded from boats or aircraft at the beginning of a military invasion or other operation. (部隊) 登陸","examples":["American forces have begun a big landing. 美軍已經開始大規模的登陸。"]}]}]},"languish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"長期受苦，受煎熬；衰敗，未能取得進展 ；變得衰弱；<古>思戀；<古>顯示出溫柔親切（或憂傷）的樣子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>languishes</b> somewhere, they are forced to remain and suffer in an unpleasant situation. 受折磨","examples":["Pollard continues to languish in prison. 波拉德繼續在牢裡受折磨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>languishes</b>, it is not successful, often because of a lack of effort or because of a lot of difficulties. (由於不努力或困難太多) 未成功","examples":["Without the founder's drive and direction, the company gradually languished. 由於沒有創始人的幹勁和指導，這家公司逐漸衰敗了。"]}]}]},"layoff":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"解僱，下崗；休養，停工期"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When there are <b>layoffs</b> in a company, people become unemployed because there is no more work for them in the company. 解僱","examples":["It will close more than 200 stores nationwide resulting in the layoffs of an estimated 2,000 employees. 在全國範圍內將關閉二百多家商店，造成約兩千人失業。"]}]}]},"large-scale":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"大規模的，大範圍的；大比例尺的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>large-scale</b> action or event happens over a very wide area or involves a lot of people or things. 大規模的","examples":["...a large scale military operation. …一次大規模的軍事行動。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>large-scale</b> map or diagram represents a small area of land or a building or machine on a scale that is large enough for small details to be shown. (地圖或圖表) 大比例尺的","examples":["...a large-scale map of the county. …一張該縣的大比例尺地圖。"]}]}]},"lasting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"持久的，耐久的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（紡）厚實斜紋織物"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"持續；繼續任職；存活（last 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>lasting</b> to describe a situation, result, or agreement that continues to exist or have an effect for a very long time. 持久的","examples":["We are well on our way to a lasting peace. 我們正邁向持久的和平。"]}]}]},"lavatory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"盥洗室，廁所；（洗手間內的）洗臉盆，洗手池"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lavatory</b> is a toilet or a room with a toilet in it. 廁所","examples":["...the ladies' lavatory. …女廁所。"]}]}]},"last-minute":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"最後一刻才完成（或決定、安排好等）的；緊急關頭的"}],"sections":[]},"lawsuit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"訴訟，訴訟案"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lawsuit</b> is a case in a court of law which concerns a dispute between two people or organizations. 訴訟案","examples":["The dispute culminated last week in a lawsuit against the government. 這場針對政府訴訟案的爭論在上星期達到了高潮。"]}]}]},"later":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"後來，隨後；<美，非正式>再見，回頭見"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"較晚的，以後的；較新式的，較現代的；晚期的，末期的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"","pos_name":"","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Later</b> is the comparative of . (late)的比較級","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>later</b> to refer to a time or situation that is after the one that you have been talking about or after the present one. 以後","examples":["He resigned ten years later. 他10年後辭職了。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>later on</b> to refer to a time or situation that is after the one that you have been talking about or after the present one. 以後","examples":["Later on I'll be speaking to Patty Davis. 以後我會和帕蒂·戴維斯談談。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>later</b> to refer to an event, period of time, or other thing which comes after the one that you have been talking about or after the present one. 後來的","examples":["At a later news conference, he said differences should not be dramatized. 在後來的新聞釋出會上，他說差異不應該被誇大。","The competition should have been re-scheduled for a later date. 本該把比賽重新安排在一個晚些的日期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>later</b> to refer to the last part of someone's life or career or the last part of a period of history. 晚年的; 後期的","examples":["He found happiness in later life. 他在晚年找到了幸福。","...the later part of the 20th century. …20世紀後期。"]}]}]},"lapse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"過失，小失誤；（一時的）行為失檢；（兩件事發生的）間隔時間；（活動的）暫停，中斷；開始說，開始做；（因未繼續繳費而導致的）終止，結束"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（時間）流逝；（合同、協議等）失效，期滿終止；（狀態，活動）中止，結束；背棄，放棄（宗教信仰）；開始（以某種方式）說話、行事（lapse into）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lapse</b> is a moment or instance of bad behaviour by someone who usually behaves well. (一時的) 行為失檢","examples":["On Friday he showed neither decency nor dignity. It was an uncommon lapse. 星期五他既不莊重也不體面。這可是他少有的失禮。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>lapse</b> <b>of</b> something such as concentration or judgment is a temporary lack of that thing, which can often cause you to make a mistake. (一時的) 走神; 判斷錯誤","examples":["I had a little lapse of concentration in the middle of the race. 我在比賽中走了一下神。","He was a genius and because of it you could accept lapses of taste. 他是一個天才，因此他偶失得體，人們也可以接受。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Lapse</b> is also a noun. 開始說; 開始做","examples":["Her lapse into German didn't seem peculiar. After all, it was her native tongue. 她開始說德語並不奇怪，畢竟那是她的母語。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A <b>lapse</b> <b>of</b> time is a period that is long enough for a situation to change or for people to have a different opinion about it. (時間的) 間隔","examples":["...the restoration of diplomatic relations after a lapse of 24 years. …間隔24年後外交關係的恢復。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lapse</b> <b>into</b> a quiet or inactive state, you stop talking or being active. 陷入 (某種靜止狀態)","examples":["She muttered something unintelligible and lapsed into silence. 她咕噥了幾句難以理解的話，然後就陷入了沉默。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>lapses</b> <b>into</b> a particular way of speaking, or behaving, they start speaking or behaving in that way, usually for a short period. 開始 (以某種方式) 說話; 開始行事","examples":["She lapsed into a little girl voice to deliver a nursery rhyme. 她用小女孩的聲音唱起了一首童謠。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a period of time <b>lapses</b>, it passes. 流逝","examples":["New products and production processes are transferred to the developing countries only after a substantial amount of time has lapsed. 只有經過很長時間以後，新產品和新生產流程才轉移到發展中國家。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a situation or legal contract <b>lapses</b>, it is allowed to end rather than being continued, renewed, or extended. 終止","examples":["The terms of the treaty lapsed in 1987. 協定的條款在1987年就終止了。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a member of a particular religion <b>lapses</b>, they stop believing in it or stop following its rules and practices. 放棄 (宗教信仰)","examples":["I lapsed in my 20s, returned to it, then lapsed again, while writing the life of historical Jesus. 我20來歲就放棄信教，後來又信了。到後來在寫歷史上的耶穌生平時又放棄了信教。"]}]}]},"leading":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要的，最重要的；在（比賽或行列中）首位的，居前的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"行距；領導；（用於屋頂的）鉛皮，鉛板"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"領導（lead 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>leading</b> person or thing in a particular area is the one which is most important or successful. 主要的","examples":["...a leading member of the city's Sikh community. …該市錫克教團體的一名主要成員。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>leading</b> role in a play or film is the main role. A <b>leading</b> lady or man is an actor who plays this role. 主要的 (角色); 擔任主要角色的","examples":["...an offer to play the leading role in an Arthur Miller play. …一個在亞瑟·米勒的劇目中出演主角的提議。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>leading</b> group, vehicle, or person in a race or procession is the one that is at the front. 在前面的","examples":["The leading car came to a halt. 行駛在前面的車停了下來。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"the spacing between lines of photocomposed or digitized type 行距 (Also called interlinear spacing)","examples":[]}]}]},"leaflet":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傳單，小冊子；小葉，初生葉（統稱）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"散發傳單（或小冊子）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>leaflet</b> is a little book or a piece of paper containing information about a particular subject. 傳單","examples":["Campaigners handed out leaflets on passive smoking. 發起人分發了關於被動吸菸的傳單。"]}]}]},"leakage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（機密或秘密的）洩露，透露；（液體或氣體的）滲漏，洩漏；（液體或氣體的）漏出量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>leakage</b> is an amount of liquid or gas that is escaping from a pipe or container by means of a crack, hole, or other fault. (液體或氣) 洩漏","examples":["A leakage of kerosene has polluted water supplies. 洩漏的煤油已汙染了水源。"]}]}]},"legalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使合法化，使得到法律認可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is legalized</b>, a law is passed that makes it legal. 使合法化","examples":["Divorce was legalized in 1981. 離婚在1981年被合法化了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"合法化","examples":["Legalization of drugs would drive the drug-dealing business off the streets. 毒品合法化會將毒品買賣從大街上清除。"]}]}]},"letterhead":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"信頭；印有信頭的信紙"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>letterhead</b> is the name and address of a person, company, or organization which is printed at the top of their writing paper. 信頭","examples":["Colleagues at work enjoy having a letterhead with their name at the top. 同事們喜歡有一個以其名字作為開端的信頭。"]}]}]},"liability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（法律上應承擔的）責任，義務；惹麻煩的人（或事）；負債，債務；傾向；可能性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>a</b> <b>liability</b>, you mean that they cause a lot of problems or embarrassment. 累贅","examples":["As the president's prestige continues to fall, they're clearly beginning to consider him a liability. 隨著總統的威信持續下降，他們顯然開始認為他是一個累贅。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A company's or organization's <b>liabilities</b> are the sums of money which it owes. 負債","examples":["The company had assets of $138 million and liabilities of $120.5 million. 該公司有1.38億美元資產和1.205億美元的負債。"]}]}]},"leverage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"影響力，手段；槓桿力，槓桿作用；<美>槓桿比率"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>舉債經營；充分利用（資源、觀點等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Leverage</b> is the ability to influence situations or people so that you can control what happens. 影響力","examples":["His position as mayor gives him leverage to get things done. 他的市長身份使他有能力辦成一些事情。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>leverage</b> a company or investment means to use borrowed money in order to buy it or pay for it. 舉債經營","examples":["He might feel that leveraging the company at a time when he sees tremendous growth opportunities would be a mistake. 他可能感覺到在看到巨大的發展機會時舉債經營公司是一個錯誤。"]}]}]},"lease":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"租約，租契"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"出租，租用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lease</b> is a legal agreement by which the owner of a building, a piece of land, or something such as a car allows someone else to use it for a period of time in return for money. 租約","examples":["He took up a 10-year lease on the house. 他為這房子簽了10年的租約。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>lease</b> property or something such as a car from someone or if they <b>lease</b> it <b>to</b> you, they allow you to use it in return for regular payments of money. 租進; 租出","examples":["He went to Toronto, where he leased an apartment. 他去了多倫多，在那裡租了一套公寓。","She hopes to lease the building to students. 她希望把大樓租給學生。"]}]}]},"locksmith":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"鎖匠，修鎖工"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>locksmith</b> is a person whose job is to make or repair locks. 鎖匠","examples":[]}]}]},"limited":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有限的；受限的；受憲法限制的；（公司）有限責任的 (=Ltd)"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"高階快車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"限制（limit 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>limited</b> is not very great in amount, range, or degree. 有限的","examples":["They may only have a limited amount of time to get their points across. 他們可能只有有限的時間來闡述清楚他們的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>limited</b> company is one whose owners are legally responsible for only a part of any money that it may owe if it goes bankrupt. 有限責任的 (公司)","examples":[]}]}]},"lucrative":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"獲利多的，賺大錢的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>lucrative</b> activity, job, or business deal is very profitable. 獲利豐厚的","examples":["Thousands of ex-army officers have found lucrative jobs in private security firms. 成千上萬的退役軍官在私人保安公司找到了薪水豐厚的工作。"]}]}]},"logistics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"後勤，組織工作；物流"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>logistics</b> of doing something complicated that involves a lot of people or equipment, you are referring to the skilful organization of it so that it can be done successfully and efficiently. 後勤","examples":["The skills and logistics of getting such a big show on the road pose enormous practical problems. 這樣的一個大型節目進行巡演在技術和後勤方面都會面臨大量實際問題。"]}]}]},"loom":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（尤指陰森森地）隱約出現，赫然聳現；逼近，臨近"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"織布機；（尤指海上物體在黑暗或濃霧中的）隱隱顯現；（雲或霾等將不能直接見到的光折射出來的）暗影，上現蜃景"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>looms</b> <b>over</b> you, it appears as a large or unclear shape, often in a frightening way. (常以可怕的方式) 赫然出現; 隱約顯現","examples":["Vincent loomed over me, as pale and grey as a tombstone. 文森特赫然出現在我面前，臉色蒼白陰沉得像塊墓碑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a worrying or threatening situation or event <b>is looming</b>, it seems likely to happen soon. (令人擔憂的或危險的情形或事件) 可能發生; 逐漸逼近","examples":["Another government spending crisis is looming in the United States. 又一次政府開支危機正在美國醞釀。","The threat of renewed civil war looms ahead. 新一輪內戰的威脅在逼近。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>loom</b> is a machine that is used for weaving thread into cloth. 織布機","examples":[]}]}]},"madness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"瘋狂，精神錯亂；愚蠢的行為；狂熱"}],"sections":[]},"mailing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵寄，郵遞；郵件（尤指一次批次寄發的）；<蘇格蘭>農場租金"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（作定語）郵寄的，郵遞的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"郵寄，寄出（mail 的現在分詞或動名詞）；給……披上鎧甲，給……裝甲（mail 的現在分詞或動名詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mailing</b> is the activity of sending things to people through the postal service. 郵寄","examples":["The newsletter was printed toward the end of June and ready for mailing July 1. 該簡訊接近6月底時印了出來，7月1日可以郵遞。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mailing</b> is something that is sent to people through the postal service. 郵件","examples":["Most of Mahony's expenses were for mass mailings to conservatives across the state. 馬奧尼的大部分花銷都用於給全州的保守派寄送批次郵件。"]}]}]},"mainframe":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）大型機，大型計算機，主機"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mainframe</b> or <b>mainframe computer</b> is a large, powerful computer which can be used by many people at the same time and which can do very large or complicated tasks. 主機 (指可同時供多人使用的大型計算機)","examples":["I downloaded the whole thing into the hospital mainframe before I left work today. 我今天下班前把全部內容下載到了醫院的主機上。"]}]}]},"managerial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"經營上的，管理上的；經理的，管理人的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Managerial</b> means relating to the work of a manager. 經理的; 管理上的","examples":["...his managerial skills. …他的管理技能。","...a managerial career. …管理生涯。"]}]}]},"lifestyle":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"生活方式"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"生活方式類的，時尚生活的（常用於名詞前，修飾雜誌、電視節目、產品等）；保健的（指旨在提高生活質量而非治療特定疾病的藥物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>lifestyle</b> of a particular person or group of people is the living conditions, behaviour, and habits that are typical of them or are chosen by them. 生活方式","examples":["They enjoyed an income and lifestyle that many people would envy. 他們享有很多人會羨慕的收入和生活方式。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Lifestyle</b> magazines, television programmes, and products are aimed at people who wish to be associated with glamorous and successful lifestyles. 關於時尚生活的 (雜誌、電視節目、產品等)","examples":["This year people are going for luxury and buying lifestyle products. 今年人們在追求奢侈品，購買時尚生活產品。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Lifestyle</b> drugs are drugs that are intended to improve people's quality of life rather than to treat particular medical disorders. 保健的","examples":["\"I see anti-depressants as a lifestyle drug,\" says Dr. Charlton. “我把抗抑鬱藥視為一種保健藥物，”查爾頓醫生說道。"]}]}]},"located":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"位於，坐落在"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"確定……的位置，探明；設立，建立；遷居，開辦公司（locate 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>located</b> in a particular place, it is present or has been built there. 位於…的","examples":["A boutique and beauty salon are conveniently located within the grounds. 時裝與美容店就在院內，很方便。"]}]}]},"manually":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"手動地；用手"}],"sections":[]},"mandate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"授權，委託；任期；命令，指令；託管權，委任統治權；賬戶代理書面委託"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"強制執行，頒佈；授權，委任；命令，指示；（領土）（由國際聯盟）授權託管"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a government or other elected body has a <b>mandate</b> to carry out a particular policy or task, they have the authority to carry it out as a result of winning an election or vote. (政府或機構經選舉而獲得的) 授權","examples":["The president and his supporters are almost certain to read this vote as a mandate for continued economic reform. 總統和他的支持者們幾乎肯定地認為這次投票是對繼續進行經濟改革的授權。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is given a <b>mandate</b> to carry out a particular policy or task, they are given the official authority to do it. (個人所獲得的) 授權","examples":["How much longer does the independent prosecutor have a mandate to pursue this investigation? 這名獨立檢察官獲得授權去調查這件事情的許可權還有多長？"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can refer to the fixed length of time that a country's leader or government remains in office as their <b>mandate</b>. 任期","examples":["...his intention to leave politics once his mandate ends. …他任期一結束就將離開政界的打算。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>is mandated</b> <b>to</b> carry out a particular policy or task, they are given the official authority to do it. 授權","examples":["He'd been mandated by the West African Economic Community to go in and to enforce a ceasefire. 他受西非經濟共同體授權去介入並執行停火協定。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>mandate</b> something means to make it mandatory. 強制執行","examples":["The proposed initiative would mandate a reduction of carbon dioxide of 40%. 這個倡議將把二氧化碳排放量強制降低40%。","Sixteen years ago, Quebec mandated that all immigrants send their children to French schools. 16年前，魁北克省規定所有移民都要送孩子上法語學校。"]}]}]},"maternal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"慈母般的；作為母親的；母系的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Maternal</b> is used to describe feelings or actions which are typical of those of a kind mother toward her child. 母親般的","examples":["She had little maternal instinct. 她幾乎沒有母性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Maternal</b> is used to describe things that relate to the mother of a baby. 母親的","examples":["Maternal smoking can damage the unborn child. 母親吸菸可能會傷害未出生的孩子。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>maternal</b> relative is one who is related through a person's mother rather than their father. 母系的","examples":["Her maternal grandfather was mayor of Karachi. 她的外祖父曾是卡拉奇市的市長。"]}]}]},"mediocre":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"平庸的，中等（質量）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>mediocre</b>, you mean that it is of average quality but you think it should be better. 平庸的","examples":["His school record was mediocre. 他的學業成績一般。"]}]}]},"memo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"備忘錄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>memo</b> is a short official note that is sent by one person to another within the same company or organization. 簡報","examples":["He sent out a memo expressing his disagreement with their decisions. 他發出一份簡報表達他對他們的決定的不贊同。"]}]}]},"midmorning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"上午中段時間；上午十時左右"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"發生在上午中段時間的；上午十時左右的；與上午中段時間有關的"}],"sections":[]},"merger":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司、組織的）合併；<法律>兼併，吸收"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>merger</b> is the joining together of two separate companies or organizations so that they become one. 合併","examples":["...a merger between two of America's biggest trade unions. …美洲兩個最大的工會的合併。"]}]}]},"mentor":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"導師，指導者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給予培訓"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A person's <b>mentor</b> is someone who gives them help and advice over a period of time, especially help and advice related to their job. 導師","examples":["Leon Sullivan was my mentor and my friend. 利昂·沙利文既是我的導師，也是我的朋友。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mentor</b> someone means to give them help and advice over a period of time, especially help and advice related to their job. 指導","examples":["He had mentored scores of younger doctors. 他指導過許多更年輕的醫生。"]}]}]},"meticulous":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"一絲不苟的，注意細節的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>meticulous</b>, you mean that they do things very carefully and with great attention to detail. 小心謹慎的","examples":["He was so meticulous about everything. 他對任何事情都很小心謹慎。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"細緻地","examples":["The flat had been meticulously cleaned. 這間公寓被仔仔細細地打掃過了。"]}]}]},"midday":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"中午，正午"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Midday</b> is twelve o'clock in the middle of the day. 中午","examples":["At midday everyone would go down to Reg's Café. 中午每個人都去雷吉的小餐館。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Midday</b> is the middle part of the day, from late morning to early afternoon. 中午時分","examples":["People were beginning to tire in the midday heat. 在中午的炎炎烈日下，人們開始感到疲勞。"]}]}]},"miserably":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"痛苦地，悲慘地，可悲地；糟糕地，極差地，慘敗地；貧困地"}],"sections":[]},"minutely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"詳細地，精密地；細微地，略微地"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"每分鐘的，按分鐘計的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>minutely</b> to indicate that something is done in great detail. 詳細地","examples":["The metal is then minutely examined to ensure there are no cracks. 之後金屬被詳細地檢查來確保沒有裂縫。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>minutely</b> to indicate that the size or extent of something is very small. 細小地","examples":["The benefit of an x-ray far outweighs the minutely increased risk of cancer. x射線的好處要遠遠超過細小增加地癌症風險"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"every minute 每分鐘地","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"occurring every minute 每分鐘發生的","examples":[]}]}]},"mildly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"溫和地，和善地；適度地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>to put it mildly</b> to indicate that you are describing something in language that is much less strong, direct, or critical than what you really think. 說得委婉些","examples":["But not all the money, to put it mildly, has been used wisely. 但是說得委婉些，並不是所有的錢都用得很明智。"]}]}]},"mid-range":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"中檔的，大眾型的；中等的，平均的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>mid-range</b> to describe products or services which are neither the most expensive nor the cheapest of their type. 中檔的","examples":["...the price of a mid-range family car. …中檔家用轎車的價格。"]}]}]},"mistreatment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"虐待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Mistreatment</b> of a person or animal is cruel behaviour towards them, especially by making them suffer physically. (尤指身體上的)虐待","examples":["...issues like police brutality and mistreatment of people in prisons. ...類似警察施暴和囚犯受虐的問題。"]}]}]},"millennium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"一千年；千週年紀念日，千禧年（the millennium）；世界末日前基督治理世界的一千年（the millennium）；（作為烏托邦的）美滿時期，太平盛世（the millennium）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>millennium</b> is a period of one thousand years, especially one which begins and ends with a year ending in \"000,\" for example the period from the year 1000 to the year 2000. 一千年","examples":["...the dawn of a new millennium. …新千年的開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Many people refer to the year 2000 as <b>the</b> <b>Millennium</b>. 2000年; 千禧年","examples":["...the eve of the Millennium. …千禧年的前夜。"]}]}]},"mistaken":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（信念、想法、觀點等）不正確的，錯誤的；判斷錯誤的，被誤解的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"誤解，搞錯（mistake 的過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>mistaken</b> <b>about</b> something, you are wrong about it. 弄錯的","examples":["I see I was mistaken about you. 我明白我錯看了你。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>mistaken</b> belief or opinion is incorrect. (信念或觀點) 錯誤的","examples":["I had a mistaken view of what was happening. 我對於所發生事情的看法是錯誤的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use expressions such as <b>if I'm not mistaken</b> and <b>unless I'm very much mistaken</b> as a polite way of emphasizing the statement you are making, especially when you are confident that it is correct. 如果我沒搞錯的話 (委婉地表示強調，尤指自信為正確)","examples":["I think Alfred wanted to marry Jennifer, if I am not mistaken. 我想如果我沒搞錯的話,當時艾爾弗雷德想娶珍妮弗。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"錯誤地","examples":["He says they mistakenly believed the standard licences they held were sufficient. 他說他們錯誤地以為持有標準許可證就足夠了。"]}]}]},"mistreat":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"虐待，苛待，粗暴對待"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>mistreats</b> a person or an animal, they treat them badly, especially by making them suffer physically. (尤指在身體上)虐待","examples":["She has been mistreated by men in the past. 過去她受過男人的虐待。"]}]}]},"misunderstanding":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"誤解，誤會；小爭執，分歧"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"誤解，誤會（misunderstand 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>misunderstanding</b> is a failure to understand something properly, for example a situation or a person's remarks. 誤解","examples":["There has been some misunderstanding of our publishing aims. 對於我們的出版目的存在一些誤解。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to a disagreement or slight quarrel as a <b>misunderstanding</b>. 分歧; 爭執","examples":["There was a little misunderstanding with the police and he was arrested. 由於與警方有些小爭執，他被捕了。"]}]}]},"mitigate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>減輕，緩和"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>mitigate</b> something means to make it less unpleasant, serious, or painful. 緩解","examples":["...ways of mitigating the effects of an explosion. …減輕爆炸後果的方法。"]}]}]},"moderately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"有合理限度地，適中地；一般地，勉強地"}],"sections":[]},"modification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"修改的行為（過程）；修改，更改；修飾"}],"sections":[]},"monetize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使……商業化，靠……賺錢（常指透過網站訪客、流量或內容等獲取收入）；把……定為法定貨幣，使成為合法貨幣；把……鑄造成貨幣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to establish as the legal tender of a country 使貨幣化","examples":[]}]}]},"myriad":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>無數，大量；（多用於古典歷史劇中）一萬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無數的，大量的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"quant.","pos_name":"數量詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>A myriad</b> or <b>myriads</b> <b>of</b> people or things is a very large number or great variety of them. 大量; 各種各樣","examples":["They face a myriad of problems bringing up children. 他們在撫養孩子上面臨著各種問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Myriad</b> means having a large number or great variety. 大量的; 各種各樣的","examples":["The magazine has been celebrating pop in all its myriad forms. 該雜誌一直在讚美各種形式的流行音樂。"]}]}]},"mortgage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"按揭，抵押貸款；抵押貸款額"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"抵押；（為眼前好處）使承受（未來）風險"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>mortgage</b> is a loan of money which you get from a bank or savings and loan association in order to buy a house. 房屋抵押貸款","examples":["...an increase in mortgage rates. …房屋抵押貸款利率的上升。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mortgage</b> your house or land, you use it as a guarantee to a company in order to borrow money from them. 抵押","examples":["They had to mortgage their home to pay the bills. 他們不得不抵押他們的房子來還賬。"]}]}]},"narration":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"敘述，講故事；（電影、戲劇等中的）旁白，解說"}],"sections":[]},"nationwide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"全國性的，全國各地的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在全國"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nationwide</b> activities or situations happen or exist in all parts of a country. 全國性的","examples":["The rising number of car crimes is a nationwide problem. 汽車犯罪不斷增加是個全國性的問題。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nationwide</b> is also an adverb. 遍及全國地","examples":["The figures show unemployment falling nationwide last month. 數字顯示，上個月失業數字正全國性地下降。"]}]}]},"mull":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細考慮，斟酌，琢磨（常與 over 連用）；加糖和香料燙熱（葡萄酒、麥芽酒等）；研磨，粉碎；使醉"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"軟薄布，麥爾紗；混亂，一團糟（英式非正式，常用於 make a mull of something）；岬，海角（蘇格蘭）；馬爾島（蘇格蘭西部島嶼）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>mull</b> something, you think about it for a long time before deciding what to do. 斟酌","examples":["Last month, a federal grand jury began mulling evidence in the case. 上個月，一個聯邦大陪審團開始仔細斟酌該案的證據。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to heat (wine, ale, etc) with sugar and spices to make a hot drink 加糖和香料並燙熱(葡萄酒、麥芽酒等)","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"a promontory 岬; 海角","examples":[]}]}]},"neglectful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"馬虎的，不重視的，忽視的；不負責的，不盡職的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as <b>neglectful</b>, you think they fail to do everything they should do to take care of someone or something properly. 失職的","examples":["...neglectful parents. …失職的家長們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>neglectful</b> <b>of</b> something, they do not give it the attention or consideration that it should be given. 忽視的","examples":["Have I been neglectful of my friend, taking him for granted? 我忽視了我的朋友、沒有把他當回事嗎？"]}]}]},"naturally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"自然地，天然地；當然地，必然地；天生地，天性地；不做作地；合乎常理地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>naturally</b> to indicate that you think something is very obvious and not at all surprising under the circumstances. 自然而然地","examples":["When things go wrong, all of us naturally feel disappointed and frustrated. 出問題時，我們自然而然都會覺得失望和沮喪。","Naturally these comings and goings excited some curiosity. 這些來來往往自然會引發一些好奇心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing develops <b>naturally</b> from another, it develops as a normal consequence or result of it. 自然地","examples":["A study of yoga leads naturally to meditation. 習練瑜珈自然地導致冥想。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can use <b>naturally</b> to talk about a characteristic of someone's personality when it is the way that they normally act. 大方地","examples":["He has a lively sense of humour and appears naturally confident. 他有一種生動的幽默感，看起來大方自信。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone is <b>naturally</b> good at something, they learn it easily and quickly and do it very well. 天生地","examples":["Some individuals are naturally good communicators. 一些人天生善於溝通。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>comes naturally</b> <b>to</b> you, you find it easy to do and quickly become good at it. (對…而言) 輕而易舉","examples":["Humanitarian work comes naturally to them. 人道主義工作對他們而言輕而易舉。"]}]}]},"negotiable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可協商的，可討論的；流通的，可兌現的，可轉讓的；可通行的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>negotiable</b> can be changed or agreed upon when people discuss it. 可協商的","examples":["He warned that his economic programme for the country was not negotiable. 他告誡說他為國家制訂的經濟計劃是不容商榷的。"]}]}]},"negligence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"疏忽，大意；<法律>翫忽職守"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is guilty of <b>negligence</b>, they have failed to do something which they ought to do. 瀆職","examples":["The soldiers were ordered to appear before a disciplinary council on charges of negligence. 士兵們被控翫忽職守，被要求接受紀律委員會審查。"]}]}]},"negotiator":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"談判者，磋商者，交涉者；（金融）議付人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Negotiators</b> are people who take part in political or financial negotiations. 談判人","examples":["On Thursday night the rebels' chief negotiator at the peace talks announced that dialogue had gone as far as it could go. 週四晚上，參加和談的叛亂分子的首席談判代表宣佈已經儘可能深入地進行了對話。"]}]}]},"narrowly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"剛好，勉強地；狹隘地，受限地；仔細地，嚴密地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you look at someone <b>narrowly</b>, you look at them in a concentrated way, often because you think they are not giving you full information about something. 嚴密的; 仔細的","examples":["He grimaced and looked narrowly at his colleague. 他做了個鬼臉，然後仔細地看著同事。"]}]}]},"nexus":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>聯絡，關係，關聯；連結，連繫；一系列相互關聯的事物；中心，焦點，樞紐；（生物學）縫隙連線，融合膜；（語言學）聯絡式"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>nexus</b> is a connection or series of connections within a particular situation or system. 關聯","examples":["...the nexus between the dominant class and the State. ...統治階級和國家間的關聯。"]}]}]},"newsletter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（機構定期寄發給成員的）通訊，簡報"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>newsletter</b> is one or more printed sheets of paper containing information about an organization that is sent regularly to its members. (組織等定期印發給其成員的) 內部通訊","examples":["The organization now has around 18,000 members who receive a quarterly newsletter. 該組織目前約有18000名會員收到內部通訊季刊。"]}]}]},"necessarily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"必定，必然；必要地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>not</b> <b>necessarily</b> the case, you mean that it may not be the case or is not always the case. 必要地","examples":["Anger is not necessarily the most useful or acceptable reaction to such events. 生氣未必是對待此類事件最有用或最適合的反應。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something <b>necessarily</b> happens or is the case, you mean that it has to happen or be the case and cannot be any different. 必然地","examples":["Brookman & Langdon were said to manufacture the most desirable pens and these necessarily command astonishingly high prices. 據說布魯克曼蘭登公司製造的鋼筆最令人滿意，而這必然地導致高得驚人的價格。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you reply \"<b>Not necessarily</b>,\" you mean that what has just been said or suggested may not be true. 不一定","examples":["\"He was lying, of course.\"—\"Not necessarily.\" “他當然是在撒謊。”—“不一定。”"]}]}]},"null":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無約束力的，無效的；零值的，等於零的；（數）（集合，矩陣）空的，元素只有零的；無特徵的，無內涵的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<文>零；（密碼中的）無意義暗碼；（電子）無訊號；無電磁輻射的方向"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（訊號）與另一訊號結合產生無訊號狀態，抵消"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an agreement, a declaration, or the result of an election is <b>null and void</b>, it is not legally valid. 無法律效力的","examples":["A spokeswoman said the agreement had been declared null and void. 一位女發言人說那個協議已被宣佈為無效的。"]}]}]},"novelty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"新穎，新奇性；新奇的事物（或人、環境）；廉價小飾物，小玩意兒"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"新奇的，風格獨特的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Novelty</b> is the quality of being different, new, and unusual. 新奇","examples":["In the contemporary western world, rapidly changing styles cater to a desire for novelty and individualism. 在當代西方世界，快速變換著的款式迎合了人們對新奇和獨特性的追求。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>novelty</b> is something that is new and therefore interesting. 新奇的事物","examples":["Stores really like orange cauliflower because it's a novelty, it's something different. 商店真地喜歡橘黃色花椰菜，因為它是一種新奇的東西，與眾不同。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Novelties</b> are cheap toys, ornaments, or other objects that are sold as presents or souvenirs. 新奇的小玩意兒","examples":["At Easter, we give them plastic eggs filled with small toys, novelties, and coins. 在復活節，我們送給他們裝有小玩具、新奇的小玩意兒和硬幣的塑膠蛋。"]}]}]},"obligatory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有義務的，強制性的；慣常的，趕時髦的；（規定，裁決）有約束力的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>obligatory</b>, you must do it because of a rule or a law. 規定性的","examples":["Most women will be offered an ultrasound scan during pregnancy, although it's not obligatory. 大部分婦女懷孕期間都將進行超聲波檢查，儘管不是規定性的。"]}]}]},"nursing":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"護理，看護；哺乳，母乳餵養；養育"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"看護，照料；給…餵奶；養育（nurse 的現在分詞／動名詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Nursing</b> is the profession of caring for people who are ill. 護理工作","examples":["She had no aptitude for nursing. 她沒有從事護理工作的能力。"]}]}]},"obviously":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於強調）顯然，顯而易見；明顯地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>obviously</b> when you are stating something that you expect the person who is listening to know already. 顯然地","examples":["Obviously, they've had sponsorship from some big companies. 顯然，他們已有一些大公司贊助。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>obviously</b> to indicate that something is easily noticed, seen, or recognized. 明顯地","examples":["They obviously appreciate you very much. 他們明顯很欣賞你。"]}]}]},"obsolete":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"淘汰的，廢棄的；（生物特徵的一部分）退化的"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"<美>淘汰（產品），廢棄（想法）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>obsolete</b> is no longer needed because something better has been invented. 被淘汰的","examples":["So much equipment becomes obsolete almost as soon as it's made. 很多裝置幾乎剛製造出來就過時了。"]}]}]},"occupancy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"居住，佔用；佔用人數，容納人數；（尤指酒店的）入住率，居住率"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Occupancy</b> is the act of using a room, building, or area of land, usually for a fixed period of time. 佔用","examples":["Hotel occupancy has been as low as 40%. 酒店入住率已低至40%。"]}]}]},"occupied":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"忙於……的，從事……的；（床、椅子、房間等）已被佔用的；（地方）被佔領的，遭侵佔的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"佔用，居住；佔（空間或一段時間）；（用武力）佔領，侵佔（occupy 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The people who <b>occupy</b> a building or a place are the people who live or work there. 佔用 (某建築、某地)","examples":["There were over 40 tenants, all occupying one wing of the building. 有40多位房客，都住在該大樓的一翼。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a room or something such as a seat <b>is occupied</b>, someone is using it, so that it is not available for anyone else. 佔用 (座位等)","examples":["The hospital bed is occupied by his wife. 那張病床由他妻子佔用。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If a group of people or an army <b>occupies</b> a place or country, they move into it, using force in order to gain control of it. 佔領","examples":["U.S. forces now occupy a part of the country. 美國軍隊現在佔領著該國的一部分地區。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone or something <b>occupies</b> a particular place in a system, process, or plan, they have that place. 佔有 (某位置)","examples":["Many men still occupy more positions of power than women. 許多男性仍比女性佔有更多的權力職位。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> you, or if you <b>occupy</b> yourself, your time, or your mind with it, you are busy doing that thing or thinking about it. (某事物) 佔據 (某人); 使 (自己、自己的時間、自己的思維) 被 (某事物) 佔據","examples":["Her career occupies all of her time. 她的事業佔用了她所有的時間。","He occupied himself with packing the car. 他忙於裝那輛車。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> you, it requires your efforts, attention, or time. (某事物) 佔用 (某人)","examples":["I had other matters to occupy me, during the day at least. 我有別的事要做，至少白天要被佔用。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"If something <b>occupies</b> a particular area or place, it fills or covers it, or exists there. (某事物) 佔據 (某區域、某地)","examples":["Even small aircraft occupy a lot of space. 即便小飛機也佔很多空間。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"佔用的","examples":["Keep the brain occupied. 不讓腦子閒下來。"]}]}]},"offence":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"違法行為，犯罪；冒犯，得罪；過錯，不當；討厭的東西，引起反感的事物；<正式>攻擊，攻擊行為"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>offence</b> is a crime that breaks a particular law and requires a particular punishment. 犯罪行為","examples":["A first offence carries a fine of $1,000. 初犯要罰款$1000。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Offence</b> or an <b>offence</b> is behaviour that causes people to be upset or embarrassed. 冒犯行為","examples":["He said he didn't mean to give offence. 他說他無意冒犯。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In sports such as football or basketball, <b>the</b> <b>offence</b> is the team which has possession of the ball and is trying to score. (足球、籃球等運動中的) 進攻方","examples":["Between plays the coach was talking to the offence in the huddle. 賽間休息時，教練對圍攏的攻方隊員講話。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Some people say \"<b>no offence</b>\" to make it clear that they do not want to upset you, although what they are saying may seem rude. 無意冒犯","examples":["\"No offence,\" she said, \"but your sister seems a little gloomy.\" “沒有冒犯的意思，”她說：“不過你妹妹似乎有點悲觀。”"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>takes offence</b> <b>at</b> something you say or do, they feel upset, often unnecessarily, because they think you are being rude to them. 生氣","examples":["Instead of taking offence, the woman smiled. 那女人不但不生氣反而笑了。"]}]}]},"omission":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"省略，遺漏；被省略（或排除）的人（或物）；（尤指道德上或法律義務的）疏忽"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>omission</b> is something that has not been included or has not been done, either deliberately or accidentally. 刪節; 遺漏","examples":["He was surprised by his wife's omission from the guest list. 他對於賓客名單上他夫人名字的遺漏感到吃驚。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Omission</b> is the act of not including a particular person or thing or of not doing something. 省略; 排除","examples":["...the prosecution's seemingly malicious omission of recorded evidence. …控方對在案證據似為惡意的疏略。"]}]}]},"out-of-date":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"過時的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>out of date</b> is old-fashioned and no longer useful. 過時的","examples":["The regulations were out of date and confusing. 那些規定已經過時，而且令人費解。"]}]}]},"opportune":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<正式>合時宜的，恰好的；適當的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something happens at an <b>opportune</b> time or is <b>opportune</b>, it happens at the time that is most convenient for someone or most likely to lead to success. 適當的; 適時的","examples":["I believe that I have arrived at a very opportune moment. 我想我到得正是時候。","The timing of the meetings was opportune. 會議的時間安排得恰到好處。"]}]}]},"outgun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"（在競賽、競爭等中）勝過，擊敗；在火力方面超過（對方）；槍打得比……準"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In a battle, if one army <b>is outgunned</b>, they are in a very weak position because the opposing army has more or better weapons. (在火力上)壓過","examples":["First Airborne Division was heavily outgunned by German forces. 第一空降師完全被德軍的兇猛火力壓住了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>are outgunned</b> in a contest, you are beaten because your rival is stronger or better than you. (在競賽中)超過","examples":["Clearly, the network is being outgunned by HBO's original drama. 很顯然，美國HBO電視臺原創劇集的收視勝過了網路電視臺的節目。","He soon hit top speed to outgun all his rivals in the opening qualifying session. 他在首場資格賽中很快就跑出了最快速度，擊敗了所有對手。"]}]}]},"originally":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"起初，原來；獨創地，新穎地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When you say what happened or was the case <b>originally</b>, you are saying what happened or was the case when something began or came into existence, often to contrast it with what happened later. 起初","examples":["The plane has been kept in service far longer than originally intended. 這架飛機的服役時間已經遠遠超過了起初的預料。"]}]}]},"outmaneuver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"以計謀勝過，運用策略擊敗"}],"sections":[]},"offset":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"補償，抵銷，抵消；襯托出；使偏離直線方向，使與……不在一條直線上；（墨水，剛印好的頁面）轉印下一頁"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"抵消物，補償；偏離量，偏離距離；（測繪）支距；（電壓或電流的）偏離；側枝，短匐莖；（山的）支脈；（建築）壁階；膠印法"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"膠印的，平版印刷的；偏離中心的，偏置的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>is offset</b> by another, the effect of the first thing is reduced by the second, so that any advantage or disadvantage is cancelled out. 抵消","examples":["The increase in pay costs was more than offset by higher productivity. 工資成本的增加遠非更高的生產率所能抵消的。"]}]}]},"outbound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外出的，向外的，駛向外國的；（通訊、計算機、物流）外發的，外呼的，出站的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>outbound</b> flight is one that is leaving or about to leave a particular place. 開往某地的","examples":["Airport officials say at least 20 outbound flights were delayed. 機場官員說，至少有二十個離港航班被延誤。"]}]}]},"outrun":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"跑得比……快；從……逃脫；超過，超出"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>outrun</b> someone, you run faster than they do, and therefore are able to escape from them or to arrive somewhere before they do. 跑得過","examples":["There are not many players who can outrun me. 跑得過我的選手不太多。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If one thing <b>outruns</b> another thing, the first thing develops faster than the second thing. 超過","examples":["Spending could outrun the capacity of businesses to produce the goods. 支出可能超過行業生產這些貨物的能力。"]}]}]},"outskirt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郊區，市郊（城鎮外圍地區，通常用複數形式 outskirts，常與 of 連用）"}],"sections":[]},"outsmart":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"比……更聰明；用計謀打敗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>outsmart</b> someone, you defeat them or gain an advantage over them in a clever and sometimes dishonest way. 智取","examples":["Troy was very wise for his age and had already figured out ways to outsmart her. 特洛伊以他的年紀來說是非常聰明的，而且已經弄明白了智取她的方法。"]}]}]},"ow":{"summaries":[{"pos":"int.","zh":"（表示疼痛）哦，哎喲"}],"sections":[{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"\"<b>Ow!</b>\" is used in writing to represent the noise that people make when they suddenly feel pain. 哎喲 (書面語中表示突然疼痛時的叫聲)","examples":["Ow! Don't do that! 哎喲！別那樣做！"]}]}]},"outweigh":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"(在重要性或意義上) 超過；比 (某人) 重"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>outweighs</b> another, the first thing is of greater importance, benefit, or significance than the second thing. (在重要性或意義上) 超過","examples":["The advantages of this deal largely outweigh the disadvantages. 這筆交易的利遠大於弊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>outweigh</b> someone, you are heavier than them. 比 (某人) 重","examples":["Young outweighed her opponent by about 60 pounds. 楊比她的對手重約60磅。"]}]}]},"overview":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"概述，綜述"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"概述，綜述"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>overview</b> <b>of</b> a situation is a general understanding or description of it as a whole. 概述","examples":["The central section of the book is a historical overview of drug use. 本書的中心部分是對藥物使用的一個歷史概述。"]}]}]},"oversee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"監管，監督；看到，無意中看到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone in authority <b>oversees</b> a job or an activity, they make sure that it is done properly. 監督","examples":["Use a surveyor or architect to oversee and inspect the different stages of the work. 用一名監察員或建築師去監督和檢查工程的不同階段。"]}]}]},"overtime":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"加班，加班時間；加班費；<美>加時，加時賽"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"超時的，加班的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"超時地"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使（曝光等）超過時間"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Overtime</b> is time that you spend doing your job in addition to your normal working hours. 加班","examples":["He would work overtime, without pay, to finish a job. 他會無償地加班把一件工作完成。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Overtime</b> is an additional period of time that is added to the end of a sports game in which the score is tied, so that one team can score and win the game. 加時賽","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>is working overtime</b> to do something, you mean that they are using a lot of energy, effort, or enthusiasm trying to do it. 全力以赴地做","examples":["We had to battle very hard and our defence worked overtime to keep us in the game. 我們只得苦戰，我們的防守隊員全力以赴確保我們不被淘汰。"]}]}]},"offender":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"犯罪者，違法者；造成問題的人（或事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>offender</b> is a person who has committed a crime. 罪犯","examples":["The authorities often know that sex offenders will attack again when they are released. 當局通常知道性犯罪者被釋放後還會再犯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to someone or something which you think is causing a problem as an <b>offender</b>. 製造麻煩者; 造成麻煩之物","examples":["The plant's leaves can often turn brown, and I sometimes cut off the worst offenders. 那種植物的葉子常會變成褐色，我有時會把最有問題的剪掉。"]}]}]},"part-time":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"兼職的，非全日制的，部分時間的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"兼職地，以非全日制方式，用部分時間地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is a <b>part-time</b> worker or has a <b>part-time</b> job, they work for only part of each day or week. 部分時間的; 兼職的","examples":["Many businesses are cutting back by employing lower-paid part-time workers. 許多商家正透過僱傭低工資的兼職工來削減開支。","Part-time work is generally hard to find. 兼職工作一般很難找。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Part-time</b> is also an adverb. 部分時間地; 兼職地","examples":["I want to work part-time. 我想做兼職。"]}]}]},"payroll":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公司員工的）工資名單；（公司的）發放工資總額；（公司員工的）薪資管理；受聘職員總數"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"資助，補貼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The people <b>on</b> the <b>payroll</b> of a company or an organization are the people who work for it and are paid by it. 在職人員工薪名冊","examples":["They had 87,000 employees on the payroll. 他們有87000人在在職人員工薪名冊上。"]}]}]},"payable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"應付的；到期的；可付的；可獲利的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"應付款"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an amount of money is <b>payable</b>, it has to be paid or it can be paid. 應支付的; 可支付的","examples":["The money is not payable until January 31. 這錢要到1月31日才可支付。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a cheque or postal order is made <b>payable to</b> you, it has your name written on it to indicate that you are the person who will receive the money. 應支付 (給某人) 的","examples":["Make your cheque payable to \"Stanford Alumni Association.\" 把支票開給“斯坦福校友會”。"]}]}]},"particularly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常，尤其；特別是；清楚地，明確地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>particularly</b> to indicate that what you are saying applies especially to one thing or situation. 特別","examples":["Keep your office space looking good, particularly your desk. 保持你辦公的地方整潔美觀，特別是辦公桌。","More local employment will be created, particularly in service industries. 更多的面向當地的就業將被創造出來，尤其是在服務業。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Particularly</b> means more than usual or more than other things. 格外; 異乎尋常地","examples":["Progress has been particularly disappointing. 進展一直格外令人失望。"]}]}]},"penalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使處於不利地位，不公正地對待；處罰，懲罰，處以刑罰；（體育運動中）判罰"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or group <b>is penalized</b> for something, they are made to suffer in some way because of it. 處罰","examples":["Some of the players may, on occasion, break the rules and be penalized. 一些選手可能偶爾會犯規並受到處罰。"]}]}]},"pertain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"適合，關於，適用；<法律>從屬，歸屬；<正式>（在特定的時間或地點）生效，存在"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing <b>pertains</b> <b>to</b> another, it relates, belongs, or applies to it. 與…相關; 屬於; 適於","examples":["...matters pertaining to naval district defence. …與海軍區域防衛有關的問題。"]}]}]},"periodical":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指學術）期刊"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"間發性的，定期的，週期的；（雜誌，報紙）定期出版的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Periodicals</b> are magazines, especially serious or academic ones, that are published at regular intervals. (尤指內容嚴肅或學術性的) 期刊","examples":["The walls would be lined with books and periodicals. 沿這幾面牆將排放書籍和期刊。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Periodical</b> events or situations happen occasionally, at fairly regular intervals. 定期的","examples":["She made periodical visits to her dentist. 她定期去看牙醫。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"定期地","examples":["Meetings are held periodically to monitor progress on the case. 定期召開會議監控案件的進展情況。"]}]}]},"petrol":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>汽油；深藍綠色"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Petrol</b> is the fuel which is used to drive motor vehicles. 汽油","examples":[]}]}]},"pertinent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"切題的，相關的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>pertinent</b> is relevant to a particular subject. 相關的","examples":["She had asked some pertinent questions. 她問了一些相關的問題。","...name, address, and other pertinent information. …姓名、地址及其他相關資訊。"]}]}]},"phd":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"博士學位；哲學博士學位（Doctor of Philosophy）"}],"sections":[]},"placid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（用於地方、水域或生活）平靜的，寧靜的，平和的；（用於人或動物）溫和的，沉著的，不易激動的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>placid</b> person or animal is calm and does not easily become excited, angry, or upset. 溫和的","examples":["She was a placid child who rarely cried. 她是個溫和的孩子，很少哭。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>placid</b> place, area of water, or life is calm and peaceful. 平靜的","examples":["...the placid waters of Lake Erie. …伊利湖平靜的湖水。"]}]}]},"placement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"佈置，擺放；（某人的）安置，安頓；實習工作；收容所，安置所；定位球"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The</b> <b>placement</b> <b>of</b> something or someone is the act of putting them in a particular place or position. (物的) 安放; (人的) 安排","examples":["The treatment involves the placement of twenty-two electrodes in the inner ear. 治療包括在內耳安放22個電極。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>placement</b> of someone in a job, home, or school is the act or process of finding them a job, home, or school. (對某人工作、家庭或學校的) 安置","examples":["The children were waiting for placement in a foster care home. 孩子們正在等待被安置到寄養家庭裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If someone gets a <b>placement</b>, they get a job for a short period of time to gain experience. 實習職位","examples":["He spent a year studying Japanese in Tokyo, followed by a six-month work placement with the Japanese government. 他花了1年時間在東京學日語，接著是在日本政府6個月的實習工作。"]}]}]},"ordinarily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"通常地，一般地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say what is <b>ordinarily</b> the case, you are saying what is normally the case. 通常地","examples":["The streets would ordinarily have been full of people, but now they were empty. 街上通常都是熙熙攘攘的人群，但那時卻空無一人。"]}]}]},"portfolio":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"公文包，畫夾；（成冊展示的）作品集，照片集；（個人或機構的）投資組合；（部長或大臣的）職責，職務；（公司或機構提供的）系列產品，成套物品"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（職業型別）短期合同制的，兼職的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>portfolio</b> is a set of pictures by someone, photographs of their work, or examples of their writing, which they use when entering competitions or applying for work. (用於參賽或求職的) 作品選輯","examples":["After dinner that evening, Edith showed them a portfolio of her own political cartoons. 那天晚飯後，伊迪絲給他們看了她自己的政治漫畫選輯。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In finance, a <b>portfolio</b> is the combination of investments that a particular person or company owns. 投資組合","examples":["...Roger Early, a portfolio manager at Federated Investors Corp. …羅傑·厄爾利，聯合投資者公司的投資組合經理。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"In politics, a <b>portfolio</b> is a high-ranking official's responsibility for a particular area of a government's activities. (高官的) 職責","examples":["He has held the defence portfolio since the first free elections in 1990. 自從1990年的首次自由選舉以來他一直擔任國防部長一職。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"A company's <b>portfolio</b> of products or designs is their range of products or designs. (產品或設計的) 系列","examples":["The company has continued to invest heavily in a strong portfolio of products. 該公司繼續大力投資一個強大的產品系列。"]}]}]},"posting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"郵寄；把……放入；張貼（通知等）；釋出（尤指財經資訊或警告）；交付（保釋金）（post 的現在分詞）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"任命，派駐；（網際網路上的）帖子，留言；任職地點；公告（尤指招聘廣告，常作 job posting）；（會計）過賬；郵寄，投寄；摔跤攻擊術（把對手擲到角柱上）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a member of an armed force gets a <b>posting</b> <b>to</b> a particular place, they are sent to live and work there for a period.  派駐","examples":["...awaiting his posting to a field ambulance corps in early 1941. …1941年初他等著被派駐到野戰救護隊去。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>posting</b> is a message that is placed on the Internet, for example, on a newsgroup or website, for everyone to read. (在網際網路上的) 帖子","examples":["Postings on the Internet can be accessed from anywhere in the world. 網際網路上的帖子可以從世界任何地方看到。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you get a <b>posting</b> <b>to</b> a different town or country, your employers send you to work there, usually for several years. (僱員的) 派駐","examples":[]},{"num":"4.","zh":"a wrestling attack in which the opponent is hurled at the post in one of the corners of the ring (摔跤攻擊術)把對手擲到角柱上","examples":[]}]}]},"postmaster":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"郵政局（所）長；郵件管理員；（postmaster general）郵政總局局長；（計算機網路）接收郵件系統問題報告的專用郵箱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>postmaster</b> is the person in charge of a local post office. 郵政局長","examples":[]}]}]},"pr":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"公共關係（public relations）；效能要求（Performance Requirement）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"pair 對","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"the internet domain name for.","pos_name":"the internet domain name for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Puerto Rico 波多黎各","examples":[]}]}]},"pleased":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高興的，滿意的；高興，樂於（做某事）；洋洋自得的，自滿的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）開心，（使）滿意；想，選擇，喜歡；請便，隨你的便（please 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>pleased</b>, you are happy about something or satisfied with something. 開心的","examples":["Felicity seemed pleased at the suggestion. 費利西蒂似乎對這個建議很滿意。","I think he's going to be pleased that we identified the real problems. 我想他會為我們找到真正的問題所在高興的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say you will be <b>pleased</b> <b>to</b> do something, you are saying in a polite way that you are willing to do it. 樂意 (做某事) 的","examples":["We will be pleased to answer any questions you may have. 我們將願意回答你可能有的任何問題。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can tell someone that you are <b>pleased</b> <b>with</b> something they have done in order to express your approval. 滿意的","examples":["I'm pleased with the way things have been going. 我對事情的進展狀況感到滿意。","I am very pleased about the result. 我對結果很滿意。","We are pleased that the problems have been resolved. 我們很高興問題已經得到了解決。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"When you are about to give someone some news that you know will please them, you can say that you are <b>pleased</b> <b>to</b> tell them the news or that they will be <b>pleased</b> <b>to</b> hear it. 高興的 (告訴或聽到訊息)","examples":["I'm pleased to say that he is now doing well. 我很高興地告訴你，他現在很好。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"In official letters, people often say they will be <b>pleased</b> <b>to</b> do something, as a polite way of introducing what they are going to do or inviting people to do something. 願意的 (用於官方信函中禮貌地介紹打算要做的事或邀請人們做某事)","examples":["We will be pleased to delete the charge from the original invoice. 我們將願意將這筆收費從原來的發票中刪去。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone seems very satisfied with something they have done, you can say that they are <b>pleased with</b> <b>themselves</b>, especially if you think they are more satisfied than they should be. 洋洋自得","examples":["\"Sophie was glad to see you,\" he said, pleased with himself again for having remembered her name. “索菲很高興見到你，”他說，為自己記住了她的名字又暗自得意。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can say \"<b>Pleased to meet you</b>\" as a polite way of greeting someone who you are meeting for the first time. 很高興見到你 (用於初次見面問候對方)","examples":[]}]}]},"potency":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（人、行動或思想的）影響力，支配力；（男子的）性交能力；（藥物等的）效力；（遺傳）潛能；發育能力"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Potency</b> is the power and influence that a person, action, or idea has to affect or change people's lives, feelings, or beliefs. 影響力","examples":["All their songs have a lingering potency. 他們所有的歌曲都有揮之不去的影響力。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>potency</b> of a drug, poison, or other chemical is its strength. (毒品、藥品等的) 效力","examples":["Sunscreen can lose its potency if left over winter in the bathroom cabinet. 防曬霜在盥洗室櫃子裡放置一個冬天後會失去效力。"]}]}]},"precondition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"前提，先決條件（常與 for 連用）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"預處理，事先準備"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is a <b>precondition</b> <b>for</b> another, it must happen or be done before the second thing can happen or exist. 先決條件","examples":["They have demanded the release of three prisoners as a precondition for any negotiation. 他們要求釋放3名囚犯作為談判的先決條件。"]}]}]},"predictable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可預測的，可預料的；老套乏味的，墨守成規的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that an event is <b>predictable</b>, you mean that it is obvious in advance that it will happen. 可預見的","examples":["This was a predictable reaction, given the bitter hostility between the two countries. 考慮到兩國之間的強烈敵意，這種反應是可以預見的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可預見地","examples":["His article is, predictably, a scathing attack on capitalism. 可以預見，他的文章會是對資本主義的猛烈抨擊。"]}]}]},"predisposition":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"傾向，素質；易染病體質"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>predisposition</b> <b>to</b> behave in a particular way, you tend to behave like that because of the kind of person you are or the attitudes you have. (以某方式行事的) 傾向","examples":["There is a thin dividing line between educating the public and creating a predisposition to panic. 教育公眾和營造恐慌傾向之間只有細小的區別。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have a <b>predisposition</b> <b>to</b> a disease or illness, it is likely that you will suffer from that disease or illness. (患某種疾病的) 傾向","examples":["...a genetic predisposition to lung cancer. …一種遺傳性患肺癌的傾向。"]}]}]},"predominate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（數量上）佔優勢，佔大多數；占主導地位，佔支配地位； <罕>支配，主宰"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"主要的，佔支配地位的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one type of person or thing <b>predominates</b> in a group, there is more of that type of person or thing in the group than of any other. (在數量上) 佔優勢","examples":["In older age groups women predominate because men tend to die younger. 在年齡較大的人群中，女性佔多數，因為男性的壽命傾向於短些。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When a feature or quality <b>predominates</b>, it is the most important or noticeable one in a situation. 占主導地位","examples":["He wants to create a society where Islamic principles predominate. 他想建立一個伊斯蘭教信念占主導地位的社會。"]}]}]},"precisely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"精確地，準確地；恰好，正是（表示強調）；（用於表示完全同意）的確如此；嚴謹地，細緻地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Precisely</b> means accurately and exactly. 準確地","examples":["Nobody knows precisely how many people are still living in the camp. 沒有人準確地知道有多少人還生活在那個營地。","The first bell rang at precisely 10:29 a.m. 第一遍鈴聲在上午10：29準時響起。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>precisely</b> to emphasize that a reason or fact is the only important one there is, or that it is obvious. 正是","examples":["Children come to zoos precisely to see captive animals. 孩子們到動物園來正是為了看那些被關起來的動物。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You can say \"<b>precisely</b>\" to confirm in an emphatic way that what someone has just said is true. 正是地","examples":["\"All I did was write the truth.\"—\"Precisely! Now everyone knows.\" “我所做的就是把真相寫出來。” —“正是！現在大家都知道了。”"]}]}]},"premises":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（企業的）房屋建築及附屬場地，營業場所（premise 的複數）"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"以……為基礎，以……為前提；預先提出，事先提到；<古>宣告，說明（premise 的第三人稱單數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>premises</b> of a business or an institution are all the buildings and land that it occupies in one place. 經營場所; 辦公場所","examples":["There is a kitchen on the premises. 營業場所內有一個廚房。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>premise</b> is something that you suppose is true and that you use as a basis for developing an idea. 前提","examples":["The premise is that schools will work harder to improve if they must compete. 前提是各學校如必須競爭就會更加努力改進。"]}]}]},"pretense":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"假象，偽裝；藉口，託詞；裝扮遊戲角色；自稱，自詡；虛浮炫耀的語言（或行為）"}],"sections":[]},"prepaid":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"預付的，先付的，已支付的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"預付（prepay 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Prepaid</b> items are paid for in advance, before the time when you would normally pay for them. 預付了的","examples":["...prepaid funerals. …預付了費用的葬禮。"]}]}]},"pretentious":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"自命不凡的，做作的；（書、電影等）捏造的，矯飾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>pretentious</b>, you mean that they try to seem important or significant, but you do not think that they are. 做作的","examples":["His response was full of pretentious nonsense. 他的回答盡是些裝腔作勢的胡說八道。"]}]}]},"premium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"保險費；（正常價格或費用以外的）加付款，加價；很高的價值，額外價值；額外補貼，津貼；獎品，獎金；<美>優質汽油（=premium gas）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"高價的，高品質的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>premium</b> is a sum of money that you pay regularly to an insurance company for an insurance policy. 保險費","examples":["It is too early to say whether insurance premiums will be affected. 保險費會不會受到影響現在判定還為時過早。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>premium</b> is a sum of money that you have to pay for something in addition to the normal cost. 附加費","examples":["Even if customers want \"solutions,\" most are not willing to pay a premium for them. 即使顧客們想要“解決方案”，大部分人不願意為此支付附加費。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Premium</b> products are of a higher than usual quality and are often expensive. 高階的","examples":["At the premium end of the market, business is booming. 在市場的高階銷售區，生意火暴。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>at a premium</b>, it is wanted or needed, but is difficult to get or achieve. 求之難得","examples":["If space is at a premium, choose adaptable furniture that won't fill the room. 如果空間很有限，就選購不太佔地方的可改裝傢俱。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you buy or sell something <b>at a premium</b>, you buy or sell it at a higher price than usual, for example, because it is in short supply. 以高價 (買、賣)","examples":["He eventually sold the shares back to the bank at a premium. 他最終以高價將股票返售給了銀行。"]}]}]},"prevalent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"盛行的，普遍的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A condition, practice, or belief that is <b>prevalent</b> is common. 盛行的; 普遍存在的","examples":["This condition is more prevalent in women than in men. 這種情況在女性中比在男性中更為普遍。","Smoking is becoming increasingly prevalent among younger women. 吸菸在年輕女性中正變得越來越盛行。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"盛行","examples":["...the prevalence of cocaine abuse in the 1980s. …20世紀80年代可卡因濫用的盛行。"]}]}]},"previously":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"以前地，先前地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Previously</b> means at some time before the period that you are talking about. 先前地","examples":["Guyana's railways were previously owned by private companies. 蓋亞那的鐵路先前為私營公司所擁有。","The contract was awarded to a previously unknown company. 該合同給了一家先前不知名的公司。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>previously</b> to say how much earlier one event was than another event. (某時長) 之前","examples":["He had first entered the House 12 years previously. 他12年前首次進入了眾議院。"]}]}]},"primarily":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"主要地，首要地，根本地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>primarily</b> to say what is mainly true in a particular situation. 主要地","examples":["...a book aimed primarily at high-energy physicists. …一本主要以高能物理學家為目標物件的書。","Public order is primarily an urban problem. 公共秩序主要是一種城市問題。"]}]}]},"prioritize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"按優先順序列出；優先考慮（處理）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>prioritize</b> something, you treat it as more important than other things. 優先考慮","examples":["Prioritize your own wants rather than constantly thinking about others. 優先考慮你自己的需要，而不要總想著別人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>prioritize</b> the tasks that you have to do, you decide which are the most important and do them first. 確定 (任務) 優先順序","examples":["Make lists of what to do and prioritize your tasks. 把你要做的事情列出來，確定任務的輕重緩急。"]}]}]},"privatize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使私有化，使私營化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a company, industry, or service that is owned by the state <b>is privatized</b>, the government sells it and makes it a private company. 使私有化","examples":["Many state-owned companies were privatized. 許多國有公司被私有化了。","...a move to privatize prisons. …一項使監獄私有化的舉措。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"私有化","examples":["...the privatization of government services. …政府服務事業的私有化。"]}]}]},"procure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>（設法） 獲得，取得；為（某人）拉皮條，給（某人）做淫媒；<法律>說服，使（某人）做某事；<古>導致"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>procure</b> something, especially something that is difficult to get, you obtain it. 獲得 (尤指難以獲得的東西)","examples":["It remained very difficult to procure food, fuel, and other daily necessities. 當時仍然很難獲得食品、燃料和其他日用必需品。"]}]}]},"programmer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（計算機）程式設計師，程式設計員；程式設計器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A computer <b>programmer</b> is a person whose job involves writing programs for computers. (計算機) 程式設計師","examples":[]}]}]},"procurement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指為政府或機構）採購，購買；取得，獲得；"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Procurement</b> is the act of obtaining something such as supplies for an army or other organization. 獲得 (軍需品等的) 行為","examples":["Russia was cutting procurement of new weapons \"by about 80 percent,\" he said. 他說俄羅斯正“以大約百分之八十的幅度”削減新武器的補給。"]}]}]},"progression":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"發展，前進；一系列；（從一音或和絃進至另一音或和絃的）進行；占卜術"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>progression</b> is a gradual development from one state to another. (從一狀態到另一狀態的) 逐步發展","examples":["Both drugs slow the progression of HIV, but neither cures the disease. 兩種藥都能減緩艾滋病病毒的發展，但都不能治癒艾滋病。"]}]}]},"prolific":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（植物，動物，人）多產的，多育的；（藝術家，作家，作曲家）作品豐富的，多產的；（運動員）得分高的；眾多的，大批的；富庶的，肥沃的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>prolific</b> writer, artist, or composer produces a large number of works. (作家、藝術家或作曲家) 多產的","examples":["She is a prolific writer of novels and short stories. 她是位多產的長篇和短篇小說家。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An animal, person, or plant that is <b>prolific</b> produces a large number of babies, young plants, or fruit. (動物、人、植物) 多產的","examples":["They are prolific breeders, with many hens laying up to six eggs. 他們是多產的培育者，有許多能下多達6個蛋的母雞。"]}]}]},"promotional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"促銷的，推廣的；促銷的，推廣的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Promotional</b> material, events, or ideas are designed to increase the sales of a product or service. 促銷的","examples":["\"Jeans,\" according to one company's promotional material, \"are designed and made to be worn hard.\" 根據一家公司促銷材料上所說的，“牛仔褲為耐穿而設計和製作。”"]}]}]},"proximity":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（時間、空間、關係的）靠近，親近"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Proximity</b> <b>to</b> a place or person is nearness to that place or person. 接近","examples":["Part of the attraction is Darwin's proximity to Asia. 達爾文港的部分吸引力在於她與亞洲比鄰。","He became aware of the proximity of the Afghans. 他開始意識到那些阿富汗人的接近。"]}]}]},"purely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"完全地，僅僅；貞淑地，清潔地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>purely</b> to emphasize that the thing you are mentioning is the most important feature or that it is the only thing which should be considered. 純粹地; 完全地","examples":["It is a racing machine, designed purely for speed. 那是一部賽車，完全是為速度而設計的。"]}]}]},"questionable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可疑的；不確定的，有問題的；可能不誠實(或不道德)的，別有用心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>questionable</b>, you mean that it is not completely honest, reasonable, or acceptable. 可疑的; 不合理的; 不能接受的","examples":["He has been dogged by allegations of questionable business practices. 他一直被有可疑商業行為的傳言困擾著。"]}]}]},"quickly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"快速地；很快，馬上；短暫地，匆匆地"}],"sections":[]},"radioactive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"放射性的，有輻射的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>radioactive</b> contains a substance that produces energy in the form of powerful and harmful rays. 放射性的","examples":["The government has been storing radioactive waste at Fernald for 50 years. 該政府50年來一直在弗納德儲存放射性廢物。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"放射性","examples":["...the storage and disposal of solid waste that is contaminated with low levels of radioactivity. …對受到低水平放射汙染的固體廢棄物的儲存和處置。"]}]}]},"randomly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（統計）隨機地；胡亂地，任意地"}],"sections":[]},"queue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<英>（人、汽車等的）隊，行列；<英>（為得到某機會而等待的）長列，長隊；（計算機）佇列；呼叫佇列；<古>辮子"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"<英>排隊（等候）；競相，搶著（做某事）；（計算機）排成佇列，排隊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>queue</b> is a list of computer tasks which will be done in order. 佇列 (指等待計算機逐個處理的任務列表)","examples":["Your print job has already been sent from your PC to the network print queue. 你的列印任務已經從你的個人電腦輸送到網路列印佇列了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>queue</b> is a line of people or vehicles that are waiting for something. (等候的) 一隊人; 一列車輛","examples":["Children clutching empty bowls form a queue. 抓著空碗的孩子們排成一隊。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say there is a <b>queue</b> <b>of</b> people who want to do or have something, you mean that a lot of people are waiting for an opportunity to do it or have it. 眾多","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>queue</b> a number of computer tasks means to arrange them to be done in order. 將 (計算機任務) 排序","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>queue</b>, they stand in a line waiting for something. 排隊等候","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Queue up</b> means the same as . 排隊等候","examples":[]}]}]},"rapidly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"快速地，迅速地"}],"sections":[]},"rarely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"罕有，很少；異乎尋常地，極度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>rarely</b> happens, it does not happen very often. 少見地","examples":["They battled against other Indian tribes, but rarely fought with the whites. 他們與其他印第安部落交戰，但很少與白人作戰。"]}]}]},"readership":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"讀者群，讀者人數，讀者的身份；（英國大學）Reader 的職位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>readership</b> of a book, newspaper, or magazine is the number or type of people who read it. 讀者數; 讀者群","examples":["Its readership has grown to over 15,000 subscribers. 它的讀者數已超過一萬五千訂戶。"]}]}]},"quarterly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"季度的，每季的；（盾，圖記）縱橫劃成四（或更多）部分的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"一季一次地，按季度；（紋章）在盾的四分之一部分（或對角兩部分）上"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"季刊"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarterly</b> event happens four times a year, at intervals of three months. 一年四次的; 每季的","examples":["...the latest Bank of Japan quarterly survey of 5,000 companies. …日本銀行對5000家公司最新的季度調查。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Quarterly</b> is also an adverb. 一年四次地; 每季地","examples":["It makes no difference whether dividends are paid quarterly or annually. 紅利是按季度還是按年度支付沒有區別。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>quarterly</b> is a magazine that is published four times a year, at intervals of three months. 季刊","examples":["The quarterly had been a forum for sound academic debate. 這份季刊曾經是正統學術辯論的論壇。"]}]}]},"readiness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"準備就緒狀態；願意，樂意；快，迅捷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is very willing to do something, you can talk about their <b>readiness</b> <b>to</b> do it. 樂意","examples":["...their readiness to co-operate with the new U.S. envoy. …他們樂意與美國的新特使合作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you do something <b>in</b> <b>readiness</b> <b>for</b> a future event, you do it so that you are prepared for that event. 準備就緒","examples":["Security tightened in the capital in readiness for the president's arrival. 首都的安全加強了,為總統的到來做好了準備。"]}]}]},"reader":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"讀者， 愛讀書的人；（初級）讀本，簡易讀物；（英國大學中僅次於教授的）高階講師（Reader）；（美國大學的）助教；電子閱讀器，電子識讀機；縮微軟片閱讀機；（出版社的）審稿人，審閱人；校對人；抄表員；（基督教堂中）領讀經文的信徒"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>readers</b> of a newspaper, magazine, or book are the people who read it. 讀者","examples":["These texts give the reader an insight into the Chinese mind. 這些文章讓讀者對中國式的思維有了深入瞭解。","The paper's success is simple: we give our readers what they want. 本報的成功很簡單：我們給讀者他們想要的東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>reader</b> is a person who reads, especially one who reads for pleasure. 讀書的人 (尤指為獲得樂趣)","examples":["Thanks to that job I became an avid reader. 多虧那項工作我成了一個愛讀書的人。"]}]}]},"rebuild":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"重建，重造； 使復原，使恢復"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指車輛等機器的）重新組裝；（尤指車輛等）改裝的機器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When people <b>rebuild</b> something such as a building or a city, they build it again after it has been damaged or destroyed. 重建 (房屋或城市等)","examples":["They say they will stay to rebuild their homes rather than retreat to refugee camps. 他們說要留下來重建家園而不是撤到難民營中。","The old south grandstand must be rebuilt. 破舊的南看臺一定要重建。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"When people <b>rebuild</b> something such as an institution, a system, or an aspect of their lives, they take action to bring it back to its previous condition. 重建 (組織、制度和生活等)","examples":["The president's message was that everyone would have to work hard together to rebuild the economy. 總統所傳達的資訊是每個人都應一起努力工作重建經濟。"]}]}]},"recharge":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給（電池）充電；恢復體力，恢復精力；再倒滿（茶杯或玻璃杯等容器）；再襲擊"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（蓄水層）補給水分"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recharge</b> a battery, you put an electrical charge back into the battery by connecting it to a machine that draws power from another source of electricity. 給(電池)充電","examples":["The device can recharge a battery in about 25 minutes. 該充電器可在約25分鐘內完成給電池充電。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>recharge</b> your <b>batteries</b>, you take a break from activities which are tiring or difficult in order to relax and feel better when you return to these activities. 放鬆; 補充精力; 恢復精力","examples":["He wanted to recharge his batteries and come back feeling fresh and positive. 他想去放鬆休息一下，然後回來時精力充沛、積極向上。"]}]}]},"rebound":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（球或其他運動物體）彈回；回升，反彈；搶籃板球；產生事與願違的結果，適得其反"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"彈回，反彈；反彈球，回彈球；搶籃板球；回升，復興；（尤指停藥後病情的）反彈，復發；（因失戀而）處於心灰意懶的狀態"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"重捆；重新裝訂（rebind 的過去式和過去分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>rebounds</b> from a solid surface, it bounces or springs back from it. 彈回","examples":["His shot in the 21st minute of the game rebounded from a post. 他在比賽21分鐘時的射門從球門柱上彈了回來。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If an action or situation <b>rebounds</b> <b>on</b> you, it has an unpleasant effect on you, especially when this effect was intended for someone else. 反作用於 (尤指對自己產生本想施與別人的不良影響)","examples":["Mia realized her trick had rebounded on her. 米婭意識到她的伎倆反而害了自己。"]}]}]},"receptionist":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接待員"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"In an office or hospital, the <b>receptionist</b> is the person whose job is to answer the telephone, arrange appointments, and deal with people when they first arrive. (辦公室或醫院) 接待員","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a hotel, the <b>receptionist</b> is the person whose job is to reserve rooms for people and answer their questions. (賓館前臺) 接待員","examples":[]}]}]},"recently":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最近，不久前"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have done something <b>recently</b> or if something happened <b>recently</b>, it happened only a short time ago. 最近","examples":["The bank recently opened a branch in Miami. 這家銀行最近在邁阿密開了一家分行。"]}]}]},"recognizable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可辨認的，可認出的，可識別的；可承認的，可認可的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something can be easily recognized or identified, you can say that it is easily <b>recognizable</b>. 可辨認的; 可認出的","examples":["The vault was opened and the body found to be well preserved, his features easily recognizable. 地窖被開啟了, 屍體被發現儲存完好, 他的面容很容易辨認。"]}]}]},"reclaim":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"要求歸還；利用，改造（荒地）；回收（廢品中有用的東西）；感化，使糾正"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"歸還要求（或主張）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reclaim</b> something that you have lost or that has been taken away from you, you succeed in getting it back. 拿回; 收回","examples":["In 1986, they got the right to reclaim South African citizenship. 1986年，他們得到了恢復南非公民身份的權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>reclaim</b> an amount of money, for example tax that you have paid, you claim it back. 要求歸還","examples":["The good news for the industry was that investors don't seem to be in any hurry to reclaim their money. 對該行業來說，好訊息是投資者們似乎不急於要求收回他們的錢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When people <b>reclaim</b> land, they make it suitable for a purpose such as farming or building, for example by draining it or by building a barrier against the sea. 開墾; 改造","examples":["The Netherlands has been reclaiming farmland from water. 荷蘭一直在圍海造田。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a piece of land that was used for farming or building <b>is reclaimed</b> <b>by</b> a desert, forest, or the sea, it turns back into desert, forest, or sea. 重新變成 (沙漠、森林、海洋)","examples":["The diamond towns are gradually being reclaimed by the desert. 那些開採鑽石的小鎮逐漸被沙漠重新吞噬了。"]}]}]},"recruitment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"招募，招聘；（自然種群）增長；（生理）募集（反應、現象）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>recruitment</b> of workers, soldiers, or members is the act or process of selecting them for an organization or army and persuading them to join. 招聘","examples":["...the examination system for the recruitment of civil servants. …公務員招聘的考試體系。"]}]}]},"reconsider":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"重新考慮；重新審議"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"重新考慮"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reconsider</b> a decision or opinion, you think about it and try to decide whether it should be changed. 重新考慮","examples":["We want you to reconsider your decision to resign from the board. 我們希望你能重新考慮從董事會辭職的決定。","If at the end of two years you still feel the same, we will reconsider. 如果兩年後你仍然有同樣的感覺，我們將重新考慮。"]}]}]},"rectify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>糾正，矯正；整流，把（交流電）轉變成直流電；蒸餾；求曲線的直線等長"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>rectify</b> something that is wrong, you change it so that it becomes correct or satisfactory. 矯正; 改正","examples":["Only an act of Congress could rectify the situation. 只有國會的法案才能扭轉這種局面。"]}]}]},"refurbish":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"整修，翻新重灌；修改，完善"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>refurbish</b> a building or room means to clean it and decorate it and make it more attractive or better equipped. 翻新 (建築物或房間)","examples":["We have spent money on refurbishing the offices. 我們已在這些辦公室的翻新上花了錢。"]}]}]},"registering":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"登記的；（印刷、測繪等）套版，配準的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（register 的現在分詞/動名詞）登記，註冊；記錄，顯示（讀數等）；表達，流露（情感等）；託運（行李等）；感知到，意識到"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>register</b> is an official list or record of people or things. 登記簿","examples":["...registers of births, deaths, and marriages. …出生、死亡及結婚登記簿。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> to do something, you put your name on an official list, in order to be able to do that thing or to receive a service. 登記; 註冊","examples":["Have you come to register at the school? 你到學校來註冊過了嗎？","Thousands lined up to register to vote. 數千人排隊登記投票。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> something, such as the name of a person who has just died or information about something you own, you have these facts recorded on an official list. 登記","examples":["In order to register a car in Japan, the owner must have somewhere to park it. 在日本要想登記一輛汽車，車主必須要有停車的地方。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"When something <b>registers</b> <b>on</b> a scale or measuring instrument, it shows on the scale or instrument. (在儀表上) 顯示","examples":["It will only register on sophisticated X-ray equipment. 只有在先進的X光裝置上它才會顯示出來。","The earthquake registered 5.7 on the Richter scale. 這次地震顯示為里氏5.7級。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If you <b>register</b> your feelings or opinions about something, you do something that makes them clear to other people. 表示 (感情或看法)","examples":["Voters wish to register their dissatisfaction with the ruling party. 選民們希望表達他們對執政黨的不滿。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"If a piece of information does not <b>register</b> or if you do not <b>register</b> it, you do not really pay attention to it, and so you do not remember it or react to it. 留意; 留下印象","examples":["It wasn't that she couldn't hear me, it was just that what I said sometimes didn't register in her brain. 並不是她聽不到我說話，而是我的話有時候沒有在她腦子裡留下印象。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a feeling <b>registers</b> <b>on</b> someone's face, their expression shows clearly that they have that feeling. (面部表情) 流露","examples":["Surprise again registered on Rodney's face. 羅德尼的臉上再次流露出驚訝的表情。"]}]}]},"reimburse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>償還，付還（錢款）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reimburse</b> someone <b>for</b> something, you pay them back the money that they have spent or lost because of it. 報銷; 償還","examples":["I'll be happy to reimburse you for any expenses you've had. 我很樂意報銷你的所有花費。"]}]}]},"reimbursement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"賠付，償付，賠償；賠償金額"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you receive <b>reimbursement</b> <b>for</b> money that you have spent, you get your money back, for example because the money should have been paid by someone else. 報銷; 償還","examples":["She is demanding reimbursement for medical and other expenses. 她在要求醫療和其他費用的報銷。"]}]}]},"regularly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"定期地，有規律地；頻繁地，經常地；均勻地，勻稱地；（語法）變化規律地"}],"sections":[]},"reinforcement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"援兵，增援部隊（reinforcements）；加強，加固；加固物，強化劑；（尤指透過鼓勵或獎賞的）加深，增進，強化；回應"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Reinforcements</b> are soldiers or police officers who are sent to join an army or group of police in order to make it stronger. 增援部隊","examples":["Mr. Vlok promised new measures to protect residents, including the dispatch of police and troop reinforcements. 烏洛克先生答應了新的保護居民的措施，包括派遣增援的警察和軍隊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>reinforcement</b> of something is the process of making it stronger. 鞏固","examples":["I am sure that this meeting will contribute to the reinforcement of peace and security all over the world. 我確信這次會晤將為全世界和平與安全的鞏固做出貢獻。"]}]}]},"reiterate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"<正式>重申，反覆說"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>reiterate</b> something, you say it again, usually in order to emphasize it. 重申","examples":["He reiterated his opposition to the creation of a central bank. 他重申了他對創辦中央銀行的反對。"]}]}]},"relocate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）搬遷，遷移"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If people or businesses <b>relocate</b> or if someone <b>relocates</b> them, they move to a different place. 遷移; 重新安置","examples":["If the company was to relocate, most employees would move. 如果公司要遷移，大多數員工得搬家。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"遷移; 重新安置","examples":["The company says the cost of relocation will be negligible. 公司說遷移的費用微不足道。"]}]}]},"remake":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（電影或歌曲的）新版，改編版，翻拍版；重做；重製物"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"重新制作，改編，翻拍（電影或歌曲等）；重做，改造"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>remake</b> is a movie that has the same story, and often the same title, as a movie that was made earlier. 翻拍影片","examples":["...a 1953 remake of the thirties musical \"Roberta.\" ...1953年對30年代音樂劇《羅伯塔》的一次翻拍。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a movie <b>is remade</b>, a new movie is made that has the same story, and often the same title, as a movie that was made earlier. 重拍; 翻拍(電影)","examples":["Originally released in 1957, the film was remade as \"The Magnificent Seven.\" 這部電影最早在1957年上映，後被翻拍為《七俠蕩寇志》。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you have something <b>remade</b>, you ask someone to make it again, especially in a way that is better than before. 重新做; 翻新","examples":["He had all the window frames in the room remade. 他讓人把屋子裡所有的窗框都翻新了。"]}]}]},"remotely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"稍微，略微；偏僻地，邊遠地；遠端地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>remotely</b> with a negative statement to emphasize the statement. 絲毫; 根本 (用於強調否定)","examples":["We had never seen anything remotely like it before. 我們以前從未見過同它有絲毫相似的東西。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>remotely</b> placed or situated, they are a long way from other people or places. 偏遠的","examples":["...the remotely situated, five bedroom house. …那幢位置偏遠的5居室的房子。"]}]}]},"renewal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"恢復，重新開始；（有效期的）延長，續訂；更新，改建；（有神授超凡能力基督徒的）精神重生"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is a <b>renewal</b> <b>of</b> an activity or a situation, it starts again. 重新開始; 恢復","examples":["They will discuss the possible renewal of diplomatic relations. 他們將討論恢復外交關係的可能性。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>renewal</b> of a document such as a licence or a contract is an official increase in the period of time for which it remains valid. (有效期的) 延長","examples":["His contract came up for renewal. 他的合同交上來要求延期。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"<b>Renewal</b> of something lost, dead, or destroyed is the process of it growing again or being replaced. 新生; 復興","examples":["...a political lobbyist concentrating on urban renewal and regeneration. …一個專門就城市復興與重建而遊說的政客。"]}]}]},"renovation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"翻新，整修"}],"sections":[]},"repetitive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"重複乏味的；多次重複的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>repetitive</b> involves actions or elements that are repeated many times and is therefore boring. 重複 (因而乏味的)","examples":["...factory workers who do repetitive jobs. …做重複工作的工人們。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Repetitive</b> movements or sounds are repeated many times. 重複的","examples":["This technique is particularly successful where problems occur as the result of repetitive movements. 這項技術的成功之處在於能解決重複運動引起的問題。"]}]}]},"reschedule":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"重新排定日程，重訂時間表，重新計劃；（金融）重新安排（債務的）償還期限"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>reschedules</b> an event, they change the time at which it is supposed to happen. 重訂…的時間表","examples":["Since I'll be away, I'd like to reschedule the meeting. 既然我將要離開，我想重新安排一下這次會議的時間。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>reschedule</b> a debt means to arrange for the person, organization, or country that owes money to pay it back over a longer period because they are in financial difficulty. 安排緩期償還","examples":["...companies that have gone bust or had to reschedule their debts. …已經破產的或者不得不安排緩期還債的公司。"]}]}]},"replay":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"重放，回放，重播（錄音帶、錄影帶或電影）；（因未決出勝負或比賽中斷而）重新舉行（比賽），重賽；重現，重演；在腦海中反覆回想（某事）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"重放，回放，重播；重賽；重演；重演的事物，重複出現的事物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a game or match between two sports teams <b>is replayed</b>, the two teams play it again, because neither team won the first time, or because the game was stopped because of bad weather. 重新舉行 (比賽)","examples":["The game had to be replayed at the end of the season. 這場比賽不得不在賽季末重新舉行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>replay</b> something that you have recorded on film or tape, you play it again in order to watch it or listen to it. 重新播放 (電影或磁帶)","examples":["He stopped the machine and replayed the message. 他停下機器，重新播放了那條訊息。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>replay</b> an event in your mind, you think about it again and again. 反覆回想","examples":["She spends her nights lying in bed, replaying the fire in her mind. 她很多個晚上躺在床上，反覆回想著那場火災。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can refer to a game that is replayed as a <b>replay</b>. 重賽","examples":["If there has to be a replay we are confident of victory. 如果不得不重賽，我們有信心贏。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Replay</b> is also a noun. (電影或磁帶的) 重新播放; 回放","examples":["I watched a slow-motion videotape replay of his fall. 我看了他跌倒時的慢動作錄影回放。"]}]}]},"residual":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"殘留的；（數量）剩餘的；（物質狀態在成因消失後）剩餘的；（實驗誤差）捨去的；（土壤）殘餘的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（數量）剩餘；殘差；（付給表演者的）復播追加酬金；殘丘，蝕餘山；（新車購入一定時間後的）轉售值"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Residual</b> is used to describe what remains of something when most of it has gone. 殘留的","examples":["...residual radiation from nuclear weapons testing. …來自核武器試驗的殘留放射物。"]}]}]},"residue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"剩餘物，殘留物；（扣除應付款項、債款、遺贈後的）剩餘遺產，餘產"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>residue</b> of something is a small amount that remains after most of it has gone. 殘留物","examples":["Always using the same shampoo means that a residue can build up on the hair. 總是用同一種洗髮水意味著殘留物會在頭髮上越積越多。"]}]}]},"retainable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可保留的，能保持的；可聘請的"}],"sections":[]},"retailer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"零售商，零售店；講述者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>retailer</b> is a person or business that sells goods to the public. 零售商","examples":["Furniture and carpet retailers are among those reporting the sharpest annual decline in sales. 傢俱和地毯零售商們是在那些報告最大年銷售下滑的商家之中。"]}]}]},"responsive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"反應迅速的，積極反應的；反應熱烈的，熱情的；回應的，回答的；（宗教儀式一部分）用應答（或唱和）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>responsive</b> person is quick to react to people or events and to show emotions such as pleasure and affection. 敏感的","examples":["Harriet was an easy, responsive little girl. 哈麗特是個隨和、敏感的小姑娘。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>responsive</b>, they react quickly and favourably. 迅速積極反應的","examples":["With an election coming soon, your representative should be very responsive to your request. 大選在即，你們的代表應該對你們的要求作出迅速積極的反應。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"敏感","examples":["This condition decreases sexual desire and responsiveness. 這種情況會降低性的慾望和敏感。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"迅速積極的反應","examples":["Such responsiveness to public pressure is extraordinary. 對公眾壓力如此快速積極的反應是非凡的。"]}]}]},"retainer":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"預付聘金，預付費用；牙齒保持器；<舊>家臣，家僕；（機）護圈，保持架；（較少用）保持者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>retainer</b> is a fee that you pay to someone in order to make sure that they will be available to do work for you if you need them to. 預付聘金","examples":["I'll need a five-hundred-dollar retainer. 我將需要一筆500美元的預付聘金。"]}]}]},"sadly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"悲哀地，悲痛地，傷心地；令人遺憾地，可惜，不幸的是；（用於形容詞或過去分詞前）嚴重地，極為"}],"sections":[]},"sadden":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使悲傷，使難過； 悲傷，難過"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>saddens</b> you, it makes you feel sad. 使悲傷; 使難過","examples":["The cruelty in the world saddens me incredibly. 世間的殘酷令我悲傷不已。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悲傷的; 難過的","examples":["He was disappointed and saddened that legal argument had stopped the trial. 讓他失望又難過的是，法庭辯論中止了審判。"]}]}]},"savvy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>實際知識，悟性"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"理解，懂"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<非正式>聰慧的，有經驗的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone as having <b>savvy</b>, you think that they have a good understanding and practical knowledge of something. 洞察力; 見解","examples":["He is known for his political savvy and strong management skills. 他以其政治洞察力和高超的管理手段著稱。"]}]}]},"sadness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"悲傷，悲痛；使人悲傷的事（或難過）的事"}],"sections":[]},"sanitary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公共衛生的，公共保健的；乾淨的，衛生的；（用品）月經期間使用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sanitary</b> means concerned with keeping things clean and healthy, especially by providing a sewage system and a clean water supply. 公共衛生的; 有益於健康的","examples":["Sanitary conditions are appalling. 衛生條件非常惡劣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that a place is not <b>sanitary</b>, you mean that it is not very clean. 乾淨的","examples":["It's not the most sanitary place one could swim. 這不是最乾淨的游泳之地。"]}]}]},"scanner":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"掃描器，掃描裝置；（資訊或影象）掃描器；（醫用）掃描器；訊號掃掠天線；（聲吶或雷達）掃描器"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scanner</b> is a machine which is used to examine, identify, or record things, for example by using a beam of light, sound, or X-rays. 掃描裝置","examples":["...brain scanners. …大腦掃描器。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scanner</b> is a piece of computer equipment that you use for copying a picture or document into a computer. 掃描器","examples":["...a colour printer and scanner. …一臺彩色印表機和掃描器。"]}]}]},"scrutinize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"仔細檢視，細緻審查"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>scrutinize</b> something, you examine it very carefully, often to find out some information from it or about it. 仔細察看","examples":["Her purpose was to scrutinize his features to see if he was an honest man. 她的目的是仔細察看他的特徵看他是不是個誠實的人。"]}]}]},"salvage":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"搶救，救援；搶救出的物品；<法律>海難救助費，打撈費"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"打撈，搶救；挽救，挽回（珍貴或重要的事物）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is salvaged</b>, someone manages to save it, for example, from a ship that has sunk, or from a building that has been damaged. 搶救 (沉船或被毀樓房中的財物)","examples":["The team's first task was to decide what equipment could be salvaged. 該隊的首要任務是決定要搶救出什麼裝置。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you manage to <b>salvage</b> a difficult situation, you manage to get something useful from it so that it is not a complete failure. 挽救 (敗局)","examples":["Officials tried to salvage the situation. 官員們努力挽救這個局面。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you <b>salvage</b> something such as your pride or your reputation, you manage to keep it even though it seems likely you will lose it, or you get it back it after losing it. 挽回 (自尊、聲譽等)","examples":["We definitely wanted to salvage some pride for American tennis. 我們當然想為美國網球挽回些尊嚴。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Salvage</b> is the act of salvaging things from somewhere such as a damaged ship or building. (對沉船或被毀樓房中財物的) 搶救","examples":["The salvage operation went on. 搶救作業繼續進行。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>salvage</b> from somewhere such as a damaged ship or building is the things that are saved from it. (從沉船或被毀樓房中) 搶救出的財物","examples":["They climbed up on the rock with their salvage. 他們帶著搶救出來的財物爬到了礁石上。"]}]}]},"seamlessly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"無縫地，天衣無縫地"}],"sections":[]},"seam":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（縫合兩塊布等的）線縫；煤層，礦層；（木板，牆紙等的）接縫；窄長的凹陷（或傷疤）；寶貴資源；一些，一點兒"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"縫合；使生皺紋"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>seam</b> is a line of stitches which joins two pieces of cloth together. 縫合線","examples":["The skirt ripped along a seam. 那條裙子沿一條縫合線裂開了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>seam</b> of coal is a long, narrow layer of it underneath the ground. (煤) 層","examples":["The average coal seam here is three feet thick. 這裡的煤層平均為3英尺厚。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>is coming apart at the seams</b> or <b>is falling apart at the seams</b>, it is no longer working properly and may soon stop working completely. 散架; 崩潰","examples":["Our university system is in danger of falling apart at the seams. 我們的大學體系處在崩潰的危險之中。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If a place is very full, you can say that it <b>is bursting at the seams</b>. 爆滿","examples":["The hotels of Warsaw, Prague and Budapest were bursting at the seams. 華沙、布拉格和布達佩斯的旅館已經爆滿。"]}]}]},"setup":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"體制，組織方式；<非正式>栽贓，陷害；（軟體或硬體的）安裝；（故事或笑話的）引子"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A particular <b>setup</b> is a particular system or way of organizing something. 體制; 組織方式","examples":["It appears to be an idyllic domestic setup. 它看起來是一種田園式的家庭組織方式。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a situation as a <b>setup</b>, you mean that people have planned it in order to deceive you or to make it look as if you have done something wrong. 圈套; 陷阱","examples":["He was asked to pick somebody up and bring them to a party, not realizing it was a setup. 他被叫去開車接人並送他們到一個聚會，沒意識到那是個圈套。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"The <b>setup</b> of computer hardware or software is the process of installing it and making it ready to use. (電腦硬體或軟體的) 安裝","examples":["The worst part of the setup is the poor instruction manual. 安裝過程中最糟糕的部分就是差勁的操作手冊。"]}]}]},"self-employed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"個體經營的（即自己經營的、不受僱於他人的），自僱的，自由職業的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"the self-employed：個體經營者，自僱者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>self-employed</b>, you organize your own work and taxes and are paid by people for a service you provide, rather than being paid a regular salary by a person or a firm. 個體經營的; 自僱的","examples":["There are no paid holidays or sick leave if you are self-employed. 如果你是個體經營的，那就沒有帶薪休假或病假了。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>The self-employed</b> are people who are self-employed. 個體經營者","examples":["We want more support for the self-employed. 我們需要更多給個體經營者的支援"]}]}]},"severely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"非常嚴重地；嚴厲地，嚴肅地；樸素地，樸實無華地"}],"sections":[]},"shipping":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（總稱）船舶；航運，運輸；運費"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（用船、飛機、卡車）運送，運輸；遣送（某人）；推出（計算機商品），（使）上市（ship 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Shipping</b> is the transportation of cargo or goods as a business, especially on ships. 航運業","examples":["...the international shipping industry. …國際航運業。","...a coupon for free shipping of your catalogue order. …一張可免費運送你在目錄中定購的商品的優待券。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can refer to the amount of money that you pay to a company to transport cargo or goods as <b>shipping</b>. 運費","examples":["It is $39.95 plus $3 shipping. 總共是$39.95加$3的運費。"]}]}]},"shipment":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運輸，運送；運輸的貨物，裝載的貨物量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shipment</b> is an amount of a particular kind of cargo that is sent to another country on a ship, train, aeroplane, or other vehicle. 運送的貨物 (量)","examples":["After that, food shipments to the port could begin in a matter of weeks. 之後，到該港口的食物運送可能在幾周之內開始。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>shipment</b> of a cargo or goods somewhere is the sending of it there by ship, train, aeroplane, or some other vehicle. 運送","examples":["Bananas are packed before being transported to the docks for shipment overseas. 香蕉先要裝箱，然後送到碼頭運往海外。"]}]}]},"shredder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"碎紙機；檔案粉碎機；切碎機；切菜器；撕碎者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shredder</b> is a machine for shredding things such as documents, food, or parts of bushes or trees that have been cut off. 切碎機","examples":["...a document shredder. ...一臺檔案粉碎機。"]}]}]},"simulation":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"模擬，仿造物；假裝，冒充"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Simulation</b> is the process of simulating something or the result of simulating it. 模擬; 模擬結果","examples":["Training includes realistic simulation of casualty procedures. 訓練包括傷亡處理程式的實際模擬。"]}]}]},"simulate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"假裝，冒充；模擬，模仿；看上去像；計算機模擬"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"<古> 虛假的，假裝的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>simulate</b> an action or a feeling, you pretend that you are doing it or feeling it. 假裝","examples":["They rolled about on the Gilligan Road, simulating a bloodthirsty fight. 他們在吉利根路上打滾，模擬一場血腥的戰鬥。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>simulate</b> a set of conditions, you create them artificially, for example, in order to conduct an experiment. 模擬","examples":["The scientist developed one model to simulate a full year of the globe's climate. 這位科學家研製出一個模型，能模擬全年地球的氣候。"]}]}]},"sincerely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"由衷地，真誠地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say or feel something <b>sincerely</b>, you really mean or feel it, and are not pretending. 誠懇地; 真誠地","examples":["\"Congratulations,\" he said sincerely. “祝賀，”他真誠地說道。","...sincerely held religious beliefs. …虔誠遵奉的宗教信仰。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People write \"<b>Sincerely yours</b>\" or \"<b>Sincerely</b>\" before their signature at the end of a formal letter when they have addressed it to someone by name. People sometimes write \"<b>Yours sincerely</b>\" instead. 謹上","examples":["Sincerely yours, Robbie Weinz. 羅比·溫茲謹上。"]}]}]},"smoothly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"平穩地，連續而流暢地；順利地；平靜地，自信地；平整地，均勻地； 圓滑地"}],"sections":[]},"sola":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"粗糙田皂角（田皂角屬植物，學名 Aeschynomene aspera）；（Sola）人名（常見於英、俄、芬、西、葡、意、羅、瑞典語）：索拉，蘇拉"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（金融）單張的，單式的（用於 sola bill、sola draft）"}],"sections":[]},"sinful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有罪的，罪惡的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>sinful</b>, you mean that they are wicked or immoral. 罪惡的","examples":["\"I am a sinful man, Magda,\" he said quietly. “我是個罪人，馬格達，”他輕聲地說。","This is a sinful world. 這是一個罪惡的世界。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"罪惡","examples":["...the sinfulness of apartheid. …種族隔離的罪惡。"]}]}]},"solace":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"安慰，慰藉（多作不可數名詞）；安慰之物（指能給人安慰的人、事物或活動）"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"安慰，撫慰；（較少見）使快樂，排遣"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Solace</b> is a feeling of comfort that makes you feel less sad. 慰藉","examples":["I found solace in writing when my father died three years ago. 我父親3年前去世時，我從寫作中找到了慰藉。"]}]}]},"shareholder":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"股東，股票持有者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>shareholder</b> is a person who owns shares in a company. 股東","examples":["...a shareholders' meeting. …一次股東會議。"]}]}]},"solely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"單獨地，僅有地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something involves <b>solely</b> one thing, it involves only this thing and no others. 惟一地","examples":["Too often we make decisions based solely upon what we see in the magazines. 大多數時候，我們僅僅依據在雜誌上看到的東西作決定。"]}]}]},"stance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（公開表明的）觀點，態度，立場；（尤指體育運動中的）站立姿勢；（用來繫繩索的）巖架，立足點，立腳處；街邊市場，（街上小販的）貨攤，出租汽車停車處"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>stance</b> on a particular matter is your attitude to it. (對某事的) 態度; 立場","examples":["Congress had agreed to reconsider its stance on the armed struggle. 國會已經同意重新考慮其對本次武裝鬥爭的態度。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Your <b>stance</b> is the way that you are standing. 站姿","examples":["Take a comfortably wide stance and flex your knees a little. 取兩腿自然分開的站姿，雙膝微屈。"]}]}]},"specification":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"規格，規範，明細單，說明書；明確說明，詳述；（申請專利用的）發明物說明書"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>specification</b> is a requirement which is clearly stated, for example about the necessary features in the design of something. 具體要求","examples":["I'd like to buy some land and have a house built to my specification. 我想買塊地並按照我的要求建一座房子。"]}]}]},"sponsorship":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"贊助，贊助款；資助，倡議"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sponsorship</b> is financial support given by a sponsor. 贊助; 資助","examples":["Campbell is one of an ever-growing number of skiers in need of sponsorship. 坎貝爾是日益增多的需要資助的滑雪者之一。"]}]}]},"solicit":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"請求，索求，徵求（意見）；<美>兜售，推銷；拉（客），賣淫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>solicit</b> money, help, support, or an opinion <b>from</b> someone, you ask them for it. 請求給予","examples":["He's already solicited their support on health care reform. 他已經請求他們給予醫療保健改革方面的支援。"]}]},{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When prostitutes <b>solicit</b>, they offer to have sex with people in return for money. (妓女) 拉客","examples":["Prostitutes were forbidden to solicit on public roads and in public places. 娼妓被禁止在公路上和公共場所拉客。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"拉客","examples":["Girls could get very heavy sentences for soliciting – nine months or more. 年輕女孩拉客可能會被處以重罰–9個月或更長。"]}]}]},"standpoint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"立場，觀點，角度；觀景點，觀看位"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>From</b> a particular <b>standpoint</b> means looking at an event, situation, or idea in a particular way. 觀點; 角度","examples":["He believes that from a military standpoint, the situation is under control. 他認為從軍事角度來看，局勢已得到控制。"]}]}]},"steadfast":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"忠誠的，堅定的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone is <b>steadfast</b> <b>in</b> something that they are doing, they are convinced that what they are doing is right and they refuse to change it or to give up. 堅定的","examples":["He remained steadfast in his belief that he had done the right thing. 他仍然堅信自己做了正確的事情。"]}]}]},"storyline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（書、電影、戲劇等的）故事情節，劇情"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>storyline</b> of a book, movie, or play is its story and the way in which it develops. (書、電影或戲劇的)故事情節","examples":["The surprise twists in the storyline are the film's greatest strength. 故事情節的曲折離奇是這部電影的精彩之處。"]}]}]},"statistics":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"統計學；統計數字（statistic 的複數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"quantitative data on any subject, esp data comparing the distribution of some quantity for different subclasses of the population 統計資料","examples":[]}]}]},"subjectively":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"主觀地，在主觀上；臆想地；內省地"}],"sections":[]},"streamline":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"精簡（工商企業、組織、流程等）使效率更高；使……成為流線型"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（流動液體的）流線"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（液體的流動）順暢的，暢流的；<舊>流線型的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>streamline</b> an organization or process means to make it more efficient by removing unnecessary parts of it. 提高…效率","examples":["They're making efforts to streamline their normally cumbersome bureaucracy. 他們正努力提高其通常臃腫的官僚機構的效率。"]}]}]},"subside":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"趨於平靜，平息；（建築物或土地）沉降，下陷；（水）退；禁不住顯露（強烈的情感，尤指大笑）（subside in/into）；（腫）消退；坐下，跪下，躺下；沉澱"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a feeling or noise <b>subsides</b>, it becomes less strong or loud. 減弱","examples":["The pain had subsided during the night. 那疼痛在晚間已減輕了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If fighting <b>subsides</b>, it becomes less intense or general. 平息","examples":["Violence has subsided following two days of riots. 暴力在兩天的暴亂之後已經平息了。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If the ground or a building <b>is subsiding</b>, it is very slowly sinking to a lower level. 下陷","examples":["Does that mean the whole house is subsiding? 那意味著整棟房子正在下陷嗎？"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If a level of water, especially flood water, <b>subsides</b>, it goes down. (尤指洪水的水位) 回落","examples":["Local officials say the flood waters have subsided. 當地官員們說洪水已經退了。"]}]}]},"subsidiary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"子公司，附屬公司；輔助者"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"次要的，附屬的；子公司的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>subsidiary</b> or a <b>subsidiary</b> company is a company which is part of a larger and more important company. 子公司","examples":["WM Financial Services is a subsidiary of Washington Mutual. 華盛頓互惠銀行金融服務公司是華盛頓互惠銀行的子公司。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>subsidiary</b>, it is less important than something else with which it is connected. 輔助的","examples":["The marketing department has always played a subsidiary role to the sales department. 營銷部一直都扮演著銷售部的輔助角色。"]}]}]},"subsidy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"補貼，津貼，補助金；<史>（議會發給王室的）特別津貼；（特殊場合徵收的）稅收"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>subsidy</b> is money that is paid by a government or other authority in order to help an industry or business, or to pay for a public service. 補貼金","examples":["European farmers are planning a massive demonstration against farm subsidy cuts. 歐洲的農場主們正在策劃一場反對削減農場補貼的大遊行。"]}]}]},"subsidize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"資助，補助，給……發津貼；（政府）資助，出資支援；向……行賄"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a government or other authority <b>subsidizes</b> something, they pay part of the cost of it. 補貼","examples":["Around the world, governments have subsidized the housing of middle- and upper-income groups. 全世界各政府都補貼過中高收入人群的住房。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"被補貼了的","examples":["...heavily subsidized prices for housing, bread, and meat. …受到高額補貼的住房、麵包和肉類價格。"]}]}]},"supplementary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"補充的，附加的；（角）互補的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"補充者，增補物；<英>補充提問"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supplementary</b> things are added to something in order to improve it. 補充的","examples":["...the question of whether or not we need to take supplementary vitamins. …我們是否有必要補充維生素的問題。"]}]}]},"supplier":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"供應商，供應者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>supplier</b> is a person, company, or organization that sells or supplies something such as goods or equipment to customers. 供應商","examples":["...one of the country's biggest food suppliers. …該國最大的食品供應商之一。"]}]}]},"substantiate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"證實，證明（…屬實）；使具體化，使實體化"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>substantiate</b> a statement or a story means to supply evidence which proves that it is true. 證實","examples":["There is little scientific evidence to substantiate the claims. 幾乎沒有能證實這些斷言的科學證據。"]}]}]},"supervisory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"監督的，管理的，監管的（通常作定語）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Supervisory</b> means involved in supervising people, activities, or places. 管理的; 監督的","examples":["Most supervisory boards meet only twice a year. 大多數監理會一年只開兩次會。","...staff with a minor supervisory role. ...擔任少量監督工作的職員。"]}]}]},"supportive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"支援的，擁護的，給予幫助的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>supportive</b>, you are kind and helpful to someone at a difficult or unhappy time in their life. (對處境困難或不幸者) 給予幫助的","examples":["They were always supportive of each other. 他們總是互相幫助。"]}]}]},"surely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"（用於表明你相信某事極有可能）想必，諒必；無疑，肯定；<美>當然；絕不可能，絕對不會（用於表示不相信）；自信地；穩當地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>surely</b> to emphasize that you think something should be true, and you would be surprised if it was not true. 肯定地","examples":["You're an intelligent woman, surely you realize by now that I'm helping you. 你是個聰明的女人，你現在肯定意識到我在幫你。","You surely haven't forgotten Dr. Walters? 你肯定還沒忘記沃爾特斯博士吧？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something will <b>surely</b> happen or is <b>surely</b> the case, it will definitely happen or is definitely the case. 必定地","examples":["He knew that under the surgeon's knife he would surely die. 他知道在這位外科醫生的刀下他會必死無疑。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is happening <b>slowly but surely</b>, you mean that it is happening gradually but it is definitely happening. 緩慢但確實地","examples":["Slowly but surely she started to fall in love with him. 雖然緩慢，但她確實開始愛上他了。"]}]}]},"surmise":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"<正式>根據不完整的證據或線索猜測，推測"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"<正式>猜測；認為"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"<正式>基於不完整證據的推測，猜度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>surmise</b> that something is true, you guess it from the available evidence, although you do not know for certain. 猜測","examples":["There's so little to go on, we can only surmise what happened. 幾乎沒有什麼可繼續進行的，我們只能猜測發生過的事。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a particular conclusion is <b>surmise</b>, you mean that it is a guess based on the available evidence and you do not know for certain that it is true. 猜測","examples":["It is mere surmise that Bosch had Brant's poem in mind when doing this painting. 博斯畫這幅畫時頭腦裡想著勃朗特的詩，這只是猜測而已。"]}]}]},"susceptible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易得病的，易受影響的；（人）易受感動的，易動感情的；可能有······的，容許······的；<正式>（尤指想法或陳述）能被理解（或證明、解釋）的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>susceptible to</b> something or someone, you are very likely to be influenced by them. 易受…影響的","examples":["Young people are the most susceptible to advertisements. 年輕人最容易受廣告影響。","James was extremely susceptible to flattery. 詹姆斯非常容易受奉承話的影響。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>susceptible to</b> a disease or injury, you are very likely to be affected by it. 易受 (傷) 的; 易患 (病) 的","examples":["Walking with weights makes the shoulders very susceptible to injury. 負重行走使肩膀很容易受傷。"]}]}]},"takeout":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"外賣，外帶食品（美國英語，多作不可數名詞）；外賣餐館，外帶食品店（美國英語，可數名詞）；（橋牌）示意搭檔改叫的叫牌；擊飛"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"外賣的，供顧客帶出外吃的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>takeout</b> is a shop or restaurant which sells hot cooked food that you eat somewhere else. 外賣餐館","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Takeout</b> or <b>takeout</b> food is hot cooked food which you buy from a shop or restaurant and eat somewhere else. 外賣食品","examples":["...a takeout pizza. …一個外賣比薩。"]}]}]},"symposium":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"專題研討會，討論會；專題論文集；（尤指古希臘在宴會後舉行的）酒會"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>symposium</b> is a conference in which experts or academics discuss a particular subject. 專題研討會","examples":["He had been taking part in an international symposium on population. 他那時在參加一個有關人口的國際研討會。"]}]}]},"synthesis":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"綜合，綜合體；（化學物質的）合成；音響合成；（黑格爾哲學中的）合題；（語法）合成；（語言學）綜合"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>synthesis</b> <b>of</b> different ideas or styles is a mixture or combination of these ideas or styles. 結合體","examples":["His novels are a rich synthesis of Balkan history and mythology. 他的小說是一個巴爾幹半島的歷史和神話的豐富結合。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>synthesis</b> of a substance is the production of it by means of chemical or biological reactions. 合成","examples":["...the genes that regulate the synthesis of these compounds. …控制這些化合物合成的基因。"]}]}]},"systematically":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"系統地，有條理地"}],"sections":[]},"tactful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"乖巧的，圓滑的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or what they say as <b>tactful</b> you approve of them because they are careful not to offend or upset another person. 有分寸的","examples":["He had been extremely tactful in dealing with the financial question. 他在處理這個財務問題時一直非常有分寸。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"有分寸地","examples":["Alex tactfully refrained from further comment. 亞歷克斯很有分寸地不多作評論。"]}]}]},"takeover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接管；驗收"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>takeover</b> is the act of gaining control of a company by buying more of its shares than anyone else. (公司的) 收購","examples":["He lost his job in a corporate takeover. 他在一次公司收購中丟掉了工作。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>takeover</b> is the act of taking control of a country, political party, or movement by force. (用武力的) 接管","examples":["There's been a military takeover of some kind. 曾發生過一次類似軍事接管的事情。"]}]}]},"tangible":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"明確的，真實的；可觸控的，可感知的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"可觸知的東西"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>tangible</b>, it is clear enough or definite enough to be easily seen, felt, or noticed. 清晰明確的","examples":["There should be some tangible evidence that the economy is starting to recover. 應該有一些足夠清晰的證據表明經濟正開始復甦。"]}]}]},"tenure":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（土地的）居住權，保有權；（尤指大學教師的）終身職位，長期聘用；（尤指重要政治職務的）任期，任職"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"授予……終身職位（尤指教師、講師職位）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Tenure</b> is the legal right to live in a particular building or to use a particular piece of land during a fixed period of time. 居住權; (土地的) 使用權","examples":["Lack of security of tenure was a reason for many families becoming homeless. 居住權缺乏安全保障是許多家庭無家可歸的一個原因。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Tenure</b> is the period of time during which someone holds an important job. 任期","examples":["...the challenges he faced during his tenure as chief executive officer. …他在執行長任期內面臨的種種挑戰。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you have <b>tenure</b> in your job, you have the right to keep it until you retire. 終身職位","examples":[]}]}]},"technicality":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（過程、活動的，常用複數）技術性細節，具體技術要點；訴訟程式性細節，技術性細則；專門性；術語的使用"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"複數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>technicalities</b> of a process or activity are the detailed methods used to do it or to carry it out. (過程、活動的) 技術性細節","examples":["...the technicalities of classroom teaching. …課堂教學的技術性細節。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>technicality</b> is a point, especially a legal one, that is based on a strict interpretation of the law or of a set of rules but that may seem unimportant compared to a larger issue. (尤指法律的) 技術性細則","examples":["The earlier verdict was overturned on a legal technicality. 較早的裁決因法律上的一項技術性細則而遭到推翻。"]}]}]},"thoroughness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"徹底，完全，周密"}],"sections":[]},"testimonial":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"證明書；推薦書"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"證明的；褒獎的；表揚的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>testimonial</b> is a written statement about a person's character and abilities, often written by their employer. (常指僱主證明某人品德和能力的) 證明書","examples":["She could hardly expect her employer to provide her with testimonials to her character and ability. 她幾乎不指望老闆會給她寫證明她的人品和能力的證明書。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>testimonial</b> is an event which is held to honour someone for their services or achievements. 表彰會","examples":["...a testimonial dinner held in New York. …在紐約舉行的一個表彰晚宴。"]}]}]},"transact":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"辦理，處理；進行（交易、業務等）"},{"pos":"vi.","zh":"交易；談判"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>transact</b> business, you enter into a deal with someone, for example, by buying or selling something. 交易","examples":["This would free them to transact business across state lines. 這會使他們自由地跨越州界進行商業交易。"]}]}]},"timeliness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"及時性，時效性，適時性"}],"sections":[]},"testify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（通常指在法庭上）作證；證明，證實；<美>（尤指做禮拜時）見證（上帝存在）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞/不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>testifies</b> in a court of law, they give a statement of what they saw someone do or what they know of a situation, after having promised to tell the truth. (在法庭上) 作證","examples":["Several eyewitnesses testified that they saw the officers hit Miller in the face. 幾個目擊者證明他們看到那些警察們打了米勒的臉。","Eva testified to having seen Herndon with his gun on the stairs. 伊娃證明曾看見赫恩登在樓梯上拿著槍。"]}]}]},"trustee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"受託人，託管人；理事，董事"},{"pos":"vt.","zh":"移交（財產或管理權）給受託人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>trustee</b> is someone with legal control of money or property that is kept or invested for another person, company, or organization. 受託人","examples":["The trustees of your pension fund decide which fund manager will invest some or all of your future income. 你的養老基金的受託人決定哪一位基金經理將投資你部分或所有的未來收入。"]}]}]},"truly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"真實地，如實地；真正地，完全地；誠摯地，真誠地；準確地；非常，很"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>truly</b> to emphasize that something has all the features or qualities of a particular thing, or is the case to the fullest possible extent. 真正地; 完全地","examples":["...a truly democratic system. …一個真正民主的體制。","Not all doctors truly understand the reproductive cycle. 並非所有的醫生都完全地瞭解生育週期。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>truly</b> in order to emphasize your description of something. 非常","examples":["...a truly splendid man. …一個非常好的男人。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>truly</b> to emphasize that feelings are genuine and sincere. 由衷地; 真誠地","examples":["Believe me, Susan, I am truly sorry. 相信我，蘇珊，我由衷地感到愧疚。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You write <b>Yours truly</b> at the end of a formal letter, and before signing your name, to someone you do not know very well. 你忠誠的 (用於正式信件的信末署名前)","examples":["Yours truly, Phil Turner. 你忠誠的菲爾·特納。"]}]}]},"two-sided":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有兩邊的，雙面的；兩方面的，涉及兩方的，雙邊的；（統計學）雙側的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"having two sides or aspects 有兩邊的; 兩方面的","examples":[]}]}]},"terminology":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（某學科的）術語；有特別含義的用語，專門用語；術語學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>terminology</b> of a subject is the set of special words and expressions used in connection with it. 術語","examples":["...gastritis, which in medical terminology means an inflammation of the stomach. …胃炎這個詞在醫學術語裡的意思是胃部發炎。"]}]}]},"typo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"<非正式>排印錯誤"},{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"排字工，印刷工（typographer）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>typo</b> is a typographical error. 列印錯誤","examples":["It is now listed in the classifieds, with no typos or misprints. 它現在被列在分類廣告上，沒有列印錯誤或印刷錯誤。"]}]}]},"unable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不能勝任的，不會的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>unable</b> <b>to</b> do something, it is impossible for you to do it, for example because you do not have the necessary skill or knowledge, or because you do not have enough time or money. 不能做到的","examples":["The military may feel unable to hand over power to a civilian president next year. 軍方可能覺得無法在明年把政權移交給一位民選總統。"]}]}]},"turnover":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（一定時期內的）營業額，成交量；（商店的）貨物週轉率，銷售比率；人事變動率，人員流動率；半圓餡餅（用水果、肉類或蔬菜做餡）；<美>（比賽中的）易手，失誤"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"翻過來的，可翻轉的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>turnover</b> of a company is the value of the goods or services sold during a particular period of time. 營業額","examples":["The company had a turnover of $3.8 million. 那個公司擁有380萬美元的營業額。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>turnover</b> of people in an organization or place is the rate at which people leave and are replaced. 人員流動率","examples":["Short-term contracts increase staff turnover. 短期合同會增加員工的流動率。"]}]}]},"ultra":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（尤指政治上的）過激分子，極端主義者；超級馬拉松（ultramarathon的簡稱）"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"極端的，偏激的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"很，非常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"extreme or immoderate, esp in beliefs or opinions (信仰或意見)極端的; 偏激的","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"an extremist 極端分子; 偏激的人","examples":[]}]}]},"ultimately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"最終，最後；根本上，最重要地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Ultimately</b> means finally, after a long and often complicated series of events. 最終","examples":["Whatever the scientists ultimately conclude, all of their data will immediately be disputed. 無論科學家們最終得出什麼結論，他們的所有資料將隨即受到質疑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>ultimately</b> to indicate that what you are saying is the most important point in a discussion. 最重要地","examples":["Ultimately, Judge Lewin has the final say. 最重要地，盧因法官有最終發言權。"]}]}]},"unacceptable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不能接受的；不受歡迎的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>unacceptable</b>, you strongly disapprove of it or object to it and feel that it should not be allowed to continue. 不能接受的","examples":["It is totally unacceptable for children to swear. 小孩子罵人是完全不能接受的。"]}]}]},"unauthorized":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"未經許可（或批准）的，未經授權的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>unauthorized</b>, it has been produced or is happening without official permission. 未經授權的; 未經許可的","examples":["...a new unauthorized biography of the Russian president. …一本新的未經授權的俄羅斯總統傳記。","It has also been made quite clear that the trip was unauthorized. 這次旅行是未經過批准的，這一點也已經非常清楚了。"]}]}]},"unaccustomed":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不習慣的，不熟悉的；不尋常的，奇怪的，異乎慣例的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>unaccustomed to</b> something, you do not know it very well or have not experienced it very often. 不習慣的; 不瞭解的","examples":["They were unaccustomed to such military setbacks. 他們不習慣這樣的軍事失敗。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe someone's behaviour or experiences as <b>unaccustomed</b>, you mean that they do not usually behave like this or have experiences of this kind. 不尋常的","examples":["He began to comfort me with such unaccustomed gentleness. 他開始用異乎尋常的溫柔安慰我。"]}]}]},"unaccountable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無法解釋的，莫名其妙的，不可理解的；無責任的，不擔負責任的，不受問責的（用於人或機構，常含批評意味）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>unaccountable</b> does not seem to have any sensible explanation. 難以解釋的","examples":["For some unaccountable reason, it struck me as extremely funny. 很難解釋是什麼原因讓我覺得它極為可笑。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you describe a person or organization as <b>unaccountable</b>, you are critical of them because they are not responsible to anyone for their actions, or do not feel they have to explain their actions to anyone. 無解釋責任的; 不擔負責任的","examples":["Economic policy should not be run by an unaccountable committee of governors of central banks. 經濟政策不應該由中央銀行行長組成的不負責任的委員會來施行。"]}]}]},"unaware":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不知道的，未察覺到的，未意識到的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"意外地，不知不覺地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>unaware</b> <b>of</b> something, you do not know about it. 不知道的","examples":["Many people are unaware of just how much food and drink they consume. 許多人不知道自己到底消耗掉多少食物和飲料。"]}]}]},"unbalance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"使失去平衡，使失衡；使精神紊亂，使精神錯亂"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"（工程）失衡，不平衡；精神錯亂，精神失常"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something <b>unbalances</b> a relationship, system, or group, it disturbs or upsets it so that it is no longer successful or functioning properly. 使(關係、系統)失去平衡","examples":["Tax cuts may unbalance the budget. 稅收減少可能使預算失去平衡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>unbalance</b> something means to make it unsteady and likely to tip over. 使(物體)失去平衡","examples":["The driver said the load may have shifted and unbalanced the truck. 司機說可能是貨物移動使卡車失去了平衡。"]}]}]},"unbeatable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不能超越的，無與倫比的；無法擊敗的，無敵手的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>unbeatable</b>, you mean that it is the best thing of its kind. 無可匹敵的; 無與倫比的","examples":["These resorts remain unbeatable in terms of price. 這些度假勝地在價格上仍是無可匹敵的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"In a game or competition, if you describe a person or team as <b>unbeatable</b>, you mean that they win so often, or perform so well that they are unlikely to be beaten by anyone. 無敵手的","examples":["With two more days of competition to go China is in an unbeatable position. 比賽進行到最後兩天時，中國隊已處於無敵手的地位。"]}]}]},"unbiased":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"公正的，無偏見的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>unbiased</b>, you mean they are fair and not likely to support one particular person or group involved in something. 無偏見的; 公正的","examples":["There is no clear and unbiased information available for consumers. 沒有清楚公正的資訊提供給消費者。"]}]}]},"uncertainty":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"猶豫，無把握；拿不定的事，令人無把握的局面；緊張不安"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Uncertainty</b> is a state of doubt about the future or about what is the right thing to do. 不確定狀態","examples":["...a period of political uncertainty. …一段政治不穩定時期。"]}]}]},"unconventional":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"非常規的，不依慣例的；（人、態度、行為）不遵循傳統的，標新立異的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a person or their attitude or behaviour as <b>unconventional</b>, you mean that they do not behave in the same way as most other people in their society. (人、態度、行為等) 非傳統的","examples":["Linus Pauling is an unconventional genius. 萊納斯·鮑林是個奇才。","He was known for his unconventional behaviour. 他曾因另類行為而出名。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>unconventional</b> way of doing something is not the usual way of doing it, and may be surprising. (做法) 非常規的","examples":["The vaccine had been produced by an unconventional technique. 這種疫苗是用非常規的技術生產出來的。","Despite his unconventional methods, he has inspired students more than anyone else. 雖然用的是非常規的方法，他卻比其他人更多地啟發了學生。"]}]}]},"understatement":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"不充分的陳述，以退為進的陳述；淡化，輕描淡寫"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a statement is an <b>understatement</b>, you mean that it does not fully express the extent to which something is true. 不充分的陳述","examples":["To say I'm disappointed is an understatement. 說我很失望是很輕的說法。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Understatement</b> is the practice of suggesting that things have much less of a particular quality than they really have. 低調說法; 輕描淡寫","examples":["...typical British understatement. …典型的英國式低調語言。"]}]}]},"uncertain":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"猶豫的，無把握的；無法確知的，不確定的；多變的，難預料的；信心不足的；（腳步）蹣跚的，踉蹌的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>uncertain</b> <b>about</b> something, you do not know what you should do, what is going to happen, or what the truth is about something. 不確定的","examples":["He was uncertain about his brother's intentions. 他對他兄弟的意圖心中無數。","They were uncertain of the total value of the transaction. 他們不清楚這筆交易的總額。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>uncertain</b>, it is not known or definite. 未知的; 不明確的","examples":["How much practical help they can give us is uncertain. 他們能給我們多少實際幫助還是個未知數。","It's uncertain whether they will accept the plan. 他們會不會接受這項計劃現在還不清楚。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不確定地","examples":["He entered the hallway and stood uncertainly. 他走進門廳，站在那兒不知道做什麼好。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that someone tells a person something <b>in no uncertain terms</b>, you are emphasizing that they say it strongly and clearly so that there is no doubt about what they mean. 非常明確地","examples":["She told him in no uncertain terms to go away. 她非常明確地叫他走開。"]}]}]},"underway":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"在進行中的；（船、火車等）在行進中的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If an activity is <b>underway</b>, it has already started. If an activity gets <b>underway</b>, it starts. 進行中的","examples":["An investigation is underway to find out how the disaster happened. 一項調查正在進行，以查明這場災難是如何發生的。","It was a cold evening, winter well underway. 那是個寒冷的夜晚，冬天早已來臨。"]}]}]},"unfair":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不公平的，不公正的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>unfair</b> action or situation is not right or fair. 不公平的","examples":["She was awarded $5,000 in compensation for unfair dismissal. 她因不公平的解僱獲得了$5000的補償。","It was unfair that he should suffer so much. 他遭受這麼多痛苦是不公平的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不公平地","examples":["He unfairly blamed Frances for the failure. 他不公平地把失敗歸咎於弗朗西絲。"]}]}]},"unforeseen":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"未預見到的，無法預料的，意料之外的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something that has happened was <b>unforeseen</b>, it was not expected to happen or known about beforehand. 未預見的","examples":["Radiation may damage cells in a way that was previously unforeseen. 輻射也許會以以前未預見的方式損壞細胞。","Unfortunately, due to unforeseen circumstances, this year's show has been cancelled. 遺憾的是，由於意外情況，今年的演出已被取消了。"]}]}]},"unfortunately":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"不幸地，遺憾地；<正式>不恰當地，不合適地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You can use <b>unfortunately</b> to introduce or refer to a statement when you consider that it is sad or disappointing, or when you want to express regret. 遺憾地","examples":["Unfortunately, my time is limited. 遺憾的是，我的時間有限。","Unfortunately for him, his title brought obligations as well as privileges. 對他來說遺憾的是，他的頭銜既帶來了特權也帶來了義務。"]}]}]},"uniquely":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"獨特地，與眾不同地，珍奇地；唯一地，僅，僅僅；（數學/技術）單義地，唯一確定地，一一對應地；（強調）極其，特別，非常"}],"sections":[]},"unidentified":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"未被識別或確認的，身份或來源不明的；（新聞用語）不願透露姓名或名稱的，匿名的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe someone or something as <b>unidentified</b>, you mean that nobody knows who or what they are. 身份不明的; 未知的","examples":["He was shot this morning by unidentified intruders at his house. 他今天早晨在家裡遭到身份不明的闖入者槍擊。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you use <b>unidentified</b> to describe people, groups, and organizations, you do not want to give their names. 不願透露姓名的","examples":["His claims were based on the comments of anonymous and unidentified sources. 他的主張基於匿名及未知出處的資料的評論。"]}]}]},"unimaginable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"難以想象的，不可思議的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>unimaginable</b>, you are emphasizing that it is difficult to imagine or understand well, because it is not part of people's normal experience. 難以想像的","examples":["The scale of the fighting is almost unimaginable. 戰鬥的規模幾乎難以想像。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"難以想像地","examples":["Conditions in prisons out there are unimaginably bad. 那裡各監獄的條件難以想像地惡劣。"]}]}]},"uniqueness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"獨特性；獨一無二；（數學、邏輯等）唯一性"}],"sections":[]},"unlimited":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無限制的，不受限制的；（多用於數量、供給、資源等）無限量的，無窮盡的；無條件的，無保留的；（法律、金融）無限責任（用於固定搭配 unlimited liability）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If there is an <b>unlimited</b> quantity of something, you can have as much or as many of that thing as you want. 無限制的","examples":["An unlimited number of copies can still be made from the original. 無限量的複製品依然能從原物製作出來。","You'll also have unlimited access to the swimming pool. 你將還可以無限制地進入該游泳池。"]}]}]},"unsanitary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不衛生的，有礙健康的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>unsanitary</b> is dirty and unhealthy, so that you may catch a disease from it. 不衛生的","examples":["...diseases caused by unsanitary conditions. ...由於衛生條件差導致的疾病。","Discharge of raw sewage into the sea is unsanitary and unsafe. 向大海里傾倒汙水既不衛生也不安全。"]}]}]},"unnecessary":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不必要的；多餘的，無用的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>unnecessary</b>, you mean that it is not needed or does not have to be done. 不必要的","examples":["The slaughter of whales is unnecessary and inhuman. 對鯨的屠宰是不必要且不人道的。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不必要地","examples":["I didn't want to upset my husband or my daughter unnecessarily. 我不想不必要地讓我的丈夫或女兒不開心。"]}]}]},"unsatisfactory":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不令人滿意的，不符合要求的，不合格的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe something as <b>unsatisfactory</b>, you mean that it is not as good as it should be, and cannot be considered acceptable. 不能令人滿意的","examples":["He asked a few more questions, to which he received unsatisfactory answers. 他又問了一些問題，沒有得到滿意的答案。"]}]}]},"urbanize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"使城市化，使都市化；使文雅"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to make (esp a predominantly rural area or country) more industrialized and urban 使城市化","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"to cause the migration of an increasing proportion of (rural dwellers) into cities 使(農村人口)遷徙到城市","examples":[]}]}]},"upcoming":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"即將來臨的，即將到來的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Upcoming</b> events will happen in the near future. 即將發生的","examples":["We'll face a tough fight in the upcoming election. 我們在即將到來的競選中將面臨一場惡戰。"]}]}]},"useless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無用的，無價值的；差勁的，無能的；無效的，徒勞的；（身體一部分或心智因有病或受到損害而）喪失功能的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something is <b>useless</b>, you cannot use it. (指某物) 不能用的","examples":["He realized that their money was useless in this country. 他意識到他們的貨幣在這個國家不能用。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something is <b>useless</b>, it does not achieve anything helpful or good. 沒用的; 不起作用的","examples":["She knew it was useless to protest. 她知道抗議是沒用的。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone or something is <b>useless</b>, you mean that they are no good at all. (人或物) 不行的","examples":["Their education system is useless. 他們的教育制度一點兒也不好。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"If someone feels <b>useless</b>, they feel bad because they are unable to help someone or achieve anything. (某人感到) 沒用的","examples":["She sits at home all day, watching TV and feeling useless. 她整天坐在家裡，看電視、感到自己沒用。"]}]}]},"utilization":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"利用，使用 (=utilisation)； 利用，使用"}],"sections":[]},"vaccinate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"給……接種疫苗；接種疫苗"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a person or animal <b>is vaccinated</b>, they are given a vaccine, usually by injection, to prevent them from getting a disease. 給…接種疫苗","examples":["Dogs must be vaccinated against distemper. 犬類必須接種疫苗以防犬熱病。","Have you had your child vaccinated against whooping cough? 你給你的孩子接種預防百日咳的疫苗了嗎？"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"疫苗的接種","examples":["Anyone who wants to avoid the flu should consider getting a vaccination. 任何希望避免患流感的人都應該考慮接種疫苗。"]}]}]},"vaccination":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"接種疫苗，種痘"}],"sections":[]},"validate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"批准，確認……有效；證實，確認；使生效，使具有法律效力；證明有……價值，認可"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>validate</b> something such as a claim or statement means to prove or confirm that it is true or correct. 證實","examples":["This discovery seems to validate the claims of popular astrology. 這一發現似乎證實了流行占星術的一些觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"To <b>validate</b> a person, state, or system means to prove or confirm that they are valuable or worthwhile. 證實…有價值","examples":["The Academy Awards appear to validate his career. 這些奧斯卡金像獎看來證實了他的職業生涯的價值。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"確認","examples":["When we want validation for our decisions we often turn to friends for advice and approval. 當我們想要獲得對我們的決定的確認時，我們經常向朋友們求得建議和認可。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"認可","examples":["I think the film is a validation of our lifestyle. 我想這部電影是對我們的生活方式的一種認可。"]}]}]},"viable":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"可望成功的，切實可行的；能存活的，能生長發育的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Something that is <b>viable</b> is capable of doing what it is intended to do. 可行的","examples":["Cash alone will not make Eastern Europe's banks viable. 單靠現金不可能使東歐的銀行維持下去。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"可行性","examples":["...the shaky financial viability of the nuclear industry. …核工業不可靠的財政可行性。"]}]}]},"vita":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（美國英語）個人簡歷，履歷（curriculum vitae 的較不常見說法，複數 vitae 或 vitas）；（拉丁語/義大利語）生活；生命（常見於固定短語、引語或題名，如 la dolce vita）；（Vita）維塔（英、法、俄、意、葡、匈、捷、塞、芬、德人名或姓氏）；比塔（西班牙語人名或姓氏）；PS Vita（索尼掌上遊戲機）"}],"sections":[]},"vandalize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vt.","zh":"故意毀壞，肆意破壞，摧殘（英式拼作 vandalise）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something such as a building or part of a building <b>is vandalized</b> by someone, it is damaged on purpose. 故意破壞","examples":["The walls had been horribly vandalized with spray paint. 這些牆壁已被人用噴漆破壞得一塌糊塗。"]}]}]},"visibility":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"能見度，能見距離；可見性，明顯性；關注度，知名度"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Visibility</b> means how far or how clearly you can see in particular weather conditions. 能見度","examples":["Visibility was poor. 能見度差。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you refer to the <b>visibility</b> of something such as a situation or problem, you mean how much it is seen or noticed by other people. 關注程度","examples":["The plight of the Kurds gained global visibility. 庫爾德人的困境受到了全球的關注。"]}]}]},"verify":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"核實，查證；證明，證實"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>verify</b> something, you check that it is true by careful examination or investigation. 核實","examples":["I verified the source from which I had that information. 我核實了我獲知那條資訊的來源。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>verify</b> something, you state or confirm that it is true. 證實","examples":["The government has not verified any of those reports. 該政府尚未證實那些報道中的任何一個。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"核實","examples":["All charges against her are dropped pending the verification of her story. 在她的陳述得到證實前，所有針對她的指控都被撤回。"]}]}]},"viewpoint":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"觀點，看法；視角，觀察點"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Someone's <b>viewpoint</b> is the way that they think about things in general, or the way they think about a particular thing. 視點","examples":["The novel is shown from the girl's viewpoint. 這部小說是從那個女孩兒的視點展開的。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>viewpoint</b> is a place from which you can get a good view of something. 視角","examples":["You have to know where to stand for a good viewpoint. 你得知道站在哪兒才會有好的視角。"]}]}]},"vice versa":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"反之亦然：用於表示剛才所說的在相反的順序中也是正確的。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Vice versa</b> is used to indicate that the reverse of what you have said is true. For example, \"women may bring their husbands with them, and vice versa\" means that men may also bring their wives with them. 反之亦然","examples":["They want to send students from low-income homes into more affluent neighborhoods and vice versa. 他們想把來自低收入家庭的學生送到較為富裕的地區，反之亦然。"]}]}]},"volatile":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"易變的，動盪不定的，反覆無常的；（情緒）易變的，易怒的，突然發作的；（液體或固體）易揮發的，易氣化的；（計算機記憶體）易失的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"揮發物；<罕>有翅的動物"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A situation that is <b>volatile</b> is likely to change suddenly and unexpectedly. 變化無常的","examples":["There have been riots before and the situation is volatile. 先前一直就有暴亂，局勢變化無常。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone is <b>volatile</b>, their mood often changes quickly. 情緒不穩定的","examples":["He accompanied the volatile actress to Hollywood the following year. 他次年陪那個情緒反覆無常的女演員去了好萊塢。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>volatile</b> liquid or substance is one that will quickly change into a gas. 易揮發的","examples":["The blast occurred when volatile chemicals exploded. 衝擊波是在易揮發的化學品爆炸時產生的。"]}]}]},"voucher":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"代金券，票券；收據，憑單；證人，保證人，證明者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"證實……的可靠性"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>voucher</b> is a ticket or piece of paper that can be used instead of money to pay for something. 代幣券; 購物券","examples":["The winners will each receive a voucher for a pair of movie tickets. 獲勝者每人將獲得一張代幣券，可換取兩張電影票。"]}]}]},"wallpaper":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"桌布，牆紙；（計算機）螢幕背景，桌面桌布"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"給房間、牆壁貼桌布；貼桌布"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"集合名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Wallpaper</b> is thick coloured or patterned paper that is used for covering and decorating the walls of rooms. 牆紙","examples":["...the wallpaper in the bedroom. …臥室裡的牆紙。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Wallpaper</b> is the background on a computer screen. (電腦桌面的) 背景","examples":["...preinstalled wallpaper images. …預先安裝的電腦背景圖。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>wallpapers</b> a room, they cover the walls with wallpaper. 貼牆紙於","examples":["We were going to wallpaper that room anyway. 反正我們也打算給那個房間貼牆紙的。"]}]}]},"waive":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"放棄（權利、要求等）；不強制執行（規定、限制），免除（費用）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>waive</b> your right to something, such as legal representation, you choose not to have it or do it. 放棄 (權利)","examples":["He pleaded guilty to the murders of three boys and waived his right to appeal. 他對殺害了3個男孩的罪行表示認罪伏法，並放棄上訴的權利。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If someone <b>waives</b> a rule, they say that people do not have to obey it in a particular situation. 放棄 (規則)","examples":["The art gallery waives admission charges on Sundays. 美術館星期天免費開放。"]}]}]},"waver":{"summaries":[{"pos":"vi.","zh":"躊躇，猶豫不決；搖擺，擺動，搖曳；動搖，減弱"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"躊躇，猶豫；動搖；搖擺，擺動；揮動者，揮手者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vi.","pos_name":"不及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>waver</b>, you cannot decide about something or you consider changing your mind about something. 猶豫不決; 躊躇","examples":["Some military commanders wavered over whether to support the coup. 一些軍隊指揮官對是否支援政變猶豫不決。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If something <b>wavers</b>, it shakes with very slight movements or changes. 搖擺","examples":["The shadows of the dancers wavered continually. 舞者的身影搖擺不停。"]}]}]},"willingness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"樂意，意願"}],"sections":[]},"wo":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"准尉軍官（warrant officer）；陸軍部（war office）"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"籲；慢些（whoa 的另一種拼寫）"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"困難；悲傷（woe 的另一種拼寫）"}],"sections":[]},"warning":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"警示，提醒，告誡；（對不良行為的）警告；預告，預兆"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"表示警告的，告誡的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"提醒注意（可能發生的事），使警惕；勸告（使有所防備），告誡；警告（warn 的現在分詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>warning</b> is something said or written to tell people of a possible danger, problem, or other unpleasant thing that might happen. 警告; 警報","examples":["The minister gave a warning that if war broke out, it would be catastrophic. 大臣警告說戰爭一旦爆發，將會是災難性的。","He was killed because he ignored a warning to put stronger cords on his parachute. 他死了，因為他忽視了要給降落傘裝上更結實的繩索的警告。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>warning</b> is an advance notice of something that will happen, often something unpleasant or dangerous. 預告","examples":["The soldiers opened fire without warning. 士兵們未發警告就開了火。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Warning</b> actions or signs give a warning. 警告性的","examples":["She ignored the warning signals and did not check the patient's medical notes. 她忽視了一些先兆症狀，也沒有檢查病人的病歷。"]}]}]},"woeful":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"悲哀的，悲慘的，不幸的；糟糕透頂的，極差的，遺憾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone or something is <b>woeful</b>, they are very sad. 悲傷的","examples":["...a woeful ballad. …一支悲傷的歌謠。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can use <b>woeful</b> to emphasize that something is very bad or undesirable. 糟糕透頂的","examples":["...the woeful state of the economy. …這種糟糕透頂的經濟狀況。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"悲傷地","examples":["He said woefully: \"I love my country, but it does not give a damn about me.\" 他悲傷地說：“我愛我的國家，但是它壓根就不在乎我。”"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"糟糕透頂地","examples":["Public expenditure on the arts is woefully inadequate. 藝術上的公共支出嚴重不足。"]}]}]},"weakness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"虛弱，軟弱；缺點，不足；疲軟；癖好，嗜好，寵愛"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>weakness</b> <b>for</b> something, you like it very much, although this is perhaps surprising or undesirable. 癖好","examples":["Stephen himself had a weakness for cats. 史蒂芬自己偏愛貓。"]}]}]},"withdrawal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"收回，撤回，停止；（對所說人的話的）收回，撤回；撤軍，撤退；不再參加，退出（組織）；提款，取錢；戒毒過程，脫癮期；脫癮症狀；沉默寡言，孤僻"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>withdrawal</b> of something is the act or process of removing it, or ending it. 去除; 結束","examples":["If you experience any unusual symptoms after withdrawal of the treatment then contact your doctor. 如果在治療結束後感到有任何異常症狀，請和您的醫生聯絡。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"Someone's <b>withdrawal</b> <b>from</b> an activity or an organization is their decision to stop taking part in it. 退出","examples":["...his withdrawal from government in 1946. …1946年他從政府的退出。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"A <b>withdrawal</b> is an amount of money that you take from your bank account. 所取錢款","examples":["I went to the machine to make the withdrawal and it told me to see someone inside the bank. 我到取款機前取款，而機器則指示我找銀行裡的人。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Withdrawal</b> is the period during which someone feels ill after they have stopped taking a drug they were addicted to. 戒毒過程","examples":["Withdrawal from heroin is actually like a severe attack of gastric flu. 戒除海洛因癮的過程實際上就像是患了嚴重的胃腸性感冒。"]}]}]},"year-end":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"年終的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"年終"}],"sections":[]},"workaholic":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"醉心於工作的人，工作狂"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"醉心於工作的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>workaholic</b> is a person who works most of the time and finds it difficult to stop working in order to do other things. 工作狂","examples":["Eighteen percent of 30-year-olds claim they are workaholics. 18％的30歲的人聲稱他們是工作狂。"]}]}]},"yearningly":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adv.","zh":"思念地；渴望地；同情地"}],"sections":[]},"zoom-out":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"縮小，縮小顯示，拉遠鏡頭：（攝影、軟體介面）調整鏡頭或畫面，降低放大倍率，使影象顯得更小、更遠，並顯示更廣闊的範圍；（引申）退後一步看全域性，從宏觀角度考慮。"}],"sections":[{"pos":"v.","pos_name":"動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"to decrease rapidly the magnification of the image of a distant object by means of a zoom lens (透過聚焦鏡對遠處物體的映像尺寸)快速縮小","examples":[]}]}]},"zoom-in":{"summaries":[{"pos":"","zh":"拉進目標視野"}],"sections":[{"pos":"phrasal verb.","pos_name":"動詞片語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If a camera <b>zooms in</b> <b>on</b> something that is being filmed or photographed, it gives a close-up picture of it. (像機鏡頭) 拉近","examples":["...a tracking system which can follow a burglar around a building and zoom in on his face. …一套可以在樓裡追蹤竊賊並將鏡頭拉近到他面部的跟蹤系統。"]}]}]},"worldwide":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"世界範圍的，全世界的"},{"pos":"adv.","zh":"在全世界，在世界各地"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something exists or happens <b>worldwide</b>, it exists or happens throughout the world. 在全世界","examples":["His books have sold more than 20 million copies worldwide. 他的書在全世界賣出了兩千多萬本。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Worldwide</b> is also an adjective. 全世界的","examples":["Today, doctors are fearing a worldwide epidemic. 如今，醫生們在擔心一次世界性的流行。"]}]}]},"availability":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"可用性，可得性；空閒，閒暇；未婚，單身"}],"sections":[]},"clientele":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"顧客群，客戶群；（總稱）委託人"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型集體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>clientele</b> of a place or organization are its customers or clients. 顧客群; 客戶群","examples":["This pub had a mixed clientele. 這家酒吧有混雜的顧客群。"]}]}]},"endorse":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"（公開）贊同，認可；（在廣告中對某種產品）宣傳，吹捧；（尤指在支票背面）簽名，背書；(在駕駛執照上)記錄違章事項"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you <b>endorse</b> someone or something, you say publicly that you support or approve of them. 公開支援; 贊同","examples":["I can endorse their opinion wholeheartedly. 我可以全心全意地支援他們的觀點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you <b>endorse</b> a product or company, you appear in advertisements for it. 代言","examples":["The twins endorsed a line of household cleaning products. 這對雙胞胎為一系列的家庭清潔產品代言過。"]}]}]},"compliance":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"服從，遵守；屈從，遷就；可塑性，柔量"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Compliance</b> <b>with</b> something, for example a law, treaty, or agreement, means doing what you are required or expected to do. 遵從","examples":["Inspectors were sent to visit nuclear sites and verify compliance with the treaty. 監察員被派去參觀核址並核實條約的遵守情況。"]}]}]},"entrepreneur":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"企業家，創業者；主辦者，提倡者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"An <b>entrepreneur</b> is a person who sets up businesses and business deals. 創業者","examples":[]}]}]},"adjacent":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"鄰近的，毗連的；（幾何）（兩個角）相鄰的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If one thing is <b>adjacent</b> <b>to</b> another, the two things are next to each other. 相鄰的","examples":["He sat in an adjacent room and waited. 他坐在一間相鄰的房間裡等。","The schools were adjacent but there were separate doors. 這些學校相鄰，但是有各自的門。"]}]}]},"jeopardize":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"危及，損害"}],"sections":[{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"To <b>jeopardize</b> a situation or activity means to do something that may destroy it or cause it to fail. 損害; 危及","examples":["He has jeopardized his future career. 他損害了他的前程。"]}]}]},"attendee":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"出席者，與會者，在場者"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>attendees</b> at something such as a meeting or a conference are the people who are attending it. 參加者","examples":[]}]}]},"minutes":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"分鐘（minute 的複數）；會議記錄；備忘錄"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"把……記錄在案；為……測定時間（minute 的單三形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>minute</b> is one of the sixty parts that an hour is divided into. People often say \"<b>a minute</b>\" or \"<b>minutes</b>\" when they mean a short length of time. 分鐘; 片刻","examples":["The pizza will then take about twenty minutes to cook. 接下來，比薩餅大約要用20分鐘烤好。","Bye Mom, see you in a minute. 再見，媽媽，一會兒見。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"The <b>minutes</b> of a meeting are the written records of the things that are discussed or decided at it. 會議記錄","examples":["He'd been reading the minutes of the last meeting. 他一直在看上次會議的記錄。"]}]},{"pos":"vt.","pos_name":"及物動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"When someone <b>minutes</b> something that is discussed or decided at a meeting, they make a written record of it. 做會議記錄","examples":["You don't need to minute that. 你不必記錄那些。"]}]},{"pos":"convention.","pos_name":"習慣表達","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People often use expressions such as <b>wait a minute</b> or <b>just a minute</b> when they want to stop you doing or saying something. 等一下","examples":["Wait a minute, folks, something is wrong here. 等一下，夥計們，這地方不對勁。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something will or may happen <b>at any minute</b> or <b>any minute now</b>, you are emphasizing that it is likely to happen very soon. 隨時","examples":["It looked as though it might rain at any minute. 看起來隨時都有可能下雨。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>last-minute</b> action is one that is done at the latest time possible. 最後一刻","examples":["He will probably wait until the last minute. 他可能會等到最後一刻。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that something happens <b>the minute</b> something else happens, you are emphasizing that it happens immediately after the other thing. 一…就…","examples":["The minute you do this, you'll lose control. 你一干這個，就會失去控制。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that something is <b>minute</b>, you mean that it is very small. 非常小的","examples":["Only a minute amount is needed. 只需很少的一點。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"precise or detailed 精確的; 詳細的","examples":[]}]}]},"would":{"summaries":[{"pos":"v.","zh":"將，將會（will 的過去式，用於轉述）；會......（用於提出意見或徵求建議時）；會，就（表示預期或設想）；會（表示不曾發生或不可能存在的事）；才會，就會（說明動機）；想（表示某人想要某物或想做某事）；就（不），偏（不）；請…...好嗎？（表示客氣地請求別人做某事）；要不要…...？；過去老是，過去常常；總是，愛（帶出一貫的行為）；<文>但願…...（表示強烈的願望）；也許，大概（表示推測或希望）；肯定，應該（表示有充分理由猜測是某種情況）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"modal.","pos_name":"情態動詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> when you are saying what someone believed, hoped, or expected to happen or be the case. 會 (表示相信或期待)","examples":["No one believed the soldiers stationed at the border would actually open fire. 沒人相信駐紮在邊境計程車兵們會真的開火。","Would he always be like this? 他會總像這樣嗎？"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> when saying what someone intended to do. 要 (表示想要做)","examples":["The statement added that although there were a number of differing views, these would be discussed by both sides. 該宣告補充說，儘管存在著許多不同的觀點，但這些要由雙方來討論。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> when you are referring to the result or effect of a possible situation. 會 (表示可能的結果或影響)","examples":["Ordinarily it would be fun to be taken to fabulous restaurants. 被人帶到豪華飯店去通常會很開心。","It would be wrong to suggest that police officers were not annoyed by acts of indecency. 錯誤的是認為警官不會為無禮行為所惱。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"You use <b>would</b>, or <b>would have</b> with a past participle, to indicate that you are assuming or guessing that something is true, because you have good reasons for thinking it. 一定 (表示假設或猜測)","examples":["You wouldn't know him. 你一定不認識他。","His fans would already be familiar with Caroline. 他的崇拜者們一定已熟悉卡羅琳。"]},{"num":"5.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> in the main clause of some \"if\" and \"unless\" sentences to indicate something you consider to be fairly unlikely to happen. 就會 (同)(if)(和)(unless)(引導的從句連用，表示某事極不可能發生)","examples":["If only I could get some sleep, I would be able to cope. 要是我能睡一會兒，就可以應付。"]},{"num":"6.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> to say that someone was willing to do something. You use <b>would not</b> to indicate that they refused to do something. 願意","examples":["They said they would give the police their full cooperation. 他們說他們願意同警方通力合作。","He wouldn't say where he had picked up the information. 他不願意說出他是在哪裡得到這個訊息的。"]},{"num":"7.","zh":"You use <b>would not</b> to indicate that something did not happen, often in spite of a lot of effort. 就不","examples":["He kicked, pushed, and hurled his shoulder at the door. It wouldn't open. 他又踢又推，還用肩膀撞門。它就是不開。"]},{"num":"8.","zh":"You use <b>would</b>, especially with \"like,\" \"love,\" and \"wish,\" when saying that someone wants to do or have a particular thing or wants a particular thing to happen. 想要","examples":["She asked me what I would like to do and mentioned a particular job. 她問我想做什麼，而且提到了一份特別的工作。","Ideally, she would love to become pregnant again. 按理想來說，她想要再次懷孕。"]},{"num":"9.","zh":"You use <b>would</b> with \"if\" clauses in questions when you are asking for permission to do something. 會 (同)(if)(引導的從句連用，表示請求允許)","examples":["Do you think it would be all right if I smoked? 你覺得我可以吸菸嗎？"]},{"num":"10.","zh":"You use <b>would</b>, usually in questions with \"like,\" when you are making a polite offer or invitation. 想要","examples":["Would you like a drink? 你想喝一杯嗎？","Would you like to stay? 你想留下來嗎？"]},{"num":"11.","zh":"You use <b>would</b>, usually in questions, when you are politely asking someone to do something. 能 (表示請求)","examples":["Would you do me a favour and get rid of this letter I've just received? 你能幫我個忙把我剛收到的這封信處理掉嗎？","Would you come in here a moment, please? 能請你進來待一會嗎？"]},{"num":"12.","zh":"You say that someone <b>would</b> do something when it is typical of them and you are critical of it. You emphasize the word <b>would</b> when you use it in this way. 總是 (表示批評)","examples":["Well, you would say that: you're a man. 哎，你總是說：你是個男人。"]},{"num":"13.","zh":"You use <b>would</b>, or sometimes <b>would have</b> with a past participle, when you are expressing your opinion about something or seeing if people agree with you, especially when you are uncertain about what you are saying. 可能會","examples":["I think you'd agree he's a very respected columnist. 我想你可能會同意，他是個十分受人尊敬的專欄作家。","I would have thought he was too old to do that job. 我可能會認為他年紀太大不適合做那份工作。"]},{"num":"14.","zh":"You use <b>I would</b> when you are giving someone advice in an informal way. 會 (指非正式提出建議)","examples":["If I were you I would simply ring your friend's doorbell and ask for your bike back. 如果我是你，我會按你朋友的門鈴，索回自己的腳踏車。"]},{"num":"15.","zh":"You use <b>you would</b> in negative sentences with verbs such as \"guess\" and \"know\" when you want to say that something is not obvious, especially something surprising. 會 (用在否定句中表示吃驚)","examples":["Chris is so full of artistic temperament you'd never think she was the daughter of a banker. 克里絲如此充滿藝術家的氣質，你絕不會想到她是一位銀行家的女兒。"]},{"num":"16.","zh":"You use <b>would have</b> with a past participle when you are saying what was likely to have happened by a particular time. 可能會 (表示過去時態的虛擬語氣)","examples":["Within ten weeks of the introduction, 34 million people would have been reached by our television commercials. 在10周的宣傳期內，3400萬人可能會看到我們的電視廣告。"]},{"num":"17.","zh":"You use <b>would have</b> with a past participle when you are referring to the result or effect of a possible event in the past. 就會 (表示過去時態的虛擬語氣)","examples":["My daughter would have been 17 this week if she had lived. 我的女兒如果還活著，這個星期就滿17歲了。"]},{"num":"18.","zh":"If you say that someone <b>would have</b> liked or preferred something, you mean that they wanted to do it or have it but were unable to. 本想","examples":["I would have liked a life in politics. 我本想從事政治。"]}]}]},"overdue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"（到期）未付的，未還的；未能準時的，延誤的； 早該發生的，早應完成的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you say that a change or an event is <b>overdue</b>, you mean that you think it should have happened before now. 早該發生的","examples":["This debate is long overdue. 這場辯論早就應該進行了。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Overdue</b> sums of money have not been paid, even though it is later than the date on which they should have been paid. 到期未付的","examples":["There is a 2% interest charge on overdue balances. 到期未付的餘款加收2%的利息。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>overdue</b> library book has not been returned to the library, even though the date on which it should have been returned has passed. 逾期未還的","examples":["...a library book now weeks overdue. …一本逾期數週尚未歸還的圖書館藏書。"]}]}]},"venue":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（事件的）發生地點，（活動的）場所；<英，法律>審判地（指郡或區）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"The <b>venue</b> for an event or activity is the place where it will happen. 舉辦場所","examples":["The International Convention Centre is the venue for a three-day arts festival. 國際會議中心是為期3天的藝術節的舉辦場所。"]}]}]},"bored":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"無聊的，厭倦的；（槍）有特定口徑的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使厭煩；鑽；盯著看（bore 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>bored</b>, you feel tired and impatient because you have lost interest in something or because you have nothing to do. 厭煩的","examples":["I am getting very bored with this entire business. 我開始對整件事感到非常厭倦。"]}]}]},"securities":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（金融）有價證券，證券；擔保；抵押物；保證人（security 的複數）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Security</b> refers to all the measures that are taken to protect a place, or to ensure that only people with permission enter it or leave it. 保安措施; 安全措施","examples":["They are now under a great deal of pressure to tighten their airport security. 他們目前承受著加強機場保安措施的巨大壓力。","Strict security measures are in force in the capital. 嚴格的安全措施在首都實施。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A feeling of <b>security</b> is a feeling of being safe and free from worry. 安全感","examples":["He loves the security of a happy home life. 他非常喜歡幸福的家庭生活所來的那種安全感。","If an alarm gives you that feeling of security, then it's worth carrying. 如果一個報警器能給你那種安全感，那就值得攜帶。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If something is <b>security</b> for a loan, you promise to give that thing to the person who lends you money, if you fail to pay the money back. 抵押品","examples":["The central bank will provide special loans, and the banks will pledge the land as security. 中央銀行將提供特別貸款,而各家銀行將以土地作為抵押品。"]},{"num":"4.","zh":"<b>Securities</b> are stocks, shares, bonds, or other certificates that you buy in order to earn regular interest from them or to sell them later for a profit. 有價證券","examples":["National banks can package their own mortgages and underwrite them as securities. 國家銀行可以組合包裝自己的的抵押貸款,以證券形式承銷。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If something gives you <b>a false sense of security</b>, it makes you believe that you are safe when you are not. 虛假的安全感","examples":[]}]}]},"classmate":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"同班同學，同學"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Your <b>classmates</b> are students who are in the same class as you at school or college. 同班同學","examples":[]}]}]},"earring":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"耳環，耳飾"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Earrings</b> are pieces of jewellery that you attach to your ears. 耳飾","examples":["...a pair of diamond earrings. …一副鑽石耳墜兒。"]}]}]},"goodness":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"善良，美德；（尤指食物中的）營養，精華"},{"pos":"int.","zh":"天哪，啊呀（用作“上帝”的替代語，表示吃驚或憤怒等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"interj.","pos_name":"interj.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"People sometimes say \"<b>goodness</b>\" or \"<b>my goodness</b>\" to express surprise. (表示驚訝) 天哪","examples":["Goodness, I wonder if he knows. 天哪，我不清楚他知不知道。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Goodness</b> is the quality of being kind, helpful, and honest. 善良","examples":["He retains a faith in human goodness. 他依然相信人性的善。"]}]}]},"careless":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"粗心大意的，疏忽的；自然的，隨便的；淡漠的，不關心的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>careless</b>, you do not pay enough attention to what you are doing, and so you make mistakes, or cause harm or damage. 粗心的","examples":["I'm sorry. How careless of me. 對不起，我太粗心了。","Some parents are accused of being careless with their children's health. 有些父母被指責對孩子的健康掉以輕心。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>careless</b> <b>of</b> something such as their health or appearance, you mean that they do not seem to be concerned about it, or do nothing to keep it in a good condition. 不在意的","examples":["He had shown himself careless of personal safety where the life of his colleagues might be at risk. 他在同事們有生命危險時表現出不顧個人安危之舉。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"粗心地","examples":["She was fined $200 for driving carelessly. 她由於粗心駕駛被罰$200。"]}]}]},"halloween":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"萬聖節前夕（指十月三十一日夜晚）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Halloween</b> is the night of the 31st of October and is traditionally said to be the time when ghosts and witches can be seen. On Halloween, children often dress up in costumes and go from door to door asking their neighbours for sweets. 萬聖節前夕","examples":[]}]}]},"babysitter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"臨時照顧幼兒者，臨時保姆"}],"sections":[]},"headache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"頭痛；使人頭痛的事，難題"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you have a <b>headache</b>, you have a pain in your head. 頭痛","examples":["I have had a terrible headache for the last two days. 最近兩天我犯了嚴重的頭痛病。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you say that something is a <b>headache</b>, you mean that it causes you difficulty or worry. 棘手的事","examples":["The airline's biggest headache is the increase in the price of aviation fuel. 令航空公司最頭疼的問題是航空燃料價格的上漲。"]}]}]},"mrt":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"平均輻射溫度 (mean radiant temperature)；大規模快運系統 (Mass Rapid Transit)；平均滯留時間 (mean residence time)；茅利塔尼亞 (Mauritania)"}],"sections":[]},"interested":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"感興趣的，關心的；利益相關的，當事的；有私心的，有偏見的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使感興趣，引起……的關注；勸說（某人）做（或參與）（interest 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>interested</b> <b>in</b> something, you think it is important and want to learn more about it or spend time doing it. 感興趣的","examples":["I thought she might be interested in Paula's proposal. 我以為她可能會對保拉的提議感興趣。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"An <b>interested</b> party or group of people is affected by or involved in a particular event or situation. 有關的","examples":["The success was only possible because all the interested parties eventually agreed to the idea. 因為有關各方最終同意了這一意見所以才有可能成功。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that one person is <b>interested</b> <b>in</b> another person, you mean that the first person would like to have a romantic or sexual relationship with the other person. 著迷的","examples":["I heard there are a lot of guys interested in her. 我聽說很多小夥子迷上了她。"]}]}]},"interesting":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"有趣的，有吸引力的；怪異的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使感興趣，引起……的關注；勸說（某人）做（或參與）（interest 的現在分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you find something <b>interesting</b>, it attracts your attention, for example, because you think it is exciting or unusual. 有趣的","examples":["It was interesting to be in a different environment. 換一換環境很有趣。"]}]}]},"midnight":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"午夜，半夜"},{"pos":"adj.","zh":"半夜的，午夜的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Midnight</b> is twelve o'clock in the middle of the night. 午夜","examples":["It was well after midnight by the time Anne returned to her apartment. 安妮回到公寓時早已過了午夜。"]}]},{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Midnight</b> is used to describe something that happens or appears at midnight or in the middle of the night. 午夜時的","examples":["It is totally out of the question to postpone the midnight deadline. 延遲午夜的最後期限是根本不可能的。"]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If someone <b>is burning the midnight oil</b>, they are staying up very late in order to study or do some other work. 開夜車","examples":["Chris is asleep after burning the midnight oil trying to finish his article. 克里斯在熬夜趕完他的文章後，睡著了。"]}]}]},"mr":{"summaries":[{"pos":"abbr.","zh":"先生（Mister）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"abbreviation for.","pos_name":"abbreviation for.","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"Master of the Rolls (英國)上訴法院最高法官","examples":[]}]}]},"married":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"結婚的，已婚的；婚姻的，夫婦的；專心於……的，全神貫注於……的；緊密結合的"},{"pos":"n.","zh":"已婚者"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"結婚，嫁，娶；為……主持婚禮；把……嫁給，為……娶親（marry 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>married</b>, you have a husband or wife. 已婚的","examples":["We have been married for 14 years. 我們已經結婚14年了。","She is married to an Englishman. 她嫁給了一個英國人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Married</b> means relating to marriage or to people who are married. 婚姻的; 夫妻的","examples":["For the first ten years of our married life we lived in a farmhouse. 在結婚後的前10年，我們住在一間農舍裡。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you say that someone is <b>married to</b> their work or another activity, you mean that they are very involved with it and have little interest in anything else. 獻身的","examples":["\"Sam was married to his job,\" McWhorter said. “薩姆對工作全身心投入，”麥克沃特說。"]}]}]},"scooter":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（兒童的）滑板車，踏板車；小型摩托車；（能快速穿越冰、雪、水等的）輕便小車"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"騎小型摩托車，玩踏板車（或滑冰、滑雪車等）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>scooter</b> is a small light motorcycle which has a low seat. 小型摩托車","examples":[]},{"num":"2.","zh":"A <b>scooter</b> is a type of child's bicycle which has two wheels joined by a wooden board and a handle on a long pole attached to the front wheel. The child stands on the board with one foot, and uses the other foot to move forward. 踏板車","examples":[]}]}]},"seafood":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"海鮮，海味，海產食品（常用作不可數名詞）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Seafood</b> is shellfish such as lobsters, mussels, and crabs, and sometimes other sea creatures that you can eat. 海產食品","examples":["...a seafood restaurant. …一家海鮮餐館。"]}]}]},"sneakers":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"運動鞋，膠底運動鞋（sneaker 的複數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Sneakers</b> are casual shoes with rubber soles that people wear often for running or other sports. 運動鞋","examples":[]}]}]},"slippers":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"拖鞋（slipper 的複數形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Slippers</b> are loose, soft shoes that you wear at home. 拖鞋","examples":["...a pair of old slippers. …一雙舊拖鞋。"]}]}]},"stomachache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"胃痛，肚子痛"}],"sections":[]},"teapot":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"茶壺；〈習語〉 a tempest in a teapot（小題大做）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>teapot</b> is a container with a lid, a handle, and a spout, used for making and serving tea. 茶壺","examples":[]}]},{"pos":"phrase.","pos_name":"習語","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you describe a situation as <b>a tempest in a teapot</b>, you think that a lot of fuss is being made about something that is not important. 小題大做","examples":["For some, it may seem silly, a tempest in a teapot. 對有些人來說，這似乎很荒唐，是小題大做。"]}]}]},"thanksgiving":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"感恩"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"<b>Thanksgiving</b> is the giving of thanks to God, especially in a religious ceremony. (對上帝) 感恩","examples":[]}]}]},"toothbrush":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"牙刷"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toothbrush</b> is a small brush that you use for cleaning your teeth. 牙刷","examples":[]}]}]},"toothache":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"（口腔）牙痛，牙疼"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"單數型名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"A <b>toothache</b> is a pain in one of your teeth. 牙痛","examples":[]}]}]},"surprised":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"意外的，驚訝的，詫異的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"使驚奇，使詫異，使感到意外（surprise 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>surprised</b> at something, you have a feeling of surprise, because it is unexpected or unusual. 吃驚的","examples":["This lady was genuinely surprised at what happened to her pet. 這位女士確實對發生在她寵物身上的事感到吃驚。"]}]}]},"tired":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"疲倦的，累的；枯燥乏味的，陳腐的；厭煩的；破舊的"},{"pos":"v.","zh":"（使）感到累，（使）感到疲勞；厭倦，使厭倦（tire 的過去式和過去分詞形式）"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>tired</b>, you feel that you want to rest or sleep. 疲倦的","examples":["Michael is tired and he has to rest after his long trip. 邁克爾累了，他在長途旅行之後不得不休息。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"You can describe a part of your body as <b>tired</b> if it looks or feels as if you need to rest it or to sleep. (身體部位) 疲勞的","examples":["Cucumber is good for soothing tired eyes. 黃瓜對緩解眼睛疲勞很有效。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"If you are <b>tired of</b> something, you do not want it to continue because you are bored of it or unhappy with it. 厭煩的","examples":["I am tired of all the speculation. 我厭煩了所有這些猜測。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"疲倦","examples":["He had to cancel some engagements because of tiredness. 他由於疲勞不得不取消一些約會。"]}]}]},"unhappy":{"summaries":[{"pos":"adj.","zh":"不快樂的，不幸福的；對…不滿的，不高興的；不適當的，不理想的，令人遺憾的"}],"sections":[{"pos":"adj.","pos_name":"形容詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you are <b>unhappy</b>, you are sad and depressed. 不幸福的","examples":["Her marriage is in trouble and she is desperately unhappy. 她的婚姻出了問題，她極不快樂。","He was a shy, sometimes unhappy man. 他是一個害羞、有時不快樂的人。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"If you are <b>unhappy</b> <b>about</b> something, you are not pleased about it or not satisfied with it. 對…不高興的; 對…不滿意的","examples":["He has been unhappy with his son's political leanings. 他一直不滿於兒子的政治傾向。","College students are unhappy with their school bookstores. 大學生們對學校的書店不滿意。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>unhappy</b> situation or choice is not satisfactory or desirable. 不令人滿意的; 不理想的","examples":["It is our hope that this unhappy chapter in the history of relations between our two countries will soon be closed. 我們希望我們兩國關係史上這一不愉快的階段將很快過去。","The legislation represents in itself an unhappy compromise. 這項立法本身就是不可取的妥協。"]}]},{"pos":"adv.","pos_name":"副詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不快樂地","examples":["\"I don't have your imagination,\" Kevin said unhappily. “我沒有你的想像力，”凱文不快地說。"]}]},{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"不可數名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"不高興; 不滿意","examples":["He has, by submitting his resignation, signalled his unhappiness with the government's decision. 他透過遞交辭呈已表明對政府決定的不滿。"]}]}]},"appraisal":{"summaries":[{"pos":"n.","zh":"評估，估價；評價；員工工作評估"}],"sections":[{"pos":"n.","pos_name":"有變體名詞","items":[{"num":"1.","zh":"If you make an <b>appraisal</b> <b>of</b> something, you consider it carefully and form an opinion about it. 估計","examples":["What is needed in such cases is a calm appraisal of the situation. 在此類情況下需要的是對形勢的冷靜估計。"]},{"num":"2.","zh":"<b>Appraisal</b> is the official or formal assessment of the strengths and weaknesses of someone or something. Appraisal often involves observation or some kind of testing. 評估","examples":["One of the most important tools for organizational improvement is the performance appraisal. 組織改進的最重要手段之一是業績評估。"]},{"num":"3.","zh":"An <b>appraisal</b> is a judgement that someone makes about how much money something such as a house or a company is worth. 估價","examples":["It may also be necessary to get a new appraisal of the property. 可能還需要對該房產做個新的估價。"]}]}]}};
